अंगारिका|अङ्गारिका
अंगारिका [अंगारं विद्यते अस्याः मत्वर्थे ठन्<BR>कप् च]<BR>1 A portable fire-pan.<BR>--2<BR>The stalk of the sugar-cane.<BR>--3 The<BR>bud of the Butea Frondosa (किंशुक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंगारिणी|अङ्गारिणी
अंगारिणी [अंगार-मत्वर्थे इनि]<BR>1 A<BR>small fire-pan.<BR>--2 The region<BR>heated by the sun, though no longer<BR>exposed to its rays.<BR>--3 A creeper<BR>in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंगारित|अङ्गारित|अङ्गारितं|अङ्गारितः
अंगारित a. [अंगारं अस्य संजातं; तारका˚<BR>इतच्] Charred, roasted, half-burnt.<BR>--तः --तं [अंगारमिव आचरति; अंगार-क्विप्<BR>ततः कर्तरि क्त.] An early bud of the<BR>किंशुक tree.<BR>--ता<BR>1 = अंगारधानी q. v.<BR>--2<BR>A bud in general.<BR>--3 A creeper.<BR>(लतामात्रे).<BR>--4 N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

