अजनि|अजनिः
अजन --नि See under अज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन|अजनं|अजनः
अजन a. [न. ब.] Destitute of<BR>men, tenantless, desert.<BR>--नः [कुत्सितार्थे<BR>नञ्] A bad or insignificant person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजननिः|अजननि
अजननिः f. [नञ् जन्-आक्रोशे अनि<BR>P. III. 3. 112] Cessation of existence;<BR>तस्याजननिरेवास्तु जननीक्लेशकारिणः<BR>Śi. 2. 45 may he not be born, may he<BR>cease to exist!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्मन्
अजन्मन् a. Unborn, epithet of<BR>the Unborn Being, the Eternal being;<BR>पुरुषस्य पदेष्वजन्मनः R. 8. 78. --m. [<BR>नास्ति जन्म यत्र] Final beatitude,<BR>absolution; तस्मात्स योगादधिगम्य<BR>योगमजन्मनेऽकल्पत जन्मभीरुः R. 18. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजन्य|अजन्यं
अजन्य a. Not fit to be produced;<BR>not favourable to mankind.<BR>--न्यं<BR>[लौकिकहेतुभिर्न जन्यते; जन्-णिच्-यत्] A<BR>portentous phenomenon, inauspicious<BR>to mankind, such as earthquake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजपः|अजप
अजपः [अस्पष्टं जपति निंदार्थे नञ्, जप्.<BR>अच्] A Brāhmaṇa who does not<BR>(properly) repeat his prayers (कुपाठक);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">Page0024-b+ 59</a>]<BR>अजपा ब्राह्मणास्तात शूद्रा जपपरायणाः ।<BR>भविष्यंति कलौ Mb.; one who reads<BR>heretical works.<BR>--पा [प्रयत्नेन न जप्या<BR>अप्रयत्नोच्चारितत्वात्; कर्मणि अच्] N. of a<BR>Mantra called हंस, which consists of<BR>a number of inhalations and<BR>exhalations (श्वासप्रश्वासयोः बहिर्गमनागमनाभ्यां<BR>अक्षरनिष्पादनरूपो जपः, स च हंसः सोहं<BR>इत्याकार एव; उच्छ्वासैरेव निश्वासैर्हंस इत्यक्षरद्वयं ।<BR>तस्मात्प्राणश्च हंसाख्य आत्माकारेण संस्थितः ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजंभ|अजम्भ|अजम्भः
अजंभ a. [नास्ति जंभो दंतो यस्य]<BR>Toothless.<BR>--भः<BR>1 A frog.<BR>--2 The<BR>sun.<BR>--3 Toothless state (of a child).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय|अजयः
अजय a. [नास्ति परैर्जयो यस्य]<BR>1<BR>Invincible, unsurpassed, unconquerable.<BR>--यः [न. त.] A defeat; लाभालाभौ<BR>जयाजयौ Bg. 2. 38.<BR>--2 N. of Agni<BR>(अजेन छागेन याति; या-क), or of Viṣṇu<BR>(according to some); of a<BR>lexicographer.<BR>--या [नास्ति जयो मादकत्वेन<BR>अस्यां]<BR>1 Hemp or भांग.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>friend of Durgā.<BR>--3 Māyā or illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजय्य|अजय्यं
अजय्य a. [न. त.]<BR>1 Invincible;<BR>सख्युस्ते स किल शतक्रतोरजय्यः Ś. 6. 29,<BR>R. 18. 8.<BR>--2 Not proper to be won<BR>at play; ˚य्यं जिगाय तान् Bopadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर|अजरः
अजर a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Not subject to old<BR>age or decay; ever young; अजरं<BR>वृद्धत्वं K. 103; cf. वृद्धत्वं जरया विना R. 1. 23.<BR>--2 Undecaying, imperishable;<BR>पुराणमजरं विदुः R. 10. 19; अनंतमजरं ब्रह्म<BR>Bh. 3. 76, H. Pr. 3, Pt. 1. 151,<BR>Ms. 2. 148.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A god (who is<BR>not subject to old age).<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>plant वृद्धदारक or जीर्णफंजी (˚रा also).<BR>--रा<BR>1 N. of a plant गृहकन्या or<BR>घृतकुमारी Aloe Perfoliata.<BR>--2 A house-lizard<BR>(गोधालिका).<BR>--रं [न जीर्यते क्षीयते जॄ-अच्]<BR>The Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजर्य|अजर्य्य|अजर्य्यं
अजर्य a. [न जीर्यति; जॄ कर्तरि यत्<BR>P. III. 1. 105]<BR>1 Not digestible.<BR>--2 Not<BR>decaying, imperishable, everlasting,<BR>perpetual.<BR>--र्यं (with संगतं expressed<BR>or understood) Friendship; मृगैरजर्यं<BR>जरसोपदिष्टं R. 18. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरत्|अजरन्त्
अजरत्, --रयु, --रस् a. Ved. Not old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरयु
अजरत्, --रयु, --रस् a. Ved. Not old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजरस्
अजरत्, --रयु, --रस् a. Ved. Not old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजवस्
अजवस् a. [जु-असुन्] Not quick,<BR>inactive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजस्तुंदं|अजस्तुन्द
अजस्तुंदं [अजस्य इव तुंदं अस्य सुट्<BR>निपातोयं] N. of a town, P. VI. 1. 155.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजस्र|अजस्रं
अजस्र a. [न जस्-र P. III. 2. 167;<BR>जसिर्नञ्पूर्वः क्रियासातत्ये वर्तते Sk.] Not<BR>ceasing, constant, perpetual;<BR>˚दीक्षाप्रयतस्य R. 3. 44.<BR>--स्रं ind. Ever,<BR>constantly, perpetually; वृथैव<BR>संकल्पशतैरजस्रं Ś. 3. 5; तच्च धूनोत्यजस्रं U. 4. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहत्स्वार्था
अजहत्स्वार्था [न जहत् स्वार्थोऽत्र,<BR>हाशतृ न. ब.] A kind of लक्षणा, in which<BR>the primary or original sense of a word<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">Page0024-c+ 58</a>]<BR>(which is used elliptically) does not<BR>disappear; as कुंताः प्रविशंति = कुंतधारिणः<BR>पुरुषाः; श्वेतो धावति = श्वेतवर्णो ऽश्वो धावति;<BR>also called उपादानलक्षणा q. v.;<BR>स्वसिद्धये पराक्षेपः; कुंताः प्रविशंति, यष्टयः प्रविशंति<BR>इत्यादौ कुंतादिभिरात्मनः प्रवेशसिद्ध्यर्थं<BR>स्वसंयोगिनः पुरुषा आक्षिप्यंते K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहल्लिंगं|अजहल्लिङ्ग|अजहल्लिंग|अजहल्लिङ्गः
अजहल्लिंगं [न जहत् लिंगं यं; हा-शतृ] A<BR>noun which does not change its<BR>original gender, even when used like an<BR>adjective; e. g. वेदः or श्रुतिः प्रमाणं (not<BR>प्रमाणः or ˚णा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजहा
अजहा [न जहाति शूकान् हा-श.] N.<BR>of a plant, cowage, Carpopogon<BR>Pruriens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजागर|अजागरः
अजागर a. [न. ब.] Not wakeful,<BR>not requiring keeping up.<BR>--रः [<BR>जागरयतीति जागरः न जागरो यस्मात्] A<BR>plant, Verbesina Prostrata (<BR>भृंगराजवृक्ष) (सेवनेन निद्राराहित्यकारकः, यदपेक्षया<BR>अन्यस्मिन् जागरणकर्तृत्वं नास्ति.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाजिः|अजाजि
अजाजिः --जी f. [अजेन छागेन वीयते<BR>गंधोत्कटत्वात् त्यज्यते, अज्-इन् वीभावाभावः]<BR>Cumin seed (श्वेतजीरक); कृष्णजीरक<BR>Nigella Indica; काकोदुंबरिका Ficus<BR>Oppositifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाजी
अजाजिः --जी f. [अजेन छागेन वीयते<BR>गंधोत्कटत्वात् त्यज्यते, अज्-इन् वीभावाभावः]<BR>Cumin seed (श्वेतजीरक); कृष्णजीरक<BR>Nigella Indica; काकोदुंबरिका Ficus<BR>Oppositifolia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजात|अजातः
अजात [न. त.] Unborn;<BR>अजातमृतमूर्खेभ्यो मृताजातौ सुतौ वरं Pt. 1.; not<BR>yet born, produced, or fully<BR>developed; ˚ककुद्, ˚पक्ष &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरि,<BR>--शत्रु a. [न जातः शत्रुः अस्य; जातस्य<BR>जंतुमात्रस्य न शत्रुः] having no enemy or<BR>adversary, not an enemy of any one.<BR>--(रिः --त्रुः) epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira;<BR>हंत जातमजातारेः प्रथमेन त्वयारिणा<BR>Śi. 2. 102; न द्वेक्षि यज्जनमतस्त्वमजातशत्रुः<BR>Ve. 3. 13; also of Śiva and various<BR>other persons.<BR>--ककुत्-द् m. (ब.) a<BR>young bull whose hump is not yet<BR>fully developed, P. V. 4. 146.<BR>--दंत<BR>a. [न जाता दंता यस्य यस्मिन् वयसि वा]<BR>one without teeth, or (a state) in<BR>which one has got no teeth.<BR>--पक्ष a.<BR>having undeveloped or unfledged<BR>wings.<BR>--व्यंजन a. having no<BR>distinctive marks or features (as a<BR>beard.)<BR>--व्यवहारः a minor (who<BR>has not attained his majority).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजाति|अजातिः
अजाति a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Having no<BR>caste, race &c.<BR>--2 Eternal, not<BR>produced.<BR>--ति f. Non-production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानिः|अजानि
अजानिः [नास्ति जाया यस्य]<BR>Without a wife; a widower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानिक
अजानिक a. [अजेन<BR>तद्विक्रयपालनादिना आनो जीवनं अस्त्यस्य; ठन् Tv.] A<BR>goatherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजानेय|अजानेयः
अजानेय a. Of high breed,<BR>powerful, fearless, undaunted (as a horse).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-a" target="_blank">Page0025-a+ 59</a>]<BR>--यः A horse of high breed. See<BR>आजानेय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजापक्वं|अजापक्व
अजापक्वं N. of a sort of medicinal<BR>preparation of ghee (used as a<BR>remedy against cough, asthma,<BR>consumption &c.) (अजादुग्धादिभ्योजातं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजामि
अजामि a. Ved. [न. त.]<BR>1 Not of<BR>kin or related; यत्र जामयः<BR>कृणवन्नजामि Rv. 10. 10. 10 (अजामिकर्माणि<BR>भ्रातृणां अजामियोग्यानि मैथुनसंबंधानिकर्माणि<BR>करिष्यंति Nir.)<BR>--2 Not parallel or<BR>correct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजि|अजिः
अजि a. [अजति; अज्-इ Uṇ. 4. 139]<BR>Going, moving; as पदाजिः walking<BR>on foot.<BR>--जिः f. [भावे इन्]<BR>1 Motion,<BR>going.<BR>--2 Throwing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजित|अजितं|अजितः
अजित a.<BR>1 Invincible,<BR>unconquerable, irresistible; ˚तं पुण्यं… महः<BR>U. 5. 27.<BR>--2 Not conquered or won (as<BR>a country &c.); not restrained,<BR>curbed, controlled, ˚आत्मन्; ˚इंद्रिय of<BR>uncontrolled soul or passion.<BR>--तः<BR>1<BR>N. of Viṣṇu or Śiva or of Buddha.<BR>--2 N. of a powerful antidote, or a<BR>poisonous sort of rat. --(pl.) A<BR>class of deities in the first<BR>Manvantara.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आपीडः having an<BR>invincible crown; N. of a King.<BR>--बला N. of a Jaina deity who<BR>acts under orders from the Arhat<BR>Ajita.<BR>--विक्रमः ‘of unsubdued<BR>power’, N. of Candragupta II.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिनं|अजिन
अजिनं [अजति क्षिपति रजआदि<BR>आवरणेन; अज्-इनच्, अजेरज च Uṇ. 2. 48,<BR>वीभावबाधनार्थं]<BR>1 The (hairy) skin of<BR>a tiger, lion, elephant &c., especially<BR>of a black antelope (used as a seat,<BR>garment &c.); अथाजिनाषाढधरः<BR>Ku. 5. 30, 67, Ki. 11. 15; ऐणेयेनाजिनेन<BR>ब्राह्मणं रौरवेण क्षत्रियं आजिनेन वैश्यं<BR>Āśval.<BR>--2 A sort of leather bag or<BR>bellows.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रा --त्री --त्रिका [<BR>अजिनं चर्मैव सुश्लिष्टं पत्रं पक्षो यस्याः सा, गौरा˚<BR>ङीप् स्वार्थे कन्] a bat.<BR>--फला [अजिनं<BR>भस्त्रेव फलं यस्याः सा] N. of a plant (<BR>भस्त्राकारफलो वृक्षः).<BR>--योनिः [अजिनस्य योनिः<BR>प्रभवः] a deer, an antelope.<BR>--वासिन् a.<BR>[अजिनं वस्ते, वस् णिनि] clad in an<BR>antelope-hide.<BR>--संधः [अजिनं संदधाति] a<BR>furrier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिर|अजिरं|अजिरः
अजिर a. [अज् गतौ किरन् वीभावाभावः<BR>Uṇ. 1. 53.] Quick, swift (शीघ्र)<BR>--रः<BR>1 A sort of mouse, hairy<BR>mole.<BR>--2 A kind of ceremony in<BR>pronouncing curses.<BR>--रं<BR>1 A court-yard,<BR>an enclosed space, arena;<BR>उटजाजिरप्रकीर्ण K. 39, Ki. 1. 16; so रण˚, गृह˚<BR>&c.<BR>--2 The body.<BR>--3 Any object of<BR>sense.<BR>--4 The wind, air.<BR>--5 A frog.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">Page0025-b+ 58</a>]<BR>--रा<BR>1 N. of a river.<BR>--2 N. of Durgā.<BR>--रः N. of a snake priest.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिराजः [कर्म˚] Ved. ‘a quick<BR>emperor,’ epithet of death.<BR>--शोचिस् a. [अजिरं शोचिर्यस्य] glittering,<BR>having tremulous or flashing light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिरीय
अजिरीय a. [अजिरं उत्करा˚ छ]<BR>Connected with a court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्म|अजिह्मं|अजिह्मः
अजिह्म a. [न. त.]<BR>1 Straight.<BR>--2 Upright, straight-forward, honest;<BR>अजिह्मामशठां शुद्धां जीवेत् ब्राह्मणजीविकां<BR>Ms. 4. 11, 7. 32; ˚गामिभिः Śi. 1. 63<BR>straight and honest, 3. 57, 9. 62.<BR>--ह्मः<BR>1 A frog.<BR>--2 A fish (probably a<BR>corruption of अजिह्व below).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग a. [उप. स.] going straight on;<BR>व्रजेद्दिशमजिह्मगः Ms. 6. 31<BR>--(गः) an<BR>arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजिह्वः|अजिह्व
अजिह्वः [न. ब.] A frog (which<BR>is supposed to have been deprived<BR>of its tongue by the curse of Agni<BR>whom frogs had offended.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीकवं|अजीकव
अजीकवं [अज्या शरक्षेपणेन कं ब्रह्माणं<BR>वाति प्रीणाति; वा-क] Śiva's bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीगर्तः|अजीगर्त|अजीगर्त्त
अजीगर्तः [अज्यै गमनाय गर्तं अस्य]<BR>1 (One that has a hole to go into)<BR>a serpent.<BR>--2 N. of a Brāhmaṇa in<BR>the family of भृगु and father of शुनःशेफ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीत
अजीत a. [न. त.] Not faded or<BR>withered, not faint.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुनर्वण्यं N. of a twofold rite to be<BR>performed by Kṣatriyas (<BR>अप्राप्तप्राप्तिकरणार्थो विधिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीतिः|अजीति
अजीतिः f. Prosperity, freedom<BR>from decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीर्ण|अजीर्णं
अजीर्ण a. Undigested;<BR>undecomposed.<BR>--र्णं, --र्णिः f.<BR>1 Indigestion;<BR>अजीर्णे भेषजं वारि जीर्णे वारि बलप्रदम्,<BR>अजीर्णे भोजनं विषं;<BR>कैरजीर्णभयाद्भ्रातर्भोजनं परिहीयते H. 2. 57, Ms. 4. 121.<BR>--2 Vigour, energy, absence of decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीव|अजीवः
अजीव a. [न. ब.] Devoid of life;<BR>lifeless, as a jar or a dead person.<BR>--वः<BR>[न. त.]<BR>1 Non-existence, death.<BR>--2<BR>(With Jainas) All that is not a living<BR>soul, i. e. the whole of जड or<BR>inanimate and unsentient substance<BR>(opp. जीव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवन
अजीवन a. [न. ब.] Devoid of<BR>livelihood.<BR>--नं Non-existence, death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजीवनिः|अजीवनि
अजीवनिः f. [न-जीव्-अनि<BR>P. III. 3. 112] Death, non-existence (used<BR>as an imprecation); अजीवनिस्ते शठ<BR>भूयात् Sk. may death seize thee,<BR>rogue! mayest thou cease to live!<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुर
अजुर --र्य a. [अज्-कुरच् न व्यादेशः]<BR>Ved. Not subject to decay or old<BR>age; strong, very swift or speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुर्य
अजुर --र्य a. [अज्-कुरच् न व्यादेशः]<BR>Ved. Not subject to decay or old<BR>age; strong, very swift or speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजुष्टिः|अजुष्टि
अजुष्टिः f. Non-enjoyment;<BR>feeling of dissatisfaction or<BR>disappointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजेय|अजेयः
अजेय a. [न. त.] Not fit to be<BR>conquered.<BR>--यं A sort of medicinal<BR>preparation of ghee said to serve as<BR>an antidote; पिबेत् घृतमजेयाख्यं Suś.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अजोष
अजोष a. [न. त.] Not gratified<BR>or satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जुका
अज्जु(ज्जू)का [अर्जयति या सा,<BR>अर्ज्-ऊक, पृ. रकारस्य जत्वम् Tv.] A<BR>courtezan (used only in dramas.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्जूका
अज्जु(ज्जू)का [अर्जयति या सा,<BR>अर्ज्-ऊक, पृ. रकारस्य जत्वम् Tv.] A<BR>courtezan (used only in dramas.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झटा
अज्झटा [Said to be fr. अज्] N.<BR>of a plant भूम्यामलकीं Flacourtia<BR>Cataphracta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्झलं|अज्झल
अज्झलं<BR>1 A shield.<BR>--2 A live<BR>coal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञ|अज्ञः
अज्ञ a. [न जानाति, ज्ञा-क, न. त.]<BR>1 Not knowing, unaware of,<BR>unconscious, devoid of knowledge or<BR>experience; अज्ञो भवति वै बालः<BR>Ms. 2. 153; ज्ञाज्ञौ (ज्ञः ईश्वरः अज्ञः जीवः) the<BR>knowing and unknowing, supreme<BR>and individual soul.<BR>--2 Ignorant,<BR>unwise, foolish, silly, stupid (said<BR>of men as well as animals); अज्ञः<BR>सुखमाराध्यः Bh. 2. 3, Pt. 2. 3.<BR>--3 Inanimate; not endowed with<BR>the power of understanding (अचेतन.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञका
अज्ञका [स्वार्थे कन्] An ignorant<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञात
अज्ञात a. Unknown, unexpected,<BR>unconscious, unaware; ˚भुक्त<BR>Ms. 5. 21 eaten unconsciously or<BR>unawares; ˚कुलशीलस्य whose family<BR>and character are unknown; ˚पातं<BR>सलिले ममज्ज R. 16. 72.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केतु<BR>a. [ब] Ved. of secret designs.<BR>--चर्या,<BR>--वासः remaining incognito (said of<BR>the Pāṇḍavas); हंसाः संप्रति पांडवा इव<BR>वनादज्ञातचर्यां गताः Mk. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञातिः|अज्ञाति
अज्ञातिः [न. त.] Not a kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञान|अज्ञानं
अज्ञान a. [न. ब.] Ignorant,<BR>unwise.<BR>--नं [न. त.] Ignorance,<BR>unconsciousness; especially, spiritual<BR>ignorance (अविद्या) which makes one<BR>consider his self as distinct from<BR>the Supreme spirit and the material<BR>world as a reality. According to<BR>the Vedāntins, अज्ञान is not merely<BR>a negative principle (ज्ञानस्य अभावः),<BR>but a distinct positive principle;<BR>oft. identified with माया, प्रकृति &c.<BR>See अविद्या also. In compounds<BR>अज्ञान may be translated by ‘unawares,’<BR>‘inadvertently,’ ‘unconsciously’;<BR>˚आचरित, ˚उच्चारित &c.; ˚नतः, -˚नेन,<BR>˚नात् unawares, inadvertently,<BR>unconsciously, unwillingly; ˚तः स्वचरितं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-a" target="_blank">Page0026-a+ 59</a>]<BR>नृपतिः शशंस R. 9. 77 committed<BR>unintentionally or unconsciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्ञानिन्
अज्ञानिन् = अज्ञ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्मन्
अज्मन् f. [अजति गच्छति स्वर्गं दानेन<BR>अनया, अज्-करणे मनिन् न वीभावः] A<BR>cow. --n. Career, passage; battle;<BR>house (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्येष्ठ
अज्येष्ठ a. Not the eldest or best,<BR>having no elder brothers; ˚वृत्ति not<BR>acting like the eldest brother; or<BR>acting like one who has no elder<BR>brother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्र|अज्रः
अज्र a. [fr. अज् to go] Ved. Agile,<BR>quick.<BR>--ज्रः A field, plain. [cf. L.<BR>ager; Gr. agros.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अज्विन्
अज्विन् a. Ved. [fr. अज्] Quick,<BR>agile, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंच्|अञ्च्
अंच् {c1c} U. (अंचु) (अंचति-ते,<BR>आनंचचे, अंचितुं, अच्यात् or अंच्यात्, अक्त or<BR>अंचित)<BR>1 To bend, incline, curl, curve;<BR>शिरोंचित्वा Bk. 9. 40.<BR>--2 To go, move,<BR>tend towards; स्वतंत्रा कथमंचसि<BR>Bk. 4. 22; also in अवांच् tending<BR>downward, प्रांच्, उदंच्; विष्वगंचति, सहांचति,<BR>तिरोंचति &c.; तस्मिन्नद्य रसालशाखिनि<BR>दशां दैवात् कृशामंचति Bv. 1. 48 having<BR>gone, being reduced, to &c.; त्वं<BR>चेदंचसि लोभं 46 art greedy;<BR>संकोचमंचति सरः 17.<BR>--3 To worship, honour,<BR>reverence; भीमोयं शिरसांचति<BR>Ve. 5. 27 salutes; to adorn, grace; See<BR>अंचित below.<BR>--4 To request, ask or<BR>call for, desire.<BR>--5 To murmur,<BR>speak indistinctly. --Caus. or {c10c} U.<BR>To manifest, unfold; मुदमंचय<BR>Gīt. 10. [cf. Zend anku; Gr. ankulos; L.<BR>uncus.] With अप to put away, drive<BR>away; (intr.) to run away.<BR>--आ to<BR>bend; दक्षिणं जान्वाच्य; जान्वाक with<BR>bent knees.<BR>--उप to draw or raise<BR>(water).<BR>--परि to cause to revolve,<BR>whirl, twist.<BR>--वि to draw or bend<BR>asunder; to extend, stretch out.<BR>--सं<BR>to crowd or drive together, to bend<BR>together, See समक्न also; to go<BR>properly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंचित|अञ्चित|अञ्चितः
अंचित p. p.<BR>1 (a) Curved, bent;<BR>˚उत्थित Dk. 125 bent and raised;<BR>किंचिदंचितां दृष्टिं संचारयंती 143 bent or<BR>oblique look; दोर्लीलांचितचंद्रशेखरधनुः<BR>Mv. 1. 54 bent; ˚सव्यजानुः<BR>R. 18. 51, Bk. 2. 31, 9. 40; ˚लांगूलः (कपिः),<BR>˚स्कंधः (वृक्षः). (b) Arched and<BR>handsome (as eyebrows); ˚अक्षिपक्ष्मन्<BR>R. 5. 76; crisped, curled (as hair);<BR>स्वसितांचितमूर्धजा Mb.<BR>--2 Gone.<BR>--3<BR>Honoured; adorned, graced,<BR>graceful, handsome, दोर्दंडांचितमहिमा<BR>Mv. 7. 8 graced, adorned; गतेषु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-b" target="_blank">Page0026-b+ 60</a>]<BR>लीलांचितविक्रमेषु Ku. 1. 34 sportively<BR>handsome; ˚ताभ्यां गताभ्यां R. 2. 18,<BR>लीलांचितभ्रूलता Dk. 124, 151; समधुरं<BR>मधुरंचितविक्रमः R. 9. 24 of esteemed or<BR>adorable prowess; Ki. 15. 53.<BR>--4 Sewn or<BR>woven, arranged; अर्धांचिता<BR>सत्वरमुत्थितायाः (रशना) R. 7. 10<BR>halfstrung or woven (गुंफित Malli.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रं [ब.] a lotus with<BR>curved leaves.<BR>--भ्रूः a woman having<BR>arched or handsome eyebrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंचतिः|अञ्चति|अञ्चतिः
अंचतिः [अंच्-गतौ कर्तरि अति]<BR>1<BR>Wind.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 One who goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंचलः|अञ्चल|अंचलं|अञ्चलः
अंचलः --लं [अंचति प्रांतं; अंच्-अलच्]<BR>1 The border or end (of a garment),<BR>skirt or hem (Mar. पदर);<BR>क्षीणांचलमिव पीनस्तनजघनायाः Udbhaṭa.<BR>--2<BR>Corner or outer angle (as of the eye);<BR>दृगंचलैः पश्यति केवलं मनाक् ibid.;<BR>यदि चलांचले लोचने Mv. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंचलं|अञ्चल|अंचलः|अञ्चलः
अंचलः --लं [अंचति प्रांतं; अंच्-अलच्]<BR>1 The border or end (of a garment),<BR>skirt or hem (Mar. पदर);<BR>क्षीणांचलमिव पीनस्तनजघनायाः Udbhaṭa.<BR>--2<BR>Corner or outer angle (as of the eye);<BR>दृगंचलैः पश्यति केवलं मनाक् ibid.;<BR>यदि चलांचले लोचने Mv. 6. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंज्|अञ्ज्
अंज् {c7c} P. (rarely Ā.) (अनक्ति or अंक्ते,<BR>आनंज, अंजिष्यति-अंक्ष्यति,<BR>अंजित्वा-अंक्त्वा-अक्त्वा, अंजितुं, अंक्तुं, अक्त)<BR>1 To anoint, smear<BR>with, bedaub.<BR>--2 To make clear,<BR>show, represent, characterize; मा<BR>नांजी राक्षसीर्मायाः Bk. 9. 49<BR>--3 To go.<BR>--4 To<BR>shine, be beautiful.<BR>--5 To honour,<BR>celebrate.<BR>--6 To decorate. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>smear with, नांजयंतीं स्वके नेत्रे<BR>Ms. 4. 44.<BR>--2 To speak or shine.<BR>--3 To<BR>cause to go. [cf. Zend anj; L.<BR>unctum, ungo.] --With अधि to fit<BR>out, equip, furnish.<BR>--आ {1} to<BR>anoint, smear. {2} to smooth, polish,<BR>prepare. {3} to honour, respect.<BR>--नि {1} to smear. {2} to conceal or<BR>hide oneself.<BR>--प्रति {1} to smear.<BR>{2} to adorn, decorate.<BR>--सं {1} to<BR>smear. {2} to fit out, equip, harness.<BR>{3} to honour. {4} to join together,<BR>to consume, devour; to adorn,<BR>decorate, beautify (mostly Ved. in<BR>these senses). {5} to unite, to put<BR>together, compose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजनः|अञ्जन|अञ्जनं|अञ्जनः
अंजनः<BR>1 A kind of lizard.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a tree or mountain.<BR>--3 N. of the<BR>guardian elephant (of the west<BR>or s. w.)<BR>--नं [अज्यते अनेन; अंज् ल्युट्]<BR>1 Anointing, smearing with;<BR>दंतधावनमंजनं पूर्वाह्ण एव कुर्वीत Ms. 4. 152;<BR>mixing; unfolding, manifesting.<BR>--2<BR>Collyrium or black pigment used<BR>to paint the eyelashes; विलोचनं<BR>दक्षिणमंजनेन संभाव्य R. 7. 8 salve;<BR>अमृत˚ U. 4. 19 ambrosial salve;<BR>कुर्वन् ˚मेचका इव दिशो मेघः समुत्तिष्ठते<BR>Mk. 5. 8, 1. 34; (fig. also) अज्ञानांधस्य<BR>लोकस्य ज्ञानांजनशलाकया । चक्षुरुन्मीलितं<BR>येन तस्मै पाणिनये नमः Śik. 45;<BR>पटुतरविवेकांजनजुषां Bh. 3. 84; cf. also दारिद्र्यं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-c" target="_blank">Page0026-c+ 63</a>]<BR>परमांजनं; (fig.) impurity, as in<BR>निरंजन, q. v.<BR>--3 Paint, a cosmetic<BR>ointment.<BR>--4 Magic ointment.<BR>--5 A<BR>special kind of material of the black<BR>pigment, such as antimony (used<BR>as collyrium, lamp-black &c.) (सौवीर)<BR>--6 Ink.<BR>--7 Fire.<BR>--8 Night.<BR>--9 (नं<BR>ना) (Rhet.) A suggested meaning; also<BR>the process by which such meaning is<BR>suggested. It is the power of<BR>suggestion (founded on अभिधा or लक्षणा<BR>denotation or indication), by which<BR>something else is understood from<BR>a word which, though having more<BR>meanings than one, has been<BR>restricted to a single meaning by<BR>relations of conjunction,<BR>disjunction &c. (संयोग, विप्रयोग, साहचर्य,<BR>विरोधिता &c.), or, briefly, the use of<BR>a word of several meanings in a<BR>special sense determined by the<BR>context; e. g. सशंखचक्रो हरिः the<BR>adjective restricts Hari to mean ‘Viṣṇu’<BR>alone, and not ‘a lion’ or ‘monkey’;<BR>so रामलक्ष्मणौ दाशरथी, रामार्जुनौ<BR>भार्गवकार्तवीर्यौ &c.; cf. अनेकार्थस्य शब्दस्य<BR>वाचकत्वे नियंत्रिते ।<BR>संयोगाद्यैरवाच्यार्थधीकृद्व्यापृतिरंजनं ॥ K. P. 2., S. D. 23-6; See<BR>व्यंजना also.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिका [<BR>अंजनादधिका कृष्णत्वात्] a kind of lizard.<BR>--अद्रिः-गिरिः (कर्म.) [अंजनमिव कृष्णः गिरिः] N.<BR>of a mountain, See नीलगिरि.<BR>--अंभस्<BR>n. eye-water.<BR>--केशी [अंजनमिव केशो<BR>यस्याः] N. of a vegetable perfume<BR>(हट्टविलासिनीनामकं गंधद्रव्यं<BR>यत्संयोगात्केशस्यातीव कृष्णत्वं) (Mar. नखला).<BR>--नामका<BR>[ष. त.] a swelling of the eye-lid,<BR>stye.<BR>--शलाका a stick or pencil for<BR>the application of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजनकः|अञ्जनक|अञ्जनकः
अंजनकः A portion of the Vedas<BR>containing the word अंजन.<BR>--की N.<BR>of a medicinal plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजना|अञ्जना
अंजना<BR>1 N. of the female elephant<BR>of the north.<BR>--2 N. of the mother<BR>of Māruti or Hanūmat. [She was<BR>the daughter of a monkey named<BR>Kuñjara and wife of Kesarin, another<BR>monkey. She was in a former birth a<BR>celestial nymph by name Puñjikasthalī<BR>and was born on earth owing to a curse.<BR>One day while she was seated on the<BR>summit of a mountain, her garment<BR>was slightly displaced, and the God<BR>of Wind being enamoured of her<BR>beauty assumed a visible form, and asked<BR>her to yield to his desires. She<BR>requested him not to violate her chastity, to<BR>which he consented; but he told her<BR>that she would conceive a son equal to<BR>himself in strength and lustre by virtue<BR>of his amorous desire fixed on her, and<BR>then disappeared. In course of time<BR>Anjanā conceived and brought forth a son who<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-a" target="_blank">Page0027-a+ 59</a>]<BR>was called Māruti being the son of<BR>Māruta.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजनावती|अञ्जनावती
अंजनावती [अंजनं विद्यते अस्याः<BR>अधिककृष्णवर्णत्वात्]<BR>1 N. of the female<BR>elephant of the northeast quarter.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a tree कालांजनवृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजनिका|अञ्जनिका
अंजनिका [अंजना स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>1 A<BR>species of lizard; a small mouse.<BR>--2 N. of the mate of the elephant<BR>सुप्रतीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजनी|अञ्जनी
अंजनी [अज्यते चंदनकुंकुमादिभिरसौ,<BR>अंज्-कर्मणि-ल्युट् ङीप्]<BR>1 A woman<BR>decorated with the application of<BR>pigments, ointments, sandal &c., or<BR>one fit for such application.<BR>--2 [<BR>करणे-ल्युट्] N. of two plants कटुकावृक्ष<BR>and कालांजनवृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजलिः|अञ्जलि|अञ्जलिः
अंजलिः [अंज्-अलि Uṇ. 4. 2]<BR>1 A cavity<BR>formed by folding and joining the<BR>open hands together, the hollow of the<BR>hands; hence, a cavity-ful of anything<BR>(changed to अंजल or ˚लि after द्वि<BR>and त्रि in द्विगु comp., P. V. 4. 102);<BR>न वार्यंजलिना पिबेत् Ms. 4. 63; सुपूरो<BR>मूषिकांजंलिः Pt. 1. 25;<BR>अरण्यबीजांजलिदानलालिताः Ku. 5. 15; प्रकीर्णः पुष्पाणां<BR>हरिचरणयोरंजालेरंयं Ve. 1. 1 a<BR>cavityful of flowers; so जलस्यांजलयो दश<BR>Y. 3. 105 10 cavity-fuls or libations<BR>of water; श्रवणांजलिपुटपेयं Ve. 1. 4<BR>to be drunk by the cavity of the<BR>ear; अंजलिं रच्, बंध्, कृ or आधा fold<BR>the hands together and raise them<BR>to the head in supplication or<BR>salutation; बद्धः कातर्यादरविंदकुड्मलनिभो<BR>मुग्धः प्रणामांजलिः U. 3. 37.<BR>--2 Hence a<BR>mark of respect or salutation; कः<BR>शक्रेण कृतं नेच्छेदधिमूर्धानमंजलिम्<BR>Bk. 8. 84; बध्यतामभययाचनांजलिः R. 11. 78.<BR>--3 A measure of corn = कुडव; another<BR>measure = प्रसृत, or one-half of a मानिका.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. folding the hands,<BR>respectful salutation; लुब्धमर्थेन<BR>गृह्णीयात् क्रुद्धं चांजलिकर्मणा Chāṇ. 33.<BR>--कारिका {1} an earthen doll making the<BR>अंजलि (?). {2} N. of a plant, Mimosa<BR>Pudica (लज्जालु).<BR>--पुटः-टं the cavity<BR>formed by joining the hands<BR>together; hollowed palms of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजलिका|अञ्जलिका
अंजलिका [अंजलिरिव कायते प्रकाशते;<BR>कै-क टाप् Tv.] A small mouse.<BR>--कः<BR>N. of one of Arjuna's arrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजस्|अञ्जस्
अंजस् n.<BR>--(जः) [अनक्तिं गच्छति<BR>मिश्रयति वा अनेन; अंज् गतौ मिश्रणे च असन्]<BR>Speed, velocity, strength; fitness,<BR>propriety; ointment, preparation (?).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पा drinking Soma<BR>offering.<BR>--सवः rapid preparation of<BR>Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजस|अञ्जस|अञ्जसः
अंजस a. [अंज्-असच्] Not<BR>crooked, straight; honest, upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजसा|अञ्जसा
अंजसा adv. (instr. of अंजस्)<BR>1<BR>Straight on.<BR>--2 Truly, correctly,<BR>accurately, properly, justly, rightly;<BR>साक्षाद् दृष्टोसि न पुनर्विद्मस्त्वां वयमंजसा<BR>Ku. 6. 22 we do not know you<BR>rightly or correctly; विद्महे शठ<BR>पलायनच्छलान्यंजसा R. 19. 31, न हि कश्चित्प्रियः<BR>स्त्रीणामंजसा Subhāṣita; सर्वमेवांजसा<BR>वद Ms. 8. 101.<BR>--3 Directly (साक्षात्),<BR>--4<BR>Soon, quickly, instantly; स<BR>गच्छत्यंजसा सद्म शाश्वतं Ms. 2. 244.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अयन a. going straight on.<BR>--कृत<BR>a. [तृ. अलुक्] done rightly or justly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजसीन|अञ्जसीन
अंजसीन a. [अंजस्-ख] Ved.<BR>Straightforward, going straight on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजि|अञ्जि|अञ्जिः
अंजि a. Ved. [अंज्-इन्] Unctuous,<BR>slimy; lubricated; shining, brilliant.<BR>--जिः<BR>1 A mark made with sandal &c.<BR>a Tilaka mark; रोहितांजिरनड्वान् Yaj.<BR>(रक्ततिलक).<BR>--2 A commander, sender<BR>&c.<BR>--जिः --जी f.<BR>1 An ointment,<BR>pigment.<BR>--2 Colour, hue.<BR>--3 The sexual<BR>organ (?).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सक्थ a. having<BR>coloured thighs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजिव|अञ्जिव
अंजिव a. Slippery, smooth(?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजिष्ठः|अञ्जिष्ठ|अञ्जिष्ठः
अंजिष्ठः --ष्णुः [अनक्ति स्वकिरणैः विश्वं;<BR>अंज्-इष्ठच्-इष्णुच् Uṇ. 4. 2] The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजिष्णुः|अञ्जिष्णु|अञ्जिष्णुः
अंजिष्ठः --ष्णुः [अनक्ति स्वकिरणैः विश्वं;<BR>अंज्-इष्ठच्-इष्णुच् Uṇ. 4. 2] The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अक्त|अक्तः
अक्त p. p. Smeared over, bedaubed,<BR>anointed &c.; mostly as latter part<BR>of compounds; घृत˚, तैल˚, शोणित˚<BR>&c.<BR>--क्ता Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजी|अञ्जी
अंजी [अंजि, वा ङीप्]<BR>1 A blessing,<BR>auspicious desire.<BR>--2 A pounding<BR>machine (पेषणयंत्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजीरः|अञ्जीर|अंजीर|अंजीरं|अञ्जीरं|अञ्जीरः
अंजीरः --रं [अंज्-बाहु˚ईरन्; perhaps<BR>a Persian word]. A species of the<BR>fig-tree and its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंजीरं|अञ्जीर|अंजीर|अञ्जीरं|अंजीरः|अञ्जीरः
अंजीरः --रं [अंज्-बाहु˚ईरन्; perhaps<BR>a Persian word]. A species of the<BR>fig-tree and its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्
अट् {c1c} P. (rarely Ā.) (अटति, आट,<BR>अटितुं, अटित). To wander or roam<BR>about (with loc.); roam over<BR>(sometimes with acc.); भो बटो भिक्षामट Sk.<BR>go to beg alms; आट नैकटिकाश्रमान्<BR>Bk. 4. 12; महीमटन् Dk. 38 --desid. अटिटिषति;<BR>--freq. अटाट्यते to wander about<BR>habitually, as a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट
अट a. Wandering; क्षपाटः Bk. 2. 30<BR>a night-roamer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटनं|अटन
अटनं Wandering, roaming; भिक्षा˚,<BR>रात्रि˚ &.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटनिः|अटनि
अटनिः --नी f. [अटति मौर्वीं; अट्-अनि वा<BR>ङीप्] The notched extremity of a<BR>bow; सुमनसो नमयन्नटनौ धनुः N. 4. 96;<BR>निन्यतुः स्थलनिवेशिताटनी लीलयैव धनुषी<BR>अधिज्यतां R. 11. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटनी
अटनिः --नी f. [अटति मौर्वीं; अट्-अनि वा<BR>ङीप्] The notched extremity of a<BR>bow; सुमनसो नमयन्नटनौ धनुः N. 4. 96;<BR>निन्यतुः स्थलनिवेशिताटनी लीलयैव धनुषी<BR>अधिज्यतां R. 11. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटा
अटा [अट् वा अङ्] The habit of<BR>roaming about (as a religious<BR>mendicant); so अट्या, अटाट्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटल
अटल a. [न. त.] Firm, steady,<BR>solid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटरु
अटरु --रू --षः (Ety. doubtful) N.<BR>of a very useful medicinal plant, the<BR>shrub वासक Justicia Adhatoda, or<BR>Adhatoda Vasika (Mar. अडुळसा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटरू
अटरु --रू --षः (Ety. doubtful) N.<BR>of a very useful medicinal plant, the<BR>shrub वासक Justicia Adhatoda, or<BR>Adhatoda Vasika (Mar. अडुळसा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटरुषः|अटरुष
अटरु --रू --षः (Ety. doubtful) N.<BR>of a very useful medicinal plant, the<BR>shrub वासक Justicia Adhatoda, or<BR>Adhatoda Vasika (Mar. अडुळसा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटरूषः|अटरूष
अटरु --रू --षः (Ety. doubtful) N.<BR>of a very useful medicinal plant, the<BR>shrub वासक Justicia Adhatoda, or<BR>Adhatoda Vasika (Mar. अडुळसा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटविः|अटवि
अटविः --वी f. [अटंति चरमे वयसि<BR>मृगयाविहाराद्यर्थे वा यत्र; अट् अनि, वा ङीप्] A<BR>forest, wood; आहिंड्यते अठव्या अटवीं<BR>Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटवी
अटविः --वी f. [अटंति चरमे वयसि<BR>मृगयाविहाराद्यर्थे वा यत्र; अट् अनि, वा ङीप्] A<BR>forest, wood; आहिंड्यते अठव्या अटवीं<BR>Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अटविकः|अटविक
अटविकः A forester = आटविकः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट्
अट्ट् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To kill.<BR>--2 To transgress,<BR>go beyond (fig. also). --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>lessen, diminish.<BR>--2 To despise,<BR>contemn, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्ट|अट्टं|अट्टः
अट्ट a. [अट्टयति अनाद्रियते अन्यत् यत्र;<BR>अट्ट्-घञ्]<BR>1 High, lofty; loud.<BR>--2<BR>Frequent, constant (in comp).<BR>--3<BR>Dried, dry.<BR>--ट्टः --ट्टं [आधारे घञ्]<BR>1 An<BR>apartment on the roof or upper<BR>story, a garret.<BR>--2 A turret, buttress,<BR>tower; गोपुर˚ Māl. 9. 1;<BR>नरेंद्रमार्गाट्टइव R. 6. 67, 16. 11.<BR>--3 A<BR>market-place, market (probably<BR>for हट्ट).<BR>--4 A fine linen cloth.<BR>--5 A<BR>palace, palatial building.<BR>--6 Killing,<BR>injuring.<BR>--7 Excess, superiority.<BR>--ट्टं<BR>Food, boiled rice; अट्टशूला जनपदाः<BR>Mb. (अट्टं अन्नं शूलं विक्रेयं येषां ते<BR>Nīlakaṇṭha).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अट्टहासः very<BR>loud laughter.<BR>--स्थली [अट्टप्रधाना<BR>स्थली शाक. त.] a place or country<BR>full of palaces &c.<BR>--हासः,<BR>--हसितं, --हास्यं [कर्म˚] a loud or boisterous<BR>laughter, a horselaugh, cachinnation,<BR>usually of Śiva; त्र्यंबकस्य Me. 58; गिरिश˚<BR>Dk. 1.<BR>--हासिन् [अट्टं हसति-हस्-णिनि]<BR>{1} N. of Śiva. {2} one who laughs very<BR>loudly.<BR>--हासकः [अट्टहासेन कायते; कै-क]<BR>N. of a plant (कुंद) Jasminum<BR>Multiflorum or Hirsutum (<BR>शुभ्रपुष्पत्वाच्छुभ्रहासतुल्यता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टकः|अट्टक
