अट्टट्ट
अट्टट्ट ind. [अट्टोऽनादरः अट्टप्रकारः<BR>अट्टस्य गुणवाचितया द्वित्वं शकंध्वा˚ पररूपं Tv.]<BR>Very loud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टनं|अट्टन
अट्टनं [अट्ट्यते अनाद्रियते रिपुरनेन,<BR>अट्टकरणे ल्युट्] A weapon shaped like a<BR>discus (चक्राकारफलकास्त्रं).<BR>--नं [भावे<BR>ल्युट्] Disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टाट्टः|अट्टाट्ट
अट्टाट्टः [अट्टट्टवत् न पररूपं]<BR>1<BR>Overbearing conduct, contempt, disdain.<BR>--2 Excess, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालः|अट्टाल
अट्टालः --लकः [अट्टैव अलति पर्याप्तो भवति,<BR>अल्-अच् स्वार्थे कन्] An apartment on<BR>the roof, an upper story; a palace;<BR>सर्वतोभद्रं नामाट्टालकमारुह्य Mv. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालकः|अट्टालक
अट्टालः --लकः [अट्टैव अलति पर्याप्तो भवति,<BR>अल्-अच् स्वार्थे कन्] An apartment on<BR>the roof, an upper story; a palace;<BR>सर्वतोभद्रं नामाट्टालकमारुह्य Mv. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अट्टालिका
अट्टालिका [अट्टाल, स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>1 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">Page0028-a+ 59</a>]<BR>palace, a lofty mansion<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>country.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः [उपपद त.]<BR>a mason, a bricklayer (one who<BR>builds royal mansions); कुलटायां च<BR>शूद्रायां चित्रकारस्य वीर्यतः । भवेदट्टालिकाकारः<BR>पतितो जारदोषतः.<BR>--बंधः [ष. त.] a kind<BR>of base or foundation in<BR>architecture; ˚धं बद्धः P. III. 4. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अठ्
अठ् {c1c} U. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अठिल्ला
अठिल्ला N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्
अड् {c1c} P. To try, exert, attempt.<BR>{c5c} P. To pervade, attain (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्ड्
अड्ड् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To join.<BR>--2 To attack.<BR>--3 To argue, infer, discern,<BR>meditate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्डनं|अड्डन
अड्डनं [करणे ल्युट्] A shield. See<BR>अट्टनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अड्डचलः|अड्डचल
अड्डचलः A part of the plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्
अण्<BR>1 P. To sound.<BR>--2 ({c4c} A.) To<BR>breathe, live (for अन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणक|अणकः
अण(न)क a. [अणति यथेच्छं नदति,<BR>अण्-अच् कुत्सायां कन् च] Very small,<BR>contemptible, mean, insignificant,<BR>wretched; पापाणके कुत्सितैः<BR>P. II. 1. 54; oft. in comp. in the sense of<BR>deterioration or contempt; ˚कुलालः Sk.<BR>a contemptible potter.<BR>--कः A kind<BR>of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक|अनकः
अण(न)क a. [अणति यथेच्छं नदति,<BR>अण्-अच् कुत्सायां कन् च] Very small,<BR>contemptible, mean, insignificant,<BR>wretched; पापाणके कुत्सितैः<BR>P. II. 1. 54; oft. in comp. in the sense of<BR>deterioration or contempt; ˚कुलालः Sk.<BR>a contemptible potter.<BR>--कः A kind<BR>of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणव्यं|अणव्य
अणव्यं [अणोः सूक्ष्मशस्यचीनादिकस्य<BR>भवनं क्षेत्रं; अणु-यत्] A field of aṇu, see<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणिः|अणि
अणिः m.<BR>--णी [अणति शब्दायते अण्-इन्]<BR>1 The point of a needle.<BR>--2 A<BR>linchpin, the pin or bolt at the end of a<BR>pole of carriage.<BR>--3 A limit.<BR>--4 The<BR>corner of a house (used for killing<BR>animals &c.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मांडव्यः [<BR>अण्या चिह्नितो मांडव्यः] N. of a sage said<BR>to have been impaled on an अणी or<BR>linch-pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणु|अणुः
अणु a. (णु-ण्वी f.) [अण्-उन्] Minute,<BR>small, little, atomic (opp. स्थूल,<BR>महत्); अणोरणीयान् Bg. 8. 9; सर्वोप्ययं<BR>नन्वणुः Bh. 3. 26 insignificantly<BR>small; अण्वपि भयं Ms. 6. 40; अण्वपि<BR>याच्यमानः Pt. 4. 26 asked but an atom,<BR>a very small quantity, Ms. 3. 51.<BR>--णुः<BR>1 An atom, a very small<BR>particle (an exceedingly small<BR>measure); the mote in a sunbeam, the<BR>smallest perceptible quantity;<BR>अस्थूलमनण्वह्रस्वमदीर्घं ब्रह्म; अणुं पर्वतीकृ<BR>Bh. 2. 78 to magnify; cf. also ‘To make<BR>mountains of molehills.’<BR>--2 An atom<BR>of time (व्यंजनमर्धमात्रा तदर्धं अणु);<BR>it is said to be 54,675,000th part<BR>of a Muhūrta (48 minutes).<BR>--3<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--4 N. of very<BR>small grain such as सर्षप, चीनक<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">Page0028-b+ 60</a>]<BR>&c., अनणुषु दशमांशोऽणुष्वथैकादशांशः<BR>Līlā.<BR>--णु n. the fourth part of a<BR>Mātrā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः [अणुः अंतो यस्य]<BR>a hair-splitting question; (अण्वंतः<BR>सूक्ष्मांतः सूक्ष्मवस्तुनिर्णयांतः प्रश्नः Śaṅkara).<BR>--तैलं N. of a medicinal oil.<BR>--भा [<BR>अण्वी सूक्ष्मा भा प्रभा यस्याः सा] lightning.<BR>--मात्र a. [अणुः परिमाणं यस्य अणु-मात्रच्] of<BR>the size of an atom.<BR>--रेणुः [कर्म.]<BR>atomic dust.<BR>--रेवती [अणुः सूक्ष्मा रेवतीतारेव]<BR>N. of a plant (दंतीवृक्ष) Croton<BR>Polyandrum.<BR>--वादः the doctrine of<BR>atoms, atomic theory, the theory<BR>that all material substances are<BR>primarily atoms and secondarily<BR>aggregates, and that all atoms are<BR>eternal.<BR>--वीक्षणं [ष. त.] {1} minute<BR>observation, observation of very<BR>minute parts. {2} [अणुः सूक्ष्मो वीक्ष्यते<BR>अनेन करणे ल्युट्] an instrument, like the<BR>microscope, enabling one to discern<BR>the smallest objects.<BR>--व्रीहिः [कर्म.] a<BR>fine sort of grain, rice &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणिमन्
अणिमन् m. [अणु-इमनिच्], अणुता-त्वं<BR>1 Minuteness, smallness, thinness,<BR>leanness, fineness.<BR>--2 Atomic nature.<BR>--3 The superhuman power of<BR>becoming as small as an atom, one of<BR>the 8 powers or siddhis of Śiva;<BR>(अणिमा लघिमा प्राप्तिः प्राकाम्यं महिमा तथा ।<BR>ईशित्वं च वशित्वं च तथा कामावसायिता)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणुक|अणुकः
अणुक a. [स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>1 Very small,<BR>atomic.<BR>--2 Subtle, too fine.<BR>--3 Acute.<BR>--कः A small kind of grain, See अणु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्वी
अण्वी Ved. A finger(?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अण्वं|अण्व
अण्वं Ved. A fine hole in the<BR>strainer for the Soma juice (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणीयस्
अणीयस्, अणिष्ठ a. [अणु-ईयसुन्, इष्टच्]<BR>Smaller, smallest, very small;<BR>अणोरणीयांसं Bg. 8. 9 very small;<BR>अणीयसि कारणेऽनणीयानादरो दृश्यते Dk. 142<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणिष्ठ
अणीयस्, अणिष्ठ a. [अणु-ईयसुन्, इष्टच्]<BR>Smaller, smallest, very small;<BR>अणोरणीयांसं Bg. 8. 9 very small;<BR>अणीयसि कारणेऽनणीयानादरो दृश्यते Dk. 142<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अणूभू
अणूभू {c1c} P. To become minute or<BR>atomic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंठ्|अण्ठ्
अंठ् {c1c} A. (also अठ्) अंठते, अठते<BR>To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंठित|अण्ठित
अंठित p. p.<BR>1 Gone.<BR>--2 Rained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंडः|अण्ड|अंडं|अण्डं|अण्डः
अंडः --डं [अमंति संप्रयोगं यांति अनेन;<BR>अम्-ड Uṇ. 1. 111]<BR>1 The testicles.<BR>--2<BR>The scrotum.<BR>--3 An egg; oft. used<BR>with reference to the world as<BR>having sprung from the primordial<BR>egg of Brahmā; ब्रह्मांडच्छत्रंदडः<BR>Dk. 1.<BR>--4 The musk bag.<BR>--5 Semen<BR>virile.<BR>--6 N. of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आकर्षणं castration.<BR>--आकार,<BR>--आकृति a. [बहु.] egg-shaped, oval,<BR>elliptical.<BR>--(रः --तिः) an ellipse.<BR>--कटाहः,<BR>--हं [अंडं ब्रह्मांडं कटाहमिव] the shell of<BR>the ब्रह्मांड or mundane egg.<BR>--कोटरपुष्पी [अंडमिव कोटरे मध्ये पुष्पं यस्याः]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">Page0028-c+ 59</a>]<BR>N. of a plant अजांत्री or नीलवुह्ना.<BR>--कोशः --षः, --षकः [ष. त.] the<BR>scrotum.<BR>--ज a. [अंडात् जायते; जन्-ड]<BR>born from an egg.<BR>--(जः) {1} a bird,<BR>oviparous being; मूकांडजं (काननं)<BR>Ku. 3. 42. {2} a fish. {3} a snake. {4} a<BR>lizard. {5} Brahmā.<BR>--(जा) musk.<BR>--धरः<BR>[ष. त.] N. of Śiva.<BR>--वर्धनं, --वृद्धिः<BR>f. swelling of the scrotum,<BR>hydrocele.<BR>--सू a. oviparous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंडं|अण्ड|अण्डं|अंडः|अण्डः
अंडः --डं [अमंति संप्रयोगं यांति अनेन;<BR>अम्-ड Uṇ. 1. 111]<BR>1 The testicles.<BR>--2<BR>The scrotum.<BR>--3 An egg; oft. used<BR>with reference to the world as<BR>having sprung from the primordial<BR>egg of Brahmā; ब्रह्मांडच्छत्रंदडः<BR>Dk. 1.<BR>--4 The musk bag.<BR>--5 Semen<BR>virile.<BR>--6 N. of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आकर्षणं castration.<BR>--आकार,<BR>--आकृति a. [बहु.] egg-shaped, oval,<BR>elliptical.<BR>--(रः --तिः) an ellipse.<BR>--कटाहः,<BR>--हं [अंडं ब्रह्मांडं कटाहमिव] the shell of<BR>the ब्रह्मांड or mundane egg.<BR>--कोटरपुष्पी [अंडमिव कोटरे मध्ये पुष्पं यस्याः]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">Page0028-c+ 59</a>]<BR>N. of a plant अजांत्री or नीलवुह्ना.<BR>--कोशः --षः, --षकः [ष. त.] the<BR>scrotum.<BR>--ज a. [अंडात् जायते; जन्-ड]<BR>born from an egg.<BR>--(जः) {1} a bird,<BR>oviparous being; मूकांडजं (काननं)<BR>Ku. 3. 42. {2} a fish. {3} a snake. {4} a<BR>lizard. {5} Brahmā.<BR>--(जा) musk.<BR>--धरः<BR>[ष. त.] N. of Śiva.<BR>--वर्धनं, --वृद्धिः<BR>f. swelling of the scrotum,<BR>hydrocele.<BR>--सू a. oviparous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंडकः|अण्डक|अण्डकः
अंडकः [अंड, स्वार्थे कन्] The<BR>scrotum.<BR>--कं [अल्पार्थे कन्] A small egg;<BR>जगदंडकैकतरखंडमिव Śi. 9. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंडालुः|अण्डालु|अण्डालुः
अंडालुः [अंडः अस्ति अस्य; अंड आलुच्]<BR>A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंडीरः|अण्डीर|अण्डीरः
अंडीरः [अंडः अस्ति अस्य; अंड-ईरन्]<BR>A full-grown or full-developed man,<BR>a strong or powerful person;<BR>चिरादंडीरेण त्वयि तदपि रामेण गुणितं A. R. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्|अन्त्|अंत्
अत् {c1c} P. (अति), अतति, अतितुं,<BR>अत्त-अतित<BR>1 To go, walk; wander, to go<BR>constantly.<BR>--2 To obtain (mostly Ved.)<BR>--3 To bind.<BR>--4 (अंतति) To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतकः|अतक
अतकः [अतति सततं गच्छति; अत्-कन्]<BR>A wanderer, a passerby, traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतनं|अतन|अतनः
अतनं [अत्-ल्युट्] Going,<BR>wandering.<BR>--नः A wanderer, a passerby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतज्ज्ञ
अतज्ज्ञ a. [न तत्-जानाति] Not<BR>knowing that (तत् i. e. Brahma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतट|अतटः
अतट a. [न. ब.] Having no<BR>shore or beach; precipitate, steep.<BR>--टः<BR>1 A precipice, a steep crag.<BR>--2 N. of a hill.<BR>--3 The lower part<BR>of the earth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रपातः a<BR>steep precipice; a fall headlong<BR>from a precipice; a precipitate fall;<BR>मनोरथानामतटप्रपातः Ś. 6. 9 of my<BR>hopes there is a precipitate fall<BR>(some read the line as मनोरथा नाम<BR>तटप्रपातः and take it to mean<BR>‘verily our desires are like the<BR>crumblings of river banks).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतथा
अतथा ind. Not so; ˚उचित a. not<BR>deserving that, not used to such<BR>things; क्लेशानामतथोचितः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतदर्हं|अतदर्ह
अतदर्हं ind. Unjustly,<BR>undeservedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतद्गुणः|अतद्गुण
अतद्गुणः (Rhet.) The<BR>‘nonborrower’, N. of a figure of speech<BR>in which the thing in question does<BR>not assume the quality of another<BR>though there is a reason for it;<BR>परगुणाननुहारस्त्वस्य तत्स्यादतद्गुणः; e. g. धवलोसि<BR>यद्यपि सुंदर तथापि त्वया मम रंजितं हृदयम् ।<BR>रागपूरितेपि हृदये सुभग निहितो न रक्तोसि ॥<BR>K. P. 10; or<BR>संगतान्यगुणानंगीकारमाहुरतद्गुणम् । चिरं रागिणि मच्चित्ते निहितोपि न<BR>रज्यसि ॥ Kuval.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संविज्ञानः<BR>N. of a variety of Bahuvrīhi; e. g.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">Page0029-a+ 59</a>]<BR>दृष्टसमुद्रमानय; अत्र गुणीभूतस्य समुद्रस्य<BR>नानयनेऽन्वयः इति ˚नः बहुव्रीहिः; लंबकर्णमानय<BR>इति तु तद्गुणसंविज्ञानः. Tv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0028-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतंत्र|अतन्त्र
अतंत्र a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Having no<BR>ropes or musical strings (as a<BR>musical instrument); नातंत्री वाद्यते वीणा<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 Unrestrained; not<BR>necessarily binding; not being the object<BR>of the rule under consideration;<BR>थस्वग्रहणमतंत्रं, क्लीबत्वं ˚त्रं Sk.<BR>--3<BR>Without formulas or empirical actions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतंद्र|अतन्द्र
अतंद्र --द्रित --न् --ल a. Alert,<BR>unwearied, careful, vigilant; अतंद्रिता सा<BR>स्वयमेव वृक्षकान् Ku. 5. 14, R. 17. 39,<BR>H. Pr. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतंद्रित|अतन्द्रित
अतंद्र --द्रित --न् --ल a. Alert,<BR>unwearied, careful, vigilant; अतंद्रिता सा<BR>स्वयमेव वृक्षकान् Ku. 5. 14, R. 17. 39,<BR>H. Pr. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतंद्रिन्|अतन्द्रिन्
अतंद्र --द्रित --न् --ल a. Alert,<BR>unwearied, careful, vigilant; अतंद्रिता सा<BR>स्वयमेव वृक्षकान् Ku. 5. 14, R. 17. 39,<BR>H. Pr. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतंद्रिल
अतंद्र --द्रित --न् --ल a. Alert,<BR>unwearied, careful, vigilant; अतंद्रिता सा<BR>स्वयमेव वृक्षकान् Ku. 5. 14, R. 17. 39,<BR>H. Pr. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप
अतप a.<BR>1 Not excited, cool.<BR>--2<BR>Unostentations.<BR>--3 Unemployed.<BR>--पाः (pl.) N. of a class of deities<BR>among Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतपस्
अतपस् --स्क [न. ब.] One who<BR>neglects his religious austerities;<BR>अतपास्त्वनधीयानः Ms. 4. 190; an<BR>irreligious or impious man; इदं ते<BR>नातपस्काय Bg. 18. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतपस्क
अतपस् --स्क [न. ब.] One who<BR>neglects his religious austerities;<BR>अतपास्त्वनधीयानः Ms. 4. 190; an<BR>irreligious or impious man; इदं ते<BR>नातपस्काय Bg. 18. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतप्त
अतप्त a. Not heated &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तनु a. {1} One whose body is not<BR>marked (with red mudrās &c.). {2}<BR>who has not fully mortified his<BR>body by penance. {3} whose body<BR>or mass is cool (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क|अतर्कः
अतर्क a. [न. ब.] Illogical, void<BR>of reasoning.<BR>--र्कः<BR>1 Absence of<BR>argument or reasoning, bad logic.<BR>--2 An illogical reasoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्कित
अतर्कित a. Unthought of,<BR>unexpected; सममेव गतोस्यतर्कितां गतिमंगेन<BR>च जीवितेन च. Ku. 4. 22;<BR>Bh. 3. 137; ˚गमनेन Mu. 4.<BR>--तं adv.<BR>Unexpectedly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आगत, --उपनत a.<BR>occuring or befalling<BR>unexpectedly, quite accidental, sudden;<BR>˚दर्शनोल्लासितलोचनया अनया Māl. 3; ˚उपपन्नं<BR>दर्शनं Ku. 6. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतर्क्य
अतर्क्य a. Inconceivable; baffling<BR>thought or reasoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतल|अतलं|अतलः
अतल a. Bottomless.<BR>--लं [अस्य<BR>भूखंडस्य तलं पृषो˚ इदमोऽत्त्वम्] N. of a<BR>पाताल or lower region, one of the 7<BR>Pātālas, being the first among<BR>them.<BR>--लः N. of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्पृश्,<BR>--स्पर्श a. [न तले स्पृश्यते कर्मणि क्विप्; न<BR>तलस्य स्पर्शो यत्र] bottomless, very<BR>deep, unfathomable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतव्यस्
अतव्यस् a. Ved. Not very<BR>strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतस्
अतस् ind. [इदं-तसिल्]<BR>1 Than this;<BR>from this (having a comparative<BR>force); अतो देवा अवंतु नो यतो<BR>विष्णुर्विचक्रमे Rv. 1. 22. 16; किमु परमतो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-b" target="_blank">Page0029-b+ 60</a>]<BR>नर्तयसि मां Bh. 3. 6; अतोऽन्यथा<BR>Ms. 5. 31.<BR>--2 From this or that cause,<BR>hence, consequently, so, therefore<BR>(corr. to यत्, यस्मात् or हि, expressed<BR>or understood); अंतर्गतं प्राणभृतां हि<BR>वेद सर्वं भवान्भावमतोभिधास्ये<BR>R. 2. 43, 3. 50, Ku. 2. 5; अथातो<BR>ब्रह्मजिज्ञासा Ś. B. now therefore<BR>&c.<BR>--3 Hence, from this place;<BR>henceforth (of time or place); (-परं,<BR>-ऊर्ध्वं), afterwards.<BR>--4 Then (corr. of<BR>यदि-यद्).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थं --निमित्तं on this<BR>account, hence, for this reason.<BR>--एव<BR>for this very reason.<BR>--ऊर्ध्वं<BR>henceforth; afterwards.<BR>--परं (a) further<BR>on, any longer (with abl.);<BR>hereafter; निवसिष्यसि मय्येव अत उर्ध्वं<BR>Bg. 12. 8. (b) beyond this, further than<BR>this; भाग्यायत्तमतःपरं Ś. 4. 16 more<BR>than this; अतःपरं नास्ति ममोत्तरं V. 2<BR>now I have nothing more to say;<BR>(c) afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसः|अतस
अतसः [अतति गच्छति इत्यतसः<BR>अतस्-अच् Uṇ. 3. 117]<BR>1 Wind, air.<BR>--2<BR>The soul.<BR>--3 A garment made of<BR>the fibre of flax (˚सं generally).<BR>--4<BR>A weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसिः|अतसि
अतसिः Ved. [अत्-असिच्] A<BR>wandering mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतसी
अतसी<BR>1 Common flax.<BR>--2 Hemp.<BR>--3 Linseed.<BR>--4 A thicket, copse (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अति
अति ind. [अत्-इ]<BR>1 A prefix used<BR>with adjectives and adverbs,<BR>meaning ‘very’, ‘too’, ‘exceedingly’,<BR>‘excessively’, ‘very much,’ and<BR>showing उत्कर्ष; नातिदूरे not very<BR>far from; ˚कृश very lean; ˚भृशं very<BR>much; also with verbs or verbal<BR>forms; ˚सिक्तमेव भवता Sk.; स्वभावो<BR>ह्यतिरिच्यते &c.<BR>--2 (With verbs) Over,<BR>beyond; अति-इ go beyond,<BR>overstep; so ˚क्रम्, ˚चर्, ˚वह् &c. In this case<BR>अति is regarded as a preposition<BR>उपसर्ग.<BR>--3 (a) (With nouns or pronouns)<BR>Beyond, past, surpassing, superior to,<BR>eminent, respectable, distinguished,<BR>higher, above, (used with acc. as a<BR>कर्मप्रवचनीय, or as first member of<BR>Bah. or Tat. Comp.; in which<BR>last case it has usually the sense of<BR>eminence or higher degree: अतिगो,<BR>˚गार्ग्यः, = प्रशस्ता गौः, शोभनो, गार्ग्यः;<BR>˚राजन् an excellent king; or the<BR>sense of अतिक्रांत must be<BR>understood with the latter member which<BR>will then stand in the accusative<BR>case; अतिमर्त्यः = मर्त्यमतिक्रांतः; ˚मालः,<BR>अतिक्रांतो मालां; so अतिकाय, ˚केशर, q. v.); अति<BR>देवान् कृष्णः Sk.; मानुषानतिगंधर्वान्<BR>सर्वान्गंधर्व लक्षये Mb; ˚मानुषं कर्म a deed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">Page0029-c+ 59</a>]<BR>which is beyond human power, i. e.<BR>a superhuman action; ˚कशः past<BR>the whip (as a horse),<BR>unmanageable; ˚त्यद् surpassing that; ˚त्वां,<BR>˚त्वान् him or them that surpasses<BR>or surpass thee, so ˚मां, ˚यूयं &c. (b)<BR>(With nouns derived from roots)<BR>Extravagant, exaggerated, inordinate,<BR>excessive, extraordinary; e. g.<BR>˚आदरः excessive regard; ˚आशा<BR>extravagant hope; so ˚भयं, ˚तृष्णा,<BR>˚आनंदः &c. &c.; अतिदानात् बलिर्बद्धो नष्टो<BR>मानात्सुयोधनः । विनष्टो रावणो लौल्यादति<BR>सर्वत्र वर्जयेत्; cf. ‘extremes are ever<BR>bad.’ (c) Unfit, idle, improper, in the<BR>sense of असंप्रति or क्षेप ‘censure’;<BR>अतिनिद्रं = निद्रा संप्रति न युज्यते Sk. The<BR>गणरत्नमहोदधि gives the following<BR>senses of अतिः -<BR>विक्रमातिक्रमाबुद्धिभृशार्थातिशयेष्वति । e. g. अतिरथः रथाधिकं<BR>विक्रमवान्; ˚मतिः बुद्ध्यतिक्रमः; ˚गहनं<BR>बुद्धेरविषयः; ˚तप्तं भृशतप्तं; ˚वेगः अतिशयितो वेगः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकथा
अतिकथा<BR>1 An exaggerated tale.<BR>--2 Idle or meaningless talk.<BR>--थ<BR>a.<BR>1 Exaggerated, incredible (<BR>अश्रद्धेय).<BR>--2 Unfit to be told.<BR>--3 Past<BR>narration or mention, dead, lost.<BR>--4<BR>Swerving from one's caste<BR>traditions &c; lawless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकंदकः|अतिकन्दक|अतिकन्दकः
अतिकंदकः [अतिरिक्तः कंदो यस्य]<BR>N. of a tree हस्तिकंद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकर्षणं|अतिकर्षण
अतिकर्षणं a. Afflicting very much,<BR>excessive exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकाय|अतिकायः
अतिकाय a. [अत्युत्कटः कायो यस्य.]<BR>Of an extraordinary size, gigantic.<BR>--यः N. of a Rākṣasa, son of Rāvaṇa<BR>who was killed by Lakṣmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृच्छ्र|अतिकृच्छ्रः
अतिकृच्छ्र [प्रादि˚ स.] a. Very<BR>difficult.<BR>--च्छ्रं-च्छ्रः [अतिक्रांतं कृच्छ्रं प्राजापत्यं]<BR>Extraordinary hardship, a kind of<BR>severe penance to be finished in 12<BR>nights Ms. 11. 213-4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृतं|अतिकृत
अतिकृतं Overdone, done too<BR>much, excess; सर्वत्रातिकृतं लोके<BR>व्यसनायोपकल्पते Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकृतिः|अतिकृति
अतिकृतिः f.<BR>1 Overdoing.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a metre of 4 lines, each line<BR>containing 25 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिकेशरः|अतिकेशर
अतिकेशरः [अतिरिक्तानि केशराणि<BR>यस्य] N. of an aquatic plant कुब्जक<BR>Trapa Bīpinosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रम्
अतिक्रम् {c1c} U., {c4c} P.<BR>1 (a) To step<BR>or pass beyond, get across, go over,<BR>cross; यत्कथयितुं प्रवृत्तस्तत्परित्यज्य<BR>अतिदूरमतिक्रांतोस्मि K. 346 led far<BR>away from my story, rambled, made<BR>a great digression; सप्त<BR>कक्षांतराण्यतिक्रम्य 92; निमिषमात्रेणातिदूरमतिक्रामति<BR>120; समीपेप्यतिक्रामंती M. 1 going so<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-a" target="_blank">Page0030-a+ 60</a>]<BR>near; अतिक्रम्य तांस्तान्विशेषान्<BR>Me. 57. (b) To pass over, pass by, walk<BR>past, go beyond;<BR>सेनानिवेशदेशमतिक्रम्य Dk. 4, 10;<BR>कथमतिक्रांतमगस्त्याश्रमपदं Mv. 7 is it passed or left<BR>behind; तस्मिन्नतिक्रामति Ś. 7. 31 इदं<BR>कदलीगृहमतिक्रम्य दृश्यते Ratn. 3<BR>beyond the plantain-bower;<BR>तच्चातिक्रम्य कैलासगिरिः K. 121;<BR>जंबुद्वीपमतिक्रम्य शिशिरो नाम पर्वतः Rām.;<BR>अतिक्रामत्ययं K. 85 is going or departing.<BR>--2 To excel, surpass; exceed (in<BR>number, strength &c.);<BR>इरावतीमतिक्रामंती भव M. 4; अतिक्रामंतीमिवेरावतीं<BR>प्रेक्षे M. 1; वृद्धिर्नातिक्रामति पंचतां<BR>Ms. 8. 151; कर्णीसुतमप्यतिक्रांतः Dk. 74;<BR>कलासु रूपे चाप्सरसोप्यतिक्रांता 78<BR>surpassing, superior to; शक्तिमनतिक्रम्य =<BR>यथाशक्ति Sk.<BR>--3 To transgress,<BR>violate, go beyond, overstep;<BR>जनकाग्रजन्मनोः शासनमतिक्रम्य Dk. 2; नालं<BR>पुरुषो नियतिलिखितां लेखामतिक्रमितुं 61;<BR>एवमतिक्रातमर्यादे त्वयि Ve. 1,<BR>Ms. 9. 78; अये वात्सल्यादतिक्रामति प्रसंगः<BR>Māl. 6 Oh, the event through<BR>excessive affection transgresses all due<BR>limits; अतिक्रम्य सदाचारं K. 160, 181.<BR>--4 To exclude, pass by, neglect,<BR>set aside, leave; किंवा परिजनमतिक्रम्य<BR>भवान् संदिष्टः M. 4; प्रथितयशसां<BR>प्रबंधानतिक्रम्य M. 1 to the exclusion of.<BR>--5 To go or pass away, elapse, roll<BR>on (as time); सा निशा अतिचक्राम<BR>Pt. 1; यथा यथा यौवनमतिचक्राम K. 59;<BR>शैशवं 74; भवतामप्यतिक्रामति<BR>देवार्चनविधिवेला 47 is passing away (is<BR>being violated).; अतिक्रांते दशाहे<BR>Ms. 5. 76; also trans. allow to pass;<BR>द्वित्राणि दिनान्यतिक्रम्य Dk. 100;<BR>अत्यक्राममिमान्मासांस्तद्वधं परिचिंतयन् Rām.;<BR>नाहारवेलातिक्रमणीया K. 266.<BR>--6 To<BR>overcome, overpower, seize;<BR>व्यालद्विप इवास्माभिरतिक्रम्यैव दम्यसे Mv. 3. 31<BR>by seizing or falling upon, by main<BR>force; केनापि सत्त्वेन अतिक्रम्य<BR>Ś. 6.<BR>--7 To lose; स हि<BR>स्वाम्यादतिक्रामेत् ऋतूनां प्रतिरोधनात् Ms. 9. 93<BR>--Caus. To let pass, allow to go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमः|अतिक्रम
अतिक्रमः<BR>1 Act of overstepping,<BR>going beyond &c.<BR>--2 (a) Breach<BR>of decorum or duty; अहो अतिक्रमः<BR>Māl. 7. (b) Transgression, violation;<BR>उपचार˚ M. 4, 5. (c) Trespass;<BR>disrespect, injury, opposition; ब्राह्मण˚ त्यागो<BR>भवतामेव भूतये Mv. 2. 10 refraining<BR>from all trespass against Brāhmaṇas;<BR>दिशत्यपायं हि सतामतिक्रमः Ki. 14. 9;<BR>कुलान्यकुलतां यांति ब्राह्मणातिक्रमेण च<BR>Ms. 3. 63; एतस्मिन्नतिक्रमे परवतीयं M. 3;<BR>गुरुजनातिक्रमात् K. 160; शशिनो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-b" target="_blank">Page0030-b+ 59</a>]<BR>ज्येष्ठातिक्रमः 56 transgression (passing<BR>through); मर्षणीयोयमारोहणातिक्रमः 81;<BR>वात्सल्यादतिक्रमोपि Mv. 1 violation<BR>(of due limits or propriety);<BR>Mv. 4. 25.<BR>--3 Lapse, passing away (of<BR>time); अनेकसंवत्सरातिक्रमेपि U. 4; वेला˚<BR>मं कृत्वा आगतः Pt. 1; उचितवेलातिक्रमे<BR>M. 2; संध्या˚ Rām.<BR>--4 Overcoming,<BR>conquering, surpassing; mostly with<BR>दुर्; स्वजातिर्दुरतिक्रमा, स्वभावो<BR>दुरतिक्रमः &c.<BR>--5 Neglect, omission,<BR>disregard; Ms. 11. 120.<BR>--6 A<BR>vigorous attack, determined onset<BR>(= अभिक्रम q. v.).<BR>--7 Excess.<BR>--8<BR>Abuse, misapplication.<BR>--9<BR>Imposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रांत|अतिक्रान्त|अतिक्रान्तः
अतिक्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Exceeded,<BR>surpassed, gone beyond &c.; सोतिक्रांतः<BR>श्रवणविषयं Me. 103; सुदूरमतिक्रांतः<BR>K. 35 departed, gone; मनोरथ ˚दर्शना<BR>Māl. 10 beyond the reach even of<BR>desire; विचारातिक्रांतः Mu. 5. 4 past<BR>the stage of thought;<BR>चक्षुर्विषयातिक्रांतेषु पक्षिषु H. 1.<BR>--2 Past, gone by;<BR>˚कुनृपति K. 5, past, former; 169.<BR>Pt. 1. 333, Pt. 2, Bh. 3. 32;<BR>˚पार्थिवगुणान् Mu. 1 former kings.<BR>--तं A<BR>past thing, a thing of the past, the<BR>past; ˚तं भगवती कथयति M. 5 your<BR>ladyship is speaking of the past;<BR>˚ते धैर्यमवलंब्यताम् U. 3; किं ˚उपालंभेन<BR>H. 1; cf. ‘let bygones be bygones.’<BR>˚योगिन् a. with the moon in<BR>conjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमणं|अतिक्रमण
अतिक्रमणं Overstepping, spending<BR>of time, excess; fault, offence;<BR>तेनातिक्रमणेन दुःखयति नः Mv. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रमणीय
अतिक्रमणीय pot. p. To be<BR>transgressed or violated, to be<BR>disregarded, passed by, neglected or<BR>avoided; ˚यं मे सुहृद्वाक्यं Ś. 2, 3, 6, 7;<BR>अनतिक्रमणीयस्य जन्ममृत्योरिवागमं H. 4. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रुद्ध|अतिक्रुद्धः
अतिक्रुद्ध a. Very angry.<BR>--द्धः<BR>[प्रा. स.] N. of a Mantra mentioned<BR>in Tantras; (अष्टाविंशत्यक्षरो य<BR>एकत्रिंशदथापि वा ॥ अतिक्रुद्धः स विज्ञेयो निंदितः सर्वकर्मसु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्रूर|अतिक्रूरः
अतिक्रूर a. Very cruel.<BR>--रः [प्रा.<BR>स.]<BR>1 A malignant planet such as<BR>Saturn, Mars &c. (क्रूरा वक्रा अतिक्रूराः).<BR>--2 N. of a Mantra in Tantras (<BR>त्रिंशदक्षरको मंत्रस्त्रयस्त्रिंशदथापि वा । अतिक्रूरः स<BR>विज्ञेयो निंदितः सर्वकर्मसु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिक्षिप्त
अतिक्षिप्त a. [क्षिप्-क्त] Thrown<BR>beyond.<BR>--क्तं A kind of sprain or<BR>dislocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिखट्व
अतिखट्व a. Without a bedstead,<BR>able to dispense with a bedstead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगम्
अतिगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To pass, elapse,<BR>pass away (as time); दशाहेऽतिगते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">Page0030-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 To overcome, exceed, excel,<BR>See अतिग.<BR>--3 To pass over, pass by,<BR>neglect.<BR>--4 To pass away, die.<BR>--5 To<BR>escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग
अतिग a. [गम्-ड] (in comp.)<BR>Exceeding, going beyond, transcending,<BR>excelling, surpassing; सर्वलोक˚<BR>Mu. 1. 2; किमौषधपथातिगैरुपहतो<BR>महाव्याधिभिः Mu. 6 by diseases defying the<BR>powers of medicine, past the stage<BR>of physicking; बाणैर्देहातिगैः R. 12. 48<BR>piercing through their bodies; वयो˚<BR>Ms. 7. 149 advanced in years, aged;<BR>संख्यातिगाः संपदः Bh. 3. 132; वपुः<BR>प्रकर्षेण जनातिगेन Ki. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगंडः|अतिगण्ड|अतिगण्डः
अतिगंडः<BR>1 N. of a star of the<BR>6th lunar asterism.<BR>--2 A large cheek<BR>or temple.<BR>--3 One who has large<BR>cheeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगंध|अतिगन्ध|अतिगन्धः
अतिगंध a. Having an excessive or<BR>overpowering smell.<BR>--धः<BR>1 Sulphur.<BR>--2 N. of various plants: चंपक,<BR>भूततृण lemon-grass & मुद्गर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगंधालु|अतिगन्धालु|अतिगन्धालुः
अतिगंधालु N. of the plant पुत्रदात्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगव
अतिगव a. [अतिक्रांतो गां]<BR>1 Very<BR>foolish, quite stupid.<BR>--2<BR>Inexpressible, indescribable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगहन
अतिगहन, --गव्हर a. Very deep,<BR>impenetrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगव्हर
अतिगहन, --गव्हर a. Very deep,<BR>impenetrable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुण|अतिगुणः
अतिगुण a.<BR>1 Having excellent or<BR>superior qualities.<BR>--2 Devoid of<BR>merits, worthless [गुणमतिक्रांतः].<BR>--णः<BR>Excellent merits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुरु|अतिगुरुः
अतिगुरु a. Very heavy (such as<BR>mercury &c.).<BR>--रुः A very respectable<BR>person, such as a father, mother &c.<BR>(त्रयः पुरुषस्य अतिगुरवो भवंति पिता माता<BR>आचार्यश्च).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिगुहा
अतिगुहा [अतिक्रांता गुहां<BR>मध्यावकाशेन] N. of the plant पृश्निपर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्रह्
अतिग्रह् {c9c} P. To take beyond<BR>the usual measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्रह|अतिग्रहः
अतिग्रह a. [अतिक्रांतो ग्रहं] Difficult<BR>to be comprehended,<BR>incomprehensible.<BR>--हः, --ग्राहः<BR>1 Object of an<BR>apprehensive organ, such as स्पर्श ‘touch’<BR>the object of त्वच्, रस of जिह्वा &c. The<BR>Grahas are eight in number; प्राण,<BR>वाच्, जिह्वा, चक्षुस्, श्रोत्र, मनस्, हस्तौ & त्वच्;<BR>the corresponding atigrāhas being<BR>अपान, नामन्, रस, रूप, शब्द, काम, कर्मन्<BR>& स्पर्श.<BR>--2 Right knowledge, correct<BR>apprehension.<BR>--3 Act of overtaking,<BR>surpassing &c.<BR>--4 One who seizes or<BR>takes to a very great extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिग्राह्य|अतिग्राह्यः
अतिग्राह्य a. To be held in check,<BR>to be controlled.<BR>--ह्यः N. of three<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">Page0031-a+ 58</a>]<BR>libations made at the Jyotiṣṭoma<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिघ
अतिघ [अतिशयेन हंति; हन्]<BR>1 A<BR>weapon.<BR>--2 Wrath^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20240824. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/ap90/issues/issue26 readme_althw_2.txt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिघ्न
अतिघ्न a. Very destructive.<BR>--घ्नी<BR>[अतिशयेन हंति दुःखं; हन्-ठक्] A<BR>happy state of complete oblivion<BR>which drowns all thought of<BR>whatever is disagreeable in the past;<BR>अतिघ्नीमानंदस्य गत्वा Bṛ. Ār. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचमू
अतिचमू a. [चमूमतिक्रांतः]<BR>Victorious over armies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचर्
अतिचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To transgress,<BR>violate; be unfaithful to, offend (as<BR>a wife &c.); स्वं स्वमाचारमत्यचारिषुः<BR>Dk. 162; यथा चाहं नातिचरे पतीन्;<BR>पुत्राः पितॄनत्यचरन्नार्यश्चात्यचरन् पतीन्<BR>Mb.<BR>--2 To pass by, neglect, omit.<BR>--3<BR>To overtake, overcome; surpass,<BR>excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचर
अतिचर a. Very changeable,<BR>transient.<BR>--रा [अतिक्रम्य स्वस्थानं सरोंतरं<BR>गच्छति] N. of the shrub Hibiscus<BR>Mutabilis (पद्मिनी, स्थलपद्मिनी or<BR>पद्मचारिणीलता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचरणं|अतिचरण
अतिचरणं Excessive practice,<BR>overdoing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचारः|अतिचार
अतिचारः<BR>1 Transgression.<BR>--2<BR>Excelling,<BR>--3 Overtaking &c.<BR>--4 Accelerated<BR>motion of planets (कुजादिपंचग्रहाणां<BR>स्वस्वाक्रांतराशिषु भोगकालमुल्लंघ्य<BR>राश्यंतरगमनं); passage from one zodiacal sign to<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचारिन्
अतिचारिन् a. Transgressing,<BR>surpassing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिचिरं|अतिचिर
अतिचिरं adv. Very long; ˚रं मया<BR>कृतं Ratn. 1 I have been very late;<BR>नातिचिरं गतायां च तस्यां K. 178 she<BR>had not long left when &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्रः|अतिच्छत्र|अतिछत्र
अतिच्छत्रः --त्रा,--च्छत्रका [अतिक्रांतः<BR>छत्रं तुल्याकारेण] A mushroom, anise,<BR>principally Anesum or Anethum<BR>Sowa; N. of another plant, Barleria<BR>Longifolia. (˚त्रः is said by Amara<BR>to be जलतृणभेदः Mar. शेतगवत; and ˚त्रा =<BR>शतपुष्पा Mar. शोप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्रा|अतिछत्रा
अतिच्छत्रः --त्रा,--च्छत्रका [अतिक्रांतः<BR>छत्रं तुल्याकारेण] A mushroom, anise,<BR>principally Anesum or Anethum<BR>Sowa; N. of another plant, Barleria<BR>Longifolia. (˚त्रः is said by Amara<BR>to be जलतृणभेदः Mar. शेतगवत; and ˚त्रा =<BR>शतपुष्पा Mar. शोप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छत्रका
अतिच्छत्रः --त्रा,--च्छत्रका [अतिक्रांतः<BR>छत्रं तुल्याकारेण] A mushroom, anise,<BR>principally Anesum or Anethum<BR>Sowa; N. of another plant, Barleria<BR>Longifolia. (˚त्रः is said by Amara<BR>to be जलतृणभेदः Mar. शेतगवत; and ˚त्रा =<BR>शतपुष्पा Mar. शोप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छंदः|अतिच्छन्द|अतिच्छन्दः
अतिच्छंदः --दस् a. [<BR>अतिक्रांतःछंदःदं वा]<BR>1 Free from worldly desires.<BR>--2 Exceeding thought or will.<BR>--3<BR>One who violates Vedic traditions of<BR>conduct.<BR>--स् f. n.<BR>1 N. of two classes<BR>of metres (अतिक्रांता छंदः<BR>वृत्तानुसारिवर्णविन्यासभेदं)<BR>--2 Fondness, inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिच्छंदस्|अतिच्छन्दस्
अतिच्छंदः --दस् a. [<BR>अतिक्रांतःछंदःदं वा]<BR>1 Free from worldly desires.<BR>--2 Exceeding thought or will.<BR>--3<BR>One who violates Vedic traditions of<BR>conduct.<BR>--स् f. n.<BR>1 N. of two classes<BR>of metres (अतिक्रांता छंदः<BR>वृत्तानुसारिवर्णविन्यासभेदं)<BR>--2 Fondness, inclination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजगती
अतिजगती [अतिक्रांता जगतीं<BR>द्वादशाक्षरपादां एकाक्षराधिक्यात्] N. of a class<BR>of metres belonging to the<BR>अतिच्छंदस् class, with 13 letters in each<BR>line (प्रथमाऽतिजगत्यासां सा द्विपंचाशदक्षरा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजन
अतिजन a. [अतिक्रांतो जनं] Not<BR>tenanted or inhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजागर|अतिजागरः
अतिजागर a. Always wakeful.<BR>--रः The black Curlew (नीलवक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजात
अतिजात a. [अतिक्रांतो जातं-जातिं<BR>जनकं वा] (opp. अपजात) Superior to<BR>his parentage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजीव्
अतिजीव् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To survive,<BR>outlive.<BR>--2 To surpass (in the mode<BR>of living); अत्यजीवदमरालकेश्वरौ<BR>R. 19. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिजीवनं
अतिजीवनं Surviving &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिडीनं|अतिडीन
अतिडीनं Extraordinary flight<BR>(of birds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितरां
अतितरां, --अतितमां ind. [अति-तर<BR>(म) प्-आमु]<BR>1 more, higher (abl.);<BR>नृत्तादस्याः स्थितमतितरां कांतं M. 2. 7.<BR>--2 Exceedingly, very much;<BR>excessive, great; ˚सुदुःसहः R. 3. 37;<BR>˚रांकांतिमापत्स्यते Me. 15 will attain great<BR>splendour.<BR>--3 Above, higher in rank<BR>(acc.); तस्माद्वा एते देवा<BR>˚रामिवान्यान्देवान् Ken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितमां
अतितरां, --अतितमां ind. [अति-तर<BR>(म) प्-आमु]<BR>1 more, higher (abl.);<BR>नृत्तादस्याः स्थितमतितरां कांतं M. 2. 7.<BR>--2 Exceedingly, very much;<BR>excessive, great; ˚सुदुःसहः R. 3. 37;<BR>˚रांकांतिमापत्स्यते Me. 15 will attain great<BR>splendour.<BR>--3 Above, higher in rank<BR>(acc.); तस्माद्वा एते देवा<BR>˚रामिवान्यान्देवान् Ken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितीव्र
अतितीव्र --तीक्ष्ण a. Very sharp,<BR>pungent.<BR>--क्ष्णः N. of the plant<BR>शोभांजन.<BR>--व्रा dūb grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितीक्ष्ण|अतितीक्ष्णः
अतितीव्र --तीक्ष्ण a. Very sharp,<BR>pungent.<BR>--क्ष्णः N. of the plant<BR>शोभांजन.<BR>--व्रा dūb grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितृष्णा
अतितृष्णा Rapacity, excessive<BR>greed or desire; ˚ष्णा न कर्तव्या Pt. 5<BR>one should not be too greedy.<BR>--ष्ण<BR>a. Rapacious, very greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितॄ
अतितॄ {c1c} P. To cross, pass or get<BR>over, surmount, overcome;<BR>दुर्गाण्यतितरतिं ते H. 4. v. l.; तयोरात्मनश्च<BR>क्षुधमत्यतार्षं Dk. 165 satisfied or appeased<BR>hunger; तेपि चातितरंत्येव मृत्युं<BR>श्रुतिपरायणाः Bg. 13. 25 cross beyond<BR>death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितरणं|अतितरण
अतितरणं Crossing, surmounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतितारिन्
अतितारिन् a. Crossing, overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिः|अतिथि
अतिथिः [अतति गच्छति न तिष्ठति;<BR>अत्-इथिन् Uṇ. 4. 2; lit. a ‘traveller’;<BR>according to Manu एकरात्रं तु<BR>निवसन्नतिथिर्व्राह्मणः स्मृतः । अनित्यं हि स्थितो<BR>यस्मात्तस्मादतिथिरुच्यते 3. 112]<BR>1 A guest<BR>(fig. also); अतिथिनेव निवेदितं Ś. 4;<BR>कुसुमलताप्रियातिथे Ś. 6 dear or<BR>welcome guest; पुरंदरपुरातिथिषु पितृषु<BR>Dk. 2 the guests of Indra's capital<BR>i. e. dead; so समरे यमनगरातिथिरकारि<BR>12; धन्यानां श्रवणपथातिथित्वमेति<BR>(उक्तं) Ratn. 2. 7 becomes a guest of,<BR>i. e. goes to or falls on the ears of<BR>the fortunate only; करोति ते मुखं<BR>तन्वि चपेटापातनातिथिं K. P.<BR>--2<BR>Wrath.<BR>--3 N. of a son of Kuśa and<BR>Kumudavatī and grandson. of<BR>Rāma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्रिया --पूजा, --सत्कारः<BR>--सत्क्रिया, --सेवा hospitable reception of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">Page0031-c+ 59</a>]<BR>guests, rite of hospitality, hospitality,<BR>attention to the guests.<BR>--देव a. [<BR>अतिथिर्देव इव पूज्यो यस्य] treating the<BR>guest as a God.<BR>--धर्मः title or<BR>claim to hospitality; hospitality due<BR>to guests; गृह्यतां ˚र्मः Pt. 1; यदि<BR>त्वतिथिधर्मेण क्षत्रियो गृहमाव्रजेत् Ms. 3. 111<BR>should come as a guest.<BR>--धर्मिन् a.<BR>entitled to hospitality as a guest<BR>Ms. 3. 112.<BR>--पतिः the host or<BR>entertainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिन्
अतिथिन् a. Ved. Travelling,<BR>wandering. --m. (थी) N. of a King, also<BR>called सुहोत्र and अतिथि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिथिग्वः|अतिथिग्व
अतिथिग्वः An epithet of<BR>Divodāsa whom the gods helped in<BR>overcoming Śambara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदग्ध
अतिदग्ध a. Badly or<BR>excessively burnt.<BR>--ग्धं A bad kind of burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदानं|अतिदान
अतिदानं Munificence, liberality;<BR>अतिदाने बलिर्बद्धः Chāṇ. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदाहः|अतिदाह
अतिदाहः Violent inflammation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदिश्
अतिदिश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To assign, to<BR>make over, transfer.<BR>--2 To extend the<BR>application of, extend by analogy;<BR>प्रधानमल्लनिबर्हणन्यायेन अतिदिशति SB.;<BR>जनपदतदवध्योश्चेति प्रकरणे ये प्रत्यया<BR>उक्तास्तेऽत्रातिदिश्यंते P. IV. 3. 100<BR>Sk., IV. 1. 151 Mbh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदेशः|अतिदेश
अतिदेशः<BR>1 Transfer, making over,<BR>assigning.<BR>--2 (Gram.)<BR>Extended application, application by<BR>analogy, transference of one<BR>attribute to another, attraction of one<BR>case or rule to another; अतिदेशो नाम<BR>इतरधर्मस्य इतरस्मिन् प्रयोगाय आदेशः (<BR>मीमांसा); or अन्यत्रैव प्रणीतायाः कृत्स्नाया<BR>धर्मसंहतेः । अन्यत्र कार्यतः प्राप्तिरतिदेशः स उच्यते॥<BR>प्राकृतात् कर्मणो यस्मात्तत्समानेषु कर्मसु ।<BR>धर्मप्रवेशो येन स्यादतिदेशः स उच्यते ॥ This<BR>अतिदेश is of 5 kinds: शास्त्र˚, कार्य˚,<BR>निमित्त˚, व्यपदेश˚ & रूप˚. Thus in Grammar<BR>प्रकृतिवत् विकृतिः, कर्मणा कर्मवत्तुल्यक्रियः or<BR>पुंवत्, णिद्वत्, व्यपदेशीवद्भावः & इण्वदिकः are<BR>instances. गोसदृशो गवयः is an instance<BR>of रूपातिदेश or analogy;<BR>वाक्यार्थस्यातिदेशस्य स्मृतिर्व्यापार उच्यते<BR>Bhāṣā P. 80. अतिदेश is generally expressed by<BR>words showing likeness or<BR>resemblance, such as इव, वत्, सदृश &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदीप्यः|अतिदीप्य
अतिदीप्यः [अतिशयेन दीप्यते] A<BR>plant, Plumbago Rosea (रक्तचित्रक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदूर
अतिदूर a. Very far; ˚रे, ˚रात्, ˚रेण<BR>usually with न (gen.) not far from;<BR>तपोवनस्य˚ Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिदेवः|अतिदेव
अतिदेवः The Supreme or highest<BR>God; N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिद्वय
अतिद्वय a. [द्वयमतिक्रांतः; नास्ति<BR>द्बयं यस्य वा] Surpassing the two (<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">Page0032-a+ 59</a>]<BR>बृहत्कथा and वासवदत्ता), or having no<BR>second or equal, incomparable,<BR>matchless; धिया निबद्धेयमतिद्वयी कथा<BR>K. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिधन्वन्
अतिधन्वन् m. [अत्युत्कृष्टं धनुर्यस्य]<BR>1 An unrivalled archer or warrior.<BR>--2 That which surpasses a मरु or<BR>desert [धन्वानं अतिक्रांतः].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिधृतिः|अतिधृति
अतिधृतिः f. [अतिक्रांता धृतिं<BR>अष्टादशाक्षरपादां वृत्तिं एकाक्षराधिक्यात्]<BR>1 N. of a<BR>class of metres belonging to the<BR>अतिच्छंदस् group, consisting of 4 lines<BR>with 19 syllables in each (<BR>षट्सप्ततिस्त्वतिधृतिः).<BR>--2 Nineteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनाष्ट्र
अतिनाष्ट्र a. Ved. Out of danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनिचृत्
अतिनिचृ(वृ)त् f. N. of a Vedic<BR>metre of 3 Pādas, the number of<BR>syllables in each being respectively<BR>7, 6 and 7; (षट्कः सप्तकयोर्मध्ये<BR>स्तोतॄणांविवाचीति । यस्याः सातिनिवृन्नाम गायत्री<BR>द्विदशाक्षरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनिवृत्
अतिनिचृ(वृ)त् f. N. of a Vedic<BR>metre of 3 Pādas, the number of<BR>syllables in each being respectively<BR>7, 6 and 7; (षट्कः सप्तकयोर्मध्ये<BR>स्तोतॄणांविवाचीति । यस्याः सातिनिवृन्नाम गायत्री<BR>द्विदशाक्षरा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनिद्रा
अतिनिद्रा Excessive sleeping.<BR>--द्र a.<BR>1 Given to excessive sleep.<BR>--2<BR>Without sleep, sleepless.<BR>--द्रं ind.<BR>Past sleeping time (निद्रा संप्रति न<BR>युज्यते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनिर्हारिन्
अतिनिर्हारिन् a. Very attractive<BR>(as an attributive of smell);<BR>आमोदःसोऽतिनिर्हारी Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनौ
अतिनौ --नु a. [अतिक्रांतो नावं]<BR>Disembarked, landed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिनु
अतिनौ --नु a. [अतिक्रांतो नावं]<BR>Disembarked, landed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपंचा|अतिपञ्चा
अतिपंचा [पंचवर्षमतिक्रांता] A girl<BR>past five.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपत्
अतिपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To pass over;<BR>neglect, omit, transgress.<BR>--2 To fly by,<BR>beyond, or over; to cross --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>delay, neglect; see अतिपात्य below.<BR>--2<BR>To disrespect, offend; ये सत्यमेव हि<BR>गुरूनतिपातयंति Mu. 3. 34 transgress,<BR>violate; अतिपातितकालसाधना Ki. 2. 42.<BR>--3 To cause to fly past or by.<BR>--4 To<BR>make ineffectual; संशमनमेवं<BR>संशोधनमतिपातयति Suśr.<BR>--5 To snatch<BR>away, drag away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपतनं|अतिपतन
अतिपतनं Flying past or beyond;<BR>omission, neglect, missing,<BR>transgressing; exceeding, going beyond<BR>due bounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातः|अतिपात
अतिपातः<BR>1 Passing away, lapse (of<BR>time); अहो काल˚ तः Māl. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Neglect, omission; transgression; न<BR>चेदन्यकार्यातिपातः Ś. 1 if no other duty<BR>be neglected thereby, if it should<BR>not interfere with (the discharge<BR>of) any other duty; deviation from<BR>established laws or customs.<BR>--3<BR>Befalling, occurrence;<BR>दुःखातिपातेन कलुषीकियंते K. 289;<BR>जलधारातिपातः 302 falling.<BR>--4 Ill-treatment, or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">Page0032-b+ 59</a>]<BR>usage.<BR>--5 Opposition, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातित
अतिपातित p. p.<BR>1 Put off, delayed<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Quite or entirely broken;<BR>अस्थिनिःशेषतश्छिन्नमतिपातितम् Suśr.<BR>--तं<BR>Complete fracture of a bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातिन्
अतिपातिन् a.<BR>1 Acute, running a<BR>rapid course.<BR>--2 Surpassing in<BR>speed, swifter than (in comp.);<BR>ततार विद्याः पवनातिपातिभिर्दिशो<BR>हरिद्भिर्हरितामिवेश्वरः R. 3. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपात्य
अतिपात्य pot. p. To be delayed or<BR>put off; काममनतिपात्यं धर्मकार्यं देवस्य Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपत्रः|अतिपत्र
अतिपत्रः [अतिरिक्तं बृहत् पत्रं यस्य]<BR>The teak tree, or the हस्तिकंदवृक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपथिन्
अतिपथिन् m. A better road<BR>than common, a good road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपद्
अतिपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To go beyond;<BR>spring over.<BR>--2 To neglect, omit,<BR>transgress. --Caus. To allow to pass<BR>by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपद
अतिपद a. [अतिक्रांतः पदं]<BR>1 Having<BR>no feet.<BR>--2 Too long by one foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपत्तिः|अतिपत्ति
अतिपत्तिः f.<BR>1 Going beyond,<BR>passing, lapse; देशकालातिपत्तौ च गृहीत्वा<BR>स्वयमर्पयेत् Y. 2. 169.<BR>--2<BR>Non-performance, failure; लिङ्निमित्ते ऌङ्<BR>क्रियातिपत्तौ P. III. 3. 139 (the<BR>conditional is used instead of the<BR>potential, when the<BR>non-performance of an action is implied).<BR>--3<BR>[पत्तिं अतिक्रांतः] One surpassing a<BR>footsoldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपन्न
अतिपन्न p. p. Gone beyond,<BR>transgressed, missed, past &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपरिचयः|अतिपरिचय
अतिपरिचयः Excessive<BR>familiarity or intimacy; Prov.<BR>अतिपरिचयादवज्ञा ‘Familiarity breeds contempt.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपर|अतिपरः
अतिपर a. One who has<BR>vanquished his enemies.<BR>--रः A great or<BR>superior enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपरोक्ष
अतिपरोक्ष a.<BR>1 Far out of sight,<BR>not discernible; ˚वृत्ति obsolete<BR>(words).<BR>--2 Not hidden, visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपातकं|अतिपातक
अतिपातकं A very heinous sin,<BR>incest, (मातृगमनं दुहितृगमनं स्नुषागमनं,<BR>पुंसां; पुत्रपितृश्वशुरगमनं च स्त्रीणां,<BR>अतिपातकानि उच्यंते.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपादनिचृत्
अतिपादनिचृ(वृ)त् f. N. of a<BR>Vedic Metre of 3 pādas, the<BR>number of syllabes in each being<BR>respectively 6, 8 and 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिपादनिवृत्
अतिपादनिचृ(वृ)त् f. N. of a<BR>Vedic Metre of 3 pādas, the<BR>number of syllabes in each being<BR>respectively 6, 8 and 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रबंधः|अतिप्रबन्ध|अतिप्रबन्धः
अतिप्रबंधः Great continuity;<BR>˚प्रहितास्त्रवृष्टिभिः R. 3. 58 very<BR>rapidly or in rapid succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रगे
अतिप्रगे ind. Very early in the<BR>morning, in the early dawn<BR>Ms. 4. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रवृद्ध
अतिप्रवृद्ध a.<BR>1 Overbearing<BR>Ms. 9. 320.<BR>--2 Grown very much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रश्नः|अतिप्रश्न
अतिप्रश्नः [अतिक्रम्य मर्यादां प्रश्नः]<BR>A question about transcendental<BR>truths; a vexatious or extravagant<BR>question that is asked though a<BR>satisfactory reply has already been given;<BR>e. g. Bālāki's question to Yājñavalkya<BR>about Brahma in बृहदारण्यकोपनिषद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रसंगः|अतिप्रसङ्ग|अतिप्रसंग|अतिप्रसङ्गः
अतिप्रसंगः, --प्रसक्तिः f.<BR>1 Excessive<BR>attachment; नातिप्रसंगः प्रमदासुकार्यः<BR>Pt. 1. 187; स्त्रीष्वतिप्रसंगात् Dk. 101.<BR>--2<BR>Over-rudeness, impertinence;<BR>तद्विरमातिप्रसंगात् U. 5; मा भूत्पुनर्बत<BR>कथंचिदतिप्रसंगः Mv. 3. 16 indiscretion or<BR>imprudence; यदेतावतः<BR>परिभवातिप्रसंगस्य तुल्यं स्यात् Mv. 5 an insult.<BR>--3<BR>Extraordinary or unwarrantable<BR>stretch of a (grammatical) rule, or<BR>principle; also = अतिव्याप्ति q. v.<BR>--4<BR>A very close contact;<BR>अतिप्रसंगाद्विहितागसो मुहुः Ki. 8. 33 (अविच्छेदसंग).<BR>--5 Prolixity; अलमतिप्रसंगेन Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रसक्तिः|अतिप्रसक्ति
अतिप्रसंगः, --प्रसक्तिः f.<BR>1 Excessive<BR>attachment; नातिप्रसंगः प्रमदासुकार्यः<BR>Pt. 1. 187; स्त्रीष्वतिप्रसंगात् Dk. 101.<BR>--2<BR>Over-rudeness, impertinence;<BR>तद्विरमातिप्रसंगात् U. 5; मा भूत्पुनर्बत<BR>कथंचिदतिप्रसंगः Mv. 3. 16 indiscretion or<BR>imprudence; यदेतावतः<BR>परिभवातिप्रसंगस्य तुल्यं स्यात् Mv. 5 an insult.<BR>--3<BR>Extraordinary or unwarrantable<BR>stretch of a (grammatical) rule, or<BR>principle; also = अतिव्याप्ति q. v.<BR>--4<BR>A very close contact;<BR>अतिप्रसंगाद्विहितागसो मुहुः Ki. 8. 33 (अविच्छेदसंग).<BR>--5 Prolixity; अलमतिप्रसंगेन Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रेषितं|अतिप्रेषित
अतिप्रेषितं The time after the<BR>ceremony in which the प्रैष Mantras<BR>are used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिप्रौढा
अतिप्रौढा^1 A girl who has<BR>attained a marriageable age, a<BR>grown-up girl.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिबल|अतिबलः
अतिबल a. Very strong or<BR>powerful; जयत्यतिबलो रामो लक्ष्मणश्च महाबलः<BR>Rām.<BR>--लः An eminent or<BR>matchless warrior (अतिरथ).<BR>--लं<BR>1 Great<BR>strength or power.<BR>--2 A<BR>powerful army.<BR>--ला<BR>1 N. of a medicinal<BR>plant, Sidonia Cordifolia and<BR>Rhombifolia.<BR>--2 N. of a powerful charm<BR>or lore taught by Viśvāmitra to<BR>Rāma: --गृहाण द्वे इमे विद्ये बलामतिबलां<BR>तथा । न ते श्रमो जरा वाभ्यां भविता<BR>नांगवैकृतम् ॥ न च सुप्तं प्रमत्तं वा धर्षयिष्यंति नैरृताः ।<BR>न च ते सदृशो राम वीर्येणान्यो भविष्यति ॥<BR>सदेवनरनागेषु लोकेष्विह पुमांस्त्रिषु । न सौभाग्ये<BR>न दाक्षिण्ये न बुद्धिश्रुतिपौरुषे ॥ नोत्तरे<BR>प्रतिपत्तव्ये त्वत्तुल्यो वा भविष्यति । एतद्विद्याद्वयं<BR>प्राप्य यशश्चाव्ययमाप्स्यसि ॥ बलामतिबलां चैव<BR>ज्ञानविज्ञानमातरौ । क्षुत्पिपासे च ते राम नात्यर्थं<BR>पीडयिष्यतः ॥ जयश्च दुर्गकांतारप्रदेशेष्वटवीषु<BR>च । सारतां त्रिषु लोकेषु गमिष्यसि च राघव ॥<BR>पितामहसुते ह्येते विद्ये चायुर्बलावहे । See<BR>R. 11. 9 also.<BR>--3 N. of one of Dakṣa's<BR>daughters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिबालक|अतिबालकः
अतिबालक a. Childish, puerile.<BR>--कः An infant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिबाला
अतिबाला [अतिक्रांता बाल्यावस्थां]<BR>A cow two years old; वर्षमात्रा तु बाला<BR>स्यादतिबाला द्विवार्षिकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिब्रह्मचर्यं|अतिब्रह्मचर्य|अतिब्रह्मचर्यः|अतिब्रह्मचर्य्य
अतिब्रह्मचर्यं Over-continence, or<BR>abstinence (opp. अतिमैथुनं).<BR>--र्यः<BR>[अतिक्रांतो ब्रह्मचर्यं] One who has<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">Page0033-a+ 56</a>]<BR>violated the student's life, who<BR>cohabits with women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभरः|अतिभर
अतिभ(भा)रः<BR>1 Excessive<BR>burden, great load; कोऽतिभारः समर्थानां<BR>Pt. 1. 22; इति मनसि न्यस्तचिंतातिभारः<BR>Ratn. 3. 5; सा मुक्तकंठं व्यसनातिभारात्<BR>चक्रंद R. 14. 68 through<BR>excessive grief; दुःखातिभारोपि लघुः स मेने<BR>Ki. 3. 33.<BR>--2 Speed.<BR>--3 Excessive<BR>obscurity (of a sentence).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग [अतिभारं गृहीत्वापि गच्छति] a mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभारः|अतिभार
अतिभ(भा)रः<BR>1 Excessive<BR>burden, great load; कोऽतिभारः समर्थानां<BR>Pt. 1. 22; इति मनसि न्यस्तचिंतातिभारः<BR>Ratn. 3. 5; सा मुक्तकंठं व्यसनातिभारात्<BR>चक्रंद R. 14. 68 through<BR>excessive grief; दुःखातिभारोपि लघुः स मेने<BR>Ki. 3. 33.<BR>--2 Speed.<BR>--3 Excessive<BR>obscurity (of a sentence).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग [अतिभारं गृहीत्वापि गच्छति] a mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभीः
अतिभीः f. [अति बिभेति अस्याः<BR>दर्शनात्; भी-क्विप्] Lightning; flash of<BR>Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभू
अतिभू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To spring forth,<BR>arise; शब्दश्च घोरोऽतिबभूव Mb.<BR>--2 To<BR>surpass, excel; to overcome, subdue,<BR>overpower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभवः|अतिभव
अतिभवः Surpassing, defeating,<BR>conquering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभू
अतिभू a. Surpassing all, epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभूमिः|अतिभूमि
अतिभूमिः f.<BR>1 Excess, culmination,<BR>highest pitch; ˚मिं गम्-या to go to<BR>excess, to reach the climax; ˚मिं तस्या<BR>अभिनिवेशो गमिष्यति Māl. 2; मिं<BR>गतोनुरागः 7; तत्र सर्वलोकस्य˚ मिं गतः<BR>प्रवादः ibid. widely known, become<BR>notorious, noised abroad; ˚मिमयं गतो न<BR>शक्यते निवर्तयितुं K. 156;<BR>सर्वोत्सवानाभतिभूमिमिवाधिशयाना 158;<BR>सर्वपौरुषातिभूमिः Dk. 30; ˚मिं गतेन रणरणकेन<BR>U. 1, Śi. 9. 78, 10. 80.<BR>--2 Boldness,<BR>impropriety, violation of due limits<BR>(अमर्यादा); विपदि न दूषितातिभूमिः<BR>Śi. 8. 20.<BR>--3 Eminence, superiority.<BR>--4 Extensive land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिभोजनं|अतिभोजन
अतिभोजनं Voracity, surfeiting<BR>oneself, excess in eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमंगल्य|अतिमङ्गल्य|अतिमङ्गल्यः
अतिमंगल्य a. Very auspicious.<BR>--ल्यः N. of a tree, (बिल्ववृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमतिः|अतिमति
अतिमतिः f.<BR>--मानः Haughtiness, too<BR>great pride; अतिमाने च कौरवाः Chāṇ. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमर्त्य
अतिमर्त्य --मानुष a. Superhuman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमानुष
अतिमर्त्य --मानुष a. Superhuman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमर्याद|अतिमर्य्याद|अतिमर्य्यादः
अतिमर्याद a. Exceeding due<BR>limits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमर्शः|अतिमर्श
अतिमर्शः Close contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमांस
अतिमांस a. [अतिशयितं मांसं यत्र]<BR>Fleshy, plump, fat, as जंघा, अधरोष्ठ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमात्र|अतिमात्रं
अतिमात्र a. [अतिक्रांतो मात्रां,<BR>अतिशयिता मात्रा प्रमाणं यस्य वा] Exceeding the<BR>proper measure, inordinate,<BR>excessive; ˚भास्वरत्वं M. 1. 8; (in comp)<BR>very much, beyond measure;<BR>˚सुदुःसहानि Ś. 4. 3 quite insupportable;<BR>˚लोहिततलौ 1. 30;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">Page0033-b+ 55</a>]<BR>मुनिव्रतैस्त्वामतिमात्रकर्शितां Ku. 5. 48<BR>--त्रं, --मात्रशः ind.<BR>Beyond measure, inordinately,<BR>excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमान|अतिमानः
अतिमान a. [मानमतिक्रांतः]<BR>Immeasurable, very great or wide (as<BR>fame); ˚नया कीर्त्या Dk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमाय
अतिमाय a. [मायामतिक्रांतः]<BR>Finally liberated, emancipated from the<BR>Māyā or illusion of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमारुत|अतिमारुतः
अतिमारुत a. Very windy.<BR>--तः,<BR>--वातः A strong hurricane, storm,<BR>violent gust of wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमित
अतिमित a.<BR>1 Over-measured,<BR>excessive.<BR>--2 [अ-तिमित] Not wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमित्रं|अतिमित्र
अतिमित्रं A great friend, epithet<BR>of a very friendly constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्त|अतिमुक्तः
अतिमुक्त a.<BR>1 Entirely free from<BR>worldly desires, finally emancipated.<BR>--2 Barren, seedless.<BR>--3 Surpassing<BR>(a necklace of) pearls;<BR>अतिमुक्तमद्ग्रथितकेसरावली Māl. 5. 8.<BR>--क्तः --क्तकः<BR>1 A kind of creeper (माधवी, Mar.<BR>कुसरी or कस्तुरमोगरा) represented<BR>as twisting itself round the<BR>mangotree and as the beloved of that<BR>tree; cf. क इदानीं<BR>सहकारमंतरेणातिमुक्तलतां पल्लवितां सहते Ś. 3, परिगृहाण गते<BR>सहकारतां त्वमतिमुक्तलताचरितं मयि<BR>M. 4. 13.<BR>--2 N. of a tree, Dalbergia<BR>Oujeinensis (तिनिश).<BR>--3 (˚क्तकः)<BR>Mountain ebony; N. of a tree called<BR>हरिमंथ (तिंदुकवृक्ष, तालवृक्ष also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमुक्तिः|अतिमुक्ति
अतिमुक्तिः f.<BR>--मोक्षः Final liberation<BR>(from death).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमृत्यु|अतिमृत्युः
अतिमृत्यु a. Overcoming death.<BR>--त्युः Final liberation from death<BR>(मोक्ष); तमेव विदित्वा ऽतिमृत्युमेति नान्यः<BR>पंथा विद्यते Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिमोदा
अतिमोदा<BR>1 Very great fragrance.<BR>--2 N. of a plant नवमल्लिका, Jasminum<BR>Heterophyllum or Arboreum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतियवः|अतियव
अतियवः A kind of barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतियोगः|अतियोग
अतियोगः Overflow, excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरंहस्
अतिरंहस् a. Very fleet or swift;<BR>सारंगेणातिरंहसा Ś. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरक्त
अतिरक्त a. Very red or very<BR>much attached.<BR>--क्ता N. of one of<BR>the 7 tongues of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरथः|अतिरथ
अतिरथः [अतिक्रांतो रथं रथिनं] An<BR>unrivalled warrior, fighting from<BR>his car (अमितान् योधयेद्यस्तु संप्रोक्तोऽ<BR>तिरथस्तु सः); दत्त्वाऽभयं सोतिरथः Ve. 3. 26.<BR>Several Atirathas are mentioned in<BR>Bhārata Udyogaparvan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरभसः|अतिरभस
अतिरभसः Great speed,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-c" target="_blank">Page0033-c+ 57</a>]<BR>precipitateness, headlong speed,<BR>rashness; ˚कृतानां कर्मणां Bh. 2. 99; दर्शन˚<BR>प्रधावितेन K. 192 great hurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरसा
अतिरसा (Very juicy) N. of<BR>various plants, मूर्वा, रास्ना and क्लीतनक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिराजन्
अतिराजन् m.<BR>1 An extraordinary<BR>or excellent king.<BR>--2 One who<BR>surpasses a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरात्र|अतिरात्रः
अतिरात्र a. Ved. [अतिक्रांतो रात्रिं]<BR>Prepared over-night.<BR>--त्रः [<BR>अतिशयिता रात्रिः, ततः अस्त्यर्थे अच्]<BR>1 An<BR>optional part of the Jyotiṣṭoma<BR>sacrifice (एकरात्रसाध्यगवामयने प्रथमसंस्थः<BR>यागभेदः).<BR>--2 Dead of night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरिच्
अतिरिच् (Gen. used in pass.)<BR>1 To surpass, excel, be superior to<BR>(with abl.); अश्वमेधसहस्रेभ्यः<BR>सत्यमेवातिरिच्यते H. 4. 131; गृहं तु गृहिणीहीनं<BR>कांतारादतिरिच्यते Pt. 4. 81; वाचः<BR>कर्मातिरिच्यते ‘example is better than<BR>precept;’ sometimes with acc.; न<BR>च नारायणोऽत्रभवंतमतिरिच्यते K. 203;<BR>or used by itself in the sense of<BR>‘to be supreme,’ ‘prevail’,<BR>‘triumph’, ‘predominate’, ‘be<BR>mightier’; न किंचिदतिरिच्यते Ms. 9. 296<BR>none is supreme or higher than<BR>another; 12. 25; so दैवमत्रातिरिच्यते,<BR>स्वभावोतिरिच्यते H. 1. 17;<BR>स्वल्पमप्यतिरिच्यते H. 2 is of great importance.<BR>--2<BR>To be left with a surplus, be<BR>redundant or superfluous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरिक्त|अतिरिक्तः
अतिरिक्त p. p.<BR>1 Surpassed,<BR>excelled; सर्वातिरिक्तसारेण R. 1. 14 strength<BR>exceeding that of all creatures;<BR>सुतजन्मातिरिक्तेन महोत्सवेन K. 137<BR>surpassing the birth of a son.<BR>--2<BR>Redundant, superfluous, remaining<BR>over and above;<BR>परिपूरितहृदयातिरिक्तहर्षमिव K. 66 not contained in the<BR>heart.<BR>--3 Excessive, exuberant.<BR>--4<BR>Unequalled, unsurpassed; supreme,<BR>elevated; समश्नुवानाः सहसाऽतिरिक्ततां<BR>Ki. 14. 33 being raised up or<BR>elevated.<BR>--5 Different (generally<BR>व्यतिरिक्त in this sense, q. v.).<BR>--6<BR>Quite empty.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. having<BR>a redundant limb (a finger, toe &c.).<BR>--(गं) a redundant limb or member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरेकः|अतिरेक
अति(ती)रेकः [रिच्-घञ्]<BR>1 Excess,<BR>exuberance, excellence, eminence;<BR>पौरुषातिरेकः U. 6; so मद˚, वीर्य˚, गुण˚<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Redundancy, surplus,<BR>superfluity.<BR>--3 Difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीरेकः|अतीरेक
अति(ती)रेकः [रिच्-घञ्]<BR>1 Excess,<BR>exuberance, excellence, eminence;<BR>पौरुषातिरेकः U. 6; so मद˚, वीर्य˚, गुण˚<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Redundancy, surplus,<BR>superfluity.<BR>--3 Difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरुच्
अतिरुच् m. [रोचते इति रुक् स्त्रीणां<BR>ऊरुदेशः; अतिक्रांतो रुचं Tv.] The knee.<BR>--क् f. A very beautiful woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरुचिर
अतिरुचिर a. Very lovely.<BR>--रा<BR>N. of two metres, the one a<BR>variety of अतिजगती, and the other also<BR>called चूडिका or चूलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरूक्ष|अतिरूक्षः
अतिरूक्ष a.<BR>1 Very rough or<BR>barren; devoid of affection, cruel.<BR>--2 Very<BR>affectionate [अतिक्रांतो रूक्षं].<BR>--क्षः N.<BR>of a variety of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरूप|अतिरूपः
अतिरूप a.<BR>1 Formless, such as<BR>wind.<BR>--2 Very beautiful.<BR>--पं Great<BR>beauty; as ˚वती कन्या.<BR>--पः [<BR>अतिक्रांतो रूपं] the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरै
अतिरै a. (रि n.) Exceeding one's<BR>income, extravagant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरोगः|अतिरोग
अतिरोगः Consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिरोमश|अतिरोमशः
अति-लो-रोमश a. Very hairy,<BR>shaggy.<BR>--शः<BR>1 A wild goat.<BR>--2 A<BR>large monkey.<BR>--शा A potherb<BR>(नीलबुह्ना) Convolvulus Argenteus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलोमश
अति-लो-रोमश a. Very hairy,<BR>shaggy.<BR>--शः<BR>1 A wild goat.<BR>--2 A<BR>large monkey.<BR>--शा A potherb<BR>(नीलबुह्ना) Convolvulus Argenteus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलंघनं|अतिलङ्घन
अतिलंघनं<BR>1 Excessive fasting.<BR>--2 Transgression; न<BR>युक्तमत्रार्यजनातिलंघनं Ki. 14. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलंघिन्
अतिलंघिन् a. Erring,<BR>committing mistakes; नर्तकीरभिनयातिलंघिनीः<BR>R. 19. 14<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिलिहा
अतिलिहा N. of a Prākṛta<BR>Metre of four lines with 16 Mātrās<BR>in each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवक्तृ
अतिवक्तृ a. Very talkative,<BR>garrulous; आक्रोष्टाचातिवक्ता च ब्राह्मणानां<BR>Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवक्र|अतिवक्रः
अतिवक्र a. Very crooked.<BR>--क्रः<BR>N. of the five planets (भौम and<BR>others); अतिवक्रा नगाष्टके इति ज्योतिषोक्तं<BR>सूर्यस्य सप्तमाष्टमस्थितिवशात्<BR>पूर्वगतिविपरीतपश्चाद्गतिशालिभौमादिपंचकं Tv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवयस्
अतिवयस् a. Very old, aged,<BR>advanced in years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्णाश्रमिन्|अतिवर्ण्णाश्रमिन्
अतिवर्णाश्रमिन् m. One who is<BR>beyond castes and orders (यो<BR>वेदांतमहावाक्यश्रवणेनैव केवलम् । आत्मानमीश्वरं वेद सोऽ<BR>तिवर्णाश्रमी भवेत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्तुल|अतिवर्तुलः|अतिवर्त्तुल|अतिवर्त्तुलः
अतिवर्तुल a. Very round.<BR>--लः<BR>N. of a grain or potherb (कलायविशेष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवह्
अतिवह् {c1c} P. To carry over or<BR>across. --Caus.<BR>1 To spend, pass (as<BR>time); किं वा मयापि न<BR>दिनान्यतिवाहितानि Māl. 6. 13; अतिवाहयांबभूव त्रियामां<BR>R. 9. 70; ऋतून् 19. 47.<BR>--2 To let pass<BR>over, get through successfully;<BR>गुहाविसारीण्यतिवाहितानि मया<BR>कथंचिद्घनगर्जितानि R. 13. 28 allowed to pass<BR>over my head, endured; स<BR>शापस्तेनातिवाहितः Ks. 33. 91.<BR>--3 To rid<BR>oneself of, elude, avoid;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">Page0034-b+ 56</a>]<BR>अस्मिंस्तमालविटपांधकारे प्रविश्य एनमतिवाहयावः<BR>Ratn. 2 get out of his way, elude<BR>his pursuit (and thus cheat him).<BR>--4 To transplant, remove (to another<BR>place), bring or carry over;<BR>अलकामतिवाह्यैव वसतिं वसुसंपदां Ku. 6. 37.<BR>--5 To follow, tread (as a path);<BR>लोकातिवाहिते मार्गे Sarva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाहः|अतिवाह
अतिवाहः [अतीत्य देहं अन्यदेहे वाहः प्रापणं<BR>स. त.]<BR>1 Passing or conveying of<BR>the सूक्ष्मशरीर, the subtle principle of<BR>life, to other bodies at the expiry of<BR>good actions (अदृष्ट) contributing<BR>to the enjoyment of worldly<BR>pleasures.<BR>--2 Carrying over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाहकः|अतिवाहक
अतिवाहकः [अतीत्य एतं देहं बाहयति देहांतरं<BR>प्रापयति; वह्-ण्वुल्] The deity or spirit<BR>appointed by God to help in the<BR>conveying of the जीव or सूक्ष्मशरीर in<BR>the above manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाहनं|अतिवाहन
अतिवाहनं<BR>1 Passing, spending.<BR>--2<BR>Excessive toiling or enduring,<BR>bearing too much load; too heavy burden;<BR>H. 3.<BR>--3 Despatching, sending away,<BR>ridding oneself of; कथमस्य˚ नं<BR>भविष्यति Pt. 5 how shall I rid myself of<BR>him?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाहिक
अतिवाहिक a. [अतिवाहोस्त्यस्य ठन्]<BR>Able to convey to other bodies, See<BR>अतिवाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवाहित|अतिवाहितः
अतिवाहित p. p. Spent, passed.<BR>--तः<BR>An inhabitant of the lower world.<BR>--तं (सूक्ष्मशरीरं) = अतिवाह, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवादः|अतिवाद
अतिवादः<BR>1 Very harsh, abusive<BR>or insulting language, reproof;<BR>अतिवादांस्तितिक्षेत Ms. 6. 47; reprimand,<BR>correction; अतिवादाद्वदाम्येष मा<BR>धर्ममभिशंकिथाः Mb.<BR>--2 Exaggeration,<BR>exaggerated talk, hyperbole (अत्युक्ति);<BR>अतिवादं शंसति अतिवादेन वै देवा असुरान्<BR>अत्युद्य अथैनानत्यायन् Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवादिन्
अतिवादिन् a. Talkative, very<BR>eloquent; exclusively establishing one's<BR>own assertion; विजानन् विद्वान् भवते<BR>नातिवादी Muṇḍ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवासः|अतिवास
अतिवासः Fast on the day<BR>preceding a Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविकट|अतिविकटः
अतिविकट a. Very fierce.<BR>--टः A<BR>vicious elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविष
अतिविष a.<BR>1 Very poisonous.<BR>--2<BR>Counteracting poison.<BR>--षा N. of a<BR>poisonous yet highly medicinal plant<BR>(Mar. अतिविष or अतिविख) Aconitum<BR>Ferox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिविस्तरः|अतिविस्तर
अतिविस्तरः Prolixity,<BR>diffuseness; U. 1, Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवृत्
अतिवृत् {c1c} A. (P. in epic<BR>poetry).<BR>1 To pass over or by, cross<BR>(as a place &c.).<BR>--2 (a) To go<BR>beyond, exceed (fig. also);<BR>वाग्विभवातिवृत्तं आचार्यकं Māl. 1. 26<BR>exceeding or transcending the powers of<BR>speech, indescribable;<BR>मुकुलावस्थामतिवृत्तेषु तंडुलेषु Dk. 132; का ते स्तुतिः<BR>स्तुतिपथादतिवृत्तधाम्नः Mv. 4. 29<BR>transcending praise. (b) To offend,<BR>overstep, transgress, violate;<BR>योस्याः शासनमतिवर्तते Dk. 167;<BR>कोतिवर्तते दैवं 51 who can transgress the<BR>decrees of Fate? कोन्यो जीवितुकामो<BR>देवस्य शासनमतिवर्तेत Mu. 3, Śi. 6. 19.<BR>(c) To neglect, omit, let slip. (d)<BR>To have no regard to, disregard,<BR>slight; offend (especially by<BR>unfaithfulness), injure; शपथशतातिवर्ती<BR>Dk. 62 disregarding; ऋतुस्नातां<BR>सतीं भार्यां… अतिवर्तेत दुष्टात्मा; यथाहं<BR>कर्मणावाचा शरीरेण च राघवं । सततं नातिवर्तेय<BR>Rām.; अपत्यलोभाद्यातु<BR>स्त्रीभर्तारमतिवर्तते Ms. 5. 161.<BR>--3 (a) To surpass, excel;<BR>मनुष्यसंख्यामतिवर्तितुं वा Ki. 3. 40,<BR>Śi. 14. 59; बांधवस्नेहं राज्यलोभोऽतिवर्तते<BR>Ks. 41. 40 to outweigh, preponderate. (b) To<BR>overcome, subdue, vanquish, get the<BR>better of; get over, escape or get<BR>loose from; असाध्यानतिवर्तंते प्रमेहा<BR>रजनीं यथा Suśr.; किमाचारः कथं<BR>चैतांस्त्रीन् गुणानतिवर्तते Bg. 14. 21 transcend<BR>these three qualities; दैवं पौरुषेण<BR>Mb., Dk. 73, Ks. 121. 67.<BR>--4<BR>(Intrans.) To pass away, glide away,<BR>elapse (as time); to be late or delay;<BR>एवं तयोः प्रत्यहमन्योन्याहारादिदानेन<BR>कालोतिवर्तते H. 1; महता स्नेहेन कालोतिवर्तते<BR>H. 2; समयो नातिवर्तते Mv. 6; आ<BR>षोडशाद्ब्राह्मणस्य सावित्री नातिवर्तते<BR>Ms. 2. 38 is not late (नातिक्रांतकाला भवति).<BR>--5<BR>To go away from, leave, abandon<BR>(abl.); यथा एम् हृदयं नित्यं नातिवर्तति<BR>राघवात् Rām. --Caus.<BR>1 To slight, not<BR>to heed, disregard; सुहृदश्चातिवर्तिताः<BR>Dk. 136.<BR>--2 To let out, discharge<BR>(as excrement).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्तनं|अतिवर्तन|अतिवर्त्तन
अतिवर्तनं A pardonable offence or<BR>misdemeanour; exemption from<BR>punishment; ten cases are<BR>mentioned in Ms. 8. 290 यानस्य चैव यातुश्च<BR>यानस्वामिन एव च । दशातिवर्तनान्याहुः शेषे दंडो विधीयते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्तिन्|अतिवर्त्तिन्
अतिवर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Crossing, surpassing,<BR>excelling; भुवनातिवर्तिना ओजसा<BR>Ki. 12. 21; passing over,<BR>overstepping, transgressing, violating<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Excessive.<BR>--3 Foremost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवृत्तिः|अतिवृत्ति
अतिवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Surpassing, violation,<BR>transgression.<BR>--2 Exaggeration,<BR>hyperbole.<BR>--3 Violent effusion (as of<BR>blood); excessive action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवर्धनं|अतिवर्धन
अतिवर्धनं Excessive growth,<BR>increase, adding to, increasing; एतत्खलु<BR>व्यजनानिलैरति(भि)वर्धनं प्रभं जनस्य<BR>यदस्मद्विधैः परिबोधनमार्यस्य K. 289; cf.<BR>“Carrying coals to New-castle”, or “To<BR>gild refined gold, to paint the lily,<BR>… or with taper-light the eye of<BR>Heaven to garnish is wasteful and<BR>ridiculous excess”; See the other<BR>phrases on the same page.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवृद्ध|अतिवृद्धः
अतिवृद्ध a. Very old; very much<BR>grown.<BR>--द्धः N. of a Mantra in<BR>Tantras; चतुःशतं समारभ्य यावद्वर्णसहस्रकम् ।<BR>अतिवृद्धः स मंत्रस्तु सर्वशास्त्रेषु वर्जितः ॥<BR>--द्धा<BR>A very old cow (unable to chew<BR>grass &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवृष्टिः|अतिवृष्टि
अतिवृष्टिः f. Excessive or heavy<BR>rain, one of the six calamities of<BR>the season. See ईति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवेगित
अतिवेगित a. Moving or moved<BR>with great velocity, quick in motion;<BR>मौमादयोल्पमूर्तित्वाच्छीघ्रमंदोच्चसंज्ञकैः ।<BR>दैवतैरपकृष्यंते सुदूरमतिवेगिताः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवेधः|अतिवेध
अतिवेधः Close contact, N. of<BR>the contact of दशमी and एकादशी (<BR>अरुणोदयवेधः स्यात् सार्धं तु घटिकाद्वयम् ।<BR>अतिवेधो द्विघटिका प्रभासंदर्शनाद्रवेः ॥ इति<BR>स्मृत्युक्तः एकादश्याः दशमीसंपर्कभेदः Tv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिवेल|अतिवेलं
अतिवेल a. [अतिक्रांतो वेलां मर्यादां कूलं<BR>वा]<BR>1 Exceeding the due limits or<BR>boundary (as the water of the sea).<BR>--2 Excessive, extravagant;<BR>boundless.<BR>--लं adv.<BR>1 Excessively.<BR>--2 Out<BR>of season, unseasonably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्यथनं|अतिव्यथन
अतिव्यथनं --था Infliction of<BR>great pain; सपत्रनिष्पत्रादतिव्यथने<BR>P. V. 4. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्यथा
अतिव्यथनं --था Infliction of<BR>great pain; सपत्रनिष्पत्रादतिव्यथने<BR>P. V. 4. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिव्याप्तिः|अतिव्याप्ति
अतिव्याप्तिः f.<BR>1 An<BR>unwarrantable stretch of a rule or principle.<BR>--2 Including what is not intended<BR>to be included in a proposition;<BR>(in Nyāya) including or<BR>covering too much, unwarranted<BR>extension of a definition to things<BR>not intended to be defined by it,<BR>so that it includes such things as<BR>ought not to fall under it; one of<BR>the three faults to which a<BR>definition is open; अलक्ष्ये लक्षणगमनं<BR>अतिव्याप्तिः; यथा मनुष्यो ब्राह्मणः इति लक्षणस्य<BR>शूद्रेऽतिव्याप्तिः, तस्यापि मनुष्यत्वात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्करी
अतिशक्क(क्व)री A class of metres<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-b" target="_blank">Page0035-b+ 57</a>]<BR>containing 4 lines, with 15 syllables<BR>in each. It has 18 varieties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशक्वरी
अतिशक्क(क्व)री A class of metres<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-b" target="_blank">Page0035-b+ 57</a>]<BR>containing 4 lines, with 15 syllables<BR>in each. It has 18 varieties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशर्वरं|अतिशर्वर
अतिशर्वरं Ved. The dead of night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशस्त्र
अतिशस्त्र a. Surpassing weapons;<BR>˚नखन्यासः R. 12. 73 the nail-wounds<BR>surpassed the wounds of swords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशी
अतिशी {c2c} A.<BR>1 To surpass, excel;<BR>पूर्वान्महाभाग तयाऽतिशेषे R. 5. 14;<BR>चरितेन चातिशयिता मुनयः Ki. 6. 32,<BR>Bk. 7. 46, 8. 1; न शक्नुमो वयमार्यस्य<BR>मतिमतिशयितुं Mu. 3.<BR>--2 To precede in<BR>sleeping; अहं पतीन्नातिशये Mb.<BR>--3 To<BR>annoy, act as an incubus. --Caus.<BR>--(शाययति) To excel; धार्म्नातिशाययति<BR>धाम सहस्रधाम्नः Mu. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयः|अतिशय
अतिशयः [शी-अच्]<BR>1 Excess,<BR>preeminence excellence; वीर्य˚ R. 3. 62;<BR>महिम्नां… अतिशयः U. 4. 21; तस्मिन्<BR>विधानातिशये विधातुः R. 6. 11 excellence,<BR>highest perfection of art.<BR>--2<BR>Superiority (in quality, rank,<BR>quantity &c.); महार्घस्तीर्थानामिव हि महतां<BR>कोप्यतिशयः U. 6. 11; oft in comp.<BR>with adjectives, in the sense of<BR>‘exceedingly’, ‘excessively’; ˚रमणीयः<BR>Mu. 3; आसीदतिशयप्रेक्ष्यः<BR>R. 17. 25; मुक्तागुणातिशयसंभृतमंडनश्रीः<BR>V. 5. 19; or with nouns, meaning<BR>‘excellent’, ‘excessive’, ‘very great’;<BR>˚रयः, अश्वातिशयं K. 80 the best of<BR>horses; ˚दारिद्र्योपहताः.<BR>--3<BR>Advantageous result, one of the superhuman<BR>qualities attributed to Jaina saints.<BR>--a. [अतिशयः अस्त्यर्थे अच्] Superior,<BR>pre-eminent, excessive, very great,<BR>abundant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः f. {1}<BR>exaggerated or hyperbolical language,<BR>extreme assertion. {2} a figure of<BR>speech, (corr. to hyperbole) said<BR>to be of 5 kinds in S. D., but of 4<BR>in K. P.; निगीर्याध्यवसानं तु प्रकृतस्य परेण<BR>यत् । प्रस्तुतस्य यदन्यत्वं यद्यर्थोक्तौ च<BR>कल्पनम् । कार्यकारणयोर्यश्च पौर्वापर्यविपर्ययः ।<BR>विज्ञेयातिशयोक्तिः सा; Ex. of the first kind:<BR>कमलमनंभासि कमले च कुवलये तानि<BR>कनकलतिकायां । सा च सुकुमारसुभगेत्युत्पातपरंपरा<BR>केयम् ॥ {3} verbosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयन|अतिशयनं
अतिशयन a. [शी-भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>Surpassing, (in comp.); great, eminent;<BR>abundant.<BR>--नं Excess, abundance,<BR>superfluity.<BR>--नी N. of a metre of<BR>four lines, also called चित्रलेखा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयालु
अतिशयालु a. Tending to excel or<BR>surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयित
अतिशयित p. p.<BR>1 Excelled,<BR>surpassed &c.; ˚सुरासुरप्रभावं U. 5. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Excessive, exceeding, going beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशयिन्
अतिशयिन् a. [शी-इनि]<BR>1 Superior;<BR>excellent; pre-eminent;<BR>श्रियमतिशयिनीं समेत्य जग्मुः Ki. 10. 25;<BR>इदमुत्तममतिशयिनि व्यंग्ये वाच्याद् ध्वनिर्बुधैः कथितः<BR>K. P. 1; ˚यिनि समाप्ता वंश एवाशिषस्ते<BR>V. 5. 21.<BR>--2 Excessive, abundant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशायनं|अतिशायन
अतिशायनं [शी-ल्युट्] Excellence,<BR>superiority, Mv. 4. 15; अतिशायने<BR>तमबिष्ठनौ (superlative affixes)<BR>P. V. 3. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशायिन्
अतिशायिन् a. [शी-णिनि]<BR>1<BR>Excelling, surpassing; अर्थकाम˚ &c.<BR>--2<BR>Excessive.<BR>--नी N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिशेषः|अतिशेष
अतिशेषः Remainder; remnant<BR>(as of time); a small remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिश्रेयसिः|अतिश्रेयसि
अतिश्रेयसिः [श्रेयसीमतिक्रांतः] A<BR>man superior to the most excellent<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिश्व|अतिश्वः
अतिश्व a.<BR>1 Surpassing in<BR>strength a dog (such as a boar &c.).<BR>--2 Worse than a dog.<BR>--श्वा Service;<BR>cf. सेवां लाघवकारिणीं कृतधियः स्थाने श्ववृत्तिं<BR>विदुः Mu. 3.<BR>--श्वः N. of a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिश्वन्
अतिश्वन् m. An excellent dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिष्कद्वरी
अतिष्कद्वरी [fr. स्कंद्] A<BR>transgressor; a very dissolute woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिष्ठा
अतिष्ठा {c1c} P. To excel; be over<BR>(Ved.); स भूमिं विश्वतो<BR>वृत्वात्यातिष्ठद्दशांगुलं Rv. 10. 90. 1 was over and<BR>above by 10 Aṅgulas.<BR>--ष्ठा<BR>[स्था-क्विप्षत्वं] Superiority, precedence. --a.,<BR>˚वत्-वन् Surpassing, standing at the<BR>head of all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसक्तिः|अतिसक्ति
अतिसक्तिः f. Close contact or<BR>proximity; great attachment;<BR>अतिसक्तिमेत्य वरुणस्य दिशा Śi. 9. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसंधा|अतिसन्धा
अतिसंधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To deceive,<BR>overreach, cheat; त्वया चंद्रमसा च<BR>विश्वसनीयाभ्यामतिसंधीयते कामिजनसार्थः<BR>Ś. 3; कथं मया ब्रह्मबंधुरतिसंधेयः V. 2.<BR>--2 To prejudice, wrong, injure,<BR>encroach upon; मूलद्वारं<BR>नान्यैर्द्वारैरतिसंदधीत रूपर्द्ध्या Bṛ. S. 53. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसंधानं|अतिसन्धान|अतिसंधान
अतिसंधानं Cheating, deception;<BR>परातिसंधान˚ Ś. 5. 25; trick, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसंध्या
अतिसंध्या The time about the<BR>twilights, the time just before and<BR>after the morning and evening<BR>twilight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्पणं|अतिसर्पण
अतिसर्पणं Violent motion or<BR>movement (of the child in the womb).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्व|अतिसर्वः|अतिसर्व्व
अतिसर्व a. Transcending or<BR>superior to all, above all.<BR>--र्वः The Supreme<BR>Being; अतिसर्वाय शर्वाय Mugdha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसांतपनं|अतिसान्तपन
अतिसांतपनं A kind of very<BR>austere penance; (<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">Page0036-a+ 56</a>]<BR>गोमूत्रगोमयक्षीरदधिसर्पिःकुशोदकान्येकाहं द्वितीयमुपवसेत्तत्सांतपनं;<BR>त्र्यहाभ्यस्तैश्चातिसांतपनं Viṣṇu Smṛti).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसांवत्सर
अतिसांवत्सर a. (री f.)<BR>Extending over more than a year; Ms. 8. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसाम्या
अतिसाम्या [अत्यंतं साम्यं मधुना<BR>अस्याः] N. of the plant मधुयष्टि, sweet<BR>juice of the Bengal Madder, Rubia<BR>Manjith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसृ
अतिसृ {c1c} P. Ved. To extend.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To extend.<BR>--2 To exert<BR>oneself to drive out; give out (as<BR>a fluid).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर|अतिसरः
अतिसर a.<BR>1 One who goes beyond<BR>or exceeds.<BR>--2 Leader, foremost.<BR>--रः<BR>Effort or exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसारः|अतिसार
अति(ती)सारः [अतिसारयति मलं<BR>द्रवीकृत्य, वा अतेर्दीर्घः] Dysentery,<BR>violent straining at stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीसारः|अतीसार
अति(ती)सारः [अतिसारयति मलं<BR>द्रवीकृत्य, वा अतेर्दीर्घः] Dysentery,<BR>violent straining at stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसारिन्
अति(ती)सारिन् m. [अत्यंतं सारयति<BR>मलं] The disease called अतिसार. --a.,<BR>--अतिसारकिन् [अतिसारो यस्यास्ति, इनि<BR>कुक् च] Affected by, afflicted with,<BR>dysentery; सातिसारोऽतिसारकी Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीसारिन्
अति(ती)सारिन् m. [अत्यंतं सारयति<BR>मलं] The disease called अतिसार. --a.,<BR>--अतिसारकिन् [अतिसारो यस्यास्ति, इनि<BR>कुक् च] Affected by, afflicted with,<BR>dysentery; सातिसारोऽतिसारकी Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसृज्
अतिसृज् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To give, present,<BR>bestow, grant; अतिसृष्टो राज्यार्धविभागः<BR>Mu. 2; पुरा नारायणेनेयमतिसृष्टा मरुत्वते<BR>V. 1. 15; राघवाय तनयां… अतिसृष्टवान्<BR>R. 11. 48; अनसूयातिसृष्टेन 12. 27.<BR>--2<BR>To dismiss, abandon, part with.<BR>--3<BR>To permit, allow.<BR>--4 To remit,<BR>forgive (as fine &c.).<BR>--5 To leave as a<BR>remnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्गः|अतिसर्ग
अतिसर्गः<BR>1 Granting(of a wish);<BR>giving; स्रष्टुर्वरातिसर्गात्तु मया तस्य<BR>दुरात्मनः R. 10.42.<BR>--2 Granting permission<BR>(to do what one likes कामचारानुज्ञा)<BR>P. III. 3. 163, one of the senses of the<BR>Potential.<BR>--3 Dismissal, discharge,<BR>parting with; giving away; स्त्रीणां<BR>दानविक्रयातिसर्गा विद्यंतेन पुंसः Nir. --a.<BR>[सर्गं सृष्टिमतिक्रांतः] Everlasting,<BR>permanent (नित्य); emancipated (मुक्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसर्जनं|अतिसर्जन|अतिसर्ज्जनं
अतिसर्जनं<BR>1 Giving, granting;<BR>consigning; विधुरां ज्वलनातिसर्जनात्<BR>Ku. 4. 32, consigning to the flames;<BR>दीयतामिति वचोतिसर्जने Śi. 14. 48;<BR>तत्तदीयविशिखातिसर्जनात् Ki. 13. 57 giving<BR>back.<BR>--2 Liberality, munificence.<BR>--3<BR>Killing.<BR>--4 Deception.<BR>--5 Separation<BR>from, parting with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसौरभ|अतिसौरभः
अतिसौरभ a. Very fragrant.<BR>--भं<BR>Great fragrance.<BR>--भः The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिसौहित्यं|अतिसौहित्य
अतिसौहित्यं Stuffing oneself<BR>with food; न ˚त्यमाचरेत् Ms. 4. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिस्पर्श|अतिस्पर्शः
अतिस्पर्श a. Not liberal,<BR>niggardly, mean-spirited.<BR>--र्शः Slight contact<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-b" target="_blank">Page0036-b+ 57</a>]<BR>or absence of contact of the tongue<BR>and palate in pronunciation; epithet<BR>of the semivowels and vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिस्नेहः|अतिस्नेह
अतिस्नेहः Over-affection; ˚हः<BR>कार्यदर्शी V. 2 sees or finds what is to be<BR>done; ˚हः पापशंकी Ś. 4 is apt to<BR>suspect evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतिहस्तयति
अतिहस्तयति Den. P. [अतिहस्त-णि]<BR>1 To stretch out the hands (हस्तौ<BR>निरस्यति).<BR>--2 [हस्तिना अतिक्रामति] To<BR>overtake (one) on an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अती
अती [अति-इ] {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go beyond,<BR>pass on, over or beyond, cross (time or<BR>space); स्तोकमंतरमतीत्य Ś. 1;<BR>जवादतीये हिमवानधोमुखैः Ki. 14. 54 was<BR>gone to or reached; स्थातव्यं ते<BR>नयनविषयं यावदत्येति भानुः Me. 34 passes<BR>out of sight; अतीत्यैकादशाहं तु नामकर्म<BR>तथाऽकरोत् Rām. after 11 days;<BR>गृहपंक्तयश्चिरमतीयिरे जनैः Śi. 13. 53.<BR>--2 To enter, step over; अद्वारेण<BR>च नातीयात् ग्रामं वा वेश्म वा वृतं<BR>Ms. 4. 73.<BR>--3 To excel, surpass,<BR>outstrip, be more than a match for;<BR>त्रिस्रोतसः कांतिमतीत्य तस्थौ Ku. 7. 15;<BR>सत्यमतीत्य हरितो हरींश्च वर्तंते वाजिनः Ś. 1;<BR>अग्निस्त्विषा नात्येति पूषणं Śi. 2. 23;<BR>to exceed, go beyond, transcend;<BR>कुसीदवृद्धिर्द्वैगुण्यं नात्येति Ms. 8. 151 does<BR>not exceed; अतीत्य वाचां मनसां च<BR>गोचरं स्थिताय Ki. 18. 41, Śi. 16. 48.<BR>--4<BR>To overcome, subdue, vanquish,<BR>get the better of; न प्रदीप इव<BR>वायुमत्यगात् R. 19. 53 did not overcome,<BR>outlive or survive; to overtake,<BR>outdo.<BR>--5 To walk by, walk past,<BR>pass by, leave behind; स्रोतोवहां पथि<BR>निकामजलामतीत्य Ś. 6. 16; सोत्यगात्<BR>आश्रमं R. 15. 37.<BR>--6 To omit, neglect,<BR>disregard, violate, transgress, overstep;<BR>न दिष्टमर्थमत्येतुमीशो मर्त्यः कथंचन Mb.<BR>avoid; अतीत्य हि गुणान् सर्वान् स्वभावो<BR>मूर्ध्नि वर्तते H. 1. 15; देशं कालं च योऽ<BR>तीयात् Y. 2. 195; अतीयात्सागरो वेलां न<BR>प्रतिज्ञामहं पितुः Rām.; भूतान्यत्येति पंच वै<BR>Ms. 12. 90 oversteps the five<BR>elements (मोक्षं प्राप्नोति Kull.); अत्येति<BR>तत्सर्वमिदं विदित्वा Bg. 8. 28, 14. 20.<BR>--7 (Intrans.) To pass, elapse<BR>(time); अत्येति रजनी या तु सा न<BR>प्रतिनिवर्तते Rām.; अतीते दक्षिणायने &c.<BR>--8 To overflow, be redundant, be<BR>in excess.<BR>--9 To die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीत|अतीतं|अतीतः
अतीत p. p. [इ-क्त.]<BR>1 Gone<BR>beyond, crossed.<BR>--2 (Used actively) (a)<BR>exceeding, going beyond, avoiding,<BR>overstepping, having passed over or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-c" target="_blank">Page0036-c+ 58</a>]<BR>neglected &c., with acc. or in comp.;<BR>परिच्छेदातीतः Māl. 1. 30 beyond or past<BR>definition; संख्यामतीत or संख्यातीत<BR>beyond enumeration, innumerable;<BR>तामतीतस्य ते Me. 29; यमुनामतीतमथ<BR>शुश्रुवानमुं Śi. 13. 1; वयोतीतः Ki. 11. 2<BR>past youth, advanced in years;<BR>सर्वारंभपरित्यागी गुणातीतः स उच्यते<BR>Bg. 14. 25; कैर्लिंगैस्त्रीन् गुणानेतानतीतो भवति<BR>प्रभो 14. 21; बाणपथमतीतः क्रव्यभोजनः<BR>V. 5 gone beyond the reach of<BR>arrows, past bowshot; अतीतनौकेऽतिनु<BR>Ak. who has left the boat, i. e.<BR>landed, disembarked. --(b) Gone by,<BR>passed away, past (as time &c.);<BR>अतीते निशांते Dk. 11; असन्निवृत्त्यै<BR>तदतीतमेव Ś. 6. 9; ˚अनागतवर्तमानवेदिना<BR>Pt. 1; अतीते वर्षुके काले Bk. 7. 18;<BR>˚शैशवा Ms. 8. 27; अतीते कार्यशेषज्ञः<BR>शत्रुभिर्नाभिभूयते Ms. 7. 179; ˚लाभस्य च<BR>रक्षणार्थं Pt. 2. 182 of past gains; वेत्ति<BR>जन्मांतराण्यतीतानि K. 46. --(c) Dead,<BR>deceased; सब्रह्मचारिण्येकाहमतीते क्षपणं<BR>स्मृतं Ms. 5. 71; अप्रजायामतीतायां<BR>भर्तुरेव तदिष्यते 9. 196, 197.<BR>--तं The<BR>past, past time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययः|अत्यय
अत्ययः [इ-अच्]<BR>1 (a) Passing<BR>away, lapse; काल˚ Ms. 8. 145. (b)<BR>End, conclusion, termination,<BR>absence, disappearance; तपात्यये<BR>Ku. 4. 44, 5. 23; शिशिरात्ययस्य पुष्पोच्चयः<BR>3. 61; आतप˚ R. 1. 52.<BR>--2<BR>Complete disappearance, death,<BR>destruction, passing away, perishing;<BR>पितुरत्ययात् Dk. 64.<BR>--3 Danger, risk, harm,<BR>injury, evil; जीवितात्ययमापन्नः<BR>Ms. 10. 104 the life being in danger or<BR>jeopardy; प्राणानामेव चात्यये 5. 27;<BR>प्राणात्यये च संप्राप्ते Y. 1. 179,<BR>Ms. 6. 68, 8. 69; पुत्रदारात्ययं प्राप्तः 10. 99<BR>(Kull. क्षुदवसन्नपुत्रकलत्रः).<BR>--4<BR>Suffering, misery, difficulty, distress.<BR>--5 Guilt, fault, offence,<BR>transgression; क्षत्रियस्यात्यये दंडो भागाद्दशगुणो<BR>भवेत् Ms. 8. 243; दाप्योष्टगुणमत्ययं<BR>8. 400 should be made to pay as a<BR>fine for his offence.<BR>--6 Attack,<BR>assault Y. 2. 12.<BR>--7 Overcoming,<BR>mastering mentally, comprehending;<BR>बुद्धिश्च ते लोकैरपि दुरत्यया Rām.<BR>--8<BR>Overstepping; क्षुरस्य धारा निशिता<BR>दुरत्यया Ken.<BR>--9 A class, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययिक
अत्ययिक = आत्ययिक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययित
अत्ययित a.<BR>1 Exceeded, surpassed.<BR>--2 Violated, outraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययिन्
अत्ययिन् a. [इ-इनि P. III. 2. 157]<BR>Exceeding, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतींद्रिय|अतीन्द्रिय|अतीन्द्रियं|अतीन्द्रियः
अतींद्रिय a. [अतिक्रांत इंद्रियं] Beyond<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">Page0037-a+ 57</a>]<BR>the cognizance (reach) of the senses;<BR>अतींद्रियेष्वप्युपपन्नदर्शनः R. 3. 41;<BR>यत्तत्सूक्ष्ममतींद्रियं ज्ञानं यन्निर्विकल्पाख्यं<BR>तदतींद्रियमुच्यते; ˚ज्ञाननिधिः Śi. 1. 11<BR>--यः The<BR>Soul or Puruṣa, (in Sāṃkhya phil.);<BR>the Supreme Soul.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Pradhāna<BR>or Nature (in Sāṃkhya phil.).<BR>--2<BR>The mind (in Vedānta)<BR>योसावतींद्रियग्राह्यः सूक्ष्मोऽव्यक्तः सनातनः Ms. 1. 7<BR>(Kull. इंद्रियमतीत्य वर्तते इति ˚यं मनः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0036-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतीव
अतीव [अति-इव] ind.<BR>1<BR>Exceedingly, excessively, very, very much,<BR>quite, too; ˚पीडित, ˚हृष्ट &c.<BR>--2<BR>Surpassing, superior to (acc.);<BR>अतीवान्यान् भविष्यावः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुंद|अतुन्द
अतुंद a. Not bulky, lean, lank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुर
अतुर a. Ved. Not rich or liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल|अतुलः
अतुल a. [न. ब.] Unequalled,<BR>unsurpassed, matchless, peerless,<BR>incomparable, very great;<BR>भयमतुलं गुरुलोकात् Pt. 5. 31; so ˚पराक्रम,<BR>˚रूप &c.<BR>--लः The sesamum seed<BR>and plant (तिलकवृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुल्य|अतुल्यं
अतुल्य a. Unequalled &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतुषार
अतुषार a. Not cold.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः<BR>The Sun; so अतुहिनकर, ˚रश्मि, ˚धामन्<BR>˚रुचि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतूतुजि
अतूतुजि a. [न तुज्-कि द्वित्वदीर्घे] Not<BR>a donor or giver, not liberal (अदातृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतूर्त|अतूर्त्त
अतूर्त a. [न तूर्यते, तुर्-हिंसायां] Ved.<BR>Not obstructed or stopped or<BR>injured, unhurt.<BR>--र्तं The unlimited<BR>space, sky.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दक्ष a. Ved.<BR>whose plans cannot be obstructed<BR>or are unhurt.<BR>--पथिन् a. Ved. whose<BR>path cannot be obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृणादः|अतृणाद
अतृणादः [न तृणं अत्ति, अद्-अण्] ‘Not<BR>eating grass’, a newborn calf; अथ<BR>वत्सं जातमाहुरतृणाद इति Bṛ. Ār. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृण्या
अतृण्या [न. त.] A small<BR>quantity of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतृदिल
अतृदिल a. [न तृद्यते वध्यते,<BR>तृद्किलच्] Ved. Not assailable,<BR>immovable, solid, firm (as a mountain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अतेजस्
अतेजस् a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Not bright,<BR>dim.<BR>--2 Weak, feeble.<BR>--3<BR>Insignificant; so अतेजस्क, अतेजस्विन्.<BR>--स् n.<BR>Dimness, shadow, darkness; absence<BR>of vigour, feebleness, dullness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्कः|अत्क
अत्कः [अतति गच्छति सततं विकृतिं,<BR>पंथानं &c. अत्-कन् कित्त्वं Uṇ. 3. 43]<BR>{1} A traveller.<BR>--2 A limb or member<BR>(of the body).<BR>--3 (Ved.) Water,<BR>lightning, garment, armour (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्कीलः|अत्कील
अत्कीलः N. of the author of<BR>some Vedic hymns, a descendant of<BR>Viśvāmitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ता
अत्ता [अतति सततं संबध्नाति; अत्-तक्<BR>इडभावः]<BR>1 A mother.<BR>--2 An elder<BR>sister.<BR>--3 A mother-in-law; (rarely)<BR>mother's sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तिः|अत्ति
अत्तिः f., अत्तिका [अत्यते सर्वदा<BR>संबध्यते, कर्मणि क्तिन्] An elder sister &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तृ
अत्तृ &c. See under अद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्नं|अत्न|अत्नः
अत्नं [अतति जयपराजयौ अत्र, अत्-न]<BR>A battle, fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्नः|अत्न|अत्नं
अत्नः [अततिसततं गच्छति; अत्-न<BR>Uṇ. 3. 6.]<BR>1 Wind.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--3 A<BR>traveller. Written also as अत्नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यः|अत्य
अत्यः [अतति शीघ्रं गच्छति, अत् कर्तरि<BR>यत्] A courser, steed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यंहस्
अत्यंहस् a. Ved. Emancipated<BR>from sin or evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यग्नि|अत्यग्निः
अत्यग्नि a. Surpassing fire.<BR>--ग्निः<BR>Morbidly rapid digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यग्निष्टोमः|अत्यग्निष्टोम
अत्यग्निष्टोमः [अतिक्रांतोऽग्निष्टोमं<BR>अधिकफलदत्वात्] The optional second<BR>part of the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यंकुश|अत्यङ्कुश
अत्यंकुश a. [अंकुशमतिक्रांतः] Past<BR>the goad, uncontrollable,<BR>unmanageable; ˚शमिवोद्दामं गजं Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यध्वन्
अत्यध्वन् m. A long or wearisome<BR>travelling; a long journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यंत|अत्यन्त|अत्यन्तं|अत्यन्तः
अत्यंत a. [अतिक्रांतः अंतं सीमां नाशं]<BR>1 Excessive, much, very great or<BR>strong; ˚वैरं great enmity; ˚मैत्री;<BR>˚हिमोत्किरानिलाः Ku. 5. 26.<BR>--2<BR>Complete, perfect, absolute; ˚अभावः<BR>absolute non-existence; See<BR>below.<BR>--3 Endless, perpetual,<BR>permanent, everlasting, uninterrupted,<BR>unbroken; किं वा तवात्यंतवियोगमोघे<BR>हतजीविते R. 14. 65; भवत्यजरमत्यंतं<BR>Pt. 1. 151; ˚तं सुखमश्नुते Ms. 5. 46;<BR>Bg. 6. 28; कस्यात्यंतं सुखमुपनतं<BR>Me. 109; नायमत्यंतसंवासो लभ्यते येन<BR>केनचित् H. 4. 73.<BR>--तं ind.<BR>1<BR>Exceedingly, excessively, very much, to<BR>the highest degree; स्थायीभवति<BR>चात्यंतं रागः शुक्लपटे यथा Pt. 1. 33;<BR>˚शिशु Mu. 4. 14 very young.<BR>--2 For<BR>ever, to the end (of life), through<BR>life; अत्यंतमात्मसदृशेक्षणवल्लभाभिराहो<BR>निवत्स्यति Ś. 1. 27 for all time,<BR>in perpetuity; सा चात्यंतमदर्शनं<BR>नयनयोर्याता V. 4. 2.; oft in comp.;<BR>˚गता See below; प्रियमत्यंतविलुप्तदर्शनं<BR>Ku. 4. 2 for ever lost to view;<BR>R. 14. 49.<BR>--3 Absolutely, perfectly,<BR>completely.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभावः<BR>absolute or complete non-existence,<BR>absolute non-entity, a thing which<BR>does not exist at any one of the<BR>three periods of time, or does not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-c" target="_blank">Page0037-c+ 58</a>]<BR>exist for all time;<BR>त्रैकालिकसंसर्गावच्छिन्नप्रतियोगिकः. (This is considered to<BR>be नित्य or eternal and different<BR>from the other kinds of अभाव).<BR>--ग<BR>a. going or walking too much or<BR>too fast.<BR>--गत a. gone or departed<BR>for ever, gone never to return;<BR>कथमत्यंतगता न मां दहेः R. 8. 56. {2} always<BR>applicable, perfectly intimate or<BR>pertinent.<BR>--गतिः f. {1} sense of<BR>‘completely’; अनत्यंतगतौ क्तात् P. V. 4. 4. {2}<BR>completion, accomplishment.<BR>--गामिन् a. {1} going or walking very much,<BR>going too fast or quickly. {2}<BR>excessive, much.<BR>--निवृत्तिः f. complete<BR>disappearance, absolute cessation.<BR>--वासिन् m. [वस्-णिनि] one who<BR>constantly stays with his preceptor, as<BR>a student.<BR>--संयोगः close proximity,<BR>uninterrupted continuity;<BR>कालाध्वनोरत्यंतसंयोगे P. II. 1. 29. {2}<BR>Inseparable coexistence.<BR>--संपर्कः excessive<BR>sexual intercourse.<BR>--सुकुमार a. very<BR>tender.<BR>--(रः) a kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यंतिक|अत्यन्तिक|अत्यन्तिकः
अत्यंतिक a. [अत्यंतं गच्छति;<BR>अत्यंतठन्]<BR>1 Going too much or too fast.<BR>--2 Very near.<BR>--3 Not near, distant.<BR>--कं [अतिशयितं अंतिकं नैकट्यं]<BR>1 Close<BR>proximity, immediate<BR>neighbourhood or being in close proximity.<BR>--2 [अतिक्रांतं अंतिकं] Great distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यंतीन|अत्यन्तीन|अत्यन्तीनः
अत्यंतीन a. [अत्यंतं गामी अत्यंतीनः,<BR>भृशं गंता; अत्यंत-ख P. V. 2. 11]<BR>Going or walking too much, going too<BR>fast (अत्यंतगमनशील); लक्ष्मीं परंपरीणां<BR>त्वमत्यंतीनत्वमुन्नय Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यम्ल|अत्यम्लं|अत्यम्लः
अत्यम्ल a. [अतिशयितोम्लो<BR>रसःफलपत्रादौ यस्य] Very acid or sour.<BR>--म्लः N.<BR>of a tree, Spondias Mangifera.<BR>--म्ला,<BR>˚पर्णी A species of citron (वनबीजपूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यय|अत्ययः
अत्यय, अत्ययिक &c. See under<BR>अती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्ययिक
अत्यय, अत्ययिक &c. See under<BR>अती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यर्थ|अत्यर्थं
अत्यर्थ a. [अतिक्रांतः अर्थं<BR>अनुरूपस्वरूपं] Beyond the proper worth or<BR>measure, excessive, very great,<BR>intense, exorbitant; ˚तापात् M. 2. 13<BR>--र्थं adv. Very much, exceedingly,<BR>excessively; अत्यर्थं परदास्यमेत्य निपुणं<BR>नीतौ मनो दीयते Mu. 2. 5; प्रियो हि<BR>ज्ञानिनोत्यर्थमहं स च मम प्रियः Bg. 7. 17;<BR>oft. in comp.; ˚संपीडितः Ś. 7. 11<BR>excessively pinched; ˚क्रुद्ध, ˚तृषित &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यवि
अत्यवि a. Ved. Passing over or<BR>through the sieve or strainer<BR>(epithet of Soma.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यष्टिः|अत्यष्टि
अत्यष्टिः f. [अतिक्रांता अष्टिं<BR>षोडशाक्षरपादां वृत्तिं एकाक्षराधिक्यात्] A metre of 4<BR>lines, each containing 17 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यह्न
अत्यह्न a. [अतिक्रांतमहः]<BR>Exceeding a day in duration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याकारः|अत्याकार
अत्याकारः [अतिशयितः आकारः<BR>तिरस्कारः]<BR>1 Contempt, blame, censure;<BR>श्लाघात्याकारतदवेतेषु P. V. 1. 134.<BR>--2<BR>Bigness of person, a very large body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याक्रम्
अत्याक्रम् = आक्रम् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याचार|अत्याचारं|अत्याचारः
अत्याचार a. [आचारमतिक्रांतः]<BR>Deviating from established usages or<BR>customs, negligent.<BR>--रः Performance<BR>of works not sanctioned by usage<BR>(अनुचिताचरणं); irreligious conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यादित्य
अत्यादित्य a. Surpassing the<BR>(lustre of the) sun; अत्यादित्यं<BR>हुतवहमुखे संभृतं तद्धि तेजः Me. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यानंदा|अत्यानन्दा
अत्यानंदा Morbid indifference to<BR>the pleasures of sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याधानं|अत्याधान
अत्याधानं<BR>1 Laying on,<BR>imposition.<BR>--2 Transgression.<BR>--3 Violation of<BR>आधान, not keeping the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याय|अत्यायः
अत्याय a. [इ or अय्-घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Transgressing.<BR>--2 Past going time.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>Transgression, violation.<BR>--2 Excess.<BR>--3 Great gain or profit (अतिशयितोलाभः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यायु
अत्यायु n. [अति-आ-या-कु] A<BR>kind of sacrificial vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यारूढ
अत्यारूढ a. Grown to excess; ˚ढो<BR>हि नारीणामकालज्ञो मनोभवः R. 12. 33.<BR>--ढं, --ढिः f. A very high position, great<BR>elevation or rise; अत्यारूढिर्भवति<BR>महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा Ś. 4. v. {1}; अत्यारूढं<BR>रिपोः सोढं चंदनेनेव भोगिनः R. 10. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यालः|अत्याल
अत्यालः [अतिशयेन समंतात् अलति<BR>पर्याप्नोति; अति-आ-अल्-अच्] N. of a plant<BR>रक्तचित्रक Plumbago Rosea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यासः|अत्यास
अत्यासः [अति-अस्-घञ्]<BR>Allowing to pass, only in acc. sing. as णमुल्;<BR>द्व्यहात्यासं or द्व्यहमत्यासं गाः पाययति<BR>P. III. 4. 57 after an interval of 2 days<BR>(अद्य पाययित्वा द्व्यहमतिक्रम्य पुनः पाययति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्याहितं|अत्याहित
अत्याहितं [आधा-आधारे क्त,<BR>अत्यंतमाधीयते तन्निवारणार्थं मनो दीयते यस्मिन् Tv.]<BR>1<BR>A great calamity, danger or evil,<BR>misfortune, mishap, accident; न<BR>किमप्यत्याहितं Ś. 1, किं अत्याहितं सीतादेव्याः; -न<BR>केवलं ˚तं सापवादमपि U. 2; मया<BR>˚तमुपलब्धं V. 4; किमिदमुच्चैरत्याहितं Mv. 6;<BR>श्रुतमत्याहितं M. 4 evil or evil news;<BR>oft. as an exclamation, ‘Ah, me!’<BR>‘alas! alas!’, ‘how bad it is!’<BR>Māl. 3, 7; V. 5.<BR>--2 A rash or<BR>daring deed (जीवानपेक्षिकर्म);<BR>अत्याहितं किमपि राक्षसकर्म कुर्यात् Mv. 4. 50<BR>rash and demoniacal deed; पांडुपुत्रैर्न<BR>किमप्यत्याहितमाचेष्टितं भवेत् Ve. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्ता
अत्युक्ता --क्था [उक्ता-क्था<BR>एकाक्षरपादा वृत्तिः, तां अतिक्रांता] N. of a class of<BR>metres of 4 lines, each of 2 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्था
अत्युक्ता --क्था [उक्ता-क्था<BR>एकाक्षरपादा वृत्तिः, तां अतिक्रांता] N. of a class of<BR>metres of 4 lines, each of 2 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युक्तिः|अत्युक्ति
अत्युक्तिः f. Exaggeration,<BR>hyperbole, over-drawn or coloured<BR>description; अत्युक्तौ न यदि प्रकुप्यसि<BR>मृषावादं च नो मन्यसे । Udbhaṭa. See<BR>अतिशयोक्ति also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युग्र
अत्युग्र a. Very fierce.<BR>--ग्रं Asa<BR>fœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्युपध
अत्युपध a. [उपधां अतिक्रांतः] Above<BR>guiles, trustworthy, tried; अमात्ये<BR>चात्युपधे Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूमशा
अत्यूमशा ind. [ऊर्यादिगण] A<BR>particle of abuse, occurring in comp.<BR>with भू, कृ or अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूर्मि
अत्यूर्मि a. Ved. Overflowing or<BR>bubbling over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्यूहः|अत्यूह
अत्यूहः [अतिशयेन ऊहः तर्कः]<BR>1<BR>Close or deep meditation or<BR>thinking; earnest reasoning.<BR>--2 [अतिशयेन<BR>ऊहते शब्दायते; अति-ऊह्-अच्] A gallinule<BR>(दात्यूह).<BR>--हा A plant (नीलिका)<BR>Nyctanthes Tristis, or Jasminum Villosum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र (अत्रा Ved.) ind. [अस्मिन्<BR>एतस्मिन् वा, इदं-एतद्वा सप्तम्याः त्रल् प्रकृतेः<BR>अश्भावश्च Tv.]<BR>1 In this place, here;<BR>अपि संनिहितोऽत्र कुलपतिः Ś. 1.; अत्र<BR>गृह्यते अत्र गृह्यते K. 119 here-here i. e.<BR>just now.<BR>--2 In this respect, matter,<BR>or case; as to this, (serving the<BR>purpose of अस्मिन् विषये or of the forms<BR>अस्मिन् or एतस्मिन्, अस्यां &c. with a<BR>substantive or adjectival force); अहिंसा<BR>परमो धर्म इत्यत्र ऐकमत्यं H. 1; अलं प्रयत्नेन<BR>तवात्र R. 3. 50; भवंतमेवात्र गुरुलाघवं<BR>पृच्छामि Ś. 5; तदत्र परिगतार्थं कृत्वा Ś. 6<BR>informing him of this matter.<BR>--3<BR>There, in that direction.<BR>--4 Then,<BR>at that time (Ved.); कः कोत्र भोः who<BR>is there? which of the servants is<BR>in attendance? who waits there?<BR>(used in calling out to one's<BR>servants &c.; cf. Hindustāni ko hai).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरे adv. in the mean while,<BR>meantime Ś. 3. 11.<BR>--दघ्न a. (घ्नी f.)<BR>reaching so far up; as tall as this.<BR>--भवत् (m. भवान्) an honorific epithet<BR>meaning ‘worthy’, ‘revered’,<BR>‘honourable’, ‘your or his honour’, and<BR>referring to a person that is present<BR>or near the speaker, (opp. तत्रभवत्);<BR>˚भवती f. ‘your or her ladyship’ (<BR>पूज्ये तत्रभवानत्रभवांश्च भगवानपि); अत्रभवान्<BR>प्रकृतिमापन्नः Ś. 2; वृक्षसेचनादेव<BR>परिश्रांतामत्रभवतीं लक्षये Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रत्य
अत्रत्य a. [अत्र भवो जातः<BR>एतत्स्थानसंबद्धो वा; अत्र-त्यप्]<BR>1 Belonging to,<BR>or connected with, this place;<BR>दौरात्म्याद्रक्षसस्तां तु नात्रत्याः श्रद्दधुः प्रजाः<BR>R. 15. 72.<BR>--2 Produced or found<BR>here, of this place, local.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्र|अत्रः
अत्र a. Ved. Not giving or<BR>enjoying protection.<BR>--त्रः Ved. [<BR>अद्त्रन्] An eater, devourer; a demon,<BR>Rākṣasa.<BR>--त्रं Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रप
अत्रप a. [न. ब.] Shameless,<BR>impudent, immodest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रवस्
अत्रवस् ind. The year before<BR>last (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रस्त
अत्रस्त, अत्रास, --त्रस्नु a. [न. त.]<BR>Not afraid, fearless;<BR>जुगोपात्मानमत्रस्तः R. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रास
अत्रस्त, अत्रास, --त्रस्नु a. [न. त.]<BR>Not afraid, fearless;<BR>जुगोपात्मानमत्रस्तः R. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रस्नु
अत्रस्त, अत्रास, --त्रस्नु a. [न. त.]<BR>Not afraid, fearless;<BR>जुगोपात्मानमत्रस्तः R. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रि|अत्रिः
अत्रि a. [properly अत्त्रि, Uṇ. 4. 68,<BR>अदेस्त्रिनिश्च, अद्-त्रिन्] Devourer;<BR>Rv. 2. 8. 5.<BR>--त्रिः N. of a celebrated sage<BR>and author of many Vedic hymns.<BR>[He appears in the Vedas in hymns<BR>addressed to Agni, Indra, the Aśvins<BR>and the Viśvedevas. In the<BR>Svāyambhuva Manvantara he appears as one<BR>of the ten Prajāpatis or mind-born sons<BR>of Brahmā, being born from his eye.<BR>These sons having died by the curse of<BR>Śiva, Brahmā performed a sacrifice, at<BR>the beginning of the present Vaivasvata<BR>Manvantara, and Atri was born from<BR>the flames of Agni. Anasūyā was his<BR>wife in both lives. In the first she bore<BR>him three sons, Datta, Durvāsas and<BR>Soma; in the second she had two<BR>additional children, a son by name<BR>Aryaman and a daughter called Amalā. In<BR>the Rāmāyaṇa an account is given of<BR>the visit paid by Rāma and Sītā to Atri<BR>and Anasūyā in their hermitage, when<BR>they both received them most kindly;<BR>See Anasūyā. As a Ṛṣi or sage he is one<BR>of the seven sages who were all sons of<BR>Brahmā, and represents in Astronomy<BR>one of the stars of the Great Bear<BR>situated in the north. He is also the author<BR>of a code of laws known as अत्रिस्मृति or<BR>अत्रिसंहिता. In the Purāṇas he is said to<BR>have produced the moon from his eye,<BR>while he was practising austere penance,<BR>the moon being in consequence called<BR>अत्रिज, --जात, --दृग्ज, अत्रिनेत्रप्रसूत, --˚प्रभव,<BR>˚भव &c.; cf. also अथ नयनसमुत्थं<BR>ज्योतिरत्रेरिव द्यौः R. 2. 75 and अत्रेरिवेंदुः<BR>V. 5. 21.] --(pl.) descendants of Atri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्रिन्
अत्रिन् m. A devourer, a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्सरुकः|अत्सरुक
अत्सरुकः [नास्ति त्सरुर्यस्य] N. of<BR>a sacrificial vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथ
अथ (Ved. अथा) ind. [अर्थ्-ड, पृषोद˚<BR>रलोपः Tv.]<BR>1 A particle used at the<BR>beginning (of works) mostly as a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-a" target="_blank">Page0039-a+ 58</a>]<BR>sign of auspiciousness, and<BR>translated by ‘here,’ ‘now’ (begins) (मंगल,<BR>आरंभ, अधिकार). (Properly speaking<BR>‘auspiciousness’ or मंगल is not the<BR>sense of अथ, but the very utterance<BR>or hearing of the word is<BR>considered to be indicative of<BR>auspiciousness, as the word is supposed to<BR>have emanated from the throat of<BR>Brahmā: ओंकारश्चाथ शब्दश्च द्वावेतौ<BR>ब्रह्मणः पुरा । कंठं भित्त्वा विनिर्यातौ तेन<BR>मांगलिकावुभौ ॥ and therefore we find<BR>in Śaṅkara Bhāṣya अर्थांतरप्रयुक्तः<BR>अथशब्दः श्रुत्या मंगलमारचयति); अथ निर्वचनं;<BR>अथ योगानुशासनं; अथेदंप्रारभ्यते द्वितीयं<BR>तंत्रं Pt. 2. (usually followed by इति at<BR>the end, इति प्रथमोंकः here ends &c.).<BR>--2<BR>Then, afterwards (आनंतर्य) अथ<BR>प्रजानामधिपः प्रभाते वनाय धेनुं मुमोच R. 2. 1; often<BR>as a correlative of यदि or चेत्; न<BR>चेन्मुनिकुमारोयं अथ कोस्य व्यपदेशः Ś. 7;<BR>मुहूर्तादुपरि उपाध्यायश्चेदागच्छेत् अथ त्वं<BR>छंदो ऽधीष्व P. III. 3. 9. Sk.<BR>--3 If,<BR>supposing, now if, in case, but if<BR>(पक्षांतर); अथ कौतुकमावेदयामि K. 144,<BR>Ś. 5. 27; अथ मरणमवश्यमेव जंतोः<BR>किमिति मुधा मलिनं यशः कुरुध्वे Ve. 3. 4;<BR>अथ गृह्णाति Ś. 7; Ku. 5. 45; Mu. 3. 25;<BR>Ki. 1. 44; अथ चास्तमिता त्वमात्मना<BR>R. 8. 51 while, but, on the other<BR>hand; oft. followed by ततः or<BR>तथापि, Bg. 12. 9, 11; 2. 26; अथ चेत् but if<BR>Bg. 2. 33; 18. 58.<BR>--4 And, so also, as<BR>also, likewise (समुच्चय); गणितमथ कलां<BR>वैशिकीं Mk. 1. 3; Ms. 2. 1. 31; भीमोऽ<BR>थार्जुनः G. M.<BR>--5 Used in asking or<BR>introducing questions (प्रश्न), oft.<BR>with the interrogative word itself;<BR>अथ सा तत्रभवती किमाख्यस्य राजर्षेः<BR>पत्नी Ś. 7; अर्थवान् खलु मे राजशब्दः । अथ<BR>भगवाँल्लोकानुग्रहाय कुशली काश्यपः Ś. 5;<BR>अथ शक्नोषि भोक्तुं G. M.; अथात्रभवती<BR>कथमित्थंभूता M. 5; Bg. 3. 36; अथ<BR>भवंतमंतरेण कीदृशो ऽस्या दृष्टिरागः Ś. 2;<BR>अथ माठव्यं प्रति किमेवं प्रयुक्तं Ś. 6 (अथ<BR>may in these two sentences mean<BR>‘but’).<BR>--6 Totality, entirety (कार्त्स्न्य);<BR>अथ धर्मं व्याख्यास्यामः G. M. we shall<BR>explain the whole धर्म (धर्म in all its<BR>details.).<BR>--7 Doubt, uncertainty (संशय,<BR>विकल्प); शब्दोनित्यो ऽथानित्यः G. M. The<BR>senses of अथ usually given by<BR>lexicographers are:<BR>--अथोथ स्यातां समुच्चये ।<BR>मंगले संशयारंभाधिकारानंतरेषु च । अन्वादेशे<BR>प्रतिज्ञायां प्रश्नसाकल्ययोरपि ॥ Some of these<BR>senses are indentical with those in (1),<BR>while some are not in general use.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपि moreover, and again<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">Page0039-b+ 59</a>]<BR>&c. (= अथ in most cases); ˚च likewise,<BR>also.<BR>--किं what else, yes, exactly<BR>so, quite so, certainly; सर्वथा<BR>अप्सरःसंभवैषा । अथ किं Ś. 1; अपि वृषलमनुरक्ताः<BR>प्रकृतयः अथ किं Mu. 1.<BR>--वा {1} or (used<BR>like the English disjunctive<BR>conjunction ‘or’ and occupying the same<BR>place); व्यवहारं परिज्ञाय वध्यः पूज्योऽ<BR>थवा भवेत् H. 1. 58; समस्तैरथवा पृथक्<BR>Ms. 7. 198; अथवा-अथवा either-or;<BR>वाथ is often used in the same sense<BR>with वा; कार्तिके वाथ चैत्रे वा Pt. 3. 38;<BR>Ms. 7. 182; अथापि वा also used in the<BR>same sense; एतदेव व्रतं<BR>कुर्युश्चांद्रायणमथापि वा 11. 118; 8. 287. {2} or rather,<BR>or why, or perhaps, is it not so<BR>(correcting or modifying a previous<BR>statement); why should there be any<BR>thought or hesitation about it, or<BR>it is no wonder; अपि नाम<BR>कुलपतेरियमसवर्णक्षेत्रसंभवा स्यात् । अथवा कृतं संदेहेन<BR>Ś. 1., 1. 16; गमिष्याम्युपहास्यतां…<BR>अथवा कृतवाग्द्वारे वंशे ऽस्मिन् R. 1. 3-4;<BR>अथवा मृदुवस्तु हिंसितुं 8. 45; दीर्ये किं न<BR>सहस्रधाहमथवा रामेण किं दुष्करं U. 6. 40;<BR>अधोधो गंगेयं पदमुपगता स्तोकमथवा ।<BR>विवेकभ्रष्टानां भवति विनिपातः शतमुखः Bh. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथो
अथो = अथ in most senses; अथो<BR>वयस्यां परिपार्श्ववर्तिनीं… ऐक्षत Ku. 5. 51;<BR>स्त्रियो रत्नान्यथो विद्या Ms. 2. 240,<BR>3. 202, Bg. 4. 35, Ki. 5. 16, 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथरिः|अथरि
अथरिः --री Ved. m. f. A finger;<BR>finger-like or pointed flame (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथरी
अथरिः --री Ved. m. f. A finger;<BR>finger-like or pointed flame (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्यति
अथर्यति Den. P. To go constantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्य
अथर्य --र्यु a. Ved. Moving<BR>constantly, tremulous (गमनशील)<BR>Rv. 7. 1. 1; pointed like a lance, lambent (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्यु
अथर्य --र्यु a. Ved. Moving<BR>constantly, tremulous (गमनशील)<BR>Rv. 7. 1. 1; pointed like a lance, lambent (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वः|अथर्व|अथर्व्व
अथर्वः = अथर्वन् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वणः|अथर्वण|अथर्व्वण|अथर्व्वणः
अथर्वणः [अथर्वा तदुक्तविद्या अस्त्यस्य<BR>ज्ञातृत्वात् अच् न टिलोपः]<BR>1 Śiva.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>the Atharvaveda, See below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वन्|अथर्व्वन्
अथर्वन् m. [अथ-ऋ-वनिप् शकंध्वादि˚<BR>Tv.; probably connected with some<BR>word like athar fire]<BR>1 A priest<BR>who has to worship fire and Soma.<BR>--2 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--3 N. of the priest<BR>who is said to have first brought<BR>down fire from the heaven, offered<BR>Soma and recited prayers. [He is<BR>represented as the eldest son of Brahmā,<BR>sprung from his mouth; as a Prajāpati<BR>appointed by Brahmā to create and<BR>protect subordinate beings, who first<BR>learnt from Brahmā and then taught<BR>the Brahma-vidya and is considered to<BR>be the author of the Veda called after<BR>him. His wife was Śānti, daughter of<BR>Kardama Prajāpati. He had also<BR>another wife called Citti; he is also<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-c" target="_blank">Page0039-c+ 60</a>]<BR>considered identical with Aṅgiras and father<BR>of Agni.]<BR>--4 Epithet of Śiva,<BR>Vasiṣṭha. --(pl.) Descendants of<BR>Atharvan; hymns of this Veda; जिष्णुं<BR>जैत्रैरथर्वभिः R. 17. 13.<BR>--र्वा-र्व m. n., ˚वेदः<BR>The Atharvaveda, regarded as the<BR>fourth Veda. [It contains many forms<BR>of imprecations for the destruction of<BR>enemies and also contains a great<BR>number of prayers for safety and<BR>averting mishaps, evils, sins or calamities,<BR>and a number of hymns, as in the<BR>other Vedas, addressed to the gods<BR>with prayers to be used at religious<BR>and solemn rites; cf. Mv. 2. 24<BR>मूर्तिमभिरामघोरां बिभ्रदिवाथर्वणो निगमः. It has nine<BR>Śākhās and five Kalpas, and is comprised<BR>in 20 Kāṇḍas. The most important<BR>Brāhmaṇa belonging to this Veda is the<BR>Gopatha-Brāhmaṇa, and the Upaniṣads<BR>pertaining to it are stated to be 52, or,<BR>according to another account, 31.] [cf.<BR>Zend atharvan, Pers. āturbān.]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः N. of बुध<BR>Mercury (सामवेदाधिपो भौमः शशिजो ऽ<BR>थर्ववेदराट्).<BR>--निधिः, --विद् m. receptacle<BR>of the (knowledge of)<BR>Atharvaveda, or conversant with it;<BR>गुरुणाऽथर्वविदा कृतक्रियः R. 8. 4, 1. 59; (<BR>अथर्वविधिपदेन<BR>दुरितोपशमननिमित्तशांतिकपौष्टिकप्रवीणत्वं पौरोहित्योचितत्वं द्योत्यते Malli.)<BR>--भूताः (pl.) those who have<BR>become Atharvans, N. of the 12<BR>Maharshis.<BR>--शिखा, --शिरस् n. [अथर्वणो<BR>वेदस्य शिखा शिर इव वा<BR>ब्रह्मविद्याप्रतिपादकत्वेन श्रेष्ठत्वात्] N. of an Upaniṣad<BR>dealing with Brahmavidyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वणिः|अथर्वणि|अथर्व्वणि|अथर्व्वणिः
अथर्वणिः [अथर्वणि तदुक्तशांत्यादौ वा<BR>कुशलः, इस् सित्त्वेन भत्वाभावात् न टिलोपः Tv.]<BR>1 A Brāhmaṇa versed in this Veda;<BR>or skilled in the performance of the<BR>rites enjoined by it.<BR>--2 A family<BR>priest (पुरोधस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वांगिरस्|अथर्वाङ्गिरस्
अथर्वांगिरस् m. A member of the<BR>class of this name. --(pl.)<BR>1<BR>Descendants of Atharvan and of<BR>Angiras.<BR>--2 N. of the hymns of the<BR>Atharvaveda; दंडनीत्यां च<BR>कुशलमथर्वांगिरसे तथा Y. 1. 312.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वांगिरस|अथर्वाङ्गिरस|अथर्वाङ्गिरसः
अथर्वांगिरस a. (सी f.) Connected<BR>with अथर्वांगिरस्.<BR>--सं Office of this<BR>person.<BR>--साः Hymns of this Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वाणं|अथर्वाण|अथर्वाणः
अथर्वाणं Ritual of the<BR>Atharvaveda.<BR>--णः, --˚विद् One studying or<BR>versed in this Veda or the ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथर्वी
अथर्वी a. Ved. [न थुर्व्-अच्, पृषो˚<BR>उलोपः गौरा˚--ङीष् Tv.] Not injuring or<BR>hurting, not destructive; pierced by<BR>a lance (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथवा
अथवा, अथो See under अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अथो
अथवा, अथो See under अथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्
अद् {c2c} P. [अत्ति, आद, --जघास, अघसत्,<BR>अत्स्यति, अत्तुं, अन्न, -जग्ध, जग्ध्वा]<BR>1 To<BR>eat, devour.<BR>--2 To destroy.<BR>--3 = अंद्, q. v.<BR>--Caus. To feed with, cause to eat;<BR>आदयत्यन्नं बटुना Sk. --Desid. जिघत्सति<BR>To wish to eat. [cf. L. edo, Gr.<BR>edo, Germ. essen, Eng. eat; Lith.<BR>edmi, Sans. admi, Goth. at, Zend<BR>ad]. With अव to satisfy by food, get<BR>rid of with feeding; (fig.) stop the<BR>mouth of.<BR>--आ to eat &c.<BR>--प्र --सं<BR>to use up, consume, devour;<BR>समदंत्यामिषं खगाः Bk. 18. 12.<BR>--वि to gnaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अत्तृ
अत्तृ a. [अद्-तृच्] One who eats;<BR>अरक्षितारमत्तारं नृपं विद्यादधोगतिं<BR>Ms. 8. 309.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्
अद् --द a. (at the end of comp.)<BR>Eating, devouring; मांसाद<BR>carnivorous, feeding on flesh; so मत्स्य˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद|अदः
अद् --द a. (at the end of comp.)<BR>Eating, devouring; मांसाद<BR>carnivorous, feeding on flesh; so मत्स्य˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदंष्ट्र|अदंष्ट्रः
अदंष्ट्र a. [न. ब.] Toothless.<BR>--ष्ट्रः<BR>A serpent without teeth; one whose<BR>fangs have been taken out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिण
अदक्षिण a. [न. त.]<BR>1 Not right,<BR>left.<BR>--2 [न. ब.] Not bringing in<BR>Dakṣiṇā to the priests; without<BR>any gifts (as a sacrifice); मृतो<BR>यज्ञस्त्वदक्षिणः Pt. 2. 94.<BR>--3 Simple,<BR>weakminded, silly; मेनेऽथ सत्यमेवेति<BR>परिहासमदक्षिणा Rām.<BR>--4 Not handy,<BR>skilful or clever; awkward.<BR>--5<BR>Unfavourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिणीय
अदक्षिणीय --दक्षिण्य a. Not deserving<BR>Dakṣiṇā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदक्षिण्य
अदक्षिणीय --दक्षिण्य a. Not deserving<BR>Dakṣiṇā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदग्ध
अदग्ध a. Not burnt; not burnt<BR>according to the rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदंड|अदण्ड
अदंड a. [न. ब.] Free or exempt<BR>from punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदंड्य|अदण्ड्य
अदंड्य a.<BR>1 Not deserving<BR>punishment; अदंड्यान् दंडयन् राजा<BR>दंड्यांश्चैवाप्यदंडयन् Y. 2.<BR>--2 Exempt or free from<BR>punishment; नादंड्यो नाम राज्ञोस्ति यः<BR>स्वधर्मे न तिष्ठति Ms. 8. 335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्|अदन्त्
अदत् a. Toothless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्त|अदत्तं
अदत्त a.<BR>1 Not given.<BR>--2<BR>Unjustly or improperly given.<BR>--3 Not<BR>given in marriage.<BR>--4 Not having<BR>given any thing.<BR>--त्ता An<BR>unmarried girl.<BR>--त्तं A gift which is null<BR>and void (having been given under<BR>particular circumstances which make<BR>it revocable).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आदायिन् a.<BR>the receiver of such a gift; one who<BR>takes what has not been given away,<BR>such as a thief; अदत्तादायिनो हस्ताल्लिप्सेत<BR>ब्राह्मणो धनं । याजनाध्यापनेनापि यथा स्तेनस्तथैव<BR>सः ॥<BR>--पूर्वा Not affianced or<BR>betrothed before; अदत्तपूर्वेत्याशंक्यते Māl. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदत्र
अदत्र a. [अद्-वा˚ अत्रन्] Ved. Fit<BR>to be eaten; अदत्रया दयते वार्याणि<BR>Rv. 5. 49. 3 (= अदनीयानि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदद्र्यंच्|अदद्र्यञ्च्
अदद्र्यंच्^1 [अमुं अंचति<BR>अदस्-अंच् क्विप् अद्र्यागमः^2 P. VIII. 2. 80-81]<BR>Going to that, tending to that.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by @aumsanskrit on 20251225. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/104  ap90. note: headword change.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by @aumsanskrit on 20251225. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/104  ap90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदंत|अदन्त|अदन्तः
अदंत a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Toothless.<BR>--2<BR>Not yet having the teeth formed<BR>or grown (said of young ones of<BR>men or animals before the teething<BR>time).<BR>--3 Ending in अत् or अ.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A leech.<BR>--2 N. of Pūṣan, one<BR>of the 12 Ādityas, he having lost<BR>his teeth at the destruction of<BR>Dakṣa's sacrifice by Vīrabhadra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदंत्य|अदन्त्य
अदंत्य a.<BR>1 Not dental.<BR>--2 Not fit<BR>for the teeth; injurious to them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदब्ध
अदब्ध, --दंभ a. [न. त.] Ved.<BR>Unbroken or unimpaired, unhurt,<BR>uninjured; pure, true; ˚असु, or ˚आयुः<BR>having uninjured or pure life;<BR>leaving uninjured the man who<BR>sacrifices; ˚धीति, ˚व्रत whose works or<BR>religious observances are unimpaired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदंभ|अदम्भ|अदम्भः
अदब्ध, --दंभ a. [न. त.] Ved.<BR>Unbroken or unimpaired, unhurt,<BR>uninjured; pure, true; ˚असु, or ˚आयुः<BR>having uninjured or pure life;<BR>leaving uninjured the man who<BR>sacrifices; ˚धीति, ˚व्रत whose works or<BR>religious observances are unimpaired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदभ्र|अदभ्रः
अदभ्र a. [दंभ्-रक्, न. त.] Not<BR>scanty, plentiful, copious;<BR>अदभ्रदर्भामधिशय्य स स्थलीं Ki. 1. 38; ˚अभ्रनिर्घोष<BR>Dk. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदंभ|अदम्भ|अदम्भः
अदंभ a. Honest, undeceitful.<BR>--भः<BR>1 Honesty, absence of deceit.<BR>--2<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदय
अदय [न. ब.] Merciless,<BR>unkind, cruel.<BR>--यं ind. Mercilessly;<BR>ardently; fervently, closely (as an<BR>embrace) V. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदर्शः|अदर्श
अदर्शः<BR>1 Day of new moon.<BR>--2 A<BR>mirror (= आदर्श).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदर्शनं|अदर्शन
अदर्शनं<BR>1 Not seeing, non-vision;<BR>absence, not being seen;<BR>तमाहितौत्सुक्यमदर्शनेन R. 2. 73; अंतर्धौ<BR>येनादर्शनमिच्छति P. I. 4. 28 the person whose<BR>sight one wishes to avoid; ˚नं गतः<BR>Pt. 2; ˚नीभूतः Pt. 1 become invisible;<BR>अस्य ˚नं गत्वा Pt. 2 going out of his<BR>sight, beyond the reach of vision;<BR>सा चात्यंतमदर्शनं नयनयोर्याता V. 4. 2<BR>lost to view, become invisible.<BR>--2<BR>Neglect, or failure to see; ब्राह्मणादर्शनेन च<BR>Ms. 10. 43.<BR>--3 (Gram.)<BR>Disappearance, elision, omission; अदर्शनं लोपः<BR>P. I. 1. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदल|अदलः
अदल a.<BR>1 Leafless.<BR>--2 Without<BR>parts.<BR>--लः A plant (हिज्जल) Eugenia<BR>or Barringtonia Acutangula.<BR>--ला A<BR>plant (घृतकुमारी) Aloe Indica Royle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदस्
अदस् pron. a. [न दस्यते उत्क्षिप्यते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">Page0040-c+ 58</a>]<BR>अंगुलिर्यत्र इदंतया निर्द्धारणाय पुरोवर्तिनि<BR>एवांगुलिनिर्देशः संभवति नापुरोवर्तिनि, न-दस्-क्विप् Tv.]<BR>(असौ m. f., अदः n.). That, (referring<BR>to a person or thing not present or<BR>near the speaker) (विप्रकृष्ट or परोक्ष);<BR>इदमस्तु सन्निकृष्टं समीपतरवर्ति चैतदो रूपम् ।<BR>अदसस्तु विप्रकृष्टं तदिति परोक्षे विजानीयात् ॥<BR>अमुष्य विद्या रसनाग्रनर्तकी N. 1. 6.; असौ<BR>नामाऽहमस्मीति स्वनाम परिकीर्तयेत् ।<BR>Ms. 2. 122 I am that person, so and so<BR>(giving the name); असावहमिति<BR>ब्रूयात् 130, 216; Y. 1. 26. अदस् is,<BR>however, often used with reference<BR>to प्रत्यक्ष or सन्निकृष्ट objects &c. in the<BR>sense of ‘this here’, ‘yonder’;<BR>असौ शरण्यः शरणोन्मुखानां R. 6. 21 (<BR>असाविति पुरोवर्तिनो निर्देशः Malli.); अमी<BR>रथ्याः Ś. 1. 8.; अमी वह्नयः 4. 17,<BR>7. 11. It is often used in the sense of<BR>तत् as a correlative of यत्; हिंसारतश्च<BR>यो नित्यं नेहासौ सुखमेधते Ms. 4. 170 he<BR>who &c. But when it immediately<BR>follows the relative pronoun (योसौ,<BR>ये अमी &c.) it conveys the sense of<BR>प्रसिद्ध ‘well-known’, ‘celebrated’,<BR>‘renowned’; योसावतीद्रियग्राह्यः सूक्ष्मोऽ<BR>व्यक्तः सनातनः Ms. 1. 7; योसौ<BR>कुमारसेवको नाम Mu. 3; योसौ चोरः Dk. 68;<BR>sometimes अदस् used by itself<BR>conveys this sense; विधुरपि<BR>विधियोगाद्ग्रस्यते राहुणाऽसौ that (so well-known<BR>to us all) moon too. See the word<BR>तद् also and the quotations from K. P<BR>--ind. There, at that time, then, thus,<BR>ever; correlative to some pronominal<BR>forms; यदादः, यत्रादः whenever,<BR>whereever &c. By अदोऽनुपदेशे P. I. 4. 70<BR>अदस् has the force of a (गति)<BR>preposition when no direction to another<BR>is implied; अदः कृत्य अदः कृतं; । परं<BR>प्रत्युपदेशे तु अदः कृत्वा अदः कुरु । Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदस्यति
अदस्यति Den. P. To become that<BR>P. VIII. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदातृ
अदातृ a.<BR>1 Not giving, miserly;<BR>आदाननित्याच्चादातुः Ms. 11. 15 not<BR>liberal<BR>--2 Not giving (a daughter)<BR>in marriage; कालेऽदाता पिता वाच्यः<BR>Ms. 9. 4.<BR>--3 Not liable to payment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदादि
अदादि a. Having अद् at the head,<BR>a term used to mark roots of the<BR>second conjugation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदान
अदान a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Not giving,<BR>miserly.<BR>--2 Without rut (or not<BR>charitable); सदादानः परिक्षीणः शस्त<BR>एव करीश्वरः । अदानः पीनगात्रोपि निंद्य<BR>एव हि गर्दभः Pt. 2. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदान्य
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्,<BR>अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् a. Ved. Not giving,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">Page0041-a+ 57</a>]<BR>miserly, poor; irreligious, impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदायिन्
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्,<BR>अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् a. Ved. Not giving,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">Page0041-a+ 57</a>]<BR>miserly, poor; irreligious, impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदामन्
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्,<BR>अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् a. Ved. Not giving,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">Page0041-a+ 57</a>]<BR>miserly, poor; irreligious, impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाशु
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्,<BR>अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् a. Ved. Not giving,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">Page0041-a+ 57</a>]<BR>miserly, poor; irreligious, impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाशुरि
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्,<BR>अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् a. Ved. Not giving,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">Page0041-a+ 57</a>]<BR>miserly, poor; irreligious, impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाश्वस्
अदान्य, अदायिन्, अदामन्,<BR>अदाशु, अदाशुरि, -दाश्वस् a. Ved. Not giving,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">Page0041-a+ 57</a>]<BR>miserly, poor; irreligious, impious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाभ्य|अदाभ्यः
अदाभ्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Faithful, trusty.<BR>--2 Uninjured, unhurt.<BR>--3 Pure,<BR>undefiled.<BR>--4 Unapproachable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाय
अदाय a. [नास्ति दायो यस्य] Not<BR>entitled to a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदायाद
अदायाद a.<BR>1 Not entitled to be an<BR>heir; पुमान्दायादोऽदायादा स्त्री Nir.;<BR>कानीनश्च सहोढश्च क्रीतः पौनर्भवस्तथा ।<BR>स्वयंदत्तश्च शौद्रश्च षडदायादबांधवाः ॥<BR>Ms. 9. 160.<BR>--2 Destitute of heirs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदायिक
अदायिक a. (की f.) [दायमर्हति दाय-ठक्<BR>न. ब.]<BR>1 That which is not claimed<BR>by an heir; destitute of heirs;<BR>अदायिकं धनं राजगामि Kāty.<BR>--2 Not<BR>relating to inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदारः|अदार
अदारः [न. ब.]<BR>1 One who has<BR>no wife, a widower or bachelor.<BR>--2<BR>[न. त.] Not injuring or tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदासः|अदास
अदासः A free man; Ms. 10. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदाह्य
अदाह्य a.<BR>1 Incombustible.<BR>--2<BR>Not fit to be burnt on the funeral<BR>pile.<BR>--3 Not capable of being burnt,<BR>epithet of परमात्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदिक्क
अदिक्क a. Ved. Having no<BR>direction or region of the world for<BR>oneself; banished from beneath the sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदिति|अदितिः
अदिति a. [न दीयते खंड्यते बध्यते<BR>बृहत्त्वात्, दो-क्तिच्] Free, not tied;<BR>boundless, unlimited,<BR>inexhaustible; entire, unbroken; happy, pious<BR>(mostly Ved. in all these senses).<BR>--तिः [अत्ति प्राणिजातं; अद्-इतिच्]<BR>1<BR>Devourer i. e. death; यद्यदेवासृजत<BR>तत्तदत्तुमध्रियत, सर्वं वा अत्तीति तददितेरदितित्वं<BR>Bṛ. Ār. Up.<BR>--2 An epithet of God.<BR>--तिः<BR>f. [न दातुं शक्तिः]<BR>1 Inability to give,<BR>poverty.<BR>--2 [दातुं छेत्तुं अयोग्या] (a)<BR>The earth. (b) The goddess Aditi,<BR>mother of the Ādityas, in<BR>mythology represented as the mother of<BR>gods; see further on. (c) Freedom,<BR>security; boundlessness, immensity<BR>of space (opp. to the earth). (d)<BR>Inexhaustible abundance, perfection.<BR>(e) The lunar mansion called पुनर्वसु.<BR>(f) Speech; या प्राणेन<BR>संभवत्यदितिर्देवतामयी (शब्दादीनां अदनात् अदितिः Śaṅkara).<BR>(g) A cow. (h) Milk; wife (?).<BR>--ती<BR>(dual) Heaven and earth. [अदिति<BR>literally means ‘unbounded’, ‘the<BR>boundless Heaven,’ or, according to others,<BR>‘the visible infinite, the endless<BR>expanse beyond the earth, beyond<BR>the clouds, beyond the sky.’ According<BR>to Yāska अदितिरदीना देवमाता, and the<BR>verse beginning with अदितिर्द्यौः &c.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-b" target="_blank">Page0041-b+ 59</a>]<BR>Rv. 1. 89. 16 he interprets by taking अदिति to<BR>mean अदीन i. e. अनुपक्षीण, न ह्येषां<BR>क्षयोस्ति इति. In the Ṛgveda Aditi is<BR>frequently implored ‘for blessings on<BR>children and cattle, for protection and for<BR>forgiveness’. She is called ‘Devamātā’<BR>being strangely enough represented both<BR>as mother and daughter of Dakṣa. She<BR>had {8} sons; she approached the gods<BR>with 7 and cast away the 8th (Mārtaṇḍa,<BR>the sun.) In another place Aditi is<BR>addressed as ‘supporter of the sky,<BR>sustainer of the earth, sovereign of this<BR>world, wife of Viṣṇu’, but in the<BR>Mahābhārata, Rāmāyaṇa and Purāṇas,<BR>Viṣṇu is said to be the son of Aditi, one of<BR>the several daughters of Dakṣa and<BR>given in marriage to Kaśyapa by whom<BR>she was mother of Viṣṇu in his dwarf<BR>incarnation, and also of Indra, and she is<BR>called mother of gods and the gods her<BR>sons, ‘aditinandanas’; See Dakṣa and<BR>Kaśyapa also].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः, --नंदनः a<BR>god, divine being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीन
अदीन a. Not low or depressed,<BR>high-spirited; mighty, not poor;<BR>rich, happy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन्, --वृत्ति,<BR>--सत्त्व a. not depressed in spirit,<BR>highspirited, high-mettled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदीर्घ
अदीर्घ a. Not long.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सूत्र,<BR>--सूत्रिन् a. [न दीर्घं सूत्रं सूत्रवत् विस्तारो<BR>यस्य] quick, prompt in action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुःख
अदुःख a. [न. ब.] Free from evil,<BR>propitious.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नवमी the<BR>propitious 9th day in the bright half of<BR>भाद्रपद when women worship Devī to<BR>avert evil for the ensuing year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुच्छुन|अदुछुन
अदुच्छुन a. Ved. Free from evil,<BR>propitious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुर्ग
अदुर्ग a.<BR>1 Not inaccessible, not<BR>difficult of access.<BR>--2 Destitute of<BR>forts; ˚विषयः an unfortified country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदुर्मुख
अदुर्मुख a. Ved. Unremitting,<BR>zealous, cheerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदू
अदू a. Ved. Not zealous,<BR>dilatory; not worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूर
अदूर a. Not distant, near (in<BR>time or space); ˚वर्तिनीं सिद्धिं राजन्<BR>विगणयात्मनः R. 1. 87; ˚उज्झितवर्त्मसु<BR>मृगद्वंद्वेषु 1. 40; ˚त्रिंशाः Sk. not far<BR>from 30, i. e. nearly 30; ˚कोपा हि<BR>मुनिजनप्रकृतिः K. 142 easily<BR>provoked, irascible.<BR>--रं Proximity,<BR>vicinity; वसन्नदूरे किल चंद्रमौलेः R. 6. 34;<BR>त्रिंशतोऽदूरे वर्तंते इति अदूरत्रिंशाः Sk.;<BR>अदूरे, --रं, --रेण, --रतः --रात् (with gen. or<BR>abl.) not far from, at no great<BR>distance from; अदूरे प्रियासमागमं ते प्रेक्षे<BR>V. 3 not far distant, very near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदूषित
अदूषित a. Not vitiated,<BR>uncorrupted, unspoiled^1, irreproachable;<BR>˚धी possessing an uncorrupted soul.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by @aumsanskrit on 20251225. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/104  ap90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृप्त
अदृप्त a. Not proud, not vain;<BR>˚क्रतु not proud-minded, sober, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्
अदृश् a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Sightless,<BR>blind.<BR>--2 Not seeing, not perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृश्य|अदृश्यं
अदृश्य a.<BR>1 Invisible; किमपि<BR>भूतमदृश्यरूपं Ku. 4. 45.<BR>--2 Not capable of<BR>being seen, epithet of परमेश्वर.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करणं rendering invisible, a part<BR>of a conjurer's legerdemain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्ट|अदृष्टं|अदृष्टः
अदृष्ट a.<BR>1 Invisible, not seen; ˚पूर्व<BR>not seen before.<BR>--2 Not known or<BR>experienced, not felt; ˚विरहव्यथं<BR>H. 1. 145.<BR>--3 Unforeseen, not observed<BR>or thought of; unknown, unobserved.<BR>--4 Not permitted or sanctioned,<BR>illegal; न चादृष्टां (वृद्धिं) पुनर्हरेत्<BR>Ms. 8. 153.<BR>--ष्टः N. of some venomous<BR>substance or vermin.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 The<BR>invisible one.<BR>--2 Destiny, fate, luck<BR>(good or bad); दैवमिति यदपि कथयसि<BR>पुरुषगुणः सोप्यदृष्टाख्यः Pt. 5. 30.<BR>--3<BR>Virtue or vice as the eventual cause<BR>of pleasure or pain. (Fate is supposed<BR>to be the result of good or bad<BR>actions done in one state of existence<BR>and experienced in another, the<BR>performance of good deeds being<BR>rewarded with residence in Heaven, and of<BR>bad deeds, visited with<BR>condemnation to Hell; धर्माधर्मावदृष्टं स्यात् धर्मः<BR>स्वर्गादिसाधनम्… अधर्मो नरकादीनां हेतुर्निदितकर्मजः<BR>Bhāṣā P. 161-2. The Vedāntins do<BR>not recognize अदृष्ट or luck; तैर्हि कर्मणः<BR>सूक्ष्मावस्थापन्नसंस्कारविशेष एव<BR>अदृष्टस्थानीयत्वेनांगीक्रियते; अदृष्टं आत्मधर्म इति नैयायिका<BR>वैशेषिकादयश्च, सांख्यपातंजलास्तु बुद्धिधर्म<BR>इत्यभ्युपगच्छंति Tv.).<BR>--4 An unforeseen<BR>calamity or danger (such as from fire,<BR>water &c.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. [ब.]<BR>having a metaphysical or occult<BR>meaning, metaphysical; having an<BR>object not evident to the senses.<BR>--कर्मन् a. one who has had no practice<BR>or practical experience, not practical,<BR>inexperienced; कर्मस्वदृष्टकर्मा<BR>यःशास्त्रज्ञोपि विमुह्यति H. 3. 54.<BR>--नरः, --पुरुषः<BR>one of the 20 ways of peacemaking,<BR>in which no third person is seen,<BR>said of a treaty concluded by the<BR>parties themselves without a<BR>mediator H. 4. 119.<BR>--फल a. [ब.] that<BR>of which the consequences are not<BR>yet visible.<BR>--(लं) the (future)<BR>result of good or bad actions; the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-a" target="_blank">Page0042-a+ 56</a>]<BR>result or consequence hidden in the<BR>future.<BR>--हन् a. destroying<BR>poisonous vermin (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदृष्टिः|अदृष्टि
अदृष्टिः f. [विरुद्धा दृष्टिः]<BR>1 An evil or<BR>malicious eye, evil look, an angry<BR>or envious look.<BR>--2 Not being<BR>seen. --a. [न. ब.] Blind, sightless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेय
अदेय a. Not to be given; what<BR>cannot or ought not to be given<BR>away; अदेयमासीत्त्रयमेव भूपतेः<BR>R. 3. 16.<BR>--यं That which it is not<BR>right or necessary to give. Wife,<BR>sons, deposits, and a few other<BR>things belong to this class: अन्वाहितं<BR>याचितकमाधिः साधारणं च यत् । निक्षेपः<BR>पुत्रदाराश्च सर्वस्वं चान्वये सति ॥ आपत्स्वपि च<BR>कष्टासु वर्तमानेन देहिना । अदेयान्याहुराचार्या<BR>यच्चान्यस्मै प्रतिश्रुतम् ॥<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दानं<BR>an unlawful gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेव|अदेवः
अदेव a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Not god-like<BR>or divine, not pertaining to a deity.<BR>--2 Godless, impious, irreligious.<BR>--वः [न. त.] One who is not a god.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--त्र a. [न देवाः त्रायंते प्रीयंते<BR>अनेन, त्रै करणे क] not gratifying the<BR>gods, such as food.<BR>--मातृक a. [न देवो<BR>मेघो माता वृष्टिकारकः यस्य] not rained<BR>upon; (lit.) not having the god of rain<BR>as mother to suckle or water; hence<BR>(artificially) supplied with the water<BR>of rivers, canals &c., irrigated;<BR>वितन्वति क्षेममदेवमातृकाश्चिराय<BR>तस्मिन्कुरवश्चकासते Ki. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवयत्|अदेवयन्त्
अदेवयत् --यु a. [न देवं याति प्राप्नोति]<BR>Not reaching the gods by prayers,<BR>impious, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेवयु
अदेवयत् --यु a. [न देवं याति प्राप्नोति]<BR>Not reaching the gods by prayers,<BR>impious, irreligious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेशः|अदेश
अदेशः [न. त.]<BR>1 A wrong place,<BR>not one's proper place or strong<BR>position; ˚स्थो हि रिपुणा स्वल्पकेनापि<BR>हन्यते H. 4. 45; स्त्रियं स्पृशेददेशे यः<BR>Ms. 8. 358; नादेशे तर्पणं कुर्यात् &c.<BR>--2 A<BR>bad country. The Smṛtis mention<BR>several places of this description:<BR>म्लेच्छ, आनर्तक, अंग, मगध, सुराष्ट्र,<BR>दक्षिणापथ, वंग, कलिंग &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कालः<BR>wrong place and time; अदेशकाले<BR>यद्दानमपात्रेभ्यश्च दीयते । Bg. 17. 22.<BR>--स्थ<BR>a. [स. त.] in the wrong place, out<BR>of place; absent from one's country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदेश्य
अदेश्य a. [न. त. न देष्टुं योग्यः]<BR>1 Not<BR>fit to be ordered, advised, indicated<BR>or pointed out; अदेश्यं यश्च दिशति<BR>Ms. 8. 53.<BR>--2 Not on the spot or<BR>pertaining to the place or occasion<BR>referred to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रेश्य
अद्रेश्य a. Ved. Invisible (अदृश्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदैन्य
अदैन्य a. Involving no<BR>humiliation or self-degradation Bh. 3. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदैव
अदैव a. (वी f.)<BR>1 Not<BR>predestined or predetermined (by Gods<BR>or by Fate).<BR>--2 Not connected<BR>with the Gods or their action, not<BR>divine; अदैवं भोजयेच्छ्राद्धं Ms. 3. 247<BR>(Kull. वैश्वदेवब्राह्मणभोजनरहितं).<BR>--3<BR>Unfortunate, ill-fated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोग्धृ
अदोग्धृ a. Not exacting;<BR>considerate (as a king.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोमद
अदोमद --ध a. Ved. Not causing<BR>inconvenience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोमध
अदोमद --ध a. Ved. Not causing<BR>inconvenience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोहः|अदोह
अदोहः<BR>1 The time when<BR>milking is not practicable.<BR>--2 Not<BR>milking; अदोहं चादिशद्गवां R. 17. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अदोष|अदोषः
अदोष a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Free from faults,<BR>demerits, vices, or defects &c.;<BR>innocent; जायामदोषामुत संत्यजामि<BR>R. 14. 34.<BR>--2 Free from the faults of<BR>composition, such as अश्लीलता, ग्राम्यता<BR>&c., See दोष; अदोषौ शब्दार्थौ K. P. 1;<BR>अदोषं गुणवत् काव्यं Sar. K. 1.<BR>--षः Not<BR>a fault; किमित्यदोषेण तिरस्कृता वयं<BR>Ki. 14. 11 though not at fault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्गः|अद्ग
अद्गः [अद्यते देवैः, अद्-कर्मणि गन्<BR>Uṇ. 1. 120, = पुरोडाश] A sacrificial oblation<BR>called पुरोडार्श, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धा
अद्धा ind. [अत्यते अत् तं संततं गमनं<BR>ज्ञानं वा दधाति क्विप् Tv.]<BR>1 Truly,<BR>clearly, surely, undoubtedly, in truth,<BR>really, certainly, indeed; अद्धा श्रियं<BR>पालितसंगराय प्रत्यर्पयिष्यति R. 13. 65.<BR>--2 Manifestly, clearly; व्यालाधिपं च<BR>यतते परिरब्धुमद्धा Bv. 1. 95.<BR>--3 In<BR>this way, thus; ˚कृ = साक्षात्कृ.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरुषः A right or true man.<BR>--बोधेयाः (pl.) N. of a school of the<BR>Śukla Yajurveda.<BR>--लोहकर्ण a.<BR>having ears clearly or quite red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्धातिः|अद्धाति
अद्धातिः Ved. A wise man, seer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्भुत|अद्भुतं|अद्भुतः
अद्भुत a. [Uṇ. 5. 1 अदि भुवो डुतच्;<BR>according to Nir. न भूतं ‘the like of<BR>which did not take place before.]<BR>1 Wonderful, marvellous; ˚कर्मन् of<BR>wonderful deeds; ˚गंध having<BR>wonderful smell; ˚दर्शन, ˚रूप; prodigious,<BR>extraordinary, transcendental,<BR>supernatural.<BR>--2 Ved. Unobserved,<BR>invisible (opp. दृश्य).<BR>--तं<BR>1 A<BR>wonder; a wonderful thing or<BR>occurrence, a prodigy, miracle; देव<BR>अद्भुतं खलु संवृत्तं Ś. 5 a wonderful<BR>or unexpected occurrence;<BR>अकालिकमनध्यायं विद्यात्सर्वाद्भुतेषु च<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-c" target="_blank">Page0042-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Ms. 4. 118.<BR>--2 Surprise, astonishment,<BR>wonder (m.) also; ˚उद्भ्रांतदेवासुराणि<BR>विक्रांतचरितानि U. 6 lost in wonder.<BR>--तः<BR>1 One of the 8 or {9} Rasas, the<BR>marvellous sentiment; जगति जनितात्यद्भुतरसः<BR>U. 3. 44.<BR>--2 N. of the Indra of the<BR>9th Manvantara.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--एनस् a.<BR>Ved. in whom no sin is visible.<BR>--धर्मः<BR>a system of prodigies.<BR>--ब्राह्मणं N.<BR>of a portion of a Brāhmaṇa<BR>belonging to the Sāmaveda.<BR>--संकाश a.<BR>resembling a marvel; so ˚उपम.<BR>--सारः the wonderful resin (of the<BR>खदिर or Catechu plant); Mimosa<BR>Catechu.<BR>--स्वन a. having a<BR>wonderful sound.<BR>--(नः) N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मन्
अद्मन् n. Ved. Eating, a meal;<BR>a house (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मनिः|अद्मनि
अद्मनिः [अत्ति सर्वान्; अद्-मनिन्<BR>Uṇ. 2. 104 अदेर्मुट्च] Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्मर|अद्मरः
अद्मर a. [अत्तुं शीलमस्य; अद्-कर्तरि<BR>क्मरच्] Voracious, gluttonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्य
अद्य a. Eatable.<BR>--द्यं Food,<BR>anything eatable --ind. [अस्मिन्नहनि<BR>इदंशब्दस्य निपातः सप्तम्यर्थे; अस्मिन् द्यवि अहनि<BR>वा Nir.]<BR>1 To-day, this day; अद्य त्वां<BR>त्वरयति दारुणः कृतांतः Māl. 5. 25;<BR>˚रात्रौ to-night, this night; ˚प्रातरेव this<BR>very morning; oft. in comp. with<BR>दिन, दिवस, &c.; ˚दिवसनक्षत्रं of this day,<BR>to-day's; अद्यैव this very day.<BR>--2 Now;<BR>अद्य गच्छ गता रात्रिः Ks. 4. 68.<BR>--3<BR>At present, now-a-days. [cf. L.<BR>ho-die.].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपि still, yet,<BR>even now, to this day, down to the<BR>present time or moment; अद्यापि<BR>ते मन्युविषयः U. 3; अद्यापि नोच्छ्वसिति<BR>ibid.; न˚ not yet; गुरुः खेदं खिन्ने मयि<BR>भजति नाद्यापि कुरुषु Ve. 1. 11; (every<BR>one of the 50 stanzas of Ch. P.<BR>begins with अद्यापि).<BR>--अवधि {1} from<BR>to-day; ˚धि भवद्भ्यो भिन्नोहं<BR>Ve. 1. 2. till to-day.<BR>--पूर्वं before now;<BR>अद्यपूर्वोच्चारित &c.<BR>--प्रभृति ind. from<BR>to-day, this day forward, henceforth;<BR>अद्यप्रभृत्यवनतांगि तवास्मि दासः<BR>Ku. 5. 86.<BR>--श्वीन a. [अद्य श्वः परदिने वा जनिष्यते<BR>प्रसोष्यते वा, अद्य-श्वस्-ख टिलोपः<BR>P. V. 2. 13] likely to happen to-day or<BR>tomorrow, imminent; ˚नं मरणं, ˚नः<BR>वियोगः Sk. (= आसन्न).<BR>--(ना) a female<BR>near delivery (आसन्नप्रसवा);<BR>अद्यश्वीनावष्टब्धे P.; अद्य श्वो वा विजायते इति<BR>अद्यश्वीना वडवा Sk.<BR>--सुत्या extraction<BR>and consecration of Soma juice on<BR>the same day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतन|अद्यतनः
अद्यतन a. (नी f.) [अद्य भवः; अद्य ट्यु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-a" target="_blank">Page0043-a+ 57</a>]<BR>तुडागमश्च]<BR>1 Pertaining or referring<BR>to, extending over, to-day; ˚दिवस,<BR>˚काल &c.<BR>--2 Current now-a-days,<BR>prevalent at present, modern.<BR>--नः<BR>The current or this day, period of<BR>the current day (Kāśi. on P. I. 2. 57);<BR>See अनद्यतन also.<BR>--नी (scil. वृत्तिः) A<BR>name given to the Aorist tense, as<BR>it denotes an action done to-day or<BR>on the same day (= ˚भूतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यतनीय
अद्यतनीय = अद्यतन<BR>1 Of to-day;<BR>˚हिमपातो व्यर्थतां नीयते Pt. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Modern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यु
अद्यु a. Ved. Blunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्युत्
अद्युत् a. Not bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्यूत्य
अद्यूत्य a. [न द्यूतलब्धं न. त.] Not<BR>obtained by gambling, honestly got.<BR>--त्यं Unlucky gambling; the watch<BR>just before the dawn (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रव|अद्रवः
अद्रव a. [न. त.] Not liquid,<BR>not of the nature of a liquid.<BR>--वः<BR>Not a liquid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रव्यं|अद्रव्य
अद्रव्यं [न. त.] A worthless thing,<BR>an object which is good for nothing;<BR>नाद्रव्ये विहिता काचित्क्रिया फलवती<BR>भवेत् H. Pr. 43; hence, a worthless or<BR>bad pupil or recipient of<BR>instruction; विनेतुरद्रव्यपरिग्रह एव बुद्धिलाघवं<BR>प्रकाशयति M. 1; अद्रव्यमेत्य भुवि<BR>शुद्धनयोपि मंत्री Mu. 7. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिः|अद्रि
अद्रिः [अद्-क्रिन् Uṇ. 4. 65;<BR>according to Nir. fr. दॄ to tear or अद्<BR>to eat.]<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>--2 A stone,<BR>especially one for pounding Soma<BR>with or grinding it on.<BR>--3 A<BR>thunderbolt (आदृणाति येन Nir.).<BR>--4 A tree.<BR>--5<BR>The sun.<BR>--6 A mass of clouds<BR>(probably so called from its resemblance<BR>to a mountain); a cloud (आदरयितव्यो<BR>भवति ह्यसौ उदकार्थं Nir.) mostly Ved.<BR>--7 A kind of measure.<BR>--8 The<BR>number 7<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः, पतिः, नाथः &c.<BR>{1} the lord of mountains, the<BR>Himālaya. {2} N. of Śiva (Lord of Kailāsa).<BR>--कर्णी a plant (अपराजिता) Clitoria<BR>Ternatea Lin.<BR>--कीला [अद्रयः कुलपर्वताः<BR>कीलाः शंकव इव यस्याः] the earth.<BR>--(लः) N. of the mountain<BR>विष्कुंभ.<BR>--कुक्षिः a mountain cave,<BR>mountainside R. 2. 38.<BR>--ज a. [अद्रौ<BR>जायते; जण्-ड] produced from, or<BR>found among, mountains,<BR>mountain-born.<BR>--(जा) {1} a plant (सैंहली).<BR>{2}<BR>--कन्या, --तनया-सुता &c. Pārvatī.<BR>--(जं) red chalk (शिलाजतु).<BR>--जात a.<BR>mountain-born.<BR>--(तः) {1} forest<BR>conflagration. {2} the ‘Sun-born’,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-b" target="_blank">Page0043-b+ 58</a>]<BR>Haṃsa or Swan. {3} form. {4} the Supreme<BR>Being.<BR>--जूत, --दुग्ध Ved. [तृ. त.]<BR>expressed or extracted by means of<BR>stones.<BR>--तनया, --नंदिनी {1} N. of<BR>Pārvatī. {2} N. of a metre of 4 lines,<BR>each having 23 syllables.<BR>--द्विष्, --भिद्<BR>m. [अद्रिं द्वेष्टि भिनत्ति वा, द्विष्-भिद्-क्विप्]<BR>the enemy or splitter of mountains<BR>(or clouds personified), epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR>--द्रोणि-णी f. {1} a mountain<BR>valley. {2} a river taking its rise in a<BR>mountain.<BR>--पतिः --राजः &c. See ˚ईश.<BR>--बर्हस् a. Ved. [अद्रेर्बर्ह इव बर्हो यस्य]<BR>as strong or hard as a mountain;<BR>mountain-high (?).<BR>--बुध्न a. [अद्रेर्बुध्न<BR>इव बुध्नो यस्य] rooted in a mountain<BR>or rock; as hard as a stone or<BR>mountain.<BR>--भू a. [अद्रौ भवति जायते]<BR>mountain-born.<BR>--(भूः) N. of a plant (<BR>आखुकर्णी or अपराजिता).<BR>--मातृ Ved. [<BR>अद्रिः मेघः तज्जलं मिमीते, अद्रेर्माता वा मा-तृच्]<BR>producing water from clouds (<BR>मघजलनिर्मातृ); having a mountain for the<BR>mother (?).<BR>--वह्निः forest<BR>conflagration.<BR>--शय्यः (having the mountain<BR>कैलास for his bed) N. of Śiva; cf.<BR>˚ईश, ˚इंद्र,<BR>--शृंगं, --सानु mountain peak.<BR>--सुत (˚षुत),<BR>--संहत a. prepared or<BR>expressed by means of stones.<BR>--सारः<BR>[अद्रेः सार इव ष. त.] ‘the essence of<BR>mountains’, iron. (--a.) hard<BR>like a mountain; ˚मय made of iron<BR>or very hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रिवत्|अद्रिवन्त्
अद्रिवत् a. Ved. Armed with, or<BR>having, stones or thunderbolts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रुह्
अद्रुह्, --द्रुह्वन् a. [न. त.] Ved.<BR>Free from malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रुह्वन्
अद्रुह्, --द्रुह्वन् a. [न. त.] Ved.<BR>Free from malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोघ
अद्रोघ a. Ved. [द्रुह्-घञ् वेदे घत्वं न.<BR>ब.] True, not false, free from<BR>malice; ˚वाच् speaking the truth; ˚अवित<BR>guarding from malice.<BR>--घं ind.<BR>Without malice or falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्रोहः|अद्रोह
अद्रोहः Absence of malice or<BR>ill feeling; moderation, mildness Ms. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वंद्व
अद्वंद्व a. Without duality or<BR>enmity; असमस्तपदवृत्तिमिव अद्वंद्वां K. 131.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वय|अद्वयः
अद्वय a. [नास्ति द्वयं यस्य]<BR>1 Not<BR>two.<BR>--2 Without a second, unique;<BR>sole; अद्वयं ब्रह्म Ved. Sūtra.<BR>--यः [अद्वयं<BR>विज्ञानाभेदः पदार्थानां अस्त्यस्य वादकत्वेन<BR>अस्त्यर्थे अच्] N. of Buddha.<BR>--यं<BR>[न. त.] Non-duality, unity,<BR>identity; especially, the identity of<BR>Brahma and the universe, or of<BR>spirit and matter; the highest truth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आनंदः = अद्वैतानंदः q. v.<BR>--वादिन् (= अद्वैत˚) one who propounds<BR>the identity of spirit and matter<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">Page0043-c+ 58</a>]<BR>or of Brahma and the universe<BR>(सर्वमेव वस्तु चित्स्वरूपं नान्यदतो<BR>द्वितीयमस्ति इति यः प्रतिपादयति). {2} Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयत्|अद्वयन्त्
अद्वयत्, --अद्वयस् a. Ved. Having no<BR>second; सखा सुशेवो अद्वयाः<BR>Rv. 1. 187. 3 (द्वयरहित); free from<BR>duplicity, true, sincere (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयस्
अद्वयत्, --अद्वयस् a. Ved. Having no<BR>second; सखा सुशेवो अद्वयाः<BR>Rv. 1. 187. 3 (द्वयरहित); free from<BR>duplicity, true, sincere (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयाविन्
अद्वयाविन् a. [अद्वयं अस्त्यर्थे विनि छंदसि<BR>दीर्घः] Not having two ways (<BR>देवपितृयानरूपमार्गद्वयरहित); पुत्रस्य पाथः<BR>पदमद्वयाविनः Rv. 1. 159. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वयु
अद्वयु a. [द्वयं द्विप्रकारोऽस्त्यस्य बा˚ उ,<BR>न. ब.] Free from duplicity, the<BR>same internally or externally (<BR>अंतर्बाह्यैकरूप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वारं|अद्वार
अद्वारं Not a door, any passage or<BR>entrance which is not intended to<BR>serve as a regular door; अद्वारेण न<BR>चातीयाद् ग्रामं वा वेश्म वा पुरं Ms. 4. 73;<BR>नाद्वारेण विशेत् Y. 1. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वितीय|अद्वितीयः
अद्वितीय a. [नास्ति द्वितीयंयस्य]<BR>1<BR>Without a second, matchless,<BR>peerless; न केवलं रूपे शिल्पेप्यद्वितीया<BR>मालविका M. 2; किमुर्वशी अद्वितीया रूपेण<BR>V. 2.<BR>--2 Without a companion, alone.<BR>--3 Sole, only, unique, supreme.<BR>--यं<BR>Brahma; एकं ˚यं ब्रह्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्विषेण्य
अद्विषेण्य [न. त.] Not malevolent,<BR>not to be disliked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेष|अद्वेषः
अद्वेष a. [न. ब.] Free from<BR>hatred or malevolence.<BR>--षः Freedom<BR>from hatred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वेषस्
अद्वेषस् a. [द्विष-असुन्. न. त.]<BR>Friendly, not hating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अद्वैत|अद्वैतः
अद्वैत a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Not dual; of one<BR>or uniform nature, equable,<BR>unchanging; ˚तं सुखदुःखयोः U. 1. 39.<BR>--2<BR>Matchless, peerless, sole, only, unique.<BR>--तं<BR>[न. त.]<BR>1 Non-duality, identity;<BR>especially that of Brahma with the<BR>universe or with the soul, or of<BR>soul and matter; See अद्वय also.<BR>--2 The supreme or highest truth<BR>or Brahma itself.<BR>--3 N. of an<BR>Upanishad; अद्वैतेन solely, without any<BR>duplicity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आनंदः (अद्वय˚) {1}<BR>the joy arising from a knowledge of<BR>the identity of the universe and the<BR>supreme spirit. {2} N. of an author<BR>who, according to Colebrooke,<BR>flourished at the close of the 15th century.<BR>--वादिन् = अद्वयवादिन् q. v. above; a<BR>Vedāntin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध|अधः
अध, अधा ind. Ved. Used like<BR>अथ as an inceptive particle in the<BR>sense of ‘now’, ‘then’, ‘afterwards’,<BR>‘moreover,’ ‘and’, ‘partly’, ‘so<BR>much the more’ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधा
अध, अधा ind. Ved. Used like<BR>अथ as an inceptive particle in the<BR>sense of ‘now’, ‘then’, ‘afterwards’,<BR>‘moreover,’ ‘and’, ‘partly’, ‘so<BR>much the more’ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधन
अधन a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Without<BR>wealth, poor.<BR>--2 Not entitled or<BR>competent to possess independent<BR>property (in law); भार्या पुत्रश्च दासश्च त्रय<BR>एवाधनाः स्मृताः । यत्ते समधिगच्छंति यस्य ते तस्य<BR>तद्धनम् ॥ Ms. 8. 416.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधन्य
अधन्य a. Unhappy, wretched,<BR>miserable; हंत धिङ् मामधन्यं U. 1. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधम|अधमः
अधम a. [अव्-अम; अवतेः अमः, वस्य<BR>पक्षे धः Uṇ. 5. 54] The lowest, vilest,<BR>meanest; very bad, or low, or vile<BR>(in quality, worth, position &c.)<BR>(opp. उत्तम); अधममध्यमोत्तमाः or<BR>उत्तमाधममध्यमाः &c.; oft. at the end of<BR>comp.; नर˚, द्विज˚; चांडालश्चाधमो नृणां<BR>Ms. 10. 12 lowest in position; अधम˚<BR>the vilest of the vile, the meanest<BR>wretch.<BR>--मः<BR>1 An unblushing<BR>sensualist (भयदयालज्जाशून्यः कामक्रीडाविषये<BR>कर्तव्याकर्तव्याविचारकः Śabda K.); वापीं<BR>स्नातुमितो गतासि न पुनस्तस्याधमस्यांतिकं<BR>K. P. 1.<BR>--2 A sort of योग or<BR>conjunction of planets (नृणां वित्तज्ञानादिषु<BR>अधमत्वसूचकः रविचंद्रयोः स्थितिविशेषरूपो<BR>योगभेदः Tv.).<BR>--मा A bad mistress (<BR>हितकारिप्रियतमे ऽहितकारिणी). [cf. L. infimus].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं [कर्म.] the foot (opp.<BR>उत्तमांग).<BR>--अर्धं [कर्म.] the lower<BR>half of the body (below the navel).<BR>--अर्ध्य a. [अधमार्धे भवः] connected with<BR>the lower part.<BR>--आचार a. [ब.] of<BR>the vilest conduct.<BR>--(रः) (कर्म˚)<BR>the meanest conduct.<BR>--ऋणः,<BR>--ऋणिकः [अधमः अधमावस्थां प्राप्तः ऋणेन,<BR>ततः ठन्] a debtor (opp. उत्तमर्णः) (lit.<BR>reduced to a low position by his<BR>incurring debt).<BR>--भृतः --भृतकः [कर्म.]<BR>a porter, groom, a servant of the<BR>lowest class, one of the 3 kinds of<BR>servants; उत्तमस्त्वायुधीयोत्र मध्यमस्तु<BR>कृषीवलः । अधमो भारवाही स्यादित्येवं त्रिंविधो भृतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर|अधरं|अधरः
अधर a. [न ध्रियते; धृ-अच्, न. त.]<BR>1 Lower (opp. उत्तर), (lit. not<BR>held up); tending downwards;<BR>under, nether, downward; ˚वासः<BR>under garment Ki. 4. 38; cf. ˚अंबर<BR>Śi. 1. 6; ˚ओष्ठ lower or nether<BR>lip, see below. (In this sense अधर<BR>partakes of the character of a<BR>pronoun).<BR>--2 Low, mean, vile; ˚उत्तरं<BR>See below; lower in quality,<BR>inferior.<BR>--3 Silenced, worsted, not<BR>able to speak; See हीन, हीनवादिन्.<BR>--4<BR>Previous, preceding; as in अधरेद्युः,<BR>q. v.<BR>--रः The nether (or<BR>sometimes the upper) lip; a lip in<BR>general; ˚पत्रं Ku. 5. 27 leaf-like lower lip;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">Page0044-b+ 58</a>]<BR>बिंबाधरालक्तकः M. 3. 5; पक्वबिंबाधरोष्ठी<BR>Me. 82; पिबसि रतिसर्वस्वमधरं Ś. 1. 24;<BR>1. 21, 3. 24; cf. अधरंखलु बिंबनामकं<BR>फलमाभ्यमिति भव्यमन्वयम् । लभतेऽधरबिंबैत्यदः<BR>पदमस्या रदनच्छदे वदत् ॥ N. 2. 24.<BR>--रा The<BR>nadir; (अधोदिश्) or the southern<BR>direction.<BR>--रं<BR>1 The lower part (of the<BR>body); पृष्ठवंशाधरे त्रिकं Ak.<BR>--2<BR>Pudendum Muliebre (also m.).<BR>--3<BR>Address, speech (opp. उत्तर);<BR>statement, sometimes used for reply also.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्तर a. {1} higher and<BR>lower, inferior and superior, worse<BR>and better; राज्ञः समक्षमेवावयोः<BR>˚व्यक्तिर्भविष्यति M. 1; व्यत्यये कर्मणां साम्यं<BR>पूर्ववच्चाधरोत्तरं Y. 1. 96. {2} former; prior<BR>and later; sooner and later;<BR>यश्चाधरोत्तरानर्थान् विगीतान्नावबुध्यते Ms. 8. 53.<BR>{3} in a contrary way, topsy-turvy,<BR>upside down (the natural order<BR>of things being inverted); श्रुतं<BR>भवद्भिरधरोत्तरं Ś. 5 you have (certainly)<BR>learnt in a contrary way, i. e. to<BR>consider good as bad and vice versa;<BR>it might perhaps also mean “have<BR>you, i. e. the members of the King's<BR>court, heard this mean or base<BR>reply (अधरं च तदुत्तरं); (यदि न प्रणयेद्राजा<BR>दंडं) स्वाम्यं च न स्यात्कस्मिंश्चित्<BR>प्रवर्तेताधरोत्तरं Ms. 7. 21 (अधरं = शूद्रादि,<BR>उत्तरं = प्रधानं); अधर्मेण जितो धर्मः<BR>प्रवृत्तमधरोत्तरं Mb. {4} nearer and further.<BR>{5} question and answer.<BR>--ओष्ठः the<BR>lower lip; अंगुलिसंवृत˚ Ś. 3. 25;<BR>Me. 82.<BR>--(ष्ठं) the lower and upper<BR>lip.<BR>--कंठः the lower part of the<BR>neck.<BR>--कायः [अधरं कायस्य] the<BR>lower part of the body.<BR>--पानं<BR>kissing, lit. drinking the lower lip.<BR>--मधु, --अमृतं the nectar of the lips.<BR>--स्वस्तिकं the nadir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीकृ
अधरीकृ {c8c} U., अधरयति Den. P.<BR>To surpass, excel, beat down,<BR>worst; शोकं किंचिदधरीकृत्य Dk. 6<BR>lessening, forgetting; to defeat,<BR>vanquish; भवता धीरतयाऽधरीकृतः<BR>Ki. 2. 40, 6. 21; चरितैर्मुनीनधरयञ्शुचिभिः<BR>Ki. 6. 24 excelling;<BR>अधरीकृतसर्वस्नेहेन अपत्यप्रेम्णा K. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीभू
अधरीभू {c1c} P. To be worsted (in a<BR>lawsuit); to be invalidated Y. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरीण|अधरीणः
अधरीण a. [अधरे भवः अधर-ख]<BR>1<BR>Lower.<BR>--2 Traduced, vilified,<BR>reproached; अधरीणः परिणांस्यते A R. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेद्युः|अधरेद्यु
अधरेद्युः ind. [अधरे दिने; अधर-एद्युस्]<BR>1 On a previous day.<BR>--2 The day<BR>before yesterday; the other day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरस्मात्
अधरस्मात्, --रतः, --स्तात्, --रात्, --तात्, --रेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">Page0044-c+ 57</a>]<BR>ind. Below, beneath, in the lower<BR>regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरतः
अधरस्मात्, --रतः, --स्तात्, --रात्, --तात्, --रेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">Page0044-c+ 57</a>]<BR>ind. Below, beneath, in the lower<BR>regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरस्तात्
अधरस्मात्, --रतः, --स्तात्, --रात्, --तात्, --रेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">Page0044-c+ 57</a>]<BR>ind. Below, beneath, in the lower<BR>regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरात्
अधरस्मात्, --रतः, --स्तात्, --रात्, --तात्, --रेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">Page0044-c+ 57</a>]<BR>ind. Below, beneath, in the lower<BR>regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरतात्
अधरस्मात्, --रतः, --स्तात्, --रात्, --तात्, --रेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">Page0044-c+ 57</a>]<BR>ind. Below, beneath, in the lower<BR>regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरेण
अधरस्मात्, --रतः, --स्तात्, --रात्, --तात्, --रेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">Page0044-c+ 57</a>]<BR>ind. Below, beneath, in the lower<BR>regions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधरांच्|अधराञ्च्
अधरांच् a. [अधरां दक्षिणां दिशं<BR>अंचति क्विप्] Southward; tending<BR>downwards, to the nadir or lower region;<BR>tending to the south.<BR>--ची the<BR>southern direction.<BR>--क् ind. Beneath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधराचीन
अधराचीन-च्य a. [अधराचिभवः;<BR>अधराच्ख यत् वा] Tending downwards;<BR>situated in the region below; being<BR>downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधराच्य
अधराचीन-च्य a. [अधराचिभवः;<BR>अधराच्ख यत् वा] Tending downwards;<BR>situated in the region below; being<BR>downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मः|अधर्म|अधर्म्म|अधर्म्मः
अधर्मः [न. त.]<BR>1 Unrighteousness,<BR>irreligion, impiousness, wickedness,<BR>injustice; ˚दंडनं Ms. 8. 127 unjust<BR>punishment; अधर्मेण unjustly, in an<BR>improper way; यश्चाधर्मेण पृच्छति<BR>Ms. 2. 111; an unjust act; a guilty or<BR>wicked deed; sin; ˚चारिन् committing<BR>unjust or unrighteous deeds; so<BR>˚आत्मन् of an irreligious spirit; तदा<BR>कथं ˚भीरुः Ś. 5; ˚मय full of<BR>wickedness or sin; for definitions &c. of<BR>धर्म and अधर्म See Tarka K. P. 19.<BR>(धर्म and अधर्म are two of the 24<BR>qualities mentioned in Nyāya,<BR>and they pertain only to the soul.<BR>They are the peculiar causes of<BR>pleasure and pain respectively.<BR>They are imperceptible, but inferred<BR>from reasoning and from<BR>transmigration.)<BR>--2 N. of a Prajāpati or of an<BR>attendant of the sun.<BR>--र्मा<BR>Unrighteousness personified.<BR>--र्मं<BR>Devoid of attributes, an epithet of<BR>ब्रह्मन्.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अस्तिकायः the<BR>category of अधर्म, See अस्तिकाय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्मिन्|अधर्म्मिन्
अधर्मिन् a. Impious, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधर्म्य
अधर्म्य a.<BR>1 Wicked, impious.<BR>--2<BR>Illegal, unlawful; पंचानां तु त्रयो<BR>धर्म्या द्वावधर्म्यौ स्मृताविह Ms. 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधवा
अधवा [अविद्यमानो धवो भर्ता यस्याः]<BR>A widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधस्
अधस्, अधः ind. [अधर-असि,<BR>अधरशब्दस्थाने अध् आदेशः P. V. 3. 39.]<BR>1 Below, down; पतत्यधो धाम विसारि<BR>सर्वतः Śi. 1. 2; in the lower region,<BR>to the infernal regions or hell;<BR>व्यसन्यधोऽधोव्रजति स्वर्यात्यव्यसनी मृतः<BR>Ms. 7. 53. (According to the<BR>context अधः may have the sense of<BR>the nominative, ˚अंकुशः &c.;<BR>ablative, अधो वृक्षात् पतति; or locative,<BR>अधो गृहे शेते).<BR>--2 Beneath, under, used<BR>like a preposition with gen.; तरूणां˚<BR>Ś. 1. 14; rarely with abl. also;<BR>बाहित्थं तु ततोप्यधः Hemacandra;<BR>(when repeated) lower and lower,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0045-a" target="_blank">Page0045-a+ 58</a>]<BR>down and down; अधोधः पश्यतः<BR>कस्य महिमा नोपचीयते H. 2. 2;<BR>यात्यधोधो व्रजत्युच्चैर्नरः स्वैरेव कर्मभिः H. 2. 48;<BR>अधोधो गंगेयं पदमुपगता स्तोकं<BR>Bh. 2. 10; from under, just below (with<BR>acc.); नवानधोऽधो बृहतः पयोधरान् Śi. 1. 4.<BR>In comp. with nouns अधः has the<BR>sense of (a) lower, under, as<BR>˚भुवनं, ˚लोकः the lower world; ˚वासः or<BR>˚अंशुकं an undergarment; or (b)<BR>the lower part; ˚कायः the lower part<BR>of the body; अधःकृ means to<BR>surpass, eclipse, overcome, vanquish,<BR>despise, scorn; तपः शरीरैः कठिनैरुपार्जितं<BR>तपस्विनां दूरमधश्चकार सा Ku. 5. 29;<BR>अधः कृताशेषांतःपुरेण K. 177;<BR>˚कृतकुसुमायुधं 179; Śi. 1. 35, 3. 52; ˚कृतैनसः<BR>Śi. 16. 8 dispelled.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a.<BR>situated below the axle or car.<BR>--(क्षं)<BR>adv. below the car, under the axle.<BR>--अक्षजः [अक्षात् इंद्रियाज्जायते इति अक्षजं<BR>प्रत्यक्षज्ञानं, तदधरं ग्राहकत्वाभावात् हीनं यस्य<BR>सः Tv.; अधःकृतं अक्षजं इंद्रियज्ञानं येन Malli.]<BR>N. of Viṣṇu; other etymologies of<BR>the name are also found: (1) अधो न<BR>क्षीयते जातु यस्मात्तस्मादधोक्षजः; (2) द्यौरक्षं<BR>पृथिवी चाधस्तयोर्यस्मादजायत । मध्ये<BR>वैराजरूपेण ततो ऽधोक्षज इष्यते ॥<BR>--अधस् See above.<BR>--उपासनं sexual intercourse.<BR>--अंगं,<BR>--द्वारं, --मर्म the anus; Pudendum<BR>Muliebre.<BR>--करः the lower part of the<BR>hand (करभ).<BR>--करणं excelling,<BR>defeating, degradation; K. 202; so ˚क्रिया;<BR>सहते न जनोप्यधःक्रियां Ki. 2. 47<BR>degradation, dishonour.<BR>--खननं<BR>undermining.<BR>--गतिः f.,<BR>--गमनं --पातः {1} a<BR>downward fall or motion, descent; going<BR>downwards. {2} degradation, downfall.<BR>going to perdition or hell;<BR>मूलानामधोगतिः K. 41 (where ˚ति has both<BR>senses); ˚तिं आयाति Pt. 1. 150 sinks,<BR>comes down (feels dishonoured);<BR>Ms. 3. 17; अरक्षितारमत्तारं नृपं<BR>विद्यादधोगतिं 8. 309 destined to go to hell.<BR>--गंतृ m. one who digs downwards,<BR>a mouse.<BR>--गं-घं-टा [अधरात् अधस्तादारभ्य<BR>घंटेव तदाकारफलत्वात्] a plant<BR>Achyranthes Aspera (अपामार्ग).<BR>--चरः [अधः<BR>खनित्वा चरति-अच्] {1} thief. {2} one<BR>who goes downwards.<BR>--जानु n. the<BR>lower part of the knee. (--ind.)<BR>below the knee.<BR>--जिह्विका [अल्पा<BR>जिह्वा जिह्विका, अधरा जिह्विका] the uvula<BR>(Mar. पडजीभ).<BR>--तलं the lower part<BR>or surface; शय्या˚, खट्वा˚.<BR>--दिश् f.<BR>the lower region, the nadir; the<BR>southern direction.<BR>--दृष्टि a. casting<BR>a downward look; a posture in Yoga;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0045-b" target="_blank">Page0045-b+ 59</a>]<BR>करणान्यबहिष्कृत्य स्थाणुवन्निश्चलात्मकः ।<BR>आत्मानं हृदये ध्यायेत् नासाग्रन्यस्तलोचनः ॥ cf. also<BR>Ku. 3. 47.<BR>--(ष्टिः) a downward look.<BR>--पदं<BR>[अधोवृत्ति पदं, पादस्याधःस्थानं वा] the place<BR>under the foot, a lower place.<BR>--पातः =<BR>˚गति q. v. above.<BR>--पुष्पी [अधोमुखानि<BR>पुष्पाणि यस्याः] N. of two plants अवाक्पुष्पी<BR>(Pimpinella Anisum) and गोजिह्वा<BR>(Elephantopus Scaber).<BR>--प्रस्तरः a seat of<BR>grass for persons in mourning to sit<BR>upon.<BR>--भक्तं [अधरं भक्तं यस्मात्] a<BR>dose of water, medicine &c. to be<BR>taken after meals &c. (भोजनांते<BR>पीयमानं जलादिकं).<BR>--भागः {1} the lower<BR>part (of the body); पूर्वभागो गुरुः<BR>पुंसामधोभागस्तु योषितां Suśr. {2} the lower<BR>part of any thing, the region below,<BR>down below; ˚व्यवस्थितं<BR>किंचित्पुरमालोकितं Pt. 1. situated down<BR>below, See पाताल.<BR>--भूः f. lower<BR>ground, land at the foot of a hill.<BR>--मुख --वदन a. having the face<BR>downwards; ˚खी तिष्ठति; ˚खैः पत्रिभिः<BR>R. 3. 57. {2} headlong, precipitate, flying<BR>downwards. {3} upside down,<BR>topsy-turvy.<BR>--(खः) N. of Viṣṇu. (<BR>--खाखी) N. of a plant गोजिह्वा Premna<BR>Esculenta.<BR>--(खं) (नक्षत्रं) {1} flying<BR>downwards, having a downward<BR>motion; these nakṣatras are: मूलाश्लेषा<BR>कृत्तिका च विशाखा भरणी तथा । मघा पूर्वात्रयं चैव<BR>अधोमुखगणः स्मृतः ॥ Jyotiṣa. {2} N. of a<BR>hell.<BR>--यंत्रं a still.<BR>--रक्तपित्तं discharge<BR>of blood from the anus and urethra.<BR>--राम a. [अधोभागे रामः शुक्लः, दृष्टितर्पकत्वात्<BR>तस्य रामत्वं] having a white colour<BR>or white marks on the lower part of<BR>the body (said of a goat)<BR>--लंबः {1} a<BR>plummet. {2} a perpendicular. {3} the<BR>lower world.<BR>--वर्चस् a. strong<BR>in the lower regions; whose<BR>lustre penetrates downwards.<BR>--वशः<BR>Pudendum Muliebre.<BR>--वायुः [<BR>अधोगामी वायुः शाक. त.] breaking wind,<BR>flatulency.<BR>--शय-य्य a. sleeping on<BR>the ground.<BR>--(य्या) sleeping on the<BR>ground; अग्नींधनं भैक्षचर्यामधःशय्यां<BR>गुरोर्हितम् । आसमावर्तनात् कुर्यात्कृतोपनयनो द्विजः ॥<BR>Ms. 2. 108.<BR>--शिरस् a. = मुख. (--n.) N.<BR>of a hell.<BR>--स्थ, --स्थित a. situated<BR>below.<BR>--स्वस्तिकं the nadir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधः|अध
