अधिनिर्णिज्
अधिनिर्णिज् a. Veiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपः|अधिप
अधिपः [अधिपाति, अधि-पा-क] A<BR>lord, ruler, king, sovereign, head;<BR>अथ प्रजानामधिपः प्रभाते R. 2. 1;<BR>mostly in comp.; नराधिपः lord of men,<BR>king; गज˚ a lordly elephant &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपतिः|अधिपति
अधिपतिः [अधिकः पतिः]<BR>1 =<BR>अधिपः.<BR>--2 A part of the head where the<BR>wound proves immediately fatal;<BR>(मस्तकाभ्यंतरोपरिष्टात् शिरासंधिसन्निपातो<BR>रोमावर्तोधिपतिः, तत्रापि सद्यो मरणम् Suśr.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपत्नी
अधिपत्नी Ved. A female ruler,<BR>mistress (स्वामिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपाः
अधिपाः [अधिपाति-पा क्विप्] Ved.<BR>A king, ruler, lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपांशुल
अधिपांशुल a. Dusty from above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपुरुषः|अधिपुरुष
अधिपु(पू)रुषः [अधिकः<BR>पु-पूरुषः] The Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपूरुषः|अधिपूरुष
अधिपु(पू)रुषः [अधिकः<BR>पु-पूरुषः] The Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिपेषणं|अधिपेषण
अधिपेषणं [पिष्-ल्युट्] Pounding<BR>or grinding upon, serving to pound<BR>or grind upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप्रज
अधिप्रज a. [अधिका प्रजा यस्य]<BR>Having many children (as a man,<BR>woman &c.)<BR>--जं adv. [प्रजामधिकृत्य]<BR>Regarding creation (of the world)<BR>as a means of preserving the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिप्रष्टियुगं|अधिप्रष्टियुग|अधिप्रष्टियुगः
अधिप्रष्टियुगं [प्रष्टौ निहितं युगं] A<BR>yoke laid on the प्रष्टि or foremost of<BR>the three horses, used on certain<BR>sacrificial occasions.<BR>--गः The fourth<BR>horse thus attached (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिबलं|अधिबल
अधिबलं An interlocution of high<BR>words in mutual defiance; S. D. 526.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभूः
अधिभूः [अधिभवति स्वामीभवति; भू-क्विप्]<BR>A master, superior; foremost;<BR>राक्षसानामधिभुवि Mv. 6. 47;<BR>रघूणामधिभुवा 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभूतं|अधिभूत
अधिभूतं [अधिष्ठायिभूतं or भूतं<BR>प्राणिमात्रमधिकृत्य वर्तमानं] The highest being; the<BR>Supreme Spirit or its all-pervading<BR>influence; the whole inanimate<BR>creation; अधिभूतं च किं प्रोक्तं Bg. 8. 1;<BR>अधिभूतं क्षरो भावः 8. 4 ‘अधिभूत is all<BR>perishable things.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिभोजनं|अधिभोजन
अधिभोजनं [अधिकं भोजनं]<BR>1<BR>Excess in eating.<BR>--2 [अधिकं भोजनं धनं मूल्यं वा<BR>यस्य] Very costly or valuable; दश<BR>वस्त्राधिभोजना Rv. 6. 47. 23; a<BR>supplementary or additional gift (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमंथः|अधिमन्थ|अधिमन्थः
अधिमंथः [अधिकं मथ्यते अनेन;<BR>मंथ्करणे घञ्]<BR>1 Severe ophthalmia;<BR>उत्पाट्यत इवात्यर्थं नेत्रं निर्मथ्यते तथा । शिरसोर्धं तु<BR>तं विद्यादधिमंथं स्वलक्षणैः.<BR>--2 = अधिमंथनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमंथनं|अधिमन्थन
अधिमंथनं [मंथ्-भावे करणेवा ल्युट्]<BR>Rubbing together for producing fire;<BR>suitable for such friction (as wood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमंथित|अधिमन्थित
अधिमंथित a. [अधिमंथोऽस्य संजातः इतच्]<BR>Suffering from eye-disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमांसः|अधिमांस
अधिमांसः [अधिकं मांसं यत्र] A<BR>sort of disease in the white of the<BR>eye, a sort of cancer or protuberance<BR>of flesh; विस्तीर्णं मृदु बहुलं यकृत्प्रकाशं<BR>श्यावं वा तदधिमांसजार्म विद्यात् Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमांसकः|अधिमांसक
अधिमांसकः [अधिकं मांसं यत्र] A<BR>sort of cancer in the back of the<BR>gums; हनूस्ये पश्चिमे दंते महाशोथो महारुजः ।<BR>लालास्रावी (कालास्नायी) कफकृतो विज्ञेयः<BR>सोधिमांसकः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमात्र
अधिमात्र a. [अधिका मात्रा यस्य]<BR>Beyond measure, excessive,<BR>inordinate.<BR>--त्रं On the subject of prosody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमासः|अधिमास
अधिमासः [अधिको रविमासात्<BR>अतिरिक्तः शुक्लप्रतिपदादिदर्शांतश्चांद्रो मासः] An<BR>intercalary (lunar) month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमुक्तिः|अधिमुक्ति
अधिमुक्तिः f. Trust, confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिमुह्यः|अधिमुह्य
अधिमुह्यः N. of Buddha in one<BR>of his 34 former births.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियज्ञ|अधियज्ञः
अधियज्ञ a. Pertaining to a<BR>sacrifice; ˚ज्ञं ब्रह्म जपेत् Ms. 6. 83.<BR>--ज्ञः<BR>Principal sacrifice; the agency<BR>effecting or causing such sacrifice;<BR>˚ज्ञोहमेवात्र देहे देहभृतां वर Bg. 8. 4<BR>the अधियज्ञ is I myself in this body<BR>(i. e. Kṛṣṇa); अत्रास्मिन्देहे<BR>अंतर्यामित्वेन स्थितोहमधियज्ञः<BR>यज्ञादिकर्मप्रवर्तकस्तत्फलदाता चेति श्रीधरः.<BR>--ज्ञं adv. On the<BR>subject of sacrifices, so अधियाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियांग|अधियाङ्ग
अधियांग = अधिकांग, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियोगः|अधियोग
अधियोगः [अधिको योगः] An<BR>auspicious conjunction of stars for<BR>departure, expedition &c. (<BR>ज्योतिषप्रसिद्धो यात्रिकशुभयोगः); योगे<BR>क्षेममथाधियोगगमने क्षेमं रिपूणां वधः Muhūrta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधियोधः|अधियोध
अधियोधः [आधिक्येन युध्यते;<BR>युध्-अच्] The foremost hero or warrior<BR>(in fighting); न हि कोपपरीतानि<BR>हर्षवीर्योत्सुकानि च । भवंति अधियोधानां<BR>मुखानि निहते पतौ Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरज्जु
अधिरज्जु a. Ved. [अधिगता<BR>रज्जुर्येन] Fastening, fettering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरथ|अधिरथः
अधिरथ a. [अध्यारूढो रथं रथिनं वा]<BR>Being on or over a car.<BR>--थः<BR>1 A<BR>charioteer, driver.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>charioteer who was king of Aṅga and<BR>foster-father of Karṇa.<BR>--थं Ved. A<BR>cart-load.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्
अधिराज् m.<BR>--जः [अधिराजते; राज् क्विप्,<BR>राजन्-टच् वा] A sovereign or supreme<BR>ruler, an emperor; प्रायोपविष्टो<BR>गंगायामनादृत्याधिराद् श्रियं Bhāg.;<BR>अद्यास्तमेतु भुवनेष्वधिराजशब्दः U. 6. 16; king,<BR>head, lord (of men, animals &c.);<BR>हिमालयो नाम नगाधिराजः Ku. 1. 1; so<BR>मृग˚, नाग˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराज्यं|अधिराज्य
अधिराज्यं --ष्ट्रं [अधिकृतं राज्यं राष्ट्रं अत्र]<BR>1 Imperial or sovereign sway,<BR>supremacy, sole sovereignty, imperial<BR>dignity, an empire.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिराष्ट्रं|अधिराष्ट्र
अधिराज्यं --ष्ट्रं [अधिकृतं राज्यं राष्ट्रं अत्र]<BR>1 Imperial or sovereign sway,<BR>supremacy, sole sovereignty, imperial<BR>dignity, an empire.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरुक्म
अधिरुक्म a. [अधिगतं रुक्मं आभरणं<BR>येन] Having ornaments (of gold &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरुह्
अधिरुह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To ascend, mount<BR>(a throne, hill &c.); go up to, find<BR>access to, sit in or on (acc.);<BR>पादाहतंयदुत्थाय मूर्द्धानमधिरोहति Śi. 2. 46;<BR>पुराधिरूढः शयनं महाधनं Ki. 1. 38. lying<BR>on; तुरगाधिरूढं R. 7. 37 riding a<BR>horse; 12. 104; बंधुजनाधिरूढैर्गजानां<BR>वृंदैः Ku. 7. 52 mounted or seated<BR>on; योगाधिरूढाः R. 13. 52; engaged or<BR>lost in contemplation; so Pt. 1;<BR>सद्यः परस्परतुलामधिरोहतां द्वे R. 5. 68<BR>bear or acquire; प्रतिज्ञां˚ enter on;<BR>कीर्तिर्द्यामधिरोहति Śi. 2. 52.;<BR>सर्वमनोरथानामग्रमिवाधिरूढा K. 158 mounted on<BR>the summit or pinnacle; त्वां धूरियं<BR>योग्यतयाधिरूढा Ki. 3. 50 this<BR>responsibility lies on your shoulders.<BR>--2 To<BR>string; अधिरोहति गांडीवं महेषौ<BR>Ki. 13. 16.<BR>--3 (Intran.) To rise or grow over<BR>or above. --Caus. [रोह -(प) यति]<BR>1 To raise, place, seat, cause to<BR>mount or ascend; ताः स्वमंकमधिरोप्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">Page0049-c+ 57</a>]<BR>R. 19. 44 having placed or seated;<BR>Śi. 12. 46.<BR>--2 To restore, give back;<BR>पुराणशोभामधिरोपितायां (वसतौ)<BR>R. 16. 42 restored to its former grandeur.<BR>--3 To string (as a bow); कार्मुकं च<BR>बलिनाधिरोपितम् R. 11. 81.<BR>--4 To give,<BR>confer &c.; उदारक इति<BR>प्रीतलोकाधिरोपितापरश्लाध्यनामनि Dk. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरुह्
अधिरुह् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Growing on; धरणिरुहाधिरुहो लतायाः<BR>Śi. 7. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरूढ
अधिरूढ p. p.<BR>1 Mounted, ascended<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Increased; ˚समाधियोगः engaged<BR>in profound meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोपणं|अधिरोपण
अधिरोपणं Act of raising, exalting<BR>or causing to mount.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहः|अधिरोह
अधिरोहः An elephant rider<BR>Śi. 11. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहणं|अधिरोहण
अधिरोहणं Ascending, mounting;<BR>चिता˚ R. 8. 57.<BR>--णी [अधिरुह्यते अनया,<BR>रुह् करणे ल्युट्] A ladder, flight of<BR>steps (of wood &c.) (Mar. शिडी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिरोहिन्
अधिरोहिन् a. Ascending, mounting,<BR>rising above &c.<BR>--णी [अधिरोहः<BR>साधनत्वेन अस्त्यस्याः] A ladder, flight of steps.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवच्
अधिवच् {c2c} P. To speak in favour<BR>of, advocate, side with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवक्तृ
अधिवक्तृ m.<BR>1 One who advocates a<BR>particular cause (पक्षपातेन वक्तृ), an<BR>advocate.<BR>--2 An orator.<BR>--3 A comforter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवचनं|अधिवचन
अधिवचनं<BR>1 Advocacy, speaking in<BR>favour of (पक्षपातेन कथनं वचनं.).<BR>--2 A<BR>name, epithet, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवाकः|अधिवाक
अधिवाकः [वच्-घञ्] Advocacy;<BR>तमिद्धनेषु हितेष्वधिवाकाय हवंते<BR>Rv. 8. 16. 5 (पक्षपातवचनाय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवस्
अधिवस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To inhabit, fix one's<BR>abode or residence in, settle, dwell<BR>or reside in (with acc. of place);<BR>गिरिमधिवसेस्तत्र विश्रामहेतोः Me. 25;<BR>यानि प्रियासहचरश्चिरमध्यवात्सं U. 3. 8;<BR>बाल्यात्परामिव दशां मदनोध्युवास<BR>R. 5. 63; 11. 61; 13. 79; Śi. 3. 59; Bk. 5. 6;<BR>1. 3; 8. 79.<BR>--2 To settle, alight or<BR>perch on.<BR>--3 ({c2c} A.) To put on (clothes).<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to stay overnight.<BR>--2 To consecrate, set up (as an image).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवस्त्र
अधिवस्त्र a. [अध्यावृतं वस्त्रं येन]<BR>Clad, veiled; Rv. 8. 26. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासः|अधिवास
अधिवासः<BR>1 Abode, residence;<BR>dwelling; सतत˚सुभगार्पितस्तनं Māl. 5. 8;<BR>तस्यापि स एव गिरिरधिवासः K. 137;<BR>लक्ष्मी भृतोंभोधितटाधिवासान् Śi. 3. 71<BR>situated on; settlement, habitation.<BR>--2 An inhabitant, neighbour.<BR>--3<BR>Obstinate pertinacity in making a<BR>demand, sitting without food<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">Page0050-a+ 57</a>]<BR>before a person's house till he ceases<BR>to oppose or refuse it (Mar. धरणा).<BR>--4 [अधिवासयति देवता अनेन, करणे घञ्]<BR>Consecration of an image especially<BR>before the commencement of a<BR>sacrificial rite; see अधिवासनं also.<BR>--5 A<BR>garment, mantle (अधीवासः also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युषित
अध्युषित p. p. Inhabited, resorted to;<BR>विद्याधराध्युषितचारुशिलातलानि स्थानानि<BR>Bh. 2. 70; बलैरध्युषितास्तस्य R. 4. 46;<BR>9. 25; 14. 30; सप्तर्षिमंडल˚ K. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवास्
अधिवास् {c10c} P. To scent, perfume;<BR>कर्पूरपल्लवरसेन अधिवासय गंधपात्राणि<BR>K. 184; मंदारपुष्पैरधिवासितायां V. 4. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासः|अधिवास
अधिवासः Application of perfumes<BR>or fragrant cosmetics; scenting,<BR>perfuming; fragrance, scent, fragrant<BR>odour itself; अधिवासस्पृहयेव मारुतः<BR>R. 8. 34; Śi. 2. 20, 5. 42; K. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासनं|अधिवासन
अधिवासनं [वस्-णिच्, or<BR>--वास् ल्युट्.]<BR>1<BR>Scenting with perfumes or odorous<BR>substances (संस्कारो गंधमाल्याद्यैः Ak.).<BR>--2<BR>[वस्-णिच्-ल्युट्] Preliminary<BR>consecration (प्रतिष्ठा) of an image, its<BR>invocation and worship by suitable<BR>Mantras &c. before the commencement of<BR>a sacrifice; (यज्ञारंभात्प्राक् देवताद्यावाहनपूर्वकः<BR>पूजनादिकर्मभेदः); making a divinity<BR>assume its abode in an image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासिन्
अधिवासिन् a.<BR>1 Inhabiting,<BR>dwelling or siting in.<BR>--2 Scenting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवासित
अधिवासित p. p.<BR>1 Invested or<BR>clothed with.<BR>--2 Scented, perfumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवाहनं|अधिवाहन
अधिवाहनं Taking up, carrying<BR>over, conveying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविकर्तनं|अधिविकर्तन|अधिविकर्त्तन
अधिविकर्तनं The act of cutting<BR>off or cutting through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविद्
अधिविद् {c6c} U. To marry in<BR>addition to, supersede (as a wife)<BR>(said also of wives);<BR>अधिविविदुरमात्यैराहृतास्तस्य यूनः प्रथमपरिगृहीते<BR>श्रीभुवौ राजकन्याः R. 18. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिविन्ना
अधिविन्ना [विद्-क्त] A superseded<BR>wife, one whose husband has<BR>married again; according to Hindu<BR>Śāstras a wife may be superseded<BR>for any one of these {8} defects:<BR>--सुरापी व्याधिता धूर्ता वंध्यार्थध्न्यप्रियंवदा ।<BR>स्त्रीप्रसूश्चाधिवेत्तव्या पुरुषद्वेषिणी तथा Y. 1. 73,<BR>74; Ms. 9. 80-83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेत्तृ
अधिवेत्तृ m. [विद्-कर्त्तरि तृच्] A<BR>husband who supersedes his first wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेदः|अधिवेद
अधिवेदः Marrying an additional<BR>wife.<BR>--दं adv. concerning the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिवेदनं|अधिवेदन
अधिवेदनं [भावे ल्युट्] = अधिवेदः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिशी
अधिशी {c2c} A. To lie or sleep upon,<BR>sleep in, rest or recline upon; (with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">Page0050-b+ 57</a>]<BR>acc. of place); भुजांतरं R. 19. 32; अमुं<BR>13. 6; 16. 49; शिलापट्टमधिशयाना<BR>Ś. 3; अध्यशयिष्ट गां Bk. 15. 114;<BR>चंद्रापीडः शयनतलमधिशिश्ये K. 98,<BR>206; Ki. 1. 38; Dk. 112; to dwell,<BR>inhabit Bk. 10. 35; to sit in;<BR>अथाधिशिश्ये प्रयतः प्रदोषे रथं R. 5. 28.<BR>--Caus. To cause to sleep on;<BR>दर्भशय्यामधिशाय्य Dk. 105 placing on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिशयित
अधिशयित p. p. Reclining upon,<BR>used for reclining upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रि
अधिश्रि {c1c} U.<BR>1 To sleep on, ascend,<BR>mount, resort to; विलोचने<BR>बिभ्रदधिश्रितश्रिणी Śi. 1. 24 possessed of beauty;<BR>अधिश्रयंतीर्गजताः 12. 50.<BR>--2 To place<BR>over.<BR>--3 (अधिश्री also) To put on fire,<BR>make hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रयः|अधिश्रय
अधिश्रयः [श्रि-भावे अच्]<BR>1 A<BR>receptacle.<BR>--2 [श्री-अच्] Boiling, making<BR>hot (by putting on fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रयणं|अधिश्रयण
अधिश्रयणं --पणं [श्रि-श्री-भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>Placing a kettle on fire; warming,<BR>boiling.<BR>--णी [अधिश्रीयते पच्यतेऽत्र, आधारे<BR>ल्युट् ङीप्] An oven, a fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्रपणं|अधिश्रपण
अधिश्रयणं --पणं [श्रि-श्री-भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>Placing a kettle on fire; warming,<BR>boiling.<BR>--णी [अधिश्रीयते पच्यतेऽत्र, आधारे<BR>ल्युट् ङीप्] An oven, a fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिश्री
अधिश्री a. [अधिका श्रीर्यस्य] Of<BR>exalted dignity, supreme; very rich,<BR>sovereign lord; इयं<BR>महेंद्रप्रभृतीनधिश्रियश्चतुर्दिगीशानवमत्य मानिनी Ku. 5. 53;<BR>R. 7. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिषवणं|अधिषवण
अधिषवणं [अधिषूयते सोमोऽत्र;<BR>अधिसु-आधारे ल्युट्]<BR>1 A contrivance (like<BR>a hand-press) of leather &c. to<BR>extract and strain the Soma juice, or<BR>(a.) used for the act of straining &c.<BR>--2 [भावे ल्युट्] Straining Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिषवण्या
अधिषवण्या [अधिषवणाय हिता, यत्] The<BR>board or wooden plank (फलक) used<BR>in the act of extracting Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठा
अधिष्ठा {c1c} P. (used with acc.<BR>P. I. 4. 46)<BR>1 (a) To stand on or<BR>upon, to sit in or upon, occupy (as a seat<BR>&c.), resort to; अर्धासनं गोत्रभिदोऽधितष्ठौ<BR>R. 6. 73; शाखिनः केचिदध्यष्ठुः Bk. 15. 31;<BR>प्रतनुबलान्यधितिष्ठतस्तपांसि Ki. 10. 16<BR>practising; मामधिष्ठाय Rām.<BR>depending on me. (b) To stand, be;<BR>अध्यतिष्ठदंगुष्ठेन शतं समाः Mb. (c) To stand<BR>over, mount. (d) To stand by, be<BR>near; आश्रमबहिर्वृक्षमूलमधितिष्ठति U. 4.<BR>--2 To be in, dwell in, inhabit,<BR>reside, stay; भुजंगपिहितद्वारं<BR>पातालमधितिष्ठति R. 1. 80; माधिष्ठा निर्जनं वनं<BR>Bk. 8. 79; श्रीजयदेवभणितमधितिष्ठतु<BR>कंठतटीमविरतं Gīt. 11.<BR>--3 To make<BR>oneself master of, seize, take<BR>possession of, overpower, conquer; संग्रामे<BR>तानधिष्ठास्यन् Bk. 9. 72;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-c" target="_blank">Page0050-c+ 58</a>]<BR>त्वमधिष्ठास्यसि द्विषः 16. 40; स सदा<BR>फलशालिनीं क्रियां शरदं लोक इवाधितिष्ठति<BR>Ki. 2. 31 obtains; अधितिष्ठति<BR>लोकमोजसा स विवस्वानिव मेदिनीपतिः 2. 38;<BR>यक्षः कुतश्चिदधिष्ठाय बालचंद्रिकां निवसति<BR>Dk. 18.<BR>--4 (a) To lead, conduct as<BR>head or chief; महाराजदशरथस्य<BR>दारानधिष्ठाय वसिष्ठः प्राप्तः U. 4, See अधिष्ठित<BR>also. (b) To be at the head of, govern,<BR>direct, preside over, rule,<BR>superintend; प्रकृतिं स्वामधिष्ठाय Bg. 4. 6<BR>governing, controlling; श्रोत्रं चक्षुः<BR>स्पर्शनं च रसनं घ्राणमेव च । अधिष्ठाय मनश्चायं<BR>विषयानुपसेवते 15. 9 presiding over and<BR>thus turning to use.<BR>--5 To use,<BR>employ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठित
अधिष्ठित p. p. [अधिष्ठा-क्त]<BR>1 (Used<BR>actively) (a) Standing, being;<BR>दंतांतरमधिष्ठितं Ms. 5. 141; (oft. with अ<BR>dropped; ज्ञानं ज्ञेयं ज्ञानगम्यं हृदि सर्वस्य<BR>धिष्ठितं Bg. 13. 17.);<BR>वीरलोकमधिष्ठितस्तातः Mv. 5 gone to; राजप्रसाद˚ Pt. 1<BR>being in or enjoying royal favour.<BR>(b) Possessed of, dependent on. (c)<BR>Directing, presiding over;<BR>धर्माधिकरणाधिष्ठितपुरुषैः Pt. 1.<BR>--2<BR>(Passively) (a) Inhabited or resorted to<BR>by, occupied, possessed by;<BR>दनुकबंधाधिष्ठितो दंडकारण्यभागः U. 1;<BR>Ms. 5. 97; अचिराधिष्ठितराज्यः शत्रुः M. 1. 8 an<BR>enemy who has newly (not long<BR>ago) ascended the throne, a newly<BR>established king; अचिर˚ अधिकारः<BR>Dk. 64 newly established; so ग्रहेण<BR>possessed by; मयूर˚ K. 97; ˚पुरोभागां<BR>K. 10, 130, 147, 152. (b) Full of,<BR>seized with, taken possession of,<BR>smitten, affected, overpowered;<BR>अनेनाधिष्ठितानां कामिनीनां K. 236, 161, 194;<BR>कामाधिष्ठितचेतसा H. 1; Śi. 13. 39. (c)<BR>Watched over, guarded,<BR>superintended; रक्षापुरुषाधिष्ठिते प्रासादे Pt. 1;<BR>आर्यारुंधतीवसिष्ठाधिष्ठितेषु<BR>रघुकुलकदंबकेषु U. 2; प्रनष्टाधिगतं द्रव्यं<BR>तिष्ठेद्युक्तैरधिष्ठितं Ms. 8. 34. (d) Led,<BR>conducted, commanded by, presided over;<BR>सांख्यमिव कपिलाधिष्ठितं K. 40;<BR>अनेनाधिष्ठितं भुवनतलं 43, 44, 228;<BR>वसिष्ठाधिष्ठिता देव्यो गता राघवमातरः U. 1. 3; तव<BR>प्रतापाधिष्ठितेन उपायेन H. 4 aided or<BR>supported; ताताधिष्ठितानामपि बलानां<BR>Ve. 3; स्वामिनाधिष्ठितः श्वापि H. 3. 136.<BR>(e) Ridden, mounted upon;<BR>मूषकाधिष्ठितं तमवलोक्य Pt. 2 with the<BR>mouse seated upon him; विलोक्य<BR>वृद्धोक्षमधिष्ठितं त्वया Ku. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठातृ
अधिष्ठातृ [स्था-तृच्] Superintending,<BR>watching over, presiding over,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-a" target="_blank">Page0051-a+ 57</a>]<BR>guiding, governing; tutelary, guardian;<BR>as ˚त्री देवता a guardian or presiding<BR>deity. --m. (ता) A superintendent,<BR>head, chief, protector, controller,<BR>regulator, ruler; सर्वेंद्रियाधिष्ठाता<BR>Bhāṣā P.; especially with reference<BR>to the Almighty who is the ruler<BR>of the universe. See अधिदेव also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिष्ठानं|अधिष्ठान
अधिष्ठानं [अधि-स्था-ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Standing or being near, being at hand,<BR>approach (सन्निधि); अत्राधिष्ठानं कुरु<BR>take a seat here.<BR>--2 Resting upon,<BR>occupying, inhabiting, dwelling in,<BR>locating oneself in; प्राणाधिष्ठानं देहस्य<BR>&c.<BR>--3 A position, site, basis,<BR>seat; त्र्यधिष्ठानस्य देहिनः Ms. 12. 4;<BR>इंद्रियाणि मनो बुद्धिरस्याधिष्ठानमुच्यते<BR>Bg. 3. 40, 18. 14 the seat (of that<BR>desire.)<BR>--4 Residence, abode; नगरं<BR>राजाधिष्ठानं Pt. 1.; so धर्म˚; a place,<BR>locality, town; सर्वाविनयाधिष्ठानतां<BR>गच्छंति K. 106; कस्मिंश्चिदधिष्ठाने in a<BR>certain place.<BR>--5 Authority, power,<BR>power of control, presiding over;<BR>अनधिष्ठानं H. 3. 90 loss of position,<BR>dismissal from a post (of authority);<BR>समर्थस्त्वमिमं जेतुमधिष्ठानपराक्रमैः Rām.;<BR>यथेह अश्वैर्युक्तो रथः सारथिनाऽधिष्ठितः<BR>प्रवर्तते तथा आत्माधिष्ठानाच्छरीरं<BR>Gauḍapāda; महाश्वेता कृताच्च सत्याधिष्ठानात्<BR>K. 346 appeal or reference to truth.<BR>--6 Government, dominion.<BR>--7 A<BR>wheel (of a car &c.)<BR>--8 A<BR>precedent, prescribed rule.<BR>--9 A<BR>benediction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शरीरं A body<BR>which forms the medium between<BR>the subtle and the gross body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिस्त्रि
अधिस्त्रि ind. [स्त्रियमधिकृत्य]<BR>Concerning a woman or wife.<BR>--स्त्री [<BR>अधिका स्त्री] A superior or<BR>distinguished woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधिस्यंदं
अधिस्यंदं ind. [अधिकः स्यंदो वेगो<BR>यथा स्यात्तथा] More quickly Śi. 17. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधी
अधी [अधि-इ] {c2c} A.<BR>1 To study,<BR>learn (by heart), read; (with abl.<BR>of person) learn from;<BR>उपाध्यायादधीते Sk.; सोध्यैष्ट वेदान् Bk. 1. 2.<BR>--2 (P.)<BR>(a) To remember, think of, long or<BR>care for, mind, (with regret) with<BR>gen.; रामस्य दयमानोऽसावध्येति तव लक्ष्मणः<BR>Bk. 8. 119; 18. 38; ममैवाध्येति<BR>नृपतिस्तृप्यन्निव जलांजलेः Ki. 11. 74 thinks<BR>of me only. (b) To know or learn by<BR>heart, study, learn; गच्छाधीहि<BR>गुरोर्मुखात् Mb. (c) To teach, declare. (d)<BR>To notice, observe, understand. (e)<BR>To meet with, obtain; तेन<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-b" target="_blank">Page0051-b+ 58</a>]<BR>दीर्घममरत्वमध्यगुः Śi. 14. 31 --Caus. [अध्यापयति]<BR>To teach, instruct (in); with acc.<BR>of the agent of the verb in the<BR>primitive sense; (तौ) सांगं च वेदमध्याप्य<BR>R. 15. 33; विद्यामथैनं विजयां जयां च…<BR>अध्यापिपद् गाधिसुतो यथावत् Bk. 2. 21,<BR>7. 34; अध्यापितस्योशनसापि नीतिं<BR>Ku. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीत|अधीतः
अधीत p. p. Learnt, studied, read,<BR>remembered, attained &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विद्य a. who has studied the Vedas<BR>or finished his studies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतिः|अधीति
अधीतिः f. [इ-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Study,<BR>perusal; ˚बोधाचरणप्रचारणैः N. 1. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Remembrance, recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीतिन्
अधीतिन् a. [अधीतमनेन; अधीत-इनि]<BR>Well-read, proficient in (with loc.)<BR>अधीती चतुर्ष्वाम्नायेषु Dk. 120; वेदे,<BR>व्याकरणे &c.; त्वगुत्तरासंगवतीमधीतिनीं<BR>Ku. 5. 16 muttering holy prayers,<BR>engaged in repeating sacred texts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीयानः|अधीयान
अधीयानः pres. p. A student, one<BR>who goes over the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययः|अध्यय
अध्ययः [इ-भावे अच्]<BR>1 Learning,<BR>study; remembrance.<BR>--2 = अध्याय, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययनं|अध्ययन
अध्ययनं [इ-ल्युट्] Learning, study,<BR>reading (especially the Vedas); one<BR>of the six duties of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>The study of the Vedas is allowed<BR>to the first 3 classes, but not to a<BR>Śūdra Ms. 1. 88-91. अध्ययनं च<BR>अक्षरमात्रपाठ इति वैदिकाः, सार्थाक्षरग्रहणमिति<BR>मीमांसकाः; the latter view is obviously<BR>correct; cf. यथा पशुर्भारवाही न तस्य भजते<BR>फलं । द्विजस्तथार्थानभिज्ञो न वेदफलमश्नुते ॥<BR>or better still, Yāska's Nirukta:<BR>स्थाणुरयं भारहारः किलाभूदधीत्य वेदं न<BR>विजानाति योऽर्थं । अर्थज्ञ इत् (अर्थविद्) सकलं<BR>भद्रमश्नुते नाकमेति ज्ञानविधूतपाप्मा ॥ See<BR>also under अनग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापकः|अध्यापक
अध्यापकः [अधि-इ-णिच्-ण्वुल्] A<BR>teacher, preceptor, instructor;<BR>especially of the Vedas; व्याकरण˚,<BR>न्याय˚ professor or teacher of grammar,<BR>logic &c.; भृतक˚ a hired teacher,<BR>mercenary teacher; ˚उदितः styled a<BR>professor. According to<BR>Viṣṇu Smṛti an adhyāpaka is of 2 kinds:<BR>he is either an Ācārya i. e. one<BR>who invests a boy with the sacred<BR>thread and initiates him into the<BR>Vedas, or he is an Upādhyāya i. e.<BR>one who teaches for livelihood (वृत्त्यर्थं)<BR>See Ms. 2. 140-141 and the two<BR>words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापनं|अध्यापन
अध्यापनं [इ-णिच्, भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>Teaching, instructing, lecturing, especially<BR>on sacred knowledge; one of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">Page0051-c+ 57</a>]<BR>six duties of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>According to Indian law-givers अध्यापन is<BR>of three kinds: (1) undertaken<BR>for charity, (2) for wages and (3)<BR>in consideration of services<BR>rendered; cf. Hārīta: अध्यापनं च त्रिविधं<BR>धर्मार्थमृक्थकारणम् । शुश्रूषाकरणं चेति त्रिविधं<BR>परिकीर्तितम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापयितृ
अध्यापयितृ m. [इ-णिच्-तृच्] A<BR>teacher, instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याय|अध्यायः
अध्याय a. [इ-घञ् P. III. 3. 21]<BR>(At the end of comp.) A reader,<BR>student, one who studies; वेदाध्यायः<BR>a student of the Vedas; so मंत्र˚--यः<BR>1<BR>Reading, learning, study, especially<BR>of the Vedas; प्रशांताध्यायसत्कथा (<BR>नगरी) Rām.<BR>--2 Proper time for reading<BR>or for a lesson; ˚ज्ञाः प्रचक्षते<BR>Ms. 4. 102, see अनध्याय also.<BR>--3 A lesson,<BR>lecture; अधीयतेऽस्मिन् अध्यायः<BR>P. III. 3. 122; so स्वाध्यायोऽध्येतव्यः<BR>--4 A<BR>chapter, a large division of a work,<BR>such as of the Rāmāyaṇa,<BR>Mahābhārata, Manu Smṛti, Pāṇini's Sūtras<BR>&c. The following are some of the<BR>names used by Sanskrit writers to<BR>denote chapters or divisions of<BR>works:<BR>--सर्गो वर्गः<BR>परिच्छेदोद्घाताध्यायांकसंग्रहाः । उच्छ्वासः परिवर्तश्च पटलः<BR>कांडमाननं । स्थानं प्रकरणं चैव पर्वोल्लासाह्निकानि च ।<BR>स्कंधांशौ तु पुराणादौ प्रायशः परिकीर्तितौ ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यायिन्
अध्यायिन् a. [इ-णिनि] Studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येतृ
अध्येतृ m.,<BR>--त्री f. A student, learner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीकारः|अधीकार
अधीकारः [कृ-घञ् उपसर्गदीर्घत्वं]<BR>= अधिकार q. v.; स्वागतं<BR>स्वानधीकारानबलंब्य Ku. 2. 18; Ms. 11. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीन|अधीनः
अधीन a. [अधि-ख P. V. 4. 7;<BR>अधिगतः इनं प्रभुं वा] Subject to,<BR>subservient, dependent on; usually in<BR>comp.; स्थाने प्राणाः कामिनां दूत्यधीनाः<BR>M. 3. 14; त्वदधीनं खलु देहिनां सुखं<BR>Ku. 4. 10; इक्ष्वाकूणां दुरापेऽर्थे त्वदधीना हि<BR>सिद्धयः R. 1. 72; केन निमित्तेन<BR>भवदधीनो जातः Dk. 7 consigned to your care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीमंथ|अधीमन्थ
अधीमंथ = अधिमंथ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीर|अधीरः
अधीर a.<BR>1 Not bold, timid.<BR>--2<BR>Confused, lacking self-command,<BR>excited, excitable.<BR>--3 Fitful, capricious.<BR>--4 Unsteady, not fixed, tremulous,<BR>rolling; ˚विप्रेक्षितमायताक्ष्या<BR>Ku. 1. 46; ˚लोचनः Śi. 1. 53; 6. 25.<BR>--5<BR>Querulous, foolish, weak-minded.<BR>--रा<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>--2 A capricious or<BR>quarrelsome mistress; see under नायिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीवासः|अधीवास
अधीवासः [वस् आच्छादने करणे घञ्]<BR>A long coat or mantle covering the<BR>whole person (उपरिष्टादावरकं वासः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीशः|अधीश
अधीशः [अधिकः ईशः] Lord,<BR>supreme lord or master, sovereign ruler;<BR>अंग˚, मृग˚, मनुज˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीश्वरः|अधीश्वर
अधीश्वरः [अधिकः ईश्वरः]<BR>1 A<BR>supreme lord or an employer.<BR>--2 An<BR>Arhat (among Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधीष्ट|अधीष्टः
अधीष्ट a. [अधि-इष् दिवादि-क्त]<BR>Honorary, solicited.<BR>--ष्टः [भावे-क्त]<BR>Honorary office or duty; one of the cases<BR>in which लिङ् or the Potential may be<BR>used; P. III. 3. 161 (अधीष्टः =<BR>सत्कारपूर्वको व्यापारः Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुना
अधुना ind. [अस्मिन् काले; इदमः<BR>इदंशब्दस्य सप्तम्यंतात्कालवाचिनः स्वार्थे<BR>अधुनाप्रत्ययः स्यात् P. V. 3. 17 Sk.] Now,<BR>at this time; प्रमदानामधुना विडंबना<BR>Ku. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुनातन|अधुनातनं
अधुनातन a. (नी f.) [अधुना भवार्थे<BR>ट्युल् तुट्च] Belonging to the present<BR>times, modern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधुर
अधुर a. [नास्ति धूः चिंताभारो वा यस्य]<BR>Not laden, free from the burden of<BR>cares &c.<BR>--धूः [न. त.] Absence of<BR>burden or cares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधूमकः|अधूमक
अधूमकः [न. ब.] ‘Smokeless’,<BR>burning or blazing fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृत|अधृतः
अधृत a. Not held or controlled &c.<BR>--तः One of the 1000 names of<BR>Viṣṇu (सर्वेषां धारकत्वेन केनापि न धृतः<BR>स्वप्रतिष्ठितः परमेश्वरः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृतिः|अधृति
अधृतिः f.<BR>1 Want of firmness or<BR>control, looseness.<BR>--2 Incontinence.<BR>--3 Unhappiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्ट|अधृष्टः
अधृष्ट a.<BR>1 Not bold, modest, shy.<BR>--2 Invincible, irresistible; unhurt;<BR>हूतासो वसवो ऽधृष्टाः Rv. 6. 50. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधृष्य|अधृष्यः
अधृष्य a.<BR>1 Invincible,<BR>unassailable; मनसाप्यधृष्यं Ku. 3. 51<BR>unassailable even in thought;<BR>unapproachable (opp. अभिगम्य);<BR>अधृष्यश्चाभिगम्यश्च यादोरत्नैरिवार्णवः R. 1. 16.<BR>--2<BR>Modest, shy.<BR>--3 Proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधेनुः|अधेनु
अधेनुः [न. त.] A cow not<BR>yielding milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधैर्य|अधैर्य्य|अधैर्य्यः
अधैर्य a. [न. ब.] Without<BR>self-possession, courage &c., swayed by<BR>excitement.<BR>--र्यं Absence of courage,<BR>firmness or control; excitability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोक्ष
अधोऽक्ष, अधोंशुक, अधोऽक्षज See<BR>under अधस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोंशुक|अधोंशुकं
अधोऽक्ष, अधोंशुक, अधोऽक्षज See<BR>under अधस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अधोक्षज|अधोक्षजः
अधोऽक्ष, अधोंशुक, अधोऽक्षज See<BR>under अधस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्ष|अध्यक्षः
अध्यक्ष a. [अधिगतः अक्षं इंद्रियं<BR>व्यवहारं वा]<BR>1 Perceptible to the senses,<BR>visible; यैरध्यक्षैरथ निजसखं नीरदं<BR>स्मारयद्भिः Bv. 4. 17.<BR>--2 One who exercises<BR>supervision, presiding over.<BR>--क्षः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">Page0052-b+ 56</a>]<BR>1 A superintendent, president, head,<BR>lord, master, controller, ruler;<BR>मयाऽध्यक्षेण प्रकृतिःसूयते सचराचरं Bg. 9. 10;<BR>यदध्यक्षेण जगतां वयमारोपितास्त्वया<BR>Ku. 6. 17; oft. in comp.; गज˚, सेना˚, ग्राम˚,<BR>द्वार˚.<BR>--2 An eye-witness (Ved.).<BR>--3 N. of a plant (क्षीरिका)<BR>Mimusops Kauki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यक्षरं|अध्यक्षर
अध्यक्षरं ind. On the subject of<BR>syllables; above all syllables.<BR>--रं The<BR>mystic syllable ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यग्नि
अध्यग्नि ind. [अग्नौ अग्निसमीपे वा]<BR>Over, by or near the nuptial fire.<BR>--n. (ग्नि) One of the six kinds of<BR>स्त्रीधन (woman's property) mentioned<BR>in Ms. 9. 194; a gift made to a<BR>woman at the time of marriage: विवाहकाले<BR>यत्स्त्रीभ्यो दीयते ह्यग्निसन्निधौ । तदध्यग्निकृतं<BR>सद्भिः स्त्रीधनं परिकीर्तितम् ॥ So<BR>अध्यग्निकृतं-अध्यग्न्युपागतं;<BR>पितृमातृपतिभ्रातृदत्तमध्यग्न्युपागतम् । आधिवेदनिकाद्यं च स्त्रीधनं परिकीर्तितम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यंच्|अध्यञ्च्
अध्यंच् [अधि-अंच्-क्विप्]<BR>1<BR>Tending upwards; superior, eminent.<BR>--2<BR>One who obtains or acquires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यंडा|अध्यण्डा
अध्यंडा [अधिकमंडमिव बीजं यस्याः<BR>सा] N. of two plants (अजशृंगी)<BR>Carpopogon Pruriens, and भूम्यामलकी<BR>Flacourtia Cataphracta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यधि
अध्यधि ind. On high (acc.); ˚धि<BR>लोकं Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यधिक्षेपः|अध्यधिक्षेप
अध्यधिक्षेपः [अधिकः अधिक्षेपः]<BR>Excessive abuse or censure, gross<BR>abuse; Y. 3. 228.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यधीन
अध्यधीन a. [आधिक्येन अधीनः]<BR>Completely subject or dependent, as<BR>a slave; नाध्यधीनो न वक्तव्यो न दस्युर्न<BR>विकर्मकृत् । Ms. 8. 66 (Kull.<BR>अत्यंतपरतंत्रो गर्भदासः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यय|अध्ययः
अध्यय, अध्ययनं &c. See under अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्ययनं|अध्ययन
अध्यय, अध्ययनं &c. See under अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यर्ध|अध्यर्धः
अध्यर्ध a. [अधिकमर्धं यस्य] Having<BR>an additional half; एकाधिकं हरेज्ज्येष्ठः<BR>पुत्रोऽध्यर्धं ततोऽनुजः Ms. 9. 117;<BR>शतमध्यर्धमायता Mb., i. e. 150; ˚योजनशतात्<BR>Pt. 2. 18. (In comp. with a<BR>following noun) Amounting to or worth<BR>one and a half; ˚कंस amounting to<BR>one and a half Kaṃsa; so ˚काकिणीक,<BR>कार्षापण-णिक, ˚खारीक, ˚पण्य, ˚पाद्य, ˚प्रतिक,<BR>˚माष्य, ˚विंशतिकीन, ˚शत-त्य, ˚श-शा-तमान,<BR>˚शाण, ˚शाण्य, ˚शूर्प, ˚सहस्र, ˚सौवर्ण &c.<BR>(P. V. 1. 28-35.).<BR>--र्धः Wind (यदस्मिन्<BR>इदं सर्वं अध्यार्ध्नोत् अधिकमवर्धयत् तेन अध्यर्धः<BR>पवनः इति स्थितम् Bṛ. Up.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यर्बुदं|अध्यर्बुद
अध्यर्बुदं [अधिकं or अधिजातं अर्बुदं]<BR>A tumour, goitre; यज्जायतेऽन्यत्खलु<BR>पूर्वजति ज्ञेयं तदध्यर्बुदमर्बुदज्ञैः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसो
अध्यवसो {c4c} P.<BR>1 To determine,<BR>resolve; कथमिदानीं दुर्जनवचनादेवं<BR>अध्यवसितं देवेन U. 1; अदुर्लभं<BR>मरणमध्यवसितं K. 171; किमध्यवस्यंति गुरवः Ve. 1;<BR>अभिधातुमध्यवससौ न गिरा Śi. 9. 76;<BR>resolve or mean to do.<BR>--2 To attempt,<BR>exert, undertake; मा साहसं अध्यवस्यः<BR>Dk. 123; व्रतं दुष्करमध्यवसितं H. 1.<BR>--3<BR>To grapple with.<BR>--4 To conceive,<BR>apprehend, think; अकार्यं कार्यवदध्यवस्य<BR>Dk. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसानं|अध्यवसान
अध्यवसानं [भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Effort,<BR>determination &c. See अध्यवसाय.<BR>--2 (In<BR>Rhet.) Identification of two things<BR>(प्रकृत and अप्रकृत) in such a manner<BR>that the one is completely absorbed<BR>into the other; निगीर्याध्यवसानं तु<BR>प्रकृतस्य परेण यत् K. P. 10; on such<BR>identification is founded the figure called<BR>अतिशयोक्ति, and the लक्षणा called<BR>साध्यवसाना. See K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायः|अध्यवसाय
अध्यवसायः<BR>1 An attempt, effort,<BR>exertion; न स्वल्पमप्यध्यवसायभीरोः<BR>करोति विज्ञाननिधिर्गुणं हि H. 1. v. l.;<BR>˚सहचरेषु साहसेषु Dk. 161.<BR>--2<BR>Determination, resolution; mental effort<BR>or apprehension; संभावनं नाम<BR>अस्तित्वाध्यवसायः P. VI. 2. 21.<BR>--3<BR>Perseverance, diligence, energy,<BR>constancy; तत्कोयं पदे पदे<BR>महाननध्यवसायः U. 4 absence of energy or<BR>resolution, drooping of spirits;<BR>(with महानध्यवसायः as the reading,<BR>the meaning would be ‘why this<BR>effort on your part i. e. to determine<BR>whether you should go or not,<BR>hesitation’.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसायिन्
अध्यवसायिन् a. [सो-णिनि]<BR>Attempting; resolute, persevering, energetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवसित
अध्यवसित p. p. Attempted,<BR>mentally apprehended, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यवहननं|अध्यवहनन
अध्यवहननं [अधि उपरि अवहननं]<BR>Beating again what is being<BR>threshed and peeled (पूर्वावघातेन वितुषीकरणेपि<BR>पुनरवघातः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यशनं|अध्यशन
अध्यशनं [अधिकमशनं] Excessive<BR>eating, eating again before the last<BR>meal is digested; साजीर्णे भुज्यते यत्तु<BR>तदध्यशनमुच्यते Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्थि
अध्यस्थि n. [अधिरूढमस्थि] A<BR>bone growing over another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्
अध्यस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To place upon<BR>another, add or append to.<BR>--2 (In<BR>Phil.) To attribute or ascribe falsely,<BR>attribute the nature of one thing<BR>to another; सर्वो हि पुरोऽवस्थिते<BR>विषये विषयांतरमध्यस्यति,<BR>बाह्यधर्मानात्मन्यध्यस्यति Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यस्त|अध्यस्तं
अध्यस्त p. p. [अस्-क्त]<BR>1 Placed<BR>upon or over.<BR>--2 Attributed,<BR>wrongly ascribed or supposed; as शुक्तौ<BR>रजतमध्यस्तं, ब्रह्मणि जगदध्यस्तं &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासः|अध्यास
अध्यासः [अस्-घञ्]<BR>1 False<BR>attribution, wrong supposition (मिथ्याज्ञानं,<BR>अतस्मिंस्तद्बुद्धिः or अयथार्थानुभवः); स्मृतिरूपः<BR>परत्र पूर्वदृष्टावभासः; for full explanation<BR>see Ś. B. 8-22 and अध्यारोप also.<BR>--2<BR>An appendage.<BR>--3 Putting down<BR>upon; पादाध्यासे शतं दमः Y. 2. 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याक्रम्
अध्याक्रम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To fix upon, to<BR>occupy.<BR>--2 To attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याक्रांत
अध्याक्रांत a. Taken possession of,<BR>occupied; ˚ता वसतिरमुना Ś. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्म
अध्यात्म a. [आत्मनः संबद्धं, आत्मनि<BR>अधिकृतं वा] Belonging to self or<BR>person; concerning an individual.<BR>--त्मं ind. [आत्मानमधिकृत्य] Concerning<BR>self.<BR>--त्मं The supreme spirit<BR>(manifested as the individual self) or<BR>the relation between the supreme<BR>and the individual soul; अक्षरं ब्रह्म<BR>परमं स्वभावोऽध्यात्ममुच्यते Bg. 8. 3<BR>(स्वस्यैव ब्रह्मण एवांशतया जीवस्वरूपेण भावो<BR>भवनं स एव आत्मानं देहमधिकृत्य भोक्तृत्वेन<BR>वर्तमानोऽध्यात्मशब्देनोच्यते Śrīdhara.)<BR>‘Brahma is the supreme, the<BR>indestructible; its manifestation (as an<BR>individual self) is अध्यात्म’ --Telang's<BR>Bhagavadgītā; ˚चेतसा 3. 30.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञानं --विद्या knowledge of the<BR>supreme spirit or आत्मन्, theosophical<BR>or metaphysical knowledge (the<BR>doctrines taught by the<BR>Upanishads &c.); त्रयी विग्रहवत्येव<BR>सममध्यात्मविद्यया M. 1. 14; ˚विद्या विद्यानां वादः<BR>प्रवदतामहम् Bg. 10. 32 (अध्यात्मविद्या<BR>न्यायवैशेषिकमते देहभिन्नत्वेन, सांख्यादिमते<BR>प्रकृतिभिन्नत्वेन आत्मनः स्वरूपादिप्रतिपादिका,<BR>वैदांतिमते तु ब्रह्माभिन्नत्वेन इति भेदः; सर्वेषां<BR>मतेऽपि आत्मतत्त्वज्ञानरूपत्वात्तस्या<BR>अध्यात्मविद्यात्वम्.).<BR>--दृश्, --विद् a. [अध्यात्मं<BR>पश्यति वेत्ति वा] one proficient in this<BR>knowledge; नह्यनध्यात्मवित्कश्चित्<BR>क्रियाफलमुपाश्नुते Ms. 6. 82.<BR>--योगः [<BR>आत्मानं क्षेत्रज्ञमधिकृत्य योगः] concentration<BR>of the mind on the Ātman drawing it<BR>off from all objects of sense.<BR>--रति a.<BR>[स. ब.] one who delights in the<BR>contemplation of the supreme spirit;<BR>Ms. 6. 49.<BR>--रामायणं N. of a<BR>Rāmāyaṇa which treats of the relation<BR>between the supreme and the<BR>individual soul, while it narrates Rāma's<BR>story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यात्मिक
अध्यात्मिक a. (की f.) Relating to<BR>अध्यात्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापक|अध्यापकः
अध्यापक --पनं, अध्याय See under<BR>अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यापनं|अध्यापन
अध्यापक --पनं, अध्याय See under<BR>अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याय|अध्यायः
अध्यापक --पनं, अध्याय See under<BR>अधी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारुह्
अध्यारुह् {c1c} P. To ascend, mount;<BR>विष्णुपदं द्वितीयमध्यारुरोहेव रजश्छलेन<BR>R. 16. 28; (fig.) to gain ascendancy<BR>over, domineer or lord it over; लतेव<BR>विटपकानध्यारोहति K. 105;<BR>बुद्धिहीनोऽत्युच्छ्रितोऽपि भूभृत्<BR>परैरध्यारुह्यमाणमात्मानं न चेतयते Dk. 154. --Caus. [-रोहयति]<BR>1 To cause to ascend, mount or<BR>sit in.<BR>--2 (-रोपयति) (a) To place one<BR>in, entrust or appoint to; to cause,<BR>produce, bring about; कुसुमायुधस्य<BR>दुर्जयतामध्यारोपयंती K. 148; कस्य न<BR>बंधुत्वमध्यारोपयसि 202. (b) To<BR>attribute falsely; दोषानपि<BR>गुणपक्षमध्यारोपयद्भिः K. 108 (falsely)<BR>representing even vices as virtues. (c) To<BR>overdo, exaggerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारूढ|अध्यारूढः
अध्यारूढ p. p.<BR>1 Mounted,<BR>ascended.<BR>--2 Raised above, elevated.<BR>--3<BR>Above, superior to, more than (with<BR>instr.); below, inferior; ततोऽ<BR>ध्यारूढानां पदमसुजनद्वेषजननं Mu. 5. 12 of<BR>those in high office; आयुधपरिग्रहं<BR>यावदध्यारूढो दुर्योगः U. 6 my insolence<BR>went the length of taking up arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोपः|अध्यारोप
अध्यारोपः<BR>1 Raising, elevating &c.<BR>--2 (In Vedānta phil.) Act of<BR>attributing falsely or through mistake;<BR>erroneously attributing the properties<BR>of one thing to another; considering<BR>through mistake a rope (which is not<BR>really a serpent) to be a serpent, or<BR>considering Brahma (which is not<BR>really the material world) to be the<BR>material world; असर्पभूतरज्जौ<BR>सर्पारोपवत्, अजगद्रूपे ब्रह्मणि जगद्रूपारोपवत्, वस्तुनि<BR>अवस्त्वारोपोऽध्यारोपः Vedāntasāra.<BR>--3<BR>Erroneous knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोपणं|अध्यारोपण
अध्यारोपणं<BR>1 Raising &c.; अलीक˚<BR>K. 222, 108.<BR>--2 Sowing (seed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यारोपित
अध्यारोपित p. p. Falsely attributed<BR>or supposed; hyperbolical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावापः|अध्यावाप
अध्यावापः [अधि-आ-वप्-घञ्]<BR>1 Act<BR>of sowing or scattering (seed &c.).<BR>--2 [आधारे घञ्] A field wherein<BR>seed &c. is sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यावाहनिकं|अध्यावाहनिक
अध्यावाहनिकं [अध्यावाहनं<BR>पितृगृहात्पतिगृहगमनं, तत्काले लब्धं; लब्धार्थे ठन्]<BR>One of the six kinds of स्त्रीधन or<BR>woman's property, the property<BR>which she receives when leaving<BR>her father's house for her husband's;<BR>यत् पुनर्लभते नारी नीयमाना तु पैतृकात् (गृहात्) ।<BR>अध्यावाहनिकं नाम स्त्रीधनं परिकीर्तितम् ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यास्
अध्यास् {c2c} A.<BR>1 (a) To lie down,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">Page0053-c+ 57</a>]<BR>settle upon; occupy, dwell in (as a<BR>seat or habitation); seat oneself in<BR>or upon, enter upon, get into (as a<BR>path &c.) (with acc. of place);<BR>त्वरिततरमध्यास्यतामियं वनस्थली K. 28;<BR>36, 40; पर्णशालामध्यास्य R. 1. 95;<BR>द्वितीयमाश्रममध्यासितुं समयः V. 5;<BR>द्वारदेशमध्यास्ते Dk. 3 is waiting at the door;<BR>R. 2. 17; 4. 74; 6. 10; 12. 85; 13. 22, 76;<BR>15. 93; Me. 76; Bk. 1. 5; Ms. 7. 77;<BR>अये सिंहासनमध्यास्ते वृषलः Mu. 3;<BR>भगवत्या प्राश्निकपदमध्यासितव्यं M. 1<BR>occupy the seat of judge, accept the<BR>office of judge. (b) To take<BR>possession of, grasp, seize; धेन्वा<BR>तदध्यासितकातराक्ष्या R. 2. 52 with eyes<BR>tremulous on account of her being seized<BR>by him (अध्यासितं = आक्रमणं). (c) To<BR>resort to, inhabit;<BR>यदध्यासितमर्हद्भिस्तद्धि तीर्थं प्रचक्षते Ku. 6. 56.<BR>--2 To live<BR>in conjugal relation; cohabit with.<BR>--3 To be directed or fixed upon.<BR>--4<BR>To rule, govern, influence; affect,<BR>concern (mostly Ved.). --Caus. To<BR>cause one to sit down upon;<BR>भवंतमध्यासयन्नासनं Bk. 2. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासनं|अध्यासन
अध्यासनं<BR>1 Sitting down upon,<BR>occupying, presiding over.<BR>--2 A seat,<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यासः|अध्यास
अध्यासः See under अध्यस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहारः|अध्याहार
अध्याहारः --हरणं<BR>1 Supplying an<BR>ellipsis (आकांक्षाविषयपदानुसंधानं).<BR>--2<BR>Arguing; inferring; new<BR>supposition; inference or conjecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्याहरणं|अध्याहरण
अध्याहारः --हरणं<BR>1 Supplying an<BR>ellipsis (आकांक्षाविषयपदानुसंधानं).<BR>--2<BR>Arguing; inferring; new<BR>supposition; inference or conjecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युष्ट|अध्युष्टः
अध्युष्ट a. (Ety?) Coiled up three<BR>and a halftimes; ˚वलयः a snake<BR>forming a ring coiled up three and a half<BR>times; अवाप्य स्वां भूमिं<BR>भुजगनिभमध्युष्टवलयं स्वमात्मानं कृत्वा Ā. L. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्युष्ट्रः|अध्युष्ट्र
अध्युष्ट्रः [अधिगतः उष्ट्रं वाहनत्वेन] A<BR>carriage drawn or borne by camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूढ|अध्यूढः
अध्यूढ a. [अधि उपरि ऊढः]<BR>1 Raised,<BR>exalted, elevated, hanging over.<BR>--2<BR>Abundant, increased, copious.<BR>--3<BR>Rich, affluent.<BR>--ढः Śiva.<BR>--ढा A<BR>wife whose husband has married<BR>another wife and thus superseded her<BR>(= अधिविन्ना q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूध्नी
अध्यूध्नी [अधिकं ऊधो यस्याः अनङ्<BR>ङीप् च]<BR>1 A cow with full and fat<BR>udders.<BR>--2 The vessel (in the body)<BR>above the udder or above the<BR>scrotum; perhaps urethra (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूह्
अध्यूह् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To overlay, place<BR>on or upon.<BR>--2 To raise above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्यूहनं|अध्यूहन
अध्यूहनं Putting of a layer (of<BR>ashes &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्येषणं|अध्येषण
अध्येषणं [अधि-इष् प्रेरणे-ल्युट्]<BR>Causing one to do a thing, especially<BR>a preceptor &c, as an honorific duty.<BR>--णा [अधिका एषणा प्रार्थना]<BR>Solicitation, entreaty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रि
अध्रि a. [न-धृ-कि] Not<BR>restrained, irresistible.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गु-गू a.<BR>[अध्रि-गम्-कू-डिच् ऊङादेशोवा] of<BR>irresistible motion or course (अधृतगमन),<BR>impetuous; यदध्रिगावो अग्निगू इदा चिदह्नो<BR>अश्विना Rv. 8. 22. 11<BR>--(गुः) N. of a<BR>heavenly killer of sacrificial victims, or<BR>the name of the formula itself<BR>ending with an invocation of Agni.<BR>--ज a. [अध्रिं जनयति, जन्-ड] making<BR>irresistible.<BR>--पुष्पलिका the<BR>betelnut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रियमाण
अध्रियमाण a.<BR>1 Not held, not to be<BR>got hold of; not forthcoming.<BR>--2<BR>Not surviving, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुव
अध्रुव a.<BR>1 Uncertain, doubtful.<BR>--2<BR>Unsteady, moving, not fixed or<BR>permanent; स्वांगेऽध्रुवे P. III. 4. 54;<BR>separable (which can be severed or<BR>detached without fatal or disastrous<BR>effects) (येन विना न जीवनं सो ऽध्रुवः Sk.)<BR>--वं An uncertainty; यो ध्रुवाणि<BR>परित्यज्य अध्रुवाणि निषेवते । ध्रुवाणि तस्य<BR>नश्यंति अध्रुवं नष्टमेव च; cf. the English<BR>phrase ‘A bird in the hand is worth<BR>two in the bush.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्रुषः|अध्रुष
अध्रुषः Quinsy; a kind of disease<BR>attended with fever arising from the<BR>affection of blood; शोथः<BR>स्थूलस्तोददाहप्रकाशो रक्ताज्ज्ञेयः सोऽध्रुषो रुग्ज्वराढ्यः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्
अध्वन् m. [अत्ति बलं; अद्-क्वनिप्<BR>धादेशः Uṇ. 4. 115; perhaps from अत्<BR>also]<BR>1 (a) A way, road;<BR>passage, orbit (of planets &c.);<BR>मुक्ताध्वानं ये लंघयेयुर्भवंतं Me. 54. (b)<BR>Distance, space (traversed or to be<BR>traversed); पंचदशयोजनमात्रमध्वानं<BR>जगाम K. 119, 120; कियत्यध्वनि सा<BR>उज्जयिनी 207; Dk. 13; अपि लंघितमध्वानं<BR>बुबुधे न बुधोपमः R. 1. 47; उल्लंघिताध्वा<BR>Me. 45; कालाध्वनोरत्यंतसंयोगे &c.<BR>(c) Journey, travel, course,<BR>march; नैकः प्रपद्येताध्वानं Ms. 4. 60<BR>undertake a journey; अध्वसु त्रिषु<BR>विसृष्टमैथिलः R. 11. 57 after three<BR>marches; परिक्लांतः किलाध्वना Ki. 11. 2<BR>way-worn; U. 1. 34; Me. 17, 38;<BR>अध्वा वर्णकफस्थौल्यसौकुमार्यविनाशनः<BR>Suśr.<BR>--2 A recension of the Vedas<BR>and the school upholding it (<BR>शाखा, अवयव); एकविंशत्यध्वयुक्तमृग्वेदमृषयो विदुः ।<BR>सहस्राध्वा सामवेदो यजुरेकशताध्वकं ॥ अध्वा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-b" target="_blank">Page0054-b+ 57</a>]<BR>देवगतिः शाखा इति पर्यायवाचकाः ।<BR>--3<BR>Time (Kāla), time personified,<BR>(being the eater of all).<BR>--4 Air;<BR>sky, atmosphere.<BR>--5 Place.<BR>--6<BR>Means, resource; method.<BR>--7 Attack<BR>(अधिकदुरारोहणं). अध्वन् is changed to<BR>अध्व after prepositions; प्राध्वः, व्यध्वः<BR>&c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिः [अध्वानमतति,<BR>अत्-इ] {1} a traveller. {2} an<BR>intelligent person.<BR>--अधिपः, --ईशः [ष.<BR>त.] an officer in charge of the<BR>public roads.<BR>--अयनं [अध्वन्ययनं]<BR>journey, travel.<BR>--गः {1} one who travels;<BR>a traveller, wayfarer;<BR>संतानकतरुच्छायासुप्तविद्याधराध्वगं Ku. 6. 46 (<BR>˚गामिन्). {2} a camel. {3} a mule. {4} the<BR>sun; ˚भोग्यः N. of a tree, Spondias<BR>Mangifera (आम्रातकवृक्ष) अध्वगैः<BR>अयत्नलभ्यफलत्वात् भोग्यः.<BR>--(गा) the Ganges.<BR>--गत् m. [अध्वानं गच्छति; गम्-क्विप्<BR>P. VI. 4. 40] a traveller.<BR>--गत्यंतः --गंतव्यः<BR>[ष. त.] measure of length<BR>applicable to roads; देशकालाध्वगंतव्यः Vārt.<BR>--जा [अध्वनि जायते; जन्-ड] A plant<BR>(स्वर्णुली or स्वर्णपुष्पी).<BR>--पतिः {1} the sun<BR>(दिवैव पथिकानां गमनात् रात्रौ च<BR>गमननिषेधात् सूर्यस्य अध्वपालकत्वं or अध्वनः<BR>आकाशस्य पतिः). {2} inspector of the road.<BR>--रथः [अध्वने हितः पर्याप्तो रथः शाक. त.]<BR>{1} a travelling coach. {2} [अध्वैव रथो यस्य]<BR>a messenger skilled in travelling<BR>(पथि प्रज्ञो दूतः).<BR>--शल्यः [अध्वनि<BR>शल्यमिव आचरतीति क्विप्-अच् Tv.] N. of a<BR>tree (अपामार्ग) (अध्वगानां पादवस्त्रादौ<BR>शल्यवद्वेधकारकत्वात् तथात्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वनीन|अध्वनीनः
अध्वनीन, अध्वन्य a. [अध्वानं अलं<BR>गच्छति; अध्वन्-ख-यत् वा; अध्वनो यत्खौ<BR>P. V. 2. 16] Able to undertake a<BR>journey, speeding on a journey; क्षिप्रं<BR>ततो ऽध्वन्यतुरंगयायी Bk. 2. 44.<BR>--नः, --न्यः A traveller going fast, wayfarer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वन्य|अध्वन्यः
अध्वनीन, अध्वन्य a. [अध्वानं अलं<BR>गच्छति; अध्वन्-ख-यत् वा; अध्वनो यत्खौ<BR>P. V. 2. 16] Able to undertake a<BR>journey, speeding on a journey; क्षिप्रं<BR>ततो ऽध्वन्यतुरंगयायी Bk. 2. 44.<BR>--नः, --न्यः A traveller going fast, wayfarer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर|अध्वरः
अध्वर a. [न ध्वरति कुटिलो न भवति<BR>ध्वृ-अच्. न. त.; ध्वरतिर्हिंसाकर्मा<BR>तत्प्रतिषेधो निपातः अहिंस्रः Nir.]<BR>1 Not crooked,<BR>not broken, uninterrupted; इमं<BR>यज्ञमवतामध्वरं नः Yv. 27. 17 (अध्वरं =<BR>अकुटिलं शास्त्रोक्तं).<BR>--2 Intent, attentive.<BR>--3 Durable, sound.<BR>--रः [अध्वानं<BR>सत्पथं राति ददाति फलत्वेन, रा-क] A<BR>sacrifice, a religious ceremony; also<BR>a Soma sacrifice; तमध्वरे विश्वजिति<BR>R. 5. 1.<BR>--रः --रं<BR>1 Sky or air (<BR>आकाश).<BR>--2 The second of the 8 Vasus.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कल्पा an optional<BR>sacrifice (काम्येष्टि).<BR>--कांडं [ष. त.] part of<BR>the शतपथब्राह्मण which treats of<BR>sacrifices.<BR>--ग [अध्वरं गच्छति]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">Page0054-c+ 57</a>]<BR>intended for a sacrifice.<BR>--दीक्षणीया [ष. त.]<BR>consecration connected with an<BR>Adhvara; so ˚प्रायश्चित्तिः an expiation<BR>&c.<BR>--मीमांसा [ष. त.] N. of<BR>Jaimini's Pūrvamīmāṃsā.<BR>--श्रीः [ष. त.]<BR>glory of the Adhvara.<BR>--समिष्टयजुः<BR>n. N. of an aggregate of libations<BR>connected with a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वरीयति
अध्वरीयति, अध्वर्यति Den. P. To<BR>desire to have a sacrifice performed;<BR>or to perform one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्यति
अध्वरीयति, अध्वर्यति Den. P. To<BR>desire to have a sacrifice performed;<BR>or to perform one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वर्युः|अध्वर्यु|अध्वर्य्यु|अध्वर्य्युः
अध्वर्युः [अध्वरमधीते Nir.; अध्वर-क्यच्<BR>--युच् ततोंऽत्याकारलोपः Tv.]<BR>1 Any<BR>officiating priest, technically<BR>distinguished from होतृ, उद्गातृ and ब्रह्मन्. His<BR>duty was “to measure the ground,<BR>build the altar, prepare sacrificial<BR>vessels, to fetch wood and water,<BR>light the fire, bring the animal and<BR>immolate it,” and while doing this<BR>to repeat the Yajurveda; होता प्रथमं<BR>शंसति तमध्वर्युः प्रोत्साहयति Sk. See अच्छावाक<BR>also.<BR>--2 The Yajurveda itself. --pl.<BR>Adherents of that Veda.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वेदः Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वस्मन्
अध्वस्मन् a. [ध्वंस् मनिन् किच्च न. त.]<BR>Imperishable; bright (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अध्वांतं|अध्वान्त|अध्वान्तः
अध्वांतं [न. त.] Twilight, gloom,<BR>slight darkness, shade.<BR>--तः [ष. त.]<BR>End of the journey.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शात्रवः<BR>[अध्वांतस्य मार्गसीमायाः शात्रव इव Tv.]<BR>A plant (श्चोनाक) Cassia Fistula or<BR>Bignonia Indica (blossoming in<BR>shade).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्
अन् {c2c} P. [अनिति, आन-नी-त्, आन, अनितुं,<BR>अनित]<BR>1 To breathe; आनीदवातं<BR>स्वधया तदेकं Rv. 10. 129. 2.<BR>--2 To move,<BR>go about, live; को ह्येवान्यात् यद्येष<BR>आकाश आनंदो न स्यात् T. Up.<BR>--3<BR>To gasp, pant with thirst (Ved.)<BR>--Caus. आनयति; desid. अनिनिषति. -- (4<BR>A.) To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्
अन् m. [क्विप्] The soul; विश्वे<BR>चनेदना Rv. 4. 30. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनः|अन
अनः [अन्-अच्] Breath, respiration;<BR>प्राणोऽपानो व्यान उदानः समानोऽनः इत्येतत्सर्वं<BR>प्राण इति Bṛ. Up. [cf. L. animus,<BR>Gr. anemos].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननं|अनन
अननं [अन् ल्युट्] Act of breathing,<BR>living &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंश
अनंश a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Not entitled to<BR>a share in the inheritance; ˚शौ<BR>क्लीबपतितौ जात्यंधबधिरौ तथा ।<BR>उन्मत्तजडमूकाश्च ये च केचिन्निरिंद्रियाः ॥ Ms. 9. 201.<BR>Other persons are also mentioned<BR>by Devala, Baudhāyana, Kātyāyana<BR>and Nārada.<BR>--2 Without parts,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">Page0055-a+ 56</a>]<BR>undivided, portionless; an epithet<BR>of the sky or the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0054-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंशुमत्फला
अनंशुमत्फला [न अंशुमत्<BR>मोचकाभ्यंतरस्यत्वात् फलं यस्याः] The plantain<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक|अनकः
अनक a. Mean, base; See अणक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्ष्
अनक्ष् a. [न अक्ष्णोति व्याप्नोति<BR>विषयमिंद्रियेण, अक्ष्-क्विप् न. त.] Without sight,<BR>blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्ष|अनक्षः
अनक्ष a.<BR>1 Without an axle-tree.<BR>--2 Sightless, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनकदुंदुभिः|अनकदुन्दुभि|अनकदुन्दुभिः
अनकदुंदुभिः = आनकदुंदुभि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनकस्मात्
अनकस्मात् ind. [न. त.] Not<BR>causelessly, not suddenly or<BR>accidentally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षर|अनक्षरं
अनक्षर a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Unable to<BR>speak, mute, dumb, unlettered;<BR>मुखमनक्षरं स्वाकृतेः Bh. 2. 56.<BR>--2<BR>Unfit to be uttered.<BR>--रं [<BR>अप्रशस्तान्यक्षराणि यत्र] Abusive language, foul<BR>or abusive words, censure. --adv.<BR>Without the use of words, not<BR>expressed by words, mutely, dumbly;<BR>˚रं पप्रच्छ K. 219, 143; ˚व्यंजितदौर्हृदेन<BR>R. 14. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनक्षि
अनक्षि n. [अप्रशस्तं अक्षि] A bad eye,<BR>weak eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनगार|अनगारः
अनगार a. [न. ब.] Houseless.<BR>--रः<BR>A vagrant ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनगारिका
अनगारिका The houseless state of<BR>a vagrant ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनग्नि|अनग्निः
अनग्नि [न. त.]<BR>1 Non-fire,<BR>substance other than fire; यदधीतमविज्ञातं<BR>निगदेनैव शब्द्यते । अनग्नाविव शुष्कैधो न तज्ज्वलति<BR>कर्हिचित् Nir.<BR>--2 Absence of fire. --a.<BR>1<BR>Not requiring fire, dispensing with<BR>fire, without the use of fire; विदधे<BR>विधिमस्य नैष्ठिकं यतिभिः सार्धमनग्निमग्निचित्<BR>R. 8. 25; said of a sacrifice also (<BR>अग्निचयनरहितो यज्ञः).<BR>--2 Not maintaining the<BR>sacred fire; अनग्निरनिकेतः<BR>स्यान्मुनिर्मूलफलाशनः Ms. 6. 25, 43; irreligious,<BR>impious.<BR>--3 Dyspeptic.<BR>--4 Unmarried.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--त्र-त्रा a. Ved. not<BR>maintaining the sacred fire, sinful,<BR>irreligious Rv. 1. 189. 3.<BR>--दग्ध a. Not<BR>burnt with fire or on the funeral<BR>pile, Rv. 10. 15. 14 (श्मशानकर्म न<BR>प्राप्ताः); a class of Manes Ms. 3. 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनघ|अनघः
अनघ a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Sinless, innocent;<BR>अवैमि चैनामनघेति R. 14. 40.<BR>--2 Free<BR>from blame, faultless, handsome;<BR>रूपमनघं Ś. 2. 10; यस्य<BR>ज्ञानदयासिंधोरगाधस्यानघा गुणाः Ak.; ˚सर्वगात्री Dk. 123.<BR>--3 Without mishap or accident, free<BR>from danger, calamity &c.; safe,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">Page0055-b+ 57</a>]<BR>unhurt; यास्त्वामनघमद्राक्ष्म Dk. 108;<BR>कच्चिन्मृगीणामनघा प्रसूतिः R. 5. 7;<BR>मृगवधूर्यदा अनघप्रसवा भवति Ś. 4 safely<BR>delivered or brought to bed; ˚प्रसूतेः<BR>R. 14. 75.<BR>--4 Without grief or sorrow;<BR>दयालुमनघस्पृष्टं R. 10. 19.<BR>--5 Free from<BR>dirt, impurities &c., pure, spotless;<BR>R. 13. 65; 10. 80; Śi. 3, 31.<BR>--घः<BR>1<BR>White mustard.<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu;<BR>अनघो विजयो जेता; also of Śiva and of<BR>several other persons, a Gandharva,<BR>Sādhya &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंकुश|अनङ्कुश
अनंकुश a. [अंकुशेन अवश्यः]<BR>1<BR>Ungovernable, unruly.<BR>--2 Taking<BR>license (as a poet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंग|अनङ्ग|अनङ्गं|अनङ्गः
अनंग a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Bodiless, without<BR>a body; formless, incorporeal;<BR>त्वमनंगः कथमक्षता रतिः Ku. 4. 9.<BR>--2<BR>Different from the body.<BR>--3 Without a<BR>supplement or auxiliary.<BR>--गः Cupid<BR>(the bodiless one; so called from<BR>his having been reduced to ashes by<BR>Śiva with the fire of his third eye,<BR>when he tried to seduce the God's<BR>mind towards Pārvatī for the birth<BR>of a deliverer of the gods from<BR>Tāraka).<BR>--गं<BR>1 Sky, air, ether.<BR>--2<BR>The mind (आकाशस्य निरवयवत्वात्<BR>न्यायवैशेषिकमते चित्तस्य अगुणत्वेन तस्य<BR>तथात्वं).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्रीडा [तृ. त.] {1} amorous<BR>sports. {2} N. of a metre of two lines,<BR>the first with 16 long, and second<BR>with 32 short, syllables.<BR>--द a. [उप.<BR>स.] inspiring love; ˚देतनुभूते भुजलते<BR>K. 220 (also without Aṅgada);<BR>बाह्वोरनंगदत्वस्य बाले ते कारणे उभे Bhār.<BR>Ch.<BR>--द्वादशी N. of the 83rd chapter of<BR>भविष्योत्तरपुराण; ˚त्रयोदशीवतं, see under<BR>व्रत.<BR>--लेखः (मदनलेखः) a love letter;<BR>˚लेखक्रिययोपयोगं (व्रजंति) Ku. 1. 7.<BR>--रंगः N. of an erotic work<BR>describing the several postures (<BR>आसन) pertaining to sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR>--शत्रुः, --असुहृत् &c. N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--शेखरः N. of a metre of four<BR>lines, each with 15 iambic feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंगकं|अनङ्गक|अनङ्गकं
अनंगकं The mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंगुरि|अनङ्गुरि
अनंगुरि --लि a. [न. ब.] Destitute<BR>of fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंगुलि
अनंगुरि --लि a. [न. ब.] Destitute<BR>of fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनच्छ|अनच्छः
अनच्छ a. Not clear, dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनजका
अनजका, अनजिका [अप्रशस्ता अजा]<BR>A miserable or small goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनजिका
अनजका, अनजिका [अप्रशस्ता अजा]<BR>A miserable or small goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंजन|अनञ्जन|अनञ्जनं
अनंजन a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Without<BR>collyrium, pigment, or paint; नेत्रे दूरमनंजने<BR>S. D.<BR>--2 Faultless, taintless.<BR>--3<BR>Without any connection (निःसंबंध).<BR>--नं<BR>1 The sky, atmosphere.<BR>--2 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">Page0055-c+ 56</a>]<BR>supreme spirit (परब्रह्म), Viṣṇu or<BR>Nārāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुह्
अनडुह् m. [अनः शकटं वहति] (<BR>अनड्वान्, ˚ड्वाहौ, ˚डुद्भ्यां &c.)<BR>1 An ox, bull.<BR>--2<BR>The sign Taurus.<BR>--ही or अनड्वाही A<BR>cow.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जिह्वा [अनडुहो जिह्वेव<BR>पत्राणि यस्याः सा] a plant (गोजिह्वा) (<BR>अनंतमूल.)<BR>--द a. [उप. स.] a giver<BR>of oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुत्क
अनडुत्क a. Having oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनडुहः|अनडुह
अनडुहः N. of a sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनणु|अनणुः
अनणु a. [न. त.] Not small or<BR>minute or fine, coarse.<BR>--णुः Coarse<BR>grain, peas &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनति
अनति ind. Not very much;<BR>compounds beginning with अनति may be<BR>analysed by referring to अति; e. g.<BR>अनतिक्रमः moderation; अनतिक्रमणीय not<BR>to be transgressed, inviolable;<BR>अनतिदृश्य opaque; अनतिद्भुत unsurpassed, real,<BR>true, proper; अनतिव्याध्य invulnerable;<BR>अनत्यंतगति sense of diminutive words;<BR>अनत्यय imperishable, undecaying &c.;<BR>अनतिप्रश्न्य^1 not to be asked to excess;<BR>अनतिविलंबिता absence of delay;<BR>fluency as a speaker's qualification, one<BR>of the 35 Vāgguṇas, q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by @aumsanskrit on 20251225. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/104  ap90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्धा
अनद्धा ind. [न. त.] Ved. Not<BR>truly or clearly, not certainly or<BR>definitely.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरुषः not a true<BR>man; one who is not of use, either to<BR>gods, men or the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्यः|अनद्य
अनद्यः [न अद्यः भक्ष्यः अप्राशस्त्ये नञ्]<BR>White mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनद्यतन|अनद्यतनः
अनद्यतन a. (नी f.) [न. त.] Not<BR>pertaining to this or the current day;<BR>a term used by Pāṇini to denote<BR>the sense of the Imperfect or the<BR>Periphrastic future P. III. 2. 111,<BR>III. 3. 15; ˚भूते लङ्-अपचत्; ˚ने<BR>भविष्यति लुट्-पक्ता; परोक्षानद्यतने लिट् पपाच.<BR>--नः Not the current day; अतीतायाः<BR>रात्रेः पश्चार्धेन आगामिन्या रात्रेः पूर्वार्धेन सहितो<BR>दिवसोऽद्यतनः Sk., तद्भिन्नः कालः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिक
अनधिक a. [न. त.]<BR>1 Not more or<BR>excessive.<BR>--2 Boundless; perfect.<BR>--3 Not capable of being enlarged<BR>or surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारः|अनधिकार
अनधिकारः [न. त.] Absence of<BR>authority, right, claim &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चर्चा intermeddling, officiousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिकारिन्
अनधिकारिन् a. Not entitled to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधिगत|अनधिगतः
अनधिगत a. [न. त.] Not obtained,<BR>acquired or studied.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मनोरथ a. foiled in one's expectations.<BR>--शास्त्र a. who has not learnt the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनधीन|अनधीनः
अनधीन a. [न. त.] Independent.<BR>--नः --नकः [संज्ञायां कन्] An<BR>independent carpenter working on his own<BR>account (कौटतक्षः); स हि कुट्यां वसन्<BR>न कस्यचिदधीनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्यक्ष|अनध्यक्षः
अनध्यक्ष a. [न. त.]<BR>1 Not<BR>perceptible or observable, invisible;<BR>मनोऽपि न तथाज्ञानादनध्यक्षं तदा भवेत् ।<BR>Bhāṣā P.<BR>--2 Without<BR>controller or ruler &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्यायः|अनध्याय
अनध्यायः, अनध्ययनं [न. त.] Not<BR>studying, intermission of study;<BR>the time when there is or ought<BR>to be such intermission, a holiday<BR>(˚दिवसः); अद्य शिष्टानध्यायः U. 4 a<BR>holiday (given) in honor of<BR>distinguished guests. See Ms. 2. 105-6;<BR>4. 103-4; 105-8, 117-8, 126 &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनध्ययनं|अनध्ययन
अनध्यायः, अनध्ययनं [न. त.] Not<BR>studying, intermission of study;<BR>the time when there is or ought<BR>to be such intermission, a holiday<BR>(˚दिवसः); अद्य शिष्टानध्यायः U. 4 a<BR>holiday (given) in honor of<BR>distinguished guests. See Ms. 2. 105-6;<BR>4. 103-4; 105-8, 117-8, 126 &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुभावक
अननुभावक^1 a. Unable to<BR>comprehend; ˚ता non-comprehension,<BR>unintelligibility.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by @aumsanskrit on 20251225. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/104  ap90. note: headword change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अननुभाषणं|अननुभाषण
अननुभाषणं<BR>1 Not repeating a<BR>statement or proposition.<BR>--2 Tacit<BR>assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंत|अनन्त|अनन्तं|अनन्तः
अनंत a. [नास्ति अंतो यस्य] Endless,<BR>infinite, eternal, boundless,<BR>inexhaustible; ˚रत्नप्रभवस्य यस्य Ku. 1. 3.<BR>--तः<BR>1 N. of Viṣṇu; गंधर्वाप्सरसः सिद्धाः<BR>किन्नरोरगचारणाः । नांतं गुणानां जानंति (<BR>नास्यांतमधिगच्छंति) तेनानंतोऽयमुच्यते ॥; also of<BR>Viṣṇu's couch, the serpent Śeṣa;<BR>of Kṛṣṇa and his brother; of<BR>Śiva, the 14th Arhat; Vāsuki, the<BR>lord of serpents.<BR>--2 A cloud.<BR>--3 Talc.<BR>--4 N. of a plant (सिंदुवार) Vitex<BR>Trifolia.<BR>--5 The 23rd asterism श्रवण.<BR>--6 A<BR>silken cord with 14 knots tied round<BR>the right arm on the अनंतचतुर्दशी day.<BR>--7 The letter आ.<BR>--ता<BR>1 The earth (the<BR>endless).<BR>--2 The number one.<BR>--3 N. of<BR>various females; of Pārvatī.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>various plants; शारिवा, अनंतमूल (a very<BR>medicinal plant) दूर्वा, आमलकी, गुडूची,<BR>अग्निमंथ, कणा, लांगली, दुरालभा, हरीतकी,<BR>अग्निशिखा, श्यामलता, पिप्पली.<BR>--ती A<BR>small silken cord tied round the<BR>left arm of a woman.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The<BR>sky, atmosphere.<BR>--2 Infinity,<BR>eternity.<BR>--3 Absolution, final beatitude;<BR>तदनंताय कल्पते Pt. 2. 72.<BR>--4 The<BR>supreme spirit, Brahma (परब्रह्म); सत्यं<BR>ज्ञानमनंतंब्रह्मेति श्रुतिः । न व्यापित्वाद्देशतोंऽतो<BR>नित्यत्वान्नापि कालतः । न वस्तुतोऽपि<BR>सर्वात्म्यादानंत्यं ब्रह्मणि त्रिधा ॥<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् m. the Supreme spirit.<BR>--कर a.<BR>magnifying to any extent; P. III. 2. 21.<BR>--ग a. moving for ever.<BR>--गुण a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-b" target="_blank">Page0056-b+ 58</a>]<BR>possessed of endless merits; of<BR>countless or infinite number;<BR>प्लवंगानामनंतगुणतैधते Mv. 6. 55.<BR>--चतुर्दशी, --˚व्रतं<BR>[अनंतस्य आराधनं यस्यां सा चतुर्दशी] the<BR>14th day of the bright half of<BR>Bhādrapada when Ananta is worshipped.<BR>--जित् (अनंतानि भूतानि जितवान्) {1}<BR>N. of Vāsudeva, the conqueror of<BR>all. {2} N. of an Arhat deity.<BR>--तान<BR>a. of endless width, extensive.<BR>--तीर्थकृत् m. {1} one who visits many places<BR>of pilgrimage. {2} a Jaina deity.<BR>--तृतीया the third day of the bright<BR>half of भाद्रपद, मार्गशीर्ष or वैशाख; नभस्ये<BR>वाथ वैशाखे मार्गशीर्षेऽथवा पुनः ।<BR>शुक्लपक्षतृतीयायां… उक्तानंततृतीयैषा सुतानंदफलप्रदा.<BR>--दृष्टिः [अनंता दृष्टयो नेत्राणि यस्य] N. of<BR>Śiva, or of Indra.<BR>--देवः [अनंतोदेव इव] {1}<BR>the serpent Śeṣa. {2} [अनंते दीव्यति;<BR>दिव्-अच्] N. of Nārāyaṇa who sleeps<BR>on Śeṣa.<BR>--पार a. of endless width,<BR>boundless; ˚रं किल शब्दशास्त्रं Pt. 1.<BR>--मायिन् a. of endless tricks, endlessly<BR>deceitful.<BR>--मूलः a medicinal plant;<BR>(शारिवा).<BR>--राशिः an infinite quantity.<BR>--रूप a. of innumerable forms or<BR>shapes; epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--वातः a<BR>disease of the head, resembling<BR>tetanus.<BR>--विजयः [अनंतान् विजयते<BR>ध्वनिद्वारा अनेन] N. of Yudhiṣṭhira's<BR>conchshell Bg. 1. 16<BR>--वीर्यः N. of the 23rd<BR>Jaina Arhat of a future age.<BR>--व्रतं<BR>see अनंतचतुर्दशी above.<BR>--शक्ति a.<BR>of boundless power, omnipotent,<BR>epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR>--शयनं Travancore; Śrīraṅgapaṭṭaṇa (?)<BR>--शीर्ष N. of Viṣṇu or the Supreme<BR>Being.<BR>--(र्षा) N. of the wife of<BR>Vāsuki.<BR>--शुष्म a. Ved. possessing<BR>endless strength; endlessly blowing.<BR>--श्री a. of boundless magnificence,<BR>an epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंतक|अनन्तक
अनंतक a. [स्वार्थे कन्] Endless,<BR>eternal &c.<BR>--कं The Eternal or<BR>Infinite (among the Jainas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंत्य|अनन्त्य
अनंत्य a. [अनंतस्य इदं-यत्]<BR>Endless, eternal, infinite.<BR>--त्यं<BR>1<BR>Eternity, infinity.<BR>--2 The foot of हिरण्यगर्भ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंतवत्|अनन्तवत्|अनन्तवन्त्
अनंतवत् a. [अस्त्यर्थे मतुप्] Endless,<BR>eternal. --m. One of Brahma's<BR>four feet; earth, intermediate region,<BR>heaven, and ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंतर|अनन्तर|अनन्तरं
अनंतर a. [नास्ति अंतरं व्यवधानं,<BR>मध्यः, अवकाशः &c. यस्य]<BR>1 Having no<BR>interior or interior space, limitless;<BR>तदेतत् ब्रह्म अपूर्वमनंतरं अबाह्यं.<BR>--2<BR>Having no interval or interstice<BR>or pause (of space or time); compact,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-c" target="_blank">Page0056-c+ 57</a>]<BR>close; हलोऽनंतराः संयोगः P. I. 1. 7,<BR>See संयोग.<BR>--3 (a) Contiguous,<BR>neighbouring, adjoining; अनयत्<BR>प्रभुशक्तिसंपदा वशमेको नृपतीननंतरान् R. 8. 19;<BR>भारतवर्षादुत्तरेण अनंतरे किंपुरुषनाम्नि वर्षे<BR>K. 136; immediately adjoining;<BR>Ki. 2. 53, R. 7. 21; not distant from (with<BR>abl.); आत्मनोनंतरममात्यपदं ग्राहितः<BR>Mu. 4; ब्रह्मावर्तादनंतरः Ms. 2. 19 (Kull.<BR>अनंतरः किंचिदूनः); अरेः अनंतरं मित्रं 7. 158;<BR>or in comp; विषयानंतरो राजा शत्रुः<BR>Ak. who is an immediate neighbour.<BR>--4 Immediately before or after;<BR>तदिदं क्रियतामनंतरं भवता बंधुजनप्रयोजनं<BR>Ku. 4. 32 soon after, just afterwards;<BR>अनंतरोदीरितलक्ष्मभाजौ पादौ<BR>यदीयावुपजातयस्ताः Chand. M. having characteristics<BR>mentioned just before.<BR>--5 Following,<BR>coming close upon (in comp);<BR>शंखस्वनानंतरपुष्पवृष्टि Ku. 1. 23; 2. 53;<BR>˚करणीयं Ś. 4 the next duty, what<BR>should be done next.<BR>--6 Belonging<BR>to the caste immediately<BR>following; पुत्रा येऽनतरस्त्रीजाः Ms. 10. 14.<BR>--7<BR>Uninterrupted, unbroken,<BR>continuous.<BR>--रं [न. त.]<BR>1 Contiguity,<BR>proximity; अनंतरविहिते चास्यासने K. 93.<BR>--2 Brahma, the supreme soul (as<BR>being of one entire essence).<BR>--रं ind.<BR>[Strictly it is acc. of time<BR>कालात्यंतसंयोगः; नास्ति अंतरं यथा स्यात्तथा]<BR>1<BR>Immediately after, afterwards.<BR>--2 (With<BR>a prepositional force) After (with<BR>abl.); पुराणपत्रापगमादनंतरं R. 3. 7;<BR>त्यागाच्छांतिरनंतरं Bg. 12. 12.;<BR>गोदानविधेरनंतरं R. 3. 33, 36.; 2. 71;<BR>स्वामिनोनंतरं भृत्याः Pt. 1.; rarely with<BR>gen.; अंगदं चाधिरूढस्तु लक्ष्मणोऽनंतरं मम<BR>Rām.; or in comp.; घनोदयः प्राक्<BR>तदनंतरं पयः Ś. 7. 30.; R. 4. 2.;<BR>Ms. 3. 252, Y. 2. 41; वचनानंतरमेव K. 78<BR>immediately after those words.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः or जा [अनंतरस्या<BR>अनंतरवर्णाया मातुः जायते] the child of a<BR>Kṣatriyā or Vaiśyā mother, by a father<BR>belonging to the caste immediately<BR>above the mother's, Ms. 10. 4. {2}<BR>born immediately before or after;<BR>a younger or elder brother.<BR>--(जा)<BR>a younger or elder sister;<BR>अनुष्ठितानंतरजाविवाहः R. 7. 32.; so ˚जात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंतरीय|अनन्तरीय
अनंतरीय a. Next in succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंतरयः|अनन्तरय|अनन्तरयः
अनंतरयः [अंतरयः दूरीकरणं, न. त]<BR>Not leaving, non-abandonment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंतराय
अनंतराय a. [न. ब.]<BR>Uninterrupted, without a break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंतर्गर्भिन्
अनंतर्गर्भिन् m. [अंतर्गर्भो यस्य;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-a" target="_blank">Page0057-a+ 57</a>]<BR>अस्त्यर्थे इनि न. त.] N. of Kuśa grass used<BR>for the पवित्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंद|अनन्द|अनन्दः
अनंद a. [न नंदयति; नंद्-णिच् अच्]<BR>Joyless, cheerless.<BR>--दः N. of a<BR>purgatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्नं|अनन्न
अनन्नं Not food, that which is<BR>undeserving of being eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्य
अनन्य a.<BR>1 Not different, identical,<BR>same, not other than, self; अनन्या<BR>राघवस्याहं भास्करस्य प्रभायथा । सा हि<BR>सत्याभिसंधानातथानन्या च भर्तरि Rām.<BR>--2 Sole,<BR>unique, without a second.<BR>--3 [नास्ति<BR>अन्यः विषयो यस्य] Undivided,<BR>undistracted (mind &c.); having no<BR>other object or person to think of<BR>&c.; अनन्याश्चिंतयंतो मां ये जनाः पर्युपासते<BR>Bg. 9. 22. In comp. अनन्य may be<BR>translated by ‘not by another,’<BR>‘directed or devoted to no one else’,<BR>‘having no other object.’<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. not subservient to any<BR>other object, principal.<BR>--आश्रित a.<BR>independent, not resorting to another.<BR>--(तं) unencumbered estate (in<BR>law).<BR>--गतिः f. sole resort or<BR>resource.<BR>--गतिक a. [न. ब.] having no<BR>other resource or help, having no other<BR>resource left; अनन्यगतिके जने<BR>विगतपातके चातके Udb.<BR>--गुरु a. than which<BR>nothing is greater Śi. 1. 35.<BR>--चित्त, --चिंत, --चेतस्, --मनस्, --मानस, --हृदय a.<BR>giving one's undivided thought or<BR>attention to, with undivided mind;<BR>विचिंतयंती यमनन्यमानसा Ś. 4. 1; K. 75.<BR>--जः, --जन्मन् m. [नान्यस्मात् जन्म यस्य;<BR>आत्मभूचित्तभू इत्यादि तस्य व्यपदेशत्वात् or<BR>नास्ति अन्यद्यस्मात्सोऽनन्यः विष्णुः;<BR>तस्माज्जातः] Cupid, the god of love; मा<BR>मूमुहत्खलु भवंतमनन्यजन्मा Māl. 1. 32.<BR>--दृष्टि a.<BR>gazing intently or steadfastly at;<BR>˚ष्टिः सवितारमैक्षत Ku. 5. 20.<BR>--देव a.<BR>having no other (superior) God,<BR>epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR>--परता exclusive devotion or<BR>attachment; पुरश्चक्षूरागस्तदनु मनसोऽनन्यपरता<BR>Māl. 6. 15.<BR>--परायण a. devoted to no<BR>other (woman) Ś. 3. 19.<BR>--पूर्वः [<BR>नान्या पूर्वा यस्य] having no other wife;<BR>वरस्यानन्यपूर्वस्य विशोकामकरोद्गुणैः<BR>Ku. 6. 92.<BR>--(र्वा) [न अन्यः पूर्वो यस्याः सा] a<BR>virgin (who never before<BR>belonged to another), a woman having<BR>no other husband; R. 4. 7.<BR>--भाज् a. [न<BR>अन्यं अन्यां वा भजते] not devoted to<BR>any other person; अनन्यभाजं पतिमाप्नुहिं<BR>Ku. 3. 63.<BR>--विषय a. not applicable<BR>or belonging to any one else,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">Page0057-b+ 56</a>]<BR>exclusively applicable; V. 1. 1; Mv. 1. 25.<BR>--वृत्ति a. {1} of the same nature. {2}<BR>having no other means of livelihood.<BR>{3} closely attentive.<BR>--शासन a. not<BR>ruled over by any one else; R. 1. 30;<BR>Dk. 2.<BR>--सामान्य, --साधारण a. not<BR>common to any one else, uncommon,<BR>exclusively devoted, applicable or<BR>belonging to one; अनन्यनारीसामान्यो<BR>दासस्त्वस्याः पुरूरवाः V. 3. 18; ˚राजशब्दः<BR>R. 6. 38; M. 5; 4. 10; not capable of<BR>being performed by any one else,<BR>Ku. 3. 19.<BR>--सदृश a. (शी f.) having no<BR>equal, matchless, peerless;<BR>यथैताननन्यसदृशान् विदधासि Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यता
अनन्यता, --त्वं Identity, sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यत्वं|अनन्यत्व
अनन्यता, --त्वं Identity, sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्यादृश
अनन्यादृश a. (शी f.) Not like others,<BR>singular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्वयः|अनन्वय
अनन्वयः [न. त.]<BR>1 Want of<BR>connection.<BR>--2 (Rhet.) A figure of<BR>speech in which a thing is<BR>compared to itself, the object being to<BR>show that it is matchless and can<BR>have no other उपमान; उपमानोपमेयत्वं<BR>यदेकस्यैव वस्तुनः । इंदुरिंदुरिव श्रीमानित्यादौ<BR>तदनन्वयः ॥ गगनं गगनाकारं सागरः<BR>सागरोपमः । रामरावणयोर्युद्धं रामरावणयोरिव ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनन्वित
अनन्वित a. [न. त.]<BR>1<BR>Unconnected.<BR>--2 Irregular, desultory;<BR>irrelevant, incoherent.<BR>--3 Not attended<BR>with, devoid of; as पुत्र˚, भार्या˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनप
अनप a. [न संति आधिक्येन आपो यत्र]<BR>Destitute of much water (as a<BR>puddle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकरणं|अनपकरण
अनपकरणं --कर्मन्, --क्रिया<BR>1 Not<BR>injuring.<BR>--2 Non-delivery.<BR>--3 (In law)<BR>Non-payment; दत्तस्यानपकर्म च<BR>Ms. 8. 4; दत्तस्य or वेतनस्य ˚क्रिया 214.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकर्मन्|अनपकर्म्मन्
अनपकरणं --कर्मन्, --क्रिया<BR>1 Not<BR>injuring.<BR>--2 Non-delivery.<BR>--3 (In law)<BR>Non-payment; दत्तस्यानपकर्म च<BR>Ms. 8. 4; दत्तस्य or वेतनस्य ˚क्रिया 214.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपक्रिया
अनपकरणं --कर्मन्, --क्रिया<BR>1 Not<BR>injuring.<BR>--2 Non-delivery.<BR>--3 (In law)<BR>Non-payment; दत्तस्यानपकर्म च<BR>Ms. 8. 4; दत्तस्य or वेतनस्य ˚क्रिया 214.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपकारः|अनपकार
अनपकारः Harmlessness.<BR>--कारिन् a. Harmless, innocent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपजय्य
अनपजय्य a. Ved. Whose<BR>victorious character cannot be reversed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपत्य
अनपत्य a.<BR>1 Without issue,<BR>childless, without heir; ˚त्यश्च किल तपस्वी<BR>Ś. 6; K. 59, 63.<BR>--2 Not propitious<BR>or favourable to children; causing<BR>fall (पतनकारण) Rv. 3. 54. 18. ˚ता, --˚त्वं<BR>childlessness; नूनमनपत्यता मां<BR>वत्सलयति Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपत्रप
अनपत्रप a. Impudent, shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपनिहित
अनपनिहित a. Ved. Not mutilated<BR>or curtailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपभ्रंशः|अनपभ्रंश
अनपभ्रंशः Not a corrupt word; a<BR>properly formed word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपयति
अनपयति ind. Very early (before<BR>the sun starts on his journey).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपर
अनपर a. Having no other or<BR>second, having no follower, sole;<BR>तदेतद् ब्रह्मापूर्वमनपरं Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपराध|अनपराधः
अनपराध --धिन् a. Innocent,<BR>guiltless, harmless.<BR>--धः Innocence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपराधिन्
अनपराध --धिन् a. Innocent,<BR>guiltless, harmless.<BR>--धः Innocence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपवाचन
अनपवाचन a. Ved. Impossible to<BR>be talked away or wished away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपव्ययत्|अनपव्ययन्त्
अनपव्ययत् a. Ved. Not letting<BR>go; able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपसर|अनपसरः
अनपसर a. Having no egress<BR>or passage to creep out of,<BR>unjustifiable, inexcusable; निरन्वयोऽ<BR>नपसरः Ms. 8. 198 (अपसरः प्रतिग्रहक्रयादिः)<BR>--रः -- A usurper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपस्पृश्
अनपस्पृश् a. Not obstinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपस्फुर्
अनपस्फुर् --र --रत् a. (of a cow)<BR>Not refusing to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपस्फुर
अनपस्फुर् --र --रत् a. (of a cow)<BR>Not refusing to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपस्फुरत्|अनपस्फुरन्त्
अनपस्फुर् --र --रत् a. (of a cow)<BR>Not refusing to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपाय|अनपायः
अनपाय a.<BR>1 Free from loss or<BR>decay.<BR>--2 Imperishable, undiminished,<BR>undecaying; प्रणमंत्यनपायमुत्थितं (<BR>चंद्रं) Ki. 2. 11.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Imperishable<BR>nature, freedom from decay or wear<BR>and tear; permanence.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपायिन्
अनपायिन् a. Imperishable, firm,<BR>steady, unfailing, constant, durable,<BR>not transient; प्रसादाभिमुखे तस्मिञ्<BR>श्रीरासीदनपायिनी R. 17. 46.; 8. 17;<BR>अनपायिनि संश्रयद्रुमे गजभग्ने पतनाय वल्लरी<BR>Ku. 4. 31; चलेष्वर्थेषु लुब्धेन न<BR>यशःस्वनपायिषु Mu. 5. 14; Ki. 14. 37,<BR>2. 43; Śi. 8. 50, 14. 65, 17. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपावृत्
अनपावृत् [न. ब.] Not<BR>returning or coming back, non-recurrent<BR>(पुनरावृत्तिशून्य); unremitting (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेक्ष|अनपेक्षं
अनपेक्ष --क्षिन् a. [न. त.]<BR>1<BR>Regardless.<BR>--2 Careless, not minding or<BR>heeding, indifferent.<BR>--3 Independent or<BR>irrespective (of another), not<BR>requiring any other thing.<BR>--4 Impartial.<BR>--5<BR>Irrelevant, unconnected,<BR>unconcerned.<BR>--क्षा Disregard, indifference,<BR>carelessness.<BR>--क्षं adv. Without regard<BR>to, independently or irrespectively<BR>of; carelessly, accidentally; ˚त्वात्<BR>since it has no reference to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेक्षिन्
अनपेक्ष --क्षिन् a. [न. त.]<BR>1<BR>Regardless.<BR>--2 Careless, not minding or<BR>heeding, indifferent.<BR>--3 Independent or<BR>irrespective (of another), not<BR>requiring any other thing.<BR>--4 Impartial.<BR>--5<BR>Irrelevant, unconnected,<BR>unconcerned.<BR>--क्षा Disregard, indifference,<BR>carelessness.<BR>--क्षं adv. Without regard<BR>to, independently or irrespectively<BR>of; carelessly, accidentally; ˚त्वात्<BR>since it has no reference to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनपेत
अनपेत a.<BR>1 Not gone off, not past;<BR>अनपेतकालं कथयांबभूवुः Ki. 6. 30<BR>without loss of time, without delay.<BR>--2<BR>Not deviating from, faithful to, not<BR>leaving (with abl.); अर्थादनपेतं अर्थ्यं<BR>Sk.; धर्मपथ्यर्थन्यायादनपेते<BR>P. IV. 4. 92. See अपेत also.<BR>--3 Not devoid of,<BR>possessed of; ऐश्वर्यादनपेतमीश्वरमयं<BR>लोकोऽर्थतः सेवते Mu. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनप्त
अनप्त a. Ved. [न आप्तः, वेदे पृषो˚ ह्रस्वः]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">Page0058-a+ 55</a>]<BR>Not seized or overcome by the<BR>enemy (शत्रुभिरनाप्त); not watery (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनप्नस्
अनप्नस् a. [नास्ति अप्नः रूपं यस्य]<BR>Ved. Destitute of form or shape,<BR>shapeless, actionless (कर्महीन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनप्सरस्
अनप्सरस् --रा f. Not an Apsaras,<BR>unworthy of a celestial nymph;<BR>अप्सरेव प्रतिभासि V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनप्सरा
अनप्सरस् --रा f. Not an Apsaras,<BR>unworthy of a celestial nymph;<BR>अप्सरेव प्रतिभासि V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनफा
अनफा A particular configuration<BR>of planets; रविवर्जं द्वादशगैरनफा;<BR>सच्छीलं सुखान्वितंप्रभुं ख्यातियुक्तमनफायाम्<BR>Dīpikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिज्ञ|अनभिज्ञः
अनभिज्ञ a. Ignorant of,<BR>unacquainted with, unused to, (usually<BR>with gen.); ˚ज्ञः कैतवस्य Ś. 5;<BR>वृत्तांतानामनभिज्ञास्मि K. 236; ˚ज्ञः<BR>परमेश्वरगृहाचारस्य Mv. 2; Ku. 6. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिम्लान
अनभिम्लान a. [न. त.] Not faded.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्ण a. Ved. of unfaded<BR>or undiminished lustre, resplendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिलक्षितः|अनभिलक्षित
अनभिलक्षितः An impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिलाष|अनभिलाषः
अनभिलाष a. Free from desire.<BR>--षः<BR>1 Want of appetite or desire.<BR>--2 Non-relish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिशस्त
अनभिशस्त, --स्ति, --स्त्य a. Ved.<BR>Blameless, faultless; ˚शस्तेनी leading<BR>to perfection or to heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिशस्ति
अनभिशस्त, --स्ति, --स्त्य a. Ved.<BR>Blameless, faultless; ˚शस्तेनी leading<BR>to perfection or to heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिशस्त्य
अनभिशस्त, --स्ति, --स्त्य a. Ved.<BR>Blameless, faultless; ˚शस्तेनी leading<BR>to perfection or to heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिसंधानं|अनभिसन्धान|अनभिसंधान
अनभिसंधानं Absence of design<BR>or purpose; so अनभिसंधिः; ˚कृत done<BR>undesignedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभिहित|अनभिहितः
अनभिहित a.<BR>1 Not named or<BR>asserted; see अभिहित under अभिधा.<BR>--2<BR>Not fastened (Ved.).<BR>--तः N. of<BR>the chief of a Gotra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्यावृत्तिः|अनभ्यावृत्ति
अनभ्यावृत्तिः f. Non-repetition;<BR>मनागनभ्यावृत्त्या वा कामं क्षाम्यतु यः क्षमी<BR>Śi. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्याश
अनभ्याश, --स a. Not near,<BR>distant &c.; ˚समित्य a. to be shunned<BR>from afar Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्यास
अनभ्याश, --स a. Not near,<BR>distant &c.; ˚समित्य a. to be shunned<BR>from afar Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्र
अनभ्र a. Cloudless; इयमनभ्रा वृष्टिः<BR>this is (like) a shower from a<BR>cloudless sky, i. e. something quite<BR>unexpected or sudden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनभ्रि
अनभ्रि a. Ved. Epithet of<BR>rainwater; requiring no shovel (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमः|अनम
अनमः [न नमति अन्यान्] A<BR>Brāhmaṇa (one who does not bow down<BR>to others and returns salutations<BR>made to him by others with a<BR>blessing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमितंपच|अनमितम्पच|अनमितम्पचः
अनमितंपच (= मितंपच) a.<BR>Miserly, niggardly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमित्र
अनमित्र a. Having no enemies.<BR>--त्रं A state of having no enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनमीव
अनमीव a. Ved. [नास्ति अमीवो रोगे<BR>यस्य न. ब.] Well, happy, free from<BR>disease; comfortable, salubrious,<BR>sinless.<BR>--वं Good or comfortable state,<BR>happiness, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनंबर|अनम्बर|अनम्बरः
अनंबर a. Wearing no garment.<BR>--रः A Buddhist mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनम्र
अनम्र a. Not humble, haughty,<BR>proud; अनम्राणां समुद्धर्तुः R. 4. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनयः|अनय
अनयः [अप्रशस्तो नयः]<BR>1 Bad<BR>management or conduct; injustice;<BR>unfairness; समृद्धिरनयाद्विनश्यति<BR>Pt. 1. 169; Bh. 2. 42.<BR>--2 Bad policy or<BR>course of conduct, evil course;<BR>अनयो नयसंकाशो हृदयान्नापसर्पति Pt. 3. 184.<BR>--3 Adversity, calamity, distress;<BR>जीवेदेतेन राजन्यः सर्वेष्वप्यनयं गतः<BR>Ms. 10. 95 reduced to straits; 102.<BR>--4<BR>[अयः शुभावहो विधिस्तदन्यः अनयः]<BR>Misfortune, adversity; ill-luck.<BR>--5 A<BR>variety of dice-play, gambling (<BR>शाराणां वामावर्तेन अभीष्टस्थाननयनं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनरण्यः|अनरण्य
अनरण्यः N. of a king of the<BR>solar race, a descendant of Ikṣvāku<BR>and king of Ayodhyā, who was<BR>overthrown by Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनरुस्
अनरुस् a. [न. ब.] Ved. Not<BR>wounded, healthy, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्गल|अनर्गलं
अनर्गल a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Free from<BR>bar or obstruction, free to move,<BR>unrestrained, unhampered;<BR>तुरंगमुत्सृष्टमनर्गलं R. 3. 39.<BR>--2 Unlocked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ|अनर्घः
अनर्घ a. [नास्ति अर्घो मूल्यं यस्य न. ब.]<BR>Invaluable, priceless, inestimable;<BR>R. 5. 2; Śi. 14. 88.<BR>--र्घः [न. त.] Wrong or<BR>improper value.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--राघवं N.<BR>of a drama in 7 acts by Murāri<BR>Miśra; also called Murāri Nāṭaka<BR>after its author and supposed to have<BR>been written between the 12th and<BR>the 14th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घत्वं|अनर्घत्व
अनर्घत्वं --ता Pricelessness,<BR>invaluable nature; H. Pr. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घता
अनर्घत्वं --ता Pricelessness,<BR>invaluable nature; H. Pr. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्घ्य
अनर्घ्य a. Invaluable; unsurpassed<BR>in reverence due from others,<BR>highly respected; अनर्घ्यमर्घेण तमद्रिनाथः<BR>Ku. 1. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थ|अनर्थः
अनर्थ a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Useless,<BR>worthless; शुनः पुच्छमिवानर्थं पांडित्यं धर्मवर्जितं<BR>Pt. 3. 97.<BR>--2 Unfortunate, unhappy.<BR>--3 Harmful, disastrous, bad;<BR>चित्तज्ञानानुवर्तिनोऽनर्था अपि प्रियाः स्युः<BR>Dk. 160; wicked (opp. दक्षिण).<BR>--4 Not<BR>having that meaning (but another);<BR>having no meaning, nonsensical,<BR>meaningless.<BR>--5 Poor.<BR>--र्थः [न. त.]<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-c" target="_blank">Page0058-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Non-use or value.<BR>--2 A worthless or<BR>useless object.<BR>--3 A reverse, evil,<BR>calamity, misfortune; R. 18. 14;<BR>रंध्रोपनिपातिनो ऽनर्थाः Ś. 6; एकैकमप्यनर्थाय<BR>किमु तत्र चतुष्टयं H. 1; cf. छिद्रेष्वनर्था<BR>बहुलीभवंति &c.; Ms. 4. 193,<BR>H. 4. 92; harmful object, danger; अर्थमनर्थं<BR>भावय नित्यं Moha M. 2.<BR>--4 Nonsense,<BR>want of sense.<BR>--5 N. of Viṣṇu (<BR>आप्तसर्वकामत्वात्तस्य तथात्वं).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरं [न अर्थांतरं] sameness or<BR>identity.<BR>--कर a. (री f.) {1} doing useless<BR>or unprofitable things. {2}<BR>mischievous, harmful; unprofitable,<BR>productive of evil.<BR>--नाशिन् m. N. of<BR>Śiva (destroyer of calamities).<BR>--भाव<BR>a. malicious.<BR>--लुप्त a. [दृष्टार्थेन अलुप्तः]<BR>not devoid of the apparent meaning;<BR>free from all that is worthless.<BR>--संशयः [अनर्थकारी संशयः शाक. त.] {1}<BR>a great evil, hazardous adventure;<BR>प्रतिनिवर्ततामस्मादनर्थसंशयात् Māl. 5. 2.<BR>[न. त.] not a risk of one's money;<BR>safety of one's wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थ्य
अनर्थ्य, अनर्थक a.<BR>1 Useless;<BR>meaningless; सर्वमप्येतदनर्थकं Ve. 1;<BR>˚आयास K. 108; not significant, as a<BR>particle used expletively.<BR>--2<BR>Nonsensical.<BR>--3 Unprofitable.<BR>--4 Unfortunate.<BR>--कं Nonsensical or incoherent talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्थक|अनर्थकं
अनर्थ्य, अनर्थक a.<BR>1 Useless;<BR>meaningless; सर्वमप्येतदनर्थकं Ve. 1;<BR>˚आयास K. 108; not significant, as a<BR>particle used expletively.<BR>--2<BR>Nonsensical.<BR>--3 Unprofitable.<BR>--4 Unfortunate.<BR>--कं Nonsensical or incoherent talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्व
अनर्व a. Ved. Not lax or loose<BR>(अशिथिल) Rv. 1. 164. 2.; free,<BR>unobstructed, permanent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्वन्
अनर्वन् a. [अर्व्-हिंसायां कनिन्, अर्वा<BR>सपत्नः न. त.]<BR>1 Not inimical, not<BR>hostile or to be hated (अद्वेष्य);<BR>Rv. 1. 136. 5.<BR>--2 Having no horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्विश्
अनर्विश् m. [अनसा शकटेन विशति<BR>प्राप्नोति; विश्-क्विप्, अहरा˚ रुः]<BR>1 One who<BR>sits in a cart to fetch fuel &c.<BR>--2 [<BR>ऋकर्मणि विच्, अरं गंतव्यं प्रति विशति,<BR>विश्-क्विप्, न. त.] One who is not able to<BR>reach the destination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्शराति
अनर्शराति a. [अनर्शाय अपापिष्ठाय<BR>रातिर्दानं यस्य] One who does not give<BR>to sinful persons, a sinless donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनर्ह
अनर्ह a.<BR>1 Not deserving, not fit,<BR>not worthy of (with gen. or in comp);<BR>अनर्हा गृहवासस्य Pt. 4.; तान्<BR>हव्यकव्ययोर्विप्राननर्हान् मनुरब्रवीत् Ms. 3. 150.<BR>--2<BR>Inadequate, unsuitable.<BR>--3<BR>Undeserving of reward or punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलः|अनल|अनलं
अनलः [नास्ति अलः पर्याप्तिर्यस्य,<BR>बहुदाह्यदहनेपि तृप्तेरभावात् Tv.; cf. नाग्निस्तृप्यति<BR>काष्ठानां; said by some to be from अन्<BR>to breathe].<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 Agni or<BR>the god of fire. See अग्नि.<BR>--3 Digestive<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-a" target="_blank">Page0059-a+ 56</a>]<BR>power, gastric juice; मंदः संजायतेऽ<BR>नलः Suśr.<BR>--4 Wind.<BR>--5 Bile.<BR>--6 One<BR>of the 8 Vasus, the fifth.<BR>--7 N. of<BR>Vāsudeva.<BR>--8 N. of various plants;<BR>चित्रक, रक्तचित्रक Plumbago Zeylanica<BR>and Rosea, भल्लातक the marking nut<BR>tree.<BR>--9 The letter र्.<BR>--10 The number<BR>three.<BR>--11 (Astr.) The 50th year<BR>of Bṛhaspati's cycle.<BR>--12 The third<BR>lunar mansion कृत्तिका.<BR>--13 A variety<BR>of Pitṛdeva or manes (कव्यवाहोऽनलः<BR>सोमः).<BR>--14 [अनान् प्राणान् लाति<BR>आत्मत्वेन] The soul (जीव).<BR>--15 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu (न नलति गंधं प्रकटयति न वध्यते<BR>वा नल्-अच्).<BR>--16 The Supreme Being.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द a. [अनलं द्यति] {1} removing<BR>or destroying heat or fire; करिणां मुदे<BR>सनलदाऽनलदाः Ki. 5. 25. {2} = अग्निद q. v.<BR>--दीपन a. [अनलं दीपयति] promoting<BR>digestion, stomachic.<BR>--प्रभा [अनलस्य<BR>प्रभेव प्रभा यस्य] N. of a plant (ज्योतिष्मती)<BR>Helicacabum Cardiospermum.<BR>--प्रिया<BR>N. of Agni's wife स्वाहा.<BR>--सादः loss of<BR>appetite, dyspepsia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलस
अनलस a.<BR>1 Not lazy, active,<BR>diligent, watchful, R. 9. 15.<BR>--2<BR>Unable, incompetent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनलिः|अनलि
अनलिः [अनिति-अच् अनः अलिर्यत्र<BR>ब. शकंध्वा.] N. of a tree (बकवृक्ष)<BR>Sesbana Grandiflora (तत्पुष्पाणां मधुपूर्णतया<BR>तन्मधुभिर्भ्रमराणां जीवनधारणात्तथात्वं Tv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनल्प
अनल्प a.<BR>1 Numerous.<BR>--2 Not a<BR>little; not small, liberal, noble (as<BR>mind &c.); Ki. 14. 18; much;<BR>जल्पंत्यनल्पाक्षरं Pt. 1. 136 profusely, in<BR>many words; विकसितवदनामनल्पजल्पेपि<BR>Bv. 1. 100; 2. 138.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--घोष a.<BR>very clamorous or noisy.<BR>--मन्यु a.<BR>greatly enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवकाश|अनवकाशः
अनवकाश a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Having no<BR>scope or occasion, uncalled for.<BR>--2<BR>Inapplicable.<BR>--3 Having no<BR>opportunity or space.<BR>--शः [न. त.]<BR>Absence of room or scope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवग्रह
अनवग्रह a. [न. ब.] Irresistible,<BR>uncontrolled, impetuous, resistless;<BR>सुकुमारकायमनवग्रहः स्मरः (अभिहंति)<BR>Māl. 1. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवच्छिन्न
अनवच्छिन्न a.<BR>1 Not bounded or<BR>marked off, not separated or cut.<BR>--2<BR>Unlimited, immoderate, excessive.<BR>--3<BR>Undefined; दिक्कालादि˚ Bh. 2. 1; 3. 1;<BR>undiscriminated, unmodified.<BR>--4<BR>Uninterrupted, continuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवद्य
अनवद्य a. [न अवद्यः निंद्यः]<BR>Faultless, blameless, unobjectionable,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">Page0059-b+ 55</a>]<BR>irreproachable; Bh. 2. 21; R. 7. 70.<BR>--द्या N. of a damsel.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग,<BR>--रूप a. having faultless limbs or<BR>form, exquisitely handsome; रूपस्य<BR>अनवद्यता M. 2.<BR>--(गी) a woman<BR>with a faultless form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवद्राण
अनवद्राण a. Not sleepy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवधान|अनवधानं
अनवधान a. [न. ब.] Careless,<BR>inattentive.<BR>--नं Inadvertence,<BR>inattention; ˚ता carelessness,<BR>remissness in duty (प्रमाद); कर्तव्याकरणं<BR>यत्राकर्तव्यस्याथवा क्रिया । उच्यते द्वितयं तत्र<BR>प्रमादोऽनवधानता ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवधि
अनवधि a. Unlimited, infinite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवन
अनवन a. [न. ब.] Affording<BR>no help or protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवनामित
अनवनामित a. Not lowered or<BR>bent down; ˚वैजयंतः a Buddhist term<BR>for a future universe (lit. having<BR>banners unlowered).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवपृग्ण
अनवपृग्ण a. Ved. Spreading all<BR>around, not closely united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवब्रव
अनवब्रव a. [अवब्रू-अच् न वचादेशः<BR>न. त.] Irreproachable, not open to<BR>censure (अपवादवर्जित); speaking<BR>authoritatively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवभ्र
अनवभ्र a. [न भ्रंशते बा. ड. Tv.]<BR>Undiminished, undecaying, durable,<BR>lasting (अवभ्रंशशून्य); ˚राधस् Rv. 1. 166. 7<BR>having undiminished wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवम
अनवम a. Not low or inferior^1;<BR>high, exalted, superior; सुधर्मानवमां<BR>सभां R. 17. 27, 9. 14.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवरत|अनवरतं
अनवरत a. Incessant, continuous,<BR>uninterrupted; ˚धनुर्ज्यास्फालनक्रूरपूर्वं<BR>Ś. 2. 4.<BR>--तं adv. Incessantly,<BR>continuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवरार्ध्य
अनवरार्ध्य a. [अवरस्मिन् अर्धे भवः,<BR>यत् न. त.] Chief, best, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवलंब|अनवलम्ब|अनवलम्बः
अनवलंब --बन a. [न. ब.] Having<BR>no prop or support; not<BR>dependent.<BR>--बः --बनं Independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवलंबन|अनवलम्बन
अनवलंब --बन a. [न. ब.] Having<BR>no prop or support; not<BR>dependent.<BR>--बः --बनं Independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवलोभनं|अनवलोभन
अनवलोभनं [न अवलुप्यते पुमान्येन,<BR>अवलुप्-ल्युट् पृषो˚ पस्य भः Tv.] A sort of<BR>purificatory ceremony to be<BR>performed in the case of a pregnant woman<BR>in the third month after conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस
अनवस a. [अव्-असच् अवसः<BR>भोजनं प्रीतिकरत्वात् न. ब.] Ved. Having<BR>no (wholesome) food to eat (<BR>पथ्याशनरहित); Rv. 6. 66. 7; not stopping<BR>to eat by the way (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवसर|अनवसरः
अनवसर a.<BR>1 Busy, having no<BR>leisure or interval of repose.<BR>--2<BR>Ill-timed, inopportune.<BR>--3 Out of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">Page0059-c+ 56</a>]<BR>place, baseless; ˚रोयं घंटानादः H. 3.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Absence of leisure.<BR>--2<BR>Ill-timedness, unseasonableness; कं<BR>याचे यत्र तत्र ध्रुवमनवसरग्रस्त एवार्थिभावः<BR>Māl. 9. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवसान
अनवसान a. [न. ब.] Endless,<BR>having no setting; free from death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवसित
अनवसित a. [न. त.] Not<BR>ended or finished; not determined.<BR>--ता<BR>N. of a kind of Triṣṭubh metre,<BR>consisting of four lines with 11<BR>feet in each.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्कर|अनवस्करं
अनवस्कर a. Free from dirt,<BR>pure, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थ
अनवस्थ a. [नास्ति अवस्था यत्र]<BR>Unsteady; ˚स्थो निष्करुणश्च Dk. 135;<BR>unsettled, not fixed; ˚स्थो वायुः<BR>Śi. 11. 28.<BR>--स्था [न. त.]<BR>1<BR>Instability, unsettled condition, disorder,<BR>confusion.<BR>--2 Loose or unsteady<BR>conduct, incontinence.<BR>--3 (In<BR>phil.) Absence of finality or<BR>conclusion, an endless series of<BR>statements or causes and effects,<BR>one of the faults of<BR>reasoning (उपपाद्योपपादकयोरविश्रांतिः);<BR>एवमप्यनवस्था स्याद्या मूलक्षतिकारिणी<BR>K. P. 2; एवं च ˚प्रसंगः Ś. B.<BR>--4 Not being 10<BR>days old (दशाहाभावः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थान|अनवस्थानः
अनवस्थान a. Unstable, unsteady,<BR>fickle.<BR>--नः Wind.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Instability,<BR>uncertainty, unsettled nature;<BR>जयपराजयानवस्थानात् Dk. 161.<BR>--2<BR>Looseness of conduct, incontinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवस्थित
अनवस्थित a.<BR>1 Unsteady, fickle,<BR>unsettled; ˚स्तिमितमूढघूर्णन्नयनः U. 3 with<BR>unsteady eyes; Ku. 4. 28.<BR>--2<BR>Changed, altered; अहो ˚तो<BR>भूमिसंनिवेशः U. 2.<BR>--3 Faithless, loose in<BR>morals or moral conduct, dissolute<BR>(व्यभिचारिन्); नारीर्हत्वाऽनवस्थिताः<BR>Ms. 11. 139.<BR>--4 Unable to stay or<BR>remain; प्रस्थितं तमनवस्थितं प्रियाः<BR>R. 19. 31; ˚त्वं, ˚स्थितिः instability,<BR>looseness of conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवह्वर
अनवह्वर a. [अवह्वृ-कौटिल्ये-अच्. न.<BR>त.] Not crooked, straightforward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवांच्|अनवाञ्च्
अनवांच् a. Not tending<BR>downwards, looking up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवानं|अनवान
अनवानं ind. [अवानः श्वासोच्छ्वासः स<BR>यथा न स्यात्तथा] Without breathing<BR>between, in one breath, without a<BR>pause, uno tenore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवाय
अनवाय a. [अव-इ-घञ् अवायः<BR>अवयवः, न. ब.] Without parts (<BR>निरवयव); uninterrupted, unyielding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवेक्षक
अनवेक्षक a. Regardless of;<BR>careless, indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवेक्ष
अनवेक्ष-क्षा = अनपेक्ष-क्षा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवेक्षा
अनवेक्ष-क्षा = अनपेक्ष-क्षा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनवेक्षणं|अनवेक्षण
अनवेक्षणं<BR>1 Carelessness,<BR>inattention; अनवेक्षणादपि कृषिः Pt. 1. 169.<BR>--2<BR>Want of supervision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनव्रत|अनव्रतः
अनव्रत a. [न. ब.] Not altogether<BR>destitute of holy or ascetic<BR>performances.<BR>--तः A Jaina devotee who is so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनशनं|अनशन
अनशनं Fasting, abstinence from<BR>food, fasting oneself to death; ˚नं च<BR>शाययित्वा Dk. 156 making him fast;<BR>˚नात् उत्तिष्ठति Pt. 4. --a. Without<BR>food, fasting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनशनाय
अनशनाय a. Ved. Not hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्नत्|अनश्नन्त्
अनश्नत् a. Not eating; ˚सांगमनः the<BR>sacrificial fire in the sabhā which is<BR>approached before eating or breakfast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्व|अनश्वः
अनश्व a. Having no horse or<BR>horses.<BR>--श्वः Something that is not<BR>a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनश्वर|अनश्वरं
अनश्वर a. (री f.) Imperishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्
अनस् n. [अनिति शब्दायते अन्-असुन्]<BR>1<BR>A cart; उद्गाता चाप्यनः क्रये Ms. 8. 209;<BR>Y. 1. 184, 3. 269, Śi. 12. 26.<BR>--2 [<BR>अनिति जीवत्यनेन] Food, boiled rice.<BR>--3<BR>Birth.<BR>--4 A living being.<BR>--5 A<BR>kitchen.<BR>--6 A parent (father or mother);<BR>said to be f. in these two senses.<BR>At the end of Avyayībhāva comp.<BR>अनस् is changed to अनस; as अध्यनसं<BR>&c.; also at the end of Tat. Comp.;<BR>महानसं &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूय
अनसूय --यक a. [न. ब.] Free<BR>from malice, not envious, not<BR>spiteful; श्रद्दधानोऽनसूयश्च Ms. 4. 158;<BR>Bg. 18. 71.<BR>--या [न. त.]<BR>1 Absence of<BR>envy, charity of disposition,<BR>freedom from spite or ill-will; न गुणान्<BR>गुणिनो हंति स्तौति चान्यगुणानपि । न<BR>हसेच्चान्यदोषांश्च सानसूया प्रकीर्तिता.<BR>--2 N. of a friend of<BR>Śakuntalā.<BR>--3 N. of Atri's wife, the<BR>highest type of chastity and wifely<BR>devotion. [She was very pious and given<BR>to austere devotion by virtue of which she<BR>had obtained miraculous powers. Several<BR>stories are told to illustrate them. When<BR>the earth was devastated by a terrible<BR>drought which lasted for 10 years,<BR>Anasūya created water, fruits, roots &c. by<BR>means of her ascetic powers and saved<BR>many lives. On one occasion when<BR>the sage Māṇḍavya was about to be<BR>impaled, the wife of a sage happened to<BR>touch the stake as she passed by, where<BR>upon Māṇḍavya cursed her that she<BR>would become a widow at sunrise. She,<BR>however, prevented the sun from rising,<BR>and all actions of men being<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">Page0060-b+ 62</a>]<BR>consequently stopped, the gods, sages &c.<BR>went to Anasūyā, her friend, who, by<BR>the force of her penance, made the sun<BR>rise without, at the same time, bringing<BR>widowhood on her friend. Another<BR>legend is also told in which Anasūyā<BR>changed Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Maheśa<BR>into infants, when, at the instigation of<BR>their wives, they attempted to test her<BR>chastity, but restored them to their<BR>former shapes at the importunities of their<BR>humbled consorts. She is also said to<BR>have caused the three-streamed Ganges<BR>to flow down on the earth near the<BR>hermitage of her husband for the<BR>ablutions of sages; see R. 13. 51. In the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa she is represented as having<BR>been very kind and attentive to Sītā<BR>whom she favoured with sound<BR>motherly advice on the virtues of chastity, and<BR>at the time of her departure gave her<BR>an unguent (See R. 12. 27, 14. 14)<BR>which was to keep her beautiful for ever<BR>and to guard her person from the<BR>attempts of rapacious beasts, demons &c.<BR>She was the mother of the irascible<BR>sage Durvāsas].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयक
अनसूय --यक a. [न. ब.] Free<BR>from malice, not envious, not<BR>spiteful; श्रद्दधानोऽनसूयश्च Ms. 4. 158;<BR>Bg. 18. 71.<BR>--या [न. त.]<BR>1 Absence of<BR>envy, charity of disposition,<BR>freedom from spite or ill-will; न गुणान्<BR>गुणिनो हंति स्तौति चान्यगुणानपि । न<BR>हसेच्चान्यदोषांश्च सानसूया प्रकीर्तिता.<BR>--2 N. of a friend of<BR>Śakuntalā.<BR>--3 N. of Atri's wife, the<BR>highest type of chastity and wifely<BR>devotion. [She was very pious and given<BR>to austere devotion by virtue of which she<BR>had obtained miraculous powers. Several<BR>stories are told to illustrate them. When<BR>the earth was devastated by a terrible<BR>drought which lasted for 10 years,<BR>Anasūya created water, fruits, roots &c. by<BR>means of her ascetic powers and saved<BR>many lives. On one occasion when<BR>the sage Māṇḍavya was about to be<BR>impaled, the wife of a sage happened to<BR>touch the stake as she passed by, where<BR>upon Māṇḍavya cursed her that she<BR>would become a widow at sunrise. She,<BR>however, prevented the sun from rising,<BR>and all actions of men being<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">Page0060-b+ 62</a>]<BR>consequently stopped, the gods, sages &c.<BR>went to Anasūyā, her friend, who, by<BR>the force of her penance, made the sun<BR>rise without, at the same time, bringing<BR>widowhood on her friend. Another<BR>legend is also told in which Anasūyā<BR>changed Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Maheśa<BR>into infants, when, at the instigation of<BR>their wives, they attempted to test her<BR>chastity, but restored them to their<BR>former shapes at the importunities of their<BR>humbled consorts. She is also said to<BR>have caused the three-streamed Ganges<BR>to flow down on the earth near the<BR>hermitage of her husband for the<BR>ablutions of sages; see R. 13. 51. In the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa she is represented as having<BR>been very kind and attentive to Sītā<BR>whom she favoured with sound<BR>motherly advice on the virtues of chastity, and<BR>at the time of her departure gave her<BR>an unguent (See R. 12. 27, 14. 14)<BR>which was to keep her beautiful for ever<BR>and to guard her person from the<BR>attempts of rapacious beasts, demons &c.<BR>She was the mother of the irascible<BR>sage Durvāsas].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनसूयु
अनसूयु a. = अनसूय; इदं तु ते गुह्यतमं<BR>प्रवक्ष्याम्यनसूयवे Bg. 9. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्थ|अनस्थः
अनस्थ --स्थिक [न. ब.]<BR>Boneless.<BR>--स्थः<BR>1 A boneless limb or<BR>member.<BR>--2 Without parts,<BR>epithet of प्रधान of the Sāṃkhyas or<BR>ईश्वरमाया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनस्थिक
अनस्थ --स्थिक [न. ब.]<BR>Boneless.<BR>--स्थः<BR>1 A boneless limb or<BR>member.<BR>--2 Without parts,<BR>epithet of प्रधान of the Sāṃkhyas or<BR>ईश्वरमाया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनहन्
अनहन् n. [न अहः अप्रशस्तमहः] A bad<BR>or unlucky day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अना
अना ind. Ved. Thus, hereby,<BR>indeed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकार
अनाकार a. Formless, shapeless,<BR>epithet of the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकालः|अनाकाल
अनाकालः [न. त. निपातः]<BR>1<BR>Inopportune time.<BR>--2 [आसम्यक्<BR>अन्नादिसंपन्नः कालः आकालः न. त. Tv.]<BR>Famine (perhaps an irregular form for<BR>अन्नाकाल).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भृतः one who,<BR>to save himself from starvation in<BR>a famine, voluntarily becomes a<BR>slave of another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकाश|अनाकाशः
अनाकाश a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Opaque,<BR>not transparent.<BR>--2 Having no<BR>transparent atmosphere; differing from<BR>it.<BR>--शः --शं Not an atmosphere, one<BR>undeserving of its name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकुल|अनाकुलः
अनाकुल a.<BR>1 Not perplexed or<BR>confused, calm, collected,<BR>self-possessed.<BR>--2 Regular, consistent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाकृत
अनाकृत a. Not prevented (<BR>अनिवारित); unreclaimed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्रांत|अनाक्रान्त
अनाक्रांत a. Unassailed.<BR>--ता [<BR>आक्रमितुमयोग्या सर्वतः कंटकावृतत्वात्, न. त.]<BR>Prickly nightshade, Solanum<BR>Jacquini (कंटकारिवृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाक्षित्
अनाक्षित् a. Ved. Not staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाग
अनाग a. [न आ सम्यग् गच्छति स्वर्गं<BR>अनेन नागः अधर्मः; न. ब. Tv.] Sinless;<BR>Rv. 10. 12. 9 (अनागान् = अपापान्).<BR>--गा N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागत|अनागतं
अनागत a. [न आगतः, न. त.]<BR>1<BR>Not come or arrived; तावद्भयस्य<BR>भेतव्यं यावद्भयमनागतं H. 1. 57.<BR>--2 Not got<BR>or obtained;<BR>वर्धिष्णुमाश्रयमनागतमभ्युपैति Śi. 5. 14; so ˚आर्तव.<BR>--3 Future,<BR>to come; see compounds below.<BR>--4<BR>Not learnt or attained, unknown.<BR>--तं The future time, future; ˚तं<BR>यः कुरुते स शोभते Pt. 3. 164 he<BR>shines (thrives, prospers) who<BR>provides for the future; अनागतवतीं<BR>चिंतामसंभाव्यां करोति यः Pt. 5. 71.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवेक्षणं looking to the<BR>future, provident thought, foresight.<BR>--आबाधः [अनागतः आबाधः दुःखं]<BR>future (physical) trouble or<BR>calamities, illness &c. affecting the body<BR>in times to come; ˚प्रतिषेधनीयं N.<BR>of chapter 24 of the चिकित्सितस्थान<BR>in Suśruta.<BR>--आर्तवा [स्त्रीपुष्पविकासनं<BR>आर्तवं, न आगतमार्तवंयस्याः] a maiden who<BR>has not yet arrived at puberty.<BR>--विधातृ m. [अनागतं उद्दिश्य विदधाति] one<BR>who provides for the future,<BR>provident, prudent (used as the name of<BR>a fish in Pt. 1. 318; H. 4. 5);<BR>अनागतविधाता च प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिस्तथा । द्वावेतौ<BR>सुखमेधेते यद्भविष्यो विनश्यति ॥ (where<BR>Dr. Peterson translates the three<BR>names by ‘Mr.<BR>Provider-against-a-future-evil’, ‘Mr. Cool-head,’ and<BR>‘Mr. what-will-be-will-be’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागतिः|अनागति
अनागतिः f. Non-arrival,<BR>non-attainment, non-access.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम|अनागमः
अनागम a.<BR>1 Not come, not<BR>present.<BR>--2 [न. ब.] (In law) Without<BR>the title-deed or document of<BR>possession (such as purchase deed &c.),<BR>anything possessed from time<BR>immemorial and without any<BR>documentary proof; ˚उपभोगः enjoyment<BR>of property without such a deed.<BR>--मः<BR>1 Non-arrival.<BR>--2 Non-attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागम्य
अनागम्य a. Unapproachable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागामिन्
अनागामिन् a.<BR>1 Not coming, not<BR>arriving.<BR>--2 Not future, not likely<BR>to return. --m. An epithet of the<BR>third among the 4 Buddhist orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागामुक
अनागामुक a. Not likely to return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागंधित
अनागंधित a. Not smelt; (fig.) not<BR>touched or affected; सर्वदोषानागंधितं<BR>प्रतिवचनमाह Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनागस्
अनागस् a.<BR>1 Innocent, blameless;<BR>आर्तत्राणाय वः शस्त्रं न प्रहर्तुमनागसि<BR>Ś. 1. 11.<BR>--2 Conferring bliss or happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाचार|अनाचारः
अनाचार a. Devoid of customary<BR>observances or duties, improper in<BR>behaviour, unprincipled, regardless<BR>of custom, law or propriety &c.; also<BR>अनाचारिन् in this sense.<BR>--रः, --अनाचरणं<BR>Absence of due observances or<BR>customary duties, improper conduct,<BR>departure from established usage or<BR>principle; अनाचार is of two kinds<BR>विहितस्य अननुष्ठानं निषिद्धस्य चानुष्ठानम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाज्ञात
अनाज्ञात a.<BR>1 Unknown, not<BR>properly known.<BR>--2 Surpassing all<BR>that has yet been known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातप|अनातपः
अनातप a. Free from or devoid<BR>of heat or the blaze of the sun, not<BR>exposed to heat, cool, shady;<BR>वांछन्देशमनातपं विधिवशात्तालस्य मूलं गतः<BR>Bh. 2. 90.<BR>--पः Coolness, shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनातुर|अनातुरः
अनातुर a.<BR>1 Not eager,<BR>indifferent; ˚रोत्कंठितयोः v. l. for अनादर<BR>M. 3. 15.<BR>--2 Not fatigued, unwearied; भेजे<BR>धर्ममनातुरः R. 1. 21.<BR>--3 Not ill or<BR>diseased, well, healthy, in good<BR>health; अनातुरः सप्तरात्रमवकीर्णिव्रतं<BR>चरेत् Ms. 2. 187; 4. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मन्
अनात्मन् a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Destitute<BR>of spirit or mind.<BR>--2 Not spiritual,<BR>corporeal.<BR>--3 One who has not<BR>restrained his self; अनात्मनस्तु शत्रुत्वे<BR>वर्तेतात्मैव शत्रुवत् Bg. 6. 6. --m. [<BR>अप्रशस्तो भिन्नो वा आत्मा न. त.] Not self,<BR>another, something different from<BR>आत्मन् (spirit or soul) i. e. the<BR>perishable body; अप्राप्तः प्राप्यते योयमत्यंतं<BR>त्यज्यते ऽथवा । जानीयात्तमनात्मानं बुद्ध्यंतं<BR>वपुरादिकम् ॥ अनात्मन्यात्मबुद्धिर्या साऽविद्या<BR>परिकीर्तिता ॥<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञ, वेदिन् a. {1}<BR>devoid of spiritual knowledge or<BR>true wisdom. {2} not knowing<BR>oneself, foolish, silly; मा तावदनात्मज्ञे<BR>Ś. 6; कथं कार्यविनिमयेन व्यवहरति मयि ˚ज्ञः<BR>M. 1; स्फुटमापदां पदमनात्मवेदिता<BR>Śi. 15. 22.<BR>--प्रत्यवेक्षा reflection that there<BR>is no spirit or soul (with Buddhists).<BR>--संपन्न a. foolish, destitute of<BR>qualities (of the soul), not<BR>self-possessed; न त्वेवानात्मसंपन्नाद् वृत्तिमीहेत<BR>पंडितः Pt. 1. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मक
अनात्मक a. [नास्ति आत्मा स्थिरो यत्र]<BR>Unreal, transitory, of an<BR>unenduring character, an epithet (with<BR>Buddhists) for the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मनीन
अनात्मनीन a. Not adapted to, or<BR>for the benefit of, self; disinterested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्मवत्|अनात्मवन्त्
अनात्मवत् a. [आत्मा वश्यत्वेन नास्त्यस्य]<BR>Not self-possessed; having no<BR>control over the senses; अनात्मवंतः<BR>पशुवत् भुंजते येऽप्रमाणतः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्म्य
अनात्म्य a. [आत्मनः इदं आत्म्यं शरीरं<BR>न. ब.] Impersonal, incorporeal (<BR>अशरीर).<BR>--त्म्यं Want of affection for<BR>one's own family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनात्यंतिक|अनात्यन्तिक
अनात्यंतिक a.<BR>1 Not constant or<BR>perpetual, not final.<BR>--2 Intermittent,<BR>recurrent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाथ|अनाथः
अनाथ a. [न. ब.] Helpless,<BR>poor, forlorn, parentless, orphan<BR>(as a child); widowed (as a wife);<BR>having no master or natural<BR>protector, without a protector in general;<BR>नाथवंतस्त्वया लोकास्त्वमनाथा विपत्स्यसे<BR>U. 1. 43; R. 12. 12.<BR>--थं Ved.<BR>Helplessness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पिंडदः, --पिंडिकः ‘giver<BR>of food to the poor,’ N. of a merchant<BR>in whose garden Buddha Gautama<BR>used to instruct his pupils.<BR>--सभा<BR>a poorhouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादर|अनादरः
अनादर a. [न. ब.] Showing no<BR>respect, indifferent, calm,<BR>regardless; M. 3. 15.<BR>--रः [न. त.]<BR>1<BR>Disregard, disrespect, disdain, contempt;<BR>षष्ठी चानादरे P. II. 3. 38, मन्यकर्मणि<BR>अनादरे विभाषाऽ प्राणिषु 17.<BR>--2 Ease,<BR>facility (one of the senses of आदर<BR>being ‘effort or care’, see the word);<BR>˚खंडितशंकरशरासनः U. 1 (perhaps<BR>also ‘without any respect for the<BR>bow of the great god’);<BR>अनादरोपात्तधृतैकसायकं Ki. 14. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादरणं|अनादरण
अनादरणं Disrespectful conduct,<BR>neglect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादरिन्
अनादरिन् a. Disrespectful,<BR>irreverent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादि|अनादिः
अनादि a. [आदिः कारणं पूर्वकालो वा<BR>नास्ति यस्य सः] Having no beginning,<BR>eternal, existing from eternity,<BR>epithet of परमेश्वर; जगदादिरनादिस्त्वं<BR>Ku. 2. 9; अनादिरादिर्गोविंदः<BR>सर्वकारणकारणं; also of हिरण्यगर्भ.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनंत,<BR>--अंत a. without beginning and end;<BR>eternal.<BR>--(तः) N. of Śiva.<BR>--निधन a.<BR>having neither beginning nor end,<BR>eternal.<BR>--मध्यांत a. having no<BR>beginning, middle or end; eternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिता
अनादिता --त्वं State of having no<BR>beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादित्वं|अनादित्व
अनादिता --त्वं State of having no<BR>beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादिमत्|अनादिमन्त्
अनादिमत् a. Not produced or<BR>effected, having no beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादीनव
अनादीनव a. Faultless;<BR>यद्वासुदेवेनादीनमनादीनवमीरितं Śi. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादृत|अनादृतः
अनादृत a.<BR>1 Disrespected,<BR>despised; Ms. 2. 234; ˚सत्कार not accepting<BR>the hospitality.<BR>--2 Not careful,<BR>regardless of, indifferent to;<BR>अनादृतस्यामरसायकेष्वपि Ki. 14. 10.<BR>--तं<BR>Disrespect, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादेय
अनादेय a. Not fit to be taken,<BR>unacceptable; inadmissible; अनादेयस्य<BR>चादानादादेयस्य च वर्जनात् Ms. 8. 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनादेशः|अनादेश
अनादेशः Absence of direction<BR>or command.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a. doing<BR>what is not commanded; or<BR>(अन्-आदेशकर) not doing what is ordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाद्य
अनाद्य a.<BR>1 = अनादि q. v.<BR>--2 Not<BR>eatable; what ought not to be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधार
अनाधार a. Without support, an<BR>epithet applicable, according to the<BR>Naiyāyikas, to eternal objects only<BR>(such as sky), or to Brahma<BR>according to the Vedāntins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधि
अनाधि a. Without mental pain<BR>or anxiety; R. 9. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्
अनाधृष् a. Ved. Not checking<BR>or not being checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्ट
अनाधृष्ट --ष्य a.<BR>1 Invincible,<BR>unchecked, irresistible.<BR>--2 Perfect,<BR>unimpaired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाधृष्य
अनाधृष्ट --ष्य a.<BR>1 Invincible,<BR>unchecked, irresistible.<BR>--2 Perfect,<BR>unimpaired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुकृत्य
अनानुकृत्य a. Ved. Inimitable,<BR>unparalleled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुद
अनानुद a. Ved. [अनु ददाति;<BR>दाक न. त., पृ. दीर्घः] Unsurpassed in<BR>giving (अतुल्यदातृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुपूर्व्यं|अनानुपूर्व्य
अनानुपूर्व्यं<BR>1 Separation of the<BR>different members of compounds by<BR>the intervention of others.<BR>--2 Not<BR>coming in regular order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनानुभूतिः|अनानुभूति
अनानुभूतिः f. Ved. Neglect,<BR>absence of experience or observation,<BR>inattention. --(pl.) Neglectful people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापद्
अनापद् f. Absence of calamity<BR>or misfortune; Ms. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनापि
अनापि a. [आप्यते-आप् कर्मणि इन्<BR>आपिः आप्तो बंधुश्च, न. ब. Tv.] Without<BR>friends or kindreds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्त|अनाप्तः
अनाप्त a.<BR>1 Not obtained.<BR>--2 Not<BR>reaching or attaining, unsuccessful<BR>in the attempt to get.<BR>--3 Unfit, not<BR>apt, unskilful; युग्यस्थाः प्राजकेऽनाप्ते<BR>सर्वे दंड्याः शतं शतं Ms. 8. 294.<BR>--प्तः<BR>A stranger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्तिः|अनाप्ति
अनाप्तिः f. Non-attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाप्तृ
अनाप्तृ^1 a. Not getting &c.;<BR>अनाप्तुरेनसां Śi. 16. 38 not touched by sin.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: cf. ap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाभयिन्
अनाभयिन् a. Ved. [आबिभेति<BR>आभी-उणा-इनि, आभयिन् न. त.] Not at all<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">Page0062-a+ 56</a>]<BR>afraid, fearless, undaunted;<BR>अनाभयिन्नरिमा ते Rv. 8. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाभू
अनाभू a. Ved. [आभिमुख्येन<BR>भवतीत्याभूः स्तोता न. त.] Not praising or<BR>worshipping, irreligious (अस्तोतृ);<BR>not coming in front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामन्
अनामन् a.<BR>1 Nameless.<BR>--2<BR>Infamous. --m.<BR>1 ‘The nameless’ month,<BR>an intercalary month.<BR>--2 The<BR>ring finger; see अनामिका below. --n. [<BR>अननमनः, अनं जीवनं अमयति रुजति,<BR>अम्-कनिन् Tv.] Piles (अर्शोरोग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामक|अनामकं|अनामकः
अनामक a. [न. ब. स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>Nameless, infamous.<BR>--कः-कं = अनामन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामा
अनामा, अनामिका [नास्ति नाम<BR>अन्यांगुलिवत् यस्याः, स्वार्थे कन्] The ring finger;<BR>so called because it has no name<BR>like the other fingers; cf. Tv. तया हि<BR>शिवेन ब्रह्मशिरश्छिन्नं, तेन तस्या<BR>अपवित्रजातीयता; अतएव तस्याः पवित्रीकरणार्थं यज्ञादौ<BR>पवित्रनामककुशधारणं तत्र क्रियते ।<BR>अनामिकाधृता दर्भा ह्येकानामिकयापि वा ।<BR>द्वाभ्यामनामिकाभ्यांतु धार्ये दर्भपवित्रके ॥; also पुरा<BR>कवीनांगणनाप्रसंगे कनिष्ठिकाधिष्ठितकालिदासा । अद्यापि<BR>तत्तुल्यकवेरभावादनामिका सार्थवती बभूव ॥.<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामिका
अनामा, अनामिका [नास्ति नाम<BR>अन्यांगुलिवत् यस्याः, स्वार्थे कन्] The ring finger;<BR>so called because it has no name<BR>like the other fingers; cf. Tv. तया हि<BR>शिवेन ब्रह्मशिरश्छिन्नं, तेन तस्या<BR>अपवित्रजातीयता; अतएव तस्याः पवित्रीकरणार्थं यज्ञादौ<BR>पवित्रनामककुशधारणं तत्र क्रियते ।<BR>अनामिकाधृता दर्भा ह्येकानामिकयापि वा ।<BR>द्वाभ्यामनामिकाभ्यांतु धार्ये दर्भपवित्रके ॥; also पुरा<BR>कवीनांगणनाप्रसंगे कनिष्ठिकाधिष्ठितकालिदासा । अद्यापि<BR>तत्तुल्यकवेरभावादनामिका सार्थवती बभूव ॥.<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामय|अनामयं|अनामयः
अनामय a. [नास्ति आमयः रोगो यस्य]<BR>Free from disease, healthy, sound;<BR>जन्मबंधविनिर्मुक्ताः पदं गच्छंत्यनामयं<BR>Bg. 2. 51 where there is no unhappiness.<BR>--यः --यं Good or sound health; health,<BR>well-being, welfare; स<BR>भवंतमनामयप्रश्नपूर्वकमाह Ś. 5; महाश्वेता<BR>कादंबरीमनामयं पप्रच्छ K. 192 inquired about<BR>her health; अप्यनामयं राज्ञः Mv. 1<BR>how does the king do? ब्राह्मणं कुशलं<BR>पृच्छेत्क्षात्रबंधुमनामयं । वैश्यं क्षेमं समागम्य<BR>शूद्रमारोग्यमेव च Ms. 2. 127.<BR>--यः [नास्ति<BR>भयं यस्मात्] N. of Viṣṇu (or Śiva<BR>according to some); पुण्यकीर्तिरनामयः;<BR>विष्णुर्हि बाह्याभ्यंतरपीडां निवारयति<BR>तस्मादनामयः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयत्|अनामयन्त्
अनामयत् a. Ved. Not causing pain<BR>or hurt, not hurting. --n. Health (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामयित्नु
अनामयित्नु a.<BR>1 Not injuring or<BR>paining; हस्ताभ्यामनामयित्नुभ्यां<BR>Rv. 10. 137. 7.<BR>--2 Salubrious, curative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामिष
अनामिष a. Without flesh or<BR>any bait; bootless, profitless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामृण
अनामृण a. [आमृणाति हिनस्ति<BR>आमृण्क. न. ब.] Having no injurer or an<BR>enemy that can injure (हिंसकरहित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनामृत
अनामृत a. Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायक
अनायक a. Without a leader,<BR>disorderly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत
अनायत a.<BR>1 Unrestrained,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-b" target="_blank">Page0062-b+ 55</a>]<BR>unchecked.<BR>--2 Not propped or<BR>supported.<BR>--3 Not long, of short duration;<BR>अनायतस्वभावभंगुराणि सुखानि K. 175.<BR>--4 Continuous, close, unseparated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायत्त|अनायत्तः
अनायत्त a. Not dependent; ˚त्तो<BR>रोषस्य K. 45 not swayed by;<BR>uncontrolled, independent;<BR>एतावज्जन्मसाफल्यं यदनायत्तवृत्तिता H. 2. 22 freedom,<BR>independent livelihood,<BR>independence of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायन
अनायन a. [न आयनं चालनं यत्र]<BR>Invariable (एकांत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायास|अनायासः
अनायास a. Not troublesome or<BR>difficult, easy; ममाप्येकस्मिन् ˚से कर्मणि<BR>त्वया सहायेन भवितव्यं Ś. 2.<BR>--सः<BR>1<BR>Facility, ease, absence of difficulty or<BR>exertion; शरीरं पीड्यते येन शुभेनाप्यशुभेन<BR>वा । अत्यंतं तन्न कुर्वीत अनायासः स उच्यते ॥<BR>--2 Idleness, neglect; ˚सेन easily,<BR>without difficulty, readily.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत a. done easily or readily.<BR>--(तं) an infusion prepared without<BR>effort or exertion (prepared<BR>extemporaneously) Ak. See फांट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनायुष्य
अनायुष्य a. [आयुषे न हितं न. त.]<BR>Not giving long life, fatal to long<BR>life (such as excessive food, sexual<BR>union &c.); अनारोग्यमनायुष्यमस्वर्ग्यं<BR>चातिभोजनं Ms. 2. 57, 4. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारत|अनारतं
अनारत a.<BR>1 Not ceasing or<BR>stopping, continuous, uninterrupted.<BR>--2<BR>Eternal.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Continuity.<BR>--2<BR>Absolute non-entity (अत्यंताभाव). --adv.<BR>Continuously, always; eternally;<BR>अनारतं तेन पदेषु लंभिताः Ki. 1. 15, 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारंभः|अनारम्भ|अनारम्भः
अनारंभः Non-commencement,<BR>not undertaking; विकारं खलु<BR>परमार्थतोऽज्ञात्वा ˚भः प्रतीकारस्य Ś. 3; ˚भो हि<BR>कार्याणां प्रथमं बुद्धिलक्षणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारभ्य
अनारभ्य a. Unfit to be<BR>commenced or undertaken --ind. Without<BR>commencing; without reference to<BR>any particular thing; e. g. ˚वादः<BR>detached remark (upon sacrifices &c);<BR>किंचित्कर्मारभ्य उद्यते उच्यते इत्यारभ्यवादः न<BR>आरभ्यवादः.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधीत a. [न<BR>आरभ्य किंचिदधीतः] studied or taught<BR>or read without reference to any<BR>particular subject (not as part of a<BR>regular or authoritative work); learnt<BR>as a detached subject; येषां मंत्राणां<BR>कर्मविशेषे विनियोगो नोक्तः तेषां मंत्राणां<BR>अनारभ्याधीतत्वात् ब्रह्मयज्ञे एव विनियोग इति मीमांसा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारंभण|अनारम्भण
अनारंभण a. Having no support<BR>(for अनालंबन); also written अनारंबण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनारोग्य
अनारोग्य a. [नास्ति आरोग्यं यस्मात्<BR>न. ब.] Unwholesome, not conducive<BR>to good health, fatal to health;<BR>अनायुष्यमनारोग्यमस्वर्ग्यं चातिभोजनं<BR>Ms. 2. 57.<BR>--ग्यं Sickness, indisposition;<BR>˚कर unhealthy, unwholesome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्जव|अनार्जवं|अनार्ज्जव
अनार्जव a. Crooked; dishonest.<BR>--वं<BR>1 Crookedness (moral also), fraud,<BR>insincerity Śi. 8. 11.<BR>--2 [नास्ति आर्जवं<BR>सारल्यं स्वाच्छंद्यं वा यस्मिन्] Disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्तव|अनार्त्तव
अनार्तव a. (वी f.) Unseasonable,<BR>inopportune, premature (as a flower<BR>blossoming out of season).<BR>--वा A<BR>girl who has not attained to<BR>puberty (the menstruation period).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्य|अनार्यः|अनार्य्य|अनार्य्यः
अनार्य a. Not respectable (not<BR>deserving to be styled आर्य), not<BR>polite or decent; vulgar; not<BR>belonging to an Ārya, unworthy, vile, base,<BR>mean, wretched; अनार्यानार्यलिंगिनः<BR>Ms. 9. 260; अनार्यायां समुत्पन्नो<BR>ब्राह्मणात् 10. 66; H. 4. 25; कीटका नाम<BR>देशोऽनार्यनिवासः Nir. void of Āryas;<BR>शकुंतलायामनार्यमाचरितं तेन राज्ञा Ś. 4<BR>the king has behaved basely or<BR>unworthily towards Śakuntalā;<BR>कदाचिदस्मिन्नप्यनार्योऽनार्यमाचरिष्यति Ve. 4.<BR>--र्यः<BR>1 One who is not an Ārya.<BR>--2 A<BR>country not inhabited by the Āryas.<BR>--3 A Śūdra.<BR>--4 A Mleccha.<BR>--5 An<BR>ignoble person.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मिन् a.<BR>doing work unbecoming an Ārya or<BR>becoming only a non-Ārya.<BR>--ज a. of<BR>vile or base origin.<BR>--(जं) [अनार्यदेशे<BR>जातं] agallochum (being produced in<BR>the country of the Mlecchas &c.).<BR>--जुष्ट a. discarded by the good, not<BR>practised or observed by the Āryas<BR>or respectable people.<BR>--तिक्तः [<BR>अनार्याप्रियः तिक्तः शाक. त] N. of the plant<BR>Gentiana Cherayta Rox. (Mar.<BR>किराईत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्यकं|अनार्यक|अनार्य्यक|अनार्य्यकं
अनार्यकं [अनार्ये देशे भवं अनार्यकं]<BR>Agallochum or aloe wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्ष
अनार्ष a.<BR>1 Not belonging to the<BR>Ṛṣis, not Vedic; not belonging to<BR>the text of a Vedic hymn (as इति<BR>used in the Padapāṭha with certain<BR>words not followed in the Saṃhitā<BR>by इति); संबुद्धौ शाकल्यस्येतौ अनार्षे<BR>P. I. 1. 16 (= अवैदिके Sk.).<BR>--2 Not added to<BR>a Ṛṣi's name (as an affix);<BR>P. IV. 1. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनार्षेय
अनार्षेय = अनार्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालंब|अनालम्ब|अनालम्बः
अनालंब a. Without support or<BR>stay; कथंकारमनालंबा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">Page0063-a+ 55</a>]<BR>कीर्तिर्द्यामधिरोहति Śi. 2. 52.<BR>--बः Want of support;<BR>despondency.<BR>--बी Śiva's lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालंबुका|अनालम्बुका
अनालंबु(भु)का A woman<BR>during menstruation (रजस्वला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालंभुका|अनालम्भुका
अनालंबु(भु)का A woman<BR>during menstruation (रजस्वला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालाप|अनालापः
अनालाप a. [न. ब.] Reserved,<BR>taciturn.<BR>--पः Reserve, taciturnity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनालोचित|अनालोचितः
अनालोचित a. Unseen,<BR>unheeded, unconsidered, unexpected, not<BR>well considered or examined, rash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावया
अनावया a. Ved. Not yielding<BR>or desisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावर्तिः|अनावर्ति|अनावर्त्ति
अनावर्तिः f. Non-return (to birth),<BR>final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावर्तिन्
अनावर्तिन् a. Not recurring or<BR>returning; ˚र्ती कालो व्रजति स वृथा तन्न<BR>गणितं Bh. 3. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाविद्ध
अनाविद्ध a.<BR>1 Not pierced or<BR>wounded; unperforated; ˚द्धं रत्नं<BR>Ś. 2. 10.<BR>--2 Unhurt, uninjured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाविल|अनाविलः
अनाविल a.<BR>1 Not turbid or<BR>muddy, pure, clear.<BR>--2 Not marshy,<BR>wholesome, salubrious, as a country<BR>Ms. 7. 69 (रोगोपसर्गाद्यैरनाकुल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृत्त
अनावृत्त a. Not returning, not<BR>repeated, being for the first time;<BR>मलमासेप्यनावृत्तां तीर्थयात्रां विवर्जयेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृत्तिः|अनावृत्ति
अनावृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Non-return, absence<BR>of repetition or recurrence.<BR>--2<BR>Non-return (to birth), final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनावृष्टिः|अनावृष्टि
अनावृष्टिः f. Drought, one of the<BR>kinds of ईति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाव्रस्कः|अनाव्रस्क
अनाव्रस्कः Uninjured condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश
अनाश a. [न. ब. नास्ति आशा यस्य]<BR>1 Hopeless, despondent.<BR>--2 [नास्ति<BR>नाशो यस्य] Imperishable, living,<BR>undestroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशक
अनाशक a. [न आ सम्यक् यथेच्छं आशः<BR>अशनं यस्य, न नाशो यस्य वा, न. ब. कप्]<BR>Devoid of full enjoyment or<BR>indestructible, not hurtful.<BR>--कं Fast,<BR>abstaining from eating even to death;<BR>यज्ञेन दानेन तपसाऽनाशकेनैतमेव<BR>विदित्वा मुनिर्भवति Bṛ. Ār. Up.; Y. 3. 154.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशकायनं|अनाशकायन
अनाशकायनं [न नश्यति अनाशकः<BR>आत्मा तस्यायनं प्राप्त्युपायः] The state of<BR>ब्रह्मचर्य, unmarried or student's life,<BR>devoted to contemplation and<BR>knowledge of the soul; अथ<BR>यदनाशकायनमित्याचक्षते ब्रह्मचर्यमेव तत् । एष ह्यात्मा न<BR>नश्यति यं ब्रह्मचर्येणानुविंदते Ch. Up.; a course<BR>of fasting as a penance (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशस्त
अनाशस्त a. Not praised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशिन्
अनाशिन् a. [न नश्यति or न<BR>कर्मफलमश्रुते; न. त.] Imperishable,<BR>indestructible, as the Soul or Supreme<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">Page0063-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Being; अनाशिनोऽप्रमेयस्य Mb. (<BR>ईश्वरस्य कर्मफलभोक्तृत्वाभावात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाशु
अनाशु a. [नश् उण्, न. त.]<BR>1<BR>Imperishable, indestructible.<BR>--2 [अश्<BR>उण्, न. त.] Not pervading or<BR>occupying.<BR>--3 [न-आशु] Not quick, slow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रमिन्
अनाश्रमिन् m. One who does<BR>not belong to, or follow, any of the<BR>4 orders of life (गृहस्थाद्याश्रमशून्य);<BR>अनाश्रमी न तिष्ठेत्तु क्षणमेकमपि द्विजः;<BR>अनाश्रम-मे-वासः not dwelling in any<BR>Āśrama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रय|अनाश्रयः
अनाश्रय a. Defenceless,<BR>unprotected, isolated.<BR>--यः<BR>Self-dependence, isolation, absence of support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रव
अनाश्रव a. Not listening to,<BR>obstinate, turning a deaf ear to;<BR>तथानुशिष्टापि अनाश्रवैवासीत् Dk. 57;<BR>K. 350; भिषजामनाश्रवः R. 19. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्रित
अनाश्रित a. Not connected with,<BR>or dependent on, independent,<BR>detached; non-inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाश्वस्
अनाश्वस् a. [अश् भोजने क्वसु<BR>निपातः न. त. P. III. 2. 109] Not having<BR>eaten or enjoyed, fasting;<BR>धृतजयधृतेरनाशुषः Ki. 12. 2; Śi. 14. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्
अनास् a. [आस्यते निरास्यते<BR>ष्ठीवनमनेन इति आः मुखं, तन्नास्ति साधनत्वेन अस्य]<BR>Without mouth or face; without the<BR>power of speech (आस्यव्यापारशब्दरहित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनासादित
अनासादित a. Not obtained,<BR>not found or met with; not<BR>encountered or attacked; not occurred<BR>or having happened, non-existent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विग्रह a. unused to war,<BR>having had no occasion to fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्था
अनास्था<BR>1 Indifference,<BR>unconcern, want of consideration; अनास्था<BR>बाह्यवस्तुषु Ku. 6. 63; पिंडेष्वनास्था खलु<BR>भौतिकेषु R. 2. 57; स्त्री पुमानित्यनास्थैषा<BR>वृत्तं हि महितं सतां Ku. 6. 12 a male<BR>or female is no consideration &c.;<BR>Ki. 4. 34.<BR>--2 Want of faith or<BR>confidence, want of devotedness,<BR>disrespect; अत्यद्भुतैर्मम हृतस्य तथाप्यनास्था<BR>Mv. 2. 39 diffidence. --a. (स्थ)<BR>Indifferent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्थान
अनास्थान a.<BR>1 Having no fixed<BR>seat or site.<BR>--2 Having or yielding<BR>no basis or fulcrum, unfit for a<BR>fixed seat (as water); Rv. 1. 116. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्वाद|अनास्वादः
अनास्वाद a. Without taste,<BR>insipid.<BR>--दः Insipidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्वादित
अनास्वादित a. Untasted; Ś. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनास्राव
अनास्राव a. Without injury or<BR>hurt (क्लेशरहित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहत|अनाहतं|अनाहतः
अनाहत a.<BR>1 Unbeaten,<BR>unwounded, intact.<BR>--2 [आहतं छेदो भोगो<BR>वा तन्नास्ति यस्य] New and unbleached<BR>(as cloth) (Mar. कोरें).<BR>--3 Not<BR>produced by beating (as sound).<BR>--4<BR>Not multiplied.<BR>--तं --तः The 4th of<BR>the mystical Cakras in the body,<BR>(तंत्रशास्त्रे प्रसिद्धं हृदयस्थितं सुषुम्णामध्यस्थं<BR>द्वादशदलपद्मं); शब्दो ब्रह्ममयः शब्दोऽनाहतो यत्र<BR>दृश्यते । अनाहताख्यं तत् पद्मं मुनिभिः<BR>परिकीर्तितम् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहार|अनाहारः
अनाहार a. Abstaining from<BR>food, fasting.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Abstinence from<BR>food, fasting; अनाहारेणात्मानं<BR>व्यापादयिष्यामि H. 1.<BR>--2 Non-production.<BR>--3<BR>Non-seizure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहारिन्
अनाहारिन् a. Fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहार्य|अनाहार्य्य
अनाहार्य a.<BR>1 Not artificial,<BR>natural, not producible.<BR>--2 Not eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहुतिः|अनाहुति
अनाहुतिः f. Not sacrificing; a<BR>sacrifice not worthy of that name;<BR>also an improper oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनाहूत|अनाहूतः
अनाहूत a. Not called,<BR>uninvited.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपजल्पिन् an<BR>uncalled-for speaker or boaster.<BR>--उपविष्ट a.<BR>seated as an uninvited guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिकेत
अनिकेत a. Houseless, vagrant;<BR>having no fixed abode (as a<BR>recluse); Ms. 6. 25, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिक्षुः|अनिक्षु
अनिक्षुः [न इक्षुः सादृश्ये अप्राशस्त्ये वा<BR>नञ्] Not (true) sugarcane, a sort of<BR>long grass or reed producing coarse<BR>sugar; Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिगीर्ण|अनिगीर्णः|अनिगीर्ण्ण
अनिगीर्ण a.<BR>1 Not swallowed.<BR>--2<BR>(In Rhet.) Not hidden or concealed,<BR>present, not to be supplied (<BR>अनपह्नुतभेद); e. g. in अश्वः श्वेतो धावति, the श्वेतत्व<BR>of the horse is not निगीर्ण or hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिग्रह|अनिग्रहः
अनिग्रह a. Unrestrained,<BR>invincible, unconquerable.<BR>--हः<BR>1<BR>Nonrestraint.<BR>--2 Non-refutation.<BR>--3 Not<BR>admitting one's defeat in argument;<BR>˚स्थानं occasion of non-refutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिंग्य|अनिङ्ग्य
अनिंग्य^1 a. Not divisible, a<BR>word not divisible.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20151125. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/162. note: convention error, use of anusvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छ
अनिच्छ, --च्छक, --च्छु, --च्छुक, --च्छत् a.<BR>Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR>reluctant; अनिच्छंतमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छक
अनिच्छ, --च्छक, --च्छु, --च्छुक, --च्छत् a.<BR>Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR>reluctant; अनिच्छंतमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छु|अनिच्छुः|अनिछु
अनिच्छ, --च्छक, --च्छु, --च्छुक, --च्छत् a.<BR>Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR>reluctant; अनिच्छंतमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छुक
अनिच्छ, --च्छक, --च्छु, --च्छुक, --च्छत् a.<BR>Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR>reluctant; अनिच्छंतमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छत्|अनिच्छन्त्
अनिच्छ, --च्छक, --च्छु, --च्छुक, --च्छत् a.<BR>Not desirous, unwilling, averse,<BR>reluctant; अनिच्छंतमपि मां against my will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिच्छा
अनिच्छा Unwillingness,<BR>indifference, reluctance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित
अनित a. [अन्-इत] Not gone<BR>with, unattended, destitute of; ˚भा<BR>having no splendour; वनितयाऽ<BR>नितया रजनीवधूः R. 9. 38; Śi. 6. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनित्य|अनित्यः
अनित्य a.<BR>1 Not eternal or<BR>everlasting, transient, non-eternal,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-a" target="_blank">Page0064-a+ 57</a>]<BR>perishable (नश्वर) (opp. नित्य);<BR>गंधवती पृथ्वी सा द्विविधा नित्याऽनित्या च<BR>T. S. 9 (अनित्या = कार्यरूपा); See नित्य;<BR>यदि नित्यमनित्येन निर्मलं मलवाहिना ।<BR>यशः कायेन लभ्येत तन्न लब्धं भवेन्नु किं ॥<BR>H. 1. 48; Ms. 6. 77; धर्मोऽनित्यः<BR>सुखदुःखेप्यनित्ये जीवोऽनित्यो<BR>हेतुरस्याप्यनित्यः Mb.<BR>--2 Occasional, temporary,<BR>casual; not peremptory or obligatory<BR>as a rule &c., special.<BR>--3 Unusual,<BR>extraordinary; वर्णे चानित्ये<BR>P. V. 4. 30 (लोहितकः कोपेन अन्यथा तु श्वेतवर्ण इति<BR>भावः); आनाय्योऽनित्ये III. 1. 127 (स<BR>हि गार्हपत्यादानीयतेऽनित्यश्च सततमप्रज्वलनात्<BR>Sk.) See VI. 1. 147.<BR>--4 Unsteady,<BR>fickle, not permanent; अनित्यं यौवनं रूपं<BR>H. 4. 68; ˚हृदया हिताः Rām.<BR>--5<BR>Uncertain, doubtful; अनित्यो विजयो<BR>यस्माद्दृश्यते युध्यमानयोः Ms. 7. 199; विजयस्य<BR>ह्यनित्यत्वात् Pt. 3. 22.<BR>--त्यं adv.<BR>Occasionally, not permanently,<BR>incidentally, casually; अनित्यं हि स्थितो<BR>यस्मात् Ms. 3. 102.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन्, --क्रिया an occasional act, such as a<BR>sacrifice for a special purpose,<BR>a voluntary and occasional act.<BR>--दत्तः,<BR>दत्तकः, -दत्रिमः a son given by his<BR>parents to another temporarily (for<BR>temporary or preliminary adoption).<BR>--प्रत्यवेक्षा (with Buddhists) the<BR>consciousness that every thing is<BR>perishable and is passing away.<BR>--भावः transitoriness, transient state,<BR>limited nature or existence; so<BR>अनित्यता-त्वं frailty, instability.<BR>--समः<BR>a sophism or fallacious reasoning<BR>which generalizes what is<BR>exceptional (as अनित्यत्वं).<BR>--समासः a<BR>compound which it is not obligatory to<BR>form in every case (the sense of<BR>which may be equally expressed by<BR>resolving it into its constituent<BR>members.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिद्र
अनिद्र a. Sleepless, awake; (fig.)<BR>vigilant, watchful,<BR>--द्रा<BR>sleeplessness, vigilance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिधृष्ट
अनिधृष्ट a. Unchecked,<BR>unsubdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिन
अनिन a. Ved. Having no master<BR>or lord (इन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिंद्र|अनिन्द्र
अनिंद्र a. [न. ब.] Dispensing<BR>with or disregarding Indra or his<BR>worship; (इंद्रोपासनाशून्य); मामनिंद्राः<BR>कृणवन्ननुक्थाः Rv. 5. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिंद्रियं|अनिन्द्रिय
अनिंद्रियं<BR>1 Reason (that which is<BR>not the senses).<BR>--2 Not an organ<BR>of sense, the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिपद्यमान
अनिपद्यमान a. Not falling down<BR>(to sleep), untiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिपातः|अनिपात
अनिपातः Not a fall,<BR>continuance of life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिबद्ध
अनिबद्ध a. Not bound,<BR>incoherent; ˚प्रलापिन् prattling (talking<BR>incoherently).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिबाध|अनिबाधः
अनिबाध a. Unobstructed;<BR>Rv. 3. 1. 11.<BR>--धः Liberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभृत
अनिभृत a.<BR>1 Not private or<BR>reserved, public, open, not hidden.<BR>--2 Immodest, bold.<BR>--3 Unsteady, not<BR>firm, tremulous; ˚करेष्वाक्षिपत्सु प्रियेषु<BR>Me. 68; ˚वेलावीचिबाहुः Ki. 3. 60,<BR>13. 66; असौ संध्याशंखध्वनिरनिभृतः खे<BR>विचरति Māl. 2. 12 not hidden, loud;<BR>Śi. 10. 66. See निभृत also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभृष्ट
अनिभृष्ट a. [नि-भ्रंश्-क्त, निपातः न-त.]<BR>Unobstructed, unimpaired,<BR>unabated; Rv. 2. 25. 4, 10. 116. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिभ्य
अनिभ्य a. Not wealthy (इभ्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमकः|अनिमक
अनिमकः [अन्-जीवने शब्दे च, भावे<BR>बाहु˚ इमन् इत्यनिमः जीवनं, तेन कायति<BR>प्रकाशते, कै-क. Tv.]<BR>1 A frog (तस्य मरणेपि<BR>पुनरुज्जीवनात्).<BR>--2 A cuckoo.<BR>--3 A bee<BR>(उभयोरपि तयोः मधुरशब्देन प्रकाशमानत्वात्).<BR>--4 The filament of a lotus,<BR>पद्मकेशर.<BR>--5 N. of the tree मधूक Med.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमान
अनिमान a. Unbounded, immense<BR>(अपरिच्छिन्न); ˚नो धूमकेतुः Rv. 1. 27. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमित्त
अनिमित्त a. Causeless,<BR>groundless; casual, incidental;<BR>आलक्ष्यदंतमुकुलाननिमित्तहासैः Ś. 7. 17; ˚त्तं मित्रं<BR>disinterested, Dk. 25; ˚उत्कंठा M. 3. 9.<BR>--त्तं<BR>1 Absence of an adequate<BR>cause or occasion, causelessness,<BR>groundlessness.<BR>--2 A bad omen,<BR>ill omen; चारुदत्तस्यैव दर्शनमनिमित्तं<BR>प्रमार्जयिष्यति Mk. 6; ममानिमित्तानि हि<BR>खेदयंति 9. 10; शमनार्थं अनिमित्तस्य<BR>Ve. 2, 3. --adv.,<BR>--˚तः Groundlessly,<BR>causelessly, without any adequate<BR>cause; अनिमित्तमिंदुवदने किमत्रभवतः<BR>पराङ्मुखी भवसि M. 1. 18; Ms. 4. 144.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--निराक्रिया averting ill<BR>omens.<BR>--लिंगनाशः a kind of<BR>ophthalmic disease ending in total darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषं|अनिमिष|अनिमिषः
अनिमिषं --षा --मेषं ind. Ved. Without<BR>winking, vigilantly; incessantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषा
अनिमिषं --षा --मेषं ind. Ved. Without<BR>winking, vigilantly; incessantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमेषं|अनिमेष|अनिमेषः
अनिमिषं --षा --मेषं ind. Ved. Without<BR>winking, vigilantly; incessantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिष|अनिमिषं|अनिमिषः
अनिमि(मे)ष a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Not<BR>winking, steadfastly or intently<BR>fixed; ˚लोचनं सुचिरमालोक्य K. 102;<BR>˚पक्ष्मणा 131; शतैस्तमक्ष्णामनिमेषवृत्तिभिः<BR>R. 3. 43; ˚दर्शनरमणीयैः K. 50 fish<BR>and twinkleless glances.<BR>--2 Vigilant,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">Page0064-c+ 56</a>]<BR>watchful.<BR>--3 Open (as eyes, flowers).<BR>--षः<BR>1 A god (for the eyes of gods<BR>do not twinkle); Śi. 5. 57.<BR>--2<BR>A fish.<BR>--3 Viṣṇu.<BR>--4 N. of Mahākāla.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दृष्टि, --नयन, --लोचन a.<BR>looking steadfastly or with a fixed gaze,<BR>gazing intently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमेष|अनिमेषं|अनिमेषः
अनिमि(मे)ष a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Not<BR>winking, steadfastly or intently<BR>fixed; ˚लोचनं सुचिरमालोक्य K. 102;<BR>˚पक्ष्मणा 131; शतैस्तमक्ष्णामनिमेषवृत्तिभिः<BR>R. 3. 43; ˚दर्शनरमणीयैः K. 50 fish<BR>and twinkleless glances.<BR>--2 Vigilant,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">Page0064-c+ 56</a>]<BR>watchful.<BR>--3 Open (as eyes, flowers).<BR>--षः<BR>1 A god (for the eyes of gods<BR>do not twinkle); Śi. 5. 57.<BR>--2<BR>A fish.<BR>--3 Viṣṇu.<BR>--4 N. of Mahākāla.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दृष्टि, --नयन, --लोचन a.<BR>looking steadfastly or with a fixed gaze,<BR>gazing intently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिमिषीय
अनिमिषीय a. Relating to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियत|अनियतं
अनियत a.<BR>1 Uncontrolled,<BR>unrestricted.<BR>--2 Indefinite, uncertain,<BR>not fixed; irregular (forms also);<BR>˚वेलं आहारोऽश्यते Ś. 2 at irregular<BR>hours.<BR>--3 Causeless, casual, incidental,<BR>occasional; ˚रुदितस्मितं (वदनकमलकं)<BR>U. 4. 4; Māl. 10. 2.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः<BR>an indeterminate digit (in Math.).<BR>--आत्मन् a. not self-possessed, whose<BR>soul is not properly controlled.<BR>--पुंस्का<BR>a woman loose in conduct, unchaste.<BR>--वृत्ति a. {1} having no regular or<BR>fixed employment or application (as<BR>a word). {2} having no regular income.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियंत्रण
अनियंत्रण a. Unrestrained,<BR>uncontrolled, free; ˚अनुयोगो नाम<BR>तपस्विजनः Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियमः|अनियम
अनियमः<BR>1 Absence of rule,<BR>control, regulation or fixed order; no<BR>settled rule or direction; पंचमं लघु<BR>सर्वत्र सप्तमं द्विचतुर्थयोः । षष्ठे पादे गुरु ज्ञेयं<BR>शेषेष्वनियमो मतः ॥ Ch. M.<BR>--2 Irregularity,<BR>uncertainty, indefiniteness,<BR>vagueness, doubt.<BR>--3 Improper conduct.<BR>--a., अनियमित a. Irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनियुक्तः|अनियुक्त
अनियुक्तः An assessor at a<BR>court who has not been formally<BR>appointed and who is not entitled<BR>to vote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर
अनिर a. [न ईरयितुं शक्यते, ईर्-क<BR>पृ˚ थस्वः] That cannot be propelled<BR>or driven along; अप त्या अस्थुरनिरा<BR>Rv. 8. 48. 11 (प्रेरयितुमशक्य).<BR>--रा<BR>1 Want of food; utter destitution<BR>(अन्नरहितदारिद्र्यं); युयुतमस्मदनिराममीवां<BR>Rv. 7. 71. 2.<BR>--2 [नास्ति इरा अन्नं यस्याः<BR>पं. ब.] A calamity such as अतिवृष्टि,<BR>अनावृष्टि (= ईति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिराकरणं|अनिराकरण
अनिराकरणं Not obstructing or<BR>warding off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुक्त
अनिरुक्त a.<BR>1 Not articulated or<BR>clearly spoken.<BR>--2 Not clearly stated<BR>or explained, vague, not plain or<BR>well-defined; ˚क्तप्रातःसवनः प्रथमः<BR>Kāty.; एतस्मिन्नदृश्येऽनात्म्येऽनिरुक्ते<BR>Ait. Br.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गानं indistinct singing<BR>or humming, a particular mode of<BR>chanting the सामवेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0064-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिरुद्ध|अनिरुद्धं|अनिरुद्धः
अनिरुद्ध a. Unobstructed, free,<BR>uncontrolled, self-willed, unruly,<BR>ungovernable.<BR>--द्धः<BR>1 A spy, secret<BR>emissary.<BR>--2 N. of a son of Pradyumna.<BR>[Aniruddha was the son of Kāma and<BR>grandson of Kṛṣṇa. Uṣā, the daughter<BR>of a demon named Bāṇa, fell in love with<BR>him and had him brought by magic<BR>influence to her apartments in her father's city<BR>of Śoṇitapura. Bāṇa sent some guards to<BR>seize him, but the brave youth slew his<BR>assailants with only an iron club. At last,<BR>however, he was secured by means of<BR>magic powers. On discovering where<BR>Aniruddha had been carried, Kṛṣṇa,<BR>Balarāma and Kāma went to rescue him and<BR>a great battle was fought. Bāṇa, though<BR>aided by Śiva and Skanda, was<BR>vanquished, but his life was spared at the<BR>intercession of Śiva, and Aniruddha was<BR>carried home to Dvārakā with Uṣā as<BR>his wife. He had also another wife<BR>Rochanā, grand-daughter of king Rukmin<BR>of Vidarbha, who bore him a son named<BR>Vajra.].<BR>--3 Also N. of Viṣṇu; and<BR>of Śiva; of an Arhat, a<BR>contemporary of Buddha.<BR>--द्धं A cord<BR>or rope (for fastening cattle).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पथं [न निरुद्धः पंथा यत्र ब.]<BR>{1} unobstructed path. {2} the sky,<BR>atmosphere (तत्र कस्यापि गतिरोधनाभावात्).<BR>--भाविनी Aniruddha's wife Uṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्णयः|अनिर्णय
अनिर्णयः Uncertainty, indecision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्दश
अनिर्दश, अनिर्दशाह a. [न निर्गतानि<BR>दशाहानि यस्य] Within the 10 days of<BR>impurity caused either by<BR>childbirth or death; विगतं तु विदेशस्थं<BR>शृणुयाद्यो ह्यनिर्दशं Ms. 5. 75; अनिर्दशाया<BR>गोः क्षीरं 5. 8; 5. 79; 4. 212, 217;<BR>not ten days old; अनिर्दशाहां गां<BR>सूतां Ms. 8. 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्दशाह
अनिर्दश, अनिर्दशाह a. [न निर्गतानि<BR>दशाहानि यस्य] Within the 10 days of<BR>impurity caused either by<BR>childbirth or death; विगतं तु विदेशस्थं<BR>शृणुयाद्यो ह्यनिर्दशं Ms. 5. 75; अनिर्दशाया<BR>गोः क्षीरं 5. 8; 5. 79; 4. 212, 217;<BR>not ten days old; अनिर्दशाहां गां<BR>सूतां Ms. 8. 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्दिष्ट
अनिर्दिष्ट a. Undefined, not<BR>specified; क्व ˚कारणं गम्यते V. 2<BR>without a definite aim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्देशः|अनिर्देश
अनिर्देशः Absence of positive rule<BR>or direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्देश्य|अनिर्द्देश्य
अनिर्देश्य a. Undefinable, ineffable,<BR>indescribable, inexplicable,<BR>incomparable; ˚सुखः स्वर्गः कस्तं<BR>विस्मारयिष्यति V. 3. 18.<BR>--श्यं An epithet of<BR>the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्धारित|अनिर्धारितः
अनिर्धारित a. Not determined<BR>or ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्मल|अनिर्म्मल|अनिर्म्मलः
अनिर्मल a. Dirty, foul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वचनीय|अनिर्व्वचनीयः
अनिर्वचनीय a.<BR>1 Unutterable,<BR>indescribable, undefinable, epithet<BR>of the Supreme Being.<BR>--2<BR>Improper to be mentioned.<BR>--यं (In<BR>Vedānta)<BR>1 Māyā or illusion,<BR>ignorance.<BR>--2 The world.<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">Page0065-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--सर्वस्वं N. of a work by Śrīharṣa,<BR>also called खंडनखंडखाद्य; तत्र सर्वेषां<BR>पदार्थानां इदंतया निर्वक्तुमशक्यता दर्शिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वाण
अनिर्वाण a. Unwashed;<BR>unbathed; अरुंतुदमिवालानमनिर्वाणस्य दंतिनः<BR>R. 1. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वाहः|अनिर्वाह|अनिर्व्वाह|अनिर्व्वाहः
अनिर्वाहः<BR>1 Non-completion;<BR>nonaccomplishment.<BR>--2<BR>Inconclusiveness.<BR>--3 Insufficiency of income,<BR>being straitened in means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्विद|अनिर्व्विद
अनिर्विद a. Not fatigued or tired;<BR>अनिर्विदाया विदधे विधात्रा Śi. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्विण्ण|अनिर्व्विण्ण|अनिर्व्विण्णः
अनिर्विण्ण a. Not depressed or<BR>fatigued; an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वेदः|अनिर्वेद
अनिर्वेदः Non-depression, absence<BR>of dejection or despondency;<BR>self-reliance, plucking up courage;<BR>अनिर्वेदः श्रियो मूलमनिर्वेदः परं सुखं ।<BR>अनिर्वेदो हि सततं सर्वार्थेष्वनुवर्तते Rām.;<BR>अनिर्वेदप्राप्याणि श्रेयांसि V. 4; cf. ‘Faint<BR>heart never won fair lady’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वृत|अनिर्व्वृत
अनिर्वृत a.<BR>1 Ill at ease, uneasy,<BR>discomposed, unhappy.<BR>--2<BR>Unaccomplished, unfulfilled (अनिर्वृत्त also in<BR>this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वृतिः|अनिर्वृति|अनिर्व्वृति
अनिर्वृतिः --त्तिः f.<BR>1 Uneasiness,<BR>anxiety, disquietude.<BR>--2 Poverty,<BR>destitution; अनिर्वृतिनिशाचरी मम<BR>गृहांतरालं गता Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वृत्तिः|अनिर्वृत्ति
अनिर्वृतिः --त्तिः f.<BR>1 Uneasiness,<BR>anxiety, disquietude.<BR>--2 Poverty,<BR>destitution; अनिर्वृतिनिशाचरी मम<BR>गृहांतरालं गता Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्वेश
अनिर्वेश a. Destitute of<BR>employment, wretched, miserable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलः|अनिल
अनिलः [अनिति जीवति अनेन, अन्<BR>इलच् Uṇ. 1. 54]<BR>1 Wind;<BR>प्राणानामनिलेन वृत्तिरुचिता Ś. 7. 12; स सखा दीप<BR>इवानिलाहतः Ku. 4. 30. (The number<BR>of winds is 7: --आवहो निवहश्चैव उद्वहः<BR>संवहस्तथा । विवहः प्रवहश्चैव परिवाहस्तथैव च ॥<BR>and these are again subdivided<BR>into 7 divisions, the total number<BR>being 49).<BR>--2 The god of wind.<BR>--3<BR>One of the subordinate deities, 49<BR>of whom form the class of winds.<BR>--4 N. of one of the 8 Vasus, i. e.<BR>the fifth.<BR>--5 The wind in the body,<BR>one of the humours; ˚हन्, ˚हृत्, ˚घ्न.<BR>--6<BR>Rheumatism or any disease referred<BR>to disorder of the wind.<BR>--7 The letter<BR>य्.<BR>--8 Symbolical expression for the<BR>number 49.<BR>--9 N. of the lunar<BR>asterism स्वाति.<BR>--10 N. of Viṣṇu (तस्य<BR>प्राणात्मना सर्वदेहधारणात् तथात्वं).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अयनं way or course of the wind.<BR>--अशन, --आशिन् a. [अनिलमश्रातीति] {1}<BR>feeding on the wind, fasting. {2} a<BR>serpent.<BR>--अंतकः (wind-destroying)<BR>N. of a plant (Iṅgudī) or अंगारपुष्प.<BR>--आत्मजः son of the wind, epithet<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">Page0065-c+ 56</a>]<BR>of Bhīma and Hanūmat.<BR>--आमयः [<BR>अनिलकृतः आमयः शाक. त.] {1} flatulence. {2}<BR>rheumatism (वातरोग).<BR>--घ्न, --हन्, --हृत् a.<BR>curing disorders from wind.<BR>--घ्नकः<BR>a large tree (बिभीतक) Terminalia<BR>Belerica.<BR>--पर्यायः pain and swelling<BR>of the eyelids and outer parts of<BR>the eye.<BR>--प्रकृति a. of a windy<BR>nature. (-तिः) N. of the planet Saturn.<BR>--व्याधिः derangement of the bodily<BR>(internal) wind.<BR>--सखः fire (the<BR>friend of wind); so ˚बंधुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिलोडित
अनिलोडित a. Inexperienced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिर्लोडित
अनिर्लोडित a. Not well<BR>considered; ˚कार्यस्य वाग्जालं वाग्मिनो वृथा<BR>Śi. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिवर्तन|अनिवर्त्तन
अनिवर्तन a.<BR>1 Not turning away,<BR>firm, steadfast.<BR>--2 Right, not fit to<BR>be abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिवर्तिन्|अनिवर्त्तिन्
अनिवर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Brave, not<BR>retreating; also an epithet of Viṣṇu and<BR>the Almighty God.<BR>--2 Not returning;<BR>यौवनमनिवर्ति यातं तु K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिविशमान
अनिविशमान a. Not sitting<BR>down or retiring to rest, ever going,<BR>restless; पुनाना यंत्यनिविशमानाः<BR>Rv. 7. 49. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिवेशन
अनिवेशन a. Ved. Having no<BR>place of rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिश|अनिशं
अनिश a. Ved.<BR>1 Nightless, i. e.<BR>uninterrupted, incessant (निशा<BR>तद्धेतुकत्वेनोपचारात् चेष्टविनाशः सा नास्ति यस्य).<BR>--2 Ever afraid.<BR>--शं ind. Incessantly,<BR>ceaselessly; अनिशमपि मकरकेतुर्मनसो<BR>रुजमावहन्नभिमतो मे Ś. 3. 4; Bv. 2. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिशित
अनिशित a. Ved. Not resting or<BR>reposing, incessant; ˚सर्ग incessantly<BR>flowing; Rv. 10. 89. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिषिद्ध
अनिषिद्ध, अनिषेध्र Ved. a.<BR>Unforbidden, unchecked, unopposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिषेध्र
अनिषिद्ध, अनिषेध्र Ved. a.<BR>Unforbidden, unchecked, unopposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्कृत
अनिष्कृत a. Unfinished, not<BR>settled.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--एनस्, --पाप having<BR>the guilt not settled, i. e. unexpiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्ट|अनिष्टः
अनिष्ट a.<BR>1 Unwished,<BR>undesirable; unfavourable, disagreeable, ill<BR>(with gen.); ध्यायत्यनिष्टं<BR>यत्किंचित्पाणिग्राहस्य चेतसा Ms. 9. 21 whatever ill<BR>she thinks of her husband.<BR>--2 Evil,<BR>forbidden.<BR>--3 Bad, unlucky, ominous.<BR>--4 Not honoured with a sacrifice.<BR>--ष्टं An evil, mishap, misfortune,<BR>calamity, disadvantage, a crime,<BR>offence, wrong, unwelcome thing;<BR>˚एकबुद्धि Māl. 8. 12; भवत्यनिष्टादपि नाम<BR>दुःसहान्मनस्विनीनां प्रतिपत्तिरीदृशी Ku. 5. 42;<BR>ill-omen; प्रातरेव ˚दर्शनं जातं H. 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">Page0066-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुबंधिन् a. followed by<BR>or attended with calamities;<BR>विषयोपभोगेषु ˚धिषु यः सुखबुद्धिमारोपयति<BR>K. 155.<BR>--आपत्तिः f.,<BR>--आपादनं getting<BR>what is not desired, an undesired<BR>occurrence.<BR>--आशंसिन् a. (˚सूचक)<BR>indicating or boding ill.<BR>--ग्रहः an evil or<BR>malignant planet.<BR>--दुष्टधी a. having<BR>an evil and corrupt mind.<BR>--प्रसंगः {1}<BR>an undesired occurrence. {2}<BR>connection with a wrong object, argument<BR>or rule.<BR>--फलं an evil result.<BR>--शंका<BR>fear of evil.<BR>--हेतुः an evil omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टिन्
अनिष्टिन् a. One who has not<BR>sacrificed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्टृत
अनिष्टृत a. Ved. Unhurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्पत्तिः|अनिष्पत्ति
अनिष्पत्तिः f.<BR>Non-accomplishment, non-completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिष्पत्रं|अनिष्पत्र
अनिष्पत्रं ind. [निःसृतं पत्रं पक्षो यत्र<BR>तादृशं न भवति] So that the arrow (the<BR>feathery portion of it) does not<BR>come out on the other side; i. e. not<BR>with great force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनिस्तीर्ण
अनिस्तीर्ण a.<BR>1 Not crossed, set<BR>aside or got rid of.<BR>--2 Unanswered,<BR>unrefuted (as a charge).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभियोगः a defendant who has<BR>not cleared himself of a charge (by<BR>refuting it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकः|अनीक|अनीकं
अनीकः --कं [अनिति जीवत्यनेन;<BR>अन्-ईकन् Uṇ. 4. 16-17]<BR>1 Army, forces;<BR>troop, host; दृष्ट्वा तु पांडवानीकं<BR>Bg. 1. 2; पदातींश्च महीपालः पुरोऽनीकस्य<BR>योजयेत् H. 3. 80.<BR>--2 A collection, group,<BR>mass; नवांबुदानीकमुहूर्तलांछने R. 3. 53.<BR>--3 Battle, fight, combat.<BR>--4 A<BR>row, line, marching column.<BR>--5<BR>Front, head; chief; रथेषु नोऽ<BR>नीकेष्वधिश्रियः Rv. 8. 20. 12. (सेनामुखेषु);<BR>अग्निर्वै देवानामनीकं Śat. Br.;<BR>अग्निमनीकं कृत्वा.<BR>--6 Face, countenance, ibid.<BR>(मुखं) (तस्य प्राणवायुनिस्सारणात् तथात्वं);<BR>splendour; brilliance; form (तेजस्);<BR>स्वनीक Rv. 7. 2. 23, 3. 6<BR>(mostly Ved. in these two senses).<BR>--7 Edge, point.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थः {1} a<BR>warrior, combatant. {2} a sentinel,<BR>(armed) watch. {3} an<BR>elephant-driver, or its trainer. {4} a war-drum<BR>or trumpet. {5} a signal, mark, sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकं|अनीक|अनीकः
अनीकः --कं [अनिति जीवत्यनेन;<BR>अन्-ईकन् Uṇ. 4. 16-17]<BR>1 Army, forces;<BR>troop, host; दृष्ट्वा तु पांडवानीकं<BR>Bg. 1. 2; पदातींश्च महीपालः पुरोऽनीकस्य<BR>योजयेत् H. 3. 80.<BR>--2 A collection, group,<BR>mass; नवांबुदानीकमुहूर्तलांछने R. 3. 53.<BR>--3 Battle, fight, combat.<BR>--4 A<BR>row, line, marching column.<BR>--5<BR>Front, head; chief; रथेषु नोऽ<BR>नीकेष्वधिश्रियः Rv. 8. 20. 12. (सेनामुखेषु);<BR>अग्निर्वै देवानामनीकं Śat. Br.;<BR>अग्निमनीकं कृत्वा.<BR>--6 Face, countenance, ibid.<BR>(मुखं) (तस्य प्राणवायुनिस्सारणात् तथात्वं);<BR>splendour; brilliance; form (तेजस्);<BR>स्वनीक Rv. 7. 2. 23, 3. 6<BR>(mostly Ved. in these two senses).<BR>--7 Edge, point.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थः {1} a<BR>warrior, combatant. {2} a sentinel,<BR>(armed) watch. {3} an<BR>elephant-driver, or its trainer. {4} a war-drum<BR>or trumpet. {5} a signal, mark, sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकवत्|अनीकवन्त्
अनीकवत् a. Ved. forming the face<BR>or front rank; occupying the<BR>foremost rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकशः
अनीकशः adv. In rows or columns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीकिनी
अनीकिनी [अनीकानां संघः; अनीकं युद्धं<BR>प्रयोजनतया अस्त्यस्याः इति वा, अनीक-इनि]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-b" target="_blank">Page0066-b+ 56</a>]<BR>1 An army, host, forces.<BR>--2 Three<BR>chamūs or one-tenth of a complete<BR>army (अक्षौहिणी); 10935 foot, 6561<BR>horse, 2187 elephants and as many<BR>chariots.<BR>--3 A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीच
अनीच a.<BR>1 Not low or vile,<BR>decent, respectable.<BR>--2 Not pronounced<BR>with the अनुदात्त accent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुवर्तिन् a. not associating with low<BR>or vile persons. --(m.) a faithful<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीड
अनीड a. Having no abode (body),<BR>incorporeal, epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीतिः|अनीति
अनीतिः f.<BR>1 Impropriety,<BR>immorality; injustice, wrong act;<BR>indiscretion, foolish conduct.<BR>--2 (न-ईतिः)<BR>Freedom from calamity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञ, --विद् a. impolite, not discreet,<BR>not conversant with policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनील
अनील a. Not blue, white &c.;<BR>˚वाजिन् m. ‘white-horsed’; N. of<BR>Arjuna; Ki. 14. 26, 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश|अनीशः
अनीश a.<BR>1 Having no lord or<BR>superior, paramount, supreme,<BR>without a controller, uncontrolled;<BR>सर्वप्रभुरनीशस्त्वं R. 10. 20.<BR>--2 Not a<BR>master or lord, having no mastery<BR>or control over, not master of (with<BR>gen.); powerless; गात्राणामनीशोऽस्मि<BR>संवृत्तः Ś. 2; अनीशया शरीरस्य हृदयं स्ववशं<BR>मयि न्यस्तं V. 2. 19; Ms. 9. 104.<BR>--3<BR>Not one's own master, not<BR>independent (अस्वतंत्र); एको ह्यनीशः सर्वत्र.<BR>--शः<BR>N. of Viṣṇu (सर्वनियंता<BR>अनन्यस्वामिको हि सः).<BR>--शा Helplessness (<BR>दीनभाव); समाने वृक्षे पुरुषो निमग्नोऽ<BR>नीशया शोचति मुह्यमानः Muṇḍ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीश्वर
अनीश्वर a.<BR>1 Having no superior,<BR>uncontrolled.<BR>--2 Unable; शयिता<BR>सविधेप्यनीश्वरा सफलीकर्तुमहो मनोरथान्<BR>Bv. 2. 182.<BR>--3 Not relating to God;<BR>ध्यानेनानीश्वरान् गुणान्-दहेत् Ms. 6. 72.<BR>--4<BR>Not acknowledging God, atheistical.<BR>--रं The godless one (with Sāṃkhyas),<BR>epithet of the world;<BR>जगदाहुरनीश्वरम्.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वादः atheism, not<BR>acknowledging God as the Supreme<BR>Ruler.<BR>--वादिन् m. one who<BR>maintains the doctrine of no god or<BR>atheism, an atheist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीह|अनीहः
अनीह a. Indifferent, listless.<BR>--हः<BR>N. of a king of Ayodhyā.<BR>--हा<BR>Disregard, apathy, indifference,<BR>disinclination; अनीहया Ki. 2. 10 carelessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनीहित
अनीहित a. Undesired, disagreeable,<BR>unpleasant.<BR>--तं Displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनु|अनुः
अनु ind. (Either used with<BR>nouns to form adverbial compounds,<BR>or as a prefix to verbs and verbal<BR>derivatives, or as a separable<BR>preposition with acc. and regarded as a<BR>कर्मप्रवचनीय)<BR>1 After, behind, along after<BR>(पश्चात्); सर्वे नारदमनु उपविशंति V. 5;<BR>प्रमदामनु संस्थितः शुचा नृपतिः सन्<BR>R. 8. 72; तं गच्छंत्यनु ये विपत्तिषु सदा ते<BR>तत्प्रतिष्ठाशया Mu. 1. 14; असौ<BR>कुमारस्तमजोनुजातः R. 6. 78; रत्या च<BR>साशंकमनुप्रयातः Ku. 3. 23; क्रमेण सुप्तामनु<BR>संविवेश सुप्तोत्थितां प्रातरनूदतिष्ठत् R. 2. 24;<BR>अनुविष्णु = विष्णोः पश्चात् P. II. 4. 18 Sk.;<BR>तदनु कथेयर्माधवीयामवस्थां Māl. 9. 26<BR>afterwards.<BR>--2 Along, along-side, by<BR>the side of, lengthwise (यस्य च<BR>आयामः); जलानि सा तीरनिखातयूपा<BR>वहत्ययोध्यामनु राजधानीं R. 13. 61; सोऽ<BR>श्वमेधशतेनेष्ट्वा यमुनामनु वीर्यवान् । त्रिशताश्वान्<BR>सरस्वत्यां गंगामनु चतुःशतान् Mb.; अनुगंगं<BR>वाराणसी = गंगामन्वायतं (<BR>गंगादैर्घ्यसदृशदैर्घ्योपलक्षिता) situated alongside the<BR>Ganges P. II. 1. 16 Sk.;<BR>आविर्भूतप्रथममुकुलाः कंदलीश्चानुकच्छं Me. 21;<BR>गिरिरिव अनुतटपुष्पितकर्णिकारयष्टिः<BR>V. 3. 3 along the sides or slopes.<BR>--3 After,<BR>in consequence of, being indicated by;<BR>जपमनु प्रावर्षत् P. II. 3. 8 Sk. (<BR>हेतुभूतजपोपलक्षितं वर्षणं); so वृक्षमनु विद्योतते विद्युत्.<BR>--4 With, along with (सहार्थे);<BR>connected with; नदीमनु अवसिता सेमा<BR>P. I. 4. 85 Sk. (नद्यासह संबद्धा);<BR>उमास्तनोद्भेदमनु प्रवृद्धः Ku. 7. 24 along with,<BR>contemporaneously; Śi. 8. 56;<BR>दिवसोनुमित्रमगमद्विलयं 9. 17.<BR>--5 Inferior or<BR>subordinate to (हीने); मित्रलाभमनु<BR>लाभसंपदः Ki. 13. 52 inferior, lower in<BR>value or importance; अनु हरिं सुराः =<BR>हरेर्हीनाः P. I. 4. 86 Sk.<BR>--6 In a<BR>particular relation or state (इत्थंभूताख्याने<BR>प्रकारविशेषनिरूपणे); भक्तो विष्णुमनु Sk.<BR>(विष्णोरित्थंभूतः, भक्तिविशेषयुक्तः) an<BR>ardent devotee of Viṣṇu; यस्त्वां द्वेष्टि स<BR>मां द्वेष्टि यस्त्वामनु स मामनु Rām.<BR>favourably inclined or devoted to.<BR>--7<BR>Having a part or share, participation; or<BR>one that claims a share of (भागे);<BR>भागोऽस्यास्ति इति भागस्वामी; लक्ष्मीर्हरिमनु<BR>(हरेर्भागः) Sk., हरिस्वामिकभागवतीत्यर्थः.<BR>--8 Repetition, in a distributive<BR>sense, mostly in comp. (वीप्सार्थे,<BR>विषयतायां); अनुदिवसं day by day, every<BR>day; अनुक्षणं every moment;<BR>˚वेलं every time, frequently; वृक्षं<BR>वृक्षमनु सिंचति Sk. waters tree after<BR>tree, i. e. every tree (यावद्वृक्षव्यापकः<BR>सेकः).<BR>--9 Towards, in the direction of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-a" target="_blank">Page0067-a+ 56</a>]<BR>near, to, at (अनुर्यत्समया P. II. 1. 15);<BR>अनुवनमशनिर्गतः Sk.; ˚नदि Śi. 7. 24<BR>near the river; प्रजिघाय कांतमनु मुग्धतरः<BR>9. 55 to (प्रति); on or in, with the<BR>force of the locative; यदेतदस्यानुतटं<BR>विभाति 4. 39, 7. 1; तस्माद्गच्छेरनुकनखलं<BR>शैलराजावतीर्णां (जह्नोः कन्यां) Me. 50.<BR>--10 In orderly succession, according<BR>to; अनुक्रमं in regular order;<BR>अनुज्येष्ठं = ज्येष्ठस्यानुपूर्व्येण in order of<BR>seniority; ˚पूर्वं; अनुरूपं = रूपस्य योग्यं Sk.<BR>--11<BR>Corresponding with, like, in<BR>imitation of; सर्वं मामनु ते प्रियाविरहजां त्व<BR>तु व्यथां मानुभूः V. 4. 25; so अनुगर्ज्<BR>to roar after or in imitation of.<BR>--12<BR>Following, conformable to (अनुगत);<BR>तथैव सोऽभूदन्वर्थो राजा प्रकृतिरंजनात्<BR>R. 4. 12 (अनुगतोऽर्थो यस्य).<BR>--13 With<BR>regard to, towards, in respect of;<BR>अर्ध्यदानमनु चोदितो वचः Śi. 14. 53;<BR>साधुर्देवदत्तो मातरमनु.<BR>--14 On account of, by<BR>reason of (with abl.); समस्तो बत<BR>लोकोऽयं भजते कारणादनु । त्वं तु<BR>निष्कारणादेव प्रीयसे वरवर्णिनि ॥ Rām. As a<BR>separable adverb अनु is used only in<BR>the Vedas and means after,<BR>afterwards, later on, now, at this time,<BR>again, once more, then, and further.<BR>(The senses of अनु as given by G. M.<BR>are:<BR>--अनु<BR>वेदाध्ययनानुष्ठानसामीप्यपश्चाद्भावानुबंधसाम्याभिमुखहीनविसर्गलक्षणेषु; e. g. वेदे<BR>अनुवाकः; अनुष्ठाने अनुतिष्ठति; सामीप्ये<BR>अनुमेघं वर्षति; पश्चाद्भावे तदनु; अनुबंधने अनुशेते;<BR>साम्ये अनुकरोति; आभिमुख्ये मातरमनुधावति<BR>वत्सः; हीने अनुहरिं सुराः; विसर्गे अनुजानीते;<BR>लक्षणे अनुवनमशनिर्गतः). The senses of<BR>अनु may be thus expressed in verse:<BR>--आयामेऽपरभावे च (पश्चादर्थे) वीप्सायां सन्निधौ<BR>तथा । इत्थंभूते लक्षणे च भागसादृश्ययोरपि ॥<BR>योग्यतायां तथा हीने तृतीयार्थे ह्यनुक्रमे ।<BR>अर्थेष्वेतेषु बहुशो ह्यनुशब्दः प्रयुज्यते ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुः|अनु
अनुः Ved.<BR>1 A man.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>son of Yayāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक|अनुकः
अनुक a. [अनु-कन् P. V. 2. 74,<BR>अनुकामयते इति अनुकः कमिता Sk.]<BR>1<BR>Greedy; desirous.<BR>--2 Libidinous,<BR>lustful (as a lover).<BR>--3 Sloping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकथ्
अनुकथ् {c10c} P. To relate after<BR>(some one else), mention<BR>subsequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकथनं|अनुकथन
अनुकथनं<BR>1 Subsequent mention;<BR>आदेशः कथनं, अन्वादेशोऽनुकथनं Kāśi. on<BR>P. II. 4. 32.<BR>--2 Relation, narration;<BR>discourse, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकनीयस्
अनुकनीयस् a. The next<BR>youngest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकंप्|अनुकम्प्
अनुकंप् {c1c} A. To take pity or<BR>compassion on, sympathize with, pity<BR>(with acc.); किमुज्जिहानजीवितां<BR>वराकीं नानुकंपसे Māl. 10; कथं ब्राह्मणी<BR>मामनुकंपते Mk. 3; कंपसे नानुकंपसे 4. 8;<BR>with loc. also; सौहृदेन तथा प्रेम्णा सदा<BR>मय्यनुकंपसे Mb. --Caus. To pity &c.;<BR>शफरीं प्रथमा वृष्टिरिवान्वकंपयत् Ku. 4. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकंपक|अनुकम्पक
अनुकंपक a. Pitying, taking<BR>compassion on, sympathizing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकंपन|अनुकम्पन
अनुकंपन a. One who pities,<BR>kindhearted, compassionate.<BR>--नं<BR>Compassion, pity, tenderness, sympathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकंपा|अनुकम्पा
अनुकंपा [कंप्-अङ्] Compassion,<BR>commiseration, pity; with gen.;<BR>तेषामेवानुकंपार्थं Bg. 10. 11; or with loc.;<BR>भक्त्या गुरौ मय्यनुकंपया च R. 2. 63;<BR>or in comp.; भूतानुकंपा तव चेत्<BR>R. 2. 48; अनुकंपायां कन् P. V. 3. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकंपित|अनुकम्पित
अनुकंपित p. p. Pitied; ˚आत्मन्<BR>having a compassionate spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकंपिन्|अनुकम्पिन्
अनुकंपिन् a. Pitying(in comp.);<BR>sympathizing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकंप्य|अनुकम्प्य|अनुकम्प्यः
अनुकंप्य pot. p. Pitiable, worthy<BR>of sympathy; किं तन्न येनासि<BR>ममानुकप्या R. 14. 74;<BR>दुहितरमनुकंप्यामद्रिरादाय दोर्भ्यां Ku. 3. 76.<BR>--प्यः<BR>1 A<BR>courier, express messenger.<BR>--2 An<BR>ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकांक्षा|अनुकाङ्क्षा
अनुकांक्षा Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकाम|अनुकामं|अनुकामः
अनुकाम a. [कामस्य सदृशः अनुरूपो<BR>वा]<BR>1 Agreeable to desire, according<BR>to one's desire.<BR>--2 [अनुकामयते<BR>कम्-अच्] Desirous, lustful.<BR>--मं ind.<BR>At will, according to desire or wish,<BR>as desired, at pleasure.<BR>--मः [<BR>अनुरूपः कामः] Proper or worthy desire;<BR>desire; ˚कृत् fulfilling one's desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकामीन|अनुकामीनः
अनुकामीन a. [कामस्य सदृशं अनुकामं;<BR>ख प्रत्ययः; अनुकामं गामी यथेष्टं गंता इत्यर्थः<BR>P. V. 2. 11 Sk.] Going at will<BR>or pleasure; one who acts as he<BR>pleases; अनुकामीनतां त्यज Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकाल
अनुकाल a. [कालस्य योग्यः]<BR>Opportune, timely, adapted or suited<BR>to the time.<BR>--लं ind. Opportunely,<BR>on a proper occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकीर्तनं|अनुकीर्तन|अनुकीर्त्तन
अनुकीर्तनं Act of proclaiming or<BR>publishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूल|अनुकूलः
अनुकूल a. [अनुगतः कूलं तटं<BR>स्नेहादिबंधनं वा]<BR>1 Favourable, agreeable<BR>(lit. following the bank or slope,<BR>according to the current, with the<BR>grain;), as wind, fate &c.; मंदं मंदं<BR>नुदति पवनश्चानुकूलो यथा त्वां Me. 9;<BR>शांत˚पवनश्च Ś. 4. 10; ˚परिणामा संवृत्ता<BR>Ś. 7; V. 3. 20.<BR>--2 Friendly, kind,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">Page0067-c+ 58</a>]<BR>well or kindly disposed.<BR>--3<BR>Conformable to; pleasing, agreeable or<BR>favourable to, conducing to, capable<BR>of; oft. in comp.; स्पर्शानुकूला इव<BR>सूर्यकांताः Ś. 2. 7; अननुकूलोऽभिमानस्य<BR>K. 45 not inclined to pride;<BR>दर्शनानुकूलाहमस्य न वेति 197;<BR>कुशलविरचितानुकूलवेशः R. 5. 76 befitting, suitable.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A faithful or kind husband,<BR>(एकरतिः S. D. or एकनिरतः एकस्यामेव<BR>नायिकायां आसक्तः), a variety of नायक.<BR>--2 ‘Favourable to all,’ epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--ला<BR>1 N. of a tree (दंती)<BR>Croton Polyandrum.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>metre.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Favour, kindness;<BR>नारीणामनुकूलमाचरति चेत् K. P. 9.<BR>--2<BR>(Rhet.) A figure in which<BR>unfavourableness turns into kindness; अनुकूलं<BR>प्रातिकूल्यमानुकूल्यानुबंधि चेत् S. D.; कुपितासि<BR>यदा तन्वि निधाय करजक्षतम् । बधान<BR>भुजपाशाभ्यां कंठमस्य दृढं तदा ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलता
अनुकूलता --त्वं<BR>1 Favour, conformity,<BR>kindness, good will;<BR>पवनस्यानुकूलत्वात् R. 1. 42 the wind being<BR>favourable.<BR>--2 Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलत्वं|अनुकूलत्व
अनुकूलता --त्वं<BR>1 Favour, conformity,<BR>kindness, good will;<BR>पवनस्यानुकूलत्वात् R. 1. 42 the wind being<BR>favourable.<BR>--2 Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकूलयति
अनुकूलयति Den. P. To conciliate,<BR>propitiate, act in a friendly way<BR>towards; (तं) अनुकूलयतींद्रोऽपि<BR>कल्पद्रुमविभूषणैः Ku. 2. 39; Ki. 13. 71;<BR>Śi. 7. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृ
अनुकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To do after or<BR>afterwards; follow; especially to<BR>imitate, do after or in imitation of,<BR>resemble, equal, copy (with gen.);<BR>ततोऽनुकुर्याद्विशदस्य तस्याः… स्मितस्य<BR>Ku. 1. 44; श्यामतया हरेरिवानुकुर्वतीं<BR>K. 10; अनुकरोति भगवतो नारायणस्य 6, 282;<BR>ननु कलभेन यूथपतेरनुकृतम् M. 5; (also<BR>with acc.); सर्वाभिरन्याभिः<BR>कलाभिरनुचकार तं वैशंपायनः K. 76;<BR>शैलाधिपस्यानुचकार लक्ष्मीं Bk. 2. 8; बहुतरं<BR>भवंतमनुकरोति V. 5; Ms. 2. 199.<BR>--2 To<BR>requite, recompense.<BR>--3 To try on,<BR>adjust, adapt; बंधं ततोऽनुकुर्वीत Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर|अनुकरः
अनुकर a. Imitating.<BR>--रः An<BR>assistant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकरणं|अनुकरण
अनुकरणं, --कृतिः f.<BR>1 Imitation;<BR>त्वदीयसुचरितैकदेशस्यानुकरणं किलैतत्<BR>Mu. 7.<BR>--2 Copy, resemblance, similarity;<BR>शब्दानुकरणं onamatopœia;<BR>अव्यक्तानुकरणस्यात इतौ P. VI. 1. 98;<BR>V. 4. 57; I. 4. 62; धूमोद्गारानुकृतिनिपुणाः<BR>Me. 69.<BR>--3 Compliance;<BR>ओमित्येतदनुकृतिहस्म वै T. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृतिः|अनुकृति
अनुकरणं, --कृतिः f.<BR>1 Imitation;<BR>त्वदीयसुचरितैकदेशस्यानुकरणं किलैतत्<BR>Mu. 7.<BR>--2 Copy, resemblance, similarity;<BR>शब्दानुकरणं onamatopœia;<BR>अव्यक्तानुकरणस्यात इतौ P. VI. 1. 98;<BR>V. 4. 57; I. 4. 62; धूमोद्गारानुकृतिनिपुणाः<BR>Me. 69.<BR>--3 Compliance;<BR>ओमित्येतदनुकृतिहस्म वै T. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्तृ
अनुकर्तृ m.<BR>1 An imitator.<BR>--2<BR>Actor, performer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्मन्|अनुकर्म्मन्
अनुकर्मन् n.<BR>1 Imitation.<BR>--2 [<BR>पश्चात्कृतं कर्म] A subsequent rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकारः|अनुकार
अनुकारः [कृ-घञ्] Imitation,<BR>resemblance; सुलभानुकारः खलु जगति<BR>वेधसो निर्माणसंनिवेशः Māl. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकारिन्
अनुकारिन् a. Imitating,<BR>resembling (with gen. or in comp.);<BR>प्रियायाः किंचिदनुकारिणीषु लतासु दृष्टिं<BR>विलोभयामि Ś. 6; अनुकारिणि पूर्वेषां<BR>युक्तरूपमिदं त्वयि Ś. 2. 16; 1. 21;<BR>R. 1. 43, 3. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकार्य|अनुकार्य्य
अनुकार्य, --करणीय, --कर्तव्य pot. p.<BR>Fit to be imitated.<BR>--र्यं, --अनुक्रिया A<BR>subsequent rite or ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकरणीय
अनुकार्य, --करणीय, --कर्तव्य pot. p.<BR>Fit to be imitated.<BR>--र्यं, --अनुक्रिया A<BR>subsequent rite or ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्तव्य
अनुकार्य, --करणीय, --कर्तव्य pot. p.<BR>Fit to be imitated.<BR>--र्यं, --अनुक्रिया A<BR>subsequent rite or ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रीः
अनुक्रीः [अनु --कृ उणा˚ बा. ई. किच्च<BR>Tv.] A kind of sacrifical rite<BR>called साद्यस्क्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृपायते
अनुकृपायते Den. A. To<BR>sympathize or condole with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकृष्
अनुकृष् {c1c} P. To drag after<BR>oneself, to attract (in gram.); see<BR>अनुकर्ष below. --Caus. To subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षः|अनुकर्ष
अनुकर्षः --र्षणं<BR>1 Dragging after,<BR>drawing along; attraction in<BR>general.<BR>--2 Summoning or invoking (by<BR>means of spells).<BR>--3 Grammatical<BR>attraction, application or attraction of<BR>a word in a preceding rule to a<BR>subsequent rule, word &c.;<BR>नायमनुकर्षणार्थश्चकारः Mbh. on P. II. 2. 4; see also<BR>Sk. on P. VI. 1. 127.<BR>--4 [अनुकृष्यते<BR>स्वसंबद्धेन चक्रेण] The axle-tree or<BR>bottom of a carriage.<BR>--5 Delayed<BR>performance of a duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षणं|अनुकर्षण
अनुकर्षः --र्षणं<BR>1 Dragging after,<BR>drawing along; attraction in<BR>general.<BR>--2 Summoning or invoking (by<BR>means of spells).<BR>--3 Grammatical<BR>attraction, application or attraction of<BR>a word in a preceding rule to a<BR>subsequent rule, word &c.;<BR>नायमनुकर्षणार्थश्चकारः Mbh. on P. II. 2. 4; see also<BR>Sk. on P. VI. 1. 127.<BR>--4 [अनुकृष्यते<BR>स्वसंबद्धेन चक्रेण] The axle-tree or<BR>bottom of a carriage.<BR>--5 Delayed<BR>performance of a duty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकर्षन्
अनुकर्षन् m. The bottom of a<BR>carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकॢप्
अनुकॢप् {c1c} A. To follow duly.<BR>--Caus. To cause others to follow<BR>duly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुकल्पः|अनुकल्प
अनुकल्पः [अनुगतः मुख्यं कल्पं]<BR>1 A<BR>secondary direction or precept, a<BR>substitute or alternative to be used<BR>in times of necessity when the<BR>primary one (प्रथमकल्प) is not possible;<BR>as the direction to use गोधूम or तंडुल<BR>in the absence of यव; प्रभुः<BR>प्रथमकल्पस्य योऽनुकल्पेन वर्तते Ms. 11. 30, 3. 147.<BR>--2 A work connected with kalpa<BR>(one of the six auxiliaries of the<BR>Vedas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्त
अनुक्त a.<BR>1 Unuttered, unsaid<BR>(in gram.) = अनभिहित q. v. under<BR>अभिधा.<BR>--2 Unheard of, extraordinary.<BR>--3 Not told; असावनुक्तोऽपि सहाय<BR>एव Ku. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्थ
अनुक्थ a. Without hymns or<BR>songs of praise; Rv. 5. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रकच
अनुक्रकच a. [अनुगतः क्रकचं]<BR>Serrated, dentated like a saw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रंद्|अनुक्रन्द्
अनुक्रंद् {c1c} P. To cry after,<BR>reply to the sound;<BR>वीरुन्नीडकपोतकूजितमनुक्रंदंत्यमी कुक्कुटाः Māl. 9. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रंदनं|अनुक्रन्दन
अनुक्रंदनं A cry in reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रम्
अनुक्रम् {c1c} U., {c4c} P.<BR>1 To go after,<BR>follow (fig. also); महर्षिभिरनुक्रांतं<BR>धर्मपंथानमास्थितः Rām.; to betake oneself<BR>to; तीर्थयात्रामनुक्रामन् Mb.;<BR>व्यवसायमनुक्रांता कांते त्वमतिशोभनं Rām.<BR>--2 To<BR>count up, enumerate, state or go<BR>through in order; यच्चानुक्रांतं<BR>यच्चानुक्रंस्यते Mbh. on P. I. 1. 72; give a<BR>table of contents, used frequently<BR>in the Nirukta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रम|अनुक्रमः
अनुक्रम a. [अनुगतः क्रमं] In due<BR>order.<BR>--मः<BR>1 Succession, order,<BR>sequence, arrangement, method,<BR>due order; प्रचक्रमे वक्तुमनुक्रमज्ञा<BR>R. 6. 70; श्वश्रूजनं सर्वमनुक्रमेण 14. 60;<BR>Y. 2. 41.<BR>--2 A table of contents,<BR>index, such as that of the Vedic<BR>Saṃhitās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रमणं|अनुक्रमण
अनुक्रमणं<BR>1 Proceeding in order.<BR>--2 Following.<BR>--णी, --णिका [स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>A table of contents, an index<BR>showing the successive contents of<BR>a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रुश्
अनुक्रुश् {c1c} P. To shout at or<BR>after. --Caus. To join in<BR>lamenting, condole with, show sympathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्रोशः|अनुक्रोश
अनुक्रोशः<BR>1 Pity, compassion,<BR>tenderness (with loc.); भगवन्कामदेव<BR>न ते मय्यनुक्रोशः Ś. 3; Me. 115; किमपि<BR>सानुक्रोशः कृतः made to relent<BR>Ś. 4; न ते मां प्रति अनुक्रोशः Ś. 3.<BR>--2 One<BR>who has gone over a krośa (2 miles)<BR>(अनुगतः क्रोशं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षणं|अनुक्षण
अनुक्षणं ind. Every instant,<BR>constantly, frequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षत्तृ
अनुक्षत्तृ m. (त्ता) The attendant<BR>of a doorkeeper or charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुक्षेत्रं|अनुक्षेत्र
अनुक्षेत्रं Stipend given to certain<BR>temple-worshippers in Orissa (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुख्या
अनुख्या {c2c} P. Ved. To descry,<BR>see from a distance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुख्यातिः|अनुख्याति
अनुख्यातिः f.<BR>1 Descrying.<BR>--2<BR>Reporting, revealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुख्यातृ
अनुख्यातृ m. (ता) A discoverer;<BR>reporter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगम्
अनुगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go after, follow,<BR>attend, accompany; अनभिज्ञो गुणानां<BR>यो न भृत्यैरनुगम्यते Pt. 1. 73;<BR>ओदकांतात्स्निग्धो जनोऽनुगंतव्यः Ś. 4;<BR>केकारवैरनुगम्यमानो भूषणनिनादः K. 84;<BR>मार्गं मनुष्येश्वरधर्मपत्नी श्रुतेरिवार्थं<BR>स्मृतिरन्वगच्छत् R. 2. 2; छायेव तां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-c" target="_blank">Page0068-c+ 57</a>]<BR>भूपतिरन्वगच्छत् 6; Ms. 12. 115; Ki. 5. 2.<BR>--2<BR>To follow, practise, observe, obey,<BR>act up to; प्रतिशब्दक इव<BR>राजवचनमनुगच्छति जनो भयात् K. 104;<BR>पूर्वैरयमभिप्रेतो गतो मार्गोऽनुगम्यते Rām.; विषत्तौ च<BR>महाँल्लोके धीरतामनुगच्छति H. 3. 44.<BR>--3<BR>To seek, wander through; काननं वापि<BR>शैलं वा यं रामोऽनुगमिष्यति Rām.; कृत्स्नां<BR>पृथ्वीमनुगच्छत ibid. go in quest of.<BR>--4<BR>To come, arrive, approach, present<BR>oneself (as time); काले त्वनुगते Bhāg.<BR>--5 To answer or respond to;<BR>correspond with, be suitable to; imitate,<BR>resemble; धनुःश्रियं गोत्रभिदोऽनुगच्छति<BR>Ki. 4. 36; आस्फालितं<BR>यत्प्रमदाकराग्रैर्मृदंगधीरध्वनिमन्वगच्छत् R. 16. 13; न<BR>चापि कादंबरीं लक्ष्मीरनुगंतुमलं K. 203.<BR>--6 To go or die out, be extinguished;<BR>यद्येष उख्योऽग्निरनुगच्छेत् Śat. Br.<BR>--7<BR>To enter into. --Caus. [--गमयति] To<BR>cause to follow, follow;<BR>उद्ग्रीवैरनुगमितस्य पुष्करस्य M. 1. 21 followed or<BR>accompanied in sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग|अनुगः
अनुग a. [अनुगच्छतीति, गम्-ड] (In<BR>comp.) Following, going after;<BR>corresponding or tallying with,<BR>adequate to; सदा पृष्ठानुगः पुरे Pt. 1. 59;<BR>गीतानुगं वारि मृदंगवाद्यं R. 16. 64;<BR>Me. 47; कामक्रोधवशानुगं Ms. 2. 214;<BR>गोत्ररिक्थानुगः पिंडः 9. 142 governed or<BR>regulated by; 8. 239.<BR>--गः A<BR>follower, (obedient) servant, companion;<BR>तद्भूतनाथानुग R. 2. 58, 9. 82; बल˚<BR>followed by an army, being the<BR>head of an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगत|अनुगतः
अनुगत p. p.<BR>1 (Used passively)<BR>(a) Followed (lit. & fig.),<BR>attended; अनुगतमलिवृंदैर्गंडभित्तीर्विहाय<BR>R. 12. 102; M. 3. 9; Ms. 11. 71. (b) Full<BR>of, filled with; दारिद्र्येणाभिभूतेन<BR>त्वत्स्नेहानुगतेन च Mk. 4. 5;<BR>वर्षधरकलमूकानुगतेन परिजनेन K. 159 consisting or<BR>made up of; चिंतानुगतसर्वात्मन् Mb.<BR>(c) Covered, as by a dress hanging<BR>behind; शिवमिवानुगतं गजचर्मणा<BR>Ki. 5. 2 (पश्चाद्व्याप्तं). (d) Extinguished<BR>&c. (e) Acquired, obtained.<BR>--2 (Used<BR>actively) (a) Following, obeying,<BR>observing; स्वमतमनुगतः Mu. 5. 19;<BR>विभवानुगता भार्या Mk. 3. 28;<BR>दिग्विजयप्रसंगेनानुगतो भूमिमिमां K. 191 come to;<BR>Ms. 9. 267; K. 166; Mu. 6. 5; H. 2. 56;<BR>R. 15. 9. (b) Corresponding or<BR>tallying with, adapted or answering<BR>to, in harmony with; सूत्रेणानुगतं भवति<BR>Ś. B.; पादन्यासो लयमनुगतः M. 2. 9 in<BR>accompaniment to the musical time;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">Page0069-a+ 56</a>]<BR>मृदंग ˚तः संगीतमधुरः Ratn. 1; ˚वीणैः<BR>Śi. 11. 10. (c) Adequate or suitable to,<BR>fit for; प्रस्तावानुगतं पृष्टः Pt. 5. (d)<BR>Imitating; परितुष्टोऽस्मि यत्पितरमनुगतो<BR>वत्सः M. 5 I am glad that the boy<BR>takes after his father.<BR>--तं Moderate<BR>time in music.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a.<BR>having a corresponding or easily<BR>discoverable sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगतिः|अनुगति
अनुगतिः f.<BR>1 Following; बलस्य<BR>चतुरंगस्य नायकानुगतिर्नयः Rām.;<BR>गतानुगतिक्रो लोकः following, imitating; see<BR>under गत.<BR>--2 Consent, approval;<BR>अकाम˚ forced consent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगमः|अनुगम
अनुगमः --मनं<BR>1 Following;<BR>आत्मानुगमनेन गां प्रसादयितुमर्हसि R. 1. 88;<BR>बृहतेर्धातोरर्थानुगमात् Ś. B.<BR>--2<BR>Comprehending, grasping (as a sense); रसाद्यनुगतः<BR>S. D.<BR>--3 Following in death,<BR>post-cremation, self-immolation of a widow<BR>on her husband's funeral pile.<BR>--4<BR>Imitating; approaching.<BR>--5<BR>Conformity, accordance; श्रुत्यनुगमाच्च Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगमनं|अनुगमन
अनुगमः --मनं<BR>1 Following;<BR>आत्मानुगमनेन गां प्रसादयितुमर्हसि R. 1. 88;<BR>बृहतेर्धातोरर्थानुगमात् Ś. B.<BR>--2<BR>Comprehending, grasping (as a sense); रसाद्यनुगतः<BR>S. D.<BR>--3 Following in death,<BR>post-cremation, self-immolation of a widow<BR>on her husband's funeral pile.<BR>--4<BR>Imitating; approaching.<BR>--5<BR>Conformity, accordance; श्रुत्यनुगमाच्च Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगामिन्
अनुगामिन् a. Following. --m. A<BR>follower = अनुग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगामुक
अनुगामुक a. Habitually or<BR>constantly following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगर्ज्
अनुगर्ज् {c1c} P. To roar after or in<BR>imitation of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगर्जित
अनुगर्जित p. p. Roared.<BR>--तं A<BR>roaring echo, Ku. 6. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगव
अनुगव a. [गोः सदृशः आयामः, अच्]<BR>Suiting (the length of) the oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगिरं
अनुगिरं ind. By the<BR>mountainside R. 13. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगवीनः|अनुगवीन
अनुगवीनः [अनुगु गोः पश्चात्पर्याप्तं<BR>यथा गच्छति सोऽनुगवीनः गोपालः; अनुगु ख<BR>P. V. 2. 15 Sk.] A cowherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगादिन्
अनुगादिन् a. [गद्-णिनि]<BR>Repeating, following in speaking, echoing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगीति|अनुगीतिः
अनुगीति See under अनुगै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुण|अनुगुणः
अनुगुण a. [अनुकूलो गुणो यस्य]<BR>Having similar qualities, of the<BR>same nature; कांतारतापसाविक्षू<BR>वंशकानुगुणौ स्मृतौ Suśr.; conformable to,<BR>favourable or agreeable to,<BR>suitable, according to; मनोरथस्यानुगुणं<BR>सर्वदा यस्य चेष्टितं Mv. 7. 7 obedient to<BR>the will; 7. 38; गुणसंपदानुगुणतां<BR>गमितः Ki. 6. 33; 10. 13; congenial,<BR>suitable, fit; ˚अन्नलाभात् Dk. 64, 94;<BR>अननुगुणदाराणां Dk. 130 not having<BR>wives worthy of themselves; (वीणा)<BR>उत्कंठितस्य हृदयानुगुणा वयस्या<BR>Mk. 3. 3 agreeable or pleasing to the heart,<BR>exactly after the heart (Tv. here takes<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">Page0069-b+ 57</a>]<BR>˚णा to mean तंत्रीयुक्तवीणा itself); अत्र<BR>द्वावप्युपध्मानीयावेव न शांतानुगुणौ R. G.;<BR>रसानुगुणतामेति S. D.; ˚णं<BR>सर्वास्ववस्थासु यत् U. 1. 39<BR>--णः A natural<BR>peculiarity.<BR>--णं adv.<BR>1 Favourably,<BR>conformably to one's desires;<BR>चिरेणानुगुणं प्रोक्ता प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुखी<BR>Bk. 8. 95.<BR>--2 Agreeably or conformably<BR>to (in comp.); तदादेशानुगुणं<BR>भवदागमनमभूत् Dk. 11.<BR>--3 Naturally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुणत्वं|अनुगुणत्व
अनुगुणत्वं Favourableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुणयति
अनुगुणयति Den. P. To make<BR>favourable, conciliate; bring about,<BR>secure; संपदोऽनुगुणयन् सुखैषिणां<BR>Ki. 13. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगुप्त
अनुगुप्त a. Covered, sheltered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगै
अनुगै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sing after (a<BR>person), sing to (a tune); follow in<BR>singing; अनुगायति काचिदुदंचितपंचमरागं<BR>Gīt. 1; अनुजगुरथ दिव्यं दुंदुभिध्वानमाशाः<BR>Ki. 3. 60 sent back, echoed.<BR>--2 To<BR>sing; to celebrate in song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगीतं|अनुगीत
अनुगीतं Singing in response to;<BR>Ratn. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुगीतिः|अनुगीति
अनुगीतिः f. N. of a metre of<BR>two lines, the first having 27 and<BR>the second 32, mātrās, a species of<BR>the Āryā metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रह्
अनुग्रह् {c9c} P. (Ved.<BR>--गृभ्णाति).<BR>1<BR>To favour, oblige, treat with<BR>kindness; शिलातलैकदेशमनुगृह्णानु वयस्यः<BR>Ś. 3 our friend will be so good as to,<BR>or kindly, take a seat on the stone;<BR>अयं विष्टरोऽनुगृह्यतां V. 5 be pleased<BR>to sit down &c.; महेंद्रेण पुनरनुगृहीता<BR>V. 3 favoured (by modifying the<BR>curse); with instr. or abl. of that<BR>which is an obligation;<BR>अनुगृहीतोऽहमनया मघवतः संभावनया Ś. 6;<BR>कतरत्कुलमनुगृहीतं भगवत्या जन्मना K. 135;<BR>अनुगृहीतोऽस्मि अहमुपदेशाद्भवतः V. 4 I<BR>am much obliged to you &c. (अनुगृहीत<BR>is oft. used by itself in the sense of<BR>‘much obliged’, ‘many thanks,’ ‘I<BR>thank you’, ‘I esteem it a favour’).<BR>--2 To foster, cherish, protect,<BR>maintain (as fire); अग्निर्नित्यानुगृहीतः<BR>स्यात् Āśval.<BR>--3 To receive, welcome.<BR>--4 To hold up, support, uphold.<BR>--5<BR>To follow in robbing, seizing or<BR>depriving.<BR>--6 To keep to, conform or<BR>correspond to, follow, take after;<BR>आकृतिमनुगृह्णंति गुणाः Vb. 2;<BR>क्षात्रधर्मश्चानुगृहीतो भवति U. 5. --Caus. To<BR>cause to favour, or to favour;<BR>आर्यस्य दर्शनेनात्मानमनुग्राहयितुं Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रहः|अनुग्रह
अनुग्रहः, --हणं<BR>1 A favour, kindness,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">Page0069-c+ 56</a>]<BR>obligation; showing favour, obliging,<BR>rewarding (opp. निग्रह);<BR>निग्रहानुग्रहकर्ता Pt. 1; पादार्पणानुग्रहपूतपृष्ठं<BR>R. 2. 35; अनुग्रह इवेयमभ्यर्थना Ś. 1;<BR>अनुग्रहं संस्मरणप्रवृत्तं Ku. 3. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Assistance, help (shown to the poor in<BR>feeding them &c. दरिद्रादिपोषणं).<BR>--3<BR>Facilitating by spells.<BR>--4 Acceptance.<BR>--5 Rear-guard.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कातर a.<BR>anxious to please or for favour.<BR>--सर्गः creation of feelings or mental<BR>conditions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रहणं|अनुग्रहण
अनुग्रहः, --हणं<BR>1 A favour, kindness,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">Page0069-c+ 56</a>]<BR>obligation; showing favour, obliging,<BR>rewarding (opp. निग्रह);<BR>निग्रहानुग्रहकर्ता Pt. 1; पादार्पणानुग्रहपूतपृष्ठं<BR>R. 2. 35; अनुग्रह इवेयमभ्यर्थना Ś. 1;<BR>अनुग्रहं संस्मरणप्रवृत्तं Ku. 3. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Assistance, help (shown to the poor in<BR>feeding them &c. दरिद्रादिपोषणं).<BR>--3<BR>Facilitating by spells.<BR>--4 Acceptance.<BR>--5 Rear-guard.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कातर a.<BR>anxious to please or for favour.<BR>--सर्गः creation of feelings or mental<BR>conditions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्राह्य
अनुग्राह्य pot. p. Fit to be<BR>favoured or obliged; ततः<BR>कथनेनात्मानमनुग्राह्यमिच्छामि K. 134; न वयमनुग्राह्याः<BR>प्रायो देवतानां 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्राहक
अनुग्राहक a.<BR>1 Favouring,<BR>furthering, promoting.<BR>--2 Gracious, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुग्रासकः|अनुग्रासक
अनुग्रासकः A mouthful; the<BR>equivalent of a mouthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुघटनं|अनुघटन
अनुघटनं Linking together with;<BR>क्षिप्ता कथानुघटनाय मयापि वाणी K. 240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचर्
अनुचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To follow,<BR>pursue, go after; to serve, attend or<BR>wait upon; पित्रोः पादाननुचरन्<BR>K. 368 serving.<BR>--2 To traverse, seek<BR>after, go through, wander.<BR>--3<BR>To conduct oneself, behave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचरः|अनुचर
अनुचरः<BR>1 A companion, follower,<BR>attendant, servant; तेनानुचरेण धेनोः<BR>R. 2. 4; आत्मानुचरस्य भावं जिज्ञासमाना<BR>26, 52; Me. 3; Ms. 12. 47. In comp.<BR>attended or followed by; वानर˚,<BR>राक्षस˚ &c.<BR>--2 Following a spy (<BR>चरमनुगतः).<BR>--री, --रा<BR>1 A female<BR>attendant.<BR>--2 A logical or due strophe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचरित
अनुचरित p. p. Followed &c.<BR>--तं<BR>Walk; walk in life; conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचारकः|अनुचारक
अनुचारकः A follower, servant<BR>&c.<BR>--रिका A female servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचर्चिः|अनुचर्चि
