अनुचित
अनुचित a.<BR>1 Wrong, improper.<BR>--2 Unusual; unfit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिंत्|अनुचिन्त्
अनुचिंत् {c10c} P. To consider,<BR>think of, call to mind;<BR>धातुर्विभुत्वमनुचिंत्य वपुश्च तस्याः Ś. 2. 9; Bg. 8. 8;<BR>Ms. 4. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिंता|अनुचिन्ता
अनुचिंता, --चिंतनं<BR>1 Calling to mind,<BR>thinking of, meditating upon.<BR>--2<BR>Recalling, recollecting.<BR>--3 Constant<BR>thinking, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुचिंतनं|अनुचिन्तन
अनुचिंता, --चिंतनं<BR>1 Calling to mind,<BR>thinking of, meditating upon.<BR>--2<BR>Recalling, recollecting.<BR>--3 Constant<BR>thinking, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छादः|अनुच्छाद|अनुछाद
अनुच्छादः The part of a man's<BR>undergarment which is allowed to<BR>hang down in front from the waist<BR>to the feet (Mar. नित्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छित्तिः|अनुच्छित्ति
अनुच्छित्तिः f., अनुच्छेदः<BR>Nonextirpation; non-destruction;<BR>indestructibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुच्छिष्ट|अनुच्छिष्टः
अनुच्छिष्ट a. Not rejected; pure,<BR>holy; fresh, unused; ˚यौवना Dk. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजन्
अनुजन् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To be born after,<BR>arise or be produced after, to<BR>follow in being born, arising &c.;<BR>पुत्रिकायां कृतायां तु यदि पुत्रोऽनुजायते<BR>Ms. 9. 134; अथवा जायमानस्य<BR>यच्छीलमनुजायते Mb.<BR>--2 To take after<BR>(one's parents); to be born similar to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज|अनुजं|अनुजः
अनुज --जात p. p. Born after,<BR>later, younger; राममनुजातः P. III. 4. 72;<BR>असौ कुमारस्तमजोऽनुजातः R. 6. 78;<BR>पुमांसमनुरुध्य जाता पुमनुजा Sk.; so<BR>स्त्र्यनुजा.<BR>--जः, --जातः<BR>1 A younger<BR>brother; Ms. 5. 58.<BR>--2 A cadet; born<BR>again, after born, younger, later.<BR>--3 Taking after.<BR>--4 Born again,<BR>invested with the sacred thread.<BR>--जा,<BR>--जाता<BR>1 A younger sister.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>plant (त्रायमाणालता).<BR>--जं N. of a<BR>plant (प्रपौंडरीक).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवर a.<BR>lower than the younger, youngest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजात|अनुजातः
अनुज --जात p. p. Born after,<BR>later, younger; राममनुजातः P. III. 4. 72;<BR>असौ कुमारस्तमजोऽनुजातः R. 6. 78;<BR>पुमांसमनुरुध्य जाता पुमनुजा Sk.; so<BR>स्त्र्यनुजा.<BR>--जः, --जातः<BR>1 A younger<BR>brother; Ms. 5. 58.<BR>--2 A cadet; born<BR>again, after born, younger, later.<BR>--3 Taking after.<BR>--4 Born again,<BR>invested with the sacred thread.<BR>--जा,<BR>--जाता<BR>1 A younger sister.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>plant (त्रायमाणालता).<BR>--जं N. of a<BR>plant (प्रपौंडरीक).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवर a.<BR>lower than the younger, youngest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजन्मन्
अनुजन्मन् m. [अनु जन्म यस्य] A<BR>younger brother; जननाथ<BR>तवानुजन्मनां Ki. 2. 17; Śi. 13. 2, 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीव्
अनुजीव् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To depend upon<BR>for subsistence, hang on, live by or<BR>upon (something); ये च<BR>त्वामनुजीवंति नाहं तेषां न ते मम Rām.; स तु तस्याः<BR>पाणिग्राहकमनुजीविष्यति Dk. 122 hang<BR>or depend on, live (submissively)<BR>under, live as a subordinate to.<BR>--2<BR>To see without envy; यां तां<BR>श्रियमसूयामः पुरा दृष्ट्वा युधिष्ठिरे अद्य<BR>तामनुजीवामः Mb.<BR>--3 To live for any one.<BR>--4<BR>To follow or imitate in living;<BR>R. 19. 15 v. l.<BR>--5 To survive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीविन्
अनुजीविन् a. Dependent, living<BR>on or upon. --m. A dependent,<BR>servant, follower; अवंचनीयाः प्रभवोऽ<BR>नुजीविभिः Ki. 1. 4, 10; भर्तुश्चिंतानुवर्तित्वं<BR>सुवृत्तं चानुजीविनाम् Pt. 1. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुजीव्य
अनुजीव्य a. To be served (as a<BR>master).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञा
अनुज्ञा {c9c} U.<BR>1 To permit, allow<BR>(a person or thing); assent or<BR>consent to, approve; authorise,<BR>sanction; तदनुजानीहि मां गमनाय U. 3 so<BR>let me go; सेयं याति शकुंतला पतिगृहं<BR>सर्वैरनुज्ञायतां Ś. 4. 8 permitted to go;<BR>Bk. 1. 23; M. 1. 19; Ms. 2. 116;<BR>तन्मया प्रीतिमताऽनुज्ञातं Ś. 5 approved,<BR>agreed to.<BR>--2 To betroth, affiance;<BR>मां जातमात्रां धनमित्रनाम्नेऽन्वजानाद्भार्यां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">Page0070-b+ 56</a>]<BR>मे पिता Dk. 50.<BR>--3 To excuse,<BR>forgive; अनुप्रवेशे यद्वीर कृतवांस्त्वं<BR>ममाप्रियं । सर्वं तदनुजानामि Mb.<BR>--4 To repent,<BR>be sorry for.<BR>--5 To request, entreat,<BR>beg; त्वां साहमनुजानामि न गंतव्यमितो<BR>वनं Rām.<BR>--6 To treat or behave<BR>kindly, favour; ते मां वीर्येण यशसा…<BR>अस्त्रैश्चाप्यन्वजानत Mb.<BR>--7 To dismiss,<BR>bid farewell (usually in caus.).<BR>--Caus. (-ज्ञापयति)<BR>1 To ask or beg for,<BR>request.<BR>--2 To ask permission, ask<BR>for leave; take leave of, bid adieu<BR>to; सोऽपि तच्छ्रुत्वा… वानरमनुज्ञाप्य<BR>स्वाश्रयं गतः Pt. 4; तं चक्रधरमनुज्ञाप्य<BR>स्वगृहं गतः 5; Ms. 4. 122; 9. 82;<BR>स मातरमनुज्ञाप्य तपस्येव मनो दधे ।<BR>जग्मतुश्च यथाकाममनुज्ञाप्य परस्परं Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञा
अनुज्ञा, --ज्ञानं [ज्ञा-अङ्-ल्युट् वा]<BR>1<BR>Permission, consent, sanction;<BR>गुरोरनुज्ञामधिगम्य मातः R. 2. 66.<BR>--2<BR>Permission or leave to depart.<BR>--3 Excusing,<BR>forgiving, allowance made for faults.<BR>--4 An order, command.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--एषणा, --प्रार्थना requesting permission,<BR>taking leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञानं|अनुज्ञान
अनुज्ञा, --ज्ञानं [ज्ञा-अङ्-ल्युट् वा]<BR>1<BR>Permission, consent, sanction;<BR>गुरोरनुज्ञामधिगम्य मातः R. 2. 66.<BR>--2<BR>Permission or leave to depart.<BR>--3 Excusing,<BR>forgiving, allowance made for faults.<BR>--4 An order, command.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--एषणा, --प्रार्थना requesting permission,<BR>taking leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञात
अनुज्ञात p. p. Permitted, allowed,<BR>assented to, granted, honoured,<BR>favoured, authorised, dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञापकः|अनुज्ञापक
अनुज्ञापकः One who commands or<BR>orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञापनं|अनुज्ञापन
अनुज्ञापनं, --ज्ञप्तिः f.<BR>1 Authorising.<BR>--2 Issuing an order or command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्ञप्तिः|अनुज्ञप्ति
अनुज्ञापनं, --ज्ञप्तिः f.<BR>1 Authorising.<BR>--2 Issuing an order or command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुज्येष्ठ
अनुज्येष्ठ a. [अनुगतो ज्येष्ठं] Next<BR>to the eldest.<BR>--ष्ठं adv. According<BR>to seniority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतप्
अनुतप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To heat; vex, annoy<BR>(fig.).<BR>--2 ({c4c} A. or pass.) To repent,<BR>grieve, be sorry for, be stung with<BR>remorse; विविधैरनुतप्यंते<BR>दयितानुनयैर्मनस्विन्यः V. 3. 5 (v. l. for<BR>निभृतैर्व्यपत्रपंते &c.); Ki. 17. 40. --Caus. To<BR>pain, afflict, distress विरहः<BR>किमिवानुतापयेद्वद बाह्यैर्विषयैर्विपश्चितं R. 8. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतप्त
अनुतप्त p. p.<BR>1 Heated.<BR>--2 Filled<BR>with regret, repentant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापः|अनुताप
अनुतापः<BR>1 Repentance, remorse,<BR>contrition, subsequent regret or<BR>sorrow; जातानुतापेव सा V. 4. 38 stung<BR>with remorse; Ms. 11. 228.<BR>--2 Heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापन
अनुतापन a. Causing distress or<BR>regret or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतापिन्
अनुतापिन् a. Repentant, sorry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर|अनुतरं
अनुतर See under अनुतॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्षः|अनुतर्ष
अनुतर्षः [तृष्-घञ्]<BR>1 Thirst,<BR>desire to drink; सोपचारमुपशांतविचारं<BR>सानुतर्षमनुतर्षपदेन Śi. 10. 2 (thirst and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">Page0070-c+ 56</a>]<BR>liquor).<BR>--2 Wish, desire.<BR>--3<BR>Drinking spirituous liquors.<BR>--4 A<BR>drinking vessel (used in drinking<BR>spirituous liquors).<BR>--5 Liquor itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतर्षणं|अनुतर्षण
अनुतर्षणं = अनुतर्ष 3 and 4<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतिल
अनुतिल a. Following तिल (as a<BR>field).<BR>--लं ind. Grain after grain,<BR>i. e. by grains or very minutely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतुन्न
अनुतुन्न a. Ved. Depressed or<BR>repressed (in sound), unruffled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतूलयति
अनुतूलयति Den. P. To rub (as<BR>the point or end of grass) with<BR>cotton; P. III. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतूलनं|अनुतूलन
अनुतूलनं Rubbing in this manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतॄ
अनुतॄ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go across or<BR>to the end.<BR>--2 To stretch<BR>lengthwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुतरं|अनुतर
अनुतरं [अनुतीर्यते अनेन; करणे अप्]<BR>Fare, freight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्क
अनुत्क a. Not overanxious, not<BR>repentant or regretful;<BR>self-complacent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्त
अनुत्त a. Ved. [उद्-क्त न. त.]<BR>1<BR>Not moistened or wet;<BR>तुभ्यमिदद्रिवोऽनुत्तं Rv. 1. 80. 7.<BR>--2 Not sent^1, driven forth or urged (अप्रेरित);<BR>invincible (?).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by @aumsanskrit on 20240826. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101  ap90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तम|अनुत्तमः
अनुत्तम a. [न उत्तमो यस्मात्]<BR>1<BR>Than which there is nothing better,<BR>having no superior or better,<BR>unsurpassed, the very best or<BR>highest, incomparably or pre-eminently<BR>the best; सर्वद्रव्येषु विद्यैव<BR>द्रव्यमाहुरनुत्तमं H. Pr. 4; कांक्षन् गतिमनुत्तमां<BR>Ms. 2. 242; Y. 1. 87; अदस्त्वया<BR>नुन्नमनुत्तमं तमः Śi. 1. 27 all-pervading;<BR>Bg. 7. 18; Ms. 2. 9; 5. 158; 8. 81.<BR>--2 Not the best.<BR>--3 (In gram.)<BR>Not used in the उत्तम or first,<BR>person.<BR>--मः N. of Śiva or Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंभस्, --अंभसिकं a term in<BR>Sāṃkhya philosophy, said to mean<BR>‘indifference to and abstinence from<BR>sensual enjoyment, as fatiguing<BR>or involving injury to external<BR>objects.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तर|अनुत्तरं
अनुत्तर a. [नास्ति उत्तरो यस्मात्]<BR>1 Principal, chief.<BR>--2 Best,<BR>excellent; अनुत्तराणि विलसितानि<BR>Dk. 162 unsurpassed.<BR>--3 [नास्ति उत्तरं<BR>यस्य] Without a reply, silent,<BR>unable to answer; भवत्यवज्ञा च<BR>भवत्यनुत्तरात् Naiṣadha.<BR>--4 Fixed, firm<BR>(न उत्तरति चलति).<BR>--5 Low, inferior, base,<BR>mean.<BR>--6 Southern.<BR>--रं [न. त.] No<BR>reply, a reply which, being evasive,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">Page0071-a+ 54</a>]<BR>is considered to be no reply.<BR>--राः<BR>(pl.) A class of gods among<BR>Jainas (˚उपपातिक).<BR>--रा The south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्तरंग
अनुत्तरंग a. Steady, not ruffled<BR>(by waves); अपमिवाधारमनुत्तरंगं<BR>Ku. 3. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्थानं|अनुत्थान
अनुत्थानं Absence of exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पत्तिः|अनुत्पत्ति
अनुत्पत्तिः f. Failure,<BR>non-production. --a.,<BR>--त्तिक a. Not yet<BR>produced.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धर्मक्षांतिः<BR>preparation for a future state, acquiescence<BR>in the state and moral condition<BR>which is yet to come.<BR>--समः --मा a<BR>method of arguing against a thing by<BR>attempting to prove that nothing<BR>exists from which it could spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पन्न
अनुत्पन्न a. Not produced or born,<BR>unborn, unproduced &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्पादः|अनुत्पाद
अनुत्पादः Not coming into<BR>existence, not taking effect.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्षांति see अनुत्पत्तिधर्मक्षांति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्साह|अनुत्साहः
अनुत्साह a. Destitute of energy<BR>or determination.<BR>--हः Want of<BR>determination, energy &c.;<BR>listlessness, languor, indifference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सुक
अनुत्सुक a. Moderate, not<BR>overeager, retiring, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सूत्र
अनुत्सूत्र a. Not deviating from<BR>the Sūtra (of Pāṇini or of morality);<BR>not anomalous or irregular;<BR>˚पदन्यासा सद्वृत्तिः सन्निबंधना Śi. 2. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सेकः|अनुत्सेक
अनुत्सेकः Absence of<BR>haughtiness or pride; ˚को लक्ष्म्यां Bh. 2. 63;<BR>modesty; ˚कः खलु विक्रमालंकारः V. 1;<BR>cf. “Modesty is the handmaid of<BR>heroism”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुत्सेकिन्
अनुत्सेकिन् a. Not puffed up, not<BR>proud or arrogant; भाग्येषु˚ नी भव<BR>Ś. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद
अनुद a. [न नुदति or अनुददाति तुल्यं<BR>ददाति, दा-क] Ved. Not urging or<BR>driving onward; or, emulating others<BR>in giving (तुल्यरूपदातृ); see अनानुद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदक
अनुदक a.<BR>1 Waterless(as a desert).<BR>--2 Having very little water (as a<BR>puddle).<BR>--3 Devoid of the libations<BR>of water (a sort of श्राद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदग्र|अनुदग्रः
अनुदग्र a.<BR>1 Not lofty, low.<BR>--2<BR>Soft, tender; weak, not sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर
अनुदर a. Having a slender<BR>waist; thin, lank; ˚राजकन्या Sk. (<BR>अल्पार्थे नञ्, see अ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदा
अनुदा {c3c} U. To give back, restore;<BR>to yield, grant, remit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेयी
अनुदेयी<BR>1 Restoration.<BR>--2 A female<BR>companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदात्त|अनुदात्तः
अनुदात्त a. Grave (accent); not<BR>elevated or raised (not pronounced<BR>with the Udātta accent); उच्चैरुदात्तः,<BR>नीचैरनुदात्तः; accentless, having the<BR>neutral, general tone; उदात्तश्चानुदात्तश्च<BR>स्वरितश्च त्रयः स्वराः; uttered with the<BR>grave accent (as a vowel); प्रयत्नप्रेरितो<BR>वायुर्यदोर्ध्वभागे प्रतिहतोऽचं निष्पादयति स उदात्तः;<BR>एवमधोनिष्पन्नोऽच् अनुदात्तः; ताल्वादिषु<BR>सभागेषु स्थानेषु नीचभागे निष्पन्नोऽच् अनुदात्तः;<BR>˚त्तं पदमेकवर्जं Sk. (The term<BR>अनुदात्त is used by Pāṇini for the grave<BR>accent which immediately precedes<BR>the Udātta, and also for the general<BR>accentless tone neither high nor<BR>low, termed एकश्रुति, the one<BR>monotonous intonation belonging to the<BR>generality of syllables in a sentence).<BR>--त्तः The grave accent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आदिः a nominal base of which the<BR>first syllable is अनुदात्त.<BR>--इत् a verbal<BR>root having for its अनुबंध the grave<BR>accent (denoting that it takes the<BR>Ātm. terminations only).<BR>--उदयं a<BR>syllable followed (immediately)<BR>by the grave accent.<BR>--तर a. more<BR>than अनुदात्त; still lower or graver<BR>accent, i. e. that which<BR>immediately precedes a syllable having the<BR>उदात्त or स्वरित accent and is thus<BR>more depressed than the ordinary<BR>अनुदात्त accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदार|अनुदारः
अनुदार a.<BR>1 Not liberal,<BR>niggardly; not high or noble.<BR>--2<BR>Having none more liberal, very liberal,<BR>or great.<BR>--3 (अनुगतो दारान्) Adhering<BR>to or followed by a wife; यस्मिन्प्रसीदसि<BR>पुनः स भवत्युदारोऽनुदारश्च K. P. 4 (used in<BR>sense 1 also).<BR>--4 Having a suitable<BR>or worthy wife (अनुरूपाः दाराः यस्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदित
अनुदित a.<BR>1 Unsaid, not<BR>uttered.<BR>--2 Not risen or appeared forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिनं|अनुदिन
अनुदिनं --दिवसं ind. Daily, day after<BR>day; पारावतः खलु शिलाकणमात्रभोजी<BR>कामी भवेदनुदिनं वद कोऽत्र हेतुः Udb.;<BR>अनुदिवसं परिहीयसेंऽगैः Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिवसं
अनुदिनं --दिवसं ind. Daily, day after<BR>day; पारावतः खलु शिलाकणमात्रभोजी<BR>कामी भवेदनुदिनं वद कोऽत्र हेतुः Udb.;<BR>अनुदिवसं परिहीयसेंऽगैः Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदिश्
अनुदिश् {c6c} P. To point out, assign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेशः|अनुदेश
अनुदेशः<BR>1 Pointing back; a rule<BR>or direction which refers or points<BR>back to a previous rule;<BR>यथासंख्यमनुदेशः समानां P. I. 3. 10; subsequent<BR>mention of things (words, suffixes<BR>&c.) in the order of things<BR>previously mentioned, respective<BR>enumeration or statement, first for first,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">Page0071-c+ 56</a>]<BR>second for second; as in<BR>समूलाकृतजीवेषु हन्कृञ्ग्रहः P. III. 4. 36.<BR>--2<BR>Direction, order, injunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदेशिन्
अनुदेशिन् a. Pointing or referring<BR>back; being the object of an अनुदेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदृश्
अनुदृश् {c1c} P. To survey, behold;<BR>to keep in view or mind, see in<BR>prospect; न च श्रेयोऽनुपश्यामि हत्वा<BR>स्वजनमाहवे Bg. 1. 31; Bh. 3. 3. --Caus.<BR>To show, tell, inform as follows;<BR>सेनापतिः पुत्रमग्निमित्रं परिष्वज्य<BR>अनुदर्शयति M. 5 writes or informs as follows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदर्शनं|अनुदर्शन
अनुदर्शनं Inspection, survey;<BR>उत्थितश्चाप्रमत्तश्च बलानामनुदर्शने Rām.;<BR>consideration, regard;<BR>जन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिदुःखदोषानुदर्शनं Bg. 13. 8 perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदृष्टि|अनुदृष्टिः
अनुदृष्टि a. Having a favourable<BR>look.<BR>--ष्टिः f. A favourable look.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुदैर्घ्य
अनुदैर्घ्य a. [दैर्घ्यमनुगतः]<BR>Longitudinal, lengthwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धत
अनुद्धत a. Not raised or puffed<BR>up; ˚ताः सत्पुरुषाः समृद्धिभिः Ś. 5. 12;<BR>humble; modest; unsurpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धरणं|अनुद्धरण
अनुद्धरणं<BR>1 Not removing or<BR>taking away.<BR>--2 Not offering,<BR>establishing or proving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धारः|अनुद्धार
अनुद्धारः<BR>1 Non-partition; not<BR>taking a share (विंशोद्धारशून्यो विभागः).<BR>--2<BR>Non-removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्धृत
अनुद्धृत a. Undivided,<BR>unremoved, uninjured, unharmed,<BR>undestroyed, unoffered or established &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभ्यस्तमयः taking place<BR>of sunset, while the आहवनीय fire<BR>continues to be unremoved from<BR>the गार्हपत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्भट
अनुद्भट a.<BR>1 Not bold; soft,<BR>mild.<BR>--2 Not exalted or lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्यत
अनुद्यत, अनुद्यम a. Not diligent,<BR>idle, inactive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्यम
अनुद्यत, अनुद्यम a. Not diligent,<BR>idle, inactive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्यूतं|अनुद्यूत
अनुद्यूतं Repeated playing or<BR>gambling; N. of a part of the<BR>Sabhāparvan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्योग|अनुद्योगः
अनुद्योग a. Lazy, not<BR>industrious.<BR>--गः Idleness, inactivity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्रु
अनुद्रु {c1c} P.<BR>1 To run after,<BR>follow, accompany; धनुर्धरं<BR>राजसुतैरनुद्रुतं R. 3. 38; 12. 67; 16. 25;<BR>Śi. 1. 52; 5. 59.<BR>--2 To chase, pursue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्रुत|अनुद्रुतं
अनुद्रुत p. p.<BR>1 Followed, pursued;<BR>(sometimes used actively).<BR>--2 Sent<BR>or brought back (as sound).<BR>--तं A<BR>measure of time in music = half druta,<BR>or one-fourth of a Mātrā (or of the<BR>time taken to utter a short vowel);<BR>अर्धमात्रं द्रुतं ज्ञेयं द्रुतार्धं चाप्यनुद्रुतं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्वाहः|अनुद्वाह
अनुद्वाहः Non-marriage, celibacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्विग्न
अनुद्विग्न a. Easy in mind, secure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुद्वेग|अनुद्वेगः
अनुद्वेग a. Free from anxiety or<BR>apprehension.<BR>--गः Security or<BR>freedom from fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुधाव्
अनुधाव् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To run after;<BR>follow; ऋषीणां पुनराद्यानां वाचमर्थोऽ<BR>नुधावति U. 1. 10 the sense follows the<BR>words (the words being not<BR>uttered with a view to a particular sense);<BR>स्वरुचिं निश्चयतोऽनुधावति Śi. 16. 44<BR>follows his own will.<BR>--2 To run up<BR>to, approach.<BR>--3 To cleanse, wash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुधावनं|अनुधावन
अनुधावनं<BR>1 Going or running after,<BR>following, pursuing; तुरग ˚कंडितसंधेः<BR>Ś. 2.<BR>--2 Close pursuit of an object<BR>(for the knowledge of truth);<BR>research, investigation.<BR>--3 Seeking a<BR>mistress, though unattainable.<BR>--4<BR>Cleansing, purification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्यै
अनुध्यै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To think of, muse,<BR>consider attentively.<BR>--2 To wish well<BR>of, to bless, favour; प्रजानिषेकं मयि<BR>वर्तमानं सूनोरनुध्यायत चेतसेति R. 14. 60<BR>bless; अनुदध्युरनुध्येयं सांनिध्यैः प्रतिमागतैः<BR>17. 36 favoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्या
अनुध्या [ध्यै-अङ्] Thinking or<BR>wishing well of, favouring, attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्यान
अनुध्यान p. p. Mused, thought<BR>of &c.<BR>--तं --नं [ध्यै-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Thought;<BR>अनुध्यानानंतरमेव K. 262; meditation,<BR>religious contemplation.<BR>--2<BR>Thinking of, remembrance; या नः<BR>प्रीतिर्विरूपाक्ष त्वदनुध्यानसंभवा Ku. 6. 21.<BR>--3<BR>Wishing well of, affectionate<BR>solicitude for; अनुध्यातैरुपेतव्यं<BR>वत्सयोर्भद्रमस्तु वः U. 7. 11; सा त्वमंब<BR>स्नुषायामरुंधतीव सीतायां शिवानुध्यानपरा भव U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्यायः|अनुध्याय
अनुध्यायः [ध्यै कर्तरि घञ्] One who<BR>wishes well of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुध्येय
अनुध्येय a. To be favoured or<BR>wished well of; अनुदध्युरनुध्येयं<BR>R. 17. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनद्
अनुनद् {c1c} P. To sound towards<BR>or at (with acc.). --Caus. To cause<BR>to sound, make resonant, fill with<BR>echo; पृथिवीं चांतरिक्षं च<BR>सागरांश्चानुनादयन्; साधु साध्विति नादेन<BR>पृथिवीमन्वनादयन्; विहंगैरनुनादितं Mb. made<BR>musical or resonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनादः|अनुनाद
अनुनादः [अनुरूपो नादः] Sound, noise;<BR>Śi. 7. 18; reverberation, echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनादिन्
अनुनादिन् a. Echoing, sounding,<BR>resonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनय|अनुनयः
अनुनय, --नायिका See under अनुनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनायिका
अनुनय, --नायिका See under अनुनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनासिक
अनुनासिक a. [अनुगतो नासिकां]<BR>1 Nasal, pronounced through the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-b" target="_blank">Page0072-b+ 57</a>]<BR>nose; मुखसहितनासिकया उच्चार्यमाणो<BR>वर्णोऽनुनासिकसंज्ञः स्यात् Sk.;<BR>मुखनासिकावचनोऽनुनासिकः P. I. 1. 8; अमोऽ<BR>नुनासिका न थौ Śikṣā; अनुनासिक being a name<BR>for the 5 nasal consonants, the<BR>vowels or the consonants य्, व्, ल्<BR>(under certain circumstances); i. e.<BR>the letters included in the प्रत्याहार<BR>अम् except ह् and र्.<BR>--2 The sign used<BR>to mark the nasalization in the case<BR>of य्, व् or ल्.<BR>--कं The nasal twang.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आदिः a conjunct<BR>consonant beginning with a nasal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनिर्देशः|अनुनिर्देश
अनुनिर्देशः Description or<BR>relation following the previous order<BR>or sequence; भूयसामुपदिष्टानां क्रियाणामथ<BR>कर्मणाम् । क्रमशो योऽनुनिर्देशो यथासंख्यं<BR>तदुच्यते S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनिर्वापः|अनुनिर्वाप
अनुनिर्वापः Subsequent libation<BR>(with clarified butter).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनिर्वाप्या
अनुनिर्वाप्या A ceremony connected<BR>with this libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनी
अनुनी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To conciliate, win<BR>over, induce, persuade, prevail upon;<BR>request, supplicate, entreat,<BR>propitiate, pacify, appease (anger &c.);<BR>स चानुनीतः प्रणतेन पश्चात् R. 5. 54;<BR>विग्रहाच्च शयने पराङ्मुखीर्नानुनेतुमबलाः स<BR>तत्वरे 19. 38, 43; Bk. 6. 137; 5. 46,<BR>त्वत्संगमेन मम तत्तदिवानुनीतं V. 3. 20<BR>pacified, made favourable or<BR>agreeable; Ki. 13. 67; M. 5; K. 168, 178;<BR>Dk. 3, 4, 7.<BR>--2 To cherish love;<BR>विद्विषोप्यनुनय Bh. 2. 77; cf. Shakespeare<BR>“Cherish those hearts that hate<BR>thee”.<BR>--3 To bring near to (with<BR>dat. of person).<BR>--4 To train,<BR>discipline.<BR>--5 To honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनय|अनुनयः
अनुनय a. [नी-अच्] Kind,<BR>conciliatory, pacifying (as words).<BR>--यः<BR>1 Conciliation, propitiation,<BR>pacification (of anger), friendly<BR>persuasion; कथं नु शक्योऽनुनयो<BR>महर्षेर्विश्राणनाच्चान्यपयस्विनीनां R. 2. 54; कथं<BR>वा तेषामनुनयः कृतः H. 4;<BR>प्रकृतिवक्रः स कस्यानुनयं प्रतिगृह्णाति Ś. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Courtesy, civility, courteous or<BR>polite behaviour, modesty, modest or<BR>respectful deportment, conciliatory<BR>act (such as salutation); showing<BR>respect (to a guest, deity &c.);<BR>विविधैरनुतप्यंते दयितानुनयैर्मनस्विन्यः<BR>V. 3. 5; दयितजन˚ 2. 22; वाक्यैः<BR>स्निग्धैरनुनयो भवेदर्थस्य साधनं S. D. 458.<BR>--3 An humble supplication or<BR>entreaty, a request in general; भद्र प्रियं<BR>नः । किंतु त्वदभिप्रायापरिज्ञानांतरितोऽ<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">Page0072-c+ 56</a>]<BR>यमस्मदनुनयः Mu. 2; R. 6. 2;<BR>निषेधवाक्यालंकारजिज्ञासानुनये खलु Ak; ˚आमंत्रणं<BR>conciliatory address.<BR>--4 Discipline,<BR>training, regulation of conduct.<BR>--यः<BR>adv. Fitly, suitably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनयिन्
अनुनयिन् a. Courteous, polite,<BR>humble, supplicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनीतिः|अनुनीति
अनुनीतिः = अनुनय q. v.; सानुनीतिश्च<BR>सीतायै नाक्रुध्यत् Bk. 8. 75 adopting a<BR>conciliatory tone; Śi. 16. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनायक
अनुनायक a. Submissive, humble,<BR>supplicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुनायिक
अनुनायिक a. Conciliating; प्रियतमेषु<BR>वधूरनुनायिका Śi. 6. 7.<BR>--का A female<BR>character subordinate to the Nāyikā<BR>or leading character, such as a friend,<BR>nurse, maidservant &c.; सखी प्रव्रजिता<BR>दासी प्रेष्या धात्रेयिका तथा । अन्याश्च<BR>शिल्पकारिण्यो विज्ञेया ह्यनुनायिकाः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्नत
अनुन्नत a. Not raised or<BR>elevated, not lifted up.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आनत a.<BR>level (neither raised nor lowered).<BR>--गात्र a. having limbs not stout or<BR>prominent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्माद
अनुन्माद, --अनुन्मत्त a. Not mad<BR>or frantic, sober, calm, sane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुन्मत्त
अनुन्माद, --अनुन्मत्त a. Not mad<BR>or frantic, sober, calm, sane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप
अनुप = अनूप, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपकारिन्
अनुपकारिन् a.<BR>1 Not obliging,<BR>ungrateful, not making a return for<BR>benefits received.<BR>--2 Worthless,<BR>useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपक्षित
अनुपक्षित p. p. Not injured or<BR>destroyed (अनुपक्षीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपगीत
अनुपगीत a. Not praised.<BR>--तं<BR>ind. So that no other person<BR>accompanies in singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपघातः|अनुपघात
अनुपघातः Absence of damage or<BR>detriment; ˚अर्जित obtained without<BR>any detriment (to the paternal<BR>estate).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपजीवनीय
अनुपजीवनीय a. Not yielding or<BR>granting livelihood, having no<BR>livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपठ्
अनुपठ् {c1c} P. To say after, repeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपठित
अनुपठित p. p. Read through,<BR>repeated in imitation of the teacher's<BR>instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपठितिन्
अनुपठितिन् a. Who has read<BR>through, proficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपत्
अनुपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fly to or towards.<BR>--2 To fly or run after, follow (fig.<BR>also); pursue, chase; मुहुरनुपतति स्यंदने<BR>दत्तदृष्टिः Ś. 1. 7; कथमनुपतत एव मे<BR>प्रयत्नप्रेक्षणीयः संवृत्तः Ś. 1.; न यत्र<BR>प्रत्याशामनुपतति नो वा रहयति (चेतः)<BR>Māl. 9. 8 does not run after (cherish)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-a" target="_blank">Page0073-a+ 58</a>]<BR>hope or leave it; यस्यैवं भवंतः<BR>कुटुंबवृत्तिमनुपतिताः Mv. 1; Śi. 11. 40.<BR>--3 To<BR>fall upon, attack; प्राग्वीराननुपत्य<BR>Māl. 8. 9. --Caus.<BR>1 To fly to.<BR>--2 To throw<BR>another down along with oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपतनं|अनुपतन
अनुपतनं, पातः<BR>1 Falling upon,<BR>alighting upon in succession.<BR>--2<BR>Following, going after, pursuit;<BR>उपवनपवनानुपातदक्षैः Śi. 7. 27.<BR>--3 Going or<BR>proceeding in order or as a<BR>consequence.<BR>--4 [अनुरूपः त्रैराशिकेन पातः]<BR>Proportion.<BR>--5 Rule of three.<BR>--6 A<BR>degree of latitude, opposite to one<BR>given.<BR>--तं ind. (regarded as a ṇamul<BR>from पत्) Following in succession,<BR>going after; लतानुपातं कुसुमान्यगृह्णात्<BR>Bk. 2. 11 (लतां लतामनुपात्य going to<BR>creeper after creeper, or after<BR>bending the creepers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातः|अनुपात
अनुपतनं, पातः<BR>1 Falling upon,<BR>alighting upon in succession.<BR>--2<BR>Following, going after, pursuit;<BR>उपवनपवनानुपातदक्षैः Śi. 7. 27.<BR>--3 Going or<BR>proceeding in order or as a<BR>consequence.<BR>--4 [अनुरूपः त्रैराशिकेन पातः]<BR>Proportion.<BR>--5 Rule of three.<BR>--6 A<BR>degree of latitude, opposite to one<BR>given.<BR>--तं ind. (regarded as a ṇamul<BR>from पत्) Following in succession,<BR>going after; लतानुपातं कुसुमान्यगृह्णात्<BR>Bk. 2. 11 (लतां लतामनुपात्य going to<BR>creeper after creeper, or after<BR>bending the creepers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातिन्
अनुपातिन् a. Following as a result.<BR>--m. A follower; मदनुपातिनामेष पंथाः<BR>Dk. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपथ|अनुपथः
अनुपथ a. [पंथानमनुगतः]<BR>Following the road.<BR>--थः A road,<BR>favourable road; अंतस्पथा अनुपथाः<BR>Rv. 5. 52. 10 (अनुकूलमार्गाः).<BR>--थं adv. Along<BR>the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपद्
अनुपद् {c4c} A. (P. in epic poetry)<BR>1 To go after, follow, attend.<BR>--2 To<BR>be fond of, be attached to (as a<BR>wife); उतथ्यस्य यवीयांस्तु ममतामन्वपद्यत<BR>Mb.<BR>--3 To enter, go to or into.<BR>--4<BR>To fall down, come down (to the<BR>earth); वसुधामन्वपद्येतां वातनुन्नाविव<BR>द्रुमौ Mb.<BR>--5 To enter upon, betake<BR>oneself to; जितमित्येव<BR>तानक्षान्पुनरेवान्वपद्यत, ध्यानमेवान्वपद्यत Rām.; पुत्रौ दृष्ट्वा<BR>सुसंभ्रांता नान्वपद्यत किंचन Mb. did<BR>not do anything else.<BR>--6 To find,<BR>discover, see, notice; दीर्घं दध्यौ…<BR>निमित्तं सोऽन्वपद्यत Bhāg.<BR>--7 To lose<BR>(with abl.); महत्वान्नान्वपद्येतां Mb.<BR>--8 To handle.<BR>--9 To fall to the share<BR>of (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपद्
अनुपद् a. [पद्-क्विप्] Ved. Coming<BR>to pass. --f. Food (got every day)<BR>(अनुदिनलभ्यमन्नं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपद|अनुपदं|अनुपदः
अनुपद a. [पदान्यनुगतः]<BR>1<BR>Following the feet closely.<BR>--2<BR>Following every word; ˚सूत्रं a<BR>commentary (of a Brāhmaṇa)<BR>explaining the text word for word.<BR>--दः<BR>N. of a man or tribe.<BR>--दं A chorus,<BR>burden of a song or words sung<BR>again at regular intervals. --ind. [<BR>पदानां पश्चात्]<BR>1 Along the feet, near<BR>the feet; अनुपदं बद्धा अनुपदीना Sk.<BR>--2 Step by step, at every step;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">Page0073-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Śi. 9. 78.<BR>--3 Word for word.<BR>--4 On<BR>the heels of, close behind or after,<BR>immediately after (of time or<BR>space); अनुपदमन्वेष्टा अनुपदी Sk.;<BR>गच्छतां पुरो भवंतौ । अहमप्यनुपदमागत एव<BR>Ś. 3 I shall be close behind you,<BR>just follow you; ˚दमुच्चलित एव<BR>K. 263, 264; oft. with gen. or in<BR>comp. in this sense;<BR>लक्ष्मीवाननुपदमस्य संप्रतस्थे Ki. 12. 54; (तौ)<BR>आशिषामनुपदं समस्पृशत् पाणिना<BR>R. 11. 31; अमोघाः प्रतिगृह्णंतावर्ध्यानुपदमाशिषः<BR>1. 44, 14. 81; Śi. 14. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदिक
अनुपदिक a. [अनुपदमस्त्यस्य गंतृत्वेन,<BR>ठन्] Following, gone after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदिन्
अनुपदिन् a. [अनुपद्-इनि<BR>P. V. 2. 90] Following, seeking after or<BR>for, a searcher, inquirer;<BR>अनुपदमन्वेष्टा गवामनुपदी Sk.; क्षणदाकरेऽनुपदिभिः<BR>प्रयये Śi. 9. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदीना
अनुपदीना [आयामार्थे अनु,<BR>पदस्यायामतुल्यायामः, तेन बद्धा ख^1] A shoe (boot,<BR>buskin, or slippers) of the length<BR>of the foot (अनुपदं बद्धा अनुपदीना<BR>उपानत् P. V. 2. 9 Sk.)<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dhaval Patel on 20161231. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/329.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपदवी
अनुपदवी A way, road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपधः|अनुपध
अनुपधः ‘Having no उपधा or<BR>penultimate’, a letter or syllable<BR>not preceded by another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपधि
अनुपधि a. [न. ब.] Guileless,<BR>without fraud; रहस्यं साधूनामनुपधि<BR>विशुद्धं विजयते U. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपन्यासः|अनुपन्यास
अनुपन्यासः<BR>1 Not mentioning;<BR>non-statement.<BR>--2 Uncertainty,<BR>doubt, failure of proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपपत्तिः|अनुपपत्ति
अनुपपत्तिः f.<BR>1 Failure, failing to<BR>be; लक्षणा शक्यसंबंधस्तात्पर्यानुपपत्तितः<BR>Bhāṣā P. 82 (तात्पर्य˚ being the failure<BR>of the meaning aimed at, or of any<BR>connected meaning).<BR>--2<BR>Inapplicability, not being applicable.<BR>--3<BR>Inconclusive reasoning; absence of<BR>reasonable grounds (युत्तयभाव); पीनो देवदत्तो<BR>दिवा न भुंक्ते इत्यत्र दिवाऽभोजिनः पीनत्वं<BR>रात्रिभोजनं विनानुपपन्नम्; see अर्थापात्ति also.<BR>--4<BR>Penury, adversity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपपन्न
अनुपपन्न a. Improper, impossible,<BR>inapplicable, impracticable,<BR>inconclusive, irrelevant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपम|अनुपमः
अनुपम a. [न. ब.] Incomparable,<BR>matchless, peerless, best, most<BR>excellent.<BR>--मा The female elephant of<BR>the southwest (mate of कुमुद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपमेय
अनुपमेय --मित a. Matchless,<BR>incomparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपमित
अनुपमेय --मित a. Matchless,<BR>incomparable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपमर्दनं|अनुपमर्दन
अनुपमर्दनं Non-refutation of a<BR>charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपयुक्त
अनुपयुक्त a.<BR>1 Not used (as<BR>food).<BR>--2 Unsuited, unfit,<BR>improper, useless, unserviceable Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपयोग|अनुपयोगः
अनुपयोग a. Useless.<BR>--गः<BR>Uselessness, not being used (as food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपरत
अनुपरत a.<BR>1 Not dead.<BR>--2 Not<BR>stopped, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलब्ध
अनुपलब्ध a. Unobserved,<BR>unperceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलब्धिः|अनुपलब्धि
अनुपलब्धिः f. Non-recognition,<BR>non-perception (प्रत्यक्षाद्यभाव);<BR>नास्ति घटोऽनुपलब्धेः the knowledge of<BR>घटाभाव is possible because the<BR>प्रतियोगी or counter-entity is not found<BR>with the non-entity or अभाव (that<BR>is, there being no उपलब्धि or<BR>knowledge of the घट); one of the<BR>instruments of knowledge according to the<BR>Mīmāṃsakas, but not according to<BR>the Naiyāyikas.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--समः a<BR>fallacy, trying to establish a fact<BR>(say, the eternity of sound) from<BR>the impossibility of seeing the<BR>nonperception of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपलंभः|अनुपलम्भ|अनुपलम्भः
अनुपलंभः Want of apprehension;<BR>non-perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपवीतिन्
अनुपवीतिन् m. One who does<BR>not wear the sacred thread<BR>(belonging to his caste).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपशयः|अनुपशय
अनुपशयः Any thing or<BR>circumstance that aggravates a malady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपश्य
अनुपश्य a. Following with his<BR>looks, keeping in view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपसंहारिन्
अनुपसंहारिन् m. A kind of<BR>हेत्वाभास or fallacy in Nyāya, a<BR>subdivision of the अनैकांतिकहेत्वाभास;<BR>वस्तुमात्रपक्षकोऽनुपसंहारी that is, that<BR>which includes every known thing<BR>in the पक्ष and thus prevents the<BR>corroboration of a general rule of<BR>causation by illustrations, positive<BR>or negative; as सर्वं नित्यं प्रमेयत्वात्;<BR>अत्र सर्वस्यैव पक्षत्वात् प्रमेयत्वं हेतुरनुपसंहारी<BR>अन्वये व्यतिरेके वा दृष्टांताभावात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपसर्गः|अनुपसर्ग
अनुपसर्गः<BR>1 A word (particle &c.)<BR>that is not, or has not the force of,<BR>an Upasarga.<BR>--2 That which has no<BR>Upasarga.<BR>--3 That which needs<BR>no additions (as a divine being).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपसेचन
अनुपसेचन a. Having no<BR>उपसेचन i. e. some condiment, sauce, curds<BR>&c. to moisten food with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्कृत
अनुपस्कृत a.<BR>1 Unpolished, (as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">Page0074-a+ 56</a>]<BR>silver).<BR>--2 Genuine, blameless.<BR>--3<BR>Not cooked or dressed (as food).<BR>--4 Not requiring any evident object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्कार
अनुपस्कार a. Not elliptical<BR>(अध्याहारदोषरहित) Ki. 11. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थानं|अनुपस्थान
अनुपस्थानं Absence, not being<BR>at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थापनं|अनुपस्थापन
अनुपस्थापनं Not placing, offering<BR>or producing, not having ready or<BR>at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थापित
अनुपस्थापित a. Not ready or at<BR>hand, not offered or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थायिन्
अनुपस्थायिन् a. Not present, absent,<BR>distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थित
अनुपस्थित a. Not present, absent,<BR>not at hand or near; not current.<BR>--तं<BR>A word that is not उपस्थित q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपस्थितिः|अनुपस्थिति
अनुपस्थितिः f.<BR>1 Absence; मम ˚तिं<BR>क्षमंतां भवंतः your honour will be<BR>pleased to excuse my absence.<BR>--2<BR>Inability to remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपहत
अनुपहत a.<BR>1 Not injured,<BR>unimpaired, unvitiated.<BR>--2 Not used,<BR>unbleached, new (as cloth); ˚तं<BR>दुकूलयुगलं K. 110, 229. See अनाहत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपा
अनुपा {c2c} P.<BR>1 To drink after (a<BR>person or thing), drink along with;<BR>(मधु पीत्वा)… अनुपास्यसि बाष्पदूषितं<BR>जलांजलिं R. 8. 68; कल्माषान्भक्षयन्मधु<BR>चानुपिबेत् Suśr.; Bṛ. S. 76. 6.<BR>--2 To<BR>follow in drinking.<BR>--3 ({c2c} P.) =<BR>अनुपाल् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपानं|अनुपान
अनुपानं<BR>1 A drink taken with or<BR>after medicine (अनु भेषजेन सह पश्चाद्वा<BR>यत् किंचिन्मधुक्षीरादि पीयते तत्); a fluid<BR>vehicle in medicine.<BR>--2 A drink<BR>close at hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपानीय
अनुपानीय a. Serving as a liquid<BR>vehicle of medicine.<BR>--यं An<BR>after-drink, what is fit to be drunk after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपा
अनुपा {c2c} P.,<BR>--पाल् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To<BR>guard, watch over, protect, defend;<BR>बालदायादिकं रिक्थं तावद्राजानुपालयेत्<BR>Ms. 8. 27 keep in custody.<BR>--2 To<BR>conform to, obey, observe;<BR>दशरथवचनमनुपालयन् K. 21; सत्योनुपालयेत्सत्यं<BR>H. 4. 23; so प्रतिज्ञां, धर्मं, मार्गं &c.;<BR>keep, preserve; अनुपालयतां प्रभुशक्तिं<BR>Ki. 2. 10 watching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपालनं|अनुपालन
अनुपालनं Preserving, keeping up,<BR>obeying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपाकृत
अनुपाकृत a. Not rendered fit<BR>for or consecrated for sacrificial<BR>purposes.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मांसं flesh of an<BR>animal not prepared for sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपात|अनुपातः
अनुपात, --तिन् see under अनुपत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातिन्
अनुपात, --तिन् see under अनुपत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपाख्य
अनुपाख्य a. Not clearly visible<BR>or discernible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपातकं|अनुपातक
अनुपातकं [पातकं ब्रह्महत्यादि<BR>तत्सदृशं] A heinous crime such as<BR>theft, murder, adultery &c. 35<BR>such sins are enumerated in<BR>Viṣṇusmṛti; Manu mentions 30<BR>kinds; See 11. 54-58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपार्श्व
अनुपार्श्व a. Lateral, along or<BR>by the side.--(pl.) N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपावृत्त
अनुपावृत्त a. Ved. Western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपुरुषः|अनुपुरुष
अनुपुरुषः [अनुगतः अन्यं पुरुषं] A<BR>follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपुष्पः|अनुपुष्प
अनुपुष्पः [अनुगतः पुष्पं तद्विकारं] A<BR>kind of reed (शरवृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्व|अनुपूर्वं|अनुपूर्व्व
अनुपूर्व a. [अनुगतः पूर्वं परिपाटीं<BR>क्रमं वा]<BR>1 Regular, having a suitable<BR>measure, regularly shaped,<BR>symmetrical; वृत्तानुपूर्वे च न चातिदीर्घे<BR>Ku. 1. 35; ततोनुपूर्वायतवृत्तबाहुः<BR>Ki. 17. 50 (गोपुच्छाकार Malli.); जंघे<BR>अनुपूर्ववृत्ते Dk. 131; ˚ताम्रांगुली बाहुलते<BR>ibid.; ˚केश who has regular hair;<BR>˚गात्र having regularly shaped<BR>limbs; so ˚दंष्ट्र, ˚नाभि, पाणि.<BR>--2<BR>Orderly, successive, in due order or<BR>succession; coming in the order,<BR>following.<BR>--3 The lowest (<BR>निकृष्टप्रमाण); अनुपूर्वा इतरे Kāty.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज<BR>a. descended in a regular line.<BR>--वत्सा<BR>a cow that calves regularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्वशः
अनुपूर्वशः, --पूर्वेण adv. In<BR>regular order, one by one,<BR>successively, from above, downwards; from<BR>the beginning or first;<BR>वर्णानामनुपूर्वशः Ms. 8. 142; 3. 39, 7. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्वेण
अनुपूर्वशः, --पूर्वेण adv. In<BR>regular order, one by one,<BR>successively, from above, downwards; from<BR>the beginning or first;<BR>वर्णानामनुपूर्वशः Ms. 8. 142; 3. 39, 7. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपूर्व्य
अनुपूर्व्य a. Regular, orderly,<BR>successive.<BR>--र्वी = आनुपूर्वी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपृष्ठ्य
अनुपृष्ठ्य a. [अनुपृष्ठं बध्यते,<BR>अनुपृष्ठ-यत्] (A rope, cord &c.)<BR>Fastened along the back, tied<BR>lengthwise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुपेत
अनुपेत a.<BR>1 Not endowed with.<BR>--2 Not invested with the sacred<BR>thread (अनुपनीत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्त
अनुप्त a. Not sown(as seed);<BR>˚शस्य fallow, meadow, (ground &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्त्रिम
अनुप्त्रिम a. Grown without<BR>being sown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रज्ञानं|अनुप्रज्ञान
अनुप्रज्ञानं Tracing, tracking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रदानं|अनुप्रदान
अनुप्रदानं<BR>1 A gift, donation.<BR>--2<BR>A sort of external effort of the<BR>vocal organs giving rise to<BR>particular letters (बाह्यप्रयत्न); एते<BR>श्वासानुप्रदाना अघोषाश्च विबृण्वते Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रपातं|अनुप्रपात
अनुप्रपातं --दं ind. Going in<BR>succession; गेह ˚तं --दं आस्ते गेहं गेहं<BR>अनुप्रपातं-दं P. III. 4. 56 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रपादं|अनुप्रपाद
अनुप्रपातं --दं ind. Going in<BR>succession; गेह ˚तं --दं आस्ते गेहं गेहं<BR>अनुप्रपातं-दं P. III. 4. 56 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रयुज्
अनुप्रयुज् {c7c} A. To employ,<BR>apply, employ in addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रयोगः|अनुप्रयोग
अनुप्रयोगः Additional use,<BR>repetition; P. I. 3. 63; III. 4. 4-5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रवचनं|अनुप्रवचन
अनुप्रवचनं Repetition or<BR>reproduction of what has been said<BR>by the teacher; ˚आदि a class of<BR>words given in P. V. 1. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रविश्
अनुप्रविश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To enter into,<BR>join; पथिकसार्थं<BR>विदिशागामिनमनुप्रविष्टः M. 5; (fig. also); विश्रम्य<BR>लौकिकाः संस्त्यायमनुप्रविशंति Mv. 1 enter<BR>into familiar talk or conversation.<BR>--2 To accommodate or adapt<BR>oneself to; यस्य यस्य हि यो भावस्तस्य<BR>तस्य हि तं नरः । अनुप्रविश्य मेधावी<BR>क्षिप्रमात्मवशं नयेत् Pt. 1. 68; सखे<BR>वामदेव त्वमपि गाधिनंदनमनुप्रविष्टोऽसि A. R. 1<BR>you too share in his opinion, or<BR>think with him.<BR>--3 To follow<BR>in entering; sleep with.<BR>--4 To<BR>attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रवेशः|अनुप्रवेश
अनुप्रवेशः<BR>1 Entrance into; पुपोष<BR>वृद्धिं हरिदश्वदीधितेरनुप्रवेशादिव<BR>बालचंद्रमाः R. 3. 22; 10. 51.<BR>--2<BR>Adapting oneself to the will of;<BR>बलवताभिभूतस्य विदेशगमनं तदनुप्रवेशो वा<BR>नीतिः Pt. 1; भजते विदेशमधिकेन<BR>जितस्तदनुप्रवेशमथवा कुशलः Śi. 9. 48.<BR>--3 Imitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रश्नः|अनुप्रश्न
अनुप्रश्नः^1 A subsequent question<BR>(having reference to what the<BR>teacher has previously said).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: before and after words are 'anu'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रसक्तिः|अनुप्रसक्ति
अनुप्रसक्तिः f.<BR>1 Very close<BR>attachment.<BR>--2 Very close logical<BR>connection (of words).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रसद्
अनुप्रसद् Caus. To propitiate,<BR>conciliate; प्रियं V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रसादनं
अनुप्रसादनं Propitiation,<BR>conciliation; प्रिय ˚नं नाम व्रतं V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रस्थ
अनुप्रस्थ a. Latitudinal,<BR>following the breadth or latitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राण्
अनुप्राण् {c2c} P. To breathe after.<BR>--Caus. To animate, support, feed,<BR>help; mostly used in the<BR>statement of Alaṃkāras in a sentence;<BR>उत्प्रेक्षानुप्राणिता स्वभावोक्तिः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राणनं|अनुप्राणन
अनुप्राणनं Breathing after,<BR>animation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राप्
अनुप्राप् {c5c} P.<BR>1 To get, obtain.<BR>--2 To reach, go to, overtake;<BR>गंगानदीमनुप्राप्ताः Mb.<BR>--3 To imitate;<BR>लीलाखेलमनुप्रापुर्महोक्षास्तस्य विक्रमं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-a" target="_blank">Page0075-a+ 57</a>]<BR>R. 4. 22.<BR>--4 To arrive, come (intrans.);<BR>कथमिमां भूमिमनुप्राप्तः K. 132;<BR>Ve. 6.<BR>--5 To get back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राप्त
अनुप्राप्त p. p. Reached, got,<BR>obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्राप्तिः|अनुप्राप्ति
अनुप्राप्तिः f. Getting to, reaching,<BR>arriving &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्रासः|अनुप्रास
अनुप्रासः [अनुगतः रसाद्यनुगुणं<BR>प्रकृष्टमासं वर्णन्यासं समवर्णरचनां<BR>समवर्णोच्चारणं वा] Alliteration, repetition of<BR>similar letters, syllables or sounds;<BR>वर्णसाम्यमनुप्रासः K. P. 9; (<BR>स्वरवैसादृश्येऽपि व्यंजनसदृशत्वं वर्णसाम्यं रसाद्यनुगतः<BR>प्रकृष्टो न्यासः; अनुप्रासः शब्दसाम्यं वैषम्येपि<BR>स्वरस्य यत् S. D. 633.) अनुप्रास is<BR>of 5 kinds; (a) छेक˚ or single<BR>alliteration; बकुलगंधानंधीकुर्वन्,<BR>कावेरीवारिपावनः पवनः; मूर्ध्नामुद्वृत्तकृत्ताविरलगरल &c.<BR>K. P. 7. (b) वृत्ति˚ or harmonious. (c)<BR>श्रुति˚ or melodious. (d) अंत्य˚ or<BR>final; as मंदं हसंतः पुलकं वहंतः. (e)<BR>लाट˚; स्मेरराजीवनयने नयने किं निमीलिते.<BR>For definitions and examples see<BR>S. D. 633-38 and K. P. 9th Ullāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्लु
अनुप्लु {c1c} A. To run after, follow;<BR>इदमन्यतो वानरद्वयं आर्यस्य पार्ष्णिग्राहमिव<BR>संश्रयादनुप्लवते A. R. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुप्लवः|अनुप्लव
अनुप्लवः A follower, servant;<BR>सानुप्लवः प्रभुरपि क्षणदाचराणां R. 13. 75;<BR>Mv. 2, 7. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबंध्|अनुबन्ध्
अनुबंध् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To bind or fasten<BR>to, attach, tie, connect; सीमंतं<BR>निजमनुबध्नती कराभ्यां Śi. 8. 69 forming,<BR>arranging; उभयोरपि राजेंद्र<BR>संबंधेनानुबध्यतां (इक्ष्वाकुकुलं) Rām.; सखीजनानुबद्धां<BR>कथां Dk. 114 connected with.<BR>--2 (a) To have in the train (fig. also);<BR>न शिष्याननुबध्नीत Bhāg. (b) To bring<BR>about, cause, lead to, result in,<BR>produce as a consequence; नानुबध्नाति<BR>कुशलं Mb.; हे वृषल ते तथा विक्षेपोऽस्तु<BR>यथा हिंसामनुबध्नाति P. VI. 1. 141 com.<BR>--3 To press, importune, urge, request;<BR>पुनः पुनश्चानुबध्यमाना K. 69, 133, 207,<BR>233.<BR>--4 (a) To attend or follow<BR>closely, follow at the heels of,<BR>follow; को नु<BR>खल्वयमनुबध्यमानस्तपस्विनीभ्यामबालसत्त्वो बालः Ś. 7;<BR>मधुकरकुलैरनुबध्यमानं K. 139; दिष्ट्या तावदयमनंगो<BR>मामिव तमप्यनुबध्नाति K. 158, 194,<BR>319, 347; Ki. 6. 8; Mv. 7. 18;<BR>Śi. 5. 26. (b) To chase, pursue;<BR>तच्चानुबध्यमानं K. 120; अनुबध्नता तुरगमुखमिथुनं<BR>132. (c) To adhere or stick to,<BR>cling to; धन्या चित्रलेखा यामनुबध्नाति<BR>देवीप्रसादः K. 221. (d) To continue,<BR>take up; तदेवानुबध्यतां तपः 322; तान्येव<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-b" target="_blank">Page0075-b+ 58</a>]<BR>चिरपरिचितान्यक्षराणि मामनुबध्नंति U. 3<BR>v. l. for अनुरुंधंति;<BR>वैशंपायनागमनालापमेवानुबध्य K. 262. (e) To follow,<BR>succeed, come close upon; सत्योऽयं<BR>जनप्रवादो यद्विपद्विपदं संपत्संपदमनुबध्नातीति<BR>K. 73; see अनुबंधि below.<BR>--5 To foster,<BR>cherish, entertain, harbour; तेषु किं<BR>भवतः स्नेहमनुबध्नाति मानसं Mārk. P.<BR>--6<BR>To bear, endure; Ks. 49. 47.<BR>--7 Not<BR>to burst or break loose, hold or keep<BR>together; भंगेऽपि हि<BR>मृणालानामनुबध्नंति तंतवः H. 1. 95. --pass. To be<BR>related to or connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबद्ध
अनुबद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Bound, attached,<BR>tied to.<BR>--2 Following in the train,<BR>coming as a consequence;<BR>अनुबद्धार्थानर्थसंशयान् विचार्य Dk. 41.<BR>--3<BR>Connected with, related to, relating or<BR>belonging to.<BR>--4 Constantly sticking<BR>to, being in; continued, continuous;<BR>नित्यानुबद्धकुलवैरः Ve. 1;<BR>˚मुग्धकाकलीहसितं U. 3; ˚विजृंभकं K. 66;<BR>˚बिंदुभिरश्रुभिः 135 constantly flowing.<BR>--5<BR>Fixed upon, directed towards;<BR>कलहंस˚ वक्त्रायाः Dk. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबंधः|अनुबन्ध|अनुबन्धः
अनुबंधः<BR>1 Binding or fastening on,<BR>connection, attachment, tie (lit.<BR>& fig.); यस्यां<BR>मनश्चक्षुषोरनुबंधस्तस्यामृद्धिः Māl. 2; एतस्येदृशेन दर्शनेन कीदृशो<BR>मे हृदयानुबंधः इति न जानासि U. 3<BR>state of feeling; K. 257.<BR>--2<BR>Uninterrupted succession, unbroken<BR>sequence, continuous flow, continuity;<BR>series, chain; बाष्पं कुरु स्थिरतया<BR>विरतानुबंधं Ś. 4. 14; मरण˚ K. 236<BR>following up death, desire for dying;<BR>अनुबंधाद्विरमेद्वा K. 280; यदा<BR>नात्याक्षीदेवानुबंधं 309 (persistence in)<BR>following me, 317; वैर˚, मत्सर˚,<BR>Dk. 63, 161; मुच्यतां देवि शोकानुबंधः<BR>K. 63 continuous sorrow;<BR>दुर्लभजनप्रार्थना˚ Ratn. 1; 4. 16; सानुबंधाः कथं<BR>न स्युः संपदो मे निरापदः R. 1. 64<BR>continuous, uninterrupted;<BR>परिवृद्धरागमनुबंधसेवया R. 9. 69 continuous<BR>enjoyment; अयं सोऽर्थोऽनर्थानुबंधः संवृत्तः<BR>V. 5 giving rise to a chain of evils.<BR>--3 Descendants, posterity; सानुबंधा<BR>हता ह्यसि Rām.<BR>--4 Consequence,<BR>result (good or bad); आत्मदोषानुबंधेन<BR>K. 319 in consequence of; यदग्रे<BR>चानुबंधे च सुखं Bg. 18. 39, 25;<BR>अनुबंधमजानंतः कर्मणामविचक्षणाः Rām.<BR>--5<BR>Intention; design, motive, cause;<BR>अनुबंधं परिज्ञाय देशकालौ च तत्त्वतः ।<BR>सारापंराधौ चालोक्य दंडं दंड्येषु पातयेत्<BR>Ms. 8. 126; पाप˚ of evil designs.<BR>--6 An adjunct of a thing, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-c" target="_blank">Page0075-c+ 57</a>]<BR>secondary member (मुख्यानुयायि, अप्रधानं); a<BR>secondary symptom, symptomatic<BR>affection, attendant on the<BR>principal disease (वातपित्तादिदोषाणामप्राधान्यं);<BR>मूर्छानुबंधा विषमज्वराः Suśr.<BR>--7<BR>Connecting link or adjunct of a subject or<BR>topic; theme, matter of discussion;<BR>introductory reasons; (<BR>विषयप्रयोजनाधिकारिसंबंधः अनुबंधः) (an indispensable<BR>element of the Vedānta).<BR>--8 (Gram.)<BR>An indicatory syllable or letter<BR>intended to denote some peculiarity in<BR>the inflection, accent &c. of the<BR>word to which it is attached; as the<BR>ऌ in गमॢ, ण् in इण्; रिपुराप पराभवाय<BR>मध्यं प्रकृतिप्रत्यययोरिवानुबंधः Ki. 13. 19.<BR>--9 Offence, fault.<BR>--10 An obstacle,<BR>impediment; also the clog or<BR>encumbrance of a family; domestic<BR>ties or attachment.<BR>--11 A child or<BR>pupil who follows the example set<BR>by his parent or teacher (मुख्यानुयायी<BR>शिशुः).<BR>--12 Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--13 Repeated application or<BR>devotion (पौनः पुन्येन अभिनिवेश).<BR>--14<BR>Course, pursuit.<BR>--15 A small bit or<BR>part, a trifle.<BR>--16 The junction of a<BR>fraction (with an integer), as<BR>भागामुबंधपूर्णाकः.<BR>--17 Base, stem (प्रकृति).<BR>--धी<BR>[अनुबध्यते अतिश्वासेन व्याप्रियते अनया]<BR>1 Thirst.<BR>--2 Hickup.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबंधक|अनुबन्धक
अनुबंधक a. Connected, related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबंधनं|अनुबन्धन
अनुबंधनं Connection, succession,<BR>series &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबंधिन्|अनुबन्धिन्
अनुबंधिन् a. (oft. at the end of<BR>comp.)<BR>1 (a) Connected with,<BR>attached or related to; अहो<BR>सरसरमणीयानुबंधिनी स्त्रीजनकथा Māl. 1<BR>having for its contents or subject<BR>matter &c.; परिचर्यानुबंधी Dk. 101<BR>continuing. (b) Mixed or blended<BR>with; नीलकंठकलकेकानुबंधिना<BR>मंद्रहुंकृतेन मामनुमन्यते Māl. 9.<BR>--2 Followed<BR>by, accompanied with; having in<BR>its train, resulting in, having as a<BR>consequence; तदियमापत्समंततोऽ<BR>नर्थानुबंधिनी Dk. 60; अयमर्थोऽर्थानुबंधी 67;<BR>शास्त्रं शास्त्रांतरानुबंधि 156; दुःखं<BR>दुःखानुबंधि V. 4 one misfortune closely<BR>follows another, or misfortunes<BR>never come single; K. 349;<BR>Ki. 1. 20; Bg. 15. 2; गुणा गुणानुबंधित्वात्तस्य<BR>सप्रसवा इव R. 1. 22 being associated<BR>with.<BR>--3 Lasting, thriving,<BR>prosperous, growing apace, continuous,<BR>uninterrupted; अपि<BR>त्वदावर्जितवारिसंभृतं प्रवालमासामनुबंधि वीरुधां Ku. 5. 34;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">Page0076-a+ 56</a>]<BR>ऊर्ध्वं गतं यस्य न चानुबंधि R. 6. 77<BR>continuous, uninterrupted or<BR>all-pervading; K. 246, 393.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबंध्य|अनुबन्ध्य
अनुबंध्य a.<BR>1 Principal, chief,<BR>primary (which may receive an adjunct,<BR>as a root, a disease &c.).<BR>--2 [वधार्थं<BR>बंधः अनुबंधः कर्मणि ण्यत्] To be killed<BR>(as a bull), one of the three<BR>principal sacrificial animals at the ज्योतिष्टोम<BR>sacrifice; गौरनुबंध्यः K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबलं|अनुबल
अनुबलं [अनु पश्चात्स्थितं बलं] A<BR>rearguard, an auxiliary army following<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबुध्
अनुबुध् {c4c} A. To awake, to<BR>recollect; learn, obtain information of,<BR>know, be aware of; न सत्यमनुबुध्यते<BR>K. 104 does not perceive or<BR>recognise. --Caus.<BR>1 To remind, put in<BR>mind of; अये सम्यगनुबोधितोऽस्मि Ś. 1<BR>well reminded.<BR>--2 To advise,<BR>inform; इति शिष्येण किलान्वबोधयत्<BR>R. 8. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबोधः|अनुबोध
अनुबोधः<BR>1 An afterthought,<BR>recollection.<BR>--2 Reviving the scent of<BR>faded perfumes, replacing them<BR>when removed by bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुबोधनं|अनुबोधन
अनुबोधनं Recollection, reminding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुब्राह्मणं|अनुब्राह्मण
अनुब्राह्मणं A work resembling a<BR>Brāhmaṇa (ब्राह्मणसदृशो ग्रंथः<BR>P. IV. 2. 62 Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुब्राह्मणिन्
अनुब्राह्मणिन्, --क a. [तदधीते वेद वा इति<BR>इनिप्रत्ययः] One who learns or knows<BR>an अनुब्राह्मण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुब्राह्मणिक
अनुब्राह्मणिन्, --क a. [तदधीते वेद वा इति<BR>इनिप्रत्ययः] One who learns or knows<BR>an अनुब्राह्मण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभव|अनुभवः
अनुभव --भाव &c. See under अनुभू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाव|अनुभावः
अनुभव --भाव &c. See under अनुभू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाषणं|अनुभाषण
अनुभाषणं<BR>1 Repetition of an<BR>assertion to refute it.<BR>--2<BR>Repeating what has been said.<BR>--3<BR>Conversation, dialogue (अनु सह भाषणं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाषितृ
अनुभाषितृ a. Speaking in reply;<BR>R. 16. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभासः|अनुभास
अनुभासः A kind of crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभुज्
अनुभुज् {c7c} A. To enjoy,<BR>experience (good or bad things), suffer<BR>(as the due consequences of one's<BR>deeds); मेघमुक्तविशदां स चंद्रिकां<BR>अन्वभुंक्त R. 19. 39; सा<BR>मंडनान्मंडनमन्वभुंक्त Ku. 7. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभोगः|अनुभोग
अनुभोगः<BR>1 Enjoyment.<BR>--2 A<BR>grant of land in perpetuity for<BR>service done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभू
अनुभू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To enjoy; taste,<BR>experience, feel, have experience<BR>or knowledge of, notice, perceive<BR>(by the senses &c.); to suffer, bear,<BR>undergo (as misery &c.); अन्वभवं च<BR>मधुकर इव नवमालिकामार्द्रसुमनसं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-b" target="_blank">Page0076-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Dk. 121; असक्तः सुखमन्वभूत् R. 1. 21;<BR>Ku. 2. 45; R. 7. 28; आत्मकृतानां हि<BR>दोषाणामनुभवितव्यं फलमात्मनैव K. 121;<BR>अनुभवति हि मूर्ध्ना पादपस्तीव्रमुष्णं Ś. 5. 7;<BR>Ku. 4. 41; संवत्सरमात्रं प्रेष्यभावमनुभूय<BR>M. 5 undergoing the state of a<BR>servant; षष्ठमनुभवन् वर्षं K. 77 being<BR>in the sixth year, six years old.<BR>--2<BR>To learn, hear, understand;<BR>वेदान्नानुभवसि Ch. Up.<BR>--3 To try, test, put<BR>to the test; न त्वं तेनान्वभाविष्ठा<BR>नान्वभावि त्वयाप्यसौ । अनुभूता मया चासौ तेन<BR>चान्वभविष्यहं ॥ Bk. 5. 35.<BR>--4 To<BR>comprise, include, grasp; द्वे वामलके<BR>अनुभवति Ch. Up.<BR>--5 To come up with,<BR>arrive at, get, obtain (mostly Ved.<BR>in these senses). --Caus.<BR>1 To cause<BR>to enjoy, feel, or experience;<BR>अनुभावयितुं मन्ये यत्नः संप्रति मां विधेः Mu. 6. 15;<BR>स्नानभोजनादिकमनुभावितोस्मि Dk. 125;<BR>आमोदो न हि कस्तूर्याः शपथेनानुभाव्यते<BR>Bv. 1. 120.<BR>--2 To reflect on, meditate,<BR>think of; मनसा तमेव वृत्तांतमन्वभावयत्<BR>K. 176, 279.<BR>--3 To infer, know;<BR>तस्मात्परोक्षवृत्तीनां फलैः कर्मानुभाव्यते<BR>H. 4. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभवः|अनुभव
अनुभवः<BR>1 Direct perception or<BR>cognition, knowledge derived from<BR>personal observation or experiment,<BR>notion, apprehension, the impression<BR>on the mind not derived from<BR>memory, one of the kinds of<BR>knowledge; सर्वव्यवहारहेतुर्ज्ञानं बुद्धिः । सा द्विविधा<BR>स्मृतिरनुभवश्च । संस्कारमात्रजन्यं ज्ञानं स्मृतिः ।<BR>तद्भिन्नं ज्ञानमनुभवः which again is<BR>यथार्थ right & अयथार्थ wrong. See<BR>T. S. 34. (The Naiyāyikas recognize<BR>प्रत्यक्ष, अनुमान, उपमान and शाब्द as<BR>the four sources of knowledge;<BR>the Vedāntins and Mīmāṃsakas<BR>add two more अर्थापत्ति and<BR>अनुपलब्धि; the Vaiśeṣikas and Bauddhas<BR>admit the first two only, the<BR>Sāṃkhyas exclude उपमा, while the<BR>Cārvākas admit प्रत्यक्ष only. Other<BR>sections of philosophical schools<BR>add three more to the six sources<BR>of knowledge recognised by the<BR>Mīmāṃsakas;<BR>--संभव ‘equivalence’;<BR>ऐतिह्य ‘fallible testimony’, and चेष्टा<BR>‘gesture’.)<BR>--2 Experience; अनुभवं<BR>वचसा सखि लुंपसि N. 4. 105<BR>--3<BR>Understanding.<BR>--4 Result, consequence.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सिद्ध a. established by<BR>experience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभावः|अनुभाव
अनुभावः<BR>1 Dignity, consequence<BR>or dignity of person, majestic<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-c" target="_blank">Page0076-c+ 57</a>]<BR>lustre, splendour, might, power,<BR>authority; (परिमेयपुरःसरौ)<BR>अनुभावविशेषात्तु सेनापरिवृताविव R. 1. 37;<BR>संभावनीयानुभावा अस्याकृतिः Ś. 7;<BR>अनुभावसौभाग्यमात्रपरिशेषधूसरश्रीः U. 1, 3;<BR>6. 20, 41, 4. 22, K. 108, 240; V. 1;<BR>Ki. 1. 6; Dk. 29, 113; Mv. 6. 53;<BR>अहो महानुभावः पार्थिवो दुष्यंतः Ś. 3 of<BR>great might or power; जाने वो<BR>रक्षसाक्रांतावनुभावपराक्रमौ R. 10. 38,<BR>2. 75 greatness (dignity) &c., valour;<BR>Ki. 6. 28; महानुभावप्रकृतिः कापि<BR>तत एवागतवती Māl. 1 very noble or<BR>dignified.<BR>--2 (In Rhet.) An<BR>external manifestation or indication of<BR>a feeling (भाव) by appropriate<BR>symptoms, such as by look, gesture<BR>&c., called by some ensuant (<BR>भावबोधक-न); भावं मनोगतं साक्षात् स्वगतं<BR>व्यंजयंति ये तेऽनुभावा इति ख्याताः; यथा<BR>भ्रूभंगः कोपस्य व्यंजकः; उद्बुद्धं कारणं स्वैः<BR>स्वैर्बहिर्भावं प्रकाशयन् । लोके यः कार्यरूपः<BR>सोऽनुभावः काव्यनाट्ययोः ॥ S. D. 162,<BR>163 &c.; धिगेव रमणीयतां<BR>त्वदनुभावभावादृते Māl. 9. 35.<BR>--3 Firm opinion or<BR>resolution, determination, belief;<BR>अनुभाववता गुरुस्थिरत्वात् Ki. 13. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभावक
अनुभावक a. Causing to<BR>understand, making one apprehend,<BR>indicative; ˚ता understanding,<BR>knowledge; यत्पदेन विना<BR>यस्याननुभावकता भवेत् Bhāṣā P. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभावनं|अनुभावन
अनुभावनं Indication of feelings<BR>by signs, gestures &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभाविन्
अनुभाविन् a.<BR>1 Perceiving,<BR>knowing, showing signs of feeling.<BR>--2<BR>An eye-witness; अनुभावी तु यः<BR>कश्चित्कुर्यात्साक्ष्यं विवादिनां Ms. 8. 69.<BR>--3 Being or coming after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभू
अनुभू a. [भू-क्विप्] Perceiving,<BR>understanding.<BR>--भूः f. Experience,<BR>direct knowledge or perception;<BR>अयमात्मा सर्वानुभूः Bṛ. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभूतिः|अनुभूति
अनुभूतिः f.<BR>1 Perception,<BR>apprehension, experience.<BR>--2 (In Nyāya)<BR>Knowledge derived from four<BR>sources: namely direct perception,<BR>inference, comparison, and verbal<BR>knowledge; see Bhāṣā P. 51-52.<BR>--3<BR>Dignity, consequence.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रकाशः N. of the gloss or<BR>paraphrase of the principal Upaniṣads<BR>by Mādhavācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभृ
अनुभृ {c1c} {c3c} P. To praise<BR>conformably; to throw or commit into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभर्तृ
अनुभर्तृ m. Praising conformably,<BR>imitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुभ्रातृ
अनुभ्रातृ m. A younger brother<BR>(अनुगतो भ्रातरं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमद्
अनुमद् {c1c} P. Ved. To rejoice<BR>over, gladden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमत्त
अनुमत्त p. p. Intoxicated with joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमाद्य
अनुमाद्य pot. p. To be praised in<BR>succession, to be granted with praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमन्
अनुमन् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To agree or<BR>consent to, comply with, approve,<BR>sanction, grant; to permit, allow; तत्र<BR>नाहमनुमंतुमुत्सहे मोघवृत्ति कलभस्य<BR>चेष्टितम् R. 11. 39; M. 1. 12; राजन्यान्<BR>स्वपुरनिवृत्तयेऽनुमेने R. 4. 87; 14. 20; शुश्रूषमाणां<BR>गिरिशोनुमेने Ku. 1. 59, 3. 60, 5. 68;<BR>कृताभिमर्षामनुमन्यमानः सुतां Ś. 5. 20;<BR>इमां स्वसारं च यवीयसीं मे कुमुद्वतीं नार्हसि<BR>नानुमंतुं R. 16. 85 be pleased not to<BR>reject or refuse; Bh. 3. 22.<BR>--2 To<BR>follow, have recourse to;<BR>धर्मार्थावभिसंत्यज्य संरभं योनुमन्यते Mb. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To ask for leave or permission; ask<BR>the consent of; अनुमान्यतां महाराजः<BR>V. 2 ask for leave to go; take counsel<BR>with; भूयोऽपि सखीजनमनुमानयिष्यामि<BR>Ś. 3.<BR>--2 To ask for, request or beg;<BR>Y. 1. 240.<BR>--3 To honour.<BR>--4 To put<BR>to account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमत|अनुमतः
अनुमत p. p.<BR>1 Approved,<BR>assented to, agreed to, permitted, allowed,<BR>granted &c.; कृतमनुमतं दृष्टं वा यौरिदं<BR>गुरुपातकं Ve. 3. 22; ˚गमना Ś. 4. 9<BR>allowed to depart; अनुमतो गृहाय<BR>R. 5. 10; उभय˚तः साक्षी Y. 2. 72<BR>admitted by both parties &c.<BR>--2 Liked,<BR>beloved, pleasant, loved, agreeable,<BR>desired by, dear to; वृष्टिं च<BR>कर्षकजनानुमतां करोति Bṛ. S. 5. 72.<BR>--3 Being<BR>of one opinion, agreeing or<BR>concurring with.<BR>--तः A lover;<BR>घनमतो नमतोनुमतान् प्रियाः Śi. 6. 65.<BR>--तं<BR>Consent, approval, permission; प्रथमं<BR>कस्यानुमते चोरितमेतत्त्वया हृदयं V. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमतिः|अनुमति
अनुमतिः f.<BR>1 Permission, consent,<BR>approval, assent.<BR>--2 The 15th day<BR>of the moon's age on which she<BR>rises one digit less than full, when<BR>the gods and manes receive oblations<BR>with favour; personified as a<BR>goddess or worshipped in the<BR>Rājasūya sacrifice (कलाहीनचंद्रवती<BR>शुक्लचतुर्दशीयुतपूर्णिमातिथिः); अनुमत्यै हविरष्टाकपालं<BR>पुरोडाश निर्वपति Śat. Br.; Ms. 3. 86-87.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रं a deed expressing<BR>assent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमननं|अनुमनन
अनुमननं<BR>1 Assent; sufferance.<BR>--2<BR>Independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमंतृ|अनुमन्तृ
अनुमंतृ a. Consenting to,<BR>permitting, allowing, suffering (opp. to<BR>active agent); Bg. 13. 22;<BR>Ms. 5. 51 adviser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमंत्र्|अनुमन्त्र्
अनुमंत्र् {c10c} A. To consecrate or<BR>accompany with sacred hymns or<BR>magical formulas; to dismiss with<BR>sacred and auspicious words,<BR>dismiss with a blessing; विसृष्टश्च<BR>वामदेवानुमंत्रितोऽश्वः U. 2 (v. l. for<BR>अभिमंत्रित); रथमारोप्य कृष्णेन यत्र कर्णोऽ<BR>नुमंत्रितः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमंत्रणं|अनुमन्त्रण|अनुमंत्रण
अनुमंत्रणं Consecration by hymns<BR>and prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमरणं|अनुमरण
अनुमरणं See under अनुमृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमरुः|अनुमरु
अनुमरुः A country next to a<BR>desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमा
अनुमा {c3c} A., {c2c} P.<BR>1 To infer, (as<BR>from some signs, premises &c.);<BR>अलिंगां प्रकृतिं त्वाहुर्लिंगैरनुमिमीमहे Mb.;<BR>conclude, guess, conjecture;<BR>धूमादग्निमनुमाय T. S. 41; पर्याकुलत्वान्मरुतां<BR>वेगभंगोऽनुमीयते Ku. 2. 25;<BR>R. 15. 77, 17. 11; तेजोविशेषानुमितां दधानः<BR>2. 7, 68; 5. 12; Ki. 5. 47.<BR>--2 To<BR>reconcile, equal. --Caus. (-मापयति)<BR>To lead one to infer or guess,<BR>bespeak, indicate;<BR>आकृतिरेवानुमापयत्यमानुषतां K. 132, 202.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमा
अनुमा [मा-अङ्] Inference,<BR>conclusion from given premises; see<BR>अनुमिति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमातृ
अनुमातृ a. One who infers; न हि<BR>करिणि दृष्टे चीत्कारेण तमनुमिमतेऽनुमातारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमानं|अनुमान
अनुमानं<BR>1 Inferring as the<BR>instrument of an अनुमिति, conclusion from<BR>given premises; an inference,<BR>conclusion; one of the four means of<BR>obtaining knowledge according to the<BR>Nyāya system; (अनुमितिकरणमनुमानं तच्च<BR>धूमो वह्निव्याप्य इति व्याप्तिज्ञानं. It is of two<BR>kinds स्वार्थानुमानं & परार्थानुमानं); प्रत्यक्षं<BR>चानुमानं च शास्त्रं च विविधागमं । त्रयं<BR>सुविदितं कार्यं धर्मशुद्धिमभीप्सता ॥<BR>Ms. 12. 105.<BR>--2 A guess, conjecture, sign to<BR>know; इंगितैरनुमानैश्च मया ज्ञेया भविष्यति<BR>Rām.<BR>--3 Analogy, similarity; आत्मनो<BR>हृदयानुमानेन प्रेक्षसे Ś. 5 you judge (of<BR>others) by the analogy of your own<BR>heart; स्वानुमानात्कादंबरीमुत्प्रेक्ष्य<BR>K. 305.<BR>--4 (In Rhet.) A figure which<BR>consists in a notion, expressed<BR>in a peculiarly striking manner,<BR>of a thing established by proof;<BR>S. D. 711; यत्र पतत्यबलानां दृष्टिर्निशिताः<BR>पतंति तत्र शराः । तच्चापरोपितशरो धावत्यासां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">Page0077-c+ 56</a>]<BR>पुरः स्मरो मन्ये ॥ अनुमानं तदुक्तं<BR>यत्साध्यसाधनयोर्वचः K. P. 10.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्ति f.<BR>reasoning; logical inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमापक
अनुमापक a. (पिका f.) Causing an<BR>inference as an effect, being the<BR>ground of an inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमितिः|अनुमिति
अनुमितिः f. Inference from given<BR>premises; the knowledge obtained<BR>by means of अनुमान; लिङ्गपरामर्शजन्यं^1<BR>ज्ञानमनुमितिः the knowledge that arises<BR>from deduction or syllogistic<BR>reasoning.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by @aumsanskrit on 20240826. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/101  ap90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमित्सा
अनुमित्सा Desire of inferring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमेय
अनुमेय pot. p. Inferable, to be<BR>inferred; फलानुमेयाः प्रारंभाः R. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमार्गं|अनुमार्ग
अनुमार्गं adv. Along the way,<BR>according to a (particular) way, on<BR>or in the way; अनुमार्गागतया<BR>K. 100 come by this way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमाषं|अनुमाष
अनुमाषं adv. Like a kidney<BR>bean or in it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमासः|अनुमास|अनुमासं
अनुमासः [अनुगतो मासः] The<BR>following month.<BR>--सं ind. Every<BR>month, month after month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमुद्
अनुमुद् {c1c} A. (P. in epic poetry)<BR>1 To rejoice with, join in rejoicing or<BR>sympathizing with; मुदितामनुमोदते<BR>Bhāg.<BR>--2 To express approval; तदेव<BR>राममातृभिरनुमोदितं U. 2; approve,<BR>second, applaud; निषेद्धुमासीदनुमोदितुं<BR>वा R. 14. 43; to allow with<BR>pleasure, permit; अनुमोदितमाचार्यैः K. 77;<BR>अननुमोदितामात्रा 160. --Caus. To<BR>gladden, delight, favour, permit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमोदः|अनुमोद
अनुमोदः<BR>1 The feeling of pleasure<BR>arising from sympathy, subsequent<BR>pleasure.<BR>--2 = अनुमोदनं see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमोदनं|अनुमोदन
अनुमोदनं<BR>1 Approval, assent,<BR>seconding, acceptance, compliance.<BR>--2 Causing pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमृ
अनुमृ {c6c} A. To follow in death;<BR>रुदता कुत एव सा पुनर्भवता नानुमृतापि<BR>लभ्यते R. 8. 85 followed in death by<BR>you; गतिविभ्रमसादनीरवा न शुचा<BR>नानुमृतेव लक्ष्यते 58 (used actively).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुमरणं|अनुमरण
अनुमरणं Following in death;<BR>तन्मरणे चानुमरणं करिष्यामीति मे निश्चयः H. 3;<BR>post-cremation of a widow (अनुमरणं<BR>हि भर्तुर्देशांतरादिमरणे देहाद्यलाभ एव);<BR>देशांतरमृते पत्यौ साध्वी तत्पादुकाद्वयं । निधायोरसि<BR>संशुद्धा प्रविशेज्जातवेदसं ॥ This is allowed<BR>to Kṣatriya, Vaiśya and other<BR>women, but not to Brāhmaṇa women;<BR>पृथक् चितां समारुह्य न विप्रा गंतुमर्हति. Bāṇa<BR>severely condemns this practice; see<BR>K. 173-4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुया
अनुया {c2c} P.<BR>1 To follow, go after<BR>(fig. also); अनुयाहि साधुपदवीं<BR>Bh. 2. 77; अनुयास्यन्मुनितनयां Ś. 1. 29;<BR>त्वामनुयामि यद्यपि Ku. 4. 21.<BR>--2 To imitate,<BR>equal; न किलानुययुस्तस्य राजानो<BR>रक्षितुर्यशः R. 1. 27; 9. 6; अनुयातलीलः<BR>16. 71; Śi. 12. 3 followed and<BR>imitated.<BR>--3 To attend, accompany; इयं<BR>मुसलमनुयाति कलेन हुंकृतेन Mu. 1. 4;<BR>अनुयातारुंधतीको वसिष्ठः U. 3. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुया
अनुया a. Following.<BR>--याः Ved.<BR>Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयातृ
अनुयातृ m. A follower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयात्रं|अनुयात्र
अनुयात्रं --त्रा Retinue, train;<BR>attendance upon; following; त्यक्तभोगस्य मे<BR>राजन् वने वन्येन जीवतः । किं<BR>कार्यमनुयात्रेण Rām.<BR>--त्रं adv. In or after a<BR>procession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयात्रा
अनुयात्रं --त्रा Retinue, train;<BR>attendance upon; following; त्यक्तभोगस्य मे<BR>राजन् वने वन्येन जीवतः । किं<BR>कार्यमनुयात्रेण Rām.<BR>--त्रं adv. In or after a<BR>procession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयात्रिकः|अनुयात्रिक
अनुयात्रिकः [अनुयात्रा अनुगमनमस्त्यस्य<BR>ठन्] A follower, attendant; Ś. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयानं|अनुयान
अनुयानं Following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयायिन्
अनुयायिन् a. [P. III. 2. 78]<BR>1<BR>Following; attending, consequent.<BR>--2<BR>Like, similar.<BR>--3 Following a<BR>principal person as a teacher (मुख्यस्य<BR>अनुगंता शिशुः). --m. A follower (lit. &<BR>fig.); रामानुजानुयायिनः followers of<BR>the doctrines of R.; a dependent or<BR>attendant; न्यषेधि शेषोऽप्यनुयायिवर्गः<BR>R. 2. 4, 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयाजः|अनुयाज
अनुयाजः [यज्-घञ्, कुत्वाभावः<BR>P. VII. 3. 62] A part of a sacrificial<BR>ceremony (यज्ञांगं); secondary or<BR>supplementary sacrificial rite; usually<BR>written अनूयाज q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुज्
अनुयुज् {c7c} A.<BR>1 To ask, question;<BR>किं वस्तु विद्वन्गुरवे प्रदेयं त्वया कियद्वेति<BR>तमन्वयुंक्त R. 5. 18; अन्वयुंक्त गुरुमीश्वरः<BR>क्षितेः 11. 62; Śi. 13. 68.<BR>--2 To<BR>examine (as an accused), put on<BR>trial; Ms. 8. 79, 259.<BR>--3 To impart<BR>or give, as instruction.<BR>--4 To order,<BR>enjoin.<BR>--5 To select as husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुक्त|अनुयुक्तः
अनुयुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Asked,<BR>questioned, examined, ordered &c.<BR>--2<BR>Censured, reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयुक्तिन्
अनुयुक्तिन् a. [अस्त्यर्थे इनि] One<BR>who has ordered, examined; cf.<BR>गृहीतिन्, अधीतिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोक्तृ
अनुयोक्तृ m. An examiner,<BR>interrogator; inquirer; a teacher,<BR>especially hired or mercenary (भृतकाध्यापक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोगः|अनुयोग
अनुयोगः<BR>1 A question, inquiry,<BR>examination; अनियंत्रणानुयोगस्तपस्विजनः<BR>Ś. 1; निगृह्यानुयोगे P. VIII. 2. 94;<BR>वार्ता˚मधुराक्षरया च वाचा R. 13. 71.<BR>--2<BR>Censure, reproof.<BR>--3 Solicitation.<BR>--4<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-b" target="_blank">Page0078-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Exertion, effort; अनुयोगं विना तैलं<BR>तिलानां नोपजायते Pt. 2. 140.<BR>--5<BR>Religious meditation; spiritual union.<BR>--6 Comment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत् {1}<BR>an interrogator. {2} a teacher,<BR>spiritual preceptor (अनुयोगं कृंतति<BR>प्रश्नविषयसंशयं छिनत्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोगिन्
अनुयोगिन् a.<BR>1 What combines or<BR>unites; connected with, situated in<BR>or on.<BR>--2 Examining, questioning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोज्य|अनुयोज्यं|अनुयोज्यः
अनुयोज्य pot. p. Fit to be<BR>questioned, asked; asked with a reproof.<BR>--ज्यः A servant; obedient and<BR>humble servant; उभाभ्यामपि<BR>वासवानुयोज्यो दुष्यंतः प्रणमति Ś. 7; Ms. 8. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुयोजनं|अनुयोजन
अनुयोजनं A question, inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरंज्|अनुरञ्ज्
अनुरंज् {c4c} U.<BR>1 To be red;<BR>भृशमन्वरज्यदतुषारकरः Śi. 9. 7 (became red<BR>or attached).<BR>--2 To be delighted, find<BR>pleasure; तव प्रकीर्त्या<BR>जगत्प्रहृष्यत्यनुरज्यते च Bg. 11. 36.<BR>--3 To be<BR>attached or devoted to, be fond of,<BR>love, like (with acc. or loc.);<BR>समस्थमनुरज्यंति विषमस्थं त्यजंति च Rām.;<BR>अशुद्धप्रकृतौ राज्ञि जनता नानुरज्यते<BR>Pt. 1. 301; भ्रातुर्मृतस्य भार्यायां योऽनुरज्येत<BR>कामतः Ms. 3. 173. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>make red, redden, dye, colour;<BR>सरसकिसलयानुरंजितैर्वा Śi. 7. 64, 8. 17,<BR>12. 68; Dk. 168; Ki. 12. 23, 4. 27.<BR>--2 To attach oneself to, please,<BR>gratify, conciliate, keep contented<BR>or satisfied; अनुरक्तः प्रजाभिश्च<BR>प्रजाश्चाप्यन्वरंजयत् Rām.; कंष्टं जनः<BR>कुलधनैरनुरंजनीयः U. 1. 14;<BR>शिष्यगुणानुरांजितमनसं Pt. 1 pleased, gratified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरक्त|अनुरक्तः
अनुरक्त p. p.<BR>1 Reddened, dyed,<BR>coloured; कुंडलमणिप्रभानुरक्तगंडस्थलः<BR>K. 170.<BR>--2 Pleased, contented;<BR>loved, beloved; loyal, loyally<BR>devoted; अनुरक्तः शुचिर्दक्षः Ms. 7. 64;<BR>गुणानुरक्तामनुरक्तसाधनः Ki. 1. 31<BR>having all means favourable to him;<BR>˚प्रजः --लोकः beloved by people;<BR>attached or devoted to, fond of (with loc.<BR>or acc.); अपि वृषलमनुरक्ताः प्रकृतयः<BR>--अथ किम् - चंद्रगुप्ते दृढमनुरक्ताः प्रकृतयः<BR>Mu. 1; कथं वसंतसेना<BR>आर्यचारुदत्तमनुरक्ता Mk. 1; एषा भवंतमनुरक्ता<BR>Ś. 6. 18; अलभ्यमनुरक्तवान् कथय किंनु<BR>नारीजनं Mu. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरक्तिः|अनुरक्ति
अनुरक्तिः f. Love, attachment,<BR>devotion, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरंजक|अनुरञ्जक
अनुरंजक a. Gratifying, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरंजनं|अनुरञ्जन|अनुरञ्जनं
अनुरंजनं Conciliating, satisfying,<BR>gratifying, pleasing, keeping<BR>contented; युक्तः प्रजानामनुरंजने स्याः U. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरंजित|अनुरञ्जित
अनुरंजित p. p. Pleased,<BR>conciliated, kept contented &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराग|अनुरागः
अनुराग a. Become red, reddened.<BR>--गः<BR>1 Redness.<BR>--2 Devotion,<BR>attachment, contentment, loyalty (opp.<BR>अपरागः); love, affection, passion<BR>(with loc. or in comp.);<BR>आविर्भूतानुरागाः Mu. 4. 21; कंटकितेन प्रथयति<BR>मय्यनुरागं कपोलेन Ś. 3. 15; R. 3. 10;<BR>˚इंगितं a gesture or external sign<BR>expressive of love; प्रसादस्तु शब्दः<BR>स्यादनुरागजः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागिन्
अनुरागिन्, अनुरागवत् a.<BR>1<BR>Attached, enamoured, impassioned,<BR>inspired with love; स<BR>वृद्धस्तस्यामतीवानुरागवान् H. 1; सा केनापि वणिक्पुत्रेण<BR>सहानुरागवती बभूव ibid.<BR>--2 Causing or<BR>inspiring love.<BR>--णी Personification<BR>of a musical note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरागवत्|अनुरागवन्त्
अनुरागिन्, अनुरागवत् a.<BR>1<BR>Attached, enamoured, impassioned,<BR>inspired with love; स<BR>वृद्धस्तस्यामतीवानुरागवान् H. 1; सा केनापि वणिक्पुत्रेण<BR>सहानुरागवती बभूव ibid.<BR>--2 Causing or<BR>inspiring love.<BR>--णी Personification<BR>of a musical note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरणनं|अनुरणन
अनुरणनं<BR>1 Sounding<BR>conformably to; a continuous tinkling echo<BR>produced by the sounds of bells,<BR>anklets &c.<BR>--2 The power of words<BR>called व्यंजन q. v.; the meaning<BR>suggested by what is actually stated;<BR>क्रमलक्ष्यत्वादेवानुरणनरूपो यो व्यंग्यः S. D. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरतिः|अनुरति
अनुरतिः f. Love, attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरथ्या
अनुरथ्या [रथ्यामन्वायतं स्थिता] A<BR>foot-path, a by-road, the margin of a<BR>street, (a path along the margin of a<BR>road); प्रकाशीकरणार्थं च निशागमनशंकया ।<BR>दीपवृक्षांस्तथा चक्रुरनुरथ्यासु सर्वशः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरसित|अनुरसितं
अनुरसित a. Sounding, echoing;<BR>उद्ग्रीवैरनुरसितस्य पुष्करस्य M. 1. 21<BR>accompanied in sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरसः|अनुरस
अनुरसः, --रसितं Echo, reverberation;<BR>˚गुरु magnified by echo; U. 2. 21;<BR>Māl. 9. 6; Mv. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरसितं|अनुरसित
अनुरसः, --रसितं Echo, reverberation;<BR>˚गुरु magnified by echo; U. 2. 21;<BR>Māl. 9. 6; Mv. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरसः|अनुरस
अनुरसः [अनुगतो रसं]<BR>1 A secondary<BR>feeling (in Rhet.).<BR>--2 A secondary<BR>flavour; लवण˚ saltish taste; मधुरानुरसं<BR>रूक्षं लवणानुरसं लघु । नार्यास्तु मधुरं स्तन्यं<BR>कषायानुरसं हिमं Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरहस
अनुरहस a. [अनुगतं रहः] Secret,<BR>solitary, private.<BR>--सं adv. In secret,<BR>apart, privately; Śi. 7. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरात्र
अनुरात्र a. Following the night.<BR>--त्रं adv. In the night; every night,<BR>night after night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुराध|अनुराधः
अनुराध a.<BR>1 Causing welfare; also<BR>written as अनूराध; इंद्रं वयमनूराधं हवामहे<BR>Av.<BR>--2 Born under the asterism<BR>अनुराधा P. IV. 3. 34.<BR>--धा [अनुगता राधां<BR>विशाखां] N. of the 17th of the 27 lunar<BR>mansions or asterisms (so called<BR>because it follows राधा or विशाखा). It<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-a" target="_blank">Page0079-a+ 57</a>]<BR>consists of four stars.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रामः,<BR>--पुरं the ancient capital of Laṅkā or<BR>Ceylon; also called अनुरोधपुर,<BR>described by Rājaśekhara as full of<BR>curiosities. It is a large town in the north<BR>of Ceylon “with 1600 square granite<BR>pillars which supported the floor of<BR>an enormous monastery called ‘The<BR>Great Brazen Palace’ said to have<BR>been built in 161 B. C.”<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुद्
अनुरुद् {c2c} P. To weep along with,<BR>condole with, sympathize;<BR>गुरुशोकामनुरोदितीव मां Ku. 4. 15; अनुरोदितीव<BR>करुणेन पत्रिणां Śi. 4. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोदनं|अनुरोदन
अनुरोदनं Condolence, sympathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुध्
अनुरुध् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To obstruct, block<BR>up; शिलाभिर्ये मार्गमनुरुंधंति Mb.; to<BR>surround, hem in; रुद्रानुचरैर्मखो महान्…<BR>अन्वरुध्यत Bhāg.<BR>--2 To bind, fasten.<BR>--3 To stick or adhere to, follow<BR>closely, observe, practise;<BR>अनुरुध्यादघं त्र्यहं Ms. 5. 63 should observe<BR>impurity (be in mourning);<BR>पुमांसमनुरुध्य जाता पुमनुजा P. III. 2. 100<BR>Sk. born immediately after a male.<BR>--4 To love, be fond of, or devoted<BR>to, attach oneself to; समस्थमनुरुध्यंते<BR>विषमस्थं त्यजंति च Rām.;<BR>सद्वृत्तिमनुरुध्यंतां भवंतः Mv. 2 follow or adopt;<BR>स्वधर्ममनुरुंधंते नातिक्रमं Ki. 11. 78;<BR>नानुरोत्स्ये जगल्लक्ष्मीं Bk. 16. 23 love,<BR>like.<BR>--5 To conform to, obey,<BR>follow, adapt oneself to, act up to;<BR>नियतिं लोक इवानुरुध्यते Ki. 2. 12;<BR>हंत तिर्यंचोऽपि परिचयमनुरुध्यंते U. 3<BR>remember or cherish (act up to it);<BR>मद्वचनमनुरुध्यते वा भवान् K. 181, 298;<BR>वात्सल्यमनुरुध्यंते महात्मनः Mv. 6 feel<BR>the force of compassion; तेनापि रावणे<BR>मैत्रीमनुरुध्य व्यपेक्ष्यते Mv. 5. 35<BR>following up; यदि गुरुष्वनुरुध्यसे Mv. 3<BR>regard with respect, obey; अनुरुध्यस्व<BR>भगवतो वसिष्ठस्यादेशं U. 4;<BR>चंद्रकेतोर्वचनं U. 5.<BR>--6 To coax, gratify, flatter,<BR>soothe; इत्यादिभिः प्रियशतैरनुरुध्य मुग्धां<BR>U. 3. 26; अभिनवसेवकजनेऽपि<BR>एवमनुरुध्यते K. 207 please by carefully<BR>attending to &c., show regard for; 248.<BR>--7<BR>To urge, press, entreat, request;<BR>आगमनाय अनुरुध्यमानः K. 277; तया<BR>चाहमनुरुध्यमानस्तां बकुलमालां दत्तवान् Māl. 1;<BR>सा च भीमधन्वना बलवदनुरुद्धा Dk. 122<BR>courted, wooed.<BR>--8 To assent or agree<BR>to, approve; like, comply with;<BR>प्रकृतयो न मे व्यसनमनुरुध्यंते Dk. 106; यदि<BR>भगवाननुरुध्यते Mv. 4 agree with me.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरुध्
अनुरुध् a. [रुध-क्विप्]<BR>1 One who<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">Page0079-b+ 56</a>]<BR>obeys, conforms to &c.<BR>--2 Obeyed,<BR>observed, practised, wanted (अपेक्षित),<BR>written as अनूरुध् Rv. 3. 55. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधः|अनुरोध
अनुरोधः --धनं<BR>1 Compliance,<BR>gratification, fulfilling one's wishes &c.<BR>--2 Conformity, accordance,<BR>obedience, regard, consideration;<BR>धर्मानुरोधात् K. 160, 180, 192; अत्र नानुरोधं<BR>तर्कये Mv. 7 pleasure or gratification;<BR>आधारानुरोधात् Mu. 1. 2 out of<BR>regard for; कविश्रमानुरोधाद्वा Ve. 1 in<BR>consideration of; Mv. 5, 3. 28;<BR>तदनुरोधात् --धेन accordingly, in<BR>accordance with it;<BR>वदेद्विपश्चिन्महतोनुरोधात् Pt. 1. 100 after great<BR>consideration; humouring H. 2. 103;<BR>reference (of a rule.)<BR>--3 Pressing,<BR>urging, coaxing; entreaty,<BR>solicitation, request; क इवात्रानुरोधः K. 209;<BR>तदनुरोधात् 135; विनानुरोधात्स्वहितेच्छयैव<BR>Śi. 20. 81.<BR>--4 Bearing of a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधनं|अनुरोधन
अनुरोधः --धनं<BR>1 Compliance,<BR>gratification, fulfilling one's wishes &c.<BR>--2 Conformity, accordance,<BR>obedience, regard, consideration;<BR>धर्मानुरोधात् K. 160, 180, 192; अत्र नानुरोधं<BR>तर्कये Mv. 7 pleasure or gratification;<BR>आधारानुरोधात् Mu. 1. 2 out of<BR>regard for; कविश्रमानुरोधाद्वा Ve. 1 in<BR>consideration of; Mv. 5, 3. 28;<BR>तदनुरोधात् --धेन accordingly, in<BR>accordance with it;<BR>वदेद्विपश्चिन्महतोनुरोधात् Pt. 1. 100 after great<BR>consideration; humouring H. 2. 103;<BR>reference (of a rule.)<BR>--3 Pressing,<BR>urging, coaxing; entreaty,<BR>solicitation, request; क इवात्रानुरोधः K. 209;<BR>तदनुरोधात् 135; विनानुरोधात्स्वहितेच्छयैव<BR>Śi. 20. 81.<BR>--4 Bearing of a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधिन्
अनुरोधिन्, --धक a. Compliant,<BR>complying with, obeying or<BR>conforming to, having regard to,<BR>caring for; पतिव्रतानां समयानुरोधिनी Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरोधक
अनुरोधिन्, --धक a. Compliant,<BR>complying with, obeying or<BR>conforming to, having regard to,<BR>caring for; पतिव्रतानां समयानुरोधिनी Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूप|अनुरूपः
अनुरूप a. [रूपस्य सदृशः योग्यो वा]<BR>1 Like, resembling, corresponding to;<BR>शब्दानुरूपेण पराक्रमेण भवितव्यं Pt. 1;<BR>worthy of; आत्मानुरूपं वरं Ś. 1;<BR>रूपानुरूप K. 192, 203.<BR>--2 Suitable or fit,<BR>adapted to, according to; with gen.<BR>or in comp.; नैतदनुरूपं भवतः K. 146,<BR>158; भव पितुरनुरूपस्त्वं गुणैर्लोककांतैः<BR>V. 5. 21; काममननुरूपमस्या वपुषो<BR>वल्कलं Ś. 1; स्वप्रमाणानुरूपैः सेचनघटैः ibid.;<BR>Bg. 17. 3; R. 1. 33; Me. 13.<BR>--पं<BR>1 Resemblance, likeness,<BR>conformity.<BR>--2 Suitability, fitness; U. 6. 26.<BR>--पः The antistrophe, having the<BR>same metre as the स्तोत्रिय or strophe;<BR>the second of the three verses (तृच)<BR>recited together, the other two being<BR>स्तोत्रिय and पर्यास; एकस्तोत्रियेष्वहस्सु योऽ<BR>न्योऽनंतरः सोऽनुरूपः Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपतः
अनुरूपतः --पेण, --पशः adv.<BR>Conformably or agreeably to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपेण
अनुरूपतः --पेण, --पशः adv.<BR>Conformably or agreeably to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुरूपशः
अनुरूपतः --पेण, --पशः adv.<BR>Conformably or agreeably to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलग्न
अनुलग्न a. Attached to, intent on,<BR>seeking or pursuing after; येन आर्यायाः<BR>सुस्निग्धा दृष्टिरनुलग्ना Mk. 4 intently<BR>fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलापः|अनुलाप
अनुलापः Repetition, tautology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलासः|अनुलास
अनुलासः, --स्यः [लस्-नर्तने-घञ्]<BR>A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलास्यः|अनुलास्य
अनुलासः, --स्यः [लस्-नर्तने-घञ्]<BR>A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलिप्
अनुलिप् {c6c} P. To anoint, besmear<BR>(with perfumes &c. after<BR>bathing); smear, daub, cover over;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">Page0079-c+ 57</a>]<BR>वपुरन्वलिप्त न वधूः Śi. 9. 51, 9. 15;<BR>प्रभानुलिप्तश्रीवत्सं R. 10. 10 covered with;<BR>तच्छायानुलिप्तभूतलां K. 131; हरिभिरचिरभासा<BR>तेजसा चानुलिप्तैः Ś. 7. 7; so<BR>स्नातानुलिप्तः; तिमिरानुलिप्त enveloped in<BR>darkness; स्नापितोऽनुलोपितश्च Dk. 71<BR>besmeared with perfumes &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपः|अनुलेप
अनुलेपः --लेपनं<BR>1 Unction,<BR>anointing, smearing.<BR>--2 Ointment, unguent<BR>such as sandal juice, oil &c.; any<BR>emollient or oily application;<BR>˚आर्द्रमृदंगध्वनि K. 28 rubbed with paste;<BR>सुरभि कुसुमधूपानुलेपनानि K. 324.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपनं|अनुलेपन
अनुलेपः --लेपनं<BR>1 Unction,<BR>anointing, smearing.<BR>--2 Ointment, unguent<BR>such as sandal juice, oil &c.; any<BR>emollient or oily application;<BR>˚आर्द्रमृदंगध्वनि K. 28 rubbed with paste;<BR>सुरभि कुसुमधूपानुलेपनानि K. 324.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपक
अनुलेपक, --लेपिन् a. One who<BR>anoints (the body) with unguents &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलेपिन्
अनुलेपक, --लेपिन् a. One who<BR>anoints (the body) with unguents &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलीन
अनुलीन a. Hidden, clinging to,<BR>attached; Śi. 5. 46; जनादनुलीनः<BR>Dk. 104 concealed from the people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोम|अनुलोमः
अनुलोम a. [अनुगतः लोम<BR>P. V. 4. 75.]<BR>1 ‘With the hair,’ regular,<BR>in natural order, successive (opp.<BR>प्रतिलोम); (hence), favourable,<BR>agreeable; ˚सुखो वायुरनुसारयतीव मां Rām.;<BR>त्रिरेनामनुलोमामनुमार्ष्टि Śat. Br.; ˚कृष्टं<BR>क्षेत्रं प्रतिलोमं कर्षति Sk. ploughed in<BR>the regular direction.<BR>--2 Mixed as a<BR>tribe.<BR>--मा A woman of the lower<BR>caste than that of the man's whom<BR>she marries; Y. 2. 288.<BR>--मं adv.<BR>In regular or natural order;<BR>प्रतिलोममालिंपेन्नानुलोमं Suśr.<BR>--माः (pl.)<BR>Mixed castes.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अय a.<BR>having fortune, favourable.<BR>--अर्थ a.<BR>speaking in favour of;<BR>जडानप्यनुलोमार्थान् प्रवाचः कृतिनां गिरः Śi. 2. 25.<BR>--ज,<BR>--जन्मन् a. born in due gradation,<BR>offspring of a mother inferior in<BR>caste to the father; said of the<BR>mixed tribes; Ms. 10. 25; Y. 1. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमनं|अनुलोमन
अनुलोमनं<BR>1 Regular gradation,<BR>sending or putting in the right<BR>direction.<BR>--2 (In medicine)<BR>Carrying off by the regular channels,<BR>such as purging; alleviation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुलोमयति
अनुलोमयति Den. P.<BR>1 To stroke<BR>or rub with the hair or with the<BR>grain, go with the grain; तत्र<BR>प्रतिलोममनुलोमयेत् Suśr.<BR>--2 To evacuate,<BR>purge, carry off by the regular<BR>channels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुल्वण
अनुल्वण a.<BR>1 Not excessive,<BR>neither more nor less (अनतिरिक्त,<BR>अन्यूनाधिक); smoothed, free from<BR>disturbing circumstances (?).<BR>--2 Not<BR>clear or manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवंशः|अनुवंश
अनुवंशः [वंशमनुगतो वृत्तांतः]<BR>1 A<BR>genealogical table; यंत्रानुवंशं भगवान्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">Page0080-a+ 56</a>]<BR>जामदग्न्यस्तथा जगौ Mb.<BR>--2 Modern<BR>race or species; new family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवंश्य
अनुवंश्य a. [अनुवंशे भवः यत्]<BR>Relating to a genealogical table.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवक्र
अनुवक्र a. [अनुक्रमेण वक्रः] Very<BR>crooked; somewhat crooked or<BR>oblique; ˚ग moving somewhat<BR>obliquely or retrogressively (said of<BR>planets).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवच्
अनुवच् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To say or speak<BR>after or for one; येषां द्विजानां<BR>सावित्री नानूच्येत यथाविधि Ms. 11. 191.<BR>--2 To repeat, recite, reiterate;<BR>शतमनूच्यमायुष्कामस्य Ait. Br.; learn,<BR>study; परोवरं यज्ञोऽनूच्यते Śat. Br.;<BR>अरण्येऽनूच्यमानत्वादारण्यकं Sāy., see<BR>अनूचान below.<BR>--3 To concede the point,<BR>assent to, yield.<BR>--4 To name, call.<BR>--Caus. To cause to recite; to read<BR>to oneself (before reading aloud);<BR>oft. used in dramas; उभे नाम<BR>मुद्राक्षराण्यनुवाच्य परस्परमवलोकयतः Ś. 1;<BR>निपु-(गृहीत्वा) कथं वाच्यतां; देवी-अनुवाचय तावत्<BR>यद्यविरुद्धं श्रोष्यामि V. 2; Mu. 1;<BR>अनुवाचितलेखममात्यमवलोक्य M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवक्तृ
अनुवक्तृ m. Repeating, reciting(<BR>गुरुमुखोच्चारितानुरूपपाठक); replying &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवचनं|अनुवचन
अनुवचनं<BR>1 Repetition, recitation;<BR>teaching, instruction, lecture,<BR>Y. 3. 190.<BR>--2 A chapter, section, lesson,<BR>division.<BR>--3 Repetition of Mantras<BR>or texts in conformity with प्रैष or<BR>injunction said by other priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाकः|अनुवाक
अनुवाकः [अनूच्यते इति, वच् घञ् कुत्वं<BR>P. II. 4. 29 Vārt.]<BR>1 Repeating,<BR>reciting, reading.<BR>--2 A subdivision of<BR>the Vedas, section, chapter.<BR>--3<BR>Chapter or section referring to a<BR>compilation from the Ṛgveda or Yajurveda<BR>(ऋग्यजुःसमूह).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुक्रमणी N.<BR>of a table of contents attributed<BR>to Śaunaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाक्या
अनुवाक्या [वच्-ण्यत्-कुत्वं] A verse<BR>recited by the Hotṛ priest, in<BR>which the god is invoked to<BR>accept the offering prepared for him,<BR>or a sort of priest; Śi. 14. 20 (<BR>प्रशास्तृपाठ्या तदभावे होतृपाठ्या देवताह्वानी ऋक्<BR>Malli.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाच्
अनुवाच् f. [वच्-णिच् क्विप्]<BR>Repetition, recitation &c. See अनुवचनं.<BR>--m. A lecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाचनं|अनुवाचन
अनुवाचनं<BR>1 Recitation of passages<BR>of the Ṛgveda by the Hotṛ priest<BR>in obedience to the injunction<BR>(प्रैष) of the अध्वर्यु priest.<BR>--2 Causing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-b" target="_blank">Page0080-b+ 57</a>]<BR>to recite, teaching, instructing.<BR>--3<BR>Reading to oneself; see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूक्त
अनूक्त p. p. Repeated, recited<BR>after; occurring in the text studied.<BR>--क्तं, --क्तिः f.<BR>1 Subsequent mention;<BR>repetition by way of explanation or<BR>illustration.<BR>--2 Study of the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनूचान|अनूचानः
अनूचान a. or<BR>--नः [अनुवच्-कानच्<BR>निपातः P. III. 2. 109; वेदस्य अनुवचनं<BR>कृतवान् अनूचानः Sk.]<BR>1 One devoted to<BR>study, learned; especially one<BR>well-versed in the Vedas with their<BR>Aṅgas so as to be able to repeat,<BR>read and teach them; योऽनूचानः स नो<BR>महान् Ms. 2. 154; 5. 82; Y. 3. 24;<BR>इदमूचुरनूचानाः Ku. 6. 15.<BR>--2 Modest,<BR>unassuming; humble, well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवत्सरः|अनुवत्सर|अनुवत्सरं
अनुवत्सरः [अनुकूलो वत्सरो<BR>दानादिविशेषाय]<BR>1 A year.<BR>--2 The 4th year in<BR>the 5 years' cycle; or the 5th of<BR>5 cycles of 12 years in the Bṛhaspati<BR>cycle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवद्
अनुवद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To imitate in<BR>speaking, mock (with acc.); गिरं<BR>नः… अनुवदति शुकस्ते मंजुवाक् पंजरस्थः<BR>R. 5. 74 repeat; उक्तमनुवदति Sk.;<BR>(P. & Ā.) to resound, echo;<BR>अनुवदति वीणा P. I. 3. 49 Sk. अनुवदते कठः<BR>कलापस्य ibid.;<BR>सभाभित्तिप्रतिध्वानैर्भयादन्ववदन्निव Śi. 2. 67 echoed and<BR>approved also; घोषस्यान्ववदिष्टेव लंका<BR>पूतक्रतोः पुरः Bk. 8. 29.<BR>--2 To repeat or say<BR>again by way of explanation,<BR>illustration or corroboration; See Kull. on<BR>Ms. 1. 74; 2. 6.<BR>--3 To repeat, tell,<BR>say (generally); निजमनोरथमनुवदंत्या<BR>Dk. 21.<BR>--4 To abuse, rail at. --Caus.<BR>To cause to resound or echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादः|अनुवाद
अनुवादः<BR>1 Repetition (in general);<BR>गुण˚ K. 206.<BR>--2 Repetition by way<BR>of explanation, illustration or<BR>corroboration; अनुवादे चरणानां<BR>P. II. 4. 3 (सिद्धस्योपन्यासे Sk.).<BR>--3<BR>Explanatory repetition or<BR>reference to what is already<BR>mentioned, such as paraphrase or free<BR>translation; particularly, any<BR>portion of the Brāhmaṇas which<BR>comments on, illustrates, or explains a<BR>Vidhi or direction previously laid<BR>down and which does not itself<BR>lay down any directions; a<BR>supplementary repetition, opp. to विधि<BR>‘authoritative or direct injunction’;<BR>विधिविहितस्य अनुवचनमनुवादः ।<BR>नानुवादपुनरुक्तयोः विशेषः शब्दाभ्यासोपपत्तेः Nyāya Sūtra.<BR>It is of 3 kinds:--भूतार्थ˚ (सदेव<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">Page0080-c+ 55</a>]<BR>सौम्येदमग्र आसीत्); स्तुत्यर्थ˚ (वायुर्वै क्षेपिष्ठा देवता)<BR>and गुण˚ (अग्निहोत्रं जुहोति इत्युक्ते दध्ना<BR>जुहोति इति गुणविधानांत्); see अर्थवाद<BR>also.<BR>--4 Corroboration, confirmation.<BR>--5 Slander, abuse, reviling.<BR>--6<BR>Advertisement, notice; report, rumour.<BR>--7 Commencement of speech (<BR>वाचारंभणमात्रं.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादक
अनुवादक, --वादिन् a.<BR>1 Explanatory,<BR>corroborative, repeating with<BR>comment, explanation or illustration;<BR>आरंभश्च साहसानुवादी Dk. 95 bespeaks.<BR>--2 Conformable to, in harmony<BR>with, like; युक्तगीतानुवादिना Rām.;<BR>तदनुवादिगुणः कुसुमोद्गमः R. 9. 30.<BR>--न्<BR>m. N. of any one of the three<BR>notes of the gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवादिन्
अनुवादक, --वादिन् a.<BR>1 Explanatory,<BR>corroborative, repeating with<BR>comment, explanation or illustration;<BR>आरंभश्च साहसानुवादी Dk. 95 bespeaks.<BR>--2 Conformable to, in harmony<BR>with, like; युक्तगीतानुवादिना Rām.;<BR>तदनुवादिगुणः कुसुमोद्गमः R. 9. 30.<BR>--न्<BR>m. N. of any one of the three<BR>notes of the gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवाद्य
अनुवाद्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be explained<BR>or illustrated.<BR>--2 (In gram.) To be<BR>made the subject of an assertion (in a<BR>sentence), opposed to विधेय which<BR>affirms or denies something about<BR>the subject. In a sentence the<BR>अनुवाद्य or subject which is supposed to<BR>be already known is repeated to<BR>mark its connection with the विधेय or<BR>predicate and should be placed first;<BR>अनुवाद्यमनुक्त्वैव न विधेयमुदीरयेत्; in<BR>वृद्धिरादैच् आदैच् should have been<BR>placed first, though the<BR>construction is defended by Patañjali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्तन|अनुवर्तनं|अनुवर्त्तन|अनुवर्त्तनं
अनुवर्तन, --वर्तिन् &c. see अनुवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्तिन्|अनुवर्त्तिन्
अनुवर्तन, --वर्तिन् &c. see अनुवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवश|अनुवशः
अनुवश a. [वशमनुगतः] Subject<BR>to the will of another, obedient.<BR>--शः Subjection, obedience (to the<BR>will of another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवस्
अनुवस् {c1c} P. To dwell near to<BR>or along with (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासिन्
अनुवासिन् a. One who dwells near;<BR>resident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवसित
अनुवसित a. [वस्-क्त]<BR>1 Dressed<BR>clothed, wrapped up.<BR>--2 Fastened,<BR>or bound to, attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवहः|अनुवह
अनुवहः One of the 7 tongues<BR>of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवातः|अनुवात
अनुवातः [अनुगतो वातः] The<BR>windward direction; the wind which<BR>blows from the pupil to the<BR>preceptor &c.; प्रतिवातेऽनुवाते च नासीत<BR>गुरुणा सह Ms. 2. 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवारं
अनुवारं ind. Time after time,<BR>repeatedly, frequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवास्
अनुवास् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To scent,<BR>perfume.<BR>--2 To use the oily enema<BR>(see the next word); treat by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">Page0081-a+ 55</a>]<BR>using such enema; अवश्यं<BR>स्थापनीयाश्च नानुवास्याः कथंचन Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0080-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासः|अनुवास
अनुवासः --सनं<BR>1 Perfuming or<BR>scenting (in general,) with incense &c.<BR>--2 Perfuming clothes by<BR>dipping the ends.<BR>--3 (˚नः also) A<BR>syringe, clyster-pipe (Mar. पिचकारी);<BR>an oily enema or the operation<BR>itself; असाध्यता विकाराणां<BR>स्यादेषामनुवासनात् Suśr.; द्विधा वस्तिः परिज्ञेयो<BR>निरूहश्चानुवासनं । कषायाद्यैर्निरूहः स्यात्<BR>स्नेहाद्यैरनुवासनम् ॥ (अनुवसति अनुवासरं वा दीयते<BR>अनुवसन्नपि न दुष्यति अनुदिवसं वा दीयते इति<BR>अनुवासनः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासनं|अनुवासन
अनुवासः --सनं<BR>1 Perfuming or<BR>scenting (in general,) with incense &c.<BR>--2 Perfuming clothes by<BR>dipping the ends.<BR>--3 (˚नः also) A<BR>syringe, clyster-pipe (Mar. पिचकारी);<BR>an oily enema or the operation<BR>itself; असाध्यता विकाराणां<BR>स्यादेषामनुवासनात् Suśr.; द्विधा वस्तिः परिज्ञेयो<BR>निरूहश्चानुवासनं । कषायाद्यैर्निरूहः स्यात्<BR>स्नेहाद्यैरनुवासनम् ॥ (अनुवसति अनुवासरं वा दीयते<BR>अनुवसन्नपि न दुष्यति अनुदिवसं वा दीयते इति<BR>अनुवासनः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवासित
अनुवासित a.<BR>1 Fumigated,<BR>perfumed.<BR>--2 Administered as an<BR>enema; treated by this operation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविद्
अनुविद् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To find, discover,<BR>see, obtain.<BR>--2 To deem, consider.<BR>--3 To marry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवित्तिः|अनुवित्ति
अनुवित्तिः f. Finding, obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविद्ध
अनुविद्ध See under अनुव्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविधा
अनुविधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To lay down a<BR>rule, regulate.<BR>--2 To obey, act<BR>up to, follow, conform to; See<BR>अनुविधायिन्; पदमनुविधेयं च महतां Bh. 2. 28<BR>the foot-steps of the great have to<BR>be trodden in.<BR>--3 To resemble,<BR>imitate. --pass. To be trained to<BR>follow rules; obey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविधानं|अनुविधान
अनुविधानं<BR>1 Obedience.<BR>--2 Acting<BR>in conformity to (orders &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविधायिन्
अनुविधायिन् a.<BR>1 Obedient,<BR>submissive, compliant, conforming to<BR>orders; सा स्त्री यानुविधायिनी H. 2. 141;<BR>भवितव्यानुविधायीनींद्रियाणि V. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Resembling;<BR>निजवधूश्वसितानुविधायिनि Śi. 6. 23, 15. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविनश्
अनुविनश् {c4c} P. To disappear,<BR>vanish or perish after or along with<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविनाशः|अनुविनाश
अनुविनाशः Perishing after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविश्
अनुविश् {c6c} P. To enter or go<BR>after, follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेशः|अनुवेश
अनुवेशः --शनं<BR>1 Following, entering<BR>after.<BR>--2 Marriage of a younger<BR>brother before the elder is married;<BR>(ज्येष्ठातिक्रमेण कनिष्ठस्य विवाहः);<BR>यवीयसोऽनुवेशो हि ज्येष्ठस्य विधिलोपकः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेशनं|अनुवेशन
अनुवेशः --शनं<BR>1 Following, entering<BR>after.<BR>--2 Marriage of a younger<BR>brother before the elder is married;<BR>(ज्येष्ठातिक्रमेण कनिष्ठस्य विवाहः);<BR>यवीयसोऽनुवेशो हि ज्येष्ठस्य विधिलोपकः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेश्य
अनुवेश्य a. [अनुक्रमेण वेशमर्हति, यत्]<BR>A next-door neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविश्वः|अनुविश्व
अनुविश्वः (pl.) N. of a people<BR>in the northeast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविष्टंभः|अनुविष्टम्भ|अनुविष्टम्भः
अनुविष्टंभः Being obstructed in<BR>consequence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृत्
अनुवृत् {c1c} A. (sometimes P. also)<BR>1 (Transitively used) (a) To go<BR>or roll after, follow, pursue; (fig.)<BR>to follow, conform to, act according<BR>to, obey, adapt oneself to, be<BR>guided by; humour; अहं<BR>तावत्स्वामिनश्चित्तवृत्तिमनुवर्तिष्ये Ś. 2; तेऽपि<BR>परिचयमनुवर्तंते K. 289; किमत्र चित्रं यदि विशाखे<BR>शशांकलेखामनुवर्तेते Ś. 3 approve of her<BR>choice; लौकिकानां हि साधूनामर्थं<BR>वागनुवर्तते U. 1. 10 words conform to the<BR>sense; न कुलक्रममनुवर्तते K. 104 follow;<BR>मधु द्विरेफः कुसुमैकपात्रे पपौ प्रियां<BR>स्वामनुवर्तमानः Ku. 3. 36 followed his mate<BR>in drinking, drank after her;<BR>Bh. 2. 110; Bg. 3. 23; Dk. 80, 96, 126;<BR>कृतज्ञतामनुवर्तमानेन Mu. 3 following<BR>the path of gratitude; प्रभुचित्तमेव हि<BR>जनोऽनुवर्तते Śi. 15. 41; Māl. 3. 2.<BR>(b) To imitate, resemble; equal;<BR>तेऽन्ववर्तन् पितॄन्सर्वे यशसा च बलेन च<BR>Mb. (c) To gratify, humour, please;<BR>Dk. 65.<BR>--2 (Intransitively used)<BR>(a) To follow, come after; संग्राह्य<BR>इत्यनुवर्तते H. 3. (b) To continue, endure.<BR>(c) To act towards, behave. (d)<BR>(In gram.) To be repeated or<BR>supplied from a preceding rule, Sūtra<BR>or assertion (said of a word or rule<BR>which continues to exercise<BR>influence on what follows); e. g. in<BR>P. IV. 3. 95 भक्तिः सोऽस्य (occurring<BR>in Sūtra 89 before) इत्यनुवर्तते Sk.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to revolve,<BR>turn round; एवं प्रवर्तितं चक्रं<BR>नानुवर्तयतीह यः Bg. 3. 16.<BR>--2 To act up to,<BR>follow, obey; तथापि लोकयात्रानुवर्तनीया<BR>Mv. 7; पुत्रैः पितरो लोकद्वयेप्यनुवर्तनीयाः<BR>Ve. 3; K. 367.<BR>--3 To favour, oblige;<BR>comply with one's request;<BR>विधिनापि भवतेव वयमनुवर्तिताः K. 73;<BR>यथाचित्तमनुवर्तनीयः Māl. 7.<BR>--4 To put in,<BR>carry out.<BR>--5 To repeat or<BR>supply from a preceding Sūtra; केचित्तु<BR>विजायते इति नानुवर्तयंति P. V. 2. 13<BR>Sk.<BR>--6 To use, employ.<BR>--7 To lead<BR>one to, attach to.<BR>--8 To speak in<BR>favour of, speak for; to approve.<BR>--9<BR>To imitate, do after one; सतां<BR>चरितान्यनुवर्तितानि नद्रियाणि K. 298.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्तनं|अनुवर्तन|अनुवर्त्तन|अनुवर्त्तनं
अनुवर्तनं<BR>1 Following(fig. also);<BR>attending, compliance, obedience,<BR>conformity; प्रकृतस्यानुवर्तने Ak.;<BR>इदमाश्चर्यमथवा लोकस्थित्यनुवर्तनं Mv. 7. 4;<BR>दाक्षिण्य˚ Dk. 161.<BR>--2 Gratifying,<BR>obliging.<BR>--3 Approval of,<BR>concurrence in.<BR>--4 Continuance; result,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-c" target="_blank">Page0081-c+ 57</a>]<BR>consequence.<BR>--5 Supplying from a<BR>preceding Sūtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्तिन्|अनुवर्त्तिन्
अनुवर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Following, obeying,<BR>conforming to, with acc. or in comp.;<BR>राक्षसाश्चापि गृह्यंते नित्यं छंदानुवर्तिभिः<BR>Pt. 1. 69; नराधिपा नीचजनानुवर्तिनः<BR>1. 383.<BR>--2 Guided by, following<BR>the advice of; obedient, faithful,<BR>compliant; अनुवर्तिनि कलत्रे Pt. 1. 101,<BR>298.<BR>--3 Like, resembling; suitable,<BR>worthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवर्त्मन्
अनुवर्त्मन् a. [अनुगतो वर्त्म] Following,<BR>attending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृत्त
अनुवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Obeying,<BR>following &c.<BR>--2 Uninterrupted,<BR>continuously kept up, continued;<BR>अनुवृत्तस्त्वया भगीरथगृहे प्रसादः U. 7.<BR>--3<BR>Rounded off; taperingly round (<BR>क्रमशः वर्तुलाकार); दीर्घानुवृत्तपीनबाहुना<BR>K. 179.<BR>--4 Supplied from a preceding<BR>rule &c.<BR>--5 Conforming to the<BR>character (शीलानुगत).<BR>--त्तं<BR>Obedience, conformity, compliance;<BR>मूर्खं छंदोऽनुवृत्तेन (गृह्णीयात्) Chāṇ. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृत्तिः|अनुवृत्ति
अनुवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Assenting to,<BR>approval; तवानुवृत्तिं न च कर्तुमुत्सहे<BR>Ku. 5. 65.<BR>--2 Obedience, conformity,<BR>following, continuance in (opp.<BR>व्यावृत्ति); taking up; continuity;<BR>ज्येष्ठानुवृत्तिजटिलं R. 13. 78 by<BR>following the example of; अनुवृत्त्या<BR>प्रमार्ष्टुमागतः Dk. 100 service; ततान वह्निः<BR>पवनानुवृत्त्या Ki. 16. 52 in<BR>consequence of.<BR>--3 Acting according or<BR>suitably to, compliance,<BR>acquiescence; gratifying, pleasing;<BR>कांता˚चातुर्यमपि शिक्षितं वत्सेन U. 3; Māl. 9;<BR>Śi. 9. 58; Dk. 55; K. 265; M. 2. 9;<BR>राज्यं हि नाम राजधर्म˚ परस्य<BR>नृपतेर्महदप्रीतिस्थानं Mu. 3 who conforms to or<BR>is true to the duties of kings;<BR>(previous) compliant or obedient spirit,<BR>previous course of conduct; U. 7. 5.<BR>--4<BR>Remembrance Ki. 18. 18.<BR>--5 (Gram.)<BR>Being supplied or repeated in a<BR>following rule; continued influence<BR>of a preceding on a following rule.<BR>--6 Imitating, resembling &c.<BR>--7<BR>Repetition; वर्णानामनुवृत्तिरनुप्रासः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवृद्धि
अनुवृद्धि a. Ved. Increasing in<BR>regular ratio.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेलं|अनुवेल
अनुवेलं ind. Ever and anon,<BR>constantly; इति स्म पृच्छत्यनुवेलमादृतः<BR>R. 3. 5; Śi. 3. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेल्लित
अनुवेल्लित a. [वेल्ल्-क्त] Bent in<BR>conformity with; bent under.<BR>--तं<BR>Securing with bandages, bandaging;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">Page0082-a+ 56</a>]<BR>a sort of bandage (व्रणलेपनबंधभेदः) one of<BR>the 14 kinds mentioned by Suśruta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0081-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्य
अनुव्य a. [अनुव्ययति अनुगच्छति<BR>व्येक] Following (अनुगत); ˚व्यमिवासुः<BR>Kāty. (न्यग्भूमिं प्राप्ता इव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्यंजनं|अनुव्यञ्जन|अनुव्यंजन
अनुव्यंजनं A secondary token.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्यध्
अनुव्यध् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To hit or pierce<BR>again; विद्धमनुविध्यतः Ms. 9. 43.<BR>--2<BR>To wound, pierce; कामशरानुविद्धः &c.<BR>--3 To fill or mix with, blend with,<BR>see अनुविद्ध below.<BR>--4 To impel, urge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुविद्ध
अनुविद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Pierced, bored;<BR>कीटानुविद्धरत्नादिसाधारण्येन काव्यता<BR>S. D.<BR>--2 Overspread, intertwined;<BR>surrounded, full of; pervaded by,<BR>replete or filled with, abounding in,<BR>mixed or blended with, intermixed;<BR>सरसिजमनुविद्धं शैवलेनापि रम्यं Ś. 1. 20;<BR>क्वचित्प्रभालेपिभिरिंद्रनीलैर्मुक्तामयी<BR>यष्टिरिवानुविद्धा R. 13. 54 interwoven with<BR>emeralds; 16. 48, 6. 18; अलके<BR>बालकुंदानुविद्धं Me. 65; सौरभ्य˚ Mk. 1;<BR>कोपानुविद्धां चिंतां नाटयन् Mu. 3;<BR>Ku. 3. 35; पांडुतानुविद्धेव देहच्छविः<BR>Dk. 112; 137; Māl. 1.<BR>--3 Connected with,<BR>relating to; adhering to;<BR>देशवार्तानुविद्धा संकथा Dk. 117, 124;<BR>उद्रूर्णलोष्टलगुडैः परितोऽनुविद्धं Śi. 5. 25 chased,<BR>closely followed or pursued.<BR>--4 Set,<BR>inlaid; variegated;<BR>रत्नानुविद्धार्णवमेखलाया दिशः सपत्नी भव दक्षिणस्याः<BR>R. 6. 63, 14; Śi. 4. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुवेधः|अनुवेध
अनुवेधः, --व्याधः<BR>1 Hurting,<BR>piercing, perforating; न हि कीटानुवेधादयो<BR>रत्नस्य रत्नत्वं व्याहंतुमीशाः S. D. 1.<BR>--2 Contact, union; मुखामोदं मदिरया<BR>कृतानुव्याधमुद्वमन् Śi. 2. 20.<BR>--3<BR>Blending, mixture; fusion.<BR>--4<BR>Obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याधः|अनुव्याध
अनुवेधः, --व्याधः<BR>1 Hurting,<BR>piercing, perforating; न हि कीटानुवेधादयो<BR>रत्नस्य रत्नत्वं व्याहंतुमीशाः S. D. 1.<BR>--2 Contact, union; मुखामोदं मदिरया<BR>कृतानुव्याधमुद्वमन् Śi. 2. 20.<BR>--3<BR>Blending, mixture; fusion.<BR>--4<BR>Obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्यवसायः|अनुव्यवसाय
अनुव्यवसायः (In Nyāya)<BR>Consciousness of the perception; (in<BR>Vedānta phil.) perception of a<BR>sentiment or judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याख्यानं|अनुव्याख्यान
अनुव्याख्यानं [अनुरूपं व्याख्यानं]<BR>That which comments on and<BR>explains Mantras, Sūtras &c. (<BR>मंत्रविवरणं); especially, that portion of a<BR>Brāhmaṇa which explains difficult<BR>Sūtras, texts &c. occurring in<BR>another place (<BR>मंत्रादीनामनुरूपार्थप्रकाशकं व्याख्यानं.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याहरणं|अनुव्याहरण
अनुव्याहरणं, --व्याहारः<BR>1<BR>Repetition, repeated utterance;<BR>mentioning along with something else.<BR>--2<BR>A curse, imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याहारः|अनुव्याहार
अनुव्याहरणं, --व्याहारः<BR>1<BR>Repetition, repeated utterance;<BR>mentioning along with something else.<BR>--2<BR>A curse, imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्याहारिन्
अनुव्याहारिन् a. Cursing; execrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रज्
अनुव्रज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To follow, go after;<BR>तां व्रजंतीमनुवव्राज K. 132, 210; attend<BR>especially a departing guest (as far<BR>as the bank of water, lake, &c.) as<BR>a mark of respect; Y. 1. 113; तं<BR>मातरो देवमनुव्रजंत्यः Ku. 7. 38;<BR>यमिच्छेत्पुनरायांतं नैनं दूरमनुव्रजेत् Rām.<BR>--2 To visit<BR>in order, seek.<BR>--3 To go to or near;<BR>betake oneself to; मृगा मृगैः<BR>संगमनुव्रजंति Pt. 1 deer herd or associate<BR>with deer.<BR>--4 To obey, to do<BR>homage to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रजनं|अनुव्रजन
अनुव्रजनं, --व्रज्या Following, going<BR>after, especially a departing guest;<BR>Ms. 3. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रज्या
अनुव्रजनं, --व्रज्या Following, going<BR>after, especially a departing guest;<BR>Ms. 3. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्राज्य
अनुव्राज्य pot. p. To be followed<BR>as by the relatives of a dead person<BR>to the cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुव्रत|अनुव्रतः
अनुव्रत a. [अनुकूलं व्रतं कर्म यस्य]<BR>1 Devoted or faithful to, attached to<BR>(with acc. or gen.); प्रियतमा का<BR>अनुव्रता Bh. 2. 103; वैश्याः क्षत्रमनुव्रताः<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 Duly performing the vows<BR>or duties prescribed (opp. अपव्रत).<BR>--तः A class of Jaina ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशतिक
अनुशतिक a. Accompanied with,<BR>or bought for, a hundred; ˚आदिः a<BR>class of words or गण mentioned in<BR>P. VII. 3. 20, where both<BR>members undergo Vṛddhi.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशय|अनुशयः
अनुशय, --शयिन् &c. See under<BR>अनुशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयिन्
अनुशय, --शयिन् &c. See under<BR>अनुशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशरः|अनुशर
अनुशरः [अनु-शृणाति, शॄ-अच्] A sort<BR>of evil spirit, Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशस्त्रं|अनुशस्त्र
अनुशस्त्रं [अनुगतं शस्त्रं शस्त्रार्थे प्रयुक्तं]<BR>Anything used (for the time<BR>being) instead of a regular<BR>instrument, such as a fingernail; a<BR>secondary weapon or instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशास्
अनुशास् {c2c} P.<BR>1 (a) To advise,<BR>persuade, prevail upon, address;<BR>इति ध्रुवेच्छामनुशासती सुतां शशाक मेना न<BR>नियंतुमुद्यमात् Ku. 5. 5; पूर्वानुशिष्टां<BR>निजगाद भोज्यां R. 6. 59. (b) To direct,<BR>tell, order, enjoin; to teach, instruct<BR>(how to act); दशरथप्रभवानुशिष्टः<BR>R. 13. 75; वत्से त्वमधुनाऽनुशासनीयासि Ś. 4;<BR>राजपत्नीनियोगस्थमनुशाधि पुरीजनं<BR>Bk. 20. 17; को नु खलु मामेवमनुशास्ति V. 4<BR>tells, directs; मघवा वनगमनाय<BR>कृतबुद्धिं भवंतमनुशास्ति V. 5 tells, directs;<BR>माणवकं धर्ममनुशास्ति Sk.; Ms. 6. 86.<BR>--2<BR>To rule, govern.<BR>--3 To chastise, punish,<BR>correct; इयमेव तावत्प्रथममनुशासनीया<BR>Ve. 2; अरिकुलमनुशासनीयं {3}; स्वकर्म<BR>ख्यापयन्ब्रूयान्मां भवाननुशास्त्विति Ms. 11. 100,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">Page0082-c+ 57</a>]<BR>9. 233.<BR>--4 To praise, extol.<BR>--5 To<BR>accomplish, perform, execute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासक
अनुशासक, --शासिन्, --शास्तृ, --शासितृ<BR>a. One who directs, instructs,<BR>governs or punishes; कविं<BR>पुराणमनुशासितारं Bg. 8. 9 ruler; एष चोरानुशासी<BR>राजेति भयादुत्पतितः V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासिन्
अनुशासक, --शासिन्, --शास्तृ, --शासितृ<BR>a. One who directs, instructs,<BR>governs or punishes; कविं<BR>पुराणमनुशासितारं Bg. 8. 9 ruler; एष चोरानुशासी<BR>राजेति भयादुत्पतितः V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशास्तृ
अनुशासक, --शासिन्, --शास्तृ, --शासितृ<BR>a. One who directs, instructs,<BR>governs or punishes; कविं<BR>पुराणमनुशासितारं Bg. 8. 9 ruler; एष चोरानुशासी<BR>राजेति भयादुत्पतितः V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासितृ
अनुशासक, --शासिन्, --शास्तृ, --शासितृ<BR>a. One who directs, instructs,<BR>governs or punishes; कविं<BR>पुराणमनुशासितारं Bg. 8. 9 ruler; एष चोरानुशासी<BR>राजेति भयादुत्पतितः V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशासनं|अनुशासन
अनुशासनं Advice, persuasion,<BR>direction, order, command;<BR>instruction, laying down rules or precepts;<BR>a law, rule, precept; treatment (of<BR>a subject), (with the object in<BR>comp. or with gen., the agent, if<BR>expressed, being put in the instr. or<BR>gen.); भवत्यधिक्षेप इवानुशासनं<BR>Ki. 1. 28 words of advice; तन्मनोरनुशासनं<BR>Ms. 8. 139; 6. 50; 2. 159; यौवन˚ K. 146;<BR>नामलिंग˚ laying down rules on the<BR>gender of nouns, explanation of<BR>gender &c.; शब्दानुशासनं Sk.;<BR>शब्दानामनुशासनमाचार्यस्य आचार्येण वा<BR>P. II. 3. 66 Sk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पर a.<BR>obedient.<BR>--पर्वन् N. of the 13th book<BR>of the Mahābhārata (so called<BR>because it lays down precepts of<BR>advice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशिष्टिः|अनुशिष्टि
अनुशिष्टिः f. Instruction,<BR>teaching; order, command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशिक्षिन्
अनुशिक्षिन् a. Practising,<BR>learning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशिशुः|अनुशिशु
अनुशिशुः f. [अनुगता शिशुना] An<BR>animal followed by its young one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशी
अनुशी {c2c} A.<BR>1 To lie or sleep<BR>with, sleep along with; lie upon,<BR>close or along; lay oneself down; to<BR>adhere to or follow closely, cling or<BR>stick to; शयानं चानुशेते हि<BR>तिष्ठंतमनुतिष्ठति । अनुधावति धावंतं कर्म पूर्वकृतं नरं ॥<BR>Subhāṣita.<BR>--2 To repent, grieve for;<BR>दत्तमिष्टमपि नान्वशेत सः Śi. 14. 45;<BR>पुरानुशेते तव चंचलं मनः Ki. 8. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयः|अनुशय
अनुशयः [शी-अच्]<BR>1 Repentance,<BR>remorse; regret, sorrow;<BR>नन्वनुशयस्थानमेतत् Māl. 8; कुतस्तेऽनुशयः M. 3<BR>why should you be sorry; बाष्पं<BR>प्रमृज्य विगतानुशयो भवेयं Ś. 7. 25; इतो<BR>गतस्यानुशयो मा भूदिति V. 4; Śi. 2. 14.<BR>--2<BR>Intense enmity or anger;<BR>शिशुपालोऽनुशयं परं गतः Śi. 16. 2;<BR>यस्मिन्नमुक्तानुशया सदैव जागर्ति भुजंगी Māl. 6. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Hatred.<BR>--4 Close connection, as<BR>with a consequence; close<BR>attachment (to any object).<BR>--5 (In<BR>Vedānta phil.) The result or<BR>consequence of bad deeds which very<BR>closely clings to them and makes<BR>the soul enter other bodies after<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">Page0083-a+ 57</a>]<BR>enjoying temporary freedom from<BR>recurring births; (स्वर्गार्थकर्मणो<BR>भुक्तफलस्य अवशेषः कश्चिदनुशयो नाम<BR>भांडानुसारिस्नेहवत्, यथा हि स्नेहभांडं विरिच्यर्मानं सर्वात्मना<BR>न विरिच्यते भांडानुसार्येव केश्चित् स्नेहशेषो ऽ<BR>वतिष्ठते तथानुशयोऽपि Tv.).<BR>--6 Regret in<BR>the case of purchases, technically<BR>called rescission; Ms. 8. 222; see<BR>क्रीतानुशय.<BR>--यी A disease of the feet,<BR>a sort of boil or abscess on the upper<BR>part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0082-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयान
अनुशयान a. Regretting &c.<BR>--ना A<BR>variety of heroine (परकीयनायिकाभेदः);<BR>one who is sad and dejected, being<BR>apprehensive of the loss of her<BR>lover (इष्टहानिजनितानुतापवती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशयिन्
अनुशयिन् a.<BR>1 Devotedly attached<BR>to, faithful.<BR>--2 Repentant, penitent,<BR>regretful, sorry.<BR>--3 Hating<BR>intensely.<BR>--4 Connected as with a<BR>consequence.<BR>--5 Enjoying the fruits of<BR>deeds; epithet of the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशीलनं|अनुशीलन
अनुशीलनं Intent or assiduous<BR>application, constant pursuit or<BR>exercise, constant or repeated practice or<BR>study; विज्ञातसाराण्यनुशीलनेन<BR>Ki. 16. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशीलित
अनुशीलित a. Assiduously<BR>practised, repeatedly done, carefully<BR>attended to or studied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशुच्
अनुशुच् {c1c} P. To bewail, mourn<BR>over, regret; कथं तमेव<BR>चौरहतकमनुशोचसि Mk. 3; नष्टं मृतमतिक्रांतं नानुशोचंति<BR>पंडिताः Pt. 1. 333; शैशवं ते<BR>स्मृत्वात्मानमनुशोचामि K. 333; Ve. 5. 4 condole<BR>with, weep with. --Caus. To mourn<BR>over, deplore, grieve for, regret;<BR>तृणमिव वने शून्ये त्यक्ता न<BR>वाप्यनुशोचिता U. 3. 32 nor was she (her<BR>loss) regretted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशुचिका
अनुशुचिका A ceremony enjoined<BR>by the Vedas (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोकः|अनुशोक
अनुशोकः, --शोचनं Sorrow,<BR>repentance, regret; अनुशु (शो) चितं in the<BR>same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचनं|अनुशोचन
अनुशोकः, --शोचनं Sorrow,<BR>repentance, regret; अनुशु (शो) चितं in the<BR>same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचक
अनुशोचक --शोचिन् a.<BR>1 Regretful,<BR>penitent.<BR>--2 Causing regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुशोचिन्
अनुशोचक --शोचिन् a.<BR>1 Regretful,<BR>penitent.<BR>--2 Causing regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुश्रु
अनुश्रु {c5c} P.<BR>1 To hear (= श्रु);<BR>नानुशुश्रुमजात्वेतत् Ms. 9. 100; तद्यथानुश्रूयते<BR>Pt. 1 heard, related.<BR>--2 To hear<BR>repeatedly as from a sacred<BR>authority, hand down as by Vedic tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुश्रवः|अनुश्रव
अनुश्रवः Vedic or sacred tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुश्लोकं|अनुश्लोक
अनुश्लोकं [अनुश्लोक्यते गीयते, श्लोक्,<BR>कर्मणि अच्] A kind of Sāma (महाव्रतगेयः<BR>सामभेदः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषंज्|अनुषञ्ज्
अनुषंज् (˚संज्) {c1c} P. To adhere or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-b" target="_blank">Page0083-b+ 58</a>]<BR>cling to, follow closely. --pass.<BR>(-षज्यते)<BR>1 To stick, cling, adhere to,<BR>be attached to (fig. also); धर्मपूते च<BR>मनसि नभसीव न जातु रजोऽनुषज्यते<BR>Dk. 43; sometimes occurring as<BR>अनुषज्जते (from सस्ज् also); यदा हि<BR>नोंद्रियार्थेषु न कर्मस्वनुषज्जते Bg. 6. 4; 18. 10.<BR>--2 To be supplied from a preceding<BR>rule or statement. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>fasten or attach (something) to.<BR>--2 To<BR>supply (as an elliptical expression);<BR>इति पदमत्रानुषंजनीयं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषक्
अनुषक् --ट् adv. In continuous or<BR>close order, one after another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषट्
अनुषक् --ट् adv. In continuous or<BR>close order, one after another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषक्त
अनुषक्त p. p.<BR>1 Connected with,<BR>closely related or attached to;<BR>नित्य˚क्तः प्रकृतिकोपः Mv. 2 constant,<BR>ever-arising.<BR>--2 Clinging or adhering to<BR>(actively used); मृत्युर्जरा च व्याधिश्च दुःखं<BR>चानेककारणं । अनुषक्तं सदा देहे Mb.;<BR>हृदि नित्यानुषक्तेन सीताशोकेन तप्यते<BR>U. 4. 2 constantly preying on the<BR>heart; ˚मंदाकिनीपवित्रमेखलं Mv. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषंगः|अनुषङ्ग|अनुषंग|अनुषङ्गः
अनुषंगः<BR>1 Close adherence or<BR>attendance; connection, conjunction,<BR>association; सानुषंगाणि कल्याणानि U. 7<BR>good things closely follow one<BR>another (come close upon one<BR>another).<BR>--2 Coalition, commixture.<BR>--3 Connection of word with word.<BR>--4 A word or words repeated<BR>from the context to supply an<BR>ellipsis.<BR>--5 Necessary consequence,<BR>inevitable result.<BR>--6 Connection<BR>of a subsequent with a previous<BR>act.<BR>--7 Incidental mention or<BR>relation (प्रसंग).<BR>--8 Yearning, eager<BR>longing.<BR>--9 Compassion, pity,<BR>tenderness.<BR>--10 (In Nyāya)<BR>Connecting together the उपनय or<BR>application and निगमन or conclusion by the<BR>use of the pronoun इदं<BR>(उपनयवाक्यस्थस्य अयमिति पदस्य निगमनवाक्ये आकर्षणं).<BR>--11 The nasals connected with<BR>certain roots ending in consonants;<BR>P. VII. 1. 59 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषंगिक|अनुषङ्गिक
अनुषंगिक a. Following as a<BR>necessary result, consequent;<BR>concomitant, adhering to, connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषंगिन्|अनुषङ्गिन्
अनुषंगिन् a.<BR>1 Connected with,<BR>adhering or sticking to; अनीकजे<BR>रजसि मुखानुषंगिणि Śi. 17. 57.<BR>--2<BR>Following as a necessary<BR>consequence; यस्यानुषंगिण इमे भोगादयो भवंति<BR>Bh. 3. 76.<BR>--3 Related or applicable<BR>to, common, prevailing (अनुक्षणं<BR>प्रसक्त); सप्तकस्यास्य वर्गस्य<BR>सर्वत्रैवानुषंगिणः Ms. 7. 52; विभुतानुषंगि भयमेति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-c" target="_blank">Page0083-c+ 57</a>]<BR>जनः Ki. 6. 35 connected with,<BR>natural to, greatness.<BR>--4 Addicted to,<BR>devoted or attached to, fond of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषंजनं|अनुषञ्जन
अनुषंजनं Concord, grammatical<BR>connection or agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुषेकः|अनुषेक
अनुषेकः --सेचनं Rewatering,<BR>sprinkling over again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसेचनं
अनुषेकः --सेचनं Rewatering,<BR>sprinkling over again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्टुतिः|अनुष्टुति
अनुष्टुतिः f. Praise (in due order.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्टुभ्
अनुष्टुभ् {c1c} P. (˚स्तुभ्) To praise<BR>after, follow in praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्टुभ्
अनुष्टुभ् f. [अनु निरंतरं स्तुभ्यतेऽनया<BR>अनुष्टुप् वाक्]<BR>1 Following in praise;<BR>speech.<BR>--2 Sarasvatī.<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>class of metres consisting of four<BR>Pādas of 8 syllables each, the whole<BR>stanza consisting of 32 syllables (so<BR>called because it follows with its<BR>praise i. e. अनुष्टोभति the gāyatrī, which<BR>has {3} Pādas), अनुष्टोभनादनुष्टुप्. In later<BR>metrical systems it stands as a<BR>general name for all metres which have<BR>8 syllables in each foot (the highest<BR>possible number being computed to<BR>be 256); पंचमं लघु सर्वत्र सप्तमं द्विचतुर्थयोः ।<BR>गुरु षष्ठं च पादानां शेषेष्वनियमो मतः ॥ which<BR>rule is sometimes violated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठा
अनुष्ठा {c1c} U. (˚स्था)<BR>1 To do,<BR>perform or carry out, execute,<BR>attend to (order, duty &c.); bring<BR>about, effect, accomplish (business);<BR>विवाहदीक्षाविधिमन्वतिष्ठत् Ku. 7. 1, 1. 17;<BR>किमनुतिष्ठति भगवान् मारीचः Ś. 7;<BR>आज्ञापयतु आर्यः को नियोगोऽनुष्ठीयतामिति<BR>Ś. 1; ये मे मतमिदं नित्यमनुतिष्ठंति मानवाः<BR>Bg. 3. 31 follow; गुंरोर्वचनमनुतिष्ठ V. 5 do<BR>as your papa orders; अनुतिष्ठस्वात्मनो<BR>नियोगं M. 1 look or attend to your<BR>own duty, do your business.<BR>--2 To follow, practise, observe<BR>(धर्म, व्रत &c.); commit (a sin).<BR>--3 To<BR>rule, govern, superintend; appoint.<BR>--4 To stand by or near (with loc.);<BR>Ms. 11. 112; sit on; occupy;<BR>अनुष्ठास्यति रामस्य सीता प्रकृतमासनं Rām.<BR>--5 To follow, go after (lit.;)<BR>स्वकांतामनुतिष्ठति Rām.; नाराजके पतिं भार्या<BR>यथावदनुतिष्ठति Subhāṣ.; follow, obey.<BR>--6 To imitate, tread in; पदं<BR>चेहानुतिष्ठंति पूर्वेषां पूर्वजैः कृतं Bhāg.<BR>--7<BR>(Intrans.) (a) To place or put oneself<BR>on, be in a position, present<BR>oneself. (b) To remain, continue. (c)<BR>To be engaged in religious<BR>ceremonies (muttering prayers &c.);<BR>अनुतिष्ठतां ब्राह्मणानां M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठ
अनुष्ठ a. [स्था-क-षत्वं] Standing after<BR>or in succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0083-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठातृ
अनुष्ठातृ, --ष्ठायिन् a. Doing,<BR>performing, executing &c.; one who<BR>undertakes or begins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठायिन्
अनुष्ठातृ, --ष्ठायिन् a. Doing,<BR>performing, executing &c.; one who<BR>undertakes or begins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठानं|अनुष्ठान
अनुष्ठानं<BR>1 Doing, performance,<BR>practice, execution,<BR>accomplishment &c.; obeying, acting in<BR>conformity to; उपरुध्यते तपोऽनुष्ठानं<BR>Ś. 4 practice of religious austerities;<BR>कोऽपि वधोपायश्चिंत्यो यस्यानुष्ठानेन Pt. 1;<BR>नानुष्ठानैर्विहीनाः स्युः कुलजा विधवा इव<BR>Pt. 2. 95; H. 1. 103.<BR>--2 Commencing,<BR>undertaking, engaging in; यदि<BR>समुद्रेण सह वैरानुष्ठानं कार्यं Pt. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Commencement or course of conduct,<BR>procedure, course of action; कथं<BR>न्याय्यमनुष्ठानं मादृशः प्रतिषेधतु U. 5. 21.<BR>--4 Practice of religious rites or<BR>ceremonies, any religious rite or<BR>ceremony; किंत्वनुष्ठाननित्यत्वं<BR>स्वातंत्र्यमपकर्षति U. 1. 8; Mv. 4. 33.<BR>--नी<BR>Performance, doing &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शरीरं ‘the body of action’;<BR>(according to the Sāṃkhya doctrine)<BR>the intermediate body between the<BR>सूक्ष्म or subtle and the स्थूल or gross<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठापक
अनुष्ठापक a. Causing to perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठापनं|अनुष्ठापन
अनुष्ठापनं Causing to do an act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठायिन्
अनुष्ठायिन् a. Doing, performing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठित
अनुष्ठित p. p. Done, performed,<BR>accomplished &c.; practised, followed,<BR>&c.; संबंधाः सदनुष्ठिताः Ku. 6. 29<BR>brought about; तथानुष्ठिते that being<BR>done, thereupon; begun, undertaken;<BR>न युक्तं हि त्यक्तुं कार्यमनुष्ठितं Rām.;<BR>(used actively) following, practising;<BR>Ms. 10. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठिः|अनुष्ठि
अनुष्ठिः --ष्ठुः f. [स्था-कु] Proper<BR>order, succession (used only in instr.);<BR>˚ष्ठु, अनुष्ठ्या, अनुष्ठुया in proper order,<BR>duly, immediately, properly;<BR>immediate, direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठुः|अनुष्ठु
अनुष्ठिः --ष्ठुः f. [स्था-कु] Proper<BR>order, succession (used only in instr.);<BR>˚ष्ठु, अनुष्ठ्या, अनुष्ठुया in proper order,<BR>duly, immediately, properly;<BR>immediate, direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठेय
अनुष्ठेय, --ष्ठातव्य pot. p. To be<BR>effected, performed; followed, done<BR>conformably to; विदर्भगतमनुष्ठेयं M. 5<BR>what to do with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ठातव्य
अनुष्ठेय, --ष्ठातव्य pot. p. To be<BR>effected, performed; followed, done<BR>conformably to; विदर्भगतमनुष्ठेयं M. 5<BR>what to do with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्ण|अनुष्णं|अनुष्णः
अनुष्ण a.<BR>1 Not hot, cold,<BR>chilly; अनुष्णैरानंदाश्रुबिंदुभिः R. 12. 62.<BR>--2 Apathetic; lazy, sluggish (अलस).<BR>--ष्णः Cold touch or sensation.<BR>--ष्णा<BR>N. of a stream.<BR>--ष्णं A<BR>waterlily, blue lotus (उत्पल).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गुः<BR>(-गो ray) having cold rays, the<BR>moon.<BR>--वल्लिका N. of a plant नीलदूर्वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्वध
अनुष्वध a. [स्वधामनु, स्वधया सहितः]<BR>Accompanied by food.<BR>--धं adv.<BR>1<BR>Through or after food.<BR>--2 According<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">Page0084-b+ 57</a>]<BR>to food; after every sacrifice.<BR>--3<BR>Voluntarily, according to one's will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुष्यंदः|अनुष्यन्द|अनुष्यन्दः
अनुष्यंदः A hind wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंवरणं|अनुसंवरण
अनुसंवरणं Concealing in order<BR>or succession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंचर्|अनुसञ्चर्
अनुसंचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To walk<BR>alongside, follow, join.<BR>--2 To pursue,<BR>seek after.<BR>--3 To visit, go towards<BR>or to.<BR>--4 To penetrate, cross,<BR>traverse.<BR>--5 To become assimilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंचरणं|अनुसञ्चरण
अनुसंचरणं Following, pursuing.<BR>--adv. At every occasion of coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंतन्|अनुसन्तन्
अनुसंतन् {c8c} U.<BR>1 To extend<BR>everywhere; to diffuse, spread about,<BR>overspread.<BR>--2 To continue, join in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंततिः|अनुसन्तति
अनुसंततिः f. Continued succession,<BR>continuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंधा|अनुसन्धा
अनुसंधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To search into<BR>or after, look after, inquire into,<BR>investigate, explore, examine,<BR>ascertain; प्रसवयोग्यं स्थानमनुसंधीयतां<BR>H. 3; Ms. 12. 106.<BR>--2 To calm,<BR>compose, quiet; आत्मानमनुसंधेहि<BR>शोकचर्चां च परिहर H. 4.<BR>--3 To think of,<BR>aim at, refer or allude to, consider,<BR>deliberate; यथाकर्तव्यमनुसंधयितां<BR>H. 3; नैतदनुसंधाय मयोक्तं Mv. 6 after<BR>deliberation, or because I aimed at<BR>it; अलमनेनातीतोपालंभेन<BR>प्रस्तुतमनुसंधीयतां H. 3 let us consider what is<BR>before us, (turn to the matter in<BR>hand); अत्र… इति पुरावृत्तकथानुऽ<BR>संधेया Malli. on Ku. 1. 21 should be<BR>sought or referred to.<BR>--4 To plan,<BR>arrange; prepare, set in order;<BR>सारसत्वं दुर्गमनुसंधेहि, दुर्गशोधनमनुसंधातव्यं<BR>H. 3.<BR>--5 To follow, go after, attend,<BR>accompany; चरेण अनुसंधीयमानः<BR>Mu. 6; कस्ते निर्बंधः पदे पदे मामनुसंधातुं<BR>Mk. 1; एतौ तौ मामनुसंधत्तः Mk. 2 are<BR>after me.<BR>--6 To take up, follow,<BR>continue; तच्छेषमात्मवचसाप्यऽनुसंदधानः<BR>K. 240 following, making up the<BR>unfinished portion &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंधानं|अनुसन्धान|अनुसंधान|अनुसन्धानं
अनुसंधानं<BR>1 Inquiry,<BR>investigation; close inspection or scrutiny,<BR>examination; Mv. 7.<BR>--2 Aiming at.<BR>H.<BR>--3 Planning, arranging, getting<BR>ready &c.; दुर्गानुसंधाने को नियुज्यतां<BR>H. 3 equipping with the necessary<BR>materials.<BR>--4 A plan, scheme.<BR>--5<BR>Suitable connection.<BR>--6 (In the Vaiś.<BR>phil.) The 4th step in a syllogism,<BR>the उपनय or application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंधानिन्|अनुसन्धानिन्
अनुसंधानिन्, --संधायिन् a.<BR>Investigating, looking after; skilful in<BR>concerting plans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंधायिन्|अनुसन्धायिन्
अनुसंधानिन्, --संधायिन् a.<BR>Investigating, looking after; skilful in<BR>concerting plans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंहित
अनुसंहित p. p. Inquired into,<BR>investigated; connected with, in<BR>accordance or union with,<BR>conformable to; अहिंसा सर्वधर्मानुसंहिता Mb.;<BR>अर्थधर्मानुसंहितं वाक्यं Rām.<BR>--तं adv.<BR>In the Saṃhitā text; according to<BR>this text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसमापनं|अनुसमापन
अनुसमापनं Regular completion<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसमि
अनुसमि {c2c} P. (˚इ)<BR>1 To go to or<BR>visit successively or in order.<BR>--2 To<BR>join in following or being guided<BR>by.<BR>--3 To join, become assimilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसमयः|अनुसमय
अनुसमयः Regular or proper<BR>connection, as of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसंबद्ध|अनुसम्बद्ध
अनुसंबद्ध a. Connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसवनं|अनुसवन
अनुसवनं ind.<BR>1 After a sacrifice.<BR>--2 At every sacrifice, after ablutions.<BR>--3 Every moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसाम
अनुसाम a. [साम अनुगतः]<BR>Conciliated, friendly, favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसायं|अनुसाय
अनुसायं ind. Every evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसार्यकं|अनुसार्यक
अनुसार्यकं A fragrant<BR>substance, sandal, aloe &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0084-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अनुसूचक
