अंतर्गम्|अन्तर्गम्
अंतर्गम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go between,<BR>interpose, intervene (so as to<BR>exclude).<BR>--2 To be included or<BR>comprised in.<BR>--3 To vanish, disappear<BR>(mostly used in past part. only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्गत|अन्तर्गत|अन्तर्गतं
अंतर्गत p. p.<BR>--गामिन् a.<BR>1 Gone<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0094-c" target="_blank">Page0094-c+ 57</a>]<BR>into or between, crept into (as a bad<BR>word &c.).<BR>--2 Being or seated in,<BR>included in or by, existing in,<BR>belonging to; ˚शवे ग्रामे Ms. 4. 108; लघुद्वीपा<BR>जंबूद्वीपांतर्गता एव H. 3.; पार्थिवानि च<BR>भूतानि सागरांतर्गतानि च Rām.<BR>--3<BR>Being in the interior, hidden, concealed,<BR>internal, inward, secret, suppressed;<BR>अंतर्गतमपास्तं मे रजसोपि परं तमः<BR>Ku. 6. 60 inward; सौमित्रिरंतर्गतबाष्पकंठः<BR>R. 14. 53 with suppressed tears; K. 60;<BR>˚तां हृदयशुद्धिं 135 inward; अंतर्गतं<BR>प्राणभृतां हि वेद सर्वं भवान्भावम् R. 2. 43<BR>internal, seated in the breast or heart;<BR>˚फलारंभाः 10. 59; ˚तो हृदयाभिलाषः<BR>K. 143; ˚तेन चंद्रापीडेन 198;<BR>नेत्रवक्त्रविकारैश्च लक्ष्यतेंऽतर्गत मनः inward or secret<BR>motives of the mind Pt. 1. 44;<BR>बाह्यैर्विभावयेल्लिंगैर्भावमंतर्गतं नृणां<BR>Ms. 8. 25; ˚गतप्रार्थनं Ś. 7. 2 inwardly<BR>longing (for the same).<BR>--4 Slipped out<BR>of memory, forgotten.<BR>--5<BR>Vanished, disappeared.<BR>--6 Destroyed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपमा a concealed simile<BR>(the particle of comparison being<BR>omitted.)<BR>--मनस् = अंतर्मनस् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्धा|अन्तर्धा
अंतर्धा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To place or keep<BR>within, deposit; उदुंबरशाखामंतर्धाय<BR>अभिषिंचति Ait. Br.<BR>--2 To receive<BR>within or into oneself, admit, take<BR>in; तथा विश्वंभरे देवि मामंतर्धातुमर्हसि<BR>R. 15. 81; contain, comprise, include;<BR>(शास्त्रमेतत्) अंतर्धास्यति तत्सर्वमेतद्वः<BR>कथितं मया Mb.<BR>--3 To indicate, exhibit,<BR>display.<BR>--4 To hide or conceal<BR>oneself from, avoid the sight of, (with<BR>abl. and used in Ātm.);<BR>उपाध्यायादंतर्धत्ते P. I. 4. 28. Com. अंतर्धत्स्व<BR>रघुव्याघ्रात् Bk. 5. 32; अंतर्दधानां रक्षोभ्यः<BR>8. 71; मत्तो मांतर्धिथाः सीते 6. 15.<BR>--5 To<BR>cover up, conceal from view, hide,<BR>obscure, envelope, wrap up, veil;<BR>eclipse (fig.); अनृतेनात्मानमंतर्धाय Ch.<BR>Up.; भौमं (रजः) अंतर्दधे लोकमावृत्य सवितुः<BR>प्रभां Rām. enveloped, covered;<BR>पितुरंतर्दधे कीर्तिं शीलवृत्तिसमाधिभिः Mb.<BR>obscured or eclipsed. --pass. To be<BR>received within, be absorbed; to be<BR>covered up or concealed, be<BR>obscured or rendered invisible, become<BR>invisible; to vanish, disappear, cease<BR>to exist; इषुभिर्व्यतिसर्पद्भिरादित्योंऽ<BR>तरधीयत Mb.; ते चांतर्दधिरे नागाः ibid.;<BR>रात्रिरादित्योदयेंऽतर्धीयते Nir. disappears;<BR>आत्मन्यंतर्दधे, तत्रैवांतरधीयत &c. --Caus.<BR>--(धापयति) To render invisible,<BR>conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्धा|अन्तर्धा
अंतर्धा [धा भावे अङ्] Covering,<BR>concealment &c.;<BR>अंतर्धामुपययुरुत्पलावलीषु Śi. 8. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्धानं|अन्तर्धान|अन्तर्द्धानं
अंतर्धानं [धा-ल्युट्] Being invisible,<BR>disappearance, passing out of sight;<BR>˚व्यसनरसिका रात्रिकापालिकीयं K. P. 10;<BR>˚गम् or इ to become invisible,<BR>disappear.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गत a. disappeared,<BR>invisible.<BR>--चर a. moving invisibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्धायक|अन्तर्धायक
अंतर्धायक a. Concealing,<BR>rendering invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्धिः|अन्तर्धि|अन्तर्द्धिः|अन्तर्धिः
अंतर्धिः f. [धा-कि] Disappearance,<BR>concealment; hiding oneself from<BR>(another); अंतर्धौ येनादर्शनमिच्छति<BR>P. I. 4. 28; Śi. 8. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्हित|अन्तर्हित|अन्तर्हितं
अंतर्हित p. p.<BR>1 Placed between,<BR>separated, rendered invisible by<BR>interposition, hidden, concealed;<BR>अंतर्हिता शकुंतला वनराज्या Ś. 4; covered<BR>(with something else);<BR>अंतर्हिताशापथो जलदकाल इव K. 293;<BR>शेष्वानंतर्हितायां त्वं भूमौ Rām. uncovered or<BR>bare ground; पात्रेषु दर्भांतर्हितेषु अप<BR>आसिच्य Āśval.; अंतर्हिते आवां<BR>V. 2; अंतर्हिता यदि भवेद्वानिता न वेति<BR>Mk. 3. 4 a disguised male, a female in<BR>male dress.<BR>--2 Disappeared,<BR>vanished, become invisible; इति<BR>मंत्रयमाणः स्वयमंतर्हितः Ś. 4 withdrew from<BR>sight, became invisible; अंतर्हिते<BR>शशिनि Ś. 4. 2; तस्यायमंतर्हितसौधभाजः<BR>R. 13. 40 dwelling in a palace<BR>hidden under (the waters).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् m. N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्भू|अन्तर्भू
अंतर्भू {c1c} P. To be contained,<BR>comprised or included in; be<BR>inherent or implied in;<BR>केचिदंतर्भवंत्येषु K. P. 8; गुणाश्चिरंतनैरुक्ता<BR>ओजस्यंतर्भवंति ते S. D.; अंतर्भूय रहस्येषु<BR>तैर्वशीक्रियते हि सः Ks. 34. 204; वैदिके<BR>कर्मयोगे तु सर्वाण्येतान्यशेषतः । अंतर्भवंति<BR>क्रमशस्तस्मिंस्तस्मिन्क्रियाविधौ ॥ Ms. 12. 87.<BR>--Caus. To contain, include, imply,<BR>involve; अंतर्भावितण्यर्थोऽत्र नमिः<BR>P. III. 1. 88 Sk. involving a causal<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्भव|अन्तर्भव
अंतर्भव a. Inward, internal,<BR>inwardly situated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्भावः|अन्तर्भाव|अन्तर्भावः
अंतर्भावः<BR>1 The being included or<BR>comprised in, inclusion; तेषां<BR>गुणानामोजस्यंतर्भावः K. P. 8.<BR>--2 Inherent<BR>or natural condition or disposition.<BR>--3 Disappearance, becoming<BR>invisible; सर्वे अंतर्भावं गताः Dk. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्भावना|अन्तर्भावना
अंतर्भावना<BR>1 Inclusion.<BR>--2 Inward<BR>meditation or anxiety.<BR>--3 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-b" target="_blank">Page0095-b+ 56</a>]<BR>technical term in arithmetic, rectification<BR>of numbers by the differences of<BR>the products.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतर्भूत|अन्तर्भूत|अन्तर्भूतः
अंतर्भूत p. p.<BR>1 Included or<BR>contained in;<BR>कालभावाध्वदेशानामंतर्भूतक्रियांतरैः । सर्वैरकर्मकैर्योगे<BR>कर्मत्वमुपजायते ॥ Hariv.<BR>--2 Inward, internal,<BR>internally situated; एष वै भगवान्<BR>विष्णुरंतर्भूतः सनातनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंति|अन्ति|अन्तिः
अंति ind. [अंत्-इ] Ved.<BR>1 Near,<BR>before, in the presence of; न<BR>ही नु वो मरुतो अंत्यस्मे Rv. 1. 167. 9;<BR>1. 79. 11.<BR>--2 (Prep.) To, in the<BR>vicinity of (with gen.);<BR>मुग्धप्रभीतवदुपेयतुरंति मात्रोः Bhāg.<BR>--तिः f. An<BR>elder sister (in dramas).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ऊति a. ready with help. (--तिः f.)<BR>protection of what is near (आसन्नरक्षण)<BR>Rv. 1. 138. 1.<BR>--गृहं a house near one's<BR>own dwelling, the neighbourhood<BR>of the house.<BR>--देव a. being near the<BR>god; an adversary (at dice);<BR>Rv. 1. 180. 7.<BR>--मित्र, --वाम, --षुम्ण a. near or<BR>at hand with help, wealth, or<BR>kindness; अंतिवामा दूरे Rv. 7. 77. 4 (<BR>निकटस्थधना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतिका|अन्तिका
अंतिका<BR>1 An elder sister.<BR>--2 An<BR>oven, fireplace.<BR>--3 N. of a plant<BR>(सा-शा-तलाख्यौषधिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतिक|अन्तिक|अन्तिकं|अन्तिकः
अंतिक a. [अंतः सामीप्यं अस्यास्तीति<BR>मत्वर्थीयः ठन्; according to Nir. from<BR>आ-नी; अंतिकं कस्मात् आनीतं भवति<BR>सन्निकृष्टत्वात्]<BR>1 Near, proximate (with gen.<BR>or abl. P. II. 3. 34).<BR>--2 Reaching to<BR>the end of, reaching to; नासांतिक<BR>Ms. 2. 46.<BR>--3 Lasting till, until; as<BR>far as, up to; Ms. 3. 1; Y. 1. 36.<BR>--कं Nearness, proximity, vicinity,<BR>presence; न त्यजंति ममांतिकं H. 1. 46;<BR>oft. in comp.; ˚न्यस्त R. 2. 24;<BR>कर्ण˚चरः Ś. 1. 24; सिंहासनांतिकचरेण<BR>सहोपसर्पन् M. 1. 12 a servant in<BR>attendance upon the throne. --adv.<BR>(with abl. or gen. or as last<BR>member of comp.) Near (to), in the<BR>vicinity; अंतिकं ग्रामात्-ग्रामस्य वा Sk.;<BR>into the presence or proximity of;<BR>दूरस्थस्यैत्य चांतिकं Ms. 2. 197; प्रविष्टे<BR>पितुरंतिकं Rām.; so जनांतिकं, मृगांतिकं;<BR>अंतिकेन near (with gen.); अंतिकेन<BR>ग्रामस्य P. II. 3. 35; अंतिकात्<BR>near, closely, within the<BR>presence of; from the proximity of,<BR>from near, from (abl. or gen.<BR>or acc.); ˚कादागतः P. VI. 2. 49;<BR>रजःकणैः स्पृशद्भिर्गात्रमंतिकात् Rām.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-c" target="_blank">Page0095-c+ 57</a>]<BR>क्रीणीयाद्यस्त्वपत्यार्थं मातापित्रोर्यमंतिकात्<BR>Ms. 9. 174 from; so नैव प्रवृत्तिं<BR>शृणुमस्तयोः कस्यचिदंतिकात् Rām.; अंतिके<BR>near, closely, in the presence<BR>of or proximity of; Bg. 13. 15;<BR>दमयंत्यास्तदांतिके निपेतुः Nala. 1. 22;<BR>˚के स्त्रियाः Ms. 2. 22.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आश्रयः resorting to what is near,<BR>contiguous support (that given by<BR>a tree to a creeper).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतितः|अन्तित|अन्तितः
अंतितः ind. Ved. Near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंतिम|अन्तिम|अन्तिमः
अंतिम a. [अंते भवः, अंत डिमच्]<BR>1<BR>Immediately following.<BR>--2 Last,<BR>final, ultimate; अजातमृतमूर्खाणां<BR>वरमाद्यौ न चांतिमः H. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः<BR>the last digit, the number nine.<BR>--अंगुलिः the little finger (कनिष्ठिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंती|अन्ती
अंती An oven, fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंत्य|अन्त्य|अन्त्यं|अन्त्यः
अंत्य a. [अंते भवति वसति &c, अंताय<BR>हितः; अंत-यत्]<BR>1 Last, final (as a<BR>letter, word &c.); last (in time,<BR>order or place) P. I. 1. 47; as ह of<BR>letters, Revatī of asterisms, Mīna<BR>of the zodiacal signs &c.; अंत्ये वयसि<BR>in old age R. 9. 79; अंत्यं ऋणं<BR>R. 1. 71 last debt; ˚मंडनं 8. 71, Ku. 4. 22.<BR>--2 Immediately following (in<BR>comp.); अष्टम˚ ninth.<BR>--3 Lowest<BR>(in rank, degree or position),<BR>undermost, worst, inferior, base, vile,<BR>wretched; ˚अवस्थां गतः Pt. 4. 110<BR>reduced to the worst plight; अंत्यासु<BR>दशासु Pt. 1. 336 at perilous<BR>(critical) times; belonging to the lowest<BR>caste; चंडाल˚ स्त्रियः Ms. 11. 176;<BR>˚स्त्रीनिषेविणः 12. 59; अंत्यादपि वरं रत्नं<BR>स्त्रीरत्नं दुष्कुलादपि; शूद्राश्च संतः<BR>शूद्राणामंत्यानामंत्ययोनयः (साक्ष्यं कुर्युः) 8. 68,<BR>3. 9; 4. 79; Y. 1. 148, 2. 294.<BR>--त्यः<BR>1 A man of the lowest caste; see above.<BR>--2 N. of a plant (मुस्ता) (f. also)<BR>(the roots of which are prescribed<BR>for colic).<BR>--3 The last syllable of a<BR>word.<BR>--4 The last lunar month<BR>i. e. Fālguna.<BR>--5 A Mleccha,<BR>foreigner, barbarian.<BR>--6 (In<BR>Vaiśeshika phil.) A name for the category<BR>विशेष; अंत्यो नित्यद्रव्यवृत्तिर्विशेषः परिकीर्तितः ।<BR>Bhāṣā P.<BR>--त्या<BR>1 A technical name<BR>for त्रिज्या in astronomy.<BR>--2 A<BR>woman of the lowest tribe.<BR>--त्यं<BR>1 A<BR>measure of number; 1000 billions<BR>(1000,000,000,000,000.)<BR>--2 The<BR>12th sign of the zodiac.<BR>--3 The last<BR>member or term of a progression<BR>(series), the last figure; स्थाप्योंतवर्गो<BR>द्विगुणांत्यनिघ्नः Līlā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-a" target="_blank">Page0096-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--अनुप्रासः see under अनुप्रास.<BR>--अवसायिन् m.<BR>f. (˚यी, ˚यिनी) a man or woman of<BR>the lowest caste, begotten by a<BR>Cāṇḍāla on a Niṣādī woman; निषादस्त्री<BR>तु चांडालात्पुत्रमंत्यावसायिनम् । स्मशानगोचरं<BR>सूते बाह्यानामपि गर्हितं ॥ Ms. 10. 39; the<BR>following {7} are regarded as<BR>belonging to this class; चांडालः श्वपचः क्षत्ता<BR>सूतो वैदेहकस्तथा । मागधायोगवौ चैव<BR>सप्तैतेंऽत्यावसायिनः ॥.<BR>--आश्रमिन् m. one who<BR>belongs to the last or mendicant<BR>order.<BR>--आहुतिः, --इष्टिः f.<BR>--कर्मन्, --क्रिया last<BR>or funeral oblations, sacrifices or<BR>rites; ˚कर्म Ms. 11. 198, 5. 168;<BR>अंत्याहुतिं हावयितुं सविप्राः Bk.<BR>--ऋणं the<BR>last of the three debts which every<BR>one has to pay, i. e. begetting<BR>children; see अनृण.<BR>--गमनं intercourse<BR>by a woman of the higher caste with<BR>a man of the lowest caste.<BR>--ज a.<BR>latest born, younger, belonging to<BR>the lowest caste; ˚जैर्नृभिः Ms. 4. 61;<BR>˚स्त्री 8. 385.<BR>--(जः) {1} a Śūdra (<BR>अंत्यः सन् जायते, वर्णमध्ये शेषभवत्वात्). {2}<BR>one of the 7 inferior tribes;<BR>chāṇḍāla &c.; रजकश्चर्मकारश्च नटो वरुड एव च ।<BR>कैवर्तमेदभिल्लाश्च सप्तैते चांत्यजाः स्मृताः ॥ Yama;<BR>also Ms. 8. 279; Y. 1. 273.<BR>--(जा)<BR>a woman of the lowest caste;<BR>Ms. 11. 59, 171; Y. 3. 231.<BR>--जन्मन्, --जाति,<BR>--जातीय a. {1} one belonging to the lowest<BR>caste; प्रतिग्रहस्तु क्रियते शूद्रादप्यंत्यजन्मनः<BR>Ms. 10. 110. {2} a Śūdra; ˚तिता<BR>Ms. 12. 9. {3} a chāṇḍāla.<BR>--धनं the last<BR>term of a progression or series.<BR>--पदंमूलं the last or greatest root (in a<BR>square).<BR>--भं {1} the last lunar<BR>mansion रेवती. {2} the last sign of the<BR>zodiac; Pisces.<BR>--युगं the last or<BR>Kali age.<BR>--योनि a. of the lowest<BR>origin; Ms. 8. 68.<BR>--(निः) the lowest<BR>source or origin<BR>--लोपः dropping of<BR>the last letter or syllable of a<BR>word.<BR>--वर्णः, --वर्णा a man or woman<BR>of the lowest caste, a Śūdra male or<BR>female.<BR>--विपुला N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंत्यकः|अन्त्यक|अन्त्यकः
अंत्यकः A man of the lowest tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंत्रं|अन्त्र|अन्त्रं
अंत्रं [अंत्यते बध्यते देहोऽनेन,<BR>अंत्करणे ष्ट्रन्; according to Uṇ. 4. 163<BR>अम् क्त्रं] An entrail, intestine; अंत्रभेदनं<BR>क्रियते प्रश्रयश्च Mv. 3 the vitals of<BR>the heart are rent (मर्मभिदः वाचः उच्यंते<BR>इत्यर्थः).<BR>--त्री N. of a plant (used against<BR>colic or wind in the stomach; cf.<BR>अजांत्री, छगलांत्री).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आदः<BR>a worm in the intestines.<BR>--कूजः.<BR>कूजनं, --विकूजनं the rumbling noise<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">Page0096-b+ 56</a>]<BR>in the bowels; पक्वाशयस्थोंत्रकूजं शूलं<BR>नाभौ करोति वा Suśr.<BR>--पाचक [अंत्रस्थं<BR>दोषं पाचयति] N. of a medicinal plant<BR>Æschynomene Grandiflora.<BR>--मांसं<BR>a kind of roasted flesh.<BR>--वृद्धिः f.<BR>inguinal hernia, rupture, swelling of<BR>the scrotum.<BR>--शिला N. of a river<BR>rising from the Vindhya mountain.<BR>--स्रज् f. a garland of intestines<BR>(worn by नृसिंह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंत्रंधमिः|अन्त्रन्धमि|अन्त्रंधमि|अन्त्रंधमिः
अंत्रंधमिः f. Indigestion,<BR>inflammation of bowels; flatulence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंद्|अन्द्
अंद् {c1c} P. To bind, fasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंदः|अन्द|अन्दः
अंदः Binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंदुः|अन्दु|अन्दुः
अंदुः --दूः f. [अंद्यते बध्यते अनेन, अंद्-कू,<BR>कूप्रत्ययांतः निपातः Uṇ. 1. 93] also अंदुकः,<BR>अंदूकः<BR>1 A chain or fetter.<BR>--2 A chain<BR>for the elephant's feet; गजमंदूरिव<BR>निश्चलं चकार Śi. 20. 51; ˚निनादः 11. 7.<BR>--3 A sort of ornament worn round<BR>the ankles; cf. नूपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंदूः
अंदुः --दूः f. [अंद्यते बध्यते अनेन, अंद्-कू,<BR>कूप्रत्ययांतः निपातः Uṇ. 1. 93] also अंदुकः,<BR>अंदूकः<BR>1 A chain or fetter.<BR>--2 A chain<BR>for the elephant's feet; गजमंदूरिव<BR>निश्चलं चकार Śi. 20. 51; ˚निनादः 11. 7.<BR>--3 A sort of ornament worn round<BR>the ankles; cf. नूपुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंदिका|अन्दिका
अंदिका<BR>1 An oven, fireplace.<BR>--2<BR>An elder sister (cf. -अंतिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंदोलयति
अंदोलयति Den. P. To swing,<BR>agitate, rock to and fro, oscillate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंदोलनं|अन्दोलन
अंदोलनं Swinging, oscillating,<BR>waving; द्राक्चामरांदोलनात् Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंध्|अन्ध्
अंध् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To make blind, blind;<BR>अंधयन् भृंगमालाः Śi. 11. 19; तिमिरे<BR>जनस्य दृशमंधयति 9. 21.<BR>--2 To be or<BR>become blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंध|अन्ध|अन्धं|अन्धः
अंध a.<BR>1 Blind (lit. and fig.);<BR>devoid of sight, unable to see (at<BR>particular times); दिवांधाः प्राणिनः<BR>केचिद्रात्रावंधास्तथापरे; made blind,<BR>blinded; स्रजमपि शिरस्यंधः क्षिप्तां<BR>धुनोत्यहिशंकया Ś. 7. 24; मदांधः blinded<BR>by intoxication; so दर्पांधः, क्रोधांधः;<BR>काम˚, लोभ˚, अज्ञान˚; सहजांधदृशः<BR>स्वदुर्नये Śi. 16. 29 blind to his own<BR>wicked acts.<BR>--2 Making blind,<BR>preventing the sight; utter, pitchy,<BR>complete, thick (darkness)<BR>Ms. 8. 94; सीदन्नंधे तमसि U. 3. 38;<BR>Māl. 9. 8, 20; See ˚कूप, ˚तामसं infra.<BR>--धं<BR>1<BR>Darkness.<BR>--2 Spiritual ignorance;<BR>अज्ञान or अविद्या q. v.<BR>--3 Water;<BR>also, turbid water.<BR>--धः<BR>1 A kind of<BR>mendicant (परिव्राजक) who has<BR>completely controlled his organs; तिष्ठतो<BR>व्रजतो वापि यस्य चक्षुर्न दूरगम् । चतुष्पदां<BR>भुवं मुक्त्वा परिव्राडंध उच्यते ॥<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of the zodiacal signs at<BR>particular periods; (<BR>नष्टद्रव्यलाभालाभोपयोगयुक्तो राशिभेदः); मेषो वृषो मृगेंद्रश्च रात्रावंधाः<BR>प्रकीर्तिताः । नृयुक्कर्कटकन्याश्च दिवांधाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-c" target="_blank">Page0096-c+ 57</a>]<BR>परिकीर्तिताः ॥<BR>--धाः? (pl.) N. of a people<BR>see अंध्र.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अलजी a blind<BR>boil or abscess in the eyes (one<BR>that does not open or suppurate).<BR>--अहिः, --अहिकः a blind serpent, i. e.<BR>one that is not poisonous. (--हिः,<BR>--हिकः) N. of a fish (कुचिका).<BR>--कारः<BR>[अंधं करोति] darkness (lit. and<BR>fig.); लीनं दिवाभीतमिवांधकारं<BR>Ku. 1. 12; काम˚, मदन˚; अंधकारतामुपयाति चक्षुः<BR>K. 36 grows dim;<BR>बाष्पजलधारांधकारितमुखी K. 161, 286.<BR>--कूपः [<BR>अंधयतीत्यंधः, अंधः कूपः] {1} a well the<BR>mouth of which is hidden; a well<BR>overgrown with plants &c. {2} [<BR>अंधस्य दृष्ट्यभावस्य कूप इव] mental<BR>darkness, infatuation. {3} N. of a hell,<BR>to which those who tease and kill<BR>harmless creatures are condemned.<BR>--तमसं (P. V. 4. 79),<BR>--तामसं,<BR>--धातमसं deep or complete darkness;<BR>लोकमंधतमसात्क्रमोदितौ R. 11. 24;<BR>अंधतमसमिव प्रविशामि U. 7 the gloom of hell;<BR>प्रध्वंसितांधतमसस्तत्रोदाहरणं रविः Śi. 2. 33.<BR>--(सा) night.<BR>--तामिस्रः --श्रः (स्रं also).<BR>{1} complete or deep darkness<BR>(especially of the soul); तमिस्रोष्टदशधा तथा<BR>भवत्यंधतामिस्रः Sāṅ. K. 48 (<BR>भयविशेषविषयकोऽभिनिवेशः);<BR>तस्यामंधतामिस्रमभ्यध्यायत् Mv. 1. {2} spiritual ignorance<BR>(देहे नष्टे अहमेव नष्टःइतिरूपमज्ञानं);<BR>enveloped in utter darkness.<BR>--(स्रः, स्रं) N. of<BR>a division of Tartarus or infernal<BR>regions, the second of the 21 hells to<BR>which those who seduce the wives of<BR>others and enjoy them are<BR>condemned. According to Bhavabhūti persons<BR>committing suicide were condemned<BR>to this hell; cf. अंधतामिस्रा ह्यसूर्या नाम ते<BR>लोकास्तेभ्यः प्रतिविधीयंते य आत्मघातिन<BR>इत्येवमृषयो मन्यंते U. 4; Ms. 4. 88, 197;<BR>Y. 3. 224; doctrine of annihilation<BR>after death.<BR>--धी a. mentally blind.<BR>--पूतना a demoness supposed to<BR>cause diseases in children; यो द्वेष्टि<BR>स्तनमतिसारकासहिक्काछर्दीभिर्ज्वरसहिताभिरर्द्यमानः ।<BR>दुर्वर्णः सततमधःशयोऽम्लगंधिस्तं<BR>ब्रूयुर्वरभिषजोंधपूतनार्तम् Suśr.<BR>--मूषा a small covered<BR>crucible with a hole in the side.<BR>--मूषिका [अंधं दृष्ट्यभावं मुष्णाति, मुष्-ण्वुल्]<BR>N. of a plant or grass देवताड (<BR>तत्सेवनेन चक्षुष्मत्ता भवतीति वैद्यकप्रसिद्धिः).<BR>--रात्री<BR>dark night (Ved.).<BR>--वर्त्मन् m. [अंधं<BR>सूर्यप्रकाशराहित्याद्वर्त्म यत्र] the seventh<BR>skandha or region of wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधंकरण|अन्धङ्करण|अन्धंकरण
अंधंकरण a. Making blind (<BR>P. III. 2. 56).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधंभविष्णु|अन्धम्भविष्णु|अन्धंभविष्णु
अंधंभविष्णु, --भावुक a. Becoming<BR>blind (P. III. 2. 57).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधंभावुक|अन्धम्भावुक|अन्धंभावुक
अंधंभविष्णु, --भावुक a. Becoming<BR>blind (P. III. 2. 57).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधक|अन्धक|अन्धकः
अंधक a. [अंध्-कन्] Blind; अंधकः<BR>कुब्जकश्चैव Pt. 5. 91.<BR>--कः<BR>1 N. of an<BR>Asura, son of Kaśyapa and Diti<BR>and killed by Śiva. [He is<BR>represented as a demon with 1000 arms and heads,<BR>2000 eyes and feet, and called Andhaka,<BR>because he walked like a blind man,<BR>though he could see very well; स<BR>व्रजत्यंधवद्यस्मादनंधोपि हि भारत । तमंधंकोयं नाम्नेति<BR>प्रोचुस्तत्र निवासिनः ॥ He was slain by<BR>Śiva when he attempted to carry off the<BR>Pārijāta tree from heaven; whence Śiva<BR>is called Andhakaripu, -ari, -dvish &c.<BR>According to the Matsya Purāṇa Andhaka<BR>was admitted to the class of Gaṇas by<BR>Śiva, at his importunities and humble<BR>supplication, when he was about to be<BR>killed by the god for having attempted<BR>to carry off his wife Pārvatī].<BR>--2<BR>N. of a descendant of Yadu and<BR>ancestor of Kṛṣṇa and his<BR>descendants, a grandson of Kroṣṭu, son<BR>of Yudhājit who, together with his<BR>brother Vṛṣṇi is the ancestor of<BR>the celebrated family of<BR>Andhakavṛṣṇis; P. IV. 1. 114,<BR>VI. 2. 34.<BR>--3 N. of a sage, son of<BR>Mamatā and of Utathya, elder<BR>brother of Bṛhaspati.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः<BR>--रिपुः, --शत्रुः, --घाती, --असुहृद् &c. slayer<BR>of Andhaka, epithets of Śiva.<BR>--वर्तः<BR>N. of a mountain.<BR>--वृष्णि m. pl.<BR>descendants of अंधक and वृष्णि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधिका|अन्धिका
अंधिका [अंध्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 Night.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of game or sport, probably<BR>blindman's-buff; gambling (तया हि<BR>जनः अंध इव विवेकंशून्यः क्रियते Tv.).<BR>--3<BR>A woman of a particular character,<BR>one of the classes of women.<BR>--4 A<BR>disease of the eye.<BR>--5 = सर्षपी, = सिद्धा<BR>q. v. (अस्या अत्यंतसेवनात् दृष्टिर्क्षयो जायते<BR>इति वैद्यकप्रसिद्धिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधीकृ|अन्धीकृ
अंधीकृ {c8c} U. To make blind, blind;<BR>˚कृतात्मा blinded in mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधीभू|अन्धीभू
अंधीभू To become blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधस्|अन्धस्
अंधस् n. [अद्-असुन् नुम् धश्च;<BR>अदेर्नुम्धौ च Uṇ. 4. 205] Food; द्विजातिशेषेण<BR>यदेतदंधसा Ki. 1. 39; सशेष एवांधसि<BR>असावतृप्यत् Dk. 133, 157 (supposed<BR>to have in the Veda the senses of<BR>Soma, the herb itself, or its juice,<BR>juice, ghee or boiled rice, but usually<BR>taken to mean ‘food’ only by<BR>Indian lexicographers and<BR>commentators). [cf. Gr. andhos].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधुः|अन्धु|अन्धुः
अंधुः [fr. अम् Uṇ. 1. 27]<BR>1 A<BR>well; आपीनोंऽधुः P. VI. 1. 28 Sk.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-b" target="_blank">Page0097-b+ 59</a>]<BR>The male organ of generation;<BR>वाक्पाणिपादपाय्वंधुसंज्ञान्याहुर्मनीषिणः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंधुलः|अन्धुल|अन्धुलः
अंधुलः [अंध्-उलच्] A kind of<BR>tree, Acacia Sirissa (शिरीष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंध्रः|अन्ध्र|अंध्र|अन्ध्रः
अंध्रः (pl.)<BR>1 N. of a people and<BR>the country inhabited by them.<BR>[The country of the Andhras is said to<BR>be the modern Telangaṇa. But the<BR>limits were probably confined to the<BR>Ghats on the west and the rivers<BR>Godāvarī and Kṛṣṇa on the north and south.<BR>It bordered on Kaliṅga (See Dk. 7th<BR>Ullāsa), and its capital Andhranagara is<BR>probably the old town of Veṅgi or Vegi.<BR>According to Daṇḍin, there was near it a<BR>lake ‘like the ocean and crested with<BR>cranes’ which description can only refer<BR>to the lake Colair which has an area of<BR>over 150 miles; जगन्नाथादूर्ध्वभागादर्वाक्<BR>श्रीभ्रमरात्मकात् । तावदंध्राभिधो देशः].<BR>--2 N. of<BR>a dynasty of kings.<BR>--3 A man of a<BR>mixed (low) caste, being born of a<BR>Vaideha father and Kārāvara<BR>mother, who lives by killing game;<BR>Ms. 10. 36.<BR>--4 A kind of fowler.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जातिः the Andhra tribe.<BR>--भृत्याः<BR>N. of a dynasty of kings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नं|अन्न|अन्नः
अन्नं [अद्-क्त; अनित्यनेन, अन्-नन्;<BR>according to Yāska, from अद्, अद्यते<BR>अत्ति च भूतानि; or from आ-नम्, आ<BR>आभिमुख्येन ह्येतन्नतं प्रह्वीभूतं भवति भोजनाय<BR>भूतानां]<BR>1 Food (in general); अद्यतेऽत्ति<BR>च भूतानि तस्मादन्नं तदुच्यते T. Up.;<BR>मेदोऽसृङ्मांसमज्जास्थि वदंत्यन्नं मनीषिणः<BR>Ms. 3. 182; अहमन्नं भवान्भोक्ता H. 1. 54<BR>I am your prey &c.; चराणामन्नमचराः<BR>Ms. 5. 29.<BR>--2 Food as representing<BR>the lowest form in which the<BR>Supreme Soul is manifested, being the<BR>coarsest and last of the 5 vestures<BR>(कोश) in which the soul is clothed<BR>and passes from body to body in<BR>the long process of metempsychosis<BR>--“the nutrimentitious vesture or<BR>visible body in the world of sense”<BR>(स्थूलशरीर called अन्नमयकोश).<BR>--3<BR>Boiled rice; अन्नेन व्यंजनं P. II. 1. 34.<BR>--4 Corn (bread corn); ता (आपः)<BR>अन्नमसृजंत तस्माद्यत्र क्व च वर्षति तदेव<BR>भूयिष्ठमन्नं भवति Ch. Up.;<BR>आदित्याज्जायते वृष्टिर्वृष्टेरन्नं ततः प्रजाः ।<BR>Ms. 3. 76; कृत˚ 9. 219; 10. 86,<BR>12. 65.<BR>--5 Water.<BR>--6 Earth (पृथिव्या<BR>अन्नहेतुत्वादन्नशब्दवाच्यता).<BR>--7 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--न्नः The sun (स हि<BR>अन्नहेतुवृष्टिहेतुः).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अकालः = अनाकाल<BR>q. v.<BR>--अत्तृ, --आदिन् --आहारिन् eating<BR>food.<BR>--अद a. {1} eating food. {2}<BR>having a good appetite (दीप्ताग्नि).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-c" target="_blank">Page0097-c+ 58</a>]<BR>--(दः) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--अद्यं proper<BR>food, food in general; Ms. 3. 82,<BR>4. 112, 11. 144.<BR>--आच्छादनं, --वस्त्रं<BR>food and clothing, food and<BR>raiment, the bare necessaries of life.<BR>--आयुः (अन्नायु) consisting of,<BR>living by, food, desirous of food (<BR>अन्नबंधनः, अन्नजीवनः).<BR>--कालः hour of<BR>dinner; meal-time.<BR>--किट्टः = ˚मल q. v.<BR>--कूटः a large heap of boiled rice.<BR>--कोष्ठकः {1} a cupboard; granary. {2}<BR>Viṣṇu. {3} the sun.<BR>--गतिः f. the<BR>passage of food, gullet (cf.<BR>बहिःस्रोतस्).<BR>--गंधिः dysentery, diarrhœa.<BR>--ज, --जात a. produced from food as<BR>the primitive substance.<BR>--जलं food<BR>and water, bare subsistence.<BR>--तेजस्<BR>a. having the vigour caused by<BR>food.<BR>--द, --दातृ, --दायिन्, --प्रद a. {1} giving<BR>food; वारिदस्तृप्तिमाप्नोति सुखमक्षय्यमन्नदः<BR>Ms. 4. 229. {2} epithet of Śiva.<BR>--दा<BR>N. of Durgā or Annapūrṇā.<BR>--दासः<BR>[अन्नेन पालितो दासः शाक. त.] a servant<BR>who works for food only, one who<BR>becoms a servant or slave by<BR>getting food only.<BR>--देवता the deity<BR>supposed to preside over articles of<BR>food.<BR>--दोषः {1} sin arising from<BR>eating prohibited food; Ms. 5. 4.<BR>{2} a defect in the food eaten;<BR>derangement of food or the<BR>humours of the body; आलस्यादन्नदोषाच्च<BR>मृत्युर्विप्राञ् जिघांसति Ms. 5. 4.<BR>--द्वेषः<BR>dislike of food, loss of appetite.<BR>--पतिः<BR>lord or possessor of food, epithet<BR>of Savitṛ, Agni, and Śiva.<BR>--पाकः<BR>cooking of food; digestion of food<BR>(by the fire in the stomach).<BR>--पू a.<BR>purifying food, epithet of the Sun.<BR>--पूर्ण a. filled with, possessed of, food.<BR>--(र्णा) a form of Durgā (the<BR>goddess of plenty); ˚ईश्वरी N. of Durgā<BR>or a form of Bhairavī.<BR>--पेयं =<BR>वाजपेयं q. v.<BR>--प्रलय a. being<BR>dissolved into food after death.<BR>--प्राशः,<BR>--प्राशनं the ceremony of giving<BR>a newborn child food to eat for<BR>the first time, one of the 16<BR>Saṃskāras performed between the 5th<BR>and 8th month (usually in the sixth,<BR>Ms. 2. 34) with preliminary<BR>oblations to fire (Mar. उष्टावण); Ms. 2. 34;<BR>Y. 1. 12.<BR>--ब्रह्मन्, --आत्मन् m. Brahma<BR>as represented by food.<BR>--भक्त a.<BR>[अन्नार्थं भक्तः दासः] = अन्नदास q. v.<BR>--भुज्<BR>a. eating food, epithet of Śiva.<BR>--मय a. see below.<BR>--मलं {1} excrement,<BR>feces; P. VI. 1. 148 Sk. {2} spirituous<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0098-a" target="_blank">Page0098-a+ 57</a>]<BR>liquor; सुरा वै मलमन्नानां Ms. 11. 94.<BR>--रक्षा precautions as to eating food.<BR>--रसः essence of food, chyle; food<BR>and drink, nutriment;<BR>नानाविधानन्नरसान् वन्यमूलफलाश्रयान् तेभ्यो ददौ Rām.<BR>--वस्त्रं = ˚आच्छादनं q. v.<BR>--विकारः<BR>{1} transformation of food,<BR>assimilation. {2} disorder of the stomach<BR>caused by indigestion. {3} seminal<BR>discharge (of man); semen itself;<BR>cf. अन्नाद्रेतः संभवति.<BR>--व्यवहारः the law<BR>or custom relating to food, i. e. the<BR>custom of eating together or not<BR>with other persons.<BR>--शेषः leavings<BR>of food, offal.<BR>--संस्कारः<BR>consecration of food.<BR>--होमः a sacrifice (with<BR>10 materials) connected with the<BR>Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नमय
अन्नमय a. (यी f.) Consisting or<BR>made of food, composed of or<BR>containing boiled rice; ˚कोशः-षः the gross<BR>material body, the स्थूलशरीर, which<BR>is sustained by food and which is<BR>the fifth or last vesture or wrapper<BR>of the soul; see अन्न (2) above and<BR>also कोश; hence, also the material<BR>world, the coarsest or lowest form<BR>in which Brahma is considered as<BR>manifesting itself in the worldly<BR>existence.<BR>--यं Plenty of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्नावृध्
अन्नावृध् a. [अन्नं वर्धते अनेन वृध्-करणे<BR>क्विप्, पूर्वपददीर्घः] Increasing food;<BR>Rv. 10. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्य|अन्यः
अन्य a. [अन् अघ्न्यादि˚ य; अन्यः,<BR>न्यस्मै, ˚स्मात्; n. अन्यत् &c.]<BR>1 Another,<BR>different, other (भिन्न); another,<BR>other (generally); स एव त्वन्यः क्षणेन<BR>भवतीति विचित्रमेतत् Bh. 2. 40; अन्यदेव<BR>भागधेयमेते निर्वपंति Ś. 2; सर्वमन्यत्<BR>everything else; किमुतान्यहिंस्राः R. 2. 62;<BR>changed, altered; संप्रत्यन्ये वयं<BR>Bh. 3. 66 quite different persons; oft. in<BR>comp. अन्यसंगात्, अनन्यपरायण,<BR>अनन्यसाधारण &c.<BR>--2 Other than, different<BR>from, else than (with abl. or as last<BR>member of comp.); नास्ति<BR>जीवितादन्यदभिमततरमिह सर्वजंतूनां K. 35;<BR>कोस्ति धन्यो मदन्यः Bv. 4. 37; उत्थितं<BR>ददृशेऽन्यच्च कबंधेभ्योन किंचन R. 12. 49;<BR>किमन्यदस्याः परिषदः श्रुतिप्रसादनतः Ś. 1; oft.<BR>used in addition to ऋते or विना; ऋते<BR>समुद्रादन्यः को बिभर्ति वडवानलं<BR>Pt. 5. 35; किं नु खलु मे प्रियादर्शनादृते शरणमन्यत्<BR>Ś. 3.<BR>--3 Another person, one<BR>different from self (opp. स्व, आत्मीय);<BR>वासश्च धृतमन्यैर्न धारयेत् Ms. 4. 66.<BR>--4<BR>Strange, unusual, extraordinary;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0098-b" target="_blank">Page0098-b+ 57</a>]<BR>अन्य एव स प्रकारः K. 168; अन्या<BR>जगद्धितमयी मनसः प्रवृत्तिः Bv. 1. 69; धन्या<BR>मृदन्यैव सा S. D.<BR>--5 Ordinary, any one;<BR>निरातंकः कन्यामन्योपि याचते Mv. 1. 31;<BR>cf. इतर.<BR>--6 Additional, new, more;<BR>अन्यान् दशसुवर्णान्प्रयच्छ Mk. 2 another<BR>ten (coins); अन्यदन्यन्नलिनदलशयनं<BR>K. 157 new and new (changing<BR>every now and then); अन्यस्मिन्<BR>दिवसे another day; one of a number<BR>(with gen.); अन्यच्च moreover,<BR>besides, and again (used to connect<BR>sentences together); एक-अन्य the<BR>one the other; Me. 78; see under<BR>एक also; अन्य-अन्य one-another;<BR>अन्यः करोति अन्यो भुंक्ते one does,<BR>another suffers; अन्यन्मुखे<BR>अन्यन्निर्वहणे Mu. 5; अन्यदुप्तं जातमन्यत्<BR>Ms. 9. 40, 99; 8. 204; कर्णे लगति चान्यस्य<BR>प्राणैरन्यो वियुज्यते Pt. 1. 305;<BR>अन्यदुच्छृंखलं सत्त्वमन्यच्छास्त्रनियंत्रितं Śi. 2. 62;<BR>अन्य-अन्य-अन्य &c. one, another,<BR>third, fourth &c.; जल्पंति सार्धमन्येन<BR>पश्यंत्यन्यं सविभ्रमाः । हृद्गतं चिंतयंत्यन्यं<BR>प्रियः को नाम योषिताम् Pt. 1. 135;<BR>मनस्यन्यदवचस्यन्यत् कर्मण्यन्यद्दुरात्मनाम्; (in<BR>pl.) केचित्-अन्ये some-others;<BR>एके-अन्ये-तथान्ये Ms. 10. 70; 4. 9;<BR>12. 123. [cf. L. alius; Gr.<BR>allos for aljos, Zend anya].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. having a different<BR>meaning, sense, or purpose.<BR>--असाधारण a.<BR>not common to others, peculiar.<BR>--आश्रयण a. going or passing<BR>over to another.<BR>--उदर्य a. born from<BR>another.<BR>--(र्यः) a step-mother's<BR>son, a half-brother.<BR>--(र्या) a<BR>half-sister.<BR>--ऊढा a. married to<BR>another; another's wife.<BR>--कारुका a worm bred in excrement (<BR>शकृत्कीटः).<BR>--क्षेत्रं {1} another field. {2}<BR>another or foreign territory. {3}<BR>another's wife.<BR>--ग, गामिन् a. {1} going<BR>to another. {2} adulterous,<BR>unchaste; वणिजां तु कुलस्त्रीव स्थिरा<BR>लक्ष्मीरनन्यगा Ks. 21. 56; 19. 27.<BR>--गोत्र a.<BR>of a different family or lineage.<BR>--चित्त a. having the mind fixed on<BR>some thing or some one else; see<BR>˚मनस्.<BR>--ज --जात a. of a different<BR>origin.<BR>--जन्मन् n. another life or<BR>existence, regeneration,<BR>metempsychosis.<BR>--दुर्वह a. difficult to be borne<BR>by others.<BR>--देवत, --त्य, --दैवत्य a.<BR>addressed or referring to another deity<BR>(as a Vedic Mantra).<BR>--धर्मन् a.<BR>having another or different property.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0098-c" target="_blank">Page0098-c+ 58</a>]<BR>--(र्मः) different property or<BR>characteristic.<BR>--धी a. whose mind is<BR>turned away from God.<BR>--नाभि a.<BR>belonging to another family.<BR>--पदार्थः<BR>{1} another substance. {2} the sense<BR>of another word; ˚प्रधानो बहुव्रीहिः the<BR>Bahuvrīhi compound essentially<BR>depends on the sense of another word.<BR>--पर a. {1} devoted to another or<BR>something else. {2} expressing or<BR>referring to something else.<BR>--पुष्टा,<BR>--भृता ‘reared by another,’ epithet of<BR>the cuckoo, which is supposed to be<BR>reared by the crow (called अन्यभृत्);<BR>अप्यन्यपुष्टा प्रतिकूलशब्दा Ku. 1. 45;<BR>कलमन्यभृतासु भाषितं R. 8. 59.<BR>--पूर्वा [अन्यः<BR>पतिः पूर्वो यस्याः] {1} a woman already<BR>promised or betrothed to another.<BR>{2} a remarried widow (पुनर्भू)<BR>see अनन्यपूर्व.<BR>--बीज, --बीजसमुद्भव,<BR>--समुत्पन्न an adopted son (born from<BR>other parents), one who may be<BR>adopted as a son for want of<BR>legitimate issue.<BR>--भृत् m. a crow (rearing<BR>another, it being supposed to sit on<BR>the eggs of the cuckoo and to rear<BR>its young ones), cf. Ś. 5. 22.<BR>--मनस्, --मनस्क, --मानस a. {1} having the<BR>mind fixed on something else;<BR>inattentive. {2} fickle, versatile, unsteady;<BR>अन्यमनसः स्त्रियः H. 1. 111<BR>absentminded; possessed by a demon.<BR>--मातृजः a half-brother (born of another<BR>mother) Y. 2. 139.<BR>--राजन्, --राष्ट्रीय a.<BR>subject to another king or kingdom<BR>(Ved.).<BR>--रूप a. having another form,<BR>changed, altered; पद्मिनीं वान्यरूपां<BR>Me. 83.<BR>--(पं) another or changed<BR>form; ˚पेण in another form.<BR>--लिंग,<BR>--ग, --क a. following the gender of another<BR>word (i. e. the substantive), an<BR>adjective; ऊषवानूषरो द्वावप्यन्यलिंगौ Ak.<BR>--वादिन् a. {1} giving false evidence.<BR>{2} a defendant in general.<BR>--वापः the<BR>cuckoo leaving the eggs in the<BR>nests of other birds.<BR>--विवर्धित a. =<BR>पुष्ट a cuckoo.<BR>--व्रत a. following other<BR>(than Vedic) observances, devoted<BR>to other gods, infidel.<BR>--शाखः --खकः a<BR>Brāhmaṇa who has gone over to<BR>another school (of religion &c.); an<BR>apostate.<BR>--संक्रांत a. fixed on or<BR>transferred to another (woman); ˚हृदयः<BR>आर्यपुत्रः M. 3, 4.<BR>--संगमः intercourse<BR>with another; illicit intercourse.<BR>--साधारण a. common to many others.<BR>--स्त्री another's wife, a woman not<BR>one's own. [In Rhetoric she is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-a" target="_blank">Page0099-a+ 58</a>]<BR>considered as one of three chief female<BR>characters in a poetical composition,<BR>the other two being स्वीया and<BR>साधारणी स्त्री. अन्या may be either a damsel<BR>or another's wife. The ‘damsel’ is one<BR>not yet married, who is bashful and<BR>arrived at the age of puberty. As<BR>‘another's wife’ she is fond of<BR>festivals and similar occasions of<BR>amusement, who is a disgrace to her family<BR>and utterly destitute of modesty, see<BR>S. D. 108-110]. ˚गः an adulterer<BR>Ms. 8. 386. [Note. Some compounds<BR>under अन्य will be found under अनन्य.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यक
अन्यक a. Another, other (= अन्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्
अन्यत् a. (अन्य n.) Another &c.<BR>--ind. Again, moreover, besides &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ {1} having a different<BR>meaning. {2} referring to or<BR>expressing another sense.<BR>--(र्थः) a<BR>different meaning.<BR>--आशा desire of<BR>something else.<BR>--आशिस् f. another's<BR>blessing.<BR>--आस्था devotion or<BR>attachment to another.<BR>--उत्सुक a. longing<BR>for another.<BR>--रागः attachment to<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतम|अन्यतमः
अन्यतम a. [अन्य-डतम] (declined<BR>like a noun and not a pronoun)<BR>One of many, any one out of a large<BR>number (with gen. or in comp.);<BR>जपन्वान्यतमं वेदं Ms. 11. 76; 6. 32,<BR>4. 13; Y. 2. 22, 3. 253; (<BR>अन्यतरान्यतमशब्दौ अव्युत्पन्नौ प्रातिपदिके इति कैयटः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतर|अन्यतरः
अन्यतर a. (declined like a<BR>pronoun) One of two (persons or things),<BR>either of the two (with gen.);<BR>तयोर्मुनिकुमारयोरन्यतरः K. 151; संतः<BR>परीक्ष्यान्यतरद्भजंते M. 1. 2 the one or the<BR>other; युवयोरन्यतरागच्छतु Ś. 3;<BR>Ms. 2. 111.; 9. 171; other, different;<BR>अन्यतर-अन्यतर the one-the other;<BR>अन्यतरस्यां (loc. of ˚रा) either way,<BR>in both ways, optionally; frequently<BR>used by Pāṇini in his Sūtras in<BR>the sense of वा or विभाषा;<BR>हृक्रोरन्यतरस्यां, आत्मनेपदेष्वन्यतरस्यां &c. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतरतः
अन्यतरतः adv. On one of two<BR>sides; ˚दंत having teeth on one side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतरेद्युः
अन्यतरेद्युः adv. [अन्यतरस्मिन्नहनि-एद्युस्]<BR>On either of two days, on one day<BR>or on another, P. V. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतः
अन्यतः adv.<BR>1 From another; न<BR>चान्यतस्तस्य शरीररक्षा R. 2. 4; तीर्थोदकं<BR>च वह्निश्च नान्यतः शुद्धिमर्हतः U. 1. 13.<BR>--2<BR>On one side; अन्यतः-अन्यतः,<BR>एकतःअन्यतः on the one side, on the other<BR>side; तपनमंडलदीपितमेकतः<BR>सततनैशतमोवृतमन्यतः Ki. 5. 2; एकवस्तु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-b" target="_blank">Page0099-b+ 57</a>]<BR>सकलानि निमित्तान्यतो हि मनसः प्रतिपत्तिः Nīti.<BR>--3 To another place, towards some<BR>other person or direction; गंतव्यं वा<BR>ततोऽन्यतः Ms. 2. 200; अन्यतोपि<BR>नयने प्रेरयंत्या Ś. 2. 2; आर्ये व्रजामोन्यतः<BR>R. 6. 82.<BR>--4 From another ground or<BR>motive.<BR>--5 On the other side; on the<BR>contrary.<BR>--6 Otherwise; in another<BR>place, elsewhere.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरण्यं<BR>Ved. a land which is woody here<BR>and there.<BR>--एत, --एतस्, --एनी Ved.<BR>variegated or spotted on one side.<BR>--घातिन् a. striking in one direction.<BR>--वात a. suffering occasional wind<BR>(rheumatism.).<BR>--(तः) a sort of<BR>eye-disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यतस्त्यः|अन्यतस्त्य
अन्यतस्त्यः [अन्यतो भवः, त्यप्] An<BR>enemy, adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यत्र
अन्यत्र adv. [अन्य-त्रल्] (oft. =<BR>अन्यस्मिन् with a subst. or adj. force.)<BR>1<BR>Elsewhere, in another place (with<BR>abl.); अपत्याधिकारादन्यत्र<BR>लौकिकमपत्यमात्रं गोत्रं P. IV. 2. 39 Com.; sometimes<BR>with विना; विना मलयमन्यत्र चंदनं न प्ररोहति<BR>Pt. 1. 41; (with verbs of motion) to<BR>another place.<BR>--2 On another occasion,<BR>at another time than; oft. (in comp.);<BR>मधुपर्के च यज्ञे च पितुर्दैवतकर्मणि । अत्रैव<BR>पशवो हिंस्या नान्यत्रेत्यब्रवीन्मनुः<BR>Ms. 5. 41.<BR>--3 Except, without, other than;<BR>यथा फलानां जातानां नान्यत्र पतनाद्भयं ।<BR>एवं नरस्य जातस्य नान्यत्र मरणाद्भयं ॥<BR>Rām. Mv. 6. 8; R. 14. 32; Bg. 3. 9;<BR>Y. 1. 215; अन्यत्र नैमिषेयसत्रात् V. 5,<BR>Ms. 4. 164; oft. with the force of<BR>the nom. case; देवा अन्यत्रैवाश्विभ्यां<BR>सत्त्रं निषेदुः Kauṣ. Br. (अन्यत्र = अन्ये).<BR>--4 Other wise, in another way, in<BR>the other case, in the other sense;<BR>सुराज्ञि देशे राजन्वान् स्यात्ततोन्यत्र<BR>राजवान् Ak.; राजन्वती भूः, राजवानन्यत्र;<BR>चर्मण्वती नदी चर्मवती अन्यत्र<BR>P. VIII. 2. 12, 14 Sk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मनस् --चित्त a.<BR>whose mind is directed to something<BR>else, inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथा
अन्यथा ind. [अन्य-प्रकारार्थे था]<BR>1<BR>Otherwise, in another way or<BR>manner, in a different manner; यदभावि न<BR>तद्भावि भावि चेन्न तदन्यथा H. 1; with अतः,<BR>इतः or ततः otherwise than, in a<BR>manner different from; अतोन्यथा प्रवृत्तिस्तु<BR>राक्षसो विधिरुच्यते Ms. 5. 31; Bg. 13. 11.<BR>अन्यथा-अन्यथा in one way, in<BR>another (different) way; योन्यथा<BR>संतमात्मानमन्यथा भाषते Ms. 4. 255;<BR>सत्त्वभंगभयाद्राज्ञां कथयंत्यन्यथा पुरः ।<BR>अन्यथाविवृतार्थेषु स्वैरालापेषु मंत्रिणः Mu. 4. 8.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-c" target="_blank">Page0099-c+ 57</a>]<BR>अन्यथा कृ (a) to do otherwise,<BR>change or alter; न हि दैवं शक्यमन्यथा<BR>कर्तुमभियुक्तेनापि K. 62; न स्वभावोत्र<BR>मर्त्यानां शक्यते कर्तुमन्यथा Pt. 1. 258;<BR>Ś. 6. 13; (b) to act otherwise,<BR>violate, transgress, go against; त्वया<BR>कदाचिदपि मम वचनं नान्यथा कृतं Pt. 4;<BR>(c) to destroy, undo, frustrate,<BR>baffle, defeat (hope, plan &c.),<BR>कर्तुमकर्तुमन्यथाकर्तुं समर्थ ईश्वरः; ममेच्छां<BR>मान्यथा कृथाः Ks. 22. 51; लाभं<BR>कुर्याच्च योन्यथा Y. 2. 195; (d) to make<BR>false, falsify; ख्यातो लोकप्रवादोयं<BR>भरतेनान्यथा कृतः Rām.; अमात्यः<BR>प्राड्विवाको वा यत्कुर्युः कार्यमन्यथा Ms. 9. 234<BR>to do wrongly; ˚ग्रह्, --मन्, --संभावय्,<BR>समर्थय्, -विकल्पय् &c. to take or think<BR>to be otherwise, to misunderstand,<BR>understand wrongly; अलमन्यथा<BR>गृहीत्वा न खलु मनस्विनि मया प्रयुक्तमिदं<BR>M. 1. 20; अलमस्मानन्यथा संभाव्य<BR>Ś. 1; किं मामन्यथा संभावयसि K. 147;<BR>Ś. 3. 19; जनोन्यथा भर्तृमतीं विशंकते<BR>Ś. 5. 17 suspects to be otherwise<BR>(than chaste); ˚भू or या to be<BR>otherwise, be changed or altered, be<BR>falsified; न मे वचनमन्यथा भवितुमर्हति Ś. 4;<BR>शोकार्तस्य प्रवृत्तो मे श्लोको भवतु नान्यथा<BR>Rām.; तयोर्महात्मनोर्वाक्यं नान्यथा याति<BR>सांप्रतं Rām.<BR>--2 Otherwise, or else, in<BR>the contrary case; व्यक्तं नास्ति<BR>कथमन्यथा वासंत्यपि तां न पश्येत् U. 3; स्तेनोऽ<BR>न्यथा भवेत् Ms. 8. 144; Y. 1. 86, 2. 288;<BR>on the other hand, on the contrary.<BR>--3 Falsely, untruly; किमन्यथा<BR>भट्टिनी मया विज्ञापितपूर्वा V. 2;<BR>किमन्यथा भट्टिन्यै विज्ञापितं M. 4; न खल्वन्यथा<BR>ब्राह्मणस्य वचनं V. 3; यो न्यायमन्यथा<BR>ब्रूते स याति नरकं नरः Pt. 3. 107;<BR>H. 3. 20; Ms. 8. 90.<BR>--4 Wrongly,<BR>erroneously, badly, as in अन्यथासिद्ध q. v.<BR>below; see under {1} also.<BR>--5 From<BR>another motive, cause, or ground;<BR>दुर्वाससःशापादियं त्वया प्रत्यादिष्टा नान्यथा<BR>Ś. 7. [cf. L. aliuta.].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुपपत्तिः f. see अर्थापत्ति.<BR>--कारः changing,<BR>altering.<BR>--(रं) adv. in a different<BR>manner, differently P. III. 4. 27.<BR>--ख्यातिः {1} erroneous conception<BR>of the Spirit, title of a<BR>philosophical work. {2} wrong conception in<BR>general (in phil.).<BR>--भावः alteration,<BR>change, being otherwise, difference;<BR>बहूनां व्यक्तीनामेकदेशेनान्यथाभावः<BR>P. V. 4. 53; change of view or mind; मयि<BR>˚भावो न कर्तव्यः Ch. Up.<BR>--वादिन् a.<BR>speaking differently or falsely; speaking<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">Page0100-a+ 58</a>]<BR>falsely or inconsistently; (in law) a<BR>prevaricator, prevaricating witness.<BR>--वृत्ति a. {1} changed, altered. {2}<BR>affected, perturbed; disturbed by strong<BR>emotions; मेघालोके भवति<BR>सुखिनोप्यन्यथावृत्ति चेतः Me. 3.<BR>--सिद्ध a.<BR>proved or demonstrated wrongly; (in<BR>Nyāya) said of a cause (कारण) which<BR>is not the true one, but only refers<BR>to accidental and remote<BR>circumstances (as the ass employed to<BR>fetch clay &c. in the case of a घट<BR>or jar) which do not invariably<BR>contribute to the result, see कारण;<BR>this अन्यथा˚ is said to be of 3<BR>kinds in Tarka K., but 5 are<BR>mentioned in Bhāṣā P. 19-22.<BR>--द्धं,<BR>--सिद्धिः f. wrong demonstration; one<BR>in which arguments, not being true<BR>causes, are advanced; an unessential<BR>cause, an accidental or concomitant<BR>circumstance Bhāṣā P. 16.<BR>--स्तोत्रं satire, irony; Y. 2. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0099-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यथयति
अन्यथयति Den. P. To change, alter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदा
अन्यदा ind.<BR>1 At another time, on<BR>another occasion, in any other case;<BR>अन्यदा भूषणं पुंसां क्षमा लज्जेव योषिताम्<BR>Śi. 2. 44, R. 11. 73.<BR>--2 Once, one<BR>day, at one time, once upon a time.<BR>--3 Sometimes, now and then.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यदीय
अन्यदीय a.<BR>1 Belonging to<BR>another.<BR>--2 Being or existing in<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यर्हि
अन्यर्हि ind. At another time<BR>(= अन्यदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृक्ष्
अन्यादृक्ष् --श् --श a. [अन्य इव पश्यति,<BR>अन्यादृश्, कर्मकर्तरि क्स, क्विन्, कञ् वा<BR>P. III. 2. 60]<BR>1 Of another kind, like<BR>another.<BR>--2 Changed, unusual, strange;<BR>यात्राप्रतिनिवृत्तमन्यादृशं भवंतमवधारयामि<BR>Māl. 1; अन्याशदृमेव भगवत्या वचनं 2;<BR>being different or otherwise; न खलु<BR>अन्यादृशेषु युष्मादृश्यः पक्षपातिन्यो भवंति<BR>4; अन्यादृश्येव क्षणमजनिष्ट Dk. 106,<BR>K. 309; अन्यादृशीरचना कस्यापि<BR>वलीमुखस्य Mv. 6 strange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृश्
अन्यादृक्ष् --श् --श a. [अन्य इव पश्यति,<BR>अन्यादृश्, कर्मकर्तरि क्स, क्विन्, कञ् वा<BR>P. III. 2. 60]<BR>1 Of another kind, like<BR>another.<BR>--2 Changed, unusual, strange;<BR>यात्राप्रतिनिवृत्तमन्यादृशं भवंतमवधारयामि<BR>Māl. 1; अन्याशदृमेव भगवत्या वचनं 2;<BR>being different or otherwise; न खलु<BR>अन्यादृशेषु युष्मादृश्यः पक्षपातिन्यो भवंति<BR>4; अन्यादृश्येव क्षणमजनिष्ट Dk. 106,<BR>K. 309; अन्यादृशीरचना कस्यापि<BR>वलीमुखस्य Mv. 6 strange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यादृश|अन्यादृशः
अन्यादृक्ष् --श् --श a. [अन्य इव पश्यति,<BR>अन्यादृश्, कर्मकर्तरि क्स, क्विन्, कञ् वा<BR>P. III. 2. 60]<BR>1 Of another kind, like<BR>another.<BR>--2 Changed, unusual, strange;<BR>यात्राप्रतिनिवृत्तमन्यादृशं भवंतमवधारयामि<BR>Māl. 1; अन्याशदृमेव भगवत्या वचनं 2;<BR>being different or otherwise; न खलु<BR>अन्यादृशेषु युष्मादृश्यः पक्षपातिन्यो भवंति<BR>4; अन्यादृश्येव क्षणमजनिष्ट Dk. 106,<BR>K. 309; अन्यादृशीरचना कस्यापि<BR>वलीमुखस्य Mv. 6 strange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युः|अन्येद्यु
अन्येद्युः ind. [अन्य-एद्युस्<BR>P. V. 3 22]<BR>1 On the other or following day;<BR>अन्येद्युरात्मानुचरस्य भावं<BR>जिज्ञासमाना R. 2. 26.<BR>--2 One day, once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्येद्युष्क|अन्येद्युष्कः
अन्येद्युष्क a. [अन्येद्युर्भवः, कन्]<BR>Occurring every day, daily, diurnal;<BR>अन्येद्युष्कमहोरात्रादेककालं प्रवर्तते Suśr.<BR>--ष्कः A quotidian fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्य|अन्योन्यं
अन्योन्य a. [अन्य-कर्मव्यतिहारे द्वित्वं,<BR>पूर्वपदे सुश्च] One another, each other,<BR>mutual (treated like a pronoun).<BR>In many cases the use of this word<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-b" target="_blank">Page0100-b+ 57</a>]<BR>corresponds to the use of the word<BR>‘each other’ or ‘one another’ in<BR>English; अन्योन्यं ताडयतः Mk. 9<BR>they strike each other (अन्यः अन्यं<BR>ताडयति). Thus अन्यः may be regarded<BR>as the subject and अन्यं as the object<BR>of the verb, as in English. The<BR>second अन्य may, therefore, in many<BR>cases stand in the instr., gen., or<BR>loc. cases; अन्योन्यैराहताः संतः<BR>सस्वनुर्भीमनिःस्वनाः Rām.; अन्योन्यस्य<BR>व्यतिलुनंति P. I. 3. 16 Sk. But there are<BR>several instances, especially when<BR>अन्योन्य enters into compound, in<BR>which the first अन्य loses all its<BR>nominative force and becomes a sort<BR>of oblique case, or an irregular com<BR>pound of अन्य and अन्य, see<BR>P. VIII. 1. 12 Sk.; अन्योन्यस्याव्यभीचारः<BR>Ms. 9. 101; oft. in comp. and translated<BR>by ‘mutual’, ‘reciprocal’, ‘mutually’;<BR>˚शोभाजननात् Ku. 1. 42; so ˚कलह,<BR>˚दर्शन, &c.<BR>--न्यं ind. Mutually.<BR>--न्यं (In<BR>Rhet.) A figure of speech, the<BR>‘Reciprocal’, in which two things do the same<BR>act to each other;<BR>अन्योन्यमुभयोरेकक्रियायाः करणं मिथः । त्वया सा शोभते तन्वी<BR>तया त्वमपि शोभसे । रजन्या शोभते चंद्रश्चंद्रेणापि<BR>निशीथिनी S. D. 724.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्यासः<BR>reciprocal attribution of identity (<BR>अन्योन्यतादात्म्यारोपः); जलव्योम्ना घटाकाशो यथा<BR>सर्वस्तिरोहितः । तथा जीवे च कूटस्थः<BR>सोन्योन्याध्यास उच्यते ॥<BR>--अपहृत a. taken<BR>from one another, taken secretly.<BR>--अभावः mutual non-existence or<BR>negation; one of the two main kinds<BR>of अभाव; it is reciprocal negation of<BR>identity, essence, or respective<BR>peculiarity, and is equivalent to difference<BR>(भेद); तादात्म्यसंबंधावच्छिन्नप्रतियोगिकोऽ<BR>न्योन्याभावः, as घटः पटो न भवति; it exists<BR>between two notions which have no<BR>property in common.<BR>--आश्रय a.<BR>mutually dependent.<BR>--(यः) mutual or<BR>reciprocal dependence, support, or<BR>connection; reciprocal relation of<BR>cause and effect (a term in Nyāya).<BR>--उक्तिः f. conversation.<BR>--पक्षनयनं<BR>transposition of numbers from one<BR>side to another.<BR>--भेदः mutual<BR>dissension or enmity; so ˚कलह.<BR>--मिथुनं<BR>mutual union.<BR>--विभागः mutual<BR>partition of an inheritance made<BR>by the sharers (without the presence<BR>of any other party).<BR>--वृत्तिः f. mutual<BR>effect of one thing upon another.<BR>--व्यतिकरः --संश्रयः reciprocal action<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">Page0100-c+ 56</a>]<BR>or influence; mutual relation of<BR>cause and effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यंग|अन्यङ्ग
अन्यंग a. Ved. Spotless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्या
अन्या a. Not drying up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय|अन्यायः
अन्याय a. [न. ब.] Unjust,<BR>improper; ˚दंडः unjust punishment;<BR>˚यःपरदारपृच्छाव्यवहारः Ś. 5.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Any<BR>unjust or unlawful action; see न्याय;<BR>नरेष्वन्यायवर्तिषु Ms. 7. 16 acting<BR>unjustly, following evil courses;<BR>अन्यायेन unjustly, improperly; नापृष्टः<BR>कस्यचिद् ब्रूयान्न चान्यायेन पृच्छतः<BR>Ms. 2. 110.<BR>--2 Injustice, impropriety.<BR>--3 Irregularity, disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यायिन्
अन्यायिन् a. Unjust, improper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्याय्य|अन्याय्यः
अन्याय्य a.<BR>1 Unjust, unlawful.<BR>--2 Improper, unbecoming,<BR>indecorous.<BR>--3 Not authoritative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्यून|अन्यूनः
अन्यून a. Not defective or<BR>deficient, complete, whole, entire;<BR>˚अधिक neither deficient nor<BR>superfluous.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. not having<BR>a defective limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योकस्
अन्योकस् a. Not residing in<BR>one's own house (dwelling in<BR>another's).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्योन्य|अन्योन्यं
अन्योन्य See under अन्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्ष|अन्वक्षः
अन्वक्ष a. [अनुगतःअक्षं इंद्रियं गतिसमा.]<BR>1 Visible, perceptible.<BR>--2 Following,<BR>close on the heels of, immediately<BR>following.<BR>--क्षं ind.<BR>1 Afterwards,<BR>after; आरोह त्वं… सीतां चारोपयान्वक्षं<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 Immediately after,<BR>forthwith, directly; Y. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्षरसंधिः|अन्वक्षरसन्धि|अन्वक्षरसंधि|अन्वक्षरसन्धिः
अन्वक्षरसंधिः A kind of Vedic<BR>Saṃdhi, that of a vowel and<BR>consonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वंच्|अन्वञ्च्
अन्वंच् a. [अनु-अंच्-क्विप्; nom.<BR>अन्वंङ् m., अन्वक् n. अनूची f.]<BR>1 Going<BR>after, following; तस्मादिमे अन्वंचो<BR>मासा यंति Śat. Br.; त्वामन्वंचो वयं स्मसि<BR>Ait. Br.<BR>--2 Lying lengthwise,<BR>horizontal; अनूचि in the rear or behind,<BR>from behind; आगच्छतोनूचि गजस्य<BR>घंटयोः Śi. 12. 34 (पृष्ठदेशे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वक्
अन्वक् ind.<BR>1 Afterwards.<BR>--2 From<BR>behind; पिदधानमन्वगुपगम्य दृशौ<BR>Śi. 9. 76.<BR>--3 Friendly disposed,<BR>favourably; अन्वग्भूत्वा, --भावं, --आस्ते becoming<BR>friendly disposed P. III. 4. 64 Sk. (<BR>अग्रतः पार्श्वतः पृष्ठतो वानुकूलो भूत्वा आस्ते;<BR>अन्वग्भूत्वा तिष्ठति = पृष्ठतो भूत्वा).<BR>--4 (with acc.)<BR>After; तां… अन्वग्ययौ मध्यमलोकपालः<BR>R. 2. 16 went after or followed her;<BR>तमन्वगिंद्रप्रमुखाश्च देवाः Ku. 7. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वन्
अन्वन् a. [अन्-वनिप्] Following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0100-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वय|अन्वयः
अन्वय See under अन्वि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्तितृ
अन्वर्तितृ m. Ved. An inviter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वर्थ
अन्वर्थ a. [अनुगतः अर्थं] Having the<BR>meaning clear or intelligible, having<BR>a meaning easily deducible from<BR>the etymology of the word; hence,<BR>true to the sense, significant; तथैव<BR>सोभूदन्वर्थो राजा प्रकृतिरंजनात्<BR>R. 4. 12; अन्वर्था तैर्वसुंधरा Ki. 11. 64;<BR>Śi. 12. 23; अन्वर्थ एवायमधुना प्रलापो वर्तते<BR>U. 3.; अन्वर्थतोपि ननु राक्षस राक्षसोसि<BR>Mu. 5. 7 in the true sense of the<BR>word, properly so called.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रहणं literal acceptation of the<BR>meaning of a word (opp. to रूढ or<BR>conventional).<BR>--संज्ञा {1} an<BR>appropriate name, a technical term which<BR>directly conveys its own meaning;<BR>e. g. भविष्यंती a name for ‘future’ is<BR>an अन्वर्थसंज्ञा compared with ऌट्. {2}<BR>a proper name the meaning of which<BR>is obvious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववकिरणं|अन्ववकिरण
अन्ववकिरणं Scattering about<BR>successively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववचारः|अन्ववचार
अन्ववचारः Descending and<BR>following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववसर्गः|अन्ववसर्ग
अन्ववसर्गः [सृज्-घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Slackening, letting loose (opp. आयाम).<BR>--2<BR>Permission to do as one likes (<BR>कामचारानुज्ञा), one of the senses of अपि<BR>P. I. 4. 96; see अपि.<BR>--3 Following<BR>one's own will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववसित
अन्ववसित a. Connected with,<BR>bound or fastened to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववायः|अन्ववाय
अन्ववायः A race, family,<BR>lineage; अन्ववायमवदातमाकृतिः Ki. 13. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्ववेक्षा
अन्ववेक्षा Regard, consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टका
अन्वष्टका [अनुगतोऽष्टकां] The 9th<BR>day of the dark half of the three<BR>months following the full moon in<BR>मार्गशीर्ष, i. e. पौष, माघ and फाल्गुन;<BR>पितॄंश्चैवाष्टकास्वर्चोन्नित्यमन्वष्टकासुच Ms. 4. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टक्यं|अन्वष्टक्य
अन्वष्टक्यं A Śrāddha or any such<BR>ceremony performed on the अन्वष्टका<BR>days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वष्टमदिशं|अन्वष्टमदिश
अन्वष्टमदिशं ind. Towards the<BR>north-west direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वस्त
अन्वस्त a. [fr. अस् to throw] Shot<BR>or hurled along, shot; interwoven<BR>(as in silk); chequered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वहं|अन्वह
अन्वहं ind. Day after day; every<BR>day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाख्या
अन्वाख्या {c2c} P. To repeat in<BR>succession, enumerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाख्यानं|अन्वाख्यान
अन्वाख्यानं<BR>1 Subsequent mention<BR>or enumeration; an explanation<BR>referring to what is mentioned<BR>before.<BR>--2 Section, chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचयः|अन्वाचय
अन्वाचयः [प्रधानस्य पश्चादन्यः<BR>आचीयते बोध्यते यत्र, चि-अच्]<BR>1 Statement of<BR>a secondary (गौण) rite or action<BR>after the mention of a primary<BR>(प्रधान) one; adding an object of<BR>secondary importance to the main<BR>object, one of the senses of the<BR>particle च; चान्वाचये समाहारे Ak.;<BR>अन्यतरस्यानुषंगिकत्वेऽन्वाचयः; as भो<BR>भिक्षामट गां चानय where going out to beg<BR>is enjoined to the beggar as his<BR>principal object, and the bringing<BR>of a cow (if he can see any) is tack<BR>ed on to it as a secondary object.<BR>--2 Such an object itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाचित
अन्वाचित a. Secondary, inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाजे
अन्वाजे ind. [अनु आंजयत्यनेन,<BR>अनुआजि-डे Tv.] (Used like उपाजे only<BR>with कृ) So as to assist or support<BR>the weak (दुर्बलस्य बलाधाने);<BR>optionally regarded as a preposition; ˚कृत्य<BR>or ˚कृत्वा supporting, assisting (a<BR>weak person); दुर्बलस्य बलमाधाय<BR>P. I. 4. 73 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादिश्
अन्वादिश् {c6c} P. To name or<BR>mention again; to mention or refer<BR>to in a subsequent place, employ<BR>again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादिष्ट
अन्वादिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Mentioned after<BR>or according to; employed again;<BR>अन्वादिष्टः पुरुषः अनुपुरुषः P. VI. 2. 190<BR>Sk.<BR>--2 (Hence) Inferior, of<BR>secondary importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वादेशः|अन्वादेश
अन्वादेशः Subsequent or repeated<BR>mention, referring to what has<BR>been previously mentioned;<BR>reemployment of the same word in a<BR>subsequent part of a sentence, or of<BR>the same thing to perform a<BR>subsequent operation; आदेशः कथनं<BR>अन्वादेशः अनुकथनं Kāśi. on P. II. 4. 32.<BR>(इदं and एतद् are said to assume the<BR>forms एने, एनौ, एनान् &c. in the sense<BR>of अन्वादेश; किंचित्कार्यं विधातुमुपात्तस्य<BR>कार्यांतरं विधातुं पुनरुपादानं अन्वादेशः; e. g.<BR>अनेन व्याकरणमधीतं एनं छंदोऽध्यापय;<BR>अनयोः पवित्रं कुलं एनयोः प्रभूतं स्वं Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधानं|अन्वाधान
अन्वाधानं [अग्निस्थापनस्य<BR>पश्चादाधानं] Putting on or depositing fuel on<BR>the sacred fires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधिः|अन्वाधि
अन्वाधिः [अनु पश्चादाधीयते, धा-कि]<BR>1<BR>(In civil law) {1} A bail, deposit or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">Page0101-c+ 55</a>]<BR>security delivered to a third person<BR>to be handed over ultimately<BR>to the right owner; अर्थमार्गणकार्येषु<BR>अन्यास्मिन्वचनान्मम । दद्यास्त्वमिति यो दत्तः<BR>स इहान्वाधिरुच्यते ॥.<BR>--2 A second<BR>deposit.<BR>--3 [अनुगतः संततः आधिः]<BR>Constant anxiety, remorse, repentance,<BR>regret (after the committal of a<BR>bad act).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेयं|अन्वाधेय
अन्वाधेयं --यकं A sort of स्त्रीधन or<BR>woman's property, presented to her<BR>after marriage by her husband's<BR>or father's family, or by her own<BR>relatives; विवाहात्परतो यच्च लब्धं<BR>भर्तृकुलात्स्त्रिया । अन्वाधेयं तु तद्द्रव्यं लब्धं पितृ- (v. l.<BR>बंधु-) कुलात्तथा ॥ Kāty. quoted by<BR>Kull. on Ms. 9. 195; Y. 2. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाधेयकं|अन्वाधेयक
अन्वाधेयं --यकं A sort of स्त्रीधन or<BR>woman's property, presented to her<BR>after marriage by her husband's<BR>or father's family, or by her own<BR>relatives; विवाहात्परतो यच्च लब्धं<BR>भर्तृकुलात्स्त्रिया । अन्वाधेयं तु तद्द्रव्यं लब्धं पितृ- (v. l.<BR>बंधु-) कुलात्तथा ॥ Kāty. quoted by<BR>Kull. on Ms. 9. 195; Y. 2. 144.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहित|अन्वाहितं
अन्वाहित = अन्वाधि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाध्यः|अन्वाध्य
अन्वाध्यः A class of divinities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वांत्र्य|अन्वान्त्र्य
अन्वांत्र्य a. Ved. Being in the<BR>entrails.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायतन
अन्वायतन a. Latitudinal.<BR>--नं<BR>ind. In the house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायत्त
अन्वायत्त a. Ved. In accordance<BR>with (अनुगत &c.); following after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वायात्या
अन्वायात्या A deity invoked by<BR>the verb अन्वाया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारभ्
अन्वारभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To begin,<BR>commence.<BR>--2 To touch; अंसेऽध्वर्युमन्वारभते<BR>Āśval.; यदि मां संस्पृशेद्रामः<BR>सकृदन्वारभेत वा । धनं वा यौवराज्यं वा<BR>जीवेयमिति मे मतिः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारब्ध
अन्वारब्ध p. p.<BR>1 Touched on the<BR>back or on any part of the body;<BR>विष्णोः कर्माणीति वाचयति<BR>रूपमन्वारब्धमिति Kāty.<BR>--2 That which<BR>has touched or on has been placed<BR>the body (as the hand).<BR>--3 Followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारभ्य
अन्वारभ्य pot. p. To be touched<BR>along with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारंभः|अन्वारम्भ|अन्वारम्भः
अन्वारंभः, --भणं Touching, contact,<BR>especially touching the यजमान (the<BR>performer of a sacrifice) to make<BR>him entitled to the fruits and<BR>merits of the holy rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारंभणं|अन्वारम्भण
अन्वारंभः, --भणं Touching, contact,<BR>especially touching the यजमान (the<BR>performer of a sacrifice) to make<BR>him entitled to the fruits and<BR>merits of the holy rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारंभणीया|अन्वारम्भणीया
अन्वारंभणीया An initiatory or<BR>preliminary ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारुह्
अन्वारुह् {c1c} P. To follow in<BR>ascending, especially the funeral pile;<BR>to ascend, climb, mount; अन्वारोहच्च<BR>सुग्रीवः (गिरिं) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वारोहणं|अन्वारोहण
अन्वारोहणं A woman's ascending<BR>the funeral pile after or with the<BR>body of her husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वास्
अन्वास् {c2c} A.<BR>1 To be seated near<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-a" target="_blank">Page0102-a+ 56</a>]<BR>or round; सखायमन्वास्ते Mb.; to wait<BR>upon, serve, attend upon;<BR>सखीभ्यामन्वास्यते Ś. 3; अन्वासितमरुंधत्या स्वाहयेव<BR>हविर्भुजं R. 1. 56; to sit after one (acc.<BR>of person); तां अन्वास्य R. 2. 24.<BR>--2 To<BR>perform, as a religious ceremony;<BR>संध्यामन्वास्य पश्चिमां Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0101-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासनं|अन्वासन
अन्वासनं<BR>1 Service, attendance,<BR>waiting upon, worship.<BR>--2 Taking a<BR>seat after another.<BR>--3 Regret, sorrow.<BR>--4 A place of industry, manufactory,<BR>work-shop &c.<BR>--5 An oily or<BR>cooling enema.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वासीन
अन्वासीन pres. p. Sitting down<BR>after, seated along side of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहार्यः|अन्वाहार्य|अन्वाहार्य्य|अन्वाहार्य्यं
अन्वाहार्यः (also<BR>--र्यं)<BR>--र्यकं [अनु<BR>मासि मासि आह्रियते, कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>1 A<BR>sacrificial gift or offering presented to<BR>the priests (Sāy. अन्वाहरति<BR>यज्ञसंबंधिदोषजातं परिहरत्यनेन इत्यन्वाहार्यो नाम ऋत्विग्भ्यो<BR>देय ओदनः).<BR>--2 The monthly Śrāddha<BR>performed in honor of the manes on<BR>the day of new moon; पितॄणां<BR>मासिकं श्राद्धमन्वाहार्यं विदुर्बुधाः Ms. 3. 123.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पचनः the southern<BR>sacrificial fire used in the अन्वाहार्य<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहिक
अन्वाहिक a. (की f.) Daily, diurnal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वाहित|अन्वाहितं
अन्वाहित = अन्वाधेय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वि
अन्वि {c2c} P. [अनु-इ]<BR>1 To follow,<BR>come or go after, succeed; गच्छतः<BR>पृष्ठतोऽन्वियात् Ms. 4. 154; एनां… प्रयता<BR>प्रातरन्वेतु R. 1. 90; शुनीमन्वेति श्वा<BR>Bh. 3. 18; attend, accompany, accrue to;<BR>कर्मफलं कर्तारमन्वेति.<BR>--2 (a) To follow<BR>(in grammar or construction); be<BR>connected or construed with;<BR>धातुरादेशमन्वेति Mb. see अन्वय below. (b)<BR>To obey, conform to, be guided by;<BR>यश्चित्तमन्वेति परस्य Mb.<BR>--3 To seek;<BR>to fall to one's lot (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयः|अन्वय
अन्वयः [इ कर्तरि भावे वा अच्]<BR>1<BR>Going after, following; also,<BR>follower, retinue, attendants; का<BR>त्वमेकाकिनी भीरु निरन्वयजने वने Bk. 5. 66.<BR>--2 Association, connection, relation;<BR>गंधः कटुकान्वयः = कटुकान्वितः.<BR>--3 The<BR>natural order or connection of words<BR>in a sentence, construing,<BR>grammatical order or relation; पदानां<BR>परस्पराकांक्षा योग्यता च, or शब्दानां<BR>परस्परमर्थानुगमनं; तात्पर्याख्यां वृत्तिमाहुः पदार्थान्वयबोधने<BR>S. D; logical connection of words,<BR>अत्र (in the ex. तिष्ठतु सर्पिः) सर्पिःशब्दस्य<BR>स्थितिक्रियायामन्वयः P. VIII. 3. 44 Sk;<BR>परस्परनिरपेक्षस्यानेकस्य एकस्मिन्नन्वयः समुच्चयः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-b" target="_blank">Page0102-b+ 57</a>]<BR>P. II. 2. 29 Sk.<BR>--4 Drift, tenor,<BR>purport.<BR>--5 Race, family, lineage;<BR>रघूणामन्वयं वक्ष्ये R. 1. 9, 12; 3. 27; 12. 33;<BR>अन्वयगुणः Mv. 4. 22 virtue of my<BR>race.<BR>--6 Descendants, posterity; ताभ्य<BR>ऋते अन्वयः Y. 2. 117; स˚ along with<BR>the family or descendants;<BR>Ms. 2. 168; Pt. 1. 27.<BR>--7 Logical<BR>connection of cause and effect, logical<BR>continuance; जन्माद्यस्य यतोऽन्वयादितरतः<BR>Bhāg.<BR>--8 Being seen (प्रत्यक्ष);<BR>स्यात्साहसं त्वन्वयवत् प्रसभं कर्म यत्कृतं ।<BR>निरन्वयं भवेत्स्तेयं Ms. 8. 332.<BR>--9 (In<BR>Nyāya) Statement of the constant<BR>and invariable concomitance of the<BR>हेतु (middle term) and the साध्य<BR>(major term) of an Indian syllogism<BR>(हेतुसाध्ययोर्व्याप्तिरन्वयः). In the familiar<BR>instance पर्वतो वह्निमान् धूमवत्त्वात् the<BR>relation यत्र यत्र धूमस्तत्र तत्र वह्निः<BR>(wherever there is smoke there is fire) is<BR>called अन्वय or अन्वयव्याप्ति, अन्वय, in fact,<BR>corresponds to the universal A<BR>proposition of European logic ‘All A<BR>is B.’ The ‘व्यतिरेकव्याप्ति’ means an<BR>assertion of the concomitance of the<BR>absence of साध्य and the absence<BR>of हेतु (तदभावयोः हेत्वभावसाध्याभावयोः<BR>व्याप्तिः) and corresponds to the<BR>converted A proposition ‘All<BR>notB is not-A’; or in Sanskrit यत्र<BR>यत्र वह्निर्नास्ति तत्र तत्र धूमोपि नास्ति; and<BR>a cause or हेतु is said to be<BR>connected with its effect by<BR>अन्वयव्यतिरेकव्याप्ति when both the affirmative and<BR>negative relations between the<BR>thing to be proved and the cause<BR>that proves can be equally asserted;<BR>such a Hetu alone makes the<BR>argument perfectly sound and<BR>incapable of refutation. This process of<BR>arriving at the Vyāpti or universal<BR>proposition corresponds to the<BR>methods of Agreement and Difference<BR>in Mill's Logic; साध्ये निश्चितमन्वयेन<BR>घटितं Mu. 5. 10.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आगत a.<BR>hereditary; Pt. 1, 3; ˚तं वैरं Pt. 3.<BR>--ज्ञः<BR>a genealogist; अथ स्तुते बंदिभिरन्वयज्ञैः<BR>R. 6. 8.<BR>--व्यतिरेक (˚कौ or ˚कं) {1}<BR>positive and negative assertion;<BR>agreement and contrariety or difference;<BR>see above. {2} rule and exception.<BR>--व्याप्तिः f. affirmative assertion or<BR>agreement, affirmative universal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयवत्|अन्वयवन्त्
अन्वयवत् a.<BR>1 Having a connection<BR>or consequence, following.<BR>--2<BR>Belonging to a race or family; born of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">Page0102-c+ 56</a>]<BR>noble family, noble, high-born;<BR>सत्यपि अन्वयवति अवरोधजने K. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वयिन्
अन्वयिन् a. Connected as with a<BR>consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वित|अन्वितः
अन्वित p. p.<BR>1 Followed or attended<BR>by, in company with, joined by;<BR>अमात्यपुत्रैः सवयोभिरन्वितः R. 3. 28.<BR>--2 Possessed of, having,<BR>possessing, endowed with; full of, seized or<BR>struck with, overpowered by; with<BR>instr. or in compound; कुलान्वितं<BR>कुकुलजा निंदंति Pt. 1. 415; धैर्य˚;<BR>गुण˚, वित्त˚; विस्मय˚ struck with<BR>wonder; भय˚, क्रोध˚, लोभ˚ &c. &c.<BR>--3 Connected with, linked to,<BR>following (as a consequence).<BR>--4<BR>Connected grammatically; वर्णाः पदं<BR>प्रयोगार्हानन्वितैकार्थबोधकाः<BR>S. D. 9.<BR>--5 Understood, reached by the<BR>mind.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. having a<BR>meaning which is easily understood<BR>from the context. ˚वादः-अभिधानवादः<BR>a doctrine of the Mīmāṃsakas that<BR>words in a sentence convey<BR>meanings not independently or generally,<BR>but as connected with one another<BR>in that particular sentence; see<BR>अभिहितान्वयवादिन् under अभिधा and K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विति|अन्वितिः
अन्विति a. Won over or<BR>favourably disposed by means of a<BR>salutation.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1 Following.<BR>--2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विष्
अन्विष् {c6c} P. To desire, seek,<BR>search for or after, look out for,<BR>seek to get; अतः<BR>सिद्धिसमेताभ्यामुभाभ्यामन्वियेष सः R. 17. 47. (--{c4c} P.) To<BR>seek, search, look out for &c.; न<BR>रत्नमन्विष्यति मृग्यते हि तत् Ku. 5. 45;<BR>अन्वेष्टव्यो यदसि भुवने भूतनाथः शरण्यः<BR>U. 2. 13; to inquire, investigate; किं<BR>वृथा तर्केण अन्विष्यते Ś. 5. --Caus.<BR>To seek, search &c; यामन्वेषयतां<BR>प्रयांति सततं सर्वे समाप्तिं गुणाः Bh. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्विष्ट|अन्विष्टः
अन्विष्ट p. p. Desired, sought,<BR>searched; यद्वायुरन्विष्टमृगैः किरातैः<BR>Ku. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषः|अन्वेष
अन्वेषः, --षणं --णा Search after,<BR>seeking for, inquiry into or after,<BR>looking out for, watching; वयं<BR>तत्त्वान्वेषान्मधुकर हताः Ś. 1. 24; न्याय<BR>˚णतत्परौ Pt. 3. 91; रंध्रान्वेषणदक्षाणां द्विषां<BR>R. 12. 11; अस्यैवान्वेषणा वर्तते V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषणं|अन्वेषण
अन्वेषः, --षणं --णा Search after,<BR>seeking for, inquiry into or after,<BR>looking out for, watching; वयं<BR>तत्त्वान्वेषान्मधुकर हताः Ś. 1. 24; न्याय<BR>˚णतत्परौ Pt. 3. 91; रंध्रान्वेषणदक्षाणां द्विषां<BR>R. 12. 11; अस्यैवान्वेषणा वर्तते V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषणा
अन्वेषः, --षणं --णा Search after,<BR>seeking for, inquiry into or after,<BR>looking out for, watching; वयं<BR>तत्त्वान्वेषान्मधुकर हताः Ś. 1. 24; न्याय<BR>˚णतत्परौ Pt. 3. 91; रंध्रान्वेषणदक्षाणां द्विषां<BR>R. 12. 11; अस्यैवान्वेषणा वर्तते V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषक
अन्वेषक, अन्वेषिन्, अन्वेष्टृ a.<BR>Searching after, seeking for, inquiring &c;<BR>पौरा अस्मदन्वेषिणः Ś. 1.; अनुपद्यन्वेष्टा<BR>P. V. 2. 90; अंतरान्वेषी भवामि Ś. 7;<BR>R. 12. 54; H. 4. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेषिन्
अन्वेषक, अन्वेषिन्, अन्वेष्टृ a.<BR>Searching after, seeking for, inquiring &c;<BR>पौरा अस्मदन्वेषिणः Ś. 1.; अनुपद्यन्वेष्टा<BR>P. V. 2. 90; अंतरान्वेषी भवामि Ś. 7;<BR>R. 12. 54; H. 4. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वेष्टृ
अन्वेषक, अन्वेषिन्, अन्वेष्टृ a.<BR>Searching after, seeking for, inquiring &c;<BR>पौरा अस्मदन्वेषिणः Ś. 1.; अनुपद्यन्वेष्टा<BR>P. V. 2. 90; अंतरान्वेषी भवामि Ś. 7;<BR>R. 12. 54; H. 4. 102.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0102-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीक्ष्
अन्वीक्ष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To keep looking<BR>or gazing at, keep in view.<BR>--2 To<BR>search, seek for, inquire into;<BR>reflect or meditate upon, think of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीक्षणं|अन्वीक्षण
अन्वीक्षणं, --क्षा<BR>1 Search, seeking for;<BR>investigation.<BR>--2 Reflection;<BR>meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीक्षा
अन्वीक्षणं, --क्षा<BR>1 Search, seeking for;<BR>investigation.<BR>--2 Reflection;<BR>meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीत|अन्वीतः
अन्वीत = अन्वित q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वीप
अन्वीप a. [अनुगता आपो यत्र]<BR>1<BR>Near the water, situated near water.<BR>--2 Attainable or friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अन्वृचं|अन्वृच
अन्वृचं ind. Verse after verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्
अप् f. [आप्-क्विप्-ह्रस्वश्च Uṇ. 2. 58]<BR>(Declined in classical language only<BR>in pl.; आपः, अपः, अद्भिः, अद्भ्यः अपां and<BR>अप्सु, but in singular and pl. in Veda)<BR>1 Water (regarded in Ved. as sacred<BR>divinities, आपो देवीः); खानि चैव<BR>स्पृशेदद्भिः Ms. 2. 60. Water is generally<BR>considered to be the first of the 5<BR>elements of creation, as in अप एव<BR>ससर्जादौ तासु बीजमवासृजत् Ms. 1. 8,<BR>Ś. 1. 1; but in Ms. 1. 78 it is said to have<BR>been created from ज्योतिस् or तेजस्<BR>after मनस्, आकाश, वायु and ज्योतिस् or<BR>अग्नि; ज्योतिषश्च विकुर्वाणादापो रसगुणाः स्मृताः ।<BR>अद्भ्यो गंधगुणा भूमिरित्येषा सृष्टिरादितः ॥<BR>--2<BR>Air, the intermediate region.<BR>--3<BR>The star Ś virginis. For the changes<BR>of अप् at the end of comp. see<BR>P. V. 4. 74, VI. 3. 97-98. [cf. L. aqua,<BR>Gr. appos; Lith. uppe; Goth. ahva;<BR>Pers. ab; Zend ap; Old Germ. aha].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत्स्नं deep meditation by<BR>means of water.<BR>--चरः an aquatic<BR>animal.<BR>--पतिः {1} ‘Lord of waters’,<BR>N. of Varuṇa. {2} the ocean. For<BR>other comps. see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपां
अपां enters into several compounds;<BR>e. g. अपांसंवर्तः destruction of the<BR>world by water; अपांवत्सः ‘calf of<BR>waters’, N. of a star; अपांनपात्, ˚नप्ता,<BR>˚नप्त्त्रिय, ˚गर्भ, अपान्नपात्, अपोनपात् Ved.<BR>N. of Agni or fire as sprung from<BR>water; cf. Ms. 9. 321; अपांपतिः, निधिः<BR>नाथः, अप्पतिः lord of waters, the ocean;<BR>N. of Varuṇa; अपांपित्तं, अप्पित्तं fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप|अपः
अप ind. [न पाति रक्षति पतनात् पा-ड<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 (As a prefix to verbs it means)<BR>(a) Away, away from, denoting वियोग;<BR>अपयाति, अपनयति; (b)<BR>deterioration (विकृति); अपकरोति does wrongly<BR>or badly; (c) opposition, negation,<BR>contradiction (विपरीत); अपकर्षति,<BR>अपचिनोति; (d) direction or mention<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-b" target="_blank">Page0103-b+ 56</a>]<BR>or illustration (निदर्शन); अपादिशति;<BR>(e) exclusion (वर्जन); अपवह्, अपसृ<BR>caus.; (f) joy, merriment or laughter<BR>(आनद); अपहसति; (g) concealment<BR>or denial (चौर्य); अपलपति, अपवदते.<BR>--2<BR>As first member of Tat. or<BR>Bahuvrīhi comp. it has all the above<BR>senses; अपयानं, अपकर्म, अपपाठः;<BR>अपशब्दः a bad or corrupt word; ˚भी<BR>fearless; ˚कल्मष stainless; अपरागः<BR>discontent (opp. to अनुराग); ˚मेघोदयं वर्षं<BR>Ku. 6. 54 &c. In most cases अप may<BR>be translated by ‘bad’, ‘inferior’,<BR>‘corrupt,’ ‘wrong’, unworthy’ &c.<BR>It also means ‘going downwards’ as<BR>in अपानः.<BR>--3 As a separable preposition<BR>(with a noun in the abl.) (a)<BR>away from; यत्संप्रत्यप लोकेभ्यो लंकायां<BR>वसतिर्भयात् Rām; (b) without, on the<BR>outside of; अप हरेः संसारः Sk.; (c) with<BR>the exception of, excepting; अप<BR>त्रिगर्तेभ्यो वृष्टो देवः Sk. on the outside of,<BR>with the exception of. In these<BR>senses अप may form adverbial<BR>compounds also (P. II. 1. 12); ˚विष्णु<BR>संसारः Sk. without Viṣṇu; ˚त्रिगर्तं वृष्टो<BR>देवः excepting T. &c. It also implies<BR>negation, contradiction &c.; ˚कामं<BR>˚शंकं. The senses of this word as<BR>given by G. M. may be thus put in verse;<BR>वर्जने विकृतौ चौर्ये विपरीतवियोगयोः । अपकृष्टे<BR>च निर्देशे हर्षे चापः प्रयुज्यते. [cf. L. ab; Gr.<BR>apo; Goth. af. Eng. of or off; Zend<BR>apa].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकलंकः|अपकलङ्क|अपकलंक|अपकलङ्कः
अपकलंकः A deep, indelible stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकामः|अपकाम
अपकामः Ved. Abhorrence,<BR>aversion, abominableness; absence of<BR>what is dear.<BR>--मं ind.<BR>Unwillingly, against one's will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृ
अपकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To carry or bear away,<BR>remove, drag away, insult by<BR>dragging away; योऽपचक्रे वनात्सीतां<BR>Bk. 8. 20 bore forcibly away.<BR>--2 To hurt,<BR>injure, wrong, harm, do harm or<BR>injury to (usually with gen. of<BR>person); आपदि येनापकृतं Pt. 4. 16;<BR>Śi. 14. 78; न किंचिन्मया तस्यापकर्तुं शक्यं<BR>Pt. 1; किं तस्या मयापकृतं {4} what harm<BR>have I done to her? किं च<BR>राक्षसराजस्य रामेणापकृतं पुरा Rām.; sometimes<BR>with acc. or loc. also; अथ वा<BR>सौनिकाः केचिदपकुर्युर्युधिष्ठिरं Mb.; किमिव<BR>बत नाप्यन्यपकृतं Bh. 3. 115; न परेषु<BR>महौजसश्छलादपकुर्वंति मलिम्लुचा इव<BR>Śi. 16. 52. --Caus. To harm, injure &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकरणं|अपकरण
अपकरणं<BR>1 Acting improperly.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">Page0103-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Doing wrong, injuring;<BR>ill-treating, offending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्तृ|अपकर्त्तृ
अपकर्तृ a.<BR>1 Injurious, doing harm<BR>or injury, offensive.<BR>--2 Hostile,<BR>inimical. --m. An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्मन्|अपकर्म्मन्
अपकर्मन् a. [बहु. स.] Of bad or<BR>degraded actions, corrupted, depraved.<BR>--n. (˚र्म)<BR>1 Discharge, paying off<BR>(of a debt); दत्तस्यानपकर्म च<BR>Ms. 8. 4.<BR>--2 An improper or unworthy<BR>act; evil doing, conduct, or course,<BR>any degrading or impure act.<BR>--3<BR>Wickedness, violence, oppression.<BR>--4 Incompetence, laziness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारः|अपकार
अपकारः<BR>1 Harm, wrong, injury,<BR>hurt, offence, misdeed, wrong deed<BR>(opp. उपकार); स्वल्पेनाप्यपकारेण<BR>ब्राह्मण्यमिव दुष्यति Pt. 1. 66;<BR>उपकर्त्रारिणा संधिर्न मित्रेणापकारिणा ।<BR>उपकारापकारौ हि लक्ष्यं लक्षणमेतयोः Śi. 2. 37;<BR>अपकारोप्युपकारायैव संवृत्तः. &c.<BR>--2<BR>Thinking ill of, desire to offend or<BR>hurt (अनिष्टचिंता).<BR>--3 Wickedness,<BR>violence, oppression, enmity.<BR>--4 A<BR>mean or degraded action.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थिन् a. meaning to harm,<BR>malevolent, malicious.<BR>--गिर् f.<BR>--(गीः),<BR>--शब्दः abusive words, menacing or<BR>insulting speech; भर्त्सनं<BR>त्वपकारगीः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारक|अपकारकः
अपकारक, --कारिन् a. Injuring,<BR>doing harm or wrong to, mischievous,<BR>offending, harmful, hurtful,<BR>injurious; Pt. 1. 95, Śi. 2. 37.<BR>--कः, --री<BR>An evil-doer (opp. उपंकारी), enemy;<BR>अपकारिषु यः साधुः स साधुः सद्भिरुच्यते<BR>H. 1; अन्˚ harmless, not harmful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकारिन्
अपकारक, --कारिन् a. Injuring,<BR>doing harm or wrong to, mischievous,<BR>offending, harmful, hurtful,<BR>injurious; Pt. 1. 95, Śi. 2. 37.<BR>--कः, --री<BR>An evil-doer (opp. उपंकारी), enemy;<BR>अपकारिषु यः साधुः स साधुः सद्भिरुच्यते<BR>H. 1; अन्˚ harmless, not harmful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृत
अपकृत p. p.<BR>1 Injured, wronged,<BR>wickedly or maliciously committed<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Done or practised as a<BR>degrading or impure act, as funeral<BR>rites.<BR>--तं An injury, harm, offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृतिः|अपकृति
अपकृतिः f., अपकृत्यं<BR>1 Harm, injury,<BR>hurt, damage, offence.<BR>--2<BR>Opposition, enmity.<BR>--3 A degrading or<BR>impure act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रिया
अपक्रिया<BR>1 Hurt, injury, disservice;<BR>fault, wrong or faulty deed,<BR>misdeed; चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु शत्रौ<BR>सांत्वमपक्रिया Śi. 2. 54; Ki. 13. 64 fault.<BR>--2<BR>Paying or clearing off (debts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्
अपकृष् {c1c} P., {c6c} U.<BR>1 (a) To draw<BR>back or away, draw off or aside, drag<BR>down, drag away, take or carry<BR>off, take or draw out, extract;<BR>आनायिभिस्तामपकृष्टनक्रां R. 16. 55<BR>drawn out; दंताग्रभिन्नमपकृष्य निरीक्षते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-a" target="_blank">Page0104-a+ 57</a>]<BR>च Rs. 4. 14 pulling off or back. (b)<BR>To take or carry away, remove; धैर्यं<BR>शोकोऽपकर्षति Rām.; किंत्वनुष्ठाननित्यत्वं<BR>स्वातंत्र्यमपकर्षति U. 1. 8, Mv. 4. 33<BR>prevents or interferes with freedom<BR>of action; क्षात्रंतेजोपकर्षति Mv. 1. 32<BR>destroys, robs one of.<BR>--2 To<BR>diminish, decrease, omit; अपकर्षेदेवं<BR>यावत्पंचदश Suśr.<BR>--3 To bend (as a bow);<BR>धनुः श्रेष्ठमपकृष्य Mb.<BR>--4 To lower or<BR>debase, dishonour, detract from,<BR>lessen the value of, disparage;<BR>पीडयन् भृत्यवर्गं हि आत्मानमपकर्षति Mb.<BR>--5<BR>To bring or draw backwards;<BR>anticipate (as a word in a sentence)<BR>what occurs later on; अग्रिमसूत्रस्थं<BR>सर्वत्रग्रहणमिहापकृष्यते P. IV. 1. 17<BR>Com. --Caus. To remove, take away,<BR>lessen, diminish, detract from;<BR>काव्यस्यात्मभूतं रसमपकर्षयंतः<BR>काव्यस्यापकर्षकाः (दोषाः) उच्यंते S. D. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0103-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षः|अपकर्ष
अपकर्षः<BR>1 (a) Drawing off or<BR>down; diminution, decrease,<BR>reduction; मेदोऽपकर्षात् Dk. 160; loss, decay,<BR>decline, destruction; तेजोपकर्षः<BR>Ve. 1; deterioration, inferiority;<BR>उत्कर्षापकर्षविहीनो मध्यः Sk. (b) Dishonour,<BR>degradation, lowering (of esteem),<BR>infamy, disgrace (opp. उत्कर्ष in<BR>all senses); तपोबीजप्रभावैस्तु ते<BR>गच्छंति युगे युगे । उत्कर्षं चापकर्षं च<BR>मनुष्येष्विह जन्मतः ॥ Ms. 10. 42;<BR>मूल्योत्कर्ष˚ rise and fall in price, increase<BR>and decrease.<BR>--2 Anticipated<BR>performance of a duty, as of a Śrāddha.<BR>--3 Anticipation of a word<BR>occurring later on (in gram., poetry or<BR>Mīmāṃsā &c.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--समः a<BR>sort of fallacy; e. g. sound has not<BR>the quality of shape, as a jar, so<BR>sound and a jar have no qualities<BR>in common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षक
अपकर्षक a.<BR>1 Drawing or taking<BR>off or down, removing.<BR>--2<BR>Lessening, diminishing, detracting from;<BR>दोषास्तस्य (काव्यस्य) अपकर्षकाः S. D. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकर्षण
अपकर्षण a. Taking or drawing away,<BR>removing, diminishing (opp. वर्धक);<BR>न चास्ति सदृशं तेन किंचित्स्थौल्यापकर्षणं<BR>Suśr.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Removing, taking<BR>away; drawing away or down,<BR>depriving (one) of, drawing out,<BR>extracting.<BR>--2 Lessening, making<BR>inferior, detraction.<BR>--3<BR>Superseding.<BR>--4 Denying; abolishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकृष्ट|अपकृष्टं|अपकृष्टः
अपकृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Drawn or taken<BR>away, removed;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">Page0104-b+ 56</a>]<BR>अपकृष्टश्चाणक्याच्चंद्रगुप्तः Mu. 4 severed, alienated,<BR>estranged, cut off; so नृपोपकृष्टः<BR>सचिवात् 4. 14; extracted, drawn out,<BR>dragged, lost, diminished, brought<BR>down, depressed, lowered &c.<BR>--2 Drawn or attracted by; सर्वं<BR>दैवापकृष्टं मन्यते युधिष्ठिरः Ve. 5,<BR>dependent on, or the work of, Fate.<BR>--3<BR>Low, vile, base, inferior, mean<BR>(opp. उत्कृष्ट); न<BR>कश्चिद्वर्णानामपथमपकृष्टोपि भजते Ś. 5. 10; पतिं हित्वाऽपकृष्टं<BR>स्वमुत्कृष्टं या निषेवते Ms. 5. 163;<BR>8. 281; 9. 24; सहापकृष्टैर्महतां न संगतं<BR>Ki. 14. 22.<BR>--ष्टः A crow.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चेतन a. mentally debased or<BR>corrupted, low-minded.<BR>--जाति a. of a<BR>low tribe or origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकॄ
अपकॄ {c6c} P.<BR>1 To scatter, spout out<BR>(water); अपकिरति कुसुमं; गजोऽप<BR>किरति Sk.<BR>--2 To scrape with the<BR>feet (for food &c.) through joy,<BR>said of quadrupeds and birds,<BR>(changed to अपस्कृ Ā., in this sense<BR>अपाच्चतुष्पाच्छकुनिष्वालेखने सुट् P. VI. 1. 142)<BR>अपास्किरते वृषो हृष्टः, कुक्कुटो भक्षार्थी,<BR>श्वा आश्रयार्थी च Sk;<BR>शृंगैरपस्कीर्णमहत्तटीभुवां Śi. 12. 74 scratched;<BR>छायापस्किरमाणविष्किर &c. U. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकिरणं
अपकिरणं Scattering about &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपकौशली
अपकौशली News, information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्तिः|अपक्ति
अपक्तिः f.<BR>1 Unripeness,<BR>immaturity.<BR>--2 Indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्व|अपक्वः
अपक्व a. Unripe, immature,<BR>undigested (as food); uncooked, raw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रम्
अपक्रम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go away, run<BR>away, fly, escape, flee away, leave,<BR>retreat, retire (from); नगरादपक्रांतः<BR>Mu. 1; राक्षसोऽपक्रामन्नुपेक्षितः {3} while<BR>escaping.<BR>--2 To glide away,<BR>pass away, (as time).<BR>--3 To<BR>measure off by steps or by pacing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमः|अपक्रम
अपक्रमः<BR>1 Going away, flight,<BR>escape, retreat.<BR>--2 The place or limit<BR>to which one may retreat;<BR>विक्षिपत्येष विक्षेपं चंद्रादीनामपक्रमात् Sūrya S.<BR>--3 Gliding or passing away (of<BR>time). --a. [अपगतः क्रमो यस्मात्]<BR>1<BR>Without order<BR>--2 Irregular, in<BR>wrong order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमणं|अपक्रमण
अपक्रमणं, --क्रामः Retreat, retiring,<BR>flight, escape &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रामः|अपक्राम
अपक्रमणं, --क्रामः Retreat, retiring,<BR>flight, escape &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रमिन्
अपक्रमिन् a. Going forth or away;<BR>not going fast, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्रोशः|अपक्रोश
अपक्रोशः Abuse, reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्ष
अपक्ष a.<BR>1 Without wings or the<BR>power of flight.<BR>--2 Not belonging to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">Page0104-c+ 56</a>]<BR>the same side or party.<BR>--3 Having<BR>no adherents or friends.<BR>--4 Opposed<BR>to, adverse.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पातः<BR>impartiality.<BR>--पातिन् a. impartial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षि
अपक्षि {c1c} {c5c} {c9c} P. To bring to<BR>an end, destroy, annihilate. --pass.<BR>To decline, decay, waste away;<BR>wane (as the moon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षयः|अपक्षय
अपक्षयः Decline, decay, wane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षीण
अपक्षीण p. p. Declined, wasted,<BR>waned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षिप्
अपक्षिप् {c6c} P. To throw away<BR>or down, take away, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षेपः|अपक्षेप
अपक्षेपः, --क्षेपणं<BR>1 Casting away<BR>or throwing down.<BR>--2 Throwing or<BR>putting down, one of the 5 kinds<BR>of कर्मन् in the Vaiśeṣika phil.,<BR>see कर्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपक्षेपणं|अपक्षेपण
अपक्षेपः, --क्षेपणं<BR>1 Casting away<BR>or throwing down.<BR>--2 Throwing or<BR>putting down, one of the 5 kinds<BR>of कर्मन् in the Vaiśeṣika phil.,<BR>see कर्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगंडः|अपगण्ड|अपगण्डः
अपगंडः One who has attained<BR>his majority^1; see अपोगंड.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगम्
अपगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go away, depart;<BR>pass away, elapse (as time); K. 73;<BR>तन्मुखाच्छायापगता H. 3; संपदो<BR>नापगच्छंति Pt. 3. 8.<BR>--2 To fall off or<BR>down; go away, vanish, disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपग
अपग a. Going, turning away.<BR>--गा A river (wrongly for आपगा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगत|अपगतः
अपगत p. p.<BR>1 Gone away, departed,<BR>passed away, gone off; being remote;<BR>oft. as first member of comp. in<BR>the sense of ‘free from’, ‘devoid of’;<BR>˚अन्यव्यापाराः K. 43 having no other<BR>duties; ˚मत्सर 45; 47, 157, 164,<BR>207, 211; ˚निमेषेण चक्षुषा 154<BR>devoid of twinkling or winking;<BR>˚मले मनसि 102.<BR>--2 Dead, deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगमः|अपगम
अपगमः, --मनं<BR>1 Going away or off,<BR>departure, separation; समागमाः<BR>सापगमाः H. 4. 65.<BR>--2 Falling off, going<BR>away, removal, disappearance;<BR>निमित्तमुद्दिश्य हि यः प्रकुप्यति भ्रुवंस<BR>तस्यापगमे प्रसीदति ॥ Pt. 1. 283;<BR>त्वत्संरोधापगगविशदैश्चंद्रपादैः Me. 70;<BR>पुराणपत्रापगमादनंतरं R. 3. 7; lapse, passing away;<BR>कतिपयदिवसापगमे K. 66, 193.<BR>--3<BR>Death, decease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगमनं|अपगमन
अपगमः, --मनं<BR>1 Going away or off,<BR>departure, separation; समागमाः<BR>सापगमाः H. 4. 65.<BR>--2 Falling off, going<BR>away, removal, disappearance;<BR>निमित्तमुद्दिश्य हि यः प्रकुप्यति भ्रुवंस<BR>तस्यापगमे प्रसीदति ॥ Pt. 1. 283;<BR>त्वत्संरोधापगगविशदैश्चंद्रपादैः Me. 70;<BR>पुराणपत्रापगमादनंतरं R. 3. 7; lapse, passing away;<BR>कतिपयदिवसापगमे K. 66, 193.<BR>--3<BR>Death, decease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगतिः|अपगति
अपगतिः f. A bad fate (going to<BR>hell &c.); येन चापगतिर्भवेत् Pt. 2. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगरः|अपगर
अपगरः [अप-निंदार्थे गॄ भावे अप्]<BR>1<BR>Censure, reviling (निंदा);<BR>अभिगरापगरौ Kāty.<BR>--2 One who reviles or says<BR>what is disagreeable, reviler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगर्जित
अपगर्जित a. Thunderless (as a<BR>cloud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगोपुर
अपगोपुर a. Deprived of its<BR>gateways (as a town).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगल्भ
अपगल्भ a. Ved.<BR>1 Wanting in<BR>boldness, abortive.<BR>--2 Being on the<BR>side, lateral.<BR>--3 Separated from the<BR>oldest by one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगुणः|अपगुण
अपगुणः A demerit, fault;<BR>Śi. 15. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगुर्
अपगुर् {c6c} A.<BR>1 To disapprove,<BR>reject.<BR>--2 To threaten, menace; revile,<BR>censure, reproach, rail at.<BR>--3 To<BR>deprive of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगारं
अपगारं --गोरं ind. Having raised<BR>or lifted up; अस्यपगोरं-गारं युध्यंते<BR>P. VI. 1. 53 Sk. lifting their swords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगोरं
अपगारं --गोरं ind. Having raised<BR>or lifted up; अस्यपगोरं-गारं युध्यंते<BR>P. VI. 1. 53 Sk. lifting their swords.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगुह्
अपगुह् {c1c} U. To hide, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपगोहः|अपगोह
अपगोहः Ved. A hiding place,<BR>disappearance, concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघनः|अपघन
अपघनः [अपहन्यते संहत्य कर्म कृत्वा<BR>वियुज्यते, हन्-अप्-घनादेशः P. III 3. 77].<BR>A limb or member of the body, as<BR>a hand or foot (अपघनोंऽगम्<BR>III. 3. 81; अंगं शरीरावयवः स च न सर्वं किं तु पाणिः<BR>पादश्चेत्याहुः Sk. and Kāśikā.); but it is<BR>also used in the sense of ‘the<BR>body’; लौहोद्घनघनस्कंधा ललितापघनां<BR>स्त्रियं Bk. 7. 62 (where the<BR>commentators take अपघन to mean the<BR>body itself). --a. Free from the<BR>obstruction of clouds, cloudless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघातः|अपघात
अपघातः<BR>1 Striking or cutting<BR>off, warding off, preventing.<BR>--2<BR>Killing.<BR>--3 A violent death, any evil<BR>accident proving fatal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपघातिन्
अपघातिन् a. Killing, murdering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचः|अपच
अपचः [पक्तुमशक्तः Sk.]<BR>1 Unable<BR>to cook, or one who does not cook<BR>for himself.<BR>--2 A bad cook, a term<BR>of abuse (आक्रोशे); अपचो जाल्मः<BR>P. VI. 2. 157-8 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचर्
अपचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To depart.<BR>--2 To<BR>go astray, transgress; offend,<BR>commit a fault, act wrongly; यो<BR>यस्तेषामपचरेत्तमाचक्षीत वै द्विजः Mb.;<BR>तदंगनास्वपाचरन्नरेंद्रः Dk. 162 outraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचरित
अपचरित p. p. Gone away,<BR>departed; deceased.<BR>--तं A fault, wrong<BR>or wicked deed, misdeed;<BR>आहोस्वित्प्रसवो ममापचरितैर्विष्टंभितो वीरुधां Ś. 5. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारः|अपचार
अपचारः<BR>1 Departure; death;<BR>सिंहघोषश्च कांतकापचारं निर्भिद्य Dk. 72.<BR>--2<BR>Want, absence.<BR>--3 A fault; offence,<BR>misdeed, improper conduct, crime;<BR>शिष्यो गुराविव कृतप्रथमापचारः<BR>Mv. 4. 20; न राजापचारमंतरेण U. 2 (v. l.<BR>for ˚अपराधं); राजन्प्रजासु ते कश्चिदपचारः<BR>प्रवर्तते R. 15. 47.<BR>--4 Injurious or<BR>hurtful conduct, injury, Ve. 4. 10.<BR>--5<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">Page0105-b+ 57</a>]<BR>A defect, flaw, failure, deficiency;<BR>नापचारमगमन् क्वचित्क्रियाः Śi. 14. 32;<BR>mistake, omission (to do a thing)<BR>(लोप); महाध्वरे विध्यपचारदोषः<BR>Ki. 16. 48.<BR>--6 Unwholesome or improper<BR>regimen (अपथ्य); कृतापचारोपि<BR>परैरनाविष्कृतविक्रियः । असाध्यः कुरुते कोपं प्राप्ते<BR>काले गदो यथा ॥ Śi. 2. 84 (where अ˚<BR>also means hurt or injury).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचारिन्
अपचारिन् a. Offending, doing wrong;<BR>wicked, bad; भार्यापचारिणी<BR>Ms. 8. 317 a faithless wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचाय्
अपचाय् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To fear.<BR>--2 To<BR>respect, honour, worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचायित|अपचायितः
अपचायित a. Feared, honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचि
अपचि {c3c} P.<BR>1 To honour, respect.<BR>--2 To invite respectfully.<BR>--3 ({c5c} U.)<BR>To gather, collect. --pass.<BR>1 To be<BR>reduced in strength or bulk, sink,<BR>waste away; अपचितमपि गात्रं<BR>व्यायतत्वादलक्ष्यं Ś. 2. 9 reduced in bulk,<BR>emaciated, lean; to wane, decline,<BR>diminish, grow less; राजहंस तव सैव<BR>शुभ्रता चीयते न च न चापचीयते K. P. 10.<BR>--2 To fall away from, be deprived<BR>of, lose (with abl.) प्रकृतिः सूयते<BR>तद्वदानंत्यान्नापचीयते Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचयः|अपचय
अपचयः<BR>1 Diminution, decrease,<BR>decay, decline, fall (fig. also.);<BR>कफापचयः Dk. 160; तेनास्यापचयं यांति<BR>व्याधेर्मूलान्यशेषतः Suśr.; H. 3. 130;<BR>defeat Mv. 2. 13.<BR>--2 Loss,<BR>privation, failure, defect; H. 3. 133.<BR>--3<BR>N. of several planetary mansions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचित|अपचितः
अपचित p. p.<BR>1 Reduced in bulk,<BR>decreased, wasted, expended &c.;<BR>emaciated, thin, lean.<BR>--2 Honoured,<BR>respected, saluted<BR>--तं Honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचितिः|अपचिति
अपचितिः f. (P. VII. 2. 30 Vārt.)<BR>1 Loss, decay, decline, destruction.<BR>--2 Expense.<BR>--3 Atonement, amends,<BR>compensation, expiation of sin.<BR>--4<BR>Exclusion.<BR>--5 Punishing.<BR>--6 N. of a<BR>daughter of Marīci.<BR>--7 Honouring,<BR>worshipping, showing reverence,<BR>worship; विहितापचितिर्महीभृता<BR>Śi. 16. 9 (where it also means loss,<BR>destruction हानि), 1. 17; 15. 34;<BR>K. 324; Ki. 6. 46; 11. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपचित्
अपचित् f. A noxious flying<BR>insect; that which causes decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपची
अपची [अपकृष्टं पच्यते असौ, पच् कर्मकर्तरि<BR>अच् गौरा˚ ङीष्] A disease in which the<BR>glands of the neck are enlarged and<BR>swollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छत्र
अपच्छत्र a. Without a parasol<BR>or umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छाय|अपच्छायः
अपच्छाय a. [अपगता छाया यस्मात्]<BR>1 Shadowless.<BR>--2 Having a bad or<BR>unlucky shadow.<BR>--3 Devoid of<BR>brightness, dim.<BR>--यः One that has no<BR>shadow, i. e. a god; cf. N. 14. 21;<BR>श्रियं भजंतां कियदस्य देवाश्छाया नलस्यास्ति<BR>तथापि नैषाम् । इतीरयंतीव तया निरैक्षि सा<BR>(छाया) नैषधे न त्रिदशेषु तेषु ॥<BR>--या An<BR>unlucky shadow, apparition, phantom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छेदः|अपच्छेद
अपच्छेदः --दनं<BR>1 Cutting off or<BR>away.<BR>--2 Loss.<BR>--3 Interruption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्छेदनं|अपच्छेदन
अपच्छेदः --दनं<BR>1 Cutting off or<BR>away.<BR>--2 Loss.<BR>--3 Interruption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्यु
अपच्यु {c1c} A.<BR>1 To fall off, go<BR>away or off, withdraw, desert.<BR>--2<BR>To perish, die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्यवः|अपच्यव
अपच्यवः Going or coming out<BR>(निर्गम); Rv. 1. 28. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपच्युत
अपच्युत p. p. Fallen off; departed,<BR>perished; melted away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजातः|अपजात
अपजातः A bad son who has<BR>turned out ill; one inferior to his<BR>parents in qualities; मातृतुल्यगुणो<BR>जातस्त्वनुजातः पितुः समः ।<BR>अतिजातोधिकस्तस्मादपजातोऽधमाधमः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजर्गुराण
अपजर्गुराण a. (अपगॄ-यङ्लुक्<BR>चानश्) Ved. Accustomed to take off or<BR>remove the covering &c. (<BR>आच्छादनादिमोचनशील) Rv. 5. 29. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजि
अपजि {c1c} P. To defeat, conquer;<BR>turn off or away, avert, ward<BR>or keep off; येन मृत्युमपजयति Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपजयः|अपजय
अपजयः Defeat, overthrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपज्ञा
अपज्ञा {c9c} A. To deny, disown,<BR>repudiate, dissemble, conceal;<BR>शतमपजानीते P. I. 3. 44 Sk. (<BR>अपलपति); आत्मानमपजानानः शशमात्रोऽनयद्दिनं<BR>Bk. 8. 26 concealing himself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपज्ञानं|अपज्ञान
अपज्ञानं Denying, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपंचीकृतं|अपञ्चीकृत|अपंचीकृत|अपञ्चीकृतं
अपंचीकृतं A simple elementary<BR>substance not made of the five (पंच)<BR>gross elements; the five subtle<BR>elements; पंचप्राणमनोबुद्धिदशेंद्रियसमन्वितं<BR>अपंचीकृतभूतोत्थं सूक्ष्मांगं भोगसाधनम् ॥<BR>Vedānta P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटांतर|अपटान्तर|अपटान्तरं
अपटांतर a.<BR>1 Not separated<BR>(by a curtain or screen).<BR>--2<BR>Adjoining, contiguous (= अपदांतर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटी
अपटी [अल्पः पटः पटी, न. त.]<BR>1<BR>A screen or wall of cloth, particularly<BR>the screen or kanāt surrounding<BR>a tent.<BR>--2 A curtain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्षेपः (अपटक्षेपः) tossing aside<BR>the curtain; ˚क्षेपेण (= अकस्मात्)<BR>‘with a (hurried) toss of the<BR>curtain’, frequently occurring as a<BR>stage-direction and denoting<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">Page0106-a+ 55</a>]<BR>precipitate entrance on the stage which<BR>arises from fear, hurry, agitation<BR>&c., as when a character tossing up<BR>the curtain suddenly enters<BR>without the usual introduction ततः<BR>प्रविशति &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपटु|अपटुः
अपटु a.<BR>1 Not clever or skilful,<BR>slow, dull awkward, uncouth.<BR>--2<BR>Ineloquent (as a speaker).<BR>--3 Sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपठ
अपठ a. Unable to read; not<BR>reading; a bad reader; cf. अपच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपंडित|अपण्डित
अपंडित a.<BR>1 Not learned or wise,<BR>foolish, ignorant; विभूषणं<BR>मौनमपंडितानाम् Bh. 2. 7.<BR>--2 Wanting in skill,<BR>taste, appreciation &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपण्य
अपण्य a. Not saleable (the<BR>Smṛtis name several things which<BR>ought not to be sold by particular<BR>persons and on particular occasions);<BR>जीविकार्थे चापण्ये P. V. 3. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतंत्रकः|अपतन्त्रक|अपतन्त्रकः
अपतंत्रकः [अपगतं तंत्रं भिषजामधीनता<BR>यत्र कप् Tv.] A kind of वातरोग,<BR>spasmodic contraction of the body or<BR>stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतानकः|अपतानक
अपतानकः [अपक्रम्य अंतरांतरा तनुते<BR>तन् कर्तरि ण्वुल्] Spasmodic contraction<BR>with occasional convulsive fits;<BR>सोपतानकसंज्ञो यः पातयत्यंतरांतरा Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतानकिन्
अपतानकिन् a. Affected with<BR>spasmodic contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपति|अपतिः
अपति, --तिक a. Without a master;<BR>without a husband, unmarried.<BR>--तिः<BR>Ved. Not a master or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतिक
अपति, --तिक a. Without a master;<BR>without a husband, unmarried.<BR>--तिः<BR>Ved. Not a master or husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्नी
अपत्नी Unmarried, without a<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्नीक
अपत्नीक a.<BR>1 Without a wife (when<BR>she is either absent or dead).<BR>--2 To<BR>be performed without the company<BR>of a wife; अपत्नीकः पितृयज्ञः Kāty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतीर्थ
अपतीर्थ A bad Tīrtha or place<BR>of pilgrimage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतृप्
अपतृप् {c10c} P. To cause to fast or<BR>starve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपतर्पणं|अपतर्पण
अपतर्पणं<BR>1 Fasting (in sickness).<BR>--2 Absence of satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्यं|अपत्य
अपत्यं [न पतंति पितरोऽनेन, पत् बाहु˚<BR>करणे यत्, न. त. ; some derive it from<BR>अप, the termination त्य being added<BR>to it, as in तत्रत्य, अत्रत्य, sprung from<BR>a stock; Yāska gives two etymologies:<BR>अपत्यं कस्मात् अपततं भवति पितुः<BR>सकाशादेत्य पृथगिव ततं भवति, अनेन जातेन सता पिता<BR>नरके न पततीति वा]<BR>1 Offspring, child,<BR>progeny, issue (of animals and<BR>men); offspring in general (male<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-b" target="_blank">Page0106-b+ 57</a>]<BR>or female); sons or grandsons and<BR>other later generations of a Gotra;<BR>अपत्यं पौत्रप्रभृति गोत्रं P. IV. 1. 162;<BR>अपत्यैरिव नीवारभागधेयोचितैर्मृगैः<BR>R. 1. 50. (Bhavabhūti calls an apatya<BR>‘a knot for tying parents together’<BR>अन्योन्यसंश्लेषणंपित्रोः; अंतःकरणतत्त्वस्य दंपत्योः<BR>स्नेहसंश्रयात् । आनंदग्रंथिरेकोयमपत्यमिति<BR>बध्यते ॥ U. 3. 17).<BR>--2 A patronymic^1<BR>affix; स्त्रीपुंसयोरपत्यांताः Ak.;<BR>˚अधिकारप्रकरणं Sk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काम a.<BR>desirous of progeny.<BR>--जीवः N. of a<BR>plant.<BR>--द a. giving offspring (as<BR>a Mantra &c.).<BR>--(दा) N. of a<BR>plant (गर्भदात्रीवृक्ष).<BR>--पथः the vulva.<BR>--प्रत्ययः a patronymic affix.<BR>--विक्रयिन् m. a seller of his children, a<BR>father who sells his girl for money<BR>to a bridegroom.<BR>--शत्रुः [अपत्यं<BR>शत्रुर्गर्भभेदनेन नाशकं यस्याः सा] {1} ‘having the<BR>child for its enemy’, a crab (said to<BR>die in proḍucing young). {2} a<BR>serpent.<BR>--साच् a. Ved. accompanied<BR>with offspring.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्र|अपत्त्रः
अपत्र a. Leafless, without wings<BR>&c.<BR>--त्रः<BR>1 The shoot of bamboo; a<BR>sprout in general (तदवस्थायां तयोः<BR>पत्रशून्यतयोत्पत्तेस्तथात्वं).<BR>--2 A tree the<BR>leaves of which have fallen off.<BR>--3 A bird without wings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रप्
अपत्रप् {c1c} A. To be ashamed, be<BR>bashful, hang down the face<BR>through shame; (with instr. of<BR>person or thing); येनापत्रपते<BR>साधुरसाधुस्तेन तुष्यति Mb; य आत्मनापत्रपते<BR>भृशं नरः स सर्वलोकंस्य गुरुर्भवत्युत ibid.;<BR>तस्माद्बलैरपत्रेपे Bk. 14. 84 turned<BR>away from with shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रप|अपत्रपः
अपत्रप a. Shameless, impudent.<BR>--पा, --पणं<BR>1 Shame, bashfulness.<BR>--2<BR>Embarrassment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रपिष्णु|अपत्रपिष्णुः
अपत्रपिष्णु a. [अपत्रप्-इष्णुच्]<BR>Bashful; Śi. 8. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपत्रस्त
अपत्रस्त p. p. Afraid of, deterred<BR>from; तरंगापत्रस्तः (slightly) afraid<BR>of waves; P. II. 1. 38 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ|अपथं|अपथः
अपथ a. [नास्ति पंथा यत्र] Pathless,<BR>roadless; ˚थो देशः, ˚था नगरी &c.<BR>--थं,<BR>--थः (also अपंथाः P. V. 4. 72, II. {4}<BR>II. 4. 30)<BR>1 Not a way, absence of a way<BR>or road, pathless state; a bad or<BR>wrong road (lit.); (fig.)<BR>irregularity, deviation, a moral irregularity<BR>or deviation, a wrong road, bad or<BR>evil course; अपथे पदमर्पयंति हि<BR>श्रुतवंतोपि रजोनिमीलिताः R. 9. 74; 17. 54; न<BR>कश्चिद्वर्णानामपथमपकृष्टोपि भजते Ś. 5. 10<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">Page0106-c+ 57</a>]<BR>follows evil ways; कारितस्त्वमपथे पद<BR>मया Ki. 13. 45, 64.<BR>--2 Heresy,<BR>heterodoxy (in opinions).<BR>--3 The vulva.<BR>--था N. of several plants.<BR>--थं ind. By<BR>or in the wrong way, astray; अपथं<BR>वर्तते Sk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गामिन् a. pursuing<BR>evil courses; heretical.<BR>--प्रपन्न a.<BR>taking to evil ways (as man); spent or<BR>used out of place, misapplied,<BR>misspent (as money &c.); H. 3. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपथ्य|अपथ्यं
अपथ्य a. [न. त.]<BR>1 Unfit, unsuited,<BR>improper, inconsistent, obnoxious;<BR>अकार्यं कार्यसंकाशमपथ्यं पथ्यसंमितं Rām.<BR>--2 (In medicine) Unwholesome,<BR>unsalutary (as food, regimen &c.);<BR>संतापयंति कमपथ्यभुजं न रोगाः H. 3. 117;<BR>भवति पुरुषस्य व्याधिर्मरणं सेविते अपथ्ये,<BR>राजापथ्ये पुनः सेविते सकलकुलं नश्यति<BR>Mu. 6.<BR>--3 Bad, unlucky.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारिन् a. an offender; एवमपथ्यकारिषु<BR>तीक्ष्णदंडो राजा; राज ˚री क्षपणकः; अनुभव<BR>राजापथ्यकारित्वस्य फलं Mu. 1 an<BR>enemy or traitor to the king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्
अपद् --पाद् a. (पदी f.) [न पद्यते<BR>ज्ञायते. पद्-क्विप्-न. त.]<BR>1 Incomprehensible,<BR>unknowable.<BR>--2 Having no feet,<BR>footless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाद्
अपद् --पाद् a. (पदी f.) [न पद्यते<BR>ज्ञायते. पद्-क्विप्-न. त.]<BR>1 Incomprehensible,<BR>unknowable.<BR>--2 Having no feet,<BR>footless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद|अपदः
अपद a.<BR>1 Footless.<BR>--2 Having no<BR>office or post.<BR>--दः A reptile.<BR>--दं<BR>1<BR>No place or abode.<BR>--2 A wrong or<BR>bad place or abode; wrong timer<BR>चिरमपदे शंकितोऽस्मि M. 1 my doubts<BR>were out of place, ill-founded; ग्रेम<BR>पश्यति भयान्यपदोपि Ki. 9. 70<BR>unreasonably.<BR>--3 A word which is not a<BR>pada or an inflected word.<BR>--4 Ether.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतर a. adjoining,<BR>contiguous, very near.<BR>--(रं) proximity,<BR>contiguity.<BR>--रुहा, --रोहिणी N. of a<BR>parasitical plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदक्षिणं
अपदक्षिणं ind. To the left side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदम
अपदम a.<BR>1 Without<BR>self-restraint.<BR>--2 Of wavering fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदव
अपदव a. Free from forest fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदश
अपदश a. Far from ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदानं|अपदान
अपदानं --दानकं [अपदायति<BR>परिशुध्यति येन कर्मणा, दै करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Pure<BR>conduct, approved course of life;<BR>(परिशुद्धाचरणं).<BR>--2 A great or noble<BR>work, excellent work (perhaps for<BR>अवदानं q. v.).<BR>--3 A work well or<BR>completely done, an accomplished<BR>work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदानकं|अपदानक
अपदानं --दानकं [अपदायति<BR>परिशुध्यति येन कर्मणा, दै करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Pure<BR>conduct, approved course of life;<BR>(परिशुद्धाचरणं).<BR>--2 A great or noble<BR>work, excellent work (perhaps for<BR>अवदानं q. v.).<BR>--3 A work well or<BR>completely done, an accomplished<BR>work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदार्थः|अपदार्थ
अपदार्थः<BR>1 Nothing, non-entity.<BR>--2 Not the meaning of words<BR>actually used in a sentence;<BR>अपदार्थोपि वाक्यार्थः समुल्लसति K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिश्
अपदिश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To point out,<BR>indicate, show; तदागतित्वेनाहमपदेश्यः<BR>Dk. 60; assign, allot.<BR>--2 To declare,<BR>put forward, adduce, communicate;<BR>announce, say, tell; inform against,<BR>accuse; अपदिश्यापदेश्यं च Ms. 8. 54.<BR>--3<BR>To feign, pretend, hold out or plead as<BR>a pretext or excuse; मित्रकृत्यमपदिश्य<BR>R. 19. 31, 32, 54;<BR>शिरःशूलस्पर्शनमपदिशन् Dk. 56 pleading head-ache<BR>as an excuse.<BR>--4 To refer to, have<BR>reference to; रहसि भर्त्रा मद्गोत्रापदिष्टा<BR>Dk. 102 referred to, called by the<BR>name of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेशः|अपदेश
अपदेशः<BR>1 Statement, adducing<BR>(उपदेश); pointing out, mentioning<BR>the name of; नैष न्यायो यद्दातुरपदेशः<BR>Dk. 60; हेत्वपदेशात् प्रतिज्ञायाः पुनर्वचनं<BR>निगमनं Nyāya S.; दीक्षाया अपदेशात् Kāty.<BR>--2 (a) A pretext, pretence, plea,<BR>excuse; contrivance; केनापदेशेन<BR>पुनराश्रमं गच्छामः Ś. 2;<BR>रक्षापदेशान्मुनिहोमधेनोः R. 2. 8; व्रतापदेशोज्झितगर्ववृत्तिना<BR>V. 3. 12. (b) Guise, disguise, form;<BR>विकटदुष्टश्वापदापदेशकालगोचरं गता<BR>Māl. 7; मंत्रिपदापदेशं यौवराज्यं Dk. 101.<BR>--3<BR>Statement of the reason, adducing a<BR>cause, the second (हेतु) of the five<BR>members of an Indian syllogism<BR>(according to the Vaiśeṣikas).<BR>--4 A<BR>butt, mark (लक्ष्य).<BR>--5 A place,<BR>quarter.<BR>--6 Refusal, rejection.<BR>--7 Fame,<BR>reputation.<BR>--8 Deceit.<BR>--9 (अपकृष्टो<BR>देशः) A bad or wrong place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेशिन्
अपदेशिन् a. Pretending to be,<BR>assuming the appearance of (in comp.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेश्य
अपदेश्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be feigned,<BR>adduced &c.<BR>--2 Being in a wrong<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदिशं|अपदिश
अपदिशं ind. Half a point<BR>between two regions of the compass<BR>(दिशयोर्मध्ये), in an intermediate region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपदेवता
अपदेवता A goblin, evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्रव्यं|अपद्रव्य
अपद्रव्यं A bad thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपद्वारं|अपद्वार
अपद्वारं A side door or entrance,<BR>an entrance other than the proper<BR>door; अपद्वारैर्वीक्षते निर्यियासुः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधा
अपधा Ved. Shutting up,<BR>hiding (वारणार्थं निरोधः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधाव्
अपधाव् {c1c} P. To prevaricate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधावनं
अपधावनं Prevarication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपधूम
अपधूम a. Free from smoke; ˚त्व<BR>R. 10. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्यै
अपध्यै {c1c} P. To think ill of, have<BR>evil thoughts about, curse mentally;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">Page0107-b+ 56</a>]<BR>अपध्याता च विप्रेण न्यपतद्धरणतिले Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्यानं|अपध्यान
अपध्यानं Evil thoughts, thinking<BR>ill of, cursing mentally; तदपध्यानात्<BR>पिशाचतामुपगतं K. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंस्
अपध्वंस् {c1c} A. (rarely P.)<BR>1 To<BR>pack off, clear out; अपध्वंसेति बहुशो<BR>वदन् क्रोधसमन्वितः Hariv.<BR>--2 To abuse,<BR>revile, scold; न<BR>चाप्यन्यमपध्वंसेत्कदाचित्कोपसंयुतः Mb. --Caus. To free<BR>from dust; blow away (as dust &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंसः|अपध्वंस
अपध्वंसः<BR>1 Degradation, falling off<BR>or from, disgrace.<BR>--2 Concealment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः, --जा a person of a<BR>mixed, degraded and impure caste (where<BR>the mother belongs to a higher caste<BR>than the father's) Ms. 10. 41, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वंसिन्
अपध्वंसिन् a. Destroying, removing;<BR>अर्वैनसामपध्वंसि जप्यं त्रिष्वघमर्षणं Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वस्त|अपध्वस्तः
अपध्वस्त p. p.<BR>1 Reviled, cursed,<BR>accursed, contemptible, to be<BR>disdained.<BR>--2 Pounded badly or<BR>imperfectly (अवचूर्णित).<BR>--3 Abandoned.<BR>--स्तः A vile wretch, lost to all<BR>sense of right and virtue; मूर्ख<BR>अपध्वस्तोसि Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपध्वांत|अपध्वान्त
अपध्वांत a. Sounding wrongly.<BR>--तं A wrong or harsh sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनस
अपनस a. Without a nose; असिं<BR>कौक्षेयमुद्यम्य चकारापनसं मुखं Bk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनामन्
अपनामन् Having a bad name.<BR>--n.<BR>--(म) A bad name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनी
अपनी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To lead or carry<BR>away, carry or lead off; cause to<BR>retire; तमप्यपनयेत् Ms. 3. 242.<BR>--2 (a)<BR>To remove (in all senses),<BR>destroy, take away; आर्तानां<BR>भयमपनेनुमात्तधन्वा Ś. 6. 26; शत्रूनपनेष्यामि<BR>Bk. 16. 30; so तृप्णां, भयं, भ्रमं, दोषं,<BR>संशयं, &c. (b) To rob, steal, take<BR>away, carry away or off; रक्षसा भीरु<BR>यतोऽपनीता R. 13. 24.<BR>--3 To extract, take<BR>or draw out from (dart, oil &c.);<BR>अपनीताशेषशल्यं Dk. 31; दिष्ट्या शल्यं<BR>मे हृदयादपनीतमिव V. 5.<BR>--4 To put<BR>off or away, take or pull off (dress,<BR>ornaments, fetters &c.);<BR>अपनीताशेषराजचिह्ना K. 206; एषां<BR>बंधनान्यपनय H. 1; चरणान्निगडमपनय Mk. 6;<BR>अपनयंतु भवत्यो मृगयावेषं Ś. 2;<BR>R. 4. 64.<BR>--5 To deny; नैतन्मया<BR>निर्दिष्टमित्यपनयति Kull. on Ms. 8. 53.<BR>--6<BR>To except, exclude from a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनयः|अपनय
अपनयः<BR>1 Taking away,<BR>removing; refuting (as an assertion);<BR>स्वमतात्प्रच्यावनमपनयो निग्रहः<BR>P. VIII. 2. 94 Com.<BR>--2 A bad policy or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">Page0107-c+ 56</a>]<BR>conduct.<BR>--3 Injury, offence (अपकार); ततः<BR>सपत्नापनयस्मरणानुशयस्फुरा Śi. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनयनं|अपनयन
अपनयनं<BR>1 Taking away,<BR>removing, extracting &c.; गंडस्वेद˚<BR>Me. 26; नातिश्रमापनयनाय Ś. 5. 6.<BR>--2<BR>Healing, destroying, curing<BR>(disease &c.); रोगाच्चापनयने<BR>P. V. 4. 49.<BR>--3 Discharge or acquittance<BR>of a debt or obligation.<BR>--4<BR>Subtraction, deduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनीत
अपनीत p. p.<BR>1 Taken away;<BR>removed, pulled off &c.<BR>--2 Removed<BR>from, deviating from, opposed to,<BR>contradictory; तत्त्वधर्मापनीतस्य<BR>दृश्यते कर्मणः फलं Rām.<BR>--3 Badly done<BR>or executed, spoiled; अपनीतं<BR>सुनीतेन योऽर्थं प्रत्यानिनीषते Mb.<BR>--4 Paid<BR>off, discharged.<BR>--तं Bad conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुद्
अपनुद् {c6c} P. To remove, take<BR>or drive away, destroy;<BR>नारीणामपनुनुदुर्न देहखेदान् Bk. 10. 13; न हि<BR>प्रपश्यामि ममापनुद्यात् यच्छोकं Bg. 2. 8<BR>expiate, atone for (as sin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपनुत्तिः|अपनुत्ति
अपनुत्तिः f., नोदः --नोदनं Removing,<BR>taking away, removal, destroying,<BR>driving away; expiation, atonement<BR>(as of a sin); पापानामपनुत्तये<BR>Ms. 11. 210, 140, 93; Y. 3. 306; गुरुतल्प˚<BR>Ms. 11. 107; ब्रह्महत्यापनोदाय 11. 76; कृच्छ्रोयं<BR>सर्वपापापनोदनः 11. 216, 253, 261.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपन्न
अपन्न a. Ved. Not going down, not<BR>fallen or sunk, indestructible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपयस्
अपपयस् a. Waterless, dry;<BR>Ki. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपाठः|अपपाठ
अपपाठः A wrong or bad reading<BR>(in a text); mistake in reading;<BR>द्वादशापपाठा अस्य जाताः<BR>P. IV. 4. 64 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्र
अपपात्र a.<BR>1 Deprived of the use of<BR>common vessels; using separate<BR>vessels (from which no one else will eat);<BR>अपपात्राश्च कर्तव्याः Ms. 10. 51.<BR>--2 Of<BR>low caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपात्रितः|अपपात्रित
अपपात्रितः [पात्रभोजनात् बाहिष्कृतः]<BR>One who has lost his caste through<BR>some great sin or offence, and<BR>who is, therefore, not allowed by<BR>his relatives to eat or drink from<BR>a common vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपाद
अपपाद a. Having bad feet; ˚त्र<BR>having no shoe, shoeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपानं|अपपान
अपपानं A bad drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपित्वं|अपपित्व
अपपित्वं Ved. Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपपूत
अपपूत a. Having badly formed<BR>hips.<BR>--तौ Badly formed hips;<BR>P. VI. 2. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपप्रजाता
अपप्रजाता A female that has<BR>suffered a miscarriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपप्रदानं|अपप्रदान
अपप्रदानं A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपप्रोषितं|अपप्रोषित
अपप्रोषितं Ved. Fault or evil<BR>caused by wrong departure (प्रवासदोष.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपबर्हिस्
अपबर्हिस् a. Not having the<BR>use of Barhis (बर्हिर्होमराहित.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपबाहुकः|अपबाहुक
अपबाहुकः A bad arm; stiffness<BR>in the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभय
अपभय a. Free from fear,<BR>fearless, undaunted; ततः प्रहस्यापभयः<BR>पुरंदरं पुनर्बभाषे तुरगस्य रक्षिता R. 3. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभरणी
अपभरणी The last asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभर्तृ|अपभर्त्तृ
अपभर्तृ a. Ved. Taking away,<BR>destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभाष्
अपभाष् {c1c} A. To abuse,<BR>revile, defame, libel; न केवलं यो<BR>महतोपभाषते शृणोति तस्मादपि यः स पापभाक्<BR>Ku. 5. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभाषणं|अपभाषण
अपभाषणं Reviling, defamation,<BR>libel, calumny, vituperation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभू
अपभू {c1c} P. To be away, be<BR>absent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभूतिः|अपभूति
अपभूतिः f. Defeat, damage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रंश्
अपभ्रंश् {c1c} A. To fall away or off.<BR>--Caus. To dismiss, discharge;<BR>अपभ्रंशितोऽधिकारात् चाणक्यहतकः Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रंशः|अपभ्रंश
अपभ्रंशः<BR>1 Falling down or away, a<BR>fall; अत्यारूढिर्भवति महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा<BR>Ś. 4 v. l. ending in a (precipitate)<BR>fall.<BR>--2 A corrupted word,<BR>corruption; घर is an अपभ्रंश or corruption<BR>of गृह; (hence) an incorrect word<BR>whether formed against the rules of<BR>grammar or used in a sense not<BR>strictly Sanskrit; see अपशब्द.<BR>--3 A<BR>corrupt language, one of the lowest<BR>forms of the Prākṛta dialect used by<BR>cowherds &c. (in kāvyas); (in<BR>Śāstras) any language other than<BR>Sanskrit; आभीरादिगिरः काव्येष्वपभ्रंश इति स्मृताः ।<BR>शास्त्रेषु संस्कृतादन्यदपभ्रंशतयोदितम् ॥ Kāv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपभ्रष्ट
अपभ्रष्ट p. p. Fallen away,<BR>corrupted (as a dialect).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपम|अपमः
अपम a. [अपकृष्टं मीयते, मा बाहु˚ क]<BR>Ved. The most distant or remote,<BR>the last, lowest in caste, most<BR>degraded (जात्यातिनिकृष्ट).<BR>--मः (In astr.)<BR>Declination; the ecliptic; परिसरतां<BR>गगनसदां चलनं किंचिद्भवेदपमः Sid. Śir.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्या the line of the<BR>ecliptic; see क्रांतिज्या.<BR>--मंडलं, --वृत्तं the<BR>ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमर्दः|अपमर्द|अपमर्द्द
अपमर्दः What is swept away,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">Page0108-b+ 55</a>]<BR>dust, dirt; हयहस्तिकरीषाभ्यामपमर्दः कृतो<BR>महान् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमर्शः|अपमर्श
अपमर्शः Touching, grazing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमन्
अपमन् Caus. To disrespect,<BR>dishonour, despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमानः|अपमान|अपमानं
अपमानः Disrespect, dishonour,<BR>disgrace; despising, slighting,<BR>contempt; लभते बुद्ध्यवज्ञानमपमानं च पुष्कलं<BR>Pt. 1. 63; समुद्रेण मम<BR>भृत्यस्यांडान्यपहृत्य मेऽपमानस्थानं कृतं Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमानिन्
अपमानिन् a. Dishonouring,<BR>disrespecting, slighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमार्गः|अपमार्ग
अपमार्गः<BR>1 A by-path, side way;<BR>a bad way.<BR>--2 Shampooing, rubbing<BR>&c. of the body (अंगपरिमार्जनं)<BR>Śi. 9. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमित्य
अपमित्य Ved. To be thrown<BR>away.<BR>--त्यं, --त्यकं Debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमुख
अपमुख a.<BR>1 Having the face<BR>averted.<BR>--2 Ill-favoured, ill-looking.<BR>--खं ind. Without the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमूर्धन्
अपमूर्धन् a. Headless; ˚कलेवरं Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृज्
अपमृज् {c2c} P., {c10c} P. To wipe off,<BR>efface, blot or wipe out, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमार्जनं|अपमार्जन
अपमार्जनं<BR>1 Wiping away,<BR>cleansing, purifying.<BR>--2 Shaving, paring.<BR>--3 Chips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृत्युः|अपमृत्यु
अपमृत्युः [अपकृष्टो दुष्टहेतुजन्यत्वेन मृत्युः]<BR>1 Sudden or untimely death,<BR>accidental or unnatural death;<BR>भर्तृसक्तोऽपमृत्युस्तस्य संचरति Pt. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Any great danger, illness &c. from<BR>which a person, hopelessly given up<BR>for lost, recovers, quite contrary to<BR>expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपमृषित
अपमृषित a.<BR>1 Unintelligible,<BR>obscure as a वाक्य or speech.<BR>--2<BR>Unbearable, not borne or liked (असोढ,<BR>अतितिक्षित); विहितं मयाद्य<BR>सदसीदमपमृषितमच्युतार्चनं । यस्य &c. Śi. 15. 46 (for the<BR>formation of the word see Malli.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयशस्
अपयशस् n. (शः) Infamy,<BR>disgrace, ill-repute; अपयशो यद्यस्ति किं<BR>मृत्युना Bh. 2. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपया
अपया {c2c} P. To depart, go away,<BR>retire, withdraw, fall off or away,<BR>disappear; अपयातमेव हि विमानमंडलैः<BR>U. 6. 4; शोको दिनेषु गच्छत्सु<BR>वर्धतामपयाति किं H. 4. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपयानं|अपयान
अपयानं Going away, departure,<BR>retreat, flight, escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर|अपरं|अपरः
अपर a. (treated as a pronoun in<BR>some senses)<BR>1 Having nothing<BR>higher or superior, unrivalled, matchless;<BR>without a rival or second (नास्ति परो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-c" target="_blank">Page0108-c+ 57</a>]<BR>यस्मात्); स्त्रीरत्नसृष्टिरपरा प्रतिभाति सामे<BR>Ś. 2. 9; cf. अनुत्तम, अनुत्तर.<BR>--2 [न पृणाति<BR>संतोषयति पॄ-अच्] (a) Another, other<BR>(used as adj. or subst.). (b) More,<BR>additional; Ms. 11. 5. (c) Second,<BR>another Pt. 4. 37; खं केशवोऽपर इवाक्रमितुं<BR>प्रवृत्तः Mk. 5. 2 like another (rival)<BR>Keśava. (d) Different; other; अन्ये<BR>कृतयुगे धर्मास्त्रेतायां द्वापरेऽपरे Ms. 1. 85;<BR>Ks. 26. 235; Pt. 4. 6 (with gen).<BR>(e) Ordinay, of the middle sort<BR>(मध्यम); परितप्तोप्यपरः सुसंवृतिः<BR>Śi. 16. 23.<BR>--3 Belonging to another, not<BR>one's own (opp. स्व); यदि<BR>स्वाश्चापराश्चैव विंदेरन् योषितो द्विजाः Ms. 9. 85 of<BR>another caste.<BR>--4 Hinder, posterior,<BR>latter, later, (in time or space) (opp.<BR>पूर्व); the last; पूर्वासंध्यां<BR>जपंस्तिष्ठेत्स्वकाले चापरां चिरं Ms. 4. 93; रात्रेरपरः<BR>कालः Nir.; oft. used as first member<BR>of a genitive Tatpuruṣa comp.<BR>meaning ‘the hind part,’ ‘latter part<BR>or half’; ˚पक्षः the latter half of a<BR>month; ˚हेमंतः latter half of winter;<BR>˚कायः hind part of the body &c.; ˚वर्षा<BR>˚शरद् latter part of the rains, autumn<BR>&c.<BR>--5 Following, the next.<BR>--6<BR>Western; पयसि प्रपित्सुरपरांबुनिधेः Śi. 9. 1,<BR>Ku. 1. 1; Mu. 4. 21.<BR>--7 Inferior, lower<BR>(निकृष्टः); अपरेयमितस्त्वन्यां प्रकृतिं विद्धि<BR>मे परां Bg. 7. 5.<BR>--8 (In Nyāya)<BR>Nonextensive, not covering too much,<BR>one of the two kinds of सामान्य, see<BR>Bhāṣā P. 8. (परं = अधिकवृत्ति) higher,<BR>अपरं = न्यूनवृत्ति lower, or<BR>अधिकदेशवृत्तित्वं परं, अल्पदेशवृत्तित्वं अपरं Muktā.<BR>--9 Distant; opposite. When अपर is<BR>used in the singular as a correlative<BR>to एक the one, former, it means<BR>the other, the latter; एको ययौ<BR>चैत्ररथप्रदेशान् सौराज्यरम्यानपरो विदर्भान्<BR>R. 5. 60; when used in pl. it<BR>means ‘others’, ‘and others’, and<BR>the words generally used as its<BR>correlatives are एके, केचित् -काश्चित् &c.,<BR>अपरे, अन्ये; केचिद्रक्तपटीकृताश्च जाटिलाः<BR>कापालिकाश्चापरे Pt. 4. 34; एके<BR>समूहुर्बलरेणुसंहतिं शिरोभिराज्ञामपरे महीभृतः<BR>Śi. 12. 45 some-others; शाखिनः<BR>केचिदध्यष्ठुर्न्यमांक्षुरपरेंबुधौ । अन्ये त्वलंघिषुः<BR>शैलान् गुहास्क्न्ये न्येलषत ॥<BR>केचिदासिषत स्तब्धा भयात्केचिदघूर्णिषुः ।<BR>उदतारिषुरंभोधिं वानराः सेतुनापरे Bk. 15. 31-33.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The hind foot of an<BR>elephant; बद्धापराणि परितो<BR>निगडान्यलावीत् Śi. 5. 48 (Malli. चरमपादाग्राणि).<BR>--2 An enemy (न पृणाति संतोषयाति).<BR>--रा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-a" target="_blank">Page0109-a+ 58</a>]<BR>1 Western direction, the west.<BR>--2 The<BR>hind part of an elephant.<BR>--3 Sacred<BR>learning, learning the four Vedas<BR>with the 6 Aṅgas.<BR>--4 The womb; the<BR>outer skin of the embryo.<BR>--5<BR>Suppressed menstruation in pregnancy.<BR>--री Ved. The future, future times;<BR>अतापरीभ्योमघवा विजिग्ये Rv. 1. 32. 13.<BR>--रं<BR>1 The future, any thing to be<BR>done in future (कार्य);<BR>तदेतद्ब्रह्मापूर्वमपरमनंतं Bṛ. Ār. Up. (नास्ति अपरं<BR>कार्यं यस्य).<BR>--2 The hind quarter of<BR>an elephant.<BR>--रं adv. Again,<BR>moreover, in future, for the future;<BR>अपरंच moreover; अपरेण behind, west<BR>of, to the west of (with gen. or<BR>acc.). [cf. Goth. afar; Germ. aber,<BR>as in aberglauben].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्नि<BR>(अग्नी dual) {1} the southern and<BR>western fires (दक्षिण and गार्हपत्य). {2}<BR>the last fire i. e. used at the<BR>funeral ceremony (˚ग्निः).<BR>--अंगं one<BR>of the 8 divisions of गुणीभूतव्यंग्य (the<BR>second kind of काव्य) mentioned in<BR>K. P. 5. In this the व्यंग्य or<BR>suggested sense is subordinate to<BR>something else; अगूढमपरस्यांगं; अपरस्य<BR>रसादेर्वाच्यस्य वा (वाक्यार्थीभूतस्य) अंगं रसादि<BR>अनुरणनरूपं वा; e. g. अयं स<BR>रसनोत्कर्षी पीनस्तनविमर्दनः । नाभ्यूरुजघनस्पर्शी<BR>नीविविस्रंसनः करः, where शृंगार is<BR>subordinate to करुण.<BR>--अंत a. living at the<BR>western borders.<BR>--(तः) {1} the western<BR>border or extremity, the extreme<BR>end or term; the western shore. {2}<BR>(pl.) the country or inhabitants<BR>of the western-borders near the<BR>Sahya mountain; अपरांतजयोद्यतैः (<BR>अनीकैः) R. 4. 53 western people. {3}<BR>the kings of this country. {4} death,<BR>˚ज्ञानं anticipation of one's end. {5}<BR>the hind foot of an elephant;<BR>मृदुचलदपरांतोदीरितांदूनिनादं Śi. 11. 7;<BR>18. 32.<BR>--अंतकः {1} = ˚अंतः pl. {2} N. of<BR>a song; Y. 3. 113; ˚अंतिका N. of a<BR>metre consisting of 64 mātrās.<BR>--अपराः, --रे, --राणि another and another,<BR>several, various.<BR>--अर्धं the latter or<BR>second half.<BR>--अह्णः [fr. अहन् changed to<BR>अह्न, P. II. 4. 29, V. 4. 88] the latter<BR>part of the day, the afternoon,<BR>closing or last watch of the day;<BR>Ms. 3. 278; Śi. 9. 4; ˚तन, ˚ह्नेतन belonging<BR>to this time; ˚कृतं P. II. 1. 45.<BR>--इतरा the east.<BR>--कान्यकुब्ज a. situated<BR>in or belonging to the western part<BR>of Kānyakubja.<BR>--कालः later period.<BR>--गोदानं (also गोडनि or गोडानि) N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-b" target="_blank">Page0109-b+ 58</a>]<BR>of a country to the west of<BR>Mahāmeru (according to Buddhistic<BR>ideas).<BR>--ज a. born later or at the<BR>end of the world.<BR>--(जः) the<BR>destroying fire.<BR>--जनः an inhabitant of<BR>the west, the western people.<BR>--दक्षिणं ind. in the southwest<BR>(belonging to the तिष्ठद्रु class).<BR>--पक्षः {1} the<BR>second or dark half of the month.<BR>{2} the other or opposite side; a<BR>defendant (in law).<BR>--पंचालाः the<BR>western Pañcālas.<BR>--पर a. one and the<BR>other, several, various; अपरपराः सार्थाः<BR>गच्छंति P. VI. 1. 144 Sk. several<BR>caravans go; (अपरे च परे च सकृदेव गच्छंति).<BR>--पाणिनीयाः the pupils of Pāṇini<BR>living in the west.<BR>--प्रणेय a. easily<BR>led or influenced by others, docile,<BR>tractable.<BR>--भावः {1} being another or<BR>different, difference. {2} succession,<BR>continuation.<BR>--रात्रः [अपरं रात्रेः] the<BR>latter or closing part of night, the<BR>last watch of night (P. V. 4. 87);<BR>˚कृतं P. II. 1. 45.<BR>--लोकः the other<BR>world, the next world, Paradise.<BR>--वक्त्रा, --क्त्रं N. of a metre.<BR>--वैराग्यं<BR>a kind of Vairāgya mentioned by<BR>Patañjali (दृष्टानुश्राविकविषयवितृष्णस्य<BR>वशीकारसंज्ञं वैराग्यं).<BR>--सक्थं the hind<BR>thigh.<BR>--स्वस्तिकं the western point<BR>in the horizon.<BR>--हैमन a. belonging<BR>to the latter half of winter (<BR>P. VII. 3. 11).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरता
अपरता --त्वं<BR>1 Being another or<BR>different (one of the 24 guṇas);<BR>difference, opposition, contrariety,<BR>relativeness.<BR>--2 Nearness.<BR>--3<BR>Distance, posteriority (in time or<BR>space).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्वं|अपरत्व
अपरता --त्वं<BR>1 Being another or<BR>different (one of the 24 guṇas);<BR>difference, opposition, contrariety,<BR>relativeness.<BR>--2 Nearness.<BR>--3<BR>Distance, posteriority (in time or<BR>space).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरत्र
अपरत्र adv. In another place,<BR>elsewhere; एकत्र or क्वचित्-अपरत्र in one<BR>place-in another place; in the first<BR>case-in the second case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरथा
अपरथा ind. In another manner;<BR>Śi. 6. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवत्|अपरवन्त्
अपरवत् a. Like what follows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्पर|अपरस्परं
अपरस्पर a. [अपर-पर] One after<BR>another, uninterrupted, continued<BR>(as applied to an action); अपरस्पराः<BR>क्रियासातत्ये P. VI. 1. 144; सुट् निपात्यते;<BR>˚राः सार्था गच्छंति सततमविच्छेदेन<BR>गच्छंतीत्यर्थः Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरेद्युः
अपरेद्युः adv. On the following<BR>day Ms. 3. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरंज्|अपरञ्ज्
अपरंज् (Used in pass. only)<BR>To be disaffected or discontented<BR>(with abl); नयहीनादपरज्यते जनः<BR>Ki. 2. 49; K. 287.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरक्त
अपरक्त a.<BR>1 Colourless, bloodless,<BR>pale; श्वासापरक्ताधरः Ś. 6. 5.<BR>--2<BR>Discontented, dissatisfied, disaffected;<BR>चंद्रगुप्तादपरक्ताः Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरागः|अपराग
अपरागः<BR>1 Discontent,<BR>dissatisfaction, disaffection; ˚हेतून् ज्ञातुमिच्छामि<BR>Mu. 3; अपरागसमीरणेरितः Ki. 2. 50,<BR>K. 329.<BR>--2 Apathy, enmity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरतिः|अपरति
अपरतिः f.<BR>1 Cessation (= अवरति<BR>q. v.).<BR>--2 Dissatisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरवः|अपरव
अपरवः<BR>1 Contest, dispute (about<BR>the enjoyment of property); ˚उज्झित<BR>uncontested, undisputed (as<BR>possession of any thing).<BR>--2 Ill-repute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरस्पर|अपरस्परं
अपरस्पर a. [अ-परस्पर] Not<BR>reciprocal, not mutual; असत्यमप्रतिष्ठं ते<BR>जगदाहुरनीश्वरं । अपरस्परसंभूतं<BR>किमन्यत्कामहैतुकं Bg. 16. 8 (Mr. Telang renders<BR>˚र by ‘produced by union of male and<BR>female’, caused by lust, where<BR>अपरस्पर must be supposed to be<BR>connected with अपरस्पर under अपर q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरांच्
अपरांच् a. [˚राङ्, ˚राची, ˚राक्]<BR>Not averted, fronting, facing, in<BR>front. --ind. In front of.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुख a. (खी f.) {1} not turning away<BR>the face, with unaverted face. {2}<BR>presenting a bold front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजित|अपराजितः
अपराजित a. Unconquered,<BR>invincible, unsurpassed; ˚ता दिक् the<BR>northeast direction, so called because<BR>the Gods were not defeated there; त<BR>(देवासुराः) उदीच्यां प्राच्यां दिश्ययतंत ते ततो<BR>न पराजयंत सैषा दिगपराजिता Ait. Br.,<BR>Ms. 6. 31.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A sort of<BR>poisonous insect.<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu; of Śiva.<BR>--3 One of the 11 Rudras.<BR>--4 A class<BR>of divinities forming a portion of<BR>the अनुत्तर divinities of the Jainas.<BR>--5 N. of a sage.<BR>--ता<BR>1 N. of Durgā, to<BR>be worshipped on the Vijayādaśamī<BR>or Daśarā day; दशम्यां च नरैः<BR>सम्यक् पूजनीयाऽपराजिता ।… ददाति विजयं देवी<BR>पूजिता जयवर्धिनी Skanda P.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>several plants; दूर्वा, शेफालिका, जयंती,<BR>असन, शंखिनी, हपुषा, असनपणीं.<BR>--3 A kind<BR>of plant (or ओषधि) fastened round<BR>the wrist and serving as a charm or<BR>amulet; see Ś. 7. (In Vikramorvaśī<BR>Act 2, Kālidāsa uses अपराजिता in<BR>the sense of a spell or विद्या; ननु भगवता<BR>देवगुरुणा अपराजितां नाम<BR>शिखाबंधनविद्यामुपदिशता त्रिदशपरिपक्षस्यालंघनीये कृते स्वः).<BR>--4 The northeast quarter; see under<BR>˚त above.<BR>--5 A kind of metre of 4<BR>lines with 14 syllables in each.<BR>--6 A sort of Yoginī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजिष्णु
अपराजिष्णु --पराजेय a. Invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराजेय
अपराजिष्णु --पराजेय a. Invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराध्
अपराध् {c4c} {c5c} P.<BR>1 To offend, wrong,<BR>sin against, commit an offence<BR>against; (with gen. or loc. of person<BR>or thing); यौवनमत्रापराध्यति Mk. 9<BR>is to blame; यस्मिनूकस्मिन्नपि पूजर्हेऽ<BR>पराद्धा शकुंतला Ś. 4; अपराद्धोस्मि<BR>तत्रभवतः कण्वस्य Ś. 7; महतां योऽपराध्येत<BR>दूरस्थोस्मीति नाश्वसेत् Pt. 1. 307; V. 2; किं<BR>पुनरसुरावलेपेन भवतीनामपराद्धं V. 1;<BR>sometimes with dat. also; न दूये<BR>सात्वतीसूनुर्यन्मह्यमपराध्यति Śi. 2. 11.<BR>--2<BR>To annoy, disturb.<BR>--3 To prohibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्ध
अपराद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Sinned, offended,<BR>having committed an offence,<BR>guilty, an offender, criminal (used in an<BR>active sense); कृतवत्यसि<BR>नावधीरणामपराद्धेऽपि यदा चिरं मयि R. 8. 48; प्रोवाच<BR>कोशलपतिः प्रथमापराद्धः 9. 79 the first<BR>to offend.<BR>--2 Missed, not<BR>hitting the mark (as an arrow);<BR>मृगदेहापराद्धैर्नामेषुमोक्षणैः Dk. 163; ˚इषुः or<BR>˚पृषत्कः an archer whose arrows<BR>always miss the mark, an unskilful<BR>archer; निमित्तादपराद्धेषोर्धानुष्कस्येव<BR>वल्गितं Śi. 2. 27.<BR>--3 Violated,<BR>transgressed; अपराद्धा<BR>अभिषेकवेलोपाध्यायस्य V. 3.<BR>--द्धं [भावे क्तः] An offence,<BR>crime, injury; न तु ग्रीष्मस्यैवं<BR>सुभगमपराद्धं युवतिषु Ś. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराद्धिः|अपराद्धि
अपराद्धिः f.<BR>1 Fault, mistake,<BR>offence.<BR>--2 Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधः|अपराध
अपराधः An offence, a fault, guilt,<BR>crime, sin, mistake, error; (32 kinds<BR>are usually stated in Śāstras);<BR>कमपराधलवं मयि पश्यसि V. 4. 29;<BR>यथापराधदंडानां R. 1. 6; यथेंद्रशत्रुः स्वरतोऽपराधात्<BR>Śik. 52 mistake or error in accent;<BR>sometimes with gen. or loc. of<BR>person; अदः सुरेंद्रस्य कृतापराधान् दैत्यान्<BR>V. 1. 18; कृतापराधमिव<BR>त्वय्यात्मानमवगच्छति K. 203.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भंजनः<BR>the destroyer of sins, epithet of Śiva;<BR>˚स्तोत्रं a short poem by<BR>Śankarāchārya in praise of Śiva, the fourth<BR>line of the verses being usually<BR>क्षंतव्यो मेपराधः शिव शिव शिवभोः श्रीमहांदेव शंभो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपराधिन्
अपराधिन् a. Offending, guilty,<BR>offender, criminal; अपराधी नामाहं प्रसीद<BR>रंभोरु V. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरापरण
अपरापरण a. Destitute of<BR>descendants or offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिक्रम
अपरिक्रम a.<BR>1 Unable to walk<BR>round.<BR>--2 Not diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिग्रह|अपरिग्रहः
अपरिग्रह a. Without possessions<BR>or belongings, attendants &c; quite<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">Page0110-b+ 53</a>]<BR>destitute, as in निराशीरपरिग्रहः<BR>--हः<BR>1<BR>Non-acceptance, rejection,<BR>renunciation, one of the several kinds of<BR>yamas (mental restraints) stated in<BR>Yoga Śāstra by Patañjali.<BR>--2<BR>Destitution, poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचयिन्
अपरिचयिन्, --परिचेय a. Having<BR>no acquaintance; unsocial,<BR>misanthropic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिचेय
अपरिचयिन्, --परिचेय a. Having<BR>no acquaintance; unsocial,<BR>misanthropic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छद
अपरिच्छद a. Poor, destitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छिन्न|अपरिच्छिन्नं
अपरिच्छिन्न a.<BR>1 Undiscerned,<BR>undistinguished.<BR>--2 Continuous,<BR>connected, without interval or<BR>separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिच्छेदः|अपरिच्छेद
अपरिच्छेदः<BR>1 Want of<BR>distinction or division.<BR>--2 Want of order<BR>or arrangement.<BR>--3 Want of<BR>judgment.<BR>--4 Continuance, connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिज्यानिः|अपरिज्यानि
अपरिज्यानिः f. Not losing; not<BR>growing old or decaying; इष्टापूर्तस्य˚<BR>N. of a ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणयः|अपरिणय
अपरिणयः Celibacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणीता
अपरिणीता An unmarried girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिणामः|अपरिणाम
अपरिणामः Unchangeableness;<BR>˚दर्शिन् not prudent, improvident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिपर
अपरिपर a. Ved. Not going by<BR>a tortuous course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिनिष्ठित
अपरिनिष्ठित a. Not properly<BR>placed or established;<BR>˚तस्योपदेशस्यान्याय्यं प्रकाशनं M. 1 not properly<BR>grounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमाण
अपरिमाण, अपरिमित, अपरिमेय a.<BR>Immeasurable, immense, unbounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमित|अपरिमितं
अपरिमाण, अपरिमित, अपरिमेय a.<BR>Immeasurable, immense, unbounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिमेय
अपरिमाण, अपरिमित, अपरिमेय a.<BR>Immeasurable, immense, unbounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिम्लान|अपरिम्लानः
अपरिम्लान a. Not fading,<BR>withering, or decaying.<BR>--नः N. of a plant<BR>(महासहावृक्ष) Gomphrena Globosa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरियाणि
अपरियाणि [अ-परि˚] Not<BR>walking, about (used in curses only);<BR>see अप्रयाणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिविष्ट
अपरिविष्ट a. Ved. Not covered<BR>or enclosed (अव्याप्त, वेष्टनशून्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिवृत
अपरिवृत a. Not enclosed or<BR>fenced on all sides (as a field).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिशेष|अपरिशेषः
अपरिशेष a. Not leaving a<BR>remainder; all-surrounding,<BR>all-pervading; ˚षं ज्ञानं Sāṅ. K.<BR>--षः<BR>Absence of remainder or limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्करः
अपरिष्करः Want of polish or<BR>refinement (moral or physical);<BR>coarseness, rudeness, unrefined state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्कृत|अपरिष्कृतं
अपरिष्कृत a. Unpolished,<BR>unrefined, rude, coarse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिष्टिः|अपरिष्टि
अपरिष्टिः f. [रिष्टेर्हिसाया अभावः]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">Page0110-c+ 53</a>]<BR>Worship (पूजाया हिंसाहेतुकद्वेषशून्यत्वात्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिसर|अपरिसरः
अपरिसर a.<BR>1 Not near, distant.<BR>--2 Not extensive, not current.<BR>--रः<BR>Absence of extent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिसंख्यानं|अपरिसङ्ख्यान|अपरिसंख्यान
अपरिसंख्यानं Infinity,<BR>innumerableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिस्कंद|अपरिस्कन्द
अपरिस्कंद a. Motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिहरणीय
अपरिहरणीय, अपरिहार्य a.<BR>1<BR>Inevitable.<BR>--2 Not to be abandoned.<BR>--3 Not to be degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिहार्य|अपरिहार्य्य|अपरिहार्य्यं
अपरिहरणीय, अपरिहार्य a.<BR>1<BR>Inevitable.<BR>--2 Not to be abandoned.<BR>--3 Not to be degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरिह्वृत
अपरिह्वृत a. Ved. Not<BR>endangered or afflicted; straightforward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीक्षित
अपरीक्षित a.<BR>1 Unexamined;<BR>एतच्चापरीक्षितक्रयविषयं Mit.; untried,<BR>untested, unproved.<BR>--2 Ill-considered,<BR>foolish, thoughtless (of person or<BR>thing); ˚कारकं नाम पंच मं तत्रं Pt. 5<BR>‘the inconsiderate doer.’<BR>--3 Not<BR>clearly proved or established.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरीत|अपरीतः
अपरीत a. Ved. Not surrounded<BR>or encircled, not approached (<BR>अनभिगत).<BR>--तः N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरुष्
अपरुष् a. Free from anger; अपरुषा<BR>परुषाक्षरमीरिता R. 9. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरूप|अपरूपं
अपरूप a. (--पा, --पी f.) Ugly,<BR>deformed, odd-shaped.<BR>--पं<BR>1<BR>Deformity, monstrosity.<BR>--2 Delight,<BR>wonder (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्ष
अपरोक्ष a.<BR>1 Not invisible,<BR>perceptible to the senses, visible.<BR>--2<BR>Not distant or remote.<BR>--क्षं adv.<BR>In the presence of (with gen.);<BR>अपरोक्षात् perceptibly, visibly,<BR>manifestly, openly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुभूतिः f.<BR>direct cognition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोक्षयति
अपरोक्षयति Den. P. To make<BR>perceptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोधः|अपरोध
अपरोधः Exclusion, prohibition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपरोपः|अपरोप
अपरोपः Extermination,<BR>dethronement; Mu. 2. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्ण
अपर्ण a. Leafless.<BR>--र्णा N. of<BR>Durgā or Pārvatī; Kālidāsa thus<BR>accounts for the name:<BR>--स्वयंविशीर्णद्रुमपर्णवृत्तिता परा हि काष्ठा तपसस्तया पुनः ।<BR>तदप्यपाकीर्णमिति प्रियंवदां वदंत्यपर्णोति च तां<BR>पुराविदः Ku. 5. 28; cf. Śiva P. चतुर्थे<BR>त्यक्तपर्णा च अपर्णाख्यामवाप सा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्तु|अपर्तुः|अपर्त्तु
अपर्तु a.<BR>1 Untimely.<BR>--2 Past<BR>menstruation time (निवृत्तरजस्का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्यंत|अपर्यन्त|अपर्य्यन्त
अपर्यंत a. Unlimited, unbounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याप्त|अपर्य्याप्त|अपर्य्याप्तं
अपर्याप्त a.<BR>1 Not sufficient or<BR>enough, incomplete, insufficient.<BR>--2<BR>Unlimited.<BR>--3 Unable (to do its<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">Page0111-a+ 56</a>]<BR>work), incompetent; अपर्याप्तं<BR>तदस्माकं बलं भीष्माभिरक्षितं Bg. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याप्तिः|अपर्याप्ति|अपर्य्याप्ति
अपर्याप्तिः f. Insufficiency;<BR>अमात्यभूरिवसोरात्मजेत्यपर्याप्तिर्बहुमानस्य Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्याय|अपर्यायः|अपर्य्याय
अपर्याय a. Without order.<BR>--यः<BR>Want of order or method.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्युषित|अपर्य्युषित|अपर्य्युषितं
अपर्युषित a. Not standing<BR>overnight, fresh, new (as a flower); not<BR>standing over till the next day;<BR>˚प्रतिज्ञे मारुतौ Ve. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपर्वन्
अपर्वन् a. Without a joint. --n.<BR>1 No joint or point of<BR>conjunction.<BR>--2 A day which is not a पर्वन्<BR>i. e. not the proper time or season<BR>(the Parva days being अमावास्या,<BR>पौर्णिमा, अष्टमी, चतुर्दशी &c.); अपर्वणि<BR>ग्रहकलुषेंदुमंडला विभावरी कथय कथं<BR>भविष्यति M. 4. 15.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंडः a sort<BR>of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपल|अपलं
अपल a. Without flesh(पलशून्य).<BR>--लं A pin or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलप्
अपलप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To deny,<BR>disown; राजदेयमपलपितं Kull. on<BR>Ms. 8. 400; refuse; शतमपलपति P. I. 3. 44<BR>Sk.<BR>--2 To conceal, hide.<BR>--3 To detract<BR>from, slander. --Caus. To outwit,<BR>overreach, deceive; अपलापयमानस्य<BR>शत्रूंस्तस्याभवन्मतिः Bk. 8. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलपनं|अपलपन
अपलपनं, अपलापः<BR>1 Concealing,<BR>hiding; कृततिग्मद्युतिमंडलापलापैः<BR>Śi. 20. 28.<BR>--2 Concealment or denial<BR>of knowledge, evasion; न हि<BR>प्रत्यक्षसिद्धस्यापलापः कर्तुं शक्यते Ś. B.<BR>--3<BR>Detraction, concealment of truth,<BR>thoughts, feelings &c.;<BR>उन्मुखदर्शनापलपनैः पिंडार्थमायस्यतः Mu. 3. 14.<BR>--4<BR>Affection, regard.<BR>--5 (In medicine)<BR>The part between the shoulder and<BR>the ribs.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंडः (in law)<BR>a fine laid on one who denies the<BR>charge on which he is convicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलापः|अपलाप
अपलपनं, अपलापः<BR>1 Concealing,<BR>hiding; कृततिग्मद्युतिमंडलापलापैः<BR>Śi. 20. 28.<BR>--2 Concealment or denial<BR>of knowledge, evasion; न हि<BR>प्रत्यक्षसिद्धस्यापलापः कर्तुं शक्यते Ś. B.<BR>--3<BR>Detraction, concealment of truth,<BR>thoughts, feelings &c.;<BR>उन्मुखदर्शनापलपनैः पिंडार्थमायस्यतः Mu. 3. 14.<BR>--4<BR>Affection, regard.<BR>--5 (In medicine)<BR>The part between the shoulder and<BR>the ribs.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंडः (in law)<BR>a fine laid on one who denies the<BR>charge on which he is convicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलापिन्
अपलापिन् a. One who denies,<BR>disowns, hides, conceals &c.; concealing;<BR>जयंति महतां संस्तुतापलापिन्यः<BR>कल्याणिन्यो नीतयः Māl. 10;<BR>साधारणस्यापलापिन् Y. 2. 236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषिका
अपलाषिका [लाषिका पर्यायेण इच्छा,<BR>तद्विपरीता इच्छा] Excessive thirst or<BR>desire (अतिशयलालसा); (अपलासिका is<BR>sometimes used in the same sense,<BR>but regarded as an incorrect word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषिन्
अपलाषिन्, --लाषुक a.<BR>1 Thirsty (P.<BR>P. III. 2. 144.).<BR>--2 Free from thirst<BR>or desire; प्रलापिनो भविष्यंति कदा<BR>न्वेतेऽपलाषुकाः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपलाषुक
अपलाषिन्, --लाषुक a.<BR>1 Thirsty (P.<BR>P. III. 2. 144.).<BR>--2 Free from thirst<BR>or desire; प्रलापिनो भविष्यंति कदा<BR>न्वेतेऽपलाषुकाः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपल्यूलनं|अपल्यूलन
अपल्यूलनं Not cleansing or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-b" target="_blank">Page0111-b+ 57</a>]<BR>washing; यदिदं स्नानवस्त्रं विहितमपल्यूलनं कृतं<BR>भवति Śat. Br. (क्षारद्रव्यसंयोगादिनाऽधौतं);<BR>not cleansed or washed by<BR>cleaning substances (as by a washerman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवक्तृ
अपवक्तृ m. Ved. Speaking away,<BR>warning off, averting, preventing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवचनं
अपवचनं Speaking ill; Pt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाचनं|अपवाचन
अपवाचनं Act of speaking away<BR>or warning off, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवद्
अपवद् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To revile, abuse,<BR>censure, reproach; परानमी यदपवदंत<BR>आत्मनः Śi. 17. 19; नार्तोप्यपवदेद्विप्रान्<BR>Ms. 4. 236; स्वं पुत्रं अपवदंति-ते वा<BR>P. I. 3. 77. Sk. (क्रियाफलस्य कर्तृगामित्वे<BR>द्योतिते वा स्यात्); नृभ्योऽपवदमानस्य Bk. 8. 45<BR>reviling or abusing men.<BR>--2 To<BR>disown, deny (A.); न्यायमपवदते<BR>P. I. 3. 73 Sk.<BR>--3 To argue out, refute,<BR>contradict; अपवदेयुस्तानितिहासैः पुरातनैः<BR>Y. 3. 7. --Caus.<BR>1 To blame, censure.<BR>--2 To oppose or contradict as<BR>unadvisable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादः|अपवाद
अपवादः<BR>1 Censuring, reviling;<BR>censure, reproach, blame, abuse;<BR>आस्तातापवादभिन्नमर्याद U. 5; लोकापवादो<BR>बलवान्मतो मे R. 14. 40; लोकापवादाद्भयं<BR>Bh. 2. 62; scandal, evil report;<BR>चिरकालान्मया श्रुतस्तवापवादः Pt. 1;<BR>Ki. 11. 25, 14. 12; Mk. 9. 3; U. 1;<BR>Pt. 4; Y. 2. 207; देव्यामपि हि वैदेह्यां<BR>सापवादो यतो जनः U. 1. 6<BR>spreading or indulging in scandals about;<BR>न केवलभत्याहितं सापवादमपि U. 2;<BR>सापवादं censuringly Māl. 9.<BR>--2 An<BR>exception, a special rule that<BR>restricts or sets aside a general rule<BR>(opp. उत्सर्ग); मा हिंस्यात्सर्वभूतानि इति<BR>उत्सर्गः; वायव्यं श्वेतमालभेत इत्यपवादः;<BR>अपवादैरिवोत्सर्गाः कृतव्यावृत्तयः परैः<BR>Ku. 2. 27; R. 15. 7; ˚प्रत्ययः<BR>exceptional suffix; ˚स्थलं a case for a special<BR>rule.<BR>--3 An order, command;<BR>ततोपवादेन पताकिनीपतेश्चचाल<BR>निर्ह्रादवतीमहाचमूः Ki. 14. 27.<BR>--4 Refutation;<BR>(in Vedānta phil.) refutation as of<BR>a wrong imputation or belief;<BR>रज्जुविवर्तस्य सर्पस्य रज्जुमात्रत्ववत्,<BR>वस्तुभूतब्रह्मणो विवर्तस्य प्रपंचादेः वस्तुभूतरूपतोपदेशः<BR>अपवादः Tv.; अध्यारोपापवादाभ्यां<BR>वस्तुतत्त्वविनिश्चयः Vedānta; hence also, a<BR>means of refutation.<BR>--5 Confidence,<BR>trust.<BR>--6 Love; familiarity.<BR>--7 A<BR>small bell or other instrument<BR>sounded to decoy deer;<BR>मधुकरैरपवादकरैरिव Śi. 6. 9; (˚करैः = व्याधैः, अपवादं<BR>मृगवंचनाय घंटादिकुत्सितवाद्यंकुर्वंति तैः Malli.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादक
अपवादक, --अपवादिन् a.<BR>1 Blaming,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">Page0111-c+ 60</a>]<BR>censuring, reviling, traducing,<BR>defaming; मृगयापवादिना माठव्येन Ś. 2.<BR>--2 Opposing; contradicting,<BR>excepting, setting aside, excluding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवादिन्
अपवादक, --अपवादिन् a.<BR>1 Blaming,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">Page0111-c+ 60</a>]<BR>censuring, reviling, traducing,<BR>defaming; मृगयापवादिना माठव्येन Ś. 2.<BR>--2 Opposing; contradicting,<BR>excepting, setting aside, excluding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवन|अपवनं
अपवन a. Without wind or air,<BR>sheltered from wind.<BR>--नं [अपकृष्टं<BR>कृत्रिमत्वात्स्वल्पत्वाच्च वनं] A grove, a<BR>garden or park planted near a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरक|अपवरकः
अपवरक, --वारक See under<BR>अपवृ, अपवृज्-अपवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारक|अपवारकः
अपवरक, --वारक See under<BR>अपवृ, अपवृज्-अपवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्ग|अपवर्गः
अपवर्ग &c. See under<BR>अपवृ, अपवृज्-अपवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्त|अपवर्तः|अपवर्त्त
अपवर्त &c. See under<BR>अपवृ, अपवृज्-अपवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवह्
अपवह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To carry off or away,<BR>bear off or away; अपोवाह च<BR>वासोऽस्या मारुतः Mb.<BR>--2 To drive away,<BR>disperse, dispel, remove, take away;<BR>अमी जनस्थानमपोढविघ्नं मत्वा R. 13. 22<BR>freed from obstacles;<BR>अथानपोढार्गलमप्यगारं (प्रविष्टां) 16. 6 the bolts<BR>of which were not removed or<BR>unchained; तदुच्छिष्टमपोह्य Dk. 133.<BR>--3 To give up, relinquish, leave,<BR>abandon, cast off;<BR>शमिततापमपोढमहीरजः Śi. 6. 33; संभ्रमोऽभवदपोढकर्मणां<BR>(ऋत्विजां) R. 11. 25;<BR>तद्भक्त्यपोढपितृराज्यमहभिषेके (मूर्धनि) 13. 70<BR>thrown away; Dk. 67; दिव्येन शून्यं<BR>वलयेन बाहुमपोढनेपथ्यविधिर्ददर्श<BR>R. 16. 73 before he had commenced his<BR>toilet.<BR>--4 To deduct, subtract. --Caus.<BR>1 To carry off, remove, carry or<BR>draw to a distance, take away;<BR>मलयकेतुरपवाहितः Mu. 1, 3; कलत्रं 2;<BR>इमां मया सार्धमपवाह्य M. 5; Bk. 8. 86.<BR>--2 To chase or drive away, expel;<BR>हृतसर्वस्वतया अपवाहितः Dk. 47, 59.<BR>--3 To reduce to powder, pulverize.<BR>--4 To cause to carry the yoke;<BR>गामिव नासिकां विद्ध्वापवाहयति Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाहः|अपवाह
अपवाहः, --हनं<BR>1 Taking or carrying<BR>away, removal; Dk. 41; स्वराष्ट्रं<BR>वासयेद्राजा परदेशापवाहनात् H. 3. v. l.<BR>bearing away men from other<BR>countries; See अभिष्यंद.<BR>--2 Deduction,<BR>subtraction (as of fractions).<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवाहनं|अपवाहन
अपवाहः, --हनं<BR>1 Taking or carrying<BR>away, removal; Dk. 41; स्वराष्ट्रं<BR>वासयेद्राजा परदेशापवाहनात् H. 3. v. l.<BR>bearing away men from other<BR>countries; See अभिष्यंद.<BR>--2 Deduction,<BR>subtraction (as of fractions).<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवोढृ
अपवोढृ a. One who carries away<BR>or removes; Śi. 18. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोढ
अपोढ p. p. Carried away,<BR>removed &c. See above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवासः|अपवास
अपवासः [अपसृत्य वासः] Ved.<BR>1<BR>Disappearance, vanishing, retreat.<BR>--2 N. of a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविक्षत
अपविक्षत a. Uninjured,<BR>unhurt, unviolated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविघ्न
अपविघ्न a. Unobstructed,<BR>uninterrupted; शतं क्रतूनामपविघ्नमाप सः<BR>R. 3. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0111-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्ध|अपविद्धः
अपविद्ध &c. See under अपव्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्या
अपविद्या Ignorance, spiritual<BR>ignorance, Māyā or illusion (अविद्या);<BR>तत्त्वस्य संवित्तिरिवापविद्यां Ki. 16. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविष
अपविष a. Free from poison.<BR>--षा A sort of grass with aromatic<BR>roots; Kyllingia Monocephala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवीण
अपवीण a. Having no lute, or<BR>having a bad lute.<BR>--णा A bad lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृ
अपवृ {c5c} U. To open, uncover,<BR>disclose, exhibit. --Caus. or {c10c} P.<BR>To cover, wrap, envelop, screen,<BR>conceal; बाहुबंधनापवारितपयोधरोद्गमां<BR>Māl. 7 covered, or concealed;<BR>विटपेनापवारितशरीरा भूत्वा Ratn. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरकः|अपवरक
अपवरकः --का [वृ-संज्ञायां वुन्]<BR>1 An<BR>inner apartment; the lying-in<BR>chamber.<BR>--2 An air-hole, aperture;<BR>ततश्चैकस्मादपवरकात् Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरका
अपवरकः --का [वृ-संज्ञायां वुन्]<BR>1 An<BR>inner apartment; the lying-in<BR>chamber.<BR>--2 An air-hole, aperture;<BR>ततश्चैकस्मादपवरकात् Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवरणं|अपवरण
अपवरणं<BR>1 Covering, screening.<BR>--2 A garment, cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारकः|अपवारक
अपवारकः<BR>1 Covering &c.<BR>--2 An<BR>enclosed or screened place (जवनिका);<BR>˚के प्रविश्य एकांते तिष्ठ Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारणं|अपवारण
अपवारणं Covering, concealment,<BR>disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवारित|अपवारितं
अपवारित p. p. Covered, concealed;<BR>˚तं प्रवहणं तिष्ठति Mk. 6 covered;<BR>vanished, disappeared.<BR>--तं, अपवारितकं<BR>Concealed or secret manner.<BR>--तं,<BR>अपवारितकेन, अपवार्य ind. Frequently<BR>occurring in dramas in the sense of<BR>‘apart’ ‘aside to another’ (opp.<BR>प्रकाशं); it is speaking in such a way<BR>that only the person addressed may<BR>hear it; तद्भवेदपवारितं रहस्यं तु यदन्यस्य<BR>परावृत्त्य प्रकाश्यते ।<BR>त्रिपताककरेणान्यमपवार्यांतरा कथां S. D. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृतिः|अपवृति
अपवृतिः f. Opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृज्
अपवृज् {c7c} A.<BR>1 To avert, destroy,<BR>dissipate; तमः, शत्रुं &c.<BR>--2 To tear off,<BR>pull out, take out.<BR>--3 To conclude,<BR>finish; absolve. --Caus.<BR>1 To leave,<BR>quit, abandon, avoid; दूरापवर्जितच्छत्रैः<BR>शिरोभिः R. 17. 79 keeping the<BR>umbrellas at a (great) distance;<BR>त्वयात्महस्तेन मही मदच्युता मतंगजेन<BR>स्रगिवापवर्जिता Ki. 1. 29 abandoned, left,<BR>lost.<BR>--2 To let go, drop down, throw,<BR>pour; सुमनसो दिव्याः खेचरैरपवर्जिताः<BR>Bhāg.; करयुग्मपद्ममुकुलापवार्जितैः<BR>Śi. 13. 37.<BR>--3 To abandon, release,<BR>discharge, pay off (as debt &c.);<BR>absolve oneself from, fulfil, make<BR>good (as a promise).<BR>--4 To sever,<BR>separate, cut off; भल्लापवर्जितैस्तेषां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">Page0112-b+ 57</a>]<BR>शिरोभिः (महीं तस्तार) R. 4. 63,<BR>Ki. 17. 58 severed or cut off by arrows;<BR>इमान्यमूनीत्यपवर्जिते शनैः Ki. 8. 20<BR>plucked.<BR>--5 To overturn; empty;<BR>Y. 3. 300.<BR>--6 To honour, respect,<BR>esteem.<BR>--7 To give, bestow, grant,<BR>present; अपवर्जितं कोशजातं Dk. 36;<BR>दक्षिणामपवर्ज्य Mb.; अपवर्जितौ वरौ<BR>Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्गः|अपवर्ग
अपवर्गः<BR>1 Completion, end,<BR>fulfilment or accomplishment of an<BR>action; अपवर्गे तृतीया P. II. 3. 6;<BR>III. 4. 60; (अपवर्गः = क्रियाप्राप्तिः or समाप्तिः<BR>Sk.); क्रियापवर्गेष्वनुजीविसात्कृताः<BR>Ki. 1. 14; अपवर्गे तृतीयेति भणतः पाणिनेरपि<BR>N. 17. 68; Ki. 16. 49; पंच˚ coming<BR>to an end in 5 days.<BR>--2 An exception,<BR>special rule; अभिव्याप्यापकर्षणमपवर्गः<BR>Suśr.<BR>--3 Absolution, final beatitude;<BR>अपवर्गमहोदयार्थयोर्भुवमंशाविव धर्मयोर्गतौ<BR>R. 8. 16; ज्ञानेन चापवर्गः Sāṅ. K. 44<BR>--4 A gift, donation.<BR>--5<BR>Abandonment.<BR>--6 Throwing, discharge (as of<BR>arrows); Ki. 16. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्जनं|अपवर्जन|अपवर्ज्जन|अपवर्ज्जनं
अपवर्जनं<BR>1 Leaving, abandonment;<BR>making good, fulfilling (a promise);<BR>discharging (debt &c.).<BR>--2 A gift<BR>or donation; spending.<BR>--3 Final<BR>beatitude, salvation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्जित|अपवर्ज्जित
अपवर्जित p. p. Left, abandoned;<BR>fulfilled; see above; oft. in comp.<BR>in the sense of ‘free from,’ ‘being<BR>without,’ ‘destitute of’, or with<BR>instr.; षड्भिरपवर्जिताशीतिः Bṛ. S. 53. 7<BR>80 minus 6, Ki. 2. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृक्त
अपवृक्त p. p. Finished, ended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृक्तिः|अपवृक्ति
अपवृक्तिः f. Fulfilment,<BR>accomplishment, completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्
अपवृत् {c1c} A. To turn back, turn<BR>away, depart; तस्मादपावर्तत दूरकृष्टा<BR>R. 6. 58; तस्मादपावर्तत कुंडिनेशः 7. 33.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To turn back or away, turn<BR>aside, bend; व्यपोढपार्श्वैरपवर्तितत्रिकाः<BR>Ki. 4. 15; आसक्ततिर्यगपवर्तितदृष्टि<BR>वक्त्रं (वहंती) Māl. 1. 40.<BR>--2 (Math.)<BR>To divide (as by a common measure)<BR>without remainder; समेन केनाप्यपवर्त्य<BR>हारभाज्यौ भजेद्वा सति संभवे तु Līlā.<BR>--3 To reduce to a common measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्तः|अपवर्त|अपवर्त्त
अपवर्तः<BR>1 Taking away, removing.<BR>--2 (Math.) The (common)<BR>divisor which is applied to both or<BR>either of the quantities of an<BR>equation.<BR>--3 Reduction to a common<BR>measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्तकः|अपवर्तक
अपवर्तकः A common measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवर्तनं|अपवर्तन|अपवर्त्तन
अपवर्तनं<BR>1 Removal, transferring<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">Page0112-c+ 57</a>]<BR>from one place to another; स्थान˚.<BR>--2<BR>Taking away, depriving one of; न<BR>त्यागोस्ति द्विषंत्याश्च न च दायापवर्तनं<BR>Ms. 9. 79.<BR>--3 Abridging, abbreviation.<BR>--4<BR>Reducing a fraction to its lowest terms;<BR>division without remainder, or the<BR>divisor itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्त
अपवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Turned away,<BR>reversed, inverted, overturned;<BR>agitated, disturbed; ˚जठरशफरी<BR>Ki. 12. 49.<BR>--2 With downward face;<BR>व्याकीर्णस्फुरदपवृत्तरुंडखंडः Māl. 3. 17.<BR>--3<BR>Ended, finished.<BR>--त्तं The ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवृत्तिः|अपवृत्ति
अपवृत्तिः f. End.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्यध्
अपव्यध् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To pierce<BR>(badly); अपविद्धः शरैर्भृशं Mb.<BR>--2 To<BR>throw or cast in general, throw or<BR>cast off, toss away; प्रेंखयन्<BR>परिजनापविद्धया (दोलया) R. 19. 44 left, let go;<BR>भुजस्तंभापविद्ध Mv. 2. 33 thrown,<BR>or wielded; अपविद्धसर्वस्वा<BR>Dk. 61 given or spent away;<BR>Ki. 5. 30; Śi. 8. 37; हृदयमशरणं मे<BR>पक्ष्मलाक्ष्याः कटाक्षैरपहृतमपविद्धं पतिमुन्मूलितं च<BR>Māl. 1. 28 pierced through,<BR>distracted, overcome.<BR>--3 To abandon,<BR>leave, desert, cast off (as a child,<BR>ornaments &c.); पुरा श्मशाने<BR>स्रगिवापविध्यते Mb., Ms. 11. 41, Dk. 98, 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपविद्ध|अपविद्धः
अपविद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Cast or thrown off,<BR>thrown or cast away, abandoned,<BR>forsaken, dismissed, rejected,<BR>neglected, removed; oft. used in the<BR>sense of ‘freed from,’ ‘devoid of’;<BR>रक्षोविप्रकृतावास्तामपविद्धशुचाविव R. 10. 74.<BR>--2 Abject, mean.<BR>--द्धः, ˚पुत्रः A son that<BR>is abandoned by the father or mother<BR>or by both, and adopted by a stranger;<BR>one of the 12 kinds of sons among<BR>Hindus; Ms. 9. 171; Y. 2. 132.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--लोक a. dead, departed<BR>from this world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपवेधः|अपवेध
अपवेधः Piercing through (a pearl,<BR>ruby &c.) wrongly, or in the wrong<BR>direction (and thus spoiling it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययः|अपव्यय
अपव्ययः [अपकृष्टः मर्यादामुल्लंघ्य कृतः<BR>व्ययः] Extravagant expenditure,<BR>prodigality, lavishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययिन्
अपव्ययिन् --व्ययमान a.<BR>1<BR>Squandering, spending lavishly, prodigal.<BR>--2 Denying a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्ययमान
अपव्ययिन् --व्ययमान a.<BR>1<BR>Squandering, spending lavishly, prodigal.<BR>--2 Denying a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपव्रत
अपव्रत a. Ved.<BR>1 Swerving<BR>from religious observances,<BR>irreligious, impious; Rv. 1. 51. 9.<BR>--2<BR>Disobedient, unfaithful.<BR>--3<BR>Perverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशकुनं|अपशकुन
अपशकुनं A bad omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशंक|अपशङ्क
अपशंक a. Free from fear or<BR>hesitation, fearless.<BR>--कं adv.<BR>Fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशदः|अपशद
अपशदः = अपसद q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशब्दः|अपशब्द
अपशब्दः<BR>1 A bad or<BR>ungrammatical word, a corrupted word<BR>(in form or meaning); त एव<BR>शक्तिवैकल्यप्रमादालसतादिभिः । अन्यथोच्चारिताः<BR>शब्दा अपशब्दा इतीरिताः ॥; दूरतश्चापशब्दं<BR>त्यक्त्वा Bh. 3. 134 (where ˚ब्दं has<BR>also sense 4); अपशब्दशतं माघे<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Vulgar speech.<BR>--3 A form<BR>of language not Sanskrit,<BR>ungrammatical language.<BR>--4 A reproachful<BR>word, offensive expression, censure;<BR>प्रापाक्ष्णोर्गलदपशब्दमजनांभः Śi. 8. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशमः|अपशम
अपशमः Cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशव्य
अपशव्य a. Not tending to the<BR>growth of cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशिरस्
अपशिरस् --शीर्ष, --र्षन् a. Headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशीर्ष
अपशिरस् --शीर्ष, --र्षन् a. Headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशीर्षन्
अपशिरस् --शीर्ष, --र्षन् a. Headless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशु|अपशुः
अपशु a. Without cattle.<BR>--शुः<BR>Not cattle; a bad animal; any<BR>animal other than a cow and horse;<BR>अपशवो वा अन्ये गोश्वेम्यः Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशुच्
अपशुच् a. Without sorrow. --m.<BR>(Without sorrow) The soul; क<BR>उत्तमः श्लोकगुणानुवादात् पुमान् विरज्येत<BR>विनापशुग्घ्नात् Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपशोक|अपशोकः
अपशोक a. Without sorrow or<BR>grief.<BR>--कः The Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्चिम
अपश्चिम a.<BR>1 What is not<BR>followed by any other, having no other<BR>in the rear, last (used much in the<BR>same sense as पश्चिम; cf. उत्तम and<BR>अनुत्तम, उत्तर and अनुत्तर); अयमत्र ते<BR>जन्मन्यपश्चिमः पश्चिमावस्थाप्रर्थितो<BR>मकरंदबाहुपरिष्वंगः Māl. 9; अयमपश्चिमस्ते<BR>रामस्य शिरसि पादपंकजस्पर्शः U. 1 (v. l. for<BR>पश्चिम); प्रसीदतु महाराजो ममानेनापश्चिमेन<BR>प्रणयेन Ve. 6; प्रणमापश्चिमस्य पितुः<BR>पादयोः Mu. 7; तात अंब मेऽपश्चिमः प्रणामः<BR>Nāg. 5; अपश्चिमं कुरु वचनं Ve. 141.<BR>--2 Not last, first, foremost;<BR>श्रुतवतामपश्चिमः R. 19. 1.<BR>--3 Extreme;<BR>अपश्चिमामिमां कष्टामापदं प्राप्तवत्यहं Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्य
अपश्य a. Ved. Not seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्रयः|अपश्रय
अपश्रयः A bolster, pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्री
अपश्री a. Deprived of beauty;<BR>Śi. 11. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपश्वासः|अपश्वास
अपश्वासः = अपान q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठं|अपष्ठ
अपष्ठं [अप-स्था, --क सस्यं षत्वं<BR>P. VIII. 3. 97] The point of the<BR>goad of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठु|अपष्ठुः
अपष्ठु a. [अप-स्था कु Uṇ. 1. 25;<BR>P. VIII. 3. 98]<BR>1 Contrary,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">Page0113-b+ 56</a>]<BR>opposite.<BR>--2 Unfavourable, adverse,<BR>perverse.<BR>--3 Left.<BR>--ष्ठु adv.<BR>1<BR>Contrary, in the contrary or opposite<BR>way or direction.<BR>--2 Falsely,<BR>untruly, wrongly; तव धंर्मराज इति<BR>नाम कथमिदमपष्ठु पठ्यते Śi. 15. 17; अपष्ठु<BR>पठतः पाठ्यमधिगोष्ठि शठस्य ते N.<BR>--3<BR>Faultlessly.<BR>--4 Well, properly,<BR>handsomely.<BR>--ष्ठुः Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुर|अपष्ठुरं
अपष्ठुर --ल a. Contrary, opposite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपष्ठुल|अपष्ठुलं
अपष्ठुर --ल a. Contrary, opposite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्
अपस् n. [आप् असुन् थस्वश्च;<BR>आपःकर्माख्यायां थस्वो नुट्च वा स्यात् Uṇ. 4. 207.<BR>अप्नः, अपः]<BR>1 Work, action; अपसा<BR>संतु नेमे Rv. 1. 54. 8.<BR>--2 Sacred act<BR>or rite, sacrificial work.<BR>--3 Water.<BR>--a. (अपाः)<BR>1 Active, engaged in<BR>any act (कर्मयुक्त).<BR>--2 Got or<BR>obtained. According to B. and R. अपसः<BR>f. pl. stands in the Veda for (1)<BR>the hands and fingers busy in<BR>kindling the sacred fire and performing<BR>the sacrificial rites; (2) the three<BR>goddesses of sacred speech or the<BR>three divinities, fire, wind and sun;<BR>and (3) the active or running<BR>waters. [cf. L. opus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्तम
अपस्तम a. Most active or rapid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्य
अपस्य a. [अपसि कर्मणि साधुः यत्] Ved.<BR>Active, fit for an act, skilful<BR>in doing any thing (साधुकर्मकारिन्);<BR>Yv. 10. 7; flowing, watery.<BR>--स्या<BR>1<BR>Activity.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--3 A sort of<BR>brick used in preparing the<BR>sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्यति
अपस्यति Den. P. To be active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्यु
अपस्यु a. [अपस्-क्यच्-उ] Active,<BR>busily engaged, desirous of working.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसदः|अपसद
अपसदः [अपकृष्टो नीच इव सीदति,<BR>सद्-अच्]<BR>1 An outcast, a low man;<BR>usually at the end of comp. in the<BR>sense of ‘vile,’ ‘wretched’ ‘accursed’;<BR>कापालिक˚ Māl. 5; रे रे क्षत्रियापसदाः<BR>Ve. 3; नर˚, ब्राह्मण˚ &c.<BR>--2 N. for the<BR>children of six degrading<BR>connections, i. e. of men of the first three<BR>castes with women of the castes<BR>inferior to their own; विप्रस्य त्रिषु<BR>वर्णेषु नृपतेर्वर्णयोर्द्वयोः । वैश्यस्य वर्णे चैकस्मिन्<BR>षडेतेऽपसदाः स्मृताः ॥ Ms. 10. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसमं|अपसम
अपसमं ind. Last year; at the<BR>end of the year (वर्षात्यये).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर|अपसरः
अपसर-सर्प &e. See under अपसृ,<BR>अपसृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्प|अपसर्पः
अपसर-सर्प &e. See under अपसृ,<BR>अपसृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्जनं|अपसर्जन|अपसर्ज्जन|अपसर्ज्जनं
अपसर्जनं [सृज्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Leaving, abandonment.<BR>--2 A gift or<BR>donation,<BR>--3 Final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसल
अपसल = अपसव्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसलवि
अपसलवि ind. [अप सल् बा˚ अवि]<BR>1<BR>To the left (opp. प्रसलवि); ˚वि सृष्टया<BR>रज्ज्वा Kāty. (अप्रादक्षिण्येन).<BR>--2 (The<BR>space) Between the thumb and the<BR>forefinger, supposed to be sacred<BR>to the Manes, as water &c. in<BR>ceremonies like तर्पण is offered to them<BR>being poured down through that<BR>space; प्रदेशिन्यंगुष्ठयोरंतरा अपसलवि<BR>अपसव्यं वा तेन पितृभ्यो निदधाति Śabdak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्य|अपसव्यं|अपसव्यः
अपसव्य, --सव्यक a.<BR>1 Not on the<BR>left, right; अपसव्येन हस्तेन Ms. 3. 214.<BR>--2 Contrary, opposite.<BR>--व्यं ind.<BR>To the right, making the sacred<BR>thread hang down towards the left<BR>part of the body over the right<BR>shoulder (opp. सव्यं when it hangs<BR>over the left); a position of the<BR>thread in Śrāddha or other religious<BR>ceremonies at particular times of<BR>those ceremonies (the three<BR>positions being सव्य, निवीत & अपसव्य)<BR>Ms. 3. 279; ˚व्यं कृ to go round one<BR>so as to keep the right side towards<BR>him; to make the sacred thread<BR>hang over the right shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यक
अपसव्य, --सव्यक a.<BR>1 Not on the<BR>left, right; अपसव्येन हस्तेन Ms. 3. 214.<BR>--2 Contrary, opposite.<BR>--व्यं ind.<BR>To the right, making the sacred<BR>thread hang down towards the left<BR>part of the body over the right<BR>shoulder (opp. सव्यं when it hangs<BR>over the left); a position of the<BR>thread in Śrāddha or other religious<BR>ceremonies at particular times of<BR>those ceremonies (the three<BR>positions being सव्य, निवीत & अपसव्य)<BR>Ms. 3. 279; ˚व्यं कृ to go round one<BR>so as to keep the right side towards<BR>him; to make the sacred thread<BR>hang over the right shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसव्यवत्|अपसव्यवन्त्
अपसव्यवत् a. Wearing the sacred<BR>thread over the right shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसिद्धांतः|अपसिद्धान्त|अपसिद्धान्तः
अपसिद्धांतः A wrong or<BR>erroneous conclusion; सिद्धांतमभ्युपेत्यानियमात्<BR>कथाप्रसंगोऽपसिद्धांतः Gaut. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृ
अपसृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To walk off, go or<BR>get away, depart; अपसर इतः begone,<BR>avaunt, hence, get you gone;<BR>अपसराग्रतः Pt. 1.<BR>--2 To withdraw, retire,<BR>retreat, turn back; यदपसरति मेषः कारणं<BR>तत्प्रहर्तुं Pt. 3. 43.<BR>--3 To vanish,<BR>disappear; यस्यानुष्ठानेन मे<BR>संततिविनाशदुःखमपसरति Pt. 1.<BR>--4 To escape, elude the<BR>sight. --Caus. To make (a thing or<BR>person) go away or retire, take or<BR>put away, remove, drive away or<BR>off, throw aside; अपसारय घनसारं<BR>K. P. 9; अपसार्यतां वेत्रलता Pt. 1<BR>put aside, take away; Ms. 7. 149.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरः|अपसर
अपसरः<BR>1 Departure, retreat.<BR>--2 A<BR>proper excuse or apology, valid<BR>reason (for possession of a thing,<BR>such as buying &c.) Ms. 8. 198.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसरणं|अपसरण
अपसरणं<BR>1 Going away, retreating,<BR>escape; तत्ते युक्तं कर्तुमपसरणं Pt. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Egress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारः|अपसार
अपसारः<BR>1 Going out, retreating.<BR>--2 An outlet, egress (opp. प्रवेश);<BR>Pt. 3. 120; अनपसारमार्गाः Dk. 163;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">Page0114-a+ 56</a>]<BR>H. 3. 53; Śi. 18. 40.<BR>--3 Escaping,<BR>fleeing; Mk. 7. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारणं|अपसारण
अपसारणं --णा Removing to a<BR>distance, driving, expelling;<BR>किमर्थमपसारणा क्रियते Mu. 4, making room (cf.<BR>Mar. बाजू, बाजू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसारणा
अपसारणं --णा Removing to a<BR>distance, driving, expelling;<BR>किमर्थमपसारणा क्रियते Mu. 4, making room (cf.<BR>Mar. बाजू, बाजू).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृत
अपसृत p. p.<BR>1 Gone away,<BR>retreated &c.; dropped or fallen down;<BR>अपसृतपांडुपत्रा मुंचंत्यश्रूणीव लताः Ś. 4. 15.<BR>--2 Extended, held out, stretched;<BR>Ś. 6.<BR>--3 Discharged; अपसृतमिव शस्त्रं<BR>Mv. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृप्
अपसृप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To glide or move<BR>gently along, glide away or off.<BR>--2<BR>To withdraw, retire, go away;<BR>त्वरितमनेन तरुगहनेनापसर्पत U. 4;<BR>उत्प्रेक्षितविकारः अपसर्पेत Mv. 4 retire, go<BR>into voluntary exile.<BR>--3 To observe<BR>closely (as a spy); शुद्धांतचारी दुर्मुखः<BR>स मया पौरजानपदानपसर्पितुं प्रयुक्तः<BR>U. 1. --Caus. To drive away or off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्पः|अपसर्प
अपसर्पः, --र्पकः A secret agent or<BR>emissary, spy; सोपसर्पैर्जजागार<BR>यथाकालं स्वपन्नपि R. 17. 51, 14. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्पकः|अपसर्पक
अपसर्पः, --र्पकः A secret agent or<BR>emissary, spy; सोपसर्पैर्जजागार<BR>यथाकालं स्वपन्नपि R. 17. 51, 14. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसर्पणं|अपसर्पण
अपसर्पणं Going back, retreating;<BR>observing as a spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपसृप्तिः|अपसृप्ति
अपसृप्तिः f. Going away or forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्कंभः|अपस्कम्भ|अपस्कम्भः
अपस्कंभः Fastening, making firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्करः|अपस्कर
अपस्करः [अप-कॄ अप्-सुट् रथांगे<BR>निपातः P. VI. 1. 149]<BR>1 Any part of a<BR>carriage, except the wheel (रं also);<BR>अपस्करमधिष्ठाने हिमवान् विंध्यपर्वतः Mb.<BR>--2 Excrement.<BR>--3 Vulva.<BR>--4 Anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्कारः|अपस्कार
अपस्कारः The root or<BR>underpart of the knee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्खलः|अपस्खल
अपस्खलः Leaping or jumping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्तंभः|अपस्तम्भ|अपस्तम्भः
अपस्तंभः A vessel in the side of<BR>the breast containing vital air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नात|अपस्नातः
अपस्नात a. [अपकृष्टं स्नातः] One<BR>who has bathed after death or<BR>mourning or upon the death of a<BR>relation, preparatory to other<BR>ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्नानं|अपस्नान
अपस्नानं<BR>1 Bathing as after<BR>mourning or upon the death of a<BR>relative; funeral bathing.<BR>--2 Impure<BR>bathing, bathing in water in which<BR>a person has previously washed<BR>himself (स्नानशिष्टं जलं) Ms. 4. 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पश
अपस्पश a. Devoid of spies;<BR>शब्दविद्येव नो भाति राजनीतिरपस्पशा<BR>Śi. 2. 112 (where ˚शा also means<BR>without पस्पश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पृश्
अपस्पृश् a. Ved. Not letting<BR>oneself be touched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्पर्श
अपस्पर्श a. Insensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्फिग
अपस्फिग a. Having badly<BR>formed hips; (P. VI. 2. 187).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्फुर्
अपस्फुर् (--स्फूः),<BR>--र, --रत् a.<BR>Injured (Sāy.); swelling, increasing (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मारः|अपस्मार
अपस्मारः, --स्मृतिः f. [अपस्मारयति<BR>स्मरणं विलोपयति, स्मृ-णिच्, कर्तरि अच्, or<BR>अपगतः स्मारः स्मरणं यतः]<BR>1<BR>Forgetfulness, loss of memory; स्मर˚<BR>Bh. 1. 89.<BR>--2 Epilepsy, falling sickness;<BR>Suśr. thus derives it;<BR>स्मृतिर्भूतार्थविज्ञानमपश्च परिवर्जने । अपस्मार इति प्रोक्तस्ततोयं<BR>व्याधिरंतकृत् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मृतिः|अपस्मृति
अपस्मारः, --स्मृतिः f. [अपस्मारयति<BR>स्मरणं विलोपयति, स्मृ-णिच्, कर्तरि अच्, or<BR>अपगतः स्मारः स्मरणं यतः]<BR>1<BR>Forgetfulness, loss of memory; स्मर˚<BR>Bh. 1. 89.<BR>--2 Epilepsy, falling sickness;<BR>Suśr. thus derives it;<BR>स्मृतिर्भूतार्थविज्ञानमपश्च परिवर्जने । अपस्मार इति प्रोक्तस्ततोयं<BR>व्याधिरंतकृत् ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मारिन्
अपस्मारिन् a. Epileptic, having<BR>an epileptic fit; Ms. 3. 7; Śi. 3. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्मृति|अपस्मृतिः
अपस्मृति a. Forgetful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्य
अपस्य, --स्यु &c. See under अपस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्यु
अपस्य, --स्यु &c. See under अपस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपस्वरः|अपस्वर
अपस्वरः An unmusical sound or<BR>note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहन्
अपहन् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To ward or beat<BR>off, repel, destroy, kill, take away,<BR>remove; अपघ्नंतो दुरितं हव्यगंधैः<BR>Ś. 4. 7; न तु खलु तयोर्ज्ञाने शक्तिं<BR>करोत्यपहंति वा U. 2. 4 takes away;<BR>Ms. 6. 96; अपहतपाप्मानं सवितारमुपतिष्ठस्व<BR>U. 3.<BR>--2 To attack, affect, seize (as<BR>disease &c.).<BR>--3 To husk out, take off<BR>the shell or husk (as rice).<BR>--4 To<BR>shoot out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह
अपह a. [अप-हन्-ड] (At the<BR>end of comp.) Warding or<BR>keeping off, taking away, removing,<BR>destroying, repelling &c.; न<BR>दंशमशकापहं Pt. 3. 97; स्रगियं यदि जीवितापहा<BR>R. 8. 46; परकर्मापहः सोऽभूत् 17. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहतिः|अपहति
अपहतिः f. Removing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहननं|अपहनन
अपहननं Warding off, repelling &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहल
अपहल a. Having a bad plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्
अपहस् {c1c} P. To mock or scoff at,<BR>ridicule, deride; साहसापहसितकुमारेण<BR>Dk. 9 scoffed at, i. e. excelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहसितं|अपहसित
अपहसितं, --हासः Silly or causeless<BR>laughter; often laughter with<BR>tearful eyes (नीचानामपहसितं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहासः|अपहास
अपहसितं, --हासः Silly or causeless<BR>laughter; often laughter with<BR>tearful eyes (नीचानामपहसितं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तः|अपहस्त
अपहस्तः [अपसारणार्थो हस्तः]<BR>1<BR>The hand placed on the neck to<BR>drive out a person (गलहस्त); one<BR>that is so driven out.<BR>--2 Throwing<BR>away or off, taking away.<BR>--3<BR>Stealing, plundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तयति
अपहस्तयति Den. P. To seize by<BR>the neck and drive out; hence<BR>throw away, abandon, leave,<BR>discard, reject (fig. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहस्तित
अपहस्तित p. p. Thrown away,<BR>discarded, abandoned, cast off,<BR>given up; ˚सकलसखीजनं त्वयि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">Page0114-c+ 58</a>]<BR>विश्वसिति मे हृदयं K. 233, 202; ˚बांधवे त्वया<BR>Māl. 9. 19; अयं मम ˚लज्जो व्यवसायः<BR>V. 2; Ki. 9. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहा
अपहा {c2c} P. To leave, abandon;<BR>साक्षात्प्रियामुपगतामपहाय पूर्वं Ś. 6. 15.<BR>--pass. To waste away, wane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहानं|अपहान
अपहानं Leaving, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहानिः|अपहानि
अपहानिः f.<BR>1 Leaving,<BR>abandonment; stopping.<BR>--2 Ceasing,<BR>vanishing.<BR>--3 Exception, exclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहाय
अपहाय ind. Leaving, abandoning,<BR>except, without, excepting (used<BR>with the force of a preposition).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहृ
अपहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 (a) To take off,<BR>bear or snatch away, carry off;<BR>पश्चात्पुत्रैरपहृतभरः V. 3. 1 relieved of the<BR>burden; तंत्रादचिरापहृतः पटः brought<BR>P. V. 2. 70 Sk. (b) To avert, turn<BR>away; वदनमपहरंतीं (गौरीं)<BR>Ku. 7. 95 averting or turning away her<BR>face. (c) To rob, plunder, steal.<BR>--2<BR>To sever, separate, cut off;<BR>R. 15. 52.<BR>--3 To overpower, overcome,<BR>subdue; attract, ravish, captivate; affect,<BR>influence (in a good or bad sense);<BR>अपह्रिये खलु परिश्रमजनितया निद्रया<BR>U. 1 overpowered; उत्सवापहृतचेतोभिः<BR>Ratn. 1; यथा नापह्रियसे सुखेन K. 109<BR>seduced, led away, 277; न… प्रियतमा<BR>यतमानमपाहरत् R. 9. 7 did not<BR>subdue i. e. did not divert his mind.<BR>--4 To remove, take away, destroy,<BR>annihilate, deprive (one) of; कीर्तिं˚<BR>R. 11. 74; प्रिया मे दत्ता वाक् पुनर्मेऽपहृता<BR>Dk. 52.<BR>--5 To take back, resume;<BR>देयं प्रतिश्रुतं चैव दत्त्वा नापहरेत्पुनः<BR>Y. 2. 176.<BR>--6 To subtract, deduct. --Caus.<BR>To cause (others) to take away;<BR>Ki. 1. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहरणं|अपहरण
अपहरणं<BR>1 Taking or carrying away,<BR>removing.<BR>--2 Stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहर्तृ|अपहर्त्तृ
अपहर्तृ a.<BR>1 One that takes or<BR>carries away, steals, removes, destroys<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Removing, expiating;<BR>सर्वदोषापहर्तॄणां व्रतानां Ms. 11. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारः|अपहार
अपहारः<BR>1 Taking or carrying away,<BR>stealing, plundering, removing,<BR>killing, destroying; कर्णनासापहारेण<BR>भगिनी मे विरूपिता Rām. by the cutting<BR>of ears and nose; निद्रापहार, विष˚.<BR>--2 Concealing, dissembling;<BR>कथमात्मापहारं करोमि Ś. 1 how shall I<BR>dissemble myself, conceal my real<BR>name and character; see अपहारक<BR>below.<BR>--3 Spending or using<BR>another's property.<BR>--4 Loss, damage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारक|अपहारकः
अपहारक, --हारिन् a. One who or<BR>that which takes away, steals, re<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-a" target="_blank">Page0115-a+ 56</a>]<BR>moves, destroys, conceals &c.<BR>(usually in comp.); जालापहारिणः H. 1;<BR>परद्रव्य˚ plunderer, thief; परवित्त˚;<BR>वागपहारकः Ms. 11. 51; Y. 3. 210;<BR>Ms. 4. 255; 2. 88.<BR>--कः A<BR>robber, thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहारिन्
अपहारक, --हारिन् a. One who or<BR>that which takes away, steals, re<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-a" target="_blank">Page0115-a+ 56</a>]<BR>moves, destroys, conceals &c.<BR>(usually in comp.); जालापहारिणः H. 1;<BR>परद्रव्य˚ plunderer, thief; परवित्त˚;<BR>वागपहारकः Ms. 11. 51; Y. 3. 210;<BR>Ms. 4. 255; 2. 88.<BR>--कः A<BR>robber, thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपहृत
अपहृत p. p. Taken away, carried<BR>off, &c.; destitute of, free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नु
अपह्नु {c2c} A.<BR>1 To conceal, hide,<BR>disguise; Ms. 8. 53; कामदेवव्यपदेशेन<BR>सखीपुरतोऽपह्नुतः Ratn. 2 was passed<BR>off as Cupid upon her friend.<BR>--2 To<BR>deny, disown; गुणांश्चापह्नुषेऽस्माकं<BR>Bk. 5. 44; अपह्नुवानस्य जनाय यन्निजां<BR>(अधीरतां) N. 1. 49.<BR>--3 To exculpate,<BR>excuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नवः|अपह्नव
अपह्नवः<BR>1 Concealment, hiding;<BR>concealment of one's knowledge,<BR>feelings &c.<BR>--2 Denial or disowning<BR>of the truth, dissimulation; ˚वे ज्ञः<BR>P. I. 3. 44; ज्ञातं मया ते हृदयं सखे मापह्नवं<BR>कृथाः Ks. 10. 92.<BR>--3 Appeasing,<BR>satisfying.<BR>--4 Love, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्नुतिः|अपह्नुति
अपह्नुतिः f.<BR>1 Concealment of<BR>knowledge, denial.<BR>--2 (In Rhet.) A<BR>figure of speech, in which the real<BR>character of the thing in question<BR>is denied and that of another (alien<BR>or imaginary) object is ascribed<BR>to, or superimposed upon, it; प्रकृतं<BR>यन्निषिध्यान्यत्साध्यते सा त्वपह्नुतिः<BR>K. P. 10; (उपमेयमसत्यं कृत्वा उपमानं सत्यतया<BR>यत्स्थाप्यते सापह्नुतिः); e. g. नेदं<BR>नभोमंडलमंबुराशिर्नैताश्च तारा नवफेनभंगाः । नायं शशी<BR>कुंडलितः फणींद्रो नासौ कलंकः शयितो मुरारिः ॥<BR>see also K. P. 10 and S. D. 683-84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपह्रासः|अपह्रास
अपह्रासः Reduction,<BR>diminution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्
अपाक् ind. See अपाच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक|अपाकः
अपाक a.<BR>1 Ved. [fr. अंच् with<BR>अप] (a) Situated aside or behind.<BR>(b) Remote, distant. (c) Coming<BR>from a distant place. (d)<BR>Unequalled, incomparable, very great (अनल्प<BR>Sāy.); ˚चक्षस्^1 of unequalled<BR>brightness; ˚कात्-का aside, distant; ˚केस्थ<BR>standing behind.<BR>--2 Raw, unripe.<BR>--3<BR>Not matured, undigested.<BR>--4 Of<BR>matured intellect, wise; (पाकः पक्तव्यप्रज्ञः<BR>मूर्खः तद्विलक्षणः) Rv. 1. 110. 2, 6. 12. 2.<BR>--कः<BR>1 Indigestion (of food &c.).<BR>--2 Immaturity, not being ripe or<BR>cooked.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. {1} not<BR>produced by cooking or ripening. {2}<BR>natural, original; Bhāṣā P. 42, 95.<BR>--शाकं ginger.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20260102. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/2801.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृ
अपाकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To drive away,<BR>dispel, remove, destroy; keep, put,<BR>or take away; तन्नैशं तिमिरमपाकरोति<BR>चंद्रः Ś. 6. 29; स्फुटता न पदैरपाकृता<BR>Ki. 2. 27; पापमपाकरोति Bh. 2. 23; गुहोपि<BR>येषां प्रथमात्मजन्मनां न<BR>पुत्रवात्सल्यमपाकरिष्यति Ku. 5. 14 remove, reduce,<BR>lessen; Māl. 6. 4; R. 6. 57; Śi. 8. 61.<BR>--2 To cast off, reject (also an<BR>opinion), leave, give up, throw away,<BR>drop; हंसैर्यियासुभिरपाकृतमुन्मनस्कैः<BR>Mk. 5. 1; शिवा भुजच्छेदमपाचकार R. 7. 50.<BR>--3 To discharge, liquidate (as debt<BR>&c.) Ms. 6. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकरणं|अपाकरण
अपाकरणं, अपाकृतिः f.<BR>1 Driving<BR>away, removal.<BR>--2 Rejection,<BR>refutation; तदपाकरणायाह Praśna Up.<BR>--3<BR>Payment, liquidation;<BR>ऋणत्रयापकरणान्नास्त्यपवर्गः Nyāya S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृतिः|अपाकृति
अपाकरणं, अपाकृतिः f.<BR>1 Driving<BR>away, removal.<BR>--2 Rejection,<BR>refutation; तदपाकरणायाह Praśna Up.<BR>--3<BR>Payment, liquidation;<BR>ऋणत्रयापकरणान्नास्त्यपवर्गः Nyāya S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकर्मन्|अपाकर्म्मन्
अपाकर्मन् n. (˚र्म) Payment,<BR>liquidation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकरिष्णु
अपाकरिष्णु a.<BR>1 Driving away,<BR>removing.<BR>--2 Excelling, eclipsing;<BR>वर्णः स्वर्णापाकरिष्णुः Bh. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृत
अपाकृत p. p.<BR>1 Removed,<BR>destroyed, dispelled, paid &c.<BR>--2 Devoid<BR>or destitute of, free from;<BR>कृतमिदमपाकृते गुणैः Śi. 15. 33;<BR>यत्स्वयमभियोगदुःखैरपाकृतं तदेव राज्यं सुखयति Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाकृतिः|अपाकृति
अपाकृतिः f.<BR>1 Rejection, removal<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Emotion resulting from<BR>anger, fear &c.; Ki. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाक्ष|अपाक्षं
अपाक्ष a. [अपनतः अक्षमिंद्रियं]<BR>1<BR>Present, perceptible.<BR>--2 [अपगते<BR>अपकृष्टे वा अक्षिणी यस्य] Eyeless; having<BR>bad eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपांक्त|अपाङ्क्त
अपांक्त, --पांक्तेय, --पांक्त्य a. ‘Not in<BR>the same row or line’; especially one<BR>who is not allowed by his castemen<BR>to sit in the same row with them at<BR>meals; degraded, excommunicated,<BR>excluded from or inadmissible<BR>into society, an outcast; ˚उपहत<BR>defiled by the presence of<BR>excommunicated or impious persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपांक्तेय|अपाङ्क्तेय
अपांक्त, --पांक्तेय, --पांक्त्य a. ‘Not in<BR>the same row or line’; especially one<BR>who is not allowed by his castemen<BR>to sit in the same row with them at<BR>meals; degraded, excommunicated,<BR>excluded from or inadmissible<BR>into society, an outcast; ˚उपहत<BR>defiled by the presence of<BR>excommunicated or impious persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपांक्त्य|अपाङ्क्त्य
अपांक्त, --पांक्तेय, --पांक्त्य a. ‘Not in<BR>the same row or line’; especially one<BR>who is not allowed by his castemen<BR>to sit in the same row with them at<BR>meals; degraded, excommunicated,<BR>excluded from or inadmissible<BR>into society, an outcast; ˚उपहत<BR>defiled by the presence of<BR>excommunicated or impious persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपांग|अपाङ्ग|अपाङ्गः
अपांग --गक a. [अपगतं अंगं यस्य]<BR>1 Wanting or deformed in some limb<BR>of the body.<BR>--2 Maimed, crippled.<BR>--गः, --गकः [अपांगति तिर्यक् चलति नेत्रं<BR>यत्र, अप-अंग्-घञ्]<BR>1 The outer corner<BR>or angle of the eye; चलापांगां दृष्टिं<BR>Ś. 1. 24; अम्महे अपांगकः स्फुरति किमपि<BR>वामकः M. 2. 4.<BR>--2 A sectarial mark<BR>on the forehead.<BR>--3 Cupid, the god<BR>of love.<BR>--4 N. of a plant (अपामार्ग).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दर्शनं, --दृष्टिः f.,<BR>--विलोकितं,<BR>--वीक्षणं &c. a side-glance, side-long<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">Page0115-c+ 56</a>]<BR>look, wink.<BR>--देशः the place of the<BR>corner of the eye; the corner itself.<BR>--नेत्र a. (said of a lady) having<BR>eyes with beautiful (or long) outer<BR>corners; यदियं पुनरप्यपांगनेत्रा<BR>परिवृत्तार्धमुखी मयाद्य दृष्टा V. 1. 17 (a better<BR>interpretation would however be<BR>‘with the eyes turned towards the<BR>corners’ अपांगयोः प्रेरिते नेत्रे यया i. e.<BR>casting side-long looks).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपांगक|अपाङ्गक|अपाङ्गकः
अपांग --गक a. [अपगतं अंगं यस्य]<BR>1 Wanting or deformed in some limb<BR>of the body.<BR>--2 Maimed, crippled.<BR>--गः, --गकः [अपांगति तिर्यक् चलति नेत्रं<BR>यत्र, अप-अंग्-घञ्]<BR>1 The outer corner<BR>or angle of the eye; चलापांगां दृष्टिं<BR>Ś. 1. 24; अम्महे अपांगकः स्फुरति किमपि<BR>वामकः M. 2. 4.<BR>--2 A sectarial mark<BR>on the forehead.<BR>--3 Cupid, the god<BR>of love.<BR>--4 N. of a plant (अपामार्ग).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दर्शनं, --दृष्टिः f.,<BR>--विलोकितं,<BR>--वीक्षणं &c. a side-glance, side-long<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">Page0115-c+ 56</a>]<BR>look, wink.<BR>--देशः the place of the<BR>corner of the eye; the corner itself.<BR>--नेत्र a. (said of a lady) having<BR>eyes with beautiful (or long) outer<BR>corners; यदियं पुनरप्यपांगनेत्रा<BR>परिवृत्तार्धमुखी मयाद्य दृष्टा V. 1. 17 (a better<BR>interpretation would however be<BR>‘with the eyes turned towards the<BR>corners’ अपांगयोः प्रेरिते नेत्रे यया i. e.<BR>casting side-long looks).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाच्
अपाच्, अपांच् (m. ङ्, f. ची, n. क्)<BR>[अपांचति, अंच् क्विप्]<BR>1 Going or<BR>situated backwards, behind.<BR>--2 Not open<BR>or clear (अप्रकाश).<BR>--3 Western.<BR>--4<BR>Southern (opp. उदंच्); probably for<BR>अवांच्.<BR>--क् ind.<BR>1 Behind,<BR>backwards.<BR>--2 Westward or southward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपांच्|अपाञ्च्
अपाच्, अपांच् (m. ङ्, f. ची, n. क्)<BR>[अपांचति, अंच् क्विप्]<BR>1 Going or<BR>situated backwards, behind.<BR>--2 Not open<BR>or clear (अप्रकाश).<BR>--3 Western.<BR>--4<BR>Southern (opp. उदंच्); probably for<BR>अवांच्.<BR>--क् ind.<BR>1 Behind,<BR>backwards.<BR>--2 Westward or southward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाची
अपाची The south or west; ˚इतरा<BR>the north (other than south).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाचीन|अपाचीनं
अपाचीन a. [अपाच्यां भवः ख]<BR>1<BR>Situated backwards or behind, turned<BR>backwards.<BR>--2 Not visible,<BR>imperceptible; Rv. 7. 6. 4.<BR>--3 Southern.<BR>--4 Western.<BR>--5 Opposite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाच्य|अपाच्यं
अपाच्य a. [अपाच्-यत्] Western or<BR>southern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाटव|अपाटवं
अपाटव a. Unskilful.<BR>--वं<BR>1<BR>Unskilfulness.<BR>--2 Sickness, illness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाणिनीय
अपाणिनीय a.<BR>1 Not taught by<BR>Pāṇini in his works (as a rule &c.).<BR>--2 (पाणिनीयं अष्टाध्यायीरूपं ग्रंथं यो नाधीते)<BR>One who does not (properly) study<BR>Pāṇini's grammar; i. e. a superficial<BR>scholar, smatterer of Sanskrit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपात्रं|अपात्र
अपात्रं<BR>1 A worthless vessel or<BR>utensil.<BR>--2 (fig.) An unworthy or<BR>undeserving person, unfit receptacle<BR>or recipient<BR>--3 One unfit or<BR>disqualified to receive gifts; अदेशकाले<BR>यद्दानमपात्रेभ्यश्च दीयते Bg. 17. 22;<BR>Ks. 24. 26.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत्या, अपात्रीकरणं<BR>doing degrading or unworthy acts;<BR>disqualification, any action which<BR>makes a man unworthy; four<BR>disqualifications for a Brāhmaṇa are<BR>mentioned in Ms. 11. 70: -निंदितेभ्यो<BR>धनादानं वाणिज्यं शूद्रसेवनं । अपात्रीकरणं<BR>ज्ञेयमसत्यस्य च भाषणम् ॥; see also 11. 126.<BR>--दायिन् a. giving to unworthy<BR>persons.<BR>--भृत् a. supporting the<BR>unworthy or worthless;<BR>प्रायेणापात्रभृद्भवति राजा Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाद्
अपाद् = अपद् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपादा
अपादा {c3c} A. To take off or away,<BR>to remove; तत्पाष्मानमपादत्ते;<BR>मृत्पिंडमपादाय महावीरं करोति Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपादानं|अपादान
अपादानं<BR>1 Taking away, removal;<BR>ablation; a thing from which another<BR>is removed.<BR>--2 (In gram.) The sense<BR>of the ablative case; ध्रुवमपायेऽपादानं<BR>P. I. 4. 24; अपादाने पंचमी II. 3. 28;<BR>अपाये यदुदासीनं चलं वा यदि वाऽचलं ।<BR>ध्रुवमेव तदावेशात्तदपादानमुच्यते ॥ Hariv.; अपादान<BR>is of three kinds: -निर्दिष्टविषयं<BR>किंचिदुपात्तविषयं तथा । अपेक्षितक्रियं चेति<BR>त्रिधापादानमिष्यते ॥ e. g. वृक्षात् पत्रं पतति,<BR>मेघाद्विद्योतते विद्युत्, & कुतो भवान्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाध्वन्
अपाध्वन् n. A bad way;<BR>P. VI. 2. 187.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपान्
अपान् {c2c} P. [अप-अन्]<BR>1 To<BR>breathe out, respire; यद्वै प्रणिति स<BR>प्राणो यदपनिति सोऽपानः Ch. Up.<BR>--2<BR>To expire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानः|अपान|अपानं
अपानः Breathing out, respiration<BR>(opp. प्राण); प्राणापानौ समौ कृत्वा<BR>नासाभ्यंतरचारिणौ Bg. 5. 27; one of<BR>the five life-winds in the body<BR>which goes downwards and out at<BR>the anus (अपनयनान्मूत्रपुरीषादेरपानोऽ<BR>धोवृत्तिर्वायुर्नाभिस्थानः); मूत्रशुक्रवहो<BR>वायुरपान इति कीर्त्यते.<BR>--नः --नं The anus<BR>(आधारे घञ्).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दा giving<BR>Apāna.<BR>--द्वारं the anus.<BR>--पवनः, --वायुः<BR>{1} the life-wind called अपान. {2}<BR>ventris crepitus.<BR>--भृत् f. a sort of brick<BR>(cherishing the life-wind अपान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाननं|अपानन
अपाननं<BR>1 Respiration.<BR>--2 Taking<BR>downwards, urine, excrement &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपानृत
अपानृत a. Free from falsehood,<BR>true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाप|अपापः
अपाप --पिन् a. Sinless, guiltless,<BR>pure, virtuous; अपापानां कुले जाते मयि<BR>पापं न विद्यते । यदि संभाव्यते पापमपापेन च<BR>किं मया ॥ Mk. 9. 37.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काशिन् a. {1} not ill-looking. {2} not<BR>revealing evil.<BR>--वस्यसं Ved. well-being,<BR>welfare, sound health, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपापिन्
अपाप --पिन् a. Sinless, guiltless,<BR>pure, virtuous; अपापानां कुले जाते मयि<BR>पापं न विद्यते । यदि संभाव्यते पापमपापेन च<BR>किं मया ॥ Mk. 9. 37.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काशिन् a. {1} not ill-looking. {2} not<BR>revealing evil.<BR>--वस्यसं Ved. well-being,<BR>welfare, sound health, prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपांपित्त|अपाम्पित्त|अपांपित्तं|अपाम्पित्तं
अपांपित्त ˚नपात् &c. &c. see<BR>under अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपांनपात्|अपान्नपात्
अपांपित्त ˚नपात् &c. &c. see<BR>under अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपामार्गः|अपामार्ग
अपामार्गः [अपमृज्यते व्याध्यादिरनेन<BR>इत्यपामार्गः, मृज् करणे घञ् कुत्वं दीर्घश्च<BR>P. III. 3. 121 Sk.] N. of a plant<BR>Achyranthes Aspera (Mar. आघाडा)<BR>largely used in medicine, washing<BR>teeth, sacrificial and other religious<BR>purposes and in incantations;<BR>अपामार्ग त्वया वयं सर्वं तदपमृज्महे; अपामार्ग<BR>ओषधीनां सर्वासामेक इद्वशी । Av.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्षा<BR>रतैलं, -तैलं N. of two medicated oils<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपामार्जनं|अपामार्जन
अपामार्जनं Cleansing, purifying,<BR>removing (diseases, evils &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाय|अपायः
अपाय --यिन् See under अपे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपायिन्
अपाय --यिन् See under अपे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार|अपारं|अपारः
अपार a.<BR>1 Shoreless.<BR>--2<BR>Boundless, unbounded, unlimited;<BR>अपारस्याप्रमेयस्य परं पारमुपाश्रिते Rām.<BR>unfathomable, of great length.<BR>--3<BR>Inexhaustible, immense, great (अधिक);<BR>Rv. 5. 87. 6.<BR>--4 Out of reach.<BR>--5<BR>Difficult to be crossed; difficult to be<BR>surmounted or overcome (as an<BR>enemy); रावणश्च महाशत्रुरपारः<BR>प्रतिभाति मे । Rām.<BR>--रं<BR>1 A kind of<BR>mental satisfaction or acquiescence; or,<BR>reverse of mental acquiescence,<BR>nonacquiescence.<BR>--2 The opposite bank<BR>of a river.<BR>--रा The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपारक
अपारक a. Unable, incompetent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्ण
अपार्ण a. [अप-अर्द्-क्त निपातः]<BR>1<BR>Distant, remote, far.<BR>--2 Near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपार्थ
अपार्थ [अप-अर्थ], अपार्थक a.<BR>1<BR>Useless, unprofitable, worthless;<BR>सर्वमेतदपार्थं ते क्षिप्रं तौ संप्रसादय Mb.<BR>--2 Meaningless, unmeaning,<BR>senseless; अपार्थं बहु भाषते Suśr.<BR>--र्थं<BR>Senseless or incoherent talk or argument<BR>(regarded as one of the faults of<BR>composition in rhetoric);<BR>योग्यतासत्त्याकांक्षाशून्यं वाक्यं Gautama;<BR>पौर्वापर्यायोगादप्रतिबंधार्थमपार्थकं; cf. also<BR>Kāv. 3. 128; समुदायार्थशून्यं यत्तदपार्थमितीष्यते ।<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करणं advancing a false<BR>plea in a law-suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपालंकः|अपालङ्क|अपालङ्कः
अपालंकः N. of a plant, Cassia<BR>Fistula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपालंबः|अपालम्ब|अपालम्बः
अपालंबः Ved. The hinder part<BR>of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृ
अपावृ {c5c} P.<BR>1 To open, lay bare<BR>or open, unveil, uncover; expose,<BR>display, reveal; (शयनं) तस्य<BR>विभ्रमरतान्यपावृणोत् R. 19. 25.<BR>--2 To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत|अपावृतं
अपावृत p. p.<BR>1 Opened, laid bare<BR>or open; स्वर्गद्वारमपावृतं Bg. 2. 32.<BR>--2<BR>Covered, concealed; enclosed.<BR>--3 Free,<BR>unrestrained, self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृतिः|अपावृति
अपावृतिः f., अपावरणं<BR>1 Opening,<BR>laying bare or open.<BR>--2 Covering,<BR>enclosing, surrounding.<BR>--3<BR>Concealing, hiding, screening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्
अपावृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To turn away,<BR>return, turn back; to turn away from,<BR>abstain or desist from.<BR>--2 To come<BR>to nothing. --Caus. To send back,<BR>turn back; to reject, repulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावर्तनं|अपावर्तन|अपावर्त्तन
अपावर्तनं, --वृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Turning away<BR>or from, retreating, retiring; repulse,<BR>rejection.<BR>--2 Revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्तिः|अपावृत्ति
अपावर्तनं, --वृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Turning away<BR>or from, retreating, retiring; repulse,<BR>rejection.<BR>--2 Revolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपावृत्त|अपावृत्तं
अपावृत्त p. p.<BR>1 (With abl.)<BR>Turned away from, averted; reversed,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">Page0116-c+ 56</a>]<BR>repelled, driven back.<BR>--2 (Actively<BR>used) Dismissing, scorning,<BR>rejecting with contempt; प्रतिग्रहादपावृत्तः<BR>संतुष्टो येन केन चित् Mb.<BR>--त्तं Rolling<BR>on the ground (of a horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्या
अपाश्या Not a large number of<BR>snares, i. e. a few snares;<BR>P. VI. 2. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रि
अपाश्रि {c1c} U.<BR>1 To Resort to,<BR>betake oneself to; परस्परं केचिदपाश्रयंते<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 To use, practise, employ;<BR>आहारमनपाश्रित्य शरीरस्येव धारणं Mb.<BR>--3<BR>To rest on, lie on (intrans.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रय|अपाश्रयः
अपाश्रय a. Without support or<BR>refuge, helpless.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Refuge,<BR>recourse, that to which recourse is had<BR>for refuge; कर्णे कृतापाश्रयः Ve. 5. 1.<BR>--2 An awning or canopy spread over<BR>a courtyard.<BR>--3 Head; त्वदंकापाश्रयां तां<BR>Dk. 34, 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाश्रित
अपाश्रित p. p.<BR>1 (Passively used)<BR>(a) Restored to. (b) Girt round,<BR>fastened. (c) Inhabited by.<BR>--2<BR>(Actively used) Resting or<BR>reposing on, resorting to, entering on or<BR>into, being in or under.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाष्टिः|अपाष्टि
अपाष्टिः f. Ved. The heel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाष्ठः|अपाष्ठ
अपाष्ठः [स्था-क; --सस्य षत्वं] Ved. The<BR>barb or point of an arrow.<BR>--ष्ठं The<BR>remainder of the Soma plant after<BR>it has been pressed out; ˚वत् barbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपास्
अपास् [अप-अस्] {c4c} P.<BR>1 (a) To<BR>throw or fling away, cast away or<BR>off, leave, keep or put aside, reject,<BR>discard (opinion also); सारं ततो<BR>ग्राह्यमपास्य फल्गु Pt. 1;<BR>किमित्यपास्याभरणानि यौवने धृतं त्वया वार्धकशोभि<BR>वल्कलं Ku. 5. 44;<BR>निरस्तगांभीर्यमपास्तपुष्पकं Śi. 1. 55; इत्यादीनामपि<BR>काव्यलक्षणत्वमपास्तं S. D. rejected,<BR>discarded. (b) To leave, abandon, desert,<BR>quit, retire or withdraw from; यदि<BR>समरमपास्य नास्ति मृत्योर्भयं Ve. 3. 4.<BR>--2<BR>To scare, disperse, drive away; अपास्य<BR>चास्य यंतारं Mb.<BR>--3 To leave behind,<BR>leave in a deserted condition; to<BR>disregard, take no notice of, contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासनं|अपासन
अपासनं<BR>1 Throwing away,<BR>discarding.<BR>--2 Quitting.<BR>--3 Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासित
अपासित p. p. (fr. caus.) Thrown<BR>away, discarded &c.; injured,<BR>destroyed, killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासंगः|अपासङ्ग|अपासंग|अपासङ्गः
अपासंगः [संज्-घञ्-कुत्वं] A quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासरणं|अपासरण
अपासरणं Departure, retreat,<BR>removal; see अपसरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपासु
अपासु a. Lifeless, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपाहा
अपाहा {c3c} P. = अपहा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपि
अपि ind. (Sometimes with the अ<BR>dropped according to the opinion of<BR>Bhāguri; वष्टि भागुरिरल्लोपमवाप्योरुपसर्गयोः;<BR>पिधा, पिधान &c.)<BR>1 (Used with roots<BR>and nouns in the sense of) Placing<BR>near or over, taking towards,<BR>uniting with; reaching or going up to,<BR>proximity, nearness &c. [Cf. Gr.<BR>epi, Zend api, Germ. and Eng. be].<BR>(Note. अपि, as a prefix to roots, occurs<BR>mostly in Veda, its place being taken<BR>by अभि in classical literature).<BR>--2 (As<BR>a separable adverb or conjunction)<BR>And, also, too, moreover, besides, in<BR>addition, having a cumulative force<BR>(समुच्चय); अस्ति मे सोदरस्नेहोप्येतेषु; Ś. 1<BR>on one's part, in one's turn;<BR>विष्णुशर्मणापि राजपुत्राः पाटिताः Pt. 1;<BR>राजापि मुनिवाक्यमंगीकृत्यातिष्ठत् Dk. 2; अपि<BR>-अपि or अपि च as well as, and also;<BR>अपि स्तुहि, अपि सिंच P. I. 4. 96 Sk.,<BR>न नापि-न चैव, न वापि, नापि वा न चापि<BR>neither-nor; न वापि काव्यं नवमित्यवद्यं<BR>M. 1. 2 nor; वापि or; अल्पोप्येवं महान्<BR>वापि Ms. 3. 53 whether small or great.<BR>--3 It is often used to express<BR>emphasis in the sense of ‘too’, ‘even’<BR>‘very’; विधुरपि विधियोगाद् ग्रस्यते<BR>राहणासौ H. 1 the very moon;<BR>यूयमप्यनेन कर्मणा परिश्रांताः Ś. 1 even you,<BR>you also; अन्यदपि also another;<BR>अद्यापि even, yet, still, even now;<BR>इदानीमपि even now; मुहूर्तमपि even<BR>for a moment, for one moment at<BR>least; नाद्यापि not yet; यद्यपि though,<BR>although, even if; तथापि still,<BR>nevertheless, notwithstanding, yet;<BR>sometimes यद्यपि is understood,<BR>तथापि only being used; as in<BR>Ki. 1. 28.<BR>--4 Though (oft. translateable<BR>by ‘even’, ‘even if’); सरसिजमनुविद्धं<BR>शैवलेनापि रम्यं Ś. 1. 20 though<BR>overspread &c.; इयमधिकमनोज्ञा वल्कलेनापि<BR>तन्वी ibid. though in her bark dress;<BR>बलवदपि शिक्षितानाम् 1. 2 though ever<BR>so learned. In this sense अपि is most<BR>frequently used by writers to show<BR>real or imaginary opposition (विरोध);<BR>कृष्णमपि असुदर्शनं, पुष्पवत्यपि पवित्रा &c.<BR>--5<BR>But, however.<BR>--6 Used at the<BR>beginning of sentences अपि introduces<BR>a question; अपि सन्निहितोऽत्र कुलपतिः<BR>Ś. 1; अपि क्रियार्थं सुलभं समित्कुशं… अपि<BR>स्वशक्त्या तपसि प्रवर्तसे Ku. 5. 33, 34,<BR>35; अप्यग्रणीर्मंत्रकृतामृषीणां<BR>कुशाग्रबुद्धे कुशली गुरुस्ते R. 5. 4.<BR>--7 Hope,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-b" target="_blank">Page0117-b+ 58</a>]<BR>expectation (usually with the potential<BR>mood); कृतं रामसदृशं कर्म । अपि जीवेत्स<BR>ब्राह्मणशेशुः U. 2. I hope the Brāhmaṇa<BR>boy comes to life. Note-In this<BR>sense अपि is frequently used with<BR>नाम and has the sense of (a) ‘is it<BR>likely’, ‘may it be’; (b)<BR>‘perhaps’, ‘in all probability’ or (c)<BR>‘would that’, ‘I wish or hope’<BR>that’; अपि नाम<BR>कुलपतोरियमसवर्णक्षेत्रसंभवा स्यात् Ś. 1; Ś. 7; तदपि नाम<BR>मनागवतीर्णोसि रतिरमणबाणगोचरं Māl. 1<BR>perhaps, in all probability; अपि नाम<BR>तयोः कल्याणिनोः अभिमतः पाणिग्रहः<BR>स्यात् ibid.; अपि नाम रामभद्रः पुनरपीदं<BR>वनमलंकुर्यात् U. 2; ‘is it likely’, ‘I wish’;<BR>यथा वनज्योत्स्नानुरूपेण पादपेन संगता<BR>अपि नाम एवमहमप्यात्मनोऽनुरूपं वरं<BR>लभेयेति Ś. 1 would that; अपि नामाहं<BR>पुरूरवा भवेयं V. 2 I wish I were P.<BR>--8 Affixed to interrogative words<BR>अपि makes the sense indefinite,<BR>‘any’, ‘some’; कोपि some one; किमपि<BR>something; कुत्रापि somewhere; कदापि<BR>at any time; कथमपि any how &c.<BR>केऽपि एते प्रवयसः त्वां दिदृक्षवः U. 4<BR>some people. It may often be<BR>translated by ‘unknown’,<BR>‘indescribable,’ ‘inexpressible’ (अनिर्वाच्य);<BR>व्यतिषजति पदार्थानांतरः कोपि हेतुः<BR>U. 6. 12; तत्तस्य किमपि द्रव्यं यो हि यस्य<BR>प्रियो जनः 2. 19; Mu. 3. 22; K. 143;<BR>कोपि महिमा स्यात् U. 6, 6. 11, 7. 12;<BR>Māl. 1. 26; R. 1. 46.<BR>--9 After words<BR>expressing number अपि has the<BR>sense of ‘totality’, ‘all’; चतुर्णामपि<BR>वर्णानां of all the 4 castes; सर्वैरपि<BR>राज्ञां प्रयोजनं Pt. 1.<BR>--10 It sometimes<BR>expresses ‘doubt’ or ‘uncertainty,’<BR>‘fear’ (शंका); अपि चोरो भवेत् G. M.<BR>there is perhaps a thief.<BR>--11 (with<BR>pot. mood) It has the sense of संभावना<BR>‘possibility’, ‘supposition’; P. I. 4. 96;<BR>III. 3. 154; अपि स्तुयाद्विष्णुं, अपि<BR>स्तुयाद्राजानं, अपि गिरिं शिरसा भिंद्यात् Sk.;<BR>सोयमपि सिंचेत्सहस्रं द्राक्षाणां क्षणेनैकेन<BR>Dk. 127.<BR>--12 Contempt,<BR>censure, or reproof; P. I. 4. 96,<BR>III. 3. 142; धिग्देवदत्तमपि स्तुयाद्वृषलं; धिग्जाल्मं<BR>देवदत्तमपि सिंचेत् पलांडुं; अपि जायां<BR>त्यजसि जातु गणिकामाधत्से गर्हितमेतत् Sk.<BR>shame to, &c. or fie upon, Devadatta<BR>&c.<BR>--13 It is also used with the<BR>Imperative mood to mark ‘indifference<BR>on the part of the speaker’, where<BR>he permits another to do as he likes,<BR>(अन्ववसर्ग or कामचारानुज्ञा, the imperative<BR>being softened;) अपि स्तुहि Sk. you<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">Page0117-c+ 55</a>]<BR>may praise (if you like); अपि स्तुह्यपि<BR>सेधास्मांस्तथ्यमुक्तं नराशन Bk. 8. 92.<BR>--14 अपि is sometimes used as a<BR>particle of exclamation,<BR>--15 Rarely in the<BR>sense of ‘therefore,’ ‘hence’ (अत एव).<BR>--16 Used as a separable preposition<BR>with gen. it is said to express the<BR>sense of a word understood (पदार्थ),<BR>and is treated as a कर्मप्रवचनीय<BR>P. I. 4. 96; the example usually given is<BR>सर्पिषोपि स्यात् where some word like<BR>बिंदुरपि ‘a drop,’ ‘a little’ &c.<BR>has to be understood, ‘there may<BR>perhaps be a drop of ghee,’ ‘I<BR>presume there may be at least a drop’<BR>&c. अपि संभावनाप्रश्नशंकागर्हासमुच्चये ।<BR>तथायुक्तपदार्थेषु कामचारक्रियासु च ॥ Viśva.; अपिः<BR>पदार्थसंभावनान्ववसर्गगर्हासमुच्चयेषु P. I. 4. 96.<BR>G. M. adds the senses of आशिस्<BR>‘blessing’ (भद्रमपि), मृति ‘death’ (मरणमपि)<BR>and भूषा ‘decoration’ (अपि न ह्यति हारं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिकक्षः|अपिकक्ष
अपिकक्षः Ved. The region of<BR>the arm-pits and shoulder-blades,<BR>especially in animals.<BR>--क्षं ind. In<BR>the armpit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिकक्ष्य
अपिकक्ष्य a. Belonging to this<BR>region (Sāy. on Rv. 1. 117. 22 says<BR>˚क्ष्यं छिन्नस्य यज्ञशिरसः कक्षप्रदेशेन संधानभूतं<BR>प्रवर्ग्यविद्याख्यं रहस्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिकर्णं|अपिकर्ण
अपिकर्णं The region of the ears;<BR>near (समीप) Rv. 6. 48. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिगीर्ण|अपिगीर्णं
अपिगीर्ण a.<BR>1 Praised,<BR>celebrated.<BR>--2 Told, described.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिच्छिल|अपिच्छिलः
अपिच्छिल a.<BR>1 Not muddy, clear,<BR>free from sediment.<BR>--2 Deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिज|अपिजः
अपिज a. Born after or again,<BR>epithet of several deities.<BR>--जः<BR>[अपि अप्सु जायते, अलुक् वेदे<BR>अप्शब्दस्यैकवचनत्वमपि] N. of the month<BR>ofJyeṣṭha (जलक्रीडारतिसाधनत्वात्तथात्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्
अपित् a. [आपः इतो गता यस्य वेदे न<BR>जष्]<BR>1 Dry, waterless, as a river.<BR>--2 Not having the इत् or अनुबंध प्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपितृक
अपितृक a.<BR>1 Fatherless.<BR>--2 Not<BR>ancestral or paternal, not inherited<BR>(अपैतृक also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्र्य
अपित्र्य a. Not ancestral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्वं|अपित्व
अपित्वं Ved. [अपित्वरते अस्मै, त्वर्<BR>बा˚ड] A part, portion, share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपित्विन्
अपित्विन् a. Having a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधा
अपिधा {c3c} U. To shut, close,<BR>cover, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधानं|अपिधान
अपिधानं, --पिधानं<BR>1 Covering,<BR>concealing, concealment.<BR>--2 A cover,<BR>lid, covering (fig. also);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">Page0118-a+ 54</a>]<BR>अमृतापिधानमसि स्वाहा; नैकजलदच्छत्रापिधानं जगत्<BR>Mk. 5. 24; a cloth for covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिधानं|पिधान
अपिधानं, --पिधानं<BR>1 Covering,<BR>concealing, concealment.<BR>--2 A cover,<BR>lid, covering (fig. also);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">Page0118-a+ 54</a>]<BR>अमृतापिधानमसि स्वाहा; नैकजलदच्छत्रापिधानं जगत्<BR>Mk. 5. 24; a cloth for covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिधिः|अपिधि
अपिधिः f. Concealment,<BR>covering<BR>--धिः What is given to another's<BR>entire satisfaction तृप्तिपर्यंतदत्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिहित
अपिहित --पिहित p. p.<BR>1 Shut, closed,<BR>covered, concealed (fig. also);<BR>बाष्पापिहेत covered with tears.<BR>--2 Not<BR>concealed, plain, clear; अर्थो<BR>गिरामपिहितः पिहितश्च किंचित्, सत्यं<BR>चकास्ति मरहदृवधूस्तनाभः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिहित|पिहितं
अपिहित --पिहित p. p.<BR>1 Shut, closed,<BR>covered, concealed (fig. also);<BR>बाष्पापिहेत covered with tears.<BR>--2 Not<BR>concealed, plain, clear; अर्थो<BR>गिरामपिहितः पिहितश्च किंचित्, सत्यं<BR>चकास्ति मरहदृवधूस्तनाभः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिप्राण
अपिप्राण a. (णी f.) Always<BR>animating or vivifying (सर्वदाचेष्टमान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिभाग
अपिभाग a. Ved. Sharing or<BR>partaking in, having a share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिव्रत
अपिव्रत a. Sharing in the same<BR>religious acts or other works;<BR>connected by blood; अपिव्रताश्चान्वारभंते<BR>यजमानं Kāty. (संसृष्टं साधारणकर्म येषां ते<BR>अपिव्रताः अविभक्ता दायादाः, ते हि एकेनापि<BR>कृष्यादिकर्म कृतं सर्वे उपजीवंति Com.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिशर्वर|अपिशर्व्वर
अपिशर्वर a. Ved. Close to the<BR>night, being at the beginning (or<BR>end) of the night.<BR>--रं Early or<BR>untimely morning, evening (or<BR>morning) time (प्रदोषमुखं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिशलः|अपिशल
अपिशलः N. of a man; a<BR>grammarian; (pl.) his descendants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपिशस्
अपिशस् a. Ripping up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपी
अपी [अपि-इ] {c2c} P. (Mostly<BR>Vedic)<BR>1 To go in or near, enter into<BR>or upon, approach.<BR>--2 To have a<BR>share in, partake of, suffer; जरामृत्युं<BR>पुनरेवापियंति Muṇḍ.<BR>--3 To join, flow,<BR>flow into, dissolve, be resolved into;<BR>स्वमपीतो भवति तस्मादेनं स्वपितीत्याचक्षते<BR>Ch. Up.<BR>--4 To die.<BR>--5 To pour out<BR>(as a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीतिः|अपीति
अपीतिः f.<BR>1 Entering into,<BR>approaching.<BR>--2 Dissolution,<BR>destruction; loss.<BR>--3 Destruction of the<BR>world (प्रलय); अपीतौ तद्वत्<BR>प्रसंगादसमंजसं Br. Sūt. II. 1. 8.<BR>--4<BR>Encountering, joining in battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्ययः|अप्यय
अप्ययः<BR>1 Approaching, meeting,<BR>joining, juncture.<BR>--2 Pouring out<BR>(of rivers).<BR>--3 Entrance into,<BR>vanishing, disappearance; absorption,<BR>dissolution into oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्ययनं|अप्ययन
अप्ययनं<BR>1 Union, junction.<BR>--2<BR>Copulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीच्य
अपीच्य a.<BR>1 Very handsome or<BR>beautiful (अतिसुंदर).<BR>--2 Secret,<BR>concealed, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीजु
अपीजु a. Ved. Impelling,<BR>stirring up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीनसः|अपीनस|अपीनसं
अपीनसः [अपीनाय, अपीनत्वाय सीयते<BR>कल्पते कर्मकर्तरि क Tv.] Dryness of the<BR>nose; cold (in the head), rheum,<BR>catarrh; see पीनस.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपीव्य|अपीव्यं
अपीव्य a. Ved. Very handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुंस्
अपुंस् m. (˚पुमान्) Not a man,<BR>a eunuch; Ms. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुंस्त्वं|अपुंस्त्व
अपुंस्त्वं The state of a eunuch,<BR>impotent state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुंस्का
अपुंस्का f. A woman without a<BR>husband; नापुंस्कासीति मे मतिः Bk. 5. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुच्छ
अपुच्छ a. Without a tail.<BR>--च्छा<BR>N. of a tree (Mar. शीसु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुण्य
अपुण्य a. Not virtuous or holy,<BR>wicked, bad; ˚कृत् one who does<BR>not perform meritorious deeds, or<BR>who commits unrighteous deeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्रः|अपुत्र
अपुत्रः Not a son. --a.,<BR>--पुत्रकः (<BR>˚त्रिका f.) Having no son or heir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुत्रिका
अपुत्रिका The daughter of a<BR>sonless father, who herself has no<BR>male child; one who is not<BR>appointed by her father to beget<BR>male issue for him on failure of<BR>a son; cf. अकृता.<BR>--कः The father<BR>of such a daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुनर्
अपुनर् ind. Not again, once for<BR>all, for ever.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वय a. not<BR>returning; dead.<BR>--आदानं not taking<BR>back or again.<BR>--आवृत्तिः f.<BR>‘nonreturn’, exemption of the soul from<BR>further transmigration, final<BR>beatitude.<BR>--प्राप्य a. irrecoverable.<BR>--भवः<BR>{1} not being born again (of diseases<BR>also). {2} final beatitude. {3}<BR>knowledge of the Supreme Soul which<BR>tends to this step. {4} a person<BR>released from metempsychosis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुरुष
अपुरुष a. Not manlike,<BR>unmanly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः {1} a rite or<BR>ceremony which is not in the interests<BR>of the doer. {2} not the principal<BR>object of the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्कल
अपुष्कल a.<BR>1 Not much.<BR>--2 Mean,<BR>low, base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्ट
अपुष्ट a.<BR>1 Not nourished or fed,<BR>lean, not fat.<BR>--2 Not loud or<BR>violent, soft, low (as sound).<BR>--3 (In<BR>Rhet.) Not feeding or assisting (the<BR>meaning), irrelevant (<BR>मुख्यानुपकारिन्), regarded as one of the<BR>arthadoshas (faults of the sense or<BR>meaning); as in the instance given<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">Page0118-c+ 56</a>]<BR>under S. D. 576 विलोक्य वितते व्योम्नि<BR>विधुं मुंच रुषंप्रिये, the adjective वितत<BR>‘expanded,’ as applied, to the sky, does<BR>not in any way help the cessation of<BR>anger and is, therefore, irrelevant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुष्प|अपुष्पः
अपुष्प a. Flowerless, not<BR>flowering.<BR>--ष्पः The glomerous fig-tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फल, --फलद a. bearing<BR>fruits without flowering, having<BR>neither fruits nor flowers. (-लः, -दः) {1}<BR>the jack tree (Mar. फणस)<BR>Artocarpus Integrifolia. {2} the glomerous<BR>fig-tree (उदुंबर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपुस्
अपुस् n. Ved. Shape, body = वपुस्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजक
अपूजक a. Irreligious, irreverent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूजा
अपूजा Disrespect, irreverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूपः|अपूप
अपूपः [न पूयते विशीर्यते, पू-प. न. ते.<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 A small round cake of flour,<BR>meal &c. (Mar. वडा, घारगा, अनरसा<BR>&c.), thicker than ordinary cakes<BR>and mixed with sugar and spices;<BR>भीमेनातिबलेन मत्स्यभवनेऽपूपा न संघट्टिताः<BR>Pt. 3. 172.<BR>--2 Wheat.<BR>--3 Honey-comb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूपीय
अपूपीय, अपूप्य [अपूपाय हितं, यत् छ च]<BR>Belonging to, intended for, अपूप.<BR>--प्यं Flour, meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूप्य|अपूप्यः
अपूपीय, अपूप्य [अपूपाय हितं, यत् छ च]<BR>Belonging to, intended for, अपूप.<BR>--प्यं Flour, meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूरणी
अपूरणी The silk cotton tree<BR>(शाल्मली) Bombax Heptaphyllum<BR>(Mar. सांवरी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूरुष
अपूरुष a.<BR>1 Lifeless, inanimate<BR>(as wood &c.).<BR>--2 Soulless.<BR>--3<BR>Unpeopled, untenanted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्ण
अपूर्ण a. Not full or completed,<BR>incomplete, deficient, imperfect;<BR>अपूर्णमेकेन शतक्रतूनां R. 3. 38; अपूर्ण<BR>एव पंचरात्रे दोहदस्य M. 3.<BR>--र्णं<BR>Incomplete number or fraction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काल a. premature, untimely.<BR>--(लः) premature or incomplete<BR>time; ˚ज abortive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्व|अपूर्वः|अपूर्व्व|अपूर्व्वं
अपूर्व a.<BR>1 Not preceded, not<BR>having existed before, the like of which<BR>did not exist before, quite new; ˚र्वं<BR>नाटकं Ś. 1; ˚र्वं राजकुलं M. 5;<BR>K. 191; Śi. 4. 17.<BR>--2 Strange,<BR>extraordinary, wonderful; अपूर्वः कोपि<BR>बहुमानहेतुर्गुरुषु U. 4; अपूर्वो दृश्यते वाह्निः<BR>कामिन्याः स्तनमंडले । दूरतो दहतीवांगं<BR>हृदि लग्रस्तु शीतलः ॥ Ś. Til. 17;<BR>singular, unexampled,<BR>unprecedented; अपूर्व एष विरहमार्गः Ś. 6;<BR>अपूर्वरूपा दारिका M. 1; अतोऽपूर्वः<BR>खलु वोऽनुग्रहः Ś. 7;<BR>अपूर्वकर्मचांडालमयि मुग्धे विमुंच मां U. 1. 46<BR>committing an unparalleled atrocity.<BR>--3<BR>Unknown, unacquainted, stranger;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">Page0119-a+ 57</a>]<BR>Ki. 6. 39.<BR>--4 Not first.<BR>--5<BR>Preceded by अ or आ<BR>--6 (In phil.). ‘That<BR>unseen virtue which is a relation<BR>superinduced, not before<BR>possessed, unseen but efficacious to<BR>connect the consequence with its<BR>past and remote cause and to<BR>bring about at a distant period or<BR>in another world the relative effect’<BR>Colebrooke.<BR>--र्वं<BR>1 The remote<BR>consequence of an act (as the acquisition<BR>of heaven which is the result of<BR>good deeds).<BR>--2 Virtue and vice<BR>(पापपुण्यं) as the eventual cause of<BR>future happiness or misery.<BR>--र्वः<BR>The supreme soul (परब्रह्म).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. religious rites the power<BR>of which on the future is not<BR>seen before.<BR>--पतिः f. one who<BR>has had no husband before, a<BR>virgin; ˚तिः कुमारी Sk.<BR>--वादः<BR>discussion or talk about the Supreme<BR>Soul.<BR>--विधिः an authoritative<BR>direction or injunction which is<BR>quite new; it is of four kinds<BR>कर्मविधि, गुणविधि, विनियोगविधि and प्रयोगविधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वता|अपूर्व्वता
अपूर्वता --त्वं Not having existed<BR>before, incomparableness,<BR>unparalleled or extraordinary nature;<BR>अपूर्वत्वात्प्रबंधस्य Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वत्वं|अपूर्वत्व
अपूर्वता --त्वं Not having existed<BR>before, incomparableness,<BR>unparalleled or extraordinary nature;<BR>अपूर्वत्वात्प्रबंधस्य Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्ववत्|अपूर्व्ववत्
अपूर्ववत् ind. Singularly, unlike<BR>any thing else.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वेण
अपूर्वेण adv. Never before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्वीय
अपूर्वीय a. Relating to the<BR>remote consequence of an act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपूर्व्य|अपूर्व्व्य
अपूर्व्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Unpreceded,<BR>first.<BR>--2 Incomparable, unheard<BR>of before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृक्त|अपृक्तः
अपृक्त a. Not united,<BR>uncombined.<BR>--क्तः<BR>1 (In gram.) An affix (or a<BR>word) consisting of a single letter;<BR>अपृक्त एकाल्प्रत्ययः P. I. 2. 41;<BR>एकवर्णपदमपृक्तं Sk.<BR>--2 (In the Prātiśākhyas.)<BR>The preposition आ and the particle उ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृणत्|अपृणन्त्
अपृणत् a. Not filling; stingy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपृथक्
अपृथक् ind. Not separately,<BR>together with, collectively.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धर्मशील of the same religion.<BR>--धी<BR>a. maintaining the doctrine of<BR>pantheism; regarding God in all things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपे
अपे [अप-इ] {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go away,<BR>depart, withdraw, retire, run away,<BR>escape; अपेहि begone, avaunt, away,<BR>hence, get you gone; to disappear,<BR>vanish, pass away; die or perish<BR>also; धर्मश्चापैति Ms. 1. 82;<BR>हृदयात्प्रत्यादेशव्यलीकमपैतु ते Ś. 7. 24; रम्या<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-b" target="_blank">Page0119-b+ 57</a>]<BR>नवद्युतिरपैति न शाद्वलेभ्यः Ki. 5. 37<BR>does not leave.<BR>--2 To be wanting,<BR>be omitted; be deprived of, be free<BR>from.<BR>--3 To start (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपायः|अपाय
अपायः<BR>1 [इ-अच्] Going away,<BR>departure.<BR>--2 Separation; धुवमपायेऽ<BR>पादानं P. I. 4. 24 (अपायो विश्लेषः Sk);<BR>येन जातं प्रियापाये कद्वदं हंसकोकिलं<BR>Bk. 6. 75.<BR>--3 Disappearance, vanishing,<BR>absence; सूर्यापाये Me. 80 at the time of<BR>sunset; क्षणदापायशशांकदर्शनः<BR>R. 8. 74 close of night;<BR>जलापायविपांडुराणि Śi. 4. 5; 4. 54; 18. 1.<BR>--4<BR>Destruction, loss, death, annihilation;<BR>करणापायविभिन्नवर्णया R. 8. 42 loss, 83;<BR>मालत्यपायमधिगम्य Māl. 10. 9 death<BR>or disappearance of M.<BR>--5 An evil,<BR>ill, misfortune, risk, calamity,<BR>danger (oft. opp. अपाय); तदपि<BR>मरणापायचकितः Bh. 3. 9; तदनेन<BR>पापबुद्धिनोपायश्चिंतितो नापायः Pt. 1 not the<BR>danger (resulting from the plan);<BR>उपायं चिंतयेत्प्राज्ञस्तथापायं च चिंतयेत्<BR>Pt. 1. 406; अपायसंदर्शनजां<BR>विपत्तिमुपायसंदर्शनजां च सिद्धिं 1. 61; बह्वपाये वने<BR>Pt. 1 exposed to many dangers,<BR>dangerous; कायः संनिहितापायः<BR>H. 4. 65 exposed to dangers or calamities;<BR>सत्येऽप्यपायमपेक्षते H. 4. 102;<BR>Ki. 14. 19.<BR>--6 Loss, detriment,<BR>injury.<BR>--7 The end (of a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपायिन्
अपायिन् a. Departing, transient;<BR>perishable; see अनपायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेत
अपेत p. p.<BR>1 Gone away,<BR>disappeared; अपेतयुद्धभिनिवेशसौम्यः<BR>Śi. 3. 1.<BR>--2 Departing or deviating<BR>from, swerving from, contrary (with<BR>abl.); अर्थादनपेतं अर्थ्यं P. IV. 4. 92<BR>Sk. (धर्मपथ्यर्थन्यायादनपेते);<BR>स्मृत्यपेतादिकारिणः Y. 2. 4.<BR>--3 Free from, devoid<BR>of, deprived of (with abl. or in<BR>comp.); सुखादपेतः Sk.; उदवहदनवद्यां<BR>तामवद्यादपेतः R. 7. 70 faultless; ˚भीः<BR>Ms. 7. 197; भर्तर्यपेततमसि प्रभुता तवैव<BR>Ś. 7. 32 freed from (mental)<BR>darkness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--राक्षसी N. of a plant,<BR>Ocimum Sanctum (तुलसी) (अस्याः<BR>राक्षसतुल्यपापादिहरणात्तन्नामत्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्ष्
अपेक्ष् [अप-ईक्ष्] {c1c} A.<BR>1 To look<BR>round or about for something, to<BR>look or hope for, expect.<BR>--2 To<BR>wait for, await; सज्जो रथो<BR>भर्तुर्विजयप्रस्थानमपेक्षते Ś. 2 awaits; क्षणमपेक्षस्व<BR>U. 7; K. 84; न कालमपेक्षते स्नेहः<BR>Mk. 7. न स्वयं दैवमादत्ते पुरुषार्थमपेक्षते<BR>H. Pr. 35; पादेन नापैक्षत सुंदरीणां<BR>संपर्कमाशिंजितनूपुरेण Ku. 3. 26.<BR>--3 To require,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-c" target="_blank">Page0119-c+ 57</a>]<BR>want, stand in need of; wish or<BR>desire for; शब्दार्थौ सत्कविरिव द्वयं<BR>विद्वानपेक्षते Śi. 2. 86; न शालेः<BR>स्तंबकरिता वमुर्गुणमपेक्षते Mu. 1. 3; प्रभुता<BR>रमणेषु योषितां न हि भावस्खलितान्यपेक्षते<BR>V. 4. 12; Ku. 3. 18; Pt. 2. 26.<BR>--4 To<BR>have regard to, look to, have in<BR>view, have an eye to; किमपेक्ष्य फलं<BR>पयोधरान् ध्वनतः प्रार्थयते मृगाधिपः<BR>Ki. 2. 21; यतः शब्दोऽयं व्यंजकत्वेऽर्थांतरमपेक्षते<BR>S. D.<BR>--5 To take into account or<BR>consideration, consider, think of, respect,<BR>care for; उपकृतमपि नापेक्षते K. 35,<BR>197, 257, 315;<BR>नूनमस्यायमनपोक्षितास्मदवस्थो व्यापारः Māl. 9; अनलेष्विष्टवान्<BR>कस्मान्न त्वयाऽपेक्षितः पिता Bk. 6. 128<BR>Ś. 5. 16, Ms. 8. 309; with न not<BR>to like, not to care for;<BR>अनपेक्षितराजराजं Mu. 3. 18; तदानपेक्ष्य<BR>स्वशरीरमार्दवं Ku. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षा
अपेक्षा --क्षणं<BR>1 Expectation, hope,<BR>desire.<BR>--2 Need, requirement,<BR>necessity; निरपेक्ष without hope or need,<BR>regardless of; सापेक्षत्वेऽपि<BR>गमकत्वात्समासः; अनपेक्षः शुचिर्दक्षः Bg. 12. 16; or in<BR>comp.; स्फुलिंगावस्थया वह्निरेधापेक्ष इव<BR>स्थितः Ś. 7. 15 awaiting kindling.<BR>--3<BR>Consideration, reference, regard,<BR>with the obj. in loc. case; more<BR>usually in comp.; मध्यभंगानपेक्षं Ratn. 1. 17<BR>regardless of; the instr. and<BR>sometimes loc. of this word frequently<BR>occur in comp. meaning ‘with<BR>reference to’, ‘out of regard for’,<BR>‘with a view to’, ‘for the sake of’;<BR>सापि कार्यकरणापेक्षया क्षुरमेकमादाय<BR>तस्याभिमुखं प्रेषयामास Pt. 1; नियमापेक्षया<BR>R. 1. 94; वृषलापेक्षया Mu. 1;<BR>पौरजनापेक्षया {2} out of regard for;<BR>किमकौशलादुत प्रयोजनापेक्षया {3} with a view to<BR>gain some object; प्रथमसुकृतापेक्षया<BR>Me. 17; दंडं शक्त्यपेक्षं Y. 2. 26 in<BR>proportion to, in accordance with;<BR>अत्र व्यंग्यं गुणीभूतं तदपेक्षया वाच्यस्यैव<BR>चमत्कारिकत्वात् K. P. 1 as compared<BR>with it.<BR>--4 Connection, relation,<BR>dependence as of cause with effect or<BR>of individual with species;<BR>शरीरसाधनापेक्षं नित्यं यत्कर्म तद्यमः Ak.<BR>--5 Care,<BR>attention, heed; देशापेशाक्षास्तथा यूयं<BR>यातादायांगुरीयकं Bk. 7. 49.<BR>--6 Respect,<BR>deference.<BR>--7 (In gram.) = आकांक्षा q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बुद्धिः (In Vaiśeṣika phil.)<BR>the distinguishing perception by<BR>which we apprehend ‘this is one,’<BR>‘this is one &c.’ and which gives<BR>rise to the notion of duality;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">Page0120-a+ 56</a>]<BR>see Sarva. chap. 10 where अपेक्षाबुद्धिः<BR>= विनाशकविनाशप्रतियोगिनी बुद्धिः; cf.<BR>Bhāṣā P. द्वित्वादयः परार्धांता अपेक्षाबुद्धिजा<BR>मताः । अनेकाश्रयपर्याप्ता एते तु परिकीर्तिताः<BR>अपेक्षाबुद्धिनाशाच्च नाशस्तेषां निरूपितः 107-8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षणं|अपेक्षण
अपेक्षा --क्षणं<BR>1 Expectation, hope,<BR>desire.<BR>--2 Need, requirement,<BR>necessity; निरपेक्ष without hope or need,<BR>regardless of; सापेक्षत्वेऽपि<BR>गमकत्वात्समासः; अनपेक्षः शुचिर्दक्षः Bg. 12. 16; or in<BR>comp.; स्फुलिंगावस्थया वह्निरेधापेक्ष इव<BR>स्थितः Ś. 7. 15 awaiting kindling.<BR>--3<BR>Consideration, reference, regard,<BR>with the obj. in loc. case; more<BR>usually in comp.; मध्यभंगानपेक्षं Ratn. 1. 17<BR>regardless of; the instr. and<BR>sometimes loc. of this word frequently<BR>occur in comp. meaning ‘with<BR>reference to’, ‘out of regard for’,<BR>‘with a view to’, ‘for the sake of’;<BR>सापि कार्यकरणापेक्षया क्षुरमेकमादाय<BR>तस्याभिमुखं प्रेषयामास Pt. 1; नियमापेक्षया<BR>R. 1. 94; वृषलापेक्षया Mu. 1;<BR>पौरजनापेक्षया {2} out of regard for;<BR>किमकौशलादुत प्रयोजनापेक्षया {3} with a view to<BR>gain some object; प्रथमसुकृतापेक्षया<BR>Me. 17; दंडं शक्त्यपेक्षं Y. 2. 26 in<BR>proportion to, in accordance with;<BR>अत्र व्यंग्यं गुणीभूतं तदपेक्षया वाच्यस्यैव<BR>चमत्कारिकत्वात् K. P. 1 as compared<BR>with it.<BR>--4 Connection, relation,<BR>dependence as of cause with effect or<BR>of individual with species;<BR>शरीरसाधनापेक्षं नित्यं यत्कर्म तद्यमः Ak.<BR>--5 Care,<BR>attention, heed; देशापेशाक्षास्तथा यूयं<BR>यातादायांगुरीयकं Bk. 7. 49.<BR>--6 Respect,<BR>deference.<BR>--7 (In gram.) = आकांक्षा q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बुद्धिः (In Vaiśeṣika phil.)<BR>the distinguishing perception by<BR>which we apprehend ‘this is one,’<BR>‘this is one &c.’ and which gives<BR>rise to the notion of duality;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">Page0120-a+ 56</a>]<BR>see Sarva. chap. 10 where अपेक्षाबुद्धिः<BR>= विनाशकविनाशप्रतियोगिनी बुद्धिः; cf.<BR>Bhāṣā P. द्वित्वादयः परार्धांता अपेक्षाबुद्धिजा<BR>मताः । अनेकाश्रयपर्याप्ता एते तु परिकीर्तिताः<BR>अपेक्षाबुद्धिनाशाच्च नाशस्तेषां निरूपितः 107-8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्ष्य
अपेक्ष्य, --क्षितव्य, --क्षणीय pot. p. To<BR>be desired, wanted, hoped for,<BR>expected, considered &c.; desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षितव्य
अपेक्ष्य, --क्षितव्य, --क्षणीय pot. p. To<BR>be desired, wanted, hoped for,<BR>expected, considered &c.; desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षणीय|अपेक्षणीयं
अपेक्ष्य, --क्षितव्य, --क्षणीय pot. p. To<BR>be desired, wanted, hoped for,<BR>expected, considered &c.; desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षित
अपेक्षित p. p. Looked for,<BR>expected; wanted, desired, required;<BR>considered, referred to &c.<BR>--तं<BR>Desire, wish; regard, reference,<BR>consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेक्षिन्
अपेक्षिन् a. Hoping, waiting for,<BR>wishing or desiring for, wanting;<BR>considering, caring; usually as last<BR>member of comp.; गुरुर्विधिबलापेक्षी<BR>R. 15. 85; प्रयोजनापोक्षितया Ku. 3. 1<BR>according to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेय|अपेयं
अपेय a. Not fit to be drunk;<BR>अपेयेषु तडागेषु बहुतरमुदकं भवति Mk. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपेहि
अपेहि (Imper. 2nd sing.). Used<BR>as the first member of some<BR>compounds (belonging to the class<BR>मयूरव्यंसकादि P. II. 1. 72); ˚करा, ˚द्वितीया,<BR>˚प्रकसा, ˚वाणिजा, ˚स्वागता where it has<BR>the sense of ‘excluding,’ ‘expelling’,<BR>‘refusing admission to’; e. g. ˚वाणिजा a<BR>ceremony where merchants are<BR>excluded; so ˚द्वितीया &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वाता<BR>N. of a plant which expels wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोगंडः|अपोगण्ड|अपोगण्डः
अपोगंडः [अ-पोगंडः, or अपसि (वैध)<BR>कर्मणि गंडः त्याज्यः Tv.]<BR>1 Having a<BR>limb too many or too few (redundant<BR>or deficient).<BR>--2 Not under 16 years<BR>of age; बाल आषोडशाद्वर्षात्पोगंडश्चापि संज्ञितः ।<BR>Nārada; Ms. 8. 148; पोगंडः<BR>पंचमादब्दादर्वाक् च दशमाब्दतः ।<BR>--3 A child or infant<BR>(किशोर, शिशु)<BR>--4 Very timid;<BR>--5<BR>Wrinkled, flaccid.<BR>--6 One past 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोढ
अपोढ See under अप-वह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदक
अपोदक a. Ved.<BR>1 Waterless;<BR>water-tight (नौः Rv. 1. 116. 3).<BR>--2<BR>Not watery, not fluid.<BR>--कं [<BR>अपकृष्टमुदकं यस्मात्] Poison &c. that removes<BR>water (जलापकर्षहेतुविषादि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोदिका
अपोदिका f. A sort of potherb (<BR>अपनद्धमुदकं यस्याः, तत्फलेषूदकवत्त्वात्तथात्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह्
अपोह् {c1c} U. [अप-उह् or ऊह्]<BR>1 To<BR>remove, drive or push away, dispel,<BR>take away, destroy; स हि<BR>विघ्नानपोहति Ś. 3. 1; कुसुमानि… प्रभवंत्यायुरपोहितुं<BR>यदि R. 8. 44, 54; पूर्वमुत्सवमपौहदुत्सवः<BR>(उत्तरः) 19. 5 pushed away,<BR>displaced, supplanted; V. 3. 10;<BR>अकिंचिदपि कुर्वाणः सौख्यैर्दुःखान्यपोहति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">Page0120-b+ 56</a>]<BR>U. 2. 19 removes; Bk. 17. 83;<BR>15. 119; Ms. 8. 414, 11. 108; कल्पनाया<BR>अपोढः कल्पनापोढः P. II. 1. 38 Sk.<BR>removed from, or beyond,<BR>imagination.<BR>--2 To heal, cure (as illness).<BR>--3 To avoid, give up, leave;<BR>Ms. 10. 86; पंचवट्यां ततो रामः…<BR>अनपोढस्थितिस्तस्थौ R. 12. 31 not leaving<BR>(the path of) propriety.<BR>--4 To deny;<BR>स्थाप्यतेऽपोह्यते वा चेत् S. D. 730.<BR>--5 To<BR>reason, argue by way of opposing<BR>a statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहः|अपोह
अपोहः<BR>1 Removing, driving<BR>away, healing &c.<BR>--2 Removal of<BR>doubt by the exercise of the<BR>reasoning faculty.<BR>--3 Reasoning, arguing;<BR>reasoning faculty.<BR>--4 Negative<BR>reasoning (opp. ऊह) (अपरतर्कनिरासाय कृतो<BR>विपरीतस्तर्कः), one of the dhīgunas q. v.;<BR>स्वयमूहापोहासमर्थः Mbh.;<BR>ऊहापोहमिमं सरोजनयना यावद्विधत्तेतरां<BR>Bv. 2. 74; hence ऊहापोह = complete<BR>discussion of a question.<BR>--5 Excluding<BR>all things not coming under the<BR>category in point; तद्वानपोहो वा शब्दार्थः<BR>(where Maheśvara paraphrases<BR>अपोह by अतद्व्यावृत्ति i. e. तद्भिन्नत्यागः)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहनं|अपोहन
अपोहनं<BR>1 Removal &c. = अपोह<BR>above.<BR>--2 Reasoning faculty; मत्तः<BR>स्मृतिर्ज्ञानमपोहनं च Bg. 15. 15 (Mr.<BR>Telang translates अ˚ by removal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोह्य
अपोह्य, अपोहनीय pot. p. To be<BR>removed, taken away, expiated (as<BR>sin); to be established by reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपोहनीय
अपोह्य, अपोहनीय pot. p. To be<BR>removed, taken away, expiated (as<BR>sin); to be established by reason.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौरुष
अपौरुष --पौरुषेय a.<BR>1 Unmanly,<BR>cowardly, timid.<BR>--2 Superhuman,<BR>not of the authorship of man, of<BR>divine origin; अपोरुषेया वेदाः;<BR>अपौरुषेयप्रतिष्ठः सुवर्णबिंदुरित्याख्यायते Māl. 9.<BR>not set up by (the hand of) man.<BR>--षं, --षेयं<BR>1 Cowardice,<BR>pussilanimity.<BR>--2 Superhuman power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अपौरुषेय
अपौरुष --पौरुषेय a.<BR>1 Unmanly,<BR>cowardly, timid.<BR>--2 Superhuman,<BR>not of the authorship of man, of<BR>divine origin; अपोरुषेया वेदाः;<BR>अपौरुषेयप्रतिष्ठः सुवर्णबिंदुरित्याख्यायते Māl. 9.<BR>not set up by (the hand of) man.<BR>--षं, --षेयं<BR>1 Cowardice,<BR>pussilanimity.<BR>--2 Superhuman power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्त|अप्तः
अप्त a. Ved. Obtained; watery (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तस्
अप्तस् n. A sacrificial act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तु|अप्तुः
अप्तु a. Ved. Busy, active,<BR>industrious.<BR>--प्तुः (or n. Uṇ. 1. 74)<BR>1 The<BR>body.<BR>--2 Soma (सूक्ष्मरूपसोम).<BR>--3 A<BR>sacrificial animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तुर्
अप्तुर् m. [अद्भ्यः जलदानाय तुतोर्ति,<BR>जलानि प्रेरयति, तुर् क्विप् Tv.]<BR>1 Active,<BR>busy, giving water, flowing as water;<BR>an epithet of Indra (Sāy. अपां प्रेरक<BR>इंद्रः).<BR>--2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तु|अप्तुः
अप्तु --प्तूर्यं [अप्तुरो भावः बाहु ˚वेदे यत्]<BR>Sending down water (वृष्टिप्रेरकत्वं),<BR>giving of water; zeal (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तूर्यं|अप्तूर्य
अप्तु --प्तूर्यं [अप्तुरो भावः बाहु ˚वेदे यत्]<BR>Sending down water (वृष्टिप्रेरकत्वं),<BR>giving of water; zeal (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तोर्यामः|अप्तोर्याम
अप्तोर्यामः, --मन् m. N. of a sacrifice<BR>and of a verse of the Sāma Veda<BR>closing that rite; the last or 7th<BR>part of the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्तोर्यामन्
अप्तोर्यामः, --मन् m. N. of a sacrifice<BR>and of a verse of the Sāma Veda<BR>closing that rite; the last or 7th<BR>part of the Jyotiṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्त्य
अप्त्य a. [अप्तुनि देहे भवः यत् वेदे<BR>टिलोपः Tv.]<BR>1 Engaged in an act, active<BR>(देहकर्मणि स्थित).<BR>--2 Offspring (अपत्य<BR>Nir.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नः|अप्न
अप्नः, अप्नस् n. [आप् --असुन् नुट्<BR>थस्वश्च, Uṇ. 4. 207]<BR>1 Possession,<BR>property.<BR>--2 Work, sacrificial act or<BR>rite, any act.<BR>--3 Offspring.<BR>--4 Form,<BR>shape.<BR>--5 To be obtained (used<BR>actively); [cf. L. ops.]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थ a.<BR>superintending work (कर्मण्यधिकृत);<BR>(or m.) proprietor of an estate.<BR>--राजः<BR>lord of wealth or property,<BR>illustrious by means of works; directing<BR>works to be done (कर्मप्रेरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नस्
अप्नः, अप्नस् n. [आप् --असुन् नुट्<BR>थस्वश्च, Uṇ. 4. 207]<BR>1 Possession,<BR>property.<BR>--2 Work, sacrificial act or<BR>rite, any act.<BR>--3 Offspring.<BR>--4 Form,<BR>shape.<BR>--5 To be obtained (used<BR>actively); [cf. L. ops.]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थ a.<BR>superintending work (कर्मण्यधिकृत);<BR>(or m.) proprietor of an estate.<BR>--राजः<BR>lord of wealth or property,<BR>illustrious by means of works; directing<BR>works to be done (कर्मप्रेरक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नवान|अप्नवानः
अप्नवान a.<BR>1 Having progeny.<BR>--2<BR>Poor.<BR>--नः [अप्नसे आदायकर्मणे वानं<BR>यस्यपृषो ˚सलोपः Tv.]<BR>1 The arm.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>a Ṛṣi in the family of or<BR>connected with Bhṛgu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्नस्वत्|अप्नस्वन्त्
अप्नस्वत् a. Having(sacrificial)<BR>acts or works; productive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पति|अप्पतिः
अप्पति, अप्पित्तं see under अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्पित्तं|अप्पित्त
अप्पति, अप्पित्तं see under अप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्य
अप्य a. [अपां इदं तत्रसाधु संस्कृतं वा<BR>यत्; अद्भिः संस्कृतं P. IV. 4. 134]<BR>1<BR>Connected with or coming from water<BR>Rv. 2. 38. 7; watery; consisting of,<BR>consecrated with, water (as हविः).<BR>--2<BR>Obtainable.<BR>--3 Active, connected<BR>with sacrificial acts 1. 145. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्यदीक्षितः|अप्यदीक्षित
अप्यदीक्षितः N. of a celebrated<BR>Draviḍa writer, author of works on<BR>Alaṃkāra and other subjects and<BR>a contemporary of Paṇḍita<BR>Jagannātha who lived in the 16th<BR>century (written also as अप्ययादीक्षित.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्यंच्
अप्यंच् [fr. अंच्] Gone into,<BR>reaching, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्यय|अप्ययः
अप्यय &c. see under अपी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्यर्धं|अप्यर्ध
अप्यर्धं ind. Ved. Near, in the<BR>neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकंप|अप्रकम्प
अप्रकंप a.<BR>1 Unshaken (fig. also),<BR>firm, steady.<BR>--2 Unanswerable (as<BR>argument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकर
अप्रकर a. Not acting well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकरणं|अप्रकरण
अप्रकरणं Not the main or<BR>principal topic, incidental or irrelevant<BR>matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकल्पक
अप्रकल्पक a. Not explicitly<BR>enjoining, not prescribing as<BR>obligatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकांड|अप्रकाण्ड|अप्रकाण्डः
अप्रकांड a. Stemless(small).<BR>--डः A bush, a shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाश|अप्रकाशः
अप्रकाश a.<BR>1 Not shining or<BR>bright, dark, wanting in<BR>brightness (fig. also); प्रकाशश्चाप्रकाशश्च<BR>लोकालोकं इवाचलः R. 1. 68.<BR>--2<BR>Selfilluminated.<BR>--3 Hidden, secret,<BR>concealed; Ms. 8. 251; 9. 256.<BR>--शं, --शे<BR>ind. In secret, secretly; अहमप्रकाशे<BR>तिष्ठामि M. 4; सत्यवत्या हस्तेऽप्रकाशं<BR>निक्षिप्तः V. 5 secretly.<BR>--शः<BR>Indistinctness, secrecy; a secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाशक
अप्रकाशक a. Making dark; not<BR>disclosing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकाश्य
अप्रकाश्य a. Not to be disclosed,<BR>to be kept secret (one of 9 such<BR>things); जन्मर्क्षं मैथुनं मंत्रो गृहच्छिद्रं च<BR>वंचनं । आयुर्धनापमानं स्त्री न प्रकाश्यानि सर्वथा ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृत|अप्रकृतः
अप्रकृत a.<BR>1 Not principal or<BR>chief, incidental, occasional.<BR>--2 Not<BR>relevant to the subject under<BR>discussion, not to the point, irrelevant;<BR>see प्रकृत, प्रस्तुत; अप्रकृतं अनुसंधा ‘to<BR>beat about the bush’, not to come<BR>to the point.<BR>--तं (In Rhet.) उपमान<BR>i. e. the standard of comparison<BR>(opp. प्रकृत or उपमेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृतिः|अप्रकृति
अप्रकृतिः f.<BR>1 Not the inherent or<BR>natural property, accidental<BR>property or nature; an accident (विकृति).<BR>--2 Spiritual being; the Puruṣa of<BR>the Sāṃkhyas.<BR>--3 Not the original<BR>word; such as a termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रकृष्ट|अप्रकृष्टः
अप्रकृष्ट a. Not excelled, low,<BR>vile.<BR>--ष्टः A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रक्षित
अप्रक्षित a. Undecayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगम
अप्रगम a. Going too fast to be<BR>followed by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगल्भ
अप्रगल्भ a. Not bold, bashful,<BR>modest (opp. धृष्ट); धृष्टः पार्श्वे वसति<BR>नियतं दूरतश्चाप्रगल्भः H. 2. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रगुण|अप्रगुणः
अप्रगुण a. Perplexed, confounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रग्राह
अप्रग्राह a. Unrestrained,<BR>unbridled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रचंकश|अप्रचङ्कश
अप्रचंकश a. Ved. Without the<BR>power of seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रचेतस्
अप्रचेतस् a. Ved. Deficient in<BR>understanding, foolish, stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रच्छेद्य
अप्रच्छेद्य a. Inscrutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रच्युत
अप्रच्युत a. Unmoved, not<BR>swerving from, following, observing<BR>(with abl.); Ms. 12. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रज
अप्रज a.<BR>1 Without progeny,<BR>childless; शोच्यं मैथुनमप्रजं Chāṇ. 57.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">Page0121-b+ 54</a>]<BR>Unborn.<BR>--3 Unpeopled.<BR>--जा<BR>Having no child, not giving birth to<BR>children, not prolific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजस्
अप्रजस्, अप्रजात a. Childless,<BR>having no issue or progeny;<BR>अतीतायामप्रजसि बांधवास्तदवाप्नुयुः Y. 2. 144.<BR>--ता A woman who has borne no<BR>child, a barren woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजात
अप्रजस्, अप्रजात a. Childless,<BR>having no issue or progeny;<BR>अतीतायामप्रजसि बांधवास्तदवाप्नुयुः Y. 2. 144.<BR>--ता A woman who has borne no<BR>child, a barren woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रजज्ञि
अप्रजज्ञि a. Ved.<BR>1 Inexperienced,<BR>unskilful.<BR>--2 Childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रणीत
अप्रणीत a. Unconsecrated,<BR>vulgar, profane.<BR>--तं Frying clarified<BR>butter without consecrated water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतर्क्य
अप्रतर्क्य a. Incomprehensible by<BR>reason or inference, undefinable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रता
अप्रता a. Ved. Very great or<BR>extensive, affluent Rv. 8. 32. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतापः|अप्रताप
अप्रतापः<BR>1 Want of lustre,<BR>dulness, dimness.<BR>--2 Meanness, want<BR>of dignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रति
अप्रति a. Ved.<BR>1 Without<BR>opponents or foes, irresistible;<BR>Rv. 5. 32. 3; ˚वीर्य of irresistible prowess.<BR>--2 Unsurpassed, unequalled. --adv.<BR>Irresistibly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकर|अप्रतिकरः
अप्रतिकर a. Trusting, trusty,<BR>confidential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकर्मन्|अप्रतिकर्म्मन्
अप्रतिकर्मन् a.<BR>1 Of unequalled<BR>deeds or achievements.<BR>--2<BR>Irresistible, irremediable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिकार|अप्रतिकारः
अप्रति(ती)कार a.<BR>Irremediable, helpless, that cannot be<BR>remedied or helped; ˚रेयमापदुपस्थिता<BR>K. 154.<BR>--रः Not remedying,<BR>nonrequital, non-retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीकार
अप्रति(ती)कार a.<BR>Irremediable, helpless, that cannot be<BR>remedied or helped; ˚रेयमापदुपस्थिता<BR>K. 154.<BR>--रः Not remedying,<BR>nonrequital, non-retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिगृह्य
अप्रतिगृह्य a. One from whom<BR>one must not accept any thing as<BR>a gift &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिग्राहक
अप्रतिग्राहक a. Not accepting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिग्राह्य
अप्रतिग्राह्य a. Unacceptable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिघ
अप्रतिघ a.<BR>1 Not to be<BR>vanquished, invincible.<BR>--2 Not to be<BR>warded or kept off; रजः Ms. 12. 28.<BR>--3<BR>Not angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिद्वंद्व|अप्रतिद्वन्द्व
अप्रतिद्वंद्व a.<BR>1 Having no<BR>adversary in battle, irresistible.<BR>--2<BR>Unsurpassed, unrivalled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिधुर
अप्रतिधुर a. Without the<BR>fellowhorse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपक्ष|अप्रतिपक्षः
अप्रतिपक्ष a.<BR>1 Without a rival<BR>or opponent.<BR>--2 Unlike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपत्तिः|अप्रतिपत्ति
अप्रतिपत्तिः f.<BR>1<BR>Non-performance, non-acceptance.<BR>--2 Neglect,<BR>omission, disregard.<BR>--3 Want of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">Page0121-c+ 55</a>]<BR>understanding.<BR>--4 Absence of<BR>determination (what to do), perplexity;<BR>˚विह्वल &c. K. 159; (अप्रतिपत्तिर्जडता<BR>स्यादिष्टानिष्टदर्शनश्रुतिभिः);<BR>˚त्तिसाध्वसजडा K. 240; Ki. 14. 43.<BR>--5 (Hence)<BR>absence of mind or ready wit (<BR>स्फूर्त्यभाव); उत्तरस्याप्रतिपत्तिरप्रतिभा Gaut. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिपद्
अप्रतिपद् a. Not going(विकल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिबंध|अप्रतिबन्ध
अप्रतिबंध a.<BR>1 Unimpeded,<BR>unobstructed.<BR>--2 Direct, undisputed;<BR>(in law) got by birth without any<BR>obstruction, not collateral (as<BR>inheritance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिबल
अप्रतिबल a. Of irresistible<BR>might, of unequalled power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिभ|अप्रतिभः
अप्रतिभ a.<BR>1 Modest, bashful.<BR>--2<BR>Not ready-witted, dull.<BR>--भा<BR>Bashfulness, modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिभट|अप्रतिभटः
अप्रतिभट a. Unrivalled.<BR>--टः An:<BR>unrivalled warrior; आत्मानं ˚टं<BR>मन्यमानः Dk. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिम
अप्रतिम a. Without an equal or<BR>parallel, incomparable, matchless,<BR>unrivalled; so अप्रतिमान; ˚नमोजः<BR>Mv. 1. 62; ˚रूपत्वं; ˚वीर्य, ˚बुद्धि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतियत्नः|अप्रतियत्न
अप्रतियत्नः Natural or<BR>spontaneous state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतियोगिन्
अप्रतियोगिन् a.<BR>1 Without an<BR>adversary.<BR>--2 Having no opposite<BR>or counterpart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरथ|अप्रतिरथं|अप्रतिरथः
अप्रतिरथ a. or<BR>--थः<BR>1 (A hero) who<BR>has no प्रतिरथ or rival warrior, a<BR>matchless or unrivalled warrior;<BR>दौष्यंतिमप्रतिरथं तनयं निवेश्य Ś. 4. 19,<BR>Ś. 7, 7. 33.<BR>--2 Matchless Mv. 1. 46.<BR>--थः N. of a Ṛṣi.<BR>--थः, --थं N. of a<BR>hymn composed by अ˚; यद्यात्रामंगलं<BR>साम तदप्रतिरथं विदुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरव
अप्रतिरव a. Uncontested,<BR>undisputed; वर्षशताधिकभोगः संततोऽप्रतिरवः<BR>स्वत्वं गमयति Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिरूप
अप्रतिरूप a.<BR>1 Not<BR>corresponding with, unfit.<BR>--2 Of unequalled<BR>form.<BR>--3 Incomparable (in a good or<BR>bad sense).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कथा<BR>incomparable talk (संगणिका), उत्तरवाक्यरहिता<BR>वाक्.<BR>--वीर्यं irresistible power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिवीर्य|अप्रतिवीर्य्य
अप्रतिवीर्य a. Of incomparable<BR>prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिशासन
अप्रतिशासन a. Having no rival<BR>ruler, subject to one rule; R. 8. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठ|अप्रतिष्ठः
अप्रतिष्ठ a.<BR>1 Not stable or firmly<BR>fixed, fluctuating, not made<BR>permanent; U. 5. 25.<BR>--2 Thrown away,<BR>unprofitable, useless; Ms. 3. 180.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">Page0122-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--3 Disreputable, infamous.<BR>--ष्ठः N.<BR>of a hell.<BR>--ष्ठा Instability, ill-fame,<BR>ill-repute, dishonour.<BR>--ष्ठं Brahma<BR>(स्वधामप्रतिष्ठितं ब्रह्म).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठान
अप्रतिष्ठान a. Ved. Not firm,<BR>having no solid ground.<BR>--नं<BR>Instability, want of solidity or firmness (fig.<BR>also); तर्काप्रतिष्ठानादप्यन्यथानुमेयं Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिष्ठित|अप्रतिष्ठितः
अप्रतिष्ठित a. Unsettled, unfixed,<BR>uncelebrated, obscure;<BR>unconsecrated, unholy.<BR>--तः An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिसंक्रम|अप्रतिसङ्क्रम
अप्रतिसंक्रम a. Having no<BR>intermixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिसंख्य|अप्रतिसङ्ख्य
अप्रतिसंख्य a. Unobserved,<BR>unnoticed; ˚ख्य (ख्या) निरोधः unobserved<BR>nullity, annihilation of an object;<BR>one of the three topics included by<BR>the Buddhas under the category of<BR>निरूप, the other two being<BR>प्रतिसंख्यानिरोध wilful destruction, as of a jar by<BR>a mallet, and आकाश the ethereal<BR>element.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतिहत
अप्रतिहत a.<BR>1 Not obstructed or<BR>impeded, irresistible; ˚हतान् पुत्रान्<BR>K. 62; अस्मदगृहे ˚गतिः Pt. 1 free<BR>to move; U. 3. 36;<BR>जृंभतामप्रतिहतप्रसरमार्यस्य क्रोधज्योतिः Ve. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Unimpaired, unmarred, unrepulsed,<BR>unaffected, at home in every respect;<BR>सा बुद्धिरप्रतिहता Bh. 2. 40; Pt. 5. 26;<BR>so ˚चित्त, ˚मनस्.<BR>--3 Not disappointed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नेत्र a. of unimpaired<BR>eyes.<BR>--(त्रः) N. of a Buddhist deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीक
अप्रतीक a. Without parts or<BR>body, epithet of Brahma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीत
अप्रतीत a.<BR>1 Not pleased or<BR>delighted.<BR>--2 Unapproached;<BR>unassailable.<BR>--3 Unopposed.<BR>--4 (In<BR>Rhet.) Not understood or clearly<BR>intelligible (as a word), one of the<BR>defects of a word (शब्ददोष);<BR>अप्रतीतं यत्केवले शास्त्रे प्रसिद्धं K. P. 7, i. e. a<BR>word is said to be अप्रतीत if it be<BR>used in a sense which it has in<BR>particular classes of works only<BR>(and not in general or popular use);<BR>e. g. सम्यग्ज्ञानमहाज्योतिर्दलिताशयताजुषः<BR>(where आशय = वासना occurs in Yoga<BR>Śāstra only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतीतिः|अप्रतीति
अप्रतीतिः f. Unintelligibleness;<BR>mistrust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रतुलः|अप्रतुल|अप्रतुलं
अप्रतुलः<BR>1 Want of weight.<BR>--2<BR>Want, necessity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्त
अप्रत्त(˚प्रदत्त) Not given away.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">Page0122-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--त्ता A girl, one not given away in<BR>marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रदत्त
अप्रत्त(˚प्रदत्त) Not given away.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">Page0122-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--त्ता A girl, one not given away in<BR>marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यक्ष|अप्रत्यक्षः
अप्रत्यक्ष a.<BR>1 Invisible,<BR>imperceptible.<BR>--2 Unknown.<BR>--3 Absent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शिष्ट a. not distinctly<BR>taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यय|अप्रत्ययः
अप्रत्यय a.<BR>1 Diffident,<BR>distrustful (with loc.); बलवदपि<BR>शिक्षितानामात्मन्यप्रत्ययं चेतः Ś. 1. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Having no knowledge.<BR>--3 (In gram.)<BR>Having no affix.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Diffidence,<BR>distrust, disbelief, doubt;<BR>क्षेत्रमप्रत्ययानां Pt. 1. 191.<BR>--2 Not being<BR>understood.<BR>--3 Not an affix;<BR>अर्थवदधातुरप्रत्ययः प्रातिपदिकं P. I. 2. 45.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थ a. (in gram.) not pertaining<BR>to an affix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रत्यृत
अप्रत्यृत a. Not attacked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रदक्षिणं
अप्रदक्षिणं ind. From the left to<BR>the right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रदुग्ध
अप्रदुग्ध a. Ved. Not milked<BR>completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधान|अप्रधानं
अप्रधान a. Subordinate,<BR>secondary, inferior; आवां तावदप्रधानौ H. 2.<BR>--नं (˚ता, ˚त्वं)<BR>1 Subordinate or<BR>secondary state, inferiority.<BR>--2 A<BR>secondary or subordinate act. (The<BR>word अप्रधान usually occurs in the<BR>neuter gender either by itself, or as<BR>an attribute to a noun, or as last<BR>member of comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रधृष्य
अप्रधृष्य a. Unconquerable,<BR>invincible; यदाश्रौषं भीष्ममत्यंतशूरं हतं<BR>पार्थेनाहवेष्वप्रधृष्यं Mb.; यस्याप्रधृष्यः<BR>प्रभवस्त्वमुच्चैः M. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रपदनं|अप्रपदन
अप्रपदनं Ved. A bad place of<BR>refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभ
अप्रभ a.<BR>1 Obscure, dull.<BR>--2<BR>Mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभु
अप्रभु a.<BR>1 Wanting power, not<BR>powerful.<BR>--2 Having no power or<BR>control over, unable, incompetent;<BR>with gen. or loc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रभूतिः|अप्रभूति
अप्रभूतिः f. Little effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमत्त|अप्रमत्तः
अप्रमत्त a. Not careless or<BR>inattentive, careful, attentive,<BR>vigilant, watchful; Ms. 7. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमद
अप्रमद a. Devoid of festivities,<BR>sad, joyless; Bk. 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाद|अप्रमादः
अप्रमाद a. Careful, vigilant,<BR>cautious, steady.<BR>--दः Care, attention,<BR>vigilance.<BR>--दं ind. Carefully,<BR>attentively, uninterruptedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमय
अप्रमय a. Imperishable;<BR>unlimited (अप्रमेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमा
अप्रमा Incorrect knowledge (opp.<BR>प्रमा q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमाण
अप्रमाण a.<BR>1 Unlimited,<BR>immeasurable, boundless.<BR>--2 Without<BR>authority, proof or weight,<BR>unauthorized.<BR>--3 Not regarded as an<BR>authority, not trustworthy; आजन्मनः<BR>शाव्यमशिक्षितो यस्तस्याप्रमाणं वचनं<BR>जनस्य Ś. 5. 25.<BR>--णं<BR>1 That which<BR>cannot be taken as authority in<BR>actions; i. e. a rule, direction &c. which<BR>cannot be accepted as obligatory.<BR>--2 Irrelevancy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आभः,<BR>शुभः (pl.) ‘of unlimited lustre’, N.<BR>of a class of deities (with<BR>Buddhists).<BR>--विद् a. not conversant<BR>with evidence, or incapable of<BR>weighing evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमायुक
अप्रमायुक a. [प्र-मि-उण् आत्त्वे युच्,<BR>स्वार्थे कन् Tv.] Not dying suddenly,<BR>very long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमित
अप्रमित a.<BR>1 Not measured,<BR>unlimited.<BR>--2 Not proved or<BR>established by authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमूर
अप्रमूर, अप्रमूर्च्छित a. Not<BR>foolish, prudent, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमूर्च्छित
अप्रमूर, अप्रमूर्च्छित a. Not<BR>foolish, prudent, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमृष्य
अप्रमृष्य a. Indestructible,<BR>unassailable (अबाध्यं) Rv. 6. 20. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमेय
अप्रमेय a.<BR>1 Immeasurable,<BR>unbounded, boundless; ˚महिमा<BR>Mv. 4. 30.<BR>--2 That which cannot be<BR>properly ascertained, understood &c.;<BR>inscrutable, unfathomable (of person<BR>or thing); अचिंत्यस्याप्रमेयस्य<BR>कार्यतत्त्वार्थवित्प्रभुः Ms. 1. 3; 12. 94.<BR>--3<BR>Not to be proved or demonstrated<BR>(as Brahma).<BR>--यं Brahma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुभाव a. of unlimited might.<BR>--आत्मन् ‘of inscrutable spirit,’<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमोदः|अप्रमोद|अप्रमोदं
अप्रमोदः --दं<BR>1 Inability to remove<BR>pain.<BR>--2 Absence of delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रमोदं|अप्रमोद|अप्रमोदः
अप्रमोदः --दं<BR>1 Inability to remove<BR>pain.<BR>--2 Absence of delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयत्न|अप्रयत्नः
अप्रयत्न a. Not energetic or<BR>diligent, indifferent, apathetic, not<BR>zealously devoted to (with loc.);<BR>˚त्नः सुखार्थेषु Ms. 6. 26.<BR>--त्नः Absence<BR>of effort or exertion, indifference,<BR>apathy, laziness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयाणिः|अप्रयाणि
अप्रयाणिः f. [अ-प्रया-अनि<BR>P. III. 3. 112, न changed to ण by<BR>P. VIII. 4. 29] Not going or progressing<BR>(used only in uttering imprecations);<BR>अप्रयाणिस्ते शठ भूयात् Sk. mayest<BR>thou not move onward or progress!<BR>See अजीवनि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयापणि
अप्रयापणि --निः f. Not allowing to<BR>go on or progress (P. III. 3. 112;<BR>VIII. 4. 30).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयापनिः
अप्रयापणि --निः f. Not allowing to<BR>go on or progress (P. III. 3. 112;<BR>VIII. 4. 30).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयावं
अप्रयावं adv. Without<BR>interruption, attentively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयुच्चत्
अप्रयुच्चत्, अप्रयुत, अप्रयुत्वन् a.<BR>Ved. Unceasing, continual, not<BR>separated (अपृथग्भूत); careful, attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयुत
अप्रयुच्चत्, अप्रयुत, अप्रयुत्वन् a.<BR>Ved. Unceasing, continual, not<BR>separated (अपृथग्भूत); careful, attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयुत्वन्
अप्रयुच्चत्, अप्रयुत, अप्रयुत्वन् a.<BR>Ved. Unceasing, continual, not<BR>separated (अपृथग्भूत); careful, attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयुक्त
अप्रयुक्त a.<BR>1 Not used or<BR>employed, not applied.<BR>--2 Wrongly<BR>used, as a word.<BR>--3 (In Rhet.) Rare,<BR>unusual (as a word when used in<BR>a particular sense or gender though<BR>that sense or gender be sanctioned<BR>by lexicographers); अप्रयुक्तं<BR>तथाम्नातमपि कविभिर्नादृतं; तथा मन्ये दैवतोस्य पिशाचो<BR>राक्षसोऽथवा । where the mas. gender<BR>of दैवत, though sanctioned (by<BR>Amara), is not used by poets and<BR>is, therefore, अप्रयुक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रयोगः|अप्रयोग
अप्रयोगः Non-application or bad<BR>application, non-employment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रलंब|अप्रलम्ब|अप्रलम्बं
अप्रलंब a. Prompt, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्तक|अप्रवर्त्तक
अप्रवर्तक, अप्रवर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Not<BR>exciting or stimulating to action, inert,<BR>abstaining from action.<BR>--2<BR>Continuous, unbroken, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्तिन्|अप्रवर्त्तिन्
अप्रवर्तक, अप्रवर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Not<BR>exciting or stimulating to action, inert,<BR>abstaining from action.<BR>--2<BR>Continuous, unbroken, uninterrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवर्तनं|अप्रवर्तन|अप्रवर्त्तन
अप्रवर्तनं Not engaging in, not<BR>exciting to any action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवृत्तिः|अप्रवृत्ति
अप्रवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Not engaging in<BR>action or proceeding, not taking place.<BR>--2 Inertia, inactivity,<BR>non-excitement, absence of incentive or<BR>stimulus.<BR>--3 (In medic.) Suppression of<BR>the natural evacuations,<BR>constipation, ischury &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवीत
अप्रवीत a. Ved. Not approached<BR>Rv. 4. 7. 9.<BR>--ता<BR>1 Not loved<BR>(अकामिता).<BR>--2 Not impregnated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रवेद
अप्रवेद a. Difficult to be found.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रशस्त|अप्रशस्तं
अप्रशस्त a.<BR>1 Not<BR>praiseworthy, worthless, contemptible.<BR>--2<BR>Not approved, forbidden.<BR>--3 (Ved.)<BR>Disobedient.<BR>--4 Less, deficient,<BR>decayed (क्षीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसक्त
अप्रसक्त a.<BR>1 Not attached or<BR>addicted, moderate, temperate.<BR>--2<BR>Unconnected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसक्तिः|अप्रसक्ति
अप्रसक्तिः f. Non-attachment,<BR>moderation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसंगः|अप्रसङ्ग|अप्रसंग|अप्रसङ्गः
अप्रसंगः<BR>1 Want of attachment.<BR>--2 Want of connection.<BR>--3<BR>Inopportune time or occasion; अप्रसंगाभिधाने<BR>च श्रोतुः श्रद्धा न जायते ।<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसन्न|अप्रसन्नं
अप्रसन्न a.<BR>1 Not pleased.<BR>--2<BR>Turbid, muddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसादः|अप्रसाद
अप्रसादः Disfavour, displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसव|अप्रसवः
अप्रसव a. Not being prolific.<BR>--वः Not being born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसूत
अप्रसूत a. Barren, childless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसाह
अप्रसाह a. Not being affected by<BR>evils or ill omens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसिद्ध|अप्रसिद्धं
अप्रसिद्ध a.<BR>1 Unknown,<BR>unimportant, insignificant, Ku. 3. 19.<BR>--2<BR>Unusual, uncommon; ˚पदं an<BR>obsolete word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रसिद्धिः|अप्रसिद्धि
अप्रसिद्धिः f. Obscurity,<BR>insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्ताविक
अप्रस्ताविक a. (की f.) Not<BR>belonging to the subject matter,<BR>irrelevant (= अप्रारताविक q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रस्तुत|अप्रस्तुतं
अप्रस्तुत a.<BR>1 Unsuitable to the<BR>time or subject, not to the point,<BR>irrelevant.<BR>--2 Absurd, nonsensical;<BR>रे गोरंभ किमप्रस्तुतं लपसि Pt. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Accidental or extraneous.<BR>--4 Not ready.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रशंसा a figure of speech<BR>which, by describing the अप्रस्तुत (what<BR>is not the subject matter) conveys<BR>a reference to the प्रस्तुत or<BR>subjectmatter; अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा सा या सैव<BR>प्रस्तुताश्रया K. P. 10. It is of 5 kinds:<BR>--कार्ये<BR>निमित्ते सामान्ये विशेषे प्रस्तुते सति । तदन्यस्य<BR>वचस्तुल्ये तुल्यस्येति च पंचधा ॥ i. e. when<BR>the subject matter is viewed (a) as<BR>an effect, information of which is<BR>conveyed by stating the cause; (b)<BR>when viewed as a cause by stating<BR>the effect; (c) when viewed as a<BR>general assertion by stating a<BR>particular instance; (d) when viewed<BR>as a particular instance by stating<BR>a general assertion; and (e) when<BR>viewed as similar by stating what is<BR>similar to it, see K. P. 10; and<BR>S. D. 706 for examples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहत|अप्रहतं
अप्रहत a.<BR>1 Unhurt, intact.<BR>--2<BR>Waste, unploughed, K. 326.<BR>--3 New<BR>and unbleached (as cloth); ईषद्धौतं<BR>नवं श्वेतं सदशं यंत्रधारितम् । निर्णेजकाक्षालितं<BR>चाप्रहतं वास उच्यते ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहन्
अप्रहन् a. Not destroying,<BR>favouring, aiding (अनुग्राहक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रहित
अप्रहित a.<BR>1 Not sent out.<BR>--2<BR>Unattacked by foes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राकरणिक
अप्राकरणिक a. (की f.) Not<BR>belonging to the subject matter;<BR>अप्राकरणिकस्याभिधानेन<BR>प्राकरणिकस्याक्षेपोऽप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राकृत
अप्राकृत a.<BR>1 Not vulgar.<BR>--2<BR>Not original.<BR>--3 Not ordinary,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">Page0123-c+ 56</a>]<BR>extraordinary; ˚आकृतीनां K. 174,<BR>Mv. 1. 3.<BR>--4 Special.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राग्र्य|अप्राग्र्यं
अप्राग्र्य a. Secondary,<BR>subordinate; inferior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राचीन|अप्राचीनं
अप्राचीन a.<BR>1 Modern.<BR>--2 Not<BR>eastern, western.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राण|अप्राणः
अप्राण a. Lifeless; inanimate.<BR>--णः The Almighty Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्त|अप्राप्तः
अप्राप्त a.<BR>1 Not obtained or got;<BR>अप्राप्तयोस्तु या प्राप्तिः सैव संयोग ईरितः ।<BR>Bhāṣā P.<BR>--2 Not arrived or come.<BR>--3 Not authorised or following,<BR>as a rule.<BR>--4 Not come to or<BR>reached; R. 12. 96.<BR>--5 Not of a<BR>marriageable age.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काल a. {1}<BR>inopportune, ill-timed, unseasonable;<BR>˚लं वचनं बृहस्पतिरपि ब्रुवना लभते<BR>बुद्ध्यवज्ञानमपमानं च पुष्कलं Pt. 1. 63. {2}<BR>under age.<BR>--(लं) an irregular<BR>discussion (of any subject).<BR>--प्रापक a. {1}<BR>conveying (the sense of) what is not<BR>otherwise specified, such as the use of<BR>the Potential mood in स्वर्गकामो यजेत.<BR>{2} not yet tamed (as a young calf)<BR>--यौवन a. not arrived at puberty<BR>or who has not reached his youth,<BR>R. 15. 42.<BR>--व्यवहार, वयस् a. (in law)<BR>under age, not old enough to<BR>engage in public business on his own<BR>responsibility, a minor (a boy before<BR>he reaches his 16th year);<BR>अप्राप्तव्यवहारोसौ यावत् षोडशवार्षिकः Dakṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्राप्तिः|अप्राप्ति
अप्राप्तिः f.<BR>1 Non-acquisition;<BR>तदप्राप्तिमहादुःखविलीनाशेषपातका<BR>K. P. 4.<BR>--2 Not being proved or<BR>established by a rule before; विधिरत्यंतमप्राप्तौ<BR>नियमः पाक्षिके सति Mīm.<BR>--3 Not taking<BR>place or occurring.<BR>--4 Not being<BR>applicable = अनुपपत्ति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामाणिक|अप्रामाणिकः
अप्रामाणिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Unauthoritative, unwarranted; इदं<BR>वचनमप्रामाणिकं.<BR>--2 Untrustworthy,<BR>unreliable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रामि
अप्रामि a. Ved. Unhurt,<BR>unimpaired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रायत्यं|अप्रायत्य
अप्रायत्यं Ved.<BR>1 Impurity.<BR>--2<BR>Ungovernableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रायु
अप्रायु a. Ved. Not going forth<BR>(अगंतृ) Rv. 1. 89. 1; unceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रायुस्
अप्रायुस् a. Ved. With<BR>undiminished or unimpaired life or vigour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रिय|अप्रियं|अप्रियः
अप्रिय a.<BR>1 Disliked,<BR>disagreeable, unpleasant, offensive अप्रियस्य<BR>च पथ्यस्य वक्ता श्रोता च दुर्लभः Rām.;<BR>Ms. 4. 138; Ś. 5. 17; hated,<BR>distasteful.<BR>--2 Unkind, unfriendly.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">Page0124-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--यः A foe, an enemy.<BR>--या A sort<BR>of fish (शृंगीमत्स्यः).<BR>--यं An<BR>unfriendly or offensive act; पाणिग्राहस्य<BR>साध्वी स्त्री नाचरेत्किंचिदप्रियं Ms. 5. 156.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर, --कारिन्, --कारक a.<BR>unfriendly, ill-disposed.<BR>--भागिन् a.<BR>ill-fated.<BR>--वद, (˚यं˚), --वादिन् a.<BR>speaking unkind or harsh words;<BR>वंध्यार्थघ्न्यप्रियंवदा Y. 1. 73; माता यस्य<BR>गृहे नास्ति भार्या चाप्रियवादिनी Chāṇ. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0123-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रीतिः|अप्रीति
अप्रीतिः f.<BR>1 Dislike, aversion.<BR>--2 Unfriendly feeling, enmity.<BR>--3<BR>Pain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर (--री f.). {1}<BR>unkind; unfavourable. {2}<BR>disagreeable, disliked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रेतराक्षसी
अप्रेतराक्षसी = अपेतराक्षसी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रेमन्
अप्रेमन् a. Disliking, unfriendly.<BR>--n. Dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्रौढ
अप्रौढ^1 a.<BR>1 Not arrogant.<BR>--2<BR>Timid, gentle, not bold.<BR>--3 Not<BR>full-grown.<BR>--ढा<BR>1 An unmarried<BR>girl.<BR>--2 A girl very recently<BR>married and not arrived at puberty or<BR>womanhood.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: missing vowel diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्लव
अप्लव a.<BR>1 Without a ship.<BR>--2<BR>Not swimming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्लुत
अप्लुत a. Not protracted (as a vowel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्व
अप्व a. [आप् बाहु˚ व, पृषो˚ थस्वः]<BR>Attainable.<BR>--प्वा Disease, danger;<BR>the region of the throat or neck (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सः|अप्स
अप्सः --प्सा m.<BR>--(प्साः) Ved.<BR>[अपःसनोति; सन्-ड]<BR>1 Giving or yielding<BR>water; forming the essential portion<BR>of water (अपां सारभूतो रसः).<BR>--2 Not<BR>destroying.<BR>--प्सं Form, see अप्सस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सा
अप्सः --प्सा m.<BR>--(प्साः) Ved.<BR>[अपःसनोति; सन्-ड]<BR>1 Giving or yielding<BR>water; forming the essential portion<BR>of water (अपां सारभूतो रसः).<BR>--2 Not<BR>destroying.<BR>--प्सं Form, see अप्सस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरः|अप्सर
अप्सरः [अप्-सृ-अच्] Any<BR>aquatic animal (moving in water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सरस्
अप्सरस् f.<BR>--(राः --रा). [अद्भ्यः<BR>सरंति उद्गच्छंति, सृ-असुन् Uṇ. 4. 236;<BR>cf. Rām. अप्सु निर्मथनादवे<BR>रसात्तस्माद्वरस्त्रियः । उत्पेतुर्मनुजश्रेष्ठ तस्मादप्सरसोऽभवन्]<BR>1 A class of female divinities or<BR>celestial damsels who reside in the sky<BR>and are regarded as the wives of the<BR>Gandharvas. They are very fond of<BR>bathing, can change their shapes,<BR>and are endowed with superhuman<BR>power (प्रभाव). They are called<BR>स्वर्वेश्याः and are usually described as<BR>the servants of Indra, who, when<BR>alarmed by the rigorous austerities<BR>of some mighty sage, sends down<BR>one of them to disturb his penance,<BR>and her mission is generally<BR>successful; cf. या तपोविशेषपरिशंकितस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-b" target="_blank">Page0124-b+ 57</a>]<BR>सुकुमारं प्रहरणं महेंद्रस्य V. 1. They are also<BR>said to covet heroes who die<BR>gloriously on the battle-field; cf.<BR>R. 7. 53. Bāṇa mentions 14 different<BR>families of these nymphs (see K. 136).<BR>The word is usually said to be in<BR>pl. (स्त्रियां बहुष्वप्सरसः); but the singular,<BR>as also the form अप्सरा, sometimes<BR>occur; नियमविघ्नकारिणी मेनका नाम अप्सराः<BR>प्रेषिता Ś. 1; एकाप्सरः &c. R. 7. 53 and see<BR>Malli. thereon; अनप्सरेव प्रतिभासि V. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Direction or the intermediate point<BR>of the compass (दिक् च उपदिक् च).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तीर्थं N. of a sacred pool<BR>in which the Apsarasas bathe;<BR>probably it is the name of a place, see<BR>Ś. 6.<BR>--पतिः lord of the Apsarasas,<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सव
अप्सव a. [अप्सं जलरसं वाति हिनास्ति,<BR>वा-क] Devoid of the essence<BR>(freshness) of water; possessed of form or<BR>shape; giving water (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सव्य
अप्सव्य a. [अप्सु भवः यत्]<BR>Being in, or fit for, water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सस्
अप्सस् n. Ved. Form, beauty;<BR>or one possessed of beauty; cheek (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अप्सु
अप्सु a. [नास्ति प्सु रूपं यस्य Nir.]<BR>1<BR>Formless, shapeless.<BR>--2 Not beautiful.<BR>Note<BR>--अप्सु forms the first member<BR>of several compounds.<BR>--क्षित् a god.<BR>--चर a. aquatic; moving in waters.<BR>--ज, --जा a. born in the waters or<BR>in the atmosphere. (--जाः) --योनिः<BR>{1} a horse. {2} a cane or reed.<BR>--जित् vanquishing the aerial Asuras.<BR>--मत् a. possessed of what is in water;<BR>not losing one's nature in water (as<BR>lightning); getting sufficient water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफल|अफलः
अफल a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Unfruitful,<BR>fruitless, barren (lit. & fig.); ˚ला<BR>ओषधयः, ˚लं कार्यं &c.<BR>--2 Unproductive,<BR>useless, vain; यथा षंढोऽफलः स्त्रीषु<BR>यथा गौर्गवि चाफला । यथा चाज्ञेऽफलं दानं<BR>तथा विप्रोऽनृचोऽफलः Ms. 2. 158.<BR>--3<BR>Deprived of virility, castrated;<BR>emasculated; अफलोहं कृतस्तेन क्रोधात्सा च<BR>निराकृता Rām.<BR>--लः<BR>1 N. of a plant<BR>(झाबुक).<BR>--2 A goat.<BR>--ला The Aloe<BR>plant (घृतकुमारी); another plant (<BR>भूम्यामलकी).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आकांक्षिन्, --प्रेप्सु a.<BR>one who desires no reward (for<BR>his labours), disinterested;<BR>अफलाकांक्षिभिर्यज्ञः क्रियते ब्रह्मवादिभिः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अफेन|अफेनं
अफेन a. Frothless, without scum<BR>or foam.<BR>--नं Opium (perhaps a<BR>corruption of अहिफेन; अ has here<BR>a depreciative force).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्
अब् = अंब् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्ध|अबद्धं|अबद्धः
अबद्ध --द्धक a.<BR>1 At liberty,<BR>not bound or restrained.<BR>--2<BR>Unmeaning, nonsensical, absurd,<BR>contradictory; e. g. यावज्जवि महं मौनी ब्रह्मचारी च मे<BR>पिता । माता तु मम वंध्यासीदपुत्रश्च पितामहः ॥<BR>(contradictory); जरद्गवः कंबलपादुकाभ्यां<BR>द्वारि स्थितो गायति मंगलानि । ब्राह्मणी पृच्छति<BR>पुत्रकामा राजनगर्यां लवणस्य कोर्धः<BR>Rāyamukuṭa on Ak.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुख a.<BR>foulmouthed, abusive, scurrilous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबद्धक|अबद्धकं
अबद्ध --द्धक a.<BR>1 At liberty,<BR>not bound or restrained.<BR>--2<BR>Unmeaning, nonsensical, absurd,<BR>contradictory; e. g. यावज्जवि महं मौनी ब्रह्मचारी च मे<BR>पिता । माता तु मम वंध्यासीदपुत्रश्च पितामहः ॥<BR>(contradictory); जरद्गवः कंबलपादुकाभ्यां<BR>द्वारि स्थितो गायति मंगलानि । ब्राह्मणी पृच्छति<BR>पुत्रकामा राजनगर्यां लवणस्य कोर्धः<BR>Rāyamukuṭa on Ak.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुख a.<BR>foulmouthed, abusive, scurrilous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध
अबध --ध्य See अवध-ध्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्य|अबध्यं
अबध --ध्य See अवध-ध्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबंधक|अबन्धक
अबंधक a.<BR>1 Not binding.<BR>--2<BR>Without any pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबंधन|अबन्धन
अबंधन a. Free, without bonds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबंध्र|अबन्ध्र
अबंध्र a. Ved. Without ligatures;<BR>falling asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबंधु|अबन्धु
अबंधु, --बांधव a.<BR>1 Friendless,<BR>lonely.<BR>--2 Unowned.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत्<BR>a. causing want of companions.<BR>--कृत a. not brought about by<BR>relatives, growing spontaneously;<BR>Ś. 4. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबांधव|अबान्धव
अबंधु, --बांधव a.<BR>1 Friendless,<BR>lonely.<BR>--2 Unowned.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत्<BR>a. causing want of companions.<BR>--कृत a. not brought about by<BR>relatives, growing spontaneously;<BR>Ś. 4. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबल|अबलं|अबलः
अबल a.<BR>1 Weak, feeble.<BR>--2<BR>Unprotected.<BR>--लः N. of a plant (<BR>वरुणवृक्ष).<BR>--ला<BR>1 A woman (as<BR>belonging to the weaker sex); नूनं हि ते<BR>कविवरा विपरीतबोधा ये नित्यमाहुरबला इति<BR>कामिनीनाम् । याभिविंलोलतरतारकदृष्टिपातैः<BR>शक्रादयोपि विजितास्त्वबलाः कथं ताः ॥ Bh. 1. 11;<BR>compare also:<BR>--हृदये वहसि गिरींद्रौ<BR>त्रिभुवनजयिनी कटाक्षेण । अबला त्वं यदि<BR>मन्ये के बलवंतो न जानीमः ॥ Udb.; ˚जनः a<BR>woman; Ś. 4. 3; R. 9. 46.<BR>--2 One of<BR>the ten earths according to the<BR>Buddhists.<BR>--लं Weakness, want of<BR>strength; see बलाबलं also.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अबलः N. of of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबलास
अबलास a. Not consumptive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबल्यं|अबल्य
अबल्यं<BR>1 Weakness.<BR>--2 Sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाध|अबाधं|अबाधः
अबाध a.<BR>1 Unrestrained,<BR>unobstructed.<BR>--2 Free from pain.<BR>--धा The<BR>segment of the base of a triangle.<BR>--धः<BR>1 Non-obstruction.<BR>--2<BR>Nonrefutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाल
अबाल a.<BR>1 Not childish,<BR>youthful.<BR>--2 Not young, full (as the<BR>moon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबाह्य
अबाह्य a.<BR>1 Not exterior,<BR>internal; R. 14. 50.<BR>--2 (fig.) Familiar or<BR>intimately acquainted with,<BR>conversant with; गीतनृत्यवाद्यादिष्वबाह्यः<BR>Dk. 155.<BR>--3 Without an exterior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबिंधनः|अबिन्धन|अबिन्धनः
अबिंधनः [आपः एव इंधनं यस्य] The<BR>submarine fire (that feeds on the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">Page0125-a+ 56</a>]<BR>waters of the ocean); अबिंधनं वह्निमसौ<BR>बिभर्ति R. 13. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0124-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबिभीवस्
अबिभीवस् a. Ved. Fearless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्ध|अबुद्धः
अबुद्ध a. Foolish, unwise;<BR>अपवादमात्रमबुद्धानां Sāṅ. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुद्धिः|अबुद्धि
अबुद्धिः f.<BR>1 Want of<BR>understanding.<BR>--2 Ignorance, stupidity; ˚मत्<BR>foolish, ignorant. --a. Ignorant,<BR>dull-witted, stupid.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पूर्व,<BR>--पूर्वक a. {1} not preceded by<BR>knowledge or consciousness; not wanton or<BR>intentional. {2} beginning with<BR>non-intelligence.<BR>--(र्वं, --र्वकं) adv.<BR>unconsciously, ignorantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्
अबुध् --बुध a. Foolish, stupid. --m.<BR>A fool. --f. (अभुत्) Ignorance, want<BR>of intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध
अबुध् --बुध a. Foolish, stupid. --m.<BR>A fool. --f. (अभुत्) Ignorance, want<BR>of intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्य
अबुध्य a. Ved. Not to be<BR>perceived or awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोध|अबोधः
अबोध a.<BR>1 Ignorant, foolish, stupid.<BR>--2 Perplexed, puzzled.<BR>--धः<BR>1<BR>Ignorance, stupidity, want of<BR>understanding; ˚धोपहताश्चान्ये Bh. 3. 2;<BR>निसर्गदुर्बोधमबोधविक्लवाः क्व भूपतीनां चरितं क्व<BR>जंतवः Ki. 1. 6.<BR>--2 Not knowing or<BR>being aware of Śi. 6. 41<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गम्य a. incomprehensible,<BR>inconceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोध्य
अबोध्य, --बोधनीय a.<BR>1<BR>Unintelligible.<BR>--2 Not to be awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबोधनीय
अबोध्य, --बोधनीय a.<BR>1<BR>Unintelligible.<BR>--2 Not to be awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबुध्न
अबुध्न a. Having no bottom or<BR>root, bottomless.<BR>--ध्नं Ved. The air<BR>or intermediate region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्ज|अब्जः
अब्ज a. [अप्सु जायते, जण्-ड] Born<BR>in or produced from water<BR>Ms. 5. 112, 8. 100<BR>--ब्जंः<BR>1 The conch (n.<BR>also).<BR>--2 The moon.<BR>--3 Camphor.<BR>--4 N. of a tree (निचुल).<BR>--5<BR>Dhanvantari, physician of the gods,<BR>said to be produced at the<BR>churning of the ocean along with<BR>other jewels.<BR>--ब्जं<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>--2 One thousand millions.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्णिका the seed vessel<BR>of a lotus.<BR>--जः, --भवः, --भूः, --योनिः<BR>epithets of Brahmā, (being supposed<BR>to have sprung from the lotus which<BR>arose from the navel of Viṣṇu).<BR>--दृश्, --नयन, --नेत्र, --लोचन &c. a.<BR>lotuseyed, having large beautiful eyes.<BR>--बांधवः ‘a friend of lotuses,’ the<BR>sun.<BR>--भोगह् {1} the root of a lotus.<BR>{2} a cowrie (वराटक) as large as<BR>a conch.<BR>--वाहनः ‘carrying the moon<BR>on his forehead,’ epithet of Śiva.<BR>--(ना) ‘having the lotus for her seat,’<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">Page0125-b+ 56</a>]<BR>N. of Lakṣmī.<BR>--स्थितः N. of<BR>Brahmā.<BR>--हस्तः the sun (represented<BR>as holding a lotus in one hand).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जा
अब्जा m. (ब्जाः) Ved. Born in<BR>water (P. III. 2. 67, VI. 4. 21).<BR>--f. A pearl-oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जिनी
अब्जिनी<BR>1 A lotus plant.<BR>--2 A<BR>collection of lotuses.<BR>--3 A place full<BR>of lotuses.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिः the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जस्
अब्जस् n. Ved. Shape, beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्जित्
अब्जित् a. Conquering waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्द|अब्दः
अब्द a. [अपो ददाति, दा-क; said in<BR>Uṇ. 4. 98 to be from अब्;<BR>अबतीत्यब्दः] Giving water.<BR>--ब्दः<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>--2 A year (in this sense n. also).<BR>--3 N. of a grass (मुस्ता).<BR>--4 N. of a<BR>mountain<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्धं half a year.<BR>--वाहनः N. of Śiva.<BR>--शतं a century.<BR>--सारः a kind of camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दया
अब्दया adv. Ved. With a desire to<BR>give water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दिः|अब्दि
अब्दिः Ved. A cloud; ˚भृत्<BR>possessed of clouds; giving water, as a<BR>cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दुर्गः|अब्दुर्ग
अब्दुर्गः A fortress in water, one<BR>surrounded by a moat or lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्देवताक
अब्देवताक, --दैवत a. Having the<BR>waters for divinities, praising the<BR>waters; Ms. 11. 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्दैवत
अब्देवताक, --दैवत a. Having the<BR>waters for divinities, praising the<BR>waters; Ms. 11. 133.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्धिः|अब्धि
अब्धिः [आपः धीयंते अत्र, धा-कि]<BR>1 The<BR>ocean, receptacle of water; (fig. also),<BR>दुःख˚, कार्य˚, ज्ञान˚ &c.; store or<BR>reservoir of anything.<BR>--2 A pond, lake.<BR>--3 (In Math.) A symbolical<BR>expression for the number 7;<BR>sometimes for 4.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः the<BR>submarine fire.<BR>--कफः, --फेनः {1} froth,<BR>foam. {2} the cuttle-fish bone,<BR>being regarded as the froth of the<BR>ocean.<BR>--ज a. born in the ocean.<BR>--(जः) {1} the moon. {2} The conch.<BR>--(जौ) (dual) N. of the Aśvins.<BR>--(जा)<BR>{1} spirituous liquor (produced from<BR>the ocean). {2} the Goddess Lakṣmī.<BR>--झषः a sea-fish.<BR>--द्वीपा {1} the<BR>earth. {2} a portion of land<BR>surrounded by the ocean.<BR>--नगरी N. of<BR>Dvārakā, the capital of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--नवनीतकः the moon (the butter of<BR>the ocean).<BR>--मंडूकी the pearl-oyster.<BR>--शयनः N. of Viṣṇu (so called<BR>from his resting in the ocean at<BR>the destruction and renovation of<BR>the world).<BR>--सारः a gem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भक्ष|अब्भक्षः
अब्भक्ष a. Living upon water.<BR>--क्षः A serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भक्षणं|अब्भक्षण
अब्भक्षणं Living upon water, a<BR>kind of fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्भ्र|अब्भ्रं
अब्भ्र &c. = अभ्र q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मचर्य|अब्रह्मचर्य्य
अब्रह्मचर्य a. Unchaste.<BR>--र्यं --र्यकं<BR>1 Unchastity.<BR>--2 Sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मण्य|अब्रह्मण्यं
अब्रह्मण्य a.<BR>1 Not fit for a<BR>Brāhmaṇa; अब्रह्मण्यमवर्णं स्यात् ब्रह्मण्यं ब्रह्मणो<BR>हितम् Halāy.<BR>--2 Inimical to Brāhmaṇas.<BR>--ण्यं An act not befitting a<BR>Brāhmaṇa; an unbrahmanical act. In dramas<BR>usually found as an exclamation<BR>uttered by a Brāhmaṇa in the<BR>sense of ‘to the rescue’, ‘help’,<BR>‘help’, ‘a horrible or disgraceful deed<BR>has been committed’; अहो ˚ण्यं ˚ण्यं<BR>Pt. 1; Ś. 6; U. 1; अत्रांतरे ब्राह्मणेन<BR>मृतपुत्रमारोप्य राजद्वारि<BR>सोरस्ताडनमब्रह्मण्यमुद्घोषितम् U. 2 a cry of help, or<BR>distress; अथैत्ययोगनंदस्य व्याडिना<BR>क्रंदितं पुरः । अब्रह्मण्यमनुत्क्रांतजीवो<BR>योगस्थितो द्विजः Bṛ. Kath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रह्मन्
अब्रह्मन् a.<BR>1 Not accompanied by<BR>devotion; wanting in sacred or<BR>divine knowledge.<BR>--2 Separated<BR>from or devoid of Brāhmaṇas;<BR>नाब्रह्म क्षत्रमृध्नोति Ms. 9. 322.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विद् a. not knowing Brahma or<BR>the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्राह्मण|अब्राह्मणः
अब्राह्मण a. Devoid of or<BR>without Brāhmaṇas.<BR>--णः Not a<BR>Brāhmaṇa; Ms. 2. 241-2; (= शूद्र); six<BR>kinds are usually mentioned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्राह्मण्यं|अब्राह्मण्य
अब्राह्मण्यं<BR>1 Violation of the duties<BR>of a Brāhmaṇa; breach of vows or<BR>sanctity.<BR>--2 = अब्रह्मण्यं q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्रूकृतं|अब्रूकृत
अब्रूकृतं Making a growling (or<BR>Abrū) sound, an indistinct speech<BR>uttered by shutting the lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अब्लिंगं|अब्लिङ्ग
अब्लिंगं [अपां लिंगं ज्ञापनसामर्थ्यं यत्र]<BR>A hymn or verse addressed to the<BR>waters; Y. 3. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्त
अभक्त a.<BR>1 Not devoted or<BR>attached.<BR>--2 Not connected with,<BR>detached.<BR>--3 Not worshipping.<BR>--4<BR>Unaccepted.<BR>--5 Not eaten.<BR>--क्तं Not food;<BR>˚छंदस्, ˚रुच् want of appetite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्तिः|अभक्ति
अभक्तिः f.<BR>1 Want of devotion or<BR>attachment.<BR>--2 Unbelief,<BR>incredulity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्षः|अभक्ष
अभक्षः, --भक्षणं Not eating any<BR>thing; fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्षणं|अभक्षण
अभक्षः, --भक्षणं Not eating any<BR>thing; fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभक्ष्य|अभक्ष्यं
अभक्ष्य a.<BR>1 Not to be eaten.<BR>--2<BR>Prohibited from eating.<BR>--क्ष्यं A<BR>prohibited article of food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभग
अभग a. Unfortunate, ill-fated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0125-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभंग
अभंग a. Not broken &c.<BR>--गः<BR>1<BR>Absence of fracture or defeat.<BR>--2 (In<BR>Rhet.) A variety of श्लेष where<BR>another meaning is obtained without<BR>dividing the words (this<BR>corresponds to अर्थश्लेष); S. D. 644.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभंगुर|अभङ्गुर
अभंगुर a. Undisturbed, firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभद्र
अभद्र a. Inauspicious, bad, evil,<BR>ill, wicked.<BR>--द्रं<BR>1 Evil, sin,<BR>wickedness.<BR>--2 Sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभय|अभयं|अभयः
अभय a. [न. ब.] Free from fear<BR>or danger, secure, safe; वैराग्यमेवाभयम्<BR>Bh. 3. 35.<BR>--यः [न भयं यस्मात्]<BR>1<BR>An epithet of the Supreme Being,<BR>or knowledge concerning that being.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva.<BR>--3 One devoid of all<BR>worldly possessions.<BR>--4 One who<BR>fearlessly executes scriptural<BR>commandments.<BR>--5 N. of a Yoga (conjuncture<BR>or time) favourable to a march or<BR>expedition.<BR>--या<BR>1 N. of a plant<BR>(हरीतकी Mar. हिरडा).<BR>--2 A form of<BR>the goddess Durgā.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Absence<BR>or removal of fear.<BR>--2 Security,<BR>safety, protection from fear or danger;<BR>मया तस्याभयं दत्तं Pt. 1; अभयस्य हि यो<BR>दाता Ms. 8. 303; Ś. 2. 16.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a sacrificial hymn.<BR>--4 The root<BR>of a fragrant grass (वीरणमूलं, उशीरं).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत् a. {1} not terrific, mild.<BR>{2} giving safety.<BR>--गिरिवासिन् m. one<BR>dwelling on the mountain of safety,<BR>N. of a class of Kātyāyana's pupils.<BR>--डिंडिमः {1} proclamation of assurance<BR>or safety. {2} a military or war-drum.<BR>--द, --दायिन्, --प्रद a. giving a<BR>guarantee or promise of safety; भयेष्वभयदः<BR>Rām.; ˚प्रदः Ms. 4. 232.<BR>--(दः) an<BR>Arhat of the Jainas; N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--दक्षिणा, --दानं, --प्रदानं giving a promise,<BR>assurance, or guarantee of safety<BR>or protection (from danger);<BR>सर्वप्रदानेष्वभयप्रदानं (प्रधानं) Pt. 1. 290;<BR>Ms. 4. 247.<BR>--पत्रं a written document or<BR>paper granting assurance of safety;<BR>cf. the modern ‘safe-conduct’.<BR>--मुद्रा a variety of mudrā in<BR>Tantra literature.<BR>--याचना asking for<BR>protection; ˚अंजलिः R. 11. 78.<BR>--वचनं, --वाच् f. an assurance or<BR>promise of safety.<BR>--सनि a. Ved.<BR>giving safety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयंकर|अभयङ्कर
अभयंकर --कृत् a. (अ-भय --कृ with the<BR>insertion of खच् P. III. 2. 43).<BR>1<BR>Not dreadful.<BR>--2 Causing security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभयंकृत्|अभयङ्कृत्
अभयंकर --कृत् a. (अ-भय --कृ with the<BR>insertion of खच् P. III. 2. 43).<BR>1<BR>Not dreadful.<BR>--2 Causing security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभर्तृका
अभर्तृका<BR>1 A widow.<BR>--2 An<BR>unmarried woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवः|अभव
अभवः<BR>1 Non-existence; मत्त<BR>एव भवाभवौ Mb.<BR>--2 Absolution,<BR>final beatitude; प्राप्तुमभवमभिवांछति वा<BR>Ki. 12. 30, 18. 27.<BR>--3 End or<BR>destruction; भवाय सर्वभूतानामभवाय च<BR>रक्षसां Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभव्य
अभव्य a.<BR>1 Not to be, not<BR>predestined.<BR>--2 Improper, inauspicious.<BR>--3 Unfortunate, luckless;<BR>उपनतमवधीरयंत्यभव्याः Ki. 10. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभवत्
अभवत् a. Not existing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभवन्मतयोगः, --संयोगः (in Rhet.)<BR>a defect in composition; अभवन्<BR>असंभवन्नपि मतः इष्टः योगः संबंधः यत्र<BR>K. P. 7; the ‘failure of an intended<BR>connection’, or want of harmony<BR>between the ideas to be expressed<BR>and the words expressing them;<BR>e. g. ईक्षसे यत्कटाक्षेण तदा धन्वी मनोभवः,<BR>here the word यत् can have no<BR>correlation with तदा though intended<BR>by the poet. The proper reading<BR>would be ईक्षसे चेत् &c.; for other<BR>examples see S. D. 575 ad loc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभस्त्रका
अभस्त्रका, अभस्त्रिका, also अभस्त्राका<BR>[अ -भस्त्रा P. VII. 3. 47]<BR>1 A badly<BR>made or inferior pair of bellows.<BR>--2 A young woman who has no<BR>bellows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभस्त्रिका
अभस्त्रका, अभस्त्रिका, also अभस्त्राका<BR>[अ -भस्त्रा P. VII. 3. 47]<BR>1 A badly<BR>made or inferior pair of bellows.<BR>--2 A young woman who has no<BR>bellows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभस्त्राका
अभस्त्रका, अभस्त्रिका, also अभस्त्राका<BR>[अ -भस्त्रा P. VII. 3. 47]<BR>1 A badly<BR>made or inferior pair of bellows.<BR>--2 A young woman who has no<BR>bellows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाग
अभाग a.<BR>1 Without a share (of<BR>inheritance).<BR>--2 Undivided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाव|अभावः
अभाव a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Without love<BR>or affection.<BR>--2 Non-existent.<BR>--वः<BR>1<BR>Not being or existing, non-existence;<BR>गतो भवोऽभावं Mk. 1 has<BR>disappeared.<BR>--2 Absence, want, failure;<BR>सर्वेषामप्यभावे तु ब्राह्मणा रिक्थभागिनः<BR>Ms. 9. 188; mostly in comp.;<BR>सर्वाभावे हरेन्नृपः 189 in the absence of<BR>all, failing all; तोय˚, अन्न˚, आहार˚ &c.<BR>--3 Annihilation, death, destruction,<BR>non-entity; नाभाव उपलब्धेः Ś. B.;<BR>Śi. 20. 64; Ki. 18. 10.<BR>--4 (In<BR>phil.) Privation, non-existence,<BR>nullity or negation, supposed to be<BR>the seventh category or पदार्थ in the<BR>system of Kaṇāda. Strictly speaking<BR>अभाव is not a separate predicament,<BR>like द्रव्य, गुण, but is only a negative<BR>arrangement of those predicaments;<BR>all nameable things being divided<BR>into positive (भाव) and negative<BR>(अभाव), the first division including<BR>द्रव्य, गुण, कर्म, सामान्य, विशेष and समवाय<BR>and the second only one अभाव; cf.<BR>अत्र सप्तमस्थाभावकथनादेव षण्णां भावत्वं प्राप्तं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-c" target="_blank">Page0126-c+ 57</a>]<BR>तेन भावत्वेन पृथगुपन्यासो न कृतः Muktā.<BR>अभाव is defined as भावभिन्नोऽभावः (<BR>प्रतियोगिज्ञानाधीनविषयत्वं) that whose<BR>knowledge is dependent on the knowledge<BR>of its प्रतियोगी. It is of two principal<BR>kinds संसर्गाभाव and अन्योन्याभाव; the first<BR>comprising three varieties प्रागभाव,<BR>प्रध्वंसाभाव, and अत्यंताभाव.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संपत्तिः<BR>f. false attribution (= अध्यास q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावना
अभावना<BR>1 Absence of judgment<BR>or right discernment.<BR>--2 Absence of<BR>religious meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावनीय|अभावनीयः
अभावनीय a. Inconceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभावयितृ
अभावयितृ a. Not perceiving,<BR>comprehending or inferring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाविन्
अभाविन्, अभाव्य a. What is not<BR>destined to be or take place; यदभाविन<BR>तद्भावि H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाव्य
अभाविन्, अभाव्य a. What is not<BR>destined to be or take place; यदभाविन<BR>तद्भावि H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाषणं|अभाषण
अभाषणं Not speaking, silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभाषित
अभाषित a. Not told.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुंस्कः a word which cannot become<BR>mas. or neuter, i. e. always feminine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभि
अभि ind.<BR>1 (As a prefix to<BR>verbs and nouns) It means (a)<BR>‘to’, ‘towards’, ‘in the direction of’;<BR>अभिगम् go towards, अभिया, ˚गमनं,<BR>˚यानं &c.; (b) ‘for’, ‘against’;<BR>˚लष्, ˚पत् &c.; (c) ‘on’, ‘upon’;<BR>˚सिंच् to sprinkle on &c.; (d),<BR>‘over’, ‘above’, ‘across’; ˚भू to<BR>overpower, ˚तन्; (e) ‘greatly’;<BR>‘excessively’ ˚कंप्.<BR>--2 (As a prefix to nouns<BR>not derived from verbs, and to<BR>adjectives) It expresses (a)<BR>intensity or superiority; ˚धर्मः ‘supreme<BR>duty’; ˚ताम्र ‘very red, ˚नव ‘very<BR>new’; (b) ‘towards,’ ‘in the<BR>direction of,’ forming adv. compounds;<BR>˚चैद्यं, ˚मुखं, ˚दूति &c.<BR>--3 (As a<BR>separable adverb) It means<BR>towards, in the direction or<BR>vicinity of (opp. अप); in, above, aloft,<BR>on the top, (mostly Ved).<BR>--4 (As a<BR>preposition with acc.) (a) To,<BR>towards, in the direction of, against;<BR>(with acc. or in comp. in this<BR>sense); अभ्याग्नि or अग्निमभि शलभाः<BR>पतंति; वृक्षमभि द्योतते विद्युत् Sk.;<BR>Śi. 9. 56, 7. 40; अभ्यर्कबिंबं स्थितः Ś. 7. 11.<BR>(b) Near, before, in front or<BR>presence of; Śi. 7. 32; 15. 58.<BR>(c) On, upon, with regard or<BR>reference to; सायमंडनमभि त्वरयंत्यः<BR>Ki. 9. 6; साधुर्देवदत्तो मातरमभि Sk. (d)<BR>Severally, one after another (in a<BR>distributive sense); वृक्षं वृक्षमभि<BR>सिंचति Sk.; भूतभूतमभि प्रभुः Bop. By<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">Page0127-a+ 57</a>]<BR>P. I. 4. 91 अभि has all the senses of<BR>अनु given in I. 4. 90 except that of<BR>भाग; e. g. (लक्षणे) हरिमभि वर्तते; (<BR>इत्थंभूताख्याने) भक्तो हरिमभि; (वीप्सायां), देवं<BR>देवमभि सिंचति; but यदत्र ममाभिष्यात् तद्दीयतां;<BR>प्राज्ञो गोविंदमभितिष्ठति Bop. (e) In, into,<BR>to; Śi. 8. 60. (f) For, for the sake<BR>of, on account of (Ved.). According<BR>to G. M. अभि has these senses:<BR>--अभि,<BR>पूजाभृशार्थेच्छासौम्याभिमुख्यसौरूप्यवचनाहारस्वाध्यायेषु; e. g. पूजायां, अभिवंदते; भृशे,<BR>अभिनिवेशः; इच्छायां, अभिलाषः, अभिकः;<BR>सौम्ये or माधुर्ये, अभिजातः; आभिमुख्ये,<BR>अभिमुखं, अभ्यग्नि; सौरूप्ये, अभिरूपं; वचने,<BR>अभिधत्ते; आहारे, अभ्यवहरति; स्वाध्याये,<BR>अभ्यस्याति. [cf. L. ob; Gr. amphi; Zend<BR>aibi or aiwi, Goth. bi; also umbi; um].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0126-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक|अभिकः
अभि(भी)क a. [अभि-कन्<BR>निपातोयं; P. V. 2. 74] {1} Lustful,<BR>libidinous, voluptuous; सोधिकारमभिकः<BR>कुलोचितं काश्चन स्वयमवर्तयत्समाः R. 19. 4;<BR>अपि सिंचेः कृशानौ त्वं दर्पं मय्यपि<BR>योऽभिकः Bk. 8. 92.<BR>--कः A lover,<BR>voluptuous person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक|अभीकः
अभि(भी)क a. [अभि-कन्<BR>निपातोयं; P. V. 2. 74] {1} Lustful,<BR>libidinous, voluptuous; सोधिकारमभिकः<BR>कुलोचितं काश्चन स्वयमवर्तयत्समाः R. 19. 4;<BR>अपि सिंचेः कृशानौ त्वं दर्पं मय्यपि<BR>योऽभिकः Bk. 8. 92.<BR>--कः A lover,<BR>voluptuous person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकम्
अभिकम् {c10c} A. To love, desire;<BR>कः स्त्रियमभिकामयमानां नाभिनंदति<BR>Dk. 88; Ki. 18. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकाम
अभिकाम a. [कम्-अच् or अभिवृद्धः<BR>कामो यस्य] Affectionate, loving,<BR>desirous, wishing for, lustful, with the<BR>object of love in acc. or in comp.;<BR>याचे त्वामभिकामाहं Mb.<BR>--मः<BR>1<BR>Affection, love.<BR>--2 Wish, desire.<BR>--मं<BR>ind. Longingly, with desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकामिक
अभिकामिक a. Voluntary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकंप्|अभिकम्प्
अभिकंप् {c1c} A. To shake or<BR>tremble violently. --Caus.<BR>1 To stir,<BR>shake.<BR>--2 To allure, entice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकंपनं
अभिकंपनं Shaking; alluring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकांक्ष्|अभिकाङ्क्ष्
अभिकांक्ष् {c1c} U. To ask,<BR>request; long for, wish or desire for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकांक्षा|अभिकाङ्क्षा
अभिकांक्षा Wish, desire, longing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकांक्षिन्|अभिकाङ्क्षिन्
अभिकांक्षिन् a. Longing, wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकृ
अभिकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To make, render,<BR>do; कुरुक्षेत्रे निवेशमभिचक्रतुः Mb.<BR>--2<BR>To do with reference to, for the<BR>sake of, or in behalf of.<BR>--3 To<BR>procure, get, obtain, effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकरणं|अभिकरण
अभिकरणं<BR>1 Effecting, doing.<BR>--2 A<BR>charm, incantation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकृतिः|अभिकृति
अभिकृतिः f. N. of a metre<BR>containing 100 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिकृत्वन्
अभिकृत्वन् a. (m. ˚त्वा; f. ˚त्वरी)<BR>Magieal; a magician or spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रतु
अभिक्रतु a. [अभिमुख्येन क्रतुर्युद्धकर्म<BR>यस्य] Haughty, very powerful (<BR>बलीयस्) (as an enemy), Rv. 3. 34. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रंद्|अभिक्रन्द्
अभिक्रंद् {c1c} P. To shout at,<BR>roar at; neigh at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रंदः|अभिक्रन्द|अभिक्रन्दः
अभिक्रंदः A shout, roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रम्
अभिक्रम् {c1c} U., {c4c} P.<BR>1 To step or<BR>go near to, approach; तमभिक्रम्य<BR>सर्वेऽद्य वयं चार्थामहे वसु Mb.<BR>--2 To roam<BR>over, wander, pass or walk over.<BR>--3 To attack, assail, fall upon.<BR>--4<BR>To undertake, begin; to set about,<BR>prepare; गमनायाभिचक्राम Rām.<BR>--Caus. To bring near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रमः|अभिक्रम
अभिक्रमः<BR>1 Beginning, attempting,<BR>an undertaking; नेहाभिक्रमनाशोस्ति<BR>प्रत्यवायो न विद्यते Bg. 2. 40.<BR>--2 A<BR>determined attack or onset, assault,<BR>onslaught.<BR>--3 Ascending, mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रमणं|अभिक्रमण
