अभिक्रांतिः|अभिक्रान्ति|अभिक्रान्तिः
अभिक्रमणं, --क्रांतिः f. Approaching,<BR>attacking &c. = अभिक्रम above;<BR>पुंड्रदेश˚ Dk. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रांतिन्|अभिक्रान्तिन्
अभिक्रांतिन् a. [इष्टादिगण]<BR>1 One<BR>who has approached or<BR>undertaken or begun.<BR>--2 Skilled or versed<BR>in, conversant with (with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रुश्
अभिक्रुश् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To cry out at,<BR>call out to.<BR>--2 To call out (to one)<BR>in a scolding manner;<BR>अन्योन्यमभिचक्रुशुः Mb.<BR>--3 To weep over,<BR>lament with tears, bemoan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रोशः|अभिक्रोश
अभिक्रोशः<BR>1 Calling out, crying.<BR>--2 Reviling, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्रोशकः|अभिक्रोशक
अभिक्रोशकः<BR>1 One who calls out; a<BR>reviler, calumniator.<BR>--2 A herald.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षत्तृ
अभिक्षत्तृ a. Ved. A murderer,<BR>killer, destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षद
अभिक्षद a. [क्षद्-अच्] Ved. A<BR>destroyer; Rv. 6. 50. 1.; giving<BR>without being asked (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षिप्
अभिक्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To throw or<BR>fling at (as the lash of a whip at<BR>a horse); to insult.<BR>--2 To excel;<BR>Bk. 8. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिक्षिप्त
अभिक्षिप्त p. p. Thrown, surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्या
अभिख्या {c2c} P. Ved.<BR>1 To see,<BR>perceive, view.<BR>--2 To be gracious,<BR>look graciously. --Caus. (ख्यापयति) To<BR>tell, declare, make known,<BR>proclaim; कलहकंटक इत्यभिख्यापिताख्यः<BR>Dk. 136; 171; Ms. 8. 205, 9. 262.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्या
अभिख्या a. [कर्तरि क्विप्] Going<BR>towards; well-known,<BR>celebrated.<BR>--ख्या [ख्या-अङ्]<BR>1 (a)<BR>Splendour, beauty, lustre;<BR>काप्यभिख्या तयोरासीद् व्रजतोः शुद्धवेषयोः<BR>R. 1. 46; सूर्यापाये न खलु कमलं पुष्यति<BR>स्वामभिख्यां Me. 80; Ku. 1. 43;<BR>7. 18. (b) Look, view, appearance,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">Page0127-c+ 57</a>]<BR>aspect (Ved.).<BR>--2 Telling, declaring.<BR>--3 Calling, addressing.<BR>--4 A name,<BR>appellation.<BR>--5 A word, synonym.<BR>--6 Fame, glory; notoriety (in a bad<BR>sense); greatness (माहात्म्यं).<BR>--7<BR>Intellect (Nir.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्यात
अभिख्यात p. p. Become or made<BR>known; celebrated; ˚दोषः Y. 3. 301.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्यातृ
अभिख्यातृ a. Ved. Looking,<BR>supervising, superintending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिख्यानं|अभिख्यान
अभिख्यानं Fame, glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम्
अभिगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go to, go near<BR>to, approach (with acc.);<BR>एनमभिजग्मुर्महर्षयः R. 15. 59; Ki. 10. 21;<BR>मनुमेकाग्रमासीनमभिगम्य महर्षयः Ms. 1. 1;<BR>11. 100.<BR>--2 To follow, go after;<BR>अनुरागाद्वने रामं दिष्ट्या त्वमभिगच्छसि<BR>Rām.<BR>--3 To find, meet with<BR>(casually or by chance).<BR>--4 To<BR>cohabit, have sexual intercourse (with<BR>man or woman); अभिगंतास्मि भगिनीं<BR>मातरं वा तवेति ह Y. 2. 205; अभ्यगच्छः<BR>पतिं यत्त्वं भजमानं Mb.<BR>--5 To take to,<BR>undertake, betake oneself to.<BR>--6<BR>To get, to share in; be subject to;<BR>निद्रामभिगतः Rām.<BR>--7 To conceive,<BR>apprehend, understand,<BR>comprehend. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to go to<BR>or approach; take, convey, send;<BR>Dk. 102.<BR>--2 To cause to<BR>apprehend; explain, teach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगंतृ|अभिगन्तृ
अभिगंतृ a. One who approaches or<BR>has intercourse (with a woman);<BR>one who understands &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगमः|अभिगम
अभिगमः, --गमनं<BR>1 (a)<BR>Approaching, going or coming to, visit,<BR>arrival; तवार्हतो नाभिगमेन तृप्तं R. 5. 11,<BR>17. 72; ज्येष्ठाभिगमनात्पूर्वं<BR>तेनाप्यनभिनंदिता 12. 35, K. 158; Pt. 3. (b)<BR>Finding out; enjoying; कृत्वा<BR>तासामभिगममपां Me. 49 (सेवनं Malli.).<BR>--2 Sexual<BR>intercourse (with a man or woman);<BR>परदारभिगमनं K. 107; प्रसह्य<BR>दास्यभिगमे Y. 2. 291; Pt. 1; H. 1. 104;<BR>नीच˚ Y. 3. 298, 2. 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगमनं|अभिगमन
अभिगमः, --गमनं<BR>1 (a)<BR>Approaching, going or coming to, visit,<BR>arrival; तवार्हतो नाभिगमेन तृप्तं R. 5. 11,<BR>17. 72; ज्येष्ठाभिगमनात्पूर्वं<BR>तेनाप्यनभिनंदिता 12. 35, K. 158; Pt. 3. (b)<BR>Finding out; enjoying; कृत्वा<BR>तासामभिगममपां Me. 49 (सेवनं Malli.).<BR>--2 Sexual<BR>intercourse (with a man or woman);<BR>परदारभिगमनं K. 107; प्रसह्य<BR>दास्यभिगमे Y. 2. 291; Pt. 1; H. 1. 104;<BR>नीच˚ Y. 3. 298, 2. 294.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगम्य
अभिगम्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be<BR>approached, visited or sought; Ku. 6. 56.<BR>--2<BR>Accessible, that can be approached<BR>without fear, inviting;<BR>तथाप्यनभिगमनीयो लोकस्य Mk. 4; भीमकांतैर्नृपगुणैः<BR>… अधृष्यश्चाभिगम्यश्च R. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगामिन्
अभिगामिन् a. Approaching, having<BR>intercourse with; Ms. 3. 45; Y. 2. 282.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगामुक
अभिगामुक a. Inviting, leading one<BR>to approach (as qualities).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगर्ज्
अभिगर्ज् {c1c} P. To roar or bawl<BR>at, to raise wild or ferocious cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0127-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगर्जनं|अभिगर्जन
अभिगर्जनं, अभिगर्जितं A wild, savage<BR>or ferocious roar; up-roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगर्जितं|अभिगर्जित
अभिगर्जनं, अभिगर्जितं A wild, savage<BR>or ferocious roar; up-roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगा
अभिगा = अभी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगुप्
अभिगुप् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To guard,<BR>protect, defend; लंकायामाभिगुप्तायां<BR>सागरेण समंततः Rām.<BR>--2 To hide, conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगुप्तिः|अभिगुप्ति
अभिगुप्तिः f. Guarding, protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगोप्तृ
अभिगोप्तृ m. Protector, guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगुर्
अभिगुर् {c6c} U. To assent or agree<BR>to, approve of (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगूर्त|अभिगूर्त्त
अभिगूर्त p. p. Approved of;<BR>destined for an offering; uttered<BR>(with praise).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगूर्तिः|अभिगूर्ति|अभिगूर्त्ति
अभिगूर्तिः f.<BR>1 Song of praise;<BR>constant desire or thought;<BR>Rv. 1. 162. 6.<BR>--2 Effort, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगॄ
अभिगॄ {c9c} U. Ved.<BR>1 To call to or<BR>address approvingly, join in,<BR>welcome, praise.<BR>--2 To accept<BR>propitiously, allow, approve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगरः|अभिगर
अभिगरः [गॄ-अप्] Song of praise;<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगै
अभिगै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To call to, sing to.<BR>--2 To fill with song, make noisy<BR>with songs; भृंगराजाभिगीतानि (वनानि)<BR>Rām.<BR>--3 To sing, celebrate in<BR>song; तदप्येष श्लोकोऽभिगीतः Ait. Br.<BR>--4 To approve, allow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगीत
अभिगीत p. p. Sung, chanted,<BR>celebrated in song &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगेष्ण
अभिगेष्ण --ष्णु a. [गै-इष्णुच्] Singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिगेष्णु
अभिगेष्ण --ष्णु a. [गै-इष्णुच्] Singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रह्
अभिग्रह् (Ved. ग्रभ्) {c9c} U.<BR>1 To<BR>take or seize, catch, catch hold of,<BR>seize forcibly, attack; रिपुणाभिगृह्य<BR>Dk. 5, 98, 103.<BR>--2 To accept, take.<BR>--3 To receive, (as a guest).<BR>--4 To<BR>fold, lay or bring together (as the<BR>hands).<BR>--5 To set, show or bring<BR>forth (as blossom, fruit &c.). --Caus.<BR>To catch or surprise one in the<BR>very act, to let oneself be so caught;<BR>अर्यवर्यस्य कस्यचिद् गृहे चोरयित्वा<BR>रूपाभिग्रहितो बद्धः Dk. 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रहः|अभिग्रह
अभिग्रहः<BR>1 Seizing, robbing,<BR>plundering.<BR>--2 Attack, assault, onset.<BR>--3 Challenge.<BR>--4 Complaint.<BR>--5<BR>Authority, power, weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिग्रहणं|अभिग्रहण
अभिग्रहणं Robbing, seizing in the<BR>presence of the owner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघर्षणं|अभिघर्षण
अभिघर्षणं<BR>1 Rubbing, friction.<BR>--2<BR>Possession by an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघात|अभिघातः
अभिघात, --घातक, --तकिन् &c.<BR>See under अभिहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातक|अभिघातकः
अभिघात, --घातक, --तकिन् &c.<BR>See under अभिहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातकिन्
अभिघात, --घातक, --तकिन् &c.<BR>See under अभिहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघृ
अभिघृ (Used only in caus.).<BR>1 To<BR>cause to trickle down, let fall<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">Page0128-b+ 57</a>]<BR>down by drops; तां (वपां) अध्वर्युः<BR>स्रुवेणाभिघारयन्नाह Ait. Br.<BR>--2 To<BR>sprinkle with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघारः|अभिघार
अभिघारः [घृ-णिच्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Ghee<BR>or clarified butter.<BR>--2 Dropping down<BR>ghee upon offerings at sacrifices;<BR>प्रणीतपृषदाज्याभिघारघारेस्तनूनपात् Mv. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघारणं|अभिघारण
अभिघारणं Act of sprinkling (with<BR>ghee) besprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघ्रा
अभिघ्रा {c1c} P. To smell at, snuffle;<BR>to bring the nose close to<BR>another's forehead (as in caressing,<BR>kissing &c. as a token of affection).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघ्राणं|अभिघ्राण
अभिघ्राणं Smelling at or touching<BR>the forehead with the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचक्ष्
अभिचक्ष् {c2c} A.<BR>1 To look at, view,<BR>perceive, see; अभि यो विश्वा भुवनानि<BR>चष्टे (सूर्यः) Rv. 7. 61. 1.<BR>--2 To call<BR>to or address.<BR>--3 Toaddress sharply,<BR>to assail with sharp words<BR>Rv. 7. 104. 8.<BR>--4 To name, call.<BR>--5 To<BR>look graciously upon, 5. 3. .9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचक्षणं|अभिचक्षण
अभिचक्षणं Ved. Means of defence;<BR>(magical) remedy.<BR>--णा Viewing,<BR>indicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचर्
अभिचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To act wrongly<BR>towards any one, offend, trespass;<BR>तत्र विराधदनुकबंधप्रभृतयः<BR>केप्यभिचरंतीति श्रुतं Mv. 2.<BR>--2 To be faithless<BR>(as wife or husband); पतिं या<BR>नाभिचरति मनोवाग्देहसंयता Ms. 5. 165;<BR>9. 102.<BR>--3 To charm, conjure,<BR>exorcise (by spells or incantations),<BR>employ spells for magical purposes<BR>&c.; वृष्ट्यायुः पुष्टिकामो वा तथैवाभिचरन्नपि<BR>Y. 1. 295; 3. 289.<BR>--4 To possess,<BR>occupy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचरः|अभिचर
अभिचरः A follower, servant,<BR>attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचरणं|अभिचरण
अभिचरणं Enchanting, exorcising,<BR>employment of spells for<BR>malevolent purposes (such as श्येनयाग);<BR>Mu. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचरणीय
अभिचरणीय a. Fit for exorcising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचरितुः|अभिचरितु
अभिचरितुः f. Ved. Enchanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारः|अभिचार
अभिचारः<BR>1 Exorcising, enchanting<BR>employment of magical spells for<BR>malevolent purposes; magic itself<BR>(being regarded as one of the<BR>Upapātakas or minor sins); अभिचारेषु<BR>सर्वेषु कर्तव्यो द्विशतो दमः Ms. 9. 290;<BR>11. 64, 198; K. 109; Mv. 1. 62.<BR>--2 Killing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कल्पः N. of<BR>a work on incantations<BR>regarded as part of the Atharvaveda.<BR>--ज्वरः a fever caused by magical<BR>spells.<BR>--मंत्रः a magical formula,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">Page0128-c+ 56</a>]<BR>an incantation or formula for<BR>working a charm; Śi. 7. 58.<BR>--यज्ञः, --होमः<BR>a sacrifice made for magical purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारक|अभिचारकः
अभिचारक, --चारिन् (˚रिकी, रिणी f.)<BR>a. Conjuring, enchanting, using<BR>magical spells for evil purposes;<BR>magical Ki. 3. 56.<BR>--कः, --री A<BR>conjurer, magician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिचारिन्
अभिचारक, --चारिन् (˚रिकी, रिणी f.)<BR>a. Conjuring, enchanting, using<BR>magical spells for evil purposes;<BR>magical Ki. 3. 56.<BR>--कः, --री A<BR>conjurer, magician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिच्छाय
अभिच्छाय a. Being in shade<BR>or turned towards the shade.<BR>--यं<BR>adv. In shade or darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजन्
अभिजन् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To be born to or<BR>for (a person or thing), to claim<BR>as one's birth-right; स महीमभिजायते<BR>Mb.; see also under अभिजात (1)<BR>below.<BR>--2 To be born or<BR>produced, arise, spring from;<BR>कामात्कोधोऽभिजायते Bg. 2. 62;<BR>H. 1. 205.<BR>--3 To be born or produced<BR>again; Bg. 6. 41; 13. 23.<BR>--4 To<BR>be, become, be turned into; तस्याः<BR>स्पृष्ट्वैव सलिलं नरः शैलोभिजायते Rām.<BR>--5 To be born of a high family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज
अभिज a. Born or produced all<BR>round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनः|अभिजन
अभिजनः<BR>1 (a) A family, race,<BR>lineage; कलहंसकादभिजनं ज्ञात्वा Māl. 8;<BR>नाभिजनमीक्षते K. 104; Mu. 6. 6;<BR>Ms. 4. 18; Dk. 135, 170; U. 4. (b) Birth,<BR>extraction, descent; तुल्याभजिनेषु<BR>भूमिभरेषु (धरेषु?) राज्ञां वृत्तिः M. 1;<BR>Ms. 1. 100; Y. 1. 123.<BR>--2 High or<BR>noble descent, noble birth or<BR>family; स्तुतं तन्माहात्म्यं यदभिजनतो यच्च<BR>गुणतः Māl. 2. 13; शीलं<BR>शौलतटात्पतत्वभिजनः संदह्यतां वह्निना Bh. 2. 39;<BR>M. 5.<BR>--3 Forefathers, ancestors;<BR>अभिजनाः पूर्वे बांधवाः Kāśī. on<BR>P. IV. 3. 90; also descendants.<BR>--4 Native<BR>country, motherland, ancestral<BR>abode (opp. निवास); cf. Sk. on<BR>P. IV. 3. 90: --यत्र स्वयं वसति स निवासः<BR>(यत्र संप्रति उष्यते Mbh.); यत्र पूर्वैरुषितं<BR>सोऽभिजनः इति विवेकः.<BR>--5 Fame,<BR>celebrity.<BR>--6 The head or ornament of a<BR>family; यद्विद्वानपि तादृशेप्यभिजने<BR>धर्म्यात्पथो विच्युतः Mv. 1. 33.<BR>--7<BR>Attendants, retinue (= परिजन q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनन
अभिजनन (नी f.) a. Becoming<BR>one's high birth; Mv. 5. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनवत्|अभिजनवन्त्
अभिजनवत् a. Of noble descent,<BR>nobly born; ˚तीं मालविकां M. 5;<BR>˚वतो भर्तुः श्लाध्ये स्थिता गृहिणीपदे<BR>Ś. 4. 18; Bg. 16. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजनितुः|अभिजनितु
अभिजनितुः f. Ved. Being born or<BR>produced (Ved.); ˚तोः to produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0128-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजात|अभिजातः
अभिजात p. p.<BR>1 (a) Born to or<BR>for; भवंति संपदं दैवीमभिजातस्य भारत<BR>Bg. 16. 3, 4, 5. (b) Produced all<BR>around. (c) Born in consequence<BR>of.<BR>--2 Inbred, inborn.<BR>--3 Born,<BR>produced; अजातपक्षामभिजातकंठीं<BR>Rām.<BR>--4 Noble, nobly or well born,<BR>of noble descent; जात्यस्तेनाभिजातेन<BR>शूरः शौर्यवता कुशः R. 17. 4; Māl. 4;<BR>courteous, polite; अभिजातं खल्वस्य<BR>वचनं V. 1; K. 102, M. 3, Māl. 7;<BR>अनभिजाते Mu. 2.<BR>--5 Fit, proper,<BR>worthy.<BR>--6 Sweet, agreeable;<BR>प्रजल्पितायामभिजातवाचि Ku. 1. 45.<BR>--7<BR>Handsome, beautiful.<BR>--8 Learned,<BR>wise; distinguished; संकीर्णं<BR>नाभिजातेषु नाप्रबुद्धेषु संस्कृतं (वेदेत्).<BR>--तं<BR>Nobility, noble birth. --adv. Nobly,<BR>politely, courteously; ˚तं खलु एष<BR>वारितः Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजातिः|अभिजाति
अभिजातिः f. Noble birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजि
अभिजि {c1c} P.<BR>1 To conquer<BR>completely.<BR>--2 To acquire by<BR>conquest. --Desid. To desire to win<BR>or conquer, acquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजयः|अभिजय
अभिजयः Conquest; complete<BR>victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजित्
अभिजित् a. [अभि-जि-क्विप्]<BR>1<BR>Victorious, conquering completely.<BR>--2<BR>Helping in conquering completely.<BR>--3 Born under the constellation<BR>अभिजित् P. IV. 3. 36, see अभिजित<BR>--m.<BR>1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>sacrifice, part of the great sacrifice<BR>called गवामयन; Ms. 11. 75, also used<BR>for अतिरात्र q. v.<BR>--3 N. of a star; N. of<BR>one of the lunar mansions. --n.<BR>1<BR>The 8th Muhūrta of the day,<BR>midday (fit for a Śrāddha ceremony).<BR>--2 N. of a लग्न favourable to setting<BR>out.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुहूर्तः The 8th<BR>Muhūrta or period comprising 24<BR>minutes before and 24 minutes after<BR>noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजितः|अभिजित
अभिजितः N. of an asterism or the<BR>Muhūrta indicated by it; मुहूर्तेऽ<BR>भिजिते प्राप्ते सार्धरात्रे विभूषिते ।<BR>देवक्यजनयद्विष्णुं यशोदा तां तु कन्यकां ॥ V. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजितिः|अभिजिति
अभिजितिः f. Ved. Victory,<BR>conquest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजुष्
अभिजुष् {c6c} A. (or Ved. P.)<BR>1 To<BR>visit, frequent, call upon;<BR>श्रियाभिजुष्टः Mb.<BR>--2 To be pleased or<BR>contented with, like, be fond of (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिजुष्ट
अभिजुष्ट p. p. Visited, frequented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञा
अभिज्ञा {c9c} U.<BR>1 To recognize,<BR>discern; (सा) नाभ्यजानान्नलं नृपं Mb.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-b" target="_blank">Page0129-b+ 58</a>]<BR>--2 To know, understand, be<BR>acquainted with, be aware of,<BR>perceive; अहं हि नाभिजानामि भवेदेवं न<BR>वेति वा Mb.; Bg. 18. 55, 4. 14; 7. 13;<BR>भवदभिज्ञातं कथयतु Dk. 3, 78.<BR>--3 To<BR>look upon, consider or regard as,<BR>know to be.<BR>--4 To admit, own,<BR>acknowledge; नपुत्रमभिजानामि त्वयि जातं<BR>Mb.<BR>--5 To remember, recollect;<BR>used with the Future instead of the<BR>Imperfect, Imperfect with यत्, or both<BR>when interdependence of two actions<BR>is denoted, P. III. 2. 112, 114; cf.<BR>Bk. 6. 138, 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञ|अभिज्ञः
अभिज्ञ a. [ज्ञा-क]<BR>1 Knowing,<BR>aware of, one who understands or<BR>is acquainted with, experiencing or<BR>having had experience of (with gen.<BR>or loc. or in comp.).; यद्वा<BR>कौशलमिंद्रसूनुदमने तत्राप्यभिज्ञो जनः U. 5. 35;<BR>अभिज्ञाश्छेदपातानां क्रियंते नंदनद्रुमाः<BR>Ku. 2. 41, Me. 16; R. 7. 64; अनभिज्ञो<BR>भवान्सेवाधर्मस्य Pt. 1.<BR>--2 Skilled in,<BR>conversant with, proficient, skilful,<BR>clever; यदि त्वमीदृशः कथायामभिज्ञः<BR>U. 4., see अनभिज्ञ also.<BR>--ज्ञा<BR>1<BR>Recognition.<BR>--2 Remembrance,<BR>recollection; अभिज्ञावचने लृट् P. III. 2. 112.<BR>--3 A supernatural faculty or power<BR>of which five kinds are usually<BR>mentioned:-- (1) taking any form<BR>at will; (2) hearing to any<BR>distance; (3) seeing to any distance;<BR>(4) penetrating men's thoughts; (5)<BR>knowing their state and<BR>antecedents. --Monier Williams.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञानं|अभिज्ञान
अभिज्ञानं<BR>1 Recognition;<BR>तदभिज्ञानहेतोर्हि दत्तं तेन महात्मना Rām. (अभिज्ञान<BR>is a combination of अनुभव or direct<BR>perception and स्मृति or recollection;<BR>a sort of direct perception<BR>assisted by the memory; as when we<BR>say ‘this is the same man I saw<BR>yesterday’ सोयं ह्यो दृष्टो नरः, अनुभव or<BR>direct perception leading to the<BR>identification expressed by अयं<BR>and the memory leading to the<BR>reference to past action<BR>expressed by सः).<BR>--2 Remembrance,<BR>recollection; knowledge, ascertainment.<BR>--3 (a) A sign or token of<BR>recognition (person or thing); वत्स<BR>योगिन्यस्मि मालत्यभिज्ञानं च धारयामि Māl. 9;<BR>Bk. 8. 118, 124; R. 12. 62;<BR>Me. 112; उपपन्नैरभिज्ञानैर्दूतं तमवगच्छत<BR>Rām.<BR>--4 The dark portion in the<BR>disc of the moon.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आभरणं<BR>a recognition-ornament, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">Page0129-c+ 56</a>]<BR>tokenring Ś. 4.<BR>--पत्रं a certificate, letter of<BR>recommendation.<BR>--शकुंतलं N. of a<BR>celebrated drama by Kālidāsa in<BR>seven acts, in which king Duṣyanta<BR>marries Kaṇva's daughter<BR>Śakuntalā by the Gāndharva form of<BR>marriage, forgets all about her owing<BR>to the curse of Durvāsas, but<BR>ultimately recollects, at the sight of<BR>the token-ring (अभिज्ञान) that he<BR>had duly married her; अभिज्ञानेन<BR>स्मृता शकुंतला अभिज्ञानशकुंतला; तामधिकृत्य कृतं<BR>नाटकं ˚शकुंतलं; (the reading ˚शाकुंतलं<BR>is grammatically indefensible).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञापक
अभिज्ञापक a. Making known,<BR>informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिज्ञु
अभिज्ञु a. Ved. [अभिगते जानुनी<BR>येन] On the knees, kneeling up to<BR>the knees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिडीनं|अभिडीन
अभिडीनं Flying towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितड्
अभितड् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To beat, knock,<BR>thump, hit, smite, strike (fig. also);<BR>to wound; वाक्शरैरभिताडितः Rām.<BR>--2 (Astr.) To eclipse the greater<BR>part of the disc; Bṛ. S. 11. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिताडनं|अभिताडन
अभिताडनं Beating, thumping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितप्
अभितप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To irradiate with<BR>heat, heat, inflame; अभितप्तमयोपि<BR>मार्दवं भजते कैव कथा शरीरिषु R. 8. 43;<BR>19. 56.<BR>--2 To pain, distress, wound,<BR>afflict. --pass. To suffer intensely,<BR>be afflicted. --Caus. To pain,<BR>distress, afflict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितप्त
अभितप्त p. p.<BR>1 Heated,<BR>inflamed, scorched, burnt.<BR>--2 Distressed,<BR>grieving or lamenting for<BR>(actively used).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितापः|अभिताप
अभितापः Extreme heat, whether<BR>of body or mind; agitation,<BR>affliction, great distress or pain; Śi. 9. 1;<BR>Ki. 9. 4; बलवान्पुनर्मे मनसोभितापः<BR>V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितरां
अभितरां ind. Nearer to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितस्
अभितस् ind. (Used as an<BR>adverb, or preposition with acc.)<BR>1<BR>Near to, to, towards; अभितस्तं पृथासूनुः<BR>स्नेहेन परितस्तरे Ki. 11. 8.<BR>--2 (a) Near,<BR>hard by, close by, in the proximity<BR>of; ततो राजाब्रवीद्वाक्यं सुमंत्रमभितः<BR>स्थितं Rām; sometimes with gen.;<BR>निषसादाभितस्तस्य ibid. (b) Before,<BR>in the presence of; तन्वंतमिद्धमभितो<BR>गुरुमंशुजालं Ki. 2. 59.<BR>--3 Opposite to,<BR>facing, in front of; त्रिपथगामभितः<BR>Ki. 6. 1, 5. 14.<BR>--4 On both sides;<BR>चूडाचुंबितकंकपत्रमभितस्तूणीद्वयं पृष्ठतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">Page0130-a+ 56</a>]<BR>U. 4. 20; Mv. 1. 18; पादपैः<BR>पुष्पपत्राणि सृजद्भिरभितो नदीं Rām; Ś. 6. 16;<BR>Bk. 9. 137.<BR>--5 Before and after.<BR>--6<BR>On all sides, round, round about<BR>(with acc. or gen.); कीर्त्याभितः<BR>सुरभितः Dk. 1; परिजनो यथाव्यापारं<BR>राजानमभितः स्थितः M. 1; Ś. 7;<BR>यस्याभितः U. 6. 36; everywhere Ki. 8. 10.<BR>--7 Entirely, thoroughly,<BR>completely, throughout.<BR>--8 Quickly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अस्थि a. surrounded by bones.<BR>--भाविन् a. being all round,<BR>surrounding P. VI. 2. 182.<BR>--रात्रं<BR>Ved. near the night; just at the<BR>beginning or end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0129-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिताम्र
अभिताम्र a. Very red,<BR>darkred; R. 15. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितृप्
अभितृप् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To satiate,<BR>satisfy.<BR>--2 To refresh; Bṛ. S. 19. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभितर्पणं
अभितर्पणं Satiation, refreshing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदक्षिणं
अभिदक्षिणं ind. To or towards<BR>the right (= प्रदक्षिणं q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदापनं|अभिदापन
अभिदापनं The being trodden<BR>under the foot by elephants (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदृश्
अभिदृश् {c1c} P. To look at,<BR>behold. --Caus.<BR>1 To show, point out.<BR>--2 To show oneself to, appear<BR>before. --pass.<BR>1 To be seen, be<BR>visible, appear.<BR>--2 To be considered or<BR>thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिदर्शनं|अभिदर्शन
अभिदर्शनं<BR>1 Seeing.<BR>--2 Becoming<BR>visible; appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्यु|अभिद्युः
अभिद्यु a.<BR>1 Directed to heaven,<BR>tending or going to heaven,<BR>heavenward.<BR>--2 Heavenly.<BR>--3 Bright,<BR>brilliant.<BR>--द्युः A half month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रु
अभिद्रु {c1c} P.<BR>1 (a) To run up to,<BR>run near; पयस्यभिद्रवति भुवं युगावधौ<BR>Śi. 17. 40. (b) To invade, march<BR>against, fall upon, attack, assail;<BR>मकरंदेन प्रतिहतो जामाता बलात्कारेण<BR>अभिद्रवन् Māl. 7 laying violent hands<BR>on; गजा इवान्योन्यमभिद्रवंतः (वारिधराः)<BR>Mk. 5. 21; Ve. 3.<BR>--2 To overrun,;<BR>infest, harass, afflict;<BR>जन्ममृत्युजराव्याधिवेदनाभिरमिद्रुतं (देहं) Mb.<BR>--3 To<BR>come over, pass or run over.<BR>--4 To<BR>befall. --Caus. To rout, put to flight;<BR>पुररक्षानभिद्राव्य Dk. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रुत
अभिद्रुत p. p. Attacked, overrun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रवः|अभिद्रव
अभिद्रवः, --वणं An attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रवणं|अभिद्रवण
अभिद्रवः, --वणं An attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रुह्
अभिद्रुह् {c4c} P. (A. in epic poetry)<BR>To hate, seek to injure or<BR>maliciously assail, plot against (with<BR>acc.); नित्यमस्मच्छरीरमभिद्रोग्धुं यतते<BR>Mu. 1, 2; क्रूरमभिद्रुह्यति Sk.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-b" target="_blank">Page0130-b+ 57</a>]<BR>(sometimes with dat. also); मया पुनरेभ्य<BR>एवाभिद्रुग्धमज्ञेन U. 6; नभिद्रुह्यति<BR>भूतेभ्यः Bhāg., Mu. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रुह्
अभिद्रुह् a. Ved. Seeking to injure,<BR>inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिद्रोहः|अभिद्रोह
अभिद्रोहः<BR>1 Injuring, plotting<BR>against, harm, cruelty, oppression;<BR>Ms. 8. 271; Ki. 11. 21.<BR>--2 Abuse;<BR>censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधर्मः|अभिधर्म
अभिधर्मः The Supreme truth<BR>or Metaphysics according to<BR>Buddhistic dogmas.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पिटकः<BR>‘basket of Metaphysics’, one of<BR>the three sections (पिटक) of<BR>Buddhist holy writings which treat of<BR>अभिधर्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधर्षणं|अभिधर्षण
अभिधर्षणं<BR>1 Possession by evil<BR>spirits, demons &c.<BR>--2 Oppressing.<BR>--3<BR>Striking against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधा
अभिधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 (a) To say,<BR>speak, tell (with acc., rarely with<BR>dat.); सा तथ्यमेवाभिहिता भवेन<BR>Ku. 3. 63; Ms. 1. 42; Bk. 7. 78;<BR>Bg. 18. 68. (b) To denote, express or<BR>convey directly or primarily (as sense<BR>&c.); state, mention, set forth;<BR>साक्षात्संकेतितं योर्थमभिधत्ते स वाचकः K. P. 2;<BR>तन्नाम येनाभिदधाति सत्त्वं. (c) To speak<BR>or say to, address.<BR>--2 To name, call,<BR>designate; usually in pass.<BR>--(धीयते);<BR>इदं शरीरं कौंतेय क्षेत्रमित्यभिधीयते<BR>Bg. 13. 1.<BR>--3 To lay or put on, fasten, bind;<BR>to overlay, load; assail; receive,<BR>comprehend, include; to draw<BR>oneself towards, hold, support (mostly<BR>Ved. in these senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधा
अभिधा a. Ved. Naming; praised,<BR>invoked.<BR>--धा<BR>1 A name, appellation;<BR>oft. in comp.; कुसुमवसंताद्यभिधः S. D.<BR>--2 A word, sound.<BR>--3 The literal<BR>power or sense of a word, denotation,<BR>one of the three powers of a word;<BR>वाच्योर्थोऽभिधया बोध्यः S. D. 2 ‘the<BR>expressed meaning is that which is<BR>conveyed to the understanding by<BR>the word's denotation’, for it is this<BR>अभिधा that conveys to the<BR>understanding the meaning which belongs<BR>to the word by common consent or<BR>convention (संकेत) (which primarily<BR>made it a word at all); स<BR>मुख्योऽर्थस्तत्र मुख्यो यो व्यापारोऽस्याभिधोच्यते<BR>K. P. 2.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ध्वंसिन् a. losing one's<BR>name.<BR>--मूल a. founded on a word's<BR>denotation or literal meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानं|अभिधान
अभिधानं<BR>1 Telling, mentioning,<BR>speaking, naming, denotation;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-c" target="_blank">Page0130-c+ 58</a>]<BR>एतावतामर्थानामिदमभिधानं Nir.; गोशब्दस्यं<BR>वाहिकार्थाभिधानं S. D.<BR>--2 (In gram.)<BR>Asserting or predicating something<BR>of another, as the subject of an<BR>assertion, (which then can be put<BR>in the nom. case only);<BR>predication, assertion; See P. II. 3. 2 Sk.<BR>--3 A name, appellation, title,<BR>designation; अभिधानं तु पश्चात्तस्याहमश्रौषं<BR>K. 32; तवाभिधानाद् व्यथते नताननः<BR>Ki. 1. 24; (at the end of comp.) called,<BR>named; ऋणाभिधानाद् बंधनात्<BR>R. 3. 20.<BR>--4 An expression, word.<BR>--5<BR>Speech, discourse.<BR>--6 A dictionary,<BR>vocabulary (of words), lexicon (in<BR>these last {4} senses said to be also<BR>m.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चिंतामणिः N. of a<BR>celebrated vocabulary of synonyms<BR>by Hemacandra.<BR>--माला a<BR>dictionary.<BR>--रत्नमाला N. of a vocabulary<BR>of words by Halāyudha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानकं|अभिधानक
अभिधानकं A sound, voice, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधायक
अभिधायक (यिका f.), अभिधायिन्<BR>a.<BR>1 Naming, expressing, denoting;<BR>एतेषामभिधायकानि क्लीबे स्युः Sk.; कर्षूः<BR>कुल्याभिधायिनी Ak. denotes, means,<BR>has the sense of.<BR>--2 Saying,<BR>speaking, telling; लक्ष्मीमित्यभिधायिनि<BR>प्रियतमे Amaru. 23; वाच्याभिधायी पुरुषः<BR>पृष्ठमांसाद उच्यते Trik.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधेय|अभिधेयं
अभिधेय pot. p.<BR>1 To be named,<BR>mentioned, expressed &c.; वागेव मे<BR>नाभिधेयविषयमवतरति त्रपया K. 151 words<BR>refuse, through shame, to express<BR>what I have to say.<BR>--2 Nameable,<BR>as a category or predicament (in<BR>logic); अभिधेयाः पदार्थाः, अभिधेयत्वं<BR>पदार्थसामान्यलक्षणं.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Signification,<BR>meaning, sense, import; P. I. 1. 34 Sk.;<BR>Ki. 14. 5.<BR>--2 A substance.<BR>--3 The<BR>subject matter; इहाभिधेयं सप्रयोजनं<BR>K. P. 1; इति प्रयोजनाभिधेयसंबंधाः<BR>Mugdha.<BR>--4 The primary or literal sense of<BR>a word (= अभिधा);<BR>अभिधेयाविनाभूतप्रतीतिर्लक्षणोच्यते K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहित|अभिहितं
अभिहित p. p.<BR>1 (a) Said, declared,<BR>spoken, mentioned; मयाभिहितं,<BR>तेनाभिहितं &c. (b) Predicated, asserted;<BR>अनभिहिते कर्मणि द्वितीया P. II. 3. 1-2. (c)<BR>Spoken to, addressed, called, named.<BR>(d) Whispered, prompted to say;<BR>determined.<BR>--2 Fastened, placed<BR>upon.<BR>--तं A name, expression, word;<BR>˚त्वं being said or spoken to, a<BR>declaration; authority, test.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वयवादः, --वादिन् m. a particular<BR>doctrine (or the follower of that doctrine)<BR>on the import of words, as opposed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">Page0131-a+ 57</a>]<BR>to अन्विताभिधानवाद, --वादिन्. The<BR>anvitābhidhānavādins (the Mīmāṃsakas,<BR>the followers of Prabhākara)<BR>hold that words only express a<BR>meaning (अभिधान) as parts of a<BR>sentence and grammatically connected<BR>with one another (अन्वित); that they,<BR>in fact, only imply an action or<BR>something connected with an<BR>action; e. g. घटं in घटं आनय means<BR>not merely ‘jar’, but ‘jar’ as<BR>connected with the action of ‘bringing’<BR>expressed by the verb. The<BR>abhihitānvayavādins (the Naiyāyikas, or<BR>the followers of Kumārila who<BR>hold the same doctrine) on the<BR>other hand hold that words by<BR>themselves can express their own<BR>independent meanings which are<BR>afterwards combined into a sentence<BR>expressing one connected idea; that,<BR>in other words, it is the logical<BR>connection between the words of a<BR>sentence, and not the sense of the<BR>words themselves, that suggests the<BR>import or purport of that sentence;<BR>they thus believe in a tātparyārtha<BR>as distinguished from vāchyārtha;<BR>see K. P. 2 and Maheśvara's<BR>commentary ad loc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0130-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहितिः|अभिहिति
अभिहितिः f. Naming, speaking &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधानी
अभिधानी Ved. A halter, rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधाव्
अभिधाव् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To run up<BR>towards, fly at or towards.<BR>--2 To rush<BR>upon, attack, assail; Bk. 6. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधावक|अभिधावकः
अभिधावक a. Assailing, rushing<BR>upon.<BR>--कः An assailant; Y. 2. 234.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधावनं|अभिधावन
अभिधावनं Assault, pursuit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिधृष्णु
अभिधृष्णु a. Ved.<BR>Overpowering, subduing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्यै
अभिध्यै {c1c} P. (epic {c2c} P.)<BR>1 To<BR>meditate upon, reflect, consider,<BR>think of; यदभिध्याम्यहं शश्वच्छुभं वा<BR>यदि वाशुभं Mb.<BR>--2 To covet, wish<BR>or desire for; Y. 3. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्या
अभिध्या [ध्यै-अङ्]<BR>1 Coveting<BR>another's property.<BR>--2 Longing, wish;<BR>desire in general; अभिध्योपदेशात् Br.<BR>Sūt.<BR>--3 Desire of taking (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिध्यानं|अभिध्यान
अभिध्यानं<BR>1 Desiring or longing for,<BR>coveting; a wish or desire;<BR>परद्रव्येष्वभिध्यानं Ms. 12. 5.<BR>--2 Meditation,<BR>profound thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनंद्|अभिनन्द्
अभिनंद् {c1c} P. (rarely Ā.)<BR>1<BR>(a) To rejoice at or in, exult over,<BR>be glad or satisfied;<BR>आत्मविडंबनामभिनंदंति K. 108; Dk. 75. (b) To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">Page0131-b+ 57</a>]<BR>celebrate (with rejoicings^1 &c.);<BR>महोत्सवेन मज्जन्माभिनंदितवान् K. 137;<BR>नाभिनंदति न द्वेष्टि Bg. 2. 57.<BR>--2 To<BR>congratulate, hail with joy, welcome, greet;<BR>एनां परिष्वज्य तातकाश्यपेनैवं अभिनंदितं<BR>Ś. 4; तापसीभिरभिनंद्यमाना शकुंतला<BR>तिष्ठति ibid., 5, 6, 7; अभिनंदितागमेनषु<BR>समीरेषु K. 49, 63; अभिनंद्य ब्रवीति<BR>Mv. 2 says (writes) after compliments;<BR>R. 2. 74, 3. 68, 7. 69, 71;<BR>30; 16. 64; 17. 15, 60; Y. 1. 332.<BR>--3 To rejoice at, approve, praise,<BR>applaud, commend; यो रत्नराशीनपि<BR>विहाय अभिनंद्यते Ś. 2; अतस्ते<BR>वचो नाभिनंदामि ibid. do not approve;<BR>तद्युक्तमस्या अभिलाषोऽभिनंदितुं Ś. 3;<BR>श्रूयंते परिणीतास्ताः (कन्यकाः)<BR>पितृभिश्चाभिनंदिताः 3. 24; नाम यस्याभिनंदंति<BR>द्विषोपि स पुमान्पुमान् Ki. 11. 73; 4. 4;<BR>with न reject; R. 12. 35.<BR>--4 To care<BR>for, like, desire or wish for, respect,<BR>delight in (usually with न in this<BR>sense); नाभिनंदति केलिकलाः Māl. 3;<BR>नाहारमभिनंदति K. 61; Dk. 159;<BR>आर्यपुत्रस्यैव मनोरथंसपत्तिमभिनंदामि Ve. 2<BR>wish or desire; नाभिनंदेत मरणं<BR>नाभिनंदेत जीवितं Ms. 6. 45, H. 4. 4.<BR>--5<BR>To bless, grant success to; U. 5. 28.<BR>--Caus. To gladden, delight.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनंद|अभिनन्द|अभिनन्दः
अभिनंद a. That which delights,<BR>encourages, praises &c.<BR>--दः<BR>1<BR>Rejoicing, delighting, joy, delight.<BR>--2<BR>Praising, applauding, approving,<BR>greeting, congratulating.<BR>--3 Wish,<BR>desire.<BR>--4 Encouraging, inciting to<BR>action.<BR>--5 Very little happiness<BR>(सुखलव).<BR>--6 An epithet of परमात्मन्<BR>the Supreme Being.<BR>--दा Delight;<BR>wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनंदनं|अभिनन्दन|अभिनन्दनः
अभिनंदनं<BR>1 Rejoicing at, greeting,<BR>welcoming.<BR>--2 Praising, approving.<BR>--3 Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनंदनीय|अभिनन्दनीय
अभिनंदनीय --नंद्य pot. p. To be<BR>rejoiced at, praised, or applauded;<BR>काममेतदभिनंदनीयं Ś. 5; R. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनंद्य|अभिनन्द्य
अभिनंदनीय --नंद्य pot. p. To be<BR>rejoiced at, praised, or applauded;<BR>काममेतदभिनंदनीयं Ś. 5; R. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनंदिन्|अभिनन्दिन्
अभिनंदिन् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Rejoicing at, approving, praising &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनभः
अभिनभः, --नभ्यं adv. Ved. Towards<BR>the clouds or heaven; Śi. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनभ्यं|अभिनभ्य
अभिनभः, --नभ्यं adv. Ved. Towards<BR>the clouds or heaven; Śi. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनम्
अभिनम् {c1c} P. To bow, to bend,<BR>to turn towards a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनम्र
अभिनम्र a. Bent, deeply bowed or<BR>bent; स्तनाभिरामस्तबकाभिनम्रां R. 13. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनव|अभिनवः
अभिनव a. [आधिक्येन नवः, भृशार्थे<BR>अभिरत्र]<BR>1 (a) Quite new or fresh<BR>(in all senses); पदपंक्तिर्दृश्यतेऽभिनवा<BR>Ś. 3. 8; 5. 1; ˚कंठशोणित 6. 26;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">Page0131-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Me. 98; R. 9. 29; ˚वा वधूः K. 2 newly<BR>married. (b) Quite young or fresh,<BR>blooming, youthful (as body, age<BR>&c.); Ś. 1. 19; U. 5. 12; the younger;<BR>˚शाकटायनः; ˚भोजः &c. (c) Fresh,<BR>recent.<BR>--2 Very young, not<BR>having experience.<BR>--वः [अभिनु अप्]<BR>Praise to win over, flattery.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्भिद् --दः a new shoot or bud.<BR>--चंद्रार्धविधिः a ceremony performed at<BR>the time of the new moon.<BR>--तामरसं {1} a fresh-blown lotus. {2} a kind<BR>of metre.<BR>--यौवन, --वयस्क a. youthful,<BR>very young.<BR>--वैयाकरणः one who has<BR>newly begun his study of grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनह्
अभिनह् {c4c} P. To bind up(as the<BR>eyes), to bind, tie, fasten; Śi. 6. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनहनं|अभिनहन
अभिनहनं A bandage (over the<BR>eyes), a blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिधन|अभिनिधनं
अभिनिधन a. [अभिगतो निधनं मरणं]<BR>About to perish, approaching one's<BR>doom.<BR>--नं N. of certain verses of<BR>the Sāmaveda repeated at this time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिधानं|अभिनिधान
अभिनिधानं<BR>1 Putting on,<BR>setting up.<BR>--2 Euphonic suppression,<BR>weakening in the pronunciation of<BR>words, especially the suppression of<BR>an initial अ after ए or ओ; cf. अवग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनियुक्त
अभिनियुक्त a. Occupied in, busy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनियोगः
अभिनियोगः Close application,<BR>attention or intentness, absorption;<BR>कार्य˚ Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्मुक्त|अभिनिर्मुक्तः|अभिनिर्म्मुक्त
अभिनिर्मुक्त a.<BR>1 Left or quitted<BR>(by the sun when it sets).<BR>--2 One<BR>asleep at sunset and thus not doing<BR>the duties to be then performed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्याणं|अभिनिर्याण|अभिनिर्य्याण
अभिनिर्याणं<BR>1 A march.<BR>--2<BR>Invasion, marching against an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिर्वृत्तिः|अभिनिर्वृत्ति
अभिनिर्वृत्तिः^1 f. Accomplishment,<BR>completion.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: missing 'r' diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवर्तः|अभिनिवर्त|अभिनिवर्त्त
अभिनिवर्तः Turning towards,<BR>turning again and again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिविश्
अभिनिविश् {c6c} A. (P. I. 4. 47)<BR>(a) To enter into, be settled in; to<BR>occupy, set foot in. (b) To take<BR>possession of, resort to, be attached to<BR>(with acc.); अभिनिविशते सन्मार्गं Sk.<BR>takes to, follows, a good path; सैवं<BR>धन्या गणिकादारिका यामेवं<BR>भवन्मनोऽभिनिविशते Dk. 57, Mu. 5. 12,<BR>Bk. 8. 80. --Caus. To make one enter or<BR>occupy, lead, carry or conduct to; (fig.)<BR>apply, direct or turn (as mind, heart<BR>&c.) towards something;<BR>प्रतिबंधवत्स्वपि विषयेषु अभिनिवेश्य M. 3, Śi. 1. 15<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिविष्ट
अभिनिविष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Intent on,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-a" target="_blank">Page0132-a+ 57</a>]<BR>engrossed in, engaged in or<BR>occupied with, applying oneself to;<BR>माधवापकारं प्रति अभिनिविष्टा भवामि<BR>Māl. 6.<BR>--2 Firmly or steadily<BR>fixed, uncontrollably fixed, steady,<BR>attentive, intent;<BR>अत्यभिनिविष्टवित्तदर्पस्य Dk. 29; Māl. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Endowed with, possessed of;<BR>गुरुभिरभिनिविष्टं (गर्भं) लोकपालानुभावैः<BR>R. 2. 75.<BR>--4 Determined, resolute,<BR>persevering.<BR>--5 (In a bad sense)<BR>Obstinate, perverse; Śi. 16. 43;<BR>Ki. 17. 11.<BR>--6 Well-versed or proficient<BR>in.<BR>--ष्टं Perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0131-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिविष्टता
अभिनिविष्टता Resoluteness,<BR>determination of purpose;<BR>निंदाक्षेपापमानादेरमर्षोऽभिनिविष्टता S. D. i. e.<BR>adhering to one's purpose, not minding<BR>censure, abuse, dishonour &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवेशः|अभिनिवेश
अभिनिवेशः<BR>1 (a) Devotion,<BR>attachment, intentness, being<BR>occupied with, adherence to, close<BR>application, with loc. or in comp.;<BR>कतमस्मिंस्ते भावाभिनिवेशः V. 3; अहो<BR>निरर्थकव्यापारेष्वभिनिवेशः K. 120, 146, Dk. 81;<BR>Māl. 7. (b) Firm attachment, love,<BR>fondness, affection; बलीयान् खलु<BR>मेऽभिनिवेशः Ś. 3; अनुरूपोऽस्या ˚शः ibid.,<BR>V. 2; असत्यभूते वस्तुन्यभिनिवेशः Mit.<BR>--2 Earnest desire, ardent longing or<BR>expectation; wish, desire;<BR>Māl. 5. 27.<BR>--3 Resolution, determined<BR>resolve, determination of purpose,<BR>firmness of resolve, perseverance;<BR>जनकात्मजायां नितांतरूक्षाभिनिवेशमीशं<BR>R. 14. 43; अनुरूप˚ शतोषिणा Ku. 5. 7;<BR>Śi. 3. 1. (b) Idea, thought; Ms. 12. 5;<BR>Y. 3. 155.<BR>--4 (In Yoga phil.) A sort<BR>of ignorance causing fear of death;<BR>instinctive clinging to worldly life<BR>and bodily enjoyments and the fear<BR>that one might be cut off from all of<BR>them by death; अविद्याऽ<BR>स्मितारागद्वेषाभिनिवेशाः पंचक्लेशाः Yoga S.; cf. also<BR>Sāṅ. K. 150 and Malli. on<BR>Śi. 4. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिवेशिन्
अभिनिवेशिन् a.<BR>1 Devoted to,<BR>intent on, adhering or clinging to;<BR>कल्याणाभिनिवेशिनः K. 136 of blessed<BR>or noble resolve, 191.<BR>--2 Fixing on,<BR>directing or turning (the mind) to;<BR>गुणेष्वभिनिवेशिनो भर्तुरपि प्रिया M. 3;<BR>अहो नु खलु दुर्लभ ˚शी मदनः V. 1;<BR>Dk. 57.<BR>--3 Determined, resolute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्कारिन्
अभिनिष्कारिन् a. Ved.<BR>1 Doing<BR>completely.<BR>--2 Injuring, thinking<BR>ill of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्क्रमणं|अभिनिष्क्रमण
अभिनिष्क्रमणं<BR>1 Going out or<BR>forth.<BR>--2 (With Buddhists)<BR>Leaving the house to become an anchorite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्टानः|अभिनिष्टान
अभिनिष्टानः [स्तन्-घञ्, सस्य च षत्वं<BR>P. VIII. 3. 86]<BR>1 A sound which<BR>dies away; विसर्जनीयोऽभिनिष्टानः.<BR>--2 A<BR>letter of the alphabet (˚नो वर्णः).<BR>--3<BR>The Visarga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पत्
अभिनिष्पत् {c1c} P. To rush out,<BR>issue, sally, go forth; to spring or<BR>shoot forth; Bk. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पतनं|अभिनिष्पतन
अभिनिष्पतनं Sallying, issuing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पद्
अभिनिष्पद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To go or come<BR>to.<BR>--2 To enter into, become.<BR>--3 To<BR>appear, become visible. --Caus. To<BR>bring to, help to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिष्पत्तिः|अभिनिष्पत्ति
अभिनिष्पत्तिः f. Completion, end,<BR>accomplishment, fulfilment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनिह्नवः|अभिनिह्नव
अभिनिह्नवः Denial, concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनी
अभिनी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring near,<BR>conduct or lead towards, carry to;<BR>तटाभिनीतेनांभसा Ki. 8. 32; अमात्यस्य<BR>गृहजनं स्वगृहमभिनीय रक्षसि Mu. 1,<BR>5; 6. 15; दृष्ट्वा शरं ज्यामभिनीयमानं Mb.<BR>being fitted to the bow.<BR>--2 To act,<BR>represent or exhibit dramatically,<BR>gesticulate; mostly occurring in<BR>stagedirections; श्रुतिमभिनीय Ś. 3 acting<BR>as if he heard something; Mu. 1. 2,<BR>3. 31, M. 2. 6.<BR>--3 To quote, adduce,<BR>introduce.<BR>--4 To allow to elapse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनयः|अभिनय
अभिनयः<BR>1 Acting, gesticulation,<BR>any theatrical action (expressive<BR>of some sentiment, passion &c. by<BR>look, gesture, posture &c.);<BR>नृत्याभिनयक्रियाच्युतं Ku. 5. 79; अभिनयान्<BR>परिचेतुमिवोद्यता R. 9. 33;<BR>नर्तकीरभिनयातिलंघिनीः 19. 14; Ki. 10. 42.<BR>--2 Dramatic representation,<BR>exhibition on the stage; ललिताभिनयं तमद्य<BR>भर्ता मरुतां द्रष्टुमनाः सलोकपालः V. 2. 18.<BR>S. D. thus defines and classifies<BR>अभिनयः-भवेदभिनयोऽवस्थानुकारः स चतुर्विधः ।<BR>अंगिको वाचिकश्चैवमाहार्यः सात्त्विकस्तथा ॥<BR>274, ‘acting is the imitation of<BR>condition’; it is of four kinds:-- (1)<BR>gestural, conveyed by bodily<BR>actions; (2) vocal, conveyed by words;<BR>(3) extraneous, conveyed by dress,<BR>ornaments, decoration &c.; (4)<BR>internal, conveyed by the<BR>manifestation of internal feelings such as<BR>perspiration, thrilling &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचार्यः a dancing preceptor<BR>M. 1. 10.<BR>--विद्या science of acting or<BR>dramatic representation, art of<BR>dancing; मया तीर्थादभिनयविद्याशिक्षिता M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनीत|अभिनीतः
अभिनीत p. p.<BR>1 Brought near,<BR>conveyed.<BR>--2 Performed,<BR>represented dramatically.<BR>--3 Highly finished<BR>or polished, most excellent.<BR>--4<BR>Highly ornamented or decorated.<BR>--5 Fit,<BR>proper, suitable (योग्य); अभिनीततरं<BR>वाक्यमित्युवाच युधिष्ठिरः Mb.<BR>--6<BR>Patient, forgiving, even-minded.<BR>--7<BR>Angry (युक्तेऽतिसंस्कृतेमर्षिण्यभिनीतः Ak.<BR>where the word may be अमर्षिणि as<BR>well).<BR>--8 Kind, friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनीतिः|अभिनीति
अभिनीतिः f.<BR>1 Gesture, expressive<BR>gesticulation.<BR>--2 Kindness,<BR>friendship, patience; सांत्वपूर्वमभिनीतिहेतुकं<BR>Ki. 13. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेय
अभिनेय, --नेतव्य pot. p. To be acted<BR>or dramatically represented &c.;<BR>दृश्यं तत्राभिनेयं तद्रूपारोपात्तु रूपकं<BR>S. D. 273; M. 1; तस्य (प्रबंधस्य)<BR>एकदेशः अभिनेयार्थः कृतः U. 4 a part of it<BR>has been adapted to the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेतव्य
अभिनेय, --नेतव्य pot. p. To be acted<BR>or dramatically represented &c.;<BR>दृश्यं तत्राभिनेयं तद्रूपारोपात्तु रूपकं<BR>S. D. 273; M. 1; तस्य (प्रबंधस्य)<BR>एकदेशः अभिनेयार्थः कृतः U. 4 a part of it<BR>has been adapted to the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिनेतृ
अभिनेतृ m. An actor.<BR>--त्री An<BR>actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिन्न
अभिन्न a.<BR>1 Not broken or cut,<BR>unbroken; not split; अभिन्नपुटोत्तरान्<BR>R. 17. 12.<BR>--2 Unaffected;<BR>क्लेशलेशैरभिन्नं Ś. 2. 4.<BR>--3 Not changed or<BR>altered, unchanged; ˚गतयः Ś. 1. 14<BR>with their gait unchanged.<BR>--4 Not<BR>different from, the same, identical<BR>(with abl.);<BR>जगन्मिथोभिन्नमभिन्नमीश्वरात् Prab.<BR>--5 Undivided, whole,<BR>one (as number).<BR>--6 Holding<BR>together, continuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिन्यासः|अभिन्यास
अभिन्यासः A kind of fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपत्
अभिपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fly near, go<BR>or hasten near, approach;<BR>हंतुमभिपतति पांडुसुतं Ki. 12. 36;<BR>अधिरोढुमस्तगिरिमभ्यपतत् Śi. 9. 1; Dk. 72, 128;<BR>Mk. 9. 12; Ki. 10. 42.<BR>--2 To fall upon,<BR>attack, assail; यंता गजस्याभ्यपतद्गजस्थं<BR>R. 7. 37; Dk. 62, 70, 96; Ki. 7. 19.<BR>--3 To<BR>fall down, fall (as tears).<BR>--4 To<BR>fall into, enter or come into.<BR>--5 To<BR>overtake in flying.<BR>--6 To pass over,<BR>traverse.<BR>--7 To get, back, withdraw,<BR>retire; Śi. 7. 51; Ki. 10. 54.<BR>--8 (4A.)<BR>To be lord or master of (Ved.).<BR>--Caus. To throw upon, throw<BR>down into; ज्वलनमभिपातयामि Ve. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपतनं|अभिपतन
अभिपतनं<BR>1 Approaching.<BR>--2<BR>Falling upon, assault, attack.<BR>--3 Going<BR>forth, departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपद्
अभिपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To go to, draw<BR>near, approach (with acc.);<BR>रावणावरजा तत्र राघवं मदनातुरा । अभिपेदे निदाघार्ता<BR>व्यालीव मलयद्रुमं ॥ R. 12. 32; 19. 11;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">Page0133-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Dk. 166; K. 265; to enter (into)<BR>Śi. 3. 25; sometimes with loc. also.<BR>--2 To look upon, consider, regard;<BR>to take or know to be;<BR>क्षणमभ्यपद्यत जनैर्न मृषा गगनं गणाधिपतिमूर्तिरिति<BR>Śi. 9. 27.<BR>--3 To help, assist; मयाभिपन्नं तं<BR>चापि न सर्पो धर्षयिष्यति Mb.<BR>--4 To seize,<BR>catch hold of; overpower, attack,<BR>subdue, take possession of,<BR>overcome, afflict; सर्वतश्चाभिपन्नैषा धार्तराष्ट्री<BR>महाचमूः, चंडवाताभिपन्नानामुदधीनामिव<BR>स्वनः Mb.; see अभिपन्न also.<BR>--5 (a) To take,<BR>assume; Ms. 1. 30. (b) To accept,<BR>receive; निरास्वाद्यतमं शून्यं (राज्यं)<BR>भरतो नाभिपत्स्यते Rām.<BR>--6 To apply<BR>or devote oneself to, undertake,<BR>fall to, observe; स चिंतामभ्यपद्यत<BR>Rām.<BR>--7 To honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0132-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपत्तिः|अभिपत्ति
अभिपत्तिः f.<BR>1 Approaching,<BR>drawing near.<BR>--2 Completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपन्न|अभिपन्नः
अभिपन्न p. p.<BR>1 Gone or come near,<BR>approached, run towards, gone to (a<BR>state &c.); त्वमन्यमाकारमिवाभिपन्नः<BR>Ki. 3. 46.<BR>--2 Fled, fugitive, seeking<BR>refuge with.<BR>--3 Subdued, overpowered,<BR>afflicted, seized &c.; कालाभिपन्नाः<BR>सीदंति सिकतासेतवो यथा Rām.; यदिदं<BR>सर्वं मृत्युनाभिपन्नं Śat. Br.; दोष˚,<BR>कश्मल˚, व्याघ्र˚ &c.<BR>--4 Unfortunate,<BR>fallen into difficulties &c.<BR>--5<BR>Accepted.<BR>--6 Guilty.<BR>--7 Removed to a<BR>distance.<BR>--8 Dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपद्म
अभिपद्म a. Very beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपरिप्लुत
अभिपरिप्लुत a. Overflowed,<BR>filled with, inundated; (fig.)<BR>overwhelmed, affected; attacked; shaken;<BR>शोकेन, मन्युना &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपित्वं|अभिपित्व
अभिपित्वं a. or s. Ved. [पा भावे<BR>कित्वन्]<BR>1 Come, approaching (<BR>अभिप्राप्त).<BR>--2 Visiting, putting up (for<BR>the night at an inn &c.); the time<BR>of coming.<BR>--3 Approaching time.<BR>--4 Close or departure of day,<BR>evening.<BR>--5 Dawn sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपुष्प
अभिपुष्प a. [अभितः पुष्पाण्यस्य]<BR>Covered over with flowers (as a<BR>tree).<BR>--ष्पं An excellent flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपूज्
अभिपूज् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To adorn,<BR>worship.<BR>--2 To honour; approve,<BR>assent to; तथेति भरतो वाक्यं<BR>वसिष्ठस्याभिपूज्य तत् Rām. ; Ms. 6. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपूजनं|अभिपूजन
अभिपूजनं Honouring; approving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपूर्वं|अभिपूर्व
अभिपूर्वं ind. One after another,<BR>successively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपॄ
अभिपॄ {c3c} {c9c} P. To fill. --pass. To<BR>become full. --Caus.<BR>1 To fill, make<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">Page0133-b+ 56</a>]<BR>full.<BR>--2 To load with (as animals);<BR>cover with.<BR>--3 To present with.<BR>--4<BR>To overwhelm, overpower, master<BR>completely; शोको मामभ्यपूरयत् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिपूरणं|अभिपूरण
अभिपूरणं Filling, overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रज्ञा
अभिप्रज्ञा Thinking constantly of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणी
अभिप्रणी {c1c} P. To lead to, bring<BR>towards; consecrate; जज्वाल<BR>लोकस्थितये स राजा यथाध्वरे वह्निरभिप्रणीतः<BR>Bk. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणयः|अभिप्रणय
अभिप्रणयः Affection, favour,<BR>propitiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रणयनं|अभिप्रणयन
अभिप्रणयनं Consecrating by sacred<BR>hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रतप्त
अभिप्रतप्त a.<BR>1 Intensely<BR>heated.<BR>--2 Dried up.<BR>--3 Exhausted<BR>with pain, fever &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रथनं|अभिप्रथन
अभिप्रथनं Spreading or<BR>extending over, throwing over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रदक्षिणं
अभिप्रदक्षिणं ind. Towards the<BR>right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रपद्
अभिप्रपद् = प्रपद् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रमुर्
अभिप्रमुर् f. The tongue of fire<BR>(जुहू); completely raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रवृत्
अभिप्रवृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To advance<BR>up to, approach, go up to.<BR>--2 To<BR>fall or flow into; यत्र भागीरथीं गंगां<BR>यमुनाऽभिप्रवर्तते Rām.<BR>--3 To become<BR>conversant with. --Caus. To roll<BR>onward or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रवर्तनं|अभिप्रवर्तन|अभिप्रवर्त्तन
अभिप्रवर्तनं<BR>1 Advancing up to.<BR>--2<BR>Proceeding, acting.<BR>--3 Flowing,<BR>coming forth, as of sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रवृत्त
अभिप्रवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Advancing,<BR>going up to.<BR>--2 Occurring.<BR>--3 Engaged<BR>or occupied in (with loc.); Bg. 4. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रश्निन्
अभिप्रश्निन् a. Ved. Desirous of<BR>asking many questions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राणनं|अभिप्राणन
अभिप्राणनं Exhaling (opp. अपाननं)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राप्
अभिप्राप्, --प्तिः &c. = प्राप् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राप्तिः|अभिप्राप्ति
अभिप्राप्, --प्तिः &c. = प्राप् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रीतिः|अभिप्रीति
अभिप्रीतिः f. Wish; rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रे
अभिप्रे [अभिप्र-इ] {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go to<BR>or near, approach; कर्मणा यमभिप्रैति स<BR>संप्रदानं P. I. 4. 32.<BR>--2 To intend,<BR>aim at, think of, mean; cf. अभिप्रेत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्राय|अभिप्रायः
अभिप्राय a. [इ-अच्] Going near,<BR>approaching; aiming at,<BR>intending, meaning, accruing to;<BR>कर्माभिप्राये क्रियाफले P. I. 3. 72.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>Aim, purpose, object, intention, wish,<BR>desire; अभिप्राया न सिद्ध्यंति तेनेदं वर्तते<BR>जगत् Pt. 1. 158; साभिप्रायाणि वचांसि<BR>Pt. 2 earnest words; भावः<BR>कवेरभिप्रायः<BR>--2 Meaning, sense, import,<BR>implied sense of a word, passage &c.;<BR>तेषामयमभिप्रायः such is the meaning<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">Page0133-c+ 55</a>]<BR>intended, import (of the passage<BR>&c.).<BR>--3 Opinion, belief.<BR>--4<BR>Relation, reference.<BR>--5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रेत|अभिप्रेतं
अभिप्रेत p. p.<BR>1 Meant, aimed at,<BR>intended; designed; अत्रायमर्थोऽभिप्रेतः;<BR>किमभिप्रेतमनया Bh. 3. 67;<BR>निवेदयाभिप्रेतं Pt. 1.<BR>--2 Wished, desired;<BR>यथाभिप्रेतमनुष्ठीयतां H. 1.<BR>--3 Approved,<BR>accepted; पूर्वैरयमभिप्रेतो गतो<BR>मार्गोनुगम्यते Rām.<BR>--4 Dear or agreeable to,<BR>favourite with, beloved;<BR>धर्मस्तवाभिप्रेतः Dk. 42; Ś. 6.<BR>--5 Wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्रोक्षणं|अभिप्रोक्षण
अभिप्रोक्षणं Sprinkling upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्लु
अभिप्लु {c4c} A.<BR>1 To go up to,<BR>jump or leap towards.<BR>--2 To over<BR>flow; (fig.) affect, fill with,<BR>overwhelm; तमसाभिप्लुते लोके रजसा च<BR>Mb.; रजसाभिप्लुतां नारीं Ms. 4. 41<BR>being in her courses; Y. 2. 50.<BR>--3<BR>To spring to or over, spring upon.<BR>--Caus. To wash or ripple against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिप्लवः|अभिप्लव
अभिप्लवः<BR>1 Affliction, disturbance.<BR>--2 Inundation, overflowing.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a religious ceremony performed<BR>as part of the sacrifice गवामयन.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of the Prājāpatya Āditya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिबलं|अभिबल
अभिबलं A technical term in<BR>Rhetoric; अभिबलमभिसंधिश्छलेन यः<BR>S. D. 375 ‘an inquiry or<BR>examination by an artifice’. See Ratn. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिबुद्धिः|अभिबुद्धि
अभिबुद्धिः f. An organ of<BR>apprehension, a बुद्धींद्रिय or ज्ञानेंद्रिय (opp.<BR>कर्मेद्रिय); these are the eye, tongue,<BR>ear, nose and skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभंगः|अभिभङ्ग|अभिभङ्गः
अभिभंगः<BR>1 Breaking down.<BR>--2<BR>One who breaks down or destroys.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभा
अभिभा {c2c} P. To glitter or shine;<BR>दिवि स्थितः सूर्य इवाभिभाति Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभा
अभिभा Ved. [अभिभा-अङ्]<BR>1<BR>Apparition, phenomenon; an<BR>inauspicious omen.<BR>--2 A calamity, state of<BR>being overpowered.<BR>--3 Superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभार
अभिभार a. Very heavy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाष्
अभिभाष् A. (P. in epic<BR>poetry)<BR>1 To speak to, address;<BR>talk or converse with (with acc.);<BR>भोभवत्पूर्वकं त्वेनमभिभाषेत धर्मवित्<BR>Ms. 2. 128; sometimes with instr. also;<BR>Ms. 4. 57.<BR>--2 To speak, say (as<BR>वाणीं, वचः &c.); इति अभिभाषंते so<BR>they say.<BR>--3 To relate, narrate,<BR>speak of.<BR>--4 To proclaim, announce,<BR>confess; Ms. 11. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाषणं|अभिभाषण
अभिभाषणं Speaking to,<BR>addressing, conversing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0133-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाषिन्
अभिभाषिन् a. Addressing,<BR>speaking to; speaking, talking;<BR>स्मितपूर्वाभिभाषिणं R. 17. 31 whose words are<BR>preceded by a smile, speaking with<BR>a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभू
अभिभू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To overcome,<BR>subdue, conquer, vanquish (of persons<BR>or things); prevail over,<BR>predominate, defeat; (hence) excel, surpass;<BR>अभिभवति मनः कदंबवायौ Ki. 10. 23;<BR>अभिभूय विभूतिमार्तवीं R. 8. 36; 4. 56;<BR>6. 29, 16. 10; K. 52, 53;<BR>Mu. 3. 20; Ms. 7. 5; धर्मे नष्टे कुलं<BR>कृत्स्नमधर्मोऽभिभवत्युत Bg. 1. 40 predominates<BR>over, overpowers; so शोकाभिभूत,<BR>विपद्˚, काम˚ &c.<BR>--2 To attack, seize<BR>or fall upon, assail; विपदोऽ<BR>भिभवंत्यविक्रमं Ki. 2. 14; अभ्यभावि<BR>भरताग्रजस्तया R. 11. 16, 84; Bṛ. S. 33. 30;<BR>ममापि सत्त्वैरभिभूयंते गृहाः Ś. 6<BR>infested; परित्रायध्वं मामनेन<BR>मधुकरेणाभिभूयमानां Ś. 1 attacked, troubled;<BR>अभ्यभून्निलयं भ्रातुः Bk. 6. 117.<BR>--3 To humiliate,<BR>mortify, insult, disrespect;<BR>अंडभंगाभिभूता Pt. 1.<BR>--4 To go up to, turn<BR>to or towards (Ved.) --Caus. To<BR>overpower, surpass, defeat &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवः|अभिभव
अभिभवः<BR>1 Defeat, subjugation,<BR>subjection, overpowering;<BR>इतरेतरानभिभवेन मृगास्तमुपासते गुरुमिवांतसदः<BR>Ki. 6. 34 (cf. K. 45 and the Bible<BR>“The wolf shall also dwell with<BR>the lamb” &c.); 8. 28; स्पर्शानुकूला<BR>इव सूर्यकांतास्तदन्यतेजोभिभवाद्वमंति<BR>Ś. 2. 7 when assailed, opposed,<BR>overpowered by another energy;<BR>अभिभवः कुत एव सपत्नजः R. 9. 4, 4. 21.<BR>--2 Being overpowered;<BR>जराभिभवविच्छायं K. 346; being attacked or<BR>affected, stupefied (by fever &c.); न<BR>रोगशांतिर्न चाभिभवः Suśr.<BR>--3 Contempt,<BR>disrespect; निरभिभवसाराः परकथाः<BR>Bh. 2. 64.<BR>--4 Humiliation,<BR>mortification (of pride);<BR>अलभ्यशोकाभिभवेयमाकृतिः Ku. 5. 43; K. 195.<BR>--5<BR>Predominance, prevalence, rise, spread;<BR>अधर्माभिभवात्कृष्ण प्रदुष्यंति कुलस्त्रियः<BR>Bg. 1. 41; Ki. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभवनं|अभिभवन
अभिभवनं Overpowering,<BR>overcoming, being subjected to or<BR>overpowered by; Ms. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभावनं|अभिभावन
अभिभावनं Making victorious,<BR>overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभाविन्
अभिभाविन्, --भाव(वु)क a.<BR>1<BR>Overpowering, defeating, conquering;<BR>शोकाभिभाविना भयेनाभिभूता K. 170<BR>fear which conquered grief.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">Page0134-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Surpassing, excelling; सर्वतेजोभिभाविना<BR>R. 1. 14; Ki. 11. 6.<BR>--3<BR>Disrespecting, humiliating.<BR>--4 Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभावक
अभिभाविन्, --भाव(वु)क a.<BR>1<BR>Overpowering, defeating, conquering;<BR>शोकाभिभाविना भयेनाभिभूता K. 170<BR>fear which conquered grief.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">Page0134-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Surpassing, excelling; सर्वतेजोभिभाविना<BR>R. 1. 14; Ki. 11. 6.<BR>--3<BR>Disrespecting, humiliating.<BR>--4 Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभावुक
अभिभाविन्, --भाव(वु)क a.<BR>1<BR>Overpowering, defeating, conquering;<BR>शोकाभिभाविना भयेनाभिभूता K. 170<BR>fear which conquered grief.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">Page0134-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Surpassing, excelling; सर्वतेजोभिभाविना<BR>R. 1. 14; Ki. 11. 6.<BR>--3<BR>Disrespecting, humiliating.<BR>--4 Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभुः|अभिभु
अभिभुः --भूः Ved. One who<BR>surpasses or prevails over, a superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूः
अभिभुः --भूः Ved. One who<BR>surpasses or prevails over, a superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूति|अभिभूतिः
अभिभूति a. That which defeats,<BR>conquers &c.<BR>--तिः<BR>1 Predominance,<BR>prevalence, excessive or superior<BR>power.<BR>--2 Conquering, defeat,<BR>subjugation; अभिभूतिभयादसूनतः<BR>सुखमुज्झंति न धाम मानिनः Ki. 2. 20.<BR>--3<BR>Disrespect, disgrace, humiliation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ओजस् a. of superior or<BR>predominant power. (--n.). superior<BR>power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूयं|अभिभूय
अभिभूयं Ved. Superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिभूवन्
अभिभूवन् a. Ved. Prevailing or<BR>victorious over; surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमद्
अभिमद् {c4c} P. Ved. To gladden,<BR>exhilarate, inebriate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमादः|अभिमाद
अभिमादः Intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाद्यत्क
अभिमाद्यत्क a. Half drunk, partially<BR>intoxicated, stammering (like a<BR>drunkard).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्
अभिमन् {c4c} A. (P. epic)<BR>1 To wish<BR>or desire, long for, covet, like; न<BR>त्वेवं ज्यायसीं वृत्तिमभिमन्येत कर्हिचित्<BR>Ms. 10. 95; see अभिमत below.<BR>--2<BR>To assent to, approve of, allow,<BR>admit; give a grant (to any one, dat.).<BR>--3 To think, fancy, imagine,<BR>consider, believe, regard;<BR>तामार्यामसावन्यथाऽभ्यमन्यत Dk. 164; Bk. 5. 71,<BR>U. 5.<BR>--4 To injure, threaten (Ved.)<BR>--5<BR>({c8c} A.) To think of self.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमत|अभिमतं|अभिमतः
अभिमत p. p.<BR>1 Desired, wished,<BR>liked, dear, beloved, favourite<BR>(person or thing); agreeable, desirable;<BR>नास्ति जीवितादन्यदभिमततरमिह जगति<BR>सर्वजंतूनां K. 35, 58; अभिमतफलशंसी<BR>चारु पुस्फोर बाहुः Bk. 1. 27;<BR>यद्येवमभिमतं Pt. 1 if you like to do so;<BR>तयोरभिमतं वद Mv. 6. 21 choose which<BR>you will; U. 1. 44, Ś. 3. 4,<BR>Ku. 3. 23, Pt. 1. 70, Me. 49,<BR>Mu. 3. 4.<BR>--2 Agreed or assented to,<BR>liked, approved, accepted, admitted;<BR>न किल भवतां स्थानं देव्या गृहेऽभिमतं ततः<BR>U. 3. 32; प्रसिद्धमाहात्म्याभिमतानामपि<BR>कपिलकणभुक्प्रभृतीनां Ś. B. honoured,<BR>respected.<BR>--तं Wish, desire.<BR>--तः<BR>A beloved person, lover; Śi. 7. 72,<BR>8. 68, 10. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमतिः|अभिमति
अभिमतिः f.<BR>1 Desire.<BR>--2 Pride.<BR>--3<BR>Respect, regard, see अभिमान below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमनस्
अभिमनस् a. Intent on, desirous of,<BR>anxious, longing for; भवतोभिमनाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-c" target="_blank">Page0134-c+ 57</a>]<BR>समीहते सरुषः कर्तुमुपेत्य माननां Śi. 16. 2<BR>(where अ˚ also means undaunted,<BR>of fearless mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमनायते
अभिमनायते Den. A. To have life,<BR>be full of life and joy, be pleased or<BR>delighted, to long for; अभ्यमनायिष्ट<BR>चांतरात्मा Dk. 111, 119; कांतिं (<BR>विलोक्य) नाभिमनायेत को वा स्थाणुसमोपि ते<BR>Bk. 5. 73 (Com. = सचेताः or प्रीतमनाः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमंतुः|अभिमन्तु|अभिमन्तुः
अभिमंतुः f. Ved. Injuring,<BR>harming, destroying; ˚तोः to destroy; to<BR>claim as ones' own, pretending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमंतृ|अभिमन्तृ
अभिमंतृ a. Longing for;<BR>self-conceited, referring all objects to self;<BR>Ms. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानः|अभिमान
अभिमानः<BR>1 Pride(in a good sense),<BR>self-respect, honourable or worthy<BR>feeling; सदाभिमानैकधना हि मानिनः<BR>Śi. 1. 67; Bh. 3. 5; अभिमानधनस्य<BR>गत्वरैः Ki. 2. 19;<BR>संकल्पयोनेरभिमानभूतं Ku. 3. 24.<BR>--2 Self-conceit,<BR>pride, arrogance, haughtiness,<BR>egotism, high-opinion of oneself;<BR>शिथिल˚नाः संवृत्ताः M. 2, Bh. 3. 46,<BR>Bg. 16. 4; ˚वत् proud, conceited.<BR>--3<BR>Referring all objects to self, the act of<BR>अहंकार, personality, misconception<BR>(मिथ्याज्ञानं), see अहंकार.<BR>--4 Conceit,<BR>conception; supposition, belief,<BR>opinion; Ki. 13. 7.<BR>--5 Knowledge,<BR>consciousness (बुद्धि, ज्ञान);<BR>साधारण्याभिमानतः S. D.<BR>--6 Affection, love.<BR>--7 Desire, wishing for.<BR>--8 Laying<BR>claim to.<BR>--9 Injury, killing,<BR>seeking to injure.<BR>--10 A sort of state<BR>occasioned by love.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शालिन् a. proud<BR>--शून्य a. void of pride<BR>or arrogance, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानितं|अभिमानित
अभिमानितं<BR>1 Egotism.<BR>--2 Love;<BR>copulation, sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानिन्
अभिमानिन् a.<BR>1 Possessed of<BR>selfrespect; Ki. 1. 31; K. 212.<BR>--2<BR>Having a high opinion of oneself,<BR>proud, arrogant, conceited.<BR>--3<BR>Regarding all objects as referring to<BR>one's own self; अभिमानिव्यपदेशस्तु<BR>विशेषानुगतिभ्यां Br. Sūt.<BR>--4 Fancying,<BR>pretending, or regarding oneself to<BR>be; नरेंद्र˚ Dk. 51; K. 194. --m. A<BR>form of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमानुक
अभिमानुक a. Ved. [मन् वाहु˚ उकच्]<BR>Striving to hurt or injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमंत्र्|अभिमन्त्र्
अभिमंत्र् {c10c} A. (P. also)<BR>1 To<BR>consecrate or accompany with<BR>sacred hymns; पशुरसौ योऽभिमंत्र्य क्रतौ<BR>हतः Ak.; वामदेवाभिमंत्रितोऽश्वः U. 2;<BR>Y. 3. 326; 2. 102; 3. 278.<BR>--2 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">Page0135-a+ 61</a>]<BR>consecrate with magical formulas,<BR>charm, enchant, invoke or invite<BR>by means of charms; तदभिमंत्रितेन<BR>चरणेन Dk. 138; पानीयैरभिमंत्रितैः Mb.<BR>--3 To speak to, address, invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0134-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमंत्रणं|अभिमन्त्रण|अभिमन्त्रणं
अभिमंत्रणं<BR>1 Consecrating, hallowing,<BR>making sacred by repetition of<BR>special formulas or Mantras;<BR>Y. 1. 237; मंत्रमुच्चारयन्नेव मंत्रार्थत्वेन संस्मरेत् ।<BR>शेषिणं तन्मना भूत्वा स्यादेतदभिमंत्रणम् ॥<BR>Mīmāmsā.<BR>--2 Charming, enchanting.<BR>--3 Addressing, inviting; advising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमंथः|अभिमन्थ|अभिमन्थः
अभिमंथः^1 = अधिमंथः q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: due to ref. to hw adhimaṁthaḥ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमन्युः|अभिमन्यु
अभिमन्युः N. of a son of Arjuna<BR>by his wife Subhadrā, sister of<BR>Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma; also known by<BR>the metronymic Saubhadra. [He<BR>was called Abhimanyu because at his<BR>very birth he appeared to be heroic,<BR>longarmed and very fiery (अभिवृद्धः<BR>मन्युर्यस्य). When the Kauravas at the advice<BR>of Droṇa formed the peculiar<BR>battlearray called ‘Chakravyūha,’ hoping<BR>that, as Arjuna was away, none of the<BR>Pāṇḍavas would be able to break<BR>through it, Abhimanyu assured his<BR>uncles that he was ready to try, if they<BR>only assisted him. He accordingly<BR>entered the Vyūha, killed many<BR>warriors on the Kaurava side, and was for a<BR>time more than a match even for such<BR>veteran and elderly heroes as Droṇa,<BR>Karṇa, Duryodhana &c. He could not,<BR>however, hold out long against fearful<BR>odds, and was at last overpowered and<BR>slain. He was very handsome. He had<BR>two wives, Vatsalā daughter of<BR>Balarāma and Uttarā daughter of the king<BR>of Virāṭa. Uttarā was pregnant when<BR>he was slain and gave birth to a son<BR>named Parīkṣita who succeeded to<BR>the throne of Hastināpura].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमरः|अभिमर
अभिमरः [मृ-अच्]<BR>1 Killing,<BR>destruction, slaughter.<BR>--2 War,<BR>combat.<BR>--3 Treachery in one's own<BR>camp; danger from one's own men or<BR>party.<BR>--4 Binding, confinement;<BR>a tie or fetter.<BR>--5 One's own party or<BR>army.<BR>--6 One who desperately goes<BR>to fight with tigers, elephants &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाति|अभिमातिः
अभिमाति a. [मे कर्तरि क्तिन् न इत्त्वं]<BR>Striving or seeking to injure,<BR>inimical.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1 Seeking to injure,<BR>hurting, plotting against.<BR>--2 An<BR>enemy, a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमातिन्
अभिमातिन् a. [मे-क्त, इष्टादिभ्यः इन्]<BR>One who hurts or injures, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमाय|अभिमायः
अभिमाय a. [अभिगतो मायामविद्यां]<BR>Bewildered (इतिकर्तव्यतामूढ);<BR>ignorant, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमिह्य
अभिमि(मे)ह्य a. Ved. To be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-b" target="_blank">Page0135-b+ 57</a>]<BR>wetted (by making water upon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमेह्य
अभिमि(मे)ह्य a. Ved. To be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-b" target="_blank">Page0135-b+ 57</a>]<BR>wetted (by making water upon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुख|अभिमुखं|अभिमुखः
अभिमुख a. (खी f.) [अभिगतं मुखं<BR>यस्य P. VI. 2. 185]<BR>1 With the face<BR>turned or directed towards, in the<BR>direction of, towards, turned<BR>towards, facing; अभिमुखे मयि<BR>संहृतमीक्षितं Ś. 2. 11; ˚खा शाला Sk.;<BR>गच्छन्नभिमुखो वह्नौ नाशं याति पतंगवत्<BR>Pt. 1. 237; with the acc.;<BR>राजानमेवाभिमुखा निषेदुः; पंपामभिमुखो यंयौ Rām.;<BR>Bg. 11. 28; K. 264; sometimes with<BR>dat., or gen. or loc.; आश्रमायाभिमुखा<BR>बभूवुः Mb.; यस्ते तिष्ठेदभिमुखे रणे Rām.;<BR>मय्यभिमुखीभूय Dk. 124; also in<BR>comp.; शकुंतलाभिमुखो भूत्वा Ś. 1<BR>turning towards Ś.; Ku. 3. 75, 7. 9.<BR>--2<BR>Coming or going near, approaching,<BR>near or close at hand;<BR>अभिमुखीष्विव वांछितसिद्धिषु व्रजति निर्वृतिमेकपदे<BR>मनः V. 2. 9; यौवनाभिमुखी संजज्ञे Pt. 4;<BR>R. 17. 40.<BR>--3 Disposed or intending<BR>to, inclined to; ready for, about (to do<BR>something), in comp.;<BR>चंद्रापीडाभिमुखहृदया K. 198, 233; अस्ताभिमुखे<BR>सूर्ये Mu. 4. 19; प्रसादाभिमुखो वेधाः<BR>प्रत्युवाच दिवौकसः Ku. 2. 16; 5. 60;<BR>U. 7. 4, Māl. 10. 13; कर्मण्यभिमुखेन स्थेयं<BR>Dk. 89; अनभिमुखः सुखानां K. 45;<BR>प्रातः प्रयाणाभिमुखाय तस्मै R. 5. 29; निद्रा<BR>चिरेण नयनाभिसुखी बभूव 5. 64;<BR>sometimes as first member of comp.<BR>in this sense; फलमभिमुखपाकं<BR>राजजंबूद्रुमस्य V. 4. 13.<BR>--4 Favourable,<BR>friendly or favourably disposed;<BR>आनीय झटिति घटयति<BR>विधिरभिमतमभिमुखीभूतः Ratn. 1. 7.<BR>--5 Taking one's<BR>part, nearly related to.<BR>--6 With the<BR>face turned upwards.<BR>--खी One of<BR>the 10 earths according to<BR>Buddhists.<BR>--खं, --खे ind. Towards, in<BR>the direction of, facing, in front or<BR>presence of, near to; with acc., gen.<BR>or in comp., or by itself; ये<BR>गताभिमुखं विष्णुं Rām.; आसीताभिमुखं गुरोः<BR>Ms. 2. 193; तिष्ठन्मुनेरभिमुखं स<BR>विकीर्णधाम्नः Ki. 2. 59; Śi. 13. 2;<BR>Ki. 6. 46; नेपथ्याभिमुखमवलोक्य<BR>Ś. 1; स पुराभिमुखं प्रतस्थे Pt. 3;<BR>Me. 68; कर्णं ददात्यभिमुखं मयि भाषमाणे<BR>Ś. 1. 31; also at the beginning of comp.;<BR>अभिमुखनिहतस्य Bh. 2. 112 killed in<BR>the front ranks of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखता
अभिमुखता<BR>1 Presence, proximity.<BR>--2 Favourableness; ˚तां नी to win<BR>over Ki. 10. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखीकृ
अभिमुखीकृ, --मुखयति To propitiate,<BR>win over; Ki. 12. 19; K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखयति
अभिमुखीकृ, --मुखयति To propitiate,<BR>win over; Ki. 12. 19; K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमुखीकरणं|अभिमुखीकरण
अभिमुखीकरणं Causing (one) to<BR>turn the face towards; speaking<BR>to, addressing (in gram.);<BR>संबोधनमभिमुखीकरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमूर्छित
अभिमूर्छित a. Utterly confused,<BR>bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृद्
अभिमृद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To crush by<BR>standing, tread under foot, trample<BR>down; oppress, devastate (as a<BR>country).<BR>--2 (In astr.) To contend<BR>against, oppose, be in opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दः|अभिमर्द|अभिमर्द्द|अभिमर्द्दः
अभिमर्दः<BR>1 Rubbing, friction.<BR>--2<BR>Crushing down, trampling down,<BR>ravage, devastation of a country (by<BR>an enemy).<BR>--3 War, battle.<BR>--4<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्दन|अभिमर्द्दन
अभिमर्दन a. Crushing down,<BR>oppressing.<BR>--नं Crushing, oppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमृश्
अभिमृश् {c6c} P. To touch (in all<BR>senses); come in contact with;<BR>strike or rub gently; पदाभिमृष्ट, वचसा˚,<BR>पादतल˚, गदा˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिमर्शः|अभिमर्श
अभिमर्शः, --र्शनं, --मर्षः, --र्षणं<BR>1 Touch,<BR>contact; उष्णांशुकरभिमर्षात् Śi. 4. 16.<BR>--2 Assault, violence, attack,<BR>outraging, touching carnally, sexual<BR>intercourse; कृताभिमर्षामनुमन्यमानः<BR>Ś. 5. 20 carnally touched or<BR>embraced, seduced, outraged;<BR>पराभिमर्शो न तवास्ति Ku. 5. 43 (Malli. =<BR>परधर्षणं); Ms. 8. 352, Y. 2. 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0135-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

