अभिशंसिन्
अभिशंसक, --शंसिन् a. Accusing,<BR>charging, calumniating, insulting,<BR>abusive; Y. 3. 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंसनं|अभिशंसन
अभिशंसनं Accusation, charge,<BR>(whether true or false); मिथ्या˚ Y. 2. 289;<BR>abuse, insult, affront; पंचाशद् ब्राह्मणो<BR>दंड्यः क्षत्रियस्याभिशंसने Ms. 8. 268.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्त|अभिशस्तः
अभिशस्त p. p.<BR>1 Charged, falsely<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">Page0139-a+ 57</a>]<BR>accused, calumniated, abused,<BR>insulted; Ms. 8. 116, 373; Y. 1. 161.<BR>--2 Hurt, injured, attacked<BR>(supposed to be from अभिशस्); देवि<BR>केनाभिशस्तासि केन वासि विमानिता Rām.;<BR>Ms. 11. 113 threatened.<BR>--3<BR>Cursed (for अभिशप्त).<BR>--4 Wicked, sinful,<BR>infamous.<BR>--स्तं = अभशस्ति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0138-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तक
अभिशस्तक a.<BR>1 Falsely accused,<BR>defamed; wicked; Y. 1. 223; a<BR>person of bad repute; 2. 70.<BR>--2<BR>Caused by imprecation or curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तिः|अभिशस्ति
अभिशस्तिः f.<BR>1 A curse.<BR>--2 Effect<BR>of an imprecation, misfortune, evil,<BR>calamity.<BR>--3 Censure, calumny,<BR>abuse, defamation, charge, insult.<BR>--4 Asking, begging.<BR>--5 What curses<BR>or injures; the cause or source<BR>of injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंक्|अभिशङ्क्
अभिशंक् {c1c} A. To doubt,<BR>mistrust, suspect, be suspicious of (with<BR>acc. of person or thing);<BR>माभिशंकीर्वचो मम Mb.; Mk. 9. 8; Ms. 8. 96;<BR>also with abl.; be afraid of; Bk. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंका|अभिशङ्का
अभिशंका Doubt, suspicion,<BR>apprehension, fear, alarm, anxiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशंकित|अभिशङ्कित
अभिशंकित p. p. Doubtful,<BR>suspicious, apprehensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशप्
अभिशप् {c1c} U. To curse, execrate;<BR>अभिशप्तः फलमेतदन्वभूत् Ku. 4. 41.<BR>--Caus. To conjure, invoke (as by<BR>charms), charm, enchant; सत्येन<BR>माभिरक्ष त्वं वरुणेत्यभिशाप्य कं Y. 2. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशपनं|अभिशपन
अभिशपनं --शापः<BR>1 A curse,<BR>imprecation.<BR>--2 A serious charge,<BR>accusation; Y. 2. 99; अभिशापः<BR>पातकाभियोगः Mit.<BR>--3 Slander, calumny,<BR>false charge; असतो दोषस्य अध्याहारोऽ<BR>भिशापः.<BR>--4 An injury, hurt.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्वरः fever caused by the<BR>pronunciation of a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशापः|अभिशाप
अभिशपनं --शापः<BR>1 A curse,<BR>imprecation.<BR>--2 A serious charge,<BR>accusation; Y. 2. 99; अभिशापः<BR>पातकाभियोगः Mit.<BR>--3 Slander, calumny,<BR>false charge; असतो दोषस्य अध्याहारोऽ<BR>भिशापः.<BR>--4 An injury, hurt.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्वरः fever caused by the<BR>pronunciation of a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशापनं|अभिशापन
अभिशापनं Pronouncing a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशब्दित
अभिशब्दित a. Declared,<BR>announced, said, named.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्
अभिशस् {c1c} P. To hurt, injure,<BR>attack (= अभिशंस् q. v.). --f. Ved.<BR>Accusation, charge, imprecation &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्त|अभिशस्तः
अभिशस्त p. p. Hurt, attacked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशस्तृ
अभिशस्तृ m. An enemy, injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशिरोग्र
अभिशिरोग्र a. With the top and<BR>bottom inverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशीत
अभिशीत, --श्यात [श्यै-क्त] a. Cold,<BR>chilly, as wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्यात
अभिशीत, --श्यात [श्यै-क्त] a. Cold,<BR>chilly, as wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशीन
अभिशीन, --श्यान a. Congealed,<BR>coagulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्यान
अभिशीन, --श्यान a. Congealed,<BR>coagulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशोकः|अभिशोक
अभिशोकः<BR>1 Intense grief.<BR>--2<BR>Warmth; ardour (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशोच
अभिशोच a.<BR>1 Shining, glowing<BR>with heat.<BR>--2 Causing great grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशोचनं|अभिशोचन
अभिशोचनं<BR>1 Intense grief or<BR>pain, torment.<BR>--2 That which<BR>torments; a spirit or demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशोचयिष्णु
अभिशोचयिष्णु a. Tormenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्रवणं|अभिश्रवण
अभिश्रवणं Repeating Vedic<BR>texts, while Brāhmaṇas are sitting<BR>down to a Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्रावः|अभिश्राव
अभिश्रावः Hearing; becoming<BR>renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्री
अभिश्री a. Ved.<BR>1 Joining,<BR>connected with, mixing.<BR>--2 Combining;<BR>arranging.<BR>--3 Approaching, having<BR>recourse to.<BR>--4 Worthy.<BR>--5<BR>Shining.<BR>--6 Powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्रिष्
अभिश्रिष् --श्लिष् f.<BR>--(ट्) Ved. A<BR>ligature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्लिष्
अभिश्रिष् --श्लिष् f.<BR>--(ट्) Ved. A<BR>ligature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्लेषणं|अभिश्लेषण
अभिश्लेषणं A bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्वस्
अभिश्वस् m. Ved. One who<BR>breathes upon or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्वसः|अभिश्वस
अभिश्वसः Ved. Breathing forth<BR>or upon, eructation (of the<BR>stomach).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिश्वासः|अभिश्वास
अभिश्वासः Breathing or blowing<BR>upon; blowing into a flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषंज्|अभिषञ्ज्
अभिषंज् {c1c} P. [˚संज्, स् being<BR>changed to ष् by P. VIII. 3. 65].<BR>To be in contact with, touch;<BR>attach oneself to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषंगः|अभिषङ्ग|अभिषंग|अभिषङ्गः
अभिषंगः (also अभिसंगः)<BR>1<BR>Complete contact or union; attachment,<BR>connection, association; कन्यका<BR>दुन्वंति हृदयं मनुष्याणामीदृशाद्दुरभिसंगात्<BR>Māl. 7 ill attachment or union;<BR>Māl. 8; मुहुरिति वनविभ्रमाभिषंगात्<BR>Śi. 7. 68; K. 146, 290.<BR>--2 Defeat,<BR>mortification, discomfiture; जाताभिषंगो<BR>नृपतिः R. 2. 30.<BR>--3 A sudden blow,<BR>shock, or grief, a sudden calamity<BR>or misfortune, unexpected reverse;<BR>ततोऽभिषंगानिलविप्रविद्धा R. 14. 54,<BR>77; Ku. 3. 73; ˚जडं विजज्ञिवान्<BR>R. 8. 75.<BR>--4 Possession by devils or<BR>evil spirits;<BR>अभिघाताभिषंगाभ्यामभिचाराभिशापतः Mādh. N.<BR>--5 An oath.<BR>--6 Embracing; copulation.<BR>--7 A<BR>curse or imprecation, abuse.<BR>--8<BR>A false charge or accusation,<BR>calumny or defamation.<BR>--9 Contempt,<BR>disrespect.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्वरः fever<BR>caused by the action of evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषंजनं|अभिषञ्जन
अभिषंजनं = अभिषंग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषव|अभिषवं|अभिषवः
अभिषव see under अभिषु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषह्य
अभिषह्य ind. By force, forcibly,<BR>violently; insolently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषाच्
अभिषाच् a. [अभि-सच् स्वार्थे णिच्<BR>क्विप्] Ved.<BR>1 Following.<BR>--2<BR>Honouring, devoted.<BR>--3 Defeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषाह्
अभिषाह् a.<BR>1 Bearing, patient.<BR>--2 Overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषिच्
अभिषिच् {c6c} U. [˚सिच्, स् changed<BR>to ष् by P. VIII. 3. 65]<BR>1 To sprinkle,<BR>pour down upon, water, wet,<BR>shower upon (fig. also);<BR>स्नातीहाभ्यषिचज्जलैः Bk. 6. 21; 15. 3; 6. 23;<BR>संगे पुनर्बहुतराममृताभिषिक्तां Ch. P. 29<BR>v. l.; अथ वपुरभिषेक्तुं तास्तदांभोभिरीषुः<BR>Śi. 7. 75.<BR>--2 To anoint, consecrate, appoint<BR>&c. (by sprinkling water on the<BR>head); to crown, install, inaugurate<BR>(with loc. of the post of authority);<BR>अग्निवर्णमभिषिच्य राघवः स्वे पदे<BR>R. 19. 1, 17. 13; सोऽटवीराज्येऽभिषिक्तः<BR>H. 2; V. 5. 23. --Caus.<BR>1 To have<BR>another consecrated, inaugurated<BR>&c.<BR>--2 To let oneself be crowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेकः|अभिषेक
अभिषेकः<BR>1 Sprinkling, watering,<BR>wetting.<BR>--2 Anointing, inaugurating<BR>or consecrating by sprinkling water<BR>(a king, idol &c.).<BR>--3 (Particularly)<BR>Coronation, inauguration,<BR>installation (of kings); royal unction;<BR>अथाभिषेकं रघुवंशकेतोः R. 14. 7.<BR>--4<BR>The (holy) water required at<BR>inauguration, coronation water;<BR>अमात्यपरिषदं ब्रूहि संभ्रियतामायुषो<BR>राज्याभिषेक इति V. 5; यौवराज्य˚ ibid.;<BR>R. 17. 14.<BR>--5 Bathing; ablution,<BR>holy or religious bathing;<BR>अभिषेकोत्तीर्णाय काश्यपाय Ś. 4;<BR>अत्राभिषेकाय तपोधनानां R. 13. 51, 1. 85,<BR>10. 63, 13. 58, 14. 82; K. 22, 36,<BR>96; Ku. 5. 16; 7. 11; Ś. 7. 12;<BR>H. 4. 87.<BR>--6 Bathing or sprinkling<BR>with water (of a divinity to whom<BR>worship is offered).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अहः<BR>day of coronation.<BR>--शाला<BR>coronation-hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेक्तृ
अभिषेक्तृ a. One who sprinkles,<BR>anoints, inaugurates.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेचनं|अभिषेचन
अभिषेचनं<BR>1 Sprinkling.<BR>--2<BR>Coronation, inauguration; R. 8. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेचनीय|अभिषेचनीयः
अभिषेचनीय, --षेच्य, --क्य<BR>1 Worthy<BR>of inauguration, fit to be crowned.<BR>--2 Belonging to coronation.<BR>--यः<BR>N. of a sacrificial ceremony<BR>performed at the coronation of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेच्य
अभिषेचनीय, --षेच्य, --क्य<BR>1 Worthy<BR>of inauguration, fit to be crowned.<BR>--2 Belonging to coronation.<BR>--यः<BR>N. of a sacrificial ceremony<BR>performed at the coronation of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेक्य
अभिषेचनीय, --षेच्य, --क्य<BR>1 Worthy<BR>of inauguration, fit to be crowned.<BR>--2 Belonging to coronation.<BR>--यः<BR>N. of a sacrificial ceremony<BR>performed at the coronation of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषु
अभिषु {c5c} P. (˚सु)<BR>1 To extract<BR>Soma juice or any juice; अभिषुण्वंत<BR>आसते Ait. Br.<BR>--2 To apply water<BR>to or press out; Ms. 5. 10 (Kull.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">Page0140-a+ 57</a>]<BR>उदकेन संधा).<BR>--3 To moisten,<BR>sprinkle; Bk. 9. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0139-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषवः|अभिषव|अभिषवं
अभिषवः [अभि-सु-अप्]<BR>1<BR>Extracting or pressing out the Soma<BR>juice.<BR>--2 Distillation or<BR>extraction (of liquors &c.).<BR>--3<BR>Religious bathing, ablution preparatory<BR>to religious rites.<BR>--4 Bathing or<BR>ablution (in general); Ki. 3. 28.<BR>--5 Drinking the Soma juice.<BR>--6 A<BR>sacrifice in general.<BR>--7 Ferment,<BR>yeast; any substance producing<BR>fermentation.<BR>--8 A finger used in<BR>extracting Soma juice. (Nir.)<BR>--वं<BR>Sour gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषवणं|अभिषवण
अभिषवणं<BR>1 Bathing; Ki. 6. 23.<BR>--2 Means of extracting or pressing<BR>out Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषवणी
अभिषवणी A mechanical<BR>contrivance to press out the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषावकः|अभिषावक
अभिषावकः, --षोतृ m. The priest<BR>who extracts the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषोतृ
अभिषावकः, --षोतृ m. The priest<BR>who extracts the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषुत|अभिषुतं
अभिषुत p. p. Extracted, pressed<BR>out, as Soma juice.<BR>--तं Sour gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेण
अभिषेण a. Ved. Approaching<BR>(as an enemy) with an army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेणनं|अभिषेणन
अभिषेणनं Marching against an<BR>enemy, encountering a foe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिषेणयति
अभिषेणयति Den. P. [अभिसेना-णिच्<BR>P. III. 1. 25, VIII. 3. 65] To march<BR>against (with an army), to attack,<BR>to face or encounter (another) with<BR>an army; कः सिंधुराजमभिषेणयितुं समर्थः<BR>Ve. 2. 25; Śi. 6. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टनः|अभिष्टन
अभिष्टनः [अभि-स्तन्-अप् षत्वं] Ved.<BR>Roaring, a loud shout (सिंहनाद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टि|अभिष्टिः
अभि(भी)ष्टि a. (Ved.) To be<BR>worshipped by offering sacrifices<BR>(Sāy. अभियष्टव्य); an assistant, a<BR>protector, one who is praised or<BR>worshipped as a protector, one who<BR>approaches to assist or attack, one<BR>who assails or overpowers an enemy,<BR>one who approaches in order to<BR>obtain, desiring, desire (these<BR>meanings are given by European<BR>scholars).<BR>--ष्टिः f. Assistance, help,<BR>worshipping, praising; a sacrifice;<BR>a hymn; approaching to assist or<BR>approaching in general; access.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्टि
अभि(भी)ष्टि a. (Ved.) To be<BR>worshipped by offering sacrifices<BR>(Sāy. अभियष्टव्य); an assistant, a<BR>protector, one who is praised or<BR>worshipped as a protector, one who<BR>approaches to assist or attack, one<BR>who assails or overpowers an enemy,<BR>one who approaches in order to<BR>obtain, desiring, desire (these<BR>meanings are given by European<BR>scholars).<BR>--ष्टिः f. Assistance, help,<BR>worshipping, praising; a sacrifice;<BR>a hymn; approaching to assist or<BR>approaching in general; access.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टिमत्|अभिष्टिमन्त्
अभिष्टिमत् a. Ved. Desirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टु
अभिष्टु {c2c} P.<BR>--(स्तु)<BR>1 To praise,<BR>laud, extol; अथ इतरामभिष्टुवंति U. 5;<BR>Śi. 15. 20.<BR>--2 To consecrate, invoke;<BR>Y. 3. 307.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्टवः|अभिष्टव
अभिष्टवः Praise, eulogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यंद्
अभिष्यंद् {c1c} A. (स् changed to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">Page0140-b+ 55</a>]<BR>ष् by P. VIII. 3. 72)<BR>1 To ooze,<BR>flow, trickle; अभिस्यं --ष्यं --दते दुग्धं<BR>Sk.; सततमभिष्यंदमानमेघमेदुरितनीलिमा<BR>(गिरिः) U. 1 raining or pouring<BR>down water.<BR>--2 (fig.) To be melted<BR>(with pity, love &c), to overflow<BR>with; यदि त्वामीदृशं रामभद्रः पश्येत्<BR>तदास्य हृदयं स्नेहेनाभिष्यंदते U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यंदः|अभिष्यन्द|अभिष्यन्दः
अभिष्यं(स्यं)दः<BR>1 Oozing,<BR>flowing, trickling.<BR>--2 Weakness of, or<BR>running at, the eyes.<BR>--3 Great<BR>increase or enlargement, surplus,<BR>excess, superfluous portion;<BR>स्वर्गाभिष्यंदवमनं कृत्वेवोपनिवेशितं (ओषधिप्रस्थं)<BR>Ku. 6. 37 by drawing off the<BR>surplus population i. e. by emigration<BR>(अभिष्यंदः अतिरेकः अतिरिक्तजन इति यावत्<BR>तस्य वमनं निःसारणं कृत्वा स्थितमिव); cf. also<BR>R. 15. 29 Hemacandra's remarks<BR>thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्यंदः|अभिस्यन्द|अभिस्यन्दः
अभिष्यं(स्यं)दः<BR>1 Oozing,<BR>flowing, trickling.<BR>--2 Weakness of, or<BR>running at, the eyes.<BR>--3 Great<BR>increase or enlargement, surplus,<BR>excess, superfluous portion;<BR>स्वर्गाभिष्यंदवमनं कृत्वेवोपनिवेशितं (ओषधिप्रस्थं)<BR>Ku. 6. 37 by drawing off the<BR>surplus population i. e. by emigration<BR>(अभिष्यंदः अतिरेकः अतिरिक्तजन इति यावत्<BR>तस्य वमनं निःसारणं कृत्वा स्थितमिव); cf. also<BR>R. 15. 29 Hemacandra's remarks<BR>thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्यंदिन्|अभिष्यन्दिन्
अभिष्यं(स्यं)दिन् a.<BR>1 Oozing,<BR>flowing, trickling.<BR>--2 Laxative, opening<BR>the bowels.<BR>--3 Causing defluxions or<BR>watery effusion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रमणं a<BR>suburb, a smaller city appended to<BR>and regarded as part of a larger one;<BR>cf. शाखानगरं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्यंदिन्|अभिस्यन्दिन्
अभिष्यं(स्यं)दिन् a.<BR>1 Oozing,<BR>flowing, trickling.<BR>--2 Laxative, opening<BR>the bowels.<BR>--3 Causing defluxions or<BR>watery effusion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रमणं a<BR>suburb, a smaller city appended to<BR>and regarded as part of a larger one;<BR>cf. शाखानगरं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिष्वंगः|अभिष्वङ्ग|अभिष्वंग|अभिष्वङ्गः
अभिष्वंगः [स्वंज्-घञ्]<BR>1 Contact.<BR>--2 Intense attachment, love,<BR>affection; विद्यास्वभिष्वंगः Dk. 155; अहो<BR>अभिष्वंगः Māl. 1; काम˚ ibid. Bg. 13. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंयोगः|अभिसंयोग
अभिसंयोगः Close contact^1 or<BR>union, intimate connection.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंवृत
अभिसंवृत a. Clothed, clad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंशीन
अभिसंशीन a. [श्यै-क्त]<BR>Coagulated, congealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंश्रयः|अभिसंश्रय
अभिसंश्रयः Refuge, shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंसारः|अभिसंसार
अभिसंसारः Coming together or<BR>in groups or flocks.<BR>--रं adv.<BR>Having approached together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंस्कृ
अभिसंस्कृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To shape,<BR>form, build.<BR>--2 To make, render.<BR>--3 To consecrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंस्कारः|अभिसंस्कार
अभिसंस्कारः<BR>1 Idea, thought,<BR>imagination.<BR>--2 Vain or profitless<BR>performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंस्तवः|अभिसंस्तव
अभिसंस्तवः High praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंक्षिप्|अभिसङ्क्षिप्
अभिसंक्षिप्<BR>--संक्षेपः = संक्षिप्, &c. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंख्या|अभिसङ्ख्या
अभिसंख्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 To enumerate.<BR>--2 To infer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंख्य|अभिसङ्ख्य
अभिसंख्य a. Inferable, clearly<BR>ascertainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंचारिन्|अभिसञ्चारिन्
अभिसंचारिन् a.<BR>1 Moving or<BR>wandering about.<BR>--2 Fickle,<BR>changeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसत्वन्
अभिसत्वन् a. Ved.<BR>Surrounded by heroes; (cf. अभिवीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंतप्|अभिसन्तप्
अभिसंतप् {c1c} P. To torment, =<BR>संतप् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंतापः|अभिसन्ताप|अभिसंताप|अभिसन्तापः
अभिसंतापः War, battle, contest;<BR>जन्यं स्यादभिसंतापः Halāy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंदृष्ट
अभिसंदृष्ट a. Compressed,<BR>tightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंदेहः|अभिसन्देह|अभिसंदेह
अभिसंदेहः<BR>1 Exchange.<BR>--2 Organ<BR>of generation (written also<BR>अभिसंदोह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधा|अभिसन्धा
अभिसंधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To hold together<BR>--2 To acknowledge, recognize;<BR>own.<BR>--3 To fit or fix a missile,<BR>arrow &c. to the bow.<BR>--4 To throw<BR>or shoot at, aim at; (शूलं) चिक्षेप<BR>परमक्रुद्धो लक्ष्मणायाभिसंहितं Rām.<BR>--5<BR>To aim at, have in view, think of,<BR>(with acc.); पदाविद्धं यांती<BR>स्खलितमभिसंधाय बहुशः V. 4. 28 calling to<BR>mind, thinking of my fault;<BR>ऋष्यमूकमभिसंधाय Mv. 5 towards,<BR>in the direction of; Mv. 6;<BR>Bg. 17. 12, 25; sometimes with dat.;<BR>अभिसंदधते ये च विश्वासायास्य मानवाः<BR>Mb.<BR>--6 To deceive, cheat; जनं<BR>विद्वानेकः सकलमभिसंधाय Māl. 1. 14.<BR>--7<BR>To come to an understanding or<BR>agreement; फलं त्वनभिसंधाय<BR>Ms. 9. 52 (एवं यत्र नियमो न कृतः).<BR>--8 To win<BR>over, make friendship with, ally<BR>oneself with; तान्<BR>सर्वानभिसंदध्यात्सामादिभिरुपक्रमैः Ms. 7. 159 (वशीकुर्यात्).<BR>--9 To declare solemnly, agree,<BR>promise.<BR>--10 To calumniate,<BR>traduce.<BR>--11 To add.<BR>--12 To prefer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधः|अभिसन्ध
अभिसंधः, --धकः<BR>1 A deceiver,<BR>cheat.<BR>--2 Traducer, calumniator;<BR>Ms. 4. 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधकः|अभिसन्धक|अभिसंधक
अभिसंधः, --धकः<BR>1 A deceiver,<BR>cheat.<BR>--2 Traducer, calumniator;<BR>Ms. 4. 195.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधा|अभिसन्धा
अभिसंधा<BR>1 Speech, declaration;<BR>word, assertion, promise; तेन<BR>सत्याभिसंधेन त्रिवर्गमनुतिष्ठता Rām. true to<BR>his word.<BR>--2 Deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधानं|अभिसन्धान|अभिसंधान|अभिसन्धानं
अभिसंधानं<BR>1 Speech, word,<BR>deliberate declaration, promise; सा हि<BR>सत्याभिसंधाना Rām.<BR>--2 Cheating,<BR>deception; पराभिसंधानपरं यद्यप्यस्य<BR>विचेष्टितं R. 17. 76.<BR>--3 Aim, intention,<BR>purpose;<BR>अन्याभिसंधानेनान्यवादित्वमन्यकर्तृत्वं च Mit.<BR>--4 Making peace.<BR>--5<BR>Attachment or interest in any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधायः|अभिसन्धाय|अभिसंधाय
अभिसंधायः = अभिसंधि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंधिः|अभिसन्धि|अभिसंधि|अभिसन्धिः
अभिसंधिः<BR>1 Speech; deliberate<BR>declaration, promise.<BR>--2 Intention,<BR>object, purpose, aim; तस्या<BR>अभिसंधिना विधेयीकृतोपि Māl. 1; Dk. 38;<BR>स्वर्ग˚ Ku. 6. 47.<BR>--3 Implied sense,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">Page0141-a+ 55</a>]<BR>the meaning intended, as in<BR>अयमभिसंधिः (frequently occurring in<BR>explanatory glosses).<BR>--4 Opinion, belief.<BR>--5 Special agreement, terms of an<BR>agreement, condition, stipulation;<BR>अथावश्यमेव माधवसेनः पूज्येन मोचयितव्यः<BR>श्रूयतामभिसंधिः M. 1.<BR>--6<BR>Deception.<BR>--7 Making peace or alliance.<BR>--8 Junction, combination.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत a. done intentionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0140-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसमवायः|अभिसमवाय
अभिसमवायः Union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपत्|अभिसम्पत्
अभिसंपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fly towards,<BR>hasten, jump upon;<BR>महीतलात्कोचिदुदीर्णवेगाः पुनर्द्रुमाग्रानभिसपतंति Rām.<BR>--2 To<BR>fly along; शस्त्रैश्च दिव्यैरभिसंपतद्भिः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपातः|अभिसम्पात|अभिसंपात|अभिसम्पातः
अभिसंपातः<BR>1 Meeting together,<BR>concourse, confluence.<BR>--2 War,<BR>battle, contest.<BR>--3 A curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपद्|अभिसम्पद्
अभिसंपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To become<BR>(any thing); to be changed to, be<BR>similar to, assume the state of;<BR>इष्टकामग्निरभिसंपद्यते Śat. Br. श्रोत्रे हीमे<BR>सर्वे वेदा अभिसंपन्नाः ibid.<BR>--2 To come<BR>or go to, arrive at.<BR>--3 To get,<BR>obtain. --Caus. To make similar to,<BR>change into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपत्तिः|अभिसम्पत्ति|अभिसंपत्ति
अभिसंपत्तिः f. Becoming or being<BR>effected completely; going over,<BR>transition; being changed into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपद्|अभिसम्पद्
अभिसंपद् f. Becoming complete;<BR>complete number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपन्न|अभिसम्पन्न
अभिसंपन्न p. p. Complete,<BR>completely effected; वदत्ययमभिसंपन्नमार्षेण<BR>संस्कारेण U. 5 quite in keeping with<BR>his holy instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंपरायः|अभिसम्पराय|अभिसंपराय
अभिसंपरायः Futurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंबंध्|अभिसम्बन्ध्|अभिसंबन्ध्
अभिसंबंध् {c9c} P. To bind together.<BR>--pass. To be connected with, to<BR>relate or refer to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंबंधः|अभिसम्बन्ध|अभिसंबन्ध|अभिसंबन्धः
अभिसंबंधः Connection, relation;<BR>conjunction, contact; sexual<BR>connection; Ms. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंबाध|अभिसम्बाध
अभिसंबाध a. Very much<BR>contracted or confined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसंमुख|अभिसम्मुख
अभिसंमुख a. Facing, fronting;<BR>looking respectfully towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर|अभिसरः
अभिसर, --सर्ग, --सर्जन &c. see under<BR>अभिसृ, अभिसृज् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्ग|अभिसर्गः
अभिसर, --सर्ग, --सर्जन &c. see under<BR>अभिसृ, अभिसृज् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्जन|अभिसर्जनं|अभिसर्ज्जन|अभिसर्ज्जनं
अभिसर, --सर्ग, --सर्जन &c. see under<BR>अभिसृ, अभिसृज् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्पणं|अभिसर्पण
अभिसर्पणं Approaching,<BR>drawing near (with hostile intention).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसांत्व्|अभिसान्त्व्
अभिसां(शां)त्व् {c10c} P. To<BR>conciliate, propitiate, pacify, comfort,<BR>console.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशांत्व्|अभिशान्त्व्
अभिसां(शां)त्व् {c10c} P. To<BR>conciliate, propitiate, pacify, comfort,<BR>console.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसांत्वः|अभिसान्त्व|अभिसान्त्वः
अभिसां(शां)त्वः, --त्वनं Conciliation,<BR>consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशांत्वः|अभिशान्त्व|अभिशान्त्वः
अभिसां(शां)त्वः, --त्वनं Conciliation,<BR>consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसांत्वनं
अभिसां(शां)त्वः, --त्वनं Conciliation,<BR>consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिशांत्वनं
अभिसां(शां)त्वः, --त्वनं Conciliation,<BR>consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसायं|अभिसाय|अभिसायः
अभिसायं ind. At sunset, about<BR>evening; श्रितोदयाद्रेरभिसायमुच्चकैः<BR>Śi. 1. 16; Ki. 11. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसृ
अभिसृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go up to,<BR>go towards, approach; to go to<BR>some place or other, go or<BR>proceed; पुरोभिसस्रे सुरसुंदरीजनैः<BR>Ki. 8. 4.<BR>--2 To attack, assail.<BR>--3 To<BR>go or advance to meet (as at an<BR>appointed place); सुंदरीरभिससार<BR>K. 58; Dk. 51, 52, 91; Śi. 6. 26.<BR>--Caus. To visit, approach, go to<BR>meet; वल्लभानभिसिसारयिषूणां<BR>10. 20, 21; S. D. 115; Ki. 9. 38; Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसरः|अभिसर
अभिसरः<BR>1 A follower, an<BR>attendant; Dk. 73, 127.<BR>--2 A companion;<BR>मन्मथाभिसरा तदागारमभिसरामि Dk. 15.<BR>--3 N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसरणं|अभिसरण
अभिसरणं<BR>1 Approaching, going<BR>to meet (also with hostile intentions).<BR>--2 Meeting, rendezvous, assignation<BR>or appointment of lovers;<BR>त्वदभिसरणरभसेन वलंती पतति पदानि कियंति चलंती<BR>Gīt. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्तृ
अभिसर्तृ a. One who attacks; an<BR>assistant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारः|अभिसार
अभिसारः<BR>1 Going to meet (as a<BR>lover), appointment, assignation;<BR>रतिसुखसारे गतमभिसारे मदनमनोहरवेशं<BR>Gīt. 5.<BR>--2 The place where lovers<BR>meet by appointment, rendezvous;<BR>त्वरितमुपैति न कथमभिसारं Gīt. 6.<BR>--3 An<BR>attack, assault; श्वोऽभिसारः पुरस्य नः<BR>Rām.<BR>--4 War, battle.<BR>--5 A follower,<BR>companion.<BR>--6 Might, power.<BR>--7 An<BR>instrument.<BR>--8 A purificatory rite.<BR>--9<BR>(˚राः pl.) N. of a people.<BR>--री N.<BR>of a town.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थानं a place<BR>fit for making appointments; see<BR>under अभिसारिका below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारणं|अभिसारण
अभिसारणं Going to meet a lover<BR>&c.; Ki. 10. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिका
अभिसारिका A woman who either<BR>goes to meet her lover or keeps an<BR>appointment made by him;<BR>Ku. 6. 43; R. 16. 12; अभिसारयते कांतं<BR>या मन्मथवशंवदा । स्वयं वाभिसरत्येषा<BR>धीरैरुक्ताऽभिसारिका S. D. 115;<BR>कांतार्थिनी तु या याति संकेतं साभिसारिका Ak.<BR>The directions as to dress &c. to be<BR>observed by the different kinds of<BR>अभिसारिका are given in S. D. 116.<BR>The S. D. further recommends the<BR>following {8} places as eligible spots<BR>for lovers to meet:-- (1) a field; (2)<BR>a garden; (3) a ruined temple; (4)<BR>the house of a female messenger;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">Page0141-c+ 57</a>]<BR>(5) forest; (6) caravansary (a place<BR>for pilgrims &c.); (7) a cemetery,<BR>and (8) the bank of a river; क्षेत्रं<BR>वाटी भग्नदेवालयो दूतीगृहं वनं । मालयं च श्मशानं<BR>च नद्यादीनां तटी तथा ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसारिन्
अभिसारिन् a. Going to meet,<BR>visiting; attacking, rushing out,<BR>going forth; युद्धभिसारिणः U. 5.<BR>--णी<BR>1 = अभिसारिका see above.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>a species of the त्रिष्टुभ् metre in<BR>which the Pādas contain 12 instead<BR>of 11 syllables, and which is<BR>therefore said to approach (अभिसरति)<BR>another metre called जगती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसृज्
अभिसृज् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To pour out<BR>or forth; Rv. 1. 135. 6.<BR>--2 To<BR>make, prepare; तस्य चितेयमभिसृष्टा<BR>Mv. 5.<BR>--3 To unloose, untie.<BR>--4 To give,<BR>grant; अभिसृज्य वरद्वयं Rām.<BR>--5 To<BR>fall upon, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्गः|अभिसर्ग
अभिसर्गः Creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसर्जनं|अभिसर्जन|अभिसर्ज्जन|अभिसर्ज्जनं
अभिसर्जनं<BR>1 A gift, donation.<BR>--2<BR>Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिसेवनं|अभिसेवन
अभिसेवनं<BR>1 Practising,<BR>observing.<BR>--2 Cultivating.<BR>--3 Fondness<BR>of, indulgence in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्कंदः|अभिस्कन्द|अभिस्कन्दः
अभिस्कंदः Ved.<BR>1 An attack,<BR>assault.<BR>--2 An assailant, enemy.<BR>--दं adv. By attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्नेहः|अभिस्नेह
अभिस्नेहः Attachment,<BR>affection; love, desire; यः सर्वत्रानभिस्नेहः<BR>Bg. 2. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्फुरित
अभिस्फुरित a. Expanded to<BR>the full, full-grown (as a blossom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वृ
अभिस्वृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To assent or<BR>agree to, approve of.<BR>--2 To praise,<BR>invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वर्
अभिस्वर् f. (or n. according to<BR>some) [अभितः स्वः स्वरणशब्दो यस्य] Ved.<BR>1 Invocation, calling into one's<BR>presence.<BR>--2 A song or hymn of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वरः|अभिस्वर
अभिस्वरः Urging towards, driving<BR>onwards.<BR>--रे Very close or near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिस्वर्तृ
अभिस्वर्तृ m. Praising; invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहन्
अभिहन् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To strike, smite,<BR>beat (fig. also); thump at;<BR>अभिहंति हंत कथमेष माधवं (स्मरः)<BR>Māl. 1. 39; लोष्टैरभिघ्नंतो नयत U. 4;<BR>कल्लोलमालाभिहतः पोतः Dk. 7.<BR>--2 To hurt,<BR>injure, kill, destroy.<BR>--3 To drive or<BR>beat off, ward off;<BR>आलोलपत्राभिहतद्विरेफं (अरविंदं) R. 6. 13.<BR>--4 To strike<BR>or beat (as a drum &c.) Bg. 1. 13.<BR>--5<BR>To befall, attack; affect, overpower;<BR>Dk. 6. --Caus. To strike &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहत
अभिहत p. p.<BR>1 Struck(fig. also),<BR>beaten, smitten, attacked, injured;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">Page0142-a+ 56</a>]<BR>धाराभिरातप इवाभिहतं सरोजं M. 5. 3,<BR>Amaru. 2; struck against (as sound);<BR>Śik. 9.<BR>--2 Struck, affected, overcome;<BR>शोक˚, काम˚, दुःख˚, क्षुत्तृषा˚.<BR>--3<BR>Obstructed.<BR>--4 (In math.) Multiplied;<BR>अन्योन्यहाराभिहतौ हरांशौ Līlā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहतिः|अभिहति
अभिहतिः f.<BR>1 Striking, beating,<BR>hurting &c.<BR>--2 (In Math.)<BR>Multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातः|अभिघात
अभिघातः<BR>1 Striking, (fig. also);<BR>beating, smiting, attack, injury,<BR>hurt; तटाभिघातादिव लग्नपंके<BR>Ku. 7. 49; शीतातपाभिघातान् Ms. 12. 77<BR>attacks of heat and cold; so दुःख˚,<BR>शोक˚ &c.<BR>--2 (In Vaiśeṣika phil.)<BR>Striking against (such as gives rise<BR>to sounds &c.), regarded as a kind<BR>of संयोग.<BR>--3 Striking back, driving<BR>or warding off.<BR>--4 Extirpation,<BR>complete destruction or removal;<BR>दुःखत्रयाभिघाताज्जिज्ञासा तदभिघातके हेतौ<BR>Sāṅ. K. 1.<BR>--5 Abrupt or vehement<BR>articulation of words (as of<BR>Vedic texts); sudden shock.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The<BR>combination of the 4th letter of<BR>any class with the first or third<BR>letter of that class; of the second<BR>with the first; and of the third with<BR>the second letter of any class;<BR>अभिघातं स्यात्पूर्वं वेदद्वित्र्यादिवर्णाश्चेत् । नववर्गाणां<BR>नवतो धरणीचंद्रद्विरामाद्याः Śabdak.<BR>--2 A<BR>harsh pronunciation caused by the<BR>neglect of Saṃdhi rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातक|अभिघातकः
अभिघातक a. Striking; keeping<BR>or beating back, repelling,<BR>extirpating.<BR>--कः An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिघातिन्
अभिघातिन् Striking, hurting. --m.<BR>An enemy; assailant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहवः|अभिहव
अभिहवः [ह्वे-अंप्]<BR>1 Invocation,<BR>calling.<BR>--2 Sacrificing fully or<BR>completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहूतिः|अभिहूति
अभिहूतिः f. Calling, invocation;<BR>worshipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहस्य
अभिहस्य a. Ved. Ridiculous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहासः|अभिहास
अभिहासः Jest, joke, mirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहित|अभिहितं
अभिहित, --ति See under अभिधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहिति|अभिहितिः
अभिहित, --ति See under अभिधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहु
अभिहु {c3c} P. To make an oblation,<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहवः|अभिहव
अभिहवः An oblation, a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहोमः|अभिहोम
अभिहोमः Offering an oblation of<BR>clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहृ
अभिहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To carry or bear<BR>off, snatch away, remove, take<BR>away.<BR>--2 To tear off, pull down.<BR>--3 To bring; bring near. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To cause to take away.<BR>--2 To bring<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">Page0142-b+ 56</a>]<BR>on the table, serve up in dishes &c.<BR>(as food).<BR>--3 To lay or put on (as<BR>a coat).<BR>--4 To attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहरः|अभिहर
अभिहरः Carrying off, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहरणं|अभिहरण
अभिहरणं<BR>1 Bringing near,<BR>fetching; R. 11. 43.<BR>--2 Robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहर्तृ
अभिहर्तृ m.<BR>1 One who takes away,<BR>bears off, or takes by violence.<BR>--2<BR>A ravisher, robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिहारः|अभिहार
अभिहारः<BR>1 Carrying away,<BR>robbing, stealing.<BR>--2 An attack,<BR>assault.<BR>--3 Arming oneself, taking up<BR>arms.<BR>--4 Mingling together,<BR>mixture.<BR>--5 An effort.<BR>--6 A drunkard;<BR>drinker of smoking drinks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्रुत्
अभिह्रुत् a. Ved. Bending,<BR>causing crookedness, acting injuriously.<BR>--f. Fall; defeat, loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्रुति|अभिह्रुतिः
अभिह्रुति a. Offensive, injurious;<BR>acting crookedly.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1<BR>Causing to fall.<BR>--2 Defeat; loss.<BR>--3<BR>Offence, injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्वर|अभिह्वरः
अभिह्वर, --ह्वार a. Falling off,<BR>crooked.<BR>--रः Crookedness, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभिह्वार
अभिह्वर, --ह्वार a. Falling off,<BR>crooked.<BR>--रः Crookedness, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभी
अभी [अभि-इ] {c2c} P.<BR>1 To<BR>approach, come or draw near, go up<BR>to (with acc.) अस्मानत्तुमितोऽभ्येति<BR>Bk. 7. 84.; Ki. 2. 54.<BR>--2 To<BR>go along or after, follow, serve.<BR>--3 (a) To go into, enter;<BR>Bk. 5. 67; Ms. 8. 75. (b) To go over to,<BR>reach, arrive at; Me. 34 v. l. (c) To<BR>fall to one's share, come to;<BR>Bk. 7. 99.<BR>--4 To get, meet with, fall into,<BR>suffer, undergo (said of good or<BR>bad things); कार्यं संसिद्धिमभ्येति Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीतिः|अभीति
अभीतिः f. Ved. Approach, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत्वन्
अभीत्वन् a. (री f.), अभीत्वर a.<BR>Approaching, attacking, assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्ययः|अभ्यय
अभ्ययः<BR>1 Going over, approach,<BR>arrival.<BR>--2 Entering.<BR>--3 Setting (of<BR>the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभी
अभी a. Without fear;<BR>R. 9. 63; 15. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक|अभीकः
अभीक a. [For ety. see अभिक]<BR>1 Longing after, desirous,<BR>anxious.<BR>--2 Lustful, libidinous,<BR>voluptuous; मेदस्विनः सरभसोपगतानभीकान्<BR>Śi. 5. 64.<BR>--3 Fearless.<BR>--4 Gone<BR>to (अभिगत).<BR>--5 Dreadful.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>lover, husband.<BR>--2 A poet.<BR>--3 A<BR>master.<BR>--कं Ved.<BR>1 Proximity,<BR>nearness.<BR>--2 Collision; combat,<BR>encounter, opposition. The form अभीके<BR>frequently occurs in the Vedas in<BR>the sense of (a) near; (b) at the same<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">Page0142-c+ 55</a>]<BR>time or place, at the right time, just<BR>in time; (c) in a moment,<BR>instantaneously, or (used like a<BR>preposition with abl.), (d) from, out of; (e)<BR>on account of, with regard to; (f.)<BR>from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्ण|अभीक्ष्णं
अभीक्ष्ण a. [अभिगतः क्षणं पृषो˚;<BR>अभीक्ष्णं अभिक्षणं भवाति, तद्धि क्षणमाभिमुख्येन<BR>स्थितं भवति Nir.]<BR>1 Repeated,<BR>frequent.<BR>--2 Constant, perpetual.<BR>--3<BR>Excessive.<BR>--क्ष्णं ind.<BR>1 Frequently,<BR>repeatedly; क्षते प्रहारा निपतंत्यभीक्ष्णं<BR>Pt. 2. 178.<BR>--2 Constantly,<BR>--3 Very<BR>much, exceedingly.<BR>--4 Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीक्ष्णशः
अभीक्ष्णशः ind. Repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीघात
अभीघात = अभिघात q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीज्य|अभीज्यः
अभीज्य a. [fr. यज्] To be<BR>sacrificed to; one to whom a sacrifice^1 is<BR>offered.<BR>--ज्यः A God.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीत
अभीत, --ति a. Not afraid,<BR>fearless.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1 Fearlessness.<BR>--2<BR>Approach, attack.<BR>--3 Nearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीति|अभीतिः
अभीत, --ति a. Not afraid,<BR>fearless.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1 Fearlessness.<BR>--2<BR>Approach, attack.<BR>--3 Nearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीद्ध
अभीद्ध [इंध्-क्त] Inflamed,. shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीपत्
अभीपत् m. [अभि-पत्-क्विप् दीर्घः]<BR>One who goes or resorts to (<BR>अभिगमनवान् Sāy.), a pond or any spot<BR>in which water collects; a favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सित|अभीप्सितं
अभीप्सित a. Desired, wished.<BR>--तं A wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सिन्
अभीप्सिन्, अभीप्सु a. Wishing for,<BR>desirous of obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीप्सु
अभीप्सिन्, अभीप्सु a. Wishing for,<BR>desirous of obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीम|अभीमः
अभीम a. Not causing fear, not<BR>terrific.<BR>--मः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमान
अभीमान = अभिमान q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीमोदः|अभीमोद
अभीमोदः Joy, delight.<BR>--मुद्<BR>Ved. great joy, or (a.)<BR>excessively delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरः|अभीर
अभीरः [अभिमुखीकृत्य ईरयति गाः, ईर्,<BR>अच्]<BR>1 A cowherd.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>pastoral people; more usually written<BR>आभीर q. v.<BR>--री The language of<BR>the अभीर people.<BR>--रं N. of a metre<BR>see आभीर.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पल्ली a hamlet of<BR>cowherds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरणी
अभीरणी A kind of serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीराजी
अभीराजी N. of a poisonous<BR>insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरु|अभीरुः
अभीरु a. (रुः, --रू f.)<BR>1 Fearless.<BR>--2 Unterrific, harmless.<BR>--रुः N. of<BR>Śiva or Bhairava.<BR>--रुः f.<BR>--अभीरुपत्री<BR>N. of a plant (Mar. शतावरी)<BR>Asparagus Racemosus.<BR>--रु n. A place<BR>of battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीरुण
अभीरुण a. Fearless, innocent<BR>--णं<BR>ind. Before or in front.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलं|अभील
अभीलं<BR>1 A difficulty, distress.<BR>--2<BR>A dreadful scene.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलु
अभीलु --लुक = अभीरु q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलुक
अभीलु --लुक = अभीरु q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीलापः|अभीलाप
अभीलापः [लप् घञ्-दीर्घः] Discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवर्गः|अभीवर्ग
अभीवर्गः Circuit, compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवर्तः|अभीवर्त|अभीवर्त्त
अभीवर्तः [वृत्-करणे घञ्]<BR>1 N.<BR>of a Sāman, Brahma Sāman.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a hymn (Rv. 10. 174) recited<BR>in attacking the enemy.<BR>--3 A year.<BR>--4 A sort of oblation (B. and R.<BR>take this word to mean ‘existing<BR>everywhere’, ‘attacking<BR>successfully’, ‘successful attack or victory.’)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवृत्
अभीवृत् a. Existing everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीवृत
अभीवृत a. Covered, surrounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशापः|अभीशाप
अभीशापः A curse; see अभिशाप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीशुः|अभीशु
अभीशुः --षुः [अभि-अश्-उन्, पृषो˚ अत<BR>इत्वं]<BR>1 A rein, bridle; तेन हि<BR>मुच्यंतामभीशवः Ś. 1.<BR>--2 A ray of light;<BR>प्रफुल्लतापिच्छनिभैरभीषुभिः Śi. 1. 22; ˚मत्<BR>resplendent, splendid.<BR>--3 An arm<BR>(अभ्यश्नुते कर्माणि Nir.).<BR>--4 A finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषुः|अभीषु
अभीशुः --षुः [अभि-अश्-उन्, पृषो˚ अत<BR>इत्वं]<BR>1 A rein, bridle; तेन हि<BR>मुच्यंतामभीशवः Ś. 1.<BR>--2 A ray of light;<BR>प्रफुल्लतापिच्छनिभैरभीषुभिः Śi. 1. 22; ˚मत्<BR>resplendent, splendid.<BR>--3 An arm<BR>(अभ्यश्नुते कर्माणि Nir.).<BR>--4 A finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्
अभीष् {c6c} P. To wish or desire for,<BR>seek for, strive to get.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीष्ट|अभीष्टं|अभीष्टः
अभीष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Wished, desired.<BR>--2<BR>Dear, favourite, darling;<BR>अनभीष्टदंपत्योः Pt. 1. 175; oft. with gen. of<BR>person; H. 1. 12.<BR>--3 Optional.<BR>--ष्टः<BR>A darling.<BR>--ष्टा<BR>1 A mistress,<BR>beloved woman.<BR>--2 Betel.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 An<BR>object of desire.<BR>--2 A desirable<BR>object (अभिमत); अन्यस्मै हृदयं देहि<BR>नानभीष्टे घटामहे Bk. 20. 24.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--देवता favourite deity.<BR>--लाभः,<BR>--सिद्धिः f. gaining a desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषंग|अभीषङ्ग|अभीषङ्गः
अभीषंग = अभिषंग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषया
अभीषया adv. Fearlessly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभीषाह्
अभीषाह् a. Overpowering;<BR>guaranteeing safety from enemies (<BR>परेभ्योऽभयदाता; अभिषहमाणः सपत्नान्,<BR>अभिभवति शत्रून् Nir.). --f. (ट्) Great<BR>power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुक्त|अभुक्तः
अभुक्त a.<BR>1 Uneaten, unenjoyed,<BR>unused; Bh. 3. 25.<BR>--2 (Actively<BR>used) One who has not eaten,<BR>enjoyed, used &c.; cf. पीत.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मूलं the interval between the<BR>closing part of Jyeṣṭhā and the<BR>beginning of Mūla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुज्
अभुज् a. Ved. One who has not<BR>experienced or enjoyed; one who does<BR>not keep a promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुंजत्|अभुञ्जत्|अभुञ्जन्त्
अभुंजत् a.<BR>1 Not eating.<BR>--2 Not<BR>allowing to enjoy.<BR>--3 Not protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुग्न
अभुग्न a.<BR>1 Not bent or crooked,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">Page0143-b+ 55</a>]<BR>straight.<BR>--2 Well, free from disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुज
अभुज a. Armless, maimed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभुजिष्या
अभुजिष्या Not a slave or servant,<BR>an independent woman; Mk. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूः
अभूः ‘Unborn,’ N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूत
अभूत a. Non-existent, what is<BR>not or has not been; not true or<BR>real, false; Mu. 3. 16, Ki. 14. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आहरणं ‘utterance of an<BR>unreality,’ a covert expression, a<BR>speech founded on fraud, one of<BR>the members of garbha S. D. 365.<BR>--तद्भावः the becoming or being<BR>changed into, or making, that which it<BR>is not before; कृभ्वस्तियोंगे संपद्ये कर्तरि<BR>च्वि P. V. 4. 50; अभूततद्भावे इति वक्तव्यं;<BR>अकृष्णः कृष्णः संपद्यते तं करोति<BR>कृष्णीकरोति Sk.; cf. पयोधरीभूतचतुःसमुद्रां<BR>R. 2. 3.<BR>--पूर्व a. unprecedented,<BR>unsurpassed; अभूत् ˚र्वो राजा चिंतामणिर्नाम Vās. 1,<BR>Ve. 3. 2, Śi. 3. 3.<BR>--प्रादुर्भावः<BR>becoming manifest of what has not been<BR>before.<BR>--शत्रु a. having no enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूतिः|अभूति
अभूतिः f.<BR>1 Non-existence,<BR>non-entity.<BR>--2 Want of power.<BR>--3<BR>Poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूमिः|अभूमि
अभूमिः f.<BR>1 Non-earth, any<BR>thing but earth.<BR>--2 An unfit place<BR>or object, no proper object for,<BR>beyond the reach or scope of; अभूमिरियं<BR>मालविकायाः M. 3; अभूमिरियमविनयस्य<BR>Ś. 7; स खलु<BR>मनोरथानामप्यभूमिर्विसर्जनावसरसत्कारः ibid. far exceeded or<BR>transcended my (highest)<BR>expectations; Śi. 1. 42; Śānti. 4. 22,<BR>K. 45, 196, 204.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज {1}<BR>produced in a bad or improper place.<BR>{2} not produced in earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभूरि
अभूरि a. Few, some; several; so<BR>अभूमन्, अभूयिष्ठ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृत
अभृत, --अभृत्रिम a.<BR>1 Not hired or<BR>paid; Ms. 8. 231.<BR>--2 Not supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृत्रिम
अभृत, --अभृत्रिम a.<BR>1 Not hired or<BR>paid; Ms. 8. 231.<BR>--2 Not supported.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभृश|अभृशं
अभृश a. Not much, little, few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद|अभेदः
अभेद a.<BR>1 Undivided.<BR>--2<BR>Identical, same, alike; तयोरभेदप्रतिपत्तिरस्ति<BR>मे Bh. 3. v. l.<BR>--दः<BR>1 Absence of<BR>difference or distinction, identity,<BR>sameness; तद्रूपकमभेदो य उपमानोपमेययोः<BR>K. P. 10, Śi. 13. 25.<BR>--2 Close<BR>union; इच्छतां सह वधूभिरभेदं Ki. 9. 13;<BR>H. 3. 79; आशास्महे विग्रहयोरभेदं Bh. 1. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभेद्य|अभेद्यं
अभेद्य, अभैदिक a.<BR>1 Not to be<BR>divided, broken or pierced through,<BR>impenetrable.<BR>--2 Indivisible.<BR>--द्यं<BR>A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभैदिक
अभेद्य, अभैदिक a.<BR>1 Not to be<BR>divided, broken or pierced through,<BR>impenetrable.<BR>--2 Indivisible.<BR>--द्यं<BR>A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोक्तृ
अभोक्तृ, --भोगिन् a. Not using or<BR>enjoying, abstemious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोगिन्
अभोक्तृ, --भोगिन् a. Not using or<BR>enjoying, abstemious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोगः|अभोग
अभोगः Non-enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्
अभोज् a. Ved. Not sacrificing;<BR>not giving food to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजनं|अभोजन
अभोजनं Not eating, fasting,<BR>abstinence; Ms. 11. 167, 204, 216.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोजिन्
अभोजिन् a. Not eating, fasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभोज्य
अभोज्य a. Not to be eaten,<BR>prohibited as food, impure, unholy; ˚अन्न a.<BR>one whose food is prohibited from<BR>being eaten by others; Ms. 4. 221.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभौतिक
अभौतिक a. (की f.) Not<BR>material, not elemental, not produced<BR>by the gross elements; mental.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभौम
अभौम = अभूमिज q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यग्र|अभ्यग्रं
अभ्यग्र a. [अभिमुखं अग्रं यस्य]<BR>1<BR>Near, proximate.<BR>--2 Fresh, new; इदं<BR>शोणितमभ्यग्रे संप्रहारेऽच्युतत्तयोः Mb.<BR>--ग्रं Proximity, vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंक|अभ्यङ्क
अभ्यंक a. Recently marked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंज्|अभ्यञ्ज्
अभ्यंज् {c7c} P.<BR>1 To smear, anoint<BR>as with oily substances.<BR>--2 To<BR>decorate, adorn (Ved.)<BR>--3 To defile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यक्त
अभ्यक्त p. p. Smeared, anointed<BR>(with oil, perfumes &c.); अभ्यक्तमिव<BR>स्नातः Ś. 5. 11; Y. 1. 68; Ms. 4. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंगः|अभ्यङ्ग|अभ्यंग|अभ्यङ्गः
अभ्यंगः<BR>1 Smearing the body with<BR>unctuous or oily substances,<BR>smearing with oil; अभ्यंगनेपथ्यमलंचकार<BR>Ku. 7. 7; स्तन्यदानाभ्यंगपोषणादिभिः<BR>पुपोष Pt. 5, Ms. 2. 178.<BR>--2 Smearing<BR>in general, inunction.<BR>--3 An<BR>unguent, salve, liniment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंजनं|अभ्यञ्जन|अभ्यंजन|अभ्यञ्जनं
अभ्यंजनं<BR>1 Smearing the body with<BR>oily substances, inunction;<BR>Ms. 10. 91.<BR>--2 Smearing or anointing in<BR>general.<BR>--3 Applying collyrium to<BR>the eyelashes; Ms. 2. 211.<BR>--4 An<BR>oily substance; oil, unguent.<BR>--5 An<BR>ornament, decoration (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यतीत
अभ्यतीत p. p. Dead, passed<BR>away; Ms. 4. 252.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यधिक
अभ्यधिक a.<BR>1 More than,<BR>exceeding, beyond; सद्यः<BR>प्रसूताप्रियापीतादभ्यधिकं U. 4. 1 remaining<BR>after &c. Pt. 2.<BR>--2 Surpassing, more<BR>than in quality or quantity, higher,<BR>greater; एष चाभ्यधिकोऽस्माकं गुणः<BR>Rām.; न त्वत्समोस्त्यभ्यधिकः कुतोन्यः<BR>Bg. 11. 43; M. 3. 3, Ms. 7. 177;<BR>Y. 2. 295; sometimes with abl.<BR>or instr.; धान्यं दशभ्यः कुंभेभ्यो<BR>हरतोऽभ्यधिकं वधः Ms. 8. 320, 322;<BR>Y. 2. 27; प्रभुः क्षमावान् वीरश्च दाता<BR>चाभ्यधिको नृपैः Nala. 21. 13.<BR>--3 More<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-a" target="_blank">Page0144-a+ 56</a>]<BR>than ordinary, extraordinary,<BR>preeminent; भव पंचाभ्यधिकः Ś. 6. 2.<BR>--कं adv. Very much, exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यध्वं|अभ्यध्व
अभ्यध्वं adv. Towards the way,<BR>on the way.<BR>--ध्वे Near the way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञा
अभ्यनुज्ञा {c9c} U.<BR>1 To permit,<BR>assent or agree to, approve; अतोऽ<BR>भ्यनुजानातु भवती K. 209; M. 3;<BR>Ms. 2. 1.<BR>--2 To permit one to go, grant<BR>leave to, dismiss. --Caus. To ask<BR>for leave to depart, take leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञा
अभ्यनुज्ञा, --ज्ञानं<BR>1 Consent,<BR>approval, permission; कृताभ्यनुज्ञा गुरुणा<BR>गरीयसा Ku. 5. 7, R. 2. 69.<BR>--2<BR>Order, command.<BR>--3 Granting<BR>leave of absence, dismissing.<BR>--4<BR>Admission of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनुज्ञानं|अभ्यनुज्ञान
अभ्यनुज्ञा, --ज्ञानं<BR>1 Consent,<BR>approval, permission; कृताभ्यनुज्ञा गुरुणा<BR>गरीयसा Ku. 5. 7, R. 2. 69.<BR>--2<BR>Order, command.<BR>--3 Granting<BR>leave of absence, dismissing.<BR>--4<BR>Admission of an argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यनूक्त
अभ्यनूक्त a. Said agreeably to<BR>what was said before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंतर|अभ्यन्तर|अभ्यन्तरं
अभ्यंतर a. [अभिगतमंतरं]<BR>1 Interior,<BR>internal, inner (opp. बाह्य);<BR>R. 17. 45; K. 66; Y. 3. 293.<BR>--2 Being<BR>included in, one of a group or body;<BR>देवीपरिजनाभ्यंतरः M. 5; गणाभ्यंतर<BR>एव च Ms. 3. 154; R. 8. 95.<BR>--3<BR>Initiated in, skilled or proficient in,<BR>familiar or conversant with; with<BR>loc., or sometimes gen., or in comp.;<BR>संगीतकेऽभ्यंतरेस्वः M. 5; अहो<BR>प्रयोगाभ्यंतरःप्राश्निकः M. 2; अनभ्यंतरे आवां<BR>मदनगतस्य वृत्तांतस्य Ś. 3; मंत्रेष्वभ्यतंराः के स्युः<BR>Rām., see अभ्यंतरीकृ below.<BR>--4<BR>Nearest, intimate, closely or intimately<BR>related; त्यक्ताश्चाभ्यंतरा येन Pt. 1. 259.<BR>--रं<BR>1 The inside or interior,<BR>inner or interior part (of any<BR>thing), space within; प्रविश्याभ्यंतरं<BR>रिपुः (नाशयेत्) Pt. 2. 38; K. 15, 17,<BR>18; ˚गतः आत्मा M. 5 inmost soul;<BR>शमीमिवाभ्यंतरलीनपावकां R. 3. 9;<BR>Bg. 5. 27, V. 2, Mk. 1, Ś. 7. 8.<BR>--2<BR>Included space, interval (of time<BR>or place); षण्मासाभ्यंतरे Pt. 4<BR>--3<BR>The mind.<BR>--रं, --रतः adv. In the<BR>interior, inside, inward.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आयामः {1} curvature of the spine<BR>by spasm. {2} emprosthotonos.<BR>--आराम a. internally delighted; see<BR>अंतराराम.<BR>--करण a. having the organs<BR>(concealed) inside, internally<BR>possessed of the powers of perception<BR>&c; ˚णया मया प्रत्यक्षीकृतवृत्तांतो<BR>महाराजः V. 4<BR>--(णं) the internal organ<BR>i. e. अंतःकरण.<BR>--कला the secret art,<BR>the art of coquetry or flirtation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंतरकः|अभ्यन्तरक|अभ्यन्तरकः
अभ्यंतरकः An intimate friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंतरीकृ|अभ्यन्तरीकृ
अभ्यंतरीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To initiate,<BR>familiarize with; प्रागल्भ्याद्वक्तुमिच्छंति<BR>मंत्रेष्वभ्यंतरीकृताः Rām.<BR>--2 To admit<BR>or introduce to; सर्वविश्रंभेषु<BR>अभ्यंतरीकरणीया K. 101; Dk. 159, 162;<BR>मुष्टिमर्धमुष्टिं वाभ्यंतरीकृत्य Dk. 156<BR>throwing down into (the belly).<BR>--3<BR>To make a near friend of (a person);<BR>बाह्याश्चाभ्यंतरीकृताः Pt. 1. 259.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यंतरीकरणं|अभ्यन्तरीकरण
अभ्यंतरीकरणं Initiating,<BR>introducing &c.; सजीवनिर्जीवासु च<BR>द्यूतकलास्वभ्यंतरीकरणं Dk. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यम्
अभ्यम् {c1c} P. Ved.<BR>1 To injure,<BR>pain, attack.<BR>--2 To overcome.<BR>--3 To<BR>be angry with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमनं|अभ्यमन
अभ्यमनं<BR>1 Attack, assault, injury.<BR>--2 Disease; ˚वत् diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित|अभ्यमितः
अभ्यमित, अभ्यांत p. p.<BR>1 Diseased,<BR>sick.<BR>--2 Injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यांत|अभ्यान्त
अभ्यमित, अभ्यांत p. p.<BR>1 Diseased,<BR>sick.<BR>--2 Injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमिन्
अभ्यमिन् a. [अम्-णिनि<BR>P. III. 2. 157]<BR>1 Attacking, inclined to<BR>attack.<BR>--2 Diseased, sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रं|अभ्यमित्र
अभ्यमित्रं An attack on an<BR>enemy. --adv. Towards or against the<BR>enemy; to face the enemy;<BR>Ki. 16. 5; Mv. 6; Ve. 5. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रीणः|अभ्यमित्रीण
अभ्यमित्रीणः, --यः, --मित्र्यः [अभ्यमित्र<BR>ख, छ, or यत्; अमित्रानभिमुखं सुष्ठु<BR>गच्छतीत्यर्थः P. V. 2. 17.] A warrior<BR>who valiantly encounters his enemy;<BR>उद्योगमभ्यमित्रीणो यथेष्टं त्वं च संतनु<BR>Bk. 5. 47; मारीचोऽनुनयंस्त्रासादभ्यमित्र्यो<BR>भवामि ते 46; Dk. 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्रीयः|अभ्यमित्रीय
अभ्यमित्रीणः, --यः, --मित्र्यः [अभ्यमित्र<BR>ख, छ, or यत्; अमित्रानभिमुखं सुष्ठु<BR>गच्छतीत्यर्थः P. V. 2. 17.] A warrior<BR>who valiantly encounters his enemy;<BR>उद्योगमभ्यमित्रीणो यथेष्टं त्वं च संतनु<BR>Bk. 5. 47; मारीचोऽनुनयंस्त्रासादभ्यमित्र्यो<BR>भवामि ते 46; Dk. 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यमित्र्यः|अभ्यमित्र्य
अभ्यमित्रीणः, --यः, --मित्र्यः [अभ्यमित्र<BR>ख, छ, or यत्; अमित्रानभिमुखं सुष्ठु<BR>गच्छतीत्यर्थः P. V. 2. 17.] A warrior<BR>who valiantly encounters his enemy;<BR>उद्योगमभ्यमित्रीणो यथेष्टं त्वं च संतनु<BR>Bk. 5. 47; मारीचोऽनुनयंस्त्रासादभ्यमित्र्यो<BR>भवामि ते 46; Dk. 171.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यय|अभ्ययः
अभ्यय See under अभी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्च्
अभ्यर्च् {c1c} {c10c} P.<BR>1 To honour,<BR>worship, R. 1. 35.<BR>--2 To praise,<BR>celebrate in song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्चनं|अभ्यर्चन|अभ्यर्च्चन
अभ्यर्चनं, --र्चा Worship, adoration,<BR>reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्चा|अभ्यर्च्चा
अभ्यर्चनं, --र्चा Worship, adoration,<BR>reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ण|अभ्यर्णं|अभ्यर्ण्ण
अभ्यर्ण a. [अभि-अर्द्-क्त,<BR>P. VII. 2. 25 Sk.] Near, proximate, adjoining,<BR>being close or near (of space);<BR>approaching, drawing near (of time);<BR>अभ्यर्णमागस्कृतमस्पृशद्भिः R. 2. 32; आश्रम˚<BR>भूमिः U. 4; Mu. 6; K. 69, 125,<BR>208, 286; Māl. 5. 13; Ratn. 3. 10,<BR>Bk. 3. 28.<BR>--र्णं Proximity, vicinity;<BR>अंधकारिणि वनाभ्यर्णे किमुद्भ्राम्यति<BR>Gīt. 7; अभ्यर्णे परिरभ्य निर्भरभरः प्रेमांधया<BR>राधया Gīt. 1, Śi. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्णता
अभ्यर्णता Proximity; Śi. 12. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थ्
अभ्यर्थ् {c10c} A.<BR>1 To request, beg,<BR>solicit, ask, entreat (with two acc.);<BR>इमं सारगं प्रियाप्रवृत्तिनिमित्तं अभ्यर्थये<BR>V. 4; मां अनभ्यर्थनीयमभ्यर्थयते Māl. 7;<BR>अवकाशं किलोदन्वान् रामायाभ्यर्थितो ददौ<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">Page0144-c+ 56</a>]<BR>R. 4. 58.<BR>--2 To long for, desire, woo,<BR>court; यदि सा तापसकन्यका<BR>अनभ्यर्थनीया Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थनं|अभ्यर्थन
अभ्यर्थनं --ना A request, an entreaty<BR>petition, suit; ˚नाभंगभयेन Ku. 1. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थना
अभ्यर्थनं --ना A request, an entreaty<BR>petition, suit; ˚नाभंगभयेन Ku. 1. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थनीय
अभ्यर्थनीय, --र्थ्य pot. p. To be<BR>asked, requested or desired; R. 10. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थ्य
अभ्यर्थनीय, --र्थ्य pot. p. To be<BR>asked, requested or desired; R. 10. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्थिन्
अभ्यर्थिन् a. One who begs, asks, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्दनं
अभ्यर्दनं Torturing, distressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ध
अभ्यर्ध a. Ved.<BR>1 Being on this<BR>side.<BR>--2 Near.<BR>--3 Increasing.<BR>--र्धं<BR>Nearness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--यज्वन् m.<BR>granting gifts, increasing the sacrificer's<BR>prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्ह्
अभ्यर्ह् {c1c} {c10c} P. To salute,<BR>honor, worship, pay one's respects<BR>or compliments; परशुरामो<BR>माल्यवंतमभ्यर्हयति Mv. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हणा
अभ्यर्हणा<BR>1 Worship.<BR>--2 Respect,<BR>honour, reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हणीय
अभ्यर्हणीय pot. p. Respectable,<BR>venerable; ˚ता Ms. 9. 23 a<BR>position of honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यर्हित
अभ्यर्हित a.<BR>1 Honoured, revered,<BR>greatly respectable or venerable;<BR>अभ्यर्हितं च (द्वंद्वे पूर्वं स्यात्) Sk, K. 209.<BR>--2 Fit, becoming, suitable; अभ्यर्हिता<BR>बंधुषु तुल्यरूपा वृत्तिर्विशेषेण तपोधनानां<BR>Ki. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवकर्षणं|अभ्यवकर्षण
अभ्यवकर्षणं Extraction,<BR>drawing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवकाशः|अभ्यवकाश
अभ्यवकाशः An open space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवदान्य
अभ्यवदान्य Ved. Not liberal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहित
अभ्यवहित Laid, allayed, put<BR>down (e. g. dust).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कंद्|अभ्यवस्कन्द्
अभ्यवस्कंद्^1 {c1c} P. To jump up<BR>or upon, attack.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20160121. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/243. note: Bv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कंदः|अभ्यवस्कन्द|अभ्यवस्कन्दः
अभ्यवस्कंदः --दनं<BR>1 Vigorously<BR>encountering an enemy, impetuous<BR>attack, marching against an enemy.<BR>--2 Striking so as to disable an<BR>enemy.<BR>--3 A blow in general.<BR>--4<BR>Overtaking, reaching up to.<BR>--5 A fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवस्कंदनं|अभ्यवस्कन्दन|अभ्यवस्कन्दनं
अभ्यवस्कंदः --दनं<BR>1 Vigorously<BR>encountering an enemy, impetuous<BR>attack, marching against an enemy.<BR>--2 Striking so as to disable an<BR>enemy.<BR>--3 A blow in general.<BR>--4<BR>Overtaking, reaching up to.<BR>--5 A fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहृ
अभ्यवहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To throw, fling,<BR>cast.<BR>--2 To collect, draw in, procure,<BR>obtain.<BR>--3 To use as food or drink,<BR>eat; सक्तून् पिब धानाः खादेत्यभ्यवहरति<BR>P. III. 4. 5 Sk. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause<BR>to throw down (in water).<BR>--2 To<BR>cause to take or eat (as food), feed<BR>(one with something); शक्नोषि<BR>किमनेन शालिप्रस्थेन<BR>संपन्नमन्नमस्मानभ्यवहारयितुं Dk. 131, 72, 132; to take or<BR>eat (oneself).<BR>--3 To lay or put on<BR>(snares &c.).<BR>--4 To attack; get<BR>one to oppose another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहरणं|अभ्यवहरण
अभ्यवहरणं<BR>1 Throwing away or<BR>down.<BR>--2 Eating, taking food;<BR>Throwing down the throat (<BR>कंठादधोनयनं Mit.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहारः|अभ्यवहार
अभ्यवहारः<BR>1 Eating, taking food,<BR>eating, drinking &c.<BR>--2 Food;<BR>जंभशब्दोऽभ्यवहारार्थवाची Kāśi.;<BR>˚संवादापेक्षी M. 4; V. 2; Ratn. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवहार्य|अभ्यवहार्य्य
अभ्यवहार्य pot. p. Fit to eat, eatable.<BR>--र्यं Food; सर्वत्रौदरिकस्य<BR>अभ्यवहार्यमेव विषयः V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवे
अभ्यवे [˚इ] {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go down,<BR>descend; अवभृथमभ्यवैति Ait. Br.<BR>--2 To<BR>perceive, understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यवायनं|अभ्यवायन
अभ्यवायनं Going down,<BR>descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यश्
अभ्यश् {c5c} A. (P. also in Ved.)<BR> To pervade, reach to, get, gain;<BR>to make oneself master of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यशनं|अभ्यशन
अभ्यशनं Pervading, reaching to,<BR>gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्याश a. Near, proximate.<BR>--शः<BR>1 Reaching to, pervading.<BR>--2 Proximate neighbourhood,<BR>vicinity (also written as अभ्यास<BR>q. v.); वायसाभ्याशे समुपविष्टः Pt. 2:<BR>सहसाभ्यागतां भैमीमभ्याशपरिवर्तिनीं Mb.,<BR>Dk. 62.<BR>--3 Result, consequence.<BR>--4<BR>Prospect, hope of gaining; hence<BR>oft. used in the sense of ‘quickly’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्
अभ्यस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To practise,<BR>exercise; धन्यो वन्यमतंगजः<BR>परिचयप्रागल्भ्यमभ्यस्यति Māl. 9. 32;<BR>अभ्यस्यतीव व्रतमासिधारं R. 13. 67;<BR>Ms. 11. 107.<BR>--2 To repeat, perform<BR>repeatedly; मृगकुलं रोमंथमभ्यस्यतु Ś. 2. 6;<BR>अभ्यस्यंति तटाघातं Ku. 2. 50;<BR>K. 183.<BR>--3 To learn, study, acquire<BR>or learn by practice, recite, read;<BR>वेदमेव सदाभ्यस्येत् Ms. 2. 166;<BR>4. 147; 4. 149; Y. 3. 204; K. 79.<BR>--4<BR>To throw down upon, heap one<BR>upon another, accumulate, lay on (Ved.).<BR>--5 To throw or fling at, shoot or<BR>aim at (as arrows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसनं|अभ्यसन
अभ्यसनं<BR>1 Repetition, repeated<BR>practice or exercise;<BR>ब्रह्मध्यानाभ्यसनविधिना Bh. 3. 41; स्वाध्यायाभ्यसनं<BR>Bg. 17. 15.<BR>--2 Constant study, close<BR>application (to any thing); (तां)<BR>विद्यामभ्यसनेनेव प्रसादयितुमर्हसि R. 1. 88;<BR>अनभ्यसनशीलस्य विद्येव तनुतां गता Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्त|अभ्यस्तं
अभ्यस्त p. p.<BR>1 Repeated,<BR>frequently practised, exercised;<BR>नयनयोरभ्यरतमामीलनं Amaru. 92; used or<BR>accustomed to; अनभ्यस्तरथचर्याः<BR>U. 5 not accustomed to the use of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-b" target="_blank">Page0145-b+ 58</a>]<BR>chariot; ˚गुणा च वाणी Māl. 3. 11.<BR>--2 Learnt, studied; शैशवेऽ<BR>भ्यस्तविद्यानां R. 1. 8; Bh. 3. 89.<BR>--3 (In<BR>Math.) Multiplied; अयुतं दशकृत्वोऽ<BR>भ्यस्तं नियुतमुच्यते Nir.<BR>--4 (In gram.)<BR>Reduplicated.<BR>--स्तं Reduplicated<BR>base of a root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासः|अभ्यास
अभ्यासः<BR>1 Repetition in general;<BR>व्याख्याता व्याख्याता इति पदाभ्यासोऽ<BR>ध्यायपरिसमाप्तिं द्योतयति Ś. B.;<BR>नाभ्यासक्रममीक्षते Pt. 1. 151; Ms. 12. 74;<BR>Y. 3. 323.<BR>--2 Repeated practice or exercise,<BR>continued practice or use;<BR>अविरतश्रमाभ्यासात् K. 30, Pt. 1. 133;<BR>अभ्यासेन तु कौंतेय वैराग्येण च गृह्यते<BR>Bg. 6. 35, 44 by constant practice (to<BR>remain pure and unmodified); 12. 12;<BR>योग˚ Y. 3. 51 practice of<BR>concentration; hence sometimes used for<BR>‘concentration of mind upon one<BR>subject’; ˚निगृहीतेन मनसा R. 10. 23; so<BR>शर˚, अस्त्र˚ &c.<BR>--3 Habit, custom,<BR>practice; मिथ्योपपदात् कृञोऽभ्यासे<BR>P. I. 3. 71; तद् यथाभ्यासं अभिधीयतां<BR>U. 1 therefore address me as<BR>is your wont; अमंगलाभ्यासरतिं<BR>Ku. 5. 65; Y. 3. 68.<BR>--4<BR>Discipline in arms, exercise, military<BR>discipline.<BR>--5 Reciting, study,<BR>repeated reading or learning by heart;<BR>काव्यज्ञशिक्षयाभ्यासः K. P. 1; K. 146,<BR>200; Ms. 5. 4; वेद˚ is of 5 kinds:<BR>--वेदस्वीकरणं पूर्वं विचारोऽभ्यसनं जपः । तद्दानं<BR>चैव शिष्येभ्यो वेदाभ्यासो हि पंचधा ॥ Dakṣa.<BR>--6 Vicinity, proximity,<BR>neighbourhood (for अभ्याश); चूतयष्टिरिवाभ्यासे<BR>(शे) मधौ परभृतोन्मुखी Ku. 6. 2; (<BR>अभ्यासे-शे मधौ must mean here speaking<BR>to ‘Madhu who was near her,’ scil.<BR>by having manifested himself<BR>before her, which fully<BR>preserves the simile of Pārvatī, herself<BR>silent, speaking to her lover who<BR>was near her through her friend);<BR>अर्पितेयं तवाभ्यासे सीता पुण्यव्रता वधूः<BR>U. 7. 17 given in your charge;<BR>Śi. 3. 40; अभ्यासा-शा-दागतः<BR>P. II. 1. 38 Sk. (regarded as an Aluk<BR>compound).<BR>--7 (In gram.)<BR>Reduplication.<BR>--8 The first syllable of a<BR>reduplicated base, reduplicative<BR>syllable; पूर्वोऽभ्यासः P. VI. 1. 4; अत्र<BR>ये द्वे विहिते तयोः पूर्वोऽभ्याससंज्ञः स्यात् Sk.<BR>--9 (In Math.) Multiplication.<BR>--10<BR>(In poetry) Repetition of the<BR>last verses or lines (as of a<BR>chorus); chorus, burden of a<BR>song.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गत a. approached,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">Page0145-c+ 56</a>]<BR>gone near.<BR>--परिवर्तिन् a. wandering<BR>about or near.<BR>--योगः abstraction of<BR>mind resulting from continuous<BR>deep meditation; अभ्यासयोगेन ततो<BR>मामिच्छाप्तुं धनंजय Bg. 12. 9.<BR>--लोपः<BR>dropping of the reduplicative<BR>syllable.<BR>--व्यवायः interval caused by the<BR>reduplicative syllable; ˚येपि though<BR>separated by this syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासिन्
अभ्यासिन् a. Practising, exercising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयति
अभ्यसूयति Den. P.<BR>1 To be<BR>angry with, bear malice against, envy,<BR>be jealous of (with acc.); न च<BR>मांयोऽभ्यसूयति Bg. 18. 67; प्रहसंति स्म तां<BR>केचिदभ्यसूयंति चापरे Mb.<BR>--2 Not to like,<BR>detract from, calumniate; ये<BR>त्वेतदभ्यसूयंतो नानुतिष्ठंति मे मतं Bg. 3. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूय
अभ्यसूय a. Angry, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूयक
अभ्यसूयक a. (यिका f.) Jealous,<BR>envious; a detractor, calumniator;<BR>मामात्मपरदेहेषु प्रद्विषंतोऽभ्यसूयकाः Bg. 16. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यसूया
अभ्यसूया Envy, jealousy, disfavour,<BR>anger; शुक्राभ्यसूयाविनिवृत्तये यः<BR>R. 6. 74; रूपेषु वेशेषु च साभ्यसूयाः 7. 2, 9. 64;<BR>Me. 39, Ku. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तं|अभ्यस्त
अभ्यस्तं ind. [अस्तमभि] Towards<BR>sunset; ˚गम्-इ, --या to go down or<BR>set (as the sun) during or with<BR>reference to some act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तमयः|अभ्यस्तमय
अभ्यस्तमयः Setting of the sun<BR>during or with reference to some act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यस्तमित
अभ्यस्तमित a. One on whom the<BR>sun has set while asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकर्षः|अभ्याकर्ष
अभ्याकर्षः Striking the breast<BR>with the flat of the hand as a sign<BR>of defiance (as by wrestlers &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकांक्षितं|अभ्याकाङ्क्षित|अभ्याकांक्षित|अभ्याकाङ्क्षितं
अभ्याकांक्षितं<BR>1 A false charge,<BR>groundless complaint.<BR>--2 A desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याकारं
अभ्याकारं adv. By drawing to<BR>oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याक्रामं
अभ्याक्रामं ind. By or in<BR>stepping near or mutually, in stepping<BR>rapidly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याख्यात
अभ्याख्यात a. Falsely accused,<BR>traduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याख्यानं|अभ्याख्यान
अभ्याख्यानं A false charge;<BR>calumny, detraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागम्
अभ्यागम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go near to,<BR>draw near, approach; visit; see<BR>अभ्यागत below; to come, arrive (as<BR>time).<BR>--2 To come to, fall into, go to<BR>any state; चिंतामभ्यागतः fell to<BR>thinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागत|अभ्यागतः
अभ्यागत p. p.<BR>1 Come near,<BR>approached, arrived; भोभवानभ्यागतोऽतिथिः Pt. 4;<BR>क्रमादभ्यागतं द्रव्यं Y. 2. 119; तस्मिन्नभ्या<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">Page0146-a+ 55</a>]<BR>गते काले Rām.<BR>--2 Come as a guest;<BR>सर्वत्राभ्यागतो गुरुः H. 1. 108;<BR>श्रोत्रियाय अभ्यागताय U. 4; Śi. 4. 68.<BR>--तः<BR>A guest, visitor; ˚क्रियया नियोजितः<BR>Pt. 2; K. 280; Śi. 3. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागमः|अभ्यागम
अभ्यागमः<BR>1 Coming or going near,<BR>arrival; a visit; तपोधनाभ्यागमसंभवा<BR>मुदः Śi. 1. 23; किं वा मदभ्यागमकारणं<BR>ते R. 16. 8; Mv. 2. 22; वसंतमास˚<BR>K. 308.<BR>--2 Vicinity, neighbourhood.<BR>--3 Arriving at or enjoying a result.<BR>--4 Rising, getting up.<BR>--5 Striking,<BR>killing.<BR>--6 Encountering, attacking.<BR>--7 War, battle.<BR>--8 Enmity, hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागमनं|अभ्यागमन
अभ्यागमनं Approach, arrival, visit;<BR>हेतुं तदभ्यागमने परीप्सुः Ki. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यागारिकः|अभ्यागारिक
अभ्यागारिकः [अभ्यागारे<BR>तत्संबंधिकर्मणि व्यापृतः ठन्] One who is diligent<BR>in supporting a family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याघातः|अभ्याघात
अभ्याघातः<BR>1 An attack, assault,<BR>striking.<BR>--2 Persuading to steal;<BR>Ms. 9. 272.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याघातिन्
अभ्याघातिन् a. Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याचर्
अभ्याचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To approach.<BR>--2<BR>To use, practise, perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याचारः|अभ्याचार
अभ्याचारः Ved. Approaching (as<BR>an enemy); disturbing, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याज्ञायः|अभ्याज्ञाय
अभ्याज्ञायः Ved. [ज्ञां-घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Recognition.<BR>--2 Order, command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यातन्
अभ्यातन् {c8c} U. To take aim at,<BR>shoot or hurl (missiles) against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यातानः|अभ्यातान
अभ्यातानः Spreading over,<BR>stretching, expansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यात्म
अभ्यात्म a. Directed towards<BR>oneself.<BR>--त्मं adv. Towards oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यादा
अभ्यादा {c3c} A.<BR>1 To take, seize,<BR>snatch.<BR>--2 To put on, wear (garland<BR>&c.).<BR>--3 To take up (the<BR>conversation), to commence speaking (after<BR>another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यात्त
अभ्यात्त p. p.<BR>1 Obtained, got.<BR>--2<BR>Occupied or pervaded; epithet of<BR>the Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यादानं|अभ्यादान
अभ्यादानं Beginning,<BR>commencement, first beginning; ओमभ्यादाने<BR>P. VIII. 2. 87 (˚ने = आरंभे Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याधा
अभ्याधा {c3c} U. To lay on, add<BR>(fuel &c.) to apply, throw under;<BR>Ms. 8. 372; यथाग्निरभ्याहितं दहति Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याधानं|अभ्याधान
अभ्याधानं Laying on, adding (as<BR>fuel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहित
अभ्याहित p. p. Laid down, put on;<BR>˚पशुः a sort of gift or present;<BR>P. VI. 3. 10 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यांत|अभ्यान्त
अभ्यांत See under अभ्यम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यापातः|अभ्यापात
अभ्यापातः A calamity,<BR>misfortune, evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यामर्दः|अभ्यामर्द|अभ्यामर्द्द
अभ्यामर्दः, --मर्दनं War, battle,<BR>conflict, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यामर्दनं|अभ्यामर्दन
अभ्यामर्दः, --मर्दनं War, battle,<BR>conflict, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यायम्
अभ्यायम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To stretch,<BR>extend, lengthen (sound), draw or<BR>pull (as a rudder).<BR>--2 To give.<BR>--3<BR>To aim at.<BR>--4 To restrain.<BR>--5 To<BR>approach, visit (= अभ्यागम्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यायंसेन्य
अभ्यायंसेन्य a. [यम्-कर्मणि वाहु˚ सेन्य]<BR>To be restrained, to be made<BR>subject; (अभितो नियंतव्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारं
अभ्यारं adv. Near, at hand; by<BR>going near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारुह्
अभ्यारुह् {c1c} P. To ascend, go<BR>up to, reach, get to (mostly Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारूढ
अभ्यारूढ p. p.<BR>1 Ascended, gone<BR>up to.<BR>--2 Surpassed, excelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोहः|अभ्यारोह
अभ्यारोहः, --रोहणं<BR>1 Ascending,<BR>mounting, going up to.<BR>--2<BR>Ascending in prayer or devotion,<BR>muttering holy prayers.<BR>--3 Transition from<BR>one place or state to another.<BR>--4<BR>Progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोहणं|अभ्यारोहण
अभ्यारोहः, --रोहणं<BR>1 Ascending,<BR>mounting, going up to.<BR>--2<BR>Ascending in prayer or devotion,<BR>muttering holy prayers.<BR>--3 Transition from<BR>one place or state to another.<BR>--4<BR>Progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यारोहणीयः|अभ्यारोहणीय
अभ्यारोहणीयः N. of a religious<BR>ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावृत्
अभ्यावृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To come up to,<BR>approach.<BR>--2 To come again, be<BR>repeated. --Caus.<BR>1 To come down,<BR>approach.<BR>--2 To repeat (as सावित्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावर्तः|अभ्यावर्त|अभ्यावर्त्त
अभ्यावर्तः<BR>1 Repetition.<BR>--2 A hymn<BR>the verses of which are repeated<BR>in singing (आवृत्तिस्तोत्रं).<BR>--र्तं adv.<BR>By repeating, repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावर्तिन्|अभ्यावर्त्तिन्
अभ्यावर्तिन् a. Recurring, Śi. 18. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावृत्त|अभ्यावृत्तः
अभ्यावृत्त p. p. Come near to,<BR>repeated.<BR>--त्तः The residue of<BR>sacrificial offerings (होमशेषद्रव्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यावृत्तिः|अभ्यावृत्ति
अभ्यावृत्तिः f. Repetition,<BR>recurrence (so many times); see<BR>P. V. 4. 17, and Sk. thereon; see<BR>अनभ्यावृत्ति also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याश|अभ्याशः
अभ्याश --स see under अभ्यश्-स्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यास|अभ्यासः
अभ्याश --स see under अभ्यश्-स्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासद्
अभ्यासद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To get, obtain,<BR>attain; स्वमिव पुरुषकारं शैलमभ्याससाद<BR>Ki. 5. 52.<BR>--2 To sit oneself in (acc.).<BR>--Caus. To attack, assail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यासादनं|अभ्यासादन
अभ्यासादनं Attacking or facing an<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहन्
अभ्याहन् {c2c} P. To strike, smite,<BR>wound, injure, kill, destroy; वृक्षस्य<BR>यो मूलेऽभ्याहन्यात् Ch. Up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहत
अभ्याहत p. p.<BR>1 Struck, beaten.<BR>--2 Affected, smitten; अभ्याहतं<BR>कीर्तिविपर्ययेण (हृदयं) R. 14. 33; मृत्युना<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">Page0146-c+ 55</a>]<BR>˚तः &c.<BR>--3 Impeded, obstructed;<BR>रक्षोभिरभ्याहतकर्मवृत्तिः Bk. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहननं|अभ्याहनन
अभ्याहननं<BR>1 Striking, hurting,<BR>killing.<BR>--2 Impeding, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहृ
अभ्याहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring towards,<BR>bring near; to give or hand over;<BR>गृहीत्वा फलमूलं च रामस्याभ्याहरन् बहु<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 To rob, plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहारः|अभ्याहार
अभ्याहारः<BR>1 Bringing near or<BR>towards, conveying.<BR>--2 Robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्याहार्य|अभ्याहार्य्य
अभ्याहार्य pot. p. To be eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्त
अभ्युक्त a. Said with reference<BR>to some object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्ष्
अभ्युक्ष् {c1c} {c6c} U. To sprinkle over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युक्षणं|अभ्युक्षण
अभ्युक्षणं<BR>1 Sprinkling over,<BR>wetting; परस्पराभ्युक्षणतत्पराणां (तासां)<BR>R. 16. 57.<BR>--2 Consecration by<BR>sprinkling; (प्रोक्षण, अभ्युक्षण and अवोक्षण<BR>are thus distinguished; उत्तानेनैव<BR>हस्तेन प्रोक्षणं परिकीतिंतम् । न्यंचताभ्युक्षणं प्रोक्तं<BR>तिरश्चावोक्षणं स्मृतम् ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युचित
अभ्युचित a. Usual, customary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युच्चयः|अभ्युच्चय
अभ्युच्चयः [चि-अच्]<BR>1 Increase,<BR>augmentation, growth.<BR>--2 Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युच्छ्रित
अभ्युच्छ्रित a. Uplifted,<BR>upraised; elevated by, distinguished for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्क्रुष्ट
अभ्युत्क्रुष्ट p. p. Praised with loud<BR>acclamations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्क्रोशनं|अभ्युत्क्रोशन
अभ्युत्क्रोशनं Loud acclamation;<BR>˚मंत्र a hymn of applause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्था
अभ्युत्था {c1c} P. To rise for another,<BR>rise in honour of, rise to greet;<BR>नाभ्युत्तिष्ठंति गुरून् K. 108; Ś. 3;<BR>M. 5. 6; Śi. 4. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थानं|अभ्युत्थान
अभ्युत्थानं<BR>1 Rising(from a seat)<BR>to do honour, rising in honour<BR>of; नाभ्युत्यानक्रिया यत्र Pt. 2. 62.<BR>--2<BR>Starting, departure, setting out;<BR>अभ्युत्थानं च युद्धार्थे Rām.<BR>--3 Rise<BR>(lit. and fig.), elevation, exaltation,<BR>prosperity, dignity, a position of<BR>dignity or authority; (तस्य)<BR>नवाभ्युत्थानदर्शिन्यो ननंदुः सप्रजाः प्रजाः R. 4. 3;<BR>यदा यदा हि धर्मस्य ग्लानिर्भवति भारत ।<BR>अभ्युत्थानमधर्मस्य तदात्मानं सृजाम्यहं<BR>Bg. 4. 7 when impiety increases or is<BR>in the ascendant.<BR>--4 Sunrise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थायिन्
अभ्युत्थायिन् a. Rising to greet or<BR>in honour of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्थित
अभ्युत्थित p. p.<BR>1 Risen, arisen,<BR>gone up.<BR>--2 Blazing, flaming (fire);<BR>R. 1. 53.<BR>--3 Elevated, exalted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्पत्
अभ्युत्पत् {c1c} P. To fly up to,<BR>jump up to, leap upon. --Caus.<BR>To cause to fly up to (acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युत्पतनं|अभ्युत्पतन
अभ्युत्पतनं Springing or leaping<BR>against, sudden spring or leap,<BR>assault; अलक्षिताभ्युत्पतनो नृपेण<BR>R. 2. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदाहरणं|अभ्युदाहरण
अभ्युदाहरणं An example or<BR>illustration of a thing by its reverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदि
अभ्युदि {c2c} P. [उद्-इ]<BR>1 To rise<BR>(fig. also); go up (as the sun);<BR>Ms. 4. 104.<BR>--2 To rise over (one); Ms. 2. 220,<BR>219.<BR>--3 To come into existence,<BR>happen, originate.<BR>--4 To engage in<BR>combat with (one), encounter,<BR>(लोकवीरान्) को जीवितार्थी समरेऽभ्युदीयात्<BR>Mb.<BR>--5 To prosper, thrive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदय|अभ्युदयः
अभ्युदय a. Rising.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Rise(of<BR>heavenly bodies); sunrise.<BR>--2 Rise,<BR>prosperity, good fortune, elevation,<BR>success; स्पृशंति नः स्वामिनमभ्युदयाः<BR>Ratn. 1 success; भवो हि लोकाभ्युदयाय<BR>ताटृशां R. 3. 14; Ms. 3. 254; Bh. 2. 63;<BR>R. 12. 3, V. 5.<BR>--3 A festival; any<BR>religious or festive celebration,<BR>festive occasion; ˚कालः joyous or festive<BR>occasion; Ś. 7; Ms. 9. 84.<BR>--4<BR>Beginning, commencement.<BR>--5 Occurrence,<BR>happening.<BR>--6 Accomplishment of a<BR>desired object (which is the cause of<BR>festivity).<BR>--7 The tonsure<BR>ceremony.<BR>--8 A Śrāddha performed on<BR>account of child-birth (वृद्धिश्राद्धं)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थकं a Śrāddha for<BR>prosperity or elevation.<BR>--इष्टिः f. N. of<BR>a particular expiatory sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदयिन्
अभ्युदयिन् a. Rising, going up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युदित|अभ्युदितः
अभ्युदित p. p.<BR>1 Risen; occurred.<BR>--2 Elevated, risen to prosperity.<BR>--3<BR>Asleep at sunrise, over whom the<BR>sun has risen; Ms. 2. 221.<BR>--4<BR>Celebrated as a festival.<BR>--ता N. of a religious<BR>ceremony.<BR>--तं Rising; sunrise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गम्
अभ्युद्गम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go forth to<BR>meet.<BR>--2 To extend, spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्ग
अभ्युद्ग a. Rising, uprisen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गत
अभ्युद्गत p. p.<BR>1 Gone forth to<BR>meet.<BR>--2 Extended, spread; elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गमः|अभ्युद्गम
अभ्युद्गमः, --मनं, --गतिः f.<BR>1 Going<BR>forth to meet or to do honour (to a<BR>guest or to a venerable person).<BR>--2 Rising, occurring, originating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गमनं|अभ्युद्गमन
अभ्युद्गमः, --मनं, --गतिः f.<BR>1 Going<BR>forth to meet or to do honour (to a<BR>guest or to a venerable person).<BR>--2 Rising, occurring, originating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्गतिः|अभ्युद्गति
अभ्युद्गमः, --मनं, --गतिः f.<BR>1 Going<BR>forth to meet or to do honour (to a<BR>guest or to a venerable person).<BR>--2 Rising, occurring, originating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्दृष्टं|अभ्युद्दृष्ट
अभ्युद्दृष्टं Becoming visible (of<BR>a star).<BR>--ष्टा N. of a ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्धृत
अभ्युद्धृत a.<BR>1 Taken out, taken<BR>up.<BR>--2 Got without solicitation.<BR>--3 Got after a request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्यम्
अभ्युद्यम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring, offer.<BR>--2 To lift up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युद्यत
अभ्युद्यत p. p.<BR>1 Raised, lifted up;<BR>as ˚आयुध, ˚शस्त्र, ˚कर &c.<BR>--2 Prepared<BR>or ready, exerting oneself for (with<BR>inf., dat., loc. or in comp.);<BR>M. 3. 20, Ku. 3. 70;<BR>Bṛ. S. 12. 6; Me. 57; Ms. 9. 302.<BR>--3 Gone<BR>forth, risen, appearing forth or<BR>approaching; कुलमभ्युद्यतनूतनेश्वरं<BR>R. 8. 15.<BR>--4 Given or brought unsolicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युन्नत
अभ्युन्नत a.<BR>1 Raised, elevated;<BR>अभ्युन्नता पुरस्तात् Ś. 3. 8.<BR>--2<BR>Projecting upwards; very high; Ku. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युन्नतिः|अभ्युन्नति
अभ्युन्नतिः f. Great elevation or<BR>prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगम्
अभ्युपगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 (a) To go to<BR>or near, approach; परलोकमभ्युपगते<BR>(भर्तरि) विविशुः Śi. 9. 13. (b) To<BR>come to the help of; वयमभ्युपगच्छामः<BR>कृष्णेन त्वां प्रधर्षितं Hariv. (c) To have<BR>recourse to. (d) To arrive at (a point<BR>of time); आषाढीमभ्युपगतो भरतः<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 To obtain, get.<BR>--3 To<BR>admit, grant, own; अभ्युपगतं<BR>तावदस्माभिरेवं Ś. 5 we admit all this; Mu. 3.<BR>--4 To assent to, agree to, undertake,<BR>promise; Dk. 73. --Caus. To<BR>induce or cause one to assent to or<BR>grant; मामभ्युपगमय्य Dk. 60, 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगत|अभ्युपगतः
अभ्युपगत p. p.<BR>1 Approached,<BR>agreed or assented to; granted;<BR>suffered; Ratn. 4. 20; promised &c.<BR>--2 Inferred, probable.<BR>--3 Similar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगमः|अभ्युपगम
अभ्युपगमः<BR>1 Approach, arrival.<BR>--2<BR>Granting, admitting, accepting to<BR>be true P. VIII. 3. 74 Sk.;<BR>confession (as of guilt); Ratn. 2. 19.<BR>--3 Undertaking, promising; निर्णय˚<BR>M. 1; a contract, agreement,<BR>promise; Ms. 9. 53.<BR>--4 Probable<BR>ascertainment, belief; judgment, a view<BR>accepted; Mv. 1. 38; supposition,<BR>inference.<BR>--5 Analogy, affinity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सिद्धांतः an admitted<BR>proposition or axiom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपगमित|अभ्युपगमितः
अभ्युपगमित caus. p. p. Made to<BR>consent, obtained by free consent.<BR>--तः A slave for a fixed term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपद्
अभ्युपपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To deliver (from<BR>distress), protect; to console,<BR>comfort, take compassion or pity on,<BR>pity, favour; रतिमभ्युपपत्तुमातुरां<BR>मधुरात्मानमदर्शयत्पुरः Ku. 4. 25; (कदा)<BR>तपःकृशामभ्युपपत्स्यते सखीं वृषेव सीतां<BR>तदवग्रहक्षतां 5. 61; U. 2, 3, 7; Māl. 4.<BR>--2<BR>To ask for help, seek protection,<BR>submit; अभ्युपपन्नवत्सलः Mk. 7.<BR>--3 To<BR>furnish with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपत्तिः|अभ्युपपत्ति
अभ्युपपत्तिः f.<BR>1 Approaching to<BR>assist, taking pity or compassion on,<BR>favouring; a favour, kindness;<BR>अभ्युपपत्त्या अस्या जीवितमवलंबस्व Ś. 3;<BR>अनयाभ्युपपत्त्या Ś. 4; मम˚ निमित्तं<BR>Mk. 1.<BR>--2 Consolation.<BR>--3 Protection,<BR>defence; ब्राह्मणाभ्युपपत्तौ च शपथे नास्ति<BR>पातकं Ms. 8. 112, 349; 10. 62;<BR>आर्त˚ Dk. 39.<BR>--4 An agreement,<BR>assent, promise.<BR>--5 Impregnation of a<BR>woman (especially of a brother's<BR>widow as an act of duty).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपपादनं|अभ्युपपादन
अभ्युपपादनं Protection &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपस्थित
अभ्युपस्थित a. Accompanied,<BR>assisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपाकृत
अभ्युपाकृत a. Asked to take<BR>part in a ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपे
अभ्युपे {c2c} P. [˚उप-इ]<BR>1 To go<BR>near, approach, arrive, enter;<BR>व्यतीतकालस्त्वहमभ्युपेतः R. 5. 14, 16. 22;<BR>त्रिरह्नोऽभ्युपयन्नपः Ms. 11. 260 entering the<BR>water i. e. bathing; Y. 3. 3.<BR>--2 To go to or<BR>enter a particular state, attain to; सत्यं<BR>न तद्यच्छलमभ्युपैति H. 3. 61; so<BR>ब्राह्मणतां, वैश्यतां, सखित्वं &c.<BR>--3 To agree,<BR>(to do something), accept, promise,<BR>undertake; मंदायंने न खलु<BR>सुहृदामभ्युपेतार्थकृत्याः Me. 38; अस्यै दास्यमभ्युपेतं<BR>मया Dk. 44, 55, 89, 138, 159.<BR>--4<BR>To admit, grant, own, acknowledge,<BR>Śi. 11. 67; श्रुत्यैव च<BR>तर्कस्याभ्युपपेतत्वात् Ś. B.; Dk. 45.<BR>--5 To approve,<BR>agree with, assent to.<BR>--6 To obey,<BR>submit to, be faithful to; विरोध्य<BR>मोहात्पुनरभ्युपेयुषां Ki. 18. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपायः|अभ्युपाय
अभ्युपायः<BR>1 A promise, an<BR>engagement, agreement.<BR>--2 A means, an<BR>expedient, remedy; अस्मिन्सुराणां<BR>विजयाभ्युपाये Ku. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपायनं|अभ्युपायन
अभ्युपायनं A complimentary<BR>present; inducement, bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युपेत्य
अभ्युपेत्य ind. Having approached<BR>having agreed or promised.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अशुश्रूषा one of the 18 titles of<BR>Hindu law, breach of contract or<BR>engagement between master and<BR>servant (where the servant does not<BR>work having agreed to do so).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युषः|अभ्युष
अभ्युषः, अभ्यूषः, अभ्योषः [अभितः<BR>उऊ-ष्यते अग्निना दह्यते, उ-ऊ-ष् वाहु˚ क]<BR>1<BR>A sort of cake or bread (Mar. पोळी or<BR>रोटी) (अर्धस्विन्नयवादेर्घृतादिना भर्जितयवादेर्वा<BR>घृतपक्वान्नस्य पोळी इति ख्यातस्य नाम).<BR>--2<BR>Half parched food (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूषः|अभ्यूष
अभ्युषः, अभ्यूषः, अभ्योषः [अभितः<BR>उऊ-ष्यते अग्निना दह्यते, उ-ऊ-ष् वाहु˚ क]<BR>1<BR>A sort of cake or bread (Mar. पोळी or<BR>रोटी) (अर्धस्विन्नयवादेर्घृतादिना भर्जितयवादेर्वा<BR>घृतपक्वान्नस्य पोळी इति ख्यातस्य नाम).<BR>--2<BR>Half parched food (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्योषः|अभ्योष
अभ्युषः, अभ्यूषः, अभ्योषः [अभितः<BR>उऊ-ष्यते अग्निना दह्यते, उ-ऊ-ष् वाहु˚ क]<BR>1<BR>A sort of cake or bread (Mar. पोळी or<BR>रोटी) (अर्धस्विन्नयवादेर्घृतादिना भर्जितयवादेर्वा<BR>घृतपक्वान्नस्य पोळी इति ख्यातस्य नाम).<BR>--2<BR>Half parched food (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युष्य
अभ्यु(भ्यू)ष्य-षीय, अभ्योष्य, अभ्योषीय<BR>a. Belonging to, consisting of, or<BR>fit for, the above cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युषीय
अभ्यु(भ्यू)ष्य-षीय, अभ्योष्य, अभ्योषीय<BR>a. Belonging to, consisting of, or<BR>fit for, the above cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूष्य
अभ्यु(भ्यू)ष्य-षीय, अभ्योष्य, अभ्योषीय<BR>a. Belonging to, consisting of, or<BR>fit for, the above cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूषीय
अभ्यु(भ्यू)ष्य-षीय, अभ्योष्य, अभ्योषीय<BR>a. Belonging to, consisting of, or<BR>fit for, the above cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्योष्य
अभ्यु(भ्यू)ष्य-षीय, अभ्योष्य, अभ्योषीय<BR>a. Belonging to, consisting of, or<BR>fit for, the above cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्योषीय
अभ्यु(भ्यू)ष्य-षीय, अभ्योष्य, अभ्योषीय<BR>a. Belonging to, consisting of, or<BR>fit for, the above cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्युषित|अभ्युषितः
अभ्युषित a. [वस्-क्त] Dwelling<BR>near or with.<BR>--तः A servant who<BR>is in attendance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूढ
अभ्यूढ a. [वह्-क्त] Brought near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूह्
अभ्यूह् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To cover over,<BR>clothe.<BR>--2 (A.) To watch for; form<BR>a plot against.<BR>--3 To infer, guess.<BR>--4<BR>To reason, argue, think over;<BR>Dk. 90.<BR>--5 To supply an ellipsis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्यूहः|अभ्यूह
अभ्यूहः [ऊह्-घञ्]<BR>1 Arguing,<BR>reasoning, discussion.<BR>--2 Deduction,<BR>inference, guess, conjecture;<BR>पराभ्यूहस्थानान्यपि तनुतराणि स्थगयति<BR>Māl. 1. 14.<BR>--3 Supplying an ellipsis<BR>--4<BR>Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्येषणं|अभ्येषण
अभ्येषणं [इष्-घञ्]<BR>1 Desiring,<BR>wishing.<BR>--2 Going towards, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्र्
अभ्र् {c1c} P. [अभ्रति, आनभ्र, अभ्रित] To<BR>go, wander about; वनेष्वानभ्र निर्भयः<BR>Bk. 4. 11; 14. 110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रं|अभ्र
अभ्रं [अभ्-अच्; but more correctly<BR>अप्-भृ; अपो बिभर्ति, भृ-क; अभ्रं अब्भरणात् Nir.<BR>being filled with water]<BR>1 A cloud;<BR>अग्निर्वै धूमो जायते धूमादभ्रमभ्राद् वृष्टिः Śat.<BR>Br.; अभ्रं वा अपां भस्म; धूमो भूत्वा अभ्रं<BR>भवति अभ्रं भूत्वा मेघो भवति मेघो भूत्वा<BR>प्रवर्षति Ch. Up. (these quotations<BR>show the conception of the ancient<BR>Ṛṣis about the formation of clouds).<BR>--2 Atmosphere, sky; परितो विपांडु<BR>दधदभ्रशिरः Śi. 9. 3, see अभ्रंलिह &c.<BR>--3<BR>Talc, mica.<BR>--4 Gold.<BR>--5 Camphor.<BR>--6<BR>A kind of reed; Calamus Rotang.<BR>--7 Cyperus Rotundus (मुस्ता).<BR>--8<BR>(In arith.) A zero or cypher. [cf. L.<BR>imber; Gr. ombros, appros; Zend<BR>awra, Pers. abr.]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवकाशः clouds as the only shelter; fall<BR>of rain.<BR>--अवकाशिक, --काशिन् a.<BR>exposed to the rain (and so<BR>practising penance), not seeking shelter<BR>from the rain; Ms. 6. 23.<BR>--उत्थः<BR>‘sky born’, the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>--कूटं a peak of a (mountain-like)<BR>cloud.<BR>--गंगा the heavenly river;<BR>K. 50.<BR>--घनः a mass of clouds; R. 13. 77.<BR>--जा a. Ved. born from clouds,<BR>caused by vapours.<BR>--नागः one of<BR>the elephants supporting the globe;<BR>N. of Airāvata.<BR>--पथः {1}<BR>atmosphere. {2} balloon.<BR>--पिशाचः, --चकः<BR>‘sky-demon’, epithet of Rāhu.<BR>--पुष्पः<BR>N. of a cane (Mar. वेत) Calamus<BR>Rotang.<BR>--(ष्पं) {1} water. {2} ‘a<BR>sky flower’, anything impossible,<BR>a castle in the air.<BR>--प्रुष् (ट्) f.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">Page0148-b+ 56</a>]<BR>sprinkling of clouds, rain.<BR>--मांसी N.<BR>of a plant (जटामांसी).<BR>--मातंगः Indra's<BR>elephant, Airāvata.<BR>--माला, --वृंदं<BR>a line, succession, or mass of<BR>clouds; R. 7. 69, 13. 76, 16. 25.<BR>--रोहं the lapis lazuli.<BR>--लिप्ती {1}<BR>sky covered with a few clouds.<BR>{2} a woman smeared with mustā<BR>grass.<BR>--वर्ष a. Ved. rained upon,<BR>sprinkled with water.<BR>--(र्षः)<BR>downpour of rain.<BR>--वाटिकः, --का N.<BR>of a tree (आम्रातक).<BR>--विलायं ind. just<BR>as clouds melt away; Ki. 11. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंलिह|अभ्रंलिहः
अभ्रंलिह a. [अभ्रं लेढि स्पृशति; खश्<BR>मुमागमश्च P. III. 2. 32]<BR>‘Cloudlicking’, touching or scraping the<BR>clouds (very high); अभ्रंलिहाग्राः<BR>प्रासादाः Me. 64; प्रासादमभ्रंलिहमारुरोह<BR>R. 14. 29.; K. 270; Śi. 5. 65.<BR>--हः Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रकं|अभ्रक
अभ्रकं [स्वार्थे कन्] Talc, mica;<BR>said to be produced from Pārvatī's<BR>menstrual discharge.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भस्मन् n. calx of talc.<BR>--सत्वं steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रंकष|अभ्रङ्कष|अभ्रंकषः|अभ्रङ्कषः
अभ्रंकष a. [अभ्रं कषति पीडयति<BR>तुंगत्वात्; खच् मुमागमश्च P. III. 2. 42]<BR>Touching or scraping the clouds,<BR>very high; आदायाभ्रंकषं प्रायान्मलयं<BR>फलशलिनं Bk.; K. 33; Dk. 110;<BR>Mv. 6. 7.<BR>--षः<BR>1 Wind, air; अभ्रंकषो<BR>वायुः Sk.<BR>--2 A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रायते
अभ्रायते Den. A. To create clouds,<BR>make cloudy; अभ्रं करोति अभ्रायते Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रित
अभ्रित a. [अभ्राणि अस्य संजातानि;<BR>अभ्रइतच् तारकादिगण] Overcast with clouds,<BR>clouded; R. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रिय|अभ्रियः
अभ्रिय a. [अभ्रे भवः घ;] Belonging<BR>to or produced from clouds, sky or<BR>mustaka.<BR>--यः Lightning.<BR>--यं A<BR>mass of thunder-clouds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रयः
अभ्रयः ‘One who is clothed only<BR>by the air’, an ascetic who is<BR>starknaked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रम|अभ्रमः
अभ्रम a. Not mistaking,<BR>steady, clear.<BR>--मः Composure, steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रमुः|अभ्रमु
अभ्रमुः f. The female elephant of<BR>the east, the mate of Airāvata,<BR>Indra's elephant; Śi. 1. 52.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रियः, --वल्लभः Airāvata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रातृव्य
अभ्रातृव्य a. Without a rival or<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रांत|अभ्रान्त|अभ्रान्तः
अभ्रांत a. Composed, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रांतिः|अभ्रान्ति|अभ्रान्तिः
अभ्रांतिः f. Composure, steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रिः|अभ्रि
अभ्रिः --भ्री f. [अभ्रति गच्छति मलं<BR>यस्मात् or येन; अभ्र्-इन्]<BR>1 A wooden scraper<BR>or sharp-pointed stick (for cleaning<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">Page0148-c+ 57</a>]<BR>a boat).<BR>--2 A spade, hoe in general;<BR>Ms. 11. 134.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खातं ‘dug up<BR>with a spade’, a ploughed field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्री
अभ्रिः --भ्री f. [अभ्रति गच्छति मलं<BR>यस्मात् or येन; अभ्र्-इन्]<BR>1 A wooden scraper<BR>or sharp-pointed stick (for cleaning<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">Page0148-c+ 57</a>]<BR>a boat).<BR>--2 A spade, hoe in general;<BR>Ms. 11. 134.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खातं ‘dug up<BR>with a spade’, a ploughed field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्रेषः|अभ्रेष
अभ्रेषः Non-deviation, fitness,<BR>propriety P. III. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अभ्व
अभ्व a.<BR>1 Huge, large(महत् Nir).<BR>--2 Mighty strong or powerful.<BR>--भ्वं<BR>1 Immense power, immensity.<BR>--2 Monstrosity, hugeness; (the great<BR>pervading principle of the universe;<BR>water; a cloud; embarrassed state,<BR>calamity; a monster; closeness;<BR>offspring, given by B. and R.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्
अम् ind.<BR>1 Quickly.<BR>--2 A little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्
अम् {c1c} P. [अमति अमितुं, अमित; Ved.<BR>pres. अमिति; अमीति]<BR>1 To go; to go to<BR>or towards.<BR>--2 To serve, honour.<BR>--3 To<BR>sound.<BR>--4 To eat. {c10c} P. or Caus. (<BR>आमयति)<BR>1 To come upon, attack, afflict<BR>with sickness or pain from disease.<BR>--2 To be ill or be afflicted or<BR>diseased. --With सं Ved. {c1c} A. {1} to<BR>convince oneself of, ascertain. {2}<BR>to ally or connect oneself with.<BR>--3 To fix or settle oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम|अमं|अमः
अम a. Unripe (as fruit).<BR>--मः<BR>1<BR>Going.<BR>--2 Pressure, weight; strength,<BR>power (बलं).<BR>--3 Fright, terror.<BR>--4<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>--5 A servant, follower,<BR>an attendant.<BR>--6 Vital air, life-wind<BR>(प्राण).<BR>--7 This, self.<BR>--8 Unmeasured<BR>state.<BR>--मा<BR>1 Soul.<BR>--2 Unmeasured<BR>state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमवत्|अमवन्त्
अमवत् a. Ved.<BR>1 Violent, strong,<BR>stormy (winds); powerful (sound<BR>also).<BR>--2 Persevering, constant.<BR>--3<BR>Capable, fit, proper.<BR>--4 Attended by<BR>ministers.<BR>--5 Attended by diseases.<BR>--6 Possessed of self. --ind. Violently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतः|अमत
अमतः [अम्-अतच् Uṇ. 3. 110]<BR>1<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>--2 Death.<BR>--3 Time.<BR>--4<BR>Dust, particle of dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमतिः|अमति
अमतिः [अम्-अति Uṇ. 4. 59]<BR>1<BR>Time.<BR>--2 The moon.<BR>--3 (Ved.)<BR>Form, shape (Nir).<BR>--4 Want, poverty.<BR>--a.,<BR>--अमतीवत् a. Ved.<BR>1 Evil-minded,<BR>wicked (दुष्ट, अप्रशस्तबुद्धिमत् Sāy.).<BR>--2<BR>Poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमंगल|अमङ्गल|अमङ्गलं|अमङ्गलः
अमंगल --ल्य a.<BR>1 Inauspicious,<BR>evil, ill; R. 12. 43; ˚अभ्यासरतिं<BR>Ku. 5. 65; अमंगल्यं शीलं तव भवतु<BR>नामैकमखिलं Puṣpadanta.<BR>--2 Unlucky,<BR>unfortunate.<BR>--लः The castor-oil tree<BR>(एरंड).<BR>--लं Inauspiciousness,<BR>illluck; evil; oft. used in dramatic<BR>literature; शांतं पापं प्रतिहतममंगलं; cf.<BR>God forbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमंगल्य|अमङ्गल्य|अमङ्गल्यः
अमंगल --ल्य a.<BR>1 Inauspicious,<BR>evil, ill; R. 12. 43; ˚अभ्यासरतिं<BR>Ku. 5. 65; अमंगल्यं शीलं तव भवतु<BR>नामैकमखिलं Puṣpadanta.<BR>--2 Unlucky,<BR>unfortunate.<BR>--लः The castor-oil tree<BR>(एरंड).<BR>--लं Inauspiciousness,<BR>illluck; evil; oft. used in dramatic<BR>literature; शांतं पापं प्रतिहतममंगलं; cf.<BR>God forbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमंड|अमण्ड|अमण्डः
अमंड a.<BR>1 Without decoration<BR>or ornaments.<BR>--2 Without froth or<BR>scum (as boiled rice).<BR>--डः The<BR>castor oil tree (एरंड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत|अमतः
अमत a.<BR>1 Not felt, not<BR>perceptible by the mind, unknown.<BR>--2<BR>Disliked, not agreed to, see under<BR>अम् also.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--परार्थता ‘an<BR>unaccepted second sense’, one of<BR>the faults of a word (शब्ददोष); अमतः<BR>प्रकृतविरुद्धः परार्थो यत्र; e. g. in<BR>राममन्मथशरेण ताडिता &c. (R. 11. 20) the<BR>second sense suggestive of शृंगाररस<BR>is opposed to the proper rasa of<BR>the passage which is either वीर or<BR>बीभत्स; K. P. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमति|अमतिः
अमति a. Evil-minded, wicked,<BR>depraved.<BR>--तिः A rogue, cheat.<BR>--तिः f. Ignorance,<BR>unconsciousness, absence of knowledge,<BR>intention, or fore-thought; अमत्यैतानि<BR>षड् जग्ध्वा Ms. 5. 20; 4. 222. For<BR>some of the other senses see under<BR>अम्.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पूर्व a. unconscious,<BR>unintentional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्र|अमत्रं
अमत्र a. Ved. [अम्-अत्रन्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 105] Overpowering (enemies),<BR>strong or disposed to march on (<BR>गमनशील) Rv. 1. 61. 9.<BR>--त्रं [अमति भुक्तें<BR>अन्नमत्र, आधारे अत्रन्]<BR>1 A pot, vessel,<BR>utensil.<BR>--2 Strength, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्रिन्
अमत्रिन् a. Ved.<BR>1 Strong,<BR>powerful.<BR>--2 Having a drinking vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमद
अमद a.<BR>1 Free from<BR>intoxication, grave, serious.<BR>--2 Sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्त
अमत्त a. Sober, sane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमत्सर|अमत्सरः
अमत्सर a. Not jealous or<BR>envious, charitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमधव्य
अमधव्य a. Not sweet, not worthy<BR>of the sweetness of Soma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनस्
अमनस्, --अमनस्क a.<BR>1 Without<BR>the organ of desire, thought &c.<BR>--2<BR>Devoid of intellect (as a child).<BR>--3 Inattentive, careless.<BR>--4 Having<BR>no control over the mind.<BR>--5 Devoid<BR>of affection. --n.<BR>--(नः)<BR>1 Not the<BR>organ of desire, non-perception.<BR>--2 Inattention. --m. The Supreme<BR>Being.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गत a. unknown,<BR>unthought of.<BR>--नीत --ज्ञ a. disapproved,<BR>condemned; reprobate.<BR>--योगः<BR>absence of concentration of mind,<BR>inattention.<BR>--हर a. displeasing,<BR>disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनस्क
अमनस्, --अमनस्क a.<BR>1 Without<BR>the organ of desire, thought &c.<BR>--2<BR>Devoid of intellect (as a child).<BR>--3 Inattentive, careless.<BR>--4 Having<BR>no control over the mind.<BR>--5 Devoid<BR>of affection. --n.<BR>--(नः)<BR>1 Not the<BR>organ of desire, non-perception.<BR>--2 Inattention. --m. The Supreme<BR>Being.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गत a. unknown,<BR>unthought of.<BR>--नीत --ज्ञ a. disapproved,<BR>condemned; reprobate.<BR>--योगः<BR>absence of concentration of mind,<BR>inattention.<BR>--हर a. displeasing,<BR>disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनस्विन्
अमनस्विन् a.<BR>1 Unintelligent.<BR>--2<BR>Inhuman (as a demon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनिः|अमनि
अमनिः [अम्-अनिः, अमति गच्छत्यत्र<BR>Uṇ. 2. 101] Motion (गतिः); way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनाक्
अमनाक् ind. Not a little,<BR>greatly, very much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमनुष्य|अमनुष्यः
अमनुष्य a.<BR>1 Not human, not<BR>manly.<BR>--2 Not frequented by man.<BR>--ष्यः<BR>1 Not a man.<BR>--2 A demon,<BR>fiend (= रक्षःपिशाचादि Sk. on P. II. 4. 23).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमंतु|अमन्तु
अमंतु a. Ved.<BR>1 Unwise, foolish.<BR>--2 Guiltless, innocent.<BR>--3 Despising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमंत्र|अमन्त्र
अमंत्र, --त्रक a.<BR>1 Not accompanied<BR>by Vedic verses, not requiring the<BR>repetition of Vedic texts, as a<BR>ceremony &c.; Ms. 3. 121, 2. 66.<BR>--2 Not<BR>entitled to Vedic verses, such as a<BR>Śūdra, a female &c.; Ms. 9. 18.<BR>--3<BR>Not knowing Vedic texts;<BR>अव्रतानाममंत्राणां 12. 114.<BR>--4 Not<BR>accompanied by the use of spells or<BR>incantations, as a cure &c.; अनया<BR>कथमन्यथावलीढा न हि जीवंति जना मनागमंत्राः<BR>Bv. 1. 111.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तंत्र a.<BR>without the use of spells or the<BR>magical feats attendant on them,<BR>without the use of magical arts; Pt. 1. 70.<BR>--विद् a. Not knowing Vedic hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमंत्रक|अमन्त्रक
अमंत्र, --त्रक a.<BR>1 Not accompanied<BR>by Vedic verses, not requiring the<BR>repetition of Vedic texts, as a<BR>ceremony &c.; Ms. 3. 121, 2. 66.<BR>--2 Not<BR>entitled to Vedic verses, such as a<BR>Śūdra, a female &c.; Ms. 9. 18.<BR>--3<BR>Not knowing Vedic texts;<BR>अव्रतानाममंत्राणां 12. 114.<BR>--4 Not<BR>accompanied by the use of spells or<BR>incantations, as a cure &c.; अनया<BR>कथमन्यथावलीढा न हि जीवंति जना मनागमंत्राः<BR>Bv. 1. 111.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तंत्र a.<BR>without the use of spells or the<BR>magical feats attendant on them,<BR>without the use of magical arts; Pt. 1. 70.<BR>--विद् a. Not knowing Vedic hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमंद|अमन्द|अमन्दः
अमंद a.<BR>1 Not slow or dull, active,<BR>intelligent; M. 2. 8.<BR>--2 Sharp,<BR>strong, violent (wind &c.).<BR>--3 Not<BR>little, much, excessive, great,<BR>violent; अमंदमददुर्दिन U. 5. 5;<BR>अमंदमिलदिंदिरे निखिलमाधुरीमंदिरे Bv. 4. 1;<BR>˚दष्टौष्ठकरावधूननं Ki. 8. 6 violently bit.<BR>--दः<BR>N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्यमान
अमन्यमान a. Ved.<BR>1 Not<BR>understanding; offering no homage.<BR>--2 Not<BR>being aware of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमन्युत
अमन्युत a. Ved. Not bearing<BR>illwill towards another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम|अममः
अमम a. Without egotism,<BR>without any selfish or worldly<BR>attachment, devoid of personal ties or de.<BR>sires; शरणेष्वममश्चैव वृक्षमूलनिकेतनः<BR>Ms. 6. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अममता
अममता, --त्वं Indifference,<BR>disinterestedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अममत्वं|अममत्व
अममता, --त्वं Indifference,<BR>disinterestedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमम्रि
अमम्रि a. Ved. Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर|अमरः
अमर a. [मृ-पचाद्यच् न. त.]<BR>Undying, immortal, imperishable;<BR>अजरामरवत् प्राज्ञो विद्यामर्थं च साधयेत् H. Pr. 3,<BR>Ms. 2. 148.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A god, deity.<BR>--2 N. of a Marut.<BR>--3 N. of a plant<BR>(स्नुहीवृक्ष).<BR>--4 Quicksilver.<BR>--5 Gold.<BR>--6 A species of pine.<BR>--7 The number<BR>33 (that being the number of Gods).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-c" target="_blank">Page0149-c+ 58</a>]<BR>--8 N. of Amarasiṃha, see below; of<BR>of a mountain.<BR>--9 Mystical<BR>signification of the syllable उ.<BR>--10 A heap<BR>of bones.<BR>--रा<BR>1 The residence of<BR>Indra (cf. अमरावती).<BR>--2 The naval<BR>string; umbilical cord.<BR>--3 The womb.<BR>--4 A house-post (स्थूणा).<BR>--5 N. of<BR>several plants; इंद्रवारुणी, वटी, महानीली,<BR>घृतकुमारी, स्नुही, गुडूची, दूर्वा.<BR>--री The<BR>same as अमरा.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगना, --स्त्री<BR>a celestial nymph, heavenly<BR>damsel; मुषाण रत्नानि हरामरांगनाः<BR>Śi. 1. 51.<BR>--अद्रिः ‘mountain of the gods’,<BR>N. of the mountain Sumeru.<BR>--अधिपः,<BR>--इंद्रः, ईशः, ईश्वरः, पतिः, भर्ता, राजः &c. ‘the<BR>lord of the gods’, epithets of Indra;<BR>sometimes of Śiva and Viṣṇu also.<BR>--आचार्यः, --गुरुः, --इज्यः ‘preceptor<BR>of the gods’, epithets of<BR>Bṛhaspati.<BR>--आपगा, --तटिनी, --सरित् f.<BR>the heavenly river, an epithet of<BR>the Ganges; ˚तटिनीरोधसि वसन्<BR>Bh. 3. 123.<BR>--आलयः the abode of the<BR>gods, heaven.<BR>--उत्तम a. the best<BR>of the gods.<BR>--उपम a. God-like.<BR>--कंटकं N. of that part of the Vindhya<BR>range which is near the source of<BR>the river Narmadā.<BR>--कोटः ‘the<BR>fortress of the immortals’, N. of the<BR>capital of a (modern) Rajaput state.<BR>--कोशः, --षः N. of the most popular<BR>Sanskrit lexicon called after the<BR>author अमरसिंह.<BR>--जः N. of a tree, a<BR>kind of खदिर.<BR>--तरुः, --दारुः {1} a celestial<BR>tree, a tree in the paradise of Indra;<BR>अमरुतरुकुसुमसौरभसेवनसंपूर्णसकलकामस्य Bv. 1. 28. {2} देवदारु. {3} the<BR>wishyielding tree.<BR>--द्विजः a Brāhmaṇa who<BR>lives by attending a temple or idol;<BR>or one who superintends a temple.<BR>--पुरं {1} the residence of the gods,<BR>celestial paradise. {2} N. of various<BR>other towns.<BR>--पुष्पः, --ष्पकः {1} N. of<BR>several plants (केतक, चूत). {2} N. of<BR>a kind of grass. {3} the<BR>wish-yielding tree (कल्पवृक्ष).<BR>--पुष्पिका N. of<BR>a plant (अधःपुष्पीवृक्ष); a kind of<BR>anise.<BR>--प्रख्य, --प्रभ a. like an immortal.<BR>--प्रभुः one of the 1000 names of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--माला N. of a lexicon.<BR>--रत्नं<BR>a crystal.<BR>--लोकः the world of the<BR>gods, heaven; ˚ता heavenly bliss;<BR>तेषु सम्यग्वर्तमानो गच्छत्यमरलोकतां<BR>Ms. 2. 5.<BR>--वल्लरी N. of a plant (<BR>आकाशवल्ली).<BR>--सिंहः N. of the author of<BR>Amarakoṣa; he was a Jaina and<BR>is said to have been one of the 9<BR>gems that adorned the court of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">Page0150-a+ 56</a>]<BR>king Vikramāditya. The dates of<BR>many of these ‘gems’ are still<BR>doubtful, but if he was really a<BR>contemporary of Kālidāsa, he could<BR>not have lived later than the 7th<BR>century which is usually assigned<BR>to Kālidāsa as the terminus ad quem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरणं|अमरण
अमरणं Not dying, immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरता
अमरता, --त्वं The state of the gods,<BR>immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरत्वं|अमरत्व
अमरता, --त्वं The state of the gods,<BR>immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरावती
अमरावती [अमर-वत्, र being changed<BR>to रा by P. VI. 3. 119]<BR>1 Abode of<BR>the gods, residence of Indra (said to<BR>be above Meru or the sun's orb; cf.<BR>Ki. 7. 2); ससंभ्रमेंद्रद्रुतपातितार्गला<BR>निमीलिताक्षीव भियाऽमरावती K. P. 1.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>modern town in Berar, Amraoti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरिष्णु
अमरिष्णु, अमर्त a. Ved. Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त|अमर्त्त
अमरिष्णु, अमर्त a. Ved. Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्त्य|अमर्त्यः
अमर्त्य a. Immortal, divine,<BR>imperishable; ˚भावेपि R. 7. 53; ˚भुवनं<BR>heaven; ˚ता immortality.<BR>--र्त्यः A<BR>god.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आपगा the celestial<BR>river, epithet of the Ganges;<BR>Vikr. 18. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमरुः|अमरु
अमरुः N. of a king and poet<BR>who composed 100 verses which are<BR>usually known by the name<BR>अमरुशतक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्मन्
अमर्मन् a. Ved. Not a vital<BR>organ or part of the body, having no<BR>joint or vital part.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जात<BR>a. not produced in a vital organ.<BR>--वेधिन् a. not injuring the vital<BR>parts; mild, soft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्याद|अमर्य्याद
अमर्याद a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Exceeding<BR>due limits or bounds, transgressing<BR>every bound, disrespectful,<BR>improper; मर्यादायाममर्यादाः स्त्रियस्तिष्ठंति<BR>सर्वदा Pt. 1. 142; तादृशं<BR>त्वममर्यादं कर्म कर्तुं चिकीर्षसि Rām.<BR>--2<BR>Boundless, infinite.<BR>--दा<BR>Transgression of due limits or bounds,<BR>impropriety of conduct, forwardness,<BR>disrespect, violation of due respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्ष|अमर्षः
अमर्ष a. Not enduring or bearing.<BR>--र्षः<BR>1 Non-endurance, tolerance,<BR>impatience; अमर्षशून्येन जनस्य जतुना<BR>न जातहार्देन न विद्विषादरः Ki. 1. 33;<BR>jealousy, jealous anger; किं नु<BR>भवतस्तातप्रतापोत्कर्षेप्यमर्षः U. 5. In Rhet.<BR>अमर्ष is one of the 33 minor<BR>feelings or व्यभिचारिभाव See S. D.; R. G.<BR>thus defines it: परकृतावज्ञादिनानापराधजन्यो<BR>मौनवाक्पारुष्यादिकारणभूतश्चित्तवृत्तिविशेषोऽ<BR>मर्षः.<BR>--2 Anger, passion, wrath;<BR>पुत्रवधामर्षोद्दीपितेन गांडीविना Ve. 2; सामर्ष<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">Page0150-b+ 56</a>]<BR>angry, indignant; सामर्षं angrily.<BR>--3 Impetuosity, violence.<BR>--4<BR>Determination of purpose.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a.<BR>arising from anger or impatience.<BR>--हासः an angry laugh, sarcastic<BR>sneer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षण|अमर्षणः
अमर्षण, --र्षित, --र्षिन्, --र्षवत् a.<BR>1<BR>Impatient, intolerant, unforgiving;<BR>विशेषात्परिपूर्णस्य याति शत्रोरमर्षणः आभिमुख्यं<BR>Pt. 1. 326.<BR>--2 Angry, indignant,<BR>passionate; हृदि क्षतो गोत्रभिदप्यमर्षणः<BR>R. 3. 53; अभिमन्युवधामर्षितैः पांडुपुत्रैः<BR>Ve. 4.<BR>--3 Impetuous, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षित
अमर्षण, --र्षित, --र्षिन्, --र्षवत् a.<BR>1<BR>Impatient, intolerant, unforgiving;<BR>विशेषात्परिपूर्णस्य याति शत्रोरमर्षणः आभिमुख्यं<BR>Pt. 1. 326.<BR>--2 Angry, indignant,<BR>passionate; हृदि क्षतो गोत्रभिदप्यमर्षणः<BR>R. 3. 53; अभिमन्युवधामर्षितैः पांडुपुत्रैः<BR>Ve. 4.<BR>--3 Impetuous, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षिन्
अमर्षण, --र्षित, --र्षिन्, --र्षवत् a.<BR>1<BR>Impatient, intolerant, unforgiving;<BR>विशेषात्परिपूर्णस्य याति शत्रोरमर्षणः आभिमुख्यं<BR>Pt. 1. 326.<BR>--2 Angry, indignant,<BR>passionate; हृदि क्षतो गोत्रभिदप्यमर्षणः<BR>R. 3. 53; अभिमन्युवधामर्षितैः पांडुपुत्रैः<BR>Ve. 4.<BR>--3 Impetuous, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमर्षवत्
अमर्षण, --र्षित, --र्षिन्, --र्षवत् a.<BR>1<BR>Impatient, intolerant, unforgiving;<BR>विशेषात्परिपूर्णस्य याति शत्रोरमर्षणः आभिमुख्यं<BR>Pt. 1. 326.<BR>--2 Angry, indignant,<BR>passionate; हृदि क्षतो गोत्रभिदप्यमर्षणः<BR>R. 3. 53; अभिमन्युवधामर्षितैः पांडुपुत्रैः<BR>Ve. 4.<BR>--3 Impetuous, determined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमल|अमलं
अमल a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Free from dirt<BR>or impurities, pure, undefiled,<BR>stainless, spotless; Ku. 7. 32, 33; अमलाः<BR>सुहृदः Pt. 2. 171 pure, sincere.<BR>--2<BR>White, bright, shining;<BR>कर्णावसक्तामलदंतपत्रं Ku. 7. 23; R. 6. 80.<BR>--ला<BR>1 N. of the goddess Lakṣmī.<BR>--2<BR>The navel cord.<BR>--3 N. of a tree<BR>(Mar. आंवळा) Emblica Officinalis<BR>Gærtn; also of a plant (सातलावृक्ष)<BR>also n. in this sense.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Purity.<BR>--2 Talc.<BR>--3 The Supreme Spirit.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a. of pure or<BR>undefiled mind.<BR>--पतत्रिन् m. (त्री) the<BR>wild goose.<BR>--रत्नं, --मणिः a crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलयति
अमलयति Den. P. To make pure<BR>or spotless, brighten; Ki. 5. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलिन
अमलिन a. Clean, spotless, pure<BR>(morally also); कुलममलिनं न<BR>त्वेवायं जनो न च जीवितं Māl. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमलानकं|अमलानक
अमलानकं Globe-amaranth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमवत्|अमवन्त्
अमवत् See under अम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमविष्णु
अमविष्णु a. Going in different<BR>directions, up and down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमसः|अमस
अमसः [अम्-असच्]<BR>1 Disease.<BR>--2 Stupidity.<BR>--3 A fool.<BR>--4 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमसृण
अमसृण a. Not soft or bland,<BR>harsh, violent, strong, intense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमस्तु
अमस्तु n. Curds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमा
अमा a. [न मा-का] Measureless.<BR>--ind. Ved.<BR>1 At home, in the house;<BR>कामश्चरताममाभूत् Rv. 2. 38. 6.<BR>--2 In<BR>this world, here below (इहलोके).<BR>--3<BR>With, near, close to; अमैवासां<BR>तद्भवति Śat. Br.<BR>--4 Together with, in<BR>conjunction or company with, as in<BR>अमात्य, अमावास्या q. v.; अमाकृ to draw near,<BR>have near oneself. --f.<BR>1 The day of<BR>the new moon, the day of the<BR>conjunction of the sun and moon;<BR>अमायां तु सदा सोम अषेधीः प्रतिपद्यते Vyāsa.<BR>--2 The sixteenth digit of the moon.<BR>--3 The fifteenth digit also. --m. The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">Page0150-c+ 56</a>]<BR>soul.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्त a. Ved. met,<BR>come together.<BR>--अंतः the end of the<BR>day of new moon.<BR>--जुर् f. living at<BR>home during life, growing old at<BR>home; Rv. 10. 39. 3; being<BR>without husband in the same dwelling<BR>with her parents, as a maiden (<BR>पितृषद्); Rv. 2. 17. 7.<BR>--पर्वन् n. the<BR>sacred time of अमा, day of new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमांस|अमांसः
अमांस a.<BR>1 Without flesh, not<BR>containing flesh.<BR>--2 Lean, thin, weak,<BR>enfeebled.<BR>--सं Not flesh, any thing<BR>but flesh.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ओदनिक a. (की<BR>f.) not relating to a preparation of<BR>rice with meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्
अमात् ind. Ved. From near,<BR>at hand. --a. Not measuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृ
अमातृ --तृक a. Motherless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृक
अमातृ --तृक a. Motherless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमातृभोगीण
अमातृभोगीण a. Not fit for the<BR>use of a mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्यः|अमात्य
अमात्यः (अमा सह वसति, अमा-त्यप्,<BR>P. IV. 2. 104 Vārt.)<BR>1 One living<BR>with or near another, an inmate<BR>of the same house or family (Ved.).<BR>--2 A companion or follower of<BR>a king, minister; अमात्यपुत्रैः<BR>सवयोभिरन्वितः R. 3. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्र|अमात्रः
अमात्र a. [नास्ति मात्रा इयत्ता यस्य]<BR>1 Boundless, immeasurable.<BR>--2 Not<BR>whole or entire.<BR>--3 Not elementary.<BR>--4 Having the measure or<BR>quantity of the letter अ.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1<BR>Non-measure.<BR>--2 Not a measure or quantity.<BR>--त्रः The Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमात्रवत्वं
अमात्रवत्वं<BR>1 Spirit, spiritual<BR>essence.<BR>--2 Defect, deficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाननं|अमानन
अमाननं, --ना Disrespect, insult;<BR>disobedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानना
अमाननं, --ना Disrespect, insult;<BR>disobedience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानव
अमानव a.<BR>1 Not human; animal.<BR>--2 Superhuman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानस्यं|अमानस्य
अमानस्यं Pain(मानसे साधु न भवति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिन्
अमानिन् a. Modest, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानिता
अमानिता, --त्वं Modesty, humility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानित्वं|अमानित्व
अमानिता, --त्वं Modesty, humility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष|अमानुषः
अमानुष a. (षी f.)<BR>1 Not human,<BR>not belonging to man, supernatural,<BR>unearthly, superhuman;<BR>आकृतिरेवानुमापयत्यमानुषतां K. 132; ˚आकृतिः<BR>K. 131, 132, 258; ˚शक्तित्वं 103;<BR>˚गीतध्वनिं 126 an unearthly<BR>melody.<BR>--2 Inhuman, monster-like;<BR>ill-disposed towards man.<BR>--3<BR>Tenantless, desolate; ˚षं वनं 135.<BR>--षः,<BR>--षी One not a man, an irrational<BR>animal; Ms. 9. 284, Ś. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमानुष्य
अमानुष्य a. Not human,<BR>superhuman &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमामसी
अमाम(मा)सी = अमावसी or<BR>अमावास्या q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमामासी
अमाम(मा)सी = अमावसी or<BR>अमावास्या q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमाय
अमाय a.<BR>1 Not cunning or<BR>sagacious, guileless, sincere, honest.<BR>--2<BR>Immeasurable.<BR>--या<BR>1 Absence of<BR>fraud or deceit, honesty, sincerity.<BR>--2 (In Vedānta phil.) Absence of<BR>delusion or error, knowledge of the<BR>supreme truth.<BR>--यं The Supreme<BR>Spirit (ब्रह्म).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिक|अमायिकः
अमायिक, --मायिन् a. Guileless,<BR>honest, sincere, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमायिन्
अमायिक, --मायिन् a. Guileless,<BR>honest, sincere, true.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमारः|अमार
अमारः Not dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमार्ग|अमार्गः
अमार्ग a. Pathless.<BR>--र्गः Not a<BR>road, absence of road; a bad road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावस्या
अमावस्या, --वास्या, --वसी, --वासी<BR>(also written अमा मसी-मासी) [<BR>अमावस् -ण्यत्, अमा सह वसतः चंद्रार्कौ अस्यां सा<BR>P. III. 1. 122 Sk.]<BR>1 The day of new<BR>moon, when the sun and moon dwell<BR>together or are in conjunction; the<BR>15th day of the dark half of every<BR>lunar month; सूर्याचंद्रमसोः यः परः<BR>सन्निकर्षः साऽमावास्या Gobhila.<BR>--2 A<BR>sacrifice offered at that time.<BR>--3 The<BR>sacrificial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्या
अमावस्या, --वास्या, --वसी, --वासी<BR>(also written अमा मसी-मासी) [<BR>अमावस् -ण्यत्, अमा सह वसतः चंद्रार्कौ अस्यां सा<BR>P. III. 1. 122 Sk.]<BR>1 The day of new<BR>moon, when the sun and moon dwell<BR>together or are in conjunction; the<BR>15th day of the dark half of every<BR>lunar month; सूर्याचंद्रमसोः यः परः<BR>सन्निकर्षः साऽमावास्या Gobhila.<BR>--2 A<BR>sacrifice offered at that time.<BR>--3 The<BR>sacrificial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावसी
अमावस्या, --वास्या, --वसी, --वासी<BR>(also written अमा मसी-मासी) [<BR>अमावस् -ण्यत्, अमा सह वसतः चंद्रार्कौ अस्यां सा<BR>P. III. 1. 122 Sk.]<BR>1 The day of new<BR>moon, when the sun and moon dwell<BR>together or are in conjunction; the<BR>15th day of the dark half of every<BR>lunar month; सूर्याचंद्रमसोः यः परः<BR>सन्निकर्षः साऽमावास्या Gobhila.<BR>--2 A<BR>sacrifice offered at that time.<BR>--3 The<BR>sacrificial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावासी
अमावस्या, --वास्या, --वसी, --वासी<BR>(also written अमा मसी-मासी) [<BR>अमावस् -ण्यत्, अमा सह वसतः चंद्रार्कौ अस्यां सा<BR>P. III. 1. 122 Sk.]<BR>1 The day of new<BR>moon, when the sun and moon dwell<BR>together or are in conjunction; the<BR>15th day of the dark half of every<BR>lunar month; सूर्याचंद्रमसोः यः परः<BR>सन्निकर्षः साऽमावास्या Gobhila.<BR>--2 A<BR>sacrifice offered at that time.<BR>--3 The<BR>sacrificial oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्य
अमावास्य, --स्यक a. [अमावास्या,<BR>वुन्-अष् P. IV. 3. 30-31; अमावास्यायां जातः]<BR>Born or produced on the night of<BR>new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमावास्यक
अमावास्य, --स्यक a. [अमावास्या,<BR>वुन्-अष् P. IV. 3. 30-31; अमावास्यायां जातः]<BR>Born or produced on the night of<BR>new moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित
अमित a.<BR>1 Unmeasured,<BR>boundless, unlimited, infinite, great,<BR>immense; मितं ददाति हि पिता मितं भ्राता<BR>मितं सुतः । अमितस्य हि दातारं भर्तारं का<BR>न पूजयेत् Rām.<BR>--2 Neglected,<BR>disregarded.<BR>--3 Unknown.<BR>--4<BR>Unpolished.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षर a. not having<BR>a fixed number of syllables; prosaic.<BR>--अशनः powerful devourer, epithet<BR>of परमेश्वर; of Viṣṇu.<BR>--आभ a. of<BR>great lustre, of unbounded splendour.<BR>--(भः) a class of divinities<BR>mentioned in V. P.<BR>--ओजस् a. of<BR>unbounded energy, all-powerful,<BR>Almighty; Ms. 1. 4.<BR>--क्रतु a. of<BR>unbounded wisdom or energy.<BR>--तेजस्,<BR>--द्युति a. of unbounded lustre or<BR>glory.<BR>--विक्रमः {1} of unbounded<BR>valour. {2} a name of Viṣṇu.<BR>--वीर्य<BR>a. of immense strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रः|अमित्र
अमित्रः [नमित्रं; by Uṇ. 4. 173 fr.<BR>अम् to go against; अमेद्विंषति चित्; अमित्रः<BR>शत्रुः] Not a friend, an enemy, adversary,<BR>a foe, rival, opponent; स्याताममित्रौ<BR>मित्रे च सहजप्राकृतावपि Śi. 2. 36; तस्य<BR>मित्राष्यमित्रास्ते 101; Dk. 109, 171;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">Page0151-b+ 55</a>]<BR>M. 1; प्रकृत्यमित्रा हि सतामसाधवः<BR>Ki. 14. 21; Ms. 7. 83; 12. 79; 2. 239.<BR>--त्रा An enemy; ˚युध् Ved.<BR>subduing one's enemies.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खाद्<BR>a. devouring one's enemies, epithet<BR>of Indra.<BR>--घात, --घातिन्, --घ्न, --हन्<BR>killing enemies.<BR>--जित् a. conquering<BR>one's enemies;<BR>अभित्रजिन्मित्रजिदोजसा यत् N. 1. 13; N. of a son of<BR>Suvarṇa.<BR>--दंभन a. Ved. hurting one's<BR>enemies.<BR>--स (सा) ह a. enduring<BR>or overpowering one's enemies,<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>--सेना a hostile<BR>army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रता
अमित्रता, --त्वं Enmity; Pt. 2. 98,<BR>Mk. 1. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रत्वं
अमित्रता, --त्वं Enmity; Pt. 2. 98,<BR>Mk. 1. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रयति
अमित्रयति Den. P., अमित्रायते Ā.<BR>To act like an enemy, act hostilely<BR>towards, hate; Bh. 3. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रिन्
अमित्रिन् a. Hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्रीय
अमित्रीय, --त्र्य a. Hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमित्र्य
अमित्रीय, --त्र्य a. Hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिथित
अमिथित a. Ved. Not reviled,<BR>not provoked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिथ्या
अमिथ्या adv. Not falsely, truly;<BR>तामूचतुस्ते प्रियमप्यमिथ्या R. 14. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिन्
अमिन् a. Sick, diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिन
अमिन a. Ved. Inviolable(<BR>अहिंस्य); immense (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिनत्|अमिनन्त्
अमिनत् a. Ved. Not hurting;<BR>unhurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिलातकं|अमिलातक
अमिलातकं Globe-amaranth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्र
अमिश्र, --श्रित a. Unmixed,<BR>unblended; not shared by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिश्रित
अमिश्र, --श्रित a. Unmixed,<BR>unblended; not shared by others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमिष|अमिषं
अमिष a. [न. ब.] Free from<BR>guile or deceit.<BR>--षं [अम् भोगे-कर्मणि<BR>इषन्]<BR>1 An object of worldly<BR>enjoyment, luxury.<BR>--2 Honesty,<BR>absence of fraud or deceit.<BR>--3 Flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीत
अमीत a. Unhurt; ˚वर्णाः of<BR>unhurt or unextinguishable colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमीवा
अमीवा [अम्-वन्-ईडागमः निपातः]<BR>1 Ved. Affliction, sickness, disease.<BR>--2<BR>Distress, terror.<BR>--3 A demon;<BR>tormenting spirit.<BR>--वः An enemy, one<BR>who afflicts or torments.<BR>--वं<BR>Affliction, distress, pain, injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक|अमुकं
अमुक pron. a. [अदस्-टेरकच्<BR>उत्वमत्त्वे Tv.] A certain person or thing,<BR>so and so (to be used when a<BR>person or thing is referred to<BR>without a name); मतं मेऽ<BR>मुकपुत्रस्य यदत्रोपरिलेखितम् Y. 2. 86-87;<BR>उभयाभ्यर्थितेनैतन्मया ह्यमुकसूनुना ।<BR>लिखितं ह्यमुकेनेति लेखकोंते ततो लिखेत् 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्त|अमुक्तं
अमुक्त a.<BR>1 Not loosened, not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">Page0151-c+ 56</a>]<BR>let go.<BR>--2 Not liberated from<BR>recurring birth and death, not having<BR>got final beatitude.<BR>--क्तं A weapon<BR>(a knife, sword &c.) that is always<BR>grasped and not thrown.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हस्त a. one whose hand is not<BR>open or free (to give), sparing,<BR>stingy (in a bad sense); frugal,<BR>economical, prudent (in a good sense);<BR>सदा प्रहृष्टया भाव्यं व्यये चामुक्तहस्तया<BR>Ms. 5. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुक्तिः|अमुक्ति
अमुक्तिः f.<BR>1 Non-liberation.<BR>--2<BR>Want of freedom or liberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुच्
अमुच् f. Ved. Non-liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुची
अमुची f. Ved. Not unbinding, not<BR>setting at liberty (said of an evil<BR>spirit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुतः
अमुतः ind.<BR>1 From there, there.<BR>--2 From that place, from above,<BR>i. e. from the other world or<BR>heaven.<BR>--3 Upon this, thereupon;<BR>henceforth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्र
अमुत्र ind. (opp. इह) [अदस्-त्रल्]<BR>1 There, in that place, therein;<BR>अमुत्रासन् यवनाः Dk. 127.<BR>--2 There<BR>(in what precedes or has been<BR>said), in that case.<BR>--3 There<BR>above, in the next world,<BR>in the life to come; यावज्जीवं च<BR>तत्कुर्याद्येनामुत्र सुखं वसेत्; यत्तु वाणिजके<BR>दत्तं नेह नामुत्र तद्भवेत् Ms. 3. 181;<BR>Bg. 6. 40.<BR>--4 There; अनेनैवार्भकाः सर्वे<BR>नगरेऽमुत्र भक्षिताः Ks.<BR>--5 Thither, that<BR>way.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भूयं Ved. being<BR>in the other world; dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुत्रत्य
अमुत्रत्य a. Belonging to a future<BR>life, being of the next world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुथा
अमुथा ind. Thus, in that<BR>manner, like that; ˚अस् to be thus,<BR>euphemistically for ‘to fare very ill’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुया
अमुया ind. Ved. In that<BR>manner, thus and thus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुर्हि
अमुर्हि ind. Then, at that time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुवत्
अमुवत् ind. Like a person or<BR>thing referred to without name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमुष्य
अमुष्य (gen. of अदस्) Of such<BR>a one (in comp. only).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कुल<BR>a. [अलुक् स.] belonging to the<BR>family of such a one.<BR>--(लं) a<BR>wellknown family.<BR>--पुत्रः, --त्री the son or<BR>daughter of such a one or of a good<BR>or well-known family or origin; see<BR>आमुष्यायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृश्
अमूदृश्, -श, -क्ष, a. (--शी, --क्षी f.<BR>cf. अन्यादृश) Such-like, such a one, of<BR>such a form or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृश|अमूदृशः
अमूदृश्, -श, -क्ष, a. (--शी, --क्षी f.<BR>cf. अन्यादृश) Such-like, such a one, of<BR>such a form or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृक्ष
अमूदृश्, -श, -क्ष, a. (--शी, --क्षी f.<BR>cf. अन्यादृश) Such-like, such a one, of<BR>such a form or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृशी
अमूदृश्, -श, -क्ष, a. (--शी, --क्षी f.<BR>cf. अन्यादृश) Such-like, such a one, of<BR>such a form or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूदृक्षी
अमूदृश्, -श, -क्ष, a. (--शी, --क्षी f.<BR>cf. अन्यादृश) Such-like, such a one, of<BR>such a form or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर
अमूर a. Ved. Not perplexed or<BR>bewildered, not ignorant, infallible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्त|अमूर्तः|अमूर्त्त|अमूर्त्तः
अमूर्त a. Formless, shapeless,<BR>incorporeal, unembodied (opp. मूर्त<BR>where Muktā. says मूर्तत्वं =<BR>अवच्छिन्नपरिमाणवत्त्वं).<BR>--र्तः N. of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गुणः (In Vaiś. phil.) a quality<BR>considered to be अमूर्त or incorporeal<BR>such as धर्म, अधर्म &c.; धर्माधर्मौ भावना<BR>च शब्दो बुद्ध्यादयोपि च । एतेऽमूर्तगुणाः सर्वे<BR>Bhāṣa<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्ति|अमूर्तिः|अमूर्त्ति
अमूर्ति a. Formless, shapeless.<BR>--र्तिः<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--र्तिः f.<BR>Shapelessness; (m. pl.) A class of Manes<BR>who have no definite form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूर्तिमत्|अमूर्तिमन्त्|अमूर्त्तिमत्
अमूर्तिमत् a. Formless &c. --m.<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल
अमूल, --लक a.<BR>1 Rootless(lit.);<BR>पशवोऽमूला ओषधयो मूलिन्यः Śat. Br.;<BR>(fig.) without basis or support,<BR>baseless, groundless.<BR>--2 Without<BR>authority; not being in the original;<BR>नामूलं लिख्यते किंचित् Malli.<BR>--3<BR>Without material cause, as the Pradhāna<BR>of the Sāṃkhyas; मूलं मूलाभावादमूलं.<BR>--4 Not fixed in the earth, moving.<BR>--ला N. of a plant (अग्निशिखा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूलक|अमूलकं
अमूल, --लक a.<BR>1 Rootless(lit.);<BR>पशवोऽमूला ओषधयो मूलिन्यः Śat. Br.;<BR>(fig.) without basis or support,<BR>baseless, groundless.<BR>--2 Without<BR>authority; not being in the original;<BR>नामूलं लिख्यते किंचित् Malli.<BR>--3<BR>Without material cause, as the Pradhāna<BR>of the Sāṃkhyas; मूलं मूलाभावादमूलं.<BR>--4 Not fixed in the earth, moving.<BR>--ला N. of a plant (अग्निशिखा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमूल्य
अमूल्य a. Priceless, invaluable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृक्त
अमृक्त a. Ved.<BR>1 Unhurt,<BR>unharmed, safe.<BR>--2 Unwashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृणालं|अमृणाल
अमृणालं [सादृश्ये नञ्] The root<BR>of a fragrant grass (वीरण, Mar. काळा<BR>वाळा) used for screens &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत|अमृतं|अमृतः
अमृत a.<BR>1 Not dead; अमृते<BR>जारजः कुंडः Ak.<BR>--2 Immortal; अपाम<BR>सोमममृता अभूम Rv. 8. 48. 3; U. 1. 1;<BR>Bg. 14. 27.<BR>--3 Imperishable, indestructible,<BR>eternal.<BR>--4 Causing immortality.<BR>--5 Beautiful, agreeable, desired.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A god, an immortal, deity.<BR>--2 N. of Dhanvantari, physician<BR>of the gods; also N. of Indra, of<BR>the sun, of Prajāpati, of the soul,<BR>Viṣṇu and Śiva.<BR>--3 N. of a plant<BR>(वनमुद्ग).<BR>--4 N. of the root of a<BR>plant (वाराहीकंद).<BR>--ता<BR>1 Spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>--2 N. of various plants; e. g.<BR>आमलकी, हरीतकी, गुडूची; मागधी; तुलसी,<BR>इंद्रवारुणी, ज्योतिष्मती, गोरक्षदुग्धा; अतिविषा;<BR>रक्तत्रिवृत्; दूर्वा, स्थूलमांसहरीतकी.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of one of the Nāḍīs in the<BR>body; Māl. 5. 2.<BR>--4 One of the<BR>rays of the sun; R. 10. 58.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>(a) Immortality, imperishable state;<BR>न मृत्युरासीदमृतं न तर्हि Rv. 10. 129. 2;<BR>Ms. 12. 85. (b) Final beatitude,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-b" target="_blank">Page0152-b+ 58</a>]<BR>absolution; तपसा किल्बिषं हंति<BR>विद्ययामृतमश्नुते Ms. 12. 104; स श्रिये<BR>चामृताय च Ak.<BR>--2 The collective body of<BR>immortals.<BR>--3 (a) The world of<BR>immortality, Paradise, Heaven; the<BR>power of eternity, immortal light,<BR>eternity.<BR>--4 Nectar of immortality,<BR>ambrosia, beverage of the gods (opp.<BR>विष) supposed to be churned out of<BR>the ocean; देवासुरैरमृतमंबुनिधिर्ममंथे<BR>Ki. 5. 30; विषादष्यमृतं ग्राह्यं Ms. 2. 239;<BR>विषमप्यमृतं क्वचिद्भवेदमृतं वा<BR>विषमीश्वरेच्छया R. 8. 46; oft. used in<BR>combination with words like वाच्, वचनं,<BR>वाणी &c; कुमारजन्मामृतसंमिताक्षरं<BR>R. 3. 16; आप्यायितोसौ वचनामृतेन Mb.;<BR>अमृतं शिशिरे वह्निरमृतं क्षीरभोजनं<BR>Pt. 1. 128 the height of pleasure or<BR>gratification.<BR>--5 The Soma juice.<BR>--6<BR>Antidote against poison.<BR>--7 The<BR>residue or leavings of a sacrifice;<BR>(यज्ञशेष) Ms. 3. 285.<BR>--8<BR>Unsolicited alms, alms got without<BR>solicitation; मृतं स्याद्याचितं भैक्ष्यममृतं<BR>स्यादयाचितं Ms. 4. 4-5.<BR>--9 Water;<BR>अमृताध्मातजीमूत U. 6. 21;<BR>अमृतादुन्मथ्यमानात् K. 136; cf. also the<BR>formulas अमृतोपस्तरणमसि स्वाहा and<BR>अमृतापिधानमसि स्वाहा repeated by Brāhmaṇas<BR>at the time of sipping water<BR>before the commencement and at the<BR>end of meals.<BR>--10 A drug.<BR>--11 Clari<BR>fied butter; अमृतं नाम यत् संतो<BR>मंत्रजिह्वेषु जुह्वति Śi. 2. 107.<BR>--12 Milk.<BR>--13<BR>Food in general.<BR>--14 Boiled rice.<BR>--15<BR>Any thing sweet, any thing lovely<BR>or charming; a sweetmeat.<BR>--16<BR>Property.<BR>--17 Gold.<BR>--18 Quicksilver.<BR>--19 Poison.<BR>--20 The poison called<BR>वत्सनाभ.<BR>--21 The Supreme Spirit<BR>(ब्रह्म).<BR>--22 N. of a sacred place.<BR>--23<BR>N. of particular conjunctions of<BR>Nakṣatras (lunar asterisms) with<BR>week days (वारनक्षत्रयोग) or of<BR>lunar days with week days (तिथिवारयोग).<BR>--24 The number four.<BR>--25<BR>Splendour, light. [cf. Gr.<BR>ambrotos, ambrosia; L. immortalis].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुः, --करः, --दीधितिः, --द्युतिः, --रश्मिः &c.<BR>epithets of the moon;<BR>अमृतदीधितिरेष विदर्भजे N. 4. 104; अमृतांशूद्भव<BR>born from the moon; from whom<BR>was born the moon, N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--अक्षर a. immortal and<BR>imperishable; क्षरं प्रधानममृताक्षरं हरः Śvet. Up.<BR>--अंधस्, --अशनः, --आशिन् m. ‘one<BR>whose food is nectar’; a god, an<BR>immortal.<BR>--असु a. whose soul is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-c" target="_blank">Page0152-c+ 58</a>]<BR>immortal.<BR>--आशः {1} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>{2} a god.<BR>--आसंगः a sort of<BR>collyrium.<BR>--आहरणः N. of Garuḍa who once<BR>stole Amṛta.<BR>--इष्टका a kind of<BR>sacrificial brick shaped like the golden<BR>head of men, beasts &c. (पशुशीर्षाणि).<BR>--ईशः, --ईश्वरः N. of Śiva.<BR>--उत्पन्ना a fly.<BR>(--न्नं), --उद्भवं a kind of collyrium<BR>(खर्परीतुत्थं).<BR>--(वः) N. of the Bilva tree.<BR>--कुंडं a vessel containing nectar.<BR>--क्षारं sal ammoniac.<BR>--गतिः N. of a<BR>metre consisting of 40 syllables.<BR>--गर्भ a. filled with water or nectar;<BR>ambrosial.<BR>--(र्भः) {1} the individual<BR>soul {2} the supreme soul.<BR>--चितिः<BR>f. an arrangement or accumulation<BR>of sacrificial bricks conferring<BR>immortality.<BR>--ज a. produced by or<BR>from nectar.<BR>--(जः) a sort of plant,<BR>Yellow Myrobalan.<BR>--जटा N. of a<BR>plant (जटामांसी).<BR>--तरंगिणी<BR>moonlight.<BR>--तिलका N. of a metre of 4<BR>lines, also called त्वरितगति.<BR>--द्रव a.<BR>shedding nectar.<BR>--(वः) flow of<BR>nectar.<BR>--धार a. shedding nectar.<BR>--(रा) {1}<BR>N. of a metre. {2} flow of nectar.<BR>--पः {1} a drinker of nectar, a god or<BR>deity. {2} N. of Viṣṇu. {3} one<BR>who drinks wine;<BR>भ्रुवममृतपनामवाछंयासावधरममुं मधुपस्तवाजिहीते Śi. 7. 42<BR>(where अ˚ has sense 1. also).<BR>--पक्षः<BR>{1} having golden or immortal wings,<BR>a sort of hawk. {2} the immortal or<BR>golden wings of sacrificial fire. {3}<BR>fire itself.<BR>--फलः N. of two trees<BR>पटोल and पारावत.<BR>--(ला) {1} a bunch of<BR>grapes, vine plant, a grape (द्राक्षा).<BR>{2} = आमलकी.<BR>--(लं) a sort of fruit<BR>(रुचिफल) found in the country of<BR>the Mudgalas according to Bhāva<BR>P.<BR>--बंधुः Ved. {1} a god or deity in<BR>general. {2} a horse or the moon.<BR>--भल्लातकी a sort of medicinal<BR>preparation of ghee mentioned by<BR>Cakradatta.<BR>--भुज् m. an immortal,<BR>a god, deity; one who tastes the<BR>sacrificial residues.<BR>--भू a. free from<BR>birth and death.<BR>--मति = ˚गति q. v.<BR>--मंथनं churning (of the ocean)<BR>for nectar.<BR>--मालिनी N. of Durgā.<BR>--योगः see under अमृत.<BR>--रसः {1}<BR>nectar, ambrosia; काव्यामृतरसास्वादः<BR>H. 1; विविधकाव्यामृतरसान् पिबामः<BR>Bh. 3. 40. {2} the Supreme spirit.<BR>--(सा)<BR>{1} dark-coloured grapes. {2} a sort of<BR>cake (Mar. अनर्सा).<BR>--लता, --लतिका<BR>a nectar-giving creeping plant<BR>(गुडूची).<BR>--वाक a. producing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">Page0153-a+ 55</a>]<BR>nectar-like sweet words.<BR>--संयावं a sort<BR>of dish mentioned in Bhāva P.<BR>--सार a. ambrosial; ˚राणि प्रज्ञानानि<BR>U. 7.<BR>--(रः) {1} clarified butter. {2}<BR>a sort of अयः पाक. ˚जः raw sugar,<BR>molasses (गुड).<BR>--सूः, --सूतिः {1} the moon<BR>(distilling nectar). {2} mother of<BR>the gods.<BR>--सोदरः {1} ‘brother of<BR>nectar,’ the horse called उच्चैःश्रवस्.<BR>{2} a horse in general.<BR>--स्रवः flow<BR>of nectar.<BR>--(वा) N. of a plant and<BR>tree (रुदंती).<BR>--स्रुत् a. shedding or<BR>distilling nectar; Ku. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतता
अमृतता, --त्वं Immortality;<BR>Rv. 10. 90. 2; Ms. 6. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतत्वं|अमृतत्व
अमृतता, --त्वं Immortality;<BR>Rv. 10. 90. 2; Ms. 6. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतमय
अमृतमय a. (यी f.)<BR>1 Consisting<BR>of nectar, ambrosial, full of nectar.<BR>--2 Immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतकं|अमृतक
अमृतकं The nectar of immortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृताफलं|अमृताफल|अमृताफलः
अमृताफलं The fruit of the<BR>Trichosanthes (पटोलफल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतायते
अमृतायते Den. A. To be like<BR>nectar; R. 2. 61; Ki. 12. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृतेशयः|अमृतेशय
अमृतेशयः N. of Viṣṇu(sleeping<BR>in waters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृत्यु|अमृत्युः
अमृत्यु a.<BR>1 Immortal; causing<BR>immortality.<BR>--त्युः Not death,<BR>immortality.<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृध्र
अमृध्र a. Ved.<BR>1 Unassailable,<BR>invulnerable.<BR>--2 Unremitting,<BR>unceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृषा
अमृषा ind. Not falsely, truly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमृष्ट
अमृष्ट a. Unrubbed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मृज a. of unimpaired purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेदस्क
अमेदस्क a. Fatless, lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेधस्
अमेधस् a. [अ-मेधा; नित्यमसिच्<BR>P. V. 4. 122] Foolish, stupid, an idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेध्य|अमेध्यं
अमेध्य a.<BR>1 Not able or allowed<BR>to sacrifice.<BR>--2 Unfit for a sacrifice;<BR>नामेध्यं प्रक्षिपेदग्नौ Ms. 4. 53, 56;<BR>5. 5, 132.<BR>--3 Unholy, filthy, foul,<BR>dirty, impure; Bg. 17. 10;<BR>Bh. 3. 106.<BR>--ध्यं<BR>1 Excrement, ordure;<BR>समुत्सृजेद्राजमार्गे यस्त्वमेध्यमनापदि<BR>Ms. 9. 282; 5. 126, 128; 12. 71.<BR>--2 An<BR>unlucky or inauspicious omen;<BR>अमेध्यं दृष्ट्वा सूर्यमुपतिष्ठेत Kāty.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कुणपाशिन् a. feeding on carrion.<BR>--युक्त, --लिप्त a. smeared with ordure,<BR>foul, defiled, dirty.<BR>--लेपः smearing<BR>with ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेन
अमेन Ved.<BR>1 Having no wife, a<BR>widower.<BR>--2 Not injuring or hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेय
अमेय a.<BR>1 Immeasurable,<BR>boundless; अमेयो मितलोकस्त्वं R. 10. 18.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">Page0153-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 Unknowable.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन्<BR>a. possessing an immeasurable soul,<BR>magnanimous, large-minded. (--m.)<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमेष्ट
अमेष्ट a. [अम-इष्ट] Ved.<BR>Sacrificed at home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्य
अमोक्य a. Ved. Not to be<BR>unloosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोचनं|अमोचन
अमोचनं Not loosening or letting<BR>go, non-liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोक्ष|अमोक्षः
अमोक्ष a. Not liberated, unloosed.<BR>--क्षः<BR>1 Bondage, confinement.<BR>--2<BR>Non-liberation from worldly<BR>existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोघ|अमोघः
अमोघ a.<BR>1 Unfailing, reaching<BR>the mark; धनुष्यमोघं समधत्त बाणं<BR>Ku. 3. 66; R. 3. 53; 12. 97;<BR>कामिलक्ष्येष्वमोधैः Me. 73.<BR>--2 Unerring,<BR>infallible (words, boon &c.); अमोधाः<BR>प्रतिगृह्णंतावर्घ्यानुपदमाशिषः R. 1. 44;<BR>युतममोघतया Ki. 6. 40.<BR>--3 Not vain<BR>or useless, efficacious, fruitful,<BR>productive; यदमोघमपामंतरुप्तं बीजमज त्वया<BR>Ku. 2. 5; so ˚बलं, ˚शक्ति, ˚वीर्य,<BR>˚क्रोध &c.<BR>--घः<BR>1 Not failing or<BR>erring, unerringness.<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu<BR>(or of Śiva according to some).<BR>--3 N. of a river.<BR>--घा<BR>1 N.<BR>of the plant पाटलां (Mar. पाडळी)<BR>(the trumpet flower).<BR>--2 N. of<BR>another plant विडंग (Mar.<BR>वावडिंग) the seed of which is used as a<BR>vermifuge, and hence also called<BR>कृमिघ्न.<BR>--3 = पथ्या.<BR>--4 N. of a spear or<BR>शक्ति.<BR>--5 N. of Śiva's wife.<BR>--6<BR>Mystical name of the conjunct consonant<BR>क्ष.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंडः unerring in<BR>punishment, N. of Śiva.<BR>--दर्शिन्, --दृष्टि a. of<BR>unerring mind or view.<BR>--बल a. of<BR>never-failing strength or vigour.<BR>--वाच् f. words not vain or idle, that<BR>are sure to be fulfilled or realized. (a.)<BR>one whose words are not vain.<BR>--वांछित a. never disappointed.<BR>--विक्रमः<BR>of never-failing valour, N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोत
अमोत a. [अमा-उत] Ved. The hems<BR>or skirts of which are not cut;<BR>woven at home, taken care of or<BR>protected at home; ˚पुत्रका a maiden<BR>protected at home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमोतकः|अमोतक
अमोतकः<BR>1 One protected at home<BR>(as a child).<BR>--2 A weaver (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अमौनं|अमौन
अमौनं<BR>1 Non-silence.<BR>--2<BR>Knowledge of the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्नस्
अम्नस् ind. Ved. (स् being<BR>changed to र् by P. VIII. 2. 70)<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-c" target="_blank">Page0153-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Unawares, quickly.<BR>--2 At present.<BR>--3 A little.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंब्|अम्ब्
अंब् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 (A.) To<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबः|अम्ब|अंब|अम्बः
अंबः<BR>1 A father.<BR>--2 Sound; the<BR>Veda.<BR>--3 One who sounds.<BR>--बा see<BR>below.<BR>--बं<BR>1 The eye.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--ब ind. A particle of affirmation;<BR>‘well,’ ‘well now.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबकं|अम्बक|अंबक|अम्बकं
अंबकं<BR>1 An eye (in त्र्यंबक).<BR>--2<BR>A father.<BR>--3 Copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबया|अम्बया
अंबया Ved. A mother; good<BR>woman (as a courteous mode of<BR>address); or, conveying water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबरं|अम्बर|अंबर|अम्बरं|अम्बरः
अंबरं [अंबः शब्दः तं राति धत्ते, रा-क]<BR>1 Sky, atmosphere, ether;<BR>तावतर्जयदंबरे R. 12. 41.<BR>--2 Cloth, garment,<BR>clothing, apparel, dress;<BR>दिव्यमाल्यांबरधरं Bg. 11. 11; R. 3. 9; दिगंबर;<BR>सागरांबरा मही the sea-girt earth.<BR>--3<BR>Saffron.<BR>--4 Talc.<BR>--5 A kind of perfume<BR>(Ambergris).<BR>--6 Cotton.<BR>--7<BR>N. of a people.<BR>--8 Circumference,<BR>compass.<BR>--9 Neighbourhood,<BR>surrounding country (Nir.).<BR>--10 Lip.<BR>--11 Evil, sin.<BR>--12 Destroyer of<BR>elephants (नागभिद् Trik.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः {1} the end of a garment. {2}<BR>the horizon.<BR>--ओकस् m. dwelling<BR>in heaven, a god; (भस्मरजः)<BR>विलिप्यते मौलिभिरंबरौकसां Ku. 5. 79.<BR>--ग<BR>a. sky-going.<BR>--दं cotton.<BR>--मणिः<BR>the sun.<BR>--युगं two principal<BR>garments used by men; upper and<BR>lower.<BR>--लेखिन् a. sky-touching;<BR>R. 13. 26.<BR>--शैलः a high mountain<BR>touching the sky.<BR>--स्थली the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबर्यति
अंबर्यति Den. P. To bring together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबरीषं|अम्बरीष|अंबरीष|अम्बरीषं|अम्बरीषः
अंबरीषं [In some senses अंबरीषः<BR>also; ˚षः only by Uṇ. 4. 29; क्लीबेंऽ<BR>बरीषं भ्राष्ट्रो^1 ना Ak.]<BR>1 A frying-pan.<BR>--2<BR>Regret, remorse.<BR>--3 War, battle.<BR>--4 One of the hells.<BR>--5 A young<BR>animal, colt.<BR>--6 The sun.<BR>--7 The<BR>hog-plum plant (आम्रातक).<BR>--8 N.<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--9 N. of Śiva.<BR>--10 N.<BR>of a king of the solar race who<BR>was celebrated as a worshipper of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dhaval Patel on 20161231. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/329.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबष्ठः|अम्बष्ठ|अंबष्ठ|अम्बष्ठः
अंबष्ठः<BR>1 The offspring of a man<BR>of the Brāhmaṇa and a woman of<BR>the Vaiśya tribe;<BR>ब्राह्मणाद्वैश्यकन्यायामंबष्ठो नाम जायते Ms. 10. 8, 13, 15;<BR>Y. 1. 91. (According to<BR>Ms. 10. 47 the duty of an अंबष्ठ is the<BR>curing of diseases; अंबष्ठानां चिकित्सितं).<BR>--2 An elephant-driver.<BR>--3 (pl.) N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-a" target="_blank">Page0154-a+ 60</a>]<BR>of a country and its inhabitants<BR>(they seem to have occupied the<BR>country to the east of Tāk,<BR>comprising the modern district of<BR>Lahore).<BR>--ष्ठा N. of several plants:<BR>(a) गणिका, यूथिका (Mar. जुई); (b)<BR>पाठा (Mar. पाहाडमूळ). (c) चुक्रिका (Mar.<BR>चुका); (d) another plant (Mar.<BR>अंबाडा).<BR>--ष्ठा, --ष्ठी An Ambaṣṭha<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबष्ठकी|अम्बष्ठकी
अंबष्ठकी = अंबष्ठा (पाठा) see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबष्ठिका|अम्बष्ठिका
अंबष्ठिका N. of a plant (ब्राह्मी.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबा|अम्बा
अंबा [अंब्-घञ्] (Voc. अंबे Ved.;<BR>अंब in later Sanskrit)<BR>1 A mother;<BR>also used as an affectionate or<BR>respectful mode of address; ‘good<BR>woman’, ‘good mother’; किमंबाभिः<BR>प्रेषितः; अंबानां कार्यं निर्वर्तय Ś. 2;<BR>कृतांजलिस्तत्र यदंब सत्यात् R. 14. 16.<BR>--2 N. of a plant (अंबष्ठा d.).<BR>--3 N.<BR>of Durgā, wife of Śiva.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>an Apsaras; of a sister of Pāṇḍu's<BR>mother, a daughter of Kāśīrāja.<BR>[She and her two sisters were carried off<BR>by Bhīṣma to be the wives of<BR>VichitraVīrya who had no issue. Ambā, however,<BR>had been previously betrothed to a<BR>king of Śāla and Bhīṣma sent her to<BR>him; but the latter rejected her because<BR>she had been in another man's house.<BR>So she came back to Bhīṣma and prayed<BR>him to accept her; but he could<BR>not break his vow of life-long<BR>celibacy, and being enraged she returned<BR>to the forest and practised austere<BR>penance to revenge herself on Bhīṣma.<BR>Śiva favoured her and promised her<BR>the desired vengeance in another birth.<BR>Afterwards she was born as<BR>Śikhaṇḍinī, daughter of Drupada, who came<BR>to be called Śikhaṇḍin and<BR>became the cause of Bhīṣma's death.]<BR>--5 A term in astrology to denote the<BR>fourth condition. [cf. Dravid<BR>Amma; Germ. amme; old Germ. Amma].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबाडा|अम्बाडा
अंबाडा (Ved.<BR>--ला) A mother;<BR>P. VI. 1. 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबायुः|अम्बायु|अम्बायुः
अंबायुः f. A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबालिका|अम्बालिका
अंबालिका<BR>1 A mother; good<BR>woman (as a term of respect or<BR>endearment.)<BR>--2 N. of a plant (Mar.<BR>अंबाडा).<BR>--3 N. of the youngest<BR>daughter of Kāśīrāja, wife of<BR>Vichitra-Vīrya. She became the mother<BR>of Pāṇḍu by Vyāsa who was<BR>invoked by Satyavatī to beget a son to<BR>Vicitra-Vīrya who had died<BR>without issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबिः|अम्बि|अम्बिः
अंबिः f. Ved. Water; woman;<BR>mother; nurse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबिका|अम्बिका
अंबिका<BR>1 A mother, good<BR>woman, also used like अंबा as a term of<BR>respect or endearment; अत्तिके<BR>अंबिके शृणु मम विज्ञप्तिं Mk. 1.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>plant (अंबा 2); of another plant<BR>कटुकी.<BR>--3 N. of Pārvatī, wife of<BR>Śiva; आशीर्भिरेधयामासुः पुरः<BR>पाकाभिरंबिकां Ku. 6. 90.<BR>--4 N. of the<BR>middle daughter of Kāśīrāja and the<BR>eldest wife of Vicitra-Vīrya. Like<BR>her youngest sister she had no<BR>progeny, and Vyāsa begot on her a<BR>son named धृतराष्ट्र.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिः,<BR>--भर्ता N. of Śiva.<BR>--पुत्रः, --सुतः<BR>N. of धृतराष्ट्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबिकेयः|अम्बिकेय|अंबिकेय|अम्बिकेयः
अंबिकेयः, --यकः N. of Gaṇeśa,<BR>Kārttikeya or Dhṛtarāṣṭra; more<BR>correctly written आंबिकेय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबिकेयकः|अम्बिकेयक|अम्बिकेयकः
अंबिकेयः, --यकः N. of Gaṇeśa,<BR>Kārttikeya or Dhṛtarāṣṭra; more<BR>correctly written आंबिकेय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबु|अम्बु
अंबु n. [अंब्-शब्दे उण्]<BR>1 Water;<BR>गांगमंबु सितमंबु यामुनं K. P. 10.<BR>--2 The<BR>watery element of the blood (cf. imber).<BR>--3 N. of a metre.<BR>--4 A term in<BR>astrology (लग्नावधिकं चतुर्थस्थानं).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कणः a drop of water.<BR>--कंटकः (short-nosed), alligator.<BR>--किरातः alligator.<BR>--कीशः, --कूर्मः a<BR>tortoise^1 (शिशुमार); particularly<BR>Gangetic.<BR>--केशरः lemon-tree (छालंगवृक्ष).<BR>--क्रिया libation of water;<BR>presentation of water to the Manes of the<BR>deceased.<BR>--ग, --चर, --चारिन् a.<BR>moving or living in water, aquatic<BR>(as fish &c.)<BR>--घनः hail.<BR>--चत्वरं a<BR>lake.<BR>--चामरं an aquatic plant<BR>(शैवाल).<BR>--ज a. produced in water,<BR>aquatic (opp. स्थलज); सुगंधीनि च<BR>माल्यानि स्थलजान्यंबुजानि च Rām.<BR>--(जः) {1} the moon. {2} camphor.<BR>{3} the Sārasa bird. {4} the conch<BR>{5} N. of a tree (हिज्जल).<BR>--(जं) {1}<BR>a lotus; इंदीवरेण नयनं मुखमंबुजेन<BR>Ś. Til. 3. {2} the thunderbolt of<BR>Indra. ˚भूः, ˚आसनः ‘the lotus-born<BR>god,’ Brahmā; ˚आसना the<BR>goddess Lakṣmī.<BR>--जन्मन् n. a lotus.<BR>(--m.) {1} the moon. {2} the conch.<BR>{3} Sārasa.<BR>--तस्करः ‘water-thief’,<BR>the sun (whose heat drinks up<BR>water).<BR>--तालः = ˚चामर.<BR>--द a.<BR>giving or yielding water.<BR>--(दः) {1} a<BR>cloud; नवांबुदानीकमुहूर्तलांछने<BR>R. 3. 53.<BR>--धर [धरतीति धरः, अंबूनां धरः;<BR>धृअच्] {1} a cloud; वशिनश्चांबुधराश्च<BR>योनयः Ku. 4. 43; शरत्प्रमृष्टांबुधरोपरोधः<BR>R. 6. 44. {2} the plant मुस्तक. {3}<BR>talc.<BR>--धिः [अंबूनि धीयंते अत्र; धा-कि] {1}<BR>any receptacle of waters; such as a<BR>jar; अंबुधिर्घटः Sk. {2} the ocean; क्षार˚<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-c" target="_blank">Page0154-c+ 58</a>]<BR>Bh. 2. 6. {3} the number four (in<BR>Math.). ˚प्रसवा N. of a plant (<BR>घृतकुमारी).<BR>--निधिः ‘treasure of waters’,<BR>the ocean; देवासुरैरमृतमंबुनिधिर्ममंथे<BR>Ki. 5. 30.<BR>--प a. drinking water.<BR>--(पः)<BR>{1} the ocean. {2} Varuṇa, the regent<BR>of waters; रक्षोंबुपानिलशशीशपुराणि<BR>चाष्टौ Sid. Śir. {3} N. of a plant (<BR>चक्रमर्दक).<BR>--पत्रा N. of a plant (<BR>उच्चटावृक्ष).<BR>--पद्धतिः f.,<BR>--पातः current,<BR>flow or stream of water,<BR>cascade; गंगांबुपातप्रतिमा गृहेभ्यः<BR>Bk. 1. 8.<BR>--प्रसादः, --प्रसादनं [अंबूनि प्रसादयति]<BR>the clearing nut tree (कतक)<BR>Strychnos Potatorum (the nuts of this<BR>tree are used for purifying water;<BR>when rubbed on the inner surface of<BR>the vessel, they precipitate the<BR>impurities which the water contains; फलं<BR>कतकवृक्षस्य यद्यप्यंबुप्रसादकं । न नामग्रहणादेव<BR>तस्य वारि प्रसीदति).<BR>--भवं a lotus.<BR>--भृत्<BR>m. {1} water-bearer, a cloud. {2}<BR>the ocean. {3} = ˚पत्रा q. v. {4} N.<BR>of a plant मुस्तक. {5} talc.<BR>--मात्रज a.<BR>produced only in water.<BR>--(जः) a<BR>conch-shell.<BR>--मुच् m. a cloud;<BR>ध्वनितसूचितमंबुमुचां चयं Ki. 5. 12.<BR>--राजः<BR>{1} the ocean. {2} Varuṇa.<BR>--राशिः<BR>receptacle or store of water, the<BR>ocean; त्वयि ज्वलत्यौर्व इवांबुराशौ Ś. 3. 3;<BR>चंद्रोदयारंभ इवांबुराशिः Ku. 3. 67,<BR>R. 6. 57; 9. 82.<BR>--रुह् n. {1} a lotus. {2}<BR>Sārasa.<BR>--रुहः, --हं, a lotus;<BR>विपुलिनांबुरुहा न सरिद्वधूः Ki. 5. 10.<BR>--(हा) N.<BR>of the land-lotus plant (स्थलपद्मिनी).<BR>--रोहिणी a lotus.<BR>--वाची [अंबु तद्वषर्णं<BR>वाचयति सूचयति] an epithet applied to<BR>the earth during four days from the<BR>10th to the 13th in the dark half<BR>of the month of Āṣāḍha when it<BR>is supposed to be unclean (रजस्वला<BR>इव) and agriculture is prohibited;<BR>˚प्रदः the 10th day; ˚त्यागः 13th day.<BR>--वासिनी, --वासी N. of a plant (<BR>पाटला), the trumpet flower.<BR>--वाहः [<BR>अंबु वहतीति] {1} a cloud;<BR>तडित्वंतमिवांबुवाहं Ki. 3. 1; भर्तुर्मित्रं प्रियमविधवे<BR>विद्धि मामंबुवाहं Me. 99. {2} a lake. {3}<BR>water-bearer. {4} the number 17.<BR>{5} a sort of grass.<BR>--वाहिन् a.<BR>carrying or conveying water. (m.) {1} a<BR>cloud. {2} = मुस्तक.<BR>--(नी) {1} a wooden<BR>vessel, a sort of bucket. {2} a woman<BR>fetching water. {3} N. of a stream.<BR>--विहारः sporting in water.<BR>--विस्रवा<BR>= घृतकुमारी.<BR>--वेतसः a kind of cane or<BR>reed growing in water.<BR>--शिरीषिका<BR>N. of a plant.<BR>--सरणं flow or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-a" target="_blank">Page0155-a+ 56</a>]<BR>current of water.<BR>--सर्पिणी a leech (<BR>अंबुनि सर्पति)<BR>--सेचनी a wooden<BR>baling vessel.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबुमत्|अम्बुमत्|अम्बुमन्त्
अंबुमत् a. Watery, containing<BR>water.<BR>--ती N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंबूकृत|अम्बूकृत|अम्बूकृतं
अंबूकृत a. Sputtered, pronounced<BR>indistinctly in shutting the lips,<BR>the sound thus remaining as it were<BR>in the mouth; uttered while<BR>emitting saliva from the mouth.<BR>--तं A<BR>sputtering noise, the growling of a<BR>bear; दधति कुहरभाजामत्र<BR>भल्लूकयूनामनुरसितगुरूणि स्त्यानमंबूकृतानि U. 2. 21;<BR>Māl. 9. 6; Mv. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंब्यः|अम्ब्य|अम्ब्यः
अंब्यः Ved. A chanter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंभ्|अम्भ्
अंभ् {c1c} A. [अंभते, अंभित] To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंभस्|अम्भस्
अंभस् [By Uṇ. 4. 209<BR>आप्-असुन्; or अंभ् शब्दे असुन्]<BR>1 Water;<BR>कथमप्यंभसामंतरानिष्पत्तेः प्रतीक्षते<BR>Ku. 2. 37; स्वेद्यमानज्वरं प्राज्ञः कोंभसा<BR>परिषिंचति Śi. 2. 54; अंभसाकृतं done by<BR>water P. VI. 3. 3.<BR>--2 The sky.<BR>--3<BR>The fourth sign of the zodiac.<BR>--4<BR>Mystical name of the letter व्.<BR>--5<BR>A God.<BR>--6 A man.<BR>--7 The world<BR>of the Manes.<BR>--8 A Rākṣasa or<BR>Asura.<BR>--9 (In phil.) तुष्टि or<BR>acquiescence of the soul.<BR>--10 Power;<BR>splendour; fruitfulness. -- (dual.)<BR>अंभसी Heaven and earth. --(pl.)<BR>Collective name for Gods, men, Manes, and<BR>demons. [cf. L. imber: Gr. ombpos]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. produced in water,<BR>aquatic.<BR>--(जः) {1} the moon. {2} the<BR>(Indian) crane or Sārasa.<BR>--(जं) a<BR>lotus; बाले तव मुखांभोजे कथमिंदीवरद्वयं<BR>Ś. Til. 17; so पाद˚, नेत्र˚; ˚खंडः a<BR>group of lotus flowers; कुमुदवनमपश्रि<BR>श्रीमदंभोजखंडं Śi. 9. 11, 64; ˚जन्मन् m.,<BR>--जनिः, --योनिः the lotus-born God,<BR>epithet of Brahmā.<BR>--जन्मन् n. a lotus.<BR>--दः, --धरः {1} a cloud. {2} the plant<BR>मुस्तक.<BR>--धिः, --निधिः, --राशिः ‘receptacle of<BR>waters’, the ocean; संभूयांभेधिमभ्येति<BR>महानद्या नगापगा Śi. 2. 100;<BR>यादवांभोनिधीन्रुंद्धे वेलेव भवतः क्षमा 58; so अंभसां<BR>निधिः; शिखाभिराश्लिष्ट इवांभसां निधिः<BR>Śi. 1. 20; ˚वल्लभः a coral.<BR>--रुह् n.<BR>(ट्),<BR>--रुहं a lotus; हेमांभोरुहसस्यानां<BR>तद्वाप्यो धाम सांप्रतं Ku. 2. 44. (--m.)<BR>the (Indian) crane.<BR>--सारं a pearl.<BR>--सूः smoke; cloudiness.<BR>--स्थ a.<BR>living in water; what holds or<BR>contains water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंभोजिनी|अम्भोजिनी
अंभोजिनी<BR>1 A lotus-plant or its<BR>flowers; ˚वननिवासविलासं Bh. 2. 18.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-b" target="_blank">Page0155-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--2 A group of lotus flowers.<BR>--3 A<BR>place abounding in lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंभृण|अम्भृण|अम्भृणः
अंभृण a. Ved.<BR>1 Powerful, great,<BR>mighty (महत्).<BR>--2 Roaring terribly.<BR>--णः<BR>1 A vessel or tub used in<BR>preparing the Soma juice.<BR>--2 The father<BR>of Vāc.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्मय|अम्मयं
अम्मय a. (यी f.) [अप्-मय]<BR>Watery, formed from water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्यक्
अम्यक् Ved. Towards, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्र|अम्रः
अम्र = आम्र q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्रातः|अम्रात
अम्रातः --तकः A species of<BR>hog-plum; see आम्रातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्रातकः|अम्रातक
अम्रातः --तकः A species of<BR>hog-plum; see आम्रातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्ल|अम्लं|अम्लः
अम्ल a. [अम्-क्ल Uṇ. 4. 108.]<BR>Sour, acid;<BR>कट्वम्ललवणात्युष्णतीक्ष्णरूक्षविदाहिनः (आहाराः) Bg. 17. 9.<BR>--मः<BR>1 Sourness, acidity, one of<BR>the six kinds of tastes or rasas<BR>q. v.; यो दंतहर्षमुत्पादयति मुखास्रावं जनयति<BR>श्रद्धां चोत्पादयति सोऽम्लः (रसः) Suśr.<BR>--2 Vinegar.<BR>--3 Wood-sorrel.<BR>--4 =<BR>अम्लवेतस q. v.<BR>--5 The common citron tree.<BR>--6 Belch.<BR>--म्ली = चांगेरी.<BR>--म्लं Sour<BR>curds, butter-milk, with a fourth<BR>part of water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्त a.<BR>acidulated.<BR>--अंकुशः a variety of<BR>sorrel (˚वेतस).<BR>--अध्युषितं a disease of<BR>the eye.<BR>--उद्गारः sour eructation.<BR>--कांडं N. of a plant (लवणतृण).<BR>--केशरः the citron tree.<BR>--गंधि a.<BR>having a sour smell.<BR>--गोरसः sour<BR>buttermilk.<BR>--चुक्रिका, --चूडा a sort of sorrel.<BR>--जंबीरः, --निंबकः the lime-tree.<BR>--नायकः = ˚वेतसः q. v.<BR>--निशा N.<BR>of a plant (शठी).<BR>--पंचकं, --पंचफलं a<BR>collection of five kinds of vegetables<BR>and fruits; कौलं च दाडिमं चैव वृक्षाम्लं<BR>चुक्रिका तथा । अम्लवेतसमित्येतदम्लपंचफलं<BR>स्मृतम् ॥ or जंबीरं नागरंगं च तथाम्लं<BR>वेतसं पुनः ॥ तिंतिडीकं वीजपूरमम्लपंचफलं स्मृतम्.<BR>--पुत्रः N. of a plant (अश्मंतक).<BR>--(त्री)<BR>पलाशीलता and क्षुद्राम्लिका.<BR>--पनसः N.<BR>of a tree (लकुच).<BR>--पित्तं acidity of<BR>stomach, sour bile.<BR>--पूरं = वृक्षाम्लं q. v.<BR>--फलः the tamarind tree.<BR>--(लं)<BR>tamarind fruit.<BR>--भेदनः = ˚वेतस<BR>q. v.<BR>--मेहः a kind of<BR>urinary disease.<BR>--रस a. having an<BR>acid taste.<BR>--(सः) sourness,<BR>acidity.<BR>--रुहा a kind of betel (<BR>मालवदेशजनागवल्लीभेदः).<BR>--लोणिका, --लोणी,<BR>--लोलिका wood sorrel (Mar. चुका).<BR>--वर्गः a class of sour things including<BR>plants with acid leaves and fruits.<BR>--वल्ली N. of a plant (त्रिपर्णिका<BR>नामकंदविशेषः).<BR>--वाटकः hog-plum.<BR>--वाटिका a sort of betel.<BR>--वस्तूकः a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">Page0155-c+ 57</a>]<BR>sorrel (चुक्रं).<BR>--वृक्षः the tamarind tree.<BR>--वेतसः a kind of sorrel (Mar. चुका,<BR>चांगेरी).<BR>--शाकः a sort of sorrel (<BR>शाकाम्ल, शुक्राम्ल, अम्ल, चुक्रिका, चूड)<BR>commonly used as a potherb.<BR>--(कं) = वृक्षाम्लं,<BR>चुक्रं.<BR>--सारः {1} the lime tree. {2} a<BR>sort of sorrel (˚वेतस). {3} N. of a<BR>plant (हिंताल).<BR>--(रं) rice water after<BR>fermentation (कांजिकं).<BR>--हरिद्रा N.<BR>of a plant (˚निशा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लकः|अम्लक
अम्लकः N. of a plant(लकुच), a<BR>sort of bread-fruit tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लिका
अम्लि(म्ली)का<BR>1 Sour taste in the<BR>mouth, sour eructation.<BR>--2 The<BR>tamarind tree.<BR>--3 Wood-sorrel; also<BR>पलाशीलता, श्वेताम्लिका, and क्षुद्राम्लिका.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वटकः a sort of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लीका
अम्लि(म्ली)का<BR>1 Sour taste in the<BR>mouth, sour eructation.<BR>--2 The<BR>tamarind tree.<BR>--3 Wood-sorrel; also<BR>पलाशीलता, श्वेताम्लिका, and क्षुद्राम्लिका.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वटकः a sort of cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लिमन्
अम्लिमन् m. Sourness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्व्लः|अम्व्ल
अम्व्लः Sourness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लान|अम्लानः
अम्लान a.<BR>1 Not withered or<BR>faded (flowers &c.).<BR>--2 Clean, clear,<BR>bright (face); pure, unclouded;<BR>परार्थन्यायवादेषु काणोप्यम्लानदर्शनः.<BR>--नः Globe-amaranth (Mar. आंबोली).<BR>--नं A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लानि|अम्लानिः
अम्लानि a. Vigorous, not fading.<BR>--निः f.<BR>1 Vigour.<BR>--2 Freshness;<BR>verdure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अम्लानिन्
अम्लानिन् Clear, clean.<BR>--नी A<BR>collection of globe-amaranths.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय्
अय् {c1c} A. (sometimes P. also,<BR>especially with उद्) (अयते, अयांचक्रे,<BR>अयितुं, अयित.) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अय|अयः
अय a. Going, moving.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>Going, moving (mostly in comp., as in<BR>अस्तमय).<BR>--2 Good actions of former<BR>birth.<BR>--3 Good fortune, good luck<BR>(शुभावहो विधिः); शुद्धपार्ष्णिरयान्वितः<BR>R. 4. 26.<BR>--4 A move towards the right<BR>(in chess).<BR>--5 A die or cube (to<BR>play with); कलिः सर्वानयानभिभवति<BR>Śat. Br.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वित, अयवत्<BR>a. fortunate, lucky; सुलभैः सदा<BR>नयवताऽयवता Ki. 5. 20.<BR>--शोभिन् a.<BR>bright with good fortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयन|अयनं
अयन a. [अय्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Going (at<BR>the end of comp.); यथेमा नद्यः<BR>स्यंदमानाः समुद्रायणाः Praśn. Up.<BR>--2 (As<BR>a patronymic affix) Descended from;<BR>e. g. शाकटायन.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Going, moving,<BR>walking; as in रामायणं.<BR>--2 A walk,<BR>path, way, road;<BR>अगस्त्यचिह्नादयनात् R. 16. 44.<BR>--3 A place, site,<BR>abode, place of resort; ता यदस्यायनं<BR>पूर्वं Ms. 1. 10 (occurring in the<BR>derivation of the word नारायण).<BR>--4 A<BR>way of entrance, an entrance (to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-a" target="_blank">Page0156-a+ 57</a>]<BR>an array of troops or व्यूह); अयनेषु<BR>च सर्वेषु यथाभागमवास्थिताः Bg. 1. 11.<BR>--5 Rotation, circulation period;<BR>अंगिरसां अयनं; इष्टि˚, पशु˚.<BR>--6 A particular<BR>period in the year for the<BR>performance of particular sacrificial or<BR>other religious works; N. of<BR>certain sacrificial performances; as<BR>गवामयनं.<BR>--7 The sun's passage, north<BR>and south of the equator.<BR>--8 (Hence)<BR>The period of duration of this<BR>passage, half year, the time from one<BR>solstice to another; see उत्तरायण<BR>and दक्षिणायन; cf. also सायन and<BR>निरयण.<BR>--9 The equinoctial and<BR>solstitial points; दक्षिणं अयनं winter<BR>solstice; उत्तरं अयनं summer<BR>solstice.<BR>--10 Method, manner, way.<BR>--11<BR>A Śāstra, scripture or inspired<BR>writing.<BR>--12 Final emancipation;<BR>नान्यः पंथा विद्यतेऽयनाय Śvet. Up.<BR>--13 A commentary; treatise.<BR>--14<BR>The deities presiding over the<BR>ayanas.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः, --भागः<BR>the arc between the vernal<BR>equinoctial point and the beginning of<BR>the fixed zodiac or first point in<BR>Aries.<BR>--कालः the interval between<BR>the solstices.<BR>--जः a month caused<BR>by ayanāṃśa.<BR>--संक्रमः, --संक्रांतिः<BR>f. passage through the zodiac.<BR>--वृत्तं<BR>the ecliptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयक्ष्म
अयक्ष्म a. Ved.<BR>1 Not<BR>consumptive, healthy.<BR>--2 Causing health.<BR>--क्ष्मं Healthiness, freedom from<BR>disease.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करण a. causing<BR>health, making healthy and sound.<BR>--तातिः f. health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयजुष्क
अयजुष्क a. Without a sacrificial<BR>formula or verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञ|अयज्ञः
अयज्ञ a. Not offering sacrifice.<BR>--ज्ञः No sacrifice, a bad sacrifice;<BR>Ms. 3. 120.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--साच् a. not<BR>performing a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञक
अयज्ञक a. Unfit for sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्ञिय
अयज्ञिय a.<BR>1 Not fit for sacrifice<BR>(as माष).<BR>--2 Not fit to perform a<BR>sacrifice (as a boy not invested with<BR>the sacred thread).<BR>--3 Profane,<BR>vulgar, common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्यु
अयज्यु a. Ved.<BR>1 Profane,<BR>impious.<BR>--2 Obstructor or destroyer of<BR>sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयज्वन्
अयज्वन् a. Not sacrificing<BR>according to the rites; godless, impious;<BR>Ms. 11. 14, 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्
अयत् a. Not attempting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत
अयत a. Uncontrolled, unchecked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयतिन्
अयतिन् a. Of unsubdued desires<BR>or passions, incontinent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयत्न|अयत्नः
अयत्न a. Not requiring any effort;<BR>˚पटवासतां R. 4. 55.<BR>--त्नः Absence<BR>of effort or exertion; अयत्नेन, --त्नात्,<BR>--त्नतः without effort or exertion,<BR>easily, readily.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारिन् a.<BR>making no effort or exertion,<BR>indifferent; idle.<BR>--कृत, --ज a. easily<BR>produced, spontaneous.<BR>--लभ्य a.<BR>easily obtainable; Bh. 3. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथं|अयथ
अयथं Ved. A foot, leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथा
अयथा ind. Not as it should be<BR>or is intended to be, unfitly,<BR>improperly, wrongly.<BR>--थं Ved.<BR>Without effort.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. {1} not true<BR>to the sense, unmeaning,<BR>nonsensical; Mu. 3. 4. {2} incongruous, unfit,<BR>false, Ś. 3. 2; incorrect, wrong;<BR>अनुभवो द्विविधो यथार्थोऽयथार्थश्च T. S.;<BR>˚अनुभवः incorrect or untrue<BR>knowledge, wrong notion; तदभाववति<BR>तत्प्रकारकोऽनुभवोऽयथार्थानुभवः । यथा<BR>शुक्तौरजतमिदमिति ज्ञानं सैव अप्रमेत्युच्यते.<BR>--इष्ट a. {1} not as wished or desired,<BR>disliked. {2} not enough or<BR>sufficient.<BR>--उचित a. unfit, unworthy.<BR>--(तं) unfitly.<BR>--तथ a. {1} not as it<BR>should be, unfit, unsuitable,<BR>unworthy; इदमयथातथं स्वामिनश्चेष्टितं<BR>Ve. 2. {2} vain, useless, profitless.<BR>--(थं) {1} unfitly, unsuitably {2} in vain,<BR>uselessly; तद्गच्छति अ˚ Ms. 3. 240.<BR>{3} wrongly; Ve. 5.<BR>--तथ्यं<BR>unsuitableness, incongruity;<BR>uselessness.<BR>--द्योतनं intimation or<BR>occurrence of some thing or act which is<BR>not expected.<BR>--पुर, --पूर्व a.<BR>unprecedented, unparalleled,<BR>unusual.<BR>--मुखीन a. having the face<BR>turned away.<BR>--वृत्त a. acting<BR>wrongly.<BR>--शास्त्रकारिन् a. not acting<BR>according to the Śāstras, irreligious;<BR>अयथाशास्त्रकारी च न विभागे पिता प्रभुः Nārada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयथावत्
अयथावत् ind. Wrongly,<BR>erroneously, improperly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयंत्रं|अयन्त्र
अयंत्रं<BR>1 Non-restraint; having<BR>no restraint.<BR>--2 A powerful weapon<BR>for restraining enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयंत्रित|अयन्त्रित|अयन्त्रितः
अयंत्रित a. Unrestrained,<BR>unchecked, self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयमित
अयमित a.<BR>1 Unrestrained,<BR>unchecked.<BR>--2 Untrimmed,<BR>undecorated (as nails &c.) Me. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयव|अयवः
अयव a.<BR>1 Deficient.<BR>--2 Having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-c" target="_blank">Page0156-c+ 57</a>]<BR>worthless or no barley, such as a<BR>religious ceremony (also अयवक in<BR>this sense).<BR>--वः<BR>1 Name of a worm<BR>bred in excrement.<BR>--2 (अयवन् m.,<BR>अयवस् n. also). The dark half of the<BR>month; पूर्वपक्षा वै यवा अपरपक्षा वा<BR>अयवास्तेहीदे सर्वं युवते चायुवते च Śat. Br.<BR>--3 An<BR>incongruous enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयव्य
अयव्य a. Unfit for barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्
अयशस् a. Disreputable,<BR>infamous, disgraceful; also अयशस्क<BR>in this sense. --n. (शः) Infamy,<BR>disgrace, ignominy, ill-repute, stain,<BR>dishonour, scandal; अयशो<BR>महदाप्नोति Ms. 8. 128; किमयशो ननु घोरमतः परं<BR>U. 3. 27; स्वभावलोलेत्ययशः प्रमृष्टं<BR>R. 6. 41.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a. (री f.)<BR>disgraceful, ignominious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयशस्य
अयशस्य a. Infamous, ignominious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्
अयस् a. [इ-गतौ-असुन्] Going,<BR>moving; nimble. --n.<BR>--(यः)<BR>1 Iron<BR>(एति चलति अयस्कांतसंनिकर्षं इति तथात्वं);<BR>अभितप्तमयोपि मार्दवं भजते कैव कथा<BR>शरीरिषु R. 8. 43.<BR>--2 Steel.<BR>--3 Gold.<BR>--4<BR>A metal in general.<BR>--5 Aloe wood.<BR>--6 An iron instrument.<BR>--7 Going.<BR>--m. Fire. [cf L. aes, aeris; Goth.<BR>ais, eisarn; Ger. eisin].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रं --अग्रकं a hammer, a mace or<BR>club tipped with iron; a pestle<BR>for cleaning grain.<BR>--अपाष्टि a. Ved.<BR>furnished with iron claws or<BR>heels.<BR>--कंसः --सं an iron goblet.<BR>--कांडः {1} an iron-arrow. {2}<BR>excellent iron. {3} a large quantity of<BR>iron.<BR>--कांतः (अयस्कांतः) {1} ‘beloved<BR>of iron’, a magnet, load-stone;<BR>शंभोर्यतध्वमाक्रष्टुमयस्कांतेन लोहवत्<BR>Ku. 2. 59; स चकर्ष परस्मात्तदयस्कांत इवायसं<BR>R. 17. 63; U. 4. 21. {2} a precious<BR>stone; ˚मणिः a loadstone;<BR>अयस्कांतमणिशलाकेव लोहधातुमंतःकरणमाकृष्टवती<BR>Māl. 1.<BR>--कारः {1} an iron-smith,<BR>blacksmith. {2} the upper part of the thigh.<BR>--कीटं rust of iron.:<BR>--कुंभः an iron<BR>vessel, boiler &c.; so ˚पात्रं.<BR>--कुशा a<BR>rope partly consisting of iron.<BR>--कृतिः<BR>f. a preparation of iron; one of the<BR>ways of curing leprosy (<BR>महाकुष्ठचिकित्साभेदः).<BR>--गः an iron hammer.<BR>--गुडः<BR>{1} a pill; one made of some<BR>preparation of iron. {2} an iron ball;<BR>Ms. 3. 133.<BR>--घनः [अयो हन्यते अनेन इति<BR>P. III. 3. 82] an iron hammer, forge<BR>hammer; अयोघनेनाय इवाभितप्तं<BR>R. 14. 33.<BR>--चूर्णं iron filings.<BR>--जाल a.<BR>having iron nets; of impenetrable guiles.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-a" target="_blank">Page0157-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--(लं) an iron net-work.<BR>--ताप a.<BR>making iron red-hot.<BR>--दत्, --दंष्ट्र a.<BR>Ved. iron-toothed, having iron rims<BR>(as chariots); having iron weapons.<BR>--दती a proper name; (P. V. 4. 143).<BR>--दंडः an iron club, K. 76.<BR>--धातुः<BR>iron metal; U. 4. 21.<BR>--पानं (अयः पानं)<BR>N. of a hell (where red-hot iron is<BR>forced down the throats of those<BR>who are condemned to it).<BR>--प्रतिमा<BR>(अयःप्रतिमा) an iron image.<BR>--मलं<BR>rust of iron; so ˚रजः, ˚रसः.<BR>--मुख a.<BR>(खी f.) {1} having an iron<BR>mouth, face, or beak. {2} tipped<BR>or pointed with iron; Ms. 10. 84.<BR>--(खः) an arrow (iron-pointed);<BR>भेत्स्यत्यजः कुंभमयोमुखेन R. 5. 55.<BR>--शंकुः {1} an iron spear. {2} an iron<BR>nail, pointed iron spike, R. 12. 95.<BR>--शय a. lying in, made of, iron,<BR>(said of fire).<BR>--शूलं {1} an iron lance.<BR>{2} a forcible means, a violent<BR>proceeding (तीक्ष्णः उपायः Sk.); (cf.<BR>आयःशूलिक; also K. P. 10; अयःशूलेन<BR>अन्विच्छतीत्यायःशूलिकः).<BR>--स्थूण a. (अय˚ or<BR>यः˚) having iron pillars or stakes.<BR>--हत a. Ved. embossed in<BR>ironwork, made by a priest who wears<BR>a golden ring on his finger (B. and<BR>R.).<BR>--हृदय a. iron-hearted, stern,<BR>cruel, unrelenting; सुहृदयोहृदयः<BR>प्रतिगर्जताम् R. 9. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0156-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस्मय
अयस्मय,(अयोमय) a. (यी f.) Ved.<BR>Made of iron or of any metal.<BR>--यी N. of one of the three<BR>habitations of Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोमय
अयस्मय,(अयोमय) a. (यी f.) Ved.<BR>Made of iron or of any metal.<BR>--यी N. of one of the three<BR>habitations of Asuras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोच्छिष्टं|अयोच्छिष्ट
अयोच्छिष्टं Rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयस
अयस (At the end of comp.) see<BR>कार्ष्णायस, कालायस &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अया
अया ind. Ved. Thus, in this<BR>manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाचक|अयाचकः
अयाचक a. One who does not<BR>ask or solicit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाचित|अयाचितं|अयाचितः
अयाचित a. Unasked,<BR>unsolicited (as alms, food &c.); अमृतं<BR>स्यादयाचितं Ms. 4. 5; 11. 212.<BR>--तः N.<BR>of the sage Upavarṣa.<BR>--तं<BR>Unsolicited alms.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपनत,<BR>--उपस्थित a. got unasked or without<BR>solicitation; अयाचितोपस्थितमंबु केवलं<BR>Ku. 5. 22.<BR>--वृत्तिः, --व्रतं subsisting on<BR>alms got without begging or<BR>solicitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाज्य
अयाज्य a.<BR>1 (A person) for whom<BR>one must not perform sacrifices,<BR>not competent to offer sacrifices (as<BR>a Śūdra &c.).<BR>--2 (Hence), Out-cast;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">Page0157-b+ 56</a>]<BR>degraded, not admissible to or<BR>incapable of religious ceremonies.<BR>--3<BR>Not fit for sacrificial offerings.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--याजनं, --संयाज्यं sacrificing<BR>for a person for whom one must not<BR>perform sacrifices; Ms. 3. 65; 11. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयात
अयात a. Not &c. gone.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पूर्व a. following, succeeding,<BR>subsequent to.<BR>--याम a. not old or<BR>weakened, not stale, fresh, not worn<BR>out by use; ˚मं च यौवनं Dk. 123<BR>fresh, blooming; ˚मं वयः 158;<BR>छंदांस्ययातयामानि Bhāg. (where Śrīdhara<BR>says अ˚ = विगतदोषाणि free from faults,<BR>faultless, pure.<BR>--(मं) N. of certain<BR>texts of the Yajurveda revealed<BR>to Yājñavalkya. ˚यामता freshness,<BR>unimpaired nature, strength, or<BR>vigour, purity.)<BR>--यामन् a.<BR>Ved. not weak, fresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयातु|अयातुः
अयातु a. Ved. Not demoniacal;<BR>free from evil spirits.<BR>--तुः Not a<BR>demon, not an evil spirit, not<BR>destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाथार्थिक
अयाथार्थिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Not<BR>true, wrong, unjust, improper.<BR>--2<BR>Not real or genuine, incongruous,<BR>absurd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाथार्थ्यं|अयाथार्थ्य
अयाथार्थ्यं<BR>1 Unfitness,<BR>incorrectness.<BR>--2 Absurdity, incongruity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयानं|अयान
अयानं<BR>1 Not going or moving;<BR>stopping, halt.<BR>--2 Natural<BR>disposition, nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयानयं|अयानय|अयानयः
अयानयं [अयश्च अनयश्च तयोःसमाहारः]<BR>Good or bad luck.<BR>--यः A<BR>particular position of the pieces on a<BR>chessboard (आनीयंते शारा अस्मिन् इत्यानयः;<BR>अयेन दक्षिणावर्तेन अपसव्यगमनेन आनयः<BR>अयानयः शीर्षस्थानं Saralā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयानयीनः|अयानयीन
अयानयीनः [अयानय-ख] A piece at<BR>chess or backgammon; अयानयः<BR>स्थलविशेषः तं नेयोऽयानयीनः शारः P. V. 2. 9 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयावक
अयावक a. Naturally red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयावनं|अयावन
अयावनं Not causing to unite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयाशु
अयाशु a. Ved.<BR>1 Unfit for<BR>copulation.<BR>--2 Destructive of good<BR>things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयास्
अयास् a. [fr. इ ‘to go’ Nir.] Ved.<BR>Agile, nimble.<BR>--याः ind. [इ-आसिः<BR>Uṇ. 4. 221] Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयास्य|अयास्यः
अयास्य a. Ved. Indefatigable,<BR>inexhaustible, valiant, invincible.<BR>--स्यः<BR>1 A mystical name for the<BR>chief life-wind.<BR>--2 N. of Aṅgirasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयासोमीयं|अयासोमीय
अयासोमीयं N. of some verses of<BR>the Sāma Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयि
अयि ind.<BR>1 As a gentle address<BR>in the sense of ‘friend’, ‘oh’ ‘ah’<BR>(कोमलामंत्रणे); or simply as a<BR>vocative particle; अयि<BR>विवेकविश्रांतमभिहितं M. 1; अयि कठोर U. 3. 27 Oh<BR>you ruthless one; अयि भो महर्षिपुत्र<BR>Ś. 7; अयि विद्युत्प्रमदानां त्वमपि च दुःखं<BR>न जानासि Mk. 5. 32; अयि<BR>मातर्देवयजनसंभवे देवि सीते U. 4; see also<BR>Bv. 1. 5, 11, 44.<BR>--2 As a particle of<BR>entreaty or solicitation (अनुनय),<BR>‘I pray’, ‘prythee’; अयि संप्रति देहि<BR>दर्शनं Ku. 4. 28; also of encouragement<BR>or persuasion; अयि मंदस्मितमधुरं वदनं<BR>तन्वंगि यदि मनाक्कुरुषे Bv. 2. 150.<BR>--3 As a particle of gentle or kind<BR>inquiry (प्रश्न); अयि जीवितनाथ जीवसि<BR>Ku. 4. 3; अयीदमेवं परिहासः 5. 62;<BR>अयि जानीषे रोभिलस्य सार्थवाहस्य गृहं<BR>Mk. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्त|अयुक्तं
अयुक्त a.<BR>1 Not yoked or<BR>harnessed.<BR>--2 Not joined, united or<BR>connected.<BR>--3 Not devout or pious,<BR>inattentive, negligent.<BR>--4<BR>Unpractised, unused, unemployed; ˚बुद्धि,<BR>˚चार.<BR>--5 Unfit, improper, unsuitable;<BR>अयुक्तोयं निर्देशः P. IV. 2. 64, Mbh.<BR>--6 Untrue, wrong.<BR>--7 Unmarried.<BR>--8 Opening externally.<BR>--9<BR>Reduced to straits, miserable.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. an official (perhaps for<BR>आयुक्त˚).<BR>--कृत् a. doing improper<BR>or wrong acts.<BR>--पदार्थः the sense of<BR>a word to be supplied, as the sense<BR>of अपि q. v.<BR>--रूप a. incongruous,<BR>unsuitable; ˚पं किमतःपरं वद Ku. 5. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुक्तिः|अयुक्ति
अयुक्तिः f.<BR>1 Disunion,<BR>separation.<BR>--2 Unreasonableness, want of<BR>conformity to correct principles.<BR>--3<BR>Unfitness, impropriety, incongruity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग
अयुग, --गल a.<BR>1 Separate, single.<BR>--2<BR>Odd, uneven.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्चिस् m.<BR>Fire.<BR>--नेत्रः, --नयनः, --शरः See under<BR>अयुग्म.<BR>--सप्तिः having seven horses;<BR>Śi. 11. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगल
अयुग, --गल a.<BR>1 Separate, single.<BR>--2<BR>Odd, uneven.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्चिस् m.<BR>Fire.<BR>--नेत्रः, --नयनः, --शरः See under<BR>अयुग्म.<BR>--सप्तिः having seven horses;<BR>Śi. 11. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगपद्
अयुगपद् ind. Not all together,<BR>gradually, seriatim.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रहणं apprehending gradually.<BR>--भावः<BR>successive order, successiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुगूः
अयुगूः f. A woman that bears<BR>only one child. (= काकवंध्या q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुग्म
अयुग्म a.<BR>1 Not in pairs or<BR>couples; single, separate.<BR>--2 Odd,<BR>uneven (as a number) अयुग्मासु<BR>रात्रिषु Ms. 3. 48.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--छदः, --पत्रः<BR>having an odd (i. e. 7) number of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">Page0158-a+ 56</a>]<BR>leaves; the सप्तपर्ण tree; Ki. 1. 16.<BR>--नयनः, --नेत्रः, --लोचनः having odd (3)<BR>eyes, N. of Śiva; Ku. 3. 51, 69.<BR>--बाणः, --शरः &c. having odd (5)<BR>arrows; N. of Cupid.<BR>--वाहः, --सप्तिः<BR>having seven horses, the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुज्
अयुज् a. Not being in couples,<BR>odd, uneven (opp. युज् even);<BR>अयुजि नयुगरेफतो यकारो युजि तु नजौ<BR>जरगाश्च पुष्पिताग्रा V. Ratn.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इषुः, --बाणः, --शरः N. of Cupid (having {5}<BR>arrows).<BR>--छदः = सप्तवर्ण (Mar. सातवण);<BR>ववुरयुक्छदगुच्छसुगंधयः Śi. 6. 50.<BR>--पलाशः = सप्तपलाश.<BR>--पादयमकं a kind<BR>of alliteration having the same<BR>syllables (in a different sense) in the<BR>first and third pādas.<BR>--नेत्र, --लोचन,<BR>--अक्ष, --शक्तिः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुज
अयुज a.<BR>1 Having no equal or<BR>companion.<BR>--2 Separate, single, odd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुंग|अयुङ्ग
अयुंग a. Ved. Not existing in<BR>couples, odd, uneven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुत|अयुतं|अयुतः
अयुत a.<BR>1 Disjoined, detached,<BR>not connected.<BR>--2 Uninterrupted,<BR>undisturbed (Ved.)<BR>--तं Ten<BR>thousand, a myriad.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्यापकः a good teacher.<BR>--सिद्ध a. (in<BR>Vaiś. phil.) proved to be inseparable<BR>and inherent.<BR>--सिद्धिः f. proof that<BR>certain things or notions are<BR>inseparable and inherent.<BR>--होम a<BR>kind of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध
अयुद्ध a. Ved.<BR>1 Not fighting.<BR>--2 Unconquered, irresistible.<BR>--द्धं<BR>Absence of fighting or war.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सेन a. of unconquerable armies<BR>(or arrows), irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुद्ध्वी
अयुद्ध्वी ind. Without fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुधः|अयुध
अयुधः A non-combatant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुध्य
अयुध्य a. Unconquerable,<BR>irresistible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुध्विन्
अयुध्विन् m. Not a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयुव
अयुव a.<BR>1 Undisturbed,<BR>unshaken.<BR>--2 Unconnected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अये
अये ind.<BR>1 As a vocative particle,<BR>or as a kind of gentle address ( =<BR>अयि); अये गौरीनाथ त्रिपुरहर शंभो<BR>त्रिनयन Bh. 3. 123.<BR>--2 An interjection<BR>showing (a) ‘surprise’ or ‘wonder’<BR>and translated by ‘oh’ ‘ah’, अये<BR>मातलिः Ś. 6; अये कुमारलक्ष्मणः प्राप्तः<BR>U. 1; अये मय्येव भ्रुकुटीधरः संवृत्तः<BR>U. 5; (b) ‘grief’, ‘dejection’; अये<BR>दवेपादपद्मोपजीविनोऽवस्थेयं Mu. 2 (alas!);<BR>(c) ‘anger’; अये अश्वमेध इति<BR>विश्वविजयिनां क्षत्रियाणां महानुत्कर्षनिकषः U. 4;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">Page0158-b+ 57</a>]<BR>(d) ‘fear,’ ‘flurry’, ‘agitation;’ (e)<BR>‘recollection’; (f) ‘fear’; (g)<BR>‘fatigue’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग|अयोगः
अयोग a.<BR>1 Unconnected with.<BR>--2 Indistinctly connected.<BR>--3<BR>Making vigorous efforts.<BR>--गः<BR>1<BR>Separation, disjunction, interval.<BR>--2<BR>Unfitness, impropriety, incongruity.<BR>--3 An improper conjunction.<BR>--4<BR>Inefficacy of a remedy or medicine (as<BR>of a purgative or emetic).<BR>--5<BR>Strong or vigorous effort.<BR>--6<BR>Medical treatment against the<BR>symptoms.<BR>--7 Non-application or<BR>misapplication of remedies.<BR>--8 A sort<BR>of disease (cured by prescribing<BR>emetics).<BR>--9 A widower; absent<BR>lover or husband (विधुर).<BR>--10 A<BR>hammer (for अयोग्र, अयोघन).<BR>--11<BR>Dislike.<BR>--12 A conjunction of two<BR>planets (also inauspicious).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वाहः a term for अनुस्वार, विसर्जनीय,<BR>उपध्मानीय, and जिह्वामूलीय as standing<BR>between vowels and consonants;<BR>अनुस्वारो विसर्गश्च ZकVपौ चैव पराश्रितौ ।<BR>अयोगवाहा विज्ञेया आश्रयस्थानभागिनः ।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगवः|अयोगव
अयोगवः (वा or वी f.) The son<BR>of a Śūdra man and Vaiśya woman;<BR>Ms. 10. 32; see आयोगव; (his<BR>business is carpentry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगुड|अयोगुडः
अयोगुड, --जाल &c. see under<BR>अयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोजाल
अयोगुड, --जाल &c. see under<BR>अयस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोगूः
अयोगूः A blacksmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोग्य
अयोग्य a.<BR>1 Unfit, improper,<BR>unsuitable, useless.<BR>--2 Not<BR>ascertainable by senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोद्धृ
अयोद्धृ m.<BR>1 No warrior, a bad<BR>warrior.<BR>--2 One who is not equalled<BR>by other warriors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोध्य
अयोध्य a. Not to be warred<BR>against, unassailable; irresistible;<BR>अद्यायोध्या महाबाहो अयोध्या प्रतिभाति नः<BR>Rām.<BR>--ध्या The capital of solar<BR>kings, born of the line of Raghu,<BR>(the modern Oudh) situated on<BR>the river Sarayū. [It is said to have<BR>extended 48 miles in length and 12 miles<BR>in breadth. It was also called Sāketa,<BR>and one of its suburbs was Nandi-grāma,<BR>where Bharata governed the kingdom<BR>during the absence of Rāma. The town<BR>plays an important part in the story of<BR>the Rāmāyaṇa; the second book (<BR>अयोध्याकांड) dealing mostly with events<BR>that took place in that city during the<BR>youthful days of Rāma.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनि|अयोनिः
अयोनि a.<BR>1 Without origin or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">Page0158-c+ 56</a>]<BR>source, eternal; जगद्योनिरयोनिस्त्वं<BR>Ku. 2. 9.<BR>--2 Not born from the womb;<BR>born in a manner not approved by law<BR>or religion.<BR>--निः f.<BR>1 Not the womb;<BR>Y. 2. 293; Ms. 11. 174.<BR>--2 Not a<BR>particular verse of the Sāmaveda.<BR>--निः<BR>1 N. of Brahmā and Śiva.<BR>--2 A<BR>pestle.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज, --जन्मन् a.<BR>not born from the womb, not<BR>produced in the ordinary course of<BR>generation; शरीरं द्विविधं<BR>योनिजमयोनिजं चेति T. S; तनयां अयोनिजां<BR>R. 11. 47, 48; कन्यारत्नमयोनिजन्म<BR>भवतामास्ते Mv. 1. 30.<BR>--(जः) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>˚ईशः, ईश्वरः N. of Śiva. (--जा),<BR>--संभवा N. of Sītā, daughter of<BR>Janaka, who was born from a<BR>furrow in a field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयोनिक
अयोनिक a. Without the words<BR>एष ते योनिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौगपद्यं|अयौगपद्य
अयौगपद्यं Absence of<BR>simultaneity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौगिक
अयौगिक (की f.) Not<BR>etymologically derived (as a word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अयौक्तिक
अयौक्तिक a. Inconsistent with<BR>reason, unreasonable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर|अरं|अरः
अर a. [इयर्ति गच्छत्यनेन, ऋ-अच्]<BR>1<BR>Speedy, swift.<BR>--2 Little.<BR>--3 Going<BR>(at the end of comp.).<BR>--रः<BR>1 The<BR>spoke or radius of a wheel; (˚रं also);<BR>अरैः संधार्यते नाभिर्नाभौ चाराः प्रतिष्ठिताः<BR>Pt. 1. 81.<BR>--2 A spoke of the<BR>timewheel; a jaina division of time.<BR>--3 A corner (कोण) or angle;<BR>त्रिपंचारे पीठे Śyāmāstava.<BR>--4 Moss (<BR>शैवाल).<BR>--5 = पर्पट q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतर (pl.) the intervals of the spoke;<BR>V. 1. 4.<BR>--घट्टः, --घट्टकः [अरैः घट्ट्यते रच्यते असौ]<BR>{1} a wheel or machine for raising<BR>water from a well (Mar. राहाट).<BR>(It usually consists of a single<BR>wheel with spokes on each side<BR>serving as handles to turn it, and<BR>a rope with a bucket attached to it<BR>passes over this wheel); ˚दृं खेलयमानः<BR>Pt. 4 turning this machine; ˚घटी<BR>a bucket so used; कूपमासाद्य<BR>˚टीमार्गेण सर्पस्तेनानीतः Pt. 4. {2} a deep well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरक्षस्
अरक्षस् a.<BR>1 Not disturbed by<BR>evil spirits.<BR>--2 Harmless, honest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंकृ|अरङ्कृ
अरंकृ, --गम् See under अरं below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंगम्|अरङ्गम्
अरंकृ, --गम् See under अरं below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंगिन्|अरङ्गिन्
अरंगिन् a. Passionless; ˚सत्त्वः a<BR>passionless being; a class of<BR>divinitieswith Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजस्
अरजस्, अरज, अरजस्क a.<BR>1<BR>Dustless, clean, pure (fig. also).<BR>--2 Free<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-a" target="_blank">Page0159-a+ 57</a>]<BR>from passion (रजस्).<BR>--3 Not having<BR>the monthly courses. --f.<BR>--(जाः)<BR>A young girl who has not reached<BR>the age of puberty; a girl before<BR>menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरज
अरजस्, अरज, अरजस्क a.<BR>1<BR>Dustless, clean, pure (fig. also).<BR>--2 Free<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-a" target="_blank">Page0159-a+ 57</a>]<BR>from passion (रजस्).<BR>--3 Not having<BR>the monthly courses. --f.<BR>--(जाः)<BR>A young girl who has not reached<BR>the age of puberty; a girl before<BR>menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजस्क
अरजस्, अरज, अरजस्क a.<BR>1<BR>Dustless, clean, pure (fig. also).<BR>--2 Free<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-a" target="_blank">Page0159-a+ 57</a>]<BR>from passion (रजस्).<BR>--3 Not having<BR>the monthly courses. --f.<BR>--(जाः)<BR>A young girl who has not reached<BR>the age of puberty; a girl before<BR>menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0158-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरजायते
अरजायते Den. A.<BR>1 To become<BR>dustless or pure.<BR>--2 To lose the<BR>monthly courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरज्जु
अरज्जु a. Not consisting of, or<BR>furnished with, cords. --n. A<BR>prisonhouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण|अरणं
अरण a. (णी f.) Ved.<BR>1<BR>Departed, gone away; belonging to<BR>others, strange, unusual, foreign;<BR>distant, remote. (opp. स्व, नित्य or<BR>अमा); (Sāy. grieved, sorry<BR>दुःखित, अरममाण); inimical, hostile,<BR>(with whom one is not on<BR>speaking terms).<BR>--2 Not fighting.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Moving, going.<BR>--2 Entering<BR>into, being inserted.<BR>--3 A refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणिः|अरणि
अरणिः m. f.,<BR>--णी f. [ऋ-अनि<BR>Uṇ. 2. 101; अरणिः अग्नेर्योनिः] A piece of<BR>wood (of the Śamī tree) used for<BR>kindling the sacred fire by<BR>attrition, the fire-producing wooden<BR>stick; cf. Pt. 1. 216.<BR>--णी (dual)<BR>The two pieces of wood used<BR>in kindling the sacred fire.<BR>--णिः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 Flint.<BR>--4 N. of several fire-producing<BR>plants, particularly अग्निमंथ.<BR>--णिः f.<BR>1 A path, way.<BR>--2 Ved.<BR>Stinginess.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केतुः = अग्निमंथ<BR>Premna Intergrifolia.<BR>--सुतः N. of<BR>Śuka, a celebrated sage (born from the<BR>seed of Vyāsa fallen upon an Araṇi<BR>at the sight of the nymph<BR>Ghṛtāchī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरणिमत्|अरणिमन्त्
अरणिमत् a. Related to the two<BR>Araṇis; to be produced by them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यं|अरण्य|अरण्यः
अरण्यं (sometimes m. also,) [अर्यते<BR>गम्यते शेषे वयसि ऋ-अन्यच्चनित्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 102] A land neither cultivated nor<BR>grazed, a wilderness, forest, desert;<BR>प्रियानाशे कृत्स्नं किल जगदरण्यं हि भवति<BR>U. 6. 30; माता यस्य गृहे नास्ति भार्या<BR>चाप्रियवादिनी । अरण्यं तेन गंतव्यं यथारण्यं<BR>तथा गृहं । Chāṇ. 44; oft. used as<BR>first member of comp. in the sense<BR>of ‘wild’, ‘grown or produced in<BR>forest;’ ˚बीजं wild seed; ˚कार्पासी,<BR>˚कुलत्थिका; ˚कुसुंभः &c; so ˚मार्जार, ˚मूषकः.<BR>--ण्यः N. of a plant कट्फल.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्यक्षः headman or<BR>superintendent of a forest district; forest<BR>keeper or ranger.<BR>--अयनं, --यानं going<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-b" target="_blank">Page0159-b+ 58</a>]<BR>into the forest, becoming a hermit;<BR>अथ यदरण्यायनमित्याचक्षते ब्रह्मचर्यमेव तद्<BR>Ch. Up.<BR>--ओकस्, --सद् a. {1} dwelling<BR>in woods, being in a forest; किंतु<BR>˚सदोवयं अनभ्यस्तरथचर्याः U. 5; वैक्लव्यं<BR>मम तावदीदृशमपि स्नेहादरण्यौकसः Ś. 4. 5.<BR>{2} especially, one who has left his<BR>family and become an anchorite,<BR>forest-dweller.<BR>--कणा wild cumin<BR>seed.<BR>--कदली wild plantain.<BR>--कांडं<BR>N. of the third book of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa which embodies Rāmā's exploits<BR>in the course of his journey through<BR>the forests in company with<BR>Viśvāmitra.<BR>--गजः a wild elephant<BR>(not tamed).<BR>--गानं N. of one of<BR>the four hymn-books of the<BR>Śāmaveda (to be chanted in the forest).<BR>--चटकः a wild sparrow.<BR>--चंद्रिका<BR>(lit.) moonlight in a forest; (fig.)<BR>an ornament or decoration which is<BR>useless, or does not serve its purpose;<BR>just as moonlight in a forest is<BR>useless there being no human beings<BR>to view, enjoy and appreciate it, so<BR>is decoration when not viewed and<BR>appreciated by those for whom it is<BR>intended; thus Malli. on स्त्रीणां<BR>प्रियालोकफलो हि वेषः Ku. 7. 22 remarks:<BR>अन्यथाऽरण्यचंद्रिका स्यादिति भावः.<BR>--चर<BR>(˚ण्येचर also),<BR>--जीव. a. wild,<BR>living in woods.<BR>--ज a. wild;<BR>˚आर्द्रका wild ginger.<BR>--जीरं wild cumin.<BR>--दमनः N. of the plant called dona.<BR>--द्वादशी, --व्रतं N. of a ceremony<BR>performed on the 12th day of<BR>MārgaŚīrṣa.<BR>--धर्मः {1} wild state or usage,<BR>wild nature; तथारण्यधर्माद्वियोज्य<BR>ग्राम्यधर्मे नियोजितः Pt. 1. {2} the duties<BR>of a Vānaprastha or anchorite.<BR>--धान्यं, --शालिः wild rice (नीवार).<BR>--नृपतिः, --राज् (ट्),<BR>--राजः ‘lord of the<BR>woods’, epithet of a lion or a tiger;<BR>so अरण्यानां पतिः.<BR>--पंडितः [अरण्ये<BR>एव पंडितः, नतु नगरादिषु जनसमाजेषु] ‘wise<BR>in a forest’; (fig.) a foolish person<BR>(who can display his learning only<BR>in a forest where no one will hear<BR>him and correct his errors).<BR>--भव<BR>a. growing in a forest, wild;<BR>यथा˚वास्तिलाः Pt. 2. 86.<BR>--मक्षिका a gadfly.<BR>--मूद्गकः a kind of wild bean.<BR>--यानं<BR>retiring to the woods.<BR>--रक्षकः<BR>conservator of forests, forest-keeper.<BR>--राज्यं<BR>sovereignty of the woods.<BR>--रुदितं<BR>(˚ण्ये˚) ‘weeping in a forest’, a cry in<BR>the wilderness; (fig.) a vain or<BR>useless speech, or a cry with no one to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-c" target="_blank">Page0159-c+ 57</a>]<BR>heed it, or any thing done to no<BR>purpose; अरण्ये मया रुदितं Ś. 2; प्रोक्तं<BR>श्रद्धाविहीनस्य अरण्यरुदितोपमं<BR>Pt. 1. 393; तदलमधुनारण्यरुदितैः Amaru. 76.<BR>--वायसः a wild crow, raven.<BR>--वासः, --समाश्रयः {1} retiring into woods,<BR>residence in a forest; ˚योन्मुखं पितरं<BR>R. 8. 12. {2} a hermitage, forest<BR>habitation.<BR>--वासिन् a. living in a forest,<BR>wild. (--m.) a forest-dweller, an<BR>anchorite.<BR>--(नी) N. of a plant<BR>अत्यम्लपर्णी.<BR>--वास्तु (स्तू) कः N. of a plant.<BR>वनवेतः.<BR>--विलपितं, --विलापः (˚ण्ये˚) =<BR>˚रुदितं above.<BR>--श्वन् m. ‘a wild hound’,<BR>wolf.<BR>--पष्ठी N. of a festival<BR>celebrated on the 6th day of the bright halt<BR>of Jyeṣṭha.<BR>--सभा a forest-court.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यकं|अरण्यक
अरण्यकं<BR>1 Forest-court.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानिः|अरण्यानि
अरण्यानिः --नी f. [अरण्य-आनुक्,<BR>ङीप् च; P. IV. 1. 49; हिमारण्ययोर्महत्त्वे]<BR>1<BR>A large forest or desert, vast<BR>wilderness; यथारण्यान्यामुत्साश्चरंतः Śat. Br.<BR>--2 The spirit or presiding deity of<BR>the woods and mother of wild<BR>animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यानी
अरण्यानिः --नी f. [अरण्य-आनुक्,<BR>ङीप् च; P. IV. 1. 49; हिमारण्ययोर्महत्त्वे]<BR>1<BR>A large forest or desert, vast<BR>wilderness; यथारण्यान्यामुत्साश्चरंतः Śat. Br.<BR>--2 The spirit or presiding deity of<BR>the woods and mother of wild<BR>animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्यीय
अरण्यीय a.<BR>1 Containing a forest.<BR>--2 Near a forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्येनूच्यः|अरण्येनूच्य
अरण्येऽनूच्यः (scil. पुरोडाश)<BR>1 A<BR>kind of oblation (अरण्ये अनूच्याः<BR>पठनीयाः मंत्रा यस्य).<BR>--2 N. of a Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरण्येतिलकः|अरण्येतिलक
अरण्येतिलकः (P. II. 1. 44) Wild<BR>sesamum yielding no oil; (fig.) any<BR>thing which does not answer to<BR>one's expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत
अरत a.<BR>1 Dull, languid,<BR>apathetic.<BR>--2 Dissatisfied, discontented,<BR>averse to.<BR>--तं Non-copulation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--त्रप a. not ashamed of<BR>copulation.<BR>--(पः) a dog (as<BR>copulating even in the streets without<BR>shame).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरति|अरतिः
अरति a.<BR>1 Dissatisfied,<BR>discontented.<BR>--2 Dull, languid, restless.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1 Absence of pleasure or<BR>amusement, regarded as arising<BR>from the longings of love;<BR>स्वाभीष्टवस्त्वलाभेन चेतसो याऽनवस्थितिः । अरतिः<BR>सा S. D.; one of the ten states of<BR>love-lorn persons (अनंगदशा).<BR>--2<BR>Pain, distress; Ki. 10. 49.<BR>--3<BR>Anxiety, regret, uneasiness, agitation;<BR>संधत्ते भृशमरतिं हि सद्वियोगः Ki. 5. 51.<BR>--4 Dissatisfaction, discontent.<BR>--5<BR>Languor, dulness.<BR>--6 A bilious<BR>disease.<BR>--तिः [ऋ-अति]<BR>1 Anger,<BR>passion.<BR>--2 Ved. Going, moving<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">Page0160-a+ 56</a>]<BR>quickly.<BR>--3 Moving flame.<BR>--4<BR>Occupying, attacking.<BR>--5 Servant,<BR>manager, assistant.<BR>--6 A master.<BR>--7<BR>An intelligent being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्निः|अरत्नि
अरत्निः (m. or f.) [ऋ-कत्नि रत्निः<BR>स नास्ति यत्र]<BR>1 The elbow; sometimes<BR>the fist itself.<BR>--2 A cubit of the<BR>middle length, from the elbow to<BR>the tip of the little finger, an ell;<BR>अरत्निस्तु निष्कनिष्ठेन मुष्टिना Ak.;<BR>मध्यांगुलीकूर्परयोर्मध्ये प्रामाणिकः करः ।<BR>बद्धमुष्टिकरो रत्निररत्निः सकनिष्ठिकः ॥ Halāy.;<BR>Ki. 18. 6.<BR>--3 The arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरत्निकः|अरत्निक
अरत्निकः The elbow; Y. 3. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरथिन्
अरथिन् a. One who does not<BR>fight in a car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरथीः
अरथीः Ved. Not a charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरद
अरद a.<BR>1 Toothless (as a child).<BR>--2 Whose teeth are broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरध्र
अरध्र a. Ved.<BR>1 Not lazy, not to<BR>be subdued, invincible.<BR>--2<BR>Prosperous (समृद्ध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंधनं|अरन्धन|अरन्धनं
अरंधनं Absense of cooking (as<BR>on सिंह and कन्या संक्रांत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरपस्
अरपस् a. Ved.<BR>1 Unhurt, safe.<BR>(also अरप); sinless, pure.<BR>--2 Not<BR>hurting, sound; salutary,<BR>beneficial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरपचनः|अरपचन
अरपचनः A mystical collective<BR>name of the 5 Buddhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरं|अर|अरः
अरं ind. Ved. [ऋ-अम्]<BR>1 Swiftly,<BR>near, at hand, present.<BR>--2 Readily,<BR>fitly, suitably, so as to answer some<BR>purpose.<BR>--3 Enough, sufficiently<BR>(cf. अलं); excessively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंकृ|अरङ्कृ
अरंकृ To prepare, make ready,<BR>serve; ˚कृत् gratifying, decorating,<BR>adorning, serving as a worshipper;<BR>˚कृतिः decorating, gratification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंगम्|अरङ्गम्
अरंगम् To be present, come or go<BR>near (to help); become visible,<BR>appear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंगमः|अरङ्गम|अरंगम
अरंगमः Coming near or into the<BR>presence, becoming visible, being<BR>present to help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंगरः|अरङ्गर|अरंगर
अरंगरः<BR>1 Praising readily.<BR>--2<BR>Factitious or made up poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरंघुष|अरङ्घुष
अरंघुष a. Praising readily,<BR>sounding aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरम|अरमः
अरम a. Low, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमणस्
अरमणस् a. Ved.<BR>1 Hostile.<BR>--2<BR>Obedient, devoted to the worship of<BR>God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमति|अरमतिः
अरमति a. Not resting, active,<BR>going everywhere.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1<BR>Splendour.<BR>--2 Readiness to serve,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">Page0160-b+ 55</a>]<BR>obedience, devotion to God; hence<BR>personified in the Vedas as a Goddess<BR>protecting the worshippers of the<BR>gods and pious works in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमिष्
अरमिष् a. Ved. Going near<BR>quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरमण
अरमण, अरममाण a.<BR>1 Not<BR>pleasing or gratifying, disagreeable,<BR>unpleasant.<BR>--2 Unceasing, incessant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरममाण
अरमण, अरममाण a.<BR>1 Not<BR>pleasing or gratifying, disagreeable,<BR>unpleasant.<BR>--2 Unceasing, incessant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररं|अरर|अररः
अररं [ऋ-अरन्; अरश्चित् स्यात्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 132]<BR>1 The leaf or panel of a door<BR>(कपाटं), सरभसमरराणि द्रागपावृत्य<BR>Mv. 6. 27 (--रः, --री also);<BR>चंचूकोटिविपाटिताररपुटो यास्याम्यहं पंजरात् Bv. 1. 58.<BR>--2<BR>A door.<BR>--3 The sheath of a bamboo<BR>shoot (करीरकोष).<BR>--4 A covering or<BR>sheath in general.<BR>--रः<BR>1 An awl.<BR>--2 A<BR>part of a sacrifice.<BR>--3 War, fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररिः|अररि
अररिः The leaf of a door; a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररिंदं|अररिन्द
अररिंदं^1 Ved. Water(अररिं<BR>पिपासोपशमं ददाति).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: missing anusvAra. cf. MW ararinda (n.) and AP, who has quotation..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररिवस्
अररिवस् m. f.<BR>1 Not giving<BR>or offering.<BR>--2 Hard, unfriendly,<BR>envious, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररु|अररुः
अररु a. Ved.<BR>1 Moving(<BR>गमनस्वभाव).<BR>--2 = अररिवस् above.<BR>--रुः [अर्तेः<BR>अरुः Uṇ. 4. 79].<BR>1 An enemy.<BR>--2<BR>A weapon<BR>--3 N. of an Asura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अररे
अररे ind. A vocative particle<BR>expressive of (1) great haste; (2)<BR>contempt or disdain; अररे महाराजं<BR>प्रति कुतः क्षत्रियाः G. M.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरर्यति
अरर्यति Den. P.<BR>1 To work<BR>with an awl.<BR>--2 To try, put to the<BR>test.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविंदं|अरविन्द|अरविन्दं|अरविन्दः
अरविंदं [अरान् चक्रांगानीव पत्राणि<BR>विंदते विंद् श P. III. 1. 138 Vārt.]<BR>1<BR>A lotus (it is one of the 5 arrows<BR>of Cupid; see under पंचबाण);<BR>शक्यमरविंदसुरभिः Ś. 3. 7. It is a sun<BR>lotus; cf. सूर्यांशुभिर्भिन्नमिवारविंदं<BR>Ku. 1. 32; स्थल˚, चरण˚, मुख˚ &c.<BR>--2<BR>Also a red or blue lotus.<BR>--दः<BR>1 The<BR>(Indian) crane.<BR>--2 Copper.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a. lotus-eyed, an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--दलप्रभं copper.<BR>--नाभिः,<BR>--भः N. of Viṣṇu, from whose navel<BR>sprang the lotus which supported<BR>Brahmā; हृदये मदीये देवश्चकास्तु<BR>भगवानरविंदनाभः Bv. 4. 8.<BR>--सद् m. N.<BR>of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरविंदिनी|अरविन्दिनी
अरविंदिनी<BR>1 A lotus plant;<BR>प्रपीतमधुका भृंगैः सुदिवेवारविंदिनी Bk. 5. 70.<BR>--2<BR>An assemblage of lotus flowers.<BR>--3<BR>A place abounding in lotus flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरस|अरसः
अरस a.<BR>1 Sapless, not juicy,<BR>tasteless, insipid.<BR>--2 Dull, flat.<BR>--3<BR>Weak, having no strength,<BR>inefficacious.<BR>--सः No juice, absence of<BR>juice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशः {1} eating sapless<BR>food. {2} maceration of the body.<BR>--आशिन् a. {1} eating sapless food.<BR>{2} macerating the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरसिक|अरसिकः
अरसिक a.<BR>1 Devoid of taste,<BR>sapless, insipid, flavourless (of a<BR>thing).<BR>--2 Void of feeling or taste,<BR>dull, unfeeling, inappreciative,<BR>insensible to the charms (of poetry<BR>&c.); अरसिकेषु कवित्वनिवेदनं शिरसि मा<BR>लिख मा लिख मा लिख Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहस्
अरहस् n. Absence of secrecy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरहायते
अरहायते Den. A. To become known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराग
अराग, अरागिन् a. Cool,<BR>dispassionate; तमहमरागमकृष्णं कृष्णद्वैपायनं<BR>वंदे Ve. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरागिन्
अराग, अरागिन् a. Cool,<BR>dispassionate; तमहमरागमकृष्णं कृष्णद्वैपायनं<BR>वंदे Ve. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजक|अराजकः
अराजक a. Having no king,<BR>anarchical; नाराजके जनपदे Rām.;<BR>Ms. 7. 3; अराजके जीवलोके दुर्बला वलवत्तरैः ।<BR>पीड्यंते न हि वित्तेषु प्रभुत्वं कस्यचित्तदा ॥<BR>Mb.; शोच्यं राज्यमराजकं Chāṇ. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजन्
अराजन् m. Not a king.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भोगीन a. not fit for the use of<BR>a king.<BR>--स्थापित a. not established<BR>by a king, illegal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराजिन्
अराजिन् a. Ved. Unchecked,<BR>unrestrained, or without splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराटकी
अराटकी Ved. N. of the plant<BR>अजशृंगी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातिः|अराति
अरातिः [न राति ददाति सुखं, रा-क,<BR>न. त.]<BR>1 An enemy, foe; देशः<BR>सोयमरातिशोणितजलैर्यस्मिन्ह्रदाः पूरिताः Ve. 3. 31;<BR>(in the Veda) non-offering (of<BR>sacrifices), stinginess, hardness,<BR>malignity, malevolence, failure or<BR>adversity; malignity personified; evil<BR>spirit whose aim it was to defeat<BR>the good intentions and disturb<BR>the happiness of man (used in f.).<BR>--2 The number six.<BR>--3 The sixth<BR>position (in astronomy).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दूषण, --दूषि, --ह a. Ved. destroying<BR>adversities or enemies.<BR>--भंगः<BR>destruction of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातियति
अराति(ती)यति Den. P. Ved. To<BR>desire not to offer; to act like an<BR>enemy, act maliciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीयति
अराति(ती)यति Den. P. Ved. To<BR>desire not to offer; to act like an<BR>enemy, act maliciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीयत्
अरातीयत् a. Not offering,<BR>unfriendly, malicious, acting like an<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीयु
अरातीयु a. Ved. Not accustomed<BR>to offer; inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरातीवन्
अरातीवन् a. Not offering;<BR>unfriendly, malicious, hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराद्धिः|अराद्धि
अराद्धिः f. Transgression, sin,<BR>offence; envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराधस्
अराधस् a. [राधः; धनं- Nir. न. ब.]<BR>Poor, not able to perform sacrifices,<BR>stingy; hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराय|अरायः
अराय a. [नास्ति राधनं यस्य वेदे<BR>षच्समासः]<BR>1 Devoid of wealth, without<BR>sacrificial gifts.<BR>--2 Stingy,<BR>niggardly.<BR>--यः, --यी Any malignant or evil<BR>spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराल|अरालं|अरालः
अराल a. [ऋ-विच् अरं आलाति,<BR>लाक] Spreading like the spokes of<BR>a wheel, curved, crooked;<BR>पादावरालांगुली M. 2. 3.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A bent or<BR>crooked arm.<BR>--2 The resin of the<BR>plant Shorea Robusta (सर्जरस).<BR>--3 An elephant in rut.<BR>--ला<BR>1 An<BR>unchaste woman, harlot, courtezan.<BR>--2 A modest woman (अधृष्टा).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केशी a woman with curled<BR>hair; भित्त्वा निराक्रामदरालकेश्याः<BR>R. 6. 81.<BR>--पक्ष्मन् a. having curved<BR>eyelashes; Ku. 5. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरावन्
अरावन् a. Ved. Not offering<BR>malignant, epithet of evil spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अराष्ट्रं|अराष्ट्र
अराष्ट्रं Loss of royal power or<BR>sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरि|अरिः
अरि a. [ऋ-इन्] Moving, going,<BR>reaching; obtaining, aspiring,<BR>devoted to, zealous (Ved.).<BR>--रिः<BR>1 An<BR>enemy, foe (cf. Uṇ. 4. 138); (used<BR>in the Veda like an adjective in<BR>the sense of ‘ungenerous’,<BR>‘malicious’, ‘not worshipping or devoted,’<BR>‘hostile’); विजितारिपुरःसरः R. 1. 59, 61;<BR>4. 4.<BR>--2 An enemy of mankind<BR>(said of the six feelings which<BR>disturb man's mind); कामः<BR>क्रोधस्तथा लोभो मदमोहौ च मत्सरः;<BR>कृतारिषड्वर्गजयेन Ki. 1. 9.<BR>--3 A species of खदिर<BR>or Mimosa (विट्खदिर).<BR>--4 N. of the<BR>number six (from the six enemies).<BR>--5 N. of a condition in astronomy.<BR>--6 Any part of a carriage.<BR>--7 A<BR>wheel.<BR>--8 A lord, master.<BR>--9 The<BR>wind.<BR>--10 A pious or religious<BR>man.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्षण a. tamer or<BR>subduer of enemies.<BR>--कुलं {1} a host<BR>of enemies. {2} an enemy.<BR>--गूर्त a.<BR>Ved. ready for the destruction of<BR>enemies; praised by devoted men<BR>or worshippers.<BR>--घ्नः destroyer of<BR>enemies.<BR>--चिंतनं, --चिंता schemes<BR>directed against enemies;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">Page0161-b+ 55</a>]<BR>administration of foreign affairs.<BR>--त्र a.<BR>protecting from enemies.<BR>--धायस् a.<BR>possessed by lords only (i. e. very<BR>precious).<BR>--नंदन a. ‘an enemy's joy’,<BR>affording triumph to an enemy.<BR>--निपातः invasion made by enemies.<BR>--भद्रः the foremost or most<BR>powerful enemy; R. 14. 31.<BR>--मर्दः<BR>‘crushing enemies’ N. of a plant (काममर्द).<BR>--मर्दन a. crushing or trampling foes,<BR>destroying enemies.<BR>--मेदः N. of a<BR>tree (विट्खदिर); N. of a country;<BR>Bṛ. S. 14. 2.<BR>--मेदकः N. of an<BR>insect bred in excrement.<BR>--स्थानकं<BR>consternation, defeat.<BR>--सूदनः, --हन्,<BR>--हिंसकः destroyer of enemies; R. 9. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिंदम|अरिन्दम|अरिन्दमः
अरिंदम a. [अरीन् दाम्यति दमयति वा;<BR>खच् मुम्च] Subduer of enemies,<BR>victorious, conquering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थभाज्
अरिक्थभाज्, अरिक्थीय a. Not<BR>entitled to a share in the ancestral<BR>property (as an heir incapacitated<BR>by impotence &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिक्थीय
अरिक्थभाज्, अरिक्थीय a. Not<BR>entitled to a share in the ancestral<BR>property (as an heir incapacitated<BR>by impotence &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिणिन्
अरिणिन् m. A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरितृ
अरितृ [ऋ-तृच्-इडागमः] A<BR>rower, helmsman (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरित्र|अरित्रं|अरित्रः
अरित्र a. [गच्छत्यनेन; ऋ-इत्र<BR>P. III. 2. 184] Ved.<BR>1 Propelling, urging<BR>onwards.<BR>--2 Protecting on all sides.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1 An oar; लोलैररित्रैश्चरणैरिवाभितः<BR>Śi. 12. 71.<BR>--2 A rudder, helm.<BR>--3<BR>A ship, boat.<BR>--4 A part of a<BR>carriage.<BR>--5 A Soma vessel.<BR>--त्रः A<BR>Soma vessel. [cf. L. aratrum; Gr.<BR>eretmos].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गाध a.<BR>‘oardeep,’ shallow (water).<BR>--परण a.<BR>Ved. crossing by means of oars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिन्
अरिन् n. (रि) A wheel; discus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिप्र
अरिप्र a. [रिप्रं पापनाम Nir.,<BR>तन्नास्ति यस्य] Ved. Sinless, spotless,<BR>blameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिफित
अरिफित a. Not changed to र्<BR>(said of the Visarga).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषं|अरिष|अरिषः
अरिषं [न रिष्यते विच्छिद्यते] A<BR>continuous downpour of rain.<BR>--षः A<BR>sort of disease in the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषण्य
अरिषण्य a. Ved. Not harming<BR>or injuring, inoffensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिषण्यत्|अरिषण्यन्त्
अरिषण्यत् a. Ved. Not being hurt<BR>or injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्ट|अरिष्टं|अरिष्टः
अरिष्ट a. Unhurt; perfect,<BR>complete; imperishable, undecaying,<BR>secure, safe; अरिष्टं गच्छ पंथानं,<BR>अरिष्टं मार्गमातिष्ठत् पुण्यं वा तु निषेवितं Rām.<BR>--ष्टः<BR>1 A heron (कंक).<BR>--2 A raven,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-c" target="_blank">Page0161-c+ 58</a>]<BR>crow.<BR>--3 An enemy; अरिष्टस्त्वाष्ट्रस्य<BR>Mv. 4. 18.<BR>--4 N. of various plants:<BR>(a) the soap-berry tree (Mar. रिठा);<BR>(b) another plant (Mar. निंब).<BR>--5<BR>Garlic.<BR>--6 A distilled mixture.<BR>--7 N. of<BR>a demon killed by Kṛṣṇa; a son<BR>of Bali.<BR>--ष्टा<BR>1 A bandage.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>a medical plant (कटुका).<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>daughter of Dakṣa and one of the<BR>wives of Kaśyapa.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 Bad or<BR>ill luck, evil, misfortune, calamity.<BR>--2 A portentous phenomenon<BR>foreboding misfortune, unlucky omen<BR>(such as earthquake).<BR>--3<BR>Unfavourable symptom, especially of<BR>approaching death; रोगिणो मरणं यस्मादवश्यं<BR>भावि लक्ष्यते । तल्लक्षणमरिष्टं<BR>स्याद्रिष्टमप्यभिधीयते ॥<BR>--4 Good fortune or luck,<BR>happiness.<BR>--5 The lying-in-chamber,<BR>delivery-room, women's apartments<BR>(अंतःपुरं); अपस्नात इवरिष्टं प्रविवेश<BR>गृहोत्तमं Rām.<BR>--6 Butter-milk.<BR>--7<BR>Spirituous liquor; Śi. 18. 77.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--असु a. Ved. having one's life unhurt.<BR>--गातु a. Ved. dwelling securely.<BR>--गृहं<BR>the lying-in-chamber.<BR>--ग्राम a. Ved.<BR>of undivided group, having a<BR>complete troop.<BR>--ताति a. Ved. making<BR>fortune or happy, auspicious. (--तिः f.)<BR>safeness, security, succession of<BR>good fortune, continuous happiness<BR>(अरिष्टं करोतीति ˚तातिः; अरिष्टस्य भावो वा<BR>P. IV. 4. 143-4Sk.); तदत्रभवता निष्पन्नाशिषां<BR>काममरिष्टतातिमाशास्महे Mv. 1.<BR>--दुष्टधी<BR>a. apprehensive of death, alarmed<BR>at the approach of death.<BR>--पुरं N. of a<BR>place; cf. अरिष्टाश्रितपुरं P. VI. 2. 100.<BR>--भर्मन् a. granting security.<BR>--मथनः<BR>N. of Śiva or Viṣṇu.<BR>--शय्या a<BR>lyingin couch; अरिष्टशय्यां परितो विसारिणा<BR>R. 3. 15.<BR>--सूदनः, --हन् m. killer of<BR>Ariṣṭa, epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टकः|अरिष्टक
अरिष्टकः = अरिष्टः The soap-berry tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्टिः|अरिष्टि
अरिष्टिः f. Security; safety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरिष्यत्|अरिष्यन्त्
अरिष्यत् a. Not hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरीळ्ह
अरीळ्ह a. (= अरीढ) Ved. Not<BR>licked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुः|अरु
अरुः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>plant (रक्तखदिर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुंषिका
अरुंषिका [अरूंषि मर्मस्थानान्यधिकृत्य<BR>जाता] Scab on the head (Mar. खवडे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुच्
अरुच् a. Ved. Lightless, dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचिः|अरुचि
अरुचिः f.<BR>1 Aversion, dislike in<BR>general; क्व सा भोगानामुपर्यरुचिः<BR>K. 146.<BR>--2 Want of appetite, disrelish,<BR>disgust;<BR>सन्निपातक्षयश्वासकासहिक्कारुचिप्रणुत् Suśr.<BR>--3 Absence of a<BR>satisfactory explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुचिर
अरुचिर, अरुच्य a. Disagreeable,<BR>disgusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुच्य
अरुचिर, अरुच्य a. Disagreeable,<BR>disgusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुज्
अरुज् a.<BR>1 Free from disease,<BR>sound, healthy.<BR>--2 Not festering<BR>(as a boil).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुग्ण
अरुग्ण a. Not broken, not<BR>diseased, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुज|अरुजः
अरुज a.<BR>1 Sound, healthy;<BR>यावत्स्वस्थमिदं शरीरमरुजं Bh. 3. 88. v. l.<BR>--2 Not breaking, not suppurating.<BR>--जः N. of a plant (आरग्वध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुण|अरुणं|अरुणः
अरुण a. (णा, --णी f.) [ऋ-उनन्; cf.<BR>Uṇ. 3. 60]<BR>1 Reddish brown, tawny,<BR>red, ruddy (of the colour of the<BR>morning as opposed to the darkness<BR>of night); प्रत्याख्यातविशेषकं कुरबकं<BR>श्यामावदातारुणं M. 3. 5;<BR>नयनान्यरुणानि घूर्णयन् Ku. 4. 12.<BR>--2 Perplexed,<BR>embarrassed.<BR>--3 Dumb.<BR>--णः<BR>1 Red<BR>colour, the colour of the dawn or<BR>morning twilight.<BR>--2 The dawn<BR>personified as the charioteer of the sun;<BR>आविष्कृतारुणपुरःसर एकतोर्कः Ś. 4. 1,<BR>7. 4; विभावरी यद्यरुणाय कल्पते<BR>Ku. 5. 44; R. 5. 71. [Aruṇa is represented as<BR>the elder brother of Garuḍa, being the<BR>son of Vinatā by Kaśyapa. Vinatā<BR>prematurely hatched the egg and the child<BR>was born without thighs, and hence he is<BR>called Anūru ‘thighless’, or Vipāda<BR>‘footless.’ He cursed his mother that since she<BR>had brought him forth before the due<BR>season she would be a slave to her rival<BR>Kadrū; but at her earnest entreaties, he<BR>modified the curse and said that her next<BR>son would deliver her from bondage.<BR>Aruṇa now holds the office of the<BR>charioteer of the sun. His wife was Śyenī, who<BR>bore him two sons Sampāti and Jaṭāyu].<BR>--3 The sun; रागेण बालारुणकोमलेन<BR>Ku. 3. 30, 5. 8; संसृज्यते<BR>सरसिजैररुणांशुभिन्नैः R. 5. 69; Ś. 1. 32.<BR>--4<BR>A kind of leprosy with red spots<BR>and insensibility of the skin.<BR>--5<BR>A little poisonous creature.<BR>--6 N.<BR>of a plant पुंनाग; also a synonym<BR>of अर्क q. v.<BR>--7 Molasses (गुड)<BR>--8<BR>N. of a peak of the Himālaya<BR>situated to the west of Kailāsa.<BR>--9<BR>N. of one of the 12 Ādityas,<BR>the one presiding over Māgha.<BR>--णा<BR>1 N. of several plants (a)<BR>अतिविषा (Mar. अतिविख); (b)<BR>Madder (मंजिष्ठा); (c) त्रिवृत् commonly<BR>called Teori; (d) a black kind of<BR>the same (श्यामाका); (e) bitter<BR>apple (इंद्रवारुणी); (f) the Guñja<BR>plant that yields the red and black<BR>berry (गुंज) used as a weight by<BR>jewellers &c. (g) मुंडतिक्ता.<BR>--2 N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-b" target="_blank">Page0162-b+ 57</a>]<BR>of a river.<BR>--णी<BR>1 A red cow (Nir.).<BR>--2 The early dawn.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Red<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Gold.<BR>--3 Saffron.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रजः N. of Garuḍa (अरुणः<BR>अग्रजो यस्य).<BR>--अनुजः, --अवरजः N. of<BR>Garuḍa, younger brother of Aruṇa.<BR>--अर्चिस् m. the sun.<BR>--अश्व a. having<BR>red horses, epithet of the Maruts.<BR>--आत्मजः {1} son of Aruṇa, N. of<BR>Jaṭāyu. {2} N. of Saturn, Sāvarṇi<BR>Manu, Karṇa, Sugrīva, Yama and<BR>the two Aśvins.<BR>--(जा) N. of<BR>Yamunā and Tāptī.<BR>--ईक्षण a. red-eyed.<BR>--उदकं N. of a lake.<BR>--(का) N. of<BR>a river.<BR>--उदयः break of day, dawn;<BR>चतस्रो घटिकाः प्रातररुणोदय उच्यते.<BR>--उपलः a ruby.<BR>--कमलं a red lotus.<BR>--ज्योतिस् m. N. of Śiva.<BR>--दूर्वा<BR>reddish fennel.<BR>--प्रिय a.<BR>‘beloved of red flowers and lotuses’,<BR>N. of the sun.<BR>--(या) {1} the sun's<BR>wife. {2} shadow.<BR>--प्सु a. [अरुणं प्सु<BR>रूपं यस्य] Ved. of reddish shape or<BR>colour.<BR>--बभ्रु a. reddish-yellow.<BR>--युज् a. furnished with red rays of<BR>light, epithet of the dawn.<BR>--लोचन<BR>a. red-eyed.<BR>--(नः) a pigeon.<BR>--सारथिः<BR>‘having Aruṇa for his charioteer,’<BR>the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणित
अरुणित, अरुणीकृत a. Reddened,<BR>dyed red, impurpled;<BR>स्तनांगरागारुणिताच्च कंदुकात् Ku. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणीकृत
अरुणित, अरुणीकृत a. Reddened,<BR>dyed red, impurpled;<BR>स्तनांगरागारुणिताच्च कंदुकात् Ku. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणिमन्
अरुणिमन् m., अरुणता Redness,<BR>red colour; अरुणिम्ना पिहितोपि<BR>शुक्लभावः Bv. 2. 180.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणीयः|अरुणीय
अरुणीयः, --˚योगः The 25th<BR>Upanishad of the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुणीययोगः
अरुणीयः, --˚योगः The 25th<BR>Upanishad of the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुत
अरुत a. Ved. Not to be broken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुंतुद|अरुन्तुद|अरुन्तुदः
अरुंतुद a. [अरूंषि मर्माणि तुदति;<BR>अरुस्-तुद्, खश् मुमागमश्च P. III. 2. 35;<BR>VI. 3. 67]<BR>1 Cutting or wounding<BR>the vital parts, inflicting wounds,<BR>corrosive, painful, sharp (fig. also);<BR>caustic; अरुंतुदमिवालानमनिर्वाणस्य<BR>दंतिनः R. 1. 71; Ki. 14. 55;<BR>Śi. 2. 109.<BR>--2 Acrimonious, sour<BR>(disposition); Ms. 2. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुंधती|अरुन्धती
अरुंधती [न रुंधती प्रतिरोधकारिणी]<BR>1<BR>A medicinal climbing plant.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>the wife of Vasiṣṭha;<BR>अन्वासितमरुंधत्या स्वाहयेव हविर्भुजं R. 1. 56.<BR>--3 The<BR>morning star personified as the<BR>wife of Vasiṣṭha; one of the<BR>Pleiades.<BR>--4 N. of the daughter of<BR>प्राचेतसदक्ष, one of the 10 wives of<BR>Dharma. [In mythology Arundhatī<BR>is represented as the wife of the sage<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">Page0162-c+ 59</a>]<BR>Vasiṣṭha, one of the 7 sages. She was<BR>one of the 9 daughters of Kardama<BR>Prajāpati by Devahūti. She is regarded as<BR>the highest pattern of conjugal<BR>excellence and wifely devotion and is so<BR>invoked by the bridegroom at nuptial<BR>ceremonies. Though a woman she was<BR>regarded with the same-even<BR>more-veneration as the Saptarṣis; cf. Ku. 6. 12:<BR>तामगौरवभेदेन मुनींश्चापश्यदीश्वरः । स्त्री<BR>पुमानित्यनास्थैषा वृत्तं हि महितं सताम् ॥ cf. also<BR>Janaka's remarks in. U. 4. 10. She, like<BR>her husband, was the guide and<BR>controller of Raghu's line in her own<BR>department, and acted as guardian angel to<BR>Sītā after she had been abandoned by<BR>Rāma. It is said that Arundhatī (the<BR>star) is not seen by persons whose<BR>end has approached: cf. Suśruta:<BR>न पश्यति सनक्षत्रां यस्तु देवीमरुंधतीं ।<BR>ध्रुवमाकाशगंगां च तं वदंति गतायुषं ॥; see<BR>H. 1. 76 also].<BR>--5 The tongue (personified).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जातिः, --नाथः, --पतिः N. of<BR>Vasiṣṭha, one of the seven Ṛṣis<BR>or stars in the Ursa Major<BR>--दर्शनन्यायः see under न्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्
अरुष् --ष्ट a. Not angry, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्ट
अरुष् --ष्ट a. Not angry, calm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष|अरुषं|अरुषः
अरुष a.<BR>1 Not angry.<BR>--2<BR>Shining, bright; reddish.<BR>--3 Unhurt.<BR>--4<BR>Moving, going about (as a horse).<BR>--षः<BR>1 The red horse of Agni; a<BR>flame.<BR>--2 The sun; the day as<BR>presided over by the sun.<BR>--3 The red<BR>storm-cloud.<BR>--षी<BR>1 The dawn.<BR>--2<BR>A flame.<BR>--3 N. of the wife of<BR>Bhṛgu and mother of Aurva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुषति
अरुष(ष्य)ति Den. P. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्यति
अरुष(ष्य)ति Den. P. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुष्कः|अरुष्क
अरुष्कः [अरुर्मर्भस्थानं कायति पीडयति]<BR>N. of a tree (भल्लातक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुस्
अरुस् a. [ऋ-उस् Uṇ. 2. 116]<BR>Wounded, sore. --m.<BR>--(रुः)<BR>1 The Arka<BR>tree.<BR>--2 Red Khadira. --n.<BR>1 A<BR>vital part.<BR>--2 A wound, sore (--m.<BR>also).<BR>--3 An eye.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर<BR>a. [अरुस्-कृ-टः P. III. 2. 21]<BR>causing or inflicting wounds, wounding.<BR>--(रः) N. of a tree अरुष्क q. v.<BR>--(रं)<BR>the nut of this tree.<BR>--कृत a.<BR>wounded, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुसिका
अरुसिका Eruption on the scalp<BR>with acute pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरुहा
अरुहा N. of a plant(भूम्यामलकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूक्ष
अरूक्ष a. Not hard, soft; bland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूक्षित
अरूक्षित, अरूक्ष्ण a. Ved. Soft,<BR>tender, supple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूक्ष्ण
अरूक्षित, अरूक्ष्ण a. Ved. Soft,<BR>tender, supple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूप|अरूपः
अरूप a.<BR>1 Formless, shapeless.<BR>--2 Ugly, deformed.<BR>--3 Dissimilar,<BR>unlike.<BR>--पं<BR>1 A bad or ugly figure.<BR>--2 The Pradhāna of the Sāṃkhyas<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">Page0163-a+ 55</a>]<BR>and Brahma of the Vedāntins.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हार्य a. not to be<BR>attracted or won over by beauty;<BR>अरूपहार्यं मदनस्य निग्रहात् Ku. 5. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपक
अरूपक a. Without any figure<BR>or metaphor, not figurative, literal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपता
अरूपता --त्वं Shapelessness,<BR>deformity, dissimilarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूपत्वं|अरूपत्व
अरूपता --त्वं Shapelessness,<BR>deformity, dissimilarity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरूषः|अरूष
अरूषः [ऋ-ऊषन् Uṇ. 4. 73]<BR>1 The<BR>sun.<BR>--2 A kind of serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरे
अरे ind. An interjection of(a)<BR>calling to inferiors; आत्मा वा<BR>अरेद्रष्टव्यः श्रोतव्यः; न वा अरे पत्युः<BR>कामायास्याः पतिः प्रियो भवति Śat. Br. (said by<BR>Yājñavalkya to his wife Maitreyī);<BR>(b) of anger; अरे महाराजं प्रति कुतः<BR>क्षत्रियाः U. 4; (c) of envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरेणु|अरेणुः
अरेणु a. Not dusty; not soiled<BR>with dust, not touching the dust<BR>(of the earth). --n.<BR>--(णु) What is<BR>not dust, the ether.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरेपस्
अरेपस् a. [नास्ति रेपः पापं यस्य]<BR>1<BR>Sinless, spotless.<BR>--2 Clear, pure,<BR>bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरेरे
अरेरे ind. An interjection of<BR>(a) calling out angrily; अरेरे<BR>दुर्योधनप्रमुखाः कुरुबलसेनाप्रभवः Ve. 3; अरेरे<BR>वाचाट ibid.; or of (b) addressing<BR>inferiors or by way of contempt;<BR>अरेरे राधागर्भभारभूत सूतापसद ibid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोक|अरोकः
अरोक a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Without<BR>holes (अच्छिद्र).<BR>--2 Without<BR>splendour, obscured, dim.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दत्, --दंत<BR>a. [P. V. 4. 144] {1} having black<BR>teeth. {2} having thick-set teeth<BR>(निबिडदंत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोग|अरोगः
अरोग a. Free from disease,<BR>healthy, sound, well; अरोगाः<BR>सर्वसिद्धार्थाश्चतुर्वर्षशतायुषः Suśr.<BR>--गः Sound<BR>health; न नाममात्रेण करोत्यरोगं<BR>H. 1. 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगण
अरोगण a. Ved.<BR>1 Freeing from<BR>disease.<BR>--2 Free from disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोगिन्
अरोगिन्, --अरोग्य a. Healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोग्य
अरोगिन्, --अरोग्य a. Healthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचक|अरोचकः
अरोचक a. (चिका f.)<BR>1 Not<BR>shining or bright.<BR>--2 Causing loss of<BR>appetite, producing loathing or<BR>disgust.<BR>--कः Loss of appetite;<BR>disgust, loathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचकिन्
अरोचकिन् a. Suffering from loss<BR>of appetite or indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचमान
अरोचमान a.<BR>1 Not shining.<BR>--2<BR>Not attached; Ms. 3. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोचिष्णु
अरोचिष्णु a.<BR>1 Not shining,<BR>dark.<BR>--2 Disagreeable, ugly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरोषः|अरोष
अरोषः Absence of anger,<BR>calmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अरौद्र
अरौद्र a. Not terrible or fierce;<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क्
अर्क् {c10c} P. [अर्कयति, अर्कयितुं,<BR>अर्कित]<BR>1 To heat or warm.<BR>--2 To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क|अर्कः|अर्क्क
अर्क a. [अर्च्-घञ्-कुत्वं Uṇ. 3. 40]<BR>Fit to be worshipped (अर्चंनीय).<BR>--र्कः<BR>1 A ray of light, a flash of<BR>lightning (Ved.).<BR>--2 The sun;<BR>आविष्कृतारुणपुरःसर एकतोर्कः Ś. 4. 1.<BR>--3 Fire.<BR>--4 A crystal.<BR>--5 Copper.<BR>--6 Sunday.<BR>--7 Membrum virile.<BR>--8 N.<BR>of the sun-plant, Calatropis<BR>Gigantea (Mar. रुई), a small tree<BR>with medicinal sap and rind;<BR>अर्कस्योपरि शिथिलं च्युतमिव<BR>नवमल्लिकाकुसुमं Ś. 2. 8; यमाश्रित्य न विश्रामं क्षुधार्ता<BR>यांति सेवकाः । सोऽर्कवन्नृपतिस्त्याज्यः<BR>सदापुष्पफलोऽपि सन् Pt. 1. 51.<BR>--9<BR>N. of Indra.<BR>--10 A sort of<BR>religious ceremony.<BR>--11 Praise, hymn;<BR>praising, extolling, song of praise.<BR>--12 A singer (Ved. in these<BR>two senses).<BR>--13 A learned man.<BR>--14 An elder brother.<BR>--15 Food<BR>(अर्कं also).<BR>--16 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--17<BR>A kind of decoction.<BR>--18 The seventh<BR>day of a month.<BR>--19 The उत्तरफल्गुनी<BR>asterism.<BR>--20 The number 12.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः, --कला a digit or 12th part<BR>of the sun's disc.<BR>--अश्मन् m.<BR>--उपलः<BR>{1} the sun-stone, heliotrope, girasol.<BR>{2} a sort of crystal or ruby.<BR>--आह्वः<BR>the swallow wort.<BR>--इंदुसंगमः the<BR>time of conjunction of the sun and<BR>moon (दर्श or अमावास्या).<BR>--कांता {1}<BR>N. of a plant commonly called<BR>हुढुडिया. {2} sun's wife. {3} sun's<BR>shadow.<BR>--क्षेत्रं {1} the field of the sun;<BR>the sign Leo, presided over<BR>by the sun. {2} N. of a holy<BR>place in Orissa.<BR>--चंदनः a kind of<BR>red sandal (रक्तचंदन).<BR>--जः epithet<BR>of Karṇa, Yama, Sugrīva.<BR>--(जौ) the<BR>two Aśvins regarded as the<BR>physicians of Heaven.<BR>--तनयः ‘a son of<BR>the sun’, an epithet of Karṇa, Yama,<BR>Manu Vaivasvata, Manu Sāvarṇi<BR>and Saturn; see अरुणात्मज.<BR>--(या) N.<BR>of the rivers Yamunā and Tāptī.<BR>--त्विष् f. light of the sun.<BR>--दिनं,<BR>--वासरः Sunday.<BR>--दुग्धं milky sap or<BR>exudation of arka.<BR>--नंदनः, --पुत्रः,<BR>--सुतः, --सूनुः N. of Saturn, Karṇa or<BR>Yama.<BR>--नयन a. one whose eyes are<BR>difficult to be gazed at.<BR>--(नः) an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">Page0163-c+ 57</a>]<BR>epithet of Virāj Puruṣa. नामन् m.<BR>the red arka tree.<BR>--पत्रः, --पर्णः N. of<BR>the plant अर्क.<BR>--(त्रा) a kind of<BR>birthwort (सुनंदा, अर्कमूंला) with<BR>wedgeshaped leaves.<BR>--(त्रं, --र्णं) the<BR>leaf of the अर्क plant.<BR>--पादपः N. of<BR>a plant (निंब); another tree (आकंद).<BR>--पुष्पं a flower of arka.<BR>--(ष्पी),<BR>--पुष्पिका N. of a plant (कुटुंबिनी).<BR>--प्रिया N. of a plant (जवा).<BR>--बंधुः,<BR>--बांधवः {1} N. of Buddha Śākyamuni.<BR>{2} a lotus (the sun-lotus).<BR>--भं {1}<BR>an asterism influenced by the sun.<BR>{2} the sign Leo. {3}<BR>उत्तराफल्गुनीनक्षत्र.<BR>--भक्ता = ˚कांता q. v.<BR>--मंडलं the<BR>disc of the sun.<BR>--मूलः, --ला = ˚पत्रा;<BR>विलिखति वसुधामर्कमूलस्य हेतोः<BR>Bh. 2. 100.<BR>--वर्षः a solar year.<BR>--वल्लभः {1}<BR>N. of a plant (बंधूक). {2} a lotus.<BR>--विवाहः marriage with the arka plant<BR>(enjoined to be performed before a<BR>man marries a third wife, who thus<BR>becomes his fourth); चतुर्थादिविवाहार्थं<BR>तृतीयोऽर्कं समुद्वहेत् Kāśyapa.<BR>--वेधः N.<BR>of a tree (तालीशपत्र).<BR>--व्रतः --तं {1} a vow<BR>performed on माघशुक्लसप्तमी. {2} the<BR>law or manner of the sun; when<BR>a king exacts taxes from his subjects<BR>only to add to their material comforts<BR>and happiness, just as the sun draws<BR>up water during {8} months of the year,<BR>only to give it back increased a<BR>thousandfold, he is said to follow अर्कव्रत;<BR>अष्टौ मासान् यथादित्यस्तोयं हरतिरश्मिभिः ।<BR>तथा हरेत्करं राष्ट्रान्नित्यमर्कव्रतं हि तत् ॥<BR>Ms. 9. 305; cf. R. 1. 18 (the point<BR>of comparison may also be the<BR>imperceptible way in which the sun<BR>absorbs water, see Pt. 1. 221).<BR>--शोकः<BR>Ved. brilliancy of rays.<BR>--सातिः f.<BR>{1} finding of rays. {2} poetical<BR>inspiration; finding out hymns.<BR>--सोदरः ‘brother of the sun’, an<BR>epithet of Airāvata.<BR>--हिता = ˚कांता q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कवत्|अर्कवन्त्
अर्कवत् a. Containing flashes of<BR>lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्किन्
अर्किन् a. Ved.<BR>1 Shining, bright.<BR>--2<BR>Praising.<BR>--3 Praised or worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्कीय
अर्कीय, अर्क्य a. [अर्क-छ; अर्च्-ण्यत्<BR>कुत्वं]<BR>1 Belonging to arka.<BR>--2 To be<BR>praised or worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्क्य
अर्कीय, अर्क्य a. [अर्क-छ; अर्च्-ण्यत्<BR>कुत्वं]<BR>1 Belonging to arka.<BR>--2 To be<BR>praised or worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गडः|अर्गड
अर्गडः = अर्गल below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलः|अर्गल|अर्गलं
अर्गलः --ला --ली --लं [अर्ज् कलच्<BR>न्यंक्वादि˚ कुत्वं Tv.]<BR>1 A wooden bolt, pin,<BR>bar &c. (for fastening a door or<BR>the cover of a vessel), a bolt, latch,<BR>bar; पुरार्गलादीर्घभुजो बुभोज R. 18. 4;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">Page0164-a+ 57</a>]<BR>16. 6; अनायतार्गलं Mk. 2.;<BR>ससंभ्रमेंद्रद्रुतपातितार्गला निमीलिताक्षीव<BR>भियाऽमरावती K. P. 1; दत्तं च बहिरर्गलं<BR>Ks. 4. 62 bolted from without; oft.<BR>used figuratively in the sense of a bar,<BR>impediment, something intervening<BR>as an obstruction; वाक्यार्गलया<BR>निवारिताः Pt. 2; Śi. 2. 118; ईप्सितं<BR>तदवज्ञानाद्विद्धि सार्गलमात्मनः R. 1. 79<BR>obstructed; वार्यर्गलामंग इव प्रवृत्तः<BR>5. 45; कंटे केवलमर्गलेव निहिता जीवस्य<BR>निर्गच्छतः K. P. 8; see अनर्गल also.<BR>--2 A wave or billow.<BR>--3 The leaf of<BR>a door (कपाटं).<BR>--4 A kind of stotra<BR>or hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गला
अर्गलः --ला --ली --लं [अर्ज् कलच्<BR>न्यंक्वादि˚ कुत्वं Tv.]<BR>1 A wooden bolt, pin,<BR>bar &c. (for fastening a door or<BR>the cover of a vessel), a bolt, latch,<BR>bar; पुरार्गलादीर्घभुजो बुभोज R. 18. 4;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">Page0164-a+ 57</a>]<BR>16. 6; अनायतार्गलं Mk. 2.;<BR>ससंभ्रमेंद्रद्रुतपातितार्गला निमीलिताक्षीव<BR>भियाऽमरावती K. P. 1; दत्तं च बहिरर्गलं<BR>Ks. 4. 62 bolted from without; oft.<BR>used figuratively in the sense of a bar,<BR>impediment, something intervening<BR>as an obstruction; वाक्यार्गलया<BR>निवारिताः Pt. 2; Śi. 2. 118; ईप्सितं<BR>तदवज्ञानाद्विद्धि सार्गलमात्मनः R. 1. 79<BR>obstructed; वार्यर्गलामंग इव प्रवृत्तः<BR>5. 45; कंटे केवलमर्गलेव निहिता जीवस्य<BR>निर्गच्छतः K. P. 8; see अनर्गल also.<BR>--2 A wave or billow.<BR>--3 The leaf of<BR>a door (कपाटं).<BR>--4 A kind of stotra<BR>or hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गली
अर्गलः --ला --ली --लं [अर्ज् कलच्<BR>न्यंक्वादि˚ कुत्वं Tv.]<BR>1 A wooden bolt, pin,<BR>bar &c. (for fastening a door or<BR>the cover of a vessel), a bolt, latch,<BR>bar; पुरार्गलादीर्घभुजो बुभोज R. 18. 4;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">Page0164-a+ 57</a>]<BR>16. 6; अनायतार्गलं Mk. 2.;<BR>ससंभ्रमेंद्रद्रुतपातितार्गला निमीलिताक्षीव<BR>भियाऽमरावती K. P. 1; दत्तं च बहिरर्गलं<BR>Ks. 4. 62 bolted from without; oft.<BR>used figuratively in the sense of a bar,<BR>impediment, something intervening<BR>as an obstruction; वाक्यार्गलया<BR>निवारिताः Pt. 2; Śi. 2. 118; ईप्सितं<BR>तदवज्ञानाद्विद्धि सार्गलमात्मनः R. 1. 79<BR>obstructed; वार्यर्गलामंग इव प्रवृत्तः<BR>5. 45; कंटे केवलमर्गलेव निहिता जीवस्य<BR>निर्गच्छतः K. P. 8; see अनर्गल also.<BR>--2 A wave or billow.<BR>--3 The leaf of<BR>a door (कपाटं).<BR>--4 A kind of stotra<BR>or hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलं|अर्गल|अर्गलः
अर्गलः --ला --ली --लं [अर्ज् कलच्<BR>न्यंक्वादि˚ कुत्वं Tv.]<BR>1 A wooden bolt, pin,<BR>bar &c. (for fastening a door or<BR>the cover of a vessel), a bolt, latch,<BR>bar; पुरार्गलादीर्घभुजो बुभोज R. 18. 4;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">Page0164-a+ 57</a>]<BR>16. 6; अनायतार्गलं Mk. 2.;<BR>ससंभ्रमेंद्रद्रुतपातितार्गला निमीलिताक्षीव<BR>भियाऽमरावती K. P. 1; दत्तं च बहिरर्गलं<BR>Ks. 4. 62 bolted from without; oft.<BR>used figuratively in the sense of a bar,<BR>impediment, something intervening<BR>as an obstruction; वाक्यार्गलया<BR>निवारिताः Pt. 2; Śi. 2. 118; ईप्सितं<BR>तदवज्ञानाद्विद्धि सार्गलमात्मनः R. 1. 79<BR>obstructed; वार्यर्गलामंग इव प्रवृत्तः<BR>5. 45; कंटे केवलमर्गलेव निहिता जीवस्य<BR>निर्गच्छतः K. P. 8; see अनर्गल also.<BR>--2 A wave or billow.<BR>--3 The leaf of<BR>a door (कपाटं).<BR>--4 A kind of stotra<BR>or hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलिका
अर्गलिका A small door-pin, small<BR>bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलित
अर्गलित a. Fastened by a bolt,<BR>chained, bolted; ˚द्वारा K. 357.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गलीय
अर्गलीय, --ल्य a. Belonging to a<BR>bolt or pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्गल्य
अर्गलीय, --ल्य a. Belonging to a<BR>bolt or pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्
अर्घ् {c1c} P. [अर्घति, अर्घितुं, अर्घित] To<BR>be worth, have value, to cost;<BR>परीक्षका यत्र न संति देशे नार्घंति रत्नानि<BR>समुद्रजानि Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घः|अर्घ
अर्घः [अर्घ्-घञ्]<BR>1 Price, value;<BR>कुर्युरर्घं यथापण्यं Ms. 8. 398;<BR>Y. 2. 251; कुत्स्याः स्युः कुपरीक्षका हि मणयो<BR>यैरर्घतः पातिताः Bh. 2. 15 reduced in<BR>their true value, depreciated; so<BR>अनर्घ priceless; महार्घ very costly.<BR>--2 A material of worship,<BR>respectful offering or oblation to gods<BR>or venerable men, consisting<BR>of rice, Dūrvā grass &c. with<BR>or without water; दूर्वासर्षपपुष्पाणां<BR>दत्त्वार्घं पूर्णमंजलिं Y. 1. 290;<BR>कुटजकुसुमैः कल्पितार्घाय तस्मै Me. 4; the<BR>ingredients of this offering are: -आपः<BR>क्षीरं कुशाग्रं च दधि सर्पिः सतंडुलम् । यवः<BR>सिद्धार्थकश्चैव अष्टांगोऽर्घः प्रकीर्तितः ॥ see<BR>अर्घ्य below.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्ह a.<BR>worthy of a respectful offering.<BR>--दानं<BR>presentation of a respectful offering.<BR>--बलाबलं rate of price, proper price,<BR>the cheapness or dearness of<BR>articles, fall or rise in prices;<BR>Ms. 9. 329.<BR>--संख्यानं, संस्थापनं the price<BR>of commodities, appraising, assizes<BR>of goods; कुर्वीत चैषां (वणिजां)<BR>प्रत्यक्षमर्घसंस्थापनं नृपः Ms. 8. 402.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घीशः|अर्घीश
अर्घीशः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घ्य|अर्घ्यं
अर्घ्य a. [अर्घ-यत् अर्घमर्हति]<BR>1<BR>Valuable; अनर्घ्य invaluable; see s. v.<BR>--2 Venerable, deserving respectful<BR>offering; तानर्घ्यानर्घ्यमादाय<BR>दूरात्प्रत्युद्ययौ गिरिः Ku. 6. 50; Śi. 1. 14;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">Page0164-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Y. 1. 110.<BR>--र्घ्यं<BR>1 A respectful<BR>offering or oblation to a god or<BR>venerable person (see अर्घ); अर्घः<BR>पूजाविधिः तदर्थं द्रव्यं अर्घ्यं Sk.; अर्घ्यमस्मै<BR>V. 5.; ददतु तरवः पुष्पैरर्घ्यं फलैश्च<BR>मधुश्चुतः U. 3. 24; अर्घ्यमर्घ्यमिति वादिनं<BR>नृपं R. 11. 69; 1. 44; Ku. 1. 58,<BR>6. 50; (it often consists only of<BR>water given in a droṇa and forms<BR>part of the Madhuparka ceremony).<BR>--2 A kind of honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्घटं|अर्घट
अर्घटं Ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्
अर्च् {c1c} U. (अर्चति-ते, आनर्च,<BR>आर्चीत्, अर्चितुं, अर्चित)<BR>1 (a) To adore<BR>worship, salute, welcome with<BR>respect; R. 2. 21, 1. 6, 90; 4. 84,<BR>12. 89; Ms. 3. 93; आर्चीद्<BR>द्विजातीन् परमार्थविंदान् Bk. 1. 15, 14. 63;<BR>17. 5; यस्यार्चत्यसौ शासनं Mv. 1. 29<BR>honours, respectfully obeys. (b) To<BR>honour, i. e. decorate, adorn; U. 2. 9.<BR>--2 To praise (Ved.).<BR>--3 To shine.<BR>--{c10c} P. or Caus.<BR>1 To honour, adore,<BR>worship; स्वर्गौकसामर्चितमर्चयित्वा<BR>Ku. 1. 59.<BR>--2 To praise.<BR>--3 To cause to<BR>shine. --Desid. [अर्चिचिषति] To wish<BR>to worship --WITH अनु to<BR>congratulate, hail with joy.<BR>--प्र {1} to praise,<BR>sing praises of. {2} to honour,<BR>worship; प्रानर्चुरर्च्या जगदर्चनीयं<BR>Bk. 2. 20; (--caus.) to honour.<BR>--सं {1}<BR>to worship, adore. {2} to fix, settle,<BR>establish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च|अर्च्च
अर्च a. Ved. Shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चक|अर्चकः|अर्च्चक|अर्च्चकः
अर्चक a. [अर्च्-ण्वुल्] Worshipping,<BR>adoring.<BR>--कः A worshipper;<BR>गुरुदेवद्विजार्चकः Ms. 11. 225.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चत्रि
अर्चत्रि a. Ved. [अर्च् वेदे बाहु˚ अत्रि]<BR>Adorable, venerable (Sāy.);<BR>roaring aloud, singing loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चत्र्य
अर्चत्र्य a. Ved. To be praised or<BR>worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चन|अर्च्चनं
अर्चन a. [अर्च्-ल्युट्] Worshipping,<BR>praising.<BR>--नं, --ना Worship,<BR>reverence or respect paid to deities and<BR>superiors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चनीय
अर्चनीय, अर्च्य pot. p.<BR>[अर्च्-अनीयर् ण्यत्] To be adored or<BR>worshipped, venerable, adorable,<BR>respectable R. 2. 10; Bk. 6. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्च्य
अर्चनीय, अर्च्य pot. p.<BR>[अर्च्-अनीयर् ण्यत्] To be adored or<BR>worshipped, venerable, adorable,<BR>respectable R. 2. 10; Bk. 6. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चा|अर्च्चा
अर्चा [अर्च्-अङ्]<BR>1 Worship,<BR>adoration.<BR>--2 An idol or image<BR>intended to be worshipped;<BR>मौर्यैर्हिरण्यार्थिभिरर्चाः प्रकल्पिताः Mbh. (there is some<BR>dispute among scholars as to the<BR>precise meaning of this passage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिः|अर्चि|अर्च्चिः
अर्चिः f. [अर्च्-इन्] Ray, flame (of<BR>fire or of the morning twilight);<BR>आसीदासन्ननिर्वाणः प्रदीपार्चिरिवोषसि<BR>R. 12. 1; नैशस्यार्चिर्हुतभुज इव<BR>छिन्नभूयिष्ठधूमा V. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिमत्|अर्चिमन्त्
अर्चिमत्, --वत् a. Ved. Shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिवत्|अर्चिवन्त्
अर्चिमत्, --वत् a. Ved. Shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चित|अर्च्चितः
अर्चित p. p. Worshipped,<BR>respected, honoured; R. 10. 55; Ms. 4. 235;<BR>Ku. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चितिन्
अर्चितिन् a. Honouring, adoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिन्
अर्चिन् a.<BR>1 Praising,<BR>honouring, worshipping.<BR>--2 Shining as<BR>a ray of light, radiating. --m.<BR>(र्ची) A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिस्|अर्च्चिस्
अर्चिस् n.<BR>--(र्चिः) [अर्च्-इसि<BR>Uṇ. 2. 107]<BR>1 A ray of light, flame; यत्ते<BR>पवित्रमर्चिष्यग्ने विततमंतरा<BR>Rv. 9. 67. 23; प्रदक्षिणार्चिर्हविरग्निराददे R. 3. 14.<BR>--2 Light, lustre; प्रशमादर्चिषां<BR>Ku. 2. 20; Ratn. 4. 16 (said to be also.<BR>f.) --f. N. of the wife of कृशाश्व and<BR>mother of धूमकेतु. --m.<BR>1 A ray of<BR>light.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्चिष्मत्|अर्चिष्मन्त्
अर्चिष्मत् a. [अस्त्यर्थे मतुप्] Flaming,<BR>brilliant, bright; V. 3. 2. --m.<BR>1 Fire,<BR>the god of fire.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--3 A<BR>sort of subordinate deity.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--ती<BR>1 N. of the town or<BR>world of Agni.<BR>--2 One of the 10<BR>earths according to Buddhists.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ज्
अर्ज् {c1c} P. [अर्जति, आनर्ज, अर्जिष्यति,<BR>आर्जीत्, अर्जितुं, आर्जीत]<BR>1 To procure,<BR>secure, gain, earn, usually in the<BR>caus. in this sense; पितृद्रव्याविरोधेन<BR>यदन्यत्स्वयमर्जितं Y. 2. 118.<BR>--2 To<BR>take up; आनर्जुर्नृभुजोस्त्राणि Bk. 14. 74.<BR>--{c10c} P. or caus.<BR>1 To procure, acquire,<BR>obtain; स्वयमर्जित, स्वार्जित obtained<BR>by one's own exertions, self-acquired.<BR>--2 To work or manufacture make,<BR>prepare (सतोगुणांतराधानं). --WITH<BR>अति {1} to allow, permit, let go.<BR>{2} to remove, despatch, make away<BR>with.<BR>--अनु to let go, set free,<BR>deliver.<BR>--अपि to add to.<BR>--अन्वव<BR>{1} to cause to go after or in a<BR>particular direction. {2} to visit with<BR>any thing, overcome.<BR>--अप्यति to<BR>add, append; say something in<BR>addition to what is already said.<BR>--अव<BR>to permit to leave, release, let go.<BR>--उद् to drive out, remove.<BR>--प्र<BR>caus. to furnish, supply, procure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जक|अर्जकः|अर्ज्जक|अर्ज्जकः
अर्जक a. [अर्ज्-ण्वुल्] (--र्जिका f.)<BR>Procuring, acquiring; one who<BR>acquires or gets; अर्जको ह्यंशमाहरेत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-a" target="_blank">Page0165-a+ 65</a>]<BR>Smṛti.<BR>--कंः N. of several plants<BR>सितपर्णास, वर्वरीभेद; सामान्यतुलसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जनं|अर्जन|अर्ज्जनं
अर्जनं [अर्ज्-ल्युट्] Getting,<BR>acquisition; अर्थानामर्जने दुःखं Pt. 1. 163;<BR>अर्जयितृव्यापारोऽर्जनं Dāy. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुन|अर्जुनं|अर्जुनः
अर्जुन a. [अर्ज्-उनन् णिलुक् च<BR>Uṇ. 3. 58] (ना-नी f.).<BR>1 White, clear,<BR>bright, of the colour of day; अहश्च<BR>कृष्णमहरर्जुनं च Rv. 6. 9. 1;<BR>पिशंगमौंजीयुजमर्जुनच्छविं Śi. 1. 6.<BR>--2 Silvery.<BR>--नः<BR>1 The white colour.<BR>--2 A<BR>peacock.<BR>--3 A sort of cutaneous disease.<BR>--4 A tree (Mar. अर्जुनसादडा), with<BR>useful rind.<BR>--5 N. of the third<BR>Pāṇḍava who was a son of Kuntī<BR>by Indra and hence called ऐंद्रि also.<BR>[Arjuna was so called because he was<BR>‘white’ or ‘pure in actions’ (पृथिव्यां<BR>चतुरंतायां वर्णोमे दुर्लभः समः । करोमि कर्म शुद्धं च तेन<BR>मामर्जुनं विदुः). He was taught the use of<BR>arms by Droṇa and was his favourite<BR>pupil. By his skill in arms he won<BR>Draupadī at her Svayaṃvara (see Draupadī).<BR>For an involuntary transgression he<BR>went into temporary exile and during<BR>that time he learnt the science of arms<BR>from Paraśurāma. He married Ulūpī, a<BR>Nāga Princess, by whom he had a son<BR>named Irāvat, and also Citrāṅgadā,<BR>daughter of the king of Maṇipura, who<BR>bore him a son named Babhruvāhana.<BR>During this exile he visited Dvārakā,<BR>and with the help and advice of Kṛṣṇa<BR>succeeded in marrying Subhadrā. By<BR>her he had a son named Abhimanyu.<BR>Afterwards he obtained the bow Gāṇḍīva<BR>from the god Agni whom he assisted in<BR>burning the Khāṇḍava forest. When<BR>Dharma, his eldest brother, lost the<BR>kingdom by gambling, and the five brothers<BR>went into exile, he went to the<BR>Himālayas to propitiate the gods and to obtain<BR>from them celestial weapons for use in the<BR>contemplated war against the Kauravas.<BR>There he fought with Śiva who<BR>appeared in the disguise of a Kirāta; but when<BR>he discovered the true character of his<BR>adversary he worshipped him and Śiva<BR>gave him the Pāśupatāstra. Indra,<BR>Varuṇa, Yama and Kubera also<BR>presented him with their own weapons. In<BR>the 13th year of their exile, the<BR>Pāṇḍavas entered the service of the King of<BR>Virāṭa and he had to act the part of a<BR>cunuch, and music and dancing master.<BR>In the great war with the Kauravas<BR>Arjuna took a very distinguished part.<BR>He secured the assistance of<BR>Kṛṣṇa who acted as his charioteer and<BR>related to him the Bhagavadgītā when<BR>on the first day of the battle he<BR>hesitated to bend his bow against his<BR>own kinsmen. In the course of the great<BR>struggle he slew or vanquished several<BR>redoubtable warriors on the side of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-b" target="_blank">Page0165-b+ 62</a>]<BR>Kauravas, such as Jayadratha, Bhīṣma,<BR>Karṇa &c. After Yudhiṣṭhira had been<BR>installed sovereign of Hastināpura, he<BR>resolved to perform the Aśvamedha sacrifice,<BR>and a horse was let loose with Arjuna as<BR>its guardian. Arjuna followed it through<BR>many cities and countries and fought with<BR>many kings. At the city of Maṇipura<BR>he had to fight with his own son<BR>Babhruvāhana and was killed; but he was<BR>restored to life by a charm supplied by his wife<BR>Ulūpī. He traversed the whole of Bharata<BR>khaṇḍa and returned to Hastināpura,<BR>loaded with spoils and tributes, and<BR>the great horse-sacrifice was then duly<BR>performed. He was afterwards called<BR>by Kṛṣṇa to Dvārakā amid the intestine<BR>struggles of the Yādavas and there he<BR>performed the funeral ceremonies of<BR>Vasudeva and Kṛṣṇa. Soon after this the<BR>five Pāṇḍavas repaired to heaven having<BR>installed Parīkṣit-the only surviving<BR>son of Abhimanyu-on the throne of<BR>Hastināpura. Arjuna was the bravest of the<BR>Pāṇḍavas, high-minded, generous,<BR>upright, handsome and the most prominent<BR>figure of all his brothers. He has several<BR>appellations, such as Pārtha, Guḍākeśa,<BR>Savyasācī, Dhanaṃjaya, Phālguna,<BR>Kirīṭin, Jiṣṇu, Śvetavāhana, Gāṇḍīvin &c.<BR>&c.]<BR>--6 N. of Kārtavīrya, slain<BR>by Paraśurāma. See कार्तवीर्य.<BR>--7 N. of<BR>a country Bṛ. S. 14. 25.<BR>--8 The only<BR>son of his mother.<BR>--9 N. of Indra.<BR>--नी<BR>1 A procuress, bawd.<BR>--2 A<BR>cow.<BR>--3 A kind of serpent.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of Uṣā wife of Aniruddha.<BR>--5 N.<BR>of a river commonly called करतोया.<BR>--6 (न्यौ, --न्यः dual and pl.) N. of the<BR>constellation Phalgunī.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Silver.<BR>--2 Gold.<BR>--3 Slight inflammation of<BR>the white of the eye.<BR>--4 Grass.<BR>--नाः<BR>(pl.) The descendants of Arjuna.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपमः the teak tree; also<BR>शाकदुम and महापत्राख्यवृक्ष.<BR>--कांड a.<BR>having a white stem or appendage.<BR>--छवि a. white, of a white colour.<BR>--ध्वजः ‘white-bannered’, N. of<BR>Hanūmat.<BR>--पाकी N. of a plant and<BR>its fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनक|अर्जुनकः
अर्जुनक a. Belonging to Arjuna.<BR>--कः A worshipper of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्जुनस
अर्जुनस a. [तृणादिगण] Overgrown<BR>with Arjuna plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ण|अर्णः
अर्ण a. [ऋ-न]<BR>1 Being in motion,<BR>agitated; restless.<BR>--2 Foaming,<BR>effervescing.<BR>--र्णः<BR>1 A flood, stream;<BR>water (Ved.)<BR>--2 The teak tree.<BR>--3<BR>A letter (of the alphabet); पंचार्णो<BR>मनुरीरितः.<BR>--4 N. of a metre<BR>having 10 feet and belonging to the<BR>class called Daṇḍaka.<BR>--र्णा A river<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">Page0165-c+ 56</a>]<BR>(Ved.).<BR>--र्णं Tumult or din of battle<BR>confused noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णव|अर्णवः|अर्ण्णव
अर्णव a. Being agitated,<BR>foaming, restless (Ved.); full of water<BR>(Sāy.).<BR>--वः [अर्णांसि संति यस्मिन्,<BR>अर्णस्-व सलोपः P. V. 2. 109 Vārt.].<BR>1<BR>A stream, flood, wave.<BR>--2 The<BR>(foaming) sea, ocean (fig. also);<BR>शोक˚ ocean of grief; so चिंता˚;<BR>जन˚ ocean of men; संसारार्णवलंघन<BR>Bh. 3. 10.<BR>--3 The ocean of air.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of a metre.<BR>--5 N. of the sun or<BR>Indra (as givers of water).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः the extremity of the ocean.<BR>--उद्भवः {1} N. of a plant अग्निजार.<BR>{2} the moon.<BR>--(वा) Lakṣmī.<BR>--(वं)<BR>nectar.<BR>--ज a. sea-born, marine. (--जं,<BR>जः) cuttle-fish.<BR>--पोतः, --यानं a boat<BR>or ship.<BR>--मंदिरः {1} ‘inhabiting the<BR>ocean’, N. of Varuṇa, regent of<BR>the waters. {2} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णस्
अर्णस् n. [ऋ-असुन्-नुट् Uṇ. 4. 196]<BR>1 Water; a wave, flood, stream;<BR>सवर्णमर्णः कथमन्यथास्य Śi. 12. 69.<BR>--2<BR>The sea, ocean (usually ˚सः).<BR>--3<BR>The ocean of air.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दः {1} a<BR>cloud. {2} N. of a plant मुस्तक.<BR>--भवः<BR>conch-shell.<BR>--वृत् a. Ved.<BR>including the waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्णस्वत्|अर्णस्वन्त्
अर्णस्वत् a. Having much water.<BR>--m. The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तगलः|अर्तगल|अर्त्तगल|अर्त्तगलः
अर्तगलः = आर्तगल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तन|अर्त्तन|अर्त्तनं
अर्तन a. [ऋत्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Blaming,<BR>reviling.<BR>--2 Sorry, grieved.<BR>--नं<BR>Censure, reproach, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तिः|अर्ति|अर्त्ति|अर्त्तिः
अर्तिः f. [अर्द्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Pain,<BR>sorrow, grief; शिरोऽर्ति head-ache.<BR>--2<BR>The end of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तिका|अर्त्तिका
अर्तिका [ऋत्-ण्वुल्] An elder<BR>sister (in dramas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्तुक|अर्त्तुक
अर्तुक a. Ved. [ऋत्-बाहु˚उकञ्]<BR>Provoking, quarrelsome (स्पर्धक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्
अर्थ् {c10c} A. [अर्थयते, epic अर्थते;<BR>अर्थयांचके, अर्थयिष्यते, आर्तथत, अर्थयितुं,<BR>अर्थित]<BR>1 To request, beg, supplicate,<BR>ask, entreat, solicit (with two acc.);<BR>त्वामिममर्थमर्थयते Dk. 71; तमभिक्रम्य<BR>सर्वेऽद्य वयंचार्थामहे वसु Mb.;<BR>प्रहस्तमर्थयांचक्रे योद्धुं Bk. 14. 88.<BR>--2 To strive<BR>to obtain, desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थः|अर्थ
अर्थः [In some of its senses from<BR>अर्थ्; in others from ऋ-थन् Uṇ. 2. 4;<BR>अर्यते ह्यसौ अर्थिभिः Nir.]<BR>1 Object,<BR>purpose, end and aim; wish, desire;<BR>ज्ञातार्थो ज्ञातसंबंधः श्रोतुं श्रोता प्रवर्तते;<BR>सिद्ध˚, ˚परिपंथी Mu. 5; ˚वशात् 5. 8;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0166-a" target="_blank">Page0166-a+ 58</a>]<BR>स्मर्तव्योस्मि सत्यर्थे Dk. 117 if it be<BR>necessary; Y. 2. 46; M. 4. 6; oft. used<BR>in this sense as the last member of<BR>compounds and translated by ‘for’,<BR>‘intended for’, ‘for the sake of’,<BR>‘on account of’, ‘on behalf of,’ and<BR>used like an adj. to qualify nouns;<BR>अर्थेन तु नित्यसमासो विशेष्यनिघ्नता च Vārt.;<BR>संतानार्थाय विधये R. 1. 34; तां<BR>देवतापित्रतिथिक्रियार्थां (धेनुं) 2. 16; द्विजार्थां<BR>यवागूः Sk.; यज्ञार्थात्कर्मणोऽन्यत्र<BR>Bg. 3. 9. It mostly occurs in this sense as<BR>अर्थं, अर्थे or अर्थाय and has an<BR>adverbial force; (a) किमर्थं for what<BR>purpose, why; यदर्थं for whom or<BR>which; वेलोपलक्षणार्थं Ś. 4;<BR>तद्दर्शनादभूच्छंभोर्भूयान्दारार्थमादरः Ku. 6. 13; (b)<BR>परार्थे प्राज्ञ उत्सृजेत् H. 1. 44; गवार्थे<BR>ब्राह्मणार्थे च Pt. 1. 420; मदर्थे<BR>त्यक्तजीविताः Bg. 1. 9; (c) सुखार्थाय<BR>Pt. 4. 18; प्रत्याख्याता मया तत्र नलस्यार्थाय<BR>देवताः Nala. 13. 19; ऋतुपर्णस्य<BR>चार्थाय 23. 9.<BR>--2 Cause, motive, reason,<BR>ground, means; अलुप्तश्च मुनेः क्रियार्थः<BR>R. 2. 55 means or cause; अतोऽर्थात्<BR>Ms. 2. 213.<BR>--3 Meaning, sense,<BR>signification, import; अर्थ is of 3 kinds:<BR>वाच्य or expressed, लक्ष्य or indicated<BR>(secondary), and व्यंग्य or suggested;<BR>तददोषौ शब्दार्थौ K. P. 1; अर्थो वाच्यश्च<BR>लक्ष्यश्च व्यंग्यश्चेति त्रिधा मतः ॥ S. D. 2;<BR>वागर्थाविव R. 1. 1; अवेक्ष्य<BR>धातोर्गमनार्थमर्थवित् 3. 21.<BR>--4 A thing, object,<BR>substance; अर्थो हि कन्या परकीय एव<BR>Ś. 4. 21; that which can be<BR>perceived by the senses, an object of sense;<BR>इंद्रिय˚ H. 1. 146; Ku. 7. 71;<BR>R. 2. 51; न निर्बद्धा उपसर्गा अर्थान्निराहुः Nir.;<BR>इंद्रियेभ्यः परा ह्यर्था अर्थेभ्यश्च परं मनः<BR>Kaṭh. (the objects of sense are five<BR>रूप, रस, गंध, स्पर्श and शब्द).<BR>--5 (a)<BR>An affair, business, matter, work;<BR>प्राक् प्रतिपन्नोऽयमर्थोंऽगराजाय Ve. 3;<BR>अर्थोऽयमर्थांतरभाव्य एव Ku. 3. 18;<BR>अर्थोऽर्थानुबंधी Dk. 67; संगीतार्थः Me. 56<BR>business of singing, i. e. musical<BR>concert (apparatus of singing);<BR>संदेशार्थाः Me. 5 matters of message,<BR>i. e. messages; (b) Interest, object;<BR>स्वार्थसाधनतत्परः Ms. 4. 196;<BR>द्वयमेवार्थसाधनं R. 1. 19; 2. 21; दुरापेऽर्थे<BR>1. 72; सर्वार्थाचिंतकः Ms. 7. 121;<BR>मालविकायां न मे कश्चिदर्थः M. 3 I have no<BR>interest in M. (c) subject matter,<BR>contents (as of letters &c.);<BR>त्वामवगतार्थं करिष्यति Mu. 1 will acquaint<BR>you with the matter; उत्तरोऽयं<BR>लेखार्थः ibid.; तेन हि अस्य गृहीतार्था भवामि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0166-b" target="_blank">Page0166-b+ 58</a>]<BR>V. 2 if so I should know its<BR>contents; ननु परिगृहीतार्थोस्मि कृतो भवता<BR>V. 5; तया भवतोऽविनयमंतरेण<BR>परिगृहीतार्थाकृता देवी M. 4 made acquainted<BR>with; त्वया गृहीतार्थया अत्रभवती कथं<BR>न वारिता 3; अगृहीतार्थे आवां Ś. 6;<BR>इति पौरान् गृहीतार्थान् कृत्वा ibid.<BR>--6 Wealth, riches, property, money<BR>(said to be of 3 kinds:<BR>--शुक्ल<BR>honestly got; शबल got by more or less<BR>doubtful means, and कृष्ण<BR>dishonestly got;) त्यागाय संभृतार्थानां R. 1. 7;<BR>धिगर्थाः कष्टसंश्रयाः Pt. 1. 163;<BR>अर्थानामर्जने दुःखं ibid.; यस्यार्थास्तस्य मित्राणि<BR>1. 3; तेषामर्थे नियुंजीत शूरान् दक्षान्<BR>कुलोद्गतान् Ms. 7. 62.<BR>--7 Attainment<BR>of riches or worldly prosperity,<BR>regarded as one of the four ends of<BR>human existence, the other three<BR>being धर्म, काम and मोक्ष; with अर्थ and<BR>काम, धर्म forms the well-known triad;<BR>cf. Ku. 5. 38; अप्यर्थकामौ<BR>तस्यास्तां धर्म एव मनीषिणः R. 1. 25.<BR>--8 (a)<BR>Use, advantage, profit, good; तथा<BR>हि सर्वे तस्यासन् परार्थैकफला गुणाः<BR>R. 1. 29 for the good of others;<BR>अर्थानर्थावुभौ बुद्ध्वा Ms. 8. 24 good and evil;<BR>क्षेत्रिणामर्थः 9. 52.; यावानर्थ उदपाने<BR>सर्वतः संप्लुतोदके Bg. 2. 46; also व्यर्थ,<BR>निरर्थक q. v. (b) Use, want, need,<BR>concern, with instr.; कोऽर्थः पुत्रेण जातेन<BR>Pt. 1 what is the use of a son being<BR>born; कश्च तेनार्थः Dk. 59;<BR>कोर्थस्तिरश्चां गुणैः Pt. 2. 33 what do brutes<BR>care for merits; Bh. 2. 48; योग्येनार्थः<BR>कस्य न स्याज्जनेन Śi. 18. 66; नैव तस्य<BR>कृतेनार्थो नाकृतेनेह कश्चन<BR>Bg. 3. 18; यदि प्राणैरिहार्थो वो निवर्तध्वं Rām.<BR>को नु मे जीवितेनार्थः Nala. 12. 65.<BR>--9<BR>Asking, begging; request, suit,<BR>petition.<BR>--10 Action, plaint (in law).<BR>--11 The actual state, fact of the<BR>matter; as in यथार्थ, अर्थतः,<BR>˚तत्त्वविद्.<BR>--12 Manner, kind, sort.<BR>--13<BR>Prevention, warding off; मशकार्थो<BR>धूमः; prohibition, abolition (this<BR>meaning may also be derived from<BR>{1} above).<BR>--14 Price (perhaps an<BR>incorrect form for अर्घ).<BR>--15 Fruit,<BR>result (फलं).<BR>--16 N. of a son of<BR>धर्म.<BR>--17 The second place from<BR>the लग्न (in astr.).<BR>--18 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिकारः charge of money,<BR>office of treasurer ˚रे न नियोक्तव्यौ H. 2.<BR>--अधिकारिन् m. a treasurer, one<BR>charged with financial duties,<BR>finance minister.<BR>--अन्वेषणं inquiry<BR>after a matter.<BR>--अंतरं {1} another or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0166-c" target="_blank">Page0166-c+ 58</a>]<BR>different meaning. {2} another<BR>cause or motive; अर्थोयमर्थांतरभाव्य एव<BR>Ku. 3. 18. {3} a new matter or<BR>circumstance, new affair. {4} opposite or<BR>antithetical meaning, difference of<BR>meaning. ˚न्यासः a figure of speech<BR>in which a general proposition is<BR>adduced to support a particular<BR>instance, or a particular instance, to<BR>support a general proposition; it is<BR>an inference from particular to<BR>general and vice versa; उक्तिरर्थांतरन्यासः<BR>स्यात् सामान्यविशेषयोः । (१)<BR>हनुमानब्धिमतरद् दुष्करं किं महात्मनां ॥ (२)<BR>गुणवद्वस्तुसंसर्गाद्याति नीचोपि गौरवं । पुष्पमालानुषंगेण<BR>सूत्रं शिरसि धार्यते Kuval.; cf. also<BR>K. P. 10 and S. D. 709. (Instances of<BR>this figure abound in Sanskrit<BR>literature, especially in the works of<BR>Kālidāsa, Māgha and Bhāravi).<BR>--अन्वित a. {1} rich, wealthy. {2}<BR>significant.<BR>--अर्थिन् a. one who longs<BR>for or strives to get wealth or gain<BR>any object.<BR>--अलंकारः a figure of<BR>speech determined by and<BR>dependent on the sense, and not on sound<BR>(opp. शब्दालंकार).<BR>--आगमः {1}<BR>acquisition of wealth, income; ˚गमाय स्यात<BR>Pt. 1. {2} collection of property.<BR>{3} conveying of a sense; S. D. 737.<BR>--आपत्तिः f. [अर्थस्य अनुक्तार्थस्य आपात्तिः<BR>सिद्धिः] {1} an inference from<BR>circumstances, presumption, implication,<BR>one of the five sources of<BR>knowledge or modes of proof, according<BR>to the Mīmāṃsakas. It is<BR>‘deduction of a matter from that which<BR>could not else be’; it is<BR>‘assumption of a thing, not itself<BR>perceived but necessarily implied by<BR>another which is seen, heard, or<BR>proved’; it is an inference used to<BR>account for an apparent inconsistency;<BR>as in the familiar instance पीनो देवदत्तो<BR>दिवा न भुक्तें the apparent<BR>inconsistency between ‘fatness’ and ‘not<BR>eating by day’ is accounted for by the<BR>inference of his ‘eating by night’;<BR>पीनत्वविशिष्टस्य देवदत्तस्य<BR>रात्रिभोजित्वरूपार्थस्य शब्दानुक्तस्यापि आपत्तिः. Strictly<BR>speaking it is no separate mode of<BR>proof; it is only a case of अनुमान<BR>and can be proved by a व्यतिरेकव्याप्ति;<BR>cf. Tarka K. 17 and S. D. 460. {2}<BR>a figure of speech (according to<BR>some rhetoricians) in which a<BR>relevant assertion suggests an<BR>inference not actually connected with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0167-a" target="_blank">Page0167-a+ 58</a>]<BR>the subject in hand, or vice versa;<BR>it corresponds to what is popularly<BR>called कैमुतिकन्याय or दंडापूपन्याय; e. g.<BR>हारोयं हरिणाक्षीणां लुठति स्तनमंडले ।<BR>मुक्तानामप्यवस्थेयं के वयं स्मरकिंकराः<BR>Amaru. 100; अभितप्तमयोपि मार्दवं भजते कैव कथा<BR>शरीरिषु R. 8. 43. S. D. thus defines<BR>the figure: --दंडापूपिकयान्यार्थागमोऽ<BR>र्थापत्तिरिष्यते.<BR>--उत्पत्तिः f. acquisition of wealth;<BR>so ˚उपार्जनं.<BR>--उपक्षेपकः an<BR>introductory scene (in dramas);<BR>अर्थोपक्षेपकाः पंच S. D. 308.<BR>--उपमा a simile<BR>dependent on sense and not on<BR>sound; see under उपमा.<BR>--उष्मन् m.<BR>the glow or warmth of wealth;<BR>अर्थोष्मणा विरहितः पुरुषः स एव Bh. 2. 40.<BR>--ओघः, --राशिः treasure, hoard of<BR>money.<BR>--कर (--री f.),<BR>--कृत् a. {1}<BR>bringing in wealth, enriching;<BR>अर्थकरी च विद्या H. Pr. 3. {2}<BR>useful, advantageous.<BR>--कर्मन् n. a<BR>principal action (opp. गुणकर्मन्).<BR>--काम a. desirous of wealth. (--मौ<BR>dual), wealth and (sensual) desire or<BR>pleasure; R. 1. 25.<BR>--कृच्छ्रं {1} a<BR>difficult matter. {2} pecuniary<BR>difficulty; न मुह्येदर्थकृच्छ्रेषु Nīti.<BR>--कृत्यं<BR>doing or execution of a business;<BR>अभ्युपेतार्थकृत्याः Me. 38.<BR>--क्रमः due<BR>order or sequence of purpose.<BR>--गत<BR>a. {1} based on the sense (as a दोष).<BR>{2} devoid of sense.<BR>--गौरवं depth<BR>of meaning; भारवेरर्थगौरवं Udb.,<BR>Ki. 2. 27.<BR>--घ्न a. (घ्नी f.) extravagant,<BR>wasteful, prodigal; Y. 1. 73;<BR>Ms. 9. 80.<BR>--चिंतक a. {1} thinking of profit.<BR>{2} having charge of affairs;<BR>सर्वार्थचिंतकः Ms. 7. 121.<BR>--चिंता, --चिंतनं<BR>charge or administration of (royal)<BR>affairs; मंत्री स्यादर्थचिंतायां S. D.<BR>--जात a. {1} full of meaning. {2}<BR>wealthy (जातधन).<BR>--(तं) {1} a<BR>collection of things. {2} large amount<BR>of wealth, considerable property;<BR>Dk. 63, Ś. 6; Mk. 2. 6. {3} all<BR>matters; Śi. 11. 6. {4} its own<BR>meaning; Ki. 3. 48.<BR>--ज्ञ a. knowing<BR>the sense or purpose; अर्थज्ञ इत्सकलं<BR>भद्रमश्नुते Nir.<BR>--तत्वं {1} the real<BR>truth, the fact of the matter;<BR>H. 4. 94. {2} the real nature or cause<BR>of any thing.<BR>--द a. {1} yielding<BR>wealth; Dk. 41. {2} advantageous,<BR>productive of good, useful. {3} li<BR>beral, munificent Ms. 2. 109. {4}<BR>favourable, compliant.<BR>--(दः) N. of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--दर्शनं perception of<BR>objects; Ki. 2. 33; Dk. 155.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0167-b" target="_blank">Page0167-b+ 59</a>]<BR>--दूषणं {1} extravagance, waste;<BR>H. 3. 115; Ms. 7. 48. {2} unjust<BR>seizure of property or withholding<BR>what is due. {3} finding fault with<BR>the meaning. {4} spoiling of another's<BR>property.<BR>--दोषः a literary fault or<BR>blemish with regard to the sense, one<BR>of the four doshas or blemishes of<BR>literary composition, the other three<BR>being पददोष, पदांशदोष, and वाक्यदोष;<BR>for definitions &c. see K. P. 7.<BR>--नित्य a. = अंर्थप्रधान Nir.<BR>--निबंधन a.<BR>dependent on wealth.<BR>--निश्चयः<BR>determination, decision.<BR>--पतिः {1} ‘the<BR>lord of riches’; a king;<BR>किंचिद्विहस्यार्थपतिं बभाषे R. 2. 46; 1. 59; 9. 3;<BR>18. 1; Pt. 1. 74. {2} an epithet of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--पर, --लुब्ध a. {1} intent on<BR>gaining wealth, greedy of wealth,<BR>covetous. {2} niggardly,<BR>parsimonious; Bh. 2. 47; Pt. 1. 425.<BR>--प्रकृतिः f. the leading source or<BR>occasion of the grand object in a<BR>drama; (the number of these ‘sources’<BR>is five: --बीजं बिंदुः पताका च प्रकरी<BR>कार्यमेव च । अर्थप्रकृतयः पंच ज्ञात्वा योज्या<BR>यथाविधि S. D. 317.)<BR>--प्रयोगः {1} usury.<BR>{2} administration of the affairs (of<BR>a state).<BR>--प्राप्त a. derived or<BR>understood from the sense.<BR>--बंधः {1}<BR>arrangement of words, composition,<BR>text; stanza, verse; Ś. 7. 5;<BR>ललितार्थबंधं V. 2. 14 put or expressed in<BR>elegant words. {2} connection (of the<BR>soul) with the objects of sense.<BR>--बुद्धि a. selfish.<BR>--बोधः indication<BR>of the (real) import.<BR>--भाज् a.<BR>entitled to a share in the division of<BR>property.<BR>--भृत् a. receiving high<BR>wages (as a servant).<BR>--भेदः<BR>distinction or difference of meaning;<BR>अर्थभेदेन शब्दभेदः.<BR>--मात्रं, --त्रा {1}<BR>property, wealth; Pt. 2. {2} the whole<BR>sense or object.<BR>--युक्त a. significant,<BR>full of meaning; Ku. 1. 13.<BR>--लाभः<BR>acquisition of wealth.<BR>--लोभः<BR>avarice.<BR>--वादः {1} declaration of any<BR>purpose. {2} affirmation, declaratory<BR>assertion, an explanatory remark,<BR>exegesis; speech or assertion having<BR>a certain object; a sentence. It<BR>usually recommends a विधि or<BR>precept by stating the good arising from<BR>its proper observance, and the<BR>evils arising from its omission, and<BR>also by adducing historical<BR>instances in its support; स्तुतिर्निदा<BR>परकृतिः पुराकल्प इत्यर्थवादः Gaut. S.;<BR>(said by Laugākṣi to be of three<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0167-c" target="_blank">Page0167-c+ 58</a>]<BR>kinds: --गुणवादो विरोधे स्यादनुवादोऽवधारिते ।<BR>भूतार्थवादस्तद्धानादर्थवादस्त्रिधा मतः; the last<BR>kind includes many varieties.)<BR>{3} one of the six means of finding<BR>out the tātparya (real aim and<BR>object) of any work. {4} praise,<BR>eulogy; अर्थवाद एषः । दोषं तु मे<BR>कंचित्कथय U. 1.<BR>--विज्ञानं comprehending<BR>the sense, one of the six exercises<BR>of the understanding (धीगुण).<BR>--विद्<BR>a. sensible, wise, sagacious.<BR>--विप्रकर्षः difficulty in the comprehension<BR>of the sense.<BR>--विकरणं = अर्थविक्रिया<BR>change of meaning.<BR>--विकल्पः {1}<BR>deviation from truth, perversion of<BR>fact. {2} prevarication; also<BR>˚वैकल्यं.<BR>--विशेषणं a reprehensive<BR>repetition of something uttered by<BR>another; S. D. 490.<BR>--वृद्धिः f.<BR>accumulation of wealth.<BR>--व्ययः<BR>expenditure; ˚ज्ञ a. conversant with<BR>money-matters.<BR>--शास्त्रं {1} the<BR>science of wealth (political economy).<BR>{2} science of polity, political<BR>science, politics; Dk. 120; इह खलु<BR>अर्थशास्त्रकारास्त्रिविधां सिद्धिमुपवर्णयंति<BR>Mu. 3; ˚व्यवहारिन् one dealing with<BR>politics, a politician; Mu. 5. {3}<BR>science giving precepts on general<BR>conduct, the science of practical life;<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--शौचं purity or honesty in<BR>money-matters; सर्वेषां चैव<BR>शौचानामर्थशौचं परं स्मृतं Ms. 5. 106.<BR>--संस्थानं {1}<BR>accumulation of wealth. {2} treasury.<BR>--संग्रहः, --संचयः accumulation or<BR>acquisition of wealth, wealth,<BR>treasure, property.<BR>--समाजः aggregate<BR>of causes.<BR>--समाहारः {1} treasure.<BR>{2} acquisition of wealth.<BR>--संपद् f.<BR>accomplishment of a desired object;<BR>Ki. 1. 15.<BR>--संबंधः connection of<BR>the sense with he word or sentence.<BR>--साधक a. {1} accomplishing any<BR>object. {2} bringing any matter to<BR>a conclusion.<BR>--सारः considerable<BR>wealth; Pt. 2. 42.<BR>--सिद्ध a.<BR>understood from the very context (though<BR>not expressed in words),<BR>inferable from the connection of words.<BR>--सिद्धिः f. fulfilment of a desired<BR>object, success.<BR>--हर a. inheriting<BR>wealth.<BR>--हीन a. {1} deprived of<BR>wealth, poor. {2} unmeaning,<BR>nonsensical. {3} failing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थतः
अर्थतः ind. [अर्थ-तसिल्]<BR>1 With<BR>reference to the meaning or a<BR>particular object; यच्चार्थतो गौरवं<BR>Māl. 1. 7 depth of meaning; Śi. 7. 28.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">Page0168-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--2 In fact, really, truly; न नामतः<BR>केवलमर्थतोऽपि Śi. 3. 56; इत्यादिष्टमर्थतो<BR>भवति Mv. 3.<BR>--3 For the sake of<BR>money, gain or profit;<BR>ऐश्वर्यादनपेतमीश्वरमयं लोकोर्थतः सेवते Mu. 1. 14.<BR>--4<BR>On account of, by reason of.<BR>--5 By<BR>reason of wealth or a particular<BR>purpose; अर्थतः पुरुषो नारी या नारी<BR>सार्थतः पुमान् Mk. 3. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थना
अर्थना Request, entreaty, suit,<BR>petition; N. 5. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवत्|अर्थवन्त्
अर्थवत् a.<BR>1 Wealthy, rich;<BR>R. 14. 23.<BR>--2 Significant, full of sense or<BR>meaning; अर्थवान् खलु मे राजशब्दः<BR>Ś. 5; Pt. 1. 136; Ki. 3. 51.<BR>--3 Having<BR>meaning; अर्थवदधातुरप्रत्ययः प्रातिपदिकं<BR>P. I. 2. 45.<BR>--4 Serving some purpose;<BR>successful, useful; स पुमानर्थवज्जन्मा<BR>Ki. 11. 62; 10. 62. --adv. According<BR>to a purpose. --m.<BR>--(वान्) A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थवत्ता
अर्थवत्ता Wealth, property; Mu. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थात्
अर्थात् ind. (abl. of अर्थ)<BR>1 As<BR>a matter of course, of course, in fact;<BR>मूषिकेण दंडो भक्षित इत्यनेन<BR>तत्सहचरितमपूपभक्षणमर्थादायातं भवति S. D. 10.<BR>--2 According to the circumstances<BR>or state of the case; as a matter of<BR>fact.<BR>--3 That is to say, namely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थापय
अर्थापय = अर्थ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिकः|अर्थिक
अर्थिकः [अर्थयते इत्यर्थी कन्]<BR>1 A<BR>crier, watchman.<BR>--2 Especially, a<BR>minstrel whose duty it is to<BR>announce (by song &c.) the different<BR>fixed periods of the day, such as<BR>the hours of rising, sleeping,<BR>eating &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थित
अर्थित p. p. Requested, asked,<BR>desired.<BR>--तं [भावे-क्त] Wish, desire;<BR>supplication, petition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिता
अर्थिता, --त्वं<BR>1 State or condition of<BR>a supplicant, begging, request; न<BR>व्यहन्यत कदाचिदर्थिता R. 11. 2; M. 3;<BR>K. 141,; तेनार्थित्वं त्वयि<BR>विधिवशाद् दूरबंधुर्गतोऽहं Me. 6; Mv. 2. 9.<BR>--2<BR>Wish, desire; R. 14. 42;<BR>अनर्थित्वान्मनुष्याणां Pt. 1. 142; Ki. 13. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थित्वं|अर्थित्व
अर्थिता, --त्वं<BR>1 State or condition of<BR>a supplicant, begging, request; न<BR>व्यहन्यत कदाचिदर्थिता R. 11. 2; M. 3;<BR>K. 141,; तेनार्थित्वं त्वयि<BR>विधिवशाद् दूरबंधुर्गतोऽहं Me. 6; Mv. 2. 9.<BR>--2<BR>Wish, desire; R. 14. 42;<BR>अनर्थित्वान्मनुष्याणां Pt. 1. 142; Ki. 13. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थिन्
अर्थिन् a. [अर्थ्-इनि]<BR>1 Seeking to<BR>gain or obtain, wishing for, desirous<BR>of, with instr. or in comp; तुषैरर्थिनः<BR>Dk. 132; कोषदंडाभ्यां Mu. 5; को<BR>वधेन ममार्थी स्यात् Mb., Ve. 6. 25; अर्थार्थी<BR>Pt. 1. 4, 9.<BR>--2 Entreating or begging<BR>any one (with gen.); अर्थी<BR>वररुचिर्मेऽस्तु Ks.<BR>--3 Possessed of desires;<BR>अनर्थी प्रार्थनावहः R. 10. 18. --m.<BR>1 One<BR>who asks, begs or solicits; a beggar,<BR>suppliant, suitor; यथाकामार्चितार्थिनां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-b" target="_blank">Page0168-b+ 57</a>]<BR>R. 1. 6; 2. 64; 5. 31; 9. 27; कोर्थी<BR>गतो गौरवं Pt. 1. 146;<BR>कन्यारत्नमयोनिजन्म भवतामास्ते वयं चार्थिनः<BR>Mv. 1. 30.<BR>--2 (In law) A plaintiff,<BR>complainant, prosecutor; स धर्मस्थसखः<BR>शश्वदार्थिप्रत्यर्थिनां स्वयं । ददर्श संशयच्छेद्यान्<BR>व्यवहारानतंद्रितः R. 17. 39.<BR>--3 A servant,<BR>follower.<BR>--4 A master or lord.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भावः state of a suppliant,<BR>begging, request; Māl. 9. 30.<BR>--सात्<BR>adv. at the disposal of beggars;<BR>विभज्य मेरुर्न यदर्थिसात्कृतः N. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थीय
अर्थीय a. [अर्थ-छ] (In comp.)<BR>1<BR>Destined or intended for, doomed<BR>to suffer; शरीरं यातनार्थीयं Ms. 12. 16.<BR>--2 Belonging or relating to; कर्म चैव<BR>तदर्थीयं Bg. 17. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्थ्य|अर्थ्यं|अर्थ्यः
अर्थ्य a. [अर्थ्-कर्मणि ण्यत्]<BR>1 Fit to<BR>be asked or sought for.<BR>--2 [अर्थादनपेतः,<BR>अर्थ-यत्] Fit, proper, suitable; अर्थ्यो<BR>विरोधः Mv. 2. 7.<BR>--3 Appropriate,<BR>not deviating from the sense,<BR>significant; स्तुत्यं स्तुतिभिरर्थ्याभिरुपतस्थे<BR>सरस्वती R. 4. 6, 1. 59; Ku. 2. 3.<BR>--4<BR>Rich, wealthy.<BR>--5 Wise, intelligent.<BR>--र्थ्यं Red chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्द्|अर्द्द्
अर्द् {c1c} P. [अर्दति, आनर्द, आर्दीत्,<BR>अर्दितुं, अर्दित or अर्ण]<BR>1 To afflict,<BR>torment; strike, hurt, kill; रक्षःसहस्राणि<BR>चतुर्दशार्दीत् Bk. 12. 56, see caus. below.<BR>--2 To beg, request, ask;<BR>निर्गलितांबुगर्भं शरद्घनं नार्दति चातकोपि R. 5. 17.<BR>--3 To go.<BR>--4 To move, be agitated<BR>or moved; be scattered (as dust);<BR>fly in pieces, dissolve (Ved.). (The<BR>past participle is usually अर्दित, but<BR>अर्ण when the root is preceded by<BR>अभि, नि, वि, सं; cf. P. VII. 2. 24-5).<BR>--Caus. (or {c10c} P.)<BR>1 (a) To afflict,<BR>torment, distress; तत एनं<BR>महावेगैरर्दयामास तोमरैः Mb.; कामार्दित, कोप˚,<BR>भय˚ &c. (b) To strike, hurt,<BR>injure, kill; येनार्दिदत् दैत्यपुरं पिनाकी<BR>Bk. 2. 46; 9. 19; 15. 90.<BR>--2 To stir<BR>up, rouse, agitate, shake<BR>vehemently, make agitated or restless.<BR>--3 To<BR>distort; अर्दयित्वानिलो वक्त्रमर्दितं<BR>जनयत्यतः Suśruta. --WITH अति to<BR>torment excessively, fall upon or<BR>attack; अत्यार्दीत् वालिनः पुत्रं<BR>Bk. 15. 115.<BR>--अभि to distress, afflict, pain,<BR>oppress; अभ्यर्दितो वृषलः (शीतेन<BR>पीडितः) P. VII. 2. 25 Sk.<BR>--नि Ved. to<BR>stream forth, flow out.<BR>--प्र to<BR>overwork, to work or exert oneself<BR>beyond measure; to cause to flow away.<BR>--प्रति to oppress or press hard in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-c" target="_blank">Page0168-c+ 57</a>]<BR>return, assail in return, return an<BR>attack.<BR>--वि Ved. to go or move<BR>away; to oppress, harass, pain.<BR>(--caus.) to cause to be scattered<BR>or dissolved, destroy, annihilate.<BR>--सं caus. to pain greatly, wound,<BR>distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दन|अर्दनं|अर्दनः|अर्द्दन
अर्दन a.<BR>1 Distressing, afflicting,<BR>tormenting; पुर˚, बल˚.<BR>--2 Moving<BR>restlessly, being agitated.<BR>--नं [भावे<BR>ल्युट्] Distressing, afflicting; pain,<BR>trouble, anxiety, disturbance,<BR>excitement, agitation, restlessness.<BR>--नं, --ना<BR>1 Going, moving.<BR>--2<BR>Asking, begging.<BR>--3 Killing, hurting,<BR>giving pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दनिः|अर्दनि
अर्दनिः<BR>1 Asking, begging.<BR>--2<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>--3 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दित|अर्दितं|अर्द्दित|अर्द्दितः
अर्दित p. p. [अर्द्-क्त] Tormented,<BR>afflicted; begged &c.<BR>--तं A disease,<BR>spasm of the jaw-bones, tetanus or<BR>hemiplegia^1 (paralysis of the muscles<BR>on one side of the face and neck).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्दितिन्|अर्द्दितिन्
अर्दितिन् a. [अर्दितमस्त्यस्य-इनि]<BR>Suffering from the spasms of jaw-bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ध|अर्द्धं|अर्द्धः|अर्धः
अर्ध a. [ऋध्-णिच् अच्; according<BR>to Nir. from धृ, or ऋध्] Half,<BR>forming a half (divided into 2 parts);<BR>अर्ध-अर्ध the one half-the other half.<BR>--र्धः [ऋध्-घञ्]<BR>1 A place, region,<BR>country; house, habitation (Ved.).<BR>--2 Increase (वृद्धि).<BR>--3 Wind.<BR>--4 A<BR>part, portion, side.<BR>--र्धं, --र्धः<BR>1 A half,<BR>half portion; सर्वनाशे समुत्पन्ने अर्धं<BR>त्यजति पंडितः; गतमर्धं दिवसस्य V. 2;<BR>पूर्वार्धः first half; so उत्तर˚ latter half;<BR>दक्षिण˚ southern half (half on the<BR>right side); so जघन˚, अवर˚, पर˚,<BR>ग्राम˚ &c.; यदर्धे विच्छिन्नं Ś. 1. 9<BR>divided in half; ऋज्वायतार्धं M. 27;<BR>R. 3. 59, 12. 99; रात्रौ तदर्धं गतं Bh. 3. 107; one<BR>part of two, apart, partly (Ved.);<BR>--2 Nearness, proximity; see अर्धदेव.<BR>अर्ध may be compounded with<BR>almost every noun and adjective;<BR>as first member of compound<BR>with nouns it means ‘a half of’,<BR>and forms an एकदोशिसमास or तत्पुरुष;<BR>˚कायः = अर्धं कायस्य; ˚पिप्पली, ˚मार्गः;<BR>˚पुरुषः &c.; with adjectives, it has an<BR>adverbial force; ˚श्याम half dark;<BR>˚भुक्त half eaten; so ˚पिष्ट, ˚पूर्ण &c.;<BR>with numeral adjectives it may<BR>mean either ‘a half of’ or ‘with an<BR>additional half’; ˚शतं half of 100 i. e.<BR>50; or अर्धेन सहितं शतं i. e. 150; with<BR>ordinal numerals ‘with a half of that<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0169-a" target="_blank">Page0169-a+ 58</a>]<BR>number;’ ˚तृतीयं containing two and<BR>the third only half; i. e. two and a<BR>half; so ˚चतुर्थ three and a half.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षि n. side-look, wink;.<BR>Mk. 8. 42.<BR>--अंगं half the body.<BR>--अंतरं half the distance; ˚एकपदता a<BR>fault in composition; see S. D. 575.<BR>--अंशः a half, the half.<BR>--अंशिन् a.<BR>sharing a half.<BR>--अर्धः, --र्धं {1} half of a<BR>half, quarter; चरोरर्धार्धभागाभ्यां<BR>तामयोजयतामुभे R. 10. 56. {2} half and half.<BR>--अवभेदकः {1} pain in half the head,<BR>hemicrania (Mar. अर्धशिशी).<BR>--(कं)<BR>dividing in equal parts.<BR>--अवशेष a.<BR>having only a half left.<BR>--आकारः {1} half<BR>the letter अ. {2} N. of अवग्रह q. v.<BR>--आसनं {1} half a seat; अर्धासनं<BR>गोत्रभिदोधितष्ठौ R. 6. 73; मम हि दिवौकसां<BR>समक्षमर्धासनोपवेशितस्य Ś. 7 (it being<BR>considered a mark of very great<BR>respect to make room for a guest<BR>&c. on the same seat with oneself).<BR>{2} greeting kindly or with great<BR>respect. {3} exemption from<BR>censure.<BR>--इंदुः {1} the half or crescent<BR>moon. {2} semicircular<BR>impression of a fingernail,<BR>crescentshaped nail-print; N. 6. 25. {3}<BR>an arrow with a crescent-shaped<BR>head (= अर्धचंद्र below.); ˚मौलि N. of<BR>Śiva Me. 56.<BR>--इंद्र a. that of which<BR>a half belongs to Indra.<BR>--उक्त a.<BR>half said or uttered; रामभद्र इति<BR>अर्धोक्ते महाराज U. 1.<BR>--उक्तिः f. a broken<BR>speech; an interrupted speech.<BR>--उदकं<BR>water reaching half the body.<BR>--उदयः<BR>{1} the rising of the half moon. {2}<BR>partial rise. {3} a kind of parvan; ˚आसनं<BR>a sort of posture in meditation.<BR>--उदित a. {1} half risen. {2} half<BR>uttered.<BR>--ऊरुकं a. [अर्धमूरोः अर्धोरु तत्र काशते]<BR>reaching to the middle of the thighs.<BR>--(कं) {1} a short petti-coat (Mar.<BR>परकर); see चंडातक. {2} mantle, veil.<BR>--कृत a. half done, incomplete.<BR>--केतुः N. of Rudra.<BR>--कोशः a<BR>moiety of one's treasure.<BR>--कौडविक a.<BR>measuring half a kuḍava.<BR>--खारं, --री a<BR>kind of measure, half a Khāri;<BR>P. V. 4. 101.<BR>--गंगा N. of the river Kāverī;<BR>(स्नानादौ गंगास्नानार्धफलदायिनी); so<BR>˚जाह्नवी.<BR>--गर्भ a. Ved. {1} in the<BR>middle of the womb. {2} N. of the<BR>rays of the sun.<BR>--गुच्छः a necklace<BR>of 24 strings.<BR>--गुंजा half a gunja.<BR>--गोलः a hemisphere.<BR>--चक्रवर्तिन्,<BR>--चक्रिन् m. N. of the nine black<BR>Vasudevas and the nine enemies of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0169-b" target="_blank">Page0169-b+ 58</a>]<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--चंद्र a. crescent-shaped.<BR>--(द्रः)<BR>{1} the half moon, crescent moon;<BR>सार्धचंद्रं बिभर्ति यः Ku. 6. 75. {2}<BR>the semicircular marks on a<BR>peacock's tail. {3} an arrow with a<BR>crescent-shaped head;<BR>अर्धचंद्रमुखैर्बाणैश्चिच्छेद कदलीसुखम् R. 12. 96. {4}<BR>a crescent-shaped nail-print. {5}<BR>the hand bent into a semicircle, as<BR>for the purpose of seizing or<BR>clutching anything; ˚द्रं दा to seize by the<BR>neck and turn out; दीयतामेतस्यार्धचंद्रः<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--(द्रा) N. of a plant (कर्णस्फोट).<BR>--चंद्राकार, --चंद्राकृति a.<BR>half-moonshaped. (--रः, --तिः f.) a meniscus.<BR>--चंद्रिका N. of a climbing plant.<BR>--चोलकः a short bodice.<BR>--जरतीयन्यायः a kind of न्याय, see under न्याय.<BR>--तनुः f. half the body.<BR>--तिक्तः N.<BR>of a plant (नेपालनिंब).<BR>--तूरः a kind<BR>of musical instrument.<BR>--दिनं, --दिवसः<BR>{1} half a day, mid-day. {2} a day of<BR>12 hours.<BR>--देवः {1} demi-god. {2}<BR>Ved. being near the gods; (देवानां<BR>समीपे वर्तमानः Sāy.).<BR>--द्रौणिक a.<BR>measuring a half drona.<BR>--धारः a<BR>knife or lancet with a single edge<BR>(one of the 20 surgical instruments<BR>mentioned by Suśruta).<BR>--नाराचः a<BR>crescent-shaped iron-pointed arrow;<BR>गृध्रलक्षवेधी अर्धनाराचः V. 5.<BR>--नारायणः a form of Viṣṇu.<BR>--नारीशः,<BR>--नारीश्वरः a form of Śiva, (half male<BR>and half female).<BR>--नावं half a boat.<BR>--निशा midnight.<BR>--पंचाशत् f.<BR>twenty-five.<BR>--पणः a measure<BR>containing half a paṇa.<BR>--पथं half way.<BR>--(थे)<BR>midway Y. 2. 198.<BR>--पादः half a pāda<BR>or foot; अर्धपादं किष्कुविष्कंभमुद्धृत्य<BR>Dk. 109.<BR>--पादिक a. having half a<BR>foot; Ms. 8. 325.<BR>--पांचालिक a. born<BR>or produced in the ardhapanchāla.<BR>--पारावतः a kind of pigeon (<BR>अर्धेनांगेन पारावत इव).<BR>--पुलायितः a half<BR>gallop, canter; चित्रं चकार<BR>पदमर्धपुलायितेन Śi. 5. 10.<BR>--प्रहरः half a watch,<BR>one hour and a half.<BR>--भागः a half,<BR>half a share or part; तदर्धभागेन<BR>लभस्व कांक्षितं Ku. 5. 50; R. 7. 45.<BR>--भागिक a. sharing a half; मृते पितरि<BR>कुर्युस्तं भ्रातरस्त्वर्धभागिकं Y. 2. 134.<BR>--भाज् a. {1} sharing a half, entitled<BR>to a half; Ms. 8. 39. {2} a<BR>companion, sharer.<BR>--भास्करः mid-day.<BR>--भोटिका a kind of cake.<BR>--भ्रमः, --मकः a<BR>kind of artificial composition; for<BR>instances see Ki. 15. 27;<BR>Śi. 19. 72. The Sar. K. describes it as a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0169-c" target="_blank">Page0169-c+ 58</a>]<BR>figure of speech thus:<BR>--आहुरर्धभ्रमं नाम<BR>श्लोकार्धभ्रमणं यदि.<BR>--माणवकः, --माणवः a<BR>necklace of 12 strings (माणवक<BR>consisting of 24).<BR>--मात्रा {1} half a (short)<BR>syllable. {2} a term for a consonant<BR>(व्यंजनं चार्धमात्रकं).<BR>--मार्गे ind.<BR>midway; V. 1. 3.<BR>--मासः half a month,<BR>a fortnight.<BR>--मासतम = ˚मासिक see<BR>P. V. 2. 57.<BR>--मासिक a. {1}<BR>happening every fortnight. {2} lasting for<BR>a fortnight; Y. 2. 177.<BR>--मुष्टिः f. a<BR>half-clenched hand.<BR>--यामः half a<BR>watch.<BR>--रथः [अर्धः असंपूर्णः रथः रथी]<BR>a warrior who fights on a car with<BR>another (who is not so skilled as a<BR>रथी); रणे रणेऽभिमानी च विमुखश्चापि<BR>दृश्यते । घृणी कर्णः प्रमादी च तेन मेऽर्धरथो<BR>मतः Mb.<BR>--रात्रः [अर्धं रात्रेः] {1}<BR>midnight; अथार्धरात्रे स्तिमितप्रदीपे R. 16. 4;<BR>स्थितेऽर्धरात्रे Dk. 109. {2} a night<BR>containing half a whole day of 24 hours.<BR>--रात्रार्धदिवसः equinox.<BR>--लक्ष्मीहरिः<BR>Hari having a form half like<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR>--विसर्गः, --विसर्जनीयः the Visarga<BR>sound before क्, ख्, प्, and फ्, so called<BR>because its sign is the half of a<BR>Visarga (H).<BR>--वीक्षणं a side-look, glance,<BR>leer.<BR>--वृद्ध a. middle-aged.<BR>--वैनाशिकः N. of the followers of Kaṇāda<BR>(arguing half perishableness).<BR>--वैशसं half or incomplete murder; विधिना<BR>कृतमर्धवैशसं ननु मां कामवधे विमुंचता<BR>Ku. 4. 31.<BR>--व्यासः the radius of a<BR>circle.<BR>--शतं fifty.<BR>--शनं [अर्धमशनस्य<BR>शकं˚] half a meal.<BR>--शफरः a kind of<BR>fish.<BR>--शब्द a. having a low voice.<BR>--शेष a. having only a half left.<BR>--श्याम<BR>a. half clouded.<BR>--श्लोकः half a<BR>śloka or verse.<BR>--सम a. equal to a half.<BR>--(मं) N. of a class of metres in<BR>which the 1st and 3rd and 2nd<BR>and 4th lines have the same<BR>syllables and Gaṇas; such as पुष्पिताग्रा.<BR>--सस्य a. half the crops, half grown.<BR>--सीरिन् m. {1} a cultivator,<BR>ploughman who takes half the crop for his<BR>labour; Y. 1. 166. {2} = अर्धिक q. v.<BR>--हर, --हारिन् a. occupying the half<BR>(of the body); Ku. 1. 50,<BR>Bh. 3. 121.<BR>--हारः a necklace of 64 strings.<BR>--थस्वः half a (short) syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धक
अर्धक a. Half; see अर्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धर्चः|अर्धर्च|अर्द्धर्चः|अर्द्धर्च्च|अर्धर्चं
अर्धर्चः --चं Half a verse, hemistich;<BR>˚आदिगणः a class of words either<BR>m. or n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धर्चं|अर्धर्च|अर्द्धर्चः|अर्द्धर्च्च|अर्धर्चः
अर्धर्चः --चं Half a verse, hemistich;<BR>˚आदिगणः a class of words either<BR>m. or n.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धिक|अर्धिकः
अर्धिक a. (की f.) [अर्धमर्हति ठन्]<BR>1<BR>Measuring a half; तदर्धिक Ms. 3. 1.<BR>--2 Entitled to half a share;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">Page0170-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Y. 2. 296.<BR>--कः A half-caste man;<BR>वैश्यकन्यासमुत्पन्नो ब्राह्मणेन तु संस्कृतः । अर्धिकःस तु<BR>विज्ञेयो भोज्यो विप्रैर्न संशयः Parāśara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धिन्
अर्धिन् a. [अर्ध-अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>Sharing or entitled to a half; Ms. 8. 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्धुक
अर्धुक a. Prospering, succeeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ध्य
अर्ध्य a.<BR>1 Belonging to the half<BR>(of anything).<BR>--2 Fit to be<BR>increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पणं|अर्पण
अर्पणं [ऋ-णिच्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Placing<BR>or putting upon, setting upon;<BR>पादार्पणानुग्रहपूतपृष्ठं R. 2. 35.<BR>--2 Inserting,<BR>placing or putting in.<BR>--3 Giving,<BR>offering, resigning; स्वदेहार्पणनिष्क्रयेण<BR>R. 2. 55; मुखार्पणेषु प्रकृतिप्रगल्भाः<BR>13. 9; तत्कुरुष्व मदर्पणं Bg. 9. 27.<BR>--4<BR>Restoration, delivery, giving back; न्यास˚<BR>Ak.<BR>--5 Piercing, perforating;<BR>तीक्ष्णतुंडार्पणैर्ग्रीवां नखैः सर्वां व्यदारयत् Rām.<BR>(Said to mean also fire, god, an<BR>oblation, a Mantra and the tongue<BR>of fire-Tv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्पिसः|अर्पिस
अर्पिसः [ऋ-णिच्-इसुन् Uṇ. 4. 2]<BR>The heart; flesh in the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ब्
अर्ब् {c1c} P. (अर्बति, आनर्ब, अर्बितुं)<BR>1<BR>To go towards.<BR>--2 To kill, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्बुदः|अर्बुद|अर्बुदं|अर्ब्बुद|अर्ब्बुदः
अर्बु(र्वु)दः, --दं<BR>1 A swelling,<BR>tumour, (of various kinds); मांस˚,<BR>नासा˚, शोणित˚ &c.<BR>--2 One hundred<BR>millions.<BR>--3 N. of a mountain in<BR>the west of India (Abu).<BR>--4 A<BR>serpent-like demon killed by<BR>Indra.<BR>--5 A serpent.<BR>--6 A cloud.<BR>--7<BR>A place of pilgrimage (of the Jainas).<BR>--8 A long round mass, lump of flesh;<BR>यदि पिंडः पुमान्स्त्री चेत् पेशी नपुंसकं<BR>चेदर्बुदं Suśr; Y. 3. 75, 89 (मांसपिंड).<BR>--9 N. of a people.<BR>--10 N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वुदः|अर्वुद|अर्वुदं
अर्बु(र्वु)दः, --दं<BR>1 A swelling,<BR>tumour, (of various kinds); मांस˚,<BR>नासा˚, शोणित˚ &c.<BR>--2 One hundred<BR>millions.<BR>--3 N. of a mountain in<BR>the west of India (Abu).<BR>--4 A<BR>serpent-like demon killed by<BR>Indra.<BR>--5 A serpent.<BR>--6 A cloud.<BR>--7<BR>A place of pilgrimage (of the Jainas).<BR>--8 A long round mass, lump of flesh;<BR>यदि पिंडः पुमान्स्त्री चेत् पेशी नपुंसकं<BR>चेदर्बुदं Suśr; Y. 3. 75, 89 (मांसपिंड).<BR>--9 N. of a people.<BR>--10 N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्बुदं|अर्बुद|अर्बुदः|अर्ब्बुद|अर्ब्बुदः
अर्बु(र्वु)दः, --दं<BR>1 A swelling,<BR>tumour, (of various kinds); मांस˚,<BR>नासा˚, शोणित˚ &c.<BR>--2 One hundred<BR>millions.<BR>--3 N. of a mountain in<BR>the west of India (Abu).<BR>--4 A<BR>serpent-like demon killed by<BR>Indra.<BR>--5 A serpent.<BR>--6 A cloud.<BR>--7<BR>A place of pilgrimage (of the Jainas).<BR>--8 A long round mass, lump of flesh;<BR>यदि पिंडः पुमान्स्त्री चेत् पेशी नपुंसकं<BR>चेदर्बुदं Suśr; Y. 3. 75, 89 (मांसपिंड).<BR>--9 N. of a people.<BR>--10 N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वुदं|अर्वुद|अर्वुदः
अर्बु(र्वु)दः, --दं<BR>1 A swelling,<BR>tumour, (of various kinds); मांस˚,<BR>नासा˚, शोणित˚ &c.<BR>--2 One hundred<BR>millions.<BR>--3 N. of a mountain in<BR>the west of India (Abu).<BR>--4 A<BR>serpent-like demon killed by<BR>Indra.<BR>--5 A serpent.<BR>--6 A cloud.<BR>--7<BR>A place of pilgrimage (of the Jainas).<BR>--8 A long round mass, lump of flesh;<BR>यदि पिंडः पुमान्स्त्री चेत् पेशी नपुंसकं<BR>चेदर्बुदं Suśr; Y. 3. 75, 89 (मांसपिंड).<BR>--9 N. of a people.<BR>--10 N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्बुदिः|अर्बुदि
अर्बुदिः<BR>1 A serpent-like demon<BR>conquered by Indra.<BR>--2<BR>All-pervading lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्बुदिन्
अर्बुदिन् a. Afflicted with swelling<BR>or tumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भ|अर्भः
अर्भ a. [ऋ-भन् Uṇ. 3. 152] Ved.<BR>Little, small, unimportant;<BR>--र्भः A<BR>child, pupil. [cf. L. orbus.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भक|अर्भकः
अर्भक a. [According to Nir.<BR>अवहृतं भवति ह्रस्वं तस्मादर्भकः.]<BR>1 Small,<BR>minute, short; नमो महद्भ्यो<BR>नमोअर्भकेभ्यः Rv. 1. 27. 13.<BR>--2 Weak,<BR>emaciated, lean.<BR>--3 Foolish.<BR>--4 Young,<BR>childish.<BR>--5 Like, similar.<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>A boy, child; श्रुतस्य यायादयमंतमर्भकः<BR>R. 3. 21, 25, 7. 67.<BR>--2 The young<BR>of an animal.<BR>--3 A fool, idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्भग
अर्भग a. Ved. Youthful, young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्मः|अर्म|अर्मं|अर्म्म|अर्म्मं
अर्मः --र्मं [ऋ-मन् Uṇ. 1. 137]<BR>1<BR>A disease of the eye.<BR>--2 A country<BR>to which one should go (गंतव्यदेशः<BR>or चिरंतनग्रामनिवासः).<BR>--3 A cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्मं|अर्म|अर्मः|अर्म्म|अर्म्मं
अर्मः --र्मं [ऋ-मन् Uṇ. 1. 137]<BR>1<BR>A disease of the eye.<BR>--2 A country<BR>to which one should go (गंतव्यदेशः<BR>or चिरंतनग्रामनिवासः).<BR>--3 A cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्मक
अर्मक a. Narrow, thin.<BR>--कं<BR>Narrowness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्मणं|अर्मण|अर्म्मण|अर्म्मणः
अर्मणं A measure of one droṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्मन्|अर्म्मन्
अर्मन् n. [ऋ-मनिन्] A disease of<BR>the eye (said to be of 5 kinds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्य|अर्यः|अर्य्य|अर्य्यः
अर्य a. [ऋ-यत्]<BR>1 Excellent, best.<BR>--2 Respectable.<BR>--3 Attached, true,<BR>devoted.<BR>--4 Dear, kind.<BR>--र्यः<BR>1 A<BR>master, lord; अर्यः प्रेम्णा नो तथा<BR>वल्लभस्य Śi. 18. 52; Śānti. 1. 18.<BR>--2 A man<BR>of the third tribe, Vaiśya.<BR>--र्या<BR>1 A<BR>mistress.<BR>--2 A woman of the Vaiśya<BR>tribe.<BR>--र्यी The wife of a Vaiśya.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जारा the mistress of an<BR>Ārya.<BR>--पत्नी the wife of a true or<BR>legitimate husband.<BR>--वर्यः a Vaiśya<BR>of rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्याणी|अर्य्याणी
अर्याणी [अर्य-आनुक्-ङीप् च] A<BR>woman of the Vaiśya tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्यमन्|अर्य्यमन्
अर्यमन् m. [अर्यं श्रेष्ठं मिमीते,<BR>मा-कनिन् निपातोयं Uṇ. 1. 156]<BR>1 The sun;<BR>प्रोषितार्यमणं मेरोरंधकारस्तटीमिव<BR>Śi. 2. 39.<BR>--2 The head of the Pitṛs or<BR>Manes; पितॄणामर्यमा चास्मि Bg. 10. 29.<BR>--3 The constellation उत्तराफल्गुनी.<BR>--4<BR>N. of the arka plant.<BR>--5 One of the<BR>Ādityas.<BR>--6 A bosom-friend,<BR>play-fellow.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--देवा N. of the 12th<BR>lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्यमिक|अर्य्यमिक
अर्यमिक a. Compassionate;<BR>(diminutive of अर्यमदत्त P. V. 3. 84).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्यम्यः|अर्यम्य|अर्य्यम्य
अर्यम्यः The sun; a bosom-friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्व्
अर्व् {c1c} P. To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वटं|अर्वट|अर्व्वट
अर्वटं Ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वन्|अर्व्वन्
अर्वन् a. [ऋ-वनिप्]<BR>1 Going,<BR>moving, running.<BR>--2 Mean, unworthy,<BR>censurable (गर्ह्य Uṇ. 4. 112; कुत्सित<BR>5. 54). --m. (अर्वा, अर्वंतौ, अर्वंतः &c.)<BR>1 A<BR>horse: श्लथीकृतप्रग्रहमर्वतां व्रजाः<BR>Śi. 12. 31.<BR>--2 An epithet of a horse<BR>or its driver.<BR>--3 One of the ten<BR>horses of the moon.<BR>--4 Indra.<BR>--5<BR>A short span (गोकर्णपरिमाण).<BR>--ती<BR>1 A mare.<BR>--2 A bawd, procuress.<BR>--3 A nymph.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वसुः one of<BR>the principal seven rays of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वश
अर्वश a. Possessed of coursers,<BR>quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वांच्|अर्वाञ्च्
अर्वांच् a. [अवरे काले देशे वा अंचति<BR>पृषो˚ अर्वादेशः]<BR>1 Coming hitherward<BR>(opp. परांच्).<BR>--2 Turned towards<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-c" target="_blank">Page0170-c+ 57</a>]<BR>coming to meet any one.<BR>--3 Being<BR>on this side (as the bank of a river);<BR>(opp. पर).<BR>--4 Being below or<BR>behind (in time or place).<BR>--5<BR>Following, subsequent.<BR>--क् ind.<BR>1<BR>Hitherward, on this side.<BR>--2<BR>From a certain point.<BR>--3 Before<BR>(in time or place); यत्सृष्टेरर्वाक्<BR>सलिलमयं ब्रह्मांडमभूत् K. 125; अर्वाक्<BR>संवत्सरात्स्वामी हरेत परतो नृपः Y. 2. 173, 113;<BR>1. 254; Ms. 8. 30; 5. 59.<BR>--4 On the<BR>lower side, behind, downwards (opp.<BR>ऊर्ध्वं).<BR>--5 Afterwards, subsequently.<BR>--6 (With loc.) Within, near; एते<BR>चार्वागुपवनभुवि छिन्नदर्भांकुरायां । Ś. 1. 15.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कालः posterior time.<BR>--कालिक a. belonging to proximate time,<BR>modern; ˚ता modernness, posterity<BR>of time; Ms. 12. 96.<BR>--कूलं the near<BR>bank of a river.<BR>--बिल a. Ved.<BR>having the hole or mouth hitherward.<BR>--वसु a. offering riches.<BR>--(सुः) {1} rain.<BR>{2} a cloud.<BR>--सामन् n. Ved. epithet<BR>of three days during which the Soma<BR>sacrifice is performed.<BR>--स्रोतस् m. N.<BR>of a creation of beings in which the<BR>current of nutriment tends<BR>downwards, or where the men are<BR>addicted to sensual enjoyments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वाके
अर्वाके ind. In the proximity of,<BR>near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वाचीन|अर्व्वाचीन|अर्व्वाचीनः
अर्वाचीन a. [अर्वाच्-ख]<BR>1 Turned<BR>towards; favouring.<BR>--2 Being on<BR>this side, below.<BR>--3 Born afterwards,<BR>posterior.<BR>--4 Modern, recent.<BR>--5<BR>Reverse, contrary; ˚ता state of<BR>being posterior or recent; state of being<BR>contrary.<BR>--नं ind. (With abl.)<BR>1<BR>On this side of.<BR>--2 Thenceforward.<BR>--3 Less than.<BR>--4 Later than; यदूर्ध्वं<BR>पृथिव्या अर्वाचीनमंतरीक्षात् Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वावत्|अर्व्वावत्
अर्वावत् a. [अवरकालोऽस्त्यस्य मतुप्<BR>पृषो˚] Later, modern. --f. Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वावसु|अर्व्वावसु
अर्वावसु N. of the Hotṛ of the<BR>Gods (देवानां होता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्वुक|अर्व्वुक
अर्वुक [अर्व्-हिंसनें बाहु˚ उकञ्] N. of<BR>a tribe or people in the south<BR>mentioned in the Mahābhārata and<BR>conquered by Sahadeva; N. of kings<BR>living in the southern forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्श|अर्शं|अर्शः
अर्श a. Bringing misfortune,<BR>sinful; indecent.<BR>--र्शः<BR>1 Damage, hurt.<BR>--2 = अर्शस् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस्
अर्शस् n. [ऋ-असुन् व्याधौ शुट् च<BR>Uṇ. 4. 195] Piles.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--घ्न a.<BR>destroying piles.<BR>--(घ्नः) {1} N. of the plant<BR>शुरण, so called because it is said<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-a" target="_blank">Page0171-a+ 57</a>]<BR>to cure piles. {2} one part of<BR>buttermilk with three parts of water.<BR>--(घ्नी) {1} N. of the plant Curculigo<BR>Archioides Lin. {2} the marking<BR>nut plant (भल्लातक).<BR>--युज् a. afflicted<BR>with piles.<BR>--हित a. curing piles.<BR>--(तः) the marking nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शस|अर्शसः
अर्शस a. [अर्शस्-अस्त्यर्थे-अच्]<BR>Afflicted with piles; Ms. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शिन्
अर्शिन् a. [अर्शमस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>Afflicted with piles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्शसान|अर्शसानः
अर्शसान a. [ऋश्-असानुच् सुट्च]<BR>Striving to hurt, malicious.<BR>--नः<BR>1<BR>Fire.<BR>--2 N. of a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्षण
अर्षण a. [ऋष् गतौ ल्युट्] Flowing,<BR>moveable.<BR>--णं Going, moving.<BR>--णी<BR>1 Means of moving, conveyance.<BR>--2 A piercing or pricking pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह्
अर्ह् {c1c} P. [अर्हति, अर्हितुं, आनर्ह, अर्हित]<BR>(epic A. as रावणो नार्हते पूजां Rām.)<BR>1<BR>To deserve, merit, be worthy of<BR>(with acc. or inf.); किमिव<BR>नायुष्मानमरेश्वरान्नार्हति Ś. 7; so दंडं, प्रायश्चित्तं,<BR>वधं &c.<BR>--2 To have a right to, be<BR>entitled to, be allowed to do any<BR>thing (with acc.); ननु गर्भः पित्र्यं<BR>रिक्थमर्हति Ś. 6; न स्त्री स्वातंत्र्यमर्हति<BR>Ms. 9. 3; also with inf.; न स<BR>तल्लब्धुमर्हति Ms. 8. 147; 11. 7, 18.<BR>--3 To<BR>be obliged or required to do a thing,<BR>oft. implying duty or obligation;<BR>नान्यत्स्त्री दातुमर्हति Y. 2. 49; इमां<BR>प्रसादयितुमर्हसि R. 1. 88.<BR>--4 To be fit or<BR>deserve to be done; अर्थना मयि<BR>भवद्भिः कर्तुमर्हति N. 5. 112; Dk. 137.<BR>--5<BR>To be equal to; be worth, न ते<BR>गात्राण्युपचारमर्हंति Ś. 3. 18 are not<BR>equal to; सर्वे ते जपयज्ञस्य कलां<BR>नार्हंति षोडशीं Ms. 2. 86; 3. 131.<BR>--6<BR>To be able, translateable by ‘can’;<BR>न मे वचनमन्यथा भवितुमर्हति Ś. 4;<BR>विनाशमव्ययस्यास्य न कश्चित्कर्तुमर्हति<BR>Bg. 2. 17; अनुद्योगेन तैलानि तिलेभ्यो<BR>नाप्तुमर्हति H. Pr. 30 cannot get.<BR>--7 To<BR>worship, honour; see caus. below.<BR>--8 (Used with inf. in the second<BR>pers. and sometimes in the third)<BR>अर्ह् represents a mild form of<BR>command, advice or courteous request,<BR>and may be translated by ‘pray’,<BR>‘deign’, ‘be pleased to’, ‘will be<BR>pleased to’; द्वित्राण्यहान्यर्हसि सोढुमर्हन्<BR>R. 5. 25 pray wait &c; नार्हसि मे प्रणयं<BR>विहंतुं 2. 58; तं संतः श्रोतुमर्हंति 1. 10<BR>will be pleased or be good enough<BR>to listen to it; Ku. 6. 32;<BR>Ms. 1. 2; Bg. 10. 16, 2. 17; R. 1. 72; 1. 88;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">Page0171-b+ 58</a>]<BR>3. 46. --Caus. or {c10c} P. To honour,<BR>worship; राजार्जिहत्तं मधुपर्कपाणिः<BR>Bk. 1. 17; Ms. 3. 3, 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह|अर्हः
अर्ह a.<BR>1 Respectable, worthy of<BR>respect, deserving; अर्हावभोजयन्<BR>विप्रो दंडमर्हति माषकं Ms. 8. 392.<BR>--2<BR>Worthy of, having a claim to,<BR>entitled to, with acc., inf., or in comp.;<BR>नैवार्हः पैतृकं रिक्थं पतितोत्पादितो हि सः<BR>Ms. 9. 144; संस्कारमर्हस्त्वं न च लप्स्यसे<BR>Rām.; तस्मान्नार्हा वयं हंतुं धार्तराष्ट्रान्<BR>स्वबांधवान् Bg. 1. 37; प्रदक्षिणक्रियार्हायां<BR>R. 1. 76; so मान˚, वध˚, दंड˚ &c.<BR>--3<BR>Being required, obliged, or allowed<BR>(with inf.).<BR>--4 Becoming, proper,<BR>fit; केवलं यानमर्हं स्यात् Pt. 3; with<BR>gen. also; स भृत्योर्हो महीभुजां<BR>Pt. 1. 87-92; or in comp; तदर्हेण प्रायश्चित्तेन<BR>1. 275; so नृप˚, यज्ञ˚ Ak.<BR>--5 Worth<BR>(in money), costing; see below.<BR>--र्हः<BR>[अर्ह्-घञ्]<BR>1 N. of Indra.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 Price (as in महार्ह);<BR>महार्हशय्यापरिवर्तनच्युतैः Ku. 5. 12 (<BR>महानर्हो यस्याः Malli.).<BR>--4 Fitness,<BR>propriety.<BR>--5 Motion, course (गति).<BR>--र्हा<BR>Worship, adoration; Ki. 2. 58;<BR>R. 1. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हणं|अर्हण
अर्हणं-णा [अर्ह-भावे-ल्युट्] Worship,<BR>adoration, honour, treating with<BR>respect or veneration; अर्हणामर्हते<BR>चक्रुर्मुनयो नयचक्षुषे R. 1. 55; Śi. 15. 22;<BR>14. 58, R. 11. 23, Ms. 3. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हणा
अर्हणं-णा [अर्ह-भावे-ल्युट्] Worship,<BR>adoration, honour, treating with<BR>respect or veneration; अर्हणामर्हते<BR>चक्रुर्मुनयो नयचक्षुषे R. 1. 55; Śi. 15. 22;<BR>14. 58, R. 11. 23, Ms. 3. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हणा
अर्हणा ind. Ved. According to what<BR>is due; according to one's means.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हणीय
अर्हणीय pot. p. Fit to be<BR>worshipped, adored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हत्|अर्हन्त्
अर्हत् a. [अर्ह-शतृ]<BR>1 Worthy,<BR>deserving, deserving respect,<BR>respectable, adorable; Ś. 5. 15; R. 5. 25;<BR>1. 55; Ku. 6. 56; Ms. 3. 128.<BR>--2<BR>Praised, celebrated (स्तुत, ख्यात).<BR>--3<BR>Worthy of, deserving, entitled to<BR>(mostly Ved.). --m.<BR>1 A Buddha;<BR>the highest rank in Buddhist<BR>hierarchy.<BR>--2 A superior divinity with<BR>the Jainas; सर्वज्ञो<BR>जितरागादिदोषस्त्रैलोक्यपूजितः । यथास्थितार्थवादी च देवोर्हन् परमेश्वरः ।;<BR>see the word जैन also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हंत|अर्हन्त|अर्हन्तः
अर्हंत a. [अर्ह्र-बा˚ झ] Worthy,<BR>deserving.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A Buddha.<BR>--2 A<BR>Buddhist mendicant.<BR>--3 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हंती
अर्हंती The quality of being fit to<BR>be worshipped, veneration, adoration;<BR>श्रौत्रार्हंतीचणैर्गुण्यैः Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्ह्य
अर्ह्य pot. p. [अर्ह्-ण्यत्]<BR>1 Worthy.<BR>respectable.<BR>--2 Fit to be praised,<BR>--3 Right, fit, proper.<BR>--4 Fit to be<BR>obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अर्हरिष्वणि
अर्हरिष्वणि a. Ved. Making<BR>enemies cry aloud; exultant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्
अल् {c1c} U. (अलति-ते, अलितुं, अलित)<BR>1 To adorn.<BR>--2 To be competent or<BR>able.<BR>--3 To prevent, ward off;<BR>see अलम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलं|अल
अलं [अल्-अच्]<BR>1 The sting in the<BR>tail of a scorpion.<BR>--2 Yellow<BR>orpiment; cf. आल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकः|अलक|अलकं
अलकः [अल्-क्वुन्, अलति भूषयति मुखं]<BR>1 A curl, lock of hair, hair in general;<BR>ललाटिकाचंदनधूसरालका Ku. 5. 55;<BR>अस्पृष्टालकवेष्टनौ R. 1. 42; 4. 54;<BR>अलकभंगतां गतः K. 4; अलके<BR>बालकुंदानुविद्धं Me. 65 (the word is n. also, as<BR>appears from a quotation of Malli.:<BR>स्वभाववक्राण्यलकानि तासां).<BR>--2 Curls on<BR>the fore-head.<BR>--3 Saffron besmeared<BR>on the body.<BR>--4 A mad dog (for<BR>अलर्क).<BR>--का<BR>1 A girl from eight to<BR>ten years of age.<BR>--2 N. of the<BR>capital of Kubera (situated on a peak<BR>of the Himālaya above the peak<BR>of Meru, inhabited also by Śiva), and<BR>of the lord of the Yakṣas;<BR>अलकामतिवाह्यैव Ku. 6. 37; विभाति यस्यां<BR>ललितालकायां मनोहरा वैश्रवणस्य लक्ष्मीः<BR>Bv. 2. 10; गंतव्या ते वसतिरलका नाम<BR>यक्षेश्वराणां Me. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः,<BR>--पतिः, --ईश्वरः ‘lord of Alakā’, N. of<BR>Kubera; अत्यजीवदमरालकेश्वरौ<BR>R. 19. 15.<BR>--अंतः the end of a curl or ringlet;<BR>Śi. 4. 9; Me. 8.<BR>--नंदा {1} N. of the<BR>Ganges, or a river falling into it.<BR>{2} a girl from eight to ten years of<BR>age.<BR>--प्रभा N. of the capital of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--प्रियः N. of a tree (<BR>पीतसाल).<BR>--संहतिः f. rows of curls;<BR>Śi. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलकं|अलक|अलकः
अलकं ind. In vain, for nothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्तः|अलक्त
अलक्तः --क्तकः [न रक्तोऽस्मात्, रस्य<BR>लत्वं, स्वार्थे कन् Tv.] The red resin<BR>of certain trees, red lac or sap<BR>(formerly used by women to dye<BR>certain parts of their body,<BR>particularly the soles of the feet and lip);<BR>(दंतवाससा) चिरोज्झितालक्तकपाटलेन<BR>Ku. 5. 34, 68; 7. 58;<BR>बिंबाधरालक्तकः M. 3. 5; अलक्तकांकां पदवीं ततान<BR>R. 7. 7; स्त्रियो हृतार्थाः पुरुषं निरर्थं<BR>निष्पीडितालक्तकवत्त्यजंति Mk. 4. 15.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रसः red lac, juice;<BR>अलक्तरसरक्ताभावलक्तरसवर्जितौ । अद्यापि चरणौ तस्याः<BR>पद्मकोशसमप्रभौ Rām.<BR>--रागः the red<BR>colour of alakta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्तकः|अलक्तक
अलक्तः --क्तकः [न रक्तोऽस्मात्, रस्य<BR>लत्वं, स्वार्थे कन् Tv.] The red resin<BR>of certain trees, red lac or sap<BR>(formerly used by women to dye<BR>certain parts of their body,<BR>particularly the soles of the feet and lip);<BR>(दंतवाससा) चिरोज्झितालक्तकपाटलेन<BR>Ku. 5. 34, 68; 7. 58;<BR>बिंबाधरालक्तकः M. 3. 5; अलक्तकांकां पदवीं ततान<BR>R. 7. 7; स्त्रियो हृतार्थाः पुरुषं निरर्थं<BR>निष्पीडितालक्तकवत्त्यजंति Mk. 4. 15.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रसः red lac, juice;<BR>अलक्तरसरक्ताभावलक्तरसवर्जितौ । अद्यापि चरणौ तस्याः<BR>पद्मकोशसमप्रभौ Rām.<BR>--रागः the red<BR>colour of alakta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षण|अलक्षणं
अलक्षण a.<BR>1 Having no signs<BR>or marks.<BR>--2 Having no characteristic<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">Page0172-a+ 57</a>]<BR>or distinguishing marks; undefined,<BR>undistinguished; Ms. 1. 5.<BR>--3<BR>Having no good marks, inauspicious,<BR>unfortunate, ill-omened; क्लेशावहा<BR>भर्तुरलक्षणाहम् R. 14. 5.<BR>--णं<BR>1 A bad<BR>or inauspicious sign; Ms. 4. 156.<BR>--2 That which is no definition, a<BR>bad definition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्षित
अलक्षित a.<BR>1 Unseen,<BR>unperceived, unobserved; अलक्षितोपस्थित<BR>H. 1; अलक्षिताभ्युत्पतनो नृपेण R. 2. 27.<BR>--2 Uncharacterized; not marked.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतक a. suddenly dead.<BR>--उपस्थित a. one who has<BR>approached unobserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्य
अलक्ष्य a.<BR>1 Invisible, unknown,<BR>unobserved.<BR>--2 Unmarked.<BR>--3<BR>Having no particular marks.<BR>--4<BR>Insignificant in appearance.<BR>--5 Having no<BR>pretence, free from fraud.<BR>--6 Not<BR>लक्ष्य or secondary (as meaning).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गति a. moving invisibly.<BR>--जन्मता unknown birth, obscure<BR>origin; वपुर्विरूपाक्षमलक्ष्यजन्मता<BR>Ku. 5. 72.<BR>--लिंग a. disguised,<BR>incognito.<BR>--वाच् a. addressing words<BR>to no visible object; Ku. 5. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलक्ष्मीः
अलक्ष्मीः f. Evil fortune, bad<BR>luck, distress, poverty; कामान् दुग्धे<BR>विप्रकर्षत्यलक्ष्मीं U. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलगर्दः|अलगर्द|अलगर्द्द
अलगर्दः [Ety. ?] A<BR>water-serpent, the black variety of the Cobra<BR>de Capello (also written अलगर्थ).<BR>--र्दा A large poisonous leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलग्ल
अलग्ल a.<BR>1 Speaking<BR>unconnectedly.<BR>--2 Stammering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलघु
अलघु (घु-घ्वी f.)<BR>1 Not light,<BR>heavy, big, weighty (as breasts, hips<BR>&c.); आयासादलघुतरस्तनैः Śi. 8. 1;<BR>7. 5.<BR>--2 Not short, long (in prosody).<BR>--3 Serious, solemn.<BR>--4 Intense,<BR>violent, very great.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपलः<BR>a rock.<BR>--ऊष्मन् m. intense heat.<BR>--प्रतिज्ञ a. solemnly pledged or promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाघवं|अलाघव
अलाघवं Meanness, niggardliness;<BR>R. 9. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंघनं|अलङ्घन|अलंघन
अलंघनं Not surmounting, not<BR>transgressing, not passing over or<BR>beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंघनीय|अलङ्घनीय
अलंघनीय a. Insurmountable,<BR>impassable, inaccessible, beyond the<BR>reach of; त्रिदशपंरिपक्षस्यालंघनीये कृते<BR>स्वः V. 2 proof against injury; V. 4,<BR>Ki. 14. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंघनीयता|अलङ्घनीयता
अलंघनीयता<BR>1 Impassableness,<BR>insurmountableness, inaccessibility;<BR>Śi. 2. 48.<BR>--2 Inviolability;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">Page0172-b+ 56</a>]<BR>respectability.<BR>--3 Authoritative or<BR>absolute rule, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंघ्य|अलङ्घ्य
अलंघ्य a.<BR>1 Not to be<BR>transgressed, overcome &c.; Śi. 3. 64.<BR>--2<BR>Beyond the reach of, impossible to be<BR>done; Ki. 13. 7.<BR>--3 Difficult to<BR>secure or attain, unattainable;<BR>Ki. 10. 6, 13; Śi. 8. 57; ˚ता state of being<BR>proof against an attack or injury;<BR>Ki. 11. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलजः|अलज
अलजः A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलजी
अलजी Inflammation of the eye;<BR>a sort of disease of the joints.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलज्ज
अलज्ज a. Shameless.<BR>--ज्जा<BR>1<BR>Boldness.<BR>--2 Impudence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंजरः|अलञ्जर|अलञ्जरः
अलंजरः, --जुरः [अलं सामर्थ्यं जृणाति,<BR>जॄ-अच्, पृषो˚उत् Tv.] An earthen jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंजुरः|अलञ्जुर|अलञ्जुरः
अलंजरः, --जुरः [अलं सामर्थ्यं जृणाति,<BR>जॄ-अच्, पृषो˚उत् Tv.] An earthen jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलतिः|अलति
अलतिः [अल्-बा˚ अतिच्]<BR>Commencement of the notes of a song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलब्ध
अलब्ध a. Unobtained.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभीप्सित a. disappointed in one's<BR>desired object.<BR>--नाथ a. friendless,<BR>without a patron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलभ्य
अलभ्य a. Unobtainable,<BR>unattainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलम्
अलम् ind. [अल्-बाहु˚ अम्]<BR>1 (a)<BR>Enough, sufficient for, adequate<BR>to (with dative or inf.); तस्यालमेषा<BR>क्षुधितस्य तृप्त्यै R. 2. 39; Ku. 6. 82;<BR>अन्यथा प्रातराशाय कुर्याम त्वामलं वयम्<BR>Bk. 8. 98; Śi. 2. 40, 106, 110;<BR>K. 133; Bh. 3. 22; Ms. 11. 77;<BR>R. 2. 39, 9. 32; 15. 64; Me. 64, 88. (b)<BR>A match for, equal to (with dat.);<BR>दैत्येभ्यो हरिरलं Sk.; अलं मल्लो मल्लाय<BR>Mbh.<BR>--2 Able, competent (with<BR>inf.); अलं भोक्तुं Sk.; वरेण शमितं<BR>लोकानलं दग्धुं हि तत्तपः Ku. 2. 56;<BR>V. 3. 10; with loc. also;<BR>त्रयाणामपि लोकानामलमस्मि निवारणे Rām.<BR>--3<BR>Away with, enough of, no need of, no<BR>use of (having a prohibitive force),<BR>with instr. or gerund; अलमन्यथा<BR>गृहीत्वा M. 1. 20; अलमलं बहु विकत्थ्य<BR>M. 1; आलप्यालमिदं बभ्रोर्यत्स दारानपाहरत्<BR>Śi. 2. 40; अलं महीपाल तव श्रमेण R. 2. 34;<BR>Ku. 5. 82; अलमियद्भिः कुसुमैः Ś. 4 so<BR>many flowers will do; Śi. 10. 75;<BR>sometimes used, though less<BR>correctly, with the inf. in the same<BR>sense; अलमात्मानं खेदयितुं Ve. 2, 3;<BR>अलं सुप्तजनं प्रबोधयितुं Mk. 3.<BR>--4 (a)<BR>Completely, thoroughly; अर्हस्येनं<BR>शमयितुमलं वारिधारासहस्रैः Me. 53;<BR>त्वमपि विततयज्ञः स्वर्गिणः प्रीणयालम् Ś. 7. 34;<BR>R. 10. 80; K. 169; Śi. 3. 58;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-c" target="_blank">Page0172-c+ 57</a>]<BR>4. 39. (b) Greatly, excessively, to a<BR>high degree; तुदंति अलम् K. 2; यो<BR>गच्छत्यलं विद्विषतः प्रति Ak.; Mv. 6. 40;<BR>इत्यलमन्वशान् मुनिर्मां Ki. 13. 13 again<BR>and again, pressingly.<BR>--5 In vain.<BR>--6 Surely, verily.<BR>--7 In the sense of<BR>अस्ति and भूषण also.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मीण<BR>a. [अलं समर्थः कर्मणे ख] competent to<BR>do any act; skilful, clever.<BR>--कुमारि a.<BR>[अलं कुमार्यै] sufficient to support a<BR>maiden (धनं); P. I. 2. 44.<BR>--कृ, --कार<BR>&c. see separately below.<BR>--गामिन् a.<BR>[अलं पर्याप्तं गच्छति, णिनि] going after,<BR>following in due or proper manner;<BR>P. V. 2. 15.<BR>--जीविक a. [अलं जीविकायै<BR>चत.] sufficient for livelihood.<BR>--जुष a.<BR>[अलंजुष्यते कर्मणि बाहु˚ क] sufficient,<BR>adequate to eating.<BR>--तम a. able,<BR>sufficient, having power.<BR>--धन a. [अलं<BR>प्रभूतं धनमस्त्यस्य अच्] possessing<BR>sufficient wealth, rich; निरादिष्टधनश्चेत्तु<BR>प्रतिभूः स्यादलंधनः Ms. 8. 162.<BR>--धूम<BR>a. [अलमत्यर्थो धूमः] thick smoke,<BR>volume of smoke.<BR>--पशुः [अलं यज्ञे<BR>निरर्थः पशुः] a bad or useless animal (for<BR>sacrifice). (--a.) able to keep cattle.<BR>--पुरुषीण a. [अलं समर्थं पुरुषाय;<BR>स्वार्थेख] {1} fit for a man, becoming a man.<BR>{2} sufficient for a man.<BR>--(णः) a man<BR>who is chief of the opposite<BR>warriors in a battle.<BR>--बल a. {1} strong<BR>enough, having sufficient power. {2}<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--बुद्धिः {1}<BR>sufficient sense. {2} false notion (<BR>मिथ्याबुद्धि).<BR>--भूष्णु a. [अलं सामर्थ्ये भू-ग्स्नु]<BR>able, competent;<BR>विनाप्यस्मदलंभूष्णुरिज्यायै तपसः सुतः Śi. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकृ|अलङ्कृ
अलंकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To prepare, make<BR>ready (Ved.).<BR>--2 To ornament,<BR>decorate, grace; तत्र च<BR>शयनीयमलंचकार K. 207; कतमो वंशोऽलंकृतः Ś. 1.<BR>--3 To prevent from, impede (with<BR>gen.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकरणं|अलङ्करण|अलंकरण|अलङ्करणं
अलंकरणं<BR>1 Decoration,<BR>ornamenting.<BR>--2 An ornament (lit. and<BR>fig.); सृजति तावदशेषगुणाकरं<BR>पुरुषरत्नमलंकरणं भुवः Bh. 2. 92.<BR>--3<BR>Preparation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकरिष्णु|अलङ्करिष्णु|अलंकरिष्णुः|अलङ्करिष्णुः
अलंकरिष्णु a.<BR>1 Fond of ornaments.<BR>--2 Decorating, skilled in decorating.<BR>--3 Ornamented.<BR>--ष्णुः An epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकर्तृ|अलङ्कर्तृ|अलङ्कर्त्तृ
अलंकर्तृ a. A decorator, skilled<BR>in decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकारः|अलङ्कार|अलंकार|अलङ्कारः
अलंकारः<BR>1 Decoration, act of<BR>decorating or ornamenting.<BR>--2 An<BR>ornament (fig. also); अलंकारः स्वर्गस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">Page0173-a+ 56</a>]<BR>V. 1; अनुत्सेकः खलु विक्रमालंकारः ibid.<BR>--3 A figure of speech of which<BR>there are three kinds:<BR>--शब्द˚, अर्थ˚,<BR>and शब्दार्थ˚; शब्दार्थयोरस्थिरा ये धर्माः<BR>शोभातिशायिनः । रसादीनुपकुर्वंतोऽलंकारास्तेंऽ<BR>गदादिवत् ॥ S. D. 631; उपकुर्वंति लं<BR>संतंयेंऽगद्वारेण जातु चित् ।<BR>हारादिवदलंकारास्तेनुप्रासोपमादयः K. P. 8.<BR>--4 The whole<BR>science of Rhetoric.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चंद्रिका a commentary on<BR>Kuvalayānanda.<BR>--शास्त्रं the science and art of<BR>rhetoric, poetics.<BR>--सुवर्णं gold used<BR>for ornaments.<BR>--सूरः N. of a kind of<BR>meditation in Buddhism.<BR>--हीन a.<BR>unadorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकारकः|अलङ्कारक
अलंकारकः Ornament, decoration;<BR>Ms. 7. 220.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंकृतिः|अलङ्कृति|अलंकृति
अलंकृतिः f.<BR>1 Decoration.<BR>--2 An<BR>ornament; कर्णालंकृति Amaru. 13.<BR>--3 A rhetorical ornament, a figure<BR>of speech; तददौषौ शब्दार्थौ<BR>सगुणावनलंकृती पुनः क्वापि K. P. 1; यो विद्वान्<BR>मन्यते काव्यं शब्दार्थावनलंकृती । असौ न<BR>मन्यते कस्मादनुष्णमनलं कृती ॥;<BR>Chandr. 1; सालंकृतिः श्रंवणकोमलवर्णराजिः<BR>Bv. 3. 6 (where अ˚ has senses 2. and 3.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंक्रिया|अलङ्क्रिया
अलंक्रिया Adorning, ornamenting,<BR>decoration (fig. also); प्रशमस्तस्य<BR>भवत्यलंक्रिया Ki. 2. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंपट|अलम्पट|अलम्पटः
अलंपट a. Not libidinous,<BR>chaste.<BR>--टः Women's apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंबुषः|अलम्बुष|अलंबुष|अलम्बुषः
अलंबुषः<BR>1 Vomiting.<BR>--2 The palm<BR>of the hand with the fingers<BR>extended.<BR>--3 Prahasta, the minister of<BR>Rāvaṇa.<BR>--4 A demon killed by<BR>Ghaṭotkacha.<BR>--षा<BR>1 N. of a nymph or of a<BR>class of nymphs.<BR>--2 A kind of plant<BR>(लज्जालु).<BR>--3 A barrier, a line of water<BR>drawn to prevent entrance (<BR>अन्याप्रवेशार्थं दत्ता जलरेखा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलय|अलयः
अलय a. [नास्ति लयः अवस्थानं यस्य]<BR>1 Houseless, vagrant, moving about;<BR>Śi. 4. 57.<BR>--2 Without destruction<BR>or loss, imperishable.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>Nondestruction, permanence^1.<BR>--2 Birth,<BR>production.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलंबुसा
अलंबुसा N. of a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलर्कः|अलर्क
अलर्कः<BR>1 A mad dog or one<BR>rendered furious.<BR>--2 A fabulous<BR>animal like a hog with eight legs.<BR>--3<BR>A kind of worm.<BR>--4 N. of a plant<BR>(श्वेतार्क).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलपस्
अलपस् n. Merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलले
अलले ind. A word of no import,<BR>occurring in the dialect of the<BR>Piśāchas (mostly used in dramas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलवालं|अलवाल
अलवालं A basin for water at<BR>the root of a tree; see आलवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलस्
अलस् a. Not shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलस|अलसः
अलस a. [न लसति व्याप्रियते,<BR>लस्-अच्]<BR>1 Inactive, without energy,<BR>lazy, idle, indolent.<BR>--2 Tired,<BR>fatigued, languid; मार्गश्रमादलसशरीरे<BR>दारिके M. 5; Amaru. 4, 90; खेदालसेव<BR>K. 143, 197, 211, 62, 98; Śi. 8. 7;<BR>V. 3. 2; Dk. 20, Śi. 13. 48; 9. 39;<BR>U. 1. 24; Ki. 10. 60, V. 5; गमनमलसं<BR>Māl. 1. 17.<BR>--3 Soft, gentle.<BR>--4 Slow,<BR>dull (as in gait or motion);<BR>श्रोणीभारादलसगमना Me. 82; तस्याः<BR>परिस्फुरितगर्भभरालसायाः U. 3. 28.<BR>--सः<BR>1 A<BR>sore or ulcer between the toes.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of tree.<BR>--3 N. of a sage.<BR>--4<BR>N. of a small poisonous animal.<BR>--सा<BR>N. of a plant (हंसपदी).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईक्षणा a woman with languishing looks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलसक|अलसकः
अलसक a. Indolent, idle.<BR>--कः<BR>Flatulence, intumescence of the<BR>abdomen, with constipation and<BR>wind; प्रयाति नोर्ध्वं नाधस्तादाहारो न च<BR>पच्यते । आमाशयोऽलसीभूतस्तेन सोऽलसकः स्मृतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलस्य
अलस्य a. Idle, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलांडुः|अलाण्डु|अलाण्डुः
अलांडुः N. of a small noxious<BR>insect or other animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलातः|अलात|अलातं
अलातः --तं [ला-क्त, न. त.] A<BR>firebrand, half-burnt wood; निवार्णालात<BR>लाघवं Ku. 2. 23 coal; ˚सदृशेक्षणा<BR>Rām.; ˚चक्रप्रतिमं V. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलातं|अलात|अलातः
अलातः --तं [ला-क्त, न. त.] A<BR>firebrand, half-burnt wood; निवार्णालात<BR>लाघवं Ku. 2. 23 coal; ˚सदृशेक्षणा<BR>Rām.; ˚चक्रप्रतिमं V. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलातृण|अलातृणः
अलातृण a. Ved.<BR>1 Disposed to<BR>afflict or injure very much.<BR>--2 Not<BR>granting anything.<BR>--णः A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबुः|अलाबु
अलाबुः --बूः f.<BR>[न-लंबते; न-लंब्-उणित् नलोपश्च वृद्धिः Tv.] The bottle-gourd.<BR>--बु (n.)<BR>1 A vessel made of gourd.<BR>--2 A fruit of the gourd which is<BR>very light and floats in water; किं<BR>हि नामैतत् अंबुनि मज्जंत्यलाबूनि ग्रावाणः<BR>प्लवंत इति Mv. 1; Ms. 6. 54.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कटं the dust or down (रजः) of<BR>the bottle-gourd.<BR>--पात्रं a jar made<BR>of the bottle-gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबूः
अलाबुः --बूः f.<BR>[न-लंबते; न-लंब्-उणित् नलोपश्च वृद्धिः Tv.] The bottle-gourd.<BR>--बु (n.)<BR>1 A vessel made of gourd.<BR>--2 A fruit of the gourd which is<BR>very light and floats in water; किं<BR>हि नामैतत् अंबुनि मज्जंत्यलाबूनि ग्रावाणः<BR>प्लवंत इति Mv. 1; Ms. 6. 54.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कटं the dust or down (रजः) of<BR>the bottle-gourd.<BR>--पात्रं a jar made<BR>of the bottle-gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाबुमय
अलाबुमय a. Made of a bottle;<BR>Y. 3. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाभ|अलाभः
अलाभ a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Without gain<BR>or profit.<BR>--भः Non-acquirement;<BR>Ms. 2. 43; 6. 57, 2. 184.<BR>--2 Loss;<BR>Ms. 9. 331, 11, 81; Bg. 2. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलाय्य
अलाय्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Going<BR>forward (to meet).<BR>--2 An assailing<BR>enemy, an assailant.<BR>--3 Epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलारं|अलार
अलारं A door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलासः|अलास
अलासः Inflammation and<BR>abscess at the root of the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलास्य
अलास्य a. Devoid of dancing,<BR>idle, unengaged; R. 16. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिः|अलि
अलिः [अल्-इन् Uṇ. 4. 138]<BR>1 A<BR>black bee.<BR>--2 A scorpion.<BR>--3 A crow.<BR>--4 The (Indian) cuckoo.<BR>--5 The sign<BR>of the zodiac called वृश्चिक.<BR>--6<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कुलं a flight<BR>or number of bees; ˚संकुल full of a<BR>swarm of bees;<BR>अलिकुलसंकुलकुसुमनिराकुलनवदलमालतमाले Gīt. 1.;<BR>˚संकुलः the kubja plant.<BR>--जिह्वा,<BR>--ह्विका [अलिरिव क्षुद्रा जिह्वा] the uvula, soft.<BR>palate.<BR>--दूर्वा N. of a plant (मालादूर्वा).<BR>--पत्रिका, --पर्णी N. of a tree (<BR>वृश्चिकपत्राख्यवृक्षः).<BR>--प्रिय a. pleasing to the bees.<BR>--(यः) the red lotus.<BR>--(या) the<BR>trumpet flower.<BR>--माला a flight of<BR>bees.<BR>--मोदा N. of a plant (गणिकारी).<BR>--विरावः, --रुतं song or hum of a bee.<BR>--वल्लभः = ˚प्रिय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन्
अलिन् m. [अल्-इनि]<BR>1 A scorpion.<BR>--2 A bee; मलिनिमाऽलिनि<BR>माधवयोषिताम् Śi. 6. 4.<BR>--नी A swarm of bees;<BR>अरमतालिनी शिलींभ्रे Śi. 6. 72;<BR>अलिनीजिष्णुः कचानां चयः Bh. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिंशः|अलिंश
अलिंशः Ved. A kind of demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिकं|अलिक
अलिकं [अल्यते भूष्यते अल्-कर्मणि इकन्]<BR>The forehead; अलिकेन च हेमकांतिना<BR>Bv. 2. 171; Vb. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिक्लवः|अलिक्लव
अलिक्लवः A kind of carrion bird<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिगर्दः|अलिगर्द
अलिगर्दः A kind of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिंग|अलिङ्ग|अलिङ्गः
अलिंग a.<BR>1 Having no<BR>characteristic marks, having no marks.<BR>--2<BR>Having bad marks.<BR>--3 (In gram.)<BR>Having no gender.<BR>--गः An epithet<BR>of the Supreme Being.<BR>--गं Absence<BR>of marks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिंगिन्|अलिङ्गिन्
अलिंगिन् m. An impostor, a<BR>pretended ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिंजरः|अलिञ्जर|अलिंजर|अलिञ्जरः
अलिंजरः A water-jar; see अलंजर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिन|अलिनः
अलिन a. [अल्-बाहु˚ इनन्] Greatly<BR>advanced in penance (तपोभिरतिवृद्ध).<BR>--नः N. of a tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिंदः|अलिन्द|अलिन्दः
अलिंदः [अल्यते भूष्यते,<BR>अल्-कर्मणि-किंदच्]<BR>1 A terrace before a<BR>housedoor; मुखालिंदतोरणं M. 5, Dk. 74.<BR>--2 A place (like a square) at the<BR>door.<BR>--3 (pl.) N. of a country or<BR>its inhabitants; or its ruler also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिपकः|अलिपक
अलिपकः<BR>1 A cuckoo.<BR>--2 A bee.<BR>--3 A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिप्सा
अलिप्सा Freedom from desire<BR>or cupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

