अलिमकः = अनिमक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिंपक|अलिम्पक
अलिंपक --बक see अनिमक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलिंबक|अलिम्बक|अलिम्बकः
अलिंपक --बक see अनिमक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीक|अलीकं
अलीक a. [अल्-वीकन् Uṇ. 4. 25<BR>निपातः]<BR>1 Unpleasing, disagreeable.<BR>--2 Untrue, false, pretended; ˚मुग्धः<BR>K. 84; अलीककोपकांतेन K. 147;<BR>˚वचन Amaru. 23, 33, 43.<BR>--3 Little, not<BR>much, few.<BR>--कं<BR>1 The forehead;<BR>दिशामलीकालकभंगतां गतः K. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Anything displeasing, falsehood,<BR>untruth.<BR>--3 Heaven.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मत्स्यः<BR>a kind of dish resembling the taste<BR>of fish (‘mock-fish’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीकायते
अलीकायते Den. A. To be deceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीकिन्
अलीकिन् a.<BR>1 Disagreeable,<BR>unpleasant.<BR>--2 False, deceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीक्य
अलीक्य a. False.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलीगर्दः|अलीगर्द
अलीगर्दः A snake; see अलिगर्द.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुः|अलु
अलुः [अल्-उन्] A small water pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुक्
अलुक्, ˚समासः [नास्ति विभक्तेः लुक्<BR>लोपो यत्र] A compound in which the<BR>case terminations are not dropped,<BR>but retained; e. g. सरसिजं, आत्मनेपदं,<BR>जनुषांधः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुक्समासः|अलुक्समास
अलुक्, ˚समासः [नास्ति विभक्तेः लुक्<BR>लोपो यत्र] A compound in which the<BR>case terminations are not dropped,<BR>but retained; e. g. सरसिजं, आत्मनेपदं,<BR>जनुषांधः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुप्त
अलुप्त a.<BR>1 Not cut off,<BR>undiminished.<BR>--2 Not destroyed, preserved;<BR>R. 2. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलुब्ध|अलुब्धः
अलुब्ध a. Moderate, content, not<BR>covetous; ˚त्वं contentment,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलूक्ष
अलूक्ष a. Soft (Ved. for अरूक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अले
अले ind. Unmeaning words<BR>in the dialect of the<BR>Piśācas chiefly introduced in plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेले
अलेले ind. Unmeaning words<BR>in the dialect of the<BR>Piśācas chiefly introduced in plays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेपक|अलेपकः
अलेपक a. Stainless.<BR>--कः An<BR>epithet of the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेश
अलेश a. Not little, much, large.<BR>--शं ind. Not at all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलेशैज
अलेशैज a. Firm, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोक|अलोकः
अलोक a.<BR>1 Not having space<BR>(Ved.).<BR>--2 That which cannot be<BR>seen, as in लोकालोक इवाचलः<BR>R. 1. 68 (न लोक्यत इत्यलोकः Malli.); see<BR>लोकालोक also.<BR>--3 Having no people.<BR>--4 One who does not go to any<BR>other world after death (not<BR>having performed meritorious deeds).<BR>--कः, --कं<BR>1 Not the world.<BR>--2<BR>End or destruction of the world;<BR>absence of people; रक्ष<BR>सर्वानिमाल्लोँकान् नालोकं कर्तुमर्हसिं Rām.<BR>--3<BR>The immaterial or spiritual world.<BR>--4 The nether world (पाताल).<BR>--5<BR>A Ṛtvij or any such priest.<BR>--6 One<BR>who is not a seer or observer.<BR>--का<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">Page0174-b+ 56</a>]<BR>A kind of bird.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सामान्य a.<BR>extraordinary, uncommon;<BR>˚गुणस्तनूजः Māl. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकनं|अलोकन
अलोकनं Invisibility,<BR>disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकनीय
अलोकनीय a. Invisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोकित
अलोकित a. Unseen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोक्य
अलोक्य a. Not securing the other<BR>world or heaven; unusual,<BR>unallowed; Ms. 2. 161; ˚ता unfitness for<BR>heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोपांग|अलोपाङ्ग
अलोपांग a. Not defective in a<BR>single limb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोभः|अलोभ
अलोभः<BR>1 Freedom from<BR>covetousness, moderation.<BR>--2<BR>Non-confusion; right process.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोभिन्
अलोभिन् a. Not wanting or<BR>desiring anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोल
अलोल a.<BR>1 Tranquil, unagitated.<BR>--2 Firm, steady.<BR>--3 Not fickle.<BR>--4<BR>Not thirsty, free from desire.<BR>--लं<BR>N. of a metre of 14 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलु
अलोलु a. Indifferent to sensual<BR>objects; ˚त्वं indifference to sensual<BR>objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोलुप
अलोलुप a.<BR>1 Free from desire.<BR>--2 Not greedy or covetous,<BR>apathetic, indifferent to sensual objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलोहित|अलोहितं
अलोहित a. Bloodless, not red.<BR>--तं Nymphæa Rubra, a red lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अलौकिक|अलौकिकः
अलौकिक a. (--की f.)<BR>1 Not<BR>current in the world, not<BR>relating to this world, uncommon,<BR>supernatural.<BR>--2 Unusual, rare.<BR>--3<BR>Not current in the usual language,<BR>peculiar to the sacred writings, not<BR>used in classics, Vedic; अधिहरि हरि<BR>ङि इत्यलौकिकं.<BR>--4 Theoretical; ˚त्वं rare<BR>occurrence of a word; अलौकिकत्वादमरः<BR>स्वकोषे न यानि नामानि समुल्लिलेख । विलोक्य<BR>तैरप्यधुना प्रचारमयं प्रयत्नः पुरुषोत्तमस्य<BR>Trik. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संनिकर्षः proximity not<BR>common to the world (of three<BR>kinds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्कः|अल्क
अल्कः<BR>1 A tree.<BR>--2 A member of<BR>the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्प|अल्पं|अल्पः
अल्प a. [अल्-प]<BR>1 Trifling,<BR>unimportant, insignificant (opp. महत्<BR>or गुरु); Ms. 11. 36.<BR>--2 Small, little,<BR>minute, scanty (opp. बहु); अल्पस्य<BR>हेतोर्बहु हातुमिच्छन् R. 2. 47; 1. 2;<BR>अल्पकुचांतरा V. 4. 26.<BR>--3 Mortal, of<BR>short existence; अथ यदल्पं तन्मर्त्यं Ch.<BR>Up.<BR>--4 Young.<BR>--5 Seldom, rare.<BR>--ल्पं<BR>Very little.<BR>--ल्पं, --ल्पेन, --ल्पात् adv.<BR>1<BR>A little.<BR>--2 For a slight reason;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-c" target="_blank">Page0174-c+ 58</a>]<BR>प्रीतिरल्पेन भिद्यते Rām.<BR>--3 Easily, without<BR>much trouble or difficulty.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अल्प a. very little or minute,<BR>little by little; Ms. 7. 129; ˚भासं<BR>Me. 81.<BR>--असु = ˚प्राण q. v.<BR>--आकांक्षिन् a.<BR>desiring little, contented or<BR>satisfied with little.<BR>--आयुस् a.<BR>shortlived; Ms. 4. 157. (--युः m.) {1} a<BR>young one, cub. {2} a goat.<BR>--आरंभः<BR>a small or gradual beginning.<BR>--आहार, --आहारिन् a. eating little,<BR>moderate in diet, abstemious.<BR>--(रः)<BR>taking little food, moderation,<BR>abstinence in food.<BR>--इच्छु a. moderate in<BR>wishes, seeking little.<BR>--इतर a. {1}<BR>other than small, large. {2} other than<BR>few, many; as ˚राः कल्पनाः many or<BR>various ideas.<BR>--ईशाख्य a. named<BR>after an insignificant chief or<BR>master, of low origin.<BR>--ऊन a. slightly<BR>defective, not quite complete.<BR>--उपायः small means.<BR>--कार्यं a small<BR>matter.<BR>--केशी {1} N. of a plant (<BR>भूतकेशी). {2} the root of a sweet flag.<BR>--क्रीत a. bought for a small sum,<BR>cheap.<BR>--गंध a. having little scent<BR>or odour.<BR>--(धं) a red lotus.<BR>--चेष्टित a. inert.<BR>--छद, --छाद a. scantily<BR>clad, Mk. 1. 37.<BR>--ज्ञ a.<BR>knowing little, shallow, superficial,<BR>--तनु<BR>a. {1} of short stature, dwarfish,<BR>short. {2} weak, thin. {3} having<BR>small bones.<BR>--(नुः) a kind of tree.<BR>--दक्षिण a. defective in presents (as<BR>a ceremony), not liberal in<BR>sacrificial gifts; Ms. 11. 39-40.<BR>--दृंष्टि a.<BR>narrow-minded, short-sighted.<BR>--धन<BR>a. of little wealth, not affluent or<BR>rich, poor; Ms. 3. 66; 11. 40.<BR>--धी<BR>a. weak-minded, having little sense,<BR>foolish.<BR>--पत्रः {1} N. of a plant (a<BR>species of the Tulasi). {2} a tree<BR>having a few leaves.<BR>--पद्मं a red lotus.<BR>--पशु a. Ved. having a small<BR>number of cattle.<BR>--प्रजस् a.<BR>having few descendants or<BR>subjects.<BR>--प्रभाव a. of small weight<BR>or consequence, insignificant,<BR>unimportant; ˚त्वं insignificance.<BR>--प्रमाण, --प्रमाणक a. {1} of little weight or<BR>measure. {2} of little authority,<BR>resting on little evidence. (--णः,<BR>--णकः) common cucumber.<BR>--प्रयोग<BR>a. of rare application or use,<BR>rarely used.<BR>--प्राण, --असु a. having little<BR>power or strength, having short<BR>breath, asthmatic; ˚णश्च क्रियासु<BR>भवति Suśr.<BR>--(णः) {1} slight breathing or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-a" target="_blank">Page0175-a+ 58</a>]<BR>weak aspiration. {2} (in gram.) a name<BR>given to the unaspirated letters of<BR>the alphabet (in pronouncing which<BR>little effort is required); अयुग्मा<BR>वर्गयमगा यणश्चाल्पासवः स्मृताः Sk. i. e. the<BR>vowels, semivowels, nasals and the<BR>letters क् च् ट् त् प् ग् ज् ड् द् ब्.<BR>--बल a.<BR>weak, feeble, having little strength.<BR>--बाध a. causing little annoyance<BR>or inconvenience, not very harmful.<BR>--बुद्धि --मति a. weak-minded, unwise,<BR>silly, ignorant; Ms. 12. 74.<BR>--भषिन्<BR>a. speaking little, taciturn.<BR>--मध्यम a.<BR>slender-waisted.<BR>--मात्रं {1} a little, a<BR>little merely. {2} a short time, a few<BR>moments.<BR>--मारिषः [अल्पः मारिषः शाक˚<BR>कर्म˚] a kind of amaranth (शाक)<BR>Amaranthus Polygamus.<BR>--मूर्ति a.<BR>small-bodied, diminutive, dwarfish.<BR>(--र्तिः f.) a small figure or object.<BR>--मूल्य a. of small value, cheap.<BR>--मेधस्<BR>a. of little understanding, ignorant,<BR>silly.<BR>--वयस् a. young in age,<BR>youthful.<BR>--वादिन् a. speaking little,<BR>taciturn.<BR>--विद्य a. ignorant,<BR>illtaught, uneducated.<BR>--विषय a. {1}<BR>of limited range or capacity; क्व<BR>चाल्पविषया मतिः R. 1. 2. {2} engaged<BR>in trifling matters.<BR>--शक्ति a. of<BR>little strength, weak, feeble.<BR>--शमी<BR>a small tree like शमी.<BR>--सरस् n. a<BR>basin, a small pond (one which is<BR>shallow or dry in hot seasons).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पक|अल्पकः
अल्पक a. (ल्पिका f.)<BR>1 Small,<BR>little, minute.<BR>--2 Contemptible,<BR>mean; Śi. 16. 28; नाग्निपरिशुद्धिमपि<BR>अल्पकाः प्रतिपद्यंते U. 4.<BR>--कं Little.<BR>--कः N. of a plant (यवास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पता
अल्पता, --त्वं<BR>1 Smallness,<BR>minuteness; Bh. 3. 47.<BR>--2 Smallness of<BR>intellect, folly; Ki. 6. 37.<BR>--3<BR>Inferiority, insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पत्वं|अल्पत्व
अल्पता, --त्वं<BR>1 Smallness,<BR>minuteness; Bh. 3. 47.<BR>--2 Smallness of<BR>intellect, folly; Ki. 6. 37.<BR>--3<BR>Inferiority, insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पंपच|अल्पम्पच|अल्पंपचः
अल्पंपच a. Cooking little, stingy,<BR>niggardly.<BR>--चः A miser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पशः
अल्पशः ind.<BR>1 In a low degree,<BR>slightly, a little; बहुशो ददाति<BR>आभ्युदयिकेषु, अल्पशः श्राद्धेषु P. V. 4. 42<BR>Com.; P. II. 1. 38.<BR>--2 Separately.<BR>--3<BR>Seldom, now and then.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पित
अल्पित a. [अल्प कृतार्थे णिच् कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>1 Diminished.<BR>--2 Lowered in<BR>estimation, disparaged; मृषा न चक्रेऽ<BR>ल्पितकल्पपादपः N. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पिष्ठ|अल्पिष्ठः
अल्पिष्ठ a. [अतिशयेन अल्पः इष्ठन्] Least,<BR>smallest, very small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीकृ
अल्पीकृ {c8c} U. To make small,<BR>diminish, reduce in number,<BR>comminute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीभूत
अल्पीभूत a. Become small,<BR>diminished, reduced in number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्पीयस्
अल्पीयस् a. [अतिशयेन अल्पः ईयसुन्]<BR>Smaller, less; very small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अल्ला
अल्ला (Ety.?)<BR>1 A mother (Voc.<BR>अल्ल) P. VII. 3. 107.<BR>--2 The<BR>Supreme Goddess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्
अव् {c1c} P. [अवति, आव, आवीत्,<BR>अविष्यति, अवितुं, अवित or ऊत]<BR>1 To<BR>protect, defend; यमवतामवतां च धुरि<BR>स्थितः R. 9. 1; प्रत्यक्षाभिः<BR>प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः Ś. 1. 1.<BR>--2 To<BR>please, satisfy, give pleasure to; do<BR>good to; विक्रमस्तेन मामवति नाजिते त्वयि<BR>R. 11. 75; न मामवति सद्वीपा<BR>रत्नसूरपि मेदिनी. 1. 65.<BR>--3 To like, wish,<BR>desire, love.<BR>--4 To favour, promote,<BR>animate. (In the Dhātupāṭha<BR>several other meanings are assigned<BR>to this root, but they are very<BR>rarely used in classical literature;<BR>e. g. गति, कांति, अवगम, प्रवेश, श्रवण,<BR>स्वाम्यर्थ or सामर्थ्य, याचन, क्रिया, दीप्ति, अवाप्ति,<BR>ग्रहण, व्याप्ति, आलिंगन, हिंसा, आदान, दहन,<BR>भाव, भाग and वृद्धि). --Caus. To<BR>consume, devour. --WITH अनु to<BR>encourage, inspire.<BR>--उद् {1} to regard,<BR>attend to. {2} to wait for. {3} to<BR>promote, impel.<BR>--उप {1} to cherish,<BR>behave friendly towards. {2} to<BR>encourage.<BR>--सं {1} to satisfy, satiate. {2}<BR>to protect, maintain. [cf. L. aveo].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवन|अवनं
अवन a. [अव्-ल्युट्] Protecting,<BR>defending; अनवनी नवनीपवनावलिः<BR>Śi. 6. 37.<BR>--नं Protection &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव|अवः
अव ind. (the initial अ is<BR>sometimes dropped, as in पूर्वापरौ तोयनिधी<BR>वगाह्य Ku. 1. 1)<BR>1 (As a<BR>preposition) Away, off, away from, down.<BR>--2 (As a prefix to verbs) It<BR>expresses (a) determination; अवधृ,<BR>अवसो; (b) diffusion, pervasion;<BR>अवकॄ, --कीर्ण; (c) disrespect; अवज्ञा,<BR>अवमन्; (d) littleness; व्रीहीनवहंति;<BR>(e) support, resting upon; अवलंब्;<BR>(f) purification, अवदात; (g)<BR>depreciation, discomfiture; अवहंति<BR>शत्रून् (पराभवति); (h) commanding;<BR>अवकॢप्; (i) depression, bending<BR>down; अवतॄ, अवगाह्; (j) knowledge;<BR>अवगम्, अवै.<BR>--3 As the first member<BR>of Tat. compounds it means अवक्रुष्ट;<BR>अवकोकिलः = अवक्रुष्टः कोकिलया Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंशः|अवंश
अवंशः A bad family, wrong<BR>family; ˚पतितो राजा Chāṇ. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकट|अवकटं
अवकट a. [अव-स्वार्थे-कटच्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">Page0175-c+ 56</a>]<BR>P. V. 2. 30]<BR>1 Downwards; backwards.<BR>--2 Opposite, contrary.<BR>--टं<BR>Contrariety, opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकटिका
अवकटिका Dissimulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर|अवकरः
अवकर, --कर्त &c. See under<BR>अवकॄ-कृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्त|अवकर्तः
अवकर, --कर्त &c. See under<BR>अवकॄ-कृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्ण्
अवकर्ण् {c10c} P. To hear; Śi. 15. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्णनं|अवकर्णन
अवकर्णनं Hearing; K. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्षणं|अवकर्षण
अवकर्षणं Drawing with strength,<BR>removing a thing from one place to<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकलित|अवकलितः
अवकलित a.<BR>1 Seen, observed.<BR>--2 Known.<BR>--3 Taken, received.<BR>--4<BR>Wicked, perverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवका
अवका A grassy plant(शैवाल)<BR>growing in marshy land.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद a. eating moss.<BR>--उल्ब a.<BR>covered or surrounded with अवका plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाश्
अवकाश् {c1c} {c4c} A. To be visible,<BR>to be manifest. --Caus. To cause to<BR>look at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाशः|अवकाश
अवकाशः<BR>1 Occasion,<BR>opportunity; ताते चापद्वितीये वहति<BR>रणधुरां को भयस्यावकाशः Ve. 3. 5;<BR>उत्तरावकाशमपाहरंत्या K. 204, 265;<BR>साहाय्यदानावकाशः Dk. 96; M. 3. 13;<BR>M. 2; oft. used with लभ् in the<BR>sense of ‘to get an opportunity or<BR>scope for action’; लब्धावकाशोऽ<BR>विध्यन्मां तत्र दग्धो मनोभवः Ks. 1. 41.<BR>--2 (a)<BR>Place, space, room; अवकाशं<BR>किलोदन्वान्रामायाभ्यर्थितो ददौ R. 4. 58;<BR>अन्यमवकाशमवगाहे V. 4; Ms. 3. 207;<BR>यथावकाशं नी to take to its proper<BR>place, R. 6. 14; अस्माकमस्ति न<BR>कथंचिदिहावकाशः Pt. 4. 8; अवकाशो<BR>विविक्तोयं महानद्योः समागमे Rām.;<BR>सदोषावकाश इव ते वाक्यशेषः V. 3 your<BR>unfinished sentence shows that<BR>there is room to find fault. (b)<BR>Footing, admission, scope,<BR>access, entrance; (छाया) शुद्धे तु<BR>दर्पणतले सुलभावकाशा Ś. 7. 32; oft. used<BR>in these senses with लभ्;<BR>लब्धावकाशा मे प्रार्थना, लब्धावकाशो मे मनोरथः<BR>Ś. 1; शोकावेगदूषिते मे मनसि विवेक एव<BR>नावकाशं लभते Prab.; also with कृ or<BR>दा ‘to make room for’, ‘admit’, ‘give<BR>way to’; असौ हि दत्वा तिमिरावकाशं<BR>Mk. 3. 6; तस्माद्देयो<BR>विपुलमतिभिर्नावकाशोऽधमानां Pt. 1. 366; शयने दत्तोऽ<BR>वकाशः Amaru. 18; अदत्तावकाशो मत्सरस्य<BR>K. 45 not swayed by malice;<BR>Ms. 9. 271; Y. 2. 276; ददौ च निजचित्तेपि<BR>सोवकाशं मनोभुवः Ks. 20. 71;<BR>K. 132, 141, 207; Ratn. 2. 14; अवकाशं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">Page0176-a+ 55</a>]<BR>रुध् to obstruct, hinder or impede;<BR>नयनसलिलोत्पीडरुद्धावकाशां (निद्रां)<BR>Me. 91.<BR>--3 Interval, intermediate space<BR>or time.<BR>--4 An aperture, opening.<BR>--5<BR>A glance cast on anything.<BR>--6 N. of<BR>certain verses during the recitation<BR>of which the eyes must be fixed<BR>upon certain objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाशवत्|अवकाशवन्त्
अवकाशवत् a. Spacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकाश्य
अवकाश्य a. Admitted in the<BR>recitation of the Avakāśa verses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्ण|अवकीर्णः
अवकीर्ण, --र्णिन् See under अवकॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिन्|अवकीर्ण्णिन्
अवकीर्ण, --र्णिन् See under अवकॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुंचनं|अवकुञ्चन|अवकुंचन
अवकुंचनं<BR>1 Bending, curving,<BR>contraction.<BR>--2 A kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुटार|अवकुटारं
अवकुटार a. [अव-स्वार्थे अतिशये वा<BR>कुटारच्] Very deep, downwards,<BR>backwards.<BR>--रं Deformity. See अवकट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुट्टित
अवकुट्टित a.<BR>1 Vexed, inflamed.<BR>--2 Cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुंठनं|अवकुण्ठन
अवकुंठनं<BR>1 Investing,<BR>surrounding.<BR>--2 Attracting, engaging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुंठित|अवकुण्ठित
अवकुंठित a.<BR>1 Invested,<BR>surrounded.<BR>--2 Attracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुत्स्
अवकुत्स् {c10c} U. To blame, revile,<BR>contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकुत्सित
अवकुत्सित p. p. Blamed, reviled<BR>&c.<BR>--तं Blame, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृत्
अवकृत् {c6c} P. To cut off or away.<BR>--Caus. To cause to cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्तः|अवकर्त
अवकर्तः A part cut off, a strip;<BR>वस्त्रावकर्तेन संवीता Nala. 10. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्तनं|अवकर्तन|अवकर्त्तन
अवकर्तनं Cutting off, excision;<BR>वस्त्रार्धस्यावकर्तनं Nala. 10. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्तिन्
अवकर्तिन् a. Cutting off or out;<BR>चर्म˚ Ms. 4. 218.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृष्
अवकृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To draw off or<BR>away, to pull off, drag down or pull<BR>down.<BR>--2 To extract, take out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकर्षणं|अवकर्षण
अवकर्षणं<BR>1 Taking or pulling out,<BR>extraction.<BR>--2 Expulsion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकृष्ट|अवकृष्टः
अवकृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Drawn away or<BR>down, pulled down.<BR>--2 Removed.<BR>--3 Expelled, turned out or away.<BR>--4 Inferior, low, degraded,<BR>outcast (opp. उत्कृष्ट or प्रकृष्ट); ˚जातिः<BR>Ms. 8. 177; प्रतिकर्तुं प्रकृष्टस्य नावकृष्टेन<BR>युज्यते Rām.<BR>--ष्टः A servant who<BR>performs the lowest menial duties<BR>(such as sweeping &c.) (<BR>संमार्जनशोधनविनियुक्त); पणो देयोऽवकृष्टस्य<BR>षडुत्कृष्टस्य वेतनं Ms. 7. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकॄ
अवकॄ {c6c} P.<BR>1 To bestow, pour<BR>upon, to shower upon, cover with,<BR>fill; Śi. 11. 62; (तं) अवाकिरन्<BR>बाललताः प्रसूनैः R. 2. 10, 4. 27;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">Page0176-b+ 57</a>]<BR>लाजांजलिभिरवकीर्यमाणः K. 86;<BR>Ki. 6. 2; अवकीर्योत्तरीयाणि Mb.<BR>spreading on the ground; तीर्थानि अवकीर्णानि<BR>तपस्विभिः Mb. filled with; Y. 3. 281;<BR>Me. 54.<BR>--2 To pour out, throw out<BR>Ms. 6. 48.<BR>--3 To shake off, throw<BR>off, leave.<BR>--4 (Atm.) (Used<BR>reflexively) (a) To extend, spread itself;<BR>अवकिरते हस्ती स्वयमेव Sk. (b) To fall<BR>asunder. (c) To pass away, fall off.<BR>(d) To become faithless or untrue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकरः|अवकर
अवकरः [कॄ-अप्] Dust,<BR>sweepings; अवकरनिकरं विकिरति Bh. 2. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्ण|अवकीर्णः
अवकीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Scattered, filled,<BR>covered over; किमपौति<BR>रजोभिरौर्वरैरवकीर्णस्य मणेर्महार्घता Śi. 16. 27.<BR>--2<BR>Coarsely pounded.<BR>--3 Destroyed.<BR>--4 Violated (as the vow of a ब्रह्मचारी),<BR>degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकीर्णिन्|अवकीर्ण्णिन्
अवकीर्णिन् a. [अवकीर्णमनेन इष्टा˚ इनि]<BR>Violating the vow or engagements<BR>of continence. --m.<BR>--(र्णी) A<BR>religious student who has committed<BR>an act of incontinence (such as<BR>sexual intercourse) against his vow<BR>of celibacy; अवकीर्णी भवेद्गत्वा ब्रह्मचारी तु<BR>योषितम् । गर्दभं पशुमालभ्य नैरृतं स विशुध्यति ॥<BR>Y. 3. 280; Ms. 3. 155, 11. 118-9; ˚व्रतं<BR>penance for an act of incontinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकॢप्
अवकॢप् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To correspond<BR>with, to answer.<BR>--2 To be right or fit,<BR>to be possible; इतश्च न प्रधानस्य<BR>प्रवृत्तिरवकल्पते Ś. B.<BR>--3 To help to, to serve,<BR>to accomplish, result in (with dat.);<BR>शरीरिणां संसृतयेऽवकल्पते Bhāg. --Caus.<BR>1 To put in order, to prepare; to<BR>make ready; संभारानवकल्पय Mb.<BR>--2 To<BR>use or employ becomingly.<BR>--3 To<BR>consider as possible;<BR>नावकल्प्यमिदंग्लायेद्यत्कृच्छ्रेषु भवानपि Bk. 19. 17;<BR>यत्तत्रभवान्वृषलं याजयेन्नावकल्पयामि<BR>P. III. 3. 147 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकल्पित
अवकल्पित p. p. Corresponding<BR>with; right, fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकॢप्तिः|अवकॢप्ति
अवकॢप्तिः f.<BR>1 Considering as<BR>possible, possibility, probability;<BR>क्वेव भोक्ष्येस अनवकॢप्तावेव Sk. (<BR>अनवकॢप्तिरसंभावना).<BR>--2 Suitableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकेश
अवकेश a. Having the hair<BR>hanging down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकेशिन्
अवकेशिन् a.<BR>1 Unfruitful, barren<BR>(as a tree).<BR>--2 [अवसन्नाः केशा विद्यंते<BR>अस्य इनि] Having small or very<BR>few hair. --m. A fruitless tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवकोकिल
अवकोकिल a. [अवक्रुष्टः कोकिलया]<BR>Drawn or called down to by a<BR>cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्तव्य|अवक्तव्यं
अवक्तव्य a.<BR>1 Not fit to be<BR>uttered, improper.<BR>--2 Censurable (as a<BR>saying).<BR>--3 False.<BR>--4 Indescribable,<BR>inexpressible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्त्र
अवक्त्र a. Having no opening (as<BR>a vessel, wound &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्र
अवक्र a. Not crooked, straight;<BR>(fig.) honest, upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रक्षिन्
अवक्रक्षिन् [अव-कृष् णिनि पृ˚]<BR>Dashing down, overcoming; अवक्रक्षिणं<BR>वृषभं यथा जुरम् Rv. 8. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रंद्|अवक्रन्द्
अवक्रंद् {c1c} U. To cry out, roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रंद|अवक्रन्द|अवक्रन्दः
अवक्रंद a. Crying slowly, roaring,<BR>neighing.<BR>--दः A cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रंदनं|अवक्रन्दन
अवक्रंदनं Crying out, weeping aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रम्
अवक्रम् {c1c} U., {c4c} P.<BR>1 To step<BR>down or away, run away, escape,<BR>withdraw.<BR>--2 To tread down,<BR>overcome; वज्रेणैवेनमवक्रामति Śat. Br.<BR>--3 To descend, come down. --Caus.<BR>To cause to go down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रमः|अवक्रम
अवक्रमः Descending, descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रांतिः|अवक्रान्ति|अवक्रान्तिः
अवक्रांतिः f.<BR>1 Descending, descent.<BR>--2 Approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रामिन्
अवक्रामिन् a. Ved. Running away,<BR>escaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रिया
अवक्रिया Neglect, omission,<BR>nonperformance of prescribed acts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्री
अवक्री {c9c} U.<BR>1 To purchase.<BR>--2<BR>To let out, hire.<BR>--3 To bribe, buy off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रयः|अवक्रय
अवक्रयः<BR>1 Price.<BR>--2 Wages, hire,<BR>farm, rent.<BR>--3 Letting out to hire,<BR>leasing; Y. 2. 238.<BR>--4 A tax or tribute<BR>(to be paid to the king), duty (<BR>राजग्राह्यं द्रव्यं Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रुश्
अवक्रुश् {c1c} P. To call down to;<BR>to revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रुष्ट
अवक्रुष्ट p. p. Sounded ill or badly,<BR>reviled, censured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्रोशः|अवक्रोश
अवक्रोशः<BR>1 Discordant noise.<BR>--2 A<BR>curse.<BR>--3 Abuse, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लिन्न
अवक्लिन्न a. Wet, thoroughly wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लेदः|अवक्लेद
अवक्लेदः<BR>1 Trickling, descent of<BR>moisture.<BR>--2 Ichor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्लेदनं|अवक्लेदन
अवक्लेदनं Trickling, falling (as dew<BR>or moisture).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्वणः|अवक्वण
अवक्वणः A discordant note.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्वाथः|अवक्वाथ
अवक्वाथः Imperfect digestion or<BR>decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षामः|अवक्षाम
अवक्षामः Ved. Propitiatory<BR>offering; satisfaction of claims,<BR>compensation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षि
अवक्षि {c1c} {c5c} {c9c} P. To remove,<BR>carry off, destroy. --Pass. To waste<BR>away, decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षयः|अवक्षय
अवक्षयः<BR>1 Destruction, decay,<BR>waste, loss; लब्धं रक्षेदवक्षयात्<BR>H. 2. 8.<BR>--2 A kind of malady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षयणं|अवक्षयण
अवक्षयणं Means of extinguishing<BR>(fire &c.); as in अंगार˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षीण
अवक्षीण p. p. Wasted, emaciated.<BR>--णं Loss, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षिप्
अवक्षिप् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To fling away,<BR>to throw or cast off;<BR>सूक्ष्मवस्त्रमवक्षिप्य मुनिवस्त्राण्यवस्त ह Rām.; to<BR>hurl.<BR>--2 To cause to fly down or<BR>away.<BR>--3 To reprimand, revile any<BR>one, censure, slander;<BR>मदलेखामवक्षिप्य K. 317; अवाक्षिपद्वासुदेवं Mb.<BR>--4 To<BR>grant, yield. --Caus. To cause to<BR>fall down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षिप्त
अवक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Thrown down;<BR>badly thrown.<BR>--2 Said sarcastically,<BR>imputed, insinuated.<BR>--3 Reviled,<BR>censured, blamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षेपः|अवक्षेप
अवक्षेपः<BR>1 Blaming, reviling.<BR>--2<BR>Objection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षेपणं|अवक्षेपण
अवक्षेपणं<BR>1 Throwing down,<BR>considered as one of the five kinds of<BR>karman, q. v.<BR>--2 Contempt,<BR>despising; अवक्षेपणे कन् P. V. 3. 95.<BR>--3<BR>Censure, blame; P. I. 3. 32;<BR>VI. 2. 195.<BR>--4 Overcoming, subduing.<BR>--णी Rein, bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षु
अवक्षु {c2c} P. To sneeze upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवक्षुत|अवक्षुतं
अवक्षुत p. p. Sneezed upon;<BR>द्विषदन्नं नगर्यन्नं पतितान्नमवक्षुतं Ms. 4. 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवखंड्|अवखण्ड्
अवखंड् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To cut down,<BR>break into pieces.<BR>--2 To waste away,<BR>wear away; अर्धयाममात्रावखंडितायां<BR>विभावर्यां K. 49 when the night had<BR>advanced only half a watch.<BR>--3 To<BR>destroy, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवखंडनं|अवखण्डन
अवखंडनं Dividing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवखातं|अवखात
अवखातं [निम्नः खातः] A deep<BR>ditch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवखादः|अवखाद
अवखादः [अवज्ञातः निंदितः खादः खाद्यं]<BR>Bad or contemptible meal; an<BR>unworthy oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगण्
अवगण् {c10c} P. To disregard, not<BR>to heed, disrespect, despise, slight;<BR>पर्वतीय इति मावजीगणः Ki. 13. 67;<BR>अवगणितखलीनाकर्षणः Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगणनं|अवगणन
अवगणनं<BR>1 Disobedience,<BR>disrespect, contempt, disregard.<BR>--2<BR>Censure, blame.<BR>--3 Insult, mortification.<BR>--4 Defeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगण
अवगण a. Separated from one's<BR>companions, isolated, solitary, alone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगंडः|अवगण्ड|अवगण्डः
अवगंडः A boil or pimple upon<BR>the face or cheeks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगथ|अवगथः
अवगथ a. [निपातः Uṇ. 2. 9]<BR>Bathed early in the morning (प्रातःस्नात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगदितः|अवगदित
अवगदितः<BR>1 Having exception.<BR>--2 Censured, blamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगम्
अवगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go down,<BR>descend; अंजः समुद्रमवजग्मुरापः<BR>Rv. 1. 32. 2.<BR>--2 To come to, visit, go near.<BR>--3 To reach, obtain.<BR>--4 (a) To<BR>know, learn, understand, think,<BR>believe; कृतापराधमिवावगच्छति आत्मानं<BR>K. 203; मामेवमवगच्छति V. 2;<BR>कथं शांतमित्यभिहिते श्रांत इत्यवगच्छति<BR>मूर्खः Mk. 1; न खल्ववगच्छामि,<BR>परस्तादवगम्यत एव Ś. 1; तत्तदेवावगच्छ त्वं मम<BR>तेजोंशसंभवं Bg. 10. 41; R. 8. 88;<BR>Bk. 5. 81. (b) To consider, regard, look<BR>upon.<BR>--5 To assure oneself, be<BR>convinced. --Caus.<BR>1 To bring near.<BR>--2<BR>To inform oneself of, find out, know;<BR>तावदेतेभ्यः प्रियाप्रवृत्तिरवगमयितव्या<BR>V. 4.<BR>--3 To inform, cause to know,<BR>teach; पुरुषविशेषमवगमयति Mu. 5;<BR>सर्वमिदं पित्रोरवगमय्य Dk.<BR>--4 To<BR>indicate, show; संनाहोयं<BR>साहसमवगमयति Dk. 96; Bk. 10. 53, 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगत|अवगतं
अवगत p. p.<BR>1 Gone away or<BR>down.<BR>--2 Known, learnt,<BR>understood; sometimes used actively;<BR>तदैव ध्यानादवगतोस्मि Ś. 7 I learnt;<BR>ऊढपूर्वां तद्दुहितरमवगतोहं ibid. came to<BR>know.<BR>--3 Assented, promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगतिः|अवगति
अवगतिः f.<BR>1 Knowledge,<BR>perception, comprehension.<BR>--2 True or<BR>determinate knowledge; ब्रह्मावगतिर्हि<BR>पुरुषार्थः; ब्रह्मावगतिस्त्वप्रतिज्ञाता Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगमः|अवगम
अवगमः --गमनं<BR>1 Going near,<BR>descending.<BR>--2 Understanding,<BR>comprehension, perception, knowledge,<BR>being acquainted with.<BR>--3 True or<BR>determinate knowledge;<BR>प्रत्यक्षावगमं धर्म्यं सुसुखं कर्तुमव्ययम् Bg. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगमनं|अवगमन
अवगमः --गमनं<BR>1 Going near,<BR>descending.<BR>--2 Understanding,<BR>comprehension, perception, knowledge,<BR>being acquainted with.<BR>--3 True or<BR>determinate knowledge;<BR>प्रत्यक्षावगमं धर्म्यं सुसुखं कर्तुमव्ययम् Bg. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगादः|अवगाद
अवगादः A small wooden basin<BR>for baling water out of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाह्
अवगाह् {c1c} A.<BR>1 (a) To bathe<BR>oneself in, plunge into, dive into;<BR>with acc. or loc.; तमोपहंत्रीं तमसां<BR>वगाह्य R. 14. 76;<BR>अन्यमवकाशमवगाहिष्ये V. 4; स्वप्नेऽवगाहतेत्यर्थं जलं<BR>Y. 1. 272; Bk. 6. 29, 16. 38.<BR>(b) To go deep into, be<BR>absorbed into (fig.);<BR>अमात्यराक्षसेनाप्यनवगाहितयार्यचाणक्यस्य<BR>चरितमवगाहितुमिच्छसि Mu. 6.<BR>--2 To enter,<BR>penetrate, fully pervade;<BR>विमानशृंगाण्यवगाहमानः (घोषः) Ku. 7. 40; पूर्वापरौ<BR>तोयनिधी वगाह्य Ku. 1. 1;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">Page0177-c+ 56</a>]<BR>पूर्वापरसमुद्रावगाढः Ś. 7; Mk. 2; see अवगाढ also.<BR>--Caus. To bathe, cause to bathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाढ
अवगाढ p. p.<BR>1 Plunged into,<BR>entered into, immersed; जलावगाढस्य<BR>वनद्विपस्य Mk. 2; अमृतथदमिवावगाढोस्मि<BR>Ś. 7; अवगाढः शोकसागरं Rām.;<BR>समुद्रमवगाढानि पत्तनानि Rām.<BR>--2<BR>Depressed, low, deep (lit. and fig.);<BR>अभ्युन्नता पुरस्तादवगाढा जघनगौरवात्पश्चात्<BR>Ś. 3. 8; मन्युरभजदवगाढतरः Śi. 15. 2.<BR>--3 That in which one bathes;<BR>अवगाढा च पीता च (गंगा) पुनात्यासप्तमं<BR>कुलं Mb.<BR>--4 Congealed, curdling (as<BR>blood).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाहः|अवगाह
अवगाहः, --हनं<BR>1 Bathing;<BR>सुभगसलिलावगाहाः Ś. 1. 3;<BR>अवगाहप्रस्थितमिव वनमहिषयूथं K. 29;<BR>सदावगाहक्षमवारिसंचयः Rs. 1. 1.<BR>--2 Plunging,<BR>immersing (in general);<BR>entering into; हुतभुगवगाहनसाहसिकां<BR>Dk. 16; परदेशावगाहनात् H. 3. 95;<BR>जलावगाहक्षणमात्रशांता R. 5. 47;<BR>दग्धानामवगाहनाय विधिना रम्यं सरो निर्मितं Ś.<BR>Til. {1}<BR>--3 (fig.) Mastering,<BR>learning, studying completely;<BR>सकलशास्त्रावगाहगंभीरबुद्धिः K. 56.<BR>--4 A place of<BR>bathing.<BR>--5 A bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाहनं|अवगाहन
अवगाहः, --हनं<BR>1 Bathing;<BR>सुभगसलिलावगाहाः Ś. 1. 3;<BR>अवगाहप्रस्थितमिव वनमहिषयूथं K. 29;<BR>सदावगाहक्षमवारिसंचयः Rs. 1. 1.<BR>--2 Plunging,<BR>immersing (in general);<BR>entering into; हुतभुगवगाहनसाहसिकां<BR>Dk. 16; परदेशावगाहनात् H. 3. 95;<BR>जलावगाहक्षणमात्रशांता R. 5. 47;<BR>दग्धानामवगाहनाय विधिना रम्यं सरो निर्मितं Ś.<BR>Til. {1}<BR>--3 (fig.) Mastering,<BR>learning, studying completely;<BR>सकलशास्त्रावगाहगंभीरबुद्धिः K. 56.<BR>--4 A place of<BR>bathing.<BR>--5 A bucket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगाह्य
अवगाह्य pot. p.<BR>1 Fit for bathing.<BR>--2 Fit to be plunged into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुणः|अवगुण
अवगुणः A fault, defect,<BR>demerit; अन्यदोषं परावगुणं Malli. on<BR>Ki. 13. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुंठ्|अवगुण्ठ्
अवगुंठ् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To cover with,<BR>shroud; परुषचर्मावगुंठितं Pt. 1;<BR>Ms. 4. 49.<BR>--2 To draw over, conceal, veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुंठनं|अवगुण्ठन|अवगुण्ठनं
अवगुंठनं<BR>1 The act of covering the<BR>head of women; hiding, veiling.<BR>--2 A veil (for the face); (fig. also);<BR>अवगुंठनसंवीता कुलजाभिसरेद्यदि S. D.;<BR>चांडालस्मिमिरावगुंठनपटक्षेपं विधत्ते विधुः<BR>ibid.; कृतशीर्षावगुंठनः Mu. 6;<BR>उत्सृष्टसत्पुरुषोचितलज्जावगुंठनानां Ve. 3;<BR>Mk. 4. 24; Śi. 5. 17.<BR>--3 A covering,<BR>mantle (in general).<BR>--4 A<BR>sweeping broom.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुद्रा [<BR>अवगुंठनाय मुद्रा] a sort of religious<BR>ceremony; सव्यहस्तकृता मुष्टिर्दीर्घाधोमुखतर्जनी ।<BR>अवगुंठनमुद्रेयमभितो भ्रमिता मता ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुंठनवत्
अवगुंठनवत् a. Covered with a veil,<BR>veiled; ˚वती नारी Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुंठिका|अवगुण्ठिका
अवगुंठिका<BR>1 Veiling, hiding.<BR>covering.<BR>--2 A veil.<BR>--3 A curtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुंठित|अवगुण्ठित|अवगुण्ठितं
अवगुंठित p. p.<BR>1 Veiled, covered,<BR>concealed; रजनीतिमिरावगुंठिते<BR>Ku. 4. 11 enveloped in nocturnal<BR>darkness.<BR>--2 Powdered, pounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुंडित|अवगुण्डित
अवगुंडित a. Pounded, ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुंफित
अवगुंफित a. Woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुर्
अवगुर् {c6c} U. To assail with<BR>threats, to attack, to raise a weapon<BR>for the purpose of striking a blow<BR>(with loc. or dat.); न कदाचिद् द्विजे<BR>तस्माद्विद्वानवगुरेदपि Ms. 4. 169;<BR>ब्राह्मणायावगुर्यैव 165; 11. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुरणं
अवगुरणं-गोरणं Menacing,<BR>assaulting with intent to kill, assailing<BR>with weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगोरणं|अवगोरण
अवगुरणं-गोरणं Menacing,<BR>assaulting with intent to kill, assailing<BR>with weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगुह्
अवगुह् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To cover, to hide,<BR>conceal; (रविः) पांशुपुंजावगूढः Mb.<BR>--2<BR>To put into or inside; उष्णीषं संवेष्ट्य<BR>निवीतेऽवगूहते Kāty.<BR>--3 To embrace; या<BR>ममोद्विजते नित्यं सा मामद्यावगूहते Pt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगूहनं|अवगूहन
अवगूहनं<BR>1 Hiding, concealing.<BR>--2 Embracing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगै
अवगै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sing in a<BR>discorddant tone.<BR>--2 To sing deprecatingly,<BR>satirize in a song, revile, reproach<BR>(mostly used in p. p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगीत|अवगीतं|अवगीतः
अवगीत p. p.<BR>1 Sung in a<BR>discordant tone, sung badly<BR>--2 Reproached,<BR>abused, censured; अनवगीतः परिचयः<BR>U. 2. 2; अवगीतां गमिते दशामिमां<BR>Ki. 2. 7; सोढावगीतप्रथमायुधस्य 17. 28;<BR>Śi. 11. 10.<BR>--3 Wicked, vile.<BR>--4<BR>Satirized in a song.<BR>--5 Seen frequently,<BR>well-known (मुहुर्दृष्ट).<BR>--तं<BR>1 A satire in<BR>song, derision.<BR>--2 Reproach, blame.<BR>--3 Bad or discordant singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रह्
अवग्रह् {c9c} U.<BR>1 To let loose, let<BR>go (as reins).<BR>--2 To divide, separate<BR>(as words or parts of words);<BR>पितृपाणमित्यत्र हि पितृ पाणमित्यृकारोऽवगृह्यते<BR>P. VIII. 2. 46 Com.<BR>--3 To break off,<BR>discontinue; to distinguish,<BR>discriminate, discern.<BR>--4 To punish, chastise;<BR>मंदोपि नाम न महानवगृह्य साध्यः Śi. 5. 49.<BR>--5 To seize, choke;<BR>गद्गदिकावगृह्यमाणकंठा K. 307, 328.<BR>--6 To capture, take<BR>in possession, overpower;<BR>स्वामिनमवशमवगृह्णंति Dk. 157; Dk. 32;<BR>Ve. 46.<BR>--7 To oppose, resist, hinder,<BR>obstruct.<BR>--8 To lay hold of (with the<BR>feet). --Caus. To knead, make<BR>dough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगृहीत
अवगृहीत p. p. Obstructed,<BR>impeded, restrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवगृह्य
अवगृह्य a. Separable.<BR>--ह्यं A pada<BR>having the name प्रगृह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रहः|अवग्रह
अवग्रहः<BR>1 Separation of the<BR>component parts of a compound, or of<BR>other grammatical forms.<BR>--2 The<BR>mark or interval of such a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">Page0178-b+ 57</a>]<BR>separation; समासेऽवग्रहो थस्वसमकालः.<BR>--3 The<BR>syllable or letter after which such<BR>separation occurs; ऋदवग्रहात्<BR>P. VIII. 4. 26.<BR>--4 A hiatus, absence of sandhi<BR>(as in धिक् तां च तं च मदनं च इमां च मां<BR>च instead of चेमांच) Bh. 2. 2.<BR>--5<BR>The mark (') used to mark the<BR>elision of अ after ए and ओ.<BR>--6<BR>Withholding of rain, drought, failure of<BR>rain; वृष्टिर्भवति शस्यानामवग्रहविशोषिणां<BR>R. 1. 62; रावणावग्रहक्लांतमिति वागमृतेन<BR>सः 10. 48; नभोनभस्ययोर्वृष्टिमवग्रह<BR>इवांतरे 12. 29; वृषेव सीतां तदवग्रहक्षतां<BR>Ku. 5. 61.<BR>--7 An obstacle,<BR>impediment, hindrance, restraint; संसार˚<BR>Māl. 1 the bonds or fetters of<BR>worldly existence; प्रसह्य<BR>रक्षोभिरवग्रहं च Rām.; see अनवग्रह and निरवग्रह.<BR>--8 A herd of elephants.<BR>--9 The<BR>forehead of an elephant.<BR>--10 Nature,<BR>original temperament.<BR>--11 A sort<BR>of knowledge, a false idea.<BR>--12<BR>Punishment (opp. अनुग्रह);<BR>अनुग्रहावग्रहयोर्विधाता Śi. 1. 71.<BR>--13 An<BR>imprecation, a term of abuse.<BR>--14 An<BR>iron hook with which elephants<BR>are driven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्रहणं|अवग्रहण
अवग्रहणं<BR>1 An obstacle,<BR>impediment.<BR>--2 Disrespect, disregard.<BR>--3<BR>Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवग्राहः|अवग्राह
अवग्राहः<BR>1 Breaking, separation.<BR>--2 Impediment; अवग्राहस्ते भूयात् Sk.<BR>--3 A curse; see अवग्रह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्ट्
अवघट्ट् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To push or brush<BR>away or off.<BR>--2 To split, break or<BR>cut asunder; पंचबाणान् अवघट्टयंती<BR>Dk. 124.<BR>--3 To touch, feel, rub;<BR>जलौकोव्रणान्मधुनाऽवघट्टयेत् Suśr.<BR>--4<BR>To stir up, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्टः|अवघट्ट
अवघट्टः<BR>1 A hole in the ground,<BR>a cave, a cavern.<BR>--2 A grindstone,<BR>stone-mill for grinding corn.<BR>--3<BR>Stirring up, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघट्टनं|अवघट्टन
अवघट्टनं Rubbing away or off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघुष्
अवघुष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To proclaim aloud.<BR>--2 To send for, summon, convoke;<BR>as a conclave (समाज).<BR>--3 To fill<BR>with cries, make resonant; नदीषु<BR>कौंचावघुष्टासु Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघोषः|अवघोष
अवघोषः, --षणं Proclaiming,<BR>denouncing.<BR>--णा A proclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघोषणं|अवघोषण
अवघोषः, --षणं Proclaiming,<BR>denouncing.<BR>--णा A proclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्ण्
अवघूर्ण् {c1c} U. To whirl round,<BR>brandish, move to and fro; as in<BR>अवघूर्णमानताम्रदृष्टिः; वने यथा शाल<BR>इवावघूर्णितः Mb. rocked to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्णः|अवघूर्ण
अवघूर्णः Whirling round, a<BR>whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघूर्णनं|अवघूर्णन|अवघूर्ण्णन
अवघूर्णनं Rolling or whirling round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघृष्
अवघृष् {c1c} U. To rub off, rub to<BR>pieces, grind to powder; मृदुना<BR>सलिलेन खन्यमानान्यवघृष्यंति गिरेरपि स्थलानि<BR>Pt. 1 v. l. --Caus. To rub off, scratch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघर्षणं|अवघर्षण
अवघर्षणं<BR>1 Rubbing into.<BR>--2<BR>Grinding.<BR>--3 Cleaning, rubbing off;<BR>सलिलैः शुद्धिरेतेषां गोवालैश्चावघर्षणात्<BR>Y. 3. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघोटित
अवघोटित a. Covered on all<BR>sides, concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघ्रा
अवघ्रा {c1c} P.<BR>1 To smell at; touch<BR>with the mouth; Ms. 3. 218.<BR>--2 To<BR>kiss (as the head); मूर्धनि त्रिरवघ्राय<BR>Āśval.; अवघ्रातश्च मूर्धनि Rām. --Caus.<BR>--(घ्रापयति) To cause to smell at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघ्राणं|अवघ्राण
अवघ्राणं The act of smelling at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच
अवच a. Lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचक्ष्
अवचक्ष् {c2c} A.<BR>1 To look down<BR>upon (Ved.).<BR>--2 To perceive, observe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचक्षण
अवचक्षण a. One telling a<BR>censured tale.<BR>--णं Looking down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचन
अवचन a. [न. ब.] Not<BR>speaking, silent, speechless; शकुंतला<BR>साध्वसादवचना तिष्ठति Ś. 1.<BR>--नं [अभावे<BR>न. त.]<BR>1 Absence of assertion,<BR>silence, taciturnity; अवचनेऽग्निष्टोमः<BR>Kāty.<BR>--2 Censure, blame, reproof;<BR>˚कर a. not doing what one is bid,<BR>disobedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचनीय
अवचनीय a.<BR>1 Not to be spoken<BR>or uttered, obscene or indecent<BR>(language); वादेष्ववचनीयेषु तदेव द्विगुणं<BR>भवेत् Ms. 8. 269.<BR>--2 Not censurable,<BR>not blamable, free from censure;<BR>लोकैरवचनीया भवति Mk. 2; ˚ता;<BR>impropriety of speech, freedom from<BR>censure; सर्वथा व्यवहर्तव्ये कुतो<BR>ह्यवचनीयता U. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचस्कर|अवचस्करः
अवचस्कर a. Not speaking,<BR>silent, taciturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचंद्रमसं|अवचन्द्रमस
अवचंद्रमसं The looking down<BR>of the moon (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचर्
अवचर् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To move or come<BR>down.<BR>--2 To go down towards.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to move or<BR>descend upon.<BR>--2 To employ, use,<BR>apply; लेपान्, शस्त्रं, कषायं &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचार|अवचारः
अवचार a. Going or moving down<BR>in or upon.<BR>--रः A place of descent,<BR>road; field of action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचारण
अवचारण a. Moving, going.<BR>--णं<BR>1<BR>Employing, application, mode of<BR>proceeding.<BR>--2 A kind of saline<BR>preparation (क्षारपाकविधि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचार्य|अवचार्य्य
अवचार्य a. To be cast down, to be<BR>given, to be put on or applied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचि
अवचि {c3c} P.<BR>1 To worship, honour,<BR>respect.<BR>--2 ({c5c} U.) To gather, pick up,<BR>pluck (with two acc.); गता<BR>स्यादवचिन्वाना कुसुमान्याश्रमद्रुमान् Bk. 6. 10;<BR>वृक्षमवचिनोति फलानि Sk.<BR>--3 To take<BR>off.<BR>--4 To let down behind, to open<BR>(one's cloak).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचयः|अवचय
अवचयः Gathering (such as<BR>flowers, fruits &c.); ततः प्रविशतः<BR>कुसुमावचयमभिनयंत्यौ सख्यौ Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचायः|अवचाय
अवचायः [अव-चि-घञ्] Gathering<BR>flowers (with the hands);<BR>अविरतकुसुमावचायखेदात् Śi. 7. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचायिन्
अवचायिन् a. Gathering, picking off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचित
अवचित p. p.<BR>1 Gathered.<BR>--2<BR>Filled, inhabited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूडः|अवचूड
अवचूडः --लः [अवनता चूडा अग्रं यस्य<BR>वा डो लः] The pendent cloth on a<BR>chariot, an ornament (like a chowri)<BR>hanging from the top of a banner;<BR>पिच्छावचूडमनुमाधवधाम जग्मुः Śi. 5. 13;<BR>दिवसकरवारणस्यावचूलचामरकलापः<BR>K. 26, 114, 116; Śi. 20. 46, 12. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूलः|अवचूल
अवचूडः --लः [अवनता चूडा अग्रं यस्य<BR>वा डो लः] The pendent cloth on a<BR>chariot, an ornament (like a chowri)<BR>hanging from the top of a banner;<BR>पिच्छावचूडमनुमाधवधाम जग्मुः Śi. 5. 13;<BR>दिवसकरवारणस्यावचूलचामरकलापः<BR>K. 26, 114, 116; Śi. 20. 46, 12. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्ण्
अवचूर्ण् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To sprinkle<BR>with meal, dust.<BR>--2 To cover, put<BR>on or over, overlay; चूर्णैः<BR>शनैर्व्रणमुखमवचूर्ण्य Suśr.; भेर्यो<BR>दिव्यपुष्पावचूर्णिताः Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्णनं|अवचूर्णन|अवचूर्ण्णन
अवचूर्णनं<BR>1 Pounding, grinding,<BR>reducing to powder.<BR>--2 Sprinkling<BR>with powder; especially, throwing<BR>absorbent powders on wounds.<BR>--3<BR>A kind of disease or wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूर्णित|अवचूर्णितं|अवचूर्ण्णित
अवचूर्णित a.<BR>1 Pounded coarsely;<BR>त्रिजातावचूर्णितेन mixed with<BR>Dk. 133.<BR>--2 Ground, crushed, reduced<BR>to powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूल|अवचूलः
अवचूल = अवचूड q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूलकः|अवचूलक|अवचूलकं
अवचूलकः, --कं A chowri or brush<BR>(formed of a cow's tail or peacock's<BR>feathers) for fanning off flies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवचूलकं|अवचूलक|अवचूलकः
अवचूलकः, --कं A chowri or brush<BR>(formed of a cow's tail or peacock's<BR>feathers) for fanning off flies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छद्
अवच्छद् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To cover over,<BR>overspread.<BR>--2 To conceal, obscure,<BR>leave in darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छदः|अवच्छद
अवच्छ(च्छा)दः A cover,<BR>covering; कांचनावच्छादान् (खरान्) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छादः
अवच्छ(च्छा)दः A cover,<BR>covering; कांचनावच्छादान् (खरान्) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छिद्
अवच्छिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To cut off,<BR>separate, tear in pieces, break<BR>asunder.<BR>--2 To discriminate, distinguish,<BR>characterize.<BR>--3 To define, limit,<BR>modify (as by time, space &c.,) used<BR>in Nyāya; see अवच्छिन्न below.<BR>--4<BR>To detach, excerpt.<BR>--5 To interrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छिन्न|अवच्छिन्नं
अवच्छिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Cut off.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">Page0179-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Separated, divided, detached,<BR>excerpted.<BR>--3 (In Logic) Separated<BR>or excluded from all other things by<BR>the properties predicated of a thing<BR>as peculiar to itself.<BR>--4 Bounded,<BR>modified, determined;<BR>दिक्कालाद्यनवच्छिन्न Bh. 2. 1.<BR>--5 Particularized,<BR>distinguished, characterized, as by<BR>an attributive word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदः|अवच्छेद
अवच्छेदः<BR>1 A part, portion, (<BR>अवयव).<BR>--2 Boundary, limit.<BR>--3<BR>Separation.<BR>--4 Distinction, distinguishing,<BR>particularization (as by attributes).<BR>--5 Determination, decision,<BR>settlement; शब्दार्थस्यानवच्छेदे विशेषस्मृतिहेतवः<BR>Vāk. P.<BR>--6 That property of a thing<BR>which distinguishes it from every<BR>thing else, a characteristic property.<BR>--7 Bounding, defining.<BR>--8<BR>Pervading (व्याप्तिः). ˚अवच्छेदः generalizing,<BR>removing distinctions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदक|अवच्छेदकं|अवच्छेदकः
अवच्छेदक a.<BR>1 Separating.<BR>--2<BR>Determining, deciding,<BR>प्रतियोगिकावच्छेदकावच्छिन्नं<BR>--3 Bounding, limiting.<BR>--4<BR>Pervading.<BR>--5 Distinguishing,<BR>particularizing.<BR>--6 Peculiar, characteristic.<BR>--कः<BR>1 That which distinguishes.<BR>--2 A predicate, characteristic<BR>property.<BR>--3 Boundary, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छेदनं|अवच्छेदन
अवच्छेदनं Cutting off, separating;<BR>determining, bounding &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवच्छुरित|अवच्छुरितं|अवछुरित
अवच्छुरित a. Mixed.<BR>--तं A<BR>horselaugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजि
अवजि {c1c} P.<BR>1 To spoil (deprive<BR>by conquest), to win; अवजित्य च<BR>तद्धनं Mb.; Ms. 11. 81; पुष्पकं नाम<BR>विमानं वीर्यादवजितं Rām.<BR>--2 To<BR>recover; हृतां कृष्णामवाजयत् Mb.<BR>--3 To<BR>ward off, prevent.<BR>--4 To conquer;<BR>अवजितमधुना तवाहमक्ष्णोः Śi. 7. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजयः|अवजय
अवजयः Defeat, victory over;<BR>येनेंद्रलोकावजयाय दृप्तः R. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजित
अवजित p. p. Conquered;<BR>contemned, disregarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजितिः|अवजिति
अवजितिः f. Conquest, defeat;<BR>Ki. 6. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवजुष्ट
अवजुष्ट a. Visited, frequented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञा
अवज्ञा {c9c} P. To have a low<BR>opinion of, to despise, to treat with<BR>contempt, disregard; अवजानासि<BR>मां यस्मात् R. 1. 77; अवजानंति मां<BR>मूढा मानुषीं तनुमाश्रितं Bg. 9. 11;<BR>Bk. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञा
अवज्ञा [अव-ज्ञा-अङ्] Disrespect,<BR>contempt; slighting, low opinion;<BR>नात्मन्यवज्ञा कर्तव्या H. 1;<BR>disregard (with the obj. in loc. or gen.);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">Page0179-c+ 56</a>]<BR>आत्मन्यवज्ञां शिथिलीचकार R. 2. 41;<BR>ये नाम केचिदिह नः प्रथयंत्यवज्ञां<BR>Māl. 1. 6; Śānti. 3. 23; अविज्ञावज्ञेयं परितपति<BR>नोच्चैरपि बुधं Udb.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपहत<BR>a. treated with contempt,<BR>humiliated.<BR>--दुःखं the agonies of<BR>humiliation; मा जीवन् यः परावज्ञादुःखदग्धोपि<BR>जीवति Śi. 2. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञात|अवज्ञातं
अवज्ञात p. p. Disrespected,<BR>contemned, disregarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञानं|अवज्ञान
अवज्ञानं Disrespect, disregard,<BR>contempt; ईप्सितं तदवज्ञानात् विद्धि<BR>सार्गलमात्मनः R. 1. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवज्ञेय
अवज्ञेय pot. p. To be treated with<BR>disrespect; contemptible; विप्रा हि<BR>क्षत्रियात्मानो नावज्ञेयाः कदाचन Y. 1. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवट|अवटः
अवट a. [अव-अटन्] Produced in<BR>a hole.<BR>--टः<BR>1 A hole, cavity.<BR>--2<BR>A pit; अवटे चापि मे राम प्रक्षिपेमं<BR>कलेवरं; अवटे ये निधीयंते Rām.<BR>--3 A<BR>well.<BR>--4 Any low or depressed part<BR>of the body, sinus; अवटश्चैवमेतानि<BR>स्थानान्यत्र शरीरके Y. 3. 98.<BR>--5 A<BR>juggler.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कच्छपः a tortoise<BR>in a hole; (fig.) one who has had<BR>no experience, who has seen nothing<BR>of the world.<BR>--निरोधनः N. of a<BR>particular hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटिः|अवटि
अवटिः, --टी f. [अव्-अटि]<BR>1 A hole.<BR>--2 A well.<BR>--3 A sinus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटी
अवटिः, --टी f. [अव्-अटि]<BR>1 A hole.<BR>--2 A well.<BR>--3 A sinus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटीट|अवटीटः
अवटीट a. [नासिकायाः नतं अवटीटं,<BR>अव-टीटन् नासिकायाः संज्ञायां; नासिकाप्यवटीटा,<BR>पुरुषोप्यवटीटः P. V. 2. 31 Sk.]<BR>Having a flat nose, flat-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवटुः|अवटु
अवटुः [अव-टीक् मित˚ डु]<BR>1 A hole<BR>in the ground.<BR>--2 A well.<BR>--3 The<BR>back or nape of the neck.<BR>--4 The<BR>depressed part of the body.<BR>--5 A kind<BR>of tree.<BR>--टुः f. The raised portion of<BR>the neck.<BR>--टु n. A hole, a rent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः a hind curl, the hair<BR>on the back of the head; Śi. 10. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवट्य
अवट्य a. Ved. Being in a hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवडंगः|अवडङ्ग|अवडङ्गः
अवडंगः --कः= A market, a mart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवडंकः|अवडङ्क|अवडङ्कः
अवडंगः --कः= A market, a mart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवडीनं|अवडीन
अवडीनं [अव-डी-भावे-क्त] The<BR>flight of a bird, flying down-wards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंड|अवण्ड
अवंड a. Ved. Not without a<BR>tail (said of a cow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतः|अवत
अवतः [अव-अटच् वेदे पृ˚ टस्य तः] A<BR>well, cistern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसः|अवतंस|अवतंसं
अवतंसः --सं [अव-तंस्-घञ्]<BR>1 A<BR>garland.<BR>--2 An ear-ing, a<BR>ring-shaped ornament, an ear-ornament (fig.<BR>also); गणां नमेरुप्रसवावतंसाः Ku. 1. 55;<BR>स्ववाहनक्षोभचलावतंसाः 7. 38;<BR>चंदनपल्लवावतंसां K. 11, 12, 140, 97;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">Page0180-a+ 56</a>]<BR>R. 13. 49; Dk. 5, 88; Ki. 3. 11;<BR>Śi. 3. 81; ˚उत्पलं a lotus used as an<BR>ornament; Ku. 4. 8; oft. with अ<BR>omitted; यैर्वतंसकुसुमैः प्रियमेताः Śi. 10. 67.<BR>--3 An ornament worn on the head,<BR>crest; (fig.) anything that serves<BR>as an ornament; ‘decked with’;<BR>तामरसावतंसा जलसंनिवेशाः Chāt. 2. 3;<BR>पुंडरीकावतंसाभिः परिखाभिः Rām.;<BR>पुष्पावतंसं सलिलं Suśr.; कल्याणावतंसा<BR>कल्याणसंपद् Māl. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसं|अवतंस|अवतंसः
अवतंसः --सं [अव-तंस्-घञ्]<BR>1 A<BR>garland.<BR>--2 An ear-ing, a<BR>ring-shaped ornament, an ear-ornament (fig.<BR>also); गणां नमेरुप्रसवावतंसाः Ku. 1. 55;<BR>स्ववाहनक्षोभचलावतंसाः 7. 38;<BR>चंदनपल्लवावतंसां K. 11, 12, 140, 97;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">Page0180-a+ 56</a>]<BR>R. 13. 49; Dk. 5, 88; Ki. 3. 11;<BR>Śi. 3. 81; ˚उत्पलं a lotus used as an<BR>ornament; Ku. 4. 8; oft. with अ<BR>omitted; यैर्वतंसकुसुमैः प्रियमेताः Śi. 10. 67.<BR>--3 An ornament worn on the head,<BR>crest; (fig.) anything that serves<BR>as an ornament; ‘decked with’;<BR>तामरसावतंसा जलसंनिवेशाः Chāt. 2. 3;<BR>पुंडरीकावतंसाभिः परिखाभिः Rām.;<BR>पुष्पावतंसं सलिलं Suśr.; कल्याणावतंसा<BR>कल्याणसंपद् Māl. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0179-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसयति
अवतंसयति Den. P. To use as<BR>ear-rings, make ear-rings of;<BR>अवतंसयंति दयमानाः प्रमदाः<BR>शिरीषकुसुमानि Ś. 1. 4; अवतंसयैनं M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसकः|अवतंसक
अवतंसकः An ear-ornament, an<BR>ornament in general;<BR>अशोकस्तबकेनेव दिङ्मुखस्यावतंसकं V. 5. 3;<BR>प्रासादादृवितंसका (लंका) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतंसित
अवतंसित a. Having a garland,<BR>crested; (fig.) decked, adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतक्षणं|अवतक्षण
अवतक्षणं<BR>1 Anything cut in<BR>pieces.<BR>--2 Chopped straw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतड्
अवतड् {c10c} P. To strike<BR>downwards; विद्युदवताडयति Nir.; to crush<BR>under, trample down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवताडनं|अवताडन
अवताडनं<BR>1 Crushing, trampling or<BR>treading under; नैसर्गिकी सुरभिणः<BR>कुसुमस्य सिद्धा मूर्ध्नि स्थितिर्न<BR>चरणैरवताडनानि U. 1. 14.<BR>--2 Striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतन्
अवतन् {c8c} U.<BR>1 To stretch or<BR>extend downwards; ऋज्वीर्दधानैरवतत्य<BR>कंधराः Śi. 12. 18; विशालमूलावततः (<BR>न्यग्रोध) Hariv.<BR>--2 To overspread, cover;<BR>नभसि मेघावतते Suśr.; खमवतत्य<BR>सलिलदाः Bṛ. S. 24. 19.<BR>--3 To loosen,<BR>undo (especially a bow-string).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतत
अवतत p. p.<BR>1 Overspread, covered;<BR>लताशतैरवतता (नदी) Rām.;<BR>तुरंगौघैरवतता (भूः) ibid.<BR>--2 Loosened,<BR>slackened; ˚धन्वन् whose bow is unbent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवततिः|अवतति
अवततिः f. Stretching, extend<BR>ing; प्रालेयावततिम्लान Ki. 11. 4<BR>(snow-fall).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतानः|अवतान
अवतानः<BR>1 Stretching.<BR>--2 The<BR>unbending of a bow.<BR>--3 A<BR>downward face.<BR>--4 The spreading of<BR>a plant; लताशतैरवततामवतानशतैस्तथा<BR>Rām.<BR>--5 A cover (in general); an<BR>awning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतप्
अवतप् {c1c} P. To radiate heat or<BR>light downwards. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>irradiate, heat; अथावताप्य पृथिवीं<BR>पूषा दिवससंक्षये जगामास्तं Mb.<BR>--2 To<BR>illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतप्त
अवतप्त p. p. Heated,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-b" target="_blank">Page0180-b+ 56</a>]<BR>irradiated; अवतप्तेनकुलस्थितं an ichneumon's<BR>standing on hot ground<BR>(metaphorically said of the inconstancy of<BR>man) P. II. 1. 47; अवतप्तेनकुलस्थितं त<BR>एतत् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतापिन्
अवतापिन् a. (A place) where the<BR>sun strikes vertically down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतमसं|अवतमस
अवतमसं [अवततं व्याप्तं तमः<BR>अच्समासः P. V. 4. 79]<BR>1 Slight or dim<BR>darkness; क्षीणेऽवतमसं तमः Ak.<BR>--2<BR>Darkness (in general); अवतमसभिदायै<BR>भास्वताभ्युद्गतेन Śi. 11. 57 (where Malli.<BR>says यद्यपि क्षीणेऽवतमसं तमः इत्युक्तं तथापि<BR>इह विरोधाद्विशेषानादरेण सामान्यमेव ग्राह्यं).<BR>--3 Obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरं|अवतर|अवतरः
अवतरं ind. Ved. Farther away,<BR>more distantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतस्
अवतस् ind. Below, in the lower<BR>world; Ki. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतर्पणं|अवतर्पण
अवतर्पणं A soothing remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतॄ
अवतॄ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To descend, alight,<BR>come down; रथादवततार च R. 1. 54,<BR>13. 68; वसन् ददर्शावतरंतमंबरात्<BR>Śi. 1. 1; यमुनातटमवतीर्णः Pt. 1;<BR>मेघपदवीमवतीर्णौ स्वः Ś. 7; कदैतदंवतरिष्यति<BR>चक्रंमस्तकात् Pt. 5; (fig. also); इति मतिरेव<BR>न बोंधपदवीमवतरति K. 289 fails to<BR>see; वागेव मे नाभिधेयविषयमवतरति त्रपया<BR>151 I cannot speak for very shame<BR>--2 To flow or run into, discharge<BR>contents, join (as a river); सागरं<BR>वर्जयित्वा कुत्र वा महानद्यवतरति Ś. 3; see<BR>अवतीर्ण also.<BR>--3 To enter, to enter<BR>into, to come to; M. 1. 22;<BR>Śi. 9. 32; त्वदीयं देशमवतीर्य M. 5.<BR>--4 To<BR>begin, commence; अवतरतु भवान्<BR>Dk. 152; तत्प्रेयसीमाहूय संगीतकमवतरामि<BR>Dhūrt. 1.<BR>--5 To present oneself,<BR>appear forth, come; प्रसभमवततार<BR>चित्तजन्मा Ki. 10. 17.<BR>--6 To descend (as<BR>a deity) into the world in the form<BR>of a mortal; शापावतीर्ण Ks. 2. 21;<BR>मुनिकन्या च सा शापात्तस्यां जाताववातरत्<BR>2. 31. Rāj. T. 1. 130; 5. 66;<BR>विष्णुरेवावतीर्णोसौ Mārk. P.<BR>--7 To get over,<BR>subdue, conquer; अवतीर्णोस्मि<BR>यद्रोगमतिदुस्तरं Ks. 21. 194; अव तस्य बलं तिर<BR>Rv. 10. 133. 5. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to<BR>descend, bring or fetch down; मार्गे<BR>कथंचिदवतार्य Mu. 3. 9; रथात्, वृक्षात्,<BR>शूलाग्रात् &c.<BR>--2 To take down, put or<BR>set down; अवतारय सलिलसमीपं K. 38;<BR>मात्रां कक्षांतरादवतार्य Pt. 1;<BR>स्वभुजादवतारिता R. 1. 34; अवतार्यतां रथः V. 1.<BR>--3 To take off, remove, withdraw,<BR>put aside; स्वगात्रादवतार्य भूषणानि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-c" target="_blank">Page0180-c+ 58</a>]<BR>Mu. 2, 5; अथांगराजादवतार्य चक्षुः<BR>R. 6. 30, अथोरुदेशादवतार्य पादं Ku. 3. 11,<BR>Śi. 9. 36.<BR>--4 To bring downwards.<BR>--5 To<BR>bend down.<BR>--6 To introduce, set<BR>a-going, make current, begin; तेन<BR>विद्यावतारिता Rāj. T. 4. 485; तत्र तया<BR>सत्रेऽवतारिते 2. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरः|अवतर|अवतरं
अवतरः Descent; N. 3. 53; Śi. 1. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरणं|अवतरण
अवतरणं<BR>1 Descending for bathing<BR>in water &c., गंगा˚, अप्सरस्तीर्थ˚;<BR>descending or alighting (in general),<BR>coming down; स्तन्य˚.<BR>--2 An<BR>incarnation; see अवतार.<BR>--3 Crossing.<BR>--4 Sudden disappearance.<BR>--5 Steps<BR>or stairs leading to a river.<BR>--6<BR>A holy bathing-place (तीर्थ).<BR>--7<BR>Translating from one language into<BR>another.<BR>--8 Introduction.<BR>--9 An<BR>extract, a quotation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरणिका
अवतरणिका<BR>1 A short prayer at<BR>the beginning of a work which, it<BR>is supposed, causes the divinity so<BR>addressed to descend from heaven.<BR>--2 Introduction, preface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतरणी
अवतरणी [अवतरति ग्रंथोऽनया<BR>अवतॄकरणे-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Preface.<BR>--2 Succession,<BR>order, method.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारः|अवतार
अवतारः [अव-तॄ करणे घञ्]<BR>1 Descent,<BR>alighting; descending or going<BR>down into; (fig.)<BR>accepting, resorting to; पाखंडिपथावतारः<BR>Dk. 47; advent, setting in;<BR>वसंतावतारसमये Ś. 1.<BR>--2 Form,<BR>manifestation; मत्स्यादिभिरवतारैरवतारवता<BR>वताऽवतावसुधां Śaṅkara.<BR>--3 Descent<BR>of a deity upon earth, incarnation<BR>in general; कोप्येष संप्रति नवः<BR>पुरुषावतारः U. 5. 34; धर्मार्थकाममोक्षाणामवतार<BR>इवांगवान् R. 10. 84; ऋष्यवतारोयं नृपतिः<BR>Ks. 7. 18.<BR>--4 An incarnation of<BR>Viṣṇu; विष्णुर्येन दशावतारगहने क्षिप्तो<BR>महासंकटे Bh. 3. 95. There are ten<BR>incarnations of Viṣṇu; the<BR>following verse from Gīt. describes them;<BR>वेदानुद्धरते जगन्निवहते भूगोलमुद्बिभ्रते दैत्यं<BR>दारयते बलिं छलयते क्षत्रक्षयं कुर्वते । पौलस्त्यं<BR>जयते हलं कलयते कारुण्यमातन्वते<BR>म्लेच्छान्मूर्च्छयते दशाकृतिकृते कृष्णाय तुभ्यं नमः ॥.<BR>मत्स्यः कूर्मो वराहश्च नरसिंहोथ वामनः । रामो<BR>रामश्च कृष्णश्च बुद्धः कल्की च ते दश ॥.<BR>--5<BR>Any new appearance, growth, rise;<BR>नवावतारं कमलादिवोत्पलम् R. 3. 36;<BR>परीवादनवावतारः 5. 24; यौवनावतारे<BR>K. 289; Ve. 3; Śānti. 2. 26;<BR>3. 14; Ks. 8. 30.<BR>--6 Any<BR>distinguished person (who, in the language of<BR>respect, is called an अवतार or<BR>incarnation of a deity).<BR>--7 Aiming at<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">Page0181-a+ 56</a>]<BR>an object.<BR>--8 A landing-place; रुद्धे<BR>गजेन सरितः सरुषावतारे Śi. 5. 33.<BR>--9<BR>A sacred bathing-place.<BR>--10<BR>Translation.<BR>--11 A pond, tank.<BR>--12<BR>Introduction, preface.<BR>--13 Crossing; ˚रं<BR>लभ् to gain one's object (with gen.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कथा account of an अवतार,<BR>N. of a chapter in शंकरविजय.<BR>--मंत्रः<BR>the prayer causing the descent of a<BR>deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0180-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारक
अवतारक a. (--रिका f.)<BR>1 Making<BR>one's appearance.<BR>--2 Making a<BR>descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारणं|अवतारण
अवतारणं<BR>1 Causing to descend.<BR>--2<BR>Translation.<BR>--3 Possession by an<BR>evil spirit.<BR>--4 Worship, adoration.<BR>--5 The ends or border of a garment.<BR>--6 Preface or introduction (to a<BR>work).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतारिन्
अवतारिन् a. Making one's<BR>appearance, making a descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतीर्ण|अवतीर्णः|अवतीर्ण्ण
अवतीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Descended,<BR>alighted, come down; शैलराजावतीर्णां<BR>जह्नोः कन्यां Me. 50; जलनिधिमनुरूपं<BR>जह्नुकन्यावतीर्णा R. 6. 85;<BR>संसारपथमवतीर्णानां K. 175 who have entered<BR>upon mundane life.<BR>--2 Bathed in;<BR>उदधिमिवावतीर्णः K. 158; come to,<BR>entered into.<BR>--3 Appeared as an<BR>incarnation; तदर्थमवतीर्णोऽसौ<BR>मन्नियोगाच्चतुर्भुजः Mb.; Pt. 1.<BR>--4 Crossed,<BR>passed over; अपि नामावतीर्णोसि<BR>बाणगोचरं Māl. 1 crossed the path, gone<BR>within the range, of arrows;<BR>दर्शनपथमवतीर्णः Ś. 3.<BR>--5 Fallen (as the<BR>night); अवतीर्णायां तस्यां यामिन्यां<BR>K. 269; भरेणावतीर्णायां रजन्यां K. 368.<BR>--6 Translated.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ऋण a.<BR>absolved from debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतूलयति
अवतूलयति Den. P. To rub with<BR>cotton; तूलैरवकुष्णाति तूलेन<BR>तृणाग्रमवघट्टयति Bop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवतोका
अवतोका [अवपतितं तोकं अस्याः; प्रा˚<BR>ब˚] A woman or a cow miscarrying<BR>from accident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्त
अवत्त, अवत्तिन् See under अवदो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्तिन्
अवत्त, अवत्तिन् See under अवदो.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्रस्त
अवत्रस्त a. Terrified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्सीय
अवत्सीय a. Not suitable for a<BR>calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदंशः|अवदंश
अवदंशः [अवदश्यते पानरुच्यर्थं;<BR>अवदंश् कर्मणि घञ्] Any pungent food<BR>which excites thirst, stimulant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदत्त
अवदत्त a.<BR>1 Given away.<BR>--2<BR>Finished, accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदह्
अवदह् {c1c} P. To burn down,<BR>destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाघः|अवदाघ
अवदाघः<BR>1 Heat, burning down.<BR>--2<BR>The hot season, summer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाहः|अवदाह|अवदाहं
अवदाहः --हं [अवसादितो दाहो येन; प्रा˚<BR>ब˚]<BR>1 N. of the root of a plant<BR>(वीरण).<BR>--2 Burning down, heat;<BR>˚इष्टकापथं the root of the वीरण plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदाहं|अवदाह|अवदाहः
अवदाहः --हं [अवसादितो दाहो येन; प्रा˚<BR>ब˚]<BR>1 N. of the root of a plant<BR>(वीरण).<BR>--2 Burning down, heat;<BR>˚इष्टकापथं the root of the वीरण plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदात|अवदातं|अवदातः
अवदात a. [अव-दै-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Beautiful; अवदातकांतिः Dk. 107, 37.<BR>--2<BR>Clean, clear, pure, spotless, refined,<BR>purified, polished; सर्वविद्यावदातचेताः<BR>K. 36; so विद्यावदातं मुखं; शास्त्र˚.<BR>--3<BR>Bright, white; आपिशंगावदातया<BR>देहप्रभया K. 36, 65, 128, 187, 189, 43,<BR>62, 95; रजनिकरकलावदातं कुलं K. 233;<BR>कुंदावदाताः कलहंसमालाः Bk. 2. 18;<BR>cf. also Bh. 2. 25; Ki. 11. 75,<BR>3. 25; 13. 37; Śānti. 3. 14.<BR>--4<BR>Virtuous, meritorious; अन्यस्मिञ् जन्मनि<BR>न कृतमवदातं कर्म K. 62.<BR>--5 Yellow.<BR>--तः White or yellow colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदानं|अवदान
अवदानं<BR>1 A pure or approved<BR>occupation.<BR>--2 An accomplished<BR>act.<BR>--3 A valorous or glorious act,<BR>prowess, heroic act, heroism,<BR>glorious achievement;<BR>संगीयमानत्रिपुरावदानः Ku. 7. 48; Śi. 7. 2, 18. 16;<BR>प्रापदस्त्रमवदानतोषितात् R. 11. 21;<BR>Ki. 17. 16; तत्त्वत्पूर्वावदानेभ्यो न रोचते<BR>Dk. 52; Ki. 3. 43, 13. 32.<BR>--4 Object of<BR>a legend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदान्य
अवदान्य a. Niggardly, stingy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदावद
अवदावद a. Ved. Having no bad<BR>reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदॄ
अवदॄ {c9c} P. To split or force open,<BR>to rend or tear asunder. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To cause to burst, to rend, split;<BR>मनःशिलागिरेः शृंगं वज्रेणेवावदारितं Rām.<BR>--2 To dig down, excavate;<BR>तदर्थमुर्वीमवदारयद्भिः R. 13. 3; वसुधां<BR>चावदारयेत् Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदरणं|अवदरण
अवदरणं Breaking(as a boil),<BR>bursting, separating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदारणं|अवदारण
अवदारणं<BR>1 Tearing, dividing,<BR>digging down, cutting into pieces.<BR>--2<BR>(करणे-ल्युट्) A spade, hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदीर्ण|अवदीर्णं
अवदीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Split into two,<BR>divided, broken;<BR>अवदीर्णशुक्तिपुटमुक्तमौक्तिकप्रकरैः Śi. 13. 37.<BR>--2<BR>Melted, fused, liquefied.<BR>--3 Bewildered,<BR>perplexed; भयावदीर्णः संत्रासादबद्धं बहु<BR>भाषसे Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदो
अवदो {c4c} P.<BR>1 To cut off, divide.<BR>--2 (Ved.) To appease (anger).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्त
अवत्त p. p. [अव-दो-खंडने कर्मणि क्त]<BR>Cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवत्तिन्
अवत्तिन् a. [अवत्तमनेन इष्टा˚ इनि]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">Page0181-c+ 60</a>]<BR>One who divides or cuts off; पंच˚<BR>dividing into five parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदानं|अवदान
अवदानं [अव-दो-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Cutting or<BR>dividing into pieces.<BR>--2 A part,<BR>portion; हृदयाद्यवदानानाम् Ś. B.<BR>--3<BR>Transgression.<BR>--4 The root of a<BR>plant; see अवदान also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवदोहः|अवदोह
अवदोहः<BR>1 Milking.<BR>--2 Milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्य|अवद्यं
अवद्य a.<BR>1 Fit to be<BR>condemned, censurable, not to be praised;<BR>न चापि काव्यं नवमित्यवद्यं<BR>M. 1. 2; किमवद्यः करिकुंभजो मणिः<BR>Śi. 16. 45.<BR>--2 Defective, faulty, blamable,<BR>disagreeable, disliked; उदवहदनवद्यां<BR>तामवद्यादपेतः R. 7. 70; see अनवद्य<BR>also.<BR>--3 Unfit to be told.<BR>--4 Low,<BR>inferior.<BR>--5 Sinful.<BR>--द्यं<BR>1 A fault,<BR>defect, imperfection.<BR>--2 Sin, vice.<BR>--3 Blame, censure, reproach;<BR>उदवहदनवद्यां तामवद्यादपेतः R. 7. 70.<BR>--4<BR>Shame.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गोहन a.<BR>concealing or keeping off want.<BR>--भीः f.<BR>fear of vices or sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्यवत्|अवद्यवन्त्
अवद्यवत् a. Ved. Disgraceful,<BR>lamentable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्योतनं|अवद्योतन
अवद्योतनं Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्योतिन्
अवद्योतिन् a. Shining down upon,<BR>illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवद्रंगः|अवद्रङ्ग|अवद्रङ्गः
अवद्रंगः A market.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध|अवधः
अवध a. Ved. Inviolable,<BR>invulnerable.<BR>--धः Exemption from<BR>death; Ms. 5. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्य
अवध्य a. Not to be killed,<BR>inviolable, sacred; ˚ता, ˚भावः, ˚त्वं<BR>exemption from death, inviolability;<BR>वधार्हाणामवध्यताम् R. 17. 19;<BR>सदैवावध्यभावेन दूतो वदति नान्यथा H. 3. 15;<BR>R. 10. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधर्ष्य
अवधर्ष्य a. To be defied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधा
अवधा {c3c} A.<BR>1 To place down,<BR>deposit; अवधाय श्वभ्रे मृत्पिंडं Kāty.; यथा<BR>क्षुरः क्षुरधानेऽवहितः Śat. Br.;<BR>ततस्तांस्तेषु कुंडेषु गर्भानवदधे तदा Mb.; वासुदेवः<BR>स्वमाययात्मन्यवधीयमानः Bhāg.; to fix:<BR>पादाग्रे दृशमवधाय निश्चलांगी Mu. 5. 13.<BR>--2 To apply (as the mind).<BR>--3 To<BR>be attentive; इतोऽवधत्तां देवराजः<BR>Mv. 6.<BR>--4 To shut, close, press together.<BR>--Pass. To be placed, applied,<BR>or directed (mind); अवधीयतां listen,<BR>hear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधातव्य
अवधातव्य pot. p. To be<BR>attended to, deserving<BR>attention and care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधानीय
अवधानीय pot. p. To be<BR>attended to, deserving<BR>attention and care.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधानं|अवधान
अवधानं<BR>1 Attention, अवधानपरे<BR>चकार सा प्रलयांतोन्मिषिते विलोचने<BR>Ku. 4. 2; अवधानं दीयमानं प्रार्थये Ve. 1;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">Page0182-a+ 57</a>]<BR>intentness, attentiveness; दत्तावधानः<BR>शृणोति hears attentively.<BR>--2 Devotion,<BR>care, carefulness; अवधानात् carefully<BR>or attentively; शृणुत जना अवधानात्<BR>क्रियामिमां कालिदासस्य V. 1. 2. v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0181-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधानिन्
अवधानिन् a. Attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधिः|अवधि
अवधिः [अव-धा-कि]<BR>1<BR>Application, attention.<BR>--2 Boundary, limit<BR>exclusive or inclusive, (in time or<BR>space); conclusion, determination;<BR>एकैकस्य जगत्त्रयप्रमथनत्राणावधिर्योग्यता<BR>Mv. 1. 46;<BR>रवितेजसामवधिनाधिवेष्टितम् Ki. 12. 22.<BR>--3 Furthest limit;<BR>दृष्ट आह्लादनीयानामवधिः K. 124;<BR>स्मरशापावधिदां सरस्वतीं Ku. 4. 43;<BR>conclusion; oft. at the end of comp., in<BR>the sense of ‘ending with,’ ‘as far<BR>as’, ‘till’; एष ते जीवितावधिः प्रवादः U. 1;<BR>तत्प्रत्यागमनकालावधयोपि तावत् ध्रियंतां<BR>प्राणाः K. 171; व्याडी रक्षतु मे देहं ततः<BR>प्रत्यागमावधि Ks. 4. 100; स्कंधः<BR>स्यान्मूलाच्छाखावधिस्तरोः Ak.<BR>--4 Period of<BR>time, time; सर्वे निदाघावधिना प्रमृष्टाः<BR>R. 16. 52; शेषान् मासान्<BR>विरहदिवसस्थापितस्यावधेर्वा Me. 87; अपि समाप्तः<BR>वनवासस्यावधिः Mv. 7, 2. 48; विवाहं<BR>मासावधिकमकल्पयत् Dk. 54, 174;<BR>K. 328; Ki. 12. 17; यदवधि-तवधि from<BR>or ever since, till, Bv. 2. 79; अथ<BR>चेदवधिः प्रतीक्ष्यते Ki. 2. 16.<BR>--5 An<BR>engagement, appointment;<BR>रमणीयोवधिर्विधिना विसंवादितः Ś. 6.<BR>--6 A division,<BR>district, department; जनपदतदवध्योश्च<BR>P. IV. 2. 124.<BR>--7 A hole, pit. ˚ता,<BR>˚त्वं limit, limitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधिमत्|अवधिमन्त्
अवधिमत् a. Limited, bounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधेय
अवधेय pot. p.<BR>1 To be placed<BR>down or deposited.<BR>--2 To be<BR>attended to, to be believed.<BR>--3 To be<BR>known or apprehended.<BR>--यं<BR>Attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित|अवहितं
अवहित p. p.<BR>1 Deposited, placed.<BR>--2 Attentive, careful; शृणुत<BR>मनोभिरवहितैः V. 1. 2; शृणु मेऽवहिता वचः<BR>Rām.; Me. 100.<BR>--3 Clebrated, known;<BR>˚ता application, attention.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजलि a. with joined hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधाव्
अवधाव् {c1c} U. To run down, to<BR>drop down, to run after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावनं|अवधावन
अवधावनं<BR>1 Running after,<BR>pursuing, seizure.<BR>--2 Cleaning, washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधावित
अवधावित p. p.<BR>1 Chased, pursued.<BR>--2 Cleaned, washed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीर्
अवधीर् {c10c} P. To disregard,<BR>disrespect, treat with contempt, slight;<BR>अवधीरितसुहृद्वचनस्य H. 1; Śi. 9. 59,<BR>Amaru. 83; to despise, repudiate,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">Page0182-b+ 56</a>]<BR>repulse; तत्किमवधीरयति मामार्यपुत्रः M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरणं|अवधीरण
अवधीरणं Treating with disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरणा
अवधीरणा Disrespect, despising;<BR>repulse; कृतवत्यसि नावधीरणामपराद्धे<BR>ऽपि यदा चिरं मयि R. 8. 48; M. 3. 19;<BR>अयं स ते तिष्ठति संगमोत्सुको विशंकसे भीरु<BR>यतोवधीरणां Ś. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरित
अवधीरित p. p. Disrespected,<BR>disregarded, slighted; अवधीरितार्तवगुणं<BR>Ki. 6. 25 excelled, set at naught;<BR>अचेतनं नाम गुणं न लक्षयेन्मयैव<BR>कस्मादवधीरिता प्रिया Ś. 6. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधीरिन्
अवधीरिन् a.<BR>1 Despising, scorning.<BR>--2 Excelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधू
अवधू {c5c} U.<BR>1 To shake. move,<BR>wave, cause to tremble; रेणुः<BR>पवनावधूतः R. 7. 43; लीलावधूतैः चामरैः<BR>Me. 35; Rs. 6. 15; Ki. 6. 3; Śi. 13. 36.<BR>--2 To shake off or out, shake, toss<BR>(lit. and fig.), remove (fig. also);<BR>overcome, get the better of;<BR>राजसत्त्वमवधूय मातृकं R. 11. 90;<BR>सुरवधूरवधूतभयाः शरैः 9. 19 removing the fears<BR>of; अवधूय तद्व्यथां 3. 61; व्रजंति<BR>शत्रूनवधूय निस्पृहाः शमेन सिद्धिं मुनयो न<BR>भूभृतः Ki. 1. 42; रुषावधूय रक्षांसि Rām.<BR>--3 To discard, spurn, reject or treat<BR>with contempt, disregard; चंडी<BR>मामवधूय पादपतितं V. 4. 38; Ku. 3. 8;<BR>अवधूतप्रणिपाताः V. 3. 5;<BR>अवधूतदुहितृप्रार्थनस्य Dk. 13. --Caus. (-धूनयति)<BR>To shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूत|अवधूतः
अवधूत p. p.<BR>1 Shaken, waved.<BR>--2<BR>Discarded, rejected, despised;<BR>R. 19. 43.<BR>--3 Insulted, humiliated.<BR>--4<BR>Excelled, surpassed; Ratn. 2. 8.<BR>--5<BR>Attacked, overcome.<BR>--6 Separated<BR>from worldly attachments.<BR>--तः An<BR>ascetic who has renounced all<BR>worldly attachments and<BR>connections; यो विलंघ्याश्रमान्वर्णानात्मन्येव स्थितः<BR>पुमान् । अतिवर्णाश्रमी योगी अवधूतः स उच्यते ॥<BR>or अक्षरत्वात् वरेण्यत्वात् धूतसंसारबंधनात् ।<BR>तत्त्वमस्यर्थसिद्धत्वादवधूतोऽभिधीयते ॥.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वेश a. undressed, naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूननं|अवधूनन
अवधूननं<BR>1 Shaking, waving;<BR>पादस्पर्शस्तु रक्षांसि दुष्कृतीनवधूननं<BR>Ms. 3. 230; अमंददष्टौष्ठकरावधूननम् Ki. 8. 6.<BR>--2 The practice of medicine, curing.<BR>--3 Agitation, trembling.<BR>--4<BR>Disregarding.<BR>--5 Trampling on, treading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूकः|अवधूक
अवधूकः One having no wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूपित
अवधूपित a. Perfumed with<BR>incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधूलनं|अवधूलन
अवधूलनं Sprinkling absorbent<BR>powders on sores.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधृ
अवधृ {c10c} U.<BR>1 (a) To<BR>determine, fix, resolve; इत्यवधार्य Pt. 1;<BR>यन्मयाऽवधारितं Mk. 4.<BR>चयस्त्विषामित्यवधारितं पुरा Śi. 1. 3;<BR>विदर्भगतमनुष्ठेयमवधारितं M. 5. (b) To ascertain,<BR>determine accurately, make out,<BR>know, perceive, understand; न<BR>विश्वमूर्तेरवधार्यते वपुः Ku. 5. 78; Mu. 3, 4.<BR>--2 To consider or regard, think,<BR>look upon; मृता मामवधारय Mb.;<BR>कुलीनेत्यवधार्यतां Ks. 21. 124; Śi. 9. 22.<BR>--3 To hear, listen to, become<BR>acquainted with; वानप्रस्थस्य धर्मं ते<BR>कथयाम्यवधार्यतां Mārk. P.<BR>--4 To reflect,<BR>consider, think; बालकोयमित्यवधार्य<BR>Pt. 4.<BR>--5 To limit, restrict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारः|अवधार
अवधारः Accurate determination,<BR>limitation; सर्वत्र यदवधारेणोच्यते स<BR>एकांतः Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारक
अवधारक a.<BR>1 Determining<BR>accurately; इष्टावधारकं वाक्यं आशीः<BR>Bharata.<BR>--2 Restricting oneself to<BR>anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारण|अवधारणं
अवधारण a. Restrictive, limiting.<BR>--णं --णा<BR>1 Ascertainment,<BR>determination; मान˚ Dk. 161.<BR>--2 Affirmation,<BR>emphasis.<BR>--3 Limitation (of the<BR>sense of words); यावदवधारणे,<BR>एवावधारणे; मात्रं कार्त्स्न्येऽवधारणे Ak.;<BR>तुरत्रावधारणार्थः.<BR>--4 Restriction to a certain<BR>instance or instances to the<BR>exclusion of all others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारणीय
अवधारणीय, अवधर्य pot. p. To be<BR>ascertained, determined or<BR>considered; विष्णोरिवास्यानवधारणीयं<BR>R. 13. 5; परिणतिरवधार्या यत्नतः पंडितेन<BR>Bh. 2. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधर्य
अवधारणीय, अवधर्य pot. p. To be<BR>ascertained, determined or<BR>considered; विष्णोरिवास्यानवधारणीयं<BR>R. 13. 5; परिणतिरवधार्या यत्नतः पंडितेन<BR>Bh. 2. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधारित|अवधारितः
अवधारित p. p. Ascertained,<BR>known, well observed, marked;<BR>सम्यगवधारितं Ratn. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवधृत
अवधृत p. p.<BR>1 Determined,<BR>resolved, settled.<BR>--2 Heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्य
अवध्य See under अवध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्र
अव(ब)ध्र a. Ved. Not injurious,<BR>innoxious, beneficent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबध्र
अव(ब)ध्र a. Ved. Not injurious,<BR>innoxious, beneficent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वंस्
अवध्वंस् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To apply<BR>oneself to, set about.<BR>--2 To strew over,<BR>scatter, spread; चूर्णैरवध्वंसते Sk.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cast down.<BR>--2 To<BR>strew over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वंसः|अवध्वंस
अवध्वंसः<BR>1 Abandoning, quitting.<BR>--2 Powder, dust.<BR>--3 Disrespect,<BR>censure, blame.<BR>--4 Falling off or from.<BR>--5 Sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवध्वस्त|अवध्वस्तः
अवध्वस्त p. p.<BR>1 Destroyed,<BR>perished.<BR>--2 Censured, disrespected.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">Page0183-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Pounded coarsely or badly.<BR>--4<BR>Abandoned.<BR>--5 Sprinkled.<BR>--6 Scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0182-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनं|अवन
अवनं [अव्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Protection,<BR>defence; भुजोऽनवने P. I. 3. 66,<BR>Nalod. 1. 4.<BR>--2 Gratifying, pleasing.<BR>--3 Wish<BR>desire.<BR>--4 Delight, satisfaction.<BR>--5<BR>Hurry, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनक्षत्रं|अवनक्षत्र
अवनक्षत्रं The disappearance of<BR>the stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनम्
अवनम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bow down, to<BR>bend down, stoop; Śi. 9. 74<BR>--2 To<BR>bend oneself, hang down; त्वय्यादातुं<BR>जलमवनते Me. 46. See अवनत also.<BR>--Caus. (अवन-ना-मयति) To bend down,<BR>bend; अवनमंय द्विषतां शिरांसि K. 109;<BR>श्वपुच्छमवनामितम् Pt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनत|अवनतं
अवनत p. p.<BR>1 Bent down, hung<BR>down, downcast; विनय˚, प्रश्रय˚,<BR>लज्जा, ˚उत्तरकायं R. 9. 60;<BR>फलपुष्पैरवनतान् Rām.<BR>--2 Verging in the west,<BR>setting; रजनिरवनतेंदुर्लज्जयाधोमुखी च<BR>Śi. 10. 91.<BR>--3 Bending, stooping,<BR>deepened, not projecting.<BR>--4<BR>Humble.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. with stooping;<BR>limbs; Ku. 5. 86.<BR>--काय a.<BR>bending the body, crouching down.<BR>--मुख a. with down-cast<BR>countenance.<BR>--शीर्षन् a. bowing the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनतिः|अवनति
अवनतिः f.<BR>1 Bending, bowing<BR>down, stooping; अवनतिमवनेः<BR>Mu. 1. 2, 3. 8; Śi. 9. 8.<BR>--2 Declining in the<BR>west, setting; Śi. 9. 8.<BR>--3 A bow,<BR>prostration.<BR>--4 Bending (as a bow);<BR>धनुषामवनतिः K. (where अ˚ also<BR>means ‘stooping’).<BR>--5 Modesty,<BR>absence of insolence, humility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनम्र
अवनम्र a. Bowed, bent;<BR>पर्याप्तपुष्पस्तबकावनम्रा Ku. 3. 54; पाद˚<BR>fallen at the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामः|अवनाम
अवनामः<BR>1 Bending or bowing,<BR>falling at the feet; गलितनयनवारेर्याति<BR>पादावनामं Śi. 11. 35.<BR>--2 Causing<BR>to bend down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामक
अवनामक a. What depresses or<BR>causes to bend or bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनामिन्
अवनामिन् a. Bending or bowing<BR>down; Ki. 7. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनह्
अवनह् {c4c} U. To bind on, tie on,<BR>put over, cover with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनद्ध|अवनद्धं
अवनद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Formed, made.<BR>--2 Fixed, seated;<BR>स्त्यानावनद्धघनशोणितशोणपाणिः Ve. 1. 21.<BR>--3 Covered,<BR>encircled;<BR>तांबूलीलतावनद्धपूगखंडमंडितैः K. 19; Śi. 3. 7; bound on, tied;<BR>चर्मावनद्धं दुर्गंधिपूर्णं मूत्रपुरीषयोः<BR>Ms. 6. 76; हेममालावनद्धः (रथः) Mb.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">Page0183-b+ 55</a>]<BR>पुष्पभारावनद्धः (पादपः) Rām.; Bṛ. S. 3. 19.<BR>20, 67, 59, 84; fastened, woven,<BR>put together; स्रगवनद्धमनोरमपल्लवा<BR>Śi. 6. 53; 7. 52.<BR>--द्धं A drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाहः|अवनाह
अवनाहः Binding, girding,<BR>putting on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनाट|अवनाटः
अवनाट a. [नतं नासिकायाः; अव-नाटच्<BR>see अवटीट] Flat-nosed.<BR>--टं The<BR>condition of having a flat nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिः|अवनि
अवनिः --नी f. [अव्-अनि<BR>Uṇ. 2. 101]<BR>1 The earth; oft used at the<BR>end of comp. meaning ‘ground’,<BR>‘place’; काननावनौ Dk. 7, 13;<BR>लीलावनौ place of recreation 25.<BR>--2 A<BR>finger (Nir.).<BR>--3 A river;<BR>Rv. 1. 190. 7.<BR>--4 N. of a plant.<BR>--5 Course, bed of<BR>a river. अवनिंगत a. fallen prostrate<BR>on the ground.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः, --ईश्वरः<BR>--नाथः, --पतिः, --पालः lord of the earth,<BR>king; पतिरवनिपतीनां तैश्चकाशे चतुर्भिः<BR>R. 10. 86, 11. 93.<BR>--चरः a. roving<BR>over the earth, vagabond.<BR>--ध्रः a<BR>mountain Śi. 16. 78.<BR>--तल the<BR>surface of the earth.<BR>--मंडलं the globe.<BR>--रुहः, --ट् a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनी
अवनिः --नी f. [अव्-अनि<BR>Uṇ. 2. 101]<BR>1 The earth; oft used at the<BR>end of comp. meaning ‘ground’,<BR>‘place’; काननावनौ Dk. 7, 13;<BR>लीलावनौ place of recreation 25.<BR>--2 A<BR>finger (Nir.).<BR>--3 A river;<BR>Rv. 1. 190. 7.<BR>--4 N. of a plant.<BR>--5 Course, bed of<BR>a river. अवनिंगत a. fallen prostrate<BR>on the ground.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः, --ईश्वरः<BR>--नाथः, --पतिः, --पालः lord of the earth,<BR>king; पतिरवनिपतीनां तैश्चकाशे चतुर्भिः<BR>R. 10. 86, 11. 93.<BR>--चरः a. roving<BR>over the earth, vagabond.<BR>--ध्रः a<BR>mountain Śi. 16. 78.<BR>--तल the<BR>surface of the earth.<BR>--मंडलं the globe.<BR>--रुहः, --ट् a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिज्
अवनिज् {c3c} U. To wash, purify,<BR>cleanse, to wipe off. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>cause to wash off.<BR>--2 To fill with,<BR>pervade; सुसुगंधतयावनेजितानां Ghaṭ. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनिक्त
अवनिक्त p. p.<BR>1 Washed, cleansed.<BR>--2 Searched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनेज्य
अवनेज्य a. Used for washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनेजनं|अवनेजन
अवनेजनं<BR>1 Washing, ablution;<BR>न कुर्याद्गुरुपुत्रस्य पादयोश्चावनेजनम्<BR>Ms. 2. 209.<BR>--2 Washing off, ablution.<BR>--3 Water for washing, foot-bath;<BR>आपः पादावनेजनीः Ait. Br.<BR>--4<BR>Sprinkling water on the darbha grass at<BR>a Śrāddha ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

