अवनिष्ठीवनं|अवनिष्ठीवन
अवनिष्ठीवनं Spitting upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनी
अवनी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To lead or bring<BR>down, to push into; अश्वानपोऽ<BR>वनीयमानान् Kāty.<BR>--2 To cause to descend<BR>or flow.<BR>--3 To lead away.<BR>--4<BR>To pour down or over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनयः|अवनय
अवनयः<BR>1 Throwing down,<BR>precipitating.<BR>--2 Causing to descend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनयनं|अवनयन
अवनयनं Leading down, pouring<BR>down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनायः|अवनाय
अवनायः Throwing down &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवनायक
अवनायक a. Causing to descend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंतिः|अवन्ति|अवंति|अवन्तिः
अवंतिः --ती f. [अव्-बाहु˚ झिच्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 50]<BR>1 N. of a city, the modern<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-c" target="_blank">Page0183-c+ 58</a>]<BR>उज्जयिनी, one of the seven sacred cities of<BR>the Hindus, to die at which is said to<BR>secure eternal happiness; cf. अयोध्या<BR>मथुरा माया काशी कांचिरवंतिका । पुरी<BR>द्वारावती चैव सप्तैता मोक्षदायिकाः ॥. The women<BR>of Avanti are said to be very<BR>skilful in all erotic arts; cf. आवंत्य एव<BR>निपुणा सुदृशो रतकर्मणि B. R. 10. 82.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a river. --m. pl. N. of a<BR>country and its inhabitants; its<BR>capital being उज्जयिनी on the river<BR>सिप्रा; and there is also the temple<BR>of महाकाल in the suburbs. [According to<BR>Hemacandra अबंति is synonymous with<BR>Mālava or the modern Mālavā; but the<BR>latter country covered in ancient times,<BR>as now, a wider area than Avanti, as<BR>Bāṇa applies the name to a neighbouring<BR>kingdom in the east, whose capital was<BR>Vidiśā on the Vetravatī or Betvā. In<BR>the time of the Mahābhārata Avanti<BR>appears to have extended on the<BR>south to the banks of the Narmadā<BR>and on the west probably to the<BR>banks of the Myhe or Mahi];<BR>अवंतिनाथोऽयमुदग्रबाहुः R. 6. 32; असौ<BR>महाकालनिकेतनस्य वसन्नदूरे किल<BR>चंद्रमौलेः 6. 34, 35;<BR>प्राप्यावंतीनुदयनकथाकोविदग्रामवृद्धान् Me. 30;<BR>अवंतीषूज्जयिनी नाम नगरी K. 52.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरं the city of Avanti<BR>उज्जयिनी.<BR>--ब्रह्मः [अवंतिषु ब्रह्मा अच् समासः<BR>P. V. 4. 104] a Brāhmaṇa residing<BR>in Avanti.<BR>--सोमः [अवंतिषु सोम इव]<BR>sour gruel prepared from the<BR>fermentation of rice-water (कांजिकं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंती|अवन्ती
अवंतिः --ती f. [अव्-बाहु˚ झिच्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 50]<BR>1 N. of a city, the modern<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-c" target="_blank">Page0183-c+ 58</a>]<BR>उज्जयिनी, one of the seven sacred cities of<BR>the Hindus, to die at which is said to<BR>secure eternal happiness; cf. अयोध्या<BR>मथुरा माया काशी कांचिरवंतिका । पुरी<BR>द्वारावती चैव सप्तैता मोक्षदायिकाः ॥. The women<BR>of Avanti are said to be very<BR>skilful in all erotic arts; cf. आवंत्य एव<BR>निपुणा सुदृशो रतकर्मणि B. R. 10. 82.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a river. --m. pl. N. of a<BR>country and its inhabitants; its<BR>capital being उज्जयिनी on the river<BR>सिप्रा; and there is also the temple<BR>of महाकाल in the suburbs. [According to<BR>Hemacandra अबंति is synonymous with<BR>Mālava or the modern Mālavā; but the<BR>latter country covered in ancient times,<BR>as now, a wider area than Avanti, as<BR>Bāṇa applies the name to a neighbouring<BR>kingdom in the east, whose capital was<BR>Vidiśā on the Vetravatī or Betvā. In<BR>the time of the Mahābhārata Avanti<BR>appears to have extended on the<BR>south to the banks of the Narmadā<BR>and on the west probably to the<BR>banks of the Myhe or Mahi];<BR>अवंतिनाथोऽयमुदग्रबाहुः R. 6. 32; असौ<BR>महाकालनिकेतनस्य वसन्नदूरे किल<BR>चंद्रमौलेः 6. 34, 35;<BR>प्राप्यावंतीनुदयनकथाकोविदग्रामवृद्धान् Me. 30;<BR>अवंतीषूज्जयिनी नाम नगरी K. 52.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरं the city of Avanti<BR>उज्जयिनी.<BR>--ब्रह्मः [अवंतिषु ब्रह्मा अच् समासः<BR>P. V. 4. 104] a Brāhmaṇa residing<BR>in Avanti.<BR>--सोमः [अवंतिषु सोम इव]<BR>sour gruel prepared from the<BR>fermentation of rice-water (कांजिकं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंध्य|अवन्ध्य
अवंध्य a. Not barren, fruitful,<BR>productive; अवंध्यवांछितफलप्रदान<BR>K. 260; अवंध्यपातेन बाणेन V. 2. 2; H. 2. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपट्
अवपट् {c10c} P. To split. --Pass.<BR>To split oneself, to be split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपाटिका
अवपाटिका Laceration of the<BR>prepuce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपत्
अवपत् {c1c} P. To fall down, fly<BR>down, jump down, descend, alight,<BR>pounce or swoop upon;<BR>श्येनावपातमवपत्य Prab.; फलैर्वृक्षावपतितैः Rām.<BR>--Caus. To throw down, fell down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपतनं|अवपतन
अवपतनं Alighting, descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपातः|अवपात
अवपातः<BR>1 Falling down; जलं<BR>कूलावपातेन प्रसन्नं कलुषायते Mk. 9. 24;<BR>अधश्चरणावपातं Bh. 2. 31 falling down<BR>at the feet; (fig.) cringing.<BR>--2<BR>Descent, descending; शस्त्रावपातः<BR>Y. 2. 277; कपोत˚ H. 1; श्येन˚ चकिता<BR>Māl. 8. 8 sudden swoop or<BR>pouncing.<BR>--3 A hole, pit.<BR>--4 Particularly,<BR>a hole or pit for catching elephants;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">Page0184-a+ 56</a>]<BR>अवपातस्तु हस्त्यर्थे गर्ते छन्ने तृणादिना<BR>Yādava; रोधांसि निघ्नन्नवपातमग्नः करीव<BR>वन्यः परुषं ररास R. 16. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0183-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपातनं|अवपातन
अवपातनं Felling, knocking down,<BR>throwing down; द्रुमाणां<BR>Ms. 11. 65; कुड्यावपातनं Y. 2. 223.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपद्
अवपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To go down, glide<BR>down; to descend, fall down as केश,<BR>गर्भ &c.<BR>--2 To be deprived of (with<BR>abl.).<BR>--3 To fall, meet with an<BR>accident.<BR>--4 To overthrow, ruin.<BR>--Caus. To cause to glide or go down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपन्न
अवपन्न p. p.<BR>1 Mixed with.<BR>--2<BR>Cooked together with.<BR>--3 Fallen on<BR>or into.<BR>--4 Alighted, descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपादः|अवपाद
अवपादः Falling down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपाक|अवपाकः
अवपाक a.<BR>1 Badly or ill-cooked.<BR>--2 Without a net.<BR>--कः Bad<BR>cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपात्र
अवपात्र a. [अवरं भोजनायोग्यं पात्रं<BR>यस्य] A Mleccha whose eating<BR>in a vessel makes it useless for others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपात्रित
अवपात्रित a. [अवपात्र कृत्यर्थे<BR>णिच्-क्त] One who has lost his caste, a<BR>person not allowed by his kindred<BR>to eat in a common vessel; see<BR>अपपात्रित (= भिन्नोदकीकृत Dāy. B.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपालित
अवपालित a. Unprotected,<BR>neglected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपाशित
अवपाशित a. [अवपाशः समंतात् पाशो<BR>जातोऽस्य तार˚ इतच्] Snared, having<BR>a snare laid over (on all sides);<BR>पश्याम्यैव हि कंठे त्वां कालपाशावपाशितं<BR>Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीड्
अवपीड् {c10c} P. To compress;<BR>ममज्जेव मही तस्य भूरिभारावपीडिता Mb.;<BR>पादौ शिरोभिरवपीडितौ Rām.; to press or<BR>squeeze together; एकीकृतस्त्वचि<BR>निषिक्त इवावपीड्य Māl. 6. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीड|अवपीडः
अवपीड a. Pressed on all sides.<BR>--डः<BR>1 Pressing down, pressure.<BR>--2 A kind of medicinal drug used<BR>to cause sneezing, sternutatory.<BR>--3<BR>A kind of medical treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपीडनं|अवपीडन
अवपीडनं<BR>1 The act of pressing<BR>down.<BR>--2 A sternutatory.<BR>--ना<BR>Damage, violation; Ms. 8. 287.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवपूर्ण
अवपूर्ण a. Full of, filled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवप्रज्जनः|अवप्रज्जन
अवप्रज्जनः The end of the warp<BR>of a web.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवफः|अवफ
अवफः Flatulence, wind from<BR>the bowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबधा
अवबधा Segment of the base of<BR>a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबंध्
अवबंध् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To bind, fasten<BR>(fig. also); नीत्वा कामं गौरवेणावबद्धः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">Page0184-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Śi. 18. 19.<BR>--2 To arrest, rivet;<BR>शिल्पकुशलतयाऽवबध्नाति दृष्टिं Mk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबंधः|अवबन्ध
अवबंधः<BR>1 Falling or palsy of<BR>the eyelids, Blepharoptosis;<BR>व्याधिर्वेत्रावबंधकः Suśr.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>disease.<BR>--3 Binding on all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबाधा
अवबाधा<BR>1 Pain, agony.<BR>--2<BR>Resistance, opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबाहुकः|अवबाहुक
अवबाहुकः [अवबद्धो बाहुर्येन प्रा˚<BR>स˚] Spasm in the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबुध्
अवबुध् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To awake; to<BR>recognise; तं चावबुध्याब्रवम् Dk. 127.<BR>--2 To become sensible or aware of,<BR>feel, perceive, know, understand;<BR>त्वक्स्पर्शं नावबुध्यते Mb.;<BR>एकांतमौग्ध्यानवबुद्धविभ्रमैः Śi. 12. 39; Bk. 15. 101;<BR>Ms. 8. 53; अधीत्यावबुद्ध्य च;<BR>येनावबुध्यते तत्त्वं प्रकृतेः पुरुषस्य च Bhāg.<BR>knows. --Caus.<BR>1 To awaken, rouse;<BR>रामो रामावबोधितः R. 12. 23.<BR>--2 To<BR>make one aware of, inform;<BR>ब्रह्मचोदनानुपुरुषमवबोधयत्येव केवलं Ś. B.;<BR>प्रागेव विदुरो वेद तेनास्मानवबोधयत् Mb.<BR>--3 To remind, put in mind of;<BR>आर्ये सम्यगवबोधितोऽस्मि Ś. 1. v. l.<BR>--4 To teach, instruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबुद्ध
अवबुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Known.<BR>--2 [<BR>कर्तरिक्त] One who knows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधः|अवबोध
अवबोधः<BR>1 Waking, becoming<BR>awake (opp. स्वप्न); यौ तु स्वप्नावबोधौ<BR>तौ भूतानां प्रलयोदयौ Ku. 2. 8;<BR>Bg. 6. 17.<BR>--2 Knowledge, perception;<BR>स्वभर्तृनामग्रहणाद्वभूव सांद्रे रजस्यात्मपरावबोधः<BR>R. 7. 41; भावावबोधकलुषा दयितेव रात्रौ<BR>5. 64; प्रतिकूलेषु तैक्ष्णस्यावबोधः क्रोध<BR>इष्यते S. D.; M. 3. 10; स्वात्मावबोधं महः<BR>Prab. 1. 1.<BR>--3 Discrimination,<BR>judgment; अवबोधवारि रजसः शमनं<BR>Ki. 6. 41.<BR>--4 Teaching, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधक|अवबोधकः
अवबोधक a. Indicating, showing;<BR>निजपराक्रमावबोधकानि चरितानि<BR>Dk. 175.<BR>--कः<BR>1 The awakener, the sun.<BR>--2 A panegyrist, bard.<BR>--3 A teacher.<BR>--4 Thought, intention; मदवबोधकं<BR>प्रकटयता Dk. 153; ˚त्वं instruction,<BR>guidance, explanation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवबोधनं|अवबोधन
अवबोधनं Knowledge, perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवब्रवः|अवब्रव
अवब्रवः [कुत्सितः ब्रवः] Ill-report,<BR>defamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभंज्|अवभञ्ज्
अवभंज् {c7c} P. To break off, smash;<BR>वनस्पतिं व्रज इवावभज्य Ku. 3. 74;<BR>अवभग्नश्च मे मानः Rām., broken down,<BR>humbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभंगः|अवभङ्ग|अवभङ्गः
अवभंगः Humbling, overcoming,<BR>defeating; मानावभंगनिपुणं त्वममोघमस्त्रं<BR>V. 4. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभंजनं|अवभञ्जन
अवभंजनं Breaking, off, tearing,<BR>humbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभाषणं|अवभाषण
अवभाषणं Speaking, telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभास्
अवभास् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To shine;<BR>नात्यर्थमस्त्रैरवभासमानः Ki. 3. 46; स<BR>तेजसा सूर्य इवावभासते Mb.<BR>--2 To<BR>shine forth, become manifest;<BR>आहोस्विन्मुखमवभासते युवत्याः Śi. 8. 29.<BR>--3 To appear, seem (apparently<BR>or falsely); एतत्त्रयं<BR>तप्तायःपिंडवदेकत्वेनावभासते Vedānta. --Caus. To<BR>irradiate, illuminate;<BR>अधिकावभासितदिशां निकरः Śi. 9. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासः|अवभास
अवभासः<BR>1 Splendour, lustre,<BR>light.<BR>--2 Knowledge, perception.<BR>--3 Appearance, manifestation, in<BR>spiration; येनास्य तत्त्वेषु कृतेऽवभासे<BR>Ki. 3. 26.<BR>--4 Space, reach, compass.<BR>--5<BR>False knowledge.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः N.<BR>of a divinity.<BR>--प्रभाः (pl.) N. of a<BR>whole class of deities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासक
अवभासक a. Luminous,<BR>irradiating.<BR>--कं The Supreme spirit; ˚त्वं<BR>luminousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासित
अवभासित p. p.<BR>1 Illumined,<BR>lighted, irradiated.<BR>--2 Evident,<BR>manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभासिन्
अवभासिन् a. Shining, bright.<BR>--नी<BR>The outer skin or cuticle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभिद्
अवभिद् {c7c} P. To break off,<BR>shatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभेदः
अवभेदः Breaking off, shattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभेदिन्
अवभेदिन् a. Breaking off,<BR>shattering, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभुज्
अवभुज् {c6c} P. To bend down,<BR>curve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभुग्न
अवभुग्न p. p. Contracted, bent,<BR>crooked; अवभुग्नभोगिफणमंडलां भुवं<BR>Śi. 15. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभृथः|अवभृथ
अवभृथः [अव-भृ-क्थन् Uṇ. 2. 3]<BR>1 The end or completion of a<BR>principal sacrifice.<BR>--2 Bathing at the<BR>end of a principal sacrifice for<BR>purification; नावभृथं सरस्वत्यां Kāty.;<BR>भुवं कोष्णेन कुंडोध्नी मेध्येनावभृथादपि<BR>R. 1. 84; प्रीत्याश्वमेधावभृथार्द्रमूर्तेः<BR>6.; 9. 22; 11. 31; 13. 61; Y. 3. 244;<BR>Ms. 11. 83.<BR>--3 Purification by<BR>bathing of the sacrificer and the<BR>sacrificial vessels at the end of a<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--4 The water of purification.<BR>--5 A supplementary sacrifice to<BR>atone for defects in a principal and<BR>preceding one; a sacrifice in general;<BR>स्नातवत्यवभृथे ततस्त्वयि Śi. 14. 10.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्नानं ablution after a<BR>sacrificial ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0184-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभ्रः|अवभ्र
अवभ्रः Abduction, carrying off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवभ्रट|अवभ्रटः
अवभ्रट a. [नतं नासिकायाः; अव-भ्रटच्<BR>P. V. 2. 31] Flat-nosed; see अवटीट.<BR>--टं The state of having a flat nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवम|अवमं|अवमः
अवम a. [अव-अमच् Uṇ. 5. 54.]<BR>1 Sinful, wicked.<BR>--2 Contemptible,<BR>mean, undermost, lowest.<BR>--3 Base,<BR>low, inferior (opp. परम);<BR>अनलकानलकानवमां पुरीं R. 9. 14; see अनवम;<BR>या त उक्तिरवमा या परमा Rv. 6. 25. 1.<BR>--4<BR>Next, intimate.<BR>--5 Last, youngest.<BR>--6<BR>decreasing.<BR>--मः<BR>1 A protector.<BR>--2<BR>A class of Manes; त्रिविधाः पितरः<BR>अवमा ऊर्वाः काव्याश्च.<BR>--मं<BR>1 Sin.<BR>--2 A<BR>lunar day exactly coinciding with<BR>a solar one; the difference between<BR>a Cāndra (29 days, 31 Ghaṭikās<BR>and 50 Palas) and a solar month<BR>(30 days); तिथ्यंतद्वंयमेको दिनवारः<BR>स्पृशति यत्र तद्भवत्यवमदिनं Jyotiṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमन्
अवमन् {c4c} A. (or Poet. P.)<BR>1 To<BR>despise, contemn, disregard,<BR>disrespect; चतुर्दिगीशानवमत्य मानिनी<BR>Ku. 5. 53; Ms. 2. 11, 4. 135, 7. 150;<BR>V. 2. 11.<BR>--2 To undervalue, depreciate,<BR>slight, make light of; तदीशितारं<BR>चेदीनां भवांस्तमवमंस्त मा Śi. 2. 95;<BR>जगन्मंगलमात्मानं कथं त्वमवमन्यसे U. 7. 8;<BR>Bk. 8. 81; 12. 25; 15. 14, 66.<BR>--Caus. To despise &c.; या चैनं<BR>नावमानयेत् Ms. 2. 50, 4. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमत|अवमतं
अवमत p. p. Despised, contemned<BR>&c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकुशः a restive<BR>elephant (that disdains the hook), one<BR>in rut; अन्वेतुकामोऽवमतांकुशग्रहः<BR>Śi. 12. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमतिः|अवमति
अवमतिः A master, an owner.<BR>--तिः<BR>f.<BR>1 Disregard, disrespect.<BR>--2<BR>Aversion, dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमंतव्य|अवमन्तव्य
अवमंतव्य, अवमान्य pot. p.<BR>1 To<BR>be treated with disrespect, or<BR>slighted; बालोऽपि नावमंतव्यो मनुष्य इति<BR>भूमिपः Ms. 7. 8, 9. 82.<BR>--2 Contemptible,<BR>mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमान्य|अवमान्यः
अवमंतव्य, अवमान्य pot. p.<BR>1 To<BR>be treated with disrespect, or<BR>slighted; बालोऽपि नावमंतव्यो मनुष्य इति<BR>भूमिपः Ms. 7. 8, 9. 82.<BR>--2 Contemptible,<BR>mean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमंतृ|अवमन्तृ
अवमंतृ a.<BR>1 Disrespectful,<BR>contemptuous, despising.<BR>--2 Arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानः|अवमान
अवमानः Disrespect, contempt,<BR>disregard; अमृतस्येव चाकांक्षेदवमानस्य<BR>सर्वदा Ms. 2. 162; Bg. 14. 25. ˚ता, --त्वं<BR>dishonourableness, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमाननं|अवमानन
अवमाननं, --ना Despising,<BR>disrespect, contempt; अवमाननार्थमिह किं<BR>निमंत्रितैः Śi. 15. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानना
अवमाननं, --ना Despising,<BR>disrespect, contempt; अवमाननार्थमिह किं<BR>निमंत्रितैः Śi. 15. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमानिन्
अवमानिन् a. Contemning,<BR>despising, slighting, undervaluing; धिङ्<BR>मामुपस्थितश्रेयोवमानिनं Ś. 6; अयि<BR>आत्मगुणावमानिनि Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमंथ|अवमन्थ|अवमन्थः
अवमंथ a. [अवमथ्नाति अव-मंथ्-अच्]<BR>Producing swellings.<BR>--थः A kind<BR>of disease, swellings caused by boils<BR>or contusions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्षः|अवमर्ष
अवमर्षः<BR>1 Consideration,<BR>investigation.<BR>--2 One of the five principal<BR>parts or Saṃdhis of a play; यत्र<BR>मुख्यफलोपाय उद्भिन्नो गर्भतोऽधिकः । शापाद्यैः<BR>सांतरायश्च सोऽवमर्ष इति स्मृतः S. D. 336; also<BR>written विमर्ष.<BR>--3 Attacking;<BR>वीर्यावदानेषु कृतावमर्षः Ki. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्षणं|अवमर्षण
अवमर्षणं<BR>1 Intolerance, impatience.<BR>--2 Effacing, obliterating, banishing<BR>from recollection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमुच्
अवमुच् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To let loose,<BR>loosen (as a horse).<BR>--2 To take off (a<BR>garment &c.); मेखलां, किरीटं, वासांसि,<BR>भूषणानि &c.<BR>--3 To unharness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमोचनं|अवमोचन
अवमोचनं Setting at liberty,<BR>loosening, letting go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमूर्धन्
अवमूर्धन् a. [अवनतो मूर्द्धाऽस्य]<BR>With one's head hanging down.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शय a. [अवमूर्द्धा सन् शेते;<BR>शीअच्] lying with the head<BR>hanging down.<BR>--(यः) one who sleeps<BR>with his head hanging down, such<BR>as man (opp. देव); उत्तानशया देवा<BR>अवमूर्धशया मनुष्याः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमृज्
अवमृज् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To rub off, to<BR>strip off, remove; लेपमवमार्ष्टि.<BR>--2 To<BR>efface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमार्जनं|अवमार्जन
अवमार्जनं Washing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमृद्
अवमृद् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To grind or pound<BR>down, to reduce by friction; crush,<BR>tread down, trample upon; अवमृद्रन्स<BR>राष्ट्राणि पार्थिवानां हयोत्तमः Mb.<BR>--2 To<BR>rub. --Caus. To pound down &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्दः|अवमर्द|अवमर्द्द
अवमर्दः<BR>1 Trampling upon.<BR>--2<BR>Pain, toils; रणावमर्दमासाद्य Rām.<BR>--3<BR>An expedient of a Government,<BR>inflicting punishment on an enemy<BR>by laying his country waste,<BR>devastation, oppression; अवमर्दः<BR>प्रतीघातस्तथा चैव बलीयसां Mb.<BR>--4 Slaying,<BR>killing; U. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्दन
अवमर्दन a. Trampling down,<BR>grinding, crushing; शत्रुबल˚ Rām.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Rubbing, shampooing; हस्तपाद˚<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--2 Oppression, crushing down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमृश्
अवमृश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To touch;<BR>अवमृशंती कलहंसकान् K. 232.<BR>--2 To<BR>consider, ponder, reflect. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>cause to touch.<BR>--2 To destroy;<BR>interrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवमर्शः|अवमर्श
अवमर्शः Touch, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयज्
अवयज् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To expiate (sin),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">Page0185-c+ 56</a>]<BR>drive away, expel, disperse<BR>(enemies &c.) by performing sacrifices.<BR>--2 Not to worship; to abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयजनं|अवयजन
अवयजनं Purification, means of<BR>expiating; देवकृतस्यैनसोऽवयजनमसि<BR>&c. Tāṇḍya Br. (अपगमनसाधनं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयाज्
अवयाज् f. [अव-यज्-ण्वि] A<BR>particular portion of a sacrifice. --m. (-याः,<BR>-याजौ) A kind of priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयवः|अवयव
अवयवः [अवयूयते कार्यद्रव्येण संबध्यते,<BR>अव-यु-कर्मणि-अप्]<BR>1 A limb (of the<BR>body); मुखावयवलूनां तां R. 12. 43,<BR>Amaru. 40, 46; a member (in general);<BR>कस्मिंश्चिदपि जीवति नंदान्वयावयवे<BR>Mu. 1.<BR>--2 A part, portion (as of a whole);<BR>पदे न वर्णा विद्यंते वर्णेष्ववयवा न च<BR>Bhartṛ.; द्रव्याणां केनचिदवयवेन Dk. 61;<BR>क्तेनाहोरात्रावयवाः P. II. 1. 45; I. 1. 46.<BR>--3<BR>A member or a component part of a<BR>logical argument or syllogism.<BR>(These are five: --प्रतिज्ञा, हेतु, उदाहरण,<BR>उपनय and निगमन).<BR>--4 The body.<BR>--5<BR>A component, constituent,<BR>ingredient (in general), as of a<BR>compound &c.<BR>--6 A means (साधन,<BR>उपकरण).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः the meaning<BR>of the component parts of a word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयवशः
अवयवशः ind. Part by part,<BR>severally, piece-meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयविन्
अवयविन् a. [अवयवः कारणत्वेनास्त्यस्य<BR>इनि] Having limbs, having portions<BR>or subdivisions (as a whole);<BR>अवयविना सह पूर्वादयः समस्यंते P. II. 2. 1.<BR>Sk. --m. (वी)<BR>1 A whole, any<BR>substance formed of several<BR>constituents; ननु अवयविनि किं मानं Sid.<BR>Mukt.<BR>--2 A syllogism, or any<BR>logical argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवया
अवया {c2c} U.<BR>1 To go down, to<BR>give way.<BR>--2 To desist from, turn off<BR>or away.<BR>--3 To know, understand;<BR>अथवा न धर्ममसुबोधसमयमवयात बालिशाः<BR>Śi. 15. 19.; न जनोऽयमित्यवयये स तापसैः<BR>Ki. 12. 15.<BR>--4 To avert, prevent,<BR>remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवया
अवया, --यात a. Ved. Giving way,<BR>desisting, ceasing; ˚हेळः Ved. one<BR>whose anger is appeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयात
अवया, --यात a. Ved. Giving way,<BR>desisting, ceasing; ˚हेळः Ved. one<BR>whose anger is appeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयातृ
अवयातृ a.<BR>1 One who separates.<BR>--2 Turning away, averting.<BR>--3<BR>Appeasing, pacifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयानं|अवयान
अवयानं<BR>1 Going away, retreat<BR>(Ved.).<BR>--2 Appeasing, pacification.<BR>--3 Expiation (of sins &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवयुन
अवयुन a. [वयुनं प्रज्ञा निरु˚ न. ब.]<BR>Having no intellect (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0185-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर|अवरं|अवरः
अवर a. [वृ-बा˚. अप् न. त.]<BR>1 (a)<BR>Younger (in years); मासेनावरः =<BR>मासावरः Sk. (b) Later; posterior, hinder<BR>(in time or space); दक्षो विवस्वानवरः<BR>Rām.; पूर्वजे नावरः पुत्रो ज्येष्ठो राज्येऽ<BR>भिषिच्यते Rām.; यदवरं कौशांब्याः,<BR>यदवरमाग्रहायण्याः P. III. 3. 136-7 Sk.;<BR>रामाद्वर्षेणाधोक्षजोऽवरः Bop.<BR>--2<BR>Following, succeeding; जरावराः (शब्दाः)<BR>Ak.; चतुरोऽवरान् Ms. 3. 23.<BR>--3<BR>Below, under, lower, inferior, less;<BR>वर्णावरो भ्राता M. 1.<BR>--4 Mean,<BR>unimportant, worst, lowest (opp. उत्तम);<BR>अव्यंग्यमवरं स्मृतं K. P. 1; दूरेण ह्यवरं<BR>कर्म बुद्धियोगाद्धनंजय Bg. 2. 49;<BR>श्रद्दधानं शुभां विद्यामाददीतावरादपि Ms. 2. 238.<BR>--5 Last (opp. प्रथम); सामान्यमेषां<BR>प्रथमावरत्वं Ku. 7. 44.<BR>--6 Least;<BR>usually as the last member of comp.<BR>with numerals; त्र्यवरैः साक्षिभिर्भाव्यः<BR>Ms. 8. 60, 3. 187; 11. 81, 12. 110;<BR>त्र्यवरा परिषद् ज्ञेया 112; Y. 2. 69.<BR>--7<BR>Western.<BR>--8 Nearer, next.<BR>--9 Most<BR>excellent (अत्यंतश्रेष्ठ).<BR>--रः<BR>1 A<BR>country behind.<BR>--2 Time gone.<BR>--रा<BR>1 A<BR>Direction.<BR>--2 N. of Durgā.<BR>--रं The<BR>hind thigh of an elephant (also ˚रा).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्धः {1} the least part, the<BR>minimum. {2} the last half. {3} the<BR>hinder part of the body.<BR>--(र्धं) ind.<BR>in a certain succession of parts,<BR>successively. ˚तः ind. from below.<BR>--अर्ध्य<BR>a. [अवरार्धे भवः यत्] {1} being on the<BR>lower or near side. {2} belonging to<BR>the last half. {3} beginning from<BR>below. {4} defective (न्यून).<BR>--(र्ध्यं) the<BR>least or smallest part.<BR>--अवर a.<BR>lowest, most inferior of all; न हि<BR>प्रकृष्टान् प्रेष्यांस्तु प्रेषयंत्यवरावरान् Rām.<BR>--उक्त a. named last.<BR>--ज a. {1}<BR>younger, junior, born afterwards;<BR>Śi. 14. 74. {2} of a low birth, inferior.<BR>--(जः)<BR>{1} a younger brother; R. 11. 54;<BR>14. 11, 36. {2} a Śūdra.<BR>--(जा) a<BR>younger sister; विदर्भराजावरजा<BR>R. 6. 58, 84; 12. 32.<BR>--परं ind. one after<BR>another.<BR>--पुरुषाः (pl.) one's<BR>descendants.<BR>--वर्ण a. belonging to a low caste<BR>or tribe.<BR>--(र्णः) {1} a Śūdra, a man<BR>of the fourth tribe. {2} the last or<BR>fourth tribe; Ms. 3. 241, 9. 248.<BR>--वर्णकः, --वर्णजः a Śūdra.<BR>--व्रत a.<BR>having no vow (हीनव्रत or अधमव्रत).<BR>--(तः) [अवरं अत्यंतश्रेष्ठं व्रतमस्य] {1} the<BR>Sun. {2} a kind of tree (arka).<BR>--शैलः [अवरः पश्चाद्वर्ती शैलः] the<BR>western mountain (behind which the<BR>sun is supposed to set).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरतः|अवरत
अवरतः ind. [अवर-तसिल्] Behind,<BR>afterwards, hinder, posterior,<BR>downwards, below, from below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरस्तात्
अवरस्तात् ind. [अवर-प्रथमाद्यर्थे<BR>अस्ताति P. V. 3. 29, 41] Behind, hinder,<BR>posterior, below, downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरीण|अवरीणं
अवरीण a. Degraded, censured,<BR>debased, despised (अधरीण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरेण
अवरेण ind. (With acc.) Below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्यति
अवर्यति Den. P. To become lower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरम्
अवरम् {c1c} A. To leave off, cease<BR>(only in p. p.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरत|अवरतः
अवरत p. p. Stopped, ceased,<BR>resting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरतिः|अवरति
अवरतिः f.<BR>1 Stopping, ceasing,<BR>cessation.<BR>--2 Repose, relaxation,<BR>rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरहस
अवरहस a. [अवततं रहः अच्<BR>P. V. 4. 81] Having no people, desolate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुग्ण
अवरुग्ण a.<BR>1 Broken, torn;<BR>अवरुग्णतुंगसुरदारुतरौ Ki. 6. 5.<BR>--2 Diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुध्
अवरुध् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To obstruct,<BR>hinder, stop, prevent, detain; मा गा<BR>इत्यवरुद्धया Ś. 2. 2.<BR>--2 To shut up, besiege;<BR>अवरोधि गौर्गौपेन; अवारुद्ध गौः; (<BR>स्वयमेव) P. III. 1. 64 Sk.; so पुरमवारुणत्;<BR>to confine, lock up (oft. with two<BR>acc.); शोकं चित्तनवारुधत् Bk. 6. 9;<BR>व्रजमवरुणद्धिगां Sk.; with loc. case also;<BR>आत्मानमात्मन्यवरुध्य Bhāg.<BR>--3 To<BR>furnish, supply, procure, obtain (for<BR>one), get, attain to; कामं, अन्नं.<BR>--4 To<BR>suspend; attach oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुद्ध
अवरुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Obstructed, stopped,<BR>checked, hindered.<BR>--2 Shut up or<BR>in, enclosed.<BR>--3 Incognito,<BR>disguised; अस्ति कश्चिद्राजसूनुरवरुद्धश्चरन्<BR>Dk.; अवरुद्धोऽचरत्पार्थो वर्षाणि त्रिदशानि<BR>च Mb.<BR>--4 Protected, and not seen<BR>by others; Y. 2. 290; Ms. 8. 236.<BR>--5 Imprisoned, secluded as in the<BR>inner apartments.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--देह a.<BR>incarcerated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुद्धिः|अवरुद्धि
अवरुद्धिः f. [रुध्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Obstruction,<BR>restraint; इंद्रियाणां वीर्याणां चावरुद्धौ<BR>Ait. Br.<BR>--2 Besieging.<BR>--3 Gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधः|अवरोध
अवरोधः<BR>1 Hindrance, obstruction;<BR>फेनायमानं स्रोतोऽवरोधः Suśr.<BR>--2<BR>Restraint; अंतःप्राणावरोध Mk. 1. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Inner apartments or women's<BR>apartments, harem, seraglio; निन्ये<BR>विनीतैरवरोधदक्षैः Ku. 7. 73; Śi. 5. 7;<BR>अवरोधजनः K. 57; ˚गृहेषु राज्ञः Ś. 5. 3, 6. 11.<BR>--4 The wives of a king taken<BR>collectively (oft. pl.); अवरोधे महत्यपि<BR>R. 1. 32, 4. 68, 87, 6. 48, 16. 58,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-c" target="_blank">Page0186-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Mv. 6. 20.<BR>--5 An enclosure, confinement.<BR>--6 Siege, investment, blockade;<BR>दुर्गावरोधः H. 3.<BR>--7 A covering, lid.<BR>--8 A<BR>fence, a pen.<BR>--9 A watchman.<BR>--10<BR>Depression, hollow.<BR>--11 Layer (plant);<BR>see under अवरुह्.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अयनं {1}<BR>a seraglio. {2} siege.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधक|अवरोधकः
अवरोधक a.<BR>1 Obstruction,<BR>hindering, impeding.<BR>--2 Besieging; सुधन्वा<BR>वीर्यवान्नाजा मिथिलामवरोधकः Rām.<BR>--कः A guard.<BR>--कं A barrier, fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधनं|अवरोधन
अवरोधनं<BR>1 A siege, blockade.<BR>--2<BR>Hindering, obstructing.<BR>--3 An<BR>obstacle, impediment.<BR>--4 A closed<BR>or private place.<BR>--5 The innermost<BR>part of anything.<BR>--6 The inner or<BR>women's apartments in a royal<BR>palace; राजावरोधनवधूरवतारयंतः<BR>Śi. 5. 18; अवरोधने स्थास्यति Dk. 120.<BR>--7 An inmate of the harem, a<BR>queen, wife; अवरोधनानि सिंधोः<BR>Śi. 8. 8 (समुद्रमहिष्यो नद्यः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिक|अवरोधिकः
अवरोधिक a. Obstructive,<BR>impeding.<BR>--कः [अवरोधे तद्रक्षणादौ नियुक्तः<BR>ठन्] A guard of the queen's<BR>apartments.<BR>--का A female of the inner<BR>apartments; ययुस्तुरंगाधिरुहोऽवरोधिकाः<BR>Śi. 12. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधिन्
अवरोधिन् a.<BR>1 Obstructing,<BR>hindering.<BR>--2 Besieging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरुह्
अवरुह् {c1c} P. To descend, alight,<BR>go down to; कूपं, पंथानं &c.; come<BR>down (in general); to dismount,<BR>get down;<BR>यानासनस्थश्चैवैनमवरुह्याभिवादयेत् Ms. 2. 202; R. 4. 80;<BR>Bk. 8. 104; so प्रासादात्, वृक्षाग्रात्; ऐश्वर्यात्<BR>अवरूढः come down from, bereft of,<BR>prosperity. --Caus. (रोहयति or<BR>रोपयति)<BR>1 To cause to descend or alight;<BR>तामवारोहयत् R. 1. 54; helped her<BR>down; to bring down, or set<BR>down; तां सरस्तीरेऽवरोप्य Dk. 139;<BR>वृक्षाद्धनूंषि, गांडीवं &c.<BR>--2 To lower,<BR>lessen, reduce; Ms. 1. 82.<BR>--3 To<BR>plant (as trees).<BR>--4 To depose,<BR>dethrone, dismiss, remove (as from<BR>a throne &c.); मयाऽधिकाराभ्यामवरोप्य<BR>Mu. 3; चाणक्यं साचिव्यादवरोपयेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरूढ
अवरूढ p. p.<BR>1 Descended.<BR>alighted; dismounted.<BR>--2 Uprooted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधः|अवरोध
अवरोधः<BR>1 Moving down,<BR>descending.<BR>--2 A shoot sent up by the<BR>root of a plant; a slip (for planting);<BR>the pendent shoots of the (Indian)<BR>fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोधनं|अवरोधन
अवरोधनं Ved. Descending motion,<BR>descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0186-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोपणं|अवरोपण
अवरोपणं<BR>1 Uprooting.<BR>--2 Causing<BR>to descend.<BR>--3 Taking away,<BR>depriving, diminishing.<BR>--4 Setting (as<BR>of the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोपित
अवरोपित p. p.<BR>1 Uprooted.<BR>--2<BR>Deprived of, curtailed.<BR>--3<BR>Diminished, lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहः|अवरोह
अवरोहः<BR>1 Descent, going or<BR>coming down.<BR>--2 A creeping plant<BR>winding itself round a tree from the<BR>bottom to the top (such as the गुडूची<BR>creeper).<BR>--3 Heaven (तस्माद्धि<BR>भोगावसाने सर्वेऽवरोहंति).<BR>--4 Mounting,<BR>ascending.<BR>--5 A shoot sent out by a plant,<BR>a pendent branch, one that strikes<BR>fresh roots into the earth, as of the<BR>fig-tree (वट); अवरोहशताकीर्णं<BR>वटमासाद्य तस्थतुः Rām.<BR>--6 The growth of a<BR>plant or vine.<BR>--7 (In music) The<BR>descending scale of notes.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शायिन् the Indian fig-tree; so<BR>--शाखः, --शाखिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहणं|अवरोहण
अवरोहणं<BR>1 Alighting, descending.<BR>--2 Ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहिका
अवरोहिका N. of a plant अश्वगंधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहिन्
अवरोहिन् a. Descending. --m. (ही)<BR>N. of the Indian fig-tree (वट).<BR>--णी<BR>A particular condition (दशा) brought<BR>about by a particular position of<BR>the stars; उच्चांगपंचभस्थस्य दशा<BR>स्यादवरोहिणी ॥ तस्यामल्पमवाप्नोति फलं क्लेशाच्छुभं<BR>नरः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरूप
अवरूप a.<BR>1 Mis-shapen,<BR>deformed.<BR>--2 Degenerated, degraded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोकिन्
अवरोकिन् a. Ved. Shining,<BR>brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोचकः|अवरोचक
अवरोचकः A kind of disease,<BR>loss of appetite; स्नेहगंधिमुखं तत्र<BR>कामश्वासावरोचकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवरोहित
अवरोहित a. Light red-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ग|अवर्गः
अवर्ग a. Having no class.<BR>--र्गः<BR>The vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्चस्
अवर्चस् a. Ved. Without<BR>splendour, mean-looking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्जिवस्
अवर्जिवस् a. Ved. Not<BR>hindering, not being able to prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ण|अवर्णः
अवर्ण a.<BR>1 Colourless, having<BR>no marks.<BR>--2 Bad, low, destitute<BR>of good qualities.<BR>--र्णः<BR>1 Scandal,<BR>ill-repute, stigma, spot; सोढुं न<BR>तत्पूर्वमवर्णमीशे R. 14. 38.<BR>--2 Blame,<BR>censure; न चावदद्भर्तुरवर्णमार्या 57<BR>spoke no ill words.<BR>--3 Epithet of<BR>18 letters according to थस्व, दीर्घ,<BR>प्लुत, उदात्त, अनुदात्त &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वादः<BR>reproach, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्तन|अवर्त्तन
अवर्तन a. Destitute of<BR>livelihood.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Want of livelihood.<BR>--2 Non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्तिः|अवर्ति
अवर्तिः f. Ved. Bad fortune,<BR>poverty, distress, want.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्त्र
अवर्त्र a. Ved. Not turning back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्षः|अवर्ष
अवर्षः, अवर्षणं Want of rain,<BR>drought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्षणं|अवर्षण
अवर्षः, अवर्षणं Want of rain,<BR>drought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्षुक
अवर्षुक a. Ved. Not raining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवर्ष्य
अवर्ष्य a. Being active in<BR>rainless bright weather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलक्ष|अवलक्षः
अवलक्ष a. (also written वलक्ष)<BR>White.<BR>--क्षः [अवलक्ष्यते, अव-लक्ष्-घञ्]<BR>The white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलग्न|अवलग्नः
अवलग्न a.<BR>1 Clinging or<BR>adhering to, touching, in contact with;<BR>विपुलतरनिरंतरावलग्न Śi. 7. 71.<BR>--2<BR>Hanging down.<BR>--3 Placed<BR>contiguously, impressed.<BR>--ग्नः The waist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलंब्|अवलम्ब्
अवलंब् {c1c} A.<BR>1 (a) To hang,<BR>slip or glide down, hang down, be<BR>suspended; कनकशृंखलावलंबिनी Mu. 2<BR>suspended by a golden chain;<BR>स्तनवदवलंबतेः यः कंठेऽजानां मणिः स विज्ञेयः<BR>Bṛ. S. 65. 3; शाखायां मृतकमवलंबितमास्ते<BR>Vet. (b) To rest, recline, sink down,<BR>remain; यस्य वचनात्तत्रावलंबिताः<BR>H. 1.<BR>--2 To catch hold of, hold,<BR>cling to, throw or support oneself<BR>on, lean on, rest on; ययौ<BR>तदीयामवलंब्य चांगुलिं R. 3. 25; उर्वशी<BR>राजानमवलंबते V. 1; दंडकाष्ठमवलब्यं स्थितः Ś. 2;<BR>चित्रलेखाहस्तावलंबिता V. 1 leaning on,<BR>supported by; K. 17, 185.<BR>--3 To<BR>hold up, bear up, support, sustain,<BR>take up; अवलंब्यतां पुत्रः Ś. 7;<BR>हस्तेनावलंब्योर्वशीं V. 3; हृदयमवललंबे<BR>रात्रिसंभोगलक्ष्मीः Ki. 9. 78; अधीकारानवलंब्य<BR>Ku. 2. 18; हृदयं न त्ववलंबितुं क्षमाः<BR>R. 8. 60; नात्मनैवावलंबे Me. 109; हस्तेन<BR>तस्थाववलंब्य वासः R. 7. 9; Ku. 3. 55,<BR>6. 68; 7. 58; तदर्हस्या जीवितमवलंबितुं<BR>Ś. 3; Dk. 162; Ve. 4; M. 3;<BR>V. 2; Mu. 5; K. 163.<BR>--4 To depend on<BR>or upon, hang or hinge on; सर्वोऽयं<BR>जनस्त्वामवलंबते Bk. 18. 41; व्यवहारोयं<BR>चारुदत्तमवलंबते, वसंतसेनामातरमवलंबते<BR>Mk. 9; Bhāṣā P. 167.<BR>--5 To have<BR>recourse to, resort to; नैराश्यमवलंबितं<BR>H. 1; व्यथां Bk. 7. 71; वैक्लव्यं<BR>Māl. 8^1 to give way to despair;<BR>धैर्यमवलंब् to summon or pluck up courage,<BR>not to despair; माध्यस्थ्यमिष्टेऽ<BR>प्यवलंबतेऽर्थे Ku. 1. 52; दाक्षिण्यमवलंब्य M. 2<BR>politely; K. 155; Ki. 2. 15; K. 220;<BR>आशां to cherish hopes; किं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-c" target="_blank">Page0187-c+ 57</a>]<BR>स्वातंत्र्यमवलंबसे Ś. 5 act wantonly, quite<BR>independently; अवलंब्योत्तरां दिशं<BR>Ks. 37. 33 taking the northern<BR>direction.<BR>--6 To be slow or tardy, be late.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to hang down,<BR>suspend; तं कलशं नागदंतेऽवलंब्य Pt. 4.<BR>--2 To make one rest upon or catch<BR>hold of.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by User geymonat on 20161106. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/319. note: abbrev. for mAlatImADava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलंबः|अवलम्ब|अवलम्बः
अवलंबः<BR>1 Hanging down.<BR>--2<BR>Hanging on, dependence on (fig. also);<BR>तंतुजालावलंबाः Me. 70;<BR>कुनृपतिभवनद्वारसेवा˚ Bh. 1. 67.<BR>--3 A prop, stay,<BR>support (lit. and fig.); help,<BR>assistance (fig.); सावलंबगमना R. 19. 50<BR>walking supported by others; नभसि<BR>निरवलंबे Chāt. 1. 8;<BR>संततिविच्छेदनिरवलंबानां Ś. 6; दैवेनेत्थं दत्तहस्तावलंबे<BR>Ratn. 1. 8; चित्रलेखादत्तहस्तावलंबा<BR>V. 1; see हस्तावलंब also.<BR>--4 Hence, a<BR>crutch or stick for support.<BR>--5 A<BR>suspender.<BR>--6 An appendage.<BR>--7<BR>A perpendicular line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलंबकः|अवलम्बक|अवलम्बकः
अवलंबकः N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलंबनं|अवलम्बन|अवलम्बनं
अवलंबनं<BR>1 A prop, support,<BR>stay; अवलंबनाय दिनभर्तुरभून्न<BR>पतिष्यतः करसहस्रमपि Śi. 9. 6;<BR>सहिष्यते तत्प्रथमावलंबनं Ku. 5. 66; कथं<BR>स्यात्पुनरिहावलंबनं भवत्याः H. 3;<BR>प्रस्थानविक्लवगतेरवलंबनार्थं Ś. 5. 3; मम पुच्छे<BR>करावलंबनं कृत्वोत्तिष्ठ H. 1.<BR>--2 Help,<BR>assistance.<BR>--3 Having recourse to,<BR>resorting to; adoption;<BR>इतरपक्षावलंबनद्वारेण K. 160.<BR>--4 Walking-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलंबित|अवलम्बित|अवलम्बितं
अवलंबित p. p.<BR>1 Supported,<BR>protected.<BR>--2 Suspended, hung down;<BR>सौधावलंबितया वरत्रया Pt. 2;<BR>चूतशाखावलंबिते समुद्गके Ś. 4.<BR>--3 Expeditious,<BR>prompt (शीघ्र).<BR>--4 Alighting,<BR>descending (actively used).<BR>--5<BR>Depending upon, trusting to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलंबितव्य|अवलम्बितव्य
अवलंबितव्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be caught<BR>hold of or grasped.<BR>--2 Expeditious,<BR>quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलंबिन्|अवलम्बिन्
अवलंबिन् a. Hanging down,<BR>depending upon, resting or reclining<BR>on, holding, supporting &c.;<BR>अस्ताचलचूडावलंबिनि कुमुदिनीनायके H. 1;<BR>अथ धूमाभिताम्राक्षं वृक्षशाखावलंबिनं<BR>R. 15. 49; गवाक्षविवरावलंबिना 19. 7;<BR>अपरधुर्यपदावलंबी 5. 66, Ku. 7. 37; इयं<BR>हि निद्रा नयनावलंबिनी Mk. 3. 8;<BR>पुष्पभारावलंबिभिः (तरुभिः) Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्
अवलिप् {c6c} P. To smear, anoint,<BR>(generally used in p. p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिप्त|अवलिप्तः
अवलिप्त p. p. [लिप्-क्त]<BR>1 Proud,<BR>arrogant, haughty.<BR>--2 Anointed,<BR>plastered, smeared.<BR>--3 Killed; केना<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">Page0188-a+ 56</a>]<BR>न्येनावलिप्ताः Mu. 3. 27. ˚ता, ˚त्वं<BR>unction; pride, arrogance, vanity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0187-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेपः|अवलेप
अवलेपः<BR>1 Pride, haughtiness;<BR>प्रियसंगमेष्वनवलेपमदः Śi. 9. 51 (where अ˚<BR>also means ointment); व्यक्तमानावलेपाः<BR>Mu. 3. 22; R. 5. 53; हस्त˚ Me. 14.<BR>--2 Violence, attack, assault, insult,<BR>outrage; किं भवतीनामसुरावलेपेनापराद्धं<BR>V. 1; असुर˚ ibid.; ददृशे पवनावलेपजं<BR>सृजती बाष्पमिवांजनाविलं R. 8. 35.<BR>--3<BR>Smearing, anointing.<BR>--4 Ornament<BR>(भूषा).<BR>--5 Union, association (संग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेपनं|अवलेपन
अवलेपनं<BR>1 Anointing.<BR>--2 Oil, any<BR>unctuous substance.<BR>--3 Union,<BR>association.<BR>--4 Pride, arrogance.<BR>--5<BR>The sandal tree (चंदन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलिह्
अवलिह् {c2c} U. To lick, lap; see<BR>अवलीढ below. --freq. (लेलोढि) To<BR>lick again and again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीढ|अवलीढं
अवलीढ p. p.<BR>1 Eaten, chewed;<BR>दर्भैरर्धावलीढैः Ś. 1. 7; Ms. 4. 208.<BR>--2<BR>Licked, lapped; touched (fig. also);<BR>विषज्वालावलीढावयवा Dk. 9;<BR>नवयौवनावलीढावयवा 17, 75 pervaded by youth;<BR>अस्त्रज्वालावलीढप्रतिबलजलधेरंतरौर्वायमाणे Ve. 3. 5 surrounded (on all sides);<BR>Ki. 13. 11; bit; बीजांजलिः पतति<BR>कीटमुखावलीढः Mk. 1. 9.<BR>--3 Devoured,<BR>destroyed.<BR>--ढा Disregard,<BR>contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेहः|अवलेह
अवलेहः<BR>1 Licking, lapping.<BR>--2 An<BR>extract (as of Soma).<BR>--3 An electuary,<BR>confection; दाडिम˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेहनं|अवलेहन
अवलेहनं Licking with the tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेहिका
अवलेहिका = अवलेह (3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवली
अवली {c4c} A. To stick, hang on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीन
अवलीन p. p. Sticking to,<BR>clinging to, resting under;<BR>विहगादिभिरवलीनैः Bṛ. S. 53. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलीला
अवलीला [अवरा-लीला]<BR>1 Sport,<BR>play, mirth.<BR>--2 Disrespect, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुंच्|अवलुञ्च्
अवलुंच् {c1c} P. To pull down or<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुंचनं|अवलुञ्चन|अवलुंचन
अवलुंचनं<BR>1 Cutting off, tearing or<BR>pulling out; केश˚.<BR>--2 Uprooting.<BR>--3 Not tying up, allowing to hang<BR>down.<BR>--4 Taking away, pulling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुंठनं|अवलुण्ठन|अवलुण्ठनं
अवलुंठनं<BR>1 Rolling or<BR>wallowing on the ground.<BR>--2 Robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुप्
अवलुप् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To rush upon<BR>(as a wild beast on its prey), to<BR>burst or break in upon; वृकवच्चावलुंपेत.<BR>--2 To eat, devour, swallow (fig.<BR>also); अन्योन्यस्यावलुंपंति सारमेया<BR>यथामिषं Mb.; सर्वमेवावलुंपति H. 2. 99;<BR>अवलुप्यमान इव वृष्टिपातैः K. 93, 109.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">Page0188-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--3 To suppress, crush, keep down,<BR>stifle; रक्षत्यवलुंपते च यः Bhāg.;<BR>जरावलुप्तमानावमानचिंतः having lost all<BR>sense of &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलुंपनं|अवलुम्पन
अवलुंपनं Leaping on suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोपः|अवलोप
अवलोपः<BR>1 Cutting off or away;<BR>destruction.<BR>--2 Biting, kissing (as<BR>a lip); Śi. 7. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोप्य
अवलोप्य a. That can be broken<BR>in upon or assailed suddenly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेखः|अवलेख
अवलेखः<BR>1 Breaking, scraping or<BR>scratching off.<BR>--2 Anything<BR>scraped off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेखनं|अवलेखन
अवलेखनं Scraping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलेखा
अवलेखा<BR>1 Rubbing.<BR>--2 Adorning<BR>the person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोक्
अवलोक् {c1c} A. or {c10c} P.<BR>1 To see,<BR>behold, view, look at; observe (lit.);<BR>नोलूकोप्यवलोकते यदि दिवा सूर्यस्य किं<BR>दूषणं Bh. 2. 93; परिक्रम्यावलोक्य च<BR>(in dramas); सलिलेष्ववलोकयत<BR>इवात्मानं प्रतिष्ठानस्य V. 2 being reflected<BR>in; मार्गं or वर्त्म अवलोक् to wait for;<BR>प्रयोगं witness a performance;<BR>M. 2; निमित्तानि Bṛ. S. 53. 105; look<BR>out for, seek; consult (as opinions).<BR>--2 To look at or see (in astron.);<BR>exercise influence upon;<BR>सुरपतिगुरुणावलोकिते 5. 62; शुक्रवाचस्पतिभ्यां च तव<BR>भार्यावलोकिता Mārk. P.<BR>--3 To find,;<BR>observe, see; be aware of, meditate<BR>or reflect upon;<BR>आत्मानमात्मन्यवलोकयंतं Ku. 3. 50; R. 8. 74; 11. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकः|अवलोक
अवलोकः<BR>1 Seeing, beholding;<BR>जृंभांगभंगनयनमीलनांगावलोककृत् S. D.;<BR>वनशोभावलोकाय V. 4. 31.<BR>--2 Sight.<BR>--3 Looking down upon with<BR>compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकक
अवलोकक a. Looking at, wishing<BR>to see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकनं|अवलोकन
अवलोकनं<BR>1 Looking at, beholding,<BR>seeing; नो बभूवुरवलोकनक्षमाः<BR>R. 11. 60.<BR>--2 Looking over, commanding a<BR>view of; दीर्घिकावलोकनगवाक्षगता<BR>M. 1.<BR>--3 Sight, eye.<BR>--4 A look, glance;<BR>योगनिद्रांतविशदैः पावनैरवलोकनैः<BR>R. 10. 14.<BR>--5 Looking out for, inquiry,<BR>seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकयितृ
अवलोकयितृ a. Looking upon,<BR>considering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकित|अवलोकितं|अवलोकितः
अवलोकित p. p. Seen &c.<BR>--तः N.<BR>of a Buddha.<BR>--तं A look, glance;<BR>परिवृत्यावलोकितं R. 4. 72.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईश्वरः N. of a Bodhisattva<BR>worshipped by the northern Buddhists<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोकिन्
अवलोकिन् a. Looking at, seeing.<BR>चतुरावलोकिनः (चक्षुषः) Ku. 5. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोभनं|अवलोभन
अवलोभनं Sensual desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवलोम
अवलोम a. [अवनद्धं लोम आनुकूल्यं<BR>P. V. 4. 75] One who is favourable;<BR>suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवल्गुज|अवल्गुजः
अवल्गुज a. Of no good origin or<BR>extraction.<BR>--जः N. of a plant<BR>सोमराजी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवल्गुली
अवल्गुली A poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववदः|अववद
अववदः --वदनं Censure, an evil<BR>report or reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववदनं|अववदन
अववदः --वदनं Censure, an evil<BR>report or reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववदितृ
अववदितृ a.<BR>1 One who speaks<BR>finally or decisively.<BR>--2 An<BR>adjudicator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववादः|अववाद
अववादः<BR>1 Censure, reproach.<BR>--2<BR>Trust, confidence.<BR>--3 Disregard,<BR>disrespect.<BR>--4 Support, dependence on.<BR>--5 Evil report.<BR>--6 A command, an<BR>order.<BR>--7 Information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववरकः|अववरक
अववरकः<BR>1 An aperture.<BR>--2<BR>Window; see अपवरक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अववर्षणं|अववर्षण
अववर्षणं Raining upon<BR>(completely).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवविद्ध
अवविद्ध a. Cast down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवव्रश्च्
अवव्रश्च् {c6c} P. To splinter, to<BR>cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवव्रश्चः|अवव्रश्च
अवव्रश्चः A splinter, chip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश
अवश a. [नास्ति वशं आयत्तत्वं यस्य]<BR>1 Independent, free.<BR>--2 Not<BR>compliant or docile, disobedient,<BR>selfwilled; स्त्री चावशा Pt. 1. 424;<BR>Ms. 5. 33.<BR>--3 Not subjected to or swayed;<BR>अवशो विषयाणां K. 45; uncontrolled,<BR>unrestrained; ˚इंद्रियचित्तानां<BR>H. 1. 18; 2. 182; Dk. 34; मधुरैरवशानि<BR>लंभयन् वशं Ki. 2. 55 wild.<BR>--4 Not<BR>master of oneself, subject to the<BR>senses; कमपरमवशं न विप्रकुर्युः<BR>Ku. 6. 95.<BR>--5 Not having one's own<BR>will, dependent, helpless,<BR>powerless; सकलमवशं सीदति जगत्<BR>H. 2. 77; कार्यते ह्यवशः Bg. 3. 5; K. 174;<BR>Pt. 1. 335; U. 3; कथमवशो<BR>ह्ययशोविषं पिबामि Mk. 10. 13; विमुंचंत्यवशा<BR>देहं कालस्य वशमागताः Rām.;<BR>Mu. 1. 12.<BR>--6 Necessary, certain; किमस्य<BR>भवतो यथा सुहृद एव नाशोऽवशः Mu. 6.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इंद्रियचित्त a. whose<BR>mind and senses are not held in<BR>subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशंगमः|अवशङ्गम
अवशंगमः Not submitting to<BR>another's will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिका
अवशिका = अवश; Mk. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीभूत
अवशीभूत a.<BR>1 Unrestrained,<BR>independent.<BR>--2 Not influenced by<BR>magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0188-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्य|अवश्यं
अवश्य a.<BR>1 Untameable,<BR>ungovernable, unruly.<BR>--2 Inevitable; अथ<BR>मरणमवश्यमेव जंतोः Ve. 3. 4.<BR>--3<BR>Indispensable, necessary.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुत्रः a son whom it is impossible<BR>to govern or teach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यं|अवश्य
अवश्यं ind. [अव-श्यै-डमु Tv.]<BR>1<BR>Necessarily, inevitably; त्वामप्यस्रं<BR>नवजलमयं मोचयिष्यंत्यवश्यं Me. 93.<BR>--2<BR>Certainly, at all events, by all means,<BR>surely, of course; अवश्यं याति<BR>तिर्यक्त्वं जग्ध्वा चैवाहुतं हविः Ms. 12. 68;<BR>अवश्यं यातारश्चिरतरमुषित्वापि विषयाः<BR>Bh. 3. 16; तां चावश्यं<BR>दिवसगणनातत्परामेकपत्नीं (द्रक्ष्यसि) Me. 10, 61.<BR>अवश्यमेव Most surely; if<BR>compounded with pot. pass. the<BR>final nasal is dropped; अवश्यपाच्य<BR>to be necessarily cooked; अवश्यकार्य<BR>to be necessarily done.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यंभाविन्
अवश्यंभाविन् a. Destined to take<BR>place, inevitable; ˚आदेशः M. 5;<BR>अवश्यंभावि लक्षणम् H. 3;<BR>अवश्यंभाविनो भावा भवंति महतामपि H. Pr. 28; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यक
अवश्यक a. Necessary, inevitable,<BR>indispensable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यकता
अवश्यकता, --त्वं Necessity,<BR>obligation, certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यकत्वं
अवश्यकता, --त्वं Necessity,<BR>obligation, certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशक्थिका
अवशक्थिका = अवसक्थिका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशस्
अवशस् f. [अव-शंस्-क्विप्]<BR>1 A<BR>wrong desire.<BR>--2 Censure, abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशा
अवशा Ved. Not a cow, a bad<BR>cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशातनं|अवशातन
अवशातनं<BR>1 Destroying, cutting<BR>or lopping off.<BR>--2 Withering,<BR>drying up.<BR>--3 Emaciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिरस्
अवशिरस् a. Having the head<BR>bent or hung down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्
अवशिष् (Used mostly in pass.)<BR>To be left last or as a remainder,<BR>to remain over or behind; Bg. 7. 2.<BR>--Caus. To leave as a remainder;<BR>देहमात्रावशेषितः Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशिष्ट|अवशिष्टः
अवशिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Left, remaining;<BR>स्तंबेन नीवार इवावशिष्टः R. 5. 15;<BR>किमवशिष्टमह्नः Ratn. 3;<BR>निद्रागमसीम्नः कियदवशिष्टं Mv. 6; कियदवशिष्टं<BR>रजन्याः Ś. 4 how much of the<BR>night yet remains (has yet to run).<BR>--2 Remaining over and above,<BR>surplus.<BR>--ष्टं, --ष्टकं Rest, remainder,<BR>remnant; Y. 2. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेषः|अवशेष
अवशेषः Remnant, rest, leavings,<BR>remainder; रक्षसामवशेषेण, अह्नः,<BR>पुण्यानां Rām.; वृत्तांत˚ M. 5 the rest of<BR>the story; in this sense usually in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">Page0189-b+ 56</a>]<BR>comp.; अर्ध˚ having only one half<BR>left; कथा˚ or नाम˚ one who survives<BR>only in narration or name, having<BR>only the tale or name left behind;<BR>used figuratively for dead; see the<BR>words s. v.; भस्म˚ remaining only<BR>in ashes, reduced to ashes; Ś. 3. 3;<BR>भस्मावशेषं मदनं चकार reduced to ashes<BR>Ku. 3. 72, Śi. 10. 16; सावशेषमिव<BR>भट्टिन्या वचनं M. 4 unfinished; सावशेषो<BR>विषवेगः ibid. still remaining;<BR>शीर्षावशेषीकृतः Bh. 2. 34; Ratn. 2. 2;<BR>R. 2. 69; शृणु मे सावशेषं वचः Ś. 2 hear<BR>me out, let me finish my speech;<BR>अल्पावशेषायुः K. 46 having a short<BR>span of life; see निरवशेष also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशेषित
अवशेषित p. p. Left, remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीनः|अवशीन
अवशीनः A scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीर्ष|अवशीर्षः
अवशीर्ष --र्षक a. [अवनतं शीर्षं यस्यवा<BR>कप्] Having the head bent down.<BR>--र्षः<BR>1 An error made in sleeping<BR>(as regards position).<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>eye-disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवशीर्षक
अवशीर्ष --र्षक a. [अवनतं शीर्षं यस्यवा<BR>कप्] Having the head bent down.<BR>--र्षः<BR>1 An error made in sleeping<BR>(as regards position).<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>eye-disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्या
अवश्या [अव-श्यै क]<BR>1 Hoar-frost, a<BR>fog or mist.<BR>--2 An independent<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्यायः|अवश्याय
अवश्यायः [अव-श्यै-ण<BR>P. III. 1. 141]<BR>1 Frost, dew.<BR>--2<BR>Hoarfrost, white dew अवश्यायावसिक्तस्य<BR>पुंडरीकस्य चारुतां U. 6. 29.<BR>--3 Pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवश्रयणं|अवश्रयण
अवश्रयणं Taking anything from<BR>off the fire (opp. अधिश्रयण);<BR>अधिश्रयणावश्रयणांतादिपूर्वापरीभूतो व्यापारकलापः<BR>पाकादिशब्दवाच्यः S. D. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्कयणी
अवष्कयणी A cow that bears a<BR>calf after a long interval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टंभ्|अवष्टम्भ्
अवष्टंभ् {c5c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To lean or<BR>rest upon; धनुरवष्टभ्य Mv. 5; so दंडं;<BR>प्रकृतिं स्वामवष्टभ्य Bg. 9. 8 by the help<BR>of; वृद्धां भार्यामवष्टभ्य Rām. on account<BR>of.<BR>--2 To block up;<BR>कोसलनृपतेर्द्वारमवष्टभ्य Ratn. 4.<BR>--3 To wrap, envelop,<BR>cover with; K. 116;<BR>तिमिरेणावष्टभ्यमाने जीवलोके 159; occupy; Dk. 159.<BR>--4 To support, prop, hold up; clasp,<BR>embrace; अवष्टभ्यासौ मां Mv. 5. 5;<BR>क्रोडविभागेन मामवष्टभ्य K. 33, 42, 54.<BR>--5<BR>To hinder, stop, arrest, hold or keep<BR>back; अवष्टभ्यमान इव जलधरैः K. 303.<BR>--6 To be near<BR>--7 To be astounded<BR>or bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टब्ध|अवष्टब्धं
अवष्टब्ध p. p. [अवस्तंभ्-क्त, षत्वम्]<BR>1<BR>Supported; rested on, protected;<BR>held, seized.<BR>--2 Hanging from<BR>or upon; अवष्टब्धा यष्टिः Sk.<BR>--3<BR>Near, contiguous; अद्यश्वीनावष्टब्धे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-c" target="_blank">Page0189-c+ 57</a>]<BR>P. V. 2. 13, Bk. 9. 72.<BR>--4<BR>Obstructed, stopped, suspended.<BR>--5<BR>Paralysed.<BR>--6 Bound, tied, attached.<BR>--7<BR>Wrapped up, enfolded.<BR>--8 Opposed.<BR>--9 Surpassed, overcome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टंभः|अवष्टम्भ|अवष्टम्भः
अवष्टंभः [स्तंभ्-घञ्, सस्य षत्वं]<BR>1<BR>Leaning, resting upon.<BR>--2 Support, prop;<BR>पक्षाभ्यामीषत्कृतावष्टंभः K. 34, 44, 186,<BR>231, 248; खडलतावष्टंभनिश्चलः<BR>Māl. 3; (hence) having recourse to,<BR>plucking up or summoning (as courage);<BR>तत्कथमहं धैर्यावष्टंभं करोमि Pt. 1; so<BR>पौरुष˚, धीरत्व˚ Māl. 2; सहजसत्त्व˚<BR>K. 286.<BR>--3 Haughtiness, pride,<BR>dignity, majestic greatness; सावष्टंभाकृतिना<BR>K. 179 dignified, noble, see सावष्टंभ.<BR>--4<BR>A post, pillar.<BR>--5 Gold.<BR>--6<BR>Commencement, beginning.<BR>--7 Stopping,<BR>standing till, staying.<BR>--8 Courage,<BR>steadiness; K. 156, 157; resolute<BR>determination; ईदृशोऽस्यावष्टंभः Ratn. 4;<BR>अविनयकोपितोऽवष्टंभं कृत्वा K. 261 plucking<BR>up courage; पलायनमवष्टंभो वा Pt. 4<BR>holding out (as opposed to पलायनं).<BR>--9 Obstruction, impediment.<BR>--10<BR>Paralysis, stupefaction K. 141.<BR>--11<BR>Excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टंभमय|अवष्टम्भमय
अवष्टंभमय a. (यी f.) Golden,<BR>made of gold, or as large as<BR>a post; रघोरवष्टंभमयेन पत्रिणा<BR>R. 3. 53 (अ˚ is usually rendered in the<BR>above manner, but from the<BR>immediate context, it should more<BR>properly mean ‘full of dignified<BR>boldness’, ‘breathing defiance’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्टंभनं|अवष्टम्भन
अवष्टंभनं<BR>1 Resting upon, having<BR>recourse to.<BR>--2 Supporting.<BR>--3<BR>Paralysing, stupefying.<BR>--4 A post,<BR>pillar.<BR>--5 Stopping, staying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्वन्
अवष्वन् {c1c} P. To smack (one's<BR>lips), make a noise in eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवष्वाणः|अवष्वाण|अवष्वाणं
अवष्वाणः [अव-स्वन्-घञ् षत्वम्]<BR>Noisy eating, smacking (the lips),<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्
अवस् n. [अव्-भावे असिच्] Ved.<BR>1<BR>Protection, assistance.<BR>--2 Fame,<BR>celebrity.<BR>--3 Food, provision.<BR>--4<BR>Wealth; riches.<BR>--5 Going.<BR>--6<BR>Satisfaction, pleasure.<BR>--7 Wish, will, desire,<BR>aspiration. --ind. [अवर-प्रथमायाः<BR>पंचम्या सप्तम्या वाऽर्थे असि, अव् आदेशः<BR>P. V. 3. 39]<BR>1 Below, downwards,<BR>hitherward.<BR>--2 (As a preposition<BR>with instr. or abl.) (a) Below, at<BR>the lowest place. (b) Without, on<BR>the outside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्वत्|अवस्वन्त्
अवस्वत् a. Ved. Striving,<BR>aspiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0189-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसः|अवस|अवसं
अवसः [अव्-असच् Uṇ. 3. 117;<BR>अवतीत्यवसो राजा भानुश्च Ujjval.]<BR>1 A<BR>king.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--3 A kind of tree<BR>(अर्क).<BR>--सं<BR>1 Refreshment, food,<BR>provision (especially for a journey),<BR>viaticum (˚सः also); एतत्ते रुद्रावसं<BR>Yv. 3. 61.<BR>--2 Preserving, protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्थिका
अवसक्थिका [अवबद्धे सक्थिनी<BR>यस्यां कप्]<BR>1 A cloth girt round the<BR>legs and knees (by a person),<BR>when sitting on his hams; also, the<BR>act of girding round this cloth, or<BR>the posture itself; शयानः प्रौढपादश्च<BR>कृत्वा चैवावसक्थिकाम् Ms. 4. 112;<BR>अहिना अवसक्थिकाबंधहेतुभूतेन Malli. on<BR>Ki. 12. 22.<BR>--2 (Hence) A wrapper,<BR>a girth or band in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसंज्|अवसञ्ज्
अवसंज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To suspend,<BR>attach, cling to, throw, place;<BR>अशिथिलमपरावसज्य कंठे Śi. 7. 16; so<BR>स्कंधे पाणिं, शरीरे भूषणानि &c.<BR>--2 To<BR>entrust to, throw on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसक्त
अवसक्त p. p.<BR>1 Suspended from,<BR>placed; कर्णावसक्तामलदंतपत्रं<BR>Ku. 7. 23, K. 206; Ki. 7. 40; Śi. 5. 16,<BR>18, 9. 7, Ch. P. 4.<BR>--2 In contact<BR>with, bound round, touching;<BR>अविज्ञातावसक्तेन दूषिता मम वाससा<BR>Mk. 1. 54.<BR>--3 Engaged in, intent on, eager.<BR>--क्तं Contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसंजनं|अवसञ्जन
अवसंजनं Embracing, clinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसज्जनं|अवसज्जन
अवसज्जनं Embracing, clinging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसंडीनं|अवसण्डीन|अवसंडीन
अवसंडीनं The downward flight<BR>of birds in a body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथः|अवसथ
अवसथः [अव-सो-कथन्]<BR>1 A<BR>dwelling place, habitation.<BR>--2 A village.<BR>--3 A school, college (छात्रालयः, मठः);<BR>see आवसथ.<BR>--थं A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसथ्यः|अवसथ्य
अवसथ्यः [अवसथ-स्वार्थे यत्] A<BR>college, school.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसद्
अवसद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sink down,<BR>faint, fail, give way; करिणी<BR>पंकमिवावसीदति Ki. 2. 6 sinks or fails;<BR>पौरुषं 7; अवसीदंति मे प्राणाः Mb.; न<BR>हींगितज्ञोऽवसरेऽवसीदति Ki. 4. 20 fails<BR>not (does not shut his lips); न<BR>कृच्छ्रेष्ववसीदति Mb.; Ms. 4. 187,<BR>Bk. 6. 24.<BR>--2 To suffer, be neglected or<BR>interfered with; नावसीदति वा गुरु<BR>प्रयोजनं K. 181.<BR>--3 To become<BR>disheartened or exhausted; Dk. 127.<BR>--4 To perish, come to an end, be<BR>ruined; सर्वमस्मत्कुटुंबकमवसीदेत्<BR>Dk. 60; नास्त्युद्यमसमो बंधुः कृत्वा यं<BR>नावसीदति Bh. 2. 86. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause<BR>to sink; to dispirit, render<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">Page0190-b+ 57</a>]<BR>downhearted, to ruin; कुटुंबकं<BR>चावसादितं Dk. 41, ruined; आत्मानमात्मनाऽ<BR>नवसाद्यैवोद्धरंति संतः 54 without<BR>ruining or killing; Bg. 6. 5; राज्यस्य<BR>मूलं हस्त्यश्वमवसादयेत् Mu. 3. ruin.<BR>--2 To allay, remove;<BR>औत्सुक्यमात्रमवसादयति प्रतिष्ठा Ś. 5. 6;<BR>अयमहमवसादयामि वः सपत्नान् Dk. 127 destroy,<BR>kill; अवसादितवाचां Śi. 10. 30<BR>rendered speechless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्न|अवसन्नः
अवसन्न p. p.<BR>1 Sunk down (fig.<BR>also), enervated, sinking, drooping;<BR>अतिप्रबलपिपासावसन्नानि K. 36;<BR>Śi. 15. 85; मदावसन्नहस्त Dk. 62<BR>powerless.<BR>--2 Dispirited, sad, melancholy,<BR>unhappy; दधिकर्णोऽवसन्नो ब्रूते H. 2<BR>lean, weakened.<BR>--3 Ended,<BR>terminated, gone off;<BR>अवसन्नतापमतमिस्रमभात् Śi. 9. 12 devoid of heat;<BR>अवसन्नायां रात्रौ H. 1.<BR>--4 Unable to do<BR>one's duty.<BR>--5 Lost, deprived of;<BR>पित्रोः सकाशमवसन्नदृशोर्निनाय<BR>R. 9. 77 who had lost their sight.<BR>--6<BR>(In law) Non-suited, defeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्नता
अवसन्नता --त्वं<BR>1 Affliction, dejection.<BR>--2 Termination, completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसन्नत्वं
अवसन्नता --त्वं<BR>1 Affliction, dejection.<BR>--2 Termination, completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादः|अवसाद
अवसादः<BR>1 Sinking, fainting,<BR>sitting down; Ki. 18. 47; अनवसादः<BR>safety, protection; failure, as of the<BR>voice.<BR>--2 Ruin, loss, destruction,<BR>decline; पर्यायजयावसादा Ki. 17. 18;<BR>विपदेति तावदवसादकरी Ki. 18. 23,<BR>6. 41, 3. 38; Mv. 2.<BR>--3 End,<BR>termination.<BR>--4 Want of energy,<BR>exhaustion, languor, fatigue;<BR>किमिवावसादकरमात्मवतां Ki. 6. 19.<BR>--5 (In law)<BR>Badness of a cause, defeat, losing (a<BR>cause); अलं स्वपक्षावसादशंकया M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादक
अवसादक a.<BR>1 Causing to sink,<BR>faint, or fail.<BR>--2 Causing dejection or<BR>fatigue; एष शोकः परित्यक्तः<BR>सर्वकार्यावसादकः Rām.<BR>--3 Exhausting,<BR>wearisome, tiresome, fatiguing.<BR>--4<BR>Ending, finishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादनं|अवसादन
अवसादनं<BR>1 Decline, loss,<BR>destruction; असूनामवसादनं Ve. 6.<BR>--2<BR>Inability to do one's duty.<BR>--3<BR>Oppression.<BR>--4 Finishing.<BR>--5 An escharotic.<BR>--6 Removing proud flesh (from<BR>boils) by escharotic application;<BR>उत्सन्नमृदुमांसानां व्रणानामवसादनं Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसादिन्
अवसादिन् a. Sinking, drooping;<BR>Śi. 15. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसभ
अवसभ a. Ved. Excluded from<BR>society.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसृ
अवसृ {c1c} P. To spread, pervade;<BR>गगनांगनावकाशावसरत्कलकलं Māl. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसरः|अवसर
अवसरः<BR>1 Occasion, opportunity,<BR>time; उत्पन्नावसरमर्थित्वं M. 3;<BR>नास्यावसरं दास्यामि Ś. 2; भवद्गिरामवसरप्रदानाय<BR>वचांसि नः Śi. 2. 8; विसर्जन˚ सत्कारः<BR>Ś. 7; ˚प्राप्तं suited to the occasion<BR>M. 1; K. 158; ˚तुलिताभिः Pt. 5. 28<BR>equal to the occasion; वेदस्यावसरोऽत्र<BR>कः Ks. 5. 62 what has the Veda to<BR>do here?<BR>--2 (Hence) A fit or proper<BR>opportunity, proper or opportune time;<BR>शशंस सेवावसरं सुरेभ्यः Ku. 7. 40;<BR>अवसरोयमात्मानं प्रकाशयितुं Ś. 1; see<BR>अनवसर also; अवसरोपसर्पणीया राजानः<BR>Ś. 6.<BR>--3 Space, room, scope; कुमुदेंगना<BR>मनसि चावसरं (अलभत) Śi. 9. 41.<BR>--4<BR>Leisure, advantageous position.<BR>--5<BR>Introduction.<BR>--6 A kind of संगति q. v.<BR>--7 A year.<BR>--8 Raining.<BR>--9 Descent.<BR>--10 A consultation in private.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसरणं
अवसरणं^1 Removing, causing to<BR>move.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: alph. order - cf. AP.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पः|अवसर्प
अवसर्पः A spy, a secret emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पणं|अवसर्पण
अवसर्पणं Stepping or going down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्पिन्
अवसर्पिन् a. Stepping down.<BR>--णी<BR>A long period of time (with the<BR>Jainas); according to Hemacandra<BR>it is equal to 2000,000,000,000,000<BR>Sāgaras of years.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसव्य|अवसव्यं
अवसव्य a. Not left(= अपसव्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसामं|अवसाम
अवसामं [अवरं साम अच्समा˚<BR>P. V. 4. 75] A bad song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसिच्
अवसिच् {c6c} P. To sprinkle,<BR>bedew, bespatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसिक्त
अवसिक्त p. p. Sprinkled; ˚अंग<BR>having the limbs sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेकः|अवसेक
अवसेकः<BR>1 Sprinkling, bedewing;<BR>देशः को नुजलावसेकाशिथिलः Mk. 3. 12.<BR>--2 A disease of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेकिमः|अवसेकिम
अवसेकिमः [अवसेकेन निर्वृत्तः<BR>अवसेकइमन्] A kind of cake, pulse ground<BR>with oil and butter (वटकभेदः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेचनं|अवसेचन
अवसेचनं<BR>1 Sprinkling.<BR>--2 Water<BR>used for sprinkling; पाद˚<BR>Ms. 4. 151.<BR>--3 Bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसुप्त
अवसुप्त a. Asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसृज्
अवसृज् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To throw or cast<BR>down, pour out, let fall, drop;<BR>U. 3. 23; Ms. 1. 8; so सायकान्, बीजं,<BR>वृष्टिं &c.<BR>--2 To let loose, liberate,<BR>dismiss &c.<BR>--3 To remit.<BR>--4 To form;<BR>create.<BR>--5 To place on, throw or cast<BR>at.<BR>--6 To leave, give up, abandon;<BR>as क्रोधं, वैरं &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्गः|अवसर्ग
अवसर्गः<BR>1 Letting off, relaxation.<BR>--2 Non-prevention, allowing one<BR>to follow one's inclinations.<BR>--3<BR>Independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0190-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसर्जनं|अवसर्जन
अवसर्जनं Liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसृष्ट
अवसृष्ट p. p. Given away, left,<BR>abandoned, dismissed, let go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसो
अवसो {c4c} P.<BR>1 To finish,<BR>accomplish.<BR>--2 To destroy.<BR>--3 To<BR>determine, understand; किमप्यनवसीयमानं<BR>K. 278; अवासासीच्च वैयासिकीं (वाणीं)<BR>Malli.<BR>--4 (Intrans.) To fail; be at an<BR>end; शक्तिर्ममावस्यति हीनयुद्धे<BR>Ki. 16. 17.<BR>--5 To put up (as at an inn).<BR>--6 To let loose, liberate.<BR>--7 To draw<BR>near, approach.<BR>--8 To dwell, stay.<BR>--9 To settle, fix.<BR>--10 To stand<BR>firm, to persist in.<BR>--11 To know;<BR>Bk. 19. 28.<BR>--12 To get, attain to, reach.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to be completed,<BR>finish, complete; अथ विधिमवसाय्य<BR>शास्त्रदृष्टं R. 5. 76.<BR>--2 To<BR>understand, comprehend; अवसाययितुं क्षमाः<BR>सुखं Ki. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसा
अवसा Ved. Liberation, release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसातृ
अवसातृ m. Ved. A deliverer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसानं|अवसान
अवसानं [अव-सो-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Stopping.<BR>--2 Conclusion, termination,<BR>cessation, end; दोहावसाने पुनरेव दोग्ध्रीं<BR>R. 2. 23, 45; तच्छिष्याध्ययननिवोदितावसानां<BR>1. 95; इत्येतदवसानं कथायाः M. 5<BR>thus ends the story; ˚विरसे K. 180;<BR>आत्मनः सुखावसानेन V. 3 at the<BR>sacrifice of; (at the end of comp.)<BR>ending with, terminating at; स<BR>चायमंगुलीयकदर्शनावसानः Ś. 7; यत्खलु<BR>दुःखावसानमेव दुःखं K. 328.<BR>--3 Death,<BR>decease; अवसानेंऽगराजस्य योद्धव्यं<BR>भवता किल Ve. 5. 38; मूलपुरुषावसाने<BR>संपदः परमुपतिष्ठंति Ś. 6.<BR>--4 Boundary,<BR>limit; विलोकिता दर्शनीयानामवसानभूमिः<BR>K. 124 furthest or highest limit.<BR>--5 (In gram.) The last part of a<BR>word or period (opp. आदि);<BR>आदिमध्यावसानेषु यरता यांति लाघवं;<BR>अनीकपदावसानं देवादि नाम R. 18. 10 (i. e.<BR>देवानीक); वर्णानामभावोऽवसानसंज्ञः स्यात्<BR>P. I. 4. 110; VIII. 3. 15.<BR>--6 A<BR>pause.<BR>--7 The end of a verse, or the<BR>verse itself;<BR>एकावसाना-द्व्यवसाना-ऋक्.<BR>--8 A place of dismounting<BR>from a horse.<BR>--9 A place (स्थान);<BR>resting place, residence; ˚दर्श a.<BR>looking at one's place of destination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसानक
अवसानक a. Coming to an end,<BR>dying, perishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसान्य
अवसान्य a. Ved. Belonging to<BR>the end of a verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसायः|अवसाय
अवसायः [अव-सो-घञ्<BR>P. III. 1. 141]<BR>1 Conclusion, end,<BR>termination; destruction;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-b" target="_blank">Page0191-b+ 57</a>]<BR>शरवर्षैरवसायमाश्रयाशः Śi. 20. 72.<BR>--2 Remainder.<BR>--3<BR>Completion.<BR>--4 Determination,<BR>resolution, decision, certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसायिन्
अवसायिन् a. Residing, dwelling<BR>in; cf. अंत्यावसायिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसित|अवसितं
अवसित p. p. [सो-क्त]<BR>1 Finished,<BR>ended, completed; अवसितो दर्शनार्थः<BR>M. 2; यूपवत्यवसिते क्रियाविधौ<BR>R. 11. 37; अवसितश्च पशुरसौ Dk. 91 it is all<BR>over with the brute; ˚मंडनासि Ś. 4;<BR>वचस्यवसिते तस्मिन्ससर्ज गिरमात्मभूः<BR>Ku. 2. 53; अनवसितवचन एव मयि Dk. 103;<BR>Bk. 10. 6.<BR>--2 Known, understood.<BR>--3<BR>Well cooked; matured.<BR>--4 Resolved,<BR>determined, ascertained.<BR>--5<BR>Standing in a pause<BR>--6 Stored, gathered<BR>(as grain).<BR>--7 Tied, fastened, bound.<BR>--8 Gone.<BR>--9 Remaining, dwelling<BR>(Ved.).<BR>--तं<BR>1 A dwelling place;<BR>नवावसिते वैनमाहरेयुः Śat. Br.<BR>--2 Corn<BR>ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवसेय
अवसेय pot. p.<BR>1 To be<BR>determined, finished.<BR>--2 Perishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कंद्|अवस्कन्द्
अवस्कंद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To attack, storm,<BR>assault; overpower, overwhelm;<BR>छायामप्यवस्कंदितुं Mv. 3; प्रभुरिव<BR>मामवस्कंदयितुं ibid. to attack or insult;<BR>पुरीमवरकंद लुनीहि नंदनं Śi. 1. 51;<BR>स्नेहावस्कन्नहृदया Rām. affected.<BR>--2 To<BR>spring or leap down.<BR>--3 To pour out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कंदः|अवस्कन्द|अवस्कन्दः
अवस्कंदः, --दनं<BR>1 Attacking; attack,<BR>assault; ˚प्रदानं Pt. 3. 39 leading an<BR>assault.<BR>--2 Descending; स<BR>नद्यवस्कंदमुपास्पृशच्च Bk. 2. 11.<BR>--3 A camp (<BR>जिगीषूणां निवेशस्थानं Halāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवस्कंदनं|अवस्कन्दन|अवस्कन्दनं
