अवहननं|अवहनन
अवहननं<BR>1 Threshing, beating off<BR>rice; अवहननायोलूखलं Mbh.<BR>--2 The<BR>lungs; वपा वसावहननं Y. 3. 94 (<BR>अवहननं = फुप्फुसः Mit.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघातः|अवघात
अवघातः [अव हन्-घञ्]<BR>1 Striking.<BR>--2 Hurting, killing.<BR>--3 A violent or<BR>sharp blow, stroke or blow in general;<BR>कर्णावघातनिपुणेन च ताड्यमाना<BR>दूरीकृताः करिवरेण (भृंगाः) Nītipr. 2; अधरे<BR>दत्तदंतावघाते S. D.<BR>--4 Threshing corn<BR>by bruising it with a wooden pestle<BR>in a mortar.<BR>--5 Unnatural or<BR>accidental death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवघातिन्
अवघातिन् a. Striking, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहस्
अवहस् {c1c} P. To deride, mock,<BR>laugh or scoff at, ridicule; Bk. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहासः|अवहास
अवहासः<BR>1 Smiling, a smile.<BR>--2<BR>A jest, joke, ridicule,<BR>यच्चावहासार्थमसत्कृतोसि Bg. 11. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहास्य
अवहास्य pot. p. To be derided or<BR>ridiculed, ridiculous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहस्तः|अवहस्त
अवहस्तः [अवरं हस्तस्य एक˚ त˚]<BR>The back of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहा
अवहा To leave, abandon (used<BR>only in derivatives).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहानिः
अवहानिः f. Loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहीन
अवहीन p. p. Abandoned, left;<BR>अवहीनाः कथाः Dk. 129 over, at an<BR>end; अस्मास्ववहीनेषु Ś. 2 we being left<BR>behind, having fallen in the rear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहालिका
अवहालिका A wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित्था
अव(ब)हित्था --त्थं<BR>1<BR>Dissimulation in general.<BR>--2 Dissimulation<BR>or concealment of an internal feeling,<BR>regarded as one of the 33 subordinate<BR>feelings (व्यभिचारिभाव);<BR>भयगौरवलज्जादेर्हर्षाद्याकारगुप्तिरवहित्था S. D.; or according<BR>to R. G. व्रीडादिना निमित्तेन हर्षाद्यनुभावानां<BR>गोपनाय जनितो भावविशेषोऽवहित्थं; for ex.<BR>see Ku. 6. 84, or Bv. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबहित्था
अव(ब)हित्था --त्थं<BR>1<BR>Dissimulation in general.<BR>--2 Dissimulation<BR>or concealment of an internal feeling,<BR>regarded as one of the 33 subordinate<BR>feelings (व्यभिचारिभाव);<BR>भयगौरवलज्जादेर्हर्षाद्याकारगुप्तिरवहित्था S. D.; or according<BR>to R. G. व्रीडादिना निमित्तेन हर्षाद्यनुभावानां<BR>गोपनाय जनितो भावविशेषोऽवहित्थं; for ex.<BR>see Ku. 6. 84, or Bv. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहित्थं|अवहित्थ
अव(ब)हित्था --त्थं<BR>1<BR>Dissimulation in general.<BR>--2 Dissimulation<BR>or concealment of an internal feeling,<BR>regarded as one of the 33 subordinate<BR>feelings (व्यभिचारिभाव);<BR>भयगौरवलज्जादेर्हर्षाद्याकारगुप्तिरवहित्था S. D.; or according<BR>to R. G. व्रीडादिना निमित्तेन हर्षाद्यनुभावानां<BR>गोपनाय जनितो भावविशेषोऽवहित्थं; for ex.<BR>see Ku. 6. 84, or Bv. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबहित्थं
अव(ब)हित्था --त्थं<BR>1<BR>Dissimulation in general.<BR>--2 Dissimulation<BR>or concealment of an internal feeling,<BR>regarded as one of the 33 subordinate<BR>feelings (व्यभिचारिभाव);<BR>भयगौरवलज्जादेर्हर्षाद्याकारगुप्तिरवहित्था S. D.; or according<BR>to R. G. व्रीडादिना निमित्तेन हर्षाद्यनुभावानां<BR>गोपनाय जनितो भावविशेषोऽवहित्थं; for ex.<BR>see Ku. 6. 84, or Bv. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहृ
अवहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To take away, put<BR>or lay aside; place down; अर्भकं<BR>कस्मादवहृतं भवति Nir.<BR>--2 To hold, contain;<BR>कुडवमवहरति Sk.<BR>--3 To throw or<BR>knock down (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहरणं|अवहरण
अवहरणं<BR>1 Taking away, removing.<BR>--2 Throwing away.<BR>--3 Stealing,<BR>plundering.<BR>--4 Removing from the<BR>battle-field to the camp.<BR>--5<BR>Re-delivery.<BR>--6 Temporary suspension<BR>of hostilities, truce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहारः|अवहार
अवहारः [अवहृ-कर्तरि ण P. III. 1. 141]<BR>1 A thief.<BR>--2 A shark, a<BR>waterelephant.<BR>--3 Taking away the wealth<BR>of invited Brāhmaṇas.<BR>--4<BR>Temporary cessation of hostilities,<BR>suspension of arms, truce.<BR>--5 Removing<BR>to the camp; ततोऽवहारं सैन्यानां तव<BR>तेषां च भारत Mb.<BR>--6 Cessation, stop<BR>(in general).<BR>--7 Summoning,<BR>inviting.<BR>--8 Any object fit to be brought<BR>near (उपनेतव्यं).<BR>--9 Apostacy,<BR>abandoning a sect or caste.<BR>--10<BR>Re-delivery, redeeming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहारक|अवहारकः
अवहारक a.<BR>1 One taking away<BR>from one place to another.<BR>--2 One<BR>who desists from fighting.<BR>--3<BR>Preventing, stopping.<BR>--कः A shark,<BR>a marine monster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहार्य|अवहार्य्य|अवहार्य्यः
अवहार्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be taken away<BR>or removed.<BR>--2 Finable, punishable;<BR>Ms. 8. 198.<BR>--3 What one is forced<BR>to restore or redeem;<BR>आधिश्चोपनिधिश्चोभौ न कालात्ययमर्हतः । अवहार्यौ<BR>भवेतां तौ दीर्घकालमवस्थितौ ॥ Ms. 8. 145.<BR>--4 To be completed,<BR>--5 Recoverable,<BR>redeemable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0192-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहृत
अवहृत p. p.<BR>1 Taken off, back or<BR>away.<BR>--2 Seized, stolen.<BR>--3 Fined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलः|अवहेल|अवहेलं
अवहेलः --ला Disrespect, disdain,<BR>contempt, disregard; सावहेलं K. 244;<BR>अवहेलां कुटज मधुकरे मा गाः Bv. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेला
अवहेलः --ला Disrespect, disdain,<BR>contempt, disregard; सावहेलं K. 244;<BR>अवहेलां कुटज मधुकरे मा गाः Bv. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलनं|अवहेलन
अवहेलनं --ना Disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलना
अवहेलनं --ना Disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवहेलित|अवहेलितं
अवहेलित a. Disregarded, slighted,<BR>contemned; किमिति बकैरवहेलितानभिज्ञैः<BR>Bv. 1. 8.<BR>--तं Disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवह्वर|अवह्वरः
अवह्वर a. [अव-व्हृ-अच्] Crooked.<BR>--रः A crooked way; (fig.) deceit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकिन्
अवाकिन् Ved. Not speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्क
अवाक्क Ved. Speechless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकॄ
अवाकॄ {c6c} P. To strew, pour upon;<BR>sprinkle with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाकरः|अवाकर
अवाकरः A mint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्ष|अवाक्षः
अवाक्ष a. [अवनतान्यक्षाणि इंद्रियाणि<BR>यस्य] A guardian, keeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाग्र|अवाग्रं
अवाग्र a. [अवनतमग्रमस्य] Having<BR>the head bent down, stooping, bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्
अवाच् a. [न. ब.] Speechless<BR>dumb. --n. Brahma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मनसगोचर a. beyond the power of thought<BR>and words, indescribable and<BR>inconceivable.<BR>--श्रुति a. deaf and dumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्य|अवाच्यं|अवाच्यः
अवाच्य a.<BR>1 Not proper to be<BR>addressed; अवाच्यो दीक्षितो नाम्ना<BR>यवीयानपि यो भवेत् Ms. 2. 128.<BR>--2<BR>Improper to be uttered; vile, bad; अवाच्यं<BR>वदतो जिह्वा कथं न पतिता तव Rām.;<BR>˚वादांश्च बहून् वदिष्यंति तवाहिताः<BR>Bg. 2. 36.<BR>--3 Not distinctly expressed, not<BR>expressible in words; ˚ता, ˚त्वं<BR>impropriety; reproach, calumny.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--देशः ‘the unspeakable place,’ the<BR>vulva (योनि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवांच्|अवाञ्च्
अवांच् a. [अवांचति अव-अच्-क्विप्]<BR>1 Turned downwards, bent down,<BR>stooping; कुर्वंतमित्यतिभरेण नगानवाचः<BR>Śi. 6. 79; वनाल्यवांचीव चकार संहतिः<BR>Ki. 14. 34.<BR>--2 Being or situated<BR>below, lower than (with abl.)<BR>यदवाक् पृथिव्याः Śat. Br.<BR>--3 Headlong,<BR>looking downwards.<BR>--4 South. --m.,<BR>n. Brahma.<BR>--ची<BR>1 The south.<BR>--2 The<BR>lower region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाक्
अवाक् ind.<BR>1 Downwards.<BR>--2<BR>Southern, southward.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञानं<BR>disrespect.<BR>--पुष्पी [अवाक् अधोमुखं<BR>पुष्पमस्याः] N. of a plant Anethum<BR>Sowa Roxb (अधःपुष्पी).<BR>--भागः the<BR>part below.<BR>--भव a. southern.<BR>--मुख<BR>a. (खी f.) {1} looking downwards,<BR>with the face hung downwards;<BR>अवाङ्मुखस्योपरि पुष्पवृष्टिः R. 2. 60;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">Page0193-b+ 55</a>]<BR>तस्थुस्तेऽवाङ्मुखाः सर्वे 15. 78. {2}<BR>headlong.<BR>--(खः) N. of a weapon.<BR>--शाखः [अवाच्यः शाखा अस्य] ‘having<BR>the branches turned downwards’,<BR>epithet of the sacred fig-tree (अश्वत्थ).<BR>--शिरस् a. having the head hung<BR>downwards; स मूढो नरकं याति<BR>कालसूत्रमवाक्शिराः Ms. 3. 249, 8. 94, 11. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाचीन|अवाचीनं
अवाचीन a. [अवाच्-ख P. V. 4. 8]<BR>1 Downward, headlong.<BR>--2 Southern.<BR>--3 Descended, gone down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवांचित
अवांचित a. Bent, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाच्य|अवाच्यं|अवाच्यः
अवाच्य a. Southern, southerly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाजिन्
अवाजिन् m. A bad horse (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवात
अवात a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Windless,<BR>not shaken by wind.<BR>--2 Not<BR>breathing the air.<BR>--3 Not exposed to, or<BR>not dried up by, wind.<BR>--4<BR>Unattacked, unconquered (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवादिन्
अवादिन् a.<BR>1 One who is no<BR>speaker or disputer.<BR>--2 One who<BR>does not prosecute or bring any<BR>action, peace-loving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान्
अवान् {c2c} P. [अव-अन्] To breath<BR>or inhale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवानः|अवान|अवानं
अवानः Breathing, inhaling; see<BR>अनवान also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवान|अवानं|अवानः
अवान a. [अव-अन्-अच्] Dried, dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवांतर|अवान्तर|अवान्तरं
अवांतर a. [अवगतमंतरं मध्यं प्रा. स.]<BR>1 Situated or standing between; see<BR>compounds.<BR>--2 Included, involved.<BR>--3 Subordinate, secondary.<BR>--4 Not<BR>closely connected, extraneous, extra.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दिश्, --दिशा an<BR>intermediate quarter (such as the आग्नेयी,<BR>ऐशानी, नैरृती and वायवी).<BR>--देशः a place<BR>situated between (two others), an<BR>intermediate region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवांतराम्|अवान्तराम्
अवांतराम् ind. [अवांतर बा˚ आसु]<BR>Between (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्
अवाप् {c5c} U.<BR>1 To get, obtain,<BR>secure, gain; तमवाप्य सत्पतिं R. 3. 33;<BR>दीर्घमायुः Ms. 4. 76; कीर्ति, फलं, कामं<BR>&c.; पुत्रं सम्राजमवाप्नुहि Ś. 4. 6.<BR>--2<BR>To reach, go to, enter.<BR>--3 To suffer,<BR>incur, receive, meet with;<BR>निंदामवाप्नोति Ms. 5. 161; so दोषं &c.;<BR>मृत्युमवाप्नोति meets with death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्त
अवाप्त p. p. Got, obtained,<BR>received; अनवाप्तचक्षुः फलोऽसि Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्तव्य
अवाप्तव्य pot. p. Attainable;<BR>Bg. 3. 22, R. 10. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्तिः|अवाप्ति
अवाप्तिः f. Obtaining, getting; तपः<BR>किलेदं तदवाप्तिसाधनं Ku. 5. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्य
अवाप्य pot. p. Attainable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाप्य
अवाप्य a. [न. त.] Uncut, not<BR>to be cut (as hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवापित
अवापित a.<BR>1 Not sown(as grain)<BR>but planted.<BR>--2 Not cut (as hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाम
अवाम a.<BR>1 Not left, right.<BR>--2<BR>Favourable, not adverse.<BR>--3<BR>Inauspicious, inelegant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवायः|अवाय
अवायः [अव-इ-घञ्]<BR>1 A limb.<BR>--2<BR>Giving way, conceding, complying<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारः|अवार|अवारं
अवारः, --रं [न वार्यते जलेन वृ-कर्मणि<BR>घञ्]<BR>1 The near bank of a river.<BR>--2<BR>This side; यो वै संवत्सरस्यावारं पारं च वेद<BR>Ait. Br. ˚तस् ind. to this side.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पारः The ocean (P. IV. 2. 93,<BR>V. 2. 11.).<BR>--पारीण a. [अवारपारे<BR>गच्छति, ख P. IV. 2. 93] {1} belonging to<BR>the ocean. {2} crossing a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारं|अवार|अवारः
अवारः, --रं [न वार्यते जलेन वृ-कर्मणि<BR>घञ्]<BR>1 The near bank of a river.<BR>--2<BR>This side; यो वै संवत्सरस्यावारं पारं च वेद<BR>Ait. Br. ˚तस् ind. to this side.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पारः The ocean (P. IV. 2. 93,<BR>V. 2. 11.).<BR>--पारीण a. [अवारपारे<BR>गच्छति, ख P. IV. 2. 93] {1} belonging to<BR>the ocean. {2} crossing a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारीण|अवारीणः
अवारीण a. [अवारं गच्छति, ख<BR>P. IV. 2. 93] Crossing a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार्य|अवार्य्य|अवार्य्यं
अवार्य a. Being on the near side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारण
अवारण a. Insufferable, not to<BR>be remedied, irremediable.<BR>--णं<BR>Not warding off or preventing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारणीय
अवारणीय a.<BR>1 Unable to be<BR>warded off (as enemies).<BR>--2 Treating of<BR>incurable diseases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवार्य|अवार्य्य|अवार्य्यं
अवार्य, अवारयितव्य a. Not to be<BR>warded or kept off, irremediable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारयितव्य
अवार्य, अवारयितव्य a. Not to be<BR>warded or kept off, irremediable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवारिका
अवारिका [नास्ति वारि यत्र] N. of<BR>a plant (धन्याक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवावटः|अवावट
अवावटः The son of a woman by<BR>any man (of the same caste) other<BR>than her first husband; द्वितीयेन तु यः<BR>पित्रा सवर्णायां प्रजायते । अवावट इति ख्यातः<BR>शूद्रधर्मा स जातितः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवावन्
अवावन् m. [Said to be fr. ओण्<BR>P. VI. 4. 41] A thief, stealing away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवासस्
अवासस् a. Unclothed, naked.<BR>--m. N. of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवास्तव|अवास्तवं
अवास्तव a. (वी f.)<BR>1 Unreal,<BR>unsubstantial.<BR>--2 Unfounded, irrational<BR>(as an argument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवास्तु
अवास्तु a. Ved. Having no<BR>abode, homeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवाहन
अवाहन a. Having no carriage,<BR>not driving in a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवि|अविः
अवि a. Ved. [अव्-इन्]<BR>Favourable, kindly or favourably<BR>disposed.<BR>--विः<BR>1 A sheep; (f. also in<BR>this sense); जीनकार्मुकवस्तावीन्<BR>Ms. 11. 139, 3. 6, 12. 55.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--3 N. of a tree (अर्क).<BR>--4 A goat.<BR>--5 A mountain.<BR>--6 Air, wind.<BR>--7 A woollen blanket (of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">Page0194-a+ 55</a>]<BR>skin of mice).<BR>--8 A blanket, shawl<BR>in general.<BR>--9 A woollen strainer (for<BR>Soma juice).<BR>--10 A master.<BR>--11 A<BR>wall, enclosure.<BR>--12 A rat.<BR>--विः f.<BR>1 An ewe.<BR>--2 Shame.<BR>--3 A woman<BR>in her courses. [cf. L. ovis; Gr. ois].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कटः [अवि संघाते कटच्<BR>P. V. 2. 29 Vārt.] a flock of sheep.<BR>--कटोरणः [अविकटे मेघसंघाते देयः<BR>उरणः भेषः P. VI. 3. 10] a kind of<BR>tribute (consisting of sheep).<BR>--गंधा,<BR>--गंधिका N. of a plant (= अजगंधा).<BR>--दुग्धं, --दूसं, --मरीसं, --सोढं the milk of<BR>an ewe.<BR>--पटः sheep's skin, a woollen<BR>cloth.<BR>--पालः [अवीन् पालयति उप. स.]<BR>a shepherd.<BR>--प्रियः a kind of grass<BR>liked by sheep.<BR>--(या) N. of a plant.<BR>--स्थलं sheep-place; N. of a town;<BR>अविस्थलं वृकस्थलं माकंदी वारणावतं Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0193-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकः|अविक|अविकं
अविकः [अविरेव अविकः, अवि-क<BR>P. V. 4. 28] A sheep.<BR>--का An ewe.<BR>--कं<BR>A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविता
अविता An ewe, a sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकत्थ
अविकत्थ a. Not boasting, not<BR>bragging or vaunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकत्थन
अविकत्थन a. One who does<BR>not boast, not vaunting;<BR>सत्यप्रतिज्ञेप्यविकत्थनेपि R. 14. 73;<BR>विद्वांसोऽबिकत्थना भवंति Mu. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल
अविकल a.<BR>1 Unimpaired, not<BR>defective, entire, perfect, whole, all;<BR>तानींद्रियाण्यविकलानि Bh. 2. 40;<BR>Pt. 5. 26; ˚लं फलं Me. 24, 34; ˚शरच्चंद्रमधुरः<BR>Māl. 2. 11 full, full-orbed; ˚इंद्रियः<BR>K. 35, 71; Mv. 2. 17, 4. 29;<BR>˚लमरक्षत् 5. 5 entirely, completely;<BR>यल्लोकेष्वविकलमाप्तमाधिपत्यं Ki. 18. 36<BR>entire, supreme.<BR>--2 Regular,<BR>orderly; consistent, not discordant;<BR>कलमविकलतालं गायकैर्बोधहेतोः Śi. 11. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकल्प|अविकल्पः
अविकल्प a. Unchangeable<BR>--ल्पः<BR>1 Absence of doubt.<BR>--2 Absence<BR>of option or alternative.<BR>--3<BR>Positive act or precept.<BR>--ल्पं ind.<BR>Without doubt, unhesitatingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकार|अविकारः
अविकार a. Immutable,<BR>unchangeable.<BR>--रः Immutability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकृत
अविकृत a. Unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविकृतिः|अविकृति
अविकृतिः f.<BR>1 Absence of change.<BR>--2 (In Sān. phil.) The inanimate<BR>principle called प्रकृति,<BR>regarded as the material cause of the<BR>universe; मूलप्रकृतिरविकृतिः Sāṅ. K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रिय
अविक्रिय a. Unchangeable,<BR>immutable.<BR>--यं Brahma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रम|अविक्रमः
अविक्रम a. Powerless, feeble.<BR>--मः Cowardice, timidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्रांत|अविक्रान्त
अविक्रांत a.<BR>1 Unsurpassed.<BR>--2<BR>Feeble, powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्लमः|अविक्लम
अविक्लमः Absence of fatigue,<BR>vigour, freshness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षत
अविक्षत a. Unimpaired,<BR>uninjured; unhurt, whole, entire; विक्रेतुः<BR>प्रतिदेयं तत्तस्मिन्नेवाह्न्यविक्षतम् Smṛti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षित
अविक्षित a. Unimpaired, unhurt;<BR>undiminished (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षिप
अविक्षिप a. [P. VI. 2. 157-8]<BR>Unable to distribute or dispense<BR>(आक्रोशार्थे), (विक्षेप्तुं न शक्तः or यो न<BR>विक्षिपति); not distributing or badly<BR>distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविक्षिप्त
अविक्षिप्त a.<BR>1 Not thrown away.<BR>--2 Attentive, composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगत
अविगत a. Not gone off,<BR>retained, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविगम|अविगमः
अविगम a. Unseparated,<BR>unremoved.<BR>--मः Non-separation, association,<BR>inherence, presence, existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविग्नः|अविग्न
अविग्नः N. of a fruit-tree(<BR>करमर्दक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविग्रह|अविग्रहः
अविग्रह a. [नास्ति विग्रहो यस्य]<BR>1<BR>Bodiless, incorporeal; epithet of the<BR>Supreme Being (who has no body).<BR>--2 Not known.<BR>--हः (In gram.) A<BR>compound the sense of which<BR>cannot be expressed by its constituent<BR>parts separately (नित्यसमास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविघात|अविघातः
अविघात a. Unimpeded,<BR>unobstructed; ˚गति a. unobstructed in<BR>one's course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविघ्न
अविघ्न a. Unobstructed, free<BR>from impediments; ˚क्रियोपलंभाय<BR>Ś. 1.<BR>--घ्नं Freedom from obstacle or<BR>impediment, welfare (this word is<BR>usually neuter, though विघ्न is m.);<BR>साधयाम्यहमविघ्नमस्तु ते R. 11. 91;<BR>अविघ्नमस्तु ते स्थेयाः पितेव धुरि पुत्रिणां<BR>1. 91; अविघ्नमस्तु सावित्र्याः प्रदाने<BR>दुहितुस्तव Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचाचल
अविचाचल a. Ved. Not<BR>staggering or fluctuating, standing firmly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचार|अविचारः
अविचार a.<BR>1 Void of judgment,<BR>undiscriminating, ill-judging,<BR>unwise.<BR>--2 Unhesitating, prompt.<BR>--3<BR>Having spies.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Absence of<BR>judgment, indiscretion, error,<BR>folly.<BR>--2 Promptitude.<BR>--3 A country<BR>fit for the grazing of sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारणीय
अविचारणीय a. Not to be<BR>called in question; आज्ञा गुरूणां<BR>ह्यविचारणीया R. 14. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारित|अविचारितः
अविचारित a.<BR>1 Ill-judged, not<BR>well thought out or considered.<BR>--2 Determined, certain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--निर्णयः a prejudice, prejudiced<BR>opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचारिन्
अविचारिन् a.<BR>1 Unthinking,<BR>inconsiderate, indiscreet.<BR>--2 Prompt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचालित
अविचालित a<BR>1 Unmoved,<BR>unshaken.<BR>--2 Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविचृत्य
अविचृत्य a. Ved. Not to be<BR>loosened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्छिन्न|अविच्छिन्नं|अविछिन्न
अविच्छिन्न a.<BR>1 Not<BR>separated, undivided.<BR>--2 Continuous,<BR>uninterrupted; ˚संताना संततिः K. 65,<BR>R. 17. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्छेद|अविच्छेदः|अविछेद
अविच्छेद a.<BR>1 Uninterrupted.<BR>--2<BR>Undivided, entire, whole.<BR>--दः<BR>1<BR>Entirety, wholeness.<BR>--2<BR>Connection, continuity; Ki. 14. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविच्युत
अविच्युत a.<BR>1 Not deviated<BR>from, observed or followed strictly.<BR>--2 Eternal, permanent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविजात
अविजात a. Ved. Not having<BR>brought forth, having no offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविजातीय
अविजातीय a. Of the same kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञ|अविज्ञः
अविज्ञ a.<BR>1 Ignorant, untaught.<BR>--2 Clumsy, stupid, awkward; ˚ता<BR>ignorance, folly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञात
अविज्ञात a.<BR>1 Unknown.<BR>--2<BR>Unintelligible, doubtful, indistinct.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गद a. Ved. speaking in<BR>an unintelligible way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञातृ
अविज्ञातृ a.<BR>1 Not knowing. --m.<BR>(ता) The Supreme Being (परमेश्वर).<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu; अविज्ञाता सहस्रांशुः<BR>V. Sah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविज्ञेय|अविज्ञेयं|अविज्ञेयः
अविज्ञेय a. Undistinguishable, not<BR>to be recognized or known,<BR>unknowable.<BR>--यः The Supreme God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविडीनं|अविडीन
अविडीनं A direct flight of<BR>birds (पाक्षिणामाभिमुख्याभिगमनं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितथ|अवितथं
अवितथ a.<BR>1 Not false, true;<BR>तदवितथमवादीर्यन्ममत्वं प्रियेति Śi. 11. 33;<BR>अवितथा वितथा सखि मा गिरः 6. 18.<BR>--2 Realised, not fruitless;<BR>अवितथफलाः स्वप्नाः K. 65; कुरु गुरुवचनमवितथं<BR>K. 178; चकारावितथां भ्रातुः प्रतिज्ञां<BR>R. 15. 95; 5. 26.<BR>--थं Truth;<BR>अवितथमाह प्रियंवदा Ś. 3, P. is right, what<BR>P. says is right; Ve. 2.<BR>--थं ind.<BR>Not falsely, according to truth;<BR>Ms. 2. 144.<BR>--था N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवितारिन्
अवितारिन् a. Ved.<BR>1 Not doing<BR>any harm, harmless (अनपायिन्).<BR>--2<BR>Not departing, remaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0194-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्त
अवित्त a.<BR>1 Not famous,<BR>unknown.<BR>--2 Poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्ति|अवित्तिः
अवित्ति a.<BR>1 Not obtaining or<BR>getting.<BR>--2 Unwise, foolish.<BR>--त्तिः f.<BR>1 Not finding, getting, or possessing.<BR>--2 Want of wisdom.<BR>--3 Poverty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्यजः|अवित्यज|अवित्यजं
अवित्यजः --जं Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवित्यजं|अवित्यज|अवित्यजः
अवित्यजः --जं Quicksilver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविथुर
अविथुर a. Not separated,<BR>united (Ved. for अविधुर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविथ्या
अविथ्या [अवये हिता, अवि थ्यंन्<BR>P. V. 1. 8] N. of the plant अजथ्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदग्ध
अविदग्ध a.<BR>1 Unlearned,<BR>inexperienced, stupid.<BR>--2 Not well<BR>burnt, undigested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदाहिन्
अविदाहिन् a.<BR>1 Imperfectly<BR>digested, producing heart-burn.<BR>--2 Not<BR>burning or afflicting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदस्य
अविदस्य a. Ved. Unceasing,<BR>inexhaustible, perennial, perpetual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदासिन्
अविदासिन् a. Perennial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदित|अविदितः
अविदित a. Unknown; ˚गतयामा<BR>रात्रिः U. 1. 27 the watches of which<BR>stole away (glided imperceptibly<BR>away).<BR>--तः The Supreme God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदीधयु
अविदीधयु a. Ved.<BR>1 Not<BR>delaying or hesitating.<BR>--2 Shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविदूर
अविदूर a. Not distant, near,<BR>contiguous.<BR>--रं Proximity, vicinity.<BR>--रं ind. Near to, not far from; so<BR>अविदूरेण, अविदूरात्, --दूरतः, --विदूरे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्ध|अविद्धः
अविद्ध a. Unpierced.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्णा, --र्णी [अविद्धः अछिद्रः पर्णरूपः<BR>कर्णोऽस्याः] N. of a plant (पाठा)<BR>Cissampelos Hexaudra.<BR>--दृश् a.<BR>all-seeing.<BR>--वर्चस् a. of unimpaired glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्य|अविद्यः
अविद्य a.<BR>1 Not educated,<BR>unlearned, foolish, unwise; अविद्यानां<BR>तु सर्वेषामीहातश्चेद्धनं भवेत् Ms. 9. 205.<BR>--2 Not pertaining to knowledge.<BR>--द्या<BR>1 Ignorance, folly, want of<BR>learning.<BR>--2 Spiritual ignorance.<BR>--3<BR>Illusion, illusion personified or<BR>Māyā (a term frequently occurring in<BR>Vedānta; by means of this illusion<BR>one perceives the universe, which<BR>does not really exist, as inherent in<BR>Brahma which alone really exists).<BR>The term appears also in the<BR>systems of Gautama, Patañjali, Kapila,<BR>where it has different bearings;<BR>(with Buddhists) ignorance<BR>together with non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्यामय
अविद्यामय a. Caused by ignorance<BR>or illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविद्रिय
अविद्रिय a. Ved.<BR>1 Without a<BR>rent or hole.<BR>--2 Impenetrable, solid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधवा
अविधवा Not a widow, a married<BR>woman whose husband is still<BR>living; भर्तुर्मित्रं प्रियमविधवे विद्धि मामंबुवाहं<BR>Me. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधा
अविधा ind. An interjection<BR>meaning ‘help, help’ used in<BR>calling for help in danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधान
अविधान a. [न. ब.] Deviating<BR>from the fixed rule, irregular.<BR>--नं<BR>Absence of a definite rule;<BR>irregularity, deviation from rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधि|अविधिः
अविधि a. Not lawful, contrary<BR>to rule.<BR>--धिः Irregularity, absence<BR>of a rule or precept; ˚पूर्वक not<BR>according to rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविधेय
अविधेय a. Unmanageable, adverse;<BR>विधेरविधेयतां Mu. 4. 2;<BR>हर्षविषादयोरविधेयत्वं Dk. 161 not being<BR>influenced or swayed by &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनः|अविन
अविनः [अवति यज्ञं, अव्-इनच्<BR>Uṇ. 2. 46]<BR>1 A sacrificer.<BR>--2 An<BR>officiating priest at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनय|अविनयः
अविनय a. [न. ब.] Immodest,<BR>insolent, ill-behaved, ill-mannered.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Want of good manners or<BR>modesty; बहवोऽविनयान्नष्टा राजानः<BR>सपरिच्छदाः Ms. 7. 40, 41.<BR>--2 Rude<BR>behaviour, rudeness, immodest or<BR>rude act; ˚बहुलतया चाभिनवयौवनस्य<BR>K. 143; अयमाचरत्यविनयं मुग्धासु<BR>तपस्विकन्यासु Ś. 1. 25; indecorum,<BR>impropriety of conduct.<BR>--3<BR>Incivility, disrespect.<BR>--4 Offence, crime,<BR>fault.<BR>--5 Pride, arrogance,<BR>insolence; अविनयमपनय विष्णो Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनीत|अविनीतः
अविनीत a.<BR>1 Immodest, ill bred,<BR>unmannered.<BR>--2 Acting improperly,<BR>wicked, vile.<BR>--3 Insolent, rude.<BR>--4<BR>Not tamed, ill-trained; Ms. 4. 67.<BR>--ता An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनश्वर|अविनश्वरः
अविनश्वर a. Destructible.<BR>--रः The<BR>Supreme God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनाभावः|अविनाभाव
अविनाभावः<BR>1 Non-separation.<BR>--2<BR>Inherent or essential character,<BR>inseparable connection.<BR>--3 Connection<BR>(in general); अविनाभावोऽत्र संबंधमात्रं<BR>न तु नांतरीयकत्वं K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविनिगमः|अविनिगम
अविनिगमः An illogical<BR>conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविंध्यः|अविन्ध्य|अविन्ध्यः
अविंध्यः N. of a Rākṣasa,<BR>minister of Rāvaṇa.<BR>--ध्या N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपक्व
अविपक्व a. Not ripe (fig. also);<BR>immature, undigested.; ˚बुद्धि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">Page0195-c+ 55</a>]<BR>inexperienced, of undeveloped<BR>understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपाक|अविपाकः
अविपाक a. Suffering from<BR>indigestion.<BR>--कः The state of not<BR>being ripe, indigestion, a disease<BR>arising from indigestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपद्
अविपद् f. Absence of misery,<BR>prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविपन्न
अविपन्न a.<BR>1 Uninjured, unhurt.<BR>--2 Not defiled or polluted, pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्र|अविप्रः
अविप्र a. Ved.<BR>1 Not (spiritually)<BR>excited, not inspired.<BR>--2 Not a<BR>worshipper or praiser.<BR>--प्रः One not<BR>a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविप्लुत
अविप्लुत a. Undeviating, steadily<BR>observing; unviolated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभक्त|अविभक्तः
अविभक्त a.<BR>1 Undivided,<BR>unpartitioned, joint, (as property of a<BR>family, or co-heirs); अविभक्ता<BR>विभक्ता वा सपिंडाः स्थावरे समाः.<BR>--2 Not<BR>broken, entire.<BR>--3 Not different.<BR>--4<BR>Existing everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाग|अविभागः
अविभाग a. Unpartitioned,<BR>undivided.<BR>--गः<BR>1 Not dividing.<BR>--2<BR>Undivided inheritance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभाज्य|अविभाज्यं
अविभाज्य a. Indivisible.<BR>--ज्यं<BR>1<BR>Indivisibility.<BR>--2 Not being liable<BR>to be partitioned; (said of certain<BR>articles which are not to be divided<BR>at the time of partition); e. g. वस्त्रं<BR>पात्रमलंकारं कृतान्नमुदकं स्त्रियः । योगक्षेमं प्रचारं<BR>च न विभाज्यं प्रचक्षते Ms. 9. 219. ˚ता<BR>indivisibility, unfitness for partition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावना
अविभावना --नं Non-perception;<BR>disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावनं|अविभावन
अविभावना --नं Non-perception;<BR>disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविभावनीय
अविभावनीय a. Imperceptible,<BR>undistinguishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमुक्त|अविमुक्तं|अविमुक्तः
अविमुक्त a. Unloosed, not<BR>quitted or let go.<BR>--क्तं<BR>1 N. of a Tīrtha<BR>or sacred place near Benares, or<BR>Benares itself; न विमुक्तं शिवाभ्यां<BR>यदविमुक्तं ततो विदुः.<BR>--2 The space<BR>between the chin and the head.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईश्वरः a celebrated Śiva-linga at<BR>Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमृष्य
अविमृष्य a. Undoubted,<BR>unquestionable; Ki. 6. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविमोक्य
अविमोक्य a. Ved. Not to be<BR>loosened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियुक्त
अवियुक्त a. Undivided,<BR>conjoined, united; not separated, absent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवियोग|अवियोगः
अवियोग a. Not separated, united,<BR>connected.<BR>--गः<BR>1 Non-separation,<BR>presence.<BR>--2 Conjunction,<BR>association.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तृतीया N. of a certain<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">Page0196-a+ 56</a>]<BR>festival or holiday.<BR>--व्रतं a vow<BR>to be observed by women on the<BR>third day of the first fortnight of<BR>Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0195-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरत|अविरतं
अविरत a.<BR>1 Not desisting or<BR>ceasing from (with abl.);<BR>uninterrupted, continual, unbroken, perpetual;<BR>अविरतोत्कंठमुत्कंठितेन Me. 102; Prov.<BR>मंदोप्यविरतोद्योगः सदैव विजयी भवेत्<BR>‘slow and steady wins the race’.<BR>--2 Abandoned.<BR>--तं ind. Eternally,<BR>continually; अविरतं परकार्यकृतां सतां<BR>Bv. 1. 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरति|अविरतिः
अविरति a. Incessant, ceaseless.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1 Continuity,<BR>uninterruptedness.<BR>--2 Incontinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविराम|अविरामः
अविराम a. Uninterrupted,<BR>continuous.<BR>--मः Uninterrupted<BR>succession, continuance.<BR>--मं ind.<BR>Uninterruptedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरल|अविरलं
अविरल a.<BR>1 Thick, dense;<BR>˚वारिधारा U. 6 sharp-driving shower;<BR>˚अश्रुबिंदु; not thin, many;<BR>सादरमभिमुखदत्ताविरलपदः K. 95.<BR>--2<BR>Contiguous, close.<BR>--3 Coarse, gross,<BR>substantial.<BR>--4 Uninterrupted,<BR>continuous.<BR>--लं ind.<BR>1 Closely;<BR>अविरलमालिंगितुं पवनः Ś. 3. 7.<BR>--2<BR>Uninterruptedly, incessantly, constantly;<BR>U. 3. 24.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धारासारः an<BR>incessant down-pour of heavy rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरलित
अविरलित a. Closely stuck, lying<BR>very close; ˚कपोलं U. 1. 27 cheek<BR>to cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविराधयत्|अविराधयन्त्
अविराधयत् a. Ved. Not<BR>withdrawing oneself; not desisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरुद्ध
अविरुद्ध a.<BR>1 Not opposed,<BR>compatible, consistent with.<BR>--2 Living<BR>together.<BR>--3 Unobstructed,<BR>unhindered, unimpeded.<BR>--4 Allowed;<BR>proper; यद्यविरुद्धं श्रोष्यामि V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरोधः|अविरोध
अविरोधः<BR>1 Consistency,<BR>compatibility, congruity; सामान्यास्तु<BR>परार्थमुद्यमभृतः स्वार्थाविरोधेन ये Bh. 2. 74<BR>consistently with their own interest;<BR>सर्वेषामविरोधेन ब्रह्मकर्म समारभे<BR>Pūjāmantra.<BR>--2 Absence of impediment.<BR>--3 Assent, concurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरेचनं|अविरेचन
अविरेचनं Anything which causes<BR>constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविरेच्य
अविरेच्य a. Not to be purged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलक्ष्य
अविलक्ष्य a.<BR>1 Having no aim or<BR>mark.<BR>--2 Guileless.<BR>--3 Irremediable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलंघनं|अविलङ्घन
अविलंघनं Non-transgression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलंघनीय|अविलङ्घनीय
अविलंघनीय a.<BR>1 Not to be<BR>transgressed.<BR>--2 Prescribed, fixed, settled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलंब|अविलम्ब|अविलम्बः
अविलंब a. Prompt, not<BR>delaying, quick.<BR>--बः Absence of delay,<BR>quickness, promptitude.<BR>--बं,<BR>अविलंबेन ind. Without delay, quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलंबित|अविलम्बित|अविलम्बितं|अविलम्बितः
अविलंबित a. Without delay,<BR>quick, expeditious, prompt.<BR>--तं<BR>ind. Quickly, without delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविला
अविला [अव्-इलच्] An ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलास|अविलासः
अविलास a. Free from whims,<BR>faithful, constant.<BR>--सः Absence<BR>of pastime or whim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविलिख
अविलिख a.<BR>1 Not writing or<BR>painting, or unable to do so; (<BR>P. VI. 2. 157-8).<BR>--2 Writing badly.<BR>--3 Different from one who writes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवक्षित
अविवक्षित a.<BR>1 Not intended or<BR>aimed at; भ्रातरः इत्यत्र एकशेषग्रह<BR>मविवक्षितं.<BR>--2 Not to be said or spoken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवादः|अविवाद
अविवादः Agreement, consent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवादिन्
अविवादिन् a. Not contending,<BR>quiet, peaceable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवाहिन्
अविवाहिन् a.<BR>1 Not marrying,<BR>remaining single or celibate.<BR>--2 Not<BR>relating to marriage.<BR>--3 Interdicted<BR>as to marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविविक्त
अविविक्त a.<BR>1 Uninvestigated,<BR>not properly thought out.<BR>--2<BR>Indiscriminate, confounded.<BR>--3<BR>Public.<BR>--4 Making no difference; ˚दृश्<BR>viewing all as one with God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेक|अविवेकः
अविवेक a. Wanting in judgment<BR>or discrimination, thoughtless.<BR>--कः<BR>1 Want of discrimination or<BR>judgment, absence of prudence,<BR>imprudence; अविवेकः परमापदां पदं Ki. 2. 30.<BR>--2 Hastiness, rashness, recklessness.<BR>--3 Ignorance (<BR>अन्योन्यतादात्म्यरूपमिथ्याज्ञानं).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत a. done rashly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेकिन्
अविवेकिन् a.<BR>1 Undiscriminating,<BR>inconsiderate, thoughtless.<BR>--2<BR>Superficial, short-sighted, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविवेन
अविवेन a. Ved. Not disaffected.<BR>--नं ind. Not disaffectedly,<BR>favourably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशंक|अविशङ्क
अविशंक a. Having no fears or<BR>doubt, fearless.<BR>--कां Absence of<BR>doubt or fear, confidence,<BR>certainty.<BR>--कं, --अविशंकेन ind. Without<BR>doubt, hesitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशंकित|अविशङ्कित
अविशंकित a.<BR>1 Unapprehensive,<BR>fearless.<BR>--2 Without doubt,<BR>confiding; गृध्रवाक्यात्कथं<BR>मूढास्त्यजध्वमविशंकिताः K. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशस्तृ
अविशस्तृ m. An unskilful<BR>cutter up or killer (of animals at a<BR>sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशुद्धिः|अविशुद्धि
अविशुद्धिः f. Impurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविशेष|अविशेषः
अविशेष a. Without any<BR>difference, alike, similar, uniform.<BR>--षः,<BR>--षं<BR>1 Absence of difference,<BR>uniformity, similarity.<BR>--2 Identity,<BR>sameness.<BR>--3 The subtle elements (in<BR>Sān. phil.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञ a. not<BR>knowing the difference (in things),<BR>undiscriminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्रांत|अविश्रान्त|अविश्रान्तः
अविश्रांत a.<BR>1 Untiring,<BR>incessant, ceaseless; Ś. 6.<BR>--2 Unhurt.<BR>--तं ind. Incessantly, continuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वास|अविश्वासः
अविश्वास a. Not inspiring<BR>confidence, mistrusted.<BR>--सः<BR>Mistrust, suspicion.<BR>--सा A cow<BR>calving after long intervals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वस्त|अविश्वस्तः
अविश्वस्त a. Not trusted,<BR>suspected; न विश्वसेदविश्वस्ते H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविश्वासिन्
अविश्वासिन् a. Mistrusting,<BR>unbelieving, diffident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष|अविषः
अविष a.<BR>1 Not poisonous.<BR>--2<BR>Anti-venomous, antidote.<BR>--3<BR>Protecting.<BR>--षः [अव्-टिषच् Uṇ. 1. 45]<BR>1 An ocean.<BR>--2 A king.<BR>--3 Sky.<BR>--षा N. of a plant (निर्विषातृण).<BR>--षी<BR>1 A river.<BR>--2 The earth.<BR>--3 Heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषय|अविषयः
अविषय a.<BR>1 Unperceived,<BR>invisible, beyond the reach of the<BR>senses.<BR>--2 Insensible.<BR>--3 Disregarding<BR>objects of sense; ˚मनसां यतीनां<BR>M. 1. 1.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Absence, disappearance;<BR>रवेरविषये किं न प्रदीपस्य प्रकाशनं<BR>H. 2. 79.<BR>--2 Not an object of<BR>(anything), not within the reach of,<BR>beyond, transcending; न<BR>कश्चिद्धीमतामविषयो नाम Ś. 4;<BR>सकलवचनानामविषयः Māl. 1. 30 beyond the reach<BR>(power) of words; सौमित्रेरपि<BR>पत्रिणामविषये तत्र प्रिये क्वासि भोः U. 3. 45.<BR>--3 Disregard of the objects of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविषयीकरणं|अविषयीकरण
अविषयीकरणं Not making<BR>anything an object of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष्ठ
अविष्ठ Ved. Gladly<BR>accepting, protecting very carefully or<BR>attentively; Rv. 7. 28. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष्या
अविष्या [अव् गतौ इसुन्<BR>अविर्गतिमिच्छति क्यच् भावे अ Tv.]<BR>1 Wish to go<BR>(गमनेच्छा); Rv. 2. 38. 3.<BR>--2 Wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविष्यु
अविष्यु a. Ved.<BR>1 Attacking.<BR>--2<BR>Desirous, wishing.<BR>--3 Violent,<BR>vehement.<BR>--4 Wishing to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्
अविस् n. [अव्-भावे इसुन्]<BR>1<BR>Protection.<BR>--2 Going. --m. An<BR>extender, enlarger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसंवादिन्
अविसंवादिन् a. Unfailing, not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">Page0197-a+ 55</a>]<BR>false; Ki. 13. 15; लक्षणान्येव<BR>तवाविसंवादीनि Dk. 67 entirely agreeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0196-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविसर्गिन्
अविसर्गिन् a. Not quitting,<BR>retaining, adhering to. --m.<BR>--(गी) An<BR>unintermittent fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तर
अविस्तर a. Of small extent or<BR>length, concise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तारः|अविस्तार
अविस्तारः Absence of amplification<BR>or diffuseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तीर्ण
अविस्तीर्ण a. Not extended or<BR>amplified, curtailed, concise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्तृत
अविस्तृत a. Compact, compressed,<BR>close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविस्पष्ट|अविस्पष्टं
अविस्पष्ट a. Not clear or plain,<BR>indistinct, obscure.<BR>--ष्टं An indistinct<BR>speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविहर्यत|अविहर्य्यत
अविहर्यत a. Not desired (<BR>अनभिलषित); येनाविहर्यतक्रतोः Rv. 1. 63. 2<BR>doer of undesired acts; whose will<BR>cannot be averted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविह्रुत
अविह्रुत a. Ved.<BR>1 Not to be<BR>killed, unassailable.<BR>--2 Unbent,<BR>unbroken.<BR>--3 Not curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अविह्वरत्|अविह्वरन्त्
अविह्वरत् a. Ved.<BR>1 Not<BR>slipping, not falling.<BR>--2 Undeviating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवी
अवी [अवत्यात्मानं लज्जया अव्-ई<BR>Uṇ. 3. 158] A woman in her courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीचि|अवीचिः
अवीचि a. Waveless.<BR>--चिः N.<BR>of a particular hell; ˚मयः a place of<BR>punishment for liars (यत्र जलमिव<BR>स्थलमश्मपृष्ठमवभासते Bhāg.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीज|अवीजः
अवीज --जक(अबीज)<BR>1 Seedless;<BR>Ms. 10. 71.<BR>--2 Impotent; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>--3 Having no prime cause.<BR>--जः<BR>Restraint, controlling the mental<BR>passions.<BR>--जा Vine plant.<BR>--जं<BR>1<BR>Bad seed, bad grain; ˚विक्रयिन्<BR>Ms. 9. 291.<BR>--2 Absence of seed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हन् a. Ved. not pernicious to men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीजक
अवीज --जक(अबीज)<BR>1 Seedless;<BR>Ms. 10. 71.<BR>--2 Impotent; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>--3 Having no prime cause.<BR>--जः<BR>Restraint, controlling the mental<BR>passions.<BR>--जा Vine plant.<BR>--जं<BR>1<BR>Bad seed, bad grain; ˚विक्रयिन्<BR>Ms. 9. 291.<BR>--2 Absence of seed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हन् a. Ved. not pernicious to men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबीज|अबीजः
अवीज --जक(अबीज)<BR>1 Seedless;<BR>Ms. 10. 71.<BR>--2 Impotent; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>--3 Having no prime cause.<BR>--जः<BR>Restraint, controlling the mental<BR>passions.<BR>--जा Vine plant.<BR>--जं<BR>1<BR>Bad seed, bad grain; ˚विक्रयिन्<BR>Ms. 9. 291.<BR>--2 Absence of seed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हन् a. Ved. not pernicious to men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अबीजक
अवीज --जक(अबीज)<BR>1 Seedless;<BR>Ms. 10. 71.<BR>--2 Impotent; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>--3 Having no prime cause.<BR>--जः<BR>Restraint, controlling the mental<BR>passions.<BR>--जा Vine plant.<BR>--जं<BR>1<BR>Bad seed, bad grain; ˚विक्रयिन्<BR>Ms. 9. 291.<BR>--2 Absence of seed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हन् a. Ved. not pernicious to men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीतं|अवीत
अवीतं A variety of अनुमान or<BR>inference; (व्यतिरेकमुखेन प्रवर्तमानं<BR>निषेधकमवीतं; यथा पृथिवी पृथिवीतरभिन्ना गंधवत्त्वात्<BR>Tv.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीर|अवीरः
अवीर a.<BR>1 Unmanly, effeminate,<BR>cowardly.<BR>--2 Having no son (as a<BR>woman).<BR>--3 Helpless.<BR>--4 Destitute<BR>of men.<BR>--रा A woman who has<BR>neither sons nor husband; अजातपुत्रा<BR>विधवा साऽवीरा परिकीर्तिता; (opp. वीरा<BR>which is thus defined; पतिपुत्रवती नारी<BR>वीरा प्रोक्ता मनीषिभिः); अनर्चितं वृथा<BR>मांसमवीरांयाश्च योषितः Ms. 4. 213;<BR>Y. 1. 163.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवीर्य
अवीर्य a. Ved. Weak, ineffective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृक
अवृक a.<BR>1 Free from danger,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">Page0197-b+ 56</a>]<BR>safe.<BR>--2 Not hurting, inoffensive,<BR>true.<BR>--3 Free from one who<BR>obscures.<BR>--कं<BR>1 Safety, peace,<BR>security.<BR>--2 Quiet, repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृजिन
अवृजिन a. Ved. Straightforward,<BR>sincere, not deserting (friends); an<BR>epithet of the Ādityas; Rv. 2. 27. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृत
अवृत a.<BR>1 Unchecked,<BR>unimpeded.<BR>--2 Unselected.<BR>--3 Uncovered,<BR>unprotected.<BR>--4 Unsubdued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृत्ति|अवृत्तिः
अवृत्ति a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Not<BR>existing, not present, not being in.<BR>--2<BR>Having no livelihood.<BR>--त्तिः f.<BR>1<BR>Absence of subsistence or means of<BR>livelihood, inadequate support;<BR>अवृत्तिकर्षिता हि स्त्री प्रदुष्येत् स्थितिमत्यपि<BR>Ms. 9. 74; 10. 101;<BR>आददीताममेवास्मादवृत्तावेकरात्रिकं 4. 223.<BR>--2 Absence<BR>of wages; ˚त्वं non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृथा
अवृथा ind. Not in vain,<BR>successfully.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. successful,<BR>gaining one's desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृद्धिक
अवृद्धिक a. Not augmentative,<BR>not bearing interest (as capital).<BR>--कं Original capital, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृध
अवृध a. Ved.<BR>1 Not increasing.<BR>--2 Not promoting, not honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवृष्टि|अवृष्टिः
अवृष्टि a. Not pouring down rain<BR>(as a cloud).<BR>--ष्टिः Want of rain,<BR>drought; famine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवे
अवे {c2c} P. [अव इ]<BR>1 (a) To know,<BR>understand, learn, perceive, be aware<BR>of; अवैमि ते तस्यां सोदर्यस्नेहं Ś. 4;<BR>अवैमि चैनामनघेति R. 14. 40;<BR>द्विषदभियोग इत्यवैति Mu. 1. 7.; अवैमि ते सारं<BR>Ku. 3. 13; R. 2. 35. (b) To know,<BR>look upon or consider, regard,<BR>तदवैमि कैतवं Ku. 4. 9; Ś. 5. 11;<BR>Bk. 7. 33; किं मां सुतक्षयकरं सुत इत्यवैषि<BR>Ve. 5. 2.<BR>--2 To go or move away.<BR>--3<BR>To go to, approach (with acc.).<BR>--4<BR>To rush upon, come down upon<BR>(Ved.) --Freq. or Pass. (अवेयते) To<BR>beg pardon for, conciliate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेत
अवेत p. p.<BR>1 Elapsed, past.<BR>--2<BR>Obtained, attained.<BR>--3 Joined or<BR>united with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्ष्
अवेक्ष् {c1c} A. [अव-ईक्ष्]<BR>1 To look<BR>at, perceive, observe, behold.<BR>--2 To<BR>aim at, have in view; योत्स्यमानानवेक्षेहं<BR>Bg. 1. 23; take into account or<BR>consideration, have regard to; अवेक्ष्य<BR>धातोर्गमनार्थमर्थविद् R. 3. 21; किमपि<BR>निमित्तमवेक्ष्य V. 5;<BR>त्रिदिवोत्सुकयाप्यवेक्ष्य मां R. 8. 60 out of regard for me;<BR>K. 329; oft. with न meaning ‘not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">Page0197-c+ 56</a>]<BR>to mind or heed,’ ‘disregard’;<BR>R. 11. 69; न हि कमलिनीं दृष्ट्वा ग्राहमवेक्षते<BR>मतंगजः M. 3 (it may also mean<BR>‘expect’ here); निद्रावशेन भवता<BR>ह्यनवेक्ष्यमाणा R. 5. 67.<BR>--3 To look to or<BR>after, attend to; अवेक्षमाणं महतीं<BR>मुहुर्मुहुः Śi. 1. 10.<BR>--4 To take care of,<BR>guard, watch over, protect;<BR>वसुधेयमवेक्ष्यतां त्वया R. 8. 83; श्लाघ्यां<BR>दुहितरमवेक्षस्व जानकीं U. 1, 7.<BR>--5 To think,<BR>consider; यदवोचदवेक्ष्य मानिनी<BR>Ki. 2. 3.<BR>--6 To look into or examine,<BR>inspect; स कदाचिदवेक्षितप्रजः R. 8. 32;<BR>प्रकृतीरवेक्षितुं 18 inquire into;<BR>Ś. 6.<BR>--7 To expect, hope for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षक
अवेक्षक a.<BR>1 Showing, showing<BR>all round.<BR>--2 Inspecting,<BR>supervising; a superintendent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षणं|अवेक्षण
अवेक्षणं<BR>1 Looking towards or at,<BR>seeing.<BR>--2 Guarding, watching over,<BR>protection, taking care of,<BR>attending to, supervision, inspection;<BR>वर्णाश्रमावेक्षणजागरूकः R. 14. 85;<BR>हस्त्यश्वावेक्षणेऽनाभियुक्तः Mu. 3.<BR>--3 Attention,<BR>care, observation.<BR>--4 Regarding,<BR>considering; see अनवेक्षणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षणीय
अवेक्षणीय pot. p. To be looked to<BR>or respected, to be looked upon or<BR>considered; तपस्विसामान्यमवेक्षणीया<BR>R. 14. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षा
अवेक्षा<BR>1 Seeing, looking at.<BR>--2<BR>Attention, care, regard; लब्धं रक्षेदवेक्षया<BR>Ms. 7. 101; अत्रास्त्यवेक्षा त्वयि मे<BR>Rām.<BR>--3 Agreement, engagement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षितृ
अवेक्षितृ a. Looking at; thinking<BR>of, regarding &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेक्षिन्
अवेक्षिन् a. Seeing, observing;<BR>धर्मावेक्षिता Ś. 5. regard for justice or<BR>righteousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेणि
अवेणि a.<BR>1 Not braided.<BR>--2<BR>Having no braid of hair.<BR>--3 Not flowing<BR>together or commingled (as the<BR>waters of rivers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदयान
अवेदयान a. Not knowing, not<BR>ascertaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेदिः|अवेदि
अवेदिः f. Absence of<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेद्य|अवेद्यः
अवेद्य a.<BR>1 Unknowable, secret.<BR>--2 Unattainable.<BR>--द्यः A calf.<BR>--द्या<BR>(A woman) not to be married;<BR>Ms. 10. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेनत्|अवेनन्त्
अवेनत् a. Ved. Unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेल|अवेलः
अवेल a.<BR>1 Having no boundary<BR>or limit, unlimited.<BR>--2 Having no<BR>time, untimely.<BR>--लः Concealment<BR>of knowledge.<BR>--ला<BR>1 Unfavourable<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">Page0198-a+ 55</a>]<BR>time.<BR>--2 Chewed betel (supposed<BR>to be = अव+इला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0197-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवेष्टिः|अवेष्टि
अवेष्टिः Ved. Expiation(of sins)<BR>by sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैध|अवैधं
अवैध a. (धी f.)<BR>1 Irregular, not<BR>conformable to law or rule; अवैधं<BR>पंचमं कुर्वन् राज्ञो दंडेन शुध्यति.<BR>--2 Not<BR>sanctioned by the Śāstras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैमत्यं|अवैमत्य
अवैमत्यं Unanimity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवैरहत्यं|अवैरहत्य
अवैरहत्यं Ved. Security from<BR>slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोक्षणं|अवोक्षण
अवोक्षणं [अव-उक्ष्-भावे ल्युट्] Ved.<BR>Sprinkling with the hand slightly<BR>bent; उत्तानेनैव हस्तेन प्रोक्षणं परिकीर्तितं ।<BR>न्यंचताभ्युक्षणं प्रोक्तं तिरश्चावोक्षणं स्मृतं ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोद|अवोदं|अवोदः
अवोद a. [अव-उंद्-भावे घञ् निपातः<BR>नलोपः P. VI. 4. 29] Wet, moist.<BR>--दः Sprinkling, moistening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोदेव
अवोदेव a. [देवानामवस्तात् अव्ययी˚]<BR>Bringing down the gods; below (the<BR>region of the) gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवोषः|अवोष
अवोषः Hot food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्य|अव्यः
अव्य a. [अवि भवार्थे यत्] Coming or<BR>belonging to a sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यक्त|अव्यक्तं|अव्यक्तः
अव्यक्त a.<BR>1 Indistinct, not<BR>manifest or apparent, inarticulate;<BR>˚वर्ण indistinct accents Ś. 7. 17;<BR>फलमव्यक्तमब्रवीत्.<BR>--2 Invisible,<BR>imperceptible.<BR>--3 Undetermined;<BR>अव्यक्तोयमचिंत्योयं Bg. 2. 25; 8. 20.<BR>--4 Undeveloped, uncreated.<BR>--5 (In<BR>alg.) Unknown (as a quantity or<BR>number).<BR>--क्तः<BR>1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva.<BR>--3 Cupid.<BR>--4<BR>Primary matter which has not yet<BR>entered into real existence.<BR>--5 A<BR>fool.<BR>--क्तं (In Vedānta phil.)<BR>1<BR>The Supreme Being or universal<BR>Spirit, Brahma.<BR>--2 Spiritual<BR>ignorance.<BR>--3 The subtle body.<BR>--4<BR>The state of sleep (सुषुप्त्यवस्था).<BR>--5<BR>(In Sān. phil.) The primary<BR>germ of nature (सर्वकारण), the<BR>primordial element or productive<BR>principle from which all the<BR>phenomena of the material world are<BR>developed; बुद्धेरिवाव्यक्तमुदाहरंति R. 13. 60;<BR>महतः परमव्यक्तमव्यक्तात्पुरुषः परः Kaṭh.,<BR>Sāṅ. K. 2, 10, 14, 16, 58.<BR>--6 The<BR>soul.<BR>--7 Nature.<BR>--क्तं ind.<BR>Imperceptibly, indistinctly, inarticulately.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुकरणं imitating<BR>inarticulate or unmeaning sounds;<BR>P. V. 4. 57; VI. 1. 98.<BR>--आदि a.<BR>whose beginning is inscrutable.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-b" target="_blank">Page0198-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--क्रिया {1} an algebraic calculation. {2}<BR>any act of an indistinct character.<BR>--पद a. inarticulate.<BR>--मूर्ति a.<BR>having an incomprehensible form.<BR>--मूलप्रभवः the tree of mundane<BR>existence (in Sān. phil.).<BR>--राग a.<BR>darkred, ruddy.<BR>--(गः) the colour of<BR>the dawn; अव्यक्तरागस्त्वरुणः Ak.<BR>--राशिः an unknown number or<BR>quantity (in algebra).<BR>--लक्षणः --व्यक्तः<BR>an epithet of Śiva (whose qualities are<BR>not perceptible).<BR>--लिंग a. whose signs<BR>are invisible (as a disease).<BR>--(गः)<BR>an ascetic (संन्यासी).<BR>--(गं) the great<BR>principle (महत्) (in Sān. phil.).<BR>--वर्त्मन्, --मार्ग a. whose ways are<BR>mysterious or inscrutable.<BR>--वाच् a.<BR>speaking indistinctly.<BR>--साम्यं an<BR>equation of unknown quantities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यग्र
अव्यग्र a.<BR>1 Not agitated or<BR>ruffled, steady, cool.<BR>--2 Not engaged or<BR>occupied (in business); अव्यग्रस्य<BR>पुनरस्य U. 2.<BR>--3 Indifferent,<BR>undisturbed.<BR>--4 Attentive, careful.<BR>--ग्रं<BR>ind. Quietly, at ease, coolly,<BR>leisurely; क्रव्यमव्यग्रमत्ति Māl. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यंग|अव्यङ्ग|अव्यङ्गः
अव्यंग a.<BR>1 Not mutilated or<BR>defective, well-made, sound, perfect;<BR>अव्यंगांगीं सौम्यनाम्नीं Ms. 3. 10.<BR>--2<BR>Plain, not figurative (as a meaning).<BR>--गा<BR>1 = अव्यंडा q. v.<BR>--2 A legume or<BR>pod of the awn of barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यचस्
अव्यचस् a. Ved. Not spacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यंजन|अव्यञ्जन|अव्यञ्जनः
अव्यंजन a.<BR>1 Having no<BR>distinctive or characteristic marks or<BR>signs (as of the sex); ˚ना कन्या.<BR>--2 Having no good marks.<BR>--3<BR>Indistinct.<BR>--4 Not figurative.<BR>--नः An<BR>animal without horns, though of an<BR>age to have them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यंडा|अव्यण्डा
अव्यंडा [न विगतमंडं बीजमस्याः]<BR>1<BR>N. of the plant Carpopogon Pruriens<BR>Roxb.<BR>--2 A legume or pod of the<BR>awn of barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यतिः|अव्यति
अव्यतिः f. Ved.<BR>1 Satisfaction,<BR>satiating.<BR>--2 Desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यतिकीर्ण|अव्यतिकीर्ण्ण
अव्यतिकीर्ण a. Unmixed,<BR>unblended, distinct; specific, separate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथ|अव्यथः
अव्यथ a.<BR>1 Not giving or<BR>inflicting pain, merciful.<BR>--2 Free from<BR>pain.<BR>--थः [न व्यथते पद्भ्यां न संचलति<BR>व्यथ् भयचलनयोः अच्] A snake.<BR>--था<BR>1 N. of two plants; Terminalia<BR>Citrina Roxb.; and Hibiscus<BR>Mutabilis.<BR>--2 Dry ginger.<BR>--3 (Ved.)<BR>Firmness, steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथयः|अव्यथय
अव्यथयः A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथि|अव्यथिः
अव्यथि a. Ved. [व्यथ्-इन्, न. त.]<BR>Not tremulous or tottering (in steps),<BR>steady, sure-footed, undaunted;<BR>epithet of the horses of the Aśvins.<BR>--थिः f.<BR>1 A firm step.<BR>--2<BR>Undauntedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिन्
अव्यथिन् a. [cf. P. III. 2. 157]<BR>1<BR>Free from pain.<BR>--2 Free from fear,<BR>fearless; Śi. 15. 12.<BR>--3 Not giving<BR>pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथिषः|अव्यथिष
अव्यथिषः [न-व्यथ्-टिषच्<BR>Uṇ. 1. 49]<BR>1 The Sun.<BR>--2 The ocean.<BR>--षी<BR>1 The earth.<BR>--2 Midnight; night<BR>(अव्यथिषी धरारात्र्योः Ujjval.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यथ्य|अव्यथ्यः
अव्यथ्य a. Free from pain; not<BR>giving pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यध
अव्यध a. Not pierced; Śi. 18. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यनत्|अव्यनन्त्
अव्यनत् a. Ved. Not breathing,<BR>lifeless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यपेक्षा
अव्यपेक्षा Carelessness; ˚च्यूतने<BR>M. 3. 20 inadvertently fallen down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभिचारः|अव्यभिचार
अव्यभि(भी)चारः<BR>1<BR>Non-separation; अन्योन्यस्याव्यभीचारो<BR>भवेदामरणांतिकः Ms. 9. 101.<BR>--2 Constancy,<BR>steadiness, fidelity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभीचारः|अव्यभीचार
अव्यभि(भी)चारः<BR>1<BR>Non-separation; अन्योन्यस्याव्यभीचारो<BR>भवेदामरणांतिकः Ms. 9. 101.<BR>--2 Constancy,<BR>steadiness, fidelity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यभिचारिन्
अव्यभिचारिन् a.<BR>1 Not opposed or<BR>adverse, favourable;<BR>भवंत्यव्यभिचारिण्यो भर्तुरिष्टे पतिव्रताः Ku. 6. 86.<BR>--2<BR>Not subject to exceptions, true in<BR>all cases, without any instance to<BR>the contrary; यदुच्यते पार्वति पापवृत्तये<BR>न रूपमित्यव्यभिचारि तद्वचः Ku. 5. 36;<BR>रंध्रोपनिपातिनोऽनर्था इति यदुच्यते<BR>तदव्यभिचारि वचः Ś. 6;<BR>इंद्रियार्थसंनिकर्षज्ञानमव्यपदेश्यमव्याभिचारि Gaut. S.<BR>--3<BR>Virtuous, moral, chaste.<BR>--4 Steady,<BR>permanent, faithful (as devotion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यय|अव्ययं|अव्ययः
अव्यय a. [नास्ति व्ययो यस्य]<BR>1 (a)<BR>Not liable to change, imperishable,<BR>undecaying, immutable; वेदाविनाशिनं<BR>नित्यं य एनमजमव्ययं Bg. 2. 21;<BR>विनाशमव्ययस्यास्य न कश्चित्कर्तुमर्हति 17, 4. 1,<BR>6, 13; 7. 24-5; 15. 5, 17; Ms. 1. 18,<BR>19, 57; 2. 81; R. 8. 24. (b) Eternal,<BR>everlasting; अश्वत्थं प्राहुरव्ययं<BR>Bg. 15. 1; अकीर्तिं कथयिष्यंति तेऽव्ययां 2. 34.<BR>--2<BR>Unexpended, unwasted.<BR>--3<BR>Economical.<BR>--4 Giving imperishable fruit.<BR>--यः<BR>1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 N of Śiva.<BR>--यं<BR>1 (In the Vedānta) A member<BR>or corporeal part of an organized<BR>body.<BR>--2 Brahma.<BR>--3 (In gram.)<BR>An indeclinable particle &c.; सदृशं<BR>त्रिषु लिंगेषु सर्वासु च विभक्तिषु । वचनेषु च<BR>सर्वेषु यन्न व्येति तदव्ययम् ॥.<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">Page0199-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--आत्मन् of an imperishable or<BR>eternal nature.<BR>--(त्मा) the soul or<BR>spirit.<BR>--वर्गः the class of<BR>indeclinable words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0198-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययत्वं|अव्ययत्व
अव्ययत्वं Imperishableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्ययीभावः|अव्ययीभाव
अव्ययीभावः [अनव्ययमव्ययं भवत्यनेन;<BR>अव्यय-च्वि-भू करणे घञ्]<BR>1 N. of one of<BR>the four principal kinds of<BR>compounds in Sanskrit, an adverbial<BR>or indeclinable compound (formed<BR>of an indeclinable, i. e. a<BR>preposition or an adverb, and a noun);<BR>अधिहरि, सतृणं &c.<BR>--2 Absence of<BR>expenditure (owing to poverty);<BR>द्वंद्वो द्विगुरपि चाहं मद्गेहे नित्यमव्ययीभावः ।<BR>तत्पुरुष कर्मधारय येनाहं स्यां बहुव्रीहिः ॥<BR>Udb. (which, by the bye, gives the<BR>names of compounds in Sanskrit).<BR>--3 Unchangeable state,<BR>imperishableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यर्थ|अव्यर्थः
अव्यर्थ a.<BR>1 Not useless or<BR>fruitless, fruitful, profitable.<BR>--2<BR>Effectual, successful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यलीक
अव्यलीक a.<BR>1 Not false, true.<BR>--2 Agreeable, having no<BR>disagreeable feelings (प्रिय); इत्थं गिरः<BR>प्रियततमा इव सोऽव्यलीकाः शुश्राव सूततंनयश्च<BR>तदा व्यलीकाः Śi. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवधान
अव्यवधान a.<BR>1 Close,<BR>immediate, without any intervening<BR>object, direct.<BR>--2 Not screened or<BR>concealed, open.<BR>--3 Not covered,<BR>bare (as ground).<BR>--4<BR>Careless, inattentive.<BR>--नं<BR>Carelessness; ˚ता, ˚त्वं contiguity;<BR>carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहित|अव्यवहितं
अव्यवहित a. = अव्यवधान (1) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्थ
अव्यवस्थ a.<BR>1 Not fixed,<BR>moving, unstable;<BR>स्थलारविंदश्रियमव्यवस्थां Ku. 1. 33.<BR>--2 Unlimited.<BR>--3<BR>Unsettled, indiscriminate; भंगं जयं<BR>चापतुरव्यवस्थं R. 7. 54; disorderly,<BR>irregular.<BR>--स्था<BR>1 Irregularity, deviation<BR>from established rule; किमव्यवस्थां<BR>चलितोऽपि केशवः Śi. 12. 36.<BR>--2 An<BR>incorrect opinion given on a point<BR>of religious or civil law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवस्थित|अव्यवस्थितः
अव्यवस्थित a.<BR>1 Not conformable<BR>to law or practice, unacquainted with<BR>the law or custom.<BR>--2<BR>Ill-regulated, fickle, unstable;<BR>अव्यवस्थितचित्तस्य प्रसादोपि भयंकरः Nīti. 9<BR>--3 Not<BR>in due order, unmethodical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यवहार्य|अव्यवहार्य्य|अव्यवहार्य्यं
अव्यवहार्य a.<BR>1 Not entitled<BR>to eat, drink, or commune in general<BR>with people of the same caste,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">Page0199-b+ 56</a>]<BR>excommunicated.<BR>--2 Not to be made<BR>the subject of litigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यसन
अव्यसन a. Free from evil<BR>practices, not vicious, moral.<BR>--नं<BR>Absence of vice, morality, virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यस्त
अव्यस्त a.<BR>1 Undecomposed,<BR>simple.<BR>--2 Not separated, collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याकृत
अव्याकृत a.<BR>1 Not developed,<BR>not manifest; तद्धेदं<BR>तर्ह्यव्याकृतमासीत्, इदं नामरूपाभ्यामव्याकृतं. Ś. B.<BR>--2<BR>Not decomposed, elementary.<BR>--तं<BR>(In Vedānta phil.)<BR>1 An elementary<BR>substance from which all things<BR>were created (considered<BR>identical with Brahma.)<BR>--2 (In Sān. phil.)<BR>The prime germ of nature (प्रधान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्या
अव्याख्या, --ख्यानं Want of<BR>clearness or explanation, obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्यानं|अव्याख्यान
अव्याख्या, --ख्यानं Want of<BR>clearness or explanation, obscurity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्यात
अव्याख्यात a. Unexplained,<BR>obscure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याख्येय
अव्याख्येय a.<BR>1 Inexplicable,<BR>unintelligible.<BR>--2 Not requiring<BR>explanation, easy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याज|अव्याजं|अव्याजः
अव्याज a. Free from guile or<BR>fraud.<BR>--जः, --जं<BR>1 Absence of<BR>guile or fraud, honesty.<BR>--2<BR>Simplicity, artlessness; oft. in comp.<BR>with सुंदर, मनोहर &c. in the sense<BR>of ‘artlessly’, ‘naturally’; इदं<BR>किलाव्याजमनोहरं वपुः Ś. 1. 18; M. 2. 14;<BR>˚रमणीयं प्रेम K. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापक
अव्यापक a.<BR>1 Not<BR>comprehensive.<BR>--2 Not spread over or pervading<BR>the whole; not an invariable<BR>concomitant, special, individual,<BR>peculiar; ˚ता, --˚त्वं<BR>non-comprehensiveness, speciality, individuality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापिन्
अव्यापिन् a.<BR>1 Not comprehensive,<BR>not invariably concomitant, special,<BR>individual.<BR>--2 Partial, limited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्त
अव्याप्त a.<BR>1 Not pervaded, peculiar,<BR>special.<BR>--2 Limited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्तिः|अव्याप्ति
अव्याप्तिः f.<BR>1 Inadequate extent<BR>or pervasion of a proposition.<BR>--2<BR>Non-inclusion or exclusion of a<BR>part of the thing defined, one of<BR>the three faults of a definition;<BR>लक्ष्यैकदेशे लक्षणस्यावर्तनमव्याप्तिः; यथा<BR>शिखासूत्रवान् ब्राह्मणः इत्यस्य संन्यासिन्यव्याप्तिः,<BR>तस्य ब्राह्मणत्वेपि शिखासूत्रत्वाभावात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याप्य|अव्याप्यं
अव्याप्य a. Not extending to the<BR>whole circumstances, not pervading<BR>the whole extent; वह्निर्धूमस्याव्याप्यः.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. (In Vaiś. phil.) a<BR>category of limited application,<BR>partial inherence with regard to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">Page0199-c+ 56</a>]<BR>time or space, as pleasure, pain &c.;<BR>अव्याप्यवृत्तिः क्षणिको विशेषगुण इष्यते<BR>Bhāṣā P. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यापार|अव्यापारः
अव्यापार a. Having no work,<BR>unemployed.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Cessation from<BR>work, state of being unemployed.<BR>--2 A business not practised or<BR>understood.<BR>--3 Not one's own<BR>business; अव्यापारेषु व्यापारं कृ to meddle<BR>with affairs not one's own (which do<BR>not concern one).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यायाम|अव्यायामः
अव्यायाम a. Having no exercise.<BR>--मः Non-exertion, absence of<BR>fatigue from exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्यायत
अव्यायत a. Not occupied; not<BR>detached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्याहत|अव्याहतं
अव्याहत a. Not broken or<BR>interrupted, unobstructed; obeyed;<BR>भर्तुरव्याहताज्ञा R. 19. 57.<BR>--तं A true or<BR>uncontradicted statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्युत्पन्न|अव्युत्पन्नः
अव्युत्पन्न a.<BR>1 Not proficient,<BR>inexperienced, not practised,<BR>ignorant; अव्युत्पन्नो बालभावः K. 196.<BR>--2<BR>Having no proper or regular<BR>derivation (as a word) (अवयवार्थशून्य),<BR>उणादयोऽव्युत्पन्नाः प्रातिपदिकं.<BR>--न्नः A<BR>person not versed in the grammar,<BR>idiom &c. of a language, a<BR>smattering or superficial linguist (<BR>शब्दावयवार्थानभिज्ञोऽवैयाकरणः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रण
अव्रण a. Without wounds or<BR>scars or rents, unhurt, sound.<BR>--णं<BR>One of the four diseases of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रत
अव्रत a. Not observing (the<BR>prescribed) religious rites or<BR>obligations; अव्रतानाममंत्राणां<BR>जातिमात्रोपजीविनामासहस्रशः समेतानां परिषत्त्वं न विद्यते ॥<BR>Ms. 12. 114; 3. 170; 10. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अव्रत्यं|अव्रत्य
अव्रत्यं [व्रताय हितं, यत् न. त.]<BR>Violation of religious duties,<BR>offenceagainst the rule of an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्
अश् {vI.v} {c5c} A. [अश्नुते, आनशे,<BR>आशिष्ट-आष्ट, अशिता-अष्टा,<BR>अशिष्यतेअक्ष्यते, अशितुं-अष्टुं, अशित-अष्ट]<BR>1 To<BR>pervade, fill completely, penetrate;<BR>खं प्रावृषेण्यैरिव चानशेऽब्दैः<BR>Bk. 2. 30; सदिगश्नुवानमिव विश्वमोजसा<BR>Ki. 12. 21; Śi. 17. 46, 65.<BR>--2 To<BR>reach, go or come to, arrive at,<BR>attain to; सर्वमानंत्यमश्नुते Y. 1. 260.<BR>--3 To get, gain, obtain, enjoy,<BR>experience; अत्युत्कटैः पापपुण्यैरिहैव<BR>फलमश्नुते H. 1. 83; उदयमस्तमयं च<BR>रघूद्वहादुभयमानशिरे वसुधाधिपाः<BR>R. 9. 9; न वेदफलमश्नुते Ms. 1. 109; 4. 149;<BR>5. 46; अर्थज्ञ इत्सकलं भद्रमश्नुते Nir.; फलं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-a" target="_blank">Page0200-a+ 57</a>]<BR>दृशोरानशिरे महिष्यः N. 6. 43; Bg. 3. 4;<BR>5. 21; Bk. 3. 37; 5. 14; 14. 19.<BR>--4 To<BR>become master of; to master, to<BR>be able (Ved.).<BR>--5 To heap,<BR>accumulate. WITH अनु {1} to reach, come<BR>up to. {2} to equal.<BR>--आ {1} to reach<BR>to. {2} to obtain, get. {3} to addict<BR>oneself to.<BR>--उद् {1} to reach to the<BR>top of. {2} to reach, obtain, get.<BR>{3} to be master of.<BR>--उप {1} to<BR>obtain, enjoy, acquire; न च<BR>लोकानुपाश्नुते Mb.; क्रियाफलमुपाश्नुते Ms. 6. 82,<BR>12. 20, 81. {2} to become master<BR>of.<BR>--परि to reach, attain; fill<BR>competely, pervade.<BR>--प्र {1} to arrive<BR>at, reach, occupy, fill completely. {2}<BR>to fall to the lot of one (acc.).<BR>{vII.v} {c9c} P. (rarely Ā.) (अश्नाति,<BR>आशीत्, आश, अशिता, अशिष्यति, अशित)<BR>1<BR>To eat, to consume; निवेद्य गुरवेऽ<BR>श्नीयात् Ms. 2. 51; अश्नीमहि वयं<BR>भिक्षां Bh. 3. 117.<BR>--2 To taste,<BR>enjoy; यद्ददाति यदश्नाति तदेव<BR>धनिनो धनं H. 1. 164-165;<BR>अश्नंति दिव्यान् दिवि देवभोगान् Bg. 9. 20;<BR>प्रत्यक्षं फलमश्नंति कर्मणां Mb. --Caus.<BR>(आशयति) To feed, give to eat, cause<BR>to eat or drink (with acc. of<BR>person); आशयच्चामृतं देवान् Sk.;<BR>Ms. 3. 83, 94, 219, 220; (for derivatives<BR>from the causal see under आ).<BR>--WITH अति to precede or surpass<BR>in eating.<BR>--उप to eat; taste, enjoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0199-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशन|अशनं|अशनः
अशन a. [अश्-ल्युट्] Reaching,<BR>reaching across.<BR>--नः N. of a tree = असन<BR>q. v.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Pervasion, penetration.<BR>--2 The act of eating, feeding.<BR>--3<BR>Tasting, enjoying.<BR>--4 Food; अशनं<BR>धात्रा मरुत्कल्पितं व्यालानां Bh. 3. 10;<BR>मांसाशनं च नाश्नीयुः Ms. 5. 73;<BR>यज्ञशिष्ट˚ 3. 118; फलमूलाशनैः 5. 54; oft.<BR>at the end of adjective comp. in<BR>the sense of ‘eating’, ‘one whose food<BR>is’ &c.; फलमूलाशन, हुताशन, पवनाशन &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत् a. Ved. preparing<BR>food.<BR>--पतिः lord of food.<BR>--पर्णी a<BR>kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशना
अशना [अशनमिच्छति अशन-क्यच्<BR>क्विप्] Desire to eat, hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनायति
अशनायति Den. P. To desire food,<BR>to be hungry; P. VII. 4. 34;<BR>यावद्वै पुरुषस्य स्वं भवति नैव तावदशनायति<BR>Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनाया
अशनाया [अशनमिच्छति अशन-क्यच्<BR>स्त्रियां भावे अ] Hunger; च्युताशनायः<BR>फलवद्विभूत्या Bk. 3. 40; अन्नाद्वाऽशनाया<BR>निवर्तते पानात्पिपासा Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनायित|अशनायितं
अशनायित, अशनायुक a. Hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनायुक
अशनायित, अशनायुक a. Hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशित|अशितं
अशित p. p. [अश्-कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>1 Eaten, satisfied.<BR>--2 Enjoyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशितंगवीन|अशितङ्गवीन|अशितङ्गवीनं
अशितंगवीन a. Formerly grazed by<BR>cattle; see आशितंगवीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशितृ
अशितृ a. [अश्-तृच्] An eater,<BR>eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिन्
अशिन् a. [अअ-निनि] Reaching<BR>far; enduring, lasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशकुनः|अशकुन|अशकुनं
अशकुनः --नं An inauspicious or<BR>bad omen; Śi. 9. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशकुनं|अशकुन|अशकुनः
अशकुनः --नं An inauspicious or<BR>bad omen; Śi. 9. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्त|अशक्तं
अशक्त a. Unable, incompetent;<BR>˚ता, --˚त्वं inability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्तिः|अशक्ति
अशक्तिः f.<BR>1 Weakness,<BR>impotence, powerlessness.<BR>--2 Inability,<BR>incapacity; श्रमेण तदशक्त्या वा न<BR>गुणानामियत्तया R. 10. 32.<BR>--3 (In Sān.<BR>phil.) Incapacity of the intellect to<BR>produce knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशक्य|अशक्यं
अशक्य a. Impossible,<BR>impracticable; यदशक्यं न तच्छक्यं H. 1. 90.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. unavailing, useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशंक|अशङ्क
अशंक, अशंकित a.<BR>1 Fearless,<BR>undaunted; प्रविशत्यशंकः H. 1. 81.<BR>--2 Secure, certain, having no doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशंकित|अशङ्कित
अशंक, अशंकित a.<BR>1 Fearless,<BR>undaunted; प्रविशत्यशंकः H. 1. 81.<BR>--2 Secure, certain, having no doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशत्रु|अशत्रुः
अशत्रु a.<BR>1 One who has no enemy.<BR>--2 One whom no enemy defies or<BR>challenges.<BR>--3 Without<BR>opposition from foes.<BR>--त्रु n. The<BR>condition of having no enemies.<BR>--त्रुः<BR>The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशन्
अशन् m. Ved. A stone for<BR>slinging; a stone or cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशनिः|अशनि
अशनिः m. f. [अश्नुते संहति, अश्<BR>अनि Uṇ. 2. 101]<BR>1 Indra's<BR>thunderbolt; शक्रस्य महाशनिध्वजं R. 3. 56.<BR>--2 Flash of lightning;<BR>अनुवनमशनिर्गतः Sk.; अशनिः कल्पित एष वेधसा<BR>R. 8. 47; अशनेरमृतस्य<BR>चोभयोर्वशिनश्चांबुधराश्च योनयः Ku. 4. 43.<BR>--3 A<BR>missile.<BR>--4 The tip of a missile.<BR>--5 A<BR>sacrificial rite (अनुयाज) to kill an<BR>enemy.<BR>--6 A master.<BR>--निः m.<BR>1<BR>Indra.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 Fire produced<BR>from lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशब्द|अशब्दः
अशब्द a. Not expressed in words;<BR>किमर्थमशब्दं रुद्यते K. 60 inaudibly.<BR>--ब्दं<BR>1 The ‘inexpressible,’ i. e.<BR>Brahma.<BR>--2 (In Sān. phil.) प्रधान or<BR>primary germ of nature;<BR>ईक्षतेर्नाशब्दं Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशम्
अशम् ind. Ved. Non-welfare,<BR>harm, mischief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरण
अशरण a. Helpless, forlorn,<BR>destitute of refuge; बलवदशरणोस्मि<BR>Ś. 6; so अशरण्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीर|अशरीरः
अशरीर a. Bodiless,<BR>incorporeal.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The Supreme Being<BR>(परमात्मन्), Brahma.<BR>--2 (In<BR>Mīmāmsā) A god or deity in general.<BR>--3<BR>Cupid, the god of love चेतांसि<BR>चिंताभिरिवाशरीरः Ki. 17. 10: Śi. 9. 61.<BR>--4 An ascetic who has renounced<BR>all worldly connections; ˚त्वं --ता<BR>absolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशरीरिन्
अशरीरिन् a. Incorporeal,<BR>unearthly, heavenly; usually with words<BR>like वाणी, वाक् &c. U. 2, Ve. 3, Ś, {4}<BR>1 Brahmā.<BR>--2 A god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशर्मन्|अशर्म्मन्
अशर्मन् a. Unhappy, afflicted,<BR>sorry. --n. Unhappiness, misery,<BR>affliction, sorrow; एकौघभूतं तदशर्म<BR>कृष्णां (प्रपेदे) Ki. 3. 35; 12. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्
अशस् a. Ved.<BR>1 Not blessing,<BR>not praising.<BR>--2 Cursing, hating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्त
अशस्त a. Ved.<BR>1 Inexpressible,<BR>untold.<BR>--2 Not esteemed, hated,<BR>ill-starred.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वार a. Ved,<BR>who is not asked for wealth, i. e.<BR>who grants it of his own accord;<BR>Rv. 10. 99. 5; having<BR>indescribable treasures(?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्तिः|अशस्ति
अशस्तिः f. Ved.<BR>1 Not wishing<BR>well, an evil wish or design, curse,<BR>imprecation.<BR>--2 A curser, hater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशस्त्र
अशस्त्र a. Having no<BR>weaponsunarmed.<BR>--स्त्रं Not a weapon;<BR>˚विहितो वधः H. 2. 85; ˚पूतं<BR>मरणमुपदिशामि Ve. 2 (आत्मघातित्वेन शस्त्रेण न पूतं);<BR>अशस्त्रपूतं Māl. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशांत|अशान्त
अशांत a.<BR>1 Not quelled,<BR>violent, wild, restless, anxious; नास्ति<BR>बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य अशांतस्य कुतः सुखं Mb.<BR>--2 Not sacred, irreligious, profane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाम्य
अशाम्य a. Unappeasable,<BR>implacable, irreconcilable (as hatred,<BR>enmity &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशारीरिक
अशारीरिक = अशरीरिन् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशाश्वत
अशाश्वत a. Perishable, transient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासन
अशासन a. Having no order or<BR>rule.<BR>--नं Want of government,<BR>anarchy, disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशासनीय
अशासनीय a. Ungovernable,<BR>unruly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्र
अशास्त्र a. Not conformable to<BR>sacred authority, not scriptural,<BR>heterodox.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विहित, --सिद्ध<BR>a. not sanctioned or enjoined by<BR>scriptures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशास्त्रीय
अशास्त्रीय a. Unscriptural,<BR>heterodox; illegal, immoral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0200-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशित्रः|अशित्र
अशित्रः [अश्-संहतौ इत्र<BR>Uṇ. 4. 172]<BR>1 A thief.<BR>--2 An oblation of<BR>rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरः|अशिर|अशिरं
अशिरः [अश्-इरच्]<BR>1 The fire.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--3 Wind.<BR>--4 A demon;<BR>N. of a Rākṣasa.<BR>--रा The wife<BR>of a Rākṣasa.<BR>--रं A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिरस्
अशिरस् a. Headless. --m. A body<BR>without head, a trunk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्नानं bathing the whole body<BR>except the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिव|अशिवः
अशिव a.<BR>1 Inauspicious,<BR>causing or threatening mischief; अशिवा<BR>दिशि दीप्तायां शिवास्तत्र भयावहाः<BR>(रुरुवुः) Rām.<BR>--2 Unlucky,<BR>unfortunate.<BR>--3 Unkind, unfriendly,<BR>envious.<BR>--4 Pernicious, dangerous.<BR>--वः N. of a certain divine being.<BR>--वा A female demon or goblin.<BR>--वं<BR>1 Ill-luck, misfortune.<BR>--2<BR>Mischief.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचारः {1} improper<BR>behaviour, rudeness of conduct. {2}<BR>conduct opposed to every (sacred)<BR>authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिशु|अशिशुः
अशिशु a. Childless, without<BR>young ones.<BR>--शुः A youth.<BR>--श्वी,<BR>अशिश्विका<BR>1 A childless female;<BR>without young ones (as a cow).<BR>--2<BR>A childless woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्ट
अशिष्ट a.<BR>1 Ill-bred,<BR>ill-behaved, rude.<BR>--2 Unrefined, barbarous,<BR>not respectable, unworthy;<BR>˚आलापेन Pt. 4.<BR>--3 Atheistical, profane.<BR>--4 Not sanctioned by any<BR>recognized authority.<BR>--5 Not prescribed<BR>in any work of authority; ˚ता, ˚त्त्वं<BR>rudeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्य
अशिष्य a. Not to be taught,<BR>not to be informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशिष्ठ|अशिष्ठः
अशिष्ठ a.<BR>1 Eating much.<BR>--2<BR>Ved. Reaching very far.<BR>--ष्ठः Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीत|अशीतः
अशीत a. Not cold, hot.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः, --रश्मिः &c. the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिः|अशीति
अशीतिः f. [निपातोयं P. V. 1. 59]<BR>Eighty (used in the singular and<BR>fem. gender whatever be the<BR>number and gender of the noun<BR>it qualifies); sometimes in dual and<BR>pl.; पिंडानां तिस्रोऽशीतीः Ms. 11. 221.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भागः the eightieth<BR>part, one part out of eighty;<BR>Ms. 8. 140.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीतिक
अशीतिक a. [अशीतिः परिमाणं यस्य,<BR>ठन्]<BR>1 An octogenarian, one eighty<BR>years of age.<BR>--2 Measuring eighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशीर्षक
अशीर्षक a. = अशिरस् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशील
अशील a.<BR>1 Ill-behaved, vulgar,<BR>rude.<BR>--2 Indifferent.<BR>--लं Bad<BR>manners, rudeness, depravity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुचि|अशुचिः
अशुचि a.<BR>1 Not clean, dirty,<BR>foul, impure; सोऽशुचिः सर्वकर्मसु;<BR>in mourning; त्रिरात्रमशुचिर्भवेत्.<BR>--2<BR>Black.<BR>--चिः The black colour.<BR>--चिः<BR>f.<BR>1 Impurity.<BR>--2 Degradation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्ध|अशुद्धं
अशुद्ध a.<BR>1 Impure, foul.<BR>--2<BR>Inaccurate, incorrect, wrong.<BR>--3<BR>Unknown, unascertained.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वासकः a vagrant, a suspicious person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुद्धि|अशुद्धिः
अशुद्धि a.<BR>1 Impure, foul.<BR>--2<BR>Wicked.<BR>--द्धिः f. Impurity, foulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोधन
अशोधन, --धित a. Unclean.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Uncleanliness.<BR>--2 Inaccuracy,<BR>incorrectness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोधित
अशोधन, --धित a. Unclean.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Uncleanliness.<BR>--2 Inaccuracy,<BR>incorrectness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुभ|अशुभं
अशुभ a.<BR>1 Inauspicious.<BR>--2<BR>Impure, dirty, foul (opp. शुभ);<BR>शुभेनाशुभेन वोपायेन K. 158 by any<BR>means, fair or foul.<BR>--3 Unlucky,<BR>unfortunate.<BR>--भं<BR>1<BR>Inauspiciousness.<BR>--2 Sin, a shameful deed.<BR>--3<BR>Misfortune, calamity; नाथे<BR>कुतस्त्वय्यशुभं प्रजानां R. 5. 13; प्रायः शुभं<BR>विदधात्यशुभं च जंतोः Māl. 1. 23.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदयः an inauspicious<BR>omen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशुष
अशुष a. Ved.<BR>1 Eating,<BR>consuming, voracious.<BR>--2 [न शुष्यति<BR>शुष्क, न˚ त˚] Not causing to dry up;<BR>Rv. 1. 174. 3.<BR>--3 Not extinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशून्य
अशून्य a.<BR>1 Not empty or vacant;<BR>तस्य निन्यतुरशून्यतामुभे R. 19. 13<BR>occupied.<BR>--2 Not unattended to,<BR>fulfilled, executed; स्वनियोगमशून्यं कुरु<BR>(occurring frequently in dramas),<BR>execute or go about your<BR>business.<BR>--न्यं<BR>1 Not a void.<BR>--2<BR>Something sent to accompany another;<BR>लेखस्याशून्यार्थं किंचिदनुप्रेषितं Mu. 5;<BR>अयं लेखस्याशून्यार्थो भविष्यति ibid. (an<BR>accompaniment such as a customary<BR>present accompanying a letter).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शयनं, --शयनद्वितीया,<BR>--शयनव्रतं N. of a certain ceremony or<BR>vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशूला
अशूला The tree Vitex Alata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशृत|अशृतं
अशृत a. Uncooked, raw, unripe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशृथित
अशृथित a. Ved. Not loosened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेव
अशेव a. [शी-वनिप्-न˚ त˚]<BR>Giving pleasure or happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेष|अशेषं|अशेषः
अशेष a. [न. ब.] Without<BR>remainder, whole, all, entire,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-c" target="_blank">Page0201-c+ 57</a>]<BR>complete, perfect; अशेषशेमुषीमोषं<BR>माषमश्नामि केवलं Udb.; क्रतोरशेषेण फलेन<BR>युज्यतां R. 3. 65, 48.<BR>--षः Non-remainder.<BR>--षं, अशेषेण, अशेषतः ind. Wholly,<BR>entirely, completely;<BR>तथाविधस्तावदशेषमस्तु सः Ku. 5. 82; येन<BR>भूतान्यशेषेण द्रक्ष्यस्यात्मन्यथो मयि Bg. 4. 35,<BR>10. 16; एतद्वोयं भृगुः शास्त्रं<BR>श्रावयिष्यत्यशेषतः Ms. 1. 59, 2. 66, 9. 105.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--साम्राज्यः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेषता
अशेषता Totality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेषयति
अशेषयति Den. P. To finish<BR>completely; स वेद निःशेषमशेषितक्रियः<BR>Ki. 1. 20; Ku. 7. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशेषस्
अशेषस्^1 a. Ved. Without offsprings<BR>or descendents.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशैक्षः|अशैक्ष
अशैक्षः An Arhat (no longer a<BR>pupil).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोक|अशोकं|अशोकः
अशोक a. Without sorrow, not<BR>feeling or causing sorrow.<BR>--कः<BR>1 N.<BR>of a tree having red flowers<BR>(Jonesia Aśoka Roxb.); (said, according<BR>to the convention of poets, to put<BR>forth flowers when struck by ladies<BR>with the foot decked with jingling<BR>anklets; cf. असूत सद्यः कुसुमान्यशोकः…<BR>पादेन नापैक्षत सुंदरीणां संपर्कमाशिंजितनूपुरेण<BR>Ku. 3. 26; Me. 78; R. 8. 62;<BR>M. 3. 12, 16; also<BR>पादाघातादशोकस्तिलककुरबकौ वीक्षणालिंगनाभ्यां स्त्रीणां स्पशांत्<BR>प्रियंगुविंकसति बकुलः सीधुगंडूषसेकात् । मंदारो<BR>नर्मवाक्यात् पटुमृटुहसनाच्चंपको वक्त्रवातात्<BR>चूतो गीतान्नमेरुविंकसति च पुरो<BR>नर्तनात्कर्णिकारः).<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a minister of king Daśaratha.<BR>--4 N. of a celebrated king of the<BR>Maurya dynasty, said to have reigned<BR>from 234-198 B. C.<BR>--5 N. of the tree<BR>बकुल.<BR>--कं<BR>1 N. of a medical plant<BR>(कटुक).<BR>--2 The sixth day in the<BR>first half of Chaitra.<BR>--3 One of the<BR>female domestic deities of the<BR>Jainas.<BR>--का<BR>1 Quicksilver.<BR>--2 The<BR>blossom of the Aśoka plant<BR>(forming one of the five arrows of<BR>Cupid).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः the कदंब<BR>tree.<BR>--अष्टमी [नास्ति शोको यस्याः कर्म˚]<BR>the eighth day in the first half of<BR>Chaitra.<BR>--तरुः, --नगः, --वृक्षः the<BR>Aśoka tree.<BR>--तीर्थं a holy place named<BR>Aśoka near Benares.<BR>--त्रिरात्रः, --त्रं N.<BR>of a festival or व्रत which lasts for<BR>three nights; अस्त्यशोकत्रिरात्राख्यं<BR>व्रतं शोकभयापहं । त्रिरात्रं तच्च कर्तव्यं व्रतं<BR>शोकविनाशनं ॥.<BR>--पूर्णिमा N. of a certain<BR>holiday, a ceremony to be observed on<BR>the 15th day of the month of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">Page0202-a+ 55</a>]<BR>Phālguna.<BR>--मंजरी N. of a metre.<BR>--रोहिणी<BR>N. of a medical plant (कटुका).<BR>--वनिका<BR>a grove of Aśoka trees; ˚न्याय see<BR>under न्याय.<BR>--षष्ठी N. of a certain<BR>holiday; चैत्रे मास्यसिते पक्षे षष्ठ्यां षष्ठीं<BR>प्रपूजयेत् । सुखाय पुत्रलाभाय शुक्लपक्षे तथैव च ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0201-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोचः|अशोच
अशोचः<BR>1 Absence of care or<BR>anxiety.<BR>--2 Tranquility, calmness.<BR>--3 Modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशोच्य|अशोच्यं
अशोच्य a. Not to be lamented<BR>or deplored; अशोच्यानन्वशोचस्त्वं<BR>प्रज्ञावादांश्च भाषसे Bg. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अशौचं|अशौच
अशौचं<BR>1 Impurity, dirtiness,<BR>foulness; Pt. 1. 195.<BR>--2 Legal impurity<BR>or contamination; defilement<BR>caused either by child-birth (called<BR>जननाशौच) or by the death of some<BR>relation (called मृताशौच); it lasts for<BR>10 days; during the मृताशौच a person<BR>defiled by it is not to touch any body<BR>else, or to eat with others in the<BR>same row or to do any sacred action;<BR>अहोरात्रमुपासीरन्नशौचं बांधवैः सह<BR>Ms. 11. 184.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः end of<BR>defilement.<BR>--संकरः blending or<BR>coming together of two or more<BR>defilements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्न|अश्नः
अश्न a. [अश्नुते व्याप्नोति अश्नाति वा,<BR>अश-नन्]<BR>1 Pervading.<BR>--2 Eating,<BR>voracious.<BR>--3 Pervaded, filled.<BR>--श्नः<BR>1 N. of a demon.<BR>--2 A cloud (Nir.).<BR>--3 A stone to grind Soma on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्नया
अश्नया Hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्नीतपिबता
अश्नीतपिबता [अश्नीत विबत इत्युच्यते<BR>यस्यां निदेशक्रियायां, सयू˚ स˚] Invitation<BR>to eat and drink, a feast where<BR>people are called to eat and drink;<BR>अश्नीतपिबतीयंती प्रसृता स्मरकर्मणि<BR>Bk. 5. 92.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मः|अश्म
अश्मः<BR>1 A mountain, a rock (at<BR>the end of comp.).<BR>--2 (Ved.) A<BR>cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मकः|अश्मक
अश्मकः [अश्मेव स्थिरः, इवार्थे कन्]<BR>1 N. of a sage.<BR>--2 N. of a country<BR>in the south; तथाश्मकाः पुलिंदाश्च<BR>कलिंगाश्च विशेषतः Rām.; (probably<BR>an old name of Travancore);<BR>according to Bṛ. S. 14. 22 it is in<BR>the north-west.<BR>--3 The inhabitants<BR>of the country (pl.).<BR>--4 A part of<BR>the साल्व country or its inhabitants;<BR>or its king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मन्
अश्मन् a. Ved. Eating or<BR>pervading. --m. [अश्नुते व्याप्नोति संहंत्यनेन<BR>बा˚ मनिन् Uṇ. 4. 146]<BR>1 A stone;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-b" target="_blank">Page0202-b+ 56</a>]<BR>नाराचक्षेपणीयाश्मनिष्पेषोत्पतितानलं<BR>R. 4. 77.<BR>--2 A hard stone, rock.<BR>--3 Flint.<BR>--4 A cloud.<BR>--5 A thunderbolt.<BR>--6<BR>A mountain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्य a.<BR>having a stone-mouth or source,<BR>flowing from a rock.<BR>--उत्थं<BR>bitumen.<BR>--कदली N. of a plant, a<BR>kind of कदली.<BR>--कुट्ट, --कुट्टक a. {1}<BR>breaking anything on stones.<BR>{2} broken by a stone.<BR>--(ट्टः, --ट्टकः)<BR>a class of devotees; a वानप्रस्थ;<BR>Y. 3. 49; Ms. 6. 17.<BR>--केतुः [अश्मेव केतुर्यस्य]<BR>N. of a plant.<BR>--गंधा N. of a plant.<BR>--गर्भः, --र्भं, --गर्भजः, --जं, --योनिः an<BR>emerald.<BR>--गर्भजः fire produced from<BR>a flint.<BR>--गुडः --डा a kind of weapon.<BR>--घ्नः N. of a tree.<BR>--चक्र a.<BR>furnished with a disc of stone.<BR>--जः,<BR>--जं {1} red-chalk. {2} iron.<BR>--जतु n.,<BR>--जतुकं bitumen.<BR>--जातिः an emerald<BR>named पान्ना.<BR>--दारणः an axe or crow<BR>for breaking stones.<BR>--(णं) breaking<BR>stones or rocks.<BR>--दिद्यु a. one who<BR>has obtained a stony weapon,<BR>having adamantine weapons or grasped<BR>weapons (व्याप्तायुध, अश्ममयायुध).<BR>--पुष्पं bitumen, benzoin.<BR>--भालं a<BR>mortar of stone or iron.<BR>--भिद्, --भेदः,<BR>--भेदकः the plant Coleus<BR>Scutellarioides (supposed to dissolve<BR>stone in the bladder.).<BR>--रथः<BR>N. of a sage.<BR>--व्रज a.<BR>included in rocks.<BR>--सार a. like<BR>iron or stone.<BR>--(रः, --रं) {1} iron; प्राणाः<BR>सत्वरमश्मसारकठिना गच्छंति गच्छंत्वमी<BR>S. D. {2} sapphire. ˚मय a. made of<BR>iron.<BR>--हन्मन् n. {1} a weapon of iron;<BR>Rv. 7. 104. 5. {2} a stroke of the<BR>thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्ममय
अश्ममय, अश्मवत् a. Stony, made<BR>of stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मवत्|अश्मवन्त्
अश्ममय, अश्मवत् a. Stony, made<BR>of stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मर|अश्मरः
अश्मर a. [अश्मन्-र]<BR>1 Stony, rocky.<BR>--2 Pertaining to stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मरी
अश्मरी [अश्मानं राति रा-क गौरा˚ ङीष्]<BR>(In medicine) A disease called<BR>stone (in the bladder), gravel,<BR>strangury.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--घ्नः N. of the tree<BR>वरुण (used as a lithontriptic).<BR>--भेदनं a lithontriptic.<BR>--हरः N. of the<BR>tree Pentaptera Arjuna, used as a<BR>lithontriptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मीरः|अश्मीर|अश्मीरं
अश्मीरः --रं Stone or gravel (the<BR>disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मीरं|अश्मीर|अश्मीरः
अश्मीरः --रं Stone or gravel (the<BR>disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मंत|अश्मन्त|अश्मन्तं|अश्मन्तः
अश्मंत a.<BR>1 Inauspicious.,<BR>unlucky (अशुभ).<BR>--2 Unlimited.<BR>--तः<BR>N. of a Marut.<BR>--तं [अश्मनोंऽतोऽत्र<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">Page0202-c+ 56</a>]<BR>शकं˚ पररूपम्]<BR>1 A fireplace.<BR>--2 A<BR>field, plain.<BR>--3 Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मंतकः|अश्मन्तक|अश्मंतकं|अश्मन्तकं|अश्मन्तकः
अश्मंतकः --कं<BR>1 A fireplace.<BR>--2<BR>The shade for a lamp (दीपाधार).<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of grass.<BR>--कः N. of several<BR>trees:--(a) अम्लोटक; its leaf;<BR>Māl. 9. 7; (b) N. of a tree कोविदारक; (c) N.<BR>of a plant from the fibres of which<BR>a Brāhmaṇa's girdle may be made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मंतकं|अश्मन्तक|अश्मन्तकं|अश्मंतकः|अश्मन्तकः
अश्मंतकः --कं<BR>1 A fireplace.<BR>--2<BR>The shade for a lamp (दीपाधार).<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of grass.<BR>--कः N. of several<BR>trees:--(a) अम्लोटक; its leaf;<BR>Māl. 9. 7; (b) N. of a tree कोविदारक; (c) N.<BR>of a plant from the fibres of which<BR>a Brāhmaṇa's girdle may be made.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रः|अश्र|अश्रं
अश्रः A corner, mostly at the end<BR>of comp.; चतुरश्र, त्र्यश्र &c.<BR>--श्रं [<BR>अश्नुते नेत्रं, अश्-रक्]<BR>1 A tear.<BR>--2<BR>Blood (usually written अस्र q. v.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पः a blood-drinker, a<BR>fiend, cannibal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रिन्
अश्रिन् a. Having tears, in tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्ध
अश्रद्ध a. Without faith,<BR>unbelieving, diffident.<BR>--द्धा Unbelief,<BR>diffidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्दधान|अश्रद्दधानः
अश्रद्दधान a. Unbelieving,<BR>incredulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रद्धेय|अश्रद्धेयं
अश्रद्धेय a. Not to be believed,<BR>incredible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रम|अश्रमः
अश्रम a. Ved. Indefatigable,<BR>untiring.<BR>--मः<BR>1 Freedom from fatigue,<BR>freshness, vigour.<BR>--2 Absence of<BR>toil, laziness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रमण|अश्रमणः
अश्रमण a. Indefatigable.<BR>--णः<BR>One who is not an ascetic or<BR>Buddhist mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रांत|अश्रान्त|अश्रान्तं|अश्रान्तः
अश्रांत a.<BR>1 Unwearied, not<BR>fatigued, untired.<BR>--2 Incessant,<BR>continual; अश्रांतपुण्यकर्माणः<BR>Mv. 1. 26.<BR>--तं Absence of rest.<BR>--तं ind.<BR>Incessantly, continually;<BR>मयूखैरश्रांतं तपति यदि देवो दिनकरः U. 6. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रवण|अश्रवणः
अश्रवण a. Deaf, having no ears.<BR>--णः A snake.<BR>--णं Loss of hearing,<BR>deafness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्राव्य
अश्राव्य a.<BR>1 Not to be heard.<BR>--2<BR>Unfit to be heard, not be spoken of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रातस्
अश्रातस् ind. Ved. In an<BR>uncooked manner, raw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्राद्ध|अश्राद्धः
अश्राद्ध a. Not performing the<BR>Śrāddha ceremony; not entitled to<BR>it, not belonging or relating to it.<BR>--द्धः Non-performance of a Śrāddha<BR>q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भोजिन् a. one who has<BR>vowed not to eat during the<BR>performance of a Śrāddha ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रिः|अश्रि
अश्रिः --श्री f. [अश्यते संहन्यते अनया<BR>अश् वंक्र्यादि˚ क्रि; cf. Uṇ. 4. 137]<BR>1 A<BR>corner, angle (of a room, house &c.)<BR>(changed to अश्र at the end of<BR>comp. with चतुर्, त्रि, षट् and a few<BR>other words; see चतुरस्र);<BR>--अष्टाश्रिर्वै<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">Page0203-a+ 56</a>]<BR>वज्रः Ait. Br.<BR>--2 The sharp side<BR>or edge (of a weapon &c.); वृत्रस्य<BR>हंतुः कुलिशं कुंठिताश्रीव लक्ष्यते<BR>Ku. 2. 20.<BR>--3 The sharp side of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्री
अश्रिः --श्री f. [अश्यते संहन्यते अनया<BR>अश् वंक्र्यादि˚ क्रि; cf. Uṇ. 4. 137]<BR>1 A<BR>corner, angle (of a room, house &c.)<BR>(changed to अश्र at the end of<BR>comp. with चतुर्, त्रि, षट् and a few<BR>other words; see चतुरस्र);<BR>--अष्टाश्रिर्वै<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">Page0203-a+ 56</a>]<BR>वज्रः Ait. Br.<BR>--2 The sharp side<BR>or edge (of a weapon &c.); वृत्रस्य<BR>हंतुः कुलिशं कुंठिताश्रीव लक्ष्यते<BR>Ku. 2. 20.<BR>--3 The sharp side of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0202-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रिमत्|अश्रिमन्त्
अश्रिमत् a. Cornered, angular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रित
अश्रित a. Ved. Difficult of access.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीक
अश्रीक a.<BR>1 Having no<BR>splendour, without beauty, pale;<BR>Śi. 15. 96.<BR>--2 Unlucky, unpropitious, not<BR>prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीमत्|अश्रीमन्त्
अश्रीमत् a. Unfortunate, unlucky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रीर
अश्रीर [न श्रीः अश्रीः अस्त्यर्थ˚ र] Ved.<BR>1 Ugly, ill-looking; Rv. 8. 2. 20.<BR>--2<BR>Inauspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रील
अश्रील = अश्रीक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रु
अश्रु n. [अश्नुते व्याप्नोति नेत्रमदर्शनाय,<BR>अश्-क्रुन् Uṇ. 5. 29, 2. 13, 4. 102]<BR>A tear; पपात भूमौ सह सैनिकाश्रुभिः<BR>R. 3. 61. [cf. Zend asru; Pers. ars.].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपहत a. affected by<BR>tears, covered with tears.<BR>--कला a<BR>tear-drop.<BR>--नाली Fistula<BR>Lachrymalis.<BR>--परिपूर्ण a. filled with tears;<BR>˚अक्ष having eyes filled with tears.<BR>--परिप्लुत a. suffused or filled with<BR>tears, bathed in tears.<BR>--पातः flow<BR>of tears, shedding tears.<BR>--पूर्ण a.<BR>filled with tears; ˚आकुल troubled<BR>and filled with tears; Bg. 2. 1.<BR>--मुख a. suffused with tears,<BR>(suddenly) bursting into tears;<BR>एकपदेऽश्रुमुखी संवृत्ता V. 5; संसदश्रुमुखी बभौ<BR>R. 15. 66; Ku. 6. 92.<BR>--लोचन, --नेत्र<BR>a. with tears in the eyes, with<BR>tearful eyes.<BR>--शालिन् a. having tears,<BR>tearful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुत|अश्रुतं
अश्रुत a.<BR>1 Unheard,<BR>inaudible.<BR>--2 Contrary to the Vedas.<BR>--3<BR>Not acquainted with the Śāstras,<BR>foolish, uneducated; भागं<BR>विद्याधनात्तस्मात् स लभेताश्रुतोऽपि सन् Dāy. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रौत
अश्रौत a. Not sanctioned by the<BR>Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रुति|अश्रुतिः
अश्रुति a. Without ears.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>Not hearing, forgetfulness;<BR>अश्रुतिमभिनीय U. 3.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धर a. {1} not<BR>striking the ear or attention. {2}<BR>not knowing the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेयस्
अश्रेयस् a.<BR>1 Not better, inferior,<BR>worse; Ms. 10. 64.<BR>--2 Worthless,<BR>useless. --n. (स्) Mischief,<BR>unhappiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्रेष्ठ
अश्रेष्ठ a. Not the best, inferior,<BR>worse; bad, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लाघा
अश्लाघा Absence of self-praise,<BR>modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लाघ्य
अश्लाघ्य a.<BR>1 Undeserving of<BR>praise or honour, worthless.<BR>--2<BR>Base, mean, censurable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लीक
अश्लीक a. Unlucky,<BR>unpropitious; Ms. 4. 206.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लील
अश्लील a. [न श्रियं लाति, ला-क]<BR>1<BR>Unpleasant, ugly.<BR>--2 Vulgar,<BR>obscene, coarse; अश्लीलप्रायान् कलकलान्<BR>Dk. 49; ˚परिवार Y. 1. 33.<BR>--3<BR>Abusive.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Rustic or coarse<BR>language, low abuse.<BR>--2 (In Rhet.) A<BR>fault of composition; using such<BR>words as produce in the mind of<BR>the hearer a feeling of shame,<BR>disgust or inauspiciousness; त्रिधा<BR>अश्लीलं; त्रिधेति व्रीडाजुगुप्सामंगलव्यंजकत्वात्<BR>K. P. 7; e. g. in साधनं सुमहद्यस्य, मुग्धा<BR>कुट्मलिताननेन दधती वायुं स्थिता तत्र सा, and<BR>मृदुपवनविभिन्नो मत्प्रियाया विनाशात्, the<BR>words साधन, वायु and विनाश are अश्लील,<BR>and produce respectively a sense of<BR>shame, disgust and inauspiciousness,<BR>साधन suggesting the sense of लिंग<BR>(male organ of generation), वायु, of<BR>the अपान wind (that escaping at<BR>the anus), and विनाश, of मृत्यु (death);<BR>cf. the instances under S. D. 574;<BR>दृप्तारिविजये राजन् साधनं सुमहत्तव । प्रससार<BR>शनैर्वायुविंनाशे तन्वि ते तदा ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लेषा
अश्लेषा [न श्लिष्यति यत्रोत्पन्नेन शिशुना,<BR>श्लिष्-घञ् Tv.]<BR>1 The 9th Nakṣatra<BR>or lunar mansion containing five<BR>stars.<BR>--2 Disunion, disjunction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः, --भवः, --भूः N. of<BR>Ketu, i. e. the descending node.<BR>--शांतिः f. an expiatory ceremony<BR>performed on account of the birth<BR>of a child under the Aśleṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्लोन
अश्लोन a. Ved. Not lame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वः|अश्व
अश्वः [अश्नुते अध्वानं व्याप्नोति,<BR>महाशनो वा भवति Nir.; अश्-क्वन् Uṇ. 1. 149]<BR>1<BR>A horse; the horses are said to have<BR>{7} breeds: --अमृताद्बाष्पतो वह्रेर्वेदेभ्योंऽडाच्च<BR>गर्भतः । साम्नो हयानामुत्पत्तिः सप्तधा परिकीर्तिता ॥.<BR>--2 A symbolical expression for the<BR>number ‘seven’ (that being the<BR>number of the horses of the sun);<BR>सूर्याश्वैर्मसजस्तताः सगुरवः<BR>शार्दूलविक्रीडितं V. Ratn.<BR>--3 A race of men<BR>(horselike in strength); काष्ठतुल्यवपुर्धृष्यो<BR>मिथ्याचारश्च निर्भयः । द्वादशांगुलमेढ्रश्च<BR>दरिद्रस्तु हयो मतः ॥<BR>--श्वौ (du.) A horse and<BR>a mare. [cf. L. equus; Gr. hippos;<BR>Zend aspa; Pers. asp.]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः N. of a plant देवसर्षप.<BR>--अजनी a whip.<BR>--अधिक a. strong in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-c" target="_blank">Page0203-c+ 58</a>]<BR>cavalry, superior in horses.<BR>--अध्यक्षः<BR>a guardian of horses, commander of<BR>cavalry.<BR>--अनीकं a troop of horse<BR>men, cavalry.<BR>--अरिः a buffalo.<BR>--अवरोहकः N. of a tree अश्वगंधा.<BR>--आयुर्वेदः veterinary science.<BR>--आरूढ a.<BR>mounted, sitting on horse-back.<BR>--आरोह a. riding or mounted on<BR>a horse.<BR>--(हः) {1} a horseman, rider.<BR>{2} one who is fighting. {3} a ride.<BR>(--हा), --आरोहकः N. of the plant<BR>अश्वगंधा.<BR>--आरोहिन् a. mounted or<BR>riding on horseback.<BR>--इषित a.<BR>hurried along by horses.<BR>--उरस<BR>a. broad-chested like a horse.<BR>--(सं)<BR>the chief or principal horse.<BR>--कंदा,<BR>--कंदिका N. of a plant अश्वगंधा.<BR>--कर्णः, --कर्णकः {1} a kind of tree<BR>(Vatica Robusta) Māl. 9. {2}<BR>the ear of a horse. {3} a term in<BR>surgery for a particular fracture of<BR>the bones.<BR>--(र्णः) N. of a mountain.<BR>--कुटी a stable for horses; Pt. 5.<BR>--कुशल, --कोविद a. skilled in<BR>managing horses.<BR>--क्रंदः {1} N. of a bird.<BR>{2} a general of the army of the gods.<BR>--खरजः [अश्वश्च खरीच अश्वाच खरश्च वा<BR>ताभ्यां जायते पुंवद्भावः Tv.] a kind of horse,<BR>mule.<BR>--खुरः {1} a horse's hoof. {2}<BR>a kind of perfume.<BR>--(रा) N. of the<BR>plant अपराजिता.<BR>--गतिः f. {1} the<BR>pace of a horse. {2} N. of a metre<BR>containing four lines of sixteen<BR>syllables in each.<BR>--गंधा [अश्वस्य गंध<BR>एकदेशो मेढ्रमिव मूलमस्याः] N. of a plant<BR>Physalis Flexuosa Lin; ˚तैलं a kind<BR>of oil.<BR>--गोयुगः, --गं a pair of horses.<BR>--गोष्ठं a stable.<BR>--ग्रीवः {1} N. of a<BR>demon who was a foe of Viṣṇu,<BR>more commonly called Haya-grīva.<BR>{2} an incarnation of Viṣṇu.<BR>--घासः<BR>a pasture for horses.<BR>--घ्नः [अश्वं हंति<BR>अमनुष्यकर्तृकत्वात्] {1} a horse-bane. {2}<BR>N. of a kind of Oleander, Nerium<BR>Odorum Ait.<BR>--चक्रं {1} a collection of<BR>horses. {2} a kind of wheel.<BR>--चलनशाला a riding-house.<BR>--चिकित्सकः --वैद्यः a<BR>farrier, a veterinary surgeon.<BR>--चिकित्सा farriery, veterinary science.<BR>--चेष्टितं {1} the motion of horses.<BR>{2} an omen, auspicious or<BR>inauspicious.<BR>--जघनः a kind of centaur;<BR>a creature having his lower limbs<BR>like those of a horse.<BR>--जित् a.<BR>gaining horses by conquest.<BR>--तीर्थं<BR>N. of a place of pilgrimage near<BR>Kānyakubja on the Gaṅgā.<BR>--द a.<BR>giving horses.<BR>--दंष्ट्रा the plant<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0204-a" target="_blank">Page0204-a+ 60</a>]<BR>Tribulus Lanuginosus (गोक्षुर).<BR>--दाः,<BR>--दावन् m. giving horses.<BR>--दूतः a<BR>riding messenger.<BR>--नदी N. of a<BR>river.<BR>--नायः one who has the charge<BR>of a drove of grazing horses; a<BR>horseherd.<BR>--निबंधिकः a groom, a<BR>horsefastener.<BR>--निर्णिज् a. Ved. decorated<BR>or embellished with horses.<BR>--पः<BR>Ved. a groom.<BR>--पतिः {1} lord of<BR>horses. {2} N. of several persons;<BR>of a king of Madra and father of<BR>Sāvitrī.<BR>--पर्ण a. [अश्वानां पर्णं गमनं<BR>यत्र] {1} having horses (as a<BR>chariot); Rv. 1. 88. 1. {2} a cloud<BR>(that penetrates everywhere).<BR>--पालः, --पालकः, --रक्षः a horse-groom.<BR>--पुच्छी N. of the tree माषपणीं.<BR>--पृष्ठं<BR>horse-back.<BR>--पेशस् a. decorated or<BR>embellished with horses.<BR>--बंधः a<BR>groom.<BR>--बंधन a. used for<BR>fastening horses.<BR>--(नं) fastening of horses.<BR>--बला N. of a vegetable.<BR>--बालः<BR>{1} a kind of reed, Saccharum<BR>Spontaneum Lin. {2} the tail or<BR>hair of a horse.<BR>--बुध्न a. Ved.<BR>based on horses, standing on<BR>horses, i. e. on a carriage drawn by<BR>horses.<BR>--बुध्य a. Ved. based on<BR>horses, having its origin in horses<BR>(wealth); distinguished by horses.<BR>--भा lightning.<BR>--महिषिका [<BR>अश्वमहिषयोर्वैरं वुन्] the natural enmity<BR>between a horse and a buffalo.<BR>--मारः,<BR>--मारकः, --हंतृ m.<BR>‘horse-destroying,’ a kind of Oleander, Nerium<BR>Odorum Ait.<BR>--मालः a kind of<BR>serpent.<BR>--मुख a. [अश्वस्य मुखमिव<BR>मुखमस्य] having the head or face of<BR>a horse.<BR>--(खः) a horse-faced<BR>creature, a Kinnara or celestial<BR>chorister; (according to others) a kind<BR>of demigod distinct from the<BR>preceding.<BR>--(खी) a Kinnara woman;<BR>भिंदंति मंदां गतिमश्वमुख्यः Ku. 1. 11.<BR>--मुक् m. a horse-stealer.<BR>--मेधः [अश्वः<BR>प्रधानतया मेध्यते हिंस्यतेऽत्र, मेध् हिंसने<BR>घञ्] a horse-sacrifice; यथाश्वमेधः<BR>क्रतुराट् सर्वपापापनोदनः Ms. 11. 261.<BR>[In Vedic times this sacrifice was<BR>performed by kings desirous of offspring; but<BR>subsequently it was performed only by<BR>kings and implied that he who<BR>instituted it was a conqueror and king of kings.<BR>A horse was turned loose to wander at<BR>will for a year, attended by a guardian;<BR>when the horse entered a foreign country,<BR>the ruler was bound either to submit or<BR>to fight. In this way the horse returned<BR>at the end of a year, the guardian<BR>obtaining or enforcing the submission of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0204-b" target="_blank">Page0204-b+ 59</a>]<BR>princes whom he brought in his train.<BR>After the successful return of the horse,<BR>the rite called Aśvamedha was<BR>performed amidst great rejoicings. It was<BR>believed that the performance of 100 such<BR>sacrifices would lead to the attainment of the<BR>seat or world of Indra, who is, therefore,<BR>always represented as trying to prevent<BR>the completion of the hundredth sacrifice].<BR>˚कांडं N. of the thirteenth book of<BR>the Śatapatha Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--मेधिक,<BR>--मेधीय a. fit for a horse-sacrifice, or<BR>relating to it.<BR>--(कः, --यः) a horse fit<BR>for the Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR>--(कं) the<BR>fourteenth parvan in the<BR>Mahābhārata; ततोऽश्वमेधिकं पर्व प्रोक्तं तच्च चतुर्दशं<BR>Mb.<BR>--युज् a. {1} yoking the horses.<BR>{2} having horses yoked to it (as a<BR>carriage); रथेनाश्वयुजा Rām. {3} born<BR>under the constellation अश्वयुज्. (--f.)<BR>{1} N. of a constellation, the head of<BR>Aries. {2} the first lunar mansion.<BR>{3} the month of Āśvina. {4} a<BR>chariot having horses.<BR>--यूपः the<BR>post to which the sacrificial horse<BR>was bound.<BR>--योग a. {1} causing the<BR>yoking of horses. {2} joining or<BR>reaching as quickly as horses.<BR>--रक्षः<BR>the keeper or rider of a horse, a<BR>groom.<BR>--रथः a carriage drawn by<BR>horses.<BR>--(था) N. of a river near<BR>गंधमादन.<BR>--रत्नं, --राजः the best or lord<BR>of horses; i. e. उच्चैःश्रवस्.<BR>--राधस् a.<BR>Ved. furnishing horses.<BR>--रोधकः<BR>N. of a plant (अश्वमार).<BR>--लक्षणं a sign or mark of a horse.<BR>--ललितं N. of a species of the<BR>Vikṛti metre.<BR>--लाला a kind of snake.<BR>--लोमन् n. horse-hair; a kind of snake.<BR>--वक्त्रः = अश्वमुख q. v.; a Kinnara or<BR>Gandharva.<BR>--वडवं a stud of horses<BR>and mares.<BR>--(वौ) a horse and a<BR>mare.<BR>--(वाः) horses and mares.<BR>--वदनः = ˚मुख.<BR>--वहः a horseman.<BR>--वारः<BR>--वालः, --वारकः [अश्वं वारयति उप. स.]<BR>a horseman, groom; दुःखेन<BR>निश्चक्रमुरश्ववाराः Śi. 3. 66.<BR>--वारणं N. of<BR>the Bos Gavæus (गवय).<BR>--वाहः,<BR>--वाहकः [अश्वं वाहयति चालयति] a<BR>horseman.<BR>--विक्रयिन् a. a horse-dealer.<BR>--विद् a. {1} skilled in taming or<BR>managing horses. {2} [अश्वं विंदते<BR>विद्-क्विप्] procuring horses. (--m.) {1} a<BR>jockey. {2} an epithet of Nala.<BR>--वृषः<BR>a stallion.<BR>--वैद्यः a farrier.<BR>--शकृत् n.,<BR>--शकं Ved. {1} excrements of a horse,<BR>horse-dung. {2} N. of a river.<BR>--शंकुः<BR>a pillar to tie a horse.<BR>--शाला a stable.<BR>--शावः a colt, a foal.<BR>--शास्त्रं a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0204-c" target="_blank">Page0204-c+ 57</a>]<BR>manual or text-book of veterinary<BR>science.<BR>--शिरस् a. having the head of a<BR>horse, an epithet of Nārāyaṇa. (--n.)<BR>{1} a horse's head. {2} N. of a<BR>Dānava.<BR>--शृगालिका [अश्वशृगालयोर्वैरं द्वंद्वात्<BR>वैरे वुन्] the natural enmity between<BR>a horse and a jackal.<BR>--षड्गवं a set<BR>or team of six horses.<BR>--सनि, --षा,<BR>--सा a. Ved. (P. VIII. 3. 110 and<BR>Mbh.) gaining or procuring horses,<BR>giving horses.<BR>--सादः, --सादिन् m. a<BR>horseman, a rider, a horse-soldier;<BR>R. 7. 47.<BR>--सारथ्यं coachmanship,<BR>charioteership, management of horses<BR>and chariots; सूतानामश्वसारथ्यं<BR>Ms. 10. 47.<BR>--सूनृत a. Ved. {1} praised<BR>sincerely for (the gift of) horses.<BR>{2} whose praise for (giving) horses<BR>is agreeable and true.<BR>--सेनः {1} N.<BR>of a king. {2} N. of a Nāga.<BR>--स्तोमीय a. relating to the praise of the<BR>sacrificial horse.<BR>--स्थान a. born in<BR>a stable.<BR>--(नं) a stable or stall for<BR>horses.<BR>--हंतृ a. killing a horse.<BR>--(ता)<BR>N. of a fragrant plant.<BR>--हय a. [अश्वेन<BR>हिनोति गच्छति हि कर्तरि अच्] {1} driving<BR>or spurring a horse, riding a horse;<BR>Rv. 10. 26. 5. {2} to be traversed<BR>by a horse; Rv. 9. 96. 2.<BR>--हरकः<BR>a horse-stealer.<BR>--हृदयं [अश्वस्य हृदयं<BR>मनोगतभावादि] {1} the desire or<BR>intention of a horse. {2} a kind of<BR>veterinary science. {3} horsemanship;<BR>अश्वहृदये निवेश्यात्मानं K. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0203-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वा
अश्वा A mare.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मघ a.<BR>rich in horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0204-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वक|अश्वकः
अश्वक a. Horselike, acting like<BR>a horse.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A small horse;<BR>horse.<BR>--2 A hack, a bad horse.<BR>--3<BR>A stray horse, one whose owner<BR>is not known.<BR>--4 A horse (in<BR>general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0204-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

