अश्विक a. [P. IV. 4. 10.] Drawn<BR>or carried by horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विन्
अश्विन् a. [अश्व-अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>Possessed of horses, consisting of horses;<BR>Rv. 4. 2. 5. --m. A cavalier, a horse-tamer.<BR>--नौ (du.)<BR>1 The two physicians of<BR>the gods who are represented as the<BR>twin sons of the sun by a nymph<BR>in the form of a mare; cf. त्वाष्ट्री तु<BR>सवितुर्भार्या वडवारूपधारिणी ॥ असूयत<BR>महाभागा सांतरीक्षेऽश्विनावुभौ ॥. [According to<BR>Vedic conception they are the<BR>harbingers of Uṣas or the dawn; they are<BR>young, beautiful, bright, swift &c.; and,<BR>according to Yāska, they represent the<BR>transition from darkness to light, when<BR>the intermingling of both produces that<BR>inseparable duality expressed by the twin<BR>nature of these deities; according to<BR>different interpretations quoted in the<BR>Nirukta they were ‘heaven and earth’,<BR>‘day and night’, ‘two kings,<BR>performers of holy acts’ which may be traced<BR>to their dual and luminous nature.<BR>Mythically they were the parents of Nakula<BR>and Sahadeva and the physicians of the<BR>gods and are called Gadāgadau,<BR>Svarvaidyau, Dasrau, Nāsatyau, Vādaveyau,<BR>Abdhijau &c. They were celebrated for<BR>their active benevolence and curative<BR>power which they showed in restoring<BR>the sage Cyavana, when grown<BR>old and decrepit, to youth, and prolonged<BR>his life.].<BR>--2 Two horses.<BR>--3 (In<BR>astr.) The twins of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विनी
अश्विनी [अश्वस्तदुत्तमांगाकारोऽस्त्यस्य<BR>इनि ङीप्]<BR>1 The first of the 27<BR>Nakṣatras or lunar mansions<BR>(consisting of three stars).<BR>--2 A nymph<BR>considered in later times as the<BR>mother of the Aśvins, the wife of<BR>the sun, who concealed herself in<BR>the form of a mare.<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">Page0205-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--कुमारौ, --पुत्रौ, --सुतौ the twin sons of<BR>Aśvinī, the sun's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विमत्|अश्विमन्त्
अश्विमत् a. Containing the word<BR>Aśvin (such as a Mantra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्विय
अश्विय a. Referring to horses.<BR>--या<BR>Ved. (pl.) A troop of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीन|अश्वीनः
अश्वीन a. [अश्व --ख] Distant, a<BR>day's journey for a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वीय|अश्वीयं|अश्वीयः
अश्वीय a. [अश्व-छ] Belonging<BR>or relating to a horse, agreeable to<BR>horses.<BR>--यं [अश्वानां समूहः<BR>P. IV. 2. 48] A number of horses, cavalry;<BR>Śi. 18. 5; K. 222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्व्य|अश्व्यः
अश्व्य a. [अश्व-यत्]<BR>1 Belonging to<BR>a horse.<BR>--2 Consisting of horses.<BR>--श्व्यं<BR>1 A number of horses.<BR>--2<BR>Possession of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वंत|अश्वन्त|अश्वन्तं|अश्वन्तः
अश्वंत a.<BR>1 Unlucky,<BR>inauspicious.<BR>--2 Unbounded, unlimited.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Death.<BR>--2 A field.<BR>--3 A<BR>fireplace.<BR>--4 Termination, limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तन
अश्वस्तन, --स्तनिक a.<BR>1 Not of<BR>to-morrow, of to-day.<BR>--2 One who<BR>makes no provision for the morrow<BR>Ms. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्वस्तनिक
अश्वस्तन, --स्तनिक a.<BR>1 Not of<BR>to-morrow, of to-day.<BR>--2 One who<BR>makes no provision for the morrow<BR>Ms. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्
अष् {c1c} U. [अषति-ते, अषितुं]<BR>1 To<BR>shine.<BR>--2 To go, move.<BR>--3 To receive,<BR>take (trans.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषडक्षीण|अषडक्षीणः
अषडक्षीण a. Not seen by six<BR>eyes, known or determined by two<BR>persons only, (to the exclusion of<BR>a third); ˚णो मंत्रः द्वाभ्यामेव कृत इत्यर्थः<BR>P. V. 4. 7 Sk.<BR>--णं A secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषतर
अषतर a. Ved. More accessible<BR>or acceptable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढ|अषाढः
अषाढ a.<BR>1 Ved. Not to be<BR>overcome, invincible;<BR>Rv. 2. 21. 2.<BR>--2 Born under the constellation<BR>Aṣāḍha (P. IV. 3. 34).<BR>--ढः<BR>1 The month Aṣāḍha<BR>commencing with the sun's entrance<BR>into Gemini (usually written आषाढ).<BR>--2 A staff made of the wood<BR>of Palāśa, carried by a religious<BR>student or ascetic.<BR>--3 N. of the<BR>Malaya mountain.<BR>--ढा N. of a<BR>constellation, the twentieth (पूर्वाषाढा)<BR>and twenty-first (उत्तराषाढा) lunar<BR>mansions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अषाढकः|अषाढक
अषाढकः The month of Aṣāḍha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टन्
अष्टन् num. a. [अश्-व्याप्तौ कनिन्<BR>तुट् च Uṇ. 1. 154.] (nom. acc. अष्ट-ष्टौ)<BR>Eight. It often occurs in comp. as<BR>अष्टा with numerals and some other<BR>nouns; as अष्टादशन्, अष्टाविंशतिः, अष्टापद &c.<BR>[cf. L. octo; Gr. okto; Zend.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0206-a" target="_blank">Page0206-a+ 58</a>]<BR>astan; Pers. hasht.].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षर a. consisting of eight letters or<BR>parts.<BR>--(रः) N. of a metre.<BR>--अंग a.<BR>consisting of eight parts or members.<BR>--(गं) {1} the eight parts of the body<BR>with which a very low obeisance<BR>is performed; ˚पातः, --प्रणामः,<BR>साष्टांगनमस्कारः a respectful obeisance made<BR>by the prostration of the eight<BR>limbs of the body; साष्टांगपातं प्रणनाम<BR>fell prostrate on the ground in<BR>reverence; (जानुभ्यां च तथा पद्भ्यां<BR>पाणिभ्यामुरसा धिया । शिरसा वचसा दृष्ट्या प्रणामोऽ<BR>ष्टांग ईरितः). {2} the 8 parts of yoga<BR>or concentration; यमो<BR>नियमश्चासनं च प्राणायामस्ततः परं । प्रत्याहारो<BR>धारणा च ध्यानं सार्धं समाधिना । अष्टांगान्याहुरेतानि<BR>योगिनां योगसिद्धये ॥. {3} materials of<BR>worship taken collectively. {4} the<BR>eight parts of every medical science;<BR>(they are: --शल्यं, शालाक्यं, कायचिकित्सा,<BR>भूतविद्या, कौमारभृत्यं, अगदतंत्रं, रसायनतंत्रं,<BR>and वाजीकरणतंत्रं). {5} the eight parts<BR>of a court; {1} the law, {2} the judge,<BR>{3} assessors, {4} scribe, {5} astrologer,<BR>{6} gold, {7} fire, and {8} water. {6} any<BR>whole consisting of eight parts. {7}<BR>a die, dice. ˚अर्घ्यं an offering of<BR>eight articles. ˚धूपः a sort of medical<BR>incense removing fever. ˚मैथुनं ‘sexual<BR>enjoyment of 8 kinds’; the eight<BR>stages in the progress of a love-suit;<BR>स्मरणं कीर्तनं केलिः प्रेक्षणं गुह्यभाषणं ।<BR>संकल्पोऽध्यवसायश्च क्रियानिष्पत्तिरेव च ॥.<BR>˚हृदयं N. of a medical work.<BR>--अध्यायी<BR>N. of Pāṇini's grammatical work<BR>consisting of 8 Adhyāyas or<BR>chapters.<BR>--अर a. having a wheel<BR>with 8 spokes.<BR>--अस्रं an octagon.<BR>--अस्रिय a. octangular.<BR>--अह (न्) a.<BR>lasting for 8 days.<BR>--आदिशाब्दिकाः<BR>the first eight expounders of the<BR>science of words (grammar);<BR>इंद्रश्चंद्रः काशकृत्स्नापिशली शाकटायनः ।<BR>पाणिन्यमरजैनेंद्रा जयंत्यष्टादिशाब्दिकाः ॥.<BR>--कपाल<BR>a. (˚ष्टा˚) prepared or offered in ‘eight’<BR>pans.<BR>--(लः) a sacrifice in which<BR>ghee is offered in eight pans.<BR>--कर्ण<BR>a. one who has the number eight<BR>as a mark burnt in his ears (<BR>P. VI. 3. 115).<BR>--(र्णः) eight-eared, an<BR>epithet of Brahmā.<BR>--कर्मन् m.,<BR>--गतिकः a king who has {8} duties to<BR>perform; they are: -- आदाने च विसर्गे च<BR>तथा प्रैषनिषेधयोः । पंचमे चार्थवचने व्यवहारस्य<BR>चेक्षणे ॥ दंडशुद्ध्योः सदा रक्तस्तेनाष्टगतिको<BR>नृपः ।.<BR>--कृत्वस् ind. eight times.<BR>--कोणः {1} an octagon. {2} a kind<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0206-b" target="_blank">Page0206-b+ 58</a>]<BR>of machine.<BR>--खंडः a title of a<BR>collection of several sections of the<BR>Ṛgveda.<BR>--गवं [अष्टानां गवां समाहारः]<BR>a flock of 8 cows.<BR>--गाढ् m. {1} a<BR>fabulous animal supposed to have eight<BR>legs. {2} a spider.<BR>--गुण a.<BR>eightfold; अन्नादष्टगुणं चूर्णं;<BR>दाप्योष्टगुणमत्ययं Ms. 8. 400.<BR>--(णं) the eight<BR>qualities which a Brāhmaṇa should<BR>possess; दया सर्वभूतेषु, क्षांतिः, अनसूया, शौचं,<BR>अनायासः, मंगलं, अकार्पण्यं, अस्पृहा चेति ॥<BR>Gautama. ˚आश्रय a. endowed<BR>with these eight qualities.<BR>--ष्ट (ष्टा)<BR>चत्वारिंशत् a. forty-eight.<BR>--तय<BR>a. eight-fold.<BR>--तारिणी the eight<BR>forms of the goddess तारिणी; तारा<BR>चोग्रा महोग्रा च वज्रा काली सरस्वती । कामेश्वरी<BR>च चामुंडा इत्यष्टौ तारिण्यो मताः ॥.<BR>--त्रिंशत्<BR>--(ष्टा) a. thirty-eight.<BR>--त्रिकं [अष्टावृत्तं<BR>त्रिकं] the number 24.<BR>--दलं {1} a lotus<BR>having eight petals. {2} an octagon.<BR>--दशन् (˚ष्टा˚) see below after अष्टातय.<BR>--दिश् f. [कर्म˚ संज्ञात्वान्न द्विगुः] the<BR>eight cardinal points; पूर्वाग्नेयी दक्षिणा च<BR>नैरृती पश्चिमा तथा । वायवी चोत्तरैशानी दिशा<BR>अष्टाविमाः स्मृताः ॥. ˚करिण्यः the eight<BR>female elephants living in the eight<BR>points; करिण्योऽभ्रमुकपिलापिंगलानुपमाः<BR>क्रमात् । ताम्रकर्णी शुभ्रदंती चांगना चांजनावती ॥<BR>Ak. ˚पालाः the eight regents of the<BR>cardinal points; इंद्रो वह्रिः पितृपतिः (यमः)<BR>नैरृतो वरुणो मरुत् (वायुः) । कुबेर ईशः पतयः<BR>पूर्वादीनां दिशां क्रमात् ॥ Ak. ˚गजाः the<BR>eight elephants guarding the 8<BR>quarters; ऐरावतः पुंडरीको वामनः कुमुदोंऽजनः ।<BR>पुष्पदंतः सार्वभौमः सुप्रतीकश्च दिग्गजाः ॥ Ak.<BR>--द्रव्यं the eight materials of a<BR>sacrifice;<BR>अश्वत्थोडुंबरप्लक्षन्यग्रोधसमिधस्तिलाः । सिद्धार्थपायसाज्यानि द्रव्याण्यष्टौ<BR>विटुर्बुधाः ॥.<BR>--धातुः the eight metals taken<BR>collectively; स्वर्णं रूप्यं च ताम्रं च रंगं<BR>यशदमेव च । शीसं लौहं रसश्चेति धातवोऽष्टौ<BR>प्रकीर्तिताः ॥.<BR>--पद --द् (˚ष्ट or ष्टा˚) a. {1}<BR>eight-footed. {2} a term for a<BR>pregnant animal.<BR>--पदः (˚ष्टा˚) {1} a<BR>spider. {2} a fabulous animal called<BR>Śarabha. {3} a worm. {4} a wild<BR>sort of jasmin. {5} a pin or bolt.<BR>{6} the mountain Kailāsa (the<BR>abode of Kubera).<BR>--(दः, --दं) [अष्टसु<BR>धातुषु पदं प्रतिष्ठा यस्य Malli.] {1} gold;<BR>आवर्जिताष्टापदकुंभतोयैः Ku. 7. 10;<BR>Śi. 3. 28. {2} a kind of chequered cloth<BR>or a board for drafts, dice-board<BR>(Mar. पट); ˚परिचयचतुराभिः K. 196.<BR>˚पत्रं a sheet of gold.<BR>--प (पा) दिका<BR>N. of a plant.<BR>--पदी (˚ष्ट-ष्टा˚) {1}<BR>wild sort of jasmin. {2} a variety of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0206-c" target="_blank">Page0206-c+ 58</a>]<BR>metre, often used in Jayadeva's<BR>Gītagovinda.<BR>--पलं a kind of<BR>medicinal preparation of ghee.<BR>--पाद्य a.<BR>(˚ष्टा˚) eight-fold.<BR>--मंगलः a horse<BR>with a white face, tail, mane, breast<BR>and hoofs.<BR>--(लं) [अष्टगुणितं मंगलं शा˚<BR>त˚] a collection of eight lucky<BR>things; according to some they are:<BR>--मृगराजो वृषो नागः कलशो व्यंजनं तथा । वैजयंती<BR>तथा भेरी दीप इत्यष्टमंगलम् ॥; according to<BR>others लोकेऽस्मिन्मंगलान्यष्टौ ब्राह्मणो<BR>गौर्हुताशनः । हिरण्यं सर्पिरादित्य आपो राजा तथाष्टमः ॥.<BR>--मानं one kuḍava.<BR>--मासिक a.<BR>occurring once in 8 months.<BR>--मुष्टिः a<BR>measure called कुंचि; अष्टमुष्टिर्भवेत् कुंचिः,<BR>--मूर्तिः the ‘eight-formed’, an epithet<BR>of Śiva; the 8 forms being the 5<BR>elements (earth, water, fire, air and ether),<BR>the sun and moon, and the<BR>sacrificing priest; cf Ś. 1. 1--या सृष्टिः स्रष्टुराद्या<BR>वहति विधिहुतं या हविर्या च होत्री । येद्वे कालंविधत्तः<BR>श्रुतिविषयगुणा या स्थिता व्याप्य विश्वं । यामाहुः<BR>सर्वभूतप्रकृतिरिति यया प्राणिनः प्राणवंतः ।<BR>प्रत्यक्षाभिः प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः ॥;<BR>or, briefly expressed, the names in<BR>Sanskrit (in the above order)<BR>are:--जलं वह्निस्तथा यष्टा सूर्याचंद्रमसौ तथा ।<BR>आकाशं वायुरवनी मूर्तयोऽष्टौ पिनाकिनः ॥.<BR>˚धरः ‘having {8} forms’, Śiva.<BR>--रत्नं<BR>the eight jewels taken collectively;<BR>the title of a collection of 8<BR>Ślokas on morality.<BR>--रसाः the<BR>{8} sentiments in dramas &c.;<BR>शृंगारहास्यकरुणरौद्रवीरभयानकाः । बीभत्साद्भुतसंज्ञौ<BR>चेत्यष्टौ नाट्ये रसाः स्मृताः ॥ K. P. 4 (to<BR>which is sometimes added a 9th<BR>Rasa called शांत; निर्वेदस्थायिभावोस्ति<BR>शांतोपि नवमो रसः ibid.); ˚आश्रय a.<BR>embodying or representing the<BR>eight sentiments; V. 2. 18.<BR>--लोहकं<BR>a class of 8 metals; सुवर्णं रजतं ताम्रं<BR>सीसकं कांतिकं तथा । वंगं लौहं तीक्ष्णलौहं<BR>लौहान्यष्टाविमानि तु ॥.<BR>--वर्गः {1} a sort of<BR>diagram (चक्र) showing the good or<BR>bad stars of a person. {2} the 8<BR>classes of letters; (अवर्ग, क˚, च˚, ट˚,<BR>त˚, प˚, य˚, श˚,). {3} a class of three<BR>principal medicaments.<BR>--वक्रः (ष्टा)<BR>see below.<BR>--विध a. [अष्ट विधाः प्रकाराः<BR>अस्य] eight-fold, of eight kinds.<BR>--विंशतिः f. (˚ष्टा˚) [अष्टाधिका विंशातिः शा.<BR>त.] the number twenty-eight.<BR>--शतं<BR>eight hundred.<BR>--श्रवणः, --श्रवस N. of<BR>Brahmā (having {8} ears or four<BR>heads).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0205-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टक|अष्टकः
अष्टक a. [अष्ट परिमाणमस्य कन्]<BR>Consisting of 8 parts, eight-fold;<BR>क्रोधजोऽपि गणोऽष्टकः Ms. 7. 48.<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-a" target="_blank">Page0207-a+ 58</a>]<BR>[अष्टकं (पाणिनेः), विदंति अधीयते वा इत्यष्टकाः<BR>P. IV. 2. 65 Sk.] One who studies<BR>or is acquainted with the eight<BR>books of Pāṇini's grammar.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a son of Viśvāmitra.<BR>--का [<BR>अश्नंति पितरोऽस्यां तिथौ अश्-तकन्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 148]<BR>1 A collection of three days<BR>(7th, 8th, and 9th) beginning<BR>from the seventh day after the full<BR>moon.<BR>--2 The 8th day of three<BR>months on which the Manes are to<BR>be propitiated.<BR>--3 A Śrāddha to be<BR>performed on the above days;<BR>worship of the Manes on certain days.<BR>--4 The 8th day of a month;<BR>Ms. 4. 113-4.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A whole<BR>consisting of 8 parts.<BR>--2 The {8} chapters<BR>of Pāṇini's sūtras; अष्टावध्यायाः<BR>परिमाणमस्य इत्यष्टकं; पाणिनेः सूत्रं Sk..<BR>--3 The study of the Sūtras.<BR>--4<BR>A division of the Ṛgveda (it<BR>being divided into 8 Aṣṭakas or 10<BR>Maṇḍalas).<BR>--5 Any group of eight;<BR>as वानराष्टकं, ताराष्टकं, गंगाष्टकं &c.<BR>--6 The<BR>number eight.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः, --गं<BR>a kind of board or cloth for playing<BR>with dice on (having eight<BR>divisions).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0206-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकिक
अष्टकिक, अष्टकिन् a. [अष्टकाऽस्त्यस्य<BR>ठन् इनि वा] Having eight parts.<BR>--की<BR>One who performs an Aṣṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टकिन्
अष्टकिक, अष्टकिन् a. [अष्टकाऽस्त्यस्य<BR>ठन् इनि वा] Having eight parts.<BR>--की<BR>One who performs an Aṣṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टक्य
अष्टक्य a. [अष्टकेन क्रीतः यत्<BR>P. V. 1. 2] Bought for eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टतय
अष्टतय a. [अष्टावयवा अस्य अष्टन्-तयप्]<BR>Having eight parts or limbs.<BR>--यं<BR>An aggregate of eight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टधा
अष्टधा ind. [अष्टन्-प्रकारे धाच्]<BR>1<BR>Eight-fold, eight times.<BR>--2 In {8}<BR>parts or sections; भिन्ना प्रकृतिरष्टधा<BR>Bg. 7. 4; भिन्नोष्टधा विप्रससार वंशः<BR>R. 16. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टम|अष्टमः
अष्टम a. (मी f.) Eighth; गर्भाष्टमेऽब्दे<BR>कुर्वीत ब्राह्मणस्योपनायनं Ms. 2. 36.<BR>--मः<BR>The eighth part.<BR>--मी<BR>1 The eighth<BR>day in a lunar half month; चतुर्दश्यष्टमी<BR>चैव अमावास्या च पूर्णिमा । पर्वाण्येतानि राजेंद्र<BR>रविसंक्रातिरेव च ॥.<BR>--2 N. of a medical<BR>plant (कोटालता). [cf. L. octavus;<BR>Zend. astemo].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः an<BR>8th part.<BR>--कालिक a. [अष्टमः कालः<BR>भोजनेऽस्त्यस्य ठन्] one who omits seven<BR>meal times (i. e. full three days and<BR>the morning of the fourth) and<BR>partakes only of the 8th;<BR>Ms. 6. 19.<BR>--भावः the eighth condition or<BR>position (in astr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमक
अष्टमक^1 a. The eighth;<BR>योंशमष्टमकं हरेत् Y. 2. 244.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टमिका
अष्टमिका A weight of four Tolas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टातय|अष्टातयः
अष्टातय a. Consisting of eight<BR>parts.<BR>--यः A collection of eight<BR>things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टादशन्
अष्टादशन् a. [अष्ट च दश च] Eighteen;<BR>अगाहताष्टादशतां जिगीषया<BR>नवद्वयद्वीपपृथग्जयश्रियां N. 1. 5.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः<BR>--गं the eighteen parts of medical<BR>science.<BR>--उपचारः [कर्म˚ संज्ञात्वान्न द्विगुः]<BR>the eighteen modes of<BR>showing respect or worshipping;<BR>आसनं स्वागतं पाद्यमर्घ्यमाचमनीयकं स्नानं<BR>वस्त्रेपवीतं च भूषणानि च सर्वशः । गंधपुष्पे तथा<BR>धूपदीपावन्नं च तर्पणं । माल्यानुलेपनं चैव<BR>नमस्कारविसर्जने । अष्टादशोपचारैस्तु मंत्री पूजां<BR>समाचरेत् Tantra.<BR>--उपपुराणं a secondary<BR>or minor Purāṇa; अष्टान्युपपुराणानि मुनिभिः<BR>कथितानि तु । आद्यं सनत्कुमारोक्तं नारासींहमतः<BR>परं । तृतीयं नारदं प्रोक्तं कुमारेण तु भाषितं ।<BR>चतुर्थं शिवधर्माख्यं साक्षान्नंदीशभाषितं ।<BR>दुर्वाससोक्तमाश्चर्यं नारदोक्तमतःपरं । कापिलं मानवं<BR>चैव तथैवोशनसेरितं । ब्रह्मांडं वारुणं चाथ<BR>कालिकाह्वयमेव च । माहेश्वरं तथा शांबं<BR>सौरं सर्वार्थसंचयं । पराशरोक्तं प्रवरं तथा<BR>भागवतद्वयं । इदमष्टादशं प्रोक्तं पुराणं<BR>कौर्मसंज्ञितं । चतुर्धा संस्थितं पुण्यं संहितानां<BR>प्रभेदतः ॥ Hemādri.<BR>--धान्यं the 18 kinds<BR>of corn; यवगोधूमधान्यानि तिलाः<BR>कंगुकुलत्थकाः । माषा मुद्गा मसूराश्च निष्पावाः<BR>श्यामसर्षपाः ॥ गवेधुकाश्च नीवारा ओढक्योऽथ<BR>सतीनकाः । चणकाश्चीनकाश्चैव धान्यान्यष्टादशैव तु ॥.<BR>--पुराणं the eighteen Purāṇas: ब्राह्मं<BR>पाद्मं वैष्णवं च शैवं भागवतं तथा ।<BR>तथान्यन्नारदीयं च मार्कंडेयं च सप्तमं ॥ आग्नेयमष्टकं प्रोक्तं<BR>भविष्यन्नवमं तथा । दशमं ब्रह्मवैवर्तं<BR>लिंगमेकादशं तथा ॥ वाराहं द्वादशं प्रोक्तं स्कांदं चात्र<BR>त्रयोदशं । चतुदर्शं वामनं च कौर्मं पंचदशं<BR>तथा ॥ मात्स्यं च गारुडं चैव ब्रह्मांडाष्टादशं तथा ॥.<BR>--भुजा an epithet of the goddess<BR>महालक्ष्मी.<BR>--विद्या the eighteen kinds of<BR>learning or lores; अंगानि वेदाश्चत्वारो<BR>मीमांसा न्यायविस्तरः । धर्मशास्त्रं पुराणं च<BR>विद्या ह्येताश्चर्तुदश ॥ आयुर्वेदो धनुर्वेदो<BR>गांधर्वश्चेति ते त्रयः । अर्थशास्त्रं चतुर्थं तु विद्या<BR>ह्यष्टादशैव तु ॥.<BR>--विवादपदं the eighteen<BR>subjects of litigation (causes of<BR>dispute); see Ms. 8. 4-7.<BR>--स्मृतिकारिन् m. pl. the eighteen Smṛtikāras<BR>or law-givers of the Āryas; विष्णुः<BR>पराशरो दक्षः संवर्तव्यासहारिताः । शातातपो<BR>वसिष्ठश्च यमापस्तंबगौतमाः । देवलः शंखलिखितौ<BR>भरद्वाजोशनोत्रयः । शौनको याज्ञवल्क्यश्च दशाष्टौ<BR>स्मृतिकारिणः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टावक्रः|अष्टावक्र
अष्टावक्रः [अष्टकृत्वः अष्टसु भागेषु वा वक्रः]<BR>N. of a celebrated Brāhmaṇa,<BR>son of the great sage Kahoḍa.<BR>[Kahoḍa married a daughter of his<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-c" target="_blank">Page0207-c+ 59</a>]<BR>preceptor Uddālaka, but he was so<BR>devoted to study that he generally neglected<BR>her. When once she was far advanced in<BR>pregnancy, the unborn son was<BR>provoked at his father's neglect of her and<BR>rebuked him for his absorption in study<BR>to the neglect even of his wife. The<BR>sage was very angry at this<BR>impertinence and condemned him to be born<BR>crooked; so he came forth with his<BR>eight (aṣṭa) limbs crooked (vakra);<BR>whence his name; यस्मात्कुक्षौ वर्तमानो ब्रवीषि<BR>तस्माद्वक्रो भवितास्यष्टकृत्वः Mb. When<BR>Kahoḍa was drowned into a river as the<BR>result of a wager in a dispute with a<BR>Buddhist, young Aṣṭāvakra defeated the<BR>sage and delivered his father, who,<BR>being pleased, directed his son to bathe<BR>into the Samaṅgā river, on doing which<BR>the lad became perfectly straight].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टिः|अष्टि
अष्टिः f. [अस्यते भूमौ क्षिप्यते अस्-क्तिन्<BR>पृषो˚ षत्वं]<BR>1 A die for playing.<BR>--2 A<BR>metre consisting of sixty-four<BR>syllables.<BR>--3 [अक्ष्-व्याप्तौ-क्तिन्]<BR>Pervasion, reaching (Ved.).<BR>--4 The body<BR>(the instrument of enjoyment).<BR>--5<BR>The number sixteen.<BR>--6 Seed.<BR>--7<BR>Kernel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्टिन्
अष्टिन् a. Consisting of eight<BR>members or parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ट्रा
अष्ट्रा [अक्ष्यते चाल्यतेऽनया अक्ष्-करणे<BR>ष्ट्रन्]<BR>1 A prick or goad for driving<BR>cattle, whip; Rv. 4. 57. 4, 6. 53. 9.<BR>--2 A part of the wheel of a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठिः|अष्ठि
अष्ठिः f.<BR>1 A stone or kernel.<BR>--2<BR>Seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीला
अष्ठीला [अष्ठिस्तत्तुल्यकठिनाश्मानं<BR>राति; रा-क, रस्य लः दीर्घः Tv.]<BR>1 A<BR>round swelling below the navel<BR>produced by wind.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>disease of urine.<BR>--3 A globular or<BR>round body (in general).<BR>--4 A round<BR>pebble or stone.<BR>--5 Kernel.<BR>--6<BR>Seedcorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीलिका
अष्ठीलिका<BR>1 A kind of abscess.<BR>--2 A pebble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अष्ठीवत्|अष्ठीवन्त्
अष्ठीवत् m. n. [निपातोयं<BR>P. VIII. 2. 12;] The knee, the kneebone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्
अस् {vI.v} {c2c} P. [अस्ति, आसीत्, अस्तु,<BR>स्यात्; defective in non-conjugational<BR>tenses, its forms being made up from<BR>the root भू].<BR>1 To be, live, exist<BR>(showing mere existence);<BR>नासदासीन्नो सदासीत् Rv. 10. 129. 1;<BR>श्रुतिद्वैधं तु यत्र स्यात् Ms. 2. 14; शपथे<BR>नास्ति पातकं 8. 112; न त्वेवाहं जातु नासं<BR>Bg. 2. 12; आसीद्राजा नलो नाम<BR>Nala. 1. 1; Ms. 5. 79; न अस् not to be, to<BR>be lost, disappear, perish,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-a" target="_blank">Page0208-a+ 58</a>]<BR>नायमस्तीति दुःखार्ता Nala. 7. 16; अस्ति भोक्तुं<BR>Sk. it has to be eaten; (for other<BR>uses of अस्ति see अस्ति s. v.).<BR>--2 To be (used as a copula<BR>or verb of incomplete predication,<BR>being followed by a noun or<BR>adjective or adverb, or some other<BR>equivalent); भक्तोसि मे सखा च Bg. 4. 3;<BR>धार्मिके सति राजनि Ms. 11. 11;<BR>आचार्ये संस्थिते सति 5. 80; so एवमेव<BR>स्यात्, तूष्णीमासीत् &c.<BR>--3 To belong<BR>to, be in the possession of<BR>(expressed in English by have), with gen.<BR>of possessor; यन्ममास्ति हरस्व तत्<BR>Pt. 4. 76; यस्य नास्ति स्वयं प्रज्ञा 5. 70;<BR>न हि तस्यास्ति किंचित्स्वं Ms. 8. 417;<BR>नास्ति बुद्धिरयुक्तस्य Bg. 2. 66.<BR>--4 To<BR>fall to the share of, to happen to or<BR>befall any one (with gen.); यदिच्छामि<BR>ते तदस्तु Ś. 4; तस्य प्रेत्य फलं नास्ति<BR>Ms. 3. 139 he cannot enjoy or get.<BR>--5 To arise, spring out, occur;<BR>आसीच्च मम मनसि K. 142 (this)<BR>occurred to my mind.<BR>--6 To become;<BR>तां दृष्ट्वा दशविस्तारामासं विंशतियोजनः<BR>Rām.; also शुक्लीस्यात्, राजसात् स्यात्<BR>&c. Sk.<BR>--7 To lead or tend to, turn<BR>out or prove to be (with dat.);<BR>स स्थाणुः स्थिरभक्तियोगसुलभो<BR>निःश्रेयसायास्तु वः V. 1. 1; संगतं<BR>श्रीसरस्वत्योर्भूतयेस्तु सदा सतां 5. 24; oft. with dat.<BR>alone without अस्; यतस्तौ<BR>स्वल्पदुःखाय Pt. 1.<BR>--8 To suffice (with dat.);<BR>सा तेषां पावनाय स्यात् Ms. 11. 86;<BR>अन्यैर्नृपालैः परिदीयमानं शाकाय वा<BR>स्याल्लवणाय वा स्यात् Jagannātha.<BR>--9 To<BR>stay, reside, dwell, live; हा पितः<BR>क्वासि हे सुभ्रु Bk. 6. 11.<BR>--10 To take<BR>place, happen.<BR>--11 To be in a<BR>particular relation, to be affected (with<BR>loc.); किंनु खलु यथा<BR>वयमस्यामेवमियमप्यस्मात् प्रति स्यात् Ś. 1. अस्तु well, let<BR>it be; एवमस्तु, तथास्तु so be it, amen.<BR>The form आस joined to roots in<BR>forming their periphrastic perfect<BR>is sometimes separated from the<BR>root and used by itself; तं पातयां<BR>प्रथममास पपात पश्चात् R. 9. 61, 16. 86.<BR>[Cf. L. est and Gr. esti with<BR>अस्ति; esse; Zend. āsti; Pers. hast,<BR>ast]. --WITH अति to be over, excel,<BR>surpass.<BR>--अनु to be at hand, reach.<BR>--अपि (with loc. or an adv. of place)<BR>{1} to be in anything. {2} to belong<BR>to, be closely connected with.<BR>--अभि {1} to belong to, to fall to<BR>one's share; यन्ममाभिष्यात् Sk. {2}<BR>to be over. {3} to excel, surpass. {4} to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-b" target="_blank">Page0208-b+ 58</a>]<BR>domineer or to tyrannize over, rule<BR>over.<BR>--आविस् to arise, spring up, be<BR>visible; आचार्यकं विजयि<BR>मान्मथमाविरासीत् Māl. 1. 26.<BR>--उप to be near to<BR>or in.<BR>--परि {1} to be in the way. {2} to<BR>surpass. {3} to pass or spend (time).<BR>{4} to pervade.<BR>--प्र {1} to be in front<BR>of. {2} to be in an extraordinary<BR>degree, to preponderate, excel,<BR>surpass.<BR>--प्रति {1} to be equal to, be a<BR>match for. {2} to rival, emulate, vie<BR>with. {3} to be a representative of,<BR>stand in place of.<BR>--प्रादुस् to appear,<BR>spring up; प्रादुरासीत्तमोनुदः Ms. 1. 6;<BR>R. 11. 15.<BR>--व्यति (Atm. व्यतिहे,<BR>व्यतिसे; व्यतिस्ते) to excel, surpass, be<BR>above or superior to, out-weigh;<BR>अन्यो व्यतिस्ते तु ममापि धर्मः Bk. 2. 35.<BR>{vII.v} {c4c} P. (अस्यति, आस, आस्थत्,<BR>असितुं, अस्त)<BR>1 To throw, cast, hurl,<BR>discharge, shoot (with loc. of the<BR>mark); तस्मिन्नास्थदिषीकास्त्रं<BR>R. 12. 23; Bk. 15. 91, 14. 77; sometimes<BR>with dat. or gen.; दस्यवे हेतिमस्य<BR>Rv. 1. 103. 3.<BR>--2 To drive away,<BR>remove.<BR>--3 To frighten or scare away.<BR>--4 To throw or take away, let go,<BR>leave, give up; as in अस्तमान,<BR>अस्तशोक, अस्तकोप; see अस्त. --WITH अति<BR>to shoot beyond or at, overpower<BR>(with arrows); अत्यस्त having shot<BR>beyond, having surpassed or<BR>excelled; joined in acc. Tat. comp.;<BR>P. II. 1. 24.<BR>--अभिप्र to throw over or<BR>upon, hurl at.<BR>--परिनि to stretch.<BR>{vIII.v} {c1c} U. (असति-ते, असित).<BR>1 To<BR>go.<BR>--2 To take or receive, seize.<BR>--3<BR>To shine (The examples usually<BR>cited to illustrate this sense are<BR>निष्प्रभश्च प्रभुरास भूभृतां R. 11. 81; तेनास लोकः<BR>पितृमान् विनेत्रा 14. 23; लावण्य उत्पाद्य<BR>इवास यत्नः Ku. 1. 35. But the sense<BR>of दिदीपे or ‘shone’ is far-fetched,<BR>though Vāmana is disposed to take<BR>it. It seems preferable to regard आस<BR>in these instances as equivalent to<BR>बभूव, either taking it, as Śākaṭāyana<BR>does, as an indeclinable<BR>तिङंतप्रतिरूपकमव्ययं, or considering it, as Vallabha<BR>does, as an ungrammatical form used<BR>against the rules of grammar,<BR>प्रामादिकः प्रयोगः; see Malli. on Ku. 1. 35).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0207-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त p. p.<BR>1 Thrown, cast, given<BR>up, left; असमये यत्त्वयास्तोऽभिमानः<BR>Ve. 6.<BR>--2 Finished.<BR>--3<BR>Despatched.<BR>--स्ता Ved. A missile, an<BR>arrow.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करुण a.<BR>merciless; Māl. 5. 24.<BR>--कोप, --रुष् a. whose<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-c" target="_blank">Page0208-c+ 57</a>]<BR>anger is pacified; Śi. 6. 65.<BR>--धी a.<BR>foolish.<BR>--व्यस्त a. scattered here<BR>and there, confused, disordered;<BR>Ratn. 4. 6.<BR>--संख्य a.<BR>innumerable; Ki. 16. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तृ
अस्तृ a. Ved. Throwing, a shooter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तः|अस्त|अस्तं
अस्तः [अस्यंते सूर्यकिरणा यत्र अस्-आधारे<BR>क्त]<BR>1 Setting or western mountain<BR>(behind which the sun is supposed<BR>to set); अधिरोढुमस्तगिरिमभ्यपतत्<BR>Śi. 9. 1; विडंबयत्यस्तनिमग्नसूर्यं<BR>R. 16. 11; यात्येकतोस्तशिखरं पतिरोषधीनां<BR>Ś. 4. 1.<BR>--2 Sunset.<BR>--3 Setting in<BR>general; (fig.) fall, decline; see<BR>below.<BR>--4 Conjunction of a planet<BR>with the sun: शक्रास्त, बुधास्त &c.<BR>--स्तं<BR>1 Home, abode, residence<BR>(Ved.); Rv. 7. 1. 2, 10. 34. 10.<BR>--2 Death, end.<BR>--3 The seventh<BR>house (in astr.); (लग्नात्सप्तमं स्थानं).<BR>--स्तं ind. At home, home; अस्तं गम्,<BR>--या, --इ, --प्राप् (a) To set, decline in<BR>the western horizon; गतोस्तमर्कः the<BR>sun has set; (fig.) it is time to<BR>do the duties to be performed at<BR>sunset; e. g. for a cowherd to<BR>drive home his cattle, for a religious<BR>person to begin his prayers, for<BR>a thief to begin his nightly work<BR>&c.; कथमिहवै युवयोरस्तमितः सूर्यः V. 3<BR>and Sarva. S. 1. (b) To cease, vanish,<BR>be removed, disappear, be at an<BR>end; विषयिणः कस्यापदोऽस्तं गताः<BR>Pt. 1. 146; धृतिरस्तमिता R. 8. 66;<BR>दंडेनास्तमितत्विषा Ku. 2. 23; अस्तमितैषा<BR>कथा K. 156 at an end, over; 198, 204.<BR>(c) To die; अथ चास्तमिता त्वमात्मना<BR>R. 8. 51, 12. 11.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अचलः,<BR>--अद्रिः, --गिरिः, --पर्वतः the setting or<BR>western mountain.<BR>--अवलंबनं the<BR>resting of a heavenly body on the<BR>western part of the horizon, being<BR>about to set.<BR>--उदयौ (dual) rising<BR>and setting, rise and fall;<BR>अस्तोदयावदिशदप्रविभिन्नकालं Mu. 3. 17.<BR>--ग<BR>a. set, become invisible (as a planet<BR>or star).<BR>--गमनं {1} setting,<BR>disappearance. {2} death, sunset of life; Māl. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तकः|अस्तक
अस्तकः Final beatitude,<BR>absolution (मोक्ष).<BR>--कं Ved. Home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ततातिः|अस्तताति
अस्ततातिः Ved. Home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमनं|अस्तमन
अस्तमनं Setting (of the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमयः|अस्तमय
अस्तमयः<BR>1 Setting (of the sun);<BR>करोत्यकालास्तमयं विवस्वतः Ki. 5. 35; (opp.<BR>उदय).<BR>--2 Destruction, end, decline,<BR>loss; भाग्यास्तमयमिवाक्ष्णोः M. 2. 12.<BR>--3 Fall, subjugation; उदयमस्तमयं च<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">Page0209-a+ 56</a>]<BR>रघूद्वहात् R. 9. 9.<BR>--4 Obscuring,<BR>eclipsing; प्रभाप्ररोहास्तमयं रजांसि<BR>R. 6. 33.<BR>--5 Conjunction (of a planet)<BR>with the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0208-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तमिके
अस्तमिके, अस्ता ind. Ved. At hand,<BR>near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ता
अस्तमिके, अस्ता ind. Ved. At hand,<BR>near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ति|अस्तिः
अस्ति ind. [अस्-शतिप्]<BR>1 Being,<BR>existent, present; as in अस्तिक्षीरा,<BR>˚काय.<BR>--2 Often used at the<BR>commencement of a tale or narrative<BR>in the sense of ‘so it is’, ‘there’, or<BR>merely as an expletive; अस्ति सिंहः<BR>प्रतिवसति स्म Pt. 4; अस्त्यत्र नगरे… त्रयः<BR>पुरुषा देवस्य श्रियं न सहंते Mu. 1, 5;<BR>अस्ति पूर्वमहं व्योमचारी विद्याधरोऽभवम्<BR>Ks. 22. 56, 1. 27; अस्ति तत्रभवान्<BR>वृषलं याजयिष्यति P. III. 3. 146 is<BR>it that &c.<BR>--स्तिः f. N. of a sister<BR>of Prāpti, daughter of Jarāsaṃdha<BR>and wife of Kaṃsa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कायः<BR>[अस्ति कायः स्वरूपं यस्य] a category or<BR>predicament (with the Jainas); these<BR>categories are 5:<BR>--जीव˚, पुद्गल˚, धर्म˚,<BR>अधर्म˚, and आकाश˚.<BR>--क्षीर a. [अस्ति<BR>क्षीरं यस्य P. II. 2. 24 Vārt.]<BR>having milk.<BR>--नास्ति ind. doubtful,<BR>partly true and partly not; ˚त्वं,<BR>ता doubtful or partial existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तित्वं|अस्तित्व
अस्तित्वं Existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिमत्|अस्तिमन्त्
अस्तिमत् a. [अस्ति विद्यमानं धनमस्य]<BR>Possessed of property, wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तु
अस्तु ind. (Strictly 3rd. pers. sing.<BR>Imperative of अस्) Let it be, be it<BR>so, well, implying permission; it is<BR>also said to have the senses of pain,<BR>contest, jealousy, superiority,<BR>acceptance, praise, indication, and<BR>acceptance with envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तुंकार
अस्तुंकार a. [P. VI. 3. 70 Vārt.]<BR>1 Efficacious, working (as a<BR>medicine).<BR>--2 Producing that which the<BR>physician promises shall be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयत|असंयतः
असंयत a.<BR>1 Unrestrained, not<BR>under control.<BR>--2 Not tied, as in<BR>असंयतोऽपि मोक्षार्थी; ˚आत्मन् having<BR>the soul unrestrained.<BR>--तः N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयमः|असंयम
असंयमः Absence of control or<BR>restraint, especially of the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयुक्त
असंयुक्त a.<BR>1 Separated.<BR>--2 Not<BR>conjunct (as a consonant).<BR>--क्तं<BR>1<BR>Non-combination.<BR>--2 (In gram.)<BR>Hiatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंयुत|असंयुतः
असंयुत a. Unblended,<BR>ununited.<BR>--तः An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंविदान
असंविदान a. Ignorant, foolish;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">Page0209-b+ 54</a>]<BR>असंविदानेव जामात्रे कुप्यसिं U. 7;<BR>Ki. 18. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंवृत
असंवृत a. Uncovered, exposed.<BR>--तं N. of a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंव्यवहित
असंव्यवहित a. Immediate,<BR>without any interval (of time or space).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंशय
असंशय a. Free from doubt,<BR>certain.<BR>--यं ind. Without doubt,<BR>undoubtedly, certainly, assuredly;<BR>असंशयं क्षत्रपरिग्रहक्षमा Ś. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्रव
असंश्रव a. Out of hearing,<BR>inaudible; असंश्रवे out of the hearing<BR>of; असंश्रवे चैव गुरोर्न किंचिदपि<BR>कीर्तयेत् Ms. 2. 203.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंश्लिष्ट|असंश्लिष्टः
असंश्लिष्ट a. Not joined or<BR>united.<BR>--ष्टः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसृतिः|असंसृति
असंसृतिः f. Non-return to<BR>worldly existence, absorption into<BR>the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंसृष्ट
असंसृष्ट a.<BR>1 Not mixed with,<BR>not connected.<BR>--2 Not living in<BR>common, not reunited after<BR>partition of property (as an heir).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्कृत|असंस्कृतः
असंस्कृत a.<BR>1 Unpolished, not<BR>refined or cleansed &c.<BR>--2 Not<BR>decorated or adorned.<BR>--3 One over whom<BR>no purificatory rite (any one of the<BR>samskāras) has been performed.<BR>--तः<BR>An ungrammatical form (अपशब्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्तुत
असंस्तुत a.<BR>1 Unknown,<BR>unacquainted, not familiar; असंस्तुत इव<BR>परित्यक्तो बांधवो जनः K. 173, 308;<BR>Ki. 3. 2.<BR>--2 Unusual, strange;<BR>असंस्तुतेषु प्रसभं भयेषु Ki. 3. 21.<BR>--3 Not<BR>in harmony or agreement with;<BR>धावति पश्चादसंस्तुतं चेतः Ś. 1. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थानं|असंस्थान
असंस्थानं<BR>1 Absence of cohesion.<BR>--2 Disorder, confusion.<BR>--3 Want,<BR>destitution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थित
असंस्थित a.<BR>1 Not arranged,<BR>disordered, irregular;<BR>असंस्थितमभूयिष्ठं H. 3. 109.<BR>--2 Not collected.<BR>--3<BR>Moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंस्थितिः|असंस्थिति
असंस्थितिः f. Disorder, confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंहत|असंहतः
असंहत a. Not joined or united,<BR>scattered, loose, straggling.<BR>--तः<BR>The Puruṣa or soul (in Sān. phil.).<BR>--तं A form of array, open order<BR>of troops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकृत्
असकृत् ind. Not once,<BR>repeatedly, often and often;<BR>असकृदेकरथेन तरस्विना R. 9. 23; Me. 92, 93.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--समाधिः repeated<BR>meditation.<BR>--गर्भवासः repeated birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असकौ
असकौ a. = असौ this or that;<BR>Śi. 7. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्त
असक्त a.<BR>1 Not excessively<BR>attached, not feeling interested in,<BR>indifferent (to); असक्तः सुखमन्वभूत्<BR>R. 1. 21.<BR>--2 Not entangled;<BR>Ś. 2. 12.<BR>--3 Not united, detached.<BR>--4<BR>Not attached to worldly feelings<BR>and connections.<BR>--क्तं ind.<BR>1<BR>Without being excessively attached or<BR>addicted to; Ki. 1. 11.<BR>--2 Without<BR>any hindrance, quickly; Dk. 35.<BR>--3<BR>Incessantly, ceaselessly; Ki. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्थ
असक्थ a. Thighless (<BR>P. V. 4. 121).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असक्र
असक्र a. Ved. Not ceasing to<BR>flow, not drying up; not going<BR>elsewhere (असंक्रमणी); Rv. 6. 63. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असखिः|असखि
असखिः An enemy, adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असगोत्र
असगोत्र a. Not belonging to<BR>the same Gotra or family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंकसुक|असङ्कसुक
असंकसुक a. Not fickle, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंकुल|असङ्कुल|असंकुलः|असङ्कुलः
असंकुल a. Not crowded, open,<BR>clear, broad, (as a road &c.).<BR>--लः<BR>A broad road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंक्रांत
असंक्रांत a. Not gone over or<BR>transmitted; ˚मासः an intercalary<BR>month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्य|असङ्ख्य|असंख्यः|असङ्ख्यः
असंख्य a. Beyond calculation,<BR>numberless, countless, innumerable;<BR>Ms. 1. 80; 12. 15; ˚ता, --त्वं infinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्यात|असङ्ख्यात|असंख्यातं
असंख्यात a. Countless,<BR>innumerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंख्येय|असङ्ख्येय|असंख्येयः
असंख्येय a. Innumerable.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--2 An epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu; V. Sahas.<BR>--यं An<BR>exceedingly large number.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गुण a. innumerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंग|असङ्ग|असंगः
असंग a.<BR>1 Not attached, free<BR>from worldly ties.<BR>--2 Not hindered<BR>or obstructed, not blunted;<BR>असंगमद्रिष्वपि सारवत्तया R. 3. 63; तस्य<BR>मूर्घ्नि शितं खड्गमसक्तं पर्वतेष्वपि Mb.<BR>--3<BR>Not united, solitary, unassailed.<BR>--गः<BR>1 Non-attachment; Ms. 6. 75.<BR>--2 Puruṣa or soul (in Sān. phil.)<BR>˚वत् a. not attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगत|असङ्गत
असंगत a.<BR>1 Ununited,<BR>unaccompanied with.<BR>--2 Improbable,<BR>inconsistent.<BR>--3 Unequal.<BR>--4<BR>Unesteemed.<BR>--5 Unbecoming, improper.<BR>--6<BR>Rude, ill-mannered, unpolished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगतिः|असङ्गति|असंगति
असंगतिः f.<BR>1 Not associating with.<BR>--2 Incongruity, improbability.<BR>--3<BR>(In Rhet.) A figure of speech in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-a" target="_blank">Page0210-a+ 56</a>]<BR>which a cause and the effect are<BR>represented as locally different or<BR>separated (in which there is an apparent<BR>violation of the relation between<BR>cause and effect); भिन्नदेशतयात्यंतं<BR>कार्यकारणभूतयोः । युगपद्धर्मयोर्यत्र ख्यातिः सा<BR>स्यादसंगतिः ॥ K. P. 10; विरुद्धं<BR>भिन्नदेशत्वं कार्यहेत्वोरसंगतिः । विषं जलधरैः पीतं<BR>मूर्छिताः पथिकांगनाः ॥ Kuval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0209-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगम|असङ्गम|असंगमः
असंगम a. Not united.<BR>--मः<BR>1<BR>Separation, disunion.<BR>--2 Incongruity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंगिन्|असङ्गिन्
असंगिन् a.<BR>1 Not united or<BR>associated.<BR>--2 Not attached to the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असचद्विष्
असचद्विष् a. Ved.<BR>1 Persecuting<BR>those who are not (his)<BR>worshippers.<BR>--2 Having no enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असजात
असजात a. Ved. Not related<BR>by blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असजात्य
असजात्य a. Without<BR>consanguinity or blood-relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंज्ञ
असंज्ञ a. Insensible.<BR>--ज्ञा<BR>Disunion, disagreement, discord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्|असन्त्
असत् a.<BR>1 Not being or<BR>existing; तदभावे सदप्यसत् H. 3. 3;<BR>असति त्वयि Ku. 4. 12; Ms. 9. 154.<BR>--2<BR>Non-existent, unreal; आत्मनो<BR>ब्रह्मणोऽभेदमसंतं कः करिष्यति.<BR>--3 Bad (opp.<BR>सत्); सदसद्व्यक्तिहेतवः R. 1. 10.<BR>--4<BR>Wicked, vile, evil; as ˚विचार.<BR>--5<BR>Not manifest.<BR>--6 Wrong, improper,<BR>false, untrue; इति यदुक्तं तदसत् (oft.<BR>occurring in controversial works).<BR>--7 Not answering its purpose. --m.<BR>(न्) Indra. --n. (त्)<BR>1<BR>Non-existence, non-entity; नासदासीन्नो सदासीत्<BR>Rv. 10. 129. 1; असद्वा इदमग्र आसीत्<BR>ततो वै सदजायत Ait. Br., Ms. 12. 118;<BR>1. 11, 14, 74.<BR>--2 An evil, a harm.<BR>--3 Untruth, falsehood.<BR>--ती An<BR>unchaste woman; असती भवति सलज्जा<BR>Pt. 1. 418.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्येतृ m.<BR>a Brāhmaṇa who reads heterodox<BR>works, one who neglects his<BR>ownŚākhā and studies another; also cal<BR>led शाखारंडः; स्वशाखां यः परित्यज्य अन्यत्र<BR>कुरुते श्रमं । शाखारंडः स विज्ञेयो वर्जयेत्तं<BR>क्रियासु च ॥.<BR>--आगमः {1} a heterodox<BR>Śāstra or doctrine. {2} acquisition<BR>(of wealth) by unfair or foul means.<BR>{3} a foul means itself.<BR>--आचार a.<BR>following evil practices, wicked.<BR>--(रः) an evil practice.<BR>--आचारिन्<BR>a. one who follows evil practices,<BR>wicked, vile.<BR>--कर्मन्, --क्रिया &c. see<BR>below.<BR>--कल्पना {1} an untrue action,<BR>one which never took place. {2}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">Page0210-b+ 57</a>]<BR>fabrication of falsehood.<BR>--ख्यातिः f. wrong<BR>or improper perception or<BR>knowledge.<BR>--ग्र (ग्रा) हः {1} a bad trick.<BR>{2} a bad opinion, prejudice. {3}<BR>childish desire.<BR>--चेष्टितं harm,<BR>injury; प्राणिष्वसच्चेष्टितं Ś. 5. 9.<BR>--जनः<BR>a bad, wicked, or contemptible man.<BR>--दृश् a. evil-eyed.<BR>--पथः {1} a bad road<BR>(lit.). {2} evil practices or doctrines;<BR>नाशो हंत सतामसत्पथजुषामायुः समानां<BR>शतं Bv. 4. 36.<BR>--परिग्रहः acceptance<BR>of a bad road.<BR>--पुत्रः {1} a childless<BR>man. {2} a bad son or disreputable<BR>son.<BR>--प्रतिग्रहः {1} present of bad<BR>things. {2} receiving unfit presents<BR>(such as तिल) or from improper<BR>persons.<BR>--भावः {1} non-existence,<BR>absence. {2} a bad or wicked opinion.<BR>{3} an evil disposition.<BR>--वृत्ति,<BR>--व्यवहार a. following evil practices,<BR>wicked. (--त्तिः f.) {1} a low or<BR>degrading occupation. {2} wickedness.<BR>--व्यवहार a. following evil practices.<BR>--(रः) evil practice.<BR>--शास्त्रं {1} a<BR>wrong doctrine. {2} a heterodox<BR>doctrine (such as that of the<BR>Buddhas).<BR>--संसर्गः bad company.<BR>--हेतुः<BR>{1} a statement having exceptions (in<BR>न्याय). {2} a bad or fallacious hetu;<BR>see हेत्वाभास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असतायी
असतायी Wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृ
असत्कृ {c8c} U. To disrespect,<BR>dishonour, not to receive hospitably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कर्मन्|असत्कर्म्मन्
असत्कर्मन् a. Of bad conduct,<BR>wicked. --n.<BR>--(र्म)<BR>1 A bad action<BR>(prohibited by the Vedas).<BR>--2<BR>Wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कारः|असत्कार
असत्कारः, असत्क्रिया Disrespect,<BR>dishonour, bad or inhospitable<BR>reception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्क्रिया
असत्कारः, असत्क्रिया Disrespect,<BR>dishonour, bad or inhospitable<BR>reception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्कृत
असत्कृत a.<BR>1 Not honoured,<BR>disrespected.<BR>--2 Done from improper<BR>motives.<BR>--तं A bad or wicked deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्ता
असत्ता<BR>1 Non-existence.<BR>--2<BR>Untruth.<BR>--3 Wickedness, badness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्त्व
असत्त्व a.<BR>1 Without energy or<BR>strength.<BR>--2 Having no animal.<BR>--3 Having no goodness.<BR>--त्त्वं<BR>1<BR>Non-existence.<BR>--2 Unreality,<BR>untruth.<BR>--3 Wickedness, badness.<BR>--4<BR>Duet.<BR>--5 Darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असत्य|असत्यः
असत्य a.<BR>1 Untrue, false.<BR>--2<BR>Imaginary, unreal;<BR>असत्यकंठार्पितबाहुबंधना Ku. 5. 57.<BR>--त्यः A liar.<BR>--त्यं<BR>Falsehood, untruth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वादिन्<BR>a. speaking falsely, liar.<BR>--संध a.<BR>not true to one's promise, false,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">Page0210-c+ 58</a>]<BR>perfidious, treacherous; ˚धे जने सखी पदं<BR>कारिता Ś. 4.<BR>--सन्निभ a. improbable,<BR>unlikely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असदृश|असदृशः
असदृश a. (शी f.)<BR>1 Dissimilar,<BR>unlike.<BR>--2 Unfit, improper,<BR>incongruous; ˚व्यवहारिन् behaving<BR>improperly H. 2; ˚संयोगकारिन्<BR>K. 12 unworthy; मातः किमप्यसदृशं<BR>विकृतं वचस्ते Ve. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असद्यस्
असद्यस् ind. Not immediately,<BR>after delay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्
असन् n. Blood(used only in<BR>the declension of असृज् after acc.<BR>pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असनं|असन|असनः
असनं Throwing, discharging,<BR>casting; as in इष्वसनं a bow.<BR>--नः N.<BR>of a tree (पीतसाल);<BR>निरसनैरसनैरवृथार्थता Śi. 6. 47.<BR>--ना Ved. A missile,<BR>an arrow.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पर्णी N. of a<BR>tree (सातल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असनिः|असनि
असनिः One who throws &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंतति|असन्तति|असन्ततिः
असंतति a. Having no issue,<BR>childless.<BR>--तिः, --नः<BR>Childlessness, failure of issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंतान|असन्तान|असन्तानः
असंतान a. Having no issue,<BR>childless.<BR>--तिः, --नः<BR>Childlessness, failure of issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंदिग्ध|असन्दिग्ध
असंदिग्ध a.<BR>1 Not doubtful,<BR>distinct, certain, clear.<BR>--2 Not<BR>vanished.<BR>--3 Confident,<BR>unsuspected.<BR>--ग्धं ind. Certainly,<BR>undoubtedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंदित|असन्दित
असंदित --न a. Ved. Not<BR>restrained, free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंदिन
असंदित --न a. Ved. Not<BR>restrained, free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असन्न
असन्न a. Ved. Without rest or<BR>repose, untiring, restless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंधि|असन्धि|असंधिः
असंधि a.<BR>1 Not joined together<BR>(as words).<BR>--2 Not bound or<BR>restrained, at liberty.<BR>--धिः Absence<BR>of Saṃdhi or euphony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनद्ध|असन्नद्ध|असन्नद्धः
असंनद्ध a.<BR>1 Unarmed.<BR>--2<BR>Pretending to knowledge,<BR>conceited (पंडितंमन्य).<BR>--3 Proud, arrogant.<BR>--4 Born or produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिकर्षः|असन्निकर्ष|असंनिकर्ष
असंनिकर्षः<BR>1 Non-perception of<BR>objects, not bringing them to the<BR>mind.<BR>--2 Remoteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिकृष्ट|असन्निकृष्ट
असंनिकृष्ट a.<BR>1 Unperceived.<BR>--2<BR>Not near, remote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिधिः|असन्निधि|असंनिधि
असंनिधिः, --निधानं<BR>1 Absence,<BR>distance.<BR>--2 Confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिधानं|असन्निधान|असंनिधान
असंनिधिः, --निधानं<BR>1 Absence,<BR>distance.<BR>--2 Confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिहित|असन्निहित
असंनिहित a.<BR>1 Not near, distant.<BR>--2 Placed in a wrong manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंनिवृत्तिः|असन्निवृत्ति
असंनिवृत्तिः f. Non-return;<BR>असंनिवृत्त्यै तदतीतमेव Ś. 6. 9 gone<BR>never to return; R. 8. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपत्न
असपत्न a.<BR>1 Without a rival<BR>wife.<BR>--2 Not an enemy, friendly.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">Page0211-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--3 Without enemies, not attacked.<BR>--त्नं Undisturbed condition, peace.<BR>--त्नी A sort of brick (इष्टकाभेदः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0210-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असपिंड|असपिण्ड
असपिंड a. Not connected by<BR>offerings of rice-balls; or, not<BR>connected by blood-relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असभ्य|असभ्यः
असभ्य a. Unfit for an<BR>assembly, vulgar, low, obscene, indecent<BR>(words &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम|असमः
असम a.<BR>1 Uneven, odd (as a<BR>number); असमशीलाः खलु मृगाः<BR>Bv. 1. 2 mean, contemptible.<BR>--2 Unequal<BR>(in space, number or dignity);<BR>असमैः समीयमानः Pt. 1. 74.<BR>--3<BR>Unequalled, matchless, unsurpassed;<BR>समवतारसमैरसमैस्तटैः Ki. 5. 7;<BR>वाद्यविशेषाणामसमः श्रोता K. 12;<BR>Ms. 10. 73.<BR>--4 Uneven, not level (as<BR>ground).<BR>--मः N. of Buddha.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इषुः, --बाणः, --सायकः ‘having<BR>an odd number of arrows,’ epithets<BR>of Cupid who has five arrows.<BR>--नयन, --नेत्र, --लोचन a. ‘having an odd<BR>number of eyes’, epithets of Śiva,<BR>who has three eyes.<BR>--वृत्तं a metre<BR>in which the ganas are not the<BR>same in all lines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमग्र
असमग्र a. Incomplete; partial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमंजस|असमञ्जस|असमञ्जसं
असमंजस a.<BR>1 Indistinct,<BR>unintelligible;<BR>स्खलदसमंजसमुग्धजल्पितं ते U. 4. 4; Māl. 10. 2 faltering,<BR>inarticulate and pretty prattle.<BR>--2<BR>Unbecoming, improper; यद्यपि न<BR>कापि हानिर्द्राक्षामन्यस्य रासभे चरति ।<BR>असमंजसमिति मत्वा तथापि तरलायते<BR>चेतः ॥ Udb.<BR>--3 Absurd,<BR>nonsensical, foolish.<BR>--सं Non-conformity,<BR>disparity, difference. --ind.<BR>1<BR>Unbecomingly, improperly.<BR>--2 In a<BR>fluctuating or confused manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमद्
असमद् f. Ved. Non-conflict,<BR>harmony, concord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमद
असमद a. [सह मदेन गर्वेण समदः कलहः<BR>स नास्ति यत्र] Without a quarrel or<BR>opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमन
असमन a.<BR>1 Of different colours<BR>or minds.<BR>--2 Going in different<BR>directions.<BR>--3 Uneven, unequal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमयः|असमय
असमयः<BR>1 Unseasonableness.<BR>--2<BR>Unfit or unfavourable time; असमये<BR>मतिरुन्मिषति ध्रुवं N. 4. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमर्थ|असमर्थः
असमर्थ a.<BR>1 Not able or<BR>competent.<BR>--2 Weak, feeble.<BR>--3 (In<BR>Rhet.) Powerless to convey the<BR>intended meaning, a defect of a word;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">Page0211-b+ 65</a>]<BR>यत्तदर्थं पठ्यते न च तत्रास्य शाक्तिः तदसमर्थत्वं<BR>K. P. 7; e. g. in कुंजं हंति कृशोदरी, हन्,<BR>though read in root-books in<BR>the sense of ‘going’, is here<BR>powerless to convey that meaning.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--समासः a compound in which the<BR>conjunction of words is not as it<BR>should be; e. g. in अश्राद्धभोजिन्,<BR>असूर्यंपश्य, अ goes not with श्राद्ध or सूर्य<BR>but with भोजिन् or पश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवायिन्
असमवायिन् a. Not intimate<BR>or inherent, accidental, separable.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारणं (In logic) an<BR>accidental cause, not inherent and<BR>intimate relation;<BR>गुणकर्ममात्रवृत्तिज्ञेयमथाप्यसमवायिहेतुत्वं Bhāṣā P.; यथा तंतुयोगः<BR>पटस्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमवेत
असमवेत a. Not classed together,<BR>incoherent; ˚रूपं incoherently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमस्त
असमस्त a.<BR>1 Incomplete,<BR>imperfect, partial, not whole.<BR>--2 (In<BR>gram.) Not joined in a compound,<BR>not compounded.<BR>--3 Uncollected.<BR>--4 Separate, detached, unconnected<BR>(opp. व्यस्त).<BR>--स्तं An<BR>uncompounded word (the sentence showing the<BR>dissolution of a compound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाति
असमाति a. Having nothing<BR>equal, unparalleled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमान|असमानं
असमान a. Unequalled,<BR>matchless; ˚लावण्यं Dk. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाप्त|असमाप्तं
असमाप्त a.<BR>1 Not completed or<BR>finished, left incomplete; R. 8. 76;<BR>Ku. 4. 19.<BR>--2 Not fully acquired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावृत्तः|असमावृत्त
असमावृत्तः --त्तकः A religious<BR>student who has<BR>not completed<BR>the period of his residence with his<BR>preceptor; Ms. 11. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावृत्तकः|असमावृत्तक
असमावृत्तः --त्तकः A religious<BR>student who has<BR>not completed<BR>the period of his residence with his<BR>preceptor; Ms. 11. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावर्तकः|असमावर्तक|असमावर्त्तक
असमावर्तकः A religious<BR>student who has<BR>not completed<BR>the period of his residence with his<BR>preceptor; Ms. 11. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमावृत्तिकः|असमावृत्तिक
असमावृत्तिकः A religious<BR>student who has<BR>not completed<BR>the period of his residence with his<BR>preceptor; Ms. 11. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमाहार|असमाहारः
असमाहार a. Not joined.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>Non-recovery of anything.<BR>--2<BR>Disunion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असमीक्ष्य
असमीक्ष्य ind. Not having<BR>(properly) considered.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारिन्<BR>a. acting inconsiderately,<BR>imprudent, not circumspect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंपत्ति|असम्पत्ति|असंपत्तिः
असंपत्ति a. Unlucky, poor,<BR>miserable.<BR>--त्तिः f.<BR>1 Ill-luck, want of<BR>success or wealth.<BR>--2<BR>Non-accomplishment, failure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंपूर्ण|असम्पूर्ण|असम्पूर्ण्ण
असंपूर्ण a.<BR>1 Not complete,<BR>unfinished.<BR>--2 Not whole or entire.<BR>--3 Not full, partial, as the moon;<BR>चंद्रमसंपूर्णमंडलमिदानीं Mu. 1. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंप्रज्ञात
असंप्रज्ञात a. Not well discerned<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">Page0211-c+ 56</a>]<BR>or distinguished, a kind of समाधि<BR>(= निर्विकल्पसमाधि q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबद्ध|असम्बद्ध|असम्बद्धं
असंबद्ध a.<BR>1 Unconnected,<BR>incoherent.<BR>--2 Nonsensical, absurd,<BR>unmeaning; ˚प्रलापिणी talking<BR>nonsense; असंबद्धः खल्वसि Mk. 9<BR>absurd fellow; ˚मनोरथा Māl. 2;<BR>˚द्धं प्रलपितुं प्रवृत्तः Ratn. 2.<BR>--3<BR>Improper, wrong; Ms. 12. 6.<BR>--द्धं An<BR>absurd sentence, unmeaning or<BR>nonsensical speech; e. g. यावज्जीवमहं<BR>मौनी when uttered by some one; see<BR>अबद्ध also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबंध|असम्बन्ध|असंबन्ध|असंबन्धः
असंबंध a. Unconnected, not<BR>relating or belonging to.<BR>--धः<BR>Nonconnection, absence of any relation<BR>or connection; यद्वा<BR>साध्यवदन्यस्मिन्नसंबंध उदाहृतः Bhāṣā P. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंबाध|असम्बाध
असंबाध a.<BR>1 Not narrow,<BR>spacious, wide.<BR>--2 Not crowded with<BR>people, lonely, solitary.<BR>--3 Open,<BR>accessible; Ki. 3. 53.<BR>--4<BR>Separated by an interval;<BR>द्विपैरसंबाधमयांबभूवे Śi. 3. 67.<BR>--5 Without pain.<BR>--धा<BR>N. of a metre consisting of 56<BR>syllables.<BR>--धं Ved. Open space.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभव|असम्भव|असंभवः
असंभव a. Improbable, unlikely;<BR>inconsistent; असंभवं हेममृगस्य जन्म<BR>H. 1. 28.<BR>--वः<BR>1 Non-existence; रामेणापि<BR>कथं न हेमहरिणस्यासंभवो लक्षितः<BR>Pt. 2. 4; Śi. 16. 34.<BR>--2 Improbability,<BR>impossibility.<BR>--वा, --वं An<BR>extraordinary event.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभव्य
असंभव्य, असंभाविन् a.<BR>1<BR>Impossible; असंभव्यं न वक्तव्यं.<BR>--2<BR>Incomprehensible.<BR>--व्यं ind. In an<BR>incomprehensible or extraordinary manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभाविन्
असंभव्य, असंभाविन् a.<BR>1<BR>Impossible; असंभव्यं न वक्तव्यं.<BR>--2<BR>Incomprehensible.<BR>--व्यं ind. In an<BR>incomprehensible or extraordinary manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभावना|असम्भावना
असंभावना<BR>1 Difficulty or<BR>impossibility of comprehending.<BR>--2<BR>Improbability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभावनीय|असम्भावनीय
असंभावनीय, असंभाव्य a.<BR>1<BR>Impossible.<BR>--2 Inconceivable,<BR>incomprehensible.<BR>--व्यं = असंभव्यं q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभाव्य
असंभावनीय, असंभाव्य a.<BR>1<BR>Impossible.<BR>--2 Inconceivable,<BR>incomprehensible.<BR>--व्यं = असंभव्यं q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभूतिः|असम्भूति|असंभूति
असंभूतिः f.<BR>1 Non-existence.<BR>--2<BR>Not being born again.<BR>--3<BR>Undeveloped cause (प्रकृति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभृत
असंभृत a.<BR>1 Not brought about<BR>by artificial means, not artificial,<BR>natural; असंभृतं मंडनमंगयष्टेः<BR>Ku. 1. 31.<BR>--2 Not properly nourished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंभ्रम|असम्भ्रम|असंभ्रमः
असंभ्रम a. Free from agitation,<BR>composed, cool.<BR>--मः Calmness,<BR>steadiness; R. 4. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमत|असम्मत|असंमतः|असम्मतः
असंमत a.<BR>1 Disapproved, not<BR>allowed or permitted, not<BR>consented to; असंमतः कस्तव मुक्तिमार्गं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">Page0212-a+ 55</a>]<BR>Ku. 3. 5.<BR>--2 Disliked, averse.<BR>--3<BR>Dissentient, differing from.<BR>--तः An<BR>enemy; द्यतु दोषैरसंमतान् K. P. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आदायिन् a. taking<BR>without the consent of the possessor,<BR>such as a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0211-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमतिः|असम्मति|असंमति
असंमतिः f.<BR>1 Dissent, difference of<BR>opinion, disagreement.<BR>--2<BR>Disapproval; dislike, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमानः|असम्मान|असंमान|असम्मानं
असंमानः Disrespect, disgrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमित|असम्मित
असंमित a. Not limited, immense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमूढ|असम्मूढ
असंमूढ a.<BR>1 Not infatuated,<BR>undeluded.<BR>--2 Steady, composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमोहः|असम्मोह|असंमोह
असंमोहः<BR>1 Absence of infatuation.<BR>--2 Steadiness, composure, coolness.<BR>--3 Real knowledge, true insight<BR>(into a thing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असंमृष्ट|असम्मृष्ट
असंमृष्ट a. Ved.<BR>1 Not blended<BR>or united together.<BR>--2 Without any<BR>hurt, uninjured, safe.<BR>--3 Not<BR>cleansed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असम्यंच्|असम्यञ्च्
असम्यंच् a. (--मीची f.)<BR>1 Bad,<BR>improper, incorrect.<BR>--2 Imperfect,<BR>incomplete.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारिन् a.<BR>{1} inexpert, incompetent. {2}<BR>ill-conducted, profligate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असरुः|असरु
असरुः [सरति सृ-उन् न˚ त˚] N. of<BR>a medicinal plant; Blumea Lacera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असर्व
असर्व a. Not all; ˚वीर a. Ved.<BR>not having all one's men collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असलं|असल
असलं [अस्यते क्षिप्यतेऽनेन; अस् +<BR>कलच्]<BR>1 Iron.<BR>--2 A Mantra used in<BR>discharging a missile.<BR>--3 Arms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असवर्ण|असवर्ण्ण
असवर्ण a. Of a different caste<BR>or tribe; अपि नाम<BR>कुलपतोरियमसवर्णक्षेत्रसंभवा स्यात् Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असश्चत्|असश्चन्त्
असश्चत् a. Ved.<BR>1 Not disposed<BR>to go, not going; Rv. 8. 31. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Unceasing, inexhaustible, not drying<BR>up.<BR>--3 Not closed up, not defeated<BR>or overcome, untouched (as by any<BR>one attempting to enter a door).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अससत्|अससन्त्
अससत् a. Ved. Not sleeping,<BR>watchful, wakeful; Rv. 1. 143. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असह
असह a.<BR>1 Not enduring,<BR>intolerant, impatient of; कालक्षेपासहः<BR>Ks. 9. 37.<BR>--2 Unable to bear, support, or<BR>endure; oft. with gen. of object;<BR>कुमुमपातस्याप्यसहं शरीरं K. 250; सा<BR>स्त्रीस्वभावादसहा भरस्य Mu. 4. 13; असहतरा<BR>कुचकुंभयोर्भरस्य Śi. 7. 48; 10. 81;<BR>Ki. 7. 7.<BR>--हं The middle of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहन|असहनः
असहन a. Not enduring,<BR>intolerant, impatient, envious, jealous;<BR>दूरारूढः खलु प्रणयोऽसहनः V. 4; 4. 27;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">Page0212-b+ 66</a>]<BR>Me. 54; Ratn. 3. 15; Śi. 15. 39.<BR>--नः An enemy.<BR>--नं Intolerance,<BR>impatience; परगुणासहनं = असूया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहनीय
असहनीय a. Unbearable,<BR>insufferable,<BR>intolerable; असह्यपीडं<BR>भगवन्नृणमंत्यमवेहि मे R. 1. 71; 18. 25;<BR>Ku. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहितव्य
असहितव्य a. Unbearable,<BR>insufferable,<BR>intolerable; असह्यपीडं<BR>भगवन्नृणमंत्यमवेहि मे R. 1. 71; 18. 25;<BR>Ku. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असह्य|असह्यः
असह्य a. Unbearable,<BR>insufferable,<BR>intolerable; असह्यपीडं<BR>भगवन्नृणमंत्यमवेहि मे R. 1. 71; 18. 25;<BR>Ku. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहमान
असहमान a. Impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहिष्णु
असहिष्णु a.<BR>1 Impatient,<BR>unenduring, envious or jealous of; as in<BR>परसुखासहिष्णुः.<BR>--2 Quarrelsome; ˚ता<BR>impatience, envy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहाय
असहाय a.<BR>1 Friendless, lonely,<BR>solitary; एकमसहायमगारं<BR>P. V. 1. 113 Com.<BR>--2 Without companions<BR>or assistants; Ms. 7. 30, 55; ˚ता,<BR>--त्वं loneliness, solitude; Ms. 6. 44;<BR>˚वत् without companions, friendless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असहित
असहित a. Unassociated,<BR>unaccompanied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षात्
असाक्षात् ind.<BR>1 Not before the<BR>eyes, invisibly, imperceptibly.<BR>--2<BR>Not present (used adjectively).<BR>--3<BR>Indirectly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः absence;<BR>non-perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षिक
असाक्षिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Having no<BR>witness, unattested, unwitnessed;<BR>असाक्षिकेषु त्वर्थेषु मिथो विवदमानयोः<BR>Ms. 8. 109.<BR>--2 Without a ruler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्षिन्
असाक्षिन् a.<BR>1 Not an eye-witness.<BR>--2 One whose evidence is not<BR>admissible (in law).<BR>--3 One who is<BR>disqualified to attest a legal<BR>document.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाक्ष्यं|असाक्ष्य
असाक्ष्यं Want of evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाद
असाद a. Ved. Not sitting;<BR>having no seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधन
असाधन a. Without means,<BR>destitute of resources, materials, or<BR>instruments; Pt. 2. 1.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Non-accomplishment.<BR>--2 Not proving or<BR>establishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधनीय
असाधनीय, असाध्य a.<BR>1 Not to be<BR>accomplished or completed, not<BR>proper, easy, or capable of being<BR>accomplished; नास्ति असाध्यं नाम मनोभुवः<BR>K. 157.<BR>--2 Not capable of being<BR>proved.<BR>--3 Incurable, irremediable<BR>(as a disease or patient); असाध्यः<BR>कुरुते कोपं प्राप्ते काले गदो यथा<BR>Śi. 2. 84; असाध्य इति वैद्येनातुर इव V. 3;<BR>Mv. 4. 23; भिषजामसाध्यं R. 8. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाध्य|असाध्यं
असाधनीय, असाध्य a.<BR>1 Not to be<BR>accomplished or completed, not<BR>proper, easy, or capable of being<BR>accomplished; नास्ति असाध्यं नाम मनोभुवः<BR>K. 157.<BR>--2 Not capable of being<BR>proved.<BR>--3 Incurable, irremediable<BR>(as a disease or patient); असाध्यः<BR>कुरुते कोपं प्राप्ते काले गदो यथा<BR>Śi. 2. 84; असाध्य इति वैद्येनातुर इव V. 3;<BR>Mv. 4. 23; भिषजामसाध्यं R. 8. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधारण|असाधारणं|असाधारणः
असाधारण a.<BR>1 Not common,<BR>peculiar, special, specific.<BR>--2 (In<BR>logic) Existing neither in सपक्ष or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-c" target="_blank">Page0212-c+ 56</a>]<BR>विपक्ष as a hetu; यस्तूभयस्माद् व्यावृत्तः<BR>स त्वसाधारणो मतः.<BR>--3 Not to be<BR>claimed by any one else, exclusively<BR>belonging to one (as wealth &c.);<BR>पिता पुत्रांतरेष्वपि साधारणो माता<BR>त्वसाधारणी Mit.<BR>--णः A fallacy or हेत्वाभास in<BR>Logic; one of the three kinds of<BR>अनैकांतिक q. v.<BR>--णं Speciality,<BR>special property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाधु
असाधु a.<BR>1 Not good, bad,<BR>distasteful, unpleasant; अतोर्हसि<BR>क्षंतुमसाधु साधु वा Ki. 1. 4.<BR>--2 Wicked.<BR>--3<BR>Illbehaved (with loc.); असाधुर्मातरि Sk.<BR>--4 Corrupt, not properly formed or<BR>Sanskrit (as a word).<BR>--ध्वी An<BR>unchaste woman. ˚ता, --त्वं<BR>Wickedness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वृत्ता an unchaste<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामयिक
असामयिक a.(की f.)<BR>Inopportune, unseasonable; Ki. 2. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामान्य
असामान्य a.<BR>1 Not common,<BR>peculiar, exclusive, sole; R. 15. 39.<BR>--2 Extraordinary.<BR>--न्यं A peculiar or<BR>special property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असामि
असामि a. Ved. Not half, whole,<BR>complete.<BR>--मि ind. Completely,<BR>fully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असांप्रत|असाम्प्रत|असाम्प्रतं
असांप्रत a. Unfit, unbecoming,<BR>improper; अनाचक्षाणयाऽसांप्रतं कृतं<BR>M. 5.<BR>--तं ind. Improperly, unfitly;<BR>oft. used with an adjectival force =<BR>असांप्रत; विषवृक्षोऽपि संवर्ध्य स्वयं<BR>छेत्तुमसांप्रतं Ku. 2. 55; संप्रत्यसांप्रतं वक्तुमुक्ते<BR>मुसलपाणिना Śi. 2. 71. R. 8. 61;<BR>Pt. 1. 245.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाम्यं|असाम्य
असाम्यं<BR>1 Difference,<BR>dissimilarity.<BR>--2 Unsuitableness (in medicine<BR>or diet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असार|असारं|असारः
असार a. [न. ब.]<BR>1 Sapless,<BR>insipid.<BR>--2 (a) Without essence,<BR>useless; असारः खलु संसारः Udb.; (b)<BR>worthless, unsubstantial, without<BR>strength, stuff or value, deprived of<BR>its essence; असारं संसारं परिमुषितरत्नं<BR>त्रिभुवनं Māl. 5. 30; U. 1; असारे खलु<BR>संसारे सारमेतच्चतुष्टयं Dharm. 12, 13;<BR>Bh. 3. 146.<BR>--3 Vain, unprofitable;<BR>Pt. 1. 28.<BR>--4 Weak, feeble, infirm,<BR>fragile; श्रुतिपथमसारं Mu. 6. 14;<BR>बहूनामप्यसाराणां संहतिः कार्यसाधिका (<BR>समवायो हि दुर्जयः) Pt. 1. 331; Śi. 2. 50.<BR>--5 Poor; Dk. 40.<BR>--रः, --रं<BR>1<BR>Unessential or unimportant portion;<BR>कुर्यादसारभंगो हि सारभंगमपि स्फुटं<BR>H. 3. 89.<BR>--2 N. of a tree (एरंड).<BR>--3 Aloe<BR>wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0212-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असारता
असारता<BR>1 Saplessness.<BR>--2<BR>Worthlessness; Y. 2. 60.<BR>--3 Unsubstantial<BR>nature; transitory or frail state;<BR>धिगिमां देहभृतामसारतां R. 8. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असाहसं|असाहस
असाहसं Absence of violence,<BR>gentleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिः|असि
असिः [अस्यते क्षिप्यते; अस्-इन्<BR>Uṇ. 4. 139]<BR>1 A sword.<BR>--2 A knife used<BR>for killing animals.<BR>--3 [अस्यति सेवनेन<BR>पापानि] N. of a river to the south of<BR>Benares.<BR>--4 Breath (श्वास).<BR>--सि ind.<BR>The 2nd pers. sing. of the Present<BR>of अस् to be, used as an<BR>indeclinable in the sense of ‘त्वम्’ thou;<BR>as in कृतवानसि विप्रियं न मे<BR>Ku. 4. 7 (where however असि may be taken<BR>as a verb).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--असि ind.<BR>sword against sword.<BR>--गंडः a<BR>small pillow for the cheeks; (असिः<BR>क्षिप्तो गंडो यत्र Tv.).<BR>--जीविन् a. one who<BR>earns his livelihood by means of<BR>swords, a soldier fighting for wages.<BR>--दंष्ट्रः, --दंष्ट्रकः the marine monster<BR>makara or crocodile (painted on<BR>the banner of Kāmadeva).<BR>--दंतः<BR>a crocodile.<BR>--धारा the edge of a<BR>sword; सुरगज इव दंतैर्भग्नदैत्यासिधारैः<BR>R. 10. 86, 41.<BR>--धाराव्रतं [असिधारायां<BR>स्थितिरिव दुष्करं व्रतं] {1} (according to<BR>some) the vow of standing on the<BR>edge of a sword; (according to<BR>others) the vow of keeping<BR>constant company with a young wife<BR>and yet steadily resisting the<BR>temptation of sexual intercourse with<BR>her; यत्रैकशयनस्थापि प्रमदा नोपभुज्यते ।<BR>असिधाराव्रतं नाम वदंति मुनिपुंगवाः ॥ or<BR>शयने मध्ये खड्गं विधाय स्त्रीपुंसौ यत्र ब्रह्मचर्येण<BR>स्वपतस्तत्; or युवा युवत्या सार्धं<BR>यन्मुग्धभर्तृवदाचरेत् । अंतर्निवृत्तसंगः स्यादसिधाराव्रतं हि<BR>तत् Yādava. {2} (hence fig.) any<BR>hopelessly difficult task; सतां<BR>केनोद्दिष्टं विषममसिधाराव्रतमिदं Bh. 2. 28, 64;<BR>असिधाराव्रतमिदं यदरिणासह संवासः<BR>Pt. 3.<BR>--धावः, --धावकः an armourer,<BR>furbisher.<BR>--धेनुः, --धेनुका [असिर्धेनुरिव<BR>यस्याः वा कप्] a knife; Vikr. 4. 69.<BR>--पत्र a. having sword-shaped leaves;<BR>जातं तमात्मन्यसिपत्रवृक्षं R. 14. 48.<BR>--(त्रः) {1} the sugar-cane. {2} a kind of<BR>tree which grows in the lower world.<BR>{3} a hell paved with swords.<BR>--(त्रं)<BR>{1} the blade of a sword. {2} a sheath,<BR>a scabbard. ˚वनं a hell where the<BR>trees have leaves as sharp as swords.<BR>--पत्रकः a sugar-cane.<BR>--पथः, --थं the<BR>course of the breath.<BR>--पुच्छः, --पुच्छकः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-b" target="_blank">Page0213-b+ 57</a>]<BR>the Gangetic porpoise.<BR>--पुत्रिका, --पुत्री<BR>a knife (असेः पुत्रीव).<BR>--मेदः [असिरिव<BR>तीक्ष्णो मेदो निर्यासो यस्य] the fetid<BR>Khadira (विट्खदिर).<BR>--हत्य a. to be killed<BR>with a sword.<BR>--(त्यं) fighting with<BR>knives or swords.<BR>--हेतिः [असिर्हेतिः<BR>साधनमस्य] a swordsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिकं|असिक
असिकं The part of the face<BR>between the underlip and the chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्नी
असिक्नी [सिता केशादौ शुभ्रा जरती,<BR>तद्भिन्ना अवृद्धा, सित-क्नादेशः ङीप् च<BR>P. IV. 1. 39 Vārt.]<BR>1 A young<BR>maidservant of the harem.<BR>--2 Night (Nir.).<BR>--3 N. of a river in the Punjaub,<BR>mentioned along with others in the<BR>line इमं मे गंगे यमुने &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिक्निका
असिक्निका A young<BR>woman-servant; गतो गणस्तूर्णमसिक्निकानां Kāśi.<BR>on P. IV. 1. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असित|असितः
असित a.<BR>1 Unbound (Ved.)<BR>--2<BR>[न सितः शुभ्रः] Not white, black,<BR>dark-blue, dark-coloured; असिता<BR>मोहरजनी Śānti. 3. 4; Y. 3. 166; ˚लोचना,<BR>˚नयना &c.<BR>--तः<BR>1 The dark or blue<BR>colour.<BR>--2 The dark fortnight of a<BR>lunar month.<BR>--3 N. of the planet<BR>Saturn.<BR>--4 A black snake.<BR>--5 N. of<BR>the sage देवल.<BR>--6 N. of a being<BR>presiding over darkness and magic.<BR>--ता<BR>1 The Indigo plant.<BR>--2 A girl<BR>attending upon the harem (whose hair<BR>is not whitened by age); see असिक्नी.<BR>--3 The river Yamunā.<BR>--4 N. of a<BR>daughter of Vīraṇa and wife of<BR>Dakṣa.<BR>--5 N. of the river Akesines in the<BR>Punjab.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंबुजं, --उत्पलं the<BR>blue lotus.<BR>--अचिंस् m. fire.<BR>--अश्मन्,<BR>m.<BR>--उपलः a dark-blue stone; lapis<BR>lazuli.<BR>--केशा a woman having black<BR>hair.<BR>--केशांत a. having black locks<BR>of hair.<BR>--गिरिः, --नगः ‘the blue<BR>mountain’; N. of a mountain.<BR>--ग्रीव<BR>a. having a black neck.<BR>--(वः) fire.<BR>--जु a. (for ˚जानु) having black<BR>knees.<BR>--नयनं a. black-eyed;<BR>Me. 112.<BR>--पक्षः the dark fortnight;<BR>Pt. 1. 173.<BR>--फलं the sweet cocoanut.<BR>--भ्रू a. having black eye-lids.<BR>--मृगः<BR>the black antelope.<BR>--यवन = कालयवन<BR>q. v.; Śi. 15. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्ध|असिद्धं|असिद्धः
असिद्ध a.<BR>1 Not accomplished.<BR>--2 Imperfect, incomplete.<BR>--3<BR>Unproved.<BR>--4 Unripe, raw, uncooked.<BR>--5 Not derivable by inference.<BR>--द्धः<BR>A fallacious hetu; one of the<BR>five principal divisions of<BR>हेत्वाभास or fallacies. It is of three<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-c" target="_blank">Page0213-c+ 56</a>]<BR>kinds:--(1) आश्रयासिद्ध where the<BR>existence of any such locality (आश्रय)<BR>as that where the property is said<BR>to reside, is not established; as<BR>‘गगनारविंदं सुरभि अरविंदत्वात्’; (2)<BR>स्वरूपासिद्ध where the nature (स्वरूप) alleged<BR>does not really reside in the subject<BR>(पक्ष); as शब्दो गुणः चाक्षुषत्वात्; and (3)<BR>व्याप्यतासिद्ध where the alleged<BR>invariableness of concomitance is not<BR>real (the साध्यत्व not residing in<BR>साध्य); as पर्वतो वह्निमान् कांचनमयधूमात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिद्धिः|असिद्धि
असिद्धिः f.<BR>1 Imperfect<BR>accomplishment, failure.<BR>--2 Want of ripe<BR>ness.<BR>--3 Non-accomplishment (in<BR>Yoga phil.).<BR>--4 (In logic)<BR>Conclusion not warranted by the premises.<BR>--5 Want of resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिन्व
असिन्व a. Ved. Insatiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असिरः|असिर
असिरः [अस् क्षेपे किरच्]<BR>1 A<BR>beam, a ray.<BR>--2 An arrow, a bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असी
असी N. of a river; see असि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुः|असु
असुः [अस्यते क्षिप्यते अस्-उन्<BR>Uṇ. 1. 10; cf. Nir.; स हि अस्तः शरीरे भवति तस्य<BR>तत्र नित्यमवस्थानं]<BR>1 Breath, life,<BR>spiritual life.<BR>--2 Life of departed<BR>spirits.<BR>--3 Water.<BR>--4 Heat.<BR>--5 (pl.)<BR>(a) The five vital breaths or<BR>lifewinds in the body; असुभिः स्थास्नु<BR>यशश्चिचीषतः Ki. 2. 19; परीक्षितं दुर्लभानसून्<BR>प्रापितवान् K. 175; Bh. 2. 110; (b)<BR>wisdom (प्रज्ञा Nir.).<BR>--6 The time taken<BR>in pronouncing 10 long syllables.<BR>--7 A sixth part of a pala q. v. --n.<BR>--(सु)<BR>1 Reflection, thought.<BR>--2 Heart,<BR>mind.<BR>--3 Grief.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धारणं --णा<BR>sustenance of life, life, existence.<BR>--नीतः the lord of spirits.<BR>--(तं) the<BR>world of spirits.<BR>--नीतिः f. the life<BR>or the world of the spirits<BR>(personified as a female deity invoked for<BR>the preservation of life.).<BR>--भंगः {1}<BR>destruction or loss of life;<BR>मलिनमसुभंगेप्यसुकरं Bh. 2. 28. {2} danger<BR>or fear about life.<BR>--भृत् m. a living<BR>being, a creature.<BR>--सम a. as dear<BR>as life, dearly loved.<BR>--(मः) a husband,<BR>lover; मुहुरसुसममाघ्नती नितांतं Śi. 7. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुमत्|असुमन्त्
असुमत् a. Living, breathing. --m.<BR>1 A living being;<BR>सततमसुमतामगम्यरूपाः Śi. 4. 29.<BR>--2 Life, the principle<BR>of vitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुख|असुखं
असुख a.<BR>1 Unhappy, sorrowful.<BR>--2 Not easy (to obtain), difficult<BR>Ki. 5. 49.<BR>--खं Sorrow, pain,<BR>affliction; असुखं दर्शितं विकारेण M. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-a" target="_blank">Page0214-a+ 59</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवह a. pained with grief.<BR>--आविष्ट a. afflicted with grief<BR>or pain, causing great pain.<BR>--उदय a.<BR>causing or ending in unhappiness;<BR>Ms. 4. 70.<BR>--उदर्क a. productive of or<BR>ending in unhappiness; Ms. 11. 10.<BR>--जीविका an unhappy life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0213-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुखिन्
असुखिन् a. Unhappy, sorrowful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुत
असुत a.<BR>1 Childless.<BR>--2 Ved.<BR>Not pressed out, not cleared or<BR>purified (as the Soma juice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुन्व
असुन्व [सु अभिषवे बा˚ श, न. त.]<BR>Not pressing out the Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुतृप्
असुतृप् a. Insatiable.<BR>--पः A<BR>servant of Yama, messenger of<BR>death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुप्त
असुप्त a. Not asleep; ˚दृश् not<BR>closing the eyes in sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुम्न
असुम्न a. Ved. Contrary, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर|असुरः
असुर a. [असु-र Uṇ. 1. 42]<BR>1<BR>Living, alive, spiritual.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of the Supreme Spirit or<BR>Varuṇa.<BR>--3 Incorporeal, superhuman,<BR>divine.<BR>--रः [According to Nir.<BR>अ सुरताः स्थानेषु न सुष्ठु रताः स्थानेषु चपला<BR>इत्यर्थः; or अस्ताः प्रच्याविता देवैः स्थानेभ्यः;<BR>or from असु; असुः प्राणः तेन तद्वंतो भवंति<BR>रो मत्वर्थे; or सोर्देवानसृजत तत्सुराणां सुरत्वं,<BR>असोः असुरानसृजत तदसुराणामसुरत्वं; सोः =<BR>प्रशस्तादात्मनः प्रदेशात्]<BR>1 An evil<BR>spirit, a demon; the Rām. thus accounts<BR>for the name:--सुराप्रतिग्रहाद्देवाः सुरा<BR>इत्यभिविश्रुताः । अप्रतिग्रहणात्तस्या<BR>दैतेयाश्चासुरास्तथा [In the oldest parts of the<BR>Ṛgveda the term asura is used for the<BR>Supreme spirit and in the sense of ‘god’,<BR>‘divine’; it was applied to several of<BR>the chief deities such as Indra, Agni,<BR>and Varuṇa. It afterwards acquired<BR>an entirely opposite meaning, and came<BR>to signify a demon or an enemy of the<BR>gods. The Brāhmaṇas state that<BR>Prajāpati created asuras with the breath<BR>(asu); particularly from the lower<BR>breath. The Vāyu P. says that Asuras<BR>were first produced as sons from<BR>Prajāpati's groin; cf. also Nir. above].<BR>--2 A general name for the enemies<BR>of gods, Daityas and Dānavas,<BR>distinguished from Rākṣasas<BR>descended from Pulastya.<BR>--3 A ghost<BR>or spectre.<BR>--4 The sun (said to<BR>be from अस् to shine).<BR>--5 An<BR>elephant.<BR>--6 An epithet of Rāhu.<BR>--7<BR>A cloud.<BR>--8 N. of a warrior tribe.<BR>--रा<BR>1 Night.<BR>--2 A zodiacal sign.<BR>--3<BR>A prostitute.<BR>--री<BR>1 A female<BR>demon, wife of an Asura.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>the plant Sinapis Racemosa Roxb.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">Page0214-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः, --राज्, --जः {1} the lord<BR>of the Asuras. {2} an epithet of Bali,<BR>grandson of Prahlāda.<BR>--आचार्यः,<BR>--गुरुः {1} N. of the preceptor of the<BR>Asuras, Śukrācārya. {2} the planet<BR>Venus.<BR>--आह्वं bell-metal.<BR>--क्षयण,<BR>--क्षिति a. destroying the Asuras.<BR>--द्विष् m. an enemy of the Asuras, i. e.<BR>a god.<BR>--माया demoniacal magic.<BR>--रक्षस् n. (pl.) the Asuras and<BR>Rākṣasas.<BR>--(सं) a demoniacal being<BR>partaking of the qualities of both the<BR>classes.<BR>--रिपुः, --सूदनः ‘destroyer of<BR>Asuras’, an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--हन्<BR>m. {1} one who destroys the Asuras,<BR>an epithet of Agni, Indra &c. {2}<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुर्य|असुर्यः|असुर्य्य
असुर्य a. [असुराय हिता गवा˚ यत्]<BR>1<BR>Incorporeal, spiritual, divine.<BR>--2<BR>Demoniacal, belonging to the Asuras<BR>or sprung from them (असुरस्य स्वं<BR>P. IV. 4. 123).<BR>--र्यं<BR>1 The water of the<BR>clouds.<BR>--2 Spirituality, divine<BR>nature.<BR>--3 The collective body of<BR>spiritual beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरत्वं|असुरत्व
असुरत्वं Spirituality,<BR>supernatural or divine nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुरसा
असुरसा [न सुष्टु रसो यस्याः] N. of a<BR>plant; a variety of तुलसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुलभ
असुलभ a. Not easily attainable,<BR>difficult to secure; असुलभा<BR>सकलेंदुमुखी च सा V. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुष्वि
असुष्वि a. [सु-बा˚ कि द्वित्वम् न. त.<BR>Tv.] Not pressing out the Soma<BR>juice, irreligious, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुसूः
असुसूः [असून् प्राणान् सुवति सू-क्विप्]<BR>An arrow; स सासिः सासुसूः सासो<BR>येयायेयाययाययः Ki. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुस्थ|असुस्थः
असुस्थ a. Unwell, indisposed;<BR>˚ता indisposition, sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असुहृद्
असुहृद् m. An enemy; Śi. 2. 117.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असू
असू a. Not bringing forth,<BR>barren (as a cow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूत
असूत, असूतिक a. One who has not<BR>brought forth, barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूतिक
असूत, असूतिक a. One who has not<BR>brought forth, barren.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूतिः|असूति
असूतिः f.<BR>1 Non-production,<BR>barrenness.<BR>--2 Obstruction, removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूक्षणं|असूक्षण
असूक्षणं [सूक्ष्-आदरे ल्युट् अभावे<BR>न. त.] Disrespect; also in the same<BR>sense, असुक्षणं, असुर्क्षणं, असूर्क्षणं, अस्तर्क्षणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयति
असूयति Den. P. (P. III. 1. 27)<BR>1 To envy, to be jealous of; कथं<BR>चित्रगतो भर्ता मयाऽसूयितः M. 4.<BR>--2<BR>To detract from; murmur, grumble<BR>at, be displeased with, scorn, be<BR>discontented with or angry with (with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">Page0214-c+ 57</a>]<BR>dat. of person or thing); असूयंति<BR>सचिवोपदेशाय K. 108; असूयंति मह्यं<BR>प्रकृतयः V. 4; न्यसनाय ससौरभस्य<BR>कस्तरुसूनस्य शिरस्यसूयति Śi. 16. 20;<BR>Bg. 3. 31; sometimes with acc.; असूयंति हि<BR>राजानो जनाननृतवादिनः Mb. --Caus.<BR>To cause to murmur at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयक|असूयकः
असूयक a. [असूय्-ण्युल्<BR>P. III. 2. 146]<BR>1 Envious, detracting,<BR>calumnious.<BR>--2 Discontented,<BR>displeased.<BR>--कः A detractor, an envious<BR>man; Ms. 2. 114; Śānti. 3. 7,<BR>Y. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयनं|असूयन
असूयनं<BR>1 Detraction, calumny.<BR>--2<BR>Envy, jealousy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूया
असूया<BR>1 Envy, intolerance,<BR>jealousy (of the happiness of others);<BR>क्रुधद्रुहेर्ष्यासूयार्थानां यं प्रति कोपः<BR>P. I. 4. 37; III. 4. 28; VIII. 1. 8; सासूयं<BR>enviously.<BR>--2 Calumny, detraction<BR>(of the merits of others); असूया<BR>परगुणेषु दोषाविष्करणं Sk. (= दोषारोपो गुणेष्वपि<BR>Ak.); Ms. 7. 48; R. 4. 23.<BR>--3<BR>Anger, indignation; वधूरसूयाकुटिलं<BR>ददर्श R. 6. 82; सासूयमुक्ता सखी Ś. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयितृ
असूयितृ a. Envious, detracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूयुः|असूयु
असूयुः<BR>1 Envious, jealous.<BR>--2<BR>Displeased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर
असूर a. Ved. Devoid of praise<BR>or worship; Rv. 8. 10. 4 (स्तोत्ररहित).<BR>--रं Ved. Absence of a person to<BR>extract the Soma juice; a place devoid<BR>of praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्त|असूर्त्त
असूर्त a. Not moving(अप्रेरित).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्य
असूर्य a. Sunless.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग a.<BR>not entering into the sun, i. e. not<BR>set; R. 3. 13; (रविणास्तमयो योगो<BR>वियोगस्तूदयो भवेत् ।).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असूर्यंपश्य
असूर्यंपश्य a. [सूर्यमपि न पश्यति<BR>दृश्खश् मुम्च P. III. 2. 36] Not seeing<BR>even the sun; said of the wives<BR>of a king who, being shut up in the<BR>harem, have no opportunity of<BR>seeing the sun; असूयपर्श्यां राजदाराः Sk.<BR>--श्या A chaste and loyal wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृज्
असृज् n. [न सृज्यते इतररागवत् संसृज्यते<BR>सहजत्वात् न-सृज्-क्विन् Tv.]<BR>1 Blood.<BR>--2 The planet Mars.<BR>--3 Saffron.<BR>--m. N. of the 16th of the 27 Yogas;<BR>धनी कुरूपः कुमती दुरात्मा विदेशगामी<BR>रुधिरप्रकोपः । महाप्रलोभी पुरुषो<BR>बलीयानसृक्प्रसूतौ किल यस्य जंतोः ॥. Śabdak.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः [असृक् शोणितं करोति कृ-ट] the<BR>essence of the body; lymph, serum;<BR>(the process of रस turning into blood<BR>&c., is thus described by Suśr.:<BR>--रसाद्रक्तं ततो मांसं मांसान्मेदः प्रजायते ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">Page0215-a+ 55</a>]<BR>मेदसोस्थि ततो मज्जा मज्ज्नः शुक्रस्य संभवः).<BR>--दरः<BR>an irregular or excessive<BR>menstruation, mœnorrhagia.<BR>--दाहेः shedding<BR>blood.<BR>--धरा the skin.<BR>--धारा {1} a<BR>stream of blood. {2} the skin.<BR>--पः,<BR>--पाः ‘a blood-drinker’, a Rākṣasa.<BR>--पातः the falling of blood. (pl.)<BR>drops of blood.<BR>--पावन् a. Ved.<BR>drinking blood.<BR>--वहा a blood-vessel;<BR>pulse.<BR>--विमोक्षणं blood-letting,<BR>bleeding.<BR>--श्रा (स्रा) वः bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0214-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृपाटः|असृपाट
असृपाटः --टी [असृजः पाटी परिपाटी पृ˚]<BR>A stream of blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृपाटी
असृपाटः --टी [असृजः पाटी परिपाटी पृ˚]<BR>A stream of blood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृणि
असृणि a. Unrestrained(as by<BR>a goad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असृष्ट
असृष्ट a.<BR>1 Uncreated.<BR>--2<BR>Continued.<BR>--3 Unpresented or<BR>undistributed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्न a. one who<BR>does not distribute food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेचन
असेचन, --नक a. That on which<BR>one cannot look enough, charming,<BR>lovely; नयनयुगासेचनकं मानसवृत्त्यापि<BR>दुष्प्रापम् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेचनक|असेचनकं
असेचन, --नक a. That on which<BR>one cannot look enough, charming,<BR>lovely; नयनयुगासेचनकं मानसवृत्त्यापि<BR>दुष्प्रापम् S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेन्य
असेन्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Not befitting<BR>an army.<BR>--2 Not striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवन
असेवन a.<BR>1 Not serving,<BR>disregarding.<BR>--2 Not following or<BR>practising, shunning.<BR>--नं Disregard,<BR>disobedience, inattention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असेवित
असेवित a. Neglected; disused,<BR>abstained from.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईश्वर or<BR>˚द्वार a. not waiting at the doors of<BR>the rich or great.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौनामन्
असौनामन् a. Ved. Having such<BR>and such a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौम्य
असौम्य a. Not lovely, ugly,<BR>disagreeable; ˚स्वर a. having a bad or<BR>croaking voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

असौष्ठव|असौष्ठवं
असौष्ठव a.<BR>1 Devoid of beauty<BR>or loveliness, not in good trim;<BR>शरीरमसौष्ठवं Māl. 1. 17.<BR>--2 Ugly,<BR>deformed.<BR>--वं<BR>1 Worthlessness, absence<BR>of merit.<BR>--2 Deformity, ugliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कन्न
अस्कन्न a.<BR>1 Not split.<BR>--2 Not<BR>poured out or effused.<BR>--3 Not<BR>sprinkled, not covered.<BR>--4<BR>Permanent, durable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कंदित|अस्कन्दित
अस्कंदित a. Not split; not gone;<BR>not attacked; ˚व्रत true to one's<BR>vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्कृधोयु
अस्कृधोयु a. Not short or<BR>deficient, abundant, uninterrupted (<BR>अविच्छिन्न Sāy.); Rv. 7. 53. 3; 6. 67. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्खलित
अस्खलित a.<BR>1 Unshaken,<BR>unyielding, firm, permanent.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">Page0215-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Unhurt, sound and safe; ˚भ्रातृशतः<BR>Ve. 5.<BR>--3 Not stumbling or<BR>slipping, undeviating, careful; समे<BR>चिरायास्खलितोपचारां R. 5. 20; ˚प्रयाण<BR>a. with unfaltering steps, not<BR>stumbling in gait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त|अस्तं|अस्तः
अस्त, अस्तु &c. see under अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तु
अस्त, अस्तु &c. see under अस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तब्ध
अस्तब्ध a. Not firm or<BR>self-possessed, confused; ˚त्वं want of<BR>self-possession, confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तर्क्षणं|अस्तर्क्षण
अस्तर्क्षणं = असूक्षणं q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ताघ|अस्ताघः
अस्ताघ a. Very deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तिकः
अस्तिकः N. of a sage whose<BR>intercession saved the serpents from<BR>being burnt down in the sacrificial<BR>fire of Janamejaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तृत
अस्तृत a. Ved. Not overcome,<BR>invincible; ˚यज्वन् a. Ved.<BR>sacrificing untiringly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्तेयं|अस्तेय
अस्तेयं Not stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्यानं|अस्त्यान
अस्त्यानं Reproach, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रं|अस्त्र
अस्त्रं [अस्यंते क्षिप्यते अस्-ष्ट्रन्<BR>Uṇ. 4. 158]<BR>1 A missile; a weapon in<BR>general; प्रयुक्तमप्यस्त्रमितो वृथा स्यात्<BR>R. 2. 34; प्रत्याहतास्त्रो गिरिशप्रभावात्<BR>2. 41, 3. 58; अशिक्षतास्त्रं पितुरेव<BR>R. 3. 31 the science of missiles.<BR>--2 An<BR>arrow; sword.<BR>--3 A bow.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अ(आ)गारं an arsenal, armoury.<BR>--आघातः a wound, a cut (made by<BR>a weapon).<BR>--आहत a. struck,<BR>wounded, killed.<BR>--कंटकः [अस्त्रं कंटक इव]<BR>an arrow.<BR>--कारः, --कारकः,<BR>--कारिन् a maker of weapons.<BR>--क्षेपक<BR>a. shooting arrows.<BR>--चिकित्सकः<BR>a surgeon.<BR>--चिकित्सा surgery.<BR>--जित् m. N. of a plant<BR>--जीवः,<BR>--जीविन् m.<BR>--धारिन् m. a soldier,<BR>professional warrior.<BR>--धारणं the<BR>bearing of arms.<BR>--निवारणं the warding<BR>of a weapon.<BR>--मंत्रः a Mantra to be<BR>repeated in discharging or<BR>withdrawing a missile; R. 5. 57, 59.<BR>--मार्जः --र्जकः a furbisher.<BR>--युद्धं<BR>fighting with weapons.<BR>--लाघवं<BR>dexterity in wielding or throwing<BR>missiles.<BR>--विद् a. skilled in the<BR>science of arms.<BR>--विद्या, --शास्त्रं, --वेदः<BR>the art or science of throwing<BR>missiles, military science, science of<BR>arms; Ki. 13. 62, U. 6. 9.<BR>--वृष्टिः<BR>f. a shower of missiles.<BR>--शस्त्रं all<BR>sorts of weapons.<BR>--शिक्षा military<BR>exercise.<BR>--सायकः {1} an iron arrow.<BR>{2} the नाराच missile.<BR>--हीन a.<BR>unarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रिन्
अस्त्रिन् a. Fighting with a missile<BR>weapon, an archer; अस्त्री जनः पुनरनेन<BR>कृतः किल स्त्री Udb. (a pun on the<BR>word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्री
अस्त्री<BR>1 Not a woman.<BR>--2 (In<BR>gram.) The masculine and neuter<BR>genders; वल्कं वल्कलमस्त्रियां Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रीक
अस्त्रीक a. Having no wife;<BR>without a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रैण
अस्त्रैण a. Ved. Without a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थन्
अस्थन् n. (the base used in<BR>some of the cases of अस्थि after acc.)<BR>A bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्था
अस्था Ved. A thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाग|अस्थागं
अस्थाग a. Very deep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थान|अस्थानं
अस्थान a. Very deep.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>A bad or wrong place; अस्थाने<BR>पततामतीव महतामेतादृशी स्याद्गतिः S. D.<BR>--2<BR>An improper place or object or<BR>occasion; ˚वर्षी Dk. 81 (= अपात्रदायिन्);<BR>अस्थानं परिभूतेः K. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थाने
अस्थाने ind. Unseasonably, out<BR>of place, inopportunely, in a wrong<BR>place, on an unworthy object;<BR>उभयोरप्यस्थाने प्रयत्नः Mu. 2; अस्थाने<BR>महानर्थोत्सर्गः क्रियते Mu. 3; अस्थाने<BR>कोपः M. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थायिन्
अस्थायिन् a. Not permanent,<BR>transitory, perishable; प्रायेण<BR>साधुवृत्तानामस्थायिन्यो विपत्तयः Bh. 2. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थावर|अस्थावरं
अस्थावर a.<BR>1 Moveable,<BR>moving, not fixed.<BR>--2 (In law)<BR>Personal, as property, money, cattle &c.<BR>as opposed to land (= जंगम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थि
अस्थि n. [अस्यते अस्-कथिन्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 154]<BR>1 A bone (changed to अस्थ<BR>at the end of certain compounds;<BR>cf. अनस्थ, पुरुषास्थ).<BR>--2 The kernel<BR>or stone of a fruit; न कार्पासास्थि न<BR>तुषान् Ms. 4. 78. [cf. L. os; Gr.<BR>osteon; Zend. asta; Pers. astah]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत्, --तेजस्, --संभवः, --सारः,<BR>--स्नेहः marrow; Māl. 5. 18.<BR>--छलितं<BR>a particular fracture of the bone;<BR>(पार्श्वयोरस्थिहीनोद्गतं).<BR>--जः {1} marrow.<BR>{2} thunderbolt.<BR>--तुंडः [अस्थीव<BR>कठिनं तुंडमस्य] {1} a kind of bird whose<BR>mouth or beak is as hard as a bone.<BR>{2} a bird.<BR>--तोदः pain in the bones.<BR>--त्वच् f. periosteum.<BR>--धन्वन् m.<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--पंजरः ‘a cage of bones’,<BR>a skeleton.<BR>--प्रक्षेपः throwing the<BR>bones of the dead into the Ganges<BR>or any holy waters.<BR>--भक्षः, --भुक्<BR>‘an eater of bones’, a dog.<BR>--भंगः<BR>fracture of the bones.<BR>--भूयस्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">Page0216-a+ 56</a>]<BR>a. consisting chiefly of bones,<BR>dried up.<BR>--भेदः {1} fracturing or<BR>breaking a bone. {2} a sort of bone.<BR>--भेदकः a bone-breaker.<BR>--माला {1} a<BR>string or wreath of bones. {2} a row<BR>of bones.<BR>--मालिन् m. N. of Śiva.<BR>--युज् m. [अस्थि युनक्ति] a kind of<BR>tree (हस्तिशुंडावृक्ष).<BR>--योगः the<BR>joining of a broken limb.<BR>--विग्रह a.<BR>reduced to a skeleton.<BR>--(हः) N. of<BR>भृंगिन्ं, Śiva's attendant.<BR>--शृंखला,<BR>--संहारः, --संहारिका N. of the plant<BR>Heliotropium Indicum (ग्रंथिमतीवृक्ष).<BR>--शेष a. [अस्थिमात्रं शेषोऽस्य] very<BR>lean, reduced to a skeleton.<BR>--शोषः<BR>dryness and decay of the bones.<BR>--संहारकः {1} bone-seizer. {2} the<BR>adjutant bird.<BR>--संचयः {1} collecting the<BR>bones or their ashes after burning a<BR>corpse. {2} a heap of bones.<BR>--संधिः<BR>{1} a joint, an articulation. {2}<BR>uniting a broken bone.<BR>--समर्पणं<BR>throwing the bones of the dead body into<BR>the Ganges or holy waters.<BR>--स्थूणः<BR>‘having the bones for its pillars’,<BR>the body.<BR>--स्रंस a. Ved. causing<BR>the bones to fall asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0215-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थन्वत्|अस्थन्वन्त्
अस्थन्वत्, अस्थिमत्, अस्थिमय a.<BR>Bony, consisting of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमत्|अस्थिमन्त्
अस्थन्वत्, अस्थिमत्, अस्थिमय a.<BR>Bony, consisting of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिमय
अस्थन्वत्, अस्थिमत्, अस्थिमय a.<BR>Bony, consisting of bones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थित
अस्थित a. Not firm or fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिति|अस्थितिः
अस्थिति a.<BR>1 Not firm.<BR>--2 Having<BR>no settled boundary or limit.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1 Want of firmness or fixity (fig.<BR>also.).<BR>--2 Want of good manners or<BR>decorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थिर|अस्थिरः
अस्थिर a.<BR>1 Not stable or firm,<BR>unsteady, fickle.<BR>--2 Uncertain.<BR>--3<BR>Unworthy of confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थैर्य|अस्थैर्य्य|अस्थैर्य्यं
अस्थैर्य a. Unsteady.<BR>--र्यं<BR>Instability, unsteadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्थूरिः|अस्थूरि
अस्थूरिः A cart furnished with<BR>more than one horse (एकाश्वयुक्तशकटं<BR>स्थूरि तद्विपरीतं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नाविर
अस्नाविर a.<BR>1 Without sinews<BR>or bands.<BR>--2 Without the gross body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्निग्ध
अस्निग्ध a.<BR>1 Not smooth, hard,<BR>dry.<BR>--2 Unkind.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दारु n. a<BR>kind of pine tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्नेह|अस्नेहः
अस्नेह a. Unkind, cruel.<BR>--हः<BR>Unkindness, want of affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पंद|अस्पन्द
अस्पंद a. Not trembling or<BR>moving, motionless; U. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्श|अस्पर्शः
अस्पर्श a. Not touching, not in<BR>contact.<BR>--र्शः Absence of contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पर्शनं|अस्पर्शन
अस्पर्शनं Non-contact, avoiding the<BR>contact (of anything); प्रक्षालनाद्धि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">Page0216-b+ 55</a>]<BR>पंकस्य दूरादस्पर्शनं वरं; cf.<BR>‘Prevention is better than cure’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृश्य
अस्पृश्य a.<BR>1 Not to be touched.<BR>--2<BR>Impure, unholy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्ट
अस्पृष्ट a. Untouched.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रजस्, --तमस्क a. perfectly pure.<BR>--वह्नि a. unsheathed by fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृष्टिः|अस्पृष्टि
अस्पृष्टिः f. Not touching,<BR>avoiding contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पष्ट|अस्पष्टं
अस्पष्ट a.<BR>1 Not clear, not<BR>clearly visible.<BR>--2 Indistinct, not<BR>clearly understood, doubtful;<BR>अस्पष्टब्रह्नलिंगानि वेदांतवाक्यानि Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्पृत
अस्पृत a. Irresistible, invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्फुट|अस्फुटं
अस्फुट a. Indistinct, obscure.<BR>--टं An indistinct speech.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फलं indistinct fruit or result.<BR>--वाच् a. lisping, speaking<BR>indistinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्
अस्मद् pron. [अस्-मदिक्<BR>Uṇ. 1. 136] A pronominal base from<BR>which several cases of the 1st<BR>personal pronoun are derived; it is also<BR>abl. pl. of the word. --m. The<BR>individual soul, the embodied soul;<BR>यूयं वयं वयं यूयमित्यासीन्मतिरावयोः ।<BR>किं जातमधुना येन यूयं यूयं वयं वयं ॥<BR>Bh. 3. 65 (quite estranged from<BR>each other).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द्रुह् a. Ved.<BR>forming a plot against us or me,<BR>inimical.<BR>--विध, --अस्मादृश a. similar<BR>or like us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मत्रा
अस्मत्रा ind. To us, with or<BR>among us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मदीय
अस्मदीय a. [अस्मद् --छ] Our, ours;<BR>यदस्मदीयं न हि तत्परेषां Pt. 2. 105;<BR>सहास्मदीयैरपि योधमुख्यैः Bg. 12. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मद्र्यंच्|अस्मद्र्यञ्च्
अस्मद्र्यंच् a. [अस्मानंचति<BR>P. VIII. 2. 80-81] Turned towards us.<BR>--क्<BR>ind. Towards us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मयु
अस्मयु a. Endeavouring to secure<BR>us, desiring us.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्माक
अस्माक a. Ved. for आस्माक (our,<BR>ours).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मंतं|अस्मन्त|अस्मन्तं
अस्मंतं = अश्मंतं q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मरणं|अस्मरण
अस्मरणं Forgetfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मार्त|अस्मार्त्त
अस्मार्त a.<BR>1 Not within memory,<BR>immemorial.<BR>--2 Illegal, not<BR>according to the Aryan institutes of Law.<BR>--3 Not belonging to the Smārta sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मृतिः|अस्मृति
अस्मृतिः f.<BR>1 Want of memory,<BR>forgetfulness.<BR>--2 Not forming part of<BR>the institutes of law.<BR>--ति ind. Ved.<BR>Inattentively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मि
अस्मि ind. (Strictly 1st. pers.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">Page0216-c+ 55</a>]<BR>sing. Pres. of अस् to be) Used in<BR>the sense of ‘I’, अहं; आसंसृतेरस्मि<BR>जगत्सु जातः Ki. 3. 6; दासे कृतागसि<BR>भवत्युचितः प्रभूणां पादप्रहार इति सुंदरि<BR>नास्मि दूये ॥ quoted by Malli.; त्वामस्मि वच्मि<BR>विदुषां समवायोऽत्र तिष्ठति S. D.;<BR>अन्यत्र यूयं कुसुमावचायं कुरुध्वमत्रास्मि<BR>करोमि सख्यः K. P. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मिता
अस्मिता Egotism;<BR>दृग्दर्शनशक्त्योरेकात्मतेवास्मिता Pat. Sūtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्मेर
अस्मेर a. Ved. Not sullen,<BR>confiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्यवामीयं|अस्यवामीय
अस्यवामीयं [अस्यवामिति शब्दोऽ<BR>स्त्यत्र सूक्ते मत्वर्थे छ] The hymn<BR>beginning with the words अस्य वाम्<BR>(Rv.1. 164).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्युद्यत
अस्युद्यत a. = उद्यतासि with the<BR>sword raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रः|अस्र|अस्रं
अस्रः [अस्-रन्]<BR>1 A corner, an<BR>angle.<BR>--2 Hair of the head.<BR>--स्रं<BR>1 Tear; अस्रोत्तरमीक्षितामिमां<BR>Ku. 5. 61.<BR>--2 Blood.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्जक a.<BR>producing blood.<BR>--(कः) {1} the white<BR>Tulasī plant. {2} the humour<BR>producing blood.<BR>--कंठः [अस्रः<BR>कोणः इव कंठोऽस्य] an arrow.<BR>--खदिरः<BR>the red Mimosa.<BR>--जं flesh.<BR>--जित् =<BR>अश्रजित् q. v.<BR>--पः {1} ‘a blood-drinker’,<BR>a Rākṣasa or goblin; वध्यंतेऽ<BR>स्रपपुंगवाः Mv. 6. 24. {2} the Nakṣatra<BR>मूला.<BR>--पा {1} a leech. {2} a Ḍākinī<BR>or female imp.<BR>--पत्रकः N. of a<BR>plant (भिंडावृक्ष).<BR>--पित्तं hemorrhage,<BR>involuntary discharge of blood<BR>from the mouth, nostrils &c.<BR>--फला,<BR>--ली N. of a plant (सल्लकी).<BR>--मातृका<BR>chyle, chyme.<BR>--रोधिनी the plant<BR>लज्जालु Mimosa Pudica.<BR>--बिंदुच्छदा N.<BR>of a tuberous plant (लक्षणावृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रायते
अस्रायते Den. A. To shed tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रिः|अस्रि
अस्रिः<BR>1 An angle.<BR>--2 Ten<BR>millions; see अश्रि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रिध्
अस्रिध्, अस्त्रेधत् a. Ved. Devout,<BR>faithful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्त्रेधत्
अस्रिध्, अस्त्रेधत् a. Ved. Devout,<BR>faithful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रु
अस्रु = अश्रु q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्रेमन्
अस्रेमन् a.<BR>1 Praiseworthy.<BR>--2<BR>Undecaying, immortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्व|अस्वः
अस्व a.<BR>1 Indigent, poor (नास्ति<BR>स्वं धनं यस्य).<BR>--2 Not one's own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वक
अस्वक, --अस्वकीय, अस्विक a. Not one's<BR>own, belonging to another.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग a. Ved. not going to one's<BR>home, homeless; ˚ता Ved.<BR>homelessness.<BR>--जातिः a. of a different caste<BR>or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वकीय
अस्वक, --अस्वकीय, अस्विक a. Not one's<BR>own, belonging to another.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग a. Ved. not going to one's<BR>home, homeless; ˚ता Ved.<BR>homelessness.<BR>--जातिः a. of a different caste<BR>or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्विक
अस्वक, --अस्वकीय, अस्विक a. Not one's<BR>own, belonging to another.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग a. Ved. not going to one's<BR>home, homeless; ˚ता Ved.<BR>homelessness.<BR>--जातिः a. of a different caste<BR>or kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0216-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वत्वं|अस्वत्व
अस्वत्वं --ता Absence of ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वता
अस्वत्वं --ता Absence of ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वच्छंद|अस्वच्छन्द|अस्वच्छन्दः
अस्वच्छंद a.<BR>1 Not self-willed,<BR>dependent.<BR>--2 Docile, tractable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वतंत्र|अस्वतन्त्र|अस्वतन्त्रः
अस्वतंत्र a.<BR>1 Dependent, subject,<BR>not one's own master; अस्वतंत्रा<BR>स्त्री पुरुषप्रधाना Vasiṣṭha.<BR>--2 Docile,<BR>humble, tractable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वंत|अस्वन्त|अस्वन्तः
अस्वंत a. Ending, ill.<BR>--तः<BR>Death.<BR>--तं fireplace (अश्मंत q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वप्न|अस्वप्नः
अस्वप्न a. Sleepless, wakeful.<BR>--प्नः<BR>1 A god, deity.<BR>--2<BR>Sleeplessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वप्नज्
अस्वप्नज् a. Sleepless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वभाव|अस्वभावः
अस्वभाव a. Of a different<BR>nature.<BR>--वः Different or unnatural<BR>character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर|अस्वरः
अस्वर a.<BR>1 Having a bad voice.<BR>--2 Indistinct, not loud, in a low<BR>tone (as a speech).<BR>--रः<BR>1 A low<BR>tone.<BR>--2 A consonant.<BR>--3 Absence<BR>of any accent.<BR>--रं ind. Not aloud,<BR>in a low tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वरूप
अस्वरूप a. Essentially different,<BR>unlike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वर्ग्य
अस्वर्ग्य a. Not securing or<BR>leading to heaven; अस्वर्ग्यं लोकविद्विष्टं<BR>धर्ममप्याचरेन्न तु Y. 1. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्ववेश
अस्ववेश a. Expelled from<BR>home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाध्यायः|अस्वाध्याय
अस्वाध्यायः [न स्वाध्यायो<BR>वेदाध्ययनमस्य]<BR>1 One who has not yet<BR>commenced his studies, not being<BR>invested with the sacred thread.<BR>--2<BR>Interruption of studies (as on अष्टमी,<BR>eclipses &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वस्थ
अस्वस्थ a. Not well, unwell,<BR>indisposed, sick; बलवत् अस्वस्था Ś. 3<BR>seriously indisposed; ˚शरीरा ibid.,<BR>K. 159, 211; ˚ता want of firmness,<BR>weakness, ill-ness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वास्थ्यं|अस्वास्थ्य
अस्वास्थ्यं<BR>1 Indisposition, sickness.<BR>--2 Absence of ease or comfort,<BR>trouble, anxiety; य<BR>इत्थमस्वास्थ्यमहर्दिवं दिवः Śi. 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिक|अस्वामिकं
अस्वामिक a. Unowned,<BR>unclaimed.<BR>--कं (Unclaimed) Treasure &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वामिन्
अस्वामिन् a.<BR>1 Having no right<BR>to anything, not being master of it.<BR>--2 Unowned, unclaimed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विक्रयः a sale without ownership;<BR>निक्षिप्तं वा परद्रव्यं नष्टं लब्ध्वाऽपहृत्य वा ।<BR>विक्रीयतऽसमक्षं यत् स ज्ञेयोऽ<BR>स्वामिविक्रयः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अस्वाम्य|अस्वाम्यं
अस्वाम्य a.<BR>1 Unowned.<BR>--2 Not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">Page0217-b+ 57</a>]<BR>one's own.<BR>--म्यं Absence of right to<BR>property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह्
अह् {vI.v} {c1c} A. or {c10c} U. = अंह् q. v.<BR>{vII.v} {c1c} P. To sing together, compose,<BR>celebrate, prepare. {vIII.v} {c5c} P. (अह्नोति,<BR>आहीत्, आह) To pervade. {vIV.v} (a<BR>defective verb preserved only in five<BR>forms आत्थ, आहथुः, आह, आहतुः, आहुः)<BR>1 To say, speak, mention.<BR>--2 To<BR>acknowledge, accept, state.<BR>--3 To<BR>declare, express, signify.<BR>--4 To hold,<BR>consider, regard.<BR>--5 To call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अह|अहं|अहः
अह ind. A particle implying(a)<BR>praise (पूजा); (b) separation; (c)<BR>resolution, ascertainment, certainty;<BR>and translated by ‘surely,’<BR>‘certainly,’ ‘yes,’ ‘well’; (d) rejecting; (e)<BR>sending; (f) deviation from<BR>custom, impropriety; त्वमह ग्रामं गच्छ,<BR>त्वमह रथेतारण्यं गच्छ Sk.; स्वयमह<BR>रथेन याति ३ उपाध्यायं पदातिं गमयति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहत|अहतं
अहत a.<BR>1 Not hurt or struck,<BR>uninjured.<BR>--2 Unbeaten (as cloth<BR>in washing).<BR>--3 Unwashed, new.<BR>--4<BR>Unblemished, unsoiled.<BR>--5 Not<BR>frustrated or disappointed (as hopes &c.).<BR>--तं An unwashed or new cloth;<BR>cf. अप्रहत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहतिः|अहति
अहतिः, अहंतिः f. Ved. Safety,<BR>security from danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंतिः|अहन्ति|अहन्तिः
अहतिः, अहंतिः f. Ved. Safety,<BR>security from danger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंत्य|अहन्त्य
अहंत्य, अहंत्र, अहन्य a. Ved.<BR>Indestructible, invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंत्र
अहंत्य, अहंत्र, अहन्य a. Ved.<BR>Indestructible, invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्य
अहंत्य, अहंत्र, अहन्य a. Ved.<BR>Indestructible, invincible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहन्
अहन् n. [न जहाति न त्यजति सर्वथा<BR>परिवर्तनं, न, हा-कनिन् Uṇ. 1. 55] (Nom.<BR>अहः, अह्नी-अहनी, अहानि, अह्ना,<BR>अहोभ्यां &c.; अहरिति हंति पाप्मानं जहाति च<BR>Śat. Br.)<BR>1 A day (including day and<BR>night); अघाहानि Ms. 5. 84.<BR>--2 Day<BR>time; सव्यापारामहनि न तथा<BR>पीडयेन्मद्वियोगः Me. 88; यदह्ना कुरुते पापं by day.<BR>--3 The sky (as traversed by the sun);<BR>समारूढे च मध्यमह्नः सवितरि K. 99;<BR>M. 2.<BR>--4 A sacrificial or festival day.<BR>--5 A day's work.<BR>--6 Viṣṇu.<BR>--7<BR>Night.<BR>--8 A portion of a book<BR>appointed for a day.<BR>--9 A day<BR>personified as one of the eight Vasus.<BR>--नी (du.) Day and night. (At the<BR>end of comp. अहन् is changed to<BR>अहः, --हं or to अह्न; see P. V. 4. 88-91;<BR>VI. 3. 110, VIII. 4. 7. Note. At the<BR>beginning of comp. it assumes the<BR>forms अहस् or अहर्; e. g. सप्ताहः, एकाहः,<BR>पूर्वाह्णः, अपराह्णः, पुण्याहं, सुदिनाहं,<BR>अहःपतिः or अहर्पतिः &c. &c.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आगमः (अहरा˚) the approach of<BR>day.<BR>--आदिः dawn; Śi. 11. 62.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-c" target="_blank">Page0217-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--करः (˚हः or ˚स्करः) {1} the sun;<BR>अलवकारास्य वधूरहस्करः Śi. 1. 58;<BR>(P. III. 2. 21.). {2} a kind of tree.<BR>--गणः, (˚हर्ग˚) {1} a series of<BR>sacrificial days. {2} a month. {3} any<BR>calculated term (Wilson).<BR>--जरः<BR>[अहोभिः परिवर्तमानो लोकान् जरयति<BR>जॄ-णिच्-अच्, अहानि वा अस्मिन् जीर्यंति आधारे<BR>अप्वा Tv.] Ved. the year as making<BR>days old.<BR>--जात a. Ved. born in<BR>the day or from day, not belonging<BR>to night.<BR>--दिव a. (˚हर्दि˚) existing<BR>every day.<BR>--(वं) ind. [अहश्च दिवा च<BR>समा˚ द्वं˚] daily, every day, day by<BR>day; य इत्थमस्वास्थ्यमहर्दिवं दिवः<BR>Śi. 1. 51.<BR>--दिवि ind. day by day, every<BR>day, constantly.<BR>--दृश् a. Ved.<BR>belonging to the day; living.<BR>--नाथः<BR>{1} the sun, the lord of the day. {2}<BR>a kind of tree.<BR>--निशं [अहश्च निशा च<BR>समा˚ द्वं˚] a day and night, a whole<BR>day; Ms. 1. 74, 4. 97.<BR>--(शं) ind.<BR>day and night, during the whole<BR>day, continually.<BR>--पतिः [अहःपतिः,<BR>अहर्पतिः, अहस्पतिः P. VIII. 2. 70<BR>Vārt.] {1} the sun; ननु राह्वाह्वमहर्पतिं<BR>तमः Śi. 16. 57; R. 10. 54. {2} an<BR>epithet of Śiva. {3} a kind of tree.<BR>{4} swallow wort.<BR>--बांधवः the sun.<BR>--भाज्, --लोक a. Ved. partaking of<BR>the day.<BR>--मणिः the sun.<BR>--मुखं<BR>commencement of the day, morning,<BR>dawn.<BR>--रथंतरं (P. VIII. 2. 68 Vārt.)<BR>a portion of Sāma to be chanted at<BR>day.<BR>--रात्रः (--त्रं also) {1} a day and<BR>night (P. II. 4. 29); त्रीनहोरात्रान्<BR>Nala. 12. 44; त्रिंशत्कला मुहूर्तः<BR>स्यादहोरात्रं तु तावतः Ms. 1. 64, 65; Ms. 11. 84;<BR>Y. 1. 147. {2} a day of the Pitṛs, a<BR>month of the gods and a year of<BR>Brahmā.<BR>--विद् a. Ved. {1} existing<BR>many days. {2} known long ago. {3}<BR>one who knows the fit time or<BR>season of a sacrifice.<BR>--शेषः, --षं (<BR>˚हःशेषं) {1} evening. {2} the last day<BR>of defilement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहना
अहना Dawn, morning(उषा Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहम्
अहम् pron. (Nom. Sing. of<BR>अस्मद्). I [cf. Zend azem; L. ego; Germ.<BR>ich.]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रिका a contest<BR>for superiority, rivalry.<BR>--अहमिका<BR>[अहमहं शब्दोऽस्त्यत्र वीप्सायां द्वित्वं ठन् न<BR>टिलोपः P. II. 1. 72] {1} emulation,<BR>competition, assertion of<BR>superiority; अहमहमिका तु सा स्यात्परस्परं यो<BR>भवत्यहंकारः Ak.; अहमहमिकया<BR>प्रणामलालसानां K. 14, 81; अहमहमिकया<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0218-a" target="_blank">Page0218-a+ 57</a>]<BR>मधुकरकुलैरनुबध्यमानं 139, Mv. 6. 54.<BR>{2} egotism. {3} military vaunting.<BR>--कर्तव्य a. to be referred to self.<BR>--(व्यं) the object of अहंकार.<BR>--कारः<BR>{1} egotism, sense of self, self-love<BR>considered as an अविद्या or spiritual<BR>ignorance in Vedānta phil.;<BR>Bg. 2. 71, 7. 4; Ms. 1. 14; Y. 3. 177. {2}<BR>pride, self-consciousness, self-conceit,<BR>haughtiness. {3} (in Sān. phil.) the<BR>third of the eight producers or<BR>elements of creation, i. e. the conceit or<BR>conception of individuality, one of<BR>the 25 elements; Sāṅ. K. 22, 24, 25;<BR>˚वत् a. selfish, proud.<BR>--कारिन् a.<BR>proud, self-conceited.<BR>--कार्यं that<BR>which is to be done by oneself,<BR>personal business or object.<BR>--कृत a.<BR>{1} egotistic; Bg. 18. 17. {2} proud,<BR>haughty, Y. 3. 151.<BR>--कृतिः f.<BR>egotism, high opinion of oneself, pride.<BR>--पूर्व a. desirous of being first.<BR>--पूर्विका, --प्रथमिका [अहं पूर्वोऽहं पूर्व<BR>इत्यभिधानं यत्र] {1} the running<BR>forward of soldiers with emulation;<BR>(hence) emulation, competition;<BR>जवादहंपूर्विकया यियासुभिः Ki. 14. 32.<BR>{2} bragging, vaunting.<BR>--प्रत्ययः [<BR>अहमित्याकारकः प्रत्ययः] self-conceit.<BR>--भद्रं<BR>[अहमेव भद्र इति निर्णयो यत्र]<BR>self-conceit, high opinion of one's own<BR>superiority.<BR>--भावः {1} pride, egotism;<BR>अहंभावावृतो निस्त्रपः Bv. 4. 10. {2} = ˚मति<BR>q. v.<BR>--मतिः f. {1} self-love or<BR>self-illusion regarded as spiritual<BR>ignorance (in Vedānta phil.). {2}<BR>conceit, pride, egotism.<BR>--वादिन् a.<BR>speaking only of oneself, proud,<BR>haughty; Bg. 18. 26.<BR>--श्रेयस् or ˚सं<BR>n. claiming superiority for oneself;<BR>अहंश्रेयसे विवदमानाः Śat. Br.<BR>--सन a.<BR>Ved. gaining for oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0217-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहंयु|अहंयुः
अहंयु a. [अहं अहंकारोऽस्त्यस्य, अहं<BR>युस् P. V. 2. 140] Selfish, proud,<BR>haughty; Bk. 1. 20.<BR>--युः A warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहर|अहरः
अहर a. Not taking away; so<BR>अहरिन्.<BR>--रः A pure quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अहरणीय
अहरणीय, अहार्य a.<BR>1 Not to be<BR>stolen, removed, or taken away;<BR>अहार्यं ब्राह्मणद्रव्यं राज्ञां नित्यमिति<BR>स्थितिः Ms. 9. 189.<BR>--2 Not to be<BR>won over (by fraud), devoted,<BR>loyal; Ms. 7. 217.<BR>--3 Firm,<BR>unflinching, inexorable; ˚निश्चया Dk. 41,<BR>Ku. 5. 8.<BR>--र्यः A mountain; ˚ता,<BR>--त्वं not being liable to be taken<BR>away, security; H. Pr. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0218-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

