अहीन|अहीनः
अहीन a.<BR>1 Unimpaired, whole,<BR>entire, all; भृतभूतिरहीनभोगभाक्<BR>Śi. 16. 71.<BR>--2 Not inferior, great;<BR>अहीनबाहुद्रविणः शशास R. 18. 14; 9. 5.<BR>--3<BR>Not deprived of, possessed of;<BR>Ms. 2. 183.<BR>--4 Not outcast or vile.<BR>--5 (अहोभिः<BR>साध्यते, अहन्-ख P. IV. 2. 43) Lasting<BR>for several days; द्व्यहीन, त्र्यहीन &c.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A sacrifice lasting for several<BR>days (--नं also); Ms. 11. 198.<BR>--2 A<BR>large snake.<BR>--3 The lord of serpents,<BR>Vāsuki (अहि-इनः).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गुः N.<BR>of a king of the solar race;<BR>R. 18. 14.<BR>--वादिन् m. a witness unfit or<BR>incapable of giving evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

