अहुत|अहुतः
अहुत a.<BR>1 Not sacrificed or<BR>offered (as an oblation); Ms. 12. 68.<BR>--2 One who has not yet received<BR>any oblation.<BR>--तः Religious<BR>meditation, prayer, and the study of the<BR>Vedas (considered as one of the<BR>five great Yajñas and necessary<BR>duties); अहुतं च हुतं चैव तथा प्रहुतमेव च ।<BR>ब्राह्मं हुतं प्राशितं च पंचयज्ञान् प्रचक्षते ॥<BR>Ms. 3. 73, 74.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद a. {1}<BR>not eating of a sacrifice. {2} not<BR>allowed to partake of a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0219-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

