आकिंचनं, आकिंचन्यं Poverty,<BR>want of any possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीम्
आकीम् ind. Ved. From(with<BR>abl.); leaving, excluding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुंच्|आकुञ्च्
आकुंच् {c1c} A., {c6c} P. To bend.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To draw together,<BR>contract, bend inward, curve,<BR>compress; आकुंचितसव्यपादं Ku. 3. 70;<BR>R. 6. 15; Bh. 1. 3.<BR>--2 To shorten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुंचनं|आकुञ्चन|आकुञ्चनं
आकुंचनं<BR>1 Bending, contraction,<BR>compression; K. 78.<BR>--2 Contraction<BR>regarded as one of the 5 karmans<BR>q. v.<BR>--3 Collecting, heaping.<BR>--4<BR>Curving.<BR>--5 Contortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुल|आकुलं
आकुल a.<BR>1 Full of, burdened or<BR>filled with (in general);<BR>प्रचलदूर्मिमालाकुलं (समुद्रं) Bh. 2. 4;<BR>मृगपक्षिगणाकुलं Rām.; बाष्पाकुलांवाचं<BR>Nala. 4. 18; आलापकुतूहलाकुलतरे श्रोत्रे<BR>Amaru. 81.<BR>--2 Overcome, affected or<BR>afflicted, smit; हर्ष˚, शोक˚, विस्मय˚, स्नेह˚<BR>&c.<BR>--3 Busily or intently engaged or<BR>absorbed in; Ś. 4. 18.<BR>--4 Confounded,<BR>agitated, flurried, distracted;<BR>अभिचैद्यं प्रतिष्ठासुरासीत्कार्यद्वयाकुलः<BR>Śi. 2. 1; perplexed, at a loss what to<BR>do, undetermined; Ki. 2. 54.<BR>˚आकुल very much agitated;<BR>K. 10, 28; Ki. 14. 32.<BR>--5 Dishevelled,<BR>disordered (as hair);<BR>असंयताकुलालकान् K. 60, 243; Ratn. 1. 17;<BR>Ki. 8. 18.<BR>--6 Wild, dreary; Ś. 2.<BR>--7 Taken out of one's natural<BR>condition.<BR>--8 Incoherent, contradictory.<BR>--लं An inhabited place;<BR>रहितेष्वाकुलेषु च Rām. --adv. In bewilderment;<BR>Śi. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलता
आकुलता, --त्वं<BR>1 A multitude.<BR>--2<BR>Perplexity, bewilderment,<BR>confusion; Amaru. 72; Bh. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलत्वं|आकुलत्व
आकुलता, --त्वं<BR>1 A multitude.<BR>--2<BR>Perplexity, bewilderment,<BR>confusion; Amaru. 72; Bh. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलयति
आकुलयति Den. P. To confound,<BR>make disordered, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलित
आकुलित a.<BR>1 Distressed,<BR>confounded, agitated;<BR>मार्गाचलव्यतिकराकुलितेव सिंधुः Ku. 5. 85.<BR>--2 Entangled;<BR>K. 83.<BR>--3 Obscured, blinded; धूम˚<BR>दृष्टेः Ś. 4.<BR>--4 Overcome or affected;<BR>शोक˚, पिपासा˚ &c.<BR>--5 Disordered,<BR>deranged; R. 16. 67; Rs. 6. 17.<BR>--6<BR>Tilled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलीकृ
आकुलीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To fill with.<BR>--2 To confound, perplex, bewilder.<BR>--3 To overcome;<BR>कुतूहलेनाकुलीक्रियमाणो लघिमा K. 134.<BR>--4 To trouble,<BR>pain; Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकुलीभू
आकुलीभू {c1c} P. To be perplexed<BR>or agitated; इति प्रतिपादितमाकुलीभवेत्<BR>Ś. B. this conclusion would be<BR>shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूणित
आकूणित a. [आ-कूण्-क्त]<BR>Contracted, a little;<BR>मदनशरशल्यवेदनाकूणितत्रिभागेन K. 166, 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूतं|आकूत
आकूतं [आ-कू-भावे-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Meaning, intention, purpose;<BR>इतीरिताकूतमनीलवाजिनं Ki. 14. 26.<BR>--2 A<BR>feeling, state of heart, emotion;<BR>चूडामंडलबंधनं तरलयत्याकूतजो वेपथुः<BR>U. 5. 36; भावाकूतं Amaru. 4; Sāṅ. K. 31;<BR>Māl. 9. 11; स्नेहाकूत U. 6. 35; साकूतं<BR>feelingly, meaningly (oft. occurring<BR>in plays as a stage-direction).<BR>--3<BR>Wonder or curiosity; सर्वं ˚करं U. 4.<BR>--4 Wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकूतिः|आकूति
आकूतिः f. [आ-कू-भावे-क्तिन्]<BR>Intention, wish, desire; Rv. 10. 128. 4;<BR>आकूतीनां च चित्तीनां प्रवर्तकः Mb. ˚प्र^1 a.<BR>accomplishing one's own intentions.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by @aumsanskrit on 20251225. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/104  ap90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृ
आकृ {c8c} U., {c5c} P.<BR>1 To bring near<BR>or towards; to drive near or<BR>together.<BR>--2 To bring down; form<BR>wholly (Ved.). --Caus.<BR>1 To invite,<BR>call, summon; रदनिकामाकारय Mk. 3;<BR>Dk. 174; Pt. 1; मध्यस्थस्य<BR>दृष्टिमाकारयति Mk. 4 calls or arrests; Śi. 16. 52.<BR>--2 To prompt, incite, propel; ममापि<BR>कौतूहलेनाकारित एषः Ś. 6.<BR>--3 To call<BR>out boldly, challenge; Mk. 2.<BR>--4<BR>To cause to appear, produce.<BR>--5 To<BR>ask anything of one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारः|आकार
आकारः [आ-कृ-घञ्]<BR>1 Form, shape,<BR>figure; द्विधा˚ of two forms or sorts;<BR>Pt. 3. 37.<BR>--2 Aspect, appearance,<BR>mien, countenance; आकारसदृशप्रज्ञः<BR>R. 1. 15, 16. 7; Ś. 1.<BR>--3<BR>(Particularly) expression of the face, as giving<BR>a clue to one's inward thoughts<BR>or mental disposition; तस्य<BR>संवृतमंत्रस्य गूढाकारेंगितस्य च R. 1. 20;<BR>Pt. 1; भवानपि संवृताकारमास्तां<BR>V. 2; Ś. 7; Ki. 1. 14; साकारो निस्पृहः<BR>Pt. 3. 88 giving no clue to his<BR>inward thoughts, reserved; K. 233;<BR>Mv. 6; Ms. 7. 63, 8. 25-6.<BR>--4 Hint,<BR>sign, token.<BR>--5 Identity, oneness.<BR>--6<BR>Recognition of identity (in Sān.<BR>phil.).<BR>--7 The letter आ.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गुप्तिः, --गोपनं, --गूहनं dissimulation,<BR>suppressing all outward<BR>manifestation of the internal feelings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारणं|आकारण
आका(क)रणं, --णा<BR>1 Invitation,<BR>calling; भवदाकारणाय Dk. 175.<BR>--2 A<BR>challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरणं|आकरण
आका(क)रणं, --णा<BR>1 Invitation,<BR>calling; भवदाकारणाय Dk. 175.<BR>--2 A<BR>challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारणा
आका(क)रणं, --णा<BR>1 Invitation,<BR>calling; भवदाकारणाय Dk. 175.<BR>--2 A<BR>challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरणा
आका(क)रणं, --णा<BR>1 Invitation,<BR>calling; भवदाकारणाय Dk. 175.<BR>--2 A<BR>challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारवत्|आकारवन्त्
आकारवत् a.<BR>1 Embodied.<BR>--2<BR>Symmetrical, well-formed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकारित
आकारित a.<BR>1 Called.<BR>--2 Agreed<BR>upon.<BR>--3 Demanded, exacted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृत
आकृत p. p. Ved. Brought near to,<BR>being near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतिः|आकृति
आकृतिः f.<BR>1 Form, figure, shape (of<BR>anything); गोवर्धनस्याकृतिरन्वकारि<BR>Śi. 3. 4.<BR>--2 Bodily form, body;<BR>किमिव हि मधुराणां मंडनं नाकृतीनां<BR>Ś. 1. 20; विकृताकृति Ms. 11. 53; घोर˚,<BR>सौम्य˚ &c.<BR>--3 Appearance; oft.<BR>a good or noble appearance, good<BR>form; न ह्याकृतिः सुसदृशं विजहाति वृत्तं<BR>Mk. 9. 16; यत्राकृतिस्तत्र गुणा वसंति<BR>Subhāṣ.; आकृतिमनुगृह्णंति गुणाः<BR>Vb. 2.<BR>--4 Specimen, character.<BR>--5<BR>Tribe, species.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गणः a list<BR>of words belonging to a certain<BR>grammatical rule which does not give<BR>every word belonging to that rule,<BR>but only specimens, a list of specimens<BR>(frequently occurring in the<BR>Gaṇapāṭha); e. g. अर्श आदिगण, स्वरादिगण, चादि<BR>गण &c.<BR>--छत्रा the plant Achyranthes<BR>Aspera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृतिमत्|आकृतिमन्त्
आकृतिमत् a.<BR>1 Embodied.<BR>--2<BR>Selfformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्
आकृष् {c1c} P., {c6c} U.<BR>1 To draw<BR>towards, draw, drag, pull,<BR>attract (fig. also); केशेष्वाकृष्य चुंबति<BR>H. 1. 109; दूरममुता सारंगेण वयमाकृष्टाः<BR>Ś. 1; (मनः) शंभोर्यतध्वमाक्रष्टुमयस्कांतेन<BR>लोहवत् Ku. 2. 59; अनाकृष्टस्य विषयैः<BR>R. 1. 23 not attracted or seduced;<BR>लोभाकृष्टः H. 1; Śānti. 3. 5, 4. 16;<BR>पादाकृष्टव्रतति Ś. 1. 33, Amaru. 2, 72.<BR>--2 To draw or bend (as a bow);<BR>Śi. 9. 40; Ś. 3. 5.<BR>--3 To draw or<BR>take out; हस्तात्कटकमाकृष्य Mk. 2;<BR>U. 1.<BR>--4 To extract, borrow (from<BR>another source) H. Pr. 9.<BR>--5 To<BR>draw or carry along; to waft or be<BR>charged with; U. 3. 2.<BR>--6 To deprive,<BR>take away by force, snatch;<BR>Bk. 16. 30.<BR>--7 To supply a word or words<BR>from another rule or sentence.<BR>--Caus. To draw near to oneself,<BR>pull together; वस्त्रमाकर्षयंती<BR>Rs. 5. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षः|आकर्ष
आकर्षः<BR>1 Attracting or drawing<BR>towards oneself.<BR>--2 Drawing away<BR>from, withdrawing; U. 3. 46.<BR>--3<BR>Drawing (a bow).<BR>--4 Attraction,<BR>fascination.<BR>--5 Spasm.<BR>--6 Playing<BR>with dice; आकर्षस्तेऽवाक्फलः Mb.<BR>--7 A die or dice.<BR>--8 A board for a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">Page0223-a+ 57</a>]<BR>game with dice.<BR>--9 An organ of<BR>sense.<BR>--10 A magnet, a loadstone.<BR>--11 A touch-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0222-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षक|आकर्षकः
आकर्षक a. Attracting, attractive.<BR>--कः A magnet, a loadstone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षण|आकर्षणं
आकर्षण a. Attracting, carrying<BR>to another place.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Pulling,<BR>drawing, attracting.<BR>--2 Seduction.<BR>--णी<BR>1 A curved stick for pulling<BR>down fruits, flowers &c. (standing<BR>on elevated places); any instrument<BR>for pulling.<BR>--2 A variety of Mudrā<BR>(or mark on the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिक
आकर्षिक a. (की f.) Magnetic,<BR>attractive (आकर्षेण चरति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकर्षिन्
आकर्षिन् a. Attractive(as a smell<BR>at a distance).<BR>--णी A rod with a<BR>hook at the end for pulling down<BR>boughs in order to gather fruits &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकृष्टिः|आकृष्टि
आकृष्टिः f.<BR>1 Attraction(in<BR>general).<BR>--2 Attraction,<BR>gravitation (in astr.); आकृष्टिशक्तिश्च मही तया<BR>यत् खस्थ गुरु स्वाभिमुखं स्वशक्त्या । आकृष्यते<BR>तत्पततीव भाति समे समंतात् क्व पतत्वियं खे ॥<BR>Golādh. 1.<BR>--3 Drawing or bending<BR>of a bow; ज्या˚ Amaru. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मंत्रः an incantation by which<BR>another person is attracted;<BR>आकृष्टिमंत्रोपमं H. 1. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकॄ
आकॄ {c6c} P.<BR>1 To scatter or spread<BR>over, fill, fill up, cover, heap up (used<BR>chiefly in p. p. q. v.).<BR>--2 To dig up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरः|आकर
आकरः [by P. III. 3. 118<BR>आकुर्वंत्यस्मिन्; कॄ-अप्]<BR>1 A mine; मणिराकरोद्भवः<BR>R. 3. 18; आकरे पद्मरागाणां जन्म<BR>काचमणेः कुतः H. Pr. 44; Ms. 7. 62;<BR>Y. 3. 242; (fig.) a mine or rich source<BR>of anything (उत्पत्तिस्थानं); मासो नु<BR>पुष्पाकरः V. 1. 9; अशेषगुणाकरं<BR>Bh. 2. 92; Mk. 8. 38; Mu. 7. 7.<BR>--2 A<BR>collection, group; पद्माकरं दिनकरो<BR>विकचीकरोति Bh. 2. 73; Ku. 2. 29;<BR>Māl. 9. 47.<BR>--3 Best, excellent.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of a country.<BR>--5 N. of the<BR>Mahābhāshya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरिकः|आकरिक
आकरिकः [आकरे नियुक्तः ठञ्] A<BR>person appointed (by the king) to<BR>superintend a mine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकरिन्
आकरिन् a. [आकर-इनि]<BR>1<BR>Produced in a mine, mineral.<BR>--2 Of good<BR>breed; दधतमाकरिभिः करिभिः क्षतैः<BR>Ki. 5. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकीर्ण|आकीर्णं|आकीर्ण्ण
आकीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Scattered or spread<BR>over.<BR>--2 Filled or overspread with,<BR>crowded, full of, abounding in;<BR>जनाकीर्णं मन्ये हुतवहपरीतं गृहमिव Ś. 5. 10;<BR>आकीर्णमृषिपत्नीनामुटजद्वाररोधिभिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">Page0223-b+ 56</a>]<BR>R. 1. 50; Pt. 1. 375; Ms. 6. 51.<BR>--र्णं A<BR>crowd; V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आके
आके ind. Ved.<BR>1 Near, in the<BR>neighbourhood.<BR>--2 Distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकेकर
आकेकर a. Half-shut, half-closed<BR>(eyes); निमीलदाकेकरलोलचक्षुषा<BR>Ki. 8. 53; Māl. 5; K. 81; Mu. 3. 21;<BR>दृष्टिराकेकरा किंचित्स्फुटापांगे प्रसारिता ।<BR>मीलितार्धपुटालोके ताराव्यावर्तनोत्तरा ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकेनिप
आकेनिप a. Ved. Advancing<BR>near (as rays of light); wise (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आकोकेरः|आकोकेर
आकोकेरः The sign Capricornus;<BR>(a word of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रंद्|आक्रन्द्
आक्रंद् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To lament, weep,<BR>cry, cry out, creak, scream;<BR>तृणाग्रलग्नैस्तुहिनैः पतद्भिराक्रंदतीवोषसि शीतकालः<BR>Rs. 4. 7; Bk. 15. 50.<BR>--2 To shout,<BR>roar.<BR>--3 To invoke, call out to;<BR>आक्रंदीद्भीमसेनं वै Mb. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>cause to weep or cry.<BR>--2 To call out<BR>to; एह्येहीति शिखंडिनां पटुतरैः<BR>केकाभिराक्रंदितः Mk. 5. 23.<BR>--3 To inspire<BR>courage by the sound of a drum.<BR>--4<BR>To shout or roar at; to cry<BR>incessantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रंदः|आक्रन्द|आक्रन्दः
आक्रंदः<BR>1 Weeping, crying out;<BR>किं क्रंदसि दुराक्रंद Pt. 4. 29.<BR>--2<BR>Calling, invoking, calling out to;<BR>Ms. 8. 292.<BR>--3 Sound, war-cry, a cry<BR>(in general); आक्रंद उदभूत्तत्र<BR>Ks. 10 94.<BR>--4 A friend, defender.<BR>--5 A<BR>brother.<BR>--6 A fierce or violent<BR>combat, war, battle.<BR>--7 A place of crying.<BR>--8 A king who prevents an ally<BR>from aiding another; a king whose<BR>kingdom lies next but one;<BR>प्रार्ष्णिग्राहं च संप्रेक्ष्य तथाक्रंदं च मंडले<BR>Ms. 7. 207 (see Kull. thereon).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रंदनं|आक्रन्दन
आक्रंदनं<BR>1 Lamentation, weeping,<BR>cry of lamentation.<BR>--2 Calling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रंदिक|आक्रन्दिक
आक्रंदिक a. [आक्रंदं धावति ठञ्<BR>P. IV. 4. 38] One who runs to a place<BR>where cries (of distress) are heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रंदित|आक्रन्दित
आक्रंदित p. p.<BR>1 Roaring, crying or<BR>weeping bitterly.<BR>--2 Invoked,<BR>called.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A cry, roar; R. 2. 28.<BR>--2<BR>Lamentation, weeping, V. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रंदिन्|आक्रन्दिन्
आक्रंदिन् a. Calling out in a<BR>weeping tone, weeping, shouting at;<BR>Ku. 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रम्
आक्रम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To go towards<BR>or near, approach; अंतरिक्षं, आश्रमं<BR>&c.<BR>--2 To step or tread upon,<BR>enter, fill, take possession of,<BR>cover; भुजगपतिरयं मे मार्गमाक्रम्य सुप्तः<BR>Mk. 9. 12 covering; खं केशवोऽपर<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-c" target="_blank">Page0223-c+ 58</a>]<BR>इवाक्रमितुं प्रवृत्तः 5. 2;<BR>छायामप्याक्रमितु Ve. 3; Śi. 8. 28 to enter or<BR>cross; Ms. 4. 130; Y. 1. 152; पदा<BR>मस्तकमाक्रम्य Ms. 11. 43;<BR>जंबुद्वीपमाक्रम्य H. 3; आक्रामति धूमो हर्म्यतलं<BR>Mbh.<BR>--3 To occupy, extend over;<BR>योजनानां सहस्राणि बहूनाक्रम्य तिष्ठति<BR>Ks. 1. 15.<BR>--4 To attack, invade,<BR>seize, fall upon, conquer, overcome,<BR>vanquish; पक्षिशावकानाक्रम्य H. 1;<BR>2. 97;<BR>पौरस्त्यानेवमाक्रामंस्तांस्ताञ्जनपदाञ्जयी R. 4. 34; H. 4; तं<BR>न… शेकुराक्रमितुमन्यपार्थिवाः<BR>R. 19. 48; Bh. 1. 70; Śi. 1. 70.<BR>--5 To<BR>surpass, excel, eclipse.<BR>--6 To<BR>undertake, begin, commence<BR>--7 (A.) To<BR>rise, come up (as the sun);<BR>यावत्प्रतापनिधिराक्रमते न भानुः R. 5. 71, आक्रमते<BR>सूर्यः Mbh.<BR>--8 To ascend, mount,<BR>occupy (as sky, throne &c);<BR>दिवमाक्रममाणेव Bk. 8. 23; Śi. 18. 14, 51;<BR>सिंहासनं, स्वर्गलोकं; ध्वजं &c.<BR>--9 To lie<BR>heavily upon, to press (as a load).<BR>(For further illustrations of the<BR>several senses see आक्रांत below). --Caus.<BR>(क्र-क्रा-मयति) To cause to enter,<BR>introduce, show into; स<BR>तैराक्रमयामास शुद्धांतं Ku. 6. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रमः|आक्रम
आक्रमः, --मणं<BR>1 Coming near,<BR>approaching.<BR>--2 Falling upon,<BR>attacking; an attack; Śi. 16. 34.<BR>--3<BR>Seizing, taking, covering, occupying.<BR>--4<BR>Overcoming; obtaining.<BR>--5<BR>Spreading or going over, surpassing.<BR>--6<BR>Overloading.<BR>--7 Might, valour.<BR>--8<BR>Possession of learning &c.<BR>--9 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रमणं|आक्रमण
आक्रमः, --मणं<BR>1 Coming near,<BR>approaching.<BR>--2 Falling upon,<BR>attacking; an attack; Śi. 16. 34.<BR>--3<BR>Seizing, taking, covering, occupying.<BR>--4<BR>Overcoming; obtaining.<BR>--5<BR>Spreading or going over, surpassing.<BR>--6<BR>Overloading.<BR>--7 Might, valour.<BR>--8<BR>Possession of learning &c.<BR>--9 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रांत|आक्रान्त|आक्रान्तः
आक्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Seized, taken<BR>possession of, overpowered, defeated,<BR>vanquished, overcome;<BR>आक्रांतविमानमार्गं R. 13. 37 reaching upto; रुजा˚<BR>Pt. 5. 52; दिदृक्षा˚ हृदयः Dk. 141<BR>seized with; आतपाक्रांतोयमुद्देशः<BR>M. 3 exposed to heat;<BR>आक्रांतपूर्वमिव भुजंगं R. 9. 79 trodden or<BR>trampled under foot; filled with,<BR>full of, occupied, covered,<BR>overspread; शुशुभे तेन चाक्रांतं मंगलायतनं<BR>महत् R. 17. 29; Bh. 2. 108;<BR>वलिभिर्मुखमाक्रांतं Bh. 3. 14, 62; U. 2. 20;<BR>Mv. 5. 40; Śi. 1. 70; H. 1. 24; Dk. 141;<BR>K. 55; Ve. 2. 26; ˚मति having the<BR>mind engrossed or occupied;<BR>U. 5. 19; Māl. 9. 48; so मदन, ˚भय, ˚शोक˚<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Loaded (as with a burden);<BR>भाराक्रांता वसुंधरा Mk. 8. 6; K. 118;<BR>Amaru. 30.<BR>--3 Surpassed, eclipsed,<BR>superseded; R. 10. 38, Ve. 5,<BR>M. 3. 5.<BR>--4 Obtained, possessed of;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">Page0224-a+ 56</a>]<BR>वर्णांतराक्रांतपयोधराग्रां R. 14. 27;<BR>Ki. 11. 7.<BR>--5 Accompanied, attended.<BR>--6<BR>Pained, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0223-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रांतिः|आक्रान्ति|आक्रान्तिः
आक्रांतिः f.<BR>1 Placing upon,<BR>occupying; stepping or treading upon;<BR>आक्रांतिसंभावितपादपीठं Ku. 3. 11.<BR>--2<BR>Overcoming, pressing upon,<BR>loading; Mu. 3. 10.<BR>--3 Ascending,<BR>rising.<BR>--4 Might, valour, force;<BR>Śi. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रामकः|आक्रामक
आक्रामकः An invader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्री
आक्री {c9c} U. To purchase, buy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रयः|आक्रय
आक्रयः A dealer, petty trader,<BR>a pedlar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीड्
आक्रीड् {c1c} U. To play, sport,<BR>amuse oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीड|आक्रीडः
आक्रीड a. Playing, sporting.<BR>--डः,<BR>--डं<BR>1 Play, sport, pleasure.<BR>--2 A<BR>pleasure-grove, pleasure-garden;<BR>आक्रीडपर्वतास्तेन कल्पिताः स्वेषु वेश्मसु<BR>Ku. 2. 43; कमप्याक्रीडमासाद्य तत्र<BR>विशश्रमिषुः Dk. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडनं|आक्रीडन
आक्रीडनं Sporting, playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रीडिन्
आक्रीडिन् a. Playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रुश्
आक्रुश् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To cry, cry out<BR>loudly; अयं गौरीनाथ त्रिपुरहर शंभो त्रिनयन<BR>प्रसीदेत्याक्राशन् Bh. 3. 123; call out<BR>loudly to; पतिमाचुक्रुशुः Rām.<BR>--2 To<BR>revile, abuse, scold, assail with<BR>angry words; परस्य हेतोर्मामाक्रोशसि<BR>Dk. 58, 97; शतं ब्राह्मणमाक्रुश्य<BR>क्षत्रियो दंडमर्हति Ms. 8. 267; 6. 48;<BR>Bk. 5. 39.<BR>--3 To curse.<BR>--4 To censure,<BR>express displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रुष्ट
आक्रुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Scolded, reviled,<BR>censured, abused, calumniated &c.<BR>Śi. 12. 27.<BR>--2 Sounded, vociferated.<BR>--3 Cursed.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 Calling out.<BR>--2 A<BR>harsh cry or sound, an abusive speech<BR>(परुषभाषणं); मार्जारमूषिकास्पर्शे आक्रुष्टे<BR>क्रोधसंभवे Kāty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशः|आक्रोश
आक्रोशः, --शनं<BR>1 Calling or crying<BR>out, vociferation, loud cry or sound.<BR>--2 Censure, blame, reviling;<BR>आक्रोशमपि परिहासमाकलयंति K. 235,<BR>291; abuse Y. 2. 302.<BR>--3 A curse,<BR>imprecation; ˚गर्भमेवमुक्तं K. 291,<BR>346.<BR>--4 An oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशनं|आक्रोशन
आक्रोशः, --शनं<BR>1 Calling or crying<BR>out, vociferation, loud cry or sound.<BR>--2 Censure, blame, reviling;<BR>आक्रोशमपि परिहासमाकलयंति K. 235,<BR>291; abuse Y. 2. 302.<BR>--3 A curse,<BR>imprecation; ˚गर्भमेवमुक्तं K. 291,<BR>346.<BR>--4 An oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोशक|आक्रोशकः
आक्रोशक, --क्रोष्टृ a.<BR>1 Vociferous,<BR>one who calls out or vociferates.<BR>--2 A reviler, abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्रोष्टृ
आक्रोशक, --क्रोष्टृ a.<BR>1 Vociferous,<BR>one who calls out or vociferates.<BR>--2 A reviler, abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्ली
आक्ली ind. An indeclinable<BR>joined to the roots, कृ, भू and अस्;<BR>see Gaṇa on P. I. 4. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्लेदः|आक्लेद
आक्लेदः Moistening, wetting,<BR>sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षद्यूतिक
आक्षद्यूतिक a. (की f.) [अक्षद्यूतेन<BR>निर्वृत्तम् ठक्] Effected or completed<BR>by gambling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपणं|आक्षपण
आक्षपणं Fasting, purifying by<BR>fasting, abstinence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाटिकः|आक्षपाटिक
आक्षपाटिकः [अक्षपट-ठक्]<BR>1 A<BR>judge at playing with dice,<BR>superintendent of a gambling house.<BR>--2<BR>A judge, arranger of law-suits; see<BR>अक्षपाटक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षपाद|आक्षपादः
आक्षपाद a. (दी f.) [अक्षपाद-अण्]<BR>Taught by Akṣapāda or Gautama.<BR>--दः A follower of the Nyāya<BR>system of philosophy, a logician.<BR>--दं<BR>The Nyāya system of philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षर्
आक्षर् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To abuse, revile,<BR>accuse falsely, calumniate;<BR>यस्त्वनाक्षारितः पूर्वं Ms. 8. 355, 354, 275.<BR>--2 To punish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारः|आक्षार
आक्षारः A charge or calumny,<BR>accusation (of adultery).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारणं|आक्षारण
आक्षारणं, --णा Calumnious<BR>accusation (especially of adultery): तत्र<BR>त्वाक्षारणा यः स्याद क्रोशो मैथुनं प्रति Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारणा
आक्षारणं, --णा Calumnious<BR>accusation (especially of adultery): तत्र<BR>त्वाक्षारणा यः स्याद क्रोशो मैथुनं प्रति Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षारित|आक्षारितं
आक्षारित p. p.<BR>1 Calumniated.<BR>--2 Accused of adultery or<BR>fornication.<BR>--3 Guilty, criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षि
आक्षि {c2c} {c6c} P. Ved.<BR>1 To abide,<BR>dwell in, stay (with).<BR>--2 To be or<BR>exist.<BR>--3 To possess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षित्
आक्षित् a. Abiding, dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिक|आक्षिकः
आक्षिक a. (की f.) [अक्षेण दीव्यति<BR>जयति जितं वा; अक्ष-ठक् P. IV. 4. 2]<BR>1<BR>One who plays at dice.<BR>--2 One<BR>who uses loaded dice (<BR>भारभूतानक्षानाहरति वहति).<BR>--3 One who gains by<BR>gambling.<BR>--4 Won by gambling.<BR>--5<BR>Relating to dice or gambling;<BR>आक्षिकं ऋणं Ms. 8. 159 incurred in<BR>gambling.<BR>--कः N. of a tree (=<BR>अक्षिक q. v.).<BR>--कं<BR>1 Money gained by<BR>gambling.<BR>--2 Gambling debt, money<BR>lost at play.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पणः a<BR>stake, a wager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्
आक्षिप् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To throw or cast<BR>down, dash down; फलं तरंगाक्षिप्तं<BR>Pt. 4; शिलायामाक्षिप्य Pt. 1.<BR>--2 To<BR>attract, entice, allure, win over;<BR>यथा नाक्षिप्यसे विषयैः K. 109;<BR>Śi. 10. 79.<BR>--3 To strike with a dart, missile<BR>&c.<BR>--4 To draw near or together,<BR>contract, convulse (used in medicine).<BR>--5<BR>To interrupt, cut short; एवंवादिनो<BR>वचनमाक्षिप्य K. 18, 207; Ve. 6.<BR>--6 To draw back or withdraw;<BR>take or throw off, snatch or draw<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-c" target="_blank">Page0224-c+ 58</a>]<BR>away, pull off; अग्रपादमाक्षिप्य<BR>R. 7. 7; Ku. 7. 58; वासो बलादाक्षिपन्<BR>Bh. 1. 43; Me. 68.<BR>--7 To chase, drive<BR>out of a place, remove; स<BR>एतानाक्षिपद्राष्ट्रात् Mb.; आक्षिप्ताधिकारयोः<BR>Mu. 1.<BR>--8 To hang out, expose to<BR>view (as a banner).<BR>--9 To point to,<BR>refer to, hint at, indicate; वस्तुतस्तु नेह<BR>पूर्वपदमाक्षिप्यते P. VI. 3. 34 Sk.;<BR>अश्वादय आक्षिप्यंते S. D. 2.<BR>--10 To<BR>reject, neglect, disregard, spurn;<BR>Amaru. 79.<BR>--11 To object to (as<BR>argument).<BR>--12 To insult; अरेरे<BR>राधागर्भभारभूत किमेवमाक्षिपसि Ve. 3;<BR>to blame; Śānti. 1. 18.<BR>--13 To<BR>eclipse, obscure; आक्षिपंतीमिव प्रभां<BR>शशिनः स्वेन तेजसा Mb.<BR>--14 To infer<BR>(from circumstances); जात्या<BR>व्यक्तिराक्षिप्यते K. P. 2.<BR>--15 To say or<BR>state ironically.<BR>--16 To pass (as<BR>time); Śi. 14. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्त
आक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Cast, thrown down.<BR>--2 Overthrown, repulsed;<BR>Ratn. 4. 12.<BR>--3 Seized, grasped, snatched<BR>away; V. 5. 5.<BR>--4 Drawn, attracted,<BR>overpowered; कौतुक˚, कुतूहल˚<BR>U. 4; seduced, enticed; K. 281.<BR>--5<BR>Perplexed, distracted, bewildered;<BR>˚मिव मे चेतः Ve. 2.<BR>--6 Insulted,<BR>reviled, abused.<BR>--7 Equal or<BR>equivalent to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षिप्तिका
आक्षिप्तिका A particular air or song<BR>sung by a character while<BR>approaching the stage; V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपः|आक्षेप
आक्षेपः<BR>1 Throwing off, tossing,<BR>pulling off, snatching away;<BR>अशुकाक्षेपविलज्जितानां Ku. 1. 14;<BR>withdrawing; Ku. 7. 95; movement,<BR>shaking; K. 13.<BR>--2 Reviling,<BR>censure, blame, abuse, reproach,<BR>defiant censure; ˚प्रचंडत्तया U. 5. 29;<BR>विरुद्धमाक्षेपवचरिततिक्षितं Ki. 14. 25;<BR>Bh. 2. 69.<BR>--3 Drawing together,<BR>attraction, diverting;<BR>कथारसस्याक्षेपसामंर्थ्यं K. 346, 348 power to<BR>interest.<BR>--4 Distraction, allurement;<BR>विषयाक्षेपपर्यस्तबुद्धेः Bh. 3. 47, 23.<BR>--5 Throwing away, giving up.<BR>--6<BR>Applying, laying on, putting in<BR>or into (as a colour);<BR>गोरोचनाक्षेपनितांतगौरैः Ku. 7. 17.<BR>--7 Hinting<BR>at, reference to, taking to oneself or<BR>assuming (as the meaning of another<BR>word); स्वसिद्धये पराक्षेपः K. P. 2.<BR>--8 An inference.<BR>--9 A deposit.<BR>--10 An objection or doubt.<BR>--11<BR>Convulsion, palpitation.<BR>--12<BR>Sustaining, as a sound.<BR>--13 (In Rhet.) A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">Page0225-a+ 55</a>]<BR>figure of speech (cf. Greek paralipsis)<BR>in which something really intended<BR>to be said is apparently<BR>suppressed or denied to convey a<BR>particular meaning; आक्षेपः स्वयमुक्तस्य<BR>प्रतिषेधो विचारणात् । चंद्र<BR>संदर्शयात्मानमथवास्ति प्रियामुखम् ॥ Kuval. For fuller<BR>definitions and explanations see<BR>K. P. 10, S. D. 714 and<BR>Ākṣepaprakaraṇa in R. G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0224-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपक|आक्षेपकः
आक्षेपक^1 a.<BR>1 Drawing; drawing<BR>or snatching off.<BR>--2 Censuring,<BR>reviling.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A thrower.<BR>--2 A<BR>detractor, calumniator, accuser.<BR>--3 A<BR>hunter.<BR>--4 (In medic.)<BR>Convulsion, spasm.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: prev. word akzI.., next is akze....<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपणं|आक्षेपण
आक्षेपणं Throwing, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षेपिन्
आक्षेपिन् a.<BR>1 Drawing or<BR>snatching up; Māl. 9. 51.<BR>--2 Drawing in<BR>with a minute eye;<BR>बाह्याभ्यंतरविषयाक्षेपी चतुर्थः Pat. Sūt.<BR>--3 Applying to,<BR>regarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षीव
आक्षीव a.<BR>1 Somewhat drunk.<BR>--2 Intoxicated.<BR>--वः = अक्षीव q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षैत्रज्ञ्यं|आक्षैत्रज्ञ्य
आक्षैत्रज्ञ्यं [अक्षेत्रज्ञ --ष्यञ्]<BR>Spiritual ignorance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोटः|आक्षोट
आक्षोटः --डः A walnut; see अक्षोट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोडः|आक्षोड
आक्षोटः --डः A walnut; see अक्षोट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्षोदनं|आक्षोदन
आक्षोदनं Hunting (for आच्छोदनं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आक्ष्यत्|आक्ष्यन्त्
आक्ष्यत् a. (fr. अश् or अक्ष्)<BR>Leading to completion (as days),<BR>epithet of certain days on which the<BR>ceremony Ayana performed for the<BR>Ādityas and Aṅgirasas is finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखण
आखण a. Hard(to dig up)<BR>(as a stone).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखंडलः|आखण्डल|आखण्डलः
आखंडलः [आखंडयति भेदयति<BR>पर्वतान्, खंड्-डलच् डस्य नेत्वम् Tv.] Indra;<BR>आखंडलः काममिदं बभाषे Ku. 3. 11;<BR>तमीशः कामरूपाणामत्याखंडलविक्रमम्<BR>R. 4. 83; Me. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखः|आख
आखः, आखनः [खन् --ड<BR>P. III. 3. 125] A spade, hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनः|आखन
आखः, आखनः [खन् --ड<BR>P. III. 3. 125] A spade, hoe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनिकः|आखनिक
आखनिकः [आ --खन् --इकन्<BR>Uṇ. 2. 45]<BR>1 A digger, ditcher, miner.<BR>--2<BR>A mouse or rat.<BR>--3 A hog.<BR>--4 A<BR>thief.<BR>--5 A spade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखनिकबकः|आखनिकबक
आखनिकबकः [आ-खन्-करणे कर्त्तरि वा<BR>इकबक P. III. 3. 125 Vārt.]<BR>1 A stork<BR>in relation to a mouse; (fig.) a man<BR>who behaves like a hero towards a<BR>weak person.<BR>--2 = आखनिक q. v. above<BR>(= खनित्रं Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखरः|आखर
आखरः<BR>1 A spade.<BR>--2 A digger,<BR>miner.<BR>--3 A cover of any animal;<BR>a stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखातः|आखात|आखातं
आखातः --तं A natural pond or<BR>pool of water, bay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखातं|आखात|आखातः
आखातः --तं A natural pond or<BR>pool of water, bay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखानः|आखान
आखानः [आ-खन्-घञ्]<BR>1 Digging<BR>all around.<BR>--2 A spade, a digger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखुः|आखु
आखुः [आखनतीत्याखुः, आखण्-डु<BR>Uṇ. 1. 33]<BR>1 A mouse, rat, mole; अत्तुं<BR>वांछति शांभवो गणपतेराखुं क्षुधार्तः फणी<BR>Pt. 1. 159.<BR>--2 A thief.<BR>--3 A hog.<BR>--4<BR>A spade.<BR>--5 A miser; विभवे सति नैवात्ति<BR>न ददाति जुहोति न तमाहुराखुं.<BR>--6 The<BR>grass Lipeocercis Serrata (देवताड).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्करः a mole-hill.<BR>--उत्थ<BR>a. produced from a mouse.<BR>--(त्थः)<BR>[आखूनामुत्थानं P. III. 2. 4 Vārt.]<BR>the rising or appearance of rats,<BR>a swarm of rats.<BR>--करीषं a mole-hill.<BR>--कर्णपर्णिका, --पर्णिका, --कर्णी, --पर्णी the<BR>plant Salvinia Cucullata Roxb.<BR>--गः, --पत्रः, --रथः, --वाहनः epithets of<BR>Gaṇeśa (whose vehicle is a rat);<BR>तमाखुपत्रं राजेंद्र भज माज्ञानदायकं Subhāṣ.<BR>--घातः a Śūdra or a man of low<BR>caste and profession; (lit.) rat-catcher<BR>or killer.<BR>--पाषाणः {1} a kind of<BR>mineral. {2} a loadstone.<BR>--भुज्, --भुजः<BR>a cat.<BR>--विषहा a kind of grass (<BR>देवताडवृक्ष, देवतालीलता) considered as a<BR>remedy for a rat's bite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटः|आखेट
आखेटः [आखिट्यंते त्रास्यंते प्राणिनोऽत्र,<BR>आ-खिट्-घञ् Tv.] Hunting, chase.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शीर्षकं {1} a smooth floor or<BR>ground (कुट्टिमभेद). {2} a mine, cavern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटक|आखेटकः
आखेटक a. Hunting, frightening<BR>(as beasts of prey &c.).<BR>--कः A<BR>hunter; Pt. 1. 129, 388.<BR>--कं Hunting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखेटिक|आखेटिकः
आखेटिक a. [आखेटे कुशलः ठक्]<BR>1<BR>Skilful in chase.<BR>--2 Terrible,<BR>frightful.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A hunter.<BR>--2 A hound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आखोटः|आखोट
आखोटः The walnut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
आख्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 (a) To tell, say,<BR>inform, communicate, narrate<BR>(usually with dat. of person); ते<BR>रामाय वधोपायमाचख्युर्विबुधद्विषः R. 15. 5,<BR>41, 71, 93; 12. 42, 91; Bg. 11. 31,<BR>18. 63; Me. 100; Ms. 8. 224, 9. 73,<BR>Y. 1. 66, 2. 65; sometimes with gen.<BR>of person; आख्याहि भद्रे प्रियदर्शनस्य<BR>Pt. 4. 15; केनाहं तवाख्यातः Mb. (b) To<BR>declare, announce, signify; R. 2. 11.<BR>--2 To call, denominate, name;<BR>सुवर्णबिंदुरित्याख्यायते Māl. 9; R. 10. 21,<BR>Ms. 4. 6.<BR>--3 To look at, count; to<BR>recite (Ved.). --Caus. (ख्यापयति)<BR>1<BR>To cause to tell or narrate.<BR>--2 To<BR>declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्या
आख्या [आ-ख्यायते अनेन; आख्या<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-c" target="_blank">Page0225-c+ 58</a>]<BR>अङ्] A name, appellation; किं वा<BR>शकुंतलेत्यस्य मातुराख्या Ś. 7, 7. 33;<BR>पश्चादुमाख्यां सुमुखी जगाम Ku. 1. 26;<BR>तदाख्यया भुवि पप्रथे R. 15. 101<BR>became known by that name; often<BR>at the end of compounds meaning<BR>‘named’ or ‘called’; अथ<BR>किमाख्यस्य राजर्षेः सा धर्मपत्नी Ś. 7; रघुवंशाख्यं<BR>काव्यं &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यात|आख्यातं
आख्यात p. p.<BR>1 Said, told,<BR>declared.<BR>--2 Counted, recited.<BR>--3 Made<BR>known.<BR>--4 Inflected or conjugated,<BR>--तं A verb; भावग्रधानमाख्यातं Nir.;<BR>धात्वर्थेन विशिष्ठस्य विधेयत्वेन बोधने । समर्थः<BR>स्वार्थयत्नस्य शब्दो वाख्यातमुच्यते ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातिः|आख्याति
आख्यातिः f.<BR>1 Telling, informing,<BR>communication, publication (of a<BR>report &c.).<BR>--2 Fame.<BR>--3 A name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यातृ
आख्यातृ m.<BR>1 One who tells,<BR>communicates &c.<BR>--2 A teacher,<BR>instructor; P. I. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यानं|आख्यान
आख्यानं<BR>1 Speaking, declaration,<BR>making known, relation,<BR>communication; इत्थंभूताख्याने P. I. 4. 90;<BR>रामसंदेश˚ Rām.<BR>--2 Allusion to some<BR>old tale; आख्यानं पूर्ववृत्तोक्तिः S. D.; (<BR>e. g. देशः सोऽयमरातिशोणितजलैर्यस्मिन्ह्रदाः<BR>पूरिताः Ve. 3. 31).<BR>--3 A tale, story;<BR>especially, a legendary story, legend;<BR>अप्सराः पुरूरवसं चकम<BR>इत्याख्यानविदआचक्षते Māl. 2; Ms. 3. 232.<BR>--4 A<BR>legendary work such as the<BR>Mahābhārata.<BR>--5 A reply; प्रश्नाख्यानयोः<BR>P. VIII. 2. 105, III. 3. 110.<BR>--6 A<BR>differentiating property (भेदकधर्म).<BR>--7<BR>A canto of an epic poem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यानकं|आख्यानक
आख्यानकं A tale, a short<BR>legendary narrative, an episode;<BR>आख्यानकाख्यायिकेतिहासपुराणाकर्णनेन K. 7;<BR>P. IV. 2. 60 Vārt.<BR>--की N. of a metre<BR>which is a combination of<BR>Indravajrā and Upendravajrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायक|आख्यायकः
आख्यायक a. Telling, informing.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A messenger, courier;<BR>आख्यायकेभ्यः श्रुतसूनुवृत्तिः Bk. 2. 44.<BR>--2 A herald; U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायिका
आख्यायिका<BR>1 A species of prose<BR>composition, a connected story or<BR>narrative; आख्यायिका कथावत् स्यात्<BR>कवेर्वंशादिकीर्तनं । अस्यामन्यकवीनां च वृत्तं गद्यं<BR>क्वचित् क्वचित् । कथांशानां व्यवच्छेद आश्वास<BR>इति बध्यते । आर्यावक्त्रापवक्त्राणां छंदसा येन<BR>केनचित् । अन्यापदेशेनाश्वासमुखे<BR>भाव्यर्थसूचनं । S. D. 568. Writers on<BR>Rhetoric usually divide prose<BR>composition into कथा and आख्यायिका and<BR>make a distinction between them<BR>thus they regard Bāṇa's हर्षचरित as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-a" target="_blank">Page0226-a+ 57</a>]<BR>an आख्यायिकां and कादंबरी as a कथा;<BR>according to Daṇḍin, however, (<BR>Kāv. 1. 28) there is no distinction<BR>between the two: तत्कथाख्यायिकेत्येका<BR>जातिः संज्ञाद्वयांकिता ।.<BR>--2 Narration (of<BR>what is known).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0225-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्यायिन्
आख्यायिन् a. One who tells,<BR>informs, or communicates;<BR>रहस्याख्यायीव स्वनसि मृदु कर्णांतिकचरः Ś. 1. 24;<BR>Ms. 7. 223.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आख्येय
आख्येय pot. p. Fit to be<BR>communicated or told; शब्द˚ fit to be<BR>told in words, a verbal message;<BR>Me. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगम्
आगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To come, come<BR>near, approach.<BR>--2 To arrive at,<BR>attain, reach; fall into (a particular<BR>state or condition); आनृण्यमागम् to<BR>become free from debt; so विश्वासं,<BR>ध्यानं &c.<BR>--3 To have recourse to.<BR>--Caus. (-गमयति)<BR>1 To cause to<BR>come or draw near.<BR>--2 To lead<BR>towards, take, convey; आगमितापि विदूरं<BR>Gīt. 12.<BR>--3 To announce the<BR>arrival of; राजानमागमयति =<BR>राजागमनमाचष्टे Sk.<BR>--4 To ascertain,<BR>inform oneself about; प्रज्ञामेवागमयति<BR>यः प्राज्ञेभ्यः स पंडितः Vop.<BR>--5 To<BR>learn, acquire, study; सम्यगागमिता<BR>विद्या प्रबोधविनयाविव R. 10. 71;<BR>तदप्यागमितं मया Mb.; आगमय दंडनीतिं<BR>कुलविद्यां Dk. 155; Mv. 5;<BR>Śi. 9. 79.<BR>--6 (Atm.) To wait for, have<BR>patience; आगमयस्व तावत् = क्षमस्व Sk.;<BR>आगमयते कालं Vop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग|आगः
आग a. Accidental, sudden; ˚त्वं<BR>accident, chance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगत|आगतं
आगत p. p.<BR>1 Come, arrived.<BR>--2<BR>Occurred, happened.<BR>--3 Obtained,<BR>got; न्यायागतधनं Y. 3. 205; ˚साध्वस<BR>afraid; ˚क्षोभ perplexed; अन्वय˚<BR>hereditary; ˚मन्यु angry; ˚विस्मय<BR>surprised.<BR>--4 Reduced to, fallen<BR>into (a particular state); दासत्वं, पंचत्वं,<BR>संदेहं, विस्मयं &c.<BR>--5 Living or<BR>residing in.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Coming, arrival.<BR>--2<BR>Occurrence, event.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगतिः|आगति
आगतिः f.<BR>1 Arrival, coming;<BR>लोकस्यास्य गतागतिं Rām.; इति<BR>निश्चितप्रियतमागतयः Śi. 9. 43.<BR>--2 Obtaining,<BR>acquisition; Y. 3. 170.<BR>--3 Return.<BR>--4 Origin.<BR>--5 Accident, chance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगंतव्य|आगन्तव्य
आगंतव्य pot. p. Likely to come,<BR>to be arrived; coming necessarily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगंतु|आगन्तु|आगन्तुः
आगंतु a. [आ-गम्-तुन्]<BR>1<BR>Coming, arriving.<BR>--2 Stray.<BR>--3 Coming<BR>from the outside; external (as a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-b" target="_blank">Page0226-b+ 57</a>]<BR>cause &c.).<BR>--4 Adventitious,<BR>accidental, casual; नियमस्तु स यत्कर्म<BR>नित्यमागंतुसाधनं Ak.<BR>--तुः A new-comer,<BR>stranger, guest; R. 5. 62; H. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. arising accidentally<BR>or casually; आगंतुजे रोगे Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगंतुक|आगन्तुक|आगन्तुकं
आगंतुक a. (का, की f.)<BR>1<BR>Coming of one's own accord, arriving<BR>uninvited; आगंतुका वयं Dhūrtas.<BR>--2<BR>Stray (as an animal); Y. 2. 163.<BR>--3 Incidental, accidental;<BR>adventitious; इत्यागंतुका विकाराः Āśval.<BR>--4<BR>Interpolated, spurious (as a<BR>reading), having crept in without<BR>authority; अत्र<BR>गंधवद्गंधमादनमित्यागंतुकः पाठः Malli. on Ku. 6. 46.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An intruder, interloper.<BR>--2<BR>A stranger, guest, new-comer;<BR>Ś. 4, {6}<BR>--3 Interpolated reading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमः|आगम|आगमं
आगमः<BR>1 Coming, arrival, approach,<BR>appearance; लतायां पूर्वलूनायां<BR>प्रसूनस्यागमः कुतः U. 5. 20; Śi. 1. 30;<BR>अव्यक्ताद् व्यक्तयः सर्वाः प्रभवंत्यहरागमे ।<BR>रात्र्यागमे प्रलीयंते Bg. 8. 18; R. 14. 80;<BR>Pt. 3. 48; Ms. 8. 401; so व्यसन˚,<BR>अंधकार˚ &c.<BR>--2 Acquisition; एषोऽस्या<BR>मुद्राया आगमः Mu. 1; Ś. 6 this<BR>is how I came by this ring;<BR>Dk. 139; वेदानामागमः K. 18;<BR>विद्यागमनिमित्तं V. 5.<BR>--3 Birth, origin,<BR>source; आगमापायिनोऽ<BR>नित्यास्तांस्तितिक्षस्व भारत Bg. 2. 14 coming and going,<BR>of short birth or duration, transient;<BR>आगमः काव्यामृतरसानां K. 5.<BR>--4<BR>Addition, accumulation, acquisition<BR>(of wealth); अर्थ˚, धन˚ &c.<BR>--5 Flow,<BR>course, current (of water);<BR>Ms. 8. 252, 9. 281; रक्त˚, फेण˚.<BR>--6 A<BR>voucher or written testimony; see<BR>अनागम.<BR>--7 Knowledge;<BR>शिष्यप्रदेयागमाः Bh. 2. 15; प्रज्ञया सदृशागमः<BR>आगमैः सदृशारंभः R. 1. 15; यस्यागमः<BR>केवलजीविकायै M. 1. 17; Y. 2. 212,<BR>92.<BR>--8 Supply of money, income,<BR>revenue.<BR>--9 Lawful acquisition of<BR>anything; आगमोपे बलं नैव भुक्तिः<BR>स्तोकापि यत्र नो Y. 2. 27, 28.<BR>--10<BR>Increase of property.<BR>--11 A traditional<BR>doctrine or precept, a sacred writing<BR>or scripture, Śāstra; अनुमानेन न चागमः<BR>क्षतः Ki. 2. 28, 5. 18; परिशुद्ध आगमः<BR>2. 33; K. 55, 337.<BR>--12 The study<BR>of Śāstras, sacred knowledge or<BR>learning.<BR>--13 Science, a system of<BR>philosophy; सांख्यागमेनेव<BR>प्रधानपुरुषोपेतेन K. 51; बहुधाप्यागमैर्भिन्नाः<BR>पंथानः सिद्धिहेतवः R. 10. 26.<BR>--14 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">Page0226-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Vedas, the sacred scripture;<BR>न्यायनिर्णीतसारत्वान्निरपेक्षमिवागमे<BR>Ki. 11. 39.<BR>--15 The last of the<BR>four kinds of proof, recognized<BR>by the Naiyāyikas (also called शब्द<BR>or आप्तवाक्य, the Vedas being so<BR>regarded).<BR>--16 An affix or suffix.<BR>--17<BR>The addition or insertion of a letter;<BR>भवेद्वर्णागमाद्धंसः Sk.<BR>--18 An<BR>augment; इडागमः.<BR>--19 Theory (opp.<BR>प्रयोग); चतुःषष्टिकलागमप्रयोगचतुरः<BR>Dk. 120.<BR>--20<BR>--(मः, --मं) A work<BR>inculcating the mystical worship of<BR>शिव and शक्ति, a Tantra; आगतं<BR>पंचवक्त्रात्तु गतं च गिरिजानने । मतं च<BR>वासुदेवस्य तस्मादागममुच्यते ॥ Śabdak.<BR>--21<BR>The mouth of a river.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवर्ता N. of the plant Targia<BR>Involucrata Lin. (वृश्चिकाली).<BR>--निरपेक्ष<BR>a. independent of a voucher.<BR>--नीत<BR>a. studied, read, examined.<BR>--रहित<BR>a. {1} without a voucher. {2} devoid<BR>of Śāstras.<BR>--वृद्ध a. advanced in<BR>knowledge, a very learned man; प्रतीप<BR>इत्यागमवृद्धसेवी R. 6. 41.<BR>--वेदिन्<BR>a. {1} knowing the Vedas. {2} learned<BR>in Śāstras. (--m.) an epithet of<BR>Śankarāchārya's preceptor Gauḍapāda.<BR>--साक्षेप a. supposed by a voucher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमवत्|आगमवन्त्
आगमवत् a.<BR>1 Having an augment<BR>or addition.<BR>--2 Having approached<BR>for sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमनं|आगमन
आगमनं<BR>1 Coming, approaching,<BR>arrival; R. 12. 24.<BR>--2 Return,<BR>returning.<BR>--3 Acquisition, getting<BR>into; एतत्ते सर्वमाख्यातं वैरस्यागमनं<BR>महत् Rām.<BR>--4 Arising, birth.<BR>--5<BR>Approaching a woman for sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमिन्
आगमिन्, आगामिन् a. [आ-गम् णिनि वा<BR>थस्वः]<BR>1 Coming, future;<BR>कथयत्यागामिनमर्थं K. 46.<BR>--2 Impending,<BR>arriving.<BR>--3 Learned, versed in theory;<BR>द्वावप्यागमिनौ M. 3.<BR>--4 An intruder.<BR>--5 Having an augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामिन्
आगमिन्, आगामिन् a. [आ-गम् णिनि वा<BR>थस्वः]<BR>1 Coming, future;<BR>कथयत्यागामिनमर्थं K. 46.<BR>--2 Impending,<BR>arriving.<BR>--3 Learned, versed in theory;<BR>द्वावप्यागमिनौ M. 3.<BR>--4 An intruder.<BR>--5 Having an augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगमिष्ठ
आगमिष्ठ a. Coming very quickly,<BR>or gladly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामिक
आगामिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Relating<BR>to the future time; मतिरागामिका<BR>ज्ञेया बुद्धिस्तत्कालदर्शिनी Haima.<BR>--2<BR>Impending, arriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगामुक
आगामुक a. [आ-गम्-उकञ्<BR>P. III. 2. 154]<BR>1 Coming, arriving.<BR>--2 Future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगरः|आगर
आगरः [आगॄ-अप्] The day of<BR>new moon (अमावास्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगलित
आगलित a. Drooping, languid,<BR>dejected, sad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0226-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगवीन
आगवीन a. [गोः प्रत्यर्पणपर्यंतं यः<BR>कर्म करोति स आगवीनः P. V. 2. 14 Sk.<BR>आगो-ख] One who is engaged in<BR>business till the return of the cows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्
आगस् n. [इ-असुन्-आगादेशः<BR>Uṇ. 4. 211]<BR>1 Fault, offence,<BR>transgression; सहिष्ये शतमागांसि<BR>सूनोस्त इति यत्त्वया Śi. 2. 108, 1. 61;<BR>द्वौ रिपू मम मतौ समागसौ R. 11. 74;<BR>कृतागाः Mu. 3. 11; N. 3. 52;<BR>Amaru. 41, 43.<BR>--2 Sin.<BR>--3 Punishment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत् a. committing an<BR>offence, offender, criminal;<BR>अभ्यर्णमागस्कृतमरपृशद्भिः R. 2. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्ती
आगस्ती [अगस्त्यस्य इयं, अण्, यलोपः]<BR>The south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्तीय
आगस्तीय a. [अगस्तये हितः यलोपः]<BR>Relating to or for the advantage of<BR>अगस्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्त्य|आगस्त्यः
आगस्त्य a. [अगस्त्यस्येदम् यञ् यलोपः]<BR>1 Southern (दिग्भाग).<BR>--2 Pertaining<BR>to Agastya; ˚आख्यानं सरः Mb.<BR>--3<BR>Originating from the plant Agasti<BR>Grandiflorum.<BR>--स्त्यः, स्त्यी<BR>1 The<BR>descendants of Agasti.<BR>--2 Persons<BR>of their race (गोत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगस्त्यायन
आगस्त्यायन a. Connected with<BR>Agasti; U. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगाध|आगाधं
आगाध a. [अगाध एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>1<BR>Very deep or unfathomable (fig.<BR>also).<BR>--2 Difficult to obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगारं|आगार
आगारं [आगमृच्छति ऋ-अण्] A<BR>house, dwelling; room, covered place.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गोधिका a small lizard.<BR>--दाहः setting a house on fire.<BR>--दाहिन् a. an incendiary.<BR>--धूमः {1} smoke<BR>coming out from a house. {2} N. of<BR>a plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुर्
आगुर् {c6c} A. To approve, agree or<BR>assent to, promise to pronounce the<BR>आगुर्, see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुर्
आगुर् f. [आ-गुर्-क्विप्]<BR>1 Assent,<BR>agreement, promise.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>class of plauditory exclamations or<BR>formularies used by the priests in<BR>sacrificial rites; ये ३ यजामह इत्यागूः<BR>Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुरणं|आगुरण
आगु(गू)रणं<BR>1 Recitation of the<BR>Āgur.<BR>--2 A secret suggestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूरणं|आगूरण
आगु(गू)रणं<BR>1 Recitation of the<BR>Āgur.<BR>--2 A secret suggestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्ण|आगूर्ण्ण
आगूर्ण --र्त p. p. Repeated(as an<BR>exclamation &c.).<BR>--र्णं --र्तं Exertion,<BR>resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्त|आगूर्त्त
आगूर्ण --र्त p. p. Repeated(as an<BR>exclamation &c.).<BR>--र्णं --र्तं Exertion,<BR>resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूर्तिन्|आगूर्त्तिन्
आगूर्तिन् a. [आगूर्त-इनि]<BR>1<BR>Performing or pronouncing the Āgur;<BR>आगूतीं वा एष भवति यो दर्शपौर्णमासाभ्यां यजते<BR>Śat. Br.<BR>--2 Resolute, industrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगुरव
आगुरव a. (वी f.) Belonging to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">Page0227-b+ 55</a>]<BR>agallochum (अगुरु); Śi. 4. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगूः
आगूः (f.) An agreement,<BR>promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगै
आगै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sing to.<BR>--2 To<BR>obtain by singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगातृ
आगातृ a. Obtaining by singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आगानं|आगान
आगानं Obtaining by singing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नापौष्ण
आग्नापौष्ण a. [अग्नापूषणौ देवते<BR>अस्यअण्] Belonging or referring to Agni<BR>and Pūṣan (as an oblation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नावैष्णव
आग्नावैष्णव a.<BR>1 Referring to<BR>Agni and Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 Containing<BR>the word अग्नाविष्णू (as a chapter<BR>अध्याय, or अनुवाक section).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निक
आग्निक a. (की f.) [अग्नेरिदं बा˚<BR>ठक्] Belonging to fire, belonging to<BR>the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निपद
आग्निपद a. [अग्निपदे दीयते कार्यं वा<BR>व्युष्टा˚ अण्] To be done at or given<BR>to the fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निमारुत
आग्निमारुत a. [अग्नामरुतौ देवते अस्य<BR>अण्] Belonging to Agni and Marut<BR>(offerings &c.); so आग्निवारुण<BR>belonging to Agni and Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्निष्टोमिक
आग्निष्टोमिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अग्निष्टोमठक्]<BR>1 Belonging to the अग्निष्टोम; ˚कं<BR>भक्तं, ˚की दक्षिणा.<BR>--2 One who<BR>recites or is conversant with अग्निष्टोम<BR>(अग्निष्टोममधीते वेद वा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र|आग्नीध्रं|आग्नीध्रः
आग्नीध्र a. Belonging to the अग्नीध्र<BR>(the priest who kindles the<BR>fire).<BR>--ध्रं [आग्निमिंधे अग्नीत् तस्य शरणं, रण्<BR>भत्वान्न जश् Tv.]<BR>1 The place where the<BR>sacrificial or sacred fire is kindled.<BR>--2 The duty of the priest who<BR>kindles the sacred fire.<BR>--ध्रा Care<BR>of the sacred fire.<BR>--ध्रः The priest<BR>who kindles the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्रीय|आग्नीध्रीयः
आग्नीध्रीय a. Being within the<BR>आग्नीध्र.<BR>--यः<BR>1 The fire within the<BR>आग्नीध्र.<BR>--2 The fireplace within the<BR>आग्नीध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नीध्र्य
आग्नीध्र्य a. Belonging to the priest<BR>who kindles the sacred fire.<BR>--ध्र्या<BR>The place for the fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेंद्र|आग्नेन्द्र
आग्नेंद्र a. [अग्निश्च इंद्रश्च-अण्<BR>P. VI. 3. 28, VII. 3. 22] Belonging to<BR>Agni and Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्नेय|आग्नेयं|आग्नेयः
आग्नेय a. (यी f.) [अग्नेरिदं अग्निर्देवता<BR>वास्य ढक्]<BR>1 Belonging to Agni; fiery.<BR>--2 Offered or consecrated to Agni;<BR>Y. 3. 287.<BR>--3 Similar to fire (as an<BR>insect).<BR>--4 Increasing the fire in<BR>the stomach; stimulating digestion.<BR>--5 Kindling the fire (as ghee &c.).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-c" target="_blank">Page0227-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--6 Belonging to Agnāyī.<BR>--यः<BR>1 An<BR>epithet of Skanda or Kārtikeya.<BR>--2 N. of Agastya.<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>country.<BR>--4 A worshipper of Agni.<BR>--5<BR>An offering or oblation to Svāhā.<BR>--यी<BR>1 N. of the wife of Agni.<BR>--2 The south-east quarter<BR>(presided over by Agni).<BR>--3 The<BR>first day of a month (प्रतिपत्तिथि which<BR>is presided over by Agni).<BR>--यं<BR>1<BR>The lunar mansion called Kṛttikā.<BR>--2 Gold.<BR>--3 Blood.<BR>--4 Lac, the<BR>red animal dye.<BR>--5 Ghee.<BR>--6 A<BR>missile presided over by Agni.<BR>--7<BR>A Mantra used in the worship of<BR>Agni.<BR>--8 A descendant of Agni.<BR>--9<BR>Bathing by applying sacred ashes<BR>to the body (भस्ममर्दनपूर्वकस्नानं).<BR>--10<BR>A kind of worm.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीटः<BR>a kind of insect which flies into<BR>the fire.<BR>--पुराणं = अग्निपुराण q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्न्याधानिकी
आग्न्याधानिकी [अग्न्याधानस्य<BR>यज्ञस्य दक्षिणा ठञ्] The Dakṣiṇā or<BR>a gift of money given to Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रभोजनिकः|आग्रभोजनिक
आग्रभोजनिकः [अग्रभोजनं नियतं<BR>दीयते अस्मै ठञ् P. IV. 4. 66] A<BR>Brāhmaṇa always entitled to occupy<BR>the foremost seat at a dinner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रयणः|आग्रयण|आग्रयणं
आग्रयणः [अग्रे अयनं भोजनं<BR>शस्यादेर्येन कर्मणा पृ˚ ह्रस्वदीर्घः व्यत्ययः]<BR>1 The<BR>first Soma libation at the<BR>Agniṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR>--2 A form of Agni.<BR>--3 The time of the sacrifice.<BR>--णी<BR> An oblation consisting of<BR>firstfruits; see आग्रयणं.<BR>--णं An<BR>oblation consisting of first-fruits at the<BR>end of the rainy season (आश्विनीपूर्णिमा);<BR>आग्रयणं त्रिविधं श्यामाक˚, व्रीहि˚, यव˚,<BR>यथापूर्वं वर्षासु शरदि वसंते च तत्करणोपदेशात्<BR>Ārya. S.; आग्रयणेनेष्ट्वा नवान्नं प्राश्नीयात्<BR>Ait. Br.; आग्रयणं व्रीहिश्यामाकयवानां<BR>Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रह्
आग्रह् {c9c} U.<BR>1 To seize, take hold<BR>of, catch.<BR>--2 To draw tight (as<BR>the reins) Ś. 1 v. l.<BR>--3 To persist in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहः|आग्रह
आग्रहः<BR>1 Seizing, taking.<BR>--2<BR>Attack.<BR>--3 Determination, strong<BR>attachment, persistence, insisting<BR>(स्नेह, अभिनिवेश); चलेपि काकस्य<BR>पदार्पणाग्रहः Naiṣadha.; Dk. 176; also<BR>Malli. on Ku. 5. 7.<BR>--4 Favour,<BR>patronage.<BR>--5 Surpassing, surmount<BR>ing.<BR>--6 Moral power, courage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहिका
आग्रहिका Favour, patronage, help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणः|आग्रहायण
आग्रहायणः [= अग्रहायण-अण्] N. of<BR>the month of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR>--णी<BR>1 The<BR>full moon day of मार्गशीर्ष; कार्तिक्या<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">Page0228-a+ 56</a>]<BR>आग्रहायणी मासे Sk.<BR>--2 A particular<BR>kind of Pāka-yajna.<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>constellation called मृगशिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0227-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणक|आग्रहायणकः
आग्रहायण(णि)क a. [आग्रहायण्यां<BR>देयमृणं वुञ् ठञ् वा P. IV. 3. 50] To<BR>be paid on the full moon day in<BR>मार्गशीर्ष (as debt.).<BR>--कः (--णिकः)<BR>[आग्रहायणी पौर्णिमास्यस्मिन् मासे ठक्<BR>P. IV. 2. 22] The month of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहायणिक|आग्रहायणिकः
आग्रहायण(णि)क a. [आग्रहायण्यां<BR>देयमृणं वुञ् ठञ् वा P. IV. 3. 50] To<BR>be paid on the full moon day in<BR>मार्गशीर्ष (as debt.).<BR>--कः (--णिकः)<BR>[आग्रहायणी पौर्णिमास्यस्मिन् मासे ठक्<BR>P. IV. 2. 22] The month of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आग्रहारिक
आग्रहारिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अग्रहारठञ्; see आग्रभोजनिक] One who<BR>appropriates to himself an अग्रहार<BR>(endowments of land conferred upon<BR>Brāhmaṇas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्ट्
आघट्ट् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To strike against,<BR>touch; आघट्टयामास गतागताभ्यां<BR>Ki. 17. 38.<BR>--2 To move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टक|आघट्टकः
आघट्टक a. Moving.<BR>--कः The red<BR>Apāmārga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघट्टना
आघट्टना<BR>1 Moving, shaking,<BR>striking against; रणद्भिराघट्टनया नभस्वतः<BR>Śi. 1. 10.<BR>--2 Friction, contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षः|आघर्ष
आघर्षः, --र्षणं Rubbing, friction,<BR>striking against;<BR>गंडस्थलाघर्षगलन्मदोदकद्रवद्रुमस्कंघनिलायिनोऽलयः<BR>Śi. 12. 64.<BR>--णी A brush, rubber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघर्षणं|आघर्षण
आघर्षः, --र्षणं Rubbing, friction,<BR>striking against;<BR>गंडस्थलाघर्षगलन्मदोदकद्रवद्रुमस्कंघनिलायिनोऽलयः<BR>Śi. 12. 64.<BR>--णी A brush, rubber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघाटः|आघाट
आघाटः [आ-हन् घञ् निपातः]<BR>1<BR>Killing, striking (sometimes used<BR>as an adj.).<BR>--2 A musical instrument.<BR>--3 A cymbal or rattle.<BR>--4 Boundary,<BR>limit.<BR>--5 N. of a plant (अपामार्ग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघाटिः|आघाटि
आघाटिः m. f. Musical<BR>instruments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघातः|आघात
आघातः See under आहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघुष्
आघुष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To proclaim, cry<BR>aloud, declare.<BR>--2 To praise.<BR>--3 To<BR>listen.<BR>--4 To make oneself audible.<BR>--{c10c} P. or Caus.<BR>1 To make a noise,<BR>to cause to sound.<BR>--2 To proclaim,<BR>announce publicly.<BR>--3 To complain<BR>continually, weep bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषः|आघोष
आघोषः Calling out, invocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषणं|आघोषण
आघोषणं --णा A proclamation,<BR>public announcement; एवमाघोषणायां<BR>कृतायां Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघोषणा
आघोषणं --णा A proclamation,<BR>public announcement; एवमाघोषणायां<BR>कृतायां Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्ण्
आघूर्ण् {c1c} A., {c6c} P.<BR>1 To roll,<BR>stagger, whirl, toss about;<BR>आघूर्णतीवानिलैः (अंबरं) Mk. 5. 27;<BR>पवनाघूर्णितपादप Hariv., Bk. 14. 77.<BR>--2 To swim,<BR>roll (as eyes); Ku. 3. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघूर्णनं|आघूर्णन
आघूर्णनं Rolling, tossing about,<BR>whirling round, swimming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघृ
आघृ {c10c} P. or Caus. To pour<BR>down upon, sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघारः|आघार
आघारः<BR>1 Sprinkling(in general).<BR>--2 Especially, sprinkling clarified<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">Page0228-b+ 56</a>]<BR>butter upon the fire at certain<BR>sacrifices.<BR>--3 Ghee, clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघृणि|आघृणिः
आघृणि a. [आगतो घृणिर्दीप्तिरस्य]<BR>Glowing with heat or endowed with<BR>splendour, having splendid wealth.<BR>--णिः The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रा
आघ्रा {c1c} P.<BR>1 To smell, smell at;<BR>गंधमाघ्राय Me. 21.<BR>--2 To kiss, touch<BR>(with the nose) as the head;<BR>Bk. 14. 12.<BR>--3 (Fig.) To attack,<BR>devour, seize upon; मामाघ्रातुमागतवान्<BR>Dk. 6; कामाघ्रातया अनया 116<BR>smitten, affected; Māl. 5. 29;<BR>Bh. 3. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्राण|आघ्राणं
आघ्राण a.<BR>1 Smelt(as flowers).<BR>--2<BR>Satisfied.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Smelling.<BR>--2<BR>Satisfaction, satiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघ्रात|आघ्रातः
आघ्रात p. p.<BR>1 Smelt, scented,<BR>touched.<BR>--2 Satisfied.<BR>--3<BR>Surmounted, surpassed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंक्षी|आङ्क्षी
आंक्षी A musical instrument, a<BR>tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंकुशिकः|आङ्कुशिक|आङ्कुशिकः
आंकुशिकः [अंकश-ठक्] One who<BR>strikes with the goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंग|आङ्ग|आङ्गं|आङ्गः
आंग a. (गी f.) [अंग-स्वार्थे-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Bodily, corporeal.<BR>--2 (In gram.)<BR>Relating to the base (अंग).<BR>--3<BR>Having limbs or parts.<BR>--4 Relating<BR>to the minor personages in a drama.<BR>--5 Belonging to a portion of the<BR>Vedas.<BR>--6 Produced or born in the<BR>country of the Aṅgas.<BR>--गः A prince<BR>of the Aṅga country.<BR>--गं A<BR>delicate body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंगक|आङ्गक|आङ्गकः
आंगक a. (की f.) [अंगेषु जनपदेषु भवः<BR>वुञ्] Produced in the अंग country;<BR>ruler of that country.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An<BR>inhabitant of the Aṅga country.<BR>--2 A ruler of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंगविद्य|आङ्गविद्य
आंगविद्य a. [अंगविद्यां वेद अण्]<BR>Occurring in, or being familiar with,<BR>अंगविद्या (chiromancy or the<BR>knowledge of lucky and unlucky marks on<BR>the body).<BR>--द्या A work on अंगविद्या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंगिक|आङ्गिक|आङ्गिकः
आंगिक a. (की f.) [अंगनिर्वृत्तार्थे-ठक्]<BR>1 Bodily, corporeal.<BR>--2<BR>Gesticulated, expressed by bodily actions;<BR>आंगिकोऽभिनयः, see अभिनय.<BR>--कः A<BR>player on a tabor or drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंगारं|आङ्गार|आंगार|आङ्गारं
आंगारं [अंगाराणां समूहः अण्] A<BR>multitude of fire-brands, charcoal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंगिरस|आङ्गिरस|आङ्गिरसः
आंगिरस a. (सी f.)<BR>Descended from or referring to Aṅgiras.<BR>--सः<BR>1 N. of Bṛhaspati, son of Aṅgiras;<BR>Ms. 2. 151.<BR>--2 Descendants of<BR>Angiras (pl.).<BR>--3 A particular Sūkta<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">Page0228-c+ 57</a>]<BR>or hymn in the Atharvaveda.<BR>--4<BR>The soul.<BR>--5 A Kṣatriya by will<BR>of Brahmā and by profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंगूषः|आङ्गूष|आङ्गूषः
आंगूषः [अंगूष-स्वार्थे-अण्] Praise,<BR>hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्ष्
आचक्ष् {c2c} A.<BR>1 To speak,<BR>announce, declare, teach, tell, relate,<BR>communicate, say, narrate (usually<BR>with dat. of person); गुरवे…<BR>प्रस्तुतमाचचक्षे R. 5. 19, 12. 55, 14. 36;<BR>Ms. 4. 59, 81; M. 5; इत्याख्यानविद<BR>आचक्षते Māl. 2; sometimes with<BR>acc.; तत्त्वां किमाचक्ष्महे Bv. 1. 63 say<BR>to or address.<BR>--2 To name, call, say;<BR>शर्व इति प्राच्या आचक्षते Śat. Br.<BR>--3<BR>To divine, bespeak; यथा मे<BR>हृदयमाचष्टे M. 4.<BR>--4 To make known,<BR>acquaint, introduce to.<BR>--5 To<BR>look at, inspect (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचक्षुस्
आचक्षुस् m. [Uṇ. 2. 120] A learned<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचतुरं|आचतुर
आचतुरं ind. [चतुः पर्यंतं अच् समा˚]<BR>Till the fourth generation; आचतुरं<BR>हीमे पशवो द्वंद्वं मिथुनायंते<BR>P. VIII. 1. 15 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचम्
आचम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sip, lick, lap<BR>drink (a small quantity); नाचेमे<BR>हिममपि वारि वारणेन Ki. 7. 34;<BR>पर्याप्तमाचामति U. 4. 1; Bv. 4. 38;<BR>Ms. 2. 60, 5. 139.<BR>--2 To rinse the mouth<BR>(with instr. of the thing);<BR>Ms. 2. 61.<BR>--3 To lick up, dry or drink up,<BR>absorb; आचामति स्वेदलवान् मुखे ते<BR>R. 13. 20. --Caus. To cause to sip<BR>water; Ms. 3. 251, 5. 142.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमः|आचम
आचमः Rinsing the mouth,<BR>sipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनं|आचमन
आचमनं<BR>1 Rinsing the mouth,<BR>sipping water before religious<BR>ceremonies, before and after meals &c.<BR>from the palm of the hand;<BR>दद्यादाचमनं ततः Y. 1. 242, 195 (part of<BR>the water sipped being usually<BR>allowed to drop down).<BR>--2 The<BR>water used for rinsing the mouth.<BR>--3 Gargling the throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनकं|आचमनक|आचमनकः
आचमनकं [स्वार्थे आधारे वा कन्]<BR>1<BR>The water used for sipping.<BR>--2<BR>A spitting pot (Mar. पिकदाणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचमनीय|आचमनीयं
आचमनीय pot. p. Used for rinsing<BR>the mouth.<BR>--यं Water used for<BR>rinsing the mouth; a gargle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचांत|आचान्त|आचान्तः
आचांत p. p.<BR>1 Sipped and ejected<BR>as water.<BR>--2 (Actively used) One who<BR>has rinsed his mouth or sipped<BR>water.<BR>--3 Fit for sipping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचामः|आचाम
आचामः [चम् भावे-घञ्]<BR>1 Sipping<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">Page0229-a+ 57</a>]<BR>water, rinsing the mouth.<BR>--2 The<BR>water or foam of boiled water (Mar.<BR>पेज); Y. 3. 322.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0228-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचामक
आचामक a. Rinsing the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचामनकं|आचामनक
आचामनकं A spitting pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचाम्य
आचाम्य pot. p. To be rinsed.<BR>--म्यं Water used for rinsing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचयः|आचय
आचयः<BR>1 Collecting, gathering.<BR>--2 A collection, heap, plenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचयक
आचयक a. Skilful in collecting or<BR>gathering (आचये कुशलः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचर्
आचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To act, practise,<BR>do, perform, undertake, exercise;<BR>तपस्विकन्यास्वविनयभाचरति Ś. 1. 25<BR>practises rudeness; स्थितिं R. 1. 89,<BR>12. 22; त्वं च तस्येष्टमाचरेः V. 5. 20, 1. 17;<BR>नाचंरेत्किंचिदप्रियं Ms. 5. 156;<BR>Y. 3. 65; न चाप्याचरितः पूर्वैरयं धर्मः Mb.;<BR>so सेवां, विधिं, स्नानं, वृत्तिं.<BR>--2 To act or<BR>behave towards (with loc.); तस्यां<BR>त्वं साधु नाचरः R. 1. 76;<BR>विष्णाविवाचरति शिवे Vop.<BR>--3 To act, proceed,<BR>manage (without loc.); जडवल्लोक<BR>आचरेत् Ms. 2. 110.<BR>--4 To treat;<BR>पुत्रं मित्रवदाचरेत् Chāṇ. 11; पुत्रमिवाचरति<BR>शिष्यं Sk.; Ms. 8. 102.<BR>--5 To observe<BR>the usual formality; Ś. 7.<BR>--6 To come<BR>near, approach (Ved.); आ वां चरंतु<BR>वृष्टयः Rv. 8. 25. 6.<BR>--7 To step upon,<BR>pass through, wander over or about;<BR>frequent, resort to, follow;<BR>तस्कराचरितो मार्गः Rām.; श्वापदाचरिते बने Mb.;<BR>अगस्त्याचरितामाशां R. 4. 44;<BR>परेताचरितां दिशं Rām.; अविद्वज्जनाचरित एष<BR>मार्गः K. 173.<BR>--8 To have<BR>intercourse with; Ms. 11. 181, 190.<BR>--9<BR>To devour, eat into, corrode.<BR>--10 To<BR>help forward, put into; हस्तेनाचरति<BR>Kāty. (हस्तेन प्रेरयति प्रक्षिपति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरणं|आचरण
आचरणं<BR>1 Practising, doing,<BR>performing, following, observing; धर्म˚,<BR>मंगल˚ &c.<BR>--2 Conduct, behaviour;<BR>अधीतिबोधाचरणप्रचारणैः N. 1. 4<BR>example (opp. precept); अधर्म˚, दुर्˚<BR>&c.<BR>--3 Usage, practice.<BR>--4 An<BR>institute; rite or rule of conduct.<BR>--5<BR>Approaching, arrival.<BR>--6 A chariot,<BR>carriage, cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरणीय
आचरणीय, आचरितव्य, आचर्य<BR>pot. p. To be done, performed, followed,<BR>observed &c.; fit, right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरितव्य
आचरणीय, आचरितव्य, आचर्य<BR>pot. p. To be done, performed, followed,<BR>observed &c.; fit, right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचर्य|आचर्य्य
आचरणीय, आचरितव्य, आचर्य<BR>pot. p. To be done, performed, followed,<BR>observed &c.; fit, right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरित|आचरितं
आचरित p. p.<BR>1 Done, observed,<BR>practised, as a rite or usage &c.<BR>--2<BR>Usual, customary.<BR>--3 Enjoined,<BR>fixed by rule.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Conduct,<BR>behaviour.<BR>--2 One of the five means of<BR>recovering or paying back debt;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-b" target="_blank">Page0229-b+ 58</a>]<BR>Ms. 8. 49; see also Bṛhaspati quoted by<BR>Kull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारः|आचार
आचारः [आचर्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Conduct, behaviour, manner of action or<BR>of conducting oneself; सदाचारः good<BR>conduct; नीच˚ &c.; लोकाचारविवर्जिताः<BR>Pt. 5. 40 ignorant of the ways of<BR>the world.<BR>--2 Good conduct or<BR>behaviour; Bg. 16. 7; Ms. 1. 109,<BR>5. 4, 3. 165.<BR>--3 A custom, usage,<BR>practice; तस्मिन्देशे य आचारः<BR>पारंपर्यक्रमागतः Ms. 2. 18; Y. 1. 342.<BR>--4 An<BR>established usage, fixed rule of<BR>conduct in life, customary law,<BR>institute or precept (opp. व्यवहार in law);<BR>आचार्य आचाराणां K. 56; Ms. 1. 109;<BR>oft. as the first member of comp.<BR>in the sense of ‘customary’, ‘usual’,<BR>‘as is the custom’, ‘according to<BR>form’, ‘as a formality’; ˚पुष्पग्रहणार्थं<BR>M. 4; see ˚धूम, ˚लाज below;<BR>˚परिकर्मन् Ś. 2.<BR>--5 (a) Any customary<BR>observance or duty; ˚प्रयतः V. 3. 2;<BR>गृहाचारव्यपदेशेन U. 3. (b) A form,<BR>formality; आचार इत्यवहितेन मया<BR>गृहीता Ś. 5. 3; Mv. 3. 26. (c) The<BR>customary salutation or bow, usual<BR>formality; आचारं प्रतिपद्यस्व Ś. 4;<BR>V. 2; अविषयस्तावदाचारस्य Mv. 2.<BR>--6<BR>Diet.<BR>--7 A rule (of conduct).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं title of the first<BR>twelve sacred books of the Jainas.<BR>--तंत्रं one of the four classes of the<BR>Tantras (with Buddhists).<BR>--दीपः<BR>[आचारार्थः नीराजनार्थो दीपः] {1} ‘a lamp of<BR>religious customs’, title of a work.<BR>{2} a lamp waved about a person as a<BR>formality and token of<BR>auspiciousness.<BR>--धूमग्रहणं inhaling smoke as<BR>a customary rite (as of the<BR>sacrificial ceremony); R. 7. 27; Ku. 7. 82.<BR>--पूत a. purified by customary<BR>observances, of pure conduct;<BR>R. 2. 13.<BR>--भेदः difference in the<BR>customary law.<BR>--भ्रष्ट, --पतित a. apostate,<BR>fallen from established usages or<BR>rules of conduct.<BR>--लाज (m. pl.)<BR>fried grain customarily showered<BR>upon a king or other important<BR>personage as a mark of respect (as<BR>when he passes through the streets<BR>of his capital); R. 2. 10.<BR>--वर्जित,<BR>--हीन a. {1} irregular, out of rule. {2}<BR>outcast, who has renounced all<BR>customary observances.<BR>--वेदी [<BR>आचारस्य वेदीव] ‘altar of religious<BR>customs’, N. of Āryāvarta, the<BR>sacred region of the Āryas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारवत्|आचारवन्त्
आचारवत् a. Well-conducted,<BR>virtuous; Ms. 12. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिक
आचारिक a. [आचार-ठक्]<BR>Conformable to rule or practice,<BR>authorized, prescriptive.<BR>--कं Rules for the<BR>preservation of health; hygiene,<BR>regimen, diet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारिन्
आचारिन् a. [आचर्-णिनि, आचार-इनि<BR>वा] Following established customs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचारी
आचारी N. of a plant(हिलमोचिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यः|आचार्य|आचार्य्य|आचार्य्यः
आचार्यः [आ-चर्-ण्यत्<BR>P. VI. 2. 36]<BR>1 A teacher or preceptor (in<BR>general).<BR>--2 A spiritual guide<BR>or preceptor, holy teacher (one<BR>who invests a boy with the<BR>sacred thread, instructs him in<BR>the Vedas &c.); उपनीय तु यः शिष्यं<BR>वेदमध्यापयेत् द्विजः । सकल्पं सरहस्यं च<BR>तमाचार्यं प्रचक्षते Ms. 2. 140, see अध्यापक also.<BR>--3 One who propounds a particular<BR>doctrine.<BR>--4 (When affixed to<BR>proper names) Learned, venerable<BR>(somewhat like the English Dr.).<BR>--5<BR>An adviser or preceptor at a<BR>sacrifice &c.<BR>--6 An epithet of Droṇa.<BR>--र्या A female preceptor, a<BR>spiritual preceptress.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपासनं<BR>waiting upon or serving the<BR>spiritual preceptor.<BR>--करणं acting as a<BR>teacher; P. I. 3. 36.<BR>--देवः one<BR>whose preceptor is his god.<BR>--भोगीन<BR>a. [आचार्यभोगाय हितं ख] to be enjoyed<BR>by, fit for the use of, a preceptor;<BR>delighting the preceptor.<BR>--मिश्र a.<BR>venerable, honourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यक|आचार्य्यक
आचार्यक a. Originating from a<BR>spiritual preceptor; P. IV. 2. 104<BR>Vārt.<BR>--कं<BR>1 Instruction, tuition,<BR>teaching (lessons &c.); लंकास्त्रीणां<BR>पुनश्चक्रे विलापाचार्यकं शरैः R. 12. 78;<BR>आचार्यकं विजयि मान्मथमाविरासीत्<BR>Māl. 1. 26; Bv. 4. 37.<BR>--2 The proficiency<BR>of a spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यता
आचार्यता, --त्वं The office or<BR>proficiency of a holy teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यत्वं|आचार्यत्व|आचार्य्यत्व
आचार्यता, --त्वं The office or<BR>proficiency of a holy teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचार्यानी
आचार्यानी [आचार्य-स्त्रियां आनुक्<BR>P. VI. 1. 49 Vārt.] The wife of an<BR>आचार्य or holy preceptor;<BR>शत्रुमूलमनुत्खाय न पुनर्द्रष्टुमुत्सहे । त्र्यंबकं<BR>देवमाचार्यमाचार्यानीं च पार्वतीं Mv. 3. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचीर्ण
आचीर्ण p. p. Devoured or eaten<BR>into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचरण्यति
आचरण्यति Den. P. To move<BR>oneself, to move or extend towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचि
आचि {c5c} U.<BR>1 To accumulate,<BR>heap up, collect.<BR>--2 To load with,<BR>fill or cover with, cover over<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">Page0230-a+ 57</a>]<BR>spread; शैलैरिवाचिनोद्भूमिं Bk. 17. 69,<BR>14. 46, 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0229-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचित|आचितं|आचितः
आचित p. p.<BR>1 Filled, loaded<BR>with, covered with; कचाचितौ<BR>विष्वगिवागजौ गजौ Ki. 1. 36; कुसुमाचिता<BR>वनराजी, आचितनक्षत्रा द्यौः &c.<BR>--2 Tied,<BR>strung, woven; अर्धाचिता<BR>सत्वरमुत्थितायाः R. 7. 10 (v. l. for अर्धांचिता);<BR>Ku. 7. 61; inlaid, set (as with gems).<BR>--3 Collected, accumulated, heaped.<BR>--4 Spread, diffused.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A<BR>cart-load.<BR>--2 (n. also) A measure of 10<BR>Bhāras or cart-loads (80, 000 Tolas);<BR>आचितं दश भाराः स्यात् शाकटो भार आचितः.<BR>--3 A measure equal to 2000 palas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचितिक
आचितिक (की f.), आचितीन a.<BR>[आचित ठञ् ख वा P. V. 1. 53-4]<BR>Holding, or being equal to, or<BR>cooking, a quantity equal to an Acita;<BR>e. g. त्र्याचितक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आचूषणं|आचूषण
आचूषणं<BR>1 Suction, sucking up.<BR>--2 Sucking out.<BR>--3 (In medic.)<BR>Application of cupping-glasses to the<BR>skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छद्|आछद्
आच्छद् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To cover (in<BR>general); नाच्छादयति कौपीनं Pt. 3. 97.<BR>--2 To hide; भानोराच्छादयत्प्रभां Mb.<BR>--3 To clothe, dress, put on clothes;<BR>Ms. 3. 27; अनेन वाससाच्छन्नः Mb.;<BR>वस्त्रं, प्रावारान् &c. आच्छादयति &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छद्|आछद्
आच्छद् f. Ved.<BR>1 A cover, covering.<BR>--2 A sheath; ˚विधानं an<BR>arrangement made for defence, a means for<BR>covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादः|आच्छाद|आछाद
आच्छादः [छद्-घञ्] Cloth, clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादक
आच्छादक a. Covering, concealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादनं|आच्छादन|आछादन
आच्छादनं<BR>1 Covering, concealing,<BR>hiding.<BR>--2 A covering, sheath.<BR>--3<BR>Cloth, clothes; भूषणाच्छादनाशनैः<BR>Y. 1. 82.<BR>--4 A mantle, cloak &c.<BR>--5<BR>Disappearance.<BR>--6 The wooden<BR>frame of a roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छादिन्
आच्छादिन् a. Covering,<BR>concealing; Ś. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छाकः|आच्छाक
आच्छा(च्छु)कः N. of a tree<BR>(= आक्षिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुकः|आच्छुक
आच्छा(च्छु)कः N. of a tree<BR>(= आक्षिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छिद्
आच्छिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To cut off or<BR>away, tear, cut in pieces, break;<BR>आच्छिद्य धमनीमपि Mb.; धनुः, ज्यां &c.<BR>--2 To snatch away, tear from, take<BR>away; जातवेदोमुखान्मायी<BR>मिषतामाच्छिनत्ति नः Ku. 2. 46; Māl. 5. 28, 8. 9;<BR>Dk. 99.<BR>--3 To disregard, take no notice of<BR>(as words); मम वच आच्छिद्य in spite<BR>of, notwithstanding, my words.<BR>--4<BR>To cut off, exclude; भर्तारमाच्छेत्स्यासि<BR>कामिनीभ्यः Mb.<BR>--5 To remove.<BR>--6 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">Page0230-b+ 56</a>]<BR>take out, extract, draw or pull off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छेदः|आच्छेद
आच्छेदः, --दनं<BR>1 Cutting off,<BR>exclusion.<BR>--2 Cutting a little.<BR>--3 Taking<BR>away by force, snatching away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छेदनं|आच्छेदन
आच्छेदः, --दनं<BR>1 Cutting off,<BR>exclusion.<BR>--2 Cutting a little.<BR>--3 Taking<BR>away by force, snatching away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुरित|आच्छुरितं|आछुरित
आच्छुरित a.<BR>1 Mixed, blended<BR>with.<BR>--2 Scratched.<BR>--3 Irritated.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Making a noise with the<BR>fingernails by rubbing them on<BR>one another (नखवाद्यं).<BR>--2 A<BR>horselaugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छुरितकं|आच्छुरितक|आछुरितक
आच्छुरितकं<BR>1 A scratch with a<BR>fingernail.<BR>--2 A horselaugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छोटनं|आच्छोटन
आच्छोटनं Cracking the fingers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आच्छोदनं|आच्छोदन|आछोदन
आच्छोदनं Hunting, chase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजनिः|आजनि
आजनिः f. Ved. A stick for<BR>driving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज|आजं|आजः
आज a. (जी f.) [अजस्येदं-अण्]<BR>Coming from, belonging to, or<BR>produced by, goats.<BR>--जः A vulture.<BR>--जं<BR>1 Ghee or clarified butter.<BR>--2<BR>Throwing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजकं|आजक
आजकं [अजानां समूहः वुञ्] A flock<BR>of goats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजकारः|आजकार
आजकारः Śiva's bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजगर
आजगर a. (री f.) [अजगर-अण्]<BR>Relating to ajagara or the boa; a<BR>chapter in the Mahā-bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजगवं|आजगव
आजगवं<BR>1 The bow of Śiva.<BR>--2<BR>A strong bow like that of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजन्
आजन् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To be born or come<BR>into existence, to be produced or<BR>born from.<BR>--2 To beget, cause to be<BR>born, render prolific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजननं|आजनन
आजननं High birth or origin,<BR>famous or well-known origin. --ind.<BR>From birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजन्म|आजन्मं
आजन्म --न्मं ind. From or ever<BR>since birth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सुरभिपत्रः N.<BR>of a plant (the leaves of which are<BR>fragrant from their first appearance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजन्मं|आजन्म
आजन्म --न्मं ind. From or ever<BR>since birth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सुरभिपत्रः N.<BR>of a plant (the leaves of which are<BR>fragrant from their first appearance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजातिः|आजाति
आजातिः f. Birth, origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजानः|आजान
आजानः [आ-जन्-घञ्]<BR>1 Birth,<BR>origin.<BR>--2 Generating cause (said to be<BR>n. also in these two senses).<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Birth-place.<BR>--2 Birth, descent, species<BR>(Ved.). --ind. From the time of the<BR>creation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. born since<BR>the creation (as gods &c).<BR>--देवः a<BR>god from the very creation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजानिः|आजानि
आजानिः f.<BR>1 One giving birth,<BR>parent, especially a mother (Sāy).<BR>--2<BR>Birth, descent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजानेय|आजानेयः
आजानेय a. (यी f.)<BR>1 Of good<BR>breed (as a horse).<BR>--2 Of noble<BR>birth, fearless, undaunted.<BR>--यः A<BR>well-bred horse; शक्तिभिर्भिन्नहृदयाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">Page0230-c+ 55</a>]<BR>स्खलंतोपि पदे पदे । आजानंति यतः<BR>संज्ञामाजानेयास्ततः स्मृताः ॥ Śabdak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजानेय्य
आजानेय्य a. Ved. Of good breed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजमीढ
आजमीढ a. Belonging to or<BR>produced in the country of अजमीढ<BR>(or अजमीर).<BR>--ढाः (pl.) The kings<BR>of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजवनं|आजवन
आजवनं Rushing upon, fighting,<BR>attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजानु
आजानु ind. Up to the knees;<BR>˚विलंबिबाहुं R. 18. 26, 16. 84<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिः|आजि
आजिः m. f. [अजंत्यस्यां, अज्-इण्<BR>P. III. 3. 108 Vārt.]<BR>1 A battle, fight,<BR>combat; ते तु यावन्त एवाजौ तावांश्च<BR>ददृशे स तैः R. 12. 45.<BR>--2 A fighting or<BR>running match; आजिं धाव् or इ, -अज्<BR>or सृ to run with or against any<BR>one for prize.<BR>--3 Battle-field, place<BR>for running; race-course, level<BR>ground; शस्त्राण्याजौ नयनसलिलं<BR>चापि तुल्यं मुमोच Ve. 3. 9.<BR>--4 Limit,<BR>boundary.<BR>--5 A road, way (m.).<BR>--6<BR>An instant (m.).<BR>--7 Abuse,<BR>invective.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः the goal in a<BR>race-course.<BR>--कृत् a. Ved. {1}<BR>running for a prize. {2} making a<BR>war.<BR>--क्रिया fighting.<BR>--तुर् a.<BR>Ved. victorious in battles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजि|आजिः
आजि {c1c} P. To conquer, win,<BR>acquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजयनं|आजयन
आजयनं<BR>1 Conquering.<BR>--2 A battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिगीषु
आजिगीषु a. Ambitious, wishing<BR>to excel or surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिग्रह
आजिग्रह a. One who takes or<BR>seizes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिज्ञासेन्य
आजिज्ञासेन्य a. Liable to be<BR>investigated.<BR>--न्याः (pl.) N. of a short<BR>section of the Kuntāpa hymns in<BR>the Aitareya Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिरि
आजिरि a. [अजिर-इञ्] Situated<BR>near the court-yard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजिरेय
आजिरेय a. Belonging to or<BR>produced in a court-yard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव्
आजीव् {c1c} P. To live by or<BR>maintain oneself with; to have the use<BR>or enjoyment of; to subsist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवः|आजीव
आजीवः, --वनं<BR>1 Livelihood,<BR>subsistence, maintenance; भवत्याजीवनं<BR>तस्मात् Pt. 1. 48; cf. words like<BR>रूपाजीव, अजाजीव, शस्त्राजीव, स्त्र्याजीव<BR>&c.; आजीवनार्थः Ms. 10. 79 means<BR>of livelihood.<BR>--2 Profession, the<BR>means of maintaining oneself;<BR>विशुद्ध इदानीमाजीवः Ś. 6.<BR>--वः A Jaina<BR>beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवनं|आजीवन
आजीवः, --वनं<BR>1 Livelihood,<BR>subsistence, maintenance; भवत्याजीवनं<BR>तस्मात् Pt. 1. 48; cf. words like<BR>रूपाजीव, अजाजीव, शस्त्राजीव, स्त्र्याजीव<BR>&c.; आजीवनार्थः Ms. 10. 79 means<BR>of livelihood.<BR>--2 Profession, the<BR>means of maintaining oneself;<BR>विशुद्ध इदानीमाजीवः Ś. 6.<BR>--वः A Jaina<BR>beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0230-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीवकः|आजीवक
आजीवकः A beggar, one who<BR>earns his livelihood everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीविका
आजीविका Profession, means of<BR>subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीविन्
आजीविन् a.<BR>1 Having a<BR>livelihood.<BR>--2 A particular kind of<BR>beggar (एकदंडिन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजीव्य
आजीव्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be<BR>practised (as a profession).<BR>--2 Fit for or<BR>affording a livelihood.<BR>--3 Habitable,<BR>fertile; Y. 1. 320; Ms. 7. 69.<BR>--व्यं<BR>A means of subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आजुर्
आजुर् f.,<BR>--आजू f.<BR>1 Working<BR>without wages.<BR>--2 A servant working<BR>without wages.<BR>--3 Doomed<BR>residence in a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञा
आज्ञा {c9c} P. To know, under<BR>stand, learn, obtain information,<BR>ascertain, notice, perceive. --Caus.<BR>(ज्ञापयति)<BR>1 To order, command,<BR>direct.<BR>--2 To assure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञप्तिः|आज्ञप्ति
आज्ञप्तिः f. An order, injunction,<BR>command; ˚हर a. bearing a message,<BR>messenger; Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञा
आज्ञा [आ-ज्ञा-अङ्]<BR>1 An order,<BR>command; तथेति शेषामिव भर्तुराज्ञां<BR>Ku. 3. 22.<BR>--2 Permission, allowance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुग, --अनुगामिन्,<BR>--अनुयायिन्, --अनुवर्तिन्, --अनुसारिन्, --संपादक, --वह a.<BR>obedient, submissive.<BR>--कर, --कारिन् a.<BR>obeying or executing orders,<BR>obedient.<BR>--(रः) a servent;<BR>˚करत्वमधिगम्य V. 3. 19 being the obedient<BR>servant; कार्याणां गतयो विधेरपि<BR>नयंत्याज्ञाकरत्वं चिरात् Mu. 7. 16<BR>subjection.<BR>--करणं, --पालनं obedience,<BR>execution of commands.<BR>--चक्रं a mystical<BR>circle or diagram; one of the six<BR>described in Tantras.<BR>--पत्रं an edict,<BR>written order.<BR>--प्रतिघातः, --भंगः {1}<BR>disobedience, insubordination,<BR>नाज्ञाभंगं सहंते नृवर नृपतयस्त्वादृशाः<BR>सार्वभौमाः Mu. 3. 22. {2} rebellion,<BR>disloyalty.<BR>--विधेय a. obedient to commands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञातृ
आज्ञातृ a. Ved. One who orders<BR>or directs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञानं|आज्ञान
आज्ञानं The act of observing,<BR>perceiving (आज्ञानं = आज्ञप्तिः ईश्वरभावः<BR>Śaṅkara.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापक|आज्ञापकः
आज्ञापक a. Giving orders, a<BR>commander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञापनं|आज्ञापन
आज्ञापनं<BR>1 Ordering,<BR>commanding.<BR>--2 Making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्ञायिन्
आज्ञायिन् a. Perceiving,<BR>knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आज्यं|आज्य
आज्यं [आज्यते, आ-अंज्-क्यप्]<BR>1<BR>Clarified butter, ghee; आज्यधूमोद्गमेन<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">Page0231-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Ś. 1. 15; (it is often distinguished from<BR>घृत; सपिंविंलीनमाज्यं स्याद् घनीभूतं घृतं भवेत्).<BR>--2 (In a wider sense) Oil, milk<BR>&c. used instead of clarified butter;<BR>घृतं वा यदि वा तैलं पयो वा दधि यावकं ।<BR>आज्यस्याने नियुक्तानामाज्यशब्दो विधीयते ॥.<BR>--3<BR>N. of a sort of chant or religious<BR>service (सामस्तोमभेदः);<BR>आजिमीयुस्तस्मादाज्यानामाज्यत्वं Nir.<BR>--4 Turpentine.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दोहं a hymn to be<BR>recited by a Sāmavedin.<BR>--प a.<BR>drinking ghee. (--पाः pl.) a class<BR>of Manes who are the sons of<BR>Pulastya and the ancestors of the Vaiśya<BR>order; पुलस्त्यस्याज्यपाः पुत्राः Mb.;<BR>Ms. 3. 197-8.<BR>--पात्रं, --स्थाली a vessel or<BR>dish to hold clarified butter.<BR>--भज्<BR>m. {1} an epithet of Agni (the<BR>consumer of clarified butter). {2}<BR>a god, deity.<BR>--वारिः ‘sea of clarified<BR>butter’, one of the seven seas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंचनं|आञ्चन
आंचनं Partial extraction of<BR>thorns, arrows and the like from<BR>the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंछ्|आञ्छ्
आंछ् {c1c} P. (आंछति, आनंछ, आंछित)<BR>1 To lengthen, stretch, extend.<BR>--2<BR>To make straight.<BR>--3 To regulate,<BR>bring or draw into the right<BR>position; set (as a bone or leg.);<BR>चक्रयोगेनांछेदूर्वस्थि निर्गतं Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंछनं|आञ्छन
आंछनं Setting(a bone or leg);<BR>bringing into the right position by<BR>stretching, bending, or drawing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंजन|आञ्जन|आञ्जनः
आंजन a. (नी f.) [अंजनस्येदं-अण्]<BR>Anointing or belonging to ointment.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Ointment, especially for the<BR>eyes.<BR>--2 Fat.<BR>--नः N. of Māruti or<BR>Hanūmat;<BR>दाशरथिबलैरिवांजननीलनलपरिगतप्रांतैः K. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंजनी
आंजनी Ointment, especially for<BR>the eyes.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारी a woman<BR>who anoints or prepares ointments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंजनिक्यं|आञ्जनिक्य
आंजनिक्यं [पुरोहितादिगण<BR>P. V. 1. 128] That which is used to<BR>prepare ointments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंजनेयः|आञ्जनेय|आञ्जनेयः
आंजनेयः [अंजनायाः अपत्यं ढक्] N.<BR>of Māruti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंजलिक्यं|आञ्जलिक्य
आंजलिक्यं [cf. आंजनिक्यं]<BR>Folding the hands in supplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंजिनेयः|आञ्जिनेय|आञ्जिनेयः
आंजिनेयः [अंजिन्यां भवः ढक्] A kind<BR>of insect, a kind of lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटरूषः|आटरूष
आटरूषः [अटरूष एव, स्वार्थे अण्] N.<BR>of a tree, see अटरूष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटविकः|आटविक
आटविकः [अटव्यां चरति भवो वा<BR>ठक्]<BR>1 A forester, a woodman,<BR>inhabitant of a forest.<BR>--2 A pioneer.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">Page0231-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--3 One of the six kinds of armies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटवी
आटवी [अटव्याः सन्निकृष्टा पूः अण्] N.<BR>of a city of the Yavanas in the<BR>south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिः|आटि
आटिः [आ-अट्-इण्]<BR>1 A kind of<BR>bird (शरारि) (also written आटि).<BR>--2<BR>A sort of fish.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुखः, --खं a<BR>surgical instrument used in<BR>bloodletting (so called from its being<BR>like the beak of the bird आटि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिक
आटिक, आटिक्य a. [आटाय गमनाय प्रवृत्तः<BR>ठण्, ष्यञ् वा] Able to wander, being<BR>on a voyage or journey.<BR>--की A<BR>woman fit to go out (<BR>अनुपजातपयोधरादिस्त्रीव्यंजना Śaṅkara).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटिक्य
आटिक, आटिक्य a. [आटाय गमनाय प्रवृत्तः<BR>ठण्, ष्यञ् वा] Able to wander, being<BR>on a voyage or journey.<BR>--की A<BR>woman fit to go out (<BR>अनुपजातपयोधरादिस्त्रीव्यंजना Śaṅkara).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटीकनं|आटीकन
आटीकनं [आटीक्-ल्युट्] The<BR>leaping motion of a calf; so आटीलकं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटीकरः|आटीकर
आटीकरः A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आटोपः|आटोप
आटोपः [आ-तुप्-घंञ् पृषो˚ टत्वं Tv.]<BR>1 Pride, self-conceit, arrogance;<BR>साटोपं proudly, in a stately or<BR>majestic manner, frequently used as a<BR>stage direction.<BR>--2 Swelling,<BR>spreading, expanding, puffing; Prov.<BR>फटाटोपो भयंकर; said also of clouds; अद्यापि<BR>साटोपा मेघा दृश्यंते Pt. 1; Śi. 3. 74.<BR>--3 Flatulence (in the belly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडंबरः|आडम्बर|आडम्बरः
आडंबरः [आ-डंब्-क्षेपे, अरन्]<BR>1<BR>Pride, arrogance.<BR>--2 Show; means,<BR>external appendage;<BR>विरचितनारसिंहरूपाडंबरं K. 5, 309; निर्गुणः शोभते नैव<BR>विपुलाडंबरोपि ना Bv. 1. 115.<BR>--3 The<BR>sounding of a trumpet as a sign of<BR>attack.<BR>--4 Commencement.<BR>--5 Fury,<BR>anger, passion; दंतिनामाडंबररवेण<BR>K. 114.<BR>--6 Happiness, pleasure.<BR>--7<BR>The roaring of clouds and of<BR>elephants; Bv. 1. 4.<BR>--8 The eyelid.<BR>--9<BR>A drum used in a battle.<BR>--10<BR>(Hence) A charge sounded by<BR>musical instruments; the din or<BR>uproar of the battle.<BR>--रं Rubbing<BR>and kneading the body.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आघातः one who beats a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडंबरिन्|आडम्बरिन्
आडंबरिन् a. Arrogant, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडिः|आडि
आडिः = आटि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आडूः
आडूः [अल्-ऊ, लस्य डः नि˚ वृद्धि Tv.]<BR>A raft, a float.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकः|आढक|आढकं
आढकः, --कं A measure of grain,<BR>the 4th of a Droṇa = 64<BR>Prasthas = 16 Kuḍavas = (nearly {7}<BR>lbs. 11 ozs. avoir.); अष्टमुष्टिर्भवेत कुंचिः<BR>कुंचयोऽष्टौ तु पुष्कलं । पुष्कलानि च चत्वारि<BR>आढकः परिकीर्तितः ॥.<BR>--की<BR>1 A kind of<BR>pulse.<BR>--2 A kind of fragrant earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकं|आढक|आढकः
आढकः, --कं A measure of grain,<BR>the 4th of a Droṇa = 64<BR>Prasthas = 16 Kuḍavas = (nearly {7}<BR>lbs. 11 ozs. avoir.); अष्टमुष्टिर्भवेत कुंचिः<BR>कुंचयोऽष्टौ तु पुष्कलं । पुष्कलानि च चत्वारि<BR>आढकः परिकीर्तितः ॥.<BR>--की<BR>1 A kind of<BR>pulse.<BR>--2 A kind of fragrant earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकिक|आढकिकः
आढकिक, आढकीन a. [cf. आचितिक]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">Page0232-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Holding an Āḍhaka, sown with<BR>an Āḍhaka of seed; cooking an<BR>Āḍhaka (of rice &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढकीन|आढकीनः
आढकिक, आढकीन a. [cf. आचितिक]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">Page0232-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Holding an Āḍhaka, sown with<BR>an Āḍhaka of seed; cooking an<BR>Āḍhaka (of rice &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0231-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्य|आढ्यः
आढ्य a. [आ-ध्यै-क-पृषो˚ Tv.]<BR>1 Rich, wealthy; आढ्योऽ<BR>भिजनवानस्मि कोन्योस्ति सदृशो मया Bg. 16. 15;<BR>Pt. 5. 8; Ms. 8. 169.<BR>--2 (a) Rich<BR>in, abounding in, possessing<BR>abundantly, with instr. or as the<BR>last member of comp.; सत्य˚<BR>Pt. 3. 9 very truthful; वंशसंपल्लावण्याढ्याय<BR>Dk. 18; एवमादिगुणैराढ्यः Vet.;<BR>समुद्रमिव रत्नाढ्यं Rām. (b) Mixed with,<BR>watered with; गंधाढ्य; स्रज<BR>उत्तमगंधाढ्याः Mb.; मूत्राढ्यैः करंजफलसर्षपैः<BR>Suśr.<BR>--3 Abundant, copious.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आडु a. striving to get wealth.<BR>--कुलीन a. [आढ्यकुले भवः ख]<BR>Descended from a rich family.<BR>--चर<BR>a. (री f.) [भूतपूर्व आढ्यः चरट्] once<BR>opulent.<BR>--वातः [आढ्यो वातो यत्र] a<BR>convulsive or rheumatic palsy of<BR>the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यंकरण|आढ्यङ्करण
आढ्यंकरण^1 a. (णी f.) [<BR>P. III. 2. 56] Enriching.<BR>--णं The means<BR>of enriching, wealth, prosperity.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यंभविष्णु|आढ्यम्भविष्णु
आढ्यंभविष्णु, --भावुक a. [<BR>P. III. 2. 57] Becoming rich or eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यंभावुक|आढ्यम्भावुक
आढ्यंभविष्णु, --भावुक a. [<BR>P. III. 2. 57] Becoming rich or eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आढ्यता
आढ्यता Opulence, wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणक|आणकः
आणक a. [अणक एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>Low, inferior, vile.<BR>--कं Sexual<BR>enjoyment in a particular position;<BR>आणकं सुरतं नाम दंपत्योः पार्श्वसंस्थयोः ।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणव
आणव a. (वी f.) Exceedingly<BR>small.<BR>--वं Exceeding smallness<BR>or minuteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणवीन|आणवीनं
आणवीन a. [अणुधान्यानां भवनं क्षेत्रं<BR>वा खञ्] Bearing or fit to bear Aṇu<BR>(Panicum Miliaceum).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आणिः|आणि
आणिः m. f. [अण्-इण् स्त्रियां वा ङीप्]<BR>1 The pin of the axle of a cart, the<BR>linch-pin.<BR>--2 The part of the leg<BR>just above the knee (जानुन<BR>ऊर्ध्वमुभयतस्त्र्यंगुलमणिर्नाम Suśr.).<BR>--3 The corner<BR>of a house.<BR>--4 A boundary, limit.<BR>--5 The edge of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंड|आण्ड|आण्डः
आंड a. [अंडे भवः अण्] Born from<BR>an egg (as a bird).<BR>--डः An epithet<BR>of Hiraṇyagarbha or Brahmā.<BR>--डं<BR>1<BR>A multitude of eggs, brood.<BR>--2<BR>Scrotum.<BR>--डौ (Ved.) The testicles.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. born from eggs.<BR>--(जः) a bird or a serpent.<BR>--(जं)<BR>the body of a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंडी|आण्डी
आंडी Ved. A testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंडीक|आण्डीक
आंडीक a. Bearing eggs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंडीर|आण्डीर
आंडीर a. [आंडमस्त्यस्य ईरच्]<BR>1<BR>Having many eggs.<BR>--2 Grown up,<BR>full-grown (as a bull.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत्
आत् The letter आ. --ind. Ved.<BR>1<BR>Afterwards, then; generally used<BR>antithetically to यद्, यदा, यदि and<BR>then sometimes strengthened by<BR>the particles अह, उ, इद् &c.<BR>--2 Then,<BR>further, also, and (अपिच).<BR>--3<BR>Sometimes it only strengthens the<BR>meaning of another word or gives<BR>emphasis to an interrogative pronoun<BR>like उ, अंग, नु added to किं (possibly,<BR>at all).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आत|आतः
आत a. [आ-अत्-अच्] Spread<BR>around.<BR>--तः Ved.<BR>1 A quarter of<BR>the sky.<BR>--2 A scaffold.<BR>--3 The<BR>frame of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतंच्|आतञ्च्
आतंच् {c7c} P. To coagulate, to<BR>cause to shrink or contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतंकः|आतङ्क|आतंक|आतङ्कः
आतंकः [आ-तंच्-घञ्, --कुत्वं]<BR>1<BR>Disease, sickness of the body;<BR>दीर्घतीव्रामयग्रस्तं ब्राह्मणं गामथापि वा । दृष्ट्वा पथि<BR>निरातंकं कृत्वा वा ब्रह्महा शुचिः ॥ Y. 3. 245.<BR>--2 Fever.<BR>--3 Pain, affliction (of<BR>the mind), disquietude; anguish,<BR>agony; किन्निमित्तोयमातंकः;<BR>आतंकस्फुरितकठोरगर्भगुर्वीं U. 1. 49; Ś. 3; V. 3.<BR>--4 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR>--5 Fear,<BR>apprehension; पुरुषायुषजीविन्यो<BR>निरातंका निरीतयः R. 1. 63; fright, terror;<BR>Ratn. 2. 2.<BR>--6 The sound of a drum<BR>or tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतंचनं|आतञ्चन|आतञ्चनं
आतंचनं<BR>1 Causing to coagulate<BR>or curdle, casting butter-milk into<BR>heated milk to turn it.<BR>--2<BR>Causing to contract in general.<BR>--3<BR>Curdled milk.<BR>--4 That which causes<BR>coagulation, a runnet.<BR>--5 A sort of<BR>whey.<BR>--6 Conveying.<BR>--7 Gratifying,<BR>satisfying.<BR>--8 Casting away,<BR>destroying.<BR>--9 Danger, calamity.<BR>--10<BR>Speed, velocity.<BR>--11 Calcining,<BR>adding flux to metals in fusion.<BR>--12<BR>The flux so used.<BR>--13 Making fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतन्
आतन् {c8c} U.<BR>1 To extend, stretch<BR>over, overspread, cover;<BR>निषादिवक्षःस्थलमातनोति Ki. 16. 15 pervade,<BR>penetrate; Ki. 7. 25.<BR>--2 To spread,<BR>diffuse.<BR>--3 To cause, produce;<BR>आनंदनेन जडतां पुनरातनोति U. 3. 12;<BR>Ki. 6. 18, 7. 39; K. 176; Māl. 5. 9;<BR>Mv. 4. 31.<BR>--4 To bring to pass,<BR>effect, accomplish, do, perform;<BR>सुरतमाततान K. 57; सपर्यां 64.<BR>--5 To<BR>illuminate.<BR>--6 To take hold of;<BR>seek to attain.<BR>--7 To assume a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">Page0232-c+ 57</a>]<BR>hostile attitude.<BR>--8 To stretch (as<BR>a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतत
आतत p. p.<BR>1 Spread, extended.<BR>--2 Stretched (as a bow-string);<BR>R. 1. 19; ˚ज्य stretched out on the bow;<BR>11. 45, 16. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आततायिन्
आततायिन् a. or s. [आततेन विस्तीर्णेन<BR>शस्त्रादिना अयितुं शीलमस्य Tv.]<BR>1 ‘One whose<BR>bow is stretched to take another's<BR>life’, endeavouring to kill some one;<BR>a desperado; गुरुं वा बालवध्वौ वा ब्राह्मणं<BR>वा बहुश्रुतं । आततायिनमायांतं<BR>हन्यादेवाविचारयन् ॥ Ms. 8. 350-1; Bg. 1. 36.<BR>--2<BR>Any one who commits a heinous<BR>crime, such as a thief, ravisher,<BR>murderer, incendiary, a felon &c;<BR>अग्निदो गरदश्चैव शस्त्रोन्मत्तो धनापहः ।<BR>क्षेत्रदारहरश्चैतान् षड् विद्यादाततायिनः ॥ Śukra.<BR>˚ता, --त्वं murdering, stealing,<BR>destroying &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतताविन्
आतताविन् a. Ved. One whose bow<BR>is stretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतनं|आतन
आतनं<BR>1 Spreading, penetrating,<BR>expanding.<BR>--2 Sight, view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतनि
आतनि a. Ved. [तन्-इन्]<BR>Spreading; pervading.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतानः|आतान
आतानः [तन्-घञ्]<BR>1 An extended<BR>cord or string (Ved.).<BR>--2 Long<BR>extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्
आतप् {c1c} P. To radiate, heat.<BR>blaze; inflame, to cause to glow.<BR>--pass. To suffer pain, be afflicted;<BR>to inflict (austerities) upon<BR>oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्
आतप् a. Ved. Heating(आतापिन्)<BR>--f. Heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप|आतपः
आतप a. Ved. Causing pain or<BR>affliction.<BR>--पः<BR>1 Heat (of the sun,<BR>fire &c.), sunshine; आतपायोज्झितं<BR>धान्यं Mb. exposed to the sun;<BR>तमातपक्लांतं R. 2. 13; शीतातपाभिघातान्<BR>Ms. 12. 77; प्रचंड˚ Rs. 1. 11, 10; सूर्य˚<BR>Me. 108; बालातपः Ms. 4. 69 the<BR>morning sun; ˚आक्रांत exposed<BR>to heat.<BR>--2 Light; छायातपौ ब्रह्मविदो<BR>वदंति Kaṭh.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अत्ययः<BR>passing of the sun's heat, sunset;<BR>आतपात्ययसंक्षिप्तनीवारासु R. 1. 52.<BR>--अभावः non-existence of the sun's<BR>heat, shadow.<BR>--उदकं mirage.<BR>--त्रं,<BR>--त्रकं [आतपात् त्रायते, त्रै-क] an<BR>umbrella (of silk or leaves used as a<BR>parasol); तमातपक्लांतमनातपत्रं R. 2. 13,<BR>47; पद्म˚ 4. 5; राज्यं<BR>स्वहस्तधृतदंडमिवातपत्रं Ś. 5. 6.<BR>--लंघनं being<BR>exposed to heat, catching the sun-stroke;<BR>आतपलंघनाद्वलवदस्वस्थशरीरा शकुंतला<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">Page0233-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Ś. 3.<BR>--वर्ष्य a. (water &c.) produced by<BR>rain during sunshine.<BR>--वारणं [आतपं<BR>वारयति] an umbrella, parasol;<BR>नृपतिककुदं दत्वा यूने सितातपवारणं R. 3. 70,<BR>9. 15.<BR>--शुष्क a. dried in the<BR>sunshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0232-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपनः|आतपन
आतपनः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपवत्|आतपवन्त्
आतपवत् a. Exposed to sunshine,<BR>sunny; Ku. 1. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतपीय
आतपीय a. Sunny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतप्य
आतप्य a. Ved. Being in the<BR>sunshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतमाम्
आतमाम् ind. Very near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतापिः|आतापि
आतापिः [आ-तप्-इण्] N. of a<BR>demon; आतापिर्भक्षितो येन वातापिश्च<BR>महासुरः । समुद्रः शोषितो येन स मेऽगस्त्यः<BR>प्रसीदतु ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतापिन्
आतापि(यि)न् N. of a bird,<BR>a kite, falcon (Falco Cheela).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतायिन्
आतापि(यि)न् N. of a bird,<BR>a kite, falcon (Falco Cheela).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आताली
आताली ind. Compounded with<BR>अस्, भू and कृ; P. I. 4. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिः|आति
आतिः A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिः|आति
आतिः = आटि q. v. (cf.<BR>P. III. 3. 108 and Uṇ. 4. 130).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथेय|आतिथेयः
आतिथेय a. (यी f.) [अतिथिषु साधुः<BR>ढञ्; अतिथये इदं ढक्]<BR>1 Attentive to<BR>guests, hospitable (as a man);<BR>प्रत्युज्जगामातिथिमातिथेयः R. 5. 2, 12. 25<BR>तमातिथेयी बहुमानपूर्वया Ku. 5. 31.<BR>--2<BR>Proper for, or suited to, a guest,<BR>intended for a guest; आतिथेयः<BR>सत्कारः Ś. 1.<BR>--यं Hospitality;<BR>आतिथेयमनिवारितातिथिः Śi. 14. 38;<BR>Ms. 3. 18; सज्जातिथेया वयं Mv. 2. 50.<BR>--यी Hospitality; Bv. 1. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिथ्य|आतिथ्यं|आतिथ्यः
आतिथ्य a. [अतिथेरिदं ष्यञ्]<BR>Hospitable, proper for a guest &c. ( =<BR>आतिथेय); हविरातिथ्यं, आतिथ्या इष्टिः &c.<BR>--थ्यः A guest.<BR>--थ्यं<BR>1 Hospitable<BR>reception, hospitality;<BR>तमातिथ्यक्रियाशांतरथक्षोभपरिश्रमं R. 1. 58.<BR>--2 A<BR>particular rite, the reception of<BR>Soma when it is brought to the<BR>sacrificial place (also called<BR>आतिथ्येष्टिः).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रूप a. being in<BR>the place of the आतिथ्य sacrifice.<BR>--सत्कारः, --सत्क्रिया the rites of<BR>hospitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिदेशिक
आतिदेशिक a. (की f.) (In<BR>gram.) Connected with आतिदेश q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0233-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आतिरेक्यं|आतिरेक्य
