आप्
आप् {c5c} P., rarely {c1c} P. (आप्नोति or<BR>आपति, आप, आपत्, आप्स्यति, आप्तुं, आप्त)<BR>1 To obtain, attain, get;<BR>पुत्रमेवंगुणोपेतं चक्रवर्तिनमाप्नुहि Ś. 1. 12;<BR>अनुद्योगेन तैलानि तिलेभ्यो नाप्तुमर्हति<BR>H. Pr. 30; शतं क्रतुनामपविघ्नमाप सः<BR>R. 3. 38; so फलं, कीर्ति, सुखं &c.<BR>--2 To reach,<BR>go to; overtake, meet, fall in with;<BR>शबरीमापतुर्वने Bk. 6. 59.<BR>--3 To<BR>pervade, occupy, enter into.<BR>--4 To<BR>undergo, suffer, meet with;<BR>दिष्टांतमाप्स्यति भवान् R. 9. 79; Ms. 8. 188.<BR>--5 To equal. --pass. (आप्यते)<BR>1 To<BR>be reached, found, met with,<BR>obtained &c.<BR>--2 To arrive at one's<BR>end or aim.<BR>--3 To become filled.<BR>--Caus. (आपयति)<BR>1 To cause to<BR>reach or obtain.<BR>--2 To cause any<BR>one to feel or perceive.<BR>--3 To hit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपः|आप
आपः [आप्-घञ्]<BR>1 N. of one of<BR>the 8 demigods called Vasus.<BR>--2<BR>(At the end of comp.) दुराप<BR>difficult to be obtained.<BR>--पं [अपां समूहः]<BR>1 A flood or stream of water, water.<BR>--2 Sky (Nir.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपक
आपक a. [आप्-ण्वुल्] Getting,<BR>obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपनं|आपन
आपनं [आप्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Getting,<BR>obtaining, reaching &c.<BR>--2 Pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपयितृ
आपयितृ a. [आप्-णिच्-तृच्] One who<BR>gets or procures, procuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0243-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिः|आपि
आपिः [आप्-णिच्-इन्]<BR>1 Obtaining<BR>wealth &c.<BR>--2 A friend,<BR>acquaintance, ally (बंधु); ˚त्वं friendship,<BR>alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त|आप्तः
आप्त p. p. [आप्-क्त]<BR>1 Got,<BR>obtained, gained; ˚कामः, ˚शापः &c.<BR>--2<BR>Reached, overtaken, equalled.<BR>--3<BR>Reaching to, extending as far as.<BR>--4<BR>Trustworthy, reliable, credible (as<BR>news &c.).<BR>--5 Trusty, confidential,<BR>faithful (person); R. 3. 12; 5. 39;<BR>Ms. 8. 63.<BR>--6 (a) Clever, skilful;<BR>प्राजकश्चेद्भवेदाप्तः Ms. 8. 294. (b) Apt,<BR>fit.<BR>--7 Full, complete, abundant;<BR>यजेत राजा क्रतुभिर्विविधैराप्तदक्षिणैः<BR>Ms. 7. 79.<BR>--8 True, exact.<BR>--9 Intimate,<BR>closely related, acquainted; कन्यायाः<BR>किल पूजयंति पितरो जामातुराप्तं जनं<BR>U. 4. 17 relatives; Ms. 5. 101.<BR>--10<BR>Appointed.<BR>--11 Generally received,<BR>commonly used; authentic.<BR>--12 Accused,<BR>prosecuted.<BR>--13 Reasonable, sensible.<BR>--प्तः<BR>1 A trustworthy, reliable, or<BR>fit person; credible person or source,<BR>guarantee; आप्तः यथार्थवक्ता T. S.<BR>--2 A relative, friend;<BR>निग्रहात्स्वसुराप्तानां वधाच्च धनदानुजः R. 12. 52;<BR>कथमाप्तवर्गोयं भवत्याः M. 5; Y. 1. 28,<BR>2. 71; Ms. 2. 109, 8. 64.<BR>--3 An<BR>Arhat.<BR>--प्ता A twisted lock of<BR>hair.<BR>--प्तं<BR>1 A quotient.<BR>--2 (In<BR>Math.) Equation of a degree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः f. {1} an augment.<BR>{2} an affix. {3} a word of received<BR>acceptation and established by<BR>usage only; see आप्तवाच् also.<BR>--काम<BR>a. {1} one who has obtained his<BR>desire. {2} one who has renounced<BR>all worldly desires and attachments.<BR>--(मः) the supreme soul.<BR>--कारिन्<BR>a. doing things in a fit or<BR>confidential manner; Ms. 9. 12. (--m.)<BR>a trusty agent or confidential<BR>servant.<BR>--गर्भा a pregnant woman.<BR>--दक्षिण a. having proper or<BR>abundant gifts.<BR>--बचनं {1} received text<BR>or authority, revelation. {2} the words<BR>of a credible or trustworthy person<BR>R. 11. 42, 15. 48.<BR>--वाक्यं a true<BR>or correct sentence; = वचनं above.<BR>--वाच् a. worthy of belief,<BR>regarded as authority, one whose words<BR>are credible and authoritative;<BR>परातिसंधानमधीयते यैर्विद्येति ते संतु<BR>किलाप्तवाचः Ś. 5. 25. (--f.) {1} the<BR>advice of a friend or credible per<BR>son. {2} the Vedas or Śruti<BR>a word of authority (said to apply to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">Page0244-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Smṛtis, Itihāsas and Purāṇas also,<BR>which are considered as<BR>authoritative evidence); आप्तवागतुमानाभ्यां<BR>साध्यं त्वां प्रति का कथा R. 10. 28.<BR>--श्रुतिः<BR>f. {1} the Vedas. {2} Smṛtis &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0243-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्तिः|आप्ति
आप्तिः f. [आप् क्तिन्]<BR>1 Getting,<BR>obtaining, gain, acquisition; मित्र˚,<BR>काम˚ &c.<BR>--2 Reaching, overtaking,<BR>meeting with.<BR>--3 Binding,<BR>connection, relation.<BR>--4 Union; especially<BR>with a woman (Med.).<BR>--5 Fitness,<BR>aptitude, propriety.<BR>--6 Completion,<BR>fulfilment; कामस्याप्तिं जगतः प्रतिष्ठां<BR>Kaṭh.<BR>--7 Future time. --pl. N.<BR>of 12 sacrificial verses beginning<BR>with Āpaye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
आप्य a. [अपां इदं अण् स्वार्थे ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Watery.<BR>--2 Obtainable, attainable<BR>(आप्-ण्यत्).<BR>--प्यः A class of gods.<BR>--प्यं Ved. Confederation, alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपकर
आपकर a. (री f.) [अपकरे भवः अण्<BR>अञ् च] Offensive, unfriendly,<BR>mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपक्व|आपक्वं
आपक्व a. Crude, raw,<BR>half-baked.<BR>--क्वं A cake, bread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगा
आपगा [अपां समूहः आपं; तेन गच्छति<BR>गम् ड] A river, stream; फेनायमानं<BR>पतिनापगानां Śi. 3. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपगेयः|आपगेय
आपगेयः [आपगायां गंगायां भवः ढक्]<BR>A son of the river, an epithet of<BR>Bhīshma or Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणः|आपण
आपणः [आपण्-घञ्] A market;<BR>shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपणिक|आपणिकः
आपणिक a. [आपणादागतः ठक्]<BR>1<BR>Relating to traffic, market &c.,<BR>mercantile.<BR>--2 Got from the market (as<BR>duties).<BR>--कः<BR>1 A shop-keeper,<BR>merchant, dealer.<BR>--2 A tax on<BR>market shops.<BR>--3 Assize, market-rate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्
आपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fall upon,<BR>attack, assail; उदायुधानापततः<BR>R. 12. 44, 5. 50; Bk. 3. 48.<BR>--2 To<BR>approach, come towards; K. 202;<BR>एतत्प्रायेण श्रुतिविषयमापतितमेव K. 136<BR>has reached the ears; 268.<BR>--3 To<BR>fly towards, come in flying, come or<BR>drive in haste, rush upon.<BR>--4 (a)<BR>To happen, take place, occur, come<BR>to pass; कथमिदमापतितं U. 2;<BR>K. 262, 158; अहो न शोभनमापतितं Pt. 2.<BR>(b) To fall to one's lot or share,<BR>befall; अहोऽस्माकं महद्भोजममापतितं<BR>Pt. 1; आपतंति हि<BR>संसारपथमवतीर्णानामेते वृत्तांताः K. 175, 132; सर्वस्यैव<BR>स्खलितमापतति 291; H. 1. 30, 173.<BR>--5<BR>(a) To occur to, cross (the mind);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">Page0244-b+ 57</a>]<BR>इति हृदये नापतितं K. 288. (b) To be<BR>felt or regarded; मधुरतराण्यापतंति<BR>मतसः K. 103 are felt or regarded;<BR>202, 236, 329. --Caus. (पातयति)<BR>To go towards, approach (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतनं|आपतन
आपतनं<BR>1 Approaching, coming,<BR>assailing &c.<BR>--2 Happening,<BR>occurrence.<BR>--3 Descending, alighting<BR>--4 Obtaining.<BR>--5 Knowledge;<BR>क्वचित्<BR>प्राकरणिकादर्थादप्राकरणिकस्यार्थस्यापतनं S. D. 10.<BR>--6 Natural sequence,<BR>necessarily following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपति|आपतिः
आपति a. Ved. Coming in haste,<BR>rushing on.<BR>--तिः The wind (always<BR>blowing) (सततगतिर्पायुः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतिक|आपतिकः
आपतिक a. (की f.) Accidental,<BR>unforeseen, sent from heaven.<BR>--कः<BR>A hawk, falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपतित
आपतित a.<BR>1 Fallen to the lot of.<BR>--2 Happened, befallen, occurred,<BR>come to pass.<BR>--3 Alighted,<BR>descended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपात|आपातः
आपात a. Rushing upon,<BR>attacking.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Rushing or falling<BR>upon, attack, descending, alighting;<BR>तदापातभयात्पथि Ku. 2. 45;<BR>गरुडापातविश्लिष्टमेघनादास्त्रबंधनः R. 12. 76.<BR>--2 Throwing down.<BR>--3 Causing to<BR>descend or fall, falling down;<BR>धारापातैः Me. 48.<BR>--4 (a) The present or<BR>current moment, the instant;<BR>आपातरम्या विषयाः पर्यंतपरितापिनः Ki. 11. 12,<BR>आपतसुरसे भोगे निमग्नाः किं न कुर्वते<BR>S. D.; H. 4. 75; Bv. 1. 115;<BR>Māl. 5. (b) (Hence) First sight or<BR>appearance; see आपाततः<BR>--5<BR>Happening, becoming apparent,<BR>appearance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दुःसह a.<BR>unbearable at the first attack; U. 7.<BR>--दुष्प्रसह a. unbearable in its onset,<BR>making a furious charge; M. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाततः
आपाततः ind. At the first sight<BR>or attack, instantly, immediately;<BR>S. D. 632.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपातिन्
आपातिन् a. Falling on, attacking,<BR>descending, happening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्य
आपत्य a. (त्यी f.) [अपत्य-अण्]<BR>1 Relating to offspring.<BR>--2 (In<BR>gram.) Relating to the formation of<BR>patronymic words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपथि|आपथिः
आपथि a. Ved. Being on the<BR>way or journey.<BR>--थिः, --थीः, --थ्यः<BR>Ved. A wanderer, traveller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्
आपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To go near, walk<BR>towards, approach; एष रावणिरापादि<BR>वानराणां भयंकरः Bk. 15. 89.<BR>--2 To<BR>enter into, go to, attain to (a place,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-c" target="_blank">Page0244-c+ 57</a>]<BR>state &c.); वक्तमापद्य मारुतः Śik. 9;<BR>निर्वेदनापद्यते becomes disgusted<BR>Mk. 1. 14; आपेदिरेंऽबरपथं Bv. 1. 17; क्षीरं<BR>दधिभावमापद्यते Ś. B. milk turns into<BR>curds; पांडुरतामापद्यमानस्य K. 69<BR>becoming pale; 160; विस्मयमापेदे 179;<BR>श्लोकत्वमापद्यत यस्य शोकः R. 14. 70<BR>assumed the form of a verse;<BR>चिंतामापेदे Dk. 130 fell a-thinking; so<BR>विश्वासं, निर्वृतिं, संशयं, वशं, पंचत्वं &c.<BR>--3 To get into trouble, fall into<BR>misfortune; अर्थधर्तौ परित्यज्य यः<BR>काममनुवर्तते । एवमापद्यते क्षिप्रं राजा दशरथो<BR>यथा ॥ Rām.; see आपन्न below.<BR>--4 To<BR>happen, occur; Bk. 6. 31; एवमापद्यते<BR>M. 1 so it is. --Caus.<BR>1 To bring<BR>about, bring to pass, accomplish,<BR>effect; कूजद्भिरापादितवंशकृत्यं<BR>R. 2. 12; Śānti. 3. 19.<BR>--2 To lead or<BR>reduce to, cause to suffer; R. 5. 5.<BR>--3<BR>To cause, to produce, bring on;<BR>लघिमानमापादयति K. 105, 109; दोषमपि<BR>गुणत्वमापादयति makes the best of a bad<BR>matter.<BR>--4 To reach or attain to.<BR>--5<BR>To spread, circulate (as news).<BR>--6<BR>To turn or change into; एकामपि<BR>काकिणीं कार्षापणलक्षमापादयेम Dk. 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपत्तिः|आपत्ति
आपत्तिः f. [आ-पद्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Turning<BR>or changing into, entering into<BR>any state or condition.<BR>--2 Obtaining,<BR>procuring, getting; स्थानापत्तेर्द्रव्येषु<BR>धर्मलाभः Kāty.<BR>--3 Misfortune,<BR>calamity, adversity; Y. 3. 42.<BR>--4 A<BR>fault, transgression.<BR>--5<BR>Remonstrance, expostulation.<BR>--6 (In phil.)<BR>An undesirable conclusion or<BR>occurrence (अनिष्टप्रसंग).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपद्
आपद् f. [आ-पद् क्विप्] A calamity,<BR>misfortune, danger, distress,<BR>adversity; दैवीनां मानुषीणां च प्रतिहर्ता<BR>त्वमापदां R. 1. 60; अविवेकः परमापदां पदम्<BR>Ki. 2. 30, 14; प्रायो गच्छति यत्र<BR>भाग्यरहितस्तत्रैव यांत्यापदः Bh. 2. 90; आपदि<BR>स्था, आपदं प्राप् to fall into difficulty.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कल्पः an alternative to<BR>be used in times of difficulty;<BR>Ms. 11. 28.<BR>--कालः days of adversity,<BR>time of distress, hour of danger;<BR>अब्राह्मणादध्ययनमापत्काले विधीयते<BR>Ms. 2. 241.<BR>--कालिक a. (का-की f.)<BR>occurring in time of difficulty.<BR>--गत, --ग्रस्त-प्राप्त a. {1} fallen into<BR>misfortune, involved in difficulties.<BR>{2} unfortunate, unhappy,<BR>distressed.<BR>--धर्मः [आपदि कर्तव्यो धर्मः] a<BR>practice, profession, or course of<BR>procedure, not usually proper for a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">Page0245-a+ 56</a>]<BR>caste, but allowable in times of<BR>extreme distress or calamity;<BR>Ms. 1. 116, 10. 130.<BR>--(र्मं) N. of a पर्व<BR>in Bhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0244-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपदा
आपदा f. Misfortune, calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपन्न|आपन्नः
आपन्न p. p.<BR>1 Gained, obtained,<BR>acquired; जीविकापन्नः for<BR>आपन्नजीविकः Sk.<BR>--2 Gone or reduced to,<BR>fallen into; कष्टां दशामापन्नोपि<BR>Bh. 2. 29; so दुःख˚.<BR>--3 Afflicted,<BR>distressed, being in difficulty;<BR>आपन्नाभयसत्रेषु दीक्षिताः खलु पौरवाः<BR>Ś. 2. 16; Me. 53; H. 4. 106, V. 2.<BR>--4 Befallen; परिच्छेदो हि पांडित्यं<BR>यदापन्ना विपत्तयः H. 1. 148.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सत्त्वा pregnant, quick or big with<BR>child; a pregnant woman;<BR>सममापन्नसत्त्वास्ता रेजुरापांडुरत्विषः R. 10. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपादः|आपाद
आपादः [आ-पद्-वञ्]<BR>1<BR>Attainment, obtaining.<BR>--2 Reward,<BR>remuneration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपादनं|आपादन
आपादनं Causing to arrive at,<BR>leading or contributing to,<BR>bringing about; tending to; द्रव्यस्य<BR>संख्यांतरापादने Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपनिकः|आपनिक
आपनिकः [आ-पन्-इकन् Uṇ. 2. 46]<BR>1 An emerald, sapphire.<BR>--2 A<BR>Kirāta or barbarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपमित्यक|आपमित्यकं
आपमित्यक a. [अपमित्य परिवर्त्य<BR>निर्वृत्तम् कक्] Received by barter or<BR>exchange.<BR>--कं Property or<BR>anything obtained by barter or for a<BR>consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपया
आपया [आपेन जलपूरेण याति या-क]<BR>N. of a river near the Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपराह्णिक
आपराह्णिक a. (की f.) Being in<BR>the afternoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपर्तुक|आपर्त्तुक
आपर्तुक a. (की f.) Not<BR>restricted to particular times or seasons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपवः|आपव
आपवः An epithet of Vasiṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपवर्ग्य
आपवर्ग्य a. Conferring final<BR>beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्
आपस् n. [आप्-असुन्]<BR>1 Water;<BR>आपोमिर्मार्जनं कृत्वा.<BR>--2 Sin.<BR>--3 A<BR>religious ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपस्कारं|आपस्कार
आपस्कारं The root or extremity<BR>of the trunk or body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपा
आपा {c1c} P.<BR>1 To drink up (lit. and<BR>fig.); षडाननापीतपयोधरासु R. 14. 22;<BR>आपीतसूर्यं नभः Mk. 5. 20 quite concealed<BR>or obscured; दिवाकरापीतरसा महौषधीः<BR>Mb.<BR>--2 To drink with the ears or<BR>eyes, hear or see intently; ता राघवं<BR>दृष्टिभिरापिबंत्यः R. 7. 12; K. 86;<BR>भगवत्कथासुधामापीयकर्णांजलिभिः Bhāg.<BR>--3 To eclipse, surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपानं|आपान
आपानं, --नकं<BR>1 A drinking party,<BR>banquet; Mk. 8; आपाने पानकलिता<BR>दैवनाभिपणोदिताः Mb.<BR>--2 A tavern,<BR>liquor-shop, a place for drinking in<BR>company (˚भूमि); तांबूलीनां दलैस्तत्र<BR>रचितापानभूतयः R. 4. 42; Ku. 6. 42;<BR>आपानकमुत्सवः K. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपानकं|आपानक
आपानं, --नकं<BR>1 A drinking party,<BR>banquet; Mk. 8; आपाने पानकलिता<BR>दैवनाभिपणोदिताः Mb.<BR>--2 A tavern,<BR>liquor-shop, a place for drinking in<BR>company (˚भूमि); तांबूलीनां दलैस्तत्र<BR>रचितापानभूतयः R. 4. 42; Ku. 6. 42;<BR>आपानकमुत्सवः K. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपायिन्
आपायिन् a. Drinking, fond of<BR>drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपाकः|आपाक
आपाकः [समंतात् परिवेष्ट्य पच्यतेऽत्र]<BR>A baking oven, a potter's kiln.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपांग्यं|आपाङ्ग्य
आपांग्यं [अपांगे देयं ञ्य] To be<BR>used for anointing the corners of<BR>the eyes (as अंजन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपालिः|आपालि
आपालिः A louse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिंजर|आपिञ्जर|आपिञ्जरं
आपिंजर a. Somewhat red,<BR>reddish; R. 16. 51.<BR>--रं Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिशलिः|आपिशलि
आपिशलिः N. of an old<BR>grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपिशल|आपिशलः
आपिशल a. Originating from<BR>आपिशलि.<BR>--लः A pupil of आपिशलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपी
आपी, आपीन See आप्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीन|आपीनं|आपीनः
आपी, आपीन See आप्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीड्
आपीड् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To press, weigh<BR>down; पयोधरभारेणापीडितः Gīt. 12;<BR>भुजाभ्यां तमापीड्य clasping him to<BR>the bosom.<BR>--2 To press hard, afflict,<BR>perplex, worry.<BR>--3 To compress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीड|आपीडः
आपीड a.<BR>1 Giving pain, hurting.<BR>--2 Squeezing, compressing.<BR>--3 A<BR>chaplet (tied on the crown of the<BR>head), garland in general;<BR>चूडापीडकपालसंकुलगलन्मंदाकिनीवारयः<BR>Māl. 1. 2.<BR>--4 (Hence fig.) A crest jewel;<BR>तस्मिन्कुलापीडनिभे विपीडं R. 18. 29;<BR>Māl. 1, 6, 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडनं|आपीडन
आपीडनं<BR>1 Compressing,<BR>squeezing; tying tightly.<BR>--2 Embracing,<BR>clasping.<BR>--3 Giving pain, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीडित
आपीडित p. p.<BR>1 Compressed,<BR>bound tightly; embraced &c.<BR>--2<BR>Decorated with chaplets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीत|आपीतं|आपीतः
आपीत a.<BR>1 Yellowish.<BR>--2<BR>Drunk or sipped a little (as<BR>water).<BR>--तः Yellowish colour.<BR>--तं A pyritic mineral (माक्षिकधातु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूपिक|आपूपिकं|आपूपिकः
आपूपिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अपूपठक्]<BR>1 A good maker of अपूप<BR>(cakes).<BR>--2 Accustomed to eat<BR>cakes.<BR>--3 Fond of cakes, eating<BR>cakes (with benefit).<BR>--4 Selling<BR>cakes.<BR>--5 Baking cakes.<BR>--6 Forming<BR>an ingredient of cakes, good for<BR>cakes (as गुड).<BR>--कः A baker;<BR>confectioner.<BR>--कं A multitude of<BR>cakes (अपूपानां समूहः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूप्यः|आपूप्य
आपूप्यः [अपूपाय साधुः वा˚ य] Flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूषं|आपूष
आपूषं A kind of metal<BR>(perhaps tin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्
आपृच् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To fill, pervade,<BR>occupy completely.<BR>--2 To mix<BR>or blend with.<BR>--3 (A.) To satiate<BR>oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्
आपृच् a. [पृच् क्विप्] Connected,<BR>blended. --ind. In a mixed manner,<BR>confusedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपॄ
आपॄ {c9c} U. or Caus. To fill;<BR>R. 16. 65; Bg. 11. 30; Bk. 6. 118;<BR>(fig.) to make full, complete, to<BR>fulfil (wishes); भृत्यैरापूर्यते नृपः<BR>H. 2. 74. --pass. To be filled, to be filled<BR>with wind, be blown (as a conch);<BR>आपूर्यमाणानां स्नानशंखानां K. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर|आपूरः
आपूर a. Becoming full.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>Flow, current, large flood, quantity;<BR>स्वेदापूरो युवति चरितां व्याप गंडस्थलानि<BR>Śi. 7. 74; हर्षभरापूरपीडनोत्फुल्लया दृशा<BR>Ks. 23. 71.<BR>--2 Filling, making full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूरण
आपूरण a. Becoming full.<BR>--णं<BR>Filling, making full; गर्त˚ कृतं Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्ण
आपूर्ण p. p. filled &c.; आपूर्णश्च<BR>कलाभिरिन्दुरमलः Māl. 9. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्तिः|आपूर्ति|आपूर्त्ति|आपूर्त्तिः
आपूर्तिः f.<BR>1 Filling.<BR>--2 Fulness,<BR>satisfaction, satiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपूर्यमाण|आपूर्य्यमाण
आपूर्यमाण a. Becoming full,<BR>being filled; ˚पक्षः the crescent or<BR>waxing moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपेक्षिक
आपेक्षिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अपेक्षाठक्] Raising expectations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोक्लिमं|आपोक्लिम
आपोक्लिमं N. of the 3rd, 6th,<BR>9th, or 12th position; तृतीयं<BR>षष्ठनवमभंत्यं चापोक्लिमं विदुः [cf. Gr. apoklima].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोमय
आपोमय a. (यी f.)<BR>[आपस्-विकारे प्राचुर्ये वा मयट] Consisting of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोमात्रा
आपोमात्रा The subtle elementary<BR>principle of water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपोशानः|आपोशान
आपोशानः N. of a kind of<BR>prayer or formula repeated<BR>before and after eating (the<BR>formulas being respectively अमृतोपस्तरणमसि<BR>स्वाहा and अमृतापिधानमसि स्वाहा);<BR>आपोशानक्रियापूर्वं सत्कृतान्नमकुत्सयन् Y. 1. 31,<BR>106.<BR>--नं The act of making an<BR>उपस्तरण (seat) and अपिधान<BR>(covering) for the food eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त|आप्तः
आप्त, आप्य See आप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्य|आप्यं|आप्यः
आप्त, आप्य See आप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्त्यः|आप्त्य
आप्त्यः Ved. N. of a class of<BR>deities, especially of the deity<BR>Trita as belonging to that class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यै
आप्यै {c1c} A.<BR>1 To grow fat, stout,<BR>or full, become full, increase;<BR>आहुत्य, प्यायते सूर्यः Y. 3. 71.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">Page0246-a+ 57</a>]<BR>To make full, strengthen,<BR>enlarge. --Caus. (-प्याययति)<BR>1 To<BR>make fat, full, or comfortable,<BR>increase, enlarge; तेजसा तव तेजश्च<BR>विष्णुराप्याययिष्यति Mb.; सैव<BR>कांतिर्मन्मथाप्यायिता द्युतिः S. D.;<BR>वायुभिराप्यायितशरीरः Pt. 1; Me. 44; Ms. 9. 314.<BR>--2<BR>To gratify, regale, satisfy, please;<BR>आप्यायितो वचनामृतेन H. 1; K. 124,<BR>Mv. 1, 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0245-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपी
आपी a. Fat, stout.<BR>--पीः f. The<BR>20th Nakṣatra or lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपीन|आपीनं|आपीनः
आपीन p. p. [प्यै-क्त] Stout, fat,<BR>strong.<BR>--नः A well; आपीनोंऽधुः Sk.<BR>--नं An udder, teat;<BR>आपीनभारोद्वहनप्रयत्नात् R. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यान
आप्यान p. p.<BR>1 Fat, stout, robust,<BR>strong; Bk. 5. 56, 9. 2.<BR>--2 Pleased,<BR>satisfied.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Love.<BR>--2 Growth,<BR>increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायः|आप्याय
आप्यायः Becoming full or fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायन|आप्यायनं
आप्यायन a. Causing fulness or<BR>stoutness, promoting welfare.<BR>--नं,<BR>--ना [प्याय्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 The act of<BR>making full or fat.<BR>--2 Satisfying,<BR>refreshing, pleasing.<BR>--3 Satisfaction,<BR>satiety: देवस्याप्यायना भवति Pt. 1.<BR>--4<BR>Advancing, promoting.<BR>--5<BR>Corpulency, growing fat or stout.<BR>--6<BR>Anything which causes corpulency or<BR>good condition.<BR>--7 A<BR>strengthening medicine.<BR>--8 Pouring water on<BR>Soma and thus causing it to swell.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शील a. satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्यायित|आप्यायितः
आप्यायित a.<BR>1 Satisfied, pleased<BR>--2 Improved; grown, increased.<BR>--3 Stout, fat, robust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्र
आप्र a. Ved. [आ-पृ-मूल˚ क]<BR>1<BR>Filling.<BR>--2 Able to reach (Sāy.).<BR>--3 Busy, zealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रच्छ्|आप्रछ्
आप्रच्छ् {c6c} A.<BR>1 To bid adieu,<BR>bid farewell; आपृच्छस्व प्रियसखममुं<BR>तुंगमालिंग्य शैलं Me. 12; R. 8. 49,<BR>12. 103; Māl. 7.; Bk. 14. 63.<BR>--2 To<BR>salute on receiving, but<BR>particularly parting with a visitor (साधो यामि<BR>इति वचनं).<BR>--3 To ask.<BR>--4 To extol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छा
आपृच्छा [प्रच्छ्-अङ्]<BR>1<BR>Conversation.<BR>--2 Bidding farewell.<BR>--3<BR>Curiosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आपृच्छ्य|आपृछ्य
आपृच्छ्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be saluted,<BR>welcomed or honoured.<BR>--2<BR>Praiseworthy, commendable.<BR>--3 Beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रच्छनं|आप्रच्छन
आप्रच्छनं<BR>1 Bidding adieu, taking<BR>leave at the time of departure.<BR>--2<BR>Welcoming, hailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रच्छन्न|आप्रच्छन्नं
आप्रच्छन्न a. Secret, hidden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रदिवं
आप्रदिवं ind. For ever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदं|आप्रपद
आप्रपदं [प्रपदं पदाग्रं तत्पर्यंतं अव्ययी˚]<BR>A dress reaching to the feet. --ind.<BR>To the end of the foot, reaching to<BR>the feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रपदीन|आप्रपदीनं
आप्रपदीन^1 a. [आप्रपदं व्याप्नोति ख]<BR>Reaching to the feet (as dress);<BR>K. 130; (आप्रपदीनकं also).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्री
आप्री f. [आप्रीणात्यनया<BR>आ-प्री-डगौरा˚ ङीष्] Ved.<BR>1 Conciliation,<BR>propitiation, gaining one's favour.<BR>--2<BR>(pl.) ‘Propitiatory verses’, a name<BR>given to certain invocations<BR>addressed to several deified objects in<BR>consecutive order, and said to be<BR>introductory to the animal sacrifice;<BR>some take the Āprīs to represent<BR>the objects themselves, the verses<BR>being consequently called Āprī<BR>verses. The objects invoked are<BR>12:--Susamiddha, Tanūnapāt,<BR>Narāśaṃsa, the divine being bearing<BR>invocations to the gods, Barhis, the<BR>doors of the sacrificial chamber, night<BR>and dawn, the two divine beings<BR>protecting the sacrifice, the three<BR>goddesses Ilā, Sarasvatī, and Mahī,<BR>Tvaṣṭṛ, Vanaspati and Svāhā,<BR>(all these being regarded by Sāyaṇa<BR>to be different forms of Agni);<BR>स एता आप्रीरपश्यत्ताभिर्वैस मुखत<BR>आत्मानमाप्रीणीत; cf. also Max Müller's<BR>Hist. Anc. Lit. pp. 463-466.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रीतपः|आप्रीतप
आप्रीतपः, --पाः N. of Viṣṇu<BR>(protecting those who have appeased<BR>his anger).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्रीतपा
आप्रीतपः, --पाः N. of Viṣṇu<BR>(protecting those who have appeased<BR>his anger).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लु
आप्लु {c1c} A.<BR>1 To jump up, dance,<BR>spring; आप्लुत्य पदान्यष्टौ Mb.; (रथं)<BR>आपुप्लुवे सिंह इवाचलाग्रं.<BR>--2 To bathe,<BR>wash, immerse oneself (fig. also);<BR>प्रयागे आप्लुत्य गात्राणि Mb.;<BR>आप्लुत्याकाशगंगायां ibid.; Ms. 7. 216, 11. 203.<BR>--Caus. (प्लावयति)<BR>1 To cause to be<BR>washed or bathed; आप्लावयत गात्राणि<BR>Mb.<BR>--2 To wash, wet, sprinkle;<BR>अन्नमाप्लाव्य वारिणा Ms. 3. 244,<BR>11. 98.<BR>--3 To overflow, overwhelm,<BR>inundate, flood over.<BR>--4 To set in<BR>commotion.<BR>--5 (Atm.) To bathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवः|आप्लव
आप्लवः, --प्लवनं<BR>1 Bathing,<BR>immersing.<BR>--2 Sprinkling with water (on<BR>all sides).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--व्रतिन् or<BR>आप्लुतव्रतिन् m. a house-holder who has<BR>passed through the first order (<BR>ब्रह्मचर्य) and is admitted into the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">Page0246-c+ 56</a>]<BR>second (गार्हस्थ्य), an initiated<BR>householder; cf. स्नातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लवनं|आप्लवन
आप्लवः, --प्लवनं<BR>1 Bathing,<BR>immersing.<BR>--2 Sprinkling with water (on<BR>all sides).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--व्रतिन् or<BR>आप्लुतव्रतिन् m. a house-holder who has<BR>passed through the first order (<BR>ब्रह्मचर्य) and is admitted into the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">Page0246-c+ 56</a>]<BR>second (गार्हस्थ्य), an initiated<BR>householder; cf. स्नातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लावः|आप्लाव
आप्लावः<BR>1 Bathing, immersing.<BR>--2<BR>Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>--3<BR>Submerging.<BR>--4 A flood, an inundation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्लुत|आप्लुतः
आप्लुत p. p.<BR>1 Bathed; अवभृथाप्लुतो<BR>मुनिः R. 11. 31; Ku. 6. 5.<BR>--2<BR>Wetted, sprinkled; R. 17. 37.<BR>--3<BR>Overflowing with, filled or overcome<BR>with; बाष्प, ˚व्यसन˚, रुधिर˚ &c.<BR>--तः,<BR>˚व्रती An initiated house-holder, see<BR>आप्लवव्रतिन्.<BR>--तं Bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्वन्
आप्वन् m. [आप्-वन् Uṇ. 1. 152]<BR>Wind, air (आप्वः according to Ujjval.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आप्वा
आप्वा The neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आफूकं|आफूक
आफूकं Opium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबंध्|आबन्ध्
आबंध् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To bind, fasten,<BR>tie on, place, fix; क्व समाधानमाबध्नातु<BR>अवष्टंभः K. 290; न क्वचिन्निर्भरमाबध्नाति<BR>पदं 104 places; तेऽपि पोषिताः पोषितरि<BR>स्नेहमाबध्नंति 289.<BR>--2 To make, form;<BR>आबद्धांजलिः, see आबद्ध below.<BR>--3<BR>To hold fast, cling to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबद्ध|आबद्धः
आबद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Bound, tied.<BR>--2<BR>Fixed; स्यंदनाबद्धदृष्टिषु R. 1. 40.<BR>--3<BR>Formed, made; आबद्धमंडला<BR>तापसपरिषद् K. 49 sitting in a circle;<BR>आबद्धरेखमभितो रविमंजरीभिः Gīt. 11;<BR>Bk. 3. 30; Ki. 5. 33.<BR>--4 Obtained.<BR>--5<BR>Hindered.<BR>--द्धं (द्धः also)<BR>1<BR>Binding, joining.<BR>--2 A yoke.<BR>--3<BR>Ornament.<BR>--4 Affection.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--माल<BR>a. forming a wreath, arranged in a<BR>row; Me. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबधः|आबध
आबधः Ved. Binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबंधः|आबन्ध|आबन्धः
आबंधः, --धनं<BR>1 A tie or bond (fig.<BR>also); प्रेमाबंधविवार्धित Ratn. 3. 18;<BR>Amaru. 38.<BR>--2 The tie of a yoke, or<BR>that which fastens the ox to the<BR>yoke, or the yoke to the plough.<BR>--3 Ornament, decoration.<BR>--4<BR>Affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबंधनं|आबन्धन
आबंधः, --धनं<BR>1 A tie or bond (fig.<BR>also); प्रेमाबंधविवार्धित Ratn. 3. 18;<BR>Amaru. 38.<BR>--2 The tie of a yoke, or<BR>that which fastens the ox to the<BR>yoke, or the yoke to the plough.<BR>--3 Ornament, decoration.<BR>--4<BR>Affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्ह|आबर्हः
आबर्ह a. Having the power of<BR>tearing or pulling out.<BR>--र्हः, --र्हणं<BR>[-आ-बर्ह- हिंसायां घञ् ल्युट् वा]<BR>1<BR>Tearing or pulling out.<BR>--2 Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्हिन्
आबर्हिन् a. [आबर्ह्-इनि] Fit for<BR>tearing out; मूलमस्याबर्हि<BR>P. IV. 4. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबल्यं|आबल्य
आबल्यं [अबलस्य भावः] Weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाध्
आबाध् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To check, rein<BR>in, restrain.<BR>--2 To interrupt,<BR>obstruct.<BR>--3 To annoy, harass, attack,<BR>molest, injure.<BR>--4 To set forth or<BR>declare wrongly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाधः|आबाध
आबाधः<BR>1 Affliction, injury,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">Page0247-a+ 55</a>]<BR>trouble, molestation, damage; न<BR>प्राणाबाधमाचरेत् Ms. 4. 54, 51.<BR>--2<BR>Interruption, hinderance.<BR>--3 Attack<BR>(Ved.).<BR>--धा<BR>1 Pain, distress.<BR>--2<BR>Mental agony or anguish.<BR>--3<BR>Segment of the base of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0246-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबाल्यं|आबाल्य
आबाल्यं Age ending with<BR>childhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबिल|आबिलः
आबिल a.<BR>1 Turbid, dirty (=<BR>आविल q. v.).<BR>--2 Clearing, breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबुत्त|आबुत्तः
आबुत्त = आवुत्त q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबुध्
आबुध् {c1c} P. To perceive, notice,<BR>understand (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबोधनं|आबोधन
आबोधनं<BR>1 Knowledge,<BR>understanding.<BR>--2 Instructing, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आब्द
आब्द a. (ब्दी f.) [अब्द-अण्]<BR>Belonging to, or produced from, a<BR>cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आब्दिक
आब्दिक a. (की f.) [अब्द-ठक्]<BR>Annual, yearly; आब्दिकः करः<BR>Ms. 7. 129, 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभगः|आभग
आभगः Ved. A partner (of any<BR>thing); to be shared in (Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरणं|आभरण
आभरणं See under आभृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभा
आभा {c2c} P.<BR>1 To shine, blaze;<BR>सुतरां रत्नमाभाति चामीकरनियोजितं<BR>Subhāṣ.; R. 3. 33.<BR>--2 To appear, look<BR>like; आभासि तीर्थप्रतिपादितर्द्धिः<BR>R. 5. 15, 70, 13. 14; Bk. 7. 8, 66.<BR>--3 To<BR>outshine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभा
आभा [भा-अङ्]<BR>1 Light,<BR>splendour, lustre; दीपाभां शलभा यथा<BR>Pt. 4.<BR>--2 Colour, appearance, beauty;<BR>प्रशांतमिव शुद्धाभं Ms. 12. 27.<BR>--3<BR>Likeness, resemblance; oft. at the end of<BR>comp. in these two senses; रुक्माभं<BR>appearnig or shining like gold;<BR>यमदूताभं Pt. 1. 58; मरुत्सखाभं R. 2. 10.<BR>--4 A<BR>reflected image, shadow, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभातिः|आभाति
आभातिः f. [आ-भा-क्तिच्]<BR>1<BR>Reflection.<BR>--2 Splendour, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाणकः|आभाणक
आभाणकः A popular saying,<BR>proverb; तथा च लौकिकानामाभाणकः<BR>as the proverb goes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष्
आभाष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To address,<BR>speak to, converse with;<BR>वैशंपायनश्चंद्रापीडमाबभाषे K. 117; कुरुते<BR>नालापमाभाषिता Nāg. 4.<BR>--2 To say or speak<BR>(something) (with two acc.);<BR>आभाषि रामेण वचः कनीयान् Bk. 3. 51.<BR>--3<BR>To say or speak; सखी वेत्रभृदाबभाषे<BR>R. 6. 82, 14. 44.<BR>--4 To name.<BR>--5 To<BR>talk aloud, shout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाषः|आभाष
आभाषः [भाष्-घञ्]<BR>1 Addressing.<BR>--2<BR>An introduction, preface.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाषणं|आभाषण
आभाषणं<BR>1 Addressing, speaking<BR>to (संबोधन).<BR>--2 Conversation;<BR>संबंधमाभाषणपूर्वमाहुः R. 2. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभाष्य
आभाष्य pot. p. To be<BR>addressed, worthy of being spoken to;<BR>जनमाभाष्यमिमं न मन्यसे R. 8. 48.<BR>--ष्यं<BR>What is to be said by way of<BR>address; Me. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्
आभास् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To shine, blaze.<BR>--2 To be bright.<BR>--3 To appear,<BR>seem, look like; स्थानांतरं स्वर्ग<BR>इवाबभासे Ku. 7. 3; R. 7. 43, 63;<BR>14. 12.<BR>--4 To appear untruly,<BR>have an appearance; शुक्तिः<BR>रजतवदाभासते; Ki. 17. 21. --Caus. To<BR>illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्
आभास् f. Splendour, lustre, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासः|आभास
आभासः [भास्-अच्]<BR>1 Splendour,<BR>light, lustre.<BR>--2 A reflection;<BR>तत्राज्ञानं धिया नश्येदाभासात्तु घटः स्फुरेत्<BR>Vedānta.<BR>--3 (a) Resemblance,<BR>likeness; oft. at the end of comp.;<BR>नभश्च रुधिराभासं Rām. &c.; चिदाभास,<BR>(b) Semblance, phantom;<BR>युक्तिवाक्यतदाभाससमाश्रयाः S.B.; तत्साहसाभासं<BR>Māl. 2 looks like wantonness.<BR>--4<BR>Any unreal or fallacious appearance<BR>(as in हेत्वाभास); पुनरुक्तवदाभासः S. D.<BR>--5 A fallacy, fallacious<BR>reasoning, semblance of a reason, an<BR>erroneous but plausible argument;<BR>see हेत्वाभास; S. D. 270.<BR>--6 An<BR>intention, purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासनं|आभासन
आभासनं Making apparent or<BR>clear; illuminating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभासुर|आभासुरः
आभासु(स्व)र a. Splendid,<BR>bright, shining.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A collective<BR>name of 64 demigods.<BR>--2 N. of an<BR>attendant Gaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभास्वर|आभास्वरः
आभासु(स्व)र a. Splendid,<BR>bright, shining.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A collective<BR>name of 64 demigods.<BR>--2 N. of an<BR>attendant Gaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिचरणिक
आभिचरणिक, आभिचारिक a.<BR>(की f.) [अभिचरण-चार-ठञ्]<BR>1<BR>Magical.<BR>--2 Imprecatory, maledictory.<BR>--कं A spell or incantation, magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिचारिक
आभिचरणिक, आभिचारिक a.<BR>(की f.) [अभिचरण-चार-ठञ्]<BR>1<BR>Magical.<BR>--2 Imprecatory, maledictory.<BR>--कं A spell or incantation, magic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजन|आभिजनः
आभिजन a. (नी f.) [अभिजन-अण्]<BR>Relating to birth (अभिजन),<BR>patronymic (as a name); तां<BR>पार्वतीत्याभिजनेन नाम्ना Ku. 1. 26.<BR>--नं<BR>Nobility or loftiness of birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजात्यं|आभिजात्य
आभिजात्यं [अभिजातस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Nobility of birth; ˚शंसिनी च<BR>नम्रता Dk. 137; Ratn. 3. 18;<BR>Mv. 2. 18.<BR>--2 Rank.<BR>--3 Learning.<BR>--4 Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिजित
आभिजित a. [अभिजिति नक्षत्रे जातः<BR>अण्] Born under the constellation<BR>Abhijit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधा
आभिधा [अभिधैव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>1 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">Page0247-c+ 55</a>]<BR>sound, word.<BR>--2 A name;<BR>mentioning; see अभिधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानिक|आभिधानिकः
आभिधानिक a. (की f.)<BR>Contained in a dictionary.<BR>--कः A<BR>lexicographer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिधानीयक
आभिधानीयक a. Relating to a<BR>word or name.<BR>--कं The property<BR>of a name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिप्लविक
आभिप्लविक a. (की f.) [<BR>अभिप्लव-ढक्] Relating to the religious<BR>ceremony called अभिप्लव q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिमुख्यं|आभिमुख्य
आभिमुख्यं [अभिमुखस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Direction towards; ˚ख्यं याति<BR>goes to meet or encounter.<BR>--2<BR>Being in front of or face to face;<BR>नीताभिमुख्यं पुनः Ratn. 1. 2.<BR>--3<BR>Favourableness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिरामिक
आभिरामिक a. (की f.) Good,<BR>agreeable; Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिरूपकं|आभिरूपक
आभिरूपकं, आभिरूप्यं [<BR>अभिरूपवुञ् ष्यञ् च] Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिरूप्यं|आभिरूप्य
आभिरूपकं, आभिरूप्यं [<BR>अभिरूपवुञ् ष्यञ् च] Beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिषेचनिक
आभिषेचनिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अभिषेचन-ठञ्] Relating to the<BR>inauguration of a king; आभिषेचनिकं यत्ते<BR>रामार्थमुपकल्पितं Rām.; Mv. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभिहारिक
आभिहारिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अभिहार-ठञ्]<BR>1 To be offered as a<BR>present.<BR>--2 Taken by force, or fraud.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A present.<BR>--2 A room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीकं|आभीक
आभीकं [आभीकेन दृष्टं साम अण्] N.<BR>of a Sāma melody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीक्ष्ण्यं|आभीक्ष्ण्य
आभीक्ष्ण्यं [अभीक्ष्णस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>Continued repetition; बहुलमाभीक्ष्ण्ये<BR>P. III. 2. 81, 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीय
आभीय a. Contained in a<BR>chapter of Pāṇini which ends with<BR>bha (भ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभीरः|आभीर
आभीरः [आ समंतात् भियं राति, रा-क<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 A cowherd;<BR>आभीरवामनयनाहृतमानसाय दत्तं मनो यदुपते तदिदं गृहाण Udb.;<BR>according to Ms. 10. 15 आभीर is<BR>the offspring of a Brāhmaṇa and a<BR>female of the Ambaṣṭha tribe.<BR>--2<BR>(pl.) N. of a country or its<BR>inhabitants; श्रीकोंकणादयोभागे तापीतः पश्चिमे<BR>तटे । आभीरदेशो देवेशि विंध्यशैले व्यवस्थितः ॥.<BR>--री<BR>1 A cowherd's wife.<BR>--2 A<BR>woman of the Ābhīra tribe.<BR>--3 The<BR>language of the Ābhīras; आभीरेषु<BR>तथाभीरी (प्रयोक्तव्या) S. D. 432.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पल्लिः, --ल्ली f.,<BR>--पल्लिका a<BR>station or abode of herdsmen, a<BR>village inhabited by cowherds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभील|आभीलं|आभीलः
आभील a. [आभियं लाति ददाति<BR>लाक]<BR>1 Fearful, terrible; Śi. 18. 78.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">Page0248-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 Suffering from.<BR>--लं Injury,<BR>physical pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0247-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभु
आभु a. [आ-भू-डु] Pervading,<BR>reaching (Sāy.); empty; stingy,<BR>empty-handed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूक
आभूक a. Ved. Empty, powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभुग्न
आभुग्न a. A little curved or<BR>bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभू
आभू {c1c} P. Ved. To be present,<BR>continue one's existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभू
आभू a. Ved.<BR>1 Approaching(as a<BR>praiser.)<BR>--2 Strong, sufficient,<BR>efficacious.<BR>--3 Applied according to<BR>rule (as a hymn).<BR>--4 Very<BR>prosperous. --m. A prison, a place of<BR>confinement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूतिः|आभूति
आभूतिः f.<BR>1 Pervasion.<BR>--2<BR>Overpowering strength.<BR>--3 Capability,<BR>efficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभूषेण्य
आभूषेण्य a. Ved. Praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभृ
आभृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring; आ नो अग्ने<BR>रयिं भर Rv. 1. 79. 8; कदपत्याभृत<BR>दुःखं Bhāg.<BR>--2 To carry.<BR>--3 To fill,<BR>fill with.<BR>--4 To bear, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरणं|आभरण
आभरणं<BR>1 An ornament,<BR>decoration (fig. also);<BR>किमित्यपास्याभरणानि यौवने धृतं त्वया वार्द्धकशांभि वल्कलं<BR>Ku. 5. 44; प्रशमाभरणं पराक्रमः<BR>Ki. 2. 32. (आभरण occurs in the names of<BR>works; e. g. सरस्वतीकंठाभरण).<BR>--2 The<BR>act of nourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभरित
आभरित p. p.<BR>1 Filled.<BR>--2<BR>Decorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभेरी
आभेरी One of the modes of<BR>music (रागिणी) personified as a<BR>female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोगः|आभोग
आभोगः [आ-भुज्-घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Curving, winding.<BR>--2 A curve;<BR>आभोगकुटिला (गङ्गा) Mb.; crumpling.<BR>--3<BR>Circuit, circumference, expanse,<BR>extension, precincts, environs;<BR>अकथितोऽपि ज्ञायत एव<BR>यथायमामोगरतपोवनस्येति Ś. 1; गगनाभोगः the expanse<BR>of heaven, wide firmament of the<BR>sky; Bh. 3. 57; Mv. 6. 30;<BR>Māl. 9. 16.<BR>--4 Magnitude, fulness, extent.<BR>expansive form; गंडाभोगात् Me. 92<BR>from the broad cheek; प्रतिरवाभोग<BR>Māl. 3. 8, 4. 10, 5. 11; प्रतिभयाभोगैः प्लवंगाधिपैः<BR>Mv. 6. 24 bodily form or stature;<BR>U. 2, 2. 14; भवाभोगोद्विग्नाः<BR>Bh. 3. 42, 86; Mv. 2; K. 305, 333.<BR>--5<BR>Effort.<BR>--6 The expanded hood of<BR>a cobra (used by Varuṇa as his<BR>umbrella).<BR>--7 Enjoyment, satiety,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">Page0248-b+ 55</a>]<BR>completion; विषयाभोगेषु नैवादरः<BR>Śāntilakṣaṇa.<BR>--8 A serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोगय
आभोगय a. [आभोगं याति या-क]<BR>To be enjoyed (as Soma juice).<BR>--यं<BR>Livelihood (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभोगिः|आभोगि
आभोगिः Ved.<BR>1 Enjoyment.<BR>--2<BR>Living, supporting life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यंतर|आभ्यन्तर|आभ्यन्तरः
आभ्यंतर a. (री f.) [अभ्यंतरे भवः<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Interior, inner, inward;<BR>as आभ्यंतरो भृत्यवर्ग.<BR>--2 One<BR>of the two kinds of प्रयत्न or effort<BR>giving rise to the vocal sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यवकाशिक
आभ्यवकाशिक a. (की f.)<BR>Living in the open air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यवहारिक
आभ्यवहारिक a. (की f.) [अभ्यवहाराय<BR>हितं ठक्] Eatable (as food &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यादायिकं|आभ्यादायिक
आभ्यादायिकं [अभ्यादान-ठक्] A<BR>kind of स्त्रीधन or woman's property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्यासिक
आभ्यासिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अभ्यासठक्]<BR>1 Resulting from practice.<BR>--2<BR>Practising, repeating.<BR>--3 Being near,<BR>neighbouring, adjoining (आभ्याशिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्युदयिक|आभ्युदयिकं
आभ्युदयिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अभ्युदयठक्]<BR>1 Tending to good, granting<BR>prosperity; अनाभ्यदयिकं श्रमणकदर्शनं<BR>Mk. 8.<BR>--2 Relating to the rise or<BR>beginning of anything; सुख˚<BR>Ms. 12. 88.<BR>--3 High, exalted, important.<BR>--कं A Śrāddha or offering to<BR>ancestors; an occasion of rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आभ्रिक
आभ्रिक^1 a. (की f.) [अभ्र्या खनति<BR>ठक्] One who digs with a spade.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्
आम् ind. An interjection of(a)<BR>assent, acceptance, ‘oh’, ‘yes’; आं कुर्मः<BR>M. 1; (b) recollection; आं<BR>तस्मिन्नुर्वश्या वचनं स्खलितमासीत् V. 3; आं<BR>ज्ञातम् Ś. 3, Oh, I see it now; M. 3;<BR>(c) determination, ‘surely,’ ‘verily’,<BR>आं चिरस्य खलु प्रतिबुद्धोस्मि; (d) reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम|आमं|आमः
आम a. [आम्यते ईषत् पच्यते; आ-अम<BR>कर्मणि घञ् Tv.]<BR>1 Raw, uncooked,<BR>undressed (opp. पक्व) (oft. applied to<BR>the cow in the Veda); आमान्नं<BR>Ms. 4. 223; Y. 1. 287.<BR>--2 Unripe,<BR>immature.<BR>--3 Unbaked, unannealed<BR>(as a jar).<BR>--4 Undigested.<BR>--मं<BR>1 State<BR>of being raw.<BR>--2 Constipation,<BR>passing hard excretion.<BR>--3 Grain freed<BR>from chaff.<BR>--मः<BR>1 Disease; sickness.<BR>--2 Indigestion; आहारस्य रसः सारः यो<BR>न पक्वोऽग्निलाधवात् । आमसज्ञां स लभते<BR>महाव्याधिसमाश्रयः ॥ Suśr.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिसारः dysentery or diarrhœa caused<BR>by vitiated mucus in the abdomen<BR>(the excretion being in this case<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">Page0248-c+ 56</a>]<BR>mixed with hard and fetid matter).<BR>--अद् a. eating raw flesh or food.<BR>--अन्नं undressed rice.<BR>--आशयः [<BR>आमस्यापक्वान्नस्याशयः] ‘receptacle of<BR>undigested food’, the upper part of<BR>the belly to the navel, stomach.<BR>--कुंभः a jar of unbaked clay;<BR>H. 4. 66.<BR>--गंधि n. smelling of raw meat<BR>or of a burning corpse.<BR>--गंधिकं<BR>the smell of raw meat.<BR>--ज्वरः<BR>a kind of fever; cf. रवेद्यमानज्वरं<BR>प्राज्ञः कोंऽभसा परिषिंचति Śi. 2. 54.<BR>--त्वच् a. of tender skin.<BR>--पाकः a<BR>preliminary stage of the disease<BR>called dropsy.<BR>--पात्रं an unannealed<BR>vessel; विनाशंव्रजति<BR>क्षिप्रमामपात्रमिवांभसि Ms. 3. 179.<BR>--पीनसं running at<BR>the nose, defluxion.<BR>--मांसाशिन् m. a<BR>cannibal, an eater of raw flesh.<BR>--रक्तं dysentery.<BR>--रसः imperfect<BR>chyme.<BR>--वातः constipation, torpor<BR>of the bowels attended with<BR>flatulence and intumescence.<BR>--शूलः pain<BR>of indigestion, colic.<BR>--श्राद्धं a<BR>Śrāddhaperformed with uncooked food;<BR>आपद्यनग्नौ तीर्थे च चंद्रसूर्यग्रहे तथा । आमश्राद्धं<BR>द्विजैः कार्यं शूद्रेण च सदैव हि ॥ Prācetasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमक
आमक a. Raw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमता
आमता, --त्वं Rawness, unreadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमत्वं
आमता, --त्वं Rawness, unreadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंजु
आमंजु a. Lovely, charming;<BR>U. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंडः|आमण्ड|आमण्डः
आमंडः The castor-oil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमनं|आमन
आमनं Ved. Friendly disposition<BR>or inclination, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमनस्यं|आमनस्य
आम(मा)नस्यं [अमनस्-ष्यञ्]<BR>Pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमानस्यं|आमानस्य
आम(मा)नस्यं [अमनस्-ष्यञ्]<BR>Pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंत्र्|आमन्त्र्
आमंत्र् {c10c} A.<BR>1 To bid<BR>farewell, bid adieu; आमंत्रयस्व सहचरं<BR>Ś. 3; लताभगिनीं Ś. 4; Ku. 6. 94;<BR>K. 223.<BR>--2 To speak to, call<BR>out to, address, converse with;<BR>तमामंत्रयांबभूव K. 81, 197, Ve. 1;<BR>A. R. 3.<BR>--3 To say, speak;<BR>परिजनोप्येवमामंत्रयते K. 195.<BR>--4 To call, invite, ask<BR>(to come); आमंत्रयध्वं राष्ट्रेषु ब्राह्मणान्<BR>Mb.<BR>--5 To invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंत्रणं|आमन्त्रण|आमन्त्रणं
आमंत्रणं --णा<BR>1 Addressing, calling,<BR>calling out to अबेति वै योषाया आमंत्रणं<BR>Śat. Br.<BR>--2 Bidding adieu, taking<BR>leave of.<BR>--3 Greeting, welcome,<BR>courtesy.<BR>--4 Invitation;<BR>अनिंद्यामंत्रणादृते Y. 1. 112.<BR>--5 Permission.<BR>--6<BR>Conversation. अत्योन्यामंत्रणं<BR>यत्स्याज्जनांते तज्जनांतिकं S. D. 6.<BR>--7 The<BR>vocative case.<BR>--8 Deliberation;<BR>asking; interrogation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंत्रणा
आमंत्रणं --णा<BR>1 Addressing, calling,<BR>calling out to अबेति वै योषाया आमंत्रणं<BR>Śat. Br.<BR>--2 Bidding adieu, taking<BR>leave of.<BR>--3 Greeting, welcome,<BR>courtesy.<BR>--4 Invitation;<BR>अनिंद्यामंत्रणादृते Y. 1. 112.<BR>--5 Permission.<BR>--6<BR>Conversation. अत्योन्यामंत्रणं<BR>यत्स्याज्जनांते तज्जनांतिकं S. D. 6.<BR>--7 The<BR>vocative case.<BR>--8 Deliberation;<BR>asking; interrogation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0248-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंत्रयितृ|आमन्त्रयितृ
आमंत्रयितृ a. Asking, inviting,<BR>calling &c. --m.<BR>--(ता) An inviter,<BR>entertainer, especially of<BR>Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंत्रित|आमन्त्रित
आमंत्रित p. p.<BR>1 Invited, called.<BR>--2 Appointed to do unnecessary<BR>things.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Addressing.<BR>--2 Talk,<BR>conversation; V. 2.<BR>--3 The<BR>vocative case; संबोधने या प्रथमा सामंत्रितसंज्ञा<BR>स्यात् Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंत्र्य|आमन्त्र्य
आमंत्र्य pot. p. To be addressed<BR>or called to, to be invited &c.<BR>--त्र्यं<BR>A word in the vocative case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंत्रः|आमन्त्र|आमन्त्रः
आमंत्रः Castor-oil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमंद्र|आमन्द्र|आमन्द्रः
आमंद्र a. Having a slightly<BR>deep tone, uttering a low,<BR>muttering sound, rambling; आमंद्राणा फल<BR>मविकलं लप्स्यसे गर्जितानां Me. 34.<BR>--द्रः<BR>A slightly deep tone, rumbling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयः|आमय|आमयं
आमयः [आ-मी करणे अच्; Tv.; said<BR>to be fr. अम् also]<BR>1 Disease,<BR>sickness, distemper; दर्पामयः<BR>Mv. 4. 22; आमयस्तु रतिरागसंभवः<BR>R. 19. 48; समौ हि शिष्टिराम्नातौ वजर्यंतावामयः<BR>स च । Śi. 2. 10.<BR>--2 Damage,<BR>hurt.<BR>--3 Indigestion.<BR>--यं N. of<BR>the medical plant Costus<BR>Speciosus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमयाविन्
आमयाविन् a. [आमय-विन्-निपातः<BR>P. V. 2. 122 Vāit.] Sick, dyspeptic,<BR>affected with indigestion; ˚पित्वं<BR>indigestion, dyspepsia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणांत|आमरणान्त
आमरणांत, --तिक a. (की f.)<BR>Lasting till death, lasting for life;<BR>आमरणाताः प्रणयाः कोपास्तत्क्षणभंगुराः<BR>H. 1. 118; अन्योन्यस्याव्यभीचारो<BR>भवेदामरणांतिकः Ms. 9. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरणांतिक|आमरणान्तिक
आमरणांत, --तिक a. (की f.)<BR>Lasting till death, lasting for life;<BR>आमरणाताः प्रणयाः कोपास्तत्क्षणभंगुराः<BR>H. 1. 118; अन्योन्यस्याव्यभीचारो<BR>भवेदामरणांतिकः Ms. 9. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमरीतृ
आमरीतृ^1 m. Ved. A destroyer.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: AP quote has 'I'; mw72 has short 'i'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्षः|आमर्ष
आमर्षः --र्षणं Anger, wrath,<BR>impatience; see अमर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्षणं|आमर्षण
आमर्षः --र्षणं Anger, wrath,<BR>impatience; see अमर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमलकः|आमलक|आमलकं
आमलकः, --की<BR>1 The tree, Emblic<BR>Myrobalan, Emblica Officinalis<BR>Gærtn (Mar. आंवळा).<BR>--2 N. of<BR>another tree (वासक).<BR>--कं Fruit of<BR>the Emblic Myrobalan;<BR>बदरामलकाम्रदाडिमानां Bv. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमलकी
आमलकः, --की<BR>1 The tree, Emblic<BR>Myrobalan, Emblica Officinalis<BR>Gærtn (Mar. आंवळा).<BR>--2 N. of<BR>another tree (वासक).<BR>--कं Fruit of<BR>the Emblic Myrobalan;<BR>बदरामलकाम्रदाडिमानां Bv. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमहीया
आमहीया f. N. of a particular<BR>Ṛk or verse of the Ṛg-veda; (<BR>Rv. 8. 48. 3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमात्यः|आमात्य
आमात्यः [अमात्य एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>1<BR>A minister, counsellor.<BR>--2 A<BR>general; see अमात्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमानस्यं|आमानस्य
आमानस्यं [अमानस-ष्यञ्] Pain,<BR>sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमावास्य
आमावास्य a. (स्यी f.) [<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">Page0249-b+ 55</a>]<BR>अमावास्या अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to the new<BR>moon or its festival.<BR>--2 Happening<BR>or born at the time of new moon or<BR>conjunction.<BR>--स्यं The new moon<BR>oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्षा
आमिक्षा [आमिष्यते सिच्यते, मिष सक्<BR>Tv.] Curd of milk and whey, a<BR>mixture of boiled and coagulated<BR>milk; तप्ते पयसि दध्यानयति सा<BR>वैश्वदेव्यामिक्षा भवति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्ष्यं|आमिक्ष्य
आमिक्ष्यं, आमिक्षीयं [आमिक्षा यत्-छ]<BR>Curd suitable for the preparation<BR>of Āmikṣā; so आनिक्षीणं in the<BR>same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिक्षीयं|आमिक्षीय
आमिक्ष्यं, आमिक्षीयं [आमिक्षा यत्-छ]<BR>Curd suitable for the preparation<BR>of Āmikṣā; so आनिक्षीणं in the<BR>same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमित्र
आमित्र a. [अमित्र-अण] Inimical;<BR>odious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमित्रिः|आमित्रि
आमित्रिः m. f. The child of an<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिश्र
आमिश्र --श्ल a. Readily mixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिश्ल
आमिश्र --श्ल a. Readily mixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिष्
आमिष् n. [आ-मिष्-क्विप्] Flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषं|आमिष
आमिषं [अम्टिषच् दीर्घश्च Uṇ. 1. 46]<BR>1<BR>{1} Flesh; उपानयत् पिंडमिवामिषरय<BR>R. 2. 59; ययामिषं जले मत्स्यैर्भक्ष्यते श्वापदैर्भुवि ।<BR>आकाशे पक्षिभिश्चैव तथा सर्वत्र वित्तवान्<BR>--2 (Hence fig.) A prey, victim,<BR>object of enjoyment; (राज्यं)<BR>रंध्रान्वेषणदक्षाणां द्विषामामिषतां ययौ<BR>R. 12. 11 fell a prey &c.; Dk. 164.<BR>--3<BR>Food, bait.<BR>--4 A bribe.<BR>--5 Desire, lust;<BR>as in निरपेक्षो निरामिषः Ms. 6. 49.<BR>--6<BR>Enjoyment; pleasing or lovely object.<BR>--7 Form.<BR>--8 A leaf.<BR>--9 The fruit<BR>of the Jambīra tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशिन् a. carnivorous, eating<BR>flesh.<BR>--प्रियः, --भुज् ‘fond of flesh,’ a<BR>kind of bird, heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिस्
आमिस् m. Ved.<BR>1 Raw flesh or<BR>meat.<BR>--2 A dead body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमिषी
आमिषी N. of a plant(जटामांसी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीक्षा
आमीक्षा = आमिक्षा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमील्
आमील् {c1c} P. To close (the eyes);<BR>नेत्रे चामीलयन्नेष Kāv. 2. 11; to shut;<BR>चैतन्यं Mv. 2. 22 benumbing;<BR>धाराकदबरजोवृष्टिषु चामीलयन् K. 303<BR>being absorbed in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीलनं|आमीलन
आमीलनं Shutting or closing of<BR>the eyes; K. 256.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमीवत्|आमीवन्त्
आमीवत् a. Ved. Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुखं|आमुख
आमुखं<BR>1 Commencement.<BR>--2<BR>(In dramas) A prologue, prelude<BR>(प्रस्तावना); every Sanskrit play is<BR>introduced by आमुख. It is thus<BR>defined in S. D. नटी विदूषको वापि<BR>पारिपार्श्वक एव वा । सूत्रधरेण सहिताः संलापं यत्र<BR>कर्वते ॥ चित्रैर्वाक्वैः स्यकार्योत्त्यैः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">Page0249-c+ 56</a>]<BR>प्रस्तुताक्षेपिमिर्मिथः । आमुखं तत्तु विज्ञेयं नाम्ना<BR>प्रस्तावनापि सा ॥ 287.<BR>--खं ind. To the face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुच्
आमुच् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To loosen, let go.<BR>--2 To wear, tie round or fasten; put<BR>on (as a garment &c.); accoutre<BR>with; करोऽयमामुक्तविवाहकौतुकः<BR>Ku. 5. 66, 7. 21; आमुंचतीवाभरणं द्वितीयं<BR>R. 13. 21, 12. 86, 16. 74, 17. 25;<BR>Ki. 11. 15; आमुंचद्वर्म रत्नाढ्यं Bk. 17. 6.<BR>--3 To throw, cast, discharge;<BR>आमोक्ष्यंते त्वयि कटाक्षान् Me. 35.<BR>--4<BR>To throw or cast off, take off, put<BR>aside (as garments &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्त|आमुक्तः
आमुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Loosened, let go,<BR>liberated.<BR>--2 Put on, worn &c., see<BR>above.<BR>--3 Discharged, cast, shot<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुक्तिः|आमुक्ति
आमुक्तिः f.<BR>1 Liberation, being<BR>let loose.<BR>--2 Final beatitude.<BR>--3<BR>Putting on, wearing (clothes,<BR>ornaments &c.).<BR>--क्ति ind. Till final<BR>beatitude is obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोचनं|आमोचन
आमोचनं<BR>1 Loosing, liberating.<BR>--2 Emitting, shedding, letting<BR>forth, discharging.<BR>--3 Putting or<BR>tying on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुर्
आमुर्, --रि a. Ved. Destroying,<BR>hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुरि
आमुर्, --रि a. Ved. Destroying,<BR>hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्मिक
आमुष्मिक a. (की f.) [अमुष्मिन्<BR>परलोके भवः ठक्] Belonging to the<BR>next or other world; आमुष्मिकं श्रेयः<BR>Suśr.; नैवालोच्य गरीयसीरपि<BR>चिरादामुष्प्निकीर्यातनाः S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमुष्यायण|आमुष्यायणः
आमुष्यायण a. or<BR>--णः (णी f.) [<BR>अमुष्य ख्यातस्यापत्यं नडा˚ फक् अलुक्]<BR>Wellborn, a son or descendant of such a<BR>one; i. e. of an illustrious person<BR>or family; आमुष्यायणो वै त्वमसि<BR>Śat. Br.; तदामुष्यायणरय तत्रभवतः<BR>सुगुहीतनाम्नो भट्टगापालस्य पौत्रः Māl. 1;<BR>Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृण
आमृण a. Vulnerable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृद्
आमृद् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To crush by<BR>rubbing.<BR>--2 To crumple.<BR>--3 To press,<BR>squeeze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्दः|आमर्द
आमर्दः<BR>1 Crushing.<BR>--2 Roughly<BR>handling; अर्धपीतस्तनं<BR>मातुरामर्दक्लिष्टकेशरं Ś. 7. 14.<BR>--3 Pressing,<BR>squeezing.<BR>--4 N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्दिन्|आमर्द्दिन्
आमर्दिन् a. Crushing, pressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृश्
आमृश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To touch; handle<BR>(roughly), lay hands upon;<BR>नवातपामृष्टसरोजचारुभिः Ki. 4. 14; (तां)<BR>मुहुरामृशन्मृगधरोऽग्रकरैः Śi. 9. 34;<BR>शरासनज्यां मुहुराममर्श Ku. 3. 64;<BR>K. 163; Dk. 71; Ś. 7. 2.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">Page0250-a+ 56</a>]<BR>(a) To seize upon, eat up; R. 5. 9.<BR>(b) To attack, assail; आमृष्टं नः परैः<BR>पदं Ku. 2. 31.<BR>--3 To rub, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0249-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्शः|आमर्श
आमर्शः, --र्शनं<BR>1 Touching, close<BR>contact.<BR>--2 Rubbing, wiping.<BR>--3<BR>Counsel, advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमर्शनं|आमर्शन
आमर्शः, --र्शनं<BR>1 Touching, close<BR>contact.<BR>--2 Rubbing, wiping.<BR>--3<BR>Counsel, advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमृष्ट
आमृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Touched, attacked,<BR>seized &c.<BR>--2 Sweetened, made<BR>delicious; Pt. 4.<BR>--3 Rubbed, struck<BR>against; Ś. 7. 2.<BR>--4 Wiped, rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमेन्य
आमेन्य a. To be measured from<BR>all sides; to be reached with an<BR>arrow or bolt (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोटनं|आमोटन
आमोटनं Crushing; Māl. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोद|आमोदः
आमोद a. Gladdening, cheering<BR>up, delighting.<BR>--दः<BR>1 Joy, pleasure,<BR>delight; आमोदं परमं जग्मुः Rām.<BR>--2<BR>Fragrance (diffusive), perfume;<BR>आमोदमुपजिघ्रंतौ स्वनिःश्वासानुकारिणं<BR>R. 1. 43; आमोदं कुसुमभवं मृदेव धत्ते मृद्गंधं<BR>न हि कुसुमानि धारयंति Subhāṣ.;<BR>Śi. 2. 20; Me. 31.<BR>--3 Strong smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदन|आमोदनं
आमोदन a. Delighting, pleasing.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Delighting, rejoicing.<BR>--2<BR>Making fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदित|आमोदितः
आमोदित p. p.<BR>1 Pleased,<BR>delighted.<BR>--2 Made fragrant, scented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोदिन्
आमोदिन् a.<BR>1 Happy, delighted.<BR>--2 Fragrant; fragrant or perfumed<BR>with; oft. at the end of comp.;<BR>नवकुटजकदंबामोदिनो गंधवाहाः<BR>Bh. 1. 35. --m.<BR>--(दी) A perfume for the<BR>mouth (made in the form of a pill<BR>of camphor &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोष|आमोषः
आमोष a. Robbing, stealing.<BR>--षः<BR>Theft, robbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोषिन्
आमोषिन् m. A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आमोहनिका
आमोहनिका A kind of fragrant<BR>odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्ना
आम्ना {c1c} P.<BR>1 (a) To hand down<BR>traditionally or in sacred texts;<BR>भवत्प्रणीतमाचारमामनंति हि साधवः<BR>Ku. 6. 31; एवं किल सूत्रकारा आमनंति<BR>Māl. 7. (b) Hence, to regard, consider,<BR>mention, lay down; त्वामामनंति प्रकृतिं<BR>पुरुषार्थप्रवर्तिनीं Ku. 2. 13, 5. 81;<BR>M. 1. 4; Bk. 18. 5; Kām. 8. 24; U. 5;<BR>Mv. 4. 30.<BR>--2 To keep in mind,<BR>commit to memory, learn, study,<BR>repeat; आमनन्मंत्रमुत्तमं Bk. 17. 30; यद्<BR>ब्रह्म सम्यगाम्नातं Ku. 6. 16 learnt.<BR>--3<BR>To celebrate, hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नात
आम्नात p. p.<BR>1 Considered,<BR>regarded, said to be; समौ हि शिष्टैराम्नातौ<BR>वर्त्स्यंतावामयः स (शत्रुः) च Śi. 2. 10.<BR>--2<BR>Studied, repeated.<BR>--3 Remembered,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">Page0250-b+ 56</a>]<BR>kept in mind.<BR>--4 Handed down in<BR>sacred texts or traditionally.<BR>--तं<BR>Study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नातिन्
आम्नातिन् a. [आम्नात-इनि] One who<BR>has studied the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नानं|आम्नान
आम्नानं [आ-म्ना-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Recitation or study of the sacred texts or<BR>Vedas.<BR>--2 Mention; repetition in<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नायः|आम्नाय
आम्नायः [आ-म्ना-घञ्]<BR>1 (a) Sacred<BR>tradition, sacred texts handed down<BR>by tradition or repetition. (b) Hence,<BR>the Veda, Vedas taken collectively<BR>(including Brāhmaṇas, Upaniṣads<BR>and Āraṇyakas also); अधीती<BR>चतुर्ष्वाम्नायेषु Dk. 120; आम्नायवचनं<BR>सत्यमित्ययं लोकसंग्रहः । आम्नायेभ्यः पुनर्वेदाः<BR>प्रसृताः सर्वतोमुखाः ॥ Mb.<BR>--2 A sacred<BR>text or precept in general; U. 4.<BR>--3<BR>Traditional usage, family or<BR>national customs.<BR>--4 Received doctrine.<BR>--5 Advice or instruction (in past<BR>and present usage).<BR>--6 A Tantra.<BR>--7<BR>A series of families.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सारिन्<BR>a. {1} pious, observing the traditional<BR>usages. {2} containing the essence<BR>of the Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्नायवत्
आम्नायवत् a. Attended with, or<BR>learnt by, traditional instruction;<BR>U. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंबरीषपुत्रकः|आम्बरीषपुत्रक|आम्बरीषपुत्रकः
आंबरीषपुत्रकः A country<BR>inhabited by the Ambarīṣaputras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंबष्ठः|आम्बष्ठ|आम्बष्ठः
आंबष्ठः An inhabitant of<BR>Ambaṣṭha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंबिकेयः|आम्बिकेय|आम्बिकेयः
आंबिकेयः [अंबिकाया अपत्यं ढक्]<BR>An epithet of (a) Dhṛtarāṣṭra;<BR>(b) Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंभस|आम्भस
आंभस a. (सी f.) [अंभस्-अण्]<BR>Watery, fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आंभसिक|आम्भसिक|आम्भसिकः
आंभसिक a. (की f.) [अंभसा वर्तते<BR>ठक्] Aquatic.<BR>--कः A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रः|आम्र
आम्रः [अम् गत्यादिषु रन् दीर्घश्च<BR>Uṇ. 2. 16] The mango-tree.<BR>--म्रं The<BR>fruit of the mango-tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवर्तः {1} N. of a tree (आम्रातक). {2}<BR>inspissated mango juice.<BR>--(र्तं) the<BR>fruit of आम्रातक.<BR>--कूटः the name<BR>of a mountain; सानुमानाम्रकूटः Me. 17.<BR>--गंधकः N. of a plant (समष्ठिलवृक्ष).<BR>--पेशी [आम्रस्य पेशीव] a portion of<BR>dried mango-fruit.<BR>--वणं [आम्रस्य वनं<BR>cf. P. VIII. 4. 5] a grove of mango<BR>trees; सोहमाम्रवणं छित्त्वा Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रातः|आम्रात
आम्रातः [आम्रं आम्ररसं अतति<BR>अत्-अच् Tv.] The hog-plum, Spondias<BR>Mangifera (its juice resembling<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">Page0250-c+ 55</a>]<BR>that of the mango).<BR>--तं The fruit<BR>of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रातकः|आम्रातक
आम्रातकः<BR>1 The hog-plum.<BR>--2<BR>Inspissated mango juice (Mar. साट);<BR>आम्रस्य सहकारस्य कटे विस्तारितो रसः ।<BR>घर्मशुष्को मुहुर्दत्त आम्रातक इति स्मृतः ॥<BR>Bhāva P.<BR>--3 N. of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रिमन्
आम्रिमन् m. Acid taste; see Gaṇa<BR>to P. V. 1. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेड्
आम्रेड् Caus. To repeat; एतदेव<BR>यदा वाक्यमाम्रेडयति देवराट् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडनं|आम्रेडन
आम्रेडनं Tautology; repetition of<BR>words or sounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्रेडित|आम्रेडितं
आम्रेडित p. p. Reiterated,<BR>repeated (as words).<BR>--तं<BR>1 Repetition<BR>of sound or word.<BR>--2 (In gram.)<BR>Reduplication, the second word in<BR>reduplication; द्बितीयाम्रेडितांतेषु Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लः|आम्ल
आम्लः, --म्ला The tamarind tree.<BR>--म्लं Sourness, acidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्ला
आम्लः, --म्ला The tamarind tree.<BR>--म्लं Sourness, acidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लिका
आम्लि(म्ली)का<BR>1 The tamarind<BR>tree.<BR>--2 Acidity of stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आम्लीका
आम्लि(म्ली)का<BR>1 The tamarind<BR>tree.<BR>--2 Acidity of stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयः|आय
आयः [आ इ-अच्, अय्-घञ् वा]<BR>1<BR>Arrival, approach.<BR>--2 Gaining or<BR>acquisition of money, acquiring<BR>(opp. व्यय); आये दुःखं व्यये दुःखं<BR>Pt. 1. 163.<BR>--3 Income, revenue, receipt;<BR>ग्रामेषु स्वामिग्राह्यो भाग आयः Sk.;<BR>Y. 1. 322, 326; Mk. 2. 6; आयद्वाराणि<BR>Dk. 162 sources of income;<BR>आयव्ययौ च नियतावाकरान् कोषमेव च<BR>Ms. 8. 419; आयाधिकं व्ययं करोति<BR>he lives beyond his means.<BR>--4<BR>Gain, profit.<BR>--5 The eleventh house<BR>(in astrology).<BR>--6 The guard of<BR>the women's apartments.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--व्ययौ (dual) receipt and<BR>disbursement, income and expenditure.<BR>--स्थानं a place where revenues are<BR>collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्
आयत् a. Ved. Coming,<BR>approaching; ˚वसु one to whom good or<BR>wealth comes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतीगवम्
आयतीगवम् ind. At the time<BR>when cows return home;<BR>प्रक्रांतामायतीगवं Bk. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयनं|आयन
आयनं Ved. Coming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयिन्
आयिन् a. Ved. Coming or driving<BR>near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयःशूलिक|आयःशूलिकः
आयःशूलिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अयःशूलठक् P. V. 2. 76] Active, diligent,<BR>indefatigable.<BR>--कः A man who, in<BR>order to gain an object, uses<BR>forcible instead of gentle means (<BR>तीक्ष्णोपायेन योऽन्विच्छेत्स आयःशूलिको जनः)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">Page0251-a+ 56</a>]<BR>cf. K. P. 10; अयःशूलेन अन्विच्छति<BR>(scil. अर्थान्) इत्यायः शूलिकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0250-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयज्
आयज् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To honour,<BR>worship (the gods).<BR>--2 To give, present,<BR>furnish, supply.<BR>--3 To consecrate,<BR>ordain, dedicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयजि
आयजि a. Ved. Performing<BR>sacrifices from all sides; procuring,<BR>granting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयजिष्ठ
आयजिष्ठ a. Sacrificing or<BR>procuring best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयज्यु
आयज्यु a. Inclined to sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयागः|आयाग
आयागः A gift given at a<BR>sacrifice; ˚भूत a. obtained by sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्
आयत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To strive,<BR>endeavour.<BR>--2 To rest or depend on,<BR>rest with (with loc.); वयं<BR>त्वय्यायतामहे Mv. 1. 49, 3. 34; Dk. 42.<BR>--3 To arrive, come to, reach, dwell<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतनं|आयतन
आयतनं [आयतंतेऽत्र, यत् आधारे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Place, abode, house, resting-place;<BR>(fig. also); शूलायतनाः Mu. 7<BR>hangmen; स्नेहस्तदेकायतनं जगाम<BR>Ku. 7. 5 was centred in her;<BR>R. 3. 36; सर्वाविनयानामेकैकमप्येषामायतनं<BR>K. 103; ˚मृगेण 130 domestic deer;<BR>Chāṇ. 32; (hence) a receptacle,<BR>home, support, seat.<BR>--2 The place<BR>of the sacred fire, altar, shed for<BR>sacrifices.<BR>--3 A sanctuary,<BR>sacred place; as in देवायतनं, मठायतनं<BR>&c.<BR>--4 The site of a house,<BR>groundplot.<BR>--5 A barn.<BR>--6 An inner seat<BR>(with Buddhists who consider the<BR>five senses with manas as the six<BR>Āyatanas).<BR>--7 The cause of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतनत्वं|आयतनत्व
आयतनत्वं State of being an altar<BR>or seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतनवत्|आयतनवन्त्
आयतनवत् a. Having a certain<BR>seat or home. --m. N. of the fourth<BR>foot of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्त|आयत्तः
आयत्त p. p. [आ-यत्-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Dependent on, resting with (with<BR>loc. or in comp.); दैवायत्तं कुले जन्म<BR>मदायत्तं तु पौरुषं Ve. 3. 33;<BR>भाग्यायत्तमतः परं Ś. 4. 16.<BR>--2 Docile,<BR>tractable.<BR>--3 Attempted, tried; ˚ता, त्वं<BR>dependence, humility, docility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत्तिः|आयत्ति
आयत्तिः f. [आ-यत्-क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>Dependence, subjection.<BR>--2 Affection.<BR>--3<BR>Strength, power, might.<BR>--4<BR>Boundary, limit.<BR>--5 An expedient,<BR>remedy.<BR>--6 Majesty, dignity.<BR>--7 A day.<BR>--8 Steadiness of conduct,<BR>continuance in the right path.<BR>--9 Length.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-b" target="_blank">Page0251-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--10 Future time (These two senses<BR>should perhaps be referred to<BR>आयति q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयथातथ्यं|आयथातथ्य
आयथातथ्यं Unfitness,<BR>unsuitableness, impropriety; Śi. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयम्
आयम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To extend,<BR>lengthen out, stretch out;<BR>वस्त्रं-पाणिंआयच्छते Sk.; स्वांगमायच्छमानः<BR>Ś. 4. v. l.; आयच्छति कूपाद्रज्जुं Sk. draws<BR>up; बाणमुद्यतमायसीत् Bk. 6. 119<BR>stretched out.<BR>--2 To restrain, draw in (as<BR>breath &c.); Ms. 3. 217, 11. 100;<BR>Y. 1. 24.<BR>--3 To stretch oneself, to grow<BR>long (Atm.); P. I. 3. 28.<BR>--4 To<BR>grasp, possess; Bk. 8. 46.<BR>--5 To<BR>bring or lead towards. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To lengthen, stretch, spread or<BR>draw out.<BR>--2 To remove, transplant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयत|आयतः
आयत p. p.<BR>1 Long; दशांगुलमायता<BR>यष्टिः a stick ten fingers long;<BR>शतमध्यर्धं (योजनं) आयता Mb.; ˚स्वभावानि<BR>च दुःखानि K. 175 lasting.<BR>--2<BR>Diffuse, prolix.<BR>--3 Big, large, great;<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--4 Drawn, attracted.<BR>--5<BR>Longdrawn, distant.<BR>--6 Curbed,<BR>restrained.<BR>--तः An oblong (in geometry).<BR>--तं ind. Deeply, long; as in आयतं<BR>निश्वस्य.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a. (क्षी f.),<BR>--ईक्षण, --नेत्र, --लोचन a. (a woman)<BR>with large eyes.<BR>--अपांग a. having<BR>long-cornered eyes.<BR>--अर्धः half an<BR>oblong.<BR>--आयतिः f. long<BR>continuance, remote futurity; Śi. 14. 5.<BR>--छदा<BR>a plantain tree.<BR>--लेख a.<BR>long-curved; Ku. 1. 47.<BR>--स्तूः m. [आयतं<BR>स्तौति, नि˚ दीर्घः] a panegyrist, bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतिः|आयति
आयतिः f.<BR>1 Length, extension.<BR>--2 Future time, the future; ˚भंग<BR>K. 55 (length also), 58, Dk. 29;<BR>भूयसी तव यदायतायतिः Śi. 14. 5;<BR>रहयत्यापदुपेतमायतिः Ki. 2. 14;<BR>Ms. 7. 169; अनायति क्षमं वचः Pt. 3. 112<BR>imprudent, not good for the future;<BR>˚ग्लानिभूतः Mu. 4. 12; स्थिर˚ Ki. 1. 23,<BR>permanent.<BR>--3 Future consequence<BR>or result; आयतिं सर्वकार्याणां तदात्वं च<BR>विचारयेत् Ms. 7. 178; Ki. 1. 15,<BR>2. 43, 3. 43; Ki. 4. 21 fruit-yielding<BR>season.<BR>--4 Majesty, dignity.<BR>--5<BR>Stretching the hand, accepting,<BR>obtaining.<BR>--6 Work (कर्मन्); यथा<BR>मित्रं ध्रुवं लब्ध्वा कृशमप्यायतिक्षमं<BR>Ms. 7. 208 (कर्मक्षमं Kull.).<BR>--7 Connection,<BR>junction.<BR>--8 Meeting, union.<BR>--9<BR>Source, descent; तदायतिः Dk. 154<BR>descended from him.<BR>--10 Restraint<BR>(of mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयतिमत्
आयतिमत् a.<BR>1 Long, extended.<BR>--2<BR>Dignified, majestic, stately.<BR>--3<BR>Selfrestrained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयंतृ|आयन्तृ
आयंतृ m. Ved. One who<BR>approaches, one who fastens or raises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयमनं|आयमन
आयमनं<BR>1 Length, extension.<BR>--2<BR>Restraint, curbing.<BR>--3 Stretching<BR>(as a bow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामः|आयाम
आयामः [आ-यम् घञ्]<BR>1 Length;<BR>तिर्यगायामाशोभी Me. 57.<BR>--2<BR>Expansion, extension; Ki. 7. 6.<BR>--3<BR>Stretching, extending.<BR>--4 Restraint,<BR>control, stopping; प्राणायामपरायणाः<BR>Bg. 4. 29; प्राणायामः परं तपः Ms. 2. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामवत्|आयामवन्त्
आयामवत् a. Extended, long;<BR>V. 1. 4; Śi. 12. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामित
आयामित a. Stretched out,<BR>extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयामिन्
आयामिन् a.<BR>1 One who restrains.<BR>--2 Long (in space or time); K. 25,<BR>55; ˚यामासु Ki. 11. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयल्लकः|आयल्लक|आयल्लकं
आयल्लकः Impatience, longing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयवनं|आयवन
आयवनं Ved. A spoon for<BR>stirring or any similar implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयवसः|आयवस|आयवसं
आयवसः, --सं Pasture-ground,<BR>place for feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयवसं|आयवस|आयवसः
आयवसः, --सं Pasture-ground,<BR>place for feeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्
आयस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To exert<BR>oneself; पिंडार्थमायस्यतः Mu. 3. 14.<BR>--2 To<BR>weary oneself, become exhausted or<BR>fatigued; नायस्यसि तपस्यंती Bk. 6. 69,<BR>14. 104, 15. 54. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>trouble, afflict; आयासयति मां<BR>जलाभिलाषः K. 35; Mu. 7. 8; V. 2.<BR>--2<BR>To weary, tire out, worry.<BR>--3 To<BR>injure, affect; lessen, diminish;<BR>Bk. 8. 61.<BR>--4 To string (as a bow);<BR>अनायासितकार्मुकः Pt. 1. 385.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्त|आयस्तः
आयस्त p. p. [यस्-क्त]<BR>1 Pained,<BR>distressed, afflicted.<BR>--2 Hurt,<BR>injured, killed.<BR>--3 Vexed, angry.<BR>--4<BR>Effected with difficulty.<BR>--5 Thrown,<BR>cast, sent forth.<BR>--6 Sharpened,<BR>whetted.<BR>--7 (Actively used) Toiling,<BR>labouring, exerting oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासः|आयास
आयासः [आ-यस्-घञ्]<BR>1 Effort,<BR>exertion, trouble, difficulty, pain,<BR>labour; बहुलायास Bg. 18. 24; cf.<BR>अनायास also.<BR>--2 Fatigue, weariness;<BR>स्नेहमूलानि दुःखानि देहजानि भयानि च ।<BR>शोकहर्षौ तथायासः सर्वं स्नेहात् प्रवर्तते ॥<BR>Mb.<BR>--3 Mental pain, anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासक
आयासक a. [आ-यस्-ण्वुल्] Causing<BR>fatigue, wearisome; troublesome;<BR>Bh. 3. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयासिन्
आयासिन् a. [आ-यस्-णिनि]<BR>1<BR>Exhausted, fatigued.<BR>--2 Making<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">Page0252-a+ 56</a>]<BR>exertions, striving; मनस्तु<BR>तद्भावदर्शनायासि Ś. 2. 1. v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0251-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस|आयसं
आयस a. (सी f.) [अयसो विकारः<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Made of iron, iron, metallic;<BR>आयसं दंडमेव वा Ms. 8. 315; सखि मा<BR>जल्प तवायसी रसज्ञा Bv. 2. 59.<BR>--2<BR>Armed with an iron weapon.<BR>--सी<BR>A coat of mail, an armour for<BR>the body.<BR>--सं<BR>1 Iron; मूढं<BR>बुद्धमिवात्मानं हैमीभूतमिवायसं Ku. 6. 55; स<BR>चकर्ष परस्मात्तदयत्कांत इवायसं<BR>R. 17. 63.<BR>--2 Anything made of iron.<BR>--3 A weapon.<BR>--4 A wind<BR>instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयस्कारः|आयस्कार
आयस्कारः The upper part of the<BR>thigh of an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आया
आया {c2c} P.<BR>1 To come, arrive,<BR>approach.<BR>--2 To reach, attain, go to<BR>(any particular state); क्षयं, वशं, बधंन,<BR>तुलां &c.<BR>--3 To follow, result.<BR>--4 To<BR>be possible or practicable (with<BR>inf.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयात|आयातं
आयात a. Come, approached.<BR>--तं Excess, superabundance (उद्रेक);<BR>Ki. 5. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयातिः|आयाति
आयातिः f. [आ-या-क्तिच्]<BR>Coming near, arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयानं|आयान
आयानं<BR>1 Coming, arrival.<BR>--2<BR>Natural temperament, disposition,<BR>nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयापनं|आयापन
आयापनं Causing to come,<BR>inviting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयाचित
आयाचित a. Urgently<BR>requested or asked for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयु|आयुः
आयु a. [इ-उण् Uṇ. 1. 2] Ved.<BR>Living, going, moveable.<BR>--युः<BR>1 A<BR>living being, man.<BR>--2 Mankind,<BR>human race.<BR>--3 Living beings<BR>taken collectively.<BR>--4 The first<BR>man.<BR>--5 Life, duration of life.<BR>--6<BR>Wind.<BR>--7 A son, descendant,<BR>offspring.<BR>--8 The son of Purūravas<BR>and Urvaśī.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--षक् a.<BR>attached to; joined with men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुज्
आयुज् {c7c} U. or Caus.<BR>1 To join,<BR>fasten or tie, yoke (to anything).<BR>--2 To appoint.<BR>--3 To fix or direct<BR>(the mind) towards;<BR>आयोजितस्तपस्यात्मा K. 173. --Caus.<BR>1 To fix, or<BR>place; Rs. 2. 21.<BR>--2 To make or<BR>form; कुसुमायोजितकार्मुको मधुः<BR>Ku. 4. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुक्त|आयुक्तः
आयुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Appointed, charged<BR>with (with gen. or loc.);<BR>कुशलोऽन्वेषणस्याहमायुक्तो दूतकर्मणि<BR>Bk. 8. 115.<BR>--2 United, joined, obtained.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">Page0252-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--क्तः A minister, an agent or<BR>deputy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोगः|आयोग
आयोगः<BR>1 Appointment, en<BR>trusting one with something.<BR>--2<BR>Action, performance of an act.<BR>--3<BR>Offering flowers, perfumes &c.<BR>--4 A<BR>shore or bank; a quay to which boats<BR>are attached.<BR>--5 Connection, union;<BR>स देशो भ्रमरायोगः प्रदीप इव लक्ष्यते Rām.<BR>--6 Obstruction (रोध).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोजनं|आयोजन
आयोजनं<BR>1 Joining.<BR>--2 Taking.<BR>seizing.<BR>--3 Collecting.<BR>--4 Effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुत
आयुत a.<BR>1 Mixed, mingled.<BR>--2<BR>Melted.<BR>--तं Half-melted butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुध्
आयुध् {c4c} A. To fight with, attack,<BR>oppose. --Caus. To oppose, attack,<BR>fight with; रथिनः पादचारमायोधयंति<BR>U. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधः|आयुध|आयुधं
आयुधः, --धं [आयुध् घञर्थेक]<BR>1 A<BR>weapon, shield &c.; it is of 3 kinds (1)<BR>प्रहरण, e. g. a sword; (2) हस्तमुक्त, e. g.<BR>a disc; (3) यंत्रमुक्त, e. g. an arrow;<BR>न मेत्वदन्येन विसोढनायुधं R. 3. 63.<BR>--2<BR>A vessel (Ved.).<BR>--धं<BR>1 Gold used<BR>for ornaments.<BR>--2 (pl.) Water (Ved.).<BR>--Comp. (--अ) आगारं an armoury,<BR>arsenal; अहमप्यायुधागारं<BR>प्रविश्यायुधसहायो भवामि Ve. 1; Ms. 9. 280<BR>--जीविन् a. living by one's weapon.<BR>(--m.) a warrior, soldier.<BR>--धर्मिणी the<BR>tree called जयंती (रोगनाशने तस्या<BR>आयुधधर्भत्वात्).<BR>--पिशाचिका ‘devil of arms,’<BR>devilish warlike spirit; Mv. 3;<BR>A. R. 4; B. R. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधं|आयुध|आयुधः
आयुधः, --धं [आयुध् घञर्थेक]<BR>1 A<BR>weapon, shield &c.; it is of 3 kinds (1)<BR>प्रहरण, e. g. a sword; (2) हस्तमुक्त, e. g.<BR>a disc; (3) यंत्रमुक्त, e. g. an arrow;<BR>न मेत्वदन्येन विसोढनायुधं R. 3. 63.<BR>--2<BR>A vessel (Ved.).<BR>--धं<BR>1 Gold used<BR>for ornaments.<BR>--2 (pl.) Water (Ved.).<BR>--Comp. (--अ) आगारं an armoury,<BR>arsenal; अहमप्यायुधागारं<BR>प्रविश्यायुधसहायो भवामि Ve. 1; Ms. 9. 280<BR>--जीविन् a. living by one's weapon.<BR>(--m.) a warrior, soldier.<BR>--धर्मिणी the<BR>tree called जयंती (रोगनाशने तस्या<BR>आयुधधर्भत्वात्).<BR>--पिशाचिका ‘devil of arms,’<BR>devilish warlike spirit; Mv. 3;<BR>A. R. 4; B. R. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिक|आयुधिकः
आयुधिक a. Relating to arms.<BR>--कः [आयुधेन जीवति ठञ्] A soldier,<BR>warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधिन्
आयुधिन्, आयुधीय a. [आयुध-इनि-छ]<BR>Bearing or using weapons.<BR>--धी,<BR>--धीयः A warrior; Śi. 18. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुधीय|आयुधीयः
आयुधिन्, आयुधीय a. [आयुध-इनि-छ]<BR>Bearing or using weapons.<BR>--धी,<BR>--धीयः A warrior; Śi. 18. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोधनं|आयोधन
आयोधनं<BR>1 A battle, fight, war;<BR>आयोधने कृष्णगतिं सहायं R. 6. 42;<BR>आयोधनाग्रसरतां त्वयि वीर याते 5. 71.<BR>--2<BR>Battle-field; प्रययौ तूर्णमायोधनं प्रति<BR>Mb.<BR>--3 Slaughter, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुस्
आयुस् n. [इ-असि-णिच्च<BR>Uṇ. 2. 117]<BR>1 Life, duration of life;<BR>दीर्घमायुः R. 9. 62, 12. 48;<BR>तक्षकेणापि दष्टस्य आयुर्मर्माणि रक्षति H. 2. 16;<BR>आयुर्वर्षशतं नृणां परिमितं Bh. 3. 107;<BR>शतायुर्वै पुरुषः Ait. Br.; प्राणो हि<BR>भूतानामायुः । तस्मात्सर्वायुषमुच्यते ।<BR>सर्वमेव त आयुर्यांति T. Up.<BR>--2 Vital<BR>power.<BR>--3 Food.<BR>--4 N. of a ceremony<BR>called आयुष्टोम performed to secure<BR>long life. (In comp. the final स् of<BR>this word is changed to ष् before<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-c" target="_blank">Page0252-c+ 57</a>]<BR>hard consonants, and to र् before<BR>soft ones).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a. (री f.)<BR>promoting long life; K. 351.<BR>--काम<BR>a. wishing for long life or health.<BR>--कृत् a. giving or producing life.<BR>--द्रव्यं {1} a medicament. {2} ghee.<BR>--योगः N. of a योग in astronomy.<BR>--वृद्धिः f. long life, longevity.<BR>--वेदः [आयुरस्मिन् विद्यतेऽनेन वा<BR>आयुर्विदतीत्यायुर्वेदः Suśr.] the science of<BR>health or medicine, counted as a<BR>sacred science, and regarded as<BR>a supplement to the<BR>Atharvaveda; it comprises {8}<BR>different departments; (1) शल्यं surgery;<BR>(2) शालाक्यं diagnosis of diseases<BR>belonging to the head and its organs;<BR>(3) कायचिकित्सा treatment of diseases<BR>of the whole body; (4) भूतविद्या<BR>treatment of diseases of the mind<BR>supposed to be caused by the<BR>influence of evil spirits; (5)<BR>कौमारभृत्यं treatment of children; (6)<BR>अगदतंत्रं doctrine of antidotes; (7)<BR>रसायनतंत्रं doctrine of elixirs; and<BR>(8) वाजीकरणतंत्रं treatment of<BR>remedies to increase generative power.<BR>--वेददृश्, --वेदमय, --वेदिक, --वेदिन् a. {1}<BR>belonging to medicine. {2}<BR>acquainted with medical science, medical.<BR>(--m.) a physician.<BR>--शेषः {1}<BR>remainder of life; ˚शेषतया Pt. 1;<BR>˚जीवित Pt. 4. being destined to live<BR>longer. {2} end or decline of life.<BR>--स्तोमः (आयुष्टोमः) a sacrifice<BR>performed to obtain long life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्मत्|आयुष्मन्त्
आयुष्मत्^1 a. [आयुस् मतुप्]<BR>1 Alive,<BR>living.<BR>--2 Long-lived; आयुष्मंतं सुतं सूते<BR>Ms. 3. 263. (Generally used in<BR>dramas by elderly persons in<BR>addressing a nobly-born person; e. g.<BR>a charioteer addresses a prince as<BR>आयुष्मन्. A Brāhmaṇa is also so<BR>addressed in saluting; cf. Ms. 2. 125;<BR>आयुष्मान् भव सौम्येति वाच्यो विप्रोऽमिवादने).<BR>--3 Lasting.<BR>--4 Old. --m.<BR>1 The third<BR>of the 27 Yogas or divisions of the<BR>ecliptic.<BR>--2 The Yoga star कृत्तिका;<BR>the third lunar mansion.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: lost virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुषं|आयुष
आयुषं (At the end of a few<BR>comps.) Life; e. g. पुरुषायुषजीविन्यः<BR>R. 1. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्कः|आयुष्क
आयुष्कः [आयुः कायते, कै-क Tv.]<BR>1 That which proclaims age or<BR>duration of life.<BR>--2 (With Jainas)<BR>Connection with the body or<BR>person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0252-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयुष्य|आयुष्यं
आयुष्य a. [आयुः प्रयोजनमस्य, यत्]<BR>Promoting long life, vital,<BR>preservative of life; इदं<BR>यशस्यमायुष्यमिदं निःश्रेयसं परं Ms. 1. 106, 3. 106,<BR>4. 13; M. 4. 4 v. l.; Dk. 158.<BR>--ष्यं<BR>1 Vital power, abundance of<BR>life or vigour.<BR>--2 N. of a ceremony<BR>performed after the birth of a<BR>child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आये
आये ind. An interjection of<BR>calling, expressive of affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आयोगवः|आयोगव
आयोगवः [अयोगव एव, स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>The son of a Śūdra by a Vaiśya wife<BR>(his business being carpentry; cf<BR>Ms. 10. 48); शूद्रादायोगवः क्षत्ता<BR>चांडालश्चधमो नृणाम् । वैश्यराजन्यविप्रास्तु जायंते<BR>वर्णसंकराः ॥.<BR>--वी A woman of this tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरः|आर|आरं
आरः, --रं [आ-ऋ-घञ्]<BR>1 Brass.<BR>--2<BR>Oxide of iron.<BR>--3 An angle, corner.<BR>--4 N. of a tree (मधुराम्रफल).<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>The planet Mars.<BR>--2 The planet<BR>Saturn.<BR>--3 Going.<BR>--4 Distance.<BR>--5<BR>Nearness, as in आरात् q. v.<BR>--6<BR>Extremity (प्रांतभाग).<BR>--रा (आ-ऋ-अच्)<BR>1 A shoemaker's awl.<BR>--2 A knife,<BR>probe, instrument of iron.<BR>--3 A<BR>spoke; cf. अर.<BR>--4 A goad, or whip;<BR>उद्यम्यारामग्रकायोत्थितस्य Śi. 18. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्र {1} the point of an<BR>awl. {2} the iron thong at the end<BR>of a whip.<BR>--आवलिः N. of a chain of<BR>mountains, a part of the Vindhya.<BR>--कूटः, --टं brass; U. 5. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरं|आर|आरः
आरः, --रं [आ-ऋ-घञ्]<BR>1 Brass.<BR>--2<BR>Oxide of iron.<BR>--3 An angle, corner.<BR>--4 N. of a tree (मधुराम्रफल).<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>The planet Mars.<BR>--2 The planet<BR>Saturn.<BR>--3 Going.<BR>--4 Distance.<BR>--5<BR>Nearness, as in आरात् q. v.<BR>--6<BR>Extremity (प्रांतभाग).<BR>--रा (आ-ऋ-अच्)<BR>1 A shoemaker's awl.<BR>--2 A knife,<BR>probe, instrument of iron.<BR>--3 A<BR>spoke; cf. अर.<BR>--4 A goad, or whip;<BR>उद्यम्यारामग्रकायोत्थितस्य Śi. 18. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्र {1} the point of an<BR>awl. {2} the iron thong at the end<BR>of a whip.<BR>--आवलिः N. of a chain of<BR>mountains, a part of the Vindhya.<BR>--कूटः, --टं brass; U. 5. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरकात्
आरकात् ind. Ved. Far from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्ष|आरक्षं|आरक्षः
आरक्ष a. Preserved, defended,<BR>fit to be protected.<BR>--क्षः, --क्षा<BR>1<BR>Protection, preservation, guard;<BR>आरक्षे मध्यमे स्थितान् Rām;<BR> Śānti. 3. 5; Ms. 3. 204.<BR>--2 The junction<BR>of the frontal sinuses of an elephant<BR>(कंभसंधि).<BR>--3 The part of the forehead<BR>below this junction.<BR>--4 An army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षकः|आरक्षक
आरक्ष(क्षि)कः<BR>1 A watchman,<BR>patrol, sentinel.<BR>--2 A village or police<BR>magistrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरक्षिकः|आरक्षिक
आरक्ष(क्षि)कः<BR>1 A watchman,<BR>patrol, sentinel.<BR>--2 A village or police<BR>magistrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरग्वधः|आरग्वध
आरग्वधः The tree Cassia<BR>Fistula (Mar. बाहवा) largely used in<BR>medicinal recipes.<BR>--धं Its fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरचित
आरचित a. Arranged, prepared,<BR>formed &c; see रचित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरटः|आरट
आरटः [आ-रट्-अच्] An actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरट्टः|आरट्ट
आरट्टः<BR>1 N. of a country to the<BR>northeast of Panjab, famous for<BR>its breed of horses; (the people of<BR>Guzarath in Rāvalpinḍi still call<BR>their country Hairat or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-b" target="_blank">Page0253-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Airatdeśa); the inhabitants of this<BR>country (pl.).<BR>--2 A horse from this<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणं|आरण
आरणं Ved.<BR>1 Depth, abyss.<BR>--2 A precipice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणिः|आरणि
आरणिः [आ-ऋ-अनि] An eddy,<BR>whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरणेय|आरणेयः
आरणेय a. (यी f.) [अरणि-ठक्]<BR>Relating to or sprung from Araṇi<BR>q. v.<BR>--यः N. of Śuka.<BR>--यं or ˚पर्वन्<BR>Title of the last section of the<BR>third book of the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्य|आरण्यः
आरण्य a. (ण्या, --ण्यी f.) [अरण्ये<BR>भवः ण्] Wild, forest-born, relating<BR>to a forest (opp. ग्राम्य); ˚पशुः<BR>Ms. 10. 48; (आरण्यपशु is of 7 kinds:<BR>--सरीसृपो रुरुश्चैव महिषो वानरस्तथा । पृषतर्क्षौ<BR>मृगश्चैव पशुर्वै सप्तधा मतः ।)<BR>--ण्यः, --ण्यं<BR>1 A forest.<BR>--2 A kind of corn<BR>growing without sowing seed.<BR>--3 N. of<BR>certain signs of the zodiac (see ˚राशि<BR>below).<BR>--4 Cow-dung (--ण्यः only).<BR>--5 N.<BR>of a Parvan in the Mahābhārata.<BR>--6<BR>N. of a Kāṇḍa in the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कुक्कुटः a wild cock.<BR>--गानं<BR>one of the four Gānas or<BR>psalmbooks of the Sāma-veda<BR>--पर्वन् n.<BR>N. of the third book of the<BR>Mahābhārata, usually called Vana-Parvan.<BR>--पशुः a wild beast.<BR>--मुद्गा a kind of<BR>bean.<BR>--राशिः (in the zodiac) {1}<BR>the signs Leo, Aries, and Taurus.<BR>{2} the former half of Capricorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरण्यक|आरण्यकः
आरण्यक a. [अरण्ये भवः वुञ्]<BR>Relating to or produced in a forest, wild,<BR>forest-born (usually with the words<BR>अध्याय, मनुष्य, न्याय, पथिन्, विहार, and<BR>हस्तिन् P. IV. 2. 129 Vārt).<BR>--कः A<BR>forester, an inhabitant of the<BR>woods; तपःषड्भागमक्षय्यं<BR>ददत्यारण्यका हि नः Ś. 2. 13; R. 5. 15.<BR>--कं An Āraṇyaka; it is one<BR>of a class of religious and<BR>philosophical writings (connected with<BR>the Brāhmaṇas) which are either<BR>composed in forests, or must be<BR>studied there; e. g. ऐतरेयारण्यकं,<BR>बृहदारण्यकं and तैत्तिरीयारण्यकं; अरण्येऽ<BR>नूच्यमानत्वात् आरण्यकं Bṛ. Ār. Up.; (अरण्येऽ<BR>ध्ययनादेव आरण्यकमुदाहृतं).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कांडं<BR>the title of the third book of the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरथः|आरथ
आरथः [ईषत्स्वल्यो रथः] A carriage<BR>drawn by one horse or ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरनालं|आरनाल
आरनालं Gruel made from the<BR>fermentation of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभ्
आरभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To begin,<BR>commence, undertake; आरभंतेऽल्पमेवाज्ञाः<BR>Subhāṣ.; आरब्धा बलिविग्रहं<BR>Bk. 5. 38.<BR>--2 To be active or energetic,<BR>be busy; अप्यनारभमाणस्य<BR>Śi. 2. 91.<BR>--3 To rely on.<BR>--4 To reach<BR>or attain to, obtain.<BR>--5 To seize,<BR>grasp.<BR>--6 To form, make; भूतैः<BR>पंचभिरारब्धे देहे Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्ध|आरब्धं
आरब्ध p. p. Begun, commenced.<BR>--ब्धं Beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरब्धिः|आरब्धि
आरब्धिः f. Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभटः|आरभट
आरभटः [आरभ्-अटि] An<BR>enterprising or courageous man.<BR>--टः, --टी<BR>Boldness, confidence.<BR>--टी<BR>1 A<BR>branch of the dramatic art,<BR>machinery of the drama, representation of<BR>supernatural, horrible events on the<BR>stage; मायेंद्रजालंसग्रामक्रोधोद्भ्रांतादिचेष्टितैः<BR>संयुक्ता वधबंधाद्यैरुद्धतारभटी मता ॥ (said<BR>to be of four kinds, see S. D. 420<BR>et seq.)<BR>--2 A kind of literary<BR>style (वृत्ति).<BR>--3 A particular style<BR>of dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरभ्य
आरभ्य ind. Having begun,<BR>beginning with, ever since, since, with a<BR>prepositional force (with abl.);<BR>मालत्याः प्रथमावलोकदिवसादारभ्य<BR>Māl. 6. 3; Ś. 3; K. 102, 134, 196; sometimes<BR>with acc. also; प्रतिपद्दिनमारभ्य Bhāg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरंभः|आरम्भ|आरम्भः
आरंभः [आ रभ्-घञ् मुम्]<BR>1<BR>Beginning, commencement; ˚उपायः plan<BR>of commencement; नृत्यारंभे हर<BR>पशुपतेरार्द्रनागाजिनेच्छां Me. 99.<BR>--2 An<BR>introduction.<BR>--3 (a) An act,<BR>undertaking, deed, work; आगमैः<BR>सदृशारंभः R. 1. 15; Ku. 7. 71; V. 3;<BR>Bh. 2. 69; R. 7. 31; Bg. 12. 16. (b)<BR>Preparation; U. 4. (c) A thing<BR>begun; U. 4.<BR>--4 Haste, speed,<BR>velocity; चंडारंभः समीरः Ve. 2. 18.<BR>--5 Effort, exertion; Bg. 14. 12.<BR>--6 Scene, action; चित्रार्पितारंभ<BR>इवावतस्थे R. 2. 31.<BR>--7 Pride.<BR>--8 Killing,<BR>slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरंभक|आरम्भक
आरंभक a. [आ-रभ्-ण्वुल् मुम्]<BR>Undertaking, beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरंभणं|आरम्भण
आरंभणं [आ-रभ् ल्युट् मुम्]<BR>1 Taking<BR>hold of, seizing.<BR>--2 The place of<BR>seizing, a handle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरंभिन्|आरम्भिन्
आरंभिन् a. Enterprizing; one who<BR>forms new projects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरम्
आरम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To delight in, take<BR>pleasure in, sport; आरमंतं परं स्मरे<BR>Bk. 8. 52, 3. 38.<BR>--2 To<BR>cease, stop (to speak); leave off;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">Page0254-a+ 56</a>]<BR>विरामोऽस्त्विति चारमेत् Ms. 2. 73.<BR>--3<BR>To rest, take rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0253-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरत
आरत p. p.<BR>1 Stopped, ceased;<BR>Ki. 5. 6; see अनारत also.<BR>--2 Quiet,<BR>gentle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरतिः|आरति
आरतिः f.<BR>1 Cessation, stopping.<BR>--2 Waving lights before an image<BR>(Mar. आरती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरमणं|आरमण
आरमणं<BR>1 Taking delight.<BR>--2<BR>Cessation, pause.<BR>--3 A resting place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराम|आरामः
आराम a. [रम्-घञ्] Pleasing,<BR>delightful; रामभद्र गुणाराम<BR>Mv. 7. 40.<BR>--मः<BR>1 Delight, pleasure;<BR>इंद्रियारामः Bg. 3. 16; आत्मारामाः<BR>Ve. 1. 31; एकाराम Y. 3. 58.<BR>--2 A garden,<BR>grove; प्रियारामा हि वैदेह्यासीत् U. 2;<BR>आरामाधिपतिर्विवेकविकलः Bv. 1. 31.<BR>[cf. Pers. ārām].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शीतला<BR>N. of a fragrant plant (आनंदी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरामिकः|आरामिक
आरामिकः A gardener.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरंबणं|आरम्बण
आरंबणं (Vedic for आलंबनं)<BR>Support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरव|आरवः
आरव &c. See under आरु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरस्यं|आरस्य
आरस्यं [अरसस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>Insipidity, tastelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरा
आरा See under आर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्
आरात् ind. [आ-रा-बा˚ आति Tv.;<BR>abl. of आर q. v.]<BR>1 Near, in the<BR>vicinity of; (with abl. or by itself);<BR>तमर्च्यमारादभिवर्तमानं R. 2. 10; 5.<BR>{3}<BR>--2 Far from; with acc. also in<BR>both these senses; Śi. 3. 31, 8. 29,<BR>12. 28; to a distant place, distant.<BR>--3 Far, from a distance; U. 2. 24.<BR>--4 Directly, immediately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरातीय
आरातीय a. [आरात्-छ;<BR>P. IV. 2. 104 Vārt.]<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>--2<BR>Remote, distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्तात्
आरात्तात् ind. Ved. From a<BR>distant place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरातिः|आराति
आरातिः [आ-राक्तिच्] An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरात्रिकं|आरात्रिक
आरात्रिकं [अरात्रावपि निर्वृत्तं ठञ्]<BR>1<BR>Waving a light (or the vessel<BR>containing it) at night before an<BR>idol (Mar. आरती ओंवाळणें); सर्वेषु<BR>चांगेषु च सप्तवारान् आरात्रिकं<BR>भक्तजनस्तु कुर्यात्.<BR>--2 The light so waved;<BR>शिरसि निहितभारं पात्रमारात्रिकस्य भ्रमयति<BR>मयि भूयस्ते कृपार्द्रः कटाक्षः Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराध्
आराध् {c5c} {c10c} P.<BR>1 To propitiate,<BR>conciliate, please, try to win the<BR>favour of; परेषां चेतांसि<BR>प्रतिदिवसमाराध्य बहुधा Bh. 3. 34, 2. 4-5;<BR>R. 1. 77, 81, 10. 86, 18. 23; Me. 45.<BR>--2 To honour, worship,<BR>respect.<BR>--3 To deserve, merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधक
आराधक a. A worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधनं|आराधन
आराधनं<BR>1 Pleasing, satisfaction,<BR>entertainment, gratification;<BR>येषामाराधनाय U. 1; यदि वा जानकीमपि<BR>आराधनाय लोकानां मुंचतो नास्ति मे व्यथा<BR>1. 12, 41.<BR>--2 Serving, worshipping,<BR>adoration, propitiation (as of a deity);<BR>आराधनायास्य सखीसमेताम् Ku. 1. 58;<BR>Bg. 7. 22; कृतमाराधनं रवेः Mb.<BR>--3<BR>A means of pleasing; इदं तु ते<BR>भक्तिनम्रं सतामाराधनं वपुः Ku. 6. 73.<BR>--4<BR>Honouring, respecting; U. 4. 17.<BR>--5 Cooking.<BR>--6 Accomplishment,<BR>undertaking.<BR>--7 Acquirement,<BR>attainment; Bh. 3. 4.<BR>--ना Service.<BR>--नी Worship, adoration,<BR>propitiation (of a deity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधनीय
आराधनीय, आराध्य pot. p. Fit<BR>to be worshipped or propitiated;<BR>R. 16. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराध्य
आराधनीय, आराध्य pot. p. Fit<BR>to be worshipped or propitiated;<BR>R. 16. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधयितृ
आराधयितृ a. An adorer, humble<BR>servant, worshipper;<BR>तन्वयमाराधयिता जनस्तव समीपे वर्तते Ś. 3;<BR>पितरमाराधयिता भव V. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराधयिष्णु
आराधयिष्णु^1 a. Endeavouring to<BR>please, desirous of worshipping.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: cf AP and MW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरालिकः|आरालिक
आरालिकः [अरालं कुटिलं चरति<BR>ठक्] ‘One who deals crookedly’,<BR>a cook; (धनलोभेन परप्रोत्साहितः पाचको<BR>विषादिसंसृष्टं पचतीति तस्य तथात्वं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरिच्
आरिच् {c7c} U. To empty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेकः|आरेक
आरेकः [आ-रिच् घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Emptying.<BR>--2 Contraction.<BR>--3 Doubt.<BR>--4<BR>Excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेचित
आरेचित a. [अ-रिच्-णिच् क्त]<BR>1<BR>Emptied.<BR>--2 Mixed.<BR>--3 Contracted;<BR>आरेचितभ्रूचतुरैः कटाक्षैः Ku. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरित्रिक
आरित्रिक a. [P. IV. 2. 116]<BR>Pertaining to an oar &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरु|आरुः
आरु {c2c} P.<BR>1 To cry out, shout;<BR>Ki. 17. 24, to low (as cows).<BR>--2 To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरवः|आरव
आर(रा)वः [आ-रु-अप् पक्षे घञ्]<BR>1 A cry, howling; वानराश्चक्रुरारवं<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 Sound; Śi. 11. 8, 12. 18,<BR>8. 45.<BR>--3 N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरावः|आराव
आर(रा)वः [आ-रु-अप् पक्षे घञ्]<BR>1 A cry, howling; वानराश्चक्रुरारवं<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 Sound; Śi. 11. 8, 12. 18,<BR>8. 45.<BR>--3 N. of a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आराविन्
आराविन् a. Sounding, noisy;<BR>नूपुराराविणा M. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुः|आरु
आरुः [ऋ-उण्]<BR>1 A hog.<BR>--2 A<BR>crab.<BR>--3 N. of a tree.<BR>--रुः f. A<BR>pitcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुकः|आरुक
आरुकः A medicinal plant<BR>having cooling properties (growing on<BR>the Himālayas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुच्
आरुच् Caus. To regard as<BR>pleasant, choose, like; वासं<BR>नारोचयेऽरण्ये Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोकः|आरोक
आरोकः<BR>1 Shining through.<BR>--2<BR>Small points of light between the<BR>threads of a web.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोचन
आरोचन a. Shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुज्
आरुज्, --ज a. [आ-रुज्-क]<BR>1<BR>Distressing, giving pain.<BR>--2 Killing,<BR>destroying, breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुज
आरुज्, --ज a. [आ-रुज्-क]<BR>1<BR>Distressing, giving pain.<BR>--2 Killing,<BR>destroying, breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुजत्नु
आरुजत्नु a. Ved. Breaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणि|आरुणिः
आरुणि a. [अरुणस्य अपत्यं इण्]<BR>Belonging to, or sprung from, Aruṇa,<BR>q. v.<BR>--णिः<BR>1 N. of Uddālaka.<BR>--2<BR>Descendants of the sage अरुण.<BR>--3 The<BR>son of the sun, as Yama.<BR>--4 The<BR>son of Vinatā (वैनतेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुणी
आरुणी f. Ved. ‘The red one’, a<BR>name given to the horses of the<BR>Maruts which are females.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुध्
आरुध् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To keep or ward<BR>off, keep away, restrain; बंधुता<BR>शुचमारुणत् Bk. 17. 49.<BR>--2 To shut up,<BR>confine.<BR>--3 To besiege.<BR>--4 To hold<BR>fast, grasp. --Caus. To obstruct,<BR>impede, block, besiege.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोधनं|आरोधन
आरोधनं Ved. Obstruction, means<BR>of obstruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुषी
आरुषी N. of a daughter of<BR>Manu and the mother of और्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुष्करं|आरुष्कर
आरुष्करं The fruit of the tree<BR>called भल्लातक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह्
आरुह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To ascend, mount,<BR>bestride, get upon (with acc.,<BR>sometimes loc.); सिंहासनमारुरोह K. 111;<BR>आरुरुहू रथादिषु Bk. 14. 8;<BR>आरूढकुलालचक्रमिव Mu. 5. 5<BR>mounted on a potter's wheel; 7. 12.<BR>--2<BR>To ride upon, get ascendancy over,<BR>domineer over (fig.); वृषल भृत्यमिव<BR>मामारोढुमिच्छसि Mu. 3; Pt. 1. 36.<BR>--3 To venture upon, undertake,<BR>enter upon, make; प्रतिज्ञामारोढुं<BR>पुनरपि चलत्येष चरणः Mu. 3. 30, 27; so<BR>यौवनारूढ, योगारूढ.<BR>--4 To attain, gain,<BR>get to, reach; सौंदर्यस्य पारमारूढा न वा<BR>Dk. 88; Ki. 2. 13; तुलां<BR>यदारोहतिदंतवाससा Ku. 5. 34; आरुरोह<BR>कुमुदाकरोपमां R. 19. 34. The senses of this<BR>root are modified according to the<BR>noun with which it is joined;<BR>आरूढरुषा Ku. 7. 67 excited to<BR>anger; तदागमारूढगुरुप्रहर्षः R. 5. 61;<BR>मंत्रिपदमारूढः Mu. 6; तर्कारूढा 6. 19<BR>engaged in guessing; Ś. 5. 9;<BR>शीघ्रं बुद्धिमारोहति Ś. B. strikes the<BR>mind; यौवनपदवीमारूढः attained his<BR>majority; अवस्थांतरमारूढा M. 3;<BR>संशयं पुनरारुह्य H. 1. 7 running a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-a" target="_blank">Page0255-a+ 57</a>]<BR>risk; संशयमारुरोह शैलः Ki. 13. 16.<BR>--Caus. (रोह-प-यति)<BR>1 To cause<BR>to go up or ascend, raise up, elevate;<BR>अमात्योऽस्मान्पुरातनीमवस्थामारोपयिष्यति<BR>Mu. 2 will raise or elevate;<BR>शूलानारोपयेत् Y. 2. 273;<BR>आरोपितामनोविषयमात्मनः Ku. 6. 17.<BR>--2 To cause to<BR>mount or sit (on oneself) (Atm.);<BR>करेणुरारोहयते निषादिनं Śi. 12. 5.<BR>--3<BR>To cause to grow, plant (lit.).<BR>--4<BR>To establish, instal, seat (fig.);<BR>राज्ये चारोपिता वयं Mu. 7. 18;<BR>इत्यारोपितपुत्रास्ते R. 15. 91.<BR>--5 To cause,<BR>produce, bring out; उष्माणं K. 105;<BR>प्रणयं 134, 142; आरोपितप्रीतिरभूत् 173, 212;<BR>प्रतापमारोपयितुं 110, 119 show or<BR>exhibit.<BR>--6 To place, fix, direct;<BR>अंकमारोप्य placing in the lap; R. 3. 26,<BR>14. 27; Ku. 1. 37; चक्षुः˚ cast a<BR>look at; Pt. 1. 243; आशीर्वादमारोपयंतः<BR>Ki. 18. 46 conferring or<BR>pronouncing; आभरणभारमंगेषु नारोपयंति K. 203<BR>put or wear; पत्रे आरोपितं कुरु Ś. 6<BR>commit to paper; आरोप्यते शिला शैले<BR>H. 2. 47.<BR>--7 To entrust to, appoint<BR>to, charge with; मंत्रिणि राज्यभारमारोप्य<BR>K. 57; अमात्यपदे आरोपितः Pt. 1.<BR>--8<BR>To cause to go to or attain a<BR>particular state; करतलं कर्णपूरतामारोपितं<BR>K. 60; आरोपय गरीयस्त्वं 207 raise to<BR>greatness; 315; Dk. 118.<BR>--9 To ascribe,<BR>attribute, impute;<BR>आत्मन्यारोपिताभिमानाः K. 108, 185; छाया हि भूमेः<BR>शशिनो मलत्वेनारोपिता शुद्धिमतः प्रजाभिः<BR>R. 14. 40.<BR>--10 To string (as a bow);<BR>धनुरारोपयन् U. 4; तं<BR>देशमारोपितपुष्पचापे Ku. 3. 35; Bk. 14. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0254-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुरुक्षु
आरुरुक्षु a. Wishing to ascend,<BR>mount or reach; कैलासगौरं वृषमारुरुक्षोः<BR>R. 2. 35; योगं Bg. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह्
आरुह् a. Ved. Ascending. --f.<BR>1 Excrescence.<BR>--2 A shoot (of a<BR>plant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरुह|आरुहः
आरुह a. [आ-रुह्-क] Ascending,<BR>mounting &c.<BR>--हः Ascent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढ|आरूढः
आरूढ p. p.<BR>1 Mounted, ascended;<BR>seated on; आरूढो वृक्षो भवता Sk.;<BR>oft. used actively; आरूढमद्रीन्<BR>R. 6. 77; Me. 8, 18; Ś. 4; so वृक्षं, नावं,<BR>हयं, रथं &c.; चक्र˚, दोला˚.<BR>--2 Raised<BR>up, elevated on high.<BR>--3 Arisen,<BR>produced.<BR>--ढं Ascending,<BR>mounting; see अत्यारूढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरूढिः|आरूढि
आरूढिः f. Ascent, mounting; rise,<BR>elevation (lit. and fig.);<BR>अत्यारूढिर्भवति महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा Ś. 4. v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपः|आरोप
आरोपः<BR>1 Attributing the nature or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">Page0255-b+ 57</a>]<BR>properties of one thing to another;<BR>वस्तुन्यवस्त्वारोपोऽध्यारोपः Vedānta S.;<BR>attributing or assigning to,<BR>imputation; दोषारोपो गुणेष्वपि Ak.<BR>--2 Considering as equal;<BR>identification (as in सारोपा लक्षणा).<BR>--3<BR>Superimposition.<BR>--4 Imposing (as a<BR>burden), burdening or charging<BR>with.<BR>--5 Placing in or upon.<BR>--6<BR>Relating to.<BR>--7 Superior position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपक
आरोपक a. Placing, fixing,<BR>planting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपणं|आरोपण
आरोपणं<BR>1 Placing or fixing in or<BR>upon, putting;<BR>आर्द्राक्षतारोपणमन्वभूतां R. 7. 28; Ku. 7. 88; (fig.)<BR>establishing, installing; अधिकारारोपणं<BR>Mu. 3.<BR>--2 Causing to mount or<BR>ascend, raising (to heaven).<BR>--3<BR>Planting.<BR>--4 The stringing of a bow.<BR>--5 Trusting, delivering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोपित|आरोपितं
आरोपित p. p.<BR>1 Raised, elevated.<BR>--2 Fixed, placed, made.<BR>--3 Strung<BR>(as a bow).<BR>--4 Deposited, entrusted.<BR>--5 Consecrated, hallowed.<BR>--6<BR>Accidental, adventitious, ascribed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहः|आरोह
आरोहः [आ-रुह्-घञ्]<BR>1 One who<BR>mounts, a rider, as in अश्वारोह,<BR>स्यंदनारोह; सारोहाणां च वाजिनां Rām.; one<BR>who is seated in a carriage.<BR>--2<BR>Ascent, rising, mounting, ascending,<BR>riding.<BR>--3 An elevated place,<BR>elevation, altitude, height; नगाद्यारोह<BR>उच्छ्रायः Ak.<BR>--4 Haughtiness, pride.<BR>--5 A mountain, a heap.<BR>--6 A<BR>woman's waist; the buttocks; सा रामा न<BR>वरारोहा Udb.;<BR>आरोहैर्निबिडबृहन्नितंबबिंबैः Śi. 8. 8.<BR>--7 Length.<BR>--8 A kind of<BR>measure.<BR>--9 A mine.<BR>--10 Descending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहक|आरोहकः
आरोहक a.<BR>1 Ascending,<BR>mounting, riding.<BR>--2 Raising up,<BR>elevating.<BR>--3 Rising.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A rider,<BR>driver; हस्त्यारोहकः Pt. 2.<BR>--2 A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहणं|आरोहण
आरोहणं<BR>1 The act of rising,<BR>ascending, mounting; आरोहणार्थं<BR>नवयौवनेन कामस्य सोपानमिव प्रयुक्तं<BR>Ku. 1. 39.<BR>--2 Riding (on a horse &c).<BR>--3 A stair-case, ladder.<BR>--4 The<BR>rising or growing of new shoots,<BR>growing (of plants).<BR>--5 A raised stage<BR>for dancing.<BR>--6 A carriage (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहणिक
आरोहणिक a. Relating to<BR>mounting or ascending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोहिन्
आरोहिन् a. Ascending, mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरू
आरू a. Of a tawny colour.<BR>--रू<BR>m.<BR>1 The tawny colour.<BR>--2 A hog;<BR>a crab; see आरु.<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>medicinal plant on the Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरे
आरे ind. Ved.<BR>1 Far, far from,<BR>(with abl.).<BR>--2 Near.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अघ<BR>a. Ved. having evil far removed.<BR>--अवद्य a. one from whom blame<BR>is far removed.<BR>--शत्रु a. one whose<BR>enemies are driven far away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेवतः|आरेवत|आरेवतं
आरेवतः N. of a tree(आरग्बघ<BR>q. v.).<BR>--तं The fruit of this tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरेहणं|आरेहण
आरेहणं Ved. Licking, kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आरोग्यं|आरोग्य
आरोग्यं [अरोगस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>Freedom from disease, good health<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शाला an hospital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्किः|आर्कि
आर्किः [अर्कस्य अपत्यं इञ्] A son<BR>of अर्क, epithet of (1) Yama, (2)<BR>the planet Saturn, (3) Karṇa, (4)<BR>Sugrīva, (5) वैवस्वतमनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्ष|आर्क्षः
आर्क्ष (र्क्षी f.) [ऋक्षस्येदं अण्]<BR>Stellar, regulated by stars or<BR>pertaining to them.<BR>--र्क्षः A son or<BR>descendant of Ṛkṣa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्षः<BR>a stellar year or revolution of a<BR>constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्क्षोद
आर्क्षोद [ऋक्षोद-अण्]<BR>Inhabiting the mountain Ṛkṣoda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्गलः|आर्गल
आर्गलः --ली [अर्गलमेव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>A bolt or bar; see अर्गलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्गली
आर्गलः --ली [अर्गलमेव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>A bolt or bar; see अर्गलं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ग्वध|आर्ग्वधः
आर्ग्वध = आरग्वध q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्घा
आर्घा [आ-अर्घ-अच्] A kind of<BR>yellow bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्घ्य|आर्घ्यं
आर्घ्य a. Relating to this bee.<BR>--र्घ्यं<BR>Wild honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्च|आर्च्च
आर्च a. (र्ची f.) [अर्चा<BR>अस्त्यस्य ण P. V. 2. 101]<BR>1 Devout,<BR>worshipping, pious.<BR>--2 Relating to,<BR>the Ṛk or Ṛgveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्चिक|आर्च्चिक
आर्चिक a. (की f.) [ऋचि भवः.<BR>ऋचो व्याख्यानो ग्रंथो वा ठञ्] Relating to<BR>the Ṛgveda, or explaining it.<BR>--कं<BR>An epithet of the Sāma-Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्चीक|आर्चीकः
आर्चीक a. [ऋचीके पर्वते भवः अण्]<BR>Belonging to the ऋचीक mountain.<BR>--कः The mountain ऋचीक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जवं|आर्जव
आर्जवं [ऋजोर्भावः अण्]<BR>1<BR>Straightness; दूरं यात्युदरं च रोमलतिका नेत्रार्जवं<BR>धावति S. D.<BR>--2 Straightforwardness,<BR>rectitude of conduct, uprightness,<BR>honesty, sincerity,<BR>open-heartedness; अहिंसा क्षांतिरार्जवं Bg. 13. 7;<BR>क्षेत्रमार्जवस्य K. 45; Bh. 2. 22.<BR>--3<BR>Simplicity, humility; Ki. 4. 13;<BR>Mv. 5. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जीक|आर्जीकः
आर्जीक a. [ऋजीकस्येदं अण्]<BR>Belonging to the ऋजीक country, or<BR>a vessel called ऋजीक.<BR>--कः A lake<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">Page0256-a+ 57</a>]<BR>in the ऋजोक country; (according to<BR>others) perhaps a milk-vessel or<BR>celestial-vessel in which the<BR>heavenly Soma is purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0255-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जीकीय
आर्जीकीय = आजींक a.<BR>--या<BR>1 A<BR>terrestrial river.<BR>--2 N. of a river<BR>(विपाशा.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्जुनिः|आर्जुनि|आर्ज्जुनि
आर्जुनिः [अर्जुनस्य अपत्यं इञ्] The<BR>son of Arjuna, अभिमन्यु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त|आर्त्त|आर्त्तः
आर्त a. [आ-ऋ-क्त]<BR>1 Afflicted with,<BR>struck by, suffering from, pained<BR>by; usually in comp., कामार्त, क्षुधार्त<BR>तृषार्त &c.<BR>--2 Sick, diseased; आर्तस्य<BR>यथौषधं R. 1. 28; Ms. 4. 236.<BR>--3<BR>Distressed, afflicted, struck by<BR>calamity, oppressed, unhappy;<BR>आर्तत्राणाय वः शस्त्रं न ग्रहर्तुमनागसि<BR>Ś. 1. 11, R. 2. 28, 8. 31, 12. 10, 32.<BR>--4 Perishable (विनाशिन्).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नादः, --ध्वनिः, स्वरः a cry of distress,<BR>--बधुः, --साधुः a friend of the<BR>distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तिः|आर्ति|आर्त्ति|आर्त्तिः
आर्तिः f. [आ-ऋ-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Distress,<BR>affliction, suffering, pain, injury<BR>(bodily or mental); आर्तिं न पश्यसि<BR>पुरूरवसस्तदर्थे V. 2. 16;<BR>आपन्नार्तिप्रशमनफलाः संपदो ह्युत्तमानां Me. 53.<BR>--2<BR>Mental agony, anguish; उत्कंठार्ति<BR>Amaru. 39.<BR>--3 Evil, mischief.<BR>--4<BR>Sickness, disease.<BR>--5 The end of<BR>a bow.<BR>--6 Ruin, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तिमत्|आर्तिमन्त्
आर्तिमत् a. Suffering from pain,<BR>afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तगलः|आर्तगल|आर्त्तगल|आर्त्तगलः
आर्तगलः N. of a tree नीलझिंटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तना
आर्तना Ved.<BR>1 A mortal<BR>combat.<BR>--2 An uncultivated ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तव|आर्तवः|आर्त्तव|आर्त्तवं|आर्त्तवः
आर्तव a. (वा वी f.) [ऋतुरस्य प्राप्तः,<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Conforming or relating to<BR>the season; seasonal; अभिभूय<BR>विभूतिमार्तवीं R. 8. 36, स्वयमंगेषु ममेदमार्तवं<BR>Ku. 4. 68; V. 1. 13; vernal;<BR>R. 9. 28, 48.<BR>--2 Menstrual, relating<BR>to or produced by this discharge.<BR>--वः A section of the year, a<BR>combination of several seasons (Ved.).<BR>--वी A mare.<BR>--वं<BR>1 The menstrual<BR>discharge (of women);<BR>नोपगच्छेत्प्रमत्तोऽपि स्त्रियमार्तवदर्शने Ms. 4. 40,<BR>3. 48.<BR>--2 Certain days after<BR>menstrual discharge, favourable to<BR>conception.<BR>--3 A flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्तवेयी
आर्तवेयी A woman during her<BR>courses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्निः|आर्त्नि
आर्त्निः The end of a bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्विजीन
आर्त्विजीन a. (नी f.) [ऋत्विजं<BR>तत्कर्मार्हति खञ्] Fit for the office of a<BR>sacrificial priest (ऋत्विज्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्त्विज्यं|आर्त्विज्य
आर्त्विज्यं [ऋत्विजो भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्]<BR>The office of a priest, his rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थ
आर्थ a. (र्थी f.) [अर्थादागतः अण्]<BR>1 Relating to a thing or object.<BR>--2 Relating to, dependent on, sense<BR>(opp. शाब्द); आर्थि उपमा &c.<BR>--3<BR>Material, significant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थपत्यं|आर्थपत्य
आर्थपत्यं Power over a thing,<BR>possession of a thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्थिक
आर्थिक a. (की f.) [अर्थं गृह्णाति ठक्]<BR>1 Significant.<BR>--2 Wise.<BR>--3 Rich.<BR>--4 Substantial, real, material.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्र|आर्द्रं
आर्द्र a. [आ-अर्द्-रक् दीर्घश्च<BR>Uṇ. 2. 18]<BR>1 Wet, moist, damp, तंत्रीमार्द्रां<BR>नयनसलिलैः Me. 86, 43;<BR>आर्द्राक्षतारोपणमन्वभृतां R. 7. 28.<BR>--2 Succulent.<BR>living, not dry, green, juicy; आर्द्रं<BR>द्रव्यं द्विधा प्रोक्तं सरसं नीरसं तथा.<BR>--3<BR>Fresh, new; कानीवार्द्रापराधः<BR>Amaru. 2; कांतमार्द्रापराधं M. 3. 12; R. 14. 4.<BR>--4 Soft, tender; oft. used with<BR>words like स्नेह, दया, करुणा in the<BR>sense of ‘flowing with,’ moved’,<BR>‘melted’; स्नेहार्द्रं हृदयं a heart wet or<BR>melted with pity; करुणा˚, दया˚;<BR>प्रेमार्द्राः चेष्टाः Māl. 5. 7.<BR>--5 Full of<BR>feeling, warm.<BR>--6 Loose, flaccid.<BR>--र्द्रा N.<BR>of a constellation or the sixth<BR>lunar mansion so called (consisting<BR>of one star). [cf. Gr. ardo].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काष्ठं green wood.<BR>--दानु a. Ved.<BR>giving moisture.<BR>--नयन a. weeping<BR>--पदी a woman with wet feet.<BR>--पवित्र a. Ved. having a wet<BR>strainer, epithet of the Soma.<BR>--पृष्ठ a.<BR>watered, refreshed; आर्द्रपृष्ठाः क्रियंतां<BR>वाजिनः Ś. 1.<BR>--माषा a. leguminous<BR>shrub (माषपर्णी).<BR>--शाकं fresh ginger.<BR>--लुब्धकः (˚र्द्रा˚ the dragon's tail or<BR>descending node, N. of Ketu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रता
आर्द्रता Wetness, moisture,<BR>freshness, tenderness, softness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रक|आर्द्रकं
आर्द्रक a. (की f.) Born under<BR>the constellation Ārdrā; cf.<BR>P. IV. 3. 28.<BR>--कं Ginger in its undried<BR>state, wet ginger (Mar. आलें).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्द्रयति
आर्द्रयति Den. P. To wet, moisten;<BR>Bh. 2. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ध
आर्ध a. (Only used at the<BR>beginning of comp.) Half.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धातुक a. (की f.) (In gram.)<BR>applicable to half the root or to the<BR>shorter form of the verbal base.<BR>--(कं) a name given to those<BR>terminations and affixes which belong<BR>to the six non-conjugational or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-c" target="_blank">Page0256-c+ 57</a>]<BR>general tenses (opp. सार्वधातुक); cf.<BR>P. III. 4. 114, I. 1. 4; II. 4. 35;<BR>VII. 2. 35 &c.<BR>--प्रस्थिक, --कंसिक a. (--की f.)<BR>bought with half a Prastha or<BR>Kaṃsa.<BR>--मासिक a. (की f.) lasting<BR>for half a month, observing or<BR>practising (penance &c.) for a<BR>fortnight.<BR>--रात्रिकाः (pl.) N. of an<BR>astronomical school who reckoned the<BR>beginning of the motions of the<BR>planets from midnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धिक|आर्धिकः
आर्धिक a. (की f.) [अर्धमर्हति ठक्]<BR>Sharing half, relating to a half.<BR>--कः<BR>One who ploughs the land for half<BR>the crop; one born of a Vaiśya<BR>woman, and brought up by a<BR>Brāhmaṇa; see the quotation under<BR>आर्धिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्धुक
आर्धुक a. (की f.) Ved.<BR>Conducive to success, beneficial,<BR>profitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्पयितृ
आर्पयितृ m. Ved. One who<BR>injures or hurts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्भव
आर्भव a. (वी f.) Belonging or<BR>sacred to the Ṛbhus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्य|आर्यः|आर्य्य|आर्य्यः
आर्य a. [ऋ-ण्यत्]<BR>1 Āryan.<BR>--2<BR>Worthy of an Ārya.<BR>--3 Worthy,<BR>venerable, respectable, honourable,<BR>noble, high; यदार्यमस्यामभिलाषि मे<BR>मनः Ś. 1. 22; so आर्यवेषः<BR>respectable dress; oft. used in theatrical<BR>language as an honorific adjective<BR>and a respectful mode of address;<BR>आर्यचाणक्यः, आर्या अरुंधती &c.; आर्य<BR>revered or honoured Sir; आर्ये revered<BR>or honoured lady. The following<BR>rules are laid down for the use of<BR>आर्य in addressing persons:-- (1)<BR>वाच्यौ नटीसूत्रधारावार्यनाम्ना परस्परं । (2)<BR>वयस्येत्युत्तमैर्वाच्यो मव्यैरार्येति चाग्रजः । (3) (<BR>वक्तव्यो) अमात्य आर्येति घेतरैः । (4) स्वेच्छया<BR>नाममिविंप्रैविंप्र आर्येति चेतरैः । S. D. 431.<BR>--4 Noble, fine, excellent.<BR>--र्यः<BR>1 N.<BR>of the Hindu and Iranian people, as<BR>distinguished from अनार्य, दस्यु and<BR>दासः विजानीह्यार्याव्ये च दरयवः<BR>Rv. 1. 51. 8.<BR>--2 A man who is faithful to the<BR>religion and laws of his country;<BR>कर्तव्यमाचरन् कार्यमकर्तव्यमनाचरन् । तिष्ठति<BR>प्रकृताचारे स वा आर्य इति स्मृतः ॥.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of the first three castes (as opp. to<BR>शूद्र).<BR>--4 A respectable or honourable<BR>man, esteemed person; वृत्तेन हि<BR>भवत्यार्यो न धनेन न विद्यया Mb.<BR>--5 A<BR>man of noble birth.<BR>--6 A man of<BR>noble character.<BR>--7 A master, owner.<BR>--8 A preceptor.<BR>--9 A friend.<BR>--10<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-a" target="_blank">Page0257-a+ 58</a>]<BR>A Vaiśya.<BR>--11 A father-in-law (as<BR>in आर्यपुंत्र).<BR>--12 A Buddha.<BR>--13 (With<BR>the Buddhists) A man who has<BR>thought on the four chief principles<BR>of Buddhism and lives according<BR>to them.<BR>--14 A son of Manu<BR>Sāvarṇa.<BR>--र्या<BR>1 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>--2 A<BR>mother-in-law.<BR>--3 A respectable<BR>woman.<BR>--4 N. of a metre, see<BR>Appendix.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अष्टशतं title<BR>of a work of Ārya Bhaṭṭa<BR>consisting of eight hundred verses.<BR>--आवर्तः [आर्या आवर्तंते अत्र] ‘abode<BR>of the noble or excellent (Āryas);’<BR>particularly N. of the tract<BR>extending from the eastern to the western<BR>ocean, and bounded on the north<BR>and south by the Himālaya and<BR>Vindhya respectively; cf. Ms. 2. 22;<BR>आसमुद्रात्तु वै पूर्वादासमुद्राच्च पश्चिमात् ।<BR>तयोरेवांतरं गिर्योः (हिमवद्विंध्ययोः) आर्यावर्तं<BR>विदुर्बुधाः; also 10. 34.<BR>--गृह्य a. [आर्यस्य गृह्यः<BR>पक्षः] {1} to be respected by the<BR>noble {2} a friend of the noble,<BR>readily accessible to honourable<BR>men; तमार्यगृह्यं निगृहीतधेनुः<BR>R. 2. 33. {3} respectable, right, decorous.<BR>--देशः a country inhabited by the<BR>Āryas.<BR>--पुत्रः {1} son of an<BR>honourable man. {2} the son of a spiritual<BR>preceptor. {3} honorific designation<BR>of the son of the elder brother; of<BR>a husband by his wife; or of a<BR>prince by his general &c. {4} the son<BR>of the father-in-law, i. e. a husband<BR>(occurring in every drama; mostly<BR>in the vocative case in the last two<BR>senses).<BR>--प्राय a. {1} inhabited by<BR>the Āryas. {2} abounding with<BR>respectable people.<BR>--भट्टः N. of a<BR>renowned astronomer, the inventor<BR>of Algebra among the Hindus; he<BR>flourished before the 5th century<BR>of the Christian era.<BR>--भावः<BR>honourable character or behaviour.<BR>--मार्गः the path or course of<BR>the respectable, a respectable way.<BR>--मिश्र a. respectable, worthy,<BR>distinguished.<BR>--(श्रः) a gentleman, a<BR>man of consequence; (pl.) {1} worthy<BR>or respectable men, an assembly of<BR>honourable men; आर्यमिश्रान्<BR>विज्ञापयामि V. 1. {2} your reverence or<BR>honour (a respectful address);<BR>नन्वार्यमिश्रैः प्रथममेव आज्ञप्तं Ś. 1; आर्यमिश्राः<BR>प्रमाणं M. 1.<BR>--युवन् m. an Āryan<BR>youth.<BR>--रूप a. having only the<BR>form of an Āryan, a hypocrite,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-b" target="_blank">Page0257-b+ 56</a>]<BR>impostor.<BR>--लिंगिन् m. an impostor;<BR>Ms. 9. 260.<BR>--वृत्त a. virtuous, good,<BR>pious; Ms. 9. 253; R. 14. 55.<BR>--(त्तं)<BR>the conduct of an Āryan or<BR>nobleman; Ms. 4. 175.<BR>--वेश a.<BR>well-clothed, having a respectable dress, fine.<BR>--व्रत a. observing the laws and<BR>ordinances of the Āryans or<BR>noblemen.<BR>--(तं) the duty of an Āryan.<BR>--श्वेतः a noble or honourable man.<BR>--संघः the whole body of the Āryans.<BR>--सत्यं a noble or sublime truth;<BR>(there are four such truths<BR>forming the chief principles of<BR>Buddhism).<BR>--हलं ind. [cf. P. I. 1. 47]<BR>forcibly.<BR>--हृद्य a. liked by the<BR>noble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0256-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यकः|आर्यक|आर्य्यक|आर्य्यकं|आर्य्यकः
आर्यकः [आर्य-स्वार्थे-कन्]<BR>1 An<BR>honourable or respectable man.<BR>--2 A<BR>grand-father.<BR>--3 N. of a cowherd<BR>who became a king; cf. Mk. 7.<BR>--कं A ceremony performed to the<BR>manes or the vessel used in<BR>sacrifices to the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यका|आर्य्यका
आर्यका, आर्यिका<BR>1 A respectable<BR>woman.<BR>--2 N. of a Nakṣatra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यिका|आर्य्यिका
आर्यका, आर्यिका<BR>1 A respectable<BR>woman.<BR>--2 N. of a Nakṣatra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्वाक्|आर्व्वाक्
आर्वाक् ind. After, afterwards;<BR>behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्श
आर्श a. Belonging to the<BR>antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्ष|आर्षः
आर्ष a. (र्षी f.) [ऋषेरिदं अण्]<BR>1<BR>Used by a Ṛṣi only, relating or<BR>belonging to sages, archaic, Vedic (opp.<BR>लौकिक or classical); आर्षःप्रयोगः; संबुद्धौ<BR>शाकल्यस्येतावनार्षे Sk.; आर्षो धर्मः<BR>Ms. 3. 29; Y. 1. 59; आर्षः प्रत्ययः<BR>P. II. 4. 58.<BR>--2 Sacred, holy, divine,<BR>superhuman; U. 6.<BR>--र्षः A form<BR>of marriage derived from the<BR>Ṛṣis; one of the eight forms<BR>of marriage in which the father<BR>of the bride receives one or two<BR>pairs of cows from the bride-groom;<BR>आदायार्षस्तु गोद्वयम् Y. 1. 59;<BR>Ms. 3. 53, 9. 196; for the names of the<BR>{8} forms see उद्वाह; आर्षोढा a wife<BR>married according to this form.<BR>--र्षा A class of Vedic metres.<BR>--र्षं<BR>1 The holy text, the Vedas.<BR>--2 Sacred descent.<BR>--3 Derivation<BR>(of a poem) from a Ṛṣi author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षेय
आर्षेय a. (यी f.) [ऋषि-ढक्]<BR>1 Relating to a Ṛṣi.<BR>--2 Worthy,<BR>venerable, respectable.<BR>--यं<BR>1<BR>Sacred descent.<BR>--2 A collection of<BR>Ṛṣis (ऋषिसमूहः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभ
आर्षभ a. (भी f.) [ऋषभ-अण्]<BR>Derived from or produced by a bull;<BR>Ms. 9. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्षभ्यः|आर्षभ्य
आर्षभ्यः [ऋषभ-ञ्य] A steer<BR>sufficiently full-grown to be used or<BR>let loose, one fit to be castrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत|आर्हतः
आर्हत a. (ती f.) [अर्हत्-अण्]<BR>Belonging to the Jaina doctrines.<BR>--तः A Jaina, a follower of Jaina<BR>doctrines.<BR>--तं The doctrines of the<BR>Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हत्यं|आर्हत्य
आर्हत्यं The quality or practice of<BR>an Arhat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हंती
आर्हंती --त्यं [P. V. 1. 124 Vārt.]<BR>Fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्हंत्यं|आर्हन्त्य
आर्हंती --त्यं [P. V. 1. 124 Vārt.]<BR>Fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आल|आलं|आलः
आल a. [आ-अल्-पर्याप्तौ अच्] Large,<BR>extensive.<BR>--लः, --लं<BR>1 Spawn, any<BR>discharge of venomous matter<BR>from poisonous animals; ˚अक्त<BR>anointed with poison as an<BR>arrow.<BR>--2 Trick, fraud; येषां<BR>श्रुतमालजालाय K. 288; ˚जालानि चिंतयंती<BR>310.<BR>--3 Yellow arsenic, orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्ष्
आलक्ष् {c10c} U. To descry, behold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्षि
आलक्षि a. [लक्ष्-इन्] Knowing,<BR>seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्ष्य
आलक्ष्य pot. p.<BR>1 Visible,<BR>apparent; R. 13. 30.<BR>--2 Slightly<BR>visible; ˚दंतमुकुलान् Ś. 7. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलक्षण्यं|आलक्षण्य
आलक्षण्यं [अलक्षणस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>Misfortune, crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलगर्दः|आलगर्द|आलगर्द्द|आलगर्द्दः
आलगर्दः [अलगर्द एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>A water cobra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलप्
आलप् {c1c} P. To address, speak<BR>to, converse; कमालपामि K. 164; तस्या<BR>नामधेयेन भर्त्रादेव्यालपिता V. 2<BR>addressed. --Caus. To talk with, engage<BR>in conversation with, to question;<BR>यदा कश्चित्त्वामालापयिष्यति Pt. 5,<BR>1. 387; K. 188.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापः|आलाप
आलापः<BR>1 Talking, speaking to,<BR>speech, conversation; अये दक्षिणेन<BR>वृक्षवाटिकामालाप इव श्रूयते Ś. 1;<BR>प्रवसनालाप Amaru. 97; ललितालापे<BR>Śrut. 36.<BR>--2 Narration, mention.<BR>--3<BR>The seven notes in music (Mar. सा,<BR>रि, ग, म, प, ध, नि).<BR>--4 Statement of<BR>a question in an arithmetical or<BR>algebraical sum.<BR>--5 A question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापन
आलापन a. Causing to speak or<BR>converse with.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Speaking to,<BR>conversation.<BR>--2 Congratulation (<BR>स्वस्तिवाचनं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाप्य|आलाप्यः
आलाप्य, --लापनीय pot. p. To be<BR>spoken to, conversed with or<BR>narrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापनीय
आलाप्य, --लापनीय pot. p. To be<BR>spoken to, conversed with or<BR>narrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0257-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलापिन्
आलापिन् a. Speaking to,<BR>conversing with.<BR>--नी A lute made of a<BR>gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभ्
आलभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To touch;<BR>गामालभ्यार्कमीक्ष्य वा Ms. 5. 87, 4. 117;<BR>Bk. 14. 91; सत्येनायुधमालभे; सत्येन (सत्यं)<BR>आत्मानमालभे Mb.<BR>--2 To get, attain<BR>to; अतितरां कांतिमालप्स्यते ते (वपुः)<BR>Me. 15 v. l.; Kām. 9. 63.<BR>--3 To kill,<BR>immolate (as a victim in sacrifices);<BR>प्रातर्वै पशूनालभंते Śat. Br.; गर्दभं<BR>पशुमालभ्य Y. 3. 280.<BR>--4 To take hold<BR>of, seize, grasp, handle.<BR>--5 To gain<BR>or win over. --Caus.<BR>1 To touch.<BR>--2 To commence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलब्ध
आलब्ध p. p.<BR>1 Touched; united or<BR>in contact with.<BR>--2 Killed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलब्धिः|आलब्धि
आलब्धिः f.<BR>1 Touching.<BR>--2<BR>Killing; immolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभनं|आलभन
आलभनं<BR>1 Taking hold of, seizing.<BR>--2 Touching.<BR>--3 Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभ्य
आलभ्य, आल(लं)भनीय pot. p.<BR>To be killed or sacrificed; to be<BR>touched or rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलभनीय
आलभ्य, आल(लं)भनीय pot. p.<BR>To be killed or sacrificed; to be<BR>touched or rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलंभनीय|आलम्भनीय
आलभ्य, आल(लं)भनीय pot. p.<BR>To be killed or sacrificed; to be<BR>touched or rubbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलंभः|आलम्भ|आलम्भः
आलंभः, --भनं [आ-लभ् घञ् ल्यट् मुम्]<BR>1<BR>Taking hold of, seizing, touching;<BR>Y. 3. 157; Ms. 2. 179.<BR>--2 Tearing<BR>off, uprooting (of plants);<BR>Ms. 11. 145.<BR>--3 Killing (especially an<BR>animal at a sacrifice); अश्वालंभं<BR>गवालंभं Ādipurāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलंभनं|आलम्भन
आलंभः, --भनं [आ-लभ् घञ् ल्यट् मुम्]<BR>1<BR>Taking hold of, seizing, touching;<BR>Y. 3. 157; Ms. 2. 179.<BR>--2 Tearing<BR>off, uprooting (of plants);<BR>Ms. 11. 145.<BR>--3 Killing (especially an<BR>animal at a sacrifice); अश्वालंभं<BR>गवालंभं Ādipurāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलंभिन्|आलम्भिन्
आलंभिन् a. Touching, seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलंब्|आलम्ब्
आलंब् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To rest or lean<BR>upon, support oneself on;<BR>शाखामालंब्य Rām.<BR>--2 To lay hold of, seize,<BR>take; अथालंब्य धनू रामः Bk. 6. 35,<BR>14. 95.<BR>--3 To support, hold or take<BR>up; आधोरणालंबितं R. 18. 39.<BR>--4 To<BR>win, conquer, overcome; तस्य<BR>कविता मच्चित्तमालंबते Dhūrtas.<BR>--5 To<BR>resort to, have recourse to, take,<BR>assume; अमुमेवार्थमालंब्य Mu. 2. 20;<BR>स्वातंत्र्यमालंब्य K. 181; Ki. 13. 14;<BR>यशःशरीरं नवमाललंबे Mv. 7. 18 obtained;<BR>Ki. 17. 34; so ध्यानं, धैर्यं, क्रोधं, औदास्यं,<BR>दक्षिणां दिशं &c.<BR>--6 To hang from,<BR>be suspended; मुखालंबितहेमसूत्रं<BR>V. 5. 2.<BR>--7 To depend upon; तमालंब्य<BR>रसोद्गमात् S. D. 63.<BR>--8 To stretch<BR>forth; V. 4. 34.<BR>--9 To strike up<BR>(a tune or note).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलंब|आलम्ब|आलम्बः
आलंब a. Hanging down.<BR>--बः<BR>1<BR>Depending on or from.<BR>--2 That on<BR>which one rests or leans, prop, stay;<BR>इह हि पततां नास्त्यालंबो न चापि निवर्तनं<BR>Śānti. 3. 2.<BR>--3 Support, protection;<BR>तवालंबादंव स्फुरदलघुगर्वेण सहसा Jag.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-b" target="_blank">Page0258-b+ 58</a>]<BR>सीतां शून्ये यथासुखं निरालंबां हरिष्यामि<BR>Rām.<BR>--4 Receptacle.<BR>--5 A<BR>perpendicular.<BR>--बा N. of a plant with<BR>poisonous leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलंबनं|आलम्बन|आलम्बनं
आलंबनं<BR>1 Depending on or from,<BR>hanging from.<BR>--2 Support, prop,<BR>stay; Ki. 2. 13; Pt. 1. 32;<BR>sustaining, supporting; Me. 4.<BR>--3<BR>Receptacle, abode; U. 6. 10.<BR>--4 Reason,<BR>cause.<BR>--5 Base.<BR>--6 (In Rhet.) That<BR>on which a रस or sentiment, as it<BR>were hangs, person or thing with<BR>reference to which a sentiment<BR>arises, the natural and necessary<BR>connection of sentiment with the cause<BR>which excites it. The causes (विभाव)<BR>giving rise to a Rasa are classified<BR>as two:<BR>--आलंबन and उद्दीपन; e. g. in<BR>the Bībhatsa sentiment stinking<BR>flesh &c. is the आलंबन of the Rasa,<BR>and the attendant circumstances<BR>which enhance the feeling of<BR>loathing (the worms &c. in the flesh)<BR>are its उद्दीपनानि (exciters); for the<BR>other Rasas see S. D. 210-238.<BR>--7<BR>The mental exercise practised by<BR>the Yogin in endeavouring to bring<BR>before his thoughts the gross form<BR>of the Eternal.<BR>--8 Silent repetition<BR>of a prayer.<BR>--9 (With Buddhists)<BR>The five attributes of things<BR>corresponding to the five senses, i. e. रूप,<BR>रस, गंध, स्पर्श and शब्द.<BR>--10 Dharma<BR>or law corresponding to manas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलंबित|आलम्बित
आलंबित p. p.<BR>1 Pendent,<BR>suspended.<BR>--2 Supported, sustained, held;<BR>R. 7. 7; V. 5. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलंबिन्|आलम्बिन्
आलंबिन् a.<BR>1 Hanging from,<BR>resting or leaning upon; दशालंबी शाटकः<BR>Pt. 1. 144; depending on; R. 12. 85.<BR>--2 Laying hold of, supporting,<BR>maintaining, upholding; कुलालंबी<BR>पुत्रः H. Pr. 20.<BR>--3 Wearing;<BR>गजाजिनालंबि Ku. 5. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलर्क
आलर्क a. [अलर्कस्येदं अण]<BR>Relating to or caused by a mad dog;<BR>आलर्कं विषमिव सर्वतः प्रसृप्तं U. 1. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवण्यं|आलवण्य
आलवण्यं [अलवणस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Insipidity, tastelessness.<BR>--2<BR>Ugliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलवालं|आलवाल
आलवालं [आसमंतात् लवं जललवं<BR>आलाति, आ-ला-क Tv.] A basin or<BR>trench for water (round the root<BR>of a tree); ˚पूरणे नियुक्ता Ś. 1;<BR>विश्वासाय विहङ्गानामालवालाम्बुपायिनां<BR>R. 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस|आलसः
आलस a. (सी f.) [आलसति ईषत्<BR>व्याप्रियते अच्] Idle, lazy, slothful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलस्य|आलस्यं|आलस्यः
आलस्य a. Idle, slothful, apathetic.<BR>--स्यं [अलसस्य भावः, ष्यञ्]<BR>Idleness, sloth, want of energy; शक्तस्य<BR>चाप्यनुत्साहः कर्मस्वालस्यमुच्यते Suśr.;<BR>आलस्य ‘want of energy’ is<BR>regarded as one of the 33 subordinate<BR>feelings (व्यभिचारिभाव); for<BR>example: --न तथा भूषयत्यंगं न तथा भाषते<BR>सखीं । जृंभते मुहुरासीना बाला<BR>गर्भभरालसा S. D. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलातं|आलात
आलातं [अलातमेव स्वार्थे अण्] A<BR>fire-brand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलानं|आलान
आलानं [आलीयतेऽत्र, आ-ली-ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>The post to which an elephant is<BR>tied; tying post, also the rope that<BR>ties him; अरुंतुदमिवालानमनिर्वाणस्य<BR>दंतिनः R. 1. 71, 4. 69, 81; आलाने गृह्यते<BR>हस्ती Mk. 1. 50.<BR>--2 A fetter, tie.<BR>--3<BR>A chain, rope, string.<BR>--4 Tying,<BR>binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलानिक
आलानिक a. (की f.) [आलान-ठक्]<BR>Serving as a post to which an<BR>elephant is tied; आलानिकं स्थाणुमिव<BR>द्विपेंद्रः R. 14. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाबुः|आलाबु
आलाबुः(बूः) f. A pumpkin<BR>gourd; see अलाबु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलाबूः
आलाबुः(बूः) f. A pumpkin<BR>gourd; see अलाबु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलावर्तं|आलावर्त|आलावर्त्त|आलावर्त्तं
आलावर्तं A fan made of cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलास्यः|आलास्य
आलास्यः [आलं पर्याप्तमास्यं अस्य]<BR>A crocodile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलि|आलिः
आलि a.<BR>1 Useless, idle,<BR>unmeaning.<BR>--2 Honest, sincere (विशदाशय).<BR>--लिः<BR>1 A scorpion.<BR>--2 A bee.<BR>--लिः,<BR>--ली f.<BR>1 A female companion or<BR>friend (of a woman); निवार्यतामालि<BR>किमप्ययं बटुः Ku. 5. 83, 7. 68;<BR>Amaru. 23.<BR>--2 A row, range, continuous<BR>line; (cf. आवलि);<BR>तोयांतर्भास्करालीव रेजे मुनिपरंपरा Ku. 6. 49; रथ्यालि<BR>Amaru. 89; खद्योतालि Me. 81.<BR>--3 A<BR>line, streak.<BR>--4 A bridge.<BR>--5 A<BR>dike.<BR>--6 A line, race, family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिख्
आलिख् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To write,<BR>delineate, draw lines; मनो निष्ठाशून्यं भ्रमति<BR>च किमप्यालिखति च Māl. 1. 31;<BR>Mk. 2.<BR>--2 To paint, draw in a picture;<BR>आलिखित इव सर्वतो रंगः Ś. 1; V. 2;<BR>त्वामालिख्य प्रणयकुपितां Me. 105;<BR>R. 19. 19; M. 2. 2.<BR>--3 To portray, write,<BR>sketch.<BR>--4 To scratch, scrape, touch;<BR>as in विंध्यमालिखंतमिवांबरं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखः|आलेख
आलेखः<BR>1 Writing.<BR>--2 A letter,<BR>document.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेखनं|आलेखन|आलेखनः
आलेखनं a. Scratching, painting.<BR>--नी A brush, pencil.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Writing.<BR>--2 Painting.<BR>--3 Scratching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेख्य|आलेख्यं
आलेख्य pot. p. To be written,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">Page0259-a+ 57</a>]<BR>painted &c.<BR>--ख्यं<BR>1 A painting, picture;<BR>इति संरंभिणो वाणीर्बलस्यालेख्यदेवताः<BR>Śi. 2. 67; R. 3. 15; V. 2. 10.<BR>--2<BR>A writing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--लेखा a<BR>painting.<BR>--शेष a. having nothing left<BR>but a painting, i. e. deceased,<BR>dead; आलेख्यशेषस्य पितुः R. 14. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0258-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिंग्|आलिङ्ग्
आलिंग् {c1c} U. or {c10c} P. To<BR>embrace, clasp, encircle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिंगः|आलिङ्ग|आलिङ्गः
आलिंगः<BR>1 Embracing.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिंगनं|आलिङ्गन|आलिंगन|आलिङ्गनं
आलिंगनं Embracing, clasping, an<BR>embrace; (स प्राप) आलिंगननिर्वृतिं<BR>R. 12. 65; (said to be of seven kinds;<BR>आमोद˚, मुदित˚, प्रेमन्˚, मानस˚, रुचि˚,<BR>मदन˚ and विनोद˚).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिंगित|आलिङ्गित|आलिङ्गितः
आलिंगित p. p. Embraced, clasped.<BR>--तः A kind of Mantra of 20 letters.<BR>--तं An embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिंगिन्|आलिङ्गिन्
आलिंगिन् a. Embracing &c. --m.<BR>(--गी), आलिंग्यः A small drum<BR>shaped like a barley-corn (यव);<BR>चतुरंगुलहीनोंक्यान्मुखे चैकांगुलेन यः । यवाकृतिः<BR>स आलिंग्य आलिंग्य स हि वाद्यते ॥<BR>Śabdārṇava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिंजरः|आलिञ्जर|आलिंजर|आलिञ्जरः
आलिंजरः [अलिंजर एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>A large earthen water-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिंदः|आलिन्द|आलिंद|आलिन्दः
आलिंदः, --दकः [अलिंद एव स्वार्थे<BR>अण्]<BR>1 A terrace before a house.<BR>--2<BR>A raised place for sleeping upon;<BR>see अलिंद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिंदकः|आलिन्दक|आलिन्दकः
आलिंदः, --दकः [अलिंद एव स्वार्थे<BR>अण्]<BR>1 A terrace before a house.<BR>--2<BR>A raised place for sleeping upon;<BR>see अलिंद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिन्
आलिन् m. A scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिप्
आलिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To anoint,<BR>besmear; आलिंपन्नमृतमयैरिव प्रलेपैः<BR>U. 3. 39; plaster, bedaub.<BR>--2 To rub (on<BR>the body); आलिप्यते चंदनमंगनाभिः<BR>Rs. 6. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिप
आलिप a. Anointing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलिंपनं|आलिम्पन|आलिम्पनं
आलिंपनं [लिप्-ल्युट्-मुम्]<BR>Whitening the walls, floor &c. on festive<BR>occasions; cf. आदीपन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलेप|आलेपः
आलेप a. To be anointed.<BR>--पः,<BR>--पनं<BR>1 Anointing, smearing.<BR>--2<BR>Liniment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आली
आली = आलि q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आली
आली {c4c} A.<BR>1 To settle down<BR>upon; निर्भिद्योपरि<BR>कर्णिकारकुसुमान्यालीयते षट्पदः V. 2. 23.<BR>--2 To faint;<BR>मुहुरालीयते भीता Mb.<BR>--3 To melt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलयः|आलय|आलयं
आलयः, --यं [आलीयतेऽस्मिन्, आली-अच्]<BR>1 An abode, a house, a dwelling;<BR>आलयं देवशत्रूणां सुघोरं खांडवं वनं Mb.;<BR>न हि दुष्टात्मनामार्या निवसंत्यालये चिरं<BR>Rām.; सर्वाञ्जनस्थानकृतालयान् Rām.<BR>who lived or dwelt in Janasthāna.<BR>--2 A receptacle, seat, place;<BR>हिमालयो नाम नगाधिराजः Ku. 1. 1; so<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">Page0259-b+ 56</a>]<BR>देवालयं, विद्यालयं &c; fig. also; दुःख˚<BR>Bg. 8. 15; गुण˚.<BR>--3 Contact.<BR>--यं<BR>ind. Till destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलयं|आलय|आलयः
आलयः, --यं [आलीयतेऽस्मिन्, आली-अच्]<BR>1 An abode, a house, a dwelling;<BR>आलयं देवशत्रूणां सुघोरं खांडवं वनं Mb.;<BR>न हि दुष्टात्मनामार्या निवसंत्यालये चिरं<BR>Rām.; सर्वाञ्जनस्थानकृतालयान् Rām.<BR>who lived or dwelt in Janasthāna.<BR>--2 A receptacle, seat, place;<BR>हिमालयो नाम नगाधिराजः Ku. 1. 1; so<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">Page0259-b+ 56</a>]<BR>देवालयं, विद्यालयं &c; fig. also; दुःख˚<BR>Bg. 8. 15; गुण˚.<BR>--3 Contact.<BR>--यं<BR>ind. Till destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीन
आलीन p. p.<BR>1 Embraced.<BR>--2<BR>Sticking or clinging to;<BR>आलीनचंदनौ R. 4. 51; so ˚भ्रमरे पद्मे.<BR>--3<BR>Melted, fused.<BR>--नं, --नकं<BR>1 Tin.<BR>--2<BR>Lead.<BR>--3 Contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढ|आलीढं
आलीढ p. p. [आ-लिह् क्त]<BR>1<BR>Licked, eaten, lapped, scraped.<BR>--2<BR>Wounded, hurt;<BR>सेनान्यमालीढमिवासुरास्त्रैः R. 2. 37.<BR>--3 Closed (as in sleep)<BR>Dk. 117.<BR>--ढं A particular attitude<BR>in shooting, the right knee being<BR>advanced and the left leg retracted;<BR>अतिष्ठदालीढविशेषशोभिना R. 3. 52;<BR>see Malli. on Ku. 3. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलीढकं|आलीढक
आलीढकं The frolicking of a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुः|आलु
आलुः<BR>1 An owl.<BR>--2 An esculent<BR>root (not applied to potato &c.).<BR>--3 Ebony; black ebony.<BR>--लुः f.<BR>A pitcher, water-jar.<BR>--लु (n.) A<BR>raft, float.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुकः|आलुक|आलुकं
आलुकः<BR>1 A kind of ebony (कामालु).<BR>--2 An epithet of Śeṣa.<BR>--कं An<BR>esculent root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुंचनं|आलुञ्चन
आलुंचनं Rending, tearing to<BR>pieces; श्येनो ग्रहालुंचने Mk. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुड्
आलुड् {c1c} P. or Caus. To stir up,<BR>agitate, shake, disturb;<BR>कौरववनमालोडयंतौ Ve. 3, 4; विषमालोड्य<BR>पास्यामि Mb.; (fig.) to dive into;<BR>Pt. 1; to examine scrutinizingly;<BR>भरतादिमतं सर्वमालोड्यातिप्रयत्नतः ।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोडनं|आलोडन
आलोडनं<BR>1 Stirring, shaking,<BR>agitating.<BR>--2 Mixing, blending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोडित
आलोडित p. p.<BR>1 Shaken, agitated.<BR>--2 Mixed, blended.<BR>--3 Powdered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुंटनं|आलुण्टन
आलुंटनं Plundering, taking<BR>away by force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलुल
आलुल a. Shaking, unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलू
आलू See आलु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलून
आलून p. p. Cut, cut off;<BR>Ku. 2. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोक्
आलोक् {c1c} A., {c10c} P.<BR>1 To see,<BR>perceive, behold; त्वन्मार्गमालोकते<BR>S. D.; अथालुलोके तपोवनं Bk. 2. 24;<BR>used in an astrological sense also.<BR>--2 To consider, regard, contemplate;<BR>तृणमिब जगज्जालमालोकयामः<BR>Bh. 3. 66.<BR>--3 To express congratulations,<BR>greet; इति वीरलोक आलोकयितुं प्रवृत्तः<BR>Ve. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकः|आलोक
आलोकः, --कनं<BR>1 Seeing, beholding.<BR>--2 Sight, aspect, appearance;<BR>यदालोके सूक्ष्मं Ś. 1. 9; Ku. 7. 22, 46;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">Page0259-c+ 55</a>]<BR>सुख˚ V. 4. 24; Ś. 1. 33;<BR>R. 1. 84; Me. 3, 37.<BR>--3 Range of sight;<BR>आलोके ते निपतति पुरा सा बलिव्याकुला<BR>वा Me. 85; R. 7. 5; Ku. 2. 45.<BR>--4<BR>Light, lustre, splendour; आलोकमार्गं<BR>सहसा व्रजंत्या R. 7. 6 air-hole, or<BR>window; निरालोकं लोकं Māl. 5. 30;<BR>9. 37; 10. 4, 11; Ve. 2; K. 160,<BR>290, 348, 68, 98.<BR>--5 Panegyric,<BR>praise, complimentary language;<BR>especially, a word of praise uttered<BR>by a bard (such as जय, आलोकय);<BR>ययावुदीरितालोकः R. 17. 27, 2. 9;<BR>K. 14.<BR>--6 Section, chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकनं|आलोकन
आलोकः, --कनं<BR>1 Seeing, beholding.<BR>--2 Sight, aspect, appearance;<BR>यदालोके सूक्ष्मं Ś. 1. 9; Ku. 7. 22, 46;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">Page0259-c+ 55</a>]<BR>सुख˚ V. 4. 24; Ś. 1. 33;<BR>R. 1. 84; Me. 3, 37.<BR>--3 Range of sight;<BR>आलोके ते निपतति पुरा सा बलिव्याकुला<BR>वा Me. 85; R. 7. 5; Ku. 2. 45.<BR>--4<BR>Light, lustre, splendour; आलोकमार्गं<BR>सहसा व्रजंत्या R. 7. 6 air-hole, or<BR>window; निरालोकं लोकं Māl. 5. 30;<BR>9. 37; 10. 4, 11; Ve. 2; K. 160,<BR>290, 348, 68, 98.<BR>--5 Panegyric,<BR>praise, complimentary language;<BR>especially, a word of praise uttered<BR>by a bard (such as जय, आलोकय);<BR>ययावुदीरितालोकः R. 17. 27, 2. 9;<BR>K. 14.<BR>--6 Section, chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकित
आलोकित p. p. Seen, beheld &c.<BR>--तं A look, glance; Māl. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोकिन्
आलोकिन् a. Seeing, beholding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोच्
आलोच् {c1c} A., {c10c} U.<BR>1 To see,<BR>perceive.<BR>--2 To consider, reflect, think,<BR>ponder over, study; K. 7;<BR>आलोचयंतो विस्तारमंभसां दक्षिणोदधेः<BR>Bk. 7. 40; इति-एवं-आलोच्य so thinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचक
आलोचक a.<BR>1 Seeing, beholding.<BR>--2 Causing to see.<BR>--कं The faculty<BR>of vision, the cause of sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचनं|आलोचन
आलोचनं, --ना<BR>1 Seeing, perceiving,<BR>survey, view.<BR>--2 Considering,<BR>reflecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोचना
आलोचनं, --ना<BR>1 Seeing, perceiving,<BR>survey, view.<BR>--2 Considering,<BR>reflecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोल|आलोलः
आलोल a. Slightly<BR>1 trembling,<BR>rolling (as eyes); आलोलायतलोचनाः<BR>Bh. 3. 48.<BR>--2 Shaken, agitated;<BR>आलोलामलकावलीं Amaru. 3; क्रीडालोलाः<BR>Me. 61.<BR>--लः Trembling, agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आलोलित
आलोलित a. Shaken, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवक
आवक a. [अव्-ण्वुल्] Protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवत्|आवन्त्
आवत् f. Ved. Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवनेयः|आवनेय
आवनेयः [अवंन्या अपत्यं ढक्] ‘Son<BR>of the earth’, an epithet of the<BR>planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवंतः|आवन्त|आवन्तः
आवंतः [अवंतेरयं राजा अण्] A<BR>king of Avantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवंतिक|आवन्तिक|आवन्तिकः
आवंतिक a. (की f.) Coming from<BR>or belonging to Avantī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवंत्य|आवन्त्य|आवन्त्यः
आवंत्य a. [अवंतिषु भवः ञ्य] Coming<BR>from or belonging to Avantī.<BR>--त्यः<BR>1 A prince or an inhabitant of<BR>Avantī.<BR>--2 The offspring of a<BR>degraded Brāhmaṇa; see<BR>Ms. 10. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवप्
आवप् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To scatter, throw<BR>about; वयोभ्यश्चावपेद्भुवि Mb.; so अक्षान्<BR>throws.<BR>--2 To sow (as seed).<BR>--3 To fit<BR>in, insert.<BR>--4 To pour out or forth.<BR>--5 To offer (as in a sacrifice),<BR>perform (as a Śrāddha). --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">Page0260-a+ 55</a>]<BR>shave, cut off.<BR>--2 To trim.<BR>--3 To<BR>mix with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0259-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवपनं|आवपन
आवपनं<BR>1 The act of sowing,<BR>throwing, scattering.<BR>--2 Sowing<BR>seed.<BR>--3 Wearing.<BR>--4 Shaving.<BR>--5<BR>A vessel, jar, ewer.<BR>--6 Instilling,<BR>inserting.<BR>--नी Ved. A vessel, jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवपंतिक|आवपन्तिक
आवपंतिक a. Ved. Scattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाप|आवापः
आवाप a. [आवप्-घञ्] Throwing,<BR>scattering; (as in अक्षावाप q. v.).<BR>--पः<BR>1 Sowing seed.<BR>--2 Scattering,<BR>throwing in general; casting,<BR>directing.<BR>--3 Mixing, inserting.<BR>--4<BR>Especially, throwing additional<BR>ingredients into a compound in<BR>course of preparation.<BR>--5 A basin<BR>for water round the root of a tree<BR>(आलवाल).<BR>--6 A vessel, jar for corn.<BR>--7 Setting out or arranging vessels.<BR>--8 Hostile purpose, intention of<BR>fighting (with another); foreign<BR>affairs; Śi. 2. 88.<BR>--9 A principal<BR>sacrifice or oblation to fire.<BR>--10 A<BR>kind of drink.<BR>--11 A bracelet (<BR>आवापक).<BR>--12 Uneven ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापकः|आवापक
आवापकः A bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापनं|आवापन
आवापनं<BR>1 A loom.<BR>--2 A reel or<BR>frame for winding thread.<BR>--3<BR>Shaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवापिक
आवापिक a. [आवापाय साधु ठक्]<BR>1<BR>Good for sowing, shaving &c.<BR>--2<BR>Additional, supplementary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवयः|आवय
आवयः<BR>1 Coming.<BR>--2 One who<BR>comes.<BR>--3 N. of a country.<BR>--यः,<BR>--या Water (Ved.).<BR>--यं Ved.<BR>Nonconception, barrenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवयाज्
आवयाज् m. One who makes a<BR>sacrifice to reach the gods (Sāy.);<BR>or one who averts by means of<BR>sacrifices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरक
आवरक, आवरण &c. see आवृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरण|आवरणं
आवरक, आवरण &c. see आवृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरसमक
आवरसमक a. (की f.) [<BR>अवरसमे देयमृणं वुञ्] (A debt) To be paid<BR>in the following year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्हित|आवर्हितः
आव(ब)र्हित a. Eradicated,<BR>uprooted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आबर्हित
आव(ब)र्हित a. Eradicated,<BR>uprooted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवलिः|आवलि
आवलिः, --ली f. [आ-वल्-इन् वा<BR>ङीप्]<BR>1 A line, row, range;<BR>अरावलीं V. 1. 4; so अलक˚, धूम˚, दंत˚,<BR>हार˚, रत्न˚ &c.<BR>--2 A series,<BR>continuous line.<BR>--3 A dynasty, lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवली
आवलिः, --ली f. [आ-वल्-इन् वा<BR>ङीप्]<BR>1 A line, row, range;<BR>अरावलीं V. 1. 4; so अलक˚, धूम˚, दंत˚,<BR>हार˚, रत्न˚ &c.<BR>--2 A series,<BR>continuous line.<BR>--3 A dynasty, lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवलित
आवलित a. [वल्-क्त] Slightly<BR>turned; K. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवल्गित
आवल्गित a. Shaking gently;<BR>Ki. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवल्गुज
आवल्गुज a. Produced from the<BR>plant अवल्गुज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यं|आवश्य
आवश्यं [अवश्य-अण्] Necessity,<BR>inevitable act or conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यक|आवश्यकं
आवश्यक a. (की f.) [अवश्य-वुञ्]<BR>Inevitable, necessary;<BR>एतेष्वावश्यकस्त्वसौ Bhāṣā P. 22, 20.<BR>--कं<BR>1<BR>Necessity, inevitable act or duty.<BR>˚कृ to do what nature compels<BR>one to do; Ms. 4. 93.<BR>--2 An<BR>inevitable conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यकता
आवश्यकता, --त्वं Necessity,<BR>inevitability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवश्यकत्वं|आवश्यकत्व
आवश्यकता, --त्वं Necessity,<BR>inevitability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवस्
आवस् {c1c} P. (With acc.)<BR>1 To<BR>inhabit, dwell in; रविमावसते सतां<BR>क्रियायै V. 3. 7; पुरीमिमामावसत् Rām.;<BR>sometimes with loc.; Ms. 7. 69;<BR>Y. 1. 320.<BR>--2 To be occupied or<BR>engaged, enter upon; गृहस्थाश्रमं<BR>Ms. 3. 2.<BR>--3 To take part carnally;<BR>cohabit.<BR>--4 To pass, spend (as night).<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To allow one to dwell,<BR>receive hospitably.<BR>--2 To inhabit,<BR>settle in a place.<BR>--3 To halt or<BR>encamp (for the night).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसतिः|आवसति
आवसतिः f. Night(the time<BR>during which one rests); mid-night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथः|आवसथ|आवसथं
आवसथः [आवस्-अथच् Uṇ. 3. 116]<BR>1 A dwelling, dwelling-place,<BR>residence, house, habitation;<BR>निवसन्नावसथे पुराद्बहिः R. 8. 14.<BR>--2 A<BR>resting place; asylum.<BR>--3 A dwelling<BR>for pupils and ascetics.<BR>--4 A village.<BR>--5 A particular religious<BR>observance.<BR>--6 A fire-sanctuary, a place<BR>where sacrificial fire is preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथिक|आवसथिकः
आवसथिक a. (की f.) [आवसथे गृहे<BR>वसति ठण् Tv.]<BR>1 Inhabiting a house.<BR>--2 Household, domestic.<BR>--3<BR>Keeping a sacred fire in a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसथ्य|आवसथ्यः
आवसथ्य a. [आवसथ-ञ्य] Being in<BR>a house.<BR>--थ्यः The sacred fire kept<BR>in the house, one of the five fires<BR>used in sacrifices; see पंचाग्नि.<BR>--थ्यः --थ्यं<BR>A dwelling for pupils and ascetics.<BR>--थ्यं<BR>1 Placing a sacred fire within<BR>a house.<BR>--2 A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवासः|आवास
आवासः (a) A house, habitation,<BR>abode; आवासवृक्षोन्मुखबर्हिणानि<BR>R. 2. 17. (b) Apartment, room. (c)<BR>A place of refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसान
आवसान a. [अवसानमभिजनोऽस्य<BR>अञ्] Living at the extremity of a<BR>town (as a चांडाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवसित|आवसितं
आवसित a. [आ-अव-सो-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Finished or completed.<BR>--2 Decided,<BR>determined, settled.<BR>--3 Stored<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">Page0260-c+ 57</a>]<BR>(as grain); winnowed.<BR>--4 Ripe,<BR>full-grown.<BR>--तं Ripe corn (when<BR>thrashed.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवस्थिक
आवस्थिक a. (की f.) [अवस्थायां<BR>भवः ठञ्] Suited or adapted to<BR>circumstances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवह्
आवह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring; अग्ने<BR>पत्नीरिहावह Rv. 1. 22. 9.<BR>--2 To bring<BR>home (as a bride).<BR>--3 To conduce,<BR>lead or tend to, produce, bring on;<BR>व्रीडमावहति मे स संप्रति R. 11. 73<BR>shames me; मनोरुजमावहन् Ś. 3. 4<BR>tending to mental anguish; न मे<BR>सौख्यमावहति does not tend to<BR>my happiness Pt. 1; संगमं K. 174;<BR>Ms. 3. 82.<BR>--4 To pay; Y. 2. 193.<BR>--5 To lead forth, conduct away.<BR>--6 To flow (as blood &c.).<BR>--7<BR>To bear, support, wear;<BR>मंडनमावहंतिं Ch. P. 18.<BR>--8 To apply, use,<BR>employ; मा रोदीर्धैर्यमावह Mārk. P.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To send for, cause to be<BR>brought.<BR>--2 To invoke a deity<BR>(by means of Mantras);<BR>गणपतिमावाहयामि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवह|आवहः
आवह a. (As last member of<BR>comp.) Producing, leading or<BR>tending to, bringing on,<BR>क्लेशावहा भर्तुरलक्षणाऽहं R. 14. 5; so<BR>दुःख˚, भय˚, क्षय˚ &c.<BR>--हः<BR>1 N. of one<BR>of the seven winds or bands of air,<BR>usually assigned to the भुवर्लोक or<BR>atmospheric region between the<BR>भूर्लोक and स्वर्लोक.<BR>--2 One of the<BR>seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहनं|आवहन
आवहनं Bringing near, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवहमान|आवहमानं
आवहमान a.<BR>1 Bringing near.<BR>--2<BR>Followed or succeeded by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाहः|आवाह
आवाहः Marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवाहनं|आवाहन
आवाहनं<BR>1 Sending for, inviting,<BR>calling.<BR>--2 Invoking a deity (to<BR>be present) (opp. विसर्जन); आवाहने<BR>विनियोगः, आवाहनं न जानामि न जानामि<BR>तवार्चनं Pūjā Mantra.<BR>--3 Offering<BR>oblations to fire; Y. 1. 251.<BR>--नी<BR>A particular position of the hands<BR>at the time of invoking a deity;<BR>हस्ताभ्यामंजलिं बद्ध्वाऽनामिकामूलपर्वणोः ।<BR>अंगुष्ठौ निक्षिपेत्सेयं मुद्रा त्वावाहनी स्मृता ॥<BR>Śabdak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवालं|आवाल
आवालं [आ-वल्-णिच् अच् Tv.] A<BR>basin for water round the root of a<BR>tree; cf. आलवालं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविक|आविकः
आविक a. (की f.) [अविना<BR>तल्लोम्ना निर्मितं ठक्]<BR>1 Relating to a sheep;<BR>आविकं क्षीरं Ms. 5. 8, 2. 41.<BR>--2<BR>Woollen.<BR>--कं A woollen cloth,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">Page0261-a+ 56</a>]<BR>blanket; Ms. 5. 120.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सौत्रिक a. made of woollen thread;<BR>Ms. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0260-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविग्न|आविग्नः
आविग्न a. Distressed, troubled.<BR>--ग्नः N. of a fruit-tree (अविग्न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्
आविद् Caus.<BR>1 To make known,<BR>report, declare, announce, tell,<BR>communicate, inform; किमिति<BR>नावेदयसि-अथवा किमावेदितेन Ve. 1; राज्ञ<BR>आवेदयध्वं मां संप्राप्तं Rām; आयुषः<BR>प्रमाणमावेदयति K. 46, 47; आवेदयंति<BR>प्रत्यासन्नमानंदं… निमित्तानि 65, 67<BR>--2 foreshadow; 81, 168; Bk. 3. 49;<BR>Ku. 6. 21; R. 5. 23; आत्मनः सुमहत्कर्म<BR>व्रणैरावेद्य R. 12. 55; K. 158.<BR>--3 To<BR>bring to, offer, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्
आविद् a. Ved.<BR>1 Knowledge.<BR>--2 A<BR>technical name of the Vedic<BR>formulas beginning with आविस् and<BR>आवित्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्वस्
आविद्वस् a. Ved. Knowing<BR>fully, skilled in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदक|आवेदकः
आवेदक a. Making known,<BR>reporting, communicating.<BR>--कः<BR>1 One<BR>who makes known, an informer.<BR>--2<BR>A suitor, plaintiff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदनं|आवेदन
आवेदनं<BR>1 Communicating,<BR>reporting, or addressing respectfully.<BR>--2<BR>Representation.<BR>--3 Stating a<BR>complaint (in law); राज्ञे कुर्यात् पूर्वमावेदनं<BR>यः Nārada.<BR>--4 A plaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदनीय
आवेदनीय, --वेद्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be<BR>declared or reported.<BR>--2 To be made<BR>the subject of a plaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेद्य
आवेदनीय, --वेद्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be<BR>declared or reported.<BR>--2 To be made<BR>the subject of a plaint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदित|आवेदितः
आवेदित p. p. Made known,<BR>communicated &c.<BR>--तः The person to<BR>whom something is made known.<BR>--तं That which is communicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेदिन्
आवेदिन् a.<BR>1 Declaring,<BR>announcing.<BR>--2 Giving orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविदूर्यं|आविदूर्य|आविदूर्य्य
आविदूर्यं [अविदूरस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्ध
आविद्ध, आविध See under आव्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविध|आविधः
आविद्ध, आविध See under आव्यध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भाव|आविर्भावः
आविर्भाव &c. See आविस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविल
आविल a. [आविलति दृष्टिं स्तृणाति विल्<BR>स्तृतौ-क Tv.]<BR>1 Turbid, foul, dirty,<BR>muddy; पंकच्छिदः फलस्येव<BR>निकषेणाविलं पयः M. 2. 8;<BR>तस्याविलांभःपरिशुद्धिहेतोः R. 13. 36.<BR>--2<BR>Impure, spoiled; Ki. 8. 37; fig. also;<BR>त्वदीयैश्चरितैरनाविलैः Ku. 5. 37.<BR>--3<BR>Dark-coloured, dark-blue, darkish;<BR>V. 5. 8.<BR>--4 Dim, obscure; आविलां मृगलेखां<BR>R. 8. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविलयति
आविलयति Den. P. To sully, make<BR>turbid, stain, blot; Ś. 5. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविश्
आविश् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To enter;<BR>गौरीगुरोर्गह्वरमाविवेश R. 2. 26, 3. 28.<BR>--2<BR>To take possession of, possess,<BR>affect; मूढमाविशंति न पंडितं H. 1. 3;<BR>so भयं, मोहः, क्रोधः &c.<BR>--3 To go<BR>towards, approach.<BR>--4 To go or attain<BR>to a particular state; सुखं, मन्युं &c.<BR>--5 To arise. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to<BR>enter.<BR>--2 To possess; K. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्ट|आविष्टः
आविष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Entered.<BR>--2<BR>Possessed (by an evil spirit); K. 120, 167,<BR>318.<BR>--3 Possessed of, seized or<BR>filled with, full of, overpowered or<BR>overcome; भय˚, क्रोध˚, निद्रा˚;<BR>कृपयाविष्टं Bg. 2. 1; भोगिनः कंचुकाविष्टाः<BR>Pt. 1. 65 covered with, clad in.<BR>--4 Engrossed or occupied in,<BR>intent on (तत्पर, उद्युत्क).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--लिंग<BR>a. (a noun) which in every<BR>relationship preserves its own gender<BR>(नियतलिंग); e. g. प्रधानं, अर्धः, उपसर्जनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशः|आवेश
आवेशः<BR>1 Entering into, entrance;<BR>आवेशं कृ Pt. 1 to enter or infuse<BR>oneself into.<BR>--2 Taking possession of,<BR>influence, exercise; स्मय˚ influence of<BR>pride R. 5. 19; so मदन˚, क्रोध˚, भय˚<BR>&c.<BR>--3 Intentness, devotedness to an<BR>object, complete absorption in one<BR>wish or idea.<BR>--4 Pride, arrogance.<BR>--5 Flurry, agitation, anger, passion;<BR>K. 291.<BR>--6 Demoniacal possession.<BR>--7<BR>Apoplectic or epileptic giddiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशनं|आवेशन
आवेशनं<BR>1 Entering, entrance.<BR>--2<BR>Demoniacal possession.<BR>--3 Passion,<BR>anger, fury.<BR>--4 A manufactory,<BR>work-shop; Ms. 9. 265.<BR>--5 The disc<BR>of the sun or the moon.<BR>--6 A house,<BR>dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेशिक|आवेशिकः
आवेशिक a. (की f.) [आवेश-ठञ्]<BR>1 Peculiar, one's own (असाधारण).<BR>--2 Inherent.<BR>--कः A guest, visitor.<BR>--कं<BR>1 Entering into.<BR>--2 Hospitality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविस्
आविस् ind. A particle meaning<BR>‘before the eyes’, ‘openly’,<BR>‘evidently’ (usually prefixed to the<BR>roots अस्, भू and कृ); आचार्यकं<BR>विजयि मान्मथमाविरासीत् Māl. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भू
आविर्भू {c1c} P. To become manifest,<BR>appear, become visible, show<BR>oneself to; तमस्तपति घर्मांशौ<BR>कथमाविर्भविष्यति Ś. 5. 14; तेषामाविरभूद् ब्रह्मा<BR>परिम्लानमुखश्रियां Ku. 2. 2;<BR>आविर्बभूव कुशगर्भमुखं मृगाणां यूथं R. 9. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविर्भावः|आविर्भाव
आविर्भावः<BR>1 Manifestation,<BR>presence, appearance.<BR>--2 An incarnation.<BR>--3 Nature or property of things.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्कृ
आविष्कृ {c8c} U. To make apparent,<BR>lay bare, reveal, show, manifest,<BR>put forth; (याति)<BR>आविष्कृतारुणपुरस्सर एकतोर्कः Ś. 5. 1; Śi. 20. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्करणं|आविष्करण
आविष्करणं, --ष्कारः<BR>1 Manifestation,<BR>making visible, showing; असूया<BR>मुणेषु दोषाविष्करणं Sk.<BR>--2 The means<BR>of making visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्कारः|आविष्कार
आविष्करणं, --ष्कारः<BR>1 Manifestation,<BR>making visible, showing; असूया<BR>मुणेषु दोषाविष्करणं Sk.<BR>--2 The means<BR>of making visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविष्य
आविष्य a. Ved. Manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविस्तराम्
आविस्तराम् ind. In a more<BR>manifest way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवी
आवी f. [अवीरेव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>1 A<BR>woman in her courses.<BR>--2 A<BR>pregnant woman.<BR>--3 The pangs of<BR>childbirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीत
आवीत a. [आ-व्ये-क्त]<BR>1 Worn,<BR>put on, held after throwing round.<BR>--2 Entered, passed, gone.<BR>--तं The<BR>sacrificial cord worn in any<BR>particular position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीतिन्
आवीतिन् m. [आवीत-इति] A<BR>Brāhmaṇa who makes the sacrificial cord<BR>hang over the right shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवीरचूर्णः|आवीरचूर्ण|आवीरचूर्णं|आवीरचूर्ण्ण
आवीरचूर्णः The opposite-leaved<BR>fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवुकः|आवुक
आवुकः A father(in theatrical<BR>language).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवुत्तः|आवुत्त
आवुत्तः A sister's husband;<BR>brother-in-law; U. 1; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृ
आवृ {c5c} {c9c} {c10c} U.<BR>1 To cover, hide,<BR>conceal; आवृणोदात्मनो रंध्रं R. 17. 61;<BR>K. 199; आवरीतुमिवाकाशं Bk. 9. 24;<BR>धूमेनाव्रियते वह्निः Bg. 3. 38.<BR>--2 To fill,<BR>pervade; सर्वमावृत्य तिष्ठति Bg. 13. 13;<BR>Ms. 2. 144.<BR>--3 To choose, desire.<BR>--4 To enclose, obstruct, shut, hem<BR>in, block; आवृत्य पंथानमजस्य तस्थौ<BR>R. 7. 31; 12. 28.<BR>--5 To keep off;<BR>Bk. 14. 109. --Caus.<BR>1 To cover or<BR>conceal.<BR>--2 To ward or keep off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरक
आवरक a. Covering, concealing.<BR>--कं A cover, veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरण|आवरणं
आवरण a. Covering, hiding,<BR>obscuring, obstructing; नेत्रावरणमश्रु<BR>R. 14. 71.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Covering,<BR>concealing, hiding, obscuring; सूर्ये<BR>तपत्यावरणाय दृष्टेः कल्पेत लोकस्य कथं<BR>तमिस्रा R. 5. 13, 10. 46, 19. 16.<BR>--2 Shutting, enclosing, fencing.<BR>--3 A covering, anything that<BR>covers or protects &c.; हस्तौ स्वौ नयति<BR>स्तनावरणतां M. 4. 14; Ś. 3. 22; (fig.)<BR>protection, defence; शीलमावरणं<BR>स्त्रियाः Rām.; चरित्रावरणाः स्त्रियः<BR>Chāṇ. 76.<BR>--4 Obstruction, interruption,<BR>restraint (of bashfulness &c.);<BR>कालेनावरणात्ययात् U. 1. 39.<BR>--5 An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">Page0262-a+ 58</a>]<BR>enclosure, fence, surrounding wall;<BR>लब्धांतरा सावरणेपि गेहे R. 16. 7;<BR>Ki. 5. 25.<BR>--6 A bolt, latch.<BR>--7 A shield.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शक्तिः mental ignorance<BR>(which veils the real nature of<BR>things).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0261-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरितृ
आवरि(री)तृ a. One that covers<BR>or envelops; Ki. 18. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवरीतृ
आवरि(री)तृ a. One that covers<BR>or envelops; Ki. 18. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवारः|आवार
आवारः Enclosing, keeping off, as<BR>in दुरावार q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवारिः|आवारि
आवारिः [आवृ बाहु˚ इण्] A shop,<BR>a stall (n. according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत|आवृतः
आवृत p. p.<BR>1 Covered, screened,<BR>concealed.<BR>--2 Invested, blocked.<BR>--3 Enclosed, surrounded (by a<BR>ditch, wall &c.).<BR>--4 Spread,<BR>overspread, overcast; आवृते नभस्तले H. 3.<BR>--5 Filled or abounding with.<BR>--तः<BR>A man of mixed origin, the son of<BR>a Brāhmaṇa by a woman of the<BR>Ugra caste; Ms. 10. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृतिः|आवृति
आवृतिः f. Covering, hiding; see<BR>आवरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृज्
आवृज् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To bestow, give<BR>(Ved.).<BR>--2 To turn to or towards.<BR>--3 To choose. --Caus.<BR>1 To bend,<BR>bend down; incline; गौरवेणावर्जितः<BR>Pt. 4.; आवर्ज्य शाखाः सदयं च यासां<BR>R. 16. 19; 13. 17, 24; Mv. 5. 63;<BR>K. 14, 58; Ku. 2. 26, 3. 54;<BR>7. 54; Me. 46.<BR>--2 To subdue, win or<BR>gain over, attract, please; आवर्जितानि<BR>मनांसि Nāg. 1; मरीचिमावर्जितवतीव<BR>श्लाघसे Dk. 45, 58, 133, 155;<BR>Mv. 2; K. 368.<BR>--3 To bring, collect;<BR>R. 6. 76.<BR>--4 To pour out, offer, give;<BR>अपि त्वदावर्जितवारिसंभृतं Ku. 5. 34;<BR>R. 15. 80; तनयावर्जितपिंडकांक्षिणः<BR>8. 26; 1. 62, 67; Mu. 4;<BR>K. 241.<BR>--5 To draw or force out;<BR>Nāg. 4.<BR>--6 To empty, pour out the<BR>contents of (as a jar &c.); कलशमावर्जयति<BR>Ś. 1; V. 5; Ku. 7. 10; K. 82, 310.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्जनं|आवर्जन
आवर्जनं<BR>1 Bending down &c.<BR>--2<BR>Giving.<BR>--3 Winning over, Dk. 139,<BR>172.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्
आवृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To turn round,<BR>revolve.<BR>--2 To return, come or turn<BR>back; धेनुराववृते वनात् R. 1. 82,<BR>2. 19; Bg. 8. 26.<BR>--3 To go to or<BR>towards.<BR>--4 To be restless or<BR>uneasy; Māl. 1. 41. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause<BR>to turn or revolve; अक्षबलयमावर्तयंतं<BR>K. 42 telling the beads.<BR>--2 To roll,<BR>turn about or over.<BR>--3 To cause<BR>to roll down, shed (as tears &c.).<BR>--4 To attract, win over (see आवृज्)<BR>--5 To repeat, recite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तः|आवर्त|आवर्त्त|आवर्त्तं|आवर्त्तः
आवर्तः<BR>1 Turning round,<BR>winding, revolving; प्रदक्षिणावर्तशिखः<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 A whirlpool, an eddy,<BR>whirl; नृपं तमावर्तमनोज्ञनाभिः<BR>R. 6. 52; दर्शितावर्तनाभेः Me. 28; Dk. 2;<BR>आवर्तः संशयानां Pt. 1. 191.<BR>--3<BR>Deliberation, revolving (in the mind),<BR>anxiety.<BR>--4 A lock of hair curling<BR>backwards, especially on a horse.<BR>--5<BR>The two depressions of the forehead<BR>above the eye-brows.<BR>--6 A crowded<BR>place (where many men live closely<BR>together).<BR>--7 A kind of jewel.<BR>--8 N.<BR>of a form of cloud personified;<BR>आवर्तो निर्जलो मेघः.<BR>--9 Melting (of metals).<BR>--10 Doubt.<BR>--11 Worldly existence<BR>(संसार).<BR>--र्तं A mineral substance,<BR>pyrites (माक्षिकधातु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तक|आवर्तकः|आवर्त्तक
आवर्तक a. [आवर्त एव स्वार्थे कन्]<BR>Revolving again and again.<BR>--कः<BR>1 N. of a form of cloud personified;<BR>जातं वंशे भुवनविदिते पुष्करावर्तकानां<BR>Me. 6; Ku. 2. 50.<BR>--2 Depression<BR>above the eye-brows.<BR>--3 A<BR>whirlpool.<BR>--4 Revolution.<BR>--5 Revolution<BR>of the mind from the influence of<BR>the senses.<BR>--6 A curl of hair.<BR>--7 A<BR>sort of poisonous insect.<BR>--की N.<BR>of a creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तन|आवर्तनः|आवर्त्तन|आवर्त्तनं
आवर्तन a.<BR>1 Turning round or<BR>towards.<BR>--2 Revolving.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Turning round, returning,<BR>revolution.<BR>--2 Circular motion, gyration.<BR>--3 Churning or stirring up<BR>anything in fusion.<BR>--4 Melting<BR>together, fusion, alligation (said of<BR>metals).<BR>--5 Mid-day, the time when<BR>shadows are cast in an opposite<BR>direction.<BR>--6 Repeating, doing over<BR>and over again^1.<BR>--7 Study, practising.<BR>--नः Viṣṇu.<BR>--नी<BR>1 A crucible.<BR>--2 A spoon, ladle.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवर्तिन्|आवर्त्तिन्
आवर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Whirling or<BR>turning upon itself, returning;<BR>आब्रह्मभुवनाल्लोकाः पुनरावर्तिनोऽर्जुन<BR>Bg. 8. 16; कालांतरावर्ति H. 1. 207.<BR>--2<BR>Melting, mixing &c. --m.<BR>--(र्ती) A<BR>horse having curls of hair on<BR>various parts of the body (considered<BR>as a sign of auspiciousness).<BR>--नी<BR>1 A whirlpool.<BR>--2 N. of a plant<BR>(अजशृंगी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्
आवृत् f.<BR>1 Causing to turn<BR>towards.<BR>--2 Turning towards or<BR>round; entering.<BR>--3 Order,<BR>succession, method, mode, manner;<BR>अनयैवावृता कार्यं पिंडनिर्वपणं सुतैः<BR>Ms. 3. 248; Y. 3. 2.<BR>--4 Progress of an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">Page0262-c+ 56</a>]<BR>action; occurrence.<BR>--5 Turn of a path,<BR>course, direction.<BR>--6 A purificatory<BR>rite; Ms. 2. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्त|आवृत्तः
आवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Turned round,<BR>whirled, returned; Māl. 1. 29.<BR>--2<BR>Repeated; द्विरावृत्ता दश द्विदशाः Sk.<BR>--3<BR>Learnt (by heart), studied; U. 6.<BR>--4<BR>Reverted, returned.<BR>--5 Averted.<BR>--6 Retreated, fled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृत्तिः|आवृत्ति
आवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Turning towards;<BR>return, coming back; तपोवनावृत्तिपथं<BR>R. 2. 18; Bg. 8. 23.<BR>--2<BR>Reversion, retreat, flight.<BR>--3<BR>Revolving, whirling, going round;<BR>Māl. 5. 4.<BR>--4 Recurrence to the same<BR>point or place (of the sun);<BR>उदगावृत्तिपथेन नारदः R. 8. 33.<BR>--5<BR>Repetition of birth and death,<BR>worldly existence; अनावृत्तिभयं<BR>Ku. 6. 77.<BR>--6 Repetition in general;<BR>an edition (modern use);<BR>सप्तमीयमंकनावृत्तिः seventh edition.<BR>--7<BR>Repeated reading, study; आवृत्तिः<BR>सर्वशास्त्राणां बोधादपि गरीयसी Udb.<BR>--8 Use,<BR>employment, application.<BR>--9 Turn<BR>of a way, course or direction.<BR>--10<BR>Occurrence.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दीपकं a<BR>rhetorical figure; त्रिविधं दीपकावृत्तौ<BR>भवेदावृत्तिदीपकम् । (पदस्यार्थस्योभयोर्वा आवृत्तिः).<BR>क्रमेणोदाहरणंः-वर्षत्यंबुदमालेयं वर्षत्येषा च<BR>शर्वरी ॥ उन्मीलंति कदंबानि स्फुटांति कुटजोद्गमाः ।<BR>माद्यंति चातकास्तृप्ता माद्यंति च शिखाबलाः ॥<BR>Kuval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवृष्टिः|आवृष्टि
आवृष्टिः f. Raining, a shower<BR>of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेगः|आवेग
आवेगः<BR>1 Uneasiness, anxiety,<BR>excitement, agitation, flurry;<BR>अलमावेगेन Ś. 3, 7; Amaru. 83; शोक˚, दुःख˚,<BR>साध्वस˚ &c.<BR>--2 Hurry, haste; Ś. 4.<BR>--3 Agitation, regarded as one of<BR>the 33 subordinate feelings.<BR>--गी<BR>N. of a tree (वृद्धदारकवृक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्ट्
आवेष्ट् {c10c} P. To surround;<BR>तृणैरावेष्ट्यते रज्जुः is made or formed of<BR>straw; Pt. 1. 331.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टकः|आवेष्टक
आवेष्टकः A wall, fence, an<BR>enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आवेष्टनं|आवेष्टन
आवेष्टनं<BR>1 Wrapping round, tying,<BR>binding.<BR>--2 A wrapper, an envelope.<BR>--3 A wall, fence, enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्य
आव्य a. (वी f.) [अवेर्मेषस्य<BR>विकारः ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Belonging to a sheep.<BR>--2 Woollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्यध्
आव्यध् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To hit, pierce; see<BR>अनाविद्ध.<BR>--2 To wound.<BR>--3 To break<BR>or pierce through.<BR>--4 To put on;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">Page0263-a+ 55</a>]<BR>Bk. 20. 11.<BR>--5 To shoot at, throw or<BR>cast towards.<BR>--6 To throw away, cast<BR>off.<BR>--7 To wave, brandish.<BR>--8 To pin<BR>on.<BR>--9 To rouse, agitate, stir up.<BR>--10 To drive away, expel;<BR>निर्बंधमाविध्यति Mv. 5. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0262-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविद्ध
आविद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Pierced, bored, rent,<BR>splintered, broken down;<BR>उत्पाताविद्धमूर्तिः Mv. 5. 44 rent or contracted;<BR>R. 12. 73.<BR>--2 Curved, crooked,<BR>uneven; V. 4. 28; हर्षाविद्धमभ्युत्थितः<BR>Dk. 37.<BR>--3 Cast with force; दूरनिक्षेप˚<BR>Māl. 8 cast forth in taking<BR>long strides; Mv. 2; Ms. 9. 40;<BR>thrown, put in motion.<BR>--4<BR>Disappointed.<BR>--5 Fallacious, false.<BR>--6<BR>Stupid, foolish.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्णी,<BR>--कर्णिका N. of a plant (पाठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आविधः|आविध
आविधः [आ-व्यध्-घञर्थे-क] An awl;<BR>drill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्याधिन्
आव्याधिन् a. [आ-व्यध्-णिनि] Giving<BR>pain, wounding, attacking.<BR>--नी A<BR>gang of robbers (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्रश्च्
आव्रश्च् {c6c} P. To tear off, cut off,<BR>tear in pieces, interrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्रश्चनं|आव्रश्चन
आव्रश्चनं<BR>1 Cutting or tearing<BR>off.<BR>--2 The stump of a tree<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्रस्कः|आव्रस्क
आव्रस्कः Being torn off or tearing<BR>itself off (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आव्रीडकः|आव्रीडक
आव्रीडकः [अव्रीडानां विषयो देशः]<BR>A country of the shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश|आशः
आश a. One who eats, eater<BR>(mostly as the last member of comp.);<BR>e. g. हुताश, आश्रयाश &c. &c.<BR>--शः<BR>[अश्-घञ्] Eating (as in प्रातराश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशकं|आशक
आशकं Eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशयितृ
आशयितृ a.<BR>1 Feeding, a feeder.<BR>--2 Protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिः|आशि
आशिः f. The act of eating food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशित|आशितं
आशित a.<BR>1 Eaten, given to eat.<BR>--2 Satisfied by eating.<BR>--3 Voracious,<BR>gluttonous.<BR>--तं Eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितंगवीन|आशितङ्गवीन|आशितङ्गवीनं
आशितंगवीन a. [आशिता अशनेन<BR>तृप्ता गावो यत्र, खञ् नि˚ मुम्] Formerly<BR>grazed by cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितंभव|आशितम्भव|आशितम्भवं
आशितंभव a. [आशितोऽशनेन तृप्तो<BR>भवत्यनेन P. III. 2. 45] Satiating,<BR>satisfying (as food).<BR>--वं<BR>1 Food,<BR>victuals.<BR>--2 Satisfaction, satiety<BR>(m. also); फलैर्येष्वासितंभवं Bk. 4. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशितृ
आशितृ a. Voracious, gluttonous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिन्
आशिन् a. Eating(in comp.);<BR>फलाशी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंस्
आशंस् {c1c} A. (rarely P.)<BR>1 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">Page0263-b+ 56</a>]<BR>hope for, expect, desire, wish or<BR>long for; स्वकार्यसिद्धिं पुनराशशंसे<BR>Ku. 3. 57; Bk. 14. 70, 90;<BR>Ś. 2. 15; M. 1; मनोरथाय नाशंसे Ś. 7. 13.<BR>--2 To bless, wish well to; एवं ते देवा<BR>आशंसंतु Mk. 1; इत्याशशंसे<BR>करणैरबाह्यैः R. 14. 50.<BR>--3 To speak, say.<BR>--4 To tell; Ku. 3. 14.<BR>--5 To ask<BR>for, beg.<BR>--6 To praise.<BR>--7 To repeat,<BR>recite.<BR>--8 To fear, be afraid of.<BR>--Caus. To render famous or<BR>celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसनं|आशंसन
आशंसनं<BR>1 Expecting, wishing;<BR>इष्टाशंसनमाशीः Sk.<BR>--2 Telling,<BR>declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसा
आशंसा<BR>1 Desire, wish,<BR>expectation, hope; निदधे विजयाशंसां चापे सीतां<BR>च लक्ष्मणे R. 12. 44; Bk. 19. 5.<BR>--2 Speech, declaration.<BR>--3<BR>Indication, reference; शरत्समयवर्णनाशंसया<BR>Ve. 1.<BR>--4 Imagination;<BR>आशंसापरिकल्पितास्वपि भवत्यानंदसांद्रो लयः<BR>Māl. 5. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसित
आशंसित a.<BR>1 Wished, hoped,<BR>expected.<BR>--2 Said, declared.<BR>--3<BR>Considered, said to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसितृ
आशंसितृ, आशंसिन् a.<BR>1 Wishing,<BR>desiring, expecting; V. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Announcing, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसिन्
आशंसितृ, आशंसिन् a.<BR>1 Wishing,<BR>desiring, expecting; V. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Announcing, declaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंसु|आशंसुः
आशंसु a. [आ-शंस्-उ] Desirous,<BR>hopeful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशस्
आशस् a. Ved. [आ-शंस्-क्विप्]<BR>Hoping. --f.<BR>1 Praise.<BR>--2 Desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्
आशक् {c5c} P. Ved. To make one<BR>capable or a master or possessor (of<BR>a thing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्त|आशक्तः
आशक्त a. Able, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशक्तिः|आशक्ति
आशक्तिः f. Power, ability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंक्|आशङ्क्
आशंक् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To suspect,<BR>distrust; दयितां साध्वीं त्वमाशंकिष्वथाः<BR>कथं Bk. 21. 1.<BR>--2 To suspect or<BR>believe to be; आशंकसे यदग्निं<BR>Ś. 1. 28; Śi. 3. 72; Bk. 6. 6.<BR>--3 To be in<BR>doubt or suspense; M. 4. 5.<BR>--4 To<BR>fear, be afraid, apprehend;<BR>भरतागमनमाशंक्य R. 12. 24; Pt. 392;<BR>दत्तपूर्वेत्याशंक्यते Māl. 4.<BR>--5 To start<BR>a doubt or objection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंकनीय|आशङ्कनीय
आशंकनीय pot. p.<BR>1 To be<BR>doubted or suspected.<BR>--2 To be<BR>apprehended.<BR>--3 Doubtful,<BR>questionable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंका|आशङ्का
आशंका<BR>1 Fear, apprehension;<BR>नष्टाशंका हरिणशिशवो मंदमंदं चरंति<BR>Ś. 1. 16; आशंकया भुक्तं Bh. 3. 5.<BR>--2 Doubt,<BR>uncertainty; इत्याशंकायामाह<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">Page0263-c+ 54</a>]<BR>Gadādhara.<BR>--3 Distrust, suspicion;<BR>˚अन्वित a. apprehensive, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंकित|आशङ्कित
आशंकित p. p. Feared, dreaded;<BR>इदं तदाशंकितं गुरुजनेनापि U. 3;<BR>doubted, suspected.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Fear,<BR>apprehension.<BR>--2 Doubt, uncertainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशंकिन्|आशङ्किन्
आशंकिन् a. Doubting, fearing;<BR>R. 4. 21; attended with fears;<BR>Pt. 1. 284.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशन|आशनः
आशन a. [अशन-अण्] One who<BR>feeds.<BR>--नः<BR>1 N. of a tree; see अशन.<BR>--2 The thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशय|आशयः
आशय &c. See under आशी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशरः|आशर
आशरः [आ-शॄ-अच्]<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 A<BR>demon, goblin (रक्षस्).<BR>--3 Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशारिकः
आशारिकः Violent and acute<BR>pain in the limbs (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशलः|आशल
आशलः A tree; see जीवक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशवं|आशव
आशवं [आशोर्भावः अण्]<BR>1 Speed,<BR>quickness.<BR>--2 Distilled spirit, more,<BR>usually written आसव q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशसनं|आशसन
आशसनं Ved. Cutting up an<BR>animal (when killed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशा
आशा [आसमंतात् अश्नुते आ-अश्-अच्]<BR>1 (a) Hope, expectation, prospect;<BR>तामाशां च सुरद्विषां R. 12. 96; आशा<BR>हि परमं दुःखं नैराश्यं परमं सुखं Subhāṣ.;<BR>त्वमाशे मोघाशे Bh. 3. 6; so भग्न, ˚हत,<BR>˚निराश &c. (b) Wish, desire (in Bh. 3. 25<BR>आशा is compared to a river).<BR>--2<BR>False hope or expectation.<BR>--3 Space,<BR>region, quarter of the compass,<BR>direction;<BR>अगस्त्याचरितामाशामनाशास्यजयो ययौ R. 4. 44;<BR>Ki. 7. 9.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वित, --जनन a.<BR>hopeful, inspiring hope; V. 3. 9.<BR>--कृत a. attended with the hope of<BR>success.<BR>--गजः a guardian elephant<BR>of a quarter or point of the compass;<BR>see अष्टदिग्गज.<BR>--तंतुः a thread of hope,<BR>slender hope; Māl. 4. 3, 9. 26.<BR>--पालः<BR>a guardian or regent of the regions<BR>or quarters; see अष्टदिक्पाल.<BR>--पिशाचिका deceptive or illusive hope,<BR>phantom of hope.<BR>--पुरगुग्गुलुः or<BR>--संभवः<BR>a kind of Bdellium.<BR>--प्राप्त a.<BR>successful (= प्राप्ताश).<BR>--बंधः {1} the tie or<BR>bond of hope, confidence, trust,<BR>expectation; गुर्वपि विरहदुःखमाशाबंधः<BR>साहयति Ś. 4. 15; Ve. 6. 25; V. 3; U. 3;<BR>Me. 10. {2} consolation. {3} a spider's<BR>web.<BR>--भंगः disappointment.<BR>--वह<BR>a. inspiring hope.<BR>--(हः) N. of<BR>a son of heaven.<BR>--विभिन्न a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-a" target="_blank">Page0264-a+ 55</a>]<BR>disappointed in expectation.<BR>--हीन a.<BR>despairing, despondent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0263-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशावत्|आशावन्त्
आशावत् a. Having hopes,<BR>trusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशाढः|आशाढ
आशाढः See अ(आ) षाढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशारः|आशार
आशारः Shelter; ˚एषिन् seeking<BR>shelter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशास्
आशास् {c2c} A.<BR>1 To bless,<BR>pronounce or give a blessing;<BR>ऋक्छंदसा आशास्ते Ś. 4; किमन्यदाशास्महे केवलं<BR>वीरप्रसवा भूयाः U. 1.<BR>--2 To desire,<BR>wish, hope, expect; यस्य भवान्<BR>मंगलमाशास्ते Ve. 6; Ms. 3. 80;<BR>सर्वमस्मिन्वयमाशास्महे Ś. 7; शांतिं Bk. 17. 1.<BR>--3 To order, command, relate (P.<BR>also in this sense).<BR>--4 To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशास्य
आशास्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be<BR>obtained by a boon.<BR>--2 To be<BR>blessed; Mv. 4. 13.<BR>--3 To be wished<BR>for, desirable; अनाशास्यजयो ययौ<BR>R. 4. 44 (who had not to wish for<BR>victory, to whom victory came<BR>unsought).<BR>--स्यं<BR>1 A thing to be<BR>wished for, wish, desire; संपन्नास्ते<BR>सर्वाशिषः Mu. 7; M. 5. 20.<BR>--2 A<BR>blessing, benediction;<BR>आशास्यचिंतास्तिमितो बभूव Ku. 7. 87;<BR>आशास्यमन्यत् पुनरुक्तभूतं R. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिस्
आशिस् f. (˚शीः, ˚शीर्भ्यां &c.) [<BR>आशास्-क्विप्, अत इत्वम्]<BR>1 A blessing,<BR>benediction. (It is thus defined:<BR>--वात्सल्याद्यत्र मान्येन कनिष्ठस्याभिधीयते ।<BR>इष्टावधारकं वाक्यमाशीः सा परिकीतिंता ॥). आशिस्<BR>is sometimes distinguished from वर,<BR>the former being taken to be merely<BR>an expression of one's good wishes<BR>which may or may not be realized;<BR>while a वर is a boon which is more<BR>permanent in character and surer of<BR>fulfilment; cf. वरः खल्वेषनाशीः Ś. 4;<BR>आशिषो गुरुजनवितीर्णा वरतामापद्यंते<BR>K. 291; अमोघाः प्रतिगृह्णंतावर्घ्यानुपदमाशिषः<BR>R. 1. 44, 11. 6; Ku. 5. 76, 7. 47.<BR>--2 Act of bestowing a blessing<BR>upon others.<BR>--3 A prayer, wish, desire;<BR>Ku. 5. 76, Bg. 4. 21, 6. 10.<BR>--4 A<BR>serpent's fang (cf. आशी).<BR>--5 One of<BR>the eight chief medicaments (वृद्धि).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वादः, --वचनं (<BR>आशीर्वादः &c.) a blessing, benediction,<BR>expression of a prayer or wish;<BR>आशीर्वचनसंयुक्तां नित्यं यस्मात् प्रकुर्वते<BR>S. D. 6; Ms. 2. 33.<BR>--विषः (आशीर्विषः)<BR>‘having poison in its fangs,’ a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिंजित|आशिञ्जित
आशिंजित a. Tinkling(as of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">Page0264-b+ 55</a>]<BR>the ornaments worn on the hands<BR>and feet); Ku. 3. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशित|आशितं
आशित, आशिन् &c. See under<BR>आश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिन्
आशित, आशिन् &c. See under<BR>आश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिन
आशिन a. Ved. Aged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिर्
आशिर् f. [आश्रीयते पच्यते आ-श्री-क्विप्<BR>Tv.] Milk &c. that is being boiled;<BR>(क्षीरादिकं श्रपणद्रव्यं Sāy.); the milk<BR>mixed with the Soma juice to<BR>purify it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिर|आशिरः
आशिर a. Voracious.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--3 A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशी
आशी [आशीर्यतेऽनया, आ-शॄ-क्विप् पृ˚]<BR>1 A serpent's fang.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>venom.<BR>--3 A blessing, benediction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विषः [आश्यां विषमस्य] {1} a<BR>snake; गरुत्मदाशीविषभीमदर्शनैः R. 3. 57.<BR>{2} a particular kind of snake;<BR>कर्णाशीविषभोगिनिप्रशमिते Ve. 6. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशी
आशी {c2c} A.<BR>1 To lie or sleep on;<BR>कुसुमान्याशेरते षट्पदाः V. 2. 23 v. l.<BR>--2 To pass (the night) in sleep.<BR>--3 To wish, pray for.<BR>--4 To dwell,<BR>live, inhabit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशयः|आशय
आशयः [आ-शी-अच्]<BR>1 A<BR>bedchamber, resting-place, asylum.<BR>--2<BR>A place of residence, abode, seat,<BR>retreat; वायुर्गंधानिवाशयात्<BR>Bg. 15. 8; अपृथक्˚ U. 1. 45.<BR>--3 Sleeping,<BR>lying down.<BR>--4 Receptacle, reservoir;<BR>विषमोपि विगाह्यते नय कृततीर्थः<BR>पयसामिवाशयः Ki. 2. 3; cf. also words<BR>like जलाशय, आमाशय, रक्ताशय &c.<BR>--5 Any recipient vessel or viscus<BR>of the body; the Āśayas are 7:<BR>--वात˚, पित्त˚, श्लेष्मन्˚, रक्त˚, आम˚, पक्व˚<BR>(and गर्भ˚ in the case of women).<BR>--6<BR>The stomach; आशयाग्निदीप्तिः<BR>Dk. 160.<BR>--7 Meaning, intention,<BR>purport, gist; इत्याशयः; एवं कवेराशयः<BR>(oft. used by commentators; see<BR>अभिप्राय).<BR>--8 The seat of feelings,<BR>mind, heart; अहमात्मा गुडाकेश<BR>सर्वभूताशयस्थितः Bg. 10. 20; Mv. 2. 37.<BR>--9<BR>Disposition of mind.<BR>--10<BR>Prosperity.<BR>--11 A barn.<BR>--12 Will or<BR>pleasure.<BR>--13 Virtue or vice (as the<BR>eventual cause of pleasure or pain).<BR>--14 Fate, fortune.<BR>--15 Property,<BR>possession.<BR>--16 A miser.<BR>--17 A<BR>kind of pit (made for catching<BR>animals); आस्ते परमसंतप्तो नूनं सिंह<BR>इवाशये Mb.<BR>--18 N. of a tree (पनस).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशः fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशु|आशुः
आशु a. [अश्-व्याप्तौ उण्] Fast,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">Page0264-c+ 54</a>]<BR>quick.<BR>--शुः Ved.<BR>1 ‘The quick<BR>one’, a horse.<BR>--2 Rice (ripening<BR>quickly in the rainy season).<BR>--शु<BR>ind. Fast, quickly, immediately,<BR>directly; वर्त्म भानोस्त्यजाशु Me. 39,<BR>22. [cf. L. acu; Gr. okus.].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आपस् a. obtaining<BR>quickly.<BR>--कारिन्, --कृत् a. {1} doing<BR>anything quickly, smart, active.<BR>{2} operating quickly (as a<BR>medicine).<BR>--कोपिन् a. irascible,<BR>irritable.<BR>--क्रिया quick operation of a<BR>medicine.<BR>--ग a. swift, quick.<BR>--(गः) {1} the wind. {2} the sun.<BR>{3} an arrow;<BR>पपावनास्वादितपूर्वमाशुगः R. 3. 54, 11. 83, 12. 91.<BR>--गामिन् a. going quickly. (--m.). the<BR>sun.<BR>--तोष a. easily appeased or<BR>pleased.<BR>--(षः) an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--पत्री a tree which yields<BR>frankincense (शल्लकीलता).<BR>--पत्वन् a. flying<BR>quickly.<BR>--बोध a. teaching quickly,<BR>N. of a grammar.<BR>--या a. going<BR>quickly. (--ind.) quickly.<BR>--व्रीहिः<BR>rice ripening in the rainy season.<BR>--षेण a. Ved. having swift arrows.<BR>--हेमन् a. running on quickly, urging<BR>the horses.<BR>--हेषस् a. Ved. quickly<BR>neighing; having quick horses,<BR>quickly praised; (शीघ्रशब्दायमान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुत्वं|आशुत्व
आशुत्वं, --ता Quickness, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुता
आशुत्वं, --ता Quickness, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशिमन्
आशिमन् m. [आशोर्भावः इमनिच्]<BR>Quickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशुशुक्षणि|आशुशुक्षणिः
आशुशुक्षणि a. [आ शुष् सन् अनि<BR>Uṇ. 2. 102]<BR>1 Being worshipped on<BR>account of shining very quickly, or<BR>causing sorrow to one's enemies<BR>(Sāy).<BR>--2 Shining forth.<BR>--णिः<BR>1<BR>Wind, air.<BR>--2 Fire; मंत्रपूतानि हवींषि<BR>प्रतिगृह्णात्येतत्प्रीत्याशुशुक्षणिः K. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशू
आशू a. Quick, fast (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशेकुटिन्
आशेकुटिन् m. A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशोकेय
आशोकेय a. (यी f.) [अशोक-ढञ्]<BR>(A place &c.) Near an Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशोषणं|आशोषण
आशोषणं The act of drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आशौचं|आशौच
आशौचं [अशुचेर्भावः अण्;<BR>P. VII. 3. 30] Impurity, see अशौचं; दशाहं<BR>शावमाशौचं ब्राह्मणस्य विधीयते<BR>Ms. 5. 59, 61, 62, 74, 80; Y. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्य|आश्चर्य्य|आश्चर्य्यं
आश्चर्य a. [आ-चर्-ण्यत् सुट्<BR>P. VI. 1. 147] Marvellous, wonderful,<BR>extraordinary, astonishing, strange,<BR>curious; आश्चर्यो गवां दोहोऽगोपेन Sk.;<BR>तदनु ववृषुः पुष्पमाश्चर्यमेघाः R. 16. 87;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">Page0265-a+ 56</a>]<BR>˚दर्शनो मनुष्यलोकः Ś. 7.<BR>--र्यं<BR>1 A<BR>wonder, miracle, marvel; किमाश्चर्यं<BR>क्षारदेशे प्राणदा यमदूतिका Udb.;<BR>कर्माश्चर्याणि U. 1 wonderful deeds;<BR>K. 65; Mv. 1; Bg. 11. 6, 2. 29.<BR>--2<BR>Surprise, wonder, astonishment;<BR>˚मय Bg. 11. 11.<BR>--3 A strange<BR>appearance, prodigy.<BR>--4 (Used as an<BR>exclamation) A wonder, how<BR>strange or curious; आश्चर्यं परिपीडितो<BR>ऽभिरमते यच्चातकस्तृष्णया Chāt. 2. 4;<BR>usually with यच्च, यत्र or यदि with a<BR>following potential or future.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भूत a. wonderful, being<BR>an object of wonder; K. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0264-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्यता
आश्चर्यता, --त्वं Wonderfulness,<BR>astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चर्यत्वं|आश्चर्यत्व|आश्चर्य्यत्व
आश्चर्यता, --त्वं Wonderfulness,<BR>astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्चोतन
आश्चोऌ^1(श्च्यो)तन a. Sprinkling.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Aspersion, sprinkling.<BR>--2<BR>Applying ghee &c. to the eyelids.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: ASco(Scyo)tana - headword markup error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्च्योतन
आश्चोऌ^1(श्च्यो)तन a. Sprinkling.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Aspersion, sprinkling.<BR>--2<BR>Applying ghee &c. to the eyelids.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: ASco(Scyo)tana - headword markup error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्म|आश्मः
आश्म a. (श्मी f.) [अश्मन्-अण्]<BR>Made of stone, stony.<BR>--श्मः<BR>Anything made of stone.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भारिक a. having a mass of stones.<BR>--रथ्यः N. of a teacher of ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मन|आश्मनः
आश्मन a. (नी f.) [अश्मनो विकारः<BR>अण्] Stony, made of stones.<BR>--नः<BR>1 Anything made of stone.<BR>--2<BR>N. of Aruṇa, the charioteer of<BR>the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मरिक|आश्मरिकः
आश्मरिक a. (की f.) [अश्मर्येव<BR>स्वार्थे बा˚ ठञ्] Suffering from stone in<BR>the bladder.<BR>--कः N. of a disease<BR>(अश्मरी q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्मिक
आश्मिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Made of<BR>stone.<BR>--2 Carrying or bearing stones.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्यै
आश्यै {c1c} A. To become<BR>congealed or coagulated, to become dry;<BR>यावन्नाश्यायते वेदिः R. 17. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्यान
आश्यान p. p.<BR>1 Congealed,<BR>consolidated; पंकैरिवाश्यानवनैस्तटानि<BR>Ki. 16. 10.<BR>--2 Partially dried;<BR>पथश्चाश्यानकर्दमान् R. 4. 24; Ku. 7. 9; dried<BR>by fumigation (as hair); R. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रं|आश्र
आश्रं [अश्रमेव, स्वार्थेऽण्] Tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रपणं|आश्रपण
आश्रपणं [आ-श्रा-णिच् ल्युट्] The<BR>act of cooking or boiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमः|आश्रम|आश्रमं
आश्रमः, --मं [आ-श्रम् आधारे घञ् वृद्ध्य<BR>भावः]<BR>1 A hermitage, hut, cell,<BR>dwelling or abode of ascetics.<BR>--2 A<BR>stage, order, or period of the<BR>(religious) life of a Brāhmaṇa. These<BR>are four:<BR>--ब्रह्मचर्य the life of a student;<BR>गार्हस्थ्य the life of a house holder:<BR>वानप्रस्य the life of an anchorite or<BR>hermit, and संन्यास the life of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-b" target="_blank">Page0265-b+ 58</a>]<BR>Bhikṣu or beggar. Kṣatriyas (and<BR>Vaiśyas also) can enter upon the<BR>first three Āśramas; cf. Ś. 7. 20;<BR>V. 5; (according to some authorities<BR>they can enter the fourth also;<BR>cf. सकिलाश्रममंत्यमाश्रितः R. 8. 14);<BR>पूर्वाश्रमः Ku. 5. 50.<BR>--3 A<BR>college, school.<BR>--4 A wood or thicket<BR>(where ascetics practise penance).<BR>--5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गुरुः<BR>the head of a religious order, a<BR>preceptor, principal.<BR>--धर्मः {1} the<BR>special duties of each order or life.<BR>{2} the duties of one leading a<BR>hermit's life; य इमामाश्रमधर्मे नियुङ्क्ते Ś. 1.<BR>--पदं, --मंडलं, --स्थानं {1} a hermitage<BR>(including the surrounding grounds),<BR>a penance forest (तपोवनं);<BR>शांतमिदमाश्रमपदं Ś. 1. 16. {2} a period in the<BR>religious life of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--भ्रष्ट a. fallen from any religious<BR>order, apostate.<BR>--वासः residence in<BR>a hermitage.<BR>--वासिक a. relating to<BR>residence in a hermitage; ˚कं पर्व<BR>the 15th book of the Mb.<BR>--वासिन्,<BR>--आलयः, --सद् m. an ascetic, hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमं|आश्रम|आश्रमः
आश्रमः, --मं [आ-श्रम् आधारे घञ् वृद्ध्य<BR>भावः]<BR>1 A hermitage, hut, cell,<BR>dwelling or abode of ascetics.<BR>--2 A<BR>stage, order, or period of the<BR>(religious) life of a Brāhmaṇa. These<BR>are four:<BR>--ब्रह्मचर्य the life of a student;<BR>गार्हस्थ्य the life of a house holder:<BR>वानप्रस्य the life of an anchorite or<BR>hermit, and संन्यास the life of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-b" target="_blank">Page0265-b+ 58</a>]<BR>Bhikṣu or beggar. Kṣatriyas (and<BR>Vaiśyas also) can enter upon the<BR>first three Āśramas; cf. Ś. 7. 20;<BR>V. 5; (according to some authorities<BR>they can enter the fourth also;<BR>cf. सकिलाश्रममंत्यमाश्रितः R. 8. 14);<BR>पूर्वाश्रमः Ku. 5. 50.<BR>--3 A<BR>college, school.<BR>--4 A wood or thicket<BR>(where ascetics practise penance).<BR>--5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गुरुः<BR>the head of a religious order, a<BR>preceptor, principal.<BR>--धर्मः {1} the<BR>special duties of each order or life.<BR>{2} the duties of one leading a<BR>hermit's life; य इमामाश्रमधर्मे नियुङ्क्ते Ś. 1.<BR>--पदं, --मंडलं, --स्थानं {1} a hermitage<BR>(including the surrounding grounds),<BR>a penance forest (तपोवनं);<BR>शांतमिदमाश्रमपदं Ś. 1. 16. {2} a period in the<BR>religious life of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--भ्रष्ट a. fallen from any religious<BR>order, apostate.<BR>--वासः residence in<BR>a hermitage.<BR>--वासिक a. relating to<BR>residence in a hermitage; ˚कं पर्व<BR>the 15th book of the Mb.<BR>--वासिन्,<BR>--आलयः, --सद् m. an ascetic, hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रमिक|आश्रमिकः
आश्रमिक a., आश्रमिन् a. [आश्रम-ठन्<BR>इति]<BR>1 Belonging to one of the four<BR>orders or periods of religious life;<BR>Ms. 6. 90-91, 12. 111, 3. 78.<BR>--2<BR>Belonging to a hermitage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रवः|आश्रव|आश्रवं
आश्रवः<BR>1 Stream, river.<BR>--2<BR>Fault, transgression; see आस्रव and<BR>under आश्रु also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रि|आश्रिः
आश्रि {c1c} U.<BR>1 (a) To resort or<BR>betake oneself to; to have<BR>recourse to (a place, way, course<BR>of action &c.);<BR>विचरितमृगयूथान्याश्रयिष्ये वनानि V. 5. 17; Rs. 1. 27 v. l.;<BR>दक्षिणां मूर्तिमाश्रित्य K. 128, 132; न<BR>वयं कुमारमाश्रयामहे Mu. 4; आशिश्राय<BR>च भूतलं Bk. 14. 111 fell on the<BR>ground; 17. 92; वृतिमाश्रित्य वैतसीं<BR>R. 4. 35 resorting to or following;<BR>so धैर्यं, शोकं, बलं, मित्रभावं,<BR>संस्कृतमाश्रित्य &c.; आश्रित्य having recourse or<BR>reference; तामाश्रि य M. 4. 1;<BR>कततत्प्रकरणमाश्रित्य गीयतां Ś. 1 (b) To seek<BR>refuge with, dwell with or in,<BR>inhabit (as a place &c); शरण्यमेनमाश्रयन्ते<BR>R. 13. 7; Pt. 1. 51; तथा<BR>गृहस्थमाश्रित्य वर्तंते सर्व आश्रमाः Ms. 3. 77; सर्वे<BR>गुणाः कांचनमाश्रयंत्।.<BR>--2 To go through,<BR>experience; एकोरसः…<BR>पृथक्पृथगिवाश्रयते विवर्तान् U. 3. 47.<BR>--3 To rest or<BR>depend upon.<BR>--4 To adhere or stick to,<BR>fall to the lot of, happen, occur;<BR>पापमेवाश्रयेदस्मान् Bg. 1. 36 we shall incur<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-c" target="_blank">Page0265-c+ 56</a>]<BR>sin.<BR>--5 To choose, prefer.<BR>--6 To<BR>assist, help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयः|आश्रय
आश्रयः [आश्रि-अच्]<BR>1 A<BR>restingplace, seat, substratum;<BR>सौहृदादपृथगाश्रयामिमां U. 1. 45 v. l.; so<BR>आश्रयासिद्ध q. v. below.<BR>--2 That on which<BR>anything depends or rests, or<BR>with which it is closely<BR>connected.<BR>--3 Recipient, receptacle, a<BR>person or thing in which any<BR>quality is present or retained &c.;<BR>तमाश्रयं दुष्प्रसहस्य तेजसः R. 3. 58.<BR>--4<BR>(a) A place of refuge, asylum;<BR>shelter; भर्ता वै ह्याश्रयः स्त्रीणां Vet.;<BR>तदहमाश्रयोन्मूलनेनैव त्वामकामां करोमि<BR>Mu. 2. (b) A dwelling, house.<BR>--5<BR>Having recourse or resort to, resort;<BR>oft. in comp. साभूद्रामाश्रया भूयः<BR>R. 12. 35; नानाश्रया प्रकृतिः &c.<BR>--6<BR>Following, practising; Ms. 2. 11.<BR>--7<BR>Choosing, taking, attaching oneself<BR>to.<BR>--8 Dependence on; oft. in comp.;<BR>मम सर्वे विषयास्त्वदाश्रयाः R. 8. 69.<BR>--9<BR>Patron, supporter; विनाश्रयं न तिष्ठंति<BR>पंडिता वनिता लताः Udb.<BR>--10 A prop,<BR>support; R. 9. 60.<BR>--11 Help,<BR>assistance, protection.<BR>--12 A quiver;<BR>बाणमाश्रयमुखात् समुद्धरन् R. 11. 26.<BR>--13 Authority, sanction, warrant.<BR>--14 Connection, relation,<BR>association.<BR>--15 Union, attachment.<BR>--16<BR>A plea, an excuse.<BR>--17 Contiguity,<BR>vicinity.<BR>--18 Seeking shelter or<BR>protection with another (= संश्रय),<BR>one of the six gunas, q. v.<BR>--19 An<BR>appropriate act, or one consistent<BR>with character.<BR>--20 Source, origin.<BR>--21 (In gram.) The subject, or that<BR>to which the predicate is attached.<BR>--22 (With Buddhists) The five<BR>organs of sense with Manas or<BR>mind.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--असिद्धः, --द्धिः f. a<BR>kind of fallacy, one of the three<BR>sub-divisions of असिद्ध; (that whose<BR>substratum is false or fictitious);<BR>e. g. गगमारनिंदं सुरभि अरविंदत्व<BR>त्सरोजारविंदवत्.<BR>--आशः, --भुज् a. consuming<BR>every thing with which it comes<BR>in contact.<BR>--(शः, --क्) {1} fire;<BR>दुर्वृत्तः क्रियते धूर्तैः श्रीमानात्मविवृद्धये ।<BR>किं नाम खलसंसर्गः कुरुते नाश्रयाशवत् ॥<BR>Udb. {2} a forfeiter of asylum. {3}<BR>the constellation कृत्तिका.<BR>--भूत a. one<BR>who is the refuge or support (of<BR>another person).<BR>--लिंगं an adjective<BR>(a word which must agree in gender<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-a" target="_blank">Page0266-a+ 57</a>]<BR>with the word which it qualifies or<BR>refers to).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0265-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयण
आश्रयण a. (णी f.)<BR>1 Resorting<BR>to, seeking refuge with; Ku. 4. 20.<BR>--2 Referring to.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Betaking<BR>oneself to, taking refuge with.<BR>--2<BR>Accepting, choosing.<BR>--3 Joining.<BR>--4<BR>Refuge, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयणीय
आश्रयणीय pot. p.<BR>1 To be had<BR>recourse to; R. 17. 60.<BR>--2 To be<BR>practised or followed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रयिन्
आश्रयिन् a.<BR>1 Resting with,<BR>dependent on.<BR>--2 Related to, concerning;<BR>तदाश्रयिणी कथा V. 3. 10; K. 213.<BR>--3 Resorting to; R. 6. 4; Ratn. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रित|आश्रितः
आश्रित p. p. (Used actively)<BR>(with an acc.)<BR>1 Resorting to,<BR>having recourse to; स किलाश्रममंत्यमाश्रितः<BR>R. 8. 14; कृष्णाश्रितः = कृष्णमाश्रितः Sk.;<BR>मानुषीं तनुं Bg. 9. 11; R. 1. 13.<BR>--2<BR>Dwelling in, inhabiting, seated or<BR>resting on, stationing oneself at or<BR>on; इदं स्फटिकतलमाश्रितो भवामि<BR>M. 4; so वातायनमाश्रितः पश्यति;<BR>द्रव्याश्रितो गुणः Ak.; R. 12. 21, 1. 75;<BR>ह्वार˚, दुर्ग˚ &c.<BR>--3 Using, employing.<BR>--4 Following, practising, observing;<BR>माध्यस्थ्यं, धर्मं, प्रव्रज्यां; Ku. 6. 6;<BR>Bk. 7. 42.<BR>--5 Receiving<BR>anything as an inherent or integral<BR>part.<BR>--6 Dependent on; राष्ट्रं<BR>बाहुबलाश्रितं Ms. 9. 255.<BR>--7 Referring to,<BR>regarding; भीष्माश्रिताः कथाः Mb.<BR>--8 (Passively used) Resorted to,<BR>inhabited &c.; चटकाश्रिता शाखा<BR>Pt. 1; R. 3. 11.<BR>--तः A dependent,<BR>servant, follower; अस्मदाश्रितानां<BR>H. 1; प्रभूणां प्रायश्चलं गौरवमाश्रितेषु<BR>Ku. 3. 1.<BR>--तं (pl.) The objects perceived<BR>by the senses and mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रिः|आश्रि
आश्रिः f. The edge of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रु
आश्रु {c5c} P.<BR>1 To hear, listen<BR>to.<BR>--2 To promise (with dat. of<BR>person; cf. P. I. 4. 40;<BR>Y. 2. 196).<BR>--3 To accept, undertake.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to hear.<BR>--2 To call, particularly in ritualistic<BR>formulas; ओमित्याश्रावयति Ch. Up.<BR>--3 To draw towards, win over,<BR>attract; Bk. 12. 30.<BR>--4 To say,<BR>repeat (as a Mantra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रव|आश्रवं|आश्रवः
आश्रव a. [आ-श्रु-अच्] Obedient,<BR>compliant; भिषजामनाश्रवः<BR>R. 19. 49; N. 3. 84.<BR>--वः<BR>1 A promise,<BR>engagement.<BR>--2 Fault,<BR>transgression.<BR>--3 One of the categories<BR>according to the Jainas; see आस्रव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रावणं|आश्रावण
आश्रावणं<BR>1 Calling out so as to<BR>make one listen.<BR>--2 N. of certain<BR>short words uttered at ceremonies;<BR>ॐ स्वधेत्याश्रावणमस्तु स्वधेति प्रत्याश्रावणं<BR>Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुत|आश्रुतः
आश्रुत p. p.<BR>1 Heard.<BR>--2<BR>Promised, agreed, accepted.<BR>--तं<BR>Calling so as to make one listen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुतिः|आश्रुति
आश्रुतिः f.<BR>1 Hearing.<BR>--2<BR>Accepting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्रुकर्ण
आश्रुकर्ण a. One whose ears hear<BR>all around (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लिष्
आश्लिष् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To embrace, clasp;<BR>Bh. 3. 92.<BR>--2 To cleave or stick to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लिष्ट
आश्लिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Embraced, clasped;<BR>used actively also; आश्लिष्टो लक्ष्मीं Sk.<BR>--2 Connected, interwoven, blended;<BR>परस्पराश्लिष्टशाखैः पादपैः Mb.<BR>--3 Joined<BR>to, touching, in contact with;<BR>अवनितलाश्लिष्टललाटरेखया K. 67; अंगद˚ भुज<BR>R. 6. 53; Śi. 3. 72; मेघमाश्लिष्टसानुं<BR>Me. 2.<BR>--4 Joining what adheres or<BR>attaches to.<BR>--5 Invested; spread.<BR>--6 Deduced, concluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्लेषः|आश्लेष
आश्लेषः<BR>1 Embracing, clasping, an<BR>embrace;<BR>आश्लेषलोलुपवधूस्तनकार्कश्यसाक्षिणीं Śi. 2. 17; Amaru. 15, 72,<BR>94; कंठाश्लेषप्रणयिनि जने Me. 3, 106.<BR>--2<BR>Contact, intimate connection;<BR>relation;<BR>सामीप्याश्लेषविषयैर्व्याप्त्याधारश्चतुर्विधः Mugdha.<BR>--3 The site of an<BR>act.<BR>--षा f. (pl.) N. of the ninth<BR>Nakṣatra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्व|आश्वं
आश्व a. (श्वी f.) [अश्वस्येदं अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to or coming from a<BR>horse, equestrian; आश्वं कफहरं मूत्रं<BR>कृमिदद्रुषु शस्यते Suśr.<BR>--2 Drawn by<BR>horses (as a chariot).<BR>--श्वं<BR>1 A<BR>number of horses.<BR>--2 A chariot drawn<BR>by horses.<BR>--3 The state or action<BR>of a horse (अश्वस्य भावः कर्म वा Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वत्थ|आश्वत्थं
आश्वत्थ a. (त्थी f.), आश्वथिक a.<BR>(की f.) [अश्वत्थस्येदं अण् ठक् वा]<BR>1<BR>Relating to or made of the holy<BR>fig-tree.<BR>--2 Relating to the<BR>fruit-bearing season of this tree, as<BR>a मुहूर्त.<BR>--त्था The night having the<BR>अश्वत्थ Nakṣatra.<BR>--त्थं The fruit of<BR>the holy fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वभारिक
आश्वभारिक a. (की f.) = अश्वभारं हरति,<BR>वहति आवहति वा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वमेधिक
आश्वमेधिक a. (की f.) [अश्वमेधाय<BR>हितं ठण्] Belonging to the<BR>horsesacrifice.<BR>--कं N. of the 14th<BR>Parvan of Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुज|आश्वयुजः
आश्वयुज a. (जी f.) [अश्वयुज-अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to the month Āśvina.<BR>--2 Born under the constellation<BR>अश्वयुज्.<BR>--जः The month आश्विन;<BR>भाद्रपदाश्वयुजौ वर्षाः Suśr.; Ms. 6. 15;<BR>Y. 3. 47.<BR>--जी The day of the<BR>full moon in Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वयुजक
आश्वयुजक a. (की f.) Sown at<BR>the day of full moon in Āśvina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वरथ
आश्वरथ a. (थी f.) [अश्वरथ-अञ्]<BR>Belonging to a chariot drawn by<BR>horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलक्षणिक|आश्वलक्षणिकः
आश्वलक्षणिक a. (की f.) [<BR>अश्वलक्षणठक्] Knowing the marks of horses.<BR>--कः A farrier, groom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विक|आश्विकः
आश्विक a. (की f.) [अश्व-ठञ्]<BR>Relating to a horse, drawn by horses,<BR>equestrian, cavalier.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>cavalier.<BR>--2 A combination of stars or<BR>omens presaging acquisition of<BR>horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विन|आश्विनः
आश्विन a. (नी f.)<BR>1<BR>Belonging or sacred to the Aśvins (अश्विनौ<BR>देवते अस्य).<BR>--2 Pervading.<BR>--नः<BR>1 N.<BR>of a month (in which the moon is<BR>near ths constellation Aśvinī).<BR>--2<BR>A sacrifice or a weapon presided over<BR>by the Aśvins.<BR>--3 (du.) The Aśvins.<BR>--नी<BR>1 N. of certain bricks.<BR>--2 A<BR>pile, stack (चितिभेदः).<BR>--नं A day's<BR>journey for a horse or rider (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्विनेय|आश्विनेयः
आश्विनेय m. [अश्विन्याः अपत्यं ढक्]<BR>The two Aśvins (physicians of gods).<BR>--नः<BR>1 N. of Nakula and Sahadeva,<BR>the last two of the five Pāṇḍava<BR>princes.<BR>--2 A day's journey for a<BR>horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीन|आश्वीनं|आश्वीनः
आश्वीन a. (नी f.) [अश्व-खञ्]<BR>Made or traversed by a horse (as<BR>a journey &c.); ˚नोऽध्वा Sk.<BR>--नः --नं<BR>The distance travelled by a horse<BR>in a day; सहस्राश्वीने वा इतः स्वर्गो<BR>लोकः Ait. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वीयं|आश्वीय
आश्वीयं A number of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वलायनः|आश्वलायन
आश्वलायनः N. of the author<BR>of a celebrated ritual work, called<BR>the Āśvalāyana Sūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वस्
आश्वस् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To breathe;<BR>सुखमाश्वसंति गिरयः Mv. 5. 51 are<BR>lying at ease.<BR>--2 To breathe freely,<BR>recover breath, take courage,<BR>take heart, rest secure, be at ease;<BR>प्रत्ययादाश्वसत्यः Me. 8; Pt. 1. 307;<BR>Bk. 4. 38, 5. 23.<BR>--3 To revive.<BR>--4 To have confidence in. --Caus.<BR>1 To encourage, comfort, console,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">Page0267-a+ 56</a>]<BR>cheer up; तदा<BR>संकीर्तनेनाश्वासयाम्यात्मानं V. 3; R. 12. 5. 14. 58. 15. 45;<BR>Me. 113; V. 5. 16.<BR>--2 To<BR>refresh, gratify;<BR>छायाश्वासितपथिकजनसार्थः Pt. 2.<BR>--3 To conciliate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0266-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासः|आश्वास
आश्वासः<BR>1 Taking or recovering<BR>breath, breathing freely, recovery,<BR>revival.<BR>--2 Consolation, cheering<BR>up, inspiring confidence; U. 6. 10.<BR>--3 An assurance of safety or<BR>protection.<BR>--4 Cessation, completion, stop.<BR>--5 A chapter or section of a book.<BR>--6<BR>A probable story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासक|आश्वासकः
आश्वासक a. Consolatory,<BR>comforting.<BR>--कः Clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासनं|आश्वासन
आश्वासनं Consoling,<BR>encouraging, cheering up, consolation; तदिदं<BR>द्वितीयं हृदयाश्वासनं Ś. 7; देवस्याश्वासनं<BR>भवति Pt. 1 cheering up of spirits,<BR>recovery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आश्वासिन्
आश्वासिन् a. [आ-श्वस्-णिनि]<BR>1<BR>Breathing freely, reviving,<BR>becoming cheerful; Ś. 2. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Consoling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढः|आषाढ
आषाढः [आषाढीपूर्णिमा अस्मिन्मासे<BR>अण्]<BR>1 N. of a Hindu month<BR>(corresponding to June and July);<BR>आषाढस्य प्रथमदिवसे Me. 2; शेते विष्णुः<BR>सदाषाढे कार्तिके प्रतिबोध्यते V. P.<BR>--2<BR>A staff of the Palāśa wood carried<BR>by an ascetic; अथाजिनाषाढधरः<BR>प्रगल्भवाक् Ku. 5. 30.<BR>--3 The Malaya<BR>mountain.<BR>--ढा The 20th and the<BR>21st lunar mansions, usually called<BR>पूर्वाषाढा and उत्तराषाढा.<BR>--ढी The day<BR>of full moon in the month of<BR>Āṣāḍha.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भव, --भू a.<BR>produced in the month of Āṣāḍha.<BR>--(वः, --भूः) the planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढकः|आषाढक
आषाढकः The month आषाढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढिन्
आषाढिन् a. Bearing a Palāśa<BR>staff; K. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आषाढीय
आषाढीय a. [आषाढा-छ] Born under<BR>the constellation Āṣāḍhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्टमः|आष्टम
आष्टमः [अष्टमो भागः, अष्टम-ञ] The<BR>8th part; P. V. 3. 50-1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ट्रं|आष्ट्र
आष्ट्रं [अश्-व्याप्तौ ष्ट्रन् Uṇ. 4. 159]<BR>Sky, ether, atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आष्ट्री
आष्ट्री<BR>1 An extensive forest.<BR>--2<BR>A kitchen, fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस्, आः ind. An interjection,<BR>implying (a) Recollection; आः<BR>उपनयतु भवान् भूर्जपत्रं V. 2. (b) Anger;<BR>आः कथमद्यापि राक्षसत्रासः U. 1; आः<BR>पापे तिष्ठ तिष्ठ Māl. 8. (c) Pain; आः<BR>शीतं K. P. 10. (d) Angry<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-b" target="_blank">Page0267-b+ 57</a>]<BR>contradiction (अपाकरण); आः क एष मयि<BR>स्थिते Mu. 1; आः वृथामंगलपाठक Ve. 1.<BR>(e) Sorrow, regret; विद्यामातरमाः<BR>प्रदर्श्य नृपशून् भिक्षामहे निस्त्रपाः Udb.;<BR>(आः स्मरणेऽपाकरणे कोपसंतापयोस्तथा<BR>Med.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आः
आस्, आः ind. An interjection,<BR>implying (a) Recollection; आः<BR>उपनयतु भवान् भूर्जपत्रं V. 2. (b) Anger;<BR>आः कथमद्यापि राक्षसत्रासः U. 1; आः<BR>पापे तिष्ठ तिष्ठ Māl. 8. (c) Pain; आः<BR>शीतं K. P. 10. (d) Angry<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-b" target="_blank">Page0267-b+ 57</a>]<BR>contradiction (अपाकरण); आः क एष मयि<BR>स्थिते Mu. 1; आः वृथामंगलपाठक Ve. 1.<BR>(e) Sorrow, regret; विद्यामातरमाः<BR>प्रदर्श्य नृपशून् भिक्षामहे निस्त्रपाः Udb.;<BR>(आः स्मरणेऽपाकरणे कोपसंतापयोस्तथा<BR>Med.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्
आस् {vI.v} {c2c} A. (आस्ते, आसांचक्रे, आसिष्ट;<BR>आसितुं, आसित)<BR>1 To sit, lie, rest;<BR>एतदासनमास्यतां V. 5; आस्यतामिति<BR>चोक्तः सन्नासीताभिमुखं गुरोः Ms. 2. 193.<BR>--2 To live, dwell; तावद्वर्षाण्यासते<BR>देवलोके Mb.; यत्रास्मै रोचते तत्रायमास्तां<BR>K. 196; कुरूनास्ते Sk.;<BR>यत्रामृतास आसते Rv. 9. 15. 2; Bk. 4. 6,<BR>8. 79.<BR>--3 To sit quietly, take no<BR>hostile measures, remain idle; आसानं<BR>त्वामुत्थापयति द्वयम् Śi. 2. 57.<BR>--4 To be,<BR>exist.<BR>--5 To be contained in; जगंति<BR>यस्यां सविकाशमासत Śi. 1. 23.<BR>--6 To<BR>abide, remain, continue or be in any<BR>state, be doing anything, last; oft.<BR>used with present participles to<BR>denote a continuous or uninterrupted<BR>action; विदारयन्प्रगर्जंश्चास्ते Pt. 1 kept<BR>on, continued, tearing up and<BR>bellowing; used in this sense also<BR>with an adj., subst., indeclinable,<BR>past part., an adverb (तूष्णीं &c.),<BR>or with the instr. of a noun;<BR>सुखेनास्ते &c.<BR>--7 To lead to, result in<BR>(with dat.); आस्तां मानसतुष्टये<BR>सुकृतिनां नीतिर्नवोढेव वः H. 1. 212.<BR>--8<BR>To cease, have an end.<BR>--9 To<BR>solemnize, celebrate.<BR>--10 To let go,<BR>lay or put aside; आस्तां तावत् let<BR>it aside, let it go, to say<BR>nothing of, not to mention; K. 18.<BR>--Caus. To cause to sit, seat, fix;<BR>आसयत्सलिले पृथ्वीं Sk. --Desid.<BR>आसिसिषते To wish to sit &c. {vII.v} {c4c} P.<BR>[आस्यति, आसितुं]<BR>1 To enclose,<BR>border.<BR>--2 To admit (as water) into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसः|आस
आसः [आस्-घञ्]<BR>1 A seat.<BR>--2 A<BR>bow (--सं also); स सासिः सासुसूः<BR>सासः Ki. 15. 5.<BR>--3 Ashes.<BR>--सं<BR>1 Seat<BR>or lower part of the body.<BR>--2<BR>Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसनं|आसन|आसनः
आसनं [आस्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Sitting down.<BR>--2 A seat, place, stool; स<BR>वासवेनासनसन्निकृष्टं Ku. 3. 2; आसनं मुच् to<BR>leave one's seat, rise; R. 3. 11.<BR>--3<BR>A particular posture or mode of<BR>sitting; cf. पद्म˚, वीर˚, भद्र˚, वज्र˚ &c.<BR>--4 Sitting down or halting,<BR>stopping, encamping.<BR>--5 Abiding,<BR>dwelling; Ms. 2. 245, 6. 59.<BR>--6 Any<BR>peculiar mode of sexual enjoyment<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">Page0267-c+ 57</a>]<BR>(84 such asanas are usually<BR>mentioned).<BR>--7 Maintaining a post<BR>against an enemy (opp. यानं), one<BR>of the six modes of foreign policy;<BR>which are: --संधिर्ना विग्रहो यानमासनं<BR>द्वैधमाश्रयः Ak.; प्रतिबद्धशक्त्योः कालप्रतीक्षया<BR>तूष्णीमवस्थानमासनं; परस्परस्य<BR>सामर्थ्यविघातादासनं स्मृतं Agni P.; Ms. 7. 160,<BR>162, 166; Y. 1. 346; Pt. 3.<BR>--8 The<BR>front part of an elephant's body,<BR>withers.<BR>--9 Throwing (fr. अस् to<BR>throw).<BR>--10 N. of two trees (असन and<BR>जीवक).<BR>--ना A seat, stool, stay.<BR>--नी<BR>1 Stay, abiding, sitting.<BR>--2 A small<BR>seat or stool.<BR>--3 A shop, stall.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बंधधीर a. resolute to sit<BR>down, firm in one's seat;<BR>निषेदुषीमासनबंधधीरः R. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसित
आसित p. p. [आस्-क्त] Seated, at<BR>rest; आसितः सः; आसितं तेन Sk.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Sitting down.<BR>--2 A seat;<BR>इदमेषामासितं Sk.<BR>--3 Abode, a place where<BR>one has lived; a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसीन|आसीनः
आसीन pres. p. Sitting, seated;<BR>˚प्रचलायितं nodding when seated,<BR>falling asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्या
आस्या Sitting, abode, state of rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसा
आसा, आसः (Instr. and abl.<BR>of आस्) Before one's eyes, by word of<BR>mouth, personally; in close vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसः|आस
आसा, आसः (Instr. and abl.<BR>of आस्) Before one's eyes, by word of<BR>mouth, personally; in close vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंसार
आसंसार, --संसृति a. Liable to<BR>progress or alteration.<BR>--रं, --ति ind.<BR>1 Till the end of the world or<BR>worldly existence; Pt. 1.<BR>--2 Within<BR>the limits or range of worldly<BR>existence, throughout the sphere<BR>of worldly life; Bh. 3. 46;<BR>Ki. 3. 6 (Malli. यावत्संसारं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंसृति
आसंसार, --संसृति a. Liable to<BR>progress or alteration.<BR>--रं, --ति ind.<BR>1 Till the end of the world or<BR>worldly existence; Pt. 1.<BR>--2 Within<BR>the limits or range of worldly<BR>existence, throughout the sphere<BR>of worldly life; Bh. 3. 46;<BR>Ki. 3. 6 (Malli. यावत्संसारं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंगत्यं|आसङ्गत्य|आसंगत्य
आसंगत्यं Detachment, disunion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंज्|आसञ्ज्
आसंज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fasten, fix on,<BR>attach to, join or add to, place or put<BR>on (dress, armour &c.); चापमासज्य<BR>कंठे Ku. 2. 64; अनुबंध आसज्यते<BR>Sk.; आसज्यमानेक्षणः Ś. 3. 26 with<BR>the eyes intently fixed; (fig. also);<BR>भुजे… स भूमेर्धुरमाससंज R. 2. 74; so पुत्रे<BR>राज्यं; जने दोषं &c.; आससंज भयं तेषां<BR>Bk. 14. 104 fear overtook them.<BR>--2 To confer upon, conduce to;<BR>Ki. 13. 44.<BR>--3 To stick or adhere to,<BR>depend upon.<BR>--4 To take up.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to attach, have<BR>anything fastened or put on.<BR>--2<BR>To place, put, throw round;<BR>आसंजयामास यथाप्रदेशं कंठे गुणं R. 6. 83.<BR>--3 To entrust or appoint. --pass.<BR>(सज्यते) To adhere, stick, be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-a" target="_blank">Page0268-a+ 57</a>]<BR>attached; यदि नेष्टात्मनः पीडा मासजि<BR>भवता जने Ki. 11. 29; cf. “Do unto<BR>others as you would be done by.”.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0267-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्त|आसक्तं|आसक्तः
आसक्त p. p.<BR>1 Strongly attached<BR>to, intent on, devoted or addicted<BR>to, (usually with loc. or in comp.);<BR>द्यूत˚, मृगया˚.<BR>--2 Absorbed or<BR>engaged in, zealously following or<BR>pursuing.<BR>--3 Fixed on, directed<BR>towards, joined or<BR>attached to, placed or resting on;<BR>मन्मुखासक्तदृष्टिः K. 158; यदासक्तं सख्यं<BR>जने Mv. 5. 58 formed;<BR>शिखरासक्तमेघाः Ku. 6. 40 resting on;<BR>˚बाहुलतया 8.<BR>--4 Surrounded, encircled.<BR>--5 Continuous, perpetual, eternal.<BR>--6 Trusting to, confiding in.<BR>--क्तं<BR>ind. Eternally, perpetually.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चित्त, --चेतस्, --मनस् a. having<BR>the mind fixed on any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसक्तिः|आसक्ति
आसक्तिः f.<BR>1 Attachment,<BR>devotion, fondness; बालिशचरितेष्वासक्तिः<BR>K. 120; intentness, application.<BR>--2 Waylaying (Ved.).<BR>--क्ति ind.<BR>Ved. Purposely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंग|आसङ्ग|आसङ्गं|आसङ्गः
आसंग a. Uninterrupted,<BR>perpetual.<BR>--गः<BR>1 Attachment, devotion<BR>(to any object) (to enjoy or<BR>protect it); सुख˚ लुब्धः K. 173;<BR>U. 3; Bh. 3. 60.<BR>--2 Intentness,<BR>close application.<BR>--3 Contact,<BR>adnerence, clinging; (पंकजं)<BR>सशैवलासंगमपि प्रकाशते Ku. 5. 9; 3. 46;<BR>व्रततिवलयासंगसंजातपाशः Ś. 1. 33;<BR>Mu. 1. 14; अनासंगः absence of<BR>consolation; Māl. 2.<BR>--4 Association,<BR>connection, union; त्यक्त्वा<BR>कर्मफलासंगं Bg. 4. 20; so कांतासंग &c.<BR>--5 Fixing, fastening to.<BR>--6 Pride<BR>about the authorship of a thing<BR>(कर्तृत्वाभिमान).<BR>--7 That which is<BR>fastened; cf. उत्तरासंग.<BR>--8<BR>Waylaying (?).<BR>--गं A kind of fragrant<BR>earth; (सौराष्ट्रमृत्तिका).<BR>--गं ind.<BR>Without interruption, eternally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंगिनी|आसङ्गिनी
आसंगिनी A whirlwind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंगिमः|आसङ्गिम|आसङ्गिमः
आसंगिमः [आसंगे भवः डिमच्] (In<BR>surgery) A kind of bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंजनं|आसञ्जन
आसंजनं<BR>1 Fastening to, fixing,<BR>putting on the body (as dress,<BR>armour &c.).<BR>--2 Getting entangled,<BR>clinging; व्रततिवलयासंजनात् Ś. 1. 33 v. l.<BR>--3<BR>Attachment, devotion.<BR>--4 Contact,<BR>proximity.<BR>--5 A handle, hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसद्
आसद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sit down or<BR>near (with acc. or loc.).<BR>--2 To<BR>watch or lie in wait for.<BR>--3 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-b" target="_blank">Page0268-b+ 57</a>]<BR>approach, reach, to go to or towards<BR>(a place &c.);<BR>हिमालयस्यालयप्ताससाद Ku. 7. 69; Bk. 7. 31; Śi. 2. 2;<BR>आसनं R. 6. 4, 53; 11. 23.<BR>--4 To<BR>meet with, find, form; सख्य R. 5. 60;<BR>14. 25; अपायं Bk. 3. 26 suffering;<BR>4. 43.<BR>--5 To encounter, attack.<BR>--6<BR>To commence, undertake.<BR>--7 To<BR>place. --{c10c} P. or Caus.<BR>1 (a) To<BR>meet with, find; मृत्युभयमासादितः<BR>Bhāg. (b) To get, obtain;<BR>अमरगणतालेख्यमासाद्य R. 8. 95;<BR>Ms. 4. 227; धनं, सुखं &c.<BR>--2 To approach,<BR>go to, reach; नक्रः स्वस्थानमासाद्य<BR>गजेंद्रमपि कर्षति; ते पुण्यमासाद्य सुरेंद्रलोकं<BR>Bg. 9. 20; Me. 34; Bk. 8. 37.<BR>--3 To<BR>overtake, come up with; अनेन<BR>रथवेगेन पूर्वप्रस्थितं वैनतेयमप्यासादयेयं<BR>V. 1, Ve. 3. 7.<BR>--4 To encounter,<BR>attack; आसादितौ कथं ब्रूतं न गजैः<BR>कूलमुद्रुजैः Bk. 6. 95.<BR>--5 To effect, occasion,<BR>accomplish.<BR>--6 To make one sit<BR>down (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसत्तिः|आसत्ति
आसत्तिः f. [आ-सद्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Meeting,<BR>junction.<BR>--2 Intimate union,<BR>nearness, close contact; किमपि किमपि मंदं<BR>मंदमासत्तियोगात् U. 1. 27.<BR>--3 Gain,<BR>profit, acquirement.<BR>--4 (In Logic)<BR>Proximity, the absence of<BR>interruption in the apprehension of what is<BR>said, relation between two or more<BR>proximate terms and the sense<BR>conveyed by them; कारणं सन्निधानं तु<BR>पदस्यासत्तिरुच्यते Bhāṣā P. 83; वाक्यं स्याद्<BR>योग्यताकांक्षासत्तियुक्तः पदोच्चयः S. D. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसदनं|आसदन
आसदनं<BR>1 Gain, profit.<BR>--2<BR>Contact, union.<BR>--3 Nearness,<BR>proximity.<BR>--4 The act of sitting down.<BR>--5 A seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्न|आसन्नः
आसन्न p. p.<BR>1 Drawn near,<BR>approached, near (in time, place or<BR>number); आसन्नविंशाः nearly or<BR>about 20; at hand, close by,<BR>impending, imminent; आसन्नपतने कूले<BR>Ś. B.; ˚मरण, ˚काल q. v.<BR>--2 Adjacent,<BR>adjoining.<BR>--3 Well-placed.<BR>--4<BR>About to die.<BR>--न्नः The setting sun.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कालः {1} the hour of<BR>death. {2} one whose death is near.<BR>--परिचारकः, --चारिका personal<BR>attendant, body-guard; U. 1; Ś. 6.<BR>--प्रसव a. about to be confined or<BR>delivered; about to bring forth or<BR>lay eggs (as a hen &c.).<BR>--मृत्यु<BR>--शरीरपात a. one whose death has<BR>drawn near; Ku. 3. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादः|आसाद
आसादः Ved. Cushion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादनं|आसादन
आसादनं<BR>1 Putting or laying<BR>down.<BR>--2 Attacking.<BR>--3<BR>Overtaking, meeting with, going towards.<BR>--4 Obtaining, attaining,<BR>accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादयितव्य
आसादयितव्य, आसाद्य pot. p.<BR>Attainable, to be attained &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाद्य
आसादयितव्य, आसाद्य pot. p.<BR>Attainable, to be attained &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसादित|आसादितः
आसादित p. p.<BR>1 Obtained, got.<BR>--2 Reached, gone to.<BR>--3 Spread,<BR>extended.<BR>--4 Effected, completed.<BR>--5 Met with, attacked, overtaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्
आसन् n. Mouth; (a word<BR>optionally substituted for आस्य in all<BR>cases after acc. dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्वत्|आसन्वन्त्
आसन्वत् a. Ved. Having a mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसन्य
आसन्य a. Ved. Being in the<BR>mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंदः|आसन्द|आसन्दः
आसंदः [आसीदत्यस्मिन् प्रलयकाले<BR>निपातः] Viṣṇu or Vāsudeva.<BR>--दी<BR>[आसद्यतेऽस्याम्]<BR>1 A small couch or<BR>oblong chair; an arm-chair;<BR>K. 94; इयं वा आसंदी अस्यां हीदं<BR>सर्वमासन्नं Śat. Br.<BR>--2 A raised seat in a<BR>hall or assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंदिका
आसंदिका [स्वल्पार्थे कन्] A small<BR>chair; K. 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसंबाध|आसम्बाध
आसंबाध a. Blocked up,<BR>obstructed, confined (on all sides);<BR>आसंबाधा भविष्यंति पंथानः शरवृष्टिभिः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसव|आसवः
आसव see under आसु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसा
आसा Ved. Proximity, nearness;<BR>आसया near, in the presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसाधनं|आसाधन
आसाधनं Accomplishment,<BR>attainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसारः|आसार
आसारः [आ-सृ-घञ्]<BR>1 A hard or<BR>sharp-driving shower (of anything);<BR>आसारसिक्तक्षितिबाष्पयोगात् R. 13. 29;<BR>Me. 17; पुष्पासारैः 43; so तुहिन˚,<BR>रुधिर˚ &c.; बाष्पासारा M. 3. 20<BR>flooded or suffused with tears;<BR>धारासारैर्वृष्टिर्बभूव H. 3 it rained in torrents.<BR>--2<BR>Surrounding an enemy.<BR>--3 Attack,<BR>incursion.<BR>--4 The army of an ally<BR>or king (whose dominions are<BR>separated by other intervening<BR>states).<BR>--5 Provision, food; Pt. 3. 41,<BR>51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिकः|आसिक
आसिकः [असिः प्रहरणमस्य ठक्] A<BR>swordsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिका
आसिका [पर्यायेण आसनं, आस्-ण्वुल्]<BR>Turn or order of sitting, sitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिधारं|आसिधार
आसिधारं [असिधारा इव अस्त्यत्र<BR>अण्] N. of a particular vow;<BR>अभ्यस्यतीव व्रतमासिधारं R. 13. 67; for<BR>explanation see अप्तिधारा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0268-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिच्
आसिच् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To pour in<BR>or on, wet, water, sprinkle.<BR>--2 To<BR>fill with. --Caus. To have<BR>anything poured in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिच्
आसिच् f. An oblation which is<BR>poured out; a dish, vessel (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेकः|आसेक
आसेकः Wetting, watering,<BR>pouring in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेक्यः|आसेक्य
आसेक्यः A kind of eunuch or<BR>neuter man; पित्रोस्तु<BR>तुल्यवीर्यत्वादासेक्यः पुरुषो भवेत् ।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेचन|आसेचनः
आसेचन a. (नी f.) Charming,<BR>beloved; so आसेचनक.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Pouring<BR>into, wetting, sprinkling.<BR>--2 A<BR>vessel for fluids (Ved.); ˚वत् hollow,<BR>concave.<BR>--नी A small vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसिध्
आसिध् {c1c} P. To arrest, keep in<BR>custody (only in p. p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेद्धृ
आसेद्धृ m. One who arrests<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेधः|आसेध
आसेधः Arrest, custody, legal<BR>restraint; it is of four kinds:<BR>--स्यानासेधः कालकृतः प्रवासात् कर्मणस्तथा Nārada;<BR>i. e. confinement to a place,<BR>limitation of time, prohibition against<BR>departure, and restriction from<BR>doing anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेधक
आसेधक a. Restraining, confining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसु
आसु {c5c} U.<BR>1 To press out Soma<BR>juice, distil (mostly Ved.).<BR>--2<BR>(P.) To excite, enliven (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसवः|आसव
आसवः [आ सु-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Distillation.<BR>--2 Decoction.<BR>--3 Any<BR>spirituous liquor (distilled from sugar,<BR>molasses &c.); अनासवाख्यं करणं मदस्य<BR>Ku. 1. 31; कुमारी˚, द्राक्षा˚ &c; यच्च<BR>पक्वौषधांबुभ्यां सिद्धं मद्यं स आसवः Bhāva P.<BR>--4 A vessel for liquor.<BR>--5 Exciting.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द्रुः [आसवस्य कारणं द्रुः शाक˚<BR>त˚] N. of the Palmyra tree (the<BR>juice of which, on fermenting, forms<BR>a spirituous liquor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसावः|आसाव
आसावः A praiser, or one who<BR>extracts Soma juice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुतिः|आसुति
आसुतिः f.<BR>1 Distilling, distillation.<BR>--2 Decoction.<BR>--3 A drought so<BR>prepared.<BR>--4 Birth, production (प्रसव).<BR>--5 Exciting, enlivening (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुतीवलः|आसुतीवल
आसुतीवलः^1 [आसुतिरस्त्यस्य बलच् दीर्घः<BR>P. V. 2. 112]<BR>1 A sacrificing<BR>priest (who extracts Soma juice).<BR>--2 A sacrificer at the full and<BR>change of the moon.<BR>--3 A distiller.<BR>--4 A guardian of girls (कन्यापालक).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: also balac -> valac.  The affix is 'valac', not 'balac' acc. to abhyankar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुर|आसुरं|आसुरः
आसुर a. (री f.) [असुरस्येदं अण्<BR>opp. दैव]<BR>1 Belonging to Asuras.<BR>--2 Belonging to evil spirits; आसुरी<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">Page0269-b+ 56</a>]<BR>माया, आसुरी रात्रिः &c.<BR>--3 Infernal,<BR>demoniacal; आसुरं भावमाश्रितः<BR>Bg. 7. 15 (for a full exposition of what<BR>constitutes आसुर conduct, see<BR>Bg. 16. 7-24).<BR>--4 Not performing<BR>sacrifices.<BR>--5 Divine, spiritual.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>A demon [स्वार्थे अण्].<BR>--2 One of the<BR>eight forms of marriage, in which<BR>the bridegroom purchases the<BR>bride from her father or other<BR>paternal kinsmen; (see उद्वाह); आसुरो<BR>द्रविणादानात् Y. 1. 61; Ms. 3. 31.<BR>--3 (pl.)<BR>The stars of the southern hemisphere.<BR>--4 A prince of the warrior-tribe<BR>Asura.<BR>--री<BR>1 Surgery, curing by<BR>cutting by instruments.<BR>--2 A<BR>female demon, demoness;<BR>संभ्रमादासुरीभिः Ve. 1. 3.<BR>--3 N. of a plant<BR>Sinapis Ramosa Roxb. (Mar. मोहरी;<BR>रुई).<BR>--रं<BR>1 Blood.<BR>--2 Black salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरिः|आसुरि
आसुरिः A pupil of Kapila.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसुरीय
आसुरीय a. Belonging to or<BR>coming from Āsuri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसूत्रित
आसूत्रित a.<BR>1 Forming or<BR>wearing a garland.<BR>--2 Interwoven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेव्
आसेव् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To carry out,<BR>practise, perform zealously; धंर्म, व्रतं &c.<BR>--2 To indulge in, enjoy;<BR>अग्रवातमासेवमाना M. 1; V. 4; Ku. 1. 15.<BR>--3<BR>To accomplish; attend to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवा
आसेवा, --वनं<BR>1 Zealous practice,<BR>assiduous performance of any<BR>action.<BR>--2 Frequency, repetition;<BR>P. VIII. 3. 102; आसेवनं पौनःपुन्यं<BR>Sk.<BR>--3 Intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवनं|आसेवन
आसेवा, --वनं<BR>1 Zealous practice,<BR>assiduous performance of any<BR>action.<BR>--2 Frequency, repetition;<BR>P. VIII. 3. 102; आसेवनं पौनःपुन्यं<BR>Sk.<BR>--3 Intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेवित
आसेवित p. p.<BR>1 Performed, done.<BR>--2 Repeated.<BR>--तं Performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आसेविन्
आसेविन् a. Performing<BR>assiduously, indulging in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कंद्|आस्कन्द्
आस्कंद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To invade, attack;<BR>कथमिदानीमुन्मादोपरागो माधवेंदुमास्कंदति<BR>Māl. 9; आस्कंदल्लक्ष्मणं बाणैः Bk. 17. 82.<BR>--2 To step over, tread; Ki. 2. 20.<BR>--3 To depend or hang on (as the<BR>Vedāṅgas on the Vedas).<BR>--4 To<BR>jump, leap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कंदः|आस्कन्द|आस्कन्दः
आस्कंदः, --दनं<BR>1 An attack, assault;<BR>assailing, outraging; परवनिता<BR>˚प्रगल्भस्य Ve. 2.<BR>--2 Ascending,<BR>mounting; treading, stepping over;<BR>Ki. 13. 18.<BR>--3 Reproach, abuse.<BR>--4 The<BR>walk of a horse.<BR>--5 An assailant.<BR>--6<BR>Battle, war.<BR>--7 Drying.<BR>--8<BR>Effacing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कंदनं|आस्कन्दन|आस्कन्दनं
आस्कंदः, --दनं<BR>1 An attack, assault;<BR>assailing, outraging; परवनिता<BR>˚प्रगल्भस्य Ve. 2.<BR>--2 Ascending,<BR>mounting; treading, stepping over;<BR>Ki. 13. 18.<BR>--3 Reproach, abuse.<BR>--4 The<BR>walk of a horse.<BR>--5 An assailant.<BR>--6<BR>Battle, war.<BR>--7 Drying.<BR>--8<BR>Effacing, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कंदितं|आस्कन्दित|आस्कन्दितं
आस्कंदितं, --तकं The walk of a horse,<BR>galloping at full speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कंदितकं|आस्कन्दितक|आस्कन्दितकं
आस्कंदितं, --तकं The walk of a horse,<BR>galloping at full speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्कंदिन्|आस्कन्दिन्
आस्कंदिन् a.<BR>1 Jumping upon,<BR>assailing, attacking; R. 17. 52.<BR>--2<BR>Causing to flow.<BR>--3 Granting.<BR>--4<BR>Spending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्क्र
आस्क्र a.<BR>1 Attacking or<BR>assailing enemies, approaching.<BR>--2<BR>Joined or united.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तावः|आस्ताव
आस्तावः [आ-स्तु-घञ्]<BR>1 The<BR>place of reciting hymns in a<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--2 Praise, hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक|आस्तिकः
आस्तिक a. (की f.) [अस्ति परलोकः<BR>इति मतिर्यस्य, ठक्]<BR>1 One who believes<BR>in God and another world; यन्नास्त्येव<BR>तदस्ति वस्त्विति मृषा जल्पद्भिरेवास्तिकैः<BR>Prab. 2.<BR>--2 A believer in sacred<BR>tradition.<BR>--3 Pious, faithful, believing;<BR>आस्तिकः श्रद्दधानश्च Y. 1. 268.<BR>--कः or<BR>आस्तीकः N. of a Muni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकता
आस्तिकता, --त्वं, आस्तिक्यं<BR>1 Belief<BR>in God and another world;<BR>आस्तिक्यशुद्धमवतः प्रियधर्म धर्मं Ki. 18. 43.<BR>--2<BR>Piety, faith, belief; Bg. 18. 42;<BR>आस्तिक्यं श्रद्दधानता परमार्थेष्वागमार्थेषु<BR>Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिकत्वं|आस्तिकत्व
आस्तिकता, --त्वं, आस्तिक्यं<BR>1 Belief<BR>in God and another world;<BR>आस्तिक्यशुद्धमवतः प्रियधर्म धर्मं Ki. 18. 43.<BR>--2<BR>Piety, faith, belief; Bg. 18. 42;<BR>आस्तिक्यं श्रद्दधानता परमार्थेष्वागमार्थेषु<BR>Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तिक्यं|आस्तिक्य
आस्तिकता, --त्वं, आस्तिक्यं<BR>1 Belief<BR>in God and another world;<BR>आस्तिक्यशुद्धमवतः प्रियधर्म धर्मं Ki. 18. 43.<BR>--2<BR>Piety, faith, belief; Bg. 18. 42;<BR>आस्तिक्यं श्रद्दधानता परमार्थेष्वागमार्थेषु<BR>Śaṅkara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तीक|आस्तीकः
आस्तीक a. Relating to, or<BR>treating of, the sage आस्तीक.<BR>--कः N.<BR>of an old saint, son of Jaratkāru;<BR>(at whose intercession King<BR>Janamejaya spared the Nāga Takṣaka<BR>from the destruction to which<BR>he had doomed the serpent race).<BR>Mb. gives the following etymology<BR>of the name; नाम चास्याभवत्ख्यातं<BR>लोकेष्वास्तीक इत्युत । अस्तीत्युक्त्वा गतो यस्मात्पिता<BR>गर्भस्थमेव तम् ॥.<BR>--कं A section (पर्व)<BR>of the first book of the<BR>Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तृ
आस्तृ --स्तॄ {c5c} {c9c} U. To spread<BR>over, strew, cover, scatter over,<BR>bestrew, deck; दर्भानास्तीर्य,<BR>वसनमास्तीर्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तॄ
आस्तृ --स्तॄ {c5c} {c9c} U. To spread<BR>over, strew, cover, scatter over,<BR>bestrew, deck; दर्भानास्तीर्य,<BR>वसनमास्तीर्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरः|आस्तर
आस्तरः [आ-स्तृ-अप्]<BR>1 A<BR>covering, coverlet.<BR>--2 A carpet, bed,<BR>mat; वासो वल्कलमास्तरः किसलयानि<BR>Śānti. 2. 20.<BR>--3 Spreading (clothes<BR>&c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरण|आस्तरणं
आस्तरण a. Spreading, covering.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Spreading, strewing.<BR>--2 A<BR>bed, layer; कुसुम˚ a bed of flowers;<BR>Ku. 4. 35; सकुसुम˚ strewn with<BR>flowers Ś. 3; तमालपत्रास्तरणासु रंतुं<BR>R. 6. 64.<BR>--3 A cushion, quilt,<BR>bedclothes; गत˚ without the<BR>bedclothes.<BR>--4 A rug, carpet.<BR>--5 An<BR>elephant's housings, painted cloth<BR>(thrown on his back).<BR>--6 A layer<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-a" target="_blank">Page0270-a+ 57</a>]<BR>of Kuśa grass spread out at a<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0269-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तरणिक
आस्तरणिक a. (की f.) [आस्तरणं<BR>प्रयोजनमस्य ठक्]<BR>1 For spreading (as<BR>clothes &c.).<BR>--2 Resting on a carpet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्तारः|आस्तार
आस्तारः [आ-स्तॄ-घञ्] Spreading,<BR>strewing, scattering.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पंक्तिः<BR>N. of a metre, see App.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्त्र
आस्त्र a. [अस्त्रस्येदं अण्]<BR>Belonging to a missile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्था
आस्था {c1c} U.<BR>1 To stand or<BR>remain on or by, to occupy.<BR>--2 To<BR>ascend, mount; रथं, स्यंदनं &c.<BR>--3<BR>To use, have recourse to, resort to,<BR>practise, take, assume, follow; यथा<BR>यथा हि सद्वृत्तमातिष्ठंत्यनसूयकाः<BR>Ms. 10. 128, 2. 133, 10. 101;<BR>समाधिमास्थाय Ku. 5. 2 practising<BR>concentration of mind; स्वरूपं Ku. 5. 84<BR>assuming his own form; तनुं<BR>Mu. 7. 19; R. 6. 72; कूर्मसंकोचं Pt. 3. 21<BR>contracting himself like a tortoise;<BR>पदमातस्थुषा Ku. 6. 72 taking a place<BR>among; व्रतं Ve. 3. 19; so स्त्रीरूपं<BR>Pt. 3. 31; आस्थितविषादधियः Ki. 6. 29<BR>gloomy; Bg. 7. 20; K. 165;<BR>आस्थितविष्टरः R. 15. 79; सुहृदास्थितायां सभा<BR>यां Ku. 7. 29; विषमग्निं जलं रज्जुमा<BR>स्थास्ये तव कारणात् Mb. use;<BR>चिंतामौनमिवास्थिता V. 4. 38 lost in moody<BR>abstraction.<BR>--4 To do, perform,<BR>carry out.<BR>--5 To recognise,<BR>acknowledge, own.<BR>--6 To exhibit, aim at.<BR>--7 To undertake, promise, agree.<BR>--8 To behave. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause<BR>to stand.<BR>--2 To hold fast, cling to.<BR>--3 To collect, obtain.<BR>--4 To place<BR>in, infix.<BR>--5 To show, represent,<BR>introduce; प्रविश्य<BR>स्थापकस्तद्वत्काव्यमास्थापयेत्ततः S. D. 283; Mv. 1. 13.<BR>--6 To step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्था
आस्था [आस्था-अङ्]<BR>1 Regard,<BR>care, respect, consideration, care for<BR>(with loc.); मर्त्येष्वास्थापराङ्मुखः<BR>R. 10. 43; मय्यप्यास्था न ते चेत्<BR>Bh. 3. 30; 2. 98; see अनास्था<BR>also.<BR>--2 Assent, promise.<BR>--3 Prop,<BR>support, stay.<BR>--4 Hope, confidence;<BR>जयलक्ष्म्यां बबंधास्थां Rāj. T. 5. 245.<BR>--5 An effort.<BR>--6 State, condition.<BR>--7 An assembly.<BR>--8 A place or<BR>means of abiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थातृ
आस्थातृ a. Standing, mounting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थानं|आस्थान
आस्थानं<BR>1 A place, site.<BR>--2 Ground,<BR>base.<BR>--3 An assembly.<BR>--4 Care,<BR>regard; see आस्था.<BR>--5 A hall of<BR>audience; K. 8, 14.<BR>--6 Recreation-ground<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">Page0270-b+ 56</a>]<BR>(विश्रामस्थानं).<BR>--नी An assembly-room.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गृहं, --निकेतनं, --मंडपः an<BR>assembly-room;<BR>तदीयमास्थाननिकेतनाजिरं Ki. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थापनं|आस्थापन
आस्थापनं<BR>1 Placing, fixing, causing<BR>to stay or remain.<BR>--2 A<BR>strengthening remedy.<BR>--3 An enema of oil or<BR>ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थायिका
आस्थायिका An audience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थित
आस्थित p. p. (Used actively)<BR>1<BR>Dwelt, abiding; यत्नं Pt. 1. 220 using<BR>efforts carefully; उपायमास्थितस्यापि<BR>Śi. 2. 80, 9. 84; so नियमं, ध्यानं, धर्मं &c.<BR>--2 Having recourse to, resorting to,<BR>using, practising, betaking oneself<BR>to; सलिलाशयं Pt. 2.<BR>--3<BR>Having obtained or got, having reached<BR>to; ऐश्वर्यं, कामवशं &c.<BR>--4 Occupied;<BR>enclosed (as a hunting ground);<BR>R. 9. 53; दानवास्थितः शैलः Rām.<BR>--5<BR>Engrossed, engaged.<BR>--6 Covered<BR>(व्याप्त); Ki. 9. 9; spread,<BR>overspread.<BR>--7 Got, obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्थितिः|आस्थिति
आस्थितिः f. Condition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्नानं|आस्नान
आस्नानं<BR>1 Purity.<BR>--2 Water<BR>for washing, bath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्नेय
आस्नेय a. Bloody(fr. असन्);<BR>being in the mouth (fr. आसन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पदं|आस्पद
आस्पदं [आ-पद्-घ सुट्च]<BR>1 A place,<BR>site, seat, room; तस्यास्पदं<BR>श्रीर्युवराजसंज्ञितं R. 3. 36; ध्यानास्पदं<BR>भूतपतेर्विवेश Ku. 3. 43, 5. 10, 48, 69;<BR>कथं तादृशानां गिरि वैतथ्यमास्पदं कुर्यात्<BR>K. 174; राजन्यास्पदमलभत Dk. 160<BR>obtained a hold on the king.<BR>--2<BR>(Fig.) An abode, subject, receptacle;<BR>निधनता सर्वापदामास्पदं Mk. 1. 14;<BR>करिण्यः कारुण्यास्पदं Bv. 1. 2; आस्पदं<BR>त्वमसि सर्वसंपदां Ki. 13. 39; so दोष˚,<BR>उपहास˚ &c.<BR>--3 Rank, position,<BR>station; काव्यार्थभावनेनायमपि<BR>सभ्यपदास्पदं S. D.<BR>--4 Dignity, authority,<BR>office; लब्धास्पदोस्मीति विवादभीरोः<BR>M. 1. 17.<BR>--5 Business, affair.<BR>--6 Prop,<BR>support.<BR>--7 The tenth place from the<BR>लग्न q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्धा
आस्पर्धा Emulation, rivalry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्पर्धिन्
आस्पर्धिन् a. Emulous, striving<BR>after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फल्
आस्फल्, --स्फुल् {c10c} P. or Caus.<BR>1 To cause to flap, rock or shake;<BR>to strike or press against; आस्फालितं<BR>यत्प्रमदाकराग्रैः R. 16. 13; पयोराशेरोघः<BR>प्रलयपवनास्फालित इव U. 5. 9 lashed,<BR>stirred; Nāg. 1; शिलायामास्फालितः<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--2 To twang; धनुरास्फालयन्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">Page0270-c+ 55</a>]<BR>U. 4.<BR>--3 To sound, play upon (as a<BR>lute), strike; वीणामास्फालयंतीं K. 131;<BR>Śi. 1. 9.<BR>--4 To rend assunder, tear<BR>in pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फुल्
आस्फल्, --स्फुल् {c10c} P. or Caus.<BR>1 To cause to flap, rock or shake;<BR>to strike or press against; आस्फालितं<BR>यत्प्रमदाकराग्रैः R. 16. 13; पयोराशेरोघः<BR>प्रलयपवनास्फालित इव U. 5. 9 lashed,<BR>stirred; Nāg. 1; शिलायामास्फालितः<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--2 To twang; धनुरास्फालयन्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">Page0270-c+ 55</a>]<BR>U. 4.<BR>--3 To sound, play upon (as a<BR>lute), strike; वीणामास्फालयंतीं K. 131;<BR>Śi. 1. 9.<BR>--4 To rend assunder, tear<BR>in pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालः|आस्फाल
आस्फालः<BR>1 Striking, rubbing,<BR>causing to move gently.<BR>--2 Flapping.<BR>--3 Particularly, the flapping motion<BR>of an elephant's ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फालनं|आस्फालन
आस्फालनं<BR>1 Rubbing, striking or<BR>pressing against, stirring (as water<BR>&c.); flapping;<BR>अनवरतधनुर्ज्यास्फालमक्रूरपूर्वं Ś. 2. 4; आसां<BR>जलास्फालनतत्पराणां R. 16. 62, 3. 55, 6. 73;<BR>Amaru. 54; कुचतट˚ K. 6, 14, 57; ऐरावत˚<BR>कर्कशेन हस्तेन Ku. 3. 22 striking<BR>against.<BR>--2 Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फुजित्
आस्फुजित् m. N. of the planet<BR>Venus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटः|आस्फोट
आस्फोटः<BR>1 The Arka plant.<BR>--2<BR>The sound made by striking on the<BR>arms (Mar. छड्डू ठोकणें); कर˚ मिश्रेण<BR>K. 28.<BR>--3 Trembling, quivering.<BR>--4<BR>Striking or rubbing against, blow;<BR>पुच्छ˚ Mv. 5. 63; लांगूलास्फोटशब्दाच्च<BR>चलितः स महागिरिः Mb.<BR>--टा The<BR>नवमल्लिका plant, wild variety of<BR>jasmin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटक|आस्फोटकः
आस्फोटक a. Making a sound by<BR>striking on the arms.<BR>--क =<BR>पर्वतजपीलुभेदः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोटनं|आस्फोटन
आस्फोटनं<BR>1 Flapping, moving to<BR>and fro.<BR>--2 Trembling, shaking.<BR>--3<BR>Blowing, expanding.<BR>--4 Contracting,<BR>closing.<BR>--5 Slapping or clapping<BR>the arms, or the sound produced<BR>by it.<BR>--6 Disclosing, manifesting.<BR>--7 Winnowing, thrashing.<BR>--नी A<BR>gimlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोतः|आस्फोत
आस्फोतः, --तकः [आ-स्फुट् अच् पृषो˚<BR>टस्य तत्वं] N. of several trees; अर्क,<BR>कोविदार, भूपलाश.<BR>--ता, --तका N. of<BR>several plants; मल्लिका, अपराजिता, सारिवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्फोतकः|आस्फोतक
आस्फोतः, --तकः [आ-स्फुट् अच् पृषो˚<BR>टस्य तत्वं] N. of several trees; अर्क,<BR>कोविदार, भूपलाश.<BR>--ता, --तका N. of<BR>several plants; मल्लिका, अपराजिता, सारिवा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्माक
आस्माक a. (की f.), आस्माकीन<BR>a. [अस्मद्-अण्-खञ् अस्माकादेशः] Our,<BR>ours; आस्माकदंतिसान्निध्यात् Śi. 2. 63,<BR>8. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्य|आस्यं
आस्य a. Belonging to the mouth<BR>or face.<BR>--स्यं [अस्यते ग्रासोऽत्र,<BR>अस्ण्यत्]<BR>1 The mouth, jaws; आस्यकुहरे,<BR>विवृतास्यः.<BR>--2 Face; आस्यकमलं.<BR>--3 A<BR>part of the mouth used in<BR>pronouncing letters; तुल्यास्यप्रयत्नं सवर्णं<BR>P. I. 1. 9; आस्ये भवमास्यं ताल्वादिस्थानं<BR>Sk.; षडास्यानि Pt. 5. 55; (the six parts<BR>being the throat, head or brain<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">Page0271-a+ 55</a>]<BR>palate, tooth, lip, and nose).<BR>--4<BR>Mouth, opening; व्रणास्यं, अंकास्यं &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आसवः spittle, saliva.<BR>--पत्रं a lotus.<BR>--लांगलः {1} a dog. {2}<BR>a boar.<BR>--लोमन् n. beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0270-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यंधय
आस्यंधय a. [आस्यं धयति धे-ख मुम्]<BR>Kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्यंदनं|आस्यन्दन
आस्यंदनं Flowing, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्या
आस्या See under आस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रं|आस्र
आस्रं [अस्रमेव स्वार्थेऽण्] Blood.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पः {1} ‘blood-drinker’,<BR>demon. {2} the 19th lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्रवः|आस्रव
आस्रवः [आस्रु-अप्]<BR>1 Pain,<BR>affliction, distress.<BR>--2 Flowing,<BR>running.<BR>--3 Discharge,<BR>emission.<BR>--4 Fault, transgression.<BR>--5<BR>The foam on boiling rice.<BR>--6 (With<BR>Jainas) The impulse called योग or<BR>attention which the soul<BR>participates in the movement of its<BR>various bodies; it is defined as the<BR>‘action of the senses which impels the<BR>soul towards external objects’; it<BR>is good or evil according as it is<BR>directed towards good or evil<BR>objects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्राव|आस्रावः
आस्राव a. Flowing, running.<BR>--वः<BR>1 A wound.<BR>--2 Flow, issue,<BR>discharge.<BR>--3 Spittle, saliva.<BR>--4 Pain,<BR>affliction.<BR>--5 A disease of the body.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भेषजं medicament,<BR>medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्राविन्
आस्राविन् a. Flowing, emitting<BR>fluid or humour; an epithet of<BR>the elephant when ichor is issuing<BR>from its temples.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वद्
आस्वद् {c1c} A. To taste. --Caus. To<BR>taste, enjoy; संभोगं Me. 87;<BR>R. 3. 54; (fig.) to plunder, defraud;<BR>नास्वाद्यसे भुजंगैः K. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वाद|आस्वादः
आस्वाद a. Tasting, eating.<BR>--दः<BR>1<BR>Tasting, eating;<BR>चूतांकुरास्वादकषायकंठः Ku. 3. 32; काव्यामृतरसास्वादः<BR>H. 1. 152; मूखास्वादः Y. 3. 229<BR>kissing.<BR>--2 Relish, flavour, taste;<BR>ज्ञातास्वादो विवृतजघनां को विहातुं समर्थः<BR>Me. 41; सुखास्वादपरः H. 4. 76;<BR>चित्रास्वादकथैर्भृत्यैः Pt. 1.<BR>--3 Enjoying,<BR>experiencing; ˚वत् a. delicious in<BR>flavour, palatable; आस्वादवद्भिः<BR>कवलैस्तृणानां R. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादक
आस्वादक a. Tasting, enjoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वादनं|आस्वादन
आस्वादनं Tasting, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वाद्य
आस्वाद्य pot. p. To be tasted,<BR>delicious, sweet, palatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आस्वनित
आस्वनित or आस्वांत [आ-स्वन्-क्त]<BR>Sounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह
आह ind.<BR>1 An interjection<BR>showing (a) reproof; (b) severity;<BR>(c) command; (d) casting,<BR>sending.<BR>--2 An irregular verbal form of<BR>the 3rd. pers. sing. Pres. of a<BR>defective verb meaning ‘to say,’ or<BR>‘to speak’ (supposed by Indian<BR>grammarians to be derived from ब्रू<BR>and by European scholars from अह्;<BR>the only forms of the root existing<BR>in the language are:-- आत्थ, आहथुः,<BR>आह, आहतुः, and आहुः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहकः|आहक
आहकः [आ-हण्-ड-कन्] A<BR>peculiar disease of the nose; तनुना<BR>रक्तशोथेन युक्तो नासापुटांतरे । गात्रशूलज्वरकरः<BR>श्लेष्मणा ह्याहको ज्वरः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहंकार्यं|आहङ्कार्य
आहंकार्यं Conceitedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहन्
आहन् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To strike, hit, beat;<BR>कुट्टिममाजघान K. 10; परस्य शिर<BR>आहंति Sk.; Śi. 7. 17; दुर्जयान् करिणः<BR>… आहन्यात् Kām. 19. 60; said to be<BR>Atm. when the object is some<BR>limb of one's own body; आहते शिरः;<BR>but cf. आजघ्ने विषमविलोचनस्य वक्षः<BR>Ki. 17. 63; so आहध्वं मा रघूत्तमं;<BR>Bk. 8. 15, 5. 102 (see Sk. on<BR>P. I. 3. 28 also).<BR>--2 To strike, ring, beat (as a<BR>bell, drum &c.); Bk. 1. 27, 17. 7,<BR>Me. 66; R. 17. 11.<BR>--3 To kill, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहत|आहतं|आहतः
आहत p. p.<BR>1 Struck, beaten (as<BR>a drum &c.); Ku. 4. 25, 30; R. 4. 23,<BR>12. 77.<BR>--2 Trodden; पादाहतं यदुत्थाय<BR>मूर्धानमधिरोहति Śi. 2. 46; गजदंताहता<BR>वृक्षाः Rām.<BR>--3 Injured, killed.<BR>--4<BR>Dispelled, destroyed, removed.<BR>--5 Multiplied (in Math.);<BR>सूर्याब्धिसंख्यया द्वित्रिसागरैरयुताहतैः Sūrya S.;<BR>एकैकमब्देषु नवाहतेषु Bṛ. S. 8. 22.<BR>--6 Known, understood.<BR>--7 Rolled<BR>(as dice).<BR>--8 Uttered falsely.<BR>--तः<BR>A drum.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A new cloth or<BR>garment.<BR>--2 An old garment.<BR>--3<BR>A nonsensical or meaningless<BR>speech, an assertion of<BR>impossibility; e. g. एष वंध्यासुतो याति Subhāṣ.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--लक्षण a. = आहितलक्षण q. v.<BR>under आधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहतिः|आहति
आहतिः f.<BR>1 Killing.<BR>--2 A blow,<BR>hit, striking.<BR>--3 Coming (आगति).<BR>--4 Multiplication; अंशाहतिच्छेदवधेन<BR>भक्ता Līlā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहननं|आहनन
आहननं<BR>1 Striking at, beating.<BR>--2<BR>A stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहननीय
आहननीय a. Making oneself<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">Page0271-c+ 55</a>]<BR>known by beating a drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहनस्
आहनस् a. [आ-हन्-असुन्] To be<BR>beaten or pressed out (as Soma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघातः|आघात
आघातः [आ-हन्-घञ्]<BR>1 Striking,<BR>striking against; अभ्यस्यंति तटाघातं<BR>Ku. 2. 50; U. 5. 9.<BR>--2 A blow,<BR>stroke;<BR>तीव्राघातप्रतिहततरुस्कंधलग्नैकदंतः Ś. 1. 33; कठिनकुचतट˚<BR>Amaru. 55; पवन˚; पाद˚ &c.<BR>--3 A wound.<BR>--4 Killing: प्राणाघातान्निवृत्तिः<BR>Bh. 2. 26; Y. 3. 275.<BR>--5 One who beats or<BR>strikes.<BR>--6 A misfortune, distress.<BR>--7 Retention of urine (मूत्राघात).<BR>--8 A slaughter-house; आघातं<BR>नीयमानस्य वध्यस्येव पदे पदे H. 4. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आघातनं|आघातन
आघातनं<BR>1 Striking. killing.<BR>--2 A<BR>slaughter-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहव|आहवः
आहव, आहाव, आहवन &c.,<BR>See under आहु and आह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहाव|आहावः
आहव, आहाव, आहवन &c.,<BR>See under आहु and आह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवन|आहवनं
आहव, आहाव, आहवन &c.,<BR>See under आहु and आह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिकः|आहिक
आहिकः [अहिरिव, कन् स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>1<BR>The descending node (केतु).<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिंड्|आहिण्ड्
आहिंड् {c1c} A. To roam about,<BR>wander; आहिंड्यते अटव्या अटवीं Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहिंडिकः|आहिण्डिक|आहिण्डिकः
आहिंडिकः A man of mixed<BR>origin, the son of a Niṣāda father<BR>and Vaidehī mother; आहिंडिको<BR>निषादेन वैदेह्यामेव जायते Ms. 10. 37;<BR>(according to Kull., he was employed<BR>as a watchman on the outside of<BR>jails, and hence called आहिंडिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहितुंडिकः|आहितुण्डिक|आहितुण्डिकः
आहितुंडिकः [अहितुंडेन दीव्यति ठक्]<BR>A juggler, a snake-catcher, conjurer;<BR>अहंखल्वाहितुंडिको जीर्णविषो नाम Mu. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहीरणिन्
आहीरणिन् m. A two-headed<BR>snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहु|आहुः
आहु {c3c} U. To sacrifice, offer an<BR>oblation, worship (as fire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवः|आहव
आहवः A sacrifice; तत्र नाभवदसौ<BR>महाहवे Śi. 14. 44 (for other<BR>meanings see under आह्वे).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनं|आहवन
आहवनं<BR>1 A sacrifice;<BR>द्रष्टुमाहवनमग्रजन्मनाम् Śi. 14. 38.<BR>--2 An<BR>oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीय|आहवनीयः
आहवनीय pot. p. To be offered<BR>as an oblation.<BR>--यः A consecrated<BR>fire taken from the house-holder's<BR>perpetual fire, one of the three fires (i. e.<BR>the eastern) burning at a sacrifice;<BR>गार्हपत्यादाहवनीयं ज्वलंतमुद्धरेत् । पिता वा<BR>एषोऽग्नीनां यद्दक्षिणः पुत्रो गार्हपत्यः पौत्र<BR>आहवनीयः Āśval.; see also अग्नित्रेता under<BR>अग्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवनीयक|आहवनीयकः
आहवनीयक a. Fit for a burnt<BR>offering.<BR>--कः A consecrated fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0271-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहावः|आहाव
आहावः [आ-हु आधारे घञ्] Fire;<BR>see under आह्वे also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुत|आहुतं
आहुत p. p. Offered to the gods,<BR>sacrificed.<BR>--तं<BR>1 An offering made<BR>to men, hospitality.<BR>--2 The<BR>nourishment of all created beings (भूतयज्ञ<BR>or मनुष्ययज्ञ), regarded as one of the<BR>five principal sacrifices of the<BR>Hindus; cf. पंचयज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुतिः|आहुति
आहुतिः f.<BR>1 Offering an oblation to<BR>a deity, any solemn rite accompanied<BR>with oblations; होतुराहुतिसाधनं<BR>R. 1. 82.<BR>--2 An oblation offered to a<BR>deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुकः|आहुक
आहुकः N. of a prince,<BR>grandfather of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--काः N. of<BR>a people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुल्यं|आहुल्य
आहुल्यं N. of a leguminous shrub;<BR>(तगर, तरवट &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहृ
आहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring, fetch;<BR>यदेव वव्रे तदपश्यदाहृतं R. 3. 6; पुष्पं फलं<BR>चार्तवमाहरंत्यः 14. 77, 18. 8; प्रतिवाक्यं<BR>to bring an answer; वार्तां bring<BR>news.<BR>--2 To bring near, give;<BR>चंद्रगुप्ताय मेदिनीं Kām. 1. 5;<BR>अयाचिताहृत Y. 1. 215.<BR>--3 To recover,<BR>bring back.<BR>--4 To obtain, get,<BR>receive; Ms. 2. 183, 6. 27, 7. 80,<BR>8. 151, 11. 12; Y. 1. 97.<BR>--5 To have,<BR>assume; आजह्नतुस्तच्चरणौ… श्रियं<BR>Ku. 3. 33.<BR>--6 To cause, produce, lead<BR>to; बलोपचयं K. 105; प्रीतिं, क्रोधं &c;<BR>जनकानां कुले कीर्तिमाहरिष्यति मे सुता<BR>Rām.<BR>--7 To bring near (as wife),<BR>marry; Ku. 6. 28.<BR>--8 To wear,<BR>put on (as armour &c.); Ki. 1. 35.<BR>--9 To offer in a sacrifice, to<BR>perform (as a sacrifice); स<BR>विश्वजितमाजह्ने R. 4. 86, 14. 87.<BR>--10 To<BR>take away, attract (as mind).<BR>--11<BR>To separate, remove, draw off from.<BR>--12 To scare or frighten away,<BR>drive forth.<BR>--13 To use as food or<BR>drink, eat.<BR>--14 To speak, say, name,<BR>call. --Caus.<BR>1 To make one fetch<BR>or bring, cause to give or pay;<BR>Ms. 10. 119.<BR>--2 To eat.<BR>--3 To bring<BR>together, collect; Pt. 3. 151.<BR>--4 To<BR>cause, produce.<BR>--5 To exact.<BR>--6 To<BR>show, exhibit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर|आहरः
आहर a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Bringing, fetching, taking,<BR>seizing; समित्कुशफलाहरैः R. 1. 49.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Taking, seizing.<BR>--2<BR>Accomplishing, performing.<BR>--3 Offering a<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--4 Drawing in breath, inhaling.<BR>--5 The air so inhaled.<BR>--6 Inspiration,<BR>breath inspired.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करटा,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-b" target="_blank">Page0272-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--चेला, --निवपा, --निष्किरा, --वसना,<BR>--वितना, --सेना compounds of the class<BR>called मयूरव्यंसकादि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहरण|आहरणं
आहरण a. Taking away, robbing;<BR>as in अमृताहरणः.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Fetching,<BR>bringing (near); समिदाहरणाय प्रस्थिता<BR>वयं Ś. 1.<BR>--2 Seizing, taking; R. 6. 75.<BR>--3<BR>Removing, extracting.<BR>--4<BR>Performing, accomplishing (as sacrifice);<BR>अश्वमेधस्य कौरव्य चकाराहरणे मतिं Mb.<BR>--5 A<BR>dowry or present given to a bride (at<BR>the time of her marriage);<BR>सत्वानुरूपाहरणीकृतश्रीः R. 7. 32.<BR>--6<BR>Causing, inducing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहर्तृ|आहर्त्तृ
आहर्तृ a.<BR>1 One who takes or<BR>seizes.<BR>--2 Bringing, fetching.<BR>--3 Performing; आहर्ता क्रतूनां<BR>K. 5.<BR>--4 Causing, bringing on; आत्मनो<BR>वधमाहर्ता क्वासौ विहगतस्करः V. 5. 1. --m.<BR>--(र्ता) A copy-holder (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार|आहारः
आहार a. (रा or री f.)<BR>1<BR>Bringing near, procuring, getting;<BR>भाराहारः कार्यवशात् Sk.<BR>--2 Going to<BR>fetch; अयं गच्छति भर्ता मे फलाहारो<BR>महावनं Sāv. 4 23.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>Taking, fetching, or bringing near.<BR>--2 Employing, using.<BR>--3<BR>Taking food.<BR>--4 Food; (आहरंति<BR>रसमस्मादित्याहारः Sk.); ˚वृत्तिमकरोत् Pt. 1 took<BR>his dinner; फलाहार, ˚वृत्तिः means of<BR>livelihood; भैक्षाहारः living on alms;<BR>यवाहार, निराहार &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थिन्<BR>a. begging or seeking for food.<BR>--निःसरणमार्गः the posterior part, passage<BR>of voiding excrements.<BR>--पाकः {1}<BR>cooking. {2} digestion (of food).<BR>--विरहः want of food, privation,<BR>starvation.<BR>--संभवः the juice of the<BR>body, chyle, lymph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारक
आहारक a. Going to fetch or bring;<BR>एधानाहारको व्रजति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहारिकं|आहारिक
आहारिकं (With the Jainas) One<BR>of the five bodies belonging to the<BR>soul; according to Colebrooke, it is<BR>‘a minute form issuing from the<BR>head of a meditative sage to<BR>consult an omniscient saint and<BR>returning with the desired information.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहार्य|आहार्यः|आहार्य्य|आहार्य्यं|आहार्य्यः
आहार्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be taken or<BR>seized.<BR>--2 To be fetched or brought<BR>near.<BR>--3 To be extracted or removed.<BR>--4 To be pervaded (व्याप्य).<BR>--5<BR>Artificial, adventitious, incidental,<BR>external, accessory;<BR>आहार्यशोभारहितैरमायैः Bk. 2. 14; न रम्यमाहार्यमपेक्षते<BR>गुणं Ki. 4. 23; निसर्गसुभगस्य<BR>किमाहार्यकाडंबरेण Malli. on Ku. 7. 20.<BR>--6<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-c" target="_blank">Page0272-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Purposed, intended (as for<BR>instance, the identification or आरोप<BR>of उपमान or उपमेय in रूपक of which<BR>the speaker is fully cognisant);<BR>अयं चंद्रो मुखभित्यादौ चंद्रभिन्ने मुखे<BR>चंद्राभेदज्ञानं तच्चाहार्यमेव Tv.<BR>--7 Conveyed or<BR>effected by decoration or ornamentation,<BR>one of the 4 kinds of अभिनय q. v.<BR>--8 To<BR>be eaten.<BR>--9 To be worshipped (as<BR>Agni).<BR>--र्यः A kind of bandage<BR>(बंध).<BR>--र्यं<BR>1 Any disease to be<BR>treated by means of extracting.<BR>--2<BR>Extraction.<BR>--3 A vessel.<BR>--4 The<BR>ornamentative part of the drama, such<BR>as dress, decorations &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहेय|आहेयं
आहेय a. [अहेरिदं ढक्]<BR>Pertaining to a serpent; Pt. 1. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहो
आहो ind. An interjection<BR>expressing (a) Doubt or alternative<BR>(or), and usually standing as a<BR>correlative of किं; किं वैखानसं व्रतं<BR>निषेवितव्यं… आहो निवत्स्यति समं<BR>हरिणांगनाभिः Ś. 1. 27; दारत्यागी भवाम्याहो<BR>परस्त्रीस्पर्शपांसुलः Ś. 5. 29. (b)<BR>Interrogation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरुषिका [<BR>अहोपुरुषवुञ् P. II. 1. 72] {1} great<BR>self-conceit or pride; आहोपुरुषिका दर्पाद्या<BR>स्यात्संभावनात्मनि Ak.; आहोपुरुषिकां पश्य<BR>मम सद्रत्नकांतिभिः Bk. 5. 27. {2}<BR>military vaunting, boasting. {3}<BR>vaunting of one's own prowess;<BR>निजभुजबलाहोपुरुषिकां Bv. 1. 84.<BR>--स्वित्<BR>ind. a particle implying doubt, ‘or<BR>perhaps,’ or may it be &c.’ (corr. of<BR>किं); आहोस्वित्प्रसवो ममापचरितैर्विष्टंभितो<BR>वीरुधाम् Ś. 5. 9; किं द्विजः पचति<BR>आहोस्विद् गच्छति P. VIII. 1. 44 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्न|आह्नः
आह्न a. (ह्नी f.) Daily, performed in<BR>a day.<BR>--ह्नं [अह्रां समूहः अञ्] A series<BR>of days, many days,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्निक|आह्निकं
आह्निक a. (की f.) [अह्नि भवः,<BR>अह्ना निर्वृत्तः साध्यः ठञ्]<BR>1 Daily, diurnal,<BR>performed every day or on a day;<BR>आह्निकः स्वाध्यायः daily course of study;<BR>˚आचारः daily observances.<BR>--2<BR>Employed or occurring every day (as<BR>a teacher, servant, or fever).<BR>--कं<BR>1 Any religious rite or duty<BR>which is to be performed every<BR>day at a fixed hour; अत्राह्निकं<BR>सुरश्रेष्ठो जपते Mb.<BR>--2 Anything to be<BR>performed daily, such as taking<BR>meals, bathing &c.; कृताह्निकः संवृत्तः<BR>V. 4; समुद्रे कृताह्निकः Mv. 5.<BR>--3 Daily<BR>food.<BR>--4 Daily work or<BR>occupation, what may be read on one day.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">Page0273-a+ 28</a>]<BR>--5 A division of a work (such<BR>as that of the Mahābhāṣya).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0272-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादः|आह्लाद
आह्लादः Delight, joy; साह्लादं<BR>वचनं Pt. 4; ˚दुघ a. conferring<BR>delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादन
आह्लादन a. Giving delight.<BR>--नं<BR>Gladdening, delighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्लादिन्
आह्लादिन् a.<BR>1 Delighted, glad.<BR>--2<BR>Giving delight, gladdening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वृ
आह्वृ {c1c} P. Ved. To make crooked,<BR>injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूर्य
आहूर्य a.<BR>1 To be invoked.<BR>--2<BR>To be bent down or brought near.<BR>--3 To be made favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्रुत
आह्रुत p. p. Injured; ˚भेषज a.<BR>curing what is injured or bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वरकः|आह्वरक
आह्वरकः A low or expelled man<BR>(who, after having offered a sacrifice<BR>to the manes, takes the sacrificial<BR>food for himself); अन्नमपहर्तार<BR>आह्वरका भवंति थाद्धे सिद्धे P. III. 2. 135 Com.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वारकः|आह्वारक
आह्वारकः A recension of the black<BR>Yajur-veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वृति
आह्वृति a. Making crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वे
आह्वे {c1c} P.<BR>1 To call, summon.<BR>--2 To invite, invoke (in a<BR>liturgical sense).<BR>--3 (A.) To provoke,<BR>challenge; कृष्णश्चाणूरमाह्वयते Sk.; आह्वत<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-b" target="_blank">Page0273-b+ 29</a>]<BR>चेदिराण्मुरारिं Śi. 20. 1; Bk. 6. 25,<BR>8. 18, 15. 28, 42, 89. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>send for, call; कविमाह्वाययामास<BR>प्रस्तुतप्रतिपत्तये R. 15. 75; Bk. 6. 121.<BR>--2 To cause to invite or summon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहवः|आहव
आहवः [आहूयंतेऽरयोऽत्र, आ-ह्वे-अप्]<BR>1<BR>Battle, war, fight; एवंविधेनाहवचेष्टितेन<BR>R. 7. 67; हत्वा स्वजनमाहवे Bg. 1. 31.<BR>--2 Challenge, provoking, calling;<BR>˚काम्या desire of fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहावः|आहाव
आहावः<BR>1 A trough near a well<BR>for watering cattle.<BR>--2 War, battle.<BR>--3 Invoking, calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहुतिः|आहुति
आहुतिः f. Calling, invoking,<BR>challenging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूः
आहूः Ved. Calling, invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूत|आहूतं|आहूतः
आहूत p. p.<BR>1 Called, invoked,<BR>invited; यियक्षमाणेनाहूतः पार्थेनाथ<BR>द्विषन्मुरम् Śi. 2. 1.<BR>--2 Named, called.<BR>--तं<BR>Calling.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रपलायिन् m. a<BR>defendant or witness not appearing<BR>when summoned.<BR>--संप्लवः the time<BR>of universal destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आहूतिः|आहूति
आहूतिः f. [आ-ह्वे-क्तिन्] Calling,<BR>invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्व
आह्व a. [आ-ह्वे-ड]<BR>1 Who or<BR>what calls, a crier.<BR>--2 Named,<BR>called.<BR>--ह्वा [आ-ह्वे-अङ्]<BR>1 Calling,<BR>calling out.<BR>--2 A name, appellation,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-c" target="_blank">Page0273-c+ 30</a>]<BR>oft. at the end of comp.; अमृताह्वः,<BR>शताह्वा &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वयः|आह्वय
आह्वयः<BR>1 A name, appellation (as<BR>last member of comp.); काव्यं<BR>रामायणाह्वयं Rām.; चक्रसाह्वयं,<BR>चरणाह्वयाः; वृद्धेरप्याह्वया इमे Ak.<BR>--2 A<BR>lawsuit arising from a dispute about<BR>games with animals, as<BR>cock-fighting &c.; (one of the 18 titles of<BR>law); पणपूर्वकपक्षिमेषादियोधनं आह्वयः<BR>Rāghavānanda on Ms. 8. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वयन
आह्वयन a. Taking one's name.<BR>--नं Name, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वानं|आह्वान
आह्वानं<BR>1 Calling, inviting.<BR>--2 A<BR>call, invitation, summons (in<BR>general); सुहृदाह्वानं प्रकुवर्ति<BR>Pt. 3. 47.<BR>--3 A legal summons (from<BR>court or govt. to appear before a<BR>tribunal); Mk. 9.<BR>--4 Invocation<BR>of a deity; Ms. 9. 126.<BR>--5 A<BR>challenge.<BR>--6 A name, appellation.<BR>--7<BR>N. of a liturgical formula.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दर्शनं day of trial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वानयति
आह्वानयति Den. P. (In law) To<BR>summon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वायः|आह्वाय
आह्वायः<BR>1 A summons.<BR>--2 A<BR>name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आह्वायक|आह्वायकः
आह्वायक a. Calling, inviting.<BR>--कः A messenger, courier;<BR>आह्वायकान् भूमिपतेरयोध्यां Bk. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ The third letter of the<BR>Devanāgarī alphabet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इः|इ
इः [अ-इञ्] N. of Kāmadeva. --ind.<BR>An interjection of (1) anger; (2)<BR>calling; (3) compassion; (4)<BR>reproach; (5) wonder; (6) sorrow;<BR>(7) distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इ|इः
इ {vI.v} {c2c} P. (In Dhātup. written as<BR>इण्) (एति, इयाय, अगात्, एतुं, इत)<BR>1<BR>To go, go to or towards, come to<BR>or near; शशिनं पुनरेति शर्वरी<BR>R. 8. 56; ईयुर्भरद्वाजमुनेर्निकेतं Bk. 3. 40.<BR>--2 To arrive at, reach, obtain,<BR>attain to, go to or be reduced to a<BR>particular state, fall into;<BR>निर्बुद्धिः क्षयमेति Mk. 1. 14 goes to ruin,<BR>is ruined; so वशं, शत्रुत्वं, शूद्रतां &c.<BR>--3 To return.<BR>--4 To go away, retire;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1b" target="_blank">Page0273-1b+ 19</a>]<BR>elapse, pass.<BR>--5 To spring from,<BR>come or arise from.<BR>--6 To undertake<BR>anything (with acc.); सत्रमायन् Vāj.<BR>--7 To ask, beg.<BR>--8 To be; to appear.<BR>--9 To be employed in, go on with,<BR>be in a particular condition or<BR>relation, with a part. or instr.; कृषंतो<BR>ह स्म वैवपंतो यंति Śat. Br.; गवामयनेनेयुः<BR>Kāty.<BR>--10 To thrive, prosper. {vII.v}<BR>{c1c} U. = अय् q. v. {vIII.v} {c4c} A.<BR>1 To come,<BR>appear.<BR>--2 To run, wander.<BR>--3 To go<BR>quickly or repeatedly.<BR>--4 To ask,<BR>request. --Caus. To cause to go or<BR>come. [cf. L. eo; Gr. eimi with एमि].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्
इत् a. [इ-क्विप्] Going(at the end<BR>of a few comp.; as अर्थेत्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत|इतः
इत p. p. [इ-क्त]<BR>1 Gone to;<BR>रुचिरंकमनीयत रागमिता Śi. 6. 71.<BR>--2<BR>Returned.<BR>--3 Obtained.<BR>--4 Remembered.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1c" target="_blank">Page0273-1c+ 18</a>]<BR>--5 Attended by; स खलु तुरगैः<BR>सप्तभिरितः K. P. 10.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Course, mode<BR>of going.<BR>--2 A way.<BR>--3 Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिः|इति
इतिः f. Going, moving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्य|इत्यः
इत्य a. To be gone towards or<BR>approached; इत्यः शिष्येण गुरुवत्.<BR>--त्या<BR>1 Going; way.<BR>--2 A litter, palanquin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वन्
इत्वन् a. [इ-क्वनिन्] Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्वर|इत्वरः
इत्वर a. (री f.) [इ-क्वरप्]<BR>1 Going,<BR>travelling, a traveller.<BR>--2 Cruel,<BR>harsh.<BR>--3 Low, vile.<BR>--4 Despised,<BR>contemned.<BR>--5 Poor.<BR>--रः A eunuch.<BR>--री<BR>1 A disloyal or unchaste<BR>woman.<BR>--2 An abhisārikā q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

एष्यत्|एष्यन्त्
एष्यत् a. Future, to come;<BR>Ki. 1. 23; Śi. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इकटः|इकट
इकटः A sprout or stem of a<BR>reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0273-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्कटः|इक्कट
इक्कटः A kind of reed or grass<BR>for mats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्कवालः|इक्कवाल
इक्कवालः (In astr.) Good<BR>fortune, prosperity [cf. Pers. iqbāl].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुः|इक्षु
इक्षुः [इष्यतेऽसौ माधुर्यात्, इष्-क्सु<BR>Uṇ. 3. 157]<BR>1 Sugar-cane.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of another tree कोफिला.<BR>--3 Wish,<BR>desire.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कांडः, --डं N. of<BR>two different species of sugar-cane<BR>(काश and मुंजतृण).<BR>--कुट्टकः a gatherer<BR>of sugar-cane.<BR>--गंधः Saccharum<BR>Spontaneum.<BR>--ज a. produced from<BR>sugar-cane.<BR>--दंडः, --यष्टिः f. the stem<BR>or cane of Saccharum Officinale.<BR>--दर्भा a kind of grass.<BR>--दा N. of a<BR>river.<BR>--नेत्रं {1} a kind of sugar-cane.<BR>{2} the eye of sugar-cane.<BR>--पत्रः a<BR>kind of grain.<BR>--पाकः molasses.<BR>--प्रः<BR>N. of a tree (शरवृक्ष).<BR>--बालिका a<BR>kind of grass (काश).<BR>--भक्षिका a<BR>meal of sugar and molasses.<BR>--भक्षिती a woman who eats a sugar-cane.<BR>--मती, --मालिनी, --मालवी N. of a river.<BR>--मूलं the root of sugar-cane; a kind of<BR>sugar-cane.<BR>--मेहः diabetes or diabetes<BR>mellitus (cf. मधुमेह).<BR>--मेहिन् a.<BR>diabetic.<BR>--यंत्रं a sugar-mill.<BR>--योनिः<BR>[इक्षोरिव योनिः यस्य] Saccharum<BR>Officinarum (पुंड्रकैक्षु).<BR>--रसः {1} the<BR>juice of sugar-cane. {2} molasses,<BR>unrefined sugar. {3} a kind of काश<BR>grass; ˚क्वाथः raw or unrefined<BR>sugar, molasses.<BR>--वणं a sugar-cane<BR>wood.<BR>--वल्लरी, --वल्ली the common<BR>yellow cane.<BR>--वारि n.,<BR>--समुद्रः the<BR>sea of syrup, one of the seven seas.<BR>--वालिका [इक्षुरिव वलति वल्-ण्वुल्] {1}<BR>N. of a tree. (Mar. तालिमखाना.) {2} the<BR>काश grass.<BR>--वाटिका, --वाटी {1} a kind<BR>of sugar-cane (पुंड्रक). {2} a garden<BR>of sugar-canes.<BR>--विकारः {1} sugar,<BR>molasses. {2} any sweetmeat.<BR>--शाकटं, --शाकिनं a field fit for planting<BR>the sugar-cane.<BR>--सारः molasses,<BR>raw or unrefined sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुकः|इक्षुक
इक्षुकः Sugar-cane; see इक्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुकीया
इक्षुकीया A place abounding in<BR>sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्षुरः|इक्षुर
इक्षुरः<BR>1 Sugar-cane.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>kind of grass (काश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इक्ष्वाकुः|इक्ष्वाकु
इक्ष्वाकुः<BR>1 N. of the celebrated<BR>ancestor of the solar kings who ruled<BR>in Ayodhyā; he was the first of the<BR>Solar kings and was a son of Manu<BR>Vaivasvata; (cf. Bhāg. क्षुवतस्तु<BR>मनोर्जज्ञ इक्ष्वाकुर्घ्राणतः सुतः); इक्ष्वाकुवंशोऽ<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">Page0274-b+ 56</a>]<BR>भिमतः प्रजानां U. 1. 44.<BR>--2 A<BR>descendant of Ikṣvāku;<BR>गलितवयसामिक्ष्वाकूणामिदं हि कुलव्रतं R. 3. 70.<BR>--कुः f.<BR>A kind of bitter gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इख्
इख्, इंख् {c1c} P. (एखति, इंखति) To<BR>go, move; usually with प्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंख्|इङ्ख्
इख्, इंख् {c1c} P. (एखति, इंखति) To<BR>go, move; usually with प्र, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंग्|इङ्ग्
इंग् {c1c} U. (इंगति-ते, इंगितुं, इंगित)<BR>1<BR>To move, shake, be agitated; यथा<BR>दीपो निवातस्थो नेंगते Bg. 6. 19, 14. 23;<BR>त्वया सृष्टमिदं विश्वं यच्चेंगं यच्च नेंगति Mb.<BR>--2 To go, move. --Caus.<BR>1 To move,<BR>agitate, shake.<BR>--2 (In gram.) To<BR>separate the members of a<BR>compound; cf. इंग्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंग|इङ्ग|इङ्गं|इङ्गः
इंग a.<BR>1 Moveable; त्वया सृष्टमिदं<BR>विश्वं यच्चेंगं यच्च नेंगति Mb.<BR>--2<BR>Wonderful, surprising.<BR>--गः<BR>1 A hint<BR>or sign.<BR>--2 An indication of a<BR>sentiment by gesture.<BR>--3<BR>Knowledge.<BR>--गा A kind of counting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंगनं|इङ्गन|इंगन
इंगनं [इंग्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Moving, shaking,<BR>causing to move.<BR>--2 Knowledge.<BR>--3<BR>The operation of separating one<BR>member of a compound from<BR>another, as by an Avagraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंगित|इङ्गित|इङ्गितं
इंगित p. p. Moved, shaken.<BR>--तं<BR>[भावे-क्त]<BR>1 Palpitation, shaking.<BR>--2<BR>Internal thought, inward thought<BR>or secret aim, intention, purpose;<BR>˚आकारवेदिभिः K. 7; Pt. 1. 43;<BR>अगूढसद्भावमितींगितज्ञया Ku. 5. 62; तस्य<BR>संवृतमंत्रस्य गूढाकारेंगितस्य च R. 1. 20;<BR>Śi. 9. 69.<BR>--3 A hint, sign, gesture;<BR>Pt. 1. 44.<BR>--4 Particularly, the<BR>gesture or motion of the various<BR>limbs of the body indicating one's<BR>intentions; gesture suited to betray<BR>internal feelings; आकारैरिंगितैर्गत्या<BR>… गृह्यतेंऽतर्गतं मनः Ms. 8. 26.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कोविद, --ज्ञ a. skilled in the<BR>interpretation of internal sentiments<BR>by external gestures,<BR>understanding signs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंग्य|इङ्ग्य
इंग्य pot. p.<BR>1 Moveable from its<BR>place.<BR>--2 (In the Prātiśākhyas) A<BR>term for those words or parts of a<BR>compound which in certain<BR>grammatical operations may be separated<BR>from the preceding parts; a word<BR>which in the Pada-Pāṭha is<BR>divided by the Avagraha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंगुः|इङ्गु|इङ्गुः
इंगुः A disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंगुदः|इङ्गुद|इंगुद|इङ्गुदः
इंगुदः, --दी, इंगुलः N. of a medicinal<BR>tree, Terminalia Catappa; (Mar.<BR>हिंगणबेट); इंगुदीपादपः सोऽयं U. 1. 2;<BR>प्रस्निग्धाः क्वचिदिंगुदीफलभिदः सुच्यंत<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">Page0274-c+ 54</a>]<BR>एवोपलाः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>--दं The nut of the<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंगुदी|इङ्गुदी
इंगुदः, --दी, इंगुलः N. of a medicinal<BR>tree, Terminalia Catappa; (Mar.<BR>हिंगणबेट); इंगुदीपादपः सोऽयं U. 1. 2;<BR>प्रस्निग्धाः क्वचिदिंगुदीफलभिदः सुच्यंत<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">Page0274-c+ 54</a>]<BR>एवोपलाः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>--दं The nut of the<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंगुलः|इङ्गुल|इङ्गुलः
इंगुदः, --दी, इंगुलः N. of a medicinal<BR>tree, Terminalia Catappa; (Mar.<BR>हिंगणबेट); इंगुदीपादपः सोऽयं U. 1. 2;<BR>प्रस्निग्धाः क्वचिदिंगुदीफलभिदः सुच्यंत<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">Page0274-c+ 54</a>]<BR>एवोपलाः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>--दं The nut of the<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इचिकिलः|इचिकिल
इचिकिलः A pond; mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छक|इच्छकः
इच्छक, इच्छा See under इष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छा
इच्छक, इच्छा See under इष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छकः|इच्छक
इच्छकः N. of a tree, the citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्जलः|इज्जल
इज्जलः A small tree growing<BR>near water (हिज्जल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इज्य|इज्यः
इज्य pot. p. (of यज्) To be<BR>worshipped.<BR>--ज्यः<BR>1 A teacher.<BR>--2<BR>An epithet of बृहस्पति, the teacher<BR>of the gods.<BR>--3 The Puṣya<BR>Nakṣatra.<BR>--4 The Supreme being.<BR>--5<BR>An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--ज्या<BR>1 A<BR>sacrifice; जगत्प्रकाशं तदशेषमिज्यया<BR>R. 3. 48, 1. 68, 15. 2; Bg. 11. 53, 9. 25.<BR>--2 A gift, donation.<BR>--3 An image.<BR>--4 Worship, reverence.<BR>--5 Meeting,<BR>union.<BR>--6 A bawd or procuress.<BR>--7 A cow.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शीलः a<BR>constant sacrificer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंचाकः|इञ्चाक|इञ्चाकः
इंचाकः A shrimp (जलवृश्चिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट्
इट् {c1c} P. [एटति, इटित]<BR>1 To go,<BR>go to or towards.<BR>--2 To err.<BR>--3<BR>To make haste (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इटः|इट
इटः Ved.<BR>1 Cane or grass.<BR>--2 A<BR>mat, a web made of cane or grass.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सूनं a mat (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इट्चरः|इट्चर
इट्चरः [इषा कामेन चरति] A bull<BR>or steer allowed to go at liberty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इड्
इड् f. (also written इल् in Veda).<BR>[इल्-क्विप्, वा लस्य डः]<BR>1 An offering<BR>or oblation, libation offered to the<BR>gods.<BR>--2 Prayer, flow of speech.<BR>--3 The earth.<BR>--4 Food.<BR>--5 The<BR>rainy season.<BR>--6 The third of the<BR>five prayāgas (इडो यजति).<BR>--7 People<BR>or subjects.<BR>--8 (--pl.) The object of<BR>devotion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--देवता a deity<BR>of libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडस्पतिः|इडस्पति
इड(ल)स्पतिः N. of Viṣṇu or<BR>of Pūṣan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलस्पतिः
इड(ल)स्पतिः N. of Viṣṇu or<BR>of Pūṣan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडः|इड
इडः An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडा
इडा --ला [इल्-अच्, वा लस्य डत्वं]<BR>1<BR>The earth; प्रबुध्यते नूनमिडातलस्थः Mb.<BR>--2 Speech.<BR>--3 An offering, libation.<BR>(coming between प्रयाग and अनुयाग).<BR>--4 Refreshing draught.<BR>--5 (Hence)<BR>Food.<BR>--6 (Fig.) Steam or flow of<BR>praise or worship personified<BR>as the goddess of sacred speech.<BR>--7<BR>Libation and offering of milk.<BR>--8<BR>A cow.<BR>--9 N. of a goddess,<BR>daughter of Manu. (She is the wife of<BR>Budha and mother of Purūravas;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">Page0275-a+ 57</a>]<BR>she is also called मैत्रावरुणी as the<BR>daughter of मित्र and वरुण).<BR>--10 N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--11 Heaven.<BR>--12 A tubular<BR>vessel (नाडीभेद), (being in the<BR>right side of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इला
इडा --ला [इल्-अच्, वा लस्य डत्वं]<BR>1<BR>The earth; प्रबुध्यते नूनमिडातलस्थः Mb.<BR>--2 Speech.<BR>--3 An offering, libation.<BR>(coming between प्रयाग and अनुयाग).<BR>--4 Refreshing draught.<BR>--5 (Hence)<BR>Food.<BR>--6 (Fig.) Steam or flow of<BR>praise or worship personified<BR>as the goddess of sacred speech.<BR>--7<BR>Libation and offering of milk.<BR>--8<BR>A cow.<BR>--9 N. of a goddess,<BR>daughter of Manu. (She is the wife of<BR>Budha and mother of Purūravas;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">Page0275-a+ 57</a>]<BR>she is also called मैत्रावरुणी as the<BR>daughter of मित्र and वरुण).<BR>--10 N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--11 Heaven.<BR>--12 A tubular<BR>vessel (नाडीभेद), (being in the<BR>right side of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0274-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडावत्|इडावन्त्
इडावत् a.<BR>1 Possessed of<BR>sacrificial food.<BR>--2 Refreshing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडाचिका
इडाचिका A wasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिका
इडिका The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इडिक्कः|इडिक्क
इडिक्कः A wild goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इड्वरः|इड्वर
इड्वरः see इट्चर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंड्रः|इण्ड्र|इंड्रं|इण्ड्रः
इंड्रः, --ड्रं(इंड्वं) (Dual) Two<BR>round small plates used as<BR>coverings for the hands in taking the<BR>fire-pans from the fire; अथैनमिंड्राभ्यां<BR>परिगृह्णाति Śat. Br. (उखा याभ्यां गृह्यंते तौ<BR>इंड्रौ Karka).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंड्रं|इण्ड्र|इंड्रः|इण्ड्रः
इंड्रः, --ड्रं(इंड्वं) (Dual) Two<BR>round small plates used as<BR>coverings for the hands in taking the<BR>fire-pans from the fire; अथैनमिंड्राभ्यां<BR>परिगृह्णाति Śat. Br. (उखा याभ्यां गृह्यंते तौ<BR>इंड्रौ Karka).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंड्वं|इण्ड्व
इंड्रः, --ड्रं(इंड्वं) (Dual) Two<BR>round small plates used as<BR>coverings for the hands in taking the<BR>fire-pans from the fire; अथैनमिंड्राभ्यां<BR>परिगृह्णाति Śat. Br. (उखा याभ्यां गृह्यंते तौ<BR>इंड्रौ Karka).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतर|इतरः
इतर pron. a. (रा f.,<BR>--रत् n.)<BR>1<BR>Another, the other (of two), the<BR>remaining one of the two; इतरो<BR>दहने स्वकर्मणां R. 8. 20 v. l.<BR>--2 The rest<BR>or others (pl.).<BR>--3 Other than,<BR>different from (with abl.);<BR>इतरतापशतनि यथेच्छया वितर तानि सहे<BR>चतुरानन Udb.; इतरो रावणादेष राघवानुचरो<BR>यदि Bk. 8. 106.<BR>--4 Opposite of,<BR>either used by itself as an adj. or<BR>at the end of comp.; जंगमानीतराणि<BR>च Rām.; विजयायेतराय वा Mb.;<BR>सुलभेतरसंप्रयोगां M. 5. 3 opposite of,<BR>other than easy, difficult; so<BR>दक्षिण˚ left; वाम˚ right &c.<BR>--5 Low,<BR>mean, vulgar, ordinary; इतर इव<BR>परिभूय ज्ञानं मन्मथेन जडीकृतः K. 154,<BR>160, 203, 273. इतर-इतर the one-the<BR>other, this-that.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इतर<BR>pron. a. respective, reciprocal, one with<BR>another (chiefly in oblique cases or<BR>in comp.); वियुक्तावितरेतरं<BR>Ms. 9. 102; ˚काम्यया 3. 35; R. 7. 54.<BR>˚आश्रयः mutual dependence,<BR>inter-connection. ˚योगः {1} mutual<BR>connection or union; Śi. 10. 24. {2} a<BR>variety of the Dvandva compound<BR>(opp. समाहारद्वंद्ब) where each<BR>member of the compound is<BR>viewed separately; as प्लक्षन्यग्रोधौ<BR>छिनत्ति.<BR>--जनाः (pl.) {1} other men.<BR>{2} euphemistically said of certain<BR>beings considered as spirits of<BR>darkness of which Kubera is one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरतः
इतरतः, इतरत्र ind. Otherwise than,<BR>different from, elsewhere; see अन्यतः,<BR>अन्यत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरत्र
इतरतः, इतरत्र ind. Otherwise than,<BR>different from, elsewhere; see अन्यतः,<BR>अन्यत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरथा
इतरथा ind.<BR>1 In another manner,<BR>in a contrary manner.<BR>--2<BR>Perversely.<BR>--3 On the other hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतरेद्युः
इतरेद्युः ind. On another day, the<BR>other day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतस्
इतस् ind. [इदम्-तसिल् इशादेशः Tv.]<BR>1 Hence, from here or hence.<BR>--2<BR>From this person, from me; इतः स<BR>दैत्यः प्राप्तश्रीर्नेत एवार्हति क्षयं<BR>Ku. 2. 55.<BR>--3 In this direction, towards<BR>me, here; इतो निषीदेति विसृष्टभूमिः<BR>Ku. 3. 2; प्रयुक्तमप्यस्त्रमितो वृथा स्यात्<BR>R. 2. 34; इतः स्वपिति केशवः &c. Bh. 2. 76;<BR>इतोगतमनुरागं V. 2; ˚गतवृत्तांतं न<BR>स्मरति Ś. 4 news of this place; इत इतो<BR>देवः this way, this way, my lord (in<BR>dramas).<BR>--4 Hence, for this reason,<BR>on this ground; इतश्च परमात्मैवेहात्ता<BR>भवितुमर्हति Ś. B.<BR>--5 From this world.<BR>--6 From this time. इतः-इतः (a)<BR>on the one hand-on the other<BR>hand; इतस्तपस्विकार्यमितो<BR>गुरुजनाज्ञा Ś. 2; (b) in one place-in<BR>another place, here-there; K. 27;<BR>इतश्चेतश्च hither and thither; hence<BR>and thence, here and there, to and<BR>fro; इतश्चेतश्च धावतां; now,<BR>therefore; इतस्ततः here and there,<BR>hither and thither, to and fro;<BR>लांगूलविक्षेपविसर्पिशोभैरितस्ततश्चंद्रमरीचिगौरैः<BR>Ku. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इति|इतिः
इति ind.<BR>1 This particle is<BR>most generally used to report the<BR>very words spoken or supposed to be<BR>spoken by some one, as represented<BR>by the quotation marks in English.<BR>The speech reported may be<BR>(1) a single word used merely<BR>to express what the form of the<BR>word is, when it is used as it is<BR>(शब्दस्वरूपद्योतक); राम रामेति रामेति<BR>कूजंतं मधुराक्षरं Rām.; अत एव गवित्याह<BR>Bhartṛ.; (2) or a substantive, which<BR>must be put in the nominative case<BR>when its meaning is to be<BR>indicated (प्रातिपदिकार्थद्योतक);<BR>चयस्त्विषामित्यवधारितं पुरा… क्रमादमुं नारद<BR>इत्यबोधि सः Śi. 1. 3; अवैमि चैनामनघेति<BR>R. 14. 40; दिलीप इति राजेंदुः R. 1. 12;<BR>sometimes with acc. कैवर्तमिति यं<BR>प्राहुः Ms. 10. 34; Bg. 6. 2; (3)<BR>or a whole sentence when इति is<BR>merely used at the end of that<BR>sentence; (वाक्यार्थद्योतक); ज्ञास्यसि<BR>कियद्भुजो मे रक्षति मौर्वीकिणांक इति<BR>Ś. 1. 13; तयोर्मुनिकुमारयोरन्यतरःकथयति<BR>अक्षमालामुपयाचितुमागतोस्मीति K. 151.<BR>--2<BR>Besides this general sense इति has<BR>the following senses:-- (a) Cause,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-c" target="_blank">Page0275-c+ 57</a>]<BR>as expressed by ‘because’, ‘since’,<BR>‘on the ground that’, in English;<BR>वैदेशिकोस्मीति पृच्छामि U.; पुराणमित्येव न<BR>साधु सर्वं M. 1. 2; oft. with किं<BR>q. v. (b) Purpose or motive, as<BR>expressed by ‘that’ ‘in order that’<BR>शरीरस्य विनाशो मा भूदिति मयेदमुत्क्षिप्य<BR>समानीतं K. 320; R. 1. 37. (c)<BR>Thus, to mark the conclusion<BR>(opp. अथ); इति प्रथमोंऽकः thus<BR>or here ends the first Act. (d) It is<BR>often used to include under one head<BR>a number of separate objects grouped<BR>together; पृथिव्यापस्तेजो वायुराकाशं<BR>कालो दिगात्मा मन इति द्रव्याणि T. S.<BR>(e) So, thus, in this manner;<BR>इत्युक्तवंतं परिरभ्य दोर्भ्यां Ki. 11. 80. (f)<BR>Of this nature or description;<BR>गौरश्वः पुरुषो हस्तीति जातिः. (g) As<BR>follows, to the following effect;<BR>रामामिधानो हरिरित्युवाच R. 13. 1. (h)<BR>As for, in the capacity of, as<BR>regards, showing capacity or<BR>relation; पितेति स पूज्यः, अध्यापक इति<BR>निंद्यः, शीघ्रमिति सुकरं, निभृतमिति<BR>चिंतनीयं भवेत् Ś. 3. (i) It is often<BR>used with the name of an author to<BR>form an Avyayībhāva comp;<BR>इतिपाणिनि thus according to Pāṇini.<BR>(j) Illustration (usually with<BR>आदि); इंदुरिंदुरिव श्रीमानित्यादौ तदनन्वयः<BR>Chandr.; गौः शुक्लश्चलो डित्थ इत्यादौ<BR>K. P. 2. (k) A quotation or an<BR>opinion accepted; इति पाणिनिः,<BR>इत्यापिशलिः, इत्यमरः, विश्वः &c. (l) It is often<BR>used by commentators after<BR>quoting a rule in the sense of<BR>‘according to such a rule’; शकि लिङ् च (<BR>P. III. 3. 172) इति शक्यार्थे लिङ् Malli. Other<BR>senses mentioned are:-- (m.)<BR>Manifestation. (n.) Order. (o)<BR>Arrangement. (p) Identity. (q)<BR>Proximity. (r) Visibility. (s)<BR>Excess or superiority. (t) Requiring.<BR>(इति स्वरूपे सान्निध्ये विवक्षानियमे मते । हेतौ<BR>प्रकारप्रत्यक्षप्रकाशेप्यवधारणे, एवमर्थे समाप्तौ<BR>च ॥ Hem.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः sum<BR>and substance, meaning in short<BR>(often used by commentators).<BR>--अर्थं<BR>ind. for this purpose, hence.<BR>--आदि<BR>a. having such a thing or things at<BR>the beginning, so forth, et cætera<BR>(&c.).<BR>--उक्तं information, report.<BR>--कथ a. {1} not fit to be<BR>believed, untrustworthy. {2} wicked, lost.<BR>--(था) a meaningless or<BR>nonsensical talk.<BR>--कर्तव्य, --करणीय<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">Page0276-a+ 56</a>]<BR>a. proper or necessary to be<BR>done according to certain rules.<BR>--(व्यं, --यं) duty, obligation; एवं<BR>सर्वं विधायेदमितिकर्तव्यमात्मनः Ms. 7. 142,<BR>Ki. 7. 17; ˚ता, --कार्यता, कृत्यता any<BR>proper or necessary duty, obligation;<BR>इतिकर्तव्यतामूढः wholly at a loss what<BR>to do, embarrassed, perplexed.<BR>--मात्र<BR>a. of such extent or quality.<BR>--वृत्तं<BR>{1} occurrence, event {2} a tale, story.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0275-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिथ
इतिथ a. Ved. Such a one, such.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिवत्
इतिवत् ind. In the same manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिह
इतिह ind. Thus indeed, quite in<BR>conformity to tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इतिहासः|इतिहास
इतिहासः [fr. इति-ह-आस (3rd. pers.<BR>sing. Perf. of अस् to be); so it has<BR>been]<BR>1 History (legendary or<BR>traditional);<BR>धर्मार्थकाममोक्षाणामुपदेशसमन्वितं । पूर्ववृत्तं कपायुक्तमितिहासं प्रचक्षते ॥<BR>--2 Heroic history (such as the<BR>Mahābhārata).<BR>--3 Historical<BR>evidence, tradition (which is<BR>recognized as a proof by the<BR>Paurāṇikas).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--निबंधनं legendary<BR>composition or narrative; Ś. 3.<BR>--पुराणं history and legendary<BR>stories.<BR>--वादः historical story,<BR>legend; Māl. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्किला
इत्किला N. of a perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थं|इत्थ
इत्थं ind. Thus, so, in this<BR>manner; इत्थं रतेः किमपि भूतमदृश्यरूपं<BR>Ku. 4. 45; इत्थंगते under these<BR>circumstances, such being the case;<BR>इत्थंगते किमस्माभिः करणीयं Ś. 4;<BR>R. 9. 81.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारं ind. in this<BR>manner.<BR>--भूत a. {1} so circumstanced,<BR>being in this state, being thus;<BR>˚आख्याने P. I. 4. 90; Me. 94;<BR>Ku. 6. 26; Ś. 3, 5; कथमित्थंभूता M. 5,<BR>K. 146. {2} true or faithful (as a<BR>story).<BR>--भावः being thus endowed,<BR>having these qualities.<BR>--विध a. {1} of<BR>such kind. {2} endowed with such<BR>qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थशालः|इत्थशाल
इत्थशालः N. of the third Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्था
इत्था ind. Ved.<BR>1 In this<BR>manner, thus.<BR>--2 A particle of<BR>affirmation used to lay stress on a<BR>following word, indeed.<BR>--3 Truly, really.<BR>˚धी a. performing such or true<BR>works.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इत्थात्
इत्थात् ind. Thus, in this way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्
इद् ind.<BR>1 A particle of<BR>affirmation, even, just, only; especially in<BR>strengthening a statement; अर्थज्ञ<BR>इत्सकलं भद्रमश्नुते Nir.<BR>--2 It is often<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-b" target="_blank">Page0276-b+ 56</a>]<BR>added to words expressing excess<BR>or exclusion; विश्व इत्, एक इत् &c.<BR>--3<BR>At the beginning of sentences it<BR>often adds emphasis to pronouns,<BR>prepositions &c. (Its place is taken<BR>by एव in classical Sanskrit).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदं|इद
इदं pron. a. [अयं m., इयं f., इदं<BR>n.]<BR>1 This here, referring to<BR>something near the speaker; (इदमस्तु<BR>संनिकृष्टं रूपं); इदं तत्… इति यदुच्यते Ś. 5 here<BR>is the truth of the saying.<BR>--2<BR>Present, seen; the nominative forms<BR>are used with verbs in the sense<BR>of ‘here’; इयमस्मि here am I; so<BR>इमे स्मः; अयमागच्छामि here I come.<BR>--3 It often refers to something<BR>immediately following, while एतद्<BR>refers to what precedes;<BR>अनुकल्पस्त्वयं ज्ञेयः सदा सद्भिरनुष्टितः । Ms. 3. 147<BR>(अयं = वक्ष्यमाणः Kull.); श्रुत्वैतदिदमूचुः.<BR>--4 It occurs connected with यत्,<BR>तत्, एतद्, अदस्, किं or a personal<BR>pronoun, either to point out<BR>anything more distinctly and<BR>emphatically, or sometimes pleonastically;<BR>कोयमाचरत्यविनयं Ś. 1. 25; सेयं, सोयं,<BR>this here; so इमास्ताः; अयमहं भोः Ś. 4<BR>ho, here am I. --ind. Ved.<BR>1 Here,<BR>to this place.<BR>--2 Now.<BR>--3 There.<BR>--4 With these words, herewith.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रथम a. doing anything<BR>for the first time.<BR>--प्रकारं ind. in<BR>this manner.<BR>--युगं the present<BR>Yuga.<BR>--रूप a. of this shape.<BR>--वसु<BR>a. Ved. rich in this and that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंतन
इदंतन a. (नी f.) Of this time,<BR>present; momentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंता
इदंता [इदमो भावः] Identity,<BR>sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंमय
इदंमय a. Made or consisting of this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदंयु
इदंयु a. Wishing this.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदा
इदा ind. Now, at this<BR>(present) moment; oft. with अहन्;<BR>इदाचिदह्नः; इदा ह्यः only yesterday.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वत्सरः, so इदुवत्सरः or<BR>इद्वत्सरः one of the five years in which<BR>gifts of clothes and food are said to<BR>be productive of great rewards.<BR>--वत्सरीय or इद्वत्सरीय a. belonging<BR>to such a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानीं
इदानीं ind. [इदं-दानीं इश् च]<BR>1<BR>Now, at this moment, in this case,<BR>just now, even now; वत्से<BR>प्रतिष्ठस्वेदानीं Ś. 4; आर्यपुत्र इदानीमसि U. 3;<BR>इदानीमह्नः now a days; इदानीमेव just<BR>now; इदानीमपि now also, in this<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">Page0276-c+ 54</a>]<BR>case also; तत इदानीं thereupon,<BR>then, from that time.<BR>--2 As a<BR>measure of time, it is equal to<BR>onefifteenth part of an एतर्हि; cf.<BR>यावंत्येतर्हीणि तावंति पंचदशकृत्व इदानीनि Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इदानींतन|इदानीन्तन|इदानीन्तनं
इदानींतन a. (नी f.) Present,<BR>momentary, of the present<BR>moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्म|इध्मं|इध्मः
इध्म, इद्ध See under इंध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्ध|इद्धं|इद्धः
इध्म, इद्ध See under इंध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्
इन् {c6c} {c8c} P. Ved.<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To<BR>advance or rush upon, press upon;<BR>drive.<BR>--3 To invigorate.<BR>--4 To<BR>force, compel.<BR>--5 To drive away,<BR>remove.<BR>--6 To take possession of,<BR>pervade, fill.<BR>--7 To dispose.<BR>--8 To<BR>be lord or master (of anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन|इनः
इन a.<BR>1 Able, strong, powerful,<BR>mighty.<BR>--2 Bold, determined.<BR>--3<BR>Glorious.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A lord, master.<BR>--2 The sun; Śi. 2. 65.<BR>--3 A king;<BR>न न महीनमहीनपराक्रमं R. 9. 5.<BR>--4<BR>The lunar mansion Hasta.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कांतः sunstone (सूर्यकांत); Bh. 2. 37.<BR>--सभं a royal court or assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इनक्षति
इनक्षति (Desid. of नक्ष्) Ved. To<BR>try to reach, strive to get.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंथिहा|इन्थिहा
इंथिहा An astronomical term<BR>taken from the Arabic (= मुथहा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्|इन्द्
इंद् {c1c} P. [इंदति, इंदितुं] To be<BR>powerful (occurring in the<BR>etymology of इंद्र q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदंबरं|इन्दम्बर|इन्दम्बरं
इंदंबरं = इंदीवर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदिंदिरः|इन्दिन्दिर|इन्दिन्दिरः
इंदिंदिरः A large bee; लोभादिंदिंदिरेषु<BR>निपतत्सु Bv. 2. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदिरा|इन्दिरा
इंदिरा [इंद्-किरच्] N. of Lakṣmī,<BR>wife of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आलयं<BR>‘abode of Indirā,’ the blue lotus.<BR>--मंदिरः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--(रं) the blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदिवरं|इन्दिवर|इंदिवर|इन्दिवरं
इंदि(दी)वरं [इंदीर्लक्ष्मीस्तस्या वरं<BR>वरणीयं Tv.] The blue lotus; बाले तव<BR>मुखांभोजे कथमिंदीवरद्वयं Ś. Til. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदीवरं|इन्दीवर|इंदीवर|इन्दीवरं
इंदि(दी)वरं [इंदीर्लक्ष्मीस्तस्या वरं<BR>वरणीयं Tv.] The blue lotus; बाले तव<BR>मुखांभोजे कथमिंदीवरद्वयं Ś. Til. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदीवरिणी|इन्दीवरिणी
इंदीवरिणी A group of blue lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदीवारः|इन्दीवार|इन्दीवारं|इन्दीवारः
इंदीवारः A blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदुः|इन्दु|इन्दुः
इंदुः [उनत्ति क्लेदयति चंद्रिकया भुवनं<BR>उंद्-उ आदेरिच्च Uṇ. 1. 12]<BR>1 The moon;<BR>दिलीप इति राजेंदुरिंदुः क्षीरनिधाविव<BR>R. 1. 12 (इंदु is said to mean in the Veda a<BR>drop of Soma juice, a bright drop or<BR>spark; सुतास इंदवः Rv. 1. 16. 6).<BR>--2 The मृगशिरस् Nakṣatra.<BR>--3 (In<BR>Math.) The number ‘one’.<BR>--4<BR>Camphor. --(pl.)<BR>1 The periodical changes<BR>of the moon.<BR>--2 The time of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0277-a" target="_blank">Page0277-a+ 57</a>]<BR>moonlight, night.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कमलं the<BR>white lotus.<BR>--कला {1} a digit of<BR>the moon. (These are 16, each<BR>of which is mythologically said<BR>to be devoured by 16 deities<BR>in succession). {2} N. of several<BR>plants; अमृता, गुडूची, सोमलता.<BR>--कलिका {1} N. of a plant (केतकी). {2} a<BR>digit of the moon.<BR>--कांतः the<BR>moon-stone.<BR>--(ता) {1} night. {2}<BR>N. of a plant (केतकी).<BR>--क्षयः {1}<BR>waning or disappearance of the<BR>moon. {2} the new moon day.<BR>--जः, --पुत्रः the planet Mercury.<BR>--(जा) N. of the river Revā or<BR>Narmadā.<BR>--जनकः {1} the ocean<BR>(the moon being produced amongst<BR>other jewels at the churning of the<BR>ocean). {2} the sage अत्रि.<BR>--दलः<BR>a digit, crescent.<BR>--पुष्पिका N. of a<BR>plant (कलिकरी or जांगली).<BR>--भं {1}<BR>the sign called Cancer. {2} the<BR>Nakṣatra called मृगाशिरस्.<BR>--भा a<BR>kind of water-lily.<BR>--भृत्, --शेखरः,<BR>--मौलिः ‘the moon crested god,’<BR>epithets of Śiva.<BR>--मणिः {1} the<BR>moon-stone. {2} a pearl.<BR>--मंडलं<BR>the orb or disc of the moon.<BR>--रत्नं<BR>a pearl.<BR>--ले(रे)खा {1} a digit of<BR>the moon. {2} N. of several plants, see<BR>इंदुकला.<BR>--लोकः the world of the moon.<BR>--लोहकं, --लौहं silver.<BR>--वदना N.<BR>of a metre; see Appendix.<BR>--वारः<BR>a kind of yoga.<BR>--वासरः<BR>Monday.<BR>--व्रतं a religious<BR>observance depending on the age of the<BR>moon. It consists in diminishing<BR>the quantity of food by a certain<BR>portion daily, for a fortnight or a<BR>month; cf. चांद्रायण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0276-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदुमत्
इंदुमत् m. An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदुमती|इन्दुमती
इंदुमती<BR>1 A day of full moon.<BR>--2<BR>The wife of अज and sister of भोज.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंदूरः|इन्दूर|इन्दूरः
इंदूरः A rat, mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रः|इन्द्र|इन्द्रः
इंद्रः [इंद्-रन्; इंदतीति इंद्रः; इदि<BR>ऐश्वर्ये Malli.]<BR>1 The lord of gods.<BR>--2 The god of rain, rain; cloud.<BR>--3 A lord or ruler (as of<BR>men &c.); first or best (of any<BR>class of objects), always as the<BR>last member of comp.; नरेंद्रः a lord<BR>of men i. e. a king; so मृगेंद्रः a lion;<BR>गजेंद्रः the lord or chief of elephants;<BR>so योगींद्रः, कपींद्रः.<BR>--4 A prince, king.<BR>--5 The pupil of the right eye.<BR>--6<BR>N. of the plant कुटज.<BR>--7 Night.<BR>--8<BR>One of the divisions of भारतवर्ष.<BR>--9<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0277-b" target="_blank">Page0277-b+ 69</a>]<BR>N. of the 26th Yoga.<BR>--10 The<BR>human or animal soul.<BR>--11 A<BR>vegetable poison.<BR>--12 The Yoga star in<BR>the 26th Nakṣatra.<BR>--13 Greatness.<BR>--द्रा The wife of Indra, Indrāṇī.<BR>[Indra, the god of the firmament, is<BR>the Jupiter Pluvius of the Indian Āryans.<BR>In the Vedas he is placed in the first<BR>rank among the gods; yet he is not<BR>regarded as an uncreated being, being<BR>distinctly spoken of in various passages<BR>of the Vedas as being born, and as having<BR>a father and a mother. He is sometimes<BR>represented as having been produced by<BR>the gods as a destroyer of enemies, as<BR>the son of Ekāṣṭakā, and in<BR>Rv. 10. 90. 13 he is said to have sprung from the<BR>mouth of Puruṣa. He is of a ruddy or<BR>golden colour, and can assume any form<BR>at will. He rides in a bright golden<BR>chariot drawn by two tawny horses. His<BR>most famous weapon is the thunderbolt<BR>which he uses with deadly effect in his<BR>warfare with the demons of darkness,<BR>drought and inclement weather, variously<BR>called Ahi, Vṛtra, Śambara, Namuci<BR>&c. He storms and breaks through<BR>their castles, and sends down fertilizing<BR>showers of rain to the great delight of<BR>his worshippers. He is thus the lord of<BR>the atmosphere, the dispenser of rain,<BR>and governor of the weather. He is<BR>represented as being assisted by the Maruts<BR>or storm-gods in his warfare. Besides<BR>the thunderbolt he uses arrows, a large<BR>hook, and a net. The Soma juice is his<BR>most favourite food, and under its<BR>exhilarating influence he performs great<BR>achievements (cf. Rv. 10. 119), and pleases<BR>his devout worshippers, who are said to<BR>invite the god to drink the juice. He is<BR>their friend and even their brother; a<BR>father, and the most fatherly of fathers;<BR>the helper of the poor, and the deliverer<BR>and comforter of his servants. He is a<BR>wall of defence; his friend is never slain<BR>or defeated. He richly rewards his adorers,<BR>particularly those who bring him<BR>libations of Soma, and he is supplicated<BR>for all sorts of temporal blessings, as<BR>cows, horses, chariots, health,<BR>intelligence, prosperous days, long life, and<BR>victory in war. In the Vedas Indra's<BR>wife is Indrani, who is invoked among<BR>the goddesses.<BR>Such is the Vedic conception of<BR>Indra. But in later mythology he falls<BR>in the second rank. He is said to<BR>be one of the sons of Kaśyapa and<BR>Dākṣāyaṇī or Aditi. He is inferior<BR>to the triad Brahmā, Viṣṇu and Maheśa<BR>(though in some places Viṣṇu is<BR>regarded as his younger brother, cf. R. 14. 59,<BR>15. 40), but he is the chief of all the<BR>other gods, and is commonly styled<BR>Sureśa, Devendra &c. As in the Vedas<BR>so in later mythology, he is the regent of<BR>the atmosphere, and of the east quarter,<BR>and his world is called Svarga. He sends<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0277-c" target="_blank">Page0277-c+ 67</a>]<BR>the lightning, uses the thunderbolt and<BR>sends down rain. He is frequently at<BR>war with Asuras, whom he constantly<BR>dreads, and by whom he is sometimes<BR>defeated. The Indra of mythology is<BR>famous for his incontinence and adultery,<BR>one prominent instance of which is his<BR>seduction of Ahalyā, the wife of Gautama<BR>(see Ahalyā), and for which he is often<BR>spoken of as Ahalyā-jāra. The curse<BR>of the sage impressed upon him a<BR>1000 marks resembling the female<BR>organ, and he was therefore called<BR>Sayoni; but these marks were<BR>afterwards changed into eyes, and he is<BR>hence called Netra-yoni and Sahasrākṣa.<BR>In the Rāmāyaṇa Indra is<BR>represented as having been defeated and carried<BR>off to Laṅkā by Rāvaṇa's son called<BR>Meghanāda, who for this exploit<BR>received the title of ‘Indrajit.’ It was only<BR>at the intercession of Brahmā and the<BR>gods that Indra was released, and this<BR>humiliation was regarded as a<BR>punishment for his seduction of Ahalyā. He<BR>is also represented as being in constant<BR>dread of sages practising potent<BR>penances, and as sending down nymphs to<BR>beguile their minds (see. Apsaras). In<BR>the Purāṇas he is said to have destroyed<BR>the offspring of Diti in her womb, and<BR>to have cut off the wings of mountains<BR>when they grew troublesome. Other<BR>stories are also told in which Indra was<BR>once worsted by Raja, grandson of<BR>Purūravas, owing to the curse of<BR>Durvāsas, and other accounts show that he and<BR>Kṛṣṇa were at war with each other for<BR>the Pārijāta tree which the latter<BR>wanted to remove from Svarga, and<BR>which he succeeded in doing in spite<BR>of Indra's resistance. His wife is<BR>Indrani, the daughter of the demon<BR>Puloman, and his son is named Jayanta.<BR>He is also said to be father of Arjuna.<BR>His epithets are numerous; mostly<BR>descriptive of his achievements, e. g.<BR>वृत्रहन्, बलभिद्, पाकशासन, गोत्रभिद्, पुरंदर,<BR>शतक्रतु, जिष्णु, नमुचिसूदन &c. (see<BR>Ak. I. 1. 44-47). The Heaven of Indra<BR>is Svarga; its capital, Amarāvatī;<BR>his garden, Nandana; his elephant,<BR>Airāvata; his horse, Uccaiḥśravas; his bow,<BR>the rainbow, and his sword, Parañja].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः the fire produced<BR>from the contact of clouds; ˚धूमः<BR>frost, snow; ˚देवता the 16th<BR>lunarmansion.<BR>--अनुजः, --अवरजः an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu and of Nārāyaṇa.<BR>--अरिः an Asura or demon.<BR>--अवसानः a desert.<BR>--अशनः {1} hemp<BR>(dried and chewed). {2} the shrub<BR>which bears the seed used in<BR>jeweller's weight, (गुंजावृक्ष)<BR>--आयुधं<BR>Indra's weapon, the rainbow;<BR>इंद्रायुधद्योतिततोरणांकं R. 7. 4,<BR>12. 79; K. 127.<BR>--(धः) {1} N. of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0278-a" target="_blank">Page0278-a+ 59</a>]<BR>horse in Kādambarī (i. e.<BR>Kapinjala changed into a horse). {2}<BR>a horse marked with black about<BR>the eyes.<BR>--(धा) a kind of leech.<BR>--आसनं {1} the throne of<BR>Indra. {2} a throne in general.<BR>{3} a foot of five short syllables.<BR>--इज्यः N. of बृहस्पति the preceptor<BR>of gods.<BR>--ईश्वरः one of the forms<BR>of Śiva-linga.<BR>--उत्सवः a festival<BR>honouring Indra.<BR>--ऋषभ a. having<BR>Indra as a bull, or impregnated by<BR>Indra, an epithet of the earth.<BR>--कर्मन् m. an epithet of Viṣṇu<BR>(performing Indra's deeds).<BR>--कीलः {1}<BR>N. of the mountain मंदर. {2} a rock.<BR>--(लं) the banner of Indra.<BR>--कुंजरः<BR>Indra's elephant, Airāvata.<BR>--कूटः<BR>N. of a mountain.<BR>--कृष्ट a. ‘ploughed<BR>by Indra,’ growing exuberantly or<BR>in a wild state.<BR>--(ष्टः) a kind of<BR>corn produced by rain-water.<BR>--केतुः<BR>Indra's banner.<BR>--कोशः --षः, --षकः {1}<BR>a couch, sofa. {2} a plat-form. {3} a<BR>projection of the roof of a house.<BR>{4} a pin or bracket projecting<BR>from the wall (नागदंत).<BR>--गिरिः the<BR>महेंद्र mountain.<BR>--गुरुः, आचार्यः the<BR>teacher of Indra; i. e. बृहस्पति.<BR>--गोपः, --गोपकः [इंद्रो गोपो रक्षकोऽस्य,<BR>वर्षाभवत्वात्तस्य] a kind of insect of<BR>red or white colour; K. 100.<BR>--चंदनं the white sandal wood.<BR>--चापं,<BR>--धनुस् n. {1} a rainbow;<BR>विद्युत्वंतंललितवनिताः सेंद्रचापं सचित्राः Me. 64;<BR>Śi. 7. 4. {2} the bow of Indra.<BR>--छंदस् n. [इंद्र इव सहस्रनेत्रेण सहस्रगुच्छेन<BR>छाद्यते] a necklace consisting of<BR>1000 strings.<BR>--जननं Indra's birth.<BR>--जननीय a. treating of Indra's<BR>birth (as a work).<BR>--जा a. Ved.<BR>born or arising from Indra.<BR>--जालं<BR>[इंद्रस्य परमेश्वरस्य जालं मायेव] {1} the net<BR>of Indra. {2} a weapon used by<BR>Arjuna; a stratagem or trick in war.<BR>{3} deception, cheating. {4}<BR>conjuring, jugglery, magical tricks;<BR>स्वप्नेंद्रजालसदृशः खलु जीवलोकः<BR>Śānti. 2. 2; K. 105.<BR>--जालिक a. [इंद्रजाल-ठन्]<BR>deceptive, unreal, delusive.<BR>--(कः)<BR>a juggler, conjurer.<BR>--जित् m.<BR>‘conqueror of Indra’, N. of a son<BR>of Rāvaṇa who was killed by<BR>Lakṣmaṇa. [Indrajit is another name<BR>of Meghanāda, a son Rāvaṇa. When<BR>Rāvaṇa warred against Indra in his own<BR>heaven, his son Meghanāda was with<BR>him, and fought most valiantly. During<BR>the combat, Meghanāda, by virtue of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0278-b" target="_blank">Page0278-b+ 60</a>]<BR>the magical power of becoming invisible<BR>which he had obtained from Śiva, bound<BR>Indra, and bore him off in triumph to<BR>Laṅkā. Brahmā and the other gods<BR>hurried thither to obtain his release, and<BR>gave to Meghanāda the title of Indrajit,<BR>‘conqueror of Indra’; but the victor<BR>refused to release his prisoner unless<BR>he were promised immortality. Brahmā<BR>refused to grant this extravagant<BR>demand, but he strenuously persisted, and<BR>achieved his object. In the Rāmāyaṇa<BR>he is represented to have been<BR>decapitated by Lakṣmaṇa while he was<BR>engaged in a sacrifice]. ˚हंतृ or विजयिन्<BR>m. N. of Lakṣmaṇa.<BR>--ज्येष्ठ a. Ved.<BR>led by Indra.<BR>--तापनः the<BR>thundering of clouds.<BR>--तूलं, तूलकं a flock of<BR>cotton.<BR>--दमनः the son of Bāṇāsura.<BR>--दारुः the tree Pinus Devadāru.<BR>--द्रुः, द्रुमः {1} the plant Terminalia<BR>Arjuna (अर्जुन). {2} the plant कुटज.<BR>--द्वीपः --पं one of the 9 Dvīpas or<BR>divisions of the continent (of<BR>India).<BR>--ध्वजः a flag raised on the<BR>12th day of the bright half of<BR>Bhādra.<BR>--नक्षत्रं Indra's lunar mansion<BR>फल्गुनी.<BR>--नेत्रं {1} the eye of Indra.<BR>{2} the number one thousand.<BR>--नीलः [इंद्र इव नीलः श्यामः] a sapphire;<BR>R. 13. 54; 16. 69; Me. 46, 77.<BR>--नीलकः an emerald.<BR>--पत्नी Indra's<BR>wife, शची.<BR>--पर्णी, --पुष्पा N. of a<BR>medicinal plant.<BR>--पर्वतः {1} the महेंद्र<BR>mountain. {2} a blue<BR>mountain.<BR>--पुत्रा N. of अदिति.<BR>--पुरोगम, --पुरःसर, --श्रेष्ठ a. led or<BR>preceded by Indra, having Indra<BR>at the head.<BR>--पुरोहितः N. of<BR>बृहस्पति.<BR>--(ता) the asterism Puṣya.<BR>--प्रस्थं N. of a city on the Yamunā,<BR>the residence of the Pāṇḍavas<BR>(identified with the modern Delhi);<BR>इंद्रप्रस्थगमस्तावत्कारि मा संतु चेदयः<BR>Śi. 2. 63.<BR>--प्रहरणं Indra's weapon, the<BR>thunderbolt.<BR>--भेषजं dried ginger.<BR>--मखः a sacrifice in honour of Indra.<BR>--महः {1} a festival in honour of<BR>Indra. {2} the rainy season;<BR>˚कामुकः a dog.<BR>--मादन a. animating<BR>or delighting Indra.<BR>--मेदिन् a. Ved.<BR>whose friend or ally is Indra.<BR>--यवः,<BR>--वं seed of the Kuṭaja tree.<BR>--लुप्तः,<BR>--प्तं, --लुप्तकं {1} excessive baldness of<BR>the head. {2} loss of beard.<BR>--लोकः<BR>Indra's world, Svarga or Paradise.<BR>--लोकेशः {1} lord of the Indra's<BR>world, i. e. Indra. {2} a guest (who,<BR>if hospitably received, confers<BR>paradise on his host).<BR>--वंशा, --वज्रा N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0278-c" target="_blank">Page0278-c+ 57</a>]<BR>of two metres, see Appendix.<BR>--वल्लरी, --वल्ली N. of a plant (पारिजात)<BR>or of इंद्रवारुणी.<BR>--वस्तिः [इंद्रस्य आत्मनः<BR>वस्तिरिव] the calf (of the leg).<BR>--वाततम a. Ved. desired by Indra.<BR>--वायू (du) Indra and Vāyu.<BR>--वारुणी, --वारुणिका Colocynth, a wild<BR>bitter gourd (Mar. मोठी कंवडळ).<BR>--वाह् a. carrying Indra.<BR>--वृक्षः the<BR>Devadāru tree.<BR>--वृद्धा a kind of<BR>abscess.<BR>--वैडूर्यं a kind of precious<BR>stone.<BR>--व्रतं Indra's rule of conduct;<BR>one of the duties of a king (who<BR>is said to follow इंद्रव्रत when he<BR>distributes benefits as Indra pours<BR>down rain); वार्षिकांश्चतुरो मासान्<BR>यर्थेद्रोप्यभिवर्षति । तथाभिवर्षेत्स्वं राष्ट्रं कामैरिंद्रव्रतं<BR>चरन् ॥.<BR>--शक्तिः f. Indrāṇī, the wife<BR>of Indra, or his energy personified.<BR>--शत्रुः {1} an enemy or destroyer of<BR>Indra (when the accent is on the<BR>last syllable), an epithet of प्रह्लाद;<BR>R. 7. 35. {2} [इंद्रः शत्रुः यस्य] one<BR>whose enemy is Indra, an epithet<BR>of वृत्र (when the accent is on the<BR>first syllable). This refers to a<BR>legend in the Śat. Br., where it is<BR>said that Vṛtra's father intended<BR>his son to become the destroyer of<BR>Indra, and asked him to say<BR>इंद्रशत्रुर्वधस्व &c., but who, through mistake,<BR>accented the word on the first<BR>syllable, and was killed by Indra;<BR>cf. Śik. 52: --मंत्रो हीनः स्वरतो वर्णतो वा<BR>मिथ्याप्रयुक्तो न तमर्थमाह । स वाग्वज्रो यजमानं<BR>हिनास्ति यथेंद्रशत्रुः स्वरतोपराधात् ॥.<BR>--शलभः<BR>a kind of insect.<BR>--संधा connection<BR>or alliance with Indra.<BR>--सारथिः. {1} N<BR>of Mātalī. {2} an epithet of Vāyu,<BR>driving in the same carriage<BR>with Indra.<BR>--सुतः, --सूनुः {1} N.<BR>of (a) Jayanta; (b) Arjuna;<BR>(c) Vāli, the king of<BR>monkeys. {2} N. of the अर्जुन tree.<BR>--सुरसः, --सुरा a shrub the leaves of<BR>which are used in discutient<BR>applications (निर्गुंडी).<BR>--सेना Indra's<BR>missile or host.<BR>--सेनानीः the leader<BR>of Indra's armies, epithet of<BR>Kārtikeya.<BR>--स्तुत् m.,<BR>--स्तोमः {1} praise<BR>of Indra, N. of a particular hymn<BR>addressed to Indra in certain<BR>ceremonies. {2} a sacrifice in honour<BR>of Indra.<BR>--हवः invocation of Indra.<BR>--हस्तः a kind of medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0277-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रकं|इन्द्रक|इन्द्रकं
इंद्रकं [इंद्रस्य राज्ञः कं सुखं यत्र Tv.]<BR>An assembly room, a hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0278-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रतम
इंद्रतम a. Ved. Most Indra-like,<BR>mighty, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रता
इंद्रता, --त्वं Power and dignity of<BR>Indra, kingship, might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रत्वं|इन्द्रत्व
इंद्रता, --त्वं Power and dignity of<BR>Indra, kingship, might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रस्वत्
इंद्रस्वत् a. Ved. Accompanied by<BR>Indra, possessed of power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रयु|इन्द्रयु
इंद्रयु a. Longing to go to Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्राणिका|इन्द्राणिका
इंद्राणिका The plant निर्गुंडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्राणी|इन्द्राणी
इंद्राणी [इंद्रस्य पत्नी आनुक् ङीप्]<BR>1<BR>The wife of Indra.<BR>--2 N. of Durgā,<BR>considered as one of the eight<BR>mothers or divine energies.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of coitus.<BR>--4 Large cardamoms.<BR>--5 N. of a tree (नीलसिंदुवार); also<BR>the plant निर्गुंडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रिय|इन्द्रिय|इन्द्रियं|इन्द्रियः
इंद्रिय a. Fit for or belonging to<BR>or agreeable to, Indra.<BR>--यः A friend<BR>or companion of Indra.<BR>--यं<BR>[इंद्र-घ; इंद्रेण दुर्जयं; by P. V. 2. 93<BR>इंद्रियं =<BR>इंद्रलिंगमिंद्रदृष्टमिंद्रसृष्टमिंद्रजुष्टमिंद्रदत्तमिति वा]<BR>1 Power, force, the quality<BR>which belongs to Indra.<BR>--2 An<BR>organ of sense, sense or faculty of<BR>sense. (Indriyas are often<BR>compared to restive horses, which, if<BR>not properly checked, will lead one<BR>astray; cf. मा भूवन्नपथहरास्तवेंद्रियाश्वाः<BR>Ki. 5. 50.). There are two kinds<BR>of Indriyas: (a) ज्ञानेंद्रियाणि or<BR>बुद्धींद्रियाणिः --श्रोत्रं त्वक्चक्षुषी जिह्वा नासिका चैव<BR>पंचमी (also मनः according to<BR>some); and (b) कर्मैद्रियाणिः-पायूपस्थं<BR>हस्तपादं वाक् चव दशमी स्मृता<BR>Ms. 2. 90. In the Vedānta मनः, बुद्धि,<BR>अहंकार and चित्त are said to be the<BR>four internal organs, the total<BR>number of organs being,<BR>therefore, 14, each presided over by its<BR>own ruler or नियंतृ. In Nyāya each<BR>organ is connected with its own<BR>peculiar element; the eye, ear,<BR>tongue, nose, and skin being<BR>connected respectively with Light or<BR>fire, Ether, Water, Earth and Air.<BR>--3 Bodily or virile power, power<BR>of the sense.<BR>--4 Semen.<BR>--5<BR>Symbolical expression for the number ‘5.’<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अगोचर a. imperceptible.<BR>--अर्थः {1} an object of sense; these<BR>objects are: --रूपं शब्दो गंधरसस्पर्शाश्च<BR>विषया अमी Ak.; Bg. 3. 34; Bh. 3. 58;<BR>R. 14. 25. {2} anything exciting<BR>these senses.<BR>--असंगः<BR>non-attachment to sensual objects, stoicism.<BR>--आत्मन् m. {1} an epithet of Viṣṇu<BR>{2} an organ of sense.<BR>--आदिः the<BR>principle called ahankāra (in Sān.<BR>phil.).<BR>--आयतनं {1} the abode of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-b" target="_blank">Page0279-b+ 57</a>]<BR>the senses, i. e. the body. {2} the<BR>soul.<BR>--आराम a. given to enjoying<BR>the objects of sense.<BR>--ईशः the soul.<BR>--गोचर a. perceptible to the<BR>senses.<BR>--(रः) an object of sense.<BR>--ग्रामः, --वर्गः the assemblage or<BR>collection of organs, the five<BR>organs of sense taken collectively;<BR>बलवानिंद्रियग्रामो विद्वांसमपि कर्षति<BR>Ms. 2. 215, 100, 175; निर्ववार<BR>मधुनींद्रियवर्गः Śi. 10. 3.<BR>--ज a. in one's<BR>presence, visible.<BR>--ज्ञानं consciousness,<BR>the faculty of perception.<BR>--निग्रहः<BR>restraint of senses.<BR>--बुद्धिः f.<BR>perception by the senses, exercise of<BR>any organ of sense.<BR>--बोधन a.<BR>exciting power; stimulating or<BR>sharpening the senses.<BR>--(नं) any<BR>excitement of senses, a stimulus.<BR>--वधः insensibility.<BR>--विप्रतिपत्तिः f.<BR>perversion of the organs, wrong<BR>perception.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. function of the<BR>organs.<BR>--सुख sensual pleasures;<BR>R. 19. 47.<BR>--सन्निकर्षः the contact of an<BR>organ of sense (either with its object<BR>or with the mind).<BR>--स्वापः<BR>insensibility, unconsciousness, stupor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रियवत्
इंद्रियवत् a.<BR>1 One who has curbed<BR>his senses.<BR>--2 One having the<BR>organs of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंध्|इन्ध्
इंध् {c7c} A. (इंद्धे or इंधे, इंधांचक्रे, ऐंधिष्ट,<BR>इद्ध) To kindle, light, set on fire.<BR>--pass. (इध्यते) To be lighted, blaze,<BR>flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इद्ध|इद्धं|इद्धः
इद्ध p. p. [इंध्-क्त]<BR>1 Kindled,<BR>lighted; Mv. 1. 53; क्रोध˚<BR>Ratn. 1. 4; Mu. 1. 2; ˚राग Ś. 7. 16<BR>whose glow or red colour has just<BR>broken out.<BR>--2 Shining, glowing,<BR>blazing, bright; Ki. 2. 59; Śi. 1. 63;<BR>˚बोधैः Bk. 1. 5 (पटुबुद्धिभिः) sharp.<BR>--3<BR>Clean, clear.<BR>--4 Wonderful.<BR>--5<BR>Obeyed, unresisted (as order); ˚शासनः<BR>Ki. 1. 22<BR>--द्धं<BR>1 Sunshine, heat.<BR>--2<BR>Refulgence, splendour.<BR>--3 Wonder.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दीधितिः fire; Śi. 16. 35.<BR>--मन्यु a. having the anger excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्मः|इध्म|इध्मं
इध्मः [इध्यतेऽग्निरनेन इंध्-मक्] Fuel,<BR>especially that used for the sacred<BR>fire; ग्रीष्म इध्मः शरद्धविः Rv. 10. 90. 6;<BR>R. 14. 70.<BR>--ध्मं Wood, fuel.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जिह्वः fire.<BR>--प्रव्रश्चनः a hatchet,<BR>an axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इध्या
इध्या f. Kindling, lighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंध|इन्ध|इन्धः
इंध a. [इंध्-अच्] Kindling,<BR>lighting.<BR>--धः [इंध्-घञ्]<BR>1 Fuel.<BR>--2<BR>The Supreme being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंधन|इन्धन|इन्धनं
इंधन a. [इंध्-णिच्-ल्युट्] Kindling,<BR>lighting.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Kindling, lighting.<BR>--2 Fuel, wood &c.; शोकानलेंधनतां<BR>K. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंधनवत्
इंधनवत् a. Possessed of fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंधन्वन्
इंधन्वन् a. Ved. Possessed of fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्व्
इन्व् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To<BR>pervade, surround.<BR>--3 To seize, take<BR>possession of.<BR>--4 To invigorate,<BR>gladden; see इन् also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इन्वकाः
इन्वकाः Stars in the head of<BR>Orion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभः|इभ
इभः [इ-भन्-किच्च Uṇ. 3. 151]<BR>1<BR>An elephant.<BR>--2 Fearless power or<BR>servants, dependants (Ved.).<BR>--भी A female elephant. [cf. L. ebur].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः a lion.<BR>--आख्यः,<BR>--केशरा the plant नागकेशर.<BR>--आननः<BR>N. of Gaṇeśa; cf. गजानन.<BR>--उषणा,<BR>--कणा a kind of aromatic plant (<BR>गजपिप्पली).<BR>--गंधा N. of a plant (the<BR>fruit of which is poisonous).<BR>--निभीलिका {1} shrewdness, sagacity,<BR>sharpness. {2} hemp (भंगा).<BR>--पालकः<BR>the driver or keeper of an elephant.<BR>--पोटा [पोटा पुंलक्षणा इभी] a young<BR>female elephant.<BR>--पोतः a young<BR>elephant, a cub.<BR>--भरः a collection<BR>of elephants.<BR>--युवतिः f. a female<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभमाचलः|इभमाचल
इभमाचलः [इभमाचलयति] A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभया
इभया N. of the tree स्वर्णक्षीरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्य|इभ्यः
इभ्य a. [इभं गजमर्हति यत्]<BR>1 Wealthy, opulent, rich; Dk. 41.<BR>--2 Belonging to one's servants<BR>(Ved.).<BR>--भ्यः<BR>1 A king.<BR>--2 An<BR>elephant-driver.<BR>--3 An enemy or foe<BR>(Sāy.).<BR>--भ्या<BR>1 A female elephant.<BR>--2 N. of the Olibanum tree,<BR>Boswellia Serrata.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तिल्वि (व)<BR>ल a. wealthy, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इभ्यक
इभ्यक a. Wealthy, rich.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इमथा
इमथा ind. Ved. As here, as<BR>now.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयक्षु
इयक्षु a. Ved. Longing for,<BR>seeking to gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्|इयन्त्
इयत् a. So much, so large, of<BR>this extent; इयत्तवायुः Dk. 93; इयंति<BR>वर्षाणि तया सहोग्रं R. 13. 67 so many<BR>years; द्बयं नीतिरितीयती Śi. 2. 30 this<BR>much; इयतो दिवसानुत्सव आसीत् U. 1<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्ता
इयत्ता, इयत्त्वं<BR>1 (a) So much,<BR>fixed measure or quantity; ईदृक्तया<BR>रूपमियत्तया वा R. 13. 5; न… यशः<BR>परिच्छेत्तुमियत्तयालं 6. 77; K. 129, 182.<BR>(b) Limited number, limitation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">Page0280-a+ 55</a>]<BR>न गुणानामियत्तया R. 10. 32.<BR>--2 Limit,<BR>standard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्त्वं|इयत्त्व
इयत्ता, इयत्त्वं<BR>1 (a) So much,<BR>fixed measure or quantity; ईदृक्तया<BR>रूपमियत्तया वा R. 13. 5; न… यशः<BR>परिच्छेत्तुमियत्तयालं 6. 77; K. 129, 182.<BR>(b) Limited number, limitation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">Page0280-a+ 55</a>]<BR>न गुणानामियत्तया R. 10. 32.<BR>--2 Limit,<BR>standard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0279-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयत्तक
इयत्तक a. So small, very small.<BR>--का A bad limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयस्
इयस् a. Ved. Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इयसा
इयसा Ved. Low spirits,<BR>dejection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्
इर् {c6c} P. (इरति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरज्य
इरज्य Ved. (इरज्यति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>grow.<BR>--2 To be jealous.<BR>--3 To<BR>order, prepare; arrange, dispose of.<BR>--4 To be master of.<BR>--5 To lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरज्यु
इरज्यु a. Ved. Engaged in<BR>preparations for the sacrificial rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरणं|इरण
इरणं<BR>1 A desert.<BR>--2 Salt or<BR>barren ground; cf. इरिण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरंमद|इरम्मद|इरम्मदः
इरंमद a. [cf. P. III. 2. 37]<BR>Delighting in drinking, an epithet<BR>of Agni.<BR>--दः<BR>1 A flash of lightning,<BR>the fire attending the fall of a<BR>thunderbolt; इरंमदमिव मेघमालाऽसूत<BR>K. 70.<BR>--2 The submarine fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरस्यति
इरस्यति Ved.<BR>1 To behave<BR>insolently, be angry.<BR>--2 (With<BR>dat.) To be ill-affected towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरस्या
इरस्या<BR>1 Ill will, malevolence.<BR>--2 Wish for food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरा
इरा [इ-रन् Uṇ. 2. 28; इं कामं राति<BR>रा-क वा Tv.]<BR>1 The earth.<BR>--2 Speech.<BR>--3 The goddess of speech,<BR>Sarasvatī.<BR>--4 Water.<BR>--5 Food.<BR>--6<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>--7 Any drinkable<BR>fluid; a draught (especially of<BR>milk).<BR>--8 Refreshment, comfort<BR>(Ved. in the last three senses).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः {1} N. of<BR>Varuṇa, of Viṣṇu and of Gaṇeśa. {2}<BR>a king, sovereign.<BR>--क्षीर a. Ved.<BR>whose milk is a refreshment or<BR>enjoyment.<BR>--(रः) the milk ocean.<BR>--चर a. earth-born, terrestrial.<BR>{2} aquatic.<BR>--(रं) hail; so इरावरं.<BR>--जः<BR>N. of Kāma or Cupid.<BR>--वेल्लिका<BR>pimples on the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरावत्|इरावन्त्
इरावत् a.<BR>1 Granting drink or<BR>refreshment, satiating.<BR>--2 Endowed<BR>with provisions, comfortable. --m.<BR>--(वान्)<BR>1 Ocean.<BR>--2 A cloud.<BR>--3 A<BR>king.<BR>--4 N. of a son of Arjuna.<BR>--ती<BR>1 N. of a river in the Panjab<BR>(रावी).<BR>--2 N. of a plant.<BR>--3<BR>N. of Durgā, Rudra's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिका
इरिका N. of a plant or tree.<BR>˚वनं a grove of such trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिणं|इरिण|इरिणः
इरिणं [ऋ-इनच्-किदिच्च Uṇ. 2. 51]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">Page0280-b+ 55</a>]<BR>1 A salt ground, saline soil;<BR>यथेरिणे बीजमुप्त्वा न वप्ता लभते फलं<BR>Ms. 3. 142; Y. 1. 151.<BR>--2 Hence,<BR>a bare or barren soil, desert, dreary<BR>region.<BR>--3 Non-support.<BR>--4 A rivulet,<BR>well (Ved.).<BR>--5 A hollow, hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिण्य
इरिण्य a. Belonging or relating<BR>to a desert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिन्
इरिन् a. Ved.<BR>1 Instigating.<BR>--2<BR>Powerful, violent.<BR>--3 A proud or<BR>overbearing fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिमेदः|इरिमेद
इरिमेदः = अरिमेद q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इरिविल्ला
इरिविल्ला or इरिविल्लिका Pimples<BR>on the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्गलं|इर्गल
इर्गलं, --ला = अर्गल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्गला
इर्गलं, --ला = अर्गल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्य|इर्य्य
इर्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Instigating(प्रेरक).<BR>--2 Destroying the enemies.<BR>--3 A<BR>lord, master.<BR>--4 Active,<BR>powerful, an epithet of Pūṣan and of<BR>the Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वारु|इर्वारुः|इर्व्वारु|इर्व्वारुः
इर्वारु --लु a. Destructive,<BR>carnivorous (हिंसक).<BR>--रुः m. f. A<BR>cucumber.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--(लु) शुक्तिका a<BR>kind of melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वालु|इर्व्वालु|इर्व्वालुः
इर्वारु --लु a. Destructive,<BR>carnivorous (हिंसक).<BR>--रुः m. f. A<BR>cucumber.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--(लु) शुक्तिका a<BR>kind of melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इर्वारुकः|इर्वारुक
इर्वारुकः An animal living in<BR>caves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्
इल् {c6c} P. (इलति, इयेल, ऐलीत्, एलितुं,<BR>इलित) or {c10c} U. (इलयति or एलयति,<BR>ऐलयीत् or ऐलिलत्).<BR>1 To go, to move.<BR>--2<BR>To sleep.<BR>--3 To throw, send, cast.<BR>--4<BR>To keep still, not to move.<BR>--5 To<BR>become quiet. [cf. Germ. Eile, Gr.<BR>elao].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलय
इलय a. Motionless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलव|इलवः
इलव a. Ved. Loud, noisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलविला
इलविला N. of the wife of<BR>Viśravas and mother of Kubera;<BR>(hence the name ऐलविल for Kubera).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल
इल a. [इल्-क] Sleepy.<BR>--ला<BR>1<BR>The earth.<BR>--2 A cow.<BR>--3 Speech;<BR>&c, see इडा.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गोलः, --लं the<BR>earth, the globe.<BR>--तलं {1} the fourth<BR>place in the circle of the zodiac. {2}<BR>the surface of the earth.<BR>--धरः a<BR>mountain; Śi. 20. 54.<BR>--वृतं one of<BR>the nine Varṣas or divisions of<BR>the known world; पश्चान्माल्यवतः प्राच्यां<BR>गंधमादनशैलतः । इलावृतं नीलगिरेर्याम्यतो<BR>निषधादुदक् ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलिका
इलिका The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इली
इली [इल्-क ङीष्] A cudgel,<BR>a stick shaped like a sword, a short<BR>sword (करवाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलीबिशः|इलीबिश
इलीबिशः^1 N. of a demon<BR>conquered by Indra.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: Wrong spelling of a name of a demon from RV..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इलीशः|इलीश
इलीशः^1, इल्लिशः A sort of fish,<BR>commonly hilsa or sable.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: sergeA thought it should be left unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्लिशः|इल्लिश
इलीशः^1, इल्लिशः A sort of fish,<BR>commonly hilsa or sable.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: sergeA thought it should be left unchanged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वकाः
इल्वकाः, --लाः (pl.) N. of the<BR>five stars in the head of Orion (<BR>मृगशिरस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इल्वलाः
इल्वकाः, --लाः (pl.) N. of the<BR>five stars in the head of Orion (<BR>मृगशिरस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इव
इव ind.<BR>1 Like, as (showing<BR>उपमा or comparison); वागर्थाविव<BR>संपृक्तौ R. 1. 1; वैनतेय इव विनतानंदनः<BR>K. 5.<BR>--2 As if, as it were<BR>(denoting उत्प्रेक्षा); पश्यामीव पिताकिनं<BR>Ś. 1. 6; लिंपतीव तमोंगानि वर्षतीवांजनं<BR>नभः Mk. 1. 34.<BR>--3 A little,<BR>somewhat, perhaps; कडार इवायं G. M.<BR>--4 (Added to interrogative words),<BR>‘Possibly’, ‘I should like to<BR>know’, ‘indeed’; विना सीतादेव्या<BR>किमिव हि न दुःखं रघुपतेः U. 6. 30; क<BR>इव of what sort, what-like; क इव<BR>कालः Māl. 2 what a long time has<BR>elapsed.<BR>--5 इव is frequently used<BR>with adverbs, especially with such<BR>as involve restriction, by way of<BR>emphasis in the sense of even or<BR>just so, just, exactly, quite,<BR>indeed, very; मुहूर्तमिव but for a<BR>moment; किंचिदिव just a little bit;<BR>so ईषदिव, नाचिरादिव &c.; (इव is<BR>considered by grammarians as forming<BR>compounds with the word after<BR>which it stands; इवेन नित्यसमासो<BR>विभक्त्यलोपश्च).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
इष् {vI.v} {c6c} P. (इच्छति, इयेष, ऐषीत्,<BR>एषितुं-एष्टुं, इष्ट)<BR>1 To wish, desire, long<BR>for; इच्छामि संवर्धितमाज्ञया ते<BR>Ku. 3. 3; oft. with pot. or imperat.<BR>mood; इच्छामि भुंजीत or भुंक्तां भवान्;<BR>भुंजीयेतीच्छति Sk.<BR>--2 To choose; मूत्रेण<BR>मौंड्यमिच्छेत् तु क्षत्रियं दंडमेव वा<BR>Ms. 8. 384.<BR>--3 To endeavour to obtain,<BR>strive or seek for; भूतिमिच्छता, स्वर्गं<BR>&c.<BR>--4 To be willing, be about<BR>to do anything, mean or intend<BR>(with. inf.).<BR>--5 To ask or expect<BR>anything (acc.) from any one (loc.<BR>or abl.); देवेषु यज्ञे भागमीषिरे Śat.<BR>Br.<BR>--6 To acknowledge, regard.<BR>--7<BR>To request, ask.<BR>--8 To be<BR>favourable.<BR>--9 To try to make favourable.<BR>--10 To assent or consent. --pass.<BR>1 To be wished or liked.<BR>--2 To be<BR>asked, or requested.<BR>--3 To be<BR>prescribed or laid down; हस्तच्छेदनमिष्यते<BR>Ms. 8. 322; त्रिरात्रं दशरात्रं वा<BR>शावमाशौचमिष्यते Y. 3. 18.<BR>--4 To be<BR>approved, accepted, or regarded as;<BR>जंभो दंतेपि चेष्यते Trik. {vII.v} {c4c} P. (इष्यति,<BR>इयेष, एषिष्यति, एषितुं)<BR>1 To move;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">Page0281-a+ 58</a>]<BR>to cause to move.<BR>--2 To let fly,<BR>cast, throw.<BR>--3 To raise (as one's<BR>voice).<BR>--4 To sprinkle. {vIII.v} {c9c} P.<BR>(इष्णाति)<BR>1 To cause to move<BR>quickly, let fly, cast.<BR>--2 To fly off, escape.<BR>--3 To strike, smite.<BR>--4 To impel,<BR>urge, incite, animate, promote. {vIV.v}<BR>{c1c} U. (एषति-ते, ऐषीत्-ऐषिष्ट) To go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0280-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छक|इच्छकः
इच्छक a. Wishing, desiring &c.<BR>--कः<BR>1 (In Arith.) The sum sought.<BR>--2 N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छत्
इच्छत् pres. p. Wishing, desirous,<BR>willing; अनिच्छतोपि तस्य against his<BR>will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छा
इच्छा [इष् भावे श]<BR>1 Wish, desire,<BR>inclination of mind, will; इच्छया<BR>according to one's desire, at will.<BR>--2<BR>Willingness.<BR>--3 (In Math.) A<BR>question or problem.<BR>--4 (In gram.)<BR>The form of the Desiderative.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दानं fulfilment of a wish.<BR>--निवृत्तिः f. suppression of desire,<BR>indifference to worldly desires.<BR>--फलं the solution of a question or<BR>problem.<BR>--रतं desired sports,<BR>favourite pastimes; Me. 89.<BR>--वसु a.<BR>‘possessing wealth according to<BR>wish’, epithet of Kubera.<BR>--संपद् f.<BR>fulfilment of one's wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छु|इच्छुः
इच्छु a. Wishing, desirous;<BR>usually in comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इच्छुक|इच्छुकः
इच्छुक a. Wishing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्
इष् a.<BR>1 Speedy, going quickly.<BR>--2 Wishing, desirous. --f. Ved.<BR>1 A<BR>draught, refreshment, food.<BR>--2<BR>Libation.<BR>--3 Strength, power, sap,<BR>freshness.<BR>--4 Comfort; increase.<BR>--5<BR>Affluence.<BR>--6 Refreshing waters of<BR>the sky.<BR>--7 Wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषः|इष
इषः<BR>1 One possessed of sap or<BR>strength.<BR>--2 The month आश्विन;<BR>ध्वनिमिषेऽनिमिषेक्षणमग्रतः Śi. 6. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषणयते
इषणयते Den. A. To move,<BR>excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषणिः|इषणि
इषणिः f.<BR>1 Sending, despatching.<BR>--2 Wish, desire, impulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषण्यति
इषण्यति Den. P. To excite, drive,<BR>urge on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषण्या
इषण्या Impulse, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषयति
इषयति Den. P.<BR>1 To be juicy.<BR>--2 To swell, increase.<BR>--3 To be<BR>fresh or active.<BR>--4 To animate,<BR>strengthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषव्य
इषव्य a.<BR>1 (The object) of aim.<BR>--2<BR>Skilled in archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषि
इषि a. [इष्-कि] Wishing, desiring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषित
इषित p. p. (fr. इष् {4} cl.).<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-b" target="_blank">Page0281-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Moved, driven, sent, despatched.<BR>--2 Excited, animated.<BR>--3 Quick,<BR>speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिर|इषिरः
इषिर a. Ved. [इष्-गतौ-किरच्]<BR>1<BR>Juicy, succulent, refreshing, fresh.<BR>--2 Powerful, strong, quick, active.<BR>--3 Moving.<BR>--रः Fire.<BR>--रं ind.<BR>Quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्ट|इष्टं|इष्टः
इष्ट p. p. [इष् इच्छायां कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Wished, desired, longed for,<BR>wished for; उपपन्नो गुणैरिष्टैः Nala. 1. 1.<BR>--2 Beloved, agreeable, liked,<BR>favourite, dear; ˚आत्मजः Mu. 2. 8 fond of<BR>sons.<BR>--3 Worshipped, reverenced,<BR>--4<BR>Respected.<BR>--5 Approved, regarded<BR>as good.<BR>--6 Desirable; see इष्टापूर्त.<BR>--7 Valid.<BR>--8 Sacrificed,<BR>worshipped with sacrifices.<BR>--9 Supposed<BR>(कल्पित); oft. used in Līlāvatī.<BR>--ष्टः<BR>1 A lover, husband, beloved<BR>person; इष्टप्रवासजनितानि Ś. 4. 2.<BR>--2 A friend; Pt. 1. 57; 2. 167.<BR>--3<BR>N. of a tree (एरंड).<BR>--4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--5 A sacrifice.<BR>--ष्टा N. of a tree (शमी).<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>--2 A holy<BR>ceremony or संस्कार.<BR>--3 A sacrifice; see<BR>इष्टापूर्त. --ind. Voluntarily.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः desired object. ˚उद्युक्त a.<BR>zealously engaged in gaining one's<BR>desired object.<BR>--आपत्तिः f. occurrence<BR>of what is desired; a statement by<BR>a debater which is favourable to his<BR>opponent also; इष्टापत्तौ दोषांतरमाह<BR>Jag.<BR>--कर्मन् n. (In arith.) rule of<BR>supposition, operation with an<BR>assumed number.<BR>--कापथः the root<BR>of a fragrant grass (वीरणमूल).<BR>--कामदुह् a. granting the desired<BR>objects, an epithet of the cow of<BR>plenty.<BR>--गंध a. fragrant.<BR>--(धः) any<BR>fragrant substance.<BR>--(धं) sand.<BR>--जनः<BR>a beloved person (whether man<BR>or woman); U. 3.<BR>--देवः, --देवता a<BR>favourite god, one's tutelary deity.<BR>--यामन् a. going according to one's<BR>desire.<BR>--व्रत a. {1} performing<BR>desired vows. {2} obeying one's<BR>wish. {3} (food &c.) for the<BR>fulfilment of a vow. {4} that by which<BR>good works succeed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टापूर्तं|इष्टापूर्त|इष्टापूर्त्त|इष्टापूर्त्तं
इष्टापूर्तं [इष्टं च पूर्तं च तयोः समाहारः<BR>पूर्वपददीर्घत्वं] Performance of pious<BR>or charitable deeds; performing<BR>sacrifices, and digging wells and<BR>doing other acts of charity;<BR>इष्टापूर्तविधेः सपत्नशमनात् Mv. 3. 1;<BR>वापीकूपतडागादिदेवतायतनानि च ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">Page0281-c+ 57</a>]<BR>अन्नप्रदानमारामाः पूर्तमर्थ्याः प्रचक्षते ॥<BR>एकाग्निकर्महवनं त्रेतायां यच्च हूयते । अंतर्वेद्यां च<BR>यद्दानमिष्टं तदभिधीयते ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिः|इष्टि
इष्टिः f. [इष्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Wish,<BR>request, desire.<BR>--2 Seeking,<BR>striving to get.<BR>--3 Any desired object.<BR>--4 A desired rule or desideratum;<BR>(a term used with reference to<BR>Patañjali's additions to Kātyāyana's<BR>Vārtikas; इष्टयो भाष्यकारस्य, इति<BR>भाष्यकारेष्ट्या &c., cf. उपसंख्यान).<BR>--5<BR>Impulse, hurry.<BR>--6 Invitation, order.<BR>--7 (यज्-क्तिन्) A sacrifice.<BR>--8 An<BR>oblation consisting of butter, food<BR>&c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अयनं a sacrifice<BR>lasting for a long time.<BR>--पचः {1} a<BR>miser. {2} a demon; an Asura;<BR>so ˚मुष्.<BR>--पशु an animal to be<BR>killed at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टुः|इष्टु
इष्टुः f. A wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्म|इष्मः
इष्म a. [इष्-इच्छायां कर्मणि मक्]<BR>Wishing.<BR>--ष्मः<BR>1 Cupid, god of<BR>love.<BR>--2 The spring.<BR>--3 Course,<BR>going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्मिन्
इष्मिन् a. Speedy, impetuous, an<BR>epithet of the winds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्यः|इष्य|इष्यं
इष्यः, --ष्यं [इष्-क्यप्] The spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्यं|इष्य|इष्यः
इष्यः, --ष्यं [इष्-क्यप्] The spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषिका
इषि(षी)का [इष् गत्यादौ क्वुन् अत<BR>इत्वं]<BR>1 Reed, rush, stalk of grass;<BR>कुशकाशशरेषिकाः Rām.; ˚अस्त्रं<BR>R. 12. 23.<BR>--2 An arrow.<BR>--3 A sort of<BR>sugar-cane; Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>--4 A small stick of wood or iron<BR>used to see whether gold in a<BR>crucible is melted or not.<BR>--5 A<BR>brush.<BR>--6 The eye ball of an<BR>elephant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तूलं the point or<BR>upper part of a reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषीका
इषि(षी)का [इष् गत्यादौ क्वुन् अत<BR>इत्वं]<BR>1 Reed, rush, stalk of grass;<BR>कुशकाशशरेषिकाः Rām.; ˚अस्त्रं<BR>R. 12. 23.<BR>--2 An arrow.<BR>--3 A sort of<BR>sugar-cane; Saccharum Spontaneum.<BR>--4 A small stick of wood or iron<BR>used to see whether gold in a<BR>crucible is melted or not.<BR>--5 A<BR>brush.<BR>--6 The eye ball of an<BR>elephant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तूलं the point or<BR>upper part of a reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुः|इषु
इषुः [इष्-उ; cf. also Uṇ. 1. 13]<BR>1<BR>An arrow.<BR>--2 The number five.<BR>--3 (In Math.) A versed sine.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of a Soma ceremony.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रं,<BR>--अनीकं the point of an arrow.<BR>--असनं, --अस्त्रं the bow;<BR>राममिष्वसनदर्शनोत्सुकं R. 11. 37; ˚यंत्रमुक्तो बाणः<BR>Dk. 9.<BR>--आस a. throwing arrows.<BR>--(सः)<BR>{1} a bow. {2} an archer, a warrior;<BR>Bg. 1. 4, 17.<BR>--कारः, --कृत् m. an<BR>arrow-maker.<BR>--धरः, --भृत् m. an<BR>archer.<BR>--पथः, --विक्षेपः an arrow-shot,<BR>the range of an arrow.<BR>--प्रयोगः<BR>discharging an arrow; R. 2. 42.<BR>--मात्र a. having the length of an<BR>arrow (about {5} short spans or<BR>three feet.).<BR>--(त्रं) {1} the length of<BR>an arrow. {2} an altar (कुंड).<BR>--हस्त<BR>a. carrying arrows in the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0281-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुस्त्रिकांडा
इषुस्त्रिकांडा ‘The three-fold arrow’,<BR>N. of a constellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुक
इषुक a. Arrow-like.<BR>--का Ved.<BR>An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुधिः|इषुधि
इषुधिः [इषवो धीयंतेऽत्र धा-कि] A<BR>quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुध्यति
इषुध्यति Den. P.<BR>1 To contain<BR>arrows.<BR>--2 To implore, request, ask.<BR>--3<BR>To desire oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुध्या
इषुध्या Imploring, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषुध्यु
इषुध्यु a.<BR>1 Going.<BR>--2 Requesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इषूयति
इषूयति Den. P.<BR>1 To long for food.<BR>--2 To request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्वः|इष्व
इष्वः A spiritual teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कृ
इष्कृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To arrange, set in<BR>order.<BR>--2 To prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कर्तृ|इष्कर्त्तृ
इष्कर्तृ a. Arranging &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कृत
इष्कृत a. Arranged &c. ˚आहव a.<BR>whose Soma vessel is prepared or<BR>ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्कृतिः|इष्कृति
इष्कृतिः f. A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टका
इष्टका [इष्-तकन् टाप् Uṇ. 3. 148]<BR>1 A brick; Mk. 3.<BR>--2 A brick used<BR>in preparing the sacrificial altar &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गृहं a brick house.<BR>--चयनं<BR>collecting fire by means of a brick.<BR>--चित a. made of bricks; Dk. 84;<BR>also इष्टकचित.<BR>--न्यासः laying the<BR>foundation of a house.<BR>--पथः a<BR>road made of bricks.<BR>--राशिः a pile<BR>of bricks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इष्टिका
इष्टिका A brick &c.; see इष्टका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इस्
इस् ind. An interjection of anger,<BR>pain, or sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इह
इह ind. [इदं-ह इशादेशः<BR>P. V. 3. 11 Sk.]<BR>1 Here (referring<BR>to time, place or direction); in this<BR>place or case.<BR>--2 In this world<BR>(opp. परत्र or अमुत्र); oft. with जगति;<BR>K. 35.<BR>--3 In this case; in this book<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-c" target="_blank">Page0282-c+ 21</a>]<BR>or system.<BR>--4 Now, at this time.<BR>[cf. Zend idha].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अमुत्र<BR>ind. in this world and the next<BR>world, here and there.<BR>--आगत a.<BR>come here.<BR>--इह ind. here and there,<BR>now and then, repeatedly. ˚मातृ<BR>a. {1} whose mother is here and<BR>there; that is, everywhere. {2}<BR>of whose mothers one is here<BR>and one there.<BR>--कालः this life.<BR>--क्रतु, --चित्त a. whose intentions<BR>or thoughts are centred in this world<BR>or place.<BR>--भव or<BR>--तन a.<BR>belonging to this world.<BR>--लोकः this world<BR>or life; ˚के in this world.<BR>--समये ind.<BR>here, now, at such a time as this.<BR>--स्थ a. standing here.<BR>--स्थान a.<BR>one whose residence is on the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहत्य
इहत्य a. [इह-त्यप्] Being here, of<BR>this place or world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इहलः|इहल
इहलः N. of a country(चेदि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईः
ईः (m.) N. of Kāmadeva, Cupid.<BR>--f. N. of Lakṣmī. --ind. An<BR>interjection of (1) dejection; (2) pain;<BR>(3) sorrow; (4) anger; (5)<BR>compassion; (6) perception or consciousness;<BR>(7) calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ई
ई {vI.v} {c4c} A. (ईयते) To go. {vII.v} {c2c} P.<BR>1<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To shine.<BR>--3 To pervade.<BR>--4<BR>To desire, wish.<BR>--5 To throw.<BR>--6 To<BR>eat.<BR>--7 To beg (A.).<BR>--8 To become<BR>pregnant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्ष्
ईक्ष् {c1c} A. (ईक्षते, ईक्षांचक्रे, ऐक्षिष्ट,<BR>ईक्षितुं, ईक्षित्वा, ईक्षित)<BR>1 To see,<BR>behold, view, perceive, observe,<BR>look or gaze at.<BR>--2 To regard,<BR>consider, look upon;<BR>सर्वभूतस्थमात्मानं… ईक्षते योगयुक्तात्मा Bg. 6. 29.<BR>--3 To take into account, care for;<BR>नाभिजनमीक्षते K. 104, न<BR>कामवृत्तिर्वचनीयमीक्षते Ku. 5. 82.<BR>--4 To think,<BR>reflect; तत्तेज ऐक्षत बहु स्यां प्रजायेय<BR>Ch. Up.<BR>--5 To require; Pt. 1. 151.<BR>--6 To look to, or to investigate,<BR>the good or bad luck of any one<BR>(with dat. of the person); कृष्णाय<BR>ईक्षते गर्गः Sk. (शुभाशुभं पर्यालोचयति);<BR>Bk. 8. 76 --With अधि to suspect;<BR>सत्येप्यपायमधीक्षते H. 4. 102 v. l.<BR>--अन्वव<BR>{1} to see, behold. {2} to consider.<BR>{3} to care for, take into account.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षकः|ईक्षक
ईक्षकः [ईक्ष्-ण्वुल्] A spectator,<BR>beholder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणं|ईक्षण
ईक्षणं [ईक्ष्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Seeing,<BR>beholding &c.<BR>--2 A look, sight,<BR>aspect, view.<BR>--3 An eye;<BR>इत्यद्रिशोभाप्रहितेक्षणेन R. 2. 27; so अलसेक्षणा.<BR>--4<BR>Regarding, looking after, caring<BR>for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षणिकः|ईक्षणिक
ईक्षणिकः [ईक्षण-ठन्] A<BR>fortun-eteller; Ms. 9. 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षतिः|ईक्षति
ईक्षतिः [ईक्ष्-शतिप्] Looking, sight;<BR>ईक्षतेर्नाशब्दं Br. Sūt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षा
ईक्षा [ईक्स्-अ टाप्]<BR>1 Sight.<BR>--2<BR>Viewing, considering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षिका
ईक्षिका<BR>1 An eye.<BR>--2 A glance,<BR>look; Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षित
ईक्षित p. p. Seen, beheld,<BR>regarded &c.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A look, sight.<BR>--2 An<BR>eye; अभिमुखे मयि संहृतमीक्षितं Ś. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षितृ
ईक्षितृ a. [ईक्ष्-तृच्] Seeing,<BR>beholding, a beholder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईक्षेण्य
ईक्षेण्य a. Ved. Deserving to be<BR>seen; curious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईख्
ईख्, ईंख् {c1c} P. (ईंखति, ईंखांचक्रे,<BR>ईंखितुं, ईंखित) To go, move, vacillate.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To move backwards and<BR>forwards, swing, oscillate.<BR>--2 To<BR>shake, cause to tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईंख्|ईङ्ख्
ईख्, ईंख् {c1c} P. (ईंखति, ईंखांचक्रे,<BR>ईंखितुं, ईंखित) To go, move, vacillate.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To move backwards and<BR>forwards, swing, oscillate.<BR>--2 To<BR>shake, cause to tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईज्
ईज् --ईंज् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To<BR>censure, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईंज्
ईज् --ईंज् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To<BR>censure, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईजान
ईजान^1 a. [यज्-ताच्छील्ये कानच्]<BR>Performing sacrifices.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: affix कानच् should give आन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्
ईड् {c2c} A. (ईट्टे, ईडांचक्रे, ऐडिष्ट, ईडितुं,<BR>ईडित)<BR>1 To praise; अग्निमीडे पुरोहितं<BR>Rv. 1. 1. 1; शालीनतामव्रजदीड्यमानः<BR>R. 18. 17; नेडिषे यदि काकुत्स्थं<BR>Bk. 9. 57, 18. 15.<BR>--2 To implore,<BR>request, ask for (with two acc.);<BR>उपस्थाय मातरमन्नमैट्ट Rv. 3. 48. 3.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To ask.<BR>--2 To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्
ईड् f. Refreshment, libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडनं|ईडन
ईडनं [ईड्-ल्युट्] Praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडा
ईडा [ईड्-अ टाप्] Praise,<BR>commendation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईडेन्य
ईडे(ले)न्य Ved. = ईड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलेन्य
ईडे(ले)न्य Ved. = ईड्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईड्य
ईड्य pot. p. To be praised or<BR>glorified, praiseworthy, laudable;<BR>भवंतमीड्यं भवतः पितेव R. 5. 34;<BR>Bg. 11. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईण्मत्|ईण्मन्त्
ईण्मत् a. [ईट्-अस्त्यस्य मतुप्]<BR>Having a lord or master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईति|ईतिः
ईति a. [ई-क्तिच्]<BR>1 Produced,<BR>effected.<BR>--तिः f. Plague, distress,<BR>a calamity of the season. The ītis<BR>are usually said to be six:-- {1}<BR>excessive rain; {2} drought; {3} locusts; {4}<BR>rats; {5} parrots; and {6} foreign<BR>invasions; अतिवृष्टिरनावृष्टिः शलभामूषकाः शुकाः ।<BR>प्रत्यासन्नाश्च राजानः षडेता ईतयः स्मृताः ॥<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">Page0283-a+ 57</a>]<BR>(some read for the second line स्वचक्रं<BR>परचक्रं च सप्तैता ईतयः स्मृताः ॥ making the<BR>total number seven); M. 5. 20;<BR>Mv. 7. 42; निरातंका निरीतयः R. 1. 63.<BR>--2<BR>An infectious disease.<BR>--3<BR>Travelling (in a foreign country),<BR>sojourning (प्रवास).<BR>--4 An affray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0282-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ष|ईदृक्षः
ईदृक्ष --श a. (क्षी --शी f.), also ईदृश्<BR>Such, of this kind, of this aspect,<BR>endowed with such qualities.<BR>--क् n.<BR>Such a condition; such occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृश|ईदृशः
ईदृक्ष --श a. (क्षी --शी f.), also ईदृश्<BR>Such, of this kind, of this aspect,<BR>endowed with such qualities.<BR>--क् n.<BR>Such a condition; such occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईदृक्ता
ईदृक्ता Quality (opp. इयत्ता);<BR>विष्णोरिवास्यानवधारणीयं ईदृक्तया<BR>रूपमियत्तया वा R. 13. 5; मामीदृक्तया जानाति<BR>knows me to be so.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईंत्|ईन्त्
ईंत् {c1c} P. To bind; cf. अत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सा
ईप्सा [आप्तुमिच्छा आप्-सन्-अ]<BR>1<BR>Desire to obtain.<BR>--2 A wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सित
ईप्सित a. Desired, wished for,<BR>dear to; अपीप्सितं क्षत्रकुलांगनानां<BR>R. 14. 4; Ś. 3. 14.<BR>--तं Desire, wish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईप्सु
ईप्सु a. Striving to obtain,<BR>wishing or desiring to get (with acc.<BR>or inf., but usually in comp.);<BR>सौरभ्यमीप्सुरिव ते मुखमारुतस्य R. 5. 69;<BR>काम˚, घन˚ &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--यज्ञः a<BR>particular Soma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईम्
ईम् ind. [ई-बा˚ मुच्] Ved.<BR>1 A<BR>particle of affirmation or<BR>restriction; usually after short words at<BR>the beginning of a sentence, after<BR>यत्, relative pronouns, prepositions<BR>and particles like उत, अथ &c.<BR>--2<BR>Now.<BR>--3 This, here (एनं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईय
ईय [ई-बा˚ क्यप्] Pervading;<BR>˚चक्षस् of pervading sight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्
ईर् {c2c} A. (इर्ते, ईरांचक्रे, ऐरिष्ट, ईरितुं,<BR>ईर्ण); also {c1c} P. (p. p. ईरित)<BR>1 To go,<BR>move, shake (trans. also).<BR>--2 To<BR>rise, arise or spring from.<BR>--3 To go<BR>away, retire.<BR>--4 To agitate, elevate;<BR>raise one's voice. --{c10c} U. or Caus.<BR>(ईरयति, ईरित)<BR>1 To agitate, throw,<BR>cast; Śi. 8. 39; discharge, dart,<BR>hurl; ऐरिरच्च महाद्रुमं Bk. 15. 52;<BR>R. 15. 20.<BR>--2 To excite, prompt,<BR>urge; Bk. 12. 6.<BR>--3 To cause to<BR>rise, produce.<BR>--4 To utter,<BR>pronounce, proclaim, say, repeat;<BR>Māl. 1. 25; इतीरयंतीव तया निरैक्षि<BR>N. 14. 21; Śi. 9. 69; Ki. 1. 26;<BR>R. 9. 8; निबोध चेमां गिरमीरितां मया<BR>Sāv. 5. 23.<BR>--5 To cause to go, set<BR>in motion, move, shake;<BR>वातेरितपल्लवांगुलिभिः Ś. 1; अपरागसमीरणेरितः<BR>Ki. 2. 50; Śi. 8. 20.<BR>--6 To draw<BR>towards, attract; Śi. 10. 32.<BR>--7<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">Page0283-b+ 55</a>]<BR>To employ, use.<BR>--8 To bring to<BR>life, revive.<BR>--9 To elevate.<BR>--10 To<BR>raise oneself (A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरण|ईरणः
ईरण a. [ईर्-ल्युट्] Agitating,<BR>driving.<BR>--णः The wind.<BR>--णं<BR>1<BR>Agitating, moving, driving.<BR>--2 Going.<BR>--3 = इरण q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरित|ईरितं
ईरित p. p.<BR>1 Sent, despatched.<BR>--2<BR>Said, uttered &c.; ˚आकूतं declared<BR>purpose or intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिन्
ईरिन् a. [ईर्-णिनि]<BR>1 Moving,<BR>agitating.<BR>--2 Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्य
ईर्य a. To be excited.<BR>--र्या<BR>Wandering about as a religious<BR>mendicant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पथः {1} the<BR>observances of a religious mendicant to<BR>obtain knowledge. {2} the four<BR>positions of the body, i. e. going,<BR>standing upright, sitting, and lying<BR>down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईरिण|ईरिणं
ईरिण a. [ईर्-इनन्] Desert,<BR>barren.<BR>--णं A desert, barren soil;<BR>मुहूर्तमिव निःशब्दमासीदीरिणसंनिभं Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्क्ष्य्
ईर्क्ष्य् See ईर्ष्य्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्म|ईर्मः|ईर्म्म
ईर्म a. [ईर्-मक्]<BR>1 Agitated.<BR>--2<BR>Going constantly or instigating<BR>everything (Sāy.) --ind. Here, in<BR>or to this place.<BR>--र्मः The arm; the<BR>fore-quarter of an animal.<BR>--र्मं A<BR>wound, sore (m. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्मांत|ईर्मान्त
ईर्मांत a. Ved. Full-haunched, or<BR>thin-haunched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्वारुः|ईर्वारु|ईर्व्वारु|ईर्व्वारुः
ईर्वारुः m. f. A cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्षा = ईर्ष्या q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य्
ईर्ष्य्, ईर्क्ष्य् {c1c} P. (ईर्ष्यति,<BR>ईर्ष्यांचकार, ईर्ष्यितुं, ईष्यिंत) To envy, be jealous<BR>of, be impatient of the success of<BR>(with dat. of person); हरये ईर्ष्यति<BR>Sk.; Śi. 8. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्क्ष्य्
ईर्ष्य्, ईर्क्ष्य् {c1c} P. (ईर्ष्यति,<BR>ईर्ष्यांचकार, ईर्ष्यितुं, ईष्यिंत) To envy, be jealous<BR>of, be impatient of the success of<BR>(with dat. of person); हरये ईर्ष्यति<BR>Sk.; Śi. 8. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्य
ईर्ष्य, ईर्ष्यु, ईर्ष्यक a. Envious,<BR>jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यु
ईर्ष्य, ईर्ष्यु, ईर्ष्यक a. Envious,<BR>jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यक
ईर्ष्य, ईर्ष्यु, ईर्ष्यक a. Envious,<BR>jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्या
ईर्ष्या --र्षा [ईर्ष्य्-अप्] Envy,<BR>jealousy, envy of another's success,<BR>spite, malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षा
ईर्ष्या --र्षा [ईर्ष्य्-अप्] Envy,<BR>jealousy, envy of another's success,<BR>spite, malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यालु|ईर्ष्यालुः
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु, ईर्ष्यु(र्षु) a.<BR>Envious, impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षालु|ईर्षालुः
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु, ईर्ष्यु(र्षु) a.<BR>Envious, impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्ष्यु
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु, ईर्ष्यु(र्षु) a.<BR>Envious, impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईर्षु
ईर्ष्या(र्षा)लु, ईर्ष्यु(र्षु) a.<BR>Envious, impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईलिः|ईलि
ईलिः^1 (ली f.)<BR>1 A weapon, a<BR>cudgel or a short sword.<BR>--2 A<BR>stick shaped like a sword (<BR>करवालिका).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: By alph. order..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईवत्|ईवन्त्
ईवत् a.<BR>1 Going.<BR>--2 So large, so<BR>stately or magnificent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्
ईश् {c2c} A. (ईष्टे, ईशांचक्रे, ऐशिष्ट,<BR>ईशिता, ईशितुं, ईशित)<BR>1 To rule, be<BR>master of, govern, command (with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-c" target="_blank">Page0283-c+ 57</a>]<BR>gen.) नायं गात्राणामीष्टे K. 312 v. l.;<BR>अर्थानामीशिषे त्वं वयमपि च गिरामीश्महे<BR>यावदर्थं Bh. 3. 30; sometimes with acc.;<BR>इमाँल्लोकानीशत ईशनीभिः Śvet. Up.<BR>(also used in the Veda with gen.<BR>of an infinitive or loc. of an<BR>abstract noun).<BR>--2 To be able, have<BR>power; expressed by ‘can’;<BR>माधुर्यमीष्टे हरिणान् ग्रहीतुं R. 18. 13, 14. 38;<BR>कमिवेशते रमयितुं न गुणाः Ki. 6. 24;<BR>U. 7. 4; Śi. 1. 38; Māl. 10. 13.<BR>--3 To act like a master, allow.<BR>--4 To own, possess.<BR>--5 To belong to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्
ईश् m. A master, lord, the<BR>Supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश|ईशं|ईशः
ईश a. [ईश्-क]<BR>1 Owning,<BR>possessing, sharing, master or lord of;<BR>see below.<BR>--2 One who is<BR>completely master of anything.<BR>--3<BR>Capable of (with gen.).<BR>--4<BR>Powerful, supreme.<BR>--शः<BR>1 A lord,<BR>master; with gen. or in comp.;<BR>कथंचिदीशा मनसां बभूवुः Ku. 3. 34<BR>with great difficulty controlled<BR>(were masters of) their minds; so<BR>वागीश, सुरेश &c.<BR>--2 A husband.<BR>--3<BR>A Rudra.<BR>--4 The number 11<BR>(derived from the eleven Rudras).<BR>--5 N. of Śiva (as regent of the<BR>northeast quarter).<BR>--शा<BR>1<BR>Supremacy, power, dominion,<BR>greatness.<BR>--2 N. of Durgā.<BR>--3 A woman<BR>having supremacy; a rich lady.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कोणः the northeast<BR>quarter.<BR>--पुरी, --नगरी N. of Benares.<BR>--बलं the missile पाशुपत.<BR>--सरघः an<BR>epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशनं|ईशन
ईशनं [ईश्-ल्युट्] Commanding,<BR>reigning &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशान|ईशानं|ईशानः
ईशान a. [ईश् ताच्छील्ये चानश्]<BR>1<BR>Owning, possessing, master or lord.<BR>--2 Reigning, ruling.<BR>--3 Wealthy,<BR>rich.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A ruler, master, lord.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva; ईशानसंदर्शनलालसानां<BR>Ku. 7. 56; K. 10.<BR>--3 The Ārdrā<BR>Nakṣatra.<BR>--4 One of the Rudras.<BR>--5 The number ‘eleven’.<BR>--6 The sun<BR>as a form of Śiva.<BR>--7 A Sādhya.<BR>--8 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--नी N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--नी, --नः The silk-cotton<BR>tree (शाल्मली).<BR>--नं Light, splendour.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आदिपंचमूर्तिः f. one of the<BR>five forms of Śiva.<BR>--कृत् a. {1}<BR>making one a master or able. {2}<BR>acting like a competent person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशितृ
ईशितृ a. [ईश्-तृच्] An owner, a<BR>master, proprietor. --m. The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-a" target="_blank">Page0284-a+ 45</a>]<BR>lord of the Universe; Śi. 18. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0283-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशितव्यं|ईशितव्य
ईशितव्यं Power, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशिता
ईशिता, --त्वं Superiority, greatness,<BR>one of the eight Siddhis or<BR>attributes of Śiva. See अणिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशित्वं|ईशित्व
ईशिता, --त्वं Superiority, greatness,<BR>one of the eight Siddhis or<BR>attributes of Śiva. See अणिमन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईशिन्
ईशिन् a. [ईअ-निनि] Commanding,<BR>reigning &c. --m.<BR>1 A god.<BR>--2 A<BR>husband.<BR>--3 A lord, master.<BR>--नी<BR>Supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वर|ईश्वरं|ईश्वरः
ईश्वर a. (रा-री f.) [ईश्-वरच्<BR>P. III. 2. 175]<BR>1 Powerful, able,<BR>capable of (with inf.); Ku. 4. 11;<BR>R. 15. 7.<BR>--2 Rich, wealthy;<BR>Pt. 2. 67.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A lord, master; ईश्वरं<BR>लोकोर्थतः सेवते Mu. 1. 14; so कपीश्वरः,<BR>कोशलेश्वरः, हृदयेश्वरः &c.<BR>--2 A king,<BR>prince, ruler; राज्यमस्तमितेश्वरं<BR>R. 12. 11; Ms. 4. 153, 9. 278.<BR>--3 A rich<BR>or great man; तृणेन कांर्य भवतीश्वराणां<BR>Pt. 1. 71; R. 3. 46; Bh. 3. 59; मा<BR>प्रयच्छेश्वरे धनं H. 1. 15; cf. “To<BR>carry coals to Newcastle.”<BR>--4 A<BR>husband; नेश्वरे परुषता सखि साध्वी<BR>Ki. 9. 39.<BR>--5 The Supreme God<BR>(परमेश्वर); ईश एवाहमत्यर्थं न च<BR>मामीशते परे । ददाभि च सदैश्वर्यमीश्वरस्तेन<BR>कीर्तितः ॥.<BR>--6 N. of Śiva; V. 1. 1.<BR>--7<BR>The God of love, Cupid.<BR>--8 The<BR>Supreme soul; the soul.<BR>--9 The<BR>eleventh year (संवत्सर) of the<BR>Śālivāhana era.<BR>--रा, --री N. of Durgā;<BR>of Lakṣmī; or of any other of the<BR>saktis; ईश्वरीं सर्वभूतानां त्वामिहोपह्वये<BR>श्रियं.<BR>--री N. of several plants<BR>and trees; लिंगिनीलता, वंध्याकर्कटी,<BR>क्षुद्रजटा and नाकुलीवृक्ष.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधीन a. subject to a lord or king,<BR>dependent on a lord or god.<BR>--निषेधः denial of the existence of<BR>god, atheism.<BR>--निष्ठ a. trusting in<BR>god.<BR>--पूजक a. pious, devout.<BR>--पूजा<BR>worship of god.<BR>--प्रसादः divine<BR>favour.<BR>--भावः royal or imperial<BR>state.<BR>--विभूतिः f. the several forms of<BR>the Supreme god; for a full<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-b" target="_blank">Page0284-b+ 45</a>]<BR>enumeration, see Bg. 10. 19-42.<BR>--सद्मन्<BR>n. a temple.<BR>--सभं a royal court or<BR>assembly.<BR>--सेवा worship of god.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरता
ईश्वरता, --त्वं Superiority, supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईश्वरत्वं|ईश्वरत्व
ईश्वरता, --त्वं Superiority, supremacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्
ईष् {c1c} U. (ईषति-ते, ऐषीत्, ईषितुं, ईषित)<BR>1<BR>To fly away, escape.<BR>--2 To creep<BR>along.<BR>--3 To glean, collect a few<BR>grains.<BR>--4 To look, see.<BR>--5 To give.<BR>--6 To attack, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषः|ईष
ईषः [ईष्-क]<BR>1 The month Āśvina;<BR>cf. इष.<BR>--2 A servant of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषण
ईषण, ईषणिन् a. Hastening.<BR>--णा<BR>Haste, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषणिन्
ईषण, ईषणिन् a. Hastening.<BR>--णा<BR>Haste, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषत्
ईषत् ind. [ईस्-अति] Slightly, to<BR>some extent, a little; ईषत् चुंबितानि<BR>Ś. 1. 3; ईषच्च कुरुते सेवां Pt. 1. 141.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उष्ण a. tepid, slightly<BR>warm.<BR>--ऊन a. not quite complete, a<BR>little less than; ईषदूनार्थे कल्यब्.<BR>--कर<BR>a. {1} doing little. {2} easy to be<BR>accomplished; Mv. 4.<BR>--(रं) very<BR>little.<BR>--गुण a. of little merit.<BR>--जलं<BR>shallow water, a little water.<BR>--दर्शनं a glance, sight, view, glimpse.<BR>--नाद a. slightly sounding (a<BR>term applied to unaspirated soft<BR>consonants).<BR>--निमय a. exchanged<BR>for a little.<BR>--पांडु a. a little white<BR>or pale, whitish.<BR>--(डुः) a pale or<BR>light-brown colour.<BR>--पान a. that of<BR>which a little is drunk.<BR>--(नं) a<BR>small draught.<BR>--परुषः a mean or<BR>contemptible person.<BR>--रक्त a. pale<BR>red.<BR>--(क्तः) {1} pale-red colour. {2}<BR>undistinguishable colour.<BR>--लभ,<BR>--प्रलंभ a. to be got for little.<BR>--विवृत a.<BR>slightly open.<BR>--श्वास a. slightly<BR>resounding.<BR>--स्पृष्ट a. slightly<BR>touched (applied to the semi-vowels).<BR>--हासः slight laughter, a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषा
ईषा [ईष्-क]<BR>1 The pole or shafts<BR>of a carriage or a plough.<BR>--2 A<BR>part of a chariot.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंहः the<BR>handle of a plough; Śi. 18. 43.<BR>--दंत a.<BR>with projecting teeth.<BR>--(तः) {1} an.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">Page0284-c+ 43</a>]<BR>elephant with a large tusk or<BR>tooth. {2} the handle of a plough;<BR>Śi. 18. 38. {3} the tusk of an<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिका
ईषिका<BR>1 An elephant's eye-ball.<BR>--2 A painter's brush.<BR>--3 A weapon,<BR>arrow, dart.<BR>--4 A kind of missile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषिरः|ईषिर
ईषिरः [ईष्-किरच्] Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईषीका
ईषीका<BR>1 A painter's brush.<BR>--2<BR>An ingot-mould.<BR>--3 = इषीका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्म|ईष्मः
ईष्म, --ष्वः See इष्मः, इष्वः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईष्वः|ईष्व
ईष्म, --ष्वः See इष्मः, इष्वः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईह्
ईह् {c1c} A. (ईहते, ईहांचक्रे, ऐहिष्ट,<BR>ईहिष्यते, ईहितुं, ईहित)<BR>1 To wish, desire,<BR>long for; have in mind, think of<BR>(with acc. or inf.); ईहंते…<BR>अर्थसंचयान् Bg. 16. 12, 7. 22;<BR>Ms. 4. 15, 3. 126; ऐहिष्ट तं कारयितुं कृतात्मा<BR>Bk. 1. 11.<BR>--2 To endeavour to<BR>obtain.<BR>--3 To aim at or attempt,<BR>endeavour, strive; माधुर्यं मधुबिंदुना<BR>रचयितुं क्षारांबुधेरीहते Bh. 2. 6;<BR>Y. 2. 116.<BR>--4 To take care of. --Caus.<BR>To impel, urge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहः|ईह
ईहः Attempt; as in ऊर्ध्वेहः<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहा
ईहा [ईह्-अ]<BR>1 Wish, desire;<BR>जलनिधिमकरोत्तरीतुमीहां Rām.; see अनीह<BR>also.<BR>--2 An undertaking, act.<BR>--3<BR>Effort, exertion, activity;<BR>ईहातश्चेद्धनं भवेत् Ms. 9. 205.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थिन्<BR>a. aiming at any object, seeking<BR>wealth; Ms. 2. 37.<BR>--मृगः [ईहाप्रधानो<BR>मृगः] {1} a wolf. {2} an artificial deer. {3}<BR>a division of the drama consisting<BR>of four acts; for definition &c. see<BR>S. D. 518 = वृकः a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ईहित
ईहित p. p. [ईह्-क्त]<BR>1 Wished<BR>desired; शिरसीहितः Ratn. 1. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Attempted, sought, striven for;<BR>Ve. 1. 24.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A wish, desire;<BR>--2 Effort, exertion.<BR>--3 An<BR>undertaking, deed, act; प्रतीयते धातुरिवेहितं<BR>फलैः Ki. 1. 20, 8. 46, 11. 43,<BR>18. 31; Śi. 9. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उ|उः
उ {vI.v} {c1c} A. (अवते, ऊवे, औष्ट, ओतुं, उत)<BR>1 To sound, make a noise.<BR>--2 To<BR>roar, bellow (as a bull &c.). {vII.v} {c5c} P.<BR>(उनोति) Ved. To ask, demand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उः|उ
उः<BR>1 N. of Śiva, the second of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284--1b" target="_blank">Page0284--1b+ 5</a>]<BR>the three syllables in ओम्; see अ.<BR>--2 N. of Brahmā.<BR>--3 The orb of the<BR>moon. --ind.<BR>1 As a particle used<BR>expletively; उ उमेशः Sk.<BR>--2 An<BR>interjection of:-- (a) calling; उ मेति मात्रा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-1c" target="_blank">Page0284-1c+ 6</a>]<BR>तपसो निषिद्धा पश्चादुमाख्यां सुमुखी जगाम<BR>Ku. 1. 26; (b) anger; (c)<BR>compassion; (d) command; (e) acceptance; (f)<BR>interrogation; or (g) used merely as an<BR>expletive. In the Veda used as an<BR>enclitic copula implying restriction<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">Page0285-a+ 57</a>]<BR>and emphasis (and, but, on the<BR>other hand, now, I ask &c.);<BR>in classical literature used<BR>chiefly with अथ (अथो), न (नो) and<BR>किम् (किमु); see these words. उ-उ<BR>or उत on the one hand-on the other<BR>hand, partly-partly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0284-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकारः|उकार
उकारः<BR>1 The vowel उ.<BR>--2 The<BR>god Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकानहः|उकानह
उकानहः A horse of a red and<BR>yellow (or red and black) colour,<BR>a bay or chesnut horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उकुणः|उकुण
उकुणः A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्त|उक्तं|उक्तः
उक्त, उक्ति see under वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ति|उक्तिः
उक्त, उक्ति see under वच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थं|उक्थ|उक्थः
उक्थं [वच्-थक्]<BR>1 A saying,<BR>sentence, verse, hymn (स्तोत्रं).<BR>--2<BR>Eulogy, praise.<BR>--3 N. of the<BR>Sāmaveda (Trik.); a variety of<BR>Sāma; (सामभेदः सामविशेषः).<BR>--4 (In<BR>ritual) A kind of recitation or certain<BR>recited verses (opp. सामन् chanted,<BR>and यजुस् muttered verses).<BR>--5 The<BR>उक्थ sacrifice.<BR>--क्था N. of a metre,<BR>see Appendix<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रः<BR>{1} a sacrifice (having verses as<BR>its vehicle or leaves). {2} a<BR>sacrificer (यजमान).<BR>--पात्रं {1} a sacrificer.<BR>{2} vessels or libations offered<BR>during the recitation of an उक्थ.<BR>--भृत्<BR>m. a sage who offers or divides<BR>Ukthas.<BR>--वर्द्धन a. to be magnified or<BR>celebrated in praise, an epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR>--वाहस् a. offering verses; or<BR>one to whom verses are offered.<BR>--शंसिन् a. praising, uttering the Ukthas.<BR>(--m.) a kind of priest.<BR>--शस्, --शास्,<BR>शस a. Ved. uttering a verse,<BR>praising.<BR>--शुष्म a. whose strength is<BR>praise. {2} loudly resonant with<BR>verses. (--क्था) -वी a. fond of or reciting<BR>verses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थिन्
उक्थिन् a. [उक्थ-इनि]<BR>1 Uttering<BR>verses, praising.<BR>--2 Accompanied by<BR>praise or Ukthas. --m. Indra and<BR>others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्थ्य|उक्थ्यः
उक्थ्य a. [उक्थमर्हति यत्]<BR>1<BR>Accompanied by praise.<BR>--2 Deserving<BR>praise or verses.<BR>--क्थ्यः<BR>1 A<BR>libation at the morning and midday<BR>sacrifices.<BR>--2 N. of a sacrifice<BR>formng part of the ज्योतिष्टोम sacrifice.<BR>--3 A Soma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष्
उक्ष् {c1c} {c6c} U. (उक्षति, उक्षांचकार,<BR>ववक्ष-क्षे Ved., औक्षीत्, उक्षितुं, उक्षित)<BR>1<BR>To sprinkle, wet, moisten, pour<BR>down upon; औक्षन् शोणितमंभोदाः<BR>Bk. 17. 9, 3. 5; Śi. 5. 30; R. 11. 5,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">Page0285-b+ 58</a>]<BR>20; Ku. 1. 54.<BR>--2 To emit, send<BR>forth.<BR>--3 To scatter, throw out (as<BR>sparks).<BR>--4 To clean, purify.<BR>--5 To<BR>grow up, become strong (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्ष|उक्षः
उक्ष a. [उक्स्-अच्]<BR>1 Sprinkling.<BR>--2 Sprinkled.<BR>--3 Large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षणं|उक्षण
उक्षणं [उक्ष्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Sprinkling.<BR>--2<BR>Consecrating as by sprinkling;<BR>वसिष्ठमंत्रोक्षणजात् प्रभावात् R. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षण्यति
उक्षण्यति Den. P. To desire one<BR>who sends down riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षण्यु
उक्षण्यु a. Desirous of one who<BR>sends down riches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षन्
उक्षन् a.<BR>1 Large.<BR>--2 Sprinkling.<BR>--m.<BR>--(क्षा) [उक्ष्-कनिन् Uṇ. 1. 156]<BR>1<BR>An ox or bull; Ku. 7. 70; (changed to<BR>उक्ष in some comp. महोक्षः, वृद्धोक्षः,<BR>&c.).<BR>--2 An epithet of Soma; the<BR>Maruts; the sun and Agni.<BR>--3<BR>One of the eight chief medicaments<BR>(ऋषभौषधि).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्न a. one<BR>whose food is oxen (Ved.).<BR>--तरः<BR>a small bull or ox; Śi. 12. 10; cf.<BR>वत्सतर.<BR>--वश a. dependent on a bull<BR>(यदि वशां न विंदेदप्युक्षवश एव स्यात्);<BR>male calf (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षाल|उक्षालः
उक्षाल a. Swift, terrible, high;<BR>large, excellent.<BR>--लः A monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उक्षित
उक्षित p. p. [उक्ष्-क्त]<BR>1 Sprinkled,<BR>moistened.<BR>--2 Cleansed, perfumed.<BR>--3 Adult, of full growth.<BR>--4 Old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्
उख्, उंख् {c1c} P. (ओखति, उंखति, उवोख<BR>or उंखांचकार, ओखित, उंखित) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंख्
उख्, उंख् {c1c} P. (ओखति, उंखति, उवोख<BR>or उंखांचकार, ओखित, उंखित) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखः|उख
उखः A boiler, pot, vessel.<BR>--खा<BR>1 A boiling vessel, a boiler or<BR>cooking pot (such as a sauce-pan).<BR>--2 A<BR>fireplace at a sacrifice.<BR>--3 A part of<BR>the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उख्य|उख्यं|उख्यः
उख्य a. [उखायां संस्कृतं यत्]<BR>1<BR>Dressed or boiled in a pot (as flesh &c.);<BR>शूल्यमुख्यं च होमवान् Bk. 4. 9.<BR>--2 Being<BR>in a boiler (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखर्वलः|उखर्वल|उखर्व्वल|उखर्व्वलः
उखर्वलः, उखलः A kind of<BR>grass (भूरिपत्रः तृणभेदः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उखलः|उखल
उखर्वलः, उखलः A kind of<BR>grass (भूरिपत्रः तृणभेदः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उगण
उगण a. Ved. Consisting of<BR>troops with uplifted or ready<BR>weapons (उदायुधगणोपेत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्र|उग्रं|उग्रः
उग्र a. [उच्-रन् गश्चांतादेशः<BR>Uṇ. 2. 28]<BR>1 Fierce, cruel, ferocious,<BR>savage (as a look &c.); ˚दर्शनः<BR>having a fierce or cruel look.<BR>--2<BR>Formidable, terrific, frightful, fearful;<BR>सिंहनिपातमुग्रं R. 2. 60; Bg. 11. 30;<BR>Ms. 6. 75, 12. 75; ˚दंतः, ˚नासिकः &c.<BR>--3 Powerful, mighty, strong,<BR>violent, intense; उग्रातपां वेलां Ś. 3.<BR>intensely hot; उग्रशोकां Me. 113 v.l.<BR>--4<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-c" target="_blank">Page0285-c+ 58</a>]<BR>Sharp, pungent, hot.<BR>--5 High,<BR>noble.<BR>--6 Angry, passionate, wrathful.<BR>--7 Ready to do any work,<BR>industrious.<BR>--ग्रः<BR>1 N. of Śiva or Rudra.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a mixed tribe, descendant<BR>of a Kṣatriya father and Śūdra<BR>mother (his business being to<BR>catch or kill animals dwelling in<BR>holes, such as snakes; cf.<BR>Ms. 10. 9, 13, 15.).<BR>--3 N. of a tree<BR>शोभांजनवृक्ष.<BR>--4 A group of five asterisms;<BR>their names are: -- पूर्वाफाल्गुनी, पूर्वाषाढा,<BR>पूर्वाभाद्रपदा, मघा and भरणी.<BR>--5 N. of a<BR>country called Kerala (Modern<BR>Malabar).<BR>--6 The sentiment called रौद्र.<BR>--7<BR>Wind.<BR>--ग्रा<BR>1 N. of different plants;<BR>वचा, यवानी, धन्याक.<BR>--2 A cruel<BR>woman.<BR>--ग्री A kind of being<BR>belonging to the class of demons.<BR>--ग्रं<BR>1 A certain deadly poison, the<BR>root of Aconitum Ferox (वत्सनाभविषं).<BR>--2 Wrath, anger.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः<BR>the mighty or terrible lord, N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--कर्मन् a. fierce in action,<BR>cruel.<BR>--कांडः a sort of gourd<BR>(कारवेल).<BR>--गंध a. strong-smelling.<BR>--(धः) {1} the Campaka tree. {2}<BR>N. of other trees also; कट्फल,<BR>अर्जकबृक्ष. {3} garlic.<BR>--(धा) {1} Orris root.<BR>{2} a medicinal plant. {3} N. of<BR>various plants; यवानी, वचा, अजमोदा.<BR>--(धं) Asa fœtida.<BR>--गंधिन् a.<BR>strong-smelling.<BR>--चयः a strong<BR>desire.<BR>--चारिणी, --चंडा N. of Durgā.<BR>--जाति a. base-born.<BR>--तारा N.<BR>of a goddess.<BR>--तेजस् a. endowed<BR>with powerful or terrible energy.<BR>--दंष्ट्र a. having terrific teeth.<BR>--दंड<BR>a. ruling with a rod of iron, stern,<BR>cruel, relentless; Pt. 3.<BR>--दर्शन,<BR>--रूप a. frightful in appearance,<BR>fiercelooking, grim, terrible.<BR>--दुहितृ f. the<BR>daughter of a powerful man.<BR>--धन्वन् a. having a powerful bow.<BR>(--m.) N. of Śiva and Indra.<BR>--नासिक a. large-nosed.<BR>--पुत्र a. born<BR>in a mighty family.<BR>--(त्रः) N. of<BR>Kārttikeya.<BR>--पूति a. horribly<BR>stinking; Māl. 5. 16.<BR>--रेतस् m. a form<BR>of Rudra.<BR>--वीर a. having<BR>powerful men.<BR>--शासन a. strict in<BR>orders, severe in commands.<BR>--शेखरा ‘crest of Śiva’, N. of the<BR>Ganges.<BR>--शोक a. sorely-grieving,<BR>deeply afflicted.<BR>--श्रवणदर्शन a.<BR>terrible to hear and see.<BR>--सेनः {1}<BR>N. of a son of Dhṛtarāṣṭra. {2}<BR>N. of a king of Mathurā and father<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">Page0286-a+ 57</a>]<BR>of Kaṃsa. He was deposed by his<BR>son; but Kṛṣṇa after having slain<BR>Kaṃsa restored him to the throne.<BR>--(ना) N. of the wife of Akrūra;<BR>˚जः N. of Kaṃsa, the uncle and<BR>enemy of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0285-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रक
उग्रक a. Brave, powerful &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रता
उग्रता, --त्वं Violence, fearfulness,<BR>passion, anger, pungency,<BR>acrimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रत्वं|उग्रत्व
उग्रता, --त्वं Violence, fearfulness,<BR>passion, anger, pungency,<BR>acrimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उग्रंपश्य|उग्रम्पश्य
उग्रंपश्य a. [उग्रं पश्याति, उग्र-दृश्,<BR>खश्-मुम्]<BR>1 Fierce-looking, frightful,<BR>hideous.<BR>--2 Malignant, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंकुणः|उङ्कुण|उङ्कुणः
उंकुणः A bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्
उच् {c4c} P. (उच्यति, उवोच, औचीत्,<BR>उचिष्यति, उचितुं, उचित or उग्र mostly<BR>used in p. p.)<BR>1 To collect, to<BR>gather together.<BR>--2 To take<BR>pleasure in, delight in, be fond of.<BR>--3 To be accustomed or used to.<BR>--4 To be suitable, suit, fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचित|उचितं
उचित p. p.<BR>1 Fit, proper, right,<BR>suitable; उचितस्तदुपालंभः U. 3;<BR>usually with inf.; उचितं न ते<BR>मंगलकाले रोदितुं Ś. 4.<BR>--2 Usual,<BR>customary; उचितेषु करणीयेषु Ś. 4, 7. 12;<BR>K. 64; M. 3. 3.<BR>--3 Accustomed or used<BR>to, in comp.; नीवारभागधेयोचितैः<BR>R. 1. 50, 2. 25; 3. 54, 60; 11. 9;<BR>चंदनोचितः Ki. 1. 34.<BR>--4 Praiseworthy.<BR>--5 Delightful, agreeable,<BR>pleasurable.<BR>--6 Known, understood.<BR>--7<BR>Entrusted, deposited.<BR>--8 Measured,<BR>accurate, adjusted (भित).<BR>--9<BR>Acceptable (ग्राह्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचथं|उचथ
उचथं [उच्येत स्तूयतेऽनेन वच्-कथन्]<BR>Praise, verse (स्तोत्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उचथ्य
उचथ्य a. [उचय-यत्] Deserving<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्च|उच्चं|उच्चः
उच्च a.<BR>1 High(in all senses);<BR>tall; क्षितिधारणोच्चं Ku. 7. 68;<BR>elevated, superior, exalted (family &c.).<BR>--2 Loud, high-sounding; उच्चाः<BR>पक्षिगणाः Śi. 4. 18.<BR>--3 Intense, violent,<BR>strong.<BR>--4 (In astr.) Ascendant;<BR>see उच्चसंश्रय below.<BR>--च्चः The apex of<BR>the orbit of a planet.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तरुः<BR>{1} the cocoa-nut tree. {2} a lofty<BR>tree in general.<BR>--तालः (heightened)<BR>music, dancing &c. at a tavern.<BR>--देवता time personified, chronos.<BR>--नीच a. {1} high and low. {2} various,<BR>multiform.<BR>--(चं) {1} the upper or lower<BR>stations of planets. {2} change of<BR>accent.<BR>--भाषणं speaking aloud,<BR>vociferous.<BR>--भाषिन् a. shouting,<BR>bawling.<BR>--ललाटा, --टिका a woman<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">Page0286-b+ 58</a>]<BR>with a high or projecting forehead.<BR>--संश्रय a. occupying a high station<BR>(said of a planet); R. 3. 13; see<BR>Malli. thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चता
उच्चता, --त्वं Height, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चत्वं|उच्चत्व
उच्चता, --त्वं Height, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चकैः
उच्चकैः ind.<BR>1 High, above, lofty<BR>(fig. also); श्रितोदयाद्रेरभिसायमुच्चकैः<BR>Śi. 1. 16, 16. 46; Ki. 2. 57.<BR>--2<BR>Pre-eminently; Śi. 1. 70.<BR>--3 Loud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चा
उच्चा ind. High, above, upwards,<BR>aloft; ˚चक्र, ˚बुध्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैः
उच्चैः ind. [cf. Uṇ. 5. 12]<BR>1 Aloft,<BR>high, on high, above, upwards (opp.<BR>नीचं-चैः); पश्चादुच्चैर्भवति हरिणः Ś. 4. v. l.;<BR>विपद्युच्चैः स्थेयं Bh. 2. 28; उच्चैरुदात्तः<BR>P. I. 2. 29.<BR>--2 Loudly, with a loud<BR>noise; उच्चैर्विहस्य; R. 2. 12, 51;<BR>Bg. 1. 12.<BR>--3 Powerfully, intensely,<BR>very much, greatly; विदधति<BR>भयमच्चैर्वीक्ष्यमाणा वनांताः Rs. 1. 22; आश्लेषमर्पय<BR>मदर्पितपूर्वमुच्चैः Amaru. 94.<BR>--4 (Used<BR>as an adj. in comp. or by itself)<BR>(a) high, noble;<BR>जनोयमुच्चैःपदलंघनोत्सुकः Ku. 5. 64, 6. 75; ˚कुलं चात्मनः<BR>Ś. 4. 16; किंपुनर्यस्तथोच्चैः Me. 17;<BR>Ratn. 4. 16. (b) distinguished, pre-eminent,<BR>famous; उच्चैरुच्चैःश्रवास्तेन Ku. 2. 47,<BR>M. 5. 17.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a. making<BR>acutely accented.<BR>--घुष्टं {1} clamour,<BR>great uproar. {2} loud proclamation.<BR>--घोष a. boisterous, crying, roaring.<BR>--(षः) {1} loud noise. {2} a form of<BR>Rudra.<BR>--द्विष् a. having strong or<BR>powerful enemies; Ku. 3. 14.<BR>--भुजतरु a. having trees like<BR>outstretched arms; Me. 36.<BR>--वादः high<BR>praise; जामदग्न्यस्य दमन इति कोऽ<BR>यमुच्चैर्वादः U. 5.<BR>--शिरस् a. high-minded,<BR>one of high rank, magnanimous;<BR>क्षुद्रपि नूनं शरणं प्रपन्ने ममत्वमुच्चैःशिरसां<BR>सतीव Ku. 1. 12.<BR>--श्रवस्, --स a. {1}<BR>long-eared. {2} deaf. (--m.) N. of<BR>the horse of Indra (said to be<BR>churned out of the occan); उच्चैरुच्चैःश्रवास्तेन<BR>हयरत्नमहारि च Ku. 2. 47.<BR>--स्वर<BR>a. high-sounding.<BR>--(रः) a loud<BR>sound or voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तम
उच्चैस्तम a. Highest, tallest, loudest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तमां
उच्चैस्तमां ind.<BR>1 Exceedingly high.<BR>--2 Very loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तर|उच्चैस्तरं
उच्चैस्तर a. Higher, taller, louder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तरं|उच्चैस्तर
उच्चैस्तरं --रां ind.<BR>1 Very loud.<BR>--2<BR>Exceedingly high, on high;<BR>Ku. 7. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चैस्तरां
उच्चैस्तरं --रां ind.<BR>1 Very loud.<BR>--2<BR>Exceedingly high, on high;<BR>Ku. 7. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चक्षुस्
उच्चक्षुस् a.<BR>1 With the eyes<BR>directed upwards, looking upwards;<BR>सर्वा उच्चक्षुषः पश्यंति V. 1.<BR>--2 With<BR>the eyes taken out, blind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चघनं|उच्चघन
उच्चघनं A secret smile, a laughter<BR>in the mind not expressed in the<BR>countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चट्
उच्चट् {c1c} P. To go away,<BR>disappear. --Caus.<BR>1 To scare or drive<BR>away, expel.<BR>--2 To destroy, root<BR>out; Bh. 3. 129; N. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चाटनं|उच्चाटन|उच्चाटनः
उच्चाटनं<BR>1 Driving away,<BR>expulsion, removal from a place.<BR>--2<BR>Separation.<BR>--3 Eradication,<BR>extirpation (of a plant).<BR>--4 A kind of<BR>charm or magical incantation.<BR>--5<BR>Working this charm, ruining one's<BR>enemy, making a person leave his<BR>business by magical spells by<BR>making him disgusted with it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चटा
उच्चटा<BR>1 Pride, arrogance.<BR>--2<BR>Habit, usage.<BR>--3 A kind of garlic.<BR>--4 N. of different plants; गुंजा,<BR>चूडाला भूम्यामलकी, नागरमुस्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चंड|उच्चण्ड|उच्चण्डः
उच्चंड a.<BR>1 Fierce, terrible,<BR>formidable; U. 6.<BR>--2 Quick,<BR>expeditious.<BR>--3 Loud.<BR>--4 Angry, irascible,<BR>violent.<BR>--5 Hanging down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चंद्रः|उच्चन्द्र|उच्चंद्र|उच्चन्द्रः
उच्चंद्रः [उच्छिष्टः चंद्रो यत्र] The last<BR>watch of the night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चर्
उच्चर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go upwards, to<BR>rise; बाष्पमुच्चरति Mbh.; K. 14.<BR>--2<BR>To ascend (as the sun), issue or<BR>go forth, go up; Śi. 17. 52;<BR>Māl. 5. 21.<BR>--3 To arise, appear forth,<BR>rise (as a voice), to be heard;<BR>उच्चचार निनदोंभसि तस्याः R. 9. 73;<BR>15. 46; 16. 87; कोलाहलध्वनिरुदचरत्<BR>K. 27; U. 2; Ratn. 1.<BR>--4 To empty<BR>the body by evacuations, void one's<BR>excrement;<BR>तिरस्कृत्योच्चरेत्काष्ठलोष्टपत्रतृणादिना Ms. 4. 49.<BR>--5 To emit<BR>(sounds), utter, pronounce; शब्द<BR>उच्चरित एव मामगात् R. 11. 73.<BR>--6 (Used<BR>in the Atm.) (a) To quit, leave. (b) To<BR>sin against, be unfaithful (to a<BR>husband or wife), transgress against;<BR>धर्ममुच्चरते Sk. (c) To violate or<BR>transgress in general, stray or deviate<BR>from; Bk. 8. 31. (d) To rise up to,<BR>ascend (trans.); N. 5. 48; Śi. 17. 52.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to issue.<BR>--2 To<BR>utter, pronounce, declare.<BR>--3 To<BR>void one's excrement.<BR>--4 To emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरणं|उच्चरण
उच्चरणं<BR>1 Going up or out.<BR>--2<BR>Utterance, pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चरित
उच्चरित p. p.<BR>1 Gone up or out,<BR>risen.<BR>--2 Uttered, pronounced &c.<BR>--तं Excrement, fæces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारः|उच्चार
उच्चारः<BR>1 Utterance, pronunciation,<BR>declaration; वर्ण˚, काम˚.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">Page0287-a+ 55</a>]<BR>Excrement, dung, fæces; मातुरुच्चार एव सः<BR>H. Pr. 16; Ms. 4. 50.<BR>--3 Discharge<BR>(in general).<BR>--4 Passage (of<BR>heavenly bodies) to another zodiacal<BR>sign or asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0286-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारणं|उच्चारण
उच्चारणं^1<BR>1 Pronunciation,<BR>utterance; वाचः Śik. 2; वेद˚.<BR>--2<BR>Declaration, announcement, enunciation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. {1} useful for<BR>pronunciation. {2} necessary for<BR>pronunciation, such as a redundant<BR>letter only used to facilitate<BR>pronunciation.<BR>--ज्ञः a linguist.<BR>--स्थानं the part of the throat from<BR>which certain sounds (such as<BR>nasals, gutturals &c.) issue.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/334 - comment. note: cf AP..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारित
उच्चारित^1 p. p.<BR>1 Pronounced,<BR>uttered.<BR>--2 Having excrement.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/334 - comment. note: cf AP..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चारक
उच्चारक a. Pronouncing,<BR>uttering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चल्
उच्चल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To start, set out;<BR>स्थितः स्थितामुच्चलितः प्रयातां R. 2. 6;<BR>उच्चचाल बलभित्सखो वशी 11. 51;<BR>sometimes with dat. of place;<BR>नगरायोदचलं Dk.<BR>--2 To go or remove away<BR>or fly away (from one's place),<BR>fly away from; स्थानादनुच्चलन्नपि<BR>Ś. 1. 29; पुष्पोच्चलितषट्पदं R. 12. 27.<BR>--3 To free or extricate oneself<BR>from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चल|उच्चलं
उच्चल a. Moving.<BR>--लं Mind,<BR>understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलनं|उच्चलन
उच्चलनं Moving away, setting out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चलित
उच्चलित p. p.<BR>1 On the point of<BR>going, setting out.<BR>--2 Gone up or<BR>out; winnowed (as grain).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चावच|उच्चावचः
उच्चावच a. [मयूरव्यंसकादिगण]<BR>1<BR>High and low, uneven,<BR>irregular, undulating; Ms. 6. 73.<BR>--2<BR>Great and small, variegated,<BR>heterogeneous.<BR>--3 Various, multiform, of<BR>various kinds, diverse; उच्चावचाश्च<BR>पदार्था भवंतीति गार्ग्यः Nir.;<BR>Ms. 1. 38; Śi. 4. 46; Dk. 48, 104, 156.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चि
उच्चि {c5c} U. To collect, gather,<BR>accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चयः|उच्चय
उच्चयः<BR>1 A collection, heap,<BR>multitude; रूपोच्चयेन Ś. 2. 9;<BR>पदोच्चयः S. D. 2; cf. शिलोच्चय also.<BR>--2 Gathering, collecting (flowers<BR>&c.); पुष्पोच्चयं नाटयति Ś. 4;<BR>Ku. 3. 61.<BR>--3 The knot of a woman's<BR>(wearing) garment (नीविबंध);<BR>Ki. 8. 15, 51.<BR>--4 Nīvāra rice (collected<BR>by winnowing).<BR>--5 Prosperity,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">Page0287-b+ 54</a>]<BR>rise; उच्चयापचयौ H. 3. 133.<BR>--6 The<BR>opposite side of a triangle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिंगटः|उच्चिङ्गट|उच्चिङ्गटः
उच्चिंगटः<BR>1 A passionate or<BR>angry man.<BR>--2 A kind of crab.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिटंगः|उच्चिटङ्ग|उच्चिटङ्गः
उच्चिटं(टिं)गः A crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चिटिंगः|उच्चिटिङ्ग|उच्चिटिङ्गः
उच्चिटं(टिं)गः A crab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चित्र
उच्चित्र a. With the pictures<BR>prominently appearing; Māl. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चूडः|उच्चूड
उच्चूडः --लः<BR>1 The flag of a<BR>banner, or the banner itself.<BR>--2 An<BR>ornament fastened on the top of a<BR>banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्चूलः|उच्चूल
उच्चूडः --लः<BR>1 The flag of a<BR>banner, or the banner itself.<BR>--2 An<BR>ornament fastened on the top of a<BR>banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छन्न|उच्छन्नं
उच्छन्न a. [उद्-छद्-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Destroyed, cut down (perhaps for उत्सन्न); see<BR>उच्छिन्न.<BR>--2 Extinct (as a work).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छल्
उच्छल् {c1c} U. To fly upwards or<BR>away, move onwards, wave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलत्|उच्छलन्त्
उच्छलत् pres. a.<BR>1 Shining,<BR>moving about; Śi. 3. 37;<BR>Māl. 3; स्वच्छंदोच्छलदच्छ &c. K. P.<BR>--2 Appearing, bursting forth;<BR>Māl. 7.<BR>--3 Moving, going on; ibid.<BR>--4<BR>Flying up or away, going up high.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलनं|उच्छलन
उच्छलनं Going or moving<BR>upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छलित
उच्छलित p. p.<BR>1 Moved, waved<BR>above.<BR>--2 Shaken.<BR>--3 Gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छादनं|उच्छादन
उच्छादनं<BR>1 Covering.<BR>--2<BR>Rubbing the body with perfumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छासन
उच्छासन a. [उत्क्रांतः शासनं] Not<BR>amenable to rule or command,<BR>ungovernable, unruly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छास्त्र
उच्छास्त्र, ˚वर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Contrary or<BR>opposed to शास्त्र (civil or religious<BR>law-books).<BR>--2 Deviating from or<BR>transgressing the law-books;<BR>Y. 1. 140; Ms. 4. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छास्त्रवर्तिन्|उच्छास्त्रवर्त्तिन्
उच्छास्त्र, ˚वर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Contrary or<BR>opposed to शास्त्र (civil or religious<BR>law-books).<BR>--2 Deviating from or<BR>transgressing the law-books;<BR>Y. 1. 140; Ms. 4. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिख
उच्छिख a. [उद्गता शिखा यस्य]<BR>1<BR>Crested, with erected crest;<BR>U. 3. 18.<BR>--2 Having the flame pointed<BR>upwards, flaming, blazing up;<BR>Ki. 1. 32; K. 127; R. 16. 87.<BR>--3<BR>Radiant, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिंघनं|उच्छिङ्घन
उच्छिंघनं Breathing through<BR>the nostrils, snoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिद्
उच्छिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 (a) To cut off,<BR>extirpate, eradicate, destroy;<BR>नोच्छिंद्यादात्मनो मूलं परेषां चातितृष्णया Mb.;<BR>किं वा रिपूंस्तव गुरुः स्वयमुच्छिनत्ति<BR>R. 5. 71, 2. 23; Pt. 1. 47, 365. (b) To<BR>dispel, chase away; उच्छेत्तुं प्रभवति<BR>यन्न सप्तसप्तिः Ś. 6. 29. (c) To snap<BR>(thread); Māl. 9. 26.<BR>--2 To<BR>interfere with, interrupt, stop;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">Page0287-c+ 55</a>]<BR>न्यायानुच्छिद्य Mb.; तैस्तैर्भावैरनुच्छिन्नाः<BR>S. D. --pass.<BR>1 To be cut or snapped.<BR>--2 To be stopped or interrupted,<BR>cease; उच्छिद्यंते क्रियाः सर्वाः ग्रीष्मे<BR>कुसरितो यथा Pt. 2.<BR>--3 To waste<BR>away, fail, be wanting or deficient;<BR>एतान्यपि सतां गेहे नोच्छिद्यंते कदाचन<BR>Ms. 3. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छित्तिः|उच्छित्ति
उच्छित्तिः f. Extirpation,<BR>destruction; कोसल˚ Ratn. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिन्न|उच्छिन्नः
उच्छिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Extirpated,<BR>destroyed, cut down or off;<BR>उच्छिन्नाश्रयकातरेव कुलटा गोत्रांतरं श्रीगर्ता<BR>Mu. 6. 5.<BR>--2 Abject, vile.<BR>--न्नः Peace<BR>obtained by ceding valuable lands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेत्तृ
उच्छेत्तृ a. An extirpator, destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेदः|उच्छेद
उच्छेदः, --दनं<BR>1 Cutting off.<BR>--2<BR>Extirpation, eradication, destruction,<BR>putting an end to; सतां<BR>भवोच्छेदकरः पिंता ते R. 14. 74.<BR>--3 Excision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेदनं|उच्छेदन
उच्छेदः, --दनं<BR>1 Cutting off.<BR>--2<BR>Extirpation, eradication, destruction,<BR>putting an end to; सतां<BR>भवोच्छेदकरः पिंता ते R. 14. 74.<BR>--3 Excision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेदिन्
उच्छेदिन् a. Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिरस्
उच्छिरस् a. [उन्नतं शिरोऽस्य]<BR>1<BR>With the neck raised (lit.).<BR>--2<BR>High, lofty.<BR>--3 (Hence) Noble,<BR>great, exalted; शैलात्मजापि<BR>पितुरुच्छिरसोऽभिलाषं Ku. 3. 75, 6. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिलींध्र|उच्छिलीन्ध्र
उच्छिलींध्र a. Full of mushrooms<BR>(shot up); कर्तुं यच्च ग्रभवति<BR>महीमुच्छिलींध्रामवंध्याम् Me. 11.<BR>--ध्रं A<BR>mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्
उच्छिष् {c7c} P. (chiefly in pass.) To<BR>leave (as a remainder), reject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छिष्ट|उच्छिष्टं
उच्छिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Left as a remainder<BR>--2 Rejected, abandoned; अन्˚<BR>R. 12. 15.<BR>--3 Stale; ˚कल्पना stale idea<BR>or invention.<BR>--4 (Used actively)<BR>One who has not washed his mouth<BR>and hands after meals, and hence<BR>considered impure; न चोच्छिष्टः क्वचिद्<BR>व्रजेत् Ms. 2. 56.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 Leavings,<BR>fragments, remainder (especially of<BR>food or sacrifice); नोच्छिष्टं कस्यचिद्<BR>दद्यात् Ms. 2. 56; so द्विज˚, गृध्र˚.<BR>--2<BR>Honey.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्नं leavings, offal.<BR>--चांडालिनी a form of the goddess<BR>मातंगी.<BR>--भोजन, --भोजिन्, --भोक्तृ a. one<BR>who eats the leavings of another or<BR>eats the leavings of offerings to gods<BR>(as an attendant upon an idol).<BR>--भोजनं eating the leavings of<BR>another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेषः|उच्छेष
उच्छेषः, --षणं<BR>1 Rest, remainder;<BR>सरस्वतीमुखग्रहणोच्छेषणीकृतो दशनच्छद<BR>एष चुंबितुं Dk. 27.<BR>--2 Leavings (of<BR>food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छेषणं|उच्छेषण
उच्छेषः, --षणं<BR>1 Rest, remainder;<BR>सरस्वतीमुखग्रहणोच्छेषणीकृतो दशनच्छद<BR>एष चुंबितुं Dk. 27.<BR>--2 Leavings (of<BR>food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0287-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छीर्षक|उच्छीर्षकं
उच्छीर्षक a. Having the head<BR>raised.<BR>--कं [उत्थापितं शीर्षं यस्मिन्]<BR>1 A pillow.<BR>--2 The head; Ms. 3. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छुष्
उच्छुष् Caus. To dry up, make<BR>dry, wither up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छुष्क
उच्छुष्क a. Dried up, withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छोषण
उच्छोषण a.<BR>1 Making dry,<BR>withering up; यच्छोकमुच्छोषणमिंद्रियाणाम्<BR>Bg. 2. 8.<BR>--2 Burning, parching.<BR>--णं<BR>Drying up; parching, withering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छोषुक
उच्छोषुक a. Making dry, drying<BR>up, withering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छुष्मं|उच्छुष्म
उच्छुष्मं Confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छूडा
उच्छूडा = उच्चूड q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छून|उच्छूनं
उच्छून a. [उद्-श्वि-क्त]<BR>1 Swollen;<BR>प्रबलरुदितोच्छूननेत्रं प्रियायाः Me. 84;<BR>उत्तानोच्छूनमंडूकपाटितोदरसंनिभे<BR>K. P. 7; अनवरतरुदितोच्छूनताम्रदृष्टिं Dk. 95.<BR>--2 Fat, bulky.<BR>--3 High, lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छृंखल|उच्छृङ्खल|उच्छृङ्खलं
उच्छृंखल a.<BR>1 Unbridled,<BR>unrestained, uncurbed; ˚वाचा Pt. 3;<BR>अन्यदुच्छृंखलं सत्त्वमन्यच्छास्त्रनियंत्रितं<BR>Śi. 2. 62.<BR>--2 Self-willed, perverse.<BR>--3 Irregular, desultory, unsystematic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छोचनं|उच्छोचन
उच्छोचनं Burning(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छोफः|उच्छोफ
उच्छोफः Swelling; Māl. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रावणं|उच्छ्रावण
उच्छ्रावणं Making one hear<BR>loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रि
उच्छ्रि [उद्-श्रि] U.<BR>1 To rise, be<BR>erected (A.).<BR>--2 To raise, erect, lift<BR>up.<BR>--3 To praise, extol. --Caus.<BR>To increase; Mv. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रयः|उच्छ्रय
उच्छ्र(च्छ्रा)यः [उद्-श्रि-अच् घञ्<BR>वा]<BR>1 Rising (of a planet &c.);<BR>Y. 1. 147.<BR>--2 Raising, erecting.<BR>--3<BR>Height, elevation (physical and<BR>moral); शृंगोच्छ्रायैः कुमुदविशदैर्यो<BR>वितत्य स्थितः खं Me. 58; K. 105;<BR>Ki. 7. 27, 8. 23, 17. 61; Śi. 4. 10,<BR>8. 22.<BR>--4 Growth, increase, intensity;<BR>गुण˚ Ki. 8. 21, 16. 10; नीतोच्छ्रायं<BR>5. 31, 14. 21.<BR>--5 Pride.<BR>--6 The upright<BR>side of a triangle.<BR>--यी (उच्छ्रायी)<BR>Plank.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपेत a. possessing<BR>height, high, lofty, elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रायः|उच्छ्राय
उच्छ्र(च्छ्रा)यः [उद्-श्रि-अच् घञ्<BR>वा]<BR>1 Rising (of a planet &c.);<BR>Y. 1. 147.<BR>--2 Raising, erecting.<BR>--3<BR>Height, elevation (physical and<BR>moral); शृंगोच्छ्रायैः कुमुदविशदैर्यो<BR>वितत्य स्थितः खं Me. 58; K. 105;<BR>Ki. 7. 27, 8. 23, 17. 61; Śi. 4. 10,<BR>8. 22.<BR>--4 Growth, increase, intensity;<BR>गुण˚ Ki. 8. 21, 16. 10; नीतोच्छ्रायं<BR>5. 31, 14. 21.<BR>--5 Pride.<BR>--6 The upright<BR>side of a triangle.<BR>--यी (उच्छ्रायी)<BR>Plank.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपेत a. possessing<BR>height, high, lofty, elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रयण
उच्छ्रयण a. Raised, erected.<BR>--णं<BR>Raising, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रायिन्
उच्छ्रायिन् a. High, raised, lofty;<BR>Śi. 5. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रित|उच्छ्रितं
उच्छ्रित p. p.<BR>1 Raised, lifted up;<BR>H. 2. 164; R. 17. 33.<BR>--2 Gone up,<BR>risen; ˚सितांशुकर Śi. 4. 25;<BR>K. 206.<BR>--3 High, tall, lofty,<BR>exalted; Ki. 5. 1; Bg. 6. 11; R. 9. 19;<BR>पंचयोजनमुच्छ्रिता Mb.<BR>--4 Produced,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-b" target="_blank">Page0288-b+ 56</a>]<BR>born.<BR>--5 Increasing, growing,<BR>prosperous; Ms. 7. 170; increased (in<BR>size or bulk), grown.<BR>--6 Proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रितिः|उच्छ्रिति
उच्छ्रितिः = उच्छ्रय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्रेय
उच्छ्रेय a. High, lofty, tall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्लकः|उच्छ्लक
उच्छ्लकः Ved. A part of the<BR>human body (used only in dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वंकः|उच्छ्वङ्क|उच्छ्वङ्कः
उच्छ्वंकः Ved. Gaping; cleaving<BR>open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वस्
उच्छ्वस् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To breathe, live;<BR>आस्मेच्छया न शक्यमुच्छ्वसितुमपि<BR>K. 175; Ve. 5. 15; Ms. 3. 72;<BR>अनुच्छ्वस्य without breathing, in one<BR>breath.<BR>--2 To take heart or courage,<BR>cheer up, revive, breathe a sigh of<BR>relief; नाद्याप्युच्छ्वसिति U. 3, 7;<BR>त्वत्सन्निधावुच्छ्वसितीव चेतः Ki. 3. 8<BR>is delighted; Śi. 18. 58; Ratn. 4;<BR>दिगंतः Ki. 9. 21.<BR>--3 To open,<BR>bloom (as a lotus); नोच्छ्वसिति<BR>तपनकिरणैः (कुमुदं) V. 3. 16;<BR>M. 2. 11; Śi. 10. 58, 11. 15.<BR>--4 To take<BR>a deep breath, pant, sigh deeply;<BR>Bk. 6. 120, 14. 55.<BR>--5 To throb,<BR>heave, palpitate.<BR>--6 To be<BR>loosened or relaxed. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to<BR>breathe.<BR>--2 To console, cheer up,<BR>delight; Rs. 6. 8; U. 3; Śi. 9. 34.<BR>--3<BR>To loosen, relax, disjoin; Me. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वसनं|उच्छ्वसन
उच्छ्वसनं<BR>1 Breathing, sighing.<BR>--2<BR>Taking a deep breath, heaving.<BR>--3<BR>Loosening; Māl. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वसित|उच्छ्वसितं
उच्छ्वसित p. p. (Used actively).<BR>1 Heaving, breathing; U. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Emitting or sending out vapour<BR>(refreshed); V. 4.<BR>--3 Full-blown,<BR>opened, expanded; Māl. 4; ˚मूर्तिः<BR>K. 92 raised up, Ch. P. 13.<BR>--4 (a)<BR>Enlivened, gladdened, refreshed;<BR>Me. 42. (b) Inspired or animated with<BR>hope; Ku. 6. 14.<BR>--5 Breathing a<BR>sigh of relief; M. 3. 6; R. 10. 73;<BR>K. 181.<BR>--6 Consoled;<BR>उत्कंठोच्छ्वसितहृदया Me. 100.<BR>--7 Waving,<BR>dishevelled; ˚अलकं R. 8. 55.<BR>--8<BR>Effaced (सम्˚); Ku. 3. 38.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Breath, the (very) life; सा<BR>कुलपतेरुच्छ्वसितमिव Ś. 3; Ku. 7. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Blooming, blowing.<BR>--3 Exhalation;<BR>R. 8. 3.<BR>--4 Heaving, upheaval,<BR>throbbing; R. 6. 68; V. 1.<BR>--5<BR>Becoming loose or relaxed.<BR>--6<BR>Sighing.<BR>--7 The vital airs of<BR>the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वासः|उच्छ्वास
उच्छ्वासः<BR>1 Breath, exhalation,<BR>breathing out; मुखोच्छ्वासगंधं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">Page0288-c+ 55</a>]<BR>V. 4. 22; Rs. 1. 3; Me. 102.<BR>--2 Support of<BR>life, being alive; U. 3. 30; K. 158.<BR>--3 A sigh.<BR>--4 Consolation,<BR>encouragement; Amaru. 11.<BR>--5 Expiring,<BR>dying.<BR>--6 An air-hole.<BR>--7 A<BR>division or chapter of a book, as of the<BR>Harṣa-charita; cf. अध्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वासित
उच्छ्वासित p. p.<BR>1 Breathless, out<BR>of breath.<BR>--2 Much, excessive.<BR>--3<BR>Loosened, released.<BR>--4 Detached,<BR>separated, divided.<BR>--5 Consoled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्वासिन्
उच्छ्वासिन् a.<BR>1 Breathing,<BR>inhaling air.<BR>--2 Heaving, throbbing;<BR>V. 1. 6; Me. 102.<BR>--3 Sighing.<BR>--4<BR>Expiring, dying.<BR>--5 Vanishing, fading<BR>away; Ku. 7. 82.<BR>--6 Pausing,<BR>stopping.<BR>--7 Rising, coming forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उच्छ्|उछ्
उच्छ् {c6c} P. (उच्छति, औच्छीत्, उच्छितुं,<BR>उष्ट)<BR>1 To finish.<BR>--2 To bind.<BR>--3 To<BR>abandon, transgress.<BR>--4 To cease,<BR>stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जस्
उज्जस् Caus. To kill, destroy,<BR>extirpate (with gen.);<BR>बिडौजसोज्जासयितुं जगद्द्रुहां Śi. 1. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जासनं|उज्जासन
उज्जासनं Killing, slaughter;<BR>चोरस्योज्जासनं Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयनी
उज्जय(यि)नी N. of a city,<BR>the modern Oujein in Mālvā, the<BR>capital of Vikramāditya. It is one<BR>of the seven sacred cities of the<BR>Hindus (cf. अवंति), and the first<BR>meridian of their geographers from<BR>which they calculate longitude;<BR>सौधोत्संगप्रणयविमुखो मा स्म भूरुज्जयिन्याः<BR>Me. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जयिनी
उज्जय(यि)नी N. of a city,<BR>the modern Oujein in Mālvā, the<BR>capital of Vikramāditya. It is one<BR>of the seven sacred cities of the<BR>Hindus (cf. अवंति), and the first<BR>meridian of their geographers from<BR>which they calculate longitude;<BR>सौधोत्संगप्रणयविमुखो मा स्म भूरुज्जयिन्याः<BR>Me. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जानकः|उज्जानक
उज्जानकः N. of a province in<BR>the North.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जि
उज्जि {c1c} P.<BR>1 To win, acquire by<BR>conquest, conquer.<BR>--2 To be<BR>victorious, triumph. --Caus. (जापयति)<BR>1 To cause to conquer.<BR>--2 To<BR>help one in winning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जितिः|उज्जिति
उज्जितिः f. Ved.<BR>1 Victory.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of certain verses in the<BR>VājasaneyiSaṃhitā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जेष|उज्जेषः
उज्जेष a. Victorious.<BR>--षः<BR>Obtaining prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जिघ्र
उज्जिघ्र a. [उद्-घ्रा-श] Smelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जीव्
उज्जीव् {c1c} P. To revive, return to<BR>life. --Caus. To restore life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जीवनं
उज्जीवनं Revival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जीविन्
उज्जीविन् Reviving, coming to life<BR>again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जृंभ्|उज्जृम्भ्
उज्जृंभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To gape, open.<BR>--2 To part asunder.<BR>--3 To become<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">Page0289-a+ 56</a>]<BR>visible, come or break forth, expand,<BR>rise, go up; वक्त्रेंदौ तव सत्ययं यदपरः<BR>शीतांशुरुज्जृंभते Ratn. 3. 13; K. 290<BR>--4 To revive, come to senses;<BR>Mv. 6. 52. --Caus.<BR>1 To display, show.<BR>--2<BR>To produce; U. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0288-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जृंभ|उज्जृम्भ|उज्जृम्भं|उज्जृम्भः
उज्जृंभ a.<BR>1 Blown, expanded;<BR>उज्जृंभवदनांभोजा भिनत्यंगानि सांगना<BR>S. D.<BR>--2 Gaping, open.<BR>--भः<BR>1<BR>Opening, expansion, blowing.<BR>--2<BR>Gaping of the mouth.<BR>--3 Breaking<BR>asunder, parting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जृंभा
उज्जृंभा, --भणं<BR>1 The act of gaping,<BR>opening the mouth, yawning,<BR>--2<BR>Spreading, increase; Māl. 5. 23.<BR>--3<BR>Flurry, agitation; U. 3. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जृंभणं|उज्जृम्भण|उज्जृंभण
उज्जृंभा, --भणं<BR>1 The act of gaping,<BR>opening the mouth, yawning,<BR>--2<BR>Spreading, increase; Māl. 5. 23.<BR>--3<BR>Flurry, agitation; U. 3. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्जृंभित|उज्जृम्भित|उज्जृम्भितं
उज्जृंभित a. Opened, stretched,<BR>expanded, blown.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The act of<BR>gaping.<BR>--2 Effort, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्य
उज्ज्य [उद्गता ज्या यस्य] Having the<BR>bow-string loosened.<BR>--ज्ज्यं A bow<BR>with the string fastened to it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वल्
उज्ज्वल् {c1c} P. To blaze up, shine.<BR>--Caus. (ज्वलयति) To light up,<BR>illuminate, irradiate; Śi. 9. 42; Gīt. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वल|उज्ज्वलं|उज्ज्वलः
उज्ज्वल a.<BR>1 Bright, shining,<BR>luminous, splendid; उज्ज्वलकपालं मुखं<BR>Śi. 9. 48, 47.<BR>--2 Burning.<BR>--3 Clean, clear,<BR>white; Śi. 6. 5.<BR>--4 Lovely, beautiful;<BR>सर्गो निसर्गोज्ज्वलः N. 3. 136.<BR>--5 Mixed<BR>with, seasoned; Mk. 8. 13.<BR>--6<BR>Blown, expanded.<BR>--7 Unrestrained,<BR>full; Śi. 5. 48<BR>--लः Love, passion.<BR>--ला<BR>1 Splendour, brightness.<BR>--2<BR>Clearness.<BR>--3 A form of the Jagatī<BR>metre.<BR>--लं Gold.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दत्तः N.<BR>of the author of a commentary on<BR>the Uṇādi Sūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वलनं|उज्ज्वलन
उज्ज्वलनं<BR>1 Burning, shining.<BR>--2<BR>Splendour, brilliance.<BR>--3 Fire.<BR>--4<BR>Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्ज्वलित
उज्ज्वलित p. p. Lighted, shining,<BR>brilliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्झ्
उज्झ् {c6c} P. [उज्झति, उज्झांचकार,<BR>उज्झितुं, उज्झित]<BR>1 To abandon, leave,<BR>quit; सपदि विगतनिद्रस्तल्पमुज्झांचकार<BR>R. 5. 75; तत्क्षणोज्झतवृक्षकं<BR>R. 1. 40, 51; आतपायोज्झितं धान्यं<BR>Mb. exposed to the sun.<BR>--2<BR>To avoid, escape from; उदये<BR>मदवाच्यमुज्झता R. 8. 84; Śi. 1. 63.<BR>--3 To emit, give out, drop or pour<BR>down; अविरतोज्झितवारिविपांडुभिः<BR>Ki. 5. 6; Śi. 4. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्झ|उज्झः
उज्झ a. [उज्झ्-अच्] Leaving,<BR>quitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्झकः|उज्झक
उज्झकः<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>--2 A devotee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्झनं|उज्झन
उज्झनं [उज्झ्-ल्युट्] Abandoning,<BR>removing, leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उज्झटित
उज्झटित a. Perplexed,<BR>bewildered, confounded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंछ्|उञ्छ्
उंछ् {c6c} P. (उंछति, उंछितुं, उंछित)<BR>To glean, gather (bit by bit);<BR>शिलानप्युंछतः Ms. 3. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंछः|उञ्छ|उञ्छं|उञ्छः
उंछः [उंछ्-घञ्] Gleaning or<BR>gathering grains; तान्युंछषष्ठांकितसैकतानि<BR>R. 5. 8; Ms. 10. 112.<BR>--छं Gleaning.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वृत्ति, --शील a. one who<BR>lives by gleaning grains, a gleaner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंछनं|उञ्छन|उञ्छनं
उंछनं Gleaning grains of corn in<BR>market-places &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उटं|उट|उटः
उटं<BR>1 A leaf.<BR>--2 Grass.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः, --जं [उटेभ्यो जायते] a hut, cottage,<BR>the residence of hermits, or saints, a<BR>hermitage (being mostly made of<BR>grass or leaves); उटजद्वारविरूढं<BR>नीवारबलिं विलोकयतः Ś. 4. 20; मृगैर्वर्तितरोमन्थ<BR>मुटजाङ्गनभूमिषु R. 1. 52, 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उठ्
उठ् = ऊठ् {c1c} P. (ओठति, उवोठ, ओठीत्<BR>उठितुं, उठित)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To strike<BR>or knock down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुः|उडु
उडुः f. उडु n. [उड्-वा˚ क]<BR>1 A<BR>lunar mansion; a star;<BR>इंदुप्रकाशांतरितोडुतुल्याः R. 16. 65.<BR>--2 Water<BR>(said to been. only).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चक्रं<BR>zodiacal circle.<BR>--पः --पं [उडुनि जले<BR>पाति] a raft, boat; तितीर्षुर्दुस्तरं<BR>मोहाढुडुपेनास्मि सागरं R. 1. 2; केनोडुपेन पर<BR>लोकनदीं तरिष्ये Mk. 8. 23<BR>--(पः) the<BR>moon; Mk. 4. 23.<BR>--पतिः, --राज् {1}<BR>the moon; जितमुडुपतिना Ratn. 1. 5;<BR>रसात्मकस्योडुपतेश्च रश्मयः Ku. 5. 22.<BR>{2} Varuṇa, regent of waters.<BR>--पथः<BR>the sky, the firmament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडुंबरः|उडुम्बर|उडुंबर|उडुम्बरं|उडुम्बरः
उडुंबरः<BR>1 N. of a tree; Ficus<BR>Glomerata (Mar. औदुंबर).<BR>--2 The<BR>threshold of a house.<BR>--3 A<BR>eunuch.<BR>--4 A part of a sacrifice.<BR>--5 A kind of leprosy with copper<BR>spots (--रं also).<BR>--6 A kind of worm<BR>said to be produced in the blood<BR>and to produce leprosy.<BR>--रं<BR>1 The<BR>fruit of the उदुंबर tree.<BR>--2 Copper.<BR>--3 A Karṣa, a measure of two<BR>tolas.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दला, --पर्णी the plant<BR>Croton Polyandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उडूपः|उडूप
उडूपः = उडुपः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डामर|उड्डामरं
उड्डामर a.<BR>1 Agreeable,<BR>excellent, respectable.<BR>--2 Formidable,<BR>terrific;<BR>उड्डामरव्यस्तविस्तारिदोःखंडपर्यासितक्ष्माधरम Māl. 5. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डी
उड्डी {c1c} {c4c} A. To fly up, soar.<BR>--Caus. To scare away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डयनं|उड्डयन
उड्डयनं Flying up, soaring; गतो<BR>विरुत्योड्डयने निराशतां N. 1. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डीन|उड्डीनं
उड्डीन p. p. Flown up, flying<BR>up.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Flying up, soaring.<BR>--2<BR>A particular flight of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डीयनं|उड्डीयन
उड्डीयनं Flying up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्डीशः|उड्डीश
उड्डीशः<BR>1 N. of a work<BR>containing charms and incantation.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उड्रः|उड्र
उड्रः N. of a country; the<BR>modern Orissa; see ओड्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उणक
उणक a. (की f.) Removing,<BR>driving out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उणादिः|उणादि
उणादिः A class of terminations<BR>beginning with उण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंडुकः|उण्डुक|उण्डुकः
उंडुकः<BR>1 A species of leprosy.<BR>--2 A texture, net.<BR>--3 A part of<BR>the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंडेरकः|उण्डेरक|उंडेरक|उण्डेरकः
उंडेरकः A ball of flour,<BR>rollloaf; तथैवोंडेरकस्रजः Y. 1. 288.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्
उत् ind. A particle of(a) doubt;<BR>(b) interrogation; (c) deliberation;<BR>(d) intensity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत|उतं
उत ind.<BR>1 A particle expressing<BR>(a) doubt, uncertainty guess (or);<BR>तत्किमयमातपदोषः स्यादुत यथा मे मनसि<BR>वर्तते Ś. 3; स्थाणुरयमुत पुरुषः G. M.<BR>(b) alternative; usually a correlative<BR>of किं (whether, or); किमिद<BR>गुरुभिरुपदिष्टमुत धर्मशास्त्रेषु पठितमुत<BR>मोक्षप्राप्तियक्तिरियं K. 155; किं येन सृजसि<BR>व्यक्तमुत येन बिभर्षि तत् Ku. 6. 23;<BR>the place of उत is also taken by<BR>आहो or आहोस्वित्; sometimes आहो,<BR>आहोस्वित् or स्वित् are joined to उत.<BR>(c) association, connection,<BR>(having a cumulative force, ‘and’,<BR>‘also’); उत बलवानुताबलः; (d)<BR>interrogation; उत दंडः पतिष्यति; (e)<BR>deliberation; (f) intensity; (g)<BR>wishing (especially at the beginning<BR>of a sentence followed by a<BR>potential ‘would that’); (h) sometimes<BR>used as an expletive; (i) oft. used<BR>for the sake of emphasis especially<BR>at the end of a line after इति or a<BR>verb; तदा विद्याद्विवृद्धं सत्त्वमित्युत<BR>Bg. 14. 11; धर्मे नष्टे कुलं कृत्स्नमधर्मोऽ<BR>भिभवत्युत 1. 40.<BR>--2 With a preceding<BR>प्रति = on the contrary, on the other<BR>hand; but; सामवादाः सकोपस्य तस्य<BR>प्रत्युत दीपकाः Śi. 2. 55; न केवलं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">Page0290-a+ 54</a>]<BR>ध्रियते प्रत्युत पर्युपास्यमानस्तिष्ठति Nāg. 5.<BR>--3 With a preceding किं = how much<BR>more or how much less; see किम्.<BR>उत, --उत Either-or; एकमेव वरं<BR>पुंसामुतराज्यमुताश्रमः G. M. उत वा or else,<BR>and; वा-उतवा, उताहोवा पि-वा either-or.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0289-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उतथ्यः|उतथ्य
उतथ्यः N. of a son of Aṅgiras<BR>and elder brother of Bṛhaspati.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुजः, --अनुजन्मन् m.<BR>Bṛhaspati, teacher of the gods, तथ्य<BR>मुतथ्यानुजवज्जगादाग्रे गदाग्रजं Śi. 2. 69.<BR>--तनयः N. of Gautama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क|उत्कः
उत्क a. [उद्-स्वार्थे कन्; उत्कः = उ.<BR>त्कंठितः; उत्क उन्मनाः P. V. 2. 80 Sk.]<BR>1 Desirous<BR>of, longing for, anxiously wishing<BR>for (in comp.); अद्रिसुतासमागमोत्कः<BR>Ku. 6. 95; मानसोत्काः Me. 11;<BR>sometimes with an inf.; Śi. 4. 18.<BR>--2<BR>Regretting, sad, sorrowful.<BR>--3<BR>Absent-minded.<BR>--त्कः<BR>1 Desire.<BR>--2<BR>Opportunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कता
उत्कता<BR>1 A state of longing or<BR>regret, anxiety.<BR>--2 N. of a plant<BR>having aromatic seeds (गजपिप्पली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कायते
उत्कायते Den. A. To long for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कयति
उत्कयति Den. P. To make<BR>uneasy; Śi. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कच
उत्कच a.<BR>1 Having the hair<BR>erect; as in घटोत्कच.<BR>--2 Having no<BR>hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कच्छा
उत्कच्छा A metre of six lines,<BR>each line containing eleven syllabic<BR>instants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कंचुक|उत्कञ्चुक
उत्कंचुक a.<BR>1 Without bodice, or<BR>jacket.<BR>--2 Without a coat of mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कट्
उत्कट् {c1c} P. To start or burst out;<BR>Mv. 5. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कट|उत्कटं|उत्कटः
उत्कट a.<BR>1 Large, spacious;<BR>U. 4. 29.<BR>--2 Powerful, mighty,<BR>extraordinary, fierce; Pt. 1. 103;<BR>Mv. 1. 39, 5. 33.<BR>--3 Excessive, much;<BR>अत्युत्कटैः पापपुण्यीरहेव फलमश्नुते<BR>H. 1. 83.<BR>--4 Prominently visible,<BR>conspicuous; ˚लांछनस्य U. 5. 36.<BR>--5<BR>Abounding in, richly endowed with;<BR>पादपान् कुसुमोत्कटान् Rām.<BR>--6 Drunk,<BR>mad, furious; मदोत्कटः.<BR>--7 Superior,<BR>high.<BR>--8 Proud, haughty.<BR>--9<BR>Uneven.<BR>--10 Difficult.<BR>--टः<BR>1 A fluid<BR>(ichor) dropping from the temples<BR>of an elephant in rut.<BR>--2 An<BR>elephant in rut.<BR>--3 The plant<BR>Saccharum Sara.<BR>--4 Pride, intoxication.<BR>--टा The plant Laurus Cassia (<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">Page0290-b+ 54</a>]<BR>सैहीलता).<BR>--टं The fragrant bark of<BR>Laurus Cassia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कटुकासनं|उत्कटुकासन
उत्कटुकासनं Sitting on the<BR>hams, squatting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कणिका
उत्कणिका A raised particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कंठ|उत्कण्ठ|उत्कण्ठः
उत्कंठ a. [उन्नतः कंठो यस्य]<BR>1<BR>Having the neck uplifted, ready, on<BR>the point of (doing anything), in<BR>comp.; आज्ञावचनोत्कंठः Ś. 2;<BR>रथस्वनोत्कंठमृगे वाल्मीकीये तपोवने R. 15. 11.<BR>--2 (Hence) Anxious. eager.<BR>--ठः,<BR>--ठा A mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कंठते
उत्कंठते Den. A.<BR>1 To be anxious.<BR>pine or be sorry for; Ś. 4;<BR>Śi. 9. 54.<BR>--2 To yearn, be eagerly<BR>desirous of (with gen. or dat.);<BR>स्वर्गाय नोत्कंठते V. 3. 4; Mv. 6; उत्कंठते<BR>च युष्मत्सन्निकर्षस्य U. 6, 6. 21;<BR>Māl. 4; Bk. 5. 72. --Caus. (<BR>उत्कठयति) To create anxiety or longing,<BR>inspire with tender emotions;<BR>Bh. 1. 35; Ghaṭ. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कंठा|उत्कण्ठा
उत्कंठा<BR>1 Anxiety, uneasiness (in<BR>general); य स्यत्यद्य शकुंतलेति हृदयं<BR>संस्पृष्टमुत्कंठया Ś. 4. 5; अवाप्त˚<BR>Māl. 2. 12 seized with fright, suddenly<BR>startled.<BR>--2 Longing for a beloved<BR>person or thing; दृष्टिरधिकं<BR>सोत्कंठमुद्वीक्षते Amaru. 24.<BR>--3 Regret, sorrow,<BR>missing anything or person;<BR>गाढोत्कंठा Māl. 1. 15; Me. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कंठित|उत्कण्ठित|उत्कण्ठितं
उत्कंठित p. p.<BR>1 Anxious, uneasy.<BR>--2 Regretting, grieving for,<BR>sorrowful.<BR>--3 Longing for a beloved<BR>person or thing.<BR>--ता A mistress<BR>longing for her absent lover or<BR>husband, one of the eight heroines;<BR>she is thus defined<BR>--आगंतुं<BR>कृतचित्तोऽपि दैवान्नायाति यत्प्रियः । तंदनागमदुःखार्ता<BR>विरहोत्कंठिता तु सा ॥ S. D. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कंधर|उत्कन्धर|उत्कन्धरं
उत्कंधर a. [उन्नतः कंधरोऽस्य]<BR>Having the neck uplifted; उत्कंधरं<BR>दारुकमित्युवाच Śi. 4. 18.<BR>--रं<BR>Bending back the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कंप्|उत्कम्प्
उत्कंप् {c1c} A. To tremble, quiver,<BR>shake. --Caus. To cause to tremble,<BR>shake, agitate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कंप|उत्कम्प|उत्कम्पः
उत्कंप a. Trembling; श्वास˚ कुचं<BR>Amaru. 90.<BR>--पः, --पनं Trembling,<BR>tremor, agitation;<BR>किमधिकत्रासोत्कंपं दिशः समुदीक्षसे Amaru. 28; Me. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कंपिन्|उत्कम्पिन्
उत्कंपिन्<BR>1 Trembling.<BR>--2<BR>Agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करः|उत्कर
उत्करः See under उत्कॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्करः|उत्कर्कर
उत्कर्करः A kind of musical<BR>instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्ण|उत्कर्णः|उत्कर्ण्ण
उत्कर्ण a. Having the ears erect.<BR>--र्णः An erect ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कल|उत्कलं|उत्कलः
उत्कल a. Excessive, piteous;<BR>K. 306.<BR>--लः<BR>1 N. of a country, the<BR>modern Orissa, or the inhabitants<BR>of that country (pl.);<BR>जगन्नाथप्रांतदेश उत्कलः परिकीर्तितः; see आंड्र;<BR>उत्कलादर्शितपथः R. 4. 38.<BR>--2 A fowler,<BR>bird-catcher.<BR>--3 A porter (carrying<BR>a load with him).<BR>--4 A<BR>sub-division of Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कलित|उत्कलितः
उत्कलित a.<BR>1 Unbound loosened.<BR>--2 Regretting, sorry for.<BR>--3<BR>Opened, blossomed (as flowers).<BR>--4<BR>Rising, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कलाप
उत्कलाप a. Having the tail<BR>erect and expanded; R. 16. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कलापयति
उत्कलापयति Den. P.<BR>1 To ask<BR>(one) permission to go, take leave<BR>of: Pt. 5.<BR>--2 To cause the<BR>peacock to spread its plumage.<BR>--3 To<BR>cause (one) to be proud, produce<BR>conceit by an acknowledgment of<BR>merit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कलिका
उत्कलिका<BR>1 Anxiety in general,<BR>uneasiness; जाता नोत्कलिका<BR>Amaru. 78; K. 138, 205, 210, 234;<BR>Dk. 17, 20.<BR>--2 Longing for,<BR>regretting, missing anything or<BR>person.<BR>--3 Wanton sport,<BR>dalliance (हेला)<BR>--4 A bud.<BR>--5 A wave;<BR>वनावलीरुत्कलिकासहस्रं Śi. 3. 70;<BR>क्षुभितमुत्कलिकातरलं मनः ruffled by<BR>waves Māl. 3. 10 (where<BR>उत्कलिका also means anxiety); K. 161.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रायं a variety of<BR>prosecomposition abounding in<BR>compound words and hard letters;<BR>भवेदुत्कलिकाप्रायं समासाढ्यं दृढाक्षरं<BR>Cand. M. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कषणं|उत्कषण
उत्कषणं<BR>1 Tearing, pulling up.<BR>--2 Ploughing, drawing through<BR>(as a plough); सद्यः<BR>सीरोत्कषणसुरभि क्षेत्रमारुत्द्य मालं Me. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्काका
उत्काका A cow calving every<BR>year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्काशनं|उत्काशन
उत्काशनं Ordering,<BR>commanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कासः|उत्कास
उत्कासः, --सनं, उत्कासिका<BR>Hemming, clearing the throat of<BR>mucus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कासनं|उत्कासन
उत्कासः, --सनं, उत्कासिका<BR>Hemming, clearing the throat of<BR>mucus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कासिका
उत्कासः, --सनं, उत्कासिका<BR>Hemming, clearing the throat of<BR>mucus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0290-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीलित
उत्कीलित a. Nailed up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुंचिता|उत्कुञ्चिता
उत्कुंचिता, --का The plant<BR>Nigella Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुंचिका|उत्कुञ्चिका
उत्कुंचिता, --का The plant<BR>Nigella Indica.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुटं|उत्कुट
उत्कुटं [उन्नतः कुटो यत्र] Lying<BR>down or sleeping with the face<BR>(or head) upwards, stretching out<BR>on the back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुटक
उत्कुटक a. Stretched on the<BR>back with the face upwards.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आसनं a posture with the<BR>face upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुणः|उत्कुण
उत्कुणः<BR>1 A bug.<BR>--2 A louse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुल
उत्कुल a. [उत्क्रांतः कुलात्] Fallen<BR>from the family, disgracing or<BR>dishonouring one's family; यदि यया<BR>वदति क्षितिपस्तथा । त्वमसि किं<BR>पितुरुत्कुलया त्वया ॥ Ś. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूजः|उत्कूज
उत्कूजः The singing (of the<BR>cuckoo).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूटः|उत्कूट|उत्कूटं
उत्कूटः [उन्नतं कूटमस्य] A parasol<BR>or umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूर्दनं|उत्कूर्दन
उत्कूर्दनं Jumping up, springing<BR>upwards; ˚शक्तिर्नास्ति Pt. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूल
उत्कूल a. [उत्क्रांतः कूलात]<BR>1<BR>Going uphill (as rivers), (Ved.).<BR>--2<BR>Reaching the bank.<BR>--3 Overflowing<BR>the bank; K. 303.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कूलित
उत्कूलित a. Brought to the bank<BR>or shore, reaching the bank;<BR>प्रतिक्षणोत्कूलितशेवलाभाः Śi. 3. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृ
उत्कृ {c8c} A. To inform against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृतिः|उत्कृति
उत्कृतिः f. N. of a class of metres<BR>having 104 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृत्
उत्कृत् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To cut out or off,<BR>tear out or off; तत्मिन्रामशरोत्कृत्ते<BR>बले R. 12. 49; Ms. 11. 105;<BR>Y. 3. 259.<BR>--2 To cut to pieces, cut up,<BR>hack, butcher; उत्कृत्योत्कृत्य कृत्तिं<BR>Māl. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्तनं|उत्कर्तन|उत्कर्त्तन
उत्कर्तनं<BR>1 Cutting off, tearing out,<BR>cutting to pieces.<BR>--2 Rooting out,<BR>eradication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्
उत्कृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To draw or pull<BR>up, raise or lift up; उदकर्षि<BR>Śi. 13. 60; to draw or take out, extract,<BR>extricate; अंगदकोटिलग्नं प्रालंबमुत्कृष्य<BR>R. 6. 14.<BR>--2 To draw, attract;<BR>Ś. 17. 42.<BR>--3 To pull or put off.<BR>--4 To<BR>increase, enhance (opp. अपकृष्).<BR>--5<BR>To bend (as a bow).<BR>--6 To tear<BR>asunder. --Caus. To elevate, raise,<BR>increase. --pass.<BR>1 To be lifted,<BR>raised.<BR>--2 To rise, be supreme or<BR>eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्ष|उत्कर्षः
उत्कर्ष a.<BR>1 Superior, eminent.<BR>--2<BR>Much, abundant.<BR>--3 Exaggerated,<BR>boastful.<BR>--4 Attractive.<BR>--र्षः<BR>1<BR>Pulling off or upwards, drawing or<BR>pulling up.<BR>--2 Elevation, eminence,<BR>rise, prosperity; निनीषुः कुलमुत्कर्षं<BR>Ms. 4. 244, 9. 24.<BR>--3 Increase,<BR>abundance, excess; पचानामपि<BR>भूतानामुत्कर्षं पुपुषुर्गुणाः R. 4. 11.<BR>--4<BR>Excellence, highest merit, glory; उत्कर्षः<BR>स च धन्विनां यदिषवः सिध्यंति लक्ष्ये चले<BR>Ś. 2. 5.<BR>--5 Self conceit, boasting.<BR>--6 Joy, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्षक
उत्कर्षक a. Drawing upwards,<BR>raising, elevating, increasing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्षणं|उत्कर्षण
उत्कर्षणं<BR>1 Drawing upwards.<BR>--2<BR>Taking or pulling off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर्षिन्
उत्कर्षिन् a. Drawing or pulling up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्ट|उत्कृष्टं
उत्कृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Drawn up or out,<BR>raised, elevated.<BR>--2 Extracted.<BR>--3<BR>Excellent, eminent, superior, best,<BR>highest; Ms. 5. 163, 7. 126, 8. 281;<BR>बल˚ Pt. 3. 36 superior in strength;<BR>so ज्ञान˚, गुण˚ &c.<BR>--4 Much,<BR>excessive, very great, increased; जिह्वालौ<BR>ल्य˚ Pt. 1.<BR>--5 Tilled; ploughed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपाधिता state of high<BR>illusion.<BR>--भूमः a good soil.<BR>--वेदनं {1}<BR>marrying a man of a higher caste;<BR>Ms. 3. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कृष्टता
उत्कृष्टता, त्वं Excellence,<BR>eminence; greatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्वं|त्व|त्वः
उत्कृष्टता, त्वं Excellence,<BR>eminence; greatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कॄ
उत्कॄ {c6c} U.<BR>1 To scatter upwards,<BR>throw up, pile up or heap;<BR>रजानिस्तुरगोत्कीर्णैः R. 1. 42.<BR>--2 To dig up,<BR>excavate.<BR>--3 To engrave, carve,<BR>sculpture; उत्कीर्णा इव वासयष्टिषु<BR>निशानिद्रालसा बर्हिणः V. 3. 2; R. 4. 59;<BR>see उत्कीर्ण also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कर|उत्करः
उत्कर a. (--रा, री f.) [कॄ-अप्] That<BR>which piles or throws up or raises.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A heap, multitude;<BR>नखांशूत्कर Ki. 8. 5.<BR>--2 A pile, stack.<BR>--3 Rubbish, what is thrown up<BR>(मूषिकोत्कर) Mk. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करिका
उत्करिका A sort of sweetmeat<BR>made with milk, treacle, and ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्करीय
उत्करीय a. Belonging to a heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कारः|उत्कार
उत्कारः [कॄ-घञ् P. III. 3. 30]<BR>1<BR>Winnowing corn.<BR>--2 Piling up corn.<BR>--3 One who sows corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कारिका
उत्कारिका [कॄ-ण्वुल्] Poultice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्किर
उत्किर a. [कॄ-कर्तरि श] Carrying<BR>or bearing away, wafting, scattering<BR>upwards (at the end of comp.);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">Page0291-c+ 56</a>]<BR>पुष्परेणूत्किरैः R. 1. 38; निनाय<BR>सात्यंतहिमोत्किरानिलाः Ku. 5. 26; 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्ण|उत्कीर्ण्ण
उत्कीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Thrown or piled<BR>up, scattered.<BR>--2 Engraven, carved,<BR>sculptured; Māl. 5. 10; K. 17, 36,<BR>79, 106, 129, 133, 141, 186, 206;<BR>˚नामधेयं engraven with a name.<BR>--3<BR>Bored, perforated; घुण˚ Pt. 3. 139<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कॄत्
उत्कॄत् {c10c} P. To proclaim,<BR>celebrate, praise, extol; महिमानं यदुत्कीर्त्य<BR>R. 10. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्तनं|उत्कीर्तन|उत्कीर्त्तन
उत्कीर्तनं<BR>1 Crying out,<BR>proclaiming.<BR>--2 Praising, celebrating,<BR>extolling; S. D. 495.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कीर्तित|उत्कीर्त्तित
उत्कीर्तित p. p.<BR>1 Proclaimed,<BR>promulgated.<BR>--2 Praised, celebrated,<BR>renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोचः|उत्कोच
उत्कोचः [उत्कुच्-घञ्] A bribe<BR>(lit. bending one from the right<BR>path); उत्कोचमिव ददती K. 232,<BR>Dk. 155; Y. 1. 338.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोचक|उत्कोचकः
उत्कोचक a. Bribed.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>bribe.<BR>--2 The receiver of a bribe;<BR>Ms. 9. 258.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोटि
उत्कोटि a. Pointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कम्
उत्कम् {c1c} U., {c4c} P.<BR>1 To go up, step<BR>up, ascend.<BR>--2 To step beyond;<BR>उत्क्रांतशैशवौ R. 15. 33 past childhood.<BR>--3 To step out, go out or away,<BR>depart; ऊर्ध्वं प्राणा ह्युत्कामतिं<BR>Ms. 2. 120; Mv. 1.<BR>--4 To pass away, die.<BR>--5 To go or pass over, omit.<BR>--6 To<BR>disregard, not to notice, neglect;<BR>आर्षं प्रमाणमुत्क्रम्य, धर्ममुत्क्रग्य Mb.<BR>--7<BR>To transgress, violate; उत्क्रांतसीमा<BR>Dk. 101, 97. --Caus. (क्रामयति) To<BR>cause to go up or ascend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमः|उत्क्रम
उत्क्रमः<BR>1 Going up or out,<BR>departure.<BR>--2 Progressive increase.<BR>--3<BR>Going astray, deviation,<BR>transgression, violation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमणं|उत्क्रमण
उत्क्रमणं<BR>1 Going up or out,<BR>departure.<BR>--2 Ascent, soaring aloft.<BR>--3<BR>Surpassing, exceeding.<BR>--4 The<BR>flight or passage of the soul (out of<BR>the body), i. e. death (= प्राणोत्क्रमणं)<BR>Ms. 6. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रमणीय
उत्क्रमणीय pot. p. To be<BR>transgressed, to be given up or abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रांत|उत्क्रान्त
उत्क्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Gone forth or out,<BR>departed; उत्क्रांतमिवासुभिः K. 33;<BR>R. 7. 53.<BR>--2 Faded, effaced (as<BR>colour); R. 16. 17.<BR>--3 Gone over<BR>or beyond, passed, surpassed.<BR>--4<BR>Dead.<BR>--5 Trespassing, exceeding,<BR>surpassing (actively used).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0291-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रांतिः|उत्क्रान्ति|उत्क्रांति
उत्क्रांतिः f.<BR>1 Going up or out,<BR>departure.<BR>--2 The flight or passage<BR>of the soul (out of the body),<BR>death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रांतिन्|उत्क्रान्तिन्
उत्क्रांतिन् a. Passing away, gone,<BR>departed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रामः|उत्क्राम
उत्क्रामः<BR>1 Going out or up,<BR>departure.<BR>--2 Surpassing, excelling.<BR>--3<BR>Violation, transgression.<BR>--4<BR>Opposition, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कुश्
उत्कुश् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To cry out,<BR>exclaim, cry aloud.<BR>--2 To call out to;<BR>उदक्रोशत् स पांडवान् Mb.<BR>--3 To<BR>proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रुष्ट
उत्क्रुष्ट p. p. Crying out,<BR>exclaiming.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 Crying out, calling,<BR>exclaiming.<BR>--2 Loud speaking or<BR>conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्रोशः|उत्क्रोश
उत्क्रोशः<BR>1 Clamour, outcry, loud<BR>noise.<BR>--2 Proclamation.<BR>--3 An<BR>osprey (कुररी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कोदः
उत्कोदः Ved. Exultation, joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लिश्
उत्क्लिश् {c9c} P. To feel uneasy or<BR>distressed. --Caus.<BR>1 To excite,<BR>stir up, agitate, torment.<BR>--2 To<BR>expel, drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशः|उत्क्लेश
उत्क्लेशः<BR>1 Excitement,<BR>disquietude, agitation.<BR>--2 Disorder of the<BR>humours (of the body).<BR>--3 Sickness;<BR>particularly, sea sickness, nausea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशक|उत्क्लेशकः
उत्क्लेशक a. Causing the disorder<BR>of the humours.<BR>--कः A kind of<BR>poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशन
उत्क्लेशन, --शिन् a. Exciting,<BR>stirring up, producing disorder; as in<BR>कफ˚ exciting phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेशिन्
उत्क्लेशन, --शिन् a. Exciting,<BR>stirring up, producing disorder; as in<BR>कफ˚ exciting phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेदः|उत्क्लेद
उत्क्लेदः Becoming wet or moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्लेदिन्
उत्क्लेदिन् a.<BR>1 Wet.<BR>--2 Making wet<BR>or moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्
उत्क्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To throw or toss<BR>up, raise, set up, erect; उत्क्षिप्तगात्रः<BR>Śi. 12. 5, 8. 14; बलिमाकाश उत्क्षिपेत्<BR>Ms. 3. 90; Rs. 1. 22; so बाहुं, भ्रुवं<BR>&c.; R. 6. 14.<BR>--2 To throw away,<BR>reject, get rid of.<BR>--3 To emit, vomit<BR>up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्त|उत्क्षिप्तः
उत्क्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Thrown upwards,<BR>tossed, raised.<BR>--2 Held up,<BR>supported; R. 15. 83.<BR>--3 Seized or<BR>overcome with, distracted by, struck<BR>with; विस्मय˚ Ratn. 1; so लोभ˚,<BR>अनुराग˚.<BR>--4 Demolished, destroyed.<BR>--5 Thrown out, rejected, dismissed.<BR>--प्तः The thorn apple, the<BR>Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षिप्तिका
उत्क्षिप्तिका A crescent-shaped<BR>ornament worn in the upper part of<BR>the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेप|उत्क्षेपः
उत्क्षेप a. Throwing up, tossing.<BR>--पः<BR>1 Throwing or tossing up;<BR>पक्ष्मोत्क्षेप Me. 47.<BR>--2 That which is<BR>thrown or tossed up; बिंदूत्क्षेपान्<BR>पिपासुः M. 2. 13.<BR>--3 Sending,<BR>despatching.<BR>--4 Throwing away,<BR>rejecting.<BR>--5 Vomiting.<BR>--6 The<BR>region above the temples (dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपक|उत्क्षेपकः
उत्क्षेपक a. One who throws or<BR>tosses up, who or what elevates<BR>or raises; Y. 2. 274.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A stealer<BR>of clothes &c.;<BR>वस्त्राद्युत्क्षिपत्यपहरतीत्युत्क्षेपकः Mit.<BR>--2 One who sends or<BR>orders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्क्षेपणं|उत्क्षेपण
उत्क्षेपणं<BR>1 Throwing upwards,<BR>lifting or tossing up; अतिमात्रलोहिततलौ<BR>बाहू घटोत्क्षेपणात् Ś. 1. 30.<BR>--2<BR>Throwing upwards, regarded by the<BR>Vaiśeṣikas as one of the five<BR>karmans q. v.<BR>--3 Vomiting.<BR>--4<BR>Sending away, despatching.<BR>--5 A<BR>kind of basket for cleaning corn;<BR>a kind of stick for threshing corn.<BR>--6 A fan.<BR>--7 A measure of sixteen<BR>Paṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खचित
उत्खचित a. Intermixed,<BR>interwoven, set or inlaid with;<BR>कुसुमोत्खचितान् वलीभृतः R. 8. 53, 13. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खन्
उत्खन् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To dig up or out,<BR>excavate; उत्खातं निधिशंकया क्षितितलं<BR>Bh. 3. 4.<BR>--2 To tear up by the<BR>roots, eradicate; वंगानुत्खाय तरसा<BR>R. 4. 36, 33; 14. 73; 18. 22;<BR>Me. 52; Bk. 12. 5, 15. 55.<BR>--3<BR>To draw or tear out (eye &c.);<BR>Bk. 14. 32.<BR>--4 To draw or pull<BR>out; Śi. 5. 59, 18. 37; उत्खातखड्गः<BR>Ve. 3 unsheathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खात|उत्खातं
उत्खात p. p.<BR>1 Excavated, dug up.<BR>--2 Extracted, drawn out; उत्खातं<BR>परित्यागशल्यं U. 3.<BR>--3 Uprooted,<BR>plucked up by the roots (lit.);<BR>लीला˚ uprooted in sport<BR>U. 3. 16; Māl. 9. 34.<BR>--4 (fig.) (a)<BR>Eradicated, totally destroyed,<BR>annihilated; किमुत्खातं नंदवंशस्य<BR>Mu. 1; ˚लवणो मधुरेश्वरः प्राप्तः U. 7. (b)<BR>Deposed, deprived of power or<BR>authority; फलैः<BR>संवर्धयामासुरुत्खातप्रतिरोपिताः R. 4. 37 (where उत्खात<BR>means ‘uprooted’ also).<BR>--तं A hole,<BR>cavity, hollow, uneven ground;<BR>अनुत्खातस्तिमित not stopped by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">Page0292-c+ 55</a>]<BR>uneven ground; Ś. 7. 33.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केलिः f. digging out earth in sport<BR>(by means of horns, tusks &c.);<BR>उत्खातकेलिः शृंगाद्यैर्वप्रक्रीडा निगद्यते.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खातिन्
उत्खातिन् a. [उत्खात-इनि]<BR>1<BR>Uneven, having ups and downs,<BR>rugged (opp. सम), उत्खातिनी भूमिरिति<BR>मया रश्मिसंयमनाद्रथस्य मंदीकृतो वेगः<BR>Ś. 1.<BR>--2 Destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खला
उत्खला A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खिद्
उत्खिद् {c6c} P. To draw out,<BR>extract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्खेदः|उत्खेद
उत्खेदः Cutting out; drawing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त|उत्तं
उत्त See उंद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंसः|उत्तंस
उत्तंसः [उद् तंस् अच्]<BR>1 A crest,<BR>chaplet, an ornament worn on<BR>the crown of the head; उत्तं निहरत<BR>वारि मूर्धजेभ्यः Śi. 8. 57;<BR>सुधांशुकलितोत्तंसस्तापं हरतु वः शिवः Chandr. 5. 59,<BR>cf. कर्णोत्तंस.<BR>--2 An ear-ring;<BR>Māl. 5. 18; Bv. 2. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंसयति
उत्तंसयति Den. P.<BR>1 To cause<BR>to serve as a crest, to deck, adorn.<BR>--2 To tie or bind up (as hair);<BR>Ve. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंसित
उत्तंसित a.<BR>1 Having ear-rings.<BR>--2 Put or worn on the crest;<BR>Bh. 3. 129; अंजलिकिसलय˚ Dk. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तट
उत्तट a. [उत्क्रांतः तटं]<BR>Overflowing the bank; उत्तटा इव नदीरयाः<BR>स्थलीं R. 11. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तन्
उत्तन् {c8c} U.<BR>1 To stretch<BR>upwards or out.<BR>--2 To try to rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तान|उत्तानं
उत्तान a.<BR>1 Stretched out, spread<BR>out, expanded, dilated;<BR>उत्तानतारक्रस्य लोचनयुगलस्य K. 143; U. 3. 23.<BR>--2 (a) Lying on the back, with<BR>the face upwards, supine;<BR>Māl. 3; उत्तानोच्छूनमंडूकपाटितोदरसंनिभे<BR>K. P. 7; Y. 1. 248. (b) Upright,<BR>erect.<BR>--3 Open, turned upwards;<BR>उत्तानपाणिद्वयसंनिवेशात् Ku. 3. 45;<BR>˚रशिमषु Pt. 3. 150.<BR>--4 Open,<BR>unreserved, frank, candid;<BR>स्वभावोत्तानहृदयं Ś. 5 frank-minded.<BR>--5<BR>Elevated; Māl. 7.<BR>--6 Concave;<BR>having the mouth upwards.<BR>--7 Shallow.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मकं a particular<BR>posture in sitting.<BR>--पत्रकः a species<BR>of Ricinus (रक्तैरंड).<BR>--पद् f.<BR>vegetation, the whole creation of<BR>upwardgerminating plants (Sāy.).<BR>--पाद<BR>a. with extended legs (children).<BR>--(दः) {1} N. of a king, father of<BR>Dhruva. {2} the Supreme Spirit. ˚जः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">Page0293-a+ 56</a>]<BR>N. of Dhruva, the polar star.<BR>--शय a. sleeping supinely or on<BR>the back, lying with the face<BR>upwards; कदा उत्तानशयः पुत्रकः<BR>जनयिष्यति मे हृदयाह्लादं K. 62.<BR>--(यः, --या) a<BR>little child, suckling, infant.<BR>--शीवन्<BR>a. lying extended; stagnant.<BR>--हस्त<BR>a. having the hands stretched out<BR>in prayers.<BR>--(स्तौ) (du.) the two<BR>hands with the fingers stretched<BR>out and with the backs turned<BR>towards the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0292-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानकः|उत्तानक
उत्तानकः A species of the Cyperus<BR>grass (उच्चटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानिका
उत्तानिका N. of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तानित
उत्तानित a.<BR>1 Raised, up-lifted;<BR>K. 38, 209, 298.<BR>--2 Dilated,<BR>expanded; K. 82, 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तप्
उत्तप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To warm, make<BR>hot, heat thoroughly, scorch,<BR>burn, sear; उत्तप्तनाराचलीलां<BR>Śi. 11. 50; उत्तपति सुवर्णं सुवर्णकारः Mbh.<BR>melts; so चैत्रो मैत्रस्य पाणिमुत्तपति.<BR>(Used in the Atm. when used<BR>intransitively ‘to shine’, or when<BR>it has a limb of the body for its<BR>object; उत्तपमानः आतपः Bk. 8. 15<BR>scorching heat; Śi. 20. 40; उत्तपते<BR>पाणी Mbh.).<BR>--2 To pain, torment,<BR>torture by heat; कुसुप्तेषुरुत्तपति<BR>यद्विशिखैः Śi. 9. 67.<BR>--3 To excite, urge<BR>on, press hard. --Caus. To warm,<BR>heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तप्त|उत्तप्तं|उत्तप्तः
उत्तप्त p. p.<BR>1 Burnt, heated,<BR>seared, made red-hot. ˚कनक K. 43, 36;<BR>U. 5. 14.<BR>--2 Bathed, washed.<BR>--3<BR>Anxious.<BR>--4 Enraged, inflamed, fired;<BR>Ve. 2.<BR>--प्तं<BR>1 Dried flesh.<BR>--2 Great<BR>heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तापः|उत्ताप
उत्तापः<BR>1 Great heat,<BR>inflammation.<BR>--2 Affliction, torment, distress.<BR>--3 Excitement, passion; प्रत्यूहः<BR>सर्वसिद्धीनामुत्तापः प्रथमः किल H. 3. 45.<BR>--4 Anxiety, ardour.<BR>--5 Energy,<BR>effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तापित
उत्तापित a.<BR>1 Heated, made hot.<BR>--2 Tormented, distressed.<BR>--3<BR>Excited, urged, roused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम्
उत्तम् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be afflicted or<BR>distressed, lose heart, faint.<BR>--2<BR>To be uneasy or impatient, be<BR>anxious; हृदय मा उत्ताम्य Ś. 1; K. 85,<BR>231, 268, 275; Māl. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमनं
उत्तमनं Losing heart, impatience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तम|उत्तमः
उत्तम a. [उद्-तमप्]<BR>1 Best,<BR>excellent (oft. in comp.); द्विजोत्तमः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-b" target="_blank">Page0293-b+ 57</a>]<BR>the best of Brāhmaṇas; so सुर˚, नर˚<BR>&c.; प्रायेणाधममध्यमोत्तमगुणः संसर्गतो<BR>जायते Bh. 2. 67.<BR>--2 Foremost,<BR>uppermost, highest (opp. हीन, जघन्य).<BR>--3<BR>Most elevated, chief, principal.<BR>--4<BR>Greatest, first; Ms. 2. 249.<BR>--मः<BR>1<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 The last person<BR>(= first person according to English<BR>phraseology).<BR>--मा<BR>1 An excellent<BR>woman.<BR>--2 A kind of pustule or<BR>pimple.<BR>--3 The plant Asclepias<BR>Rosea Roxb.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं ‘the<BR>best limb ‘of the body’, the head;<BR>कश्चिद् द्विषत्खड्गहृतोत्तमांगः R. 7. 51;<BR>Ms. 1. 93, 8. 300; Ku. 7. 41;<BR>Bg. 11. 27.<BR>--अधम a. high and low ˚मध्यम<BR>good, middling, and bad; high, low,<BR>and middling; (the order is often<BR>reversed); cf. Pt. 1. 210.<BR>--अंभस्<BR>n. a sort of satisfaction<BR>(acquiescence) in Sān. phil.<BR>--अरणी the<BR>plant Asparagus Racemosus (इंदीवरी).<BR>--अर्धः {1} the best half. {2} the<BR>last half or part.<BR>--अर्ध्य a. pertaining<BR>to the best half.<BR>--अहः the last or<BR>latest day; a fine or lucky day.<BR>--उपपद a. one to whom the best<BR>term is applicable, best, excellent.<BR>--ऋणः, --ऋणिकः (उंत्तमर्णः) a<BR>creditor (opp. अधमर्णः) धारेरुत्तमर्णः<BR>P. I. 4. 35; Ms. 8. 47, 50; Y. 2. 42.<BR>--ओजस् a. of excellent valour.<BR>--गंधाढ्य<BR>a. possessing copiously the most<BR>delicious fragrance.<BR>--गुण a. of the best<BR>qualities, best, highest; Mu. 2. 17.<BR>--पदं a high office.<BR>--पु(पू)रुषः<BR>{1} the last person in verbal<BR>conjugation; (=first person according<BR>to English phraseology; in Sanskrit<BR>verbs are conjugated by putting the<BR>English 1st person last and 3rd<BR>person first). {2} the Supreme<BR>Spirit. {3} an excellent man.<BR>--लाभः<BR>an excellent profit.<BR>--वेशः N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--शाखः a tree having<BR>excellent branches.<BR>--श्लोक a. of<BR>excellent fame, illustrious, glorious,<BR>well-known, famous.<BR>--संग्रहः (˚स्त्री˚)<BR>intriguing with another man's<BR>wife, i. e. speaking with her<BR>privately, looking amorously at her &c.<BR>--साहसः, --सं {1} the highest (of the<BR>fixed) pecuniary punishments; a<BR>fine of 1000 (or according to some<BR>80,000) paṇas; Ms. 9. 240;<BR>Y. 1. 365; पणानां द्वे शते सार्धे प्रथमः साहसः स्मृतः ।<BR>मध्यमः पंचविज्ञेयः सहस्रं त्वेष चोत्तमः ॥.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-c" target="_blank">Page0293-c+ 55</a>]<BR>Capital punishment, banishment,<BR>confiscation, and mutilation are also<BR>regarded as forms of this<BR>punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमता
उत्तमता --त्वं<BR>1 Excellence.<BR>--2<BR>Goodness, good quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमत्वं|उत्तमत्व
उत्तमता --त्वं<BR>1 Excellence.<BR>--2<BR>Goodness, good quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमाय्य
उत्तमाय्य a. Ved. Made excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तमीय
उत्तमीय a. Uppermost, highest,<BR>best, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंभ्|उत्तम्भ्
उत्तंभ् {c5c} {c9c} P. [उद्-स्तंभ्] To<BR>stay, prop, support, hold up;<BR>K. 281, Ve. 6;<BR>स्कंधोत्तंभिततीर्थवारिकलशाः Ve. 6; Śi. 4. 25. --Caus.<BR>1 To increase, heighten, rouse;<BR>Ki. 2. 48.<BR>--2 To bind up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंभः|उत्तम्भ|उत्तंभ|उत्तम्भः
उत्तंभः, --भनं<BR>1 Upholding,<BR>propping, supporting; भुवनोत्तंभनस्तंभान्<BR>K. 260; Śi. 18. 46.<BR>--2 A prop,<BR>stay, support.<BR>--3 Stopping, ar,<BR>resting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तंभनं|उत्तम्भन|उत्तंभन
उत्तंभः, --भनं<BR>1 Upholding,<BR>propping, supporting; भुवनोत्तंभनस्तंभान्<BR>K. 260; Śi. 18. 46.<BR>--2 A prop,<BR>stay, support.<BR>--3 Stopping, ar,<BR>resting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तर|उत्तरं|उत्तरः
उत्तर a. [उद्-तरप्]<BR>1 Being or<BR>produced in the north, northern<BR>(declined like a pronoun).<BR>--2<BR>Upper, higher (opp. अधर);<BR>उत्तरेअधरे दंताः Śat. Br.; अवनतोत्तरकायं<BR>R. 9. 60; P. II. 2. 1.<BR>--3 (a)<BR>Later-latter, following, subsequent (opp.<BR>पूर्व); पूर्वमेघः, उत्तरमेघः, ˚भीमांसा;<BR>उत्तरार्धः &c.; ˚रामचरितं later<BR>adventures of Rāma U. 1. 2; पूर्वः-उत्तरः<BR>former-latter H. 1. 9; Ms. 2. 136. (b)<BR>Future, concluding; ˚कालः subsequent<BR>time; ˚फलं; ˚वचनं a reply.<BR>--4 Left<BR>(opp. दक्षिण).<BR>--5 Superior, chief,<BR>excellent; dominant, powerful.<BR>--6<BR>Exceeding, transgressing, beyond;<BR>तर्कोत्तरां Mv. 2. 6.<BR>--7 More, more<BR>than (generally as the last member<BR>of a comp. with numerals);<BR>षडुत्तरा विंशतिः 26; अष्टोत्तरं शतं 108.<BR>--8<BR>Accompanied or attended with, full<BR>of, consisting chiefly of, followed<BR>by (at the end of comp); राज्ञां तु<BR>चरितार्थता दुःखोत्तरैव Ś. 5; चषकोत्तरा<BR>R. 7. 49; अस्रोत्तरमीक्षितां Ku. 5. 61;<BR>उत्सवोत्तरो मंगलविधिः Dk. 39, 166;<BR>K. 311; H. 1. 150; प्रवाल˚ पुष्पशय्ये<BR>R. 6. 50 over spread with; धर्मोत्तरं<BR>13. 7 rich in; 18. 7; कंप˚ 13. 28;<BR>17. 12; 19. 23.<BR>--9 To be crossed<BR>over.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Future time, futurity.<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 N. of Śiva.<BR>--रा<BR>1 The north; अस्त्युत्तरस्यां दिशि<BR>देवतात्मा Ku. 1. 1.<BR>--2 A lunar<BR>mansion.<BR>--3 N. of the daughter of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0294-a" target="_blank">Page0294-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Virāṭa and wife of Abhimanyu.<BR>--रं<BR>1 An answer, reply; प्रचक्रमे च<BR>प्रतिवक्तुमुत्तरं R. 3. 47; उत्तरादुत्तरं<BR>वाक्यं वदतां संप्रजायते Pt. 1. 60 a<BR>reply is suggested to a reply.<BR>--2<BR>(In law) Defence, a rejoinder.<BR>--3 The last part or following<BR>member of a compound.<BR>--4 (In Mīm.)<BR>The fourth member of an अधिकरण<BR>q. v.; the answer.<BR>--5 The upper<BR>surface or cover.<BR>--6 Conclusion.<BR>--7<BR>Remainder, rest, what followed or<BR>took place next; U. 3. 26.<BR>--8<BR>Superiority, excellence.<BR>--9 Result, the<BR>chief or prevalent result or<BR>characteristic.<BR>--10 Excess, over and<BR>above; see above (उत्तर a. 8).<BR>--11<BR>Remainder, difference (in arith.).<BR>--रं<BR>ind.<BR>1 Above.<BR>--2 Afterwards, after;<BR>तत उत्तरं, इत उत्तरं &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधर<BR>a. higher and lower (fig. also).<BR>(--रौ du.) the upper and under lip,<BR>the two lips; पुनर्विवक्षुः स्फुरितोत्तराधरः<BR>Ku. 5. 83; (स्फरणभूयिष्ठोऽधरो यस्य Malli.).<BR>--अधिकारः, --रिता, --त्वं right to<BR>property, heirship, inheritance.<BR>--अधिकारिन् m. an heir or claimant<BR>(subsequent to the death of the original<BR>owner).<BR>--अपरा north-west.<BR>--अयनं<BR>(˚यणं न being changed to ण) {1} the<BR>progress of the sun to the north (of<BR>the equator); Bg. 8. 24. {2} the<BR>period or time of the summer<BR>solstice.<BR>--अरणिः, --णी f. the upper<BR>अरणि (which by cutting becomes<BR>the प्रमंथ or churner).<BR>--अर्थ a. for<BR>the sake of what follows.<BR>--अर्धं {1}<BR>the upper part of the body. {2} the<BR>northern part. {3} the latter half<BR>(opp. पूर्वार्ध). {4} the further end.<BR>--अर्ध्य a. being on the northern<BR>side.<BR>--अहः the following day.<BR>--आभासः a false reply, an<BR>indirect, evasive, or prevaricating<BR>reply. ˚ता, --त्वं the semblance of a<BR>reply without reality.<BR>--आशा the<BR>northern direction. ˚अधिपतिः, --पतिः<BR>the regent of the northern direction,<BR>an epithet of Kubera.<BR>--आषाढा the<BR>21st lunar mansion consisting of<BR>three stars.<BR>--आसंगः {1} an upper<BR>garment; कृतोत्तरासंगं K. 43;<BR>Śi. 2. 19; Ku. 5. 16. {2} contact with<BR>the north.<BR>--इतर a. other than उत्तर<BR>i. e. southern.<BR>--(रा) the southern<BR>direction.<BR>--उत्तर a. [उत्तरस्मादुत्तरः]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0294-b" target="_blank">Page0294-b+ 56</a>]<BR>{1} more and more, higher and<BR>higher, further and further. {2}<BR>successive, ever increasing; ˚स्नेहेन दृष्टः<BR>Pt. 1; Y. 2. 136.<BR>--(रं) {1} a reply<BR>to an answer, reply on reply;<BR>अलमुत्तरोत्तरेण Mu. 3. {2} conversation,<BR>a rejoinder. {3} excess, exceeding<BR>quantity or degree. {4} succession,<BR>gradation, sequence. {5} descending.<BR>--(रं) ind. higher and higher, in<BR>constant continuation, more and<BR>more; उत्तरोत्तरमुत्कर्षः K. P. 10;<BR>उत्तरोत्तरं वर्धते H. 1.<BR>--उत्तरिन् a. {1}<BR>ever-increasing. {2} one following<BR>the other.<BR>--ओष्ठः the upper lip (उ<BR>त्तरो-रौ-ष्ठः).<BR>--कांडं the seventh book<BR>of the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>--कायः the upper<BR>part of the body; R. 9. 60.<BR>--कालः<BR>{1} future time. {2} time calculated<BR>from one full moon to another.<BR>--कुरु (m. pl.) one of the nine<BR>divisions of the world, the country of<BR>the northern Kurus (said to be<BR>a country of eternal beatitude).<BR>--कोसलाः (m. pl.) the northern<BR>Kosalas; पितुरनंतरमुत्तरकोसलान् R. 9. 1.<BR>--कोशला the city of Ayodhyā;<BR>यदुपतेः क्व गता मथुरा पुरी रघुपतेः क्व<BR>गतोत्तरकोशला ॥ Udb.<BR>--क्रिया funeral<BR>rites, obsequies.<BR>--खंडं the last<BR>section or book.<BR>--खंडनं refutation.<BR>--ग्रंथः supplement to a work.<BR>--छदः<BR>a bed-covering, covering (in<BR>general); R. 5. 65, 17. 21;<BR>नागचर्मोत्तरच्छदः Mb.<BR>--ज a. born<BR>subsequently or afterwards; Y. 1. 59.<BR>--ज्या the versed sine of an arc<BR>(Wilson); the second half of the<BR>chord halved by the versed sine<BR>(B. and R.).<BR>--ज्योतिषाः (m. pl.)<BR>the northern Jyotiṣas.<BR>--तंत्रं N.<BR>of a supplementary section in the<BR>medical work of Suśruta.<BR>--दायक<BR>a. replying, disobedient, pert,<BR>impertinent; H. 2. 121.<BR>--दिश् f. the<BR>north. ˚ईशः, --पालः {1} Kubera, the<BR>regent of the north. {2} the planet<BR>बुध. ˚बलिन् {1} the planet Venus.<BR>{2} the moon.<BR>--देशः the country<BR>towards the north.<BR>--धेय a. to be<BR>done subsequently.<BR>--पक्षः {1} the<BR>northern wing or side. {2} the<BR>dark half of a lunar month. {3} the<BR>second part of an argument, i. e. a<BR>reply, the reason pro. (opp. पूर्वपक्ष);<BR>प्रापयन् पवनव्याधेर्गिरमुत्तरपक्षताम्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0294-c" target="_blank">Page0294-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Śi. 2. 15. {4} a demonstrated truth or<BR>conclusion {5} the minor proposition in<BR>a syllogism. {6} (in Mīm.) the fifth<BR>member of an Adhikaraṇa q. v.<BR>--पटः {1} an upper garment. {2} a<BR>bed-covering (उत्तरच्छदः).<BR>--पथः<BR>the northern way, way leading to<BR>the north.<BR>--पथिक a. travelling in<BR>the northern country.<BR>--पदं {1} the<BR>last member of a compound. {2} a<BR>word that can be compounded with<BR>another.<BR>--पदिक, पदकीय a. relating<BR>to, studying, or knowing the last<BR>word or term.<BR>--पश्चार्धः the<BR>northwestern half.<BR>--पश्चिम a.<BR>northwestern.<BR>--(मः) the north-western<BR>country.<BR>--(मा) [उत्तरस्याः पश्चिमायाश्च<BR>दिशोंतरालं] the north-west.<BR>--पादः<BR>the second division of a legal<BR>plaint, that part which relates to<BR>the reply or defence; पूर्वपक्षः स्मृतः<BR>पादो द्वितीयश्चोत्तरः स्मृतः । क्रियापादस्तृतीयः<BR>स्याच्चतुर्योनिर्णयः स्मृतः ॥<BR>--पुरस्तात् ind.<BR>northeastward (with gen.).<BR>--पुरुषः<BR>= उत्तमपुरुषः q. v.<BR>--पूर्व a.<BR>northeastern.<BR>--(र्वा) the northeast.<BR>--प्रच्छदः a coverlid, quilt.<BR>--प्रत्युत्तरं<BR>{1} a dispute, debate, a rejoinder,<BR>retort. {2} the pleadings in a<BR>lawsuit.<BR>--फ (फा) ल्गुनी the twelfth<BR>lunar mansion consisting of two<BR>stars (having the figure of a bed).<BR>--भाद्रपद्-दा the 26th lunar mansion<BR>consisting of two stars (figured<BR>by a couch).<BR>--मंद्रा a loud but slow<BR>manner of singing.<BR>--मात्रं a mere<BR>reply.<BR>--मीमांसा the later Mīmāṃsā,<BR>the Vedānta philosophy, an<BR>inquiry into the nature of Brahma<BR>or Jñāna Kāṇḍa (distinguished<BR>from मांमांसा proper which is<BR>usually called पूर्वमीमांसा).<BR>--रहित a.<BR>without a reply.<BR>--रामचरितं-त्रं N. of a<BR>celebrated drama by Bhavabhūti,<BR>which describes the later life of<BR>Rāma.<BR>--लक्षणं the indication of an<BR>(actual) reply.<BR>--लोमन् a. having<BR>the hair turned upwards.<BR>--वयसं,<BR>--स् n. old age, the declining period<BR>of life.<BR>--वस्तिः a kind of small<BR>syringe.<BR>--वस्त्रं, --वासस् n. an upper<BR>garment, mantle, cloak.<BR>--वादिन् m. {1}<BR>a defendant, respondent; Y. 2. 17.<BR>{2} one whose claims are of later<BR>date than another's.<BR>--वेदिः {1} the<BR>northern altar made for the sacred<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">Page0295-a+ 56</a>]<BR>fire. {2} N. of a Tīrtha near the<BR>कुरुक्षेत्र.<BR>--सक्यं the left thigh.<BR>--संज्ञित a. denoted or named in reply<BR>(as a witness).<BR>--(तः)<BR>hearsay-witness.<BR>--साक्षिन् m. {1} a witness for<BR>the defence. {2} a witness deposing<BR>to facts from the reports of others.<BR>--साधक a. {1} finishing what<BR>remains or follows, assisting at a<BR>ceremony. {2} who or what proves<BR>a reply.<BR>--(कः) an assistant, helper.<BR>--हनुः Ved. the upper jaw bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0293-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरंगं|उत्तरङ्ग|उत्तरंग|उत्तरङ्गं
उत्तरंगं [उत्तरमंगं शकंध्वा˚ गण] A<BR>wooden arch surmounting the<BR>doorframe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरतर
उत्तरतर a. Still further, or higher,<BR>remote, distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरतः
उत्तरतः, --रात् ind.<BR>1 From the north;<BR>to the north.<BR>--2 To the left (opp.<BR>दक्षिणतः).<BR>--3 At the top, above.<BR>--4 Behind.<BR>--5 Afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरात्
उत्तरतः, --रात् ind.<BR>1 From the north;<BR>to the north.<BR>--2 To the left (opp.<BR>दक्षिणतः).<BR>--3 At the top, above.<BR>--4 Behind.<BR>--5 Afterwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरत्र
उत्तरत्र ind.<BR>1 Subsequently, later<BR>or further on, below (in a work),<BR>in the sequel.<BR>--2 In the second<BR>case (opp. पूर्वत्र in the first case).<BR>--3 Northward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तराहि
उत्तराहि ind. [उत्तर-आहि]<BR>Northerly to the north of (with abl.);<BR>Bk. 8. 107.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरिन्
उत्तरिन् a. Superior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरीयं|उत्तरीय
उत्तरीयं, --यकं [उत्तर-छ वा-कप्] An<BR>upper garment; R. 16. 17, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरीयकं|उत्तरीयक
उत्तरीयं, --यकं [उत्तर-छ वा-कप्] An<BR>upper garment; R. 16. 17, 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेण
उत्तरेण ind. [उत्तर एनप्] (With<BR>gen., acc. or at the end of a comp.)<BR>Northward, on the north side of;<BR>तत्रागारं धनपतिगृहानुत्तरेणास्मदीयं<BR>Me. 75. v. l., K. 120; निषधस्योत्तरेण तु<BR>V. P., Māl. 9. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरेद्युः
उत्तरेद्युः ind. On a subsequent<BR>day, on the day following, to-morrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरंग|उत्तरङ्ग|उत्तरंगं|उत्तरङ्गं
उत्तरंग a.<BR>1 Ruffled or washed<BR>by waves, inundated; trembling,<BR>tremulous; Mu. 6. 3.<BR>--2 With<BR>surging waves; R. 7. 36; Ku. 3. 48.<BR>--3 Bouncing; Dk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरंगि
उत्तरंगि a. Heaving, panting;<BR>Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तर्जनं|उत्तर्जन
उत्तर्जनं [उच्चैस्तर्जनं] Violent<BR>threatening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तलित
उत्तलित Thrown or cast<BR>upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तान|उत्तानं
उत्तान see under उत्तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्ताल|उत्तालः
उत्ताल a.<BR>1 Great, strong;<BR>अनुत्तालतालवृंतवात K. 251.<BR>--2 (a) Violent,<BR>loud (as sound); Māl. 1;<BR>Śi. 12. 31. (b) Roaring, gusty (wind);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">Page0295-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Māl. 5. 4.<BR>--3 Formidable, terrific, fierce;<BR>उत्तालास्त इमे गभीरपयसः पुण्याः<BR>सरित्संगमाः U. 2. 30; ˚तुमुल U. 6; Śi. 20. 68;<BR>Māl. 5. 11, 23.<BR>--4 Huge, of<BR>monstrous shape; ˚ताडका Mv. 1. 37.<BR>--5 Arduous, difficult.<BR>--6 Manifest;<BR>distinctly visible; Śi. 18. 54.<BR>--7<BR>Speedy, swift.<BR>--8 Best, excellent;<BR>Śi. 12. 31.<BR>--9 Elevated, lofty, tall;<BR>Śi. 3. 80.<BR>--लः An ape.<BR>--लं A<BR>particular number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तिज्
उत्तिज् Caus. P. To excite,<BR>stimulate, instigate, stir up,<BR>animate, provoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजक
उत्तेजक a.<BR>1 Instigating, stirring<BR>up.<BR>--2 Exciting, stimulating;<BR>क्षुध्,˚ काम˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजनं|उत्तेजन
उत्तेजनं, --ना<BR>1 Excitement,<BR>instigation, animating, stirring up;<BR>˚समथः श्लोकैः Mu. 4; Mv. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Urging on, driving.<BR>--3 Sending,<BR>despatching.<BR>--4 Whetting,<BR>sharpening, furbishing, polishing<BR>(weapons &c.); Śi. 3. 6.<BR>--5 An exciting<BR>speech.<BR>--6 An inducement,<BR>incentive, stimulant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजना
उत्तेजनं, --ना<BR>1 Excitement,<BR>instigation, animating, stirring up;<BR>˚समथः श्लोकैः Mu. 4; Mv. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Urging on, driving.<BR>--3 Sending,<BR>despatching.<BR>--4 Whetting,<BR>sharpening, furbishing, polishing<BR>(weapons &c.); Śi. 3. 6.<BR>--5 An exciting<BR>speech.<BR>--6 An inducement,<BR>incentive, stimulant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेजित|उत्तेजितं
उत्तेजित p. p.<BR>1 Instigated, excited.<BR>--2 Animated.<BR>--3 Sent<BR>--4<BR>Sharpened, polished &c.<BR>--तं<BR>1 An<BR>inducement.<BR>--2 One of the five paces<BR>of a horse, sidling; moderate<BR>velocity in a horse's pace; उत्तेजितं मध्यवेगं<BR>योजनं श्लथवल्गया ।.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुंग|उत्तुङ्ग|उत्तुङ्गः
उत्तुंग^1 a.<BR>1 Lofty, high, tall;<BR>करप्रचेयामुत्तुगः प्रभुशक्तिं प्रथीयसीं<BR>Śi. 2. 89; ˚हेमपीठानि 2. 5.<BR>--2 Swollen,<BR>increased (as a stream).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: (checked by the source of the quotation - ed. 1815).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुंडितं|उत्तुण्डित
उत्तुंडितं The head of a thorn<BR>(which enters the skin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुल्
उत्तुल् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To raise up (by<BR>means of a balance).<BR>--2 To raise,<BR>erect, lift up.<BR>--3 To weigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तोलनं|उत्तोलन
उत्तोलनं Lifting up, raising (by<BR>means of a balance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तुषः|उत्तुष
उत्तुषः [उद्गतः तुषोऽस्मात्] ‘Freed<BR>from husks’, fried grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तॄ
उत्तॄ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To pass out of (water),<BR>disembark, come out of; Śi. 8. 63,<BR>64; to get or jump out of, rise<BR>from; 12. 31; पल्वलोत्तीर्ण R. 2. 17;<BR>अभिषेकोत्तीर्णाय, स्नानोत्तीर्णः Ś. 4.<BR>--2<BR>To cross, pass or get over (a river<BR>&c.); उदतारिषुरंभोधिं Bk. 15. 33, 10;<BR>शोकसागरमुत्तीर्य Ve. 3; तेनोत्तीर्य पथा<BR>R. 12. 71, 16. 33; Me. 47.<BR>--3<BR>To vanquish, overcome, get out of,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">Page0295-c+ 56</a>]<BR>escape from (a difficulty); व्यसनमह<BR>र्णवादुत्तीर्णं Mk. 10. 49.<BR>--4 To descend,<BR>alight; तद्गृहे उत्तीर्णौ Vet.<BR>--5 To give<BR>up, leave, quit.<BR>--6 To raise,<BR>strengthen, increase. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to<BR>come out, deliver, lift up, rescue;<BR>Śi. 11. 44; Dk. 30, 77.<BR>--2 To take<BR>down, to take off (as ornaments);<BR>let down, place down.<BR>--3 To<BR>cause to cross over, convey,<BR>transport across.<BR>--4 To land,<BR>disembark.<BR>--5 To vomit up, emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तर|उत्तरं|उत्तरः
उत्तर a.<BR>1 Crossing over.<BR>--2 To be<BR>crossed over, as in दुरुत्तर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तरण|उत्तरणं
उत्तरण a. Coming out of,<BR>crossing.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Coming forth or out of<BR>(water &c.).<BR>--2 Landing,<BR>disembarking.<BR>--3 Crossing, passing<BR>over; संसारसमुद्र˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तार|उत्तारः
उत्तार a.<BR>1 Surpassing others,<BR>exceilent, pre-eminent.<BR>--2 Having<BR>the eye balls turned up (as eyes).<BR>--रः<BR>1 Transporting over,<BR>conveying.<BR>--2 Fording, crossing;<BR>सुखोत्तारतां K. 326.<BR>--3 Landing,<BR>disembarking.<BR>--4 Delivering, rescuing.<BR>--5 Getting rid of.<BR>--6 Vomiting.<BR>--7 Instability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारकः|उत्तारक
उत्तारकः<BR>1 A deliverer, saviour.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारण|उत्तारणः
उत्तारण a. Transporting or<BR>bringing over, conveying; rescuing,<BR>delivering.<BR>--णः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--णं<BR>1 The act of landing, delivering or<BR>rescuing.<BR>--2 Transportation,<BR>conveying across.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तारिन्
उत्तारिन्<BR>1 Transporting over.<BR>--2<BR>Unsteady, unstable, changeable.<BR>--3 Sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तार्य|उत्तार्य्य
उत्तार्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be vomited;<BR>Ms. 11. 161.<BR>--2 To be made to<BR>land.<BR>--3 To be crossed over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तीर्ण|उत्तीर्णं|उत्तीर्ण्ण
उत्तीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Landed, crossed,<BR>passed over.<BR>--2 Rescued, delivered.<BR>--3 Released from obligation.<BR>--4 One<BR>who has finished his course of<BR>studies; experienced, clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तेरितं|उत्तेरित
उत्तेरितं One of the five paces<BR>of a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्तोरण
उत्तोरण a. [उन्नतं तोरणमत्र]<BR>Adorned with raised or upright arches;<BR>उत्तोरणं राजपथं प्रपेदे Ku. 7. 63;<BR>R. 14. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्यक्त|उत्त्यक्तः
उत्त्यक्त a.<BR>1 Abandoned, left.<BR>--2 Thrown, tossed.<BR>--3 Free from<BR>passion or attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0295-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्यागः|उत्त्याग
उत्त्यागः<BR>1 Abandonment, leaving.<BR>--2 Throwing, throwing up, tossing.<BR>--3 Renunciation of all worldly<BR>attachments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रस्
उत्त्रस् {c1c} {c4c} P. To be afraid.<BR>--Caus. To frighten, alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रासः|उत्रास
उत्त्रासः Extreme fear, terror,<BR>alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्त्रिपदं|उत्रिपद
उत्त्रिपदं An upright tripod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्था
उत्था {c1c} P. [उद्-स्था]<BR>1 To get<BR>up, stand, rise, raise oneself;<BR>उत्तिष्ठेत्प्रथमं चास्य Ms. 2. 194; R. 9. 59;<BR>Śi. 9. 39.<BR>--2 To get up from, leave,<BR>give up or cease from;<BR>अनशनादुत्तिष्ठति Pt. 4.<BR>--3 To rise, come up (as<BR>the sun &c.).<BR>--4 To rebound (as a<BR>ball); कराभिघातोत्थितकन्दुकेयं<BR>R. 16. 83.<BR>--5 To come forth, arise, spring<BR>or originate from, accrue from; ग्रा<BR>माच्छतमुत्तिष्ठति Mbh; यदुत्तिष्ठति<BR>वर्णेभ्यो नृपाण क्षयितत्फलं Ś. 2. 13;<BR>अन्यदमृतादुत्थितम् K. 136; उदतिष्ठन् प्रशंसावाचः<BR>Dk. 49 shouts of applause burst forth<BR>(were heard); N. 22. 44.<BR>--6 To rise,<BR>increase in strength or power, grow,<BR>(as an enemy, disease &c.); (Atm.)<BR>उत्तिष्ठमानस्तु परो नोपेक्ष्यः पथ्यमिच्छता<BR>Śi. 2. 10 (= Pt. 1. 234.)<BR>--7<BR>To become animated, rise (from<BR>the dead); मृतेत्थिता Ku. 7. 4.<BR>--8<BR>To be active or brave, rise up;<BR>हृदयदौर्बल्यं त्यक्त्वोत्तिष्ठ Bg. 2. 3, 37;<BR>Mv. 2; Pt. 3. 21.<BR>--9 To make<BR>efforts; take pains, strive, try;<BR>उत्तिष्ठमानं मित्रार्थे कस्त्वां न बहु मन्यते<BR>Bk. 8. 12; 20. 18; Mv. 4. 6;<BR>मुकावुत्तिष्ठते जनः Ki. 11. 13; उदस्थित क्रतौ<BR>Śi. 14. 17.<BR>--10 To excel, surpass. --Caus.<BR>(उत्थापयति)<BR>1 To cause to stand up,<BR>raise, lift up: उत्थाप्यते ग्रावा<BR>H. 3. 42; R. 14. 59; raise or throw<BR>up (as dust); R. 7. 39.<BR>--2 To<BR>instigate, excite, rouse to action;<BR>त्वामुत्थापयति द्वयं Śi. 2. 57, 102;<BR>Kām. 5. 40; H. 3. 92; Dk. 107.<BR>--3 To arouse, awaken, raise to<BR>life, make alive; प्राणो हीदं<BR>सर्वमुत्थापयति Śat. Br.<BR>--4 To support, feed,<BR>aid; अत्र परिकरोत्थापितोऽ<BR>र्थांतरन्यासालंकारः Malli. on Ki. 8. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थ|उत्थः
उत्थ a. [उद्-स्था-क] (Used only<BR>at the end of comp.)<BR>1 Born or<BR>produced from, arising, springing<BR>up, or originating from; दरीमुखोत्थेन<BR>समीरणेन Ku. 1. 8; 6. 59; R. 12. 82;<BR>आनंदोत्थं नयनसलिलं Me. v. l.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-b" target="_blank">Page0296-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Pt. 1. 274.<BR>--2 Standing up, coming up<BR>or forth.<BR>--त्थः Arising, coming<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थातृ
उत्थातृ a. Ved.<BR>1 One who rises<BR>or gets up.<BR>--2 Resolving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थान|उत्थानं
उत्थान a. Causing to arise or<BR>spring up.<BR>--नं<BR>1 The act of rising or<BR>standing up, getting up; शनैर्यष्ट्युत्थानं<BR>Bh. 3. 9.<BR>--2 Rising (as of<BR>luminaries); इंदुं नवोत्थानमिवेंदुमत्यै R. 6. 31<BR>newly risen.<BR>--3 Rise, origin.<BR>--4<BR>Resurrection.<BR>--5 (a) Effort, exertion,<BR>activity; मेदश्छेदकृशोदरं लघु<BR>भवत्युत्थानयोग्यं वपुः Ś. 2. 5; ˚शीलः Dk. 153<BR>disposed to work; Mv. 6. 23; यद्युत्थानं<BR>भवेत्सह Ms. 9. 215, effort (for money),<BR>acquisition of property. (b) Manly<BR>exertion, manhood.<BR>--6 Energy.<BR>--7<BR>Joy, pleasure.<BR>--8 War, battle.<BR>--9 An<BR>army.<BR>--10 Evacuating (by stool &c.).<BR>--11 A book.<BR>--12 A court yard.<BR>--13<BR>A shed where sacrifices are offered.<BR>--14 A term, limit, boundary.<BR>--15<BR>Business (cares &c.) of a family or<BR>realm.<BR>--16 Reflection.<BR>--17 Proximate<BR>cause of a disease.<BR>--18 Awakening.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--एकादशी the eleventh day<BR>in the light fortnight of Kārttika<BR>when Viṣṇu rises from his four<BR>months' sleep (also called प्रबोधिनी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापक|उत्थापकः
उत्थापक a.<BR>1 Raising up, causing<BR>to get up.<BR>--2 Exciting, instigating,<BR>animating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थापनं|उत्थापन
उत्थापनं<BR>1 Causing to rise, come<BR>up, or get up.<BR>--2 Raising,<BR>elevating.<BR>--3 Causing to leave (a<BR>house).<BR>--4 Exciting, instigating.<BR>--5 Awakening, rousing (fig. also).<BR>--6 Vomiting.<BR>--7 Finishing,<BR>completing.<BR>--8 Bringing about.<BR>--9<BR>Bringing forth.<BR>--10 (In Math.)<BR>Finding the quantity sought, an<BR>answer to the question,<BR>substitution of a value (Colebr.).<BR>--नी The<BR>concluding verse (ऋच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थाप्य
उत्थाप्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be raised or<BR>lifted.<BR>--2 To be excited or<BR>animated.<BR>--3 To be mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थायिन्
उत्थायिन् a. Rising(fig. also);<BR>coming forth, becoming visible;<BR>चंद्रगुप्तसहोत्थायिनां Mu. 3; Pt. 3. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थित|उत्थितं
उत्थित p. p.<BR>1 Risen or rising (as<BR>from a seat); वचो<BR>निशम्योत्थितमुत्थितः सन् R. 2. 61, 7. 10, 3. 61;<BR>Ku. 7. 61; Śi. 1. 15.<BR>--2 Raised, gone up;<BR>पांशुः Śi. 5. 11; R. 6. 33; Śi. 4. 1,<BR>17. 7.<BR>--3 Rescued, saved; Ratn. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">Page0296-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--4 Born, produced, sprung up,<BR>arisen; वचः R. 2. 61, 12. 49;<BR>broken out (as fire); अग्निः<BR>Ratn. 4. 14; हृदयेऽग्निरिवोत्थितः R. 4. 2.<BR>burst into a flame.<BR>--5 Striving,<BR>active, diligent; Kām. 1. 17; 8. 49.<BR>--6<BR>Increasing, growing (in strength),<BR>advancing.<BR>--7 Bounded up,<BR>rebounded; पतिता उत्थिता Mu. 1.<BR>--8 Occurring.<BR>--9 High, lofty,<BR>eminent.<BR>--10 Extended, stretched;<BR>आपर्वभाग˚ Ś. 4. 4.<BR>--11 An epithet of<BR>a Pragātha consisting of ten Pādas.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगुलिः the palm of the<BR>hand with the fingers extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्थितिः|उत्थिति
उत्थितिः f. Elevation, rising up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पक्ष्मन्
उत्पक्ष्मन् a. With up turned<BR>eyelashes; उत्पक्ष्मणोर्नयनयोरुपरुद्धवृत्तिं<BR>Ś. 4. 15; V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पचिष्णु
उत्पचिष्णु a. Apt to ripen or<BR>cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पट्
उत्पट् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To root up,<BR>extirpate, eradicate, pull up by the<BR>roots; R. 15. 19; Ku. 2. 43.<BR>--2<BR>To tear up or out, draw out;<BR>दंतैर्नोत्पाटयेन्नखान् Ms. 4. 69; कीलमुत्पाटयन्<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--3 To remove, dispel; भय,<BR>रुषं, कोपं &c.; राज्यात् to depose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पटः|उत्पट
उत्पटः Sap issuing from the cleft<BR>of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटः|उत्पाट
उत्पाटः<BR>1 Uprooting, eradication,<BR>destroying root and branch.<BR>--2 A<BR>disease of the external ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटकः|उत्पाटक
उत्पाटकः<BR>1 One who roots out.<BR>--2 A disease of the external ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटनं|उत्पाटन
उत्पाटनं Uprooting, eradicating,<BR>destroying root and branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटिका
उत्पाटिका The external bark of<BR>a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाटिन्
उत्पाटिन् a. (oft. at the end of<BR>comp.) Eradicating, tearing out;<BR>कीलोत्पाटीव वानरः Pt. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्
उत्पत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 (a) To fly or<BR>jump up; मंक्षूदपाति परितः पटलैरलीनां<BR>Śi. 5. 37, 3. 77; oft. with acc. or<BR>dat. of place; पितुः पदं मध्यममुत्पतंती<BR>V. 1. 19; उत्पतोदङ्मुखः खं Me. 14;<BR>Bk. 5. 30, 6. 89; Ku. 6. 36; K. 46,<BR>132; V. 4; स्वर्गायोत्पतिता भवेत्<BR>V. 4. 2. (b) To go or rush<BR>towards; R. 9. 63. (c) To start up,<BR>emerge into view; मातंगचक्रैः<BR>सहसोत्पतद्भिः R. 13. 11.<BR>--2 To rebound<BR>(as a ball); पातितोपि कराघातैरुत्पतत्येव<BR>कंदुकः Bh. 2. 85.<BR>--3 To rise, be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-a" target="_blank">Page0297-a+ 55</a>]<BR>produced or originated;<BR>निष्पेषोत्पतितानलं R. 4. 77; रसात्तस्माद्वरस्त्रिय उत्पेतुः<BR>Rām.; Rs. 1. 26.<BR>--4 To be born<BR>(as from the womb).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0296-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतः|उत्पत
उत्पतः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतनं|उत्पतन
उत्पतनं<BR>1 Flying up, a leap, spring.<BR>--2 Rising or going up,<BR>ascending.<BR>--3 Throwing up.<BR>--4 Birth,<BR>production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पतिष्णु|उत्पतिष्णुः
उत्पतिष्णु a. Flying, going up,<BR>springing up; R. 4. 47; Pt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातः|उत्पात
उत्पातः<BR>1 Flying up, a spring,<BR>jump; एकोत्पातेन at one jump.<BR>--2<BR>Rebounding, rising up (fig. also);<BR>करनिहतकंदुकसमाः पातोत्पाता<BR>मनुष्याणां H. 1. v. l.<BR>--3 A portent, any<BR>portentous or unusual phenomenon<BR>boding calamity; उत्पातेन ज्ञापिते च<BR>Vārt.; ˚जलधरः K. 111, 287;<BR>Ve. 1. 22; सापि<BR>मुकुमारसुभगेत्युत्पातपरंपरा केयं K. P. 10;<BR>Mv. 1. 37.<BR>--4 Any public calamity (as<BR>an eclipse, earthquake &c.); ˚केतु<BR>K. 5; ˚धूमलेखा Ketu; Māl. 9. 48.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पवनः, --वातः, --वातालिः<BR>portentous or violent wind,<BR>whirlwind, a hurricane; R. 15. 23; Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पातक|उत्पातकः
उत्पातक a.<BR>1 Causing a calamity.<BR>--2<BR>Flying up.<BR>--कः = उत्पादकः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पताक
उत्पताक a. [उत्तोलिता पताका यत्र]<BR>With uplifted banners, where flags<BR>are hoisted; पुरंदरश्रीः पुरमुत्पताकं<BR>R. 2. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पथः|उत्पथ
उत्पथः [उत्क्रांतः पंथानं] A wrong<BR>road (fig. also); गुरोरप्यवलिप्तस्य<BR>कार्याकार्यमजानतः । उत्पथप्रतिपन्नस्य<BR>न्याय्यं भवति शासनं Mb. (परित्यागो<BR>विधीयते Pt. 1. 306); Ms. 2. 214;<BR>Śi. 12. 24; a mistaken path, (wrong<BR>guess), error; U. 4. 22.<BR>--थं ind.<BR>Astray, on the wrong road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पद्
उत्पद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To be born or<BR>produced, arise, originate, spring up;<BR>उत्पत्स्यतेऽस्ति मम कोपि समानधर्मा<BR>Māl. 1. 6; वायोः ज्योतिरुत्पद्यते Ms. 1. 77.<BR>--2<BR>To occur, happen; उदपादि चास्य मनसि<BR>K. 132 it occurred to his mind;<BR>युद्धमुत्पत्स्यते महत् Mb.;<BR>उत्पन्नावसरमर्थित्वं M. 3 for which an occasion has<BR>presented itself; Ms. 5. 48. --Caus.<BR>1 To produce, beget, cause, effect,<BR>bring about, prepare; वस्त्राणि<BR>सदैवोत्पादयति Pt. 2; Ms. 1. 63, 2. 147,<BR>9. 60; so दुःखं, दोषं, भयं, शंकां &c.<BR>--2 To bring forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पत्तिः|उत्पत्ति
उत्पत्तिः f.<BR>1 Birth;<BR>विपदुत्पत्तिमतामुपस्थिता R. 8. 83.<BR>--2 Production;<BR>कुसुमे कुसुमोत्पत्तिः श्रूयते न तु दृश्यते<BR>Ś. Til. 17.<BR>--3 Source, origin; उत्पत्तिः<BR>साधुतायाः K. 45.<BR>--4 Rising, going<BR>up, becoming visible, coming into<BR>existence.<BR>--5 Profit, productiveness,<BR>produce; स्वल्पोत्पत्तिदेशः<BR>Rāj. T. 5. 68.<BR>--6 Producing as a result or<BR>effect.<BR>--7 Resurrection.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कालीन a. taking place at the time<BR>of birth.<BR>--क्रमः order of birth.<BR>--प्रयोगः {1} production by the combined<BR>action of cause and effect. {2}<BR>purport, meaning.<BR>--व्यंजकः a type of<BR>birth (as investiture with the sacred<BR>thread); a mark of the twice-born;<BR>Ms. 2. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पन्न|उत्पन्नः
उत्पन्न p. p.<BR>1 Born, produced,<BR>arisen.<BR>--2 Risen, gone up.<BR>--3<BR>Acquired, gained.<BR>--4 Effected,<BR>accomplished.<BR>--5 Occurred.<BR>--6 Known,<BR>ascertained.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तंतु a. having<BR>a line of descendants.<BR>--भक्षिन् a.<BR>living from hand to mouth, (eating<BR>what is earned).<BR>--विनाशिन् a.<BR>perishing as soon as born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाद|उत्पादः
उत्पाद a. With the feet up-lifted.<BR>--दः Birth, production, appearance;<BR>दुःखे च शोणितोत्पादे शाखांगच्छेदने तथा<BR>Y. 2. 225; ˚भंगुरं Pt. 2. 177.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शयः, --यनः {1} a child. {2} a kind<BR>of partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादक|उत्पादकः
उत्पादक a. (दिका f.) Productive,<BR>effective, bringing about;<BR>अर्थस्योत्पादकं मंत्रिणं H. 3. 17 acquiring.<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>A producer, generator, a father;<BR>Ms. 2. 146; 9. 32.<BR>--2 A fabulous animal<BR>with eight feet, called शरभ.<BR>--कं<BR>Origin, cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादन|उत्पादनं
उत्पादन a. Bringing forth,<BR>producing.<BR>--नं Giving birth, production,<BR>generating; उत्पादनमपत्यस्य जातस्य<BR>परिपालनं Ms. 9. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादिन्
उत्पादिन् a.<BR>1 Produced, born;<BR>सर्वमुत्पादि भंगुरं H. 1. 208.<BR>--2 Bringing<BR>forth, causing, producing (in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पादिका
उत्पादिका<BR>1 N. of a certain insect,<BR>the white ant.<BR>--2 A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पल|उत्पलं|उत्पलः
उत्पल a. [उत्क्रांतः पलं मांसं]<BR>Fleshless, emaciated, lean.<BR>--ली A kind<BR>of cake made with unwinnowed<BR>corn.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A blue lotus, any lotus<BR>or water-lily; नवावतारं<BR>कमलादिवोत्पलं R. 3. 36, 12. 86; Me. 26;<BR>नीलोत्पलपत्रधारया Ś. 1. 18; so रक्त,˚<BR>--2 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">Page0297-c+ 52</a>]<BR>plant Costus Speciosus.<BR>--3 A plant in<BR>general.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष, --चक्षुस् a.<BR>lotuseyed.<BR>--आभ a. lotus-like.<BR>--गंधिकं<BR>a variety of sandal of the colour of<BR>brass (which is very fragrant).<BR>--पत्रं {1} a lotus-leaf. {2} a wound<BR>caused by a female's fingernail,<BR>nail-print. {3} a Tilaka or mark on<BR>the forehead made with sandal. {4}<BR>a broad-bladed knife or lancet.<BR>--पत्रकं a broad-bladed knife or<BR>lancet.<BR>--भेद्यकः a kind of bandage.<BR>--माला N. of a lexicon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पलिन्
उत्पलिन् a. Abounding in<BR>lotusflowers.<BR>--नी<BR>1 An assemblage of lotus<BR>flowers.<BR>--2 A lotus plant having<BR>lotuses.<BR>--3 A species of the<BR>Atijagatī metre (= चंद्रिका q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवनं|उत्पवन
उत्पवनं See under उत्पू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पश्य|उत्पश्यः
उत्पश्य a. Looking upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पारणं|उत्पारण
उत्पारणं Ved. Conveying over,<BR>transportation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पाली
उत्पाली Health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिंजर|उत्पिञ्जर
उत्पिंजर --ल a.<BR>1 Unconfined,<BR>uncaged.<BR>--2 Out of order,<BR>excessively confused, disordered;<BR>कुर्वाणमुत्पिंजलजातपत्रैः Śi. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिंजल|उत्पिञ्जल|उत्पिञ्जलः
उत्पिंजर --ल a.<BR>1 Unconfined,<BR>uncaged.<BR>--2 Out of order,<BR>excessively confused, disordered;<BR>कुर्वाणमुत्पिंजलजातपत्रैः Śi. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिष्
उत्पिष् {c7c} P.<BR>1 To rub together.<BR>--2 To crush, grind, reduce to<BR>powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पिष्ट
उत्पिष्ट a. Ground, rubbed.<BR>--ष्टं A<BR>disease, a grating of the bones or<BR>of the joints upon each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीड्
उत्पीड् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To press against,<BR>strike or rub against;<BR>अन्योन्यमुत्पीडयदुत्पलाक्ष्याः Ku. 1. 40; Śi. 3. 66.<BR>--2<BR>To throw or strike upwards; press<BR>out, propel. urge; R. 16. 66, 5. 46.<BR>--3<BR>To overwhelm, overpower, trouble;<BR>K. 242.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीड|उत्पीडः
उत्पीड a. Pressing out.<BR>--डंः<BR>1<BR>Pressing out.<BR>--2 (a) Gush, gushing<BR>flow, rushing column or mass;<BR>बाष्पोत्पीडः K. 296; उत्पीड इव धूमस्य<BR>मोहः प्रागावृणोति मां U. 3. 9;<BR>नयनसलिलोत्पीडरुद्धावकाशां Me. 91. (b) Overflow,<BR>excess; पूरोत्पीडे तडागस्य परीवाहः<BR>प्रतिक्रिया U. 3. 29; Māl. 6, 7.<BR>--3<BR>Froth, foam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पीडनं|उत्पीडन
उत्पीडनं<BR>1 Pressing out.<BR>--2<BR>Pressing or striking against; K. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुच्छ
उत्पुच्छ a. With the tail erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0297-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुच्छयते
उत्पुच्छयते Den. A.<BR>1 To raise the<BR>tail.<BR>--2 (P.) To make one raise the<BR>tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुट
उत्पुट a. Blown, expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुटकः|उत्पुटक
उत्पुटकः A sort of disease in the<BR>lobe of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पुलक
उत्पुलक a.<BR>1 Thrilled, bristling.<BR>--2 Joyful, delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पू
उत्पू {c9c} U.<BR>1 To cleanse, purify;<BR>सवितुर्वः प्रसव उत्पुनाम्यच्छिद्रेण पवित्रेण<BR>Vāj.<BR>--2 To extract anything that<BR>has been purified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवनं|उत्पवन
उत्पवनं<BR>1 Cleansing, purifying;<BR>द्रव्याणां चैव सर्वेषां शुद्धिरुत्पवनं स्मृतं<BR>Ms. 5. 115.<BR>--2 Straining liquids for<BR>domestic or religious purposes.<BR>--3<BR>Any instrument for cleansing.<BR>--4<BR>Sprinkling ghee (or other fluids)<BR>on the sacrificial fire with two<BR>blades of Kuśa grass, the ends of<BR>which are held in either hand and<BR>the centre dipped into the liquid;<BR>अप्रच्छिन्नाग्रावनंतर्गर्भौ प्रादेशमात्रौ कुशौ नानां.<BR>तयोर्गृहीत्वा अंगुष्ठोपकनिष्ठिकाभ्यामुत्तानाभ्यां<BR>प्रागुत्पुनाति सकृन्मंत्रेण द्विस्तूष्णीं Āśval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पवितृ
उत्पवितृ a. Purifying, a purifier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्पावः|उत्पाव
उत्पावः [पू-घञ्] Purifying ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रबंध
उत्प्रबंध a. Continuous, unceasing;<BR>Māl. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रभ|उत्प्रभः
उत्प्रभ a. Flashing forth or<BR>diffusing light, bright.<BR>--भः Blazing<BR>fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रसवः|उत्प्रसव
उत्प्रसवः Abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्राशनं|उत्प्राशन
उत्प्राशनं Eating by lifting up<BR>anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रासः|उत्प्रास
उत्प्रासः, --सनं<BR>1 Hurling,<BR>flinging away.<BR>--2 Jest, joke.<BR>--3 Violent<BR>burst of laughter.<BR>--4 (a) Ridicule,<BR>derision. (b) Satire, irony;<BR>Ratn. 3; Mv. 6; S. D. 478.<BR>--5 Excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रासनं|उत्प्रासन
उत्प्रासः, --सनं<BR>1 Hurling,<BR>flinging away.<BR>--2 Jest, joke.<BR>--3 Violent<BR>burst of laughter.<BR>--4 (a) Ridicule,<BR>derision. (b) Satire, irony;<BR>Ratn. 3; Mv. 6; S. D. 478.<BR>--5 Excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रुष्
उत्प्रुष् f. Ved. A bubble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्ष्
उत्प्रेक्ष् {c1c} A. [उत्प्र-ईक्ष्]<BR>1 To<BR>look up to; Pt. 1. to expect;<BR>K. 35, 229; to anticipate, see in<BR>prospect; उत्प्रेक्षमाणा जघनाभिघातं Mu. 2.<BR>--2 To see, perceive, behold.<BR>--3 To guess, conjecture; भगवति<BR>किमुत्प्रेक्षसे कुतस्त्योयमिति U. 4, 6;<BR>K. 67, 121, 198-9.<BR>--4 To believe,<BR>fancy; K. 108; Ve. 2. 9; उत्प्रेक्षामो<BR>वयं तावन्मतिमंतं बिभीषणं Rām.<BR>--5 To<BR>remember, think of; Amaru. 38;<BR>U. 6. 37.<BR>--6 To transfer (with loc.).<BR>--7 To illustrate by a supposed<BR>simile; see उत्प्रेत्क्षा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षणं|उत्प्रेक्षण
उत्प्रेक्षणं<BR>1 Looking into,<BR>perceiving.<BR>--2 Looking upwards.<BR>--3 Guess,<BR>conjecture.<BR>--4 Comparing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्रेक्षा
उत्प्रेक्षा<BR>1 Conjecture, guess.<BR>--2<BR>Disregarding, carelessness,<BR>indifference.<BR>--3 (In Rhet.) A figure<BR>of speech, ‘Poetical fancy,’ which<BR>consists in supposing उपमेय and उपमान<BR>as similar to each other in some<BR>respects and in indicating, expressly<BR>or by implication, a probability of<BR>their identity based on such<BR>similarity; it is the imagining of one<BR>object under the character of<BR>another; संभावनमथोत्प्रेक्षा प्रकृतस्य परेण<BR>यत् K. P. 10; e. g. लिंपतीव तमोंगानि<BR>वषंतीवांजनं नभः Mk. 1. 34; स्थितः पृथिव्या इव<BR>मानदंडः Ku. 1. 1. It is usually<BR>expressed by इव, or by words like<BR>मन्ये, शंके, ध्रुवं, प्रायः, नूनं &c. (see<BR>Kāv. 2. 234); cf. S. D. 686-692 and<BR>R. G. under उत्प्रेक्षा also.<BR>--4 A parable.<BR>--5 An ironical comparison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लु
उत्प्लु {c1c} A.<BR>1 To jump or leap up,<BR>bound, bound away; Śi. 12. 22, 5. 5;<BR>leap out of; Rs. 1. 18.<BR>--2 To spring<BR>or jump upon; यामुत्प्लुत्य वृको हन्यात्<BR>Ms. 8. 236.<BR>--3 To float; K. 42.<BR>--4<BR>To be fluctuating; K. 296.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवः|उत्प्लव
उत्प्लवः A jump, leap, bound.<BR>--वा<BR>A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्प्लवनं|उत्प्लवन
उत्प्लवनं<BR>1 Jumping or leaping up,<BR>springing upon.<BR>--2 Skimming off<BR>impure oil or ghee or any dirt<BR>floating upon a liquid by passing a<BR>blade of Kuśa grass over it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फल्
उत्फल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To spring, leap.<BR>--2 To part asunder, expand, open (as<BR>a flower). --Caus. To open, cause to<BR>expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फालः|उत्फाल
उत्फालः<BR>1 A jump, spring,<BR>leaping up; rapid motion; Mk. 6.<BR>--2<BR>Shuffling of feet.<BR>--3 The jumping<BR>attitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फुल्ल|उत्फुल्लः
उत्फुल्ल p. p. [उद्-फल्-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Opened, full blown (as flowers);<BR>उत्फुल्लनीलनलिनोदरतुल्यभासः Śi. 11. 36.<BR>--2 Widely opened, expanded,<BR>dilated (eyes); विस्मय ˚नयनः Pt. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Swollen, increased in bulk.<BR>--4<BR>Sleeping supinely or on the back;<BR>cf. उत्तान.<BR>--ल्लं<BR>1 The female organ of<BR>generation (स्त्रीकरणं).<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्फलं|उत्फल
उत्फलं An excellent fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सः|उत्स
उत्सः [उनत्ति जलेन, उंद्-स किच्च<BR>नलोपः Uṇ. 3. 68]<BR>1 A spring,<BR>fountain; यथारण्यान्यामुत्साश्चरंतः Śat.<BR>Br.<BR>--2 A watery place.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धिः Ved. a well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सक्थ
उत्सक्थ a. Opening the thighs<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्संकलित
उत्संकलित Permitted; अनुत्˚<BR>K. 260, 275.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्संगः|उत्सङ्ग|उत्संग|उत्सङ्गः
उत्संगः [उद्-संज्-आधारे घञ्]<BR>1<BR>The lap; पुत्रपूर्णोत्संगा with a boy<BR>seated in the lap U. 1;<BR>V. 5. 10; न केवलमुत्संगश्चिरान्मनोरथोपि मे<BR>पूर्णः U. 4; Me. 87.<BR>--2 Embrace,<BR>contact, union; Māl. 8. 6.<BR>--3<BR>Interior, vicinity;<BR>दरीगृहोत्संगनिषक्तभासः Ku. 1. 10; कर्ण˚<BR>K. 15; शय्योत्संगे Me. 93.<BR>--4 Surface,<BR>side, slope; दृषदो वासितोत्सगाः<BR>R. 4. 74; 14. 76.<BR>--5 The haunch or<BR>part above the hip (नितंब).<BR>--6 The<BR>upper part, top; सौधोत्संगप्रणयविमुखो<BR>मा स्म भूरुज्जयिन्याः Me. 27; K. 52.<BR>--7 (a) The acclivity or edge of a<BR>hill; तुंगं नगोत्संगमिवारुरोह R. 6. 3;<BR>(b) Peak, summit; उत्संगे महाद्रेः<BR>Ki. 7. 21.<BR>--8 The roof of a house.<BR>--9 Vault, canopy (as of sky);<BR>Mv. 5. 53.<BR>--10 The bottom or deep part<BR>of an ulcer.<BR>--11 A high number<BR>(= 100 Vivāhas).<BR>--12 An ascetic<BR>(उत्क्रांतः संगं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्संगित|उत्सङ्गित
उत्संगित a.<BR>1 Associated, joined,<BR>brought in contact with;<BR>उत्संगितांभःकणिको नभस्वान् Śi. 3. 79 wafting<BR>sprays.<BR>--2 Taken in the lap;<BR>˚एकैकदारकाभ्यां U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्संगिन्|उत्सङ्गिन्
उत्संगिन् a.<BR>1 Associating with,<BR>an associate, partner.<BR>--2<BR>Deepseated (as an ulcer). --m. An ulcer,<BR>a deep sore.<BR>--नी Pimples on the<BR>inner edge of the eye-lids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्संजनं|उत्सञ्जन|उत्संजन
उत्संजनं Throwing upwards,<BR>lifting up; P. I. 3. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सद्
उत्सद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sink (fig. also),<BR>fall into ruin or decay; उत्सीदेयुरिमे<BR>लोकाः Bg. 3. 24.<BR>--2 To leave off,<BR>quit.<BR>--3 To rise up. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>destroy, annihilate, bring to ruin;<BR>उत्साद्यंते जातिधर्माः Bg. 1. 43;<BR>Ms. 9. 267.<BR>--2 To overturn, upset<BR>(pots &c.).<BR>--3 To rub in, anoint<BR>(as with oil, perfumes &c.);<BR>Y. 1. 277.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सन्न
उत्सन्न p. p.<BR>1 Decayed.<BR>--2<BR>Destroyed, ruined, uprooted, left<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-a" target="_blank">Page0299-a+ 57</a>]<BR>off; उत्सन्नोस्मि K. 164 undone;<BR>मकरध्वज इवोत्सन्नविग्रहः K. 54;<BR>Bg. 1. 44; ˚निद्रा K. 171; उत्सन्नो<BR>युधिष्ठिरः Ve. 2 extirpated.<BR>--3 Curseed,<BR>wretched; K. 198.<BR>--4 Fallen<BR>into disuse, extinct (as a book).<BR>--5 Finished, completed.<BR>--6 Risen,<BR>increased (opp. अवसन्न).<BR>--7<BR>Accomplished easily (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0298-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादः|उत्साद
उत्सादः<BR>1 Destruction, decay, ruin,<BR>loss; गीतमुत्सादकारि मृगाणां K. 32.<BR>--2<BR>A particular part of the sacrificial<BR>animal (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादक
उत्सादक a. Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादनं|उत्सादन
उत्सादनं<BR>1 Destroying,<BR>overturning; उत्सादनार्थं लोकानां Mb.;<BR>Bg. 17. 19.<BR>--2 Suspending, interrupting.<BR>--3<BR>Cleaning the person with perfumes,<BR>chafing the limbs; Ms. 2. 209, 211.<BR>--4 Healing a sore.<BR>--5 Going up,<BR>ascending, rising.<BR>--6 Elevating,<BR>raising.<BR>--7 Ploughing a field twice<BR>(or thoroughly).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादनीय
उत्सादनीय pot. p. To be<BR>destroyed, effected or ascended &c.<BR>--यं<BR>Any application to a sore that<BR>produces granulations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सादित|उत्सादितं
उत्सादित p. p.<BR>1 Destroyed.<BR>--2<BR>Cleansed, purified with oil or<BR>perfumes &c.<BR>--3 Risen, ascended.<BR>--4<BR>Raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सवः|उत्सव
उत्सवः [उद्-सू-अप्]<BR>1 A festival,<BR>joyous or festive occasion, jubilee;<BR>रत˚ Ś. 6. 19; तांडव˚ festive or joyous<BR>dance U. 3. 18; Ms. 3. 59.<BR>--2<BR>Joy, merriment, delight, pleasure;<BR>स कृत्वा विरतोत्सवान् R. 4. 78,<BR>16. 10; Mv. 3. 41; Ratn. 1. 23;<BR>Śi. 2. 61; पराभवोप्युत्सव एव मानिनां<BR>Ki. 1. 41.<BR>--3 Height, elevation.<BR>--4<BR>Wrath.<BR>--5 Wish, rising of a wish.<BR>--6 A section of a book.<BR>--7<BR>Enterprise.<BR>--8 An undertaking,<BR>begining.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संकेताः (m. pl.) N.<BR>of a people, a wild tribe of the<BR>Himālaya; शरैरुत्सवसंकेतान् स कृत्वा<BR>विरतोत्सवान् R. 4. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सह्
उत्सह् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To be able, have<BR>power or energy; (expressed by<BR>‘can’); dare, venture (with inf.);<BR>तवानुवृत्तिं न च कर्तुमुत्सहे Ku. 5. 65;<BR>Ś. 5; Mu. 4. 14; Śi. 14. 83;<BR>Bk. 3. 54, 5. 59, 14. 89; sometimes with<BR>acc. and dat. also; Pt. 1.<BR>--2<BR>To attempt, be prompted or<BR>incited; Ki. 1. 36; to cheer up, not to<BR>sink or give way; अज्ञवन्नोत्सहेथास्त्वं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-b" target="_blank">Page0299-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Bk. 19. 16.<BR>--3 To feel at ease,<BR>enjoy pleasure; क्षणमप्युत्सहते न मां विना<BR>Ku. 4. 36.<BR>--4 To go forward, march<BR>on; K. 249. --Caus. To encourage,<BR>excite, instigate, incite;<BR>वरुणोत्साहितेन वेधसा K. 22; Bk. 9. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहः|उत्साह
उत्साहः [उद्-सह्-घञ्]<BR>1 Effort,<BR>exertion; धृत्युत्साहसमन्वितः Bg. 18. 26.<BR>--2 Energy, inclination, desire;<BR>मंदोत्साहः कृतोस्मि मृगयापवादिना<BR>माठव्येन Ś. 2; ममोत्साहभंगं मा कृथाः<BR>H. 3 do not damp my energy.<BR>--3 Perseverance, strenuous effort,<BR>energy, one of the three Śaktis or<BR>powers of a ruler (the other two<BR>being मंत्र and प्रभाव);<BR>नीताविवोत्साहगुणेन संपद् Ku. 1. 22.<BR>--4<BR>Determination, resolution; हसितेन<BR>भाविमरणोत्साहस्तया सूचितः Amaru. 10.<BR>--5 Power,<BR>ability; Ms. 5. 86.<BR>--6 Firmness,<BR>fortitude, strength.<BR>--7 (In Rhet.)<BR>Firmness or fortitude regarded<BR>as the feeling which gives rise to<BR>the वीर or heroic sentiment; कार्यारंभेषु<BR>संरंभः स्थेयानुत्साह उच्यते S. D. 3;<BR>परपराक्रमदानादिस्मृतिजन्मा औन्नत्याख्य उत्साहः<BR>R. G.<BR>--8 Happiness.<BR>--9 A thread.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्धनः the heroic<BR>sentiment (वीररस).<BR>--(नं) increase of energy,<BR>heroism.<BR>--वृत्तांतः plan or scheme of<BR>encouraging or exciting; Ś. 2.<BR>--शक्तिः<BR>f. firmness, energy; see (3) above.<BR>--संपन्न a. active, energetic,<BR>persevering.<BR>--हेतुक a. one who encourages<BR>or excites to exertion; अपेहिरे<BR>उत्साहहेतुक Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहक
उत्साहक a. Persevering, active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहनं|उत्साहन
उत्साहनं<BR>1 Effort, perseverance.<BR>--2 Encouraging, exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्साहिन्
उत्साहिन् a. Active, persevering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिच्
उत्सिच् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To sprinkle, spread,<BR>pour down.<BR>--2 To make proud.<BR>--Pass.<BR>1 To spout or foam up;<BR>उत्सिच्यमाने पयसि Bhāg.<BR>--2 To be<BR>puffed up or proud, be elated; न<BR>तस्योत्सिषिचे मनः R. 17. 43;<BR>स्तूयमाना नोत्सिच्यंते K. 329.<BR>--3 To<BR>overflow, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सिक्त|उत्सिक्तः
उत्सिक्त p. p.<BR>1 Sprinkled.<BR>--2<BR>Proud, haughty, puffed up.<BR>--3<BR>Flooded, overflowing, excessive.<BR>--4<BR>Enlarged, increased.<BR>--5 Raised,<BR>elevated.<BR>--6 Fickle, disturbed (in<BR>mind); जानीयादस्थिरां वाचमुत्सिक्तमनसां<BR>तथा Ms. 8. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेकः|उत्सेक
उत्सेकः<BR>1 Sprinkling, pouring.<BR>--2<BR>Spouting out or over, showering.<BR>--3 Overflow, increase, excess;<BR>रुधिरोत्सेकाः Mv. 5. 33 streams of blood;<BR>Me. 55 v. l.; दर्प˚, बल˚ &c.<BR>--4 Pride,<BR>haughtiness, insolence; उपदा विविशुः<BR>शश्वन्नोत्सेकाः कोसलेश्वरं R. 4. 70;<BR>अनुत्सेको लक्ष्म्यां Bh. 2. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेकिन्
उत्सेकिन् a.<BR>1 Overflowing,<BR>excessive; Mu. 1. 26.<BR>--2 Proud, haughty,<BR>puffed up; भाग्येष्वनुत्सेकिनी Ś. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेचनं|उत्सेचन
उत्सेचनं The act of showering or<BR>spouting upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुक|उत्सुकः
उत्सुक a.<BR>1 Anxiously desirous,<BR>eagerly expecting, striving for (any<BR>object) (with instr. or loc. or in<BR>comp.); निद्रया निद्रायां वोत्सुकः Sk.; मनो<BR>नियोगक्रिययोत्सुकं मे R. 5. 11;<BR>सोत्सुका सुतजन्मनि Ks. 21. 139; R. 2. 45;<BR>Me. 99; संगम˚ Ś. 3. 14; so रण˚,<BR>गमन˚, जय˚ &c.<BR>--2 Restless, uneasy,<BR>anxious; R. 12. 24.<BR>--3 Fond of,<BR>attached to; वत्सोत्सुकापि R. 2. 22.<BR>--4<BR>Regretting, repining, sorrowing for.<BR>--कः Longing for, anxious desire;<BR>प्रकुर्वते कस्य मनो न सोत्सुकं Rs. 1. 6<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकता
उत्सुकता, --त्वं<BR>1 Restlessness,<BR>uneasiness.<BR>--2 Zeal, ardent desire.<BR>--3<BR>Attachment, affection.<BR>--4 Sorrow,<BR>regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकत्वं|उत्सुकत्व
उत्सुकता, --त्वं<BR>1 Restlessness,<BR>uneasiness.<BR>--2 Zeal, ardent desire.<BR>--3<BR>Attachment, affection.<BR>--4 Sorrow,<BR>regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकयति
उत्सुकयति Den. P. To make<BR>uneasy; M. 5. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सुकायते
उत्सुकायते Den. A. To become<BR>uneasy or anxious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूत्र
उत्सूत्र a. [उत्क्रांतः सूत्रं]<BR>1<BR>Unstrung, loose, detached (from the<BR>string); ˚मणिभिः Śi. 8. 53.<BR>--2<BR>Irregular.<BR>--3 Deviating from the rule<BR>(सूत्र) of Pāṇini; अनुत्सूत्रपदन्यासा<BR>सद्वृत्तिः सन्निबंधना Śi. 2. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सूरः|उत्सूर
उत्सूरः [उत्क्रांतः सूरं सूर्यं] Evening,<BR>twilight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृ
उत्सृ Caus.<BR>1 To expel, turn<BR>out, drive away; वेत्रदंडैरिवोत्सार्यंते<BR>गुणाः K. 106; Mv. 4. 39.<BR>--2 To<BR>remove, keep or put aside; K. 204;<BR>to push far; R. 4. 53; परमेश्वरस्य<BR>चार्वाकेण दूरोत्सारितत्वात् Sarva. S. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सरः|उत्सर
उत्सरः A variety of the अतिशक्वरी<BR>metre having 15 syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्या|उत्सर्य्या
उत्सर्या [उद्-सृ-यत्] A cow when<BR>she is fit to take the bull (<BR>गर्भयोग्यावस्थापन्ना गौः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारकः|उत्सारक
उत्सारकः<BR>1 A policeman, (one<BR>who drives away men and makes<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-a" target="_blank">Page0300-a+ 56</a>]<BR>room for others).<BR>--2 A guard.<BR>--3 A<BR>porter, doorkeeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0299-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सारणं|उत्सारण
उत्सारणं<BR>1 Removing, keeping at<BR>a distance, driving out of the way;<BR>˚वेत्रलता K. 106, 112.<BR>--2 Helping<BR>one to step out (of a palanquin &c.).<BR>--3 Reception of a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृज्
उत्सृज् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To pour out, emit,<BR>send forth or down;<BR>व्यलीकनिश्वासमिवोत्ससर्ज Ku. 3. 25; सहस्रगुणमुत्स्रष्टुमादत्ते<BR>हि रसं रविः R. 1. 18 to give back;<BR>Bg. 9. 19; so बाष्पं, वारि.<BR>--2 (a) To<BR>quit, leave, abandon, give up;<BR>मातापितृभ्यामुत्सृष्टं Ms. 9. 171;<BR>नियतमात्मानमुत्स्रक्ष्यामि K. 177, 191, 194; R. 5. 51,<BR>6. 46, 7. 7; Ku. 2. 36, 5. 86; kill; so<BR>तनुं, प्राणान्, रणं &c.; परार्थे प्राज्ञ उत्सृजेत्<BR>H. 1. 44. (b) To put off, lay aside;<BR>भयोत्सृष्टविभूषाणां R. 4. 54, 3. 60.<BR>--3<BR>To let loose, allow to roam at liberty;<BR>तुरंगं R. 3. 39.<BR>--4 To avoid,<BR>escape.<BR>--5 To cast forth or away,<BR>discharge, throw (as arrows);<BR>Bk. 14. 45.<BR>--6 To let fall down, sow, scatter<BR>(as seed &c.); Ms. 10. 71.<BR>--7 To<BR>present, give; Māl. 10. 23.<BR>--8 To<BR>widen, stretch out, extend.<BR>--9 To<BR>abolish (as a rule), restrict or limit<BR>the scope of a rule.<BR>--10 To send one<BR>to a place.<BR>--11 To permit to go,<BR>discharge, dismiss.<BR>--12 To adjourn.<BR>--13 To hear to the end.<BR>--14 To<BR>make, form, shape (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्गः|उत्सर्ग
उत्सर्गः<BR>1 Laying or leaving side,<BR>abandoning, suspension; Ku. 7. 45.<BR>--2 Pouring out, dropping down,<BR>emission; तोयोत्सर्गद्रुततरगतिः Me. 19,<BR>37; so शुक्र˚.<BR>--3 A gift, donation,<BR>giving away; Ms. 11. 194.<BR>--4<BR>Spending; अर्थ˚ Mu. 3.<BR>--5<BR>Loosening, letting loose; as in वृषोत्सर्गः.<BR>--6<BR>An oblation, libation.<BR>--7 Excretion,<BR>voiding by stool &c.; पुरीष˚, मलमूत्र˚.<BR>--8 Completion (as of study or a<BR>vow); cf. उत्सृष्टा वै वेदाः (opp. उपाकृता<BR>वै वेदाः).<BR>--9 A general rule or<BR>precept (opp. अपवाद a particular<BR>rule or exception); अपवादैरिवोत्सर्गाः<BR>कृतव्यावृत्तयः परैः Ku. 2. 27; अपवाद<BR>इवोत्सर्गं व्यावर्तयितुमीश्वरः R. 15. 7<BR>--10 Offering what is promised (to<BR>gods, Brāhmaṇas &c.) with due<BR>ceremonies.<BR>--11 The anus;<BR>मित्रमुत्सर्गे Ms. 12. 121.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्गतः
उत्सर्गतः ind. Generally, without<BR>any exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्गिन्
उत्सर्गिन् a.<BR>1 Leaving out or<BR>off.<BR>--2 Omitting, abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्जनं|उत्सर्जन
उत्सर्जनं<BR>1 Leaving, abandoning,<BR>letting loose, quitting &c.<BR>--2 A<BR>gift, donation.<BR>--3 Suspension of a<BR>Vedic study.<BR>--4 A ceremony<BR>connected with this suspension (to be<BR>performed half yearly); Ms. 4. 96;<BR>वेदोत्सर्जनाख्यं कर्म करिष्ये<BR>Śrāvaṇī Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्ट|उत्सृष्टः
उत्सृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Left, cast, thrown.<BR>--2 Used, employed; Pt. 1. 206.<BR>--3<BR>Given, offered.<BR>--4 Poured forth,<BR>cast into or upon.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पशु a<BR>bull set at liberty upon particular<BR>occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृष्टिः|उत्सृष्टि
उत्सृष्टिः f. Abandonment, leaving,<BR>emission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सृप्
उत्सृप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go upwards,<BR>glide or soar upwards.<BR>--2 To go up<BR>to, approach; सरित्प्रवाहस्तटमुत्ससर्प<BR>R. 5. 46.<BR>--3 To spread out.<BR>--4 To rise<BR>(as the sun).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पः|उत्सर्प|उत्सर्प्प
उत्सर्पः, --र्पणं<BR>1 Going or gliding<BR>upwards.<BR>--2 Swelling, heaving,<BR>undulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पणं|उत्सर्पण|उत्सर्प्पण
उत्सर्पः, --र्पणं<BR>1 Going or gliding<BR>upwards.<BR>--2 Swelling, heaving,<BR>undulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सर्पिन्|उत्सर्प्पिन्
उत्सर्पिन् a.<BR>1 Moving or gliding<BR>upwards, rising; पयोधरोत्सर्पिषु (<BR>शीकरेषु) R. 16. 62.<BR>--2 Soaring,<BR>towering; उत्सर्पिणी खलु महतां प्रार्थना Ś. 7.<BR>--3 Transcendental.<BR>--णी f. A<BR>division of time (with the Jainas), a<BR>long period said to be = ten crores of<BR>crores of oceans of year; cf.<BR>अवसर्पिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्सेध|उत्सेधः
उत्सेध a. High, tall.<BR>--धः<BR>1 A<BR>height, elevation; (fig. also);<BR>पयोधरोत्सेधविशीर्णसंहति (वल्कलं)<BR>Ku. 5. 8, 24 high or projecting breasts;<BR>सोत्सेधैः स्कंधदेशैः Mu. 4. 7 raised<BR>high up.<BR>--2 Thickness, fatness.<BR>--3<BR>Intumescence, swelling.<BR>--4 The<BR>body.<BR>--5 Sublimity, greatness.<BR>--धं<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मि
उत्स्मि {c1c} A. To smile at, deride.<BR>--Caus. To ridicule, make a fool of<BR>one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्मयः|उत्स्मय
उत्स्मयः Smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्य
उत्स्य a. Coming from a well or<BR>fountain (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्वन|उत्स्वनः
उत्स्वन a. High-sounding.<BR>--नः<BR>A loud sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्स्वप्नायते
उत्स्वप्नायते Den. A. To talk in<BR>one's sleep, dream through<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-c" target="_blank">Page0300-c+ 56</a>]<BR>uneasiness; सीतोत्स्वप्नायते U. 1; सांप्रतं<BR>मालविकामुत्स्वप्नायते M. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् ind. A prefix to verbs and<BR>nouns. G. M. gives the following<BR>senses with illustrations:--<BR>1<BR>Superiourity in place, rank or power;<BR>up, upwards, upon, on, over, above;<BR>(उद्बल).<BR>--2 Separation, disjunction;<BR>out, out off, from, apart &c.;<BR>उद्गच्छति.<BR>--3 Motion upwards (<BR>उत्तिष्ठति).<BR>--4 Acquisition, gain; उपार्जति.<BR>--5 Publicity; उच्चरति.<BR>--6 Wonder;<BR>anxiety; उत्सुक.<BR>--7 Liberation; उद्गत.<BR>--8 Absence; उत्पथ.<BR>--9 Blowing,<BR>expanding, opening; उत्फुल्ल.<BR>--10<BR>Pre-eminence; उद्दिष्ट.<BR>--11 Power;<BR>उत्साहः; उत्<BR>प्राबल्यवियोगोर्ध्वकर्मलाभप्रकाशाश्चर्यमोक्षणाभावदलप्राधान्यशाक्तिषु. With<BR>nouns it forms adj. and adv.<BR>compounds; उदर्चिस्, उच्छिख, उद्बाहु, उन्निद्रं,<BR>उत्पथं, उद्दामं &c. It is sometimes<BR>used in the Veda as an expletive<BR>simply to fill out the verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्
उद् = उंद् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकं|उदक
उदकं [उंद्-ण्वुल् नि˚ नलोपश्च<BR>Uṇ. 2. 39] Water; अनीत्वा पंकतां धूलिमुदकं<BR>नावतिष्ठते Śi. 2. 34. उदकं दा,<BR>-प्रदा or कृ To offer a libation<BR>of water to a dead person;<BR>उदकं उपस्पृश् to touch certain parts<BR>of the body with water, bathe;<BR>[cf. Gr. hudor; L. unda ‘a wave’].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः margin of water,<BR>bank, shore; ओदकांतात्स्निग्धो<BR>जनोऽनुगंतव्य इति श्रूयते Ś. 4.<BR>--अर्थिन् a.<BR>desirous of water, thirsty.<BR>--आत्मन्<BR>a. chiefly consisting of water.<BR>--आधारः a reservoir, a cistern, well.<BR>--उदंजनः a water-jar.<BR>--उदरं dropsy.<BR>--उदरिन् a. dropsical.<BR>--ओदनः rice<BR>boiled with water.<BR>--कर्मन्, --कार्यं,<BR>--क्रिया, --दानं presentation of (a<BR>libation) of water to dead ancestors<BR>or the manes; वृकोदरस्योदकक्रियां<BR>कुरु Ve. 6; Y. 3. 4.<BR>--कुंभः a water-jar.<BR>--कृच्छ्रः a kind of vow.<BR>--गाहः<BR>entering water, bathing.<BR>--गिरिः,<BR>पर्वतः a mountain abounding in<BR>streams of water.<BR>--ग्रहणं drinking<BR>water; Pt. 1.<BR>--चंद्रः a kind of<BR>magic.<BR>--द, --दातृ, --दायिन्, --दानिक a.<BR>giver of water.<BR>--(दः) {1} a giver of<BR>water to the manes. {2} an heir, near<BR>kinsman.<BR>--दानं = ˚कर्मन् q. v.<BR>--धरः a<BR>cloud.<BR>--परीक्षा a kind of ordeal.<BR>--पूर्वकं ind. preceded by the pouring of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-a" target="_blank">Page0301-a+ 58</a>]<BR>water, by pouring water on the hand<BR>as preparatory to or confirmatory<BR>of a gift or promise.<BR>--प्रतीकाश a.<BR>watery, like water.<BR>--भारः, --वीवधः a<BR>yoke for carrying water.<BR>--भूमः water<BR>or moist soil.<BR>--मंडलुः a water-pitcher<BR>(Ved.).<BR>--मंथः a kind of peeled grain.<BR>--मेहः a sort of diabetes (passing<BR>watery urine).<BR>--मेहिन् a. suffering<BR>from this disease.<BR>--वज्रः {1} a<BR>thunder-shower. {2} thunderbolt in the<BR>form of shower; Śi. 8. 39.<BR>--शाकं<BR>any aquatic herb.<BR>--शांतिः f.<BR>sprinkling holy or consecrated water<BR>over a sick person to allay fever;<BR>cf. शांत्युदकं.<BR>--शुद्ध a. bathed,<BR>purified by ablutions.<BR>--सक्तुः ground<BR>rice moistened with water.<BR>--स्पर्शः {1} touching different parts of the<BR>body with water. {2} touching water<BR>preparatory to or in confirmation<BR>of an oath, gift, or promise.<BR>--हारः<BR>a water-carrier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0300-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकेचरः|उदकेचर
उदकेचरः An aquatic animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकेविशीर्ण
उदकेविशीर्ण a. Dried in water;<BR>figuratively used for anything<BR>unheard of or impossible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकल
उदक(कि)ल a. [cf. P. V. 2. 97]<BR>Watery, containing water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदकिल
उदक(कि)ल a. [cf. P. V. 2. 97]<BR>Watery, containing water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्य
उदक्य a. [उदकमर्हति दंडा˚ यत्]<BR>1<BR>Requiring water.<BR>--2 Being in water.<BR>--क्या A woman in her courses<BR>(requiring water for purification).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्र|उदग्रं
उदग्र a. [उद्गतमग्रं यस्य]<BR>1 With<BR>elevated top, projecting, pointing<BR>upwards; as in ˚दंत.<BR>--2 Tall, lofty,<BR>high, elevated, exalted (fig. also);<BR>उदग्रदशनांशुभिः Śi. 2. 21, 4. 19; उदग्रः<BR>क्षत्रस्य शब्दः R. 2. 53;<BR>उदग्रप्लुतत्वात् Ś. 1. 7 high leaps; Śi. 12. 65;<BR>˚ग्रावन् Dk. 6; विक्रमोदग्रं शिरः<BR>R. 15. 27 exalted; गंधोदग्रं पुष्पं 16. 87 rich<BR>in odour.<BR>--3 Large, broad, vast, big;<BR>अवंतिनाथोयमुदग्रबाहुः R. 6. 32;<BR>Mu. 6. 12.<BR>--4 Noble, good-looking<BR>(उदार); Ki. 14. 41.<BR>--5 Advanced in<BR>age.<BR>--6 Conspicuous, distinguished,<BR>exalted, magnified, increased; स<BR>मंगलोदग्रतरप्रभावः R. 2. 71, 9. 64,<BR>13. 50.<BR>--7 Intense, unbearable (as heat);<BR>Śi. 4. 12.<BR>--8 Fierce, fearful; संदधे<BR>दृशमुदग्रतारकां R. 11. 69.<BR>--9 Excited,<BR>furious, enraptured; मदोदग्राः<BR>ककुद्मंतः R. 4. 22.<BR>--10 Mighty, strong;<BR>Ki. 18. 1; वेगोदग्रं विषं V. 5. 18 strong<BR>or sharp (deadly).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दत् a.<BR>having projecting teeth,<BR>largetoothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदग्रयति
उदग्रयति Den. P. To display<BR>prominently; Mu. 6. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदज्
उदज् {c1c} U. [उद्-अज्] To drive<BR>out, expel, pull off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदजः|उदज
उदजः Driving out or forth (of<BR>cattle &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाजः|उदाज
उदाजः The driving out (of cattle);<BR>leading out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंच्|उदञ्च्
उदंच् {c1c} U. [उद्-अंच्]<BR>1 To raise,<BR>elevate, lift or throw up, draw up<BR>(as water); एकैकमेव पादमुदच्य तिष्ठति<BR>अश्वः Śat. Br.; उदंचिताक्षः Bk. 2. 31;<BR>उदंचय मुखं मनाक् Vb. 3. 27.<BR>--2 To<BR>utter, send forth, cause to sound;<BR>हरिमनुगायति काचिदुदंचितपंचमरागं<BR>Gīt. 1.<BR>--3 (Intrans.) (a) To go up;<BR>(b) to rise, rise forth; उदंचन्मात्सर्य<BR>G. L. 6; Bv. 2. 76; K. 221; welter<BR>up; Mv. 3. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्त
उदक्त p. p.<BR>1 Raised or lifted up<BR>(as water from a well); उदक्तमुदकं<BR>कूपात् Sk.<BR>--2 Risen, ascended.<BR>--3<BR>Sent forth, uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंकः|उदङ्क|उदंक|उदङ्कः
उदंकः [अंच्-घञ्] A leathern<BR>vessel (for oil &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदच्
उदच्, उदंच् a. (m. उदङ्, n. उदक्,<BR>f. उदीची)<BR>1 Turned or going<BR>upwards.<BR>--2 Upper, higher; ˚कूलः,<BR>˚तीरः &c.<BR>--3 Northern, turned<BR>towards the north.<BR>--4 Subsequent.<BR>--क ind.<BR>1 Above.<BR>--2 Northward,<BR>to the north of (with abl.);<BR>Ms. 3. 217.<BR>--3 Subsequently.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद्रिः the northern mountain,<BR>Himālaya.<BR>--अयनं the sun's<BR>progress north of the equator (=<BR>उत्तरायणं q. v.).<BR>--आवृत्तिः f. return from<BR>the north; उदगावृत्तिपथेन नारदः<BR>R. 8. 33.<BR>--दश a. having its skirts or<BR>border turned upwards or towards<BR>the north (as a garment).<BR>--पथः<BR>a northern country.<BR>--प्रवण a.<BR>{1} inclining or sloping towards<BR>the north. {2} proceeding well (as a<BR>sacrifice).<BR>--भूमः, --भूमिः good or<BR>fertile soil.<BR>--मुख a. facing the<BR>north; उत्पतोदङ्मुखः खं Me. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंच्|उदञ्च्
उदच्, उदंच् a. (m. उदङ्, n. उदक्,<BR>f. उदीची)<BR>1 Turned or going<BR>upwards.<BR>--2 Upper, higher; ˚कूलः,<BR>˚तीरः &c.<BR>--3 Northern, turned<BR>towards the north.<BR>--4 Subsequent.<BR>--क ind.<BR>1 Above.<BR>--2 Northward,<BR>to the north of (with abl.);<BR>Ms. 3. 217.<BR>--3 Subsequently.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद्रिः the northern mountain,<BR>Himālaya.<BR>--अयनं the sun's<BR>progress north of the equator (=<BR>उत्तरायणं q. v.).<BR>--आवृत्तिः f. return from<BR>the north; उदगावृत्तिपथेन नारदः<BR>R. 8. 33.<BR>--दश a. having its skirts or<BR>border turned upwards or towards<BR>the north (as a garment).<BR>--पथः<BR>a northern country.<BR>--प्रवण a.<BR>{1} inclining or sloping towards<BR>the north. {2} proceeding well (as a<BR>sacrifice).<BR>--भूमः, --भूमिः good or<BR>fertile soil.<BR>--मुख a. facing the<BR>north; उत्पतोदङ्मुखः खं Me. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्तात्
उदक्तात् ind. Towards the north,<BR>northwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंचनं|उदञ्चन|उदंचन|उदञ्चनं
उदंचनं [अंच् करणे-ल्युट्]<BR>1 A<BR>bucket, a pail for drawing water<BR>out of a well; उदंचनं सरज्जुं पुरः चिक्षेप<BR>Dk. 130.<BR>--2 Throwing upwards.<BR>--3 Rising, ascending.<BR>--4 A cover<BR>or lid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंचु|उदञ्चु
उदंचु a. [अंच्-उन्] Turned or<BR>going upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीची
उदीची The north; तेनोदीचीं<BR>दिशमनुसरेः Me. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीचीन|उदीचीनं
उदीचीन a.<BR>1 Turned towards the<BR>north.<BR>--2 Northern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्य|उदीच्यं|उदीच्यः
उदीच्य a. Situated or living in<BR>the north.<BR>--च्यः<BR>1 The country<BR>to the north and west of the river<BR>Sarasvatī; northern country.<BR>--2<BR>(pl.) The inhabitants of the north;<BR>R. 4. 66.<BR>--च्यं A kind of perfume.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वृत्तं a kind of Vaitālīya<BR>metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंजलि|उदञ्जलि
उदंजलि a. One who hollows<BR>the palms and then raises them,<BR>folding the hands in supplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंडपालः|उदण्डपाल|उदंडपाल|उदण्डपालः
उदंडपालः<BR>1 A fish.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदधिः|उदधि
उदधिः See under {2} उदन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्
1 उदन् {c2c} P. (उद्-अन्) To breathe<BR>upwards, send out the breath in<BR>an upward direction (opp. अपान्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदानः|उदान
उदानः [अन्-घञ्]<BR>1 Breathing<BR>upwards.<BR>--2 Breathing, breath in<BR>general.<BR>--3 One of the five<BR>vital airs or life-winds which<BR>rises up the throat and enters into<BR>the head; the other four being प्राण,<BR>अपान, समान and व्यान; स्पंदयत्यधरं वक्त्रं<BR>गात्रनेत्रप्रकोपनः । उद्वेजयति मर्मणि उदानो नाम<BR>मारुतः ॥.<BR>--4 (With Buddhists) An<BR>expression of praise or joy.<BR>--5 The<BR>navel.<BR>--6 An eyelash.<BR>--7 A kind<BR>of snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्
2 उदन् n. [उंद्-कनिन्] Water<BR>(usually occurring in compounds<BR>either at the beginning or at the<BR>end, and as an optional substitute<BR>for उदक after the acc. dual. It has<BR>no forms for the first five<BR>inflections. In comp. it drops its न्); e. g.<BR>उदधि, अच्छोद, क्षीरोद &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ओदनः water-meal.<BR>--कीर्णः --र्यः N.<BR>of a tree (महाकरंज) (the bark of<BR>which is rubbed and thrown in<BR>water to stun the fishes).<BR>--कुंभः a<BR>water-jar; Ms. 2. 182, 3. 68.<BR>--ग्रामः<BR>a cloud (Ved.).<BR>--ज a. aquatic,<BR>watery, produced in or by water.<BR>--धानः [उदकं धीयते अत्र] {1} a<BR>waterjar. {2} a cloud<BR>--धिः [उदकानि<BR>धीयंतेऽत्र धा-कि उदादेशः] {1} the receptacle<BR>of waters, ocean; उदधेरिव<BR>निम्नगाशतेष्वभवन्नास्य विमानना क्वचित् R. 8. 8.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-a" target="_blank">Page0302-a+ 57</a>]<BR>{2} a cloud. {3} a lake, any large<BR>reservoir of water. {4} a water-jar.<BR>{5} a symbolical expression for the<BR>number {4} or {7} ˚कन्या, तनया, सुता<BR>Lakṣmī, the daughter of the ocean<BR>(produced from the ocean among<BR>the 14 jewels). ˚क्रमः, -क्राः m. a<BR>voyager, mariner. ˚मलः {1}<BR>cuttle-fishbone. {2} the foam of the ocean.<BR>˚मेखला the earth (girdled by the ocean,<BR>sea-girt). ˚राजः the king of waters,<BR>i. e. the chief ocean.<BR>--सुता N. of<BR>Lakṣmī; and of Dvārakā, the capital of<BR>Kṛṣṇa (said to have been<BR>reclaimed from the ocean).<BR>--प a. crossing<BR>the water (as a boat).<BR>--पात्रं, --त्री a<BR>water-jug, vessel.<BR>--पानः, -नं a<BR>small pool or pond near a well, or<BR>the well itself; K. 50. ˚मडूंकः (lit.)<BR>a frog in a well; (fig.) one who<BR>has had no experience of the<BR>world at large, a man of limited<BR>ideas who knows only his own<BR>neighbourhood; cf. कूपमंडूक.<BR>--पेषं<BR>a paste, anything ground with<BR>water.<BR>--(षं) ind. by grinding in<BR>water.<BR>--प्रुत् a. Ved. causing water<BR>to flow; swimming or splashing in<BR>water (?).<BR>--प्लुत a. swimming in<BR>water.<BR>--बिंदुः a drop of water;<BR>Ku. 5. 24.<BR>--भारः a water-carrier, i. e. a<BR>cloud.<BR>--मंथः barley-water.<BR>--मानः,<BR>नं a fiftieth part of an आढक q. v.<BR>--मेघः {1} a watery cloud. {2} a<BR>shower of rain.<BR>--लावणिक a.<BR>salted, prepared with brine, briny.<BR>--वज्रः {1} a thunder-shower;<BR>water-spout. {2} thunderbolt in<BR>the form of water; Śi. 8. 39.<BR>--वापः<BR>one who offers waters to the manes.<BR>--वासः standing or residence in<BR>water; सहस्यरात्रीरुदवासतत्परा<BR>Ku. 5. 26.<BR>--(सं) a house on the borders<BR>of a stream or pond.<BR>--वासिन् a.<BR>standing in water; K. 23.<BR>--वाह a.<BR>bringing water.<BR>--(हः) a cloud.<BR>--वाहनं a water-vessel.<BR>--वीवधः a<BR>yoke for carrying water.<BR>--शरावः a<BR>jar filled with water.<BR>--शुद्धः a<BR>water-jar.<BR>--श्वित् n. [उदकेन जलेन<BR>श्वयाति] butter-milk containing fifty<BR>per cent water (i. e. {2} parts of<BR>butter-milk and {1} part of water).<BR>--स्थानं {1} a place full of water.<BR>{2} residence in water.<BR>--स्थाली<BR>a kettle, vessel for holding water.<BR>--हरणः a vessel for drawing water.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">Page0302-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--हार a. fetching or carrying water.<BR>--(रः) a cloud (water-carrier).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0301-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्वत्|उदन्वन्त्
उदन्वत् a. Wavy, watery,<BR>abounding in water (Ved.). --m. The ocean;<BR>उदन्वच्छन्ना भूः B. R. 1. 8; R. 4. 52,<BR>58, 10. 6; नवैरुदन्वानिव चंद्रपादैः<BR>Ku. 7. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्य
उदन्य a.<BR>1 Thirsty.<BR>--2 Watery.<BR>--न्या Thirst; निर्वर्त्यतामुदन्याप्रतीकारः<BR>Ve. 6; व्यस्यन्नुदन्यां शिशिरैः पयोभिः<BR>Bk. 3. 40.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. Ved. born or<BR>living in water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्यति
उदन्यति Den. P.<BR>1 To be thirsty.<BR>--2 To irrigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्यु
उदन्यु a.<BR>1 Thirsty, seeking water.<BR>--2 Walking in water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदक्
उदक् See under उदंच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंत|उदन्त|उदन्तः
उदंत a. [उद्गतोंऽतो यस्य] Reaching<BR>to the end or border of<BR>anything.<BR>--तः [उद्गतोंऽतो निर्णयो यस्मात्]<BR>1 News, intelligence, report,<BR>full tidings, account, history;<BR>श्रुत्वा रामः प्रियोदंतं R. 12. 66;<BR>आत्मोदंत कथयिष्यति K. 132; कांतोदंतः<BR>सुहृदुपगतः संगमात्किंचिदूनः Me. 100.<BR>--2 A pure and virtuous man (साधु).<BR>--3 Supporting oneself by<BR>sacrificing for others (वृत्तियाजनं).<BR>--4 One<BR>who gets a livelihood by a trade<BR>&c. (Wilson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंतकः|उदन्तक|उदंतक|उदन्तकः
उदंतकः News, intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंतिका|उदन्तिका
उदंतिका Satisfaction, satiety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंत्य|उदन्त्य
उदंत्य a. Living beyond a limit<BR>or boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदन्य
उदन्य See under उदन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदंभस्
उदंभस् a. Full of water;<BR>R. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

