उदरं|उदर|उदरः
उदरं [उद्-ऋ-अप्]<BR>1 The belly;<BR>दुष्पूरोदरपूरणाय Bh. 2. 119; cf.<BR>कृशोदरी, उदरभरणं, उदरंभरि &c.<BR>--2 The<BR>interior or inside of anything, cavity;<BR>तडाग˚ Pt. 2. 150; R. 5. 70; U. 2. 16,<BR>4. 29; त्वां कारयामि कमलोदरबंधनस्थं<BR>Ś. 6. 19; Śānti. 1. 5; Ś. 1. 19; Amaru. 88;<BR>जलदोदरेभ्यः Mk. 5; Rs. 3. 12; घनानां<BR>वारिगर्भोदराणां Ś. 7. 4.<BR>--3 Enlargement of<BR>the abdomen from dropsy or<BR>flatulence; तस्य होदरं जज्ञे Ait. Br.<BR>--4 Any<BR>morbid abdominal affection, such<BR>as liver, spleen &c. (said to be of<BR>{8} kinds वात˚, पित्त˚, कफ˚, त्रिलिंग˚<BR>or दूषी˚, प्लीहा˚, बद्धगुद˚, आगंतुक˚<BR>and जल˚).<BR>--5 Slaughter. [cf. L.<BR>uterus; Zend. udara].<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">Page0302-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--आध्मानः flatulence of the belly.<BR>--आमयः disease of the belly,<BR>dysentery, diarrhœa.<BR>--आमयिन् a.<BR>suffering from dysentery.<BR>--आवर्तः<BR>the navel.<BR>--आवेष्टः the tape-worm.<BR>--ग्रंथिः --गुल्मः disease of the spleen.<BR>--त्राणं {1} a cuirass, armour covering<BR>the front of the body. {2} a<BR>bellyband.<BR>--पिशाच a. [उदरे तत्पूर्तौ पिशाच<BR>इव] gluttonous, voracious (having a<BR>devilish appetite).<BR>--(चः) a<BR>glutton.<BR>--पूरं ind. till the belly is full;<BR>उदरपूरं भुंक्ते Sk. eats his fill.<BR>--पोषणं,<BR>--भरणं feeding the belly, support of<BR>life.<BR>--शय a. sleeping on the face<BR>or the belly.<BR>--(यः) fœtus.<BR>--सर्वस्वः<BR>a glutton, an epicure (one to whom<BR>the belly is all-in-all).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरक
उदरक a. Abdominal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरंभरि|उदरम्भरि|उदरम्भरिः
उदरंभरि a. [उदरं बिभर्त्ति, भृ खि मुम्च<BR>P. III. 2. 26]<BR>1 Nourishing one's<BR>own belly, selfish.<BR>--2 Gluttonous,<BR>voracious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरवत्|उदरवन्त्
उदरवत्, उदरिक-ल a. Having a<BR>large belly, corpulent, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिक
उदरवत्, उदरिक-ल a. Having a<BR>large belly, corpulent, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिल|उदरिलः
उदरवत्, उदरिक-ल a. Having a<BR>large belly, corpulent, fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरिन्
उदरिन् a. [उदर-इनि]<BR>1 Having a<BR>large belly, fat, corpulent.<BR>--2<BR>Abdominal.<BR>--णी A pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्य|उदर्यः|उदर्य्य
उदर्य a. [उदर-यत्] Belonging to<BR>the belly.<BR>--र्यं Contents of the<BR>belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदरथिः|उदरथि
उदरथिः [उद्-ऋ-घथिन् Uṇ. 4. 88]<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्कः|उदर्क
उदर्कः [Said to be fr. ऋच्]<BR>1 (a)<BR>End, conclusion; ˚स्वादुनः कर्मणः<BR>Dk. 79; सुखोदर्कं K. 328. (b)<BR>Result, consequence, future result of<BR>an action; उदर्कस्तव कल्याणो भविता<BR>Nala. 12. 67; किंतु कल्याणोदर्कं<BR>भविष्यति U. 4; प्रयत्नः सफलोदर्क<BR>एव Māl. 8; Ms. 4. 176, 11. 10,<BR>9. 25, 12. 18; Pt. 5. 73.<BR>--2<BR>Remote consequence, reward.<BR>--3<BR>Future time, futurity.<BR>--4 Elevation<BR>of a building (as a tower).<BR>--5<BR>Surpassing.<BR>--6 N. of a tree<BR>Vanguiera Spinosa Roxb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्चिस्|उदर्च्चिस्
उदर्चिस् a. [ऊर्ध्वमर्चिः शिखाऽस्य]<BR>Shining or blazing upwards,<BR>resplendent, radiant, glowing;<BR>स्फुरन्नुदर्चिः सहसा तृतीयादक्ष्णः कृशानुः किल<BR>निष्पपात Ku. 3. 71, 7. 79;<BR>R. 7. 24, 15. 76. --m.<BR>1 Fire;<BR>प्रक्षिप्योदर्चिषं कक्षे शेरते तेऽभिमारुतं Śi. 2. 42,<BR>20. 75.<BR>--2 The god of love.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0302-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्दः|उदर्द|उदर्द्द
उदर्दः [अर्द-अच्] (In Medic.)<BR>Erysipelas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदर्धः|उदर्ध
उदर्धः Scarlet fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवग्रहः|उदवग्रह
उदवग्रहः A Svarita accent<BR>depending on an Udātta which stands<BR>in the Avagraha q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवसानीय
उदवसानीय a. Ved. Last, final.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदवसितं|उदवसित
उदवसितं [उद् --अव --सो --क्त] A<BR>house, dwelling; जानीषे<BR>रेभिलस्योदवसितं Mk. 4; Śi. 11. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदश्रु
उदश्रु a. [उद्गतान्यश्रूणि यस्य]<BR>Bursting into tears, one whose tears<BR>gush forth, weeping; तस्य पश्यन्<BR>ससौमित्रेरुदश्रुर्वसतिद्रुमान् R. 12. 14;<BR>Amaru. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्
उदस् {c4c} P. [उद्-अस्]<BR>1 To cast<BR>up, throw up; Śi. 15. 81; to<BR>raise, lift up, elevate, erect;<BR>स्वयमिति मुग्धवधूमुदास दोर्भ्यां<BR>Śi. 7. 49; पुच्छमुदस्यति Sk.<BR>--2 To<BR>throw down; उदस्ताधोरणः Dk. 35.<BR>--3 To throw out, expel, drive away,<BR>leave, quit; उदस्य धैर्यं दयितेन सादरं<BR>Ki. 8. 50.<BR>--4 To destroy, dispel;<BR>रिपुतिमिरं Ki. 1. 46.<BR>--5 To drive,<BR>propel; Ki. 8. 55.<BR>--6 To turn<BR>away.<BR>--7 To take pains, make<BR>efforts. --pass. To be driven off,<BR>fall off, deviate from; अतिमूढ उदस्यते<BR>नयात् Ki. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदसनं|उदसन
उदसनं<BR>1 Throwing, raising,<BR>erecting.<BR>--2 Expelling, turning out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदस्त
उदस्त p. p.<BR>1 Thrown or cast up,<BR>raised, erected.<BR>--2 Turned out,<BR>expelled.<BR>--3 Removed, scattered.<BR>--4<BR>Shamed, humbled, humiliated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासः|उदास
उदासः [उद्-अस्-घञ्]<BR>1 Throwing<BR>upwards, elevation, raising.<BR>--2<BR>Expulsion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्त|उदात्तं|उदात्तः
उदात्त a. [उद्-आदा-क्त]<BR>1 High,<BR>elevated, lofty, exalted, noble; ˚अन्वयैः<BR>K. 92; Ratn. 4; sublime; Ve. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Noble, dignified; अत्युदात्तसुजनश्चंद्रकेतुः<BR>U. 6.<BR>--3 Generous, bountiful, donor.<BR>--4 Famous, illustrious, great;<BR>Śi. 20. 82; ललितोदात्तमहिमा<BR>Bv. 1. 79.<BR>--5 Dear, beloved.<BR>--6 Highly<BR>or acutely accented (as a Svara),<BR>see below.<BR>--त्तः<BR>1 The acute<BR>accent, a high or sharp tone;<BR>उच्चैरुदात्तः P. I. 2. 29; ताल्वादिषु सभागेषु<BR>स्थानेषुर्ध्वभागे निष्पन्नोऽजुदात्तः Sk.; see<BR>under अनुदात्त also; निहंत्यरीनेकपदे<BR>यउदात्तः स्वरानिव Śi. 2. 95.<BR>--2 Gift,<BR>donation.<BR>--3 A kind of musical<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-b" target="_blank">Page0303-b+ 56</a>]<BR>instrument, a large drum.<BR>--4 A variety<BR>of the hero; see धीरोदात्त.<BR>--त्तं (In<BR>Rhet.) A figure of speech which<BR>describes supermundane<BR>prosperity, or an action of one that is<BR>great represented collaterally to<BR>the subject in hand;<BR>लोकातिशयसंपत्तिवर्णनोदात्तमुच्यते । यद्वापि प्रस्तुतस्यांगं महतां<BR>चरितं भवेत् ॥ S. D. 752; cf. also<BR>K. P. 10; उदात्तं वस्तुनः संपन्महतां चोपलक्षणं.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--श्रुति a. Pronounced with<BR>the acute accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदात्ततर
उदात्ततर a. More elevated, more<BR>acute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदान|उदानः
उदान See under {1} उदन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाप्यं
उदाप्यं ind. Ved. Against the<BR>stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदायुध
उदायुध a. With uplifted<BR>weapon, upraising weapons;<BR>मनुजपशुभिर्निर्मर्यादैर्भवद्भिरुदायुधैः Ve. 3. 22;<BR>उदायुधानापततस्तान्दृप्तान्प्रेक्ष्य राघवः<BR>R. 12. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदार|उदारः
उदार a.<BR>1 Generous, liberal,<BR>munificent.<BR>--2 (a) Noble, exalted,<BR>dignified; स तथेति विनेतुरुदारमतेः<BR>R. 8. 91, 5. 12; वाचः 65; Bg. 7. 18. (b)<BR>High, lofty, great, best, illustrious,<BR>distinguished; ˚कीर्तेः Ki. 1. 18;<BR>तपसः Bh. 3. 51.<BR>--3 Honest,<BR>sincere, upright.<BR>--4 Good, nice, fine;<BR>उदारः कल्पः Ś. 5.<BR>--5 Proper, right.<BR>--6 Eloquent.<BR>--7 Kind, soft,<BR>agreeable; ˚वाचः कन्यकाः R. 14. 77.<BR>--8<BR>Rich, plentiful; उदारमभ्यवहारविधिं<BR>Dk. 49; Mu. 3. 8.<BR>--9 Large, extensive,<BR>grand, splendid;<BR>साकेतोपवनमुदारमध्युवास R. 13. 79; उदारनपथ्यभृतां 6. 6<BR>richly dressed.<BR>--10 Beautiful,<BR>charming, lovely; Ku. 7. 14;<BR>Śi. 5. 21; see उदारदर्शन below;<BR>R. 16. 26, 51.<BR>--11 Unperplexed.<BR>--12 Exciting, driving forth (Ved.).<BR>--रं ind.<BR>1 Loudly; Śi. 4. 33.<BR>--2<BR>By means of arguments;<BR>Ki. 12. 40.<BR>--रः Ved.<BR>1 A rising fog or<BR>vapour.<BR>--2 A sort of grain with<BR>long stalks.<BR>--3 A figure in<BR>Rhetoric which attributes greatness to<BR>inanimate objects.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन्,<BR>चेतस्, -चरित, -मनस्, -सत्त्व a.<BR>nobleminded, magnanimous; उदारचरितानां<BR>तु वसुधैव कुटुंबकं H. 1.<BR>--धी a. {1} of<BR>sublime genius, highly intelligent;<BR>धियः समग्रैः स गुणैरुदारधीः R. 3. 30.<BR>{2} noble-minded. (--m.) N. of<BR>Viṣṇu. (--f.) good abilities.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">Page0303-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--दर्शन a. good-looking (having<BR>large eyes); तथा हि ते शीलमुदारदर्शने<BR>Ku. 5. 36.<BR>--रमणीय a. grand and<BR>lovely, transcendental; Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारता
उदारता<BR>1 Liberality, generosity.<BR>--2 Richness (as of expression);<BR>वचसां Māl. 1. 7; Ś. 6; (as applied<BR>to words) उदारता =<BR>कठिनवर्णघटनारूपविकटत्वलक्षणा R. G.; (as applied to the<BR>sense) = चुंबनं देहि मे भार्ये कामचांडाल तृप्तये<BR>इत्यादिग्राम्यार्थपरिहारः ibid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदारथि|उदारथिः
उदारथि a.<BR>1 Going upwards.<BR>--2<BR>Rising, enlightening the organs of<BR>sense.<BR>--3 Steaming (as a hot dish).<BR>--थिः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावत्सरः|उदावत्सर
उदावत्सरः A year, one of the<BR>five years forming a period.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदावर्तः|उदावर्त|उदावर्त्त|उदावर्त्तः
उदावर्तः A disease of the bowels,<BR>‘iliac passion’ (characterized by<BR>the retention of excrements).<BR>--र्ता<BR>A painful menstruation with foamy<BR>blood; सफेनिलमुदावर्ता रजः कृच्छ्रेण<BR>मुंचति Suśr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्
उदास् {c2c} A. [उद्-आस्] To be<BR>indifferent or unconcerned, be<BR>careless or apathetic; to be passive or<BR>inactive; तत्किमित्युदासते भरताः<BR>Māl. 1; विधाय वैरं सामर्षे नरोऽरौ य<BR>उदासते Śi. 2. 42; Bg. 9. 9; Sān.<BR>K. 20; not to share in, show no<BR>interest in; Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास|उदासः
उदास, --सिन् a. Indifferent,<BR>apathetic, unconcerned.<BR>--सः, --सिन् m.<BR>1 A<BR>stoic, philosopher.<BR>--2 One who<BR>has no passion for anything, a<BR>religious mendicant in general.<BR>--3<BR>Indifference, apathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासिन्
उदास, --सिन् a. Indifferent,<BR>apathetic, unconcerned.<BR>--सः, --सिन् m.<BR>1 A<BR>stoic, philosopher.<BR>--2 One who<BR>has no passion for anything, a<BR>religious mendicant in general.<BR>--3<BR>Indifference, apathy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासितृ
उदासितृ a. Indifferent, apathetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदासीन|उदासीनः
उदासीन pres. p.<BR>1 Indifferent,<BR>unconcerned, apathetic, passive;<BR>तद्दर्शिनमुदासींनं त्वामेव पुरुष विदुः Ku. 2. 13<BR>(taking no part in the creation of<BR>the material universe); see सांख्य;<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--2 (In law) Not involved in<BR>any dispute.<BR>--3 Neutral (as a king<BR>or nation).<BR>--नः<BR>1 A stranger.<BR>--2<BR>A neutral, an indifferent person;<BR>अरिमित्रोदासीनव्यवस्था Mu. 5;<BR>Ms. 7. 158; Y. 1. 345; Bg. 6. 9.<BR>--3 A<BR>common acquaintance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदास्थित|उदास्थितः
उदास्थित a. Set over, appointed<BR>to.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A superintendent.<BR>--2 A<BR>doorkeeper.<BR>--3 A spy, an emissary.<BR>--4 An ascetic who has given up<BR>his vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0303-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहित
उदाहित a. Elevated, raised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृ
उदाहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To relate, narrate,<BR>declare, announce.<BR>--2 To say, speak,<BR>utter; उदाजहार द्रुपदात्मजा गिरः<BR>Ki. 1. 27; Mk. 9. 4; Pt. 2.;<BR>चिकित्सका दोषमुदाहरंति M. 2; Māl. 1;<BR>त्वां कामिनो मदनदूतिमुदाहरंति V. 4. 11;<BR>mutter, repeat; धर्माक्षराणि Mk. 8.<BR>--3 To cite as an instance or<BR>illustration, illustrate; त्वमुदाथियस्व<BR>कथमन्यथा जनैः Śi. 15. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहरणं|उदाहरण
उदाहरणं<BR>1 Relating, declaration,<BR>saying, utterance.<BR>--2 Narration,<BR>recital, opening a conversation;<BR>अथांगिरसमग्रण्यमुदाहरणवस्तुषु Ku. 6. 65;<BR>अद्भुतोदाहरणानि Mv. 5 stories or<BR>narrations.<BR>--3 A declaratory song or<BR>poem, a sort of panegyric<BR>beginning with words like जयति and full<BR>of alliteration; पत्रे निवेशितमुदाहरणं<BR>प्रियायाः V. 2. 14; चारणेभ्यस्त्वदीयं<BR>जयोदाहरणं श्रुत्वा V. 1; जयोदाहरणं<BR>बाह्वोर्गापयामास किन्नरान् R. 4. 78;<BR>(येन केनापि तालेन गद्यपद्यसमन्वितं ।<BR>जयत्युपक्रमं मालिन्यादिप्रासविचित्रितम् ॥ तदुदाहरणं<BR>नाम विभक्त्यष्टांगसंयुतं । Pratāparudra.)<BR>--4 An instance, example,<BR>illustration; समूलघातमघ्नंतः परान्नोद्यंति<BR>मानिनः । प्रध्वंसितांधतमसस्तत्रोदाहरणं रविः ॥<BR>Śi. 2. 33; किमुदाहरणं Kāśi.<BR>--5 (In<BR>Nyāya) The third member of an<BR>Indian syllogism (which has five<BR>members).<BR>--6 Beginning,<BR>commencement, introduction.<BR>--7<BR>Exhibition, illustration; U. 1.<BR>--8 (In<BR>Rhet.) An illustration reckoned as<BR>a figure of speech by some<BR>rhetoricians. It resembles अर्थांतरन्यास;<BR>e. g. अमितगुणोपि पदार्थो दोषेणैकेन निंदितो<BR>भवति । निखिलरसायणराजो गंधेनोग्रेण लशुन<BR>इव ॥ R. G. (For a clear distinction<BR>between the two figures see R. G.,<BR>under उदाहरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहारः|उदाहार
उदाहारः<BR>1 An example or<BR>illustration.<BR>--2 The beginning of a speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृत
उदाहृत p. p.<BR>1 Said, uttered.<BR>--2<BR>Named, called; श्रुतान्वितो दशरथ<BR>इत्युदाहृतः Bk. 1. 1.<BR>--3 Illustrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदाहृतिः|उदाहृति
उदाहृतिः f. An example,<BR>illustration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदि
उदि {c2c} P.<BR>1 To rise (as a star,<BR>cloud &c.) (fig. also); come up;<BR>उदेति पूर्वं कुसुमं ततः फलं Ś. 7. 30;<BR>उदेति सविता ताम्रस्ताम्र एवास्तमोति च<BR>Subhāṣ.; Māl. 2. 10; Ki. 2. 36;<BR>Bk. 6. 110, 8. 35, 18. 20; to be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-b" target="_blank">Page0304-b+ 57</a>]<BR>seen, appear.<BR>--2 To be produced,<BR>come out or arise from, spring or<BR>proceed from; उदितदयः Dk. 13;<BR>पुण्यः कृशानोरुदियाय धूमः R. 7. 26;<BR>उदितश्रियं 1. 93 v. l.; Ś. 1. 26.<BR>--3<BR>To go out, escape.<BR>--4 To start up;<BR>R. 17. 77.<BR>--5 To rise up against;<BR>Ku. 2. 57; य एनमुदीयाद्रथी Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदय|उदयः
उदय a. (In gram.) Following,<BR>coming after or upon (as a letter,<BR>accent &c.); उदयशब्दः परशब्दसमानार्थः<BR>प्रातिशाख्येषु प्रसिद्धः,<BR>--यः<BR>1 Rise (fig<BR>also); चंद्रोदय इवोदधेः R. 12. 36,<BR>2. 73; going upwards, ascending (as<BR>of the sun, stars &c.).<BR>--2 (a)<BR>Rising up, coming forth; द्रविण˚<BR>acquisition of wealth; Pt. 2.; so<BR>भाग्य˚ dawn of fortune; Amaru. 25;<BR>स्वगुणोदयेन Pt. 1. 94. (b)<BR>Appearance, becoming visible, production;<BR>घनोदयः प्राक् Ś. 7. 30; मेघ˚<BR>Ku. 6. 54; हसितमन्यनिमित्तकृतोदयं Ś. 2. 11<BR>raised from some other cause;<BR>Amaru. 88; Ś. 7. 8; फलोदय R. 1. 5<BR>rising or accomplishment of the<BR>fruit; Ms. 3. 169; Ku. 3. 18.<BR>--3<BR>Creation (opp. प्रलय); यौ तौ<BR>स्वप्नावबोधौ तौ भूतानां प्रलयोदयौ Ku. 2. 8.<BR>--4 The eastern mountain (behind<BR>which the sun is supposed to<BR>rise); यैर्यत्र दृश्यते भास्वान्स तेषामुदयः<BR>स्मृतः; उदयगूढशशांकमरीचिभिः V. 3. 6.<BR>--5 Advancement, prosperity, rise;<BR>(opp. व्यसन); तेजोद्वयस्य<BR>युगपद्व्यसनोदयाभ्यां Ś. 4. 1; उदये मदवाच्यमुज्झता<BR>R. 8. 84; K. 5; importance,<BR>celebrity; ˚उन्मुखे त्वयि R. 11. 73.<BR>--6<BR>Elevation, exaltation, rise, growth;<BR>उदयमस्तमयं च रघूद्वहात् R. 9. 9;<BR>तमुदयाय न वा नवयौवना 7; आत्मोदयः परग्लानिः<BR>Śi. 2. 30, 11. 60.<BR>--7 Result,<BR>consequence; असुखोदयं कर्म Ms. 4. 70;<BR>Amaru. 42; following;<BR>नोदात्तस्वरितोदयं P. VIII. 4. 67.<BR>--8<BR>Accomplishment, fulfilment; उपस्थितोदयं<BR>R. 3. 1; प्रारंभसदृशोदयः 1. 15.<BR>--9 Profit,<BR>advantage.<BR>--10 Income, revenue;<BR>Ms. 7. 55; Y. 2. 43.<BR>--11 Interest,<BR>consideration paid for the use of money;<BR>Y. 2. 67, 146.<BR>--12 Light, splendour.<BR>--13 Outlet, exit.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अचलः<BR>--अद्रिः, --गिरिः, --पर्वतः, --शैलः the<BR>eastern mountain behind which the<BR>sun moon &c. are supposed to rise;<BR>उदयगिरिवनालीबालमंदारपुष्पं Udb.;<BR>श्रितोदयाद्रेरीभसायमुच्चकैः Śi. 1. 16; तत<BR>उदयगिरेरिवैक एव Māl. 2. 10.<BR>--क्रमः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">Page0304-c+ 56</a>]<BR>gradual rise; नाडीनां Māl. 5. 2 by<BR>gradually inflating or filling with<BR>wind the Nāḍīs, (as in the act of<BR>restraining the wind).<BR>--पुरं N. of<BR>the capital of Mārwār.<BR>--प्रस्थः the<BR>plateau of the mountain behind<BR>which the sun is supposed to rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयनं|उदयन|उदयनः
उदयनं<BR>1 Rising, ascending, going<BR>up.<BR>--2 Result, consequence.<BR>--3<BR>End, conclusion.<BR>--नः<BR>1 N. of<BR>Agastya.<BR>--2 N. of the king Vatsa;<BR>प्राप्यावंतीनुदयनकथाकोविदग्रामवृद्धान्<BR>Me. 30. [A celebrated Prince of the lunar<BR>race, who is usually styled Vatsarāja.<BR>He reigned at Kauśāmbī.<BR>Vāsavadattā, Princess of Ujjayinī, saw<BR>him in a dream and fell in love with<BR>him. He was decoyed to that city<BR>and there kept in prison by<BR>Chaṇḍamahāsena, the king. But on being released<BR>by the minister he carried off<BR>Vāsavadattā from her father and a<BR>rival suitor. Udayana is the hero of the<BR>play called Ratnāvalī and his life has<BR>been made the subject of several other<BR>minor compositions. See Vatsa also].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयनीय
उदयनीय a. Belonging to the end<BR>or conclusion, concluding (as<BR>a ceremony).<BR>--या A concluding<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदयिन्
उदयिन् a.<BR>1 Rising or ascending.<BR>--2 Streaming or flowing forth;<BR>Māl. 5. 17.<BR>--3 Prosperous, flourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदित|उदितः
उदित p. p.<BR>1 Risen, ascended;<BR>उदितभूयिष्ठः Māl. 1 mostly risen;<BR>Bv. 2. 85; नित्योदितः Bh. 3. 80<BR>ever-existing.<BR>--2 High, tall, lofty.<BR>--3 Grown,<BR>augmented.<BR>--4 Born, produced.<BR>--5 Spoken, uttered (fr. वद्).<BR>--तं<BR>1 A kind of perfume.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>accent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदित a. well<BR>grounded in the Śāstras.<BR>--होमिन्<BR>a. sacrificing after sunrise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदितिः|उदिति
उदितिः f.<BR>1 Ascending, rising (of<BR>the sun).<BR>--2 Setting.<BR>--3 Speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेष्यत्
उदेष्यत् a. Increasing, rising;<BR>Śi. 2. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्ष्
उदीक्ष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To look up to,<BR>look at, view, behold;<BR>सप्रणाममुदीक्षिताः Ku. 6. 7, 7. 67; Amaru. 71.<BR>--2 To expect, look out for, wait for,<BR>शत्रुव्यसनं Mu. 4; त्रीणि वर्षाण्युदीक्षेत<BR>कुमार्यृतुमती सती Ms. 9. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीक्षणं|उदीक्षण
उदीक्षणं<BR>1 Looking up to.<BR>--2<BR>Seeing, beholding, seeking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीचीन|उदीचीनं
उदीचीन, उदीच्य See under उदंच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीच्य|उदीच्यं|उदीच्यः
उदीचीन, उदीच्य See under उदंच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0304-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीप|उदीपः
उदीप a. [उद्गता आपो यत्र, अप ईप्]<BR>Flooded.<BR>--पः High water,<BR>inundation, flood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्
उदीर् {c2c} A. [उद्-ईर्]<BR>1 To rise<BR>(sound &c.); उदैरत रणितानि Dk. 123<BR>were heard.<BR>--2 To start (to go or<BR>come).<BR>--3 To move upwards,<BR>ascend, go up.<BR>--4 To arise, originate.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to rise or move.<BR>--2 To utter, pronounce, speak;<BR>गिरमुदीरयति K. 13; U. 5, 6;<BR>उदीरितोर्थः पशुनापि गृह्यते Pt. 1. 43; so<BR>आलोकशद्वं R. 2. 9.<BR>--3 To<BR>call, name; स भीमरूपः शिव इत्युदीर्यते<BR>Ku. 5. 77.<BR>--4 To put forth;<BR>यदशोकोयमुदीरयिष्यति R. 8. 62.<BR>--5 To cast,<BR>throw, roll down (as dice);<BR>उदीरयामास सलीलमक्षान् R. 6. 18; to<BR>discharge, drive forward.<BR>--6 To raise,<BR>throw up; उदीरितं रजः Śi. 12. 58;<BR>उदैरयच्छिरः Dk. 103 expanded its<BR>hood.<BR>--7 To display, manifest, make<BR>visible, cause;<BR>तिसृभिस्त्वमवस्थाभिर्महिमानमुदीरयन् Ku. 2. 6; Śi. 11. 7.<BR>--8<BR>To bring about, effect; Ki. 13. 28.<BR>--9 To rouse, excite, stimulate;<BR>उदीरितेंद्रियः Ku. 4. 41; ˚धी<BR>acuteminded. --pass.<BR>1 To be cast or<BR>thrown upwards, excited, uttered<BR>&c.<BR>--2 To sound.<BR>--3 To issue forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीरणं|उदीरण
उदीरणं<BR>1 Utterance,<BR>pronunciation, expression; उद्घातः प्रणवो यासां<BR>न्यायैस्त्रिभिरुदीरणं Ku. 2. 12.<BR>--2<BR>Speaking, saying.<BR>--3 Throwing,<BR>discharging (as a missile.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीर्ण|उदीर्णः
उदीर्ण p. p. [ईर्-क्त]<BR>1 Grown,<BR>ascended, risen, produced, caused;<BR>Śi. 18. 37.<BR>--2 Puffed up, elated,<BR>grown haughty;<BR>भवल्लब्धवरोदीर्णस्तारकाख्यो महासुरः Ku. 2. 32.<BR>--3<BR>Excited, stimulated, roused;<BR>Śi. 1. 32; Dk. 43, 47.<BR>--4 Increased,<BR>intense.<BR>--5 Generous, great;<BR>excellent.<BR>--6 Uttered, pronounced;<BR>Śi. 13. 42.<BR>--7 Ready, strung; ˚धन्वा<BR>U. 5. 11.<BR>--र्णः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दीधिति a. intensely bright.<BR>--वेग a. violent, impetuous in<BR>its course (as a torrent).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदीषित
उदीषित a. Risen, elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुंबरः|उदुम्बर|उदुंबर|उदुम्बरं|उदुम्बरः
उदुंबरः See उडुंबर. ˚मशक =<BR>कूपमंडूक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुंबल|उदुम्बल|उदुम्बलः
उदुंबल a. Ved. Mighty, of<BR>extended power (उरुबल).<BR>--लः The<BR>fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदुष्ट
उदुष्ट a. Ved. Red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदूखल|उदूखलं
उदूखल = उलूखल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदृच्
उदृच् f. [उत्कृष्टा ऋक्]<BR>1 An<BR>excellent Ṛk.<BR>--2 Future time.<BR>--3<BR>Remainder, conclusion, end.<BR>--4<BR>Prosperity, rise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदेजय
उदेजय a. Shaking, causing to<BR>tremble, terrifying; उदेजयान्<BR>भूतगणान् न्यषेधीत् Bk. 1. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदोजस्
उदोजस् a. Very powerful,<BR>violent (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गंधि|उद्गन्धि
उद्गंधि a.<BR>1 Fragrant;<BR>विजृंभणोद्गंधिषु कुड्मलेषु R. 16. 47.<BR>--2 Having<BR>a strong smell (good or bad).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गम्
उद्गम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To rise or go up,<BR>ascend (as a star &c.);<BR>असह्यवातोद्गतरेणुमंडला Rs. 1. 10. v. l.<BR>--2 To<BR>shoot up, dart upwards, appear;<BR>अचिरोद्गतपल्लवं V. 4. 23; Rs. 6. 18;<BR>so उद्गतशृंगो वत्सः.<BR>--3 To rise or<BR>spring from, proceed, originate,<BR>arise; इत्युद्गताः पौरवधूमुखेभ्यः शृण्वन्<BR>कथाः R. 7. 16; Amaru. 91.<BR>--4 To<BR>go out, break out, depart (as life<BR>&c.).<BR>--5 To be famous or<BR>wellknown, spread; उन्नाभ इत्युद्गतनामधेयः<BR>R. 18. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गत|उद्गतं
उद्गत p. p.<BR>1 Gone up, risen,<BR>ascended.<BR>--2 Proceeded forth or from.<BR>--3 Gone, departed.<BR>--4 Vomited.<BR>--ता N. of a metre.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--असु<BR>a. deceased, dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गतिः|उद्गति
उद्गतिः f.<BR>1 Going up, rising,<BR>ascent.<BR>--2 Appearance; कुसुम˚ K. 59;<BR>rise, origin.<BR>--3 Vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमः|उद्गम
उद्गमः<BR>1 Going up, rising (of<BR>stars); ascent; आज्यधूमोद्गमेन<BR>Ś. 1. 15.<BR>--2 Standing erect (of hair);<BR>रोमोद्गमः प्रादुरभूदुमायाः Ku. 7. 77;<BR>व्यक्तरोमोद्गमत्वात् M. 4. 1;<BR>Amaru. 36.<BR>--3 Going out, departure,<BR>expiry; as in प्राण˚.<BR>--4 Birth,<BR>production, creation; पारिजातस्योद्गमः<BR>Māl. 2; appearance; फलेन सहकारस्य<BR>पुष्पोद्गम इव प्रजाः R. 4. 9; V. 4. 38;<BR>Bh. 2. 70; कतिपयकुसुगोद्गमः कदंबः<BR>U. 3. 20; so मांस˚, पक्ष˚, ग्रंथि˚ &c.;<BR>Amaru. 81; origin, parentage;<BR>Māl. 2.<BR>--5 Action, vision (of eyes);<BR>Māl. 1. 35.<BR>--6 Projection,<BR>elevation; पयोधरोद्गमां Māl. 7.<BR>--7 A shoot<BR>(of a plant); हरिततृणोद्गमशंकया<BR>मृगीभिः Ki. 5. 38.<BR>--8 Vomiting, casting<BR>up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमनं|उद्गमन
उद्गमनं Rising, becoming visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गमनीय|उद्गमनीयं
उद्गमनीय pot. p. To be gone up<BR>or ascended.<BR>--यं A pair of<BR>bleached or washed clothes (तत्स्यादुद्गमनीयं<BR>यद्धौतयोर्वस्त्रयोर्युगं); धौतोद्गमनीयवासिनी<BR>Dk. 42; गृहीतपत्युद्गमनीयवस्त्रा<BR>Ku. 7. 11 (where Malli. renders उ˚ by<BR>धौतवस्त्रं, and says युगग्रहणं तु<BR>प्रायिकाभिप्रायं &c.; see ad loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गाढ|उद्गाढं
उद्गाढ a. Deep, intense,<BR>violent, strong, excessive, much;<BR>उद्गाढरागोदयाः Māl. 5. 7, 6. 6.<BR>--ढं<BR>Excess. --ind. Excessively, extremely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गातृ
उद्गातृ, उद्गार &c. See under उद्गै,<BR>उद्गॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गार|उद्गारः
उद्गातृ, उद्गार &c. See under उद्गै,<BR>उद्गॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गुर्
उद्गुर् {c6c} A. To raise the voice<BR>in a menacing manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गूर्ण|उद्गूर्णं|उद्गूर्ण्ण
उद्गूर्ण p. p. [गुर्-क्त]<BR>1 Raised,<BR>uplifted, held up; क्रोधोद्गूर्णगदस्य<BR>Ve. 6. 12; Śi. 5. 25.<BR>--2 Erected,<BR>excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गॄ
उद्गॄ {c6c} P.<BR>1 To eject, spit out,<BR>vomit; उद्गिरतो यद्गरलं फणिनः पुष्णासि<BR>परिमलोद्गारैः Bv. 1. 11; उद्गिरन्निव स्नेहं<BR>Śi. 14. 1.<BR>--2 (a) To emit, send or put<BR>forth, pour down or out, discharge,<BR>belch out; सहांभसैवापदमुद्गिरंति<BR>Pt. 5. 67; निक्षेपणात् रागमिवोद्गिरंतौ<BR>Ku. 1. 33. (b) To send out of the<BR>mouth, speak, utter (as words);<BR>महीपतेः शासनमुज्जगार R. 14. 53;<BR>Ve. 5. 14; यदुद्गिरति भ्रमरः Mu. 2. 11<BR>(where it also means ‘vomits’<BR>or ‘emits’).<BR>--3 To breathe out.<BR>--4<BR>To rise from. --Caus. To cause to<BR>pour forth, raise (as sound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गारः|उद्गार
उद्गारः [उद्-गॄ-घञ् P. III. 3. 29]<BR>1 (a) Ejection, spitting out,<BR>vomiting, giving out, emitting;<BR>खर्जूरीस्कंधनद्धानां मदोद्गारसुगंधिषु R. 4. 57;<BR>Bh. 2. 36; सलिलोद्गारमुच्चैर्विमानाः<BR>Me. 63, 69; Śi. 12. 9. (b) Oozing,<BR>flowing out, stream, issuing out;<BR>सनिर्झरोद्गार इवाद्रिराजः R. 6. 60;<BR>रुधिर˚दिग्धाखिलांगाः Mv. 6. 33.<BR>--2<BR>Repeating, narration, citing repeatedly;<BR>Māl. 2. 13; साम˚ K. 42;<BR>H. 3. 106; सौजन्य˚ Mv. 4 expression of<BR>goodness.<BR>--3 Quantity, mass (thrown<BR>out); Mu. 3.<BR>--4 Spittle, saliva.<BR>--5 Eructation, belching.<BR>--6 Sound,<BR>roaring, echo, hissing sound (शब्दः,<BR>कंठगर्जनं, नागवायुकर्म); Śānti. 1. 21;<BR>गंभीरगह्वर˚ Māl. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गारिन्
उद्गारिन्<BR>1 Going up, rising, being<BR>sent forth; Mv. 3. 29; U. 4. 29<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">Page0306-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 Emitting, sending forth,<BR>pouring down; धारास्वनोद्गारिदरीमुखोऽसौ<BR>R. 13. 47; Mk. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0305-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गिरणं|उद्गिरण
उद्गिरणं<BR>1 Vomiting.<BR>--2 Ejecting<BR>anything (as saliva) from the<BR>mouth, slavering.<BR>--3 Eructation,<BR>belch.<BR>--4 Extermination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गै
उद्गै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sing in a loud<BR>tone, sing aloud; उद्गास्यतामिच्छति<BR>किन्नराणां Ku. 1. 8; गेयमुद्गातुकामा<BR>Me. 86; to sing (in general); उद्गीयमानं<BR>वनदेवताभिः R. 2. 12; निभृताक्षरमुज्जगे<BR>Śi. 6. 20.<BR>--2 To begin to sing.<BR>--3<BR>To sing or chant (applied to the<BR>singing of Sāmaveda); साम<BR>सामविदसंगमुज्जगौ Śi. 14. 21; cf. उद्गातृ.<BR>--4<BR>To announce, to celebrate in song.<BR>--5 To sing before one (with acc.).<BR>--6 To fill or make resonant with<BR>song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गातृ
उद्गातृ m. One of the four<BR>principal priests at a sacrifice, one who<BR>chants the hymns of the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गाथा
उद्गाथा A variety of the Āryā<BR>measure, the same as Gīti q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीतिः|उद्गीति
उद्गीतिः f.<BR>1 Singing aloud.<BR>--2<BR>Chanting of the Sāmaveda.<BR>--3<BR>A variety of the Āryā metre; see<BR>Appendix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्गीथः|उद्गीथ
उद्गीथः [उद्-गै-थक्]<BR>1 Chanting<BR>of the Sāmaveda (the office of an<BR>udgātṛ).<BR>--2 The second part of<BR>the Sāmaveda; भूयांस उद्गीथविदो<BR>वसंति U. 2. 3.<BR>--3 Designation of<BR>ओम्, the three syllabled name of<BR>God.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रंथ्|उद्ग्रन्थ्
उद्ग्रंथ् {c1c} {c9c} U.<BR>1 To bind up, tie<BR>into bundles.<BR>--2 To tie up, put or<BR>sew together (as garlands &c.);<BR>इयमुद्ग्रथते स्रजो विचित्राः Mu. 1. 4;<BR>tie or fasten, intertwine;<BR>लताप्रतानोद्ग्रथितैः स केशैः R. 2. 8.<BR>--3 To<BR>unbind, loosen (as a knot &c.);<BR>Śi. 10. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रंथ|उद्ग्रन्थ|उद्ग्रन्थः
उद्ग्रंथ a. Unbound, loosened.<BR>--थः<BR>A section, chapter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रंथि|उद्ग्रन्थि
उद्ग्रंथि a.<BR>1 Untied (fig. also).<BR>--2 Free from worldly ties or<BR>attachments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रह्
उद्ग्रह् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To take up, lift up;<BR>शक्तिं चोग्रामुदग्रहीत् Bk. 15. 52;<BR>elevate, erect, raise; उद्गृहीतालकांताः<BR>Me. 8.<BR>--2 To take or draw out,<BR>take away.<BR>--3 To deposit.<BR>--4 To<BR>preserve.<BR>--5 To cease (to rain).<BR>--6<BR>To break off, discontinue<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">Page0306-b+ 56</a>]<BR>(speaking). --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to take up,<BR>or out; cause to pay.<BR>--2 To state,<BR>place before, adduce; विशेषविदुषः<BR>शास्त्रं यत्तवोद्ग्राह्यते पुरः Śi. 2. 75.<BR>--3<BR>To extol, laud up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रभणं|उद्ग्रभण
उद्ग्रभणं, --उद्ग्राभः<BR>1 Ved. Taking<BR>up, raising.<BR>--2 Giving, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राभः|उद्ग्राभ
उद्ग्रभणं, --उद्ग्राभः<BR>1 Ved. Taking<BR>up, raising.<BR>--2 Giving, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रहः|उद्ग्रह
उद्ग्रहः, --हणं<BR>1 Taking up, raising.<BR>--2 An object that can be<BR>accomplished by religious or other acts.<BR>--3 Eructation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रहणं|उद्ग्रहण
उद्ग्रहः, --हणं<BR>1 Taking up, raising.<BR>--2 An object that can be<BR>accomplished by religious or other acts.<BR>--3 Eructation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राहः|उद्ग्राह
उद्ग्राहः<BR>1 Lifting or taking up.<BR>--2<BR>(In the Prātiśākhyas) The rule of<BR>Saṃdhi which causes the change of<BR>the terminations अः, ए and ओ to अ<BR>before a following vowel.<BR>--3<BR>Replying in argument; rejoinder.<BR>--4<BR>An objection.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पदवृत्तिः f.<BR>the Saṃdhi called Udgrāha; see<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राहणिका
उद्ग्राहणिका Replying in argument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्राहित|उद्ग्राहितः
उद्ग्राहित p. p.<BR>1 Lifted or taken up.<BR>--2 Taken away.<BR>--3 Excellent;<BR>exalted.<BR>--4 Deposited, delivered.<BR>--5<BR>Bound, tied.<BR>--6 Recalled,<BR>remembered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रीव
उद्ग्रीव, उद्ग्रीविन् a. With the<BR>neck uplifted; उद्ग्रीवैर्मयूरैः<BR>M. 1. 21; Amaru. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ग्रीविन्
उद्ग्रीव, उद्ग्रीविन् a. With the<BR>neck uplifted; उद्ग्रीवैर्मयूरैः<BR>M. 1. 21; Amaru. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घः|उद्घ
उद्घः [उद्-हन् अप् नि˚]<BR>1<BR>Excellence, eminence; (at the end<BR>of comp.); ब्राह्मणोद्धः = an<BR>excellent or superior Brāhmaṇa;<BR>उद्घादयश्च नियतलिंगा न तु विशेष्यलिंगाः<BR>Sk.; cf. मतल्लिकामचर्चिका<BR>प्रकांडमुद्घतल्लजौ प्रशस्तवाचकान्यमूनि Ak.<BR>--2<BR>Happiness.<BR>--3 The hollow hand.<BR>--4 Fire.<BR>--5 A model.<BR>--6 Organic<BR>air in the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घनः|उद्घन
उद्घनः A carpenter's bench (the<BR>plank on which he works);<BR>लौहोद्घनघनस्कंधां ललितापघनां स्त्रियं<BR>Bk. 7. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घातिन्
उद्घातिन् a. Uneven, rough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्
उद्घट् {c1c} A. To open; Ku. 7. 53.<BR>--Caus. (घाटयति)<BR>1 To open,<BR>unlock; निरयनगरद्वारमुद्घाटयंती<BR>Bh. 1. 63; कपाटमुद्घाटयामि Mk. 3.<BR>--2 To<BR>peel off, shell.<BR>--3 To reveal, expose,<BR>make known.<BR>--4 To undertake,<BR>commence.<BR>--5 To rub over, stroke<BR>gently, tickle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घटितं|उद्घटित
उद्घटितं A hint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटः|उद्घाट
उद्घाटः A watch or guard-house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटकः|उद्घाटक|उद्घाटकं
उद्घाटकः<BR>1 A key; उद्घाटको<BR>भवति यंत्रट्टढे कपाटे Mk. 3. 16.<BR>--2 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">Page0306-c+ 55</a>]<BR>rope and bucket of a well (--कं<BR>also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटन|उद्घाटनं
उद्घाटन a. (नी f.) Opening,<BR>unlocking; धर्मं यो न करोति निंदितमतिः<BR>स्वर्गार्गलोद्घाटनं H. 1. 153.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Opening; Ve. 1.<BR>--2 Raising, lifting<BR>up, hoisting.<BR>--3 A key, any means<BR>of opening.<BR>--4 The rope and<BR>bucket of a well; a water-wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घाटित|उद्घाटितः
उद्घाटित p. p.<BR>1 Opened,<BR>manifested.<BR>--2 Undertaken;<BR>commenced.<BR>--3 Raised, lifted up.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. {1} naked. {2} intelligent,<BR>wise.<BR>--ज्ञ a. wise, intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टकः|उद्घट्टक
उद्घट्टकः A kind of time (in<BR>music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टनं|उद्घट्टन
उद्घट्टनं, --ना<BR>1 Friction, striking<BR>against; Me. 61.<BR>--2 Opening<BR>upwards (as a lid).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टना
उद्घट्टनं, --ना<BR>1 Friction, striking<BR>against; Me. 61.<BR>--2 Opening<BR>upwards (as a lid).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घट्टित
उद्घट्टित a.<BR>1 Opened, unlocked.<BR>--2 Separated; Śi. 11. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घसं|उद्घस
उद्घसं Flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घातः|उद्घात
उद्घातः<BR>1 Beginning,<BR>commencement; उद्घातः प्रणवो यासां Ku. 2. 12;<BR>आकुमारकथोद्घातं शालिगोप्यो जगुर्यशः<BR>R. 4. 20.<BR>--2 Allusion, reference;<BR>कथोद्घाताः U. 2.<BR>--3 Striking,<BR>wounding, inflicting an injury.<BR>--4 A stroke,<BR>blow, wound.<BR>--5 Tripping, slipping,<BR>jolting, shaking (as of a carriage);<BR>ययावनुद्घातसुखेन सोऽध्वना Śi. 12. 2;<BR>R. 2. 72; Ve. 2. 28; चक्र˚ V. 1;<BR>U. 5. 1.<BR>--6 Rising, elevation.<BR>--7 A<BR>club, mallet.<BR>--8 A weapon (in<BR>general).<BR>--9 Breathing through the<BR>nostrils as a religious exercise<BR>(Wilson).<BR>--10 A division of a<BR>book, chapter; section.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घुष्
उद्घुष् {c1c} P. To sound, cry out or<BR>shout. {c10c} P. or Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>proclaim, declare aloud.<BR>--2 To fill<BR>with cries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घुष्ट
उद्घुष्ट p. p. Sounded out,<BR>proclaimed.<BR>--ष्टं A sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घोषः|उद्घोष
उद्घोषः<BR>1 Announcing aloud,<BR>proclaiming.<BR>--2 Popular talk, general<BR>report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घृष्
उद्घृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To rub; lessen by<BR>rubbing.<BR>--2 To rub over, strike<BR>against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घर्षणं|उद्घर्षण
उद्घर्षणं<BR>1 Rubbing, rubbing up;<BR>यस्योद्घर्षणलोष्टकैरपि सदा पृष्ठे न जातः<BR>किणः Mk. 2. 11.<BR>--2 Rubbing the<BR>skin with hard substances.<BR>--3 A<BR>cudgel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0306-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्घृष्टं|उद्घृष्ट
उद्घृष्टं A peculiar fault in<BR>pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दंशः|उद्दंश
उद्दंशः<BR>1 A bug.<BR>--2 A louse.<BR>--3<BR>A mosquito, gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दंड|उद्दण्ड|उद्दण्डः
उद्दंड a.<BR>1 With the stalk, stem,<BR>or staff raised or rising up;<BR>उद्दंडपद्म गृहदीर्घिकाणां R. 16. 46;<BR>˚धवलातपत्राः Māl. 6 long; H. 2. 29.<BR>--2 Formidable, terrific.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पालः {1} a punisher (whether<BR>king or magistrate). {2} a kind of<BR>fish. {3} a kind of serpent; cf. (<BR>उदंडपाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दंतुर|उद्दन्तुर|उद्दन्तुरः
उद्दंतुर a.<BR>1 Large-toothed or<BR>having projecting teeth.<BR>--2 High,<BR>tall (उत्तुंग).<BR>--3 Terrific,<BR>formidable (कराल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दमः|उद्दम
उद्दमः Subduing, overpowering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दांत|उद्दान्त
उद्दांत a.<BR>1 Energetic.<BR>--2 Humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दानं|उद्दान
उद्दानं [दो बंधने ल्युट्]<BR>1 Binding,<BR>confinement; उद्दाने क्रियमाणे तु<BR>मत्स्यानां तत्र रज्जुभिः Mb.<BR>--2 Taming,<BR>subduing.<BR>--3 The middle, the<BR>waist.<BR>--4 A fireplace.<BR>--5 The<BR>submarine fire.<BR>--6 Entrance of the sun<BR>into a zodiacal sign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दाम|उद्दामः
उद्दाम a.<BR>1 Unbound,<BR>unrestrained, unchecked, free, bold; Śi. 4. 10.<BR>--2 (a) Strong, powerful, violent;<BR>Pt. 3. 148; Māl. 3. 7;<BR>˚देहपरिदाहमहाज्वराणि 6. 13. (b) Furious,<BR>intoxicated; स्रोतस्युद्दामदिग्गजे R. 1. 78;<BR>Śi. 11. 19; U. 3. 6.<BR>--3 Dreadful,<BR>formidable; ˚शरीरसंनिवेशः Māl. 3.<BR>--4 Self-willed.<BR>--5 Luxuriant, large,<BR>great, excessive; Me. 25;<BR>उद्दामोत्कलिकां Ratn. 2. 4, 4. 22; गंधोद्दामा<BR>धरा exhaling great smell<BR>Mk. 5. 22.<BR>--6 Proud, haughty;<BR>पौलस्त्यविजयोद्दाम Mv. 3. 45 elated.<BR>--7<BR>Unlimited, extraordinary.<BR>--मः<BR>1 N.<BR>of Yama.<BR>--2 N. of Varuṇa.<BR>--मं<BR>ind. Violently, fiercely, strongly;<BR>अद्योद्दामं ज्वलिष्यतः U. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दित|उद्दितः
उद्दित a. [उद्-दो-क्त] Tied, bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दालः|उद्दाल
उद्दालः<BR>1 N. of a plant, Cordia<BR>Myxa or Latifolia (बहुवारक) (Mar.<BR>भोंकरी).<BR>--2 The sage उद्दालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दालकः|उद्दालक
उद्दालकः =<BR>1 उद्दाल q. v.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a sage.<BR>--कं A kind of honey.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुष्पभंजिका [उद्दालकानां<BR>पुष्पाणि भज्यंते यत्र क्रीडायां ण्वुल्] a sort of<BR>game played by the people in the<BR>eastern districts (in which<BR>Uddālaka flowers are broken or crushed).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिनं|उद्दिन
उद्दिनं Midday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिश्
उद्दिश् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To point out,<BR>signify, declare, denote, mention,<BR>tell; प्रथमोद्दिष्टमास्पदं Ku. 6. 35;<BR>Ms. 8. 52, 3. 182; Me. 30;<BR>यथोद्दिष्टव्यापारा Ś. 3; अनेडमूक उद्दिष्टः शठे Med.<BR>denotes or signifies.<BR>--2 To<BR>enunciate, prophesy; त्वं साधुभिरुद्दिष्टः<BR>Ś. 5.<BR>--3 To refer or allude to, have<BR>reference to; स्मरमुद्दिश्य Ku. 4. 38;<BR>Ś. 6, see उद्दिश्य below.<BR>--4 To mean,<BR>intend, aim at, direct towards,<BR>destine for, assign to, dedicate to;<BR>K. 40; उद्दिष्टामुपनिहितां भजस्व पूजां<BR>Māl. 5. 25; फलमुद्दिश्य Bg. 17. 21.<BR>--5<BR>To explain, teach, advise; सतां<BR>केनोद्दिष्टं विषममसिधाराव्रतमिदं Bh. 2. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिश्य
उद्दिश्य ind.<BR>1 With reference to,<BR>aiming at, in the direction of,<BR>towards; वध्यशिलामुद्दिश्य प्रस्थितः<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--2 For, for the sake of, on<BR>account of, in the name of; त्वां˚<BR>Ś. 3 on thy account; किं˚ for what<BR>purpose, on what account; निमित्तं˚<BR>Pt. 1. 283 for some cause;<BR>त्वामुद्दिश्य सभाजनाक्षराणि M. 5. in your name.<BR>--3 Demanding, stipulating for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दिष्ट
उद्दिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Mentioned,<BR>particularized, specially told.<BR>--2 Desired,<BR>wished for.<BR>--3 Explained, taught &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देशः|उद्देश
उद्देशः<BR>1 Pointing to or at,<BR>directing; सूर्योद्देशेन तिला दातव्याः Pt. 2<BR>in the name of.<BR>--2 Mention,<BR>specification; सार्धप्रहरद्वयोद्देशे Pt. 5;<BR>स्वरसंस्कारोद्देशः Nir.<BR>--3 Illustration,<BR>explanation, exemplification.<BR>--4<BR>Ascertainment, determination,<BR>inquiry, investigation, search.<BR>--5 A<BR>brief statement or account; एष<BR>तूद्देशतः प्रोक्तो विभूतेर्विस्तरो मया<BR>Bg. 10. 40.<BR>--6 Assignment, allotment.<BR>--7<BR>Stipulation, bargain.<BR>--8 Object,<BR>motive.<BR>--9 A spot, region, place; अहो<BR>प्रवातसुभगोयमुद्देशः Ś. 3; M. 3; वन˚ a<BR>part of the forest.<BR>--10 Upper region,<BR>high position.<BR>--11 (In phil.) The<BR>enunciation of a thing by its name<BR>(which is to be further discussed<BR>and explained), the other two<BR>processes being लक्षण and परीक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देशक|उद्देशकः
उद्देशक a. Illustrative.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An<BR>illustration, example.<BR>--2 An<BR>illustrator, a guide.<BR>--3 (In Math.) A<BR>question, problem; अत्रोद्देशकः<BR>(frequently occurring in Līlāvatī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देश्य|उद्देश्यः
उद्देश्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be illustrated<BR>or explained.<BR>--2 To be intended<BR>or aimed at.<BR>--3 That to which one<BR>refers or which one has in view.<BR>--श्यं<BR>1 The object in view, an<BR>incentive.<BR>--2 The subject of an<BR>assertion (opp. विधेय); see the word<BR>अनुवाद्य also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देष्टृ
उद्देष्टृ a.<BR>1 Pointing out.<BR>--2 One<BR>who acts with a certain object in<BR>view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्
उद्दीप् {c4c} A. To flame, blaze up,<BR>be kindled; वाणवदनमुददीपि भिये<BR>Śi. 15. 48; उद्दीप्यस्व जातवेदः Kauś.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To light up, inflame,<BR>illuminate, kindle; उद्दीपितकोपानलाः<BR>Ve. 2.<BR>--2 To excite, animate, fire.<BR>पुत्रवधामर्षोद्दीपितेन Ve. 2; न वैरमुद्दीपयति<BR>प्रशांतं Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपः|उद्दीप
उद्दीपः<BR>1 Inflaming, lighting.<BR>--2<BR>An inflamer.<BR>--3 That which<BR>animates or excites.<BR>--पं Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपक|उद्दीपकः
उद्दीपक a.<BR>1 Exciting, rendering<BR>more intense; गरलस्योद्दीपकतया<BR>Dk. 9 virulence.<BR>--2 Lighting,<BR>inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीपनं|उद्दीपन
उद्दीपनं<BR>1 Inflaming, exciting;<BR>क्रोध˚, अग्नि˚.<BR>--2 (In Rhet.) That which<BR>excites or feeds (a sentiment or<BR>rasa), any aggravating or attendant<BR>circumstance which gives<BR>poignancy to a feeling or passion;<BR>उद्दीपनविभावास्ते रसमुद्दीपयंति ये S. D. 160;<BR>see आलंबनं also.<BR>--3 Illuminating,<BR>lighting, setting fire to, burning;<BR>Ve. 5. 25.<BR>--4 Burning of a body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्त|उद्दीप्तः
उद्दीप्त p. p.<BR>1 Lighted, set on fire.<BR>--2 Shining, bright.<BR>--3 Inflamed,<BR>excited, aggravated (as passion).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दीप्र|उद्दीप्रं|उद्दीप्रः
उद्दीप्र a. [दीप्-रन्] Shining,<BR>blazing.<BR>--प्रः, --प्रं Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दृश्
उद्दृश् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To see above, look<BR>upwards (lit.).<BR>--2 To look into the<BR>future; expect; look up to; Mv. 6;<BR>उत्पश्यतः सिंहनिपातमुग्रं R. 2. 60.<BR>--3 To doubt.<BR>--4 To be aware of.<BR>--Caus. To make visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्दर्शनं|उद्दर्शन
उद्दर्शनं Making visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्देहिका
उद्देहिका The white ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्युत्
उद्द्युत् {c1c} A. To blaze up, shine.<BR>--Caus. {1} To cause to shine; (hence)<BR>adorn, grace; जाते पुनरप्युद्द्योतयोत्संगं<BR>U. 4;<BR>अलमुद्द्योतयामासुर्देवारण्यमिवर्तवः R. 10. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्योत|उद्द्योतः
उद्द्योत a. Shining, blazing.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Light, lustre (lit. and fig.);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">Page0308-a+ 56</a>]<BR>त्रिभिर्नेत्रैः कृतोद्द्योतं Mb.; कुलोद्द्योतकरी<BR>तव Rām. adorning or gracing.<BR>--2<BR>Revelation.<BR>--3 A division of a book,<BR>chapter, section.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0307-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्द्राव|उद्द्रावः
उद्द्राव a. Running away.<BR>--वः<BR>Flight, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धन्
उद्धन् {c2c} P. [उद्-हन्] To raise up,<BR>elevate (fig. also); see उद्धत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धत|उद्धतं|उद्धतः
उद्धत p. p.<BR>1 Raised up, elevated,<BR>lifted up; लांगूलमुद्धतं धुन्वन्<BR>Bk. 9. 7; आत्मोद्धतैरपि रजोभिः Ś. 1. 8 raised;<BR>खुर˚ R. 9. 50, heaved; Ki. 8. 53.<BR>--2<BR>Excessive, very much, exceeding.<BR>--3 Haughty, vain, puffed up;<BR>अक्षवधोद्धतः R. 12. 63.<BR>--4 Harsh;<BR>Śi. 16. 27.<BR>--5 Excited, inflamed,<BR>intensified; ˚मनोभवरागा Ki. 9. 68,<BR>69; मदोद्धताः प्रत्यनिलं विचेरुः<BR>Ku. 3. 31.<BR>--6 Majestic, stately;<BR>ill-mannered.<BR>--तः A king's wrestler.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मनस्, --मनस्क a.<BR>high-minded, haughty, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धतिः|उद्धति
उद्धतिः f.<BR>1 Elevation.<BR>--2 Pride,<BR>haughtiness; Śi. 3. 28.<BR>--3<BR>Rudeness, insolence; 16. 72.<BR>--4 A stroke,<BR>shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धम|उद्धमः
उद्धम See under उद्ध्मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर
उद्धर, उद्धार See under उद्धृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धार|उद्धारं|उद्धारः
उद्धर, उद्धार See under उद्धृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्ष|उद्धर्षः
उद्धर्ष a. Delighted, glad.<BR>--र्षः<BR>1<BR>Great joy or delight.<BR>--2 Courage to<BR>undertake a thing.<BR>--3 A festival<BR>(especially a religious one).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्षण|उद्धर्षणं
उद्धर्षण a. Animating,<BR>encouraging, exciting; हितमुद्धर्षणं चैव उवाच<BR>प्रथितं वचः Rām.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Animating.<BR>--2 Erection of the hair (on the<BR>body), thrill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्षिन्
उद्धर्षिन्<BR>1 a. Encouraging.<BR>--2<BR>Ved. One whose hair is erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धवः|उद्धव
उद्धवः<BR>1 A sacrificial fire.<BR>--2 A<BR>festival, holiday.<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>Yādava, uncle and friend of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>When Kṛṣṇa was taken by Akrūra<BR>to Mathurā Uddhava was implored by<BR>the citizens of Gokula to go and<BR>fetch him. He was very much attached<BR>to Kṛṣṇa. On seeing the destruction<BR>of the Yādavas to be inevitable, he<BR>went to Kṛṣṇa and asked him what<BR>to do; whereupon he was told to<BR>go to Badarikāśrama to practise<BR>penance and to secure heaven. He<BR>is the subject of two short poems,<BR>उद्धवदूत and उद्धवसंदेश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धस्त
उद्धस्त a. Extending or raising<BR>the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धा
उद्धा I. {c3c} P. Ved.<BR>1 To abandon or<BR>expose (an infant).<BR>--2 To set up, erect,<BR>build. II. {c3c} A.<BR>1 To go or move<BR>upwards, rise (as the sun, dust &c.); यतो<BR>रजः पार्थिवमुज्जिहीते R. 13. 64;<BR>Mu. 4. 21; Bk. 18. 27; N. 22. 45, 55.<BR>--2 To<BR>go away from, depart;<BR>उज्जिहानजीवितां Māl. 10.<BR>--3 To raise; शिरसा<BR>यूपमुज्जिहीते Kāty.<BR>--4 To throw up,<BR>knit (as eyebrows); Bk. 3. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धान|उद्धानं|उद्धानः
उद्धान a.<BR>1 Ejected, vomited.<BR>--2<BR>Inflated, corpulent, fat.<BR>--3 Gone<BR>up, ascended, risen.<BR>--नं<BR>1 A<BR>fireplace.<BR>--2 Ejecting, vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धिः|उद्धि
उद्धिः [उद्-धा-कि] Ved.<BR>1 A<BR>particular part of a carriage (the part<BR>which rests on the axles).<BR>--2 An<BR>earthen stand on which the Ukhā<BR>rests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धित
उद्धित p. p. Set up, erected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धांत|उद्धान्त|उद्धान्तः
उद्धांत a. Ejected, vomited.<BR>--तः<BR>An elephant out of rut (from whose<BR>temples ichor ceases to flow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धुर
उद्धुर a. [उद्गता धूरस्मात्]<BR>1 Freed<BR>from a burden or yoke,<BR>unrestrained, unchecked, free.<BR>--2 Firm,<BR>intrepid, bold; अभियोग˚ Mv. 6.<BR>--3 Victorious, conquering.<BR>--4 High,<BR>loud (voice &c);<BR>पितरमुद्धुरध्वनिमहाजनानुयातमानीय Dk. 104.<BR>--5 Heavy,<BR>full of; Śi. 5. 64.<BR>--6 Thick, gross.<BR>--7 Lively, cheerful.<BR>--8 Able,<BR>competent; Bv. 4. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धू
उद्धू {c5c} {c9c} U.<BR>1 To shake, move up,<BR>raise, throw up, wave (as a chawari);<BR>कैर्नोद्धूतानि चामराणि K. 117, 200;<BR>Ku. 2. 29; उद्धुनीयात सत्केतून्<BR>Bk. 19 8; Ki. 5. 39.<BR>--2 To shake or<BR>throw off; Śi. 18. 8, dispel, destroy<BR>(fig.), उद्धूतपापाः Me. 55.<BR>--3 To<BR>disturb, excite, rouse up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूत
उद्धूत p. p.<BR>1 Shaken off, fallen<BR>from; raised or thrown up;<BR>मारुतभरोद्धूतोपि धूलिव्रजः Dhan. V.<BR>--2<BR>Exalted, high, loud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूननं|उद्धूनन
उद्धूननं<BR>1 Throwing upwards,<BR>raising.<BR>--2 Shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूपनं|उद्धूपन
उद्धूपनं Fumigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूलनं|उद्धूलन
उद्धूलनं<BR>1 Powdering,<BR>sprinkling with dust or powder; भस्मोद्धूलन<BR>K. P. 10; K. 129.<BR>--2 An article<BR>used to season food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूलयति
उद्धूलयति Den. P. To powder,<BR>sprinkle with powder or dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धूषणं|उद्धूषण
उद्धूषणं Erection of the hair (on<BR>the body), thrill, horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृ
उद्धृ {vI.v} {c1c} {c10c} P.<BR>1 To draw out, raise<BR>up.<BR>--2 To save, deliver; भगवति<BR>तव स्पृष्टानद्भिश्चिरादुददीधरत् U. 1. 23.<BR>{vII.v} [उद्-हृ]<BR>1 To draw or take out,<BR>extract, extricate; शरं… उद्धर्तुमैच्छत्<BR>R. 2. 30; 3. 64; to deliver from,<BR>relieve of, save, rescue, protect<BR>(with abl.); मां तावदुद्धर शुचो<BR>दयिताप्रवृत्त्या V. 4. 15; Pt. 1. 358;<BR>Bg. 6. 5.<BR>--2 To uproot, extirpate, eradicate;<BR>tear or pull out; नमयामास<BR>नृपाननुद्धरन् R. 8. 9, 4. 66;<BR>त्रिदिवमुद्धृतदानवकंटकं Ś. 7. 3; Mv. 3. 13; Māl. 9. 22;<BR>उद्धरणीये चक्षुषी Dk. 102.<BR>--3 To<BR>pluck up (flowers &c.); K. 21, 144.<BR>--4 To raise, lift up, elevate,<BR>extend (as hands); पातयितुमेव<BR>शक्तिर्नान्नपिटमुद्धर्तुं Pt. 1. 363;<BR>Ms. 4. 62; V. 4. 34.<BR>--5 To take up, absorb<BR>(water); R. 4. 66; Śi. 3. 75.<BR>--6<BR>To sustain, bear up; राज्यधुरमुद्धर्तुं<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--7 To separate, abstract.<BR>--8 To<BR>remove, put away.<BR>--9 To deduct,<BR>subtract.<BR>--10 To select, pick out;<BR>Ms. 9. 116.<BR>--11 To present, offer;<BR>Y. 1. 159.<BR>--12 To prove; Y. 2. 28.<BR>--13 To divide (as with partners).<BR>--14 To publish, make known.<BR>--Caus. To cause to extract or<BR>draw out; R. 9. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धरणं|उद्धरण
उद्धरणं<BR>1 Drawing or taking out,<BR>taking off (clothes &c.).<BR>--2<BR>Extraction, pulling or tearing out; कंटक˚<BR>Ms. 9. 252; चक्षुषोरुद्धरणं Mit.; so<BR>शल्य˚<BR>--3 Extricating, deliverance,<BR>rescuing (from danger);<BR>दीनोद्धरणोचितस्य R. 2. 25; स बंधुर्यो<BR>विपन्नानामापदुद्धरणक्षमः H. 1. 3.<BR>--4<BR>Destruction, eradication,<BR>extermination, deposition, dethronement;<BR>चंद्रगुप्तस्योद्धरणात् Mu. 4.<BR>--5<BR>Lifting, raising.<BR>--6 Taking a part or<BR>share.<BR>--7 Taking from the<BR>Gārhapatya fire to supply the other sacred<BR>fires.<BR>--8 Vomiting.<BR>--9 Anything<BR>vomited.<BR>--10 Final emancipation.<BR>--11 Acquittance of debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धर्तृ|उद्धर्त्तृ
उद्धर्तृ, उद्धारक a.<BR>1 One who raises<BR>or lifts up.<BR>--2 A sharer, coheir.<BR>--3 One who recovers property. --m.<BR>1 A destroyer, exterminator;<BR>Y. 2. 271.<BR>--2 A saviour, deliverer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारक
उद्धर्तृ, उद्धारक a.<BR>1 One who raises<BR>or lifts up.<BR>--2 A sharer, coheir.<BR>--3 One who recovers property. --m.<BR>1 A destroyer, exterminator;<BR>Y. 2. 271.<BR>--2 A saviour, deliverer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारः|उद्धार|उद्धारं
उद्धारः<BR>1 Drawing out, extraction.<BR>--2 Deliverance, redemption,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-a" target="_blank">Page0309-a+ 56</a>]<BR>saving, rescuing, extrication.<BR>--3<BR>Raising, lifting up.<BR>--4 Deduction, a<BR>part to be set aside.<BR>--5 (In law)<BR>A part to be set aside from the<BR>paternal property for the benefit of<BR>the eldest son; the surplus allowed<BR>by Law to the eldest beyond the<BR>shares of the younger brothers;<BR>Ms. 9. 112.<BR>--6 The sixth part of<BR>booty taken in war which belongs<BR>to the king; Ms. 7. 97.<BR>--7<BR>An obligation.<BR>--8 Debt,<BR>particularly such as bears no interest.<BR>--9<BR>Recovering property.<BR>--10<BR>Marching out.<BR>--11 Citing (a passage),<BR>quoting.<BR>--12 Final beatitude.<BR>--13<BR>Prosperity, elevation.<BR>--रा The<BR>plant गुडूची.<BR>--रं A fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0308-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धारणं|उद्धारण
उद्धारणं<BR>1 Raising, elevating.<BR>--2<BR>Rescuing, drawing out of<BR>(danger), delivering.<BR>--3 Sharing,<BR>dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृत|उद्धृतः
उद्धृत p. p.<BR>1 Drawn up or out<BR>(water), extracted &c.<BR>--2 Raised,<BR>elevated, lifted up, thrown up or<BR>upwards; निक्षेपणाय पदमुद्धृतमुद्वहंती<BR>Ku. 5. 85.<BR>--3 Uprooted, eradicated;<BR>उद्धृतारिः R. 2. 30.<BR>--4 Separated, set<BR>apart.<BR>--5 Divided, partitioned.<BR>--6 Selected.<BR>--7 Dispersed,<BR>scattered.<BR>--8 Holding, containing.<BR>--9<BR>Uncovered.<BR>--10 Vomited, cast up.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्धार a. {1} one who has<BR>received his share of the<BR>patrimony. {2} that from which the<BR>proper part has been deducted;<BR>Ms. 10. 85.<BR>--स्नेह a. skimmed (as<BR>milk).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धृतिः|उद्धृति
उद्धृतिः f.<BR>1 Drawing or pulling<BR>out, extracting.<BR>--2 An extract,<BR>passage selected.<BR>--3 Delivering,<BR>rescuing.<BR>--4 Especially, delivering or<BR>purifying from sin, final liberation;<BR>त्रपंते तीर्थानि त्वरितमिह यस्योद्धृतिविधौ<BR>G. L. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ध्मा
उद्ध्मा {c1c} P.<BR>1 To breathe out,<BR>puff, blow.<BR>--2 To inflate, to make<BR>known by blowing (a trumpet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्धम|उद्धमः
उद्धम a. [उद्-ध्मा-श] Sounding,<BR>blowing.<BR>--मः<BR>1 Sounding, blowing.<BR>--2 Breathing hard, panting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ध्मानं|उद्ध्मान
उद्ध्मानं A fireplace, stove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ध्यः|उद्ध्य
उद्ध्यः [P. III. 1. 115; cf.<BR>उज्झत्युदकमिति उद्ध्यः Malli.] N. of a river;<BR>तोयदागम इवोद्ध्यभिद्ययोः R. 11. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्ध्वंसः|उद्ध्वंस
उद्ध्वंसः Hoarseness (of sound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बंध्|उद्बन्ध्
उद्बंध् {c9c} P. To hang, tie up;<BR>कंठमुद्बध्नाति Mu. 6; पादपे आत्मानमुद्बध्य<BR>व्यापादयामि Ratn. 3; Pt. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बंध|उद्बन्ध|उद्बन्धः
उद्बंध a. Loosened; R. 16. 67.<BR>--धः, --धनं<BR>1 Tying up, hanging.<BR>--2<BR>Hanging oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बंधकः|उद्बन्धक|उद्बन्धकः
उद्बंधकः N. of a mixed tribe<BR>(doing the duty of washermen); cf<BR>Uśanas:<BR>--आयोगवेन विप्रायां<BR>जातास्ताम्रोपजीविनः । तस्यैव नृपकन्यायां जातःसूनिक<BR>उच्यते ॥ सूनिकस्य नृपायां तु जाता उद्बंधकाः स्मृताः ।<BR>निर्णेजयेयुर्वस्त्राणि अस्पृशाश्च भवंत्यतः ॥<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बंधुकः|उद्बन्धुक|उद्बन्धुकः
उद्बंधुकः One who hangs up<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बल
उद्बल a. Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बाष्प
उद्बाष्प a. Filled or suffused with<BR>tears; Ki. 3. 59; न… मम<BR>नयनयोरुद्बाष्पत्वं सखे न भविष्यति V. 2. 10<BR>tears will gush up in the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बाहु
उद्बाहु a.<BR>1 Having the arms<BR>raised, stretching or extending<BR>the arms; प्रांशुलभ्ये फले<BR>लोभादुद्बाहुरिव वामनः R. 1. 3.<BR>--2 Having the<BR>trunk upraised (as an elephant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बिल
उद्बिल a. Out of the hole (an<BR>animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बुध्
उद्बुध् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To awaken, remind.<BR>--2 To arouse, animate, excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बुद्ध|उद्बुद्धः
उद्बुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Awakened,<BR>aroused, excited; मनसि उद्बुद्धमात्रो<BR>विकारो भावः S. D.<BR>--2 Opened,<BR>expanded, full-blown; ˚कनकाब्ज<BR>Māl. 1. 40.<BR>--3 Reminded, made to think<BR>of.<BR>--4 Recalled to memory (as<BR>an object seen before).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संस्कारः association of ideas,<BR>calling anything to mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बोधः|उद्बोध
उद्बोधः, --धनं<BR>1 Awakening,<BR>reminding.<BR>--2 Recalling to memory, rousing<BR>up; ननु कथं रामादिरत्याद्युद्बोधकारणैः<BR>सीतादिभिः सामाजिकानां रत्युद्बोधः<BR>S. D. 3; so रस˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बोधनं|उद्बोधन
उद्बोधः, --धनं<BR>1 Awakening,<BR>reminding.<BR>--2 Recalling to memory, rousing<BR>up; ननु कथं रामादिरत्याद्युद्बोधकारणैः<BR>सीतादिभिः सामाजिकानां रत्युद्बोधः<BR>S. D. 3; so रस˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्बोधक|उद्बोधकः
उद्बोधक a.<BR>1 Reminding, that<BR>which reminds or calls to<BR>remembrance.<BR>--2 Exciting, rousing.<BR>--3<BR>Discovering, exhibiting, showing.<BR>--कः N. of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भट|उद्भटः
उद्भट a.<BR>1 Excellent,<BR>pre-eminent; पदे पदे संति भटा रणोद्भटाः<BR>N. 1. 132.<BR>--2 Exalted, magnanimous.<BR>--टः<BR>1 A fan for winnowing corn.<BR>--2 A tortoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भव|उद्भवः
उद्भव, उद्भावना &c. See under<BR>उद्भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावना
उद्भव, उद्भावना &c. See under<BR>उद्भू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भास्
उद्भास् {c1c} A. To shine. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To light up, illuminate, render<BR>beautiful, decorate; ornament;<BR>उद्भासितं मंगलसंविधाभिः R. 7. 16; काले<BR>घनोद्भासिते Mk. 5. 35.<BR>--2 (fig.) To<BR>bring into prominence, elevate,<BR>exalt; उद्भासिताखिलखलस्य Bh. 2. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भासः|उद्भास
उद्भासः Radiance, splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भासिन्
उद्भासिन्, उद्भासुर a. Shining,<BR>radiant, splendid; विभूषणोद्भासि<BR>पिनद्धभोगि वा Ku. 5. 78; क्रीडारसोद्भासिनि<BR>Mk. 8. 38; Bh. 1. 80; Amaru. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भासुर
उद्भासिन्, उद्भासुर a. Shining,<BR>radiant, splendid; विभूषणोद्भासि<BR>पिनद्धभोगि वा Ku. 5. 78; क्रीडारसोद्भासिनि<BR>Mk. 8. 38; Bh. 1. 80; Amaru. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिद्
उद्भिद् {c7c} U. To break up. --pass.<BR>To break out, burst forth, become<BR>visible, be produced; अद्यापि पक्षावपि<BR>नोद्भिद्येते K. 347; उद्भिद्यमानपक्ष तिः 33,<BR>29, 46; उद्भिन्नपयोधरया K. 100<BR>developed; Ve. 4. 10. --Caus. To<BR>bring out, develop, unfold;<BR>Mu. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिद्
उद्भिद् a. [उद्-भिद्-क्विप्]<BR>1<BR>Sprouting, germinating, shooting forth.<BR>--2 Penetrating.<BR>--3 Destroying.<BR>--4<BR>Causing to come forth. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>sprout or shoot (of a plant);<BR>अंकुरोऽभिनवोद्भिदि Ak.<BR>--2 A plant;<BR>उद्भिदस्तरुगुल्माद्याः Ak.<BR>--3 A spring,<BR>fountain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. (उद्भिज्ज)<BR>sprouting, germinating (as a<BR>plant).<BR>--(ज्जः) a plant; उद्भिज्जाः<BR>स्थावराः सर्वे बीजकांडप्रारेहिणः<BR>Ms. 1. 46.<BR>--विद्या the science of botany.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिद|उद्भिदं
उद्भिद a. Sprouting, germinating.<BR>--दं Culinary salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भिन्न
उद्भिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Produced,<BR>generated, developed; formed; स्वयमेव<BR>ब्रह्मबंधुनोद्भिन्नो दुर्गप्रयोगः M. 4;<BR>R. 13. 21; Rs. 1. 20.<BR>--2 Shot forth,<BR>germinated; नीतिपादपस्य पुष्पमुद्भिन्नं<BR>M. 1; Ku. 1. 24.<BR>--3 Opened,<BR>expanded, budded; as in यौवनोद्भिन्नशैशवा.<BR>--4 Breaking out, appearing;<BR>˚रोमपुलकैः Ch. P. 34; Ś. 6.<BR>--5<BR>Betrayed; उद्भिन्नास्मि सहवासिन्या विस्रंभेण<BR>Māl. 7; Kām. 17. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भेदः|उद्भेद
उद्भेदः, --दनं<BR>1 Breaking through or<BR>out, becoming visible, appearance,<BR>display, manifestation, growth,<BR>development; किसलयोद्भेदप्रतिद्वंद्विभिः<BR>Ś. 4. 4; उमास्तनोद्भेदमनु प्रवृद्धः<BR>Ku. 7. 24; तं यौवनोद्भेदविशेषकांतं R. 5. 38;<BR>Śi. 18. 36; Mu. 5. 3.<BR>--2 Breaking,<BR>splitting; प्रस्तरोद्भदयोग्यः U. 3. 25.<BR>--3 A spring, fountain.<BR>--4<BR>Horripilation; as in पुलकोद्भेद, रोमोद्भेद.<BR>--5<BR>Treason, betrayal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भेदनं|उद्भेदन
उद्भेदः, --दनं<BR>1 Breaking through or<BR>out, becoming visible, appearance,<BR>display, manifestation, growth,<BR>development; किसलयोद्भेदप्रतिद्वंद्विभिः<BR>Ś. 4. 4; उमास्तनोद्भेदमनु प्रवृद्धः<BR>Ku. 7. 24; तं यौवनोद्भेदविशेषकांतं R. 5. 38;<BR>Śi. 18. 36; Mu. 5. 3.<BR>--2 Breaking,<BR>splitting; प्रस्तरोद्भदयोग्यः U. 3. 25.<BR>--3 A spring, fountain.<BR>--4<BR>Horripilation; as in पुलकोद्भेद, रोमोद्भेद.<BR>--5<BR>Treason, betrayal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0309-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भू
उद्भू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To arise, spring up,<BR>be produced from; उदभून्मुरजध्वनिः,<BR>अंतरीक्षात्सरस्वती &c. see उद्भव below.<BR>--2 To occur, take place;<BR>उदभवत्तीव्रो दुर्भिक्षः Ks. 27. 94.<BR>--3 To ascend,<BR>go up, mount.<BR>--4 To suffice.<BR>--5<BR>To rise in arms, revolt, rebel.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to exist, create,<BR>produce; मायां मयोद्भाव्य परीक्षितोसि<BR>R. 2. 62.<BR>--2 To proclaim; माहात्म्यं<BR>K. 109.<BR>--3 To use, employ.<BR>--4 To<BR>raise, elevate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भवः|उद्भव
उद्भवः<BR>1 Production, creation,<BR>birth, generation (lit. and fig.); इति<BR>हेतुस्तदुद्भवे K. P. 1; Y. 3. 80; oft. at<BR>the end of comp. in the sense of<BR>‘springing or arising from,’<BR>‘produced from’; ऊरूद्भवा V. 1. 3;<BR>मणिराकरोद्भवः R. 3. 18.<BR>--2 Source, origin;<BR>उद्भवो यशसः K. 54.<BR>--3 N. of Viṣṇu;<BR>उद्भवः क्षोभनो देवः V. Sah.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a. productive.<BR>--क्षेत्रं<BR>birthplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावः|उद्भाव
उद्भावः<BR>1 Production, generation.<BR>--2 Magnanimity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावनं|उद्भावन
उद्भावनं<BR>1 Thinking, thinking over.<BR>--2 Production, generation,<BR>creation.<BR>--3 Speaking, saying.<BR>--4<BR>Inattention, neglect, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भावयितृ
उद्भावयितृ a. Raising upwards,<BR>lifting up, exalting (fig. also);<BR>उद्भावयिता बंधून् Dk. 153.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूत|उद्भूतः
उद्भूत p. p.<BR>1 Born, produced,<BR>generated.<BR>--2 Lofty (lit. and fig.).<BR>--3 Visible, perceptible, capable of<BR>being perceived by the senses; as<BR>a गुण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भूतिः|उद्भूति
उद्भूतिः f.<BR>1 Generation,<BR>production.<BR>--2 Elevation, exaltation,<BR>prosperity; वरः शंभुरलं ह्येष त्वत्कुलोद्भूतये<BR>विधिः Ku. 6. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रम्
उद्भ्रम् {c1c} {c4c} P. To wander, roam<BR>about; धावत्युद्भ्रमति प्रमीलति<BR>पतत्युद्याति मूर्छत्यपि Gīt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रमः|उद्भ्रम
उद्भ्रमः<BR>1 Whirling, turning round,<BR>flourishing (as of a sword).<BR>--2<BR>Wandering.<BR>--3 Regret.<BR>--4 N. of a<BR>class of beings attending on Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रमणं|उद्भ्रमण
उद्भ्रमणं<BR>1 Moving or wandering<BR>about.<BR>--2 Rising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भ्रांत|उद्भ्रान्त|उद्भ्रान्तं
उद्भ्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Agitated,<BR>bewildered, distracted; ˚चेतनां R. 12. 74;<BR>gone mad; Mv. 4.<BR>--2 Terrified,<BR>frightened; मारीचोद्भ्रांतहारीताः<BR>R. 4. 46; U. 6.<BR>--3 Whirled, flourished,<BR>waved (as a sword).<BR>--4<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">Page0310-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Wandering upwards.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Flourishing a<BR>sword.<BR>--2 (˚--तकं) Rising (in<BR>the air).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्मन्
उद्मन् n. Ved. Flooding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यम्
उद्यम् {c1c} A. (P. in some cases)<BR>1 To raise, elevate, lift up; बाहू<BR>उद्यम्य Ś. 1; परस्य दंडं नोद्यच्छेत्<BR>Ms. 4. 164, 8. 280; Bg. 1. 20;<BR>R. 15. 23, 11. 17; भारमुद्यच्छते Sk.; Bk. 4. 31,<BR>17. 92.<BR>--2 To offer, give.<BR>--3 To prepare,<BR>become ready for, begin, set about<BR>(with dat., loc. or inf.); उद्यच्छमाना<BR>गमनाय पश्चात् R. 16. 29; Bk. 8. 47;<BR>see उद्यत.<BR>--4 To strive, be diligent,<BR>strive hard for; उद्यच्छति वेदं Sk.<BR>--5<BR>To reign, manage, govern.<BR>--6 To<BR>keep back, stop, hinder.<BR>--7 To rise.<BR>--Caus. To prompt, stimulate;<BR>Ki. 9. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यत|उद्यतं|उद्यतः
उद्यत p. p.<BR>1 Raised, lifted up;<BR>उद्यतेष्वपि शस्त्रेषु H. 3. 15; so ˚असिः,<BR>˚पाणिः &c.<BR>--2 Persevering, diligent,<BR>active.<BR>--3 Bent, drawn (as a bow);<BR>Ki. 1. 21.<BR>--4 Ready, prepared, on<BR>the point of, eager, bent or intent<BR>on, engaged in; with dat., loc., inf.,<BR>or usually in comp; अनर्थायोद्यता<BR>Rām.; उद्यतः स्वेषु कर्मसु R. 17. 61;<BR>हंतुं स्वजनमुद्यताः Bg. 1. 45;<BR>पक्षच्छेदोद्यतं शक्रं R. 4. 40; जय˚, वध˚ &c.<BR>--5<BR>Trained, disciplined.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Time<BR>(in music).<BR>--2 A section, chapter, or<BR>any such division of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यत्|उद्यन्त्
उद्यत् a. Rising. --m. A star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यतिः|उद्यति
उद्यतिः f.<BR>1 Raising, elevation.<BR>--2<BR>Effort, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यंतृ|उद्यन्तृ
उद्यंतृ a. Raising, elevating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमः|उद्यम
उद्यमः<BR>1 Raising, elevation.<BR>--2<BR>Strenuous or assiduous effort,<BR>exertion, diligence, perseverance;<BR>निशम्य चैनां तपसे कृतोद्यमां Ku. 5. 3;<BR>शशाक मेना न नियंतुमुद्यमात् 5, firm<BR>resolve; उद्यमेन हि सिध्यंति कार्याणि न<BR>मनोरथैः Pt. 2. 131.<BR>--3 Readiness,<BR>preparation; गंतुमुद्यमो विहितः became ready<BR>to go Pt. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भंगः<BR>discouragement.<BR>--भृत् a. undergoing<BR>exertions, striving hard; Bh. 2. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमनं|उद्यमन
उद्यमनं Raising, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यमिन्
उद्यमिन् a. Diligent, persevering,<BR>active.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यामः|उद्याम
उद्यामः<BR>1 Erecting, stretching out,<BR>elevation.<BR>--2 A rope, a cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्या
उद्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go up, rise,<BR>ascend; क्रमशस्ते पुनस्तस्य<BR>चापात्सममिवोद्ययुः R. 12. 47; पतत्युद्याति Gīt. 4.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">Page0310-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 To originate, spring, arise; इति<BR>मतिरुदयासीत् पक्षिणः प्रेक्ष्य भैमीं<BR>N. 2. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यानं|उद्यान|उद्यानः
उद्यानं (--नः also)<BR>1 Going or<BR>walking out.<BR>--2 A garden, park,<BR>pleasure garden;<BR>बाह्योद्यानस्थितहरशिरश्चंद्रिकाधौतहर्म्या Me. 7, 26, 33; oft.<BR>opp. to वन; cf. दूरीकृताः खलु<BR>गुणैरुद्यानलता वनलताभिः Ś. 1. 17.<BR>--3<BR>Purpose, motive.<BR>--4 N. of a country<BR>to the North of India.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पालः, --पालकः, --रक्षकः a gardener,<BR>superintendent or keeper of a<BR>garden; उद्यानपालसामान्यमृतवस्तमुपासते<BR>Ku. 2. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यानकं|उद्यानक
उद्यानकं A garden, park.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यापनं|उद्यापन
उद्यापनं Bringing to a<BR>conclusion, completing, finishing (as<BR>व्रतोद्यापन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यापित
उद्यापित a. Brought to a<BR>conclusion, accomplished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यावः|उद्याव
उद्यावः [उद्-यु-घञ्] Mixing,<BR>joining; blending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्यासः|उद्यास
उद्यासः [उद्-यस्-घञ्] Effort,<BR>exertion (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्युज्
उद्युज् {c7c} U. (Usually A. only)<BR>1 To excite, make active or quick,<BR>stimulate to exertion.<BR>--2 (Intrans.)<BR>To exert, attempt, strive (with inf.);<BR>भवंतमभियोक्तुमुद्युंक्ते Dk. 3.<BR>--3 To<BR>prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्युक्त|उद्युक्तः
उद्युक्त p. p. Zealously active,<BR>persevering, diligent, industrious;<BR>engaged, ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्योगः|उद्योग
उद्योगः<BR>1 Effort, exertion,<BR>industry; तद्दैवमिति संचिंत्य<BR>त्यजेन्नोद्योगमात्मनः Pt. 2. 140; उद्योगः खलु कर्तव्यः<BR>फलं मार्जारवत् भवेत् ।.<BR>--2 Work, duty,<BR>office; तुल्योद्योगस्तव दिनकृतश्चाधिकारो<BR>मतो नः V. 2. 1.<BR>--3 Perseverance,<BR>diligence.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पर्वन् n. title of<BR>the 5th book of the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्योगिन्
उद्योगिन् a. Active, diligent,<BR>persevering, industrious; उद्योगिनं<BR>पुरुषसिंहमुपैति लक्ष्मीर्दैवं हि दैवमिति कापुरुषा<BR>वदंति Pt. 1. 361.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रः|उद्र
उद्रः A kind of aquatic animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रिन्
उद्रिन् a. Springing; abounding in<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रंकः|उद्रङ्क|उद्रङ्कः
उद्रंकः, --गः N. of the town of<BR>हरिश्चंद्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रंगः|उद्रङ्ग|उद्रङ्गः
उद्रंकः, --गः N. of the town of<BR>हरिश्चंद्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रथः|उद्रथ
उद्रथः [उद्गतो रथो यस्मात्]<BR>1 The<BR>pin of the axle of a carriage.<BR>--2 A<BR>cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रावः|उद्राव
उद्रावः A loud noise, uproar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0310-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रिच्
उद्रिच् (chiefly used in pass.)<BR>1 To excel, surpass (with abl.);<BR>ममैवोद्रिच्यते जन्म-तव जन्मनः Mb.<BR>--2 To increase, exceed,<BR>preponderate.<BR>--3 To abound in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रिक्त|उद्रिक्तं
उद्रिक्त p. p.<BR>1 Increased,<BR>excessive, abundant.<BR>--2 Distinct,<BR>evident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रेकः|उद्रेक
उद्रेकः<BR>1 Increase, excess,<BR>preponderance, abundance;<BR>ज्ञानोद्रेकाद्विघटिततमोग्रंथयः सत्त्वनिष्ठाः Ve. 1. 23;<BR>गत्वोद्रेकं जघनपुलिने Śi. 7. 74; so<BR>मोह˚, धन˚, मद˚.<BR>--2 Commencement,<BR>outset.<BR>--का The plant (महानिंब).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भंगः discouraging a<BR>thing at the very beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रेकिन्
उद्रेकिन् a. Abounding in,<BR>increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रुज
उद्रुज a.<BR>1 Destroying, breaking<BR>down.<BR>--2 Undermining (as a bank);<BR>as in कूलमुद्रुज q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्रोधनं|उद्रोधन
उद्रोधनं Rising, growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वत्
उद्वत् a.<BR>1 Excellent.<BR>--2 Raised,<BR>elevated. --f. An elevation, hill<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वत्सरः|उद्वत्सर
उद्वत्सरः A year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वप्
उद्वप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To pour out, send<BR>forth.<BR>--2 To raise, elevate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वपनं|उद्वपन
उद्वपनं<BR>1 A gift, donation.<BR>--2<BR>Pouring or shaking out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वापः|उद्वाप
उद्वापः<BR>1 Ejection, throwing out.<BR>--2 Shaving.<BR>--3 (In logic)<BR>Nonexistence of a subsequent<BR>consequent on the absence of an<BR>antecedent (Wilson).<BR>--4 Rooting up.<BR>--5 Raising, elevating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वम्
उद्वम् {c1c} P. To throw up, eject,<BR>vomit (fig. also); उद्ववाम वरौ<BR>R. 12. 5 spoke out or uttered; shed (tears<BR>&c.); Mu. 6. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वमनं|उद्वमन
उद्वमनं, उद्वांतिः f. Vomiting,<BR>ejecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वांतिः|उद्वान्ति|उद्वांति|उद्वान्तिः
उद्वमनं, उद्वांतिः f. Vomiting,<BR>ejecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वांत|उद्वान्त|उद्वान्तं|उद्वान्तः
उद्वांत^1 p. p.<BR>1 Vomited.<BR>--2 Out of<BR>rut (as an elephant).<BR>--3 Dropped<BR>down; Ś. 6.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: seems to be misspelled when copied from MW72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वयस्
उद्वयस् a. Throwing down food<BR>(as wind) (अन्नापातक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्धनं|उद्वर्धन|उद्वर्द्धनं
उद्वर्धनं<BR>1 Increase.<BR>--2 Sly or<BR>suppressed laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वस्
उद्वस् Caus. To banish, expel,<BR>drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वासः|उद्वास
उद्वासः<BR>1 Banishment.<BR>--2<BR>Abandonment.<BR>--3 Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वासनं|उद्वासन
उद्वासनं<BR>1 Expelling, banishing.<BR>--2 Abandoning.<BR>--3 Taking out of<BR>or away (from the fire).<BR>--4<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वास्य
उद्वास्य a.<BR>1 Relating to the<BR>killing of a sacrificial animal.<BR>--2 To<BR>be raised or lifted up.<BR>--3 To be<BR>taken out or extracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वस
उद्वस a From which honey has<BR>been extracted (as a bee-hive);<BR>Vb. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वह्
उद्वह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To marry, lead<BR>home (as a bride); पार्थिवीमुदवहद्रघूद्वहः<BR>R. 11. 54; नोद्वहेत्कपिलां कन्यां<BR>Ms. 3. 8, 10, 15; Y. 1. 52; Bk. 2. 48.<BR>--2 To bear up, raise up, elevate.<BR>--3<BR>To hold up, sustain, support;<BR>पदमुद्वहंती Ku. 5. 85; उद्वह धुरं K. 109;<BR>Ku. 6. 30; आत्मानमुद्वोढुमशक्गुवत्यः<BR>R. 16. 60, 11. 66; Śi. 9. 73;<BR>Bk. 9. 7; भारं &c.<BR>--4 To suffer,<BR>experience, feel; Māl. 6. 9;<BR>स्वाम्यर्थमुद्वहन् Mu. 2. 21 adhering to his<BR>master's cause.<BR>--5 To possess, have,<BR>assume, be endowed with;<BR>पुरुषाभिमानमुद्वहद्भिः Mu. 4. यौवनमुद्वहंत्या<BR>Ku. 1. 19; श्रियमुद्वहति मुखं ते<BR>बालातपरक्तकमलस्य V. 4. 42; M. 5. 14;<BR>so शब्दं, अंगुलिं, पाणिं, ज्ञानं, गर्वं,<BR>प्रमोदं &c.<BR>--6 To carry off or<BR>away, take or lead away; तमुद्वहंतं<BR>पथि भोजकन्यां R. 7. 35, 70.<BR>--7 To<BR>lead to termination, finish;<BR>प्रारब्धमुत्तमजनास्त्वमिवोद्वहंति Mu. 2. 17<BR>v. l. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to marry.<BR>--2 To spread above; Śi. 12. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उदूढ|उदूढः
उदूढ p. p.<BR>1 Married.<BR>--2 Coarse,<BR>gross.<BR>--3 Acquired, obtained;<BR>Śi. 1. 74.<BR>--4 Tall, protuberant, high;<BR>Ki. 14. 31.<BR>--5 Heavy, fat.<BR>--6<BR>Material, substantial.<BR>--7 Excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वह|उद्वहः
उद्वह a.<BR>1 Carrying, leading up,<BR>taking up or away.<BR>--2 Continuing,<BR>perpetuating (as a family); कुल˚<BR>U. 4; so रघु˚ 4. 22; R. 9. 9; 11. 54.<BR>--3 Eminent, head, principal, best,<BR>foremost.<BR>--हः<BR>1 A son.<BR>--2 One<BR>(i. e. the 4th) of the seven courses<BR>of air.<BR>--3 The vital air which<BR>conveys nourishment upwards.<BR>--4<BR>One of the seven tongues of fire.<BR>--5 Marriage.<BR>--हा A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वहनं|उद्वहन
उद्वहनं<BR>1 Marrying.<BR>--2<BR>Supporting, holding or lifting up, bearing,<BR>carrying; भुवः प्रयुक्तोद्वहनक्रियायाः<BR>R. 13. 8; कैलासनाथोद्वहनाय भूयः 14. 20;<BR>Māl. 10; R. 2. 18; Ku. 3. 13.<BR>--3<BR>Being carried on, riding;<BR>खरेणोद्वहनं तथा Ms. 8. 370.<BR>--4 Possessing,<BR>having; लज्जा˚, विनय˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहः|उद्वाह
उद्वाहः<BR>1 Bearing up, supporting.<BR>--2 Marriage, wedding; असवर्णास्वयं<BR>ज्ञेयो विधिरुद्वाहकर्मणि Ms. 3. 43. (The<BR>Smṛtis mention {8} forms of<BR>marriage:<BR>--ब्राह्मो दैवस्तथा चार्षः<BR>प्राजापत्यस्तथासुरः । गांधर्वो राक्षसश्चैव पैशाचश्चाष्टमः स्मृतः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहन|उद्वाहनं
उद्वाहन a. That which raises or<BR>draws up (in comp.); घटीयंत्रं<BR>सलिलोद्वाहनं प्रहेः Ak.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Lifting up.<BR>--2<BR>Ploughing a field twice.<BR>--3 Marriage.<BR>--4 Anxiety, anxious regret.<BR>--नी<BR>1<BR>A cord, rope.<BR>--2 A small shell,<BR>cowarie (वराटिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहिक|उद्वाहिकः
उद्वाहिक a. [उद्वाह-ठक्] Relating<BR>to marriage, matrimonial (as a<BR>Mantra); Ms. 9. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहित|उद्वाहितः
उद्वाहित p. p.<BR>1 Raised, lifted<BR>up.<BR>--2 Married.<BR>--3 Eradicated,<BR>pulled up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वाहिन्
उद्वाहिन् a.<BR>1 Raising, drawing up.<BR>--2 Marrying.<BR>--नी A rope, cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वोढृ
उद्वोढृ m. A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वादनं|उद्वादन
उद्वादनं Crying aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वान|उद्वानः
उद्वान a. Vomited, ejected.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Ejecting, vomiting.<BR>--2 A stove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वास|उद्वासः
उद्वास, --सस् a. One who has put<BR>off one's clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वासस्
उद्वास, --सस् a. One who has put<BR>off one's clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विज्
उद्विज् {c6c} A. (P. epic.)<BR>1 To be<BR>grieved or afflicted, be agitated;<BR>नोद्विजेत्प्राप्यं चाप्रियं Bg. 5. 20; tremble,<BR>shake (lit. and fig.).<BR>--2 To<BR>fear, be afraid of, shrink from,<BR>abhor (with abl.); तीक्ष्णादुद्विजते<BR>Mu. 3. 5; Bg. 12. 15; लोकापवादान्नोद्विग्नं<BR>K. 197 नायमुद्विजितुं कालः स्वामिकार्यात्<BR>Bk. 7. 92.<BR>--3 To be tired or sick of,<BR>be disgusted with; जीवितादुद्विजमानेन<BR>Māl. 3; sometimes with gen.; या<BR>ममोद्विजते नित्यं साद्य मामवगूहते<BR>Pt. 4. 76.<BR>--4 To grieve, afflict, frighten.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To trouble, harass, afflict,<BR>oppress; उद्वेजयत्यंगुलिपार्ष्णिभागान्<BR>Ku. 1. 11; उद्वेजिता वृष्टिभिः 5;<BR>म्लेच्छैरुद्वेज्यमाना Mu. 7. 19.<BR>--2 To terrify,<BR>frighten; उद्वेजिताः कूजितैः U. 2. 29.<BR>--3<BR>To produce disgust or abhorrence;<BR>रमणीयाप्युद्वेजयति K. 12;<BR>सीधुपानोद्वेजितस्य M. 3; Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्विग्न|उद्विग्नः
उद्विग्न p. p.<BR>1 Grieved, afflicted,<BR>sorrowful, anxious (as for any<BR>absent lover); ˚चित्त, --मनस् depressed<BR>in mind, sorry, anxious.<BR>--2<BR>Alarmed, frightened; U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेग|उद्वेगं|उद्वेगः
उद्वेग a. [उद्गतो वेगोऽस्मात्]<BR>1 Going<BR>swiftly (as an express messenger),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">Page0312-a+ 56</a>]<BR>courier.<BR>--2 Steady, calm, tranquil.<BR>--3 Ascending, mounting.<BR>--4 One<BR>whose arms by long practice<BR>continue always raised above the head<BR>(as an ascetic).<BR>--गः<BR>1 Trembling,<BR>shaking, waving.<BR>--2 Agitation,<BR>excitement; Bg. 12. 15.<BR>--3 Alarm,<BR>fear; शांतोद्वेगस्तिमितनयनं<BR>दृष्टभक्तिर्भवान्या Me. 36; सहसोद्वेगमियं व्रजेदिति<BR>R. 8. 7.<BR>--4 Anxiety, regret, sorrow,<BR>distress (caused by separation from<BR>one's favourite object.).<BR>--5<BR>Admiration, astonishment.<BR>--गं A<BR>betelnut (fruit.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0311-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजिन्
उद्वेजि(गि)न्, --जक a.<BR>1 Agitating,<BR>distressing, causing pain or distress.<BR>--2 Suffering distress, anxious,<BR>unhappy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेगिन्
उद्वेजि(गि)न्, --जक a.<BR>1 Agitating,<BR>distressing, causing pain or distress.<BR>--2 Suffering distress, anxious,<BR>unhappy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजक
उद्वेजि(गि)न्, --जक a.<BR>1 Agitating,<BR>distressing, causing pain or distress.<BR>--2 Suffering distress, anxious,<BR>unhappy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजन|उद्वेजनं
उद्वेजन a. Causing to tremble<BR>(with fear); hurting the feelings.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Agitation, anxiety.<BR>--2<BR>Infliction of pain, torture, affliction;<BR>उद्वेजनकरैर्दंडैश्चिह्नयित्वा प्रवासयेत्<BR>Ms. 8. 352 painful.<BR>--3 Regret, sorrow<BR>for one's absence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेजयितृ
उद्वेजयितृ a. Terrifying; Śi. 3. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीक्ष्
उद्वीक्ष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To look up, view,<BR>see, perceive; दृष्टिरधिकं<BR>सोत्कंठमुद्वीक्षते Amaru. 24; प्रियस्य पदवीमुद्वीक्ष्य<BR>74 looking at (waiting for);<BR>R. 13. 68.<BR>--2 To examine, consider;<BR>आत्मनः शक्तिमुद्वीक्ष्य Pt. 1. 236.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीक्षणं|उद्वीक्षण
उद्वीक्षणं<BR>1 Looking up or upwards.<BR>--2 Sight, an eye; seeing, looking<BR>at; सखीजनोद्वीक्षणकौमुदीमुखं R. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीज्
उद्वीज् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To fan.<BR>--2 To blow<BR>upon or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वीजनं
उद्वीजनं Fanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृंहणं|उद्वृंहण
उद्वृंहणं Increase, growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृत्
उद्वृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To go upwards,<BR>ascend.<BR>--2 To fly asunder, burst out;<BR>उद्वर्तमानमूलबंधनं U. 4 the strings<BR>of which are giving way or being<BR>snapped.<BR>--3 To tumble over, fall<BR>down.<BR>--4 To go out, depart.<BR>--5<BR>To rise, swell, increase.<BR>--6 To be<BR>puffed up with pride, be haughty.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To extirpate, eradicate,<BR>destroy; उद्वर्तितं रसांतरेण लज्जालुत्वं<BR>Mv. 2.<BR>--2 To throw up, elevate.<BR>--3 To turn round, roll (as eyes).<BR>--4 To anoint, smear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्त|उद्वर्तः|उद्वर्त्त|उद्वर्त्तः
उद्वर्त a.<BR>1 Superfluous,<BR>redundant, plentiful.<BR>--2 Left over as a<BR>remainder, surplus.<BR>--र्तः<BR>1 A<BR>remainder, surplus.<BR>--2 Excess,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">Page0312-b+ 55</a>]<BR>preponderance.<BR>--3 Rubbing or<BR>smearing the body with perfumes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्तक|उद्वर्तकः|उद्वर्त्तक
उद्वर्तक a.<BR>1 Causing to rise.<BR>--2<BR>Rubbing and cleaning the body.<BR>--कः (In Math.) The quantity<BR>assumed for the purpose of the<BR>operation (Colebrooke).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्तनं|उद्वर्तन|उद्वर्त्तन|उद्वर्त्तनं
उद्वर्तनं<BR>1 Going up, rising.<BR>--2<BR>Springing up, growth (of plants,<BR>grain &c.).<BR>--3 Prosperity,<BR>elevation.<BR>--4 Turning from side to side;<BR>springing up, popping the head;<BR>चटुलशफरोद्वर्तनप्रेक्षितानि^1 Me. 40.<BR>--5<BR>Griding, pounding.<BR>--6 Drawing<BR>out metal, wire-drawing.<BR>--7<BR>Anointing, smearing; करोद्वर्तनार्थे<BR>चंदनं समर्पयामि.<BR>--8 Particularly,<BR>rubbing and cleaning the body with<BR>perfumes or fragrant unguents, or<BR>the unguents used for this<BR>purpose or to relieve pain; Y. 1. 152;<BR>Ms. 4. 132 (<BR>अभ्यंगमलापकर्षणपिष्टकादि Kull.).<BR>--9 Bad behaviour or<BR>conduct, rudeness.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by User geymonat on 20211001. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/659.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्तित|उद्वर्त्तित
उद्वर्तित a.<BR>1 Risen, elevated.<BR>--2<BR>Sprung up, drawn out.<BR>--3<BR>Perfumed, scented, rubbed, kneaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृत्त|उद्वृत्तः
उद्वृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Raised, elevated<BR>(स्तन, दंत, मेघ &c.).<BR>--2 Flowing out,<BR>not contained in, swollen,<BR>overflowing; हृदयभरितोद्वृत्तविस्मय Māl. 4;<BR>अपामुद्वृत्तानां Mu. 3. 8 overflowing;<BR>उद्वृतः क इव सुखावहः परेषां Śi. 8. 18.<BR>(where उ˚ means also ‘gone astray,<BR>ill-behaved’).<BR>--3 Grown, increased.<BR>--4 Exalted, prosperous.<BR>--5 Proud,<BR>furious, haughty; ˚मृगपति K. 90.<BR>--6 Vomited up.<BR>--7 Left as a<BR>remainder.<BR>--8 Ill-conducted,<BR>ill-mannered, rude.<BR>--9 Agitated;<BR>उद्वृत्तनक्रात् सहसोन्ममज्ज R. 16. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वृह्
उद्वृह् {c6c} P.<BR>1 raise up, elevate.<BR>--2<BR>To draw up, eradicate, uproot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वर्हित|उद्वर्हितः
उद्वर्हित a. Drawn up; eradicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेग|उद्वेगं|उद्वेगः
उद्वेग See under उद्विज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेदि
उद्वेदि a. [उन्नता वेदिर्यत्र] Having a<BR>raised seat or throne in it; विमानं<BR>नवमुद्वेदि R. 17. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेपः|उद्वेप
उद्वेपः Shaking, trembling,<BR>excessive tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेल|उद्वेलः
उद्वेल a. [उत्क्रांतो वेलां]<BR>1<BR>Overflowing its banks (as a river);<BR>भयमप्रलयोद्वेलादाचख्युर्नैरृतोदधेः<BR>R. 10. 34; K. 333.<BR>--2 Transgressing the<BR>proper limits.<BR>--3 Excessive; K. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेल्ल्
उद्वेल्ल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To shake, wave;<BR>Māl. 2, 6; उद्वेल्लद्बालकदली Ratn. 2.<BR>--2<BR>To roll or move about, turn round;<BR>उद्वेल्लंति पुराणचंदनतरुस्कंधेषु कुंभीनसाः<BR>U. 2. 29; Mv. 5. 2; Māl. 8. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेल्लित
उद्वेल्लित p. p. Shaken, tossed up.<BR>--तं Shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्ट|उद्वेष्टः
उद्वेष्ट a. Investing,<BR>surrounding, covering on all sides.<BR>--ष्टः<BR>1<BR>Surrounding.<BR>--2 Investing or<BR>besieging (as a town &c.).<BR>--3<BR>Devastating.<BR>--4 Overcoming in battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्टन
उद्वेष्टन a.<BR>1 Loosened;<BR>कयाचिदुद्वेष्टनवांतमाल्यः R. 7. 6; Ku. 7. 57.<BR>--2<BR>Freed from bonds, unfettered,<BR>unbound.<BR>--नं<BR>1 The act of<BR>surrounding or enclosing.<BR>--2 An enclosure,<BR>fence.<BR>--3 A pain in the buttocks<BR>or back of the body; हृदय˚<BR>convulsive pain in the heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्टयति
उद्वेष्टयति Den. P. To open,<BR>unfasten, untie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्वेष्टित
उद्वेष्टित a. Surrounded, invested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उधस्
उधस् An udder; see ऊधस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उध्रस्
उध्रस् {c9c} {c10c} P. (उध्रस्नाति,<BR>उध्रासयति)<BR>1 To glean or gather little<BR>by little at a time.<BR>--2 To throw<BR>or cast upwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंद्|उन्द्
उंद् {c7c} P. [उनत्ति, उंदांचकार, औंदीत्,<BR>उंदितुं, उत्त-उन्न;]<BR>1 To wet, moisten,<BR>bathe; याः पृथिवीं पयसोंदंति.<BR>--2 To<BR>flow or issue out, spring (as water).<BR>--Caus. (aor. औंदिदत्) To wet.<BR>--desid. (उंदिदिषति) [cf. L. unda].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंदनं|उन्दन
उंदनं Moistening, wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्न|उन्नः
उन्न p. p.<BR>1 Wet, wetted, moist.<BR>--2 (fig.) Kind, moved to pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंदरुः|उन्दरु|उंदरु|उन्दरुः
उंदरुः, उंदुरः, उंदुरुः, उंदूरुः<BR>[उंद्-उर-उरु वा] A mouse, rat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्णी,<BR>--कर्णिका the plant Salvinia<BR>Cuccullata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंदुरः|उन्दुर|उंदुर|उन्दुरः
उंदरुः, उंदुरः, उंदुरुः, उंदूरुः<BR>[उंद्-उर-उरु वा] A mouse, rat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्णी,<BR>--कर्णिका the plant Salvinia<BR>Cuccullata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंदुरुः|उन्दुरु|उंदुरु|उन्दुरुः
उंदरुः, उंदुरः, उंदुरुः, उंदूरुः<BR>[उंद्-उर-उरु वा] A mouse, rat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्णी,<BR>--कर्णिका the plant Salvinia<BR>Cuccullata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंदूरुः|उन्दूरु|उन्दूरुः
उंदरुः, उंदुरः, उंदुरुः, उंदूरुः<BR>[उंद्-उर-उरु वा] A mouse, rat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्णी,<BR>--कर्णिका the plant Salvinia<BR>Cuccullata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नद्
उन्नद् {c1c} P. To roar or below<BR>aloud, sound, roar (in general);<BR>असोढसिंहध्वनिरुन्ननाद Ku. 1. 56;<BR>कालमेघ इवोन्नदन् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नादः|उन्नाद
उन्नादः Crying out, roar,<BR>humming, chirping &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नम्
उन्नम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 (a) To rise,<BR>appear; उन्नम्योन्नम्य लीयंते दरिद्राणां<BR>मनोरथाः Pt. 2. 91. (b) To hang over,<BR>arise, impend; उन्नमत्यकालदुर्दिनम्<BR>Mk. 4, 5 an untimely storm<BR>impends; बहलोन्नमदंबुधराः Māl. 9. 18.<BR>(c) To rise, ascend, go up (fig.<BR>also); उन्नमति नमति वर्षति गर्जति मेघः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">Page0313-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Mk. 5; नम्रत्वेनोन्नमंतः Bh. 2. 69.<BR>--2<BR>To bend up, raise, elevate, erect;<BR>Ki. 16. 35. --Caus. (नमयति)<BR>1 To<BR>bend upwards, raise, erect;<BR>मुखमुन्नमय्य Ku. 7. 23; Ś. 3. 25; R. 1. 41.<BR>--2 (fig.) To elevate, raise to<BR>eminence; उन्नमय बंधुवर्गं K. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0312-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नत|उन्नतः
उन्नत p. p.<BR>1 Raised, elevated,<BR>uplifted (fig. also);<BR>उपासितगुरुप्रज्ञाभिमानोन्नताः Bh. 3. 24; Śi. 9. 79;<BR>नतोन्नतभूमिभागे Ś. 4. 14.<BR>--2 High (fig.<BR>also), tall, lofty; great, eminent;<BR>स्थितः सर्वोन्नतेनोर्वी क्रांत्वा मेरुरिवात्मना<BR>R. 1. 14; V. 5. 22; Ki. 5. 15, 14. 23;<BR>Pt. 1. 29; ˚इच्छः R. 6. 71; Śi. 7. 27;<BR>˚चेतस् a. noble-minded; Pt. 1. 122.<BR>--3 Projecting, plump, full (as<BR>breasts); M. 2. 3; Rs. 1. 7.<BR>--तः A<BR>boa (अजगर).<BR>--तं<BR>1 Elevation.<BR>--2<BR>Ascension, altitude.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आनत<BR>a. elevated and depressed, uneven,<BR>high and low; बंधुरं तून्नतानतं Ak.<BR>--चरण a. with uplifted paws,<BR>rampant.<BR>--नाभि a. having a<BR>projecting navel, i. e. corpulent, fat.<BR>--शिरस् a. carrying the head high,<BR>holding up the head, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतत्वं|उन्नतत्व
उन्नतत्वं Height, sublimity, majesty;<BR>R. 5. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतिः|उन्नति
उन्नतिः f.<BR>1 Elevation, height (fig.<BR>also); see उन्नतिमत् below.<BR>--2<BR>Exaltation, dignity, rise, prosperity,<BR>increase; स्तोकेनोन्नतिमायाति<BR>स्तोकेनायात्यधोगतिं Pt. 1. 150; ध्वजानामुन्नतिः<BR>K. 55; Śi. 16. 22, 72; Bv. 1. 40;<BR>महाजनस्य संपर्कः कस्य नोन्नतिकारकः<BR>H. 3. v. l.; मान˚ Bh. 2. 23.<BR>--3<BR>Raising.<BR>--4 The wife of Garuḍa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः N. of Garuḍa (Lord of<BR>उन्नति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नतिमत्|उन्नतिमन्त्
उन्नतिमत् a.<BR>1 Elevated,<BR>projecting, plump (as breasts); सा<BR>पीनोन्नतिमत्पयोधरयुगं धत्ते Amaru. 30;<BR>Śi. 9. 72.<BR>--2 High, sublime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमनं|उन्नमन
उन्नमनं<BR>1 Raising, lifting up.<BR>--2<BR>Height, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नमित|उन्नमितः
उन्नमित p. p.<BR>1 Raised, lifted up.<BR>--2 Heightened, increased, proved<BR>to be superior; ˚उपदेशः M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नम्र
उन्नम्र a. Erect, upright, lofty,<BR>high (fig. also);<BR>उन्नम्रताम्रपटमंडपमंडितं तत् Śi. 5. 68; ˚ता erectness,<BR>uprightness (of the body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नामः|उन्नाम
उन्नामः Raising, lifting up;<BR>शतबुद्धिः कृतोन्नामः Pt. 5. 45 lifted up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नय|उन्नयः
उन्नय --यनं See under उन्नी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयनं|उन्नयन
