उन्नस
उन्नस a. [उन्नता नासिका यस्य]<BR>Having a prominent nose; उन्नसं<BR>दधती वक्त्रं Bk. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नह्
उन्नह् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To tie up, bind up,<BR>fasten round.<BR>--2 To draw out, pull<BR>out.<BR>--3 To come out of, rise from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नद्ध
उन्नद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Tied or bound up,<BR>fastened; तेऽस्य मुक्तागुणोन्नद्धं<BR>मौलिमंतर्गतस्रजं R. 17. 23; 18. 50;<BR>Ku. 3. 46.<BR>--2 Swelled, increased, heaving;<BR>श्वासोन्नद्धपयोधर Gīt. 12.<BR>--3<BR>Unbound.<BR>--4 Elated, flushed with;<BR>वीर्य˚, मद˚, बल˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाहः|उन्नाह|उन्नाहं
उन्नाहः<BR>1 Projection,<BR>protuberance; स्तन˚ Māl. 9; rise;<BR>बलाहक˚ K. 26.<BR>--2 Tying up.<BR>--हं Sour<BR>gruel made from the fermentation<BR>of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाभ|उन्नाभः
उन्नाभ a. Having a<BR>projecting navel, corpulent.<BR>--भः N. of a<BR>king of the Solar race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नाल
उन्नाल a. With the stalk<BR>prominently appearing; Māl. 9. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्निद्र|उन्निद्रः
उन्निद्र a. [उद्गता निद्रा यस्य]<BR>1<BR>Sleepless, awake, without one wink of<BR>sleep; तामुन्निद्रामवनिशयनां<BR>सौधवातायनस्थः Me. 88; विगमयत्युन्निद्र एव क्षपाः<BR>Ś. 6. 4; Mu. 4. 2; Māl. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Expanded, full-blown, budded (as<BR>lotuses.); ˚अरविंदं K. 22;<BR>उन्निद्रपुष्पाक्षिसहस्रभाजा Śi. 4. 13, 31, 8. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नी
उन्नी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To lead upwards,<BR>bring up.<BR>--2 To raise, erect, lift<BR>up (A.); दंडमुन्नयते Sk.; स्वदंष्ट्रोन्नीतधरो<BR>वराहः Bhāg.<BR>--3 To bring out of, free<BR>from, help, rescue, redeem; रसाया<BR>लीलयोन्नीतां उर्वीं Bhāg.<BR>--4 To draw up<BR>(as water).<BR>--5 To stroke;<BR>straighten out.<BR>--6 To lead out or<BR>aside, lead away; एकांतमुन्नीय Mb.<BR>--7 To press out, extract.<BR>--8 To<BR>infer, ascertain, guess,<BR>conjecture; कथमपि स इत्युन्नेतव्यस्तथापि दृशोः<BR>प्रियः U. 3. 22, 1. 29, 6. 26; V. 4;<BR>प्रकृतिप्रत्ययाद्यर्थैः संकीर्णे लिंगमुन्नयेत्<BR>Ak.<BR>--9 To fill completely.<BR>--10 To<BR>lead off (in singing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयः|उन्नय
उन्नयः, उन्नायः<BR>1 Raising,<BR>elevating.<BR>--2 Height, elevation.<BR>--3<BR>Analogy, resemblance.<BR>--4 Inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नायः|उन्नाय
उन्नयः, उन्नायः<BR>1 Raising,<BR>elevating.<BR>--2 Height, elevation.<BR>--3<BR>Analogy, resemblance.<BR>--4 Inference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नयन|उन्नयनं
उन्नयन a. With the eyes raised<BR>upwards; R. 4. 3.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Raising,<BR>elevating, lifting up.<BR>--2 Drawing<BR>up water.<BR>--3 The vessel out<BR>of which a fluid is taken.<BR>--4<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">Page0313-c+ 55</a>]<BR>Leading away, extracting.<BR>--5 Making<BR>straight, smoothing; सीमंत˚.<BR>--6<BR>Deliberation, discussion.<BR>--7<BR>Inference; श्रवणादनु पश्चादीक्षा अन्वीक्षा उन्नयनं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नायक
उन्नायक a.<BR>1 Raising, lifting up.<BR>--2 What leads to an inference or<BR>conclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नेतृ
उन्नेतृ a.<BR>1 Raising, leading up.<BR>--2 Leading to an inference. --m.<BR>One of the 16 priests at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्नेत्रं|उन्नेत्र
उन्नेत्रं The office of the उन्नेतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्ज्
उन्मज्ज्(मस्ज्) {c6c} P. To emerge,<BR>rise up; वन्यः सरित्तो गज उन्ममज्ज<BR>R. 5. 43, 16. 79; उन्ममज्ज<BR>शनकैस्तुहिनांशुः Ki. 9. 23; Ś. 7. 8; Śi. 9. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मस्ज्
उन्मज्ज्(मस्ज्) {c6c} P. To emerge,<BR>rise up; वन्यः सरित्तो गज उन्ममज्ज<BR>R. 5. 43, 16. 79; उन्ममज्ज<BR>शनकैस्तुहिनांशुः Ki. 9. 23; Ś. 7. 8; Śi. 9. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्जक|उन्मज्जकः
उन्मज्जक a. Emerging, rising up.<BR>--कः A kind of ascetic; कंठदघ्ने जले<BR>स्थित्वा तपः कुर्वन् प्रवर्तते । उन्मज्जकः स<BR>विज्ञेयस्तापसो लोकपूजितः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मज्जनं|उन्मज्जन|उन्मज्जनः
उन्मज्जनं Emerging, coming out of<BR>water.<BR>--नः An attendant of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मथ्
उन्मथ्, उन्मंथ् {c1c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To<BR>shake up, disturb, excite, stir; pain.<BR>--2 To strike, kill, destroy;<BR>मीमांसाकृतमुन्ममाथ सहसा हस्ती मुनिं जैमिनिं<BR>Pt. 2. 33; धैर्यमुन्मथ्य Māl. 1. 18;<BR>विकल्पनिद्रामुन्मथ्य Prab.<BR>--3 To tear,<BR>cut off, peel off; वन्यद्विपेनोन्मथिता<BR>त्वगस्य R. 2. 37.<BR>--4 To mix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मंथ्
उन्मथ्, उन्मंथ् {c1c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To<BR>shake up, disturb, excite, stir; pain.<BR>--2 To strike, kill, destroy;<BR>मीमांसाकृतमुन्ममाथ सहसा हस्ती मुनिं जैमिनिं<BR>Pt. 2. 33; धैर्यमुन्मथ्य Māl. 1. 18;<BR>विकल्पनिद्रामुन्मथ्य Prab.<BR>--3 To tear,<BR>cut off, peel off; वन्यद्विपेनोन्मथिता<BR>त्वगस्य R. 2. 37.<BR>--4 To mix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मथन
उन्मथन a. Tearing, disturbing,<BR>paining.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Shaking off,<BR>throwing off or down.<BR>--2 Killing,<BR>slaughter; अन्योन्यसूतोन्मथनात् R. 7. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मंथः|उन्मन्थ|उन्मंथ|उन्मन्थः
उन्मंथः<BR>1 Agitation, disturbance.<BR>--2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>--3 A disease<BR>of the outer ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मंथक|उन्मन्थक|उन्मन्थकः
उन्मंथक a.<BR>1 Shaking off,<BR>agitating, stirring.<BR>--2 Throbbing,<BR>beating.<BR>--कः Inflammation of the<BR>outer ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मंथनं|उन्मन्थन|उन्मंथन
उन्मंथनं<BR>1 Shaking off, agitating.<BR>--2 Killing, slaughter, hurting.<BR>--3<BR>Beating (with a stick).<BR>--4 Probing,<BR>stirring a dart lodged in the body.<BR>--5 The instrument used for this<BR>purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माथ|उन्माथः
उन्माथ a. Destroying or killing.<BR>--थः<BR>1 Torment, pang, deep pain;<BR>˚वेगाः Māl. 9. 45.<BR>--2 Shaking,<BR>agitation.<BR>--3 Killing, slaughter.<BR>--4<BR>A snare or trap; प्रयोजयति चोन्माथं<BR>नित्यमस्तं गते रवौ Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माथिन्
उन्माथिन् a.<BR>1 Shaking, agitating.<BR>--2 Tormenting, excruciating;<BR>Māl. 9. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0313-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मद्
उन्मद् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be or become<BR>mad.<BR>--2 To delight, gratify. --Caus.<BR>(म-मा-दयति) To madden, inebriate,<BR>render drunk (lit. and fig.);<BR>लक्ष्म्योन्मादिताः K. 107; Ki. 4. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्त|उन्मत्तः
उन्मत्त p. p.<BR>1 Drunk,<BR>intoxicated.<BR>--2 Insane, frantic, mad;<BR>द्वावत्रोन्मत्तौ V. 2; अहो उन्मत्तास्मि संवृत्ता<BR>U. 3, 5. 30; Ś. 6; Ms. 9. 79.<BR>--3 (a)<BR>Puffed, elevated. (b) Furious, wild;<BR>मदोन्मत्तस्य भूपस्य कुंजरस्य च गच्छतः<BR>Pt. 1. 161; U. 2; Śi. 6. 31.<BR>--4<BR>Possessed by a ghost or an evil spirit;<BR>Y. 2. 32; Ms. 3. 161 (<BR>वातपित्तश्लेष्मसंनिपातग्रहसंभवेनोपसृष्टः Mit.).<BR>--त्तः The<BR>thorn apple (धत्तूर); N. of another<BR>tree (मुचकुद).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीर्तिः, --वेशः<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--गंगं N. of a country<BR>(where the Gaṅgā roars furiously<BR>along).<BR>--दर्शन, --रूप a. maniac-like,<BR>mad in appearance.<BR>--प्रलपित a.<BR>spoken in drunkenness or madness.<BR>--(तं) the words of a madman.<BR>--लिंगिन् a. pretending to be mad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मत्तक
उन्मत्तक a.<BR>1 Insane, mad.<BR>--2<BR>Drunk, intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मद|उन्मदः
उन्मद a.<BR>1 Intoxicated, drunk;<BR>उदीरयामासुरिवोन्मदानाम् R. 2. 9, 16. 54.<BR>--2 Mad, furious, extravagant;<BR>Śi. 10. 4, 12. 44, 77; 16. 59.<BR>--3<BR>Causing intoxication, intoxicating;<BR>मधुकरांगनया मुहुरुन्मदध्वनिभृता<BR>निभृताक्षरमुज्जगे Śi. 6. 20.<BR>--दः<BR>1 Insanity.<BR>--2<BR>Intoxication, ecstacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदन
उन्मदन a. [उद्भूतो मदनोऽस्य]<BR>Affected or inflamed with love;<BR>तदाप्रभृत्युन्मदना बभूव Ku. 5. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मदिष्णु|उन्मदिष्णुः
उन्मदिष्णु a.<BR>1 Mad, insane.<BR>--2<BR>Intoxicated, drunk.<BR>--3 In rut (as<BR>an elephant); Śi. 12. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्माद|उन्मादः
उन्माद a.<BR>1 Mad, insane.<BR>--2<BR>Extravagant.<BR>--दः<BR>1 Madness,<BR>insanity; अहो उन्मादः U. 3; Māl. 9.<BR>--2<BR>Intense passion, intoxication or<BR>extravagance of love; Māl. 3, 2. 11;<BR>वीररभसेन्मादः Mv. 2. 22 rapturous joy.<BR>--3 Lunacy, mania (considered as a<BR>disease of the mind); मदयंत्युद्धता दोषा<BR>यस्मादुन्मार्गमाश्रिताः । मानसोऽयमतो<BR>व्याधिरुन्माद इति कीर्तितः ॥ Suśr.<BR>--4 (In<BR>Rhet.) Madness considered as one of<BR>the 33 subordinate feelings;<BR>चित्तसंमोह उन्मादः कामशोकभयादिभिः<BR>S. D. 3; or according to R. G.<BR>विप्रलंभमहापत्तिपरमानंदादिजन्माऽ<BR>न्यस्मिन्नन्यावभास उन्मादः.<BR>--5 Bloom; उन्मादं वीक्ष्य<BR>पद्मानां S. D. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादकः|उन्मादक
उन्मादकः N. of the plant धत्तूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादन|उन्मादनः
उन्मादन a. Maddening, exciting,<BR>intoxicating.<BR>--नः One of the five<BR>arrows of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादयितृक
उन्मादयितृक a. Intoxicating,<BR>enrapturing; Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादिन्
उन्मादिन् a. Mad, intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मादुक
उन्मादुक a. Fond of drinking<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनस्
उन्मनस्, --नस्क a. [उद्भ्रांतं मनोऽस्य]<BR>1 Excited or disturbed in mind,<BR>perplexed, agitated, uneasy; उन्मनाः<BR>प्रथमजन्मचेष्टितान्यस्मरन्नपि बभूव राघवः<BR>R. 11. 22; Ki. 14. 45.<BR>--2 Regretting,<BR>repining for a lost or departed<BR>friend.<BR>--3 Anxious, eager, impatient;<BR>गंतुं पावकमुन्मनस्तदभवत् Bh. 2. 75.<BR>--4<BR>Proud (मनस्विन्); Śi. 16. 3 (where it<BR>also means “anxious”).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनस्क
उन्मनस्, --नस्क a. [उद्भ्रांतं मनोऽस्य]<BR>1 Excited or disturbed in mind,<BR>perplexed, agitated, uneasy; उन्मनाः<BR>प्रथमजन्मचेष्टितान्यस्मरन्नपि बभूव राघवः<BR>R. 11. 22; Ki. 14. 45.<BR>--2 Regretting,<BR>repining for a lost or departed<BR>friend.<BR>--3 Anxious, eager, impatient;<BR>गंतुं पावकमुन्मनस्तदभवत् Bh. 2. 75.<BR>--4<BR>Proud (मनस्विन्); Śi. 16. 3 (where it<BR>also means “anxious”).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनायते
उन्मनायते Den. A., उन्मनीभू {c1c} P.<BR>To become excited or disturbed in<BR>mind, be uneasy, regret; अस्मद्विना<BR>मा भृशमुन्मनीभूः Ki. 3. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मनीकृ
उन्मनीकृ {c8c} U. To make excited,<BR>disturb; Ki. 10. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मयूख
उन्मयूख a. Shining, radiant;<BR>R. 16. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मर्दनं|उन्मर्दन
उन्मर्दनं<BR>1 Rubbing, kneading.<BR>--2 A fragrant essence used for the<BR>purpose of rubbing.<BR>--3 Act of<BR>purifying air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मा
उन्मा Ved. A measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मानं|उन्मान|उन्मानः
उन्मानं<BR>1 Weighing, measuring<BR>upwards; ऊर्ध्वमानं किलोन्मानं.<BR>--2 A<BR>measure of size or quantity.<BR>--3<BR>Price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मित
उन्मित a. Measured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मितिः|उन्मिति
उन्मितिः f. Measure; price.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेय
उन्मेय a. To be weighed; what is<BR>weighed.<BR>--यं Weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्ग|उन्मार्गः
उन्मार्ग a. [उत्क्रांतः मार्गात्] Going to<BR>a wrong path.<BR>--र्गः<BR>1 A wrong road,<BR>deviation from the right road (fig.<BR>also); नित्यमुन्मार्गगामिनां Pt. 1.<BR>--2<BR>An improper conduct, evil course,<BR>moral turpitude; उन्मार्गप्रस्थितानि<BR>इंद्रियाणि K. 155; ˚प्रवर्तकः 103.<BR>--र्गं<BR>ind. Astray, by a wrong way;<BR>Pt. 1. 161.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गत a. going<BR>wrong.<BR>--गमनं following evil courses.<BR>--गामिन्, --वर्तिन् a. going wrong,<BR>erring, taking a wrong road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्गिन्
उन्मार्गिन् a. Going astray; finding<BR>an outlet (as water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिश्र
उन्मिश्र a. Mixed with,<BR>variegated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिष्
उन्मिष् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To open the eyes;<BR>उन्मिमेष तदा मुनिः Bhāg. Bg. 5. 9;<BR>Dk. 111.<BR>--2 To open (as the eyes);<BR>प्रलयांतोन्मिषिते विलोचने Ku. 4. 2.<BR>--3 To open, bloom, be expanded<BR>(as lotuses); उन्मिषदुत्पलवन<BR>K. 22.<BR>--4 To rise, peep up (as stars);<BR>उन्मिषत्सु ग्रहग्रामणीषु K. 176.<BR>--5 To<BR>shine, glitter, flash; as तेजस<BR>--6<BR>To arise, originate; उन्मिषद्रोमहर्ष,<BR>उन्मिषत्तोषं &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिष|उन्मिषः
उन्मिष a. Blown, opened.<BR>--षः<BR>Opening the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मिषित|उन्मिषितः
उन्मिषित p. p. Opened(as eyes),<BR>blown, expanded &c.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A<BR>look, glance; Ku. 5. 25; K. 72.<BR>--2 Opening; R. 5. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेषः|उन्मेष|उन्मेषं
उन्मेषः, --षणं<BR>1 Opening (of the<BR>eyes), winking, twinkling (of<BR>eyes); प्रत्यग्रोन्मेषजिह्मा Mu. 3. 21.<BR>--2<BR>Blowing, opening, expansion; उन्मेषं<BR>यो मम न सहते जातिवैरी निशायां<BR>K. P. 10; दीर्घिकाकमलोन्मेषः Ku. 2. 33.<BR>--3 Light, flash, brilliancy; सतां<BR>प्रज्ञोन्मेषः Bh. 2. 114 light or flash;<BR>विद्युदुन्मेषदृष्टिं Me. 81.<BR>--4 Awakening,<BR>rising, becoming visible,<BR>manifestation; ज्ञान˚ Śānti. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेषणं|उन्मेषण
उन्मेषः, --षणं<BR>1 Opening (of the<BR>eyes), winking, twinkling (of<BR>eyes); प्रत्यग्रोन्मेषजिह्मा Mu. 3. 21.<BR>--2<BR>Blowing, opening, expansion; उन्मेषं<BR>यो मम न सहते जातिवैरी निशायां<BR>K. P. 10; दीर्घिकाकमलोन्मेषः Ku. 2. 33.<BR>--3 Light, flash, brilliancy; सतां<BR>प्रज्ञोन्मेषः Bh. 2. 114 light or flash;<BR>विद्युदुन्मेषदृष्टिं Me. 81.<BR>--4 Awakening,<BR>rising, becoming visible,<BR>manifestation; ज्ञान˚ Śānti. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेषिन्
उन्मेषिन् a. Flying about,<BR>glittering about; Māl. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मील्
उन्मील् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To open (as the<BR>eyes); उदमीलीच्च लोचने Bk. 15. 102;<BR>16. 8.<BR>--2 To be awakened or<BR>roused, be excited; उन्मिमील विशदं<BR>विषमेषुः Śi. 10. 72; Bk. 1. 33.<BR>--3 To<BR>expand, blow (as lotuses);<BR>सरोभिरुन्मीलितपद्मलोचनैः Ki. 4. 3;<BR>Māl. 1. 38, 9. 15.<BR>--4 To be diffused or<BR>spread, cluster round;<BR>प्रांतोन्मीलन्मनोहरकुंतलैः U. 1. 20; उन्मीलन्मधुगंध<BR>Gīt. 1.<BR>--5 To appear, become<BR>manifest; खं वायुर्ज्वलनो जलं क्षितिरिति<BR>त्रैलोक्यमुन्मीलति Prab. 1. 2.<BR>--6 To break<BR>forth, burst out; U. 4. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>open (eyes, lotuses &c.); तदेतदुन्मीलय<BR>चक्षुरायतं V. 1. 5; Mk. 1. 33.<BR>--2 To<BR>display, show; त्वयाद्य साधुतोन्मीलिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलः|उन्मील
उन्मीलः, --लनं<BR>1 Opening (of the<BR>eyes), awaking;<BR>ज्ञानांजनशलाकाभिर्नेत्रोन्मीलनकारकः Mb.<BR>--2 Unfolding,<BR>opening (in general);<BR>प्रियागुणसहस्राणामेकोन्मीलनपेशलः U. 6. 34.<BR>--3<BR>Touching up, painting; आलेख्य˚<BR>K. 267.<BR>--4 Expanding, blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलनं|उन्मीलन
उन्मीलः, --लनं<BR>1 Opening (of the<BR>eyes), awaking;<BR>ज्ञानांजनशलाकाभिर्नेत्रोन्मीलनकारकः Mb.<BR>--2 Unfolding,<BR>opening (in general);<BR>प्रियागुणसहस्राणामेकोन्मीलनपेशलः U. 6. 34.<BR>--3<BR>Touching up, painting; आलेख्य˚<BR>K. 267.<BR>--4 Expanding, blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0314-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मीलित|उन्मीलितः
उन्मीलित p. p.<BR>1 Opened;<BR>अज्ञानतिमिरांधस्य ज्ञानांजनशलाकया ।<BR>चक्षुरुन्मीलितं येन तस्मै पाणिनये नमः ॥ Śik. 58;<BR>Ki. 16. 12.<BR>--2 Blown, expanded;<BR>ते चोन्मीलितमालतीसुरभयः प्रौढाः<BR>कदंबानिलाः; K. P. 1; awakened;<BR>Mv. 1. 48; K. 110.<BR>--3 Touched up, painted;<BR>उन्मीलितं तूलिकयेव चित्रं Ku. 1. 32.<BR>--तं (In Rhet.) An open reference<BR>(to anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुख|उन्मुखः
उन्मुख a. (खी f.) [उद्-ऊर्ध्वं मुखं<BR>यस्य]<BR>1 Raising the face, looking<BR>up; ˚दर्शन looking upwards; अद्रेः<BR>शृंगं हरति पवनः किंस्विदित्युन्मुखीभिः<BR>Me. 14, 100; R. 1. 39, 11. 26; आश्रम˚<BR>1. 53.<BR>--2 Ready, intent on, on the<BR>point of, about to, prepared for;<BR>तमरण्यसमाश्रयोन्मुखं R. 8. 12 about<BR>to retire to the woods; 16. 9,<BR>3. 12; उदयोन्मुखचंद्रिका M. 5. 7;<BR>भेदोन्मुखं V. 2. 7; Ku. 6. 48.<BR>--3 Eager,<BR>waiting for, expecting, looking up<BR>to; तस्मिन् संयमिनामाद्ये जाते<BR>परिणयोन्मुखे Ku. 6. 34; लक्ष्मीरिव<BR>गुणोन्मुखी R. 12. 26, 6. 21, 11. 23.<BR>--4 Sounding, speaking or<BR>making a sound; परभृतोन्मुखी Ku. 6. 2<BR>speaking through the cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुखर
उन्मुखर a. Loud-sounding, noisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुच्
उन्मुच् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To unfasten, pull<BR>off; उन्मुच्य सूत्रेण विनैव हाराः<BR>R. 6. 28; take off (clothes &c.);<BR>आत्मकंठादुन्मुच्य K. 147, 67; Bk. 3. 22.<BR>--2 To loosen, liberate, free from<BR>(as a bond); ऋणमुन्मुच्य देवानां Mb.;<BR>open (as a letter); लेखमुन्मुच्य<BR>Rāj. T. 3. 235; K. 221.<BR>--3 To raise,<BR>elevate, send forth (as sound);<BR>आर्तनादो हि यः पौरैरुन्मुक्तः Rām.<BR>--4<BR>To fling, hurl (as a missile).<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To extricate, loosen, free;<BR>Mv. 6. 46.<BR>--2 To deliver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुक्त
उन्मुक्त p. p. Pulled off, loosened<BR>&c.; ˚कंठं bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मोचनं|उन्मोचन
उन्मोचनं Unfastening, loosening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मुद्र|उन्मुद्रः
उन्मुद्र a. [उद्गता मुद्रा यस्मात्]<BR>1<BR>Unsealed.<BR>--2 Opened, blown,<BR>expanded (as a flower).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूल्
उन्मूल् {c10c} P. To eradicate,<BR>pluck up by the roots, exterminate;<BR>समूलमुन्मूलयतीव मे मनः Ki. 1. 41;<BR>उन्मूलिता हलधरेण पदावघातैः Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मूलनं|उन्मूलन
उन्मूलनं Plucking up by the<BR>roots, eradication, destroying,<BR>uprooting; न पादपोन्मूलनशक्ति रंहः<BR>R. 2. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृज्
उन्मृज् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To rub or wipe<BR>off, clean by washing; Y. 1. 20.<BR>--2 To efface, blot out, obliterate.<BR>--3 To receive, accept (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मार्जनं|उन्मार्जन
उन्मार्जनं Rubbing, wiping off,<BR>removing; मनःशल्य˚ Dk. 161.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृजावमृजा
उन्मृजावमृजा Repeatedly rubbing<BR>up and down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मृष्ट
उन्मृष्ट p. p. Blotted out, effaced,<BR>cleared, removed, wiped off;<BR>R. 15. 32; Y. 2. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उन्मेदा
उन्मेदा f. Corpulence, fatness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप
उप ind.<BR>1 As a prefix to verbs<BR>and nouns it expresses towards,<BR>near to, by the side of, with,<BR>under, down (opp. अप). According to<BR>G. M. the following are its senses:<BR>--उप<BR>सामीप्यसामर्थ्यव्यात्याचार्यकृतिमृतिदोषदानक्रियावीप्सारंभाध्ययनपूजनेषुः-- (1)<BR>nearness, contiguity; उपविशति, उपगच्छति<BR>goes near; (2) power, ability;<BR>उपकरोति; (3) pervasion; उपकीर्ण; (4) advice,<BR>instructing as by a teacher; उपदिशति,<BR>उपदेश; (5) death, extinction, उपरत;<BR>(6) defect, fault; उपघात; (7) giving;<BR>उपनयति, उपहरति; (8) action,<BR>effort; उप त्वानेष्ये; (9) beginning,<BR>commencement; उपक्रमते, उपक्रम;<BR>(10) study; उपाध्यायः; (11)<BR>reverence, worship; उपस्थानं, उपचरति पितरं<BR>पुत्रः. It is also said to have the<BR>senses of disease, ornament,<BR>command, reproof, killing, wish,<BR>resemblance &c.<BR>--2 As unconnected<BR>with verbs and prefixed to nouns,<BR>it expresses direction towards,<BR>nearness, resemblance, relationship,<BR>contiguity in space, number, time,<BR>degree &c., but generally involving<BR>the idea of subordination or<BR>inferiourity; उपकनिष्ठिका the finger next<BR>to the little finger; उपपुराणं a<BR>secondary Purāṇa; उपगुरुः an assistant<BR>master; उपाध्यक्षः a vice-president.<BR>It usually, however, forms Avyayī.<BR>comp. in these senses; उपगंगं = गंगायाः<BR>समीपे; उपकूलं, ˚वनं &c.; these are<BR>again compounded with other<BR>words; उपकूपजलाशयः, उपकंठनिवासिनी.<BR>Prefixed to proper nouns it means<BR>a ‘younger brother’; उपेंद्रः.<BR>--3 With<BR>numerals it forms संख्याबहुव्रीहि and<BR>means ‘nearly,’ ‘almost’; उपत्रिंशाः<BR>nearly thirty; उपविंशाः about twenty<BR>&c.<BR>--4 As a separable preposition<BR>(a) with acc. when it means<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">Page0315-c+ 54</a>]<BR>inferiority (P. I. 4. 87); उप हरिं सुराः Sk<BR>the gods are under i. e. are inferior<BR>to Hari; शक्रादय उपाच्युतं Vop. (b)<BR>With loc. it expresses (1) over,<BR>above, superior to; उप निष्के कार्षापणं,<BR>उप परार्धे हरेर्गुणाः; (2) addition; (3)<BR>near to, towards, in the direction of,<BR>under; (4) at, on, upon; (5)<BR>upto, in, above; e. g. उप सानुषु on or above<BR>the peaks; वयो न वसतीरुप; or<BR>sometimes (c) with the instr.; with, at<BR>the same time with, according. to<BR>--5<BR>As a separable adverb it is rarely<BR>used in the senses of further,<BR>moreover. उपासन्नेऽधिके हीने सादृश्यप्रतियत्नयोः ।<BR>तद्योगव्याप्तिपूजासु शक्तावारंभदानयोः ॥<BR>दक्षिणाचार्यकरणदोषाख्यानात्ययेषु च ।. [cf. Gr.<BR>hupo; L. sub; Goth. up; Germ. ob.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकक्ष
उपकक्ष a. Ved. Reaching to the<BR>shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकंठ|उपकण्ठ|उपकण्ठं|उपकण्ठः
उपकंठ a. Near, proximate.<BR>--ठः,<BR>--ठं<BR>1 Proximity, vicinity,<BR>neighbourhood; प्राप तालीवनश्याममुपकंठं<BR>महोदधेः R. 4. 34; 13. 48;<BR>Ku. 7. 51; Māl. 9. 2; आकृष्य चापं<BR>श्रवणोपकंठे Ś. 3. 5 to the very ear.<BR>--2<BR>Space near a village or its boundary.<BR>--3 One of a horse's paces. --ind.<BR>1 Upon the neck, near the throat;<BR>प्रेम्णोपकंठं मुहुरंकभाजः Śi. 3. 36.<BR>--2<BR>In the vicinity of, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकथा
उपकथा A short story or tale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकनिष्ठिका
उपकनिष्ठिका [उपगता कनिष्ठिकां]<BR>The finger next to the little finger,<BR>the last but one finger (अनामिका);<BR>Śik. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकन्या
उपकन्या The friend of one's<BR>daughter; ˚पुरं near the woman's<BR>apartments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्ण्
उपकर्ण् {c10c} U. To hear; Śi. 20. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णं|उपकर्ण|उपकर्ण्ण
उपकर्णं ind. Close to the ear, into<BR>the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णनं
उपकर्णनं Hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्णिका
उपकर्णिका Rumour, report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकिरण|उपकिरणं
उपकिरण See under उपकॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकीचकः|उपकीचक
उपकीचकः<BR>1 A relation or<BR>follower of Kīcaka.<BR>--2 The army of<BR>Virāṭa under Kīcaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुंचिः|उपकुञ्चि|उपकुञ्चिः
उपकुंचिः, --चिका<BR>1 The plant<BR>Nigella Indica (कृष्णजीरक).<BR>--2<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुंचिका|उपकुञ्चिका
उपकुंचिः, --चिका<BR>1 The plant<BR>Nigella Indica (कृष्णजीरक).<BR>--2<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुंभ|उपकुम्भ|उपकुम्भं
उपकुंभ a.<BR>1 Near, proximate.<BR>--2 Solitary, retired, secluded.<BR>--भं<BR>ind. Near a jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0315-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुल्या
उपकुल्या<BR>1 The plant Piper<BR>Longum.<BR>--2 A canal, trench.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुशः|उपकुश
उपकुशः Gum-boil; a disease of<BR>the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूज्
उपकूज् {c1c} P. To fill with cooing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूजित
उपकूजित p. p. Made to resound<BR>(with cooing).<BR>--तं Filling with<BR>cooing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूपं|उपकूप|उपकूपः
उपकूपं --पे ind. Near a well;<BR>˚जलाशयः a trough near a well for<BR>watering cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूपे
उपकूपं --पे ind. Near a well;<BR>˚जलाशयः a trough near a well for<BR>watering cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकूलं|उपकूल
उपकूलं ind. On the shore;<BR>R. 15. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृ
उपकृ {c8c} U. (a) उपकरोति-कुरुते.<BR>1<BR>To place or bring near, furnish<BR>or provide with, do or render;<BR>किं ते भूयः प्रियमुपकरोतु पाकशासनः<BR>V. 5; Ms. 2. 149, 245, 5. 32.<BR>--2 To<BR>assist, serve, befriend, oblige,<BR>favour, benefit, help; प्राणैरप्युपकुर्वते<BR>Pt. 1. 83; Bk. 8. 18; (oft. with<BR>gen. of person); सा लक्ष्मीरुपकुरुते<BR>यया परेषां Ki. 7. 28, 8. 13;<BR>आत्मनश्चोपकर्तुं Me. 101; Śi. 20. 74;<BR>K. 174; न हि दीपौ परस्परस्योपकुरुतः Ś. B.;<BR>sometimes with loc. also;<BR>Ms. 8. 394.<BR>--3 To foster, take care of.<BR>--4<BR>To render homage, serve, wait or<BR>attend upon (with acc.); हरिमुपकुरुते<BR>Sk.<BR>--5 To begin, set about<BR>anything (with dat.).<BR>--6 To subdue,<BR>overcome. (b) उपस्करोति, -स्कुरुते.<BR>1 To add, supply (वाक्याध्याहारे);<BR>उपस्कृतं ब्रूते P. VI. 1. 139 Sk.<BR>--2<BR>To provide or furnish with;<BR>सितातपत्रव्यजनैरुपस्कृतः Bhāg.<BR>--3 To<BR>attend or wait on, serve.<BR>--4 To<BR>adorn, decorate, elaborate, refine,<BR>polish, prepare, perfect; राजतं<BR>चानुपस्कृतं Ms. 5. 112; उपस्कृता कन्या<BR>Sk.; Bh. 2. 15.<BR>--5 (a) To care for,<BR>take care of (with acc. of person);<BR>P. I. 3. 32, VI. 1. 139. (b) To<BR>make efforts (with gen. of thing);<BR>एधोदकस्योपस्कुरुते, मा कस्यचिदुपस्कृथाः<BR>Bk. 8. 19, 119.<BR>--6 To furnish<BR>badly, deform; Ms. 3. 257.<BR>--7 To<BR>corrupt, defile, censure; 7. 98.<BR>--8 To<BR>bring or call together; उपस्कृता<BR>ब्राह्मणाः (= समुदिताः Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकरणं|उपकरण
उपकरणं<BR>1 Doing service or<BR>favour, helping, assisting.<BR>--2<BR>Material, implement, instrument, means;<BR>स्वेषूपकरणेषु U. 5; ˚द्रव्यं Mk. 3;<BR>उपकरणीभावमायाति U. 3. 3 serve as<BR>helping instruments, or assistants;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-b" target="_blank">Page0316-b+ 55</a>]<BR>परोपकारोपकरणं शरीरं K. 207; so स्नान˚<BR>bathing materials; Pt. 1; व्यायाम˚ athletic<BR>materials; आत्मा परोपकरणीकृतः<BR>H. 2. 24; K. 80, 102, 198, 204;<BR>Y. 2. 276, Ms. 9. 270.<BR>--3 An engine,<BR>machine, apparatus, paraphernalia<BR>(in general).<BR>--4 Means of<BR>subsistence, anything supporting life.<BR>--5 A means or expedient; कर्म˚,<BR>वेद˚, यज्ञ˚ &c.<BR>--6 Fabricating,<BR>composing, elaborating.<BR>--7 The<BR>insignia of royalty.<BR>--8 The attendants<BR>of a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकर्तृ|उपकर्त्तृ
उपकर्तृ a. One who does a<BR>service or favour, useful, friendly;<BR>आपत्सूपकर्ता Dk. 160; हीनान्यनुपर्कतॄणि<BR>प्रवृद्धानि विकुर्वते R. 17. 58; उपकर्त्री<BR>रसादीनां S. D. 624; Śi. 2. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारः|उपकार
उपकारः<BR>1 Service, help, assistance,<BR>favour, kindness, obligation (opp.<BR>अपकार); उपकारापकारौ हि लक्ष्यं<BR>लक्षणमेतयोः Śi. 2. 37; शाम्येत्प्रत्यपकारेण<BR>नोपकारेण दुर्जनः Ku. 2. 40, 3. 73;<BR>Y. 3. 284; Pt. 1. 22; उपकारे वृत् to<BR>be of service or useful (to another).<BR>--2 Preparation.<BR>--3 Ornament,<BR>decoration.<BR>--4 Particularly, flowers,<BR>garlands &c. suspended at gate-ways<BR>as embellishments on festive<BR>occasions.<BR>--री<BR>1 A royal tent, palace.<BR>--2<BR>Caravansera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारक
उपकारक a. Doing service or<BR>favour, helping, contributing to,<BR>assisting, productive (of good<BR>results); उपकारकमायतेर्भृशं Ki. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिका
उपकारिका<BR>1 Protectress, a<BR>female assistant.<BR>--2 A palace.<BR>--3 A<BR>tent, a caravansera.<BR>--4 A kind of<BR>cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकारिन्
उपकारिन् a. Helping, serving,<BR>beneficial &c.; subservient, benefactor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकार्य|उपकार्य्य|उपकार्य्यः
उपकार्य a. Deserving<BR>assistance or favour, fit to be assisted.<BR>--र्या A royal house, palace; रम्यां<BR>रघुप्रतिनिधिः स नवोपकार्यां<BR>बाल्यात्परामिव दशां मदनोध्युवास R. 5. 63; a<BR>royal tent; तस्योपकार्यारचितोपचाराः<BR>5. 41, 11. 93, 13. 79, 16. 55, 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकुर्वाण|उपकुर्वाणः|उपकुर्व्वाण|उपकुर्व्वाणः
उपकुर्वाण a. Doing service &c.<BR>--णः A Brāhmaṇa in a state of<BR>pupilage (ब्रह्मचारिन्) who wishes to<BR>pass on to the state of a<BR>householder (गृहस्थ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृत
उपकृत p. p. Assisted, benefited,<BR>served &c.<BR>--तं Aid, favour,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">Page0316-c+ 55</a>]<BR>obligation; गता नाशं तारा<BR>उपकृतमसाधाविव जने Mk. 5. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकृतिः|उपकृति
उपकृतिः f., उपक्रिया Favour,<BR>obligation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकॄ
उपकॄ {c6c} P.<BR>1 To bestrew, scatter<BR>or throw down, scatter or pour<BR>upon; रत्नोपकीर्णां वसुधां Mb.<BR>--2 (<BR>उपस्कॄ) (a) To cut up, split, lop.<BR>(b) To hurt, strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकिरणं|उपकिरण
उपकिरणं<BR>1 Scattering or<BR>throwing over, covering up; burying.<BR>--2<BR>Pervasion. --ind. Near the rays.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकॢप्
उपकॢप् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To be fit for;<BR>तत्रेदमुपकल्पते Bhāg.<BR>--2 To be prepared<BR>or ready (at hand); आसनेषूपकॢप्तेषु<BR>Ms. 3. 208, 8. 333.<BR>--3 To result in,<BR>serve as, lead to (with dat.); वार्यपि<BR>श्रद्धया दत्तमक्षयायोपकल्पते Ms. 3. 202.<BR>--4 To become, take a (particular)<BR>form or shape. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>prepare, get ready, equip; रथं Ve. 2.<BR>--2 To appoint, assign, allot;<BR>उपकल्पितं पशुं Pt. 1; U. 2; Y. 1. 109.<BR>--3<BR>To vow, promise; देवतोपकल्पित<BR>Pt. 4.<BR>--4 To set up, exhibit.<BR>--5 To<BR>render (homage), communicate.<BR>--6 To bring near, fetch.<BR>--7 To<BR>assume, take.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पनं|उपकल्पन
उपकल्पनं, --ना<BR>1 Preparation; एवं<BR>विज्ञाय मतिमान् भोजनस्योपकल्पनां Suśr.<BR>--2 Fabricating, making &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पना
उपकल्पनं, --ना<BR>1 Preparation; एवं<BR>विज्ञाय मतिमान् भोजनस्योपकल्पनां Suśr.<BR>--2 Fabricating, making &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकल्पित
उपकल्पित p. p.<BR>1 Prepared,<BR>made &c.<BR>--2 Secondary, substituted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपकॢप्त
उपकॢप्त p. p.<BR>1 Brought near, at<BR>hand.<BR>--2 Ready, prepared.<BR>--3<BR>Fitted for, adapted to.<BR>--4 Formed,<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रम्
उपक्रम् {c1c} A., {c4c} P.<BR>1 To go near,<BR>approach, come to, advance<BR>towards; राज्ञस्तस्याज्ञया देवी<BR>वसिष्ठमुपचक्रमे Mb.; Bk. 8. 25.<BR>--2 To do,<BR>perform, set about; यथोक्तं<BR>निपुणमुपक्रांतवान् Dk. 120;<BR>माधवसमक्षमुत्तरमुपक्रमिष्ये Māl. 3, 2. 7; Y. 3. 200.<BR>--3 To begin, commence. (with inf.<BR>or dat.); (Atm.); प्रसभं वक्तुमुपक्रमेत<BR>कः Ki. 2. 28; प्रतिग्रहीतुं…<BR>त्रिलोचनस्तामुपचक्रमे च Ku. 3. 66; R. 17. 13.<BR>--4 To<BR>go against, attack, assail,<BR>उपचक्रमाते वाग्भिः Rām.<BR>--5 To make<BR>advances (of love) to;<BR>सर्वोपायैरुपक्रम्य सीतां Rām.; win over; Dk. 65.<BR>--6 To step over, stride, traverse.<BR>--7 To treat, act towards, attend<BR>on (as a physician); cure or heal<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">Page0317-a+ 56</a>]<BR>(as wounds); यत्नादुपक्रम्यतां Ś. 3<BR>v. l.; सर्वथोपक्रांतः Dk. 68; ˚व्रणा 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0316-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रंतृ|उपक्रन्तृ
उपक्रंतृ A beginner, one who<BR>undertakes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमः|उपक्रम
उपक्रमः<BR>1 Beginning,<BR>commencement; रामोपक्रममाचख्यौ रक्षःपरिभवं<BR>नवं R. 12. 42 begun by Rāma;<BR>किमुपक्रमो रावणः Mv. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Approach, advance; साहस˚ forcible<BR>advance Māl. 7; so योषितः<BR>सुकुमारोपक्रमाः ibid.<BR>--3 An undertaking,<BR>work, enterprize.<BR>--4 A plan,<BR>contrivance, means, expedient,<BR>stratagem, remedy; सामादिभिरुपक्रमैः<BR>Ms. 7. 107, 159; M. 3; R. 18. 15;<BR>Y. 1. 345; Śi. 20. 76.<BR>--5 Attendance on<BR>a patient, treatment, practice of<BR>medicine, physicking.<BR>--6 A test of<BR>honesty, trying the fidelity of a<BR>friend &c.; see उपधा.<BR>--7 A kind of<BR>ceremony preparatory to reading<BR>the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमणं|उपक्रमण
उपक्रमणं<BR>1 Approaching.<BR>--2<BR>Undertaking.<BR>--3 Commencement.<BR>--4<BR>(Medic.) Treatment, physicking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमणिका
उपक्रमणिका A preface,<BR>introduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमणीय
उपक्रमणीय a.<BR>1 To be gone to,<BR>approached, commenced &c.<BR>--2<BR>Relating to the attendance (on a<BR>patient).<BR>--यं A work on medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमितव्य
उपक्रमितव्य, उपक्रम्य pot. p.<BR>1 To<BR>be commenced or undertaken.<BR>--2<BR>Curable; अनुपक्रम्य आतंकः V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रम्य
उपक्रमितव्य, उपक्रम्य pot. p.<BR>1 To<BR>be commenced or undertaken.<BR>--2<BR>Curable; अनुपक्रम्य आतंकः V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रमितृ
उपक्रमितृ a. One who begins &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रीडा
उपक्रीडा A play-ground, a place<BR>for playing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रुश्
उपक्रुश् {c1c} P. To blame, chide,<BR>revile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रोशः|उपक्रोश
उपक्रोशः, --शनं Censure, reproach,<BR>ignominy; प्राणैरुपक्रोशमलीमसैर्वा<BR>R. 2. 53; वाक्सतंक्षणैर्लोकोपक्रोशनैः<BR>Dk. 41, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रोशनं|उपक्रोशन
उपक्रोशः, --शनं Censure, reproach,<BR>ignominy; प्राणैरुपक्रोशमलीमसैर्वा<BR>R. 2. 53; वाक्सतंक्षणैर्लोकोपक्रोशनैः<BR>Dk. 41, 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्रोष्टृ
उपक्रोष्टृ a. Censuring, blaming<BR>--m. An ass (braying aloud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्वणं|उपक्वण|उपक्वणः
उपक्व(क्वा)णं [उप-क्वण्-शब्दे,<BR>अप्-घञ् वा] The sound of a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्वाणं|उपक्वाण|उपक्वाणः
उपक्व(क्वा)णं [उप-क्वण्-शब्दे,<BR>अप्-घञ् वा] The sound of a lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्वसः|उपक्वस
उपक्वसः Ved. A kind of worm<BR>or insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षि
उपक्षि {c1c} P. or pass.<BR>1 To waste<BR>away, decay, be exhausted,<BR>disappear.<BR>--2 ({c2c} {c6c} P.) To dwell near<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षय|उपक्षयः
उपक्षय a. Decayed, wasted.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Waste, decay, loss.<BR>--2<BR>Expenditure.<BR>--यं ind. Near the abode.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षित्
उपक्षित् a. Ved.<BR>1 Dwelling near.<BR>--2 Clinging or attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षीण
उपक्षीण p. p.<BR>1 Decayed,<BR>exhausted, consumed, disappeared.<BR>--2<BR>Powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षेतृ
उपक्षेतृ a. One who draws near; or<BR>one who dwells near, attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षिप्
उपक्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To throw at, cast<BR>on, hurl against; वपुषि वधाय तत्र<BR>तव शस्त्रमुपक्षिपतः Māl. 5. 31; to<BR>direct; त्वयि उपक्षिप्त आत्मा M. 2; to<BR>entrust, assign; M. 3.<BR>--2 To insult,<BR>upbraid, accuse, charge with;<BR>परस्परं वाग्भिरुपक्षिपंति Rām.<BR>--3 To throw<BR>out (a hint), hint, indicate, put<BR>forth, adduce; छन्नं कार्यमुपक्षिपंति<BR>Mk. 9. 3; इति उपक्षिप्तमनेन Mu. 1;<BR>Māl. 1.<BR>--4 To throw down.<BR>--5 To<BR>commence, introduce, set on foot, begin;<BR>उपक्षिप्तमनेन किमपि Mu. 1; K. 162;<BR>Dk. 59; उपक्षिप्तो भित्तिबंधः M. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षेपः|उपक्षेप
उपक्षेपः<BR>1 Throwing at, hurling.<BR>--2 Mention, allusion, hint,<BR>suggestion; कार्योपक्षेपमादौ तनुमपि रचयन्<BR>Mu. 4. 3; दारुणः खलूपक्षेपः पापस्य<BR>Ve. 5.<BR>--3 A threat, specific mention<BR>or charge; कर्णनासाच्छेदोपभीषिताभ्यां<BR>Dk. 61.<BR>--4 Commencement; उपाय˚<BR>M. 3.<BR>--5 Poetical or figurative<BR>style (Wilson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपक्षेपणं|उपक्षेपण
उपक्षेपणं<BR>1 Throwing or casting<BR>down.<BR>--2 Accusing, charging; ˚धर्मः<BR>= शूद्रस्वामिकामान्नस्य पाकार्थं ब्राह्मणगृहे<BR>समर्पणं Śabdak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगण|उपगणः
उपगण a. Forming a small or<BR>subordinate class.<BR>--णः<BR>1 A small<BR>or subordinate class.<BR>--2 A small<BR>number less than a troop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगंधः|उपगन्ध|उपगन्धः
उपगंधः Perfume, scent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगम्
उपगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go to, approach;<BR>attain, reach (fig. also.), arrive at,<BR>visit; शशिनमुपगतेयं कौमुदी मेघमुक्तं<BR>R. 6. 85; so दैवादुपगतं तृणं Pt. 4;<BR>पदमुपगता Bh. 2. 10; Bk. 1. 1; तदुपगतं<BR>Mu. 5 duly received.<BR>--2 To enter<BR>into, penetrate; Śi. 9. 39.<BR>--3<BR>To undergo, suffer; तपो घोरमुपागतं<BR>Rām.<BR>--4 To go to the state of,<BR>attain, acquire; तानप्रदायित्वमिवोपगंतुं<BR>Ku. 1. 8; प्रतिकूलतामुपगते हि विधौ<BR>Śi. 9. 6; so निद्रावशं, हर्षं, तृप्तिं, शांतिं,<BR>विषादं &c.<BR>--5 To approach a woman<BR>(for sexual intercourse); सुप्तां मत्तां<BR>प्रमत्तां वा रहो यत्रोपगच्छति Ms. 3. 34,<BR>4. 40.<BR>--6 To come upon, attack.<BR>--7 To occur, happen, present itself;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">Page0317-c+ 56</a>]<BR>कस्यात्यंतं सुखमुपगतं Me. 109 v. l.<BR>--8<BR>To undertake, begin.<BR>--9 To suffer,<BR>share in.<BR>--10 To admit, agree to,<BR>consent, allow; वेदांतोपगतं फलं<BR>Ms. 2. 160. --Caus. To cause to come<BR>near or approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग
उपग a. (At the end of comp.<BR>only)<BR>1 Approaching, following,<BR>joining.<BR>--2 Receiving; ओषध्यः<BR>फलपाकांता बहुपुष्पफलोपगाः Ms. 1. 46;<BR>Śi. 16. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगत|उपगतः
उपगत p. p.<BR>1 Gone to, approached,<BR>arrived.<BR>--2 Occurred, happened.<BR>--3<BR>Near, at hand.<BR>--4 Got, obtained.<BR>--5 Undergone, experienced.<BR>--6<BR>Furnished with.<BR>--7 Gone to,<BR>become.<BR>--8 Promised, agreed.<BR>--9<BR>Passed away, dead.<BR>--10 Feeling,<BR>suffering (actively used).<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Wealth acquired.<BR>--2 Receipt; धनी<BR>वोपगतं दद्यात् स्वहस्तपरिचिह्नितं<BR>Y. 2. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगतिः|उपगति
उपगतिः f.<BR>1 Approach, going near.<BR>--2 Knowledge, acquaintance.<BR>--3<BR>Acceptance, receipt.<BR>--4 Attainment,<BR>acquirement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगंतृ
उपगंतृ a.<BR>1 Approaching.<BR>--2<BR>Getting, acquiring.<BR>--3 Knowing.<BR>--4<BR>Accepting, receiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगमः|उपगम
उपगमः, --मनं<BR>1 Going to, drawing<BR>towards, approach; सीमंते च<BR>त्वदुपगमजं यत्र नीपं वधूनां Me. 65 your<BR>advent; व्यावर्ततान्योपगमात्कुमारी<BR>R. 6. 69, 9. 50.<BR>--2 Knowledge,<BR>acquaintance.<BR>--3 Attainment, acquiring;<BR>विश्वासोपगमादभिन्नगतयः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>--4<BR>Intercourse (as of the sexes).<BR>--5<BR>Society, company; न पुनरधमानामुपगमः<BR>H. 1. 136.<BR>--6 Undergoing, suffering,<BR>feeling.<BR>--7 Acceptance, receipt.<BR>--8<BR>An agreement, promise.<BR>--9 A<BR>particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगमनं|उपगमन
उपगमः, --मनं<BR>1 Going to, drawing<BR>towards, approach; सीमंते च<BR>त्वदुपगमजं यत्र नीपं वधूनां Me. 65 your<BR>advent; व्यावर्ततान्योपगमात्कुमारी<BR>R. 6. 69, 9. 50.<BR>--2 Knowledge,<BR>acquaintance.<BR>--3 Attainment, acquiring;<BR>विश्वासोपगमादभिन्नगतयः Ś. 1. 14.<BR>--4<BR>Intercourse (as of the sexes).<BR>--5<BR>Society, company; न पुनरधमानामुपगमः<BR>H. 1. 136.<BR>--6 Undergoing, suffering,<BR>feeling.<BR>--7 Acceptance, receipt.<BR>--8<BR>An agreement, promise.<BR>--9 A<BR>particular high number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगामिन्
उपगामिन् a. Coming near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगिरि|उपगिरिः
उपगिरि --रं ind. Near a<BR>mountain.<BR>--रिः N. of a country situated<BR>near a mountain in the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगिरं|उपगिर
उपगिरि --रं ind. Near a<BR>mountain.<BR>--रिः N. of a country situated<BR>near a mountain in the north.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगु|उपगुः
उपगु ind. Near a cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगुप्त
उपगुप्त a. Hidden, concealed;<BR>˚वित्त whose wealth is concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगुरुः|उपगुरु
उपगुरुः An assistant teacher.<BR>--रु ind. Near a teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगुह्
उपगुह् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To clasp, embrace;<BR>तरंगहस्तैरुपगूहतीव R. 13. 63, 18. 47;<BR>Bk. 14. 52; Śi. 9. 38.<BR>--2 To hide,<BR>conceal, cover, encircle, gird round;<BR>वनमालोपगूढः K. 24, 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0317-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगूढ
उपगूढ p. p.<BR>1 Hidden, concealed;<BR>R. 13. 30.<BR>--2 Embraced, clasped.<BR>--3 Held, supported;<BR>कश्चित्कराभ्यामुपगूढनालं R. 6. 13.<BR>--4 Suppressed.<BR>--ढं An embrace; उपगूढानि सवे --थूनि<BR>च Ku. 4. 17; Śi. 10. 88;<BR>कंठाश्लेषोपगूढं Bh. 3. 82; Me. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगूहनं|उपगूहन
उपगूहनं<BR>1 {1} Hiding, concealing.<BR>--2<BR>An embrace.<BR>--3 Astonishment,<BR>surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगोह्य|उपगोह्यः
उपगोह्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be<BR>embraced.<BR>--2 To be taken or seized.<BR>--ह्यः<BR>1 An embrace.<BR>--2 A kind of fire<BR>regarded as impure (and therefore<BR>to be hidden).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगै
उपगै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sing to any one<BR>(with dat. or acc.); साम्नैनमुपागात्<BR>Ch. Up.<BR>--2 To join in singing.<BR>--3<BR>To praise in song, celebrate, extol;<BR>तपोलक्ष्म्या दीप्तं दिनकृतमिवोच्चैरुपजगुः<BR>Ki. 18. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगा
उपगा m. (गाः) A priest in a<BR>sacrifice who sings the hymns. --f.<BR>Accompaniment of a song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगातृ
उपगातृ a. Singing near. --m. One<BR>who accompanies the song of the<BR>Udgātṛ priest, a chorister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीत
उपगीत p. p.<BR>1 Celebrated, sung<BR>by bards.<BR>--2 Commencing to sing;<BR>Śi. 4. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपगीतिः|उपगीति
उपगीतिः f. A variety of the Āryā<BR>metre; see App.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रंथः|उपग्रन्थ|उपग्रन्थः
उपग्रंथः A subsidiary writing or<BR>a class of such writings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रह्
उपग्रह् {c9c} U.<BR>1 To hold under,<BR>seize or collect from below; as रसं.<BR>--2 To seize, take, take possession<BR>of; तवैव पादावुपगृह्य Rām.;<BR>उपगृह्यास्पदं चैव Ms. 7. 184.<BR>--3 To meet<BR>with, obtain; स मृत्युमुपगृह्णाति<BR>गर्भमश्वतरी यथा Chāṇ. 19.<BR>--4 To subdue,<BR>vanquish.<BR>--5 To provide.<BR>--6 To<BR>conciliate, take as one's ally, favour,<BR>support; तदुपगृहीतेन म्लेच्छराजबलेन<BR>Mu. 1.<BR>--7 To conceive with one's<BR>mind, grasp mentally.<BR>--8 To decide,<BR>determine.<BR>--9 To accept, approve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रहः|उपग्रह
उपग्रहः<BR>1 Confinement, seizure.<BR>--2 Defeat, frustration; Mu. 4. 2.<BR>--3 A prisoner.<BR>--4 Joining, addition.<BR>--5 (a) Favour, encouragement,<BR>assistance, conciliation; सोपग्रहं<BR>K. 156. (b) Favourableness,<BR>kindness, complacence; सोपग्रह K. 264.<BR>--6 Use.<BR>--7 A kind of peace<BR>purchased by giving over every thing;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">Page0318-b+ 56</a>]<BR>cf H. 4. 121.<BR>--8 The voice or<BR>pada of a verb.<BR>--9 A pile or heap<BR>of kuśa grass.<BR>--10 The presiding<BR>spirit or cause which directs a<BR>planet's motion.<BR>--11 A minor planet<BR>(राहु, केतु &c.), a secondary<BR>heavenly body, such as a comet, meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्रहणं|उपग्रहण
उपग्रहणं<BR>1 Seizing (from below);<BR>taking hold of; as in<BR>पादोपग्रहणं.<BR>--2 Seizure, capture, taking one<BR>prisoner.<BR>--3 Supporting, furthering,<BR>promoting.<BR>--4 Holy study, study<BR>of the Vedas (after being<BR>initiated into them); वेदोपग्रहणार्थाय<BR>तावग्राहयत प्रभुः Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्राहः|उपग्राह
उपग्राहः<BR>1 Making a present.<BR>--2 A<BR>present; उच्चावचानुपग्राहान् राजभिः<BR>प्रापितान् बहून् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपग्राह्य|उपग्राह्यः
उपग्राह्य pot. p. To be favoured or<BR>retained in service; Mu. 5.<BR>--ह्यः<BR>1 An offering or present.<BR>--2<BR>Particularly, a present or offering to<BR>a great man or king; the modern<BR>Nazarānā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघात|उपघातः
उपघात See under उपहन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघुष्
उपघुष् {c1c} {c10c} P. To fill with<BR>noise, make resonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघुष्ट
उपघुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Resounding with,<BR>noisy.<BR>--2 Resonant.<BR>--3 Sounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघोषणं|उपघोषण
उपघोषणं Proclaiming,<BR>publication, making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघ्नः|उपघ्न
उपघ्नः [उप-हन्-क]<BR>1 Contiguous<BR>support; पर्वतोपघ्नः Sk.;<BR>छेदादिवोपघ्नतरोर्व्रतत्यौ R. 14. 1.<BR>--2 Shelter,<BR>support, stay, protection.<BR>--3 That<BR>which rests upon or is supported by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचक्रः|उपचक्र
उपचक्रः [उपगतः चक्रं चक्रवाकं] A<BR>variety of the ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचक्षुस्
उपचक्षुस् n. [उपगतं चक्षुरिवः] An<BR>eye-glass, spectacles; cf. उपनेत्रं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्
उपचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 (a) To serve,<BR>wait or attend upon; गिरिशमुपचचार<BR>Ku. 1. 60; निमित्तज्ञान् K. 64;<BR>Ms. 3. 193, 4. 254; सममुपचर भद्रे सुप्रियं<BR>चाप्रियं च Mk. 1. 31; K. 326. (b)<BR>To honour, worship; प्रतिमाः<BR>पूजासत्कारेणोपचर्यंते K. 40, 323; V. 3.<BR>--2<BR>To treat, deal with, act towards;<BR>entertain; मित्रत्वेन उपचरितस्य<BR>Dk. 71 treated as a friend; भोजनादिना<BR>मामुपाचरत् 77, 117; तां<BR>प्रियसखीमिवोपाचरत् 134; उपाचरत् कृत्रिमसंविधाभिः<BR>R. 14. 17 honoured or entertained;<BR>5. 62; स्थाने इयं देवीशब्देनोपचर्यते V. 3<BR>honoured with the title of queen.<BR>--3 To attend on (as a patient),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-c" target="_blank">Page0318-c+ 56</a>]<BR>treat, tend, nurse; यत्नादुपचर्यतां<BR>Ś. 3; मंत्रवादिभिरुपचर्यमाणः Pt. 1.<BR>--4<BR>To approach, go towards.<BR>--5 To<BR>undertake, begin (mostly Vedic<BR>in these senses). --pass. To be<BR>used figuratively or metaphorically,<BR>be applied figuratively to any<BR>one (with loc.); तस्माच्चेतनवदुपचर्यते<BR>Ś. B.; पर एवात्मा बालैः शारीर<BR>इत्युपचर्यते ibid.; कालोयं द्विपरार्धाख्यो निमेष<BR>उपचर्यते Bhāg.; भुक्ता ब्राह्मणा इत्यत्र<BR>अन्नस्य भुक्तत्वं ब्राह्मणेषूपचर्यते Malli. on<BR>Ki. 1. 1; Bṛ. S. 5. 15; प्रत्यासत्त्या<BR>उपचर्य योज्यते K. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचरः|उपचर
उपचरः<BR>1 Cure, treatment;<BR>त्वग्भेदी व्रणः सूपचरः easily curable.<BR>--2<BR>--उपचरणं Approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्य|उपचर्य्य
उपचर्य pot. p. To be served or<BR>waited upon; to be honoured or<BR>worshipped; Ms. 5. 154; अनुपचर्ये<BR>(भृत्ये) Pt. 1. 101 not requiring<BR>flattery, unassuming; दुःख˚<BR>Mu. 3. 5 difficult to serve.<BR>--र्या<BR>1 Service,<BR>attendance.<BR>--2 Physicking, treating,<BR>curing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारः|उपचार
उपचारः<BR>1 Service, attendance;<BR>honouring, worshipping,<BR>entertaining; Mk. 4; अस्खलितोपचारां<BR>R. 5. 20; K. 344.<BR>--2 Civility, politeness,<BR>courtesy, polite behaviour,<BR>(external display of courtesy); ˚परिभ्रष्टः<BR>H. 1. 133 devoid of civility,<BR>uncourteous; ˚विधिर्मनस्विनीनां M. 3. 3;<BR>उपचारैरुपाचरत् Ks. 16. 29;<BR>मिथ्योपचारैश्च वशीकृतानां H. 1. 78; नोपचारेण<BR>ब्रूयाः Rām.; ˚पदं न चेदिदं Ku. 4. 9<BR>a merely complimentary saying, a<BR>flattering compliment; ˚मात्रमधुरं<BR>K. 222, 207; M. 4; ˚क्रिया<BR>Ms. 8. 357 showing marks of favour,<BR>courting, (sending perfumes &c.).<BR>--3 Salutation, usual or customary<BR>obeisance, homage; नोपचारमर्हंति<BR>Ś. 3. 18; ˚यंत्रणया M. 4; ˚अतिक्रमं 4,<BR>5; ˚अंजलिः R. 3. 11 folding the<BR>hands in salutation.<BR>--4 A form or<BR>mode of address or salutation;<BR>रामभद्र इत्येव मां प्रत्युपचारः शोभते<BR>तातपरिजनस्य U. 1; यथा गुरुस्तथोपचारेण 6;<BR>V. 5; Śi. 9. 78.<BR>--5 External show<BR>or form, ceremony; प्रावृषेण्यैरेव<BR>लिंगैर्मम राजोपचारः V. 4 royal service,<BR>pomp or state of royalty;<BR>भूषणाद्युपचारेण Mu. 3. 23 v. l.<BR>--6 A<BR>remedy, physicking, application of<BR>cure or remedy; शिशिर˚ Dk. 15;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-a" target="_blank">Page0319-a+ 55</a>]<BR>शीत˚ Pt. 1; Dk. 23; K. 102.<BR>--7<BR>Practice, performance, art, conduct,<BR>management, procedure; व्रतचर्या˚<BR>Ms. 1. 111; प्रसाधन˚ 10. 32,<BR>9. 259; कामोपचारेषु Dk. 81 in the<BR>conduct of love-affairs; समंत्रं सोपचारं<BR>(अस्त्रं) Mb.; अवेशसदृशप्रणयोपचारां<BR>Mk. 8. 23 course of love &c.;<BR>वाक्योपचारे कुशला Rām. skilled in<BR>the employment of words; use,<BR>usage; यत्र लौकिकानामुपचारः v. l. for<BR>व्याहारः in U. 6.<BR>--8 Means of doing<BR>homage or showing respect;<BR>प्रकीर्णाभिनवोपचारं (राजमार्गं) R. 7. 4<BR>(hanging garlands &c.); 5. 41.<BR>--9<BR>Hence, any necessary or requisite<BR>article (of worship, ceremony,<BR>decoration, furniture &c.);<BR>presenting flowers, perfumes &c.;<BR>सन्मंगलोपचाराणां R. 10. 77; कॢप्तोपचारां<BR>चतुरस्रवेदीं Ku. 7. 88; कुसुमैः<BR>कृतोपचारः V. 2; so ˚रमणीयतया Ś. 6;<BR>˚वत्सु मंचेषु R. 6. 1 the necessary<BR>decorations (canopy &c.); (the<BR>Upachāras or articles of worship are<BR>variously numbered, being 5, 10,<BR>16, 18 or 64).<BR>--10 Behaviour,<BR>conduct, demeanour; वैश्यशूद्रोपचारं च<BR>Ms. 1. 116; (religious) conduct<BR>in life; साधूनामुपचारज्ञः Rām.;<BR>परिजन˚ Mk. 1.<BR>--11 Use, employment;<BR>K. 183.<BR>--12 Any religious<BR>performance, a ceremony;<BR>प्रयुक्तपाणिग्रहणोपचारौ Ku. 7. 86; Mv. 1. 24.<BR>--13<BR>(a) Figurative or metaphorical<BR>use, secondary application (opp. मुख्य<BR>or primary sense); अचेतनेपि<BR>चेतनवदुपचारदर्शनात् S. B; कूलं<BR>पिपतिषतीत्यचेतनेपि कूले चेतनवदुपचारो दृश्यते<BR>Mbh. on P. IV. 3. 86<BR>personification; so छत्रिणो गच्छंतीत्येकेनापि<BR>छत्रिणा बहूनां छत्रिंत्वोपचारदर्शनात् Ś. B.;<BR>करणे कर्तृत्वोपचारात् ibid.; न चास्य<BR>करधृतत्वं तत्त्वतोस्तीति मुख्येपि उपचार एव<BR>शरणं स्यात् K. P. 10. (b) Supposed<BR>or fancied identification founded<BR>on resemblance; उभयरूपा चेयं शुद्धा<BR>उपचारेणामिश्रितत्वात् K. P. 2. (S. D.<BR>explains उपचार by उत्यंतं विशकलितयोः<BR>सादृश्यातिशयमहिम्ना भेदप्रतीतिस्थगनमात्रं).<BR>--14 A bribe.<BR>--15 A pretext;<BR>Śi. 10. 2.<BR>--16 A request, solicitation.<BR>--17 Occurrence of स् and ष् in the<BR>place of Visarga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0318-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचारिन्
उपचारिन् a. Attending, serving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचार्य|उपचार्यः|उपचार्य्य|उपचार्य्यः
उपचार्य pot. p. To be served or<BR>waited upon; to be worshipped &c.<BR>--र्यः Practice of medicine.<BR>--र्यं<BR>Treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्म|उपचर्मं|उपचर्म्म
उपचर्म --र्मं ind. On the skin,<BR>near the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचर्मं|उपचर्म|उपचर्म्म
उपचर्म --र्मं ind. On the skin,<BR>near the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचि
उपचि {c5c} U.<BR>1 To gather together,<BR>heap up, accumulate, collect;<BR>शश्वत्सिद्धैरुपचितबलिं Me. 55.<BR>--2 To<BR>add, increase, strengthen;<BR>उपचिन्वन् प्रभां तन्वीं प्रत्याह परमेश्वरः<BR>Ku. 6. 25; चेतःपीडामुपचिनोति Mu. 2;<BR>अधोधः पश्यतः कस्य महिमा नोपचीयते<BR>H. 2. 2; Bk. 6. 33; Śi. 4. 10;<BR>8. 6; उपचीयमानगर्भा K. 66 being<BR>developed; बलेनैव सहोपचीयते मदः<BR>K. 290; क्षीणोप्युपचीयते पुनश्चंद्रः<BR>Bh. 2. 87 waxes.<BR>--3 To cover<BR>over with; Śi. 9. 35; Ms. 6. 41.<BR>--pass.<BR>1 To be collected or<BR>accumulated; to increase, become strong,<BR>to be covered with &c.; see above.<BR>--2 To be prosperous, succeed, thrive,<BR>be better off; चत्वारस्तूपचीयंते विप्र<BR>आढ्यो वणिङ् नृपः Ms. 8. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचयः|उपचय
उपचयः<BR>1 Accumulation,<BR>addition, accession.<BR>--2 Increase, growth,<BR>excess; बल˚ K. 105; स्वशक्त्युपचये<BR>Śi. 2. 57; अंभसामुपचयाय 9. 32; भाग्य˚<BR>Ratn. 1. 6 dawn of good fortune;<BR>so ज्ञान˚, मांस˚.<BR>--3 Quantity, heap.<BR>--4 Prosperity, elevation, rise.<BR>--5<BR>The third, sixth, tenth and eleventh<BR>house or position from the first<BR>of a zodiacal sign (or a lagna q. v.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपचय (du.) rise and<BR>fall, prosperity and decay.<BR>--भवनं<BR>a species of the Daṇḍaka metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचायिन्
उपचायिन् a.<BR>1 Increasing,<BR>growing.<BR>--2 Thriving, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचाय्यः|उपचाय्य
उपचाय्यः [उपचीयतेऽग्निरत्र आधारे ण्यत्<BR>P. III. 1. 131]<BR>1 A kind of sacred<BR>fire.<BR>--2 A place for holding<BR>sacrificial fire, altar, hearth<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचित|उपचितः
उपचित p. p.<BR>1 Collected,<BR>gathered together, accumulated;<BR>अस्रैरुपचितैः Me. 105.<BR>--2 Increased, grown;<BR>U. 6. 28; R. 9. 27; ˚अवयवा मंजरी<BR>9. 44 full-grown.<BR>--3 Grown in power,<BR>strengthened; Śi. 6. 63; R. 17. 54;<BR>˚महामोहगहनः Māl. 1. 30; ˚वपुः<BR>Me. 32; लोकप्रसिद्धिः उपचिता Mu. 2 the<BR>popular idea was strengthened.<BR>--4<BR>Full of, abounding in, covered over<BR>with; R. 9. 53; वियदुपचितमेघं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">Page0319-c+ 54</a>]<BR>Bh. 1. 35.<BR>--5 Abundantly furnished with,<BR>plastered, smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचितिः|उपचिति
उपचितिः f. Accumulation,<BR>collection, growth, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचित्रा
उपचित्रा<BR>1 N. of a tree (चित्रा).<BR>--2 N. of a lunar mansion स्वाति; also<BR>हस्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपचूलनं|उपचूलन
उपचूलनं Heating, burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छदः
उपच्छदः A coverlet, cover in<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छंद्
उपच्छंद् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To wheedle,<BR>flatter, coax, entice, invite;<BR>जलेनोपच्छंदितः Ś. 5 coaxed to drink<BR>water; परदारानुपच्छंदयति Sk.<BR>--2 To<BR>conciliate.<BR>--3 To beseech, request;<BR>R. 5. 58.<BR>--4 To persuade one to do<BR>a thing.<BR>--5 To give one something.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्छंदनं|उपच्छन्दन|उपच्छंदन
उपच्छंदनं<BR>1 Coaxing, persuading;<BR>उपच्छंदनैरेव स्वं ते दापयितुं प्रयतिष्यते<BR>Dk. 65.<BR>--2 Inviting; उपमंत्रणमुपच्छंदनं Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपच्यवः|उपच्यव
उपच्यवः Passing into the<BR>chamber (from the house);<BR>Rv. 1. 28. 3; passing close to (in sexual<BR>intercourse ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजगती
उपजगती A variety of the<BR>Triṣṭubh metre in which three Pādas<BR>contain twelve instead of eleven<BR>syllables.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजन्
उपजन् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To be born or<BR>produced, originate, arise, grow;<BR>उष्मणश्चोपजायंते Ms. 1. 45; H. Pr. 44;<BR>संगस्तेषुपजायते Bg. 2. 62; 14. 11.<BR>--2 To happen, take place, become<BR>visible, appear; प्राणविपत्तिरुपजायते<BR>K. 160.<BR>--3 To be or become, be or<BR>exist; सतीत्वमुपजायते Pt. 1. 138.<BR>--4 To be born again; सर्गेपि नोपजायंते<BR>Bg. 14. 2; Y. 3. 256. --Caus. (<BR>जनयति) To produce, cause, rouse;<BR>उत्तराप्रलापोपजनितकृपः K. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज
उपज a. Increased, being<BR>produced in addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजनः|उपजन
उपजनः<BR>1 Addition, increase.<BR>--2<BR>Appendage.<BR>--3 Rise, origin.<BR>--4<BR>Addition of a letter in the formation<BR>of words; वर्ण˚ Nir.<BR>--5 Any<BR>letter, syllable or affix so added;<BR>अनर्थका उपजनाः Nir.<BR>--नं The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजा
उपजा Ved. Remote posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजात
उपजात p. p.<BR>1 Produced, caused;<BR>˚कोप, ˚क्रोध excited, moved to anger;<BR>˚विश्वास confiding, believing,<BR>trusting.<BR>--2 Happened, taken place;<BR>U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0319-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजातिः|उपजाति
उपजातिः f. A mixed metre (see<BR>App.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजप्
उपजप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To whisper into<BR>the ears of (another), win over<BR>to one's party by secretly<BR>suggesting anything in the ear; अंगारवर्षं<BR>राजवधायोपजप्य Dk. 104; क्षत्तारं<BR>कुरुराजस्तु शनैः कर्णमुपाजपत् Mb.<BR>--2<BR>(Hence) to instigate to rebellion<BR>or treachery, conspire with;<BR>उपजप्यानुपजपेत् Ms. 7. 197.<BR>--3 To commit<BR>mischief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजप्य
उपजप्य a. To be brought over<BR>or instigated to rebellion by<BR>whispering in the ear; उपजप्यानुपजपेत्<BR>Ms. 7. 197.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजापः|उपजाप
उपजापः<BR>1 Secretly whispering<BR>into the ear or communicating;<BR>परकृत्य˚ Mu. 2.<BR>--2 Secret<BR>overtures or negotiations (with the<BR>enemy's friends), sowing the seeds<BR>of dissension, treachery, treason;<BR>instigating to rebellion; उपजापः<BR>कृतस्तेन तानाकोपवतस्त्वयि Śi. 2. 99;<BR>उपजापसहान् विलंघयन् स विधाता<BR>नृपतीन्मदोद्धतः Ki. 2. 47, 16. 42; अपि<BR>सहंते अस्मदुपजापं प्रजाः Mu. 2.<BR>--3<BR>Disunion, separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजापक
उपजापक a.<BR>1 Whispering into<BR>the ears of, instigating to rebellion;<BR>Ms. 9. 275.<BR>--2 Treacherous, traitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजरस्
उपजरस् ind. Towards old age<BR>or in old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजल्प्
उपजल्प् {c1c} P. To talk to,<BR>converse with, chatter. -- To<BR>advise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजल्पनं|उपजल्पन
उपजल्पनं, उपजल्पितं A talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजल्पितं|उपजल्पित
उपजल्पनं, उपजल्पितं A talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजल्पिन्
उपजल्पिन् a. Giving advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजिह्वा
उपजिह्वा, --ह्विका<BR>1 The uvula or<BR>soft palate.<BR>--2 Enlargement of the<BR>under side of the tongue.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजिह्विका
उपजिह्वा, --ह्विका<BR>1 The uvula or<BR>soft palate.<BR>--2 Enlargement of the<BR>under side of the tongue.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीक|उपजीकः
उपजीक a. Living upon,<BR>subsisting by.<BR>--कः Ved. A water-deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव्
उपजीव् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To live upon,<BR>subsist by, derive livelihood from,<BR>be supported by;<BR>उपजीव्यमानपादच्छायः K. 5; कां वृत्तिमार्य उपजीवति<BR>Mk. 2; संवाहकस्य वृत्तिं ibid.;<BR>शेषास्तमुपजीवेयुर्यथैव पितरं तथा Ms. 9. 105;<BR>Y. 2. 301.<BR>--2 To live under, be<BR>dependent on, serve; Śi. 9. 32.<BR>--3<BR>To make use of, derive materials<BR>(for writing from); तदेतद्भारतं नाम<BR>कविभिस्तूपजीव्यते Mb.<BR>--4 To practise;<BR>Ms. 10. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव
उपजीव a. Ved. Living on &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवक
उपजीवक, --विन् a.<BR>1 Living upon,<BR>subsisting by (instr. or in comp.);<BR>जातिमात्रोपजीविनां Ms. 12. 114,<BR>8. 20; नानापण्योपजीविनां 9. 257;<BR>द्यूतोपजीव्यस्मि Mk. 2.<BR>--2 Living under,<BR>depending upon, subject to, a<BR>dependant, servant (--m.);<BR>भीमकांतैर्नृपगुणैः स बभूवोपजीविनाम् R. 1. 16;<BR>अस्मद्˚ K. 61.<BR>--कं Means of<BR>subsistence, profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीविन्
उपजीवक, --विन् a.<BR>1 Living upon,<BR>subsisting by (instr. or in comp.);<BR>जातिमात्रोपजीविनां Ms. 12. 114,<BR>8. 20; नानापण्योपजीविनां 9. 257;<BR>द्यूतोपजीव्यस्मि Mk. 2.<BR>--2 Living under,<BR>depending upon, subject to, a<BR>dependant, servant (--m.);<BR>भीमकांतैर्नृपगुणैः स बभूवोपजीविनाम् R. 1. 16;<BR>अस्मद्˚ K. 61.<BR>--कं Means of<BR>subsistence, profession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीवनं|उपजीवन
उपजीवनं, --जीविका<BR>1 Living.<BR>--2<BR>Subsistence, livelihood;<BR>निंदितार्थोपजीवनं Y. 3. 236; क्षत्रियस्यैतदेवाहुर्धर्मं<BR>कृष्णोपजीवनं Mb.<BR>--3 A means of<BR>living, such as property;<BR>किंचिद्दत्वोपजीवनं Ms. 9. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीविका
उपजीवनं, --जीविका<BR>1 Living.<BR>--2<BR>Subsistence, livelihood;<BR>निंदितार्थोपजीवनं Y. 3. 236; क्षत्रियस्यैतदेवाहुर्धर्मं<BR>कृष्णोपजीवनं Mb.<BR>--3 A means of<BR>living, such as property;<BR>किंचिद्दत्वोपजीवनं Ms. 9. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजीव्य|उपजीव्यः
उपजीव्य pot. p.<BR>1 Affording a<BR>livelihood; Y. 2. 227.<BR>--2 Giving<BR>patronage, patronizing (as a king<BR>&c.).<BR>--3 (fig.) Supplying<BR>materials for writing, that from which<BR>one derives his materials; सर्वेषां<BR>कविमुख्यानामुपजीव्यो भविष्यति Mb.<BR>--व्यः<BR>1 A patron.<BR>--2 A source or<BR>authority (from which one derives<BR>his materials); इत्यलमुपजीव्यानां<BR>मान्यानां व्याख्यानेषु कटाक्षनिक्षेपेण S. D. 2.<BR>--व्यं A means of subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजुष्ट
उपजुष्ट a.<BR>1 Approached,<BR>received with courtesy; Mv. 3. 26.<BR>--2 Frequented, resorted to; Mv. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजोषः|उपजोष
उपजोषः, --षणं<BR>1 Affection.<BR>--2<BR>Enjoyment.<BR>--3 Frequenting, resorting<BR>to.<BR>--षं ind.<BR>1 According to one's<BR>desire or pleasure.<BR>--2 Silently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपजोषणं|उपजोषण
उपजोषः, --षणं<BR>1 Affection.<BR>--2<BR>Enjoyment.<BR>--3 Frequenting, resorting<BR>to.<BR>--षं ind.<BR>1 According to one's<BR>desire or pleasure.<BR>--2 Silently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्ञा
उपज्ञा {c9c} A.<BR>1 To ascertain;<BR>to know.<BR>--2 To invent, find out, hit<BR>upon: (उपज्ञातं = विनोपदेशेन ज्ञातं); see<BR>उपज्ञा below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्ञा
उपज्ञा [उपज्ञायते इत्युपज्ञा कर्मण्यङ्]<BR>1<BR>Knowledge acquired by oneself and<BR>not handed down by tradition,<BR>invention, primitive or untaught<BR>knowledge; usually in comp. which<BR>is treated as a neuter noun (<BR>P. II. 4. 21); पाणिनेरुपज्ञा पाणिन्युपज्ञं ग्रंथः<BR>Sk.; प्राचेतसोपज्ञं रामायणं R. 15. 63.<BR>--2<BR>Undertaking or commencing a<BR>thing not done before; लोकेऽ<BR>भूद्यदुपज्ञमेव विदुषां सौजन्यजन्यं यशः Malli.<BR>on Raghuvaṃśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्ञात
उपज्ञात a. Invented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्मन्
उपज्मन् a. Ved. Striding or<BR>stepping upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपज्वलित
उपज्वलित a. Lighted, inflamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपढौक्
उपढौक् Caus.<BR>1 To present (as<BR>an offering), make a respectful<BR>offering; एकैकं पशुमुपढौकयामः H. 2.<BR>--2 To carry out, accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपढौकनं|उपढौकन
उपढौकनं A respectful offering or<BR>present, Nazarānā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतटः|उपतट
उपतटः The skirt or border;<BR>Me. 57.<BR>--टं ind. Near the skirt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्
उपतप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To make warm,<BR>heat; उपतप्तोदका नद्यः Rām.;<BR>Śi. 9. 65 (where it means to pain also).<BR>--2 To feel pain, become sick;<BR>आहिताग्निश्चेदुपतपेत् Āśval.<BR>--3 To afflict,<BR>befall (as a sickness); sometimes<BR>used impersonally. --pass.<BR>1 To be<BR>pained, become ill, be afflicted<BR>with; इत्यपूर्वमुपतप्यतेऽस्माभिः Mv. 2;<BR>so दुःखेनोपतप्यते &c.<BR>--2 To be<BR>emaciated with penance, practise<BR>penance; उपतप्यामहे तपः Av. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To kindle, ignite, burn.<BR>--2 To<BR>torment, hurt, pain.<BR>--3 To offend,<BR>oppress.<BR>--4 To mortify the body by<BR>penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतपत्|उपतपन्त्
उपतपत् m. Interior heat, disease<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतपन
उपतपन a. Paining, afflicting;<BR>Ki. 12. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्त
उपतप्त p. p.<BR>1 Heated, parched;<BR>consumed.<BR>--2 Distressed, pained,<BR>tormented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतप्तृ
उपतप्तृ a. Burning, heating. --m.<BR>1 Morbid or extraordinary heat.<BR>--2 Any cause of heat, burning or<BR>inflammation.<BR>--3 A kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापः|उपताप
उपतापः<BR>1 Heat, warmth.<BR>--2<BR>Trouble, distress, pain, sorrow; सर्वथा<BR>न कंचन न स्पृशंत्युपतापाः K. 135, 177;<BR>शरीरोपतापेन Māl. 3.<BR>--3 Calamity,<BR>misfortune.<BR>--4 Sickness, disease,<BR>injury.<BR>--5 Haste, hurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापक
उपतापक a. Heating, igniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापनं|उपतापन
उपतापनं<BR>1 Heating.<BR>--2<BR>Distressing, tormenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतापिन्
उपतापिन् a.<BR>1 Heating,<BR>inflaming; causing pain.<BR>--2 Suffering<BR>heat or pain, being sick; गुर्वर्थं<BR>पितृमात्रर्थं स्वाध्यायार्थ्युपतापिनः Ms. 11. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतारक
उपतारक a. Overflowing (as<BR>water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतिष्यं|उपतिष्य
उपतिष्यं<BR>1 N. of the lunar<BR>mansion or asterism called अश्लेषा.<BR>--2 N. of another asterism called<BR>पुनर्वसु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0320-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपतृण्यः|उपतृण्य
उपतृण्यः Ved. A serpent<BR>(lurking in the grass).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपत्य
उपत्य a. Situated under or below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपत्यका
उपत्यका [उप-त्यकन् P. V. 2. 34;<BR>पर्वतस्यासन्नं स्थलं उपत्यका Sk.] A land<BR>at the foot of a mountain, low land;<BR>मलयाद्रेरुपत्यकाः R. 4. 46; एते खलु<BR>हिमवतो गिरेरुपत्यकारण्यवासिनंः संप्राप्ताः Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंश्
उपदंश् {c1c} P. To bite or eat<BR>anything (as a relish or condiment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंशः|उपदंश
उपदंशः<BR>1 Anything which<BR>excites thirst or appetite, a relish,<BR>condiment &c.; द्वित्रानुपदंशानुपपाद्य<BR>Dk. 133; अग्रमांसोपदंशं पिब<BR>नवशोणितासवं Ve. 3<BR>--2 Biting, stinging.<BR>--3<BR>The venereal disease, chancre.<BR>--4<BR>(a) A tree the root of which is<BR>used for horse-radish (शिग्रु). (b) N.<BR>of another plant (समष्ठिल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदंशिन्
उपदंशिन् a. Afflicted with<BR>chancre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदश
उपदश a. (pl.) About or nearly<BR>ten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदस्
उपदस् {c4c} P. To fail, be wanting,<BR>dry up or be consumed. --Caus.<BR>To cause to fail or cease,<BR>extinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदासुक
उपदासुक a. Ved. Wanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदा
उपदा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To give in<BR>addition.<BR>--2 To offer, give, grant (in<BR>general).<BR>--3 To add.<BR>--4 ({c1c} A.) (Ved.)<BR>(a) To take upon oneself. (b)<BR>To erect, raise, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदा
उपदा a. Ved. Giving a present.<BR>--दा (cf. P. III. 3. 106)<BR>1 A<BR>present, an offering to a king or<BR>a great man, a Nazarānā; उपदा<BR>विविशुः शश्वन्नोत्सेकाः कोसलेश्वरं<BR>R. 4. 70, 5. 41, 7. 30; P. V. 1. 47.<BR>--2<BR>A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदीकृ
उपदीकृ {c8c} U. To offer as a<BR>present; तस्य रत्नमुपदीकृतं नृपाः Śi. 14. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदानं|उपदान
उपदानं, --नकं<BR>1 An oblation, a<BR>present (in general).<BR>--2 A gift made<BR>for procuring favour or protection,<BR>such as a bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदानकं|उपदानक
उपदानं, --नकं<BR>1 An oblation, a<BR>present (in general).<BR>--2 A gift made<BR>for procuring favour or protection,<BR>such as a bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदानवी
उपदानवी N. of the daughter<BR>of the demon Vṛṣaparvan and<BR>mother of Duṣyanta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिग्ध
उपदिग्ध a.<BR>1 Smeared, covered,<BR>anointed.<BR>--2 Spotted over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेहः|उपदेह
उपदेहः<BR>1 An ointment, liniment.<BR>--2 A cover.<BR>--3 A minor or<BR>secondary body (such as that which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-b" target="_blank">Page0321-b+ 56</a>]<BR>grows on diseased parts of the<BR>body).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्
उपदिश् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To instruct,<BR>teach, explain, advise;<BR>यद्यत्प्रयोगविषये भाविकमुपदिश्यते मया तस्य…<BR>तत्तत्प्रत्युपदिशतीव मे बाला M. 1. 5;<BR>सुखमुपदिश्यते परस्य K. 156 it is easy<BR>to advise others; ज्ञानमुपदिश्<BR>Bg. 4. 34; R. 16. 43.<BR>--2 To point,<BR>indicate, refer to; गुणशेषामुपदिश्य<BR>भामिनीं R. 8. 73; सुवर्णपुरमार्गमुपदेक्ष्यति<BR>K. 120, 92 point out or tell.<BR>--3 To<BR>assign the right place to a thing,<BR>arrange.<BR>--4 (a) To mention, specify,<BR>tell; किं कुलेनोपदिष्टेन शीलमेवात्र कारणं<BR>Mk. 9. 7; पृषोदरादीनि यथोपदिष्टं<BR>P. VI. 3. 109. (b) To inform, announce.<BR>--5 To<BR>prescribe, settle, sanction, lay<BR>down; न द्वितीयश्च साध्वीनां<BR>क्वचिद्भर्तोपदिश्यते Ms. 5. 162, 2. 190, 3. 14,<BR>43; पृषोदरादीनि यथोपदिष्टं<BR>P. VI. 3. 109.<BR>--6 To rule over, govern,<BR>command.<BR>--7 To name, call;<BR>द्रुतविलंबितमित्युपदिश्यते Śrut. 28;<BR>Ms. 12. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्
उपदिश् f., उपदिशा An<BR>intermediate quarter, such as ऐशानी, आग्नेयी,<BR>नैरृती and वायवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिश्य
उपदिश्य a. Being in an<BR>intermediate quarter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदिष्ट|उपदिष्टः
उपदिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Specified, pointed<BR>out, particularized; पृथूपदिष्टां<BR>दुदुहुर्धरित्रीं Ku. 1. 2.<BR>--2 Taught<BR>instructed, advised.<BR>--3 Put forward as<BR>a plea or reason.<BR>--4 Initiated.<BR>--ष्टं Advice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशः|उपदेश
उपदेशः<BR>1 Instruction, teaching,<BR>advice, prescription; सुशिक्षितोपि सर्व<BR>उपदेशेन निपुणो भवति M. 1 (see the<BR>act inter alia); स्थिरोपदेशामुपदेशकाले<BR>प्रपेदिरे प्राक्तनजन्मविद्याः Ku. 1. 30;<BR>अचिरप्रवृत्तोपदेशं नाट्यं M. 1, 2. 10;<BR>Ś. 2. 3; Ms. 8. 272; Amaru. 26;<BR>R. 12. 57; K. 26; M. 6; परोपदेशे पांडित्यं<BR>H. 1. 103.<BR>--2 Pointing out or referring<BR>to: शब्दानामितरेतरोपदेशः Nir.<BR>--3<BR>Specification, mentioning, naming.<BR>--4 A<BR>plea, pretext.<BR>--5 Initiation,<BR>communication of an initiatory Mantra<BR>or formula; चंद्रसूर्यग्रहे तीर्थे सिद्धक्षेत्रे<BR>शिवालये । मंत्रमात्रप्रकथनमुपदेशः स उच्यते ॥.<BR>--6 (In gram.) A form in<BR>a rule, an indicatory form; any<BR>word or part of a word, such as an<BR>affix, augment &c. with its<BR>anubandhas which show what<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">Page0321-c+ 55</a>]<BR>particular grammatical rules are to be<BR>applied.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थवाक्यं, --वचनं<BR>a parable, moral fable.<BR>--सहस्री<BR>N. of a philosophical work by<BR>Śaṅkarācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशक|उपदेशकः
उपदेशक a. Giving instruction,<BR>teaching.<BR>--कः An instructor, a<BR>guide, preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशता
उपदेशता<BR>1 The state of being a<BR>precept or rule.<BR>--2 Instruction,<BR>teaching.<BR>--3 Doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशनं|उपदेशन
उपदेशनं Advising, instructing.<BR>--ना Information, doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेशिन्
उपदेशिन् a. Advising, instructing.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A teacher, adviser.<BR>--2 A<BR>word or affix &c. in the form in<BR>which it appears in grammatical<BR>rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेष्टृ
उपदेष्टृ a. Giving instruction or<BR>advice. --m. (ष्टा) A teacher,<BR>preceptor; especially a spiritual<BR>preceptor; चत्वारो वयमृत्विजः स<BR>भगवान्कर्मोपदेष्टा हरिः Ve. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदी
उपदी N. of a plant (वंदाक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदीका
उपदीका A kind of ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदीक्षिन्
उपदीक्षिन् a.<BR>1 Partaking in an<BR>initiatory or other religious rite.<BR>--2<BR>A near relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृश्
उपदृश् {c1c} P. To see, behold,<BR>look at, perceive. --pass. To be or<BR>become visible. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause<BR>to see, show or exhibit.<BR>--2 To<BR>place before, show up, communicate,<BR>make (one) acquainted (with); राज्ञः<BR>पुरो मामुपदर्श्य H. 3; नयविद्भिर्नवे राज्ञि<BR>सदसच्चोपदर्शितं R. 4. 10.<BR>--3 To<BR>present a false appearance, deceive a<BR>person by a false appearance, illude.<BR>--4 To explain, illustrate; Y. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शक|उपदर्शकः
उपदर्शक a. Showing.<BR>--कः<BR>1 One<BR>who shows the way, a guide.<BR>--2<BR>A doorkeeper.<BR>--3 A witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदर्शनं|उपदर्शन
उपदर्शनं A commentary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृश्
उपदृश् a. Seeing, witnessing (as<BR>the sun and the moon). --f. Aspect,<BR>view (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदृष्टिः|उपदृष्टि
उपदृष्टिः f. Show, view, appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रष्टृ
उपद्रष्टृ a. Seeing, overlooking.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A supervisor, inspector.<BR>--2<BR>A witness; Bg. 13. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेवः|उपदेव
उपदेवः, --देवता A minor or<BR>inferior god (as the Yakṣas,<BR>Gandharvas and Apsarasas.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदेवता
उपदेवः, --देवता A minor or<BR>inferior god (as the Yakṣas,<BR>Gandharvas and Apsarasas.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपदोहः|उपदोह
उपदोहः<BR>1 A nipple of the udder<BR>of a cow.<BR>--2 A milking vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0321-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रु
उपद्रु {c1c} P.<BR>1 To run near to,<BR>run towards; Śi. 12. 42.<BR>--2 To<BR>attack, assault, rush at;<BR>तमुपाद्रवदुद्यम्य दक्षिणं दोर्निशाचरः R. 15. 23;<BR>प्राग्ज्योतिषमुपाद्रवत् Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रवः|उपद्रव
उपद्रवः<BR>1 An unhappy accident,<BR>misfortune, calamity.<BR>--2 Injury,<BR>trouble, harm;<BR>पुंसामसमर्थानामुपद्रवायात्मनो भवेत्कोपः Pt. 1. 324; निरुपद्रवं<BR>स्थानं Pt. 1.<BR>--3 Outrage, violence.<BR>--4 A national distress (whether<BR>caused by the king or famine,<BR>seasons &c.).<BR>--5 A national<BR>disturbance, rebellion.<BR>--6 A symptom, a<BR>supervenient disease (one brought<BR>on whilst a person is suffering from<BR>another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रविन्
उपद्रविन् a. Attacking,<BR>oppressive, tyrannical, factious. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>tyrant, an oppressor.<BR>--2 A rebel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्रुत
उपद्रुत p. p.<BR>1 Visited by<BR>calamities, oppressed, attacked,<BR>infested; वेदनाभिरुपद्रुतं H. 4. 88.<BR>--2 (In<BR>astr.) Eclipsed.<BR>--3 Boding evil,<BR>inauspicious.<BR>--तं A term used by the<BR>Bāṣkalas for a kind of Saṃdhi,<BR>also called उद्ग्राहवत् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपद्वीपः|उपद्वीप
उपद्वीपः An island.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधर्मः|उपधर्म|उपधर्म्म|उपधर्म्मः
उपधर्मः<BR>1 A bylaw, a secondary or<BR>minor religious precept (opp. पर);<BR>Ms. 2. 237, 4. 147.<BR>--2 A heretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधा
उपधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To place or lay<BR>upon, place under or in; अधिजानु<BR>बाहुमपधाय Śi. 9. 54; उपहितं<BR>शिशिरापगमश्रिया मुकुलजालमशोभत किंशुके<BR>R. 9. 31; Bk. 15. 47; Ku. 1. 44; हृदि<BR>चैनामुपधातुमर्हसि R. 8. 77 treasure<BR>uplay to heart; Ms. 4. 54;<BR>उपहितसूक्ष्मग्रंथिना Ś. 1. 19.<BR>--2 To place,<BR>lay; वामहस्तोपहितवदना Ś. 4 resting<BR>on.<BR>--3 (a) To place near; Mv. 4. 56.<BR>(b) To put to or yoke (as a horse to a<BR>carriage &c.).<BR>--4 To cause, bring<BR>on or produce; Mk. 1. 53.<BR>--5 To<BR>impose, entrust with, charge with<BR>(as a duty); तदुपहितकुदुंबः<BR>R. 7. 71.<BR>--6 To lay a command upon,<BR>enjoin, instruct in (with acc.);<BR>स्त्रीषु नृत्यमुपधाय शिक्षयन् R. 19. 36.<BR>--7<BR>To lie down upon, use as a pillow;<BR>उपधाय वामभुजमशयिषि Dk. 111.<BR>--8<BR>To apply, employ, lay or bestow<BR>upon, क्रिया हि वस्तूपहिता प्रसीदति<BR>R. 3. 29.<BR>--9 To place over, cover,<BR>conceal.<BR>--10 To add, place in<BR>addition.<BR>--11 To communicate, impart,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-b" target="_blank">Page0322-b+ 56</a>]<BR>give, bestow; उपहितशोभा Bk. 2. 55.<BR>--12 To locate; एतदुपहितं चैतन्यं<BR>Vedānta S.<BR>--13 (In gram.) To<BR>precede without the intervention<BR>of another syllable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधा
उपधा<BR>1 Imposition, forgery,<BR>fraud, deceit, trick, pretence;<BR>Ms. 8. 193.<BR>--2 Trial or test of honesty,<BR>(धर्माद्यैर्यत्परीक्षणं); (said to be of 4<BR>kinds, {1} loyalty, {2} disinterestedness,<BR>{3} continence, {4} courage); (शोधयेत्)<BR>धर्मोपधाभिर्विप्रांश्च सर्वाभिः सचिवान् पुनः<BR>Kālikā P.<BR>--3 A means or<BR>expedient; अयशोभिदुरा लोके कोपधा<BR>मरणादृते Śi. 19. 58.<BR>--4 (In gram.) A<BR>penultimate letter (अंत्याद्वर्णात्पूर्व उपधा)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भृतः a servant who has<BR>been guilty of dishonesty.<BR>--शुचि<BR>a. tried, of approved loyalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधान|उपधानं
उपधान a. Used (as a Mantra) in<BR>the putting up of the sacrificial<BR>bricks; P. IV. 4. 125.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Placing or resting upon.<BR>--2 A pillow,<BR>cushion; विपुलमुपधानं भुजलता<BR>Bh. 3. 79.<BR>--3 Peculiarity, individuality<BR>(विशेषं); फलोपाधानाभावात्<BR>P. VI. 3. 39 Sk.<BR>--4 Affection, kindness.<BR>--5<BR>A religious observance.<BR>--6<BR>Excellence or excellent quality; सोपधानां<BR>धियं धीराः स्थेयसीं खट्वयंति ये Śi. 2. 77.<BR>(where उ˚ also means a pillow).<BR>--7 Poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधानीय|उपधानीयं
उपधानीय a. To be placed near.<BR>--यं A pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधायिन्
उपधायिन् a. Using as a pillow;<BR>अशेत सा बाहलतोपधायिनी Ku. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिः|उपधि
उपधिः [उप-धा-कि]<BR>1 Fraud,<BR>dishonesty; अरिषु हि विजयार्थिनः क्षितीशा<BR>विदधति सोपधि संधिदूषणानि Ki. 1. 45,<BR>see अनुपधि also.<BR>--2 (In law)<BR>Suppression of the truth, a false<BR>suggestion; Ms. 8. 165.<BR>--3<BR>Terror, threat, compulsion, false<BR>inducement; बलोपधिविनिर्वृत्तान्<BR>व्यवहारान्निवर्तयेत् Y. 2. 31, 89.<BR>--4 The<BR>part of a wheel between the nave<BR>and the circumference, or the wheel<BR>itself.<BR>--5 Foundation (with the<BR>Buddhists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिकः|उपधिक
उपधिकः A cheat, knave, one who<BR>imposes by threats, fraud &c.; see<BR>औपधिक, the more correct form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहित
उपहित p. p.<BR>1 Placed in or upon,<BR>deposited; Ś. 1; ˚मध्यमस्वर<BR>M. 1. 21 taken as a basis.<BR>--2 Preceded by.<BR>--3 Joined, mixed, connected with.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">Page0322-c+ 54</a>]<BR>--4 Possessed of; Śi. 16. 7.<BR>--5<BR>Ready; deputed to act as a spy.<BR>--6<BR>Given, bestowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधातुः|उपधातु
उपधातुः<BR>1 An inferior metal,<BR>semimetal. They are seven; सप्तोपधातवः<BR>स्वर्णं माक्षिकं तारमाक्षिकं । तुत्थं कांस्यं<BR>च रातिश्च सिंदूरं च शिलाजतु ॥.<BR>--2 A secondary secretion of the<BR>body (six in number); e. g.<BR>milk, menses, adeps, sweat, teeth,<BR>hair, and lymph; स्तन्यं रजो<BR>वसा स्वेदो दंताः केशास्तथैव च । औजस्यं<BR>सप्तधातूनां क्रमात्सप्तोपधातवः ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधाव्
उपधाव् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To run towards,<BR>approach hastily.<BR>--2 To resort to.<BR>--3 To run, glide (A.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधावनः|उपधावन
उपधावनः A follower.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Going<BR>after, following.<BR>--2 Meditating<BR>upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधिः|उपधि
उपधिः See under उपधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधूपित|उपधूपितः
उपधूपित a.<BR>1 Fumigated.<BR>--2<BR>Being at the point of death.<BR>--3<BR>Suffering extreme pain.<BR>--तः Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधृ
उपधृ {1} {c10c} P.<BR>1 To hold up,<BR>support, sustain.<BR>--2 To bear, carry.<BR>--3 To hold as, consider or regard<BR>as; सत्त्वं तदुपधारयेत् Ms. 12. 27;<BR>Bg. 7. 6, 9. 6.<BR>--4 To comprehend, perceive,<BR>hear, experience, observe; पुरुषो<BR>रामचरितश्रवणैरुपधारयन् Bhāg.<BR>--5 To<BR>reflect or meditate upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधारणं|उपधारण
उपधारणं<BR>1 Consideration,<BR>reflection.<BR>--2 Drawing, pulling (as by a<BR>hook).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपधृतिः|उपधृति
उपधृतिः f.<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>--2<BR>Holding up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मा
उपध्मा {c1c} P. To blow or breathe<BR>out; excite by blowing, fan; नाग्निं<BR>मुखेनोपधमेत् Ms. 4. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मा
उपध्मा<BR>1 Blowing upon, breathing.<BR>--2 The effort of the voice which<BR>gives rise to the sound उपध्मानीय<BR>q. v. below<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानः|उपध्मान
उपध्मानः A lip.<BR>--नं Blowing<BR>upon, breathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानिन्
उपध्मानिन् a. Blowing upon,<BR>fanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्मानीयः|उपध्मानीय
उपध्मानीयः The aspirate Visarga<BR>before the letters प् and फ्;<BR>उपूपध्मानीयानामोष्ठौ Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपध्वस्त
उपध्वस्त a.<BR>1 Destroyed.<BR>--2<BR>Mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनक्षत्रं|उपनक्षत्र
उपनक्षत्रं A subordinate<BR>constellation, secondary star (their number<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">Page0323-a+ 57</a>]<BR>is said to be 729); सप्तविंशतिः<BR>सप्तविंशतिर्होपनक्षत्राण्येकैकं नक्षत्रमुपतिष्ठंते Śat. Br.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0322-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनखं|उपनख
उपनखं A disease of the finger<BR>nails, whitlow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनगरं|उपनगर
उपनगरं A suburb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनम्
उपनम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To come to, arrive<BR>at, approach, bend or tend towards.<BR>--2 To befall, fall to the lot of,<BR>occur, happen (used by itself or<BR>with gen., dat., or acc. of person);<BR>मत्संभोगः कथमुपनमेत् स्वप्नजोऽपि<BR>Me. 91; तत्तस्योपनमेत् Bh. 2. 121; अंध<BR>आत्मने नोपनमति Bhāg.; अपैनं सहस्रं<BR>नमति Ait. Br.<BR>--3 To share in. --Caus.<BR>1 To lead towards, introduce (with<BR>gen.).<BR>--2 To offer, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनत|उपनतः
उपनत p. p.<BR>1 (a) Come near,<BR>brought, arrived, approached,<BR>brought near to; Ś. 5. 19; R. 12. 102.<BR>(b) Got, obtained; अचिरोपनतां स<BR>मेदिनीं R. 8. 7, 5. 52; चिंतितोपनतां<BR>K. 129; V. 3. 22; V. 2.<BR>--2 Presenting<BR>itself, fallen to the lot of, befallen,<BR>occurred; कस्यात्यंतं सुखमुपनतं<BR>दुःखमेकांततो वा Me. 109; यदेवोपनतं<BR>दुःखात्सुखं तद्रसवत्तरं V. 3. 21;<BR>अनुपनतमनोरथस्य 22; 4. 3; so सुहृदुपनतः<BR>Me. 100; Māl. 10; K. 33, 132, 348;<BR>सुख˚ that readily or without<BR>efforts presented itself Ś. 3;<BR>अकामोपनतं R. 10. 39 unconsciously<BR>committed.<BR>--3 Formed, brought about,<BR>effected.<BR>--4 Presented to, offered,<BR>given; परलोकोपनतं जलांजलिं<BR>R. 8. 68.<BR>--5 Bent down, humbled,<BR>subjected, surrendered; दंडोपनतचरितं<BR>R. 17. 81, 8. 81; दंडोपनतं शत्रुं Mb.<BR>--6 Dependent on (for protection).<BR>--7 Approximate, near (in time or<BR>space.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनतिः|उपनति
उपनतिः f.<BR>1 Approach.<BR>--2<BR>Bending, bow, salutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनामुक
उपनामुक a. Ved. Bending towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनह्
उपनह् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To tie up, tie<BR>together.<BR>--2 To form into a bundle,<BR>bind together.<BR>--3 To inlay, set with;<BR>as चर्मोपनद्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनहनं|उपनहन
उपनहनं<BR>1 A cloth in which<BR>anything is bound up.<BR>--2 Binding,<BR>tying together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाहः|उपनाह
उपनाहः<BR>1 A bundle.<BR>--2 An<BR>unguent applied to a wound or sore;<BR>शोफयोरुपनाहं कुर्यात् Suśr.<BR>--3 The tie<BR>of a lute, a peg to which the strings<BR>of a lyre are attached and by which<BR>they are tightened.<BR>--4<BR>Inflammation of the ciliary glands, stye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनाहनं|उपनाहन
उपनाहनं<BR>1 Applying an unguent.<BR>--2 Anointing, plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनागरिका
उपनागरिका A variety of<BR>वृत्त्यनुप्रास. It is formed by<BR>sweet-sounding letters (माधुर्यव्यंजकवर्ण); e. g.<BR>cf. the example cited in K. P. 9;<BR>अपसारय घनसारं कुरु हारं दूर एव किं कमलैः ।<BR>अलमलमालि मृणालैरिति वदति दिवानिशं बाला ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनामन्
उपनामन् n. A surname,<BR>nickname.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनासिकं|उपनासिक
उपनासिकं The part which is<BR>near the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिक्षिप्
उपनिक्षिप् {c6c} U. To throw or<BR>place down, deposit. = निक्षिप् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिक्षेपः|उपनिक्षेप
उपनिक्षेपः<BR>1 The act of depositing<BR>or placing down.<BR>--2 An open<BR>deposit, any article given in another's<BR>charge by letting him know its form,<BR>quantity &c. Y. 2. 25; (on which<BR>Mit. says:<BR>--उपनिक्षेपो नाम<BR>रूपसंख्याप्रदर्शनेन रक्षणार्थं परस्य हस्ते निहितं द्रव्यं).<BR>--3<BR>A deposit sealed or covered up (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधा
उपनिधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To put or place<BR>near; to bring or lead near to;<BR>कर्णयोरुपनिधाय (मुखं) Āśval.; वहति समीरे<BR>मदनमुपनिधाय Gīt. 5.<BR>--2 To produce,<BR>cause; Bk. 4. 45.<BR>--3 To present;<BR>Māl. 5. 25.<BR>--4 To deposit, entrust;<BR>Ms. 8. 37, 196.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधातृ
उपनिधातृ, --धायक a. Depositing,<BR>placing near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधायक
उपनिधातृ, --धायक a. Depositing,<BR>placing near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधानं|उपनिधान
उपनिधानं<BR>1 Placing near.<BR>--2<BR>Depositing, entrusting to one's care.<BR>--3<BR>A deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिधिः|उपनिधि
उपनिधिः<BR>1 A deposit, pledge,<BR>property entrusted to another.<BR>--2 (In<BR>law) A sealed deposit; Y. 2. 25;<BR>Ms. 8. 145, 149; cf. Medhātithi:<BR>--यदप्रदर्शितरूपं सचिह्रवस्त्रादिना पिहितं<BR>निक्षिप्यते; also cf. Y. 2. 65 and Nārada<BR>quoted in Mit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिहित
उपनिहित p. p.<BR>1 Deposited with.<BR>--2 Placed near to.<BR>--3 Presented,<BR>offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपत्
उपनिपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fly down to.<BR>--2 To take place in addition.<BR>--3 To<BR>be stated incidentally or casually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपातः|उपनिपात
उपनिपातः<BR>1 Approaching, coming<BR>near.<BR>--2 A sudden and unexpected<BR>attack or occurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिपातिन्
उपनिपातिन् a. Coming<BR>(unexpectedly); रंध्रोपनिपातिनोऽनर्थाः Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिबंध्
उपनिबंध् {c9c} P. To compose,<BR>write; किंचिदुपनिबद्धं U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिबंधनं|उपनिबन्धन
उपनिबंधनं<BR>1 A means of<BR>accomplishment.<BR>--2 Binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिमंत्रणं|उपनिमन्त्रण|उपनिमंत्रण
उपनिमंत्रणं Invitation,<BR>inauguration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवपनं|उपनिवपन
उपनिवपनं The act of<BR>scattering or pouring down upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवेशित
उपनिवेशित a. Placed,<BR>established, colonized; स्वर्गाभिष्यंदमन<BR>कृत्वेवोपनिवेशितं Ku. 6. 37; R. 15. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिवेशिन्
उपनिवेशिन् a. Attached to,<BR>inherent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषद्
उपनिषद् f. [said to be from<BR>उपनि-सद् ‘knowledge derived from<BR>sitting at the feet of the preceptor’; but,<BR>according to Indian authorities, it<BR>means ‘to destroy ignorance by<BR>revealing the knowledge of the<BR>Supreme Spirit and cutting off the<BR>bonds of worldly existence’; यथा य<BR>इमां ब्रह्मविद्यामुपयंत्यात्मभावेन<BR>श्रद्धाभक्तिपुरःसराः संतस्तेषां गर्भजन्मजरारोगाद्यनर्थपूगं<BR>निशातयति परं वा ब्रह्म गमयति<BR>अविद्यादिसंसारकारणं चात्यंतमवसादयति विनाशयतीत्युपनिषद्<BR>उपनिपूर्वस्य सदेरेवमर्थस्मरणात् Śaṅkara]<BR>1 N. of certain mystical writings<BR>attached to the Brāhmaṇas, the<BR>chief aim of which is to ascertain<BR>the secret meaning of the Vedas;<BR>Bv. 2. 40; Māl. 1. 7; other<BR>etymologies also are given to explain the<BR>name:--(1) उपनीय तमात्मानं ब्रह्मापास्तद्वयं<BR>यतः । निहंत्यविद्यां तज्जं च तस्मादुपनिषद्भवेत् ॥<BR>or (2) निहत्यानर्थमूलं स्वाविद्यां प्रत्यक्तया परं ।<BR>नयत्यपास्तसंभेदमतो वोपनिषद्भवेत् ॥ or (3)<BR>प्रवृत्तिहेतून्निःशेषांस्तन्मूलोच्छेदकत्वतः ।<BR>यतोवसादयेद्विद्या तस्मादुपनिषद्भवेत् ॥. In the<BR>मुक्तकोपनिषद् 108 Upaniṣads are<BR>mentioned, but some more have been<BR>added to this number. They are said<BR>to have been the source of the<BR>six Darśanas or systems of<BR>philosophy, particularly of the Vedānta<BR>philosophy. The more important<BR>Upaniṣads are:<BR>--ईशकेनकठप्रश्नमुंडमांड्क्यतित्तिरः । ऐतरेयं च छांदोग्यं बृहदारण्यकं<BR>तथा ॥.<BR>--2 (a) An esoteric or secret<BR>doctrine, mystical meaning, words<BR>of mystery. (b) Mystical<BR>knowledge or instruction; मंत्रपारायण˚<BR>U. 6; Mv. 2. 2.<BR>--3 True<BR>knowledge regarding the Supreme Spirit.<BR>--4 Sacred or religious lore.<BR>--5<BR>Secrecy, seclusion.<BR>--6 A<BR>neighbouring mansion.<BR>--7 A lonely place.<BR>--8 A<BR>religious observance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0323-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिषादिन्
उपनिषादिन् a.<BR>1 Sitting at the<BR>feet (of another, such as a<BR>preceptor).<BR>--2 Subjected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्करः|उपनिष्कर|उपनिष्करं
उपनिष्करः A street, a principal<BR>road, high way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनिष्क्रमणं|उपनिष्क्रमण
उपनिष्क्रमणं<BR>1 Going out,<BR>issuing.<BR>--2 One of the Saṃskāras or<BR>religious rites, i. e. taking out a child<BR>for the first time into the open air<BR>(which is usually performed in the<BR>fourth month of its age); cf.<BR>Ms. 2. 34.<BR>--3 A main or royal road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनी
उपनी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring near,<BR>fetch; उपनयति मुनिकुमारकेभ्यः<BR>फलानि K. 45, 62; विधिनैवोपनीतस्त्वं<BR>Mk. 7. 6; अन्नं Ms. 3. 225; M. 2. 5;<BR>Y. 3. 122; तेन ह्युपनय शरं V. 5;<BR>R. 10. 52; Ku. 7. 72.<BR>--2 (a) To<BR>offer, present to; हरये स्वदेहमुपानयत्<BR>R. 2. 59; Bk. 6. 70; Ku. 3. 65;<BR>आर्यस्यासनमुपनय Mk. 9; M. 3. (b) To<BR>hand over, give over;<BR>अंतःपुरपरिचारिकामध्यमुपनीता K. 101; Māl. 1;<BR>Ś. 1; U. 2; अचिरोपनीता वः शिष्या M. 1<BR>recently made over (for<BR>instruction).<BR>--3 To bring to, subject,<BR>expose or put to; आत्मा क्लेशस्य<BR>पदमुपनीतः Ś. 1; R. 13. 39; K. 173.<BR>--4 To<BR>bring about, cause, produce,<BR>accomplish; उपनयन्नर्थान् Pt. 3. 180;<BR>उपनयन्नंगैरनंगोत्सवं Gīt. 1; K. 171.<BR>--5<BR>To bring information, communicate.<BR>--6 To bring into any state, lead<BR>or reduce to; अयोऽभेद्यमुपायेन<BR>द्रवतामुपनीयते Kām. 11. 47.<BR>--7 To take<BR>into one's possession, lead away,<BR>lead; K. 169.<BR>--8 To bring near to<BR>oneself, i. e. invest with the sacred thread<BR>(Atm. P. I. 3. 36); क्षात्रेण<BR>कल्पेनोपनीय U. 2; माणवकमुपनयते Sk.;<BR>R. 3. 29; Bk. 1. 15; Ms. 2. 49, 69,<BR>140.<BR>--9 To hire, employ as hired<BR>servants; कर्मकरानुपनयते Sk. --Caus.<BR>To cause (a master) to receive<BR>(a pupil), cause to invest with<BR>the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनयः|उपनय
उपनयः<BR>1 Bringing near, fetching.<BR>--2 Gaining, attaining, procuring.<BR>--3<BR>Employing.<BR>--4 Investiture with the<BR>sacred thread, initiation into sacred<BR>study, handing a youth of the first<BR>three castes to a teacher;<BR>गृह्योक्तकर्मणा येन समीपं नीयते गुरोः । बालो वेदाय<BR>तद्योगात् बालस्योपनयं विदुः ॥. By this<BR>ceremony spiritual birth is conferred<BR>upon the youth, and he becomes a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">Page0324-b+ 55</a>]<BR>द्विजन्मन्; the ages at which the<BR>ceremony may be performed by the<BR>three castes are respectively 8-16,<BR>11-22 and 12-24; (see<BR>Ms. 2. 36-38; of what materials<BR>&c. the cords should be is<BR>mentioned in 2. 41-46).<BR>--5 The fourth<BR>member of the five-membered Indian<BR>syllogism (in logic), the<BR>application to the special case in<BR>question; व्याप्तिविशिष्टस्य हेतोः<BR>पक्षधर्मताप्रतिपादकं वचनमुपनयः Tarka K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनयनं|उपनयन
उपनयनं<BR>1 Leading to or near.<BR>--2<BR>Presenting, offering; V. 4. 4.<BR>--3<BR>Investiture with the sacred thread;<BR>आसमावर्तनात्कुर्यात् कृतोपनयनो द्बिजः<BR>Ms. 2. 108, 173.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायः|उपनाय
उपनायः, --नायनं = उपनय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायनं|उपनायन
उपनायः, --नायनं = उपनय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायक|उपनायकः
उपनायक a. Leading to.<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>(उप गौणो नायकः) A character in a<BR>dramatic or any other work of art<BR>next in importance to the hero;<BR>(नायकस्य गुणोत्कर्षकथका उपनायकाः);<BR>e. g. Lakṣmaṇa in Rām.;<BR>Makaranda in Māl. &c. &c.<BR>--2 A paramour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनायिका
उपनायिका A character in a<BR>dramatic or any other work of art<BR>next in importance to the heroine;<BR>e. g. Madayantikā in Māl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनीत|उपनीतः
उपनीत p. p.<BR>1 Brought near.<BR>--2<BR>Known.<BR>--3 Obtained, attained.<BR>--4<BR>Presented, given.<BR>--5 Adduced.<BR>--तः<BR>A youth led to the teacher and<BR>invested with the sacred thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेतव्य
उपनेतव्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be brought<BR>near; M. 2. 4.<BR>--2 To be employed or<BR>observed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनेतृ
उपनेतृ a. One who leads or brings<BR>near, fetching; Ku. 1. 60;<BR>मालत्यभिज्ञानस्योपनेत्री Māl. 9. --m. (ता) A<BR>preceptor who performs the उपनयन<BR>ceremony, an Ācārya; Pt. 4. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनृत्
उपनृत् {c4c} P. To dance before some<BR>body; dance with insulting gestures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपनृत्यं|उपनृत्य
उपनृत्यं A place for dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यस्
उपन्यस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To lay upon,<BR>place or put down, put near, place<BR>before.<BR>--2 To entrust any one with,<BR>commit to the care of.<BR>--3 To<BR>explain, describe minutely.<BR>--4 To<BR>propose, suggest, hint, point out,<BR>state; मयोपन्यस्तेषु मंत्रेषू H. 3;<BR>इत्युभयलोकाविरुद्धं वचनमुपन्यस्तं Māl. 2<BR>spoken; सदुपन्यस्यति कृत्यवर्त्म यः<BR>Ki. 2. 3 tells or points out;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-c" target="_blank">Page0324-c+ 54</a>]<BR>किमिदमुपन्यस्तं Ś. 5 what is this that is<BR>proposed or said.<BR>--5 To prove,<BR>establish argumentatively; Y. 2. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यस्त
उपन्यस्त p. p.<BR>1 Placed near,<BR>deposited.<BR>--2 Said, proposed, spoken.<BR>--3 Pledged, entrusted.<BR>--4 Given,<BR>communicated.<BR>--5 Brought<BR>forward as an example, adduced,<BR>hinted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपन्यासः|उपन्यास
उपन्यासः<BR>1 Placing near to,<BR>juxta-position.<BR>--2 A deposit, pledge.<BR>--3 (a) Statement, suggestion,<BR>proposal; पावकः खलु एष वचनोपन्यासः<BR>Ś. 5; Māl. 1, 3, 8. (b) Preface,<BR>introduction; निर्यातः<BR>शनकैरलीकवचनोपन्यासमालीजनः Amaru. 23; चतुरो<BR>मधुरश्चायमुपन्यासः Ak.; so शम˚<BR>Ve. 5 overtures of peace. (c) Allusion,<BR>reference, hinting at; आत्मन<BR>उपन्यासपूर्वं Ś. 3; M. 4; S. D. 363.<BR>--4 A<BR>precept, law.<BR>--5 A kind of peace;<BR>H. 4. 114.<BR>--6 Propitiating (प्रसादनं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपक्षः|उपपक्ष
उपपक्षः Ved. The shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपक्ष्य
उपपक्ष्य a. Near the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपतिः|उपपति
उपपतिः [उपमितः पत्या, उप गौणः<BR>पतिः] A paramour; उपपतिरिव नीचैः<BR>पश्चिमांतेन चंद्रः Śi. 11. 65, 15. 63;<BR>Ms. 3. 155; 4. 216, 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपथं|उपपथ
उपपथं ind. Near the road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपद्
उपपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To reach, come to,<BR>approach, go near; यमुनातटमुपपेदे<BR>Pt. 1; उपपद्यस्व स्वकर्मोचितां गतिं Dk. 93.<BR>--2 To be got or obtained, fall to<BR>one's share; Bg. 6. 39; 13. 18.<BR>--3 To take place, occur, happen, be<BR>produced; देवि एवमुपपद्यते M. 1 even<BR>as you say, just so;<BR>अर्थास्तस्योपपत्स्यंते Mb.; उपपन्ना हि दारेषु प्रभुता<BR>सर्वतोमुखी Ś. 5. 26.<BR>--4 To be possible;<BR>कर्तव्यं वो न पश्यामि स्याच्चेत्किं<BR>नोपपद्यते Ku. 6. 61; Ms. 9. 121, 40;<BR>10. 102; नेश्वरो जगतः कारणमुपपद्यते Ś. B.<BR>--5 To be suitable, be fit for, be<BR>adequate for, fit, suit (with loc.);<BR>मा क्लैब्यं गच्छ कौंतेय नैतत्त्वय्युपपद्यते<BR>Bg. 2. 3; 18. 7; उपपद्यते it is fit; ते<BR>गुणाः परस्मिन् ब्रह्मण्युपपद्यंते Ś. B.<BR>--6<BR>To go against, attack.<BR>--7 To put<BR>in a word or statement; इति ह<BR>विश्वामित्र उपपपाद Ait. Br. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To bring into any state, cause to<BR>arrive or be obtained;<BR>विश्वासमुपपादिता Rām. inspired with confidence;<BR>get ready; रथमुपपादय Ve. 2.<BR>--2 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-a" target="_blank">Page0325-a+ 57</a>]<BR>offer, present any one with (acc.),<BR>bring to; दिष्ट्या त्वमसि मे धात्रा<BR>भीतेनेवोपपादितः R. 15. 18, 14. 8; 16. 32;<BR>Ms. 9. 72, 73; 3. 96; sometimes<BR>with dat.; Ms. 11. 77; 9. 244; or<BR>with loc.; Y. 1. 315.<BR>--3 (a) To<BR>cause to happen or occur, bring<BR>about; मरणमुपपादयेत् K. 36. (b) To<BR>accomplish, effect, cause, do,<BR>perform; यावत्तु मानुष्यके<BR>शक्यमुपपादयितुं K. 62, 113, 120, 134; देवकार्यं<BR>R. 11. 91; 17. 55; Me. 29.<BR>--4 (a) To<BR>make a statement, adduce, put<BR>forward. (b) To justify.<BR>--5 To<BR>make good, establish, prove;<BR>कथमीश्वरं विनाशधर्मिणमुपपादयसि Prab.<BR>--6<BR>To pronounce, declare.<BR>--7 To make<BR>fit or adequate for; कालोपपादिते क्षेत्रे<BR>Ms. 9. 36.<BR>--8 To furnish with,<BR>endow with; Kām. 11. 57; K. 2;<BR>आत्मानं प्रथमं राजा विनयनोपपादयेत्<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--9 To find out, ascertain;<BR>Ms. 3. 206.<BR>--10 To examine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0324-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपत्तिः|उपपत्ति
उपपत्तिः f.<BR>1 Happening,<BR>occurring, becoming visible, appearance,<BR>production, birth Śi. 1. 69 (जन्म);<BR>इष्टानिष्टोपपत्तिषु Bg. 13. 9.<BR>--2 Cause,<BR>reason, ground; प्रियेषु यैः पार्थ<BR>विनोपपत्तेः Ki. 3. 52.<BR>--3 Reasoning,<BR>argument; उपपत्तिमदूर्जितं वचः Ki. 2. 1<BR>argumentative; giving a reason for<BR>the establishment of a matter;<BR>S. D. 482.<BR>--4 Fitness, propriety.<BR>--5<BR>Termination, end.<BR>--6 Association,<BR>connection.<BR>--7 Acceptance, adoption;<BR>Mv. 5.<BR>--8 Ascertainment,<BR>demonstration, demonstrated conclusion;<BR>उपपत्तिरुदाहृता बलात् Ki. 2. 28.<BR>--9 (In<BR>Arith. or Geom.) Proof,<BR>demonstration.<BR>--10 A means, an<BR>expedient.<BR>--11 Assistance, support, help;<BR>Ki. 14. 44.<BR>--12 Doing, effecting,<BR>gaining; accomplishment;<BR>स्वार्थोपपत्तिं दुर्बलाशः R. 5. 12; तात्पर्यानुपपत्तितः<BR>Bhaṣa P.; H. 3. 118; see अनुपपत्ति.<BR>--13 Attainment, getting; असंशयं<BR>प्राक् तनयोपपत्तेः R. 14. 78;<BR>Ki. 3. 1.<BR>--14 Religious abstraction (समाधि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपन्न
उपपन्न p. p.<BR>1 Obtained; secured;<BR>अतींद्रियेष्वप्युपपन्नदर्शनः R. 3. 41;<BR>V. 5. 15; R. 1. 60.<BR>--2 Accompanied<BR>or attended by, in company with;<BR>श्रद्धेव साक्षाद्विधिनोपपन्ना R. 2. 16,<BR>22.<BR>--3 Coming, presenting<BR>itself.<BR>--4 Right, fit, proper,<BR>suitable (with gen. or loc.); उपपन्नस्ते<BR>तर्कः V. 2; उपपन्नमिदं विशेषणं वायोः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">Page0325-b+ 55</a>]<BR>ibid. this epithet befits the wind;<BR>उपपन्नमेतदास्मिन् राजनि Ś. 2.<BR>--5<BR>Possible; उभयमप्यनुपपन्नं V. 2;<BR>Ku. 3. 12.<BR>--6 Full of, endowed with,<BR>possessed of, furnished with; उपपन्नो<BR>गुणैरिष्टैः Nala. 1. 1; Ms. 9. 141, 244;<BR>तल्लक्षणोपपन्नः Ś. 5.<BR>--7 Demonstrated,<BR>proved.<BR>--8 Offered, presented.<BR>--9<BR>Cured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादक
उपपादक a.<BR>1 Producing,<BR>effecting.<BR>--2 Well reasoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादनं|उपपादन
उपपादनं<BR>1 Effecting,<BR>accomplishing, doing.<BR>--2 Giving, delivering,<BR>presenting.<BR>--3 Proving,<BR>demonstration, establishing by arguments.<BR>--4<BR>Examination, ascertainment,<BR>exposition (of a subject).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादुक|उपपादुकः
उपपादुक a. Self-produced.<BR>--कः A<BR>superhuman being, God;<BR>दिव्योपपादुका देवाः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपदं|उपपद
उपपदं<BR>1 A word prefixed or<BR>previously uttered; धनुरुपपदं वेदं<BR>Ki. 18. 44 (धनुर्वेदं); तस्याः स राजोपपदं<BR>निशांतं R. 16. 40.<BR>--2 A title, a degree;<BR>epithet of respect, such as आर्य,<BR>शर्मन्; कथं निरुपपदमेव चाणक्यमिति न<BR>आर्यचाणक्यमिति Mu. 3.<BR>--3 A<BR>secondary word of a sentence, a preposition,<BR>particle &c. prefixed to a verb or<BR>a noun derived from a verb which<BR>determines or qualifies the sense<BR>of the verb; उपपदमतिङ्<BR>P. II. 2. 19; (see Sk. thereon). ˚तत्पुरुषः<BR>a kind of Tat. comp. in which the<BR>last member is some form of a<BR>verbal character; e. g. वेदविद्, ग्रामणी,<BR>आकर्णलंबिन् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपरीक्षा
उपपरीक्षा --क्षणं Investigation,<BR>examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपरीक्षणं|उपपरीक्षण
उपपरीक्षा --क्षणं Investigation,<BR>examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपर्चन
उपपर्चन, उपपृच् a. Closely<BR>touching.<BR>--नं Impregnation or<BR>admixture (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपृच्
उपपर्चन, उपपृच् a. Closely<BR>touching.<BR>--नं Impregnation or<BR>admixture (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपर्शुका
उपपर्शुका The false ribs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातः|उपपात
उपपातः<BR>1 An unexpected occur<BR>rence.<BR>--2 A calamity, misfortune,<BR>accident.<BR>--3 Destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातकं|उपपातक
उपपातकं A minor sin, crime<BR>or sin of the second degree;<BR>महापातकतुल्यानि पापान्युक्तानियानि तु । तानि<BR>पातकसंज्ञानि तन्न्यूनमुपपातकम् ॥; Y. 2. 210.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपातकिन्
उपपातकिन् a. One who has<BR>committed an उपपातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपादुक|उपपादुकः
उपपादुक a. Having shoes, shod<BR>(as a horse).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0325-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपपापं|उपपाप
