उपसृ
उपसृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go towards,<BR>approach, draw near; राजानं… दुर्गं…<BR>उपसृत्य &c.<BR>--2 To go against, attack.<BR>--3 To have intercourse (as of a<BR>woman with a man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर|उपसरः
उपसर a. Approaching.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>Approaching (as a cow).<BR>--2 The first<BR>pregnancy of a cow; गवामुपसरः Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसरणं|उपसरण
उपसरणं<BR>1 Going towards.<BR>--2<BR>Rapid flowing of the blood towards<BR>the heart (as in sickness).<BR>--3 That<BR>which is approached as a refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्या|उपसर्य्या
उपसर्या A cow fit for a bull (cf.<BR>P. III. 1. 104).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृज्
उपसृज् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To pour out or<BR>on, offer (water &c.).<BR>--2 To add to,<BR>annex; to join, attach, connect<BR>with, bring to.<BR>--3 To beset with,<BR>oppress, infest; Ms. 4. 61; see<BR>उपसृष्ट below; रोषेण, व्याधिना &c.<BR>--4<BR>To eclipse; Ms. 4. 37; Y. 1. 272.<BR>--5 To come in contact with.<BR>--6<BR>To produce, effect, create.<BR>--7 To<BR>destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्गः|उपसर्ग
उपसर्गः<BR>1 Sickness, disease,<BR>change occasioned by a disease; also<BR>a disease superinduced on another;<BR>क्षीणं हन्युश्चोपसर्गाः प्रभूताः Suśr.<BR>--2 Misfortune, trouble, calamity,<BR>injury, harm; प्रशमिताशेषोपसर्गाः<BR>प्रजाः Ratn. 1. 10; सोपसर्गं वो नक्षत्रं<BR>M. 4.<BR>--3 Portent, natural phenomenon<BR>foreboding evil.<BR>--4 An eclipse.<BR>--5 An indication or symptom of<BR>death.<BR>--6 Addition.<BR>--7 Possession<BR>by an evil spirit.<BR>--8 A preposition<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-b" target="_blank">Page0333-b+ 56</a>]<BR>prefixed to roots; निपाताश्चादयो ज्ञेयाः<BR>प्रादयस्तूपसर्गकाः । द्योतकत्वात् क्रियायोगे<BR>लोकादवगता इमे ॥ Upasargas are 20<BR>in number:<BR>--प्र, परा, अप, सम्,<BR>अनु, अव, निस् or निर्, दुस् or दुर्, वि, आ<BR>(ङ्), नि, अधि, अपि, अति, सु, उत्, अभि,<BR>प्रति, परि, उप; or 22 if निस्-निर् and दुस्-दुर्<BR>be taken as separate words. There<BR>are two theories as to the character<BR>of these prepositions. According to<BR>one theory roots have various<BR>meanings in themselves (अनेकार्था हि धातवः);<BR>when prepositions are prefixed to<BR>them they simply bring to light<BR>those meanings already existent but<BR>hidden in them, but they do not<BR>express them, being meaningless<BR>themselves; cf. Śi. 10. 15:<BR>--संतमेव<BR>चिरमप्रकृतत्वादप्रकाशितमदिद्युतदंगे । विभ्रमं<BR>मधुमदः प्रमदानां धातुलीनमुपसर्ग इवार्थम् ॥.<BR>According to the other theory<BR>prepositions express their own<BR>independent meanings; they modify,<BR>intensify, and sometimes entirely<BR>alter, the senses of roots; cf. Sk.:<BR>--उपसर्गेण धात्वर्थो बलादन्यत्र नीयते ।<BR>प्रहाराहारसंहारविहारपरिहारवत् ॥ cf. also धात्वर्थं बाधते<BR>कश्चित्कश्चित्तमनुवर्तते । तमेव विशिनष्ट्यन्य<BR>उपसर्गगतिस्त्रिधा ॥ (The latter theory<BR>appears to be more correct. For a fuller<BR>exposition see Nirukta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्जनं|उपसर्जन|उपसर्ज्जन|उपसर्ज्जनं
उपसर्जनं<BR>1 Pouring on.<BR>--2 A<BR>misfortune, calamity (as an eclipse),<BR>portent; Ms. 4. 105.<BR>--3 Leaving.<BR>--4<BR>Eclipsing.<BR>--5 Any person or thing<BR>subordinate to another, a substitute.<BR>--6 (In gram.) A word which either<BR>by composition or derivation loses<BR>its original independent character,<BR>while it also determines the sense<BR>of another word (opp. प्रधान); e. g.<BR>in पाणिनीयः a pupil of पाणिनि, पाणिनि<BR>becomes उपसर्जन; or in राजपुरुषः, राजन्<BR>is उपसर्जन, having lost its<BR>independent character; P. I. 2. 43, 48, 57;<BR>II. 2. 30; IV. 1. 14, 54; VI. 3. 82;<BR>आचार्योपसर्जनश्चांतेवासी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृष्ट|उपसृष्टं|उपसृष्टः
उपसृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Joined, connected<BR>with, accompanied by.<BR>--2 Seized or<BR>possessed by (a demon or evil<BR>spirit). उपसृष्टा इव क्षुद्राधिष्ठितभवनाः<BR>K. 107.<BR>--3 Troubled, affected, injured;<BR>रोगोपसृष्टतनुदुर्वसतिं मुमुक्षुः R. 8. 94;<BR>K. 289.<BR>--4 Eclipsed.<BR>--5 Furnished with<BR>an उपसर्ग (as a root); क्रुधद्रुहोरुपसृष्टयोः<BR>कर्म P. I. 4. 38.<BR>--ष्टः The sun or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">Page0333-c+ 56</a>]<BR>moon when eclipsed.<BR>--ष्टं Sexual<BR>union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसृप्
उपसृप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To approach,<BR>move towards, draw near to;<BR>ममोपांतिकमुपसर्पन् M. 1; 1. 12.<BR>--2 To<BR>meet unexpectedly.<BR>--3 To move,<BR>go; प्रतिवातं न हि घनः कदाचिदुपसर्पति<BR>Pt. 3. 23; so प्रलयं, दुःखं &c.<BR>--4 To<BR>begin (with inf.); Ms. 10. 105.<BR>--5<BR>To attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्पः|उपसर्प
उपसर्पः<BR>1 Approach, access.<BR>--2<BR>Following a person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्पणं|उपसर्पण
उपसर्पणं Going near, approaching,<BR>advancing towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसर्पिन्
उपसर्पिन् a. Going near,<BR>approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेक्तृ
उपसेक्तृ a. One who sprinkles<BR>or pours down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेचन
उपसेचन a. Pouring, sprinkling.<BR>--नं, उपसेकः<BR>1 Pouring or<BR>sprinkling upon, watering.<BR>--2 Infusion;<BR>juice.<BR>--नी A ladle or cup for<BR>pouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेव्
उपसेव् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To serve,<BR>worship, honour; Ms. 4. 133.<BR>--2 To<BR>practise, follow, pursue, cultivate; as a<BR>vow.<BR>--3 To make use of.<BR>--4<BR>To be addicted to, enjoy;<BR>Bg. 15. 9; so सुखं, संधिं, विग्रहं &c.<BR>--5 To<BR>frequent, inhabit.<BR>--6 To rub or<BR>anoint with (sandal &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेवक
उपसेवक a.<BR>1 Worshipping,<BR>serving.<BR>--2 Following, practising.<BR>--3<BR>Enjoying (carnally); Y. 3. 136.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेवनं|उपसेवन
उपसेवनं, --सेवा<BR>1 Worshipping,<BR>honouring, adoring.<BR>--2 Service; राज˚<BR>Ms. 3. 64.<BR>--3 Addiction to; विषय˚<BR>Ms. 12. 7.<BR>--4 Using, enjoying<BR>(carnally also); छाया˚; परदार˚ Ms. 4. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेवा
उपसेवनं, --सेवा<BR>1 Worshipping,<BR>honouring, adoring.<BR>--2 Service; राज˚<BR>Ms. 3. 64.<BR>--3 Addiction to; विषय˚<BR>Ms. 12. 7.<BR>--4 Using, enjoying<BR>(carnally also); छाया˚; परदार˚ Ms. 4. 134.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपसेविन्
उपसेविन् a. Serving, practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कृ
उपस्कृ {c8c} U. To prepare,<BR>elaborate, perfect, adorn; (see उपकृ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्करः|उपस्कर
उपस्करः<BR>1 Any article which<BR>serves to make anything<BR>complete, an ingredient.<BR>--2 (Hence)<BR>Condiment or seasoning for food (as<BR>mustard, pepper &c.).<BR>--3 Furniture,<BR>appurtenance, apparatus,<BR>instrument (उपकरण); उपस्करो रथस्यासीत्<BR>Mb.; Śi. 18. 72.<BR>--4 Any article or<BR>implement of household use (such<BR>as a broomstick); Y. 1. 83; 2. 193;<BR>Ms. 3. 68, 12. 66, 5. 150.<BR>--5 An<BR>ornament.<BR>--6 Censure, blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्करणं|उपस्करण
उपस्करणं<BR>1 Killing, injuring.<BR>--2 A collection.<BR>--3 A change,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">Page0334-a+ 55</a>]<BR>modification.<BR>--4 An ellipsis.<BR>--5<BR>Blame, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0333-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कारः|उपस्कार
उपस्कारः<BR>1 Anything additional,<BR>a supplement.<BR>--2 (Supplying) An<BR>ellipsis; साकांक्षमनुपस्कारं विष्वग्गति<BR>निराकुलं Ki. 11. 38.<BR>--3 Beautifying,<BR>ornamenting by way of adding<BR>grace; उक्तमेवार्थं सोपस्कारमाह Malli.<BR>on R. 11. 47.<BR>--4 An ornament.<BR>--5 A stroke.<BR>--6 A collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कृत
उपस्कृत p. p.<BR>1 Prepared, perfected.<BR>--2 Censured, blamed.<BR>--3<BR>Killed, injured.<BR>--4 Collected.<BR>--5<BR>Beautified, ornamented.<BR>--6 Supplied<BR>(as ellipsis).<BR>--7 Modified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्कृतिः|उपस्कृति
उपस्कृतिः f. Supplement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तंभ्|उपस्तम्भ्
उपस्तंभ् {c5c} {c9c} P. To prop,<BR>support (fig. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तंभः|उपस्तम्भ|उपस्तंभ|उपस्तम्भः
उपस्तंभः, --भनं<BR>1 Stay, support.<BR>--2<BR>Support of life (as food, sleep &c.).<BR>--3 Encouragement, incitement,<BR>aid; मंत्रोपस्तंभेन H. 3.<BR>--4 Basis,<BR>ground, occasion; मूषकबलोपस्तंभेन<BR>कारणेन भवितव्यं H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तंभनं|उपस्तम्भन|उपस्तंभन
उपस्तंभः, --भनं<BR>1 Stay, support.<BR>--2<BR>Support of life (as food, sleep &c.).<BR>--3 Encouragement, incitement,<BR>aid; मंत्रोपस्तंभेन H. 3.<BR>--4 Basis,<BR>ground, occasion; मूषकबलोपस्तंभेन<BR>कारणेन भवितव्यं H. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तंभक|उपस्तम्भक
उपस्तंभक a. Supporting, aiding,<BR>encouraging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तरणं|उपस्तरण
उपस्तरणं See under उपस्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तिः|उपस्ति
उपस्तिः Ved.<BR>1 A tree.<BR>--2 An<BR>attendant, a follower, servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तु
उपस्तु {c2c} U.<BR>1 To praise, extol.<BR>--2 To invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तुत्
उपस्तुत् f. Ved. Praise, invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तुतिः|उपस्तुति
उपस्तुतिः f. Invocation, praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तृ
उपस्तृ, --स्तॄ {c5c} {c9c} U.<BR>1 To spread<BR>out (for another); spread under.<BR>--2 To strew or cover with.<BR>--3 To<BR>arrange, set in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तॄ
उपस्तृ, --स्तॄ {c5c} {c9c} U.<BR>1 To spread<BR>out (for another); spread under.<BR>--2 To strew or cover with.<BR>--3 To<BR>arrange, set in order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तरणं|उपस्तरण
उपस्तरणं<BR>1 Spreading out,<BR>scattering.<BR>--2 A covering, garment.<BR>--3 A bed.<BR>--4 Anything spread<BR>out (as a covering);<BR>अमृतोपस्तरणमसि स्वाहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्तिर्
उपस्तिर् f. Ved.<BR>1 Spreading.<BR>--2 A covering, what is spread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्त्री
उपस्त्री f. [गौणी स्त्री] A concubine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्था
उपस्था {c1c} U. (cf. P. I. 3. 25-6<BR>and Vārt. 1)<BR>1 To stand near; fall<BR>to one's share; नादत्तमुपतिष्ठति<BR>Pt. 2. 123; remain; Mu. 4. 13.<BR>--2 To<BR>come near, approach; मामुपतिष्ठस्व<BR>Mu. 1 come to me; रामं मुनिरुपस्थितः<BR>R. 15. 76; Ku. 2. 64; Pt. 1.<BR>राजद्वारं U. 1; R. 1. 45, 87, 2. 39, 15. 15.<BR>--3 To wait or attend upon, serve;<BR>नाटकेनोपस्थातव्यमस्माभिः Ś. 1 we<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-b" target="_blank">Page0334-b+ 56</a>]<BR>must wait upon (serve) (the<BR>audience) with a play; Ms. 2. 48, 3. 189;<BR>पुरा शक्रमुपस्थाय R. 1. 75, 14. 24;<BR>U. 1.<BR>--4 To approach with prayers,<BR>worship (said to be Atm. only in this<BR>sense); ये सूर्यमुपतिष्ठंते मंत्रैः Bk. 8. 13;<BR>न त्र्यंबकादन्यमुपास्थितासौ 1. 3;<BR>Ku. 2. 3; R. 4. 6, 10. 63, 17. 10, 18. 22;<BR>Māl.; U. 2, 3, 7; सख्येन मामुपतिष्ठते<BR>treats me as a friend.<BR>--5 To be or<BR>remain near, stay with.<BR>--6 To go<BR>to with the desire of getting (P. or<BR>A.); प्रभुमुपतिष्ठति-ते Sk.<BR>--7 To<BR>approach for intercourse; कं<BR>रहस्युपतिष्ठसे Bk. 5. 68; पतिमुपतिष्ठते नारी Vop.<BR>--8 To meet, join (as a river) (A.);<BR>गंगा यमुनामुपतिष्ठते Sk.<BR>--9 To form<BR>friendship with, make a friend of;<BR>रथिकानुपतिष्ठते Sk; उपास्थितैवमुक्ते तं<BR>सखायं राघवः पितुः Bk. 6. 42;<BR>संतमुपतिष्ठते साधुः Vop.<BR>--10 To approach<BR>with hostile intentions.<BR>--11 To lead<BR>to, go to or reach (A.) (as a way);<BR>पंथाः स्रुध्रमुपतिष्ठते Sk. (प्राप्नोति); Ms. 3. 76.<BR>--12 To pass over to, devolve upon,<BR>fall to the share of; मूलपुरुषावसाने<BR>संपदः परमुपतिष्ठंति Ś. 6; Ki. 13. 69;<BR>वीरसूरिति शब्दोयं तनयात्त्वामुपस्थितः<BR>M. 5. 16 applies to you; R. 8. 2;<BR>विपदुत्पत्तिमतामुपस्थिता 8. 83 awaits or<BR>falls to the lot of.<BR>--13 To occur,<BR>arise; be got; अहोऽस्माकं<BR>भोजनमुपस्थितं H. 1.<BR>--14 To be present (A.);<BR>स्मृत्युपस्थितौ श्लोकौ U. 6; भोजनकाले<BR>उपतिष्ठते Sk.<BR>--15 To stand under for<BR>support.<BR>--16 To resort to;<BR>वेशमुपतिष्ठंति Dk. 60.<BR>--17 To conciliate.<BR>--Caus. (-स्थापयति)<BR>1 To provide,<BR>present with, furnish with; to get<BR>ready, prepare; अस्खलितसुखसंपातं<BR>रथमुपस्थापय U. 1; सबाणासनं रथं<BR>Ś. 2.<BR>--2 To place upon or near.<BR>--3<BR>To produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थ|उपस्थः
उपस्थ a. Near, approximate.<BR>--स्थः<BR>1 The lap; उपस्थं कृ to make a lap;<BR>˚स्थे कृ to take on the lap.<BR>--2<BR>The middle part in general.<BR>--स्थः<BR>स्थं<BR>1 The organ of generation<BR>(of men and women, particularly<BR>of the latter); स्नानं<BR>मौनोपवासेज्यास्वाध्यायोपस्थनिग्रहाः Y. 3. 314 (male);<BR>स्थूलोपस्थस्थलीषु Bh. 1. 20 (female);<BR>हस्तौ पायुरुपस्थश्च Y. 3. 92 (where<BR>the word is used in both senses).<BR>--2 The anus.<BR>--3 The haunch or<BR>hip.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दघ्न a. reaching to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-c" target="_blank">Page0334-c+ 56</a>]<BR>the lap.<BR>--निग्रहः restraint of<BR>sensual passions, continence;<BR>Y. 3. 314.<BR>--पत्रः, --दलः the Indian fig-tree<BR>(so called because its leaves<BR>resemble in shape the female organ<BR>of generation).<BR>--सद् a. sitting in<BR>the lap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थातृ
उपस्थातृ a.<BR>1 Dependent on,<BR>humbled (उपनत).<BR>--2 Not late, come in<BR>time. --m.<BR>1 An attendant, a<BR>servant.<BR>--2 A sacrificial priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थानं|उपस्थान
उपस्थानं<BR>1 Presence, proximity,<BR>nearness.<BR>--2 Approaching,<BR>coming, appearance, coming into<BR>the presence of;<BR>युगपदाचार्ययोरुपस्थानं M. 1.<BR>--3 (a) Worshipping,<BR>waiting upon (with prayers);<BR>attendance, service;<BR>सूर्योपस्थानात्प्रतिनिवृत्तं पुरूरवसं मामुपेत्य V. 1;<BR>सूर्यस्योपस्थानं कुर्वः V. 4; Y. 1. 22, 3. 282.<BR>(b) Obeisance; greeting;<BR>˚स्तोत्रपद्धतिं U. 1 a form of congratulatory<BR>panegyric.<BR>--4 Attending to,<BR>guarding; रावणहित˚ Mv. 5.<BR>--5 An abode.<BR>--6 The sanctuary, any sacred place<BR>(approached with respect).<BR>--7 An<BR>assembly.<BR>--8 Remembrance,<BR>recollection, memory; Y. 3. 160.<BR>--9<BR>Obtaining, getting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थानीय
उपस्थानीय pot. p.<BR>1 To be stayed<BR>with, be kept near.<BR>--2 To be waited<BR>upon or served.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापक
उपस्थापक a.<BR>1 Placing or bringing<BR>near.<BR>--2 Explaining, teaching.<BR>--3<BR>Causing to remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थापनं|उपस्थापन
उपस्थापनं<BR>1 Placing near, getting<BR>ready.<BR>--2 The awakening of<BR>memory.<BR>--3 Attendance, service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थायकः|उपस्थायक
उपस्थायकः<BR>1 A servant.<BR>--2 A<BR>follower of Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थायिन्
उपस्थायिन् a. Standing near,<BR>waiting upon, approaching &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थित|उपस्थितः
उपस्थित p. p.<BR>1 Approached,<BR>arrived, come (person or thing);<BR>तस्मिन्नंतरे भर्तोपस्थितः M. 1; ˚श्रेयोऽ<BR>वमानिनं Ś. 6; K. 157; Ms. 3. 243;<BR>Y. 2. 62; चिंतित˚ Ku. 6. 24 come<BR>as soon as thought of.<BR>--2 Close or<BR>near, at hand, impending, drawing<BR>near; उपस्थिता रजनी Ś. 3 the night<BR>is at hand (arrived); ˚संप्रहारः<BR>V. 1; ˚उदयं R. 3. 1 approaching its<BR>fulfilment; Māl. 10; Ratn. 1;<BR>R. 14. 39.<BR>--3 Worshipped or waited<BR>upon, served.<BR>--4 Got, obtained,<BR>received; अयाचित˚ Ku. 5. 22 got<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">Page0335-a+ 55</a>]<BR>without solicitation; अचिंतित˚<BR>Pt. 2.<BR>--5 Taken place, happened,<BR>occurred, fallen to the lot;<BR>V. 5. 16.<BR>--6 Caused, occasioned,<BR>produced, felt.<BR>--7 Known.<BR>--8 Cleansed,<BR>clean.<BR>--9 Followed by the particle<BR>इति in the Pada text.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The<BR>particle used in this manner.<BR>--2<BR>The position of words before and<BR>after इति so used.<BR>--3 Service,<BR>worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0334-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्थितिः|उपस्थिति
उपस्थितिः f.<BR>1 Approach.<BR>--2<BR>Proximity, presence.<BR>--3 Obtaining,<BR>getting.<BR>--4 Accomplishing,<BR>effecting.<BR>--5 Remembrance, recollection.<BR>--6 Service, attendance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्नेहः|उपस्नेह
उपस्नेहः Moistening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्नेहयति
उपस्नेहयति Den. P. To melt (to<BR>love); U. 2, 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पृश्
उपस्पृश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To touch (water),<BR>bathe; स्नानमुपस्पृशंती K. 172;<BR>तथेत्युपस्पृश्य जलं पवित्रं R. 5. 59,<BR>18. 31; उपस्पृश्य मणिकर्णिकायां Dk. 95,<BR>110; Ms. 11. 133.<BR>--2 To wash or<BR>rinse the mouth (or teeth); to<BR>sip water (and eject it); स<BR>नद्यवस्कंदमुपास्पृशच्च Bk. 2. 11; K. 100;<BR>Ms. 2. 53, 58, 5. 63; Y. 3. 30,<BR>1. 18.<BR>--3 To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शः|उपस्पर्श
उपस्पर्शः --र्शनं<BR>1 Touching, contact.<BR>--2 Bathing, ablution, washing<BR>oneself.<BR>--3 Rinsing the mouth, sipping<BR>and ejecting water as a religious act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शनं|उपस्पर्शन
उपस्पर्शः --र्शनं<BR>1 Touching, contact.<BR>--2 Bathing, ablution, washing<BR>oneself.<BR>--3 Rinsing the mouth, sipping<BR>and ejecting water as a religious act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्पर्शिन्
उपस्पर्शिन् a.<BR>1 Touching.<BR>--2<BR>Sipping water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्मृतिः|उपस्मृति
उपस्मृतिः f. A minor law-book.<BR>(They are 18 in all).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्रवणं|उपस्रवण
उपस्रवणं<BR>1 The periodical flow<BR>of a woman, menses.<BR>--2 Flow (in<BR>general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वत्वं|उपस्वत्व
उपस्वत्वं Revenue, profit<BR>(derived from land or capital).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपस्वेदः|उपस्वेद
उपस्वेदः Moisture, sweat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहन्
उपहन् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To strike, smite;<BR>दडोपघातं गाः कालयति Sk.<BR>--2 To waste,<BR>injure, destroy, kill; अनुपघ्नन् पितृद्रव्यं<BR>Ms. 9. 208; लंका चोपहनिष्यते<BR>Bk. 16. 12, 5. 12; Bg. 3. 24.<BR>--3 To<BR>thrust in or into.<BR>--4 To err,<BR>mistake in reciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत|उपहतः
उपहत p. p.<BR>1 Injured, struck,<BR>impaired; अनुपहतविधिः पंथाः<BR>Bh. 2. 26; pained, hurt; Ku. 5. 76.<BR>--2<BR>Affected by, smit, injured, struck<BR>with, overpowered; भूत˚ K. 167;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">Page0335-b+ 56</a>]<BR>दारिद्र्य˚, लोभ˚, दर्प˚, काम˚, शोक˚ &c.;<BR>Mu. 7.<BR>--3 Struck by lightning &c.<BR>--4 Doomed (to destruction);<BR>कथमत्रापि दैवेनोपहता वयं Mu. 2;<BR>दैवेनोपहतस्य बुद्धिरथवा पूर्वं विपर्यस्यति<BR>Mu. 6. 8.<BR>--5 Censured, rebuked,<BR>disregarded.<BR>--6 Vitiated, polluted, made<BR>impure; शारीरैर्मलैः सुराभिर्मद्यैर्वा<BR>यदुपहतं तदत्यंतोपहतं Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a. agitated in mind, mentally<BR>affected.<BR>--दृश् a. dazzled, blinded;<BR>Ki. 12. 18.<BR>--धी a. infatuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतक
उपहतक a. Ill-fated, unfortunate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहतिः|उपहति
उपहतिः f.<BR>1 Stroke.<BR>--2 Killing,<BR>injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत्नु
उपहत्नु a. Ved. Attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहत्या
उपहत्या Dazzling of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहंतृ|उपहन्तृ
उपहंतृ a. Ved. Having a contrary<BR>effect, disturbing, exciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघातः|उपघात
उपघातः<BR>1 A stroke, injury,<BR>insult; Ms. 2. 179; Y. 2. 256.<BR>--2<BR>Destruction, ruin.<BR>--3 Touch, contact<BR>(with an intention to hurt).<BR>--4<BR>Personal violence, assault.<BR>--5<BR>Disease, sickness.<BR>--6 Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघातक|उपघातकः
उपघातक, --तिन् a. Injuring,<BR>hurting, offending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपघातिन्
उपघातक, --तिन् a. Injuring,<BR>hurting, offending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहस्
उपहस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To ridicule,<BR>deride, laugh at; (fig.) to excel, surpass;<BR>अमरगुरुमपि प्रज्ञयोपहसद्भिः K. 7;<BR>Dk. 10.<BR>--2 To couple oneself with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहसित|उपहसितं
उपहसित p. p. Ridiculed, derided.<BR>--तं Satirical laughter, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासः|उपहास
उपहासः<BR>1 Ridicule, derision;<BR>R. 12. 37.<BR>--2 Satirical laughter.<BR>--3<BR>Fun, play.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्पदं, --पात्रं<BR>laughing-stock, butt of ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहासक|उपहासकः
उपहासक a. Ridiculing others.<BR>--कः A jester.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहास्य
उपहास्य pot. p. Ridiculous; ˚ता<BR>ridiculousness; ˚तां गम् or या<BR>become an object of ridicule, be<BR>exposed to derision;<BR>गमिष्याम्युपहास्यतां R. 1. 3;<BR>सर्वजनस्योपहास्यतामुपयांति K. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहस्तिका
उपहस्तिका [उपगता हस्तं अत इत्वम्]<BR>A small purse (or box)<BR>containing the ingredients necessary for<BR>betel-chewing (e. g. leaves,<BR>chunam, catechu, betel &c.) (Mar.<BR>चंची, बटवा, झोळणा); उपहस्तिकायास्तांबूलं<BR>कर्पूसहितमुद्धत्य Dk. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहालकः|उपहालक
उपहालकः N. of the Kuntala<BR>country, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहृ
उपहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fetch, bring near;<BR>भक्त्युपहृत Bg. 9. 26;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-c" target="_blank">Page0335-c+ 56</a>]<BR>फलमिश्रमर्घमुपहर Ś. 1; तमस्योपहर Ś. 7; so बलिं,<BR>अन्नं &c.<BR>--2 To offer, present, give<BR>(with dat. or gen.); तथापि<BR>राजपरिग्रहोऽस्य प्रभुत्वमुपहरति M. 1 invests<BR>with importance; मातृभ्यो बलिमुपहर<BR>Mk. 1; नीवारभागधेयमस्माकमुपहरंतु Ś. 2;<BR>दर्भान् ऋत्विग्भ्य उपहरामि Ś. 3;<BR>Mv. 6. 22; K. 40, 65; R. 14. 19, 16. 86,<BR>19. 12; उपहर पादं M. 3 give.<BR>--3 To serve<BR>out or distribute (food).<BR>--4 To<BR>offer as a victim, sacrifice;<BR>प्रागुपयाचितं स्त्रीरत्नमुपहर्तव्यं Māl. 5;<BR>मालतीमुपहरन् 9.<BR>--5 To put down, throw.<BR>--6 To collect, gather together.<BR>--7<BR>To take away, destroy.<BR>--8 To<BR>employ, apply, use. --Caus. To<BR>cause to offer or bring; मां<BR>प्रियाण्युपहारय Bk. 8. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहरणं|उपहरण
उपहरणं<BR>1 Bringing near,<BR>fetching.<BR>--2 Taking, seizing.<BR>--3<BR>Offering gifts to superiors, deities &c.<BR>--4 Offering victims.<BR>--5 Serving<BR>out food or distributing it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारः|उपहार
उपहारः<BR>1 An oblation.<BR>--2 A gift,<BR>present (in general);<BR>रत्नपुष्पोपहारेण छायामानर्च पादयोः R. 4. 84;<BR>नृत्योपहारः Me. 32; K. 17, 41, 130, 183.<BR>--3 A victim, sacrifice, an offering<BR>to a deity; सपर्यां सपशूपहारां R. 16. 39;<BR>Māl. 1; उपहारीकृतास्मि Māl. 2;<BR>Ve. 4. 7.<BR>--4 A complimentary gift,<BR>present to a superior &c.<BR>--5 (a)<BR>Offering of flowers &c., flowery gifts;<BR>collection of flowers; म्लानपुष्पोपहारः<BR>R. 5. 74; Ku. 6. 42. (b) Presents<BR>(to gods) of flowers &c., materials<BR>of worship; V. 3; Śi. 11. 36.<BR>--6<BR>Honour.<BR>--7 Indemnity, presents<BR>given as the price of peace;<BR>H. 4. 110.<BR>--8 Food distributed to<BR>guests.<BR>--9 Exultation, mirth<BR>(consisting of laughter, dance, singing<BR>&c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहारिन्
उपहारिन् a.<BR>1 Giving, presenting,<BR>bringing on; परिभवोपहारिणः M. 5.<BR>--2 Sacrificing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहृत
उपहृत p. p.<BR>1 Offered, presented.<BR>--2 Immolated, offered as a victim.<BR>--3 Served out (as food).<BR>--4<BR>Taken, collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहोमः|उपहोम
उपहोमः A supplementary<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वरः|उपह्वर|उपह्वरं
उपह्वरः<BR>1 A solitary or lonely<BR>place, privacy; उपह्वरे पुनरित्यशिक्षयं<BR>धनमित्रं Dk. 54 in secret.<BR>--2<BR>Proximity.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Ved. Bend, curve,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">Page0336-a+ 55</a>]<BR>slope<BR>--2 Declivity.<BR>--3 The curved<BR>form of the Soma vessel.<BR>--4 A car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0335-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वे
उपह्वे^1 {c1c} A. (P. also)<BR>1 To invoke,<BR>call near to (in a liturgical sense);<BR>(with acc., dat. or loc.); तामिहोपह्वये<BR>श्रियं.<BR>--2 To call; त्वयोपहूतः U. 5. 8;<BR>Śi. 7. 58.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: ap90 gives ह्वे, आह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहवः|उपहव
उपहवः<BR>1 Calling to, invitation.<BR>--2 Summoning, invoking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहव्यः|उपहव्य
उपहव्यः A kind of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपहूतिः|उपहूति
उपहूतिः f. Calling, inviting;<BR>Śi. 14. 30; 17. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपह्वानं|उपह्वान
उपह्वानं<BR>1 Calling, inviting.<BR>--2<BR>Invoking with prayers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांशु|उपांशुः
उपांशु ind.<BR>1 In a low voice or<BR>whisper.<BR>--2 Secretly, in secret<BR>or private; परिचेतुमुपांशु धारणां<BR>R. 8. 18; ˚व्रतं a vow observed in<BR>secret; ˚वधमाकलय्य Mu. 2;<BR>Śi. 13. 54.<BR>--शुः<BR>1 A prayer uttered in a<BR>low voice, muttering of prayers:<BR>जिह्वोष्ठौ चालयेत् किंचित् देवतागतमानसः ।<BR>निजश्रवणयोग्यः स्यादुपांशुः स जपः स्मृतः ॥;<BR>Ms. 2. 85.<BR>--2 Hence, silence itself.<BR>--3 N. of a Soma offering.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्रीडित a. made the companion of<BR>(a king's) private amusements.<BR>--याजः a kind of sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाक
उपाक a. Ved. Joined together,<BR>near.<BR>--के (du.) An epithet of<BR>night and morning. --ind. In the<BR>immediate neighbourhood, before or<BR>in the presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृ
उपाकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To fetch, bring<BR>near; तेभ्य इमं बलिमुपाकरोति Āśval.<BR>--2 To summon, invite.<BR>--3 To<BR>deliver. offer, grant, bestow, give<BR>(to another); गोसहस्रमुपाकुरु Rām.<BR>--4 To acquire, obtain (as fame).<BR>--5 To bring about, make<BR>preparations for a sacred rite; perform a<BR>rite; Ms. 4. 95, 5. 7; Y. 1. 171.<BR>--6 To undertake, begin, enter upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकरणं|उपाकरण
उपाकरणं<BR>1 An invitation to<BR>begin, bringing near; पवमान˚,<BR>प्रातरनुवाक˚ &c.<BR>--2 A term given to<BR>certain sentences called Praiṣas<BR>(with which one priest calls<BR>another to perform a sacrifice).<BR>--3<BR>Immolation, sacrifice of an animal<BR>consecrated according to rites.<BR>--4<BR>Preparation, beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--5 Commencement of<BR>reading the Veda after the performance<BR>of the preparatory rite; cf. उपाकर्मन्;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">Page0336-b+ 55</a>]<BR>वेदोपाकरणाख्यं कर्म करिष्ये<BR>Śrāvaṇī Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकर्मन्|उपाकर्म्मन्
उपाकर्मन् n.<BR>1 Preparation,<BR>beginning, commencement; अध्याय˚.<BR>--2<BR>A ceremony performed before<BR>commencing to read the Veda after<BR>the monsoons (cf. श्रावणी);<BR>अध्यायानामुपाकर्म श्रावण्यां श्रवणेन वा । हस्तेनौषधिभावे<BR>वा पचम्यां श्रावणस्य तु ॥ Y. 1. 142;<BR>Ms. 4. 119.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाकृत|उपाकृतं|उपाकृतः
उपाकृत p. p.<BR>1 Brought near.<BR>--2<BR>invited, called with प्रैष sentences.<BR>--3 Killed at a sacrifice (an animal).<BR>--4 Begun, commenced.<BR>--5<BR>Ominous, disastrous, calamitous.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A sacrificial animal killed<BR>during the recitation of prescribed<BR>prayers.<BR>--2 A misfortune, portent.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Beginning, commencement.<BR>--2 The performance of the usual<BR>rites (संस्कार) over the sacrificial<BR>animal.<BR>--3 Invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाक्षं|उपाक्ष
उपाक्षं ind. [अक्ष्णोः समीपं] Before<BR>the eyes, in the presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्या
उपाख्या {c2c} P. To tell, narrate,<BR>relate, give an account of (with<BR>acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्या
उपाख्या<BR>1 Observing with one's<BR>own eyes; P. VI. 3. 80 (उपाख्यायते<BR>प्रत्यक्षत उपलभ्यते).<BR>--2 Describing in<BR>words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यानं|उपाख्यान
उपाख्यानं, --नकं<BR>1 A short tale or<BR>narrative, an episode; उपाख्यानैर्विना<BR>तावत् भारतं प्रोच्यते बुधैः Mb.<BR>--2<BR>Repetition of a story already heard<BR>from others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाख्यानकं|उपाख्यानक
उपाख्यानं, --नकं<BR>1 A short tale or<BR>narrative, an episode; उपाख्यानैर्विना<BR>तावत् भारतं प्रोच्यते बुधैः Mb.<BR>--2<BR>Repetition of a story already heard<BR>from others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागम्
उपागम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To come, approach,<BR>go or draw near (a person or place).<BR>--2 (a) To go to, go to the state of;<BR>पंचत्वमुपागतः or परां तृप्तिमुपागतः; so<BR>क्रोधं, मोहं, क्षयं &c. (b) To undergo,<BR>suffer, endure.<BR>--3 To obtain, get;<BR>दायादुपागतो दासः Mit.; Y. 2. 143.<BR>--4 To occur, fall to the lot of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागत
उपागत p. p.<BR>1 Come, approached;<BR>तपोधनं वेत्सि न मामुपागतं Ś. 4. v. l.<BR>--2 Occurred, happened.<BR>--3<BR>Promised.<BR>--4 Suffering, feeling, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपागमः|उपागम
उपागमः<BR>1 Approach, arrival.<BR>--2<BR>Occurrence.<BR>--3 A promise,<BR>agreement.<BR>--4 Acceptance.<BR>--5 Suffering,<BR>feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रं|उपाग्र
उपाग्रं<BR>1 The part next to the<BR>end or top.<BR>--2 A secondary<BR>member.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाग्रहणं|उपाग्रहण
उपाग्रहणं Reading the Vedas<BR>after being initiated to them.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांगः|उपाङ्ग|उपांग|उपाङ्गः
उपांगः A mark of sandal on the<BR>forehead.<BR>--गं<BR>1 A subdivision, a<BR>subhead.<BR>--2 Any minor limb or<BR>member (of anything); वर्गाः…<BR>सांगोपांगैरिहोदिताः Ak.<BR>--3 A<BR>supplement of a supplement.<BR>--4 A<BR>supplementary work (of inferior<BR>value).<BR>--5 A secondary portion of<BR>science; a class of writings<BR>supplementary to the Vedāṅgas; (these<BR>are four: --पुराणन्यायमीमांसाधर्मशास्त्राणि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचर्
उपाचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To approach.<BR>--2<BR>To attend or wait upon, serve, be<BR>attached to.<BR>--3 To be obedient or<BR>humble.<BR>--4 To treat (in medic.<BR>also); ज्वरान् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचरित|उपाचरितः
उपाचरित p. p. Attached to any<BR>one's service, obedient.<BR>--तः (In<BR>gram.) That rule of Saṃdhi by<BR>which the sound Visarga becomes<BR>स् before क् and प्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाचारः|उपाचार
उपाचारः<BR>1 Position(of a word in<BR>a sentence).<BR>--2 Procedure.<BR>--3<BR>Same as उपाचरित q. v. above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाजे
उपाजे ind. (Used only with<BR>the root कृ) Supporting;<BR>उपाजेकृत्य or कृत्वा having supported;<BR>P. I. 4. 73 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांजनं|उपाञ्जन|उपांजन
उपांजनं Anointing, plastering<BR>the ground with cow-dung,<BR>chunam &c.; Ms. 5. 105, 122, 124; (<BR>मठादेः सुधागोमयादिना संमार्जनानुलेपनं<BR>Medhātithi).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्ययः|उपात्यय
उपात्ययः<BR>1 Transgression of,<BR>deviation from, established customs.<BR>--2 Disorderly conduct, rudeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादा
उपादा {c3c} A. (p. p. उपात्त)<BR>1 To<BR>receive, accept, take.<BR>--2 To acquire,<BR>obtain; भूर्या पितामहोपात्ता निबंधो<BR>द्रव्यमेव च Y. 2. 121.<BR>--3 To give to,<BR>furnish with; Ku. 7. 41.<BR>--4 To<BR>take, appropriate to oneself, assume;<BR>Śi. 6. 23.<BR>--5 To take away or off,<BR>carry away; steal.<BR>--6 To seize,<BR>attack; Pt. 3. 154.<BR>--7 To take, lay<BR>hold of; R. 9. 54; to draw (water).<BR>--8 To assume a form<BR>--9 To feel,<BR>perceive, experience; उपात्तहर्षैः<BR>पुंस्कोकिलैः Rs. 6. 21.<BR>--10 To consider,<BR>regard.<BR>--11 To take in addition,<BR>include, comprise; अत्र<BR>तैलशब्दस्तिलभवस्नेहरूपमुख्यार्थमुपादाय सार्षपादिरनेहंषु<BR>वर्तते S. D. 2.<BR>--12 To employ, apply,<BR>use; यत्परस्य कुत्सार्थमुपादीयते Mbh.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-a" target="_blank">Page0337-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--13 To undertake, begin; as in<BR>उपात्तयज्ञः.<BR>--14 To mention,<BR>enumerate; इति पूर्वसूत्रोपात्तानां Sk. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to use, apply or employ.<BR>--2 To make use of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0336-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपात्त|उपात्तं|उपात्तः
उपात्त p. p.<BR>1 Got, received,<BR>acquired, obtained; ˚विद्यः R. 5. 1;<BR>जन्मांतर˚ K. 96, 166, 334, 346.<BR>--2 Appropriated.<BR>--3 Taken away,<BR>seized.<BR>--4 Felt, perceived, regarded.<BR>--5 Employed, used; Ku. 7. 20.<BR>--6<BR>Comprised.<BR>--7 Begun,<BR>commenced.<BR>--8 Mentioned.<BR>--9 Allowed in<BR>argument, granted, conceded.<BR>--त्तः<BR>An elephant out of rut.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रंहस् a. speedy, quick, fleet.<BR>--वर्ण<BR>a. celebrated in song; Ku. 5. 56.<BR>--शस्त्र a. taking up arms, armed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादानं|उपादान
उपादानं<BR>1 Taking, receiving,<BR>acquisition, obtaining; विश्रब्धं ब्राह्म<BR>णः शूद्रात् द्रव्योपादानमाचरेत्<BR>Ms. 8 417; 12. 7; विद्या˚ K. 75.<BR>--2<BR>Taking away, appropriating to<BR>oneself.<BR>--3 Employment, using;<BR>becoming familiar with.<BR>--4<BR>Mention, enumeration.<BR>--5 Saying,<BR>speaking.<BR>--6 Including, containing.<BR>--7<BR>Withdrawing the organs of sense<BR>and perception from the external<BR>world and its objects.<BR>--8 A cause,<BR>motive, natural or immediate cause;<BR>पाटवोपादानः भ्रमः U. 3 v. l.;<BR>प्रकृष्टपुण्यपरिपाकोपादानो महिमा स्यात् U. 6.<BR>--9<BR>The material out of which<BR>anything is made, the material cause;<BR>निमित्तमेव ब्रह्म स्यादुपादानं च वेक्षणात्<BR>Adhikaraṇamālā..<BR>--10 A mode of<BR>expression in which a word used<BR>elliptically, besides retaining its<BR>own primary sense, conveys<BR>another (in addition to that<BR>which is actually expressed);<BR>स्वसिद्धये पराक्षेपः… उपादानं K. P. 2.<BR>--11<BR>(With Buddhists) Conception.<BR>--12 Effort of body or speech.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारणं a material cause;<BR>प्रकृतिश्चोपादानकारणं च ब्रह्माभ्युपगंतव्यं<BR>Ś. B.<BR>--लक्षणा = अजहत्स्वार्था q. v.; see<BR>K. P. 2; S. D. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादेय|उपादेयः
उपादेय pot. p.<BR>1 Capable of<BR>being taken.<BR>--2 Capable of being<BR>endured; Māl. 10.<BR>--3 Acceptable,<BR>admissible.<BR>--4 To be chosen or<BR>selected.<BR>--5 Excellent, admirable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपादिकः|उपादिक
उपादिकः A sort of insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधा
उपाधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To place<BR>near or upon.<BR>--2 To offer, give,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-b" target="_blank">Page0337-b+ 56</a>]<BR>impart.<BR>--3 To put on, wear.<BR>--4 To<BR>create, cause, produce;<BR>कोपोपाहितबाष्प Bh. 3. 85; Gīt. 10.<BR>--5 To<BR>render, make, effect.<BR>--6 To keep,<BR>hold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधिः|उपाधि
उपाधिः<BR>1 Fraud, deceit, trick.<BR>--2<BR>Deception, disguise (in Vedānta).<BR>--3 Discriminative or distinguishing<BR>property, attribute, peculiarity;<BR>तदुपाधावेव संकेतः K. P. 2. It is of four<BR>kinds: --जाति, गुण, क्रिया, संज्ञा.<BR>--4 A<BR>title, nick-name; (भट्टाचार्य,<BR>महामहोपाध्याय, पंडित &c.); बी. ए. इत्युपाधिधारिणः<BR>(modern use).<BR>--5 Limitation,<BR>condition (as of time, space &c.);<BR>अनुपाधिरमणीयो देशः Prab. a country<BR>altogether (or naturally) beautiful;<BR>(oft. occurring in Vedānta phil.);<BR>देहाद्युपाधिरचितो भेदः Ś. B.;<BR>U. 6. 12; Māl. 1. 24.<BR>--6 A trace,<BR>mark; भौमा उपाधयः Mv. 7. 22.<BR>--7<BR>A purpose, occasion, object.<BR>--8 (In<BR>logic) A special cause for a<BR>general effect; साध्यव्यापकत्वे सति<BR>साधनाव्यापक उपाधिः; as आर्द्रेधनं (wet fuel) is<BR>the उपाधि of the hetu वह्निमत्त्व in the<BR>inference पर्वतो धूमवान् वह्नेः.<BR>--9<BR>Reflection on duty or a virtuous<BR>reflection.<BR>--10 A man who is careful<BR>to support his family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाधिक
उपाधिक a. Exceeding,<BR>supernumerary, additional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहित|उपाहितः
उपाहित p. p.<BR>1 Deposited, placed.<BR>--2 Put on, worn.<BR>--3 Connected,<BR>joined; ˚श्यामरुचश्च चंदनाः Ki. 8. 12<BR>showing.<BR>--4 Ascribed or attributed<BR>to (आरोपित).<BR>--5 Agreed upon,<BR>done by mutual agreement.<BR>--तः A fiery portent, danger or<BR>destruction from fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्यायः|उपाध्याय
उपाध्यायः [उपेत्याधीयते अस्मात्,<BR>उप-अधि-इ-घञ्]<BR>1 A teacher or<BR>preceptor in general.<BR>--2 Particularly,<BR>a spiritual teacher, religious<BR>preceptor; (by Y. 1. 35, a sub-teacher<BR>who instructs for wages only in<BR>a part of the Veda and is inferior<BR>to an आचार्य; एकदेशमुपाध्यायः); cf.<BR>Ms. 2. 141;<BR>--एकदेशं तु वेदरय<BR>वेदांगान्यपि वा पुनः । योऽध्यापयति वृत्त्यर्थमुपाध्यायः<BR>स उच्यते ॥ see अध्यापक and under<BR>आचार्य also.<BR>--या A female<BR>preceptor.<BR>--यी<BR>1 A female preceptor.<BR>--2 The wife of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाध्यायानी
उपाध्यायानी The wife of a<BR>preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानस्
उपानस् a. [उपगतमनः शकटं पितरं<BR>वा]<BR>1 Like a cart, being in a cart.<BR>--2 Like a father (uncle &c). --n.<BR>1<BR>The space in a carriage.<BR>--2<BR>Anything placed in a carriage,<BR>carriageload.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपानह्
उपानह् f. [उप-नह्-क्विप् उपसर्गदीर्घ]<BR>A sandal, shoe; उपानद्गूढपादस्य सर्बा<BR>चर्मवृतेव भूः H. 1. 142; Ms. 2. 246; श्वा<BR>यदि क्रियते राजा स किं नाश्नात्युपानहं<BR>H. 3. 58; cf. ‘What is bred in the<BR>bones cannot go out of flesh’, or<BR>‘Habit is second nature’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांत|उपान्त|उपान्तः
उपांत a. Near to the end, last<BR>but one.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Border, edge,<BR>margin, skirt, point (of anything);<BR>उपांतयोर्निष्कुषितं विहगैंः R. 7. 50<BR>Ku. 3. 69, 7. 32; Amaru. 23;<BR>U. 1. 26; वल्कल˚ K. 136.<BR>--2 The<BR>corner or angle of the eye; विलोचने<BR>तिर्यगुपांतलोहिते Ku. 5. 74;<BR>नयनोपांतविलोकितं च यत् 4. 23; R. 3. 26.<BR>--3 Immediate proximity, vicinity;<BR>तयोरुपांतस्थितसिद्धसैनिकं R. 3. 57,<BR>7. 24, 16. 21; Me. 24.<BR>--4 Side or<BR>slope (नितंब); Me. 18.<BR>--5 The last<BR>letter but one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांतिक|उपान्तिक
उपांतिक a. Near, proximate,<BR>neighbouring.<BR>--कं Vicinity, proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांतिम
उपांतिम a. Proximate, near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपांत्य|उपान्त्य|उपान्त्यः
उपांत्य a. Last but one;<BR>उत्तमपदमुपांत्यस्योपलक्षणार्थम् Sk.<BR>--त्यः The<BR>corner of the eye.<BR>--त्यं Vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाप्तिः|उपाप्ति
उपाप्तिः f.<BR>1 Reaching to.<BR>--2<BR>Obtaining, getting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाभृत्
उपाभृत् f. Bringing near or<BR>taking away (उपाहरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायः|उपाय
उपायः, उपायन See under उपे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायन|उपायनं
उपायः, उपायन See under उपे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायात
उपायात a. Approached, come<BR>near.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Arrival.<BR>--2 An event,<BR>incident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारः|उपार
उपारः [उप-ऋ-कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Proximity.<BR>--2 A mistake, offence, sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारम्
उपारम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sport, amuse<BR>oneself, delight in.<BR>--2 To cease,<BR>desist (from); दानप्रवृत्तेरनुपारतानां<BR>R. 16. 3; Ku. 3. 58; to rest, come<BR>to a stand-still; वातवर्षमुपारतं Rām.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारत
उपारत p. p.<BR>1 Delighted.<BR>--2<BR>Returned; Ki. 4. 10.<BR>--3 Engaged in,<BR>occupied with.<BR>--4 Frequenting,<BR>resorting to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारंभः|उपारम्भ|उपारंभ|उपारम्भः
उपारंभः Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0337-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपारूढ
उपारूढ a. Grown, increased,<BR>attaied to; ˚यौवन attained to majority;<BR>˚स्नेह K. 173 whose affection has<BR>increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्ज्
उपार्ज् {c1c} P. To bring near to<BR>--Caus. To gain, earn, acquire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्जक
उपार्जक a. Acquiring, earning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्जनं|उपार्जन|उपार्ज्जन|उपार्ज्जनं
उपार्जनं, --ना Acquiring, gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्जना
उपार्जनं, --ना Acquiring, gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपार्थ
उपार्थ a. Of little worth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालभ्
उपालभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To censure,<BR>blame, revile, scold, taunt;<BR>पयोधरविस्तारयितृकमात्मनो यौवनमुपालभस्व<BR>मां किमुपालभसे Ś. 1; रहस्युपालभ्यत<BR>चंद्रशेखरः Ku. 5. 58; R. 7. 44;<BR>Śi. 9. 60; Bk. 3. 30, 6. 125.<BR>--2 To<BR>obtain (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालंभः|उपालम्भ|उपालंभ|उपालम्भः
उपालंभः, --भनं<BR>1 Abuse, taunt,<BR>censure; अस्या महदुपालंभनं गतोस्मि<BR>Ś. 5; तवोपालंभे पतितास्मि M. 1 laid<BR>myself open to your censure;<BR>उचितस्तदुपालंभः U. 3.<BR>--2 Delaying,<BR>putting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपालंभनं|उपालम्भन|उपालंभन
उपालंभः, --भनं<BR>1 Abuse, taunt,<BR>censure; अस्या महदुपालंभनं गतोस्मि<BR>Ś. 5; तवोपालंभे पतितास्मि M. 1 laid<BR>myself open to your censure;<BR>उचितस्तदुपालंभः U. 3.<BR>--2 Delaying,<BR>putting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावसायिन्
उपावसायिन् a. Ved.<BR>Submissive, compliant, obedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावसु
उपावसु a. Ved. Bringing or<BR>granting wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावहरणं|उपावहरण
उपावहरणं Bringing down,<BR>taking down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत्
उपावृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To turn or go<BR>towards, approach.<BR>--2 To turn away<BR>from, return.<BR>--3 To give. --Caus.<BR>1 To win over, induce; Māl. 8.<BR>--2 To cause to turn; lead or bring<BR>back; M. 5.<BR>--3 To give to.<BR>--4 To<BR>cause, produce.<BR>--5 To stretch out<BR>more and more.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावर्तनं|उपावर्तन|उपावर्त्तन
उपावर्तनं<BR>1 Coming or turning<BR>back, return; त्वदुपावर्तनशंकि मे मनः<BR>(करोति) R. 8. 53.<BR>--2 Revolving,<BR>turning round.<BR>--3 Approaching.<BR>--4 Ceasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत्
उपावृत् f. Ved. Return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपावृत्त|उपावृत्तः
उपावृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Returned, come,<BR>arrived.<BR>--2 Ceased, refraining.<BR>--3<BR>Fit, proper.<BR>--4 Turned round;<BR>rolling or wallowing on the ground.<BR>--त्तः A horse rolling on the ground<BR>(to remove his fatigue).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाव्याधः|उपाव्याध
उपाव्याधः A vulnerable or<BR>unprotected place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाशंसनीय
उपाशंसनीय a. To be expected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रि
उपाश्रि {c1c} U. To have recourse to,<BR>resort to; Śi. 8. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रयः|उपाश्रय
उपाश्रयः<BR>1 Recourse(for aid),<BR>asylum, support; Bh. 2. 48;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-b" target="_blank">Page0338-b+ 55</a>]<BR>पर्यंकस्योपाश्रये K. 186 resting-place.<BR>--2<BR>Receptacle, recipient; Ki. 13. 40.<BR>--3<BR>Reliance, dependence upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाश्रित
उपाश्रित a.<BR>1 Relying or<BR>depending upon.<BR>--2 Supporting (fig. also),<BR>bearing, holding, protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्
उपास् {c2c} A.<BR>1 To sit near to (with<BR>acc.), sit at the side of (as a mark of<BR>submission and respect); wait upon,<BR>serve, worship;<BR>उद्यानपालसामान्यमृतवस्तमुपासते Ku. 2. 36;<BR>अंबामुपास्स्व सदयां Aśvad. 13; Śi. 16. 47;<BR>Ms. 3. 189.<BR>--2 To use, occupy,<BR>abide in, reside; Ms. 5. 93.<BR>--3<BR>To pass (as time); उपास्य रात्रिशेषं तु<BR>Rām.<BR>--4 To approach, go to or<BR>towards; उपासांचक्रिरे द्रष्टुं<BR>देवगंधर्वकिन्नराः Bk. 5. 107; परलोकमुपास्महे<BR>7. 89.<BR>--5 To invest or blockade (as<BR>an enemy's town).<BR>--6 To be<BR>intent upon, be engaged in, take part<BR>in, (perform as a sacred rite);<BR>उपास्य पश्चिमां संध्यां K. 176, 179;<BR>तेप्युपासंतु मे मखं Mb.; Ms. 2. 222,<BR>3. 104, 7. 223, 11. 42.<BR>--7 To<BR>undergo, suffer; अलं ते पांडुपुत्राणां भक्त्या<BR>क्लंशमुपासितुं Mb.; Ms. 11. 184.<BR>--8<BR>To remain or continue in any state<BR>or action; oft. with a pres. p.;<BR>Bg. 12. 6.<BR>--9 To expect, wait for;<BR>दिष्टमुपासीनः Mb.<BR>--10 To attach<BR>oneself to, practise; Y. 3. 192.<BR>--11<BR>To resort to, employ, apply, use;<BR>लक्षणोपास्यते यस्य कृते S. D. 2;<BR>वस्तिरुपास्यमानः Suśr.<BR>--12 To respect,<BR>recognize, acknowledge.<BR>--13 To<BR>practise archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासकः|उपासक
उपासकः<BR>1 One who waits upon,<BR>a worshipper.<BR>--2 A servant,<BR>follower.<BR>--3 A Śūdra, a low fellow.<BR>--4 A worshipper of Buddha as<BR>distinguished from the Bhikṣu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासनं|उपासन
उपासनं, --ना<BR>1 Service, serving,<BR>attendance, waiting upon; शीलं<BR>खलोपासनात् (विनश्यति); उपासनमित्य<BR>पितुः स्म सृज्यते N. 1. 34; Pt. 1. 169;<BR>Ms. 3. 107; Bg. 13. 7; Y. 3. 156;<BR>Bh. 2. 42.<BR>--2 Engaging in, being<BR>intent on, performing; संगीत˚<BR>Mk. 6; Ms. 2. 69.<BR>--3 Worship, respect,<BR>adoration.<BR>--4 Practice of archery.<BR>--5 Regarding as, reflecting upon.<BR>--6 Religious meditation.<BR>--7 The<BR>sacred fire; Y. 3. 45.<BR>--8 Injuring<BR>hurting; (fr. अस् 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासना
उपासनं, --ना<BR>1 Service, serving,<BR>attendance, waiting upon; शीलं<BR>खलोपासनात् (विनश्यति); उपासनमित्य<BR>पितुः स्म सृज्यते N. 1. 34; Pt. 1. 169;<BR>Ms. 3. 107; Bg. 13. 7; Y. 3. 156;<BR>Bh. 2. 42.<BR>--2 Engaging in, being<BR>intent on, performing; संगीत˚<BR>Mk. 6; Ms. 2. 69.<BR>--3 Worship, respect,<BR>adoration.<BR>--4 Practice of archery.<BR>--5 Regarding as, reflecting upon.<BR>--6 Religious meditation.<BR>--7 The<BR>sacred fire; Y. 3. 45.<BR>--8 Injuring<BR>hurting; (fr. अस् 2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासा
उपासा<BR>1 Service, attendance.<BR>--2<BR>Worship, adoration.<BR>--3 Religious<BR>meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासितृ
उपासितृ a. A worshipper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्तिः|उपास्ति
उपास्तिः f.<BR>1 Service, attendance<BR>upon (especially a deity).<BR>--2<BR>Worship, adoration;<BR>स्वर्गापवर्गयोर्मार्गमामनंति मनीषिणः । यदुपास्तिमसावत्र<BR>परमात्मा निरूप्यते ॥ Kusum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्य
उपास्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be served<BR>or worshipped.<BR>--2 To be performed<BR>or accomplished.<BR>--3 To be<BR>respected; ˚ता, --त्वं respectability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपासंगः|उपासङ्ग|उपासंग|उपासङ्गः
उपासंगः<BR>1 Proximity, vicinity.<BR>--2 A quiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्तमनं|उपास्तमन
उपास्तमनं Sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्तमयं
उपास्तमयं ind. About sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपास्त्रं|उपास्त्र
उपास्त्रं A secondary or minor<BR>weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहृ
उपाहृ {c1c} U.<BR>1 To offer, give.<BR>--2<BR>To cause, produce; स्पर्शसुखं K. 124.<BR>--3 To make, prepare.<BR>--4 To seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपाहारः|उपाहार
उपाहारः Slight refreshment (fruits,<BR>sweetmeats &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपे
उपे {c2c} P. [उप-इ]<BR>1 To approach,<BR>come near, arrive at, reach (a place,<BR>person &c.); लतामुपेत्य Ś. 1; so राजानं,<BR>दुर्गं &c. योगी परं स्थानमुपैति चाद्यं<BR>Bg. 8. 28, 10, 15, 9. 28.<BR>--2 To go to (a<BR>master), become a pupil.<BR>--3 To<BR>have intercourse with (a woman),<BR>cohabit; Ms. 9. 4.<BR>--4 To undergo,<BR>perform, undertake, practise; तपः,<BR>सत्रं &c.<BR>--5 To go to or pass into<BR>any state; योगं R. 16. 84; भेदं<BR>Ku. 2. 4; to fall into (misfortune &c.);<BR>क्षयं, मृत्युं, सुखं, दुःखं, निद्रां &c.<BR>--6 To<BR>obtain, attain to; उपैति शस्यं<BR>परिणामरम्यतां Ki. 4. 22.<BR>--7 To incur, be<BR>present at.<BR>--8 To fall to one's lot or<BR>share, befall; उद्योगिनं पुरुषसिंहमुपैति<BR>लक्ष्मीः Pt. 1. 361; Bg. 6. 27.<BR>--9 To<BR>consider as, admit, acknowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायः|उपाय
उपायः<BR>1 (a) Means, an expedient,<BR>remedy; उपायं चिंतयेत्प्राज्ञस्तथापायं<BR>च चिंतयेत् Pt. 1. 406; Amaru. 21;<BR>Ms. 8. 48, 7. 177. (b) A plan,<BR>contrivance; ˚निलया Mu. 1. 5. (c)<BR>A mode, way, stratagem.<BR>--2 A fact,<BR>circumstance; U. 7.<BR>--3 Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--4 Effort, exertion;<BR>Bg. 6. 36; Ms. 9. 248; 10. 2.<BR>--5<BR>A means of success against an<BR>enemy; (these are four:<BR>--सामन्<BR>conciliation or negotiation, दानं bribery;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">Page0339-a+ 57</a>]<BR>भदः sowing dissensions; and दंडः<BR>punishment, open attack; some<BR>authorities add three more:<BR>--माया<BR>deceit; उपेक्षा trick, deceit or<BR>neglect; इंद्रजाल conjuring; thus making<BR>the total number {7});<BR>चतुर्थोपायसाध्ये तु रिपौ सांत्त्रमपक्रिया Śi. 2. 54;<BR>सामादीनामुपायानां चतुर्णामपि पंडिताः<BR>Ms. 7. 109.<BR>--6 Joining (as in<BR>singing).<BR>--7 Approach.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चतुष्टयं the four expedients against<BR>an enemy; see above (5).<BR>--चिंता<BR>devising an expedient or scheme.<BR>--ज्ञ a. fertile in expedients.<BR>--तुरीयः<BR>the 4th expedient, i. e. दंड or<BR>punishment.<BR>--योगः application of<BR>means or remedy; Ms. 9. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0338-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायनं|उपायन
उपायनं<BR>1 Going near, approach.<BR>--2 Becoming a pupil of.<BR>--3<BR>Engaging in any religious rite.<BR>--4<BR>Undertaking, beginning; व्रत˚.<BR>--5 A<BR>present, gift; मालविकोपायनं प्रेषिता<BR>M. 1; तस्योपायनयोग्यानि वस्तूनि<BR>सरितां पतिः Ku. 2. 37; R. 4. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायिक
उपायिक a. Conducive to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायिन्
उपायिन् a.<BR>1 Skilled in the use<BR>of means, having means.<BR>--2<BR>Approaching.<BR>--3 Having sexual<BR>intercourse with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपायु
उपायु a. Ved. Approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेत
उपेत p. p.<BR>1 Come near,<BR>approached, arrived at.<BR>--2 Present.<BR>--3 Endowed with, possessed of,<BR>having; with instr. or in comp.;<BR>पुत्रमेवंगुणोपेतं चक्रवर्तिनमाप्नुहि<BR>Ś. 1. 12.<BR>--4 Blockaded.<BR>--5 Fallen into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेतिः|उपेति
उपेतिः f. Arrival, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेतृ
उपेतृ a.<BR>1 Approaching near to.<BR>--2 Contriving, one who uses<BR>expedients.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेय|उपेयः
उपेय pot. p.<BR>1 To be gone to or<BR>approached.<BR>--2 To be effected by<BR>means; ˚उपायदर्शने M. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Assailable.<BR>--4 To be sought.<BR>--5 To<BR>be obtained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्ष्
उपेक्ष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To neglect,<BR>overlook, disregard, connive at;<BR>किमात्मनिर्वादकथामुपेक्षे R. 14. 34; उपेक्षते यः<BR>श्लथलंबिनीर्जटाः Ku. 5. 47.<BR>--2<BR>To let escape or let go; नोपेक्षेत<BR>क्षणमपि राजा साहसिकं नरं Ms. 8. 344.<BR>--3 To quit, abandon.<BR>--4 To despise,<BR>slight.<BR>--5 To notice, consider, have<BR>regard to; एवमुच्चावच नर्थान् प्राहुः ते<BR>उपेक्षितव्याः Nir.<BR>--6 To look at,<BR>regard, perceive; प्रासादरथा ह्युपैक्षत<BR>Nala. 22. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षक
उपेक्षक a.<BR>1 Disregarding,<BR>neglecting.<BR>--2 Patient, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षणं|उपेक्षण
उपेक्षणं = उपेक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेक्षा
उपेक्षा<BR>1 Overlooking, disregard,<BR>neglect.<BR>--2 Indifference, contempt,<BR>disdain; कुर्यामुपेक्षां हतजीवितेऽस्मिन्<BR>R. 14. 65.<BR>--3 Leaving, quitting.<BR>--4 Endurance, patience.<BR>--5 Dissent.<BR>--6 Neglect, trick or deceit (one of<BR>the 7 expedients in war).<BR>--7 A<BR>sort of भावना in Yoga, q. v.<BR>--8<BR>Regard, consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेनित
उपेनित a. Driven or pressed in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपेंद्रः|उपेन्द्र|उपेंद्र|उपेन्द्रः
उपेंद्रः [उपगत इंद्रं अनुज-वात्] N. of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa as the younger<BR>brother of Indra in his 5th or dwarf<BR>incarnation; see इंद्र; उपेंद्रवज्रादपि<BR>दारुणोऽसि Gīt. 5; यदुपेंद्रस्त्वमतींद्र एव सः<BR>Śi. 16. 70.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वज्रा f. N. of<BR>a metre; see App.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढ|उपोढः
उपोढ See under उपवह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोती
उपोती = उपोदिका q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोत्तम
उपोत्तम a. Last but one.<BR>--मं<BR>(अक्षरं) The last letter but one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोदक|उपोदकः
उपोदक a. Near water.<BR>--कः<BR>Proximity of water.<BR>--कं ind.<BR>Near water.<BR>--का, --दिका, --दीका The<BR>plant Basella Rubra (पूतिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्ग्रहः|उपोद्ग्रह
उपोद्ग्रहः Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्घातः|उपोद्घात
उपोद्घातः<BR>1 A beginning,<BR>commencement<BR>--2 An introduction,<BR>a preface.<BR>--3 An example, an apposite<BR>argument or illustration.<BR>--4 An<BR>occasion, medium, means;<BR>तत्प्रतिच्छंदकमुपोद्घातेन माधवांतिकमुपेयात् Māl. 1.<BR>--5<BR>Analysis, ascertaining the elements<BR>of anything.<BR>--6 Alluding to,<BR>mentioning; Mu. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्बलयति
उपोद्बलयति Den. P. To<BR>confirm, strengthen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्बलक
उपोद्बलक a. Confirming; तस्य<BR>पक्षस्योपोद्बलकानि Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोद्बलनं|उपोद्बलन
उपोद्बलनं Confirmation,<BR>corroboration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषणं|उपोषण
उपोषणं, उपोषितं A fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोषितं|उपोषित|उपोषितः
उपोषणं, उपोषितं A fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोह्
उपोह् {c1c} P. (उप-उह्)<BR>1 To propel,<BR>push or impel towards; उपोह्य रुचिरां<BR>नावं Rām.; so धनुः.<BR>--2 To push under,<BR>insert, कूर्चावधस्तादुपोह्य Kātyāyana.<BR>--3 To bring near, produce:<BR>connected with उपवह् in this sense;<BR>q. v.<BR>--4 To accumulate, collect.<BR>--pass.<BR>1 To be brought about.<BR>--2 To advance, begin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोढ|उपोढः
उपोढ p. p.<BR>1 Brought near.<BR>--2<BR>Advanced, begun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उपोहः|उपोह
उपोहः Ved. Adding,<BR>accumulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उप्त|उप्तः
उप्त See under वप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उब्ज्
उब्ज् {c6c} P. (उब्जति, उब्जांचकार,<BR>औब्जीत्, उब्जित)<BR>1 To press down,<BR>subdue, keep under or check.<BR>--2 To<BR>make straight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ्
उभ्, उंभ् {c6c} {c9c} {c7c} P. (उभति or<BR>उंभति, उभ्नाति, उनप्ति, उंभित)<BR>1 To confine.<BR>--2<BR>To compact together.<BR>--3 To fill<BR>with; जलकुंभमुंभितरसं सपदि सरस्याः<BR>समानयंत्यास्ते Bv. 2. 144.<BR>--4 To cover or<BR>overspread with; सर्वमर्मसु<BR>काकुत्स्थमौंभत्तीक्ष्णैः शिलीमुखैः Bk. 17. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंभ्|उम्भ्
उभ्, उंभ् {c6c} {c9c} {c7c} P. (उभति or<BR>उंभति, उभ्नाति, उनप्ति, उंभित)<BR>1 To confine.<BR>--2<BR>To compact together.<BR>--3 To fill<BR>with; जलकुंभमुंभितरसं सपदि सरस्याः<BR>समानयंत्यास्ते Bv. 2. 144.<BR>--4 To cover or<BR>overspread with; सर्वमर्मसु<BR>काकुत्स्थमौंभत्तीक्ष्णैः शिलीमुखैः Bk. 17. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभ
उभ pron. a. (Used only in the<BR>dual) Both उभौ तौ न विजानीतः<BR>Bg. 2. 19; Ku. 4. 43; Ms. 2. 14;<BR>Śi. 3. 8. [cf Zend. uba; Gr. amphi; L.<BR>ambo].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभय|उभयं|उभयः
उभय pron. a. (यी f.) (Though<BR>dual in sense, it is used in the<BR>singular and plural only; according to<BR>some grammarians in the dual also)<BR>Both (of persons or things);<BR>उभयमप्यपरितोषं समर्थये Ś. 7;<BR>उभयमानशिरे वसुधाधिपाः R. 9. 9; उभयीं<BR>सिद्धिमुभाववापतुः 8. 23, 17. 38;<BR>Amaru. 60; Ku. 7. 78; Ms. 2. 55,<BR>4. 224; 9. 34.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थं ind. for a<BR>double object (for earthly<BR>prosperity and heavenly happiness also).<BR>--आत्मक a. belonging to both.<BR>--चर a. living in water and on<BR>land or in the air, amphibious.<BR>--(रः) a class of birds who<BR>live both on land and in the air.<BR>--द्युः ind. {1} on both days. {2} the<BR>day past and to come.<BR>--भागहर a.<BR>{1} applicable to two objects. {2}<BR>taking two shares.<BR>--(रं) a<BR>medicine that acts in two ways (both<BR>as an emetic and a purgative).<BR>--विद्या two fold sciences; i. e.<BR>religious knowledge and knowledge<BR>about worldly affairs.<BR>--विध a.<BR>of both kinds.<BR>--वेतन a. receiving<BR>wages from both (parties), serving<BR>two masters, treacherous, perfidious;<BR>उभयवेतनो भूत्वा Pt. 1; Śi. 2. 113.<BR>--व्यंजन a. having the marks of both<BR>sexes.<BR>--संभवः a dilemma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयतः|उभयत
उभयतः ind.<BR>1 From both sides,<BR>on both sides, to both sides<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">Page0340-a+ 55</a>]<BR>(with acc.); उभयतः कृष्णं गोपाः Sk.<BR>तज्जः पुनात्युभयतः पुरुषानेकविंशतिं<BR>Y. 1. 58; Ms. 8. 315.<BR>--2 In both<BR>cases.<BR>--3 In both ways; Ms. 1. 47.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्षुत् a. two-edged (Ved.).<BR>--दत्, --दंत a. having a double row<BR>of teeth; पशून् मृगान् मनुष्यांश्च<BR>व्यालांश्चोभयतोदतः Ms. 1. 43.<BR>--मुख a. {1}<BR>looking either way. {2} two-faced<BR>(as a house &c).<BR>--(खी) a cow;<BR>Y. 1. 206-7<BR>--ह्रस्व a. (an accented<BR>vowel) produced by two short vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0339-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयत्र
उभयत्र ind.<BR>1 In both places.<BR>--2<BR>On both sides; ˚उदात्त having an<BR>Udātta accent on both sides.<BR>--3 In<BR>both cases; Ms. 3. 125, 167.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयथा
उभयथा ind.<BR>1 In both ways;<BR>उभयथापि घटते V. 3.<BR>--2 In both cases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभया
उभया ind. Ved. In both ways.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दत् a. having teeth on<BR>both sides.<BR>--विन् a. being on both<BR>sides, partaking of both.<BR>--हस्ति<BR>ind. as much as may be grasped<BR>with both hands.<BR>--हस्त्य a. filling<BR>both hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयीय
उभयीय a. Belonging to both.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयेद्युस्
उभये(य)द्युस् ind.<BR>1 On both<BR>days.<BR>--2 On two subsequent days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उभयद्युस्
उभये(य)द्युस् ind.<BR>1 On both<BR>days.<BR>--2 On two subsequent days.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्
उम् ind. An interjection of(1)<BR>anger; (2) interrogation; (3) promise<BR>or assent; (4) cordiality or<BR>pacification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमः|उम
उमः<BR>1 A town.<BR>--2 A wharf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उमा
उमा [ओः शिवस्य मा लक्ष्मीरिव, उं शिवं<BR>माति मन्यते पतित्वेन मा-क वा Tv.]<BR>1 N. of<BR>the daughter of Himavat and Menā<BR>and wife of Śiva; Kālidāsa thus<BR>derives the name:<BR>--उ मेति (oh<BR>do not, scil. practise penance)<BR>मात्रा तपसो निषिद्धा पश्चादुमाख्यां सुमुखी<BR>जगाम Ku. 1. 26; उमावृषांकौ<BR>R. 3. 23.<BR>--2 Light, splendour.<BR>--3 Fame,<BR>reputation.<BR>--4 Tranquility, calmness.<BR>--5 Night.<BR>--6 Turmeric (हरिद्रा).<BR>--7<BR>Flax (अतसी).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कटः, --टं<BR>the pollen of flax.<BR>--गुरुः, --जनकः<BR>N. of the Himālaya (as the father<BR>of उमा).<BR>--पतिः N. of Śiva;<BR>मुहुरनुस्मरयंतमनुक्षपं त्रिपुरदाहमुमापतिसेविनः<BR>Ki. 5. 14; so ˚ईश, ˚वल्लभः, ˚सहायः<BR>&c.<BR>--वनं N. of the town Vanapura<BR>or Devīkoṭa (शोणितपुर).<BR>--सुतः N.<BR>of Kārtikeya or of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उम्यं|उम्य
उम्यं A field of linseed or of<BR>Curcuma (उमायाः क्षेत्रं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंबरः|उम्बर|उंबर|उम्बरः
उंब(बु)रः The upper timber of<BR>a door-frame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंबुरः|उम्बुर|उंबुर|उम्बुरः
उंब(बु)रः The upper timber of<BR>a door-frame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उंबी|उम्बी
उंबी f. The stalks of wheat or<BR>barley fried over a fire of wet grass<BR>(considered as a tonic); मंजरी<BR>त्वर्धपक्वा या यवगोधूमयोर्भवेत् । तृणानलेन संप्लुष्टा<BR>बुधैरुंबीति सा स्मृता ॥ Bhāva P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्
उर् To go (a Sautra root).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर|उरः
उर a. Going (Ved.).<BR>--रः A<BR>sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगः|उरग
उरगः (गी f.) [उरसा गच्छति,<BR>उरस्-गम्-ड; सलोपश्च P. III. 2. 48<BR>Vārt.]<BR>1 A serpent, snake;<BR>अंगुलीवोरगक्षता R. 1. 28, 12. 5, 91.<BR>--2 A<BR>Nāga or semi-divine serpent<BR>usually represented in mythology with a<BR>human face; देवगंधर्वमानुषोरगराक्षसान्<BR>Nala. 1. 28; Ms. 3. 196.<BR>--3 Lead.<BR>--गा N. of a city; R. 6. 59.<BR>--गी<BR>A female snake.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः,<BR>--अशनः, --शत्रुः {1} N. of Garuḍa<BR>(enemy of snakes). {2} a pea-cock.<BR>--आस्यं a kind of spade<BR>(serpentshaped hoe).<BR>--इंद्रः, --राजः N. of<BR>Vāsuki or Śeṣa.<BR>--प्रतिसर a.<BR>having a serpent for a wedding-ring.<BR>--भूषणः N. of Śiva (decked with<BR>serpents).<BR>--सारचंदनः, --नं a kind<BR>of sandal-wood.<BR>--स्थानं the abode<BR>of the Nāgas, i. e. Pātāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरगी
उरगः (गी f.) [उरसा गच्छति,<BR>उरस्-गम्-ड; सलोपश्च P. III. 2. 48<BR>Vārt.]<BR>1 A serpent, snake;<BR>अंगुलीवोरगक्षता R. 1. 28, 12. 5, 91.<BR>--2 A<BR>Nāga or semi-divine serpent<BR>usually represented in mythology with a<BR>human face; देवगंधर्वमानुषोरगराक्षसान्<BR>Nala. 1. 28; Ms. 3. 196.<BR>--3 Lead.<BR>--गा N. of a city; R. 6. 59.<BR>--गी<BR>A female snake.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः,<BR>--अशनः, --शत्रुः {1} N. of Garuḍa<BR>(enemy of snakes). {2} a pea-cock.<BR>--आस्यं a kind of spade<BR>(serpentshaped hoe).<BR>--इंद्रः, --राजः N. of<BR>Vāsuki or Śeṣa.<BR>--प्रतिसर a.<BR>having a serpent for a wedding-ring.<BR>--भूषणः N. of Śiva (decked with<BR>serpents).<BR>--सारचंदनः, --नं a kind<BR>of sandal-wood.<BR>--स्थानं the abode<BR>of the Nāgas, i. e. Pātāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरंगः|उरङ्ग|उरंग|उरङ्गः
उरंगः, --गमः A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरंगमः|उरङ्गम|उरङ्गमः
उरंगः, --गमः A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरणः|उरण
उरणः [cf. Uṇ. 5. 17.] (णी f.)<BR>1 A ram, sheep; वृकीवोरणमासाद्य<BR>मृत्युरादाय गच्छति Mb.<BR>--2 A certain<BR>demon killed by Indra.<BR>--णी A ewe.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः, --क्षकः, --आख्यः the<BR>plant Cassia Alata or Tora.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरणकः|उरणक
उरणकः<BR>1 A ram.<BR>--2 A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरभ्रः|उरभ्र
उरभ्रः<BR>1 A ram; देवि पश्याम<BR>उरभ्रसंवादं किं मुधा वेतनदानेन M. 1.<BR>--2 The<BR>plant Cassia Alata.<BR>--3 A kind of<BR>poisonous insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररी
उररी ind. A particle<BR>implying (1) assent, admission or<BR>acceptance. (In this sense it is usually<BR>used with the roots कृ, भू, or अस्, and<BR>it has the force of a गति or<BR>preposition; उररीकृत्य not उररीकृत्वा. Other<BR>forms of the word are उरी, उरुरी, ऊरी<BR>and ऊरुरी); (2) extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररीकृ
उररीकृ {c8c} U. To consent, allow,<BR>accept; गिरं न कां कामुररीचकार<BR>Bv. 2. 13; M. 5; Dk. 12; Śi. 10. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररीकारः|उररीकार
उररीकारः Promise, agreement,<BR>admission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उररीकृत|उररीकृतः
उररीकृत p. p.<BR>1 Promised, agreed,<BR>accepted.<BR>--2 Spread, extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरल
उरल a. Moving (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरशः|उरश
उरशः N. of a country inhabited<BR>by a warrior tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्
उरस् a. Best, excellent. --n.<BR>(उरः) The breast, bosom; व्यूढोरस्को<BR>वृषस्कंधः R. 1. 13; Ku. 6. 51; उरसि<BR>कृ to clasp to the bosom.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कटः {1} the sacrificial thread hung<BR>round the neck and upon the<BR>breast. {2} an upper garment (for<BR>boys).<BR>--क्षतं injury to the chest.<BR>--गामिन् a. going on the breast (as<BR>a reptile), creeping, crawling.<BR>--ग्रहः, --घातः a disease of the chest,<BR>pleurisy.<BR>--छदः, --त्राणं a cuirass,<BR>breast-plate; Śi. 15. 80.<BR>--जः,<BR>--भूः, --उरसिजः, --उरसिरुहः the<BR>female breast; रेजाते<BR>रुचिरदृशामुरोजकुंभौ Śi. 8. 53, 25, 59.<BR>--भूषणं an<BR>ornament of the breast.<BR>--सूत्रिका<BR>a necklace of pearls hanging over<BR>the breast.<BR>--स्थलं the breast,<BR>bosom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरसिलोमन्
उरसिलोमन् a. Having hair on the<BR>breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्तस्
उरस्तस् ind. From the breast,<BR>towards the bosom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्वत्|उरस्वन्त्
उरस्वत्, उरसिल a. Broad-chested,<BR>full-breasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरसिल|उरसिलः
उरस्वत्, उरसिल a. Broad-chested,<BR>full-breasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्य|उरस्यः
उरस्य a. [उरस्-यत्]<BR>1 Being in<BR>the breast.<BR>--2 Pectoral.<BR>--3<BR>Requiring an effort of the chest (as<BR>any exertion).<BR>--4 Legitimate (a son<BR>or daughter); born from a married<BR>couple of the same tribe or caste.<BR>--5 Excellent.<BR>--स्यः A son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरस्यति
उरस्यति Den. P. To be strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरा
उरा Ved. A ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उराहः|उराह
उराहः A horse of a pale<BR>colour with dark legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरी
उरी A particle of assent; see<BR>उररी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरीकृ
उरीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To allow, admit,<BR>accept; दक्षेणोरीकृतं त्वया Bk. 8. 11;<BR>R. 15. 70.<BR>--2 To follow, have<BR>recourse to; अयि रोषमुरीकरोषि नो चेत्<BR>Bv. 1. 44, 1. 12, 2. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरीकार
उरीकार = उररीकारः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरु|उरुः
उरु a. [ऊर्णु-कु नुलोपो ह्रस्वश्च<BR>Uṇ. 1. 31] (रु-र्वी f.; compar. वरीयस्;<BR>super. वरिष्ठ)<BR>1 Wide, spacious.<BR>--2<BR>Great, large; R. 6. 74.<BR>--3 Exces<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-a" target="_blank">Page0341-a+ 56</a>]<BR>sive, much, abundant; धनान्युरूणि<BR>Śi. 3. 76.<BR>--4 Excellent, precious,<BR>valuable. --n. Ved. Wide space, space<BR>or room. --ind. Far, far off (Ved.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः {1} a mountain. {2} the<BR>ocean.<BR>--कालः, --कालकः the creeper<BR>Cucumis Colocynthis.<BR>--कीर्ति a.<BR>renowned, well-known; R. 14. 74.<BR>--कृत् a. making room, granting space.<BR>--क्रम a. Ved. {1} taking wide strides.<BR>{2} of high rank.<BR>--(मः) an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu in the dwarf<BR>incarnation.<BR>--क्षय a. having spacious<BR>dwellings.<BR>--(यः) a spacious dwelling.<BR>--क्षितिः f. Ved. a spacious dwelling.<BR>--गाय a. {1} sung or praised by the<BR>great; Aśvad. 16. {2} offering wide<BR>scope for movement.<BR>--(यः) {1} N.<BR>of Viṣṇu, the Aśvins, Soma and<BR>Indra. {2} wide space or scope (--यं<BR>also). {3} praise.<BR>--चक्रि a. granting<BR>ample assistance, or allowing<BR>unrestrained motion.<BR>--चक्षुस् a. Ved.<BR>far-seeing.<BR>--जन्मन् a. nobly born;<BR>M. 5. 17.<BR>--ज्मन् a. having a wide<BR>path or range.<BR>--ज्रयस्, --ज्रि a. of<BR>great speed, of mighty impetus.<BR>--तापः great heat.<BR>--धार a. Ved.<BR>giving a broad stream (of milk, as a cow).<BR>--प्रथस् a. wide-spreading, far-spread.<BR>--मार्गः a long road.<BR>--लोक a.<BR>widely illuminating; or widely<BR>extended.<BR>--(कः) the best world.<BR>--(कं) the<BR>intermediate region between earth<BR>and heaven.<BR>--विक्रम a. valiant,<BR>mighty.<BR>--व्यचस् a. widely<BR>extended, extensive. (--m.) a malignant<BR>spirit, an imp.<BR>--व्यंच् a. Ved. {1}<BR>far-reaching, capacious. {2}<BR>perceived in a distant place (as a sound).<BR>--शंस a. {1} to be praised by many. {2}<BR>reigning over a wide region. {3}<BR>praising aloud.<BR>--शर्मन् a. Ved. widely<BR>pervading.<BR>--षा a. granting much, or<BR>granting wide or free scope.<BR>--सत्त्व<BR>a. of mighty or great strength,<BR>powerful; R. 2. 33; magnanimous, of a<BR>noble nature.<BR>--स्वन a. having a<BR>loud voice, stentorian.<BR>--हारः a<BR>valuable necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0340-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुता
उरुता, --त्वं Greatness, magnitude,<BR>vastness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुत्वं|उरुत्व
उरुता, --त्वं Greatness, magnitude,<BR>vastness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुवुः|उरुवु
उरुवुः, --वुकः, --वूकः The plant<BR>Ricinus Communis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुवुकः|उरुवुक
उरुवुः, --वुकः, --वूकः The plant<BR>Ricinus Communis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुवूकः|उरुवूक
उरुवुः, --वुकः, --वूकः The plant<BR>Ricinus Communis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुष्यति
उरुष्यति Den. P.<BR>1 To protect,<BR>guard, defend.<BR>--2 To desire wide<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">Page0341-b+ 53</a>]<BR>scope or freedom.<BR>--3 To escape<BR>from (with acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुष्या
उरुष्या A desire to protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुष्यु
उरुष्यु a. Desirous of protecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरूल
उरूल a.<BR>1 Liking space.<BR>--2 Fond<BR>of expatiating.<BR>--3 Free,<BR>unrestrained, self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्विया
उर्विया ind. Far, far off, far and<BR>near; widely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वी|उर्व्वी
उर्वी<BR>1 ‘Wide region’, the earth;<BR>स्तोकमुर्व्यां प्रयाति Ś. 1. 7; जुगोप<BR>गोरूपधरामिवोर्वीं R. 2. 3, 1. 14, 30, 75,<BR>2. 66; Me. 21.<BR>--2 Land, soil.<BR>--3 The<BR>open space or expanse (comprising<BR>six spaces; i. e. the four quarters<BR>of the sky with the upper and<BR>lower spaces).<BR>--4 A river.<BR>--5 (du.)<BR>Ved. the two worlds, or the<BR>heaven and earth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः,<BR>--ईश्वरः, --पतिः, --धवः a king.<BR>--धरः {1}<BR>a mountain. {2} the serpent Śeṣa.<BR>--भृत् m. {1} a king. {2} a<BR>mountain.<BR>--रुहः a tree; Śi. 4. 7, 5. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्या
उर्व्या<BR>1 Greatness.<BR>--2 Protection,<BR>security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्यूति
उर्व्यूति a.<BR>1 Yielding great<BR>protection.<BR>--2 Able to help far and<BR>near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरुरी
उरुरी = उररी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उरूकः|उरूक
उरूकः = उलूकः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्ज्
उर्ज् {c1c} {c10c} P. To leave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्जित|उर्ज्जित|उर्ज्जितं
उर्जित p. p.<BR>1 Aged, strong,<BR>powerful.<BR>--2 Abandoned, left.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्णनाभः|उर्णनाभ|उर्ण्णनाभ
उर्णनाभः A spider; cf. ऊर्णनाभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्णा
उर्णा<BR>1 Wool, felt.<BR>--2 A circle<BR>of hair between the eye-brows;<BR>see ऊर्णा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्द्
उर्द् {c1c} A. (उर्दते, उर्दित)<BR>1 To<BR>taste.<BR>--2 To give, grant.<BR>--3 To<BR>play.<BR>--4 To measure.<BR>--5 To be easy<BR>or cheerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्द्रः|उर्द्र
उर्द्रः An otter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्व्
उर्व् {c1c} P. (उर्वति, और्वीत्, उर्वित) To<BR>kill or hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वटः|उर्वट|उर्व्वट|उर्व्वटः
उर्वटः<BR>1 A calf.<BR>--2 A year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वरा|उर्व्वरा
उर्वरा [उरु शस्यादिकमृच्छति, ऋ-अच्]<BR>1 Fertile soil (yielding every kind<BR>of crop); पततां गणैः पिबतु सार्धमुर्वरा<BR>Śi. 15. 66.<BR>--2 Land in general.<BR>--3<BR>A mixed mass of fibres, wool &c.<BR>--4 A humorous term for curled hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वरित|उर्व्वरित
उर्वरित a.<BR>1 Much, excessive.<BR>--2<BR>Remaining after; भुक्त˚ Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वर्य
उर्वर्य a. [उर्वरायां भवः यत्]<BR>Belonging to a field sown with corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वरी
उर्वरी<BR>1 A superior woman.<BR>--2<BR>Tow, fibres drawn out of the<BR>distaff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वशी|उर्व्वशी
उर्वशी [उरून् महतोपि अश्नुते<BR>वशीकरोति, उरु-अश्-क गौरा˚ ङीष् Tv.]<BR>1 N. of<BR>a famous Apsaras or nymph of<BR>Indra's heaven who became the wife of<BR>Purūravas. [Urvaśī is frequently<BR>mentioned in the Ṛgveda; at her sight<BR>the seed of Mitra and Varuṇa fell down,<BR>from which arose Agastya and Vasiṣṭha;<BR>(see Agastya). Being cursed by Mitra<BR>and Varuṇa she came down to the world<BR>of mortals, and became the wife<BR>of Purūravas, whom she chanced to see<BR>while descending, and who made a very<BR>favourable impression upon her mind.<BR>She lived with him for some time, and<BR>went up to heaven at the expiration of<BR>her curse. Purūravas was sorely<BR>grievved at her loss, but succeeded in<BR>securing her company once more. She bore<BR>him a son named Āyus, and then left<BR>him for ever. The account given in the<BR>Vikramorvaśīyam differs in many<BR>respects, where Indra is represented to<BR>have favoured Purūravas with her<BR>lifelong company though he had himself<BR>cursed her. Mythologically she is said<BR>to have sprung from the thigh of the<BR>sage Nārāyaṇa, q. v.].<BR>--2 Wish,<BR>ardent desire.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तीर्थं N. of a<BR>sacred place referred to in Bhārata.<BR>--रमणः, --सहायः, --वल्लभः N. of<BR>Purūravas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वारुः|उर्वारु|उर्व्वारु|उर्व्वारुः
उर्वारुः A kind of cucumber; see<BR>इर्वारु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उर्वारुकं|उर्वारुक
उर्वारुकं The fruit of the above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्
उल् (A Sautra root) To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलः|उल
उलः A kind of wild animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलपः|उलप
उलपः<BR>1 A creeping plant, a<BR>spreading creeper.<BR>--2 Soft grass (<BR>कोमलं तृणं), the grass or reed<BR>Saccharum, Cylindricum;<BR>गोगर्भिणीप्रियनवोलपमालभारिसेव्योपकंठविपिनावलयो<BR>भवंति Māl. 9. 2; Ki. 10. 3; Śi. 4. 8.<BR>--3 A shrub or bush; a wick (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलप्य|उलप्यः
उलप्य a. Belonging to this grass.<BR>--प्यः N. of Rudra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलिंदः|उलिन्द|उलिन्दः
उलिंदः<BR>1 N. of a country.<BR>--2<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुप|उलुपः
उलुप = उलपः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुपिन्
उलुपिन् m. A guinea-pig,<BR>porpoise; so उल (-लू)-पिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलुलिः|उलुलि
उलुलिः Ved. Howling, a howl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूकः|उलूक|उलूकं
उलूकः<BR>1 An owl;<BR>नोलूकोप्यवलोकते यदि दिवा सूर्यस्य किं दूषणं Bh. 2. 93<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">Page0342-a+ 59</a>]<BR>त्यजति मुदमुलूकः प्रीतिमांश्चक्रवाकः<BR>Śi. 11. 64.<BR>--2 N. of Indra.<BR>--3 (pl.)<BR>N. of a country and its king<BR>who was an ally of the Kurus.<BR>--कं N. of the reed Saccharum<BR>Cylindricum; see उलप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0341-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखलः|उलूखल|उलूखलं
उलूखलः A staff of<BR>Udumbara wood.<BR>--लं A wooden mortar<BR>used for cleansing rice (from the<BR>husk &c.); अवहननायोलूखलं Mbh.;<BR>वनस्पतिभ्य इत्येवं मुषलोलूखले हरेत्<BR>Ms. 3. 88, 5. 117.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सुतः<BR>the Soma juice pressed out in a<BR>(wooden) mortar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखलकं|उलूखलक
उलूखलकं<BR>1 A mortar.<BR>--2<BR>Bdellium, a gummy substance or the<BR>plant which yields it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूखलिक
उलूखलिक a.<BR>1 Pounded in a<BR>mortar.<BR>--2 (At the end of comp.)<BR>Using as a mortar; दंत˚ using the<BR>teeth as a mortar; Ms. 6. 17; Y. 3. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूतः|उलूत
उलूतः A large snake, the Boa<BR>(अजगर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूप
उलूप, --पिन् See उलप, उलुपिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूपिन्
उलूप, --पिन् See उलप, उलुपिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उलूपी
उलूपी A Nāga princess. [She was<BR>the daughter of the serpent Kauravya.<BR>While one day she was bathing in the<BR>Ganges, she happened to see Arjuna,<BR>and being enamoured of his handsome<BR>form, she managed to have him<BR>conveyed to her home, the Pātāla, and there<BR>induced him to take her as his wife, which<BR>he, after considerable hesitation,<BR>consented to do. She bore him a son named<BR>Irāvat. When Arjuna's head was cut<BR>off by Babhruvāhana's arrow, it was with<BR>her assistance that he was restored to<BR>life; see Arjuna].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्का
उल्का (cf. Uṇ. 3. 42)<BR>1 A fiery<BR>phenomenon in the sky, a meteor;<BR>विरराज काचन समं महोल्कया<BR>Śi. 15. 92; Ms. 1. 38, 4. 103; Y. 1. 145.<BR>--2 A fire-brand, torch; न हि<BR>तापयितुं शक्यं सागरांभस्तृणोल्कया H. 1. 86.<BR>--3 Fire, flame; Me. 53.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धारिन् a. a torch-bearer.<BR>--पातः the<BR>fall of a meteor.<BR>--मालिन् m. N. of one<BR>of Śiva's attendants.<BR>--मुखः a<BR>demon or goblin (having a mouth of<BR>fire); Ms. 12. 71; Māl. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्कुषी
उल्कुषी<BR>1 A meteor.<BR>--2 A<BR>firebrand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्बं|उल्ब
उल्बं, --ल्वं<BR>1 The bag which<BR>surrounds the embryo, fœtus.<BR>--2 The<BR>vulva.<BR>--3 The womb.<BR>--4 A cave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्वं|उल्व
उल्बं, --ल्वं<BR>1 The bag which<BR>surrounds the embryo, fœtus.<BR>--2 The<BR>vulva.<BR>--3 The womb.<BR>--4 A cave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ब्यं|उल्ब्य
उल्ब्यं<BR>1 Excess and vitiation of<BR>any one of the three humours of<BR>the body; i. e. phlegm, bile, or wind<BR>(त्रिदोष).<BR>--2 Any calamity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्मुकः|उल्मुक|उल्मुकं
उल्मुकः A firebrand, torch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्बण|उल्बणः
उल्ब(ल्व)ण a.<BR>1 Thick,<BR>clotted, copious, abundant (blood &c.);<BR>˚रुधिरं Mv. 6. 33.<BR>--2 Much,<BR>excessive, intense; Śi. 10. 54, 68,<BR>12. 37; Ku. 7. 84.<BR>--3 Strong,<BR>powerful, great; Śi. 20. 41; ˚रसः<BR>U. 5. 26 the heroic sentiment; Dk. 23,<BR>25; K. 299, 302.<BR>--4 Manifest, clear;<BR>तस्यासीदुल्बणो मार्गः R. 4. 33.<BR>--5 Gaudy,<BR>showy; अनुल्बणवेषेण K. 66.<BR>--णं ind.<BR>Much, heavily (as sighing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्वण|उल्वणं
उल्ब(ल्व)ण a.<BR>1 Thick,<BR>clotted, copious, abundant (blood &c.);<BR>˚रुधिरं Mv. 6. 33.<BR>--2 Much,<BR>excessive, intense; Śi. 10. 54, 68,<BR>12. 37; Ku. 7. 84.<BR>--3 Strong,<BR>powerful, great; Śi. 20. 41; ˚रसः<BR>U. 5. 26 the heroic sentiment; Dk. 23,<BR>25; K. 299, 302.<BR>--4 Manifest, clear;<BR>तस्यासीदुल्बणो मार्गः R. 4. 33.<BR>--5 Gaudy,<BR>showy; अनुल्बणवेषेण K. 66.<BR>--णं ind.<BR>Much, heavily (as sighing).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लकसनं|उल्लकसन
उल्लकसनं Horripilation,<BR>erection of the hair of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लंघ्|उल्लङ्घ्
उल्लंघ् {c1c} A., {c10c} P.<BR>1 To leap over,<BR>pass over or beyond; उल्लंघ्योच्चैः<BR>कुचतटभुवं Śi. 7. 74, 12. 77.<BR>--2 To<BR>transgress, violate, disregard, exceed;<BR>Śi. 12. 57; Mu. 1. 10; गौरवमुल्लंघयिष्यति<BR>Mu. 4; K. 160; Śi. 3. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लंघनं|उल्लङ्घन|उल्लंघन|उल्लङ्घनं
उल्लंघनं<BR>1 Leaping or passing over.<BR>--2 Transgression, violation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लंघित|उल्लङ्घित
उल्लंघित p. p.<BR>1 Jumped over or<BR>across, passed over or beyond;<BR>˚अध्वन्.<BR>--2 Transgressed, violated;<BR>˚शासन disobedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लंबित|उल्लम्बित
उल्लंबित a. Erected, elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लल|उल्ललः
उल्लल a.<BR>1 Shaking, tremulous.<BR>--2 Covered with thick hair, shaggy<BR>--3 Affected by many diseases.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ललत्
उल्ललत् a.<BR>1 Shaking, trembling.<BR>--2 Moving irregularly or<BR>convulsively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ललित|उल्ललितः
उल्ललित p. p.<BR>1 Shaken,<BR>trembling, agitated.<BR>--2 Raised up,<BR>elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्ललयति
उल्ललयति Den. P. To jump, spring<BR>(shake the body up); तावत्खरः<BR>प्रखरमुल्ललयांचकार Śi. 5. 7; Pt. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लस्
उल्लस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To jump up, sport,<BR>play, wave, flutter;<BR>उल्लसितासितपताकासहस्रं K. 96; Śi. 5. 47, 53.<BR>--2<BR>To flash, shine, glitter, sparkle;<BR>उल्लसत्कांचनकुंडलाग्रं Śi. 3. 5, 33,<BR>5. 55; 16. 61; 20. 56; (fig.) to<BR>brighten or cheer up; K. 189.<BR>--3<BR>To rise, appear forth; Śi. 4. 58,<BR>6. 51, 16. 51; Māl. 9. 38.<BR>--4<BR>To be reflected; Śi. 11. 54.<BR>--5 To blow. open, be expanded.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to jump up or<BR>play.<BR>--2 To brighten, illuminate,<BR>grace; Ve. 1. 12; U. 4.<BR>--3 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">Page0342-c+ 55</a>]<BR>divert, delight.<BR>--4 To shake, move<BR>K. 22; Ki. 16. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लस
उल्लस a.<BR>1 Bright, shining.<BR>--2<BR>Merry, happy.<BR>--3 Going out,<BR>issuing, appearing; ˚ता splendour,<BR>brilliancy; mirth, happiness, issuing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसनं|उल्लसन
उल्लसनं<BR>1 Happiness, joy.<BR>--2<BR>Horripilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लसित
उल्लसित p. p.<BR>1 Shining, brilliant,<BR>splendid.<BR>--2 Happy, delighted.<BR>--3<BR>Drawn up, uplifted, brandishing<BR>(as a sword).<BR>--4 Gleaming,<BR>fluttering: ˚हरिणकेतनः रथः V. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लासः|उल्लास
उल्लासः<BR>1 Joy, delight; सोल्लासं<BR>U. 6; सकौतुकोल्लासं U. 2; उल्लासः<BR>फुल्लपंकेरुहपटलपतन्मत्तपुष्पंधयानां S. D.<BR>--2<BR>Light, splendour.<BR>--3 (In Rhet.) A<BR>figure of speech in which a<BR>reference is made to the merits<BR>or demerits of one thing by<BR>comparing or contrasting the merits or<BR>demerits of another;<BR>अन्यदीयगुणदोषप्रयुक्तमन्यस्य गुणदोषयोराधानमुल्लासः R. G.;<BR>for examples, see R. G. ad loc.; cf.<BR>Chandr. 5. 131-133.<BR>--4 A division of<BR>a book, such as chapter, section &c.;<BR>as the ten Ullāsas of the<BR>Kāvyaprakāśa.<BR>--5 Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लासन
उल्लासन a. Causing to leap or<BR>dance.<BR>--नं Splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लासित
उल्लासित a. Delighted, rejoicing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लासिन्
उल्लासिन् a.<BR>1 Delighted.<BR>--2 Bright,<BR>splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाघ|उल्लाघः
उल्लाघ a.<BR>1 Recovered from<BR>sickness, convalescent.<BR>--2 Dextrous,<BR>clever, skilful.<BR>--3 Pure.<BR>--4 Happy,<BR>delighted.<BR>--5 Wicked.<BR>--6 Black.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लप्
उल्लप् {c1c} P. To remove, allay;<BR>दीर्घदारुणमपि संतापं झटित्युल्लपता U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लापः|उल्लाप
उल्लापः<BR>1 Speech, words; श्रुता<BR>मयार्यपुत्रस्योल्लापाः U. 3.<BR>--2 Insulting<BR>words, taunting speech, taunt;<BR>खलोल्लापाः सोढाः Bh. 3. 6.<BR>--3 Calling out<BR>in a loud voice.<BR>--4 Change of voice<BR>by emotion, sickness &c.<BR>--5 A hint,<BR>suggestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लापिक|उल्लापिकः
उल्लापिक a. Betraying, indicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लापिन्
उल्लापिन् a. Calling out;<BR>indicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लाप्यं|उल्लाप्य
उल्लाप्यं A kind of drama; see<BR>S. D. 545.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिख्
उल्लिख् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To scratch, cut up,<BR>scrape, tear or rip up, scarify;<BR>जलदसंहतिमुल्लिखंत्यः Śi. 5. 20; K. 30; to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">Page0343-a+ 54</a>]<BR>furrow (as ground); Mv. 1. 20.<BR>--2 To rub or grind against;<BR>विषाणोल्लिखितस्कंधं H. 3. 146; K. 14.<BR>--3<BR>To grind down; polish;<BR>संस्कारोल्लिखितो महामणिः Ś. 6. 5; R. 6. 32;<BR>त्वष्टा विवस्वतमिवोल्लिलेख Ki. 17. 48.<BR>--4 To carve.<BR>--5 To paint, write,<BR>draw in a picture; Ku. 5. 58.<BR>--6<BR>To bear, raise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0342-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिखित|उल्लिखितः
उल्लिखित p. p.<BR>1 Scratched,<BR>scraped &c.<BR>--2 Thrown up, tossed.<BR>--3<BR>Written over or above.<BR>--4 Pared,<BR>made thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेखः|उल्लेख
उल्लेखः<BR>1 Allusion, mention.<BR>--2<BR>Description, utterance,<BR>pronunciation.<BR>--3 Boring or digging out.<BR>--4<BR>(In Rhetoric) A figure of speech<BR>in which an object is described<BR>according to the different impressions<BR>caused by its appearance;<BR>बहुभिर्बहुधोल्लेखोदकस्योल्लेख इष्यते । स्त्रीभिः<BR>कामोऽर्थिभिः स्वर्द्रुः कालः शत्रुभिरौक्षि सः<BR>Chandr. 5. 19; cf. S. D. 682.<BR>--5<BR>Rubbing, scratching, tearing up;<BR>खुरमुखोल्लेख K. 191; कुट्टिम˚ 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेखनं|उल्लेखन
उल्लेखनं<BR>1 Rubbing, scratching,<BR>scraping &c.<BR>--2 Digging up;<BR>Y. 1. 188; Ms. 5. 124.<BR>--3 Vomiting.<BR>--4<BR>Mention, allusion, utterance.<BR>--5<BR>Raising up, elevating.<BR>--6 Writing,<BR>painting.<BR>--7 Marking out by lines<BR>(the स्थंडिल &c. in a sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लेखिन्
उल्लेखिन् a. Tearing; K. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लिंगित|उल्लिङ्गित
उल्लिंगित a. Famous, known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लीढ
उल्लीढ a. Rubbed, polished;<BR>मणिः शाणोल्लीढः Bh. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लुंचनं|उल्लुञ्चन|उल्लुंचन
उल्लुंचनं<BR>1 Plucking out,<BR>cutting; पादकेशांशुककरोल्लुंचनेषु पणान् दश<BR>(दमः); Y. 2. 217.<BR>--2 Plucking or<BR>pulling out the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लुंठनं|उल्लुण्ठन
उल्लुंठनं^1, उल्लुंठा Irony; धीराधीरातु<BR>सोल्लुंठभाषणैः खेदयेदमुं S. D. 105; सोल्लुंठं<BR>ironically, often occurring as a<BR>stage-direction in plays.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: Alph. order,  AP,  quote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लुंठा|उल्लुण्ठा
उल्लुंठनं^1, उल्लुंठा Irony; धीराधीरातु<BR>सोल्लुंठभाषणैः खेदयेदमुं S. D. 105; सोल्लुंठं<BR>ironically, often occurring as a<BR>stage-direction in plays.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: Alph. order,  AP,  quote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लुंठित
उल्लुंठित a. Rubbed against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लू
उल्लू a. Cutting up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लोचः|उल्लोच
उल्लोचः A canopy, an awning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उल्लोल|उल्लोलः
उल्लोल a. Violently moving,<BR>excessively tremulous; ˚स्खलित<BR>Māl. 5. 3; ˚कल्लोल K. 302 high or<BR>surging; Mv. 5. 2; लोल˚ violently<BR>agitated or exercised; U. 3. 36.<BR>--लः A large wave or surge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0343-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

