ऐकान्यिकः|ऐकान्यिक
ऐकान्यिकः A pupil who<BR>commits one error in reading or<BR>reciting (the Vedas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकार्थ्यं|ऐकार्थ्य
ऐकार्थ्यं<BR>1 Sameness of aim or<BR>purpose.<BR>--2 Consistency in meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐकाहिक|ऐकाहिकं
ऐकाहिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Ephemeral.<BR>--2 Of one or the same day,<BR>quotidian.<BR>--3 Lasting for one day<BR>(as a sacrifice, fever, festival &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐक्यं|ऐक्य
ऐक्यं<BR>1 Oneness, unity, harmony;<BR>R. 10. 82; U. 6. 33.<BR>--2<BR>Unanimity.<BR>--3 Identity, sameness.<BR>--4<BR>Especially, the identity of the human<BR>soul or of the universe with the<BR>Deity.<BR>--5 An aggregate, whole.<BR>--6<BR>(In alg.) The product of the<BR>length and depth of the portions<BR>or little excavations differing<BR>in depth (Colebrooke).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0358-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

