ऐतरेय|ऐतरेयः
ऐतरेय a. [इतरा-ठक्] Originating<BR>from Aitareya.<BR>--यः, --यं A<BR>descendant of Itarā (or Itara, a sage)<BR>to whom the Aitareya Brāhmaṇa<BR>and Āraṇyaka were revealed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपनिषद् N. of an<BR>Upanishad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतरेयिन्
ऐतरेयिन् m. A reader of the<BR>Aitareya Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिहासिक|ऐतिहासिकः
ऐतिहासिक a. (की f.) [इतिहास<BR>ठक्]<BR>1 Traditional.<BR>--2<BR>Historical.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An historian.<BR>--2 One<BR>who knows or studies ancient<BR>legends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐतिह्यं|ऐतिह्य
ऐतिह्यं Traditional instruction,<BR>legendary account; ऐतिह्यमनुमानं च<BR>प्रत्यक्षमपि चागमम् Rām.; किलेत्यैतिह्ये.<BR>(ऐतिह्य is regarded as one of the<BR>Pramāṇas or proofs by the Paurāṇika as<BR>and reckoned along with प्रत्यक्ष<BR>अनुमान &c.; see अनुभव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0358-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐदंपर्यं|ऐदम्पर्य|ऐदंपर्य
