ऐंद्रशिरः A species of elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐंद्राग्न|ऐन्द्राग्न
ऐंद्राग्न a. Relating to Indra and<BR>Agni; so ऐंद्रवारुण, ऐंद्रसौम्य &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐंद्रिः|ऐन्द्रि|ऐन्द्रिः
ऐंद्रिः [इंद्रस्यापत्यं-इञ्]<BR>1 N. of<BR>Jayanta, Arjuna, or Vāli, the<BR>monkey-chief.<BR>--2 A crow; ऐंद्रिः<BR>किल नखैस्तस्या विददार स्तनौ द्विजः<BR>R. 12. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐंद्रिय|ऐन्द्रिय
ऐंद्रिय, --यक a. [इंद्रिय-अण्, वुञ् वा]<BR>1 Belonging to the senses, sensual.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">Page0359-b+ 50</a>]<BR>--2 Present, perceptible to the<BR>senses.<BR>--यं The world of the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐंद्रियक|ऐन्द्रियक|ऐन्द्रियकं
ऐंद्रिय, --यक a. [इंद्रिय-अण्, वुञ् वा]<BR>1 Belonging to the senses, sensual.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">Page0359-b+ 50</a>]<BR>--2 Present, perceptible to the<BR>senses.<BR>--यं The world of the senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐंद्रियेधी|ऐन्द्रियेधी
ऐंद्रियेधी a. Thinking only of<BR>sensual pleasures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐंधन|ऐन्धन|ऐन्धनः
ऐंधन a. (नी f.) [इंधन-अण्]<BR>Consisting of fuel.<BR>--नः N. of the<BR>sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐन्य|ऐन्यः
ऐन्य a. [इन-ण्य] Belonging to a<BR>master or the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐभ
ऐभ a. (भी f.) [इभ-अण्]<BR>Belonging to an elephant; Mu. 3. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐयत्यं|ऐयत्य
ऐयत्यं [इयत्-ष्यञ्] Quantity,<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावणः|ऐरावण
ऐरावणः (see ऐरावत below)<BR>Indra's elephant (produced at the<BR>churning of the ocean).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरावतः|ऐरावत|ऐरावतं
ऐरावतः [इरा आपः तद्वान् इरावान्<BR>समुद्रः तस्मादुत्पन्नः अण्]<BR>1 N. of the<BR>elephant of Indra.<BR>--2 An excellent<BR>elephant.<BR>--3 One of the chiefs<BR>of the Nāgas or serpent-race<BR>(inhabiting Pātāla).<BR>--4 The<BR>elephant presiding over the east.<BR>--5 A kind of rainbow.<BR>--6 A kind<BR>of lightning; (said to be n. also in<BR>these two senses).<BR>--7 The orange<BR>tree.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A vast and waterless<BR>region.<BR>--2 (pl.) N. of a Varṣa.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of the northern path of the moon.<BR>--ती<BR>1 The female of Indra's<BR>elephant.<BR>--2 Lightning.<BR>--3 N. of<BR>a plant (वटपत्री).<BR>--4 N. of the river<BR>Rāvī in the Panjāba (= इरावती).<BR>--5<BR>N. of a particular portion of the<BR>moon's path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरिणं|ऐरिण
ऐरिणं [इरिणे भवं अण्] Fossil or<BR>rock salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐरेयं|ऐरेय
ऐरेयं [इरायां अन्ने भवं ढक्]<BR>Spirituous liquor (prepared from food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐर्म्यं|ऐर्म्य
ऐर्म्यं [ईर्म-ष्यञ्] A plaster good<BR>for healing wounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलः|ऐल
ऐलः [इलाया अपत्यं अण्]<BR>1 N. of<BR>Purūravas (son of Ilā and Budha).<BR>--2 The planet Mars.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Food,<BR>a quantity of food.<BR>--2 A particular<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलवः
ऐलवः Ved. Noise, cry; ˚कारः<BR>Rudra's dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलवालुकः|ऐलवालुक
ऐलवालुकः N. of a perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलविलः|ऐलविल
ऐलविलः<BR>1 N. of Kubera;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">Page0359-c+ 52</a>]<BR>Śi. 13. 18.<BR>--2 The planet Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐलेयः|ऐलेय|ऐलेयं
ऐलेयः<BR>1 A kind of perfume.<BR>--2<BR>Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश
ऐश a. (शी f.) [ईश-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Belonging to Śiva; R. 2. 75.<BR>--2<BR>Supreme, regal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐशान
ऐशान a. [ईशान-अण्] Belonging<BR>to Śiva.<BR>--नी<BR>1 The northeastern<BR>direction.<BR>--2 N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर
ऐश्वर a. [ईश्वर-अण्] (री f.)<BR>1<BR>Belonging to or produced by a<BR>lord or the Supreme Being,<BR>majestic.<BR>--2 Powerful, mighty.<BR>--3<BR>Belonging to Śiva; R. 11. 76.<BR>--4<BR>Supreme, royal.<BR>--5 Divine.<BR>--री N.<BR>of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वरिकः|ऐश्वरिक
ऐश्वरिकः (With Buddhists) A<BR>theist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐश्वर्यं|ऐश्वर्य|ऐश्वर्य्य|ऐश्वर्य्यं
ऐश्वर्यं [ईश्वर-ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Supremacy,<BR>sovereignty; एकैश्वर्यस्थितोपि<BR>M. 1. 1; निशाचर˚.<BR>--2 Might, power,<BR>sway.<BR>--3 Dominion.<BR>--4 Affluence,<BR>wealth, greatness; ˚मत्तेषु Ś. 5. 18.<BR>--5 Superhuman power.<BR>--6 The<BR>divine faculties of omnipotence,<BR>omnipresence &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्
ऐषमस् ind. During this year,<BR>in the present year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्तन|ऐषमस्तनः
ऐषमस्तन^1 --मस्त्य a. Belonging to<BR>the present year.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: badly printed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषमस्त्य|ऐषमस्त्यः
ऐषमस्तन^1 --मस्त्य a. Belonging to<BR>the present year.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: badly printed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषावीर
ऐषावीर a. Ved. Weak,<BR>powerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐषीक
ऐषीक a. Consisting of stalks;<BR>made of reeds or canes; एषीकं पर्व a<BR>section of the सौप्तिक पर्व of Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टकं|ऐष्टक
ऐष्टकं Ved. Sacrificial bricks<BR>collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐष्टिक
ऐष्टिक a. (की f.) [इष्टि-ठक्]<BR>1<BR>Sacrificial, ceremonial.<BR>--2<BR>Treating of इष्टि or sacrifice (as a work).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पूर्तिक a. belonging to<BR>इष्टापूर्त (belonging to sacrifices or<BR>charitable works).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहलौकिक
ऐहलौकिक a. (की f.) [इहलोक-ठञ्]<BR>Happening in or belonging to this<BR>world, temporal, sublunary (opp.<BR>पारलौकिक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ऐहिक|ऐहिकं
ऐहिक a. (की f.) [इह-ठञ्]<BR>1<BR>Of this world or place, temporal,<BR>secular, worldly.<BR>--2 Local, of this<BR>place.<BR>--कं Business (of this world).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दर्शिन् a. worldly-minded<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0359-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओ
ओ m. (औः) N. of Brahmā. --ind.<BR>1 A vocative particle (oh).<BR>--2 An<BR>interjection of (1) calling; (holla,<BR>ho); (2) remembrance; (3)<BR>compassion (ah!).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकः|ओक|ओकं
ओकः<BR>1 A house.<BR>--2 A refuge,<BR>shelter.<BR>--3 A bird.<BR>--4 A Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकस्
ओकस् n.<BR>1 A house, residence;<BR>as in दिवौकस् or स्वर्गै कस् a god.<BR>--2 An<BR>asylum, refuge.<BR>--3 A resting place.<BR>--4 Pleasure, gratification. [cf. Gr.<BR>oikos].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकिवस्
ओकिवस् a. Meeting together,<BR>united (समवेत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओक्य
ओक्य a.<BR>1 Favourable to the<BR>house; i. e. to its inmates.<BR>--2 Good<BR>for a house, kind to a household.<BR>--क्यं<BR>1 Gratification, pleasure.<BR>--2<BR>A comfortable place.<BR>--3 A resting<BR>place, house (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकणः|ओकण
ओकणः(णिः) A bug; so ओकोदनी,<BR>ओक्कणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकणिः|ओकणि
ओकणः(णिः) A bug; so ओकोदनी,<BR>ओक्कणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओकुलः|ओकुल
ओकुलः A cake of flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओख्
ओख् {c1c} P. (ओखति, ओखांचकार, ओखितुं,<BR>ओखित)<BR>1 To be dry.<BR>--2 To be<BR>able; be sufficient.<BR>--3 To adorn or<BR>grace.<BR>--4 To refuse.<BR>--5 To ward off,<BR>prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओगण
ओगण a.<BR>1 United.<BR>--2 Solitary;<BR>despised, cast off by one's friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओघः|ओघ
ओघः [उच्-घञ् पृषो˚ घ]<BR>1 A flood,<BR>stream, current; पुनरोधेन हि युज्यते<BR>नदी Ku. 4. 44; so रुधिर˚, बाष्प˚ &c.<BR>--2 An inundation.<BR>--3 A heap,<BR>quantity, mass, multitude; बाण˚, अघ˚,<BR>जन˚ &c.<BR>--4 The whole.<BR>--5<BR>Continuity.<BR>--6 Quick time in music.<BR>--7<BR>Tradition, traditional instruction.<BR>--8<BR>A kind of dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओंकारः|ओङ्कार|ओंकार|ओङ्कारः
ओंकारः See under ओम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज्
ओज् {c1c} {c10c} U. (ओजति, ओजयति,<BR>ओजयितुं, ओजित)<BR>1 To be strong or<BR>able.<BR>--2 To increase, grow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज|ओजः
ओज a. Odd, uneven.<BR>--जं = ओजस्<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्
ओजस् n.<BR>1 Bodily strength,<BR>vigour; energy, ability.<BR>--2 Vitality.<BR>--3 Virility, the generative faculty.<BR>--4<BR>Splendour, light.<BR>--5 (In Rhet).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">Page0360-b+ 49</a>]<BR>An elaborate form of style,<BR>abundance of compounds;<BR>(considered by Daṇḍin to be the ‘soul of<BR>prose’); ओजः समासभूयस्त्वमेतद्गद्यस्य<BR>जीवितम् Kāv. 1. 80; see K. P. 8<BR>also; said to be of 5 kinds in<BR>R. G.<BR>--6 (In astr.) Each alternate<BR>sign of the zodiac (as the first,<BR>third &c.).<BR>--7 Water.<BR>--8 Matallic<BR>lustre.<BR>--9 Manifestation, appearance.<BR>--10 Skill in the use of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजसीन
ओजसीन, ओजस्य a. Ved. Strong,<BR>powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्य
ओजसीन, ओजस्य a. Ved. Strong,<BR>powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्वत्|ओजस्वन्त्
ओजस्वत्, ओजस्विन् a.<BR>1 Strong,<BR>vigorous, energetic, powerful; रूपं<BR>तदोजस्वि तदेव वीर्यम् R. 5. 37;<BR>Śi. 12. 35.<BR>--2 Splendid, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजस्विन्
ओजस्वत्, ओजस्विन् a.<BR>1 Strong,<BR>vigorous, energetic, powerful; रूपं<BR>तदोजस्वि तदेव वीर्यम् R. 5. 37;<BR>Śi. 12. 35.<BR>--2 Splendid, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजायते
ओजायते Den. A. To show<BR>strength or vigour, exhibit one's<BR>heroism; Bk. 5. 76; U. 5. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजिष्ठ
ओजिष्ठ a. (Super. of उग्र also)<BR>Most strong, vehement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओजीयस्
ओजीयस् a. More vehement,<BR>stronger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओज्मन्
ओज्मन् a. An instigator. --m.<BR>1 Speed.<BR>--2 Strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडक
ओडक, --डवः A musical mode<BR>which omits two of the notes of<BR>the scale (रि and प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडवः|ओडव
ओडक, --डवः A musical mode<BR>which omits two of the notes of<BR>the scale (रि and प).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडिकाः
ओडिकाः, ओडी Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओडी
ओडिकाः, ओडी Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओड्रः|ओड्र
ओड्रः (m. pl.) N. of a people<BR>and their country (the modern<BR>Orissa); Ms. 10. 44.<BR>--ड्रः The<BR>China-rose.<BR>--ड्रं The Javā-flower.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आख्या the China-rose.<BR>--पुष्पं the Javā-flower; Hibiscus<BR>Rosa Sinensis and its flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओण्
ओण् {c1c} P. (ओणति, ओणितुं) To<BR>remove, take or drag along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओणि
ओणि a. Removing.<BR>--णी (du.)<BR>1<BR>Heaven and earth.<BR>--2 Vessels used<BR>in the preparation of Soma.<BR>--3<BR>Preserving power, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओत
ओत a. [आ-वे-क्त] Woven, sewn<BR>with threads across.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रोत<BR>a. {1} sewn crosswise and<BR>lengthwise. {2} extending in all directions.<BR>--(तं) ind. crosswise and lengthwise,<BR>vertically and horizontally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओतुः|ओतु
ओतुः<BR>1 The woof or cross threads<BR>of a web.<BR>--2 A cat (f. also): as in<BR>स्थूलो(लौ)तुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदती
ओदती Issuing out, rising<BR>upwards; epithet of the dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनः|ओदन|ओदनं
ओदनः, --नं [उंद्-युच् Uṇ. 2. 76]<BR>1 Food, boiled rice; e. g. दध्योदनः,<BR>घृत˚, गुड˚, मांस˚ &c.<BR>--2 Grain<BR>mashed and cooked with milk.<BR>--3 A<BR>cloud. (Sometimes ओदन is prefixed<BR>to the names of pupils to denote<BR>that the pupil's object is more to<BR>be fed by his master than be taught;<BR>e. g. ओदनपाणिनीयाः P. VI. 2. 69 Sk.)<BR>--नी The plant (बला) Sida Cordifolia.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आह्वया, --आह्वा, --ओदनिका<BR>N. of a medicinal plant (महासमंगा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनं|ओदन|ओदनः
ओदनः, --नं [उंद्-युच् Uṇ. 2. 76]<BR>1 Food, boiled rice; e. g. दध्योदनः,<BR>घृत˚, गुड˚, मांस˚ &c.<BR>--2 Grain<BR>mashed and cooked with milk.<BR>--3 A<BR>cloud. (Sometimes ओदन is prefixed<BR>to the names of pupils to denote<BR>that the pupil's object is more to<BR>be fed by his master than be taught;<BR>e. g. ओदनपाणिनीयाः P. VI. 2. 69 Sk.)<BR>--नी The plant (बला) Sida Cordifolia.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आह्वया, --आह्वा, --ओदनिका<BR>N. of a medicinal plant (महासमंगा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओदनीयति
ओदनीयति Den. P. To wish to<BR>make mashed food of anything;<BR>पुरोडाशं यद्योदनीयंति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओद्मः|ओद्म
ओद्मः, ओद्मन् n.<BR>1 Flowing.<BR>--2<BR>Wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओद्मन्
ओद्मः, ओद्मन् n.<BR>1 Flowing.<BR>--2<BR>Wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओधस्
ओधस् n. An udder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओपशः|ओपश
ओपशः Ved. An ornament of<BR>the head; curl; a horn (Sāy.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्
ओम् ind.<BR>1 The sacred syllable<BR>om, uttered as a holy exclamation at<BR>the beginning and end of a reading<BR>of the Vedas, or previous to the<BR>commencement of a prayer or sacred<BR>work.<BR>--2 As a particle it implies<BR>(a) solemn affirmation and<BR>respectful assent (so be it, amen !). (b)<BR>assent or acceptance (yes, all right);<BR>ओमित्युच्यताममात्यः Māl. 6;<BR>ओमित्युक्तवतोथ शांर्गिण इति Śi. 1. 75;<BR>द्वितीयश्चेदोमिति ब्रूमः S. D. 1. (c)<BR>command; (d) auspiciousness; (e)<BR>removal or warding off.<BR>--3 Brahman.<BR>[This word first appears in the<BR>Upanishads as a mystic monosyllable, and is<BR>regarded as the object of the most<BR>profound religious meditation. In the<BR>Māṇḍūkya Upaniṣad it is said that this<BR>syllable is all what has been, that which<BR>is and is to be; that all is om, only om.<BR>Literally analysed, om is taken to be made<BR>up of three letters or quarters; the letter<BR>a is Vaiśvānara, the spirit of waking<BR>souls in the waking world; u is<BR>Taijasa, the spirit of dreaming souls in the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-a" target="_blank">Page0361-a+ 35</a>]<BR>world of dreams; and m. is Prājña, the<BR>spirit of sleeping and undreaming souls;<BR>and the whole om is said to be<BR>unknowable, unspeakable, into which the<BR>whole world passes away, blessed above<BR>duality; (for further account see<BR>Gough's Upaniṣads pp. 69-73). In later<BR>times om came to be used as a mystic<BR>name for the Hindu triad, representing<BR>the union of the three gods a (Viṣṇu),<BR>u (Śiva), and m. (Brahmā). It is<BR>usually called Praṇava or Ekākṣaram].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः {1} the sacred<BR>syllable ओम्. {2} the exclamation<BR>ओम्, or pronunciation of the same.<BR>{3} (fig.) commencement; एष<BR>तावदोंकारः Mv. 1; B. R. 3. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0360-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमः|ओम
ओमः Ved.<BR>1 A protector.<BR>--2 One<BR>who is favourably disposed (towards<BR>another).<BR>--3 Any one fit to be<BR>protected or favoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमन्
ओमन् m.<BR>1 Protection.<BR>--2 Favour,<BR>kindness.<BR>--3 A kind person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमन्वत्|ओमन्वन्त्
ओमन्वत् a.<BR>1 Friendly.<BR>--2<BR>Favourable, kind.<BR>--3 Satiating,<BR>pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओमात्रा
ओमात्रा Protection, kindness,<BR>assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओम्या
ओम्या Ved. Favour, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओरंफः
ओरंफः A hard scratch; Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओल|ओलं|ओलः
ओल a. Wet, damp.<BR>--लः An<BR>esculent root (शूरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओलंड्|ओलण्ड्
ओलंड् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (ओलंडति,<BR>ओलंडयति, ओलंडित) To cast or throw<BR>upwards, throw up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओल्ल|ओल्लः
ओल्ल a. Wet, damp.<BR>--ल्लः A<BR>hostage; ˚आगतः come or<BR>received as a hostage; (this word occurs<BR>once or twice in<BR>Viddhaśālabhanjikā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषः|ओष|ओषं
ओषः<BR>1 Burning, combustion.<BR>--2 Cooking, baking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषणः|ओषण
ओषणः Pungency, sharp flavour.<BR>--णी A potherb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधिः|ओषधि
ओषधिः, --धी f. [ओषः पाको धीयते<BR>अत्र, -धा कि Tv.]<BR>1 A herb, plant<BR>(in general); ओषध्यः फलपाकांताः<BR>Ms. 1. 46; cf. संजीवन˚.<BR>--2 A<BR>medicinal plant or drug.<BR>--3 An annual<BR>plant or herb which dies after<BR>becoming ripe.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः,--गर्भः,<BR>--नाथः the moon (as presiding over<BR>and feeding plants); cf. पुष्णामि<BR>चौषधीः सवोः सोमो भूत्वा रसात्मकः<BR>Bg. 15. 13; R. 2. 73: Ku. 7. 1;<BR>Ś. 4. 2.<BR>--ज a. produced from plants.<BR>--(जः) fire.<BR>--धरः, --पतिः {1} a dealer<BR>in medicinal drugs. {2} a<BR>physician. {3} the moon; Śi. 9. 36<BR>(where it means ‘physician’ also).<BR>--प्रस्थः the capital of Himālaya;<BR>तत्प्रयातौषधिप्रस्थं स्थितये हिमवत्पुरं<BR>Ku. 6. 33, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषधी
ओषधिः, --धी f. [ओषः पाको धीयते<BR>अत्र, -धा कि Tv.]<BR>1 A herb, plant<BR>(in general); ओषध्यः फलपाकांताः<BR>Ms. 1. 46; cf. संजीवन˚.<BR>--2 A<BR>medicinal plant or drug.<BR>--3 An annual<BR>plant or herb which dies after<BR>becoming ripe.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः,--गर्भः,<BR>--नाथः the moon (as presiding over<BR>and feeding plants); cf. पुष्णामि<BR>चौषधीः सवोः सोमो भूत्वा रसात्मकः<BR>Bg. 15. 13; R. 2. 73: Ku. 7. 1;<BR>Ś. 4. 2.<BR>--ज a. produced from plants.<BR>--(जः) fire.<BR>--धरः, --पतिः {1} a dealer<BR>in medicinal drugs. {2} a<BR>physician. {3} the moon; Śi. 9. 36<BR>(where it means ‘physician’ also).<BR>--प्रस्थः the capital of Himālaya;<BR>तत्प्रयातौषधिप्रस्थं स्थितये हिमवत्पुरं<BR>Ku. 6. 33, 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओषं|ओष|ओषः
ओषं ind. Immediately, quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ट्राविन्
ओष्ट्राविन् a. Burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठः|ओष्ठ
ओष्ठः [उष्यते उष्णाहारेण, उष्-कर्मणि<BR>थन् Uṇ. 2. 4] A lip (lower or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-c" target="_blank">Page0361-c+ 34</a>]<BR>upper); द्वावोष्ठौ छेदयेन्नृपः<BR>Ms. 8. 282; अधर˚, बिंब˚.--ष्ठी A creeper<BR>bearing a red fruit to which the<BR>lip is commonly compared (बिंबफल).<BR>In comp. the अ or आ of words<BR>before ओष्ठ may be optionally<BR>dropped, and the fem. may end in<BR>आ or ई; as बिंबो(बौ) ष्ठा-ष्ठी. [cf. L.<BR>ostium].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधरौ-रं the<BR>upper and lower lip.<BR>--उपमफला<BR>the creeper Bryonia Grandis<BR>(whose fruit resembles a lip).<BR>--कोपः --प्रकोपः a disease of the<BR>lips.<BR>--ज a. labial (produced by<BR>the lips).<BR>--जाहं the root of the<BR>lip.<BR>--पल्लवः --वं a sprout-like or<BR>tender lip.<BR>--पुटं the cavity made by<BR>opening the lips.<BR>--पुष्पः --ष्पं the<BR>tree वंधुक.<BR>--रोगः any disease of the<BR>lips.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठक|ओष्ठकः
ओष्ठक a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Taking care of the lips.<BR>--कः A<BR>lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ठ्य
ओष्ठ्य a. [ओष्ठ-यत्]<BR>1 Being at<BR>the lips.<BR>--2 Belonging to the lips,<BR>labial (as the sounds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओष्ण
ओष्ण a. A little warm, tepid<BR>(ईषदुष्ण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओहः|ओह
ओहः Ved.<BR>1 Bringing,<BR>performing.<BR>--2 Reaching.<BR>--3 Meditation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ब्रह्मन् a. one who has<BR>sacred knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ओहस्
ओहस् n. Praise; idea, true<BR>notion (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औ
औ m.<BR>1 A sound.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>Śeṣa or Ananta. --f. The earth.<BR>--ind. An interjection of (1)<BR>calling (ho, hola); (2) addressing<BR>(oh!); (3) opposition; (4)<BR>asseveration or determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थिकः|औक्थिक
औक्थिकः [उक्थ-ठक्] A<BR>Brāhmaṇa who knows or studies or<BR>recites the ukthas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थिक्यं|औक्थिक्य
औक्थिक्यं The text of the Ukthas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्थं|औक्थ
औक्थं A peculiar mode of recitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0361-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औक्षकं|औक्षक
