औशन, औशनस a. (नी, --सी f.)<BR>[उशनस्-अण्] Belonging or peculiar<BR>to Uśanas; originating from<BR>Uśanas, or taught by him.<BR>--सं<BR>1 The law-book of उशनस् (a<BR>treatise on civil polity).<BR>--2<BR>N. of an Upapurāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशिज
औशिज a. (जी f.) [उशिज्-अण्]<BR>Desirous, zealous, wishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीनरः|औशीनर
औशीनरः [उशीनरस्यापत्यं अङ्]<BR>The son of Uśīnara.<BR>--री N. of the<BR>wife of king Purūravas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीरं|औशीर|औशीरः
औशीरं [उशीरं-अण्]<BR>1 The<BR>handle of a fan or Chowri.<BR>--2 A bed;<BR>औशीरे कामचारः कृतोभूत् Dk. 72 at<BR>liberty to sleep or sit.<BR>--3 A seat<BR>(chair, stool &c.).<BR>--4 An unguent<BR>made of Uśīra.<BR>--5 The root of the<BR>fragrant grass उशीर q. v.<BR>--6 A fan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औशीरिका
औशीरिका<BR>1 The shoot (of a<BR>plant).<BR>--2 A basin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषणं|औषण
औषणं [उषण-अण्]<BR>1 Pungency.<BR>--2 Black pepper.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शौंडी<BR>dried ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषध|औषधं
औषध a. (धी f.) [ओषधि-अण्]<BR>Consisting of herbs.<BR>--धं<BR>1 A herb;<BR>herbs taken collectively.<BR>--2 A<BR>medicament, medicinal drug, medicine<BR>in general.<BR>--3 A vessel for herbs.<BR>--4 A mineral.<BR>--5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधिः|औषधि
औषधिः, --धी f.<BR>1 A herb, plant (in<BR>general); Y. 3. 276 v. l.; see ओषधि.<BR>--2 A medicinal herb; अचिंत्यो हि<BR>मणिमंत्रौषधीनां प्रभावः Ratn. 2.<BR>--3 An<BR>herb which emits fire; विरमंति<BR>नज्वलितुमौषधयः Ki. 5. 24 (तृणज्योतींषि<BR>Malli.); cf. Ku. 1. 10.<BR>--4 An<BR>annual or deciduous plant; ˚धीपतिः<BR>N. of Soma, the lord of plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधी
औषधिः, --धी f.<BR>1 A herb, plant (in<BR>general); Y. 3. 276 v. l.; see ओषधि.<BR>--2 A medicinal herb; अचिंत्यो हि<BR>मणिमंत्रौषधीनां प्रभावः Ratn. 2.<BR>--3 An<BR>herb which emits fire; विरमंति<BR>नज्वलितुमौषधयः Ki. 5. 24 (तृणज्योतींषि<BR>Malli.); cf. Ku. 1. 10.<BR>--4 An<BR>annual or deciduous plant; ˚धीपतिः<BR>N. of Soma, the lord of plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधीकृ
औषधीकृ {c8c} U. To reduce to a<BR>medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषधीय
औषधीय a. Medicinal, consisting<BR>of herbs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषरं|औषर
औषरं, --रकं [उषरे भवं अण्, ततः कन्]<BR>1 Rock-salt.<BR>--2 Iron stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषरकं|औषरक
औषरं, --रकं [उषरे भवं अण्, ततः कन्]<BR>1 Rock-salt.<BR>--2 Iron stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषस
औषस a. (सी f.) [उषस्-अण्]<BR>Relating to dawn, early; ˚आतप<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-a" target="_blank">Page0365-a+ 8</a>]<BR>Ki. 9. 11.<BR>--सी Day-break, morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0364-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषस्य
औषस्य a. Sacred to Uṣas or the<BR>dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषसिक
औषसिक, औषिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Walking out at day-break.<BR>--2<BR>Early born or produced at dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औषिक
औषसिक, औषिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Walking out at day-break.<BR>--2<BR>Early born or produced at dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्र
औष्ट्र a. (ष्ट्री f.) [उष्ट्र-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Relating to, or produced from, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-b" target="_blank">Page0365-b+ 8</a>]<BR>camel.<BR>--2 Abounding in camels.<BR>--ष्ट्रं<BR>1 The milk of a camel.<BR>--2<BR>Camel nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्रक|औष्ट्रकं
औष्ट्रक a. (की f.) [उष्ट्र-वुञ्]<BR>Relating to a camel.<BR>--कं A multitude<BR>of camels; Śi. 5. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ट्ररथ
औष्ट्ररथ a. (थी f.)<BR>Belonging to a carriage drawn by camels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ठ्य
औष्ठ्य a. [ओष्ठ-यत्] Relating to<BR>the lip, labial.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्णः a<BR>labial letter; i. e. उ, ऊ, प्, फ्, ब्, भ्,<BR>म्, and व्.<BR>--स्थान a. pronounced<BR>with the lips.<BR>--स्वरः a labial vowel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्णं|औष्ण
औष्णं [उष्ण-अण्] Heat, warmth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्ण्यं|औष्ण्य
औष्ण्यं, औष्म्यं [उष्ण-उष्म-ष्यञ्]<BR>Heat; R. 17. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

औष्म्यं|औष्म्य
औष्ण्यं, औष्म्यं [उष्ण-उष्म-ष्यञ्]<BR>Heat; R. 17. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क The first consonant of the<BR>alphabet, and first letter of the<BR>guttural class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कः|क|कं
कः<BR>1 Brahman.<BR>--2 Viṣṇu.<BR>--3<BR>Kāmadeva.<BR>--4 Fire.<BR>--5 Wind or air.<BR>--6 Yama.<BR>--7 The sun.<BR>--8 The soul.<BR>--9 A king or prince.<BR>--10 Knot<BR>or joint.<BR>--11 A peacock.<BR>--12 The king<BR>of birds.<BR>--13 A bird.<BR>--14 The mind.<BR>--15 Body.<BR>--16 Time.<BR>--17 A cloud.<BR>--18 A word, sound.<BR>--19 Hair.<BR>--20<BR>Light, splendour.<BR>--21 Wealth,<BR>property.<BR>--कं<BR>1 Happiness, joy, pleasure<BR>(as in नाक which is explained thus;<BR>न कं सुखं = दुःखं; न अकं यत्र).<BR>--2 Water;<BR>सत्येन माभिरक्ष त्वं वरुणेत्यभिशाप्य कं<BR>Y. 2. 108; केशवं पतितं दृष्ट्वा पांडवा<BR>हर्षनिर्भराः Subhāṣ. (where a pun is<BR>intended on केशव, the apparent<BR>meaning being Keśava).<BR>--3 The head; as<BR>in कंधरा (= कं शिरो धारयतीति).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. watery, aquatic.<BR>--दः a cloud<BR>(giving water.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क|कं|कः
क A Taddhita affix added to<BR>nouns and adjectives, mostly to the<BR>former, in the sense of diminution,<BR>deterioration, similarity,<BR>endearment, or sometimes to express the<BR>original meaning of the word<BR>itself; e. g. वृक्षकः a small tree; बालकः<BR>a chap; पुत्रकः dear boy; अश्वकः a<BR>bad horse, or like a horse, or a horse<BR>itself (स्वार्थे कन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंय्य
कंय्य a. Happy, prosperous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबूलं
कंबूलं N. of the eighth Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंस्
कंस् {c2c} A. (कंस्ते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To<BR>command.<BR>--3 To destroy; see कस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसः|कंस|कंसं
कंसः --सं<BR>1 A drinking vessel,<BR>cup, can, goblet.<BR>--2 Bell-metal,<BR>white copper.<BR>--3 A particular<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1b" target="_blank">Page0365-1b+ 45</a>]<BR>measure known as आढक, q. v.<BR>--सः<BR>N. of a king of Mathurā, son of<BR>Ugrasena and enemy of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>[He is identified with the Asura<BR>Kālanemi, and acted inimically towards<BR>Kṛṣṇa and became his implacable foe.<BR>The circumstance which made him so<BR>was the following. While, after the<BR>marriage of Devakī with Vasudeva, he was<BR>driving the happy pair home, a heavenly<BR>voice warned Kaṃsa that the eighth<BR>child of Devakī would kill him.<BR>Thereupon he threw both of them into prison,<BR>loaded them with strong fetters, and<BR>kept the strictest watch over them.<BR>He took from Devakī every child as<BR>soon as it was born and slew it, and in<BR>this way he disposed of her first six<BR>children. But the 7th and 8th, Balarāma<BR>and Kṛṣṇa, were safely conveyed to<BR>Nanda's house in spite of his vigilance,<BR>and Kṛṣṇa grew up to be his slayer<BR>according to the prophecy. When Kaṃsa<BR>heard this, he was very much enraged and<BR>sent several demons to kill Kṛṣṇa,<BR>but he killed them all with ease. At last<BR>he sent Akrūra to bring the boys to<BR>Mathurā. A severe duel was fought<BR>between Kaṃsa and Kṛṣṇa, in which<BR>the former was slain by the latter].<BR>--सा N. of a daughter of Ugrasena<BR>and sister of Kaṃsa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः,<BR>अरातिः, जित्, कृष्, द्विष्, हन् m. ‘slayer<BR>of Kaṃsa, i. e. Kṛṣṇa; स्वयं<BR>संधिकारिणा कंसारिणा दूतेन Ve. 1; निषेदिवान्<BR>कंसकृषः स विष्टरे Śi. 1. 16.<BR>--अस्थि<BR>n. bell-metal.<BR>--उद्भवा a fragrant<BR>earth.<BR>--कारः (री f.) {1} a mixed<BR>tribe; कंसकारशंखकारौ ब्राह्मणात्संबभूवतुः<BR>Śabdak. {2} a worker in pewter or<BR>white-brass, a bell-founder.<BR>--माक्षिकं<BR>a metallic substance in large grains,<BR>a sort of pyrites.<BR>--वणिक् m. a<BR>brazier or seller of brass vessels.<BR>--वधः --हननं the slaying of Kaṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसं|कंस|कंसः
कंसः --सं<BR>1 A drinking vessel,<BR>cup, can, goblet.<BR>--2 Bell-metal,<BR>white copper.<BR>--3 A particular<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1b" target="_blank">Page0365-1b+ 45</a>]<BR>measure known as आढक, q. v.<BR>--सः<BR>N. of a king of Mathurā, son of<BR>Ugrasena and enemy of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>[He is identified with the Asura<BR>Kālanemi, and acted inimically towards<BR>Kṛṣṇa and became his implacable foe.<BR>The circumstance which made him so<BR>was the following. While, after the<BR>marriage of Devakī with Vasudeva, he was<BR>driving the happy pair home, a heavenly<BR>voice warned Kaṃsa that the eighth<BR>child of Devakī would kill him.<BR>Thereupon he threw both of them into prison,<BR>loaded them with strong fetters, and<BR>kept the strictest watch over them.<BR>He took from Devakī every child as<BR>soon as it was born and slew it, and in<BR>this way he disposed of her first six<BR>children. But the 7th and 8th, Balarāma<BR>and Kṛṣṇa, were safely conveyed to<BR>Nanda's house in spite of his vigilance,<BR>and Kṛṣṇa grew up to be his slayer<BR>according to the prophecy. When Kaṃsa<BR>heard this, he was very much enraged and<BR>sent several demons to kill Kṛṣṇa,<BR>but he killed them all with ease. At last<BR>he sent Akrūra to bring the boys to<BR>Mathurā. A severe duel was fought<BR>between Kaṃsa and Kṛṣṇa, in which<BR>the former was slain by the latter].<BR>--सा N. of a daughter of Ugrasena<BR>and sister of Kaṃsa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः,<BR>अरातिः, जित्, कृष्, द्विष्, हन् m. ‘slayer<BR>of Kaṃsa, i. e. Kṛṣṇa; स्वयं<BR>संधिकारिणा कंसारिणा दूतेन Ve. 1; निषेदिवान्<BR>कंसकृषः स विष्टरे Śi. 1. 16.<BR>--अस्थि<BR>n. bell-metal.<BR>--उद्भवा a fragrant<BR>earth.<BR>--कारः (री f.) {1} a mixed<BR>tribe; कंसकारशंखकारौ ब्राह्मणात्संबभूवतुः<BR>Śabdak. {2} a worker in pewter or<BR>white-brass, a bell-founder.<BR>--माक्षिकं<BR>a metallic substance in large grains,<BR>a sort of pyrites.<BR>--वणिक् m. a<BR>brazier or seller of brass vessels.<BR>--वधः --हननं the slaying of Kaṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसकं|कंसक
कंसकं Bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसवती
कंसवती N. of a daughter of<BR>उग्रसेन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसिक
कंसिक a. (की f.) Made of<BR>bellmetal &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसीय
कंसीय a. Fit for, or relating to, a<BR>cup.<BR>--यं Bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंसारं|कंसार
कंसारं Ved.<BR>1 A bone.<BR>--2 Rice, the<BR>grain of which becomes hard in<BR>the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्
कक् {c1c} A. (ककते, ककित)<BR>1 To<BR>wish.<BR>--2 To be proud.<BR>--3 To be<BR>unsteady; see कंक्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककजाकृत
ककजाकृत a. Ved. Mutilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककंदः|ककन्द|ककन्दः
ककंदः Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककरः|ककर
ककरः A kind of bird (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककर्दुः|ककर्दु|ककर्द्दु
ककर्दुः Destruction of<BR>happiness or of enemies; Rv. 10. 102. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककाटिका
ककाटिका A part of the back of<BR>the head (घाटा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुंजलः|ककुञ्जल|ककुंजल|ककुञ्जलः
ककुंजलः The Cātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्
ककुद् f.<BR>1 A summit, peak.<BR>--2<BR>Chief, head; see ककुद below.<BR>--3 The<BR>hump on the shoulders of the Indian<BR>bull.<BR>--4 A horn.<BR>--5 An ensign or<BR>symbol of royalty (as the छत्र, चामर<BR>&c.).<BR>--6 Any projecting corner.<BR>--7<BR>N. of a daughter of Dakṣa and<BR>wife of Dharma. (According to<BR>Pāṇini V. 4. 146-147 ककुद् is the<BR>form to be substituted for ककुद in<BR>adj. or Bah. comps.; e. g. त्रिककुद्).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थः [ककुदि तिष्ठतीति] an<BR>epithet of Puraṃjaya, son of Śaśāda,<BR>a king of the solar race, and a<BR>descendant of Ikṣvāku; इक्ष्वाकुवंश्यः<BR>ककुदं नृपाणां ककुत्स्थ इत्याहितलक्षणोऽभूत्<BR>R. 6. 71. [Mythology relates that, when<BR>in their war with the demons, the gods<BR>were often worsted, they, headed by Indra,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-a" target="_blank">Page0366-a+ 55</a>]<BR>went to the powerful king Puraṃjaya,<BR>and requested him to be their friend<BR>in battle. The latter consented to do so,<BR>provided Indra carried him on his<BR>shoulders. Indra accordingly assumed the<BR>form of a bull, and Puraṃjaya, seated on<BR>its hump, completely vanquished the<BR>demons. Puraṃjaya is, therefore, called<BR>Kakutstha ‘standing on a hump’].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0365-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुदः|ककुद|ककुदं
ककुदः --दं<BR>1 The peak or summit<BR>of a mountain.<BR>--2 A hump (on the<BR>shoulders of an Indian bull).<BR>--3<BR>Chief, foremost, pre-eminent; ककुदं<BR>वेदविदां तपोधनश्च Mk. 1. 5;<BR>इक्ष्वाकुवंश्यः ककुदं नृपाणां R. 6. 71.<BR>--4 A sign<BR>or symbol of royalty; नृपतिककुदं<BR>R. 3. 70, 17. 27.<BR>--5 A species of<BR>serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुदं|ककुद|ककुदः
ककुदः --दं<BR>1 The peak or summit<BR>of a mountain.<BR>--2 A hump (on the<BR>shoulders of an Indian bull).<BR>--3<BR>Chief, foremost, pre-eminent; ककुदं<BR>वेदविदां तपोधनश्च Mk. 1. 5;<BR>इक्ष्वाकुवंश्यः ककुदं नृपाणां R. 6. 71.<BR>--4 A sign<BR>or symbol of royalty; नृपतिककुदं<BR>R. 3. 70, 17. 27.<BR>--5 A species of<BR>serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मत्|ककुद्मन्त्
ककुद्मत् a. [अस्त्यर्थे मतुप्]<BR>1 Furnished<BR>with a hump; Pt. 1.<BR>--2 Running<BR>high (as a wave). --m.<BR>1 A<BR>mountain (having peaks).<BR>--2 A buffalo;<BR>मदोदग्राः ककुद्मंतः R. 4. 22; a humped<BR>bull; 13. 47; Ku. 1. 56.<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>medicinal plant (ऋषभ).<BR>--ती The<BR>hip and the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्वत्|ककुद्वन्त्
ककुद्वत् m. A buffalo with a hump<BR>on his shoulders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुद्मिन्
ककुद्मिन् a. Peaked; furnished<BR>with a hump &c. --m.<BR>1 A bull<BR>with a hump on his shoulders.<BR>--2<BR>A mountain.<BR>--3 N. of Viṣṇu; and of<BR>king रैवतक. ˚कन्या-सुता N. of Revatī<BR>and wife of Balarāma; Śi. 2. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुंदरं|ककुन्दर|ककुंदर|ककुन्दरं
ककुंदरं The cavities of the loins;<BR>Y. 3. 96 (जघनकूप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ्
ककुभ् f.<BR>1 A direction, quarter<BR>of the compass; वियुक्ताः कांतेन स्त्रिय<BR>इव न राजंति ककुभः Mk. 5. 26;<BR>Śi. 9. 25, 3. 33.<BR>--2 Splendour, beauty.<BR>--3 A<BR>wreath of Campaka flowers.<BR>--4 A<BR>sacred treatise or Śāstra.<BR>--5 A peak,<BR>summit.<BR>--6 A Rāgiṇī or<BR>personified mode of music.<BR>--7 The<BR>personified quarter of the sky.<BR>--8 Breath,<BR>animation.<BR>--9 Unornamented hair;<BR>or hair hanging down as a tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुभ|ककुभः
ककुभ a. Ved. Distinguished,<BR>superior.<BR>--भः<BR>1 A crooked piece of<BR>wood at the end of the lute.<BR>--2 The<BR>tree Arjuna; ककुभसुरभिः शैलः U. 1. 33.<BR>--3 A kind of goblin or evil spirit.<BR>--4<BR>One of the Rāgas or personified<BR>musical modes.<BR>--भा<BR>1 Space;<BR>quarter.<BR>--2 One of the Rāgiṇīs.<BR>--भं A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">Page0366-b+ 53</a>]<BR>flower of the Kuṭaja tree; Me. 22.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदनी ‘food of the sky,’<BR>a kind of fragrance or perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककुह|ककुहः
ककुह a. Ved. Eminent;<BR>excellent.<BR>--हः A part of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ककेरुकः|ककेरुक
ककेरुकः A worm in the stomach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्क्
कक्क् {c1c} P. To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कटः|कक्कट
कक्कटः A kind of animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कुलः|कक्कुल
कक्कुलः The Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोलः|कक्कोल
कक्कोलः --ली N. of a plant<BR>bearing a berry; कक्कोलीफलजग्धि<BR>Māl. 6. 19 v. l.<BR>--लं, --लकं<BR>1 A berry of this<BR>plant.<BR>--2 A perfume prepared from<BR>its berries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्कोली
कक्कोलः --ली N. of a plant<BR>bearing a berry; कक्कोलीफलजग्धि<BR>Māl. 6. 19 v. l.<BR>--लं, --लकं<BR>1 A berry of this<BR>plant.<BR>--2 A perfume prepared from<BR>its berries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ख्
कक्ख् {c1c} P. To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खट|कक्खटः
कक्खट a.<BR>1 Hard, solid.<BR>--2<BR>Laughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्खटी
कक्खटी Chalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षः|कक्ष
कक्षः<BR>1 A lurking or<BR>hidingplace.<BR>--2 The end of the lower<BR>garment; see कक्षा.<BR>--3 A climbing plant,<BR>creeper.<BR>--4 Grass, dry grass; यतस्तु<BR>कक्षस्तत एव वह्निः R. 7. 55, 11. 75;<BR>Ms. 7. 110.<BR>--5 A forest of dead<BR>trees, dry wood.<BR>--6 The arm-pit;<BR>˚अंतर Pt. 1. the cavity of the<BR>armpit; प्रक्षिप्योदर्चिषं कक्षे शेरते तेऽ<BR>भिमारुतं Śi. 2. 42.<BR>--7 The harem of a<BR>king.<BR>--8 The interior of a forest;<BR>आश् निर्गत्य कक्षात् Rs. 1. 27;<BR>कक्षांतरगतो वायुः Rām.<BR>--9 The side or flank<BR>(of anything).<BR>--10 A woman's<BR>girdle; as in आबद्धनिबिडकक्षैः.<BR>--11 A<BR>surrounding wall.<BR>--12 A part of a<BR>boat.<BR>--13 The orbit of a planet.<BR>--14<BR>A buffalo.<BR>--15 A gate.<BR>--16 The<BR>Beleric Myrobalan or Terminalia<BR>Belerica.<BR>--17 A marshy ground.<BR>--क्षा<BR>1 Painful boils in the arm-pit.<BR>--2 An elephant's rope; also his<BR>girth.<BR>--3 A woman's girdle or zone;<BR>a girdle, waist-band (in general);<BR>Śi. 17. 24.<BR>--4 A surrounding wall;<BR>a wall.<BR>--5 The waist, middle part;<BR>Mk. 5. 21.<BR>--6 A courtyard; area.<BR>--7 An enclosure.<BR>--8 An inner<BR>apartment, a private chamber: room in<BR>general; Ku. 7. 70; Ms. 7. 224;<BR>गृहकलहंसकाननुसरन् कक्षांतरप्रधावितः<BR>K. 63, 182.<BR>--9 A harem.<BR>--10<BR>Similarity.<BR>--11 An upper garment.<BR>--12<BR>Objection or reply in argument (in<BR>Logic &c.).<BR>--13 Emulation or rivalry.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-c" target="_blank">Page0366-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--14 A secluded part of an edifice.<BR>--15 A particular part of a carriage.<BR>--16 The jeweller's weight, Retti.<BR>--17 The end of the lower garment<BR>which, after the cloth is girt round<BR>the lower part of the body, is<BR>brought up behind and tucked into<BR>the waistband (Mar. कांसोटा).<BR>--18<BR>Tying up the waist.<BR>--19 The<BR>wrist.<BR>--20 Border or lace.<BR>--21 The<BR>basin of a balance (कक्षः also).<BR>--क्षं<BR>1 A star.<BR>--2 Sin.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः<BR>wild fire, conflagration; R. 11. 92.<BR>--अंतरं inner or private apartment.<BR>--अवेक्षकः {1} a superintendent of<BR>the harem. {2} a keeper of a royal<BR>garden. {3} a doorkeeper. {4} a poet.<BR>{5} a debauchee. {6} a player;<BR>painter. {7} an actor. {8} a paramour.<BR>{9} strength of feeling or<BR>sentiment (Wilson).<BR>--उत्था a fragrant<BR>grass, (भद्रमुस्ता Cyperus).<BR>--धरं the<BR>shoulder-joint.<BR>--पः {1} a tortoise.<BR>{2} one of the 9 treasures of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--(क्षा) पटः a cloth passed<BR>between the legs to cover the privities.<BR>--पुटः the arm-pit.<BR>--रुहा = नागरमुस्ता<BR>q. v.<BR>--शायः --युः a dog.<BR>--स्थ a.<BR>seated on the hip or the flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षीकृत
कक्षीकृत a. Agreed to, promised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षायते
कक्षायते Den. A.<BR>1 To lie in<BR>ambush.<BR>--2 To intend anything wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्षीवत्|कक्षीवन्त्
कक्षीवत् m. N. of a renowned<BR>Ṛṣi, sometimes called Pajriya;<BR>author of several hymns of the<BR>Ṛgveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कक्ष्य|कक्ष्यं
कक्ष्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Consisting of<BR>shrubs or dry grass.<BR>--2 Secret.<BR>--3<BR>Filling the girth (Sāy.).<BR>--क्ष्या<BR>1 The<BR>girth of an elephant or horse.<BR>--2<BR>A woman's girdle or zone;<BR>Ki. 7. 8; Śi. 10. 62.<BR>--3 Fingers.<BR>--4<BR>The upper garment.<BR>--5 The<BR>border of a garment.<BR>--6 The inner<BR>apartment of a palace.<BR>--7 A wall,<BR>enclosure.<BR>--8 Similarity.<BR>--9 A shrub<BR>yielding the black and red berry<BR>that serves as a weight.<BR>--क्ष्यं<BR>1<BR>The cup or receptacle of a balance.<BR>--2 A part of a carriage.<BR>--3 The<BR>hinder part.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवेक्षक =<BR>कक्षावेक्षक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्
कख् {c1c} P. (कखति) To laugh at,<BR>deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कख्या
कख्या An enclosure; division of<BR>a large building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0366-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कग्
कग् {c1c} P. To act, perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंक्|कङ्क्
कंक् {c1c} A. To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंकः|कङ्क|कंक|कङ्कः
कंकः<BR>1 A heron.<BR>--2 A variety of<BR>mango.<BR>--3 N. of Yama.<BR>--4 A<BR>Kṣatriya.<BR>--5 A Vṛṣṇi.<BR>--6 A false<BR>or pretended Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--7 Name<BR>assumed by Yudhiṣṭhira in the<BR>palace of Virāṭa.<BR>--8 One of the 18<BR>divisions of the continent.<BR>--9 N. of<BR>a people (pl.)<BR>--का<BR>1 A sort of<BR>sandal.<BR>--2 Scent of the lotus.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--त्रोटः --टिः a kind of fish.<BR>--पत्र a. furnished with the feathers<BR>of a heron.<BR>--(त्रः) an arrow<BR>furnished with a heron's feathers;<BR>R. 2. 31; U. 4. 20; Mv. 1. 18.<BR>--(त्रं) a<BR>heron's feather fixed on an arrow.<BR>--पत्रिन् m. = कंकपत्रः.<BR>--माला {1} a<BR>kind of musical instrument. {2}<BR>beating time by the clapping of<BR>hands.<BR>--मुख वदन a. shaped like a<BR>heron's mouth. (--खः --खं), --वदनं a<BR>pair of tongs; Ve. 5. 1.<BR>--शायः a<BR>dog (sleeping like a heron).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंकटः|कङ्कट|कंकट|कङ्कटः
कंकटः, कंकटकः<BR>1 Mail; defensive<BR>armour; military accoutrements;<BR>Ve. 2. 26, 5. 1; R. 7. 59; Śi. 18. 20.<BR>--2 An iron hook to goad an<BR>elephant (अंकुश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंकटकः|कङ्कटक|कंकटक|कङ्कटकः
कंकटः, कंकटकः<BR>1 Mail; defensive<BR>armour; military accoutrements;<BR>Ve. 2. 26, 5. 1; R. 7. 59; Śi. 18. 20.<BR>--2 An iron hook to goad an<BR>elephant (अंकुश).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंकणः|कङ्कण|कंकण|कंकणं|कङ्कणं|कङ्कणः
कंकणः --णं<BR>1 A bracelet; दानेन<BR>पाणिर्न तु कंकणेन विभाति Bh. 2. 71; इदं<BR>सुवर्णकंकणं गृह्यतां H. 1.<BR>--2 The<BR>marriage string (fastened round the<BR>wrist); अयमागृहीतकमनीयकंकणः(करः)<BR>U. 1. 18; Māl. 9. 9; देव्यः<BR>कंकणमोक्षणाय भिलिता राजन् वरः प्रेष्यतां<BR>Mv. 2. 50.<BR>--3 An ornament in<BR>general.<BR>--4 A crest.<BR>--णः<BR>Waterspray; नितंबे हाराली नयनयुगले<BR>कंकणभरं Udb.<BR>--णी, कंकणीका<BR>1 A small<BR>bell or tinkling ornament.<BR>--2 An<BR>ornament furnished with bells<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भृषण a. adorned with<BR>tinkling ornaments.<BR>--मणी f. the<BR>jewel in a bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0367-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंकणं|कङ्कण|कंकण|कङ्कणं|कंकणः|कङ्कणः
