कंधः|कन्ध|कंध|कन्धः
कंधः<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंधरः|कन्धर|कंधर|कन्धरः
कंधरः [कं शिरो जलं वा धारयति]<BR>1<BR>The neck.<BR>--2 ‘The holder of water’,<BR>a cloud.<BR>--3 A kind of grass.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of a vegetable (मारिष).<BR>--रा The neck;<BR>कंधरां समपहाय कं धरां प्राप्य संयति जहास<BR>कस्यचित्; Y. 2. 220; Amaru. 16; see<BR>उत्कंधर also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंधिः|कन्धि|कंधि|कन्धिः
कंधिः [कं शिरो जलं वा धीयतेऽत्र] The<BR>ocean. --f. The neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्नं|कन्न
कन्नं [कन्-क्त]<BR>1 Sin.<BR>--2 A swoon,<BR>a fainting fit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यका
कन्यका<BR>1 A girl;<BR>संबद्धवैखानसकन्यकानि R. 14. 28; 11. 53.<BR>--2 An<BR>unmarried girl, virgin, maiden; गृहे<BR>गृहे पुरुषाः कुलकन्यकाः समुद्वहंति<BR>Māl. 7; Y. 1. 105.<BR>--3 A technical name<BR>for a girl ten years old; (<BR>अष्टवर्षा भवेद्गौरी नववर्षा च रोहिणी । दशमे<BR>कन्यका प्रोक्ता अत उर्ध्वं रजस्वला Śabdak.)<BR>--4 (In Rhet.) One of the several<BR>kinds of heroines; an unmarried<BR>girl serving as a chief character in a<BR>poetical composition; see under<BR>अन्यस्त्री.<BR>--5 The sign Virgo.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--छलः seduction: पैशाचः<BR>कन्यकाच्छलात् Y. 1. 61.<BR>--जनः a maiden;<BR>विशुद्धमुग्धः कुलकन्यकाजनः Māl. 7. 1.<BR>--जातः the son of an unmarried<BR>girl; Y. 2. 129 (= कानीन); for<BR>instance व्यास, कर्ण &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यना
कन्यना Ved. Calling a girl(<BR>कन्याह्वान); a girl (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यला
कन्यला Ved. A girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यसः|कन्यस
कन्यसः The youngest brother.<BR>--सा The little finger.<BR>--सी The<BR>youngest sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्या
कन्या [Uṇ. 4. 111]<BR>1 An<BR>unmarried girl or daughter; R. 1. 51,<BR>2. 10, 3. 33; Ms. 10. 8.<BR>--2 A girl<BR>ten years old.<BR>--3 A virgin, maiden;<BR>Ms. 8. 367, 3. 33.<BR>--4 A woman in<BR>general.<BR>--5 The sixth sign of the<BR>zodiac, i. e. Virgo.<BR>--6 N. of Durgā.<BR>--7 Large cardamoms.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतःपुरं the women's apartments;<BR>सुरक्षितेपि कन्यांतःपुरे कश्चित्प्रविशति<BR>Pt. 1; Mv. 2. 50.<BR>--आट a.<BR>following after or hunting young girls.<BR>--(टः) {1} the inner apartments of a<BR>house. {2} a man who hunts or goes<BR>alter young girls.<BR>--कुब्जः N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">Page0376-c+ 56</a>]<BR>country.<BR>--(ब्जं) N. of an ancient<BR>city in the north of India, situated<BR>on a tributary of the Ganges, now<BR>called Kanoja.<BR>--कुमारि f.,<BR>--री N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--गतं the position of a planet<BR>in the sign Virgo.<BR>--ग्रहणं taking a<BR>girl in marriage.<BR>--दानं giving away<BR>a girl in marriage.<BR>--दूषणं<BR>defilement of a virgin.<BR>--दोषः a defect or<BR>blemish in a girl, bad repute (such<BR>as a disease &c.).<BR>--धनं dowry.<BR>--पतिः<BR>‘daughter's husband’, a son-in-law.<BR>--पालः a dealer in slave girls.<BR>--पुत्रः,<BR>गभः the son of an unmarried daughter<BR>(called कानीन).<BR>--पुरं the women's<BR>apartments.<BR>--भर्तृ m. {1} a son-in-law.<BR>{2} N. of Kārtikeya.<BR>--रत्नं a very fine<BR>girl; कन्यारत्नमयोनिजन्म भवतामास्ते<BR>Mv. 1. 30.<BR>--राशिः the sign Virgo.<BR>--वेदिन् m. a son-in-law (marrying<BR>one's girl); Y. 1. 262.<BR>--शुल्कं money<BR>given to the bride's father as her<BR>price, purchase-money of a girl.<BR>--स्वयंवरः the choice of a husband<BR>by a maiden.<BR>--हरणं ravishment or<BR>seduction of a maiden; Ms. 3. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यका
कन्यका, कन्यिका<BR>1 Young girl.<BR>--2<BR>A virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यिका
कन्यका, कन्यिका<BR>1 Young girl.<BR>--2<BR>A virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यस|कन्यसः
कन्यस a. Younger.<BR>--सा The little<BR>finger.<BR>--सी The youngest sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्यामय
कन्यामय a. Consisting of, or in<BR>the form of, a young girl; R. 6. 11,<BR>16. 86.<BR>--यं The harem (consisting<BR>mostly of girls).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कन्युषं|कन्युष
कन्युषं The hand below the wrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कप्
कप् {c1c} P. To move see; कंप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कप
कप<BR>1 N. of वरुण.<BR>--2 A class of<BR>demons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटः|कपट|कपटं
कपटः, --टं Fraud, deceit, trick,<BR>cheating; कपटशतमयं क्षेत्रमप्रत्ययानां<BR>Pt. 1. 191; कपटानुसारकुशला<BR>Mk. 9. 5.<BR>--टी A measure equal to the<BR>capacity of the hollows of the two<BR>hands joined together.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तापसः one who pretends to be<BR>an ascetic, pseudo ascetic.<BR>--पटु a. adept in deceit, deceitful,<BR>crafty; छलयन् प्रजास्त्वमनृतेन<BR>कपटपटुरैंद्रजालिकः Śi. 15. 35.<BR>--प्रबंधः a<BR>fraudulent contrivance; H. 1.<BR>--लेख्यं a<BR>forged document.<BR>--वचनं deceitful<BR>talk.<BR>--वेश a. disguised, masked.<BR>--(शः) disguise, false dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटं|कपट|कपटः
कपटः, --टं Fraud, deceit, trick,<BR>cheating; कपटशतमयं क्षेत्रमप्रत्ययानां<BR>Pt. 1. 191; कपटानुसारकुशला<BR>Mk. 9. 5.<BR>--टी A measure equal to the<BR>capacity of the hollows of the two<BR>hands joined together.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तापसः one who pretends to be<BR>an ascetic, pseudo ascetic.<BR>--पटु a. adept in deceit, deceitful,<BR>crafty; छलयन् प्रजास्त्वमनृतेन<BR>कपटपटुरैंद्रजालिकः Śi. 15. 35.<BR>--प्रबंधः a<BR>fraudulent contrivance; H. 1.<BR>--लेख्यं a<BR>forged document.<BR>--वचनं deceitful<BR>talk.<BR>--वेश a. disguised, masked.<BR>--(शः) disguise, false dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटिकः|कपटिक
कपटिकः A rogue, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपटिन्
कपटिन् a. Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>--f. A kind of perfume (चिडा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0376-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपनः|कपन
कपनः Shaking.<BR>--नः --ना Ved.<BR>A worm, caterpillar (घुण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्दः|कपर्द|कपर्द्द|कपर्द्दः
कपर्दः, कपर्दकः<BR>1 A small shell<BR>or cowrie (used as a coin).<BR>--2<BR>Braided and matted hair, especially of<BR>Śiva; G. L. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्दकः|कपर्दक|कपर्द्दक|कपर्द्दकः
कपर्दः, कपर्दकः<BR>1 A small shell<BR>or cowrie (used as a coin).<BR>--2<BR>Braided and matted hair, especially of<BR>Śiva; G. L. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्दिका
कपर्दिका A small shell or cowrie<BR>(used as a coin); मित्राण्यमित्रतां<BR>यांति यस्य न स्युः कपर्दि(र्द)काः<BR>Pt. 2. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपर्दिन्|कपर्द्दिन्
कपर्दिन् a. [कपर्द-इनि]<BR>1 Shaggy.<BR>--2 Wearing braided and matted<BR>hair. --m. N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपलं|कपल
कपलं Ved. A half, a part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाटः|कपाट|कपाटं
कपाटः --टं [कं वातं पाटयति तद्गतिं<BR>रुणद्धि Tv.]<BR>1 Leaf or panel of a<BR>door; कपाठवक्षाः परिणद्धकंधरः<BR>R. 3. 34; स्वर्गद्वारकपाटपाटनपटुर्धर्मोपि<BR>नोपार्जितः Bh. 3. 11.<BR>--2 A door;<BR>Śi. 11. 60.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्धाटनं {1} the<BR>opening of a door. {2} a door-key.<BR>--घ्नः<BR>a house-breaker, thief.<BR>--वक्षस् a.<BR>broad-chested; R. 3. 34.<BR>--संधिः {1}<BR>the junction of the leaves of a door.<BR>{2} a manner of multiplying.<BR>--संधिकः a disease of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपाटं|कपाट|कपाटः
कपाटः --टं [कं वातं पाटयति तद्गतिं<BR>रुणद्धि Tv.]<BR>1 Leaf or panel of a<BR>door; कपाठवक्षाः परिणद्धकंधरः<BR>R. 3. 34; स्वर्गद्वारकपाटपाटनपटुर्धर्मोपि<BR>नोपार्जितः Bh. 3. 11.<BR>--2 A door;<BR>Śi. 11. 60.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्धाटनं {1} the<BR>opening of a door. {2} a door-key.<BR>--घ्नः<BR>a house-breaker, thief.<BR>--वक्षस् a.<BR>broad-chested; R. 3. 34.<BR>--संधिः {1}<BR>the junction of the leaves of a door.<BR>{2} a manner of multiplying.<BR>--संधिकः a disease of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालः|कपाल|कपालं
कपालः, --लं [कं शिरो जलं वा<BR>पालयति]<BR>1 The skull, skull-bone;<BR>चूडापीडकपालसंकुलगलन्मंदाकिनीवारयः<BR>Māl. 1. 2; रुद्रो येन कपालपाणिपुटके भिक्षाटनं<BR>कारितः Bh. 2. 95.<BR>--2 A piece of a<BR>broken jar, potsherd; कपालेन<BR>भिक्षार्थी Ms. 8. 93.<BR>--3 A multitude,<BR>collection.<BR>--4 A beggar's bowl;<BR>Ms. 6. 44.<BR>--5 A cup, jar in general;<BR>पंचकपाल.<BR>--6 A cover or lid.<BR>--7 A treaty<BR>of peace on equal terms.<BR>--लं<BR>1 The<BR>shell of an egg.<BR>--2 The cotyla of the<BR>leg of a man, any flat bone.<BR>--3 A kind<BR>of leprosy.<BR>--ली A beggar's bowl. [cf.<BR>L. caput; Gr. kephale].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नालिका a sort of pin or spindle<BR>for winding cotton &c.<BR>--पाणिः<BR>--भृत्, --मालिन्, --शिरस् m. epithets of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--मालिनी N. of Durgā.<BR>--संधिः<BR>a peace on equal terms, H. 4. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालं|कपाल|कपालः
कपालः, --लं [कं शिरो जलं वा<BR>पालयति]<BR>1 The skull, skull-bone;<BR>चूडापीडकपालसंकुलगलन्मंदाकिनीवारयः<BR>Māl. 1. 2; रुद्रो येन कपालपाणिपुटके भिक्षाटनं<BR>कारितः Bh. 2. 95.<BR>--2 A piece of a<BR>broken jar, potsherd; कपालेन<BR>भिक्षार्थी Ms. 8. 93.<BR>--3 A multitude,<BR>collection.<BR>--4 A beggar's bowl;<BR>Ms. 6. 44.<BR>--5 A cup, jar in general;<BR>पंचकपाल.<BR>--6 A cover or lid.<BR>--7 A treaty<BR>of peace on equal terms.<BR>--लं<BR>1 The<BR>shell of an egg.<BR>--2 The cotyla of the<BR>leg of a man, any flat bone.<BR>--3 A kind<BR>of leprosy.<BR>--ली A beggar's bowl. [cf.<BR>L. caput; Gr. kephale].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नालिका a sort of pin or spindle<BR>for winding cotton &c.<BR>--पाणिः<BR>--भृत्, --मालिन्, --शिरस् m. epithets of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--मालिनी N. of Durgā.<BR>--संधिः<BR>a peace on equal terms, H. 4. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिः|कपालि
कपालिः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिका
कपालिका<BR>1 A potsherd; Ms. 4. 78,<BR>8. 250.<BR>--2 The tartar of the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपालिन्
कपालिन् a.<BR>1 Furnished with or<BR>having a skull; Y. 3. 243.<BR>--2<BR>Wearing skulls; कपालि वा स्यादथवेंदुशेखरं<BR>(वपु) Ku. 5. 78. --m.<BR>1 An epithet<BR>of Śiva; करं कर्णे कुर्वंत्यपि किल<BR>कपालिप्रभृतयः G. L. 28.<BR>--2 A man of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-b" target="_blank">Page0377-b+ 57</a>]<BR>low caste (offspring of a Brāhmaṇa<BR>mother and fisherman father).<BR>--नी<BR>N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिः|कपि
कपिः [कंप्-इन् नलोपः;<BR>Uṇ. 4. 143.]<BR>1 An ape, a monkey;<BR>कपेरवासिषुर्नादात् Bk. 9. 11.<BR>--2 An<BR>elephant.<BR>--3 A species of Karañja.<BR>--4<BR>Incense, storax or impure benzoin<BR>(शिलारस).<BR>--5 The sun.<BR>--6 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--पिः f.<BR>--पी A female<BR>monkey.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आख्यः incense.<BR>--इज्यः an epithet of (1) Rāma;<BR>(2) of Sugrīva.<BR>--इंद्रः (the chief<BR>of monkeys) an epithet of (1)<BR>Hanūmat; नश्यंति ददर्श वृंदानि कपींद्रः<BR>Bk. 10. 12; (2) of Sugrīva; व्यर्थं<BR>यत्र कपींद्रसख्यमपि मे U. 3. 45; (3)<BR>of Jāmbavat.<BR>--कच्छुः f. N. of a<BR>plant.<BR>--कंदुकं the skull.<BR>--केतन,<BR>--ध्वजः N. of Arjuna; Bg. 1. 20.<BR>--चूडा, चूतः the hog-plum tree.<BR>--जः,--तैलं,--नामन् n. storax or benzoin.<BR>--प्रभुः {1} an epithet of Rāma. {2}<BR>of Sugrīva.<BR>--रथः an epithet of (1)<BR>Rāma; (2) Arjuna.<BR>--लोमन् f. a<BR>kind of perfume.<BR>--लोहं brass.<BR>--वक्त्रः<BR>N. of Nārada.<BR>--शाकः --कं a cabbage<BR>--शीर्षं the upper part (coping) of a<BR>wall.<BR>--शषिर्कं vermilion (Mar. हिंगुळ).<BR>--शीष्र्णी a kind of musical<BR>instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिंजलः|कपिञ्जल|कपिंजल|कपिञ्जलः
कपिंजलः<BR>1 The Cātaka bird.<BR>--2 The Tittiri bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपित्थः|कपित्थ
कपित्थः The wood-apple tree.<BR>--त्थं<BR>1 The fruit of the above tree.<BR>--2 A particular position of the<BR>hands and fingers.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्यः<BR>a kind of monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिल|कपिलः
कपिल a. [कपि-लच्]<BR>1 Tawny,<BR>reddish; वाताय कपिला विद्युत् Mbh.<BR>--2 Having tawny hair; Ms. 3. 8;<BR>(Kull. = कपिलकेशा).<BR>--लः<BR>1 N. of a<BR>great sage. [He reduced to ashes the<BR>60,000 sons of Sagara who, while<BR>searching for the sacrificial horse of their<BR>father taken away by Indra, fell in with<BR>him and accused him of having stolen it;<BR>(see U. 1. 23). He is also said to have<BR>been the founder of the Sāṃkhya system<BR>of philosophy].<BR>--2 A dog.<BR>--3 Benzoin.<BR>--4 Incense.<BR>--5 A form of fire.<BR>--6<BR>The tawny colour.<BR>--7 Impure<BR>benzoin.<BR>--8 N. of the sun.<BR>--9 N. of a<BR>country.<BR>--10 One of the<BR>incarnations of Viṣṇu.<BR>--ला<BR>1 A brown<BR>cow.<BR>--2 A kind of perfume.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of timber.<BR>--4 The common<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">Page0377-c+ 56</a>]<BR>leech.<BR>--5 N. of the female elephant<BR>of the south-east.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षी<BR>a kind of deer.<BR>--अंजनः N. of Śiva.<BR>--अश्वः an epithet of Indra.<BR>--आचार्यः Viṣṇu.<BR>--द्युतिः the sun.<BR>--द्राक्षा<BR>a vine with brown grapes.<BR>--द्रुमः<BR>a kind of perfume.<BR>--धारा {1} N. of the<BR>Ganges. {2} a holy place.<BR>--स्मृतिः<BR>f. the Sāṃkhya Sūtras of Kapila.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिश|कपिशः
कपिश a. [कपि-अत्वर्थे श]<BR>1 Brown,<BR>reddish-brown.<BR>--2 Reddish; (छायाः)<BR>संध्यापयोदकपिशाः पिशिताशनानां<BR>Ś. 3. 27; तोये कांचनपद्मरेणुकपिशे 7. 12;<BR>V. 2. 7; Me. 21; R. 12. 28.<BR>--शः<BR>1 The brown colour.<BR>--2 A<BR>compound of red and black colour.<BR>--3 Storax or coarse benzoin.<BR>--शा<BR>1 The Mādhavī creeper.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>river.<BR>--शा, --शी, --शं A spirit, a kind<BR>of rum.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजनः N. of Śiva.<BR>--अयनः {1} spirit, a kind of rum. {2}<BR>a deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशित
कपिशित a. Embrowned; Śi. 6. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशीका
कपिशीका A kind of liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपीतनः|कपीतन
कपीतनः N. of several plants:<BR>such as the holy fig-tree, the<BR>betelnut tree &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपुच्छलं|कपुच्छल
कपुच्छलं, कपुष्टका<BR>1 The<BR>ceremony of tonsure.<BR>--2 A patch of hair<BR>on each side of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपुष्टका
कपुच्छलं, कपुष्टका<BR>1 The<BR>ceremony of tonsure.<BR>--2 A patch of hair<BR>on each side of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपूय
कपूय a. Mean, worthless,<BR>abject, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतः|कपोत
कपोतः [को वायुः पोत इव यस्य Tv.]<BR>1<BR>A dove, pigeon.<BR>--2 A bird in<BR>general.<BR>--3 A particular position of the<BR>hands.<BR>--4 The grey colour of a pigeon.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंघ्रिः f. a sort of perfume.<BR>--अंजनं antimony.<BR>--अरिः a hawk,<BR>falcon.<BR>--आभ a. of the colour of a<BR>pigeon.<BR>--(भः) a pale or dirty white<BR>colour.<BR>--चरणा a sort of perfume.<BR>--पालिका,--पाली f. an aviary, a<BR>pigeon-house, dove-cot.<BR>--राजः the<BR>king of pigeons.<BR>--वर्णी small<BR>cardamoms.<BR>--वाणा a kind of perfume.<BR>--सारं antimony.<BR>--हस्तः a mode of<BR>folding the hands in supplication,<BR>fear &c.; कपोतहस्तकं कृत्वा Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतकः|कपोतक|कपोतकं
कपोतकः<BR>1 A small pigeon.<BR>--2 A<BR>mode of folding the hands together.<BR>--कं Antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोतकीया
कपोतकीया A place abounding in<BR>pigeons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोती
कपोती<BR>1 A female pigeon.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of sacrificial post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपोलः|कपोल
कपोलः [Uṇ. 1. 66] A cheek;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">Page0378-a+ 56</a>]<BR>क्षामक्षामकपोलमाननं Ś. 3. 10,<BR>6. 14; R. 4. 68.<BR>--ली The knee-cap.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काषः any object against<BR>which anything (especially the<BR>cheeks) is rubbed; Ki. 5. 36.<BR>--फलकः<BR>the (broad) cheeks.<BR>--भित्तिः f. the<BR>temples and cheeks; or excellent (i. e.<BR>broad) cheeks; cf. गंडमित्ति.<BR>--रागः<BR>the flush in the cheek.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0377-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफः|कफ
कफः [केन जलेन फलति फल्-ड Tv.]<BR>1<BR>Phlegm, one of the three humours<BR>of the body (the other two being<BR>वात and पित्त);<BR>कफापचयादारोग्यैकमूलमाशयाग्निदीप्तिः Dk. 160; प्राणप्रयाणसमये<BR>कफवातपित्तैः कंठावरोधनविधौ स्मरणं<BR>कुतस्ते Udb.<BR>--2 A watery foam or<BR>froth in general.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः<BR>dry ginger.<BR>--कूर्चिका saliva,<BR>spittle.<BR>--क्षयः pulmonary consumption.<BR>--घ्न, --नाशन, --हर a. removing phlegm,<BR>antiphlegmatic.<BR>--ज्वरः fever caused<BR>by excess of phlegm.<BR>--विरोधिन् m.<BR>pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफल
कफल a. Phlegmatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफिन्
कफिन् a. (नी f.) [कफ-इनि]<BR>Affected with excess of phlegm,<BR>phlegmatic. --m. An elephant (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफणिः|कफणि
कफणिः, कफोणिः (णी f.) The<BR>elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफोणिः|कफोणि
कफणिः, कफोणिः (णी f.) The<BR>elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफेलू
कफेलू a. Phlegmatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कफौडः|कफौड
कफौडः Ved. The elbow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कब्
कब् {c1c} P. (कबति, कबित)<BR>1 To colour.<BR>--2 To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबंधः|कबन्ध|कबंध|कबंधं|कबन्धं|कबन्धः
कबंधः, --धं A headless trunk<BR>(especially when it retains life);<BR>(स्वं) नृत्यत्कबंधं समरे ददर्श R. 7. 51,<BR>12. 49.<BR>--धः<BR>1 The belly.<BR>--2 A<BR>cloud.<BR>--3 A comet.<BR>--4 N. of Rāhu.<BR>--5 Water (said to be n. also in this<BR>sense); Śi. 16. 67.<BR>--6 N. of a mighty<BR>demon mentioned in the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>[While Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa lived in<BR>the Daṇḍakā forest, Kabandha attacked<BR>them and was slain by them. It is said<BR>that, though at first a heavenly being, he<BR>was cursed by Indra to assume the form<BR>of a demon and to be in that state till<BR>killed by Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa. He<BR>advised Rāma to form friendship with<BR>Sugrīva; see R. 12. 57].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबंधं|कबन्ध|कबंध|कबन्धं|कबंधः|कबन्धः
कबंधः, --धं A headless trunk<BR>(especially when it retains life);<BR>(स्वं) नृत्यत्कबंधं समरे ददर्श R. 7. 51,<BR>12. 49.<BR>--धः<BR>1 The belly.<BR>--2 A<BR>cloud.<BR>--3 A comet.<BR>--4 N. of Rāhu.<BR>--5 Water (said to be n. also in this<BR>sense); Śi. 16. 67.<BR>--6 N. of a mighty<BR>demon mentioned in the Rāmāyaṇa.<BR>[While Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa lived in<BR>the Daṇḍakā forest, Kabandha attacked<BR>them and was slain by them. It is said<BR>that, though at first a heavenly being, he<BR>was cursed by Indra to assume the form<BR>of a demon and to be in that state till<BR>killed by Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa. He<BR>advised Rāma to form friendship with<BR>Sugrīva; see R. 12. 57].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबंधिन्|कबन्धिन्
कबं(वं)धिन् a. ‘Endowed with<BR>water’, epithet of the Maruts. --m.<BR>N. of Kātyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवंधिन्
कबं(वं)धिन् a. ‘Endowed with<BR>water’, epithet of the Maruts. --m.<BR>N. of Kātyāyana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबर
कबर, --री Usually written कवर,<BR>--री q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबरी
कबर, --री Usually written कवर,<BR>--री q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबित्थः|कबित्थ
कबित्थः The wood-apple tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबिल|कबिलः
कबिल a. Tawny.<BR>--लः The tawny<BR>colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबुलिः|कबुलि
कबुलिः f. The hinder part of an<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कम् ind. Ved. A particle used<BR>as an expletive or enclitic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्
कम् {c1c} {c10c} A. (कामयते, कामित,<BR>चकमे-कामयांचक्रे, कांत)<BR>1 To love, be<BR>enamoured of, be in love with; कन्ये<BR>कामयमानं मां न त्वं कामयसे कथं<BR>Kāv. 1. 63 (an instance of ग्राम्यता);<BR>कलहंसको मंदारिकां कामयते Māl. 1.<BR>--2 To<BR>long for, wish, desire; न<BR>वीरसूशब्दमकामयेतां R. 14. 4; निष्क्रष्टुमर्थं चकमे<BR>कुबेरात् 5. 26; 4. 48; 10. 53;<BR>Bk. 14. 82.<BR>--3 To have intercourse with.<BR>--4 To value highly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमन|कमनं|कमनः
कमन a. [कम्-युच्]<BR>1 Lustful,<BR>libidinous.<BR>--2 Wishing for, desirous;<BR>Śi. 6. 74.<BR>--3 Lovely, beautiful.<BR>--नः<BR>1<BR>Cupid, the god of love.<BR>--2 The<BR>Aśoka tree.<BR>--3 N. of Brahmā.<BR>--4 A<BR>Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--छदः a heron<BR>(having beautiful plumage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमनीय|कमनीयं
कमनीय a.<BR>1 To be desired,<BR>desirable; अनन्यनारीकमनीयमंकं Ku. 1. 37.<BR>--2 Lovely, charming, beautiful;<BR>शाखावसक्तकमनीयपरिच्छदानां<BR>Ki. 7. 40; तदपि कमनीयं वपुरिदं Ś. 3. 9 v. {1}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमर|कमरः
कमर a. [कम्-अरच्] Lustful,<BR>desirous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमा
कमा Beauty, loveliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमितृ
कमितृ a. (त्री f.) Lustful, libidinous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कम्र|कम्रः
कम्र a.<BR>1 Desirous.<BR>--2 Beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमठः|कमठ|कमठं
कमठः [Uṇ. 1. 100]<BR>1 A tortoise;<BR>संप्राप्तः कमठः स चापि नियतं<BR>नष्टस्तवादेशतः Pt. 2. 184.<BR>--2 A bamboo.<BR>--3<BR>A water-jar.<BR>--ठी A female tortoise<BR>or a small tortoise.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिः a<BR>king of tortoises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमंडलुः|कमण्डलु|कमंडलु|कमण्डलुः
कमंडलुः, --लु n. A water-pot<BR>(earthen or wooden) used by ascetics;<BR>कमंडलूपमोऽमात्यस्तनुत्यागो बहुग्रहः<BR>H. 2. 91; कमंडलुनोदकं सिक्त्वा;<BR>Ms. 2. 64; Y. 1. 133.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तरुः the<BR>tree of which Kamaṇḍalus are made.<BR>--धरः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमंडलु|कमण्डलु|कमंडलुः|कमण्डलुः
कमंडलुः, --लु n. A water-pot<BR>(earthen or wooden) used by ascetics;<BR>कमंडलूपमोऽमात्यस्तनुत्यागो बहुग्रहः<BR>H. 2. 91; कमंडलुनोदकं सिक्त्वा;<BR>Ms. 2. 64; Y. 1. 133.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तरुः the<BR>tree of which Kamaṇḍalus are made.<BR>--धरः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमल|कमलं|कमलः
कमल a.<BR>1 Desirous.<BR>--2<BR>Palered.<BR>--लः<BR>1 The Sārasa bird.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of deer.<BR>--3 N. of Brahmā.<BR>--ली<BR>A collection of lotuses.<BR>--लं [<BR>कम्कलच्]<BR>1 A lotus; कमलमनंभसि कमले च<BR>कुवलये तानि कनकलतिकायां K. P. 10;<BR>so हस्त˚, नेत्र˚, चरण˚, &c.<BR>--2 Water;<BR>N. 1. 130; Ki. 5. 25.<BR>--3 Copper.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">Page0378-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--4 A medicament, drug.<BR>--5 The<BR>Sārasa bird.<BR>--6 The bladder, the<BR>right lobe of the lungs.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षी a lotus-eyed lady.<BR>--आकर;<BR>{1} an assemblage of lotuses. {2} a<BR>lake full of lotuses.<BR>--आलया an<BR>epithet of Lakṣmī; Mu. 2.<BR>--आसनः<BR>‘lotus-seated’ N. of Brahmā;<BR>कांतानि पूर्वं कमलासनेन Ku. 7. 70.<BR>--ईक्षणा<BR>a lotus-eyed lady.<BR>--उत्तरं safflower.<BR>--खंडं an assemblage of lotuses.<BR>--जं<BR>{1} an epithet of Brahmā. {2} the lunar<BR>asterism called Rohiṇī.<BR>--जन्मन् m.,<BR>--भवः, --योनिः, --संभवः ‘lotus-born’,<BR>epithets of Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलकं|कमलक
कमलकं A small lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमला
कमला<BR>1 An epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>--2 An excellent woman.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिः, --सखः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कमलिनी
कमलिनी<BR>1 A lotus-plant;<BR>साभ्रेऽह्नीव स्थलकमलिनीं न प्रबुद्धां न सुप्तां<BR>Me. 90; रम्यांतरः कमलिनीहरितैः सरोभिः<BR>Ś. 4. 10; R. 9. 30, 19. 11.<BR>--2 An<BR>assemblage of lotuses.<BR>--3 A place<BR>abounding with lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंप्|कम्प्
कंप् {c1c} A. (कंपते चकंपे, कंपित) To<BR>shake, tremble, move about; (fig.<BR>also); चकंपे तीर्णलौहित्ये तस्मिन्<BR>प्राग्ज्योतिषेश्वरः R. 4. 81; Mk. 4. 8;<BR>Bk. 14. 31, 15. 70. --Caus.<BR>1 To shake,<BR>cause to tremble.<BR>--2 To utter with a<BR>thrill or shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंपः|कम्प|कंप|कम्पः
कंपः [कंप्-घञ्]<BR>1 Shaking, tremor;<BR>कंपेन किंचित्प्रतिगृह्य मूर्ध्नः R. 13. 44<BR>with a gentle nod or bend of the<BR>head; 13. 28; Ku. 7. 46; भयकंपः,<BR>विद्युत्कंपः &c.<BR>--2 A modification of<BR>the Svarita accent.<BR>--पा Shaking,<BR>moving, tremor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वित a.<BR>tremulous, agitated.<BR>--लक्ष्मन् m. wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंपन|कम्पन|कम्पनं|कम्पनः
कंपन a. [कंप्-युच्] Trembling,<BR>shaking.<BR>--नः<BR>1 Śiśira season<BR>(November-December).<BR>--2 A kind of missile.<BR>--3 A kind of fever (सान्निपातिक).<BR>--नं<BR>1 Shaking, tremor.<BR>--2<BR>Quivering pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंपाकः|कम्पाक|कंपाक|कम्पाकः
कंपाकः Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंपिल्ल
कंपिल्ल = कांपिल्ल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंपित|कम्पित|कम्पितं
कंपित p. p.<BR>1 Trembling, shaking.<BR>--2 Shaken, swung.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Trembling,<BR>tremor.<BR>--2 Causing to shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंप्र|कम्प्र
कंप्र a. [कंप्-र]<BR>1 Shaking,<BR>tremulous, moving, agitating; विधाय कंप्राणि<BR>मुखानि कं प्रति N. 1. 142; कंप्रा शाखा<BR>Sk.<BR>--2 Agile, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंब्|कम्ब्
कंब् {c1c} P. (कंबति, कंबित) To go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0378-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबर|कम्बर|कम्बरः
कंबर a. Variegated.<BR>--रः<BR>Variegated colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबलः|कम्बल|कंबल|कम्बलं|कम्बलः
कंबलः [Uṇ. 1. 106]<BR>1 A blanket<BR>(of wool); कंबलवंतं न बाधते शीतं<BR>Subhāṣ.; कंबलावृतेन तेन H. 3.<BR>--2 A<BR>dewlap.<BR>--3 A sort of deer.<BR>--4 An upper<BR>garment of wool.<BR>--5 A wall.<BR>--6 A small<BR>worm.<BR>--लं Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वाह्यकं<BR>a kind of carriage covered with a<BR>coarse blanket, and drawn by oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबलकः|कम्बलक|कंबलकं|कम्बलकः
कंबलकः, --कं A woollen cloth,<BR>blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबलकं|कम्बलक|कंबलकः|कम्बलकः
कंबलकः, --कं A woollen cloth,<BR>blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबलिका
कंबलिका<BR>1 A small blanket.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of female deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबलिन्|कम्बलिन्
कंबलिन् a. Covered with a blanket.<BR>--m. A bullock, ox.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वाह्यकं a carriage covered with blankets<BR>and drawn by oxen, a bullock-cart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबिः|कम्बि|कम्बिः
कंबिः --बी f.<BR>1 A ladle or spoon.<BR>--2 A shoot.<BR>--3 A branch or joint of<BR>a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबी
कंबिः --बी f.<BR>1 A ladle or spoon.<BR>--2 A shoot.<BR>--3 A branch or joint of<BR>a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबु|कम्बु|कम्बुः
कंबु a. (बु or बू f.) Spotted,<BR>variegated.<BR>--बुः --बु (m., n.) A<BR>conch, shell; स्मरस्य कंबुः किमयं<BR>चकास्ति दिवि त्रिलोकीजयवादनीयः<BR>N. 22. 22; Śi. 18. 54.<BR>--बुः<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>--2<BR>The neck.<BR>--3 The variegated colour.<BR>--4 A vein of the body.<BR>--5 A bracelet.<BR>--6 A tube-shaped bone.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आतायिन् m. a kind of kite.<BR>--कंठी a lady having the neck like a<BR>conch-shell.<BR>--ग्रीवा {1} a conch-shaped<BR>neck, (i. e. a neck marked with<BR>three lines like a shell and<BR>considered as a sign of great fortune). {2} a<BR>lady having the neck like the<BR>conchshell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबुकः|कम्बुक|कम्बुकः
कंबुकः<BR>1 A conch, shell.<BR>--2 A<BR>mean or contemptible person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबू|कम्बू
कंबू a. Stealing. --m.<BR>1 A thief,<BR>plunderer.<BR>--2 A bracelet; cf.<BR>Uṇ. 1. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंबोजः|कम्बोज|कंबोज|कम्बोजः
कंबोजः<BR>1 A shell.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>elephant.<BR>--3 (pl.) N. of a country<BR>and its inhabitants; कंबोजाः समरे<BR>सोढुं तस्य वीर्यमनीश्वराः R. 4. 69 v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कंभु|कम्भु
कंभु n. The fragrant root (उशीर)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कयाधूः
कयाधूः f. The wife of<BR>Hiraṇyakaśipu and mother of Prahlāda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर|करः
कर a. (रा or री) [करोति, कीर्यते<BR>अनेन इति, कृ-कॄ-अप्] (Mostly at the end<BR>of comp.) Who or what does, makes<BR>or causes &c; दुःख˚, सुख˚, भयं˚ &c.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A hand; करं व्याधुन्वत्याः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-b" target="_blank">Page0379-b+ 57</a>]<BR>पिबसि रतिसर्वस्वमधरं Ś. 1. 24.<BR>--2 A ray<BR>of light, beam; यमुद्धर्तुं पूषा व्यवसित<BR>इवालंबितकरः V. 4. 34; also<BR>प्रतिकूलतामुपगते हि विधौ विफलत्वमेति बहुसाधनता ।<BR>अवलंबनाय दिनभर्तुरभून्न पतिष्यतः<BR>करसहस्रमपि Śi. 9. 6 (where the word is<BR>used in sense 1 also).<BR>--3 The trunk<BR>of an elephant; सेकः सीकरिणा करेण<BR>विहितः U. 3. 16; Bh. 3. 20.<BR>--4 A tax, toll, tribute; युवा<BR>कराक्रांतमहीभृदुच्चकैरसंशयं संप्रति तेजसा रविः<BR>Śi. 1. 70; (where कर means ‘ray’ also)<BR>(ददौ) अपरांतमहीपालव्याजेन रघवे करं<BR>R. 4. 58; Ms. 7. 128.<BR>--5 Hail.<BR>--6 A<BR>particular measure of length equal<BR>to 24 thumbs.<BR>--7 The asterism called<BR>हस्त.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रं {1} the forepart of<BR>the hand. {2} the tip of an elephant's<BR>trunk.<BR>--आघातः a stroke or blow with<BR>the hand.<BR>--आरोटः a finger-ring<BR>--आलंबः supporting with the hand,<BR>giving a helping hand.<BR>--आस्फोटः<BR>{1} the chest. {2} a blow with the<BR>hand.<BR>--ऋद्धिः f. {1} a cymbal. {2} a<BR>small musical instrument.<BR>--कंटकः, -कं<BR>a fingernail.<BR>--कमलं, --पंकजं, --पद्मं a<BR>lotus-like hand, beautiful hand;<BR>करकमलवितीर्णैरंबुनीवारशष्पैः U. 3. 25.<BR>--कलशः, शं the hollow of the hand<BR>(to receive water).<BR>--किसलयः, --यं {1}<BR>‘sprout-like hand’, a tender hand;<BR>करकिसलयतालैर्मुग्धया नर्त्यमानं<BR>U. 3. 19; Rs. 6. 30. {2} a finger.<BR>--कुड्मलं<BR>the finger.<BR>--कोषः the cavity of the<BR>palms, hands hollowed to receive<BR>water; ˚पेयमंबु Ghaṭ. 22.<BR>--ग्रहः,<BR>--ग्रहणं {1} levying a tax. {2} taking the<BR>hand in marriage. {3} marriage.<BR>--ग्राहः {1} a husband. {2} a tax-collector.<BR>--घर्षणः, --घर्षिन् m. the churning-stick.<BR>--छदः the teak tree.<BR>--जः a<BR>fingernail; तीक्ष्णकरजक्षुण्णात् Ve. 4. 1;<BR>Śi. 11. 37; Bv. 1. 105; Amaru. 85.<BR>--(जं)<BR>a kind of perfume.<BR>--जालं a stream<BR>of light.<BR>--तलः the palm of the hand;<BR>वनदेवताकरतलैः Ś. 4. 4; करतलगतमपि<BR>नश्यति यस्य तु भवितव्यता नारित<BR>Pt. 2. 124. ˚आमलकं (lit.) an āmalaka fruit<BR>(fruit of the Myrobalan) placed on<BR>the palm of the hand; (fig.) ease and<BR>clearness of perception, such as is<BR>natural in the case of a fruit placed<BR>on the palm of the hand;<BR>करतलामलकफलवदखिलं जगदालोकयतां K. 43.<BR>˚स्थ a. resting on the palm of the hand.<BR>--तालः, --तालकं {1} clapping the hands;<BR>स जहास दत्तकरतालमुच्चकैः Śi. 15. 39.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-c" target="_blank">Page0379-c+ 57</a>]<BR>{2} a kind of musical instrument,<BR>perhaps a cymbal.<BR>--तालिका, --ताली<BR>{1} clapping the hands; उच्चाटनीयः<BR>करतालिकानां दानादिदानीं भवतीभिरेषः<BR>N. 3. 7. {2} beating time by clapping<BR>the hands.<BR>--तोया N. of a river.<BR>--द a. {1} paying taxes {2} tributary;<BR>करदीकृताखिलनृपां मेदिनीं Ve. 6. 18.<BR>{3} giving the hand to help &c.<BR>--दक्ष<BR>a. handy, dexterous.<BR>--पत्रं {1} a saw.<BR>{2} playing in water. ˚वत् m. the<BR>palm tree.<BR>--पत्रकं a saw.<BR>--पत्रिका<BR>splashing water about while<BR>bathing or sporting in it.<BR>--पल्लवः {1} a<BR>tender hand. {2} a finger; cf.<BR>˚किसलय.<BR>--पालः, पालिका {1} a sword. {2} a<BR>cudgel.<BR>--पात्रं {1} splashing water<BR>about while bathing. {2} the hand<BR>hollowed to hold anything.<BR>--पीडनं<BR>marriage; cf. पाणिपीडन.<BR>--पुटः the<BR>hands joined and hollowed to receive<BR>anything.<BR>--पृष्ठं the back of the<BR>hand.<BR>--बालः, --वालः {1} sword;<BR>अघोरघंटः करवालपाणिर्व्यापादितः Māl. 9;<BR>म्लेच्छनिवहनिधने कलयसि करवालम्<BR>Gīt. 1, Śi. 13. 60. {2} a fingernail.<BR>--भारः<BR>a large amount of tribute.<BR>--भूः a<BR>fingernail.<BR>--भूषणं an ornament<BR>worn round the wrist, such as a<BR>bracelet.<BR>--मालः smoke.<BR>--मुक्तं a kind<BR>of weapon; see आयुध.<BR>--रुहः {1} a<BR>fingernail; अनाघ्रातं पुष्पं किसलयमलूनं<BR>कररुहैः Ś. 2. 10; Me. 96. {2} a sword.<BR>--वालिका a small club.<BR>--वीरः,<BR>--वीरकः {1} a sword or scimitar. {2} a<BR>cemetery. {3} N. of a town in the<BR>S. M. country. {4} a kind of tree.<BR>--(रा)<BR>red arsenic.<BR>--(री) {1} a woman who<BR>has borne a son, a mother {2} N. of<BR>Aditi. {3} a good cow.<BR>--(रं) the<BR>flower of the tree.<BR>--शाखा a finger.<BR>--शीकरः water thrown out by an<BR>elephant's trunk.<BR>--शूकः a fingernail.<BR>--शोथः swelling of the hands.<BR>--सादः<BR>{1} weakness of the hand. {2} the<BR>fading of rays.<BR>--सूत्रं a marriage string<BR>worn round the wrist.<BR>--स्थालिन् m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--स्वनः clapping<BR>of the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकः|करक|करकं
करकः, --कं [किरति करोति वा जलमत्र,<BR>कॄ-कृ-वुन् Tv.]<BR>1 The water-pot (of an<BR>ascetic); K. 41.<BR>--2 The shell of the<BR>cocoa-nut (used as a pot).<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>The pomegranate tree.<BR>--2 Hand.<BR>--3 Tax.<BR>--4 A kind of bird.<BR>--कः,<BR>का, --कं Hail;<BR>तान्कुर्वीथास्तुमुलकरकावृष्टिपातावकीर्णान् Me. 54; Bv. 1. 35;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">Page0380-a+ 55</a>]<BR>U. 3. 40.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंभस् m. the<BR>cocoa-nut tree.<BR>--आसारः a shower<BR>of hail.<BR>--जं water.<BR>--पात्रिका a<BR>water-pot used by ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करकं|करक|करकः
करकः, --कं [किरति करोति वा जलमत्र,<BR>कॄ-कृ-वुन् Tv.]<BR>1 The water-pot (of an<BR>ascetic); K. 41.<BR>--2 The shell of the<BR>cocoa-nut (used as a pot).<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>The pomegranate tree.<BR>--2 Hand.<BR>--3 Tax.<BR>--4 A kind of bird.<BR>--कः,<BR>का, --कं Hail;<BR>तान्कुर्वीथास्तुमुलकरकावृष्टिपातावकीर्णान् Me. 54; Bv. 1. 35;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">Page0380-a+ 55</a>]<BR>U. 3. 40.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंभस् m. the<BR>cocoa-nut tree.<BR>--आसारः a shower<BR>of hail.<BR>--जं water.<BR>--पात्रिका a<BR>water-pot used by ascetics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0379-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंकः|करङ्क|करंक|करङ्कः
करंकः<BR>1 A skeleton.<BR>--2 The skull;<BR>प्रेतरंकः करंकादंकस्थादस्थिसंस्थं<BR>स्थपुटगतमपि क्रव्यमव्यग्रमत्ति Māl. 5. 16; also<BR>5. 19.<BR>--3 A small pot (of cocoa-nut);<BR>a small box, as in तांबूलकरकंवाहिनी<BR>(used in Kādambarī).<BR>--4 A kind<BR>of sugar-cane.<BR>--5 Any bone of the<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंजः|करञ्ज|करंज|करञ्जः
करंजः [कंशिरो जलं वा रंजयति Tv.]<BR>N. of a tree (used in medicinal<BR>preparations).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटः|करट
करटः [किरति मदं, कॄ-अटन् Uṇ. 4. 81]<BR>1 An elephant's cheek.<BR>--2 Safflower.<BR>--3 A crow; Śānti. 4. 19.<BR>--4 An atheist,<BR>unbeliever.<BR>--5 A degraded<BR>Brāhmaṇa<BR>--6 A man of a low<BR>profession.<BR>--7 A musical instrument.<BR>--8 The first Śrāddha ceremony<BR>performed in honor of a dead man.<BR>--टा<BR>1 An elephant's cheek.<BR>--2 A<BR>cow difficult to be milked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटकः|करटक
करटकः<BR>1 A crow; Mk. 7.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>कर्णीरथ the propounder of the science<BR>and art of theft.<BR>--3 N. of a jackal in<BR>H. and Pt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटिन्
करटिन् m. An elephant; दिगंते श्रूयंते<BR>मदमलिनगंडाः करटिनः Bv. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करटुः|करटु
कर(रे)टुः A kind of bird<BR>(crane).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेटुः|करेटु
कर(रे)टुः A kind of bird<BR>(crane).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करण|करणं|करणः
करण a. [कृ-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Making,<BR>doing, effecting, producing.<BR>--2 (Ved.)<BR>Clever, skilled.<BR>--णः<BR>1 (Ved.) An<BR>assistant.<BR>--2 A man of a mixed tribe.<BR>--3 A writer.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Doing,<BR>performing, accomplishing, effecting; परहित˚,<BR>संध्या˚, प्रिय˚ &c.<BR>--2 Act, action.<BR>--3<BR>Religious action.<BR>--4 Business, trade.<BR>--5 An organ of sense; वपुषा<BR>करणोज्झितेन सा निपतंती पतिमप्यंपातयत्<BR>R. 8. 38, 42; पटुकरणैः प्राणिभिः Me. 5;<BR>R. 14. 50.<BR>--6 The body;<BR>उपमानमभूद्विलासिनां करणं यत्तव कांतिमत्तंया<BR>Ku. 4. 5.<BR>--7 An instrument or means of<BR>an action; उपमितिकरणमुपमानं T. S.<BR>--8 (In Logic) The instrumental<BR>cause which is thus defined:<BR>--व्यापारवदसाधारणं कारणं करणं.<BR>--9 A cause<BR>or motive (in general).<BR>--10 The<BR>sense expressed by the instrumental<BR>case (in gram.); साधकतमं करणं<BR>P. I. 4. 42; or क्रियायाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">Page0380-b+ 56</a>]<BR>परिनिष्पत्तिर्यद्व्यापारादनंतरम् । विवक्ष्यते यदा यत्र करणं<BR>तत्तदा स्मृतम् ॥.<BR>--11 (In law) A<BR>document, a bond, documentary proof;<BR>Ms. 8. 51, 52, 154.<BR>--12 A kind of<BR>rhythmical pause, beat of the hand<BR>to keep time; Ku. 6. 40.<BR>--13 (In<BR>astrol.) A division of the day; (these<BR>Karaṇas are eleven).<BR>--14 The<BR>Supreme Being.<BR>--15 Pronunciation.<BR>--16<BR>The posture of an ascetic.<BR>--17 A<BR>posture in sexual enjoyment.<BR>--18<BR>A field.<BR>--19 Plastering with the<BR>hand.<BR>--20 The usage of the writer<BR>caste.<BR>--णी<BR>1 A woman of a mixed<BR>caste.<BR>--2 A surd or irrational<BR>number.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः the soul.<BR>--ग्रामः the organs of sense taken<BR>collectively.<BR>--त्राणं the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंडः|करण्ड|करंड|करण्डः
करंडः [कृ-अंडन् Uṇ. 1. 126]<BR>1 A<BR>small box or basket (of bamboo);<BR>करंडपीडिततनोः भोगिनः Bh. 2. 84;<BR>सर्वमायाकरंडं 1. 77.<BR>--2 A bee-hive.<BR>--3 A<BR>sword.<BR>--4 A sort of duck (कारंडव).<BR>--5 Liver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंडकः|करण्डक|करण्डकः
करंडकः, --करंडिका, करंडी f. A small<BR>box made of bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंडिका
करंडकः, --करंडिका, करंडी f. A small<BR>box made of bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंडी
करंडकः, --करंडिका, करंडी f. A small<BR>box made of bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंडिन्|करण्डिन्
करंडिन् m. A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंधय
करंधय a. Kissing the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभः|करभ
करभः [कृ-अभच् Uṇ. 3. 122; करे<BR>भाति, भा-क Tv.]<BR>1 The back of the<BR>hand from the wrist to the root of<BR>the fingers; metacarpus; as in<BR>करभोरूः R. 6. 83; see करभोरू below.<BR>--2<BR>The trunk of an elephant.<BR>--3 A<BR>young elephant.<BR>--4 A young camel;<BR>Śi. 5. 3.<BR>--5 A camel in general.<BR>--6 A kind of perfume.<BR>--भी A<BR>shecamel.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ऊरूः f. a lady<BR>whose thighs resemble the back of<BR>the fore-arm; अंके निधाय करभोरु<BR>यथासुखं ते Ś. 3. 21; Śi. 10. 69;<BR>Amaru. 69; or (according to another<BR>explanation), whose thighs resemble the<BR>trunk of an elephant; cf. Ku. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभकः|करभक
करभकः A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभिन्
करभिन् m. An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करभीरः|करभीर
करभीरः A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमट्टः|करमट्ट
करमट्टः The betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करमरिन्
करमरिन् m. A prisoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंब|करम्ब|करंबः|करम्बः
करंब, करंबित a. [कृ-अंबच्;<BR>Uṇ. 4. 82]<BR>1 Mixed, intermingled,<BR>variegated; प्रकाममादित्यमवाप्य कंटकैः<BR>करंबितामोदभरं विवृण्वती N. 1. 115, 85;<BR>स्फुटतरफेनकदंबकरंबितमिव यमुनाजलपूरं<BR>Gīt. 11.<BR>--2 Set, inlaid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंबित|करम्बित|करम्बितः
करंब, करंबित a. [कृ-अंबच्;<BR>Uṇ. 4. 82]<BR>1 Mixed, intermingled,<BR>variegated; प्रकाममादित्यमवाप्य कंटकैः<BR>करंबितामोदभरं विवृण्वती N. 1. 115, 85;<BR>स्फुटतरफेनकदंबकरंबितमिव यमुनाजलपूरं<BR>Gīt. 11.<BR>--2 Set, inlaid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंभः|करम्भ|करंभ|करम्भः
करंभः(बः)<BR>1 Flour or meal<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">Page0380-c+ 56</a>]<BR>mixed with curds.<BR>--2 Mud;<BR>करंभवालुकातापान् Ms. 12. 76 (where the word is<BR>variously interpreted; but Medhātithi<BR>takes it to mean ‘mud’).<BR>--3 Groats<BR>or coarsely ground oats.<BR>--4 A mixed<BR>odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंबः|करम्ब|करंब|करम्बः
करंभः(बः)<BR>1 Flour or meal<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">Page0380-c+ 56</a>]<BR>mixed with curds.<BR>--2 Mud;<BR>करंभवालुकातापान् Ms. 12. 76 (where the word is<BR>variously interpreted; but Medhātithi<BR>takes it to mean ‘mud’).<BR>--3 Groats<BR>or coarsely ground oats.<BR>--4 A mixed<BR>odour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करंभकं|करम्भक|करम्भकं
करंभकं<BR>1 Groats.<BR>--2 Flour mixed<BR>with curds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करहाटः|करहाट
करहाटः<BR>1 N. of a country;<BR>(perhaps the modern Karhāda in<BR>Satāra district); करहाटपतेः पुत्री<BR>त्रिजगन्नेत्रकार्मणम् Vikr. 8. 2.<BR>--2 The<BR>fibrous root or stem of a lotus.<BR>--3 A<BR>group of lotuses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करांगणः|कराङ्गण|कराङ्गणः
करांगणः<BR>1 A market or fare.<BR>--2<BR>A place where revenue is collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करायिका
करायिका A bird, (a small kind.<BR>of crane.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कराल|करालं|करालः
कराल a.<BR>1 Dreadful, formidable,<BR>frightful, terrible; U. 5. 5, 6. 1;<BR>Māl. 3; Bg. 11. 23, 25, 27;<BR>R. 12. 98; Mv. 3. 48.<BR>--2 Gaping, opening<BR>wide; U. 5. 6.<BR>--3 Great, large,<BR>high, lofty.<BR>--4 Uneven, jagged;<BR>pointed; Ve. 2. 6; Māl. 1. 38.<BR>--5<BR>Harsh; Māl. 5. 3.<BR>--6 Wide,<BR>spacious; Mk. 3. 12.<BR>--7 Deformed.<BR>--लः<BR>1 Resin, pitch.<BR>--2 A disease of the<BR>teeth.<BR>--3 Black Tulasī.<BR>--ला A<BR>terrific form of Durgā; ˚आयतनं; न<BR>करालोपहाराच्च फलमन्यद्विभाव्यते<BR>Māl. 5. 33.<BR>--ली One of the seven tongues<BR>of fire.<BR>--लं A particular condiment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंष्ट् a. having terrific<BR>teeth.<BR>--वदना an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करालिकः|करालिक
करालिकः<BR>1 A tree.<BR>--2 A sword.<BR>--का N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिका
करिका Scratching, a wound<BR>caused by a fingernail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिन्
करिन् m. [कर-इनि]<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>--2 The number ‘8’ (in Math.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इंद्रः, --ईश्वरः, --वरः a large elephant,<BR>lordly elephant; सदादानः परिक्षीणः<BR>शस्त एव करीश्वरः Pt. 2. 70; दूरीकृताः<BR>करिवरेण मदांधबुद्ध्या Nītipr. 2.<BR>--कुंभः<BR>the frontal globe of an elephant;<BR>Bv. 2. 177.<BR>--कुसुंभः a fragrant<BR>powder of नागकेशर.<BR>--गर्जितं the roaring<BR>of an elephant (बृंहितं करिगर्जितं Ak.)<BR>--दंतः ivory.<BR>--दारकः a lion.<BR>--नासिका a musical instrument.<BR>--पः<BR>an elephant-driver.<BR>--पोतः, --शावः<BR>--शावकः a cub, young elephant.<BR>--बंधः a column to which an<BR>elephant is tied.<BR>--माचलः a lion.<BR>--मुखः<BR>an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR>--यादस् n.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">Page0381-a+ 56</a>]<BR>a water-elephant.<BR>--वर = ˚इंद्र q. v.<BR>--वैजयंती a flag carried by an<BR>elephant.<BR>--स्कंधः a herd or troop of<BR>elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0380-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करिणी
करिणी A female elephant;<BR>कथमेत्य मतिर्विपर्ययं करिणी पंकमिवावसीदति<BR>Ki. 2. 6; Bv. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीरः|करीर
करीरः [कॄ-ईरन् Uṇ. 4. 30]<BR>1<BR>The shoot of a bamboo.<BR>--2 A shoot in<BR>general; आनिन्यिरे वंशकरीरनीलैः<BR>Śi. 4. 14; N. 5. 14.<BR>--3 A thorny plant growing<BR>in deserts and eaten by camels; पत्रं<BR>नैब यदा करीरविटपे दोषो वसंतस्य किं<BR>Bh. 2. 93; cf. also किं पुष्पैः किं फलैस्तस्य<BR>करीरस्य दुरात्मनः । येन वृद्धिं समासाद्य<BR>न कृतः पत्रसंग्रहः Subhāṣ.<BR>--4 A<BR>waterjar.<BR>--रा --री<BR>1 The root of an<BR>elephant's tusk.<BR>--2 A cricket, a small<BR>grass-hopper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीरिका
करीरिका The root of an elephant's<BR>tusk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीरकं|करीरक
करीरकं Battle, fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषः|करीष|करीषं
करीषः, --षं [कॄ-ईषन् Uṇ. 4. 26]<BR>Dry cow-dung.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्नि fire<BR>of dry cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषं|करीष|करीषः
करीषः, --षं [कॄ-ईषन् Uṇ. 4. 26]<BR>Dry cow-dung.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्नि fire<BR>of dry cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषंकषा|करीषङ्कषा
करीषंकषा A strong wind or gale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करीषिणी
करीषिणी The goddess of wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुण|करुणः
करुण a. [करोति मनः आनुकूल्याय,<BR>कृउनन् Tv.] Tender, pathetic, pitiable,<BR>exciting pity, mournful; करुणध्वनिः<BR>V. 1; Śi. 9. 67; विकलकरुणैरार्यचरितैः<BR>U. 1. 28.<BR>--णः<BR>1 Pity, compassion,<BR>tenderness.<BR>--2 Pathetic sentiment,<BR>grief, sorrow (as one of the 8 or<BR>{9} sentiments); पुटपाकप्रतीकाशो<BR>रामस्य करुणो रसः U. 3. 1, 13; 7. 12;<BR>विलपन्… करुणार्थग्रथितं प्रियां प्रति<BR>R. 8. 70.<BR>--3 The supreme being.<BR>--4 A<BR>Jaina saint.<BR>--णं Ved. An action, a<BR>holy or sacred rite.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मल्ली<BR>the Mallikā plant.<BR>--विप्रलंभः (in<BR>Rhet.) the feeling of love in<BR>separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणा
करुणा Compassion, pity,<BR>tenderness; प्रायः सर्वो भवति<BR>करुणावृत्तिरार्द्रांतरात्मा Me. 93; so सकरुण kind;<BR>अकरुण unkind.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>tender-hearted.<BR>--आर्द्र a.<BR>tenderhearted, moved with pity,<BR>sensitive.<BR>--निधिः store of mercy.<BR>--पर, --मय<BR>a. very kind.<BR>--विमुख a. merciless,<BR>cruel; करुणाविमुखेन मृत्युना R. 8. 67.<BR>--स्वनः --ध्वनिः a cry of distress, a<BR>piteous tone, wail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करुणिन्
करुणिन् a. Pitiable, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेटः|करेट
करेटः A fingernail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणुः|करेणु
करेणुः [कृ-एणु Uṇ. 2. 1; के मस्तके<BR>रेणुरस्य Tv.]<BR>1 An elephant in<BR>general; करेणुरारोहयते निषादिनं<BR>Śi. 12. 5, 5. 48.<BR>--2 The Karṇikāra tree.<BR>--णुः --णूः f.<BR>1 A female elephant;<BR>ददौ रसात्पंकजरेणुगंधि गजाय गंडूषजलं<BR>करेणुः Ku. 3. 37; R. 16. 16.<BR>--2<BR>N. of the mother of Pālakāpya.<BR>--3 N. of a medicinal plant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भूः, --सुतः N. of Pālakāpya the<BR>founder of the science of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणुकं|करेणुक
करेणुकं The poisonous fruit of<BR>the plant Kareṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेणू
करेणू m. f. A male or female<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेनरः|करेनर
करेन(व)रः Storax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करेवरः|करेवर
करेन(व)रः Storax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोटं|करोट
करोटं, --करोटिः f.<BR>1 The skull;<BR>Mv. 5. 19.<BR>--2 A cup or basin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

करोटिः|करोटि
करोटं, --करोटिः f.<BR>1 The skull;<BR>Mv. 5. 19.<BR>--2 A cup or basin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्क्
कर्क् {c1c} P. To laugh (a Sautra<BR>root).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्क|कर्कः
कर्क a. [कृ-क Uṇ. 3. 40]<BR>1 White.<BR>--2 Good, excellent.<BR>--र्कः<BR>1 A crab.<BR>--2 Cancer, the fourth sign of the<BR>zodiac.<BR>--3 Fire.<BR>--4 A water-jar.<BR>--5<BR>A mirror.<BR>--6 A white horse. [cf.<BR>Pers. kark; L. cancer; Gr.<BR>korkinos].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चिर्भटी small<BR>cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटः|कर्कट
कर्कटः<BR>1 A crab.<BR>--2 Cancer, the<BR>fourth sign of the zodiac.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of crane.<BR>--4 The fibrous root<BR>of a lotus.<BR>--5 A thorn.<BR>--6 The<BR>curved end of the beam of a<BR>balance.<BR>--7 A kind of coitus (रतिबंध).<BR>--8 The radius of a circle.<BR>--9<BR>Compass, circuit.<BR>--10 A kind of pin<BR>or wedge.<BR>--टी<BR>1 A female crab.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of cucumber.<BR>--3 The<BR>curved end of a balance.<BR>--4 A small<BR>water-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटकः|कर्कटक
कर्कटकः<BR>1 A crab.<BR>--2 Cancer, the<BR>fourth sign of the zodiac.<BR>--3<BR>Compass, circuit.<BR>--4 A kind of<BR>sugarcane.<BR>--5 A hook.<BR>--की A female crab.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A poisonous root.<BR>--2 A<BR>particular fracture of the bones.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अस्थि n. the shell or crust of a<BR>crab.<BR>--रज्जुः a rope with a hook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटिः|कर्कटि
कर्कटिः, --टी f. A sort of cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटी
कर्कटिः, --टी f. A sort of cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटिका
कर्कटिका<BR>1 A plant and its fruit,<BR>a species of cucumber; Pt. 5.<BR>--2<BR>A kernel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कटुः|कर्कटु
कर्कटुः A kind of crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कंधुः|कर्कन्धु|कर्कंधु|कर्कन्धुः
कर्कंधुः, --धूः f. [कर्कं कंटकं दधाति<BR>धा-कू Uṇ. 1. 93]<BR>1 The jujube tree;<BR>कर्कंधूफलपाकमिश्रपचनामोदः परिस्तीर्यते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-c" target="_blank">Page0381-c+ 55</a>]<BR>U. 4. 1; कर्कंधूनामुपरि तुहिनं<BR>रंजयत्यग्रसंध्या Ś. 4. v. {1}<BR>--2 The fruit of<BR>this tree; Y. 1. 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कंधूः
कर्कंधुः, --धूः f. [कर्कं कंटकं दधाति<BR>धा-कू Uṇ. 1. 93]<BR>1 The jujube tree;<BR>कर्कंधूफलपाकमिश्रपचनामोदः परिस्तीर्यते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-c" target="_blank">Page0381-c+ 55</a>]<BR>U. 4. 1; कर्कंधूनामुपरि तुहिनं<BR>रंजयत्यग्रसंध्या Ś. 4. v. {1}<BR>--2 The fruit of<BR>this tree; Y. 1. 250.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कर|कर्करं|कर्करः
कर्कर a.<BR>1 Hard, solid.<BR>--2 Firm.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A hammer.<BR>--2 A mirror.<BR>--3<BR>A bone, broken piece (of skull);<BR>fragment; Māl. 5. 19.<BR>--4 A strap<BR>or rope of leather.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः<BR>a wag-tail.<BR>--अंगः the Khañjana<BR>bird.<BR>--अंधुकः a blind well; cf.<BR>अंधकूप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्कराटुः|कर्कराटु
कर्कराटुः A side-long look, a<BR>glance, leer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0381-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्करालः|कर्कराल
