कर्परः|कर्पर
कर्परः<BR>1 An iron sauce-pan, a<BR>frying-pan.<BR>--2 A pot or vessel<BR>in general (as of a potter).<BR>--3<BR>A potsherd, piece of a broken jar;<BR>as in घटकर्पर; जीयेय येन कबिना यमकैः<BR>परेण तस्मै वहेयमुदकं घटकर्परेण Ghaṭ. 22.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">Page0383-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--4 The skull.<BR>--5 A kind of weapon.<BR>--6 A back-bone; Māl. 5. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पासः|कर्पास|कर्पासं
कर्पासः, --सं, --सी The cotton<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पासं|कर्पास|कर्पासः
कर्पासः, --सं, --सी The cotton<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरः|कर्पूर|कर्पूरं
कर्पूरः, --रं [Uṇ. 4. 90.]<BR>Camphor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडः {1} a field of<BR>camphor. {2} a piece of camphor.<BR>--तैलं camphor liniment.<BR>--नालिका a<BR>kind of food.<BR>--मणिः {1} a kind of<BR>jewel. {2} a white mineral (used in<BR>medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरं|कर्पूर|कर्पूरः
कर्पूरः, --रं [Uṇ. 4. 90.]<BR>Camphor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडः {1} a field of<BR>camphor. {2} a piece of camphor.<BR>--तैलं camphor liniment.<BR>--नालिका a<BR>kind of food.<BR>--मणिः {1} a kind of<BR>jewel. {2} a white mineral (used in<BR>medicine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्पूरकः|कर्पूरक
कर्पूरकः Zedoary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्फरः|कर्फर
कर्फरः A mirror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्ब्
कर्ब् {c1c} P. (कर्बति) To go, move,<BR>approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बु
कर्बु a. Variegated, spotted;<BR>Y. 3. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुर|कर्बुरः|कर्ब्बुरं|कर्ब्बुरः
कर्बु(र्वु)र a.<BR>1 Variegated, or<BR>spotted; क्वचिल्लसद्घननिकुरंबकर्बुरः<BR>Śi. 17. 56.<BR>--2 Of the colour of pigeons,<BR>whitish, grey; पवनैर्भस्म कपोतकर्बुरं<BR>Ku. 4. 27.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The variegated<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Sin.<BR>--3 An evil spirit,<BR>demon.<BR>--4 The Dhattūra plant.<BR>--5<BR>Rice growing amidst inundation.<BR>--रा N. of a plant (वर्वरी).<BR>--री An<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Gold.<BR>--2<BR>Water.<BR>--3 The Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वुर|कर्व्वुरः
कर्बु(र्वु)र a.<BR>1 Variegated, or<BR>spotted; क्वचिल्लसद्घननिकुरंबकर्बुरः<BR>Śi. 17. 56.<BR>--2 Of the colour of pigeons,<BR>whitish, grey; पवनैर्भस्म कपोतकर्बुरं<BR>Ku. 4. 27.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The variegated<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Sin.<BR>--3 An evil spirit,<BR>demon.<BR>--4 The Dhattūra plant.<BR>--5<BR>Rice growing amidst inundation.<BR>--रा N. of a plant (वर्वरी).<BR>--री An<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Gold.<BR>--2<BR>Water.<BR>--3 The Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बुरित
कर्बु(र्वु)रित a. Variegated;<BR>U. 6. 4; Śi. 5. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वुरित
कर्बु(र्वु)रित a. Variegated;<BR>U. 6. 4; Śi. 5. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बूर|कर्बूरः|कर्ब्बूरं|कर्ब्बूरः
कर्बू(र्वू)र a. Variegated.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>A demon.<BR>--2 N. of a plant.<BR>--3 The<BR>variegated colour.<BR>--रा A leech.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Gold.<BR>--2 Yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वूर|कर्व्वूरः
कर्बू(र्वू)र a. Variegated.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>A demon.<BR>--2 N. of a plant.<BR>--3 The<BR>variegated colour.<BR>--रा A leech.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Gold.<BR>--2 Yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मन्|कर्म्मन्
कर्मन् n. [कृ-मनिन् Uṇ. 4. 144]<BR>1 Action, work, deed.<BR>--2 Execution,<BR>performance.<BR>--3 Business, office,<BR>duty; संप्रति विषवैद्यानां कर्म M. 4.<BR>--4<BR>A religious rite (it may be either<BR>नित्य, नैमित्तिक or काम्य).<BR>--5 A specific<BR>action, moral duty.<BR>--6 (a)<BR>Performance of religious rites as<BR>opposed to speculative religion or<BR>knowledge of Brahman (opp. ज्ञान);<BR>R. 8. 20. (b) Labour, work.<BR>--7<BR>Product, result.<BR>--8 A natural or active<BR>property (as support of the earth).<BR>--9<BR>Fate, the certain consequence of<BR>acts done in a former life; कर्मायत्तं फलं<BR>पुंसां बुद्धिः कर्मानुसारिणी Bh. 2. 89, 94.<BR>--10 (In gram.) The object of an<BR>action; कर्तुरीप्सिततमं कर्म<BR>P. I. 4. 49.<BR>--11 (In Vaiś. phil.) Motion<BR>considered as one of the seven<BR>categories of things; thus defined:<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0384-a" target="_blank">Page0384-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--एकद्रव्यमगुणं संयोगविभोगष्वनपेक्षकारणं कर्म<BR>Vaiś. Sūt. (It is five-fold:<BR>--उत्क्षेपणं<BR>ततोऽवक्षेपणमाकुंचनं तथा । प्रसारणं च गमनं<BR>कर्मांण्येतानि पंच च ॥ Bhāṣā P. 6.)<BR>--12<BR>Organ of sense.<BR>--13 (In astr.) The<BR>tenth lunar mansion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षम a. incapable of doing anything.<BR>--अंगं part of any act; part of a<BR>sacrificial rite (as प्रयाज of the Darśā<BR>sacrifice).<BR>--अधिकारः the right of<BR>performing religious rites.<BR>--अनुरूप<BR>a. {1} according to action or any<BR>particular office. {2} according to<BR>actions done in a previous existence.<BR>--अनुष्ठानं practising one's duties.<BR>--अनुसारः consequence of, or<BR>conformity to, acts.<BR>--अंतः {1} the end<BR>of any business or task. {2} a work,<BR>business, execution of business. {3}<BR>a barn, a store of grain &c.<BR>Ms. 7. 62 (कर्मातः इक्षुधान्यादि संग्रहस्थानं Kull.).<BR>{4} cultivated ground.<BR>--अंतरं {1}<BR>difference or contrariety of action.<BR>{2} penance, expiation. {3}<BR>suspension of a religious action.<BR>--अंतिक<BR>a. final.<BR>--(कः) a servant, workman.<BR>--अर्ह a. fit or suitable to an the act<BR>or rite.<BR>--(र्हः) a man.<BR>--आजीवः one<BR>who maintains himself by some<BR>profession (as that of an artisan &c.)<BR>--आत्मन् a. endowed with the<BR>principles of action, active; Ms. 1. 22.<BR>(--m.) the soul.<BR>--इंद्रियं an organ<BR>of action, as distinguished from<BR>ज्ञानेंद्रिय; (they are:<BR>--वाक्पाणिपादपायूपस्थानि; Ms. 2. 99; see under इंद्रिय<BR>also).<BR>--उदारं any valiant or noble<BR>act, magnanimity, prowess.<BR>--उद्युक्त<BR>a. busy, engaged, active, zealous.<BR>--करः {1} a hired labourer (a servant<BR>who is not a slave); कर्मकराः<BR>स्थपत्यादयः Pt. 1; Śi. 14. 16. {2} Yama.<BR>--कर्तृ m. (in gram.) an agent who<BR>is at the same time the object<BR>of the action; e. g. पच्यते<BR>ओदनः, it is thus defined:<BR>--क्रियमाणं<BR>तु यत्कर्म स्वयमेव प्रसिध्यति । सुकरैः स्वैर्गुणैः<BR>कर्तुः कर्मकर्तेति तद्विदुः ॥.<BR>--कांडः, --डं that<BR>department of the Veda which<BR>relates to ceremonial acts and<BR>sacrificial rites and the merit arising from<BR>a due performance thereof.<BR>--कारः<BR>{1} one who does any business, a<BR>mechanic, artisan (technically a worker<BR>not hired). {2} any labourer in<BR>general (whether hired or not).<BR>{3} a black-smith; हरिणाक्षि कटाक्षेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0384-b" target="_blank">Page0384-b+ 56</a>]<BR>आत्मानमवलोकय । न हि खड्गो विजानाति<BR>कर्मकारं स्वकारणम् ॥ Udb. {4} a<BR>bull.<BR>--कारिन् m. a labourer, artisan,<BR>workman.<BR>--कार्मुकः, --कं a strong<BR>bow.<BR>--कीलकः a washerman.<BR>--क्षम<BR>a. able to perform any work or<BR>duty; आत्मकर्मक्षमं देहं क्षात्रो धर्म<BR>इवाश्रितः R. 1. 13.<BR>--क्षेत्रं the land of<BR>religious acts, that is, भरतवर्ष; cf.<BR>कर्मभूमि.<BR>--गृहीत a. caught in the<BR>very act (as a thief).<BR>--घातः<BR>leaving off or suspending work.<BR>--चं(चां)<BR>डालः {1} ‘base in deed’, a man of<BR>very low acts or deeds; Vasiṣṭha<BR>mentions these kinds:<BR>--असूयकः<BR>पिशुनश्च कृतघ्नो दीर्घरोषकः । चत्वारः<BR>कर्मचांडाला जन्मतश्चापि पंचमः ॥. {2} one who<BR>commits an atrocious deed;<BR>U. 1. 46. {3} N. of Rāhu.<BR>--चेष्टा active<BR>exertion, action.<BR>--चोदना {1} the<BR>motive impelling one to ritual acts.<BR>{2} any positive rule enjoining a<BR>religious act.<BR>--ज a. resulting from<BR>an act.<BR>--(जः) {1} the holy fig-tree. {2}<BR>the Kali age. {3} the banian tree.<BR>{4} the effect arising from human<BR>acts:<BR>--संयोग, विभाग &c. {5} heaven.<BR>{6} hell.<BR>--ज्ञ a. one acquainted with<BR>religious rites.<BR>--त्यागः renunciation<BR>of worldly duties or ceremonial<BR>acts.<BR>--दुष्ट a. corrupt in action,<BR>wicked, immoral, disrespectable.<BR>--दोषः {1} sin, vice; Ms. 6. 61, 95.<BR>{2} an error, defect, or blunder (in<BR>doing an act); Ms. 1. 104. {3} evil<BR>consequence of human acts. {4}<BR>discreditable conduct.<BR>--धारयः N.<BR>of a compound, a subdivision of<BR>Tatpuruṣa, (in which the members<BR>of the compound are in apposition);<BR>तत्पुरुष कर्मधारय येनाहं स्यां बहुव्रीहिः<BR>Udb.<BR>--ध्वंसः {1} loss of fruit arising<BR>from religious acts. {2}<BR>disappointment.<BR>--नामन् (in gram.) a<BR>participial noun.<BR>--नाशा N. of a river<BR>between Kāśī and Vihāra.<BR>--निष्ठ a.<BR>devoted to the performance of<BR>religious acts.<BR>--न्यासः renunciation<BR>of the result of religious acts.<BR>--पथः {1} the direction or source<BR>of an action. {2} the path<BR>of religious rites (opp. ज्ञानमार्ग).<BR>--पाकः ripening of actions, reward<BR>of actions done in a former life;<BR>Pt. 1. 372.<BR>--प्रवचनीयः a term for<BR>certain prepositions, particles, or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0384-c" target="_blank">Page0384-c+ 56</a>]<BR>adverbs when they are not connected<BR>with verbs and govern a noun in<BR>some case; e. g. आ in आ मुक्तेः संसारः<BR>is a कर्मप्रवचनीय; so अनु in जपमनु<BR>प्रावर्षत् &c.; cf. उपसर्ग, गति and निपात<BR>also.<BR>--फलं fruit or reward<BR>of actions done in a former<BR>life; (pain, pleasure).<BR>--बंधः, --बंधनं<BR>confinement to repeated birth, as the<BR>consequence of religious acts, good<BR>or bad (by which the soul is<BR>attached to worldly pleasures &c.).<BR>--भूः,<BR>भूमिः f. {1} the land of religious rites,<BR>i. e. भरतवर्ष, this world (a place for<BR>man's probation); प्राप्येमां कर्मभूमिं<BR>Bh. 2. 100, K. 174, 319. {2} ploughed<BR>ground.<BR>--मीमांसा the Mīmāṃsā of<BR>ceremonial acts; see मीमांसा.<BR>--मूलं a<BR>kind of sacred grass called कुश.<BR>--युगं the fourth (the present) age<BR>of the world, i. e. the Kaliyuga.<BR>--योगः {1} performance of actions,<BR>worldly and religious rites. {2} active<BR>exertion, industry.<BR>--वचनं (with<BR>Buddhists) the ritual.<BR>--वज्रः an<BR>epithet of a Śūdra.<BR>--वशः fate<BR>considered as the inevitable result of<BR>actions done in a former life.<BR>--वाटी a<BR>lunar day (तिथि).<BR>--विपाक = कर्मपाक.<BR>--शाला<BR>a work-shop.<BR>--शील, --शूर a. assiduous,<BR>active, laborious.<BR>--शौचं humility.<BR>--संगः attachment to worldly<BR>duties and their results.<BR>--सचिवः a<BR>minister.<BR>--संन्यासिकः, --संन्यासिन् m.<BR>{1} a religious person who has<BR>withdrawn from every kind of worldly<BR>act. {2} an ascetic who performs<BR>religious deeds without looking to<BR>their reward.<BR>--साक्षिन् m. {1} an<BR>eye-witness; Ku. 7. 83. {2} one who<BR>witnesses the good or bad actions<BR>of man; (there are nine divinities<BR>which are said to witness and watch<BR>over all human actions; सूर्यः सोमो<BR>यमः कालो महाभूतानि पंच च । एते<BR>शुभाशुभस्येह कर्मणो नव साक्षिणः ॥)<BR>--सिद्धिः<BR>f. accomplishment of any business<BR>or desired object; success.<BR>--स्थानं<BR>a public office, a place of business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0383-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मठ|कर्मठः|कर्म्मठ|कर्म्मठः
कर्मठ a. [कर्मन्-अठच् P. V. 2. 35].<BR>1 Proficient in any work, clever.<BR>--2<BR>Working diligently.<BR>--3 Exclusively<BR>devoted to the performance of<BR>religious rites.<BR>--ठः The director of a<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मण्य|कर्म्मण्य|कर्म्मण्यः
कर्मण्य a. [कर्मन्-यत्] Skilful,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">Page0385-a+ 54</a>]<BR>clever.<BR>--ण्या Wages.<BR>--ण्यं Activity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0384-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मिन्|कर्म्मिन्
कर्मिन् a.<BR>1 Working, active, busy.<BR>--2 Engaged in any work or business.<BR>--3 One who performs religious deeds<BR>with the expectation of reward or<BR>recompense; कर्मिभ्यश्चाधिको योगी<BR>तस्माद्योगी भवार्जुन Bg. 6. 46. --m. A<BR>mechanic, artisan; Y. 2. 265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मिष्ठ|कर्म्मिष्ठ|कर्म्मिष्ठः
कर्मिष्ठ a. Skilled in business, clever,<BR>diligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मंदिन्|कर्मन्दिन्|कर्म्मन्दिन्
कर्मंदिन् m. An ascetic, a<BR>religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मरी|कर्म्मरी
कर्मरी The manna of the bamboo<BR>(वंशलोचन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मारः|कर्मार|कर्म्मार|कर्म्मारः
कर्मारः<BR>1 A blacksmith; Y. 1. 163;<BR>Ms. 4. 215.<BR>--2 A bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्मीर|कर्म्मीर|कर्म्मीरः
कर्मीर a. Variegated, spotted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्व्
कर्व् {c1c} P. (कर्वति, कर्वित) To be<BR>proud, boast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वः|कर्व|कर्व्व|कर्व्वः
कर्वः<BR>1 Love. desire.<BR>--2 A rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वटः|कर्वट|कर्व्वट|कर्व्वटं|कर्व्वटः
कर्वटः<BR>1 The market-town or<BR>capital of a district (of two hundred<BR>villages).<BR>--2 Declivity of a<BR>mountain; (also कर्वटक in this sense).<BR>--टं A city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्वर|कर्वरः|कर्व्वर
कर्व(र्ब)र a. Variegated.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Sin.<BR>--2 Tiger.<BR>--3 A demon.<BR>--4<BR>A sort of medicament.<BR>--री<BR>1 An<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>--2 Night.<BR>--3 A<BR>Rākṣasī.<BR>--4 A tigress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्बर
कर्व(र्ब)र a. Variegated.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Sin.<BR>--2 Tiger.<BR>--3 A demon.<BR>--4<BR>A sort of medicament.<BR>--री<BR>1 An<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>--2 Night.<BR>--3 A<BR>Rākṣasī.<BR>--4 A tigress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्शन|कर्शनः
कर्शन a. Rendering lean.<BR>--नः<BR>Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षः|कर्ष
कर्षः [कृस्-अच् घञ् वा]<BR>1 Drawing,<BR>dragging, pulling; Y. 2. 217.<BR>--2<BR>Attracting.<BR>--3 Ploughing.<BR>--4 A<BR>furrow, a trench.<BR>--5 A scratch.<BR>--र्षः,<BR>--र्षं A weight of gold or silver<BR>equal to 16 Māṣas.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आपण = कार्षापण q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षक|कर्षकः
कर्षक a. [कृष्-ण्वुल्] Who or what<BR>draws, attracts &c.<BR>--कः A<BR>cultivator, husbandman; Y. 2. 265.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षण|कर्षणं
कर्षण a.<BR>1 Dragging.<BR>--2<BR>Injuring.<BR>--3 Extending (in time), see<BR>below.<BR>--णं [कृष् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Drawing, dragging, pulling, bending (as<BR>of a bow); भज्यमानमतिमात्रकर्षणात्<BR>R. 11. 46, 7. 62.<BR>--2 Attracting.<BR>--3<BR>Ploughing, tilling.<BR>--4 Injuring,<BR>tormenting; emaciation; Ms. 7. 112.<BR>--5 Cultivated land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षणिः|कर्षणि
कर्षणिः f. An unchaste woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षित
कर्षित a.<BR>1 Drawn, attracted.<BR>--2<BR>Tormented, harassed &c.<BR>--3 Worn<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-b" target="_blank">Page0385-b+ 55</a>]<BR>out, decayed.<BR>--4 Ploughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षिन्
कर्षिन् a.<BR>1 Who or what draws<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Attractive. --m. A<BR>ploughman.<BR>--णी<BR>1 The bit of a bridle.<BR>--2 A medicinal moon-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्षूः
कर्षूः f.<BR>1 A furrow, trench.<BR>--2<BR>A river.<BR>--3 Canal. --m.<BR>1 A fire of<BR>dried cow-dung.<BR>--2 Agriculture,<BR>cultivation.<BR>--3 Livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हि
कर्हि ind. Ved. When, at what<BR>time?<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कर्हिचित्
कर्हिचित् ind. At any time,<BR>usually with न; Ms. 2. 4, 40, 97;<BR>4. 77; 6. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्
कल् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (कलते, कलित)<BR>1 To<BR>count.<BR>--2 To sound. {vII.v} {c10c} U.<BR>(कलयति-ते, कलित)<BR>1 To hold, bear,<BR>carry, wield, have, put on;<BR>करालकरकंदलीकलितशस्त्रजालैर्बलैः U. 5. 5;<BR>म्लेच्छनिवहनिधने कलयसि करवालं Gīt. 1;<BR>कलितललितवनमालः; हलं कलयते ibid.;<BR>कलय वलयश्रेणीं पाणौ पदे कुरु नूपुरौ 12;<BR>Śānti. 4. 18.<BR>--2 (a) To count,<BR>reckon; कालः कलयतामहं Bg. 10. 30<BR>(b) To measure, सदा पांथः पूषा<BR>गगनपरिमाणं कलयति Bh. 2. 114.<BR>--3 To<BR>assume, take, have, possess; कलयति हि<BR>हिमांशोर्निष्कलंकस्य लक्ष्मीं Māl. 1. 22;<BR>Śi. 4. 36, 9. 59.<BR>--4 To know,<BR>understand, observe, take notice of,<BR>think of; कलयन्नपि सव्यथोऽवतस्थे<BR>Śi. 9. 83; कोपितं विरहखेदितचित्ता<BR>कांतमेव कलयंत्यनुनिन्ये 10. 29; N. 2. 65,<BR>3. 12, Māl. 2. 9.<BR>--5 To think,<BR>regard, consider; कलयेदमानमनसं सखि<BR>मां Śi. 9. 58, 6. 54, 15. 55, 16. 64;<BR>Śānti. 4. 15; व्यालनिलयमिलनेन<BR>गरलमिव कलयति मलयसमीरं Gīt. 4, 7.<BR>--6<BR>To undergo, be influenced by;<BR>मदलीलाकलितकामपाल Māl. 8; धन्यः<BR>कोपि न विक्रियां कलयति प्राप्ते नवे यौवने<BR>Bh. 1. 72.<BR>--7 To do, perform.<BR>--8<BR>To go.<BR>--9 To attach to, tie on;<BR>furnish with.<BR>--10 To urge on,<BR>impel, incite; Māl. 9. 41.<BR>--11 To utter<BR>a sound, murmur.<BR>--12 To take hold<BR>of the die called Kali. {vIII.v} {c10c} P.<BR>(कालयति, कालित)<BR>1 To push on,<BR>urge, drive forward.<BR>--2 To carry<BR>off.<BR>--3 To collect.<BR>--4 To throw,<BR>cast.<BR>--5 To proclaim the time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल|कलं|कलः
कल a. [कल्-घञ्]<BR>1 Sweet and<BR>indistinct (अस्पष्टमधुर); कर्णे कलं<BR>किमपि रौति H. 1. 81; सारसैः कलनिर्ह्रादैः<BR>R. 1. 41, 8. 59; M. 5. 1. (Hence)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-c" target="_blank">Page0385-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--2 Low, soft, sweet (note &c.);<BR>melodious, pleasing.<BR>--3 Making<BR>noise, jingling, tinkling &c.;<BR>भास्वत्कलनूपुराणां R. 16. 12;<BR>कलकिंकिणीरवं Śi. 9. 74, 82; कलमेखलाकलकलः<BR>6. 14, 4. 57.<BR>--4 Weak.<BR>--5 Crude;<BR>undigested.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A low or soft<BR>and inarticulate tone.<BR>--2 (In<BR>poetry) Time equal to four Mātrās.<BR>--3<BR>(m. pl.) A class of manes.<BR>--लं<BR>Semen.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकुरः the<BR>Sārasa bird.<BR>--अनुवादिन् m. {1} a<BR>sparrow. {2} a bee. {3} the Cātaka<BR>bird.<BR>--अविकलः a sparrow.<BR>--आलापः {1} a sweet humming sound. {2}<BR>sweet and agreeable discourse;<BR>स्फुरत्कलालापविलासकोमला करोति रागं हृदि<BR>कौतुकाधिकम् K. 2. {3} a bee.<BR>--उत्ताल a. high, sharp.<BR>--कंठ a.<BR>having a sweet voice.<BR>--(ठः) (ठी f.)<BR>{1} the (Indian) cuckoo. {2} a goose,<BR>swan. {3} a pigeon.<BR>--कलः {1}<BR>murmuring or hum of a crowd. {2}<BR>indistinct or confused noise; चलितया<BR>विदधे कलमेखलाकलकलोऽ<BR>लकलोलदृशान्यया Śi. 6. 14; नेपथ्ये कलकलः (in<BR>dramas); Bh. 1. 27, 37;<BR>Amaru. 28. {3} N. of Śiva. {4} resin, pitch.<BR>--कूजिका, --कूणिका a wanton<BR>woman.<BR>--घोषः the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR>--तूलिका a wanton or lascivious<BR>woman.<BR>--धूतं silver.<BR>--धौतं {1}<BR>silver; Śi. 13. 51, 4. 41. {2} gold;<BR>विमलकलधौतत्सरुणा खद्भेन Ve. 3.<BR>{3} a low or pleasing tone. ˚लिपिः<BR>f. {1} illumination of a manuscript<BR>with gold. {2} characters written<BR>in gold;<BR>मरकतशकलकलितकलधौतलिपेरिव रतिजयलेखं Gīt. 8.<BR>--ध्वनिः {1}<BR>a low sweet tone. {2} a pigeon. {3}<BR>a peacock. {4} the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR>--नाद a. having a low and sweet<BR>tone.<BR>--(दः) a swan; see कलध्वनि.<BR>--भाषणं lisping, the prattle of<BR>childhood.<BR>--रवः {1} a low sweet tone.<BR>{2} a dove. {3} the (Indian)<BR>cuckoo.<BR>--विशुद्ध a. soft and clear;<BR>Ś. 5.<BR>--हंसः {1} a gander, a swan;<BR>वधूदुकूलं कलहंसलक्षणं Ku. 5. 67. {2}<BR>a duck, drake; Bk. 2. 18; R. 8. 59.<BR>{3} the supreme soul. {4} an<BR>excellent king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंकषः|कलङ्कष|कलंकष|कलङ्कषः
कलंकषः (षी f.)<BR>1 A lion.<BR>--2 A<BR>musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंकुरः|कलङ्कुर|कलंकुर|कलङ्कुरः
कलंकुरः A whirlpool, eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलन|कलनं|कलनः
कलन a. (at the end of comp.)<BR>Causing, effecting.<BR>--नः A sort of cane.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">Page0386-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--नं<BR>1 A spot, mark.<BR>--2 A defect, an<BR>offence, fault.<BR>--3 Taking, seizing,<BR>grasping; कलनात्सर्वभूतानां स कालः<BR>परिकीर्तितः.<BR>--4 Knowing,<BR>understanding, apprehension.<BR>--5 Sounding.<BR>--6 An<BR>embryo at the first stage after<BR>conception.<BR>--ना<BR>1 Taking, seizing.<BR>grasping; कालकलना Ā. L. 29.<BR>--2<BR>Doing, effecting.<BR>--3 Subjection.<BR>--4<BR>Understanding, comprehension.<BR>--5<BR>Putting on, wearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0385-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलित|कलितं
कलित p. p.<BR>1 Held, seized, taken;<BR>U. 5. 5.<BR>--2 Broken; Pt. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Plucked, gathered; U. 3. 6.<BR>--4<BR>Arisen, produced; U. 5. 2;<BR>कलितकुलिशघाताः केपि खेलंति वाताः R. G.<BR>--5<BR>Influenced; Māl. 8.<BR>--6 Mixed;<BR>Māl. 10. 10.<BR>--7 Known, understood;<BR>Māl. 8. 13, 2. 9.<BR>--8 Furnished,<BR>endowed, Māl. 6. 6; Ku. 6. 76.<BR>--9<BR>Gained, obtained.<BR>--10 Reckoned,<BR>counted.<BR>--11 Separated, divided.<BR>--12<BR>Sounded indistinctly, murmured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलकः|कलक
कलकः<BR>1 A kind of fish.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of prose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंकः|कलङ्क|कलंक|कलङ्कः
कलंकः<BR>1 A spot, a mark, a dark<BR>spot (lit.); R. 13. 15.<BR>--2 (Fig.)<BR>A stain, stigma, obloquy, disrepute;<BR>व्यपनयतु कलंकं स्वस्वभावेन सैव<BR>Mk. 10. 34; R. 14. 37; so कुल˚.<BR>--3 A fault,<BR>defect; Bh. 3. 48.<BR>--4 Rust of iron.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हृत् m. an epithet of Śiva<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंकयति
कलंकयति Den. P. To defame,<BR>stain with stigma, sully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंकित|कलङ्कित
कलंकित a. Spotted, stained,<BR>defamed; U. 6. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंजः|कलञ्ज|कलंज|कलञ्जः
कलंजः<BR>1 A bird.<BR>--2 A deer or any<BR>other animal struck with a poisoned<BR>weapon.<BR>--3 Tobacco.<BR>--जं Flesh of<BR>such an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलटं|कलट
कलटं The thatch of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत
कलत a. Bald-headed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलत्रं|कलत्र
कलत्रं<BR>1 A wife; वसुमत्या हि नृपाः<BR>कलत्रिणः R. 8. 83; 1. 32; 12. 34;<BR>यद्भर्तुरेव हितमिच्छति तत्कलत्रं Bh. 2. 68.<BR>--2 The hip and loins;<BR>इंदुमूर्तिमिवोद्दःममन्मथविलासगृहीतगुरुकलत्रां K. 189<BR>(where क˚ has both senses);<BR>Ki. 8. 9, 17.<BR>--3 Any royal citadel.<BR>--4 The<BR>seventh lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंदरः|कलन्दर|कलन्दरः
कलंदरः A man of a mixed tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंदिका|कलन्दिका
कलंदिका Wisdom, intelligence<BR>(सर्वविद्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलभः|कलभ
कलभः (भी f.) [कल्-अभच्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 122; करेण शुंडया भाति; भा-क, रस्य लत्वं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">Page0386-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 A young elephant, cub; ननु<BR>कलभेन यूथपतेरनुकृतं M. 5; द्विपेंद्रभावं<BR>कलभः श्रयन्निव R. 3. 32; 11. 39;<BR>18. 38.<BR>--2 An elephant 30 years old.<BR>--3 A young camel; the young of any<BR>other animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलमः|कलम
कलमः [Uṇ. 4. 84]<BR>1 Rice<BR>which is sown in May-June and<BR>ripens in December-January; सुतन<BR>पांवोः कलमस्य गोपिकां Ki. 4. 9, 34;<BR>Ku. 5. 47; R. 4. 37.<BR>--2 A pen, a<BR>reed for writing with.<BR>--3 A thief.<BR>--4<BR>A rogue, rascal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंबः|कलम्ब|कलंब|कलम्बः
कलंबः<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>--2 The<BR>Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंबिका|कलम्बिका
कलंबिका The nape of the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलंबुट|कलम्बुट|कलम्बुटं
कलंबुट (Fresh) Butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललः|कलल|कललं
कललः, --लं<BR>1 The fœtus, uterus.<BR>--2 A term for the embryo a short<BR>time after conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललं|कलल|कललः
कललः, --लं<BR>1 The fœtus, uterus.<BR>--2 A term for the embryo a short<BR>time after conception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कललजः|कललज
कललजः<BR>1 The resinous<BR>exudation of the Shorea Robusta.<BR>--2<BR>Womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलविंकः|कलविङ्क|कलविंक|कलविङ्कः
कलविंकः, --गः<BR>1 A sparrow;<BR>Ms. 5. 12; Y. 1. 174.<BR>--2 A spot, stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलविंगः|कलविङ्ग|कलविङ्गः
कलविंकः, --गः<BR>1 A sparrow;<BR>Ms. 5. 12; Y. 1. 174.<BR>--2 A spot, stain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलशः|कलश
कलशः, --सः (शं, --सं) [केन<BR>जलेन लश-स-ति Tv.]<BR>1 A pitcher,<BR>water pot, a jar, dish; स्ततौ मांसग्रथी<BR>कनककलशावित्युपमितौ Bh. 3. 20, 1. 97;<BR>स्तनकलस Amaru. 54. ˚जन्मन्,<BR>˚उद्भवः N. of Agastya.<BR>--2 A churn.<BR>--3<BR>A kind of measure.<BR>--4 A rounded<BR>pinnacle on the top of a temple.<BR>--Comp. (स) उदधिः the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलसः|कलस
कलशः, --सः (शं, --सं) [केन<BR>जलेन लश-स-ति Tv.]<BR>1 A pitcher,<BR>water pot, a jar, dish; स्ततौ मांसग्रथी<BR>कनककलशावित्युपमितौ Bh. 3. 20, 1. 97;<BR>स्तनकलस Amaru. 54. ˚जन्मन्,<BR>˚उद्भवः N. of Agastya.<BR>--2 A churn.<BR>--3<BR>A kind of measure.<BR>--4 A rounded<BR>pinnacle on the top of a temple.<BR>--Comp. (स) उदधिः the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलशी
कलशी (सी f.) A pitcher, a jar.<BR>Śi. 11. 8.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सुतः N. of<BR>Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहः|कलह|कलहं
कलहः, --हं [कलं कामं हंति हण्-ड Tv.]<BR>1 Strife, quarrel: ईर्ष्याकलहः Bh. 1. 2;<BR>लीला˚ Ś. Til. 8; so शुष्ककलहः,<BR>प्रणयकलहः &c.<BR>--2 War, battle.<BR>--3<BR>Trick, deceit, falsehood.<BR>--4 Violence,<BR>kicking, beating &c; Ms. 4. 121;<BR>(where Medhātithi and Kullūka<BR>explain कलह by दडादिनेतरेतरताडनं and<BR>दंडादंड्यादि respectively).<BR>--5 A road,<BR>way.<BR>--6 The sheath of a sword.<BR>--7<BR>A cry, sound; Māl. 9. 18.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरिता a woman separated from<BR>her lover in consequence of a<BR>quarrel with him (one who is angry<BR>and yet sorry for it); she is thus<BR>defined in S. D.:<BR>--चाटुकारमपि<BR>प्राणनाथं रोषादपास्य या । पश्चात्तापमवाप्नोति<BR>कलहांतरिता तु सा ॥ 117.<BR>--अपहृत a. taken<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-c" target="_blank">Page0386-c+ 56</a>]<BR>by main force or violence.<BR>--कार,<BR>--कारिन् a. quarrelsome, turbulent.<BR>--प्रिय a. fond of (promoting)<BR>quarrels; ननु कलहप्रियोसि M. 1.<BR>--(यः) an epithet of Nārada.<BR>--(या)<BR>a bird (सारिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलहं|कलह|कलहः
कलहः, --हं [कलं कामं हंति हण्-ड Tv.]<BR>1 Strife, quarrel: ईर्ष्याकलहः Bh. 1. 2;<BR>लीला˚ Ś. Til. 8; so शुष्ककलहः,<BR>प्रणयकलहः &c.<BR>--2 War, battle.<BR>--3<BR>Trick, deceit, falsehood.<BR>--4 Violence,<BR>kicking, beating &c; Ms. 4. 121;<BR>(where Medhātithi and Kullūka<BR>explain कलह by दडादिनेतरेतरताडनं and<BR>दंडादंड्यादि respectively).<BR>--5 A road,<BR>way.<BR>--6 The sheath of a sword.<BR>--7<BR>A cry, sound; Māl. 9. 18.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरिता a woman separated from<BR>her lover in consequence of a<BR>quarrel with him (one who is angry<BR>and yet sorry for it); she is thus<BR>defined in S. D.:<BR>--चाटुकारमपि<BR>प्राणनाथं रोषादपास्य या । पश्चात्तापमवाप्नोति<BR>कलहांतरिता तु सा ॥ 117.<BR>--अपहृत a. taken<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-c" target="_blank">Page0386-c+ 56</a>]<BR>by main force or violence.<BR>--कार,<BR>--कारिन् a. quarrelsome, turbulent.<BR>--प्रिय a. fond of (promoting)<BR>quarrels; ननु कलहप्रियोसि M. 1.<BR>--(यः) an epithet of Nārada.<BR>--(या)<BR>a bird (सारिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कला
कला [कल्-कच्]<BR>1 A small part of<BR>anything; U. 1. 1; a bit, jot;<BR>कलामप्यकृतपारेलंबः K. 304; सर्वे ते मित्रगात्रस्य<BR>कलां नार्हंति षोडशीं Pt. 2. 55;<BR>Ms. 2. 86, 8. 36.<BR>--2 A digit of the moon<BR>(these are sixteen); जगति जयिनस्ते<BR>ते भावा नवेंदुकलादयः Māl. 1. 36;<BR>Ku. 5. 71; Me. 89.<BR>--3 Interest on<BR>capital (consideration paid for the use of<BR>money); घनवीथिवीथिमवतीर्णवतो<BR>निधिरंभसामुपचयाय कलाः Śi. 9. 32 (where<BR>कला means ‘digits’ also).<BR>--4 A<BR>division of time variously computed;<BR>one minute, 48 seconds, or {8} seconds.<BR>--5 The 60th part of one thirtieth<BR>part of a zodiacal sign, a minute of<BR>a degree.<BR>--6 Any practical art<BR>(mechanical or fine); there are 64<BR>such arts, as music, dancing &c.<BR>--7<BR>Skill, ingenuity.<BR>--8 Fraud, deceit.<BR>--9 (In Prosody) A syllabic instant.<BR>--10 A boat.<BR>--11 The menstrual<BR>discharge.<BR>--12 A term for the seven<BR>substrata of the elements of the<BR>human body; (they are:<BR>--आद्या<BR>मांसधरा प्रोक्ता द्वितीया रक्तधारिणी । मेदोधरा<BR>तृतीया तु चतुर्थी श्लेष्मधारिणी ॥ पंचमी च मलं धत्ते<BR>षष्ठी पित्तधरा मता । रेतोधरा सप्तमी स्यात् इति<BR>सप्तकलाः स्मृताः ॥).<BR>--13 An atom.<BR>--14 A<BR>term for the embryo.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरं<BR>{1} another digit. {2} interest, profit;<BR>मासे शतस्य यदि पंच कलांतरं स्यात् Līlā.<BR>--अयनः a tumbler, a dancer (as on<BR>the sharp edge of a sword).<BR>--आकुलं deadly poison.<BR>--केलि a. gay,<BR>wanton.<BR>--(लिः) an epithet of Kāma.<BR>--क्षयः waning (of the moon);<BR>R. 5. 16.<BR>--धरः, --निधिः, --पूर्णः the moon;<BR>अहो महत्त्वं महतामपूर्वं विपत्तिकालेपि<BR>परोपकारः । यथास्यमध्ये पतितोपि राहोः<BR>कलानिधिः पुण्यचयं ददाति ॥ Udb.<BR>--भृत् m.<BR>{1} the moon. {2} an artist &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलावत्|कलावन्त्
कलावत् a. Versed in the(64)<BR>arts; Māl. 2. 10. --m. The moon<BR>(having digits); Ku. 5. 71;<BR>Māl. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिका
कलिका A digit of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलांकुरः|कलाङ्कुर|कलांकुर|कलाङ्कुरः
कलांकुरः<BR>1 The Sārasa bird,<BR>crane.<BR>--2 N. of Kaṃsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाचिक
कलाचिक-कलाची<BR>1 A ladle.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">Page0387-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 The fore-arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाची
कलाचिक-कलाची<BR>1 A ladle.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">Page0387-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 The fore-arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0386-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाटीनः|कलाटीन
कलाटीनः The white water<BR>wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलादः|कलाद
कलादः, --दकः A goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलादकः|कलादक
कलादः, --दकः A goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाधिकः|कलाधिक
कलाधिकः A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापः|कलाप
कलापः<BR>1 A band, bundle;<BR>मुक्ताकलापस्य च निस्तलस्य<BR>Ku. 1. 42 a round necklace of pearls;<BR>रशनाकलापः a zone of several strings.<BR>--2 A group or whole collection of<BR>things; अखिलकलाकलापालोचन K. 7.<BR>--3 A peacock's tail; तं मे जातकलापं<BR>प्रेषय मणिकंठकं शिखिनं V. 5. 13;<BR>Pt. 2. 80; Rs. 1. 16, 2. 14.<BR>--4 A<BR>woman's zone or girdle; (oft. with<BR>कांची or रशना &c.); Bh. 1. 57, 67;<BR>Rs. 3. 20; Mk. 1. 27.<BR>--5 An<BR>ornament in general.<BR>--6 The rope round<BR>an elephant's neck.<BR>--7 A quiver.<BR>--8<BR>An arrow.<BR>--9 The moon.<BR>--10 A<BR>shrewd and intelligent man.<BR>--11 A<BR>poem written in one metre.<BR>--12 A<BR>tuft (जटा˚) or knot of braided hair.<BR>--पी A bundle of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापकं|कलापक|कलापकः
कलापकं<BR>1 A series of four stanzas<BR>on the same subject and forming<BR>one grammatical sentence (चतुर्भिस्तु<BR>कलापकं); for an illustration see<BR>Ki. 3. 41, 42, 43, 44.<BR>--2 A debt to be<BR>paid when the peacocks spread their<BR>tails.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A band or bundle in<BR>general.<BR>--2 A string of pearls.<BR>--3<BR>The rope round an elephant's neck.<BR>--4 A zone or girdle (= कलाप);<BR>Śi. 9. 45.<BR>--5 A sectarian mark on the<BR>forehead (विशेषक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापिन्
कलापिन् a.<BR>1 Having a quiver.<BR>--2<BR>Spreading its tail (as a peacock). --m.<BR>1 A peacock; कलविलापि<BR>कलापिकदंबकं Śi. 6. 31; Pt. 2. 80; R. 6. 9.<BR>--2 The (Indian) cuckoo.<BR>--3 The<BR>Indian fig-tree (प्लक्ष).<BR>--4 The time<BR>(when peacocks spread their<BR>tails).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलापिनी
कलापिनी The night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलांबिः|कलाम्बि|कलाम्बिः
कलांबिः f.<BR>1 Lending, loan.<BR>--2<BR>Usury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलामकः|कलामक
कलामकः A kind of rice ripening<BR>in the cold season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलायः|कलाय
कलायः N. of a leguminous seed<BR>(Mar. वाटाणा); Śi. 13. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाविकः|कलाविक
कलाविकः A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलाहकः|कलाहक
कलाहकः A kind of musical<BR>instrument (काहल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिः|कलि
कलिः [कल्-इनि]<BR>1 Strife,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-b" target="_blank">Page0387-b+ 56</a>]<BR>quarrel, dissension, contention;<BR>Śi. 7. 55: कलिकामजित् R. 9. 33; Amaru. 19.<BR>--2 War, battle<BR>--3 The fourth age of<BR>the world, the iron age (consisting<BR>of 432,000 years of men and<BR>beginning from the 13th of February<BR>3102 B. C.); Ms. 1. 86, 9. 301;<BR>कलिवर्ज्यानि इमानि &c.<BR>--4 Kali age<BR>personified (this Kali persecuted Nala).<BR>--5 The worst of any class.<BR>--6 The<BR>Bibhītaka tree.<BR>--7 The side of a die<BR>which is marked with one point.<BR>--8<BR>A hero.<BR>--9 An arrow. --f. A bud.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः, --कारकः, --क्रियः an<BR>epithet of Nārada.<BR>--द्रुमः, --वृक्षः<BR>the Bibhītaka tree.<BR>--प्रिय a.<BR>quarrelsome.<BR>--(यः) {1} N. of Nārada. {2} a<BR>monkey, ape; Ms. 1. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिकः|कलिक
कलिकः Curlew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिका
कलिका, --कलिः f.<BR>1 An unblown<BR>flower, a bud; चूतानां चिरनिर्गतापि<BR>कलिका बध्नाति न स्वं रजः Ś. 6. 3;<BR>किमाम्रकलिकाभंगमारभसे Ś. 6;<BR>Rs. 6. 17; R. 9. 33.<BR>--2 A digit, streak.<BR>--3<BR>The bottom or peg of the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिः|कलि
कलिका, --कलिः f.<BR>1 An unblown<BR>flower, a bud; चूतानां चिरनिर्गतापि<BR>कलिका बध्नाति न स्वं रजः Ś. 6. 3;<BR>किमाम्रकलिकाभंगमारभसे Ś. 6;<BR>Rs. 6. 17; R. 9. 33.<BR>--2 A digit, streak.<BR>--3<BR>The bottom or peg of the Indian lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिंग|कलिङ्ग|कलिङ्गं|कलिङ्गः
कलिंग a.<BR>1 Clever.<BR>--2 Cunning.<BR>--गाः (pl.) N. of a country and its<BR>inhabitants; (a district on the<BR>Coromandel coast); उत्कलादर्शितपथः<BR>कलिंगाभिमुखो ययौ R. 4. 38; (its position<BR>is thus described in Tantras:<BR>--जगन्नाथात्समारभ्य कृष्णातीरांतगः प्रिये । कालिंगदेशः<BR>संप्रोक्तो वाममार्गपरायणः ॥).<BR>--गः<BR>1 The<BR>fork-tailed shrike.<BR>--2 N. of several<BR>plants; (as शिरीष, प्लक्ष &c.).<BR>--गा A<BR>beautiful woman.<BR>--गं Indra grain<BR>(इंद्रयव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिंजः|कलिञ्ज|कलिंज|कलिञ्जः
कलिंजः A mat, a screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलित|कलितं
कलित see under कल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिंदः|कलिन्द|कलिंद|कलिन्दः
कलिंदः<BR>1 N. of the mountain on<BR>which the Yamunā rises.<BR>--2 The<BR>sun.<BR>--3 The Bibhītaka plant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कन्या, --जा, --तनया, --नंदिनी, --सुता<BR>epithets of the river Yamunā;<BR>कलिंदकन्या मथुरां गतापि R. 6. 48;<BR>कलिंदजानीर Bv. 2. 120, Gīt. 3.<BR>--गिरिः<BR>the Kalinda mountain. ˚जा, ˚तनया,<BR>˚नंदिनी epithets of the river<BR>Yamunā; Bv. 4. 3, 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिल|कलिलः
कलिल a. [कल् --इलच् Uṇ. 1. 54]<BR>1 Covered with, full of.<BR>--2 Mixed,<BR>blended with; तत एवाक्रंदकलिलः<BR>कलकलः Mv. 1.<BR>--3 Affected by,<BR>subject to; अकल्ककलिलः Śi. 19. 98.<BR>--4<BR>Impervious, impenetrable.<BR>--लं A<BR>large heap, confused mass; विशसि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">Page0387-c+ 56</a>]<BR>हृदय क्लेशकलिलं Bh. 3. 34; confusion;<BR>यदा ते मोहकलिलं बुद्धिर्व्यतितरिष्यति<BR>Bg. 2. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुक्कः|कलुक्क
कलुक्कः A cymbal.<BR>--क्का<BR>1 A<BR>tavern.<BR>--2 A meteor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुष|कलुषं|कलुषः
कलुष a. [कल्-उषच् Uṇ. 4. 75]<BR>1 Turbid, dirty, muddy, foul; गंगा<BR>रोधः पतनकलुषा गृह्णतीव प्रसादं V. 1. 8;<BR>Ki. 8. 32; Ghaṭ. 13.<BR>--2 Choked,<BR>hoarse, husky; कंठः<BR>स्तंभितबाष्पवृत्तिकलुषः Ś. 4. 5.<BR>--3 Bedimmed; full<BR>of; Ś. 6. 8.<BR>--4 Angry, displeased,<BR>excited; U. 3. 13; भावावबोधकलुषा<BR>दयितेव रात्रौ R. 5. 64 (Malli. takes<BR>कलुष to mean ‘unable’,<BR>‘incompetent’).<BR>--5 Wicked, sinful, bad.<BR>--6<BR>Cruel, censurable; R. 14. 73.<BR>--7<BR>Dark, opaque.<BR>--8 Idle, lazy.<BR>--9<BR>Perverted; ˚भूतायां बुद्धौ Pt. 3. 184;<BR>कालुष्यमुपयाति बुद्धिः &c.<BR>--षः A<BR>buffalo.<BR>--षं<BR>1 Dirt, filth, mud;<BR>विगतकलुषमंभः Rs. 3. 22.<BR>--2 Sin.<BR>--3<BR>Wrath.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--योनिज a.<BR>illegitimate, of impure origin;<BR>Ms. 10. 57, 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषित
कलुषित a.<BR>1 Turbid or muddy.<BR>--2<BR>Offended, displeased; Mu. 3. 9.<BR>--3<BR>Wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलुषीकृ
कलुषीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To make turbid<BR>or unclean.<BR>--2 To obscure, taint,<BR>sully; Pt. 2. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलेवरः|कलेवर|कलेवरं
कलेवरः, --रं The body;<BR>यावत्स्वस्थमिदं कलेवरगृहं Bh. 3. 88; H. 1. 47;<BR>Bg. 8. 5; Bv. 1. 103, 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलेवरं|कलेवर|कलेवरः
कलेवरः, --रं The body;<BR>यावत्स्वस्थमिदं कलेवरगृहं Bh. 3. 88; H. 1. 47;<BR>Bg. 8. 5; Bv. 1. 103, 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्क|कल्कः
कल्क a. [कल्-क Uṇ. 3. 40]<BR>Sinful, wicked.<BR>--ल्कः, --ल्कं<BR>1 The viscous<BR>sediment deposited by oily<BR>substances when ground.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of tenacious paste; Y. 1. 277.<BR>--3<BR>(Hence) Dirt, filth (in general).<BR>--4 Ordure, fæces.<BR>--5 Meanness,<BR>deceit, hypocrisy; Śi. 19. 98.<BR>--6 Sin.<BR>--7 Levigated powder; तां लोध्रकल्केन<BR>हृतांगतैलां Ku. 7. 9.<BR>--8 Incense.<BR>--9<BR>The wax of the ear.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फलः<BR>the pomegranate plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्कनं|कल्कन
कल्कनं Deceiving, over-reaching,<BR>falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्किः|कल्कि
कल्किः The tenth and last<BR>incarnation of Viṣṇu in his capacity of<BR>the destroyer of the wicked and<BR>liberator of the world from its<BR>enemies; (Jayadeva, while referring<BR>to the several avatāras of Viṣṇu,<BR>thus refers to the last or Kalki<BR>avatāra: --म्लेच्छनिवहनिधने कलयसि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-a" target="_blank">Page0388-a+ 56</a>]<BR>करवालम् धूमकेतुमिव किमपि करालम् । केशव<BR>धृतकल्किशरीरं जय जगदीश हरे ॥ Gīt. 1.<BR>10.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0387-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्किन्
कल्किन् a.<BR>1 Foul, turbid, dirty.<BR>--2 Wicked. --m. see कल्कि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्प|कल्पः
कल्प a. [कॢप्-घञ्]<BR>1 Practicable,<BR>feasible, possible.<BR>--2 Proper, fit, right.<BR>--3<BR>Strong, vigorous.<BR>--4 Able, competent<BR>(with a gen., loc.; inf. or at the end<BR>of comp.); धर्मस्य, यशसः, कल्पः<BR>Bhāg. able to do his duty &c.;<BR>स्वक्रियायामकल्पः ibid. not competent to<BR>do one's duty; अकल्प<BR>एषामधिरोढुमंजसा पदं ibid., so स्वभरणाकल्प &c.<BR>--ल्पः<BR>1 A sacred precept or rule,<BR>law, ordinance.<BR>--2 A prescribed rule,<BR>a prescribed alternative, optional<BR>rule; प्रभुः प्रथमकल्पस्य योऽनुकल्पेन<BR>वर्तते Ms. 11. 30 ‘able to follow the<BR>prescribed rule to be observed in<BR>preference to all others’; प्रथमः कल्पः<BR>M. 1 a very good (or best)<BR>alternative; एष वै प्रथमः कल्पः प्रदाने<BR>हव्यकव्ययोः Ms. 3. 147.<BR>--3 (Hence) A<BR>proposal, suggestion, resolve,<BR>determination; उदारः कल्पः Ś. 7.<BR>--4<BR>Manner of acting, procedure, form,<BR>way, method (in religious rites);<BR>क्षात्रेण कल्पेनोपनीय U. 2;<BR>कल्पदित्कल्पयामास वन्यामेवास्य संविधां R. 1. 94;<BR>Ms. 7. 185.<BR>--5 End of the world,<BR>universal destruction.<BR>--6 A day of<BR>Brahmā or 1,000 Yugas, being a<BR>period of 432 million years of<BR>mortals and measuring the duration<BR>of the world; श्रीश्वेतवाराहकल्पे (the<BR>one in which we now live); कल्पं<BR>स्थितं तनुभृतां तनुभिस्ततः किम्<BR>Śānti. 4. 2.<BR>--7 Medical treatment of the<BR>sick.<BR>--8 One of the six Vedāṅgas,<BR>i. e. that which lays down the<BR>ritual and prescribes rules for<BR>ceremonial and sacrificial acts; see under<BR>वेदांग.<BR>--9 A termination added to<BR>nouns and adjectives in the sense of<BR>‘a little less than,’ ‘almost like,’<BR>‘nearly equal to,’ (denoting<BR>similarity with a degree of inferiority);<BR>कुमारकल्पं सुषुवे कुमारं R. 5. 36;<BR>उपपन्नमेतदस्मिन्नृषिकल्पे राजनि Ś. 2;<BR>प्रभातकल्पा शशिनेव शर्वरी R. 3. 2; so<BR>मृतकल्पः, प्रतिपन्नकल्पः &c.<BR>--10 The<BR>doctrine of poisons and antidotes.<BR>--11 One of the trees of paradise;<BR>cf. कल्पद्रुम.<BR>--ल्पा --ल्पं A kind of<BR>intoxicating liquor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-b" target="_blank">Page0388-b+ 57</a>]<BR>end of the world, universal<BR>destruction; Bh. 2. 16. ˚स्थायिन् a.<BR>lasting to the end of a कल्प.<BR>--आदि<BR>renovation of all things in the<BR>creation.<BR>--कारः {1} author of<BR>Kalpasūtra, q. v. {2} a barber.<BR>--क्षयः end<BR>of the world, universal destruction;<BR>e. g. पुरा कल्पक्षये वृत्ते जातं जलमयं<BR>जगत् Ks. 2. 10.<BR>--तरुः, --द्रुमः,<BR>--पदपः, --वृक्षः {1} one of the trees of<BR>heaven or Indra's paradise;<BR>R. 1. 75; 17. 26; Ku. 2. 39; 6. 41. {2} a<BR>tree supposed to grant all desires,<BR>‘wish-yielding tree’; न बुद्ध कल्पद्रुमतां<BR>विहाय जातं तमात्मन्यसिपत्रवृक्षं<BR>R. 14. 48; N. 1. 15. {3} (fig.) a very<BR>generous person; सकलार्थिसार्थकल्पद्रुमः<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--पालः {1} a protector of order.<BR>{2} a seller of spirituous liquors.<BR>--लता, --लतिका {1} a creeper of Indra's<BR>paradise: Bh. 1. 90. {2} a creeper<BR>supposed to grant all desires;<BR>नानाफलैः फलति कल्पलतेव भूमिः<BR>Bh. 2. 46; cf. कल्पतरु above.<BR>--विद् a.<BR>conversant with sacred precepts;<BR>R. 1. 94.<BR>--सूत्रं a manual of ritual<BR>in the form of Sūtras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पकः|कल्पक
कल्पकः [कॢप्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A rite.<BR>--2<BR>A barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पनं|कल्पन
कल्पनं [कॢप् ल्युट्]<BR>1 Forming,<BR>fashioning, arranging.<BR>--2<BR>Performing, doing, effecting.<BR>--3 Clipping,<BR>cutting.<BR>--4 Fixing.<BR>--5 Anything<BR>placed upon another for decoration.<BR>--ना<BR>1 Fixing, settlement;<BR>अनेकपितृकाणां तु पितृतो भागकल्पना Y. 2. 120,<BR>247; Ms. 9. 116.<BR>--2 Making,<BR>performing, doing.<BR>--3 Forming,<BR>arranging; विषमासु च कल्पनासु Mk. 3. 14;<BR>केश˚ Mk. 4.<BR>--4 Decorating,<BR>ornamenting.<BR>--5 Composition.<BR>--6<BR>Invention.<BR>--7 Imagination, thought;<BR>कल्पनापोढः Sk. = कल्पनाया अपोढः.<BR>--8 An idea, fancy or image<BR>(conceived in the mind);<BR>Śānti. 2. 8.<BR>--9 Fabrication.<BR>--10<BR>Forgery.<BR>--11 A contrivance, device.<BR>--12 (In Mīm. phil.) = अर्थापत्ति q. v.<BR>--13 Decorating an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पनी
कल्पनी Scissors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पनीय
कल्पनीय a.<BR>1 To be made,<BR>fashioned or contrived.<BR>--2 Feasible.<BR>--3<BR>To be substituted or supplied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पिक
कल्पिक a. Fit, proper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्पित|कल्पितः
कल्पित a. Arranged, made,<BR>fashioned, formed; Ś. 3. 22; see कॢप्<BR>caus.<BR>--तः An elephant armed or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-c" target="_blank">Page0388-c+ 55</a>]<BR>caparisoned for war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मन्
कल्मन् = कर्मन् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मलिः|कल्मलि
कल्मलिः Ved. Splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मलीकं|कल्मलीक
कल्मलीकं Brightness, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्मष|कल्मषं|कल्मषः
कल्मष a.<BR>1 Sinful, wicked.<BR>--2<BR>Foul, dirty.<BR>--षः, --षं<BR>1 Stain, dirt,<BR>dregs.<BR>--2 The hand below the wrist.<BR>--3 Sin; स हि गगनविहारी<BR>कल्मषध्वंसकारी H. 1. 21; Bg. 4. 30; 5. 16;<BR>Ms. 4. 260, 12. 18, 22.<BR>--षः Hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्माष|कल्माषः
कल्माष a. (षी f.)<BR>1<BR>Variegated, spotted.<BR>--2 Black and white.<BR>--षः<BR>1 The variegated colour.<BR>--2<BR>A mixture of black and white.<BR>--3<BR>A demon, goblin.<BR>--4 The black<BR>colour.<BR>--5 A form of Agni.<BR>--6 A<BR>kind of fragrant rice.<BR>--षी<BR>1 N. of<BR>the river Yamunā<BR>--2 The<BR>spotted cow of Jamadagni.<BR>--षं Stain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--पादः N. of a king (सौदास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्य|कल्यं|कल्यः
कल्य a. [कलयति चेष्टामत्र, कल्-यक्;<BR>कल् कर्मणि यत्, कलासु साधु कला-यत् वा<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 Sound, free from sickness,<BR>healthy; सर्वः कल्ये वयसि यतते<BR>लब्धुमर्थान्कुटुंबी V. 3. 1; Y. 1. 28; यावदेव<BR>भवेत्कल्यस्तावच्छ्रेयः समाचरेत् Mb.<BR>--2<BR>Ready, prepared; कथयस्व कथामेतां<BR>कल्याः स्मः श्रवणे तव Mb.<BR>--3 Clever.<BR>--4 Agreeable, auspicious (as a<BR>discourse).<BR>--5 Deaf and dumb.<BR>--6<BR>Instructive.<BR>--ल्यं<BR>1 Dawn, day-break.<BR>--2 To-morrow.<BR>--3 Sprituous liquor.<BR>--4 Congratulation, good wishes.<BR>--5 Good news.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशः,<BR>--जग्धिः f. the morning meal,<BR>breakfast.<BR>--पालः, --पालकः a distiller.<BR>--वर्तः morning meal, breakfast.<BR>--(र्तं) (hence) anything light,<BR>trivial, or unimportant; a trifle; ननु<BR>कल्यवर्तमेतत् Mk. 2 but a trifle;<BR>स्त्रीकल्यवर्तस्य कारणेन 4; स इदानीमर्थकल्यवर्तस्य<BR>कारणादिदमकार्यं करोति 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्या
कल्या<BR>1 Spirituous liquor.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a plant (हरीतकी).<BR>--3<BR>Congratulation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पालः, --पालकः a<BR>distiller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याण|कल्याणं|कल्याणः
कल्याण a. (णा or णी f.) [कल्ये<BR>प्रातः अण्यते शब्द्यते, अण्-घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Blessed, happy, lucky,<BR>fortunate; त्वमेव कल्याणि तयोस्तृतीया<BR>R. 6. 29; Me. 109.<BR>--2<BR>Beautiful, agreeable, lovely.<BR>--3 Excellent,<BR>illustrious.<BR>--4 Auspicious, salutary,<BR>propitious, good; U. 2. 2; कल्याणानां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">Page0389-a+ 55</a>]<BR>त्वमसि महसां भाजनं विश्वमूर्ते Māl. 1. 3.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Good fortune, happiness, good,<BR>prosperity; कल्याणं कुरुतां जनस्य<BR>भगचांश्चंद्रार्धचूडामणिः H. 1. 212; तद्रक्ष<BR>कल्याणपरंपराणां भोक्तारमूर्जस्वलमात्मदहं<BR>R. 2. 50; 17. 11; Ms. 3. 60; so<BR>˚अभिनिवेशी K. 104.<BR>--2 Virtue.<BR>--3<BR>Festival.<BR>--4 Gold.<BR>--5 Heaven.<BR>--णी<BR>1 A cow.<BR>--2 Holy or sacred cow;<BR>R. 1. 87.<BR>--3 A young cow, heifer;<BR>U. 4.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत् a. {1} doing<BR>good, beneficial, good; Bg. 6. 40.<BR>{2} propitious, lucky. {3} virtuous.<BR>--धर्मन् a. virtuous.<BR>--बीजं a kind of<BR>pulse; (Mar. मसुरा).<BR>--वचनं a<BR>friendly speech, good wishes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0388-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणक
कल्याणक a. (णिका f.)<BR>Auspicious, prosperous, blessed.<BR>--णिका<BR>Red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्याणिन्
कल्याणिन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Happy,<BR>prosperous.<BR>--2 Lucky, fortunate,<BR>blessed.<BR>--3 Propitious, auspicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल्
कल्ल् {c1c} A. (कल्लते, कल्लित)<BR>1 To<BR>sound indistinctly.<BR>--2 To sound.<BR>--3<BR>To be mute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्ल|कल्लः
कल्ल a. Deaf; ˚ता-त्वं<BR>1 Deafness.<BR>--2 Indistinctness of articulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लि
कल्लि ind. To-morrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लोल|कल्लोलः
कल्लोल a. Inimical, hostile.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A large wave, billow; आयुः<BR>कल्लोललोलं Bh. 3. 82; कल्लोलमालाकुलं<BR>Bv. 1. 59.<BR>--2 An enemy.<BR>--3 Joy,<BR>happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्लोलिनी
कल्लोलिनी A river;<BR>स्वर्लोककल्लोलिनि त्वं पापं तिरयाधुना मम<BR>भवव्यालावलीढात्मनः G. L. 50; so<BR>विपुलपुलिनाः कल्लोलिन्यः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्हारं|कल्हार
कल्हारं A white water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्
कव् {c1c} A. (कवते, कवित)<BR>1 To praise.<BR>--2 To describe, compose (as a<BR>poem).<BR>--3 To paint, picture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवकः|कवक|कवकं
कवकः A mouthful.<BR>--कं A<BR>mushroom; विड्जानि कवकानि च<BR>Y. 1. 171; Ms. 5. 5; 6. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचः|कवच|कवचं
कवचः, --चं [cf. Uṇ. 4. 2]<BR>1 An<BR>armour, coat of mail, a mail.<BR>--2<BR>An amulet, a charm, a mystical<BR>syllable (हुं-हूं) considered as a<BR>preservative like armour.<BR>--3 A<BR>kettledrum.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रः the birch<BR>tree.<BR>--हर a. {1} wearing armour.<BR>{2} old enough to wear an<BR>armour; कवचहरः कुमारः Sk.;<BR>cf. वर्महर in R. 8. 94.<BR>--(रः) a boy,<BR>child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवचं|कवच|कवचः
कवचः, --चं [cf. Uṇ. 4. 2]<BR>1 An<BR>armour, coat of mail, a mail.<BR>--2<BR>An amulet, a charm, a mystical<BR>syllable (हुं-हूं) considered as a<BR>preservative like armour.<BR>--3 A<BR>kettledrum.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रः the birch<BR>tree.<BR>--हर a. {1} wearing armour.<BR>{2} old enough to wear an<BR>armour; कवचहरः कुमारः Sk.;<BR>cf. वर्महर in R. 8. 94.<BR>--(रः) a boy,<BR>child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवटी
कवटी The leaf or panel of a<BR>door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवडः|कवड
कवडः Water for washing the<BR>mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवत्नु
कवत्नु n. A bad deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवनं|कवन
कवनं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवर|कवरं|कवरः
कव(ब)र a. [Uṇ. 4. 154.] (--रा,<BR>--री f.)<BR>1 Mixed, intermingled;<BR>Śi. 5. 19.<BR>--2 Set, inlaid.<BR>--3 Variegated.<BR>--रः, --रं<BR>1 Salt.<BR>--2 Sourness or<BR>acidity.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A braid or fillet of hair.<BR>--2 A lecturer (पाठक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबर
कव(ब)र a. [Uṇ. 4. 154.] (--रा,<BR>--री f.)<BR>1 Mixed, intermingled;<BR>Śi. 5. 19.<BR>--2 Set, inlaid.<BR>--3 Variegated.<BR>--रः, --रं<BR>1 Salt.<BR>--2 Sourness or<BR>acidity.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A braid or fillet of hair.<BR>--2 A lecturer (पाठक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरी
कव(ब)री A braid or fillet of hair;<BR>दधती विलोलकवरीकमाननं U. 3. 4;<BR>Śi. 9. 28; Amaru. 59.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भरः,<BR>--भारः a fine head of hair; घटय जघने<BR>कांचीमंच स्रजा कवरीभरं Gīt. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कबरी
कव(ब)री A braid or fillet of hair;<BR>दधती विलोलकवरीकमाननं U. 3. 4;<BR>Śi. 9. 28; Amaru. 59.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भरः,<BR>--भारः a fine head of hair; घटय जघने<BR>कांचीमंच स्रजा कवरीभरं Gīt. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवरकी
कवरकी A prisoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलः|कवल|कवलं
कवलः, --लं [केन जलेन वलते चलति,<BR>वल्-अच् Tv.]<BR>1 A mouthful;<BR>आस्वादवद्भिः कवलैस्तृणानां R. 2. 5; 9. 59;<BR>कवलच्छेदेषु संपादिताः U. 3. 16.<BR>--2<BR>A gargle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलं|कवल|कवलः
कवलः, --लं [केन जलेन वलते चलति,<BR>वल्-अच् Tv.]<BR>1 A mouthful;<BR>आस्वादवद्भिः कवलैस्तृणानां R. 2. 5; 9. 59;<BR>कवलच्छेदेषु संपादिताः U. 3. 16.<BR>--2<BR>A gargle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलयति
कवलयति Den. P. To eat, devour;<BR>Pt. 4; Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलिका
कवलिका A bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवलित|कवलितः
कवलित a.<BR>1 Eaten, swallowed up<BR>(as a mouthful).<BR>--2 Chewed.<BR>--3<BR>(Hence) Taken, seized; as in मृत्युना<BR>कवलिता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवष|कवषः
कवष, --कवष् a. Ved. Sounding,<BR>creaking (as the door).<BR>--षः A<BR>shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवष्
कवष, --कवष् a. Ved. Sounding,<BR>creaking (as the door).<BR>--षः A<BR>shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवसः|कवस
कवसः<BR>1 An armour.<BR>--2 A<BR>prickly shrub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवाट|कवाटः
कवाट See कपाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवारं|कवार
कवारं A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवारि
कवारि a. Ved. Selfish, stingy; a<BR>mean or contemptible enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवि|कविः
कवि a. [कु-इ Uṇ. 4. 138]<BR>1<BR>Omniscient; Bg. 8. 9; Ms. 4. 24.<BR>--2 Intelligent, clever, wise.<BR>--3<BR>Thinking, thoughtful.<BR>--4<BR>Praiseworthy.<BR>--विः<BR>1 A wise man, a<BR>thinker, a sage; कवीनामुशना कविः<BR>Bg. 10. 37; Ms. 7. 49, 2. 151.<BR>--2 A<BR>poet; तद्ब्रूहि रामचरितं आद्यः कविरसि<BR>U. 2; मंदः कवियशःप्रार्थी R. 1. 3;<BR>इदं कविभ्यः पूर्वेभ्यो नमोवाकं प्रशास्महे<BR>U. 1. 1; Śi. 2. 86.<BR>--3 An epithet of<BR>Śukra, the preceptor of the Asuras;<BR>कविरिव वृषपर्वणः K. 56.<BR>--4 Vālmīki, the<BR>first poet.<BR>--5 Brahmā.<BR>--6 The sun.<BR>--f. The bit of a bridle; see कविका.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">Page0389-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्येष्ठः an epithet of<BR>Vālmīki, the first poet.<BR>--पुत्रः an<BR>epithet of Śukra.<BR>--राजः {1} a great<BR>poet; श्रीहर्षं कविराजराजिमुकुटालंकारहीरः<BR>सुतं occurring in the last verse of<BR>every canto of Naiṣadha Carita.<BR>{2} N. of a poet, author of a poem<BR>called राघवपांडवीय.<BR>--रामायणः an<BR>epithet of Vālmīki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविकः|कविक|कविकं
कविकः, का The bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

का
कविकः, का The bit of a bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कविता
कविता Poetry; सुकविता यद्यस्ति<BR>राज्येन किं Bh. 2. 21;<BR>यस्याश्चोरश्चिकुरनिकरः कर्णपूरो मयूरो भासो हासः<BR>कविकुलगुरुः कालिदासो विलासः । हर्षो हर्षो<BR>हृदयवसतिः पंचबाणस्तु बाणः केषां नैषा<BR>कथय कविताकामिनी कौतुकाय ॥<BR>P. R. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवियं|कविय
कवि(वी)यं The bit of a<BR>bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवीयं|कवीय
कवि(वी)यं The bit of a<BR>bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवेलं|कवेल
कवेलं A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कवोष्ण|कवोष्णं
कवोष्ण a. Slightly warm, tepid;<BR>R. 1. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कव्यं|कव्य|कव्यः
कव्यं (opp. हव्य) An oblation of<BR>food to deceased ancestors; एष वै<BR>प्रथमः कल्पः प्रदाने हव्यकव्ययोः<BR>Ms. 3. 147, 97, 128.<BR>--व्यः A class of<BR>manes.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वालः {1} fire. {2} a<BR>class of manes.<BR>--वाह् m.,<BR>--वाहः,<BR>--वाहनः fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्
कश् {c1c} P. To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशः|कश
कशः<BR>1 A whip (usually in pl.).<BR>--शा A whip; इदानीं सुकुमारेऽस्मिन्<BR>निःशंकं कर्कशाः कशाः । तव गात्रे पतिष्यंति<BR>सहास्माकं मनोरथैः ॥ Mk. 9. 35 (where<BR>the word may be m. or f.)<BR>--2<BR>Flogging.<BR>--3 A string, rope.<BR>--4 The<BR>mouth.<BR>--5 A quality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्य|कश्यं
कश्य a. [कशामर्हति, कशा-यत्] Fit<BR>to be whipped or flogged.<BR>--श्यं<BR>1<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>--2 A horse's<BR>flank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशस्
कशस् n. Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशिकः|कशिक
कशिकः A mungoose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशिपु|कशिपुः
कशिपु m. or n.<BR>1 A mat.<BR>--2 A<BR>pillow.<BR>--3 A bed.<BR>--पुः<BR>1 Food.<BR>--2<BR>Clothing.<BR>--3 Food and clothing<BR>(according to विश्व).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरु|कशेरुः
कशे(से)रु m. n.<BR>1 The<BR>backbone.<BR>--2 A kind of grass.<BR>--रुः One<BR>of the nine divisions of<BR>Jambudvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरु|कसेरुः
कशे(से)रु m. n.<BR>1 The<BR>backbone.<BR>--2 A kind of grass.<BR>--रुः One<BR>of the nine divisions of<BR>Jambudvīpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुकः|कशेरुक|कशेरुकं
कशेरुकः, कसेरुकः --का A sort of<BR>grass.<BR>--का The back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरुकः|कसेरुक
कशेरुकः, कसेरुकः --का A sort of<BR>grass.<BR>--का The back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुका
कशेरुकः, कसेरुकः --का A sort of<BR>grass.<BR>--का The back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कशेरुका
कशेरुकः, कसेरुकः --का A sort of<BR>grass.<BR>--का The back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मल|कश्मलं
कश्मल a. [Uṇ. 1. 106.] Foul, dirty,<BR>disgraceful, ignominious;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-a" target="_blank">Page0390-a+ 59</a>]<BR>मत्संबंधात्कश्मला किंवदंती स्याच्चेदस्मिन्हंत<BR>धिङ्मामधन्यं U. 1. 42.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Dejection of<BR>mind, lowness or depression of spirits;<BR>कश्मलं महदाविशत् Mb.; कुतस्त्वा<BR>कश्मलमिदं विषमे समुपस्थितं Bg. 2. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Sin<BR>--3 A swoon.<BR>--4 Consternation,<BR>alarm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0389-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्मीरः|कश्मीर
कश्मीरः (pl.) N. of a country,<BR>the modern Kāshmīra. (Its<BR>position is thus described in Tantras:<BR>--शारदामठमारभ्य कुंकुमाद्रितटांतकः ।<BR>तावत्कश्मीरदेशः स्यात् पंचाशद्योजनात्मकः).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः, --जं, --जन्मन् m., n. saffron;<BR>कश्मीरजस्य कटुताऽपि नितांतरम्या<BR>Bv. 1. 71. v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कश्यपः|कश्यप
कश्यपः a. Having black teeth.<BR>--पः<BR>1 A tortoise.<BR>--2 A sort of fish.<BR>--3 A kind of deer.<BR>--4 N. of a<BR>Ṛṣi, the husband of Aditi and<BR>Diti, and thus the father both of gods<BR>and demons, (so called because he<BR>drank कश्य ‘liquor;’ cf. कश्यपस्तस्य<BR>पुत्रोऽभूत् कश्यपानात् स कश्यपः । Mārk. P.)<BR>[He was the son of Marīci, the son of<BR>Brahmā. He bears a very important<BR>share in the work of creation.<BR>According to Mahābhārata and other accounts,<BR>he married Aditi and 12 other<BR>daughters of Dakṣa, and begot on Aditi<BR>the twelve Ādityas. By his other<BR>twelve wives he had a numerous and<BR>very diversified progeny: serpents,<BR>reptiles, birds, demons, nymphs of<BR>the lunar constellation. He was thus<BR>the father of gods, demons, men,<BR>beasts, birds and reptiles-in fact<BR>of all living beings. He is therefore<BR>often called Prajāpati].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नंदनः an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्
कष् {vI.v} {c1c} U. (कषति-ते, कषित)<BR>1 To<BR>rub, scratch, scrape; समूलकाषं कषति<BR>Sk; Bk. 3. 49.<BR>--2 To test, try, rub<BR>on a touch-stone (as gold); छदहेम<BR>कषन्निवालसत्कषपाषाणनिभे नभस्तले<BR>N. 2. 69.<BR>--3 To injure, destroy.<BR>--4 To<BR>itch.<BR>--5 To leap. {vII.v} {c10c} P. (काषयति)<BR>To hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष|कषः
कष a. [कस्-अच्] Rubbing,<BR>scratching.<BR>--षः<BR>1 Rubbing.<BR>--2 A<BR>touchstone; छदहेम<BR>कषन्निवालसत्कषपाषाणनिभे नभस्तले N. 2. 69; Mk. 3. 17.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पट्टिका a touch-stone;<BR>Vikr. 1. 3, 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषण|कषणः
कषण a. [कष्-ल्युट्] Unripe,<BR>immature.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Rubbing, marking,<BR>scratching;<BR>कंडूलद्विपगंडपिंडकषणोत्कंपेन संपातिभिः U. 2. 9;<BR>कषणकंपनिरस्तमहाहिभिः Ki. 5. 47.<BR>--2 Test of gold<BR>by the touch-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषा
कषा = कशा^1 q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/Cologne/issues/157. note: kaSA is a headword, and alternate of kazA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाकुः|कषाकु
कषाकुः<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषि|कषिः
कषि a. Injurious, harmful,<BR>hurtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषित
कषित a. Hurt, injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्टिः|कष्टि
कष्टिः f.<BR>1 Test, trial.<BR>--2 Injury,<BR>trouble, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषाय|कषायः
कषाय a.<BR>1 Astringent; Ś. 2.<BR>--2 Fragrant;<BR>स्फुटितकमलामोदमैत्रीकषायः Me. 31; U. 2. 21;<BR>Mv. 5. 41.<BR>--3 Red, dark-red;<BR>चूतांकुरास्वादकषायकंठः Ku. 3. 32.<BR>--4 (Hence)<BR>Sweet-sounding; Māl. 7.<BR>--5 Brown.<BR>--6 Improper, dirty.<BR>--यः, --यं<BR>1<BR>Astringent flavour or taste (one of<BR>the six rasas): see कटु; यो वक्त्रं<BR>परिशोषयति जिह्वां स्तंभयति कंठं बध्नाति हृदयं<BR>कषति पीडयति च स कषायः Suśr.<BR>--2 The<BR>red colour.<BR>--3 A decoction with<BR>one part of a drug mixed with<BR>four, eight, or sixteen parts of<BR>water (the whole being boiled<BR>down until one quarter is left);<BR>Ms. 11. 154.<BR>--4 Plastering,<BR>smearing; Ku. 7. 17; anointing.<BR>--5<BR>Perfuming the body with unguents;<BR>Rs. 1. 4.<BR>--6 Gum, resin, extract or<BR>exudation from a tree.<BR>--7 Dirt,<BR>uncleanness.<BR>--8 Dulness, stupidity.<BR>--9<BR>Attachment to worldly objects.<BR>--10<BR>Decay, ruin.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Passion,<BR>emotion.<BR>--2 Kali yuga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायित
कषायित a.<BR>1 Tinged, reddened,<BR>coloured; अमुनैव कषायितस्तनी<BR>Ku. 4. 34; Śi. 7. 11.<BR>--2 Affected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषायिन्
कषायिन् a.<BR>1 Yielding a resinous<BR>exudation, astringent.<BR>--2 Dyed of<BR>a red colour.<BR>--3 Worldly-minded.<BR>--m. N. of several plants:<BR>--खर्जूर,<BR>शाल &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषिका
कषिका A bird in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषीका
कषीका A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कषेरुका
कषे(से)रुका The backbone,<BR>the spine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरुका
कषे(से)रुका The backbone,<BR>the spine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्कष|कष्कषः
कष्कषः A kind of poisonous<BR>insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कष्ट|कष्टं|कष्टः
कष्ट a. [कष्-क्त]<BR>1 Bad, evil, ill,<BR>wrong; रामहस्तमनुप्राप्य कष्टात् कष्टतरं<BR>गता R. 15. 43 ‘gone from bad to<BR>worse’, (reduced to a wretched<BR>condition).<BR>--2 Painful, grievous;<BR>मोहादभूत्कष्टतरः प्रबोधः R. 14. 56; कष्टोऽयं<BR>खलु भृत्यभावः Ratn. 1 full of cares;<BR>Ms. 7. 50; Māl. 9. 37; Y. 3. 29;<BR>कष्टा वृत्तिः पराधीना कष्टो वासो निराश्रयः ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">Page0390-c+ 53</a>]<BR>निर्धनो व्यवसायश्च सर्वकष्टा दरिद्रता ॥<BR>Chāṇ. 59<BR>--3 Difficult; स्त्रीषु कष्टोऽ<BR>धिकारः V. 3. 1; U. 7.<BR>--4 Hard to subdue<BR>(as an enemy); Ms. 7. 186, 210.<BR>--5 Mischievous, hurtful, injurious.<BR>--6 Boding evil.<BR>--7 Sorrowful,<BR>miserable.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 Evil, difficulty, misery,<BR>suffering, hardship, pain; कष्टं<BR>खल्वनपत्यता Ś. 6; धिगर्थाः कष्टसंश्रयाः<BR>Pt. 1. 163.<BR>--2 Sin, wickedness.<BR>--3<BR>Difficulty, effort; कष्टेन some how or<BR>other.<BR>--ष्टं ind. Alas! Ah.! हा धिक्<BR>कष्टं; हा कष्टं जरयाभिभूतपुरुषः<BR>पुत्रैरवज्ञायते Pt. 4. 78.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आगत a.<BR>arrived or got with difficulty.<BR>--कर a.<BR>giving pain, troublesome.<BR>--कारः --कारकः<BR>the world (as the scene of miseries).<BR>--तपस् a. one who practises hard<BR>penance; Ś. 7<BR>--संश्रय a. attended<BR>with troubles: Pt. 1. 163; 2. 118.<BR>--साध्य a. to be accomplished with<BR>difficulty.<BR>--स्थानं a bad station, a<BR>difficult or disagreeable place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्
कस् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (कसति, कसित) To<BR>move, go, approach. {vII.v} {c2c} A. (कस्ते<BR>or कंस्ते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसः|कस
कसः A touchstone; cf. कष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसना
कसना A poisonous spider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसिपुः|कसिपु
कसिपुः Food, boild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कसेरुः|कसेरु
कसेरुः A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तंभी|कस्तम्भी
कस्तंभी Ved. The prop of a<BR>carriage-pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तीरं|कस्तीर
कस्तीरं Tin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तुरिका
कस्तु(स्तू)रिका, कस्तूरी Musk;<BR>कस्तूरिकातिलकमालि विधाय सायं<BR>Bv. 2. 4; 1. 121; Ch. P. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मृगः<BR>the musk-deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरिका
कस्तु(स्तू)रिका, कस्तूरी Musk;<BR>कस्तूरिकातिलकमालि विधाय सायं<BR>Bv. 2. 4; 1. 121; Ch. P. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मृगः<BR>the musk-deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्तूरी
कस्तु(स्तू)रिका, कस्तूरी Musk;<BR>कस्तूरिकातिलकमालि विधाय सायं<BR>Bv. 2. 4; 1. 121; Ch. P. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मृगः<BR>the musk-deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्मल|कस्मलं
कस्मल = कश्मल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कस्वर
कस्वर a.<BR>1 Going;<BR>--2 Injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कहाहः|कहाह
कहाहः A buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कह्लारं|कह्लार
कह्लारं The white lotus,<BR>कह्लारपद्मकुसुमानि मुहुर्विधुन्वन् Rs. 3. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कह्वः|कह्व
कह्वः A kind of cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांशिः|कांशि
कांशिः A cup; (कंसपात्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांसीयं|कांसीय
कांसीयं White copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्य|कांस्यं|कांस्यः
कांस्य a. [कंसाय पानपात्राय हितं कंसीयं<BR>तस्य विकारः यञ् छलोपः cf. P. IV. 3. 168]<BR>Made of white copper or bell-metal;<BR>Ms. 4. 65.<BR>--स्यं<BR>1 Bell-metal or<BR>white copper; Ms. 5. 114; Y. 1. 190.<BR>--2 A gong of bell-metal.<BR>--स्यः, --स्यं<BR>A drinking vessel (of brass), a<BR>goblet; Śi. 15. 81.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-a" target="_blank">Page0391-a+ 57</a>]<BR>(री f.) a brazier, a worker in<BR>bellmetal.<BR>--तालः a cymbal.<BR>--भाजनं a<BR>brass-vessel.<BR>--मलं verdigris.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0390-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांस्यकं|कांस्यक
कांस्यकं Brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकः|काक|काकं
काकः [कै शब्दकरणे-कन् Uṇ. 3. 43]<BR>1 A crow; काकोपि जीवति चिराय बलिं च<BR>भुंक्ते Pt. 1. 24.<BR>--2 (Fig.) A<BR>contemptible fellow, base or impudent person.<BR>--3 A lame man.<BR>--4 Bathing by<BR>dipping the head only into water (as<BR>crows do).<BR>--5 A sectarial mark (<BR>तिलक).<BR>--6 A kind of measure.<BR>--7 N. of<BR>a Dvīpa.<BR>--का N. of several plants:<BR>काकनासा, काकोली &c.<BR>--की A female<BR>crow.<BR>--का<BR>1 A multitude of crows.<BR>--2<BR>A modus coeundi.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षिगोलकन्याय see under न्याय.<BR>--अरिः an<BR>owl.<BR>--उदरः a snake; काकोदरो येन<BR>विनीतदर्पः Kavirāja; काकोदरसोदरः खलो<BR>जगति Bv. 1. 76.<BR>--उलूकिका,<BR>--उलूकीयं the natural enmity of the owl and<BR>the crow; (काकोलूकीयं is the name<BR>of the third Tantra in the<BR>Panchatantra).<BR>--चिंचा the Guñjā<BR>plant.<BR>--छदः, --छदिः {1} a wag-tail.<BR>{2} a side-lock of hair; see काकपक्ष<BR>below.<BR>--जातः the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR>--तालीय a. (anything) taking place<BR>quite unexpectedly and accidentally,<BR>an accident; अहो नु खलु भोः तदेतत्<BR>काकतालीयं नाम Māl. 5;<BR>काकतालीयवत्प्राप्तं दृष्ट्वापि निधिमग्रतः H. Pr. 35;<BR>sometimes used adverbially in the sense<BR>of ‘accidentally’; फलंति काकतालीयं<BR>तेभ्यः प्राज्ञा न बिभ्यति Ve. 2. 14. ˚न्याय<BR>see under न्याय.<BR>--तांलुकिन् a.<BR>contemptible, vile.<BR>--दंतः (lit.) the tooth<BR>of a crow; (fig.) anything impossible<BR>or not existing; ˚गवेषणं searching<BR>after impossibilities, (said of any<BR>useless and unprofitable task).<BR>--ध्वजः<BR>the submarine fire.<BR>--निद्रा a light<BR>slumber (easily broken).<BR>--पक्षः,<BR>--पक्षकः side-locks of hair on the<BR>temples of boys and young men<BR>(especially of the Kṣatriya caste); क<BR>कपक्षधरमेत्य याचितः R. 11. 1, 31, 42;<BR>3. 28; U. 3.<BR>--पदं {1} the sign (⁁) in Mss.<BR>denoting that something has been left<BR>out. {2} an incision in the skin.<BR>--(दः)<BR>a particular mode of sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR>--पुच्छः, --पुष्टः the (Indian)<BR>cuckoo.<BR>--पेय a. shallow; काकपेया नदी<BR>Sk.<BR>--भीरुः an owl.<BR>--मद्गुः a gallinule.<BR>--यवः barren corn (the ear of which<BR>has no grain); यथा काकयवाः प्रोक्ता<BR>यथारण्यभवास्तिलाः । नाममात्रा न सिद्धौ हि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">Page0391-b+ 55</a>]<BR>धनहीनास्तथानराः ॥ Pt. 2. 86; तथैव पांडवाः<BR>सर्वे यथा काकयवा इव Mb.; (काकयवाः =<BR>निष्फलतृणधान्यं).<BR>--रुतं the shrill sound<BR>of a crow (considered as a sign of<BR>future good or evil under different<BR>circumstances); Śi. 6. 76.<BR>--वंध्या a<BR>woman that bears only one child.<BR>--स्वरः a shrill tone (as that of a crow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकणं|काकण
काकणं Leprosy with black and<BR>red spots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकणिः|काकणि
काकणिः A kind of small coin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरुक|काकरुकः
काकरु(रू)क a.<BR>1 Timid,<BR>cowardly.<BR>--2 Naked.<BR>--3 Poor,<BR>indigent.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A hen-pecked husband.<BR>--2 (की f.) An owl.<BR>--3 Fraud,<BR>deceit, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकरूक|काकरूकः
काकरु(रू)क a.<BR>1 Timid,<BR>cowardly.<BR>--2 Naked.<BR>--3 Poor,<BR>indigent.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A hen-pecked husband.<BR>--2 (की f.) An owl.<BR>--3 Fraud,<BR>deceit, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलः|काकल|काकलं
काक(का)लः A raven.<BR>--लं A<BR>jewel worn upon the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकालः|काकाल
काक(का)लः A raven.<BR>--लं A<BR>jewel worn upon the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलकः|काकलक
काकलकः<BR>1 The top of the<BR>windpipe.<BR>--2 The thyroid cartilage.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An ornament of the neck.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलिः|काकलि
काकलिः, --ली f.<BR>1 A low and<BR>sweet tone; अनुबद्धमुग्धकाकलीसहितं<BR>U. 3; Rs. 1. 8.<BR>--2 A musical<BR>instrument with a low tone used by<BR>thieves to ascertain whether a<BR>person is asleep or not;<BR>फणिमुखकाकलीसंदंशक… प्रभृत्यनेकोपकरणयुक्तः<BR>Dk. 49.<BR>--3 Scissors.<BR>--4 The Guñjā plant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रवः the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकली
काकलिः, --ली f.<BR>1 A low and<BR>sweet tone; अनुबद्धमुग्धकाकलीसहितं<BR>U. 3; Rs. 1. 8.<BR>--2 A musical<BR>instrument with a low tone used by<BR>thieves to ascertain whether a<BR>person is asleep or not;<BR>फणिमुखकाकलीसंदंशक… प्रभृत्यनेकोपकरणयुक्तः<BR>Dk. 49.<BR>--3 Scissors.<BR>--4 The Guñjā plant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रवः the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकलीकः|काकलीक
काकलीकः A low sweet tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकार
काकार a. Scattering water(कं<BR>जलमाकिरति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणी
काकिणी, काकिणिका<BR>1 A shell<BR>or cowrie used as a coin.<BR>--2 A sum<BR>of money equal to 20 cowries or to<BR>a quarter of a Paṇa.<BR>--3 A weight<BR>equal to a quarter of a Māṣa.<BR>--4<BR>A part of a measure.<BR>--5 The beam<BR>of a balance.<BR>--6 A cubit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिणिका
काकिणी, काकिणिका<BR>1 A shell<BR>or cowrie used as a coin.<BR>--2 A sum<BR>of money equal to 20 cowries or to<BR>a quarter of a Paṇa.<BR>--3 A weight<BR>equal to a quarter of a Māṣa.<BR>--4<BR>A part of a measure.<BR>--5 The beam<BR>of a balance.<BR>--6 A cubit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिनी
काकिनी<BR>1 A quarter of a Paṇa<BR>q. v.<BR>--2 A quarter of a measure.<BR>--3<BR>cowrie; H. 3. 123.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकिलः|काकिल
काकिलः<BR>1 A jewel worn upon<BR>the neck.<BR>--2 The upper part of<BR>the neck,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुः|काकु
काकुः f.<BR>1 Change of the voice<BR>under different emotions, such as<BR>fear, grief, anger; भिन्नकंठध्वनिर्धीरैः<BR>काकुरित्यभिधीयते S. D.;<BR>अलीककाकुकरणकुशलतां K. 222. (Hence)<BR>--2<BR>A word of negation used in such<BR>a manner that it implies the<BR>contrary (affirmative), as in questions<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">Page0391-c+ 55</a>]<BR>of appeal, (in such cases the<BR>intended meaning is suggested by a<BR>change of the voice), cf.<BR>Pt. 1. 146.<BR>--3 Muttering, murmuring.<BR>--4<BR>Tongue.<BR>--5 Stress, emphasis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुत्स्थः|काकुत्स्थ
काकुत्स्थः [ककुत्स्थस्यापत्यं,<BR>ककुत्स्थअण्] A descendant of ककुत्स्थ,<BR>an epithet of the kings of the solar<BR>dynasty; काकुत्स्थमालोकयतां नृपाणां<BR>R. 6. 2; 12. 30, 46; see ककुत्स्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकुदं|काकुद
काकुदं The palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काकोलः|काकोल|काकोलं
काकोलः<BR>1 A raven; Y. 1. 174.<BR>--2 A snake.<BR>--3 A boar.<BR>--4 A<BR>potter.<BR>--5 A division of the infernal<BR>regions or hell; Y. 3. 223.<BR>--6 A<BR>poisonous substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षः|काक्ष
काक्षः [कुत्सितमक्षं अत्र, कोः कादेशः;<BR>cf. P. VI. 3. 104] A side-long look,<BR>a glance.<BR>--क्षं Frown, look of<BR>displeasure, malicious look;<BR>काक्षेणानादरेक्षितः Bk. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काक्षी
काक्षी A perfume, a kind of<BR>fragrant earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कागः|काग
कागः A crow; cf. काक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांक्ष्|काङ्क्ष्
कांक्ष् {c1c} P. (epic Atm. also).<BR>कांक्षति, कांक्षित<BR>1 To wish, desire,<BR>long for; यत्कांक्षंति<BR>तपोभिरन्यमुनयस्तस्मिंस्तपस्यंत्यमी Ś. 7. 12; न शोचति<BR>न कांक्षति Bg. 12. 7; न कांक्षे विजयं<BR>कृष्ण 1. 32; R. 12. 58; Ms. 2. 242.<BR>--2 To expect, wait for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांक्षा|काङ्क्षा
कांक्षा [कांक्ष्-अ]<BR>1 Wish, desire.<BR>--2 Inclination, appetite; as in<BR>भक्तकांक्षा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांक्षित|काङ्क्षित
कांक्षित p. p.<BR>1 Wished, desired.<BR>--2 Expected.<BR>--तं A wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांक्षिन्|काङ्क्षिन्
कांक्षिन् a. (णी f.) [कांक्ष् णिनि]<BR>Wishing for, desirous, दर्शन˚, जल˚<BR>&c.; Bg. 11. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांक्षोरुः|काङ्क्षोरु|काङ्क्षोरुः
कांक्षोरुः A heron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचः|काच|काचं
काचः<BR>1 Glass, crystal; आकरे<BR>पद्मरागाणां जन्म काचमणेः कुतः<BR>H. Pr. 44; काचमूल्येन विक्रीतो हंत<BR>चिंतामणिर्मया Śānti. 1. 12 ; मणिर्लुठति पादेषु<BR>काचः शिरसि धार्यते । यथैवास्ते तथैवास्तां<BR>काचः काचो मणिर्मणिः ॥ H. 2. 68.<BR>--2 A<BR>loop, a swinging shelf, a string so<BR>fastened to the yoke as to support<BR>burdens.<BR>--3 An eye-disease, an<BR>affection of the optic nerve, producing<BR>dimness of sight.<BR>--4 Alkaline ashes.<BR>--5 The string of the balance.<BR>--चं<BR>1 Alkaline salt.<BR>--2 Wax.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः N. of an aquatic bird (बक).<BR>--घटी a glass ewer.<BR>--भाजनं a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">Page0392-a+ 56</a>]<BR>glass vessel.<BR>--मंणिः crystal, quartz.<BR>--मलं, --लवणं, --संभवं black salt or<BR>soda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0391-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचकः|काचक
काचकः<BR>1 A glass, stone.<BR>--2<BR>Alkaline ashes &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचित|काचितं
काचित a. Suspended in a loop<BR>or by a swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचन|काचनं
काचन, काचनकं A string or<BR>tape which ties a parcel or bundle<BR>of papers or the leaves of a<BR>manuscript; cf. कचेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचनकं|काचनक
काचन, काचनकं A string or<BR>tape which ties a parcel or bundle<BR>of papers or the leaves of a<BR>manuscript; cf. कचेल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचनकिन्
काचनकिन् m. A manuscript,<BR>writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचिघः|काचिघ
काचिघः<BR>1 A rat, mouse.<BR>--2<BR>Gold.<BR>--3 A vegetable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काचूकः|काचूक
काचूकः<BR>1 A cock.<BR>--2 The<BR>Chakravāka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

काजलं|काजल
काजलं<BR>1 A little water.<BR>--2 Bad<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांच्|काञ्च्
कांच् {c1c} A. (कांचते, कांचित)<BR>1 To<BR>shine.<BR>--2 To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांचन|काञ्चन|काञ्चनं|काञ्चनः
कांचन a. (नी f.) [कांच्-ल्युट्]<BR>Golden, made of gold; तन्मध्ये च<BR>स्फटिकफलका कांचनी वासयष्टिः Me. 79; कांचनं<BR>वलयं Ś. 6. 5; Ms. 5. 112.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Gold; (ग्राह्यं) अमेध्यादपि कांचनं<BR>Ms. 2. 239.<BR>--2 Lustre, brilliancy.<BR>--3<BR>Property, wealth.<BR>--4 The filament<BR>of a lotus.<BR>--5 Yellow orpiment.<BR>--6<BR>A binding.<BR>--नः<BR>1 The Dhattūra<BR>plant.<BR>--2 The Campaka tree.<BR>--नी<BR>1 Turmeric.<BR>--2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगी a woman with a<BR>golden (i. e. yellow) complexion;<BR>Bv. 2. 72.<BR>--कंदरः a gold-mine.<BR>--गिरिः N. of the mountain Meru.<BR>--भूः f. {1} golden (yellow) soil. {2}<BR>gold-dust.<BR>--संधिः a treaty of alliance<BR>between two parties on terms of<BR>equality; cf. H. 4. 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांचनकः|काञ्चनक|काञ्चनकं|काञ्चनकः
कांचनकः The fruit of rice or grain.<BR>--कं Yellow orpiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांचनारः|काञ्चनार|कांचनार|काञ्चनारः
कांचनारः(लः) The Kovidāra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांचनालः|काञ्चनाल|कांचनाल|काञ्चनालः
कांचनारः(लः) The Kovidāra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांचनीय|काञ्चनीय
कांचनीय a. Golden.<BR>--या Yellow<BR>orpiment (गोरोचना).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांचिः|काञ्चि|कांचि|काञ्चिः
कांचिः, --ची f. [कांच् बंधने इनि]<BR>1 A<BR>woman's girdle or zone furnished<BR>with small tinkling bells or other<BR>ornaments; एतावता नन्वनुमेयशोभि<BR>कांचीगुणस्थानमनिंदितायाः Ku. 1. 37,<BR>3. 55; Me. 28; Śi. 9. 82; R. 6. 43.<BR>--2<BR>N. of an ancient city in the south of<BR>India, regarded as one of the sacred<BR>cities of the Hindus; (for the names<BR>of the seven cities, see अवंति).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरी, नगरी the same as कांची (2).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-b" target="_blank">Page0392-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--पदं the hips and loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांची|काञ्ची
कांचिः, --ची f. [कांच् बंधने इनि]<BR>1 A<BR>woman's girdle or zone furnished<BR>with small tinkling bells or other<BR>ornaments; एतावता नन्वनुमेयशोभि<BR>कांचीगुणस्थानमनिंदितायाः Ku. 1. 37,<BR>3. 55; Me. 28; Śi. 9. 82; R. 6. 43.<BR>--2<BR>N. of an ancient city in the south of<BR>India, regarded as one of the sacred<BR>cities of the Hindus; (for the names<BR>of the seven cities, see अवंति).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरी, नगरी the same as कांची (2).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-b" target="_blank">Page0392-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--पदं the hips and loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांचिकं|काञ्चिक|काञ्चिकं
कांचिकं Sour gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0392-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

