कीनाश|कीनाशः
कीनाश a. [Uṇ. 5. 36]<BR>1<BR>Cultivating the soil.<BR>--2 Poor, indigent.<BR>--3 Niggardly.<BR>--4 Small, little.<BR>--शः<BR>1 An epithet of Yama, the god of<BR>death; विधेहि कीनाशनिकेतनातिथिं<BR>Śi. 1. 73.<BR>--2 A kind of monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीरः|कीर|कीरं
कीरः A parrot;<BR>एवंकीरवरेमनोरथमयं पीयूषमास्वादयति Bv. 1. 58;<BR>N. 3. 12.<BR>--राः (pl.) The country and<BR>the people of Kāshmīra.<BR>--रं Flesh.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इष्टः the mango tree (liked<BR>by parrots).<BR>--वर्णकं a kind of<BR>perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीरकः|कीरक
