कीर्ण|कीर्णः|कीर्ण्ण
कीर्ण p. p. [कॄ-क्त]<BR>1 Strewn,<BR>spread, cast, scattered.<BR>--2 Covered,<BR>filled.<BR>--3 Placed, put.<BR>--4 Injured,<BR>hurt.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्त्मन् a. strewing the<BR>way; Ś. 1. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्णिः|कीर्णि|कीर्ण्णि
कीर्णिः f. [कॄ-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Scattering.<BR>--2 Covering, hiding, concealing.<BR>--3<BR>Injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तनं|कीर्तन|कीर्त्तन|कीर्त्तनं
कीर्तनं [कॄत्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Telling,<BR>narrating.<BR>--2 Praising, celebrating.<BR>--3<BR>A temple; any work of art, a building;<BR>न कीर्तनैरलंकृता मेदिनी K. 280; 119.<BR>--ना<BR>1 Narration, recital.<BR>--2<BR>Fame, glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तय्
कीर्तय् = कॄत् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तिः|कीर्ति|कीर्त्ति|कीर्त्तिः
कीर्तिः f. [कॄत्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Fame,<BR>renown, glory; इह कीर्तिमवाप्नेति<BR>Ms. 2. 9; वंशस्य कर्तारमनंतकीर्ति R. 2. 64;<BR>Me. 45.<BR>--2 Favour, approbation.<BR>--3 Dirt, mud.<BR>--4 Extension,<BR>expansion.<BR>--5 Light, lustre, splendour.<BR>--6<BR>Sound.<BR>--7 Mention, speech, report.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भाज् a. famous,<BR>celebrated, renowned. (--m.) an epithet<BR>of Droṇa, the military<BR>preceptor of the Kauravas and<BR>Pāṇḍavas.<BR>--शेषः survival or remaining<BR>behind only in fame, leaving<BR>nothing behind but fame: i. e. death;<BR>cf. नामशेष, आलेख्यशेष; सरसीव<BR>कीर्तिशेषं गतवति भुवि विक्रमादित्ये Vās.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीर्तित|कीर्त्तित|कीर्त्तितः
कीर्तित p. p.<BR>1 Said, asserted.<BR>--2<BR>Mentioned, told.<BR>--3 Known;<BR>notorious.<BR>--4 Praised, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कील्
कील् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bind.<BR>--2 To pin.<BR>--3 To stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलः|कील
कीलः [कील्-घञ्]<BR>1 A wedge, a<BR>pin; कीलोत्पाटीव वानरः Pt. 1. 21.<BR>--2 A lance.<BR>--3 A post, pillar.<BR>--4 A<BR>weapon.<BR>--5 The elbow.<BR>--6 A blow<BR>with the elbow.<BR>--7 A flame.<BR>--8 A<BR>minute particle.<BR>--9 N. of Śiva.<BR>--10<BR>A gnomon.<BR>--11 A position of the<BR>fœtus just before the time of<BR>delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलकः|कीलक
कीलकः<BR>1 A wedge or pin.<BR>--2 A<BR>fence.<BR>--3 A pillar, column; see कील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलिका
कीलिका The pin of an axle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलित|कीलितः
कीलित a.<BR>1 Tied, bound.<BR>--2<BR>Fixed, nailed, pinned down; तेन मम<BR>हृदयमिदमसमशरकीलितं Gīt. 7; सा<BR>नश्चेतसि कीलितेव Māl. 5. 10.<BR>--3 Staked,<BR>impaled.<BR>--4 Pierced, transfixed.<BR>--5<BR>Set (as a stake or pole).<BR>--तं A tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीलालः|कीलाल|कीलालं
कीलालः<BR>1 A heavenly drink<BR>similar to Amṛta, beverage of the<BR>gods.<BR>--2 Honey.<BR>--3 A beast.<BR>--कं<BR>1<BR>Blood.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं flesh.<BR>--धिः the ocean.<BR>--पः a demon,<BR>goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कीशः|कीश
कीशः a. Naked.<BR>--शः<BR>1 An ape,<BR>monkey.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--3 A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुः|कु
कुः f.<BR>1 The earth.<BR>--2 The base<BR>of a triangle or any plane figure.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुत्रः Mars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु ind. A prefix implying ‘badness’,<BR>‘deterioration,’ ‘depreciation’, ‘sin,’<BR>‘reproach,’ ‘littleness,’ ‘want,’<BR>‘deficiency’ &c. Its various substitutes are<BR>कद्(कदश्व), कव(कवोष्ण), का(कोष्ण),<BR>किं (किंप्रभुः); cf. Pt. 5. 17.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. a bad deed, a mean act.<BR>--ग्रहः an unpropitious planet.<BR>--ग्रामः<BR>a petty village or hamlet (without a<BR>king's officer, an agnihotrin, a<BR>physician, or a river).<BR>--चेल a.<BR>wearing bad or ragged garments.<BR>--चर्या<BR>wickedness, evil conduct,<BR>impropriety.<BR>--जन्मन् a. low-born.<BR>--तनु a.<BR>deformed, ugly.<BR>--(नुः) an epithet of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--तंत्री a bad lute.<BR>--तर्कः {1} sophistical or fallacious<BR>argument. {2} a heterodox doctrine,<BR>freethinking; कुतर्केष्वभ्यासः<BR>सततपरपैशुन्यमननम् G. L. 31. ˚पथः a<BR>sophistical mode of arguing.<BR>--तीर्थं a bad<BR>teacher.<BR>--दिनं an evil or<BR>unpropitious day.<BR>--दृष्टिः f. {1} weak sight.<BR>{2} an evil eye, sinister eye (fig.).<BR>{3} an opinion or doctrine opposed<BR>to the Vedas, heterodox doctrines;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-a" target="_blank">Page0406-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Ms. 12. 95.<BR>--देशः {1} a bad place or<BR>country. {2} a country where the<BR>necessaries of life are not available<BR>or which is subject to oppression.<BR>--देह a. ugly, deformed.<BR>--(हः) an<BR>epithet of Kubera.<BR>--धी a. {1} foolish, silly,<BR>stupid. {2} wicked.<BR>--नटः {1} a bad<BR>actor {2} a sort of trumpet flower.<BR>{3} red arsenic.<BR>--नदिका a small<BR>river, rill; सुपूरा स्यात्कुनदिका<BR>Pt. 1. 25.<BR>--नाथः a bad master.<BR>--नामन् m.<BR>a miser.<BR>--पथः {1} a wrong road, bad<BR>way (fig. also). {2} a heterodox<BR>doctrine.<BR>--पथ्य a. unwholesome,<BR>improper.<BR>--परीक्षक a. examining<BR>badly, not valuing rightly; Bh. 2. 15.<BR>--पुत्रः a bad or wicked son.<BR>--पुरुषः a low or wicked man.<BR>--पूय a.<BR>low, vile, contemptible.<BR>--प्रिय a.<BR>disagreeable, contemptible, low,<BR>mean.<BR>--प्लवः a bad boat; कुप्लवैः<BR>संतरन् जलम् Ms. 9. 161.<BR>--ब्रह्मः, --ब्रह्मन्<BR>m. a bad or degraded Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--मंत्रः {1} bad advice. {2} a charm used<BR>to secure success in a bad cause.<BR>--योगः an inauspicious conjunction<BR>(of planets).<BR>--योगिन् m. a false<BR>devotee, impostor.<BR>--रस a.<BR>having bad juice or flavour.<BR>--(सः)<BR>a kind of spirituous liquor.<BR>--रूप a. ugly, deformed;<BR>Pt. 5. 19.<BR>--रूप्यं tin.<BR>--वंगः lead.<BR>--वचस्, --वाक्य a. abusive, bad,<BR>scurrilous; using abusive, or foul<BR>language. (--n.) abuse, bad language.<BR>--वज्रकं crystal; a stone resembling<BR>a diamond.<BR>--वर्षः a sudden or<BR>violent shower.<BR>--विवाहः a degraded or<BR>improper form of marriage;<BR>Ms. 3. 63.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. bad behaviour.<BR>--वैद्यः a bad physician, quack.<BR>--शील a. rude, wicked, unmannerly,<BR>illtempered<BR>--ष्ठलं a bad place.<BR>--सरित्<BR>f. a small river, rill; उच्छिद्यंते क्रियाः<BR>सर्वा ग्रीष्मे कुसरितो यथा Pt. 2. 85.<BR>--सृतिः f. {1} evil conduct,<BR>wickedness. {2} conjuring, magic. {3}<BR>roguery.<BR>--स्त्री a bad woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0405-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कु|कुः
कु {vI.v} {c1c} P. (कवते) To sound. {vII.v}<BR>{c6c} A. (कुवते)<BR>1 To moan, groan.<BR>--2<BR>To cry. {vIII.v} {c2c} P. (कौति) To hum,<BR>coo (as a bee).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंश्
कुंश्(स्) {c1c} {c10c} P.<BR>1 To shine.<BR>--2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंस्
कुंश्(स्) {c1c} {c10c} P.<BR>1 To shine.<BR>--2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्
कुक् {c1c} A. (कोकते) To take, accept,<BR>seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकभं|कुकभ
कुकभं A kind of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकीलः|कुकील
कुकीलः A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुदः|कुकुद
कुकु(कू)दः One who gives away<BR>a girl in marriage with suitable<BR>decorations and in accordance with<BR>prescribed ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूदः|कुकूद
कुकु(कू)दः One who gives away<BR>a girl in marriage with suitable<BR>decorations and in accordance with<BR>prescribed ceremonies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुंदरः|कुकुन्दर|कुकुंदर|कुकुन्दरं|कुकुन्दरः
कुकुंद(दु)रः The cavity of<BR>the loins just above the hips (<BR>जघनकूप); see ककुंदर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुंदुरः|कुकुन्दुर|कुकुंदुर|कुकुन्दुरः
कुकुंद(दु)रः The cavity of<BR>the loins just above the hips (<BR>जघनकूप); see ककुंदर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकुराः
कुकुराः (pl.)<BR>1 N. of a country;<BR>also called दशार्ह.<BR>--2 N. of a people, a<BR>tribe of the Yādavas; Śi. 6. 15,<BR>13. 6, 16. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूलः|कुकूल|कुकूलं
कुकूलः, --लं<BR>1 Chaff; कुकूलानां<BR>राशौ तदनु हृदयं पच्यत इव U. 6. 38.<BR>--2<BR>A fire made of chaff.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A hole,<BR>ditch (filled with stakes).<BR>--2 An<BR>armour, mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुकूलं|कुकूल|कुकूलः
कुकूलः, --लं<BR>1 Chaff; कुकूलानां<BR>राशौ तदनु हृदयं पच्यत इव U. 6. 38.<BR>--2<BR>A fire made of chaff.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A hole,<BR>ditch (filled with stakes).<BR>--2 An<BR>armour, mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटः|कुक्कुट
कुक्कुटः<BR>1 A cock, wild cock.<BR>--2<BR>A whisp of lighted straw, a<BR>firebrand.<BR>--3 A spark of fire.<BR>--टी<BR>1 A<BR>hen.<BR>--2 A small house-lizard.<BR>--3<BR>The silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटकः|कुक्कुटक
कुक्कुटकः<BR>1 A cock, wild cock.<BR>--2<BR>A man of a mixed caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटिः|कुक्कुटि
कुक्कुटिः, --टी f. Hypocrisy,<BR>interested observance of religious rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुटी
कुक्कुटिः, --टी f. Hypocrisy,<BR>interested observance of religious rites.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुभः|कुक्कुभ
कुक्कुभः<BR>1 A wild cock.<BR>--2 A<BR>cock in general.<BR>--3 Varnish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्कुरः|कुक्कुर|कुक्कुरं
कुक्कुरः (री f.) [Uṇ. 1. 41] A<BR>dog; यस्यैतच्च न कुक्कुरैरहरर्जंघांतरं<BR>चर्व्यते Mk. 2. 11.<BR>--रं A vegetable<BR>perfume.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वाच् m. a species<BR>of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षः|कुक्ष
कुक्षः The belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिः|कुक्षि
कुक्षिः<BR>1 The belly (in general);<BR>जिह्मिताध्मातकुंक्षिः (भुजगपतिः)<BR>Mk. 9. 12.<BR>--2 The womb, the part<BR>of the belly containing the fœtus;<BR>कुंभीनस्याश्च कुक्षिजः R. 15. 15;<BR>Śi. 13. 40.<BR>--3 The interior of anything:<BR>R. 10. 65 (where the word is used<BR>in sense 2 also).<BR>--4 A cavity in<BR>general.<BR>--5 A cavern, cave;<BR>R. 2. 38, 67.<BR>--6 The sheath of a sword.<BR>--7 N. of Bali.<BR>--8 A bay, gulf.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शूलः belly-ache, colic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुक्षिंभरि|कुक्षिम्भरि|कुक्षिम्भरिः
कुक्षिंभरि a.<BR>1 ‘Caring to feed his<BR>own belly’, selfish, gluttonous,<BR>voracious.<BR>--2 Filling or pervading<BR>the interior; Ku. 15. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंकुमं|कुङ्कुम|कुंकुम|कुङ्कुमं
कुंकुमं<BR>1 Saffron; लग्नकुंकुमकेसरान्<BR>(स्कंधान्); R. 4. 67; Rs. 4. 2; 5. 9;<BR>Bh. 1. 10, 25.<BR>--2 Saffron paint;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-c" target="_blank">Page0406-c+ 55</a>]<BR>Māl. 1. 37.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद्रिः N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुच्
कुच् {vI.v} {c6c} P. (कुचति, कुचित)<BR>1 To<BR>utter a shrill cry (as a bird).<BR>--2 To<BR>go.<BR>--3 To polish.<BR>--4 To contract,<BR>bend.<BR>--5 To be contracted.<BR>--6 To stop,<BR>impede.<BR>--7 To write or delineate.<BR>--8<BR>To mix, connect. {vII.v} {c1c} P., कुंच्<BR>also (कोचति, कुंचति, कुंचित)<BR>1 To<BR>make crooked, bend or curve.<BR>--2 To<BR>move or go crookedly.<BR>--3 To make<BR>small, lessen.<BR>--4 To shrink,<BR>contract.<BR>--5 To go to or towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचः|कुच
कुचः [कुच्-क] The female breast,<BR>a teat, nipple; अपि<BR>वनांतरमल्पकुचांतरा V. 4. 26.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रं, --मुखं<BR>a nipple.<BR>--तटं, --तटी the slope of<BR>the female breast, the breast, (तट<BR>being स्वार्थे or meaningless).<BR>--फलः<BR>the pomegranate tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0406-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुचित
