कुठाकुः|कुठाकु
कुठाकुः A bird, the wood-pecker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठाटंकः|कुठाटङ्क|कुठाटङ्कः
कुठाटंकः, --का An axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठाटंका
कुठाटंकः, --का An axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारः|कुठार
कुठारः --री<BR>1 An axe, or hatchet;<BR>मातुः केवलमेव यौवनवनच्छेदे कुठारा वयं<BR>Bh. 3. 11.<BR>--2 A sort of hoe or spade.<BR>--रः A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारी
कुठारः --री<BR>1 An axe, or hatchet;<BR>मातुः केवलमेव यौवनवनच्छेदे कुठारा वयं<BR>Bh. 3. 11.<BR>--2 A sort of hoe or spade.<BR>--रः A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारकः|कुठारक
कुठारकः A small axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारिकः|कुठारिक
कुठारिकः A wood-cutter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारिका
कुठारिका A small axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठारुः|कुठारु
कुठारुः<BR>1 A tree.<BR>--2 An ape, a<BR>monkey.<BR>--3 An armourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठिः|कुठि
कुठिः<BR>1 A tree.<BR>--2 mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेरः|कुठेर
कुठेरः Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुठेरुः|कुठेरु
कुठेरुः The wind produced by a<BR>fan or chowri.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्
कुड् {c6c} P. (कुडति) To play or<BR>act as a child, trifle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडंगः|कुडङ्ग|कुडंग|कुडङ्गः
कुडंगः A bower, an arbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडवः|कुडव
कुडवः<BR>--(पः) A measure of grain<BR>equal to (1/4) of a Prastha and<BR>containing 12 handfuls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडिः|कुडि
कुडिः The body; cf. Uṇ. 4. 143.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडिका
कुडिका An earthen or wooden<BR>water-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडी
कुडी A hut; cf. कुटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुडुपः|कुडुप
कुडुपः The clasp of a necklace or<BR>bracelet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्मल|कुड्मलः
कुड्मल a. [Uṇ. 1. 106] Opening,<BR>full-blown, expanding, (as the<BR>blossom of a flower); R. 18. 37.<BR>--लः<BR>An opening bud; विजृंभणोद्गंधिषु<BR>कुड्मलेषु R. 16. 47; U. 6. 17; Śi. 2. 7.<BR>--लं A particular hell; Ms. 4. 89;<BR>Y. 3. 222.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्मलित
कुड्मलित a.<BR>1 Budded, blossomed.<BR>--2 Cheerful, smiling.<BR>--3<BR>Half-closed; Māl. 9. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुड्यं|कुड्य
कुड्यं<BR>1 A wall; भेदे कुड्यावपातने<BR>Y. 2. 223; Śi. 3. 45.<BR>--2 Plastering<BR>(a wall).<BR>--3 Eagerness, curiosity.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">Page0408-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--छेदिन् m. a house-breaker,<BR>a thief.<BR>--छेद्यः a digger.<BR>--(द्यं) a<BR>ditch, pit, breach or opening (in a<BR>wall).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुण्
कुण् {vI.v} {c6c} P. (कुणति, कुणित)<BR>1 To<BR>support, aid.<BR>--2 To sound. {vII.v} {c10c} P. (<BR>कणयति)<BR>1 To counsel, advise.<BR>--2 To<BR>converse or speak with.<BR>--3 To<BR>invite.<BR>--4 To salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणकः|कुणक
कुणकः A young animal just born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणप|कुणपः
कुणप a. (पी f.) [cf. Uṇ. 3. 143]<BR>Smelling like a dead body, stinking.<BR>--पः, --पं A dead body, corpse;<BR>शासनीयः कुणपभोजनः V. 5. (a vulture);<BR>अमेध्यकुणपाशी च Ms. 12. 71; often<BR>used as a term of contempt with<BR>living beings.<BR>--पः<BR>1 A spear.<BR>--2 A foul<BR>smell, stench.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणारु
कुणारु a. Ved. Crying out, (<BR>क्विणनशील); Rv. 3. 30. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुणिः|कुणि
कुणिः<BR>1 A cripple with a withered<BR>or crooked arm.<BR>--2 A whitlow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंटक|कुण्टक|कुण्टकः
कुंटक a. (की f.) Fat, corpulent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंठ्|कुण्ठ्
कुंठ् {c1c} P. (कुंठति, कुंठित)<BR>1 To be<BR>blunted or dulled.<BR>--2 To be lame or<BR>mutilated.<BR>--3 To be dull or stupid,<BR>be idle.<BR>--4 To loosen. --Caus. or<BR>{c10c} P. To hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंठ|कुण्ठ|कुण्ठः
कुंठ a.<BR>1 Blunt, dulled; वज्रं<BR>तपोवीर्यमहत्सु कुंठं Ku. 3. 12 has no effect on<BR>&c.; कुंठत्वमायाति गुणः कवीनां<BR>साहित्यविद्याश्रमवर्जितेषु Vikr. 1. 14;<BR>Śi. 12. 12; कुंठीभवंत्युपलादिषु क्षुराः Ś. B.<BR>--2<BR>Dull, foolish, stupid.<BR>--3 Indolent,<BR>lazy.<BR>--4 Weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंठकः|कुण्ठक|कुंठक|कुण्ठकः
कुंठकः A fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंठित|कुण्ठित|कुण्ठितः
कुंठित p. p.<BR>1 Blunted, dulled;<BR>(fig. also); बिभ्रतोऽस्त्रमचलेप्यकुंठितं<BR>R. 11. 74; Bv. 2. 78; Ku. 2. 20;<BR>शास्त्रेष्वकुंठिता बुद्धिः R. 1. 19 not<BR>hampered or impeded.<BR>--2 Stupid.<BR>--3<BR>Mutilated.<BR>--4 Grasped, held.<BR>--5<BR>Encircled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंड्|कुण्ड्
कुंड् {vI.v} {c1c} A.<BR>1 To burn.<BR>--2 To<BR>eat.<BR>--3 To heap. {vII.v} {c1c} P. To maim<BR>or mutilate. {vIII.v} {c10c} U. To protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडः|कुण्ड|कुंड|कुंडं|कुण्डं|कुण्डः
कुंडः, --डी, --डं [cf. Uṇ. 1. 112]<BR>1 A<BR>bowl-shaped vessel, a basin, bowl.<BR>--2 A round hole in the ground for<BR>receiving and preserving water.<BR>--3<BR>A hole in general; अग्निकुंडं.<BR>--4 A<BR>pool, well; especially one consecrated<BR>to some deity or holy<BR>purpose.<BR>--5 The bowl of a<BR>mendicant.<BR>--डः (डा f.) A son born<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">Page0408-c+ 55</a>]<BR>in adultery, the son of a woman by<BR>a man other than her husband while<BR>the husband is alive; पत्यौ जीवति<BR>कुंडः स्यात् Ms. 3. 174; Y. 1. 222.<BR>--डा An epithet of Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशिन् m. a pander, pimp, one<BR>who depends for his livelihood on a<BR>कुंड i. e. a bastard, or adulterine;<BR>Ms. 3. 158; Y. 1. 224.<BR>--ऊधस् (<BR>कुंडोध्नी) {1} a cow with a full udder. {2}<BR>a woman with a full bosom.<BR>--कीटः<BR>{1} a keeper of concubines. {2} a<BR>follower of the Cārvāka doctrine, an<BR>atheist. {3} a Brāhmaṇa born in<BR>adultery.<BR>--कीलः a low or vile man.<BR>--गोलं, --गोलकं {1} gruel. {2} a group<BR>of कुंड and गोलक (taken together).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडी
कुंडः, --डी, --डं [cf. Uṇ. 1. 112]<BR>1 A<BR>bowl-shaped vessel, a basin, bowl.<BR>--2 A round hole in the ground for<BR>receiving and preserving water.<BR>--3<BR>A hole in general; अग्निकुंडं.<BR>--4 A<BR>pool, well; especially one consecrated<BR>to some deity or holy<BR>purpose.<BR>--5 The bowl of a<BR>mendicant.<BR>--डः (डा f.) A son born<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">Page0408-c+ 55</a>]<BR>in adultery, the son of a woman by<BR>a man other than her husband while<BR>the husband is alive; पत्यौ जीवति<BR>कुंडः स्यात् Ms. 3. 174; Y. 1. 222.<BR>--डा An epithet of Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशिन् m. a pander, pimp, one<BR>who depends for his livelihood on a<BR>कुंड i. e. a bastard, or adulterine;<BR>Ms. 3. 158; Y. 1. 224.<BR>--ऊधस् (<BR>कुंडोध्नी) {1} a cow with a full udder. {2}<BR>a woman with a full bosom.<BR>--कीटः<BR>{1} a keeper of concubines. {2} a<BR>follower of the Cārvāka doctrine, an<BR>atheist. {3} a Brāhmaṇa born in<BR>adultery.<BR>--कीलः a low or vile man.<BR>--गोलं, --गोलकं {1} gruel. {2} a group<BR>of कुंड and गोलक (taken together).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडं|कुण्ड|कुंड|कुण्डं|कुंडः|कुण्डः
कुंडः, --डी, --डं [cf. Uṇ. 1. 112]<BR>1 A<BR>bowl-shaped vessel, a basin, bowl.<BR>--2 A round hole in the ground for<BR>receiving and preserving water.<BR>--3<BR>A hole in general; अग्निकुंडं.<BR>--4 A<BR>pool, well; especially one consecrated<BR>to some deity or holy<BR>purpose.<BR>--5 The bowl of a<BR>mendicant.<BR>--डः (डा f.) A son born<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">Page0408-c+ 55</a>]<BR>in adultery, the son of a woman by<BR>a man other than her husband while<BR>the husband is alive; पत्यौ जीवति<BR>कुंडः स्यात् Ms. 3. 174; Y. 1. 222.<BR>--डा An epithet of Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशिन् m. a pander, pimp, one<BR>who depends for his livelihood on a<BR>कुंड i. e. a bastard, or adulterine;<BR>Ms. 3. 158; Y. 1. 224.<BR>--ऊधस् (<BR>कुंडोध्नी) {1} a cow with a full udder. {2}<BR>a woman with a full bosom.<BR>--कीटः<BR>{1} a keeper of concubines. {2} a<BR>follower of the Cārvāka doctrine, an<BR>atheist. {3} a Brāhmaṇa born in<BR>adultery.<BR>--कीलः a low or vile man.<BR>--गोलं, --गोलकं {1} gruel. {2} a group<BR>of कुंड and गोलक (taken together).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडलः|कुण्डल|कुंडल|कुंडलं|कुण्डलं|कुण्डलः
कुंडलः, --लं [कुंड-मत्वर्थे ल]<BR>1 An<BR>ear-ring; श्रोत्रं श्रुतेनैव न कुंडलेन<BR>Bh. 2. 71; Ch. P. 11; Rs. 2. 20, 3. 19;<BR>R. 11. 15.<BR>--2 A bracelet.<BR>--3 The<BR>coil of a rope.<BR>--4 A fetter, tie, collar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडलं|कुण्डल|कुंडल|कुण्डलं|कुंडलः|कुण्डलः
कुंडलः, --लं [कुंड-मत्वर्थे ल]<BR>1 An<BR>ear-ring; श्रोत्रं श्रुतेनैव न कुंडलेन<BR>Bh. 2. 71; Ch. P. 11; Rs. 2. 20, 3. 19;<BR>R. 11. 15.<BR>--2 A bracelet.<BR>--3 The<BR>coil of a rope.<BR>--4 A fetter, tie, collar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडलना|कुण्डलना
कुंडलना Encireling (as a word) to<BR>denote that it is to be left out or not<BR>considered; तदोजसस्तद्यशसः<BR>स्थिताविमौ वृथेति चित्ते कुरुते यदा यदा । तनोति<BR>भानोः परिवेषकैतवात्तदा विधिः कुंडलनां<BR>विधोरपि ॥ N. 1. 14; cf. {2} 95 also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडलिन्|कुण्डलिन्
कुंडलिन् (नी f.)<BR>1 Decorated with<BR>ear-rings.<BR>--2 Circular, spiral.<BR>--3<BR>Winding, coiling (as a serpent). --m.<BR>1 A snake.<BR>--2 A peacock.<BR>--3 An<BR>epithet of Varuṇa, and of Śiva.<BR>--4 The<BR>spotted or painted deer.<BR>--नी A form<BR>of Durgā or Śakti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडलीकृत|कुण्डलीकृत
कुंडलीकृत a. Forming a ring, coiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडिका|कुण्डिका
कुंडिका<BR>1 A pitcher.<BR>--2 A<BR>student's water-pot (कमंडलु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडिन्|कुण्डिन्
कुंडिन् m.<BR>1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--2 A bastard.<BR>--3 A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडिनं|कुण्डिन|कुंडिन|कुण्डिनं|कुण्डिनः
कुंडिनं N. of a city, the capital of<BR>the Vidarbhas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडिर
कुंडि(डी)र a. Strong.<BR>--रः A<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंडीर|कुण्डीर|कुण्डीरः
कुंडि(डी)र a. Strong.<BR>--रः A<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतपः|कुतप
कुतपः<BR>1 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--2 A<BR>twiceborn man (द्विजन्मन्).<BR>--3 The sun.<BR>--4 Fire.<BR>--5 A guest.<BR>--6 An ox, a<BR>bull.<BR>--7 A daughter's son.<BR>--8 A<BR>sister's son.<BR>--9 Grain.<BR>--10 The eighth<BR>Muhūrta of the day; अह्नो मुहूर्ता<BR>विख्याता दश पंच च सर्वदा । तत्राष्टमो मुहूर्तो<BR>यः स कालः कुतपः स्मृतः ॥<BR>--11 A<BR>musical instrument.<BR>--12 A time suitable<BR>for the performance of sacrifices to<BR>the manes.<BR>--पं The Kuśa grass<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0408-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्
कुतस् ind.<BR>1 From where,<BR>whence; कस्य त्वं वा कुत आयातः Moha<BR>M. 3.<BR>--2 Where, where else, in<BR>what (other) place &c.; ईदृग्विनोदः कुतः<BR>Ś. 2. 5.<BR>--3 Why, wherefore, from<BR>what cause or motive; कुत इदमुच्यते<BR>Ś. 5.<BR>--4 How, in what manner;<BR>स्फुरति च बाहुः कुतः फलमिहास्य<BR>Ś. 1. 15.<BR>--5 Much more, much less; न<BR>त्वत्समोस्त्यभ्यधिकः कुतोऽन्यः<BR>Bg. 11. 43, 4. 31; न मे स्तेनो जनपदे न<BR>कदर्यो… .न स्वैरी स्वैरिणी कुतः Ch. Up.<BR>--6 Because, for; Ś. 1. कुतस् is<BR>sometimes used merely for the abl.<BR>of किम्; कुतः कालात्समुत्पन्नं V. P.<BR>(= कस्मात् कालात् &c.). कुतः becomes<BR>indefinite when connected with the<BR>particles चिद्, चन, or अपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतस्त्य
कुतस्त्य a.<BR>1 Whence come;<BR>U. 3. 7.<BR>--2 How happened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुकं|कुतुक
कुतुकं<BR>1 Desire, inclination.<BR>--2<BR>Curiosity (= कौतुकं).<BR>--3 Eagerness,<BR>ardour, vehemence;<BR>केलिकलाकुतुकेन च काचिदमुं यमुनाजलकूले ।<BR>मंजुलवंजुलकुंजगतं विचकर्ष करेण दुकूले Gīt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतुपः|कुतुप|कुतुपं
कुतुपः, कुतूः f. A small leathern<BR>bottle for oil.<BR>--पः<BR>1 The eighth<BR>Muhūrta of the day.<BR>--2 = कुतप 12 q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूः
कुतुपः, कुतूः f. A small leathern<BR>bottle for oil.<BR>--पः<BR>1 The eighth<BR>Muhūrta of the day.<BR>--2 = कुतप 12 q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहल|कुतूहलं|कुतूहलः
कुतूहल a.<BR>1 Wonderful.<BR>--2<BR>Excellent, best.<BR>--3 Praised, celebrated.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Desire, curiosity;<BR>उज्झितशब्देन जनितं नः कुतूहलं Ś. 1; यदि<BR>विलासकलासु कुतूहलं Gīt. 1; (पपौ)<BR>कुतूहलेनेव मनुष्यशोणितम् R. 3. 54; 13. 21;<BR>15. 65.<BR>--2 Eagerness.<BR>--3 What excites<BR>curiosity, anything pleasing or<BR>interesting, a curiosity.<BR>--4 Delight,<BR>pleasure; U. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुतूहलिन्
कुतूहलिन् a.<BR>1 Desirous, struck<BR>with curiosity; Māl. 1.<BR>--2 Eager,<BR>impatient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्र
कुत्र ind.<BR>1 Where, in which place;<BR>कुत्र मे शिशुः Pt. 1; प्रवृत्तिः कुत्र<BR>कर्तव्या H. 1.<BR>--2 In which case; तेजसा<BR>सह जातानां वयः कुत्रोपयुज्यते Pt. 1. 328.<BR>(कुत्र is sometimes used for the loc. sing.<BR>of किम्). When connected with the<BR>particles चिद्, चन or अपि, कुत्र<BR>becomes indefinite in sense. कुत्रापि,<BR>--कुत्रचित् somewhere, anywhere;<BR>न कुत्रापि no where; कुत्रचित्-कुत्रचित्<BR>in one place-in another place,<BR>herehere; Ms. 9. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्रत्य
कुत्रत्य a. Where living or<BR>residing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्स्
कुत्स् {c10c} A. (कुत्सयते, कुत्सित) To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-b" target="_blank">Page0409-b+ 55</a>]<BR>abuse, revile, censure, condemn;<BR>Ms. 2. 54; Y. 1. 31; Śānti. 2. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सनं|कुत्सन
कुत्सनं, कुत्सा Abuse, contempt,<BR>reproach, abusive language;<BR>देवतानां च कुत्सनं Ms. 4. 163.<BR>--ना<BR>Expression of contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सा
कुत्सनं, कुत्सा Abuse, contempt,<BR>reproach, abusive language;<BR>देवतानां च कुत्सनं Ms. 4. 163.<BR>--ना<BR>Expression of contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुत्सित|कुत्सितं|कुत्सितः
कुत्सित p. p.<BR>1 Despised,<BR>contemptible.<BR>--2 Low, mean, vile.<BR>--तं<BR>Censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथ्
कुथ् {c4c} P. (कुथ्यति, कुथित) To<BR>stink, become putrid, or foul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथः|कुथ|कुथं
कुथः The Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0409-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुथः|कुथ|कुथं
