कोस(श)ला The city of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोहल|कोहलः
कोहल a. [कौ हलति स्पर्धते अच् पृषो˚<BR>Tv.] Speaking indistinctly.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A kind of musical instrument.<BR>--2 A sort of spirituous liquor.<BR>--3<BR>The inventor or first teacher of<BR>the drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौकृत्यं|कौकृत्य
कौकृत्यं<BR>1 Evil doing, wickedness.<BR>--2 Repentance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्कुट
कौक्कुट a. [कुक्कुट-अण्] Relating to<BR>a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्कुटिकः|कौक्कुटिक
कौक्कुटिकः [कुक्कुट-ठक्]<BR>1 A<BR>poulterer.<BR>--2 A mendicant who walks always<BR>fixing his eyes on the ground<BR>for fear of treading upon worms,<BR>insects &c.<BR>--3 (Hence) A<BR>hypocrite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्ष
कौक्ष a. (क्षी f.)<BR>1 Tied to, or<BR>being on, the sides.<BR>--2 Abdominal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्षेय
कौक्षेय (यी f.) [कुक्षि-ठञ्]<BR>1<BR>Being in the belly.<BR>--2 Being in a<BR>sheath; असिं कौक्षेयमुद्यम्य<BR>चकारापनसं मखं Bk. 4. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौक्षेयकः|कौक्षेयक
कौक्षेयकः [कुक्षौ बद्धोऽसिः ढकञ्] A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">Page0427-b+ 55</a>]<BR>sword, scimitar; बामपार्श्वावलंबिना<BR>कौक्षेयकेण K. 8; Vikr. 1. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौंकः|कौङ्क|कौंक|कौङ्कः
कौंकः, कौंकणः (pl.) N. of a<BR>country and its people or rulers; (see<BR>कोंकण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौंकणः|कौङ्कण|कौंकण|कौङ्कणः
कौंकः, कौंकणः (pl.) N. of a<BR>country and its people or rulers; (see<BR>कोंकण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौंजर|कौञ्जर
कौंजर a. Belonging to an<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौट|कौटः
कौट a. (टी f.) [कूट-अञ्]<BR>1<BR>Living in one's own house; hence,<BR>independent, free.<BR>--2 Domestic, homely,<BR>homebred.<BR>--3 Fraudulent, dishonest.<BR>--4 Snared.<BR>--टः<BR>1 Fraud, falsehood.<BR>--2 Giving false evidence.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः the Kuṭaja tree.<BR>--तक्षः (opp.<BR>ग्रामतक्षः) an independent carpenter,<BR>one who works at home on his own<BR>account and not for the village.<BR>--साक्षिन् m. a false witness.<BR>--साक्ष्यं<BR>false evidence, perjury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटकिकः|कौटकिक
कौटकिकः, कौटिकः<BR>1 One whose<BR>business is to catch birds &c. in traps.<BR>--2 One who sells the flesh of birds,<BR>animals &c.; a butcher, poacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिकः|कौटिक
कौटकिकः, कौटिकः<BR>1 One whose<BR>business is to catch birds &c. in traps.<BR>--2 One who sells the flesh of birds,<BR>animals &c.; a butcher, poacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिक|कौटिकः
कौटिक a.<BR>1 Relating to a snare or<BR>trap.<BR>--2 Dishonest, fraudulent; see<BR>कौटकिक above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटभी
कौटभी An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटल्य|कौटल्यः
कौटल्य = कौटिल्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटवी
कौटवी A naked woman; cf. कोट्टबी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिलिकः|कौटिलिक
कौटिलिकः<BR>1 A hunter.<BR>--2 A<BR>blacksmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटिल्यं|कौटिल्य|कौटिल्यः
कौटिल्यं<BR>1 Crookedness(lit. and<BR>fig.).<BR>--2 Wickedness<BR>--3 Dishonesty,<BR>fraud; Pt. 2. 185.<BR>--ल्यः ‘The<BR>crooked’, N. of Cāṇakya. a<BR>celebrated writer on civil polity, (the work<BR>being known as चाणक्यनीति), the<BR>friend and adviser of Candragupta<BR>and a very important character in<BR>the Mudrārākṣasa; कौटिल्यः<BR>कुटिलमतिः स एष येन क्रोधाग्नौ प्रसभमदाहि<BR>नंदवंशः Mu. 1. 7; स्पृशति मां भृत्यभावेन<BR>कौटिल्यशिष्यः Mu. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटीर
कौटीर a. Belonging to the plant<BR>कुटीर or made of it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटीर्या
कौटीर्या An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटुंब|कौटुम्ब
कौटुंब a. (बी f.) [कुटुंबं तद्भरणं<BR>प्रयोजनमस्य अण्] Necessary for the<BR>family or household.<BR>--बं Family<BR>relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौटुंबिक|कौटुम्बिक|कौटुम्बिकः
कौटुंबिक a. (की f.) [कुटुंबे तद्भरणे<BR>प्रसृतः ठक्] Constituting a family.<BR>--कः The father or master of a<BR>family; paterfamilias.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौणपः|कौणप
कौणपः A goblin, demon;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">Page0427-c+ 55</a>]<BR>Māl. 5.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंतः an epithet of<BR>Bhīshma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौण्यं|कौण्य
कौण्यं Distortion or paralysis of<BR>the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकं|कौतुक
कौतुकं [कुतुकस्य भावः अण्]<BR>1<BR>Desire, curiosity, wish.<BR>--2 Eagerness,<BR>vehemence, impatience.<BR>--3<BR>Anything creating curiosity or wonder.<BR>--4 The marriage thread (worn on<BR>the wrist); करोयमामुक्तविवाहकौतुकः<BR>Ku. 5. 66; R. 8. 1.<BR>--5 The ceremony<BR>with the marriage thread preceding<BR>a marriage.<BR>--6 Festivity, gaiety.<BR>--7<BR>Particularly, auspicious festivity,<BR>solemn occasion (such as marriage);<BR>प्रस्थान˚ Ś. 4; Ku. 7. 25.<BR>--8 Delight,<BR>joy, pleasure, happiness;<BR>Bh. 3. 140; ˚रसाः U. 6. 33; Māl. 10. 3;<BR>U. 3. 37.<BR>--9 Sport, pastime.<BR>--10 A<BR>song, dance, show or spectacle.<BR>--11 Joke, mirth.<BR>--12 Friendly<BR>greeting, salutation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अगारः, --रं, --गृहं a pleasure-house;<BR>कौतुकागारमागात् Ku. 7. 94.<BR>--क्रिया,<BR>--मंगलं {1} a solemn ceremony. {2}<BR>particularly, marriage ceremony;<BR>R. 11. 53;<BR>--तोरणः, --णं a triumphal arch<BR>erected on festive occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकित
कौतुकित a. Eager, eagerly<BR>interested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतुकिन्
कौतुकिन् a. Festive, gay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतूहलं|कौतूहल
कौतूहलं(ल्यं) [कुतूहल-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Desire, curiosity, interest;<BR>विषयव्यावृत्तकौतूहलः V. 1. 9; Ś. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Eagerness, vehement or eager desire.<BR>--3<BR>Anything exciting curiosity, a<BR>wonder, curiosity.<BR>--4 A solemn<BR>ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौतूहल्यं|कौतूहल्य
कौतूहलं(ल्यं) [कुतूहल-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Desire, curiosity, interest;<BR>विषयव्यावृत्तकौतूहलः V. 1. 9; Ś. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Eagerness, vehement or eager desire.<BR>--3<BR>Anything exciting curiosity, a<BR>wonder, curiosity.<BR>--4 A solemn<BR>ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौत्सं|कौत्स|कौत्सः
कौत्सं A Sāman composed by<BR>Kutsa.<BR>--त्सः<BR>1 N. of a pupil of<BR>Varatantu; R. 5. 1.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>degraded family.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौदालिकः|कौदालिक
कौदालिकः A man of a mixed<BR>caste, a fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौद्रविकं|कौद्रविक
कौद्रविकं Sochal salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौनख्यं|कौनख्य
कौनख्यं Ugliness of nails.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौंतिकः|कौन्तिक|कौंतिक|कौन्तिकः
कौंतिकः [कुंतः प्रहरणमस्य ठञ्] A<BR>spearman, lancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौंतेयः|कौन्तेय|कौंतेय|कौन्तेयः
कौंतेयः [कुंत्याः अपत्यं ढक्] ‘Son of<BR>Kuntī’, an epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira,<BR>Bhīma or Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौप|कौपं
कौप a. (पी f.) [कूप-अण्]<BR>Relating to or coming from a well (as<BR>water).<BR>--पं Well-water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपीनं|कौपीन
कौपीनं [कूप-खञ्; see Sk. on<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-a" target="_blank">Page0428-a+ 56</a>]<BR>P. V. 2. 20]<BR>1 The pudenda.<BR>--2 A<BR>privity, privy part.<BR>--3 A small<BR>piece of cloth (usually a small<BR>strip) worn over the privities;<BR>कौपीनं शतखंडजर्जरतरं कंथा पुनस्तादृशी<BR>Bh. 3. 101.<BR>--4 (Hence sometimes)<BR>A ragged or tattered garment.<BR>--5<BR>Sin, an improper or wrong act;<BR>Pt. 3. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0427-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौपोदकी
कौपोदकी The mace of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौब्ज्यं|कौब्ज्य
कौब्ज्यं [कुब्ज-ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Crookedness.<BR>--2 Hump-backedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमार|कौमारं
कौमार a. (री f.) [कुमार-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Juvenile, youthful, virgin, maidenly<BR>(of men and women); कौमारः पतिः,<BR>कौमारी भार्या.<BR>--2 Soft, tender.<BR>--3<BR>Belonging to the god of war;<BR>Māl. 1. 1.<BR>--री<BR>1 The wife of one who<BR>has not married another wife.<BR>--2<BR>The Śakti (power) of Kārtikeya.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Childhood (to the age of<BR>five).<BR>--2 Maidenhood (to the age<BR>of sixteen), virginity; पिता रक्षति<BR>कौमरे भर्ता रक्षति यौबने Ms. 9. 3;<BR>देहिनोऽस्मिन् यथा देहे कौमारं योवनं जरा<BR>Bg. 2. 13.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बंधकी a<BR>harlot; Māl. 7.<BR>--भृत्यं the rearing<BR>and general treatment of children.<BR>--राज्यं the position of an<BR>heirapparent.<BR>--हर a. marrying or<BR>gaining a woman as a girl; यः कौमारहरः<BR>स एव हि वरः K. P. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारकं|कौमारक
कौमारकं Boyhood, juvenile or<BR>tender age; कौमारकेऽपि गिरिवद्गुरुतां दधानः<BR>U. 6. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारिकः|कौमारिक
कौमारिकः A father of girls.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमारिकेयः|कौमारिकेय
कौमारिकेयः [कुमारिकाया अपत्यं ढक्]<BR>The son of an unmarried woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदः|कौमुद
कौमुदः The month Kārtika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमुदी
कौमुदी [कुमुदस्येयं प्रकाशकत्वात् अण्<BR>ङीष् Tv.]<BR>1 Moonlight; शशिना सह याति<BR>कौमुदी Ku. 4. 33; शशिनमुपगतेयं<BR>कौमुदी मेघमुक्तं R. 6. 85; (the word<BR>is thus popularly derived:--कौ मोदंते<BR>जना यस्यां तेनासौ कौमुदी मता).<BR>--2<BR>Anything serving as moonlight, i. e.<BR>causing delight and balmy coolness;<BR>त्वमस्य लोकस्य च नेत्रकौमुदी Ku. 5. 71;<BR>या कौमुदी नयनयोर्भवतः सुजन्मा<BR>Māl. 1. 34; cf. चंद्रिका.<BR>--3 The full moon<BR>day in Kārtika.<BR>--4 The full moon<BR>day in Āśvina.<BR>--5 Festivity (in<BR>general).<BR>--6 Particularly, a festive<BR>day on which temples, houses &c.<BR>are illuminated.<BR>--7 (At the end of<BR>titles of works &c.) Elucidation,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">Page0428-b+ 55</a>]<BR>throwing light on the subject<BR>treated; e. g. तर्ककौमुदी, सांख्यतत्त्वकै मुदी,<BR>सिद्धांतकौमुदी &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चारः<BR>the day of full moon in the month<BR>Āśvina.<BR>--पतिः the moon.<BR>--मुखं<BR>appearance of moonlight; R. 3. 1.<BR>--वृक्षः the stick or stand of a lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमोदकी
कौमोदकी, कौमोदी N. of the<BR>mace of Viṣṇu, कौमोदकी मोदयति स्म<BR>चेतः Śi. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौमोदी
कौमोदकी, कौमोदी N. of the<BR>mace of Viṣṇu, कौमोदकी मोदयति स्म<BR>चेतः Śi. 3. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव|कौरवः
कौरव a. (वी f.) [कुरोरपत्यं,<BR>तद्देशस्य राजा तेषु भवो वा, कुरु-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Relating to the Kurus; क्षेत्रं क्षत्रप्रधानपिशुनं<BR>कौरवं तद्भजेथाः Me. 48.<BR>--वः A<BR>descendant of Kuru; मथ्नामि कौरवशतं<BR>समरे न कोपात् Ve. 1. 15; Chāṇ. 50.<BR>--2<BR>A ruler of the Kurus. (so कौरवक,<BR>कौरवायणि and कौरवेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौरव्यः|कौरव्य
कौरव्यः [कुरु-ण्य]<BR>1 A descendant<BR>of Kuru; कौरव्यवंशदावेऽस्मिन् क एष<BR>शलभायते Ve. 1. 19, 25; कौरव्ये<BR>कृतहस्तता पुनरियं देवे यथा सीरिणि 6. 12.<BR>--2<BR>A ruler of the Kurus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्प्यः|कौर्प्य
कौर्प्यः The zodiacal sign Scorpio<BR>(a word derived from Greek).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौर्म|कौर्मः|कौर्म्म
कौर्म a. [कूर्म-अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to<BR>a tortoise.<BR>--2 Belonging to the<BR>Avatāra of Viṣṇu as a tortoise; (˚पुराण).<BR>--र्मः N. of a Kalpa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल|कौलः
कौल a. (ली f.) [कुले भवः अण्<BR>cf. P. IV. 2. 96]<BR>1 Relating to a<BR>family, ancestral, hereditary.<BR>--2<BR>Of a noble family, well-born.<BR>--लः<BR>A worshipper of शक्ति according<BR>to the left hand ritual.<BR>--लं The<BR>doctrine and practices of the left<BR>hand Śāktas (for a short description<BR>of कौलधर्म see Karpūr. 1, speech of<BR>भैरवानंद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलकेय|कौलकेयः
कौलकेय a. Sprung from a noble<BR>family, of a good family.<BR>--यः The<BR>son of an unchaste woman, a bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटिनेयः|कौलटिनेय
कौलटिनेयः [कुलटायाः अपत्यं<BR>P. IV. 1. 127]<BR>1 The son of a (chaste)<BR>female beggar.<BR>--2 A bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेयः|कौलटेय
कौलटेयः<BR>1 The son of a female<BR>beggar (chaste or unchaste).<BR>--2<BR>A bastard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलटेरः|कौलटेर
कौलटेरः<BR>1 A bastard, son or<BR>daughter of a disloyal wife.<BR>--2 The<BR>child of a beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलालक
कौलालक a. Made by, or<BR>pertaining to, a potter.<BR>--कं<BR>Earthenware, porcelain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलिक|कौलिकः
कौलिक a. (की f.) [कुलादागतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">Page0428-c+ 55</a>]<BR>ठक्]<BR>1 Belonging to a family.<BR>--2<BR>Customary in a family, ancestral.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A weaver; कौलिको विष्णुरूपेण<BR>राजकन्यां निषेवते Pt. 1. 202.<BR>--2 An<BR>impostor, a heretic.<BR>--3 A follower of<BR>the left hand Śākta ritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीन|कौलीनं|कौलीनः
कौलीन a. [कौ पृथिव्यां लीनः अलुक्स˚;<BR>कुलादागतः खञ् वा] Belonging to a<BR>noble family.<BR>--नः<BR>1 The son of a<BR>female beggar.<BR>--2 A follower of<BR>the left hand Śākta ritual.<BR>--नं<BR>1 An evil report, a scandal;<BR>मालविकागतं किमपि कौलीनं श्रूयते M. 3;<BR>तदेव कौलीनमिव प्रतिभाति V. 2;<BR>Me. 112; कौलीनमात्माश्रयमाचचक्षे<BR>R. 14. 36, 84.<BR>--2 An improper act, bad or<BR>scandalous conduct; ख्याते तस्मिन्<BR>वितमसि कुले जन्म कौलीनमेतत्<BR>Ve. 2. 10.<BR>--3 A combat of animals.<BR>--4<BR>Cock-fighting.<BR>--5 War, battle (in<BR>general).<BR>--6 High birth.<BR>--7 A<BR>privity, the pudenda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलीन्यं|कौलीन्य
कौलीन्यं<BR>1 High birth; Pt. 1. 116.<BR>--2 Family scandal.<BR>--3 Family<BR>honor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलूतः|कौलूत
कौलूतः A king of the Kulūtas;<BR>कौलूतश्चित्रवर्मा Mu. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौलेयक|कौलेयकः
कौलेयक [कुल-ढकञ्] a.<BR>1 Of a<BR>noble family.<BR>--2 Pertaining to a<BR>family.<BR>--कः A dog, hound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौल्य|कौल्यः
कौल्य a.<BR>1 Noble-born, of a high<BR>birth.<BR>--2 Of the left hand Śākta<BR>sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौवेर|कौवेरं
कौवे(बे)र a. (री f.) [कुवेरस्येदं<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to or coming<BR>from Kubera; यानं सस्मार कौबेरं<BR>R. 15. 45.<BR>--री The north (the<BR>direction presided over by Kubera);<BR>ततः प्रतस्थे कौवेरीं भास्वानिव रघुर्दिशं<BR>R. 4. 66.<BR>--2 The Śakti or female<BR>energy of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौबेर
कौवे(बे)र a. (री f.) [कुवेरस्येदं<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to or coming<BR>from Kubera; यानं सस्मार कौबेरं<BR>R. 15. 45.<BR>--री The north (the<BR>direction presided over by Kubera);<BR>ततः प्रतस्थे कौवेरीं भास्वानिव रघुर्दिशं<BR>R. 4. 66.<BR>--2 The Śakti or female<BR>energy of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौश|कौशं
कौश a. (शी f.) [कुश-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Silken.<BR>--2 Made of Kuśa grass.<BR>--शं An epithet of Kānyakubja.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलं|कौशल
कौशलं(ल्यं) [कुशल-अण् ष्यञ्<BR>वा]<BR>1 Well-being, welfare,<BR>happiness, prosperity.<BR>--2 Skill,<BR>skilfulness, cleverness;<BR>किमकौशलादुत प्रयोजनापोक्षितया Mu. 3; हावहारि<BR>हसितं वचनानां कौशलं दृशि<BR>विकारबिशेषाः Śi. 10. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्यं|कौशल्य
कौशलं(ल्यं) [कुशल-अण् ष्यञ्<BR>वा]<BR>1 Well-being, welfare,<BR>happiness, prosperity.<BR>--2 Skill,<BR>skilfulness, cleverness;<BR>किमकौशलादुत प्रयोजनापोक्षितया Mu. 3; हावहारि<BR>हसितं वचनानां कौशलं दृशि<BR>विकारबिशेषाः Śi. 10. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलिकं|कौशलिक
कौशलिकं A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलिका
कौशलिका, कौशली<BR>1 A present,<BR>an offering.<BR>--2 Friendly inquiry<BR>after one's health &c., greeting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशली
कौशलिका, कौशली<BR>1 A present,<BR>an offering.<BR>--2 Friendly inquiry<BR>after one's health &c., greeting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0428-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशलेयः|कौशलेय
कौशलेयः [कौशल्याया अपत्यं ठक्<BR>यलोपः] An epithet of Rāma, son of<BR>Kauśalyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्या
कौशल्या [कोशलदेशे भवा छय] The<BR>eldest wife of Daśaratha and mother<BR>of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशल्यायनिः|कौशल्यायनि
कौशल्यायनिः [कौशल्याया अपत्यं फिञ्]<BR>Rāma, son of Kauśalyā;<BR>Bk. 7. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशांबी|कौशाम्बी
कौशांबी [कुशांबेन निर्वृत्ता अण्] N.<BR>of an ancient city on the Ganges<BR>in the lower part of the Doab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिक|कौशिकः
कौशिक a. (की f.) [कुश-ठञ्,<BR>कुशिक-अण् वा]<BR>1 Incased, sheathed.<BR>--2 Coming from an owl.<BR>--3 Born<BR>of the family of Kuśika.<BR>--4 Silken.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An epithet of विश्वामित्र q. v.<BR>--2 An owl; U. 2. 29.<BR>--3 A<BR>lexicographer.<BR>--4 Marrow.<BR>--5 Bdellium.<BR>--6 An ichneumon.<BR>--7 A<BR>snakecatcher.<BR>--8 The sentiment of love<BR>(शृंगार).<BR>--9 One who knows<BR>hidden treasures.<BR>--10 An epithet of<BR>Indra; N. 5. 64.<BR>--11 An epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--का A cup, drinking<BR>vessel.<BR>--की<BR>1 N. of a river in<BR>Behār.<BR>--2 N. of the goddess Durgā.<BR>--3 N. of one of the four varieties<BR>of dramatic style; सुकुमारार्थसंदर्भा<BR>कौशिकी तासु कथ्यते; see S. D. 411<BR>et seq. also.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरातिः,<BR>--अरिः a crow.<BR>--आत्मजः an epithet<BR>of Arjuna.<BR>--आयुधं rainbow.<BR>--फलः<BR>the cocoa-nut tree.<BR>--प्रियः an<BR>epithet of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीधान्यं|कौशीधान्य
कौशीधान्यं A leguminous plant,<BR>pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशीलवं|कौशीलव
कौशीलवं The profession of an<BR>actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशेय|कौशेयं
कौशे(षे)य a. [कोशादुत्थितं ढक्]<BR>Silk, silken.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Silk;<BR>Pt. 1. 94.<BR>--2 A silken cloth in general;<BR>Ms. 5. 120.<BR>--3 A woman's lower<BR>garment of silk; निर्नाभि<BR>कौशेयमुपात्तबाणमभ्यंगनेपथ्यमलंचकार Ku. 7. 7;<BR>विद्युद्गणकौशेयः Mk. 5. 3; Rs. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौषेय|कौषेयं
कौशे(षे)य a. [कोशादुत्थितं ढक्]<BR>Silk, silken.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Silk;<BR>Pt. 1. 94.<BR>--2 A silken cloth in general;<BR>Ms. 5. 120.<BR>--3 A woman's lower<BR>garment of silk; निर्नाभि<BR>कौशेयमुपात्तबाणमभ्यंगनेपथ्यमलंचकार Ku. 7. 7;<BR>विद्युद्गणकौशेयः Mk. 5. 3; Rs. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसल्य|कौसल्यं|कौसल्यः
कौसल्य a. Belonging to the<BR>people of the Kosalas.<BR>--ल्यः A<BR>prince of the Kosalas.<BR>--ल्या The<BR>wife of Daśaratha and mother of<BR>Rāma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नंदनः, --मातृ m.<BR>epithets of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद
कौसीद a.<BR>1 Connected with a<BR>loan.<BR>--2 Usurious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसीद्यं|कौसीद्य
कौसीद्यं [कुसीद-ष्यञ्]<BR>1 The<BR>practice of usury.<BR>--2 Sloth, indolence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुम|कौसुमं
कौसुम a. [कुसुम-अण्] Flowery,<BR>flowering.<BR>--मं<BR>1 The ashes of brass<BR>(used as a collyrium).<BR>--2 Pollen<BR>of flowers (पराग); Śi. 7. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसुंभ|कौसुम्भ|कौसुम्भः
कौसुंभ a. [कुसुंभ-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Prepared with safflower.<BR>--2 Dyed with<BR>safflower, red.<BR>--मः Wild safflower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौसृतिकः|कौसृतिक
कौसृतिकः [कुसृत्या चरति ठक्]<BR>1<BR>A cheat, knave.<BR>--2 A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौस्तुभः|कौस्तुभ
कौस्तुभः [कुस्तुभो जलधिस्तत्र भवः<BR>अण्]<BR>1 N. of a celebrated gem<BR>obtained with 13 other jewels at the<BR>churning of the ocean and worn by<BR>Viṣṇu on his breast; सकौस्तुभं<BR>ह्रेप यतीव कृष्णं R. 6. 49; 10. 10.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of oil.<BR>--3 A manner of<BR>joining the fingers.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--लक्षणः,<BR>--वक्षस् m.<BR>--हृदयः epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नथ्
क्नथ् {c1c} {c10c} P. To hurt, injure,<BR>kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नस्
क्नस् {c4c} {c10c} P.<BR>1 To be crooked.<BR>--2 To speak.<BR>--3 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्नूय्
क्नूय् {c1c} A. (क्नूयते)<BR>1 To make a<BR>creaking sound.<BR>--2 To sink.<BR>--3 To<BR>be wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकचः|क्रकच
क्रकचः A saw; U. 4. 3.<BR>--चा<BR>The Ketaka tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--छदः<BR>the Ketaka tree.<BR>--पत्रः the teak<BR>tree.<BR>--पाद् m.,<BR>--पादः a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रकरः|क्रकर
क्रकरः<BR>1 A kind of partridge.<BR>--2 A saw.<BR>--3 A poor man.<BR>--4 A<BR>disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रतुः|क्रतु
क्रतुः [कृ-कतु Uṇ. 1. 77]<BR>1 A<BR>sacrifice; क्रतोरशेषेण फलेन युज्यतां<BR>R. 3. 65; शतं क्रतूनामपविघ्नमाप सः<BR>3. 38; M. 1. 4; Ms. 7. 79.<BR>--2 An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 One of the ten<BR>Prajāpatis; M. 1. 35.<BR>--4 Intelligence,<BR>talent.<BR>--5 Power, ability.<BR>--6 Plan,<BR>design, purpose.<BR>--7 Resolution,<BR>determination.<BR>--8 Desire, will.<BR>--9<BR>Fitness, adequacy, efficiency.<BR>--10<BR>Deliberation, consultation.<BR>--11 Inspiration.<BR>--12 Enlightenment.<BR>--13 Offering,<BR>worship.<BR>--14 An Aśvamedha<BR>sacrifice (these senses are mostly Vedic).<BR>--15 The month Āṣāḍha.<BR>--16<BR>Excess of fondness or liking.<BR>--17 An<BR>organ. [cf. Gr. kratos; Zend<BR>khratu].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्तमः the<BR>राजसूय sacrifice.<BR>--कर्मन् n. a sacrificial<BR>ceremony.<BR>--द्रुह्, --द्विष् m. a demon,<BR>goblin.<BR>--ध्वंसिन् m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva (who destroyed Dakṣa's<BR>sacrifice.)<BR>--पतिः the performer of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">Page0429-c+ 55</a>]<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--पशुः a sacrificial horse.<BR>--पुरुषः<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--भुज् m. a<BR>god, deity.<BR>--राज् m. {1} the lord of<BR>sacrifices; यथाश्वमेधः क्रतुराट्<BR>Ms. 9. 260. {2} the राजसूय sacrifice.<BR>--राजः<BR>the राजसूय sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथ्
क्रथ् {c1c} P. (क्रथति, क्रथित) To<BR>injure, hurt, kill (with gen. of person).<BR>--{c10c} U. To delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथनं|क्रथन
क्रथनं<BR>1 A slaughter.<BR>--2 Cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रथकैशिकः|क्रथकैशिक
क्रथकैशिकः^1 (pl.) N. of a<BR>country; अथेश्वरेण क्रथकैशिकानां R. 5. 39;<BR>M. 5. 2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रंद्|क्रन्द्
क्रंद् {c1c} P. (क्रंदति, चक्रंद, अक्रंदीत्,<BR>क्रंदित)<BR>1 To cry, weep, shed tears; किं<BR>क्रंदसि दुराक्रंद स्वपक्षक्षयकारक<BR>Pt. 4. 29; क्रंदत्यतः करुणमप्सरसां गणोऽयं<BR>V. 1. 3; चक्रंद विग्ना कुररीव भूयः R. 14. 68;<BR>15. 42; Bk. 3. 28, 5. 5.<BR>--2 To call<BR>out to, call out piteously to any<BR>one, (with acc.); क्रंदत्यविरतं सोऽथ<BR>भ्रातृमातृसुतानथ Mārk. P.<BR>--3 To cry<BR>out, exclaim.<BR>--4 To yell, howl.<BR>--5<BR>To neigh (as a horse).<BR>--6 To roar.<BR>--7<BR>To creak (as a wheel). --{c10c} P. or<BR>Caus.<BR>1 To cry out continuously.<BR>--2<BR>To roar, rave.<BR>--3 To cause to weep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रंदः|क्रन्द|क्रन्दः
क्रंदः Ved.<BR>1 Neighing.<BR>--2 A cry,<BR>calling out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रंदनः|क्रन्दन|क्रंदन|क्रन्दनं|क्रन्दनः
क्रंदनः [क्रंद् भावे ल्युट्] A cat.<BR>--नं<BR>1 A cry of distress or weeping,<BR>lamentation.<BR>--2 Mutual defiance.<BR>--3 Calling, inviting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रंदस्|क्रन्दस्
क्रंदस् n. Ved. Battle-cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रंदित|क्रन्दित|क्रन्दितं
क्रंदित a. [क्रंद्-क्त] Wept, called<BR>or cried out.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Cry of distress<BR>or weeping, lamentation; हा तातेति<BR>क्रंदितमाकर्ण्य विषण्णः R. 9. 75.<BR>--2<BR>Mutual defiance, challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रप्
क्रप् {c1c} A. (क्रपते)<BR>1 To pity.<BR>--2<BR>To mourn.<BR>--3 To lament.<BR>--4 To<BR>go.<BR>--5 To long for, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रम्
क्रम् {c1c} U., {c4c} P. (क्रामति, क्रमते,<BR>क्राम्यति, चक्राम, चक्रमे, अक्रमीत्, अक्रंस्त, क्रांत)<BR>1 To walk, step, go; क्रामत्यनुदिते<BR>सूर्ये वाली व्यपगतक्लमः Rām.; गम्यमानं<BR>न तेनासीदगतं क्रामता पुरः Bk. 8. 2;<BR>25.<BR>--2 To go to, approach (with acc).;<BR>देवा इमान् लोकानक्रमंत Śat. Br.<BR>--3<BR>To pass or go over, go across,<BR>traverse; U. 2. 13; सुखं<BR>योजनपंचाशत्क्रमेयं Rām.<BR>--4 To leap, jump; क्रमं बबंध<BR>क्रमितुं सकोपः (हरिः) Bk. 2. 9. 5. 51.<BR>--5 To go up, ascend; क्रामत्युच्चैर्भूभृतो<BR>यस्य तेजः Śi. 16. 83.<BR>--6 (a) To cover,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-a" target="_blank">Page0430-a+ 57</a>]<BR>occupy, take possession of, fill;<BR>क्रांता यथा चेतसि विरमयेन R. 14. 17.<BR>(b) To reach up to, pervade,<BR>penetrate; क्रामद्भिर्घनपदवीमनेकसंख्यैः<BR>Ki. 5. 34.<BR>--7 To surpass, excel;<BR>स्थितः सर्वोन्नतेनोर्वीं क्रांत्वा मेरुरिवात्मना<BR>R. 1. 14.<BR>--8 To undertake, strive<BR>after, be able or competent for, show<BR>energy for (with dat. or inf.);<BR>व्याकरणाध्ययनाय क्रमते Sk. धर्माय<BR>क्रमते साधुः Vop.;<BR>व्युत्पत्तिरावर्जितकोविदापि न रंजनाय क्रमते जडानां<BR>Vikr. 1. 16; हत्वा रक्षांसि लवितुमक्रमीन्मारुतिः<BR>पुनः । अशोकवनिकामेव Bk. 9. 23.<BR>--9 To<BR>be developed or increased to have<BR>full scope, be at home (with loc.);<BR>कृत्येषु क्रमंते Dk. 170; क्रमंतेऽ<BR>स्मिञ्शास्त्राणि, or ऋक्षु क्रमते बुद्धिः Sk.;<BR>क्रममाणोऽरिसंसदि Bk. 8. 22.<BR>--10 To<BR>succeed, have effect (Atm.); न<BR>चक्रमस्याक्रमताधिकं धरं Śi. 1. 54.<BR>--11 To be<BR>repeated (as a letter or word in the<BR>arrangement called क्रम q. v.).<BR>--12 To<BR>fulfil, accomplish.<BR>--13 To have<BR>sexual intercourse with. (By<BR>P. I. 3. 38 क्रम् by itself is used in the<BR>Atm. in the sense of ‘continuity’ or<BR>‘want of interruption,’ ‘energy or<BR>application’, and ‘development or<BR>increase’, and also ‘conquering or<BR>getting over’). --Caus. (क्रमयति, क्रामयति)<BR>1 To cause to go &c.<BR>--2 To repeat a<BR>letter (as in the क्रम arrangement).<BR>--Desid. चिक्रमिषति, चिक्रंसते &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0429-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमः|क्रम
क्रमः [क्रम्-भावकरणादौ घञ्]<BR>1 A step,<BR>pace; त्रिविक्रमः; सागरः प्लवगेंद्रेण<BR>क्रमेणैकेन लंघितः Mb.; Śi. 12. 18.<BR>--2 A<BR>foot.<BR>--3 Going, proceeding, course;<BR>कालक्रमेण; क्रमात् or क्रमेण in course<BR>of, gradually; कालक्रमेण gradually,<BR>in course of time; भाग्यक्रमः course<BR>or turn of fate; R. 3. 7, 30, 32.<BR>--4 Performance, commencement;<BR>इत्थमत्र विततक्रमे क्रतौ Śi. 14. 53.<BR>--5 (a) Regular course, order, series,<BR>succession; निमित्तनैमित्तकयोरयं क्रमः<BR>Ś. 7. 30; Ms. 7. 24, 9. 85, 2. 173,<BR>3. 69. (b) Traditional order, U. 6. (c)<BR>Order of propriety; Ku. 5. 32.<BR>--6<BR>Method, manner; नेत्रत्रमेणोपरुरोध<BR>सूर्यं R. 7. 39.<BR>--7 Grasp, hold;<BR>क्रमगता पशोः कन्यका Māl. 3. 18.<BR>--8 A<BR>position of attack (assumed by an<BR>animal before making a spring);<BR>न मया क्रमः सज्जीकृत आसीत् Pt. 4.<BR>--9<BR>Preparation, readiness; Bk. 2. 9.<BR>--10 An undertaking, enterprize.<BR>--11<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">Page0430-b+ 57</a>]<BR>An act or deed, manner of<BR>proceeding; कोप्येष कांतः क्रमः Amaru. 43,<BR>33.<BR>--12 Particular manner of<BR>reciting Vedic texts, leaving at each<BR>time one word and taking up another.<BR>--13 Power, strength.<BR>--14 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुसारः, अन्वयः<BR>regular order, due arrangement.<BR>--आगत, --आयात a. descended or<BR>inherited lineally, hereditary; Pt. 1. 73,<BR>84, 3. 167.<BR>--उद्वेगः an ox.<BR>--ज्या<BR>the sine of a planet, declination.<BR>--पाठः the Krama reading.<BR>--भंगः<BR>irregularity.<BR>--योगः succession, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमक|क्रमकः
क्रमक a.<BR>1 Orderly, methodical.<BR>--2 Going, proceeding.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>student who goes through a regular<BR>course of study.<BR>--2 One who knows<BR>the Krama arrangement of a text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमणः|क्रमण
क्रमणः [क्रामत्यनेन करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>The foot.<BR>--2 A horse.<BR>--णं<BR>1 A step.<BR>--2 Walking.<BR>--3 Proceeding.<BR>--4<BR>Transgressing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमतः
क्रमतः ind. Gradually, successively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमशः
क्रमशः ind.<BR>1 In due order,<BR>regularly, successively, seriatim.<BR>--2<BR>Gradually, by degrees; R. 12. 47;<BR>Ms. 1. 68, 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमिक
क्रमिक a. [क्रमादागतः ठन्]<BR>1<BR>Successive, serial.<BR>--2 Descended lineally,<BR>ancestral, hereditary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमुः|क्रमु
क्रमुः, क्रमुकः [क्रम्-उन्, संज्ञायां कन्]<BR>The betel-nut tree; आस्वादितार्द्रक्रमुकः<BR>समुद्रात् Śi. 3. 81; Vikr. 18. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमुकः|क्रमुक
क्रमुः, क्रमुकः [क्रम्-उन्, संज्ञायां कन्]<BR>The betel-nut tree; आस्वादितार्द्रक्रमुकः<BR>समुद्रात् Śi. 3. 81; Vikr. 18. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमेलः|क्रमेल
क्रमेलः, --क्रमेलकः A camel; निरीक्षते<BR>केलिवनं प्रविश्य क्रमेलकः कंटकजालमेव<BR>Vikr. 1. 29; Śi. 12. 18; N. 6. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रमेलकः|क्रमेलक
क्रमेलः, --क्रमेलकः A camel; निरीक्षते<BR>केलिवनं प्रविश्य क्रमेलकः कंटकजालमेव<BR>Vikr. 1. 29; Śi. 12. 18; N. 6. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रांत|क्रान्त|क्रान्तः
क्रांत p. p. Gone, passed over,<BR>traversed &c.; (p. p. of क्रम् q. v.).<BR>--तः<BR>1 A horse.<BR>--2 A foot, step.<BR>--3<BR>Declination.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Going, passing.<BR>--2<BR>A step.<BR>--3 A certain aspect in<BR>astronomy (when the moon is in<BR>conjunction with a planet).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दर्शिन् a. omniscient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रांतिः|क्रान्ति|क्रांति|क्रान्तिः
क्रांतिः f.<BR>1 Going, proceeding.<BR>--2<BR>A step, pace.<BR>--3 Surpassing.<BR>--4<BR>Attacking, overcoming.<BR>--5 Declination<BR>of a planet.<BR>--6 The ecliptic.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कक्षः, --मंडलं, --वृत्तं the ecliptic.<BR>--क्षेत्रं a figure described by the<BR>ecliptic.<BR>--ज्या the sine of the<BR>declination or of the ecliptic.<BR>--पातः the<BR>equinoctial points or nodes of the<BR>ecliptic.<BR>--भागः the declination of a<BR>point of the ecliptic.<BR>--वलयः {1} the<BR>ecliptic. {2} the tropical zone, space<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">Page0430-c+ 54</a>]<BR>within the tropics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रांतुः|क्रान्तु|क्रान्तुः
क्रांतुः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रवण
क्रवण a. Ved. Worshipping,<BR>praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रविस्
क्रविस् n. Ved. Raw flesh,<BR>carrion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रव्यं|क्रव्य
क्रव्यं Raw flesh, carrion,<BR>स्थपुटगतमपि क्रव्यमव्यग्रमत्ति Māl. 5. 16. [cf.<BR>Gr. kreas; L. caro]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद्,<BR>अद्, --भुज् a. eating raw flesh;<BR>Ms. 5. 131. (--m.) {1} a carnivorous animal,<BR>such as a tiger &c.; U. 1. 49. {2} a<BR>demon, goblin; R. 15. 16.<BR>--घातनः<BR>a deer (killed for its flesh.)<BR>--वाहनः<BR>Ved. an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रशयति
क्रशयति Den. P. To emaciate,<BR>make thin or lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रशित
क्रशित a. Made lean, emaciated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रशिमन्
क्रशिमन् m. Thinness, emaciation,<BR>leanness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्राकचिकः|क्राकचिक
क्राकचिकः A sawyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्राथः|क्राथ
क्राथः Killing, murder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिमिः|क्रिमि
क्रिमिः<BR>1 A worm.<BR>--2 An insect.<BR>see कृमि.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं aloewood.<BR>--शैलः an ant-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियः|क्रिय
क्रियः The sign of the Zodiac<BR>called Aries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिया
क्रिया [कृ भावे करणादौ वा श]<BR>1<BR>Doing, execution, performance,<BR>accomplishment; उपचार˚, धर्म˚; प्रत्युक्तं हि<BR>प्रणयिषु सताभीप्सितार्थक्रियैव Me. 114.<BR>--2 An action, act, business,<BR>undertaking; प्रणयिक्रिया V. 4. 15;<BR>Ms. 2. 4.<BR>--3 Activity, bodily action,<BR>labour.<BR>--4 Teaching, instruction;<BR>क्रिया हि वस्तूपहिता प्रसीदति R. 3. 29.<BR>--5 Possession of some art (as of<BR>singing, dancing &c.), knowledge;<BR>शिष्टा क्रिया कस्याचिदात्मसंस्था<BR>M. 1. 16.<BR>--6 Practice (opp. शास्त्र theory).<BR>--7 A literary work, composition;<BR>शृणुत मनोभिरवाहितैः क्रियामिमां<BR>कालिदासस्य V. 1. 2; कालिदासरय कियायां कथं<BR>परिषदो बहुमानः M. 1.<BR>--8 A<BR>purificatory rite, a religious rite or<BR>ceremony.<BR>--9 An expiatory rite,<BR>expiation.<BR>--10 (a) The ceremony of<BR>offering oblations to the deceased<BR>ancestors (श्राद्ध). (b) Obsequies.<BR>--11<BR>Worship.<BR>--12 Medical treatment,<BR>application of remedies, cure;<BR>शीतक्रिया M. 4 cold remedies.<BR>--13<BR>(In gram.) Action, the general idea<BR>expressed by a verb.<BR>--14 Motion<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-a" target="_blank">Page0431-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--15 Especially, motion as one of the<BR>seven categories of the Vaiśeṣikas;<BR>see कर्मन्.<BR>--16 (In law) Judicial<BR>investigation by human means<BR>(witnesses &c.) or by ordeals.<BR>--17 Burden of proof; क्रिया<BR>स्याद्वादिनोर्द्वयोः; द्वयोरपि वादिनोः क्रिया प्राप्नोति<BR>V. May.<BR>--18 A verb.<BR>--19 A noun of<BR>action.<BR>--20 Disquisition.<BR>--21 Study.<BR>--22 Means, expedients,<BR>--23<BR>Instrument, implement.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वित a.<BR>practising ritual observances.<BR>--अपवर्गः {1} completion or termination of<BR>an affair, execution of a task,<BR>क्रियापवर्गेष्वनुजीविसात् कृताः Ki. 1. 14.<BR>{2} liberation from ceremonial acts,<BR>absolution.<BR>--अभ्युपगमः a special<BR>agreement; क्रियाभ्युपगमात्त्वेतत् बीजार्थं<BR>यत्प्रदीयते Ms. 9. 53.<BR>--अवसन्न a. one<BR>who loses a law-suit through the<BR>statements of the witnesses &c.<BR>--इंद्रियं see कर्मेंद्रिय.<BR>--कलापः the<BR>whole body of ceremonies enjoined in<BR>the Hindu religious law. {2} all the<BR>particulars or points of any business.<BR>--कारः {1} an agent, worker. {2} a<BR>beginner, tyro, a fresh student. {3} an<BR>agreement.<BR>--द्वेषिन् m. a witness whose<BR>testimony is prejudicial to the cause<BR>(one of the five kinds of witnesses).<BR>--द्वैतं efficient cause.<BR>--निर्देशः<BR>evidence.<BR>--पटुं a. dexterous.<BR>--पथः<BR>mode of medical treatment.<BR>--पदं a<BR>verb.<BR>--पर a. diligent in the<BR>performance of one's duty.<BR>--पादः the<BR>third division of a legal plaint; that<BR>is, witnesses, documents and other<BR>proofs adduced by the plaintiff or<BR>complainant.<BR>--योगः {1} connection<BR>with the verb. {2} the employment<BR>of expedients or means. {3} active<BR>devotion.<BR>--लोपः omission or<BR>discontinuance of any of the essential<BR>ceremonies of the Hindu religion;<BR>क्रियालोपात् वृषलत्वं गताः Ms. 10. 43.<BR>--वशः necessary influence of acts<BR>done.<BR>--वाचक, --वाचिन् a.<BR>expressing any action, as a verbal noun.<BR>--वादिन् m. a plaintiff, complainant.<BR>--विधिः a rule of action, manner of<BR>any rite; Ms. 9. 220.<BR>--विशेषणं {1}<BR>an adverb. {2} a predicative<BR>adjective.<BR>--शक्तिः f. the power of god<BR>(in creating this world)<BR>--संक्रातिः<BR>f. imparting (to others) one's<BR>knowledge; teaching; M. 1. 19.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">Page0431-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--समभिहारः the repetition of any act<BR>Śi. 2. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0430-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रियावत्|क्रियावन्त्
क्रियावत् a.<BR>1 Engaged in any<BR>actual work, versed in the practice<BR>of a thing; यस्तु क्रियान्पुरुषः स विद्वान्<BR>H. 1. 167.<BR>--2 Performing ceremonies<BR>in the right manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रिवि|क्रिविः
क्रिवि a. Ved.<BR>1 Doing,<BR>performing.<BR>--2 Killing.<BR>--विः<BR>1 A cistern,<BR>well.<BR>--2 A leather bag; a cloud (?)<BR>--3 N. of the country of पांचाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्री
क्री {c9c} U. (क्रीणाति, क्रीणीते, क्रीत)<BR>1<BR>To buy, purchase; महता पुण्यपण्येन<BR>क्रीतेयं कायनौस्त्वया Śānti. 3. 1;<BR>क्रीणीष्व मज्जीवितमेव पण्यमन्यन्न चेदस्ति<BR>तदस्तु पुण्यं N. 3. 87, 88; क्रीणंति स्म<BR>प्राणमूल्यैर्यशांसि Śi. 18. 15;<BR>Pt. 1. 13; Ms. 9. 174.<BR>--2 To barter,<BR>exchange; कच्चित्सहस्रैर्मूर्खाणामेकं<BR>क्रीणासि पंडितं Mb.<BR>--3 To win. [cf. Pers.<BR>kharidan].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्री
क्री a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Buying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयः|क्रय
क्रयः [क्री भावे अच्] Buying,<BR>purchasing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आरोहः a market,<BR>fair<BR>--क्रीत a. bought.<BR>--लेख्यं a deed<BR>of sale, conveyance &c. (गृहं क्षेत्रादिकं<BR>क्रीत्वा तुल्यमूल्याक्षरान्वितं । पत्रं कारयते यत्तु<BR>क्रयलेख्यं तदुच्यते Bṛhaspati).<BR>--विक्रयौ<BR>(du.) trade, traffic, buying and<BR>selling; Ms. 8. 5; 7. 127.<BR>--विक्रयिकः a<BR>trader, merchant.<BR>--विक्रयिन् a.<BR>buying or selling, striking a bargain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयणं|क्रयण
क्रयणं [क्री भावे ल्युट्] Buying,<BR>purchasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रयिकः|क्रयिक
क्रयिकः [क्रय-ठन्]<BR>1 A trader,<BR>dealer.<BR>--2 A purchaser.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रय्य|क्रय्यं
क्रय्य a. [क्री-यत्] A thing<BR>exhibited for sale in the market; (opp. केय<BR>which only means ‘fit to be<BR>purchased’; cf. Sk. on P. VI. 1. 82).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रायकः|क्रायक
क्राय(यि)कः<BR>1 A purchaser.<BR>--2 A<BR>trader, merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रायिकः|क्रायिक
क्राय(यि)कः<BR>1 A purchaser.<BR>--2 A<BR>trader, merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीत|क्रीतः
क्रीत p. p. Bought; see क्री.<BR>--तः One<BR>of the twelve kinds of sons<BR>recognised in Hindu Law; a son purchased<BR>from his natural parents; क्रीतश्च<BR>ताभ्यां विक्रीतः Y. 2. 131.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुशयः ‘repenting a purchase’,<BR>rescission, returning a thing purchased to<BR>the seller (admissible in some cases<BR>by law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीतक|क्रीतकः
क्रीतक a. Got by purchase.<BR>--कः<BR>A son bought from his parents and<BR>adopted; Ms. 9. 174. cf. क्रीत above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेणिः|क्रेणि
क्रेणिः, --णी f. Buying, purchase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेणी
क्रेणिः, --णी f. Buying, purchase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेतृ
क्रेतृ m. A buyer, purchaser;<BR>Y. 2. 168.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रेय|क्रेयं
क्रेय a. Purchasable, fit to be<BR>bought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीड्
क्रीड् {c1c} P. (क्रीडति, क्रीडित)<BR>1 To<BR>play, amuse oneself; वानराः<BR>क्रीडितुमारब्धाः Pt. 1; एष क्रीडति<BR>कूपयंत्रघटिकान्यायप्रसक्तो विधिः Mk. 10. 59.<BR>--2 To gamble, play at dice; बहुविधं<BR>द्यूतं क्रीडतः Mk. 2; नाक्षैः<BR>क्रीडेत्कदाचिद्धि Ms. 4. 74; Y. 1. 138.<BR>--3 To<BR>jest, joke or trifle with;<BR>सद्वृत्तस्तनमंडलस्तव कथं प्राणैर्मम क्रीडति Gīt. 3;<BR>क्रीडिष्यामि तावदेनया V. 3;<BR>एवमाशाग्रहग्रस्तैः क्रीडंति धनिनोर्थिभिः<BR>H. 2. 23; Pt. 1. 187; Mk. 3. --WITH<BR>अनु (Atm.) to play, sport, amuse<BR>oneself; साध्वनुक्रीडमानानि पश्य<BR>वृंदानि पक्षिणां Bk. 8. 10.<BR>--आ, --परि,<BR>--सं (Atm.) to play &c.;<BR>संक्रीडंते मणिभिर्यत्र कन्याः Me. 67; but<BR>क्रीड् with सं is Paras. in the sense<BR>of ‘making a noise’; त्वन्नामवर्णा<BR>इव कर्णपीता मयास्य संक्रीडति चक्रचक्रे<BR>N. 3. 50; संक्रीडंति शकटानि Mbh. ‘the<BR>carts creak.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीड|क्रीडः
क्रीड a [क्रीड्-घञ्] Playing,<BR>sporting.<BR>--डः<BR>1 Sport, pastime, play,<BR>pleasure.<BR>--2 Jest, joke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडकः|क्रीडक
क्रीडकः<BR>1 A player.<BR>--2 A porter,<BR>doorkeeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडनं|क्रीडन
क्रीडनं [क्रीड् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Playing,<BR>sporting<BR>--2 A play-thing, toy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडनकः|क्रीडनक|क्रीडनकं
क्रीडनकः, --कं, क्रीडनीयं, --यकं A<BR>play-thing, toy; Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडनकं|क्रीडनक|क्रीडनकः
क्रीडनकः, --कं, क्रीडनीयं, --यकं A<BR>play-thing, toy; Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडनीयं|क्रीडनीय
क्रीडनकः, --कं, क्रीडनीयं, --यकं A<BR>play-thing, toy; Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडनीयकं|क्रीडनीयक
क्रीडनकः, --कं, क्रीडनीयं, --यकं A<BR>play-thing, toy; Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडा
क्रीडा [क्रीड्-भावे अ]<BR>1 Sport,<BR>pastime, play, pleasure,<BR>तोयक्रीडानिरतयुवतिस्नानतिक्तैर्मरुद्भिः Me. 33, 61.<BR>--2<BR>Jest, joke.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आकूतं a sportive<BR>purpose.<BR>--उद्देशः play ground.<BR>--काननं, --वनं a pleasure grove, park.<BR>--कोप<BR>false or feigned anger; Amaru. 12.<BR>--कौतूकं {1} wanton curiosity. {2}<BR>sport, play. {3} sexual intercourse.<BR>--गृहं, --मंदिरं a pleasure-house.<BR>--नारी<BR>a prostitute, harlot.<BR>--मयूरः a<BR>peacock kept for pleasure; R. 16. 14.<BR>--मृगः a toy-deer.<BR>--रत्नं ‘the gem of<BR>sports’, copulation.<BR>--वेश्मन् n. a<BR>pleasure-house.<BR>--शैलः, --पर्वतः an artificial<BR>hill serving as a pleasure abode, a<BR>pleasure mountain; क्रीडाशैलः<BR>कनककदलीवेष्टनप्रेक्षणीयः Me. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडि
क्रीडि a. Ved. Playing, sporting,<BR>(epithet of the wind.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रीडु
क्रीडु a. Ved. Playing, moving up<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">Page0432-a+ 56</a>]<BR>(as the Soma).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0431-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुंच्|क्रुञ्च्
क्रुंच् {c1c} P. (क्रुंचति, क्रुंचित)<BR>1 To<BR>curve or make crooked.<BR>--2 To<BR>become or be crooked.<BR>--3 To be or<BR>become small, shrink.<BR>--4 To make<BR>mall, lessen.<BR>--5 To approach,<BR>arrive at, go up to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुंच्|क्रुञ्च्
क्रुंच् m.<BR>1 A curlew, heron.<BR>--2 A<BR>swan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुंचः|क्रुञ्च|क्रुंच|क्रुञ्चः
क्रुंचः<BR>1 A curlew, heron.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of lute.<BR>--3 N. of the<BR>mountain क्रौंच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुड्
क्रुड् {c6c} P. (क्रुडति, क्रुडित)<BR>1 To<BR>sink, dive.<BR>--2 To be or become thick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुथ्
क्रुथ् {c9c} P. (क्रुथ्नाति) To kill, slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोथः|क्रोथ
क्रोथः Murder, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्
क्रुध् {c4c} P. (क्रुध्यति, क्रुद्ध) To be<BR>angry (with the dat. of the person<BR>who is the object of anger); हरये<BR>क्रुध्यति; but sometimes with words<BR>like उपरि, प्रति &c. also; ममोपरि स<BR>क्रुद्धः, न मां प्रति क्रुद्धो गुरुः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्
क्रुध् f. Anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुद्ध|क्रुद्धः
क्रुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Angry, provoked.<BR>--2 Fierce; cruel.<BR>--द्धं Anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुध्मिन्
क्रुध्मिन् a. Ved. Angry, wrathful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधः|क्रोध
क्रोधः [क्रुध्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Anger, wrath;<BR>कामात्क्रोधोऽभिजायते Bg. 2. 62; so<BR>क्रोधांधः, क्रोधानलः &c.<BR>--2 (In Rhet.)<BR>Anger considered as the feeling<BR>which gives rise to the raudra<BR>sentiment.<BR>--धा N. of a daughter of<BR>Dakṣa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इद्ध a.<BR>inflamed with anger, darting out fire;<BR>Ratn. 1. 4.<BR>--उज्झित a. free from anger,<BR>composed, cool.<BR>--कृत् a. angry.<BR>(--m.) the Supreme being.<BR>--ज a.<BR>proceeding from wrath (as the eight<BR>vices; पैशुन्यं साहसं द्रोह ईर्ष्यासूयार्थदूषणं ।<BR>वाग्दंडजं च पारुष्यं क्रोधजोऽपि गणोष्टकः ॥<BR>Ms. 7. 48).<BR>--मूर्च्छित a. overcome or<BR>infatuated with anger.<BR>--वश a.<BR>passionate, violent.<BR>--हन् m. an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधन|क्रोधनः
क्रोधन a. [क्रुध् --युच्] Wrathful,<BR>passionate, angry, irascible; यद्रामेण<BR>कृतं तदेव कुरुते द्रौणायनिः क्रोधनः<BR>Ve. 3. 31.<BR>--नः N. of a son of<BR>Kauśika.<BR>--ना A passionate woman, vixen.<BR>--नं Being angry, anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधनीय
क्रोधनीय a. Provocative.<BR>--यं<BR>Injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधालु
क्रोधालु a. [क्रुध्-आलच्] Wrathful,<BR>irascible, angry, passionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोधिन्
क्रोधिन् a. [क्रुध्-णिनि] Passionate,<BR>angry. --m.<BR>1 A buffalo.<BR>--2 A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुंथ्|क्रुन्थ्
क्रुंथ् {c9c} P. (क्रुथ्नाति)<BR>1 To<BR>embrace.<BR>--2 To be distressed, suffer<BR>pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुमुकः|क्रुमुक
क्रुमुकः Ved. A piece of wood to<BR>catch the sacrificial fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुश्
क्रुश् {c1c} P. (क्रोशति, क्रुष्ट)<BR>1 To cry,<BR>weep, lament, mourn (for);<BR>क्रोशंत्यस्तं कपिस्त्रियः Bk. 6. 124.<BR>--2 To<BR>cry out, yell, scream, bawl, call<BR>out; अतीव चुक्रोश जीवनाशं ननाश च<BR>Bk. 14. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुश्वन्
क्रुश्वन् m. A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रुष्ट|क्रुष्टं
क्रुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Cried out.<BR>--2 Called<BR>out to.<BR>--3 Called at, abused.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1<BR>Crying, a cry, yell.<BR>--2 Weeping.<BR>--3 A noise, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशः|क्रोश
क्रोशः [क्रुश्-घञ्]<BR>1 A cry, yell,<BR>shout, scream, noise.<BR>--2 A measure<BR>of distance equal to (1/4)th of a Yojana,<BR>a Koss; क्रोशार्धं प्रकृतिपुरःसरेण गत्वा<BR>R. 13. 79; समुद्रात्पुरी क्रोशौ (nom.) or<BR>क्रोशयोः (loc.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तालः, --ध्वनिः a<BR>large drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोशन
क्रोशन a. Crying.<BR>--नं A cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रूर|क्रूरः
क्रूर a. [कृत-रक् धातोः क्रूः cf.<BR>Uṇ. 2. 21]<BR>1 Cruel, wicked,<BR>hard-hearted, pitiless; तस्याभिषेकसंभारं कल्पितं<BR>क्रूरनिश्चया R. 12. 4; Me. 105;<BR>Ms. 10. 9.<BR>--2 Hard, rough.<BR>--3<BR>Formidable, terrible, fierce, ferocious,<BR>savage.<BR>--4 Destructive, mischievous.<BR>--5 Wounded, hurt.<BR>--6 Bloody.<BR>--7<BR>Raw.<BR>--8 Strong.<BR>--9 Inauspicious.<BR>--10 Hard, solid, hardened;<BR>Ś. 2. 4.<BR>--11 Hot; disagreeable, sharp;<BR>Ms. 2. 33.<BR>--रः, --रं Boiled rice.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A hawk.<BR>--2 A heron.<BR>--3 An<BR>uneven sign of the zodiac.<BR>--4 N. of a<BR>planet (Rāhu or Saturn).<BR>--रं<BR>1 A<BR>wound.<BR>--2 Slaughter, cruelty.<BR>--3<BR>Any horrible deed.<BR>--4 Any<BR>frightful appearance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आकृति a.<BR>terrible in form.<BR>--(तिः) epithet of<BR>Rāvaṇa.<BR>--आचार a. following cruel<BR>or savage practices.<BR>--आशय a. {1}<BR>containing fierce animals (as a<BR>river). {2} of a cruel disposition.<BR>--कर्मन् n. {1} a bloody act. {2} any<BR>hard labour.<BR>--कृत् a. fierce, cruel,<BR>unrelenting.<BR>--कोष्ठ a. having<BR>costive bowels (unaffected by strong<BR>purgatives).<BR>--गंधः sulphur.<BR>--दृश् a.<BR>{1} evil-eyed, having a malignant<BR>look. {2} mischievous, villainous.<BR>(--m.) N. of Saturn; also of Mars.<BR>--राविन् m. a raven.<BR>--लोचनः an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">Page0432-c+ 55</a>]<BR>epithet of the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोंचः|क्रोञ्च|क्रोंच|क्रोञ्चः
क्रोंचः N. of a mountain; see क्रौंच.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडः|क्रोड|क्रोडं
क्रोडः [क्रुड् घनीभावे संज्ञायां घञ्]<BR>1<BR>A hog.<BR>--2 The hollow of a tree,<BR>cavity; हा हा हंत तथापि<BR>जन्मविटपिक्रोडे मनो धावति Udb.<BR>--3 The chest,<BR>bosom, breast; क्रोडीकृ to clasp to<BR>the bosom; क्रोडीकरोति प्रथमं यथा<BR>जातमनित्यता । धात्रीव जननी पश्चात्तथा<BR>शोकस्य कः क्रमः ॥ Nāg. 4; Bh. 2. 35.<BR>--4 The middle part of anything;<BR>Vikr. 11. 75; see क्रोड n.<BR>--5 An<BR>epithet of the planet Saturn.<BR>--डं, --डा<BR>1 The breast, chest, the part between<BR>the shoulders.<BR>--2 The interior of<BR>anything, a cavity, hollow.<BR>--3 The<BR>breast of a horse.<BR>--4 The lap; U. 4.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः, --अंघ्रिः, --पादः a<BR>tortoise.<BR>--पत्रं {1} marginal writing. {2} a<BR>postscript to a letter. {3} a<BR>supplement. {4} a codicil to a will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडीकरणं|क्रोडीकरण
क्रोडीकरणं Embracing, clasping to<BR>the bosom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोडीमुखः|क्रोडीमुख
क्रोडीमुखः A rhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रोष्टु
क्रोष्टु m. (ष्ट्री f.) [क्रुश्-तुन् Uṇ. 1. 69].<BR>A jackal (the strong cases of this word<BR>are necessarily formed from क्रोष्टृ and<BR>the weak ones optionally); so क्रोष्टुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौंचः|क्रौञ्च|क्रौंच|क्रौञ्चः
क्रौंचः [क्रुंच् प्रज्ञा˚ अण्]<BR>1 A<BR>curlew, heron;<BR>मनोहरक्रौंचनिनादितानि सीमांतराण्युत्सुकयंति चेतः<BR>Rs. 4. 8; Ms. 12. 64.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>mountain (said to be the grandson of<BR>Himālaya and said to have been<BR>pierced by Kārtikeya and<BR>Paraśurāma); हंसद्वारं भृगुपतियशोवर्त्म यत्<BR>क्रौंचरंभ्रं Me. 57.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदनं the<BR>fibres of the stalk of a lotus.<BR>--(नी)<BR>the seed of the lotus.<BR>--अरातिः, --अरिः,<BR>--रिपुः {1} an epithet of Kārtikeya. {2} of<BR>Paraśurāma.<BR>--दारणः, --सूदनः an<BR>epithet (1) of Kārtikeya (2) of<BR>Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौर्यं|क्रौर्य|क्रौर्य्य
क्रौर्यं<BR>1 Cruelty, hard-heartedness.<BR>--2 Terribleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्रौशशतिकः|क्रौशशतिक
क्रौशशतिकः<BR>1 A mendicant who<BR>walks a hundred Krośas.<BR>--2 One who<BR>deserves to be approached from a<BR>distance of 100 Krośas (as a teacher).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लथ्
क्लथ् {c1c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To kill, hurt.<BR>--2<BR>To turn round, revolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लंद्|क्लन्द्
क्लंद् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (क्लंदति, क्लंदित)<BR>1 To<BR>call out.<BR>--2 To cry, lament, weep.<BR>{vII.v} {c1c} A. (क्लंदते or क्लदते)<BR>1 To be<BR>confused.<BR>--2 To grieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0432-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लम्
क्लम् {c1c} {c4c} P. (क्लामति, क्लाम्यति, क्लांत)<BR>1 To be fatigued or tired, be<BR>exhausted or depressed; न चक्लाम न विव्यथे<BR>Bk. 5. 102; 14. 101.<BR>--2 To feel<BR>sorry, pine for; Ś. 6. --Caus. (<BR>क्लमयति-ते) To fatigue, exhaust, depress,<BR>wither; U. 3. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमः|क्लम
क्लमः, क्लमथः, क्लमथुः Fatigue, languor,<BR>exhaustion; विनोदितदिनक्लमाः कृतरुचश्च<BR>जांबूनदैः Śi. 4. 66; Ms. 7. 151;<BR>Ś. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमथः|क्लमथ
क्लमः, क्लमथः, क्लमथुः Fatigue, languor,<BR>exhaustion; विनोदितदिनक्लमाः कृतरुचश्च<BR>जांबूनदैः Śi. 4. 66; Ms. 7. 151;<BR>Ś. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लमथुः|क्लमथु
क्लमः, क्लमथः, क्लमथुः Fatigue, languor,<BR>exhaustion; विनोदितदिनक्लमाः कृतरुचश्च<BR>जांबूनदैः Śi. 4. 66; Ms. 7. 151;<BR>Ś. 3. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लांत|क्लान्त|क्लान्तः
क्लांत p. p. [क्लम्-क्त]<BR>1 Fatigued, tired<BR>out; तमातपक्लांतं R. 2. 13, Me. 18, 35;<BR>V. 2. 23.<BR>--2 Withered, faded: क्लांतो<BR>मन्मथलेख एष नलिनीपत्रे नखैरर्पितः<BR>Ś. 3. 26; R. 10. 48.<BR>--3 Lean, thin,<BR>emaciated.<BR>--4 Depressed in spirits,<BR>exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लांतिः|क्लान्ति|क्लांति|क्लान्तिः
क्लांतिः f. [क्लम्-क्तिन्] Fatigue.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--छिद् a. refreshing,<BR>invigorating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लव्
क्लव् {c4c} A. (क्लव्यते) To fear, be<BR>afraid (according to some {1} A also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिद्
क्लिद् {c4c} P. (क्लिद्यति, क्लिन्न) To<BR>become wet, be damp, be damp, be moist.<BR>--Caus. To moisten, wet; न चैनं<BR>क्लेदयंत्यापः Bg. 2. 23; Bk. 18. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिन्न|क्लिन्नं
क्लिन्न a. Wet, moistened; running<BR>(as an eye).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a.<BR>bleareyed.<BR>--वर्त्मन् n. watering of the eyes.<BR>--हृद् a. tender-hearted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदः|क्लेद
क्लेदः [क्लिद्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Wetness,<BR>moisture, dampness; Śānti. 1. 29;<BR>R. 7. 21.<BR>--2 Running, discharge<BR>from a sore.<BR>--3 Distress, suffering;<BR>R. 15. 32 (= उपद्रव Malli.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदक|क्लेदकः
क्लेदक a. Wetting, moistening.<BR>--कः<BR>1 Phlegm.<BR>--2 One of the fires in<BR>the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदन्
क्लेदन् m. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदन|क्लेदनः
क्लेदन a. [क्लिद् णिच् ल्युट्] Wetting,<BR>making wet.<BR>--नः Phlegm.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Wetting, moistening.<BR>--2 Trickling,<BR>oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेदुः|क्लेदु
क्लेदुः<BR>1 The moon.<BR>--2 Morbid<BR>combination of the three humors<BR>of the body (संनिपात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिंद्|क्लिन्द्
क्लिंद् {c1c} U. (क्लिंदति-ते) To lament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिब्
क्लिब् f. Ved. The created world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिश्
क्लिश् {vI.v} {c4c} A. (also P. according<BR>to some authorities) (क्लिश्यते, क्लिष्ट or<BR>क्लिशित)<BR>1 To be tormented, be<BR>afflicted, suffer; अप्युपदेशग्रहणे<BR>नातिक्लिश्यते वः शिष्या M. 1; त्रयः परार्थे<BR>क्लिश्यंति साक्षिणः प्रतिभूः कुलं Ms. 8. 169.<BR>--2 To torment, molest. {vII.v} {c9c} P.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">Page0433-b+ 56</a>]<BR>(क्लिश्नाति, क्लिष्ट, क्लिशित)<BR>1 To torment,<BR>afflict, molest, distress; क्लिश्नाति<BR>लब्धपरिपालनवृत्तिरेव Ś. 5. 6;<BR>एवमाराध्यमानोपि क्लिश्नाति भुवनत्रयं Ku. 2. 40;<BR>R. 11. 58.<BR>--2 To suffer, feel pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिशित|क्लिशितः
क्लिशित, --क्लिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Distressed,<BR>suffering pain or misery.<BR>--2 Afflicted,<BR>tormented.<BR>--3 Faded.<BR>--4<BR>Inconsistent, contradictory; e. g.<BR>माता मे वंध्या.<BR>--5 Elaborate,<BR>artificial, (as a composition.).<BR>--6 Put to<BR>shame.<BR>--7 Wearied; hurt, injured.<BR>--8 Being in a bad condition, worn.<BR>--9 Marred, impaired; Ś. 5. 19;<BR>Pt. 1. 11; Ś. 6. 9; disordered; Ś. 7. 14.<BR>--10 Dimmed, made faint;<BR>Ku. 2. 19.<BR>--11 Injured, hurt; Ś. 6. 19.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>A contradictory statement.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्त्मन् n. a disease of the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्ट|क्लिष्टः
क्लिशित, --क्लिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Distressed,<BR>suffering pain or misery.<BR>--2 Afflicted,<BR>tormented.<BR>--3 Faded.<BR>--4<BR>Inconsistent, contradictory; e. g.<BR>माता मे वंध्या.<BR>--5 Elaborate,<BR>artificial, (as a composition.).<BR>--6 Put to<BR>shame.<BR>--7 Wearied; hurt, injured.<BR>--8 Being in a bad condition, worn.<BR>--9 Marred, impaired; Ś. 5. 19;<BR>Pt. 1. 11; Ś. 6. 9; disordered; Ś. 7. 14.<BR>--10 Dimmed, made faint;<BR>Ku. 2. 19.<BR>--11 Injured, hurt; Ś. 6. 19.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>A contradictory statement.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्त्मन् n. a disease of the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लिष्टिः|क्लिष्टि
क्लिष्टिः f.<BR>1 Affliction, anguish,<BR>distress, pain.<BR>--2 Service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशः|क्लेश
क्लेशः [क्लिश्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Pain,<BR>anguish, suffering, distress, trouble;<BR>किमात्मा क्लेशस्य पदमुपनीतः Ś. 1; क्लेशः<BR>फलेन हि पुनर्नवतां विधत्ते Ku. 5. 86;<BR>Bg. 12. 5.<BR>--2 Wrath, anger.<BR>--3<BR>Care, trouble.<BR>--4 Worldly<BR>occupation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपह a. allaying<BR>pain, consoling, palliative.<BR>--(हः)<BR>a son.<BR>--कर a. causing pain or<BR>trouble.<BR>--क्षम a capable of enduring<BR>trouble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशक
क्लेशक a. [क्लिश्-वुञ्] Giving pain,<BR>troublesome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशित|क्लेशितः
क्लेशित a. Pained, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेशिन्
क्लेशिन् a.<BR>1 Causing pain or<BR>suffering<BR>--2 Hurting, injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीब्
क्लीब् {c1c} A. (क्लीबते)<BR>1 To be<BR>impotent, to behave like a eunuch.<BR>--2 To<BR>be timorous, to be modest or<BR>unassuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीब|क्लीबः
क्लीब(व) a.<BR>1 Impotent, neuter,<BR>emasculated; Ms. 3. 150, 4. 205;<BR>Y. 1. 223.<BR>--2 Unmanly, timid,<BR>weak, weak-minded; R. 8. 84;<BR>क्लीबान् पालयिता Mk. 9. 5.<BR>--3<BR>Cowardly.<BR>--4 Mean, base.<BR>--5 Idle.<BR>--6 Of the neuter gender.<BR>--बः, --बं<BR>--(वः, --वं)<BR>1 An impotent man, a<BR>eunuch; न मूत्रं फेनिलं यस्य विष्ठा चाप्सु<BR>निमज्जति । मेढं चोन्मादशुक्राभ्यां हीनं<BR>क्लीबः स उच्यते ॥ Kātyāyana quoted<BR>in Dāyabhāga.<BR>--2 The neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लीव|क्लीवः
क्लीब(व) a.<BR>1 Impotent, neuter,<BR>emasculated; Ms. 3. 150, 4. 205;<BR>Y. 1. 223.<BR>--2 Unmanly, timid,<BR>weak, weak-minded; R. 8. 84;<BR>क्लीबान् पालयिता Mk. 9. 5.<BR>--3<BR>Cowardly.<BR>--4 Mean, base.<BR>--5 Idle.<BR>--6 Of the neuter gender.<BR>--बः, --बं<BR>--(वः, --वं)<BR>1 An impotent man, a<BR>eunuch; न मूत्रं फेनिलं यस्य विष्ठा चाप्सु<BR>निमज्जति । मेढं चोन्मादशुक्राभ्यां हीनं<BR>क्लीबः स उच्यते ॥ Kātyāyana quoted<BR>in Dāyabhāga.<BR>--2 The neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैब्यं|क्लैब्य
क्लैब्यं(व्यं)<BR>1 Impotence (lit.);<BR>वरं क्लैब्यं पुंसां न च परकलत्राभिगमनं<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--2 Unmanliness; timidity,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">Page0433-c+ 55</a>]<BR>cowardice; क्लैव्यं मा स्म गमः पार्थ Bg. 2. 3.<BR>--3<BR>Impotence, powerlessness; R. 12. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैव्यं|क्लैव्य
क्लैब्यं(व्यं)<BR>1 Impotence (lit.);<BR>वरं क्लैब्यं पुंसां न च परकलत्राभिगमनं<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--2 Unmanliness; timidity,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">Page0433-c+ 55</a>]<BR>cowardice; क्लैव्यं मा स्म गमः पार्थ Bg. 2. 3.<BR>--3<BR>Impotence, powerlessness; R. 12. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लु
क्लु {c1c} A. (क्लवते) To move, go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लेश्
क्लेश् {c1c} A. (क्लेशते)<BR>1 To speak<BR>articulately.<BR>--2 To impede, hinder.<BR>--3 To strike, kill.<BR>--4 To distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लैतकिकं|क्लैतकिक
क्लैतकिकं Fermented liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लोमं|क्लोम
क्लोमं, क्लोमन् n. [क्लु गतौ मनिन्]<BR>1<BR>The lungs.<BR>--2 The bladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लोमन्
क्लोमं, क्लोमन् n. [क्लु गतौ मनिन्]<BR>1<BR>The lungs.<BR>--2 The bladder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्लोशः|क्लोश
क्लोशः Ved. Fear; Rv. 6. 46. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्व
क्व ind.<BR>1 Whither, where; क्वतेऽ<BR>न्योन्यं यत्नाः क्व च नु गहनाः कौतुकरसाः<BR>U. 6. 33; क्व-क्व when repeated in<BR>co-ordinate sentences imply ‘great<BR>difference,’ or ‘incongruity’; क्व रुजा<BR>हृदयप्रमाथिनी क्व च ते विश्वसनीयमायुधं<BR>M. 3. 2; क्व सूर्यप्रभवो वंशः क्व<BR>चाल्पविषया मतिः R. 1. 2; Ki. 1. 6;<BR>Ś. 2. 18.<BR>--2 Sometimes क्व is used in<BR>the sense of the loc. of किम् क्व<BR>प्रदेशे i. e. कस्मिन्प्रदेशे. (a) With<BR>a following अपि it means (1)<BR>somewhere, anywhere; (2)<BR>sometimes. (b) With a following चित् it<BR>means (1) in some places; प्रस्निग्धाः<BR>क्वचिदिंगुदीफलभिदः सूच्यंत एवोपलाः<BR>Ś. 1. 14; Rs. 1. 2; R. 1. 41; (2) in<BR>some cases; क्वचिद् गोचरः क्वचिन्न<BR>गोचरोऽर्थः क्वचित्-क्वचित् (a) in one<BR>place-in another place, here-here;<BR>क्वचिद्वीणावाद्यं क्वचिदपि च हाहेति रुदितं<BR>Bh. 3. 125, 1. 4. (b) now-now<BR>(referring to time); क्वचित् पथा<BR>संचरते सुराणां क्वचित् घनानां पततां क्वचिच्च<BR>R. 13. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वत्य
क्वत्य a. Belonging to what place,<BR>being where.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वण्
क्वण् {c1c} P. (क्वणति, क्वणित)<BR>1 To<BR>sound (indistinctly), jingle, tinkle;<BR>इति घोषयतीव डिंडिमः करिणो<BR>हस्तिपकाहतः क्वणन् H. 2. 86; क्वणन्मणिनूपुरौ<BR>Amaru. 28; Rs. 3. 24; Me. 36.<BR>--2<BR>To hum, warble (as bees &c.); sing<BR>indistinctly; Ku. 1. 54; U. 3. 24;<BR>Bk. 6. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणः|क्वण
क्वणः, क्वणनं, क्वणितं, क्वाणः<BR>1 A sound<BR>in general.<BR>--2 The sound of any<BR>musical instrument.<BR>--नः A small<BR>earthen pot or boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणनं|क्वणन|क्वणनः
क्वणः, क्वणनं, क्वणितं, क्वाणः<BR>1 A sound<BR>in general.<BR>--2 The sound of any<BR>musical instrument.<BR>--नः A small<BR>earthen pot or boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वणितं|क्वणित
क्वणः, क्वणनं, क्वणितं, क्वाणः<BR>1 A sound<BR>in general.<BR>--2 The sound of any<BR>musical instrument.<BR>--नः A small<BR>earthen pot or boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाणः|क्वाण
क्वणः, क्वणनं, क्वणितं, क्वाणः<BR>1 A sound<BR>in general.<BR>--2 The sound of any<BR>musical instrument.<BR>--नः A small<BR>earthen pot or boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथ्
क्वथ् {c1c} P. (क्वथति, क्वथित)<BR>1 To<BR>boil, decoct.<BR>--2 To digest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथः|क्वथ
क्वथः A decoction, solution<BR>prepared with a continued or gentle<BR>heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथनं|क्वथन
क्वथनं [क्वथ्-ल्युट्] Boiling, decocting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0433-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वथित|क्वथितः
क्वथित a. [क्वथ्-क्त] Boiled, decocted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाथः|क्वाथ
क्वाथः [क्वथ्-करणे घञ्]<BR>1 A<BR>decoction, solution prepared with a<BR>continued or gentle heat.<BR>--2 The<BR>mixture of the materials for decoction.<BR>--3 Pain, sorrow, distress.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्भवं blue vitriol used as a<BR>collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वाचित्क
क्वाचित्क a. (त्की f.) Met with<BR>occasionally, rare, unusual; इति<BR>क्वाचित्कः पाठः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्वेल्
क्वेल् {c1c} P. (क्वेलति) To shake, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षः|क्ष
क्षः<BR>1 Destruction.<BR>--2<BR>Disappearance, loss.<BR>--3 Lightning.<BR>--4 A field.<BR>--5 A farmer.<BR>--6 Viṣṇu in his 4th<BR>or Narasiṃha incarnation.<BR>--7 A<BR>demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षंज्
क्षंज्, क्षज् {c10c} U. (क्षंजयति-ते) To<BR>live in distress or pain. --{c1c} A. (क्षजते)<BR>To kill. --{c1c} A. (क्षंजते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2<BR>To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षज्
क्षंज्, क्षज् {c10c} U. (क्षंजयति-ते) To<BR>live in distress or pain. --{c1c} A. (क्षजते)<BR>To kill. --{c1c} A. (क्षंजते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2<BR>To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षण्
क्षण्(न्) {c8c} U. (क्षणोति, क्षणुते, क्षत)<BR>1 To hurt, injure; इमां हृदि<BR>व्यायतपातमक्षणोत् Ku. 5. 54.<BR>--2 To break<BR>(to pieces); (धनुः) त्वं<BR>किलानमितपूर्वमक्षणोः R. 11. 72; (with परा, --परि,<BR>--वि used in the same senses as क्षण्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षन्
क्षण्(न्) {c8c} U. (क्षणोति, क्षणुते, क्षत)<BR>1 To hurt, injure; इमां हृदि<BR>व्यायतपातमक्षणोत् Ku. 5. 54.<BR>--2 To break<BR>(to pieces); (धनुः) त्वं<BR>किलानमितपूर्वमक्षणोः R. 11. 72; (with परा, --परि,<BR>--वि used in the same senses as क्षण्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणः|क्षण|क्षणं
क्षणः, --णं [क्षणोति दुःखं क्षण्-अच्]<BR>1 An<BR>instant, moment, measure of time<BR>equal to 4/5 of a second;<BR>क्षणमात्रमृषिस्तस्थौ सुप्तमीन इव ह्रदः R. 1. 73; 2. 60;<BR>Me. 26; क्षणमवतिष्ठस्व wait a moment.<BR>--2 Leisure; अहमपि लब्धक्षणः स्वगेहं<BR>गच्छामि M. 1; Pt. 1. 138; गृहीतः क्षणः<BR>Ś. 2 ‘my leisure is at your disposal’<BR>i. e. I pledge my word to do your<BR>work.<BR>--3 A fit moment or<BR>opportunity; रहो नास्ति क्षणो नास्ति नास्ति<BR>प्रार्थयिता नरः Pt. 1. 138; Me. 62; अधिगतक्षणः<BR>Dk. 147.<BR>--4 An auspicious or lucky<BR>moment.<BR>--5 A festival, joy, delight.<BR>--6 Dependence, servitude.<BR>--7 The<BR>centre, the middle.<BR>--8 A certain day<BR>of the fortnight (as the full moon).<BR>(In comp. क्षण is translated by<BR>‘momentary’, ‘temporary.’ क्षणात्, --क्षणेन<BR>in a moment, at once, immediately).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरे ind. the next<BR>moment, after a little while.<BR>--क्षेपः a<BR>momentary delay.<BR>--दः an astrologer.<BR>--(दं) {1} night-blindness. {2} water.<BR>--(दा) {1} night; क्षणादथैष क्षणदापतिप्रभः<BR>N. 1. 67; R. 8. 74; 16. 45;<BR>Śi. 3. 53. {2} turmeric. ˚करः, ˚पतिः the<BR>moon; Śi. 9. 70. ˚चरः a night-walker,<BR>a demon; सानुप्लवः प्रभुरपि क्षणदाचराणां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-b" target="_blank">Page0434-b+ 57</a>]<BR>R. 13. 75. ˚आंध्यं night-blindness,<BR>nyctalopsis.<BR>--द्युतिः f.,<BR>--प्रकाशा,<BR>--प्रभा lightning.<BR>--निःश्वासः the<BR>porpoise.<BR>--भंगुर a. transient, frail,<BR>perishable; H. 4. 130.<BR>--मात्रं ind.<BR>for a moment.<BR>--रामिन् m. a pigeon.<BR>--विध्वंसिन् a. perishable in a moment.<BR>(--m.) a class of atheistic philosophers<BR>who deny the continued identity of<BR>any part of nature, and maintain<BR>that the universe perishes and<BR>undergoes a new creation every<BR>instant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणं|क्षण|क्षणः
क्षणः, --णं [क्षणोति दुःखं क्षण्-अच्]<BR>1 An<BR>instant, moment, measure of time<BR>equal to 4/5 of a second;<BR>क्षणमात्रमृषिस्तस्थौ सुप्तमीन इव ह्रदः R. 1. 73; 2. 60;<BR>Me. 26; क्षणमवतिष्ठस्व wait a moment.<BR>--2 Leisure; अहमपि लब्धक्षणः स्वगेहं<BR>गच्छामि M. 1; Pt. 1. 138; गृहीतः क्षणः<BR>Ś. 2 ‘my leisure is at your disposal’<BR>i. e. I pledge my word to do your<BR>work.<BR>--3 A fit moment or<BR>opportunity; रहो नास्ति क्षणो नास्ति नास्ति<BR>प्रार्थयिता नरः Pt. 1. 138; Me. 62; अधिगतक्षणः<BR>Dk. 147.<BR>--4 An auspicious or lucky<BR>moment.<BR>--5 A festival, joy, delight.<BR>--6 Dependence, servitude.<BR>--7 The<BR>centre, the middle.<BR>--8 A certain day<BR>of the fortnight (as the full moon).<BR>(In comp. क्षण is translated by<BR>‘momentary’, ‘temporary.’ क्षणात्, --क्षणेन<BR>in a moment, at once, immediately).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरे ind. the next<BR>moment, after a little while.<BR>--क्षेपः a<BR>momentary delay.<BR>--दः an astrologer.<BR>--(दं) {1} night-blindness. {2} water.<BR>--(दा) {1} night; क्षणादथैष क्षणदापतिप्रभः<BR>N. 1. 67; R. 8. 74; 16. 45;<BR>Śi. 3. 53. {2} turmeric. ˚करः, ˚पतिः the<BR>moon; Śi. 9. 70. ˚चरः a night-walker,<BR>a demon; सानुप्लवः प्रभुरपि क्षणदाचराणां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-b" target="_blank">Page0434-b+ 57</a>]<BR>R. 13. 75. ˚आंध्यं night-blindness,<BR>nyctalopsis.<BR>--द्युतिः f.,<BR>--प्रकाशा,<BR>--प्रभा lightning.<BR>--निःश्वासः the<BR>porpoise.<BR>--भंगुर a. transient, frail,<BR>perishable; H. 4. 130.<BR>--मात्रं ind.<BR>for a moment.<BR>--रामिन् m. a pigeon.<BR>--विध्वंसिन् a. perishable in a moment.<BR>(--m.) a class of atheistic philosophers<BR>who deny the continued identity of<BR>any part of nature, and maintain<BR>that the universe perishes and<BR>undergoes a new creation every<BR>instant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणतुः|क्षणतु
क्षणतुः A wound, sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणनं|क्षणन
क्षणनं Injuring, killing, wounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिक|क्षणिकः
क्षणिक a. [क्षणः स्वसत्ताव्याप्यतयाऽ<BR>स्त्यस्य ठन्] Momentary, transient; स्वप्नेषु<BR>क्षणिकसमागमोत्सवैश्च R. 8. 92; एकस्य<BR>क्षणिका प्रीतिः H. 1. 66.<BR>--का<BR>Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षणिन्
क्षणिन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Having leisure.<BR>--2 Momentary.<BR>--3 Having a festival.<BR>--नी Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्
क्षत् f.<BR>1 Killing.<BR>--2 Tearing.<BR>--3<BR>Injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत|क्षतं
क्षत p. p. [क्षण्-क्त]<BR>1 Wounded, hurt,<BR>injured, bitten, torn, rent, broken<BR>down &c.; see क्षण्; रक्तप्रसाधितभुवः<BR>क्षतविग्रहाश्च Ve. 1. 7; Ku. 4. 6;<BR>R. 1. 28; 2. 56; 3. 53.<BR>--2 Diminished;<BR>trodden.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Scratching, a scratch.<BR>--2 A wound, hurt, injury; क्षते<BR>प्रहारा निपतंत्यभीक्ष्णं Pt. 2. 178; क्षते<BR>क्षारमिवासह्यं जातं तस्यैव दर्शनं U. 4. 7;<BR>क्षारं क्षते प्रक्षिपन् Mk. 5. 18; नख˚<BR>Ku. 3. 29.<BR>--3 Danger, destruction, peril;<BR>क्षतात् किल त्रायत इत्युदग्रः R. 2. 53.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरि a. victorious.<BR>--उदरं<BR>dysentery.<BR>--कासः a cough<BR>produced by injury.<BR>--जं {1} blood; स<BR>छिन्नमूलः क्षतजेन रेणुः R. 7. 43;<BR>Ve. 2. 27. {2} pus, matter.<BR>--योनिः f.<BR>a violated woman, a woman who is<BR>no longer a virgin.<BR>--विक्षत a.<BR>mangled, covered with cuts and wounds.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. destitution, being<BR>deprived of any means of support.<BR>--व्रतः a student who has violated his<BR>vow or religious engagements.<BR>--हरं<BR>aloewood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षतिः|क्षति
क्षतिः f. [क्षण्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Injury,<BR>wound.<BR>--2 Destruction, cutting,<BR>tearing down; विस्रब्धं क्रियतां<BR>वराहततिभिर्मुस्ताक्षतिः पल्वले Ś. 2. 6.<BR>--3<BR>(Fig.) Ruin, loss, disadvantage;<BR>सुखं संजायते तेभ्यः सर्वेभ्योपीति का क्षतिः<BR>S. D. 37.<BR>--4 Decline, decay,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">Page0434-c+ 56</a>]<BR>diminution; प्रतापक्षतिशीतलाः<BR>Ku. 2. 24; H. 1. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्तृ
क्षत्तृ m. [क्षद् संज्ञायाम् तृच्<BR>Uṇ. 2. 91]<BR>1 One who cuts or carves<BR>anything.<BR>--2 An attendant, a<BR>doorkeeper.<BR>--3 A coachman, charioteer.<BR>--4 A man born of a Śūdra man<BR>and Kṣatriya woman; cf.<BR>Ms. 10. 9.<BR>--5 The son of a female slave; (<BR>e. g. विदुर).<BR>--6 Brahmā.<BR>--7 A fish.<BR>--8<BR>One who fights from a chariot.<BR>--9<BR>The manager of a treasure (कोषाध्यक्ष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रः|क्षत्र|क्षत्त्रं|क्षत्त्रः|क्षत्रं
क्षत्रः, --त्रं<BR>1 Dominion, power,<BR>supremacy, might.<BR>--2 A man of<BR>the Kṣatriya caste, or the<BR>Kṣatriya tribe taken<BR>collectively; क्षतात्किल त्रायत इत्युदग्रः<BR>क्षत्रस्य शब्दो भुवनेषु रूढः R. 2. 53;<BR>11. 69, 71; असंशयं क्षत्रपरिग्रहक्षमा<BR>Ś. 1. 22; Ms. 9. 322.<BR>--3 A man of the<BR>warrior class, a soldier; क्षत्रप्रताप<BR>U. 6. 18 martial or heroic valour;<BR>6. 16.<BR>--त्री<BR>1 A woman of the<BR>military caste.<BR>--2 The rank of a<BR>member of the military caste.<BR>--3 Wealth.<BR>--4 Water.<BR>--5 The body.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतकः an epithet of Paraśurāma.<BR>--धर्मः {1} bravery, military heroism.<BR>{2} the duties of a Kṣatriya.<BR>--पः<BR>a governor, satrap.<BR>--बंधुः {1} a<BR>Kṣatriya by caste; Ms. 2. 38. {2} a mere<BR>Kṣatriya, a vile or wretched<BR>Kṣatriya; (as a term of abuse); cf.<BR>ब्रह्मबंधु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रं|क्षत्र|क्षत्त्रं|क्षत्त्रः|क्षत्रः
क्षत्रः, --त्रं<BR>1 Dominion, power,<BR>supremacy, might.<BR>--2 A man of<BR>the Kṣatriya caste, or the<BR>Kṣatriya tribe taken<BR>collectively; क्षतात्किल त्रायत इत्युदग्रः<BR>क्षत्रस्य शब्दो भुवनेषु रूढः R. 2. 53;<BR>11. 69, 71; असंशयं क्षत्रपरिग्रहक्षमा<BR>Ś. 1. 22; Ms. 9. 322.<BR>--3 A man of the<BR>warrior class, a soldier; क्षत्रप्रताप<BR>U. 6. 18 martial or heroic valour;<BR>6. 16.<BR>--त्री<BR>1 A woman of the<BR>military caste.<BR>--2 The rank of a<BR>member of the military caste.<BR>--3 Wealth.<BR>--4 Water.<BR>--5 The body.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतकः an epithet of Paraśurāma.<BR>--धर्मः {1} bravery, military heroism.<BR>{2} the duties of a Kṣatriya.<BR>--पः<BR>a governor, satrap.<BR>--बंधुः {1} a<BR>Kṣatriya by caste; Ms. 2. 38. {2} a mere<BR>Kṣatriya, a vile or wretched<BR>Kṣatriya; (as a term of abuse); cf.<BR>ब्रह्मबंधु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रिन्
क्षत्रिन् m. A man of the military<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियः|क्षत्रिय|क्षत्त्रियः
क्षत्रियः [क्षत्रे राष्ट्रे साधु तस्यापत्यं जातौ<BR>वा घः Tv.] A member of the military<BR>or second caste; ब्राह्मणः क्षत्रियो<BR>वैश्यस्त्रयो वर्णा द्विजातयः Ms. 10. 4.<BR>--यं The rank or power of the<BR>Kṣatriya class.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हनः (णः) an<BR>epithet of Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियका
क्षत्रियका, क्षत्रिया, क्षत्रियिका A woman<BR>of the Kṣatriya caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रिया
क्षत्रियका, क्षत्रिया, क्षत्रियिका A woman<BR>of the Kṣatriya caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियिका
क्षत्रियका, क्षत्रिया, क्षत्रियिका A woman<BR>of the Kṣatriya caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियाणी
क्षत्रियाणी<BR>1 A woman of the<BR>Kṣatriya caste.<BR>--2 The wife of a<BR>Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षत्रियी
क्षत्रियी The wife of a Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षद्
क्षद् {c1c} A. (क्षदते) Ved.<BR>1 To cut.<BR>--2<BR>To kill.<BR>--3 To consume, eat.<BR>--4 To<BR>cover, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षदनं|क्षदन
क्षदनं<BR>1 Carving, dividing, tearing.<BR>--2 Eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षद्मन्
क्षद्मन् n. [क्षद् भक्षणे मनिन्]<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0434-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप्
क्षप् {c1c} U. (क्षपति-ते, क्षपित) To fast,<BR>to be abstinent; Ms. 5. 69. --Caus.<BR>or {c10c} U. (क्षपयति-ते, क्षपित)<BR>1 To throw,<BR>send, cast.<BR>--2 To miss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षप्
क्षप् f. Ved.<BR>1 Night.<BR>--2 A<BR>measure of time.<BR>--3 Darkness.<BR>--4<BR>Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपः|क्षप
क्षपः Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणः|क्षपण
क्षपणः A Bauddha mendicant.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Defilement, impurity (अशौच).<BR>--2 Destroying, suppressing,<BR>expelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणकः|क्षपणक
क्षपणकः A Bauddha or Jaina<BR>mendicant; नग्नक्षपणके देशे रजकः किं<BR>करिष्यति Chāṇ. 110; कथं प्रथममेव क्षपणकः<BR>Mu. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपणी
क्षपणी<BR>1 An oar.<BR>--2 A net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपण्युः|क्षपण्यु
क्षपण्युः An offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षपा
क्षपा [क्षपयति चेष्टां; क्षि-णिच् अच्]<BR>1 A<BR>night; विगमयत्युन्निद्र एव क्षपाः Ś. 6. 4;<BR>R. 2. 20; Me. 110.<BR>--2 Turmeric.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अटः {1} night-stalker. {2}<BR>a demon, goblin; ततः क्षपाटैः<BR>पृथुपिंगलाक्षैः Bk. 2. 30.<BR>--आंध्यं<BR>night-blindness.<BR>--करः, --नाथः {1} the moon. {2}<BR>camphor.<BR>--घनः a dark cloud.<BR>--चरः<BR>a demon, goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्
क्षम् {c1c} A., {c4c} P. (क्षमते, क्षाम्यति,<BR>चक्षमे, चक्षाम, क्षांत or क्षमित)<BR>1 To<BR>permit, allow, suffer; अतो<BR>नृपाश्चक्षमिरे समेताः स्त्रीरत्नलाभं न तदात्मजस्य<BR>R. 7. 34; 12. 46.<BR>--2 To pardon,<BR>forgive (as an offence); क्षांतं न क्षमया<BR>Bh. 3. 13; क्षमस्व परमेश्वर; निघ्नस्य मे<BR>भर्तृनिदेशरौक्ष्यं देवि क्षमस्वेति बभूव नम्रः<BR>R. 14. 58.<BR>--3 To be patient or quiet,<BR>wait; R. 15. 45.<BR>--4 To endure,<BR>put up with, suffer; अपि क्षमंतेऽ<BR>स्मदुपजापं प्रकृतयः Mu. 2; नाज्ञाभंगकरान्<BR>राजा क्षमेत स्वसुतानपि H. 2. 107.<BR>--5<BR>To oppose, resist.<BR>--6 To be<BR>competent or able (to do anything);<BR>ऋने रवेः क्षालयितुं क्षमेत कः<BR>क्षपातमस्कांडमलीमसं नभः Śi. 1. 38, 9. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षंतव्य|क्षन्तव्य
क्षंतव्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be borne or<BR>endured.<BR>--2 Pardonable, fit to be<BR>forgiven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षंतृ|क्षन्तृ
क्षंतृ a. [क्षम्-तृच्] Patient,<BR>enduring, forbearing, submissive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम्
क्षम् f. Ved. The ground, earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षम|क्षमं|क्षमः
क्षम a. [क्षम्-अच्]<BR>1 Patient.<BR>--2<BR>Enduring, submissive.<BR>--3 Adequate,<BR>competent, able (with gen., loc.,<BR>inf. or in comp.); मलिनो हि यथादर्शो<BR>रूपालोकस्य न क्षमः Y. 3. 141; सा हि<BR>रक्षणविधौ तयोः क्षमा R. 11. 6; हृदयं<BR>न त्ववलंबितुं क्षमाः R. 8. 60; गमनक्षम,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">Page0435-b+ 56</a>]<BR>निमूर्लनक्षम &c.<BR>--4 Appropriate, fit,<BR>proper, suitable; तन्नो यदुक्तमशिवं न हि<BR>तत्क्षमं ते U. 1. 14; आत्मकर्मक्षमं देहं<BR>क्षात्रो धर्म इवाश्रितः R. 1. 13;<BR>Ś. 5. 27.<BR>--5 Fit for, capable of, suited<BR>to; उपभोगक्षमे देशे V. 2; तपःक्षमं<BR>साधयितुं य इच्छति Ś. 1. 18;<BR>स्पर्शक्षमं रत्नं 1. 28; 7. 5.<BR>--6<BR>Bearable, endurable.<BR>--7 Favourable,<BR>friendly.<BR>--मं<BR>1 Propriety, fitness.<BR>--2<BR>Battle, war.<BR>--मः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमणीय
क्षमणीय a.<BR>1 To be borne,<BR>patiently borne.<BR>--2 To be pardoned or<BR>forgiven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमा
क्षमा [क्षम्-अङ्]<BR>1 Patience,<BR>forbearance, forgiveness; क्षमा शत्रौ च<BR>मित्रे च यतीनामेव भूषणं H. 2; R. 1. 22;<BR>18. 9; तेजः क्षमा वा नैकांतं कालज्ञस्य<BR>महीपतेः Śi. 2. 83.<BR>--2 The earth.<BR>--3<BR>An epithet of Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः<BR>the planet Mars.<BR>--भुज्, भुजः a king.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमावत्|क्षमावन्त्
क्षमावत्, क्षमान्वित, क्षमायुक्त a. Patient,<BR>indulgent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमान्वित
क्षमावत्, क्षमान्वित, क्षमायुक्त a. Patient,<BR>indulgent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमायुक्त
क्षमावत्, क्षमान्वित, क्षमायुक्त a. Patient,<BR>indulgent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमापयति
क्षमापयति Den. P. To ask any one's<BR>pardon, beg pardon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षमितृ
क्षमितृ a. (त्री f.), क्षमिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>1 Patient, forbearing, of a forgiving<BR>nature; कामं क्षाम्यतु यः क्षमी<BR>Śi. 2. 43; Y. 2. 200, 1. 133.<BR>--2<BR>Capable, able.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षांत|क्षान्त|क्षान्तः
क्षांत p. p. [क्षम्-क्त]<BR>1 Patient,<BR>forbearing, enduring.<BR>--2 Forgiven.<BR>--3 Borne, endured.<BR>--4 Friendly.<BR>--तः<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--तां The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षांतिः|क्षान्ति|क्षांति|क्षान्तिः
क्षांतिः f. [क्षम्-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>Patience, forbearance, forgiveness;<BR>क्षांतिश्चेद्वचनेन किं Bh. 2. 21;<BR>Bg. 18. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षांतु|क्षान्तु|क्षान्तुः
क्षांतु a. [क्षम्-तुन् वृद्धिश्च] Patient,<BR>forbearing.<BR>--तुः A father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाम्य
क्षाम्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be borne.<BR>--2<BR>To be pardoned or forgiven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षय|क्षयः
क्षय See under क्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर्
क्षर् {c1c} P. [क्षरति, क्षरित] (Used<BR>transitively or intransitively)<BR>1<BR>To flow, glide.<BR>--2 To send or stream<BR>forth, pour out, emit; R. 13. 74;<BR>Bk. 9. 8.<BR>--3 To drop, trickle, ooze.<BR>--4 To waste away, wane, perish.<BR>--5 To become useless, have no<BR>effect; यज्ञोऽनृतने क्षरति तपः क्षरति<BR>विस्मयात् Ms. 4. 237.<BR>--6 To melt.<BR>--7 To slip from, be deprived of (with<BR>abl.). --Caus. (क्षारयति-ते) To accuse,<BR>traduce (usually with आ). --WITH<BR>--वि to melt away, dissolve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षर|क्षरं|क्षरः
क्षर a. [क्षरति स्यंदते मुंचति वा, क्षर्-अच्]<BR>1 Melting away.<BR>--2 Moveable.<BR>--3<BR>Perishable; क्षरः सर्वाणि भूतानि<BR>कूटस्थोऽक्षर उच्यते Bg. 15. 16.<BR>--रः A cloud.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 The body.<BR>--3<BR>Ignorance.<BR>--4 The Supreme Being.<BR>--5 Cause and effect.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः<BR>a. (also क्षरेज) a. produced by<BR>distillation or from a cloud.<BR>--भाव a.<BR>mutable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरणं|क्षरण
क्षरणं [क्षर्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 The act of<BR>flowing, trickling, dropping, oozing.<BR>--2 The act of perspiring;<BR>अंगुलीक्षरणसन्नवर्तिकः R. 19. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरित
क्षरित p. p. Dropped, liquefied,<BR>oozed, melted &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षरिन्
क्षरिन् m. The rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षार|क्षारं|क्षारः
क्षार a. [क्षर्-ज्वला बा˚ ण]<BR>1<BR>Corrosive, caustic, acid, pungent, saline.<BR>--2 Flowing, oozing.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Juice,<BR>essence.<BR>--2 Treacle, molasses.<BR>--3<BR>Any corrosive or acid substance; क्षते<BR>क्षारमिवासह्यं जातं तस्यैव दर्शनं U. 4. 7;<BR>क्षारं क्षते प्रक्षिपन् Mk. 5. 18; (क्षारं क्षते<BR>क्षिप् &c. has become proverbial, and<BR>means ‘to aggravate the pain which<BR>is already unbearable,’ ‘to make<BR>bad worse’, ‘to add insult to<BR>injury’).<BR>--4 Glass.<BR>--5 Salt.<BR>--6 Ashes.<BR>--7 A rogue, cheat.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Black<BR>salt.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अच्छं<BR>sea-salt.<BR>--अंजनं an alkaline<BR>unguent.<BR>--अंबु n. an alkaline fluid.<BR>--उदः, --उदकः, --उदधिः, --समुद्रः the salt<BR>ocean.<BR>--कर्दमः {1} a pool of saline mud.<BR>{2} N. of a hell.<BR>--तैलं oil cooked with<BR>alkaline ingredients.<BR>--त्रयं, --त्रितयं<BR>natron, salt-petre and borax.<BR>--नदी<BR>a river of alkaline water in hell.<BR>--भूमिः f.,<BR>--मृत्तिका saline soil;<BR>किमाश्चर्यं क्षारभूमौ प्राणदा यमदूतिका Udb.<BR>--मेलकः an alkaline substance.<BR>--रसः a saline flavour.<BR>--श्रेष्ठं<BR>alkaline earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारकः|क्षारक
क्षारकः [क्षर्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 Alkali.<BR>--2<BR>Juice, essence.<BR>--3 A cage, basket or<BR>net for birds.<BR>--4 A washerman.<BR>--5<BR>A blossom; a bud or new-blown<BR>flower (कलिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारणं|क्षारण
क्षारणं, --णा Accusing, especially of<BR>adultery.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Converting to alkali<BR>or ashes.<BR>--2 Distilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारणा
क्षारणं, --णा Accusing, especially of<BR>adultery.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Converting to alkali<BR>or ashes.<BR>--2 Distilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारयति
क्षारयति Den. P.<BR>1 To furnish or<BR>mix with acid substances.<BR>--2 To<BR>torture a person with acid<BR>substances.<BR>--3 To speak ill of a person,<BR>accuse.<BR>--4 To abuse, calumniate,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">Page0436-a+ 54</a>]<BR>traduce^1, censure; cf. आक्षर्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0435-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारिका
क्षारिका Hunger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारित|क्षारितः
क्षारित a.<BR>1 Distilled from saline<BR>matter.<BR>--2 Falsely accused<BR>(especially of adultery).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षल्
क्षल् {c10c} U. (क्षालयति-ते, क्षालित)<BR>1<BR>To wash, wash off, purify, cleanse;<BR>ऋते रवेः क्षालयितुं क्षमेत कः<BR>क्षपातमस्कांडमलीमसं नभः Śi. 1. 38; H. 4. 60.<BR>--2 To wipe away. --WITH वि to<BR>wash off; R. 5. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाल
क्षाल a. Cleaning, washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालनं|क्षालन
क्षालनं [क्षल्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Washing,<BR>cleansing (with water).<BR>--2<BR>Sprinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालित|क्षालितं
क्षालित p. p. [क्षल्-क्त]<BR>1 Washed,<BR>cleansed, purified.<BR>--2 Wiped away,<BR>requited; तथा वृत्तं पापैर्व्यथयति यथा<BR>क्षालितमपि U. 1. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवः|क्षव
क्षवः, क्षवथुः See under क्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवथुः|क्षवथु
क्षवः, क्षवथुः See under क्षु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्र
क्षात्र a. (त्री f.) [क्षत्रस्य कर्म भावो<BR>वा अण्] Relating or peculiar to the<BR>military tribe; क्षात्रो धर्मः श्रित इव तनुं<BR>ब्रह्मघोषस्य गुप्त्यै U. 6. 9; R. 1. 13.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1 The Kṣatriya tribe.<BR>--2 The<BR>qualifications of a Kṣatriya; the<BR>Gītā thus describes them:<BR>--शौर्यं<BR>तेजो धृतिर्दाक्ष्यं युद्धे चाप्यपलायनं ।<BR>दानमीश्वरभावश्च क्षात्रं कर्म स्वभावजं Bg. 18. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षात्रिः|क्षात्रि
क्षात्रिः The son of a Kṣatriya by a<BR>woman of another caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षांत|क्षान्त|क्षान्तः
क्षांत &c. see under क्षम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षाम|क्षामः
क्षाम a. [क्षै-कर्तरि क्त]<BR>1 Scorched,<BR>singed.<BR>--2 Diminished, thin,<BR>wasted; emaciated, lean;<BR>क्षामक्षामकपोलमाननं Ś. 3. 10; मध्ये क्षामा Me. 82;<BR>क्षामच्छायं भवनमधुना मद्वियोगेन नूनं 80,<BR>89.<BR>--3 Slight, little, small.<BR>--4<BR>Weak, infirm.<BR>--मः An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--मा The earth.<BR>--मं<BR>Destruction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्यं<BR>unwholesome diet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामन्
क्षामन् a. [क्षै-मनिन्] Destructive.<BR>--n. Ved. The earth, ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षामवत्|क्षामवन्त्
क्षामवत् a. Ved. Scorching,<BR>withering, drying; an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षारः|क्षार|क्षारं
क्षारः &c. See under क्षर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षालनं|क्षालन
क्षालनं &c. See under क्षल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षि|क्षिः
क्षि {vI.v} {c1c} P. (क्षयति, क्षित or क्षीण)<BR>1 To decay or waste.<BR>--2 To rule,<BR>govern, be master of. {vII.v} {c1c} {c5c}<BR>{c9c} P. (क्षयति, क्षिणोति, क्षिणाति)<BR>1 To<BR>destroy, affect, ruin, corrupt;<BR>न तद्यशः शस्त्रभृतां क्षिणोति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-b" target="_blank">Page0436-b+ 56</a>]<BR>R. 2. 40.<BR>--2 To diminish, cause to waste<BR>away; R. 19. 48.<BR>--3 To kill, injure.<BR>--4 To spend, pass (as time); कति<BR>पुनरहं वासराणि क्षयिष्ये Ud. S. 83.<BR>{vIII.v} {c6c} P. (क्षियति)<BR>1 To abide,<BR>stay, dwell.<BR>--2 To inhabit.<BR>--3 To<BR>remain.<BR>--4 To go, move, approach.<BR>--Pass. (क्षीयते) To waste, wane;<BR>decay, be diminished (fig. also)<BR>प्रतिक्षणमयं कायः क्षीयमाणो न लक्ष्यते<BR>H. 4. 66; प्रत्यासन्नविपत्तिमूढमनसां<BR>प्रायो मतिः क्षीयते Pt. 2. 4; Amaru. 93;<BR>Bh. 2. 19. --Caus. (क्षययति or<BR>क्षपयति)<BR>1 To destroy, remove, put an<BR>end to; ममापि च क्षपयतु नीललोहितः<BR>पुनर्भवं परिगतशक्तिरात्मभूः Ś. 7. 35,<BR>R. 8. 47; Me. 53.<BR>--2 To spend or<BR>pass (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयः|क्षय
क्षयः [क्षि-अच्]<BR>1 A house, residence,<BR>abode; यातनाश्च यमक्षये Ms. 6. 61;<BR>निर्जगाम पुनस्तस्मात्क्षयान्नारायणस्य ह<BR>Mb.<BR>--2 Loss, decline, waste, wane,<BR>decay, diminution; आयुषः क्षयः<BR>R. 3. 69; धनक्षये वर्धति जाठराग्निः<BR>Pt. 2. 178; so चंद्रक्षयः, क्षयपक्षः &c.<BR>--3<BR>Destruction, end, termination;<BR>निशाक्षये याति ह्रियैव पांडुतां Rs. 1. 9;<BR>Amaru. 60.<BR>--4 Pecuniary loss;<BR>Ms. 8. 401.<BR>--5 Fall (as of prices.)<BR>--6<BR>Removal.<BR>--7 Universal destruction<BR>(प्रलय).<BR>--8 Consumption.<BR>--9 A disease<BR>in general.<BR>--10 The negative sign or<BR>quantity, minus (in algebra).<BR>--11<BR>Family, race.<BR>--12 The house of<BR>Yama.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर (also क्षयंकर)<BR>a. causing decay or destruction,<BR>ruinous.<BR>--कालः {1} time of<BR>universal destruction. {2} the period of<BR>decline.<BR>--कासः consumptive cough.<BR>--पक्षः the dark fortnight.<BR>--युक्तिः<BR>f.,<BR>--योगः an opportunity of<BR>destroying.<BR>--रोगः consumption.<BR>--वायुः<BR>the wind that is to blow at the<BR>destruction of the world.<BR>--संपद् f.<BR>total loss, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयण|क्षयणः
क्षयण a. Destroying &c.<BR>--णः<BR>1 A<BR>place with calm water.<BR>--2 A bay or<BR>harbour.<BR>--णं A dwelling-place,<BR>habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयथुः|क्षयथु
क्षयथुः Consumptive cough,<BR>consumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयस्
क्षयस् n. A dwelling-place,<BR>habitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिन्
क्षयिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>1 Diminishing,<BR>decaying; आरंभगुर्वी क्षयिणी क्रमेण<BR>Bh. 2. 60; waning, wasting; न<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-c" target="_blank">Page0436-c+ 56</a>]<BR>चाभूत्ताविव क्षयी R. 17. 71 Ms. 9. 314.<BR>--2<BR>Consumptive.<BR>--3 Perishable, fragile.<BR>--m. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षयिष्णु
क्षयिष्णु a.<BR>1 Wasting, decaying.<BR>--2 Perishable, fragile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिः|क्षि
क्षिः f.<BR>1 Abode.<BR>--2 Going.<BR>--3<BR>Destruction.<BR>--4 Waste, loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्
क्षित् a.<BR>1 Ruling, a ruler.<BR>--2<BR>Dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित|क्षितः
क्षित p. p. [क्षि-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1 Wasted,<BR>decayed, lost.<BR>--2 Weakened.<BR>--3 Poor,<BR>miserable.<BR>--तं Killing; injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिता
क्षिता The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षितिः|क्षिति
क्षितिः f. [क्षि निवासे आधारे क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>The earth.<BR>--2 A dwelling, an abode,<BR>a house.<BR>--3 Loss, destruction.<BR>--4<BR>The end of the world.<BR>--5 Wane.<BR>--6 A man (Ved.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदितिः<BR>an epithet of Devakī, mother of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--ईशः, --ईश्वरः a king;<BR>R. 1. 5; 3. 3; 11. 1.<BR>--कणः dust.<BR>--कंपः<BR>an earthquake.<BR>--क्षित् m. a king,<BR>prince.<BR>--जः {1} a tree. {2} an<BR>earthworm. {3} the planet Mars. {4} N.<BR>of the demon Naraka killed by<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--(जं) the horizon.<BR>--(जा)<BR>an epithet of Sītā.<BR>--तलं the<BR>surface of the earth.<BR>--देवः a<BR>Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--धरः a mountain; Ku. 7. 94.<BR>--धेनुः earth considered as a<BR>milchcow; Bh. 2. 46.<BR>--नाथः, --पः, --पतिः,<BR>--पालः, --भुज् m.,<BR>--रक्षिन् m. a king,<BR>sovereign; R. 2. 51, 5. 76, 6. 86,<BR>7. 3, 9. 75.<BR>--पुत्रः {1} the planet Mars.<BR>{2} the demon Naraka.<BR>--प्रतिष्ठ a.<BR>dwelling on the earth.<BR>--भृत् m. {1}<BR>a mountain; सर्वक्षितिभृतां नाथ<BR>V. 4. 27; (where it means ‘a king’ also);<BR>Ki. 5. 20; Rs. 6. 26. {2} a king.<BR>--मंडलं the globe.<BR>--रंध्रं a ditch,<BR>hollow.<BR>--रुह् m. a tree.<BR>--वर्धनः m.<BR>a corpse, dead body.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. ‘the<BR>course of the earth’, patient<BR>behaviour.<BR>--व्युदासः a cave within the<BR>earth, an underground hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षित्वन्
क्षित्वन् m. Wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीण|क्षीणः
क्षीण p. p. [क्षि-क्त]<BR>1 Thin,<BR>emaciated, waned, become lean,<BR>diminished, worn away, expended; भार्यां<BR>क्षीणेषु वित्तेषु (जानीयात्) H. 1. 72; so क्षीणः.<BR>शशी; क्षीणे पुण्ये मर्त्यलोके विशंति.<BR>--2<BR>Slender, delicate.<BR>--3 Small, little.<BR>--4 Poor, miserable.<BR>--5 Powerless,<BR>weak.<BR>--6 Wasted away, decreased,<BR>lost, diminished.<BR>--7 Dead, destroyed;<BR>अक्षीणभक्तिः क्षीणेऽपि नंदे Mu. 2. 21,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-a" target="_blank">Page0437-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--8 Injured, broken, torn.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चंद्रः the moon on the wane.<BR>--धन<BR>a. reduced to poverty,<BR>impoverished.<BR>--पाप a. one who is purified<BR>after having suffered the<BR>consequences of sin.<BR>--पुण्य a. one who<BR>has enjoyed all his stock of merit,<BR>and must work to acquire more in<BR>another birth.<BR>--मध्य a.<BR>slenderwaisted.<BR>--वासिन् a. inhabiting a<BR>dilapidated house. (m.) a dove or<BR>pigeon.<BR>--विक्रांत a. destitute of<BR>courage or prowess.<BR>--वृत्ति a.<BR>deprived of the means of support, out of<BR>employ.<BR>--शक्ति, --बल a. weakened in<BR>strength, subsided (as a disease);<BR>Pt. 1. 235.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0436-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिण्
क्षिण् {c5c} U. (क्षिणोति-क्षिणुते, क्षित) To<BR>kill, hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिद्रः|क्षिद्र
क्षिद्रः [क्षिद्-रक]<BR>1 A disease.<BR>--2<BR>The sun.<BR>--3 A horn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्
क्षिप् {c6c} U. (but only P. when<BR>preceded by अधि, प्रति and अति), {4}<BR>P. (क्षिपति-ते, क्षिप्यति, क्षिप्त)<BR>1 To<BR>throw, cast, send, dispatch,<BR>discharge, let go (with loc. or<BR>sometimes dat.); मरुद्भ्य इति तु द्वारि<BR>क्षिपेदप्स्वद्भ्य इत्यपि Ms. 3. 88; शिलां वा<BR>क्षेप्स्यते मयि Mb.; R. 12. 95; with प्रति<BR>also; Bh. 3. 67, Śi. 15. 86.<BR>--2 To<BR>place, put on or upon, throw into,<BR>स्रजमपि शिरस्यंधः क्षिप्तां धुनोत्यहिशंकया<BR>Ś. 7. 24; Y. 1. 230; Bg. 16. 19.<BR>--3 To fix on, attach to (as a blame);<BR>भृत्ये दोषान् क्षिपति H. 2.<BR>--4 To cast<BR>or throw off, cast away, rid oneself<BR>of; किं कूर्मस्य भरव्यथा न वपुषि क्ष्मां न<BR>क्षिपत्येष यत् Mu. 2. 18.<BR>--5 (a) To take<BR>away, destroy; Māl. 1. 17. (b) To kill<BR>or slay; केसरी निष्ठुरक्षिप्तमृगयूथो<BR>मृगाधिपः Śi. 2. 53.<BR>--6 To reject, disdain.<BR>--7 To insult, revile, abuse, scold;<BR>Ms. 8. 312, 270; Śānti. 3. 10.<BR>--8<BR>To pour on, scatter, strew.<BR>--9<BR>To strike, hit.<BR>--10 To distract,<BR>afflict; Māl. 4. 8. --WITH पर्या<BR>to bind or tie up, collect<BR>(as hair); (केशांतं) पर्याक्षिपत्<BR>काचिदुदारबंधं Ku. 7. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्
क्षिप् f. Ved. A finger;<BR>Rv. 3. 23. 3, 9. 97. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप|क्षिपः
क्षिप a. [क्षिप्-क] Throwing,<BR>striking, hitting.<BR>--पः<BR>1 Throwing,<BR>casting.<BR>--2 Reviling, insulting.<BR>--पा<BR>1<BR>Sending.<BR>--2 Throwing.<BR>--3 Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपकः|क्षिपक
क्षिपकः An archer, a warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणं|क्षिपण
क्षिपणं [क्षिप् भावे बा˚ क्युन्]<BR>1<BR>Sending, throwing, casting.<BR>--2 Reviling,<BR>abusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणिः|क्षिपणि
क्षिपणिः, --णी f.<BR>1 An oar.<BR>--2 A<BR>priest.<BR>--3 A net.<BR>--4 A weapon.<BR>--णिः<BR>A stroke with a whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणी
क्षिपणिः, --णी f.<BR>1 An oar.<BR>--2 A<BR>priest.<BR>--3 A net.<BR>--4 A weapon.<BR>--णिः<BR>A stroke with a whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपणुः|क्षिपणु
क्षिपणुः [क्षिप्-अनुङ्]<BR>1 An archer.<BR>--2<BR>A weapon.<BR>--3 Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपण्यु|क्षिपण्युः
क्षिपण्यु a. [क्षिप्-कन्युच्]<BR>1 Fragrant,<BR>sweet-smelling.<BR>--2 Diffusive.<BR>--ण्युः<BR>1 The body.<BR>--2 The spring season.<BR>--3 A fragrant smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपतिः|क्षिपति
क्षिपतिः(स्तिः) Ved. The arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिपस्तिः|क्षिपस्ति
क्षिपतिः(स्तिः) Ved. The arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्त|क्षिप्तः
क्षिप्त p. p. [क्षिप्-क्त]<BR>1 Thrown,<BR>scattered, hurled, cast.<BR>--2<BR>Abandoned.<BR>--3 Disregarded, neglected,<BR>disrespected.<BR>--4 Placed.<BR>--5 Distracted,<BR>mad; (see क्षिप्).<BR>--प्ता Night.<BR>--प्तं A<BR>wound caused by shooting.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कुक्कुरः a mad dog.<BR>--चित्त a.<BR>distracted in mind, absent-minded.<BR>--देह a. prostrating the body, lying<BR>down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्तिः|क्षिप्ति
क्षिप्तिः f. [क्षिप्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Throwing,<BR>sending forth.<BR>--2 Explaining a<BR>hidden meaning (such as solving<BR>riddles).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्नु|क्षिप्नुः
क्षिप्नु a.<BR>1 Throwing, casting.<BR>--2<BR>Killing; रक्षोगणं क्षिप्तुं Bk. 2. 21;<BR>Śi. 16. 50.<BR>--3 Obstructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिप्र|क्षिप्रं
क्षिप्र a. [क्षिप्-रक्] (compar. क्षेपीयस्;<BR>superl. क्षेपिष्ठ)<BR>1 Elastic (as a bow).<BR>--2 Quick, speedy.<BR>--प्रं<BR>1 A<BR>measure of time = (1/15) of a Muhūrta.<BR>--2<BR>The part of the hand between the<BR>thumb and the forefinger.<BR>--प्रं ind.<BR>Quickly, speedily, immediately;<BR>विनाशं व्रजति क्षिप्रमामपात्रमिवांभसि<BR>Ms. 3. 179; Śānti. 3. 6; Bk. 2. 44.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारिन् a. acting quickly,<BR>prompt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपः|क्षेप
क्षेपः [क्षिप्-घञ्]<BR>1 Throwing,<BR>tossing, casting, moving about,<BR>movement (of limbs); कुंदक्षेपानुगम<BR>Me. 47; भ्रूक्षेपमात्रानुमतप्रवेशां Ku. 3. 60.<BR>--2 A throw, cast.<BR>--3 Sending,<BR>dispatching.<BR>--4 Depression; striking<BR>down.<BR>--5 Transgressing.<BR>--6 Passing<BR>away (time); कालक्षेपः.<BR>--7 Delay,<BR>dilatoriness.<BR>--8 Insult, abuse; क्षेपं<BR>करोति चेद्दंड्यः Y. 2. 204; किं क्षेपे.<BR>--9<BR>Disrespect, contempt.<BR>--10 Pride,<BR>haughtiness.<BR>--11 A nosegay.<BR>--12 A<BR>stroke (of an oar &c).<BR>--13 Laying<BR>on (as a paint &c.), besmearing.<BR>--14<BR>(in arith.) Addendum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपक|क्षेपकः
क्षेपक a. [क्षिप्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A thrower,<BR>sender.<BR>--2 Interpolated, inserted<BR>(as a passage).<BR>--3 Abusive,<BR>disrespectful.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A spurious or<BR>interpolated passage.<BR>--2 An additive<BR>quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपणं|क्षेपण
क्षेपणं [क्षिप्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Throwing,<BR>casting, sending, directing &c.<BR>--2<BR>Spending (as time).<BR>--3 Omitting.<BR>--4 Abusing.<BR>--5 A sling.<BR>--णिः, --णी<BR>f.<BR>1 An oar.<BR>--2 A net for fishing.<BR>--3 A sling or any instrument with<BR>which missiles are thrown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपणीय|क्षेपणीयं
क्षेपणीय a. [क्षिप्-अनीयर्] To be<BR>thrown or cast.<BR>--यं A sling, any<BR>instrument for casting missiles,<BR>stones &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेपिमन्
क्षेपिमन् m. Great velocity, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप्तृ
क्षेप्तृ a. A thrower, caster, sender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप्य
क्षेप्य a. To be thrown or cast &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिया
क्षिया<BR>1 Loss, destruction, waste,<BR>decay.<BR>--2 An impropriety, offence<BR>against established customs (<BR>आचारभेद); the following is an instance;<BR>स्वयमह रथेन याति उपाध्यायं पदातिं<BR>गमयति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षिव्
क्षिव् {c1c} {c4c} P. (क्षेवति or क्षीव्यति) To<BR>eject from the mouth, vomit, spit<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षी
क्षी {c1c} U. (क्षयति-ते) To kill,<BR>injure, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीज्
क्षीज् {c1c} P. (क्षीजति) To sound<BR>indistinctly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीजनं|क्षीजन
क्षीजनं [क्षीज् भावे ल्युट्] The<BR>whistling of hollow reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीण|क्षीणः
क्षीण See under क्षि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीब्
क्षीब्, क्षीब See क्षीब्, क्षीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीब|क्षीबः
क्षीब्, क्षीब See क्षीब्, क्षीव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरः|क्षीर
क्षीरः, रं<BR>1 Milk; हंसो हि<BR>क्षीरमादत्ते तन्मिश्रा वर्जयत्यपः Ś. 6. 27.<BR>--2<BR>The milky juice or sap of trees,<BR>exudation; resin; ये<BR>तत्क्षीरस्रुतिसुरभयो दक्षिणेन प्रवृत्ताः Me. 107; Ku. 1. 9.<BR>--3 Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदः an<BR>infant, a sucking child.<BR>--अब्धिः the<BR>sea of milk. ˚जः {1} the moon. {2}<BR>the Amṛta or nectar produced<BR>at the churning of the sea. {3} an<BR>epithet of Śeṣa. {4} a pearl. ˚जं<BR>sea-salt. ˚जा, ˚तनया an epithet of<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR>--आह्वः the pine tree.<BR>--उदः the sea of milk; क्षीरोदवेलेव<BR>सफेनपुंजा Ku. 7. 26. ˚तनयः, ˚नंदनः<BR>the moon. ˚तनया, ˚सुता an epithet<BR>of Lakṣmī.<BR>--उदधि = क्षीरोद q. v.<BR>above.<BR>--ऊर्मिः a wave of the sea<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">Page0438-a+ 57</a>]<BR>of milk; R. 4. 27.<BR>--ओदनः rice boiled<BR>with milk;<BR>--कंठः, कंठकः a young child<BR>(having milk in the throat); त्वया<BR>तत्क्षीरकंठेन प्राप्तमारण्यकं व्रतं<BR>Mv. 4. 52, 5. 11.<BR>--जं coagulated milk.<BR>--दात्री yielding milk (as a cow).<BR>--द्रुमः the Aśvattha tree.<BR>--धात्री<BR>a wet-nurse.<BR>--धिः, --निधिः the sea<BR>of milk; इंदुः क्षीरनिधाविव R. 1. 12.<BR>--धेनुः f. a milch cow.<BR>--नीरं {1}<BR>water and milk. {2} milk-like water.<BR>{3} a fast embrace.<BR>--पः a child.<BR>--पाणः an inhabitant of Uśīnara.<BR>--(णं, --नं) drinking milk.<BR>--(णी)<BR>any vessel out of which milk is<BR>drunk.<BR>--भृत a. supported by milk<BR>(as a Gopāla).<BR>--वारिः, --वारिधिः the<BR>sea of milk.<BR>--विकृतिः f. inspissated<BR>milk.<BR>--वृक्षः {1} N. of the four trees<BR>न्यग्रोध, उदुंबर, अश्वत्थ and मधूक. {2}<BR>the glomerous fig-tree.<BR>--शरः cream,<BR>the skim of milk.<BR>--समुद्रः the sea<BR>of milk.<BR>--सारः butter; क्षीरसारमपनीय<BR>शंकया स्वीकृतं यदि पलायनं त्वया Udb.<BR>--स्निग्ध a. unctuous with milky<BR>juice or sap; Ś. 3. 6.<BR>--स्फटिकः a<BR>precious stone.<BR>--स्वामिन् m. a<BR>commentator on the Amarakoṣa.<BR>--हिंडीरः<BR>the foam of milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रं|र|रः
क्षीरः, रं<BR>1 Milk; हंसो हि<BR>क्षीरमादत्ते तन्मिश्रा वर्जयत्यपः Ś. 6. 27.<BR>--2<BR>The milky juice or sap of trees,<BR>exudation; resin; ये<BR>तत्क्षीरस्रुतिसुरभयो दक्षिणेन प्रवृत्ताः Me. 107; Ku. 1. 9.<BR>--3 Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदः an<BR>infant, a sucking child.<BR>--अब्धिः the<BR>sea of milk. ˚जः {1} the moon. {2}<BR>the Amṛta or nectar produced<BR>at the churning of the sea. {3} an<BR>epithet of Śeṣa. {4} a pearl. ˚जं<BR>sea-salt. ˚जा, ˚तनया an epithet of<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR>--आह्वः the pine tree.<BR>--उदः the sea of milk; क्षीरोदवेलेव<BR>सफेनपुंजा Ku. 7. 26. ˚तनयः, ˚नंदनः<BR>the moon. ˚तनया, ˚सुता an epithet<BR>of Lakṣmī.<BR>--उदधि = क्षीरोद q. v.<BR>above.<BR>--ऊर्मिः a wave of the sea<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">Page0438-a+ 57</a>]<BR>of milk; R. 4. 27.<BR>--ओदनः rice boiled<BR>with milk;<BR>--कंठः, कंठकः a young child<BR>(having milk in the throat); त्वया<BR>तत्क्षीरकंठेन प्राप्तमारण्यकं व्रतं<BR>Mv. 4. 52, 5. 11.<BR>--जं coagulated milk.<BR>--दात्री yielding milk (as a cow).<BR>--द्रुमः the Aśvattha tree.<BR>--धात्री<BR>a wet-nurse.<BR>--धिः, --निधिः the sea<BR>of milk; इंदुः क्षीरनिधाविव R. 1. 12.<BR>--धेनुः f. a milch cow.<BR>--नीरं {1}<BR>water and milk. {2} milk-like water.<BR>{3} a fast embrace.<BR>--पः a child.<BR>--पाणः an inhabitant of Uśīnara.<BR>--(णं, --नं) drinking milk.<BR>--(णी)<BR>any vessel out of which milk is<BR>drunk.<BR>--भृत a. supported by milk<BR>(as a Gopāla).<BR>--वारिः, --वारिधिः the<BR>sea of milk.<BR>--विकृतिः f. inspissated<BR>milk.<BR>--वृक्षः {1} N. of the four trees<BR>न्यग्रोध, उदुंबर, अश्वत्थ and मधूक. {2}<BR>the glomerous fig-tree.<BR>--शरः cream,<BR>the skim of milk.<BR>--समुद्रः the sea<BR>of milk.<BR>--सारः butter; क्षीरसारमपनीय<BR>शंकया स्वीकृतं यदि पलायनं त्वया Udb.<BR>--स्निग्ध a. unctuous with milky<BR>juice or sap; Ś. 3. 6.<BR>--स्फटिकः a<BR>precious stone.<BR>--स्वामिन् m. a<BR>commentator on the Amarakoṣa.<BR>--हिंडीरः<BR>the foam of milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0437-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरयति
क्षीरयति Den. P. To look like<BR>milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिका
क्षीरिका A dish prepared with milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरिन्
क्षीरिन् a.<BR>1 Milky.<BR>--2 Yielding<BR>milk; क्षीरिण्यः संतु गावः Mk. 10. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीरेयी
क्षीरेयी An oblation of milk, rice,<BR>and sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीव्
क्षीव् {c1c} {c4c} P. [क्षीवति, क्षीव्यति]<BR>1<BR>To be drunk or intoxicated.<BR>--2 To<BR>spit, eject from the mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षीव|क्षीवः
क्षीव a. Excited, drunk,<BR>intoxicated; ध्रुवं जये यस्य जयामृतेन क्षीवः<BR>क्षमाभर्तुरभूत्कृपाणः Vikr. 1. 96; क्षीवो<BR>दुःशासनासृजा Ve. 5. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षु|क्षुः
क्षु {c2c} P. [क्षौति, क्षुत]<BR>1 To sneeze;<BR>अपयाति सरोषया निरस्ते कृतकं कामिनि<BR>चुक्षुवे मृगाक्ष्या Śi. 9. 83; Ch. P. 10;<BR>Bk. 14. 75.<BR>--2 To cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवः|क्षव
क्षवः [क्षु-भावादौ अप्]<BR>1 Sneezing.<BR>--2 Cough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवकं|क्षवक|क्षवकः
क्षवकं A kind of potherb.<BR>--विका<BR>1 A species of rice.<BR>--2 A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षवथुः|क्षवथु
क्षवथुः [क्षु-अथुच्]<BR>1 Sneezing.<BR>--2<BR>Cough.<BR>--3 Irritation of the throat.<BR>--4 Sore throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुत्
क्षुत् f., क्षुतं --ता, --तिः f. A sneeze or<BR>sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुः|क्षु
क्षुः Ved.<BR>1 Food.<BR>--2 A lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण्ण|क्षुण्णं
क्षुण्ण See under क्षुद् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्
क्षुद् {c7c} U. (क्षुणत्ति, क्षुंते, क्षुण्ण)<BR>1 To<BR>tread or trample upon, strike<BR>against, crush (under the foot),<BR>bruise, pound down; क्षुणद्मि सर्पान्<BR>पाताले Bk. 6. 36; ते तं व्याशिषताक्षौत्सुः<BR>पादैर्दंतैस्तथाच्छिदन् 15. 43, 17. 66.<BR>--2 To move, be agitated (A.).<BR>--WITH प्र to crush, bruise, pound;<BR>मित्रघ्नस्य प्रचुक्षोद गदयांगं बिभीषणः<BR>Bk. 14. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण्ण|क्षुण्णं
क्षुण्ण p. p. [क्षुद्-क्त]<BR>1 Pounded,<BR>crushed to pieces, bruised.<BR>--2<BR>Powdered, pulverized, ground.<BR>--3<BR>Beaten, trodden (as a path);<BR>R. 1. 17.<BR>--4 (Fig.) Practised, followed;<BR>क्षुद्रजनक्षुण्ण एष मार्गः K. 146; अ˚<BR>unusual; Māl. 3.<BR>--5 Violated (a vow).<BR>--6 Exercised, practised, skilful.<BR>--7<BR>One versed in the sacred science<BR>but unable to teach it.<BR>--8<BR>Overcome, defeated.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मनस् a.<BR>penitent, repentant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुण्णकः|क्षुण्णक
क्षुण्णकः A kind of drum beaten<BR>at a funeral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्
क्षुद् f. Grinding, crushing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुदः|क्षुद
क्षुदः Flour, meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्र|क्षुद्रः
क्षुद्र a. [क्षुद्-कर्तरि रक्] (compar.<BR>क्षोदीयस्; superl. क्षोदिष्ठ)<BR>1 Minute,<BR>small, tiny, little, trifling.<BR>--2 Mean,<BR>low, vile, base; क्षुद्रेऽपि नूनं शरणं<BR>प्रपन्ने Ku. 1. 12.<BR>--3 Wicked.<BR>--4 Cruel.<BR>--5 Poor, indigent.<BR>--6 Miserly,<BR>niggardly; Me. 17.<BR>--7 Diminutive,<BR>short.<BR>--8 Trifling, insignificant.<BR>--9<BR>Unimportant, minor.<BR>--द्रः<BR>1 A<BR>small particle of rice.<BR>--2 A bee or<BR>wasp.<BR>--द्रा<BR>1 A bee.<BR>--2 A fly or<BR>gnat.<BR>--3 A woman maimed or<BR>crippled.<BR>--4 A quarrelsome woman.<BR>--5<BR>A prostitute, whore, harlot; उपसृष्टा<BR>इव क्षुद्राधिष्ठितभवनाः K. 107.<BR>--6 A<BR>base or despicable woman.<BR>--7 A<BR>dancing girl.<BR>--द्रं Ved. A particle<BR>of dust, flour, meal.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजनं a kind of unguent applied to<BR>the eyes in certain diseases.<BR>--अंत्रः<BR>the small cavity of the heart.<BR>--उलूकः a small owl.<BR>--कंबुः a small shell.<BR>--कुलिशः a precious stone.<BR>--कुष्ठं<BR>a mild form of leprosy.<BR>--घंटिका<BR>{1} small bell. {2} a girdle of small<BR>bells.<BR>--चंदनं red sandal-wood.<BR>--जंतुः<BR>any small animal.<BR>--तंडुलः a grain<BR>of rice.<BR>--दंशिका a small gadfly.<BR>--बुद्धि a. low-minded, mean.<BR>--रसः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">Page0438-c+ 56</a>]<BR>honey.<BR>--रोगः a minor disease;<BR>(44 are enumerated by Suśruta).<BR>--शंखः a small conch-shell.<BR>--सुवर्णं<BR>low or bad gold; i. e. brass.<BR>--हन् m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रता
क्षुद्रता, --त्वं Smallness,<BR>insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रत्वं|क्षुद्रत्व
क्षुद्रता, --त्वं Smallness,<BR>insignificance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रल
क्षुद्रल a. Minute, small (applied<BR>especially to diseases and animals).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्रिका
क्षुद्रिका<BR>1 A small gadfly.<BR>--2 Small<BR>bells (for ornaments).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोत्तृ
क्षोत्तृ m. A pestle, implement for<BR>grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदः|क्षोद
क्षोदः [क्षुट्-घञ्]<BR>1 Pounding,<BR>grinding.<BR>--2 The stone on which<BR>anything is ground or powdered, a<BR>mortar.<BR>--3 Any ground substance, flour.<BR>--4 Dust, particle, any small or<BR>minute particle; U. 3. 2.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्षम a. capable of standing a test,<BR>scrutiny or investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदस्
क्षोदस् n. [क्षुद्-असुन्] Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदित|क्षोदितं
क्षोदित a. [क्षुद्-णिच्-क्त] Pounded,<BR>ground.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Powder, dust.<BR>--2<BR>Flour, any ground substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोदिमन्
क्षोदिमन् m. Minutness, smallness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुध्
क्षुध् {c4c} P. (क्षुध्यति, क्षुधित) To be<BR>hungry; Bk. 5. 66, 6. 44, 9. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुद्
क्षुद् f. क्षुधा<BR>1 Hunger; सीदति क्षुधा<BR>Ms. 7. 134, 4. 187.<BR>--2 Food.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वित, --आर्त, --आविष्ट a. afflicted<BR>by hunger.<BR>--क्षाम a. emaciated by<BR>hunger; Bh. 2. 29.<BR>--पिपासित a.<BR>hungry and thirsty.<BR>--निवृत्तिः f.<BR>cessation of hunger, appeasing of<BR>appetite (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधालु
क्षुधालु a. Hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधित|क्षुधितः
क्षुधित a. Hungry; R. 2. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुधुनः|क्षुधुन
क्षुधुनः N. of a savage race, the<BR>Mlecchas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुपः|क्षुप
क्षुपः A tree with small roots<BR>and branches, a shrub, bush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभ्
क्षुभ् {c1c} A., {c4c} {c9c} P. (क्षोभते,<BR>क्षुभ्यति, क्षुभ्नाति, क्षुभित-क्षुब्ध)<BR>1 To<BR>shake, tremble, to be agitated<BR>or disturbed; महाह्रद इव क्षुभ्यन्<BR>Bk. 9. 118; R. 4. 21;<BR>Śi. 8. 24.<BR>--2 To be unsteady.<BR>--3 To stumble<BR>(fig. also). --Caus. (क्षोभयति) To<BR>agitate, stir up, excite, perturb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभ्
क्षुभ् f. Ved. A blow, push.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभ|क्षुभः
क्षुभ a. [क्षुभ्-क] Exciting,<BR>agitating &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुभित|क्षुभितः
क्षुभित a.<BR>1 Shaken, agitated &c.;<BR>महाप्रलयमारुतक्षुभितपुष्करावर्तक &c.;<BR>Ve. 3. 2.<BR>--2 Afraid.<BR>--3 Enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0438-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुब्ध|क्षुब्धः
क्षुब्ध p. p.<BR>1 Agitated, shaken,<BR>unsteady.<BR>--2 Disturbed.<BR>--3 Afraid.<BR>--ब्धः<BR>1 A churning stick; शोभैव<BR>मंदरक्षुब्धक्षुभितांभोधिवर्णना Śi. 2. 107.<BR>--2<BR>A particular mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभः|क्षोभ
क्षोभः [क्षुभ्-घञ्]<BR>1 Shaking,<BR>moving, tossing; Me. 28, 95; so<BR>काननक्षोभः &c.<BR>--2 Jolting; R. 1. 58;<BR>V. 3. 11.<BR>--3 (a) Agitation,<BR>disturbance, excitement, emotion; क्षोक˚<BR>U. 3, 3. 29; स्वयंवरक्षोभकृतामभावः<BR>R. 7. 3; अथेंद्रियक्षोभमयुग्मनेत्रः<BR>पुनर्वशित्वाद्बलवन्निगृह्य Ku. 3. 69. (b)<BR>Provocation, irritation; प्रायः स्वं<BR>महिमानं क्षोभात्प्रतिपद्यते जंतुः Ś. 6. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभणं|क्षोभण|क्षोभणः
क्षोभणं [क्षुभ्-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>1 Agitating,<BR>disturbing.<BR>--णः One of the five<BR>arrows of Kāmadeva.<BR>--2 An epithet<BR>of (a) Viṣṇu, (b) Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुमा
क्षुमा<BR>1 Linseed, a kind of flax.<BR>--2<BR>The Indigo plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुर्
क्षुर् {c6c} P. (क्षुरति, क्षुरित)<BR>1 To cut,<BR>scratch.<BR>--2 To make lines or<BR>furrows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरः|क्षुर
क्षुरः [क्षुर्-क]<BR>1 A razor;<BR>R. 7. 46; Ms. 9. 292.<BR>--2 A razor-like<BR>barb attached to an arrow.<BR>--3 The<BR>hoof of a cow or horse.<BR>--4 An arrow.<BR>--5 The foot of a bedstead.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n.<BR>--क्रिया the act of<BR>shaving; Pt. 1. 386.<BR>--चतुष्टयं the<BR>four things necessary for shaving.<BR>--धानं, --भांडं a razor-case.<BR>--धार a.<BR>as sharp as a razor.<BR>--प्रः {1} an arrow<BR>with a sharp horse-shoe-shaped head;<BR>तं क्षुरप्रशकलीकृतं कृती R. 11. 29; 9. 62.<BR>{2} a sort of hoe, a weeding-spade.<BR>--मर्दिन्, मुंडिन् m. a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरिका
क्षुरिका, क्षुरी<BR>1 A knife, dagger.<BR>--2 A small razor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरी
क्षुरिका, क्षुरी<BR>1 A knife, dagger.<BR>--2 A small razor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरिणी
क्षुरिणी The wife of a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुरिन्
क्षुरिन् m. A barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्ल|क्षुल्लः
क्षुल्ल a. Small, little.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तातः<BR>the younger brother of one's father;<BR>cf. खुल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षुल्लक|क्षुल्लकः
क्षुल्लक a.<BR>1 Little, minute.<BR>--2 Low,<BR>vile.<BR>--3 Insignificant.<BR>--4 Wicked,<BR>malicious.<BR>--5 Poor.<BR>--6 Pained,<BR>distressed.<BR>--7 Hard<BR>--8 Young.<BR>--कः A<BR>small shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रं|क्षेत्र
क्षेत्रं [क्षि-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>1 A field, ground,<BR>soil; चीयते बालिशस्यापि सत्क्षेत्रपतिता<BR>कृषिः Mu. 1. 3.<BR>--2 Landed property,<BR>land.<BR>--3 Place, abode, region,<BR>repository; कपटशतमयं क्षेत्रमप्रत्ययानां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-b" target="_blank">Page0439-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Pt. 1. 191; Bh. 1. 77; Me. 16.<BR>--4<BR>A sacred spot, a place of pilgrimage;<BR>क्षेत्रं क्षत्रप्रधनपिशुनं कौरवं तद्भजेथाः<BR>Me. 48; Bg. 1. 1.<BR>--5 An enclosed spot<BR>of ground, portion of space,<BR>superficies, circuit.<BR>--6 Fertile soil.<BR>--7 Place<BR>of origin.<BR>--8 A wife; अपि नाम<BR>कुलपतेरियमसवर्णक्षेत्रसंभवा स्यात् Ś. 1;<BR>Ms. 3. 175.<BR>--9 The sphere of action, the<BR>body (regarded as the field of the<BR>working of the soul); योगिनो यं<BR>विचिन्वंति क्षेत्राभ्यंतरवर्तिनं Ku. 6. 77;<BR>Bg. 13. 1, 2, 3.<BR>--10 The mind.<BR>--11<BR>A house; a town.<BR>--12 A plane figure,<BR>as a triangle.<BR>--13 A diagram.<BR>--14<BR>A sign of the zodiac.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिदेवता the tutelary deity of any sacred<BR>piece of ground.<BR>--आजीवः, --करः,<BR>--कृत् m. a cultivator, peasant.<BR>--गणितं<BR>geometry.<BR>--गत a. geometrical.<BR>˚उपपत्तिः f. geometrical proof.<BR>--ज<BR>a. {1} produced in a field. {2} born<BR>from the body.<BR>--(जः) one of the 12<BR>kinds of sons allowed by the old<BR>Hindu Law, the offspring of a wife by<BR>a kinsman duly appointed to raise<BR>up issue to the husband; Ms. 9. 167,<BR>180; Y. 1. 69, 2. 128.<BR>--जात a.<BR>begotten on the wife of another.<BR>--ज्ञ a. {1} knowing places. {2}<BR>clever, dexterous.<BR>--(ज्ञः) {1} the soul;<BR>cf. Bg. 13. 1, 3; Ms. 12. 12. {2} the<BR>supreme soul. {3} a libertine. {4} a<BR>husbandman. {5} a form of Śiva. {6}<BR>a witness.<BR>--(ज्ञा) a girl fifteen years<BR>old personating Durgā at a festival.<BR>--पतिः a land-owner, a landlord.<BR>--पदं a place sacred to a deity.<BR>--पालः<BR>{1} a man employed to guard a field.<BR>{2} a deity protecting fields. {3} an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--फलं the area or<BR>superficial contents of a figure (in<BR>math.).<BR>--भक्तिः f. the division of a<BR>field.<BR>--भूमिः f. cultivated land.<BR>--राशिः quantity represented by<BR>geometrical figures.<BR>--विद् a. = क्षेत्रज्ञ<BR>q. v. (--m.) {1} a husbandman. {2}<BR>a sage, one who has spiritual<BR>knowledge; Ku. 3. 50. {3} the soul.<BR>--व्यवहारः {1} drawing a figure in<BR>geometry. {2} geometrical<BR>demonstration.<BR>--स्थ a. residing at a sacred<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिक|क्षेत्रिकः
क्षेत्रिक a. (की f.) [क्षेत्रमस्त्यस्य ठन्]<BR>Relating to a field.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A farmer;<BR>Ms. 8. 241, 9. 53.<BR>--2 A husband;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">Page0439-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Ms. 9. 145.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिन्
क्षेत्रिन् a. [क्षेत्र-इनि]<BR>1 Owning a<BR>field; cultivating land.<BR>--2<BR>Agricultural. --m.<BR>1 An agriculturist, a<BR>cultivator; Y. 2. 161.<BR>--2 A<BR>(nominal) husband; Ś. 5.<BR>--3 The soul.<BR>--4 The Supreme soul; Bg. 13. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रिय|क्षेत्रियं|क्षेत्रियः
क्षेत्रिय a. [क्षेत्र-घ]<BR>1 Relating to<BR>a field.<BR>--2 Curable in a future body,<BR>or incurable in the present life,<BR>irremediable; दंडोयं क्षेत्रियो येन<BR>मय्यपातीति साऽब्रवीत् Bk. 4. 32.<BR>--यं<BR>1 An<BR>organic disease.<BR>--2 Meadow grass,<BR>pasturage.<BR>--3 (pl.) The<BR>surrounding parts of any place.<BR>--यः<BR>1 A<BR>medicament.<BR>--2 An incurable disease.<BR>--3<BR>An adulterer.<BR>--4 Physicking,<BR>operating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रीयति
क्षेत्रीयति Den. P. To desire<BR>another's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेत्रीकृ
क्षेत्रीकृ {c8c} U. To expose to, to<BR>subject to; Mu. 7. 4; K. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेप|क्षेपः
क्षेप &c. See under क्षिप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेम|क्षेमं|क्षेमः
क्षेम a. [क्षि-मन् Uṇ. 1. 138]<BR>1<BR>Conferring happiness, ease or comfort,<BR>good, beneficial, well; धार्तराष्ट्रा रणे<BR>हन्युस्तन्मे क्षेमतरं भवेत् Bg. 1. 46.<BR>--2<BR>Prosperous, at ease, comfortable,<BR>--3 Secure, happy.<BR>--मः, --मं<BR>1<BR>Peace, happiness, ease, welfare,<BR>wellbeing; वितन्वति क्षेममदेवमातृकाश्चिराय<BR>तास्मिन् कुरवश्चकासते Ki. 1. 17; वैश्यं<BR>क्षेमं समागम्य (पृच्छेत्) Ms. 2. 127;<BR>अधुना सर्वजलचराणां क्षेमं भविष्यति<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--2 Safety, security; क्षेमेण व्रज<BR>बांधवान् Mk. 7. 7 safely; Pt. 1. 146.<BR>--3 Preserving, protection;<BR>R. 15. 6.<BR>--4 Keeping what is acquired;<BR>cf. योगक्षेम.<BR>--5 Final beatitude,<BR>eternal happiness.<BR>--6 Basis, foundation.<BR>--7 Residence, resting-place.<BR>--8<BR>A star, asterism (नक्षत्र).<BR>--मः<BR>A kind of perfume.<BR>--मा An epithet<BR>of Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर, --कार (also<BR>क्षेमंकर) a. propitious, causing peace<BR>or security.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमिन्
क्षेमिन् a. (णी f.) Safe, secure,<BR>happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेम्य|क्षेम्यं|क्षेम्यः
क्षेम्य a. [क्षेमाय साधु यत्]<BR>1 Resting,<BR>at ease.<BR>--2 Habitable, comfortable.<BR>--3 Healthy, salubrious.<BR>--4 Lucky,<BR>prosperous.<BR>--5 Giving peace.<BR>--म्यः<BR>An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षै
क्षै {c1c} P. [क्षायति, क्षाम] To wane,<BR>waste away, become emaciated,<BR>decline, decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0439-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैण्यं|क्षैण्य
क्षैण्यं<BR>1 Destruction.<BR>--2<BR>Leanness, slenderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्रं|क्षैत्र
क्षैत्रं [क्षेत्राणां सगूहः अण्]<BR>1 A<BR>multitude of fields.<BR>--2 A field.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैत्रज्ञं|क्षैत्रज्ञ
क्षैत्रज्ञं Spirituality, knowledge of<BR>the soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैप्रं|क्षैप्र
क्षैप्रं Quickness, speediness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षैरेय
क्षैरेय a. (यी f.) [क्षीरे संस्कृतं ढञ्]<BR>Milky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोडः|क्षोड
क्षोडः The post to which an<BR>elephant is tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोणिः|क्षोणि
क्षोणिः, क्षोणी f.<BR>1 The earth.<BR>--2<BR>The number ‘one’ (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोणी
क्षोणिः, क्षोणी f.<BR>1 The earth.<BR>--2<BR>The number ‘one’ (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोद|क्षोदः
क्षोद See under क्षुद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोभ|क्षोभः
क्षोभ^1 &c. See under क्षुभ्.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: badly placed diacritics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोमः|क्षोम|क्षोमं
क्षोमः, --मं [क्षु-मन्] A room on<BR>the top of a house.<BR>--मं Wove silk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षोमं|क्षोम|क्षोमः
क्षोमः, --मं [क्षु-मन्] A room on<BR>the top of a house.<BR>--मं Wove silk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौणिः|क्षौणि
क्षौणिः, --णी f. See क्षोणि.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्राचीरः the ocean.<BR>--भुज् m.,<BR>--पतिः<BR>a king.<BR>--भृत् m., धरः a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौणी
क्षौणिः, --णी f. See क्षोणि.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्राचीरः the ocean.<BR>--भुज् m.,<BR>--पतिः<BR>a king.<BR>--भृत् m., धरः a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्रः|क्षौद्र|क्षौद्रं
क्षौद्रः<BR>1 The Campaka tree.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a mixed caste.<BR>--द्रं<BR>1<BR>Smallness.<BR>--2 Meanness, lowness.<BR>--3<BR>Honey; सक्षौद्रपटलैरिव R. 4. 63.<BR>--4<BR>Water.<BR>--5 A particle of dust.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं wax.<BR>--धातुः a kind of<BR>mineral substance; (माक्षिक).<BR>--मेहः the<BR>disease diabetes mellitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौद्रेयं|क्षौद्रेय
क्षौद्रेयं Wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौमः|क्षौम|क्षौमं
क्षौमः a. [क्षु-मन् स्वार्थे अण्] Linen.<BR>--मः, --मं<BR>1 Silken cloth, wove silk;<BR>क्षौमं केनचिदिंदुपांडुतरुणा<BR>मांगल्यमाविष्कृतं Ś. 4. 4; क्षौमांतरितमेखले (अंके)<BR>R. 10. 8.<BR>--2 An airy room on the top<BR>of a house.<BR>--3 The back of an<BR>edifice.<BR>--4 A fortified place before a<BR>building.<BR>--मं<BR>1 Linen cloth.<BR>--2<BR>Linseed.<BR>--मी Flax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौरं|क्षौर
क्षौरं Shaving.<BR>--री A razor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षौरिकः|क्षौरिक
क्षौरिकः A barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णु
क्ष्णु {c2c} P. (क्ष्णौति, क्ष्णुत) To whet,<BR>sharpen. --WITH सं (Atm.) to<BR>sharpen (fig. also); Bk. 8. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णुत|क्ष्णुतः
क्ष्णुत a. [क्ष्णु-क्त] Whetted,<BR>sharpened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्णोत्रं|क्ष्णोत्र
क्ष्णोत्रं Ved. A grind-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मा
क्ष्मा<BR>1 The earth; (पुत्रं) क्ष्मां<BR>लंभयित्वा क्षमयोपपन्नं R. 18. 9; किं<BR>शेषस्य भरव्यथा न वपुषि क्ष्मां न क्षिपत्येष<BR>यत् Mu. 2. 18.<BR>--2 (In math.) The<BR>number ‘one’.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः the<BR>planet Mars.<BR>--पः, --पतिः, --भुज् m.<BR>a king; कविक्ष्मापतिः Gīt. 1;<BR>देशानामुपरि क्ष्मापाः Pt. 1. 155.<BR>--भृत् m. a<BR>king or mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्माय्
क्ष्माय् {c1c} A. (क्ष्मायते, क्ष्मायित) To<BR>shake, tremble; चक्ष्माये च मही<BR>Bk. 14. 21; 17. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्मील्
क्ष्मील् {c1c} P. (क्ष्मीलति) To wink,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-c" target="_blank">Page0440-c+ 32</a>]<BR>close the eyelids.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विड्
क्ष्विड् {c1c} U. (क्ष्वेडति-ते, क्ष्वेट्ट or<BR>क्ष्वेडित) To hum, roar, whistle, growl,<BR>murmur, sound indistinctly;<BR>Ms. 4. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विड्
क्ष्विड् {c1c} A., क्ष्विद् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be<BR>wet or unctuous.<BR>--2 To emit<BR>sap, or discharge juice, ichor &c.,<BR>exude. --WITH प्र to murmur, hum;<BR>Bk. 7. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्विण्ण|क्ष्विण्णः
क्ष्विण्ण a.<BR>1 Sounded inarticulately.<BR>--2 Soft, unctuous, oily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेड|क्ष्वेडं|क्ष्वेडः
क्ष्वेड a.<BR>1 Crooked, curved.<BR>--2 Wicked,<BR>depraved<BR>--3 Difficult to be<BR>approached.<BR>--डः<BR>1 Sound, noise.<BR>--2 Venom,<BR>poison; गुणदोषौ बुधो<BR>गृह्णन्निंदुक्ष्वेडाविवेश्वरः । शिरसा श्लाघते पूर्वं परं कंठेनियच्छति<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--3 Moistening.<BR>--4<BR>Abandonment.<BR>--5 An inarticulate sound.<BR>--डा<BR>1 The roaring of a lion.<BR>--2 A<BR>war-cry, war-whoop.<BR>--3 A bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0440-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्ष्वेडनं|क्ष्वेडन
