गुत्सकः|गुत्सक
गुत्सकः [गुत्स-स्वार्थादौ कन्]<BR>1 A<BR>bundle, bunch.<BR>--2 A nosegay.<BR>--3 A<BR>cow-tail, chowrie.<BR>--4 The section or<BR>chapter of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुद्
गुद् {c1c} A. (गोदते, गुदित) To play.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुदं|गुद
गुदं The anus; Y. 3. 93;<BR>Ms. 5. 136.; 8. 282.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकुरः piles.<BR>--आवर्तः obstruction of the bowels.<BR>--उद्धवः piles.<BR>--ओष्ठः the opening<BR>of the anus.<BR>--कीलः, --कीलकः piles.<BR>--ग्रहः constipation, flatulence.<BR>--पाकः<BR>inflammation of the anus.<BR>--भ्रंशः<BR>prolapsus ani.<BR>--वर्त्मन् n. the anus.<BR>--स्तंभः constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुध्
गुध् {vI.v} {c4c} P. (गुध्यति, गुधित) To<BR>wrap up, cover, envelop, clothe.<BR>{vII.v} {c9c} P. (गुध्नाति) To be angry.<BR>{vIII.v} {c1c} A. (गोधते) To play, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुधित
गुधित a. Surrounded, enclosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुधेर|गुधेरः
गुधेर a. Protecting; a defender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुंदलः|गुन्दल|गुंदल|गुन्दलः
गुंदलः The sound of a small<BR>oblong drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुंदालः|गुन्दाल|गुंदाल|गुन्दालः
गुंदा(द्रा)लः The Cātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुंद्रालः|गुन्द्राल|गुंद्राल|गुन्द्रालः
गुंदा(द्रा)लः The Cātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुंद्र्|गुन्द्र्
गुंद्र् {c10c} P. (गुंद्रयति) To lie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुंद्रः|गुन्द्र|गुन्द्रः
गुंद्रः A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्
गुप् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (गोपायति, गोपायित or<BR>गुप्त)<BR>1 To guard, protect, defend,<BR>watch over; गोपायंति कुलस्त्रिय<BR>आत्मानं Mb.; जुगोपात्मानमत्रस्तः R. 1. 21;<BR>जुगोप गोरूपधरामिवोर्वी 2. 3;<BR>Bk. 17. 80.<BR>--2 To hide, conceal; किं<BR>वक्षश्चरणानतिव्यतिकरव्याजेन गोपाय्यते<BR>Amaru. 22; see गुप्त. {vII.v} {c1c} A. (जुगुप्सते<BR>strictly desid. of गुप्)<BR>1 To despise,<BR>shun, abhor, detest, censure; (with<BR>abl., sometimes acc. also);<BR>पापाज्जुगुप्सते Sk.; किं त्वं मामजुगुप्सिष्ठाः<BR>Bk. 15. 19; Y. 3. 296.<BR>--2 To hide,<BR>conceal (गोपते in this sense). {vIII.v}<BR>{c4c} P. (गुप्यति) To be confused or<BR>disturbed. {vIV.v} {c10c} U. (गोपयति-ते)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>--2 To speak.<BR>--3 To<BR>conceal; तव गोप्यते किमिव Śi. 9. 59,<BR>11. 34; (the following stanza from<BR>कविरहस्य illustrates the root in its<BR>different conjugations:<BR>--गोपायति<BR>क्षितिमिमां चतुरब्धिसीमां पापाज्जुगुप्सत उदारमतिः<BR>सदैव । वित्तं न गोपयति यस्तु वणीयकेभ्यो धीरो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-c" target="_blank">Page0462-c+ 57</a>]<BR>न गुप्यति महत्यपि कार्यजाते ॥)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुपिलः|गुपिल
गुपिलः<BR>1 A king.<BR>--2 A protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्त|गुप्तं|गुप्तः
गुप्त p. p. [गुप् कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Protected, preserved, guarded;<BR>R. 10. 60.<BR>--2 Hidden, concealed, kept<BR>secret; Ms. 2. 150, 7. 76, 8. 374.<BR>--3 Secret, private.<BR>--4 Invisible,<BR>withdrawn from sight.<BR>--5 Joined.<BR>--प्तः<BR>1 An appellation usually (though<BR>not necessarily) added to the name<BR>of a Vaiśya; as चंद्रगुप्तः, समुद्रगुप्तः &c.<BR>(Usually शर्मन् or देव is added to the<BR>name of a Brāhmaṇa; गुप्त, भूति or<BR>दत्त to that of a Vaiśya; and दास to<BR>that of a Śūdra; cf. शर्मा देवश्च विप्रस्य<BR>वर्मा त्राता च भूभुजः । भूतिर्दतश्च वैश्यस्य दासः<BR>शूद्रस्य कारयेत्).<BR>--2 An epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--प्तं ind. Secretly,<BR>privately, apart.<BR>--प्ता One of the<BR>principal female characters in a poetical<BR>composition, a lady married to<BR>another (परकीया) who conceals her<BR>lover's caresses and endearments<BR>past, present or future; वृत्तसुरतगोपन<BR>वर्तिष्यमाणसुरतगोपना and<BR>वर्तमानसुरतगोपना; see Rasamañjarī 24.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कथा a secret or confidential<BR>communication, a secret.<BR>--गतिः a spy,<BR>an emissary.<BR>--चर a. going secretly.<BR>--(रः) {1} an epithet of Balarāma. {2} a.<BR>spy, an emissary.<BR>--दानं a secret<BR>gift or present.<BR>--वेशः a disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तकः|गुप्तक
गुप्तकः A preserver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुप्तिः|गुप्ति
गुप्तिः f. [गुप्-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>Preserving, protection; सर्वस्यास्य तु सर्गस्य<BR>गुप्त्यंर्थ Ms. 1. 87, 94, 99; Y. 1. 198.<BR>--2 Concealing, hiding.<BR>--3 Covering,<BR>sheathing; असिधारासु कोषगुप्तिः<BR>K. 11.<BR>--4 A hole in the ground, a<BR>cavern, sink, cellar.<BR>--5 Digging a hole<BR>in the ground.<BR>--6 A means of<BR>protection, fortification, rampart;<BR>Ku. 6. 38.<BR>--7 Confinement, prison;<BR>सरभस इव गुप्तिस्फोटमर्कः करोति<BR>Śi. 11. 60.<BR>--8 The lower deck of a boat.<BR>--9<BR>A leak in a ship.<BR>--10 Check,<BR>stoppage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपः|गोप
गोपः (पी f.) [गुप्-अच्]<BR>1 One<BR>who guards or protects; शालिगोप्यो<BR>जगुर्यशः R. 4. 20.<BR>--2 Hiding,<BR>concealment.<BR>--3 Reviling, abuse.<BR>--4<BR>Flurry, agitation.<BR>--5 Light, lustre,<BR>splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपनं|गोपन
गोपनं [गुप् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Guarding,<BR>protecting.<BR>--2 Hiding, concealing.<BR>--3 Reviling, abuse.<BR>--4 Flurry, hurry,<BR>alarm.<BR>--5 Light, lustre.<BR>--6 Envy,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">Page0463-a+ 57</a>]<BR>jealousy.<BR>--7 Perplexity, confusion.<BR>--ना<BR>1 Protection.<BR>--2 Light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0462-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपनीय|गोपनीयं
गोपनीय a.<BR>1 To be preserved or<BR>protected.<BR>--2 To be prevented.<BR>--3<BR>To be concealed or hidden.<BR>--4 Secret,<BR>mysterious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायक
गोपायक a. A preserver, defender,<BR>one who guards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायनं|गोपायन
गोपायनं Protecting, guarding,<BR>defending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायित|गोपायितं
गोपायित a. Protected, defended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपायितृ
गोपायितृ m. A protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिन्
गोपिन्, --गोपिल a. Protecting,<BR>preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोपिल|गोपिलः
गोपिन्, --गोपिल a. Protecting,<BR>preserving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्तृ
गोप्तृ a. (प्त्री f.) [गुप्-तृच्]<BR>1 A<BR>protector, preserver, guardian; तस्मिन्वनं<BR>गोप्तरि गाहमाने R. 2. 14; 1. 55;<BR>M. 5. 20; Bg. 11. 18.<BR>--2 One who hides<BR>or conceals. --m. An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्य|गोप्यः
गोप्य a. [गुप् कर्मणि यत्]<BR>1 To be<BR>protected.<BR>--2 To be kept secret or<BR>hidden; Pt. 1. 100.<BR>--3 To be kept, to<BR>be taken care of.<BR>--4 To be cherished<BR>--प्यः<BR>1 A servant, slave.<BR>--2 A son<BR>of a female slave.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आधिः<BR>a pledge to be carefully preserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गोप्यकः|गोप्यक
गोप्यकः A slave, servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुफ्
गुफ् or गुंफ् {c6c} P. (गु-गुं-फति, गुंफित)<BR>1 To put string or weave<BR>together, tie, wind round; गुंफिताः<BR>शिरसि वेणयोऽभवन् Śi. 14. 30;<BR>विश्वाभिरामगुणगौरवगुंफितानां Bv. 1. 71;<BR>Bk. 7. 105.<BR>--2 (fig.) To write,<BR>compose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुफित|गुफितः
गु(गुं)फित p. p. Strung together,<BR>tied, woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुंफित|गुम्फित|गुम्फितः
गु(गुं)फित p. p. Strung together,<BR>tied, woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुंफः|गुम्फ|गुंफ|गुम्फः
गुंफः [गुंफ्-घञ्]<BR>1 Tying, stringing<BR>together; गुंफो वाणीनां B. R. 1. 1.<BR>--2 Putting together, composing,<BR>arrangement.<BR>--3 A bracelet.<BR>--4 A<BR>whisker, a mustachio.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुंफना
गुंफना [गुंफ् --युच्]<BR>1 Stringing<BR>together.<BR>--2 Arranging, composing.<BR>--3 Good adjustment (of words and<BR>their senses), good composition;<BR>वाक्ये शब्दार्थयोः सम्यग्रचना गुंफना मता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्
गुर् {vI.v} {c6c} A. [गुरते, गूर्त-गूर्ण] To<BR>make an effort or exertion. {vII.v}<BR>{c4c} A. (p. p. गूर्ण)<BR>1 To hurt, kill,<BR>injure.<BR>--2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरणं|गुरण
गुरणं [गुर् भावे ल्युट्] Effort,<BR>perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरु|गुरुः
गुरु a. (रु-र्वी) f. [गॄ-कु उच्च<BR>Uṇ. 1. 24.] compar. गरीयस्; superl. गरिष्ठ<BR>1<BR>Heavy, weighty (opp. लघु); (fig.<BR>also); तेन धूर्जगतो गुर्वी सचिवेषु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-b" target="_blank">Page0463-b+ 57</a>]<BR>निचिक्षिपे R. 1. 34; 3. 35; 12. 102;<BR>Rs. 1. 7.<BR>--2 Great, large, long,<BR>extended.<BR>--3 Long (in duration or<BR>length); आरंभगुर्वी Bh. 2. 60; गुरुषु<BR>दिवसेष्वेषु गच्छत्सु Me. 83.<BR>--4<BR>Important, momentous, great;<BR>विभवगुरुभिः कृत्यैः Ś. 4. 18; स्वार्थात्सतां<BR>गुरुतरा प्रणयिक्रियैव V. 4. 15; Ku. 3. 13,<BR>Bh. 3. 7; R. 14. 35.<BR>--5 Arduous,<BR>difficult (to bear); कांताविरहगुरुणा<BR>शापेन Me. 1.<BR>--6 Great, excessive,<BR>violent, intense; गुरुः प्रहर्षः प्रबभूव<BR>नात्मनि R. 3. 17; गुर्वपि विरहदुःखं<BR>Ś. 4. 15; Bg. 6. 22.<BR>--7 Venerable,<BR>respectable.<BR>--8 Heavy, hard of<BR>digestion (as food).<BR>--9 Best,<BR>excellent.<BR>--10 Dear, beloved.<BR>--11<BR>Haughty, proud (as a speech).<BR>--12 (In prosody) Long, as a<BR>syllable, either in itself, or being<BR>short, followed by a conjunct<BR>consonant &c.; e. g. ई in ईड् or त in<BR>तस्कर. (It is usually represented<BR>by ग in works on prosody; मात्तौ<BR>गौ चेच्छालिनी वेदलोकैः &c.).<BR>--13<BR>Irresistible, unassailable; Māl. 6. 1.<BR>--14<BR>Mighty, powerful.<BR>--15 Valuable,<BR>highly prized.<BR>--16 Grievous.<BR>--रुः<BR>1 (a) A father; न केवलं<BR>तद्गुरुरेकपार्थिवः क्षितावभूदेकधनुर्धरोऽपि सः<BR>R. 3. 31, 48; 4. 1; 8. 29. (b) Forefather,<BR>ancestor; U. 5. 28.<BR>--2 Any<BR>venerable or respectable person, an<BR>elderly personage or relative, the elders<BR>(pl.) शुश्रूषस्व गुरून् Ś. 4. 17;<BR>Bg. 2. 5; Bv. 2. 7, 18, 19, 49; आज्ञा<BR>गुरूणां ह्यविचारणीया R. 14. 46.<BR>--3 A<BR>teacher, preceptor; गुरुशिष्यौ.<BR>--4<BR>Particularly, a religious teacher,<BR>spiritual preceptor; तौ गुरुर्गुरुपत्नी च<BR>प्रीत्या प्रतिननंदतुः R. 1. 57;<BR>(technically a Guru is one who performs<BR>the purificatory ceremonies over<BR>a boy and instructs him in the<BR>Vedas; स गुरुर्यः क्रियाः कृत्वा वेदमस्मै<BR>प्रयच्छति Y. 1. 34).<BR>--5 A lord, head,<BR>superintendent, ruler; वर्णाश्रमाणां<BR>गुरवे स वर्णी R. 5. 19 the head of the<BR>castes or orders; गुरुर्नृपाणां गुरवे निवेद्य<BR>2. 68.<BR>--6 N. of Bṛhaspati, the<BR>preceptor of the gods; गुरुं नेत्रसहस्रेण<BR>चोदयामास वासवः Ku. 2. 29;<BR>Pt. 1. 230.<BR>--7 The planet Jupiter;<BR>गुरुकाव्यानुगां बिभ्रच्चांद्रीमभिनभः श्रियं Śi. 2. 2.<BR>--8 The propounder of a new<BR>doctrine.<BR>--9 The lunar asterism called<BR>पुष्य.<BR>--10 N. of Droṇa, teacher of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-c" target="_blank">Page0463-c+ 57</a>]<BR>the Kauravas and Pāṇḍavas.<BR>--11<BR>N. of Prabhākara, the leader of a<BR>school of the Mīmāṃsakas (called<BR>after him Prābhākara).<BR>--12 The<BR>supreme spirit.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षरं a<BR>long syllable.<BR>--अंगना {1} the wife of<BR>a Guru. {2} a woman entitled to<BR>great respect.<BR>--अर्थ a. important.<BR>--(र्थः) a preceptor's fee for<BR>instructing a pupil; गुर्वर्थमाहर्तुमहं यतिष्ये<BR>R. 5. 17.<BR>--उत्तम a. highly revered.<BR>--(मः)<BR>the Supreme soul.<BR>--कारः worship,<BR>adoration.<BR>--कार्यं {1} a serious or<BR>weighty affair. {2} the office of a<BR>spiritual teacher.<BR>--कृत a. {1}<BR>worshipped. {2} made much of;<BR>Bh. 3. 20.<BR>--क्रमः instruction handed down<BR>through a series of teachers,<BR>traditional instruction.<BR>--घ्नः white<BR>mustard.<BR>--चर्या attendance upon a<BR>preceptor; Māl. 9. 51.<BR>--जनः any<BR>venerable person, an elderly<BR>relative, the elders collectively; नापेक्षितो<BR>गुरुजनः K. 158; Bv. 2. 7.<BR>--तल्पः {1}<BR>the bed (wife) of a teacher. {2}<BR>violation or violator of a teacher's bed.<BR>--तल्पगः, --तल्पिन् m. {1} one who<BR>violates his teacher's bed (wife),<BR>(ranked in Hindu law as a sinner of<BR>the worst kind, committer of an<BR>अतिपातक; cf. Ms. 11. 103). {2} one<BR>who defiles his step-mother.<BR>--दक्षिणा<BR>fee given to a spiritual preceptor;<BR>R. 5. 1.<BR>--दानं a guru's gift.<BR>--दैवतः the<BR>constellation पुष्य.<BR>--पत्रा the<BR>tamarind tree.<BR>--पाक a. difficult<BR>of digestion.<BR>--पूजा {1} the<BR>ceremonies in propitiation of Bṛhaspati<BR>when a work is to be performed or<BR>undertaken. {2} the worship of one's<BR>spiritual preceptor.<BR>--प्रसादः the<BR>product of a guru's blessing, i. e.<BR>learning.<BR>--भं {1} the constellation पुष्य.<BR>{2} a bow. {3} the sign pisces of the<BR>zodiac.<BR>--मर्दलः a kind of drum or ta<BR>bor.<BR>--रत्नं {1} topaz. {2} a gem<BR>broughfrom the Himālaya and the Indust<BR>--लाघवं relative importance or value.<BR>Ś. 5.<BR>--वर्तिन्, --वासिन् m. a student<BR>(ब्रह्मचारिन्) who resides at his<BR>preceptor's house.<BR>--वारः, --वासरः<BR>Thursday.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. the conduct of a pupil<BR>towards his preceptor.<BR>--व्यथ a.<BR>greatly distressed, heavy with grief.<BR>--शिखरिन् m. an epithet of the<BR>Himālaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुक
गुरुक a. (की f.)<BR>1 A little heavy.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">Page0464-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 Long (in prosody.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0463-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुतम|गुरुतमः
गुरुतम a. Most important.<BR>--मः<BR>1<BR>A best teacher.<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुता
गुरुता, --त्वं<BR>1 Weight, heaviness.<BR>--2<BR>Burden, trouble<BR>--3 Dignity,<BR>greatness; U. 6. 19; लोके गुरुत्वं विपरीततां<BR>वा स्वचेष्टितान्येव नरं नयंति H. 2. 46;<BR>Śi. 16. 27.<BR>--4 Respectability,<BR>venerableness.<BR>--5 The office of a teacher.<BR>--6<BR>Importance.<BR>--7 Universal gravitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुरुत्वं|गुरुत्व
गुरुता, --त्वं<BR>1 Weight, heaviness.<BR>--2<BR>Burden, trouble<BR>--3 Dignity,<BR>greatness; U. 6. 19; लोके गुरुत्वं विपरीततां<BR>वा स्वचेष्टितान्येव नरं नयंति H. 2. 46;<BR>Śi. 16. 27.<BR>--4 Respectability,<BR>venerableness.<BR>--5 The office of a teacher.<BR>--6<BR>Importance.<BR>--7 Universal gravitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्जरः|गुर्जर|गुर्ज्जर|गुर्ज्जरः
गु(गू)र्जरः<BR>1 The district of<BR>Gujarāth.<BR>--2 An inhabitant of<BR>Gujarāth; तेषां मार्गे परिचयवशादर्जितं<BR>गुर्जराणां यः संतापं शिथिलमकरोत्<BR>सोमनाथं विलोक्य Vikr. 18. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूर्जरः|गूर्जर
गु(गू)र्जरः<BR>1 The district of<BR>Gujarāth.<BR>--2 An inhabitant of<BR>Gujarāth; तेषां मार्गे परिचयवशादर्जितं<BR>गुर्जराणां यः संतापं शिथिलमकरोत्<BR>सोमनाथं विलोक्य Vikr. 18. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्विणी|गुर्व्विणी
गुर्विणी, गुर्वी A pregnant woman;<BR>e. g. गुर्विणीं नानुगच्छति न स्पृशंति<BR>रजस्वलां.<BR>--र्वी The wife of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्वी|गुर्व्वी
गुर्विणी, गुर्वी A pregnant woman;<BR>e. g. गुर्विणीं नानुगच्छति न स्पृशंति<BR>रजस्वलां.<BR>--र्वी The wife of a preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्द्
गुर्द् See गूर्द्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुर्व्
गुर्व् {c1c} P. (गुर्वति)<BR>1 To endeavour,<BR>try.<BR>--2 To raise or elevate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलः|गुल
गुलः Molasses; cf. गुड.<BR>--ली<BR>1 A<BR>pill.<BR>--2 Small-pox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्यः|गुल्य
गुल्यः Sweetness, a sweet taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलिका
गुलिका<BR>1 A ball.<BR>--2 A pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलिंकः|गुलिङ्क|गुलिङ्कः
गुलिंकः A sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलुच्छः|गुलुच्छ|गुलुछ
गुलुच्छः, गुलुंछः A bunch or<BR>cluster; see गुच्छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुलुंछः|गुलुञ्छ|गुलुंछ|गुलुञ्छः
गुलुच्छः, गुलुंछः A bunch or<BR>cluster; see गुच्छ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्फः|गुल्फ
गुल्फः The ankle;<BR>आगुल्फकीर्णापणमार्गपुष्पं Ku. 7. 55; गुल्फावलंबिना K. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मः|गुल्म|गुल्मं
गुल्मः, --ल्मं [गुड् मक् डस्य लः Tv.]<BR>1 A clump or cluster of trees, a<BR>thicket, wood, bush; Ms. 1. 48;<BR>7. 192; 12. 58; Y. 2. 229.<BR>--2 A troop of<BR>soldiers, a division of an army,<BR>consisting of 45 foot, 27 horse, 9<BR>chariots and 9 elephants.<BR>--3 A fort.<BR>--4<BR>The spleen.<BR>--5 A chronic<BR>enlargement of the spleen.<BR>--6 A<BR>village police-station.<BR>--7 A wharf<BR>of stairs (Mar. घांट).<BR>--8<BR>Disciplining an army, keeping it in a<BR>posture of defence.<BR>--ल्मी<BR>1 A cluster<BR>or clump of trees.<BR>--2 Jujube.<BR>--3<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR>--4 A tent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केतुः a small sort of cane, sorrel.<BR>--केश a. having bushy hair.<BR>--मूलं<BR>fresh ginger.<BR>--वातः, --उदरः a<BR>disease of the spleen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मं|गुल्म|गुल्मः
गुल्मः, --ल्मं [गुड् मक् डस्य लः Tv.]<BR>1 A clump or cluster of trees, a<BR>thicket, wood, bush; Ms. 1. 48;<BR>7. 192; 12. 58; Y. 2. 229.<BR>--2 A troop of<BR>soldiers, a division of an army,<BR>consisting of 45 foot, 27 horse, 9<BR>chariots and 9 elephants.<BR>--3 A fort.<BR>--4<BR>The spleen.<BR>--5 A chronic<BR>enlargement of the spleen.<BR>--6 A<BR>village police-station.<BR>--7 A wharf<BR>of stairs (Mar. घांट).<BR>--8<BR>Disciplining an army, keeping it in a<BR>posture of defence.<BR>--ल्मी<BR>1 A cluster<BR>or clump of trees.<BR>--2 Jujube.<BR>--3<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR>--4 A tent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केतुः a small sort of cane, sorrel.<BR>--केश a. having bushy hair.<BR>--मूलं<BR>fresh ginger.<BR>--वातः, --उदरः a<BR>disease of the spleen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुल्मिन्
गुल्मिन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Growing<BR>in a clump or cluster.<BR>--2 Having<BR>a diseased spleen, or a spleen<BR>affected by गुल्म.<BR>--3 Composed of<BR>different divisions (as a force &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुवाकः|गुवाक
गु(गू)वाकः The betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूवाकः|गूवाक
गु(गू)वाकः The betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुष्पित
गुष्पित a. Ved. Interlaced,<BR>intwined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्
गुह् {c1c} U. (गूहति-ते, जुगूह, जुगुहे,<BR>अगूहीत्, अगूहिष्ट, अगूढ, अघुक्षत्-त,<BR>गूहिष्यति-ते, घोक्ष्यति-ते, गूहितुं, गोढुं, गूढ)<BR>1 To<BR>cover, hide, conceal, keep secret;<BR>गुह्यं च गूहति गुणान् प्रकटीकरोति<BR>Bh. 2. 72; गूहेत्कूर्म इवांगानि Ms. 7. 105;<BR>R. 14. 49; Bk. 16. 41.<BR>--2 To cover<BR>with clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहः|गुह
गुहः [गुह्-क]<BR>1 An epithet of<BR>Kārtikeya; गुह इवाप्रतिहतशक्तिः<BR>K. 8; Ku. 5. 14.<BR>--2 A horse.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a Cāṇḍāla or Niṣāda, king<BR>of Śṛṅgavera and a friend of Rāma.<BR>--4 An epithet of Viṣṇu; also of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--राजः the<BR>peculiar form of construction of a temple.<BR>--षष्ठी the sixth day in the first<BR>fortnight of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहा
गुहा<BR>1 A cave, cavern,<BR>hidingplace; गुहानिबद्धप्रतिशब्ददीर्घं R. 2. 28,<BR>51; धर्मस्य तत्त्वं निहितं गुहायां Mb.<BR>--2 Hiding, concealing.<BR>--3 A pit,<BR>hole in the ground.<BR>--4 The heart.<BR>--5 Intellect.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आहित a.<BR>placed in the heart.<BR>--चरं Brahman.<BR>--मुख a. ‘cave-mouthed,’<BR>widemouthed, open-mouthed.<BR>--शयः {1} a<BR>mouse. {2} a tiger or lion. {3} the<BR>Supreme soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहिनं|गुहिन
गुहिनं A wood, thicket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहिलं|गुहिल
गुहिलं Wealth, property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुहेरः|गुहेर
गुहेरः<BR>1 A guardian, protector.<BR>--2<BR>A blacksmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्य|गुह्यं|गुह्यः
गुह्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be concealed,<BR>covered or kept secret, private;<BR>गुह्यं च गूहति Bh. 2. 72.<BR>--2 Secret,<BR>solitary, retired.<BR>--3 Mysterious;<BR>Bg. 18. 63.<BR>--ह्यः<BR>1 Hypocrisy.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 A tortoise.<BR>--ह्यं<BR>1 A secret, mystery; मौनं चैवास्मि<BR>गुह्यानां Bg. 10. 38; 9. 2;<BR>Ms. 12. 117; Pt. 2. 45.<BR>--2 A privity, the<BR>male or female organ of<BR>generation.<BR>--3 The anus.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गुरुः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--दीपकः the<BR>firefly.<BR>--निष्यंदः urine.<BR>--पुष्पः the<BR>Aśvattha tree (‘with concealed<BR>blossoms’).<BR>--भाषितं {1} secret speech<BR>or conversation. {2} a secret.<BR>--मयः<BR>an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गुह्यकः|गुह्यक
गुह्यकः N. of a class of demigods,<BR>who, like the Yakṣas, are<BR>attendants of Kubera and guardians<BR>of his treasures; गुह्यकस्तं ययाचे<BR>Me. 5, Ms. 12. 47.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपतिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-c" target="_blank">Page0464-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--ईश्वरः an epithet of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूढ|गूढं|गूढः
गूढ p. p. [गुह्-क्त]<BR>1 Hidden,<BR>concealed, kept secret.<BR>--2 Covered.<BR>--3 Invisible, latent.<BR>--4 Secret,<BR>private.<BR>--5 Disguised.<BR>--ढं<BR>1 A solitary<BR>or private place.<BR>--2 A private part.<BR>--3 A mystery.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः a<BR>tortoise.<BR>--अंघ्रिः a snake.<BR>--आत्मन् (the<BR>compound word being गूढोत्मन् thus<BR>accounted for in Sk.; भवेद् वर्णागमाद्<BR>हंसः सिंहो वर्णविपर्ययात् । गूढोत्मा<BR>वर्णविकृतेर्वर्णलोपात्पृषोदरः) the Supreme soul.<BR>--उपन्नः, --जः one of the 12 kinds of<BR>sons in Hindu law; he is a son born<BR>secretly of a woman, when her<BR>husband is absent, the real father being<BR>unknown; गृहे प्रच्छन्न उत्पन्नो<BR>गूढजस्तु सुतः स्मृतः Y. 2. 129; Ms. 9. 159,<BR>170.<BR>--चार --चारिन् a. going about<BR>secretly. (--m.) a spy, secret<BR>emissary.<BR>--नीडः the wag-tail.<BR>--पथः {1}<BR>a hidden path. {2} a by-path. {3}<BR>the mind, intellect.<BR>--पाद्, पादः a<BR>snake.<BR>--पुरुषः a spy, secret emissary.<BR>disguised agent.<BR>--पुष्पकः the<BR>Bakula tree.<BR>--भाषितं secret intelligence,<BR>private communication.<BR>--मार्गः {1}<BR>a passage under-ground. {2} a defile.<BR>--मैथुनः a crow.<BR>--वर्चस् m. ‘a<BR>concealed witness’, one placed to<BR>overhear secretly what has been said by<BR>the defendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गूहनं|गूहन
गूहनं Concealing, hiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0464-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गू
