चय् {c1c} A. (चयते) To go to or<BR>towards, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्
चर् {c1c} P. (चरति, चचार, अचारीत्,<BR>चरितुं, चरित or sometimes चीर्ण)<BR>1 To<BR>walk, move, go about, roam, wander;<BR>नष्टाशंका हरिणशिशवो मंदमदं चरंति<BR>Ś. 1. 15 (चर् may mean here ‘to graze’<BR>also); इंद्रियाणां हि चरतां Bg. 2. 67;<BR>कपयश्चेरुरार्तस्य रामस्येव मनोरथाः<BR>R. 12. 59; Ms. 2. 23, 6. 68; 8. 236;<BR>9. 306; 10. 55.<BR>--2 (a) To perform, do,<BR>act; रचयति रेखाः सलिले यस्तु खले<BR>चरति सत्कारं Bv. 1. 98. (b) To practise,<BR>perform, observe; चरतः किल दुश्चरं<BR>तपः R. 8. 79; Y. 1. 60; Ms. 3. 30.<BR>--3 To act, behave towards, conduct<BR>oneself (oft. with loc. of the person);<BR>चरंतीनां च कामतः Ms. 5. 90; 9. 287;<BR>आत्मवत्सर्वभूतेषु यश्चरेत् Mb.; तस्यां त्वं<BR>साधु नाचरः R. 1. 76 (where the root<BR>may be also आचर).<BR>--4 To graze;<BR>सुचिरं हि चरन् शस्यं H. 3. 9.<BR>--5 To<BR>eat, consume.<BR>--6 To be engaged in,<BR>be busy with.<BR>--7 To live, continue<BR>to be, continue in any state.<BR>--8 To<BR>spread, be diffused.<BR>--9 To live, be,<BR>exist.<BR>--10 To move, travel through,<BR>pervade, go along, follow. --Caus.<BR>(चारयति)<BR>1 To cause to move or go.<BR>--2 To send, direct, move.<BR>--3 To<BR>drive away.<BR>--4 To cause to perform<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-b" target="_blank">Page0486-b+ 57</a>]<BR>or practise.<BR>--5 To cause to copulate.<BR>--6 To cause to graze, pasture.<BR>--7<BR>To obtain knowledge of, acquaint<BR>oneself with.<BR>--8 To doubt. [cf.<BR>L. curro.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर|चरः
चर a. (री f.) [चर्-अच्]<BR>1<BR>Moving, going, walking; grazing &c.;<BR>धर्मारण्यचरेषु प्राणिषु Ś. 5. 9<BR>--2<BR>Following, practising (at the end of<BR>comp.).<BR>--3 Trembling, shaking.<BR>--4 Moveable; see चराचर below;<BR>Ms. 3. 201; Bg. 13. 15.<BR>--5 Animate;<BR>Ms. 5. 29; 7. 15.<BR>--6 (Used as an<BR>affix) formerly, late; आढ्यचर ‘one<BR>who was formerly rich’; so<BR>देवदत्तचरः अध्यापकचर late teacher &c.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A spy.<BR>--2 A wagtail.<BR>--3 A game<BR>played with dice and men.<BR>--4 A<BR>cowrie.<BR>--5 The planet Mars.<BR>--6<BR>(Hence) Tuesday.<BR>--7 The seventh<BR>Karaṇa in astrology.<BR>--8 The<BR>Karaṇas taken collectively.<BR>--9 The<BR>difference of time between two<BR>meridians.<BR>--10 The first, fourth, seventh,<BR>and tenth signs of the zodiac.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अचर a. {1} moveable and<BR>immovable; चराचराणां भूतानां कु<BR>क्षिराधारतां गतः Ku. 6. 67; 2. 5;<BR>Bg. 11. 43. {2} wished, desired. {3} shaking,<BR>trembling.<BR>--(रं) {1} the aggregate of<BR>all created things, the world;<BR>Ms. 1. 57, 63; 3. 75; Bg. 11. 7; 9. 10.<BR>{2} the sky, the atmosphere.<BR>{3} heaven.<BR>--(री) a young woman.<BR>--द्रव्यं moveables, goods and chattels.<BR>--पुष्टः a mediator.<BR>--भं, --भवनं a<BR>varying sign of the zodiac; i. e.<BR>the first, fourth, seventh and tenth.<BR>--मूर्तिः f. an idol which is carried<BR>about in procession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरकः|चरक
चरकः<BR>1 A spy.<BR>--2 A wandering<BR>mendicant, a vagrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरटः|चरट
चरटः The wag-tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणः|चरण|चरणं
चरणः --णं [चर्-करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 A<BR>foot; शिरसि चरण एष न्यस्यते वारयैनं<BR>Ve. 3. 38; जात्या काममवध्योसि चरण<BR>त्विदमुद्धृतं 39.<BR>--2 A support, pillar,<BR>prop.<BR>--3 The root of a tree.<BR>--4 The single line of a stanza.<BR>--5 A quarter.<BR>--6 A school or branch<BR>of any of the Vedas; e. g. चरणगुरवः<BR>Mv. 1, Māl. 1; Pt. 4. 3.<BR>--7 A race.<BR>--8 (In prosody) A dactyl.<BR>--णः<BR>1<BR>A footsoldier.<BR>--2 A ray of light.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Moving, roaming, wandering.<BR>--2 Performance, practising;<BR>Ms. 6. 75.<BR>--3 Conduct of life, behaviour<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-c" target="_blank">Page0486-c+ 57</a>]<BR>(moral).<BR>--4 Accomplishment.<BR>--5<BR>Eating, consuming.<BR>--6 Course.<BR>--7<BR>Acting, dealing, managing, conduct.<BR>--8 Fixed observance of any class,<BR>age (as priesthood &c).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अमृतं, --उदकं water in which the<BR>feet of a (revered) Brāhmaṇa or<BR>spiritual guide have been washed.<BR>--अरविंदं, --कमलं, --पद्मं a lotus-like foot.<BR>--आयुधः a cock<BR>--आस्कंदनं trampling,<BR>treading under foot.<BR>--गत a. fallen<BR>at the feet, prostrate.<BR>--ग्रंथिः m.,<BR>--पर्वन् n. the ankle.<BR>--न्यासः a<BR>footstep.<BR>--पः a tree.<BR>--पतनं falling<BR>down or prostration (at the feet of<BR>another); Amaru. 17.<BR>--पतित a.<BR>prostrate at the feet; Me. 105.<BR>--पातः {1} tread, trampling. {2}<BR>footfall. {3} prostration.<BR>--शुश्रूषा, --सेवा<BR>{1} prostration. {2} service, devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणं|चरण|चरणः
चरणः --णं [चर्-करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 A<BR>foot; शिरसि चरण एष न्यस्यते वारयैनं<BR>Ve. 3. 38; जात्या काममवध्योसि चरण<BR>त्विदमुद्धृतं 39.<BR>--2 A support, pillar,<BR>prop.<BR>--3 The root of a tree.<BR>--4 The single line of a stanza.<BR>--5 A quarter.<BR>--6 A school or branch<BR>of any of the Vedas; e. g. चरणगुरवः<BR>Mv. 1, Māl. 1; Pt. 4. 3.<BR>--7 A race.<BR>--8 (In prosody) A dactyl.<BR>--णः<BR>1<BR>A footsoldier.<BR>--2 A ray of light.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Moving, roaming, wandering.<BR>--2 Performance, practising;<BR>Ms. 6. 75.<BR>--3 Conduct of life, behaviour<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-c" target="_blank">Page0486-c+ 57</a>]<BR>(moral).<BR>--4 Accomplishment.<BR>--5<BR>Eating, consuming.<BR>--6 Course.<BR>--7<BR>Acting, dealing, managing, conduct.<BR>--8 Fixed observance of any class,<BR>age (as priesthood &c).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अमृतं, --उदकं water in which the<BR>feet of a (revered) Brāhmaṇa or<BR>spiritual guide have been washed.<BR>--अरविंदं, --कमलं, --पद्मं a lotus-like foot.<BR>--आयुधः a cock<BR>--आस्कंदनं trampling,<BR>treading under foot.<BR>--गत a. fallen<BR>at the feet, prostrate.<BR>--ग्रंथिः m.,<BR>--पर्वन् n. the ankle.<BR>--न्यासः a<BR>footstep.<BR>--पः a tree.<BR>--पतनं falling<BR>down or prostration (at the feet of<BR>another); Amaru. 17.<BR>--पतित a.<BR>prostrate at the feet; Me. 105.<BR>--पातः {1} tread, trampling. {2}<BR>footfall. {3} prostration.<BR>--शुश्रूषा, --सेवा<BR>{1} prostration. {2} service, devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरणिः|चरणि
चरणिः A man(मनुष्य);<BR>Rv. 8. 24. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरण्यु
चरण्यु a. Ved. moving, moveable<BR>(चरणशील).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरथ|चरथः
चरथ a. Ved.<BR>1 Moving, living.<BR>--2 Moveable.<BR>--थः, --थं<BR>1 Going,<BR>moving.<BR>--2 Moveableness.<BR>--3 Life.<BR>--4 A way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरम|चरमः
चरम a. [चर्-अमच् Uṇ. 5. 69]<BR>1<BR>Last, ultimate, final; चरमा क्रिया ‘the<BR>final or funeral ceremony.’<BR>--2<BR>Posterior, back; पृष्ठं तु चरमं तनोः Ak.<BR>--3<BR>Old (as age).<BR>--4 Outermost.<BR>--5<BR>Western, west.<BR>--6 Lowest, least.<BR>--मं ind. At last; at the end.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अचलः, --अद्रिः, --क्ष्माभृत् m. the<BR>western mountain behind which the sun<BR>and moon are supposed to set.<BR>--अवस्था the last state (old age).<BR>--कालः the hour of death.<BR>--वयस् a. old,<BR>aged; Māl. 6. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरिः|चरि
चरिः [चर्-इन्] An animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित|चरितं
चरित p. p. [चर् कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Wandered or roamed over, gone.<BR>--2<BR>Performed, practised.<BR>--3 Attained.<BR>--4<BR>Known.<BR>--5 Offered; Ś. 4. 21.<BR>--6<BR>Acted, behaved; Ś. 5. 16.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Going, moving, course.<BR>--2 Acting,<BR>doing, practice, behaviour, acts, deeds;<BR>उदारचरितानां H. 1. 70; सर्वं खलस्य<BR>चरितं मशकः करोति 1. 81.<BR>--3 Life,<BR>biography, adventures, history,; उत्तरं<BR>रामचरितं तत्प्रणीतं प्रयुज्यते U. 1. 2;<BR>दिवौकसरत्वच्चरितं लिखंति Ś. 7. 5; so<BR>दशकुमारचरितं &c.<BR>--4 Nature.<BR>--5<BR>Fixed law, due or proper observance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. {1} that has<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">Page0487-a+ 56</a>]<BR>accomplished its end or desired object,<BR>successful; रामरावणयोर्युद्धं<BR>चरितार्थमिवाभवत् R. 12. 87; चरितार्थैव भारती<BR>10. 36; Ki. 13. 62. {2} satisfied,<BR>contented. {3} effected, accomplished.<BR>{4} significant, true to its sense;<BR>Ku. 2. 17. {5} appropriate, fit;<BR>Ku. 4. 45. ˚ता the attainment of the<BR>desired object; Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0486-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरितव्य
चरितव्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be gone.<BR>--2<BR>To be followed, practised or<BR>performed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरित्रं|चरित्र
चरित्रं [चर् इत्र]<BR>1 Behaviour, habit,<BR>conduct, practice, acts, deeds.<BR>--2<BR>Performance, observance.<BR>--3 History,<BR>life, biography, account, adventures<BR>--4 Nature, disposition.<BR>--5 Duty,<BR>established or instituted observance;<BR>Ms. 2. 20, 9. 7.<BR>--6 A foot, leg.<BR>--7<BR>Going.<BR>--त्रा The tamarind tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बधकः a friendly pledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरिष्णु|चरिष्णुः
चरिष्णु a. [चर्-इष्णुच्] Moveable,<BR>active, wandering about; Ms. 1. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरीत्रं|चरीत्र
चरीत्रं Behaviour, conduct,<BR>practice &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्य|चर्य्य
चर्य a. [चर्-कर्मणि यत्] To be gone;<BR>to be practised &c.<BR>--र्या<BR>1 Going<BR>about, moving, walking about;<BR>driving or going in a carriage; रथ˚ U. 5.<BR>--2 Course, motion; as in राहुचर्या.<BR>--3<BR>Behaviour, conduct, deportment.<BR>--4<BR>Practice, performance, observance;<BR>Ms. 1. 111; व्रतचर्य, तपश्चर्या.<BR>--5 Regular<BR>performance of all rites or customs.<BR>--6 Eating.<BR>--7 A custom, usage;<BR>Ms. 6. 32.<BR>--8 Pervading; visiting.<BR>--र्यं<BR>1 Going about.<BR>--2 Behaviour,<BR>conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चरुः|चरु
चरुः [चर् उन्]<BR>1 An oblation of<BR>rice or barley boiled for presentation<BR>to the gods and the manes:<BR>अनवस्रावी निरुष्मपक्व आंदनश्चरुरिति याज्ञिकाः (It<BR>is often boiled in milk and is called<BR>पयश्चरु; cf. R. 10. 51, 54, 56; or<BR>sprinkled over with butter or ghee.)<BR>--2 A kind of vessel in which an<BR>oblation is prepared.<BR>--3 A cloud.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चेलिन् m. N. of Śiva.<BR>--स्थाली a<BR>vessel for boiling rice &c for<BR>presentation to the gods and the manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्कृतिः|चर्कृति
चर्कृतिः f. Ved. Mention, praise,<BR>glory; Rv. 5. 74. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्घ्
चर्घ् {c1c} P. (चर्घति) To go or move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्च्
चर्च् {vI.v} {c10c} U. (चर्वयति-ते चर्चित).<BR>To read, read carefully, peruse,<BR>study. {vII.v} {c6c} P. (चर्चति, चर्चित)<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">Page0487-b+ 54</a>]<BR>To abuse, condemn, censure, menace.<BR>--2 To discuss, consider,<BR>investigate.<BR>--3 To injure, hurt.<BR>--4 To<BR>anoint, smear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चः|चर्च|चर्च्च
चर्चः [चर्च्-अच्] Considering,<BR>deliberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चक
चर्चक a. [चर्च्-ण्वुल्] Repeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चनं|चर्चन
चर्चनं [चर्च्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Studying,<BR>repetition, reading repeatedly.<BR>--2<BR>Smearing the body with unguents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चरिका
चर्चरिका, चर्चरी [चर्च्-बा˚ अरन् गैरा.<BR>ङीष्]<BR>1 A kind of song.<BR>--2 Striking<BR>the hands to beat time (in music).<BR>--3 The recitation of scholars.<BR>--4<BR>Festive sport, festive cries or<BR>merriment.<BR>--5 A festival.<BR>--6 Flattery.<BR>--7 Curled hair.<BR>--8 Triple symphony.<BR>--9 Alternate recitation of a poem by<BR>two persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चरी|चर्च्चरी
चर्चरिका, चर्चरी [चर्च्-बा˚ अरन् गैरा.<BR>ङीष्]<BR>1 A kind of song.<BR>--2 Striking<BR>the hands to beat time (in music).<BR>--3 The recitation of scholars.<BR>--4<BR>Festive sport, festive cries or<BR>merriment.<BR>--5 A festival.<BR>--6 Flattery.<BR>--7 Curled hair.<BR>--8 Triple symphony.<BR>--9 Alternate recitation of a poem by<BR>two persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चरीकः|चर्चरीक|चर्च्चरीकः
चर्चरीकः<BR>1 Śiva.<BR>--2 Decoration or<BR>curling of the hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चा|चर्च्चा
चर्चा, चर्चिका<BR>1 Repetition,<BR>recitation, study, repeated reading,<BR>perusal.<BR>--2 Discussion, inquiry,<BR>investigation.<BR>--3 Reflection.<BR>--4 Smearing<BR>the body with unguents;<BR>अंगचर्चामरचयं K. 157; श्रीखंडचर्चा विष Gīt. 9.<BR>--5 An epithet of the goddess Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चिका|चर्च्चिका
चर्चा, चर्चिका<BR>1 Repetition,<BR>recitation, study, repeated reading,<BR>perusal.<BR>--2 Discussion, inquiry,<BR>investigation.<BR>--3 Reflection.<BR>--4 Smearing<BR>the body with unguents;<BR>अंगचर्चामरचयं K. 157; श्रीखंडचर्चा विष Gīt. 9.<BR>--5 An epithet of the goddess Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चिः|चर्चि
चर्चिः f. [चर्च् भावे इन्]<BR>1 Repetition.<BR>--2 Investigation (विचारणा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चिक्यं|चर्चिक्य
चर्चिक्यं<BR>1 Anointing the body.<BR>--2<BR>An unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चित|चर्च्चितं
चर्चित p. p.<BR>1 Anointed, smeared,<BR>perfumed, scented &c.;<BR>चंदनचर्चितनीलकलेवरपीतवसनवनमाली Gīt. 1;<BR>Rs. 2. 21.<BR>--2 Discussed, considered,<BR>investigated.<BR>--3 Sought, desired.<BR>--तं<BR>Anointing, smearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्चस्
चर्चस् m. N. of one of the nine<BR>treasures of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्तन
चर्तन a. Ved. Stringing together.<BR>--नं A hook, or pin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्त्य|चर्त्त्यः
चर्त्य a.<BR>1 To be strung or tied.<BR>--2 To be hurt or injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्पटः|चर्पट
चर्पटः [चृप्-अटन्]<BR>1 The open<BR>palm of the hand with the fingers<BR>extended; cf. चपेट.<BR>--2 A<BR>quantity of bubbles or specks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्पटी
चर्पटी A thin cake or biscuit of<BR>flour (पिष्टकभेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्ब्
चर्ब् {c1c} P. (चर्बति)<BR>1 To go, move,<BR>--2 To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्भटः|चर्भट
चर्भटः A kind of cucumber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्भटी
चर्भटी<BR>1 Noise of merriment.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">Page0487-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Cucumber.<BR>--3 A proud or arrogant<BR>saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मं|चर्म|चर्म्म|चर्म्मं
चर्मं<BR>1 A shield.<BR>--2 Ved. A<BR>skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मण्वती|चर्म्मण्वती
चर्मण्वती N. of a river flowing<BR>into the Ganges, the modern<BR>Chambal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मन्|चर्म्मन्
चर्मन् n. [चर्-मनिन् Uṇ. 4. 144]<BR>1 Skin (of the body).<BR>--2 Leather,<BR>hide; Ms. 2. 41, 174.<BR>--3 The sense<BR>of touch.<BR>--4 A shield; Śi. 18. 21.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः a piece or strap of<BR>leather.<BR>--अंभस् n. lymph.<BR>--अवकर्तन working in leather.<BR>--अवकर्तिन,<BR>--अवकर्तृ m. a shoe-maker.<BR>--कारः,<BR>--कारिन्, --कृत् m. {1} a shoe-maker,<BR>currier. {2} a mixed caste (from a<BR>Cāṇḍāla woman and a fisherman).<BR>--कारकः a worker in leather.<BR>--कीलः, --लं a wart.<BR>--चटकः, --का,<BR>--चटिका, --चटी a bat.<BR>--चित्रकं white<BR>leprosy.<BR>--जं {1} hair. {2} blood.<BR>--तरंगः a wrinkle.<BR>--तिल a.<BR>covered with pimples.<BR>--दंडः, --नालिका,<BR>--नासिका a whip.<BR>--दलं, --दूषिका a<BR>kind of leprosy, cutaneous disease.<BR>--द्रुमः, --वृक्षः the Bhūrja tree.<BR>--पट्टिका a flat piece of leather for<BR>playing upon with dice.<BR>--पत्रा a bat,<BR>the small house-bat.<BR>--पादुका a<BR>leather shoe.<BR>--प्रभेदिका a<BR>shoemaker's awl.<BR>--प्रसेवकः, --प्रसेविका<BR>a bellows.<BR>--बंधः a leather band or<BR>strap.<BR>--मुंडा an epithet of Durgā.<BR>--यष्टिः f. a whip.<BR>--वसनः ‘clad in<BR>skin’, N. of Śiva.<BR>--वाद्यं a drum,<BR>tabor &c.<BR>--संभवा large cardamoms.<BR>--सारः lymph, serum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मण्य|चर्म्मण्य
चर्मण्य a. Leathern.<BR>--ण्यं<BR>Leatherwork.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्ममय|चर्म्ममय
चर्ममय a. Leathern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मरुः|चर्मरु|चर्म्मरु|चर्म्मरुः
चर्मरुः, चर्मारः A shoe-maker, a<BR>worker in leather, currier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मारः|चर्मार|चर्म्मार|चर्म्मारः
चर्मरुः, चर्मारः A shoe-maker, a<BR>worker in leather, currier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मिक|चर्म्मिक
चर्मिक a. [चर्भ-ठन्] Armed with<BR>a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्मिन्|चर्म्मिन्
चर्मिन् a. (णी f.) [चर्म-इनि]<BR>1<BR>Armed with a shield.<BR>--2 Leathern.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A soldier armed with a shield.<BR>--2 Plantain.<BR>--3 The Bhūrja tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्या|चर्य्या
चर्या See under चर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्
चर्व् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (चर्वति, चर्बयति-ते,<BR>चर्वित)<BR>1 To chew, chop, eat, browse,<BR>bite; लांगूलं गाढतरं चर्वितुमारब्धवान्<BR>Pt. 4; यस्यैतच्च न कुक्कुरैरहरहर्जंघांतरं<BR>चर्व्यते Mk. 2. 11.<BR>--2 To suck up.<BR>--3 To relish, taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0487-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्वणं|चर्वण|चर्व्वण|चर्व्वणं
चर्वणं, --णा [चर्व् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Chewing, eating.<BR>--2 Sipping, tasting.<BR>--3<BR>Food which must be chewed, solid<BR>food.<BR>--4 (Fig.) Tasting, relishing,<BR>enjoying; प्रमाणं चर्वणैवात्र स्वाभिन्ने<BR>विदुषां मतं S. D. 57; (com. = चर्वणा<BR>आस्वादनं तच्च स्वादः<BR>काव्यार्थसंभेदादात्मानंदसमुद्भव इत्युक्तप्रकारं); so also; निष्पत्त्या<BR>चर्वणस्यास्य निष्पत्तिरुपचारतः 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्वणा
चर्वणं, --णा [चर्व् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Chewing, eating.<BR>--2 Sipping, tasting.<BR>--3<BR>Food which must be chewed, solid<BR>food.<BR>--4 (Fig.) Tasting, relishing,<BR>enjoying; प्रमाणं चर्वणैवात्र स्वाभिन्ने<BR>विदुषां मतं S. D. 57; (com. = चर्वणा<BR>आस्वादनं तच्च स्वादः<BR>काव्यार्थसंभेदादात्मानंदसमुद्भव इत्युक्तप्रकारं); so also; निष्पत्त्या<BR>चर्वणस्यास्य निष्पत्तिरुपचारतः 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्वा|चर्व्वा
चर्वा [चर्व्-अङ्]<BR>1 A blow with the<BR>flat of the hand (said to be also<BR>चर्वन् m.).<BR>--2 Chewing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्वित|चर्व्वित|चर्व्वितं
चर्वित p. p. [चर्व् कर्मणि-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Chewed, bitten, eaten.<BR>--2 Tasted.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चर्वणं (lit.) chewing the<BR>chewed; (fig.) tautology, useless<BR>repetition, profitless reiteration.<BR>--पात्रं a spitting pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्व्य|चर्व्व्य|चर्व्व्यं
चर्व्य a.^1 [चर्व् कर्मणि ण्यत् यत् वा] To<BR>be chewed, chewable.<BR>--र्व्यं Solid<BR>food, such as requires mastication.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Dhaval Patel on 20260624. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/691.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चर्षणि|चर्षणिः
चर्षणि a. [कृष् अनि आदेश्च चः Tv.]<BR>Ved.<BR>1 Seeing, observing.<BR>--2 Moving,<BR>moveable.<BR>--3 Swift active,<BR>--णिः A<BR>man. --f. A disloyal. woman (बंधकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चल्
चल् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (चलति, rarely चलते,<BR>चचाल, अचालीत्, चलितुं, चलित)<BR>1 To shake, tremble, move, throb,<BR>palpitate, stir; छिन्नाश्चेलुः क्षणं भुजाः<BR>Bk. 14. 40; सपक्षोद्रिरिवाचालीत्<BR>15. 24; 6. 84.<BR>--2 (a) To go, move on,<BR>walk, stir or move (from one's place);<BR>पदात्पदमपि चलितुं न शक्नोति Pt. 4; च<BR>लत्येकेन पादेनतिष्ठत्येकेन बुद्धिमान्<BR>Chāṇ. 32; चचाल बाला स्तनभिन्नवल्कला<BR>Ku. 5. 84; Mk. 1. 56. (b) To proceed<BR>(on one's way), depart, set out,<BR>start off; चेलुश्चीरपरिग्रहाः Ku. 6. 92<BR>vl.<BR>--3 To be affected, to be disturbed,<BR>confused or disordered (as mind),<BR>be agitated or perturbed; मुनेरपि<BR>यतस्तस्य दर्शनाच्चलते मनः Pt. 1. 400;<BR>लोभेन बुद्धिश्चलति H. 1. 140.<BR>--4 To<BR>deviate or swerve (with abl.);<BR>चलति नयान्न जिगीषतां हि चेतः<BR>Ki. 10. 29; to fall off, leave; Ms. 7. 15;<BR>Y. 1. 361. --Caus. (च-चा-लयति, चलित,<BR>चालित)<BR>1 To cause to move, shake,<BR>stir; R. 8. 53.<BR>--2 To drive away,<BR>dismiss, remove or expel from;<BR>चाणक्ये चलिताधिकारविमुखे Mu. 4. 15.<BR>--3 To lead away from.<BR>--4 To cherish,<BR>foster (चालयति only).<BR>--5 To<BR>disturb, agitate; सुजनं जनाश्चलयितुं क<BR>ईशते Śi. 15. 40. {vII.v} {c6c} P. (चलति,<BR>चलित) To sport, play, frolic about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चल|चलं|चलः
चल a. [चल्-अच्]<BR>1 (a) Moving,^1<BR>trembling, shaking, tremulous,<BR>rolling (as eyes &c); चलापांगां दृष्टिं<BR>स्पृशसि Ś. 1. 24<BR>चलकाकपक्षकैरमात्यपुत्रैः R. 3. 28. waving; Bh. 1. 16.<BR>(b) Moveable (opp. स्थिर),<BR>moving; चले लक्ष्ये Ś. 2. 5; परिचयं<BR>चललक्ष्यनिपातने R. 9. 49.<BR>--2 Unsteady,<BR>fickle, inconstant, loose, unfixed:<BR>दयितास्वनवस्थितं नृणां न खलु प्रेम चलं<BR>सुहृज्जने Ku. 4. 28; प्रायश्चलं<BR>गौरवमाश्रितषु 3. 1.<BR>--3 Frail, transitory,<BR>perishable; चला लक्ष्मीश्चलाः प्राणाश्चलं<BR>जीवितयौवनं Bh. 3. 128.<BR>--4 Confused.<BR>--लः<BR>1 Trembling, shaking, agitation.<BR>--2<BR>Wind.<BR>--3 Quicksilver.<BR>--4 The<BR>supreme being.<BR>--ला<BR>1 Lakṣmī, the<BR>goddess of wealth.<BR>--2 Lightning.<BR>--3<BR>A kind of perfume.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अचल<BR>a. {1} moveable and immovable. {2}<BR>fickle, unsteady, very transitory<BR>(= अतिचल); चलाचले च संसारे धर्म<BR>एको हि निश्चलः Bh. 3. 128; लक्ष्मीमिव<BR>चलाचलां Ki. 11. 30 (चलाचल = चंचला<BR>Malli.); कस्य न भवति चलाचलं धनं<BR>Mk. 2. 14; N. 1. 60.<BR>--(लः) a crow.<BR>--आतंकः rheumatism.<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>inconstant, fickle-minded.<BR>--इंद्रिय<BR>a. {1} sensitive. {2} sensual.<BR>--इषुः<BR>one whose arrow flies unsteadily or<BR>misses the mark, a bad archer.<BR>--कर्णः the true distance of a planet<BR>from the earth.<BR>--चंचुः the Cakora<BR>bird.<BR>--चित्त a. fickle-minded.<BR>--दलः, --पत्रः the Aśvattha tree.<BR>--संधिः<BR>moveable articulation of the bones.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Scott Rhodes on 20240126. note: Added comma for clarity. Rest are separated by comma. Here, it was only a line break..<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलन|चलनं|चलनः
चलन a. [चल् भावे ल्युट्] Moving,<BR>tremulous, trembling, shaking.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A foot.<BR>--2 A deer.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Trembling, shaking or shaking motion;<BR>चलनात्मकं कर्म T. S.; हस्त˚, जानु˚<BR>&c.;<BR>तरलदृगंचलचलनमनोहरवदनजनितरतिरागं Gīt. 11.<BR>--2 Turning or<BR>leaving off.<BR>--3 Roaming, wandering.<BR>--नी<BR>1 A short petticoat worn by<BR>common women.<BR>--2 The rope for<BR>tying an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलनकं|चलनक|चलनकः
चलनकं [चलनं संज्ञायां कन्] A short<BR>petticoat worn by low women.<BR>--निका Silken fringes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलित|चलितं
चलित p. p. [चल्-क्त]<BR>1 Shaken,<BR>moved, stirred, agitated.<BR>--2 Gone,<BR>departed; एवमुक्त्वा स चलितः.<BR>--3<BR>Attained.<BR>--4 Known, understood.<BR>--5 Removed, displaced. (see चल्).<BR>--तं<BR>1 Shaking, moving.<BR>--2 Going,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">Page0488-c+ 55</a>]<BR>walking.<BR>--3 A kind of dance;<BR>चलितं नाम नाट्यमंतरंण M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलुः|चलु
चलुः [चल-उन्] A mouthful (of<BR>water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलुकः|चलुक
चलुकः [चलुना मीयते कन् Tv.]<BR>1<BR>Water taken up in the hollowed<BR>palm for rinsing the mouth.<BR>--2 A<BR>handful or mouthful (of water);<BR>cf. चुलुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलद्विषः|चलद्विष
चलद्विषः The Kokila or Indian<BR>cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चलिः|चलि
चलिः A cover, wrapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चष्
चष् {vI.v} {c1c} U. (चषति ते) To eat.<BR>{vII.v} {c1c} P. (चषति) To kill, injure,<BR>hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषकः|चषक|चषकं
चषकः --कं [चष्-करणे क्वुन्] A vessel<BR>used for drinking spirits, a goblet,<BR>a wine-glass; च्युतैः शिरस्त्रैश्चषकोत्तरेव<BR>R. 7. 49; मुखं लालाक्लिन्नं पिबति चषकं<BR>सासवमिव Śānti. 1. 29; Ki. 9. 56,<BR>57; Māl. 5. 18.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A kind of<BR>spirituous liquor.<BR>--2 Honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषकं|चषक|चषकः
चषकः --कं [चष्-करणे क्वुन्] A vessel<BR>used for drinking spirits, a goblet,<BR>a wine-glass; च्युतैः शिरस्त्रैश्चषकोत्तरेव<BR>R. 7. 49; मुखं लालाक्लिन्नं पिबति चषकं<BR>सासवमिव Śānti. 1. 29; Ki. 9. 56,<BR>57; Māl. 5. 18.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A kind of<BR>spirituous liquor.<BR>--2 Honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषतिः|चषति
चषतिः [चष्-भावे अति]<BR>1 Eating.<BR>--2 Killing.<BR>--3 Decay, infirmity,<BR>decline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चषालः|चषाल
चषालः<BR>1 A wooden ring on the<BR>top of a sacrificial post.<BR>--2 An iron<BR>ring at the base of that post.<BR>--3 A<BR>hive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चह्
चह् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (चहति, चहयति ते)<BR>1 To be wicked.<BR>--2 To cheat,<BR>deceive.<BR>--3 To be proud or haughty.<BR>--4 To grind, pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाकचक्यं|चाकचक्य
चाकचक्यं Brilliancy, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्र
चाक्र a. (क्री f.) [चक्रेण निर्वृत्तं अण्]<BR>1 Carried on with the discus (as a<BR>battle).<BR>--2 Cincular.<BR>--3 Relating<BR>to a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रिक|चाक्रिकः
चाक्रिक a. (की f.) [चक्रेण चरति<BR>ठक्]<BR>1 See चाक्र above.<BR>--2 Relating<BR>to a company or circle.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>potter.<BR>--2 An oil-maker; Y. 1. 165<BR>(= तैलिक according to Mit.; शाकटिक<BR>or cartman according to others).<BR>--3<BR>A proclaimer.<BR>--4 A bard, chorister.<BR>--5 A coachman, driver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रिणः|चाक्रिण
चाक्रिणः The son of a potter or<BR>oil-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्रेय
चाक्रेय a. [चक्र-ढञ्] Relating to<BR>a wheel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्षुष|चाक्षुषं|चाक्षुषः
चाक्षुष a. (षी f.) [चक्षुषा गृह्यते,<BR>चक्षुस्-अण्]<BR>1 Depending on, or<BR>produced from, sight.<BR>--2 Belonging to<BR>the eye, visual, optical. M. 1. 4.<BR>--3<BR>Visible, to be seen.<BR>--षः N. of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">Page0489-a+ 54</a>]<BR>sixth Manu.<BR>--षं Knowledge<BR>dependent on vision.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञानं<BR>ocular evidence or proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0488-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाक्ष्म
चाक्ष्म a. Ved.<BR>1 Seeing, a seer.<BR>--2 Forbearing, gracious, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांगः|चाङ्ग|चांग|चाङ्गः
चांगः<BR>1 Wood-sorrel.<BR>--2<BR>Whiteness or beauty of the teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांचल्यं|चाञ्चल्य|चांचल्य|चाञ्चल्यं
चांचल्यं [चंचल-ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Unsteadiness, quick motion, rolling,<BR>tremour (as of the eyes &c.);<BR>Bv. 2. 60.<BR>--2 Fickleness.<BR>--3 Transitoriness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटः|चाट
चाटः [चट्-भेदे अच्] A rogue or<BR>cheat, swindler, one who wins the<BR>confidence of the person he wishes<BR>to deceive; Y. 1. 336; (चटाः =<BR>प्रतारकाः विश्वास्य ये परधनमपहरंति Mit.);<BR>Pt. 1. 343.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटकैरः|चाटकैर
चाटकैरः A young sparrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुः|चाटु
चाटुः, --टु n.<BR>1 [चट्-उण्] Pleasing<BR>or agreeable words, sweet or<BR>coaxing speech, flattery (especially of a<BR>lover to his sweet-heart); प्रियः<BR>प्रियायाः प्रकरोति चाटुं Rs. 6. 14;<BR>विरचितचाटुवचनरचनं चरणरचितप्रणिपातं<BR>Gīt. 11; Amaru. 83; Pt. 1. 175;<BR>Śānti. 3. 14; Ch. P. 20; (the greater part<BR>of the 10th canto of गीतगोविंद<BR>consists of such coaxing).<BR>--2 Distinct<BR>or clear speech.<BR>--3 Endearing words<BR>or acts; Māl. 10. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः<BR>f. {1} flattering or coaxing language.<BR>{2} service.<BR>--उल्लोल, --कार a.<BR>speaking agreeably or sweetly, flatterer;<BR>शिप्रावातः प्रियतम इव प्रार्थनाचाटुकारः<BR>Me. 31.<BR>--पटु a. skilful in using<BR>flattering or coaxing language, an<BR>accomplished flatterer.<BR>--बटुः a<BR>jester, buffoon.<BR>--लोल a. elegantly<BR>tremulous.<BR>--शतं a hundred<BR>entreaties, repeated coaxing;<BR>पटुचाटुशतैरनुकूलं Gīt. 2; गजपुंगवस्तु धीर<BR>विलोकयति चाटुशतैश्च भुंक्ते Bh. 2. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटु|चाटुः
चाटुः, --टु n.<BR>1 [चट्-उण्] Pleasing<BR>or agreeable words, sweet or<BR>coaxing speech, flattery (especially of a<BR>lover to his sweet-heart); प्रियः<BR>प्रियायाः प्रकरोति चाटुं Rs. 6. 14;<BR>विरचितचाटुवचनरचनं चरणरचितप्रणिपातं<BR>Gīt. 11; Amaru. 83; Pt. 1. 175;<BR>Śānti. 3. 14; Ch. P. 20; (the greater part<BR>of the 10th canto of गीतगोविंद<BR>consists of such coaxing).<BR>--2 Distinct<BR>or clear speech.<BR>--3 Endearing words<BR>or acts; Māl. 10. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः<BR>f. {1} flattering or coaxing language.<BR>{2} service.<BR>--उल्लोल, --कार a.<BR>speaking agreeably or sweetly, flatterer;<BR>शिप्रावातः प्रियतम इव प्रार्थनाचाटुकारः<BR>Me. 31.<BR>--पटु a. skilful in using<BR>flattering or coaxing language, an<BR>accomplished flatterer.<BR>--बटुः a<BR>jester, buffoon.<BR>--लोल a. elegantly<BR>tremulous.<BR>--शतं a hundred<BR>entreaties, repeated coaxing;<BR>पटुचाटुशतैरनुकूलं Gīt. 2; गजपुंगवस्तु धीर<BR>विलोकयति चाटुशतैश्च भुंक्ते Bh. 2. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाटुकः|चाटुक
चाटुकः, कं Pleasing or grateful<BR>discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कं|क|कः
चाटुकः, कं Pleasing or grateful<BR>discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणकीन|चाणकीनं
चाणकीन a. [चणकस्य भवनं क्षेत्रं,<BR>खञ्] Fit for, or sown with, the<BR>chickpea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणक्यः|चाणक्य
चाणक्यः N. of a celebrated<BR>writer on civil polity; also known as<BR>विष्णुगुप्त, कौटिल्य; see कौटिल्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाणूरः|चाणूर
चाणूरः A celebrated wrestler in<BR>the service of Kaṃsa. When<BR>Kṛṣṇa was taken by Akrūra to<BR>Mathurā, Kaṃsa sent this<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">Page0489-b+ 54</a>]<BR>redoubtable wrestler to fight with him;<BR>but in the duel which ensued,<BR>Kṛṣṇa whirled him round and<BR>round several times and smashed his<BR>head.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मर्दनः, --सूदनः N. of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांडं|चाण्ड
चांडं Violence, force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांडालः|चाण्डाल|चांडाल|चाण्डालः
चांडालः (ली f.) [चंडाल एव स्वार्थे<BR>अण्] An out-cast; see चंडाल;<BR>चांडालः किमयं द्विजातिरथवा Bh. 3. 56;<BR>Ms. 3. 239; 4. 79; Y. 1. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांडालिका|चाण्डालिका
चांडालिका<BR>1 = चंडालिका q. v.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातकः|चातक
चातकः (की f.) [चत् याचने कर्तरि<BR>ण्वुल्] N. of a bird which is<BR>supposed to live only on rain-drops;<BR>सूक्ष्मा एव पतंति चातकमुखे द्वित्राः<BR>पयोबिंदवः Bh. 2. 121; see also 2. 51<BR>and R. 5. 17.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आनंदनः<BR>{1} the rainy season. {2} a cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर|चातुरः
चातुर a. (री f.) [चतुर एव स्वार्थे<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Relating to four.<BR>--2 Clever,<BR>able, shrewd.<BR>--3 Speaking well,<BR>flattering.<BR>--4 Drawn by four<BR>(as a carriage).<BR>--5 Governing,<BR>ruling.<BR>--6 Visible, perceptible.<BR>--रः<BR>A small round pillow.<BR>--रं A<BR>four-wheeled carriage.<BR>--री Skill,<BR>dexterity, ability; तद्भटचातुरीतुरी<BR>N. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरक|चातुरकः
चातुरक a.<BR>1 Flattering.<BR>--2<BR>Perceptible, visible.<BR>--3 Governing.<BR>--कः A small round pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरिकः|चातुरिक
चातुरिकः A charioteer, coachman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरक्षं|चातुरक्ष|चातुरक्षः
चातुरक्षं [चतुर्भिरक्षैर्निष्पाद्यते अण्]<BR>Four casts in playing at dice.<BR>--क्षः<BR>A small round pillow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरर्थिकः|चातुरर्थिक
चातुरर्थिकः [चतुर्षु अर्थेषु विहितः<BR>ठक्] (In gram.) A suffix added to<BR>words in four different senses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुराश्रमिक
चातुराश्रमिक a. (की f.), [चतुर्षु<BR>आश्रमेषु विहितः ठक्], चातुराश्रमिन् a. (णी<BR>f.) Being in one of the four periods<BR>of the religious life of a Brāhmaṇa;<BR>see आश्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुराश्रम्यं|चातुराश्रम्य
चातुराश्रम्यं The four periods of<BR>the religious life of a Brāhmaṇa;<BR>see आश्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुरिकः|चातुरिक
चातुरिकः [चातुरीं रथचर्यां वेत्ति ठक्]<BR>A coachman, driver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्थक|चातुर्थकः
चातुर्थक, --चातुर्थिक a. (की f.) [<BR>चतुर्थे अह्नि भवः ठक् वुञ् वा] Quartan,<BR>occurring every fourth day.<BR>--कः A<BR>quartan ague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्थिक
चातुर्थक, --चातुर्थिक a. (की f.) [<BR>चतुर्थे अह्नि भवः ठक् वुञ् वा] Quartan,<BR>occurring every fourth day.<BR>--कः A<BR>quartan ague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्थाह्निक
चातुर्थाह्निक a. (की f.) Belonging<BR>to the fourth day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्दश|चातुर्द्दश
चातुर्दश a. Appearing on the<BR>fourteenth day.<BR>--शं A demon (Sk.)<BR>(चतुर्दश्यां दृश्यते इति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्दशिक|चातुर्दशिकः|चातुर्द्दशिक
चातुर्दशिक One who studies on the<BR>fourteenth day of a lunar fortnight<BR>(that being a day of अनध्याय q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्भौतिक
चातुर्भौतिक a. Consisting of four<BR>elements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मास|चातुर्म्मास
चातुर्मास a. [चतुर्षु मासेषु भवः अण्]<BR>Produced in four months.<BR>--सी<BR>1 N.<BR>of a sacrifice (इष्टि).<BR>--2 The day of full<BR>moon at this sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मासक
चातुर्मासक a. (सिका f.) One who<BR>performs the Cāturmāsya sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्मास्यं|चातुर्मास्य|चातुर्म्मास्य|चातुर्म्मास्यं
चातुर्मास्यं [चतुर्षु मासेषु भवो यज्ञः, ण्य]<BR>N. of a sacrifice performed every<BR>four months; i. e. at the beginning<BR>of कार्तिक, फाल्गुन and आषाढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्यं|चातुर्य|चातुर्य्य
चातुर्यं [चतुरस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Skill,<BR>cleverness, dexterity, shrewdness.<BR>--2<BR>Loveliness, amiableness, beauty;<BR>भ्रूचातुर्य Bh. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्वर्ण्य|चातुर्व्वर्ण्यं
चातुर्वर्ण्य a. [चतुर्वण-ष्यञ्]<BR>Suited to the four tribes, or belonging to<BR>them.<BR>--र्ण्यं<BR>1 The aggregate of the<BR>four original castes of the Hindus;<BR>एवं सामासिकं धर्मं चातुर्वर्ण्ये ऽब्रवीन्मनुः<BR>Ms. 10. 63; Bg. 4. 13.<BR>--2 The<BR>duties of these four castes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्विद्य
चातुर्विद्य a. (द्यी) Knowing the<BR>four Vedas.<BR>--द्यं The four Vedas;<BR>also चातुर्वैद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्विध्यं|चातुर्विध्य
चातुर्विध्यं Four kinds<BR>(collectively), a four-fold division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्होत्र
चातुर्होत्र a. Conducted by the<BR>four priests.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1 A sacrifice<BR>performed by four priests.<BR>--2 The office<BR>or duties of these priests.<BR>--3 The<BR>four priests taken collectively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुर्होत्रियः|चातुर्होत्रिय
चातुर्होत्रियः A sacrifice<BR>performed by four priests.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुष्कांडिक|चातुष्काण्डिक
चातुष्कांडिक a. Divided into<BR>four parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चातुष्टय
चातुष्टय a. [चतुष्टयं वेत्ति, अण्]<BR>Knowing or familiar with the चतुष्टय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चात्रं|चात्र
चात्रं [चाय् करणे ष्ट्रन्] A cylinder<BR>of catechu-wood used in producing<BR>the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चात्वालः|चात्वाल|चात्वालं
चात्वालः [cf. Uṇ. 1. 113]<BR>1 A<BR>hole in the ground to receive an<BR>oblation or the sacred fire.<BR>--2 Kuśa<BR>grass (दर्भ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0489-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांदनिक|चान्दनिक
चांदनिक a. (की f.) [चंदनेन संपद्यते<BR>ठक्]<BR>1 Made of or derived from<BR>sandal.<BR>--2 Perfumed with sandal<BR>juice &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांद्र|चान्द्र|चान्द्रं|चान्द्रः
चांद्र a. (द्री f.) [चंद्रस्येदम् अण्]<BR>Relating to the moon, lunar;<BR>गुरुकाव्यानुगां बिभ्रच्चांद्रीमभिनभः श्रियं Śi. 2. 2.<BR>--द्रः<BR>1 A lunar month.<BR>--2 The<BR>bright fortnight (शुक्लपक्ष).<BR>--3 The<BR>moon-stone.<BR>--द्रं<BR>1 The vow called<BR>चांद्रायण q. v.<BR>--2 Fresh ginger.<BR>--3 The<BR>lunar mansion called मृगशीर्ष.<BR>--द्री<BR>Moonlight.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आख्यं fresh<BR>ginger.<BR>--भागा the river<BR>Chandrabhāgā.<BR>--मासः a lunar month.<BR>--व्रतिकः one who observes the चांद्रायण<BR>vow q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांद्रकं|चान्द्रक|चांद्रक|चान्द्रकं
चांद्रकं Dried ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांद्रमस|चान्द्रमस|चान्द्रमसं|चान्द्रमसः
चांद्रमस a. (सी f.) [चंद्रमस इदम्<BR>अण्] Relating to the moon, lunar;<BR>लब्धोदया चांद्रमसीव लेखा Ku. 1. 25;<BR>चंद्रं गता पद्मगुणान्न भुंक्ते पद्माश्रिता<BR>चांद्रमसीमभिख्यां 1. 43; R. 2. 39;<BR>Bg. 8. 25.<BR>--सी N. of the wife of<BR>Bṛhaspati.<BR>--सं<BR>1 The constellation मृगशिरस्.<BR>--2 The stars in Orion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांद्रमसायनः|चान्द्रमसायन|चान्द्रमसायनः
चांद्रमसायनः, --निः [चंद्रमसोऽपत्यं फिञ्]<BR>The planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांद्रमसायनिः|चान्द्रमसायनि|चांद्रमसायनि|चान्द्रमसायनिः
चांद्रमसायनः, --निः [चंद्रमसोऽपत्यं फिञ्]<BR>The planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांद्रायणं|चान्द्रायण|चांद्रायण|चान्द्रायणं
चांद्रायणं [चंद्रस्यायनमिवायनमत्र पूर्वपदात्<BR>संज्ञायां णत्वम् संज्ञायां दीर्घः स्वार्थे अण् वा Tv.]<BR>A religious observance or expiatory<BR>penance regulated by the moon's<BR>age (the period of its waxing and<BR>waning); (in it the daily quantity of<BR>food, which consists of fifteen<BR>mouthfuls at the full moon, is diminished<BR>by one mouthful every day during<BR>the dark fortnight till it is reduced<BR>to zero at the new moon, and is<BR>increased in like manner during the<BR>bright fortnight); cf. Y. 3. 324<BR>et seq. and Ms. 11. 217.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांद्रायणिक|चान्द्रायणिक
चांद्रायणिक a. (की f.) One who<BR>performs the चांद्रायण vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापः|चाप|चापं
चापः [चपस्य वंशभेदस्य विकारः अण्<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 A bow; ताते चापद्वितीये<BR>वहति रणधुरां को भयस्यावकाशः Ve. 3. 5;<BR>so चापपाणिः ‘with a bow in hand.’<BR>--2 The rainbow.<BR>--3 (In geom.)<BR>An arc of a circle.<BR>--4 The sign of<BR>the zodiac called Sagittarius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापिन्
चापिन् a. [चापोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>Armed with a bow. --m.<BR>1 N. of Śiva.<BR>--2 The sign of the zodiac Sagittarius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापलं|चापल
चापलं, --ल्यं [चपलस्य भावः कर्म वा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">Page0490-b+ 56</a>]<BR>अण् पक्षे ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Quick motion,<BR>swiftness.<BR>--2 Fickleness,<BR>unsteadiness, transitoriness; Ki. 2. 41.<BR>--3<BR>Inconsiderate or rash conduct,<BR>rashness, rash act; धिक् चापलं U. 4;<BR>तद्गुणैः कर्णमागत्य चापलाय प्रचोदितः<BR>R. 1. 9; स्वचित्तवृत्तिरिव चापलेभ्यो<BR>निवारणीया K. 101; Ku. 3. 41.<BR>--4<BR>Restiveness (as of a horse); पुनः पुनः<BR>सूतनिषिद्धचापलं R. 3. 42.<BR>--5<BR>Boldness; Ku. 5. 40.<BR>--6 Agitation,<BR>tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चापल्यं|चापल्य
चापलं, --ल्यं [चपलस्य भावः कर्म वा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">Page0490-b+ 56</a>]<BR>अण् पक्षे ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Quick motion,<BR>swiftness.<BR>--2 Fickleness,<BR>unsteadiness, transitoriness; Ki. 2. 41.<BR>--3<BR>Inconsiderate or rash conduct,<BR>rashness, rash act; धिक् चापलं U. 4;<BR>तद्गुणैः कर्णमागत्य चापलाय प्रचोदितः<BR>R. 1. 9; स्वचित्तवृत्तिरिव चापलेभ्यो<BR>निवारणीया K. 101; Ku. 3. 41.<BR>--4<BR>Restiveness (as of a horse); पुनः पुनः<BR>सूतनिषिद्धचापलं R. 3. 42.<BR>--5<BR>Boldness; Ku. 5. 40.<BR>--6 Agitation,<BR>tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरः|चामर|चामरं
चामरः, --रं [चमर्याः विकारः<BR>तत्पुच्छनिर्मितत्वात्] (also<BR>--रा --री sometimes)<BR> A chowrie or bushy tail of the<BR>Camara (Bos Grunniens) used as<BR>a fly-flap or fan, and reckoned as one<BR>of the insignia of royalty (and<BR>sometimes used as a sort of streamer<BR>on the heads of horses); व्याधूयंते<BR>निचुलतरुभिर्मंजरीचामराणि V. 4. 4;<BR>अदेयमासीत् त्रयमेव भूपतेः शशिप्रभं<BR>छत्रमुभे च चामरे R. 3. 16; Ku. 7. 42;<BR>H. 2. 29; Me. 35; चित्रन्यस्तमिवाचलं<BR>हयशिरस्यायामवच्चामरं V. 1. 4; Ś. 1. 8.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्राहः, --ग्राहिन् m. a person<BR>who carries a chowrie.<BR>--ग्राहिणी a<BR>waiting girl who carries in her hand<BR>a chowrie and waves it over the head<BR>of a king &c.; पृष्ठे लीलावलयरणितं<BR>चामरग्राहिणीनां Bh. 3. 61.<BR>--पुष्पः,<BR>--पुष्पकः {1} the betel-nut tree. {2} the<BR>Ketaka plant. {3} the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरं|चामर|चामरः
चामरः, --रं [चमर्याः विकारः<BR>तत्पुच्छनिर्मितत्वात्] (also<BR>--रा --री sometimes)<BR> A chowrie or bushy tail of the<BR>Camara (Bos Grunniens) used as<BR>a fly-flap or fan, and reckoned as one<BR>of the insignia of royalty (and<BR>sometimes used as a sort of streamer<BR>on the heads of horses); व्याधूयंते<BR>निचुलतरुभिर्मंजरीचामराणि V. 4. 4;<BR>अदेयमासीत् त्रयमेव भूपतेः शशिप्रभं<BR>छत्रमुभे च चामरे R. 3. 16; Ku. 7. 42;<BR>H. 2. 29; Me. 35; चित्रन्यस्तमिवाचलं<BR>हयशिरस्यायामवच्चामरं V. 1. 4; Ś. 1. 8.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्राहः, --ग्राहिन् m. a person<BR>who carries a chowrie.<BR>--ग्राहिणी a<BR>waiting girl who carries in her hand<BR>a chowrie and waves it over the head<BR>of a king &c.; पृष्ठे लीलावलयरणितं<BR>चामरग्राहिणीनां Bh. 3. 61.<BR>--पुष्पः,<BR>--पुष्पकः {1} the betel-nut tree. {2} the<BR>Ketaka plant. {3} the mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरिकः|चामरिक
चामरिकः A person who carries a<BR>chowrie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामरिन्
चामरिन् m. [चामर-इनि] A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामीकरं|चामीकर
चामीकरं [चमीकरे स्वर्णाकरभेदे भवम्<BR>अण् Tv.]<BR>1 Gold; तप्तचामीकरांगदः<BR>V. 1. 14; R. 7. 5; Śi. 4. 24;<BR>Ku. 7. 49.<BR>--2 The Dhattūra plant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रख्य a. like gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चामुंडा|चामुण्डा
चामुंडा A terrific form of Durgā;<BR>Māl. 5. 25; (the word is thus<BR>derived; यस्माच्चंडं च मुंडं च गृहीत्वा त्वमुपागता ।<BR>चामुंडोति ततो लोके ख्याता देवी भविष्यसि ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांपिला|चाम्पिला
चांपिला The river Campā;<BR>(perhaps the modern Chambal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांपेयः|चाम्पेय|चांपेय|चाम्पेयः
चांपेयः<BR>1 The Campaka tree.<BR>--2 The Nāgakeśara tree.<BR>--यं<BR>1<BR>Filament, especially of a lotus flower.<BR>--2 Gold.<BR>--3 The Dhattūra plant;<BR>(m. also in the last two senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चांपेयकं|चाम्पेयक|चाम्पेयकं
चांपेयकं A stamen or filament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाम्यं|चाम्य
चाम्यं Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाय्
चाय् {c1c} U. (चायति-ते)<BR>1 To observe,<BR>discern, see; तं पार्वतीयप्रमदाश्चचायिरे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">Page0490-c+ 56</a>]<BR>विकाशविस्फारितविभ्रमेक्षणाः Śi. 12. 51.<BR>--2 To worship honour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चायनीय
चायनीय a. To be worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चायितृ
चायितृ a. Ved. Observing, seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चायु
चायु a. [चाय्-उण्] Worshipping,<BR>adoring, honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारः|चार|चारं
चारः [चर एव अण्]<BR>1 Going, walking,<BR>gait, wandering about; मंडलचारशीघ्रः<BR>V. 5. 2; क्रीडाशैले यदि च विचरेत्<BR>पादचारेण गौरी Me. 60 walk on foot.<BR>--2<BR>Motion, course, progression;<BR>मंगलचार; शनिचार, राहु˚ &c.<BR>--3 A spy, scout,<BR>secret emissary; Ms. 7. 184; 9. 261;<BR>see चारचक्षुस् below.<BR>--4 Performing,<BR>practising.<BR>--5 A prison.<BR>--6 A bond,<BR>fetter.<BR>--रं An artificial poison.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरितः a spy.<BR>--ईक्षणः,<BR>--चक्षुस् m. ‘using spies as eyes’, a<BR>king (or a statesman) who employs<BR>spies and sees through their<BR>medium; चारचक्षुर्महीपतिः Ms. 9. 256; cf.<BR>Kāmandaka: --गावः पश्यंति गंधेन वेदैः<BR>पश्यंति च द्विजाः । चारैः पश्यंति<BR>राजानश्चक्षुर्भ्यामितरे जनाः ॥ also Rām.:<BR>--यस्मात्पश्यन्ति दूरस्थाः सर्वानर्थान्नराधिपाः ।<BR>चारेण तस्मादच्यंते राजानश्चारचक्षुषः ॥<BR>--चण, --चंचु a. graceful in gait, of<BR>graceful carriage.<BR>--ज्या the sine of the<BR>ascensional difference.<BR>--पथः a<BR>place where two roads meet.<BR>--भटः a<BR>valorous man, warrior.<BR>--भटी courage.<BR>--वायुः summer-air, zephyr.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारक|चारकः
चारक a. [चारयति चर्-णिच्-ण्वुल्]<BR>Acting, doing, proceeding.<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>A spy.<BR>--2 A herdsman.<BR>--3 A leader,<BR>driver.<BR>--4 An associate.<BR>--5 A<BR>groom, cavalier.<BR>--6 A prison;<BR>निगडितचरणा चारके निरोद्धव्या Dk. 32.<BR>--7<BR>A bond, fetter.<BR>--8 Going, motion.<BR>--9 A wandering Brāhmaṇical<BR>student.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारणः|चारण
चारणः [चारयति कीर्तिं चर्-णिच् ल्यु]<BR>1<BR>A wanderer, a pilgrim.<BR>--2 A<BR>wandering actor or singer, a dancer,<BR>mimic, bard; Ms. 12. 44.<BR>--3 A<BR>celestial singer, heavenly chorister;<BR>Ś. 2. 14.<BR>--4 A reader of scriptures.<BR>--5<BR>A spy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दाराः female<BR>dancers, actresses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारणत्वं|चारणत्व
चारणत्वं The art of dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारथ
चारथ a. Ved. Wandering, going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारिका
चारिका A female attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित
चारित a.<BR>1 Caused to go.<BR>--2<BR>Distilled &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारितार्थ्यं|चारितार्थ्य
चारितार्थ्यं Attainment of an<BR>object, successfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0490-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारित्रं|चारित्र
चारित्रं [चर्-णित्रन् Uṇ. 4. 171;<BR>चरित्रमेव स्वार्थे अण् वा] (also written<BR>चारित्र्यं)<BR>1 Conduct, behaviour, manner<BR>of acting.<BR>--2 Good name or character,<BR>reputation, probity, uprightness, good<BR>conduct; अनृतं नाभिधास्यामि<BR>चारित्रभ्रंशकारणं Mk. 3. 26, 25; चारित्र्यविहीन<BR>आढ्योपि च दुर्गतो भवति 1. 43.<BR>--3<BR>Chastity, purity of life (of women).<BR>--4<BR>Disposition, temperament.<BR>--5<BR>Peculiar observance or practice.<BR>--6<BR>Hereditary observance.<BR>--त्रा The<BR>tamarind tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कवच a.<BR>clad in the armour of chastity.<BR>--देवता the presiding deity of virtue or<BR>chastity; U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारिन्
चारिन् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>1 Walking, going, moving, being,<BR>living; पाद˚, मृग˚.<BR>--2 Acting,<BR>proceeding, doing.<BR>--3 Living or feeding<BR>on. --m. A footsoldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चारु|चारुः
चारु a. (रु or र्वी f.) [चरति चित्ते चर्<BR>उण्, cf. Uṇ. 1. 3]<BR>1 Agreeable,<BR>welcome, beloved. esteemed, dear (with<BR>dat. or loc.); वरुणाय or वरुणे चारुः.<BR>--2 Pleasing, lovely, beautiful,<BR>elegant, pretty; प्रिये चारुशीले मुंच मयि<BR>मानमनिदानं Gīt. 10; सर्वं प्रिये चारुतरं<BR>वसंते Rs. 6. 2; चकासतं<BR>चारुचमूरुचर्मणा Śi. 1. 8; 4. 49.<BR>--रुः An epithet<BR>of Bṛhaspati.<BR>--रु n. Saffron.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगी a beautifully formed<BR>woman.<BR>--घोण a. handsome-nosed.<BR>--दर्शन a. good-looking, lovely.<BR>--धामा, --धारा, --रावा Śacī, Indra's<BR>wife.<BR>--नेत्र, --लोचन a. having<BR>beautiful eyes.<BR>--(नेत्रः, --नः) a deer.<BR>--पुटः<BR>a particular time in music.<BR>--फला<BR>a vine, grape.<BR>--लोचना a woman<BR>with lovely eyes.<BR>--वक्त्र a. having<BR>a beautiful face.<BR>--वर्धना a woman.<BR>--व्रता a female who fasts for a<BR>whole month.<BR>--शिला {1} a jewel,<BR>gem. {2} a beautiful slab of stone.<BR>--शील a. of a lovely disposition or<BR>character.<BR>--हासिन् a. sweet-smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्चिक
चार्चिक a. Conversant with the<BR>repetition (of the Veda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्चिक्यं|चार्चिक्य|चार्च्चिक्य|चार्च्चिक्यं
चार्चिक्यं<BR>1 Perfuming the<BR>person, smearing with sandal &c.<BR>--2<BR>An unguent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्म|चार्म्म|चार्म्मः
चार्म a. (र्मी f.) [चर्मणा परिवृतः<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Leathern.<BR>--2 Covered with<BR>leather (as a car).<BR>--3 Shielded,<BR>provided with a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मण|चार्म्मण|चार्म्मणं
चार्मण a. (णी f.) Covered with skin<BR>or leather.<BR>--णं [चर्मणां समूहः अण्]<BR>A multitude of hides or shields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मिक|चार्म्मिक
चार्मिक a. (की f.) [चर्मणा निर्वृत्तः<BR>ठक्] Made of leather; Ms. 8. 289.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्मिणं|चार्मिण|चार्म्मिण|चार्म्मिणं
चार्मिणं [चर्मिणां समूहः अण्] A<BR>number of men armed with shields.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्वाकः|चार्वाक|चार्व्वाक|चार्व्वाकः
चार्वाकः [चारुः लोकसंमतो वाको वाक्यं<BR>यस्य, पृषो˚ Tv.]<BR>1 N. of a sophistical<BR>philosopher (said to have been a<BR>pupil of Bṛhaspati), who<BR>propounded the grossest form of atheism<BR>or materialism (for a summary of<BR>the doctrines of Cārvāka, see<BR>Sarva. S. 1.).<BR>--2 N. of a Rākṣasa<BR>described in the Mahābhārata, as<BR>a friend of Duryodhana and an<BR>enemy of the Pāṇḍavas. [When<BR>Yudhiṣṭhira entered Hastināpura in<BR>triumph, he assumed the form of a<BR>Brāhmaṇa and reviled him and the<BR>assembled Brāhmaṇas, but he was soon<BR>detected, and the real Brāhmaṇas,<BR>filled with fury, are said to have killed<BR>him on the spot. He also tried to<BR>deceive Yudhiṣṭhira at the end of the<BR>great war by telling him that Bhīma<BR>was slain by Duryodhana; see Ve. 6].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चार्वी|चार्व्वी
चार्वी<BR>1 A beautiful woman.<BR>--2<BR>Moonlight.<BR>--3 Intelligence.<BR>--4<BR>Splendour, lustre, brilliancy.<BR>--5<BR>N. of the wife of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालः|चाल
चालः [चल्-ण]<BR>1 The thatch or<BR>roof of a house.<BR>--2 The blue jay.<BR>--3 Being moveable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालकः|चालक
चालकः A restive elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालनं|चालन
चालनं [चल्-णिच् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Causing to move, shaking, wagging (as<BR>a tail).<BR>--2 Loosening.<BR>--3 Muscular<BR>action.<BR>--4 Causing to pass through<BR>a sieve, sifting.<BR>--5 A sieve.<BR>--नी A<BR>sieve, strainer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चालनीय
चालनीय a.<BR>1 To be moved.<BR>--2<BR>To be loosened or shaken; also<BR>चाल्य in the same sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चाषः|चाष
चाषः --सः [चष् भक्षणे स्वार्थे णिच्-अच्]<BR>The blue jay; Māl. 6. 5; Y. 1. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चासः|चास
चाषः --सः [चष् भक्षणे स्वार्थे णिच्-अच्]<BR>The blue jay; Māl. 6. 5; Y. 1. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चि
चि {vI.v} {c5c} U. (चिनोति, चिनुते,<BR>चिकाचा-य, चिच्ये-क्ये, अचैषीत्-अचेष्ट, चेतुं, -चित;<BR>caus. चाययति, चापयति, also चययति,<BR>चपयति, desid. चिचीषति, -चिकीषति)<BR>1<BR>To collect, gather, accumulate (said<BR>to govern two accusatives being a<BR>द्विकर्मक root, but this use is very<BR>rare in classical literature); वृक्षं<BR>पुष्पाणि चिन्वती.<BR>--2 To gather for<BR>oneself, acquire, gain; चिचीषतां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-c" target="_blank">Page0491-c+ 56</a>]<BR>जन्मवतामलघ्वीं भूतिं Ki. 3. 11, 2. 19,<BR>Mv. 3. 4.<BR>--3 To search, look out for;<BR>Bh. 3. 46.<BR>--4 To pile or heap up, place<BR>in a line; पर्वतानिव ते<BR>भूमावचैर्षुवानरोत्तमान् Bk. 15. 76.<BR>--5 To set, inlay,<BR>cover or fill with, see चित. --pass. To<BR>bear fruit, grow, increase, thrive,<BR>prosper; सिच्यते चीयते चैव लता<BR>पुष्पफलप्रदा Pt. 1. 222 bears fruit; चीयते<BR>बालिशस्यापि सत्क्षेत्रपतिता कृषिः Mu. 1. 3;<BR>गजहंस तव सैव शुभ्रता चीयते न च न<BR>चापचीयते K. P. 10. {vII.v} {c3c} P. (चिकेति)<BR>Ved.<BR>1 To observe, see, perceive.<BR>--2<BR>To look steadfastly upon.<BR>--3 To be<BR>intent upon.<BR>--4 To seek for, search,<BR>investigate, make inquiries, search<BR>through. {vIII.v} {c1c} A. (चयते)<BR>1<BR>To detest, hate.<BR>--2 To revenge, take<BR>vengeance on. {vIV.v} {c1c} U. (चायति-ते)<BR>1 To fear, dread, be afraid of (with<BR>acc.).<BR>--2 To respect, honour.<BR>--3 To<BR>observe; cf. चाय्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चयः|चय
चयः [चि-अच्]<BR>1 An assemblage,<BR>collection, multitude, heap, mass;<BR>चयस्त्विषामित्यवधारितं पुरा Śi. 1. 3;<BR>मृदां चयः U. 2. 7 a lump of clay;<BR>कचानां चयः Bh. 1. 5 a braid of hair;<BR>so चमरीचयः Śi. 4. 60; कुसुमचय,<BR>तुषारचय &c.<BR>--2 A mound of earth<BR>raised to form the foundation of a<BR>building.<BR>--3 A mound of earth<BR>raised from the ditch of a fort.<BR>--4 A rampart.<BR>--5 The gate of<BR>a fort.<BR>--6 A seat, stool.<BR>--7 A<BR>pile of buildings, any edifice.<BR>--8 Stacked wood.<BR>--9 A cover, or<BR>covering.<BR>--10 Arranging or keeping<BR>the sacred fire; cf. अग्निचय.<BR>--11 The<BR>amount by which each term<BR>increases, the common increase or<BR>difference of the terms (in a<BR>progression).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चयनं|चयन
चयनं [चि भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>1 The act of<BR>collecting (especially flowers &c.).<BR>--2 Piling, heaping.<BR>--3 Keeping the<BR>sacred fire.<BR>--4 Stacking wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित|चितः
चित p. p. [चि-क्त]<BR>1 Collected,<BR>piled up, heaped, gathered.<BR>--2<BR>Hoarded, accumulated.<BR>--3 Got, acquired.<BR>--4 Covered with, full of;<BR>कृमिकुलचितं Bh. 2. 9.<BR>--5 Set or inlaid with.<BR>--तं A building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिता
चिता<BR>1 A funeral pile, pyre; कुरु<BR>संप्रति तावदाशु भे<BR>प्रणिपातांजलियाचितश्चितां Ku. 4. 35; चिताधिरोहणं R. 8. 57;<BR>चिताभस्मन् Ku. 5. 69.<BR>--2 A heap,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">Page0492-a+ 56</a>]<BR>assemblage, multitude.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः the funeral fire.<BR>--चूडकं a pyre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0491-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चितिः|चिति
चितिः f. [चि-आघारे क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>Collecting, gathering.<BR>--2 A heap, multitude,<BR>quantity.<BR>--3 A layer, pile, stack.<BR>--4 A<BR>funeral pile.<BR>--5 An oblong with<BR>quadrangular sides.<BR>--6 The<BR>understanding. --m. The thinking mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चितिका
चितिका<BR>1 A pile, stack.<BR>--2 A<BR>funeral pile.<BR>--3 A small chain (or<BR>girdle) worn as an ornament round<BR>the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्य|चित्यं|चित्यः
चित्य a.<BR>1 To be arranged in order<BR>or built up.<BR>--2 Constructed upon a<BR>foundation (as fire).<BR>--त्यं<BR>1 The place<BR>at which a corpse is burnt.<BR>--2 A<BR>monument.<BR>--त्या<BR>1 A funeral pile.<BR>--2<BR>Piling up, building (as an altar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेय
चेय pot. p.<BR>1 To be piled up.<BR>--2<BR>To be gathered or collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित
चिकित a. [चि ज्ञाने कर्मणि क्त]<BR>Known, understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकितान
चिकितान a. [कित् ज्ञाने कानच्]<BR>Knowing, perceiving, understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकितु
चिकितु a. [कित् उन् वेदे द्वित्वम्] Ved.<BR>Knowing, experienced. --f.<BR>Understanding, intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्वन्
चिकित्वन् m. Ved. Intellect,<BR>wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्वस्
चिकित्वस् a. Ved. Knowing,<BR>conversant or familiar with,<BR>experienced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्वित्
चिकित्वित् a. Knowing,<BR>conversant with; making known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सकः|चिकित्सक
चिकित्सकः [कित् स्वार्थे सन् ण्वुल्] A<BR>physician, doctor; उचितवेलातिक्रमे<BR>चिकित्सका दोषमुदाहरंति M. 2;<BR>Bh. 1. 87, Y. 1. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सनं|चिकित्सन
चिकित्सनं Healing, practising<BR>medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सा
चिकित्सा [कित् स्वार्थे सन् भावे अ]<BR>1<BR>Administering remedies or<BR>medicine, medical treatment, curing,<BR>healing.<BR>--2 (In the system of<BR>medicine) Therapeutics, one of the six<BR>sections (or स्थानानि) of medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकित्सित|चिकित्सितं
चिकित्सित a. [कित् स्यार्थे सन् कर्मणि<BR>क्त] Healed, cured.<BR>--तं Healing,<BR>curing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकिन|चिकिनः
चिकिन a. Flat-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकिलः|चिकिल
चिकिलः Mud, a slough, mire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षक
चिकीर्षक a. [कृ-सन् ण्वुल्]<BR>Wishing or meaning to do, desirous of<BR>doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षा
चिकीर्षा Desire of doing<BR>(anything), will, wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षित
चिकीर्षित a. Wished, desired,<BR>purposed.<BR>--तं Design, intention,<BR>purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकीर्षु|चिकीर्षुः
चिकीर्षु a. Desirous of doing<BR>anything, desirous for; Bg. 1. 23; 3. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकुर|चिकुरः
चिकुर a.<BR>1 Moving, tremulous,<BR>fickle, unsteady.<BR>--2 Inconsiderate,<BR>rash.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The hair of the head; मम<BR>रुचिरे चिकुरे कुरु मानद…कुसुमानि<BR>Gīt. 12; so घनचयरुचिरे रचयति चिकुरे<BR>तरलिततरुणानने 7.<BR>--2 A mountain.<BR>--3<BR>A musk-rat.<BR>--4 A reptile, snake.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उच्चयः, --कलापः, --निकरः,<BR>--पक्षः, --पाशः, --भारः, --हस्तः a mass or<BR>tuft of hair; यस्याश्चोरश्चिकुरनिकरः<BR>कर्णपूरो मयूरः P. R. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिकूरः|चिकूर
चिकूरः The hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्क्
चिक्क् {c10c} U. (चिक्कयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>give or inflict pain, distress.<BR>--2 To<BR>feel pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्क|चिक्कः
चिक्क a. Flat-nosed.<BR>--क्कः The<BR>musk-rat.<BR>--क्का<BR>1 A mouse.<BR>--2 A<BR>betel-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कण|चिक्कणं|चिक्कणः
चिक्कण a. (णा or णी f.)<BR>[चिक्क्-क्विप् चिक्, तं कणति, कण्--शब्दे अच् Tv.]<BR>1 Smooth, glossy.<BR>--2 Slippery.<BR>--3<BR>Bland.<BR>--4 Unctuous, greasy; लघु<BR>परित्रायतामेनां भवान् मा कस्यापि तपस्विन<BR>इंगुदीतैलचिक्कणशीर्षस्य हस्ते पतिष्यति<BR>Ś. 2.<BR>--णः The betel-nut tree.<BR>--णा<BR>An excellent cow.<BR>--णं A betel-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कणा
चिक्कणा, --णी<BR>1 The betel-nut tree.<BR>--2 A betel-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कणी
चिक्कणा, --णी<BR>1 The betel-nut tree.<BR>--2 A betel-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्कसः|चिक्कस
चिक्कसः Rarley-meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्किण
चिक्किण = चिक्कण q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्किरः|चिक्किर
चिक्किरः [चिक्क् बा˚ इरच्] A mouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिक्लिदं|चिक्लिद|चिक्लिदः
चिक्लिदं Moisture; freshness.<BR>--दः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिखल्लः|चिखल्ल
चिखल्लः Mud, mire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंगटः|चिङ्गट|चिङ्गटः
चिंगटः A shrimp or prawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिचिंडः|चिचिण्ड|चिचिण्डः
चिचिंडः A sort of gourd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिच्छिलाः
चिच्छिलाः (m. pl.) N. of a<BR>country and its people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंचा|चिञ्चा
चिंचा<BR>1 The tamarind tree, or<BR>its fruit.<BR>--2 The Guñjā plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिट्
चिट् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (चेटति, चेटयति-ते)<BR>To send forth or out (as a servant.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्
चित् {c1c} P., {c10c} A. (चेतति, चेतयते,<BR>चेतित)<BR>1 To perceive, see, notice,<BR>observe; नेषूनचेतन्नस्यंतं Bk. 17. 16;<BR>चिचेत रामस्तत्कृच्छ्रं 14. 62; 15. 38;<BR>2. 29.<BR>--2 To know, understand, be<BR>aware or conscious of;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-c" target="_blank">Page0492-c+ 57</a>]<BR>परैरध्यारुह्यमाणमात्मानं न चेतयते Dk. 154;<BR>कादंबरीरसभरेण समस्त एव मत्तो न किंचिदपि<BR>चेतयते जनोयं K. 240.<BR>--3 To<BR>regain consciousness.<BR>--4 To aim<BR>at, intend, design (with dat.).<BR>--5 To desire or long for.<BR>--6 To be<BR>anxious about, care for, be intent<BR>upon, be engaged in.<BR>--7 To resolve<BR>upon.<BR>--8 To appear, shine.<BR>--9 To be<BR>regarded as.<BR>--10 To make attentive,<BR>remind of.<BR>--11 To teach, instruct.<BR>--12 To form an idea, be conscious<BR>of, understand, comprehend, think,<BR>reflect upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्
चित् f. [चित्-संपदा˚ भावे क्विप्]<BR>1<BR>Thought, preception.<BR>--2 Intelligence,<BR>intellect, understanding; Bh. 2. 1;<BR>3. 1.<BR>--3 The heart, mind.<BR>--4 The<BR>soul, spirit, the animating principle<BR>of life.<BR>--5 Brahman.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् m. {1} the thinking principle or<BR>faculty. {2} pure intelligence, the<BR>Supreme Spirit.<BR>--आत्मकं<BR>consciousness.<BR>--आभासः the individual soul<BR>(जीव) (which still sticks to worldly<BR>defilements).<BR>--उल्लासः gladdening<BR>the heart or spirit.<BR>--घनः the<BR>Supreme Spirit or Brahman.<BR>--प्रवृत्तिः<BR>f. reflection, thinking.<BR>--रूप a. {1}<BR>consisting of intelligence. {2} wise,<BR>intelligent, of a liberal mind. {3}<BR>amiable, good-hearted.<BR>--(पं) pure<BR>intelligence, the Supreme Being.<BR>--शक्तिः f. mental power, intellectual<BR>capacity.<BR>--स्वरूपं the Supreme spirit.<BR>--ind. {1} A particle added to किं and<BR>its derivatives (such as कद्, कथं, क्व,<BR>कदा, कुत्र, कुतः &c.) to impart<BR>to them an indefinite sense;<BR>कुत्रचित् somewhere; केचित् some &c. {2}<BR>The sound चित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्मय
चिन्मय a. Consisting of pure<BR>intelligence, spiritual (as the Supreme<BR>spirit).<BR>--यं<BR>1 Pure intelligence.<BR>--2<BR>The Supreme spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिन्मात्रं|चिन्मात्र
चिन्मात्रं Pure intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्त|चित्तं
चित्त p. p. [चित्-क्त]<BR>1 Observed,<BR>perceived.<BR>--2 Considered, reflected or<BR>meditated upon.<BR>--3 Resolved.<BR>--4<BR>Intended, wished, desired.<BR>--5<BR>Visible, perceptible.<BR>--त्तं<BR>1 Observing,<BR>attending.<BR>--2 (a) Thought, thinking,<BR>attention; (b) desire, intention, aim;<BR>मच्चित्तः सततं भव Bg. 18. 57;<BR>अनेकचित्तविभ्रांत 16. 16.<BR>--3 The mind;<BR>यदासौ दुर्वारः प्रसरति मदश्चित्तकरिणः<BR>Śānti. 1. 22; so चलचित्त and comps. below.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-a" target="_blank">Page0493-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--4 The heart (considered as the<BR>seat of intellect).<BR>--5 Reason,<BR>intellect, reasoning faculty.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुवर्तिन् a. acting according to<BR>one's will, humouring.<BR>--अपहा --क,<BR>--अपहारिन्, --आकर्षिन्, --हारिन् a. {1}<BR>‘heart-stealing,’ attractive,<BR>captivating. {2} pleasing, agreeable,<BR>beautiful.<BR>--आभोगः attention of the mind<BR>to its own feelings, exclusive<BR>attachment to one thing.<BR>--आसंगः<BR>attachment, love.<BR>--उद्रेकः pride,<BR>arrogance.<BR>--ऐक्यं agreement,<BR>unanimity.<BR>--उन्नतिः, --समुन्नतिः f. {1}<BR>noble-mindedness. {2} pride,<BR>arrogance.<BR>--कलित a. anticipated,<BR>expected, calculated.<BR>--चारिन् a. acting<BR>according to the will of another.<BR>--जः, --जन्मन् m.,<BR>--भूः, --योनिः {1}<BR>love, passion. {2} Cupid, the god of<BR>love; चित्तयोनिरभवत्पुनर्नवः<BR>R. 19. 46; सोयं प्रसिद्धविभवः खलु चित्तजन्मा<BR>Māl. 1. 20.<BR>--ज्ञ a. knowing the<BR>mind of another.<BR>--नाशः loss of<BR>conscience.<BR>--निर्वृतिः f.<BR>contentment, happiness.<BR>--प्रमाथिन् a.<BR>moving or touching the heart,<BR>exciting passion or love.<BR>--प्रशम a.<BR>composed, tranquil.<BR>--(मः) tranquility<BR>of heart.<BR>--प्रसन्नता joy, pleasure.<BR>--भेदः {1} difference of view. {2}<BR>inconsistency, inconstancy.<BR>--मोहः<BR>infatuation of the mind.<BR>--रागः<BR>affection, passion, desire.<BR>--विकारः change<BR>of thought or feeling.<BR>--विक्षेपः<BR>distraction of the mind.<BR>--विप्लवः,<BR>--विभ्रमः aberration, disturbance or<BR>derangement of mind, madness,<BR>insanity.<BR>--विश्लेषः breach of<BR>friendship.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. {1} disposition or<BR>state of the mind, inclination,<BR>feeling;<BR>एवमात्माभिप्रायसंभावितेष्टजनचित्तवृत्तिः प्रार्थयिता विडंब्यते Ś. 2. {2}<BR>thinking, imagining. {3} inward<BR>purpose, emotion. {4} (in Yoga phil.)<BR>inward working of the mind,<BR>mental vision; योगश्चित्तवृत्तिनिरोधः Yoga<BR>S.<BR>--वेदना affliction, anxiety.<BR>--वैकल्यं bewilderment of the mind,<BR>distraction.<BR>--संख्य a. pervading the<BR>heart, penetrating the soul.<BR>--हारिन्<BR>a. fascinating, attractive, agreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0492-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तवत्|चित्तवन्त्
चित्तवत् a.<BR>1 Reasonable,<BR>endowed with reason.<BR>--2 Kind-hearted,<BR>amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तिः|चित्ति
चित्तिः f. [चित् भावे क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-b" target="_blank">Page0493-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Thinking, thought, reflection.<BR>--2<BR>Understanding, wisdom.<BR>--3 Devotion.<BR>--4<BR>Intention, aim, purpose.<BR>--5 A wise<BR>person.<BR>--6 Fame, celebrity (ख्याति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्तिन्
चित्तिन् a. Ved. Intelligent, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतक
चेतक a.<BR>1 Causing to think.<BR>--2<BR>What thinks or feels, sentient.<BR>--की N. of a plant (हरीतकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतन|चेतनः
चेतन a. (नी f.) [चित्-ल्यु]<BR>1<BR>Animate, alive, living, sentient, feeling;<BR>चेतनाचेतनेषु Me. 5 animate and<BR>inanimate.<BR>--2 Visible, conspicuous,<BR>distinguished.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A sentient<BR>being, a man.<BR>--2 Soul, mind.<BR>--3 The<BR>supreme soul.<BR>--4 An animal in<BR>general.<BR>--ना<BR>1 Sense, consciousness;<BR>चुलुकयति मदीयां चेतनां चंचरीकः<BR>R. G.; U. 3. 31; Māl. 9. 12, R. 12. 74;<BR>चेतनां प्रतिपद्यते regains one's<BR>consciousness.<BR>--2 Understanding,<BR>intelligence; पश्चिमाद्यामिनीयामात्प्रसादमिव<BR>चेतना R. 17. 1.<BR>--3 Life, vitality,<BR>animation; Bg. 13. 6.<BR>--4 Wisdom,<BR>reflection.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Appearance.<BR>--2 The<BR>thinking principle, the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतनावत्|चेतनावन्त्
चेतनावत् a. Animate, having<BR>consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतस्
चेतस् n. [चित् करणे असुन्]<BR>1<BR>Consciousness, sense.<BR>--2 Thinking soul,<BR>reasoning faculty.<BR>--3 The mind,<BR>heart, soul; चेतः प्रसादयति Bh. 2. 23;<BR>गच्छति पुरः शरीरं धावति पश्चादसंस्तुतं<BR>चेतः Ś. 1. 34.<BR>--4 Will.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जन्मन्,<BR>--भवः, --भूः m. {1} love, passion. {2}<BR>the god of love.<BR>--विकारः<BR>disturbance of the mind, emotion,<BR>agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेतोमत्|चेतोमन्त्
चेतोमत् a. Living, sentient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र|चित्रं|चित्रः
चित्र a. [चित्र्-भावे अच्; चि-ष्ट्रन् वा<BR>Uṇ. 4. 163]<BR>1 Bright, clear.<BR>--2<BR>Variegated, spotted, diversified.<BR>--3<BR>Amusing, interesting, agreeable;<BR>Māl. 1. 4.<BR>--4 Various, different,<BR>manifold; Pt. 1. 136; Ms. 9. 248;<BR>Y. 1. 288.<BR>--5 Surprising, wonderful,<BR>strange; किमत्र चित्रं R. 5. 33;<BR>Ś. 2. 15.<BR>--6 Perceptible, visible.<BR>--7<BR>Conspicuous, excellent, distinguished.<BR>--8 Rough, agitated (as the sea, opp.<BR>सम).<BR>--9 Clear, loud, perceptible (as<BR>a sound).<BR>--त्रः<BR>1 The variegated<BR>colour.<BR>--2 A form of Yama.<BR>--3 The<BR>Aśoka tree.<BR>--4 = चित्रगुप्त q. v. below.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1 A picture, painting,<BR>delineation; चित्रे निवेश्य<BR>परिकल्पितसत्त्वयोगा Ś. 2. 9; पुनरपि चित्रीकृता<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-c" target="_blank">Page0493-c+ 57</a>]<BR>कांता Ś. 6. 20, 13, 21 &c.<BR>--2 A<BR>brilliant ornament or ornament.<BR>--3 An<BR>extraordinary appearance, wonder.<BR>--4 A sectarial mark on the forehead.<BR>--5 Heaven, sky.<BR>--6 A spot.<BR>--7 The<BR>white or spotted leprosy.<BR>--8 (In<BR>Rhet.) The last of the three main<BR>divisions of Kāvya (poetry). It<BR>is of two kinds शब्दचित्र and<BR>अर्थ-वाच्य-चित्र, and the poetical charm lies<BR>mainly in the use of figures of speech<BR>dependent on the sound or sense of<BR>words. Mammaṭa thus defines it:<BR>--शब्दचित्रं वाच्यचित्रमव्यंग्यं त्ववरं स्मृतं<BR>K. P. 1. As an instance of शब्दचित्र may be<BR>cited the following verse from R. G.<BR>मित्रात्रिपुत्रनेत्राय त्रयीशात्रवशत्रवे ।<BR>गोत्रारिगोत्रजैत्राय गोत्रात्रे ते नमो नमः ॥.<BR>--9 Anything<BR>bright which strikes the eye.<BR>--10<BR>Playing upon words, punning,<BR>using conundrums, riddles &c.<BR>--त्रं<BR>ind. Oh!, how strange!, what a<BR>wonder! चित्रं बधिरो नाम<BR>व्याकरणमध्येष्यते Sk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षी, --नेत्रा,<BR>--लोचना a kind of bird commonly<BR>called Sārikā.<BR>--अंग a. striped,<BR>having a spotted body.<BR>--(गः) {1} a<BR>kind of snake. {2} N. of Arjuna.<BR>--(गं) {1} vermilion. {2} yellow<BR>orpiment.<BR>--अंगद a. decked with<BR>brilliant bracelets.<BR>--(दा) N. of a<BR>wife of Arjuna and mother of<BR>Babhruvāhana.<BR>--अंगदसूः f. an<BR>epithet of Satvavatī, mother of Vyāsa.<BR>--अन्नं rice dressed with coloured<BR>condiments; Y. 1. 304.<BR>--अपूपः a<BR>kind of cake.<BR>--अर्पित a. committed<BR>to a picture, painted. ˚आरंभ a.<BR>painted; R. 2. 31; Ku. 3. 42.<BR>--आकृतिः f. a painted resemblance,<BR>portrait.<BR>--आयसं steel.<BR>--आरंभः a<BR>painted scene, outline of a picture;<BR>V. 1. 4. v. l.<BR>--उक्तिः f. {1} agreeable or<BR>eloquent discourse; जयंति ते<BR>पंचमनादमित्रचित्रोक्तिसंदर्भविभूषणेषु<BR>Vikr. 1. 10. {2} a voice from heaven. {3} a<BR>surprising tale.<BR>--ओदनः boiled rice<BR>coloured with turmeric &c.<BR>--कंठः<BR>a pigeon.<BR>--कथालापः telling<BR>agreeable or charming stories.<BR>--कंबलः {1}<BR>painted cloth used as an elephant's<BR>housing. {2} a variegated carpet.<BR>--कर. {1} a painter. {2} an actor.<BR>--कर्मन् n. {1} an extraordinary act.<BR>{2} ornamenting, decorating. {3} a<BR>picture; Mu. 2. 4. {4} magic. (--m.). {1} a<BR>magician, one who works wonders. {2}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-a" target="_blank">Page0494-a+ 57</a>]<BR>a painter. ˚विद् m. {1} a painter. {2} a<BR>magician.<BR>--कायः {1} a tiger in<BR>general. {2} a leopard or panther.<BR>--कारः<BR>{1} a painter. {2} N. of a mixed tribe;<BR>(स्थपतेरपि गांधिक्यां चित्रकारो व्यजायत<BR>Parāśara).<BR>--कूटः N. of a hill and<BR>district near Prayāga;<BR>R. 12. 15, 13. 47, U. 1.<BR>--कृत् a.<BR>astonishing, surprising. (--m.) a painter.<BR>--कोलः a kind of lizard.<BR>--क्रिया<BR>painting.<BR>--क्षत्र a. Ved. having<BR>manifold power, or one whose<BR>wealth is visible.<BR>--ग, --गत a. {1}<BR>painted, drawn in a picture. {2}<BR>coloured, variegated.<BR>--गंधं yellow<BR>orpiment.<BR>--गुप्तः one of the beings<BR>in Yama's world recording the vices<BR>and virtues of mankind;<BR>Mu. 1. 20.<BR>--गृहं a painted room.<BR>--जल्पः<BR>a random or incoherent talk, talk<BR>on various subjects.<BR>--तंडुंल a<BR>medicinal plant said to possess<BR>anthelmintic virtues.<BR>--त्वच् m. the Bhūrja<BR>tree.<BR>--दंडकः the cotton-plant.<BR>--न्यस्त a. painted, drawn in a<BR>picture; Ku. 2. 24.<BR>--पक्षः the<BR>francoline partridge.<BR>--पटः, --ट्टः {1} a<BR>painting, a picture. {2} a coloured or<BR>chequered cloth.<BR>--पद a. {1} divided<BR>into various parts. {2} full of<BR>graceful expressions.<BR>--पादा the bird<BR>called Sārikā.<BR>--पिच्छकः a peacock.<BR>--पुंखः a kind of arrow.<BR>--पृष्ठः a<BR>sparrow.<BR>--प्रतिकृतिः f. representation<BR>in colours, a painting, picture.<BR>--फलकं a tablet for painting, a<BR>pictureboard.<BR>--बर्हः a peacock.<BR>--भानु a.<BR>of a variegated colour, shining with<BR>light.<BR>--(नुः) {1} fire. {2} the sun;<BR>(चित्रभानुर्विभातीति दिने रवौ रात्रौ वह्नौ<BR>K. P. 2 given as an instance of<BR>one of the modes of अंजन). {3} N.<BR>of Bhairava. {4} the Arka plant.<BR>{5} Śiva. {6} an epithet of the<BR>Aśvins. {7} the first year of the first<BR>cycle of Jupiter.<BR>--भूत a. painted.<BR>--मंडलः a kind of snake.<BR>--मृगः the<BR>spotted antelope.<BR>--मेखलः a peacock.<BR>--योधिन् a. fighting in a<BR>wonderful manner. (--m.) an epithet of<BR>Arjuna.<BR>--रथः {1} the sun. {2} N.<BR>of a king of the Gandharvas,<BR>one of the sixteen sons of Kaśyapa<BR>by his wife Muni; अत्र<BR>मुनेस्तनयश्चित्रसेनादीनां पंचदशानां भ्रातॄणामधिको<BR>गुणैः षोडशश्चित्ररथो नाम समुत्पन्नः<BR>K. 136; V. 1.<BR>--लिखनं painting.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-b" target="_blank">Page0494-b+ 58</a>]<BR>--लिखित a. {1} painted. {2} dumb,<BR>motionless (as in a picture).<BR>--लेख a. of beautiful outlines,<BR>highly arched; रुचिस्तव कलावती<BR>रुचिरचित्रलेखे भ्रुवौ Gīt. 10.<BR>--(खा) {1}<BR>a portrait, picture. {2} N. of a friend<BR>and companion of Uṣā, daughter<BR>of Bāṇa. [When Uṣā related to her<BR>her dream, she suggested the idea of<BR>taking the portraits of all young<BR>princes in the neighbourhood; and on<BR>Uṣā's recognising Aniruddha,<BR>Chitralekhā, by means of her magical power,<BR>conveyed him to her palace].<BR>--लेखकः<BR>a painter.<BR>--लेखनिका a painter's<BR>brush.<BR>--वदालः the sheat-fish.<BR>--वनं<BR>N. of a forest near the Gaṇḍakī.<BR>--वाजः a cock.<BR>--विचित्र a. {1}<BR>variously coloured, variegated. {2}<BR>multiform.<BR>--विद्या the art of painting.<BR>--शाला a painter's studio.<BR>--शिखंडिन् m. an epithet of the seven<BR>sages:--मरीचि, अंगिरस्, अत्रि, पुलस्त्य,<BR>पुलह, क्रतु and वसिष्ठ. ˚जः an epithet<BR>of Bṛhaspati.<BR>--शिरस् m.,<BR>--शीर्षकः<BR>a kind of venomous insect.<BR>--श्रीः<BR>great or wonderful beauty.<BR>--संस्थ<BR>a. painted.<BR>--हस्तः a particular<BR>position of the hands in fighting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0493-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रक|चित्रकं|चित्रकः
चित्रक a.<BR>1 Bright, lovely,<BR>agreeable.<BR>--2 Brave, powerful.<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>A painter.<BR>--2 A tiger in general.<BR>--3 A small hunting leopard.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of a tree.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A sectarial mark on<BR>the forehead.<BR>--2 A particular<BR>manner of fighting.<BR>--3 N. of a wood<BR>near the mountain Raivataka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रयति
चित्रयति Den. P.<BR>1 To make<BR>variegated, paint.<BR>--2 To regard as<BR>wonderful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रल|चित्रलः
चित्रल a. Variegated, spotted.<BR>--लः The variegated colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रा
चित्रा [चित्र्-अच्]<BR>1 N. of the<BR>fourteenth lunar mansion<BR>consisting of one star; हिमनिर्मुक्तयोर्योगे<BR>चित्राचंद्रमसोरिव R. 1. 46.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of snake.<BR>--3 Worldly illusion,<BR>unreality.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अटीरः {1} the<BR>moon. {2} the forehead spotted<BR>with the blood of a goat offered as<BR>a victim to a deity.<BR>--ईशः the<BR>moon.<BR>--मघा the dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिकः|चित्रिक
चित्रिकः The month Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिणी
चित्रिणी N. for a woman<BR>‘endowed with various talents and<BR>excellences’, one of the four divisions<BR>into which writers on erotic<BR>science class women:<BR>--पद्मिनी, चित्रिणी,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">Page0494-c+ 57</a>]<BR>शंखिनी and हस्तिनी or करिणी. The<BR>Ratimañjarī thus defines चित्रिणी : -<BR>भवति रतिरसज्ञा नातिखर्वा न दीर्घा<BR>तिल्कुसुमसुनासा स्निग्धनीलोत्पलाक्षी । घनकठिनकुचाढ्या<BR>सुंदरी बद्धशीला सकलगुणविचित्रा चित्रिणी<BR>चित्रवक्त्रा ॥ {5}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रित
चित्रित a.<BR>1 Variegated, spotted.<BR>--2 Painted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रिन्
चित्रिन् a. (णी f.) [चित्र्-णिनि;<BR>चित्र-अस्त्यर्थे इनि वा]<BR>1 Wonderful.<BR>--2<BR>Variegated.<BR>--3 Having variegated<BR>(black and gray) hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीकृ
चित्रीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To feel wonder.<BR>--2 To adorn, embellish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीकरणं|चित्रीकरण
चित्रीकरणं, --कारः Wonder,<BR>surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीकारः|चित्रीकार
चित्रीकरणं, --कारः Wonder,<BR>surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीकृत
चित्रीकृत a. Painted, embellished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्रीयते
चित्रीयते Den. A.<BR>1 To cause<BR>wonder, to be an object of wonder;<BR>एवमुत्तरोत्तरभावश्चित्रीयते जीवलोकः<BR>Mv. 5; Bk. 17. 64; 18. 23.<BR>--2 To<BR>wonder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चित्र्य
चित्र्य a. To be honoured or<BR>worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंत्|चिन्त्
चिंत् {c10c} U. (चिंतयति-ते, चिंतित)<BR>1<BR>To think, consider, reflect, ponder<BR>over; तच्छ्रुत्वा पिंगलकश्चिंतयामास Pt. 1<BR>चिंतय तावत्केनापदेशेन पुनराश्रमपदं<BR>गच्छामः Ś. 2.<BR>--2 To think of, have an idea<BR>of, bring before the mind;<BR>तस्मादेतत् (वित्तं) न चिंतयेत् H. 1; तस्मादस्य;<BR>वधं राजा मनसापि न चिंतयेत्<BR>Ms. 8. 381, 4. 258; Pt. 1. 135; Ch. P. 1.<BR>--3 To mind, take care of, look to;<BR>तातस्त्वां चिंतयिष्यति Ś. 4.; cf. also<BR>R. 1. 64; U. 1. 19.<BR>--4 To call to<BR>mind, remember.<BR>--5 To find out,<BR>devise, discover, think out;<BR>कोप्युपायश्चिंत्यतां H. 1.<BR>--6 To regard as,<BR>esteem.<BR>--7 To weigh, discriminate.<BR>--8 To discuss, treat of, consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंतक|चिन्तक
चिंतक a. [चिंत्-ण्वुल्] Thinking<BR>upon, reflecting on (at the end of<BR>comp); as दैव˚ an astrologer; उपाय˚.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंतनं|चिन्तन|चिंतन
चिंतनं, --ना [चिंत्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Thinking, thinking of, having an idea of;<BR>मनसाऽनिष्टचिंतनं Ms. 12. 5.<BR>--2<BR>Thought, reflection.<BR>--3 Anxious<BR>thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंतना
चिंतनं, --ना [चिंत्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Thinking, thinking of, having an idea of;<BR>मनसाऽनिष्टचिंतनं Ms. 12. 5.<BR>--2<BR>Thought, reflection.<BR>--3 Anxious<BR>thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंता|चिन्ता
चिंता [चिंत्-भावे अ]<BR>1 Thinking,<BR>thought.<BR>--2 Sad or sorrowful<BR>thought, care, anxiety; चिंताजडं<BR>दर्शनं Ś. 4. 5; so वीतचिंतः 12.<BR>--3<BR>Reflection, consideration.<BR>--4 (In Rhet.)<BR>Anxiety, considered as one of the<BR>33 subordinate feelings; ध्यानं चिंता<BR>हितानाप्तेः शून्यताश्वासतापकृत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">Page0495-a+ 55</a>]<BR>S. D. 201.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आकुल a. full of<BR>care, disturbed in mind, anxious.<BR>--कर्मन् n. anxiety.<BR>--पर a. thoughtful,<BR>anxious.<BR>--मणिः {1} a fabulous gem<BR>supposed to yield to its possessor<BR>all desires, the philosopher's stone;<BR>काचमूल्येन विक्रीतो हंत चिंतामणिर्मया<BR>Śānti. 1. 12; अपि<BR>चिंतामणिश्चिंतापरिश्रममपेक्षते Māl. 10. 22; तदेकलुब्धे हृदि<BR>मेऽस्ति लब्धुं चिता न चिंतामणिमप्यनर्ध्यं<BR>N. 3. 81, 1. 145. {2} N. of Brahmā.<BR>--वेश्मन् n. a council-hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0494-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंतित|चिन्तित|चिन्तितं
चिंतित a.<BR>1 Thought, reflected.<BR>--2<BR>Devised, found out.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Reflection, thought.<BR>--2 Care, attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंतितिः|चिन्तिति|चिंतिति|चिन्तितिः
चिंतितिः f., चिंतिया Consideration,<BR>reflection, thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंत्य|चिन्त्य
चिंत्य pot. p. [चिंत् कर्मणि यत्]<BR>1<BR>To be considered or thought over.<BR>--2 To be discovered, to be devised<BR>or found out.<BR>--3 Conceivable,<BR>comprehensible.<BR>--4 Requiring<BR>consideration, doubtful, questionable, यच्च<BR>क्वचिदस्फुटालंकारत्वे उदाहृतं (यः कौमारहरः<BR>&c.) एतच्चिंत्यं S. D. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिंतिडी|चिन्तिडी
चिंतिडी The tamarind tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपट|चिपटः
चिपट a. Flat-nosed.<BR>--टः Rice<BR>or grain flattened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपिटः|चिपिट
चिपिटः a. See चिपट.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रीव<BR>a. short-necked.<BR>--नास, --नासिक a.<BR>flat-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपिटकः|चिपिटक
चिपिटकः, --चिपुटः Flattened rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिपुटः|चिपुट
चिपिटकः, --चिपुटः Flattened rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिप्पः|चिप्प
चिप्पः A disease of the<BR>fingernail; also चिप्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिबुकं|चिबुक
चिबु(वु)कं The chin; चिबुकं<BR>सुदृशः स्पृशामि यावत् Bv. 2. 34; Y. 3. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिवुकं|चिवुक|चिवुकः
चिबु(वु)कं The chin; चिबुकं<BR>सुदृशः स्पृशामि यावत् Bv. 2. 34; Y. 3. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिमिः|चिमि
चिमिः A parrot; also चिमिकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिर|चिरं
चिर a. [चि-रक्] Long, lasting a<BR>long time, existing from a long<BR>time, old; चिरविरहः चिरकालः चिरमित्रं<BR>&c.<BR>--रं A long time. Note.--The<BR>singular of any of the oblique cases<BR>of चिर may be used adverbially in<BR>the sense of ‘long’, ‘for a long time,’<BR>‘after a long time,’ ‘long since,’ ‘at<BR>last,’ ‘finally;’ न चिरं पर्वते वसेत्<BR>Ms. 4. 60; ततः प्रजानां चिरमात्मना धृतां<BR>R. 3. 35, 62; Amaru. 79;<BR>कियच्चिरेणार्यपुत्रः प्रतिपत्तिं दास्यति Ś. 6; R. 5. 64;<BR>प्रीतास्मि ते सौम्य चिराय जीव R. 14. 59;<BR>Ku. 5. 47; Amaru. 3; चिरात्सुतस्पर्शरसज्ञतां<BR>ययौ R. 3. 26; 11. 63, 12. 87; चिरस्य<BR>वाच्यं न गतः प्रजापतिः Ś. 5. 15; चिरे<BR>कुर्यात् Śat. Br.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आयुस् a.<BR>long-lived. (--m.) a god.<BR>--आरोधः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-b" target="_blank">Page0495-b+ 55</a>]<BR>a protracted siege, blockade.<BR>--उत्थ<BR>a. existing for a long time.<BR>--कार,<BR>--कारिक, --कारिन्, --क्रिय a. acting slowly,<BR>delaying, tarrying, dilatory.<BR>--कालः<BR>a long time.<BR>--कालिक, --कालीन a. {1} of<BR>long standing, old, long-continued.<BR>{2} chronic (as a disease).<BR>--जात<BR>a. born long ago, old.<BR>--जीविन् a.<BR>long-lived (--m.) {1} an epithet<BR>of seven persons who are considered<BR>to be ‘deathless’; अश्वत्थामा<BR>बलिर्व्यासो हनुमांश्च बिभीषणः । कृपः परशुरामश्च<BR>सप्तैते चिरजीविनः ॥. {2} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>{3} a crow. {4} N. of two plants<BR>जीवक &c. शाल्मलि.<BR>--पाकिन् a.<BR>ripening late.<BR>--पुष्पः the Bakula tree.<BR>--मित्रं an old friend.<BR>--मेहिन् m. an<BR>ass.<BR>--रात्रं a period of many nights,<BR>a long time. ˚उषित a. having lodged<BR>for a long time.<BR>--विप्रोषित a. long<BR>banished, a long sojourner.<BR>--सूता,<BR>--सूतिका a cow that has borne many<BR>calves.<BR>--सेवकः an old servant.<BR>--स्थ,<BR>स्थायिन्, --स्थित a. lasting, long,<BR>enduring, continuing; durable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरंजीव
चिरंजीव a. Long lived.<BR>--वः An<BR>epithet of Kāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरंटी|चिरण्टी
चिरंटी, चिरिंटी [चिरेण अटति पितृगृहात्<BR>भर्तृगेहं अट् अच् पृषो˚ Tv.]<BR>1 A woman<BR>married or single who continues to<BR>reside after maturity in her father's<BR>house.<BR>--2 A young woman (in<BR>general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरिंटी|चिरिण्टी
चिरंटी, चिरिंटी [चिरेण अटति पितृगृहात्<BR>भर्तृगेहं अट् अच् पृषो˚ Tv.]<BR>1 A woman<BR>married or single who continues to<BR>reside after maturity in her father's<BR>house.<BR>--2 A young woman (in<BR>general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरत्न|चिरत्नः
चिरत्न a. (त्नी f.) [चिरे भवः चिर-त्न]<BR>Of long standing, old, ancient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरंतन|चिरन्तन|चिरन्तनः
चिरंतन a. (नी f.) [चिरं भवार्थे ट्युल्<BR>तुट् च] Of long standing, old,<BR>ancient; स्वहस्तदत्ते मुनिमासनं<BR>मुनिश्चिरंतनस्तावदभिन्यवीविशत् Śi. 1. 15; चिरंतनः<BR>सुहृद् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरायति
चिरायति Den. P.; also चिरायते<BR>To delay, tarry; कथं चिरयति<BR>पांचाली Ve. 1; किं चिरायितं भवता;<BR>संकेतके चिरयति प्रवरो विनोदः Mk. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरिः|चिरि
चिरिः A parrot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिरि|चिरिः
