चिहण
चिहण a. = चिक्कण q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिहुर
चिहुर = चिकुर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्न्
चिह्न् {c10c} U. (चिह्नयति-ते) To mark,<BR>stamp (properly a Denom. from the<BR>noun चिह्न).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्नं|चिह्न
चिह्नं<BR>1 Mark, spot, stamp,<BR>symbol; emblem, badge, symptom;<BR>ग्रामेषु यूपचिह्नेषु R. 1. 44; 3. 55;<BR>संनिपातस्य चिह्नानि Pt. 1. 177.<BR>--2 A sign,<BR>indication; प्रसादचिह्नानि पुरःफलानि<BR>R. 2. 22; प्रहर्षचिह्न 2. 68.<BR>--3 A sign<BR>of the zodiac.<BR>--4 Stamp, print,<BR>impression; पद˚.<BR>--5 Aim, direction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारिन् a. {1} marking,<BR>spotting. {2} striking, wounding,<BR>killing. {3} frightful, hideous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चिह्नित|चिह्नितः
चिह्नित a.<BR>1 Marked, signed,<BR>stamped, bearing the badges of an<BR>office; Y. 2. 85; 1. 319; दिवा चरेयुः<BR>कार्यार्थं चिह्निता राजशासनैः<BR>Ms. 10. 55, 2. 170.<BR>--2 Branded.<BR>--3 Known,<BR>designated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीक्
चीक् {c1c} {c10c} P. (चीकति, चीकयति)<BR>1 To endure, bear, suffer.<BR>--2 To<BR>be impatient.<BR>--3 To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीत्कारः|चीत्कार
चीत्कारः An onomatopoetic word,<BR>the cry of certain animals,<BR>particularly of the ass or elephant; स<BR>विषीदति चीत्काराद्रर्दभस्ताडितो यथा<BR>H. 2. 31; वैनायक्यश्चिरं वो वदनविधुतयः<BR>पांतु चीत्कारवत्यः Māl. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनः|चीन|चीनं
चीनः [चि-नक् पृषो˚ दीर्घः]<BR>1 N. of<BR>a country, the modern China.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of deer.<BR>--3 A sort of cloth.<BR>--4 A thread.<BR>--नाः (m. pl.) The<BR>rulers or people of China.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>A banner.<BR>--2 A kind of bandage<BR>for the corners of the eyes.<BR>--3 Lead.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुकं, --वासस् n.<BR>Chinacloth, silk, silken cloth;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">Page0496-a+ 55</a>]<BR>चीनांशुकमिव केतोः प्रतिवातं नीय्म नस्य<BR>Ś. 1. 34; Ku. 7. 3; Māl. 6. 5;<BR>Amaru. 75.<BR>--कर्पूरः a kind of camphor.<BR>--जं steel.<BR>--पट्टं lead.<BR>--पिष्टं {1} red<BR>lead. {2} lead.<BR>--वंगं lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0495-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीनाकः|चीनाक
चीनाकः A kind of camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीभ्
चीभ् {c1c} A. (चीभते)<BR>1 To coax,<BR>wheedle, flatter.<BR>--2 To boast,<BR>swagger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरं|चीर
चीरं [चि-क्रन् दीर्घश्च; Uṇ. 2. 26]<BR>1 A rag, a tattered cloth, a long<BR>stripe or garment; Ms. 6. 6.<BR>--2 A<BR>bark.<BR>--3 A cloth or garment in<BR>general.<BR>--4 A necklace of pearls<BR>consisting of four strings.<BR>--5 A<BR>stripe, stroke, line.<BR>--6 A manner<BR>of writing with strokes.<BR>--7 Lead.<BR>--8 A crest.<BR>--9 The dress of a<BR>Buddhist priest.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--परिग्रह,<BR>--वासस् a. {1} clothed in bark;<BR>Ku. 6. 92; Ms. 11. 102. {2} dressed in<BR>rags or tatters. (--m.) an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--भवंती the elder sister<BR>of a wife (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरकः|चीरक
चीरकः A manner of writing, see<BR>चीर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरित
चीरित a. Having strips, ragged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरिन्
चीरिन् a. [चीर-इनि] Clothed in<BR>bark, garments or rags.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरिः|चीरि
चीरिः f. [चि बा˚ क्रि दीर्घश्च]<BR>1 A<BR>veil for covering the eyes.<BR>--2 A<BR>cricket.<BR>--3 The hem of an<BR>undergarment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरिका
चीरि(रु)का A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीरुका
चीरि(रु)का A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीर्ण|चीर्णं|चीर्ण्ण
चीर्ण a. [चर्-नक् पृषो˚ अत ईत्वम्]<BR>1<BR>Done, performed, observed.<BR>--2<BR>Studied, repeated.<BR>--3 Split,<BR>divided.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पर्णः the Kharjūra<BR>and Nimba trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीलिका
चीलिका A cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीव्
चीव् {vI.v} {c1c} U. (चीवति-ते)<BR>1 To wear,<BR>cover.<BR>--2 To take or receive.<BR>--3<BR>To seize. {vII.v} {c10c} U. (चीवयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>shine.<BR>--2 To speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीवरं|चीवर
चीवरं [चि-ष्वरच् नि˚दीर्घः; चीव्-अरच्<BR>वा; cf. Uṇ. 3. 1]<BR>1 A garment (in<BR>general); a tatter, rag; प्रेतचीवरवसा<BR>स्वनोग्रया R. 11. 16.<BR>--2 The dress<BR>of any mendicant, particularly of a<BR>Buddhist mendicant; चीवराणि<BR>परिधत्ते Sk.; चीरचीवरपरिच्छदां Māl. 1;<BR>प्रक्षालितमेतन्मया चीवरखंडं Mk. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चीवरिन्
चीवरिन् m.<BR>1 A Buddhist or<BR>Jaina mendicant.<BR>--2 A mendicant<BR>(in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्क्
चुक्क् {c10c} U. (चुक्कयति-ते) To<BR>inflict or suffer pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्कारः|चुक्कार
चुक्कारः The roaring of a lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्रः|चुक्र|चुक्रं
चुक्रः [चक्-रक् अत उत्वं च<BR>Uṇ. 2. 15]<BR>1 A kind of cane or sorrel.<BR>--2<BR>Sourness.<BR>--क्रं Sourness, acidity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अम्लं vinegar made by the<BR>acetous fermentation of grain.<BR>--(म्ला) {1} a tamarind tree. {2} a<BR>kind of sour rice-gruel.<BR>--फलं the<BR>tamarind fruit.<BR>--वास्तूकं wood-sorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्रकं|चुक्रक
चुक्रकं, चुक्रिका A kind of<BR>woodsorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्रिका
चुक्रकं, चुक्रिका A kind of<BR>woodsorrel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्रा
चुक्रा The tamarind tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्रिमन्
चुक्रिमन् m. Sourness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुक्षा
चुक्षा<BR>1 Injuring, killing.<BR>--2<BR>Washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचिः|चुचि
चुचिः The female breast; udder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचुकः|चुचुक|चुचुकं
चुचुकः, --कं, चुचूकं The nipple<BR>of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचुकं|चुचुक|चुचुकः
चुचुकः, --कं, चुचूकं The nipple<BR>of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुचूकं|चुचूक
चुचुकः, --कं, चुचूकं The nipple<BR>of the breast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंचु|चुञ्चु|चुञ्चुः
चुंचु a. (At the end of certain<BR>comp.) Celebrated, famous,<BR>renowned, skilled in; अक्षर˚, चार˚ &c.<BR>--चुः<BR>1 The musk-rat or shrew.<BR>--2 A<BR>mixed caste born of a Brāhmaṇa<BR>father and Vaideha female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंचुरी|चुञ्चुरी
चुंचुरी A game played with<BR>tamarind seeds instead of dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुट्
चुट् {vI.v} {c6c} {c10c} P. (चुटति, चोटयति)<BR>To cut off, divide. {vII.v} {c1c} {c10c} P.<BR>(चोटति, चोटयति) To become small,<BR>to be diminished, wane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुट्ट्
चुट्ट् {c10c} P. (चुट्टयति) To become<BR>small or shallow (as a river.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुड्
चुड् I. {c6c} P. (चुडति) To conceal<BR>or hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुड्ड्
चुड्ड् {c1c} P. (चुड्डति)<BR>1 To dally,<BR>sport.<BR>--2 To hint one's meaning.<BR>--3 To act or do.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुण्
चुण् {c6c} P. (चुणति) To cut off,<BR>pierce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंट्|चुण्ट्
चुंट् {vI.v} {c1c} {c10c} P. (चुंटति, चुंटयति) To<BR>cut off. {vII.v} {c1c} P. To become small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंड्|चुण्ड्
चुंड् {vI.v} {c1c} P. To become small.<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} P. To cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंटा|चुण्टा
चुंटा, --डा A small well or<BR>reservoir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंडा
चुंटा, --डा A small well or<BR>reservoir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुत्
चुत् {c1c} P. (चोतति) To ooze,<BR>trickle, see च्युत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुतः|चुत
चुतः The anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुद्
चुद् {vI.v} {c10c} U. (चोदयति-ते, --चोदित)<BR>1<BR>To send, direct, throw forward,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">Page0496-c+ 55</a>]<BR>urge or drive on, push on;<BR>चोदयाश्वान् Ś. 1.<BR>--2 To prompt, inspire,<BR>impel, animate, excite; R. 4. 24.<BR>--3 To hasten, accelerate.<BR>--4 To<BR>question, ask.<BR>--5 To press with a<BR>request.<BR>--6 To put forward, adduce,<BR>as an argument or objection.<BR>--7 To enjoin, lay down;<BR>Ms. 2. 165.<BR>--8 To request, solicit.<BR>--9<BR>To help on.<BR>--10 To bring or<BR>offer quickly.<BR>--11 To fix, settle,<BR>direct.<BR>--12 To be quick. {vII.v} {c1c} U.<BR>Ved. (चोदति ते)<BR>1 To impel, incite.<BR>--2 To offer quickly (Soma).<BR>--3<BR>To hasten, be quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोद|चोदः
चोद a. [चोदयतीति चुद्-अच्]<BR>Animating, inspiring, promoting &c.<BR>--दः A whip or goad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदक|चोदकः
चोदक a. [चुद् ण्वुल्] Driving, urging.<BR>--कः<BR>1 Directing, invitation.<BR>--2 (in<BR>gram.) परिग्रह q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदन
चोदन a. [चुद्-भावे ल्युट्] Driving,<BR>impelling.<BR>--नं<BR>1 The act of driving.<BR>--2 Invitation.<BR>--3 Order, rule,<BR>precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदना
चोदना<BR>1 Sending, directing,<BR>throwing.<BR>--2 Urging or driving<BR>onward.<BR>--3 Prompting, inciting,<BR>encouraging, inspiration.<BR>--4 A<BR>precept, sacred commandment,<BR>scriptural injunction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गुडः a<BR>ball for playing with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोदित
चोदित p. p.<BR>1 Sent, directed.<BR>--2<BR>Urged on, driven.<BR>--3 Incited,<BR>prompted, inspired.<BR>--4 Put forward as<BR>an argument.<BR>--5 Thrown, cast.<BR>--6<BR>Appointed.<BR>--7 Ordered, directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोद्य|चोद्यं|चोद्यः
चोद्य a. [चुट्-ण्यत्]<BR>1 To be driven<BR>or impelled.<BR>--2 To be sent, thrown,<BR>or directed.<BR>--3 To be mentioned.<BR>--द्यं<BR>1 Objecting, asking a question.<BR>--2<BR>An objection.<BR>--3 Wonder, surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंदी|चुन्दी
चुंदी A procuress, bawd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुप्
चुप् {c1c} P. (चोपति) To move<BR>slowly, creep or steal along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोपन|चोपनं
चोपन a. Moving, stirring.<BR>--नं<BR>Moving slowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुबुकः|चुबुक
चुबुकः The chin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुब्रं|चुब्र
चुब्रं The mouth, face.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंब्|चुम्ब्
चुंब् {vI.v} {c1c} {c10c} U. (चुंबति-ते, चुंबयति-ते,<BR>चुंबित)<BR>1 To kiss (fig. also);<BR>श्लिष्यति चुंबति जलधरकल्पं हरिरुपगत इति<BR>तिमिरमनल्पं Gīt. 6; प्रियामुखं<BR>किंपुरुषश्चुचुंबे Ku. 3. 38, Amaru. 16;<BR>H. 4. 132.<BR>--2 To touch softly, or graze;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">Page0497-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--WITH परि to kiss; Rs. 6. 18;<BR>Amaru. 77. {vII.v} {c10c} P. To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0496-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंबः|चुम्ब|चुंब|चुम्बः
चुंबः, बा [चुंब्-भावे घञ् अच् वा] A<BR>kiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंबा
चुंबः, बा [चुंब्-भावे घञ् अच् वा] A<BR>kiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंबकः|चुम्बक|चुंबक|चुम्बकः
चुंबकः [चुंब्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A kisser.<BR>--2<BR>A lecher, a lustful man, libertine.<BR>--3 A rogue, cheat.<BR>--4 One who has<BR>kissed or dipped in a variety of<BR>subjects, a superficial scholar.<BR>--5<BR>A loadstone.<BR>--6 The upper part or<BR>middle of a balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंबनं|चुम्बन|चुंबन|चुम्बनं
चुंबनं [चुंब् भावे ल्युट्] Kissing, a<BR>kiss; चुंबनं देहि मे भार्ये कामचांडालतृप्तये<BR>R. G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंबित|चुम्बित
चुंबित p. p.<BR>1 Kissed.<BR>--2 Touched<BR>softly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुंबिन्|चुम्बिन्
चुंबिन् a.<BR>1 Kissing, sipping;<BR>Māl. 9. 7.<BR>--2 Touching, grazing;<BR>Bh. 3. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुर्
चुर् {c10c} U. (चोरयति-ते, चोरित)<BR>1<BR>To rob, steal; Ms. 8. 333; V. 3. 17.<BR>--2 (Fig.) To bear, have, possess,<BR>take, assume; अचूचुरच्चंद्रमसोभिरामतां<BR>Śi. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुर
चुर a. Stealing, robbing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुरणं|चुरण
चुरणं Robbing, theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुरा
चुरा Theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरः|चोर
चो(चौ)रः<BR>1 A thief, robber;<BR>सकलं चोर गतं त्वया गृहीतं V. 4. 16;<BR>इंदीवरदलप्रभाचोरं चक्षुः Bh. 3. 67.<BR>--2<BR>Any dishonest dealer.<BR>--3 One that<BR>steals or captivates the heart.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. theft.<BR>--गत a. robbed.<BR>--रूपः a clever thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरः|चौर
चो(चौ)रः<BR>1 A thief, robber;<BR>सकलं चोर गतं त्वया गृहीतं V. 4. 16;<BR>इंदीवरदलप्रभाचोरं चक्षुः Bh. 3. 67.<BR>--2<BR>Any dishonest dealer.<BR>--3 One that<BR>steals or captivates the heart.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. theft.<BR>--गत a. robbed.<BR>--रूपः a clever thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरिका
चो(चौ)रिका Theft, robbery;<BR>˚विवाह Māl. 1. secret marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौरिका
चो(चौ)रिका Theft, robbery;<BR>˚विवाह Māl. 1. secret marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरित
चोरित a. Stolen, robbed.<BR>--तं<BR>Theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोरितकं|चोरितक
चोरितकं<BR>1 Petty theft, larceny.<BR>--2 Anything stolen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुरिः|चुरि
चुरिः = चूरी^1 f. A small well.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/Cologne/issues/157. note: headword cUrI is the alternate of curiH, not rI.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्
चुल् {c10c} P. (चोलयति)<BR>1 To raise or<BR>elevate.<BR>--2 To rise, increase.<BR>--3 To<BR>dip, dive or plunge into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुकः|चुलुक|चुलुकं
चुलुकः [चुल्-उकञ्]<BR>1 Deep mud.<BR>--2 A mouthful of water or the<BR>hand hollowed to hold water or<BR>anything; ममौ स भद्रं चुलुके समुद्रः<BR>N. 8. 45; ज्ञात्वा विधातुश्चुलुकात् प्रसूतिं<BR>Vikr. 1. 37.<BR>--3 A small vessel.<BR>--क<BR>Water in which pulse has been<BR>steeped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुकिन्
चुलुकिन् m. A porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुंप्|चुलुम्प्
चुलुंप् {c1c} P. (चुलुंपति) To swing,<BR>rock, move to and fro, agitate.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">Page0497-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--WITH उद {1} to swing. {2} to<BR>agitate; अंभोधेर्नालिकेलीरसमिव<BR>चुलुकैरुच्चुलुंपंत्यपो ये Mv. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुंपः|चुलुम्प|चुलुंप|चुलुम्पः
चुलुंपः Fondling children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुलुंपा
चुलुंपा A she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्ल्
चुल्ल् {c1c} P. (चुल्लति)<BR>1 To play,<BR>sport, to make amorous gestures.<BR>--2 To conjecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्ल|चुल्लः
चुल्ल a. Blear-eyed.<BR>--ल्लः A blear<BR>eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्लकः|चुल्लक
चुल्लकः The palm of the hand<BR>hollowed as in the act of holding<BR>water.<BR>--की<BR>1 A kind of water-pot.<BR>--2 A porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्लिः|चुल्लि
चुल्लिः A fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुल्ली
चुल्ली<BR>1 A fireplace.<BR>--2 A funeral<BR>pile.<BR>--3 A large apartment or hall<BR>composed of three divisions, one<BR>looking north, another east, and the<BR>third west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुस्तः|चुस्त|चुस्तं
चुस्तः, --स्तं [चु क्त बा˚ सुट्]<BR>1 The<BR>burnt exterior of roast meat.<BR>--2<BR>Fried meat.<BR>--3 Chaff.<BR>--4 Rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चुस्तं|चुस्त|चुस्तः
चुस्तः, --स्तं [चु क्त बा˚ सुट्]<BR>1 The<BR>burnt exterior of roast meat.<BR>--2<BR>Fried meat.<BR>--3 Chaff.<BR>--4 Rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूचुकं|चूचुक
चूचुकं, चूचूकं The nipple of a<BR>breast; Śi. 7. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूचूकं|चूचूक
चूचुकं, चूचूकं The nipple of a<BR>breast; Śi. 7. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडः|चूड
चूडः Ved.<BR>1 A protuberance.<BR>--2<BR>The ceremony of tonsure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडकः|चूडक
चूडकः A well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडा
चूडा<BR>1 The hair on the top of<BR>the head, a single lock on the crown<BR>of the head (left after the<BR>ceremony of tonsure); R. 18. 51;<BR>U. 5. 36; 5. 3; 4. 20.<BR>--2 The<BR>ceremony of tonsure.<BR>--3 The crest of a<BR>cock or peacock; Pt. 2. 73.<BR>--4 Any<BR>crest, plume or diadem.<BR>--5 The<BR>head.<BR>--6 Top, summit.<BR>--7 A room<BR>on the top of a house.<BR>--8 A well.<BR>--9 An ornament (like a bracelet<BR>worn on the wrist).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करणं, --कर्मन् n. the ceremony of<BR>tonsure; Ms. 2. 35.<BR>--पाशः a mass of hair;<BR>चूडापाशे नवकुरबकं Me. 65.<BR>--मणिः,<BR>--रत्नं {1} a jewel worn on the top of<BR>the head, a crest jewel (fig. also).<BR>{2} best, excellent (usually at the<BR>end of comp.).<BR>--लक्षणं tonsure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडार
चूडार --ल a.<BR>1 Having a single lock<BR>of hair on the crown of the head.<BR>--2 Crested.<BR>--लं The head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडाल|चूडालं
चूडार --ल a.<BR>1 Having a single lock<BR>of hair on the crown of the head.<BR>--2 Crested.<BR>--लं The head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडिक
चूडिक, चूडिन् a.<BR>1 Having a lock<BR>of hair on the head.<BR>--2 Crested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडिन्
चूडिक, चूडिन् a.<BR>1 Having a lock<BR>of hair on the head.<BR>--2 Crested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूडाम्लं|चूडाम्ल
चूडाम्लं Vinegar prepared from<BR>fruits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूण्
चूण् {c10c} P. (चूणयति)<BR>1 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">Page0497-c+ 55</a>]<BR>contract.<BR>--2 To close, shrink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूतः|चूत
चूतः [चूष्-क्त, चोतति रसं चुत्-अच् वा<BR>पृषो˚ Tv.] The mango tree;<BR>ईषद्बद्धरजःकणाग्रकपिशा चूते नवा मंजरी<BR>V. 2. 7; चूतांकुरास्वादकषायकंठः<BR>Ku. 3. 32; one of the 5 arrows of Cupid;<BR>see पंचबाण.<BR>--तं The anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूतकः|चूतक
चूतकः<BR>1 The mango tree.<BR>--2 A<BR>small well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूतिः|चूति
चूतिः f. The anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्
चूर् {c4c} A. (चूर्यते) To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूरी
चूरी --चूरिका A small well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूरिका
चूरी --चूरिका A small well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्ण्
चूर्ण् {c10c} U. (चूर्णयति-ते, चूर्णित)<BR>1<BR>To reduce to powder, pulverize,<BR>pound.<BR>--2 To bruise, crush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णः|चूर्ण|चूर्णं|चूर्ण्ण
चूर्णः --र्णं [चूर्ण् कर्मणि अच्]<BR>1 Powder.<BR>--2 Flour.<BR>--3 Dust.<BR>--4 Aromatic<BR>powder, pounded sandal, camphor<BR>&c; भवति विफलप्रेरणा चूर्णमुष्टिः<BR>Me. 68.<BR>--र्णः<BR>1 Chalk.<BR>--2 Lime.<BR>--3<BR>Pounding.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः a<BR>limeburner.<BR>--कुंतलः a curl, curly hair;<BR>समं केरलकांतानां चूर्णकुंतलवल्लिभिः<BR>Vikr. 4. 2.<BR>--खंडः डं {1} gravel, pebble. {2}<BR>lime-stone nodule.<BR>--पदं a peculiar<BR>exercise, walking backwards and<BR>forwards.<BR>--पारदः vermilion. मुष्टिः f.<BR>a handful of perfume or powder.<BR>--योगः perfumed powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णं|चूर्ण|चूर्णः|चूर्ण्ण
चूर्णः --र्णं [चूर्ण् कर्मणि अच्]<BR>1 Powder.<BR>--2 Flour.<BR>--3 Dust.<BR>--4 Aromatic<BR>powder, pounded sandal, camphor<BR>&c; भवति विफलप्रेरणा चूर्णमुष्टिः<BR>Me. 68.<BR>--र्णः<BR>1 Chalk.<BR>--2 Lime.<BR>--3<BR>Pounding.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः a<BR>limeburner.<BR>--कुंतलः a curl, curly hair;<BR>समं केरलकांतानां चूर्णकुंतलवल्लिभिः<BR>Vikr. 4. 2.<BR>--खंडः डं {1} gravel, pebble. {2}<BR>lime-stone nodule.<BR>--पदं a peculiar<BR>exercise, walking backwards and<BR>forwards.<BR>--पारदः vermilion. मुष्टिः f.<BR>a handful of perfume or powder.<BR>--योगः perfumed powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णकः|चूर्णक|चूर्णकं
चूर्णकः [चूर्ण स्वार्थे क] Grain fried<BR>and pounded.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A fragrant<BR>powder.<BR>--2 A style of<BR>prose-composition which is easy, does not<BR>contain hard letters, and has very few<BR>compounds; अकठोराक्षरं स्वल्पसमासं<BR>चूर्णकं विदुः Cand. M. 6.<BR>--3<BR>Explaining in prose the purport of a<BR>foregoing verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णनं|चूर्णन
चूर्णनं Crushing, pounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिः|चूर्णि
चूर्णिः --र्णी f.<BR>1 Pounding, powder.<BR>--2<BR>A sum of hundred cowries.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of Patañjali's Mahābhāṣya on the<BR>Sūtras of Pāṇini.<BR>--4 A selection of<BR>an unanswerable argument.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत् m. {1} an epithet of Patañjali.<BR>{2} an annotator, commentator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णी
चूर्णिः --र्णी f.<BR>1 Pounding, powder.<BR>--2<BR>A sum of hundred cowries.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of Patañjali's Mahābhāṣya on the<BR>Sūtras of Pāṇini.<BR>--4 A selection of<BR>an unanswerable argument.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत् m. {1} an epithet of Patañjali.<BR>{2} an annotator, commentator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिका
चूर्णिका<BR>1 Grain fried and<BR>powdered.<BR>--2 A style of prose composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णित
चूर्णित a.<BR>1 Pounded, pulverized.<BR>--2 Crushed, bruised, smashed,<BR>shattered to pieces; Ku. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णिन्
चूर्णिन् a. Made or mixed up with<BR>anything powdered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णीकृ
चूर्णीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To reduce to powder,<BR>pound, grind.<BR>--2 To bruise, smash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0497-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्णीभू
चूर्णीभू {c1c} P. To become dust, fly<BR>off into minute particles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूर्तिः|चूर्ति|चूर्त्ति
चूर्तिः f. Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूलः|चूल
चूलः Hair.<BR>--ला<BR>1 An upper<BR>room.<BR>--2 A crest.<BR>--3 The crest of a<BR>comet; cf. चूडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूलिकं|चूलिक
चूलिकं A cake of flour fried with<BR>ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूलिन्
चूलिन् a. Having a crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूलिका
चूलिका [चुल् समुच्चंये ण्वुल् पृषो˚ दीर्घः]<BR>1 The crest or comb of a cock.<BR>--2<BR>The root of an elephant's ear.<BR>--3<BR>(In dramas) The hinting or<BR>indication of the occurrence of any event<BR>by characters behind the stage;<BR>अंतर्जवनिकासंस्थैः सूचनार्थस्य चूलिका<BR>S. D. 310; e. g. in the beginning of<BR>the 4th act of Mv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूष्
चूष् {c1c} P. (चूषति, चूषित) To drink,<BR>suck up or out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूषा
चूषा<BR>1 A leathern girth (for an<BR>elephant).<BR>--2 Sucking.<BR>--3 A girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चूष्यं|चूष्य
चूष्यं [चूष् कर्मणि ण्यत्] Any article<BR>of food to be sucked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोषः|चोष
चोषः<BR>1 Sucking.<BR>--2 Inflammation<BR>(in medicine).<BR>--3 Drying up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोषणं|चोषण
चोषणं Sucking, suction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोष्यं|चोष्य
चोष्यं = चूष्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चृत्
चृत् {vI.v} {c6c} P. (चृतति)<BR>1 To hurt,<BR>kill.<BR>--2 To tie, bind or connect<BR>together. {vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (चर्तति,<BR>चर्तयति-ते) To light, kindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेकितानः|चेकितान
चेकितानः<BR>1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--2 N. of a Yādava prince, who<BR>fought on the side of the Pāṇḍavas<BR>in the great war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेटः|चेट
चेटः(डः) [चिट अच्, वा टस्य डः]<BR>A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेडः|चेड
चेटः(डः) [चिट अच्, वा टस्य डः]<BR>A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेटकः|चेटक
चेटकः<BR>1 A servant, slave; any<BR>one who does a set task.<BR>--2<BR>A paramour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेटिका
चेटि(डि)का, चेटिः(टी)(डी) f. A<BR>female slave or servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेडिका
चेटि(डि)का, चेटिः(टी)(डी) f. A<BR>female slave or servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेटिः
चेटि(डि)का, चेटिः(टी)(डी) f. A<BR>female slave or servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेटी
चेटि(डि)का, चेटिः(टी)(डी) f. A<BR>female slave or servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेडी
चेटि(डि)का, चेटिः(टी)(डी) f. A<BR>female slave or servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेद्
चेद् ind. If, provided that,<BR>although (never used at the<BR>beginning of a sentence); अयि<BR>रोषमुरीकरोषि नो चेत्किमपि त्वां प्रति वारिधे<BR>वदामः Bv. 1. 44; Ku. 4. 9; इति चेद<BR>--न ‘if it be urged that… (we reply)<BR>not so’ (frequently used in<BR>controversial works); सन्निधानमात्रेण<BR>राजप्रभृतीनां दृष्टं कर्तृत्वमिति चेन्न Ś. B.;<BR>अथ चेद but if.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदिः|चेदि
चेदिः (m. pl.) N. of a<BR>country; तदीशितारं चेदीनां भवांस्तमवमंस्त<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">Page0498-b+ 55</a>]<BR>मा Śi. 2. 95, 63.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिः,<BR>--भूभृत् m.,<BR>--राज् m.,<BR>--राजः N. of<BR>Śiśupāla, son of Damaghoṣa and<BR>king of the Cedis; Śi. 2. 96; see<BR>शिशुपाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल्
चेल् {c1c} P. (चेलति)<BR>1 To go,<BR>move.<BR>--2 To shake, be disturbed,<BR>tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलं|चेल
चेलं<BR>1 A garment; कुसुंभारुणं<BR>चारु चेलं वसाना Jag.<BR>--2 (At the<BR>end of comp.) Bad, wicked, vile;<BR>भार्याचेलं ‘a bad wife.’<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशकः a moth.<BR>--प्रक्षालकः a<BR>washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलिका
चेलिका A bodice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेलुकः|चेलुक
चेलुकः A Buddhist novice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेल्ल्
चेल्ल् {c1c} P. (चेल्लति)<BR>1 To go or<BR>move.<BR>--2 To shake, tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्ट्
चेष्ट् {c1c} A. (चेष्टते, चेष्टित)<BR>1 To<BR>move about, stir, be active, show<BR>signs of life; यदा स देवो जागर्ति तदेदं<BR>चेष्टते जगत् Ms. 1. 52; Māl. 8. 8;<BR>Ś. 6. 27.<BR>--2 To make effort,<BR>endeavour, exert oneself, struggle.<BR>--3 To perform, do (anything).<BR>--4 To frequent.<BR>--5 To behave, act.<BR>--WITH वि {1} to stir, move, be in<BR>motion, move about. {2} to act,<BR>behave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टं|चेष्ट
चेष्टं<BR>1 Moving the limbs, gesture.<BR>--2 Acting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टक|चेष्टकः
चेष्टक a. [चेष्ट्-ण्वुल्] Making<BR>efforts.<BR>--कः A particular mode of<BR>sexual enjoyment or coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टनं|चेष्टन
चेष्टनं<BR>1 Motion.<BR>--2 Effort,<BR>exertion.<BR>--3 Performing, doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टा
चेष्टा [चेष्ट्-अङ्]<BR>1 Motion,<BR>movement; किमस्माकं स्वामिचेष्टानिरूपणेन<BR>H. 3; Māl. 5. 7.<BR>--2 Gesture,<BR>action; चेष्टया भाषणेन च<BR>नेत्रवक्त्रविकारैश्च लक्ष्यतेऽतर्गतं मनः<BR>Ms. 8. 26.<BR>--3 Effort, exertion.<BR>--4<BR>Behaviour; Pt. 1. 150.<BR>--5 Action,<BR>deed, performing.<BR>--नाशः destruction<BR>of the world.<BR>--निरूपणं observing a<BR>person's movements.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेष्टित|चेष्टितं
चेष्टित p. p. [चेष्ट्-कर्तरि क्त] Moved,<BR>stirred &c.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Motion, gesture,<BR>act.<BR>--2 Doing, action, behaviour;<BR>कपोलपाटलादेशि बभूव रघुचेष्टितं<BR>R. 4. 68; तत्तत्कामस्य चेष्टितं Ms. 2. 4 doing<BR>or work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैतन्यं|चैतन्य|चैतन्यः
चैतन्यं [चेतनस्य भानः ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Spirit,<BR>life, intelligence, vitality, sensation.<BR>--2 Soul, spirit, mind; U. 1. 36.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">Page0498-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--3 Consciousness, feeling, sensation,<BR>sense; U. 1. 48.<BR>--4 (In Vedānta phil.)<BR>The supreme spirit considered as<BR>the essence of all being and source<BR>of all sensation.<BR>--न्यः N. of a<BR>modern reformer of the Vaiṣṇava<BR>faith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्तसिक
चैत्तसिक a. Relating to the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्त
चैत्त a. [चित्तस्येदं अण्] Belonging<BR>to the mind, mental.<BR>--त्तं Memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्तिक
चैत्तिक a. Mental, intellectual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्य|चैत्यं|चैत्यः
चैत्य a. Relating to a pile.<BR>--त्यः<BR>1 The individual soul.<BR>--2 A pile of<BR>stones forming a land-mark.<BR>--3 A<BR>monument, tomb-stone.<BR>--4 A<BR>sacrificial shed.<BR>--5 A place of religious<BR>worship, altar, sanctuary,<BR>--6 A<BR>temple.<BR>--7 A reflection.<BR>--8 A<BR>religious fig-tree or any tree growing<BR>by the side of streets; Me. 23.<BR>(रथ्यावृक्ष Malli.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तरुः, --द्रुमः,<BR>--वृक्षः a fig-tree standing on a sacred<BR>spot.<BR>--पालः the guardian of a<BR>sanctuary.<BR>--मुखः a hermit's<BR>waterpot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रः|चैत्र|चैत्रं
चैत्रः [चि ष्ट्रण्; चित्रमेव स्वार्थे अण्;<BR>चित्रायां भवः अण् वा]<BR>1 N. of a lunar<BR>month in which the full moon<BR>stands in the constellation Citrā<BR>(corresponding to March-April).<BR>--2 A Buddhist mendicant.<BR>--3<BR>One of the seven ranges of<BR>mountains dividing the continent into<BR>Varṣas.<BR>--त्रं A temple, monument<BR>for the dead.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवलिः f.<BR>the full-moon-day of Chaitra.<BR>--सखः<BR>an epithet of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रकः|चैत्रक
चैत्रकः The month चैत्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रिः|चैत्रि
चैत्रिः, चैत्रिकः, चैत्रिन् m. The<BR>month called Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रिकः|चैत्रिक
चैत्रिः, चैत्रिकः, चैत्रिन् m. The<BR>month called Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्रिन्
चैत्रिः, चैत्रिकः, चैत्रिन् m. The<BR>month called Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्री
चैत्री The day of full-moon in<BR>the month of Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्ररथं|चैत्ररथ
चैत्ररथं(थ्यं) N. of the garden<BR>of Kubera; एको ययौ चैत्ररथप्रदेशान्<BR>सौराज्यरम्यानपरो विदर्भान् R. 5. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैत्ररथ्यं|चैत्ररथ्य
चैत्ररथं(थ्यं) N. of the garden<BR>of Kubera; एको ययौ चैत्ररथप्रदेशान्<BR>सौराज्यरम्यानपरो विदर्भान् R. 5. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैद्यः|चैद्य
चैद्यः N. of Śiśupāla; अभिचैद्यं<BR>प्रतिष्ठासुः Śi. 2. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैल|चैलः
चैल a. Made of cloth.<BR>--लं A<BR>piece of cloth, garment.<BR>--लः A<BR>month.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धावः a<BR>washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैलकः|चैलक
चैलकः A Buddhist mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चैलिकः|चैलिक
चैलिकः A piece of cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोक्ष|चोक्षः
चोक्ष a.<BR>1 Pure, clean.<BR>--2 Honest.<BR>--3 Clever, dexterous, skilful.<BR>--4<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">Page0499-a+ 34</a>]<BR>Pleasing, agreeable, delightful.<BR>--5<BR>Sharp, pungent, keen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0498-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोचं|चोच
चोचं<BR>1 A bark, rind.<BR>--2 Skin,<BR>hide.<BR>--3 The cocoa-nut.<BR>--4 The<BR>uneatable part of a fruit.<BR>--5 The fruit<BR>of the fan-palm.<BR>--6 A plantain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोचकः|चोचक|चोचकं
चोचकः A bark in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोटी
चोटी A petticoat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोडः|चोड
चोडः A bodice; चोडी also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलः|चोल
चोलः (m. pl.) [चुल् कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>N. of a country in southern<BR>India, the modern Tanjore.<BR>--लः, --ली<BR>1 A short jacket, a bodice.<BR>--2 A<BR>garment reaching to the feet.<BR>--लं<BR>A garment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उंडुकः a<BR>diadem, turban.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलकः|चोलक|चोलकं
चोलकः<BR>1 A breast-plate.<BR>--2 A<BR>bark-dress.<BR>--3 A bodice.<BR>--कं Bark,<BR>rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलकिन्
चोलकिन् m.<BR>1 A soldier armed with<BR>a breast-plate.<BR>--2 The orange tree.<BR>--3 The wrist.<BR>--4 The shoot of a<BR>bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलंडुकः|चोलण्डुक|चोलण्डुकः
चोलं(लों)डुकः A fillet for<BR>the head, a turban, tiara or diadem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोलोंडुकः|चोलोण्डुक|चोलोंडुक|चोलोण्डुकः
चोलं(लों)डुकः A fillet for<BR>the head, a turban, tiara or diadem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोस्कः|चोस्क
चोस्कः An excellent horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौक्ष|चौक्षं
चौक्ष a.<BR>1 Pure, clean.<BR>--2<BR>Pleasant, agreeable, lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौड
चौड (डी f.), चौल (ली f.) a.<BR>[चूडा प्रयोजनमस्य चूडा˚ णः वा डस्य लः]<BR>1 Crested.<BR>--2 Relating to tonsure.<BR>--डं, --लं The ceremony of tonsure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर्यं|चौर्य|चौर्य्य|चौर्य्यं
चौर्यं<BR>1 Theft, robbery.<BR>--2<BR>Trickery.<BR>--3 Secrecy, concealment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-b" target="_blank">Page0499-b+ 36</a>]<BR>--रतं secret sexual enjoyment;<BR>Pt. 1. 174.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. the habit of robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चौर्यकं|चौर्यक
चौर्यकं Theft, stealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यु
च्यु {vI.v} {c1c} A. (च्यवते, च्युत)<BR>1 To fall<BR>or drop down, slip, sink (fig. also);<BR>Ś. 2. 8.<BR>--2 To come out of, flow or<BR>issue from, drop, trickle or stream<BR>forth from; स्वतश्चयुतं वह्निमिवाद्भिरंबुदः<BR>R. 3. 58; Bk. 9. 71.<BR>--3 To deviate<BR>or swerve from, fall off or away<BR>from, leave (duty &c.); (with abl.)<BR>अस्माद्धर्मान्न च्यवेत Ms. 7. 98, 12. 71-72.<BR>--4 To lose, be deprived of;<BR>अच्योष्ट सत्त्वान्नृपतिः Bk. 3. 20, 7. 92.<BR>--5 To vanish, disappear, perish, be<BR>at an end; R. 8. 66; Ms. 12. 96.<BR>--6<BR>To decrease.<BR>--7 To bring about,<BR>make, form, create.<BR>--8 To cause to go<BR>away, cause to forget. --Caus. (<BR>च्यावयति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to move, excite,<BR>agitate.<BR>--2 (A.) To move oneself, be<BR>shaken or moved.<BR>--3 To remove,<BR>drive away, expel.<BR>--4 To deprive,<BR>take away; Pt. 1. 240.<BR>--5 To cause<BR>to fall. {vII.v} {c10c} P. (च्यावयति)<BR>1 To<BR>suffer, bear.<BR>--2 To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यवनं|च्यवन|च्यवनः
च्यवनं<BR>1 Moving, motion.<BR>--2<BR>Being deprived of, loss; deprivation.<BR>--3 Dying, perishing.<BR>--4 Sinking,<BR>falling.<BR>--5 Departure, deviation.<BR>--6 Flowing, trickling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यावन
च्यावन a. Causing to fall.<BR>--नं<BR>Expulsion, driving away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत|च्युतं
च्युत p. p. [च्यु-क्त च्युत्-क वा]<BR>1<BR>Fallen down, slipped, fallen.<BR>--2<BR>Removed, expelled.<BR>--3 Strayed,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-c" target="_blank">Page0499-c+ 35</a>]<BR>erred, deviated from.<BR>--4 Deprived.<BR>--5 Broken, disordered.<BR>--6 Dropped,<BR>oozed out.<BR>--7 Lost, gone, perished;<BR>R. 3. 45.<BR>--8 Moved, shaken.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिकार a. dismissed<BR>from office.<BR>--आत्मन् a. of a<BR>depraved soul, evil-minded; Ku. 5. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युतिः|च्युति
च्युतिः f. [च्यु-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>1 Falling<BR>down, a fall.<BR>--2 Deviation from.<BR>--3<BR>Dropping, oozing.<BR>--4 Losing,<BR>deprivation; धैर्यच्युतिं कुर्यां Ku. 3. 10.<BR>--5<BR>Vanishing, perishing.<BR>--6 The vulva.<BR>--7 The anus.<BR>--8 Quick motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युत्
च्युत् {c1c} P. (च्योतति)<BR>1 To drop,<BR>flow, ooze, trickle, stream forth;<BR>इदं शोणितमभ्यग्रं संप्रहारेऽच्युतत्तयोः<BR>Bk. 6. 28.<BR>--2 To drop or fall down,<BR>slip; इदं कवचमच्योतीत् Bk. 6. 29.<BR>--3 To cause to drop or stream<BR>forth.<BR>--4 To wet thoroughly,<BR>moisten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्योतं|च्योत
च्योतं<BR>1 Sprinkling, pouring.<BR>--2<BR>Dropping, falling.<BR>--3 Trickling,<BR>oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युपः|च्युप
च्युपः The face, mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्युस्
च्युस् {c10c} P. (च्योसयति)<BR>1 To<BR>laugh.<BR>--2 To suffer.<BR>--3 To leave.<BR>--4 To hurt, kill.<BR>--5 To loose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यूतः|च्यूत
च्यूतः The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

च्यौत्न|च्यौत्नः
च्यौत्न a. [च्यु गतौ करणे त्नण्]<BR>1<BR>Animating, enlivening.<BR>--2 A goer.<BR>--3 Oviparous.<BR>--4 Abandoned;<BR>wicked, void of virtue.<BR>--त्नं<BR>1 Shaking,<BR>concussion.<BR>--2 Enterprise.<BR>--3<BR>Management.<BR>--4 Strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ|छं|छः
छ a.<BR>1 Pure, clean.<BR>--2<BR>Trembling, unsteady.<BR>--छः<BR>1 A part,<BR>fragment.<BR>--2 Cutting, dividing.<BR>--छा<BR>1<BR>Covering, concealing.<BR>--2 An infant,<BR>a child.<BR>--3 Quick-silver.<BR>--छं A<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगः|छग
छगः (गी f.) A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगणः|छगण|छगणं
छगणः --णं Dry cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगणं|छगण|छगणः
छगणः --णं Dry cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलः|छगल|छगलं
छगलः<BR>1 A goat.<BR>--2 N. of the<BR>sage Atri.<BR>--3 N. of a country.<BR>--ला,<BR>--ली A she-goat.<BR>--लं A blue cloth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंत्रिका, --अंत्रिः a wolf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छगलकः|छगलक
छगलकः A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छटा
छटा<BR>1 Mass, lump, number,<BR>assemblage; सटाच्छटाभिन्नघनेन<BR>Śi. 1. 47; Māl. 10. 10.<BR>--2 A collection of<BR>rays of light, lustre, splendour,<BR>light; Śi. 8. 38; Māl. 5. 23.<BR>--3<BR>A continuous line, streak;<BR>छातेतरांबुच्छटा K. P. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आभा<BR>lightning.<BR>--फलः the betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रः|छत्र|छत्त्रं|छत्त्रः|छत्रं
छत्रः A mushroom.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1 A parasol,<BR>an umbrella; अदेयमासीत्त्रयमेव भूपतेः<BR>शशिप्रभं छत्रमुभे च चामरे R. 3. 16;<BR>Ms. 7. 96.<BR>--2 Concealing the faults of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-1c" target="_blank">Page0499-1c+ 13</a>]<BR>one's teacher.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धरः, --धारः<BR>the bearer of an umbrella.<BR>--धारण<BR>{1} carrying or bearing an umbrella;<BR>Ms. 2. 178. {2} carrying an<BR>umbrella as a type of royal authority.<BR>--पतिः<BR>{1} a king over whom an umbrella<BR>is carried as a mark of dignity, a<BR>sovereign, emperor. {2} N. of an<BR>ancient king in जंबुद्वीप.<BR>--भंगः {1}<BR>‘destruction of the royal parasol’,<BR>loss of dominion, deposition. {2}<BR>dependence. {3} wilfulness. {4} a<BR>forlorn condition, widowhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0499-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रकः|छत्रक|छत्त्रकः
छत्रकः<BR>1 A temple in honour of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--2 A bee-hive of a conical form.<BR>--3 A king-fisher.<BR>--त्रिका Mushroom.<BR>--कं A mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रा
छत्रा, छत्राकः A mushroom;<BR>Ms. 5. 19; Y. 1. 176; also छत्राकी-कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्राकः|छत्राक|छत्त्राकं|छत्त्राकः
छत्रा, छत्राकः A mushroom;<BR>Ms. 5. 19; Y. 1. 176; also छत्राकी-कं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिकः|छत्रिक
छत्रिकः The bearer of an umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्रिन्
छत्रिन् a. (णी f.) Having or<BR>bearing an umbrella. --m. A barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छत्वरः|छत्वर
छत्वरः<BR>1 A house.<BR>--2 A bower,<BR>arbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्
छद् {c10c} U. (छदति-ते,<BR>छादयति-ते, छन्न, छादित)<BR>1 To cover, cover<BR>over, veil; हैमैश्छन्ना Me. 76; चक्षुः<BR>खेदात्सलिलगुरुभिः पक्ष्मभिश्छादयंतीं<BR>Me. 90; छन्नोपांतः… काननाम्रैः 18.<BR>--2 To<BR>spread anything (as a cover), cover<BR>oneself.<BR>--3 To hide, conceal;<BR>Pt. 1. 287; (fig.); keep<BR>secret; ज्ञानपूर्वं कृतं कर्म छादयंते ह्यसाधवः<BR>Mb.; छन्नं दोषमुदाहरंति Mk. 9. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदः|छद
छदः, --छदनं<BR>1 A covering, cover;<BR>अल्पच्छद, उत्तरच्छद &c.<BR>--2 A wing;<BR>अन्यभृतच्छदच्छवेः Śi. 16. 50;<BR>च्छदहेम कषन्निवालसत् N. 2. 69.<BR>--3 A<BR>leaf.<BR>--4 A sheath, case.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रः the Bhūrja tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदनं|छदन
छदः, --छदनं<BR>1 A covering, cover;<BR>अल्पच्छद, उत्तरच्छद &c.<BR>--2 A wing;<BR>अन्यभृतच्छदच्छवेः Śi. 16. 50;<BR>च्छदहेम कषन्निवालसत् N. 2. 69.<BR>--3 A<BR>leaf.<BR>--4 A sheath, case.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रः the Bhūrja tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छदिः|छदि
छदिः f.,<BR>--छदिस् n. [छद्-कि-इस् वा]<BR>1 The roof of a carriage.<BR>--2 The<BR>roof or thatch of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मन्
छद्मन् n. [छाद्यते स्वरूपमनेन; छद्-मनिन्<BR>Uṇ. 4. 144]<BR>1 A deceptive dress, a<BR>disguise.<BR>--2 A plea, pretext, guise;<BR>ब्रह्मछद्मा सामर्थ्यसारः Mv. 2. 25;<BR>पलितछद्मना जरा R. 12. 2; Śi. 2. 21;<BR>कुतोऽन्यथा स्रवत्येष स्वेदच्छद्मा मृतद्रवः<BR>Ratn. 2. 17.<BR>--3 Fraud, dishonesty, trick;<BR>छद्मना परिददामि मृत्यवे U. 1. 46;<BR>Ms. 4. 199; 9. 72.<BR>--4 The thatch or<BR>roof of a house.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तापसः a<BR>religious hypocrite.<BR>--रूपेण ind.<BR>incognito, in disguise.<BR>--वेशिन् m. a<BR>player, a cheat, one dressed in<BR>disguise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छद्मिन्
छद्मिन् a. (नी f.) [छद्मन्-इनि]<BR>1<BR>Fraudulent, deceitful.<BR>--2 Disguised<BR>(at the end of comp.); e. g.<BR>ब्राह्मणछद्मिन् disguised as a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छन्न|छन्नं|छन्नः
छन्न a. [छद्-क्त नि˚]<BR>1 Covered.<BR>--2 Hidden, concealed, secret &c.<BR>see छद्.<BR>--3 Desolate, solitary.<BR>--4<BR>Private.<BR>--न्नं A secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छनच्छन्
छनच्छन् ind. An imitative sound,<BR>expressive of the noise of falling<BR>drops &c.; छनच्छनिति बाष्पकणाः<BR>पतंति Amaru. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छंद्|छन्द्
छंद् {c10c} U. (छंदयति-ते, छंदित)<BR>1 To<BR>please, gratify.<BR>--2 To persuade, coax.<BR>--3 To cover.<BR>--4 To be delighted in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छंद|छन्द|छन्दः
छंद a. [छंद्-अच्]<BR>1 Pleasing,<BR>fascinating, inviting, alluring.<BR>--2<BR>Private, solitary, secret.<BR>--3 Praising.<BR>--दः<BR>1 Wish, desire, fancy, liking, will;<BR>विज्ञाप्यतां देवी यस्ते छंद इति V. 3 just<BR>as you like; Pt. 1. 69.<BR>--2 Free will,<BR>one's own choice, whim, free or<BR>wilful conduct; षष्ठे काले त्वमपि<BR>दिवसस्यात्मनश्छं दवर्ती V. 2. 1; Gīt. 1;<BR>Y. 2. 195; स्वच्छंदं according to one's<BR>free will, independently.<BR>--3 (Hence)<BR>subjection, control.<BR>--4 Meaning,<BR>intention, purport.<BR>--5 Poison.<BR>--6<BR>Appearance, look, shape.<BR>--7 Pleasure,<BR>delight.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुवृत्तं, --त्तिः<BR>indulgence of whims, humouring,<BR>compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छंदकः|छन्दक|छन्दकः
छंदकः<BR>1 An epithet of Vāsudeva.<BR>--2 A protector.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छंदन|छन्दन
छंदन a. Pleasing, charming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छंदस्|छन्दस्
छंदस्^1 n. [छंदयति असुन्]<BR>1 Wish,<BR>desire, fancy, will, pleasure; (<BR>गृह्णीयात्) मूर्खं छंदोऽनुवृत्तेन याथातथ्येन<BR>पंडितं Chāṇ. 33.<BR>--2 Free will, free<BR>or wilful conduct.<BR>--3 Meaning,<BR>intention.<BR>--4 Fraud, trick, deceit.<BR>--5<BR>The Vedas, the sacred text of the<BR>Vedic hymns; स च<BR>कुलपतिराद्यश्छंदसां यः प्रयोक्ता U. 3. 48; बहुलं छंदसि<BR>frequently used by Pāṇini;<BR>प्रणवश्छंदसामिव R. 1. 11; Y. 1. 143;<BR>Ms. 4. 95.<BR>--6 A metre; ऋक्छंदसा आशास्ते<BR>Ś. 4; गायत्री छंदसामहं Bg. 10. 35;<BR>13. 4.<BR>--7 Metrical science, prosody;<BR>(regarded as one of the six<BR>Vedāngas or auxiliaries to the Vedas,<BR>the other five being शिक्षा, व्याकरण,<BR>कल्प, निरुक्त and ज्योतिष).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृतं any metrical part of the<BR>Vedas or other sacred compositions;<BR>यथोदितेन विधिना नित्यं छंदस्कृतं पठेत्<BR>Ms. 4. 100.<BR>--गः (--छंदोगः) {1} a reciter<BR>in metre. {2} a student or chanter<BR>of the Sāmaveda; Ms. 3. 145; (<BR>छंदोगः सामवेदाध्यायी)<BR>--भंगः a violation<BR>of the laws of metre.<BR>--विचितिः f.<BR>‘examination of metres’, N. of a<BR>work on metres, sometimes ascribed<BR>to Daṇḍin; छंदोविचित्यां<BR>सकलस्तत्प्रपंचो निदर्शितः Kāv. 1. 12.<BR>--वृत्तं a metre<BR>in general.<BR>--स्तुभ् m. N. of Aruṇa.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: lost anusvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छंदस्य|छन्दस्य
छंदस्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Fit for hymns,<BR>metrical.<BR>--2 Made at will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छंदित|छन्दित
छंदित a. Gratified, pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छंदु|छन्दु
छंदु a. Ved. Pleasing, lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छम्
छम् {c1c} P. (छमति) To eat,<BR>consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छमच्छमित
छमच्छमित An imitative word for<BR>the sound of ‘crackling’, or ‘rattling.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छमंडः|छमण्ड|छमंड|छमण्डः
छमंडः<BR>1 An orphan.<BR>--2 A single<BR>man; one who has no relative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छंप्|छम्प्
छंप् {c1c} {c10c} P. (छंपति, छंपयति) To<BR>go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्द्
छर्द् {c10c} U. (छर्दयति, छर्दित) To<BR>vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दः|छर्द|छर्द्द|छर्द्दं
छर्दः, छर्दनं, छर्दिः f., छर्दिका<BR>Vomiting, sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दनं|छर्दन|छर्दनः|छर्द्दन|छर्द्दनं
छर्दः, छर्दनं, छर्दिः f., छर्दिका<BR>Vomiting, sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिः|छर्दि|छर्द्दि|छर्द्दिः
छर्दः, छर्दनं, छर्दिः f., छर्दिका<BR>Vomiting, sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छर्दिस्
छर्दिस् f. [छर्द्-भावे इसि]<BR>1<BR>Vomiting.<BR>--2 A secure place or residence.<BR>--3 A house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलः|छल|छलं
छलः, --लं [छल्-अच्]<BR>1 Fraud,<BR>trick, deceit, deception; विद्महे शठ<BR>पलायनच्छलानि R. 19. 31; छलमत्र न<BR>गृह्यते Mk. 9. 18; Y. 1. 61;<BR>Ms. 8. 49, 187; Amaru. 16; Śi. 13. 11.<BR>--2<BR>Roguery, knavery.<BR>--3 A plea, pretext,<BR>guise, semblance (often used in this<BR>sense to denote an उत्प्रेक्षा);<BR>असुरक्षाहि बहुच्छलाः श्रियः Ki. 2. 39;<BR>परिखावलयच्छलेन या न परेषां ग्रहणस्य<BR>गोचरा N. 2. 95; प्रत्यर्प्य<BR>पूजामुपदाच्छलेन R. 7. 30, 6. 54, 16. 28;<BR>Bk. 1. 1; Amaru. 15; Māl. 9. 1.<BR>--4<BR>Intention.<BR>--5 Wickedness.<BR>--6 A<BR>family.<BR>--7 Design, device.<BR>--8<BR>Fiction, circumvention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलं|छल|छलः
छलः, --लं [छल्-अच्]<BR>1 Fraud,<BR>trick, deceit, deception; विद्महे शठ<BR>पलायनच्छलानि R. 19. 31; छलमत्र न<BR>गृह्यते Mk. 9. 18; Y. 1. 61;<BR>Ms. 8. 49, 187; Amaru. 16; Śi. 13. 11.<BR>--2<BR>Roguery, knavery.<BR>--3 A plea, pretext,<BR>guise, semblance (often used in this<BR>sense to denote an उत्प्रेक्षा);<BR>असुरक्षाहि बहुच्छलाः श्रियः Ki. 2. 39;<BR>परिखावलयच्छलेन या न परेषां ग्रहणस्य<BR>गोचरा N. 2. 95; प्रत्यर्प्य<BR>पूजामुपदाच्छलेन R. 7. 30, 6. 54, 16. 28;<BR>Bk. 1. 1; Amaru. 15; Māl. 9. 1.<BR>--4<BR>Intention.<BR>--5 Wickedness.<BR>--6 A<BR>family.<BR>--7 Design, device.<BR>--8<BR>Fiction, circumvention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलक
छलक a. Delusive, cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलयति
छलयति Den. P. To outwit,<BR>deceive, cheat; बलिं छलयते Gīt. 1;<BR>शैवाललोलांश्छलयंति मीनान् R. 16. 61;<BR>Bg. 10. 36; Amaru. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलिकं|छलिक
छलिकं A kind of drama or<BR>dancing; छलिकं दुष्प्रयोज्यमुदाहरंति M. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलनं|छलन
छलनं, --ना [छल् णिच् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Deceiving, cheating, outwitting.<BR>--2<BR>Fraud, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलना
छलनं, --ना [छल् णिच् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Deceiving, cheating, outwitting.<BR>--2<BR>Fraud, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलित
छलित a. Cheated, deceived &c.<BR>--तं Deceiving, cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छलिन्
छलिन् m. A cheat, swindler,<BR>rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्लिः|छल्लि
छल्लिः, --ल्ली f. [छद्-क्विप् तां लाति<BR>ला-क गौरा˚ डीष्]<BR>1 Bark, rind.<BR>--2 A<BR>spreading creeper.<BR>--3 Offspring,<BR>progeny, posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छल्ली
छल्लिः, --ल्ली f. [छद्-क्विप् तां लाति<BR>ला-क गौरा˚ डीष्]<BR>1 Bark, rind.<BR>--2 A<BR>spreading creeper.<BR>--3 Offspring,<BR>progeny, posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छविः|छवि
छविः f. [छ्यति असारं छिनत्ति तमो वा<BR>छो-वि किच्च् वा ङीप्; cf. Uṇ. 4. 56]<BR>1<BR>Hue, colour of the skin, complexion;<BR>हिमकरोदयपांडुमुखच्छविः R. 9. 38;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">Page0501-a+ 55</a>]<BR>छविः पांडुरा Ś. 3. 10; Me. 33;<BR>U. 6. 27.<BR>--2 Colour in general.<BR>--3 Beauty,<BR>splendour, brilliance; छविकरं<BR>मुखचूर्णमृतुश्रियः R. 9. 45.<BR>--4 Light,<BR>lustre.<BR>--5 Skin, hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0500-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छष्
छष् {c1c} U. (छषति-ते) To hurt,<BR>injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाग|छागः
छाग a. (गी f.) Relating to a<BR>goat or she-goat; Y. 1. 258.<BR>--गः<BR>(गी f.)<BR>1 A goat; ब्राह्मणश्छागतो<BR>यथा (वंचितः) H. 4. 53; Ms. 3. 269.<BR>--2 The sign Aries of the zodiac.<BR>--गं<BR>1 The milk of a she-goat.<BR>--2<BR>An oblation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भोजिन् m. a<BR>wolf.<BR>--मुखः an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>--रथः, --वाहनः an epithet of Agni,<BR>the god of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागणः|छागण
छागणः A fire of dried cowdung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागल|छागलः
छागल a. (ली f.) Coming from<BR>or relating to a goat.<BR>--लः A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छागिका
छागिका A she-goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात|छातः
छात a.<BR>1 Cut, divided.<BR>--2<BR>Feeble, thin, emaciated (p. p. of<BR>छो q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रः|छात्र|छात्त्रः|छात्रं
छात्रः [छत्रं गुरोर्वैगुण्यावरणं शीलमस्य<BR>Sk.; छत्रा˚ ण] A pupil, disciple.<BR>--त्रं A<BR>kind of honey.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गंडः an<BR>indifferent poetical scholar,<BR>knowing only the beginnings of stanzas.<BR>--दर्शनं fresh butter prepared from<BR>milk one day old.<BR>--व्यंसकः a<BR>roguish or dull-witted pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छात्रकं|छात्रक
छात्रकं Honey in the comb or<BR>hive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादं|छाद
छादं [छद्-अच्] A thatch, roof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादनं|छादन|छादनः
छादनं [छद्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 A cover,<BR>screen (fig. also); विनिर्मितं<BR>छादनमज्ञतायाः Bh. 2. 7.<BR>--2 Concealing.<BR>--3<BR>A leaf.<BR>--4 Clothing.<BR>--5 Darkening.<BR>--नी Hide, skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छादित|छादितः
छादित a. See छन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाद्मिक|छाद्मिकः
छाद्मिक a. [छद्मना चरति व्यवहरति<BR>ठक्] Fraudulent.<BR>--कः A rogue;<BR>Ms. 4. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छांदस|छान्दस|छान्दसः
छांदस a. (सी f.) [छंदः अधीते<BR>वेत्ति वा पक्षे अण्]<BR>1 Vedic, peculiar to<BR>the Vedas; as छांदसः प्रयोगः.<BR>--2<BR>Studying or familiar with the<BR>Vedas.<BR>--3 Metrical.<BR>--सः A<BR>Brāhmaṇa versed in the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छांदसीय|छान्दसीय
छांदसीय a. Metrical, familiar with<BR>metres.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छांदोमिक|छान्दोमिक
छांदोमिक a. Belonging to the<BR>छंदोमस् (as a day or सूक्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छाया
छाया [छो-ण Uṇ. 4. 109]<BR>1 Shade,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-b" target="_blank">Page0501-b+ 55</a>]<BR>shadow (changed at the end of Tat. comp.<BR>into छायं when बाहुल्य or thickness of<BR>shade is meant; e. g.<BR>इक्षुच्छायनिषादिन्यः R. 4. 20; so 7. 4, 12. 50;<BR>Mu. 4. 21); छायामधः सानुगतां निषेव्य<BR>Ku. 1. 5; 6. 46; अनुभवति हि मूर्ध्ना<BR>पादपस्तीव्रमुष्णं शमयति परितापं छायया<BR>संश्रितानां Ś. 5. 7; R. 1. 75, 2. 6; 3. 70;<BR>Me. 67.<BR>--2 A reflected image, a<BR>reflection; छाया न मूर्छति मलोपहतप्रसादे<BR>शुद्धे तु दर्पणतले सुलभावकाशा Ś. 7. 32.<BR>--3 Resemblance, likeness.<BR>--4 A<BR>shadowy fancy, hallucination.<BR>--5<BR>Blending of colours.<BR>--6 Lustre,<BR>light; छायामंडललक्ष्येण R. 4. 5;<BR>रत्नच्छायाव्यतिकरः Me. 15, 35.<BR>--7<BR>Colour; Māl. 6. 5.<BR>--8 Colour of the<BR>face, complexion; केवलं लावण्यमयी<BR>छाया त्वां न मुंचति Ś. 3; मेघैरंतरितः<BR>प्रिये तव मुखच्छायानुकारी शशी Ś. D.;<BR>Pt. 5. 88.<BR>--9 Beauty; क्षामच्छायं भवनं<BR>Me. 80, 104.<BR>--10 Protection.<BR>--11 A<BR>row, line.<BR>--12 Darkness.<BR>--13 A<BR>bribe.<BR>--14 N. of Durgā.<BR>--15 The<BR>shadow of a gnomon as indicating<BR>the sun's position.<BR>--16 The Sun.<BR>--17 Nightmare.<BR>--18 N. of a wife of<BR>the sun (she was but a shadow or<BR>likeness of संज्ञा, the wife of the Sun;<BR>consequently when संज्ञा went to<BR>her father's house without the<BR>knowledge of her husband, she put<BR>छाया in her own place. छाया bore<BR>to the Sun three children:--two<BR>sons Sāvarṇi and Śani, and one<BR>daughter Tapanī).<BR>--यः One who grants<BR>shade.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः the moon.<BR>--आत्मन् m. a reflected image or<BR>form.<BR>--करः the bearer of an umbrella.<BR>--ग्रहः a mirror.<BR>--तनयः, --सुतः,<BR>--आत्मजः Saturn, son of छाया.<BR>--तरुः,<BR>--द्रुमः a large umbrageous tree; Me. 1;<BR>Ś. 4. 11.<BR>--द्वितीय a. ‘accompanied<BR>only by one's shadow’, alone.<BR>--पथः<BR>the galaxy, the atmosphere;<BR>R. 13. 2.<BR>--भृत् m. the moon.<BR>--मानः the<BR>moon.<BR>--(नं) a measure of shadow.<BR>--मित्रं a parasol.<BR>--मृगधरः the moon.<BR>--यंत्रं a sun-dial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छायामय
छायामय a. Reflected, shadowy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छालः|छाल|छालं
छालः, --लं Bark; a bark-garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छालं|छाल|छालः
छालः, --लं Bark; a bark-garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिः|छि
छिः f. [छो-वा˚ कि] Abuse,<BR>reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिक्का
छिक्का Sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित|छितं
छित a. See छात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
छिद् {c7c} U. (छिनत्ति, छिंत्ते, चिच्छेद,<BR>अच्छिदत्, अच्छैत्सीत्, अच्छित्त, छेत्तुं, छिन्न)<BR>1 To cut, cut or lop off, hew, mow,<BR>tear, pierce, break asunder, rend,<BR>split, divide; नैनं छिंदंति शस्त्राणि<BR>Bg. 2. 23; R. 12. 80; Ms. 4. 69, 70;<BR>9. 276; Y. 2. 302.<BR>--2 To disturb,<BR>interrupt (as sleep).<BR>--3 To remove,<BR>drive off, destroy, quell, annihilate;<BR>तृष्णां छिंद्धि Bh. 2. 77; एतन्मे संशयं<BR>छिंद्धि मतिर्मे संप्रमुह्यति Mb; राघवो<BR>रथमप्राप्तां तामाशां च सुरद्विषां ।<BR>अर्धचंद्रमुखैर्बाणैश्चिच्छेद कदलीसुखं ॥ R. 12. 96;<BR>Ku. 7. 16.<BR>--4 To take away, remove,<BR>deprive of; न नः किंचिद् छिद्यते Ś. B. we<BR>do not lose anything [cf. L. scindo].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्तिः|छित्ति
छित्तिः f. [छिद्-क्तिन्] Cutting,<BR>dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छित्वर|छित्वरः
छित्वर a. (री f.) [छिद्-ष्वरप् पृषो˚ दस्य<BR>तः]<BR>1 Fit for cutting.<BR>--2 Hostile,<BR>fraudulent, roguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्
छिद् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Cutting, dividing, destroying,<BR>removing, splitting &c.;<BR>श्रमच्छिदामाश्रमपादपानां R. 5. 6; पंकच्छिदः फलस्य<BR>M. 2. 8. --m. The divisor,<BR>denominator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदकं|छिदक
छिदकं [छिद्-क्वुन्]<BR>1 Indra's<BR>thunderbolt.<BR>--2 A diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदा
छिदा Cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदिः|छिदि
छिदिः f.<BR>1 An axe.<BR>--2 Indra's<BR>thunderbolt.<BR>--3 Cutting off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदिरः|छिदिर
छिदिरः [छिद्-किरच् Uṇ. 1. 51]<BR>1<BR>An axe.<BR>--2 A sword.<BR>--3 Fire.<BR>--4 A<BR>rope, cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिदुर|छिदुरः
छिदुर a. [छिद्-कुरच्]<BR>1 Cutting,<BR>dividing, removing; Śi. 6. 8.<BR>--2<BR>Easily breaking.<BR>--3 Broken,<BR>disordered, deranged; संलक्ष्यते<BR>नच्छिदुरोऽपि हारः R. 16. 62.<BR>--4 Hostile.<BR>--5<BR>Roguish, knavish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्र|छिद्रं
छिद्र a. [छिद्-रक्, छिद्र-अच् वा]<BR>Pierced, containing holes.<BR>--द्रं<BR>1 A hole,<BR>slit; cleft, fissure, rent, pit, opening,<BR>crack; नव छिद्राणि तान्येव<BR>प्राणस्यायतनानि तु Y. 3. 99; Ms. 8. 239; अयं<BR>पटश्छिद्रशतैरलंकृतः Mk. 2. 9; so काष्ठ˚,<BR>भूमि˚ &c.<BR>--2 A defect, flaw,<BR>blemish; त्वं हि सर्षपमात्राणि परच्छिद्राणि<BR>पश्यसि । आत्मनो बिल्वमात्राणि पश्यन्नपि<BR>न पश्यसि ॥ Mb.<BR>--3 A vulnerable or<BR>weak point, weak side,<BR>imperfection, foible; नास्य छिद्रं परो<BR>विद्याद्विद्याच्छिद्रं परस्य तु । गूहेत् कूर्म इवांगानि<BR>रक्षेद्विवरमात्मनः ॥ Ms. 7. 105, 102; छिद्रं<BR>निरूप्य सहसा प्रविशत्यशंकः H. 1. 81<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-a" target="_blank">Page0502-a+ 53</a>]<BR>(where छिद्र means a hole also);<BR>Pt. 3. 39; Pt. 2. 38; Proverb: छिद्रेष्वनर्था<BR>बहुलीभवंति ‘misfortunes never come<BR>single’.<BR>--4 (Astr.) N. of the eighth<BR>house.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुजीविन्,<BR>--अनुसंधानिन्, --अनुसारिन्, --अन्वेषिन् a. {1} looking<BR>out for faults or flaws. {2} seeking<BR>the weak points of another, picking<BR>holes, censorious; सर्पाणां दुर्जनानां च<BR>परच्छिद्रानुजीविनां Pt. 1.<BR>--अंतर् m. a cane,<BR>reed.<BR>--आत्मन् a. one who exposes<BR>his weak points to the attack of<BR>others.<BR>--कर्ण a. having the ear<BR>pierced.<BR>--दर्शन a. {1} exhibiting faults. {2}<BR>seeking the weak points.<BR>--दर्शिन् a.<BR>observing faults, a captious critic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0501-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रयति
छिद्रयति Den. P. To perforate,<BR>bore, pierce through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्रित|छिद्रितः
छिद्रित a. [छिद्र्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Having holes.<BR>--2 Bored, perforated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिद्वर
छिद्वर = छित्वर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छिन्न|छिन्नं
छिन्न p. p. [छिद्-क्त]<BR>1 Cut,<BR>divided, rent, chopped, riven, torn,<BR>broken.<BR>--2 Destroyed, removed; see<BR>छिद्.<BR>--3 Decaying, declining.<BR>--4<BR>Exhausted, tired, fatigued.<BR>--न्ना A<BR>whore, harlot.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केश a. shorn,<BR>shaven.<BR>--द्रुमः a riven tree.<BR>--द्वैध a.<BR>whose doubt is dispelled.<BR>--नासिक<BR>a. noseless.<BR>--भिन्न a. cut up through<BR>and through, mutilated, mangled,<BR>cut up.<BR>--मस्त, --मस्तक a. decapitated.<BR>--(स्ता, --का) a headless form of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--मूल a. cut up by the roots;<BR>R. 7. 43.<BR>--श्वासः a kind of asthma.<BR>--संशय a. ‘one whose doubt is<BR>dispelled’, free from doubt, confirmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेत्तृ
छेत्तृ a.<BR>1 Cutter.<BR>--2 A<BR>wood-cutter.<BR>--3 Destroying, removing<BR>(doubts &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदः|छेद
छेदः [छिद् भावे घञ् अच् वा]<BR>1 Cutting,<BR>felling down, breaking down,<BR>dividing; अभिज्ञाश्छेदपातानां क्रियंते नंदनद्रुमाः<BR>Ku. 2. 41; छेदो दंशस्य दाहो वा<BR>M. 4. 4; R. 14. 1; Ms. 8. 270, 370;<BR>Y. 2. 223, 240.<BR>--2 Solving, removing,<BR>dissipating, clearing; as in संशयच्छेद.<BR>--3 Destruction, interruption;<BR>निद्राच्छेदाभिताम्रा Mu. 3. 21.<BR>--4 Cessation,<BR>end, termination, disappearance as<BR>in घर्मच्छेद Ś. 2. 5.<BR>--5 A<BR>distinguishing mark.<BR>--6 A cut, an incision,<BR>cleft.<BR>--7 Deprivation, want,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">Page0502-b+ 52</a>]<BR>deficiency.<BR>--8 Failure; संततिच्छेद Ś. 6.<BR>--9 A piece, bit, cut, fragment,<BR>section; बिसकिसलयच्छेदपाथेयवंतः<BR>Me. 11, 59; अभिनवकरिदंतच्छदपांडुः<BR>कपोलः Māl. 1. 22; Ku. 1. 4; Ś. 3. 6;<BR>R. 12. 100.<BR>--10 (In math.) A divisor,<BR>the denominator of a fraction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः a wood-cutter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदक|छेदकः
छेदक a. [छिद्-ण्वुल्] Cutting off,<BR>dividing &c.<BR>--कः The<BR>denominator of a fraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदन|छेदनं
छेदन a. [छिद् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Cutting<BR>asunder, dividing, splitting.<BR>--2<BR>Destroying, solving, removing.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Cutting, tearing, cutting off,<BR>splitting, dividing; Ms. 8. 280, 292, 322.<BR>--2 A section, portion, bit, part.<BR>--3<BR>Destruction, removal.<BR>--4 Division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदि|छेदिः
छेदि a. [छिद्-इन्]<BR>1 Cutting.<BR>--2<BR>Breaking.<BR>--दिः<BR>1 A carpenter.<BR>--2<BR>Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदित|छेदितं
छेदित a. Cut, divided, split &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेदिन्
छेदिन् a.<BR>1 Cutting or tearing off,<BR>dividing.<BR>--2 Destroying, removing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेद्य
छेद्य p. p. [छिद्-ण्यत्] To be cut or<BR>divided, divisible.<BR>--द्यं Amputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुछुंदरः|छुच्छुन्दर|छुच्छुन्दरः|छुछुंदर|छुछुन्दर
छुछुंदरः (री f.) The musk-rat;<BR>Y. 3. 213; Ms. 12. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुट्
छुट् {c6c} {c10c} P. (छुटति, छोटयति) To<BR>cut, clip off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुड्
छुड् {c6c} P. (छुडति) To cover, hide,<BR>screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुद्रं|छुद्र
छुद्रं [छद्-रक् पृषो˚]<BR>1 Retaliation,<BR>counteraction.<BR>--2 A ray (of light).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुप्
छुप् {c6c} P. (छुपति) To touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुपः|छुप
छुपः a. [छुप् कर्तरि क, घञर्थे क वा]<BR>Active, zealous, swift.<BR>--पः<BR>1 Touch.<BR>--2 A shrub, bush.<BR>--3 Combat, war.<BR>--4 Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुबुकं|छुबुक
छुबुकं Ved. The chin; see चिबुक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुर्
छुर् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (छोरति, छुरित)<BR>1 To cut,<BR>divide.<BR>--2 To engrave. {vII.v} {c6c} P. (<BR>छुरति, छुरित)<BR>1 To cover, smear, daub,<BR>inlay, coat, envelop.<BR>--2 To<BR>intermix. --Caus. (छोरयति, छुरयति)<BR>1 To<BR>inlay, set with mosaic ornaments.<BR>--2 To overspread.<BR>--3 To besmear;<BR>Māl. 9. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरणं|छुरण
छुरणं<BR>1 Smearing, anointing;<BR>ज्योत्स्नाभस्मच्छुरणधवला रात्रिकापालिकीयं<BR>K. P. 10.<BR>--2 Overspreading; U. 6. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरा
छुरा [छुर्-क] Lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरिका
छुरिका A knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरित|छुरितं
छुरित p. p. [छुर्-क्त]<BR>1 Set, inlaid.<BR>--2 Overspread, coated, covered over<BR>with; अनेकधानुच्छुरिताश्मराशेः<BR>Śi. 3. 4, 7; इंदुकिरणच्छुरितमुखीं K. 10.<BR>--3<BR>Blended, intermixed; परस्परेण<BR>छुरितामलच्छवी Śi. 1. 22.<BR>--4 Besmeared,<BR>anointed; Ve. 1. 1.<BR>--5 Cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छुरी
छुरी, छूरिका, छूरी A knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छूरिका
छुरी, छूरिका, छूरी A knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छूरी
छुरी, छूरिका, छूरी A knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृद्
छृद् {vI.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (छर्दति, छर्दयति<BR>ते) To kindle. {vII.v} {c7c} P. (छृणत्ति,<BR>छृन्न)<BR>1 To play.<BR>--2 To shine.<BR>--3 To<BR>vomit. --Caus. (छर्दयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>pour out.<BR>--2 To spit out, eject,<BR>vomit.<BR>--3 To kindle, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छृष्
छृष् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (छर्षति, छर्षयति-ते)<BR>To beg, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेक|छेकः
छेक a. [छो-बा˚ डेकन् Tv.]<BR>1 Tame,<BR>domesticated (as a beast).<BR>--2<BR>Citizen, town-bred.<BR>--3 Shrewd, trained<BR>in the acuteness and vice of towns.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A bee.<BR>--2 A kind of अनुप्रास<BR>see below.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुप्रासः one<BR>of the five kinds of अनुप्रास, ‘the<BR>single alliteration’, which is a<BR>similarity occurring once (or singly)<BR>and in more than one way among a<BR>collection of consonants; e. g.<BR>आदाय बकुलगंधानंधीकुर्वन्पदे पदे भ्रमरान् ।<BR>अयमेति मंदमंदं कावेरीवारिपावनः पवनः ॥<BR>S. D. 634.<BR>--अपह्नुतिः f. a figure of speech;<BR>one of the varieties of अपह्नुति. The<BR>Candrāloka thus defines and<BR>illustrates it: --छेकांपह्नुतिरन्यस्य शंकातस्तस्य<BR>निह्नवे । प्रजल्पन्मत्पदे लग्नः कांतः किं न हि नूपुरः<BR>5. 27.<BR>--उक्तिः f. insinuation, double<BR>entendre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेकाल
छेकाल, छेकिल a. = छेक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेकिल
छेकाल, छेकिल a. = छेक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेमंडः|छेमण्ड|छेमंड|छेमण्डः
छेमंडः An orphan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छेलकः|छेलक
छेलकः A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छैदिकः|छैदिक
छैदिकः A cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छो
छो {c4c} P. (छ्यति, अच्छात्-अच्छासीत्,<BR>छात, or छित, caus. छाययति) To cut,<BR>cut asunder, mow, reap; Bk. 14. 101,<BR>15. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोटिका
छोटिका Snapping the thumb<BR>and fore-finger together (Mar. चुटकी)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोटिन्
छोटिन् m. [छुट्-णिनि] A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोरणं|छोरण
छोरणं A bandoning, leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छोलंगः|छोलङ्ग|छोलङ्गः
छोलंगः A citron, lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

छ्यु
छ्यु {c1c} A. (छ्यवते) To go, move<BR>approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0502-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज|जः
ज a. [जि-जन्-जु-वा ड]<BR>1 (At the<BR>end of comp.) Born from or in,<BR>produced or caused by, descended<BR>from, growing in, living or being at<BR>or in &c.; अत्रिनेत्रज, कुलज, जलज,<BR>क्षत्रियज, अंडज, उद्भिज &c.<BR>--2<BR>Prepared from, made of.<BR>--3 Belonging<BR>to, connected with, peculiar to.<BR>--4<BR>Swift.<BR>--5 Victorious, conquering.<BR>--जः<BR>1 A father.<BR>--2 Production,<BR>birth.<BR>--3 Poison.<BR>--4 An imp or<BR>goblin.<BR>--5 A conqueror.<BR>--6 Lustre.<BR>--7 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--8 N. of Śiva.<BR>--9<BR>Enjoyment.<BR>--10 Speed, swiftness.<BR>--11 (In prosody) One of the eight<BR>syllabic feet (गण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंस्
जंस् {c10c} P. (जंसयति)<BR>1 To protect.<BR>--2 To liberate, release, set free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जकुटः|जकुट|जकुटं
जकुटः<BR>1 The Malaya mountain.<BR>--2 A dog.<BR>--टं A pair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्ष्
जक्ष् {c2c} P. (जक्षिति, जक्षित or जग्ध)<BR>1<BR>To eat, eat up, destroy, consume;<BR>Bk. 4. 39; 13. 28; 15. 46, 18. 19;<BR>Me. 21.<BR>--2 To laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षणं|जक्षण
जक्षणं, जक्षिः Eating, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जक्षिः|जक्षि
जक्षणं, जक्षिः Eating, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगत्
जगत् a.(ती f.)<BR>1 Moving,<BR>moveable; सूर्य आत्मा जगतस्तस्थुषश्च<BR>Rv. 1. 115. 1; इदं विश्वं जगत्सर्वमजगच्चापि<BR>यद्भवेत् Mb. --m. Wind, air. --n. The<BR>world, the universe; जगतः पितरौ वंदे<BR>पार्वतीपरमेश्वरौ R. 1. 1.<BR>--2 ‘The world<BR>of the soul’, body; Māl. 5. 2.<BR>--ती<BR>(dual) Heaven and the lower world.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंबा, --अंबिका N. of Durgā.<BR>--आत्मन् m. the Supreme spirit.<BR>--आदिः, --आदिजः the Supreme deity.<BR>--आदिजः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--आधारः {1} time. {2} air, wind.<BR>--आयुः,<BR>--आयुस् m. wind.<BR>--ईशः, --पतिः the<BR>lord of the universe,’ the Supreme<BR>deity; an epithet of Viṣṇu and<BR>Śiva.<BR>--उद्धारः salvation of the<BR>world.<BR>--कर्तृ, --धातृ m. {1} the<BR>creator of the world. {2} Brahmā.<BR>--कारणं the cause of the universe.<BR>--गुरुः {1} the Supreme deity. {2}<BR>Śiva. {3} Nārada. {4} Brahmā. {5}<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--चक्षुस् m. the sun.<BR>--जीवः<BR>a living being.<BR>--त्रयं the three<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-b" target="_blank">Page0503-b+ 48</a>]<BR>worlds i. e. heaven, earth and the<BR>lower world.<BR>--दीपः the sun.<BR>--धात्री<BR>{1} Durgā. {2} Sarasvatī.<BR>--नाथः {1}<BR>the lord of the universe. {2} Viṣṇu.<BR>{3} Dattātreya. {4} N. of a<BR>country. {5} N. of an idol at Jagannātha.<BR>{6} N. of a poet.<BR>--(थौ) Viṣṇu and<BR>Śiva.<BR>--(था) N. of Durgā.<BR>--निवासः<BR>{1} the Supreme Being. {2} an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu; जगन्निवासो<BR>वसुदेवभर्मणि Śi. 1. 1. {3} worldly existence.<BR>--प्रभुः {1} an epithet of Brahmā,<BR>Viṣṇu, and Śiva. {2} an Arhat of<BR>the Jainas.<BR>--प्राणः, --बलः wind.<BR>--बीजं<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--मातृ f. {1} Durgā. {2}<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR>--योनिः {1} the Supreme<BR>Being. {2} an epithet of Viṣṇu. {3}<BR>of Śiva. {4} of Brahmā. (--निः f.)<BR>the earth.<BR>--वंद्यः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--विनाशः the expiration of Yugas.<BR>--वहा the earth.<BR>--साक्षिन् m. {1} the<BR>Supreme spirit. {2} the sun.<BR>--सेतुः<BR>the Supreme Being.<BR>--स्रष्टृ m. {1} the<BR>creator of the world. {2} Brahmā.<BR>{3} Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगती
जगती<BR>1 The earth; (समीहते)<BR>नयेन जेतुं जगतीं सुयोधनः Ki. 1. 7;<BR>समतीत्य भाति जगती जगती 5. 20.<BR>--2<BR>People, mankind.<BR>--3 A cow.<BR>--4 The<BR>site of a house.<BR>--5 A field planted<BR>with jambu.<BR>--6 A kind of metre;<BR>(See App.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधीश्वरः,<BR>--ईश्वरः a king; N. 2. 1.<BR>--धरः a<BR>mountain.<BR>--रुह् m. a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगदः|जगद
जगदः An attendant, guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगनुः|जगनु
जगनुः(न्नुः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 An<BR>insect.<BR>--3 An animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्नुः|जगन्नु
जगनुः(न्नुः)<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 An<BR>insect.<BR>--3 An animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगरः|जगर
जगरः [जागर्ति युद्धेऽनेन जागृ-अच्<BR>पृषो˚ Tv.] An armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगल|जगलः
जगल a. Roguish, tricky, knavish.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Cowdung.<BR>--2 An armour.<BR>--3<BR>A kind of liquor (m. also in the<BR>last two senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्ध|जग्धं
जग्ध a. [अद् कर्मणि-क्त] Eaten.<BR>--ग्धं<BR>1 A place where a person has<BR>eaten.<BR>--2 Eating, dinner, food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्धिः|जग्धि
जग्धिः f. [अद्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Eating;<BR>Māl. 6. 19.<BR>--2 Food, victuals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जग्मि|जग्मिः
जग्मि a. [गम् किन् द्वित्वम्]<BR>1 Going,<BR>being in constant motion.<BR>--2 Going<BR>to, hastening or drawing towards.<BR>--ग्मिः Wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनं|जघन
जघनं [वक्रं हंति हन् यङ् अच् पृषो˚;<BR>Uṇ. 5. 32]<BR>1 The hip and the loins, the<BR>buttocks; घटय जघने कांचीमंच स्रजा<BR>कबरीभरं Gīt. 12.<BR>--2 The pudenda.<BR>--3 Rear-guard, the reserve of an<BR>army.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्धः {1} the hinder<BR>part. {2} rear-guard.<BR>--कूपकौ (dual)<BR>the hollows of the loins of a<BR>handsome woman.<BR>--गौरवं weight of the<BR>hips; Ś. 3. 8.<BR>--चपला {1} an<BR>unchaste or libidinous woman;<BR>पत्यौर्विदेशयाते परमसुखं जघनचपलायाः<BR>Pt. 1. 173. {2} a woman active in dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघनिन्
जघनिन् a. Having large buttocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघन्य|जघन्यः
जघन्य a. [जघने भवः यत्]<BR>1<BR>Hindmost, last; Bg. 14. 18; Ms. 8. 270.<BR>--2 Worst, vilest, base, lowest,<BR>censurable.<BR>--3 Of low origin or<BR>rank.<BR>--न्यः A Śūdra.<BR>--न्यं The<BR>penis.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः {1} a younger<BR>brother. {2} a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्निः|जघ्नि
जघ्निः [हन्-किन् द्वित्वं च] A weapon<BR>(offensive).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जघ्नु|जघ्नुः
जघ्नु a. [हन्-कु द्वित्वं च] Striking,<BR>killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंगम|जङ्गम|जङ्गमः
जंगम a. [गम्-यङ् अच्]<BR>1 Moving,<BR>living, moveable (opp.<BR>immovable स्थावर); चिताग्निरिव जंगमः<BR>R. 15. 16; शोकाग्निरिव जंगमः<BR>Mv. 5. 20; Ms. 1. 41.<BR>--2<BR>Derived from living beings.<BR>--मं A<BR>moveable thing; R. 2. 44.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इतर a. immovable.<BR>--कुटी an<BR>umbrella.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंगल|जङ्गल|जङ्गलं|जङ्गलः
जंगल a. [गल्-यङ्-अच् पृषो˚]<BR>Desert, waste.<BR>--लः, --लं Flesh, meat.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A desert, dreary ground, waste<BR>land.<BR>--2 A thicket, forest.<BR>--3 A<BR>secluded or unfrequented place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंगालः|जङ्गाल|जंगाल|जङ्गालः
जंगालः A ridge of earth<BR>running along the edge of a field to<BR>collect water and to form a passage<BR>over it, land-mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंगुलं|जङ्गुल|जंगुल
जंगुलं Poison, venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0503-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंघा|जङ्घा
जंघा [जंघन्यते कुटिलं गच्छति हन्<BR>यङ्लुकि अच् पृषो˚; cf. Uṇ. 5. 31]<BR>1 Leg<BR>from the ankle to the knee, the<BR>shank.<BR>--2 The upper part of the leg,<BR>the part about the loins.<BR>--3 A part<BR>of a bedstead.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः, --करिकः,<BR>--कारः, --कारिकः a runner, courier,<BR>an express.<BR>--त्राणं an armour for<BR>the legs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंघाल|जङ्घाल|जङ्घालः
जंघाल a. [जंघा वेगवती अस्त्यस्य लच्]<BR>Running swiftly, rapid.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A<BR>courier.<BR>--2 A deer, an antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंघिल|जङ्घिल
जंघिल a. [जंघ-इलच्] Running<BR>swiftly, rapid, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज्
जज्, जंज् {c1c} P. (जजति or जंजति) To<BR>fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंज्|जञ्ज्
जज्, जंज् {c1c} P. (जजति or जंजति) To<BR>fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जजः|जज|जजं
ज(जं)जः A warrior, soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जजं|जज|जजः
ज(जं)जः A warrior, soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जज्झ्
जज्झ् (जज्झति) To make a<BR>dashing sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंजन
जंजन a. [जन्-यङ् लुक्-अच् पृषो˚]<BR>1<BR>Being born again.<BR>--2 Burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जंजपूक|जञ्जपूक|जञ्जपूकः
जंजपूक a. Muttering prayers<BR>repeatedly.<BR>--कः An ascetic, or<BR>devotee (who mutters prayers); cf.<BR>P. III. 2. 166.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जट्
जट् {c1c} P. (जटति) To clot, become<BR>twisted or matted together (as<BR>hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जट
जट a. [जट्-अच्; जन् उणा˚ टन्<BR>अंत्यलोपश्च] Wearing twisted locks of<BR>hair.<BR>--टा [Uṇ. 5. 30]<BR>1 The hair<BR>matted and twisted together,<BR>matted or clotted hair; अंसव्यापि<BR>शकुंतनीडनिचितं बिभ्रज्जटामंडलं Ś. 7. 11;<BR>जटाश्च बिभृयान्नित्यं Ms. 6. 6;<BR>Māl. 1. 2.<BR>--2 A fibrous root.<BR>--3 A particular<BR>manner of reciting Vedic texts; thus<BR>the words नमः रुद्रेभ्यः repeated in<BR>this manner would stand thus:<BR>--नमो रुद्रेभ्यो रुद्रेभ्यो नमो नमो रुद्रेभ्यः.<BR>--4 A root in general.<BR>--5 A<BR>branch.<BR>--6 The शतावरी plant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चीरः, --टंकः, टीरः, --धरः<BR>epithets of Śiva.<BR>--जूटः {1} a mass of<BR>twisted hair (in general). {2} the<BR>twisted hair of Śiva; जटाजूटग्रंथौ<BR>यदसि विनिबद्धा पुरभिदा G. L. 14.<BR>--ज्वालः a lamp.<BR>--धर a. wearing matted<BR>hair.<BR>--(रः) a mendicant or ascetic.<BR>--मंडलं braided hair forming a coil<BR>on the top of the head.<BR>--मौलिः crest<BR>of (formed by) clotted hair;<BR>Ku. 2. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटायुः|जटायु
जटायुः, --जटायुस् m. A son of Śyenī<BR>and Aruṇa, a semi divine bird.<BR>[He was a great friend of Daśaratha.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">Page0504-b+ 59</a>]<BR>He once saved his life while he was<BR>thrown down along with his car by<BR>Saturn against whom he had proceeded<BR>when a drought, said to be caused by<BR>the planet, well-nigh devastated<BR>the earth. While Rāvaṇa was carrying<BR>away Sītā Jaṭāyu heard her cries in the<BR>chariot and fought most desperately<BR>with the formidable giant to rescue her<BR>from his grasp. But he was mortally<BR>wounded, and remained in that state<BR>till Rāma passed by that place in the<BR>course of his search after Sītā. The<BR>kind-hearted bird told Rāma that his<BR>wife had been carried away by<BR>Rāvaṇa and then breathed his last. His<BR>funeral rites were duly performed by<BR>Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटायुस्
जटायुः, --जटायुस् m. A son of Śyenī<BR>and Aruṇa, a semi divine bird.<BR>[He was a great friend of Daśaratha.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">Page0504-b+ 59</a>]<BR>He once saved his life while he was<BR>thrown down along with his car by<BR>Saturn against whom he had proceeded<BR>when a drought, said to be caused by<BR>the planet, well-nigh devastated<BR>the earth. While Rāvaṇa was carrying<BR>away Sītā Jaṭāyu heard her cries in the<BR>chariot and fought most desperately<BR>with the formidable giant to rescue her<BR>from his grasp. But he was mortally<BR>wounded, and remained in that state<BR>till Rāma passed by that place in the<BR>course of his search after Sītā. The<BR>kind-hearted bird told Rāma that his<BR>wife had been carried away by<BR>Rāvaṇa and then breathed his last. His<BR>funeral rites were duly performed by<BR>Rāma and Lakṣmaṇa].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटाल|जटालः
जटाल a. [जटा अस्यर्थें सिध्मा ˚लच्]<BR>1<BR>Wearing a coil of twisted hair.<BR>--2<BR>Collected together (like matted<BR>hair); दवदहनजटालज्वालजालाहतानां<BR>Bv. 1. 36.<BR>--लः<BR>1 The (Indian)<BR>fig-tree.<BR>--2 Bdellium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटालक
जटालक, --जटिक a. Wearing<BR>twisted or braided hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिक
जटालक, --जटिक a. Wearing<BR>twisted or braided hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिः|जटि
जटिः(टी) f. [जट्-इन्]<BR>1 The<BR>(Indian) fig-tree.<BR>--2 Clotted hair.<BR>--3<BR>An assemblage, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटी
जटिः(टी) f. [जट्-इन्]<BR>1 The<BR>(Indian) fig-tree.<BR>--2 Clotted hair.<BR>--3<BR>An assemblage, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिन्
जटिन् (नी f.) a. [जटा अस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>Having twisted hair. --m.<BR>1 An<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--2 The waved-leaf<BR>fig-tree (प्लक्ष).<BR>--3 An elephant<BR>sixty years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिल|जटिलः
जटिल a. [जटा अस्त्यर्थे इलच्]<BR>1<BR>Wearing matted or twisted hair (as<BR>an ascetic); विवेशकश्चिज्जटिलस्तपोवनं<BR>Ku. 5. 30; (जटिल may be here a<BR>noun meaning ‘an ascetic’).<BR>ज्येष्ठानुवृत्तिज्जटिलं च शिरोऽस्य साधोः R. 13. 78.<BR>--2 Complicated, confused,<BR>intermixed, intermingled; विजानंतोऽ<BR>प्येते वयमिह विपज्जालजटिलान् न मुंचामः<BR>कामानहह गहनो मोहमहिमा Bh. 3. 21;<BR>शिखाकलाप˚ Pt. 2. 81; Ve. 2. 18.<BR>--3 Dense, impervious; Bv. 1. 52.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A lion.<BR>--2 A goat.<BR>--3 An ascetic.<BR>--4 A Brāhmaṇa in the first period<BR>of his life.<BR>--ला Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिलीकृ
जटिलीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To twist together,<BR>form into a braid.<BR>--2 To complicate,<BR>interweave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटिलीभावः|जटिलीभाव
जटिलीभावः Complication,<BR>confusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जटुलः|जटुल
जटु(डु)लः [जट्-उलच् पृषो˚टस्य डो<BR>वा] A freckle, mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडुलः|जडुल
जटु(डु)लः [जट्-उलच् पृषो˚टस्य डो<BR>वा] A freckle, mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठर|जठरं|जठरः
जठर a. [जायते जंतुर्गर्भो वास्मिन् जन्-अर<BR>ठांत देशः Tv.]<BR>1 Hard, stiff, firm.<BR>--2<BR>Old.<BR>--3 Bound, tied.<BR>--रः, --रं<BR>1 The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">Page0504-c+ 56</a>]<BR>stomach, belly, abdomen; जठरं को<BR>न बिभर्ति केवलं Pt. 1. 22.<BR>--2 The<BR>womb.<BR>--3 A hole, cavity.<BR>--4 The<BR>interior of anything.<BR>--5 The bosom.<BR>--6 Morbid affection of the bowels.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः the digestive fire<BR>of the stomach, the gastric fluid.<BR>--आमयः dropsy.<BR>--ज्वाला, --व्यथा<BR>bellyache, colic.<BR>--यंत्रणा, --यातना pain<BR>endured by the child in the womb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठरीकृत
जठरीकृत a.<BR>1 Contained in the<BR>belly.<BR>--2 Concealed in the bosom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जठलं|जठल
जठलं Ved. The cavity or<BR>receptacle of waters.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जड|जडं|जडः
जड a. [जलति घनीभवति जल् अच् लस्य<BR>डः Tv.]<BR>1 Cold, frigid, chilly;<BR>Māl. 9. 13; U. 6. 13.<BR>--2 Dull,<BR>paralysed, motionless, benumbed;<BR>चिंताजडं दर्शनं Ś. 4. 5; U. 3. 41;<BR>6. 28; 6. 39; परामृशन् हर्षजडेन पाणिना<BR>R. 3. 68, 2. 42.<BR>--3 Dull, senseless,<BR>stupid, irrational, dull-witted;<BR>जडानंधान् पंगून्…त्रातुं G. L. 15, so<BR>जडधी, जडमति &c. Y. 2. 25;<BR>Ms. 2. 110.<BR>--4 Dulled, made senseless or<BR>apathetic, devoid of appreciation or<BR>taste; वेदाभ्यासजडः कथं नु<BR>विषयव्यावृत्तकौतूहलः V. 1. 9.<BR>--5 Stunning,<BR>benumbing, stupefying.<BR>--6 Dumb.<BR>--7 Unable to learn the Vedas<BR>(Dayabhāga).<BR>--डः<BR>1 Cold, frost,<BR>winter.<BR>--2 Idiocy, stupidity.<BR>--3<BR>Dulness, apathy, sluggishness.<BR>--डं<BR>1<BR>Water.<BR>--2 Lead.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्रिय a.<BR>slow, dilatory.<BR>--भरतः an idiot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडता
जडता, --त्वं<BR>1 Dulness, aversion<BR>to work, slothfulness.<BR>--2 Ignorance,<BR>stupidity; Pt. 1.<BR>--3 (In Rhet.)<BR>Dulness, regarded as one of the 33<BR>subordinate feelings; S. D. 175.<BR>--4<BR>Stupefaction, numbness, stupor;<BR>U. 3. 12.<BR>--5 Dulness, timidity;<BR>Māl. 6. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडत्वं|जडत्व
जडता, --त्वं<BR>1 Dulness, aversion<BR>to work, slothfulness.<BR>--2 Ignorance,<BR>stupidity; Pt. 1.<BR>--3 (In Rhet.)<BR>Dulness, regarded as one of the 33<BR>subordinate feelings; S. D. 175.<BR>--4<BR>Stupefaction, numbness, stupor;<BR>U. 3. 12.<BR>--5 Dulness, timidity;<BR>Māl. 6. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडयति
जडयति Den. P. To stupefy,<BR>benumb; Māl. 1. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडिमन्
जडिमन् m.<BR>1 Frigidity.<BR>--2<BR>Stupidity.<BR>--3 Dulness, apathy.<BR>--4 Stupor,<BR>stupefaction, Māl. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडीकृ
जडीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To stupefy, benumb.<BR>--2 To paralyse, render motionless<BR>or insensible; R. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडीभू
जडीभू {c1c} P. To become insensible<BR>or stupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडीभावः|जडीभाव
जडीभावः<BR>1 Frigidity, coldness.<BR>--2 Stupidity.<BR>--3 Apathy,<BR>sluggishness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0504-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जडुलः|जडुल
जडुलः A freckle, mark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतु|जतुः
जतु n. [जण्-ड तोंऽतादेशः<BR>Uṇ. 1. 18]<BR>1 Lac; Pt. 1. 107.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of red dye.<BR>--तुः, --तूः f. A bat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्मकं red arsenic.<BR>--गृहं<BR>a house made of lac (such as was<BR>built by Duryodhana in order to<BR>burn up the Pāṇḍavas).<BR>--पुत्रकः a<BR>man at chess.<BR>--मणिः a mole, a<BR>natural mark on the body.<BR>--रसः lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुकं|जतुक
जतुकं Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुका
जतुका<BR>1 Lac.<BR>--2 A bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतुनी
जतुनी, जतूका A bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जतूका
जतुनी, जतूका A bat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जत्रु
जत्रु n. [जन्-रु तोंऽतादेशः<BR>Uṇ. 4. 102.] The collar bone, the clavicle;<BR>जत्रुकं also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जन्
जन् {c4c} A. (जायते, जज्ञे, अजानि-अजनिष्ट,<BR>जनितुं, जात; pass. जन्यते or जायते)<BR>1 To<BR>be born or produced (with abl.<BR>of source of birth); अजनि ते वै पुत्रः<BR>Ait. Br.; Ms. 1. 9; 3. 39, 41;<BR>प्राणाद्वायुरजायत Rv. 10. 90. 12; Ms. 10. 8;<BR>3. 76; 1. 75.<BR>--2 To rise, spring up,<BR>grow (as a plant &c.).<BR>--3 To be,<BR>become, happen, take place, occur;<BR>अनिष्टादिष्टलाभेऽपि न गतिर्जायते शुभा<BR>H. 1. 6; रक्तनेत्रोऽजानि क्षणात् Bk. 6. 32;<BR>Y. 3. 226; Ms. 1. 99.<BR>--4 To be<BR>possible, applicable &c.<BR>--5 To be born<BR>or destined for anything. --Caus.<BR>(जनयति)<BR>1 To give birth, beget, cause,<BR>produce.<BR>--2 To cause, occasion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनः|जन
जनः [जन्-अच्]<BR>1 A creature, living<BR>being, man.<BR>--2 An individual or<BR>person (whether male or female);<BR>क्व वयं क्व परोक्षमन्मथो मृगशावैः<BR>सममेधितो जनः Ś. 2. 18; तत्तस्य किमपि द्रव्यं<BR>यो हि यस्य प्रियो जनः U. 2. 19; so<BR>सखीजनः a female friend; दासजनः a<BR>slave, अबलाजनः &c. (In this sense<BR>जनः or अयं जनः is often used by the<BR>speaker-whether male or female, in<BR>the sing. or pl.--instead of the first<BR>personal pronoun to speak of<BR>himself in the third person); अयं जनः<BR>प्रष्टुमनास्तपोधने Ku. 5. 40 (male); भ<BR>गवन्परवानयं जनः प्रतिकूलाचरितं<BR>क्षमस्व मे R. 8. 81 (female);<BR>पश्यानंगशरातुरं जनमिमं त्रातापि नो रक्षासि Nāg. 1. 1<BR>(female and pl.).<BR>--3 Men<BR>collectively, the people, the world (in sing. or<BR>pl.); एवं जनो गृह्णाति M. 1; सतीमपि<BR>ज्ञातिकुलैकसंश्रयां जनोऽन्यथा भर्तृमतीं<BR>विशंकते Ś. 5. 17.<BR>--4 Race, nation,<BR>tribe.<BR>--5 The world beyond<BR>Maharloka, the heaven of deified mortals.<BR>--ना Birth, production.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिग<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-b" target="_blank">Page0505-b+ 57</a>]<BR>a. extraordinary, uncommon,<BR>superhuman.<BR>--अधिपः, --अधिनाथः {1} a<BR>king. {2} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--अंतः {1} a<BR>place removed from men, an<BR>uninhabited place. {2} a region. {3} an<BR>epithet of Yama. {4} personal<BR>proximity.<BR>--अंतिकं secret communication,<BR>whispering or speaking aside (to<BR>another). (--ind.) aside (to another)<BR>(in dramas); the S. D. thus defines<BR>this stage direction:<BR>--त्रिपताककरेणान्यानपवार्यांतरा कथां । अन्योन्यामंत्रणं<BR>यत् स्याज्जनांते तज्जनांतिकं ॥ 425.<BR>--अर्णवः a large concourse of people,<BR>caravan.<BR>--अर्थशब्दः a family<BR>appellation.<BR>--अर्दनः an epithet of Viṣṇu<BR>or Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--अशनः a wolf.<BR>--आकीर्ण<BR>a. thronged or crowded with people;<BR>Ś. 5. 10.<BR>--आचारः {1} a popular usage<BR>or custom. {2} propriety, decorum.<BR>--आश्रमः an asylum for people, an<BR>inn, caravansary.<BR>--आश्रयः a pavilion.<BR>--इंद्रः, --ईशः, --ईश्वरः, a king.<BR>--इष्ट a.<BR>desired or liked by the people.<BR>--(ष्टः)<BR>a kind of jasmine.<BR>--(ष्टा) turmeric.<BR>--उदाहरणं glory, fame.<BR>--ओघः a<BR>concourse of people, crowd, mob.<BR>--कारिन् m. lac.<BR>--चक्षुस् n. ‘the<BR>people's eye’, the sun.<BR>--जन्मादिः the<BR>Supreme Being.<BR>--त्रा an umbrella, a<BR>parasol.<BR>--देवः a king.<BR>--पदः {1} a<BR>community, race, nation; Y. 1. 361 v. l. {2}<BR>a kingdom, an empire, an inhabited<BR>country; जनपदे न गदः पदमादधौ<BR>R. 9. 4; दाक्षिणात्ये जनपदे Pt. 1; Me. 48.<BR>{3} the country (opp. the town पुर,<BR>नगर); जनपदवधूलोचनैः पीयमानः<BR>Me. 16. {4} the people, subjects (opp.<BR>the sovereign); जनपदहितकर्ता<BR>त्यज्यते पार्थिवेन Pt. 1. 131. {5} mankind.<BR>--पदिन् m. the ruler of a country<BR>or community.<BR>--प्रवादः {1} rumour,<BR>report. {2} scandal, calumny.<BR>--प्रिय<BR>a. {1} philanthropic. {2} liked by<BR>the people, popular.<BR>--(यः) {1} an<BR>epithet of Śiva. {2} coriander-seed.<BR>--मरकः an epidemic disease.<BR>--मर्यादा established custom or usage,<BR>popular custom.<BR>--रंजनं gratifying the<BR>people, courting popular favour.<BR>--रवः {1} rumour. {2} calumny,<BR>scandal.<BR>--लोकः one, (i. e. the fifth),<BR>of the seven divisions of the<BR>universe situated above Maharloka.<BR>--वादः (also जनेवादः) {1} news,<BR>rumour. {2} a scandal.<BR>--व्यवहारः<BR>popular usage.<BR>--श्रुत a. well-known<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-c" target="_blank">Page0505-c+ 58</a>]<BR>among people, famous.<BR>--श्रुतिः f. a<BR>rumour, report.<BR>--संबाध a. densely<BR>crowded with people.<BR>--स्थानं N.<BR>of a part of the Daṇḍakā forest;<BR>R. 12. 42; 13. 22, U. 1. 28, 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनंगमः|जनङ्गम|जनंगम
जनंगमः A Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनक|जनकः
जनक a. (निका f.) [जन्-णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>Generating, producing, causing;<BR>क्लेशजनक, दुःखजनक &c.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>father, progenitor.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>famous king of Videha or Mithilā,<BR>foster-father of Sītā. He was<BR>remarkable for his great knowledge,<BR>good works, and holiness. After<BR>the abandonment of Sītā by Rāma,<BR>he became an anchorite-indifferent<BR>to pleasure or pain-and spent<BR>his time in philosophical<BR>discussions. The sage याज्ञवल्क्य was his<BR>priest and adviser.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मजा, --तनया, --नंदिनी, --सुता epithets of<BR>Sītā, daughter of king Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनता
जनता [जनानां समूहः तल्]<BR>1 Birth.<BR>--2<BR>A number or assemblage of people,<BR>mankind, community; पश्यति स्म<BR>जनता दिनात्यये पार्वणौ शशिदिवाकराविव<BR>R. 11. 82; 15. 67; Pt. 1. 301;<BR>Śi. 5. 14, 12. 29; 16. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनन|जननं|जननः
जनन a. [जन् भावे ल्युट्] Producing,<BR>causing &c.; भुजगानां जननीं जजाप<BR>विद्यां Śi. 20. 41.<BR>--नः The Supreme<BR>Being.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Birth, being born;<BR>यावज्जननं तावन्मरणं Moha M. 13.<BR>--2 Causing, production, creation;<BR>शोभाजननात् Ku. 1. 42.<BR>--3<BR>Appearance, manifestation, rise.<BR>--4 Life,<BR>existence; यदैव पूर्वे जनने शरीरं सा<BR>दक्षरोषात्सुदती ससर्ज Ku. 1. 53;<BR>Ś. 5. 2.<BR>--5 Race, family, lineage.<BR>--6<BR>Preparation for a religious<BR>ceremony (दीक्षा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननिः|जननि
जननिः f. [जन्-अनि]<BR>1 A mother.<BR>--2 Birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जननी
जननी [जन्-णिच् अनि ङीप्]<BR>1 A<BR>mother.<BR>--2 Mercy, tenderness,<BR>compassion.<BR>--3 A bat.<BR>--4 Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनमेजयः|जनमेजय
जनमेजयः N. of a celebrated<BR>king of Hastināpura, son of<BR>Parīkṣit, the grandson of Arjuna.<BR>[His father died, being bitten by a<BR>serpent; and Janamejaya, determined<BR>to avenge the injury, resolved to<BR>exterminate the whole serpent-race. He<BR>accordingly instituted a serpent<BR>sacrifice, and burnt down all serpents<BR>except Takṣaka, who was saved only<BR>by the intercession of the sage Āstīka,<BR>at whose request the sacrifice was<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0506-a" target="_blank">Page0506-a+ 58</a>]<BR>closed. It was to this king that<BR>Vaiśampāyana related the Mahābhārata,<BR>and the king is said to have listened<BR>to it to expiate the sin of killing a<BR>Brāhmaṇa.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0505-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयतिः|जनयति
जनयतिः f. Ved. Production,<BR>generation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयंत|जनयन्त
जनयंत a. Generating, producing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयितृ
जनयितृ a. (त्री f.) Producing,<BR>begetting, creator. --m. A father;<BR>Pt. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयित्री
जनयित्री A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनयिष्णुः|जनयिष्णु
जनयिष्णुः A progenitor, producer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0506-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

