जलाका, जलालुका, जलिका, जलुका,<BR>जलूका, जलोका, जलोकिका A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलोकिका
जलाका, जलालुका, जलिका, जलुका,<BR>जलूका, जलोका, जलोकिका A leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेजं|जलेज
जलेजं, जलेजातं A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेजातं|जलेजात
जलेजं, जलेजातं A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेवाहः|जलेवाह
जलेवाहः A diver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलेशयः|जलेशय
जलेशयः<BR>1 A fish.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जलाष
जलाष a. Ved.<BR>1 Mitigating,<BR>pacifying.<BR>--2 Healing, comforting.<BR>soothing (as a medicine);<BR>Rv. 2. 33. 7.<BR>--षं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 Happiness,<BR>comfort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्प्
जल्प् {c1c} P. (जल्पति, जल्पित)<BR>1 To<BR>speak, talk, speak or converse (with<BR>another); अविरलितकपोलं<BR>जल्पतोरक्रमेण U. 1. 27; एकेन जल्पंत्यनल्पाक्षरं<BR>Pt. 1. 136; Bh. 1. 82.<BR>--2 To<BR>murmur, speak inarticulately.<BR>--3 To<BR>chatter, prattle, babble.<BR>--4 To<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पः|जल्प
जल्पः [जल्प् भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Talk,<BR>speech.<BR>--2 Discourse, conversation.<BR>--3 Babble, prattling, gossip.<BR>--4<BR>Debate, wrangling discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पक
जल्पक a. (ल्पिका f.), जल्पाक a.<BR>Talkative, garrulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पनं|जल्पन
जल्पनं a. [जल्प्-ल्युट्] Speaking,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">Page0510-a+ 54</a>]<BR>saying, talking &c.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Saying,<BR>talking.<BR>--2 Chattering, garrulity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0509-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पिः|जल्पि
जल्पिः f. Ved. Inarticulate speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्पित|जल्पितं
जल्पित a. [जल्प् कर्मणि क्त] Said,<BR>spoken, prattled &c.<BR>--तं Talk,<BR>gossip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जल्हुः|जल्हु
जल्हुः Ved. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जव|जवः
जव a. [जु-भावे अप्] Swift,<BR>expeditious.<BR>--वः<BR>1 (a) Speed, swiftness,<BR>quickness, rapidity; जवो हि सप्तेः<BR>परमं विभूषणं Bh. 3. 121; Ś. 1. 8. (b)<BR>Haste, hurry; जवेन पीठादुदतिष्ठदच्युतः<BR>Śi. 1. 12.<BR>--2 Velocity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिकः a fleet horse, a courser.<BR>--अनिलः a strong wind, hurricane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवन|जवनं|जवनः
जवन a.(नी f.) [जु भावे ल्युट्]<BR>Quick, swift, fleet; R. 9. 56.<BR>--नः A<BR>courser, a swift horse.<BR>--नं Speed,<BR>quickness, velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनिमन्
जवनिमन् m. Speed, velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवस्
जवस् n. Ved. Quickness, speed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जविन्
जविन् a. Quick, fleet. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>horse.<BR>--2 A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जविन
जविन a. Rapid, quick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनिका
जवनिका, जवनी [जु करणे ल्युट्<BR>संज्ञायां कन्]<BR>1 A screen of cloth<BR>surrounding a tent.<BR>--2 A curtain<BR>in general; नरः संसारांते विशति<BR>यमधानीजवनिकां Bh. 3. 112.<BR>--3 The<BR>sail of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवनी
जवनिका, जवनी [जु करणे ल्युट्<BR>संज्ञायां कन्]<BR>1 A screen of cloth<BR>surrounding a tent.<BR>--2 A curtain<BR>in general; नरः संसारांते विशति<BR>यमधानीजवनिकां Bh. 3. 112.<BR>--3 The<BR>sail of a boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवसः|जवस|जवसं
जवसः Pasture-grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जवा
जवा The China rose; see जपा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जष्
जष् {c1c} U. (जषति-ते) To injure,<BR>hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस्
जस् {vI.v} {c4c} P. (जस्यति)<BR>1 To set<BR>free, release.<BR>--2 To be exhausted or<BR>tired.<BR>--3 To go. {vII.v} {c1c} {c10c} P.<BR>(जसति, जासयति)<BR>1 To hurt, injure,<BR>strike.<BR>--2 To disregard, slight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जसुः|जसु
जसुः<BR>1 An weapon(आयुध).<BR>--2<BR>Weakness, exhaustion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जसुरि|जसुरिः
जसुरि a. Ved. Exhausted, tired.<BR>--रिः Indra's thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जस्रं|जस्र
जस्रं Exhaustion, fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहक|जहकः
जहक a. Abandoning, leaving.<BR>--कः<BR>1 Time.<BR>--2 A child.<BR>--3 The<BR>slough of a snake.<BR>--का A kind of<BR>pole-cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहत्
जहत् a. (ती f.) Leaving,<BR>abandoning.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--लक्षणा, --स्वार्था a kind<BR>of लक्षणा (also called लक्षणलक्षणा) in<BR>which a word loses its primary sense,<BR>but is used in one which is in some<BR>way connected with the primary<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">Page0510-b+ 57</a>]<BR>sense; e. g. in the familiar instance<BR>गंगायां घोषः ‘a hamlet on the Ganges,’<BR>गंगा loses its primary sense and<BR>means गंगातट; cf. अजहत्स्वार्था also.<BR>{2} irony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहानकः|जहानक
जहानकः Total destruction of the<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जहुः|जहु
जहुः A young animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्नुः|जह्नु
जह्नुः N. of an ancient king, son<BR>of Suhotra, who adopted the river<BR>Gaṅgā as his daughter. [The river<BR>Ganges, when brought down from heaven<BR>by the austerities of Bhagīratha, was<BR>forced to flow over earth to follow him<BR>to the lower regions. In its course it<BR>inundated the sacrificial ground of king<BR>Jahnu, who being angry drank up its<BR>waters. But the gods and sages, and<BR>particularly Bhagīratha, appeased his<BR>anger, and he consented to discharge<BR>those waters from his ears. The river is<BR>therefore regarded as his daughter, and<BR>is styled जाह्नवी, जह्नुतनया, --कन्या,<BR>--सुता, नंदिनी &c.; cf. R. 8. 95].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जह्मन्
जह्मन् n. Ved. Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जा
जा<BR>1 A mother.<BR>--2 A husband's<BR>brother's wife.<BR>--3 A race, tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागतं|जागत
जागतं The Jagatī metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागुडं|जागुड|जागुडः
जागुडं Saffron.<BR>--डः N. of a<BR>country famous for its saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृ
जागृ {c2c} P. (जागर्ति, जागरित)<BR>1 To<BR>be awake, be watchful or attentive<BR>(fig. also); सोऽपसर्पैर्जजागार यथाकालं<BR>स्वपन्नपि R. 17. 51; गुरौ<BR>षाड्गुण्यचिंतायामार्ये चार्ये च जाग्रति Mu. 7. 13; to<BR>sit up during the night; या निशा<BR>सर्वभूतानां तस्यां जागर्ति संयमी Bg. 2. 69.<BR>--2 To be roused from sleep, awake.<BR>--3 To foresee, be provident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरा
जागरा See जागरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर|जागरः
जागर a. [जागृ भावे घञ्गुणः] A wake,<BR>watchful.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Wakefulness, waking.<BR>keeping awake; रात्रिजागरपरो<BR>दिवाशयः R. 19. 34.<BR>--2 A vision in a waking<BR>state.<BR>--3 An armour, mail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरक
जागरक a. [जागृ-ण्वुल् गुणः] Waking,<BR>awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरणं|जागरण
जागरणं [जागृ भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Waking,<BR>wakefulness.<BR>--2 Watchfulness,<BR>vigilance.<BR>--3 Sitting up at night as a<BR>part of a religious ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरित
जागरित a. One who has been<BR>long awake.<BR>--तं Waking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरितृ
जागरितृ a.(त्री f.), जागरूक a. [<BR>जागृतृच् ऊक् वा]<BR>1 Wakeful, waking,<BR>sleepless; स्वपतो जागरूकस्य याथार्थ्यं वेद<BR>कस्तव R. 10. 24.<BR>--2 Watchful,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">Page0510-c+ 55</a>]<BR>vigilant; वर्णाश्रमावेक्षणजागरूकः<BR>R. 14. 85; Śi. 20. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागरिन्
जागरिन् a. Wakeful, awake, vigilant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागृवि|जागृविः
जागृवि a. Ved.<BR>1 Watchful,<BR>attentive, vigilant.<BR>--2 A wake.<BR>--3 Clear,<BR>bright (as fire).<BR>--4 Active,<BR>animating.<BR>--विः<BR>1 A king.<BR>--2 Agni, or<BR>fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर्तिः|जागर्ति|जागर्त्ति|जागर्त्तिः
जागर्तिः, जागर्या, जाग्रिया<BR>Wakefulness, keeping awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जागर्या|जागर्य्या
जागर्तिः, जागर्या, जाग्रिया<BR>Wakefulness, keeping awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाग्रिया
जागर्तिः, जागर्या, जाग्रिया<BR>Wakefulness, keeping awake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाग्रत्
जाग्रत् a.<BR>1 Watching, being<BR>awake.<BR>--2 Attentive, careful,<BR>watchful.<BR>--3 Clear, bright. --m. Ved.<BR>Dreaming in a waking state,<BR>daydream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाघनी
जाघनी<BR>1 A tail.<BR>--2 The thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांगल|जाङ्गल|जाङ्गलं|जाङ्गलः
जांगल a. (ली f.) [जंगले भवः<BR>जंगलप्रायो वा अण्]<BR>1 Rural, picturesque.<BR>--2 Wild.<BR>--3 Savage, barbarous.<BR>--4<BR>Arid, desert.<BR>--लः The francoline<BR>partridge.<BR>--लं Flesh, flesh of deer<BR>&c.; Māl. 5. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांगलिः|जाङ्गलि|जाङ्गलिः
जांगलिः, जांगलिकः A<BR>snake-charmer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांगलिकः|जाङ्गलिक|जाङ्गलिकः
जांगलिः, जांगलिकः A<BR>snake-charmer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांगुलं|जाङ्गुल|जांगुल|जाङ्गुलं
जांगुलं Poison, venom.<BR>--ली<BR>1<BR>Knowledge of poisons, possession of<BR>charms or drugs as antidotes.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांगुलिः|जाङ्गुलि|जांगुलि|जाङ्गुलिः
जांगुलिः, जांगुलिकः A snake-doctor,<BR>a dealer in antidotes (विषवैद्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांगुलिकः|जाङ्गुलिक|जांगुलिक|जाङ्गुलिकः
जांगुलिः, जांगुलिकः A snake-doctor,<BR>a dealer in antidotes (विषवैद्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांघिक|जाङ्घिक|जाङ्घिकः
जांघिक a. [जंघाभ्यां जीवति वेतना˚<BR>ठञ्] Running.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A courier, an<BR>express.<BR>--2 A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाजिन्
जाजिन् m. A warrior,<BR>combatant; जजौजोजाजिजिज्जाजी Śi. 19. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाठर|जाठरः
जाठर a. (री f.) [जठरे भवः अण्]<BR>Belonging to or being in the<BR>stomach, stomachic, abdominal;<BR>धनक्षये वर्धति जाठराग्निः Pt. 2. 178.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>The digestive faculty, gastric fluid.<BR>--2 ‘Offspring of the womb’, a child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाड्यं|जाड्य
जाड्यं [जडस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Coldness, frigidity.<BR>--2 Apathy,<BR>sluggishness, inactivity.<BR>--3 Dulness of<BR>intellect, folly, stupidity; तज्जाड्यं<BR>वसुधाधिपस्य Bh. 2. 15; जाड्यं धियो हरति 2. 23;<BR>जाड्यं ह्रीमति गण्यते 54.<BR>--4Tastelessness<BR>of the tongue.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः<BR>the citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात|जातं|जातः
जात p. p. [जन् कर्तरि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Brought into existence, engendered,<BR>produced.<BR>--2 Grown, arisen.<BR>--3<BR>Caused, occasioned.<BR>--4 Felt, affected<BR>by, oft. in comp.; ˚दुःख &c.<BR>--5<BR>Apparent, clear.<BR>--6 Become, present.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-a" target="_blank">Page0511-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--7 Happened.<BR>--8 Ready at hand,<BR>collected; see जन्.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A son, male<BR>offspring (in dramas often used as<BR>a term of endearment; अयि जात<BR>कथयितव्यं कथय U. 4 ‘dear boy, ‘oh<BR>my darling &c.’).<BR>--2 A living being.<BR>--ता A daughter, mostly used in<BR>addressing; जाते ‘dear child.’<BR>--तं<BR>1 A<BR>creature, living being.<BR>--2<BR>Production, origin.<BR>--3 Kind, sort, class,<BR>species.<BR>--4 A collection of things<BR>forming a class;<BR>निःशेषविश्राणितक्रोशजातं R. 5. 1 all that goes to form<BR>wealth, i. e. every kind of property;<BR>so कर्मजातं the whole aggregate of<BR>actions; सुख˚ everything included<BR>under the name of सुख or pleasure;<BR>अपत्यजातं ‘the brood of young ones;’<BR>Ś. 5. 22.<BR>--5 A child, a young one.<BR>--6 Individuality, specific condition.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपत्या a mother.<BR>--अमर्ष<BR>a. vexed, enraged.<BR>--अश्रु a.<BR>shedding tears.<BR>--इष्टिः f. a sacrifice<BR>performed at the birth of a child.<BR>--उक्षः a young bullock.<BR>--कर्मन् n.<BR>a ceremony performed at the birth<BR>of a child; R. 3. 18.<BR>--कलाप a.<BR>having a tail (as a peacock).<BR>--काम a.<BR>enamoured.<BR>--पक्ष a. having wings;<BR>अजातपक्ष unfledged.<BR>--पाश a.<BR>fettered.<BR>--पुत्रा a woman who has<BR>borne a son or sons.<BR>--प्रत्यय<BR>a. inspired with confidence.<BR>--प्रेत<BR>a. born and dead; Pt. 1.<BR>--मन्मथ<BR>a. fallen in love.<BR>--मात्र a. just born.<BR>--रूप a. beautiful, brilliant.<BR>--(पं)<BR>{1} gold; अप्याकरसमुत्पन्ना<BR>मणिजातिरसंस्कृता । जातरूपेण कल्याणि न हि<BR>संयोगमर्हति M. 5. 18; N. 1. 129 {2}<BR>the form in which a person is born,<BR>i. e. nakedness. {3} the thorn apple.<BR>˚धर a. naked.<BR>--विद्या Ved.<BR>knowledge of the origin and nature of<BR>all things.<BR>--विभ्रम a. {1}<BR>confounded. {2} precipitate.<BR>--वेदस् m. an<BR>epithet of fire (or of the sun);<BR>Ku. 2. 46; Śi. 2. 51; R. 12. 104, 15. 72;<BR>the word is variously explained; cf.<BR>Nir.:--जातवेदाः कस्मात् जातानि वेद, जातानि<BR>वैनं विदुः, जाते जाते विद्यते इति वा,<BR>जातवित्तो वा जातधनो, जातविद्यो वा जातप्रज्ञानो<BR>यत्तज्जातः पशूनविंदतेति तज्जातवेदसो<BR>जातवेदस्त्वमिति ब्राह्मणम्.<BR>--वेदसी an epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--वासगृहं, --वेश्मन् m. the<BR>lying-in-chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0510-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातक|जातकं|जातकः
जातक a. [जात-स्वार्थे क] Born,<BR>produced.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A newborn infant.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-b" target="_blank">Page0511-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--2 A mendicant.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A<BR>ceremony performed after the birth of<BR>a child (जातकर्मन्).<BR>--2<BR>Astrological calculation of a nativity.<BR>--3<BR>An aggregate of similar things.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ध्वनिः a leech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिः|जाति
जातिः f. [जन्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Birth,<BR>production; Pt. 1. 38; Ms. 2. 148.<BR>--2 The form of existence fixed by<BR>birth.<BR>--3 Race, family, lineage,<BR>rank.<BR>--4 A caste, tribe or class (of<BR>men); अरे मूढ जात्या चेदवध्योऽहं एषा<BR>सा जातिः परित्यक्ता Ve. 3; (the<BR>primary castes of the Hindus are<BR>only four: --ब्राह्मण, क्षत्रिय, वैश्य and<BR>शूद्र).<BR>--5 A class, genus, kind,<BR>species; पशुजातिः, पुष्पजातिः &c.<BR>--6<BR>The properties which are peculiar<BR>to a class and distinguish it<BR>from all others, the essential<BR>characteristics of a species; as<BR>गोत्व, अश्वत्व of cows, horses &c.;<BR>see गुण, क्रिया and द्रव्य; Śi. 2. 47 and<BR>cf. K. P. 2.<BR>--7 A fireplace.<BR>--8<BR>Nutmeg.<BR>--9 The Jasmine plant or<BR>its flower; पुष्पाणां प्रकरः स्मितेन<BR>रचिंतो नो कुंदजात्यादिभिः Amaru. 40<BR>(written also as जाती in the last two<BR>senses).<BR>--10 (In Nyāya) Futile answer.<BR>--11 (In music) The seven primary<BR>notes of the Indian gamut.<BR>--12<BR>Reduction of fractions to a common<BR>denominator.<BR>--13 False<BR>generalization.<BR>--14 A figure of speech (in<BR>rhetoric) which consists in so arranging<BR>words that they may read the same<BR>in Sanskrit as well as in Prākṛta<BR>(संस्कृतप्राकृतयोः समा जातिः); cf.<BR>Vb. 1. 30.<BR>--15 A class of metres; see App.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंध a. born blind;<BR>Bh. 1. 90.<BR>--कोशः, --षः, --षं nutmeg.<BR>--कोशी, --षी the outer skin of the<BR>nutmeg.<BR>--धर्मः {1} the duties of a caste.<BR>{2} a generic property.<BR>--ध्वंसः loss<BR>of caste or its privileges.<BR>--पत्री the<BR>outer skin of the nutmeg.<BR>--फलं a<BR>nutmeg.<BR>--ब्राह्मणः a Brāhmaṇa only<BR>by birth, but not by knowledge or<BR>religious austerities, an ignorant<BR>Brāhmaṇa; (तपः श्रुतं च योनिश्च त्रयं<BR>ब्राह्मण्यकारणं । तपःश्रुताभ्यां यो हीनो<BR>जातिब्राह्मण एव सः ॥ शब्दार्थचिंतामणि).<BR>--भ्रंशः loss of caste; Ms. 11. 67.<BR>--भ्रष्ट a. outcast.<BR>--महः birth-day<BR>festival.<BR>--मात्रं {1} ‘mere birth,’<BR>position in life obtained by mere<BR>birth. {2} caste only (but not the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">Page0511-c+ 56</a>]<BR>performance of duties pertaining to<BR>it); Ms. 8. 20; 12. 114. {3} species,<BR>genus.<BR>--लक्षणं generic distinction,<BR>a characteristic of a class.<BR>--वाचक<BR>a. expressing a genus, generic (as a<BR>word); गौरश्वः पुरुषो हस्ती.<BR>--वैरं<BR>instinctive or natural hostility.<BR>--वैरिन्<BR>m. a born enemy.<BR>--वैलक्षण्यं<BR>inconsistency, incompatibility in kind.<BR>--शब्दः a name conveying the idea<BR>of a genus, a generic word, common<BR>noun; गौः, अश्वः, पुरुषः, हस्ती &c.<BR>--संकरः admixture of caste; mixed<BR>blood.<BR>--संपन्न a. belonging to a<BR>noble family.<BR>--सारं nutmeg.<BR>--स्मर<BR>a. remembering one's condition in<BR>a former life; जांतिस्मरो मुनिरस्मि<BR>जात्या K. 355.<BR>--स्वभावः generic<BR>character or nature.<BR>--हीन a. of low<BR>birth, outcast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातिमत्|जातिमन्त्
जातिमत् a. Nobly born, of high<BR>rank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाती
जाती The jasmine plant(मालती).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीय|जातीयः
जातीय, --क a. Belonging to a tribe,<BR>race, kind &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातीयक
जातीय, --क a. Belonging to a tribe,<BR>race, kind &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जात्य|जात्यः
जात्य a. [जातौ भवः यत्]<BR>1 Of the<BR>same family, related.<BR>--2 Noble,<BR>well-born, sprung from a noble<BR>family; जात्यस्तेनाभिजातेन शूरः<BR>शौर्यवता कुशः R. 17. 4.<BR>--3 Lovely,<BR>beautiful, pleasing.<BR>--4 Best,<BR>excellent.<BR>--5 (Math.) Rectangular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातु
जातु ind. A particle meaning:<BR>1 At all, ever, at any time, possibly;<BR>किं तेन जातु जातेन मातुर्यौवनहारिणा<BR>Pt. 1. 26; न जातु कामः कामानामुपभोगेन<BR>शाम्यति Ms. 2. 94; Ku. 5. 55.<BR>--2<BR>Perhaps, sometimes; R. 19. 7.<BR>--3<BR>Once, once upon a time, sometime,<BR>at some day.<BR>--4 Used with the<BR>potential mood जातु has the sense of<BR>‘not allowing or putting up with’;<BR>जातु तत्रभवान्वृषलं याजयेन्नावकल्पयामि<BR>(न मर्षयामि) Sk.<BR>--5 Used with a<BR>present indicative it denotes censure<BR>(गर्हा); जातु तत्रभवान् वृषलं याजयति<BR>ibid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुधानः|जातुधान
जातुधानः A demon, imp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातुष|जातुषं
जातुष a. (षी f.) [जनुनो विकारः<BR>अण्-षुक् च P. IV. 3. 138]<BR>1 Made<BR>of, or covered with, lac.<BR>--2 Sticky,<BR>adhesive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातूः
जातूः m. A thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जातूकर्णः|जातूकर्ण
जातूकर्णः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानं|जान
जानं Ved. Birth, production,<BR>origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0511-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानकी
जानकी [जनकस्यापत्यं स्त्री, अण्] N.<BR>of Sītā, wife of Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपदः|जानपद
जानपदः [जानेन उत्पत्त्या पद्यते पद्<BR>अप्; जनपदे भवः, अण् वा]<BR>1 An<BR>inhabitant of the country, a rustic, boor,<BR>peasant (opp. पौर).<BR>--2 A country.<BR>--3 A tax &c. from peasants.<BR>--4<BR>subject.<BR>--दा A popular expression.<BR>--दी Profession, business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानपदिक
जानपदिक a. Relating to a country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानान
जानान a. Knowing,<BR>understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानि
जानि A substitute for जाया at<BR>the end of Bah. comp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जानु
जानु n. [जन्-ञुण्] The knee;<BR>जानुभ्यामवनिं गत्वा kneeling (or<BR>falling on one's knees) on the ground.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दघ्न a. reaching to, as high<BR>as, the knees, knee-deep.<BR>--फलकं,<BR>--मंडलं the knee-pan.<BR>--विजानु n. a<BR>peculiar position in fighting<BR>(contracting and extending the knees).<BR>--संधिः the knee-joint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापः|जाप
जापः [जप्-घञ्]<BR>1 Muttering<BR>prayers, whispering, murmuring.<BR>--2 A muttered prayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापक|जापकः
जापक a. Muttering prayers.<BR>--कं<BR>A kind of fragrant wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाप्य
जाप्य a. To be muttered.<BR>--प्यं<BR>A prayer to be muttered in a low<BR>voice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जापनं|जापन
जापनं<BR>1 Declining, rejection.<BR>--2<BR>Dismissing, sending away.<BR>--3<BR>Completing, finishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबालः|जाबाल
जाबालः A goatherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाबालिः|जाबालि
जाबालिः<BR>1 N. of the author of a<BR>law-book.<BR>--2 N. of an infidel<BR>Brāhmaṇa, a priest of king Daśaratha<BR>who tried to dissuade Rāma from<BR>his resolution of going to the forest<BR>and to induce him to accept the<BR>throne offered by Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामदग्न्यः|जामदग्न्य
जामदग्न्यः N. of Paraśurāma q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामा
जामा [जम्-अदने बा˚ अण् स्त्रीत्वं]<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>--2 A<BR>daughter-inlaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृ
जामातृ m. [जायां माति मिनोति<BR>मिमीते वा नि˚; cf. Uṇ. 2. 94]<BR>1 A<BR>sonin-law; जामातृयज्ञेन वयं निरुद्धाः<BR>U. 1. 11; जामाता दशमो ग्रहः Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 A lord, master.<BR>--3 The<BR>sunflower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामातृकः|जामातृक
जामातृकः A son-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामि|जामिः
जामि a. [जम्-इन् नि˚ वृद्धिः]<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">Page0512-b+ 58</a>]<BR>Customary, usual.<BR>--2 Peculiar, or<BR>belonging to.<BR>--मिः f.<BR>1 A sister.<BR>--2 A<BR>daughter.<BR>--3 A daughter-in-law.<BR>--4<BR>A near female relative (<BR>सन्निहितसपिंडस्त्री Kull.); Ms. 3. 57-58.<BR>--5 A<BR>virtuous and respectable woman.<BR>--6<BR>Ved. A finger.<BR>--7 Water. --n.<BR>1<BR>Blood-relationship, relation of sister<BR>and brother.<BR>--2 Relation (in general),<BR>descent.<BR>--3 Tautology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामित्रं|जामित्र
जामित्रं The seventh zodiacal sign<BR>from the natal sign (लग्न); तिथौ<BR>च जामित्रगुणान्वितायां Ku. 7. 1. (<BR>जामित्रं लग्नात्सप्तमं स्थानं Malli.) Note--Some<BR>derive the word from जाया, because<BR>in astrology, the जामित्र sign<BR>indicates the future good-luck of one's<BR>wife (जायामित्रं?); but the word is<BR>obviously connected with the Greek<BR>diametron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जामेयः|जामेय
जामेयः [जाम्या भगिन्या अपत्यं ढञ्]<BR>A sister's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांबवं|जाम्बव|जांबव|जाम्बवं
जांबवं [जंब्वाः फलं अण् तस्य बा˚ न<BR>लुप् Tv.]<BR>1 Gold.<BR>--2 The fruit of<BR>the Jambu tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांबवत्|जाम्बवत्|जाम्बवन्त्
जांबवत् m. N. of a king of bears<BR>who was of signal service to Rāma<BR>at the siege of Laṅkā. He was<BR>also noted for his medical skill.<BR>[This same Jāmbavat appears to have<BR>lived up to the time of Kṛṣṇa, or<BR>perhaps he was another being of that<BR>time; for there was a fight between<BR>Kṛṣṇa and Jāmbavat for the<BR>Syamantaka jewel which the latter had got<BR>from Prasena, brother of Satrājit.<BR>Kṛṣṇa vanquished Jāmbavat, who<BR>placed the jewel, along with his<BR>daughter Jāmbavatī, at his entire<BR>disposal].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांबीरं|जाम्बीर|जांबीर
जांबीरं (--लं) A citron.<BR>--लं<BR>Ved. The knee-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांबीलं|जाम्बील|जांबील
जांबीरं (--लं) A citron.<BR>--लं<BR>Ved. The knee-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जांबूनदं|जाम्बूनद|जांबूनद|जाम्बूनदं
जांबूनदं [जंबूनद्यां भवं अण्]<BR>1<BR>Gold; R. 18. 44.<BR>--2 A golden<BR>ornament; कृतरुचश्च जांबूनदैः<BR>Śi. 4. 66.<BR>--3 The Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायकं|जायक
जायकं A kind of yellow<BR>fragrant wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाया
जाया A wife. (The word is<BR>thus derived: --पतिर्भार्यां संप्रविश्य गर्भो<BR>भूत्वेह जायते । जायायास्तद्धि जायात्वं<BR>यदस्यां जायते पुनः Ms. 9. 8; see also<BR>Malli. on R. 2. 1). As last<BR>member of Bah. comp. जाया is changed<BR>to जानि; सीताजानिः ‘one who has<BR>Sītā for his wife’; so युवजानिः,<BR>वामार्धजानिः.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुजीविन्<BR>m.,<BR>--आजीवः {1} an actor, a dancer.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-c" target="_blank">Page0512-c+ 57</a>]<BR>{2} the husband of a harlot. {3} a<BR>needy man, pauper. {4} a kind of<BR>crane (बक).<BR>--घ्नः {1} a murderer of<BR>his wife. {2} a mole or mark on<BR>the body indicative of the death of<BR>one's wife.<BR>--पती (dual)<BR>husband and wife. (The other forms<BR>of the comp. are दंपती and जंपती q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायिन्
जायिन् a. (नी f.) [जि-णिनि]<BR>Conquering, subduing. --m. The<BR>burden of a song (in music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जायु|जायुः
जायु a. Victorious.<BR>--युः<BR>1<BR>Medicine.<BR>--2 A physician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारः|जार
जारः [जीर्यत्यनेन जॄ करणे घञ्;<BR>जरयतीति जारः Nir.]<BR>1 A paramour, gallant,<BR>lover; रथकारः स्वकां भार्यां सजारां<BR>शिरसावहत् Pt. 4. 54.<BR>--2 A<BR>confidential friend.<BR>--री N. of Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः, --जन्मन्, --जातः a bastard.<BR>--भरा an adulteress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारिणी
जारिणी An adulteress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालं|जाल|जालः
जालं<BR>1 A net, snare.<BR>--2 (a) A<BR>web, cob-web. (<BR>--6) Any woven<BR>texture.<BR>--3 A coat of mail, a helmet<BR>made of wire.<BR>--4 An eye-hole,<BR>lattice, window; जालांतरप्रेषितदृष्टिरन्या<BR>R. 7. 9; धूपैर्जालाविनिः सृतैर्वलभयः<BR>संदिग्धपारावताः V. 3. 2; Ku. 7. 60.<BR>--5 A collection, an assemblage,<BR>number, mass;<BR>चिंतासंततितंतुजालनिबिडस्यूतेव Māl. 5. 10; Ku. 7. 89;<BR>Śi. 4. 56; Amaru. 58.<BR>--6 Magic.<BR>--7 Illusion, deception.<BR>--8 An<BR>unblown flower.<BR>--9 The membrane<BR>which unites the toes of many<BR>water-birds.<BR>--10 A disease of the<BR>eyes.<BR>--11 Pride, arrogance.<BR>--लः<BR>The Kadamba tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः<BR>a loop-hole, window.<BR>--कर्मन् n. the<BR>occupation of catching fish, fishing.<BR>--कारकः {1} a net-maker. {2} a<BR>spider.<BR>--गर्दभः a kind of pimple<BR>or boil.<BR>--गोणिका a kind of churning<BR>vessel.<BR>--ग्रथित a. connected by a<BR>web; Ś. 7. 16.<BR>--पाद्, --पादः a goose.<BR>--प्राया mail, armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकं|जालक|जालकः
जालकं [जालमिव कायति कै-क]<BR>1 A<BR>net.<BR>--2 A multitude, collection;<BR>बद्धं कर्णशिरीषरोधि वदने घर्मांभसां<BR>जालकं Ś. 1. 30; R. 9. 68.<BR>--3 A lattice,<BR>window.<BR>--4 A bud, an unblown flower;<BR>अभिनवैजलिकैर्मालतीनां Me. 98; so<BR>यूथिकाजालकानि 26.<BR>--5 A kind of<BR>ornament (worn in the hair);<BR>तिलकजालकजालकमौक्तिकैः R. 9. 44 (<BR>आभरणविशेषः).<BR>--6 A nest.<BR>--7 Illusion,<BR>deception.<BR>--8 A plantain or the fruit.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">Page0513-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--9 Pride.<BR>--कः A window, lattice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मालिन् a. veiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0512-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकिन्
जालकिन् m. A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालकिनी
जालकिनी A ewe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालवत्|जालवन्त्
जालवत् a.<BR>1 Furnished with a<BR>net, reticulated.<BR>--2 Covered with<BR>iron network.<BR>--3 Cunning,<BR>deceptive (मायाविन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिकः|जालिक
जालिकः [जालेन चरति पर्पा˚ ष्ठन्]<BR>1<BR>A fisherman.<BR>--2 A fowler,<BR>birdcatcher.<BR>--3 A spider.<BR>--4 The governor<BR>or chief ruler of a province.<BR>--5 A rogue,<BR>cheat.<BR>--6 A conjurer, juggler.<BR>--का<BR>1 A net.<BR>--2 A chain-armour.<BR>--3 A<BR>spider.<BR>--4 A leech.<BR>--5 A widow.<BR>--6<BR>Iron.<BR>--7 Plantain.<BR>--8 A veil, woollen<BR>cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालिनी
जालिनी<BR>1 A room ornamented<BR>with pictures.<BR>--2 A kind of melon<BR>(कोषातकी).<BR>--3 Certain boils or<BR>pustules which appear in the disease<BR>called प्रमेह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालंधरः|जालन्धर|जालंधर|जालन्धरः
जालंधरः N. of a country in the<BR>north-west of India, the territory<BR>between the rivers Beas and Sutlej.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालाषं|जालाष
जालाषं Ved. A kind of drug<BR>with healing properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्म|जाल्मः
जाल्म a. (ल्मी f.)<BR>1 Cruel,<BR>severe, harsh.<BR>--2 Rash,<BR>inconsiderate.<BR>--ल्मः (ल्मी f.)<BR>1 A<BR>rogue, rascal, villain, wretch,<BR>miscreant; अपि ज्ञायते कतमेन दिग्भागेन ग<BR>तः स जाल्म इति V. 1.<BR>--2 A poor<BR>man, a low or degraded man.<BR>--3<BR>One who reads or recites badly; cf.<BR>P. VI. 2. 158.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाल्मक
जाल्मक a. (ल्मिका f.) Despised,<BR>low, mean, contemptible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जावन्यं|जावन्य
जावन्यं<BR>1 Speed, swiftness.<BR>--2<BR>Haste, hurry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जास्पतिः|जास्पति
जास्पतिः Ved. A son-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाहं|जाह
जाहं A termination added to nouns<BR>expressive of the parts of the body<BR>in the sense of ‘the root of’; कर्णजाहं<BR>the root of the ear; so अक्षि, ˚ओष्ठ˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाहकः|जाहक
जाहकः<BR>1 A pole-cat.<BR>--2 A leech.<BR>--3 A bed, a cot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जाह्नवी
जाह्नवी [जह्रोः अपत्यं स्त्री अण् ङीप्]<BR>An epithet of the river Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जि|जिः
जि {c1c} P. (Atm. when preceded,<BR>by परा and वि) (जयति, जिगाय जिग्ये<BR>अजैषीत्-अजेष्ट, जेतुं, जित)<BR>1 To conquer,<BR>defeat, overcome, vanquish,<BR>subjugate; जयति तुलामधिरूढो भास्वानपि<BR>जलदपटलानि Pt. 1. 330;<BR>Bk. 15. 76, 19. 2.<BR>--2 To surpass, excel;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-b" target="_blank">Page0513-b+ 57</a>]<BR>गर्जितानंतरां वृष्टिं सौभाग्येन जिगाय सा<BR>Ku. 2. 53; R. 3. 34; Ghaṭ. 22;<BR>Śi. 1. 19.<BR>--3 To win (by conquest, in<BR>gambling or in a law-suit), acquire<BR>by conquest; प्रागजीयत घृणा ततो<BR>मही R. 11. 65; (where जि means<BR>‘to conquer’ also);<BR>Ms. 7. 96.<BR>--4 To curb, restrain,<BR>control, conquer (as passions).<BR>--5 To be victorious, be supreme or<BR>pre-eminent (generally used in<BR>benedictory stanzas or salutations);<BR>जयतु जयतु महाराजः (in dramas).<BR>स जयति परिणद्धः शक्तिभिः शक्तिनाथः<BR>Māl. 5. 1; जितमुडुपतिना नमः सुरेभ्यः<BR>Ratn. 1. 5; Bh. 2. 24; Gīt. 1. 1.<BR>--6 To convict.<BR>--7 To overcome or<BR>get the better of (as a disease &c.).<BR>--8 To expect from (with abl.).<BR>--Caus. (जापयति) To cause to win<BR>or conquer. --Desid. (जिगीषति)<BR>To wish to win, acquire or excel,<BR>to vie with, emulate, to seek for;<BR>चलति नयान्न जिगीषतां हि चेतः<BR>Ki. 10. 29. --WITH अधि to<BR>conquer, defeat, vanquish; Bk. 19. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयः|जय
जयः [जि भावे अच्]<BR>1 Conquest,<BR>triumph, victory, success, winning<BR>(in battle, game or a law-suit).<BR>--2<BR>Restraint, curbing, conquest as in<BR>इंद्रियजय.<BR>--3 N. of the sun.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of Jayanta, son of Indra.<BR>--5 N. of<BR>Yudhiṣṭhira, the first Pāṇḍava<BR>prince.<BR>--6 N. of an attendant of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--7 An epithet of Arjuna.<BR>--या<BR>1 N. of Durgā.<BR>--2 N. of an<BR>attendant of the goddess Durgā.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of banner.<BR>--4 The third, eighth<BR>or thirteenth lunar days of any of<BR>the two lunar fortnights.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवह a. conferring victory.<BR>--आशिस् f. {1} a prayer for victory. {2}<BR>congratulations after victory; a<BR>cheer of victory.<BR>--उद्धुर a. exulting<BR>in victory.<BR>--कोलाहलः {1} a shout<BR>of victory. {2} a kind of<BR>game with dice.<BR>--घोषः, --घोषणं,<BR>--णा a proclamation of victory.<BR>--ढक्का a kind of drum beaten as a<BR>sign of victory.<BR>--दत्तः N. of Jayanta,<BR>Indra's son.<BR>--पत्रं a record of<BR>victory.<BR>--पालः {1} a king. {2}<BR>an epithet of Brahmā. {3} an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--पुत्रकः a kind<BR>of dice.<BR>--मंगलः {1} a royal elephant. {2}<BR>a remedy for fever.<BR>--(लं) a cheer of<BR>victory.<BR>--यज्ञः the अश्वमेध sacrifice.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">Page0513-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--लक्ष्मीः, --श्रीः the goddess of<BR>victory; Ku. 2. 52.<BR>--लेखं record of<BR>victory.<BR>--वाहिनी an epithet of Śacī.<BR>--शब्दः {1} a shout of victory. {2} the<BR>exclamation ‘jaya’ (hail! glory!)<BR>uttered by bards &c.<BR>--शृंगं a horn blown<BR>to announce a victory.<BR>--स्तंभः a<BR>trophy, a column erected to<BR>commemorate a victory, a triumphal<BR>column; निचखान<BR>जयस्तंभान्गंगास्रोतोंऽतरेषुसः R. 4. 36.<BR>--स्वामिन् m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयक
जयक a. Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयत्सेनः|जयत्सेन
जयत्सेनः A name assumed by<BR>Nakula while living at Virāṭa King.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयद्वलः
जयद्वलः A name assumed by<BR>Sahadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयनं|जयन
जयनं [जि करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Conquering,<BR>subduing.<BR>--2 Armour for cavalry,<BR>elephants &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--युज् {1}<BR>caparisoned. {2} victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयिन्
जयिन् a. [जि शीलार्थे इनि]<BR>1<BR>Conquering, vanquishing; विरूपाक्षस्य<BR>जयिनीस्ताः स्तुवे वामलोचनाः Vb. 1. 2.<BR>--2 Successful, winning a law-suit;<BR>Y. 2. 79.<BR>--3 Fascinating,<BR>captivating, subduing the heart; जगति<BR>जयिनस्ते ते भावा नवेंदुकलादयः Māl. 1. 36.<BR>--m. A victor, a conqueror;<BR>पौरस्त्यानेवमाक्रामंस्तांस्ताञ्जनपदाञ्जयी R. 4. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जय्य|जय्यः
जय्य a. [जि-यत्] Conquerable,<BR>vulnerable, that can be conquered<BR>(opp. जेय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषा
जिगीषा [जि-सन् भावे अ]<BR>1 Desire<BR>of conquering, subduing or<BR>overcoming; यानं सस्मार कौबेरं वैवस्वत<BR>जिगीषया R. 15. 45.<BR>--2 Emulation,<BR>rivalry.<BR>--3 Eminence.<BR>--4 Exertion,<BR>profession, habit of life.<BR>--5<BR>Eminence.<BR>--6 Military ardour, warlike<BR>spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगीषु
जिगीषु a.<BR>1 Desirous of<BR>conquering.<BR>--2 Vying or contending with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित|जितः
जित p. p. [जि-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Conquered, subdued, curbed, restrained,<BR>(as enemies, passions &c.)<BR>--2<BR>Won, got, obtained (by conquest).<BR>--3 Surpassed, excelled.<BR>--4 Subject<BR>to, enslaved or influenced by;<BR>कामजित; स्त्रीजित &c.<BR>--तं Victory.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षर a. reading well or<BR>readily.<BR>--अमित्र a. one who has<BR>conquered his foes, triumphant,<BR>victorious. {2} one who has subdued<BR>his passions.<BR>--(त्रः) N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--अरि a. one who has conquered<BR>his enemies or passions.<BR>--(रिः) an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">Page0514-a+ 56</a>]<BR>epithet of Buddha.<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>selfsubdued, void of passion.<BR>--आहव<BR>a. victorious.<BR>--इंद्रिय a. one who<BR>has conquered his passions or<BR>subdued the senses (रूप, रस, गंध, स्पर्श<BR>& शब्द); श्रुत्वा स्पष्ट्वाथ दृष्ट्वा च भुक्वा<BR>घ्रात्वा च यो नरः । न हृष्यति ग्लायति<BR>वा स विज्ञेयो जितेंद्रियः Ms. 2. 98.<BR>--काशिः the fist doubled.<BR>--काशिन्<BR>a. appearing victorious, proud of<BR>victory, assuming the airs of a<BR>victor; चाणक्योऽपि जितकाशितया<BR>Mu. 2; जितकाशी राजसेवकः ibid.<BR>--कोप,<BR>--क्रोध, --मन्यु a. imperturbable, not<BR>excitable<BR>--(धः) an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--नेमिः a staff made of the<BR>Aśvattha tree.<BR>--लोक a. ‘one who has won<BR>heaven’ (epithet of a class of manes).<BR>--शत्रु a. victorious.<BR>--श्रम a. inured<BR>to fatigue, hardy.<BR>--स्वर्ग a. one who<BR>has won heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0513-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्
जित् a. [जि-क्विप्] (At the end of<BR>comp.) Conquering, defeating,<BR>winning &c.; तारकजित्, कंसजित्,<BR>सहस्रजित् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितिः|जिति
जितिः f.<BR>1 Victory, conquest.<BR>--2<BR>Gaining, obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्य|जित्यः
जित्य a. Conquerable.<BR>--त्या<BR>1<BR>Victory.<BR>--2 Acquisition, gain.<BR>--3<BR>A ploughshare.<BR>--त्यः A harrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वन्
जित्वन् a. Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्वर|जित्वरः
जित्वर a. [जि-क्वरप्] (री f.)<BR>Victorious, conquering, triumphant;<BR>शस्त्राण्युपायंसत जित्वराणि Bk. 1. 16;<BR>करदीकृतभूपालो भातृभिर्जित्वरैर्दिशां<BR>Śi. 2. 9.<BR>--री N. of the city Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष्णु|जिष्णुः
जिष्णु a. [जि-ग्त्स्नु]<BR>1 Victorious,<BR>triumphant; R. 4. 85; 10. 18.<BR>--2<BR>Winning, gaining.<BR>--3 (At the end<BR>of comp.) Canquering, excelling;<BR>अलिनीजिष्णुः कचानां चयः Bh. 1. 5;<BR>Śi. 13. 21.<BR>--ष्णुः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of Indra.<BR>--3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेतृ
जेतृ a. [जि-तृच्]<BR>1 Victorious,<BR>triumphant.<BR>--2 Surpassing,<BR>excelling. --m.<BR>1 A conqueror, victor.<BR>--2 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिः|जि
जिः A demon(पिशाच).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिगत्नुः|जिगत्नु
जिगत्नुः Breath, life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सा
जिघत्सा [अद् सन् घसादेशः भावे अ]<BR>1 Desire of eating, hunger.<BR>--2<BR>Striving for.<BR>--3 Contending with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्सु|जिघत्सुः
जिघत्सु a. [अद् सन् घसादेशे उ]<BR>Hungry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघत्नुः|जिघत्नु
जिघत्नुः Ved. An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसक|जिघांसकः
जिघांसक a. Revengeful,<BR>murderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसा
जिघांसा<BR>1 Desire of killing;<BR>R. 15. 19.<BR>--2 Malice, revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघांसु|जिघांसुः
जिघांसु a. [हन् सन् उ] Desirous<BR>of killing, murderous.<BR>--सुः An<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघृक्षा
जिघृक्षा [ग्रह् सन् भावे अ] Desire<BR>of taking or seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिघ्र|जिघ्रः
जिघ्र a. [घ्रा कर्तरि श जिघ्रादेशः]<BR>1<BR>Suspecting.<BR>--2 Conjecturing,<BR>guessing; observing; e. g. मनोजिघ्रः<BR>सपत्नीजनः S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासा
जिज्ञासा [ज्ञा सन् भावे अ]<BR>1<BR>Desire of knowing, curiosity,<BR>inquisitiveness.<BR>--2 Search,<BR>investigation, test, examination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासित|जिज्ञासितः
जिज्ञासित a. Investigated, asked,<BR>inquired to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिज्ञासु|जिज्ञासुः
जिज्ञासु a. [ज्ञा सन् उ]<BR>1 Desirous<BR>of knowing, inquisitive, curious;<BR>Bg. 6. 44.<BR>--2 Desirous of getting<BR>absolution (मुमुक्षु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्तमः|जित्तम
जित्तमः, जितुमः, जित्मः Gemini,<BR>the third sign of the zodiac (a word<BR>of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जितुमः|जितुम
जित्तमः, जितुमः, जित्मः Gemini,<BR>the third sign of the zodiac (a word<BR>of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जित्मः|जित्म
जित्तमः, जितुमः, जित्मः Gemini,<BR>the third sign of the zodiac (a word<BR>of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन|जिनः
जिन a. [जि-नक्]<BR>1 Victorious,<BR>triumphant.<BR>--2 Very old.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A<BR>generic term applied to a chief<BR>Bauddha or Jaina saint.<BR>--2 N.<BR>applied to the Arhats of the Jainas.<BR>--3 A very old man.<BR>--4 An epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इंद्रः, --ईश्वरः {1}<BR>a chief Bauddha saint. {2} an Arhat<BR>of the Jainas.<BR>--सद्मन् n. a Jaina<BR>temple or monastery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिव्रि|जिव्रिः
जिव्रि a. Ved. Old, decayed.<BR>--व्रिः<BR>1 Time.<BR>--2 A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिम्
जिम् {c1c} P. (जेमति) To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिरि
जिरि {c5c} P. (जिरिणोति) To kill,<BR>hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिन्व्
जिन्व् {c1c} P. (जिन्वति)<BR>1 To be active<BR>or lively, busy oneself.<BR>--2 To urge<BR>on, impel, excite.<BR>--3 To refresh,<BR>animate.<BR>--4 To promote.<BR>--5 To<BR>grant, confer.<BR>--6 To please, satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिष्
जिष् {c1c} P. (जेषति) To sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिवाजिवः|जिवाजिव
जिवाजिवः The Cakora bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहान
जिहान a.<BR>1 Going, going to.<BR>--2<BR>Getting, obtaining; See हा ‘to go’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिहानकः|जिहानक
जिहानकः Destruction of the<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्म|जिह्मं|जिह्मः
जिह्म a. [जहाति सरलमार्गं; हा-मन्<BR>सन्वत् आलोपश्च Uṇ. 1. 138]<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-c" target="_blank">Page0514-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Sloping, athwart, oblique.<BR>--2 Crooked,<BR>awry, squint; Rs. 1. 12.<BR>--3<BR>Tortuous, curved, going irregularly.<BR>--4 Curved, bent.<BR>--5 Morally<BR>crooked, deceitful, dishonest, wicked,<BR>unfair; धृतहेतिरप्यधृतजिह्ममतिः<BR>Ki. 6. 24; सुहृदर्थमीहितमजिह्मधियां Śi. 9. 62.<BR>--6 Dim, dark, pale-coloured:<BR>विधिसमयनियोगाद्दीप्तिसंहारजिह्मं Ki. 1. 46.<BR>--7 Slow, lazy.<BR>--ह्मं<BR>1 Dishonesty,<BR>falsehood.<BR>--2 The Tagara tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a. crooked-eyed,<BR>squinting.<BR>--ग a. moving slowly.<BR>--(गः) a snake.<BR>--गति a.<BR>meandering, going tortuously; Rs. 1. 13.<BR>--मेहनः a frog.<BR>--योधिन् a.<BR>fighting unfairly. (--m.) an epithet of<BR>Bhīma.<BR>--शल्यः the Khadira tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्मायति
जिह्मायति Den. P. To go crookedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वः|जिह्व|जिह्वं
जिह्वः The tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वल|जिह्वलः
जिह्वल a. Voracious, greedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जिह्वा
जिह्वा<BR>1 The tongue.<BR>--2 The<BR>tongue of fire, i. e. a flame.<BR>--3 A<BR>sentence.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्वादः<BR>licking, lapping.<BR>--उल्लेखनी, --उल्लेखनिका,<BR>--निर्लेखनं a tongue-scraper.<BR>--पः {1}<BR>a dog. {2} a cat. {3} a tiger. {4} a<BR>leopard. {5} a bear.<BR>--मलं the fur<BR>of the tongue.<BR>--मूलं the root of<BR>the tongue.<BR>--मूलीय a. a term<BR>particularly applied to the Visarga<BR>before क् and ख् and also to ऋ, ऌ<BR>and the guttural class of consonants<BR>(in gram.).<BR>--रदः a bird.<BR>--लिह्<BR>m. a dog.<BR>--लौल्यं greediness.<BR>--शल्यः the Khadira tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीतिः|जीति
जीतिः f. [जि-क्तिन् वेदे दीर्घः]<BR>1<BR>Victory.<BR>--2 Decrease, loss.<BR>--3<BR>Fading away, growing old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीन|जीनः
जीन a. [ज्या-क्त संप्रसा˚ दीर्घः]<BR>Old, aged, decayed.<BR>--नः A leather<BR>bag; जीनकार्मुकबस्तावीन् पृथग्<BR>दद्याद्विशुद्धये Ms. 11. 139.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीमूतः|जीमूत
जीमूतः [जया ति नभः, जीयते अनिलेन<BR>जीवनस्योदकस्य मूतं बंधो यत्र, जीवनं जलं<BR>मूतं बद्धं अनेन, जावनं मुंचतीति वा पृषो˚ Tv.<BR>cf. Uṇ. 3. 91]<BR>1 A cloud;<BR>जीमूतेन स्वकुशलमयीं हारयिष्यन् प्रवृत्तिं<BR>Me. 4.<BR>--2 A mountain.<BR>--3 A nourisher,<BR>sustainer.<BR>--4 An epithet of Indra.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कूटः a mountain.<BR>--केतुः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--वाहनः {1} N.<BR>of Indra. {2} N. of a king of the<BR>Vidyādharas, hero of the play<BR>called Nāgānanda; (mentioned<BR>also in कथासरित्सागर). [He was the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">Page0515-a+ 58</a>]<BR>son of Jīmūtaketu and renowned for<BR>his benevolent and charitable<BR>disposition. When his father's kingdom was<BR>invaded by his kinsmen, he scorned<BR>the idea of fighting with them and<BR>induced his father to leave it to those<BR>who sought for it and to repair with<BR>him to the Malaya mountain to lead<BR>a holy life. It is related that there<BR>he one day took the place of a young<BR>serpent who was, by virtue of an<BR>agreement, to be offered to Garuḍa as his<BR>daily meal, and induced, by his<BR>generous and touching behaviour, the<BR>enemy of serpents to give up his<BR>practice of devouring them. The story is<BR>very pathetically told in the play].<BR>--वाहिन् smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0514-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर|जीरः
जीर a. [ज्या रक् संप्रसा˚ दीर्घः]<BR>Ved. Swift, quick.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A sword.<BR>--2 Cumin-seed.<BR>--3 An atom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरकः|जीरक
जीरकः, जीरणः Cumin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरणः|जीरण
जीरकः, जीरणः Cumin-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीरिः|जीरि
जीरिः [जीर्यति जॄ-बा˚ रिक्] Ved.<BR>A man. --f. Quick or flowing water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्ण|जीर्णं|जीर्णः
जीर्ण p. p. [जॄ-क्त]<BR>1 Old, ancient.<BR>--2<BR>Worn out, ruined, wasted, decayed,<BR>tattered (as clothes); वासांसि<BR>जीर्णानि यथा विहाय Bg. 2. 22; U. 6. 38;<BR>Māl. 5. 30.<BR>--3 Digested; सुजीर्णमन्नं<BR>सुविचक्षणः सुतः H. 1. 22.<BR>--र्णः<BR>1<BR>An old man.<BR>--2 A tree.<BR>--3<BR>Cuminseed.<BR>--णा Large cumin-seed.<BR>--र्णं<BR>1 Benzoin.<BR>--2 Old age, decrepitude.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्धारः ‘renewing the old’,<BR>repairs, especially of a temple or any<BR>charitable or religious institution.<BR>--उद्यानं ruined or neglected garden.<BR>--ज्वरः lingering fever.<BR>--पर्णः the<BR>Kadamba tree.<BR>--वज्रं a particular gem.<BR>--वस्त्र a. wearing old clothes.<BR>--वाटिका a ruined house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णक
जीर्णक a. Almost dried up or<BR>withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्णिः|जीर्णि
जीर्णिः f.<BR>1 Old age, decrepitude,<BR>decay, infirmity.<BR>--2 Digestion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीर्विः|जीर्वि
जीर्विः [जॄ-क्विन्]<BR>1 An axe.<BR>--2<BR>The body.<BR>--3 A cart.<BR>--4 An animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव्
जीव् {c1c} P. (जीवति, जीवित)<BR>1 To live,<BR>be alive; यस्मिञ्जीवति जीवंति बहवः<BR>सोऽत्र जीवति Pt. 1. 23; मा जीवन् यः<BR>परावज्ञादुःखदग्धोपि जीवति Śi. 2. 45;<BR>Ms. 2. 235.<BR>--2 To revive, come to<BR>life.<BR>--3 To live by, subsist on, make<BR>a livelihood by (with instr.);<BR>सत्यानृतं तु वाणिज्यं तेन चैवापि जीव्यते<BR>Ms. 4. 6; विपणेन च जीवंतः 3. 152,<BR>162; 11. 26; sometimes used with<BR>a cognate accusative in this sense;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-b" target="_blank">Page0515-b+ 57</a>]<BR>अजिह्मामशठां शुद्धां जीवेद्ब्राह्मणजीविकां<BR>Ms. 4. 11.<BR>--4 (Fig.) To live or<BR>prey upon, depend upon as one's<BR>source of existence (with loc.); चौराः<BR>प्रमत्ते जीवंति व्याधितेषु चिकित्सकाः ।<BR>प्रमदाः कामयानेषु यजमानेषु याचकाः ॥<BR>राजा विवदमानेषु नित्यं मूर्खेषु पंडिताः<BR>Mb. --Caus.<BR>1 To restore to life.<BR>--2 To nourish, nurture, bring up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव|जीवः
जीव a. [जीव्-कर्तरि क] Living,<BR>existing.<BR>--वः<BR>1 The principle of life,<BR>the vital breath, life, soul; गतजीव,<BR>जीवत्याग, जीवाशा, &c.<BR>--2 The<BR>individual or personal soul enshrined<BR>in the human body and imparting<BR>to it life, motion and sensation<BR>(called जीवात्मन् as opposed to परमात्मन्<BR>the Supreme soul); Y. 3. 131;<BR>Ms. 12. 22-23.<BR>--3 Life, existence.<BR>--4 A<BR>creature, living being.<BR>--5<BR>Livelihood, profession.<BR>--6 N. of Karṇa.<BR>--7 N. of one of the Maruts.<BR>--8 The<BR>constellation पुष्य.<BR>--9 N. of<BR>Bṛhaspati.<BR>--10 The third lustrum in the<BR>cycle of Jupiter.<BR>--11 Association of<BR>cause and effect.<BR>--12 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतकः {1} a bird-catcher,<BR>fowler. {2} a murderer, slayer.<BR>--अजीबाधारः the world of organic and<BR>inorganic creation.<BR>--आत्मन् m. the<BR>individual soul enshrined in the<BR>human body (as opposed to परमात्मन्<BR>‘the Supreme soul’).<BR>--आदानं<BR>abstracting healthy blood,<BR>bleeding, (in medic.).<BR>--आधानं<BR>preservation of life.<BR>--आधारः the heart.<BR>--इंधनं glowing fire-wood, burning<BR>wood.<BR>--उत्सर्गः ‘casting off life,’<BR>voluntary death, suicide.<BR>--उपाधिः<BR>the three states, i. e. waking,<BR>dreaming and sleeping.<BR>--ऊर्णा the wool<BR>of a living animal.<BR>--गृहं, --मंदिरं ‘the<BR>abode of the soul,’ the body.<BR>--ग्राहः<BR>a prisoner taken alive.<BR>--घनः<BR>Brahmā.<BR>--ज a. born alive.<BR>--जीवः<BR>(also जीवंजीवः) the Cakora bird.<BR>--तोका a woman whose children are<BR>living.<BR>--दः {1} a physician. {2} an<BR>enemy.<BR>--दशा mortal existence.<BR>--धनं<BR>‘living wealth’, property in the<BR>shape of living creatures, live-stock.<BR>--धानी the earth.<BR>--निकायः a being<BR>endowed with life.<BR>--पतिः f.,<BR>--पत्नी<BR>a woman whose husband is alive.<BR>--पत्रं a fresh leaf.<BR>--पितृ, --पितृक a.<BR>(a son or daughter) whose father<BR>is still alive.<BR>--पुत्रा, --वत्सा a woman<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-c" target="_blank">Page0515-c+ 56</a>]<BR>whose son is living.<BR>--मातृका the<BR>seven mothers or female divinities;<BR>(कुमारी धनदा नंदा विमला मंगला बला ।<BR>पद्मा चेति च विख्याताः सप्तैता जीवमातृकाः).<BR>--योनिः a sentient being.<BR>--रक्तं<BR>menstrual blood.<BR>--लोकः {1} the<BR>world of living beings, the world of<BR>mortals, the world or worldly<BR>existence; त्वत्प्रयाणे शातांलोकः सर्वतो<BR>जीवलोकः Māl. 9. 37; जीवलोकतिलकः<BR>प्रलीयते 21; so स्वप्नेंद्रजालसदृशः खलु<BR>जीवलोकः Śānti. 2. 2; Bg. 11. 7;<BR>U. 4. 17. {2} living beings, mankind;<BR>दिवस इवाभ्रश्यामस्तपात्यये जीवलोकस्य<BR>Ś. 3. 12; or आलोकमर्कादिव जीवलोकः<BR>R. 5. 35.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. breeding or<BR>keeping cattle.<BR>--शेष a. one to<BR>whom only life is left, escaping only<BR>with life and nothing more.<BR>--शोणितं living, i. e., healthy blood.<BR>--संक्रमणं transmigration of the soul.<BR>--साधनं grain, corn.<BR>--साफल्यं<BR>relization or attainment of the chief<BR>end of human existence.<BR>--सूः ‘the<BR>mother of living beings’, a woman<BR>whose children are living.<BR>--स्थानं<BR>{1} a joint, an articulation. {2} the<BR>vital parts, heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवक|जीवकः
जीवक a. [जीव् --णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>1<BR>Living, making a livelihood by,<BR>generating &c.<BR>--2 One who lives a long<BR>time.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A living being.<BR>--2 A<BR>servant.<BR>--3 A Buddhist mendicant,<BR>any mendicant who lives by<BR>begging.<BR>--4 A usurer.<BR>--5 A<BR>snakecatcher.<BR>--6 A tree.<BR>--7 A medicinal<BR>plant of that name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवत्|जीवन्त्
जीवत् a. (न्ती f.) Living, alive.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तोका a woman whose<BR>children are living.<BR>--पतिः f.,<BR>--पत्नी f.<BR>a woman whose husband is living.<BR>--पितृकः one whose father is alive.<BR>--मुक्त a. ‘liberated while living’,<BR>a man who, being purified by a true<BR>knowledge of the Supreme spirit, is<BR>freed from the future birth and<BR>all ceremonial rites while yet<BR>living.<BR>--मुक्तिः f. final liberation<BR>in the present state of life.<BR>--मृत<BR>a. ‘dead while alive,’ one who, though<BR>alive, is as good as dead and useless<BR>to the world (said of a mad man or<BR>one whose character is lost).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवथ|जीवथः
जीवथ a. [जीव्-अथ]<BR>1 Long-lived.<BR>--2 Virtuous, pious.<BR>--थः<BR>1 Life,<BR>existence.<BR>--2 A tortoise.<BR>--3 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">Page0516-a+ 57</a>]<BR>peacock.<BR>--4 A cloud.<BR>--5 Virtue,<BR>piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0515-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवन|जीवनं|जीवनः
जीवन a. (नी f.) [जीव् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>Enlivening, giving life.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A<BR>living being.<BR>--2 Wind.<BR>--3 A son.<BR>--4 The Supreme Being.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Life,<BR>existence; (fig. also); त्वमासे मम<BR>भूषणं त्वमसि मम जीवनं Gīt. 10.<BR>--2 The<BR>principle of life, vital energy;<BR>Bg. 7. 9.<BR>--3 Water; बीजानां प्रभव<BR>नमोऽस्तु जीवनाय Ki. 18. 39; or जीवनं<BR>जीवनं (life) हंति प्राणान् हंति समीरणः<BR>Udb.<BR>--4 Livelihood, profession,<BR>means of existence (fig. also);<BR>Ms. 11. 77; विदुषां जीवनं मूर्खः<BR>H. 3. 33.<BR>--5 Butter made from milk<BR>one day old.<BR>--6 Marrow.<BR>--7<BR>Enlivening, making alive.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः death.<BR>--आघातं poison.<BR>--आवासः {1} ‘residing in water’,<BR>epithet of Varuṇa, the regent of water.<BR>{2} the body.<BR>--उपायः livelihood.<BR>--ओषधं {1} elixir of life. {2} a<BR>lifegiving medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनक|जीवनकं
जीवनक a. [जीवन-कन्]<BR>Enlivening.<BR>--कं Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवनीय|जीवनीयं
जीवनीय a. [जीव् --बा˚ करणे अनीयर्]<BR>1 To be lived.<BR>--2 Supporting life.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 Fresh milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवंत|जीवन्त|जीवन्तः
जीवंत a,<BR>1 Living, existing.<BR>--2<BR>Long-lived.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Life, existence.<BR>--2 A drug, medicament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवंतिकः|जीवन्तिक|जीवंतिक|जीवन्तिकः
जीवंतिकः A fowler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवल
जीवल a.<BR>1 Full of life.<BR>--2<BR>Animating, inspiriting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवा
जीवा [जीव्-अच्]<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2<BR>The earth.<BR>--3 A bow-string;<BR>मुहुर्जीवाघोषैर्बधिरयति Mv. 6. 30.<BR>--4 The<BR>chord of an arc.<BR>--5 Means of<BR>living.<BR>--6 The tinkling of metallic<BR>ornaments.<BR>--7 N. of a plant (वचा).<BR>--8 Life, existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवातु|जीवातुः
जीवातु m., n.<BR>1 Food.<BR>--2 Life,<BR>existence (fig. aloo); स खलु<BR>प्राज्ञजीवातुः सर्वशास्त्रविशारदः J. N. V.<BR>--3<BR>Restoration to life, revival; रे हस्त<BR>दक्षिण मृतस्य शिशोर्द्विजस्य जीवातवे विसृज<BR>शूद्रमुनौ कृपाणं U. 2. 10.<BR>--4 A<BR>medicine for restoring life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविका
जीविका [जीव् अकन् अत इत्वं]<BR>1<BR>Means of living, livelihood.<BR>--2 The<BR>life-giving element, i. e. water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवित|जीवितं
जीवित p. p. [जीव्-कर्तरि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Living, existent, alive;<BR>R. 12. 75.<BR>--2 Returned to life, revived.<BR>--3<BR>Animated, enlivened.<BR>--4 Lived<BR>through (as a period).<BR>--तं<BR>1 Life,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">Page0516-b+ 55</a>]<BR>existence; त्वं जीवितं त्वमसि मे हृदय<BR>द्वितीयं U. 3. 26; कन्येयं कुलजीवितं<BR>Ku. 6. 63; Me. 83; नाभिनंदेत मरणं<BR>नभिनंदेत जीवितं Ms. 6. 45;<BR>7. 111.<BR>--2 Duration of life.<BR>--3<BR>Livelihood.<BR>--4 A living being.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतकः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--आशा hope of life, love of life.<BR>--ईशः {1} a lover, husband. {2} an<BR>epithet of Yama; जीवितेशवसतिं<BR>जगाम सा R. 11. 20 (where the word<BR>is used in sense 1 also). {3} the sun.<BR>{4} the moon. {5} a drug which is said<BR>to revive the dead.<BR>--ईश्वरः Śiva.<BR>--कालः duration of life.<BR>--ज्ञा an<BR>artery.<BR>--नाथः a husband.<BR>--व्ययः<BR>sacrifice of life.<BR>--संशयः risk of life,<BR>jeopardy, danger to life; स आतुरो<BR>जीवितसंशये वर्तते ‘he is dangerously<BR>ill’; Bv. 2. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीवितव्य
जीवितव्य a. To be lived, kept alive<BR>&c.<BR>--व्यं<BR>1 The possibility of living.<BR>--2 Life.<BR>--3 Possible return to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीविन्
जीविन् a. (नी f.)<BR>[जीव्-णिनि, जीव-इनि वा] (Generally at the end of comp.)<BR>1 Living, alive, existing; R. 1. 63.<BR>--2 Living upon or by; शस्त्रजीविन्ऽ<BR>आयुधजीविन् &c. --m. A living being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीव्यं|जीव्य
जीव्यं Life.<BR>--व्या A means of<BR>livelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुकुटः|जुकुट
जुकुटः<BR>1 A dog.<BR>--2 The Malaya<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सनं|जुगुप्सन
जुगुप्सनं, जुगुप्सा<BR>1 Censure,<BR>reproach.<BR>--2 Dislike, aversion,<BR>disgust, abhorrence.<BR>--3 (In Rhet.)<BR>Disgust considered as the feeling<BR>which gives rise to the Bībhatsa<BR>sentiment, thus defined:<BR>--दोषेक्षणादिभिर्गर्हा जुगुप्सा विषयोद्भवा S. D. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुगुप्सा
जुगुप्सनं, जुगुप्सा<BR>1 Censure,<BR>reproach.<BR>--2 Dislike, aversion,<BR>disgust, abhorrence.<BR>--3 (In Rhet.)<BR>Disgust considered as the feeling<BR>which gives rise to the Bībhatsa<BR>sentiment, thus defined:<BR>--दोषेक्षणादिभिर्गर्हा जुगुप्सा विषयोद्भवा S. D. 207.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुंग्|जुङ्ग्
जुंग् {c1c} P. (जुंगति)<BR>1 To abandon,<BR>quit.<BR>--2 To exclude, set aside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुंगित|जुङ्गित|जुङ्गितः
जुंगित a. Deserted, abandoned.<BR>--तः<BR>A man of a degraded caste, a<BR>Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुटकं|जुटक
जुटकं A braid of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुटिका
जुटिका A tuft of hair on the top<BR>of the head; cf. चूडा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुड्
जुड् {vI.v} {c6c} P. (जुडति)<BR>1 To bind.<BR>--2<BR>To go. {vII.v} {c10c} P.<BR>1 To send, throw or<BR>cast, direct.<BR>--2 To grind or pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुत्
जुत् {c1c} A. (जोतते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुन्
जुन् {c6c} P. (जुनति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुंबकः|जुम्बक|जुम्बकः
जुंबकः Ved. An epithet of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्
जुर् {c6c} {c4c} P. (जुरति, जूर्यति) Ved.<BR> To decay, become or grow old,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">Page0516-c+ 56</a>]<BR>waste away, perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुर्
जुर् m. An old man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्ण
जूर्ण a. Decayed, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुल्
जुल् {c10c} P. (जोलयति) To reduce<BR>to powder, grind, pound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुवस्
जुवस् a. Ved. Speed, quickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्
जुष् {vI.v} {c6c} A. (जुषते-जुष्ट)<BR>1 To be<BR>pleased or satisfied.<BR>--2 To be<BR>favourable or propitious.<BR>--3 To like, be<BR>found of, take pleasure or delight<BR>in, enjoy; सत्त्वं जुषाणस्य भवाय देहिनां<BR>Bhāg.<BR>--4 To devote or attach<BR>oneself to, practise, undergo, suffer;<BR>पौलस्त्योऽजुषत शुचं विपन्नवंधुः<BR>Bk. 17. 112.<BR>--5 To frequent, visit,<BR>inhabit; जुप्रंते पर्वतश्रेष्ठमृषयः<BR>पर्वसंधिषु Mb.<BR>--6 To enter, seat oneself,<BR>resort to; रथं च जुजुषे शुभं<BR>Bk. 14. 95.<BR>--7 To choose.<BR>--8 To enjoy,<BR>possess, have; Māl. 5. 18.<BR>--9 To<BR>happen to.<BR>--10 To delight in granting<BR>or performing.<BR>--11 To show<BR>oneself favourable towards. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To like, be fond of.<BR>--2 To fondle,<BR>cherish.<BR>--3 To delight in, approve<BR>of, rejoice at. {vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (<BR>जोषति, जोषयति-ते)<BR>1 To reason, think.<BR>--2<BR>To investigate, examine.<BR>--3 To hurt.<BR>--4 To be satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्
जुष् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>1<BR>Liking, enjoying, taking delight in;<BR>Bh. 3. 103.<BR>--2 Visiting,<BR>approaching, going to, taking, amusing,<BR>resorting to &c.; परलोकजुषां R. 8. 85;<BR>रजोजुषे जन्मनि K. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्य|जुष्यः
जुष्य a. To be served,<BR>worshipped &c.<BR>--ष्यं Service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुष्ट|जुष्टं
जुष्ट p. p. [जुष्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Pleased, gratified.<BR>--2 Practised, resorted<BR>to, visited, suffered &c.; Bg. 2. 2.<BR>--3 Furnished or endowed with,<BR>possessed of.<BR>--4 Liked loved,<BR>agreeable.<BR>--5 Served, worshipped.<BR>--6<BR>Propitious, favourable.<BR>--7 Shared,<BR>partaken in; U. 6. 40.<BR>--ष्टं The<BR>remnants of meal (उच्छिष्ट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषः|जोष|जोषं
जोषः<BR>1 [जुष्-भावे घञ्] Satisfaction,<BR>enjoyment, happiness, pleasure.<BR>--2 Silence.<BR>--षः Happiness.<BR>--षं<BR>ind.<BR>1 According to one's wish, with<BR>ease.<BR>--2 Silently; किमिति जोषमास्यते<BR>Ś. 5; Bv. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषणं|जोषण
जोषणं, --णा<BR>1 Liking.<BR>--2<BR>Satisfaction, approval.<BR>--3 Choosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषणा
जोषणं, --णा<BR>1 Liking.<BR>--2<BR>Satisfaction, approval.<BR>--3 Choosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुराण|जुहुराणः
जुहुराण a. Making crooked or<BR>acting crookedly.<BR>--णः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0516-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहुवानः|जुहुवान
जुहुवानः [हु कर्मणि कानच्]<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 A tree.<BR>--3 A hard-hearted man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूः
जुहूः f. [हु क्विप् नि˚ द्वित्वं दीर्घश्च Tv.]<BR>1 A crescent-shaped wooden ladle<BR>used for pouring the sacrificial<BR>ghee into the fire.<BR>--2 A tongue;<BR>especially of Agni, i. e. a flame.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्यः fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूराणः|जुहूराण
जुहूरा(वा)णः<BR>1 A sacrificial priest.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूवाणः|जुहूवाण
जुहूरा(वा)णः<BR>1 A sacrificial priest.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहूवत्|जुहूवन्त्
जुहूवत् m. Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जुहोतिः|जुहोति
जुहोतिः A technical name for<BR>those sacrificial ceremonies to<BR>which the verb जुहोति is applied<BR>as distinguished from those to which<BR>यजति is applied; क्षरंति सर्वा वैदिक्यो<BR>जुहोतियजतिक्रियाः Ms. 2. 84. (See<BR>Medhātithi and other commentators;<BR>सर्वज्ञनारायण shortly renders जुहोति by<BR>उपविष्टहोम and यजति by तिष्ठद्धोम. See<BR>Āśval. 1. 2. 5. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जू
जू {c1c} U., {c9c} P. (जवति-ते, जुनाति)<BR>1<BR>To press or hurry on, move on<BR>quickly.<BR>--2 To impel quickly, urge<BR>or drive on.<BR>--3 To excite, animate,<BR>inspire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जू
जू a. Ved. Quick, speedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूः
जूः f.<BR>1 Speed.<BR>--2 Atmosphere.<BR>--3 A female demon.<BR>--4 An epithet<BR>of Sarasvatī.<BR>--5 Going speedily,<BR>quick motion.<BR>--6 A mark on the<BR>forehead of horses and oxen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूत
जूत a. [जू-क्त] (At the end of<BR>comp.)<BR>1 Impelled, urged, pressed.<BR>--2<BR>Ved. Gone.<BR>--3 Drawn.<BR>--4 Given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूतिः|जूति
जूतिः f.<BR>1 Going on, proceeding,<BR>moving.<BR>--2 Quickness, speed.<BR>--3<BR>Uninterrupted flow or motion.<BR>--4<BR>Impulse, incitement, instigation.<BR>--5<BR>Inclination, propensity, tendency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूकः|जूक
जूकः The sign Libra of the zodiac<BR>(a word of Greek origin).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूटः|जूट
जूटः The mass of twisted or<BR>matted hair; भूतेशस्य<BR>भुजंगवल्लिवलयस्रङ्नद्धजूटाजटाः Māl. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूटकं|जूटक
जूटकं Matted hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्
जूर् {c4c} A. (जूर्यते, जूर्ण)<BR>1 To hurt,<BR>injure, kill.<BR>--2 To be angry with<BR>(with dat.); भर्त्रे नखेभ्यश्च चिरं जुजूरे<BR>Bk. 11. 8.<BR>--3 To grow old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्णि|जूर्णिः
जूर्णि a. Ved.<BR>1 Swift, speedy,<BR>quick.<BR>--2 Running, proceeding<BR>quickly.<BR>--3 Praising, invoking.<BR>--र्णिः f.<BR>1 Speed.<BR>--2 An epithet of Āditya or<BR>sun.<BR>--3 The body.<BR>--4 The Brahman<BR>(n.).<BR>--5 Anger.<BR>--6 A fiery weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्तिः|जूर्ति|जूर्त्ति|जूर्त्तिः
जूर्तिः f. [ज्वर् भावे क्तिन् ऊठ्]<BR>1<BR>Fever.<BR>--2 Feverish or morbid heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूर्व्
जूर्व् {c1c} P. (जूर्वति) Ved.<BR>1 To burn.<BR>--2 To hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूष्
जूष् {c1c} U. (जूषति-ते) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूषः|जूष|जूषं
जूषः, --षं The water of boiled pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जूषं|जूष|जूषः
जूषः, --षं The water of boiled pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृ
जृ {c1c} P. (जरति)<BR>1 To make low or<BR>humiliate.<BR>--2 To excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृभ्
जृभ्, जृंभ् {c1c} A. (जृभते, जृंभते, जृंभित<BR>जृब्ध)<BR>1 To gape, yawn; Ms. 4. 43.<BR>--2 To open, expand, burst open<BR>(as a flower &c.); वरयुवतिमुखाभं<BR>पंकजं जंभतेऽद्य Rs. 3. 22.<BR>--3 To<BR>increase, spread or extend<BR>everywhere; जृंभतां जृंभतामप्रतिहतप्रसरं<BR>क्रोधज्योतिः Ve. 1; तृष्णे जृभंसि (Paras.<BR>is irregular) Bh. 3. 5; भोगः कोपि<BR>स एक एव परमो नित्योदितो जृंभते 3. 80.<BR>--4 To appear, rise, show oneself,<BR>become visible or manifest;<BR>संकल्पयोनेरभिमानभूतमात्मानमाधाय मधूर्जजृंभे<BR>Ku. 3. 24; U. 5. 13.<BR>--5 To be at<BR>ease.<BR>--6 To recoil or fly back (as<BR>a bow). --Caus. To cause to yawn<BR>or expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृंभ्|जृम्भ्
जृभ्, जृंभ् {c1c} A. (जृभते, जृंभते, जृंभित<BR>जृब्ध)<BR>1 To gape, yawn; Ms. 4. 43.<BR>--2 To open, expand, burst open<BR>(as a flower &c.); वरयुवतिमुखाभं<BR>पंकजं जंभतेऽद्य Rs. 3. 22.<BR>--3 To<BR>increase, spread or extend<BR>everywhere; जृंभतां जृंभतामप्रतिहतप्रसरं<BR>क्रोधज्योतिः Ve. 1; तृष्णे जृभंसि (Paras.<BR>is irregular) Bh. 3. 5; भोगः कोपि<BR>स एक एव परमो नित्योदितो जृंभते 3. 80.<BR>--4 To appear, rise, show oneself,<BR>become visible or manifest;<BR>संकल्पयोनेरभिमानभूतमात्मानमाधाय मधूर्जजृंभे<BR>Ku. 3. 24; U. 5. 13.<BR>--5 To be at<BR>ease.<BR>--6 To recoil or fly back (as<BR>a bow). --Caus. To cause to yawn<BR>or expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृंभः|जृम्भ|जृंभ|जृंभं|जृम्भः
जृंभः, --भा --भं [जृंभ्-घञ्]<BR>1 Yawning,<BR>gaping; U. 4. 29.<BR>--2 Opening,<BR>blossoming, expanding;<BR>कलिकाश्रयी जृंभा प्रभवति K. 257;<BR>जृंभारंभप्रविततदलोपांतजालप्रविष्टैः Ve. 2. 7;<BR>Māl. 9. 16.<BR>--3 Expansion.<BR>--4 Bursting<BR>open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृंभा
जृंभः, --भा --भं [जृंभ्-घञ्]<BR>1 Yawning,<BR>gaping; U. 4. 29.<BR>--2 Opening,<BR>blossoming, expanding;<BR>कलिकाश्रयी जृंभा प्रभवति K. 257;<BR>जृंभारंभप्रविततदलोपांतजालप्रविष्टैः Ve. 2. 7;<BR>Māl. 9. 16.<BR>--3 Expansion.<BR>--4 Bursting<BR>open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृंभं|जृम्भ|जृंभ|जृंभः|जृम्भः
जृंभः, --भा --भं [जृंभ्-घञ्]<BR>1 Yawning,<BR>gaping; U. 4. 29.<BR>--2 Opening,<BR>blossoming, expanding;<BR>कलिकाश्रयी जृंभा प्रभवति K. 257;<BR>जृंभारंभप्रविततदलोपांतजालप्रविष्टैः Ve. 2. 7;<BR>Māl. 9. 16.<BR>--3 Expansion.<BR>--4 Bursting<BR>open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृंभकः|जृम्भक|जृम्भकः
जृंभकः [जृंभ्-ण्वुल्] ‘A yawner’,<BR>a sort of demon.<BR>--कं Swelling.<BR>--भिका Gaping, yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृंभण|जृम्भण|जृम्भणं
जृंभण a. [जृंभ्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Causing to<BR>gape or yawn.<BR>--णं {1} Gaping,<BR>yawning<BR>--2 Stretching (the limbs);<BR>(अंगानि) मुहुर्मुहुर्जृंभणतत्पराणि<BR>Rs. 6. 10.<BR>--3 Blossoming, blooming; मालती<BR>शिरसि जृंभणोन्मुखी Bh. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जृंभित|जृम्भित|जृम्भितं
जृंभित p. p. [जृंभ्-क्त]<BR>1 Yawned,<BR>gaped.<BR>--2 Opened, expanded, displayed;<BR>Māl. 1. 32.<BR>--3 Opened, blown (as a<BR>flower).<BR>--4 Done, exerted.<BR>--5<BR>Enlarged, increased.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Gaping.<BR>--2<BR>Expansion, opening, blooming.<BR>--3<BR>Developing, coming into view.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जॄ
जॄ {vI.v} {c1c} {c4c} {c9c} P., {c10c} U. (जरति, जीर्यति,<BR>जृणाति, जारयति-ते, जजार, जारयामास, अजरत्<BR>अजारीत्, अजीजरत्, -जरि-री-तुं, जीर्ण or<BR>जारित)<BR>1 To grow old, wear out, wither<BR>away, decay; जीर्यंते जीर्यतः केशा दंता<BR>जीर्यंति जीर्यतः । जीर्यतश्चक्षुषी श्रोत्रे<BR>तृष्णैका तरुणायते Pt. 5. 16; Bk. 9. 41.<BR>--2 To perish, be consumed (fig.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">Page0517-c+ 55</a>]<BR>also); अजारीदिव च प्रज्ञा बलं<BR>शोकात्तथाऽजरत् Bk. 6. 30; जेरुराशा<BR>दशास्यस्य 14. 112.<BR>--3 To be dissolved or<BR>digested; जीर्णमन्नं प्रशंसीयात्<BR>Chāṇ. 79; उदरे चाजरन्नन्ये Bk. 15. 150.<BR>--4<BR>To break up or fall to pieces. --Caus.<BR>(ज-जा-र यति)<BR>1 To make old, wear<BR>out, consume.<BR>--2 To cause to be<BR>digested; to digest. {vII.v} {c1c} A. (जरते)<BR>Ved.<BR>1 To move, approach, come<BR>near.<BR>--2 To crackle (as fire).<BR>--3<BR>To roar.<BR>--4 To call out to, invoke,<BR>praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारक
जारक a. [जॄ-णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>1 Causing<BR>to decay.<BR>--2 Promoting digestion,<BR>digestive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारणं|जारण
जारणं [जॄ-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>1 Causing to<BR>decay.<BR>--2 Stimulating digestion.<BR>--3 Calcining or oxidizing metals.<BR>--4 A condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जारद्गव
जारद्गव a. (वीथिः) The portion of<BR>the moon's path occupied by the<BR>constellations श्रवण, धनिष्ठा and<BR>शततारका (according to वराहमिहिर);<BR>according to others, by विशाखा, अनुराधा and<BR>ज्येष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेंताकः|जेन्ताक|जेंताक|जेन्ताकः
जेंताकः A heated chamber for<BR>inducing perspiration, a dry hot<BR>bath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेन्य
जेन्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Of noble origin,<BR>well-born.<BR>--2 Genuine, true.<BR>--3<BR>Victorious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेमनं|जेमन
जेमनं [जिम्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Eating.<BR>--2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेष्
जेष् {c1c} A. (जेषते) To move, go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जेह्
जेह् {c1c} A. (जेहते) Ved.<BR>1 To reach,<BR>go towards.<BR>--2 To strive after,<BR>exert.<BR>--3 To open the mouth, pant,<BR>gasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जै
जै {c1c} P. (जायति) To wane,<BR>decline, decay, perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैत्र|जैत्रं|जैत्रः
जैत्र a. (त्री f.) [जेतृ-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Victorious, successful, leading to<BR>victory; इदमिह मदनस्य जैत्रमस्त्रं<BR>विफलगुणातिशयं भविष्यतीति Māl. 2. 6<BR>धनुर्जैत्रं रघुर्दधौ R. 4. 16, 16. 72.<BR>--2<BR>Superior.<BR>--त्रः<BR>1 A victor,<BR>conqueror.<BR>--2 Quick-silver.<BR>--त्रं A Victory,<BR>triumph.<BR>--3 Superiority.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रथः a victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैनः|जैन
जैनः<BR>1 A Jaina, a follower of<BR>Jaina doctrines.<BR>--2 A Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैमिनिः|जैमिनि
जैमिनिः N. of a celebrated sage<BR>and philosopher, founder of the<BR>Mīmāṃsā school of philosophy<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">Page0518-a+ 54</a>]<BR>(properly पूर्वमीमांसा);<BR>मीमांसाकृतमुन्ममाथ सहसा हस्ती मुनिं जैमिनिं Pt. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0517-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैव
जैव a. [जीवस्येदं अण्]<BR>1<BR>Belonging to जीव or the soul.<BR>--2<BR>Belonging to Jupiter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवातृक|जैवातृकः
जैवातृक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Longlived, one for whom long life is<BR>desired; जैवातृक ननु श्रूयते पतिरस्याः<BR>Dk.<BR>--2 Thin, lean.<BR>--कः<BR>1 The<BR>moon; राजानं जनयांबभूव सहसा<BR>जैवातृक त्वां तु यः Bv. 2. 78.<BR>--2<BR>Camphor.<BR>--3 A son<BR>--4 A drug,<BR>medicament<BR>--5 A peasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैवेयः|जैवेय
जैवेयः An epithet of Kaca, son<BR>of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्म्यं|जैह्म्य
जैह्म्यं Crookedness, deceit,<BR>falsehood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जैह्व्यं|जैह्व्य
जैह्व्यं The pleasure of taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोंगं|जोङ्ग
जोंगं, --गकं Aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोंगकं|जोङ्गक|जोङ्गकं
जोंगं, --गकं Aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोंगटः|जोङ्गट|जोंगट|जोङ्गटः
जोंगटः The longings of a<BR>pregnant woman (दोहद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोटिंगः|जोटिङ्ग|जोटिंग|जोटिङ्गः
जोटिंगः<BR>1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--2 A devotee who practises the<BR>most rigid austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोडः|जोड
जोडः Binding, tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषा
जोषा, जोषित् f. A woman; cf.<BR>योषा, योषित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषित्
जोषा, जोषित् f. A woman; cf.<BR>योषा, योषित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जोषिका
जोषिका<BR>1 A cluster of young buds.<BR>--2 A woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञा
ज्ञा {c9c} U. (जानाति, जानीते, जज्ञौ, जज्ञे,<BR>अज्ञासीत्-अज्ञास्त, ज्ञातुं, ज्ञात)<BR>1 To<BR>know (in all senses), to learn,<BR>become acquainted with; मा<BR>ज्ञासीस्त्वं सुखी रामो यदकार्षीत्स रक्षसां<BR>Bk. 15. 9.<BR>--2 To know, be aware<BR>of, be familiar or conversant with;<BR>जाने तपसो वीर्यं Ś. 3. 1; जानन्नपि हि<BR>मेधावी जडवल्लोक आचरेत् Ms. 2. 110,<BR>123; 7. 148.<BR>--3 To find out,<BR>ascertain, investigate; ज्ञायतां कः कः<BR>कार्यार्थीति Mk. 9.<BR>--4 To comprehend,<BR>apprehend, understand, feel,<BR>experience; as in दुःखज्ञ, सुखज्ञ &c.<BR>--5<BR>To test, try, know the true<BR>character of; आपत्सु मित्रं जानीयात्<BR>H. 1. 72; Chāṇ. 21.<BR>--6 To recognise; म<BR>त्वं दृष्ट्वा न पुनरलकां ज्ञास्यसे कामचारिन्<BR>Me. 63.<BR>--7 To regard, consider,<BR>know to be; जानामि त्वां प्रकृतिपुरुषं<BR>कामरूपं मघोनः Me. 6.<BR>--8 To act,<BR>engage in (with gen. of the<BR>instrument); सर्पिषो जानीते Sk. ‘he<BR>engages in sacrifice with clarified butter<BR>(सर्पि षः = सर्पिषा).<BR>--9 Ved. To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">Page0518-b+ 57</a>]<BR>acknowledge, approve, allow.<BR>--10 To<BR>recognise as one's own, take<BR>possession of. --Caus. (ज्ञापयति, ज्ञपयति)<BR>1 To announce, inform, make<BR>acquainted with, make known,<BR>notify.<BR>--2 To request, ask (Atm.).<BR>--3 To sharpen.<BR>--4 To satisfy.<BR>--5 To<BR>praise.<BR>--6 To immolate, kill (as an<BR>animal). --Desid. (जिज्ञासते)<BR>1 To<BR>desire to know, investigate, ascertain;<BR>R. 2. 26; Bk. 8. 33; 14. 91.<BR>--2 To<BR>conjecture, suppose, guess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञ|ज्ञः
ज्ञ a. [ज्ञा-क] (At the end of<BR>comp.)<BR>1 Knowing, familiar with;<BR>कार्यज्ञ, निमित्तज्ञ, शास्त्रज्ञ, सर्वज्ञ &c.<BR>--2 Wise; as in ज्ञंमन्य thinking<BR>oneself to be wise.<BR>--ज्ञः<BR>1 A wise<BR>and learned man.<BR>--2 The sentient<BR>soul.<BR>--3 The planet Mercury.<BR>--4<BR>The planet Mars.<BR>--5 An epithet of<BR>Brahmā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञपित|ज्ञपितः
ज्ञपित, ज्ञप्त a. Made known,<BR>informed, expounded, taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्त|ज्ञप्तः
ज्ञपित, ज्ञप्त a. Made known,<BR>informed, expounded, taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञप्तिः|ज्ञप्ति
ज्ञप्तिः f.<BR>1 Understanding.<BR>--2<BR>Intellect.<BR>--3 Promulgating.<BR>--4<BR>Satisfaction.<BR>--5 Sharpening.<BR>--6 Praise.<BR>--7 Immolating, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञात|ज्ञातं
ज्ञात a. [ज्ञा-कर्मणि-क्त] Known,<BR>ascertained, understood, learnt,<BR>comprehended &c.; आज्ञापय ज्ञातविशेष<BR>पुंसां Ku. 3. 3; see ज्ञा above.<BR>--तं<BR>Knowledge.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सिद्धांतः a<BR>man completely versed in any<BR>Śāstra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातव्य|ज्ञातव्यं
ज्ञातव्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be known or<BR>understood.<BR>--2 Conceivable,<BR>comprehensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातिः|ज्ञाति
ज्ञातिः [ज्ञा-क्तिच्]<BR>1 A paternal<BR>relation, a father, brother &c.; agnate<BR>relatives collectively.<BR>--2 A kinsman<BR>or kindred in general.<BR>--3 A distant<BR>kinsman who is not entitled to the<BR>oblations offered to deceased<BR>ancestors.<BR>--4 A father.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n.,<BR>--कार्यं the duty of a kinsman.<BR>--भावः kin, relationship.<BR>--भेदः<BR>dissension among relatives.<BR>--विद् a.<BR>one who has or makes near relatives.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातेयं|ज्ञातेय
ज्ञातेयं Relationship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञातृ
ज्ञातृ a. [ज्ञा-तृच्] Knowing,<BR>intelligent, wise. --m.<BR>1 A wise man.<BR>--2<BR>An acquaintance.<BR>--3 A bail, surety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानं|ज्ञान
ज्ञानं [ज्ञा-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Knowing,<BR>understanding, becoming acquainted<BR>with, proficiency; सांख्यस्य योगस्य च<BR>ज्ञानं Māl. 1. 7.<BR>--2 Knowledge,<BR>learning; बुद्धिर्ज्ञानेन शुध्यति Ms. 5. 109;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-c" target="_blank">Page0518-c+ 57</a>]<BR>ज्ञाने मौनं क्षमा शत्रौ R. 1. 22.<BR>--3<BR>Consciousness, cognizance, knowledge;<BR>ज्ञानतोऽज्ञानतो वापि Ms. 8. 288.<BR>knowingly or unknowingly,<BR>consciously or unconsciously.<BR>--4 Sacred<BR>knowledge; especially, knowledge<BR>derived from meditation on the<BR>higher truths of religion and<BR>philosophy which teaches man how to<BR>understand his own nature and how<BR>he may be reunited to the Supreme<BR>spirit (opp. कर्मन्); cf. ज्ञानयोग and<BR>कर्मयोग in Bg. 3. 3.<BR>--5 The organ<BR>of intelligence, sense, intellect.<BR>--6<BR>Conscience.<BR>--7 The Supreme spirit.<BR>--8 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--9 The<BR>Vedās taken collectively.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंनुत्पादः ignorance, folly.<BR>--अपोहः<BR>forgetfulness.<BR>--अभ्यासः {1} study. {2}<BR>thinking, reflection.<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>allwise.<BR>--इंद्रियं an organ of perception;<BR>(these are five त्वच, रसना, चक्षुस्, कर्ण<BR>and घ्राण the skin, tongue, eye, ear<BR>and nose; see बुद्धिंद्रिय under इंद्रिय).<BR>--कांडं that inner or esoteric portion<BR>of Veda which refers to true<BR>spiritual knowledge, or knowledge of the<BR>Supreme spirit, as distinguished<BR>from the knowledge of ceremonial<BR>rites (opp. कर्भकांड).<BR>--कृत a. done<BR>knowingly or intentionally.<BR>--गम्य<BR>a. attainable by the understanding.<BR>--चक्षुस् n. the eye of intelligence,<BR>the mind's eye, intellectual vision<BR>(opp. चर्मचक्षुस्); सर्वं तु समवेक्ष्येदं निखिलं<BR>ज्ञानचक्षुषा Ms. 2. 8; 4. 24. (--m.) a<BR>wise and learned man.<BR>--तत्त्वं true<BR>knowledge, knowledge of god.<BR>--तपस् n. penance consisting in the<BR>acquisition of true knowledge.<BR>--दः a<BR>preceptor.<BR>--दा an epithet of<BR>Sarasvatī.<BR>--दुर्बल a. wanting in knowledge.<BR>--निश्चयः certainty, ascertainment.<BR>--निष्ठ a. intent on acquiring true<BR>(spiritual) knowledge.<BR>--पतिः {1}<BR>the Supreme spirit. {2} a teacher,<BR>preceptor.<BR>--मुद्र a. ‘having the<BR>impress of wisdom’, wise.<BR>--मूल a.<BR>foundeb on spiritual knowledge.<BR>--यज्ञः a<BR>man possessed of true or spiritual<BR>knowledge, philosopher.<BR>--योगः<BR>contemplation as the principal means of,<BR>attaining the Supreme spirit or<BR>acquiring true or spiritual knowledge.<BR>--लक्षणं, --णा {1} indication, sign, a means<BR>of knowing or inferring. {2} (in<BR>logic) sign or proof of knowledge;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">Page0519-a+ 57</a>]<BR>subsequent derived from antecedent<BR>knowledge.<BR>--विज्ञानं {1} sacred and<BR>miscellaneous knowledge. {2} the Vedas<BR>with the supplementary branches of<BR>knowledge, such as medicine, arms,<BR>&c.<BR>--शास्त्रं the science of<BR>fortune-telling.<BR>--साधनं {1} a means of<BR>acquiring true or spiritual knowledge. {2}<BR>an organ of perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0518-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानतः
ज्ञानतः ind. Consciously,<BR>knowingly, intentionally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानमय|ज्ञानमयः
ज्ञानमय a.<BR>1 Consisting of<BR>knowledge, spiritual; इतरो दहने स्वकर्मणां<BR>ववृते ज्ञानमयेन वह्निना R. 8. 20.<BR>--2<BR>Containing knowledge.<BR>--यः<BR>1 The<BR>Supreme spirit.<BR>--2 An epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानिन्
ज्ञानिन् a. (नी f.) [ज्ञानमस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>Intelligent, wise. --m.<BR>1 An<BR>astrologer, a fortune-teller.<BR>--2 A sage, one<BR>possessed of true or spiritual<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानित्वं|ज्ञानित्व
ज्ञानित्वं Fortune-telling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञानीयति
ज्ञानीयति Den. P. To wish for<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापक|ज्ञापकः
ज्ञापक a. [ज्ञा --णिच् --ल्यु] Making<BR>known, teaching, informing,<BR>indicating &c.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A teacher.<BR>--2 A<BR>commander, a master.<BR>--3 A master<BR>of requests, an officer of the court<BR>of an Indian prince; Pt. 3.<BR>--कं<BR>(In phil.) A significant<BR>expression, a suggestive rule or precept,<BR>said of such rules as imply<BR>something more than what is actually<BR>expressed by the words of those<BR>rules themselves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापनं|ज्ञापन
ज्ञापनं [ज्ञा णिच् --ल्युट्] Making<BR>known, informing, teaching,<BR>announcing, indicating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञापित
ज्ञापित a. Made known, informed,<BR>announced, declared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञीप्सा
ज्ञीप्सा [ज्ञा --सन् --भावे अ] The desire<BR>of knowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्ञेय|ज्ञेयं
ज्ञेय pot. p. [ज्ञा कर्मणि यत्]<BR>1 To<BR>be investigated, or learnt or<BR>understood.<BR>--2 To be regarded as.<BR>--3<BR>Perceptible, cognizable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या I. {c9c} P. (जिनाति)<BR>1 To<BR>overpower, oppress.<BR>--2 To grow old.<BR>--3<BR>A. (जीयते) To be oppressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जीत
जीत a.<BR>1 Oppressed, overpowered.<BR>--2 Become old; also जीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यानं|ज्यान
ज्यानं Ved. Oppression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येय
ज्येय a.<BR>1 To be oppressed.<BR>--2<BR>First, best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्या
ज्या<BR>1 A bow-string; विश्रामं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-b" target="_blank">Page0519-b+ 57</a>]<BR>लभतामिदं च शिथिलज्याबंधमस्मद्धनुः<BR>Ś. 2. 6; R. 3. 59, 11. 15; 12. 104.<BR>--2<BR>The chord of an arc.<BR>--3 The earth.<BR>--4 A mother.<BR>--5 Overpowering<BR>force or strength.<BR>--6 Excessive<BR>demand, importunity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यानिः|ज्यानि
ज्यानिः f. [ज्या --नि]<BR>1 Old age,<BR>decay.<BR>--2 Quitting, abandoning.<BR>--3<BR>A river, stream.<BR>--4 Oppression.<BR>--5<BR>Deprivation, loss; Māl. 9. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यायस्
ज्यायस् a. (सी f.; compar. of<BR>प्रशस्य, वृद्ध)<BR>1 Elder, senior;<BR>प्रसवक्रमेण स किल ज्यायान् U. 6.<BR>--2<BR>Superior, more excellent or worthy;<BR>Ms. 4. 8, 3. 137; Bg. 3. 1, 8.<BR>--3 Larger,<BR>greater.<BR>--4 (In law) One not a<BR>minor, i. e. come of age and<BR>responsible for his own action.<BR>--5 Aged,<BR>old.<BR>--6 Decayed, worn out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यायिष्ठ
ज्यायिष्ठ a. (irreg.)<BR>1 The most<BR>excellent.<BR>--2 Noblest, first, best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठ|ज्येष्ठः
ज्येष्ठ a. (Superl. of प्रशस्य or वृद्ध).<BR>1 Eldest, most senior.<BR>--2 Most<BR>excellent, best.<BR>--3 Pre-eminent, first,<BR>chief, highest.<BR>--ष्ठः<BR>1 An elder<BR>brother; R. 12. 19, 35.<BR>--2 An epithet<BR>of the Supreme Being.<BR>--3 Life.<BR>--4<BR>N. of a lunar month (= ज्यैष्ठ q. v.).<BR>--ष्ठा<BR>1 An eldest sister.<BR>--2 N. of the<BR>eighteenth lunar mansion<BR>(consisting of the three stars).<BR>--3 The<BR>middle finger.<BR>--4 A small<BR>houselizard.<BR>--5 An epithet of the Ganges.<BR>--6 The goddess of misfortune, elder<BR>sister of Lakṣmī.<BR>--ष्ठी A small<BR>house-lizard.<BR>--ष्ठं<BR>1 The most<BR>excellent, the first or head.<BR>--2 Tin.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः {1} eldest brother's<BR>share. {2} the right of the eldest<BR>brother to a larger share of the<BR>patrimonial property. {3} the best<BR>share.<BR>--अंबु n. {1} water in which<BR>grain has been washed. {2} the<BR>scum of boild rice.<BR>--आश्रमः {1} the<BR>highest or most excellent order in<BR>the religious life of a Brāhmaṇa;<BR>i. e. that of a householder. {2} a<BR>householder.<BR>--तातः a father's eldest<BR>brother.<BR>--तातिः f. Ved. superiority.<BR>--वर्णः {1} the highest caste (that of<BR>Brāhmaṇas). {2} a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--वृत्तिः<BR>f. the duties of seniority.<BR>--श्वश्रूः f.<BR>{1} a wife's eldest sister. {2} the<BR>eldest mother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठामूल
ज्येष्ठामूल --मूलीयः The month ज्यैष्ठ<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्येष्ठामूलीयः|ज्येष्ठामूलीय
ज्येष्ठामूल --मूलीयः The month ज्यैष्ठ<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठः|ज्यैष्ठ
ज्यैष्ठः N. of a lunar month in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">Page0519-c+ 55</a>]<BR>which the full moon stands in the<BR>constellation ज्येष्ठा (corresponding<BR>to May-June).<BR>--ष्ठी<BR>1 The<BR>fullmoon day in the month of ज्यैष्ठ.<BR>--2<BR>A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठिनेय
ज्यैष्ठिनेय a. Born from the eldest<BR>or principal wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यैष्ठ्यं|ज्यैष्ठ्य
ज्यैष्ठ्यं<BR>1 Precedence, priority of<BR>birth, primogeniture, seniority.<BR>--2<BR>Pre-eminence, sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यु
ज्यु {c1c} A. (ज्यवते) To go near,<BR>approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्युत्
ज्युत् {c1c} U. (ज्योतति-ते) To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्युतिः|ज्युति
ज्युतिः f. Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यो
ज्यो {c1c} A. (ज्यवते)<BR>1 To advise,<BR>instruct.<BR>--2 To observe any<BR>religious obligation (such as a vow).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिस्
ज्योतिस् n. [द्युत्-इसुन् आदेर्दस्य जः,<BR>ज्युत्-इसुन् वा]<BR>1 Light, lustre,<BR>brightness, flash; ज्योतिरेकं जगाम<BR>Ś. 5. 30; R. 2. 75; Me. 5.<BR>--2 Light of<BR>Brahman, light regarded as the<BR>Supreme spirit; Bg. 5. 24, 13. 17;<BR>U. 4. 18.<BR>--3 Lightning.<BR>--4 A heavenly<BR>body.<BR>--5 A heavenly body, a luminary<BR>(planet, star &c.); ज्योतिर्भिरुद्याद्भिरिव<BR>त्रियामा Ku. 7. 21; Bg. 10. 21;<BR>H. 1. 21; Ku. 2. 19; Ś. 7. 6.<BR>--6<BR>Brightness of the sky, day-light (opp.<BR>तमस्).<BR>--7 The sun and moon (dual).<BR>--8 Light as the divine principle of<BR>life, intelligence.<BR>--9 The science of the<BR>course of heavenly bodies; astronomy.<BR>see ज्योतिष.<BR>--10 The faculty of seeing.<BR>--11 The celestial world. --m.<BR>1<BR>The sun.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इंगः, --इंगणः the<BR>fire-fly.<BR>--कणः a spark of fire.<BR>--गणः the heavenly bodies collectively;<BR>--चक्रं the zodiac.<BR>--ज्ञः an<BR>astronomer or astrologer.<BR>--मंडलं the stellar<BR>sphere.<BR>--मिलिन् m.<BR>--वी(बी)जं a<BR>firefly.<BR>--रथः (ज्योतीरथः) the polar star.<BR>--लोकः the supreme spirit.<BR>--विद् m.<BR>an astronomer or astrologer.<BR>--विद्या,<BR>--शास्त्रं (ज्योतिःश्शास्त्रं) astronomy or<BR>astrology.<BR>--स्तोमः (ज्योतिष्टोमः) a Soma<BR>sacrifice considered as the type of a<BR>whole class of sacrificial ceremonies.<BR>--हस्ता N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिर्मय
ज्योतिर्मय a. Consisting of stars,<BR>starry; R. 15. 59; Ku. 6. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष|ज्योतिषं|ज्योतिषः
ज्योतिष a. (षी f.) [ज्योतिः<BR>सूर्यादिगत्यादिकं प्रतिपाद्यतयाऽस्त्यस्य अच्]<BR>Astronomical or astrological.<BR>--षः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-a" target="_blank">Page0520-a+ 35</a>]<BR>An astronomer or astrologer.<BR>--षं<BR>1 Astronomy, astrology, the<BR>science of the course of the<BR>heavenly bodies and divisions of time<BR>resting thereon.<BR>--2 One of the six<BR>Vedāṅgas (being a short tract on<BR>astronomy).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विद्या<BR>astronomical or astrological science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0519-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषिकः|ज्योतिषिक
ज्योतिषिकः One who studies or<BR>knows astronomy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिषी
ज्योतिषी, ज्योतिष्कः A planet,<BR>star, luminary.<BR>--ष्कं N. of the<BR>shining peak of Meru.<BR>--ष्कः The<BR>चित्रक tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्कः|ज्योतिष्क
ज्योतिषी, ज्योतिष्कः A planet,<BR>star, luminary.<BR>--ष्कं N. of the<BR>shining peak of Meru.<BR>--ष्कः The<BR>चित्रक tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योतिष्मत्|ज्योतिष्मन्त्
ज्योतिष्मत् a. [ज्योतिरस्त्यस्य मतुप्]<BR>1 Luminous, bright, shining,<BR>possessed of luminous bodies;<BR>नक्षत्रताराग्रहसंकुलापि ज्योतिष्मती चंद्रमसैव<BR>रात्रिः R. 6. 22.<BR>--2 Celestial. --m.<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 N. of the third foot<BR>of Brahmā.<BR>--3 N. of one of the<BR>seven suns appearing at the<BR>destruction of the world.<BR>--ती<BR>1 The<BR>night (as illuminated by the stars).<BR>--2 (In phil.) A state of mind<BR>pervaded by सत्त्वगुण i. e. a tranquil<BR>state of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्ना
ज्योत्स्ना [ज्योतिरस्त्यस्यां ज्योतिष<BR>उपधालोपो नश्च प्रत्ययः P. V. 2. 114 Sk.]<BR>1 Moonlight;<BR>स्फुरत्स्फारज्योत्स्नाधवलिततले क्वापि पुलिने Bh. 3. 42;<BR>ज्योत्स्नावतो निर्विशति प्रदोषान् R. 6. 34.<BR>--2<BR>Light (in general).<BR>--3 An epithet<BR>of Durgā.<BR>--4 A moonlight-night.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः the moon.<BR>--प्रियः the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">Page0520-b+ 34</a>]<BR>Cakora bird.<BR>--वृक्षः a lamp-stand,<BR>a candle-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्योत्स्नी
ज्योत्स्नी A moonlight-night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौत्स्न|ज्यौत्स्नः
ज्यौत्स्न a. Bright or lit with<BR>moonlight.<BR>--त्स्नः The bright half of a<BR>month.<BR>--त्स्नी A full-moon night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौः
ज्यौः The planet Jupiter, (a word<BR>connected with Greek Zeus).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्यौतिषिकः|ज्यौतिषिक
ज्यौतिषिकः an astronomer or<BR>astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्रि
ज्रि {vI.v} {c1c} P. (ज्रयति)<BR>1 To<BR>overpower, conquer.<BR>--2 To go. {vII.v} {9}<BR>{c10c} P. (ज्रिणाति, ज्राययति) To grow old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वर्
ज्वर् {c1c} P. (ज्वरति, जूर्ण)<BR>1 To be<BR>hot with fever or passion, be<BR>feverish.<BR>--2 To be diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वर|ज्वरः
ज्वर a. [ज्वर् भावे थ]<BR>1 Heated,<BR>feverish.<BR>--2 Excited, inflamed.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>Fever, feverish heat (in medicine);<BR>स्वेद्यमानज्वरं प्राज्ञः कोंऽभसा परिषिंचति<BR>Śi. 2. 54; also used fig.; दर्पज्वरः,<BR>मदनज्वरः, मदज्वरः &c.<BR>--2 Fever of<BR>the soul, mental pain, affliction,<BR>distress, grief, sorrow; व्येतुं ते मनसो<BR>ज्वरः Rām.; मनसस्तदुपस्थिते ज्वरे<BR>R. 8. 84; Bg. 3. 30.<BR>--रा Fever.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः the paroxysm of fever.<BR>--अंकुशः a febrifuge.<BR>--प्रतीकारः cure<BR>of fever, febrifuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरित|ज्वरितः
ज्वरित, ज्वरिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>Attacked with fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वरिन्
ज्वरित, ज्वरिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>Attacked with fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वल्
ज्वल् {c1c} P. (ज्वलति, ज्वलित)<BR>1 To<BR>burn brightly, blaze, glow, shine;<BR>ज्वलति चलितेंधनोग्निः Ś. 6. 30;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-c" target="_blank">Page0520-c+ 35</a>]<BR>Ku. 5. 30.<BR>--2 To be burnt up, be<BR>consumed or afflicted (as by fire)<BR>अमृतमधुरमृदुतरवचनेन ज्वलति न सा<BR>मलयजपवनेन Gīt. 7.<BR>--3 To be ardent;<BR>जज्वाल लोकस्थितये स राजा Bk. 1. 4.<BR>--4<BR>To burn (as a wound). --Caus.<BR>(ज्वलयति-ते, ज्वालयति-ते, but प्रज्वलयति)<BR>1 To set on fire, light, kindle.<BR>--2<BR>To irradiate, illuminate, brighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वल|ज्वलः
ज्वल a. [ज्वल्-अच्]<BR>1 Flaming,<BR>blazing.<BR>--2 Bright, brilliant.<BR>--लः<BR>Flame, blaze, light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलका
ज्वलका A large flame of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलन|ज्वलनः
ज्वलन a. [ज्वल्-युच्]<BR>1 Flaming,<BR>shining.<BR>--2 Combustible.<BR>--नः<BR>1 Fire;<BR>तदनु ज्वलनं मदर्पितं<BR>त्वरयेर्दक्षिणवातवीजनैः Ku. 4. 36, 32; Bg. 11. 29.<BR>--2<BR>Corrosive alkali.<BR>--3 The number<BR>‘three’.<BR>--नं Burning, blazing, shining.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्मन् m. the sun-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वलित|ज्वलितः
ज्वलित a. [ज्वल्-क्त]<BR>1 Burnt,<BR>kindled, illuminated.<BR>--2 Flaming,<BR>blazing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वाल|ज्वालः
ज्वाल a. [ज्वल्-ण] Burning,<BR>blazing.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A flame, light;<BR>दवदहनजटालज्वालजालाहतानां Bv. 1. 36.<BR>--2<BR>A torch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वाला
ज्वाला<BR>1 A blaze, flame,<BR>illumination; R. 15. 16; Bh. 1. 95.<BR>--2<BR>Burnt rice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जिह्वः, --ध्वजः<BR>fire.<BR>--मुखी a volcano.<BR>--वक्त्रः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ज्वालिन्
ज्वालिन् a. [ज्वल्-णिनि]<BR>1 Flaming,<BR>blazing.<BR>--2 Shining. --m. An<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झ|झः
झ a.<BR>1 Asleep, sleeping.<BR>--2 Lost,<BR>destroyed.<BR>--झः<BR>1 Beating time.<BR>--2<BR>Jingling, clanking or any similar<BR>sound.<BR>--3 Wind accompanied by<BR>rain.<BR>--4 N. of Bṛhaspati.<BR>--5 A thing<BR>lost or mislaid.<BR>--6 A hurricane.<BR>--झा The descent of a cascade,<BR>waterfall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झगझगायते
झगझगायते Den. A. To flash,<BR>sparkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झगति
झग(गि)ति ind. Quickly, at<BR>once; साप्यप्सरा<BR>झगित्यासीत्तद्रूपाकृष्टलाचना Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झगिति
झग(गि)ति ind. Quickly, at<BR>once; साप्यप्सरा<BR>झगित्यासीत्तद्रूपाकृष्टलाचना Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झंकारः|झङ्कार|झंकार|झङ्कारः
झंकारः, झंकृतं A low<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520--1b" target="_blank">Page0520--1b+ 15</a>]<BR>murmuring sound, as the buzzing of bees;<BR>(अयं) दिगंतानातेने<BR>मधुपकुलझंकारभरित न् Bv. 1. 33, 4. 29; Bh. 1. 9;<BR>Amaru. 48; Pt. 5. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झंकृतं|झङ्कृत|झंकृत
झंकारः, झंकृतं A low<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520--1b" target="_blank">Page0520--1b+ 15</a>]<BR>murmuring sound, as the buzzing of bees;<BR>(अयं) दिगंतानातेने<BR>मधुपकुलझंकारभरित न् Bv. 1. 33, 4. 29; Bh. 1. 9;<BR>Amaru. 48; Pt. 5. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झंकारिणी
झंकारिणी The river Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झंकृतिः|झङ्कृति|झङ्कृतिः
झंकृतिः f. A clanking or jingling<BR>sound as of metal ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झंझनं|झञ्झन|झंझन
झंझनं<BR>1 Jingling and clanking<BR>of metal ornaments.<BR>--2 A rattling<BR>or ringing sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झंझा|झञ्झा
झंझा<BR>1 The noise of the wind or<BR>of falling rain.<BR>--2 Wind and rain,<BR>hurricane, gale.<BR>--3 A clanking<BR>sound, jingling.<BR>--4 Raining in large<BR>drops.<BR>--5 Anything lost.<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1c" target="_blank">Page0520-1c+ 15</a>]<BR>--अनिलः, --मरुत्, --वातः wind with rain, a<BR>storm, squall, stormy gale;<BR>झंझावातः सवृष्टिकः Ak.<BR>हिमांबुझंझानिलविह्वलस्य (पद्मस्य) Bv. 2. 169; Amaru. 48;<BR>Māl. 9. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झट्
झट् {c1c} P. (झट्ति)<BR>1 To become<BR>matted or clotted together (as hair).<BR>--2 To become confused or<BR>entangled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0520-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

झटिः|झटि
