टंकः, --कं [टंक्-घञ् अच् वा]<BR>1 A hatchet,<BR>an axe; a stone-cutter's chisel;<BR>टंकैर्मनः शिलगुहेव विदार्यमाणा Mk. 1. 20;<BR>R. 12. 80.<BR>--2 A sword.<BR>--3 The sheath<BR>of a sword.<BR>--4 A peak shaped like<BR>the edge of a hatchet; the slope or<BR>declivity of a hill; Bk. 1. 8.<BR>--5<BR>Anger.<BR>--6 Pride.<BR>--7 The leg.<BR>--8 A<BR>chasm, cleft.<BR>--9 The wood-apple tree.<BR>--10 Borax.<BR>--11 A weight of silver<BR>equal to four Māṣas.<BR>--12 The<BR>fruit of the wood-apple (n.).<BR>--13 A<BR>stamped coin.<BR>--14 A spade, hoe.<BR>--का The leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0522-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

टंकं|टङ्क|टंक|टंकः|टङ्कः
