डप्
डप् {c10c} A. (डापयते) To collect,<BR>amass, heap together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डम्
डम् {c1c} P. (डमति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमः|डम
डमः A despised and mixed caste<BR>(Dom).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमरः|डमर|डमरं
डमरः<BR>1 Riot, tumult, affray.<BR>--2<BR>Petty warfare between villages.<BR>--3<BR>Terrifying an enemy by shouts and<BR>gestures.<BR>--रं Running away through<BR>fear, rout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डमरुः|डमरु
डमरुः A sort of small drum,<BR>shaped like an hour-glass and<BR>generally used by Kāpālikas; (sometimes<BR>regarded as n. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डंप्|डम्प्
डंप् = डप् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डंब्|डम्ब्
डंब् {c10c} U. (डंबयति-ते)<BR>1 To throw,<BR>send.<BR>--2 To order.<BR>--3 To behold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डंबर|डम्बर|डम्बरः
डंबर a. Famous, renowned.<BR>--रः<BR>1 An assemblage, collection, mass;<BR>Māl. 9. 16.<BR>--2 Show, pomp.<BR>--3<BR>Resemblance, likeness, appearance;<BR>U. 6. 17; Māl. 3. 7.<BR>--4 Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डंभ्|डम्भ्
डंभ् {c10c} U. (डंमयति-ते) To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डलकं|डलक
डलकं, डल्लकं A sling, basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डल्लकं|डल्लक
डलकं, डल्लकं A sling, basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डवित्थः|डवित्थ
डवित्थः A wooden antelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाकिनी
डाकिनी A kind of female imp,<BR>a female goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डांकृतिः|डाङ्कृति
डांकृतिः f. The clang of a bell,<BR>ding-dong &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डामर|डामरः
डामर a.<BR>1 Terrific, dreadful,<BR>awful; पर्याप्तं मयि रमणीयडामरत्वं<BR>संधत्ते गगनतलप्रयाणवेगः Māl. 5. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Riotous, tumultuous.<BR>--3<BR>Resembling, having the appearance (i. e.<BR>lovely, beautiful); रतिगलिते ललिते<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">Page0523-b+ 42</a>]<BR>कुसुमानि शिखंडकडामरे (चिकुरे)<BR>Gīt. 12.<BR>--रः<BR>1 An uproar, rout, affray,<BR>riot.<BR>--2 The bustle and confusion<BR>of festivity or strife.<BR>--3 Any<BR>surprising sight.<BR>--4 N. of a mixed<BR>caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डालिमः|डालिम
डालिमः = दाडिमः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाहलः|डाहल
डाहलः (pl.) N. of a people<BR>and their country; कीर्तिः<BR>समाश्लिष्यति डाहलोवीं Vikr. 1. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डाहुकः|डाहुक
डाहुकः A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिक्करी
डिक्करी A young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिंगरः|डिङ्गर|डिंगर|डिङ्गरः
डिंगरः<BR>1 A servant.<BR>--2 A knave,<BR>cheat, rogue.<BR>--3 A depraved or low<BR>man.<BR>--4 A fat man.<BR>--5 Throwing,<BR>casting forth.<BR>--6 An insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिंडिमः|डिण्डिम|डिंडिम|डिण्डिमः
डिंडिमः A kind of small drum<BR>(fig. also); इति घोषयतीव डिंडिमः<BR>H. 2. 86; मुखरयस्व यशोनवडिंडिमं<BR>N. 4. 53; Amaru. 28; चंडि<BR>रणितरसनारवडिंडिममभिसर सरसमलज्जं Gīt. 11;<BR>आर्यबालचरितप्रस्तावनाडिंडिमः<BR>Mv. 1. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिंडीरः|डिण्डीर|डिंडीर|डिण्डीरः
डिंडी(डि)रः<BR>1 Cuttle-fish-bone<BR>considered as the foam of the sea.<BR>--2 Foam (in general); उद्दंडानेन<BR>डिंडीरे पिंडपंक्तिरदृश्यत Vikr. 4. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिंडिरः|डिण्डिर|डिंडिर|डिण्डिरः
डिंडी(डि)रः<BR>1 Cuttle-fish-bone<BR>considered as the foam of the sea.<BR>--2 Foam (in general); उद्दंडानेन<BR>डिंडीरे पिंडपंक्तिरदृश्यत Vikr. 4. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डित्थः|डित्थ
डित्थः<BR>1 A wooden elephant.<BR>--2 A<BR>good-looking, dark-coloured young<BR>man proficient in every science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिप्
डिप्, --डिंप् {vI.v} {c10c} A. To collect,<BR>heap together. {vII.v} {c4c} {6} {c10c} P. (डिप्यति,<BR>डिपति, डेपयति)<BR>1 To throw, cast,<BR>send.<BR>--2 To direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिंप्
डिप्, --डिंप् {vI.v} {c10c} A. To collect,<BR>heap together. {vII.v} {c4c} {6} {c10c} P. (डिप्यति,<BR>डिपति, डेपयति)<BR>1 To throw, cast,<BR>send.<BR>--2 To direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिम्
डिम् (डेमति) To hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिमः|डिम
डिमः One of the ten kinds of<BR>dramas;<BR>मार्येंद्रजालसंग्रामक्रोधोद्भ्रांतादिचेष्टितैः । उपरागैश्च भूयिष्ठो डिमः ख्यातोऽ<BR>तिवृत्तकः ॥ S. D. 517.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिंबः|डिम्ब|डिंब|डिम्बं|डिम्बः
डिंबः<BR>1 Affray, riot.<BR>--2 sound<BR>or noise occasioned by terror.<BR>--3<BR>A young child or animal.<BR>--4 An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">Page0523-c+ 42</a>]<BR>egg.<BR>--5 A globe or ball.<BR>--6<BR>Globular or round blossom; Māl. 9. 26.<BR>--7 A chrysalis.<BR>--8 The embryo in<BR>the first stage of its existence.<BR>--9<BR>The spleen.<BR>--10 The uterus.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आहवः, --युद्धं petty warfare, an<BR>affray without weapons, skirmish,<BR>sham-fight; Ms. 5. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिंबिका|डिम्बिका
डिंबिका<BR>1 A libidinous woman.<BR>--2 A bubble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिंभः|डिम्भ|डिंभ|डिम्भः
डिंभः<BR>1 A young child.<BR>--2 Any<BR>young animal such as a cub; जृंभस्व<BR>रे डिंभ दंतांस्ते गणयिष्यामि Ś. 7.<BR>--3 A<BR>fool, a block-head.<BR>--भा An infant<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डिंभकः|डिम्भक|डिंभक|डिम्भकः
डिंभकः (भिका f.)<BR>1 A young<BR>child.<BR>--2 Any young animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डी
डी {c1c} {c4c} A. (डयते, डीयते, डिड्ये,<BR>अडयिष्ट, डयितुं, डीन)<BR>1 To fly, pass<BR>through the air.<BR>--2 To go. --WITH<BR>प्र to fly up; हंसैः प्रडीनैरिव Mk. 5. 5.<BR>--प्रोद् to fly up; प्रोड्डीयेव बलाकया<BR>सरभसं सोत्कंठमालिंगितः 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डयनं|डयन
डयनं<BR>1 Flight.<BR>--2 A litter carried<BR>upon men's shoulders, palanquin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डीन|डीनं
डीन p. p. [डी-क्त] Flown up.<BR>--नं<BR>The flight of a bird. The varieties<BR>of the flight of birds are said to be<BR>101, the word prefixed to डीन<BR>showing the particular mode of flight;<BR>e. g. अवडीनं, उड्डीनं, प्रडीनं, अभिडीनं,<BR>विडीनं, परिडीनं, पराडीनं &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुंडुभः|डुण्डुभ|डुंडुभ|डुण्डुभः
डुंडुभः --मः A kind of snake not<BR>poisonous (निर्विषा डुंडुभाः स्मृताः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुंडुमः
डुंडुभः --मः A kind of snake not<BR>poisonous (निर्विषा डुंडुभाः स्मृताः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुंडुलः|डुण्डुल|डुण्डुलः
डुंडुलः A small owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुंदुकः|डुन्दुक|डुन्दुकः
डुंदुकः A gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डुलिः|डुलि
डुलिः A small turtle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डोमः|डोम
डोमः A man of a very low caste;<BR>also डोंब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

डोरः|डोर|डोरं
डोरः<BR>1 A fillet of thread (tied round<BR>the arm).<BR>--2 The string with which<BR>a packet or parcel is tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ड्वल्
ड्वल् {c10c} U. (ड्वालयति-ते) To mix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0523-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढः|ढ
ढः<BR>1 An imitative sound.<BR>--2 A<BR>large drum.<BR>--3 A dog's tail.<BR>--4 A<BR>dog.<BR>--5 A serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढक्का
ढक्का<BR>1 A large or double drum;<BR>न ते हुडुक्केन न सोपि ढक्कया न मर्दलैः<BR>सापि न तेऽपि ढक्कया ॥ N. 15. 17.<BR>--2<BR>Coveting.<BR>--3 Disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढामरा
ढामरा A goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढालं|ढाल
ढालं A shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढालिन्
ढालिन् m. A warrior armed with<BR>a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुंढनं|ढुण्ढन
ढुंढनं Seeking, investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढुंढिः|ढुण्ढि|ढुंढि|ढुण्ढिः
ढुंढिः An epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढौलः
ढौलः A large drum or tabor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढौक्
ढौक् {c1c} A. (ढौकते, ढौकित) To go,<BR>approach; यांतं वने रात्रिचरी डुढौके<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-c" target="_blank">Page0524-c+ 9</a>]<BR>Bk. 2. 23; 14. 71, 15. 49. --Caus.<BR>(ढौकयति-ते)<BR>1 To bring near, cause<BR>to approach; तन्मांसं चैव गोमायोस्तैः<BR>क्षणादाशु ढौकितं Mb.; Bk. 17. 103.<BR>--2 To present, offer. --WITH उप to<BR>present, offer; एकैकं पशुमुपढौकयामः<BR>Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ढौकनं|ढौकन
ढौकनं<BR>1 Offering.<BR>--2 A present,<BR>bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

णः|ण
णः<BR>1 Knowledge.<BR>--2 Certainty,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524--1c" target="_blank">Page0524--1c+ 4</a>]<BR>ascertainment.<BR>--3 An ornament.<BR>--4<BR>A water or summer-house.<BR>--5 A<BR>bad man.<BR>--6 Śiva.<BR>--7 The sound<BR>of negation.<BR>--8 Gift, giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0524-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तः|त|तं
तः<BR>1 A tail.<BR>--2 The tail of a<BR>jackal.<BR>--3 The breast.<BR>--4 The womb.<BR>--5<BR>The hip or flank.<BR>--6 A warrior.<BR>--7<BR>A thief.<BR>--8 A wicked man.<BR>--9 An<BR>outcast, a barbarian.<BR>--10 A Bud<BR>dha.<BR>--11 A jewel.<BR>--12 Nectar.<BR>--13<BR>(In prosody) One of the eight<BR>syllabic feet.<BR>--ता, --तं<BR>1 Passing,<BR>crossing.<BR>--2 Virtue, religious merit.<BR>--ता<BR>N. of Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंस्
तंस् {vI.v} {c1c} A. Ved. (तंसते)<BR>1 To<BR>shake.<BR>--2 To pour out.<BR>--3 To beg,<BR>request. {vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (तंसति,<BR>तंसयति-ते) To decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्
तक् {c1c} {c2c} P. Ved. (तकति, तक्ति)<BR>1<BR>To fly (as an arrow or bird), rush<BR>at or upon<BR>--2 To laugh at, deride,<BR>scoff<BR>--3 To bear, endure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक
तक a. Ved.<BR>1 Censured.<BR>--2<BR>Enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तकु
तकु a. Ved. Approaching(गामुक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्वन्
तक्वन् a. Ved. Rushing, darting<BR>along. --m.<BR>1 A bird (especially a bird<BR>of prey).<BR>--2 A fleet horse.<BR>--3 A thief,<BR>rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तकिल|तकिलः
तकिल a. Fraudulent, crafty,<BR>rogue.<BR>--ला A medicament, drug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्कन्
तक्कन् n. A child, offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्रं|तक्र
तक्रं Butter-milk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अटः<BR>a churning-stick.<BR>--सारं fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्ष्
तक्ष् {c1c} {c5c} P. (तक्षति, तक्ष्णोति, तष्ट)<BR>1 To chop, cut off, pare, chisel, slice,<BR>split; आत्मानं तक्षति ह्येष वनं परशुना<BR>यथा Mb.; निधाय तक्ष्यते यत्र काष्ठे<BR>काष्ठं स उद्घनः Ak.<BR>--2 To fashion, shape,<BR>form (out of wood &c.).<BR>--3 To make,<BR>create in general.<BR>--4 To wound, hurt.<BR>--5 To invent, form in the mind.<BR>--6<BR>To make one's own, appropriate.<BR>--7<BR>To cover.<BR>--8 To peel.<BR>--9 To make<BR>thin. --WITH निस्<BR>1 to slice out of.<BR>--2 to form, create.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्ष्
तक्ष् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Paring, cutting &c.; also तक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षकः|तक्षक
तक्षकः [तक्ष् ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A carpenter,<BR>wood-cutter (whether by caste or<BR>profession).<BR>--2 The chief actor in<BR>the prelude of a drama (i. e. the<BR>सूत्रधार).<BR>--3 N. of the architect of the<BR>gods.<BR>--4 N. of one of the principal<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">Page0525-b+ 50</a>]<BR>Nāgas or serpents of the Pātāla,<BR>son of Kaśyapa and Kadru; (saved<BR>at the intercession of the sage<BR>Āstīka from being burnt down in the<BR>serpent-sacrifice performed by king<BR>Janamejaya, in which many others<BR>of his race were burnt down to<BR>ashes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षणं|तक्षण
तक्षणं [तक्ष् भावे-ल्युट्] Paring,<BR>cutting; दारवाणां च तक्षणं Ms. 5. 115;<BR>Y. 1. 185.<BR>--णी A carpenter's adze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तक्षन्
तक्षन् m. [तक्ष्-कनिन्]<BR>1 A<BR>carpenter, wood-cutter (whether by caste<BR>or profession); अतक्षा तक्षा K. P.<BR>‘one not a तक्षन् by caste is called<BR>तक्षन् when he acts like or follows<BR>the profession of a तक्षन् (carpenter);’<BR>Śi. 12. 25.<BR>--2 N. of the architect of<BR>the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तगरः|तगर|तगरं
तगरः A kind of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंक्|तङ्क्
तंक् {c1c} P. (तंकति, तंकित)<BR>1 To<BR>endure, bear.<BR>--2 To laugh.<BR>--3 To<BR>live in distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंकः|तङ्क|तंक|तङ्कः
तंकः [तंक् भावे अच्]<BR>1 Living in<BR>distress, a miserable life.<BR>--2 Grief<BR>produced by separation from a<BR>beloved object.<BR>--3 Fear, terror.<BR>--4<BR>A stone-cutter's chisel.<BR>--5 A<BR>garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंकनं|तङ्कन
तंकनं Living in distress,<BR>miserable living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंग्|तङ्ग्
तंग् {c1c} P. (तंगति, तंगित)<BR>1 To go,<BR>move.<BR>--2 To shake, tremble.<BR>--3<BR>To stumble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंच्|तञ्च्
तंच् {vI.v} {c7c} P. (तनक्ति, तंचित) To<BR>contract, shrink; तनच्मि व्योम विस्तृतं<BR>Bk. 6. 38. {vII.v} {c1c} P. (तंचति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंज्|तञ्ज्
तंज् {c7c} P. See तंच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तट्
तट् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (तटति)<BR>1 To groan.<BR>--2 To rise, be raised or elevated.<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} U. (ताटयति-ते) To beat,<BR>strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटः|तट|तटं
तटः [तट्-अच्]<BR>1 A slope,<BR>declivity, precipice.<BR>--2 The sky or<BR>horizon.<BR>--3 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--टः --टा,<BR>--टी, --टं<BR>1 The shore or bank,<BR>declivity, slope; शीलं शैलतटात्पततु<BR>Bh. 2. 39; प्रोत्तुंगचिंतातटी Bh. 3. 45;<BR>सिंधोस्तटावोघ इव प्रवृद्धः Ku. 3. 6;<BR>U. 3. 8; उच्चारणात्पक्षिगणास्तटीस्तं Śi. 4. 18.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-c" target="_blank">Page0525-c+ 51</a>]<BR>A term applied to certain parts of the<BR>body which have, as it were, sloping<BR>sides; पद्मापयोधरतटीपरिरंभलग्न Gīt. 1; नो<BR>लुप्तं सखि चंदनं स्तनतटे Ś. Til. 7; so<BR>जघनतट, कटितट, श्रोणीतट, कुचतट,<BR>कंठतट, ललाटतट &c.<BR>--टं A field.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आघातः butting, striking<BR>against a bank or declivity;<BR>अभ्यस्यंति तटाघातं निर्जितैरावता गजाः<BR>Ku. 2. 50.<BR>--स्थ a. {1} (lit.) situated on<BR>a bank or declivity. {2} (fig.)<BR>standing aloof, neutral, indifferent,<BR>alien, passive; तटस्थः स्वानर्थान्<BR>घटयति च मौनं च भजते Māl. 1. 14; तटस्थं<BR>नैराश्यात् U. 3. 13; मया<BR>तष्टस्थस्त्वमुपद्रुतोसि N. 3. 55 (where तटस्थ has<BR>sense 1. also).<BR>--(स्थः) an<BR>indifferent person, one neither a friend<BR>nor a foe.<BR>--(स्थं) that property or<BR>लक्षण of a thing which is distinct<BR>from its nature, and yet is the<BR>property by which it is known; e. g.<BR>गंधवत्त्व in the case of पृथ्वी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटकं|तटक
तटकं A shore or bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटगः|तटग
तटगः = तडाग q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटाकः|तटाक|तटाकं
तटाकः --कं A pond (deep enough<BR>for the lotus and other aquatic<BR>plants); See तडाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटाकं|तटाक|तटाकः
तटाकः --कं A pond (deep enough<BR>for the lotus and other aquatic<BR>plants); See तडाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तटिनी
तटिनी [तटमस्त्यस्या इनि ङीप्] A<BR>river; कदा वाराणस्याममरतटिनीरोधसि<BR>वसन् Bh. 3. 123; Bv. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तट्यः|तट्य
तट्यः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तड्
तड् {c10c} U. (ताडयति-ते, ताडित)<BR>1<BR>To beat, strike (in general), dash<BR>against; गाहंतां महिषा निपानसलिलं<BR>शृंगैर्मुहस्ताडितं Ś. 2. 5; (नौः) ताडिता<BR>मारुतैर्यथा Rām.; R. 3. 61;<BR>Ku. 5. 24; Bh. 1. 50.<BR>--2 To beat, strike,<BR>punish by beating, hit; लालयेत्पंच<BR>वर्षाणि दश वर्षाणि ताडयेत् Chāṇ. 11,<BR>12; न ताडयेत्तृणेनापि Ms. 4. 169;<BR>पादेन यस्ताड्यते Amaru. 52.<BR>--3 To<BR>strike, beat (as a drum);<BR>ताड्यमानासुभेरीषु Mb.; अताडयन् मृदंगांश्च<BR>Bk. 17. 7; Ve. 1. 22.<BR>--4 To play on,<BR>strike the wires of (a musical<BR>instrument); श्रोतुर्वितंत्रीरिव ताड्यमाना<BR>Ku. 1. 45.<BR>--5 To shine.<BR>--6 To<BR>speak.<BR>--7 (In astr.) To strike<BR>against, touch, obscure or eclipse<BR>partially.<BR>--8 (In Math.) To multiply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0525-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडि|तडिः
तडि a. Beating.<BR>--डिः Striking, a<BR>stroke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड|ताडः
ताड a. [तड् भावे अच्] Beating,<BR>striking.<BR>--डः<BR>1 A blow, knock,<BR>thumb, whipping, chastisement.<BR>--2<BR>Noise, sound.<BR>--3 A sheaf.<BR>--4 A<BR>mountain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--घ a. beating<BR>with a whip or strokes of any kind.<BR>--घः, --घातः an artificer who beats<BR>or hammers, a smith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडन|ताडनं
ताडन a. [तड् भावे ल्युट्] Beating,<BR>whipping, striking.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Beating,<BR>whipping, flogging; लालने बहवो<BR>दोषास्ताडने बहवो गुणाः Chāṇ. 12;<BR>अवतंसोत्पलताडनानि वा Ku. 4. 8;<BR>Ś. Til. 9.<BR>--2 (In astr.) Touching, partial<BR>eclipse.<BR>--ना Striking.<BR>--नी A whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडित
ताडित p. p. Struck, beaten,<BR>chastised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडुल|ताडुलः
ताडुल a. Beating, striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड्यमान|ताड्यमानः
ताड्यमान a. Being beaten or<BR>struck; श्रोतुर्वितंत्रीरिव ताड्यमाना<BR>Ku. 1. 45; ताड्यमानः किं न ब्रूयात् Mu. 5.<BR>--नः A musical instrument struck<BR>with a stick &c. (as a drum).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडगः|तडग
तडगः See तडाग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाकः|तडाक
तडाकः A pond, pool.<BR>--का<BR>1 A<BR>blow.<BR>--2 A bank, shore.<BR>--3<BR>Splendour, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडागः|तडाग|तडागं
तडागः --गं<BR>1 A pond, deep pool,<BR>tank;<BR>स्फुटकमलोदरखेलितखंजनयुगमिव शरदि तडागं Gīt. 11; Ms. 4. 203;<BR>Y. 3. 237.<BR>--2 A tank.<BR>--3 A trap<BR>for catching deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडागं|तडाग|तडागः
तडागः --गं<BR>1 A pond, deep pool,<BR>tank;<BR>स्फुटकमलोदरखेलितखंजनयुगमिव शरदि तडागं Gīt. 11; Ms. 4. 203;<BR>Y. 3. 237.<BR>--2 A tank.<BR>--3 A trap<BR>for catching deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडाघातः|तडाघात
तडाघातः See तटाघात; (<BR>उच्चैःकरिकराक्षेपे तडाघातं विदुर्बुधाः Śabdak.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडित्
तडित् f.<BR>1 Lightning; घनं घनांते<BR>तडितां गुणैरिव Śi. 1. 7; Me. 77;<BR>R. 6. 65.<BR>--2 Killing, injury. --ind.<BR>Closely, near.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गर्भः<BR>a cloud.<BR>--लता forked lightning.<BR>--लेखा a streak of lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडित्वत्|तडित्वन्त्
तडित्वत् a. Containing or having<BR>lightning; अवरोहति शैलाग्रं<BR>तडित्वानिव तोयदः V. 1. 14; Ki. 5. 4. --m.<BR>A cloud; Śi. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तडिन्मय
तडिन्मय a. Consisting of<BR>lightning; Ku. 5. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंड्|तण्ड्
तंड् {c1c} A. (तंडते, तंडित) To strike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंडकः|तण्डक|तंडक|तण्डकः
तंडकः [तंड्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A juggler, a<BR>cheat.<BR>--2 Froth, foam.<BR>--3 A<BR>wagtail.<BR>--कः --कं<BR>1 Complete<BR>performance or preparation.<BR>--2 Decoration.<BR>--3 The upright post of a house.<BR>--4<BR>A composition abounding in<BR>compounds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंडा
तंडा Killing, striking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंडुरीणः|तण्डुरीण|तण्डुरीणः
तंडुरीणः<BR>1 A barbarian.<BR>--2 A<BR>fool, blockhead.<BR>--3 Water in which<BR>rice has been soaked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंडुलः|तण्डुल|तंडुल|तण्डुलः
तंडुलः [तंड्-उलच्] Grain after<BR>threshing, unhusking and<BR>winnowing; (especially rice); शस्य, धान्य,<BR>तंडुल and अन्न are thus<BR>distinguished from one another:--शस्यं क्षेत्रगतं<BR>प्रोक्तं सतुषं धान्यमुच्यते । निस्तुषस्तंडुलः प्रोक्तः<BR>स्विन्नमन्नमुदाहृतं ॥.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंबु n.<BR>gruel.<BR>--उत्थं-कं rice-gruel.<BR>--ओघः<BR>{1} a prickly sort of bamboo. {2} a<BR>heap of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत|ततं|ततः
तत See under तन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततम|ततमः
ततम a. That one(of many).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततर|ततरः
ततर a. That one(of two).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्
ततस् (ततः) ind.<BR>1 From that<BR>(person or place &c.), thence;<BR>न च निम्नदिव हृदयं निवर्तते मे ततो हृदयं<BR>Ś. 3. 1; Māl. 2. 10; Ms. 6. 7;<BR>12. 85.<BR>--2 There, thither.<BR>--3 Then,<BR>thereupon, afterwards; ततः<BR>कतिपयदिवसापगमे K. 110, Amaru. 66; Ki. 1. 27;<BR>Ms. 2. 93, 7. 59.<BR>--4 Therefore,<BR>consequently, for that reason.<BR>--5 Then,<BR>in that case (as a corr. of यदि);<BR>यदि गृहीतमिदं ततः किं K. 120;<BR>अमोच्यमश्वं यदि मन्यसे प्रभो ततः समाप्ते &c.<BR>R. 3. 65.<BR>--6 Beyond that (in place),<BR>further, further more, moreover;<BR>ततः परतो निर्मानुषमरण्यं K. 121.<BR>--7<BR>Than that, other than that; यं लब्ध्वा<BR>चापरं लाभं मन्यते नाधिकं ततः<BR>Bg. 6. 22, 2. 36.<BR>--8 Sometimes used for the<BR>ablative forms of तद् such as<BR>तस्माद्तस्याः; ततोऽन्यत्रापि दृश्यते Sk.;<BR>यतःततः means (a) where-there; यतः<BR>कृष्णस्ततः सर्वे यतः कृष्णस्ततो जयः Mb.,<BR>Ms. 7, 188. (b) since-therefore.<BR>यतो यतः --ततस्ततः wherever-there;<BR>यतोयतः षट्चरणोभिवर्तते ततस्ततः प्रेरि<BR>तवामलोचना Ś. 1. 23. ततः किं ‘what<BR>then’, ‘of what use is it’, ‘what<BR>avails it’; प्राप्ताः श्रियः स<BR>कलकामदुघास्ततः किं Bh. 3. 73, 74; Śānti. 4. 2,<BR>ततस्ततः (a) ‘here and there’, ‘to<BR>and fro’; ततो दिव्यानि माल्यानि<BR>प्रादुरासंस्ततस्ततः Mb. (b) ‘what next’,<BR>‘what further,’ well proceed<BR>(occurring in dramas); ततः प्रभृति<BR>thence-forward, (corr. of यतः प्रभृति);<BR>तृष्णाततः प्रभृति मे द्विगुणत्वमेति<BR>Amaru. 68; Ms. 9. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततस्त्य|ततस्त्यं
ततस्त्य a. Coming or proceeding<BR>from thence; Ki. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तति|ततिः
तति pron. a. (Declined only<BR>in plural, nom. and acc. तति)<BR>So many; e. g. तति पुरुषाः संति &c.<BR>(for other senses see the word<BR>under तन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततिथ
ततिथ a. (Correlative of यतिथ)<BR>That one of a number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततुरि|ततुरिः
ततुरि a.<BR>1 Preserving,<BR>cherishing.<BR>--2 Conquering.<BR>--3 Killing,<BR>hurting.<BR>--रिः An epithet of<BR>Agni and Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वं|तत्त्व
तत्त्वं (Sometimes written as<BR>तत्वं)<BR>1 True state or condition,<BR>fact; वयं तत्त्वान्वेषान्मधुकर हतास्त्वं खलु<BR>कृती Ś. 1. 24.<BR>--2 Truth, reality;<BR>न तु मामाभिजानंति तत्त्वेनातश्च्यवंति ते<BR>Bg. 9. 24.<BR>--3 True or essential<BR>nature; संन्यासस्य महाबाहो<BR>तत्वमिच्छामि वेदितुं Bg. 18. 1, 3. 28;<BR>Ms. 1. 3, 3. 96, 5. 42.<BR>--4 The real nature<BR>of the human soul or the material<BR>world as being identical with the<BR>Supreme Spirit pervading the<BR>universe.<BR>--5 A true or first principle.<BR>--6 An element, a primary substance.<BR>--7 The mind.<BR>--8 Sum and substance.<BR>--9 Slow time in music.<BR>--10 An<BR>element or elementary property.<BR>--11 The Supreme Being.<BR>--12 A<BR>kind of dance.<BR>--13 The three<BR>qualities or constituents of every<BR>thing in nature (सत्त्व, रजस् and<BR>तमस्).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभियोगः a<BR>positive charge or declaration.<BR>--अर्थः<BR>truth, reality, the exact truth, real<BR>nature.<BR>--ज्ञ, --विद् a. {1} a<BR>philosopher. {2} knowing the true nature<BR>of Brahman. {3} knowing the true<BR>nature of anything. {4} acquainted<BR>with the true principles of science.<BR>--(ज्ञः) a Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--ज्ञानं {1}<BR>knowledge of the truth. {2} a<BR>thorough knowledge of the<BR>principles of a science. {3} philosophy.<BR>--न्यासः N. of a ceremony<BR>performed in honour of Viṣṇu consisting<BR>in the application of mystical<BR>letters or other marks to different<BR>parts of the body while certain<BR>prayers are repeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वतः
तत्त्वतः --तत्त्वेन ind. Truly, really,<BR>accurately; तत्त्वत एनामुपलप्स्ये Ś. 1;<BR>Ms. 7. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्त्वेन
तत्त्वतः --तत्त्वेन ind. Truly, really,<BR>accurately; तत्त्वत एनामुपलप्स्ये Ś. 1;<BR>Ms. 7. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्र
तत्र ind.<BR>1 In that place, there,<BR>yonder, thither.<BR>--2 On that<BR>occasion, under those circumstances,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0527-a" target="_blank">Page0527-a+ 57</a>]<BR>then, in that case.<BR>--3 For that,<BR>in that; निरीतयः । यन्मदीयाः प्रजास्तत्र<BR>हेतुस्त्वद्ब्रह्मवर्चसं R. 1. 63.<BR>--4 Often<BR>used for the loc. case of तद्;<BR>Ms. 2. 112, 3. 60; 4. 186; Y. 1. 263.<BR>तत्रापि ‘even then’ ‘nevertheless’;<BR>(corr. of यद्यपि.). तत्र तत्र ‘in<BR>various places or cases, ‘here and<BR>there,’ ‘to every place’;<BR>अध्यक्षान्विविधान्कुर्यात तत्र तत्र विपश्चितः<BR>Ms. 7. 81.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भवत् a. (ती f.) his<BR>honour, his reverence, revered,<BR>respectable, worthy, a respectful<BR>title given in dramas to persons<BR>not near the speaker; (पूज्ये<BR>तत्रभवानत्रभवांश्च भगवानपि); आदिष्टोस्मि<BR>तत्रभवता काश्यपेन Ś. 4; तत्रभवान्<BR>काश्यपः Ś. 1. &c.<BR>--स्थ a. standing or<BR>being there, belonging to that<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0526-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत्रत्य|तत्रत्यः
तत्रत्य a. (तत्र भवः अव्ययात् त्यपू)<BR>Born or produced there, belonging<BR>to that place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथा
तथा [तद् प्रकारे थाल् विभक्तित्वात्]<BR>ind.<BR>1 So, thus, in that manner; तथा<BR>मां वंचयित्वा Ś. 5; सूतस्तथा करोति<BR>V. 1.<BR>--2 And also, so also, as well<BR>as; अनागतविधाता च प्रत्युत्पन्नमतिस्तथा<BR>Pt. 1. 318; R. 3. 21.<BR>--3 True,<BR>just so, exactly so; यदात्थ राजन्यकुमार<BR>तत्तथा R. 3. 48; Ms. 1. 42.<BR>--4<BR>(In forms of adjuration) As<BR>surely as (preceded by यथा); see यथा.<BR>(For some of the meanings of तथा<BR>as a correlative of यथा, see under<BR>यथा). तथापि (oft. corr. of यद्यपि)<BR>‘even then,’ ‘still’, ‘yet’,<BR>‘never-the-less’, प्रथित दुष्यंतस्य चरितं<BR>तथापीदं न लक्षये Ś. 5; वरं महत्या<BR>म्रियते पिपासया तथापि नान्यस्य<BR>करोत्युपासना Chāt. 2. 6; वपुःप्रकर्षादजयद्रुरुं<BR>रघुस्तथापि नीचैर्विनयाददृश्यत<BR>R. 3. 34, 62. तथेति shows ‘assent’ or<BR>‘promise’; तथेति शेषामिव<BR>भर्तुराज्ञामादाय मूर्ध्ना मदनः प्रतस्थे Ku. 3. 22;<BR>R. 1. 92, 3. 67; Ku. 6. 3;<BR>तथेति निष्क्रांतः (in dramas). तथैव;<BR>‘even so’, ‘just so’; ‘exactly so’;<BR>तथैव च ‘in like manner’; तथा च<BR>‘and also’, ‘and likewise’, ‘in<BR>like manner’, ‘so it has<BR>been said’; तथाहि ‘for so’ ‘as<BR>for instance’, ‘for this (it<BR>has been said)’; तं वेधा विदधे नूनं<BR>महाभूतसमाधिना । तथाहि वर्से तस्यासम्<BR>परार्थैकफला गुणाः ॥ R. 1. 29;<BR>Ś. 1. 32.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत a. thus done.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0527-b" target="_blank">Page0527-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--गत a. {1} being in such a state<BR>or condition; तथागतायां परिहासपूर्वं<BR>R. 6. 82. {2} of such a quality.<BR>--(तः) {1} Buddha; काले मितं<BR>वाक्यमुदर्कपश्यं तथागतस्येव जनः सुचेताः<BR>Śi. 20. 81. {2} a Jina.<BR>--गुण a.<BR>endowed with such qualities.<BR>--भावः<BR>{1} that state or condition. {2}<BR>reality; Māl. 1. 31.<BR>--भूत a. {1} of<BR>such qualities or nature. {2} so<BR>circumstanced, in that condition;<BR>तथाभूतां दृष्ट्वा नृपसदसि पांचालतनयां<BR>Ve. 1. 11.<BR>--राजः an epithet of<BR>Buddha.<BR>--रूप, --रूपिन् a. thus<BR>shaped, looking thus.<BR>--विध a. of<BR>such a sort, of such qualities or<BR>nature; तथाविधस्तावदशेषमस्तु सः<BR>Ku. 5. 82, R. 3. 4.<BR>--विधं ind. {1}<BR>thus, in this manner. {2} likewise.<BR>equally.<BR>--विधेय a. of such a sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0527-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथात्वं|तथात्व
तथात्वं --तथाता<BR>1 Such a state,<BR>being so.<BR>--2 True state or nature,<BR>truth.<BR>--3 The case being<BR>admitted to be as stated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथाता
तथात्वं --तथाता<BR>1 Such a state,<BR>being so.<BR>--2 True state or nature,<BR>truth.<BR>--3 The case being<BR>admitted to be as stated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तथ्य|तथ्यं
तथ्य a. [तथा साधु यत्] True, real,<BR>genuine; प्रियमपि तथ्यमाह प्रियंवदा<BR>Ś. 1.<BR>--थ्यं Truth, reality; सा<BR>तथ्यमेवाभिहिता भवेन Ku. 3. 63;<BR>Ms. 8. 274.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्
तद् pron. a. (Nom. sing. सः<BR>m., सा f., तत् n.)<BR>1 That, referring<BR>to something not present; (तदिति<BR>परोक्षे विजानीयात्).<BR>--2 He, she, it;<BR>(oft. as corr. of यद्); यस्य<BR>बुद्धिर्बलं तस्य Pt. 1.<BR>--3 That, i. e.<BR>wellknown; सा रम्या नगरी महान्स नृपतिः<BR>सामंतचक्रं च तत् Bh. 3. 37;<BR>Ku. 5. 71.<BR>--4 That (referring to<BR>something seen or experienced before,<BR>अनुभूतार्थः); उत्कांपिनी<BR>भयपरिस्खलितांशुकांता ते लोचने प्रतिदिशं विधुरे क्षिपंती<BR>K. P. 7; Bv. 2. 5.<BR>--5 The same,<BR>identical, that, very; usually with<BR>एव; तानींद्रियाणि सकलानि तदेव नाम<BR>Bh. 2. 40. Sometimes the form<BR>of तद् are used with the first<BR>and second personal pronouns,<BR>as well as with demonstratives and<BR>relatives, for the sake of emphasis;<BR>(often translatable by ‘therefore’,<BR>‘then’); सोहमिज्याविशुद्धात्मा R. 1. 69;<BR>‘I that very person’, ‘I therefore’;<BR>(I who am so and so); स त्वं<BR>निवर्तस्व विहाय लज्जां 2. 40 ‘thou,<BR>therefore, shouldst return’, &c. When<BR>repeated तद् has the sense of<BR>‘several’, ‘various’; तेषु तेषु स्थानेषु K. 369;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0527-c" target="_blank">Page0527-c+ 58</a>]<BR>Bg. 7. 20; Māl. 1. 36; ते ते भावाः<BR>1. 17. तेन the instr. of तद् is often<BR>used with adverbial force in the<BR>sense of ‘therefore’, ‘on that account,<BR>in that case’, ‘for that reason.’ तेन<BR>हि if so, well then. --ind.<BR>1 There,<BR>thither.<BR>--2 Then, in that case, at<BR>that time.<BR>--3 For that reason,<BR>therefore, consequently; तदेहि विमर्दक्षमां<BR>भूमिमवतरावः U. 5; Me. 7, 109: R. 3. 46.<BR>--4 Then (corr. of यदि); तथापि यदि<BR>महत्कुतूहलं तत्कथयामि K. 136; Bg. 1. 46.<BR>--n.<BR>1 The Supreme Spirit or<BR>Brahman.<BR>--2 This world.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिपात a. going beyond the bounds.<BR>--अनंतर a. next to that. (--ind.)<BR>immediately after that, thereupon.<BR>--अनु ind. after that, afterwards;<BR>संदेशं मे तदनु जलद श्रोष्यसि श्रोत्रपेयं<BR>Me. 13; R. 16. 87; Māl. 9. 26.<BR>--अंत a.<BR>perishing in that, ending thus.<BR>--अर्थ, --अर्थीय a. {1} intended for that.<BR>{2} having that meaning.<BR>--अर्ह a.<BR>meriting that.<BR>--अवधि ind. {1} so far,<BR>upto that period, till then; तदवधि<BR>कुशली पुराणशास्त्ररमृतिशतचारुविचारजो<BR>विवेकः Bv. 2. 14. {2} from that time,<BR>since then, श्वासो दीर्घस्तदवधि मुखे<BR>पांडिमा Bv. 2. 62.<BR>--अवस्थ a. so<BR>circumstanced.<BR>--एकाचित्त a. having<BR>the mind solely fixed on that.<BR>--कर<BR>a. serving, obeying as servant.<BR>--कालः<BR>{1} the current moment, present time.<BR>{2} that time. ˚धी a. having presence<BR>of mind.<BR>--कालं ind. {1} instantly,<BR>immediately. {2} at that time, at a<BR>certain time.<BR>--क्षणः {1} present, time be<BR>ing present or current moment;<BR>R. 1. 51. {2} the same moment. {3} a measure<BR>of time.<BR>--क्षणं, --क्षणात् ind.<BR>immediately, directly, instantly; R. 3. 14;<BR>Śi. 9. 5; Y. 2. 14; Amaru. 83.<BR>--क्रिय a.<BR>working without wages.<BR>--गत a. gone<BR>or directed to that, intent on that,<BR>devoted to that, belonging to that.<BR>--(तः) the continued multiplication<BR>of four or more like quantities.<BR>--गुण<BR>a. possessing those qualities.<BR>--(णः)<BR>{1} the quality or virtue of anything.<BR>{2} a figure of speech (in Rhet.);<BR>स्वमुत्सृज्य गुणं योगादत्युज्ज्वलगुणस्य<BR>यत् । वस्तु तद्गुणतामोति भण्यते स तु तद्गुणः<BR>K. P. 10; see Chandr. 5. 141.<BR>˚संविज्ञानः a term applied to those<BR>Bahuvrīhi compounds in which the<BR>qualities denoted by the name are<BR>perceived along with the thing<BR>itself; as लंबकर्ण; cf. अतद्गुणसंविज्ञान also<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-a" target="_blank">Page0528-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--ज a. immediate, instantaneous.<BR>--ज्ञः a knowing or intelligent man,<BR>wise man, philosopher.<BR>--तृतीय a.<BR>doing that for the third time.<BR>--धन<BR>a. miserly, niggardly.<BR>--पदार्थः the<BR>Supreme Being.<BR>--पर a. {1}<BR>following that, coming after that, inferior.<BR>{2} having that as the highest<BR>object, closely intent on, exclusively<BR>devoted to, eagerly engaged in<BR>(usually in comp.); सम्राट्<BR>समाराधनतत्परोऽभूत् R. 2. 5; 1. 66; Me. 10;<BR>Y. 1. 83; Ms. 3. 262. {3} diligent.<BR>--(रः) the thirtieth part of a<BR>twinkling of the eye. ˚ता, ˚त्वं {1}<BR>intentness, entire devotion or addiction<BR>to a thing. {2} inferiority.<BR>--परायण<BR>a. solely devoted or attached to<BR>anything.<BR>--पुरुषः {1} the original or<BR>Supreme Spirit. {2} N. of a class<BR>of compounds in which the first<BR>member determines the sense of<BR>the other member, or in which the<BR>last member is defined or qualified by<BR>the first, without losing its original<BR>independence; as तत्पुरुषः; तत्पुरुष<BR>कर्मधारय येनाहं स्यां बहुव्रीहिः Udb.<BR>--पूर्व<BR>a. {1} happening or occurring for the<BR>first time; अकारि तत्पूर्वनिबद्धया तया<BR>Ku. 5. 10, 7. 30; R. 2. 42,<BR>14. 38. {2} prior, former.<BR>--प्रथम a.<BR>doing that for the first time;<BR>Ku. 5. 66.<BR>--फल a. having that as a<BR>fruit or result.<BR>--(लः) {1} the white<BR>water-lily. {2} a kind of perfume.<BR>--बलः a kind of arrow.<BR>--भावः<BR>becoming that.<BR>--मात्रं {1} merely that,<BR>only a trifle, a very small quantity.<BR>{2} (in phil.) a subtle and primary<BR>element (such as शब्द, रस, स्पर्श, रूप<BR>and गंध).<BR>--मात्रिक a. consisting of<BR>rudimentary atoms.<BR>--राजः an affix added<BR>to some proper names to form from<BR>them the names of the ‘king’ or ‘chief’;<BR>as from अंग is formed आंग ‘king of<BR>the Aṅgas' by the affix अण्.<BR>--वाचक a.<BR>denoting or signifying that<BR>--विद् a. {1}<BR>knowing that. {2} knowing the truth.<BR>--विध a. of that kind or sort;<BR>R. 2. 22; Ku. 5. 73; Ms. 2. 112.<BR>--स्थ a.<BR>being on or in that, connected with<BR>it.<BR>--(स्थः) a particular mode of<BR>multiplication.<BR>--हित a. good for that<BR>--(तः) {1} an affix added to primary<BR>bases to form derivative or<BR>secondary bases from them {2} a noun<BR>formed by a Taddhita affix, a derivative<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-b" target="_blank">Page0528-b+ 56</a>]<BR>noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0527-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदा
तदा ind.<BR>1 Then, at that time.<BR>--2 Then, in that case; (corr. of यदा).<BR>Bg. 2. 52-53; Ms. 1. 52, 54-56;<BR>यदा यदा-तदा तदा ‘whenever’;<BR>तदाप्रभृति ‘since then,’ ‘thenceforward;’<BR>Ku. 1. 53.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुख a. begun,<BR>commenced.<BR>--(खं) beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदात्वं|तदात्व
तदात्वं The time being, present<BR>time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदानीं
तदानीं ind. Then, at that time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदानींतन
तदानींतन a. Belonging to that<BR>time, contemporary of that time;<BR>एषोस्मि<BR>कार्यवशादायोध्यिकस्तदानींतनश्चसंवृत्तः U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तदीय
तदीय a. Belonging to that, his,<BR>hers, its, theirs; R. 1. 81, 2. 28;<BR>3. 8, 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तद्वत्|तद्वन्त्
तद्वत् a. Containing or possessed<BR>of that; as in तद्वानपोहः K. P. 2. --ind.<BR>1 Like that, in that manner.<BR>--2<BR>Equally, in like manner, so also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मय
तन्मय a. (यी f.)<BR>1 Made up of<BR>that.<BR>--2 Wholly absorbed in that;<BR>Māl. 1. 41; Ś. 6. 21; M. 2. 9.<BR>--3<BR>Identical with, or become one with<BR>that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्
तन् {vI.v} {c8c} U. (तनोति, तनुते, ततान,<BR>तेने, अत-ता-नीत्, तनितुं, तत; pass. तन्यते or<BR>तायते; desid. तितंसति, तितांसति,<BR>तितनिषति)<BR>1 To stretch, extend, lengthen,<BR>lengthen out; वाह्वोः सकरयोस्ततयोः<BR>Ak.<BR>--2 To spread, shed, diffuse;<BR>Bk. 2. 3, 10. 32, 15. 91; Ku. 2. 33.<BR>--3 To cover, fill; स तमीं तमोभिरभिगम्य<BR>ततां Śi. 9. 23; Ki. 5. 11.<BR>--4 To<BR>cause, produce, form, give, grant,<BR>bestow; त्वयि विमुखे मयि सपदि<BR>सुधानिधिरपि तनुते तनुदाहं Gīt. 4; पितुर्मुदं<BR>तेन ततान सोऽर्भकः R. 3. 25; 7. 7;<BR>U. 3. 39; Māl. 9. 43; यो दुर्जनं वशयितुं तनुते<BR>मनीषां Bv. 1. 95, 10.<BR>--5 To perform,<BR>do, accomplish (as a sacrifice); इति<BR>क्षितीशो नवतिं नवाधिकां महाक्रतूनां<BR>महनीयशासनः । समारुरुक्षुर्दिवमायुषः क्षये<BR>ततान सोपानपरंपरामिव ॥ R. 3. 69;<BR>Ms. 4. 205.<BR>--6 To compose, write (as a<BR>work &c.); as in नाम्नां मालां तनोम्यहं<BR>or तनुते टीकां.<BR>--7 To stretch or bend<BR>(as a bow).<BR>--8 To spin out, weave.<BR>--9 To propagate, or be propagated.<BR>--10 To continue, last.<BR>--11 To<BR>protract, prolong, augment.<BR>--12 To<BR>emboss.<BR>--13 To prepare (a way for).<BR>--14 To direct one's way towards. [cf.<BR>L. tendo]. {vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (तनति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">Page0528-c+ 57</a>]<BR>तानयति-ते)<BR>1 To confide, trust, place<BR>confidence in.<BR>--2 To help, assist,<BR>aid.<BR>--3 To pain or afflict with<BR>disease.<BR>--4 To be harmless.<BR>--5 To<BR>sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तत|ततं|ततः
तत p. p. [तन्-क्त]<BR>1 Extended,<BR>spread; Śi. 9. 23, 6. 50; Ki. 5. 11.<BR>--2 Spreading or reaching over,<BR>extending to.<BR>--3 Covered over,<BR>concealed.<BR>--4 Protracted, continued.<BR>--5<BR>Bent (as a bow).<BR>--6 Spreading wide<BR>&c.; see तन्.<BR>--तः Ved.<BR>1 A father.<BR>--2 Wind, air.<BR>--3 Extent.<BR>--4<BR>Offspring, a child (n. also).<BR>--5 A son.<BR>--तं Any stringed musical<BR>instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ततिः|तति
ततिः f. [तन् क्तिन्]<BR>1 A series, row,<BR>line.<BR>--2 A troop, group, multitude;<BR>विस्रब्धं क्रियतां वराहततिभिमुर्स्ताक्षतिः<BR>पल्वले Ś. 2. 6; बलाहकततीः<BR>Śi. 4. 54; 1. 5.<BR>--3 A sacrificial act, a cere.<BR>mony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्
तन् f. Ved.<BR>1 Continuation,<BR>diffusion.<BR>--2 Offspring, posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनः|तन
तनः Ved. A descendant.<BR>--ना --नं<BR>Offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयः|तनय
तनयः [तनोति कुलं, तन्-कयन्]<BR>1 A<BR>son.<BR>--2 A male descendant.<BR>--3 (In<BR>astrol.) N. of the fifth lunar<BR>mansion.<BR>--या A daughter; गिरि˚,<BR>कलिंद˚ &c.<BR>--यौ (dual) A son and<BR>a daughter.<BR>--यं Posterity, family,<BR>offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनयित्नु
तनयित्नु a. Ved. Roaring,<BR>thundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनस्
तनस् m. Ved. Offspring, posterity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिका
तनिका A rope for fastening<BR>anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिमन्
तनिमन् m. [तनु-इमनिच्] Thinness,<BR>slenderness, minuteness &c. --n.<BR>The liver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनिष्ठ|तनिष्ठः
तनिष्ठ a.<BR>1 Thinnest; least.<BR>--2 Very<BR>minute, or delicate (superl. of तनु<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनीयस्
तनीयस् a. Thinner, more minute,<BR>very thin (compar. of तनु q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनु|तनुः
तनु a. (नु, न्वी f.) [तन्-उन्]<BR>1<BR>Thin, lean, emaciated<BR>--2 Delicate,<BR>slender, slim (as a limbs, as a mark<BR>of beauty); R. 6. 32; cf. तन्वंगी.<BR>--3 Fine, delicate (as cloth);<BR>Rs. 1. 7.<BR>--4 Small, little, tiny, scanty, few,<BR>limited; तनुवाग्विभवोऽपि सन् R. 1. 9,<BR>3. 2; तनुत्यागो बहुग्रहः H. 2. 91<BR>‘giving little’ &c.<BR>--5 Trifling,<BR>unimportant, little; Amaru. 27.<BR>--6 Shallow<BR>(as a river). --f.<BR>1 The body, the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-a" target="_blank">Page0529-a+ 57</a>]<BR>person.<BR>--2 Outward form,<BR>manifestation: प्रत्यक्षभिः<BR>प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः Ś. 1. 1;<BR>M. 1. 1.<BR>--3 Nature, the form or<BR>character of anything.<BR>--4 Skin. [cf. L.<BR>tenuis, Eng. thin.].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग<BR>a. having slender limbs, delicate.<BR>--(गी) a delicate woman.<BR>--ऊनः the<BR>wind.<BR>--कूपः a pore of the skin.<BR>--छद (द) a. protecting, clothing.<BR>--छदः an armour; R. 9. 51; 12. 86.<BR>--ज a. born from the body;<BR>Pt. 2. 80.<BR>--(जः) a son.<BR>--जा a<BR>daughter.<BR>--त्यज् a. {1} risking one's<BR>life. {2} giving up one's<BR>person, dying; R. 1. 8. {3} rash,<BR>desperate, fool-hardy.<BR>--त्याग a.<BR>spending little, sparing, niggardly.<BR>--त्रं,<BR>--त्राणं, an armour.<BR>--प्रकाश a. of dim<BR>lustre; R. 3. 2.<BR>--भवः a son.<BR>--(वा)<BR>a daughter.<BR>--भस्त्रा the nose.<BR>--भृत्<BR>m. any being furnished with a body,<BR>a living being; particularly a human<BR>being: कल्पं रिथतं तनुभृतां तनुभिस्ततः<BR>किं Bh. 3. 73.<BR>--बीजः the jujube.<BR>--मध्य a. having a slender waist.<BR>--रसः perspiration.<BR>--रुह् n.,<BR>--रुहं<BR>the hair of the body.<BR>--वात a<BR>kind of hell<BR>--वारं an armour<BR>--व्रणः<BR>a pimple.<BR>--संचारिणी a young<BR>woman, a girl ten years old<BR>--सरः<BR>perspiration.<BR>--ह्रदः the anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0528-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुक
तनुक a. Thin, small.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुता
तनुता Thinness, littleness, waning;<BR>Ku. 4. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुल|तनुलः
तनुल a. Spread, expanded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनुस्
तनुस्^1 n. The body.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: lost anusvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनू
तनू f. The body.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्भवः,<BR>--जः a son.<BR>--उद्भवा, --जा a daughter.<BR>--जनिः, जन्मन् a son.<BR>--तलं a measure<BR>of length equal to the arms<BR>extended, a fathom.<BR>--तापः fatigues or<BR>troubles of the body; U. 1. 23.<BR>--नपं<BR>clarified butter, ghee.<BR>--नपात् m. fire;<BR>तनूनपाद्धूमवितानमाधिजैः Śi. 1. 62; अध.<BR>कृतस्यापि तनूनपातो नाधः शिखा याति<BR>कदाचिदेव ॥ H. 2. 67. (--n.) ghee.<BR>--नप्तृ m. wind.<BR>--रुहं {1} the hair<BR>of the body (--m. also). {2} the<BR>wing of a bird, a feather.<BR>--(हः) a<BR>son.<BR>--थदः the anus, the rectum;<BR>cf. तनुथद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तनूकृ
तनूकृ {c8c} U. To make thin or fine,<BR>diminish, lessen; as in लज्जां तनूकृत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्वी
तन्वी A delicate or slender woman;<BR>इयमधिकमनोज्ञा वल्कलेनापि तन्वी<BR>Ś. 1. 20; तव तन्वि कुचावेतौ नियतं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">Page0529-b+ 57</a>]<BR>चक्रवर्तिनौ Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंतिः|तन्ति|तन्तिः
तंतिः f. [तन्-कर्मणि क्तिच्]<BR>1 A cord,<BR>line, string.<BR>--2 A row, series.<BR>--3<BR>Extension, expansion.<BR>--4 A cow.<BR>--5 A weaver.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पालः {1} a<BR>guardian of (the rows of) cows. {2}<BR>N. assumed by Sahadeva when<BR>living at the house of Virāṭa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंतुः|तन्तु|तंतु|तन्तुः
तंतुः [तन् तुन्]<BR>1 A thread, cord,<BR>wire, string, line; चिंतासंततितंतु<BR>Māl. 5. 10; Me. 70.<BR>--2 A cob-web;<BR>R. 16. 20.<BR>--3 A filament;<BR>बिसतंतुगुणस्य कारितं Ku. 4. 29.<BR>--4 An<BR>offspring, issue, race.<BR>--5 A shark.<BR>--6<BR>The Supreme Being.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काष्ठं<BR>a piece of wood or brush used by<BR>weavers for cleaning threads.<BR>--कीटः<BR>a silk-worm.<BR>--नागः a (large) shark.<BR>--निर्यार्सः the palmyra tree.<BR>--नाभः<BR>a spider.<BR>--पर्वत् n. the anniversary<BR>of the day of full-moon in the month<BR>of Śrāvaṇa when Kṛṣṇa was<BR>invested with the sacred thread.<BR>--भः<BR>{1} the mustard seed. {2} a calf.<BR>--वर्धनः ‘increasing the race’,<BR>N. of Viṣṇu, also of Śiva.<BR>--वाद्यं any stringed musical<BR>instrument.<BR>--वानं weaving.<BR>--वापः {1} a<BR>weaver. {2} a loom. {3} weaving.<BR>--वायः {1} a spider. {2} a weaver {3}<BR>weaving ˚दंडः a loom.<BR>--विग्रहा a<BR>plantain.<BR>--शाला a weaver's<BR>workshop.<BR>--संतत a. woven, sewn.<BR>--(त)<BR>wove cloth.<BR>--संततिः f.,<BR>--संतानः<BR>weaving.<BR>--सारः the betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंतुकः|तन्तुक|तंतुक|तन्तुकः
तंतुकः<BR>1 The mustard seed.<BR>--2 (At<BR>the end of comp.) A thread, rope.<BR>--की A vein or any tubular vessel<BR>of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंतुनः|तन्तुन|तन्तुनः
तंतुनः --णः A shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंतुणः|तन्तुण|तन्तुणः
तंतुनः --णः A shark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंतुरं|तन्तुर|तंतुर|तन्तुरं
तंतुरं --लं The fibrous root of a<BR>lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंतुलं|तन्तुल|तंतुल|तन्तुलं
तंतुरं --लं The fibrous root of a<BR>lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्र्|तन्त्र्
तंत्र् {c10c} U. (तंत्रयति--ते, तंत्रित)<BR>1 To<BR>rule, control, govern; प्रजाः प्रजाः<BR>स्वा इव तंत्रयित्वा Ś. 5. 5.<BR>--2 To<BR>perform or go through in order.<BR>--3 To<BR>maintain by discipline, keep in order.<BR>--4 (A.) To support, maintain (as<BR>a family).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्रं|तन्त्र|तंत्र|तन्त्रं
तंत्रं<BR>1 A loom.<BR>--2 A thread.<BR>--3<BR>The warp or threads extended<BR>lengthwise in a loom.<BR>--4 Posterity.<BR>--5<BR>An uninterrupted series<BR>--6 The<BR>regular order of ceremonies and rites,<BR>system, framework, ritual; कर्मणां<BR>युगपद्भावस्तंत्रं Kāty.<BR>--7 Main point.<BR>--8<BR>Principal doctrine, rule, theory<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">Page0529-c+ 57</a>]<BR>science; जितमनसिजतंत्रविचारं Gīt. 2.<BR>--9<BR>Subservience, dependence; as in<BR>स्वतंत्र, परतंत्रः दैवतंत्रं दुःखं Dk. 5.<BR>--10 A<BR>scientific work.<BR>--11 A chapter,<BR>section, as of a work; तंत्रैः<BR>पंचभिरेतच्चकार सुमनोहरं शास्त्रं Pt. 1.<BR>--12 A<BR>religious treatise teaching magical<BR>and mystical formularies for the<BR>worship of the deities or the<BR>attainment of superhuman power.<BR>--13 The cause of more than one<BR>effect.<BR>--14 A spell.<BR>--15 A chief remedy<BR>or charm.<BR>--16 A drug, medicament.<BR>--17 An oath, ordeal.<BR>--18 Raiment.<BR>--19<BR>The right way of doing anything.<BR>--20<BR>Royal retinue, train, court.<BR>--21 A<BR>realm, country, authority.<BR>--22 (a)<BR>Government, ruling,<BR>administration; लोकतंत्राधिकारः Ś. 5. (b)<BR>Arrangement or machinery of<BR>government; सर्वमेव तंत्रमाकुलीभूतं<BR>Mu. 1; 2. 1.<BR>--23 An army.<BR>--24 A heap,<BR>multitude.<BR>--25 A house.<BR>--26<BR>Decoration.<BR>--27 Wealth.<BR>--28<BR>Happiness.<BR>--29 Model.<BR>--30<BR>Supporting a family.<BR>--31 Providing for the<BR>security and prosperity of a<BR>kingdom.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काष्ठं = तंतुकाष्ठ q. v.<BR>--वापः, --पं {1} weaving. {2} a loom.<BR>--वायः {1} a spider. {2} a weaver.<BR>(तंत्रवापः also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्रकः|तन्त्रक|तंत्रक|तन्त्रकं|तन्त्रकः
तंत्रकः A new garment<BR>(unbleached cloth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्रणं|तन्त्रण|तंत्रण
तंत्रणं Maintenance of order,<BR>discipline, government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्रता|तन्त्रता
तंत्रता<BR>1 Arranging into a system.<BR>--2 Dependence, subjection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्रा|तन्त्रा
तंत्रा Sleepiness; cf. तंद्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्रायिन्|तन्त्रायिन्
तंत्रायिन् m. The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्रिन्|तन्त्रिन्
तंत्रिन् a.<BR>1 Having threads, made<BR>of threads.<BR>--2 Having chords or<BR>wires (as a lute).<BR>--3 Having a<BR>Tantra, or following one. --m.<BR>1<BR>A musician.<BR>--2 A soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्रिः|तन्त्रि|तंत्रि|तन्त्रिः
तंत्रिः, --त्री f.<BR>1 A string, cord;<BR>Ms. 4. 38.<BR>--2 A bow-string.<BR>--3 The<BR>wire of a lute; तंत्रीमार्द्रां<BR>नयनसलिलैः सारयित्वा कथंचित् Me. 86.<BR>--4<BR>A sinew.<BR>--5 A tail.<BR>--6 A young<BR>woman having peculiar qualities.<BR>--7 A lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंत्री|तन्त्री
तंत्रिः, --त्री f.<BR>1 A string, cord;<BR>Ms. 4. 38.<BR>--2 A bow-string.<BR>--3 The<BR>wire of a lute; तंत्रीमार्द्रां<BR>नयनसलिलैः सारयित्वा कथंचित् Me. 86.<BR>--4<BR>A sinew.<BR>--5 A tail.<BR>--6 A young<BR>woman having peculiar qualities.<BR>--7 A lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंद्र|तन्द्र
तंद्र a.<BR>1 Tired, fatigued.<BR>--2<BR>Lazy.<BR>--द्रं Ved. A series or row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंद्रा|तन्द्रा
तंद्रा<BR>1 Lassitude, weariness,<BR>fatigue, exhaustion.<BR>--2 Sleepiness,<BR>sluggishness; तंद्रालस्यविवर्जनं Y. 3. 158;<BR>Mv. 7. 42; H. 1. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0529-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंद्रालु|तन्द्रालु|तन्द्रालुः
तंद्रालु a.<BR>1 Tired, exhausted.<BR>--2<BR>Sleepy, slothful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंद्रिः|तन्द्रि|तंद्रि|तन्द्रिः
तंद्रिः, --द्री f.<BR>1 Sleepiness,<BR>drowsiness.<BR>--2 Exhaustion, fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंद्री|तन्द्री
तंद्रिः, --द्री f.<BR>1 Sleepiness,<BR>drowsiness.<BR>--2 Exhaustion, fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंद्रिका|तन्द्रिका
तंद्रिका Sloth, sleepiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंद्रित|तन्द्रित
तंद्रित a. Lazy; as in अतंद्रित<BR>‘unremitting’; Ku. 5. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंद्रिन्|तन्द्रिन्
तंद्रिन् a. Weary, lazy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्युतः
तन्युतः [तन्-युतच्]<BR>1 Wind.<BR>--2<BR>Night.<BR>--3 Roaring, thundering.<BR>--4<BR>A thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तन्मय
तन्मय See under तद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्
तप् {vI.v} {c1c} P. rarely Ā., {c4c} P. (तपति,<BR>तप्यति; तप्त)<BR>1 (Intransitively used)<BR>(a) To shine, blaze (as fire or sun);<BR>तमस्तपति घर्मांशौ कथमाविर्भविष्यति<BR>Ś. 5. 14; R. 5. 13; U. 6. 14; Bg. 9. 19.<BR>(b) To be hot or warm, give out<BR>heat. (c) To suffer pain; तपति न<BR>सा किसलयशयनेन Gīt. 7. (d) To<BR>mortify the body, undergo penance<BR>(with तपस्); अगणिततनूत पं तप्त्वा<BR>तपांसि भगीरथः U. 1. 23.<BR>--2<BR>(Transitively used) (a) To make hot,<BR>heat, warm; Bk. 9. 2; Bg. 11. 19.<BR>(b) To inflame, burn, consume<BR>by heat; तपति तनुगात्रि<BR>मदनस्त्वामनिशं मां पुनर्दहत्येव Ś. 3. 17; अंगैरनंगतप्तैः<BR>3. 7. (c) To hurt, injure, damage,<BR>spoil; यास्यन् सुतस्तप्यति मां समन्युं<BR>Bk. 1. 23; Ms. 7. 6. (d) To pain,<BR>distress. (e) To mortify the body.<BR>undergo penance (with तपस्)'<BR>--Pass. (तप्यते) (regarded by some<BR>as a root of the 4th conjugation)<BR>1 To be heated, suffer pain.<BR>--2 To<BR>undergo severe penance (oft. with<BR>तपस्) U. 2. 8. {vII.v} {c10c} U. or Caus.<BR>(तापयति-ते, तापित)<BR>1 To heat, make warm;<BR>गगनं तापितपायितासिलक्ष्मीं Śi. 20. 75; न<BR>हि तापयितुं शक्यं सागरांभस्तृणोल्कया<BR>H. 1. 86.<BR>--2 To torment, pain, distress;<BR>भृशं तापितः कंदर्पेण Gīt. 11; Bk. 8. 13.<BR>--WITH निस् {1} to heat. {2} to<BR>purify. {3} to burnish.<BR>--वि {1} to<BR>shine (Atm. like उत्तप् q. v.);<BR>रविर्वितपतेऽत्यर्थं Bk. 8. 14. {2} to warm,<BR>heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप|तपः
तप a. [तप्-अच्]<BR>1 Burning,<BR>warming, consuming by heat.<BR>--2<BR>Causing pain or trouble, distressing.<BR>--पः<BR>1 Heat, fire, warmth.<BR>--2 The<BR>sun.<BR>--3 The hot season; Śi. 1. 66.<BR>--4 Penance, religious austerities.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अत्ययः, --अंतः the<BR>end of the hot season and the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-b" target="_blank">Page0530-b+ 57</a>]<BR>beginning of the rainy season;<BR>रविपीतजला तपात्यये पुनरोघेन हि युज्यते<BR>नदी Ku. 4. 44; 5. 23; Ś. 3. 12.<BR>--आत्मक a. practising austerities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपती
तपती<BR>1 The river Tāptī.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a daughter of the sun, married<BR>to Saṃvaraṇa and mother of Kuru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपन|तपनः
तपन a. [तप्-ल्यु]<BR>1 Warming,<BR>heating, burning, shining &c.<BR>--2<BR>Causing distress, paining.<BR>--3 The<BR>sun; प्रतापात्तपनो यथा R. 4. 12;<BR>ललाटंतपस्तपति तपनः U. 6; Māl. 1.<BR>--4<BR>The hot season.<BR>--5 The sun-stone.<BR>--6<BR>N. of a hell.<BR>--7 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--8<BR>The Arka plant.<BR>--9 N. of Agastya.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Heat, burning.<BR>--2 Paining,<BR>grieving.<BR>--3 Mental agony, anguish.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुः, --करः, --दीधितिः {1} the<BR>sun. {2} a sun-beam.<BR>--आत्मजः, --तनयः<BR>an epithet (1) of Yama. (2) of Karṇa.<BR>(3) of Sugrīva.<BR>--आत्मजा, --तनया<BR>an epithet of the Yamunā and of the<BR>Godāvarī.<BR>--इष्टं copper.<BR>--उपलः,<BR>--मणिः the sun-stone.<BR>--छदः the<BR>sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनी
तपनी<BR>1 The river Godāvarī or the<BR>river Tāptī.<BR>--2 Heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपनीय|तपनीयं
तपनीय a.<BR>1 To be heated.<BR>--2 To<BR>be suffered or practised (as a<BR>penance).<BR>--यं Gold; especially gold<BR>purified with fire; तपनीयाशोकः<BR>M. 3; तपनीयोपानद्युगलमार्यः प्रसादीकरोतु<BR>Mv. 4; असंस्पृशंतौ तपनीयपीठं<BR>R. 18. 41. (Also तपनीयकं in this sense.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्
तपस् n. [तप्-असुन्]<BR>1 Warmth,<BR>heat, fire.<BR>--2 Pain, suffering.<BR>--3<BR>Penance, religious austerity,<BR>mortification; तपः किलेदं तदवाप्तिसाधनं<BR>Ku. 5. 64.<BR>--4 Meditation connected<BR>with the practice of personal<BR>selfdenial or bodily mortification.<BR>--5<BR>Moral virtue, merit.<BR>--6 Special duty<BR>or observance of any particular<BR>caste.<BR>--7 One of the seven worlds;<BR>i. e. the region above the world<BR>called जनस्.<BR>--8 The month of<BR>religious austerities.<BR>--9 A long period of<BR>time, Kalpa.<BR>--10 (In astr.) The<BR>ninth lunar mansion. --m.<BR>1 The<BR>month of Māgha; तपसि<BR>मंदगभस्तिरभीषुमान् Śi. 6. 63.<BR>--2 An epithet of<BR>Agni. --m., --n.<BR>1 The cold season;<BR>(शिशिर).<BR>--2 The winter (हेमंत).<BR>--3<BR>The hot season (ग्रीष्म).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुभावः the influence of religious<BR>penance.<BR>--अवटः the Brahmāvarta<BR>country.<BR>--कर a. undergoing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-c" target="_blank">Page0530-c+ 57</a>]<BR>penance; also तपस्कर.<BR>--क्लेशः the pain<BR>of religious austerity.<BR>--चरणं, --चर्या<BR>the practice of penance.<BR>--तक्षः an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>--धन a. {1} rich<BR>in religious penance. {2} pious,<BR>ascetic. {3} consisting in penance,<BR>--(नः) ‘rich in penance’, an ascetic,<BR>devotee; रम्यास्तपोधनानां क्रियाः<BR>Ś. 1. 13; शमप्रधानेषु तपोधनेषु 2. 7; 4. 1;<BR>Śi. 1. 23; R. 14. 19; Ms. 11. 242.<BR>--निधिः an eminently pious man,<BR>an ascetic; R. 1. 56.<BR>--निष्ठ a.<BR>performing penance.<BR>--प्रभावः, --बलं the<BR>power acquired by religious<BR>austerities; efficacy or potency of devotion.<BR>--भृत् a. ascetic, pious.<BR>--मूर्तिः {1}<BR>an ascetic. {2} the Supreme spirit.<BR>--राजः the moon.<BR>--राशिः an ascetic.<BR>--लोकः the region above the world<BR>called जनस्.<BR>--वनं a penance-grove,<BR>a sacred grove in which ascetics<BR>practise penance; कृतं त्वयोपवनं<BR>तपोवनमिति प्रेक्षे Ś. 1; R. 1. 90, 2. 18.<BR>--वासः a place of penance or religious<BR>austerities.<BR>--विशेषः excellence of<BR>devotion, pre-eminent religious<BR>austerities.<BR>--वृद्ध a. very ascetic or<BR>devout.<BR>--शील a. inclined to practise<BR>penance.<BR>--समाधिः the practice of<BR>penance or religious austerities;<BR>Ku. 3. 24; 5. 6, 18.<BR>--स्थली {1} a seat of<BR>religious austerity. {2} N. of<BR>Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपसः|तपस
तपसः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 The moon.<BR>--3 A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्य|तपस्यं|तपस्यः
तपस्य a. Produced by heat.<BR>--स्यः<BR>1 The month of Phālguna.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Arjuna.<BR>--स्या Religious<BR>austerity, penance; (also m. and n.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्यति
तपस्यति Den. P. To practise<BR>penance; सुरासुरगुरुः सोऽत्र<BR>सपत्नीकस्तपस्यति Ś. 7. 9, 12; R. 13. 41;<BR>15. 49, Bk. 18. 21; Ku. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्वत्|तपस्वन्त्
तपस्वत् a. Ved. {1} Burning, hot.<BR>{2} Ascetic, devout, pious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विता
तपस्विता<BR>1 Religious penance.<BR>--2<BR>Piety, devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपस्विन्
तपस्विन् a.<BR>1 Practising penance,<BR>devout.<BR>--2 Poor, miserable, helpless,<BR>pitiable; सा तपस्विनी निर्वृता भवतु<BR>Ś. 4; Māl. 3; N. 1. 135. --m.<BR>1 An<BR>ascetic; तपस्विसामान्यमवेक्षणीया<BR>R. 14. 67.<BR>--2 A mendicant, pauper.<BR>--3 An<BR>epithet of Nārada.<BR>--4 A sparrow.<BR>--नी<BR>1 A female ascetic.<BR>--2 A poor or<BR>wretched woman.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रः the<BR>sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0530-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपित|तपितं
तपित a. Heated, burnt &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपिष्णु
तपिष्णु a. Warming, heating,<BR>burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपु|तपुः
तपु a. Ved. Burning hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपुषी
तपुषी The heat of anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपुस्
तपुस् a. [तप्-उसि; cf. Uṇ. 2. 116]<BR>Burning hot. --m.<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 The<BR>sun.<BR>--3 An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तपोमय|तपोमयः
तपोमय a.<BR>1 Consisting in religious<BR>penance.<BR>--2 Practising penance,<BR>devout.<BR>--यः The Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तप्त|तप्तः
तप्त p. p. [तप्-क्त]<BR>1 Heated, burnt.<BR>--2 Red-hot, hot.<BR>--3 Melted, fused.<BR>--4<BR>Distressed, pained, afflicted.<BR>--5<BR>Practised (as penance).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कांचनं<BR>gold purified with fire.<BR>--कृच्छ्रं a kind<BR>of penance consisting in drinking<BR>hot water, milk and ghee for three<BR>days each, and inhaling hot air for<BR>three days; Ms. 11. 214; Y. 3. 318.<BR>--रूपं, --रूपकं purified silver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापः|ताप
तापः [तप् घञ्]<BR>1 Heat, glow;<BR>अर्कमयूखतापः Ś. 4. 10; M. 2. 13;<BR>Ms. 12. 76; Ku. 7. 84.<BR>--2<BR>Torment, pain, affliction, misery, agony;<BR>इतरतापशतानि तवेच्छया वितर तानि<BR>सहे चतुरानन Udb.; समस्तापः कामं<BR>मनसिजनिदाघप्रसरयोः Ś. 3. 9;<BR>Bh. 1. 16.<BR>--3 Sorrow, distress.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--त्रयं the three kinds of miseries<BR>which human beings have to suffer<BR>in this world; i. e. आध्यात्मिक,<BR>आधिदैविक and आधिभौतिक.<BR>--हर a. {1}<BR>removing heat, cooling. {2} consoling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापक|तापकः
तापक a. [तप्-ण्वुल्] Heating,<BR>burning, inflaming.<BR>--कः Fever, morbid<BR>heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापन|तापनः
तापन a. [तप्-णिच् भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Heating, inflaming.<BR>--2 Distressing.<BR>--नः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 The hot<BR>season.<BR>--3 The sun-stone.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>one of the arrows of Cupid.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Burning.<BR>--2 Distressing.<BR>--3<BR>Chastising.<BR>--4 A division of hell.<BR>--5<BR>Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापनीय
तापनीय a. Golden.<BR>--यं Gold of<BR>the weight of a निष्क.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापयान
तापयान a. Warming, burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापित
तापित p. p.<BR>1 Warmed Heated.<BR>--2 Distressed, pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिन्
तापिन् a.<BR>1 Suffering from a<BR>disease (moral or physical.).<BR>--2<BR>Heating.<BR>--3 Hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप्यं|ताप्य
ताप्यं Sulphuret of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम्
तम् {c4c} P. (ताम्यति, तांत)<BR>1 To choke,<BR>be suffocated.<BR>--2 To be exhausted or<BR>fatigued; ललितशिरीषपुष्पहननैरपि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-b" target="_blank">Page0531-b+ 57</a>]<BR>ताम्यति यत् Māl. 5. 31.<BR>--3 To be<BR>distressed (in body or mind), be uneasy<BR>or pained, pine, waste away;<BR>प्रविशति मुहुः कुंजं गुंजन्मुहुर्बहु ताम्यति Gīt. 5;<BR>गाढोत्कंठा ललितलुलितैरंगकैस्ताम्यतीति<BR>Māl. 1. 15, 9. 33; तृष्णे मुधा ताम्यसि<BR>Mu. 3. 1; Amaru. 7.<BR>--4 To stop,<BR>become immovable.<BR>--5 To wish,<BR>desire. --Caus. (तमयति) To suffocate,<BR>choke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमं|तम|तमः
तमं<BR>1 Darkness.<BR>--2 The tip of the<BR>foot.<BR>--मः<BR>1 An epithet of Rāhu.<BR>--2<BR>The Tamāla tree.<BR>--3 Darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमकः|तमक
तमकः A kind of asthma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमत|तमतः
तमत a. [तम्-अतच् Uṇ. 3. 110]<BR>1<BR>Desirous, longing for.<BR>--2 Wished,<BR>desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमनं|तमन
तमनं Becoming suffocated or<BR>breathless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांत|तान्त|तान्तः
तांत p. p. [तम्-क्त]<BR>1 Wearied,<BR>languid, fatigued.<BR>--2 Troubled,<BR>afflicted.<BR>--3 Faded, withered; see तम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्
तमस् n. [तम्-असुन्]<BR>1 Darkness; किं<BR>वाऽभविष्यदरुणस्तमसां विभेत्ता तं<BR>चेत्सहस्रकिरणो धुरि नाकरिष्यत् Ś. 7. 4; V. 1. 7;<BR>Me. 37.<BR>--2 The gloom or darkness<BR>of hell; Ms. 4. 242.<BR>--3 Mental<BR>darkness, illusion, error;<BR>मुनिसुताप्रणयस्मृतिरोधिना मम च मुक्तमिदं तमसा<BR>मनः Ś. 6. 7.<BR>--4 (In Sān. phil.)<BR>Darkness or ignorance, as one of<BR>the three qualities or constituents<BR>of every thing in nature (the<BR>other two being सत्त्व and रजस्);<BR>Ku. 6. 60; Ms. 12. 24.<BR>--5 Grief, sorrow.<BR>--6 Sin. --m., --n.<BR>An epithet of Rāhu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपह a. removing darkness or<BR>ignorance, illumining, enlightening;<BR>Ki. 5. 22.<BR>--(हः) {1} the sun. {2} the<BR>moon. {3} fire. {4} a Buddha.<BR>--अरिः<BR>{1} the sun. {2} the moon. {3} fire.<BR>--कांडः --डं great or spreading<BR>darkness.<BR>--गुः an epithet of Rāhu.<BR>--गुणः see तमस् above (4).<BR>--घ्नः {1}<BR>the sun. {2} the moon. {3} fire. {4}<BR>Viṣṇu. {5} Śiva. {6} knowledge. {7}<BR>a Buddha.<BR>--ज्योतिस् m. a fire-fly.<BR>--ततिः spreading darkness.<BR>--नुद् m.<BR>{1} a shining body. {2} the sun. {3}<BR>the moon; R. 3. 33. {4} fire. {5} a<BR>lamp, light.<BR>--नुदः {1} the sun. {2} the<BR>moon. {3} the Supreme Being.<BR>--प्रभा<BR>a sort of hell.<BR>--प्रवेशः {1} groping<BR>in the dark. {2} mental gloom.<BR>--भिद्, --मणिः a fire-fly.<BR>--विकारः sickness,<BR>disease.<BR>--वृत a. {1} obscured,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">Page0531-c+ 55</a>]<BR>clouded. {2} affected with anger,<BR>fear &c.<BR>--हन्, --हर a. dispersing<BR>darkness. (--m.) {1} the sun. {2} the<BR>moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस|तमसं|तमसः
तमस a. Dark-coloured.<BR>--सः<BR>1<BR>Darkness.<BR>--2 A well.<BR>--सा N. of a<BR>river.<BR>--सं<BR>1 Darkness.<BR>--2 A city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्वत्|तमस्वन्त्
तमस्वत् a. Dark, gloomy.<BR>--ती<BR>1<BR>Night.<BR>--2 Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमस्विनी
तमस्विनी, तमा A night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमा
तमस्विनी, तमा A night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालः|तमाल|तमालं
तमालः<BR>1 N. of a tree with a<BR>very dark bark;<BR>तरुणतमालनीलबहलोन्नमदंबुधराः Māl. 9. 18; R. 13. 15,<BR>49; Gīt. 11.<BR>--2 A sectarial mark<BR>of sandal upon the forehead.<BR>--3 A<BR>sword, scimitar.<BR>--4 The bark of the<BR>bamboo.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रं {1} a sectarial<BR>mark upon the forehead. {2} a<BR>Tamāla leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालकः|तमालक|तमालकं
तमालकः<BR>1 The Tamāla tree.<BR>--2<BR>The bark of a bamboo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमालिनी
तमालिनी A place over-grown with<BR>Tamāla trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमि|तमिः
तमि, --मी f.<BR>1 Night, especially<BR>a dark night; स तमीं तमोभिरभिगम्य<BR>ततां Ś. 9. 23.<BR>--2 A swoon, faint.<BR>--3<BR>Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमी
तमि, --मी f.<BR>1 Night, especially<BR>a dark night; स तमीं तमोभिरभिगम्य<BR>ततां Ś. 9. 23.<BR>--2 A swoon, faint.<BR>--3<BR>Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्र|तमिस्रं|तमिस्रः
तमिस्र a. Dark.<BR>--स्रं<BR>1 Darkness;<BR>एतत्तमालदलनीलतमं तमिस्रं Gīt. 11;<BR>करचरणोरसि मणिगणभूषणकिरणविभिन्नतमि<BR>स्रं 2.; Ki. 5. 2.<BR>--2 Mental<BR>darkness, illusion.<BR>--3 Anger, wrath.<BR>--स्रः The dark half of the month.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पक्षः the dark fortnight<BR>(of a lunar month); R. 6. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमिस्रा
तमिस्रा<BR>1 A dark night; सूर्ये<BR>तपत्यावरणाय दृष्टेः कल्पेत लोकस्य कथं<BR>तमिस्रा R. 5. 13; Śi. 6. 70; Ki. 9. 18;<BR>Ku. 6. 43.<BR>--2 Extensive darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमोमय|तमोमयः
तमोमय a.<BR>1 Covered with<BR>darkness.<BR>--2 Ignorant.<BR>--यः N. of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तम|तमं|तमः
तम A Taddhita affix of the<BR>superlative degree applied to nouns,<BR>adjectives, and also to verbs and<BR>indeclinables in which latter case it<BR>is changed to तमाम्; अश्व˚ Pt. 5.<BR>‘the best horse’; सुहृत्तम Mu. 1; so<BR>पचतितमाम्. It is also added to<BR>pronouns in the sense of ‘one of many’;<BR>e. g. कतम, यतम, ततम &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमंगः|तमङ्ग|तमङ्गः
तमंगः A platform, a stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमंगकः|तमङ्गक|तमङ्गकः
तमंगकः The projecting roof of a<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तमरं|तमर
तमरं<BR>1 Tin.<BR>--2 Lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंबा|तम्बा
तंबा, तंबिका A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तंबिका
तंबा, तंबिका A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0531-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तय्
तय् {c1c} A. (तयते)<BR>1 To go, move;<BR>अध्युवास रथं तेये पुरात् Bk. 14. 75,<BR>108.<BR>--2 To guard, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तयः|तय
तयः Protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर|तरः
तर A Taddhita affix of the<BR>comparative degree, added to<BR>adjectives, nouns, and also to verbs and<BR>indeclinables in which latter case<BR>it is changed to तराम्. It is added,<BR>like तम, to pronouns in the sense<BR>of ‘one of two,’ e. g. कतर, ततर,<BR>यतर &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर|तरः
तर, तरण, तरणि, तरंड, तरि-री, तरीष<BR>&c. See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरण|तरणं|तरणः
तर, तरण, तरणि, तरंड, तरि-री, तरीष<BR>&c. See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरणि|तरणिः
तर, तरण, तरणि, तरंड, तरि-री, तरीष<BR>&c. See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरंड|तरण्ड|तरंडं|तरंडः|तरण्डः
तर, तरण, तरणि, तरंड, तरि-री, तरीष<BR>&c. See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरि|तरिः
तर, तरण, तरणि, तरंड, तरि-री, तरीष<BR>&c. See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरी
तर, तरण, तरणि, तरंड, तरि-री, तरीष<BR>&c. See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरीष|तरीषः
तर, तरण, तरणि, तरंड, तरि-री, तरीष<BR>&c. See under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरक्षः|तरक्ष
तरक्षः, --क्षुः A hyena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरक्षुः|तरक्षु
तरक्षः, --क्षुः A hyena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरंगः|तरङ्ग|तरंग|तरङ्गः
तरंगः [तॄ-अंगच्]<BR>1 A wave;<BR>U. 3. 47; Bh. 1. 81; R. 13. 63;<BR>Ś. 3. 7.<BR>--2 A section or part of a work<BR>(as of the कथासरित्सागर).<BR>--3 A leap,<BR>jump, gallop, jumping motion<BR>(as of a horse).<BR>--4 Cloth or clothes.<BR>--5 Waving, moving to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरंगित|तरङ्गित
तरंगित a. [तरंगः संजातोऽस्य, तार˚ इतच्]<BR>1 Wavy, tossing with waves; पीडा˚<BR>Māl. 9. 11.<BR>--2 Overflowing.<BR>--3<BR>Tremulous.<BR>--तं Waving;<BR>अपांगतरंगितानि बाणाः Gīt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरंगिन्|तरङ्गिन्
तरंगिन् a. Wavy, undulating,<BR>unsteady.<BR>--णी A river; as in राजतरंगि<BR>णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरंतः|तरन्त|तरंत|तरन्तः
तरंतः [तॄ-झच्]<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>--2 A<BR>hard shower.<BR>--3 A frog.<BR>--4 A demon<BR>or Rākṣasa.<BR>--5 A devotee.<BR>--ती A<BR>boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरल|तरलः
तरल a. [तॄ-अलच्]<BR>1 trembling,<BR>waving, shaking, tremulous;<BR>तारापतिस्तरलविद्युदिवाभ्रवृंदं R. 13. 76,<BR>घन इव तर बलाके Gīt. 5; Śi. 10. 40;<BR>U. 5. 11; Ś. 1. 26.<BR>--2 Fickle,<BR>unsteady, transient; वैरायिताररतरलाः<BR>स्वयं मत्सरिणः परे Śi. 2. 115;<BR>Amaru. 27.<BR>--3 Splendid, sparkling,<BR>glittering; Pt. 1. 190.<BR>--4 Liquid.<BR>--5<BR>Libidinous, wanton.<BR>--6 Hollow.<BR>--7 Extensive, wide.<BR>--लः<BR>1 The<BR>central gem of a necklace; मुक्तामयोऽ<BR>प्यतरलमध्यः Vās. 35; or<BR>हारांस्तारांरतरलगुटिकान् (Malli. considers this as<BR>an interpolation in Meghadūta).<BR>--2 A necklace.<BR>--3 A level surface.<BR>--4 Bottom, depth.<BR>--5 A diamond.<BR>--6 Iron.<BR>--7 Thorn-apple.<BR>--ला<BR>1<BR>Rice-gruel.<BR>--2 Spirituons liquor.<BR>--3<BR>A bee.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नयना, --लोचना a<BR>woman with rolling or tremulous<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">Page0532-b+ 55</a>]<BR>eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलयति
तरलयति Den. P. To cause to<BR>shake, to wave, move to and fro;<BR>Amaru. 87; U. 5. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलायते
तरलायते Den. A. To tremble,<BR>shake, move to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलायितः|तरलायित
तरलायितः A large wave, surf.<BR>--तः,<BR>तं Fickleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरलित|तरलितं
तरलित a. Shaking, tremulous,<BR>undulating; ˚तुंगतरंग Gīt. 11; ˚हारा 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरवारिः|तरवारि
तरवारिः A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्
तरस् a. [तॄ-करणादौ असुन्] Ved.<BR>Quick, energetic. --n.<BR>1 Speed,<BR>velocity.<BR>--2 Vigour, strength, energy;<BR>कैलासनाथं तरसा जिगीषुः R. 5. 28,<BR>11. 77; Śi. 9. 72.<BR>--3 A bank,<BR>a place of crossing.<BR>--4 A float,<BR>raft.<BR>--5 A monkey.<BR>--6 A disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरसं|तरस
तरसं Meat, flesh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरसानः|तरसान
तरसानः A boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्वत्|तरस्वन्त्
तरस्वत् a.<BR>1 Quick, swift.<BR>--2 Sick.<BR>--3 Energetic, strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरस्विन्
तरस्विन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Swift, quick.<BR>--2 Strong, powerful, courageous;<BR>mighty; R. 9. 23, 11. 89; 16. 77.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A courier, an express.<BR>--2<BR>A hero<BR>--3 Air, wind.<BR>--4 An<BR>epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरांधुः|तरान्धु|तरांधु|तरान्धुः
तरांधुः, तरालुः A large<BR>flat-bottomed boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरालुः|तरालु
तरांधुः, तरालुः A large<BR>flat-bottomed boat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिः|तरि
तरिः, तरीषः &c. See<BR>under तॄ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरीषः|तरीष
तरिः, तरीषः &c. See<BR>under तॄ<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरिता
तरिता<BR>1 The fore-finger.<BR>--2<BR>Garlic, or hemp.<BR>--3 A form of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरु|तरुः
तरु a. [तॄ-उन् Uṇ. 1. 7]<BR>1<BR>Protecting.<BR>--रुः {1} A tree;<BR>नवसंरोहणशिथिलस्तरुरिव सुकरः समुद्धर्तुं M. 1. 8.<BR>--2 Ved. Velocity.<BR>--3 A wooden<BR>ladle for taking up Soma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडः --डं, --षंडः --डं an assemblage or<BR>clump of trees.<BR>--जीवनं the root of<BR>a tree.<BR>--तलं the ground about the<BR>foot of a tree, foot of a tree.<BR>--नखः<BR>a thorn.<BR>--मृगः a monkey.<BR>--राग<BR>{1} a bud or blossom. {2} a young<BR>shoot, sprout.<BR>--राजः the Tāla tree.<BR>--राजन् m. ‘the king of trees’,<BR>N. of the tree Pārijātaka; also ˚वरः.<BR>--रुहा a parasitical plant.<BR>--विलासिनी the Nav mallikā creeper.<BR>--शायिन् m. a bird.<BR>--सारः camphor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुश
तरुश a. Full of or abounding in<BR>trees.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुटः|तरुट
तरुटः The root of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुण|तरुणं|तरुणः
तरुण a. [तॄ-उनन् Uṇ. 3. 54]<BR>1<BR>Young, youthful, juvenile, (as a<BR>man).<BR>--2 (a) Young, newly-born or<BR>produced, tender, soft; Bh. 3. 49.<BR>(b) Newly risen, not high in<BR>the sky (as the sun) Ku. 3. 54.<BR>--3<BR>New, fresh; तरुणं दधि Chāṇ. 64;<BR>तरुणं सर्षपशाकं नवौदनं पिच्छिलानि च<BR>दधीनि । अल्पव्ययेन सुंदरि ग्र म्यजनो<BR>मिष्टमश्नाति ॥ Chand. M. 1.<BR>--4<BR>Lively, vivid.<BR>--णः<BR>1 A young<BR>man, youth; Pt. 1. 11;<BR>Bv. 2. 62.<BR>--2 The castor-oil plant.<BR>--3<BR>Large cumin-seed.<BR>--णी A<BR>young or youthful woman; वृद्धस्य<BR>तरुणी विषं Chāṇ. 78.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Cartilage.<BR>--2 A sprout.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अस्थि n.<BR>cartilage.<BR>--ज्वरः fever lasting for a<BR>week.<BR>--दधि n. coagulated milk<BR>five days old.<BR>--पीतिका red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणकं|तरुणक
तरुणकं A sprout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणयति
तरुणयति Den. P. To heighten,<BR>spread; Māl. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणायते
तरुणायते Den. A. To remain<BR>young or fresh; तृष्णेका तरुणायते<BR>Pt. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुणिमन्
तरुणिमन् m. Youth, juvenility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुतृ
तरुतृ Ved.<BR>1 Overcoming,<BR>conquering.<BR>--2 Impelling, driving onward.<BR>--3 Protecting (तारक)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुत्र
तरुत्र a. Ved.<BR>1 Carrying across.<BR>--2 Conquering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुषः|तरुष
तरुषः A conqueror.<BR>--षा Victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुष्यति
तरुष्यति Den. P. To attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तरुस्
तरुस् n. Ved.<BR>1 Battle.<BR>--2<BR>Superiority.<BR>--3 Overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्
तर्क् {c10c} U. (तर्कयति-ते, तर्कित)<BR>1<BR>To suppose, guess, suspect, believe,<BR>conjecture, infer; त्वं तावत्कतमां<BR>तर्कयसि Ś. 6; Me. 96.<BR>--2 To reason,<BR>speculate about, reflect.<BR>--3 To<BR>consider or regard as (with two acc.).<BR>--4 To think of, intend, mean, have<BR>in view; (पातुं) त्वं<BR>चेदच्छरफटिकविशदं तर्कयेरितर्यगंभः Me. 51.<BR>--5 To<BR>ascertain.<BR>--6 To shine.<BR>--7 To<BR>speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कः|तर्क
तर्कः (तर्क्-भावे अच्)<BR>1 Supposition,<BR>conjecture, guess; प्रसन्नस्ते तर्कः V. 2.<BR>--2 Reasoning, speculation, discussion,<BR>abstract reasoning; कुतः<BR>पुनरस्मिन्नवधारिते आगमार्थे<BR>तर्कनिमित्तस्याक्षेपस्यावकाशः; इदानीं तर्कनिमित्त आक्षेपः<BR>परिह्रियते Ś. B.; तर्कोऽप्रतिष्ठः स्मृतयो<BR>विभिन्नाः Mb.; Ms. 12. 106.<BR>--3<BR>Doubt.<BR>--4 Logic, the science of logic;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">Page0533-a+ 56</a>]<BR>यत्काव्यं मधुवर्षि धर्षितपरास्तर्केषु<BR>यस्योक्तयः N. 22. 155; तर्कशास्त्रं,<BR>तर्कदीपिका<BR>--5 (In logic) Reduction to<BR>absurdity, a conclusion opposed to<BR>the premises, a<BR>reductio ad absurdum.<BR>--6 A system of doctrine<BR>founded on pure reasoning or free<BR>thinking, a philosophical system<BR>(particularly one of the six principal<BR>darśanas q. v.).<BR>--7 A name for the<BR>number ‘six’.<BR>--8 Supplying an<BR>ellipsis.<BR>--9 Cause, motive.<BR>--10 Wish,<BR>desire.<BR>--र्का Speculation, reasoning.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आभासः fallacious<BR>reasoning, fallacy in drawing<BR>conclusions.<BR>--विद्या logic.<BR>--शास्त्रं {1} logic.<BR>{2} a philosophical work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0532-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कक|तर्ककः
तर्कक a. [तंर्क्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 Inquiring,<BR>inquisitive.<BR>--कः {1} A suitor, an<BR>inquirer, a petitioner.<BR>--2 A logician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कणं|तर्कण
तर्कणं Reasoning, speculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कित
तर्कित p. p. Doubted, guessed,<BR>discussed, investigated, examined<BR>&c.; see तर्क्.<BR>--तं A supposition,<BR>conjecture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्किन्
तर्किन् a. [तर्क्-णिनि]<BR>1 Guessing.<BR>--2 Reasoning, versed in speculation.<BR>--m. A logician, reasoner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुकः|तर्कुक
तर्कुकः A suppliant, petitioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्कुः|तर्कु
तर्कुः m., f. A spindle, an iron pin<BR>upon which cotton is first drawn<BR>out; तर्कुः कर्तनसाधनं.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पिंडः,<BR>--पीठी, --पीठः, --पाठी a ball at the lower<BR>end of a spindle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्षुः|तर्क्षु
तर्क्षुः A hyena.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्क्ष्यः|तर्क्ष्य
तर्क्ष्यः Nitre, salt-petre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ज्
तर्ज् {c1c} P., {c10c} A. (often P. also)<BR>(तर्जति, तर्जयति-ते, तर्जित)<BR>1 To threaten,<BR>menace, terrify; सखीमंगुल्या<BR>तर्जयति Ś. 1;<BR>अहिताननिलोद्धूतैस्तर्जयान्निव केतुभिः R. 4. 28, 11. 78, 12. 41;<BR>Bk. 14. 80.<BR>--2 To scold, revile,<BR>censure, blame; Bk. 6. 3, 8. 101,<BR>17. 103.<BR>--3 To mock, deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जनं|तर्जन|तर्ज्जन|तर्ज्जनं
तर्जनं --ना [तर्ज्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Threatening, frightening.<BR>--2 Censuring;<BR>R. 19. 17; Ku. 6. 45.<BR>--3 Pointing at<BR>(in ridicule or contempt).<BR>--4<BR>Putting to shame, excelling, surpassing.<BR>--5 Anger.<BR>--नी The fore-finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जना
तर्जनं --ना [तर्ज्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Threatening, frightening.<BR>--2 Censuring;<BR>R. 19. 17; Ku. 6. 45.<BR>--3 Pointing at<BR>(in ridicule or contempt).<BR>--4<BR>Putting to shame, excelling, surpassing.<BR>--5 Anger.<BR>--नी The fore-finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्जित|तर्ज्जित
तर्जित p. p.<BR>1 Threatened.<BR>--2<BR>Blamed.<BR>--3 Disgraced.<BR>--तं Threatening,<BR>a menace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्णः|तर्ण
तर्णः, तर्णकः A calf; Śi. 12. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्णकः|तर्णक
तर्णः, तर्णकः A calf; Śi. 12. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्णिः|तार्णि
तार्णिः<BR>1 A raft.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्द्
तर्द् {c1c} P. (तर्दति)<BR>1 To injure,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">Page0533-b+ 54</a>]<BR>hurt.<BR>--2 To kill, cut through;<BR>Bk. 14. 108; see तृद् also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्दु
तर्दु-र्दू f. A wooden ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्दू
तर्दु-र्दू f. A wooden ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्द्मन्
तर्द्मन् n. Ved. A hole, an opening<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्पणं|तर्पण
तर्पणं See under तृप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्फितृ
तर्फितृ a. A killer, an injurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्ब्
तर्ब् {c1c} P. (तर्बति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्बटः|तर्बट|तर्ब्बट
तर्बटः A year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्मन्|तर्म्मन्
तर्मन् n. The top of the sacrificial<BR>post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षः|तर्ष
तर्षः, तर्षणं &c. See under तृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्षणं|तर्षण
तर्षः, तर्षणं &c. See under तृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्हणं|तर्हण
तर्हणं Ved. Injuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तर्हि
तर्हि ind. [तद्-र्हिल्]<BR>1 At that<BR>time, then.<BR>--2 In that case; यदा --तर्हि<BR>‘when-then’; यदि-तर्हि ‘if-then’;<BR>कथं तर्हि ‘how then’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्
तल् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (तलति, तालयति-ते)<BR>1 To be full or complete.<BR>--2 To fix,<BR>found, establish.<BR>--3 To be fixed.<BR>--4<BR>To accomplish a vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलः|तल|तलं
तलः --लं [तल्-अच्]<BR>1 A surface;<BR>भुवस्तलमिव व्योम कुर्वन् व्योमेव भूतलं<BR>R. 4. 29; sometimes used at the end<BR>of comp. without much alteration<BR>of meaning; महीतलं ‘surface of the<BR>earth’ i. e. earth itself; शुद्धे तू<BR>दर्पणतले मुलभावकाशा Ś. 7. 32; नभस्तलं<BR>&c.<BR>--2 The palm of the hand;<BR>R. 6. 18.<BR>--3 The sole of the foot.<BR>--4 The<BR>fore-arm.<BR>--5 A slap with the hand.<BR>--6 Lowness, inferiority of position.<BR>--7 A lower part, part underneath,<BR>base, foot, bottom; रेवारोधसि<BR>वेतसीतरुतले चेतः समुत्कंठते K. P. 1.<BR>--8<BR>(Hence) The ground under a tree<BR>or any other object, shelter afforded<BR>by anything; फणी मयूरस्य तले<BR>निषीदति Rs. 1. 13.<BR>--9 A hole, pit.<BR>--10 A<BR>span.<BR>--लः<BR>1 The hilt of a sword.<BR>--2 The palmyra tree.<BR>--3 N. of Śiva.<BR>--4 Pressing the strings of a lute with<BR>the left hand.<BR>--5 A division of hell.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A pond.<BR>--2 A forest, wood.<BR>--3<BR>Cause, origin, motive.<BR>--4 A leathern<BR>fence worn round the left arm (तला<BR>also in this sense).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगुलिः<BR>f. a toe.<BR>--अतलं the fourth of the<BR>seven divisions of hell.<BR>--ईक्षणः a hog.<BR>--उदर a. having a protuberant belly,<BR>pot-bellied.<BR>--उदा a river.<BR>--घातः a<BR>slap with the palm of the hand.<BR>--तालः {1} a kind of musical instrument.<BR>{2} clapping of the hands.<BR>--त्रं, --त्राणं,<BR>--वारणं a leathern glove of an archer.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">Page0533-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--प्रहारः a slap with the hand.<BR>--युद्धं a<BR>fight with the palms of the hands.<BR>--लोकः nether world (पाताल).<BR>--सारकं<BR>a martingale.<BR>--हृदयं the centre of<BR>the sole of the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलं|तल|तलः
तलः --लं [तल्-अच्]<BR>1 A surface;<BR>भुवस्तलमिव व्योम कुर्वन् व्योमेव भूतलं<BR>R. 4. 29; sometimes used at the end<BR>of comp. without much alteration<BR>of meaning; महीतलं ‘surface of the<BR>earth’ i. e. earth itself; शुद्धे तू<BR>दर्पणतले मुलभावकाशा Ś. 7. 32; नभस्तलं<BR>&c.<BR>--2 The palm of the hand;<BR>R. 6. 18.<BR>--3 The sole of the foot.<BR>--4 The<BR>fore-arm.<BR>--5 A slap with the hand.<BR>--6 Lowness, inferiority of position.<BR>--7 A lower part, part underneath,<BR>base, foot, bottom; रेवारोधसि<BR>वेतसीतरुतले चेतः समुत्कंठते K. P. 1.<BR>--8<BR>(Hence) The ground under a tree<BR>or any other object, shelter afforded<BR>by anything; फणी मयूरस्य तले<BR>निषीदति Rs. 1. 13.<BR>--9 A hole, pit.<BR>--10 A<BR>span.<BR>--लः<BR>1 The hilt of a sword.<BR>--2 The palmyra tree.<BR>--3 N. of Śiva.<BR>--4 Pressing the strings of a lute with<BR>the left hand.<BR>--5 A division of hell.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A pond.<BR>--2 A forest, wood.<BR>--3<BR>Cause, origin, motive.<BR>--4 A leathern<BR>fence worn round the left arm (तला<BR>also in this sense).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगुलिः<BR>f. a toe.<BR>--अतलं the fourth of the<BR>seven divisions of hell.<BR>--ईक्षणः a hog.<BR>--उदर a. having a protuberant belly,<BR>pot-bellied.<BR>--उदा a river.<BR>--घातः a<BR>slap with the palm of the hand.<BR>--तालः {1} a kind of musical instrument.<BR>{2} clapping of the hands.<BR>--त्रं, --त्राणं,<BR>--वारणं a leathern glove of an archer.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">Page0533-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--प्रहारः a slap with the hand.<BR>--युद्धं a<BR>fight with the palms of the hands.<BR>--लोकः nether world (पाताल).<BR>--सारकं<BR>a martingale.<BR>--हृदयं the centre of<BR>the sole of the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलकं|तलक|तलकः
तलकं A large pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलतः
तलतः ind. From the bottom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलाची
तलाची A mat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिका
तलिका A martingale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलित|तलितं
तलित a. Fixed, having a<BR>bottom.<BR>--तं Fried meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलवारणं|तलवारण
तलवारणं A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलित्
तलित् f. Lightning; cf. तडित्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिन|तलिनं|तलिनः
तलिन a. [तल्-इनन् Uṇ. 2. 53.]<BR>1<BR>{1} Thin, meagre, spare.<BR>--2 Small,<BR>little.<BR>--3 Clear, clean.<BR>--4 Situated<BR>under or beneath.<BR>--5 Weak.<BR>--6<BR>Separate.<BR>--नं A bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलिमं|तलिम
तलिमं<BR>1 Paved ground, a<BR>pavement.<BR>--2 A bed, cot, couch.<BR>--3<BR>An awning.<BR>--4 A large sword or<BR>knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तलुन|तलुनः
तलुन a. [तल्-उनन्]<BR>1 Young.<BR>--नः<BR>{1} A youth.<BR>--2 Wind, air.<BR>--नी<BR>A girl, young woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्कं|तल्क
तल्कं A forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पः|तल्प|तल्पं
तल्पः --ल्पं [तल्-पक् Uṇ. 3. 28]<BR>1 A<BR>couch, bed, sofa; सपदि<BR>विगतनिद्रस्तल्पमुज्झांचकार R. 5. 75 ‘left the<BR>bed’, ‘rose.’<BR>--2 (Fig.) A wife<BR>(as in गुरुतल्पग q. v.).<BR>--3 The<BR>seat of a carriage.<BR>--4 An upper<BR>story, a turret, tower;<BR>R. 16. 11.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीटः a bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पं|तल्प|तल्पः
तल्पः --ल्पं [तल्-पक् Uṇ. 3. 28]<BR>1 A<BR>couch, bed, sofa; सपदि<BR>विगतनिद्रस्तल्पमुज्झांचकार R. 5. 75 ‘left the<BR>bed’, ‘rose.’<BR>--2 (Fig.) A wife<BR>(as in गुरुतल्पग q. v.).<BR>--3 The<BR>seat of a carriage.<BR>--4 An upper<BR>story, a turret, tower;<BR>R. 16. 11.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीटः a bug.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पकः|तल्पक
तल्पकः One whose business it<BR>is to make or prepare beds (as a<BR>servant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पनं|तल्पन
तल्पनं<BR>1 An elephant's back.<BR>--2 The flesh on the back-bone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्पलं|तल्पल
तल्पलं The back-bone of an<BR>elephant, (पृष्ठवंश);<BR>सांद्रत्वक्कास्तल्पलाश्लिष्टकक्षाः Śi. 18. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लः|तल्ल|तल्लं
तल्लः A reservoir, tank.<BR>--ल्ली<BR>1<BR>A youthful woman.<BR>--2 N. of the<BR>wife of Varuṇa.<BR>--3 A boat.<BR>--ल्लं<BR>A pit, hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लजः|तल्लज
तल्लजः<BR>1 Excellence, superiority,<BR>happiness.<BR>--2 (At the end of<BR>comp.) Excellent (in this sense<BR>the word is always masculine,<BR>whatever be the gender of the<BR>first member of the compound)<BR>गोतल्लजः ‘an excellent cow’; so<BR>कुमारीतल्लजः ‘an excellent maiden’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्लिका
तल्लिका A key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0533-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तल्वं|तल्व
तल्वं Scent produced from the<BR>rubbing of fragrant substances.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवक्षीरं|तवक्षीर
तवक्षीरं<BR>1 Manna of bamboo.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of extract of wheat,<BR>rice &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवराजः|तवराज
तवराजः A sort of sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवस्
तवस् a. Ved.<BR>1 Old.<BR>--2 Strong,<BR>great. --n. Strength, power (बल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवस्य
तवस्य a. Increasing strength<BR>(as an oblation).<BR>--स्यं Strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविष|तविषः
तविष a. Ved.<BR>1 Old.<BR>--2 Strong,<BR>powerful, bold, courageous.<BR>--षः<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>--2 Heaven.<BR>--3<BR>Strength.<BR>--4 Business (व्यवसाय).<BR>--षी<BR>1 Power.<BR>--2 The earth.<BR>--3 A<BR>river.<BR>--4 N. of a daughter of<BR>Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तविष्या
तविष्या Violence, force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तवीषः|तवीष
तवीषः<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>--2 Heaven.<BR>--3 Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तव्य
तव्य A Kṛt affix by means of<BR>which potential passive participles<BR>are formed from roots, e. g. कर्तव्य<BR>from कृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्ट|तष्टः
तष्ट a.<BR>1 Hewn, cut, chiseled,<BR>split.<BR>--2 Fashioned; see तक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तष्टृ
तष्टृ m.<BR>1 A carpenter in general.<BR>--2 The architect of gods (विश्वकर्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्
तस् {c4c} P. (तस्यति)<BR>1 To fade<BR>away, become exhausted.<BR>--2 To<BR>throw down.<BR>--3 To wane, decay,<BR>perish.<BR>--4 To reject, cast. [cf.<BR>Eng. toss.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्करः|तस्कर
तस्करः<BR>1 A thief, robber;<BR>मासंचर मनःपांथ तत्रास्ते स्मरतस्करः<BR>Bh. 1. 86; Ms. 4. 135, 8. 67.<BR>--2 (At<BR>the end of comp.) Anything bad<BR>or contemptible.<BR>--3 The ear.<BR>--री<BR>A passionate woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्करता
तस्करता<BR>1 Theft.<BR>--2 Hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तस्थु
तस्थु a. Stationary, immovable,<BR>stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताक्षण्यः|ताक्षण्य
ताक्षण्यः, ताक्ष्णः The son of a<BR>carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताक्ष्णः|ताक्ष्ण
ताक्षण्यः, ताक्ष्णः The son of a<BR>carpenter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताच्छीलिकः|ताच्छीलिक
ताच्छीलिकः N. of an affix used<BR>to denote a particular inclination,<BR>tendency, or habit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताच्छील्यं|ताच्छील्य
ताच्छील्यं The act of being<BR>accustomed to that; ताच्छील्ये णिनिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताजत्
ताजत् a. Quick, speedy. --ind.<BR>Suddenly, abruptly; (opp. चिरं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटंकः|ताटङ्क|ताटंक|ताटङ्कः
ताटंकः An ornament for the<BR>ear, a large ear-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटस्थ्यं|ताटस्थ्य
ताटस्थ्यं<BR>1 Proximity.<BR>--2<BR>Indifference, disregard, neutrality; see<BR>तटस्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताड|ताडः
ताड, ताडनं &c. see under तड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडनं|ताडन
ताड, ताडनं &c. see under तड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडका
ता(ट)डका<BR>1 N. of a female<BR>fiend, daughter of Suketu, wife<BR>of Sunda and mother of Mārīca.<BR>[She was changed into a fiend by the<BR>sage Agastya whose devotions she had<BR>disturbed. She was killed by Rāma<BR>when she began to disturb the<BR>sacrificial rites of Viśvāmitra. Rāma was<BR>first unwilling to bend his bow<BR>against a woman, but the sage<BR>overcame his scruples, see R. 11. 20].<BR>--2 The large dark-green pumpkin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताटका
ता(ट)डका<BR>1 N. of a female<BR>fiend, daughter of Suketu, wife<BR>of Sunda and mother of Mārīca.<BR>[She was changed into a fiend by the<BR>sage Agastya whose devotions she had<BR>disturbed. She was killed by Rāma<BR>when she began to disturb the<BR>sacrificial rites of Viśvāmitra. Rāma was<BR>first unwilling to bend his bow<BR>against a woman, but the sage<BR>overcame his scruples, see R. 11. 20].<BR>--2 The large dark-green pumpkin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडकेयः|ताडकेय
ताडकेयः [ताडकाया अपत्यं ढक्] An<BR>epithet of the demon Mārīca, son<BR>of Tāḍakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडंकः|ताडङ्क|ताडंक|ताडङ्कः
ताडंकः, ताडपत्रं See ताटंक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडपत्रं|ताडपत्र
ताडंकः, ताडपत्रं See ताटंक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडाग
ताडाग a. (गी f.) Being in or<BR>coming from tanks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडिः|ताडि
ताडिः --डी f.<BR>1 A kind of palm.<BR>--2 A kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताडी
ताडिः --डी f.<BR>1 A kind of palm.<BR>--2 A kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांडवः|ताण्डव|तांडव|तांडवं|ताण्डवं|ताण्डवः
तांडवः --वं<BR>1 Dancing in general;<BR>मदतांडवोत्सवांते U. 3. 18; भ्रू˚ dance<BR>or playful movement of the<BR>eyebrows; 3. 19.<BR>--2 Particularly, the<BR>frantic or violent dance of Śiva;<BR>त्र्यंबकानंदि वस्तांडवं देवि भूयादभीष्ट्यै च<BR>हृष्ट्यै च नः Māl. 5. 23, 1. 1.<BR>--3<BR>The art of dancing.<BR>--4 A sort of<BR>grass.<BR>--5 (In prosody) A foot of<BR>three short syllables.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तालिकः an epithet of Nandin,<BR>the doorkeeper of Śiva.<BR>--प्रियः N.<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांडवं|ताण्डव|तांडव|ताण्डवं|तांडवः|ताण्डवः
तांडवः --वं<BR>1 Dancing in general;<BR>मदतांडवोत्सवांते U. 3. 18; भ्रू˚ dance<BR>or playful movement of the<BR>eyebrows; 3. 19.<BR>--2 Particularly, the<BR>frantic or violent dance of Śiva;<BR>त्र्यंबकानंदि वस्तांडवं देवि भूयादभीष्ट्यै च<BR>हृष्ट्यै च नः Māl. 5. 23, 1. 1.<BR>--3<BR>The art of dancing.<BR>--4 A sort of<BR>grass.<BR>--5 (In prosody) A foot of<BR>three short syllables.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तालिकः an epithet of Nandin,<BR>the doorkeeper of Śiva.<BR>--प्रियः N.<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांडवित|ताण्डवित
तांडवित a.<BR>1 Dancing, made to<BR>dance; Māl. 2.<BR>--2 Moving round<BR>in a wild dance; U. 5. 36.<BR>--3<BR>Fluttering.<BR>--4 Frowning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांडिः|ताण्डि|ताण्डिः
तांडिः The science of dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातः|तात
तातः [तन्-क्त दीर्घश्च Uṇ. 3. 90]<BR>1<BR>{1} A father; मृष्यंतु लवस्य बालिशतां<BR>तातपादाः U. 6; हा तातेति<BR>क्रंदितमाकर्ण्य विषण्णः R. 9. 75.<BR>--2 A term of<BR>affection, endearment or pity,<BR>applied to any person, but<BR>usually to inferiors or juniors, pupils,<BR>children &c.; तात चंद्रापीड K. 106;<BR>Māl. 6. 16; रक्षसा भक्षितस्तात तव<BR>तातो वनांतरे Mb.<BR>--3 A term of respect<BR>applied to elders or other venerable<BR>personages; हेपिता हि बहवो<BR>नरेश्वरास्तेन तात धनुषा धनुर्भृतः R. 11. 40;<BR>तस्मान्मुच्ये यथा तात संविधातुं तथार्हसि<BR>1. 72.<BR>--4 Any person for whom one<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">Page0534-c+ 55</a>]<BR>feels pity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गु a. {1} agreeable<BR>to a father. {2} paternal.<BR>--(गुः) a<BR>paternal uncle.<BR>--तुल्यः a paternal uncle,<BR>or the most respectable of a man's<BR>male relations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातनः|तातन
तातनः The Khañjana or wagtail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातल|तातलः
तातल a.<BR>1 Paternal.<BR>--2 Hot.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A disease.<BR>--2 An iron club<BR>or spike.<BR>--3 Cooking, maturing.<BR>--4<BR>Heat.<BR>--5 A relative who may be<BR>regarded as a father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तातिः|ताति
तातिः Offspring.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>Continuity, succession, as in अरिष्टताति or<BR>शिवताति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्कालिक|तात्कालिकः
तात्कालिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Simultaneous.<BR>--2 Immediate.<BR>--3 Relating<BR>to any particular time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्काल्यं|तात्काल्य
तात्काल्यं Simultaneity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्यं|तात्पर्य|तात्पर्य्य|तात्पर्य्यं
तात्पर्यं [तत्परस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Purport, meaning, scope, अत्रेदं तात्पर्यं &c.<BR>--2 Purport of propositions; K. P. 2.<BR>--3 Aim, object, intended reference to<BR>any object, purpose, intention (with<BR>loc.); इह यथार्थकथने तात्पर्यं<BR>P. II. 3. 43 Com.<BR>--4 The object or intention<BR>of the speaker (in using particular<BR>words in a sentence); वक्तुरिच्छा तु<BR>तात्पर्यं परिकीर्तितं Bhāṣā P. 84;<BR>तात्पर्यानुपपत्तितः 82.<BR>--5 Explanation.<BR>--6 Entire devotion to or absorption<BR>in any object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्पर्यक
तात्पर्यक a. Aiming at, meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तात्त्विक
तात्त्विक a. True, real, essential;<BR>किं चासीदमृतस्य भेदविगमः साचिस्मिते<BR>तात्त्विकः Bv. 2. 81; तात्त्विकः संबंधः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादर्थिक
तादर्थिक a. Intended for that.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादर्थ्यं|तादर्थ्य
तादर्थ्यं<BR>1 Identity of aim, object.<BR>--2 Relation to.<BR>--3 Sameness of<BR>meaning.<BR>--4 Purpose, aim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादात्म्यं|तादात्म्य
तादात्म्यं Sameness of nature,<BR>identity, unity;<BR>नयनयोस्तादात्म्यमंभोरुहां Bv. 2. 81;<BR>भगवत्यात्मनस्तादात्म्यं &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तादृक्ष|तादृक्षः
तादृक्ष a. (क्षी f.), तादृश् a.,<BR>तादृश a. (शी f.) Such-like, like him,<BR>her or it, like that; तादृग्गुणा<BR>Ms. 9. 22, 36; Amaru. 46; यादृशस्तादृशः<BR>any body whoever, common or<BR>ordinary man; उपदेशो न दातव्यो यादृशे<BR>तादृशे जने Pt. 1. 390.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानः|तान|तानं
तानः [तन्-घञ्]<BR>1 A thread, fibre.<BR>--2 (In music) A protracted tone,<BR>a key-note; यथा तानं विना रागः<BR>Bv. 1. 119; तानप्रदायित्वमिवोपगंतुं<BR>Ku. 1. 8. (the number of tānas is said to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">Page0535-a+ 54</a>]<BR>be 49).<BR>--3 A monotonous tone.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Expanse, extension.<BR>--2 An object<BR>of sense.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. {1}<BR>tuning the voice as a preparatory step<BR>to singing. {2} running over the<BR>notes to catch the key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0534-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानवं|तानव
तानवं Thinness, smallness;<BR>हास्यप्रभा तानवमाससाद Vikr. 1. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तानूरः|तानूर
तानूरः A whirlpool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांत|तान्त|तान्तः
तांत See under तम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांतव|तान्तव
तांतव a. (वी f.) [तंतोर्विकारः अञ्]<BR>1<BR>Made of threads.<BR>--वं {1} Spinning,<BR>weaving.<BR>--2 A web.<BR>--3 A woven<BR>cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांतुवायिः|तान्तुवायि|तान्तुवायिः
तांतुवायिः, तांतवाय्यः The son of a<BR>weaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांतवाय्यः
तांतुवायिः, तांतवाय्यः The son of a<BR>weaver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांत्रिक|तान्त्रिक|तान्त्रिकः
तांत्रिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Well-versed in any science or doctrine.<BR>--2<BR>Relating to the Tantras.<BR>--3 Taught<BR>or contained in them.<BR>--कः A<BR>follower of Tantra doctrines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताप|तापः
ताप, तापन, &c. See under तप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापन|तापनः
ताप, तापन, &c. See under तप्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापत्यः|तापत्य
तापत्यः An epithet of Kuru; also<BR>of Arjuna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस|तापसं|तापसः
तापस a. (सी f.)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>religious penance or to an ascetic.<BR>--2 Devout.<BR>--सः (सी f.) A hermit,<BR>devotee, an ascetic.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इष्टा,<BR>--प्रिया a grape.<BR>--तरुः, --द्रुमः the tree of<BR>ascetics, also called इंगुदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापस्यं|तापस्य
तापस्यं Asceticism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापिच्छः|तापिच्छ
तापिच्छः The Tamāla tree or its<BR>flower (n.);<BR>प्रफुल्लतापिच्छनिभैरभीषुभिः Śi. 1. 22;<BR>व्योम्नस्तापिच्छगुच्छावलिभिरिव तमोवल्लंरीभिर्व्रियंते Māl. 5. 6;<BR>(तापिंज used in the same sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापीजं|तापीज
तापीजं Sulphuret of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तापी
तापी<BR>1 N. of the river Tāptī,<BR>which joins the sea near Surat.<BR>--2<BR>The river Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामः|ताम
तामः [तम्-करणे घञ्]<BR>1 An<BR>object of terror.<BR>--2 A fault, defect.<BR>--3 Anxiety, distress.<BR>--4 Desire.<BR>--5<BR>Exhaustion, fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामरं|तामर
तामरं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 Clarified<BR>butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामरसं|तामरस
तामरसं [तामरे जले सस्ति सस् ड<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 The red lotus; Pt. 1. 94;<BR>R. 6. 37, 9. 12, 37; Amaru. 70.<BR>88.<BR>--2 Gold.<BR>--3 Copper.<BR>--सी A<BR>lotus-pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामस|तामसं|तामसः
तामस a. (सी f.) [तमोऽस्त्यस्य<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Dark, consisting of darkness;<BR>Māl. 9. 52; U. 5. 12.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-b" target="_blank">Page0535-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Affected by or relating to तमस् or the<BR>quality of darkness (the third of<BR>the three qualities of nature);<BR>Bg. 7. 12, 17. 2; M. 1. 1; Ms. 12. 33-34.<BR>--3 Ignorant.<BR>--4 Vicious.<BR>--सः<BR>1 A malignant person, an<BR>incendiary, a villain.<BR>--2 A snake.<BR>--3 An<BR>owl.<BR>--4 N. of a son of Rāhu.<BR>--सं<BR>Darkness.<BR>--सी<BR>1 Night, a dark<BR>night.<BR>--2 Sleep.<BR>--3 An epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामसिक|तामसिकं
तामसिक a. (की f.) [तमसा<BR>निर्वृत्तंठञ्]<BR>1 Dark.<BR>--2 Belonging to,<BR>derived from, or connected with तमस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तामिस्रः|तामिस्र|तामिस्रं
तामिस्रः<BR>1 A division of hell.<BR>--2<BR>The dark fortnight of a month.<BR>--3<BR>Hatred.<BR>--4 Anger.<BR>--5 A demon,<BR>Rākṣasa (going about in the dark).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांबूलं|ताम्बूल|तांबूल|ताम्बूलं
तांबूलं<BR>1 The areca-nut.<BR>--2 The<BR>leaf of piper-betel, which together<BR>with the areca-nut, catechu,<BR>chunam, and spices is usually chewed<BR>after meals; तांबूलभृतगल्लोऽयं भल्लं<BR>जल्पति मानुषः K. P. 7; रागो न<BR>स्खलितस्तवाधरपुटे तांबूलसंवर्धितः<BR>Ś. Til. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिकारः the office of<BR>carrying the betel-box; Pt. 1.<BR>--करंकः, --पेटिका a betel-box; (Mar.<BR>पानदान, पानपुडा).<BR>--दः, --धरः, --वाहकः<BR>a servant attached to men of rank<BR>to carry the betel-box and to<BR>provide them with तांबूल whenever<BR>necessary.<BR>--वल्ली the betel-plant;<BR>R. 6. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांबूलिकः|ताम्बूलिक|तांबूलिक|ताम्बूलिकः
तांबूलिकः A seller of betel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांबूलिन्|ताम्बूलिन्
तांबूलिन् a. Relating to betel. --m.<BR>A servant who prepares the<BR>Tāmbūla and gives it to his master<BR>when wanted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तांबूली
तांबूली The betel-plant; तांबूलीनां<BR>दलैस्तत्र रचितापानभूमयः R. 4. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्र|ताम्रं|ताम्रः
ताम्र a. [तम्-रक् दीर्घः Uṇ. 2. 16]<BR>1 Made of copper.<BR>--2 Of a<BR>coppery red colour, red; उदेति सविता<BR>ताम्रस्ताम्र एवास्तमेति च.<BR>--म्रः A kind<BR>of leprosy with red spots.<BR>--म्रं<BR>1<BR>Copper.<BR>--2 A dark or coppery red.<BR>--म्री A copper pot having a small<BR>hole at the bottom used in<BR>measuring time by placing it in a<BR>watervessel.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः {1} a crow. {2}<BR>the (Indian) cuckoo.<BR>--अर्धः<BR>bellmetal.<BR>--अश्मन् m. a kind of jewel<BR>(पद्मराग).<BR>--आभं red sandal (<BR>रक्तचंदन).<BR>--उपजीविन् m. a coppersmith.<BR>--ओष्ठः (forming ताम्रोष्ठ or ताम्रौष्ठ) a<BR>red or cherry lip; Ku. 1. 44.<BR>--कारः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-c" target="_blank">Page0535-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--कुट्टः a brazier, coppersmith.<BR>--कृमिः. a kind of red insect (इंद्रगोप).<BR>{2} the lady bird. {3} cochineal.<BR>--गर्भ<BR>sulphate of copper.<BR>--चूडः a cock.<BR>--त्रपुजं brass.<BR>--द्रुः the red<BR>sandalwood.<BR>--द्वीपः the island of Ceylon.<BR>--धातुः red chalk.<BR>--पट्टः, --पत्रं, a<BR>copper-plate on which grants of land<BR>were frequently inscribed;<BR>Y. 1. 319.<BR>--पर्णी N. of a river rising in<BR>Malaya, celebrated for its pearls;<BR>R. 4. 50.<BR>--पल्लवः the Aśoka tree.<BR>--फलकं a copper-plate.<BR>--मुख a.<BR>copper-faced.<BR>--(खः) a Frank or<BR>European.<BR>--वर्णी the blossom of<BR>sesamum.<BR>--लिप्तः N. of a country.<BR>(--प्ताः pl.) its people or rulers.<BR>--वृक्षः<BR>a species of sandal.<BR>--शिखिन् m. a<BR>cock.<BR>--सारकः a sort of Khadira.<BR>--(कं) red sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रकं|ताम्रक
ताम्रकं Copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रिक|ताम्रिकः
ताम्रिक a. (की f.) Made of copper,<BR>coppery.<BR>--कः A brazier,<BR>coppersmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रिमन्
ताम्रिमन् m. Redness, the colour of<BR>copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रयं
ताम्रयं Redness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताय्
ताय् {c1c} A. (तायते, तायित)<BR>1 To<BR>spread, extend, proceed in a<BR>continuous line.<BR>--2 To protect, preserve.<BR>--WITH वि to spread, create;<BR>Bk. 16. 105.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तायनं|तायन
तायनं<BR>1 Proceeding well,<BR>succeeding.<BR>--2 Increase, growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तायुः|तायु
तायुः Ved. A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार|तारं|तारः
तार a. [तॄ-णिच् भावे अच्]<BR>1 High,<BR>(as a note.)<BR>--2 Loud, shrill (as<BR>a sound); Māl. 5. 20.<BR>--3 Shining,<BR>radiant, clear;<BR>हारांस्तारांस्तरलगुटिकान् (regarded as an interpolation<BR>in Me. by Malli.); उरसि निहितस्तारो<BR>हारः Amaru. 28; R. 5. 52.<BR>--4 Good,<BR>excellent, well-flavoured.<BR>--5 Clear,<BR>clean.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The bank of a river.<BR>--2 The clearness of a pearl.<BR>--3 A<BR>beautiful or big pearl;<BR>हारममलतरतारमुरसि दधतं Gīt. 11.<BR>--4 An epithet of<BR>(1) Viṣṇu, (2) Śiva.<BR>--5 The<BR>mystical syllable ओम् (प्रणव).<BR>--6<BR>Protection.<BR>--7 A high tone or note.<BR>--8<BR>Crossing, passing over.<BR>--रः, --रं<BR>1 A<BR>star or planet; (said to be f. also).<BR>--2 The pupil of the eye; (said to be<BR>m. also).<BR>--3 A pearl (said to be f.<BR>also).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभ्रः camphor.<BR>--अरिः<BR>a pyritic ore of iron.<BR>--पतनं the<BR>falling of a star or meteor.<BR>--पुष्पः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">Page0536-a+ 58</a>]<BR>the Kunda or jasmine creeper.<BR>--वायुः loud-sounding wind, a<BR>whistling breeze.<BR>--शुद्धिकरं lead<BR>--स्वर a.<BR>having a loud or shrill sound.<BR>--हारः<BR>{1} a necklace of big or beautiful<BR>pearls. {2} a shining necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0535-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकः|तारक|तारकं
तारकः N. of a demon killed by<BR>Kārtikeya. [He was the son of<BR>Vajrānga and Varāṅgī. He propitiated the<BR>god Brahmadeva by means of his<BR>penance on the Pāriyātra mountain, and<BR>asked as a boon that he should not be<BR>killed by any one except a child seven days<BR>old. On the strength of this boon he<BR>began to oppress the gods who were<BR>obliged to go to Brahmā and ask his<BR>assistance in the destruction of the demon;<BR>(see Ku. 2). But they were told that<BR>the offspring of Śiva could alone<BR>vanquish him. Afterwards Kārtikeya was<BR>born, and he slew the demon on the<BR>seventh day of his birth].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः, --जित् m. an epithet of<BR>Kārtikeya. (For other senses, see under तॄ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारका
तारका<BR>1 A star.<BR>--2 A meteor,<BR>falling star.<BR>--3 The pupil of the eye;<BR>संदधे दृशमुदग्रतारकां R. 11. 69;<BR>Ch. P. 5; Bh. 1. 11.<BR>--4 N. of the wife of<BR>Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकिणी
तारकिणी A starry night, night<BR>during which stars are visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारकित|तारकितं
तारकित a. [तारकाः अस्य संजाताः इतच्]<BR>Starry, star-spangled, studded with<BR>stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारण|तारणः
तारण, तारित, तारिक &c. See<BR>under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारित
तारण, तारित, तारिक &c. See<BR>under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारिक|तारिकं
तारण, तारित, तारिक &c. See<BR>under तॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारतम्यं|तारतम्य
तारतम्यं [तरतमयोर्भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Gradation, proportion, relative<BR>importance, comparative value.<BR>--2<BR>Difference, distinction; निर्धनं<BR>निधनमेतयोर्द्वयोस्तारतम्याविधिमुक्तचेतसां । बोधनाय<BR>विधिना विनिर्मिता रेफ एव जयवैजयंतिका ॥<BR>Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारल|तारलः
तारल a. Unsteady.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A<BR>libidinous man, lecher, libertine.<BR>--2<BR>The companion of a dissolute man<BR>(विट).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारल्यं|तारल्य
तारल्यं<BR>1 Tremulousness.<BR>--2<BR>Libidinousness, dissoluteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारा
तारा<BR>1 A star or planet in<BR>general; हंसश्रेणीसु तारासु R. 4. 19;<BR>Bh. 1. 15.<BR>--2 A fixed star; R. 6. 22.<BR>--3<BR>The pupil of the eye, the eye-ball;<BR>कांतामंतः प्रमोदादभिसरति<BR>मदभ्रांततारश्चकोरः Māl. 9. 30; विस्मयस्मेरतारैः 1. 28,<BR>Ku. 3, 47.<BR>--4 A pearl.<BR>--5 (a) N. of the<BR>wife of Vāli, king of the monkeys,<BR>and mother of Aṅgada. She in vain<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">Page0536-b+ 55</a>]<BR>tried to dissuade her husband Vāli<BR>from fighting with Rāma and<BR>Sugrīva, and married Sugrīva after<BR>Vāli had been killed by Rāma. (b)<BR>N. of the wife of Bṛhaspati, the<BR>preceptor of the gods. She was on<BR>one occasion carried off by Soma<BR>(the moon) who refused to deliver<BR>her up to her husband when<BR>demanded. A fierce contest then<BR>ensued, and Brahmā had at last to compel<BR>Soma to restore her to her husband.<BR>Tārā gave birth to a son named<BR>Budha who became the ancestor of<BR>the Lunar race of kings. (c) N. of<BR>the wife of Hariścandra and mother<BR>of Rohidāsa; (also called Tārāmatī).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः {1} the moon;<BR>Ku. 7. 48; Bh. 1. 71. {2} Śiva. {3} Bṛhaspati.<BR>{4} Vāli. {5} Sugrīva.<BR>--आपीडः the<BR>moon.<BR>--आभः quicksilver.<BR>--पतिः {1}<BR>the moon; R. 13. 76. {2} Vāli.<BR>{3} Bṛhaspati. {4} Śiva.<BR>--पथः<BR>the atmosphere, firmament.<BR>--प्रमाणं<BR>sidereal measure, sidereal time.<BR>--भूषा the night.<BR>--मंडलं {1} the<BR>starry region, the zodiac. {2} the<BR>pupil of the eye.<BR>--मृगः the<BR>constellation मृगशिरस्.<BR>--मैत्रकं ‘the<BR>friendship of the stars’,<BR>spontaneous or unaccountable love; Māl. 7,<BR>Māl. 4; U. 5.<BR>--वर्षं falling stars.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारायणः|तारायण
तारायणः The holy fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारुण
तारुण a. Youthful, young.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारुण्यं|तारुण्य
तारुण्यं<BR>1 Youth, youthfulness.<BR>--2 Freshness (fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तारेयः|तारेय
तारेयः<BR>1 The planet Mercury.<BR>--2 An epithet of Aṅgada, son of<BR>Vāli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्कव|तार्क्कव
तार्कव a. (वी f.) Spun, woven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्किकः|तार्किक|तार्क्किक
तार्किकः [तर्कं वेत्ति तच्छास्त्रमधीते वा<BR>ठञ्]<BR>1 A dialectician, logician.<BR>--2 A philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्षः|तार्क्ष
तार्क्षः N. of the sage कश्यप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्क्ष्यः|तार्क्ष्य|तार्क्ष्यं
तार्क्ष्यः<BR>1 An epithet of Garuḍa;<BR>त्रस्तेन तार्क्ष्यात् किल कालियेन<BR>R. 6. 49.<BR>--2 N. of Garuḍa's elder brother<BR>Aruṇa.<BR>--3 A car.<BR>--4 A horse.<BR>--5<BR>A snake.<BR>--6 A bird in general.<BR>--7<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--8 N. of Śiva.<BR>--9<BR>Gold.<BR>--10 A kind of antidote.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ध्वजः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--नायकः an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्ण|तार्णः
तार्ण a. (र्णी f.) [तृणस्येदं शिवा˚<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Made of grass.<BR>--2 Levied<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-c" target="_blank">Page0536-c+ 57</a>]<BR>from grass (as a tax).<BR>--र्णः Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्तीय|तार्त्तीय
तार्तीय a. [तृतीय एव, स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>1<BR>The third.<BR>--2 Belonging to the<BR>third<BR>--यं A third part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तार्तीयीक|तार्त्तीयीक
तार्तीयीक a. The third;<BR>तार्तीयीकतया मितोऽयमगमत्तस्य प्रबंधे N. 3. 136;<BR>तार्तीयीकं पुरारेस्तदवतु मदनप्लोषणं<BR>लोचनं वः Māl. 1. v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालः|ताल|तालं
तालः [तल् एव अण्]<BR>1 The<BR>palmyra tree; Bh. 2. 90; R. 15. 23.<BR>--2 A banner formed of the palm.<BR>--3 Slapping or clapping the hands<BR>together, the noise made by it;<BR>Māl. 5. 23.<BR>--4 Flapping in general.<BR>--5 Flapping of the ears of an<BR>elephant.<BR>--6 Beating time (in music);<BR>करकिसलयतालैर्मुग्धया नर्त्यमानं<BR>U. 3. 10; Me. 79.<BR>--7 A musical<BR>instrument made of bell-metal; R. 9. 71.<BR>--8 The palm of the hand.<BR>--9 A<BR>lock, bolt.<BR>--10 The hilt of a sword.<BR>--11 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--12 (In<BR>prosody) A trochee.<BR>--13 A<BR>particular measure of height.<BR>--14 A<BR>short span.<BR>--लं<BR>1 The nut of the<BR>palmyra tree.<BR>--2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः {1} N. of Balarāma.<BR>{2} the palm-leaf used for writing.<BR>{3} a book. {4} a saw. {5} N. of<BR>Śiva. {6} a man endowed with<BR>every fortunate mark or sign.<BR>--अवचरः a dancer, an actor.<BR>--केतुः<BR>an epithet of Bhīṣma.<BR>--क्षीरकं,<BR>--गर्भः the exudation of the palm.<BR>--जटा,<BR>--प्रलंबः the fibres of the palm tree.<BR>--ध्वजः, --भृत् m. an epithet of<BR>Balarāma.<BR>--पत्रं {1} the palm-leaf used<BR>for writing. {2} a kind of<BR>ear-ornament (hollow cylinder of gold thrust<BR>through the lobe of the ear).<BR>--बद्ध,<BR>--शुद्ध a. measured, rhythmical,<BR>regulated by musical time.<BR>--मर्दलः a<BR>kind of musical instrument, a<BR>cymbal.<BR>--यंत्रं {1} a kind of<BR>surgical instrument. {2} a lock, a lock<BR>and key.<BR>--रेचनकः a dancer, an<BR>actor.<BR>--लक्षणः an epithet of<BR>Balarāma.<BR>--वनं a grove of trees.<BR>--वृंतं<BR>a fan; Ś. 3. 21, Ku. 2. 35; also<BR>तालवृंतकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताली
ताली<BR>1 A species of the<BR>mountainpalm, palm-tree.<BR>--2 The common<BR>toddy (tādī).<BR>--3 Fragrant earth.<BR>--4 A sort of key.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वनं a<BR>grove of palm trees; R. 4. 34, 6. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालकं|तालक
तालकं<BR>1 Yellow orpiment.<BR>--2<BR>A fragrant earth.<BR>--3 A bolt, latch.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">Page0537-a+ 54</a>]<BR>--की The vinous exudation of the<BR>palm, toddy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आभ a.<BR>green.<BR>--(भः) the green colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0536-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालंकः|तालङ्क|तालङ्कः
तालंकः A kind of ear-ornament,<BR>(= ताडंक q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालव्य|तालव्यं
तालव्य a. Relating to the palate,<BR>palatal.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्णः a palatal<BR>letter; i. e. इ, ई, च्, छ्, ज्, झ्, ञ् and य्.<BR>--स्वरः a palatal vowel; i. e. इ and ई.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिकः|तालिक
तालिकः [तालेन निर्वृत्तः ठक्]<BR>1 The<BR>open palm of the hand.<BR>--2<BR>Clapping the hands (तालिका also);<BR>यथैकेन न हस्तेन तालिका संप्रपद्यते<BR>Pt. 2. 128; उच्चाटनीयः<BR>करतालिकानां दानादिदानीं भवतीभिरेषः N. 3. 7.<BR>--3 A tie, seal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालितं|तालित
तालितं<BR>1 Coloured cloth.<BR>--2 Any<BR>musical instrument.<BR>--3 A string, tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिन्
तालिन् m. N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालिशः|तालिश
तालिशः A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालु
तालु n. [तरंत्यनेन वर्णाः तॄ-अण् रस्य<BR>लः; cf. Uṇ. 1. 5] The<BR>palate; तृषा महत्या परिशुष्कतालवः<BR>Rs. 1. 11.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जिह्वः {1} a<BR>crocodile. {2} the uvula.<BR>--पाकः an abscess<BR>in the palate.<BR>--पुप्पुटः an indolent<BR>swelling of the palate.<BR>--मूलं the<BR>root or back-part of the palate.<BR>--स्थान a. palatal.<BR>--(नं) the palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालुकं|तालुक
तालुकं<BR>1 The palate.<BR>--2 A disease<BR>of the palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालूरः|तालूर
तालूरः A whirlpool, an eddy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तालूषकं|तालूषक
तालूषकं The palate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावक
तावक a. (की f.), तावकीन a.<BR>Thy, thine; तपः क्व वत्से क्व च तावकं<BR>वपुः Ku. 5. 4; Ki. 3. 12;<BR>Bv. 1. 36, 96.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्|तावन्त्
तावत् a. (Correlative of यावत्<BR>q. v.)<BR>1 So much, that much, so<BR>many; ते तु यावंत एवाजौ तावांश्च ददृशे<BR>स तैः R. 12. 45; H. 4. 72;<BR>Ku. 2. 33.<BR>--2 So great, so large, of this<BR>extent; यावती संभवेद् वृत्तिस्तावतीं<BR>दातुमर्हसि Ms. 8. 155, 9. 249; Bg. 2. 46.<BR>--3 All (expressing totality);<BR>यावद्दत्तं तावद्भुक्तं G. M. --ind.<BR>1 First<BR>(before doing anything else); आर्ये<BR>इतस्तावदागम्यतां Ś. 1; आह्लादयस्व<BR>तावच्चंद्रकरश्चंद्रकांतमिव V. 5. 11;<BR>Me. 13.<BR>--2 On one's part, in the<BR>meanwhile; सखे स्थिरप्रतिबंधो भव ।<BR>अहं तावत् स्वामिनश्चित्तवृत्तिमनुवर्तिष्ये<BR>Ś. 2; R. 7. 32.<BR>--3 Just, now;<BR>गच्छ तावत्.<BR>--4 Indeed, (to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">Page0537-b+ 56</a>]<BR>emphasize an expression); त्वमेव<BR>तावत्प्रथमो राजद्रोही Mu. 1 ‘thou thyself’;<BR>त्वमेव तावत्परिचिंतय स्वयं Ku. 5. 67.<BR>--5 Truly, really (to express<BR>assent); दृढस्तावद्बंधः H. 1.<BR>--6 As for,<BR>with respect to; विग्रहस्तावदुपस्थितः<BR>H. 3; एवं कृते तव तावत्क्लेशं विना<BR>प्राणयात्रा भविष्यति Pt. 1.<BR>--7 Completely;<BR>तावत्प्रकीर्णाभिनवोपचारां R. 7. 4 (<BR>तावत्प्रकीर्ण = साकल्येन प्रसारित Malli.).<BR>--8<BR>Surprise (oh!, what a wonder).<BR>(For the senses of तावत् as a<BR>correlative of यावत्, see यावत्).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत्वस् ind. so many times.<BR>--मात्रं<BR>just so much.<BR>--वर्ष a. so many<BR>years old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावतिक
तावतिक, तावत्क a. Bought for<BR>so much, worth so much, of so much<BR>value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावत्क
तावतिक, तावत्क a. Bought for<BR>so much, worth so much, of so much<BR>value.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावद्धा
तावद्धा ind.<BR>1 In such a number.<BR>--2 So often.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तावरं|तावर
तावरं A bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताविषः|ताविष
ताविषः --षी<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>--2<BR>Heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताविषी
