तिक्
तिक् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (तेकते) To go or<BR>move. {vII.v} {c5c} P. (तिक्नोति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To attack, assail.<BR>--3 To wound.<BR>--4 To seek to injure or kill.<BR>--5 To<BR>challenge; also written तिग् or<BR>तिघ् in this sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्त|तिक्तं|तिक्तः
तिक्त a. [तिज्-बा˚कर्तरि क्त]<BR>1 Bitter,<BR>pungent (as one of the six flavours<BR>or Rasas); Me. 20.<BR>--2 Fragrant;<BR>Me. 33.<BR>--क्तः<BR>1 Bitter taste; (see<BR>under कटु).<BR>--2 The Kuṭaja tree.<BR>--3 Pungency.<BR>--4 Fragrance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गंधा mustard.<BR>--तंडुला long<BR>pepper.<BR>--धातुः bile.<BR>--फलः, --मरिचः<BR>the clearing-nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिक्तक|तिक्तकः
तिक्तक a. Bitter.<BR>--कः<BR>1 The<BR>Khadira tree.<BR>--2 N. of several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिग्म|तिग्मं
तिग्म a. [तिज्-मक् जस्य गः<BR>Uṇ. 1. 45]<BR>1 Sharp, pointed (as a<BR>weapon).<BR>--2 Violent.<BR>--3 Hot,<BR>scorching.<BR>--4 Pungent, acrid.<BR>--5 Fiery,<BR>passionate.<BR>--ग्मं<BR>1 Heat.<BR>--2<BR>Pungency.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुः {1} the sun;<BR>तिग्मांशुरस्तं गतः Gīt. 5. {2} fire. {3}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-c" target="_blank">Page0537-c+ 56</a>]<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--करः, --दीधितिः, --रश्मिः,<BR>--रुच् m. the sun.<BR>--तेजस् a. Ved. {1}<BR>sharp-pointed. {2} penetrating. {3}<BR>of a violent nature. {4} of<BR>resplendent lustre.<BR>--यातना acute or violent<BR>pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तिज्
तिज् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (Strictly desid. of<BR>तिज्) (तितिक्षते, तितिक्षित)<BR>1 To<BR>endure, bear.<BR>--2 To put up with, suffer<BR>patiently or with courage;<BR>तितिक्षमाणस्य परेण निंदां M. 1. 17; तांस्तितिक्षस्व<BR>भारत Bg. 2. 14; Mv. 2. 12; Ki. 13. 68;<BR>Ms. 6. 47. {vII.v} {c10c} U. or Caus.<BR>(तेजयति-ते, तेजित)<BR>1 To sharpen, whet;<BR>कुसुमचापमतेजयदंशुभिः R. 9. 39.<BR>--2<BR>To stir up, excite, instigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षा
तितिक्षा Endurance, patience,<BR>resignation, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0537-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

तितिक्षु|तितिक्षुः
