दांत, दांतिः See under दम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दांतिक|दान्तिक
दांतिक a. (की f.) Made of<BR>ivory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापन|दापनं
दापन, दापित See under दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दापित|दापितः
दापन, दापित See under दा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामन्
दामन् n. [दो-मनिन्]<BR>1 A string,<BR>thread, fillet, rope.<BR>--2 A chaplet, a<BR>garland in general; आद्ये बद्धा<BR>विरहदिवसे या शिखा दाम हित्वा Me. 92;<BR>कनकचंपकदामगौरीं Ch. P. 1;<BR>Śi. 4. 50.<BR>--3 A line, streak (as of<BR>lightning); विद्युद्दाम्ना हेमराजीव विंध्यं<BR>M. 3. 20; Me. 27.<BR>--4 A large bandage.<BR>--5 Ved. A gift.<BR>--6 A portion, share.<BR>--7 A girdle.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंचलं,<BR>--अंजनं a foot-rope for horses, &c.;<BR>Śi. 5. 61.<BR>--उदरः an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामनी
दामनी A foot-rope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामा
दामा A string, cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दामिनी
दामिनी Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दांपत्यं|दाम्पत्य|दांपत्य
दांपत्यं Matrimony, the<BR>matrimonial relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दांभिक|दाम्भिक|दाम्भिकः
दांभिक a. (की f.) [दंभेन चरति<BR>धर्मं-ठक्]<BR>1 Deceitful, hypocritical.<BR>--2 Proud, imperious.<BR>--3<BR>Ostentatious, sanctimonious.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-b" target="_blank">Page0563-b+ 56</a>]<BR>cheat.<BR>--2 A hypocrite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायः|दाय
दायः [दा भावे-घञ्]<BR>1 A gift,<BR>present, donation; रहसि रमते प्रीत्या दायं<BR>ददात्यनुवर्तते Māl. 3. 2; प्रीतिदायः<BR>Māl. 4; Ms. 8. 199.<BR>--2 A nuptial present<BR>(given to the bride or the<BR>bridegroom).<BR>--3 Share, portion,<BR>inheritance, patrimony; अनपत्यस्य पुत्रस्य<BR>माता दायमवाप्तुयात् Ms. 9. 217, 77,<BR>164, 203.<BR>--4 A part or share in<BR>general.<BR>--5 Delivering, handing over.<BR>--6 Dividing, distributing.<BR>--7 Loss,<BR>destruction.<BR>--8 Irony.<BR>--9 Site,<BR>place.<BR>--10 Alms given to a<BR>student at his initiation, &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपवर्तनं forfeiture of inheritance;<BR>Ms. 9. 79.<BR>--अर्ह a. claiming<BR>inheritance.<BR>--आदः [दायमादत्ते, आदा-क]<BR>{1} one entitled to a share of<BR>patrimony, an heir; पुमान्दायादोऽदायादा<BR>स्त्री Nir.; Y. 2. 118; Ms. 8. 160.<BR>{2} a son. {3} a relative, kinsman<BR>near or remote, a distant<BR>descendant. {4} a claimant or pretender in<BR>general; गवां गोषु वा दायादः Sk.<BR>--आदा, --दी {1} an heiress. {2} a<BR>daughter.<BR>--आद्यं {1} inheritance. {2}<BR>the state of being an inheritor.<BR>--कालः the time of the partition of an<BR>inheritance.<BR>--बंधुः {1} a partner in<BR>the inheritance. {2} a brother.<BR>--भागः<BR>division of property among heirs,<BR>partition (of inheritance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायक|दायकः
दायक a. (यिका f.) [दा-ण्वुल्]<BR>Giving, granting, bestowing, &c.<BR>(at the end of comp.); उत्तर˚, पिंड˚,<BR>&c.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An heir, inheritor.<BR>--2 A<BR>donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दायिन्
दायिन् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>1 Giving, granting.<BR>--2 Causing,<BR>producing; as in क्लेशदायिन् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारः|दार
दारः<BR>1 A rent, gap, cleft, hole.<BR>--2<BR>A ploughed field.<BR>--राः [दारयंति<BR>भ्रातॄन्) इति दाराः. cf. P. III. 3. 20 Vārt.]<BR>(m. pl.) A wife; एते वयममी<BR>दाराः कत्येयं कुलजीवितं Ku. 6. 63;<BR>दशरथदारानधिष्ठाय वसिष्ठः प्राप्तः U. 4;<BR>Pt. 1. 100; Ms. 1. 112; 2. 217;<BR>Ś. 4. 16, 5. 29.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधीन a.<BR>dependent on a wife.<BR>--उपसंग्रहः, --ग्रहः,<BR>--परिग्रहः, --ग्रहणं marriage; नवे<BR>दारपरिग्रहे U. 1. 19.<BR>--कर्मन् n.,<BR>--क्रिया<BR>marriage; R. 5. 40.<BR>--वलिभुज् m. a<BR>crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारक|दारकः
दारक a. (रिका f.) [दॄ-ण्वुल्]<BR>Breaking, tearing, splitting; दारिका<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">Page0563-c+ 56</a>]<BR>हृदयदारिका पितुः.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A boy, a son.<BR>--2 A child, infant.<BR>--3 Any young<BR>animal.<BR>--4 A village hog.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचार्यः a schoolmaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारणं|दारण
दारणं [दॄ-णिच् युच्]<BR>1 Splitting,<BR>tearing, rending, opening, cleaving.<BR>--2 The fruit of the clearing-nut<BR>plant.<BR>--णी N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिका
दारिका<BR>1 A daughter.<BR>--2 A<BR>harlot.<BR>--3 A rent, cleft.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दानं<BR>the gift of a daughter in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारव
दारव a. (वी f.) Wooden, made of<BR>wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिः|दारि
दारिः f. Tearing, cutting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारित|दारितः
दारित p. p. Torn, divided, split,<BR>rent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिन्
दारिन् m.<BR>1 A husband.<BR>--2 A<BR>polygamist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारी
दारी<BR>1 A cleft.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>disease.<BR>--3 A chap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारदः|दारद
दारदः<BR>1 Quicksilver.<BR>--2 The<BR>ocean.<BR>--दः, --दं Vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिद्र्यं|दारिद्र्य
दारिद्र्यं, दारिद्रं [दरिद्रस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>Poverty, indigence; दारिद्र्यदोषो<BR>गुणराशिनाशी Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारिद्रं|दारिद्र
दारिद्र्यं, दारिद्रं [दरिद्रस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>Poverty, indigence; दारिद्र्यदोषो<BR>गुणराशिनाशी Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारु|दारुः
दारु a. [दीर्यते दॄ-उण्]<BR>1 Tearing,<BR>rending.<BR>--2 Liberal.<BR>--3 Kind.<BR>--रुः<BR>1 A<BR>liberal or munificent man.<BR>--2 A<BR>donor.<BR>--3 An artist.<BR>--रु n. (said to be<BR>m. also)<BR>1 Wood, a piece of wood,<BR>timber.<BR>--2 A block.<BR>--3 A lever.<BR>--4<BR>A bolt.<BR>--5 The pine or Devadāru<BR>tree.<BR>--6 Ore.<BR>--7 Brass.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंडः the peacock.<BR>--आघाटः the<BR>wood-pecker.<BR>--कृत्यं wood-work;<BR>Pt. 1. 90.<BR>--गर्भा a wooden puppet.<BR>--जः a kind of drum.<BR>--पात्रं a<BR>wooden vessel, such as a trough.<BR>--पुत्रिका, --पुत्री a wooden doll.<BR>--मुख्याह्वया, मुख्याह्वा a lizard.<BR>--यंत्रं {1}<BR>a wooden puppet moved by strings.<BR>{2} any machinery of wood.<BR>--वधूः<BR>a wooden doll.<BR>--सारः sandal.<BR>--हस्तकः a wooden spoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुकः|दारुक|दारुकं
दारुकः<BR>1 The Devadāru tree.<BR>--2<BR>N. of Kṛṣṇa's charioteer; उत्कंधरं<BR>दारुक इत्युवाच Śi. 4. 18.<BR>--का<BR>1 A<BR>puppet.<BR>--2 A wooden figure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुण|दारुणः
दारुण a. [दॄ-णिच्-उनन् Uṇ. 3. 53]<BR>1<BR>{1} Hard, rough; U. 3. 34.<BR>--2 Harsh,<BR>cruel, ruthless, pitiless; मय्येव<BR>विस्मरणदारुणचित्तवृत्तौ Ś. 5. 23;<BR>पशुमारणकर्मदारुणः 6. 1; दारुणरसः ‘of cruel<BR>resolve or nature’ U. 5. 19;<BR>Ms. 8. 270.<BR>--3 Fierce, terrible, frightful;<BR>Ś. 6. 28.<BR>--4 Heavy, violent, intense,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-a" target="_blank">Page0564-a+ 53</a>]<BR>poignant, agonizing (grief, pain<BR>&c.); हृदयकुसुमशोषी दारुणो दीर्घशोकः<BR>U. 3. 5.<BR>--5 Sharp, severe (as<BR>words).<BR>--6 Atrocious, shocking.<BR>--णः<BR>1 The sentiment of horror<BR>(भयानक).<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--णं<BR>Severity, cruelty, horror, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0563-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दारुण्यं|दारुण्य
दारुण्यं<BR>1 Harshness.<BR>--2 Cruelty.<BR>--3 Dreadfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्ढ्यं|दार्ढ्य
दार्ढ्यं [दृढस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Hardness, tightness, firmness.<BR>--2<BR>Confirmation, corroboration.<BR>--3 Strength,<BR>energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्दुरः|दार्दुर|दार्दुरं|दार्द्दुर|दार्द्दुरं
दार्दुरः --रं<BR>1 A conch-shell the<BR>valve of which opens to the right.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--3 Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्दुरं|दार्दुर|दार्दुरः|दार्द्दुर|दार्द्दुरं
दार्दुरः --रं<BR>1 A conch-shell the<BR>valve of which opens to the right.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--3 Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्भ
दार्भ a. (र्भीं f.) Made of darbha<BR>grass; दार्भं मुंचत्युटजपटलं वीतनिद्रो<BR>मयूरः Ś. 4 v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दार्व|दार्वं
