दास् {c1c} U. {c5c} P. = दाश् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासः|दास
दासः<BR>1 A slave, servant in<BR>general; गृहकर्मदासाः Bh. 1. 1; गृह˚,<BR>कर्म˚ &c.<BR>--2 A fisherman.<BR>--3 A<BR>Śūdra, a man of the fourth caste.<BR>--4<BR>A knowing man, one who knows the<BR>universal spirit.<BR>--5 N. of Vṛtrāsura.<BR>--6 A demon.<BR>--7 A savage,<BR>barbarian (opp. आर्य).<BR>--8 A worthy<BR>recipient (दानपात्र).<BR>--9 A word added<BR>to the name of a Śūdra; cf. गुप्त.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुदासः ‘a slave of a<BR>slave’, the humblest of the<BR>servants; (sometimes used by the<BR>speaker as a mark of humility).<BR>--जनः a servant or slave;<BR>कमपराधलवं मयि पश्यसि त्यजसि मानिनि<BR>दासजनं यतः V. 4. 29; (दासस्यकुलं is<BR>used as a compound in the sense<BR>of ‘the mob or the common<BR>people’).<BR>--भावः servitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासिका
दासिका A female servant or<BR>slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासी
दासी<BR>1 A female servant or slave.<BR>--2 The wife of a fisherman.<BR>--3<BR>The wife of a Śūdra.<BR>--4 An altar.<BR>--5 A harlot.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुत्रः,<BR>--सुतः the son of a female slave.<BR>--श्रोत्रियः a Brāhmaṇa (knowing<BR>the Vedas) attached to a female<BR>slave.<BR>--सभं a collection of female<BR>slaves. (The gen. sing. दास्याः<BR>enters into some compounds, but<BR>loses its literal sense; e. g. दास्याःपुत्रः,<BR>--सुतः ‘a whore-son’, used as a<BR>term of abuse; दास्याःपुत्रैः<BR>शकुनिलुब्धकैः Ś. 2; but दास्याः सदृशी ‘like<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-c" target="_blank">Page0564-c+ 54</a>]<BR>a female slave’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेयः|दासेय
दासेयः The son of a female slave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेरः|दासेर
दासेरः, --रकः<BR>1 The son of a<BR>female slave.<BR>--2 A Śūdra.<BR>--3 A<BR>fisherman.<BR>--4 A camel; Śi. 12. 32,<BR>5. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दासेरकः|दासेरक
दासेरः, --रकः<BR>1 The son of a<BR>female slave.<BR>--2 A Śūdra.<BR>--3 A<BR>fisherman.<BR>--4 A camel; Śi. 12. 32,<BR>5. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्यं|दास्य
दास्यं Servitude, slavery,<BR>service, bondage; पतिकुले तव दास्यमपि<BR>क्षमं Ś. 5. 27; Ms. 8. 410.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दास्रं|दास्र
दास्रं The first of the 27 lunar<BR>mansions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0564-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

