धांधा Cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्यं|धान्य
धान्यं [धाने पोषणे साधु यत्]<BR>1 Graint<BR>corn, rice; (for the distinction<BR>between सस्य, धान्य, तंडुल and अन्न see under<BR>तंडुल).<BR>--2 Coriander.<BR>--3 A measure<BR>equal to four sesamum seeds.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अचलः a pile of grain presented to,<BR>Brāhmaṇas as a gift.<BR>--अरिः a mouse,<BR>rat.<BR>--अर्थः wealth in rice or grain<BR>--अम्लं sour gruel made of the<BR>fermentation of rice-water.<BR>--अस्थि n.<BR>husk, chaff.<BR>--उत्तमः the best of<BR>grain, i. e. rice.<BR>--कल्कं {1} bran. {2}<BR>chaff, straw.<BR>--कोशः, --कोष्ठकं --कः a<BR>granary.<BR>--क्षेत्रं a corn-field.<BR>--चमसः<BR>rice flattened by threshing after it<BR>has been steeped and fried in the<BR>husk.<BR>--त्वच् f. the husk of corn.<BR>--मायः a corn-dealer.<BR>--राजः barley.<BR>--वर्धनं lending grain at interest,<BR>usury with grain.<BR>--वीजं (बीजं)<BR>coriander.<BR>--वीरः a sort of pulse (माष).<BR>--शीर्षकं the ear of corn.<BR>--शूकं the<BR>beard or awn of corn.<BR>--सारः<BR>threshed corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0595-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्या
धान्या, धान्याकं Coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्याकं|धान्याक
धान्या, धान्याकं Coriander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धान्वन
धान्वन a. (नी f.) Situated in a<BR>desert (धन्वन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामकः|धामक
धामकः A sort of weight, (माष<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामन्
धामन् n. [धा-मनिन्]<BR>1 A<BR>dwelling-place, abode, residence, house;<BR>तुरासाहं पुरोधाय धाम स्वायंभुवं ययुः<BR>Ku. 2. 1, 44; पुण्यं यायास्त्रिभुवनगुरोर्धाम<BR>चंडीश्वरस्य Me. 33; Bg. 8. 21;<BR>Bh. 1. 33.<BR>--2 A place, site, resort; श्रियो<BR>धाम.<BR>--3 The inmates of a house,<BR>members of a family.<BR>--4 A ray of<BR>light; धाम्नातिशाययति धाम सहस्रधाम्नः<BR>Mu. 3. 17; Śi. 9. 53.<BR>--5 Light, lustre,<BR>splendour; Mu. 3. 17; Ki. 2. 20,<BR>55, 59; 10. 6r; Amaru. 86; R. 6. 6;<BR>18. 22.<BR>--6 Majestic lustre, majesty,<BR>glory, dignity; R. 11. 85.<BR>--7 Power,<BR>strength, energy (प्रताप); Ki. 2. 47.<BR>--8 Birth.<BR>--9 The body.<BR>--10 A troop,<BR>host.<BR>--11 State, condition.<BR>--12 A<BR>class.<BR>--13 Ved. Law, rule.<BR>--14 Ved.<BR>Property, wealth.<BR>--15 A fetter.<BR>--16<BR>Fashion, mode, manner.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केशिन्, m.<BR>--निधिः the sun.<BR>--छद् m.<BR>Ved. N. of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनिका
धामनिका, धामनी See धमनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धामनी
धामनिका, धामनी See धमनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय|धायः
धाय, --धायक a. Having,<BR>possessing, holding, sustaining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायक
धाय, --धायक a. Having,<BR>possessing, holding, sustaining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायस्
धायस् a. Ved.<BR>1 Sustaining,<BR>supporting.<BR>--2 Nourishing.<BR>--3<BR>Drinking. --n. The act of drinking or<BR>sucking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धायु
धायु a.<BR>1 Sustaining, supporting.<BR>--2 Liberal.<BR>--3 Feeding, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाय्यः|धाय्य
धाय्यः A Purohita or family priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार|धारं|धारः
धार a. [धृ-णिच्-अच्]<BR>1 Holding,<BR>bearing, supporting.<BR>--2 Streaming,<BR>dripping, flowing.<BR>--रः<BR>1 An epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 A sudden and<BR>violent shower of rain, sharp-driving<BR>shower.<BR>--3 Snow, hail.<BR>--4 A deep<BR>place.<BR>--5 Debt.<BR>--6 A boundary,<BR>limit.<BR>--7 A sort of stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारक|धारकः
धारक a. Holding, possessing,<BR>bearing &c.; नाम˚, देह˚.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>vessel of any kind (box, trunk,<BR>&c.), a water-pot.<BR>--2 A debtor.<BR>--का The vulva of a female.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारण|धारणं
धारण a. (णी f.) [धृ-णिच्-ल्युट्]<BR>Holding, bearing, carrying,<BR>preserving, sustaining, protecting, having,<BR>assuming, &c.<BR>--णौ (du.) The<BR>two female breasts.<BR>--णं<BR>1 The act<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-b" target="_blank">Page0596-b+ 57</a>]<BR>of holding, bearing, supporting,<BR>preserving or keeping back.<BR>--2<BR>Possessing, possession.<BR>--3<BR>Observing; holding fast.<BR>--4<BR>Retaining in the memory;<BR>ग्रहणधारणपटुर्बालकः.<BR>--5 Being<BR>indebted (to any one.)<BR>--6 Steady<BR>abstraction of the mind.<BR>--7 Keeping,<BR>maintaining.<BR>--8 Restraining.<BR>--9 (In<BR>gram.) Pronouncing imperfectly,<BR>--णी<BR>1 A row or line.<BR>--2 A vein or<BR>tubular vessel.<BR>--3 Steadiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणकः|धारणक
धारणकः A debtor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारणा
धारणा<BR>1 The act of holding,<BR>bearing, supporting preserving, &c.<BR>--2<BR>The faculty of retaining in the mind,<BR>a good or retentive memory;<BR>धीर्धारणावती मेधा Mk.<BR>--3 Memory in<BR>general.<BR>--4 Keeping the mind collected,<BR>holding the breath suspended, steady<BR>abstraction of mind; परिचेतुमुपांशु<BR>धारणां R. 8. 18; Ms. 6. 72;<BR>Y. 3. 201; (धारणेत्युच्यते चेयं धार्यते यन्मनो<BR>तया).<BR>--5 Fortitude, firmness,<BR>steadiness.<BR>--6 A fixed precept or<BR>injunction, a settled rule, conclusion; इति<BR>धर्मस्य धारणा Ms. 8. 184, 4. 38,<BR>9. 124.<BR>--7 Understanding, intellect.<BR>--8 Continuance in rectitude,<BR>propriety, decorum.<BR>--9 Conviction or<BR>abstraction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--योगः deep<BR>devotion.<BR>--शक्तिः f. a retentive<BR>memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयिष्णु
धारयिष्णु a. Capable of holding,<BR>sustaining, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारयित्री
धारयित्री The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारा
धारा<BR>1 A stream or current of<BR>water, a line of descending fluid,<BR>stream, current; Bh. 2. 93;<BR>Me. 55; R. 16. 66; आबद्धधारमश्रु प्रावर्तत<BR>Dk. 74.<BR>--2 A shower, a hard or<BR>sharp-driving shower.<BR>--3 A<BR>continuous line or series; Bv. 2. 20.<BR>--4<BR>A leak or hole in a pitcher.<BR>--5 The<BR>pace of a horse; धाराः<BR>प्रसाधयितुमव्यतिकीर्णरूपाः Śi. 5. 60.<BR>--6 The margin,<BR>edge or border of anything; ध्रुवं स<BR>नीलोत्पलपत्रधारया शमीलतां<BR>छेत्तुमृषिर्व्यबस्यति Ś. 1. 18.<BR>--7 The sharp edge<BR>of a sword, axe, or of any cutting<BR>instrument; तर्जितः परशुधारया मम<BR>R. 11. 78; 6. 42; 10. 86, 41;<BR>Bh. 2. 28.<BR>--8 The edge of a mountain or<BR>precipice.<BR>--9 A wheel or the<BR>periphery of a wheel; R. 13. 15.<BR>--10<BR>A garden-wall, fence, hedge.<BR>--11<BR>The van or front line of an army.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-c" target="_blank">Page0596-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--12 The highest point, excellence<BR>--13 A multitude.<BR>--14 Fame.<BR>--15<BR>Night.<BR>--16 Turmeric.<BR>--17 Likeness.<BR>--18 The tip of the ear.<BR>--19 Speech.<BR>--20 Rumour, report.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रं<BR>the broad-edged head of an arrow.<BR>--अंकुरः {1} a drop of rain. {2} hail.<BR>{3} advancing before the line of an<BR>army (to defy the enemy).<BR>--अंगः a<BR>sword.<BR>--अटः {1} the Cātaka bird.<BR>{2} a horse. {3} a cloud. {4} a furious<BR>elephant, one in rut.<BR>--अधिरूढ a.<BR>raised to the highest pitch.<BR>--अवनिः f. wind.<BR>--अश्रु n. a flood of<BR>tears; Amaru. 10.<BR>--आसारः a heavy<BR>down-fall of rain, a hard or sharp<BR>driving shower; धारासारैर्महती<BR>वृष्टिर्बभूव H. 3; V. 4. 1.<BR>--उष्ण a. warm<BR>from a cow (as milk).<BR>--गृहं a<BR>bathroom with water-jets, a shower-bath<BR>or a house furnished with artificial<BR>jets or fountains of water;<BR>R. 16. 49.<BR>--धरः {1} holder of streams, a cloud.<BR>{2} a sword.<BR>--निपातः, --पातः {1} a fall<BR>of rain, a hard or pelting shower;<BR>Me. 48. {2} a stream of water.<BR>--यंत्रं<BR>a fountain, jet (of water);<BR>Amaru. 59; Ratn. 1. 12.<BR>--वर्षः, र्षं--, संपातः a<BR>hard, sharp-driving or incessant,<BR>shower; R. 4. 82.<BR>--बाहिन् a. incessant,<BR>continuous; U. 4. 3.<BR>--विषः a<BR>crooked sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाराल
धाराल, धारावत् a. Having an edge.<BR>edged (as a sword &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारावत्|धारावन्त्
धाराल, धारावत् a. Having an edge.<BR>edged (as a sword &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिणी
धारिणी The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारित
धारित a. Held, supported,<BR>maintained, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धारिन्
धारिन् a. (णी f.) [धृ-णिनि]<BR>1<BR>Carrying, bearing, sustaining,<BR>preserving, having, holding, supporting;<BR>पादांभोरुहधारि Gīt. 12; कर˚ &c.<BR>--2<BR>Keeping in one's memory,<BR>possessed of retentive memory; अज्ञेभ्यो<BR>ग्रंथिनः श्रेष्ठा ग्रंथिभ्यो धारिणो वराः<BR>Ms. 12. 103.<BR>--3 Edged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्य|धार्य्य|धार्य्यं
धार्य a.<BR>1 To be held or<BR>maintained.<BR>--2 Bearable.<BR>--3 To be worn.<BR>--4<BR>To be suffered, supportable.<BR>--5 To<BR>be borne in mind.<BR>--र्यं Clothes,<BR>garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्तराष्ट्रः|धार्तराष्ट्र|धार्त्तराष्ट्र|धार्त्तराष्ट्रः
धार्तराष्ट्रः [धृतराष्ट्रस्यापत्यं पुमान्-अण्]<BR>1 A son of Dhṛtarāṣṭra.<BR>--2 A sort<BR>of goose with black legs and bill;<BR>निपतंति धार्तराष्ट्राः कालवशान्मेदिनीपृष्ठे<BR>Ve. 1. 6 (where the word is<BR>used in both the senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्म|धार्म्म
धार्म a. [धर्मस्येदं अण्]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">Page0597-a+ 55</a>]<BR>Belonging to justice or Dharma q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0596-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिक|धार्मिकः|धार्म्मिक|धार्म्मिकः
धार्मिक a. (की f.) [धर्मं अधीते<BR>चरती वा ठक्]<BR>1 Righteous, pious, just,<BR>virtuous.<BR>--2 Resting on right,<BR>conformable to justice, equitable.<BR>--3 Religious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्मिणं|धार्मिण
धार्मिणं An assemblage of virtuous<BR>men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धार्ष्ट्यं|धार्ष्ट्य
धार्ष्ट्यं [धृष्टस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ्]<BR>Arrogance, insolence, audacity,<BR>impudence, rudeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव्
धाव् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (धावति, धावित)<BR>1<BR>(a) To run, advance; अद्यापि<BR>धावति मनः Ch. P. 36; धावंत्यमी<BR>मृगजवाक्षमयेव रथ्याः Ś. 1. 8; गच्छति पुरः<BR>शरीरं धावति पश्चादसंस्तुंतं चेतः 1. 34.<BR>(b) To move, glide.<BR>--2 To run<BR>towards, advance against, assault,<BR>encounter; Bk. 16. 67.<BR>--3 To flow,<BR>stream or flow forth; धावत्यंभसि<BR>तैलवत् Suśr.<BR>--4 To run or flee away.<BR>--5 To give milk (as a cow). {vII.v}<BR>{c1c} U. (धावति-ते, धौत or धावित)<BR>1 To<BR>wash, clean, cleanse, purify, rub off;<BR>दधाबाद्भिस्ततश्चक्षुः सुग्रीवस्य बिभीषणः<BR>विदांचकार धौताक्षः स रिपुं खे ननर्द च ॥<BR>Bk. 14. 50, Ś. 6. 24; Śi. 17. 8.<BR>--2<BR>To brighten, polish.<BR>--3 To rub<BR>into one's person (Atm.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धाव
धाव a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Washing, cleaning &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावक|धावकः
धावक a. [धाव्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 Running,<BR>flowing.<BR>--2 Quick, swift.<BR>--3<BR>Washing.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A washerman.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>a poet (said to have composed the<BR>Ratnāvalī for King Śrīharṣa)<BR>श्रीहर्षादेर्धावकादीनामिव यशः K. P. 1.<BR>v. l.; प्रथितयशसां<BR>धावकसौमिल्लकविपुत्रादीनां प्रनंधानतिक्रम्य M. 1. v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावनं|धावन
धावनं [धाव्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Running,<BR>galloping.<BR>--2 Flowing.<BR>--3 Attacking.<BR>--4 Cleansing, purifying, rubbing,<BR>washing off.<BR>--5 Rubbing with<BR>anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावित|धावितः
धावित p. p.<BR>1 Purified, cleansed.<BR>--2 Running towards, or against.<BR>--3<BR>Running, going quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धावल्यं|धावल्य
धावल्यं<BR>1 Whiteness.<BR>--2 Paleness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासस्
धासस् m. Ved. A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धासिः|धासि
धासिः Ved. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धि|धिः
धि {vI.v} {c6c} P. (धियति) To hold,<BR>have, possess. --WITH सं to<BR>make peace, treat with; cf. संधा.<BR>{vII.v} or धिन्व् {c5c} P. (धिनोति) To<BR>please, delight; satisfy; पश्यंती<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">Page0597-b+ 54</a>]<BR>चात्मरूपं तदपि विलुलितस्रग्धरेयं धिनोति<BR>Gīt. 12; धिनोति नास्माञ्जलजेन पूजा<BR>त्वयान्वहं तन्वि वितन्यमाना N. 8. 97;<BR>U. 5. 27; Ki. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिः|धि
धिः (At the end of comp. only)<BR>A receptacle, store, reservoir &c.;<BR>as in उदधि, इषुधि, वारिधि, जलधि &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्
धिक् ind. An interjection of<BR>censure, menace or displeasure<BR>(‘fie’, ‘shame;’ ‘out upon,’ ‘what<BR>a pity’ &c. usually with acc.);<BR>धिक् तां च तं च मदनं च इमां च मां च<BR>Bh. 2. 2; धिगिमां देहभृतामसारतां<BR>R. 8. 50; धिक् तान् धिक् तान् धिगेतान्<BR>कथयति सततं कीर्तनस्थो मृदंगः; धिक्<BR>सानुजं कुरुपतिं धिगजातशत्रुं Ve. 3. 11;<BR>sometimes with nom., voc., and<BR>gen. also; धिङ् मूर्ख, धिगर्थाः<BR>कष्टसंश्रयाः Pt. 1; धिगस्तु हृदयस्यास्य &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंडः reprimand, censure;<BR>Ms. 8. 129.<BR>--पारुष्यं abuse, reproach,<BR>reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कृ
धिक्कृ {c8c} U. To despise, disregard,<BR>contemn, reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कारः|धिक्कार
धिक्कारः --धिक्क्रिया Reproach,<BR>contempt, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्क्रिया
धिक्कारः --धिक्क्रिया Reproach,<BR>contempt, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्कृत|धिक्कृतः
धिक्कृत a. Censured, reproached.<BR>--तं Reproach, censure, contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिक्ष्
धिक्ष् {c1c} A. (धिक्षते)<BR>1 To kindle.<BR>--2 To live.<BR>--3 To be harassed.<BR>--4 To<BR>be weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिग्वणः|धिग्वण
धिग्वणः A man of a mixed tribe<BR>(sprung from a Brāhmaṇa and<BR>a female of the Āyogava tribe).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिप्सु
धिप्सु a. Wishing to deceive,<BR>deceptive; Bk. 9. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिन्व्
धिन्व् See धि II.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्
धिष् {c3c} P. (दिधेष्टि) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्
धिष् f. = धिषणा q. v. below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिषणः|धिषण
धिषणः N. of Bṛhaspati,<BR>preceptor of the gods.<BR>--णं A<BR>dwellingplace, an abode, residence.<BR>--णा<BR>1<BR>Speech.<BR>--2 Praise, hymn.<BR>--3<BR>Intellect, understanding; Mv. 6. 8.<BR>--4 Earth.<BR>--5 A cup, bowl<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः N. of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धिष्ण्य|धिष्ण्यं|धिष्ण्यः
धिष्ण्य a. Ved.<BR>1 To be praised or<BR>meditated upon.<BR>--2 Worthy of a high<BR>place.<BR>--ष्ण्यः<BR>1 A place for the<BR>sacrificial fire; अमी वेदिं परितः कॢप्तधिष्ण्याः<BR>Ś. 4. 7.<BR>--2 N. of Śukra, preceptor<BR>of the demons.<BR>--3 The planet<BR>Venus.<BR>--4 Power, strength.<BR>--ष्ण्यं<BR>1<BR>A seat, an abode, site, place, house;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-c" target="_blank">Page0597-c+ 56</a>]<BR>न भौमान्येव धिष्ण्यानि हित्वा<BR>ज्योतिर्मयान्यपि R. 15. 59.<BR>--2 A meteor.<BR>--3<BR>Fire (m. also).<BR>--4 A star, an<BR>asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धी
धी {c4c} A. (धीयते)<BR>1 To disregard,<BR>disrespect.<BR>--2 To propitiate.<BR>--3 To<BR>hold, contain.<BR>--4 To accomplish,<BR>fulfil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीः
धीः f. [ध्यै भावे क्विप् संप्रसारणं च]<BR>1 (a) Intellect, understanding;<BR>धियः समग्रैः स गुणैरुदारधीः<BR>R. 3. 30; cf. कुधी, सुधी &c. (b)<BR>Mind; दुष्टधी wicked-minded;<BR>Bg. 2. 54; R. 3. 30.<BR>--2 Idea,<BR>imagination, fancy, conception; न धियां पथि<BR>वर्तसे Ku. 6. 22; Pt. 1. 136.<BR>--3 A<BR>thought, intention, purpose,<BR>propensity; Ki. 1. 37.<BR>--4 Devotion,<BR>prayer.<BR>--5 A sacrifice.<BR>--6<BR>Knowledge, science.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इंद्रियं an<BR>organ of perception (= ज्ञानेंद्रिय<BR>q. v.); मनः कर्णस्तथा नेत्रं रसना चत्वचा सह ।<BR>नासिका चेति षट् तानि धींद्रियाणि प्रचक्षते ॥.<BR>--गुणाः (pl.) intellectual qualities:<BR>they are: --शुश्रूषा श्रवणं चैव ग्रहणं धारणं<BR>तथा । ऊहापोहोर्थविज्ञानं तत्वज्ञानं च धीगुणाः ॥<BR>Kāmandaka.<BR>--पतिः (धियांपतिः)<BR>Bṛhaspati, the preceptor of the gods.<BR>--मंत्रिन् m.,<BR>--सचिवः {1} a minister<BR>for counsel (opp. कर्मसचिव ‘a<BR>minister for action or execution’). {2} a<BR>wise or prudent adviser.<BR>--शक्तिः<BR>f. intellectual quality or faculty.<BR>--सखः a counsellor, adviser,<BR>minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीमत्|धीमन्त्
धीमत् a. Wise, intelligent,<BR>learned. --m. An epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीक्ष्
धीक्ष् = दीक्ष्. q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीत|धीतः
धीत a.<BR>1 Sucked, drunk; see धे.<BR>--2 Reflected upon, thought about.<BR>--3 Propitiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीतिः|धीति
धीतिः f.<BR>1 Drinking, sucking.<BR>--2<BR>Thirst.<BR>--3 Ved. The fingers.<BR>--4<BR>Thought, notion.<BR>--5 Devotion.<BR>--6<BR>Disrespect, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीदा
धीदा<BR>1 Intellect.<BR>--2 A daughter,<BR>virgin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीर|धीरं|धीरः
धीर a. [धियं राति रा-क, धियमीरयति<BR>ईर-अण् वा उप˚ स˚ Tv.]<BR>1 Brave, bold,<BR>courageous; धीरोद्धता गतिः<BR>U. 6. 19.<BR>--2 Steady, steadfast, firm,<BR>durable, lasting, constant; R. 2. 6.<BR>--3 Strong-minded, persevering,<BR>self-possessed, resolute, of firm<BR>resolve or purpose; धीरा हि तरंस्यापदं<BR>K. 175; विकारहेतौ सति विक्रियंते येषां न<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-a" target="_blank">Page0598-a+ 57</a>]<BR>चेतांसि त एव धीराः Ku. 1. 59.<BR>--4<BR>Composed, calm, collected.<BR>--5<BR>Sedate, sober, grave, solemn;<BR>R. 18. 4.<BR>--6 Strong, energetic.<BR>--7<BR>Wise, prudent, intelligent,<BR>sensible, learned, clever; धृतेश्च धीरः<BR>सदृशीर्व्यधत्त सः R. 3. 10; 5. 38,<BR>16. 74; U. 5. 31.<BR>--8 Deep, grave,<BR>loud, hollow (as sound); स्वरेण<BR>धीरेण निवर्तयन्निव R. 3. 43, 59;<BR>U. 6. 17.<BR>--9 Well-conducted,<BR>well-behaved.<BR>--10 Gentle, soft, agreeable,<BR>pleasing (as a breeze); धीरसमीरे<BR>यमुनातीरे वसति वने वनमाली Gīt. 5.<BR>--11<BR>Lazy, dull.<BR>--12 Daring.<BR>--13<BR>Headstrong.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Buddha.<BR>--3 The thinking<BR>principle, the soul (चिदात्मन्).<BR>--4 An<BR>epithet of king Bali.<BR>--रं Saffron.<BR>--रं<BR>ind. Boldly, firmly, steadfastly,<BR>steadily; Bh. 2. 31; Amaru. 11.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदात्तः the hero of a<BR>poetic composition (i. e. a play or<BR>poem) who is brave and<BR>nobleminded; अविकत्थनः<BR>क्षमावानतिगंभीरो महासत्त्वः । स्थेयान्निगूढमानो धीरोदात्तो<BR>दृढव्रतः कथितः ॥ S. D. 66.<BR>--उद्धतः the<BR>hero of a poetic composition who<BR>is brave but haughty; मायापरः<BR>प्रचंडश्चपलोऽहंकारदर्पभूयिष्ठः ।<BR>आत्मश्लाघानिरतो धीरैर्धीरोद्धतः कथितः S. D. 67.<BR>--चेतस् a. firm, resolute,<BR>strongminded, courageous.<BR>--प्रशांतः the<BR>hero of a poetic composition who is<BR>brave and calm; सामान्यगुणैर्भूयान्<BR>द्विजातिको धीरप्रशांतः स्यात् S. D. 69.<BR>--ललितः the hero of a poetic<BR>composition who is firm and brave, but<BR>sportive and reckless; निर्श्चितो<BR>मृदुरनिशं कलापरो धीरललितः स्यात्<BR>S. D. 68.<BR>--स्कंधः a buffalo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0597-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरता
धीरता<BR>1 Fortitude, courage,<BR>strength of mind; विपत्तौ च महाल्ँलोके<BR>धीरतामनुगच्छति H. 3. 44; V. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Suppression of jealousy &c.<BR>--3 Gravity,<BR>solemnity (as shown by silence &c.);<BR>प्रत्यादेशान्न खलु भवतो धीरतां कल्पयामि<BR>Me. 114.<BR>--4 Steadiness, firmness.<BR>--5<BR>Wisdom, cleverness.<BR>--6 Refusal.<BR>(For other meanings see धैर्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीरा
धीरा The heroine of a poetic<BR>composition who, though jealous of her<BR>husband or lover, suppresses all outward<BR>manifestation or expression of her<BR>resentment in his presence, or as the<BR>Rasamañjarī puts it,<BR>व्यंग्यकोपप्रकाशिका धीरा; see S. D. 102-105 also.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">Page0598-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधीरा the heroine of a<BR>poetic composition who, being jealous<BR>of her husband or lover, alternately<BR>expresses and conceals her jealousy;<BR>(व्यंग्याव्यंग्यकोपप्रकाशिका धीराधीरा<BR>Rasamañjarī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटिः|धीलटि
धीलटिः --टी f. A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीलटी
धीलटिः --टी f. A daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवन्
धीवन् a. (री f.) Clever, skilful.<BR>--m.<BR>1 An artist.<BR>--2 A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवरः|धीवर
धीवरः A fisherman;<BR>मृगमीनसज्जनानां तृणजलसंतोषविहितवृत्तीनां ।<BR>लुब्धकधीवरपिशुना निष्कारणवैरिणो जगति ॥<BR>Bh. 2. 61, 1. 85.<BR>--रं Iron.<BR>--री<BR>1<BR>A fisherman's wife.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>harpoon for catching fish.<BR>--3 A<BR>fishbasket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धीवरकः|धीवरक
धीवरकः A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धु|धुः
धु {c5c} U. (धुनोति धुनुते, धुत) See धू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुः|धु
धुः f. Shaking, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुत|धुतः
धुत a.<BR>1 Shaken; R. 11. 16.<BR>--2<BR>Left, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुन
धुन a. Ved.<BR>1 Sounding.<BR>--2<BR>Shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनयति
धुनयति Den. P.<BR>1 To sound, roar.<BR>--2 To flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुक्ष्
धुक्ष् {c1c} A. (धुक्षते, धुक्षित)<BR>1 To be<BR>kindled.<BR>--2 To live.<BR>--3 To be weary.<BR>--Caus. (धुक्षयति-ते) To kindle,<BR>inflame. --WITH सं to be kindled or<BR>excited (fig. also); संदुधुक्षे तयोः कोपः<BR>Bk. 14. 109. (--Caus.) to kindle,<BR>inflame, excite; निवार्णभूयिष्ठमथास्य<BR>वीर्यं संधुक्षयंतीव वपुर्गुणेन Ku. 3. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनिः|धुनि
धुनिः, --नी f. A river; पुराणां<BR>संहर्तुः सुरधुनि कपर्दोऽधिरुरुहे G. L. 22.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नाथः the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुनी
धुनिः, --नी f. A river; पुराणां<BR>संहर्तुः सुरधुनि कपर्दोऽधिरुरुहे G. L. 22.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नाथः the ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुंधुमारः|धुन्धुमार|धुन्धुमारः
धुंधुमारः<BR>1 A kind of insect(<BR>इंद्रगोप).<BR>--2 The smoke of a house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्
धुर् f. (Nom. sing. धूः)<BR>1 A yoke<BR>(lit.); न गर्दभा वाजिधुरं वहंति<BR>Mk. 4. 17; अत्रस्नुभिर्युक्तधुरं तुरंगैः R. 14. 47.<BR>--2 (a) That part of a yoke which rests<BR>on the shoulder. (b) The foremost<BR>part of the pole where the yoke is<BR>fixed.<BR>--3 The pin at both ends of an<BR>axle for fastening the nave of the<BR>wheel.<BR>--4 The shaft or pole of a<BR>carriage.<BR>--5 A load, burden (fig.<BR>also); responsibility, duty, task;<BR>तेन धूर्जगतो गुर्वी सचिवेषु निचिक्षिपे<BR>R. 1. 34, 2. 74, 3. 35, 5. 66; Ku. 6. 30;<BR>कार्यधुरं वहंति Mu. 1. 14;<BR>आप्तैरप्यनवाप्तपौरुषफलैः कार्यस्य धूरुज्झिता Mu. 6. 5,<BR>4. 6; Ki. 3. 50; 14. 6.<BR>--6<BR>The foremost or highest place, van,<BR>front, top, head; अपांसुलानां धुरि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-c" target="_blank">Page0598-c+ 56</a>]<BR>कीर्तनीया R. 2. 2; धुरि स्थिता त्वं<BR>पतिदेवतानां 14. 74; अविघ्नमस्तु ते स्थेयाः<BR>पितेव धुरि पुत्रिणां 1. 91; धुरि<BR>प्रतिष्ठापयितव्य एव M. 1. 16, 5. 16.<BR>--7 A finger.<BR>--8 Agitation, trembling.<BR>--9<BR>Reflection.<BR>--10 A spark of fire.<BR>--11<BR>Distress, affliction.<BR>--12 A part, portion,<BR>share.<BR>--13 Wealth.<BR>--14 N. of the<BR>Ganges. (धुरि कृ ‘to place at the head<BR>or in front of’; Ś. 7. 4).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गत<BR>(धूर्गत) a. {1} standing on the pole<BR>of a chariot. {2} standing at the<BR>head, chief, head, foremost.<BR>--जटिः<BR>(धूर्जटिः) an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--धर<BR>(धूर्धर, also धुरंधर) a. {1} bearing<BR>the yoke. {2} fit to be harnessed. {3}<BR>laden with good qualities or<BR>important duties. {4} chief, head, foremost,<BR>pre-eminent; कुलधुरंधरो भव V. 5.<BR>--(रः) {1} a beast of burden. {2} a<BR>man of business. {3} a chief, head,<BR>leader. {4} an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--वह<BR>(धूर्वह) a. {1} carrying or bearing a<BR>burden. {2} managing affairs.<BR>--(हः)<BR>a beast of burden; so धूर्वोदृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरः|धुर
धुरः (At the end of comp.)<BR>1 A<BR>yoke, pole.<BR>--2 Burden.<BR>--3 A pin at<BR>the end of an axle &c. see धुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरंधर|धुरन्धर|धुरन्धरः
धुरंधर See धूर्धर above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरा
धुरा A burden, load; रणधुरा<BR>Ve. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीण|धुरीणः
धुरीण, धुरीय a. [धुरं वहति, अर्हति वा, धुर्<BR>ख छ बा]<BR>1 Able to bear or carry a<BR>burden.<BR>--2 Fit to be harnessed.<BR>--3<BR>Charged with important duties.<BR>--णः, --यः<BR>1 A beast of burden.<BR>--2<BR>A man of business, or one charged<BR>with important duties.<BR>--3 A chief,<BR>head, leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुरीय|धुरीयः
धुरीण, धुरीय a. [धुरं वहति, अर्हति वा, धुर्<BR>ख छ बा]<BR>1 Able to bear or carry a<BR>burden.<BR>--2 Fit to be harnessed.<BR>--3<BR>Charged with important duties.<BR>--णः, --यः<BR>1 A beast of burden.<BR>--2<BR>A man of business, or one charged<BR>with important duties.<BR>--3 A chief,<BR>head, leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्य|धुर्यः|धुर्य्य|धुर्य्यः
धुर्य a. [धुरं वहति, यत्]<BR>1 Fit for a<BR>burden, able to bear a burden &c.<BR>--2 Fit to be entrusted with<BR>important duties.<BR>--3 Standing at the head,<BR>chief, foremost; see below.<BR>--र्यः<BR>1<BR>A beast of burden.<BR>--2 A horse or<BR>bullock yoked to the pole of a carriage;<BR>नाविनीतैर्व्रजेद् धुर्यैः Ms. 4. 67; येनेदं<BR>ध्रियते विश्वं धुर्यैर्यानमिवाध्वनि Ku. 6. 76;<BR>धुर्यान् विश्रामयेति R. 1. 54, 6. 78;<BR>17. 19.<BR>--3 One who carries a burden<BR>(of responsibility); R. 5. 66.<BR>--4 A<BR>chief, leader, head; न हि सति<BR>कुलधुर्ये सूर्यवंश्या गृहाय R. 7. 71.<BR>--5 A<BR>minister, one charged with important<BR>duties.<BR>--6 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--र्यं The forepart of a pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0598-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुर्व्
धुर्व् {c1c} P. (धुर्वति) To hurt, injure,<BR>kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवका
धुवका The introductory stanza<BR>of a song; cf. ध्रुवका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवित्रं|धुवित्र
धुवित्रं A sort of fan (made of<BR>deer-skin) used in kindling the<BR>sacred fire; cf. धवित्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुवनः|धुवन
धुवनः Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तुरः|धुस्तुर
धुस्तु(स्तू)रः N. of a plant<BR>(= धत्तूर q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धुस्तूरः|धुस्तूर
धुस्तु(स्तू)रः N. of a plant<BR>(= धत्तूर q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धू
धू {c6c} P., {c1c} {c5c} {c9c} {c10c} U. (धुवति,<BR>धवति-ते, धुनोति, धूनुते, धूनाति, धुनीते,<BR>धूनयति-ते, धूत- धून)<BR>1 To shake, agitate,<BR>cause to move or tremble; धुन्वंति<BR>पक्षपवनैर्न नभो बलाकाः Rs. 3. 12;<BR>धुन्वन् कल्पद्रुमकिसलयानि Me. 62;<BR>Ku. 7. 49; R. 4. 67; Bk. 5. 101, 9. 7;<BR>10. 22.<BR>--2 To shake off, remove,<BR>throw off; स्रजमपि शिरस्यंधः क्षिप्तां<BR>धुनोत्यहिशंकया Ś. 7. 24.<BR>--3 To blow<BR>away, destroy.<BR>--4 To kindle, excite,<BR>fan (as fire); वायुना धूयमानो हि वनं<BR>दहति पावकः Mb.; पवनधूतः…अग्निः<BR>Rs. 1. 26.<BR>--5 To treat roughly, hurt,<BR>injure; मा न धावीररिं रणे Bk. 9. 50;<BR>15. 61.<BR>--6 To shake off from oneself,<BR>free oneself from; (सेवकाः) आरोहंति<BR>शनैः पश्चाद्धुन्वंतमपि पार्थिवं Pt. 1. 36.<BR>--7 To strive against, resist, oppose.<BR>(The following stanza from<BR>Kavirahasya illustrates the root in its<BR>different conjugations:<BR>--धूनोति<BR>चंपकवनानि धुनोत्यशोकं चूतं धुनाति धुवति<BR>स्फुटितातिमुक्तं । वायुर्विधूनयति चंपकपुष्परेणून्<BR>यत्कानने धवति चंदनमंजरीश्च ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूः
धूः f. Shaking, trembling,<BR>agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूकः|धूक
धूकः<BR>1 Wind.<BR>--2 A rogue, cheat.<BR>--3 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूत|धूतः
धूत p. p. [धू-क्त]<BR>1 Shaken.<BR>--2<BR>Shaken off, removed.<BR>--3 Fanned.<BR>--4<BR>Abandoned, deserted.<BR>--5 Reviled.<BR>--6 Judged.<BR>--7 Disregarded, treated<BR>with contempt.<BR>--8 Judged.<BR>--ता A<BR>wife.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कल्मष, --पाप a. who<BR>has shaken off his sins, free from<BR>sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूतिः|धूति
धूतिः f.<BR>1 Shaking, moving.<BR>--2<BR>Fanning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धून|धूनः
धून p. p.<BR>1 Shaken, agitated &c.<BR>--2 Afflicted by heat or thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूननः|धूनन|धूननं
धूननः Wind.<BR>--नं Shaking,<BR>agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूनिः|धूनि
धूनिः f. Shaking, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूप्
धूप् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (धूपायति, धूपायित) To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-b" target="_blank">Page0599-b+ 57</a>]<BR>heat or to be heated. {vII.v} {c10c} U.<BR>(धूपयति-ते धूपित)<BR>1 To fumigate,<BR>perfume, incense, to make fragrant.<BR>--2 To shine.<BR>--3 To speak.<BR>--4 (In<BR>astr.) To obscure with mist,<BR>eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपः|धूप
धूपः [धूप-अच्]<BR>1 Incense,<BR>frankincense, perfume, any fragrant<BR>substance.<BR>--2 The vapour issuing from<BR>any fragrant substance (like gum,<BR>resin &c.), aromatic vapour or<BR>smoke; धूपोष्मणा त्याजितमार्द्रभावं<BR>Ku. 7. 14; Me. 32; V. 3. 2; R. 16. 50.<BR>--3 A fragrant powder.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अगुरु n. a kind of agallochum<BR>used for incense.<BR>--अंगः {1}<BR>turpentine. {2} the Sarala tree.<BR>--अर्हं a<BR>black kind of agallochum.<BR>--पात्रं a<BR>vessel for incense, censer.<BR>--वासः<BR>fumigating, perfuming.<BR>--वृक्षः a<BR>kind of pine, the Sarala tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपकः|धूपक
धूप(पि)कः A perfumer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपिकः|धूपिक
धूप(पि)कः A perfumer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपनं|धूपन|धूपनः
धूपनं<BR>1 Fumigation, perfuming.<BR>--2 Incense; Ms. 7. 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपित|धूपितः
धूपित, धूपायित a.<BR>1 Fumigated,<BR>heated, perfumed, incensed.<BR>--2<BR>Suffering pain or fatigue, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूपायित|धूपायितः
धूपित, धूपायित a.<BR>1 Fumigated,<BR>heated, perfumed, incensed.<BR>--2<BR>Suffering pain or fatigue, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमः|धूम
धूमः [धू-कंपे मक्]<BR>1 Smoke, vapour;<BR>धूमज्योतिःसलिलमरुतां सन्निपातः क्व मेघः<BR>Me. 5.<BR>--2 Mist, haze.<BR>--3 (a) A<BR>meteor. (b) The fall of a meteor.<BR>--4 A cloud.<BR>--5 Smoke inhaled (as<BR>a sternutatory).<BR>--6 Belch,<BR>eructation.<BR>--7 A place prepared for the<BR>building of a house.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आभ<BR>a. of a smoky appearance,<BR>smokecoloured.<BR>--(भः) purple.<BR>--आवलिः f.<BR>a wreath or cloud of smoke.<BR>--उत्थं<BR>ammoniac.<BR>--उद्गारः {1} issuing of<BR>smoke or vapour; Me. 69. {2}<BR>eructation, belch.<BR>--ऊर्णा N. of the wife<BR>of Yama. ˚पतिः an epithet of Yama.<BR>--केतनः, केतुः {1} fire; कोपस्य<BR>नंदकुलकाननधूमकेतोः Mu. 1. 10; R. 11. 81.<BR>{2} a meteor, comet, falling star;<BR>धूमकेतुमिव किमपि करालं Gīt. 1;<BR>धूमकेतुरिवोत्थितः Ku. 2. 32. {3} Ketu.<BR>--ग्रहः Rāhu; Māl. 2. 8.<BR>--जः a<BR>cloud. ˚अंगजं ammoniac.<BR>--ध्वजः<BR>fire.<BR>--प a. inhaling only smoke as<BR>a sort of penance.<BR>--पथः {1} a<BR>sacrifice. {2} seeking salvation by<BR>religious works. {3} an air-hole, a<BR>window.<BR>--पानं inhaling smoke or<BR>vapour.<BR>--प्राश a. feeding only on<BR>smoke (as a hermit).<BR>--लता a mass<BR>of curling smoke; Mu. 1. 9.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">Page0599-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--महिषी fog, mist.<BR>--योनिः a cloud; cf.<BR>Me. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमयति
धूमयति Den. P. To cover with<BR>smoke, obscure with mist, darken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमल|धूमलः
धूमल a. Smoke-coloured,<BR>brownish-red, purple.<BR>--लः<BR>1 Purple.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of musical instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमवत्|धूमवन्त्
धूमवत् a.<BR>1 Smoky.<BR>--2 Smoking,<BR>steaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमायति
धूमायति --ते Den. P.<BR>1 To cover or fill<BR>with smoke, vapour &c., darken;<BR>धूमायिता दश दिशो दलितारविंदाः Bv. 1. 104;<BR>Mk. 5. 27.<BR>--2 To smoke, or be<BR>covered with smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमायते
धूमायति --ते Den. P.<BR>1 To cover or fill<BR>with smoke, vapour &c., darken;<BR>धूमायिता दश दिशो दलितारविंदाः Bv. 1. 104;<BR>Mk. 5. 27.<BR>--2 To smoke, or be<BR>covered with smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमायनं|धूमायन
धूमायनं<BR>1 Smoking, steaming.<BR>--2<BR>Heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिका
धूमिका Vapour, fog, mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमित
धूमित a. Obscured with smoke,<BR>darkened; Ku. 4. 30.<BR>--ता (i. e. दिक्)<BR>The quarter towards which the sun<BR>turns first.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूमिन्
धूमिन् a. Smoking.<BR>--नी N. of one<BR>of the tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्या
धूम्या [धूमानां समूहः य] A volume<BR>or cloud of smoke, thick smoke;<BR>Māl. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्र|धूम्रः
धूम्र a. [धूमं तद्वर्णं राति रा-क]<BR>1<BR>Smoke-coloured, smoky, grey;<BR>Bh. 3. 55; R. 15. 16.<BR>--2 Dark-red.<BR>--3<BR>Dark, obscured.<BR>--4 Purple.<BR>--म्रः<BR>1 A mixture of red and black.<BR>--2<BR>Incense.<BR>--3 Purple (the colour).<BR>--4<BR>An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--म्रा An epithet<BR>of Durgā.<BR>--म्रं Sin, vice,<BR>wickedness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षिः a pearl of a<BR>of a bad colour.<BR>--अटः the fork-tailed<BR>shrike.<BR>--आभः air, atmosphere.<BR>--रुच् a. of a purple hue.<BR>--लोचनः a<BR>pigeon.<BR>--लोहित a. dark-red,<BR>deeppurple.<BR>--(तः) an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--वर्णः {1} the dark-red colour. {2}<BR>incense.<BR>--वर्णकः a kind of animal<BR>living in caves, a fox.<BR>--शूकः a<BR>camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूम्रकः|धूम्रक
धूम्रकः A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्
धूर् {c4c} A. (धूर्यते)<BR>1 To hurt, kill.<BR>--2 To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्त|धूर्तः|धूर्त्त|धूर्त्तं|धूर्त्तः
धूर्त a. [धूर्व्-धूर् वा क्त, उणा ˚तन् वा Tv.]<BR>1 Cunning, knavish, roguish, crafty,<BR>fraudulent.<BR>--2 Mischievous,<BR>injurious.<BR>--3 Hurt, injured.<BR>--4 Gay,<BR>licentious; Mu. 3. 10.<BR>--र्तः<BR>1 A<BR>cheat, rogue, swindler.<BR>--2 A<BR>gamester.<BR>--3 A lover, gallant, gay<BR>deceiver; तत्ते धूर्त हृदि स्थिता प्रियतमा<BR>काचिन्ममैवापरा Pt. 4. 6; धूर्तोऽपरां<BR>चुंबति Amaru. 16; so<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">Page0600-a+ 55</a>]<BR>धूर्तानामभिसारसत्वरहृदां Gīt. 11.<BR>--4 The<BR>thornapple (धत्तूर).<BR>--5 Hurting, injuring.<BR>--र्तं<BR>1 Rust, iron-filings.<BR>--2<BR>Blacksalt.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कितवः a gamester.<BR>--कृत् a. crafty, dishonest. (--m.)<BR>the Dhattūra plant.<BR>--जंतुः a man.<BR>--रचना a roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0599-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्तकः|धूर्तक|धूर्त्तक|धूर्त्तकः
धूर्तकः<BR>1 A jackal.<BR>--2 A rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्व्
धूर्व् {c1c} P. (धूर्वति) To hurt, injure,<BR>kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूर्वी|धूर्व्वी
धूर्वी The forepart or pole of a<BR>carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलकं|धूलक
धूलकं Poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिः|धूलि
धूलिः m. f. धूंली<BR>1 Dust; अनीत्वा<BR>पंकतां धूलिमुदकं नावतिष्ठते Śi. 2. 34.<BR>--2 Powder.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कुट्टिमं, --केदारः<BR>{1} a mound, rampart of earth.<BR>{2} a ploughed field.<BR>--ध्वजः wind.<BR>--पटलः --लं a cloud of dust.<BR>--पुष्पिका,<BR>--पुष्पी the Ketaka plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूलिका
धूलिका Fog, mist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूश्
धूश् (ष्-स्) {c10c} U. (धूशयति-ते)<BR>To adorn, decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूष्
धूश् (ष्-स्) {c10c} U. (धूशयति-ते)<BR>To adorn, decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूस्
धूश् (ष्-स्) {c10c} U. (धूशयति-ते)<BR>To adorn, decorate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसर|धूसरः
धूसर a. [धू-सर किच्च न षत्वम् Tv.] Of<BR>a dusty, greyish, or dusky-white<BR>colour, grey; शशी दिवसधूसरः<BR>Bh. 2. 56; Ku. 4. 4, 46; R. 5. 42; 16. 17;<BR>Śi. 17. 41.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The grey colour.<BR>--2<BR>A donkey.<BR>--3 A camel.<BR>--4 A pigeon.<BR>--5 An oilman.<BR>--6 Anything of a<BR>grey colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूसरित
धूसरित a. Made grey, greyish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धूस्तूरः|धूस्तूर
धूस्तूरः The thorn-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृ
धृ {vI.v} {c6c} A. (Supposed by some to<BR>be a passive form of धृ); (ध्रियते, धृत)<BR>1 To be or exist, live, continue to<BR>live, survive; आर्यपुत्र ध्रिये एषा ध्रिये<BR>U. 3; ध्रियते यावदेकोपि रिपुस्तावत्कुतः<BR>सुखं Śi. 2. 35; 15. 89.<BR>--2 To be<BR>maintained or preserved, remain,<BR>continue; सुरतश्रमसंभृतो मुखे ध्रियते<BR>स्वेदलवोद्गमोऽपि ते R. 8. 51; Ku. 4. 18.<BR>--3 To resolve upon. {vII.v} {c1c} P. {c10c} U.<BR>(धरति, usually धारयति-ते, धृत, धारित)<BR>1 To hold, bear, carry, भुजंगमपि<BR>कोपितं शिरसि पुष्पवद्धारयेत् Bh. 2. 4;<BR>वैणवीं धारयेद्यष्टिं सोदकं च कमंडलुं<BR>Ms. 4. 36; Bk. 17. 54; V. 4. 36.<BR>--2 To<BR>hold or bear up, maintain, support,<BR>sustain; धृतमंदर ए Gīt. 1; यथा<BR>सर्वाणि भूतानि धरा धारयते समं Ms. 9. 311;<BR>Pt. 1. 126; प्रातःकुंदप्रसवशिथिलं<BR>जीवितं धारयेथाः Me. 113; चिरमात्मना<BR>धृतां R. 3. 35; U. 3. 29.<BR>--3 To hold<BR>in one's possession, possess, have,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-b" target="_blank">Page0600-b+ 57</a>]<BR>keep; यां संस्कृता धार्यते Bh. 2. 19.<BR>--4<BR>To assume, take (as a form,<BR>disguise &c.); केशव धृतशूकररूप<BR>Gīt. 1; धारयति कोकनदरूपं 10.<BR>--5 To<BR>wear, put on, use (clothes,<BR>ornaments &c.); श्रितकमलाकुचमंडल<BR>धृतकुंडल ए Gīt. 1.<BR>--6 To hold in check,<BR>curb, restrain, stop, detain.<BR>--7 To<BR>fix upon, direct towards; (with<BR>dat. or loc.); ब्राह्मण्ये धृतमानसः, मनो<BR>दध्रे राजसूयाय &c.<BR>--8 To suffer,<BR>undergo.<BR>--9 To assign anything to any<BR>person, allot, assign.<BR>--10 To owe<BR>anything to a person (with dat.;<BR>rarely gen. of person, 10 only in<BR>this sense); वृक्षसेचने द्वे धारयसि मे<BR>Ś. 1; तस्मै-तस्य वा धनं धारयति<BR>&c.<BR>--11 To hold, contain.<BR>--12<BR>To observe, practise.<BR>--13 To cite,<BR>quote.<BR>--14 To keep, retain (in<BR>one's service).<BR>--15 To preserve,<BR>maintain.<BR>--16 To seize, lay hold of.<BR>--17 To hold out or on, endure.<BR>--18<BR>To fix, place, deposit. (The senses of<BR>this root may be variously modified<BR>according to the noun with which it<BR>is connected; e. g. मनसा धृ to bear<BR>in mind, remember; शिरसा, --मूर्ध्नि धृ<BR>to bear on the head, respect highly;<BR>अंतरे धृ to pledge, deposit anything<BR>as surety; समये धृ to bring to<BR>terms or agreement; दंडं धृ to<BR>punish, chastise, use force; जीवितं,<BR>--प्राणान्, --शरीरं, --गात्रं, --देहं &c. धृ to<BR>continue to live, maintain the soul &c.,<BR>preserve the vital spirits; व्रतं धृ to<BR>observe a vow; R. 2. 25; तुलया<BR>धृ to hold in a balance, weigh &c;<BR>मनः --मतिं, --चित्तं, --बुद्धिं धृ to bend the<BR>mind to a thing, fix the mind upon,<BR>think of, resolve upon; गर्भं धृ to<BR>become pregnant, conceive; धारणां<BR>धृ to practise concentration or<BR>self-control &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृक्
धृक् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Bearing, carrying, supporting &c.;<BR>कालरूप˚, शक्ति˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्
धृत् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Possessing, bearing, holder, bearer &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत|धृतः
धृत p. p. [धृ-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1 Held,<BR>carried, borne, supported.<BR>--2<BR>Possessed.<BR>--3 Kept, preserved,<BR>retained.<BR>--4 Seized, grasped, laid hold of.<BR>--5 Worn, used, put on;<BR>Ku. 5. 44.<BR>--6 Placed, deposited.<BR>--7<BR>Practised, observed.<BR>--8 Weighed.<BR>--9<BR>(Actively used) Holding, bearing.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-c" target="_blank">Page0600-c+ 61</a>]<BR>--10 Intent upon.<BR>--11 Prepared<BR>ready. See धृ also.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Falling.<BR>--2 State, existence.<BR>--3 Taking,<BR>seizing.<BR>--4 Wearing, putting on.<BR>--5 A particular manner of<BR>fighting.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>firmminded, steady, calm, collected.<BR>(--m.) an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--दंड a. {1} inflicting punishment.<BR>{2} one on whom punishment is<BR>inflicted.<BR>--दीधितिः fire.<BR>--पट a.<BR>covered with a cloth.<BR>--राजन् a.<BR>ruled by a good king (as a country).<BR>--राष्ट्रः {1} a good king. {2} a<BR>country ruled by a good king. {3}<BR>N. of the eldest son of Vyāsa by<BR>a widow of विचित्रवीर्य. [As the eldest<BR>son he was entitled to the throne, but<BR>being blind from birth, he renounced<BR>the sovereignty in favour of Pāṇḍu; but<BR>on his retirement to the woods, he<BR>undertook it himself, making<BR>Duryodhana-his eldest on-the virtual ruler. When<BR>Duryodhana was killed by Bhīma, the<BR>old king thirsted for revenge, and<BR>expressed his desire to embrace<BR>Yudhiṣṭhira and Bhīma. Kṛṣṇa readily<BR>discovered his object, and convinced that<BR>Bhīma was marked out by the King as<BR>his prey, he caused an iron image of Bhīma<BR>to be made. And when the blind king<BR>rushed forward to embrace Bhīma,<BR>Kṛṣṇa substituted the iron image which<BR>the revengeful old man pressed with so<BR>much force that it was crushed to pieces,<BR>and Bhīma escaped. Thus discomfited,<BR>he, with his wife, repaired to the<BR>Himālaya and there died after some years].<BR>--वर्मन् a. clad in armour, mailed.<BR>--व्रत a. {1} observing vows,<BR>performing religious rites. {2} devoted,<BR>attached. {3} of a fixed law or order.<BR>--(तः) an epithet of (1) Indra. (2)<BR>Varuṇa. (3) Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिः|धृति
धृतिः f. [धृ-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Taking, holding,<BR>seizing.<BR>--2 Having, possessing.<BR>--3<BR>Maintaining, supporting.<BR>--4<BR>Firmness; steadiness, constancy.<BR>--5<BR>Fortitude, energy, resolution’<BR>courage, self-command; भज धृतिं त्यज<BR>भीतिमहेतुकां N. 4. 105; Ki. 6. 11;<BR>R. 8. 66.<BR>--6 Satisfaction, contentment,<BR>pleasure, happiness, delight, joy;<BR>धृतेश्च धीरः सदृशीर्व्यधत्त सः R. 3. 10;<BR>16. 82; न चक्षुर्बध्नाति धृतिं V. 2. 8;<BR>Śi. 7. 10, 14.<BR>--7 Satisfaction<BR>considered as one of the 33 subordinate<BR>feelings (in Rhetoric);<BR>ज्ञानाभीष्टागमाद्यैस्तु संपूर्णस्पृहता धृतिः ।<BR>सौहित्यवचनोल्लाससहासप्रतिभादिकृत् S. D. 198, 168.<BR>--8<BR>A sacrifice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुष् a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">Page0601-a+ 59</a>]<BR>destroying all composure, discomposing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0600-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृतिमत्|धृतिमन्त्
धृतिमत् a.<BR>1 Firm, steady; steadfast,<BR>resolute.<BR>--2 Satisfied, happy, glad,<BR>content; R. 13. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वन्
धृत्वन् m.<BR>1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 Of Brahmā.<BR>--3 Virtue, morality.<BR>--4 The sky.<BR>--5 The sea.<BR>--6 A<BR>clever man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृत्वरी
धृत्वरी The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृज्
धृज्, धृंज् {c1c} P. (धर्जति धृंजति) To go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृंज्
धृज्, धृंज् {c1c} P. (धर्जति धृंजति) To go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्
धृष् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (धर्षति, धर्षित)<BR>1 To<BR>come together, be compact.<BR>--2 To<BR>hurt or injure. {vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U.<BR>(धर्षति, धर्षयति-ते)<BR>1 To offend, hurt,<BR>injure.<BR>--2 To insult, treat with<BR>indignity.<BR>--3 To assail, overcome,<BR>overpower, conquer, destroy.<BR>--4 To<BR>dare to attack, challenge, defy.<BR>--5<BR>To violate or outrage (as a woman).<BR>{vIII.v} {c5c} P. (धृष्णोति, धृष्ट)<BR>1 To be<BR>bold or courageous.<BR>--2 To be<BR>confident.<BR>--3 To be proud or<BR>overbearing.<BR>--4 To be impudent or<BR>impatient.<BR>--5 To dare, venture (with<BR>inf.).<BR>--6 To brave, challenge;<BR>Bk. 14. 102.<BR>--7 To insult, treat with<BR>contumely. {vIV.v} {c10c} A. (धर्षयते) To<BR>assail, attack, outrage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषित
धृषित a. Brave, bold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृषु|धृषुः
धृषु a. [धृष्-कु]<BR>1 Bold, brave.<BR>--2<BR>Clever.<BR>--षुः A heap, group, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्ट|धृष्टः
धृष्ट p. p. [धृष्-क्त]<BR>1 Bold,<BR>courageous, confident.<BR>--2 Impudent, rude,<BR>shameless, saucy, insolent; धृष्टः पार्श्वे<BR>वसति H. 2. 26.<BR>--3 Forward,<BR>presumptuous.<BR>--4 Profligate, abandoned.<BR>--5 Cruel, unkind.<BR>--ष्टः A faithless<BR>husband or lover; कृतागा अपि<BR>निःशंकस्तर्जितोऽपि न लज्जितः । दृष्टदोषोऽपि<BR>मिथ्यावाक् कथितो धृष्टनायकः S. D. 72.<BR>--ष्टा A disloyal woman.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द्युम्नः N. of a son of Drupada and<BR>brother of Draupadī. [He with his<BR>father fought on the side of the Pāṇḍavas,<BR>and for some days he acted as<BR>commander-in-chief of their forces. When<BR>Droṇa had killed Drupada after a hard<BR>struggle, Dhṛṣṭadyumna vowed that<BR>he would be revenged for the death of his<BR>father. And he was able to fulfil this vow<BR>on the morning of the 16th day of the<BR>battle, when he unfairly cut off the head<BR>of Droṇa; (see Droṇa). He was<BR>afterwards surprised by Aśvatthāman while<BR>lying asleep in the camp of the Pāṇḍavas,<BR>and was stamped to death.].<BR>--धी a.<BR>bold, presumptuous.<BR>--मानिन् a.<BR>having too high an opinion of oneself,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">Page0601-b+ 55</a>]<BR>presumptuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्टि
धृष्टि a. Ved. Bold. --m. A pair of<BR>tongs. --f. Boldness, bravery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णज्
धृष्णज् a.<BR>1 Bold, confident.<BR>--2<BR>Impudent, shameless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णिः|धृष्णि
धृष्णिः A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्णु|धृष्णुः
धृष्णु a. [धृष्-क्नु]<BR>1 Bold, confident,<BR>courageous, valiant, powerful (in a<BR>good sense).<BR>--2 Shameless,<BR>impudent.<BR>--3 Ved. Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धृष्य
धृष्य a. To be attacked, assailable,<BR>conquerable; as in अधृष्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धे
धे {c1c} P. (धयति, धीत; caus. धापयति;<BR>desid. धित्सति)<BR>1 To suck, drink,<BR>drink in, absorb (fig. also),<BR>अधाद्वसामधासीच्च रुधिरं वनवासिनां<BR>Bk. 15. 29, 6. 18; Ms. 4. 59; Y. 1. 140.<BR>--2 To kiss; धन्यो धयत्याननं<BR>Gīt. 12.<BR>--3 To suck out, draw or take<BR>away.<BR>--4 To appropriate. --Caus. To<BR>suckle, nourish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनः|धेन
धेनः [धयंति एनं धे-नन् इच्चं]<BR>1 The<BR>ocean.<BR>--2 A male river (नद).<BR>--ना<BR>1 A river.<BR>--2 Speech.<BR>--3 A milch<BR>cow (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुः|धेनु
धेनुः f. [धयति सुतान्, धीयते वत्सैर्वा, धे-नु<BR>इच्च Tv.]<BR>1 A cow, milch-cow; धेनु<BR>धीराः सूनृतां वाचमाहुः U. 5. 31.<BR>--2<BR>The female of a species (affixed<BR>to the names of other animals in<BR>this sense); as खड्गधेनुः, वडवधेनुः &c.<BR>--3 The earth. (Sometimes at the<BR>end of comp. धेनु forms a<BR>diminutive; as असिधेनुः, खड्गधेनुः).<BR>--4 A gift,<BR>present.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मक्षिका a gadfly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुकः|धेनुक
धेनुकः N. of s demon killed by<BR>Balarāma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सूदनः an<BR>epithet of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुका
धेनुका<BR>1 A female elephant.<BR>--2<BR>A milch-cow.<BR>--3 A gift, an<BR>offering.<BR>--4 A female animal in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्टरी
धेनुष्टरी A milch-cow ceasing to<BR>give milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेनुष्या
धेनुष्या A cow who or whose milk<BR>has been pledged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धेय
धेय a.<BR>1 To be held or taken.<BR>--2<BR>To be produced.<BR>--3 To be fed or<BR>nourished.<BR>--4 To be drunk.<BR>--5 An<BR>affix, as in नाम˚, भाग˚, q. v.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Nourishing.<BR>--2 Drinking.<BR>--3<BR>Holding, taking &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैनुकं|धैनुक
धैनुकं<BR>1 A herd of cows.<BR>--2 A<BR>particular mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment (रतिबंथ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैर्यं|धैर्य|धैर्य्य|धैर्य्यं
धैर्यं [धीरस्य भावः कर्म वा ष्यञ]<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">Page0601-c+ 55</a>]<BR>Firmness, durability, strength,<BR>constancy, steadiness, stability,<BR>fortitude, courage; धैर्यमवष्टभ्य<BR>Pt. 1; विपदि धैर्यं Bh. 2. 63; so<BR>धैर्यवृत्ति Śi. 9. 59.<BR>--2 Calmness,<BR>composure.<BR>--3 Gravity, patience.<BR>--4<BR>Inflexibility.<BR>--5 Boldness,<BR>forwardness; Me. 40 (धाष्ट्ये Malli.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवतः|धैवत
धैवतः The sixth of the seven<BR>primary notes of the Indian gamut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धैवत्यं|धैवत्य
धैवत्यं Cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोडः|धोड
धोडः = डुंडुभः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोर्
धोर् {c1c} P. (धोरति)<BR>1 To go quickly<BR>have good paces, run, trot.<BR>--2 To<BR>be skilful (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणं|धोरण
धोरणं [धोर् करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 A vehicle<BR>in general (as a horse, elephant<BR>&c.).<BR>--2 Going well or quickly.<BR>--3<BR>A horse's trot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणिः|धोरणि
धोरणिः --णी f. [धोर्-अनि वा ङीप्]<BR>1<BR>An uninterrupted series or<BR>continuity; यैर्माकंदवने मनोज्ञपवने सद्यः<BR>स्खलन्माधुरीधाराधोरणिधातैधामनि<BR>धराधीशत्वमालंब्यते । तेषां नित्यविनोदिनां सुकृतिनां<BR>माध्वीकपानां पुनः कालः किं न करोति<BR>केतकि यतस्त्वं चापि केलिस्थली Udb.<BR>--2<BR>Tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरणी
धोरणिः --णी f. [धोर्-अनि वा ङीप्]<BR>1<BR>An uninterrupted series or<BR>continuity; यैर्माकंदवने मनोज्ञपवने सद्यः<BR>स्खलन्माधुरीधाराधोरणिधातैधामनि<BR>धराधीशत्वमालंब्यते । तेषां नित्यविनोदिनां सुकृतिनां<BR>माध्वीकपानां पुनः कालः किं न करोति<BR>केतकि यतस्त्वं चापि केलिस्थली Udb.<BR>--2<BR>Tradition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धोरितं|धोरित
धोरितं [धोर्-भावे क्त]<BR>1 Injuring,<BR>hurting, striking.<BR>--2 Going, motion.<BR>--3 A horse's trot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौत|धौतं
धौत p. p. [धाव्-क्त ऊठ्]<BR>1<BR>Washed, washed off, cleaned, purified,<BR>laved; कुल्यांभोभिः पवनचपलैः शाखिनो<BR>धौतमूलाः Ś. 1. 15; Śik. 58;<BR>Ku. 1. 6, 6. 57; R. 16. 49; 19. 10.<BR>--2<BR>Polished, brightened.<BR>--3 Bright, white,<BR>shining, brightened, glistening;<BR>हरशिरश्चंद्रिकाधौतहर्म्या Me. 7, 44;<BR>विकसद्दंतांशुधौताधरं Gīt. 12.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Silver.<BR>--2 Cleaning, washing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कट<BR>a bag of coarse cloth.<BR>--कोषजं, --कौः<BR>षेयं bleached or purified silk.<BR>--खंर्डा<BR>sugar-candy.<BR>--शिलं rock-crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतेयः|धौतेय|धौतेयं
धौतेयः, --यं A kind of salt (सैंधव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतेयं|धौतेय|धौतेयः
धौतेयः, --यं A kind of salt (सैंधव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौतरि
धौतरि a. Ved. Shaking,<BR>trembling; Rv. 6. 44. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौति
धौति --ती f. Ved.<BR>1 A spring.<BR>--2 A<BR>river.<BR>--3 One of the ways of<BR>practising Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौती
धौति --ती f. Ved.<BR>1 A spring.<BR>--2 A<BR>river.<BR>--3 One of the ways of<BR>practising Yoga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौम्रः|धौम्र
धौम्रः<BR>1 Greyness.<BR>--2 A place for<BR>building (prepared in a particular<BR>way).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरितकं|धौरितक
धौरितकं A horse's trot; cf. धौरित.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौरेय|धौरेयः
धौरेय a. (यी f.) [धुरं वहति ढक्] Fit<BR>for a burden.<BR>--यः<BR>1 A beast of burden<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">Page0602-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 A horse.<BR>--3 A chief, leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0601-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्तकं|धौर्तक|धौर्त्तक
धौर्तकं, धौर्तिकं, धौर्त्यं Fraud,<BR>dishonesty, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्तिकं|धौर्तिक|धौर्त्तिक|धौर्त्तिकं
धौर्तकं, धौर्तिकं, धौर्त्यं Fraud,<BR>dishonesty, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्त्यं|धौर्त्य
धौर्तकं, धौर्तिकं, धौर्त्यं Fraud,<BR>dishonesty, roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

धौर्यं|धौर्य|धौर्य्य|धौर्य्यं
धौर्यं A horse's trot, cf. धोरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मा
ध्मा {c1c} P. (धमति, ध्मात; caus.<BR>ध्मापयति)<BR>1 To blow, breathe out, exhale.<BR>--2 To blow (as a wind-instrument),<BR>produce sound by blowing; शंखं<BR>दधमौ प्रतापवान् Bg. 1. 12, 18; R. 7. 63;<BR>Bk. 3. 34; 17. 7.<BR>--3 To blow a fire,<BR>excite fire by blowing, excite sparks;<BR>को धमेच्छांतं च पावकं Mb.<BR>--4 To<BR>manufacture by blowing.<BR>--5 To cast,<BR>blow, or throw away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्माकारः|ध्माकार
ध्माकारः A blacksmith, smith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मात
ध्मात p. p. [ध्मा-क्त]<BR>1 Blown(as a<BR>wind-instrument).<BR>--2 Blown up or<BR>into, inflamed, blown, fanned,<BR>excited.<BR>--3 Inflated, puffed, puffed up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मानं|ध्मान
ध्मानं Blowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मापनं|ध्मापन
ध्मापनं Inflating, swelling by<BR>blowing into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मापित
ध्मापित a. Reduced to ashes, burnt<BR>to cinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्मांक्ष्|ध्माङ्क्ष्
ध्मां(ध्वां)क्ष् {c1c} P. (ध्मांक्षति)<BR>1 To<BR>crow, or caw.<BR>--2 To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वांक्ष्|ध्वाङ्क्ष्
ध्मां(ध्वां)क्ष् {c1c} P. (ध्मांक्षति)<BR>1 To<BR>crow, or caw.<BR>--2 To desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यांक्षः
ध्यांक्षः see ध्वांक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात|ध्यातं
ध्यात, ध्यान, ध्यानिक &c. See<BR>under ध्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यान|ध्यानं
ध्यात, ध्यान, ध्यानिक &c. See<BR>under ध्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिक
ध्यात, ध्यान, ध्यानिक &c. See<BR>under ध्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्याम|ध्यामं
ध्याम a. Unclean, dirty, black,<BR>soiled; Bk. 8. 71.<BR>--मं A kind of<BR>grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यामन्
ध्यामन् m.<BR>1 Measure.<BR>--2 Light.<BR>--n. Meditation (less correctly<BR>ध्मामन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यै
ध्यै {c1c} P. (ध्यायति, ध्यात; desid.<BR>दिध्यासंति; pass. ध्यायते) To think of,<BR>meditate upon, ponder over,<BR>contemplate, reflect upon, imagine, call<BR>to mind; ध्यायतो विषयान् पुंसः<BR>संगस्तेषूपजायते Bg. 2. 62; न ध्यातं<BR>पदमीश्वरस्य Bh. 3. 11; पितॄन् ध्यायन्<BR>Ms. 3. 224; ध्यायंति चान्यं धिया Pt. 1. 136;<BR>Me. 3; Ms. 5. 47, 9. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्या
ध्या Thought, meditation,<BR>reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यात|ध्यातं
ध्यात p. p. [ध्यै-क्त] Thought of,<BR>meditated or reflected upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यातव्य
ध्यातव्य, ध्येय a.<BR>1 To be<BR>meditated upon, to be contemplated.<BR>--2 Fit<BR>for meditation.<BR>--3 To be imagined<BR>or conceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्येय|ध्येयः
ध्यातव्य, ध्येय a.<BR>1 To be<BR>meditated upon, to be contemplated.<BR>--2 Fit<BR>for meditation.<BR>--3 To be imagined<BR>or conceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यान|ध्यानं
ध्यान [ध्यै-भावे-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Meditation,<BR>reflection, thought, contemplation;<BR>ज्ञानाद् ध्यानं विशिष्यते Bg. 12. 12;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">Page0602-b+ 53</a>]<BR>Ms. 1. 12, 6. 72.<BR>--2 Especially,<BR>abstract contemplation, religious<BR>meditation; तदैव ध्यानादवगतोऽस्मि Ś. 7;<BR>R. 1. 73.<BR>--3 Divine intuition or<BR>discernment.<BR>--4 Mental<BR>representation of the personal attributes of a<BR>deity; इति ध्यानं.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गम्य a.<BR>attainable by meditation only.<BR>--तत्पर, --निष्ठ, --पर a. lost in thought,<BR>absorbed in meditation,<BR>contemplative.<BR>--मात्रं mere thought or<BR>reflection.<BR>--योगः profound<BR>meditation.<BR>--स्थ a. absorbed in<BR>meditation, lost in thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्यानिक
ध्यानिक a. Sought or obtained<BR>by pious contemplation or abstract<BR>meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्र
ध्र a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Holding, supporting; as in महीध्रः,<BR>कुध्रः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रज्
ध्रज्, ध्रंज् {c1c} P. (ध्रजति &c.) To go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रंज्
ध्रज्, ध्रंज् {c1c} P. (ध्रजति &c.) To go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रजि
ध्रजि f. Gliding motion (of wind)<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राजिः|ध्राजि
ध्राजिः f. Ved.<BR>1 = ध्रजिः.<BR>--2 Impulse.<BR>--3 Strong wind, storm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रण्
ध्रण् {c1c} P. (ध्रणति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रस्
ध्रस् {c9c} P., {c10c} U. (ध्रस्नाति,<BR>ध्रासयति-ते) To throw or toss up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रा
ध्रा {c1c} P. (ध्राति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राख्
ध्राख् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To be dry or arid.<BR>--2 To clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राघ्
ध्राघ् {c1c} A. To be able or<BR>competent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रांक्ष्|ध्राङ्क्ष्
ध्रांक्ष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To crow, caw.<BR>--2 To<BR>desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राड्
ध्राड् {c1c} A. To divide, split.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्राडिः|ध्राडि
ध्राडिः Gathering flowers (पुष्पचय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रिज्
ध्रिज् {c1c} P. To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रु
ध्रु {c1c} {c6c} P. (ध्रवति, ध्रुवति)<BR>1 To<BR>be firm or fixed.<BR>--2 To go, move.<BR>--3<BR>To ascertain, know definitely.<BR>--4 To<BR>kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुतिः|ध्रुति
ध्रुतिः f. Ved.<BR>1 Fixed destiny.<BR>--2<BR>Misleading, corrupting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुव|ध्रुवं|ध्रुवः
ध्रुव a.<BR>1 (a) Fixed, firm,<BR>immovable, stable, permanent,<BR>constant, unchangeable; इति<BR>ध्रुवेच्छामनुशासती सुतां Ku. 5. 5. (b) Perpetual,<BR>everlasting, eternal; ध्रुवेण भर्त्रा<BR>Ku. 7. 85; Ms. 7. 208.<BR>--2 Fixed (in<BR>astrology).<BR>--3 Certain, sure,<BR>inevitable; जातस्य हि ध्रुवो मृत्यर्ध्रुवं जन्म<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-c" target="_blank">Page0602-c+ 60</a>]<BR>मृतस्य च Bg. 2. 27; यो ध्रुवाणि<BR>परित्यज्य अध्रुवं परिषेवते Chāṇ. 63;<BR>Pt. 1. 419.<BR>--4 Retentive, tenacious; as<BR>in ध्रुवा स्मृतिः<BR>--5 Strong, fixed,<BR>settled (as a day).<BR>--वः<BR>1 The polar<BR>star; R. 17. 35; 18. 34; Ku. 7. 85.<BR>--2 The pole of any great circle.<BR>--3<BR>The distance of a planet from the<BR>beginning of the sidereal zodiac,<BR>polar longitude.<BR>--4 The Indian<BR>fig-tree.<BR>--5 A post, stake.<BR>--6 The stem<BR>or trunk (of a tree lopped off).<BR>--7<BR>The introductory stanza of a song<BR>(repeated as a kind of chorus; see<BR>Gīt.).<BR>--8 Time, epoch, era.<BR>--9 An<BR>epithet of Brahmā.<BR>--10 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>--11 Of Śiva.<BR>--12 A constant arc.<BR>--13 The tip of the nose.<BR>--14 A<BR>sacrificial vessel.<BR>--15 N. of the son of<BR>Uttānapāda and grandson of Manu.<BR>[Dhruva is the polar star, but<BR>personified in mythology as the son of Uttāna.<BR>pāda. The account of the elevation of<BR>an ordinary mortal to the position of<BR>the polar star runs thus. Uttānapāda<BR>had two wives, Suruci and Sunīti, but<BR>the latter was disliked by him. Suruci<BR>had a son named Uttama, and Sunīti<BR>gave birth to Dhruva. One day the boy<BR>tried, like his elder brother, to take a<BR>seat in his father's lap, but he was<BR>contemptuously treated both by the King<BR>and his favourite wife. The poor child<BR>went sobbing to its mother who told<BR>him in consolatory terms that fortune<BR>and favour were not attainable<BR>without hard exertions. At these words<BR>the youth left the paternal roof, retired<BR>to the woods, and, though quite a lad,<BR>performed such rigorous austerities<BR>that he was at last raised by Viṣṇu<BR>to the position of the Polar Star].<BR>--वं<BR>1 The sky, atmosphere.<BR>--2<BR>Heaven.<BR>--वा<BR>1 A sacrificial ladle<BR>(made of wood).<BR>--2 A virtuous<BR>woman.<BR>--3 A cow who stands still<BR>when being milked.<BR>--वं ind.<BR>Certainly, surely, verily; R. 8. 49;<BR>Ś. 1. 18.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षरः an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--आवर्तः the point on the<BR>crown of the head from which the<BR>hair radiate.<BR>--तारा, --तारकं the Polar<BR>star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवकः|ध्रुवक
ध्रुवकः<BR>1 The introductory stanza<BR>of a song (repeated as a sort<BR>of chorus); see भ्रुव.<BR>--2 A trunk,<BR>stem.<BR>--3 A post.<BR>--4 Polar longitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रुवि
ध्रुवि a. Ved. Firm, stable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रेक्
ध्रेक् {c1c} A. (ध्रेकते)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>--2<BR>To grow, increase.<BR>--3 To be filled<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">Page0603-a+ 56</a>]<BR>with joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0602-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रै
ध्रै {c1c} P. (ध्रायति) To be pleased or<BR>satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्रौव्यं|ध्रौव्य
ध्रौव्यं<BR>1 Fixedness, firmness,<BR>stability.<BR>--2 Duration.<BR>--3 Certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंस्
ध्वंस् {c1c} A. (ध्वंसते, ध्वस्त)<BR>1 To<BR>fall down, fall to pieces, be reduced<BR>to dust or powder; Bk. 15. 93;<BR>14. 55.<BR>--2 To drop, sink, despond;<BR>Māl. 9. 44.<BR>--3 To perish, be ruined or<BR>decayed.<BR>--4 To be eclipsed;<BR>Mu. 3. 28.<BR>--5 To be covered with dust.<BR>--6<BR>To scatter or sprinkle over.<BR>--7 To<BR>go. --Caus. (ध्वंसयति) To destroy,<BR>ruin, remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसः|ध्वंस
ध्वंसः [ध्वंस्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Falling<BR>down, sinking, falling to pieces.<BR>--2<BR>Vanishing, disappearance.<BR>--3 Loss,<BR>destruction, ruin.<BR>--सी A mote in<BR>the sun-beam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसन|ध्वंसनं
ध्वंसन a. [ध्वंस्-णिच् ल्यु]<BR>1<BR>Destroying, ruining.<BR>--2 Scattering,<BR>dispersing.<BR>--3 Sprinkling, covering.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Perishing, dying.<BR>--2 Loss,<BR>destruction.<BR>--3 Falling.<BR>--4 Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसिः|ध्वंसि
ध्वंसिः The hundredth part of a<BR>Muhūrta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसित
ध्वंसित a.<BR>1 Destroyed,<BR>demolished, ruined.<BR>--2 Removed, driven<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वंसिन्
ध्वंसिन् a.<BR>1 Destroying,<BR>demolishing, removing.<BR>--2 Falling,<BR>perishing, as in क्षणध्वंसिन्. --m. The Pīlu<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्त|ध्वस्तं
ध्वस्त p. p.<BR>1 Fallen.<BR>--2 Destroyed,<BR>removed.<BR>--3 Lost.<BR>--4 Covered.<BR>--5<BR>Eclipsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्तिः|ध्वस्ति
ध्वस्तिः f. Destruction, ruin, loss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वज्
ध्वज् {c1c} P. (ध्वजति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजः|ध्वज
ध्वजः [ध्वज्-अच्]<BR>1 A flag, banner,<BR>standard, ensign; R. 7. 40; 17. 32;<BR>Pt. 1. 26.<BR>--2 A distinguished or<BR>eminent person, the flag or<BR>ornament (at the end of comp.); as in<BR>कुलध्वजः ‘the head, ornament, or<BR>distinguished person of a family.’<BR>--3 A<BR>flag-staff.<BR>--4 A mark, emblem, sign,<BR>a symbol; वृषभ˚, मकर˚ &c.<BR>--5 The<BR>attribute of a deity.<BR>--6 The sign of<BR>a tavern.<BR>--7 The sign of a trade, any<BR>trademark.<BR>--8 The organ of<BR>generation, (of any animal, male or<BR>female).<BR>--9 One who prepares and<BR>sells liquors.<BR>--10 A house situated<BR>to the east of any object.<BR>--11 Pride.<BR>--12 Hypocrisy.<BR>--13 A skull carried<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-b" target="_blank">Page0603-b+ 56</a>]<BR>on a staff (as a mark of ascetics).<BR>--14 (In prosody) An iambic foot.<BR>(‘ध्वजीकृ to hoist a flag; fig. to use as a<BR>a plea or pretext).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुकं,<BR>--पटः, --टं a flag; R. 12. 85.<BR>--आहृत<BR>a. seized on the battle-field.<BR>--उत्थानं a festival in honor of Indra.<BR>--गृहं<BR>a room in which banners are kept.<BR>--द्रुमः the palm tree.<BR>--प्रहरणः air,<BR>wind.<BR>--भंगः --पातः inability to beget<BR>children.<BR>--यंत्रं any contrivance to<BR>which a flag-staff is fastened.<BR>--यष्टिः<BR>a flag-staff; Ms. 9. 285.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजवत्|ध्वजवन्त्
ध्वजवत् a.<BR>1 Adorned with flags.<BR>--2 Having a mark.<BR>--3 Having the<BR>mark of a criminal, branded. --m.<BR>1 A standard-bearer.<BR>--2 A vendor<BR>of spirituous liquors, distiller.<BR>--3 A<BR>Brāhmaṇa who carries with him the<BR>skull of the man murdered by him<BR>to places of pilgrimage by way of<BR>penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिकः|ध्वजिक
ध्वजिकः A hypocrite^1 (who only<BR>makes a pretence of religion).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजिन्
ध्वजिन् a. (नी f.) [ध्वजोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>1 Bearing or carrying a flag.<BR>--2<BR>Having as a mark.<BR>--3 Having the<BR>mark of a liquor-vessel (<BR>सुराभाजनचिह्न); Ms. 11. 93. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>standard-bearer.<BR>--2 A distiller or vendor<BR>of spirituous liquors; Y. 1. 141.<BR>--3<BR>A car, carriage, chariot.<BR>--4 A<BR>mountain.<BR>--5 A snake.<BR>--6 A peacock.<BR>--7<BR>A horse.<BR>--8 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--नी An<BR>army; R. 7. 40; Śi. 12. 66;<BR>Ki. 13. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वजीकरणं|ध्वजीकरण
ध्वजीकरणं<BR>1 Raising a standard,<BR>hoisting a flag.<BR>--2 Setting up as a<BR>pretext or claim, making anything<BR>a plea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वण्
ध्वण् {c1c} P. (ध्वणति) To sound;<BR>cf. ध्वन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वन्
ध्वन् {c1c} P. (ध्वनति, ध्वनित) To<BR>sound, produce or utter sounds, buzz,<BR>hum, echo, reverberate, thunder,<BR>roar; बिभिद्यमाना इव दध्वनुर्दिशः<BR>Ki. 14. 46; अयं धीरं धीरं ध्वनति नवनीलो<BR>जलधरः Bv. 1. 60; कपिर्दध्वान मेघवत्<BR>Bk. 9. 5; 14. 3; ध्वनति मधुपसमूहे<BR>श्रवणमपिदधाति Gīt. 5. --Caus. (ध्वनयति)<BR>To cause to sound, ring (as a bell);<BR>but ध्वानयति ‘to cause to articulate<BR>indistinctly’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनः|ध्वन
ध्वनः<BR>1 Sound, tune.<BR>--2 Hum,<BR>buzz.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मोदिन् m. a bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वननं|ध्वनन
ध्वननं [ध्वन्-करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Sounding.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">Page0603-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 Hinting at, suggesting or<BR>implying (as a meaning).<BR>--3 (In Rhet.)<BR>The same as व्यंजना q. v., or that<BR>power of a word or sentence by<BR>virtue of which it conveys a sense<BR>different from its primary or secondary<BR>meaning, suggestive power; cf.<BR>अंजन also.<BR>--4 Humming, indistinct<BR>utterance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनिः|ध्वनि
ध्वनिः [ध्वन्-इन्]<BR>1 Sound, echo,<BR>noise in general;<BR>मृदंगधीरध्वनिमन्वगच्छत् R. 16. 13; 2. 72; 4. 72;<BR>U. 6. 17.<BR>--2 Tune, note, tone; Śi. 6. 48.<BR>--3<BR>The sound of a musical instrument;<BR>R. 9. 71.<BR>--4 The roar or thunder of<BR>a cloud.<BR>--5 A mere empty sound.<BR>--6<BR>--word.<BR>--7 Hint, implied meaning.<BR>--8 (In Rhet.) The first and best of<BR>the three main divisions of काव्य or<BR>poetry, in which the implied or<BR>suggested sense of a passage is more<BR>striking than the expressed sense;<BR>or where the expressed sense is made<BR>subordinate to the suggested sense;<BR>इदमुत्तममतिशयिनि व्यंगे वाच्याद्ध्वनिर्बुधैः<BR>कथितः K. P. 1 (R. G. gives {5} kinds<BR>of ध्वनिः see under ध्वनि).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रहः {1} the ear. {2} hearing. {3} a<BR>fife, pipe.<BR>--विकारः a change of voice<BR>caused by fear, grief &c.; see काकु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वनित|ध्वनितः
ध्वनित p. p.<BR>1 Sounded.<BR>--2<BR>Implied, suggested, hinted at.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A<BR>sound.<BR>--2 The roar or thunder of a<BR>cloud; Ki. 5. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वानः|ध्वान
ध्वानः [ध्वन्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Sound(in<BR>general).<BR>--2 Buzzing, humming,<BR>murmuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्त|ध्वस्तं
ध्वस्त, ध्वस्ति &c. see under ध्वंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वस्ति|ध्वस्तिः
ध्वस्त, ध्वस्ति &c. see under ध्वंस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वसिर
ध्वसिर a. Ved. Destroyed; also<BR>ध्वस्मन्. ध्वस्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वांक्षः|ध्वाङ्क्ष|ध्वांक्ष|ध्वाङ्क्षः
ध्वांक्षः<BR>1 A crow. (Sometimes<BR>used at the end of comp. to show<BR>contempt; e. g. तीर्थध्वांक्षः q. v.).<BR>--2 A<BR>beggar.<BR>--3 An impudent fellow.<BR>--4<BR>A gull, crane.<BR>--5 A carpenter.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरातिः an owl.<BR>--पुष्टः the (Indian)<BR>cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वांतं|ध्वान्त|ध्वांत|ध्वान्तं
ध्वांतं Darkness; ध्वांतं<BR>नीलनिचोलचारु सुदृशां प्रत्यंगमालिंगति Gīt. 11;<BR>N. 19. 42; Śi. 4. 62.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उन्मेषः, --वित्तः a fire-fly.<BR>--शात्रवः,<BR>--अरातिः {1} the sun. {2} the moon. {3}<BR>fire. {4} the white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ध्वृ
ध्वृ {c1c} P. (ध्वरति)<BR>1 To bend.<BR>--2<BR>To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0603-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

न|नं|नः
न a.<BR>1 Thin, spare.<BR>--2 Vacant,<BR>empty.<BR>--3 Same, identical.<BR>--4<BR>Unwearied.<BR>--5 Praised.<BR>--6 Undivided.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A pearl.<BR>--2 N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR>--3 Wealth, prosperity.<BR>--4 A band,<BR>tie.<BR>--5 War.<BR>--6 N. of Buddha.<BR>--7 A<BR>gift. --ind. (a) A particle of<BR>negation equivalent to ‘not,’ ‘no,’ ‘nor,’<BR>‘neither’, and used in wishing,<BR>requesting, or commanding, but not<BR>in prohibition before the<BR>imperative mood. (b) Used with the<BR>potential mood न may sometimes<BR>have the force of ‘lest,’ ‘for fear<BR>lest,’ ‘that not;’ क्षत्रियैर्धार्यते शस्त्रं<BR>नार्तशब्दो भवेदिति Rām. (c) In<BR>agrumentative writings न often comes<BR>after इति चेत् and means ‘not so.’<BR>(d) When a negative has to be<BR>repeated in successive clauses of the<BR>same sentence or in different<BR>sentences, न may be simply repeated or<BR>may be used with particles like उत,<BR>च, अपि, चापि, वा &c.;<BR>नाधीयीताश्वमारूढो न वृक्षं न च हस्तिनं । न नावं न खरं<BR>नोष्ट्रं नेरिणत्थो न यानगः ॥ Ms. 4. 120;<BR>प्रविशंतं न मां कश्चिदपश्यन्नाप्यवारयत्<BR>Mb.; Ms. 2. 195; 3. 8, 9; 4. 15;<BR>Ś. 6. 17. Sometimes न may not be<BR>expressed in the second and other<BR>clauses, but represented only by च,<BR>वा, अपिवा; संपदि यस्य न हर्षोविपदि<BR>विषादो रणे च धीरत्वं H. 1. 33. (e) न<BR>is frequently joined with a second न<BR>or any other negative particle to<BR>intensify or emphasize an assertion;<BR>प्रत्युवाच तमृषिर्न तत्त्वतस्त्वां न वेद्मि पुरुषं<BR>पुरातनं R. 11. 85; न च न परिचितो न<BR>चाप्यगम्यः M. 1. 11; न<BR>पुनरलंकारश्रियं न पुष्यति Ś. 1; नादंड्यो नाम<BR>राज्ञोऽस्ति Ms. 8. 335; Me. 63, 106; नासौ<BR>न काम्यो न च वेद सम्यग् द्रष्टुं न सा<BR>R. 6. 30; Śi. 1. 55; Ve. 2. 10. (f) In<BR>a few cases न is retained at the<BR>beginning of a negative Tatpuruṣa<BR>compound; as नाक, नासत्य, नकुल;<BR>see P. VI. 3. 75. (g) न is often<BR>joined with other particles; नच,<BR>नवा, नैव नतु, नचेद्, नखलु &c. &c. (h)<BR>It is also used, especially in early<BR>Vedic literature, in the sense of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-b" target="_blank">Page0604-b+ 50</a>]<BR>‘like,’ ‘as,’ ‘as it were’; गावो न<BR>गव्यूतीरनु; Śi. 20. 4. v. l.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--असत्यौ<BR>(m. du.) Aśvins, the twin<BR>physicians of the gods.<BR>--एक a. ‘not<BR>one’, more than one, several,<BR>various.<BR>--(कः) an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>˚आत्मन् a. of a manifold or diverse<BR>nature. (--m.) N. of the Supreme<BR>Being. ˚चर a. ‘not living alone’,<BR>gregarious, living in society. ˚जः<BR>the Supreme Being. ˚धा ind. in<BR>many ways, diversely. ˚भेद, ˚रूप a.<BR>various, multiform. ˚शस् ind.<BR>repeatedly, often.<BR>--किंचन a. very poor,<BR>beggarly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंशुक|नंशुकः
नंशुक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Injurious,<BR>destructive.<BR>--2 Going astray, being.<BR>lost.<BR>--3 Small, minute, thin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुटं|नकुट
नकुटं The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नकुलः|नकुल
नकुलः<BR>1 The mungoose, an<BR>ichneumon; यदयं नकुलद्वेषी सकुलद्वेषी<BR>पुनः पिशुनः Vās.<BR>--2 N. of the fourth<BR>Pāṇḍava prince; अहं तस्य<BR>अतिशयितदिव्यरूपिणो नकुलस्य दर्शनेनोत्सुका जाता<BR>Ve. 2 (where नकुल has really sense<BR>1, but is taken in sense 2 by<BR>Duryodhana).<BR>--3 A son.<BR>--4 An epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--ली<BR>1 A female mungoose.<BR>--2 Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्क्
नक्क् {c10c} U. (नक्कयति-ते) To<BR>destroy completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्त|नक्तं
नक्त a. [नज्-क्त] Ashamed.<BR>--क्तं<BR>1 Night.<BR>--2 Eating only at night,<BR>as a sort of religious vow or<BR>penance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंध a. blind at<BR>night.<BR>--चर्या wandering at night.<BR>--चारिन् m. {1} an owl. {2} a cat. {3}<BR>a thief. {4} a demon, goblin, evil<BR>spirit.<BR>--भोजनं supper.<BR>--मालः N.<BR>of a tree; R. 5. 42.<BR>--मुखा evening.<BR>--व्रतं {1} fasting by day and eating<BR>at night. {2} any penance or<BR>religious rite observed at night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तं|नक्त
नक्तं ind. At night, by night;<BR>गच्छंतीनां रमणवसतिं योषितां तत्र नक्तं<BR>Me. 37; Ms. 6. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चरः<BR>{1} any animal that goes about at<BR>night. {2} a fiend, demon, goblin.<BR>{3} a thief.<BR>--चर्या wandering by<BR>night.<BR>--चारिन् m. = नक्तचारिन् q. v.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-c" target="_blank">Page0604-c+ 50</a>]<BR>--दिनं night and day.<BR>--दिनं, --दिवं<BR>ind. night and day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तन्
नक्तन् n., नक्तिः f. Ved. Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्तकः|नक्तक
नक्तकः Dirty or ragged cloth<BR>(कर्पटः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्रः|नक्र|नक्रं
नक्रः [न क्रामतीति]<BR>1 A crocodile,<BR>an alligator; नक्रः स्वस्थानमासाद्य<BR>गजेंद्रमपि कर्षति Pt. 3. 46; R. 7. 30;<BR>16. 55.<BR>--2 The sign Scorpio of the<BR>zodiac.<BR>--क्रं<BR>1 The upper timber of<BR>a door.<BR>--2 The nose.<BR>--क्रा<BR>1 The<BR>nose.<BR>--2 A swarm of bees or wasps.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--राज् m.,<BR>--राजः, --हारकः a<BR>shark or any other large<BR>sea-animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्ष्
नक्ष् {c1c} P. (नक्षति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2<BR>To come near, approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रं|नक्षत्र
नक्षत्रं [न क्षरति; cf. Uṇ. 3. 105<BR>also]<BR>1 A star in general.<BR>--2 A<BR>constellation, an asterism in the<BR>moon's path, lunar mansion;<BR>नक्षत्रताराग्रहसंकुलापि R. 6. 22; (they<BR>are twenty-seven).<BR>--3 A pearl.<BR>--4<BR>A necklace of 27 pearls.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः, ईश्वरः, --नाथः, --पः, --पतिः, --राजः<BR>the moon; R. 6. 66.<BR>--कांतिविस्तारः<BR>the white Yāvanāla flower.<BR>--चक्रं<BR>{1} the sphere of the fixed stars. {2}<BR>the lunar asterisms taken<BR>collectively.<BR>--दर्शः an astronomer or<BR>astrologer.<BR>--नेमिः {1} the moon. {2} the<BR>pole-star. {3} an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>(--मिः f.) Revatī, the last asterism.<BR>--पथः the starry sky.<BR>--पाठकः an<BR>astrologer.<BR>--पुरुषः {1} (in astr.)<BR>the figure of a man's body on the<BR>limbs of which are shown the<BR>various asterisms.<BR>--माला {1} a group<BR>of stars. {2} a necklace of<BR>twentyseven pearls. {3} the table of<BR>the asterisms in the moon's path.<BR>{4} a kind of neck-ornament of<BR>elephants;<BR>अनंगवारणशिरोनक्षत्रमालायमानेन मेखलादाम्ना K. 11.<BR>--योगः the<BR>conjunction of the moon with the<BR>lunar mansions.<BR>--लोकः the starry<BR>region, the firmament.<BR>--वर्त्मन् n.<BR>the sky.<BR>--विद्या astronomy or<BR>astrology.<BR>--वृष्टिः f. shooting or falling<BR>stars.<BR>--सूचकः a bad astrologer;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">Page0605-a+ 56</a>]<BR>तिथ्युत्पत्तिं न जानंति ग्रहाणां नैव साधनं ।<BR>परवाक्येन वर्तंते ते वै नक्षत्रसूचकाः ॥ or<BR>अविदित्वैव यः शास्त्रं दैवज्ञत्वं प्रपद्यते । स<BR>पंक्तिदूषकः पापो ज्ञेयो नक्षत्रसूचकः ॥<BR>Bṛ. S. 2. 17, 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0604-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रिन्
नक्षत्रिन् m.<BR>1 The moon.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नक्षत्रिय
नक्षत्रिय a.<BR>1 Belonging to the<BR>stars in general.<BR>--2 Twenty-seven.<BR>--3 Not a Kṣatriya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नख्
नख् {c1c} P. (नखति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखः|नख|नखं
नखः, --खं<BR>1 A nail of a finger or<BR>of a toe, claw, talon; नखानां पांडित्यं<BR>प्रकष्टयतु कस्मिन्मृगपतिः Bv. 1. 2;<BR>R. 2. 31; 12. 22.<BR>--2 The number<BR>‘twenty’.<BR>--खः A part, portion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः a scratch, nail-mark;<BR>Bv. 2. 32.<BR>--आघातः a scratch,<BR>nailwound; Māl. 5. 23.<BR>--आयुधः {1} a<BR>tiger; Māl. 3. 17. {2} a lion. {3} a<BR>cock.<BR>--आशिन् m. an owl.<BR>--कुदृः a<BR>barber.<BR>--जाहं the root of a nail.<BR>--दारणः a falcon, hawk.<BR>--(णं) a<BR>pair of nail-scissors.<BR>--निकृंतनं,<BR>--रंजनी a pair of nail-scissors,<BR>nailparer.<BR>--पदं, --व्रणः a nail-mark, or<BR>scratch; नखपदसुखान् प्राप्य<BR>वर्षाग्रबिंदून् Me. 35.<BR>--मुचः a bow.<BR>--लेखकः<BR>a nail-painter.<BR>--लेखा {1} a<BR>nailmark. {2} nail-painting.<BR>--विषः a<BR>man; नखविषा नरादयः.<BR>--विष्किरः a<BR>bird of prey (tearing with claws).<BR>--शंखः a small shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखं|नख|नखः
नखः, --खं<BR>1 A nail of a finger or<BR>of a toe, claw, talon; नखानां पांडित्यं<BR>प्रकष्टयतु कस्मिन्मृगपतिः Bv. 1. 2;<BR>R. 2. 31; 12. 22.<BR>--2 The number<BR>‘twenty’.<BR>--खः A part, portion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः a scratch, nail-mark;<BR>Bv. 2. 32.<BR>--आघातः a scratch,<BR>nailwound; Māl. 5. 23.<BR>--आयुधः {1} a<BR>tiger; Māl. 3. 17. {2} a lion. {3} a<BR>cock.<BR>--आशिन् m. an owl.<BR>--कुदृः a<BR>barber.<BR>--जाहं the root of a nail.<BR>--दारणः a falcon, hawk.<BR>--(णं) a<BR>pair of nail-scissors.<BR>--निकृंतनं,<BR>--रंजनी a pair of nail-scissors,<BR>nailparer.<BR>--पदं, --व्रणः a nail-mark, or<BR>scratch; नखपदसुखान् प्राप्य<BR>वर्षाग्रबिंदून् Me. 35.<BR>--मुचः a bow.<BR>--लेखकः<BR>a nail-painter.<BR>--लेखा {1} a<BR>nailmark. {2} nail-painting.<BR>--विषः a<BR>man; नखविषा नरादयः.<BR>--विष्किरः a<BR>bird of prey (tearing with claws).<BR>--शंखः a small shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखंपच|नखम्पच
नखंपच a. Nail-scorching;<BR>Śi. 9. 85; P. III. 2. 34 Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखरः|नखर|नखरं
नखरः --रं [नखं राति, रा-क नख बा˚<BR>उणा˚ अर वा] A fingernail, claw,<BR>talon; Bv. 1. 52.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आयुधः<BR>{1} a tiger. {2} a lion. {3} a cock.<BR>--आह्वः fragrant oleander (करवीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखरं|नखर|नखरः
नखरः --रं [नखं राति, रा-क नख बा˚<BR>उणा˚ अर वा] A fingernail, claw,<BR>talon; Bv. 1. 52.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आयुधः<BR>{1} a tiger. {2} a lion. {3} a cock.<BR>--आह्वः fragrant oleander (करवीर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखानखि
नखानखि ind. [नखैर्नखैः प्रहृत्येदं युद्धं<BR>प्रवृत्तं] Nail against nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नखिन्
नखिन् a. [नखः अस्त्यस्य-इनि]<BR>1<BR>Having or armed with nails, claws,<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Thorny. --m. Any animal<BR>armed with claws, such as a tiger or<BR>lion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगः|नग
नगः [न गच्छति, गम्-ड]<BR>1 A<BR>mountain; Ku. 1. 1; 7. 72;<BR>Śi. 6. 79.<BR>--2 A tree.<BR>--3 A plant in general.<BR>--4 The sun.<BR>--5 A serpent.<BR>--6 The<BR>number ‘seven’.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अटनः a<BR>monkey.<BR>--अधिपः, --अधिराजः, --इंद्रः<BR>{1} Himālaya (the lord of mountains).<BR>{2} the Sumeru mountain.<BR>--अरिः<BR>an epithet of Indra.<BR>--आवासः a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">Page0605-b+ 56</a>]<BR>peacock.<BR>--उच्छ्रायः the height of a<BR>mountain.<BR>--ओकस् m. {1} a bird (in<BR>general). {2} a crow. {3} a lion. {4}<BR>the fabulous animal called शरभ.<BR>--ज a. produced in a mountain,<BR>mountain-born; Bk. 10. 9.<BR>--(जः)<BR>an elephant.<BR>--जा, --नंदिनी epithets of<BR>Pārvatī.<BR>--पतिः {1} the Himālaya<BR>mountain. {2} the moon (as the<BR>lord of plants and herbs).<BR>--भिद् m.<BR>{1} an axe. {2} an epithet of Indra.<BR>{3} a crow.<BR>--मूर्धन् m. the crest or<BR>brow of a mountain.<BR>--रंध्रकरः an<BR>epithet of Kārtikeya; R. 9. 2.<BR>--वाहनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरं|नगर
नगरं [नगा इव प्रासादाः संत्यत्र बा˚ र;<BR>cf. P. V. 2. 107 Vārt.] A town,<BR>city (opp. ग्राम); नगरगमनाय मतिं न<BR>करोति Ś. 2.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिकृतः,<BR>--अधिपः, --अध्यक्षः {1} the chief magistrate<BR>of a town, head police-officer. {2}<BR>governor or superintendent of a<BR>town.<BR>--अभ्याशः --सः the vicinity of a<BR>town.<BR>--उपांतः a suburb, the skirt of<BR>a town.<BR>--ओकस् m. a townsman.<BR>--काकः ‘a town-crow’, an<BR>expression of contempt.<BR>--कीर्तनं repeating<BR>the name of a god while wandering<BR>through a city.<BR>--घातः an elephant.<BR>--जनः {1} townsfolk. {2} a citizen.<BR>--प्रदक्षिणा carrying an idol round a<BR>city in procession.<BR>--प्रांतः a suburb.<BR>--मर्दिन् m. an intoxicated elephant.<BR>--मार्गः a principal road, high-way.<BR>--रक्षा superintendence or<BR>government of a town.<BR>--रक्षिन् m. {1} the<BR>superintendent of a town. {2} a<BR>town-watchman.<BR>--स्थः a<BR>townsman, citizen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरी
नगरी = नगर q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काकः<BR>the (Indian) crane.<BR>--बकः a crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नगरीय
नगरीय a. [नगर-छ] Belonging to<BR>a town, urban, civil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्न|नग्नः
नग्न See under नज् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंगः|नङ्ग|नंग|नङ्गः
नंगः A lover, paramour(जार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नचिकेतस्
नचिकेतस् m. An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नचिर
नचिर a. See अचिर; Bg. 5. 6; 12. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नज्
नज् {c1c} A. (नजते) To be ashamed,<BR>modest or bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्न|नग्नः
नग्न a. [नज्-न-कर्तरि क्त तस्य नः]<BR>1<BR>Naked, nude, bare; न नग्नः<BR>स्नानमाचरेत् Ms. 4. 45; नग्नक्षपणके देशे रजकः<BR>किं करिष्यति Chāṇ. 110.<BR>--2<BR>Uncultivated, uninhabited, desolate.<BR>--ग्नः<BR>1 A naked mendicant.<BR>--2 A Buddhist<BR>mendicant (क्षपणक).<BR>--3 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">Page0605-c+ 57</a>]<BR>hypocrite.<BR>--4 A bard accompanying an<BR>army, or a wandering bard.<BR>--5 N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--ग्ना<BR>1 A naked, shameless (or<BR>wanton) woman.<BR>--2 A girl before<BR>menstruation, or less than 12 or 10<BR>(and therefore may go about naked).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अटः, --अटकः {1} one who<BR>goes about naked. {2} especially a<BR>Jaina or Buddhist mendicant (of<BR>the दिगंबर class).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नक|नग्नकः
नग्नक a. (ग्निका f.) Naked, nude.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A naked mendicant.<BR>--2 A<BR>Jaina or Buddhist mendicant (of<BR>the दिगंबर class).<BR>--3 A bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नका
नग्नका, --नग्निका<BR>1 A naked,<BR>shameless (or wanton) woman.<BR>--2 A<BR>girl before menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्निका
नग्नका, --नग्निका<BR>1 A naked,<BR>shameless (or wanton) woman.<BR>--2 A<BR>girl before menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नंकरणं|नग्नङ्करण
नग्नंकरणं Making naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नंभविष्णु
नग्नंभविष्णु, --भावुक a. Becoming<BR>naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नंभावुक
नग्नंभविष्णु, --भावुक a. Becoming<BR>naked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नीकृ
नग्नीकृ {c8c} U. To make naked, to<BR>convert into a naked (Jaina)<BR>mendicant; Pt. 4. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नग्नीकृत
नग्नीकृत a.<BR>1 Made naked,<BR>undressed.<BR>--2 Converted into a naked<BR>mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नञ्
नञ् ind. The technical term for<BR>the negative particle न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट्
नट् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (नटति, the न not<BR>changed to ण after प्र in the sense<BR>of ‘hurting’)<BR>1 To dance; यदि<BR>मनसा नटनीयं Gīt. 4.<BR>--2 To act.<BR>--3<BR>To injure (by a deceptive trick).<BR>--Caus. (नाटयति-ते)<BR>1 To act,<BR>gesticulate, represent dramatically (in<BR>dramas); शरसंधानं नाटयति Ś. 1. &c.<BR>--2 To imitate, copy;<BR>स्फटिककटकभूमिर्नाटयत्येष शैलः… अधिगतधवलिम्नः<BR>शूलपाणेरभिख्यां Śi. 4. 65. (N. B.<BR>नट् forms नटयति in the sense<BR>of ‘causing to dance’; Bh. 3. 126).<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} U. (नाटयति-ते)<BR>1 To drop<BR>or fall.<BR>--2 To shine.<BR>--3 To injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटः|नट
नटः [नट्-अच्]<BR>1 A dancer; न नटा<BR>न विटा न गायकाः Bh. 3. 27.<BR>--2 An<BR>actor; कुर्वन्नयं प्रहसनस्य नटः कृतोऽसि<BR>Bh. 3. 126, 112.<BR>--3 The son of a<BR>degraded Kṣatriya.<BR>--4 The Aśoka<BR>tree.<BR>--5 A kind of reed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतिका shame, modesty.<BR>--ईश्वरः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--चर्या the<BR>performance of an actor.<BR>--भूषणः,<BR>--मंडनः (yellow) orpiment.<BR>--रंगः a<BR>theatrical stage.<BR>--वरः ‘the chief<BR>actor’, the Sūtradhāra of a drama.<BR>--संज्ञकं yellow orpiment.<BR>--(कः) an<BR>actor, dancer.<BR>--सूत्रं directions or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">Page0606-a+ 55</a>]<BR>rules for actors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0605-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटकः|नटक
नटकः An actor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटनं|नटन
नटनं [नट् भवे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Dancing,<BR>dance.<BR>--2 Acting, gesticulation,<BR>dramatic representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटितं|नटित
नटितं Representation, gesticulation,<BR>acting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नटी
नटी<BR>1 An actress.<BR>--2 The chief<BR>actress (regarded as the wife of<BR>the Sūtradhāra).<BR>--3 A courtezan,<BR>harlot.<BR>--4 Red arsenic.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सु<BR>तः the son of a dancing girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नट्या
नट्या A company of actors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडः|नड|नडं
नडः --डं A species of reed.<BR>--डः<BR>N. of a tribe preparing a sort of<BR>bracelets.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अगारं, --आगारं a<BR>hut of reeds.<BR>--प्राय a. abounding<BR>in reeds.<BR>--भक्तं a place abounding<BR>in reeds.<BR>--वनं a thicket of reeds.<BR>--संहतिः f. a collection or quantity<BR>of reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडं|नड|नडः
नडः --डं A species of reed.<BR>--डः<BR>N. of a tribe preparing a sort of<BR>bracelets.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अगारं, --आगारं a<BR>hut of reeds.<BR>--प्राय a. abounding<BR>in reeds.<BR>--भक्तं a place abounding<BR>in reeds.<BR>--वनं a thicket of reeds.<BR>--संहतिः f. a collection or quantity<BR>of reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडकं|नडक
नडकं A bone between the<BR>shoulders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडश
नडश a. (शी f.) Covered with<BR>reeds; (also नडकीय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडिनी
नडिनी<BR>1 A quantity of reeds.<BR>--2<BR>A reed-bed, a river abounding in<BR>reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडिल
नडिल a., नड्वत् a. (ती f.)<BR>Abounding in or covered with reeds,<BR>reedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्या
नड्या A quantity of reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नड्वल|नड्वलः
नड्वल a. Abounding in reeds.<BR>--लं,<BR>--ला A quantity or a bed of reeds;<BR>यो नड्वलानीव गजः परेषां<BR>बलान्यमृद्गान्नलिनाभवक्त्रः R. 18. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नडह|नडहः
नडह a. Beautiful, lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नत|नतं|नतः
नत p. p. [नम्-क्त]<BR>1 Bent, bowed,<BR>stooping, inclined.<BR>--2 Sunk,<BR>depressed.<BR>--3 Crooked, curved.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The<BR>distance of any planet from the meridian.<BR>--2 The zenith distance at a meridian<BR>transit.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः zenith<BR>distance.<BR>--अंग a. {1} bending the body.<BR>{2} stooping, bowed.<BR>--(गी) {1} a<BR>woman with stooping limbs. {2} a<BR>woman in general.<BR>--उन्नत a. high<BR>and low; Ś. 4. 15.<BR>--नाडी, --नाडिका<BR>{1} the distance in time of any planet<BR>from the meridian. {2} any hour of<BR>birth after noon or before midnight.<BR>--नासिक a. flat-nosed.<BR>--पर्वन् a.<BR>flatjointed.<BR>--भ्रूः a woman with curved<BR>eye-brows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नतिः|नति
नतिः f. [नम्-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>1 Bending,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-b" target="_blank">Page0606-b+ 57</a>]<BR>stooping, bowing.<BR>--2 Curvature,<BR>crookedness.<BR>--3 Bending the body<BR>in salutation, a bow, courtesy.<BR>--4<BR>Parallax in latitude (in astronomy).<BR>--5 The change of a dental to a<BR>lingual letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्
नद् {c1c} P. (नदति, नदित)<BR>1 To<BR>sound, resound, thunder (as a<BR>cloud &c); वामश्चायं नदति मधुरं<BR>चातकस्ते सगंधः Me. 9; नदत्याकाशगंगायाः<BR>स्रोतस्युद्दामदिग्गजे R. 1. 78; Śi. 5. 63;<BR>Bk. 2. 4.<BR>--2 To speak, shout, cry,<BR>roar, (often with words like शब्द,<BR>स्वन, नाद &c. as object); ननाद<BR>बलवन्नादं, शब्दं घोरतरं नदंति Mb.<BR>--3 To<BR>vibrate. --Caus. (नादयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>fill with noise, make noisy or<BR>resonant.<BR>--2 To cause to make a<BR>sound. --WITH उद् to roar, cry<BR>(loudly), bellow (as a bull);<BR>Ku. 1. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदः|नद
नदः [नदति शब्दायते-अच्]<BR>1 A river.<BR>great river (such as the Indus);<BR>Śi. 4. 66 (where Malli. remarks:<BR>--प्राक्स्रेतसो नद्यः प्रत्यक्स्रोतसो नदानर्मदां विनेत्यहुः).<BR>--2 A stream, flowing stream, rivulet;<BR>Ki. 5. 27.<BR>--3 The ocean.<BR>--4 Ved.<BR>A horse.<BR>--5 A cloud.<BR>--6 A praiser<BR>(ऋषि).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिः, --राजः the<BR>ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदथुः|नदथु
नदथुः [नद्-अयुच्]<BR>1 Noise, roaring.<BR>--2 The roaring of a bull.<BR>--3 Crying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदनुः|नदनु
नदनुः<BR>1 A lion.<BR>--2 Sounding,<BR>roaring.<BR>--3 The sound of praise.<BR>--4<BR>War, battle.<BR>--5 A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदिः|नदि
नदिः Ved. Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदिका
नदिका A small river, rivulet,<BR>rill, brook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदी
नदी A river, any flowing stream;<BR>रविपीतजला तपात्यये पुतरोघेन हि युज्यते<BR>नदी Ku. 4. 44.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईनः, --ईशः,<BR>--कांतः the ocean.<BR>--कांता {1} the<BR>roseapple. {2} a shrub.<BR>--कूलप्रियः a kind<BR>of reed.<BR>--ज a. aquatic.<BR>--(जः) {1} an<BR>epithet of Bhīṣma. {2}<BR>antimony.<BR>--(जं) a lotus.<BR>--तरस्थानं<BR>a landing-place, ferry.<BR>--दोहः<BR>freight, river-toll, fare.<BR>--धरः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--पंकः the marshy<BR>bank of a river.<BR>--पतिः, --ईनः {1} the<BR>ocean. {2} an epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>--पूरः a river which has overflown<BR>its banks.<BR>--भवं river-salt.<BR>--मातृक<BR>a. watered by rivers, irrigated,<BR>supplied with the water of rivers, canals<BR>&c. (as a country &c.); N. 3. 38;<BR>cf. देवमातृक.<BR>--रयः the current of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">Page0606-c+ 55</a>]<BR>river.<BR>--वंकः the bend or arm of a<BR>river.<BR>--ष्णः (स्नः) {1} bathing in<BR>rivers. {2} knowing the dangerous<BR>spots in rivers, their depth, course<BR>&c.; ततः सताज्ञापयदाशु<BR>सर्वानानायिनस्तद्विचये नदीष्णान् R. 16. 75; (hence)<BR>{3} experienced, clever.<BR>--सर्जः the<BR>Arjuna tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्य
नद्य a. Connected with a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नदाल
नदाल a. Fortunate.<BR>--लं A<BR>potsherd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्ध|नद्धः
नद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Tied, bound,<BR>fastened, bound, round, put on.<BR>--2<BR>Covered, inlaid, interwoven.<BR>--3 Joined,<BR>connected; see नह्.<BR>--द्धं A tie, band,<BR>bond, knot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्धिः|नद्धि
नद्धिः Binding, fastening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नद्ध्री
नद्ध्री A leather-strap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननंदृ|ननन्दृ
ननंदृ, ननांदृ A husband's sister;<BR>ननांदृः पत्या च देव्याः संदिष्टमृष्यशृंगेण<BR>U. 1.<BR>--Comp. ननांदृपतिः (also ननांदुःपतिः)<BR>the husband of a husband's sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननांदृ|ननान्दृ
ननंदृ, ननांदृ A husband's sister;<BR>ननांदृः पत्या च देव्याः संदिष्टमृष्यशृंगेण<BR>U. 1.<BR>--Comp. ननांदृपतिः (also ननांदुःपतिः)<BR>the husband of a husband's sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नना
नना Ved.<BR>1 Speech.<BR>--2 Mother.<BR>--3 A daughter; Rv. 9. 112. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ननु
ननु ind. (Originally a<BR>combination of न and नु, now used as a<BR>separate word) A particle implying:<BR>1 Inquiry or interrogation; ननु<BR>समाप्तकृत्यो गौतमः M. 4.<BR>--2 Surely,<BR>certainly, indeed, is it not indeed (with<BR>an interrogative force); यदाऽ<BR>मेधाविनी शिष्योपदेशं मलिनयति तदाचार्यस्य<BR>दोषो ननु M. 1.<BR>--3 Of course, indeed,<BR>certainly (अवधारणं); उपपन्नं ननु शिवं<BR>सप्तस्वंगेषु R. 1. 60; त्रिलोकनाथेन सदा<BR>मखद्विषस्त्वया नियम्या ननु दिव्यचक्षुषा<BR>3. 45.<BR>--4 It is used as a vocative<BR>particle meaning ‘O’, ‘Oh’; ननु<BR>मानव Dk.; ननु मूर्खाः पठितमेव<BR>युष्माभिस्तत्कांडे U. 4.<BR>--5 It is used in<BR>propitiatory expressions in the sense of<BR>‘pray’, ‘be pleased’; ननु मां प्रापय<BR>पत्युरंतिकं Ku. 4. 32.<BR>--6 It is<BR>sometimes used as a corrective word like<BR>the English ‘why, or’ ‘I say’; ननु<BR>पदे परिवृत्य भण Mk. 5; ननु भणाभि<BR>चिंतित उपाय इति V. 2.; ननु भवानग्रतो<BR>मे वर्तते Ś. 2; ननु विचिनोतु भवान्<BR>V. 2.<BR>--7 In argumentative discussions<BR>ननु is frequently used to head an<BR>objection or advance a contrary<BR>proposition (generally followed by<BR>उच्यते); नन्वचेतनान्येव वृश्चिकादिशरीराणि<BR>अचेतनानां च गोमयादीनां कार्याणीति<BR>उच्यते Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0606-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंद्|नन्द्
नंद् {c1c} P. (नंदति, नंदित) To be glad,<BR>be pleased, delighted or satisfied,<BR>rejoice at (anything);<BR>ननंदतुस्तत्सदृशेन तत्समौ R. 3. 23, 11; 2. 22;<BR>4. 3; Bk. 15. 28. --Caus. (नंदयति-ते)<BR>To please, delight, gladden, make<BR>happy; अंतर्हिते शशिनि सैव कुमुद्वती मे<BR>दृष्टिं न नंदयति संस्मरणीयशोभा Ś. 4. 2;<BR>Bk. 2. 16; R. 9. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदः|नन्द|नंद|नन्दः
नंदः [नंद्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Happiness,<BR>pleasure, joy.<BR>--2 A kind of lute<BR>(11 inches long).<BR>--3 A frog.<BR>--4<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--5 N. of a cowherd,<BR>husband of Yaśodā and foster-father<BR>of Kṛṣṇa (to whose care the<BR>child was committed when Kaṃsa<BR>wanted to destroy it).<BR>--6 N. of the<BR>founder of the Nanda dynasty; or<BR>of nine brother-kings of Pāṭaliputra<BR>killed by the machinations of<BR>Chāṇakya, the minister of<BR>Chandragupta; समुत्खाता नंदा नव हृदयरोगा इव<BR>भुवः Mu. 1. 13; अगृहीते राक्षसे<BR>किमुत्खातं नंदवंशस्य Mu. 1, 3. 27, 28.<BR>--7<BR>One of the nine treasures of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--दी An epithet of Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मजः, --नंदनः an epithet<BR>of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--पालः an epithet of<BR>Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदक|नन्दक|नन्दकः
नंदक a. [नंद्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 Rejoicing,<BR>making happy, gladdening.<BR>--2<BR>Delighting or rejoicing in.<BR>--3<BR>Gladdening a family.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A frog.<BR>--2<BR>N. of the sword of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--3 A<BR>sword in general.<BR>--4 Happiness.<BR>--5<BR>Nanda, the foster-father of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदकिः|नन्दकि|नन्दकिः
नंदकिः Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदकिन्|नन्दकिन्
नंदकिन् m. An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदथुः|नन्दथु|नंदथु|नन्दथुः
नंदथुः Happiness, pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदन|नन्दन|नन्दनं|नन्दनः
नंदन a. [नंद्-ल्यु] Delighting,<BR>pleasing, gladdening; Ś. 7; Māl. 9. 21.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A son; Y. 1. 274; R. 3. 41.<BR>--2 A frog.<BR>--3 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--4 N. of Śiva.<BR>--5 N. of the<BR>twentysixth year (संवत्सर).<BR>--ना A daughter.<BR>--नं<BR>1 N. of the garden of Indra, the<BR>Elysium; अभिज्ञाश्छेदपातानां क्रियंते<BR>नंदनद्रुमाः Ku. 2. 41; R. 8. 95.<BR>--2 Rejoicing, being glad.<BR>--3 Joy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं yellow sandal-wood<BR>(हरिचंदन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदनकः|नन्दनक|नन्दनकः
नंदनकः A son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदंत|नन्दन्त|नन्दन्तः
नंदंत a. Delighting, making happy.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A son.<BR>--2 A friend.<BR>--3 A<BR>king or prince.<BR>--ती A daughter<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदा
नंदा [नंदयति नंद्-अच्]<BR>1 Delight,<BR>joy, happiness.<BR>--2 Affluence, wealth,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-b" target="_blank">Page0607-b+ 56</a>]<BR>prosperity.<BR>--3 A small earthen<BR>water jar.<BR>--4 A husband's sister.<BR>--5<BR>The first, sixth and eleventh days<BR>of a lunar fortnight (considered as<BR>auspicious tithis).<BR>--6 An epithet of<BR>Gaurī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदिः|नन्दि|नंदि|नन्दिः
नंदिः m. f. [नंद्-इन्] Joy, pleasure,<BR>delight; कौसल्यानदिवर्धनः.<BR>--दिः m.<BR>1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 Of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--3 N. of an attendant of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--4 Gambling, gaming; (n.<BR>also in this sense).<BR>--5 The speaker<BR>of a prelude or benediction (in a<BR>drama.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवर्तः a sort of<BR>building in the form of a<BR>quadrangle without a western gate; (n.<BR>also).<BR>--ईशः, --ईश्वरः {1} an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--ग्रामः N. of a village where<BR>Bharata lived during Rāma's<BR>banishment; R. 12. 18.<BR>--घोषः {1} N. of<BR>the chariot of Arjuna. {2} a sound<BR>of joy. {3} the proclamation of a<BR>herald.<BR>--तूर्यं a musical instrument<BR>played on festive occasions.<BR>--वर्धनः<BR>{1} an epithet of Śiva, {2} a friend.<BR>{3} the end of a lunar fortnight, i. e.<BR>the day of new or full moon. {4}<BR>a son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदिकः|नन्दिक|नंदिक|नन्दिकः
नंदिकः<BR>1 Joy, pleasure.<BR>--2 A<BR>small water-jar.<BR>--3 An attendant of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--का<BR>1 A small water-jar.<BR>--2<BR>= नंदा (5) above.<BR>--3 N. of Indra's<BR>pleasure-ground.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः,<BR>--ईश्वरः {1} N. of one of Śiva's chief<BR>attendants. {2} N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नंदिन्|नन्दिन्
नंदिन् a. [नंद्-णिनि]<BR>1 Happy,<BR>pleased, glad, delighted.<BR>--2 Making<BR>happy, gladdening, giving delight;<BR>U. 3. 14.<BR>--3 Delighting in, liking.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A son.<BR>--2 The speaker of a<BR>prelude or benediction in a drama.<BR>--3 N. of the doorkeeper of Śiva,<BR>his chief attendant, or of the bull<BR>which he rides; लतागृहद्वारगतोऽथ नंदी<BR>Ku. 3. 41; Māl. 1. 1.<BR>--4 An<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--5 The Indian<BR>fig-tree.<BR>--नी<BR>1 A daughter; U. 1. 9.<BR>--2 A husband's sister<BR>--3 A fabulous<BR>cow, daughter of Surabhi, yielding<BR>all desires (कामधेनु) and in the<BR>possession of the sage Vasiṣṭha;<BR>अनिंद्या नंदिनी नाम धेनुराववृते वनात्<BR>R. 1. 82, 2. 69.<BR>--4 An epithet of the<BR>Ganges.<BR>--5 The holy basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपराजित्
नपराजित् m. An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपात्
नपात् m.<BR>1 A grandson (usually<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">Page0607-c+ 56</a>]<BR>restricted to the Vedas), as in त<BR>नूनपात्.<BR>--2 A descendant, son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंस्
नपुंस् m., नपुंसः Not a man, a<BR>eunuch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसकः|नपुंसक|नपुंसकं
नपुंसकः, --कं [न पुमान् न स्त्री]<BR>1 A<BR>hermaphrodite (neither man, nor<BR>woman).<BR>--2 An impotent man, a<BR>eunuch.<BR>--3 A coward.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A<BR>word in the neuter gender.<BR>--2 The<BR>neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नपुंसकं|नपुंसक|नपुंसकः
नपुंसकः, --कं [न पुमान् न स्त्री]<BR>1 A<BR>hermaphrodite (neither man, nor<BR>woman).<BR>--2 An impotent man, a<BR>eunuch.<BR>--3 A coward.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A<BR>word in the neuter gender.<BR>--2 The<BR>neuter gender.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नप्तृ
नप्तृ m. A grandson (a son's<BR>or daughter's son).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्
नभ् {c1c} A. (नभते)<BR>1 To hurt,<BR>injure; सुग्रीवः प्रघसं नेभे Bk. 14. 33.<BR>--2<BR>To be torn or rent, to burst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्
नभ् f. Ved. Hurt, injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ|नभः
नभ a. Killing, hurting.<BR>--भः The<BR>month Śrāvaṇa.<BR>--भं The sky,<BR>atmosphere.<BR>--भा A spitting-pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभनु
नभनु a. Ved. Hurting.<BR>--नु f. A<BR>river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभन्यु
नभन्यु a. Ved.<BR>1 Injuring,<BR>destroying.<BR>--2 Ethereal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्
नभस् n. [नह्यते मेघैः नह्-असुन्<BR>भश्चांतादेशः; cf. Uṇ. 4. 210]<BR>1 The sky,<BR>atmosphere; R. 5. 29; Bg. 1. 19;<BR>Rs. 1. 11.<BR>--2 A cloud.<BR>--3 Fog,<BR>vapour.<BR>--4 Water.<BR>--5 Period of<BR>life, age. --m.<BR>1 The rains or rainy<BR>season.<BR>--2 The nose, smell.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of the month of Śrāvaṇa<BR>(corresponding to July-August), (said to be<BR>n. also in this sense); प्रत्यासन्ने नभसि<BR>दयिताजीवितालंबनार्थी Me. 4;<BR>R. 12. 29; 17. 41; 18. 6.<BR>--4 The fibres in<BR>the root of the lotus.<BR>--5 A<BR>spittingpot. --(Dual) Both the worlds,<BR>heaven and earth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंबुपः the<BR>Cātaka bird.<BR>--केतनः, --पांथः the sun.<BR>--क्रातिन् m. a lion.<BR>--ग a. going in<BR>the sky (as a star, god, bird &c.).<BR>--गजः a cloud.<BR>--गति f. soaring,<BR>flying.<BR>--चक्षुस् m. the sun.<BR>--चमसः<BR>{1} the moon. {2} magic.<BR>--चर a.<BR>moving in the sky; Ku. 5. 23.<BR>--(रः)<BR>{1} a god or demi-god; R. 18. 6. {2}<BR>a bird.<BR>--तलं {1} the atmosphere. {2}<BR>the lower region of the sky.<BR>--दुहः a<BR>cloud.<BR>--दृष्टि a. {1} blind. {2} looking<BR>towards the sky.<BR>--द्वीपः, --धूमः a<BR>cloud.<BR>--नदी the celestial Ganges.<BR>--प्राणः wind.<BR>--मणिः the sun.<BR>--मंडलं the firmament, the atmosphere;<BR>नेदं नभोमंडलमंबुराशिः S. D. 10. ˚दीपः<BR>the moon.<BR>--योनिः an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--रजस् n. darkness.<BR>--रेणुः f.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">Page0608-a+ 56</a>]<BR>fog, mist.<BR>--लयः smoke.<BR>--लिह् a.<BR>licking the sky, lofty, very high;<BR>cf. अभ्रांलिह.<BR>--श्वासः wind.<BR>--सद् m.<BR>{1} a bird. {2} a star. {3} a god;<BR>Śi. 1. 11.<BR>--सरित् f. {1} the milky way. {2}<BR>the celestial Ganges.<BR>--स्थलः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--स्थली the sky.<BR>--स्पृश्<BR>a. reaching the sky, lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0607-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस|नभसं|नभसः
नभस a. Vapoury, misty.<BR>--सः<BR>1<BR>The sky.<BR>--2 The rainy season.<BR>--3<BR>The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभसंगमः|नभसङ्गम|नभसंगम|नभसङ्गमः
नभसंगमः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्य|नभस्यः
नभस्य a. Vapoury, foggy.<BR>--स्यः<BR>N. of the month Bhādrapada<BR>(corresponding to August-September);<BR>R. 9. 54, 12. 29, 17. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभस्वत्|नभस्वन्त्
नभस्वत् a.<BR>1 Vaporous, misty,<BR>cloudy.<BR>--2 Young. --m. The wind,<BR>air; N. 1. 97; R. 4. 8; 10. 73,<BR>Śi. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्य|नभ्यं
नभ्य a. Cloudy, misty.<BR>--भ्यं The<BR>central part of a wheel; cf. नाभि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभाकः|नभाक|नभाकं
नभाकः<BR>1 Darkness.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Rāhu.<BR>--3 A cloud.<BR>--4 The<BR>sky.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नभ्राज्
नभ्राज् m. A dark cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्
नम् {c1c} P., sometimes A. (नमति-ते,<BR>ननाम, अनंसीत्, नंस्यति, नत; caus.<BR>नमयति-ते or नामयति-ते, but with a<BR>preposition नमयति only; desid. निनंसति)<BR>1 To bow to, make obeisance to,<BR>salute (as a mark of respect) (with<BR>acc. or dat.); इयं नमति वः सर्वान्<BR>त्रिलोचनवधूरिति Ku. 6. 89; Bg. 11. 37;<BR>Bk. 9. 51, 10. 31; 12. 39;<BR>Śi. 4. 57.<BR>--2 To submit or subject oneself,<BR>bow down; अशक्तः संधिमान् नमेत्<BR>Kām. 8. 55.<BR>--3 To bend, sink;<BR>go down; अनंसीद्भूर्भरेणास्य Bk. 15. 25.<BR>नेमुः सर्वदिशः K. 55; उन्नमति नमति<BR>वर्षति…मेघः Mk. 5. 26.<BR>--4 To stoop,<BR>be inclined.<BR>--5 To be bent or<BR>curved.<BR>--6 To sound.<BR>--7 To change a<BR>dental to a lingual letter. --Caus.<BR>1 To bend, make curved.<BR>--2 To<BR>bend (as a bow); Ś. 2. 3.<BR>--3<BR>To cause to sink.<BR>--4 To prevent,<BR>ward off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमत|नमतः
नमत a. [नम्-अतच्] Bent, bowed,<BR>crooked, curved.<BR>--तः<BR>1 An actor.<BR>--2 Smoke.<BR>--3 A master, lord.<BR>--4 A<BR>cloud.<BR>--तं Woollen stuff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमनं|नमन|नमनः
नमनं [नम्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Bowing down,<BR>bending, stooping.<BR>--2 Sinking.<BR>--3<BR>A bow, salutation, obeisance.<BR>--नः<BR>One who causes to bend or bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्
नमस् ind.<BR>1 A bow, salutation,<BR>obeisance, adoration; (this word is,<BR>by itself, invariably used with dat.;<BR>तस्मै वदान्यगुरवे तरवे नमोऽस्तु<BR>Bv. 1. 94; नमस्त्रिमूर्तये तुभ्यं Ku. 2. 4; but<BR>with कृ, generally with acc.; मुनित्रयं<BR>नमस्कृत्य Sk.; but sometimes with<BR>dat. also; नमस्कुर्मो नृसिंहाय ibid. The<BR>word has the sense of a noun, but<BR>is treated as an indeclinable.)<BR>--2<BR>Ved. Food.<BR>--3 A thunderbolt.<BR>--4<BR>A gift, present.<BR>--5 A sacrifice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः, --कृतिः f.<BR>--करणं<BR>bowing, respectful or reverential<BR>salutation, respectful obeisance (made by<BR>uttering the word नमस्).<BR>--कृत a.<BR>{1} bowed down to, saluted. {2}<BR>revered, adored, worshipped.<BR>--गुरुः<BR>{1} a spiritual teacher. {2} a<BR>Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--वाकं ind. uttering the word<BR>नमस्, i. e. making a low obeisance;<BR>इदं कविभ्यः पूर्वेभ्यो नमोवाकं प्रशास्महे<BR>U. 1. 1.<BR>--वृध् m. a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस|नमसः
नमस a. Favourable, kindly<BR>disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमसित|नमसितः
नमसित, नमस्यित a. Reversd,<BR>respected, saluted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यित|नमस्यितः
नमसित, नमस्यित a. Reversd,<BR>respected, saluted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यति
नमस्यति Den. P.<BR>1 To bow down<BR>to, pay homage to, worship;<BR>Bh. 2. 94.<BR>--2 To act humbly towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्य|नमस्यः
नमस्य a.<BR>1 Entitled to obeisance,<BR>revered, respectable, adorable.<BR>--2<BR>Respectful, humble.<BR>--स्या<BR>Worship, adoration, reverence, obeisance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमस्यु
नमस्यु a. Ved. Worshipping,<BR>saluting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमित|नमितः
नमित a. Bowed, bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्य
नम्य a. Venerable, respectable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्र|नम्रः
नम्र a. [नम्-र]<BR>1 Bowing,<BR>bowing down, bent, inclined, hanging<BR>down; भवंति नम्रास्तरवः फलागमैः<BR>Ś. 5. 12; स्तोकनम्रा स्तनाभ्यां Me. 82;<BR>Pt. 1. 106; Ratn. 1. 19.<BR>--2 Bowing<BR>down, making a low obeisance;<BR>अभूच्च नम्रः प्रणिपातशिक्षया R. 3. 25;<BR>इत्युच्यते ताभिरुमा स्म नम्रा Ku. 7. 28.<BR>--3<BR>Lowly, submissive, humble,<BR>reverential; as in भक्तिनम्रः Me. 55.<BR>--4<BR>Crooked, curved.<BR>--5 Worshipping.<BR>--6 Devoted or attached to<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग, --मूर्ति a. bent, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रक|नम्रकः
नम्रक a. Bent, stooping.<BR>--कः A<BR>kind of reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रता
नम्रता, --त्वं<BR>1 Obeisance, respect.<BR>--2 Submissiveness, humility.<BR>--3<BR>Condescension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रत्वं|नम्रत्व
नम्रता, --त्वं<BR>1 Obeisance, respect.<BR>--2 Submissiveness, humility.<BR>--3<BR>Condescension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नम्रित
नम्रित a. Bent or bowed down,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-c" target="_blank">Page0608-c+ 59</a>]<BR>stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमुचिः|नमुचि
नमुचिः [न मुंचति]<BR>1 N. of a demon<BR>slain by Indra; वनमुचे नमुचेररये<BR>शिरः R. 9. 22. [When Indra<BR>conquered the Asuras, there was only one called<BR>Namuci who strongly resisted and at<BR>last captured him. He offered to let<BR>Indra go provided he promised ‘not to<BR>kill by day or by night, with wet or<BR>dry’. Indra promised to do so and was<BR>released, but he cut off Namuci's head<BR>at twilight and with foam of water<BR>(which is neither wet nor dry).<BR>According to another version Namuci was<BR>a friend of Indra, and once drank up his<BR>strength and made him quite imbecile.<BR>The Aśvins (and Sarasvatī also, as the<BR>story goes) then supplied Indra with a<BR>Vajra with which he cut off the demon's<BR>head].<BR>--2 N. of the god of love.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सूदनः, --द्विष् --हन् m. epithets<BR>of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नमेरुः|नमेरु
नमेरुः N. of a tree(रुद्राक्ष or<BR>रुरपुन्नाग); गणा नमेरुप्रसवावतंसाः<BR>Ku. 1. 55; 3. 43; R. 4. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय्
नय् {c1c} A. (नयते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To<BR>protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नय|नयः
नय a. [नी भावे अच्]<BR>1 Leading,<BR>conducting.<BR>--2 A guide.<BR>--3<BR>Suitable, right, proper.<BR>--यः<BR>1 Guiding,<BR>leading, managing.<BR>--2 (a)<BR>Behaviour, course of conduct, conduct, way<BR>of life, as in दुर्नय. (b) Prudent<BR>or righteous conduct, virtue.<BR>--3<BR>Prudence, foresight, circumspection;<BR>Pt. 1. 371; 3. 176.<BR>--4 Policy,<BR>political wisdom, statesmanship, civil<BR>administration, state-policy;<BR>नयप्रचारं व्यवहारदुष्टतां Mk. 1. 7;<BR>नयगुणोपचितामिव भूपतेः सदुपकारफलां<BR>श्रियमर्थिनः R. 9. 27; नयशालिभिः Mu. 1. 22.<BR>--5 Morality, justice, rectitude, equity;<BR>चलति नयान्न जिगीषतां हि चेतः<BR>Ki. 10. 29, 2. 3, 6. 38, 16. 42.<BR>--6 A<BR>plan, design, scheme; Pt. 1. 339; 377;<BR>Mu. 6. 11, 7. 9.<BR>--7 A maxim,<BR>principle.<BR>--8 Course, method, manner.<BR>--9 A system, doctrine, opinion.<BR>--10 A philosophical system;<BR>वैशेषिके नये Bhāṣā P. 105.<BR>--11 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--12 A kind of game.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कोविद्, --ज्ञ a. skilled in<BR>policy, prudent.<BR>--चक्षुस् a. having<BR>political foresight, wise, prudent;<BR>R. 1. 55.<BR>--नेतृ m. a master in politics.<BR>--पीठी the board or cloth on which<BR>men are moved in play.<BR>--प्रयोगः<BR>political wisdom, statesmanship.<BR>--वादिन् m. a politician; Pt. 3.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-a" target="_blank">Page0609-a+ 58</a>]<BR>--विद् m.,<BR>--विशारदः a politician,<BR>statesman.<BR>--शास्त्रं {1} the science of<BR>politics. {2} any work on politics or<BR>political economy. {3} a work on<BR>morality.<BR>--शालिन् a. just, righteous;<BR>Ki. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0608-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयकः|नयक
नयकः<BR>1 A skilful manager.<BR>--2<BR>One versed in policy, a statesman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नयनं|नयन
नयनं [नी-करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Leading,<BR>guiding; conducting, managing.<BR>--2<BR>Taking, bringing to or near,<BR>drawing.<BR>--3 Ruling, governing.<BR>--4<BR>Obtaining.<BR>--5 The eye.<BR>--6 Passing,<BR>spending (as time).<BR>--ना, --नी The<BR>pupil of the eye.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभिराम a.<BR>gladdening the sight, lovely to<BR>behold.<BR>--(मः) the moon.<BR>--आमोषिन् a.<BR>blinding the sight, obscuring.<BR>--उत्सवः {1} a lamp. {2} delight of<BR>the eyes. {3} any lovely object.<BR>--उपांतः the corner of the eye;<BR>Ku. 4. 23.<BR>--गोचर a. visible, within the<BR>range of sight.<BR>--छदः an eyelid.<BR>--जलं, --वारि n. tears.<BR>--पथः the range<BR>of sight.<BR>--पुटं the cavity of the eye.<BR>--विषयः {1} any visible object. {2}<BR>the horizon. {3} the range of sight.<BR>--सलिलं tears; Me. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरः|नर|नरं
नरः [नॄ-नये-अच्]<BR>1 A man, male,<BR>person; संयोजयति विद्यैव नीचगापि<BR>नरं सरित् । समुद्रमिव दुर्धर्षं नृपं भाग्यमतः<BR>परं H. Pr. 5; Ms. 1. 96; 2. 213.<BR>--2 A man or piece at chess.<BR>--3 The<BR>pin of a sun-dial.<BR>--4 The Supreme<BR>Spirit, the original or eternal man.<BR>--5 Man's length (= पुरुष q. v.).<BR>--6<BR>N. of a primitive sage.<BR>--7 N. of<BR>Arjuna; see नरनारायण below.<BR>--8 A<BR>horse.<BR>--9 (In gram.) A personal<BR>termination.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः {1} the<BR>penis. {2} eruption on the face.<BR>--अधमः a wretch, miscreant.<BR>--अधिपः, --अधिपतिः, --ईशः, --ईश्वरः, --देवः, --पतिः,<BR>--पालः a king; Bg. 10. 27; Ms. 7. 13;<BR>R. 2. 75, 3. 42; 7. 62; Me. 37;<BR>Y. 1. 311.<BR>--अंतकः death.<BR>--अयणः an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--अशः a demon,<BR>goblin.<BR>--आधारः N. of Śiva.<BR>--(रा)<BR>the earth.<BR>--इतरः {1} a being higher<BR>than a man. {2} an animal.<BR>--इंद्रः<BR>{1} a king; R. 2. 18, 3. 33, 6. 80;<BR>Ms. 9. 253. {2} a physician, dealer<BR>in antidotes, curer of poisons; तेषु<BR>कश्चिन्नरेंद्राभिमानी तां निर्वर्ण्य Dk. 51;<BR>सुनिग्रहा नरेंद्रेण फणींद्रा इव शत्रवः<BR>Śi. 2. 88 (where the word is used in both<BR>senses). ˚मार्गः a high street, main<BR>road.<BR>--उत्तमः {1} an epithet of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-b" target="_blank">Page0609-b+ 58</a>]<BR>Viṣṇu. {2} of Buddha.<BR>--ऋषभः ‘the<BR>chief of men’, a prince, king.<BR>--कपालः a man's skull.<BR>--कीलकः the<BR>murderer of a spiritual preceptor.<BR>--केशरिन् m. {1} Viṣṇu in his fourth<BR>incarnation; cf. नरसिंह below. {2} the<BR>chief of men.<BR>--धिः the world.<BR>--द्विष् m. a demon goblin; Bk. 15. 94.<BR>--नारायणः N. of Kṛṣṇa. (--णौ dual)<BR>originally regarded as identical, but<BR>in mythology and epic poetry,<BR>considered as distinct beings, Arjuna<BR>being identified with Nara and<BR>Kṛṣṇa with Nārāyaṇa. [In some<BR>places they are called देवौ, पूर्वदेवौ,<BR>ऋषी or ऋषिसत्तमौ. They are said to have<BR>been practising very austere penance on<BR>the Himālaya, which excited the fear of<BR>Indra, and he sent down several damsels<BR>to disturb their austerities. But<BR>Nārāyaṇa put all of them to shame by<BR>creating a nymph called Urvaśī from a flower<BR>placed on his thigh who excelled them<BR>in beauty; cf. स्थाने खलु नारायणमृषिं<BR>विलोभयंत्यस्तदूरुसंभवामिमां दृष्ट्वा<BR>व्रीडिताः सर्वा अप्सरस इति V. 1.]<BR>--पशुः<BR>‘a beast-like man’, a beast in<BR>human form.<BR>--पुंगवः ‘best of men’,<BR>an excellent man.<BR>--बलिः a human<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--भुज् a. man-eating,<BR>cannibal.<BR>--भूः f. the Bharata-Varṣa,<BR>i. e. India.<BR>--मानिका, --मानिनी, --मालिनी<BR>‘manlike woman’, a woman with a<BR>beard, masculine woman or an<BR>amazon.<BR>--माला a girdle of skulls.<BR>--मेधः a<BR>human sacrifice.<BR>--यंत्रं sun-dial.<BR>--यानं,<BR>--रथः, --वाहनं a vehicle drawn by men.<BR>--लोकः {1} ‘the world of men’, the<BR>earth, terrestrial world. {2} mankind.<BR>--वाहनः an epithet of Kubera;<BR>R. 9. 11.<BR>--विष्वणः a demon, goblin.<BR>--वीरः a brave man, hero.<BR>--व्याघ्रः,<BR>--शार्दूलः an eminent man.<BR>--शृंगं<BR>‘man's horn’, an impossibility, a<BR>chimera, non-entity.<BR>--संसर्गः human<BR>society.<BR>--सखः an epithet of<BR>Nārāyaṇa; V. 1. 3.<BR>--सिंहः, --हरिः<BR>‘manlion’, Viṣṇu in his fourth<BR>incarnation; cf. तव करकमलवरे नखमद्भुतशृंगं<BR>दलितहिरण्यकशिपुतनुभृंगं । केशव<BR>धृतनरहरिरूप जय जगदीश हरे ॥ Gīt. 1.<BR>--स्कंधः a<BR>multitude or body of men.<BR>--हयं a<BR>fight or enmity between man and<BR>horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरंगं|नरङ्ग|नरंग|नरङ्गः
नरंगं<BR>1 The penis.<BR>--2 Eruption on<BR>the face; cf. नरांग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरंधिः|नरन्धि
नरंधिः Worldly life or existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरंधिषः|नरन्धिष
नरंधिषः^1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: Presume misprint of 'p' for 'z'; based on MW  AP and others.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नराशंसः|नराशंस
नराशंसः<BR>1 A sacrifice.<BR>--2 Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरी
नरी A woman; Bv. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्य|नर्यः|नर्य्य
नर्य a. Ved. [नृभ्यो हितं यत्]<BR>1<BR>Suitable to men (as food &c.).<BR>--2<BR>Manly, strong.<BR>--3 Human.<BR>--र्यः<BR>1 A<BR>man.<BR>--2 Indra.<BR>--र्यौ (du.) The two<BR>objects of human desire, i. e. Heaven<BR>and earth.<BR>--र्यं<BR>1 A manly deed.<BR>--2<BR>A gift for men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकः|नरक|नरकं
नरकः, --कं Hell, infernal regions;<BR>(corresponding to the realm of<BR>Pluto; there are said to be 21<BR>different parts of these regions where<BR>different kinds of tortures are<BR>inflicted upon sinners).<BR>--कः N. of a<BR>demon, king of Prāgjyotiṣa.<BR>[According to one account he carried off<BR>Aditi's ear-rings and Kṛṣṇa at the<BR>request of the gods killed him in a single<BR>combat and recovered the jewels.<BR>According to another account, Naraka<BR>assumed the form of an elephant and<BR>carried off the daughter of Viśvakarman and<BR>outraged her. He also seized the daughters<BR>of Gandharvas, gods, men and the<BR>nymphs themselves, and collected more<BR>than 16000 damsels in his harem. These,<BR>it is related, were transferred by<BR>Kṛṣṇa to his own harem after he had slain<BR>Naraka. The demon was born of earth,<BR>and hence called ‘Bhauma.’].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतकः, --अरिः, --जित् m. epithets of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--आमयः {1} the soul after<BR>death. {2} a ghost, spirit.<BR>--आवासः<BR>an inhabitant of hell.<BR>--कुंडं a pit in<BR>hell where the wicked are<BR>tormented; (86 such places are<BR>enumerated).<BR>--देवता ‘the deity of hell’,<BR>Nirṛti (निरृति).<BR>--रूपिन् a. hellish.<BR>--स्था the Vaitariṇī river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकं|नरक|नरकः
नरकः, --कं Hell, infernal regions;<BR>(corresponding to the realm of<BR>Pluto; there are said to be 21<BR>different parts of these regions where<BR>different kinds of tortures are<BR>inflicted upon sinners).<BR>--कः N. of a<BR>demon, king of Prāgjyotiṣa.<BR>[According to one account he carried off<BR>Aditi's ear-rings and Kṛṣṇa at the<BR>request of the gods killed him in a single<BR>combat and recovered the jewels.<BR>According to another account, Naraka<BR>assumed the form of an elephant and<BR>carried off the daughter of Viśvakarman and<BR>outraged her. He also seized the daughters<BR>of Gandharvas, gods, men and the<BR>nymphs themselves, and collected more<BR>than 16000 damsels in his harem. These,<BR>it is related, were transferred by<BR>Kṛṣṇa to his own harem after he had slain<BR>Naraka. The demon was born of earth,<BR>and hence called ‘Bhauma.’].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतकः, --अरिः, --जित् m. epithets of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--आमयः {1} the soul after<BR>death. {2} a ghost, spirit.<BR>--आवासः<BR>an inhabitant of hell.<BR>--कुंडं a pit in<BR>hell where the wicked are<BR>tormented; (86 such places are<BR>enumerated).<BR>--देवता ‘the deity of hell’,<BR>Nirṛti (निरृति).<BR>--रूपिन् a. hellish.<BR>--स्था the Vaitariṇī river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरकायते
नरकायते Den. A. To resemble a<BR>hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नरिष्ठा
नरिष्ठा Ved.<BR>1 Sport, pastime.<BR>--2 A human sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्कुटकं|नर्कुटक
नर्कुटकं Nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्त|नर्तः|नर्त्त
नर्त a. [नृत्-अच्] Dancing.<BR>--र्तः<BR>Dancing, a dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तकः|नर्तक|नर्त्तक|नर्त्तकः
नर्तकः [नृत्-कर्तरि ष्वुन्]<BR>1 A dancer;<BR>sometimes a dancing preceptor.<BR>--2<BR>An actor, mime, mummer.<BR>--3 A bard,<BR>herald.<BR>--4 An elephant.<BR>--5 A king.<BR>--6 A peacock.<BR>--7 An epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--8 N. of a mixed tribe; (<BR>वेश्यायां रजकाज्जातो नर्तको गायको<BR>भवेत्).<BR>--की<BR>1 A female dancer, a<BR>singing girl, an actress; रंगस्य<BR>दर्शयित्वा निवर्तते नर्तकी यथा नृत्यात् Sān.<BR>K. 59; Ki. 10. 41; R. 19. 14, 19.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">Page0610-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 A female elephant.<BR>--3 A<BR>peahen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0609-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तनः|नर्तन|नर्त्तन|नर्त्तनं
नर्तनः [नृत्-ल्युट्] A dancer.<BR>--नं<BR>Gesticulation, dancing, dance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गृहं, --शाला a dancing hall.<BR>--प्रियः {1} an epithet of Śiva. {2} a<BR>peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तयितृ
नर्तयितृ m. A dancing-master; अद्य<BR>नर्तयितास्मि M. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तित|नर्त्तित
नर्तित a.<BR>1 Danced, made to dance.<BR>--2 Dancing, moving to and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्तु|नर्त्तु
नर्तु a. Dancing on the edge of a<BR>sword. --f. A female dancer or<BR>actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द्
नर्द् {c1c} P. (नर्दति, नर्दित)<BR>1 To<BR>bellow, roar, sound in general;<BR>अनर्दिषुः कपिव्याघ्राः Bk. 15. 35, 15. 40,<BR>15. 28, 17. 40.<BR>--2 To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्द|नर्द्द
नर्द a. Bellowing, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दनं|नर्दन|नर्द्दन
नर्दनं [नर्द्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Bellowing,<BR>roaring.<BR>--2 Celebrating, praising<BR>aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दित|नर्दितः|नर्द्दित
नर्दित a.<BR>1 Sounded, bellowed.<BR>--2<BR>Celebrated.<BR>--तः A kind of die or a<BR>throw at dice; नर्दितदर्शितमार्गः कटेन<BR>विनिपतितो यामि Mk. 2. 8.<BR>--तं<BR>Sound, roar, bellowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्दिन्|नर्द्दिन्
नर्दिन् a. Sounding, roaring,<BR>bellowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्ब्
नर्ब् {c1c} P. (नर्बति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मः|नर्म|नर्म्म
नर्मः Ved. Sport, pastime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मटः|नर्मट|नर्म्मट|नर्म्मटः
नर्मटः<BR>1 A pot-sherd.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मठः|नर्मठ|नर्म्मठ|नर्म्मठः
नर्मठः [नर्मन्-अठन्]<BR>1 A jester.<BR>--2<BR>A lecher, rake, libertine.<BR>--3 Sport,<BR>pastime, amusement.<BR>--4 Copulation,<BR>coition.<BR>--5 The chin.<BR>--6 The nipple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मन्|नर्म्मन्
नर्मन् n. [नॄ-मनिन्]<BR>1 Sport,<BR>amusement, diversion, merriment,<BR>pleasure, amorous pastime or sport;<BR>जितकमले विमले परिकर्मय नर्मजनकमलकं<BR>मुखे Gīt. 12 (कौतुकजनक); R. 19. 28.<BR>--2 Jest, joke, humour, wit;<BR>नर्भप्रायाभिः कथाभिः K. 70 ‘jocular,<BR>humorous’.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीलः a husband.<BR>--गर्भ a. humorous, full of humour,<BR>witty.<BR>--(र्भः) a secret lover.<BR>--द a.<BR>delighting, making happy.<BR>--(दः) a<BR>jester (= नर्मसचिव q. v.).<BR>--दा N. of<BR>a river which rises in the Vindhya<BR>mountain, and falls into the gulf of<BR>Cambay.<BR>--द्युति a. bright with joy,<BR>cheerful, merry. (--तिः f.)<BR>enjoyment of a joke.<BR>--सचिवः, --सुहृद् m.<BR>‘a pleasure-companion’, an associate<BR>of the amusements of a prince or a<BR>man of rank; इदं त्वैदंपर्यं यदुत<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">Page0610-b+ 59</a>]<BR>नृपतेर्नर्मसचिवः सुतादानान्मित्रं भवतु<BR>Māl. 2. 7; तां याचते नरपतेर्नर्मसुहृन्नंदनो नृपमुखेन<BR>1. 11; Śi. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मवत्
नर्मवत् a. Humorous, witty. --n.<BR>A kind of drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्मरा
नर्मरा<BR>1 A valley, cavity.<BR>--2 A<BR>bellows.<BR>--3 An old woman past<BR>menstruation.<BR>--4 The plant Saralā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नर्य|नर्यः|नर्य्य
नर्य See under नर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्
नल् {c1c} P. (नलति)<BR>1 To smell.<BR>--2<BR>To bind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलः|नल|नलं
नलः<BR>1 A kind of reed;<BR>Pt. 1. 96.<BR>--2 N. of a celebrated king of<BR>the Niṣadhas and hero of the<BR>poem called ‘Naishadhacharita.’<BR>[Nala was a very noble-minded and<BR>virtuous king. He was chosen by<BR>Damayantī in spite of the opposition of gods,<BR>and they lived happily for some years.<BR>But Kali-who was disappointed in<BR>securing her hand-resolved to persecute<BR>Nala, and entered into his person. Thus<BR>affected he played at dice with his<BR>brother, and having lost everything,<BR>he, with his wife, was banished from the<BR>kingdom. One day, while wandering<BR>through the wilderness, he abandoned<BR>his wife, almost naked, and went away.<BR>Subsequently he was deformed by the<BR>serpent Karkoṭaka, and so deformed he<BR>entered the service of king Ṛtuparṇa of<BR>Ayodhyā as a horsegroom under the name<BR>of Bāhuka. Subsequently with the<BR>assistance of the king he regained his<BR>beloved, and they led a happy life; see<BR>ऋतुपर्ण and दमयंती also].<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>monkey-chief, son of Viśvakarman,<BR>who, it is said, built the bridge of<BR>stones called Nalasetu or ‘Adam's<BR>bridge’ over which Rāma passed<BR>to Laṅkā with his army.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A<BR>lotus.<BR>--2 Smell, odour.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीलः the knee.<BR>--कूब (व) रः N.<BR>of a son of Kubera.<BR>--दं {1} a<BR>fragrant root (उशीर); Ki. 12. 50;<BR>N. 4. 116. {2} the honey of a flower.<BR>--पट्टिका a sort of mat made of<BR>reeds.<BR>--मीनः a shrimp or prawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकं|नलक
नलकं<BR>1 Any long bone of the<BR>body; Mv. 1. 35; Māl. 5. 17.<BR>--2<BR>The radius of the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलकिनी
नलकिनी<BR>1 The knee-pan.<BR>--2 The<BR>leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनः|नलिन|नलिनं
नलिनः The(Indian) crane.<BR>--नं<BR>1 A lotus-flower, water-lily.<BR>--2<BR>Water.<BR>--3 The Indigo plant. (<BR>नलिनेशयः an epithet of Viṣṇu.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नलिनी
नलिनी<BR>1 A lotus-plant; न पर्वताग्रे<BR>नलिनी प्ररोहति Mk. 4. 17;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-c" target="_blank">Page0610-c+ 56</a>]<BR>नलिनीदलगतजलमतितरलं Moha M. 5;<BR>Ku. 4 6.<BR>--2 An assemblage of lotuses.<BR>--3<BR>A pond or place abounding in<BR>lotuses.<BR>--4 A lotus or the stalk of it.<BR>--5 The celestial Ganges.<BR>--6 The<BR>intoxicating juice of the cocoa-nut.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडं, --षंडं a group or<BR>assemblage of lotuses.<BR>--रुहः an epithet<BR>of Brahmā.<BR>--(हं) a lotus-stalk, the<BR>fibres of a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नल्वः|नल्व
नल्वः A measure of distance equal<BR>to 400 hastas or cubits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव|नवः
नव a.<BR>1 New, fresh, young,<BR>recent; चित्तयोनिरभवत्पुनर्नवः<BR>R. 19. 46; एते वयं पुनर्नवीकृताः स्मः Ś. 5;<BR>क्लेशः फलेन हि पुनर्नवतां विधत्ते Ku. 5. 86;<BR>U. 1. 19; R. 1. 83, 2. 47, 3. 53, 4. 3,<BR>11; Śi. 1. 4; नयवयसि Mu. 3. 3.;<BR>Śi. 3. 31; Ki. 9. 43.<BR>--2 Modern.<BR>--वः<BR>1 A crow.<BR>--2 Praise.<BR>--वं ind.<BR>Recently, newly, lately, not long<BR>ago.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगी a woman.<BR>--अन्नं<BR>{1} new rice or grain. {2} a ceremony<BR>performed on first eating the<BR>newrice.<BR>--अंबु n. fresh water.<BR>--अहः<BR>the first day of a fortnight.<BR>--इतर<BR>a. old; R. 8. 22.<BR>--उद्धृतं fresh<BR>butter.<BR>--ऊढा, --पाणिग्रहणा {1} a newly,<BR>married woman, a bride; H. 1. 212<BR>Bh. 1. 4; R. 8. 7. {2} a kind of<BR>heroine (in dramas).<BR>--कारिका,<BR>--कालिका, --फलिका {1} a woman newly<BR>married. {2} a woman in whom<BR>menstruation has recently commenced.<BR>--छात्रः a fresh student, novice, tyro.<BR>--नी f.,<BR>--नीतं fresh butter;<BR>अहोनवनीतकल्पहृदय आर्यपुत्रः M. 3.<BR>--नीतकं {1} clarified butter. {2} fresh<BR>butter.<BR>--पाठकः a new teacher.<BR>--प्रसूता<BR>a woman who has lately brought<BR>forth (a child).<BR>--प्राशनं eating of<BR>new rice.<BR>--मल्लिका, --मालिका a kind<BR>of jasmine.<BR>--यज्ञः an offering of the<BR>first fruits of the harvest.<BR>--यौवनं<BR>fresh youth, bloom or prime of<BR>youth.<BR>--(ना) a young woman.<BR>--रजस् f. a girl who has recently<BR>menstruated.<BR>--वधूः, --वरिका {1} a<BR>newlymarried girl. {2} a daughter-in-law.<BR>--वल्लभं a kind of sandal.<BR>--वस्त्रं<BR>new cloth.<BR>--शस्यं the first fruits of<BR>the year's harvest.<BR>--शशिभृत् m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva; Me. 43.<BR>--सूतिः f.,<BR>--सूतिका {1} a milch-cow. {2} a woman<BR>recently delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवता
नवता --त्वं Freshness, novelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवत्वं|नवत्व
नवता --त्वं Freshness, novelty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0610-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवनं|नवन
नवनं The act of praising or<BR>extolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीकृ
नवीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To make new, renew,<BR>revive.<BR>--2 To refresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवीन|नवीनं
नवीन, नव्य a,<BR>1 New, fresh, recent.<BR>--2 Modern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नव्य|नव्यं|नव्यः
नवीन, नव्य a,<BR>1 New, fresh, recent.<BR>--2 Modern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवन्
नवन् num. a. (always pl.) Nine;<BR>नवतिं नवाधिकां R. 3. 69; see comp.<BR>below. (At the beginning of comp.<BR>नवन् drops its final न्).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अशीतिः f. eighty-nine.<BR>--अर्चिस् m.,<BR>--दीधेतिः the planet Mars.<BR>--कृत्वस्<BR>ind. nine times.<BR>--ग्रहाः (m. pl.) the<BR>nine planets; see under ग्रह.<BR>--चत्वारिंश a. forty-ninth.<BR>--चत्वारिंशत् f.<BR>forty-nine.<BR>--छिद्रं, --द्वारं the body<BR>(having nine apertures; see ख).<BR>--त्रिंश a. thirty-ninth.<BR>--त्रिंशन् f.<BR>thirty nine.<BR>--दश a. nineteenth.<BR>--दशत् pl. nineteen.<BR>--दुर्गा Durgā in<BR>her nine forms.<BR>--नवतिः f.<BR>ninetynine.<BR>--निधि m. pl. the nine<BR>treasures of Kubera, i. e. महपद्मश्च पद्मश्च<BR>शखो मकरकच्छपौ । मुकुंदकुंदनीलाश्च खर्वश्च<BR>निधयो नव ॥.<BR>--पंचाश a. fifty-ninth.<BR>--पंचाशत् f. fifty-nine.<BR>--रत्नं {1} the<BR>nine precious jewels; i. e.<BR>मुक्तामाणिक्यवैदूर्यगोमेदा वज्रविद्रुमौ । पद्मरागो मरकतं<BR>नीलश्चति यथाक्रमं ॥. {2} ‘the nine gems’ or<BR>poets at the court of king<BR>Vikramāditya:<BR>--धन्वंतरिक्षपणकामरसिंहशंकुवेतालभट्टघटकर्परकालिदासाः । ख्यातो वराहमिहिरो नृपतेः<BR>सभायां रत्नानि वै वररुचिर्नव विक्रमस्य ॥.<BR>--रसाः (m. pl.) the nine<BR>sentiments in poetry; see under अष्टरस<BR>and रस also.<BR>--रात्रं {1} a period of<BR>nine days. {2} the first nine days of<BR>the month of Āśvina held sacred to<BR>Durgā.<BR>--विंश a. twenty-ninth.<BR>--विंशतिः f. twenty-nine.<BR>--विध a.<BR>ninefold, of nine kinds or sorts.<BR>--व्यूहः<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--शतं {1}<BR>one hundred and nine. {2} nine<BR>hundred.<BR>--शायकः N. given to nine<BR>inferior tribes; they are;<BR>--गोपो माली<BR>तथा तैली तंत्री मोदकवारुजी । कुलालः<BR>कर्मकारश्च नापितो नवशायकाः ॥. Parāśara.<BR>--षष्टिः f. sixty-nine.<BR>--सप्ततिः<BR>seventy-nine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवक
नवक a. Consisting of nine.<BR>--कं<BR>The aggregate of nine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवत|नवतः
नवत a. (ती f.) Ninetieth.<BR>--तः<BR>1 An elephant's painted housings.<BR>--2 A woollen cloth, blanket.<BR>--3 A<BR>cover, wrapper (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवतिः|नवति
नवतिः f. Ninety;<BR>नवनवतिशतद्रव्यकोटीश्वरास्ते Mu. 3. 27; R. 3. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवतिका
नवतिका<BR>1 Ninety.<BR>--2 A<BR>paintbrush (said to contain 90 hairs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवधा
नवधा ind. In nine ways, ninefold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवम|नवमः
नवम a. (मी f.) Ninth.<BR>--मी The<BR>ninth day of a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नवशः
नवशः ind. By nines.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्
नश् {vI.v} {c4c} P. (नश्पति, ननाश, अनशत्,<BR>नंक्ष्यति, नशिष्यति नष्ट; caus. नाशयति; desid.<BR>निनंक्षति, निनशिषति)<BR>1 To be lost, to<BR>disappear, vanish, become invisible;<BR>ध्रुवाणि तस्य नश्यंति H. 1; तथा सीमा<BR>न नश्यति Ms. 8. 247; Y. 2. 58;<BR>क्षणनष्टदृष्टतिमिरं Mk. 5. 24.<BR>--2 To be<BR>destroyed, to perish, die, be ruined;<BR>जीवनाशं ननाश च Bk. 14. 31;<BR>Ms. 8. 166, 7. 40; Mu. 6. 8.<BR>--3 To run<BR>away, fly away, escape; नश्यंति<BR>वृंदानि ददर्श कवींद्रः Bk. 10. 12; नेशुश्चित्रा<BR>निशाचराः 14. 112; Ratn. 2. 3.<BR>--4<BR>To be frustrated, become unsuccess<BR>ful. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to disappear.<BR>--2 To destroy, remove, efface, drive<BR>away, cause to fly away.<BR>--3 To<BR>violate, (as a virgin).<BR>--4 To cause to<BR>be lost, lose.<BR>--5 To forget.<BR>--6 To<BR>extinguish, put out (as fire). {vII.v}<BR>{c1c} U. (नशति-ते) Ved.<BR>1 To reach,<BR>attain.<BR>--2 To meet with, find.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्
नश् f., नशः, --नशनं Destruction,<BR>perishing, loss, disappearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्यत्प्रसूतिका
नश्यत्प्रसूतिका A woman who brings<BR>forth a dead child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नश्वर|नश्वरः
नश्वर a. (री f.) [नश्-क्वरप्]<BR>1<BR>Perishable, transitory, evanescent,<BR>transient, frail; निखिलं जगदेव नश्वरं<BR>R. G.<BR>--2 Destructive, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्ट|नष्टः
नष्ट p. p. [नश्-क्त]<BR>1 Lost,<BR>disappeared, vanished, invisible;<BR>Pt. 5. 6; 2. 167.<BR>--2 Dead, perished,<BR>destroyed.<BR>--3 Spoiled, wasted.<BR>--4<BR>Fled or run away.<BR>--5 Deprived of,<BR>free from (in comp.).<BR>--6 Depraved,<BR>corrupted, debauched.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1<BR>Destruction, loss.<BR>--2 Disappearance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः a householder who<BR>has lost his consecrated fire, (it<BR>being extinguished).<BR>--अर्थ a.<BR>reduced to poverty (having lost one's<BR>wealth).<BR>--आतंकं ind. without<BR>anxiety or fear; नष्टातंकं हरिणशिशवो<BR>मंदमंदं चरंति Ś. 1. 14 (v. l.)<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>deprived of sense.<BR>--आप्तिसूत्रं booty,<BR>plunder.<BR>--आशंक a. fearless,<BR>secure, free from fear; Ś. 1. 14.<BR>--इंदुकला<BR>the day of new moon.<BR>--इंद्रिय a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">Page0611-c+ 55</a>]<BR>deprived of senses.<BR>--चेतन, --चेष्ट, --संज्ञ<BR>a. one who has lost his senses,<BR>unconscious, insensible, fainted.<BR>--चेष्टता universal destruction.<BR>--जन्मन्<BR>n.,<BR>--जातकं subsequent calculation<BR>of a lost nativity.<BR>--स्मृति a.<BR>forgetful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नष्टिः|नष्टि
नष्टिः f. Loss, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस् {c1c} A. (नसते) Ved.<BR>1 To<BR>approach, go towards.<BR>--2 To copulate.<BR>--3 To be crooked or curved, to<BR>bend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्
नस् f. The nose (a word<BR>optionally substituted for नासिका after<BR>acc. dual).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्षुद्र a.<BR>smallnosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नसा
नसा The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तः|नस्त
नस्तः The nose.<BR>--स्तं A<BR>sternutatory, snuff.<BR>--स्ता A hole bored in<BR>the septum of the nose.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ऊतः an ox led by a string through<BR>the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तस्
नस्तस् ind. From the nose;<BR>Y. 3. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तकं|नस्तक
नस्तकं A hole bored in the septum<BR>of the nose (of cattle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्तित|नस्तितः
नस्तित a. Nozzled(with a string<BR>through the nose).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नस्य|नस्यं
नस्य a. [नासिकायै हितं तत्र भवं वा यत्<BR>नसादेशः] Nasal.<BR>--स्यं<BR>1 The hairs in<BR>the nose.<BR>--2 A sternutatory.<BR>--स्या<BR>1 The nose.<BR>--2 The string through<BR>the nose of an animal; Śi. 12. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नह्
नह् {c4c} U. (नह्यति-ते, नद्ध; desid.<BR>निनत्सति-ते)<BR>1 To tie, bind, bind on<BR>or round or together, gird round;<BR>शैलेयनद्धानि शिलातलानि Ku. 1. 56;<BR>R. 4. 57; 16. 41.<BR>--2 To put on<BR>(oneself), to dress, arm oneself<BR>(Atm.). --Caus. To cause to put<BR>on. --WITH अप to untie.<BR>--अपि<BR>(अपि being often changed to पि)<BR>1 to fasten, gird round, bind;<BR>अतिपिनद्धेन वल्कलेन Ś. 1; मंदारमाला<BR>हरिणा पिनद्धा Ś. 7. 2.<BR>--2 to put on,<BR>wear; Bk. 3. 47.<BR>--3 to cover,<BR>envelop; क्रुसुममिव पिनद्धं पांडुपत्रोदरेण<BR>Ś. 1. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहि
नहि ind. Surely or certainly not,<BR>by no means, not at all; आशंसा नाहि<BR>नः प्रेते जीवेम दशमूर्धनि Bk. 19. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुस्
नहुस् m.<BR>1 A neighbour.<BR>--2 A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुषः|नहुष
नहुषः N. of a king of the lunar<BR>race, son of Āyus and grandson of<BR>Purūravas and father of Yayāti.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-a" target="_blank">Page0612-a+ 58</a>]<BR>[He was a very wise and powerful king,<BR>and when Indra lay concealed under<BR>waters to expiate the sin of having<BR>killed the demon Vṛtra, a Brāhmaṇa, he<BR>was asked to occupy his seat. While<BR>there he thought of winning the love<BR>of Indrani and caused the seven sages to<BR>convey him in a palanquin to her house.<BR>On his way he asked each of them to<BR>be quick using the words ‘sarpa’,<BR>‘sarpa’ (move on, move on), when one<BR>of the sages (Agastya ?) cursed him to<BR>be a ‘sarpa’ (serpent). He fell down from<BR>the sky, and remained in that wretched<BR>state till he waś relieved from it by<BR>Yudhiṣṭhira].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0611-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नहुष्य|नहुष्यः
नहुष्य a. Ved. Human.<BR>--ष्यः A<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ना
ना No, not (= न q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक|नाकः
नाक a. [न कं अकं दुःखं; तन्नास्ति यत्र<BR>नभ्राडित्यादि नि˚ प्रकृतिभावः] Happy,<BR>painless.<BR>--कः<BR>1 Heaven;<BR>आनाकरथवर्त्मनां R. 1. 5; 15. 96.<BR>--2 Vault<BR>of heaven, upper sky, firmament.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आपगा the heavenly<BR>Ganges.<BR>--ईशः, --ईश्वरः N. of Indra.<BR>--ओकस् m. a god.<BR>--चरः {1} a god.<BR>{2} a demi god.<BR>--नाथः, --नायकः an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>--पृष्ठं {1} the<BR>uppermost heaven. {2} the vault of heaven.<BR>--वनिता an Apsaras.<BR>--सद् m. a god;<BR>Bk. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकिन्
नाकिन् m. A god; Śi. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाकुः|नाकु
नाकुः<BR>1 An ant-hill.<BR>--2 A<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्र|नाक्षत्रं|नाक्षत्रः
नाक्षत्र a. (त्री f.) [नक्षत्राणामिदं<BR>अण्] Starry, sidereal.<BR>--त्रं A month<BR>computed by the moon's passage<BR>through the 27 lunar mansions, a<BR>month of 30 days of sixty Ghaṭīs<BR>each; नाडीषष्ठ्या तु नाक्षत्रमहोरात्रं<BR>प्रकीर्तितं Sūrya S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाक्षत्रिक|नाक्षत्रिकः
नाक्षत्रिक a. (की f.) [नक्षत्रादागतः<BR>ठञ्] Sidereal.<BR>--कः A month of 27<BR>days (each day being the period of<BR>the moon's passage through a lunar<BR>asterism).<BR>--की The state (दशा)<BR>which a man suffers agreeably to<BR>the asterism presiding over his<BR>nativity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाग|नागं|नागः
नाग a. (गी f.)<BR>1 Serpentine,<BR>formed of snakes, snaky.<BR>--2<BR>Elephantine.<BR>--गः [न गच्छति इत्यगः न अगो नागः]<BR>1 A snake in general, particularly<BR>the cobra.<BR>--2 A fabulous<BR>serpentdemon of semi-divine being, having<BR>the face of a man and the tail of<BR>a serpent, and said to inhabit the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-b" target="_blank">Page0612-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Pātāla; Bg. 10. 29; R. 15. 83.<BR>--3<BR>An elephant; Me. 14, 36;<BR>Śi. 4. 63; V. 4. 25.<BR>--4 A shark.<BR>--5 A<BR>cruel or tyrannical person.<BR>--6 (At<BR>the end of comp.) Any<BR>pre-eminent or distinguished person, e. g.<BR>पुरुषनागः.<BR>--7 A cloud.<BR>--8 A peg<BR>projecting from a wall to hang<BR>anything upon.<BR>--9 Piper betel.<BR>--10<BR>One of the five vital airs of the<BR>body, that which is expelled by<BR>eructation.<BR>--11 The number ‘seven.’<BR>--गं<BR>1 Tin.<BR>--2 Lead.<BR>--3 One of the<BR>astronomical periods (Karaṇas)<BR>called ध्रुव.<BR>--4 The effects of that<BR>period on anything done during it.<BR>--5 The asterism called आश्लेषा.<BR>--गी<BR>1 A female Nāga.<BR>--2 A female<BR>elephant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं Hastināpura.<BR>--अंगना {1} a female elephant. {2}<BR>the proboscis of an elephant.<BR>--अंचला, --अंजना = नागयष्टि q. v.<BR>--अंजना a<BR>female elephant.<BR>--अधिपः an<BR>epithet of Śeṣa.<BR>--अंतकः, --अरातिः, --अरिः<BR>{1} an epithet of Garuḍa. {2} a<BR>peacock. {3} a lion.<BR>--अशनः {1} a<BR>peacock; Pt. 1. 159. {2} an epithet of<BR>Garuḍa. {3} a lion.<BR>--आख्यः =<BR>नागकेसर q. v.<BR>--आननः an epithet of<BR>Gaṇeśa.<BR>--आनंदं a drama by<BR>Śriharsha.<BR>--आह्वः Hastināpura.<BR>--इंद्रः {1}<BR>a lordly or superior elephant;<BR>Ku. 1. 36. {2} Airāvata, Indra's elephant.<BR>{3} an epithet of Śeṣa.<BR>--ईशः {1} an<BR>epithet of Śeṣa. {2} N. of the<BR>author of Paribhāṣenduśekhara<BR>and several other works. {3} N. of<BR>Patañjali.<BR>--उदरं {1} a breast-plate.<BR>{2} a peculiar disease of pregnancy<BR>(गर्भोपद्रवभेद).<BR>--कन्यका a<BR>serpent-virgin.<BR>--कर्णः the castor-oil plant.<BR>--किंजल्कः = नागकेसर q. v.<BR>--केसरः N. of a<BR>tree with fragrant flowers, Mesua<BR>Roxburghii.<BR>--गर्भं red lead.<BR>--चूडः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--जं {1} red<BR>lead. {2} tin.<BR>--जिह्विका red<BR>arsenic.<BR>--जीवनं tin.<BR>--दंतः, --दंतकः {1}<BR>ivory. {2} a peg or bracket<BR>projecting from a wall and used to hang<BR>things upon.<BR>--दंती {1} a kind of<BR>sunflower. {2} a harlot.<BR>--नक्षत्रं, --नायकं<BR>the constellation called Āśleṣā.<BR>--(कः) the lord of serpents.<BR>--नामकं<BR>tin.<BR>--नामन् m. holy basil.<BR>--नासा<BR>the proboscis of an elephant.<BR>--निर्यूहः a large pin or bracket<BR>projecting from a wall.<BR>--पंचमी {1} N. of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-c" target="_blank">Page0612-c+ 56</a>]<BR>festival on the fifth day in the<BR>bright half of Śrāvaṇa. {2} the<BR>fifth day in the dark half of<BR>Āshāḍha.<BR>--पतिः an epithet of (1)<BR>Airāvata. (2) Śeṣa.<BR>--पदः a mode<BR>of sexual enjoyment (रतिबंध).<BR>--पाशः<BR>{1} a sort of magical noose used in<BR>battle to entangle an enemy. {2} N.<BR>of the noose or weapon of Varuṇa.<BR>--पाशकः a kind of coitus (रतिबंध).<BR>--पुरं {1} Hastināpura. {2} N. of a city<BR>in Pātāla.<BR>--पुष्पः {1} the Campaka<BR>tree. {2} the Punnāga tree.<BR>--बंधकः an<BR>elephant-catcher.<BR>--बंधुः the holy<BR>fig-tree.<BR>--बलः an epithet of Bhīma.<BR>--भूषणः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--मंडलिकः<BR>{1} a snake-keeper. {2} a snake-catcher.<BR>--मल्लः an epithet of Airāvata.<BR>--यष्टिः<BR>f.,<BR>--यष्टिका {1} a graduated pole or<BR>post for showing the depth of water<BR>in a newly-dug pond. {2} a<BR>boringrod driven into the earth.<BR>--रक्तं,<BR>रेणुः red lead.<BR>--रंगः the orange.<BR>--राजः {1} an epithet of Śeṣa. {2}<BR>a large elephant.<BR>--रुकः the orange<BR>tree.<BR>--लता {1} the penis {2} the piper<BR>betel.<BR>--वल्लरी, --वल्ली piper betel.<BR>--लोकः the world of serpents, the<BR>race of serpents collectively, one<BR>of the regions below the earth<BR>called Pātāla.<BR>--वारिकः {1} a royal<BR>elephant. {2} an elephant-driver. {3}<BR>a peacock. {4} an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>{5} the chief of a herd of elephants.<BR>{6} the chief person in an assembly.<BR>--वीथी that part of the moon's path<BR>which contains the asterisms अश्विनी,<BR>भरणी and कृत्तिका; अश्विनी कृत्तिका<BR>याम्यानागदीथीति शाब्दिता V. P.<BR>--संभवं,<BR>संभूतं red lead.<BR>--साह्वयं Hastināpura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागिन्
नागिन् m. An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर|नागरं|नागरः
नागर a. (री f.) [नगरे भवः अण्]<BR>1 Town-born, town-bred.<BR>--2<BR>Relating to a town, civic.<BR>--3 Spoken in<BR>a town.<BR>--4 Polite, civil.<BR>--5 Clever,<BR>sharp.<BR>--6 Bad, vile, one who has<BR>contracted the vices of a town.<BR>--7<BR>Nameless.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A citizen (पौर);<BR>Me. 25, Śānti. 4. 19.<BR>--2 A<BR>husband's brother.<BR>--3 A lecturer.<BR>--4<BR>An orange.<BR>--5 Fatigue; hardship,<BR>toil.<BR>--6 Desire of final beatitude.<BR>--7 A term applied to a prince<BR>engaged in war under certain<BR>circumstances and also to a planet when<BR>in opposition to other planets (in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">Page0613-a+ 56</a>]<BR>astrol.).<BR>--8 Denial of knowledge.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Dry ginger.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>coitus.<BR>--री<BR>1 The character in<BR>which Sanskrit is generally written;<BR>cf. देवनागरी.<BR>--2 A clever, intriguing<BR>or shrewd woman; हंताभीरीः स्मरतु स<BR>कथं संवृतो नागरीभिः Ud. D. 16.<BR>--3<BR>The plant स्नुही.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आह्वं dry<BR>ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0612-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरक|नागरकः
नागरक, नागरिक a. [नगरे भवः वुञ्]<BR>1 Town-bred, town-born.<BR>--2 Polite,<BR>courteous, courtly; नागरिकवृत्त्या<BR>संज्ञापयैनां Ś. 5; साधु आर्य नागरिकोसि<BR>V. 2.<BR>--3 Clever, shrewd, cunning (विदग्ध).<BR>--कः<BR>1 A citizen.<BR>--2 A polite or<BR>courteous man, a gallant; one who<BR>shows exaggerated attention to his<BR>first mistress while he is courting<BR>some one else.<BR>--3 One who has<BR>contracted the vices of a town.<BR>--4 A<BR>thief.<BR>--5 An artist.<BR>--6 The chief<BR>of the police; V. 5; Ś. 6.<BR>--कं Dry<BR>ginger.<BR>--(रिकं) The toll levied<BR>from a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरिक
नागरक, नागरिक a. [नगरे भवः वुञ्]<BR>1 Town-bred, town-born.<BR>--2 Polite,<BR>courteous, courtly; नागरिकवृत्त्या<BR>संज्ञापयैनां Ś. 5; साधु आर्य नागरिकोसि<BR>V. 2.<BR>--3 Clever, shrewd, cunning (विदग्ध).<BR>--कः<BR>1 A citizen.<BR>--2 A polite or<BR>courteous man, a gallant; one who<BR>shows exaggerated attention to his<BR>first mistress while he is courting<BR>some one else.<BR>--3 One who has<BR>contracted the vices of a town.<BR>--4 A<BR>thief.<BR>--5 An artist.<BR>--6 The chief<BR>of the police; V. 5; Ś. 6.<BR>--कं Dry<BR>ginger.<BR>--(रिकं) The toll levied<BR>from a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरेयक|नागरेयकः
नागरेयक a. (की f.) [नगर्यां भवः<BR>ठकञ्] Belonging to a town, civic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरीटः|नागरीट
नागरीटः, --नागवीटः<BR>1 A libertine,<BR>rake.<BR>--2 A paramour.<BR>--3 A<BR>matchmaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागवीटः|नागवीट
नागरीटः, --नागवीटः<BR>1 A libertine,<BR>rake.<BR>--2 A paramour.<BR>--3 A<BR>matchmaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागरुकः|नागरुक
नागरुकः Orange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नागर्यं|नागर्य|नागर्य्य
नागर्यं Shrewdness, cleverness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाचिकेतः|नाचिकेत
नाचिकेतः Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटः|नाट
नाटः [नट्-घञ्]<BR>1 Dancing,<BR>acting.<BR>--2 N. of the Karṇāṭaka<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकं|नाटक|नाटकः
नाटकं [नट्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A play, drama<BR>(in general).<BR>--2 The first of the<BR>10 principal kinds of dramatic<BR>composition; for definition and<BR>other information; see S. D. 277.<BR>--कः An actor, a dancer.<BR>--की The<BR>court of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटकीय
नाटकीय a. [नाटक-छ] Pertaining<BR>to a drama, dramatic; पूर्वरंगः प्रसंगाय<BR>नाटकीयस्य वस्तुनः Śi. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटारः|नाटार
नाटारः [नट्या अपत्यं आरक्] The son<BR>of an actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटिका
नाटिका A short or light comedy,<BR>one of the Uparūpakas, q. v.; e. g.<BR>the Ratnāvalī, Priyadarśikā or<BR>Viddhaśālabhanjikā. The S. D. thus<BR>defines it: --नाटिका कॢप्तवृत्ता स्यात्स्त्रीप्राया<BR>चतुरंकिका । प्रख्यातो धीरललितस्तत्र<BR>स्यान्नायको नृपः ।… स्यादंतःपुरसंबंधा<BR>संगीतव्यापृताऽथवा । नवानुरागा कन्याऽत्र नायिका<BR>नृपवंशजा । संप्रवर्तेत नेतास्यां देव्यास्त्रासेन शंकितः ।<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-b" target="_blank">Page0613-b+ 55</a>]<BR>देवि पुतर्भवेज्ज्येष्ठा प्रगल्भा नृपवंशजा । पदे पदे<BR>मानवती तद्वशः संगमो द्वयोः । वृत्तिः<BR>स्यात्कौशिकी स्वल्पविमर्षाः संधयः पुनः ॥ 539.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटितकं|नाटितक
नाटितकं A mimic representation,<BR>a gesture, gesticulation;<BR>भीतिनादितकेन Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेयः|नाटेय
नाटेयः, --रः [नट्या अपत्यं ढक् ढ्रक् वा]<BR>The son of an actress or dancing<BR>girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाटेरः|नाटेर
नाटेयः, --रः [नट्या अपत्यं ढक् ढ्रक् वा]<BR>The son of an actress or dancing<BR>girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाट्यं|नाट्य|नाट्यः
नाट्यं [नटस्येदं कृत्यं ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Dancing.<BR>--2 Dramatic representation,<BR>gesticulation, acting; नाट्ये च दक्षा<BR>वयं Ratn. 1. 6; नूनं नाट्ये भवति च<BR>चिरं नोर्वशी गर्वशीला Vikr. 18. 29.<BR>--3 The science or art of dancing or<BR>acting, scenic art; नाट्यं<BR>भिन्नरुचेर्जनस्य बहुधाप्येकं समाराधनं M. 1. 4.<BR>--4 The<BR>costume of an actor.<BR>--ट्यः An actor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचार्यः a dancing<BR>preceptor.<BR>--उक्तिः f. dramatic<BR>phraseology.<BR>--धर्मिका, --धर्मी the rules of<BR>dramatic representation.<BR>--प्रियः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--शाला {1} a<BR>dancing-hall. {2} a theatre.<BR>--शास्त्रं {1} the<BR>dramatic science, dramaturgy. {2} a<BR>work on dramatic representation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाड
नाड = नाल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिः|नाडि
नाडिः, --डी f.<BR>1 The tubular<BR>stalk of any plant.<BR>--2 The hollow<BR>stalk of a lotus &c.<BR>--3 Any<BR>tubular organ of the body (such as an<BR>artery, vein);<BR>षडधिदशनाडीचक्रमध्यस्थितात्मा Māl. 5. 1, 2.<BR>--4 A pipe,<BR>flute.<BR>--5 A fistulous sore, fistula,<BR>sinus.<BR>--6 The pulse at the hand or<BR>foot.<BR>--7 A measure of time equal<BR>to twenty-four minutes.<BR>--8 A period<BR>of time =(1/2) Muhūrta.<BR>--9 A sort of<BR>bent grass.<BR>--10 A juggling trick.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चरणः a bird.<BR>--चीरं {1}<BR>a small reed. {2} a tube round<BR>which the woof is wound.<BR>--जंघः<BR>{1} a crow. {2} a kind of crane.<BR>--तरंगः<BR>{1} an astrologer. {2} a debaucher,<BR>ravisher.<BR>--नक्षत्रं = जन्मनक्षत्र q. v.<BR>--परीक्षा feeling the pulse.<BR>--मंडलं<BR>the celestial equator.<BR>--यंत्रं any<BR>tubular instrument.<BR>--व्रणः sinus, an<BR>ulcer, a fistula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडी
नाडिः, --डी f.<BR>1 The tubular<BR>stalk of any plant.<BR>--2 The hollow<BR>stalk of a lotus &c.<BR>--3 Any<BR>tubular organ of the body (such as an<BR>artery, vein);<BR>षडधिदशनाडीचक्रमध्यस्थितात्मा Māl. 5. 1, 2.<BR>--4 A pipe,<BR>flute.<BR>--5 A fistulous sore, fistula,<BR>sinus.<BR>--6 The pulse at the hand or<BR>foot.<BR>--7 A measure of time equal<BR>to twenty-four minutes.<BR>--8 A period<BR>of time =(1/2) Muhūrta.<BR>--9 A sort of<BR>bent grass.<BR>--10 A juggling trick.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चरणः a bird.<BR>--चीरं {1}<BR>a small reed. {2} a tube round<BR>which the woof is wound.<BR>--जंघः<BR>{1} a crow. {2} a kind of crane.<BR>--तरंगः<BR>{1} an astrologer. {2} a debaucher,<BR>ravisher.<BR>--नक्षत्रं = जन्मनक्षत्र q. v.<BR>--परीक्षा feeling the pulse.<BR>--मंडलं<BR>the celestial equator.<BR>--यंत्रं any<BR>tubular instrument.<BR>--व्रणः sinus, an<BR>ulcer, a fistula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिका
नाडिका<BR>1 A tubular organ &c.;<BR>see नाडि.<BR>--2 A Ghaṭikā or 24<BR>minutes; नाडिकाविच्छेदपटहः Māl. 7;<BR>K. 13, 70.<BR>--3 A hollow stalk in<BR>general.<BR>--4 A fistulous sore.<BR>--5<BR>A ray of the sun.<BR>--6 A gong,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">Page0613-c+ 54</a>]<BR>(on which the hours are struck).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिंधम|नाडिन्धम|नाडिंधमः|नाडिन्धमः
नाडिं(डीं)धम a. Causing a<BR>movement of the tubular organs (as<BR>fright &c.); नाडिंधमेन श्वासेन K. 353.<BR>--मः A goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडींधम
नाडिं(डीं)धम a. Causing a<BR>movement of the tubular organs (as<BR>fright &c.); नाडिंधमेन श्वासेन K. 353.<BR>--मः A goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिंधय|नाडिन्धय|नाडिन्धयः
नाडिंधय a. Drinking or sucking<BR>through a tube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडीका
नाडीका The wind-pipe or throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाडिकेलः|नाडिकेल
नाडिकेलः = नारिकेरः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाणकं|नाणक
नाणकं A coin, anything<BR>stamped with an impression; एषा<BR>नाणकमोषिका मकशिका Mk. 1. 23;<BR>Y. 2. 240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिचिर
नातिचिर a. Of no long duration,<BR>not very long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिदूर
नातिदूर a. Not very far or<BR>distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नातिवादः|नातिवाद
नातिवादः Avoiding abusive<BR>language.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नात्रः|नात्र|नात्रं
नात्रः<BR>1 Śiva.<BR>--2 A sage.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1<BR>Praise.<BR>--2 Surprise, wonder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथ्
नाथ् {c1c} P. (नाथति, but<BR>sometimes A. also)<BR>1 To ask, beg,<BR>solicit for anything (with dat. or<BR>two acc.); मोक्षाय नाथते मुनिः Vop.;<BR>नाथसे किमु पतिं न भूभृतः Ki. 13. 59;<BR>संतुष्टमिष्टानि तमिष्टदेवं नाथंति के नाम न<BR>लोकनाथं N. 3. 25.<BR>--2 To have<BR>power, be master, prevail.<BR>--3 To<BR>harass, trouble.<BR>--4 To bless, wish<BR>well to, give blessings to; (said<BR>to be Atm. only in this sense);<BR>नाथितशमे Mv. 1. 11; (Mammaṭa<BR>quotes the line दीनं त्वामनुनाथते<BR>कुचयुगं पत्रावृतं मा कृथाः to show that<BR>नाथ् here only means ‘to ask or<BR>beg’, and says that नाथते should,<BR>therefore, be नाथति); सर्पिषो नाथते Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथः|नाथ
नाथः [नाथ्-अच्]<BR>1 A lord, master,<BR>protector, leader; नाथे कुतस्त्वय्यशुभं<BR>प्रजानां R. 5. 13, 2. 73, 3. 45;<BR>त्रिलोक˚, कैलास˚ &c.<BR>--2 A husband.<BR>--3 A rope passed through the nose<BR>of a draft-ox.<BR>--4 A possessor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हरिः a beast (पशु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाथवत्|नाथवन्त्
नाथवत् a.<BR>1 Possessed of a lord<BR>or protector; नाथवंतस्त्वया<BR>लोकास्त्वमनाथा विपत्स्यसे U. 1. 43.<BR>--2<BR>Dependent, subject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादः|नाद
नादः [नद्-घञ्]<BR>1 A loud roar,<BR>ery, shout, sounding, roaring;<BR>सिंहनादः, घन˚ &c.<BR>--2 A sound in<BR>general; Māl. 5. 20.<BR>--3 (In Yoga phil.)<BR>The nasal sound represented by a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">Page0614-a+ 54</a>]<BR>semi-circle ( ◡ ).<BR>--4 One who<BR>praises.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0613-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादवत्|नादवन्त्
नादवत् a. Sonant, resounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादि
नादि a. Sounding, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादिन्
नादिन् a.<BR>1 Sounding, resonant;<BR>अंबुदवृंदनादी रथः Mb., R. 3. 59; 19. 5.<BR>--2 Bellowing, roaring; खर˚, सिंह˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नादेय|नादेयं|नादेयः
नादेय (यी f.) [नद्या नदस्य वा ढक्]<BR>River-born, aquatic, marine.<BR>--यं<BR>Rock-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाद्य
नाद्य a. Belonging to a river,<BR>river-born.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाध्
नाध् = नाथ् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाना
नाना ind.<BR>1 In different places,<BR>in different ways, manifoldly,<BR>variously.<BR>--2 Distinctly, separately.<BR>--3 Without (= विना); (with acc.,<BR>instr. or abl.); नाना नारीं निष्फला<BR>लोकयात्रा Vop.; (विश्वं) न नाना शंभुनां<BR>रामात् वर्षेणाधोक्षजोवंरः ibid.<BR>--4<BR>(Used as an adjective at the<BR>beginning of comp.) Manifold,<BR>various, sundry, different, diverse;<BR>नानाफलैः फलति कल्पलतेव भूमिः<BR>Bh. 2. 46; Bg. 1. 9, Ms. 9. 148.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अत्यय a. of different kinds,<BR>manifold, diverse.<BR>--अर्थ a. {1} having<BR>different aims or objects. {2}<BR>having different meanings,<BR>homonymous (as a word).<BR>--आत्मवादिन्<BR>a. maintaining the Sāṃkhya<BR>doctrine that each individual has a<BR>soul distinct from the universal<BR>spirit.<BR>--कारं ind. having done<BR>variously.<BR>--ग्रहः taking separately.<BR>--जातीय a. of diverse kinds or<BR>sorts.<BR>--ध्वनिः a musical instrument<BR>producing more than one sound.<BR>--रस a. of different or varying<BR>tastes; M. 1. 4.<BR>--रूप a. of different<BR>forms, diverse, multiform, various.<BR>--वर्ण a. of different colours.<BR>--विध<BR>a. of various sorts, diverse,<BR>manifold.<BR>--विधं ind. in various ways.<BR>--वीर्य a. having manifold energy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानानं|नानान
नानानं ind. Ved. Differently,<BR>separately &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नानांद्रः|नानान्द्र|नानांद्र|नानान्द्रः
नानांद्रः A husband's sister's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नांत|नान्त
नांत a. Endless, infinite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नांतरीयक|नान्तरीयक
नांतरीयक a. Inseparable,<BR>invariably connected; अविनाभावः<BR>संवंधमात्रं न तु नांतरीयकत्वं K. P. 2.<BR>(नांतरीयकत्वं = तदभावे तदभावरूपा व्याप्तिः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नांत्रं|नान्त्र|नांत्र|नान्त्रं
नांत्रं Praise, eulogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नांदिकरः|नान्दिकर|नांदिकर|नान्दिकरः
नांदिकरः, नांदिन् m. The speaker<BR>of the नांदी or benediction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नांदिन्|नान्दिन्
नांदिकरः, नांदिन् m. The speaker<BR>of the नांदी or benediction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नांदी|नान्दी
नांदी [नंदांति देवा अत्र नंद्-घञ् पृषो˚ वृद्धिः<BR>ङीप्]<BR>1 Joy, satisfaction, delight.<BR>--2 Prosperity.<BR>--3 Praise of a deity<BR>at the commencement of a religious<BR>rite or observance.<BR>--4 Particularly,<BR>the benedictory verse or verses<BR>recited as a sort of prologue at the<BR>beginning of a drama, benediction;<BR>आशीर्वचनसंयुक्ता नित्यं यस्मात्प्रयुज्यते ।<BR>देवद्विजनृपादीनां तस्मान्नांदीति संज्ञिता ॥ or<BR>देवद्विजनृपादीनामाशर्विचनपूर्विका । नंदंति<BR>देवता यस्यां तस्मान्नांदीति कीर्तिता ॥.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः see नांदिन्, --निनादः, --नादः,<BR>--रवः a shout of joy or rejoicing;<BR>Mv. 2. 4.<BR>--पटः the lid or cover of a<BR>well.<BR>--मुख a. (the class of manes<BR>or deceased ancestors) to whom<BR>the नांदीमुखश्राद्ध is offered. (--खं),<BR>˚श्राद्धं a Śrāddha ceremony<BR>performed in memory of the manes,<BR>preliminary to any festive occasion such<BR>as marriage &c.<BR>--(खः) the cover<BR>or lid of a well.<BR>--(खी) a female<BR>ancestor entitled to a share in the<BR>above Śrāddha.<BR>--वादिन् m. {1} the<BR>speaker of a prologue to a drama.<BR>{2} a drummer.<BR>--श्राद्धं see नांदीमुखं<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नांदीकः|नान्दीक|नान्दीकः
नांदीकः<BR>1 A post in a door-way<BR>set up for good luck.<BR>--2 = नांदीश्राद्ध<BR>see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितः|नापित
नापितः A barber, shaver.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शाला a barber's shop,<BR>shavinghouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापितायनिः|नापितायनि
नापितायनिः The son of a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नापित्यं|नापित्य|नापित्यः
नापित्यं The trade of a barber.<BR>--त्यः The son of a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभकः|नाभक
नाभकः A myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभस
नाभस a. (सी f.) Heavenly,<BR>celestial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभि|नाभिः
नाभि --भी m. f. [नह्-इञ्<BR>भश्चांतादेशः cf. Uṇ. 4. 125]<BR>1 The navel;<BR>गंगावर्तसनाभिर्नाभिः Dk. 2; &c.;<BR>निम्ननाभिः Me. 82; R. 6. 52; Me. 28.<BR>--2 Any navel-like cavity. --m.<BR>1<BR>The nave of a wheel; Pt. 1. 81.<BR>--2 The centre, focus, chief point.<BR>--3 Chief, leader, head; कृत्स्नस्य<BR>नाभिर्नृपमंडलस्य R. 18. 20.<BR>--4 Near<BR>relationship, community (of race &c.);<BR>as in सनाभि q. v.<BR>--5 A paramount<BR>sovereign or lord; R. 9. 15.<BR>--6 A<BR>near relation.<BR>--7 A Kṣatriya.<BR>--8<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-c" target="_blank">Page0614-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Home.<BR>--भिः f. Musk. (i. e. मृगनाभि).<BR>(N. B. नाभि at the end of Bah. comp.<BR>becomes नाभ when the comp. is<BR>used as an epithet; as पद्मनाभः.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवर्तः the cavity of the<BR>navel.<BR>--कंटकः, --गु (गो) लकः<BR>ruptured navel.<BR>--जः, --जन्मन् m.,<BR>--भूः<BR>epithets of Brahmā.<BR>--नाडी, --नालं {1}<BR>the umbilical cord. {2} rupture of<BR>the navel.<BR>--मूलं the part of the<BR>body immediately under the navel.<BR>--वर्धनं {1} cutting or division of the<BR>umbilical cord. {2} rupture of the<BR>navel. {3} corpulency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभी
नाभि --भी m. f. [नह्-इञ्<BR>भश्चांतादेशः cf. Uṇ. 4. 125]<BR>1 The navel;<BR>गंगावर्तसनाभिर्नाभिः Dk. 2; &c.;<BR>निम्ननाभिः Me. 82; R. 6. 52; Me. 28.<BR>--2 Any navel-like cavity. --m.<BR>1<BR>The nave of a wheel; Pt. 1. 81.<BR>--2 The centre, focus, chief point.<BR>--3 Chief, leader, head; कृत्स्नस्य<BR>नाभिर्नृपमंडलस्य R. 18. 20.<BR>--4 Near<BR>relationship, community (of race &c.);<BR>as in सनाभि q. v.<BR>--5 A paramount<BR>sovereign or lord; R. 9. 15.<BR>--6 A<BR>near relation.<BR>--7 A Kṣatriya.<BR>--8<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-c" target="_blank">Page0614-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Home.<BR>--भिः f. Musk. (i. e. मृगनाभि).<BR>(N. B. नाभि at the end of Bah. comp.<BR>becomes नाभ when the comp. is<BR>used as an epithet; as पद्मनाभः.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवर्तः the cavity of the<BR>navel.<BR>--कंटकः, --गु (गो) लकः<BR>ruptured navel.<BR>--जः, --जन्मन् m.,<BR>--भूः<BR>epithets of Brahmā.<BR>--नाडी, --नालं {1}<BR>the umbilical cord. {2} rupture of<BR>the navel.<BR>--मूलं the part of the<BR>body immediately under the navel.<BR>--वर्धनं {1} cutting or division of the<BR>umbilical cord. {2} rupture of the<BR>navel. {3} corpulency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिका
नाभिका A cavity shaped like a<BR>navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभिल
नाभिल a. [नाभिरस्त्यस्य सिध्मा˚ लच्]<BR>Relating to or coming from a navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभीलं|नाभील
नाभीलं<BR>1 The cavity of the navel.<BR>--2 Pain.<BR>--3 A ruptured navel.<BR>--4<BR>The groin of a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाभ्य|नाभ्यं|नाभ्यः
नाभ्य a. [नाभि-यत्] Relating to,<BR>proceeding from, being in, the<BR>navel, umbilical.<BR>--भ्यः An epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम
नाम ind. A particle used in the<BR>following senses:<BR>1 Named, called,<BR>by name; हिमालयो नाम नगाधिराजः<BR>Ku. 1. 1; तन्नंदिनीं सुवृत्तां नाम Dk. 7.<BR>--2 Indeed, certainly, truly,<BR>forsooth, verily, to be sure; मया नाम<BR>जितं V. 2. 17; विनीतवेषेण<BR>प्रवेष्टव्यानि तपोवनानि नान Ś. 1; आश्वासितस्य<BR>मम नाम V. 5. 16 ‘when I was just<BR>consoled’; तन्नाम निष्ठुराः पुरुषाः<BR>Mk. 5. 32 ‘that means men are cruel’.<BR>--3<BR>Probably, perhaps; oft. with मा;<BR>अये पदशब्द इव मा नाम रक्षिणः Mk. 3.<BR>‘perhaps (but I hope not) that of<BR>guards’; मा नाम अकार्यं कुर्यात् Mk. 4.<BR>--4 possibility; तवैव नामास्त्रगतिः<BR>Ku. 3. 19; त्वया नाम मुनिर्विमान्यः Ś. 5. 20<BR>‘is it possible &c’. (implying censure);<BR>frequently used with अपि in the<BR>sense of ‘I wish’, ‘would that’,<BR>‘is it likely that &c.’; see under अपि.<BR>--5 A feigned or pretended action,<BR>pretence (अलीक); कार्तांतिको नाम<BR>भूत्वा Dk. 130; so भीतो नामावप्लुत्य 104 ‘as<BR>if afraid;’ परिश्रमं नाम विनीय च क्षण<BR>Ku. 5. 32.<BR>--6 (With imperatives)<BR>Granted, though, it may be, well,<BR>it may be; तद्भवतु नाम शोकावेगाय<BR>K. 328; अतनुषु विभवेषु ज्ञातयः संतु नाम<BR>Ś. 5. 8; Bh. 1. 16; एवं नामास्तु ‘be it<BR>so, if you like,’; करोतु नाम नीतिज्ञो<BR>व्यवसायमितस्ततः H. 2. 14 ‘though he<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-a" target="_blank">Page0615-a+ 57</a>]<BR>may exert himself’; so Māl. 10. 7.<BR>--7 Anger or censure; ममापि नाम<BR>दशाननस्य परैः परिभवः G. M.; (the<BR>sentence may imply ‘censure’ also);<BR>किं नाम विस्फुरंति शस्त्राणि U. 4; ममापि<BR>नाम सत्त्वैरभिभूयंते गृहाः Ś. 6.<BR>--8<BR>Wonder; आश्चर्यमंधो नाम पुत्रं द्रक्ष्यति Sk.<BR>--9 Recollection. नाम is often used<BR>with the interrogative pronoun and<BR>its derivatives कथं, कदा &c. in the<BR>sense of ‘possibly’, ‘indeed’, ‘I<BR>should like to know’; अयि कथं<BR>नामैतत् U. 6; R. 16. 82; Bh. 2. 44;<BR>H. 1. 104; को नाम राज्ञां प्रियः Pt. 1. 146;<BR>को नाम पाकाभिमुखस्य जंतुर्द्वाराणि दैवस्य<BR>पिधातुमीष्टे U. 7. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0614-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामन्
नामन् n. [म्नायते अभ्यंस्यते नम्यते<BR>अर्भिधीयते अर्थोऽनेन वा]<BR>1 A name,<BR>appellation, personal name (opp. गोत्र);<BR>किं नु नामैतदस्याः Mu. 1. 1; नाम ग्रह्<BR>‘to address or call upon by name;’<BR>नामग्राहमरोदीत्सा Bk. 5. 5; नाम कृ or<BR>दा, नाम्ना or नामतः कृ ‘to give a name,<BR>call, name’; चकार नाम्ना रघुमात्मसंभवं<BR>R. 3. 21, 5. 36; तौ कुशलवौ चकार<BR>किल नामतः 15. 32; चंद्रापीड इति नाम<BR>चक्रे K. 74; मातरं नामतः पृच्छेयं Ś. 7.<BR>--2 The mere name; संतप्तायसि<BR>सम्स्थितस्य पयसो नामापि न ज्ञायते Bh. 2. 67<BR>‘not even the name, i. e. no trace<BR>or mark is seen’ &c.; Pt. 1. 250.<BR>--3 (In gram.) A noun, substantive<BR>(opp. आख्यात); तन्नाम येनाभिदधाति सत्त्वं;<BR>सत्त्वप्रधानानि नामानि Nir.<BR>--4 A word,<BR>name, synonymous word; इति<BR>वृक्षनामानि.<BR>--5 Substance (opp. गुण).<BR>--6<BR>Water.<BR>--7 Ved. Mark, sign, token.<BR>--8 Form, mode, manner.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंक a. marked with a name;<BR>R. 12. 103.<BR>--अनुशासनं, --अभिधानं {1}<BR>declaring one's name. {2} a<BR>dictionary, lexicon.<BR>--अपराधः abusing (a<BR>respectable man) by name, calling<BR>names.<BR>--आख्यातिक a. relating to<BR>nouns and verbs.<BR>--आवली a list of<BR>names (of a god).<BR>--करणं, --कर्मन्<BR>n. {1} the ceremony of naming a child<BR>after birth. {2} a nominal affix.<BR>--ग्रहः, --ग्रहणं addressing or<BR>mentioning by name, utterance of the name,<BR>calling to mind the name; पुण्यानि<BR>नामग्रहणान्यपि महामुनीनां K. 43;<BR>Ms. 8. 271; R. 7. 41; 6. 67.<BR>--ग्राहं ind.<BR>by naming, by mentioning the<BR>name; Bk. 5. 5.<BR>--त्यागः<BR>abandonment of name; स्वनामत्यागं करोमि<BR>Pt. 1 ‘I shall forego my name’.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">Page0615-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--द्वादशी a kind of religious<BR>ceremony, the worship of Durgā daily<BR>under one of her 12 names.<BR>--धातुः<BR>a nominal verb, denominative base<BR>(as पार्थायते, वृषस्यति &c.).<BR>--धारक,<BR>--धारिन् a. bearing only the name, in<BR>name only, nominal; Pt. 2. 84.<BR>--धेयं {1} a name, appellation;<BR>वनज्योत्स्नेति कृतनामधेया Ś. 1; किं नामधेया<BR>सा M. 4; R. 1. 45, 10. 67, 11. 8;<BR>Ms. 2. 30. {2} the ceremony of<BR>naming a child.<BR>--नामिकः an epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--निर्देशः indication by<BR>name.<BR>--मात्र a. having only the<BR>name, nominal, in name;<BR>Pt. 1. 77; 2. 86.<BR>--(त्रं) the mere name or<BR>mention (of a thing);<BR>नाममात्रप्रस्तावो भे विषादाय कल्पते Ś. 7;<BR>Pt. 3. 81; H. 1. 128; नाममात्रावशेषिताः<BR>शत्रवः Rām.<BR>--माला, --संग्रहः a list of<BR>names, glossary (of nouns).<BR>--मुद्रा<BR>a seal-ring, signet-ring; उभे<BR>नाममुद्राक्षराण्यनुवाच्य परस्परमवलोकयतः<BR>Ś. 1.<BR>--लिंगं gender of nouns.<BR>˚अनुशासनं rules on the gender of nouns.<BR>--वर्जित a. {1} nameless. {2} stupid,<BR>foolish.<BR>--वाचक a. expressing a<BR>name.<BR>--(कं) a proper name.<BR>--शेष<BR>a. having only the name left,<BR>remaining in name only, dead,<BR>deceased; U. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामक
नामक (At the end of adj. comp.)<BR>= नामन्; as कृतनामकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामतः
नामतः ind. By name, namely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधः|नामध
नामधः --धा m. Ved. A<BR>namegiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधा
नामधः --धा m. Ved. A<BR>namegiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामधा
नामधा ind. By name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामिक
नामिक a. Relating to a name or a<BR>noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामिः|नामि
नामिः An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नामित
नामित a. Bent, bowed down &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाम्य
नाम्य a. Pliable, flexible, pliant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायः|नाय
नायः [नी-कर्तरि ण]<BR>1 A leader,<BR>guide.<BR>--2 Guiding, directing.<BR>--3<BR>Policy.<BR>--4 Means, expedient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायक|नायकः
नायक a. [नी-ण्वुल्] Guiding,<BR>leading, conducting.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A guide,<BR>leader, conductor.<BR>--2 A chief,<BR>master, head, lord.<BR>--3 A<BR>pre-eminent or principal person,<BR>distinguished personage; सैन्यनायकः &c.<BR>--4 A general, commander.<BR>--5 (In<BR>Rhet.) The hero of a poetic<BR>composition (a play or drama);<BR>(according to S. D. there are four<BR>main kinds of नायकः -- धीरोदात्त,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">Page0615-c+ 58</a>]<BR>धीरोद्धत, धीरललित, and धीरप्रशांत, q. q. v. v;<BR>these are again subdivided, the total<BR>number of kinds being 48; see<BR>S. D. 64-75. The Rasamañjarī mentions {3}<BR>classes पति, उपपति and वैशिक;<BR>95. 110).<BR>--6 The central gem of a neck.<BR>lace.<BR>--7 A paradigm or leading<BR>example; दशैते स्त्रीषु नायकाः.<BR>--8 An<BR>epithet of Śākyamuni.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः a king, sovereign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नायिका
नायिका<BR>1 A mistress.<BR>--2 A wife.<BR>--3 The heroine of a poetic<BR>composition. (According to S. D. a नायिका<BR>is of three kinds स्वा or स्वीया, अन्या<BR>or परकीया, and साधारणस्त्री. For<BR>further classification, see S. D. 97-112,<BR>and Rasamañjarī 3-94; cf. अन्यस्त्री<BR>also).<BR>--4 A kind of musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार|नारं|नारः
नार a. (री f.) [नरस्येदं-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Human, mortal.<BR>--2 Spiritual.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A calf.<BR>--2 Water (said to be f.<BR>also; cf. Ms. 1. 10).<BR>--रं<BR>1 A<BR>multitude or assemblage of men.<BR>--2 Dry<BR>ginger.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीटः a deceiver,<BR>(disappointing expectations raised by<BR>himself.)<BR>--जीवनं gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारक|नारकः
नारक a. (की f.) [नरक एव प्रज्ञा˚<BR>अण् नरकस्येदं अण् वा] Hellish, relating<BR>to hell, infernal.<BR>--कः<BR>1 The<BR>infernal regions, hell.<BR>--2 An inhabitant<BR>of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकिक
नारकिक, नारकिन्, नारकीय a.<BR>Hellish. --m. An inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकिन्
नारकिक, नारकिन्, नारकीय a.<BR>Hellish. --m. An inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारकीय
नारकिक, नारकिन्, नारकीय a.<BR>Hellish. --m. An inhabitant of hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारंगः|नारङ्ग|नारंग|नारङ्गं|नारङ्गः
नारंगः<BR>1 The orange tree.<BR>--2 A<BR>lecher, libertine.<BR>--3 A living being.<BR>--4 A twin.<BR>--गं, --गकं<BR>1 The fruit of<BR>the orange tree;<BR>सद्योमुंडितमत्तहूणचिबुकप्रस्पर्धि नारंगकं.<BR>--2 A carrot.<BR>--3<BR>The juice of the pepper plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारदः|नारद
नारदः [नरस्य धर्मो नारं, तत् ददाति<BR>दा-क] N. of a celebrated Devarṣi<BR>(deified saint or divine sage).<BR>[He is one of the ten mind-born sons<BR>of Brahmā, being supposed to have<BR>sprung from his thigh. He is represented<BR>as a messenger from the gods to men<BR>and vice versa, and as being very fond<BR>of promoting discords among gods and<BR>men; hence his epithet of Kalipriya.<BR>He is said to have been the inventor<BR>of the lute or Vina. He is also the<BR>author of a code of laws which goes by<BR>his name].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारसिंह|नारसिंहः
नारसिंह a. (ही f.) Pertaining<BR>to Narasiṃha.<BR>--हः An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराचः|नाराच
नाराचः [नरान् आचामति<BR>आ-चम्ड स्वार्थे अण्, नारं आचामति वा Tv.]<BR>1 An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">Page0616-a+ 54</a>]<BR>iron arrow; तत्र नाराचदुर्दिनं<BR>R. 4. 41.<BR>--2 An arrow in general;<BR>कनकनाराचपरंपराभिरिव K. 57.<BR>--3<BR>Waterelephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0615-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराचिका
नाराचिका, नाराची A goldsmith's<BR>scales (assay balance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाराची
नाराचिका, नाराची A goldsmith's<BR>scales (assay balance).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायणः|नारायण
नारायणः<BR>1 An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu; (the word is thus derived<BR>in Ms. 1. 10; आपो नारा इति प्रोक्ता<BR>आपो वै नरसूनवः । ता यदस्यायनं पूर्वं तेन<BR>नारायणः स्मृतः ॥).<BR>--2 N. of an<BR>ancient sage said to be a companion<BR>of Nara and to have produced<BR>Urvaśī from his thigh: cf. ऊरूद्भवा<BR>नरसखस्य मुनेः सुरस्त्री V. 1. 3; see<BR>नरनारायण under नर also.<BR>--णी<BR>1<BR>An epithet of Lakṣmī the goddess<BR>of wealth.<BR>--2 An epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रियः {1} N. of<BR>Śiva. {2} yellow sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिक
नारिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Watery,<BR>aqueous.<BR>--2 Spiritual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेरः|नारिकेर
नारिकेरः, --लः The cocoa-nut;<BR>नारिकेलसमाकारा दृश्यंते हि सुहृज्जनाः<BR>H. 1. 94. (The word is also written<BR>नारिकेलि-ली, नरिकेर-ल, नारीकेलि ली, --नाडि<BR>(डी) केर, नालिकेर, नालिकेलि-ली).<BR>--ली Fermented liquor made from<BR>the water of the cocoa-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारिकेलः|नारिकेल
नारिकेरः, --लः The cocoa-nut;<BR>नारिकेलसमाकारा दृश्यंते हि सुहृज्जनाः<BR>H. 1. 94. (The word is also written<BR>नारिकेलि-ली, नरिकेर-ल, नारीकेलि ली, --नाडि<BR>(डी) केर, नालिकेर, नालिकेलि-ली).<BR>--ली Fermented liquor made from<BR>the water of the cocoa-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारी
नारी [नॄ-नर-वा जातौ ङीष् नि˚]<BR>A woman; अर्थतः पुरुषो नारी या नारी<BR>र्साथतः पुमान् Mk. 3. 27.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तरंगकः {1} a paramour. {2} a<BR>libertine.<BR>--दूषणं a woman's vice,<BR>(they are: --पानं दुर्जनसंसर्गः पत्या च<BR>विरहोऽटनम् । स्वप्नोऽन्यगृहवासश्च नारीणां<BR>दूषणानि षट् Ms. 9. 13).<BR>--प्रसंगः<BR>lechery, libertinism.<BR>--रत्नं a jewel<BR>of a woman, an excellent woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्पत्य
नार्पत्य a. Kingly, relating to<BR>royalty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नार्यंगः|नार्यङ्ग|नार्यंग|नार्यङ्गः|नार्य्यङ्ग|नार्य्यङ्गः
नार्यंगः^1 The orange tree.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: diacritics in wrong order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाल|नालं|नालः
नाल a. [नलस्येदं अण्] Consisting<BR>or made of reeds.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A<BR>hollow stalk, especially the stalk of<BR>the lotus; विकचकमलैः<BR>स्निग्धवैडूर्यनालैः Me. 76; R. 6. 13; Ku. 7. 89.<BR>(--m. also in this sense).<BR>--2 Any<BR>tubular vessel of the body.<BR>--3<BR>Yellow orpiment.<BR>--4 A handle.<BR>--लः A canal, drain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालंबी
नालंबी The lute of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाला
नाला A hollow stalk, especially<BR>that of the lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिः|नालि
नालिः --ली f. [नल्-णिच् इन् वा ङीप्]<BR>1 Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>--2 A hollow stalk, especially that<BR>of the lotus.<BR>--3 A period of 24<BR>minutes (घटिका).<BR>--4 An<BR>instrument for boring an elephant's ear.<BR>--5 A canal, drain.<BR>--6 A<BR>lotusflower.<BR>--7 A piece of metal on<BR>which the hours are struck (घटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाली
नालिः --ली f. [नल्-णिच् इन् वा ङीप्]<BR>1 Any tubular vessel of the body.<BR>--2 A hollow stalk, especially that<BR>of the lotus.<BR>--3 A period of 24<BR>minutes (घटिका).<BR>--4 An<BR>instrument for boring an elephant's ear.<BR>--5 A canal, drain.<BR>--6 A<BR>lotusflower.<BR>--7 A piece of metal on<BR>which the hours are struck (घटी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकः|नालिक
नालिकः [नलमेव नालमस्त्यस्य ठन्] A<BR>buffalo.<BR>--का<BR>1 The stalk of a lotus.<BR>--2 A tube.<BR>--3 An instrument for<BR>boring an elephant's ear.<BR>--4 A period<BR>of 24 minutes.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A lotus-flower.<BR>--2 A kind of wind-instrument, a<BR>flute.<BR>--3 Myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकेर|नालिकेरः
नालिकेर, नालिकेलि-ली See नारिकेर<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकेलि
नालिकेर, नालिकेलि-ली See नारिकेर<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालिकेली
नालिकेर, नालिकेलि-ली See नारिकेर<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीकः|नालीक
नालीकः [नाल्यां कायति कै-क Tv.]<BR>1<BR>An arrow.<BR>--2 A dart, javelin.<BR>--3 A<BR>lotus.<BR>--4 The fibrous stalk of a<BR>lotus.<BR>--5 A water-pot (कमंडलु)<BR>made of the cocoa-nut.<BR>--कं An<BR>assemblage of lotus-flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीकिनी
नालीकिनी<BR>1 A multitude or<BR>assemblage of lotus-flowers.<BR>--2 A<BR>lotuspond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नालीपः|नालीप
नालीपः = कदंबक q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाविकः|नाविक
नाविकः [नावा तरति-ठन्]<BR>1 The<BR>helmsman of a vessel, a pilot;<BR>अख्यातिरिति ते कृष्ण मग्ना नौर्नाविके त्वयि<BR>नाविकपुरुषे न विश्वासः Mb.<BR>--2 A<BR>navigator, sailor.<BR>--3 A passenger on<BR>board a ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाविन्
नाविन् m. A boatman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाव्य|नाव्यं
नाव्य a. [नावा तार्यं नौ-यत्]<BR>1<BR>Accessible by a boat or ship, navigable<BR>(as a river &c.); नाव्याः सुप्रतरा नदीः<BR>R. 4. 31; नाव्यं पयः केचिदतारिषुर्भुजैः<BR>Śi. 12. 76.<BR>--2 Praiseworthy.<BR>--व्यं<BR>Newness, novelty.<BR>--व्या Ved. A<BR>navigable river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावनीत
नावनीत a. (ती f.) Mild, soft,<BR>gentle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नावमिक
नावमिक a. (की f.) Ninth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशः|नाश
नाशः [नश्-मावे घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Disappearance; गता नाशं तारा<BR>उपकृतमसाधाविव जने Mk. 5. 25.<BR>--2 Frustration,<BR>destruction, ruin, loss; Bg. 2. 40;<BR>R. 8. 88, 12. 67; so वित्त˚, बुद्धि˚ &c.<BR>--3<BR>Death.<BR>--4 Misfortune, calamity.<BR>--5<BR>Abandonment, desertion.<BR>--6 Flight,<BR>retreat.<BR>--7 (In arith.) Elimination.<BR>--8 Want of apprehension,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">Page0616-c+ 55</a>]<BR>non-perception (अनुपलंभ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशक
नाशक a. [नश्-णिच्-ण्वुल्]<BR>Destructive, destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशन
नाशन a. [नश्-णिच्-ल्यु] (नी f.)<BR>Destroying, causing to perish,<BR>removing (in comp.).<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Destruction, ruin.<BR>--2 Removing, removal,<BR>expulsion.<BR>--3 Perishing, death.<BR>--4<BR>Forgetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशित
नाशित p. p. Destroyed, ruined,<BR>made to perish, lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाशिन्
नाशिन् a. (नी f.) [नअ-निनि]<BR>1<BR>Destruetive, destroying, removing.<BR>--2 Perishing, perishable; Bg. 2. 18<BR>Ms. 8. 185.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाश्य
नाश्य a. Destructible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाष्टिकः|नाष्टिक
नाष्टिकः The owner of anything<BR>lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाष्ट्रा
नाष्ट्रा Ved.<BR>1 Danger, destruction.<BR>--2 An evil spirit, a goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्
नास् {c1c} A. (नासते) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासत्य
नासत्य See under न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासा
नासा [नास्-भावे अ]<BR>1 The nose;<BR>स्फुरदधरनासापुटतया U. 1. 29;<BR>Bg. 5. 27.<BR>--2 The trunk of an elephant.<BR>--3 The upper timber of a door.<BR>--4<BR>A sound.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रं the tip of<BR>the nose; Māl. 1. 1.<BR>--छिद्रं, --रंध्रं,<BR>--विवरं a nostril.<BR>--दारु n. the upper<BR>timber of a door-frame.<BR>--नाहः the<BR>thickening of the membrane of the<BR>nose.<BR>--परिस्रावः running at the nose.<BR>a running cold.<BR>--पुटः, --पुटं a nostril,<BR>˚मर्यादा the septum of the nose.<BR>--वंशः the bridge of the nose.<BR>--स्रावः<BR>a running cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकंधम|नासिकन्धम|नासिकन्धमः
नासिकंधम a. Blowing or<BR>breathing through the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिकंधय|नासिकन्धय|नासिकन्धयः
नासिकंधय a. Drinking through<BR>the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिका
नासिका [नास्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 The nose<BR>see नासा.<BR>--2 Any nose-shaped object.<BR>--3 The trunk of an elephant.<BR>--4<BR>The upper timber of a door.<BR>--5 A projection.<BR>--6 An epithet of<BR>the nymph Aśvinī.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मलः<BR>the mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिक्य|नासिक्यं|नासिक्यः
नासिक्य a. [नासिका-ण्य]<BR>1 Nasal.<BR>--2 Being in the nose.<BR>--क्यः A<BR>nasal sound.<BR>--क्यौं (du.) An epithet of<BR>the Aśvins.<BR>--क्यं The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासिक्यकं|नासिक्यक
नासिक्यकं The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्यं|नास्य
नास्यं A nose-cord, the rein of a<BR>draught-ox (passed through the<BR>septum of the nostrils.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0616-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नासीरं|नासीर
नासीरं [नासाय ईर्ते ईर्-क Tv.]<BR>Advancing or fighting in front of an<BR>army.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The van or front (of<BR>an army &c.); नासीरचरयोर्भटयोः<BR>Mv. 6; N. 1. 68.<BR>--2 A champion<BR>who advances before the line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्ति
नास्ति ind. ‘It is not’,<BR>non-existence, as in नास्तिक्षीरा &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वादः assertion of the<BR>non-existence of God or a Supreme ruler,<BR>atheism, infidelity; बौद्धेनेव सर्वदा<BR>नास्तिवादशूरेण K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिक|नास्तिकः
नास्तिक a. or<BR>--कः [नास्ति<BR>परलोकस्तत्साधनमदृष्टं तत्साक्षीश्वरो वा इति मतिरस्य ठन्]<BR>An atheist, unbeliever, one who<BR>denies the authority of the Vedas<BR>and a future life or the existence of<BR>a supreme ruler or creator of the<BR>universe; Śi. 16. 7; Ms. 2. 11;<BR>8. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिक्यं|नास्तिक्य
नास्तिक्यं Atheism, infidelity,<BR>heresy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्तिदः|नास्तिद
नास्तिदः The mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नास्यं|नास्य
नास्यं See under नासा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहः|नाह
नाहः [नह् भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Binding,<BR>confinement.<BR>--2 A trap or snare.<BR>--3<BR>Costiveness, constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहुषः|नाहुष
नाहुषः --षिः An epithet of Yayāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नाहुषिः|नाहुषि
नाहुषः --षिः An epithet of Yayāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नि|निः
नि ind. Mostly used as a<BR>prefix to verbs and nouns, rarely as an<BR>adverb or preposition. It is used<BR>in the following senses (according<BR>to G. M.):<BR>1 Lowness,<BR>downward motion (‘down’, ‘under’,<BR>‘below’); निपत्, निषद्.<BR>--2 A group<BR>or collection; निकर, निकाय.<BR>--3<BR>Intensity; निकाम, निगृहीत.<BR>--4<BR>Command, order; निदेश.<BR>--5<BR>Continuance, permanence; निविशते.<BR>--6<BR>Skill; निपुण.<BR>--7 Restraint,<BR>confinement; निबंध.<BR>--8 Inclusion (‘into’,<BR>‘in’); निपीतमुदकं.<BR>--9 Proximity,<BR>nearness; निकट.<BR>--10 Insult, wrong,<BR>harm; निकृति, निकार.<BR>--11 Showing;<BR>निदर्शन.<BR>--12 Cessation; निवृत्.<BR>--13<BR>Resort, refuge; निलय.<BR>--14 Doubt.<BR>--15 Certainty.<BR>--16 Affirmation.<BR>--17<BR>Throwing, giving &c. (according<BR>to Durgādāsa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षिप्
निःक्षिप् = निक्षिप् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षिप्त
निःक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Thrown or sent<BR>away.<BR>--2 Passed, spent (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःक्षेपः|निःक्षेप
निःक्षेपः<BR>1 Throwing, sending away.<BR>--2 Spending (time).<BR>--3 Wiping<BR>(tears).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशिष्
निःशिष् Caus.<BR>1 To reduce to<BR>nothing, annihilate, destroy<BR>completely.<BR>--2 To leave no remainder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःशेष|निःशेषं
निःशेष a. [निर्गतः शेषो यस्य] Whole,<BR>complete, entire;<BR>निःशेषविश्राणितकोशजातं R. 5. 1.<BR>--षं, --षेण ind.<BR>Wholly, completely, totally,<BR>entirely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रयणी
निःश्रय(यि)णी, निःश्रेणी f.<BR>A ladder, staircase; R. 15. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रयिणी
निःश्रय(यि)णी, निःश्रेणी f.<BR>A ladder, staircase; R. 15. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेणी
निःश्रय(यि)णी, निःश्रेणी f.<BR>A ladder, staircase; R. 15. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्रेयसं|निःश्रेयस|निःश्रेयसः
निःश्रेयसं [निश्चितं श्रेयः नि˚] Final<BR>beatitude, absolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वस्
निःश्वस् (often written निश्वस्)<BR>{c2c} P. To sigh, heave a sigh of grief,<BR>pant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वसनं|निःश्वसन
निःश्वसनं Breathing out, sighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वसित
निःश्वसित p. p.<BR>1 Breathed out,<BR>sighed.<BR>--2 Sighing.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Expiration.<BR>--2 A sigh; V. 2. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःश्वासः|निःश्वास
निःश्वासः, निश्वासः<BR>1 Breathing out,<BR>expiration.<BR>--2 Sighing, a sigh,<BR>breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्वासः|निश्वास
निःश्वासः, निश्वासः<BR>1 Breathing out,<BR>expiration.<BR>--2 Sighing, a sigh,<BR>breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसह
निःसह a.<BR>1 Unable to bear,<BR>resist or suffer, impatient.<BR>--2<BR>Powerless, unnerved, spiritless, languid,<BR>fatigued; अयि विरम निःसहासि जाता<BR>Māl. 3; so Māl. 2, 7, U. 3.<BR>--3<BR>Intolerable, unbearable, irresistible<BR>(in a passive sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसृ
निःसृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To come forth,<BR>slip away from, go out, issue from;<BR>बाणैः खरकार्मुकनिःसृतैः Rām.;<BR>Śi. 9. 25.<BR>--2 To depart, set out for;<BR>Ms. 6. 4.<BR>--3 To flow forth, ooze out,<BR>exude; यो हेमकुंभस्तनानिःसृतानां R. 2. 36.<BR>--Caus. To turn out, expel, drive<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसरणं|निःसरण
निःसरणं<BR>1 Going out, exit.<BR>--2 An<BR>egress or outlet from a house, a<BR>gate.<BR>--3 Final departure, death.<BR>--4<BR>A means, expedient, remedy.<BR>--5<BR>Final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारः|निःसार
निःसारः Going forth or out, exit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारणं|निःसारण
निःसारणं<BR>1 Expelling, driving or<BR>turning out.<BR>--2 The outlet from a<BR>house, ingress or egress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःसारित|निःसारितः
निःसारित a. Expelled, dismissed,<BR>turned out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्रवः|निःस्रव
निःस्रवः Remainder, surplus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निःस्रावः|निःस्राव
निःस्रावः<BR>1 Expense, expending,<BR>expenditure.<BR>--2 The water of<BR>boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकट|निकटं|निकटः
निकट a. Near, close, hard by,<BR>proximate.<BR>--टः, --टं Proximity. (<BR>निकटे is used adverbially in the sense<BR>of ‘near’, ‘at hand’, ‘hard or close<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">Page0617-c+ 55</a>]<BR>by;’ वहति निकटे कालस्रोतः समस्तभयाव<BR>हं Śānti. 3. 2.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकम्
निकम् {c10c} A. To desire<BR>excessively, long vehemently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाम|निकामं|निकामः
निकाम a. [नि कम् घञ्]<BR>1 Plentiful<BR>copious, abundant; निकाजलां स्त्रोतोवहां<BR>Ś. 6. 16.<BR>--2 Desirous of.<BR>--मः, --मं Wish,<BR>desire.<BR>--मं ind.<BR>1 According to one's<BR>wish or desire, agreeably to desire.<BR>--2 To one's satisfaction, to the<BR>heart's content; रात्रौ निकामं<BR>शयितव्यमपि नास्ति Ś. 2 ‘I cannot even<BR>sleep at ease or comfortably at<BR>night.’<BR>--3 Very much, exceedingly<BR>निकामं क्षामांगी Māl. 2. 3; often used<BR>as the first member of comp. when<BR>it loses its final म्; निकामनिरंकुशः<BR>Gīt. 7; Ku. 5. 23; Śi. 4. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकामनं|निकामन
निकामनं Desire, longing after.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकरः|निकर
निकरः [निकॄ भावादौ अप्]<BR>1 A heap,<BR>pile.<BR>--2 A flock, multitude,<BR>collection; पपात स्वेदांबुप्रसर इव हर्षाश्रुनिकरः<BR>Gīt. 11; Śi. 4. 58; Rs. 6. 18.<BR>--3 A<BR>bundle.<BR>--4 Sap, pith, essence.<BR>--5<BR>A suitable gift, honorarium.<BR>--6 A<BR>treasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्षण|निकर्षणं
निकर्षण See under निकृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषः|निकष
निकषः(सः)<BR>1 A touch-stone,<BR>whet-stone; निकषे हेमरेखेव<BR>R. 17. 46; Mv. 1. 4.<BR>--2 (Fig.) Anything<BR>serving as a touch-stone, a test;<BR>नन्वेष दर्पनिकषस्तव चंद्रकेतुः U. 5. 10;<BR>आदर्शः शिक्षितानां सुचरितनिकषः<BR>Mk. 1. 48; Dk. 1; K. 44.<BR>--3 A streak or<BR>line of gold made on a touch-stone;<BR>कनकनिकषरुचिशुचिवसनेन श्वसिति म<BR>सा परिजनहसनेन Gīt. 7;<BR>कनकनिकषस्निग्धा विद्युत्प्रिया न ममोर्वशी<BR>V. 4. 1; 5. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपलः, --ग्रावन् m.<BR>--पाषाणः a touch-stone, whetstone;<BR>तत्प्रेमहेमनिकषोपलतां तनोति Gīt. 11;<BR>तत्त्वनिकषग्रावा तु तेषां विपद् H. 1. 210<BR>2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकसः|निकस
निकषः(सः)<BR>1 A touch-stone,<BR>whet-stone; निकषे हेमरेखेव<BR>R. 17. 46; Mv. 1. 4.<BR>--2 (Fig.) Anything<BR>serving as a touch-stone, a test;<BR>नन्वेष दर्पनिकषस्तव चंद्रकेतुः U. 5. 10;<BR>आदर्शः शिक्षितानां सुचरितनिकषः<BR>Mk. 1. 48; Dk. 1; K. 44.<BR>--3 A streak or<BR>line of gold made on a touch-stone;<BR>कनकनिकषरुचिशुचिवसनेन श्वसिति म<BR>सा परिजनहसनेन Gīt. 7;<BR>कनकनिकषस्निग्धा विद्युत्प्रिया न ममोर्वशी<BR>V. 4. 1; 5. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपलः, --ग्रावन् m.<BR>--पाषाणः a touch-stone, whetstone;<BR>तत्प्रेमहेमनिकषोपलतां तनोति Gīt. 11;<BR>तत्त्वनिकषग्रावा तु तेषां विपद् H. 1. 210<BR>2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकषा
निकषा N. of the mother of<BR>Rāvaṇa or of imps in general. --ind.<BR> Near, hard, close by, at hand<BR>(with acc.); निकषा सौधभित्तिं Dk.;<BR>विलंध्य लंकां निकषा हनिष्यति Śi. 1. 68.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मजः a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकायः|निकाय
निकायः [नि-चि-घञ् कुत्वम्]<BR>1 A<BR>heap, an assemblage, a class,<BR>multitude, flock, group in general;<BR>Mv. 1.<BR>--2 A congregation, school, an<BR>association of persons who perform<BR>like duties.<BR>--3 A house,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">Page0618-a+ 54</a>]<BR>habitation, dwelling-place; काशीनिकायः<BR>&c.<BR>--4 The body.<BR>--5 Aim, butt,<BR>mark.<BR>--6 The Supreme Being.<BR>--7<BR>Ved. Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0617-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाय्यः|निकाय्य
निकाय्यः [cf. P. III. 1. 129] A<BR>dwelling, habitation, house; न<BR>प्रणाय्यो जनः कच्चिन्निकाय्यं तेऽधितिष्ठति<BR>Bk. 6. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकार|निकारः
निकार &c. See under निकृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाशः|निकाश
निकाशः, --सः [नि-काश्-घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Appearance, sight.<BR>--2 Horizon.<BR>--3<BR>Proximity, vicinity.<BR>--4 Likeness,<BR>resemblance (at the end of comp.);<BR>Māl. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकासः|निकास
निकाशः, --सः [नि-काश्-घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Appearance, sight.<BR>--2 Horizon.<BR>--3<BR>Proximity, vicinity.<BR>--4 Likeness,<BR>resemblance (at the end of comp.);<BR>Māl. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकाषः|निकाष
निकाषः Scratching, rubbing;<BR>Ki. 7. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुंचनः|निकुञ्चन|निकुंचन|निकुञ्चनः
निकुंचनः A measure of capacity<BR>equal to (1/4) of a Kuḍava (also निकुंचक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुंजः|निकुञ्ज|निकुंज|निकुंजं|निकुञ्जं|निकुञ्जः
निकुंजः, --जं<BR>1 A bower, an arbour’<BR>a place over-grown with shrubs<BR>and creepers; यमुनातीरवानीरनिकुंजे<BR>मंदमास्थितं Gīt. 4, 2, 11; Rs. 1. 23.<BR>--2 A vault; Māl. 2. 12.<BR>--3 A<BR>cavern; Māl. 9. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुंजं|निकुञ्ज|निकुंज|निकुञ्जं|निकुंजः|निकुञ्जः
निकुंजः, --जं<BR>1 A bower, an arbour’<BR>a place over-grown with shrubs<BR>and creepers; यमुनातीरवानीरनिकुंजे<BR>मंदमास्थितं Gīt. 4, 2, 11; Rs. 1. 23.<BR>--2 A vault; Māl. 2. 12.<BR>--3 A<BR>cavern; Māl. 9. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुंभः|निकुम्भ|निकुंभ|निकुम्भः
निकुंभः<BR>1 N. of an attendant of<BR>Śiva; R. 2. 35.<BR>--2 N. of the father<BR>of Sunda and Upasunda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुंभिला|निकुम्भिला
निकुंभिला<BR>1 A cave or grove at<BR>the western gate of Laṅkā.<BR>--2 An<BR>image of Bhadrakālī on the west<BR>side of Laṅkā.<BR>--3 A place where<BR>oblations are offered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुरंबं|निकुरम्ब|निकुरंब|निकुरम्बं
निकुरं(रुं)बं A flock, collection,<BR>mass, multitude; लतानिकुरुंबं Gīt. 11.<BR>किरण˚ Ā. L. 20; चिकुर˚ 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुरुंबं|निकुरुम्ब|निकुरुंब
निकुरं(रुं)बं A flock, collection,<BR>mass, multitude; लतानिकुरुंबं Gīt. 11.<BR>किरण˚ Ā. L. 20; चिकुर˚ 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकुलीनिका
निकुलीनिका A family art, one<BR>inherited by birth, any skill or art<BR>peculiar to a race.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृ
निकृ {c8c} U. Ved.<BR>1 To humiliate,<BR>subdue, overcome.<BR>--2 To maltreat,<BR>act or treat ill.<BR>--3 To injure, wrong,<BR>offend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकारः|निकार
निकारः<BR>1 Winnowing corn.<BR>--2<BR>Lifting up.<BR>--3 Killing, slaughter.<BR>--4 Humiliation, subjugation.<BR>--5<BR>Insult, injury, wrong, offence; तीर्णो<BR>निकारार्णवः Ve. 6. 43; Mv. 3. 41;<BR>5. 14; 7. 8; Ki. 1. 43; 3. 44.<BR>--6<BR>Abuse, reproach, disrespect.<BR>--7<BR>Wickedness, malice.<BR>--8 Opposition,<BR>contradiction^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by user ekalavya01 on 20190706. note: English word misspelled in text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकारणं|निकारण
निकारणं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत|निकृतः
निकृत p. p.<BR>1 Humbled, cast<BR>down, humiliated.<BR>--2 Insulted,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">Page0618-b+ 56</a>]<BR>offended; U. 6. 14.<BR>--3 Deceived,<BR>cheated.<BR>--4 Removed.<BR>--5 Afflicted,<BR>injured.<BR>--6 Wicked, dishonest.<BR>--7<BR>Base, low, vile.<BR>--तं Humiliation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रज्ञ a. evil-minded.<BR>--मति<BR>a. depraved in mind, base.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृति|निकृतिः
निकृति a. Base, dishonest, wicked.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1 Baseness, wickedness.<BR>--2 Dishonesty, fraud, deception;<BR>अनिकृतिनिपुणं ते चेष्टितं मानशौंड<BR>Ve. 5. 21; Ki. 1. 45.<BR>--3 Insult, offence,<BR>humiliation; Mu. 4. 11.<BR>--4 Abuse'<BR>reproach.<BR>--5 Rejection, removal.<BR>--6 Poverty, indigence.<BR>--7 The<BR>earth.<BR>--8 N. of one of the eight<BR>Vasus.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रज्ञ a.<BR>evil-minded, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृतिन्
निकृतिन् a. Base, dishonest,<BR>wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृत्
निकृत् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To cut down, cut<BR>to pieces, cut or tear off, tear up;<BR>विश्वासाद्भयमुत्पन्नं मूलान्यपि निकृंतति<BR>Pt. 2. 39; निकृंतन्निव मानसं Bk. 7. 11;<BR>भल्लनिकृत्तकंठैः R. 7. 58.<BR>--2 To cut<BR>oneself (A.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्तनं|निकर्तन
निकर्तनं Cutting down or off,<BR>tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृंतन|निकृन्तन
निकृंतन a. (नी f.) Cutting down,<BR>destroying;<BR>विरहिनिकृंतनकुंतमुखाकृतिकेतकिदंतुरिताशे(वसंते) Gīt. 11.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Cutting,<BR>cutting off, destruction.<BR>--2 An<BR>instrument for cutting; एकेन<BR>नखनिकृंतनेन सर्वं कार्ष्णायसं विज्ञातं स्यात् Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्
निकृष् {c1c} {c6c} P.<BR>1 To lessen,<BR>diminish.<BR>--2 To draw or drag down,<BR>pull down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकर्षणं|निकर्षण
निकर्षणं<BR>1 An open space for<BR>recreation, or a play-ground in<BR>or near a town.<BR>--2 A court at the<BR>entrance of a house.<BR>--3<BR>Neighbourhood.<BR>--4 An uncultivated or<BR>unploughed plot of ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकृष्ट|निकृष्टः
निकृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Low, base, vile.<BR>--2<BR>Outcast, despised.<BR>--3 Vulgar.<BR>--4<BR>Near.<BR>--ष्टं Proximity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेचायः|निकेचाय
निकेचायः Piling or collecting<BR>repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतः|निकेत
निकेतः, --तकः<BR>1 A house,<BR>habitation, mansion, abode;<BR>श्रितगोकर्णनिकेतमीश्वरं R. 8. 33; 14. 58;<BR>Bg. 12. 19; Ku. 5. 25; Ms. 6. 26; Śi. 5. 26.<BR>--2 A mark, countersign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतकः|निकेतक
निकेतः, --तकः<BR>1 A house,<BR>habitation, mansion, abode;<BR>श्रितगोकर्णनिकेतमीश्वरं R. 8. 33; 14. 58;<BR>Bg. 12. 19; Ku. 5. 25; Ms. 6. 26; Śi. 5. 26.<BR>--2 A mark, countersign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकेतनः|निकेतन|निकेतनं
निकेतनः An onion.<BR>--नं A<BR>mansion, house, abode; सिंजाना<BR>मंजुमंजीरं प्रविवेश निकेतनं Gīt. 11;<BR>Ms. 6. 26, 11. 129; Ki. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निकोचनं|निकोचन
निकोचनं Contraction,<BR>compression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्रमणं|निक्रमण
निक्रमणं Ved.<BR>1 Trampling down.<BR>--2 A foot-step, foot-fall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्वणः|निक्वण
निक्वणः, निक्वाणः<BR>1 A musical tone<BR>or sound.<BR>--2 A sound in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्वाणः|निक्वाण
निक्वणः, निक्वाणः<BR>1 A musical tone<BR>or sound.<BR>--2 A sound in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्ष्
निक्ष् {c1c} P. (निक्षति) Ved.<BR>1 To<BR>pierce.<BR>--2 To kiss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षणं|निक्षण
निक्षणं Kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षा
निक्षा A nit (a wrong form for<BR>लिक्षा q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिप्
निक्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To throw or cast<BR>down, put or place down; Y. 1. 103;<BR>Amaru. 80.<BR>--2 To entrust,<BR>commit, consign to the care of; देवीहस्ते<BR>निक्षिपता Ratn. 1; Ms. 6. 3, 8. 179,<BR>R. 1. 34.<BR>--3 To deposit, place as deposit.<BR>--4<BR>To encamp.<BR>--5 To cast off, reject.<BR>--6 To give or hand over, grant,<BR>bestow (on).<BR>--7 To install, appoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षिप्त|निक्षिप्तं
निक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Thrown or put down,<BR>thrown into.<BR>--2 Deposited, pledged,<BR>pawned.<BR>--3 Sent, sent off.<BR>--4<BR>Rejected, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपः|निक्षेप
निक्षेपः<BR>1 Throwing or casting on<BR>(with acc.); अलं मान्यानां<BR>व्याख्यानेषु कटाक्षनिक्षेपेण S. D. 2.<BR>--2 A<BR>deposit, pledge; pawn in general;<BR>Pt. 1. 14; Ms. 8. 4.<BR>--3 Anything<BR>deposited without a seal in trust or<BR>as a compensation, an open deposit;<BR>समक्षं तु निक्षेपणं निक्षेपः Mit. on<BR>Y. 2. 67.<BR>--4 Sending away.<BR>--5 Throwing<BR>away, abandoning.<BR>--6 Wiping,<BR>drying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपणं|निक्षेपण
निक्षेपणं<BR>1 Putting down, placing<BR>down (the feet); Ku. 1. 33.<BR>--2 A<BR>means by which anything is kept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेपित
निक्षेपित a.<BR>1 Caused to be put<BR>down in writing, inscribed.<BR>--2<BR>Caused to be deposited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षेप्तृ
निक्षेप्तृ m. A depositor, pawner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्षुभा
निक्षुभा<BR>1 The wife of the sun.<BR>--2<BR>A female Brāhmaṇa (ब्राह्मणी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखन्
निखन् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To dig, dig up.<BR>--2<BR>To bury, inter; ऊनद्विवर्षं निखनेत्<BR>Y. 3. 1; वसुधायां निचख्नतुः R. 12. 30;<BR>Bk. 4. 3; 16. 22.<BR>--3 To erect^1 (as<BR>a column); निचखान जयस्तंभान्<BR>R. 4. 36.<BR>--4 To implant, infix, pierce<BR>into; निचखान शरं भुजे R. 12. 90, 3. 55<BR>Bk. 3. 8; H. 4. 72.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखननं|निखनन
निखननं Digging in, burying; as<BR>in स्थूणानिखननन्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0618-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखात
निखात p. p.<BR>1 Dug up,<BR>excavated.<BR>--2 Fixed, planted (as a stake),<BR>infixed; शल्यं निखातमुदहारयतामुरस्तः<BR>R. 9. 78; 13. 61;<BR>अष्टादशद्वीपनिखातयूपः 6. 38; गाढं निखात इव मे हृदये<BR>कटाक्षः Māl. 1. 29.<BR>--3 Dug in,<BR>buried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखर्व|निखर्व्व
निखर्व a. Dwarfish.<BR>--र्वं A<BR>billion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निखिल|निखिलं
निखिल a. [निवृत्तम् खिलं शेषो यस्मात्]<BR>Complete, whole, entire, all; प्रत्यक्षं<BR>ते निखिलमचिराद्भ्रातरुक्तं मया यत्<BR>Me. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगड|निगडः
निगड a. [नि-गल्-अच् लस्य डः]<BR>Fettered, chained; बद्धस्य निगडस्य<BR>च Ms. 4. 210.<BR>--डः, --डं<BR>1 An iron<BR>chain for the feet of an elephant;<BR>बद्धापराणि परितो निगडान्यलावीत्<BR>Śi. 5. 48; Bv. 4. 20.<BR>--2 A fetter, chain or<BR>shackle in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडनं|निगडन
निगडनं Chaining, fettering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडयति
निगडयति Den. P. To put in chains,<BR>fetter; (fig. also);<BR>निद्रानिगडितजनदृशि Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगडित|निगडितः
निगडित a. Fettered, put in irons,<BR>chained, bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगणः|निगण
निगणः The smoke of a sacrificial<BR>fire or burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगद्
निगद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To proclaim,<BR>declare, announce; Śi. 9. 76.<BR>--2 To<BR>declare say, speak; R. 2. 33.<BR>--3<BR>To speak to, address (any one).<BR>--4<BR>To enumerate.<BR>--5 To call, name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदः|निगद
निगदः, निगादः<BR>1 Recitation,<BR>audible recitation of prayers.<BR>--2 A prayer<BR>repeated aloud.<BR>--3 Speech, discourse.<BR>--4 Learning anything without<BR>knowing the meaning;<BR>यदधीतमविज्ञातं निगदेनैव शब्द्यते Nir.<BR>--5<BR>Mention, mentioning; इति निगदेनैव<BR>व्याख्यातम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगादः|निगाद
निगदः, निगादः<BR>1 Recitation,<BR>audible recitation of prayers.<BR>--2 A prayer<BR>repeated aloud.<BR>--3 Speech, discourse.<BR>--4 Learning anything without<BR>knowing the meaning;<BR>यदधीतमविज्ञातं निगदेनैव शब्द्यते Nir.<BR>--5<BR>Mention, mentioning; इति निगदेनैव<BR>व्याख्यातम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगदित
निगदित a. Told, said, spoken.<BR>--तं<BR>A discourse, speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगम्
निगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go to, attain,<BR>acquire, obtain; यत्र दुःखांतं च<BR>निगच्छति Bg. 18. 36, 9. 31.<BR>--2 To<BR>get knowledge, learn.<BR>--3 To be<BR>inserted.<BR>--4 To enter (with acc. or<BR>loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमः|निगम
निगमः<BR>1 The Veda or Vedic text;<BR>साढ्यै साढ्वा साढेति निगमे P. VI. 3. 113,<BR>VII. 2. 64; Māl. 9. 4.<BR>--2 Any<BR>passage or word quoted from the Vedas,<BR>a Vedic sentence; तथापि च निगमो<BR>भवति (often found in Nirukta).<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">Page0619-b+ 55</a>]<BR>A work auxiliary to, and<BR>explanatory of, the Vedas; Ms. 4. 19 and<BR>Kull. thereon.<BR>--4 A sacred precept,<BR>the words of a god or holy man.<BR>--5<BR>A root (as the source of a word).<BR>--6<BR>Certainty, assurance.<BR>--7 Logic.<BR>--8<BR>Trade, traffic.<BR>--9 A market, fair.<BR>--10<BR>A caravan of wandering merchants.<BR>--11 A road, market-road.<BR>--12 A city.<BR>--13 Insertion of the name of a deity<BR>into a liturgical formula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमनं|निगमन
निगमनं<BR>1 Quotation of a word from<BR>the Veda or the word so quoted.<BR>--2<BR>(In logic) The conclusion in a<BR>syllogism, a deduction (the fifth<BR>member of the five-membered Indian<BR>syllogism).<BR>--3 Going in or into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगमिन्
निगमिन् a. Knowing the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरः|निगर
निगरः, --रणं &c. See under निगॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरणं|निगरण|निगरणः
निगरः, --रणं &c. See under निगॄ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगु|निगुः
निगु a. Pleasing.<BR>--गुः<BR>1 The<BR>mind.<BR>--2 Dirt, excrement.<BR>--3 A<BR>root.<BR>--4 Painting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगॄ
निगॄ {c6c} P.<BR>1 To swallow, eat up,<BR>devour; Bv. 1. 38.<BR>--2 To conceal,<BR>hide (fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरः|निगर
निगरः, निगारः Swallowing,<BR>devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगारः|निगार
निगरः, निगारः Swallowing,<BR>devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगरणं|निगरण|निगरणः
निगरणं<BR>1 Swallowing, devouring.<BR>--2 (Fig.) Taking up, completely<BR>absorbing.<BR>--णः<BR>1 The throat.<BR>--2<BR>The smoke of a sacrificial fire or<BR>burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगलः|निगल
निग(गा)लः<BR>1 Swallowing,<BR>devouring.<BR>--2 The throat or neck of<BR>a horse; ˚वत् m. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगालः|निगाल
निग(गा)लः<BR>1 Swallowing,<BR>devouring.<BR>--2 The throat or neck of<BR>a horse; ˚वत् m. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगारक
निगार(ल)क a. Swallowing,<BR>eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगालक
निगार(ल)क a. Swallowing,<BR>eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगीर्ण
निगीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Swallowed,<BR>devoured.<BR>--2 (Fig.) Completely<BR>swallowed or absorbed, hidden,<BR>concealed and hence to be supplied;<BR>उपमानेनांतर्निगीर्णस्योपमेयस्य यदध्यवसानं<BR>सैका K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूढ|निगूढः
निगूढ a.<BR>1 Hidden, concealed;<BR>Śi. 13. 59.<BR>--2 Secret, private.<BR>--3<BR>Mysterious, obscure.<BR>--4<BR>Inscrutable.<BR>--ढं ind. Secretly, privately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगूहनं|निगूहन
निगूहनं Concealing, hiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रंथनं|निग्रन्थन|निग्रंथन
निग्रंथनं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रह्
निग्रह् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To keep or hold<BR>down, keep in check.<BR>--2 To curb,<BR>restrain, suppress, control; निगृह्य<BR>शोकं K. 25; स्वकं तेजो निगृह्य<BR>Pt. 3. 174; Bg. 2. 68, R. 5. 59, 14. 85.<BR>--3 To stop, obstruct; निगृहीतो बलाद<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-c" target="_blank">Page0619-c+ 57</a>]<BR>द्वांरि Mb.<BR>--4 To punish, chastise;<BR>Ms. 8. 310; 9. 308.<BR>--5 To seize, catch,<BR>apprehend, lay hold of; तमार्यगृह्यं<BR>निगृहीतधेनुः R. 2. 33.<BR>--6 To close<BR>or contract (as eyes);<BR>माथुरोऽक्षिणी निगृह्य Mk. 2.<BR>--7 To subdue,<BR>conquer, overpower, प्रज्ञया निग्रहीतुं<BR>शक्यः Mu. 1; 1. 26.<BR>--8 To draw in,<BR>restrain; निगृह्यंतामभीशवः Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीत
निगृहीत p. p.<BR>1 Seized, arrested.<BR>--2 Restrained curbed, checked,<BR>subdued.<BR>--3 Attacked.<BR>--4 Defeated in<BR>argument, caught; भो निगृहीतोसि<BR>U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निगृहीतिः|निगृहीति
निगृहीतिः f.<BR>1 Restraint, check.<BR>--2<BR>Overpowering, subjugation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहः|निग्रह
निग्रहः<BR>1 Keeping in check,<BR>restraint, curbing, subjection; as in<BR>इंद्रियनिग्रह Ms. 6. 92; Y. 1. 222;<BR>Bh. 1. 66, Bg. 6. 34.<BR>--2 Suppression,<BR>obstruction, putting down;<BR>Ms. 6. 71.<BR>--3 Overtaking, capturing,<BR>arresting; त्वन्निग्रहे तुवरगात्रि न मे प्रयत्नः<BR>Mk. 1. 22; Śi. 2. 88.<BR>--4<BR>Confinement, imprisonment.<BR>--5 Defeat,<BR>overthrow, vanquishing.<BR>--6<BR>Dispelling, destruction, removing;<BR>R. 9. 25, 15. 6; Ku. 5. 53.<BR>--7<BR>Arresting of disease, cure.<BR>--8<BR>Punishment (opp. अनुग्रह); निग्रहानुग्रहस्य<BR>कर्ता Pt. 1; निग्रहोऽप्ययमनुग्रहीकृतः<BR>R. 11. 90, 55; 12. 52, 63.<BR>--9<BR>Rebuke, reprimand, blame.<BR>--10 Aver.<BR>sion, dislike, disgust.<BR>--11 (In<BR>Nyāya phil.) A flaw in an<BR>argument, a fault in a syllogism (by<BR>which a disputant is put down in<BR>argument); cf. Mu. 5. 10.<BR>--12 A<BR>handle.<BR>--13 A limit, boundary.<BR>--14<BR>The Supreme being.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थानं<BR>the reason of defeat, unfitness to be<BR>argued with, one of the 16<BR>categories of the Naiyāyikas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्रहण
निग्रहण a. Holding back or down,<BR>suppressing.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Subduing,<BR>suppression.<BR>--2 Capture,<BR>confinement.<BR>--3 Chastisement,<BR>punishment in general.<BR>--4 Defeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निग्राहः|निग्राह
निग्राहः<BR>1 Punishment.<BR>--2<BR>Animprecation; as in निग्राहस्ते भूयात्<BR>‘confusion seize thee!’; Bk. 7. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ|निघः
निघ a. As high as broad.<BR>--घः<BR>1<BR>A ball.<BR>--2 Sin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघंटुः|निघण्टु|निघंटु|निघण्टुः
निघंटुः<BR>1 A vocabulary or glossary<BR>of words.<BR>--2 Particularly the<BR>glossary of Vedic words explained by<BR>Yāska in his Nirukta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0619-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघर्षः|निघर्ष
निघर्षः, निघर्षणं See under निघृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघर्षणं|निघर्षण
निघर्षः, निघर्षणं See under निघृष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघसः|निघस
निघसः<BR>1 Eating, dining.<BR>--2<BR>Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघातः|निघात
निघातः<BR>1 A blow, stroke;<BR>R. 11. 78.<BR>--2 Suppression or absence<BR>of accent.<BR>--3 A vowel having a grave<BR>accent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघातिः|निघाति
निघातिः f. An iron club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघुष्टं|निघुष्ट
निघुष्टं Sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्
निघृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To rub, pound,<BR>grind.<BR>--2 To graze, wear away by<BR>rubbing or grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघर्षः|निघर्ष
निघर्षः, निघर्षणं<BR>1 Rubbing,<BR>friction; Ki. 2. 51.<BR>--2 Grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघर्षणं|निघर्षण
निघर्षः, निघर्षणं<BR>1 Rubbing,<BR>friction; Ki. 2. 51.<BR>--2 Grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्ट
निघृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Rubbed, ground.<BR>--2 Chafed, grazed.<BR>--3 Subdued,<BR>overpowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघृष्व|निघृष्वः
निघृष्व a.<BR>1 Rubbed off,<BR>excoriated.<BR>--2 Small, trifling, insignificant.<BR>--ष्वः<BR>1 A hoof.<BR>--2 Wind.<BR>--3 An<BR>ass or mule.<BR>--4 A boar.<BR>--5 A road.<BR>--ष्वं The mark of a hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निघ्न|निघ्नः
निघ्न a.<BR>1 Dependent, subservient,<BR>obedient (as a servant); तथापि निघ्नं<BR>नृप तावकीनैः प्रह्वीकृतं मे हृदयं गुणौघैः<BR>Ki. 3. 12; निघ्नस्य मे भर्तृनिदेशरौक्ष्यं देवि<BR>क्षमस्वेति बभूव नम्रः R. 14. 58.<BR>--2<BR>Docile, tractable.<BR>--3 Dependent on<BR>(i. e. following the gender &c. of) a<BR>substantive; इति विशेष्यनिघ्नवर्गः.<BR>--4<BR>(After a numeral) Multiplied by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचि
निचि {c5c} U.<BR>1 To pile up, heap up<BR>--2 To cover or fill with, strew,<BR>overspread (chiefly in p. p.);<BR>निचितं खमुपेत्य नीरदैः Ghaṭ. 1;<BR>शकुंतनीडनिचितं बिभ्रज्जटामंडलं Ś. 7. 11;<BR>Bk. 10. 4.<BR>--3 To accumulate, store;<BR>Mu. 6. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचयः|निचय
निचयः<BR>1 A collection, heap,<BR>multitude; Ki. 4. 37.<BR>--2 Store, stock,<BR>provisions; as षण्मासनिचयः.<BR>--3 An<BR>assemblage of parts constituting a<BR>whole; as in शरीरनिचय.<BR>--4 Certainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचयिन्
निचयिन् a. Full of, abounding in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचायः|निचाय
निचायः A heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचित|निचितं
निचित p. p.<BR>1 Covered, overcast,<BR>overspread; Śi. 17. 14.<BR>--2 Full of,<BR>filled.<BR>--3 Raised up.<BR>--4 Piled or<BR>heaped up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचिकी
निचिकी, --नैचिकी An excellent<BR>cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैचिकी
निचिकी, --नैचिकी An excellent<BR>cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुंपुणः|निचुम्पुण|निचुम्पुणः
निचुंपुणः^1 Ved.<BR>1 The sea.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Soma.<BR>--3 N. of an<BR>avabhrita q. v.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: निचुंपुणः according to the quotation of the RV 8.93.22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुलः|निचुल
निचुलः<BR>1 A kind of reed.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a poet and friend of Kālidāsa;<BR>स्थानादस्मात् सरसनिचुलादुत्पतोदङ्मुखः<BR>खं Me. 14 (where Malli. observes:<BR>--निचुलो नाम मह कविः कालिदासस्य सहाध्यायः;<BR>but this explanation is very<BR>doubtful).<BR>--3 An upper garment, cover<BR>cf. निचोल.<BR>--4 The tree called हिज्जल,<BR>(Barringtonia Acutangula).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचुलकं|निचुलक
निचुलकं<BR>1 A breast-plate, cuirass.<BR>--2 An outer garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोलः|निचोल
निचोलः<BR>1 A cover, veil,<BR>wrapper; ध्वांतं नीलनिचोलचारु Gīt. 11;<BR>शीलय नीलनिचोलं 5.<BR>--2 A bed-cover.<BR>--3 The cover of a litter (दोलिकावरणं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निचोलकः|निचोलक
निचोलकः<BR>1 A jacket, bodice.<BR>--2<BR>A soldier's jacket serving as a<BR>breast-plate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छविः|निच्छवि|निछवि
निच्छविः N. of a district, the<BR>modern Tirhut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छिविः|निच्छिवि|निछिवि
निच्छिविः N. of one of the<BR>degraded castes (sprung from<BR>outcast Kṣatriyas); see Ms. 10. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निच्छेदः|निच्छेद
निच्छेदः<BR>1 Cutting off.<BR>--2 (In<BR>arith.) Leaving no common<BR>measure, reducing by the common<BR>divisor to the least term, so as to be<BR>capable of no further reduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निज्
निज् {c3c} U. (नेनेक्ति, नेनिक्ते,<BR>प्रणेनेक्ति, निक्त)<BR>1 To wash, cleanse,<BR>purify; सस्नुः पयः पपुरनेनिजुरंबराणि<BR>Śi. 5. 28.<BR>--2 To wash or clean oneself,<BR>to be purified (A.).<BR>--3 To nourish.<BR>WITH निस् to wash, clean, purify;<BR>R. 17. 22; Y. 1. 191; Ms. 5. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निक्त
निक्त p. p. Washed, cleansed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निज|निजं
निज a. [नितरां जायते निजण्-ड]<BR>1<BR>Innate, indigenous, native, inborn,<BR>congenial.<BR>--2 Own, one's own,<BR>relating to one-self, of one's own party<BR>or country; निजं वपुः पुनरनयन्निजां<BR>रुचिं Śi. 17. 4; R. 3. 15, 18. 27;<BR>Ms. 2. 50.<BR>--3 Peculiar.<BR>--4 Continual,<BR>perpetual. --m. pl. One's own people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निंज्|निञ्ज्
निंज् {c2c} A. (निंक्ते) To wash. --WITH<BR>प्र to wash (प्रणिंक्ते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निटलं|निटल
निटलं (Sometimes written<BR>निटिल) The forehead; निटिलतटचुंबित<BR>Dk. 4, 15.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निडीनं|निडीन
निडीनं The downward flight or<BR>swoop of birds; see डीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निण्य
निण्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Hidden,<BR>concealed.<BR>--2 Secret, mysterious.<BR>--ण्यं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-c" target="_blank">Page0620-c+ 55</a>]<BR>A secret or mystery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितंबः|नितम्ब|नितंब|नितम्बः
नितंबः [निभृतं तम्यते कामुकैः, तमु<BR>कांक्षायां]<BR>1 The buttocks, posteriors<BR>(of a woman), (the circumference<BR>of the hip and loins); यातं यच्च<BR>नितंवयोर्गुरुतया मंदं विलासादिव Ś. 2. 2;<BR>R. 4. 52, 6. 17; Me. 41; Bh. 1. 5;<BR>M. 2. 7.<BR>--2 The slope, ridge, side,<BR>flank of a mountain;<BR>सनाकवनितं नितंवरुचिरं (गिरिं) Ki. 5. 27;<BR>सेव्या नितंबाः किमु भूधराणामुत<BR>स्मरस्मेरविलासिनीनां Bh. 1. 19; V. 4. 26;<BR>Bk. 2. 8; 7. 58.<BR>--3 A precipice.<BR>--4<BR>The sloping bank of a river.<BR>--5 The<BR>shoulder.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बिंबं round or<BR>circular hips; Rs. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितंबवत्
नितंबवत् a. Having beautiful hips<BR>--ती A woman; चारु चुचुंब नितंबवती<BR>दयितं Gīt. 1; V. 4. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितंबिन्|नितम्बिन्
नितंबिन् a. [नितंब-अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>1<BR>Having beautiful hips, having<BR>wellsloped buttocks (often applied<BR>to जघन); cf. M. 2. 3; Ki. 8. 16<BR>R. 19. 26.<BR>--2 Having beautiful<BR>sides (as a mountain).<BR>--नी<BR>1 A<BR>woman with large and handsome<BR>hips; Ki. 8. 3; Śi. 7. 68;<BR>Ku. 3. 7.<BR>--2 A woman in general;<BR>Pt. 4. 32, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितरां
नितरां ind.<BR>1 Wholly, entirely,<BR>completely, प्राणांस्त्यजामि नितरां<BR>तदवाप्तिहेतोः Ch. P. 41; Bh. 1. 96.<BR>--2<BR>Exceedingly, excessively, very much;<BR>तुदंति चेतो नितरां प्रवासिनां Rs. 2. 4;<BR>Amaru. 10; Bh. 2. 18; शोषितसरसि<BR>निदाघे नितरामेवोद्धतः सिंधुः Pt. 1. 104;<BR>नितरां नीचोस्मीति Bv. 1. 9.<BR>--3<BR>Continually, always, eternally.<BR>--4 At<BR>all events.<BR>--5 Certainly.<BR>--6 Ved. In<BR>a low tone.<BR>--7 Downward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितलं|नितल
नितलं One of the seven divisions<BR>of the lower regions; see पाताल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नितांत|नितान्त|नितान्तं
नितांत a. Extraordinary,<BR>excessive, very much, intense;<BR>नितांतकठिनां रुजं मम न वेद यो मानसीं V. 2. 11;<BR>R. 3. 8.<BR>--तं ind. Excessively, very<BR>much, exceedingly, in a high degree;<BR>Pt. 2. 113.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्य|नित्यं|नित्यः
नित्य a. [नियमेन नियतं वा भवं<BR>नि-त्यप्; cf. P. IV. 2. 104 Vārt.]<BR>1<BR>(a) Continual, perpetual,<BR>constant, ever-lasting, eternal,<BR>uninterrupted; यदि नित्यमनित्येन लभ्यते<BR>H. 1. 48; नित्यज्योत्स्नाः प्रतिहतमोवृत्तिरम्याः<BR>प्रदोषाः Me. (regarded by Malli. as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-a" target="_blank">Page0621-a+ 56</a>]<BR>an interpolation); Ms. 2. 206. (b)<BR>Imperishable, indestructible; पृथिवी<BR>द्विविधा नित्याऽनित्या च Tarka K.<BR>--2 Invariable, regular, fixed, not<BR>optional, regularly prescribed (opp.<BR>काम्य).<BR>--3 Necessary, obligatory,<BR>essential.<BR>--4 Ordinary, usual (opp.<BR>नैमित्तिक).<BR>--5 (At the end of comp.)<BR>Constantly dwelling in, perpetually<BR>engaged in or busy with;<BR>जाह्नवीतीर˚, अरण्य˚, आदान˚, ध्यान˚ &c.<BR>--त्यः<BR>The ocean.<BR>--त्या An epithet of the<BR>goddess Durgā.<BR>--त्यं An<BR>indispensable or inevitable act.<BR>--त्यं ind.<BR>Daily, constantly, always, ever,<BR>perpetually, eternally.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनध्यायः invariable suspension of<BR>Vedic studies; Ms. 4. 107.<BR>--अनित्य a.<BR>eternal and perishable.<BR>--ऋतु a.<BR>regularly recurring at the seasons.<BR>--कर्मन् n.,<BR>--कृत्यं, --क्रिया any daily<BR>and necessary rite, a constant act or<BR>duty, as the five daily yajṇas.<BR>--गतिः air, wind.<BR>--दानं daily<BR>alms-giving.<BR>--नियमः an invariable rule.<BR>--नैमित्तिकं an occasional act<BR>regularly recurring, or any ceremony<BR>constantly performed to accomplish a<BR>particular object, (e. g. a पर्वश्राद्ध).<BR>--प्रलयः sleep.<BR>--मुक्तः the Supreme<BR>spirit.<BR>--यौवना (ever youthful) an<BR>epithet of Draupadī.<BR>--शंकित a.<BR>perpetually alarmed, ever suspicious.<BR>--समासः ‘a necessary compound’,<BR>a compound the meaning of which<BR>cannot be expressed by its<BR>constituent members used separately<BR>(the separate ideas having merged<BR>in one); e. g. जमदग्नि, जयद्रथ &c.;<BR>इवेन नित्यसमासः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0620-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यता
नित्यता, --त्वं<BR>1 Invariableness,<BR>constancy, continuance, eternity,<BR>perpetuity.<BR>--2 Necessity.<BR>--3<BR>Perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यत्वं|नित्यत्व
नित्यता, --त्वं<BR>1 Invariableness,<BR>constancy, continuance, eternity,<BR>perpetuity.<BR>--2 Necessity.<BR>--3<BR>Perseverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यदा
नित्यदा ind. Perpetually, always,<BR>constantly, eternally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नित्यशस्
नित्यशस् ind. Constantly, always,<BR>eternally; Bg. 8. 14; Ms. 2. 96;<BR>4. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्
निद् {c1c} U. (नेदति-ते)<BR>1 To be near.<BR>--2 To blame, censure, approach;<BR>cf. निंद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्
निद् f. Ved. Mocking, despising,<BR>censuring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद|निदं
निद a. Censuring.<BR>--दं Poison; (also<BR>निदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदद्रुः|निदद्रु
निदद्रुः<BR>1 A man.<BR>--2 One<BR>without herpes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शक
निदर्शक, --नं &c. See under निदृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शनं|निदर्शन
निदर्शक, --नं &c. See under निदृश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदाघः|निदाघ
निदाघः [नि-दह्-आधारे घञ् न्यंक्वादि<BR>कुत्वं]<BR>1 Heat, warmth.<BR>--2 The hot<BR>season, summer (the months of ज्येष्ठ<BR>and आषाढ); निदाघमिहिरज्वालाशतैः<BR>Bv. 1. 16; निदाघकालः समुपागतः प्रिये<BR>Rs. 1. 1; Pt. 1. 104; Ku. 7. 84.<BR>--3<BR>Sweat, perspiration.<BR>--4 The water<BR>of perspiration.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः the<BR>sun.<BR>--कालः summer.<BR>--सिंधुः a river<BR>in hot season, (nearly dry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदानं|निदान
निदानं<BR>1 A band, rope, halter.<BR>--2 A rope for tying up a calf.<BR>--3 A<BR>primary cause, the first or essential<BR>cause; निदिनमिक्ष्वाकुकुलस्य संततेः<BR>R. 3. 1; अथवा बलमारंभो निदानं क्षयसंपदः<BR>Śi. 2. 94.<BR>--4 A cause in general;<BR>मुंच मयि मानमनिदानं Gīt. 5.<BR>--5 (In<BR>medicine) Inquiry into the causes<BR>of a disease, pathology.<BR>--6<BR>Diagnosis of a disease.<BR>--7 End,<BR>termination.<BR>--8 Purity, purification,<BR>correctness.<BR>--9 Claiming the reward of<BR>penitential acts.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थानं one<BR>of the departments of medical<BR>science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिग्ध|निदिग्धं
निदिग्ध p. p. [नि-दिह्-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Smeared, anointed.<BR>--2 Increased,<BR>accumulated.<BR>--ग्धा Small<BR>cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासः|निदिध्यास
निदिध्यासः, निदिध्यासनं See<BR>under निध्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासनं|निदिध्यासन
निदिध्यासः, निदिध्यासनं See<BR>under निध्यै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिश्
निदिश् {c6c} P. To order, point out<BR>&c.; see निर्दिश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिष्ट
निदिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Pointed out.<BR>--2<BR>Ordered, directed.<BR>--3 Advised, enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेशः|निदेश
निदेशः<BR>1 Order, command,<BR>direction, instruction; वाक्येनेयं स्थापिता<BR>स्वे निदेशे M. 3. 14; स्थितं निदेशे<BR>पृथगादिदेश R. 14. 58; Ku. 3. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Speech, narration, conversation.<BR>--3<BR>Vicinity, neighbourhood.<BR>--4 A<BR>vessel, vase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदेशिन्
निदेशिन् a. Pointing &c.<BR>--नौ<BR>1<BR>A quarter, point of the compass.<BR>--2 A region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदृश्
निदृश् Caus.<BR>1 To show, point<BR>out; R. 6. 31.<BR>--2 To prove,<BR>establish, demonstrate.<BR>--3 To consider,<BR>treat of, discuss (as in a book).<BR>--4 To teach, explain.<BR>--5 To<BR>illustrate by an example; cf. निदर्शना.<BR>--6 To introduce, cause to enter.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">Page0621-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--7 To show oneself to (a person.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शक
निदर्शक a.<BR>1 Seeing.<BR>--2 Seeing<BR>into, perceiving.<BR>--3 Pointing out,<BR>proclaiming, indicating, showing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदर्शन|निदर्शनं
निदर्शन a.<BR>1 Pointing, showing.<BR>--2 Proclaiming, declaring<BR>announcing.<BR>--3 Teaching.<BR>--नं<BR>1 View,<BR>insight, looking into, sight, vision.<BR>--2 Pointing to, showing.<BR>--3 Proof,<BR>evidence; बलिना सह योद्धव्यमिति<BR>नास्ति निदर्शनं Pt. 3. 23.<BR>--4 An<BR>instance, example, illustration; ननु<BR>प्रभुरेव निदर्शनं Ś. 2; निदर्शनमसाराणां<BR>लघुर्बहुतृणं नरः Śi. 2. 50; R. 8. 45.<BR>--5 A scheme, system.<BR>--6 A precept,<BR>scriptural authority, an injunction.<BR>--7<BR>The third member of an Indian<BR>syllogism (usually called उदाहरण<BR>q. v.).<BR>--ना A figure of speech (in<BR>Rhetoric) thus defined:<BR>--निदर्शना ।<BR>अभवन्वस्तुसंबंध उपमापरिकल्पकः K. P. 10;<BR>e. g. R. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रा
निद्रा {c2c} P. To fall asleep, sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रा
निद्रा<BR>1 Sleep, sleepiness;<BR>प्रच्छायसुलभनिद्रा दिवसाः Ś. 1. 3; निद्रामुद्रा<BR>क्षिपन् Māl. 2. 12.<BR>--2 Sloth.<BR>--3 Shutting,<BR>budding state.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अलस a<BR>dull or languid with drowsiness,<BR>fast asleep; निद्रालसा बहिंणः V. 3. 2.<BR>--भंगः awaking.<BR>--वृक्षः darkness.<BR>--संजननं phlegm, phlegmatic<BR>humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्राण|निद्राणः
निद्राण a.<BR>1 Sleeping, asleep.<BR>--2 Shut, closed (as a bud).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रालु|निद्रालुः
निद्रालु a. Sleeping, asleep.<BR>--लुः<BR>An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निद्रित
निद्रित a. Asleep, slept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधन|निधनं|निधनः
निधन a. [निवृत्तं धनं यस्मात्;<BR>Uṇ. 2. 81.] Poor, indigent; अहो निधनता<BR>सर्वापदामास्पदं Mk. 1. 14.<BR>--नः --नं<BR>1<BR>Destruction, annihilation, death,<BR>loss; स्वधर्में निधनं श्रेयः Bg. 3. 35;<BR>म्लेच्छनिवहनिधने कलयसि करवालं<BR>Gīt. 1; कल्पांतेष्वपि न प्रयाति निधनं<BR>विद्याख्यमंतर्धनं Bh. 2. 16; Pt. 1. 21;<BR>5. 95.<BR>--2 The concluding passage<BR>at the end of a Sāman sung in<BR>chorus.<BR>--3 The finale (in music).<BR>--4 N. of the eighth lunar mansion.<BR>--5 Conclusion, end, termination.<BR>--6<BR>Ved. Residence; receptacle.<BR>--नः The<BR>head of a family.<BR>--नं Family, race.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारिन् a. fatal, destructive.<BR>--क्रिया a funeral ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधनता
निधनता Indigence, poverty;<BR>Mk. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0621-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधा
निधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To place, put, put<BR>or set down; शिरसि निदधानोंजलिपुटं<BR>Bh. 3. 123; R. 3. 50, 62; 12. 52;<BR>Śi. 1. 13.<BR>--2 To confide, or<BR>entrust, commit to the care of; निदधे<BR>विजयाशंसां चापे सीतां व लक्ष्मणे<BR>R. 12. 44; 15. 36.<BR>--3 To give, impart<BR>to, deposit with; दिनांते निहितं तेजः<BR>सवित्रेव हुताशनः R. 4. 1.<BR>--4 To put<BR>down, lay, allay, restrain;<BR>सलिलैनिंहितं रजः क्षितौ Ghaṭ. 1.<BR>--5 To<BR>bury, conceal or hide (as under<BR>ground), Ms. 5. 68.<BR>--6 To fix or<BR>direct the thoughts upon; cf. निध्यै.<BR>--7 To determine, resolve.<BR>--8 To<BR>direct one's labours, endeavour.<BR>--9 To appoint.<BR>--10 To remove,<BR>relinquish.<BR>--11 To lay up, treasure<BR>up.<BR>--12 To remember, keep or bear<BR>in mind.<BR>--13 To end, close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधा
निधा Ved.<BR>1 Laying snares.<BR>--2<BR>A net or snare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधानं|निधान
निधानं<BR>1 Putting down, laying<BR>down, depositing.<BR>--2 Keeping,<BR>preserving.<BR>--3 A place where anything<BR>is placed, a receptacle, reservoir;<BR>निधानं धर्माणां G. L. 18.<BR>--4<BR>Treasure; निधानगर्भामिव सागरांबरां<BR>R. 3. 9; Bg. 9. 18.; विद्यैव लोकस्य परं<BR>निधानं Subhāṣ.<BR>--5 Hoard, store,<BR>property, wealth.<BR>--6 A place of<BR>cessation or rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधिः|निधि
निधिः [नि-धा-आधारे कि]<BR>1 Abode,<BR>receptacle, reservoir; जल˚, तोय˚,<BR>तपोनिधि &c.<BR>--2 A store-house,<BR>treasury.<BR>--3 A treasure, store, hoard,<BR>(for the nine treasures of Kubera,<BR>see नवनिधि).<BR>--4 The ocean.<BR>--5 An<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--6 A man<BR>endowed with many good qualities.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः, --नाथः an epithet of<BR>Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निधुवनं|निधुवन
निधुवनं [नितरां धुवनं<BR>हस्तपादादिचालनमत्र]<BR>1 Agitation, trembling.<BR>--2<BR>Sexual enjoyment, coition;<BR>अतिशयमधुरिपुनिधुवनशीलं Gīt. 2, Śi. 11. 18;<BR>Ch. P. 4, 8, 25.<BR>--3 Pleasure,<BR>enjoyment, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यै
निध्यै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To think of,<BR>meditate upon, remember; Bk. 14. 65.<BR>--2 To meditate deeply upon, look<BR>steadfastly or intently at; अंगुलीयकं<BR>निध्यायंती M. 1; Śi. 8. 69; 12. 40;<BR>Ki. 10. 46, 14. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासः|निदिध्यास
निदिध्यासः, निदिध्यासनं Profound<BR>and repeated meditation, constant<BR>musing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निदिध्यासनं|निदिध्यासन
निदिध्यासः, निदिध्यासनं Profound<BR>and repeated meditation, constant<BR>musing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0622-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यात
निध्यात a. Meditated or thought<BR>on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0622-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निध्यानं|निध्यान
