निर्णेतृ
निर्णयः, निर्णीत, निर्णेतृ &c. See<BR>under निर्णी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णरः|निर्णर
निर्णरः N. of one of the horses<BR>of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णामः|निर्णाम|निर्ण्णाम
निर्णामः Ved.<BR>1 The joint of a<BR>wing(?).<BR>--2 Excesive bending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णिज्
निर्णिज् {c3c} U.<BR>1 To wash, clean,<BR>purify; R. 17. 22; Y. 1. 191;<BR>Ms. 5. 127.<BR>--2 To dress oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णिक्त|निर्णिक्तं
निर्णिक्त p. p.<BR>1 Washed, purified,<BR>cleansed; R. 17. 22.<BR>--2 Expiated,<BR>atoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णिक्तिः|निर्णिक्ति
निर्णिक्तिः f.<BR>1 Washing.<BR>--2<BR>Expiation, atonement; Mv. 4. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णिज्
निर्णिज् a. Ved.<BR>1 Clearing,<BR>washing.<BR>--2 Well-nourished. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>form, shape.<BR>--2 A bright or shining<BR>garment.<BR>--3 Purification, washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेकः|निर्णेक
निर्णेकः<BR>1 Washing, cleaning.<BR>--2<BR>Ablution.<BR>--3 Atonement, expiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेजकः|निर्णेजक
निर्णेजकः A washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेजनं|निर्णेजन
निर्णेजनं<BR>1 Ablution.<BR>--2<BR>Expiation, atonement (for an offence).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णी
निर्णी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To take or carry<BR>away or off.<BR>--2 To determine,<BR>ascertain, settle, decide, come to a<BR>decision, fix, resolve upon;<BR>कथमप्युपायमात्मनैव निर्णीय Dk.; Ki. 11. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णयः|निर्णय
निर्णयः<BR>1 Removing, removal.<BR>--2 Complete ascertainment,<BR>decision, affirmation, determination,<BR>settlement; संदेहनिर्णयो जातः Ś. 1. 28;<BR>Ms. 8. 301, 409; 9. 250, Y. 2. 10;<BR>हृदयं निर्णयमेव धावति Ki. 2. 29.<BR>--3<BR>Deduction, inference, conclusion,<BR>demonstration (in logic).<BR>--4<BR>Discussion, investigation, consideration.<BR>--5 Sentence, verdict, judgment;<BR>सर्वज्ञस्याप्येकाकिनो निर्णयाभ्युपगमो<BR>दोषाय M. 1.<BR>--6 Application of a<BR>conclusive argument.<BR>--7 (In Rhet.)<BR>Narration of events.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पादः<BR>a sentence, decree, verdict (in law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णयनं|निर्णयन
निर्णयनं<BR>1 Ascertainment,<BR>determination.<BR>--2 Positive conclusion,<BR>settlement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णायक
निर्णायक a.<BR>1 Settling, conclusive;<BR>--2 Determining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णायनं|निर्णायन|निर्ण्णायन
निर्णायनं<BR>1 Making certain.<BR>--2 The<BR>outer angle of the elephant's ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णीत|निर्णीतं
निर्णीत p. p. Settled, decided;<BR>determined, resolved. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णेतृ
निर्णेतृ a. Decisive, conclusive. --m.<BR>1 A judge.<BR>--2 A voucher.<BR>--3 A<BR>guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0632-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णुद्
निर्णुद् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To throw back,<BR>reject; धाना मत्स्यान्पयो मांसं शाकं चैव<BR>न निर्णुदेत् Ms. 4. 250.<BR>--2 To remove,<BR>dispel.<BR>--3 To drive away, expel.<BR>--4<BR>To repudiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्णोदः|निर्णोद
निर्णोदः Removal, banishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दट|निर्द्दटः
निर्दट --ड a.<BR>1 Unkind,<BR>unfeeling, unmerciful.<BR>--2 Rejoicing over<BR>the faults of others.<BR>--3 Envious.<BR>--4<BR>Abusive, slanderous.<BR>--5 Useless,<BR>unnecessary.<BR>--6 Violent.<BR>--7 Mad,<BR>intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दड
निर्दट --ड a.<BR>1 Unkind,<BR>unfeeling, unmerciful.<BR>--2 Rejoicing over<BR>the faults of others.<BR>--3 Envious.<BR>--4<BR>Abusive, slanderous.<BR>--5 Useless,<BR>unnecessary.<BR>--6 Violent.<BR>--7 Mad,<BR>intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दर|निर्दरः|निर्द्दर|निर्द्दरं
निर्दर a.<BR>1 Hard.<BR>--2 Pitiless.<BR>--3<BR>Shameless.<BR>--रः, --निर्दरिः<BR>1 A cave,<BR>cavern.<BR>--2 A waterfall, spring.<BR>--रं<BR>Essence (सार).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दलनं|निर्दलन
निर्दलनं Splitting, breaking,<BR>destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दह्
निर्दह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To burn, consume.<BR>--2 To torment, distress, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दग्ध|निर्द्दग्ध
निर्दग्ध a.<BR>1 Burnt.<BR>--2 Unburnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दहन|निर्द्दहनः
निर्दहन a.<BR>1 Burning, consuming.<BR>--2 Without fire or heat.<BR>--नं<BR>Burning, consuming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दातृ|निर्द्दातृ
निर्दातृ m.<BR>1 A digger up of<BR>weeds, weeder.<BR>--2 A donor.<BR>--3 A<BR>husbandman, reaper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दारित|निर्द्दारित
निर्दारित a.<BR>1 Torn, rent.<BR>--2<BR>Opened, split open; Śi. 18. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिग्ध|निर्द्दिग्धः
निर्दिग्ध p. p.<BR>1 Anointed,<BR>smeared.<BR>--2 Well-fed, corpulent, stout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिश्
निर्दिश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To point out,<BR>indicate, show; एकैकं निर्दिशन् Ś. 7;<BR>अंगुल्या निर्दिशति &c.<BR>--2 To assign,<BR>give; निर्दिष्टां कुलपतिना स<BR>पर्णशालामध्यास्य R. 1. 95.<BR>--3 To allude to,<BR>mention, make a reference to.<BR>--4<BR>To foretell, predict.<BR>--5 To advise,<BR>recommend.<BR>--6 To tell,<BR>communicate.<BR>--7 To enjoin, direct.<BR>--8 To<BR>enumerate, specify, name.<BR>--9 To<BR>define, determine.<BR>--10 To describe.<BR>--11<BR>To denounce, accuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्दिष्ट|निर्द्दिष्टः
निर्दिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Pointed out,<BR>shown, indicated.<BR>--2 Specified,<BR>particularized.<BR>--3 Described.<BR>--4<BR>Asigned, allotted.<BR>--5 Asserted,<BR>declared.<BR>--6 Ascertained, determined.<BR>--7 Ordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देशः|निर्देश|निर्द्देशः
निर्देशः<BR>1 Pointing out, showing,<BR>indicating.<BR>--2 Order, command,<BR>direction; R. 12. 17.<BR>--3 Advice,<BR>instruction.<BR>--4 Telling, saying,<BR>declaring.<BR>--5 Specifying,<BR>particularization, specification, specific mention;<BR>अयूक्तोयं निर्देशः Mbh.; Bg. 17. 23.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">Page0633-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--6 Ascertainment.<BR>--7 Vicinity,<BR>proximity.<BR>--8 Description, designation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देशक
निर्देशक a. Pointing out, showing<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्देष्टृ
निर्देष्टृ m. An authority, a guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धार|निर्धारः
निर्धार --रणं &c. see under निर्धृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारणं|निर्धारण
निर्धार --रणं &c. see under निर्धृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धाव्
निर्धाव् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To wash off or<BR>away, cleanse; निर्धोंते सति<BR>हरिचंदने जलौघैः Śi. 8. 51;<BR>निर्धौतदानामलगंडभित्तिः R. 5. 43, 70.<BR>--2 To stream<BR>forth, spring from.<BR>--3 To run out<BR>or escape from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धौत|निर्धौतं
निर्धौत p. p.<BR>1 Washed off,<BR>cleansed.<BR>--2 Polished, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धू
निर्धू {c5c} {c9c} U.<BR>1 To shake or<BR>throw off, remove, dispel, expel,<BR>destroy; निर्धूतोऽधरशोणिमा Gīt. 12;<BR>ज्ञाननिर्धूतकल्मषाः Bg. 5. 17;<BR>R. 12. 57.<BR>--2 To spurn, treat with<BR>contempt, disregard.<BR>--3 To abandon,<BR>forsake, throw away.<BR>--4 To<BR>repudiate, disown, reject.<BR>--5 To afflict,<BR>torment, distress.<BR>--6 To move about,<BR>brandish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धूत|निर्धूतं|निर्धूतः
निर्धूत p. p.<BR>1 Shaken off,<BR>removed; dispelled.<BR>--2 Deserted;<BR>rejected.<BR>--3 Deprived of, bereft.<BR>--4<BR>Avoided.<BR>--5 Refuted.<BR>--6 Destroyed.<BR>--7 Broken, divided.<BR>--8 Suffered,<BR>undergone.<BR>--9 Cast off or away,<BR>thrown away.<BR>--तः A man<BR>deserted by his relations and friends.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धृ
निर्धृ {c1c} P., {c10c} U.<BR>1 To<BR>determine accurately, settle, fix;<BR>निर्धारितेऽर्थे लेखेन खलूक्त्वा खलु वाचिकं<BR>Śi. 2. 70; 9. 20.<BR>--2 To specify,<BR>particularize.<BR>--3 To take out from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारः|निर्धार
निर्धारः, निर्धारणं<BR>1 Specifying or<BR>separating one out of many; यतश्च<BR>निर्धारणं P. II. 3. 41; V. 3. 92.<BR>--2<BR>Determining, settling, deciding.<BR>--3 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारणं|निर्धारण
निर्धारः, निर्धारणं<BR>1 Specifying or<BR>separating one out of many; यतश्च<BR>निर्धारणं P. II. 3. 41; V. 3. 92.<BR>--2<BR>Determining, settling, deciding.<BR>--3 Certainty, ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धारित|निर्धारितं
निर्धारित p. p. Determined,<BR>ascertained, fixed, settled, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्धार्य|निर्धार्य्य|निर्धार्य्यं
निर्धार्य a.<BR>1 Ascertainable.<BR>--2<BR>Resolute, energetic.<BR>--3 Bold,<BR>fearless, actively working.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बंध्|निर्बन्ध्
निर्बंध् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To press, urge,<BR>importune.<BR>--2 To insist upon,<BR>persist in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बद्ध
निर्बद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Fixed or fastened<BR>upon.<BR>--2 Urged, importuned, pressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बंधः|निर्बन्ध|निर्बंध|निर्बन्धः|निर्ब्बन्ध
निर्बंधः<BR>1 Insisting upon,<BR>persistence, intentness, pertinacity,<BR>निर्बंधसंजातरुषा (गुरुणा) R. 5. 21;<BR>Ku. 5. 66.<BR>--2 Importunity, a pressing<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">Page0633-c+ 56</a>]<BR>demand or request, urgency;<BR>निर्बंधपृष्टः स जगाद सर्वं R. 14. 32; अत एव<BR>खलु निर्बंधः Ś. 3.<BR>--3 Obstinacy.<BR>--4<BR>Accusation.<BR>--5 A contest, dispute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्बर्हण|निर्ब्बर्हण|निर्ब्बर्हणं
निर्बर्हण See निबर्हण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भग्न
निर्भग्न a.<BR>1 Shattered, broken in<BR>pieces.<BR>--2 Bent, bowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भट|निर्भटः
निर्भट a. Hard, firm (दृढ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्स्
निर्भर्त्स् {c10c} A.<BR>1 To revile,<BR>censure, abuse.<BR>--2 To surpass, eclipse,<BR>put to shame; Ku. 3. 53. 3 To<BR>menace; Śi. 6. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्सनं|निर्भर्त्सन
निर्भर्त्सनं --ना<BR>1 Threat, menace;<BR>Śi. 15. 87.<BR>--2 Abuse, reproach, reviling,<BR>blame.<BR>--3 Malignity.<BR>--4 Red paint,<BR>lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्सना
निर्भर्त्सनं --ना<BR>1 Threat, menace;<BR>Śi. 15. 87.<BR>--2 Abuse, reproach, reviling,<BR>blame.<BR>--3 Malignity.<BR>--4 Red paint,<BR>lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भर्त्सित|निर्भर्त्सितं
निर्भर्त्सित p. p.<BR>1 Threatened.<BR>--2<BR>Abused, reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भा
निर्भा {c2c} P.<BR>1 To shine forth, shine<BR>अक्षबीजवलयेन निर्बभौ R. 11. 66.<BR>--2<BR>To proceed, arise, start into view;<BR>वेदाद्धर्मो हि निर्बभौ Ms. 5. 44; 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भासः|निर्भास
निर्भासः Appearing or<BR>shining forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भिद्
निर्भिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To tear up, burst<BR>or tear asunder, break or pierce<BR>through; अनेन निर्भिन्नतनुः स वध्यः<BR>V. 5. 6; Bk. 9. 67; निर्भिद्योपरि<BR>कर्णिकारमुकलान्यालीयते षट्पदः V. 2. 23.<BR>--2 To<BR>disclose, betray, divulge; निर्भिन्नप्रायं<BR>रहस्यं Dk., वृत्तांतैकदेशं निर्बिभेद ibid.;<BR>Śi. 16. 23, U. 3. 1.<BR>--3 To break<BR>down, destroy.<BR>--4 To ascertain, find<BR>out, discover.<BR>--5 To excavate.<BR>--6<BR>To put out (the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भिन्न
निर्भिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Split asunder,<BR>broken open, rent.<BR>--2 Pierced<BR>through, transfixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भेदः|निर्भेद
निर्भेदः<BR>1 Bursting, dividing,<BR>splitting asunder.<BR>--2 A split, rent.<BR>--3 Disclosure, betrayal.<BR>--4<BR>Explicit mention or declaration;<BR>निर्भेदादृतेऽपि मालविकायामयमुपन्यासः<BR>शंकयति M. 4.<BR>--5 The bed of a river.<BR>--6 Determination of an affair, event.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भेद्य
निर्भेद्य a.<BR>1 Having no rent.<BR>--2 Not<BR>to be pierced through.<BR>--3<BR>Disappointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भुग्न
निर्भुग्न p. p.<BR>1 Distorted.<BR>--2<BR>straight.<BR>--3 Bent.<BR>--4 Pressing<BR>against each other; Māl. 6. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्भूति
निर्भूति f. Ved. Disappearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मंथ्|निर्मन्थ्
निर्मंथ् {c1c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To, churn, shake,<BR>stir round; अमृतस्यार्थे निर्मथिष्यामहे<BR>जलं Mb.<BR>--2 To produce or excite<BR>fire by rubbing.<BR>--3 To bruise, thresh<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">Page0634-a+ 56</a>]<BR>beat violently.<BR>--4 To destroy com<BR>pletely, crush down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0633-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मथः|निर्मथ
निर्मथः, निर्मथनं, निर्मंथः, निर्मंथनं<BR>1<BR>Rubbing, churning, stirring.<BR>--2 The<BR>wood used for producing fire by<BR>friction.<BR>--3 Rubbing two pieces of<BR>wood together to produce fire.<BR>--4 Destruction, havoc, U. 5. 8.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दारु {1} = 2 above; {2} a<BR>churning-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मथनं|निर्मथन
निर्मथः, निर्मथनं, निर्मंथः, निर्मंथनं<BR>1<BR>Rubbing, churning, stirring.<BR>--2 The<BR>wood used for producing fire by<BR>friction.<BR>--3 Rubbing two pieces of<BR>wood together to produce fire.<BR>--4 Destruction, havoc, U. 5. 8.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दारु {1} = 2 above; {2} a<BR>churning-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मंथः|निर्मन्थ|निर्मंथ|निर्मन्थः
निर्मथः, निर्मथनं, निर्मंथः, निर्मंथनं<BR>1<BR>Rubbing, churning, stirring.<BR>--2 The<BR>wood used for producing fire by<BR>friction.<BR>--3 Rubbing two pieces of<BR>wood together to produce fire.<BR>--4 Destruction, havoc, U. 5. 8.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दारु {1} = 2 above; {2} a<BR>churning-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मंथनं|निर्मन्थन|निर्मंथन|निर्म्मन्थन
निर्मथः, निर्मथनं, निर्मंथः, निर्मंथनं<BR>1<BR>Rubbing, churning, stirring.<BR>--2 The<BR>wood used for producing fire by<BR>friction.<BR>--3 Rubbing two pieces of<BR>wood together to produce fire.<BR>--4 Destruction, havoc, U. 5. 8.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दारु {1} = 2 above; {2} a<BR>churning-stick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मंथ्य|निर्मन्थ्य|निर्म्मन्थ्य
निर्मंथ्य a.<BR>1 To be stirred or<BR>churned.<BR>--2 To be produced by friction (as<BR>fire).<BR>--थ्यं The wood used for<BR>producing fire by friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मा|निर्म्मा
निर्मा {c3c} A., {c2c} P.<BR>1 To make,<BR>create, bring into existence; निर्मातुं<BR>प्रभवेन्मनोहरमिदं रूपं पुराणो मुनिः<BR>V. 1. 9; यस्मादेष सुरेंद्राणां मात्राभ्यो निर्मितो<BR>नृपः Ms. 7. 5; 1. 13.<BR>--2 (a) To build,<BR>form, construct; स्नायुनिर्मिता एते पाशाः<BR>H. 1 (b) To cause to be settled,<BR>colonize (as a town &c.); निर्ममे निर्ममोऽ<BR>र्थेषु मथुरां मधुराकृतिः R. 15. 28.<BR>--3 To<BR>cause, produce; शलाकांजननिर्मितेव<BR>Ku. 1. 47.<BR>--4 To compose, write;<BR>स्वनिर्मितया टीकया समेतं काव्यं.<BR>--5 To<BR>prepare, manufacture in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माणं|निर्माण|निर्म्माण|निर्म्माणं
निर्माणं<BR>1 Measuring, meting out;<BR>यतश्चाध्वकालनिर्मार्णं P. I. 4. 31 Vārt.<BR>--2 Measure, reach, extent;<BR>अयमप्राप्तनिर्माणः (बालः) Rām. ‘not having<BR>reached the full measure of growth’.<BR>--3 Producing, forming, making,<BR>creation, formation, manufacture; ईदृशो<BR>निर्माणभागः परिणतः U. 4.<BR>--4 A<BR>creation, created thing or object, form;<BR>निर्माणमेव हि तदादरलालनीयं Māl. 9. 49.<BR>--5 A shape, make, figure;<BR>शरीरनिर्माणसदृशो नन्वस्यानुभावः Mv. 1.<BR>--6<BR>Composition, work.<BR>--7 A building.<BR>--8 A<BR>part, portion.<BR>--9 Essence, pith,<BR>marrow.<BR>--10 (With Buddhists)<BR>Transformation.<BR>--णा Fitness, propriety,<BR>decorum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मित|निर्म्मित|निर्म्मितं
निर्मित p. p.<BR>1 Constructed, built,<BR>formed, prepared, made &c.<BR>--2 Artificial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मितिः|निर्मिति|निर्म्मिति|निर्म्मितिः
निर्मितिः f. Production, creation<BR>formation, any artistic<BR>production; नवरसरुचिरां निर्मितिमादधर्ता<BR>भारती कवेर्जयति K. P. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्माल्य|निर्म्माल्य|निर्म्माल्यं
निर्माल्य a. Pure, clean, stainless.<BR>--ल्यं<BR>1 Purity, clearness,<BR>stainlessness.<BR>--2 The remains of an offering to<BR>a deity, such as flowers;<BR>निर्माल्योज्झितपुष्पदामनिकरे का षट्पदानां रतिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">Page0634-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Ś. Til. 10.<BR>--3 Flowers used and cast off,<BR>faded or withered flowers; निर्माल्यरैथ<BR>ननृतेऽवधीरितानां Śi. 8. 60.<BR>--4 Remains<BR>in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मुच्
निर्मुच् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To free, liberate,<BR>release; हिमनिर्मुक्तयोर्योगे<BR>चित्राचंद्रमसोरिव R. 1. 46; Bg. 7. 28.<BR>--2 To<BR>leave, quit, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मुक्त|निर्मुक्तः|निर्म्मुक्त
निर्मुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Set free, freed,<BR>liberated; R. 1. 46.<BR>--2 Freed from<BR>worldly attachments.<BR>--3 Separated,<BR>disjoined.<BR>--क्तः A snake which has<BR>lately cast off its skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मुक्तिः|निर्मुक्ति
निर्मुक्तिः f. Freedom, liberation<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मोकः|निर्मोक|निर्म्मोक|निर्म्मोकः
निर्मोकः<BR>1 Setting free,<BR>liberating.<BR>--2 A hide, skin; especially, the<BR>slough of a serpent; R. 16. 17;<BR>Śi. 20. 47; N. 1.<BR>--3 Armour, mail.<BR>--4<BR>The sky, heaven.<BR>--5 Atmosphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मोक्षः|निर्मोक्ष|निर्म्मोक्षः
निर्मोक्षः Liberation, deliverance;<BR>R. 10. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मोचनं|निर्मोचन
निर्मोचनं Liberation, deliverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मूल्
निर्मूल् {c10c} U. To eradicate,<BR>extirpate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मूलनं|निर्मूलन
निर्मूलनं Eradication, uprooting,<BR>extirpating (fig. also); कर्मनिर्मूलनक्षमः<BR>Bh. 3. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मृज्
निर्मृज् {c2c} P. To wipe off, wash<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मार्जनं|निर्मार्जन
निर्मार्जनं Cleaning, washing off;<BR>wiping out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्मृष्ट
निर्मृष्ट p. p. Wiped off, washed out,<BR>rubbed out; निर्मृष्टरागोऽधरः S. D. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यत्
निर्यत् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To return, restore;<BR>निर्यातय हस्तन्यासं V. 5; Ms. 11. 164.<BR>--2 To requite, repay, retaliate;<BR>रामलक्ष्मणयोर्वैरं स्वयं निर्यातयामि वै Rām.<BR>--3<BR>To forgive, pardon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यातनं|निर्यातन|निर्य्यातन
निर्यातनं<BR>1 Returning, restoring,<BR>delivering, restitution (as of a<BR>deposit).<BR>--2 Payment of a debt.<BR>--3<BR>Gift, donation.<BR>--4 Retaliation,<BR>requital, revenge (as in वैरनिर्यातन).<BR>--5 Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्या
निर्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go out, go out,<BR>of; R. 12. 83.<BR>--2 To pass, elapse<BR>(as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्याणं|निर्याण|निर्य्याण
निर्याणं<BR>1 Exit, issue, setting out,<BR>departure.<BR>--2 Vanishing,<BR>disappearing.<BR>--3 Dying, death.<BR>--4 Eternal<BR>emancipation, final beatitude.<BR>--5<BR>The outer corner of the eye of an<BR>elephant; वारणं निर्याणभागेऽभिघ्नन्<BR>Dk. 97; निर्याणनिर्यदसृजं चलितं निषादी<BR>Śi. 5. 41.<BR>--6 A rope for tying cattle or<BR>the feet of a calf, a foot-rope in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">Page0634-c+ 56</a>]<BR>general; निर्याणहस्तस्य पुरो दुधुक्षतः<BR>Śi. 12. 41.<BR>--7 Iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यातिः|निर्याति
निर्यातिः f.<BR>1 Exit, departure.<BR>--2<BR>Departure from life, dying, death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यापणं|निर्यापण
निर्यापणं Banishing, expelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यामः|निर्याम|निर्य्याम
निर्यामः A sailor, pilot, boatman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यासः|निर्यास|निर्यासं|निर्य्यास
निर्यासः, --सं<BR>1 Exudation of<BR>trees or plants, gum, juice, resin;<BR>शालनिर्यासगंधिभिः R. 1. 38; Ms. 5. 6.<BR>--2 Extract, infusion, decoction.<BR>--3<BR>Any thick fluid substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यासं|निर्यास|निर्यासः|निर्य्यास
निर्यासः, --सं<BR>1 Exudation of<BR>trees or plants, gum, juice, resin;<BR>शालनिर्यासगंधिभिः R. 1. 38; Ms. 5. 6.<BR>--2 Extract, infusion, decoction.<BR>--3<BR>Any thick fluid substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्यूहः|निर्यूह|निर्य्यूह
निर्यूहः<BR>1 A pinnacle, turret,<BR>projection (on columns or gates); वित<BR>र्दिनिर्यूहविटंकनीडः Śi. 3. 55 (where<BR>Malli. renders निंर्यूह by<BR>मत्तवारणाख्यउपाश्रयः and quotes Vaijayantī;<BR>perhaps it was so called from its<BR>resemblance to the shape of an<BR>elephant in rut); चारुतोरणनिर्यूहा Rām.<BR>--2 A chaplet, crest, head-ornament.<BR>--3 A peg projecting from a wall.<BR>--4 Wood placed in a wall for<BR>pigeons to build their nests or to<BR>perch upon.<BR>--5 A door, gate.<BR>--6<BR>Extract, decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लुंचनं|निर्लुञ्चन|निर्लुंचन
निर्लुंचनं Pulling out or off,<BR>tearing off, peeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लुंठनं|निर्लुण्ठन|निर्लुंठन
निर्लुंठनं<BR>1 Robbing, plundering.<BR>--2 Tearing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्लेखनं|निर्लेखन
निर्लेखनं<BR>1 Scraping, scratching.<BR>--2 An instrument for scraping, a<BR>scraper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ल्वयनी
निर्ल्वयनी The slough of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वच्
निर्वच् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To interpret,<BR>explain; वेदा निर्वक्तुमक्षमाः.<BR>--2 To derive,<BR>trace to its etymology (as a word).<BR>--3 To relate, tell, declare, announce.<BR>--4 To name, call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वचनं|निर्वचन|निर्व्वचन
निर्वचनं<BR>1 Utterance,<BR>pronunciation.<BR>--2 A proverbial expression,<BR>proverb.<BR>--3 Etymological<BR>interpretation, etymology.<BR>--4 A vocabulary,<BR>an index.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वप्
निर्वप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To pour out,<BR>sprinkle.<BR>--2 To scatter, strew, (as<BR>seed).<BR>--3 To offer, present;<BR>श्रोत्रियायाभ्यागताय वत्सतरीं वा महोक्षं वा<BR>निर्वपांति गृहमेधिनः U. 4.<BR>--4 To offer<BR>libations especially to the Manes.<BR>--5 To perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वपण|निर्व्वपण|निर्व्वपणं
निर्वपण a. (णी)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>oblations.<BR>--2 Pouring out, scattering.<BR>--3 Giving, bestowing.<BR>--णं<BR>1<BR>Pouring out, offering.<BR>--2 Particularly,<BR>the presentation of funeral<BR>offerings to the Manes, a libation;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">Page0635-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Ms. 3. 248, 260.<BR>--3 Bestowing presents.<BR>--4 Gift, donation.<BR>--5 A vessel<BR>(ladle &c.) for pouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0634-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वयनी|निर्व्वयनी
निर्वयनी The slough of a snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्ण्
निर्वर्ण् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To look at<BR>carefully, mark attentively.<BR>--2 To see,<BR>behold, observe, perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्णनं|निर्वर्णन|निर्व्वर्णनं
निर्वर्णनं<BR>1 Looking at, seeing,<BR>sight.<BR>--2 Marking, observing<BR>carefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वस्
निर्वस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To live out, i. e.<BR>to go to the end of (as a period).<BR>--2 To dwell abroad. --Caus. To<BR>banish, drive away, expel;<BR>R. 14. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वासः|निर्वास
निर्वासः, निर्वासनं<BR>1 Expulsion,<BR>banishment.<BR>--2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>--3 Leaving one's home, living<BR>abroad (निर्वास only in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वासनं|निर्वासन|निर्व्वासन|निर्व्वासनं
निर्वासः, निर्वासनं<BR>1 Expulsion,<BR>banishment.<BR>--2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>--3 Leaving one's home, living<BR>abroad (निर्वास only in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वह्
निर्वह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To carry out,<BR>extricate oneself.<BR>--2 To be finished.<BR>--3 To live upon, live by the aid of.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To take to the end of,<BR>complete, finish, manage; यथा<BR>प्रियसखी बंधुजनशोचनीया न भवति तथा<BR>निर्वाहय Ś. 3.<BR>--2 To carry out,<BR>accomplish, effect.<BR>--3 To pass, spend<BR>(as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वहणं|निर्वहण|निर्व्वहण|निर्व्वहणं
निर्वहणं<BR>1 End, completion;<BR>Śi. 14. 63.<BR>--2 Maintainig, carrying to the<BR>end, sustaining; मानस्य निर्वहणं<BR>Amaru. 24.<BR>--3 Destruction, annihilation.<BR>--4 (In dramas). The catastrophe,<BR>the last stage in which the<BR>action of the play is brought<BR>to a head, the denouement;<BR>तत्किंनिमित्तं कुकविकृतनाटकस्येव<BR>अन्यन्मुखेऽन्यन्निर्वहणे Mu. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहः|निर्वाह|निर्व्वाह|निर्व्वाहः
निर्वाहः<BR>1 Carrying on,<BR>accomplishng, performing.<BR>--2 Completion, end.<BR>--3 Carrying to the end, supporting,<BR>steadfast adherence, perseverance;<BR>निर्वाहः प्रतिपन्नवस्तुषु सतामेतद्धि गोत्रव्रतं<BR>Mu. 2. 18.<BR>--4 Subsisting on.<BR>--5<BR>Sufficiency, competent provision,<BR>competency.<BR>--6 Describing,<BR>narrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहण|निर्व्वाहण|निर्व्वाहणं
निर्वाहण a.<BR>1 Carrying out,<BR>effecting.<BR>--2 Removing.<BR>--णं<BR>Accomplishment, completion; See निर्वहण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाहिन्
निर्वाहिन् a.<BR>1 Effecting.<BR>--2<BR>Discharging (as a wound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वा|निर्व्वा
निर्वा {c2c} P.<BR>1 To blow.<BR>--2 To be<BR>cooled, be cool or assuaged (fig.<BR>also); वपुर्जलार्द्रापवनैर्न निर्ववौ<BR>Śi. 1. 65; त्वयि दृष्ट एव तस्या निर्वाति मनो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-b" target="_blank">Page0635-b+ 56</a>]<BR>मनोभवज्वलितं Subhāṣ.<BR>--3 To blow<BR>out, be extinguished, be extinct;<BR>निर्वाणदीपे किमु तैलदातं Subhāṣ.;<BR>निर्वाणभूयिष्ठमथास्य वीर्यं संधुक्षयंतीव<BR>वपुर्गुणेन Ku. 3. 52; Śi. 14. 85;<BR>Mu. 3. 28. --Caus. (वापयति)<BR>1 To blow or<BR>put out, extinguish destroy,<BR>kill; R. 3. 58.<BR>--2 To cool, alleviate<BR>the heat of, act as a refrigerant;<BR>सखि अन्यादृश एव तेद्य निर्वापयति<BR>शरीरस्पर्शः Māl. 6, Ratn. 3. 11; R. 19. 56.<BR>--3<BR>To gratify, soothe, comfort;<BR>R. 12. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वाण|निर्व्वाण|निर्व्वाणं|निर्व्वाणः
निर्वाण p. p.<BR>1 Blown or put out,<BR>extinguished (as a lamp or fire);<BR>निर्वाणवैरदहनाः प्रशमादरीणां Ve. 1. 7;<BR>Ku. 2. 23.<BR>--2 Lost, disappeared.<BR>--3<BR>Dead, deceased.<BR>--4 Liberated from<BR>existence.<BR>--5 Set (as the sun).<BR>--6<BR>Calmed, quieted.<BR>--7 Plunged.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Extinction; H. 1. 131;<BR>शनैर्निर्वाणमाप्नोति निरिंधन इवानलः Mb.<BR>--2<BR>Vanishing from sight, disappearance.<BR>--3 Dissolution, death.<BR>--4 Final<BR>liberation or emancipation from<BR>matter and reunion with the<BR>Supreme Spirit, eternal bliss,<BR>निर्वाणमपि मन्येऽहमंतरायं जयश्रियः<BR>Ki. 11. 69; R. 12. 1.<BR>--5 (With<BR>Buddhists) Absolute extinction or<BR>annihilation, complete extinction of<BR>individual or worldly existence.<BR>--6<BR>Perfect and perpetual calm, repose;<BR>Ki. 18. 39.<BR>--7 Complete<BR>satisfaction or pleasure, supreme bliss,<BR>highest felicity; अये लब्धं नेत्रनिर्वाणं<BR>Ś. 3; M. 3. 1; Śi. 4. 23;<BR>V. 3. 21.<BR>--8 Cessation, desisting.<BR>--9<BR>Vacuity.<BR>--10 Union, association,<BR>confluence.<BR>--11 The bathing of an<BR>elephant; as in अनिर्वाण at R. 1. 71.<BR>--12<BR>Instruction in sciences.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुराणं offering oblations to the dead (?)<BR>--भूयिष्ठ a. almost vanished or<BR>departed; see under निर्वा (3)<BR>above.<BR>--मस्तकः final emancipation<BR>or deliverance, final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापः|निर्वाप|निर्व्वाप|निर्व्वापः
निर्वापः<BR>1 See निर्वपण.<BR>--2 Putting<BR>out, extinguishing (as fire).<BR>--3<BR>Alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापणं|निर्वापण|निर्व्वापणं
निर्वापणं<BR>1 An offering, oblation,<BR>a funeral oblation.<BR>--2 A gift<BR>donation.<BR>--3 Putting out,<BR>extinguishing.<BR>--4 Pouring out,<BR>scattering, sowing (as seed).<BR>--5 (a)<BR>Offering, giving. (b) Offering<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-c" target="_blank">Page0635-c+ 57</a>]<BR>oblations (especially funeral).<BR>--6<BR>Allaying, alleviation, pacification;<BR>कर्तव्यानि दुःखितैर्दुःखनिर्वापणानि U. 3.<BR>--7 Annihilation.<BR>--8 Killing,<BR>slaughter.<BR>--9 Cooling, refreshing;<BR>शरीरनिर्वापणाय Ś. 3.<BR>--10 A refrigerant or<BR>cooling application.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वापयितृ
निर्वापयितृ a.<BR>1 Extinguishing,<BR>blowing, blowing out.<BR>--2 Allaying<BR>the heat of, cooling; स्मर एव<BR>तापहेतुर्निर्वापयिता स एव मे जातः Ś. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वादः|निर्वाद|निर्व्वाद|निर्व्वादः
निर्वादः<BR>1 Blame, reproach.<BR>--2<BR>Seandal, bad rumour, obloquy;<BR>R. 14. 34.<BR>--3 Decision of a controversy.<BR>--4 Absence of dispute (वादाभाव).<BR>--5<BR>Rumour, report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विद्|निर्व्विद्
निर्विद् {c4c} A. To be dissatisfied or<BR>disgusted with (with instr.);<BR>Pt. 1. 240.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्ण|निर्व्विण्णः
निर्विण्ण p. p.<BR>1 Despondent,<BR>depressed; Mk. 1. 14.<BR>--2 Overcome<BR>with fear or sorrow.<BR>--3 Emaciated<BR>with grief.<BR>--4 A bused, degraded.<BR>--5<BR>Disgusted with anything;<BR>मत्स्याशनस्य निर्विण्णः Pt. 1.<BR>--6 Impaired,<BR>decayed.<BR>--7 Humble, modest.<BR>--8<BR>Known, certain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेदः|निर्वेद|निर्व्वेदः
निर्वेदः<BR>1 Disgust, loathing.<BR>--2<BR>Satiety, cloy.<BR>--3 Depression of<BR>spirits, despair, despondency;<BR>परिभवान्निर्वेदमापद्यते Mk. 1. 14.<BR>--4<BR>Humiliation.<BR>--5 Grief.<BR>--6 Complete<BR>indifference to worldly objects;<BR>Bg. 2. 52 regarded as the feeling<BR>which gives rise to the sentiment<BR>called शांत (quietude);<BR>निर्वेदस्थायिभावोस्ति शांतोऽपि नवमो रसः<BR>K. P. 4; (see R. G. under निर्वेद).<BR>--7<BR>Selfdisparagement or humiliation<BR>(regarded as one of the 33<BR>subordinate feelings); cf. the definition in<BR>R. G. under निर्वेद; (the following<BR>is there given as an instance; यदि<BR>लक्ष्पण सा मृगेक्षणा न मदीक्षासरणिं समेष्यति ।<BR>अमुना जडजीवितेन मे जगता वा विफलेन किं<BR>फलं ॥).<BR>--8 Shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विश्
निर्विश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To enjoy;<BR>ज्योत्स्नावतो निर्विशति प्रदोषान् R. 6. 34;<BR>निर्विष्ठविषयस्नैहः स दशांतमुपेयिवान्<BR>R. 12. 1; 4. 51; 6. 50; 9. 36; 13. 60;<BR>14. 80; 18. 3; 19. 47; Me. 110;<BR>Ku. 1. 29.<BR>--2 To adorn, embellish.<BR>--3 To marry; निर्वेष्टुकामोस्मि नरेंद्र<BR>V. P.<BR>--4 To feel, experience.<BR>--5 To<BR>reward, recompense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्ट|निर्व्विष्टः
निर्विष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Enjoyed, attained,<BR>experienced.<BR>--2 Fully enjoyed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">Page0636-a+ 56</a>]<BR>or used.<BR>--3 Obtained as wages;<BR>निर्विष्टं वैश्यशूद्रयोः Gautama.<BR>--4<BR>Married.<BR>--5 Engaged in.<BR>--6 Arrived<BR>at, attained to.<BR>--7 One who has<BR>maintained the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0635-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेशः|निर्वेश|निर्व्वेशः
निर्वेशः<BR>1 Gaining, obtaining.<BR>--2<BR>Wages, hire, employment.<BR>--3<BR>Eating, enjoyment, use.<BR>--4 Return of<BR>payment.<BR>--5 Expiation, atonement.<BR>--6 Marriage.<BR>--7 Fainting,<BR>swooning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृ
निर्वृ {c5c} U. (usually in p. p. only)<BR>To feel happy, be pleased or<BR>satisfied; निर्ववार मधुनींद्रियवर्गः Śi. 10. 3.<BR>See निर्वृत below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत
निर्वृत p. p.<BR>1 Satisfied, contented,<BR>happy; निर्वृतौ स्वः Ś. 2; Ś. 4;<BR>5. 1.<BR>--2 Free from care or<BR>anxiety, secure, at ease.<BR>--3 Ceased,<BR>ended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृतिः|निर्वृति
निर्वृतिः f.<BR>1 Satisfaction,<BR>happiness, pleasure, bliss; व्रजति<BR>निर्वृतिमेकपदे मनः V. 2. 9; R. 9. 38;<BR>12. 65; Ś. 7. 19; Śi. 4. 64,<BR>10. 28; Ki. 3. 8.<BR>--2 Tranquillity, rest,<BR>repose; Ku. 5. 55; Pt. 1. 208.<BR>--3 Final emancipation or liberation<BR>from worldly existence; द्वारं<BR>निर्वृतसद्मनो विजयते कृष्णेति वर्णद्वयं<BR>Bv. 4. 14.<BR>--4 Completion,<BR>accomplishment.<BR>--5 Freedom.<BR>--6<BR>Disappearance; death, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्
निर्वृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To cease, come to<BR>an end; Bk. 8. 69.<BR>--2 To be got<BR>or accomplished; R. 17. 18;<BR>Ms. 7. 61.<BR>--3 To be withheld, not to<BR>happen; Bk. 16. 6. --Caus. To<BR>perform; accomplish, finish,<BR>complete; आहारं निर्वर्तयामास K. 16;<BR>R. 2. 45; 3. 33; 11. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तक
निर्वर्तक^1 a. (र्तिका f.)<BR>1<BR>Completing, accomplishing, finishing,<BR>executing, performing &c.<BR>--2<BR>Desisting.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: first 'r' diacritic is badly printed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तनं|निर्वर्तन|निर्वर्त्तन|निर्व्वर्त्तन
निर्वर्तनं<BR>1 Accomplishment,<BR>completion, execution.<BR>--2 Desisting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वर्तिन्
निर्वर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Completing,<BR>accomplishing &c.<BR>--2 Acting rudely,<BR>uncivil, impolitic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्त|निर्वृत्तः
निर्वृत्त p. p. Accomplished,<BR>attained, performed &c.; Ku. 7. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वृत्ति|निर्वृत्तिः
निर्वृत्ति f.<BR>1 Accomplishment,<BR>fulfilment; Ms. 12. 1.<BR>--2 Completion,<BR>end.<BR>--3 (In gram.) Discontinuance<BR>of the influence of one rule over<BR>another (opp. अनुवृत्ति).<BR>--4 Result<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">Page0636-b+ 55</a>]<BR>fruit.<BR>--5 Ceasing, desisting, abstaining<BR>from.<BR>--6 Inactivity.<BR>--7 Impropriety.<BR>--8 Final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्वेष्टनं|निर्वेष्टन|निर्व्वेष्टनं
निर्वेष्टनं A weaver's shuttle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यथनं|निर्व्यथन
निर्व्यथनं<BR>1 Extreme pain,<BR>paining, afflicting.<BR>--2 Freedom from<BR>pain.<BR>--3 A hole, chasm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढ|निर्व्यूढं
निर्व्यूढ p. p.<BR>1 Completed,<BR>finished; Mu. 2. 18.<BR>--2 Grown,<BR>increased, developed; मुहूर्तनिर्व्यूढविस्मय<BR>Māl. 7; निर्व्यूढसौहृदभरेति 6. 17<BR>(उपचित Jagaddhara).<BR>--3<BR>Vindicated, fully shown, proved true,<BR>carried out faithfully or to the end;<BR>हा तात जटायो निर्व्यूढस्तेऽपत्यस्नेहः<BR>U. 3; निर्व्यूढः संभावनाभारो<BR>बुद्धरक्षितया Māl. 8; निर्व्यूढ तातस्य कापालिकत्वं<BR>Māl. 4, 9. 10; Mv. 7. 8.<BR>--4<BR>Deserted, abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्व्यूढिः|निर्व्यूढि
निर्व्यूढिः f.<BR>1 End, completion.<BR>--2<BR>A helmet, crest.<BR>--3 A door, gate.<BR>--4 A peg or bracket projecting from<BR>a wall.<BR>--5 Decoction; cf. निर्यूह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हादः|निर्हाद
निर्हादः Evacuation, voiding<BR>excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृ
निर्हृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To take or draw out<BR>from, extract; R. 14. 42.<BR>--2 To<BR>carry out the dead body; Ms. 5. 91;<BR>Y. 3. 15.<BR>--3 To remove (as a fault<BR>&c.)<BR>--4 To carry or take away.<BR>--5 To<BR>export (goods).<BR>--6 To change or<BR>mix together (clothes &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हरणं|निर्हरण
निर्हरणं<BR>1 Carrying out dead bodies<BR>to be burnt, carrying corpses to the<BR>funeral pile.<BR>--2 Taking forth,<BR>carrying or drawing out, extracting,<BR>removal.<BR>--3 Rooting up, extirpation,<BR>destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारः|निर्हार
निर्हारः<BR>1 Taking away, removing,<BR>removal.<BR>--2 Drawing out,<BR>extracting.<BR>--3 Rooting up, destruction.<BR>--4 Carrying out a dead body to be<BR>burnt.<BR>--5 Accumulation of a private<BR>store of wealth, private hoard;<BR>Ms. 9. 199.<BR>--6 Evacuation of the<BR>natural excrements of the body (opp.<BR>आहार).<BR>--7 Putting forth or out.<BR>--8<BR>Setting aside, excluding, leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हारिन्
निर्हारिन् a.<BR>1 Carrying out.<BR>--2<BR>Diffusive, spreading wide (as<BR>fragrance).<BR>--3 Fragrant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्हृतिः|निर्हृति
निर्हृतिः f. Taking out of one's<BR>way, removal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निर्ह्रादः|निर्ह्राद
निर्ह्रादः A sound in general;<BR>R. 1. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिंपः|निलिम्प|निलिंप|निलिम्पः
निलिंपः<BR>1 A god; निलिंपैर्निमुक्तानपि<BR>च निरयांतर्निपतितान् G. L. 15.<BR>--2 A<BR>troop of Maruts.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--निर्झरी<BR>the celestial Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिंपा
निलिंपा, निलिंपिका A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलिंपिका|निलिम्पिका
निलिंपा, निलिंपिका A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निली
निली {c4c} A.<BR>1 To stick or adhere<BR>to, lie or rest upon, settle<BR>down or alight upon; निलिल्ये मूर्ध्न<BR>गृध्रोऽस्य Bk. 14. 76; 2. 5.<BR>--2 To<BR>lurk or hide, hide oneself in;<BR>गुहास्वन्ये न्यलेषत Bk. 15. 32; निशि<BR>रहसि निलीय Gīt. 2.<BR>--3 To hide or<BR>conceal oneself from (with abl.);<BR>मातुर्निलीयते कृष्णः Sk.<BR>--4 To die,<BR>perish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलयः|निलय
निलयः<BR>1 A hiding place, the lair<BR>or den of animals, a nest (of birds);<BR>Śi. 9. 4.<BR>--2 An abode, residence,<BR>house, dwelling; oft. at the end of<BR>comp. in the sense of ‘living or<BR>residing in’.<BR>--3 Hiding oneself.<BR>--4<BR>Total destruction.<BR>--5 Setting,<BR>disappearance; दिनांते निलयाय गंतुं<BR>R. 2. 15 (where the word is used in<BR>sense 1 also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलयनं|निलयन
निलयनं<BR>1 Settling in a place,<BR>alighting.<BR>--2 A place of refuge<BR>house, dwelling, habitation.<BR>--3 The<BR>act of going out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निलीन|निलीनं
निलीन p. p.<BR>1 Melted or fused<BR>into.<BR>--2 Shut or wrapt up, hidden<BR>into.<BR>--3 Involved, surrounded,<BR>encompassed.<BR>--4 Destroyed, perished.<BR>--5 Changed, transformed.<BR>--6 Full.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवचने
निवचने ind. Not speaking,<BR>ceasing to speak, holding the tongue<BR>(regarded as a गति or preposition, or<BR>a separate word, when used with कृ;<BR>e. g. निवचनेकृत्य, निवचने कृत्वा;<BR>P. I. 4. 76).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवत्
निवत् f. A valley.<BR>--ता ind.<BR>Downwards; (also निवना in this<BR>sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवप्
निवप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To scatter about,<BR>sow (as seed).<BR>--2 To offer (as<BR>oblations), especially to the Manes;<BR>न्युप्य पिंडांस्ततः Ms. 3. 216; (<BR>स्मरमुद्दिश्य) निवपेः सहकारमंजरीः Ku. 4. 38.<BR>--3 To immolate, kill (as an animal).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवपनं|निवपन
निवपनं<BR>1 Scattering down, pouring<BR>out, throwing down.<BR>--2 Sowing.<BR>--3<BR>An offering to the Manes, an<BR>oblation in honour of one's deceased<BR>ancestors; को नः कुले निवपनानि<BR>नियच्छतीति Ś. 6. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0636-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापः|निवाप
निवापः<BR>1 Seed, grain, seed-corn.<BR>--2 An offering to the Manes of<BR>deceased parents or other relatives, a<BR>libation of water &c. at the Śrāddha<BR>ceremony; एको निवापसलिलं<BR>पिबसीत्ययुक्तं Māl. 9. 40; निवापदत्तिभिः<BR>R. 8. 86; निवापांजलयः पितॄणां 5. 8,<BR>15. 91, Mu. 4. 5.<BR>--3 A gift or offering<BR>in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवापकः|निवापक
निवापकः A sower, scatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर|निवरः
निवर a. Preventing, warding off.<BR>--रः<BR>1 One who prevents.<BR>--2<BR>Protection, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवरा
निवरा A virgin, an unmarried<BR>girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवस्
निवस् {vI.v} {c1c} P.<BR>1 To live, dwell,<BR>stay; आहो निवत्स्यति समं हरिणांगनाभिः<BR>Ś. 1. 26; निवसिष्यसि मय्येव<BR>Bg. 12. 8.<BR>--2 To be, exist; Pt. 1. 31.<BR>--3<BR>To occupy, settle in, take possession<BR>of.<BR>--4 To sojourn, pass the night.<BR>{vII.v} {c2c} A.<BR>1 To dress, wear or<BR>put on clothes.<BR>--2 To change one's<BR>clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसतिः|निवसति
निवसतिः f. A house, habitation,<BR>abode, residence, dwelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसथः|निवसथ
निवसथः A village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवसनं|निवसन
निवसनं<BR>1 A house, habitation,<BR>dwelling.<BR>--2 A garment, cloth, an<BR>undergarment; Śi. 10. 60;<BR>R. 19. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासः|निवास
निवासः<BR>1 Living, dwelling,<BR>residing.<BR>--2 A house; abode, habitation,<BR>resting-place; निवासश्चिंतायाः<BR>Mk. 1. 15; Śi. 4. 63, 5. 21; Bg. 9. 18;<BR>Mk. 3. 23.<BR>--3 Passing the night.<BR>--4 A dress, garment.<BR>--5<BR>Nightquarters.<BR>--6 Refuge, receptacle,<BR>asylum; जगन्निवासो वसुदेवसद्मनि Śi. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासनं|निवासन
निवासनं<BR>1 Residence.<BR>--2 Sojourn.<BR>--3 Spending time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवासिन्
निवासिन् a.<BR>1 Dwelling, residing.<BR>--2 Wearing, dressed or clothed in;<BR>Ku. 7. 26. --m. A resident, an<BR>inhabitant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवह्
निवह् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To bring or lead<BR>near.<BR>--2 To bear up, sustain,<BR>support; वेदानुद्धरते जगन्निवहते Gīt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवहः|निवह
निवहः<BR>1 A multitude, collection,<BR>quantity, heap; राजपुत्रनिवहः<BR>Bh. 3. 37; so घन˚, दैत्य˚, कपोत˚ &c.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of one of the seven winds.<BR>--3 N. of<BR>one of the seven tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवात|निवातः
निवात a. [निवृत्तोनिरुद्धो वा वातोऽस्मात्]<BR>1 Sheltered from the wind, not<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">Page0637-b+ 56</a>]<BR>windy, calm; R. 3. 17; 19. 42.<BR>--2<BR>Unhurt, uninjured, unobstructed.<BR>--3<BR>Safe, secure.<BR>--4 Well-armed,<BR>accoutred in strong mail.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A<BR>refuge, dwelling, an asylum.<BR>--2 An<BR>impenetrable coat of mail.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A<BR>place sheltered from the wind;<BR>निवातनिष्कंपमिव प्रदीपं Ku. 3. 48;<BR>Ki. 14. 37; R. 13. 52, 3. 17; Bg. 6. 19.<BR>--2 Absence of wind, calm, stillness;<BR>R. 12. 36.<BR>--3 A secure spot.<BR>--4 A<BR>strong armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवाकु
निवाकु a. Not speaking, silent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवान्या
निवान्या A cow whose calf is<BR>dead and who is milked by means<BR>of another calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविड|निविडं
निवि(बि)ड a.<BR>1 Without<BR>space or interstices, close, compact.<BR>--2 Firm, tight, fast; निबिडो मुष्टिः<BR>R. 9. 58, 19. 44.<BR>--3 Thick,<BR>impervious, dense, impenetrable;<BR>R. 11 15.<BR>--4 Gross, coarse.<BR>--5 Bulky,<BR>large.<BR>--6 Crooked-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निबिड
निवि(बि)ड a.<BR>1 Without<BR>space or interstices, close, compact.<BR>--2 Firm, tight, fast; निबिडो मुष्टिः<BR>R. 9. 58, 19. 44.<BR>--3 Thick,<BR>impervious, dense, impenetrable;<BR>R. 11 15.<BR>--4 Gross, coarse.<BR>--5 Bulky,<BR>large.<BR>--6 Crooked-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविद्
निविद् {c2c} P. (generally in the<BR>caus.)<BR>1 To tell, communicate,<BR>inform (with dat.); उपस्थितां<BR>होमवेलां गुरवे निवेदयामि Ś. 4; काश्यपाय<BR>वनस्पतिसेवां निवेदयावः ibid., R. 2. 68.<BR>--2 To declare or announce oneself;<BR>कथमात्मानं निवेदयामि Ś. 1.<BR>--3 To<BR>indicate, betray, show;<BR>शंकापीरग्रहनिवेदयिता Mu. 1; दिगंबरत्वेन निवेदितं वसु<BR>Ku. 5. 72; R. 17. 40.<BR>--4 To offer,<BR>present, give, make an offer of;<BR>स्वराज्यं चंद्रापीडाय न्यवेदयत् K. 367;<BR>राज्यमस्मै न्यवेदयत् R. 15. 70, 11. 47;<BR>Ms. 2. 51; Y. 1. 27.<BR>--5 To entrust to<BR>the care of, make or deliver over to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविद्
निविद् f. Ved.<BR>1 Speech, a short<BR>Vedic text.<BR>--2 Instruction, precept,<BR>direction.<BR>--3 Invocation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदक
निवेदक a. Informing,<BR>communicating &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदनं|निवेदन|निवेदनः
निवेदनं<BR>1 Making known, relating,<BR>proclaiming; a communication,<BR>announcement.<BR>--2 Delivering,<BR>entrusting.<BR>--3 Dedication.<BR>--4<BR>Representation.<BR>--5 An offering or oblation.<BR>--नः<BR>An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेदित|निवेदितं
निवेदित p. p.<BR>1 Made known,<BR>announced, told, communicated.<BR>--2<BR>Delivered, given, entrusted, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेद्यं|निवेद्य
निवेद्यं Offering of food to an idol;<BR>cf. नैवेद्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविरीश
निविरी(डी)श-स a.<BR>1<BR>Compact, close; उरुनिविरीसनितंबभारखेदि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-c" target="_blank">Page0637-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Śi. 7. 20.<BR>--2 Coarse, gross.<BR>--सा A<BR>crooked nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविडीश
निविरी(डी)श-स a.<BR>1<BR>Compact, close; उरुनिविरीसनितंबभारखेदि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-c" target="_blank">Page0637-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Śi. 7. 20.<BR>--2 Coarse, gross.<BR>--सा A<BR>crooked nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविरीस|निविरीसं
निविरी(डी)श-स a.<BR>1<BR>Compact, close; उरुनिविरीसनितंबभारखेदि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-c" target="_blank">Page0637-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Śi. 7. 20.<BR>--2 Coarse, gross.<BR>--सा A<BR>crooked nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविडीस
निविरी(डी)श-स a.<BR>1<BR>Compact, close; उरुनिविरीसनितंबभारखेदि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-c" target="_blank">Page0637-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Śi. 7. 20.<BR>--2 Coarse, gross.<BR>--सा A<BR>crooked nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविश्
निविश् {c6c} A.<BR>1 To sit down,<BR>take a seat; नवांबुदश्यामवपुर्न्यविक्षत<BR>(आसने) Śi. 1. 19.<BR>--2 To halt,<BR>encamp; R. 12. 68.<BR>--3 To enter;<BR>रामशालां न्यविक्षत Bk. 4. 28, 6. 143,<BR>8. 7; R. 9. 82; 12. 38.<BR>--4 To be<BR>fixed on, be directed towards;<BR>सूर्यनिविष्टदृष्टिः R. 14. 66.<BR>--5 To be<BR>devoted or attached to, be intent on,<BR>to practise; श्रुतिप्रामाण्यतो विद्वान्स्वर्धेम<BR>निविशेत वै Ms. 2. 8.<BR>--6 To marry<BR>(for निर्विश् q. v.).<BR>--7 To alight,<BR>descend. --Caus.<BR>1 To fix or direct<BR>upon, apply to (as thought, mind<BR>&c.); Bg. 12. 8.<BR>--2 To put, place,<BR>keep; मनोगतं वाचि निवेशयंति<BR>Ki. 14. 4; R. 6. 16, 4. 39, 7. 63.<BR>--3<BR>To seat, install; R. 15. 97.<BR>--4 To<BR>cause to settle in life, get married;<BR>दौष्यंतिमप्रतिरथं तनयं निवेश्य Ś. 4. 19;<BR>R. 11. 57.<BR>--5 To encamp (as an<BR>army); R. 5. 42, 16. 37.<BR>--6 To<BR>draw, paint, portray; चित्रे निवेश्य<BR>परिकल्पितसत्वयोगा Ś. 2. 9; M. 3. 11.<BR>--7 To commit to writing, inscribe<BR>on; V. 2. 14.<BR>--8 To intrust or<BR>commit to; Mu. 5. 7; R. 19. 4.<BR>--9 To<BR>introduce.<BR>--10 To found (a city).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविष्ट|निविष्टं|निविष्टः
निविष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Seated, sitting upon.<BR>--2 Encamped; R. 12. 68.<BR>--3<BR>Fixed or intent upon.<BR>--4 Concentrated,<BR>subdued, controlled; Ku. 5. 31.<BR>--5<BR>Initiated.<BR>--6 Arranged.<BR>--7 Entered,<BR>gone into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविष्टिः|निविष्टि
निविष्टिः f. Copulation, coition<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशः|निवेश
निवेशः<BR>1 Entering, entrance.<BR>--2<BR>Encamping, halting.<BR>--3 (a) A<BR>halting place, camp, encampment;<BR>सेनानिवेशं तुमुलं चकार R. 5. 49, 7. 2;<BR>Śi. 17. 40; Ki. 7. 27.<BR>--4 A house, an<BR>abode, a dwelling; Ki. 4. 19.<BR>--5<BR>Expanse, contour (of the breast);<BR>Ki. 4. 8.<BR>--6 Depositing, delivering.<BR>--7 Marrying, marriage, settling in<BR>life.<BR>--8 Impression, copy.<BR>--9<BR>Military array.<BR>--10 Ornament,<BR>decoration.<BR>--11 Founding (a town).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेशनं|निवेशन
निवेशनं<BR>1 Entering, entrance.<BR>--2<BR>Halting, encamping.<BR>--3 Marrying,<BR>marriage.<BR>--4 Entering in writing,<BR>inscribing.<BR>--5 An abode, a dwelling,<BR>house, habitation.<BR>--6 A camp.<BR>--7 A<BR>town or city.<BR>--8 A nest.<BR>--नी The<BR>earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0637-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निविशेष|निविशेषः
निविशेष a. Not different, alike.<BR>--षः Want of difference, sameness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीतं|निवीत|निवीतः
निवीतं<BR>1 Wearing the sacred<BR>thread round the neck (making it<BR>hang down like a garland); निवीतं<BR>मनुष्याणा प्राचीनावीतं पितॄणामुपवीतं<BR>देवानां J. N. V.<BR>--2 The thread so worn.<BR>--तः, --तं A veil, mantle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवीतिन्
निवीतिन् a. Wearing the sacred<BR>thread round the neck (like a<BR>garland).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृ
निवृ {c5c} {c9c} {c1c} U. To surround,<BR>enclose; Bk. 14. 29. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>ward off, keep away from, avert<BR>from (with abl.); पापान्निवारयति<BR>योजयते हिताय Bh. 2. 72; निवारयंती<BR>महतो मुनिव्रतात् Ku. 5. 3.<BR>--2 To<BR>surround, protect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारः|निवार
निवारः, निवारणं<BR>1 Keeping off,<BR>preventing, warding off;<BR>दंशनिवारणैश्च R. 2. 5.<BR>--2 Prohibition,<BR>impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवारणं|निवारण
निवारः, निवारणं<BR>1 Keeping off,<BR>preventing, warding off;<BR>दंशनिवारणैश्च R. 2. 5.<BR>--2 Prohibition,<BR>impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत|निवृतं|निवृतः
निवृत p. p. Surrounded, enclosed.<BR>--तः, --तं A veil, mantle, wrapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृतिः|निवृति
निवृतिः f. Covering, enclosing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्
निवृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To come back,<BR>return; न च निम्नादिव सलिलं निवर्तते मे<BR>ततो हृदयं Ś. 3. 1; Ku. 4. 30;<BR>R. 2. 40; Bg. 8. 21; 15. 4.<BR>--2 To flee<BR>from, retreat; Bk. 5. 102.<BR>--3 To<BR>turn away from, be averse to;<BR>R. 5. 23; 7. 61.<BR>--4 To cease, desist or<BR>abstain from; प्रसमीक्ष्य निवर्तेत<BR>सर्वमांसस्य भक्षणात् Ms. 5. 49, 1. 53;<BR>Bk. 1. 18; निवृत्तमांसस्तु जनकः U. 4.<BR>--5<BR>To be freed or absolved from, to<BR>escape; Bg. 1. 39.<BR>--6 To leave off<BR>speaking, cease, stop.<BR>--7 To be<BR>removed, come to an end, cease,<BR>disappear; Bg. 2. 59, 14. 22;<BR>Ms. 11. 185, 186.<BR>--8 To be accomplished or<BR>finished, come to an end.<BR>--9 To be<BR>withheld or withdrawn from.<BR>--10<BR>To refuse, decline.<BR>--11 To be<BR>engaged in.<BR>--12 To be reversed.<BR>--13<BR>To set (as the sun).<BR>--14 To be<BR>forbidden. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to return,<BR>send back; R. 2. 3, 3. 47, 7. 44.<BR>--2 To withdraw, keep away from;<BR>turn away, divert; R. 2. 28;<BR>Ku. 5. 11.<BR>--3 To accomplish, perform, finish,<BR>complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तक
निवर्तक a.<BR>1 Returning, coming<BR>or turning back.<BR>--2 Stopping,<BR>ceasing.<BR>--3 Abolishing, expelling,<BR>removing.<BR>--4 Bringing back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तन|निवर्त्तन
निवर्तन a.<BR>1 Causing to return.<BR>--2 Turning back, ceasing.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Returning, turning or coming back,<BR>return; इह हि पततां नास्त्यालंबो न<BR>चापि निवर्तनं Śānti. 3. 2.<BR>--2 Not<BR>happening, ceasing.<BR>--3 Desisting or<BR>abstaining from (with abl.).<BR>--4<BR>Desisting from work, inactivity (opp.<BR>प्रवर्तन); Kām. 1. 28.<BR>--5 Bringing<BR>back; Amaru. 84.<BR>--6 Repenting, a<BR>desire to improve.<BR>--7 A measure of<BR>land (20 rods).<BR>--8 Keeping back<BR>from (with abl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवर्तिन्
निवर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Turning back, flying<BR>from, returning.<BR>--2 Desisting or<BR>abstaining from.<BR>--3 Allowing to<BR>return or turn back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्त|निवृत्तः
निवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Returned, turned<BR>back.<BR>--2 Gone, departed, vanished,<BR>disappeared.<BR>--3 Ceased, refrained or<BR>abstained from, stopped, desisted;<BR>Ku. 1. 51.<BR>--4 Abstaining from<BR>worldly acts, abstracted from this<BR>world, quiet.<BR>--5 Repenting of<BR>improper conduct.<BR>--6 Finished,<BR>completed, whole; see वृत् with नि.<BR>--त्तं<BR>1 Return.<BR>--2 A mind free from the<BR>influence of passions.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् m. {1} a sage. {2} an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--कारण a. without further<BR>cause or motive.<BR>--(णः) a virtuous<BR>man, a man uninfluenced by<BR>worldly desires.<BR>--मांस a. one who<BR>abstains from eating meat; निवृत्तमां<BR>सरतु जनकः U. 4.<BR>--राग a. of<BR>subdued passions.<BR>--वृत्ति a. quitting<BR>any practice or occupation.<BR>--हृदय<BR>a. with relenting heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवृत्तिः|निवृत्ति
निवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Returning or<BR>coming back, return; Śi. 14. 64;<BR>R. 4. 87.<BR>--2 Disappearance, cessation,<BR>termination, suspension; शापनिवृत्तौ<BR>Ś. 7; R. 8. 82.<BR>--3 Abstaining from<BR>work, inactivity (opp. प्रवृत्ति).<BR>--4<BR>Abstaining from, aversion;<BR>प्राणाघातान्निवृत्तिः Bh. 3. 63.<BR>--5 Leaving<BR>off, desisting from.<BR>--6 Resignation,<BR>discontinuance of worldly acts or<BR>emotions, quietism, separation from<BR>the world.<BR>--7 Repose, rest.<BR>--8<BR>Felicity, beatitude.<BR>--9 Denial, refusal.<BR>--10 Abolition, prevention.<BR>--11<BR>Ceasing to be valid or binding (as a<BR>rule.).<BR>--12 Completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्टः|निवेष्ट
निवेष्टः A cover, an envelope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्टनं|निवेष्टन
निवेष्टनं Covering, enveloping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निवेष्य|निवेष्यः
निवेष्य a. Whirling.<BR>--ष्यः<BR>1 An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">Page0638-c+ 56</a>]<BR>eddy, a whirlpool.<BR>--2 A whirlwind or<BR>a similar phenomenon.<BR>--3<BR>Hoarfrost.<BR>--ष्यं Extent (व्याप्ति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निव्यूढं|निव्यूढ
निव्यूढं Perseverance, energy; cf.<BR>निर्व्यूढ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्
निश् f. (This word is optionally<BR>substituted for निशा in all cases after<BR>acc. dual; it has no forms for<BR>the first five inflections)<BR>1 Night.<BR>--2 Turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशठ|निशठः
निशठ a. Honest, candid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशब्द
निशब्द a. Silent, not speaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशम्
निशम् {c4c} P., {c10c} U.<BR>1 To hear,<BR>listen to, come to know; निशम्य चैनां<BR>तपसे कृतोद्यमां Ku. 5. 3; Ś. 5. 2;<BR>R. 2. 41, 52, 61; 3. 47; 4. 2; 5. 12;<BR>Bk. 2. 9; निशामय प्रियसखि Māl. 7.<BR>--2 To see, observe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशमनं|निशमन
निशमनं<BR>1 Looking at, beholding<BR>--2 Seeing, sight.<BR>--3 Hearing.<BR>--4<BR>Becoming aware of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशांत|निशान्त|निशान्तं|निशान्तः
निशांत p. p. Tranquil, calmed,<BR>quiet, patient.<BR>--तं A house,<BR>habitation, dwelling; R. 16. 40.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नारी a housewife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामः|निशाम
निशामः Observing, perceiving,<BR>seeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशामनं|निशामन
निशामनं<BR>1 Seeing, beholding.<BR>--2<BR>Sight.<BR>--3 Hearing.<BR>--4 Repeated<BR>observation.<BR>--5 A shadow, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशरणं|निशरण
निश(शा)रणं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारणं|निशारण
निश(शा)रणं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशा
निशा [नितरां श्यति तनूकरोति<BR>व्यापारान् शो-क Tv.]<BR>1 Night; यानिशा सर्वभूतानां<BR>तस्यां जागर्ति संयमी Bg. 2. 69.<BR>--2<BR>Turmeric.<BR>--3 A dream.<BR>--4 A collective<BR>name for the zodiacal signs Aries,<BR>Taurus, Gemini, Cancer,<BR>Sagittarius, and Capricorn.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अटः,<BR>--अटनः {1} an owl. {2} a demon,<BR>ghost, goblin.<BR>--अटकः bdellium.<BR>--अतिक्रमः, --अत्ययः, --अंतः, --अवसानं<BR>{1} the passing away of night. {2}<BR>daybreak.<BR>--अदः = Niṣāda q. v.<BR>--अंध a. blind at night.<BR>--(धा) the<BR>creeper called जतुका.<BR>--अधीशः, --ईशः,<BR>--नाथः, --पतिः, --मणिः, --रत्नं {1} the<BR>moon. {2} camphor.<BR>--अर्धकालः the<BR>first part of the night.<BR>--आख्या<BR>--आह्वा turmeric.<BR>--आदिः the<BR>evening twilight.<BR>--उत्सर्गः end of night<BR>daybreak.<BR>--एतः a crane.<BR>--करः {1}<BR>the moon; Ku. 4. 13. {2} a cock.<BR>{3} camphor.<BR>--केतुः the moon<BR>--गृह<BR>a bed-chamber.<BR>--चर a. (--रा --री f.)<BR>moving about by night, night<BR>stalker.<BR>--(रः) {1} a fiend, goblin, an evil<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">Page0639-a+ 56</a>]<BR>spirit; R. 12. 69. {2} an epithet of<BR>Śiva. {3} a jackal. {4} an owl. {5}<BR>a snake. {6} the ruddy goose. {7} a<BR>thief. ˚पतिः {1} an epithet of {1} Śiva.<BR>{2} of Rāvaṇa.<BR>--(री) {1} a female<BR>fiend. {2} a woman going to meet<BR>her lover at night by appointment;<BR>राममन्मथशरेण ताडिता दुःसहेन हृदये<BR>निशाचरी R. 11. 20 (where the word is<BR>used in sense 1 also). {3} a harlot.<BR>--चर्मन् m. darkness.<BR>--जलं dew,<BR>frost.<BR>--दर्शिन् m. an owl.<BR>--निशं ind.<BR>every night, always.<BR>--पुष्पं {1} the<BR>white water-lily (opening at night).<BR>{2} hoar-frost, dew.<BR>--मुखं the<BR>beginning of night.<BR>--मृगः a jackal.<BR>--वनः<BR>hemp (शन).<BR>--विहारः a demon,<BR>goblin, a Rākṣasa; प्रचक्रतू<BR>रामनिशाविहारौ Bk. 2. 36.<BR>--वेदिन् m. a cock.<BR>--हसः the white water-lily (opening<BR>at night).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0638-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशात|निशातः
निशात p. p.<BR>1 Sharpened,<BR>whetted, sharp; Ki. 14. 30.<BR>--2 Polished,<BR>burnished, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशानं|निशान
निशानं Sharpening, whetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशित|निशितं|निशितः
निशित a.<BR>1 Sharpened, whetted,<BR>sharp; निशितनिपाताः शराः Ś. 1. 10.<BR>--2 Stimulated.<BR>--तं Iron.<BR>--ता<BR>Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशितिः|निशिति
निशितिः f. Excitement, agitation<BR>(Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशादः|निशाद
निशादः A man of low caste; see<BR>निषाद. (निशादापुत्रः A pestle; so ˚शिला a<BR>mortar.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशारुकः|निशारुक
निशारुकः One of the seven<BR>Rūpakas in music.<BR>--कं An air, a<BR>sort of musical composition played<BR>as an accompaniment to dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथः|निशीथ
निशीथः<BR>1 [निशेरते जना अस्मिन्;<BR>निशीआधारे थक् Tv.] Midnight; निशीथदीपाः<BR>सहसा हतत्विषः R. 3. 15; Me. 88;<BR>Māl. 8. 10.<BR>--2 The time of sleep,<BR>night in general; शुचौ निशीथेऽनुभवंति<BR>कामिनः Rs. 1. 3; Amaru. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथिनी
निशीथिनी, निशीथ्या Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशीथ्या
निशीथिनी, निशीथ्या Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुंभः|निशुम्भ|निशुंभ|निशुम्भः
निशुंभः<BR>1 Killing, slaughter;<BR>Māl. 5. 22.<BR>--2 Breaking, bending<BR>(as of a bow); Mv. 2. 33.<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>demon killed by Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मथनी, --मर्दनी epithets of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निशुंभनं|निशुम्भन|निशुंभन|निशुम्भनं
निशुंभनं Killing, slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चल
निश्चल a.<BR>1 immovable, steady,<BR>fixed, still.<BR>--2 Invariable,<BR>unchangeable; Bg. 2. 53.<BR>--ला The earth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. firm.<BR>--(गः) {1} a<BR>species of crane. {2} a rock or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">Page0639-b+ 55</a>]<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चर्
निश्चर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To issue, go out.<BR>--2 To arise, be produced, appear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चारकं|निश्चारक|निश्चारकः
निश्चारकं<BR>1 Evacuation by stools.<BR>--2 Air, wind.<BR>--3 Obstinacy, wilful<BR>nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चि
निश्चि {c5c} U. To determine, resolve,<BR>ascertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चयः|निश्चय
निश्चयः<BR>1 Ascertainment,<BR>investigation, inquiry.<BR>--2 A fixed opinion,<BR>settled or firm conviction, firm<BR>belief.<BR>--3 A determination, resolution,<BR>resolve; एष मे स्थिरो निश्चयः Mu. 1.<BR>--4 Certainty, positiveness, positive<BR>conclusion.<BR>--5 Fixed intention,<BR>design, purpose, aim; कैकेयी क्रूरनिश्चय<BR>R. 12. 4; Ku. 5. 5.<BR>--6 N. of a figure<BR>in Rhetoric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चायक|निश्चायकः
निश्चायक a. Who or what<BR>ascertains or determines, decisive,<BR>conclusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चित
निश्चित p. p.<BR>1 Ascertained,<BR>determined, decided, settled, concluded<BR>(used actively also); अरावणमरामं वा<BR>जगदद्योति निश्चितः R. 12. 83.<BR>--2<BR>Sentenced, pronounced (as a sentence).<BR>--तं Certainty, decision.<BR>--तं ind.<BR>Decidedly, positively, certainly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चितिः|निश्चिति
निश्चितिः f.<BR>1 Ascertainment,<BR>settling.<BR>--2 A determination,<BR>resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्चुक्कणं|निश्चुक्कण
निश्चुक्कणं A powder for clearing<BR>the teeth, a kind of tooth powder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रमः|निश्रम
निश्रमः Labour bestowed upon<BR>anything, continued practice or<BR>labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रयणी
निश्रयणी, निश्रेणि, निश्रेणी A ladder,<BR>a staircase; cf. निःश्रयणी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रेणि
निश्रयणी, निश्रेणि, निश्रेणी A ladder,<BR>a staircase; cf. निःश्रयणी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्रेणी
निश्रयणी, निश्रेणि, निश्रेणी A ladder,<BR>a staircase; cf. निःश्रयणी &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्वस्
निश्वस् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To sigh, heave.<BR>--2<BR>To draw in the breath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निश्वासः|निश्वास
निश्वासः Inspiration, inhaling,<BR>sighing; cf. निःश्वास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्
निष् {c1c} A. (नेषति) To moisten, wet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषंज्
निषंज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To adhere or stick to,<BR>be thrown round or placed on; कंठे<BR>स्वयंग्राहनिषक्तबाहुं Ku. 3. 7;<BR>U. 4. 18; R. 9. 50, 11. 70, 19. 45.<BR>--2 To<BR>be reflected; Ku. 1. 10; 7. 36.<BR>--3<BR>To be attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषंगः|निषङ्ग|निषंग|निषङ्गः
निषंगः<BR>1 Attachment, clinging to.<BR>--2 Union, association.<BR>--3 A quiver;<BR>Śi. 10. 34; Ki. 17. 36; R. 2. 30,<BR>3. 64.<BR>--4 A sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषंगथिः|निषङ्गथि|निषंगथि|निषङ्गथिः
निषंगथिः<BR>1 An embrace.<BR>--2 A<BR>bowman.<BR>--3 A charioteer.<BR>--4 A car.<BR>--5<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">Page0639-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Grass.<BR>--6 The shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषंगिन्|निषङ्गिन्
निषंगिन् a.<BR>1 Attached or clinging<BR>to; Śi. 12. 26.<BR>--2 Having a quiver.<BR>--3 Bearing a sword. --m.<BR>1 An<BR>archer, a bowman.<BR>--2 A quiver.<BR>--3<BR>A sword-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्
निषद् {c1c} P. (निषीदति &c.)<BR>1 To sit<BR>down, lie, recline; उष्णालुः शिशिरे<BR>निषीदति तरोर्मूलालवाले शिखी V. 2. 23.<BR>--2 To sink down, fail, be<BR>disappointed.<BR>--3 To dwell.<BR>--4 To suffer pain,<BR>be afflicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्
निषद् f. Consecration for a<BR>sacrifice (यज्ञदीक्षा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्ण|निषण्णः
निषण्ण p. p.<BR>1 Seated; sitting on<BR>or in, rested, reclined, resting or<BR>reclining on; R. 9. 76, Ku. 4. 23<BR>--2<BR>Supported.<BR>--3 Gone to.<BR>--4 Dejected,<BR>afflicted, downcast; cf. विषण्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषण्णकं|निषण्णक
निषण्णकं A seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषत्तिः|निषत्ति
निषत्तिः f. Ved. Sitting down idly.<BR>dulness, inactivity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषदनं|निषदन|निषदनः
निषदनं Ved.<BR>1 Sitting.<BR>--2<BR>Dwelling.<BR>--3 A seat.<BR>--4 A house,<BR>residence.<BR>--नः = निषाद q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्या
निषद्या<BR>1 A small bed or couch.<BR>--2<BR>The hall of a merchant, a trader's<BR>shop.<BR>--3 A market-place, market;<BR>Śi. 18. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषद्वरः|निषद्वर
निषद्वरः<BR>1 Mud, mire.<BR>--2 The god<BR>of love.<BR>--री Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादित
निषादित p. p.<BR>1 Made to sit down.<BR>--2 Afflicted, distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादिन्
निषादिन् a. (नी f.) Sitting or lying<BR>down, resting, reclining; R. 1. 52,<BR>4. 20. --m. An elephant-driver; Śi. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषध|निषधः
निषध a. Hard, solid.<BR>--धाः (m. pl.)<BR>N. of a people and their country<BR>governed by Nala.<BR>--धः<BR>1 A ruler of<BR>the Niṣadhas.<BR>--2 N. of a mountain.<BR>--3 A musical note; cf. निषाद.<BR>--धा N.<BR>of Nala's capital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषादः|निषाद
निषादः<BR>1 N. of one of the wild<BR>aboriginal tribes in India, such as.<BR>hunters, fishermen &c.; a<BR>mountaineer; मा निषाद प्रतिष्ठां त्वमगमः<BR>शाश्वतीः समाः Rām; R. 14. 52, 70;<BR>U. 2. 5.<BR>--2 A man of a degraded tribe<BR>in general, an outcast, a Cāṇḍāla.<BR>--3 Especially, the son of a<BR>Brāhmaṇa by a Śūdra woman; cf.<BR>Ms. 10. 8.<BR>--4 (In music) The first<BR>(more properly the last or seventh)<BR>note of the Hindu gamut;<BR>गीतकलाविन्यासमिव निषादानुगतं K. 31 (where<BR>it has sense 1 also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0639-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिच्
निषिच् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To pour upon or<BR>down, sprinkle, pour in; R. 3. 26;<BR>Ś. 4. 13; Ku. 2. 57.<BR>--2 To<BR>impregnate; निषिंचन्माधवीमेतां लतां कौंदीं च<BR>नर्तयन् V. 2. 4 (where the word also<BR>means ‘to fill with honey-drops’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिक्त
निषिक्त p. p.<BR>1 Sprinkled upon.<BR>--2<BR>Infused, instilled, poured into,<BR>impregnated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेकः|निषेक
निषेकः<BR>1 Sprinkling, infusion;<BR>सुखसलिलनिषेकः Rs. 1. 28.<BR>--2<BR>Dripping, trickling, distilling;<BR>तैलनिषेकबिंदुना R. 8. 38 ‘a drop of dripping<BR>oil.’<BR>--3 Effusion, discharge.<BR>--4<BR>Seminal effusion or discharge, infusion<BR>of semen, impregnation, seed;<BR>Ku. 3. 16; R. 14. 60.<BR>--5 The ceremony<BR>performed upon impregnation.<BR>--6<BR>Irrigation.<BR>--7 Water for washing.<BR>--8<BR>Seminal impurity.<BR>--9 Dirty water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेचनं|निषेचन
निषेचनं<BR>1 Sprinkling, pouring out.<BR>--2 Watering, irrigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिध्
निषिध् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To ward off,<BR>prevent, restrain, keep back; न्यषेधि<BR>शेषोऽप्यनुयायिवर्गः R. 2. 4, 3. 42,<BR>5. 18.<BR>--2 To oppose, contradict,<BR>object to; R. 14. 43.<BR>--3 To prohibit,<BR>forbid; निषिद्धो भाषमाणस्तु सुवर्णं<BR>दंडमर्हति Ms. 8. 361.<BR>--4 To defeat,<BR>conquer; R. 18. 1.<BR>--5 To remove, drive<BR>off, counteract; न्यषेधत्पावकास्त्रेण<BR>रामस्तद्राक्षसस्ततः Bk. 17. 87, 1. 15.<BR>--Caus. To prohibit, keep off or<BR>ward off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिद्ध|निषिद्धं
निषिद्ध p. p. Forbidden, prohibited,<BR>warded off, prevented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषिद्धिः|निषिद्धि
निषिद्धिः f.<BR>1 Prohibition,<BR>warding or keeping off.<BR>--2 Defence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेधः|निषेध
निषेधः<BR>1 Prohibition, warding or<BR>keeping off, stopping, prevention.<BR>--2 Negation, denial.<BR>--3 The<BR>particle of negation; द्वौ निषेधौ प्रकृतार्थं<BR>गमयतः<BR>--4 A prohibitive rule (opp.<BR>विधि).<BR>--5 Deviation from a rule,<BR>exception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषूद्
निषूद् {c10c} U. or Caus. To kill slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषूदनं|निषूदन|निषूदनः
निषूदनं Killing, slaughter.<BR>--नः A<BR>killer; as in बलवृत्रनिषूदनः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेव्
निषेव् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To pursue, follow,<BR>attach oneself to, practise; Ś. 1. 27.<BR>--2 To enjoy; निषेवते श्रांतमना विविक्त<BR>Ś. 5. 5; Ku. 1. 5.<BR>--3 To enjoy<BR>carnally; यथा यथा तामरसेक्षणा मया<BR>पुनः सरागं नितरां निषेविता Bv. 2. 155;<BR>Pt. 1. 202.<BR>--4 To resort to, inhabit,<BR>frequent; Ku. 5. 76.<BR>--5 To use,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">Page0640-b+ 57</a>]<BR>employ; विषतां निषेवितमपक्रियया<BR>समुपैति सर्वमिति सत्यमदः Śi. 9. 68.<BR>--6 To<BR>wait upon, attend.<BR>--7 To adore,<BR>worship.<BR>--8 To draw near, approach.<BR>--9 To suffer, experience; Pt. 1. 334.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवक
निषेवक a.<BR>1 Practising, following,<BR>devoted to, fond of.<BR>--2<BR>Frequenting, inhabiting, resorting to.<BR>--3 Enjoying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवणं|निषेवण
निषेवणं, निषेवा<BR>1 Serving, service,<BR>attending waiting upon.<BR>--2 Worship,<BR>adoration.<BR>--3 Practice,<BR>performance.<BR>--4 Attachment or adherence<BR>to.<BR>--5 Living in, inhabiting,<BR>enjoying, using.<BR>--6 Familiarity with, use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवा
निषेवणं, निषेवा<BR>1 Serving, service,<BR>attending waiting upon.<BR>--2 Worship,<BR>adoration.<BR>--3 Practice,<BR>performance.<BR>--4 Attachment or adherence<BR>to.<BR>--5 Living in, inhabiting,<BR>enjoying, using.<BR>--6 Familiarity with, use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषेवित
निषेवित p. p.<BR>1 Served, waited<BR>upon, worshipped, honoured.<BR>--2<BR>Visited, resorted to, haunted,<BR>frequented.<BR>--3 Practised, observed (as a<BR>vow &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्
निष्क् {c10c} A. (निष्कयते) To weigh,<BR>measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कः|निष्क|निष्कं
निष्कः --कं<BR>1 A golden coin (of<BR>different values, but generally taken<BR>to be equal to one Karṣa or<BR>Suvarṇa of 16 Māṣas).<BR>--2 A weight of<BR>gold equal to 108 or 150<BR>Suvarṇas q. v.<BR>--3 A golden ornament for<BR>the neck or the breast; Ku. 2. 49.<BR>--4 Gold in general.<BR>--5 A golden<BR>vessel.<BR>--ष्कः A Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कं|निष्क|निष्कः
निष्कः --कं<BR>1 A golden coin (of<BR>different values, but generally taken<BR>to be equal to one Karṣa or<BR>Suvarṇa of 16 Māṣas).<BR>--2 A weight of<BR>gold equal to 108 or 150<BR>Suvarṇas q. v.<BR>--3 A golden ornament for<BR>the neck or the breast; Ku. 2. 49.<BR>--4 Gold in general.<BR>--5 A golden<BR>vessel.<BR>--ष्कः A Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कस्
निष्कस् Caus.<BR>1 To take or draw<BR>out.<BR>--2 To turn or drive out, banish,<BR>expel; निरकासयद्रविमपेतवसुं<BR>वियदालयादपरदिग्गणिका Śi. 9. 10; येनाहं<BR>जीवलोकान्निरकासयिष्ये Mu {6}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासः|निष्कास
निष्कासः(शः)<BR>1 Exit, egress,<BR>issue.<BR>--2 A portice.<BR>--3 Day-break.<BR>--4<BR>Disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्काशः|निष्काश
निष्कासः(शः)<BR>1 Exit, egress,<BR>issue.<BR>--2 A portice.<BR>--3 Day-break.<BR>--4<BR>Disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासित|निष्कासितः
निष्कासित p. p.<BR>1 Expelled,<BR>turned out, driven out.<BR>--2 Gone forth<BR>or out, issued.<BR>--3 Placed, deposited.<BR>--4 Stationed, appointed.<BR>--5<BR>Opened, blown, expanded.<BR>--6 Reviled,<BR>reproached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कासिनी
निष्कासिनी A female slave not<BR>restrained by her master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कालनं|निष्कालन
निष्कालनं<BR>1 Driving away<BR>(cattle &c.).<BR>--2 Killing, slaughter (<BR>मारण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुटः|निष्कुट
निष्कुटः<BR>1 A pleasure-grove<BR>near a house.<BR>--2 A field.<BR>--3 The<BR>female apartments, the harem of<BR>a king.<BR>--4 A door, gate.<BR>--5 The<BR>hollow of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुटिः|निष्कुटि
निष्कुटिः --टी f. Large cardamoms<BR>(एला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुटी
निष्कुटिः --टी f. Large cardamoms<BR>(एला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुष्
निष्कुष् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To extract, tear,<BR>draw out; उपांतयोर्निष्कुषितं विहंगैः<BR>R. 7. 50; Bk. 9. 30; 5. 42; so<BR>काकैर्निष्कुषितं श्वभिः कवलितं<BR>गोमायुभिर्लुंठितं Gaṅgāṣṭaka; Māl. 5. 17.<BR>--2<BR>To husk, shell.<BR>--3 To injure or hurt<BR>by tearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुषित
निष्कुषित p. p.<BR>1 Torn off, forced<BR>or drawn out, lacerated; R. 7. 50.<BR>--2 Expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषः|निष्कोष
निष्कोषः, निष्कोषणं<BR>1 Tearing,<BR>drawing off or out, extracting,<BR>extirpating.<BR>--2 Husking, shelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषणं|निष्कोषण
निष्कोषः, निष्कोषणं<BR>1 Tearing,<BR>drawing off or out, extracting,<BR>extirpating.<BR>--2 Husking, shelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कोषणकं|निष्कोषणक
निष्कोषणकं A tooth-pick; Pt. 1. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कुहः|निष्कुह
निष्कुहः The hollow of a tree; cf.<BR>निष्कुट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृ
निष्कृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To remove, drive<BR>away, expel; Ms. 11. 54.<BR>--2 To<BR>break, frustrate; Bk. 15. 51.<BR>--3 To<BR>break into pieces, destroy.<BR>--4 To<BR>prepare, fit up, equip.<BR>--5 To<BR>accomplish, finish.<BR>--6 To absolve, free<BR>from (blame, sin &c.), acquit.<BR>--7<BR>To cure, heal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कारणं|निष्कारण
निष्कारणं<BR>1 Removing, taking<BR>away.<BR>--2 Killing; cf. निकारणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृत
निष्कृत p. p.<BR>1 Taken away,<BR>removed.<BR>--2 Expiated, absolved,<BR>pardoned.<BR>--3 Disregarded, overlooked.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Expiation or atonement.<BR>--2<BR>A place of rendezvous^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृतिः|निष्कृति
निष्कृतिः f.<BR>1 Expiation, atonement;<BR>Pt. 3. 157.<BR>--2 Acquittance, requital,<BR>discharge of a debt or obligation;<BR>न तस्य निष्कृतिः शक्या कर्तुं वर्षशतैरपि<BR>Ms. 2. 227, 3. 19; 8. 105, 9. 19,<BR>11. 27.<BR>--3 Removal.<BR>--4 Restoration,<BR>cure.<BR>--5 Avoiding, escaping from.<BR>--6 Neglecting.<BR>--7 Bad conduct,<BR>roguery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृत्
निष्कृत् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To cut, cut off,<BR>divide, tear asunder, cut in pieces.<BR>--2 To loosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्तनं
निष्कर्तनं Cutting off, tearing away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृष्
निष्कृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To draw or pull<BR>out, extract.<BR>--2 To extort, exact,<BR>snatch or take by force; निष्क्रष्टुमर्थं<BR>चकमे कुबेरात् R. 5. 26.<BR>--3 To tear<BR>asunder, cut in pieces. --Caus. To<BR>destroy, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्षः|निष्कर्ष
निष्कर्षः<BR>1 Drawing out, extraction.<BR>--2 The essence, the chief or main<BR>point, pith; इति निष्कर्षः (often used<BR>by commentators); Ms. 4. 125;<BR>Bhāṣā P. 138.<BR>--3 Measuring.<BR>--4<BR>Certainty, ascertainment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कर्षणं|निष्कर्षण
निष्कर्षणं<BR>1 Drawing out,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">Page0641-a+ 55</a>]<BR>extracting, pulling off; R. 12. 97.<BR>--2<BR>Deducting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0640-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्कृष्ट
निष्कृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Pulled or drawn<BR>out, extracted.<BR>--2 Summed up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रम्
निष्क्रम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To go away or<BR>from, leave, depart.<BR>--2 To issue from,<BR>come out of; Bk. 7. 71.<BR>--3 To make<BR>an exit from the stage; इति निष्क्रांताः<BR>सर्वे.<BR>--4 To stop, cease; नैतावतापि पीडा<BR>निष्कामति Ś. 2 ‘the evil does not stop<BR>here.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रमः|निष्क्रम
निष्क्रमः<BR>1 Going out, coming forth.<BR>--2 Departure from, exit.<BR>--3 One of<BR>the Saṃskāras or religious rites;<BR>i. e. taking out a child for the first<BR>time into the open air (which is<BR>usually performed in the fourth<BR>month of its age); चतुर्थे मासि<BR>निष्क्रमः Y. 1. 12; cf. उपनिष्क्रमण also.<BR>--4<BR>Degradation, loss of caste,<BR>inferiority of tribe.<BR>--5 Intellectual faculty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रमणं|निष्क्रमण
निष्क्रमणं<BR>1 Going forth or out.<BR>--2<BR>= निष्क्रम (3) above; चतुर्थे मासि<BR>कर्तव्यं शिशोर्निष्क्रमणं गृहात् Ms. 2. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रमणिका
निष्क्रमणिका See निष्क्रम (3).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्री
निष्क्री {c9c} U. To buy off, redeem,<BR>ransom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रयः|निष्क्रय
निष्क्रयः<BR>1 Redemption, ransom;<BR>ददौ दत्तं समुद्रेण पीतेनेवात्मनिष्क्रयं<BR>R. 15. 55; 2. 55, 5. 22;<BR>Mu. 6. 20.<BR>--2 Reward.<BR>--3 Hire, wages.<BR>--4 Return, acquittance; Śi. 1. 50.<BR>--5 Exchange, barter.<BR>--6 Sale.<BR>--7<BR>Purchase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रयणं|निष्क्रयण
निष्क्रयणं Redemption, ransom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्रीतिः|निष्क्रीति
निष्क्रीतिः f. Ved. Redemption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्क्वाथः|निष्क्वाथ
निष्क्वाथः<BR>1 Decoction.<BR>--2 Broth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टप्
निष्टप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To heat, scorch.<BR>--2 To purify.<BR>--3 To burnish.<BR>--4 To<BR>roast, fry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टपनं|निष्टपन
निष्टपनं Burning, scorching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टप्त
निष्टप्त p. p.<BR>1 Burnished.<BR>--2<BR>Welldressed or cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टापः|निष्टाप
निष्टापः Burning, slight heating;<BR>Māl. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टानकः|निष्टानक
निष्टानकः Roar, murmur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्टुर्
निष्टुर् m. Ved. A conqueror<BR>of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ट्य|निष्ट्यः
निष्ट्य a. Ved. Foreign, exotic.<BR>--ष्ट्यः An outcast, a Cāṇḍāla or<BR>Mleccha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठ|निष्ठः
निष्ठ a. [नि-स्था-क षत्वटुत्वे]<BR>(Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>1 Being<BR>in or on, situated on; तन्निष्ठे फेने.<BR>--2<BR>Depending or resting on, referring<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-b" target="_blank">Page0641-b+ 57</a>]<BR>or relating to; तमोनिष्ठाः Ms. 12. 95.<BR>--3 Devoted or attached to,<BR>practising, intent on; सत्यनिष्ठ.<BR>--4 Skilled<BR>in.<BR>--5 Believing in; धर्मनिष्ठ.<BR>--ष्ठा<BR>1<BR>Position, condition, state.<BR>--2 Basis,<BR>foundation.<BR>--3 Fixity, fixedness,<BR>steadiness; मनो निष्ठाशून्यं भ्रमति च<BR>किमप्यालिखति च Māl. 1. 31.<BR>--4<BR>Devotion or application, close<BR>attachment.<BR>--5 Belief, firm adherence,<BR>faith; शास्त्रेषु निष्ठा Māl. 3. 11;<BR>Bg. 3. 3.<BR>--6 Excellence, skill,<BR>proficiency, perfection.<BR>--7 Conclusion,<BR>end, termination; अत्यारूढिर्भवति<BR>महतामप्यपभ्रंशनिष्ठा Ś. 4. v. l.<BR>--8 The<BR>catastrophe or end of a drama.<BR>--9<BR>Accomplishment, completion (समाप्ति);<BR>Ms. 8. 227.<BR>--10 The culminating<BR>point.<BR>--11 Death, destruction,<BR>disappearance from the world at the<BR>fixed time.<BR>--12 Fixed or certain<BR>knowledge, certainty.<BR>--13 Begging.<BR>--14 Suffering, trouble, distress,<BR>anxiety.<BR>--15 (In gram.) A technical<BR>term for the past participial<BR>terminations क्त, क्तवतु (i. e. त and तवत्.)<BR>--16 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठाव
निष्ठाव a. Ved. Concluding,<BR>deciding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठित|निष्ठितं
निष्ठित p. p.<BR>1 Being in or on.<BR>--2<BR>Devoted to.<BR>--3 Versed or skilled<BR>in.<BR>--4 Firm, fixed.<BR>--5 Certain,<BR>ascertained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठानं|निष्ठान
निष्ठानं Sauce, condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निष्ठिव्
निष्ठिव् {c1c} {c4c} P.<BR>1 To eject, emit,<BR>send forth; Ś. 4. 4; R. 2. 75;<BR>Bk. 14. 100, 17. 10, 18. 14; Kāv. 1. 95.<BR>--2 To eject saliva from the mouth,<BR>spit; Ms. 4. 132; Y. 2. 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0641-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

