निस्रावः|निस्राव
निस्रवः, निस्रावः<BR>1 A stream,<BR>torrent.<BR>--2 The scum of boiled rice.<BR>--3<BR>Flowing forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वनः|निस्वन
निस्वनः, निस्वानः, निस्वनितं<BR>1 Noise,<BR>voice; R. 3. 19; Rs. 1. 8; Ki. 5. 6.<BR>--2 The whistling sound of an arrow<BR>(only निस्वान in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वानः|निस्वान
निस्वनः, निस्वानः, निस्वनितं<BR>1 Noise,<BR>voice; R. 3. 19; Rs. 1. 8; Ki. 5. 6.<BR>--2 The whistling sound of an arrow<BR>(only निस्वान in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निस्वनितं|निस्वनित
निस्वनः, निस्वानः, निस्वनितं<BR>1 Noise,<BR>voice; R. 3. 19; Rs. 1. 8; Ki. 5. 6.<BR>--2 The whistling sound of an arrow<BR>(only निस्वान in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहन्
निहन् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To kill, destroy;<BR>Bk. 2. 34, 6. 10; R. 11. 71;<BR>Y. 3. 262.<BR>--2 To strike, hit; तानेव<BR>सामर्षतया निजघ्नुः R. 7. 44; Ms. 7. 27.<BR>--3<BR>To conquer, overcome; दैवं निहत्य<BR>कुरु पौरुषमात्मशक्त्या Pt. 1. 361.<BR>--4<BR>To beat, strike (as a drum);<BR>Bk. 14. 2.<BR>--5 To counteract, oppose, render<BR>void, frustrate; R. 12. 92.<BR>--6 To<BR>cure (as a disease).<BR>--7 To disregard.<BR>--8 To remove, dispel; Ki. 5. 36.<BR>--9<BR>To strike in, infix.<BR>--10 (In gram.)<BR>To cut off, separate; अतिङंतात्<BR>पदात्पदं तिङंतं निहन्यते Sk. on<BR>P. VIII. 1. 28, 29, 30. --Caus. To kill, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहत
निहत p. p.<BR>1 Struck down, smitten,<BR>killed, slain.<BR>--2 Struck into, infixed.<BR>--3 Attached or devoted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहननं|निहनन
निहननं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहंतृ|निहन्तृ
निहंतृ a.<BR>1 A killer.<BR>--2<BR>Destructive, murderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहवः|निहव
निहवः Invocation, summoning,<BR>calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहिंसनं|निहिंसन
निहिंसनं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहाका
निहाका<BR>1 The Gangetic<BR>alligator.<BR>--2 A storm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहार|निहारः
निहार See नीहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहित|निहितं
निहित p. p.<BR>1 Placed, laid,<BR>lodged, situated, deposited.<BR>--2<BR>Delivered, entrusted.<BR>--3 Bestowed upon;<BR>applied to.<BR>--4 Inserted, infixed.<BR>--5<BR>Treasured up.<BR>--6 Held.<BR>--7 Laid (as<BR>dust).<BR>--8 Uttered in a deep tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निहीन|निहीनः
निहीन a. Low, vile.<BR>--नः A low<BR>man, one of vile origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नु
निह्नु {c2c} A.<BR>1 To hide, conceal;<BR>देव्या निह्नोतुमिच्छोरिति सुरसरितं Mu. 1. 1,<BR>Bk. 10. 36.<BR>--2 To deny or<BR>dissimulate before any one, to hide from<BR>(with dat.); Bk. 8. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नवः|निह्नव
निह्नवः<BR>1 Denial, concealment of<BR>knowledge; कार्यः स्वमतिनिह्नवः<BR>Māl. 1. 12; Chandr. 5. 27.<BR>--2 Secrecy,<BR>concealment in general; Y. 2. 11<BR>267.<BR>--3 A secret.<BR>--4 Mistrust; doubt,<BR>suspicion.<BR>--5 Wickedness.<BR>--6<BR>Atonement, expiation.<BR>--7 Excuse,<BR>exculpation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्तरं an evasive<BR>reply.<BR>--वादिन् m. a defendant or<BR>witness who prevaricates or gives<BR>evasive replies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नवनं|निह्नवन
निह्नवनं<BR>1 Denial or concealment<BR>of knowledge.<BR>--2 Excuse,<BR>exculpation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुत
निह्नुत p. p.<BR>1 Denied, disowned.<BR>--2 Concealed, dissembled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्नुतिः|निह्नुति
निह्नुतिः f.<BR>1 Denial, concealment<BR>of knowledge; Amaru. 8.<BR>--2<BR>Dissimulation, reserve.<BR>--3 Secrecy,<BR>concealment in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निह्रादः|निह्राद
निह्रादः A sound; cf. निर्थाद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
नी {c1c} U. (नयति-ते, निनाय निन्ये,<BR>अनैषीत-अनेष्ट, नेष्यति-ते, नेतुं, नीत) (One of<BR>the roots that govern two<BR>accusatives, see examples below)<BR>1 To carry,<BR>lead, bring, convey, take, conduct;<BR>अजां ग्रामं नयति Sk; नय मां नवेन वसतिं<BR>पयोमुचा V. 4. 43.<BR>--2 To guide, direct,<BR>govern; M. 1. 2.<BR>--3 To lead away<BR>to, carry or bring away; सीता लंकां<BR>नीता सुरारिणा Bk. 6. 49; R. 12. 103;<BR>Ms. 6. 88.<BR>--4 To carry off;<BR>Śānti. 3. 5.<BR>--5 To carry off for oneself<BR>(Atm).<BR>--6 To spend, or pass (as<BR>time); येनामंदमरंदे दलदरविंदे<BR>दिनान्यनायिषत Bv. 1. 10; नीत्वा मासान्<BR>कतिचित् Me. 2; संविष्टः कुशशयने निशां<BR>निनाय R. 1. 95.<BR>--7 To bring or reduce<BR>any person to any state or condition;<BR>तमपि तरलतामनयदनंगः K. 143;<BR>नीतस्त्वया पंचतां Ratn. 3. 3; R. 8. 19.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-a" target="_blank">Page0645-a+ 57</a>]<BR>(In this sense the root is used with<BR>substantives much in the same way<BR>as कृ q. v.; e. g. दुःखं नी to reduce to<BR>misery; वशं नी to reduce to subjection,<BR>win over; अस्तं नी to cause to set;<BR>विनाशं नी to destroy; परितोषं नी to<BR>gratify, please; शूद्रतां-दासत्वं &c. नी<BR>to reduce to the state of a Śūdra,<BR>slave &c.; साक्ष्यं नी to admit as a<BR>witness; दंडं नी to inflict<BR>punishment upon, to punish; पुनरुक्ततां नी<BR>to render superfluous; विक्रयं नी to<BR>sell; भस्मतां-भस्मसात्-नी to reduce to<BR>ashes &c. &c.).<BR>--8 To ascertain,<BR>investigate, inquire into, settle,<BR>decide; छलं निरस्य भूतेन व्यवहारान्नयेन्नृपः<BR>Y. 2. 19; एवं शास्त्रेषु भिन्नेषु बहुधा<BR>नीयते क्रिया Mb.<BR>--9 To trace, track,<BR>find out; एतैर्लिगैर्नयेत् सीमां<BR>Ms. 8. 252, 256; यथा नयत्यसृक्पातैर्मृगस्य<BR>मृगयुः पदं 8. 44; Y. 2. 151.<BR>--10 To<BR>marry.<BR>--11 To exclude from.<BR>--12<BR>(Atm.) To instruct, give<BR>instruction in; शास्त्रे नयते Sk. --Caus. (<BR>नाययति-ते) To cause to lead, carry &c.<BR>(with instr. of agent); तेन मां<BR>सरस्तीरमनाययत् K. 38. --Desid. (<BR>निनीषति-ते) To wish to carry &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0644-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नी
नी m. (Used at the end of comp.)<BR>A leader, guide; as in ग्रामणी, सेनानी,<BR>अग्रणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीत|नीतं
नीत p. p. [नी-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1 Carried,<BR>conducted, led.<BR>--2 Gained, obtained.<BR>--3 Brought or reduced to.<BR>--4 Spent,<BR>passed away.<BR>--5 Well-behaved,<BR>correct; see नी.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Wealth.<BR>--2 Corn,<BR>grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिः|नीति
नीतिः f.<BR>1 Guidance, direction,<BR>management.<BR>--2 Conduct, manner<BR>of conducting oneself, behaviour,<BR>course of action.<BR>--3 Propriety,<BR>decorum.<BR>--4 Policy, prudence, wisdom,<BR>right course; आर्जवं हि कुटिलेषु न<BR>नीतिः N. 5. 103; R. 12. 69; Ku. 1. 22.<BR>--5 A plan, contrivance, scheme;<BR>Māl. 6. 3.<BR>--6 Politics, political<BR>science, statesmanship, political<BR>wisdom; आत्मोदयः परग्लानिर्द्वयं<BR>नीतिरितीयती Śi. 2. 30; Bg. 10. 38.<BR>--7<BR>Righteousness, moral conduct,<BR>morality.<BR>--8 The science of morality,<BR>morals, ethics, moral philosophy.<BR>--9<BR>Acquirement, acquisition.<BR>--10<BR>Giving, offering, presenting.<BR>--11<BR>Relation, support.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कुशल, --ज्ञ,<BR>--निष्ण, विद् a. {1} one versed in<BR>policits, a statesman, politician. {2}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">Page0645-b+ 56</a>]<BR>prudent, wise.<BR>--घोषः N. of the car of<BR>Bṛhaspati.<BR>--दोषः error of conduct,<BR>mistake in policy.<BR>--बीजं a germ or<BR>source of intrigue; ˚निर्वापणं कृतं<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--विद्या {1} political science,<BR>political economy. {2} moral science, ethics.<BR>--विषयः the sphere of morality<BR>or prudent conduct.<BR>--व्यतिक्रमः<BR>transgression of the rules of<BR>moral or political science. {2} error<BR>of conduct, mistake in policy.<BR>--शास्त्रं the science of ethics or of<BR>politics; morality.<BR>--संधिः method<BR>of policy; Pt. 2. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीतिमत्|नीतिमन्त्
नीतिमत् a.<BR>1 Skilled in politics.<BR>--2 Wise, prudent, sagacious.<BR>--3<BR>Moral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीथः|नीथ
नीथः Ved.<BR>1 Leading, guiding.<BR>--2 A guide, leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीका
नीका A channel for irrigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीकारः|नीकार
नीकारः See निकार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीकाश|नीकाशः
नीकाश a. See निकाश; Śi. 5. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीक्षणं|नीक्षण
नीक्षणं Ved. A stick for stirring<BR>up and testing boiling rice (पाकपरी.<BR>क्षासाधन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीच|नीचः
नीच a. [निकृष्टतमीं शोभां चिनोति, चि-ड<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 Low, short, small, little,<BR>dwarfish.<BR>--2 Situated below, being<BR>in a low position; Bg. 6. 11;<BR>Ms. 2. 198; Y. 1. 131.<BR>--3 Lowered, deep<BR>(as a voice).<BR>--4 Low, mean, base,<BR>vile, worst; प्रारभ्यते न खलु विघ्नभयेन<BR>नीचैः Bh. 2. 27; नीचस्य गोचरगतैः<BR>सुखमास्यते कैः 59; Bv. 1. 48.<BR>--5<BR>Worthless, insignificant.<BR>--चा An<BR>excellent cow.<BR>--चं The lowest point<BR>of a planet.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः f. a low<BR>or vulgar expression.<BR>--उच्चवृत्तं an<BR>epicycle.<BR>--उपगत a. situated low in<BR>the sky.<BR>--ग a. {1} going<BR>downwards, descending (as a river). {2}<BR>low, base, vile.<BR>--(गा) a river.<BR>--(गं)<BR>water.<BR>--गृहं (in astr.) the part of<BR>the heavens in which a planet stands<BR>at its lower point.<BR>--भोज्यः onion.<BR>--योनिन् a. of low origin, low-born;<BR>so नीचजाति.<BR>--वज्रः, --ज्रं a kind of<BR>gem (वैक्रांत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचक|नीचकः
नीचक a.<BR>1 Low, short, dwarfish.<BR>--2 Low, soft (as the voice).<BR>--3 Base,<BR>mean, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचका
नीच(चि)का An excellent cow;<BR>(also नीचिकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचिका
नीच(चि)का An excellent cow;<BR>(also नीचिकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचकिन्
नीचकिन् m.<BR>1 The top of anything.<BR>--2 The head of an ox.<BR>--3 The owner<BR>of a good cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचकैस्
नीचकैस् ind. See नीचैस् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचा
नीचा ind. Ved. Low, downward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचीकृ
नीचीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To lower (as the<BR>voice).<BR>--2 To utter without an accent<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचीन
नीचीन a. Ved. Being low or below,<BR>downwards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीचैस्
नीचैस् ind. (Often used with the<BR>force of an adjective)<BR>1 Low,<BR>beneath, below, underneath, down.<BR>downwards; (opp. उपरि);<BR>नीचैर्गच्छत्युपरि च दशा चक्रनेमिक्रमेण Me. 109.<BR>--2 Bowing down humbly, modestly.<BR>R. 5. 62.<BR>--3 Gently, softly;<BR>नीचैर्वास्यति Me. 42.<BR>--4 In a low tone, with<BR>a low or depressed tone; नीचैः शंस<BR>हृदि स्थितो ननु स मे प्राणेश्वरः श्रोष्यति<BR>Amaru. 67; नीचैरनुदात्तः P. I. 2. 30,<BR>--5 Short, small, dwarfish; तथापि<BR>नीचैर्विनयाददृश्यत R. 3. 34. --m. N. of<BR>a mountain; नीचैराख्यं<BR>गिरिमधिवसेस्तत्र विश्रामहेतोः Me. 25.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गतिः f. slow pace.<BR>--मुख a. with<BR>downcast countenance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडः|नीड|नीडं
नीडः, --डं [नितरामिलंति खगा अत्र<BR>निइल्-क लस्यडः Tv.]<BR>1 A bird's nest;<BR>Ś. 7. 11.<BR>--2 A bed, couch.<BR>--3 A lair, den.<BR>--4 The interior of a carriage.<BR>--5 A<BR>place in general, abode, resting place<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्भवः, --जः a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडं|नीड|नीडः
नीडः, --डं [नितरामिलंति खगा अत्र<BR>निइल्-क लस्यडः Tv.]<BR>1 A bird's nest;<BR>Ś. 7. 11.<BR>--2 A bed, couch.<BR>--3 A lair, den.<BR>--4 The interior of a carriage.<BR>--5 A<BR>place in general, abode, resting place<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्भवः, --जः a bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीडकः|नीडक
नीडकः<BR>1 A bird.<BR>--2 A nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीध्रं|नीध्र
नीध्रं(व्रं) [नितरां ध्रियते धृ मूलवि˚<BR>क दीर्घः Tv.]<BR>1 The edge of the<BR>thatch or roof.<BR>--2 A wood.<BR>--3 The<BR>circumference of a wheel.<BR>--4 The<BR>moon.<BR>--5 The asterism रेवति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीव्रं|नीव्र
नीध्रं(व्रं) [नितरां ध्रियते धृ मूलवि˚<BR>क दीर्घः Tv.]<BR>1 The edge of the<BR>thatch or roof.<BR>--2 A wood.<BR>--3 The<BR>circumference of a wheel.<BR>--4 The<BR>moon.<BR>--5 The asterism रेवति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीप|नीपः
नीप a. Situated low, deep.<BR>--पः<BR>1 The foot of a mountain.<BR>--2 The<BR>Kadamba tree (said to blossom in<BR>the rainy season); नीपः प्रदीपायते<BR>Mk. 5. 14; सीमंते च त्वदुपगमजं यत्र<BR>नीपं वधूनां Me. 65.<BR>--3 A species of<BR>Aśoka.<BR>--4 N. of a family of kings;<BR>R. 6. 46.<BR>--पं The flower of the<BR>Kadamba tree; Me. 21; R. 19. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीरं|नीर
नीरं [Uṇ. 2. 13]<BR>1 Water;<BR>नीरान्निर्मलतो जनिः Bv. 1. 63.<BR>--2 Juice,<BR>liquor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. aquatic.<BR>--(जः) {1} an otter. {2} a kind of<BR>grass (उशीर.)<BR>--(जं) {1} a lotus. {2}<BR>a pearl.<BR>--दः a cloud; धीरध्वनिभिरलं<BR>ते नीरद मे मासिको गर्भः Bv. 1. 61;<BR>Śi. 4. 52.<BR>--धरः a cloud; U. 6. 17.<BR>--धिः, --निधिः the ocean.<BR>--प्रियः a<BR>kind of reed.<BR>--रुहं a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीराज्
नीराज् (निस्-राज्) Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>cause to shine, illuminate, make<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-a" target="_blank">Page0646-a+ 57</a>]<BR>brilliant, adorn, irradiate;<BR>दिव्यास्त्रस्फुरदुग्रदीधितिशिखानीराजितज्यं धनुः<BR>U. 6. 18; नीराजयंति भूपालाः<BR>पादपीठांतभूतलं Prab. 2; Śi. 17. 17.<BR>--2 To<BR>perform the ceremony called नीराजन<BR>(q. v. below) over a person or<BR>thing (wave lights before one as a<BR>mark of respect or by way of<BR>worship); नानायोधसमाकीर्णो<BR>नीराजितहयद्विपः Kām. 4. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0645-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीराजनं|नीराजन
नीराजनं, --ना<BR>1 Lustration of arms,<BR>a kind of military and religious<BR>ceremony performed by kings or<BR>generals of armies in the month of Āśvina<BR>before they took the field; (it was,<BR>so to say, a general purification of<BR>the king's Purohita, the ministers,<BR>and all the various component parts<BR>of the army, together with the<BR>arms and implements of war, by<BR>means of sacred Mantras);<BR>R. 4. 25, 17. 12; N. 1. 144.<BR>--2 Waving<BR>lights before an idol as an act of<BR>adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीराजना
नीराजनं, --ना<BR>1 Lustration of arms,<BR>a kind of military and religious<BR>ceremony performed by kings or<BR>generals of armies in the month of Āśvina<BR>before they took the field; (it was,<BR>so to say, a general purification of<BR>the king's Purohita, the ministers,<BR>and all the various component parts<BR>of the army, together with the<BR>arms and implements of war, by<BR>means of sacred Mantras);<BR>R. 4. 25, 17. 12; N. 1. 144.<BR>--2 Waving<BR>lights before an idol as an act of<BR>adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नील|नीलं|नीलः
नील a. (ला-ली f.; the former<BR>in relation to clothes &c., the latter<BR>in relation to animals, plants &c.)<BR>1 Blue, dark-blue; नीलस्निग्धः श्रयति<BR>शिखरं नूतनस्तोयवाहः U. 1. 33.<BR>--2<BR>Dyed with indigo.<BR>--लः<BR>1 The<BR>dark-blue or black colour.<BR>--2<BR>Sapphire.<BR>--3 The Indian fig-tree.<BR>--4<BR>N. of a monkey-chief in the army<BR>of Rāma.<BR>--5 ‘The blue mountain’,<BR>N. of one of the principal ranges<BR>of mountains.<BR>--6 A kind of bird,<BR>the blue Mainā.<BR>--7 An ox of a<BR>dark-blue colour.<BR>--8 One of the nine<BR>treasures of Kubera; see नवनिधि.<BR>--9<BR>A mark.<BR>--10 An auspicious sound or<BR>proclamation.<BR>--ला<BR>1 The indigo<BR>plant.<BR>--2 A Rāgiṇī.<BR>--ले f. du.<BR>1 The two arteries in front of the<BR>neck.<BR>--2 A black and blue mark on<BR>the skin; (for other senses see<BR>नीली.)<BR>--लं<BR>1 Black-salt.<BR>--2 Blue<BR>vitriol.<BR>--3 Antimony.<BR>--4 Poison.<BR>--5 Indigo, indigo dye.<BR>--6 Darkness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः a goose.<BR>--अंगः the<BR>Sārasa bird.<BR>--अंजनं {1} antimony. {2}<BR>blue vitriol.<BR>--अंजना, --अंजसा<BR>lightning.<BR>--अब्जं, --अंबुजं, --अंबुजन्मन् n.,<BR>उत्पलं the blue lotus.<BR>--अभ्रः a dark<BR>cloud.<BR>--अंबर a. dressed in dark<BR>blue clothes.<BR>--(रः) {1} a demon.<BR>goblin. {2} the planet Saturn. {3}<BR>an epithet of Balarāma.<BR>--अरुणः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-b" target="_blank">Page0646-b+ 56</a>]<BR>early dawn, the first dawn of day.<BR>--अश्मन् m. a sapphire.<BR>--उपलः<BR>the blue stone, lapis lazuli.<BR>--कंठः {1} a peacock;<BR>Māl. 9. 30; Me. 79. {2} an epithet of Śiva. {3}<BR>a kind of gallinule. {4} a<BR>blue-necked jay. {5} a wag-tail. {6} a sparrow.<BR>{7} a bee.<BR>--(ठं) a radish. ˚अक्ष = रुद्राक्ष<BR>q. v.<BR>--केशी the indigo plant.<BR>--ग्रीवः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--छदः {1} the<BR>date-tree. {2} an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR>--जं blue steel.<BR>--तरुः the<BR>cocoanut tree.<BR>--तालः, --ध्वजः the Tamāla<BR>tree.<BR>--पंकः, --कं darkness.<BR>--पटलं {1}<BR>a dark mass, a black coating or<BR>covering. {2} a dark film over the<BR>eye of a blind man; Pt. 5.<BR>--पत्रः<BR>the pomegranate tree. (--त्रं) --पद्मं<BR>the blue water-lily.<BR>--पिच्छः a<BR>falcon.<BR>--पुष्पिका {1} the indigo plant.<BR>{2} linseed.<BR>--भः {1} the moon.<BR>{2} a cloud. {3} a bee.<BR>--मणिः, --रत्नं<BR>{1} the sapphire; नेपथ्योचितनीलरत्नं<BR>Gīt. 5; Bv. 2. 42. {2} an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; also नीलमाधवः.<BR>--मीलिकः<BR>a fire-fly.<BR>--मृत्तिका {1} iron pyrites.<BR>{2} black earth.<BR>--राजिः f. a line of<BR>darkness, dark mass, thick<BR>darkness,; निशाशशांकक्षतनीलराजयः<BR>Rs. 1. 2.<BR>--लोहित a. dark-blue, purple.<BR>--(तः) {1} a purple colour. {2} an<BR>epithet of Śiva; Ś. 7. 35; Ku. 2. 57.<BR>--वर्ण<BR>a. dark-blue, bluish.<BR>--(र्णं) a radish.<BR>--वसन, --वासस् a. dressed in<BR>darkblue clothes; see नीलांबर.<BR>--वृंतकं<BR>cotton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलकं|नीलक|नीलकः
नीलकं<BR>1 Black salt.<BR>--2 Blue steel.<BR>--3 Blue vitriol.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>darkcoloured horse.<BR>--2 (In alg.) The<BR>third unknown quantity<BR>(corresponding to z of European Algebra).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलंगुः|नीलङ्गु|नीलंगु|नीलङ्गुः
नीलं(लां)गुः<BR>1 A kind of insect.<BR>--2 An insect in general.<BR>--3 A kind<BR>of fly.<BR>--4 A jackal.<BR>--5 A large<BR>(black) bee.<BR>--6 A flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलांगुः|नीलाङ्गु|नीलांगु|नीलाङ्गुः
नीलं(लां)गुः<BR>1 A kind of insect.<BR>--2 An insect in general.<BR>--3 A kind<BR>of fly.<BR>--4 A jackal.<BR>--5 A large<BR>(black) bee.<BR>--6 A flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलति
नीलति Den. P.<BR>1 To be of a<BR>darkblue colour.<BR>--2 To dye blue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलिका
नीलिका The indigo plant; (also<BR>नीलिनी). See नीला also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीलिमन्
नीलिमन् m. Blue colour, darkness,<BR>blueness; Māl. 5. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीली
नीली<BR>1 The indigo plant; तत्र<BR>नीलीरसपरिपूर्णं महाभांडमासीत् Pt. 1; एको<BR>ग्रहस्तु मीनानां नीलीमद्यपयोर्यथा<BR>Pt. 1. 260.<BR>--2 A species of blue fly.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of disease.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--राग a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">Page0646-c+ 55</a>]<BR>firm in attachment.<BR>--(गः) {1}<BR>affection as unchangeable as the colour<BR>of indigo, unalterable or<BR>unswerving attachment. {2} a firm and<BR>constant friend.<BR>--संधानं fermentation<BR>of indigo. ˚भांडं an indigo vat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवरः|नीवर
नीवरः [Uṇ. 3. 1.]<BR>1 Trade,<BR>traffic.<BR>--2 A trader.<BR>--3 A religious<BR>mendicant.<BR>--4 A place fit for the<BR>site of a house.<BR>--5 A dwelling,<BR>residence.<BR>--6 Mud.<BR>--रं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवाकः|नीवाक
नीवाकः<BR>1 Increased demand for<BR>grain in times of dearth.<BR>--2 Famine,<BR>scarcity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवारः|नीवार
नीवारः Rice growing wild or<BR>without cultivation; नीवाराः<BR>शुकगर्भकोटरमुखभ्रष्टास्तरूणामधः Ś. 1. 14,<BR>R. 1. 50, 5. 9, 15; (also नीवारक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीविः|नीवि
नीविः, --वी f. [निव्ययति निवीयते वा<BR>निव्ये-इन्; cf. Uṇ. 4. 135]<BR>1 A cloth<BR>worn round a woman's waist, or<BR>more properly the ends of the cloth<BR>tied into a knot in front, the knot<BR>of the wearing garment;<BR>प्रस्थानभिन्नां न बबंध नीविं R. 7. 9;<BR>नीविबंधोच्छ्वसनं Māl. 2. 5; Ku. 1. 38; नीवि<BR>प्रति प्रणिहिते तु करे प्रियेण K. P. 4;<BR>Me. 68; Śi. 10. 64.<BR>--2 The outer tie<BR>of a packet in which the offerings<BR>of a Śūdra at funeral obsequies are<BR>presented.<BR>--3 Capital, principal,<BR>stock.<BR>--4 A stake, wager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवी
नीविः, --वी f. [निव्ययति निवीयते वा<BR>निव्ये-इन्; cf. Uṇ. 4. 135]<BR>1 A cloth<BR>worn round a woman's waist, or<BR>more properly the ends of the cloth<BR>tied into a knot in front, the knot<BR>of the wearing garment;<BR>प्रस्थानभिन्नां न बबंध नीविं R. 7. 9;<BR>नीविबंधोच्छ्वसनं Māl. 2. 5; Ku. 1. 38; नीवि<BR>प्रति प्रणिहिते तु करे प्रियेण K. P. 4;<BR>Me. 68; Śi. 10. 64.<BR>--2 The outer tie<BR>of a packet in which the offerings<BR>of a Śūdra at funeral obsequies are<BR>presented.<BR>--3 Capital, principal,<BR>stock.<BR>--4 A stake, wager.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीवृत्
नीवृत् m. Any inhabited country,<BR>realm, kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीव्र|नीव्रं
नीव्र See नीध्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीशारः|नीशार
नीशारः [नि-शॄ घञ् दीर्घः]<BR>1 A<BR>warm cloth, a blanket.<BR>--2 A<BR>mosquito-curtain.<BR>--3 An outer tent or<BR>screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नीहारः|नीहार
नीहारः [नि-हृ कर्मणि घञ् दीर्घः]<BR>1<BR>Fog, mist; R. 7. 60; Y. 1. 150;<BR>Ms. 4. 113.<BR>--2 Hoar-frost, heavy<BR>dew.<BR>--3 Evacuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु ind.<BR>1 A particle having an<BR>interrogative force and implying<BR>some ‘doubt’, or ‘uncertainty’;<BR>स्वप्नो नु माया नु मतिभ्रमो नु Ś. 6. 9;<BR>अस्तशैलगहनं नु विवस्वानाविवेश जलधिं<BR>नु महीं नु Ki. 9. 7; 5. 1; 8. 53,<BR>9. 15, 54; 13. 4; Ku. 1. 46;<BR>Śi. 10. 14; Ś. 2. 9.<BR>--2 It is very often<BR>compounded with the interrogative<BR>pronoun and its derivatives in the sense<BR>of ‘possibly’, ‘indeed’; किं<BR>न्वेतत्स्यात्किमन्यदितोऽथवा Māl. 1. 17; कथंनु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">Page0647-a+ 56</a>]<BR>गुणवद्विंदेयं कलत्रं Dk; see किंनु also.<BR>--3<BR>Ved. Now, even now.<BR>--4 Now<BR>therefore, now then, therefore.<BR>--5 Like,<BR>as.<BR>--6 Quickly.<BR>--7 From this time<BR>forward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0646-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नु|नुः
नु {c2c} P. (नौति, प्रणौति; नुत; caus.<BR>नावयति; desid. नुनूषति)<BR>1 To praise,<BR>extol, commend; सरस्वती तन्मिथुनं<BR>नुनाव Ku. 7. 90; Bk. 14. 112; see नू.<BR>--2 To roar, cry.<BR>--3 To sound, shout.<BR>II. {c1c} A. (नवते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुत|नुतं
नु(नू)त p. p. Praised, extolled<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूत|नूतः
नु(नू)त p. p. Praised, extolled<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुः|नु
नुः f. Praise. --m.<BR>1 A weapon.<BR>--2<BR>Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुतिः|नुति
नुतिः f.<BR>1 Praise, eulogium,<BR>panegyric; परगुणनुतिभिः (v. l.) स्वान्<BR>गुणान् ख्यापयंतः Bh. 2. 69.<BR>--2 Worship,<BR>reverence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुड्
नुड् {c6c} P. (नुडति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुद्
नुद्^1 {c6c} U. (नुदति-ते, नुत्त or नुन्न,<BR>प्रणुदते)<BR>1 To push, push or drive on,<BR>impel, propel; मंदं मंदं नुदति<BR>पवनश्चानुकूलो यथा त्वां Me. 9; U. 5. 1.<BR>--2<BR>To prompt, incite, urge on;<BR>Śi. 11. 26; Ku. 6. 65.<BR>--3 To remove, drive<BR>away, cast away, dispel; अदस्त्वया<BR>नुन्नमनुत्तमं तमः Śi. 1. 27;<BR>केयूरबंधोच्छ्वसितैर्नुनोद R. 6. 68, 8. 40; 16. 85;<BR>Ki. 3. 33.; 5. 28.<BR>--4 To throw, cast,<BR>send.<BR>--5 Ved. To raise, lift up.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To remove, drive away.<BR>--2 To prompt, incite, push on or<BR>urge forward. WITH उप to drive<BR>away, remove; Śi. 4. 61.<BR>--प्र to<BR>dispel, drive off, remove; Śi. 9. 71.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: verb missing virama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुत्त|नुत्तः
नुत्त(न्न) p. p.<BR>1 Pushed, driven<BR>onward, propelled &c.<BR>--2 Driven<BR>away, dispelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुन्न|नुन्नः
नुत्त(न्न) p. p.<BR>1 Pushed, driven<BR>onward, propelled &c.<BR>--2 Driven<BR>away, dispelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नुद
नुद a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Pushing, impelling, driving away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नू
नू {c6c} P. (नुवति) To praise &c.; see नु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूतन|नूतनः
नूतन, नूत्न a. [नव एव स्वार्थे तनप्<BR>नुरादेशश्च]<BR>1 New; नूतनो राजा<BR>समाज्ञापयति U. 1; R. 8. 15.<BR>--2 Fresh, young.<BR>--3 Present.<BR>--4 Instantaneous.<BR>--5<BR>Recent, modern.<BR>--6 Curious, strange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूत्न|नूत्नः
नूतन, नूत्न a. [नव एव स्वार्थे तनप्<BR>नुरादेशश्च]<BR>1 New; नूतनो राजा<BR>समाज्ञापयति U. 1; R. 8. 15.<BR>--2 Fresh, young.<BR>--3 Present.<BR>--4 Instantaneous.<BR>--5<BR>Recent, modern.<BR>--6 Curious, strange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूतनयति
नूतनयति Den. P. To make new,<BR>renew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूनं|नून
नूनं ind.<BR>1 Certainly, assuredly,<BR>surely, verily, indeed; अद्यापि नूनं<BR>हरकोपवह्निस्त्वयि ज्वलत्यौर्व इवांबुराशौ<BR>Ś. 3. 3; Me. 9, 18, 46; Bh. 1. 11;<BR>Ku. 1. 12, 5. 75; R. 1. 29.<BR>--2<BR>Most probably, in all probability.<BR>U. 4. 23.<BR>--3 Ved. Now; just now,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-b" target="_blank">Page0647-b+ 56</a>]<BR>just.<BR>--4 Immediately.<BR>--5 In future.<BR>--6 Now then, therefore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूपुरः|नूपुर|नूपुरं
नूपुरः --रं An anklet, an ornament<BR>for the feet; न हि चूडामणिः पादे नूपुरं<BR>मूर्ध्नि धार्यते H. 2. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नूपुरं|नूपुर|नूपुरः
नूपुरः --रं An anklet, an ornament<BR>for the feet; न हि चूडामणिः पादे नूपुरं<BR>मूर्ध्नि धार्यते H. 2. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृ
नृ [नी-ऋन् डिच्च; cf. Uṇ. 2. 101]<BR>(Nom. sing. ना, gen. pl. नृणां or नॄणां)<BR>1 A man, a person whether male or<BR>female; Ms. 3. 81; 4. 61, 7. 61, 10. 33.<BR>--2 Mankind.<BR>--3 A piece at chess.<BR>--4 The pin of a sun-dial.<BR>--5 A<BR>masculine word; संधिर्ना विग्रहो यानं Ak.<BR>--6 A leader.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अस्थिमालिन्<BR>m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--कपालं man's<BR>skull.<BR>--केसरिन् m. ‘man-lion’,<BR>Viṣṇu in his Narasiṃha incarnation;<BR>cf. नरसिंह.<BR>--चक्षस् a. Ved. {1}<BR>seeing or observing men. {2} leading<BR>or guiding men. (--m.) {1} a god.<BR>{2} a demon, goblin.<BR>--जलं human<BR>urine.<BR>--देवः a king.<BR>--धर्मन् m. an<BR>epithet of Kubera.<BR>--नमन a. to be<BR>saluted by men (as gods).<BR>--पः [नॄन्<BR>पाति रक्षति, पा-क] a ruler of men,<BR>king, sovereign. ˚अंशः {1} royal<BR>portion or revenue, i. e. a sixth, eighth<BR>&c. part of grain. {2} a prince.<BR>˚अंगनं (णं) a royal court. ˚अध्वरः N.<BR>of a sacrifice (Rājasūya)<BR>performed by an emperor or lord<BR>paramount, in which all the offices are<BR>performed by tributary princes.<BR>˚आत्मजः a prince, crown-prince.<BR>˚आभीरं, ˚मानं music played at<BR>the royal meals. ˚आमयः<BR>consumption. ˚आसनं ‘royal-seat’, a<BR>throne, the chair of state. ˚गृहं a<BR>royal palace. ˚नीतिः f. politics, royal<BR>policy, state-craft; वेश्यांगनेव<BR>नृपनीतिरनेकरूपा Bh. 2. 47. ˚प्रियः the<BR>mango tree. ˚लक्ष्मन् n., ˚लिंगं a<BR>royal symbol, an emblem of<BR>royalty, any one of the royal<BR>insignia; particularly, the white<BR>umbrella. ˚लिंगधर a. {1} assuming the<BR>insignia of royalty. {2} assuming the<BR>royal insignia (as a disguise).<BR>˚वल्लभः {1} the friend or favourite of<BR>a king. {2} a kind of mango.<BR>--(भा)<BR>a queen. ˚शासनं a royal grant or<BR>edict. ˚संश्रय a. seeking the<BR>protection of a king. ˚सुता the musk-rat.<BR>˚सभं, ˚सभा an assembly of kings.<BR>--पतिः --पालः {1} a king. {2} N. of<BR>Kubera. {3} a Kṣatriya. ˚पथः a<BR>royal or main road.<BR>--पशुः a beast<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">Page0647-c+ 57</a>]<BR>in the form of a man, a brute of a<BR>man; Bv. 4. 38.<BR>--पीतिः f. Ved.<BR>protection of men.<BR>--मिथुतं the sign<BR>Gemini (twins) of the zodiac.<BR>--मेधः a human sacrifice.<BR>--यज्ञः ‘the<BR>sacrifice to be offered to men’,<BR>hospitality, reception of guests (one of<BR>the five daily Yajñas; see पंचयज्ञ).<BR>--युग्मं = नृभिथुन q. v.<BR>--लोकः the<BR>world of mortals, the earth.<BR>--वराहः<BR>Viṣṇu in the boar-incarnation.<BR>--वाहनः an epithet of Kubera.<BR>--वेष्टनः N. of Śiva.<BR>--शृंगं ‘man's horn’;<BR>i. e. an impossibility.<BR>--सदनं (नृषदनं)<BR>the hall of sacrifice.<BR>--सद् (षद्) m.<BR>the Supreme Being.<BR>--सिंहः, --हरिः {1}<BR>‘a lion-like man’, a chief among<BR>men, an eminent or distinguished<BR>man. {2} Viṣṇu in his fourth<BR>incarnation; cf. नरसिंह. {3} a particular<BR>mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR>--सेनं,<BR>सेना an army of men.<BR>--सोमः an<BR>illustrious man, great man; R. 5. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृम्ण|नृम्णः
नृम्ण a. Making happy.<BR>--म्णः An<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--म्णं Ved.<BR>1<BR>Manhood, strength.<BR>--2 Courage.<BR>--3 Wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृवत्|नृवन्त्
नृवत् ind. Ved.<BR>1 Manly,<BR>powerfully.<BR>--2 Excessively, plentifully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृगः|नृग
नृगः A son of Manu Vaivasvata,<BR>who, it is said, was cursed by a<BR>Brāhmaṇa to be a lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्
नृत् {c4c} P. (नृत्यति, प्रणृत्यति, नृत्त)<BR>1<BR>To dance, move about; नृत्यति<BR>युवतिजनेन समं सखि Gīt. 1; लोलोर्मौ पयसि<BR>महोत्पलं ननर्त Śi. 8. 23; Bk. 3. 43.<BR>--2 To act on the stage.<BR>--3 To<BR>gesticulate, play. --Caus. (नर्तयति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to dance; त्वमाशे मोघाशे<BR>किमपरमतो नर्तयसि मां Bh. 3. 6; तालैः<BR>शिंजावलयसुभगैर्नर्तितः कांतया मे<BR>Me. 79, U. 3. 19.<BR>--2 To cause to move.<BR>--WITH आ (caus.) {1} to cause to<BR>dance. {2} to cause to dance or<BR>move quickly, shake;<BR>मरुद्भिरानर्तितनक्तमाले R. 5. 42; Amaru. 32;<BR>Rs. 3. 10.<BR>--प्र to dance &c.<BR>--प्रति to<BR>ridicule by dancing in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृतू
नृतू a. Ved.<BR>1 Dancing.<BR>--2<BR>Desstroying or injuring men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृतिः|नृति
नृतिः f. Dancing, dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृतुः|नृतु
नृतुः Ved.<BR>1 A dancer, an actor.<BR>--2 The earth.<BR>--3 A worm.<BR>--4<BR>Length.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्तं|नृत्त
नृत्तं, नृत्यं Dancing, acting, a<BR>dance, pantomime, gesticulation,<BR>नृत्तादस्याः स्थितमतितरां कांतं M. 2. 7;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">Page0648-a+ 55</a>]<BR>नृत्यं मयूरा विजहुः R. 14. 69; Me. 32,<BR>36; R. 3. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रियः {1} an<BR>epithet of Śiva. {2} a peacock.<BR>--शाला a dancing hall.<BR>--स्थानं a<BR>stage, dancing room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृत्यं|नृत्य
नृत्तं, नृत्यं Dancing, acting, a<BR>dance, pantomime, gesticulation,<BR>नृत्तादस्याः स्थितमतितरां कांतं M. 2. 7;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">Page0648-a+ 55</a>]<BR>नृत्यं मयूरा विजहुः R. 14. 69; Me. 32,<BR>36; R. 3. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रियः {1} an<BR>epithet of Śiva. {2} a peacock.<BR>--शाला a dancing hall.<BR>--स्थानं a<BR>stage, dancing room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0647-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृप|नृपः
नृप, नृपति, नृपाल &c. See under नृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपति|नृपतिः
नृप, नृपति, नृपाल &c. See under नृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृपाल|नृपालः
नृप, नृपति, नृपाल &c. See under नृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृशंस|नृशंसः
नृशंस a. [नॄन् शंसति हिंसति शंस्-अण्]<BR>1 Wicked, malicious, cruel,<BR>mischievous, base; Mk. 3. 25;<BR>Ms. 3. 41; Y. 1. 164.<BR>--2 Ved. To be praised<BR>by men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नृशंस्य
नृशंस्य a. Wicked, malicious.<BR>--स्यं<BR>Maliciousness, wickedness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेजकः|नेजक
नेजकः A washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेजनं|नेजन
नेजनं Washing, cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेतृ
नेतृ m. [नी-तृच्]<BR>1 One who<BR>leads or guides, a leader, conductor,<BR>manager, guide (of elephants,<BR>animals &c.); R. 4. 75, 14. 22, 16. 30;<BR>Me. 69; नेताश्वस्य स्रुध्नं स्रुघ्नस्य वा Sk.;<BR>Mu. 7. 14.<BR>--2 A director, preceptor;<BR>Bh. 2. 88.<BR>--3 A chief, master,<BR>head.<BR>--4 An inflictor (as of<BR>punishment); Ms. 7. 25.<BR>--5 An owner.<BR>--6 The hero of a drama.<BR>--7 The<BR>numeral ‘two’.<BR>--8 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्री
नेत्री<BR>1 A river.<BR>--2 A female<BR>leader.<BR>--3 An epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>--4<BR>An artery, a vein.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रं|नेत्र
नेत्रं [नयति नीयते वा अनेन नी-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>1<BR>Leading, conducting.<BR>--2 The eye;<BR>प्रायेण गृहिणीनेत्राः कन्यार्थेषु कुटुंबिनः<BR>Ku. 6. 85, 2. 29, 30; 7. 13.<BR>--3 The<BR>string of a churning-stick.<BR>--4<BR>Woven silk, a fine silken garment;<BR>नेत्रक्रमेणोपरुरोध सूर्यं R. 7. 39 (where<BR>some commentators take नेत्रं in its<BR>ordinary sense of the ‘eye’).<BR>--5<BR>The root of a tree.<BR>--6 An<BR>enemapipe.<BR>--7 A carriage, conveyance in<BR>general.<BR>--8 The number ‘two’.<BR>--9<BR>A leader.<BR>--10 A constellation, star<BR>(said to be. m. only in these two<BR>senses).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजनं a<BR>collyrium for the eyes; Ś. Til. 7.<BR>--अंतः<BR>the outer corner of the eye.<BR>--अंबु,<BR>--अंभस् n. tears.<BR>--अभिष्यंदः running<BR>of the eyes, a kind of eye-disease.<BR>--आमयः ophthalmia.<BR>--उत्सवः<BR>any pleasing or beautiful object.<BR>--उपमं the almond fruit.<BR>--औषधं<BR>collyrium.<BR>--कनीनिका the pupil of<BR>the eye.<BR>--कोषः {1} the eye-ball. {2}<BR>the bud of a flower.<BR>--गोचर a.<BR>within the range of sight,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">Page0648-b+ 55</a>]<BR>perceptible, visible.<BR>--छदः the eyelid.<BR>--जं, --जलं, --वारि n. tears.<BR>--पर्यंत a.<BR>as far as the eye, up to the eye.<BR>--(तः) the outer corner of the eye.<BR>--पिंडः {1} the eye-ball. {2} a cat.<BR>--मलं the mucus of the eyes.<BR>--मुष्<BR>a. stealing or captivating the eye.<BR>--योनिः {1} an epithet of Indra (who<BR>had on his body a thousand marks<BR>resembling the female organ<BR>inflicted by the curse of Gautama). {2}<BR>the moon.<BR>--रंजनं a collyrium.<BR>--रोमन् n. the eyelash.<BR>--वस्तिः m. f. a<BR>clyster-pipe with a bag.<BR>--वस्त्रं a<BR>veil over the eye, the eyelid.<BR>--विष्<BR>f. excretion of the eyes.<BR>--स्तंभः<BR>rigidity of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्रिकं|नेत्रिक
नेत्रिकं<BR>1 A pipe.<BR>--2 A ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेत्री
नेत्री See under नेतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेद्
नेद् {c1c} P. (नेदति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To<BR>censure.<BR>--3 To bring near.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदिष्ठ|नेदिष्ठं
नेदिष्ठ a. Nearest, next, very near<BR>(superl. of अंतिक q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेदीयस्
नेदीयस् a. (सी f.) Nearer, very<BR>near (compar. of अंतिक q. v.);<BR>नेदीयसि प्रियतमे Bv. 2. 6; नेदीयसी भूत्वा<BR>Māl. 1 ‘drawing near, approaching’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपः|नेप
नेपः A family-priest.<BR>--पं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपथ्यं|नेपथ्य
नेपथ्यं<BR>1 Decoration, an ornament.<BR>--2 Dress, apparel, costume, attire;<BR>उदारनेपथ्यभृत् R. 6. 6;<BR>राजेंद्रनेपथ्यविधानशोभा 14. 9; उज्ज्वलनेपथ्यविरचना<BR>Māl. 1; Ku. 7. 7; V. 5.<BR>--3<BR>Particularly, the costume of an actor;<BR>विरलनेपथ्ययोः पात्रयोः प्रवेशोस्तु M. 1.<BR>--4<BR>The tiring-room, the space where<BR>the actors attire themselves (which<BR>is always behind the curtain), the<BR>postscenium; नेपथ्ये ‘behind the<BR>scenes’.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विधानं arrangements<BR>of the tiring-room; यदि<BR>नेपथ्यविधानमवसितं Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपालः|नेपाल
नेपालः N. of a country in the<BR>north of India.<BR>--लाः pl. The people<BR>of this country.<BR>--लं Copper.<BR>--ली<BR>1 The wild date tree or its fruit.<BR>--2<BR>Red arsenic.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जा --जाता<BR>red arsenic.<BR>--मूलकं a radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपालकं|नेपालक
नेपालकं Copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेपालिका
नेपालिका Red arsenic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेम|नेमः
नेम a. (Nom. pl. नेमे-नेमाः) Half.<BR>--मः<BR>1 A part.<BR>--2 A period, time,<BR>season.<BR>--3 A boundary, limit.<BR>--4<BR>An enclosure, fence.<BR>--5 The<BR>foundation of a wall.<BR>--6 Fraud, deceit.<BR>--7<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">Page0648-c+ 54</a>]<BR>Evening.<BR>--8 A hole, ditch.<BR>--9 A<BR>root.<BR>--10 Acting, dancing.<BR>--11<BR>Upper part.<BR>--12 Ved. Food.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धित a. Ved. divided.<BR>--धितिः f.<BR>Ved. {1} a battle, conflict. {2}<BR>dividing into two.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमिः|नेमि
नेमिः --मी f.<BR>1 The<BR>circumference, ring or felly of a wheel;<BR>उपोढशब्दा न रथांगनेमयः Ś. 7. 10;<BR>चक्रनेमिक्रमेण Me. 109; R. 1. 17, 39.<BR>--2<BR>Edge, rim.<BR>--3 A windlass.<BR>--4 A<BR>circumference (in general); उदधिनेमि<BR>R. 9. 10.<BR>--5 A thunderbolt.<BR>--6 The<BR>earth.<BR>--मिः The tree तिनिश.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वृत्ति a. following the course of,<BR>acting like, the outer rims of the<BR>wheel; R. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेमी
नेमिः --मी f.<BR>1 The<BR>circumference, ring or felly of a wheel;<BR>उपोढशब्दा न रथांगनेमयः Ś. 7. 10;<BR>चक्रनेमिक्रमेण Me. 109; R. 1. 17, 39.<BR>--2<BR>Edge, rim.<BR>--3 A windlass.<BR>--4 A<BR>circumference (in general); उदधिनेमि<BR>R. 9. 10.<BR>--5 A thunderbolt.<BR>--6 The<BR>earth.<BR>--मिः The tree तिनिश.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वृत्ति a. following the course of,<BR>acting like, the outer rims of the<BR>wheel; R. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्
नेष् {c1c} A. (नेषते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्टुः|नेष्टु
नेष्टुः A clod of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नेष्टृ
नेष्टृ m. One of the chief<BR>officiating priests at a Soma sacrifice<BR>(whose number is 16).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःश्रेयस
नैःश्रेयस a. (सी f.), नैःश्रेयसिक a.<BR>(की f.) Leading to happiness or<BR>final beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःस्वं|नैःस्व
नैःस्वं, नैःस्व्यं Destitution, poverty,<BR>indigence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैःस्व्यं|नैःस्व्य
नैःस्वं, नैःस्व्यं Destitution, poverty,<BR>indigence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैक|नैकः
नैक a. (न-एक) Not one or alone;<BR>mostly in comp.; ˚आत्मन् m., ˚रूपः,<BR>˚शृगः epithets of the Supreme Being.<BR>--कः An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चर a. living in society, gregarious.<BR>--भावाश्रय a. fickle, changeable.<BR>--भेद a. manifold, various. See<BR>under न also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकधा
नैकधा ind. In various ways,<BR>variously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकशस्
नैकशस् ind.<BR>1 In great numbers.<BR>--2 Repeatedly, often, frequently.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकटिक|नैकटिकः
नैकटिक a. (की f.) Adjacent,<BR>near, contiguous.<BR>--कः An ascetic or<BR>Bhikṣu; Bk. 4. 12 (vide<BR>commentary).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकट्यं|नैकट्य
नैकट्यं Proximity,<BR>neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकषेयः|नैकषेय
नैकषेयः A demon, Rākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैकृतिक
नैकृतिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Dishonest,<BR>false (or perhaps cruel);<BR>Ms. 4. 196.<BR>--2 Low, vile, wicked.<BR>--3<BR>Morose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0648-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नैगम|नैगमः
