परिकर्षः, --कर्षणं Dragging out,<BR>extraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्षणं|परिकर्षण
परिकर्षः, --कर्षणं Dragging out,<BR>extraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकर्षित
परिकर्षित a.<BR>1 Dragged about.<BR>--2<BR>Harassed, tortured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकॄ
परिकॄ {c6c} P.<BR>1 To surround;<BR>परिकीर्णा परिवादिनी मुनेः R. 8. 35.<BR>--2 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">Page0671-b+ 56</a>]<BR>hand or give over, deliver; महीं<BR>महेच्छः परिकीर्य सूनौ R. 18. 33.<BR>--3 To<BR>scatter about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्ण
परिकीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Spread, diffused,<BR>scattered about.<BR>--2 Surrounded,<BR>crowded with, filled; Śi. 16. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकॄत्
परिकॄत् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To relate,<BR>narrate, proclaim, announce.<BR>--2 To<BR>praise, extol.<BR>--3 To name, call.<BR>--4<BR>To propound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्तनं|परिकीर्तन|परिकीर्त्तन
परिकीर्तनं<BR>1 Proclaiming, saying,<BR>talking of.<BR>--2 Boasting.<BR>--3 Naming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकीर्तित|परिकीर्त्तित
परिकीर्तित p. p.<BR>1 Proclaimed,<BR>announced.<BR>--2 Boasted of.<BR>--3 Said,<BR>declared to be.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकॢप्
परिकॢप् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To tend to.<BR>--2<BR>To give, grant, vouchsafe;<BR>U. 5. 27.<BR>--3 To think. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>decide, determine.<BR>--2 To fix upon,<BR>design, make or turn into; Ku. 1. 2.<BR>--3 To prepare, get ready.<BR>--4 To<BR>ondow with; Ś. 2. 9.<BR>--5 To destine for.<BR>--6 To perform, effect, accomplish.<BR>--7 To contrive, invent, devise.<BR>--8<BR>To distribute.<BR>--9 To invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पनं|परिकल्पन
परिकल्पनं --ना<BR>1 Settling, fixing,<BR>deciding, determining.<BR>--2<BR>Contriving, inventing, forming,<BR>arranging; Mu. 7. 15.<BR>--3 Providing,<BR>furnishing.<BR>--4 Distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पना
परिकल्पनं --ना<BR>1 Settling, fixing,<BR>deciding, determining.<BR>--2<BR>Contriving, inventing, forming,<BR>arranging; Mu. 7. 15.<BR>--3 Providing,<BR>furnishing.<BR>--4 Distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकल्पित
परिकल्पित p. p.<BR>1 Settled, decided.<BR>--2 Made, invented.<BR>--3 Got ready,<BR>prepared.<BR>--4 Contrived, arranged.<BR>--5 Distributed.<BR>--6 Provided,<BR>furnished with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिकोपः|परिकोप
परिकोपः Great anger, fury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रम्
परिक्रम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To walk about,<BR>walk around; परिक्रम्यावलोक्य च (in<BR>dramas).<BR>--2 To overtake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रमः|परिक्रम
परिक्रमः<BR>1 Roaming about,<BR>moving about; Ki. 10. 2.<BR>--2 Roaming,<BR>walking or passing over.<BR>--3<BR>Circumambulating.<BR>--4 Walking for<BR>pleasure.<BR>--5 Series, order.<BR>--6<BR>Succession.<BR>--7 Penetrating.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सहः a goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रांत|परिक्रान्त
परिक्रांत p. p. Walked round.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The place on which any one has<BR>walked about.<BR>--2 A foot-step,<BR>footprint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रांतिः|परिक्रान्ति|परिक्रान्तिः
परिक्रांतिः f. Revolution,<BR>perambulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रिया
परिक्रिया<BR>1 Enclosing with a fence<BR>or ditch, intrenching.<BR>--2<BR>Encircling or surrounding in general.<BR>--3 (In dramaturgy) = परिकर (7)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">Page0671-c+ 55</a>]<BR>q. v.<BR>--4 Attention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्री
परिक्री {c9c} A.<BR>1 To buy; संभोगाय<BR>परिक्रीतः कर्तास्मि तव नाप्रियं<BR>Bk. 8. 78.<BR>--2 To hire, purchase for a time<BR>(with instr. or dat. of the price<BR>at which one is employed on<BR>stipulated wages); शतेन शताय वा<BR>परिक्रीतः Sk.<BR>--3 To return, requite,<BR>repay; कृतेनोपकृतं वायोः<BR>परिक्रीणानमुत्थितं Bk. 8. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रयः|परिक्रय
परिक्रयः, --क्रयणं<BR>1 Wages, hire.<BR>--2 Employing on wages.<BR>--3<BR>Purchasing or buying off.<BR>--4 Barter,<BR>exchange.<BR>--5 A peace purchased<BR>with the payment of money; cf.<BR>H. 4. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्रयणं|परिक्रयण
परिक्रयः, --क्रयणं<BR>1 Wages, hire.<BR>--2 Employing on wages.<BR>--3<BR>Purchasing or buying off.<BR>--4 Barter,<BR>exchange.<BR>--5 A peace purchased<BR>with the payment of money; cf.<BR>H. 4. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लांत|परिक्लान्त
परिक्लांत a. Fatigued,<BR>exhausted, tired out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लिश्
परिक्लिश् {vI.v} {c9c} P. To torment,<BR>trouble, harass. {vII.v} {c4c} A.<BR>1 To feel<BR>pain, suffer.<BR>--2 To be vexed or<BR>troubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लिष्ट
परिक्लिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Vexed, troubled.<BR>--2 Exhausted, fatigued.<BR>--ष्टं Pain,<BR>vexation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लेशः|परिक्लेश
परिक्लेशः Fatigue, trouble, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्लेदः|परिक्लेद
परिक्लेदः Wetness, dampness,<BR>moisture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्वणन|परिक्वणनः
परिक्वणन a. Loud.<BR>--नः Ved. A<BR>cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षतिः|परिक्षति
परिक्षतिः f. Injury, hurt, harm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षा
परिक्षा Clay, mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षाम
परिक्षाम a. Emaciated, wasted<BR>away, lean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षालनं|परिक्षालन
परिक्षालनं<BR>1 Washing, cleansing.<BR>--2 Water for washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षि
परिक्षि {c5c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To decay,<BR>wane.<BR>--2 To be emaciated or lean.<BR>--3 To destroy, put an end to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षयः|परिक्षय
परिक्षयः<BR>1 Decay, waste,<BR>destruction; परिक्षयोपि अधिकं रमणीयः<BR>Mk. 1; किरण˚ Ku. 4. 46<BR>--2<BR>Disappearing, ceasing.<BR>--3 Ruin, loss,<BR>failure; Ki. 16. 57, Ms. 9. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षीण
परिक्षीण p. p.<BR>1 Vanished,<BR>disappeared.<BR>--2 Wasted, decayed.<BR>--3<BR>Emaciated, worn away, exhausted;<BR>Pt. 2. 70.<BR>--4 Impoverished,<BR>entirely ruined; Bh. 2. 45.<BR>--5 Lost,<BR>destroyed.<BR>--6 Diminished,<BR>decreased; प्राण˚ Pt. 4. 23.<BR>--7 (In law)<BR>Insolvent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षित्
परिक्षित् m.<BR>1 N. of a king, son<BR>of Abhimanyu and father of<BR>Janamejaya.<BR>--2 An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0671-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षिप्
परिक्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To surround;<BR>गंगास्रोतःपरिक्षिप्तं Ku. 6. 38.<BR>--2 To<BR>embrace.<BR>--3 To put or lay round.<BR>--4 To survey round, measure, range<BR>over.<BR>--5 To throw over or beyond.<BR>--6 To throw or put into.<BR>--7 To<BR>fetter, chain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षिप्त|परिक्षिप्तं
परिक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Scattered, diffused.<BR>--2 Encircled, surrounded;<BR>वेतसपरिक्षिप्ते मंडपे Ś. 3.<BR>--3 Intrenched.<BR>--4<BR>Overspread, overlaid.<BR>--5 Left,<BR>abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षेपः|परिक्षेप
परिक्षेपः<BR>1 Moving about, walking<BR>to and fro.<BR>--2 Scattering,<BR>spreading.<BR>--3 Surrounding, encircling,<BR>circumfluence.<BR>--4 An enclosing belt<BR>or boundary, that by which<BR>anything is surrounded; R. 12. 66.<BR>--5<BR>Abandoning, leaving.<BR>--6 An organ<BR>of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिक्षीव
परिक्षीव a. Quite intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखंडयति
परिखंडयति Den. P. To<BR>humiliate, conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखा
परिखा A moat, ditch, trench<BR>round a fort or town; R. 1. 30;<BR>12. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखातं|परिखात
परिखातं<BR>1 A moat, ditch.<BR>--2 A rut,<BR>furrow.<BR>--3 Digging round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखिद्
परिखिद् {c4c} P. To suffer pain or<BR>misery, be distressed or wearied.<BR>--Caus. To injure, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखिन्न
परिखिन्न p. p. Afflicted, troubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिखेदः|परिखेद
परिखेदः Fatigue, exhaustion,<BR>lassitude; Ku. 1. 60; Rs. 1. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्या
परिख्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 Ved. To look at,<BR>perceive.<BR>--2 To regard, consider.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिख्यातिः|परिख्याति
परिख्यातिः f. Fame, reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगण्
परिगण् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To enumerate,<BR>count.<BR>--2 To consider, regard,<BR>think; अपरिगणयन् Me. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगणनं|परिगणन
परिगणनं --ना Complete<BR>enumeration, accurate statement or<BR>calculation; श्रेणीभूताः परिगणनया निर्दिशंतो<BR>बलाकाः Me. (considered as an<BR>interpolation or क्षेपक by Malli.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगणना
परिगणनं --ना Complete<BR>enumeration, accurate statement or<BR>calculation; श्रेणीभूताः परिगणनया निर्दिशंतो<BR>बलाकाः Me. (considered as an<BR>interpolation or क्षेपक by Malli.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगम्
परिगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go or walk<BR>round; तं हयं तत्र परिगम्य Rām.; यथा<BR>हि मेरुः सूर्येण नित्यशः परिगम्यते Mb.<BR>--2 To surround; Śi. 9. 26;<BR>Bk. 10. 1; सेनापरिगत &c.<BR>--3 To spread<BR>everywhere, pervade all directions.<BR>--4 To attain to, obtain; वृषलतां &c.<BR>--5 To know, understand, learn;<BR>R. 7. 71.<BR>--6 To die, go forth (from this<BR>world); वयं येभ्यो जाताश्चिरपरिगता<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">Page0672-b+ 56</a>]<BR>एव खलु ते Bh. 3. 38.<BR>--7 To<BR>overpower, affect; as in क्षुधया परिगतः.<BR>--Caus. To pass or spend (time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगत|परिगतः
परिगत p. p.<BR>1 Surrounded,<BR>enclosed, encircled; Māl. 4. 10.<BR>--2<BR>Diffused, spread around; Ś. 7. 35.<BR>--3 Known, understood; R. 7. 71;<BR>परिगतपरिगंतव्य एव भवान् Ve. 3; Mv. 3. 47.<BR>--4 Filled or covered with, possessed<BR>of (usually in comp.); Śi. 9. 26.<BR>--5 Got, obtained; Bh. 3. 52.<BR>--6<BR>Remembered.<BR>--7 Overcome,<BR>overwhelmed.<BR>--8 Affected by, afflicted<BR>with; Pt. 1. 49.<BR>--9 Performed.<BR>--10<BR>Forgotten.<BR>--11 Obstructed,<BR>hindered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगमः|परिगम
परिगमः, परिगमनं<BR>1 Going round,<BR>surrounding.<BR>--2 Spreading,<BR>diffusing.<BR>--3 Obtaining.<BR>--4 Knowing,<BR>determining, ascertaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगमनं|परिगमन
परिगमः, परिगमनं<BR>1 Going round,<BR>surrounding.<BR>--2 Spreading,<BR>diffusing.<BR>--3 Obtaining.<BR>--4 Knowing,<BR>determining, ascertaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगलित
परिगलित p. p.<BR>1 Sunk.<BR>--2<BR>Tumbled or dropped down.<BR>--3<BR>Vanished.<BR>--4 Melted.<BR>--5 Flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगर्हणं|परिगर्हण
परिगर्हणं Excessive blame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगूढ
परिगूढ p. p.<BR>1 Quite secret.<BR>--2<BR>Incomprehensible, very difficult to<BR>understand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगै
परिगै {c1c} P. To sing, relate,<BR>describe, celebrate, or proclaim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगीति
परिगीति f. A kind of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रह्
परिग्रह् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To clasp round,<BR>embrace.<BR>--2 To encircle; surround,<BR>fence or hedge round.<BR>--3 To lay<BR>hold of, seize.<BR>--4 To take, assume.<BR>--5 To accept.<BR>--6 To favour,<BR>patronize; देवेन च परिगृहीतः M. 1; 1. 13.<BR>--7 To support, assist, guide;<BR>राक्षसमतिपरिगृहीतः Mu. 1.<BR>--8 To put on (a<BR>dress).<BR>--9 To take possession of,<BR>master, overpower.<BR>--10 To conceive,<BR>comprehend.<BR>--11 To undertake.<BR>--12<BR>To receive hospitably.<BR>--13 To take<BR>(a wife), marry; Ś. 5. 19.<BR>--14 To<BR>conform to, follow.<BR>--15 To surpass,<BR>excel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृहीत
परिगृहीत p. p.<BR>1 Grasped, seized,<BR>clutched.<BR>--2 Embraced, surrounded.<BR>--3 Accepted, taken, received.<BR>--4<BR>Assented or consented to, admitted.<BR>--5<BR>Patronized, favoured.<BR>--6 Followed,<BR>obeyed, observed.<BR>--7 Married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृहीतिः|परिगृहीति
परिगृहीतिः f. Ved.<BR>1 Grasping,<BR>comprehension.<BR>--2 Summing up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिगृह्या
परिगृह्या A married woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रहः|परिग्रह
परिग्रहः<BR>1 Seizing, holding, taking,<BR>grasping; आसनरज्जुपरिग्रहे R. 9. 46;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-c" target="_blank">Page0672-c+ 58</a>]<BR>शंकापरिग्रहः Mu. 1. ‘taking or<BR>entertaining a doubt’.<BR>--2<BR>Surrounding, enclosing, encircling, fencing<BR>round.<BR>--3 Putting on, wrapping<BR>round (as a dress); मौलिपरिग्रहः<BR>R. 18. 38.<BR>--4 Assuming, taking;<BR>मानपरिग्रहः Amaru. 92; विवाहलक्ष्मी˚<BR>U. 4.<BR>--5 Receiving, taking; accepting,<BR>acceptance; भौमो मुनेः स्थानपरिग्रहोऽयं<BR>R. 13. 36; अर्ध्यपरिग्रहांते 70; 12. 16;<BR>Ku. 6. 53; विद्यापरिग्रहाय Māl. 1;<BR>so आसनपरिग्रहं करोतु देवः U. 3 ‘your<BR>majesty will be pleased to take a<BR>seat or sit down’.<BR>--6 Possessions,<BR>property, belongings;<BR>त्यक्तसर्वपरिग्रहः Bg. 4. 21; R. 15. 55;<BR>V. 4. 26.<BR>--7 Taking in marriage, marriage;<BR>नवे दारपरिग्रहे U. 1. 19; Māl. 5. 27;<BR>Ś. 1. 22.<BR>--8 A wife, queen;<BR>प्रयतपरिग्रहद्वितीयः R. 1. 95, 92; 9. 14;<BR>11. 33; 16. 8; Ś. 5. 28, 31;<BR>परिग्रहबहुत्वेऽपि Ś. 3. 20.<BR>--9 Taking under<BR>one's protection, favouring;<BR>U. 7. 11; M. 1. 13.<BR>--10 Attendants,<BR>followers, train, retinue, suite.<BR>--11<BR>A household, family, members of<BR>a family.<BR>--12 The seraglio or<BR>household of a king, harem.<BR>--13<BR>Anything received, a present;<BR>राजपरिग्रहोयं Ś. 1.<BR>--14 Assent, consent.<BR>--15 Taking possession of,<BR>acquiring.<BR>--16 A claim.<BR>--17<BR>Entertaining, honouring, receiving (a guest<BR>&c.).<BR>--18 An entertainer.<BR>--19<BR>Assistance.<BR>--20 A husband.<BR>--21<BR>Respect, reverence.<BR>--22 Grace,<BR>favour.<BR>--23 Comprehension,<BR>understanding.<BR>--24 Undertaking,<BR>performing.<BR>--25 Subjugation.<BR>--26<BR>Dominion.<BR>--27 Punishment.<BR>--28<BR>Connection, relation.<BR>--29<BR>Summing up, totality.<BR>--30 A house,<BR>residence.<BR>--31 Removing, taking<BR>away.<BR>--32 A curse.<BR>--33 (In Ved.<BR>Gram.) The double mention of<BR>a word both before and after इति.<BR>--34 The form which precedes इति.<BR>--35 Root, origin.<BR>--36 The eclipse<BR>of the sun or moon.<BR>--37 An oath.<BR>--38 The rear of an army.<BR>--39 N.<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रहणं|परिग्रहण
परिग्रहणं Wrapping round,<BR>putting on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्रहीतृ
परिग्रहीतृ m.<BR>1 A husband;<BR>Ś. 4. 21.<BR>--2 An assistant.<BR>--3 An<BR>adoptive father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्राहः|परिग्राह
परिग्राहः The fencing round of the<BR>sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0672-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिग्लान
परिग्लान p. p.<BR>1 Languid,<BR>exhausted.<BR>--2 Averse from,<BR>disinclined to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघः|परिघ
परिघः<BR>1 An iron (or wooden)<BR>beam or bar used for locking or<BR>shutting a gate (अर्गल)); एकः कृत्स्नां<BR>नगरपरिघप्रांशुबाहुर्भुनक्ति Ś. 2. 15;<BR>R. 16. 84; Śi. 19. 32; M. 5. 2.<BR>--2<BR>(Hence) A bar barrier, hindrance,<BR>obstacle; भार्गवस्य सुकृतोऽपि सोऽ<BR>भवत्स्वर्गमार्गपरिघो दुरत्ययः R. 11. 88.<BR>--3<BR>A stick or club studded or tipped<BR>with iron; R. 12. 73.<BR>--4 An iron<BR>club in general.<BR>--5 A water-jar,<BR>pitcher.<BR>--6 A glass-pitcher.<BR>--7 A<BR>house, dwelling.<BR>--8 Killing,<BR>destroying.<BR>--9 Striking, a stroke or<BR>blow.<BR>--10 A child which assumes a<BR>peculiar cross position in birth.<BR>--11<BR>A line of clouds crossing the sun at<BR>sunrise or sunset.<BR>--12 The gate of<BR>a palace, town or house.<BR>--घौ (m.<BR>dual) Two birds flying on each side<BR>of a traveller (regarded as an omen).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघट्ट्
परिघट्ट् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To strike;<BR>Śi. 9. 64.<BR>--2 To stir up.<BR>--3 To touch or<BR>press on all sides.<BR>--4 To open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघट्टनं|परिघट्टन
परिघट्टनं Stirring up, stirring<BR>round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघर्मः|परिघर्म
परिघर्मः A vessel for preparing<BR>the hot sacrificial beverage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघातः|परिघात
परिघातः, --घातनं<BR>1 Killing,<BR>striking, removing, getting rid of.<BR>--2 A club, an iron bludgeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघातनं|परिघातन|परिघातनः
परिघातः, --घातनं<BR>1 Killing,<BR>striking, removing, getting rid of.<BR>--2 A club, an iron bludgeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिघोषः|परिघोष
परिघोषः<BR>1 Noise.<BR>--2 Improper<BR>speech.<BR>--3 Thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचक्ष्
परिचक्ष् {c2c} A.<BR>1 To declare,<BR>relate, tell.<BR>--2 To enumerate.<BR>--3 To<BR>mention.<BR>--4 To name, call;<BR>वेदप्रदानादाचार्यं पितरं परिचक्षते<BR>Ms. 2. 171.; Bg. 17. 13, 17.<BR>--5 To<BR>disregard, overlook, pass over.<BR>--6 To<BR>disapprove, reject.<BR>--7 To acknowledge,<BR>admit.<BR>--8 To address (with acc.).<BR>--9 To answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचक्षा
परिचक्षा Ved. Rejection,<BR>disapproval.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचतुर्दशन्
परिचतुर्दशन् a. Fully fourteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर्
परिचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go or walk<BR>about.<BR>--2 To serve, wait or attend<BR>upon; Ms. 2. 243; Bh. 3. 40.<BR>--3<BR>To worship, adore, reverence;<BR>Mv. 3. 36.<BR>--4 To take care of, nurse,<BR>tend. --Caus. To enclose,<BR>surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर|परिचरः
परिचर a.<BR>1 Roaming or moving<BR>about.<BR>--2 Flowing.<BR>--3 Moveable.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A servant, follower, an<BR>attendant.<BR>--2 A body-guard.<BR>--3<BR>A guard or patrol in general.<BR>--4<BR>Homage, service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचरणः|परिचरण
परिचरणः A servant, an<BR>attendant, assistant.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Serving,<BR>attending or waiting upon.<BR>--2<BR>Going about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचरितृ
परिचरितृ m. A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर्या|परिचर्य्या
परिचर्या<BR>1 Service, attendance;<BR>R. 1. 91; Bg. 18. 44.<BR>--2<BR>Adoration, worship; Śi. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारः|परिचार
परिचारः<BR>1 Service, attendance.<BR>--2 A servant.<BR>--3 A place for<BR>walking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारकः|परिचारक
परिचारकः, --परिचारिकः, --परिचारिन्<BR>m. A servant, an attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारिकः|परिचारिक
परिचारकः, --परिचारिकः, --परिचारिन्<BR>m. A servant, an attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारिन्
परिचारकः, --परिचारिकः, --परिचारिन्<BR>m. A servant, an attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचारिका
परिचारिका<BR>1 A female servant.<BR>--2<BR>(plu.) Fried grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचर्मण्यं|परिचर्मण्य
परिचर्मण्यं A strip of leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचाय्यः|परिचाय्य
परिचाय्यः Sacrificial fire<BR>(arranged in a circle).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचि
परिचि {vI.v} {c5c} U.<BR>1 To heap up,<BR>accumulate.<BR>--2 To know;<BR>Mv. 7. 11.<BR>--3 To get, acquire.<BR>--4 To<BR>increase.<BR>--5 To cover or fill with.<BR>{vII.v} {c3c} P.<BR>1 To practise, familiarize<BR>oneself with.<BR>--2 To become<BR>acquainted with.<BR>--3 Ved. To<BR>examine, investigate. --Caus. To<BR>search, seek for. --Pass. To grow,<BR>be developed; R. 3. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचयः|परिचय
परिचयः<BR>1 Heaping up,<BR>accumulation.<BR>--2 Acquaintance, familiarity,<BR>intimacy; पुरुषपरिचयेन Mk. 1. 56;<BR>अतिपरिचयादवज्ञा ‘familiarity breeds<BR>contempt’; परिचयं चललक्ष्यनिपातने<BR>R. 9. 49; सकलकलापरिचयः K. 76.<BR>--3 Trial, study, practice, frequent<BR>repetition; हेतुः परिचयस्थैर्ये<BR>वक्तुर्गुणनिकैव सा Śi. 2. 75; 11. 5;<BR>वर्णपरिचयं करोति Ś. 5.<BR>--4<BR>Recognition; Me. 9.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करुणा<BR>increasing love or tenderness;<BR>Māl. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचित|परिचितः
परिचित p. p.<BR>1 Heaped up,<BR>accumulated.<BR>--2 Familiar, intimate or<BR>acquainted with; Ś. 5. 10.<BR>--3<BR>Learnt, practised.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचितिः|परिचिति
परिचितिः f. Acquaintance,<BR>familiarity, intimacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचिंत्|परिचिन्त्
परिचिंत् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To think,<BR>consider, judge; त्वमेव तावत्परिचिंतय<BR>स्वयं कदचिदेते यदि योगमर्हतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">Page0673-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Ku. 5. 67; Bg. 10. 17.<BR>--2 To think of,<BR>remember, call to mind.<BR>--3 To<BR>devise, find out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचिंतनं
परिचिंतनं Thinking of,<BR>remembering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचुंब्|परिचुम्ब्
परिचुंब् {c1c} P. To kiss<BR>passionately; परिचुंब्य चूतमंजरीं Ś. 5. 1;<BR>Rs. 6. 17; Amaru. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिचुंबनं|परिचुम्बन
परिचुंबनं Kissing passionately;<BR>Śi. 7. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छद्
परिच्छद् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To cover, clothe;<BR>दर्भैस्तं परिच्छाद्य Pt. 2;<BR>द्वीपिचर्मपरिच्छन्नः (गर्दभः) H. 3. 9.<BR>--2 To hide,<BR>conceal.<BR>--3 To surround with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छद्
परिच्छद् f.<BR>1 Retinue, train.<BR>--2<BR>Paraphernalia.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छदः|परिच्छद|परिछद
परिच्छदः<BR>1 A covering, cover.<BR>--2<BR>A garment, clothes, dress;<BR>शाखावसक्तकमनीयपरिच्छदानां Ki. 7. 40.<BR>--3<BR>Train, retinue, attendants, circle<BR>of dependants; R. 9. 70.<BR>--4<BR>Paraphernalia, external appendage, (as<BR>छत्र, चामर); सेना परिच्छदस्तस्य<BR>R. 1. 19.<BR>--5 Goods and chattels,<BR>personal property, all one's possessions<BR>or belongings (utensils,<BR>implements &c.); विवास्यो वा<BR>भवेद्राष्ट्रात्सद्रव्यः सपरिच्छदः Ms. 9. 241, 7. 40;<BR>8. 405; 9. 78; 11. 77.<BR>--6<BR>Necessaries for travelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छंदः|परिच्छन्द|परिच्छंद|परिच्छन्दः
परिच्छंदः Train, retinue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छन्न|परिच्छन्नः|परिछन्न
परिच्छन्न p. p.<BR>1 Enveloped,<BR>covered, clothed, clad.<BR>--2 Overspread<BR>or overlaid.<BR>--3 Surrounded with<BR>(a retinue).<BR>--4 Concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छिद्
परिच्छिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To tear,<BR>cut off, tear to pieces.<BR>--2 To<BR>wound, mutilate.<BR>--3 To separate,<BR>divide, part; शतेन परिच्छिद्य Sk.<BR>--4<BR>To fix accurately, set limits to,<BR>define, decide, distinguish or<BR>discriminate; मध्यस्था भगवती नौ गुणदोषतः<BR>परिच्छेत्तुमर्हति M. 1; (न) यशः<BR>परिच्छेत्तुमियत्तयालं R. 6. 77; 17. 59;<BR>Ku. 2. 58.<BR>--5 To avert, obviate,<BR>remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छित्तिः|परिच्छित्ति|परिछित्ति
परिच्छित्तिः f. Accurate<BR>definition, limiting. --Partition;<BR>separation, division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छिन्न|परिच्छिन्नः|परिछिन्न
परिच्छिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Cut off, divided.<BR>--2 Accurately defined, determined,<BR>ascertained; Ku. 2. 58.<BR>--3 Limited,<BR>circumscribed, confined.<BR>--4<BR>Remedied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेदः|परिच्छेद|परिछेद
परिच्छेदः<BR>1 Cutting, separating,<BR>dividing, discriminating (between<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-a" target="_blank">Page0674-a+ 56</a>]<BR>right and wrong).<BR>--2 Accurate<BR>definition or distinction, decision,<BR>accurate determination,<BR>ascertainment; परिच्छेदव्यक्तिर्भवति न<BR>पुरःस्थेऽपि विषये Māl. 1. 31; परिच्छेदातीतः<BR>सकलवचनानामविषयः 1. 30<BR>‘transcending all definition or<BR>determination’;<BR>इत्यारूढबहुप्रतर्कमपरिच्छेदाकुलं मे मनः Ś. 5. 9.<BR>--3<BR>Discrimination, judgment, discernment;<BR>परिच्छेदो हि पांडित्यं यदापन्ना विपत्तयः ।<BR>अपरिच्छेदकर्तॄणां विपदः स्युः पदे पदे<BR>H. 1. 148; किं पांडित्यं परिच्छेदः 1. 147.<BR>--4 A limit, boundary, setting<BR>limits to, circumscribing; अलमलं<BR>परिच्छेदेन M. 2.<BR>--5 A section,<BR>chapter or division of a work; (for<BR>the other names for section &c.<BR>see under अध्याय).<BR>--6 A segment.<BR>--7 Remedying.<BR>--8 A measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0673-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेदकं|परिच्छेदक
परिच्छेदकं Limitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेदनं|परिच्छेदन|परिछेदन
परिच्छेदनं<BR>1 Discriminating.<BR>--2<BR>Dividing.<BR>--3 A division of a<BR>book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्छेद्य
परिच्छेद्य a.<BR>1 To be accurately<BR>defined, definable; Ms. 4. 9;<BR>R. 10. 28.<BR>--2 To be weighed or<BR>estimated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्यु
परिच्यु {c1c} A.<BR>1 To go away<BR>or fly off from, escape.<BR>--2 To<BR>proceed from.<BR>--3 To swerve, fall off<BR>from, deviate, leave.<BR>--4 To lose.<BR>be deprived of,<BR>--5 To drop or<BR>fall down.<BR>--6 To be displaced or<BR>ejected from.<BR>--7 To be freed<BR>from.<BR>--8 To come down, descend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिच्युतिः|परिच्युति
परिच्युतिः f.<BR>1 Falling down.<BR>--2<BR>Swerving, deviating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजनः|परिजन
परिजनः<BR>1 Attendants,<BR>followers, servants taken collectively;<BR>परिजनो राजानमभितः स्थितः M. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Especially, the retinue, suite, or<BR>train of females, the maids of a<BR>lady; R. 19. 23.<BR>--3 A single<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजन्मन्
परिजन्मन् m.<BR>1 The moon.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिजल्पितं|परिजल्पित
परिजल्पितं A covert indication<BR>(as by a servant) of one's own<BR>skill, superiority &c. by pointing<BR>out the cruelty, deceitfulness and<BR>such other faults of his master;<BR>Ujjvalamaṇi thus defines it:<BR>--प्रभोर्निर्दयताशाठ्यचापलाघुपपादनात् ।<BR>स्वविचणताव्यक्तिर्भंग्या स्यात्परिजल्पितम् ॥ (Wilson<BR>renders the word by ‘the covert<BR>reproaches of a mistress neglected<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">Page0674-b+ 56</a>]<BR>or ill-used by her lover’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञा
परिज्ञा {c9c} U.<BR>1 To be aware of;<BR>know, be acquainted with;<BR>वृषभोयमिति परिज्ञाय Pt. 1; Ms. 8. 126.<BR>--2 To find out, ascertain; सम्यक्<BR>परिज्ञाय Pt. 1.<BR>--3 To recognise;<BR>तपस्विभिः कैश्चित्परिज्ञातोऽस्मि Ś. 2.<BR>--4 To<BR>observe, perceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञप्तिः|परिज्ञप्ति
परिज्ञप्तिः f.<BR>1 Conversation,<BR>discourse.<BR>--2 Recognition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञा
परिज्ञा, परिज्ञानं<BR>1 Thorough<BR>knowledge, complete acquaintance.<BR>--2<BR>Recognition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञानं|परिज्ञान
परिज्ञा, परिज्ञानं<BR>1 Thorough<BR>knowledge, complete acquaintance.<BR>--2<BR>Recognition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्ञेय
परिज्ञेय a.<BR>1 To be recognised or<BR>ascertained.<BR>--2 Comprehensible,<BR>conceivable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्मन्
परिज्मन् a. Ved. Running or<BR>walking round. --m.<BR>1 The moon.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्रि
परिज्रि a. Running round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिज्वन्
परिज्वन् m.<BR>1 The moon.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 A servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिडीनं|परिडीन
परिडीनं The flight of a bird in<BR>circles; see डीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणम्
परिणम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To stoop, bend<BR>down (as an elephant to strike<BR>with his tusks);<BR>वप्रक्रीडापरिणतगजप्रेक्षणीयं ददर्श Me. 2; विष्के नागः<BR>पर्यणंसीत् स्व एव Śi. 18. 27.<BR>--2 To bend or<BR>bow down, be inclined;<BR>लज्जापरिणतैः (वदनकमलैः) Bh. 1. 4.<BR>--3 To be<BR>changed or transformed into,<BR>assume the form of (with instr.);<BR>लताभावेन परिणतमस्या रूपं V. 4;<BR>4. 28; क्षीरं जलं वा स्वयमेव दधिहिमभावेन<BR>परिणमते Ś. B.; Me. 45.<BR>--4 To result,<BR>happen; सर्वं विपरीतं परिणमति Mk. 1.<BR>--5 To be developed or matured,<BR>be ripe; Me. 18; Ki. 5. 37;<BR>M. 3. 8; Rs. 1. 26; Mv. 1. 12;<BR>see परिणत below.<BR>--6 To be advanced<BR>(in age), grow old, be aged, decay;<BR>परिणतशरच्चाद्रिकासु क्षपासु Me. 110; so<BR>जरापरिणत &c.<BR>--7 To set, decline in<BR>the west (as the sun); अनेन समयेन<BR>परिणतो दिवसः K. 47.<BR>--8 To be<BR>digested; ग्रस्तं परिणमेच्च यत् Mb.<BR>--9 To<BR>be cooked or roasted; Māl. 5. 17.<BR>--10 To elapse (as time). --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To make ripe, mature, develop,<BR>perfect.<BR>--2 To pass (as the night).<BR>--3<BR>To stoop, bend oneself down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणत|परिणतं|परिणतः
परिणत p. p.<BR>1 Bent or bowed<BR>down, stooping; Me. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Declining, old (as age); परिणते वयसि<BR>K. 35, 62, 63.<BR>--3 Ripe, matured,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-c" target="_blank">Page0674-c+ 57</a>]<BR>ripened, fully developed or formed; श<BR>ब्दब्रह्मविदः कवेः परिणतप्रज्ञस्य वाणीमिमां<BR>U. 7. 21; 1. 39, 6. 13; Me. 23;<BR>परिणतमकरंदमार्मिकास्ते Bv. 1. 8;<BR>Śi. 11. 49.<BR>--4 Full-grown, advanced,<BR>perfected; परिणतशरच्चद्रंक्रिरणैः<BR>Bh. 3. 49; Me. 110.<BR>--5 Digested (as food).<BR>--6 Transformed or changed into<BR>(with instr.); V. 4. 28.<BR>--7 Ended,<BR>come to a close, terminated.<BR>--8 Set<BR>(as the sun); Ś. 1. 32.<BR>--तः An<BR>elephant stooping to strike with his<BR>tusks, or giving a side-blow with<BR>his tusks; (तिर्यग्दंतप्रहारश्च गजः<BR>परिणतो मतः Halāy.); Śi. 4. 29;<BR>Ki. 6. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणतिः|परिणति
परिणतिः f.<BR>1 Bending or stooping<BR>down, bowing.<BR>--2 Ripeness,<BR>maturity, development; Mv. 2. 15.<BR>--3<BR>Change, transformation,<BR>transmutation.<BR>--4 Fulfilment.<BR>--5 Result,<BR>consequence, issue; परिणतिरवधार्या<BR>यत्नतः पंडितेन Bh. 2. 99; 1. 20, 3. 17;<BR>Mv. 6. 28; Māl. 4. 4.<BR>--6 End,<BR>conelusion, close, termination;<BR>परिणतिरमणीयाः प्रीतयस्त्वद्विधानां Māl. 6. 7,<BR>16; Śi. 11. 1.<BR>--7 Close of life, old<BR>age; सेवाकारा परिणतिरभूत् V. 3. 1;<BR>अभवद्गतः परिणतिं शिथिलः<BR>परिमंदसूर्यनयनो दिवसः Śi. 9. 3 (where<BR>प˚ means ‘end or conclusion’ also).<BR>--8 Digestion (of food).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणमनं|परिणमन
परिणमनं Change, transformation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामक
परिणामक a. Causing a change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणामः|परिणाम
परि(री)णामः<BR>1 Alteration,<BR>change, transformation.<BR>--2<BR>Digestion; अन्नं न सम्यक् परिणाममेति Suśr.;<BR>भुक्तस्य परिणामहेतुरौदर्यं T. S.;<BR>Pt. 4. 22.<BR>--3 Result, consequence, issue,<BR>effect; अप्रियस्यापि पथ्यस्य परिणामः<BR>सुखावहः H. 2. 135; Mk. 3. 1;<BR>परिणामसुखे गरीयसि (वचसि औषधे च)<BR>Ki. 2. 4; Bg. 18. 37, 38.<BR>--4<BR>Ripening, maturity, full development;<BR>उपैति शस्यं परिणामरम्यतां Ki. 4. 22;<BR>फलभरपरिणामश्यामजंबू &c. U. 2. 20;<BR>Māl. 9. 24.<BR>--5 End, termination,<BR>conclusion, close, decline; दिवसाः<BR>परिणामरमणीयाः Ś. 1. 3;<BR>वयःपरिणामपांडुरशिरसं K. 10; परिणाममुपैति<BR>दिवसः K. 254 ‘the day is drawing<BR>to a close’.<BR>--6 Old age; परिणामे हि<BR>दिलीपवंशजाः R. 8. 11.<BR>--7 Lapse (of<BR>time).<BR>--8 (In Rhet.) A figure of<BR>speech allied to रूपक, by which the<BR>properties of any object are<BR>transferred to that with which it is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">Page0675-a+ 56</a>]<BR>compared. (The Candrāloka thus<BR>defines and illustrates it:<BR>--परिणामः<BR>क्रियार्थश्चेद्विषयी विषयात्मना । प्रसन्नेम दृगब्जेन<BR>वीक्षते मदिरेक्षणा 5. 18; see R. G. also<BR>under परिणाम).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दार्शिन् a.<BR>prudent, fore-sighted.<BR>--दृष्टि a.<BR>prudent. (--ष्टिः f.) prudence,<BR>providence.<BR>--पथ्य a. salutary in the<BR>end.<BR>--शूलं violent or painful<BR>indigestion, colic, flatulence with pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीणामः|परीणाम
परि(री)णामः<BR>1 Alteration,<BR>change, transformation.<BR>--2<BR>Digestion; अन्नं न सम्यक् परिणाममेति Suśr.;<BR>भुक्तस्य परिणामहेतुरौदर्यं T. S.;<BR>Pt. 4. 22.<BR>--3 Result, consequence, issue,<BR>effect; अप्रियस्यापि पथ्यस्य परिणामः<BR>सुखावहः H. 2. 135; Mk. 3. 1;<BR>परिणामसुखे गरीयसि (वचसि औषधे च)<BR>Ki. 2. 4; Bg. 18. 37, 38.<BR>--4<BR>Ripening, maturity, full development;<BR>उपैति शस्यं परिणामरम्यतां Ki. 4. 22;<BR>फलभरपरिणामश्यामजंबू &c. U. 2. 20;<BR>Māl. 9. 24.<BR>--5 End, termination,<BR>conclusion, close, decline; दिवसाः<BR>परिणामरमणीयाः Ś. 1. 3;<BR>वयःपरिणामपांडुरशिरसं K. 10; परिणाममुपैति<BR>दिवसः K. 254 ‘the day is drawing<BR>to a close’.<BR>--6 Old age; परिणामे हि<BR>दिलीपवंशजाः R. 8. 11.<BR>--7 Lapse (of<BR>time).<BR>--8 (In Rhet.) A figure of<BR>speech allied to रूपक, by which the<BR>properties of any object are<BR>transferred to that with which it is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">Page0675-a+ 56</a>]<BR>compared. (The Candrāloka thus<BR>defines and illustrates it:<BR>--परिणामः<BR>क्रियार्थश्चेद्विषयी विषयात्मना । प्रसन्नेम दृगब्जेन<BR>वीक्षते मदिरेक्षणा 5. 18; see R. G. also<BR>under परिणाम).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दार्शिन् a.<BR>prudent, fore-sighted.<BR>--दृष्टि a.<BR>prudent. (--ष्टिः f.) prudence,<BR>providence.<BR>--पथ्य a. salutary in the<BR>end.<BR>--शूलं violent or painful<BR>indigestion, colic, flatulence with pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0674-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणह्
परिणह् {c4c} U.<BR>1 To surround,<BR>intertwine, encircle; स जयति परिणद्धः<BR>शक्तिभिः शक्तिनाथः Māl. 5. 1;<BR>R. 6. 64; M. 5. 10; Rs. 6. 25.<BR>--2 To<BR>bind or tie round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणद्ध
परिणद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Bound or wrapped<BR>round.<BR>--2 Broad, large;<BR>परिणद्धकंधरः R. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणहनं|परिणहन
परिणहनं Girding on, wrapping<BR>round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाहः|परिणाह
परि(री)णाहः<BR>1 Circumference,<BR>compass, expanse, extent, breadth,<BR>width; स्तनयुगपरिणाहाच्छादिना<BR>वल्कलेन Ś. 1. 19;<BR>स्तनपरिणाहविलासवैजयंती Māl. 3. 15 ‘large or expansive<BR>breasts’; ककुदे वृषस्य<BR>कृतबाहुमकृशपरिणाहशालिनि Ki. 12. 20; Mk. 3. 9;<BR>Ratn. 2. 13; Mv. 7. 24.<BR>--2<BR>Periphery or circumference of a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीणाहः|परीणाह
परि(री)णाहः<BR>1 Circumference,<BR>compass, expanse, extent, breadth,<BR>width; स्तनयुगपरिणाहाच्छादिना<BR>वल्कलेन Ś. 1. 19;<BR>स्तनपरिणाहविलासवैजयंती Māl. 3. 15 ‘large or expansive<BR>breasts’; ककुदे वृषस्य<BR>कृतबाहुमकृशपरिणाहशालिनि Ki. 12. 20; Mk. 3. 9;<BR>Ratn. 2. 13; Mv. 7. 24.<BR>--2<BR>Periphery or circumference of a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाहवत्|परिणाहवन्त्
परिणाहवत् a. Large, big, expansive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणाहिन्
परिणाहिन् a. Large, big; Ku. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिंसक
परिणिंसक a.<BR>1 Tasting, eating;<BR>फलानां परिणिंसकः Bk. 9. 106.<BR>--2<BR>Kissing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणिष्ठा
परिणिष्ठा Perfect skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणी
परिणी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To lead or carry<BR>round (the fire); तौ दंपती त्रिः<BR>परिणीय वह्निं (पुरोधाः) Ku. 7. 80;<BR>अग्निं पर्यणयं च यत् Rām.<BR>--2 To<BR>marry, espouse; परिणेष्यति पार्वतीं यदा<BR>तपसा तत्प्रवणीकृतो हरः Ku. 4. 42.<BR>--3 To ascertain, investigate;<BR>Ms. 7. 122.<BR>--4 To lead forward. --Caus.<BR>To pass, spend (time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणयः|परिणय
परिणयः, --णयनं Marriage;<BR>नवपरिणया वधूः शयने K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणयनं|परिणयन
परिणयः, --णयनं Marriage;<BR>नवपरिणया वधूः शयने K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणायः|परिणाय
परि(री)णायः<BR>1 Moving a piece<BR>at chess, draughts &c.<BR>--2 A move<BR>(at chess).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीणायः|परीणाय
परि(री)णायः<BR>1 Moving a piece<BR>at chess, draughts &c.<BR>--2 A move<BR>(at chess).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणायकः|परिणायक
परिणायकः<BR>1 A leader.<BR>--2 A<BR>husband; Śi. 9. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणीत
परिणीत p. p. Married.<BR>--ता A<BR>married woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिणेतृ
परिणेतृ m. A husband; Ś. 5. 17;<BR>R. 1. 25; 14. 26; Ku. 7. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितक्म्य
परितक्म्य a. Ved. Dangerous,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">Page0675-b+ 56</a>]<BR>risky, unsafe.<BR>--क्म्या<BR>1 Error.<BR>--2<BR>Night, darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितप्
परितप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To heat, burn,<BR>consume.<BR>--2 To inflame, set on fire.<BR>--3 To suffer pain.<BR>--4 To practise<BR>penance. --Caus.<BR>1 To scorch.<BR>--2<BR>To torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितप्त
परितप्त p. p.<BR>1 Heated, burnt.<BR>--2<BR>Tormented, pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितप्तिः|परितप्ति
परितप्तिः f. Excessive pain, anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितापः|परिताप
परितापः<BR>1 Extreme or scorching<BR>heat; (पादपः) शमयति परितापं<BR>छायया संश्रितानां Ś. 5. 7; गुरुपरितापानि<BR>गात्राणि 3. 18; Rs. 1. 22.<BR>--2 Pain,<BR>agony, anguish, grief; प्रसक्ते निर्वाणे<BR>हृदय परितापं वहसि किं M. 3. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Lamentation, wailing;<BR>विरचितविविधविलापं सा परितापं चकारोच्चैः Gīt. 7.<BR>--4 Trembling, fear.<BR>--5 Hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितर्क्
परितर्क् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To reflect,<BR>consider.<BR>--2 To examine (judicially).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितर्कणं|परितर्कण
परितर्कणं Consideration, reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितस्
परितस् ind. (Usually with a<BR>noun in the acc., sometimes by<BR>itself)<BR>1 All around, on all sides,<BR>round about, in all directions,<BR>everywhere, on every side; रक्षांसि वेदीं<BR>परितो निरास्थत् Bk. 1. 12; Śi. 5. 26,<BR>9. 36; Ś. 4. 7; 3. 27; Ki. 1. 14;<BR>गाहितमखिलं गहनं परितो दृष्टाश्च<BR>विटपिनः सर्वे Bv. 1. 21, 29.<BR>--2<BR>Towards, in the direction of;<BR>आपेदिरेंऽबरपथं परितः पतंगाः Bv. 1. 17;<BR>R. 9. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितुष्
परितुष् {c4c} P. To be satisfied,<BR>be delighted or contented;<BR>अस्मत्कृते च परितुष्यति काचिदन्या<BR>Bh. 2. 2. --Caus.<BR>1 To satisfy or please;<BR>completely.<BR>--2 To appease.<BR>--3 To<BR>flatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितुष्ट|परितुष्टः
परितुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Completely satisfied;<BR>वयमिह परितुष्टा बल्कलैस्त्वं च लक्ष्म्या<BR>Bh. 3. 50; so मनसि च परितुष्टे<BR>कोऽर्थवान् को दरिद्रः ibid.<BR>--2 Pleased,<BR>delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितुष्टिः|परितुष्टि
परितुष्टिः f.<BR>1 Contentment,<BR>complete satisfaction.<BR>--2 Delight, joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितोषः|परितोष
परितोषः<BR>1 Contentment, absence<BR>of desire (opp. लोभ); सम इह<BR>परितोषो निर्विशेषो विशेषः Bh. 3. 50.<BR>--2<BR>Complete satisfaction, gratification;<BR>आपरितोषाद्विदुषां न साधु मन्ये<BR>प्रयोगविज्ञानं Ś. 1. 2.<BR>--3 Pleasure, delight,<BR>delight in, liking for (with loc.);<BR>Ku. 6. 59; R. 11. 92; गुणिनि<BR>परितोषः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितोषण
परितोषण a. Satisfying, gratifying.<BR>--णं Satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितृप्
परितृप् {c4c} P. To be pleased or<BR>contented. --Caus.<BR>1 To satisfy,<BR>please, gratify.<BR>--2 To refresh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परितर्पणं|परितर्पण
परितर्पणं Gratifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यज्
परित्यज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To leave, quit,<BR>abandon.<BR>--2 To resign, give up,<BR>discard, renounce; प्रारब्धमुत्तमगुणा न<BR>परित्यजंति Mu. 2. 17.<BR>--3 To except;<BR>तृणमप्यपरित्यज्य सतृणं Sk.<BR>--4 To<BR>leave over, leave as a remainder.<BR>--5<BR>To neglect, disregard. --Caus. To<BR>deprive a person of, rob any one of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यक्त
परित्यक्त p. p.<BR>1 Left, quitted,<BR>abandoned.<BR>--2 Deprived or bereft<BR>of (with instr.).<BR>--3 Let go,<BR>discharged (as an arrow).<BR>--4 Wanting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यजनं|परित्यजन
परित्यजनं Abandoning, giving up,<BR>leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्यागः|परित्याग
परित्यागः<BR>1 Leaving, quitting,<BR>abandonment, desertion, repudiation<BR>(as of a wife &c.);<BR>अपरित्यागमयाचतात्मनः R. 8. 12; कृतसीतापरित्यागः<BR>15. 1.<BR>--2 Giving up, renouncing,<BR>discarding, renunciation, abdication<BR>&c.; स्वनामपरित्यागं करोमि Pt. 1. ‘I<BR>shall forego my name’; Ms. 2. 95.<BR>--3 Neglect, omission; मोहात्तस्य (<BR>कर्मणः) परित्यागस्तामसः परिकीर्तितः<BR>Bg. 18. 7.<BR>--4 Giving away, liberality.<BR>--5 Loss, privation.<BR>--6 A sacrifice.<BR>--7<BR>Separation from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्रस्त
परित्रस्त a. Frightened, afraid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्रासः|परित्रास
परित्रासः Fear, terror, fright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्रै
परित्रै {c1c} A. To rescue, save,<BR>protect; परित्रायस्व परित्रायस्व (in dramas),<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परित्राणं|परित्राण
परित्राणं<BR>1 Preservation, protection<BR>rescue, defence, deliverance;<BR>परित्राणाय साधूनां विनाशाय च दुष्कृतां<BR>Bg. 4. 8; रामापरित्राणविहस्तयोधं सेनानिवेशं<BR>तुमुलं चकार R. 5. 49.<BR>--2<BR>Self-defence.<BR>--3 Abstaining from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदरः|परिदर
परिदरः A disease of the gums in<BR>which the skin peels off and bleeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदह्
परिदह् {c1c} P. To burn completely,<BR>dry up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदहनं|परिदहन
परिदहनं Burning, scorching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदाहः|परिदाह
परि(री)दाहः<BR>1 Burning.<BR>--2<BR>Anguish, pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीदाहः|परीदाह
परि(री)दाहः<BR>1 Burning.<BR>--2<BR>Anguish, pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदंशित
परिदंशित a. Covered with mail,<BR>armed cap-a-pie (completely or from<BR>head to foot).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदा
परिदा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To hand or deliver<BR>over, consign; छद्मना परिददामि मृत्यवे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">Page0676-a+ 55</a>]<BR>U. 1. 46; Ms. 9. 327.<BR>--2 To entrust<BR>or deposit with.<BR>--3 To present.<BR>--4<BR>To lend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0675-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदा
परिदा Ved.<BR>1 Giving oneself up<BR>to the favour of another.<BR>--2<BR>Surrender.<BR>--3 Devotion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदानं|परिदान
परिदानं<BR>1 Barter, exchange.<BR>--2<BR>Devotion.<BR>--3 Restitution or<BR>restoration of a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदायिन्
परिदायिन् m. A father who gives<BR>his daughter in marriage to a man<BR>whose elder brother is not yet<BR>married; cf. परिवेत्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदिव्
परिदिव् --देव् {vI.v} {c1c} {c10c} P. To<BR>lament, moan, suffer pain; Bk. 4. 34.<BR>{vII.v} {c4c} P. To sell, deal in (with acc.<BR>or gen.); शतं शतस्य वा परिदीव्यति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेव्
परिदिव् --देव् {vI.v} {c1c} {c10c} P. To<BR>lament, moan, suffer pain; Bk. 4. 34.<BR>{vII.v} {c4c} P. To sell, deal in (with acc.<BR>or gen.); शतं शतस्य वा परिदीव्यति Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवः|परिदेव
परिदेवः Wailing, lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवनं|परिदेवन
परिदेवनं, --ना, परिदेवितं<BR>1<BR>Lamentation, complaint, bewailing; अथ तैः<BR>परिदेविताक्षरैः Ku. 4. 25; R. 14. 83;<BR>Bg. 2. 28; तत्र का परिदेवना H. 4. 71;<BR>Y. 3. 9.<BR>--2 Repentance, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवना
परिदेवनं, --ना, परिदेवितं<BR>1<BR>Lamentation, complaint, bewailing; अथ तैः<BR>परिदेविताक्षरैः Ku. 4. 25; R. 14. 83;<BR>Bg. 2. 28; तत्र का परिदेवना H. 4. 71;<BR>Y. 3. 9.<BR>--2 Repentance, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदेवितं|परिदेवित
परिदेवनं, --ना, परिदेवितं<BR>1<BR>Lamentation, complaint, bewailing; अथ तैः<BR>परिदेविताक्षरैः Ku. 4. 25; R. 14. 83;<BR>Bg. 2. 28; तत्र का परिदेवना H. 4. 71;<BR>Y. 3. 9.<BR>--2 Repentance, regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिद्यून
परिद्यून a. Sorrowful, sad,<BR>miserable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिदृश्
परिदृश्^1 {c1c} P.<BR>1 To see, view,<BR>behold.<BR>--2 To consider, investigate,<BR>find out.<BR>--3 To know.<BR>--4 To<BR>frequent. --Pass. To appear, become<BR>visible. --Caus.<BR>1 To show.<BR>--2 To<BR>explain, expound.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: missing vowel diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिद्रष्टृ
परिद्रष्टृ m. A spectator, looker<BR>on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधर्षणं|परिधर्षण
परिधर्षणं^1<BR>1 An assault, attack,<BR>outrage.<BR>--2 Insult, affront, abuse.<BR>--3 Ill-treatment, rough usage.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधा
परिधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To put or wear<BR>(as a garment); त्वचं स मेध्यां<BR>परिधाय रौरवीं R. 3. 31.<BR>--2 To<BR>surround, enclose.<BR>--3 To direct<BR>towards.<BR>--4 To put or place round.<BR>--5 To cast round the eyes, turn the<BR>glance upon.<BR>--6 To conclude, close<BR>(as the recitation of a hymn).<BR>--Caus. To cause to put on, clothe<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधानं|परिधान
परि(री)धानं<BR>1 Putting on a<BR>garment, dressing.<BR>--2 A garment,<BR>especially an undergarment, clothes<BR>in general; आत्तचित्रपरिधानविभूषाः<BR>Ki. 9. 1; Śi. 1. 61; 4. 68;<BR>Pt. 5. 23.<BR>--3 Closing or concluding.<BR>--4<BR>Ved. Putting round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीधानं|परीधान
परि(री)धानं<BR>1 Putting on a<BR>garment, dressing.<BR>--2 A garment,<BR>especially an undergarment, clothes<BR>in general; आत्तचित्रपरिधानविभूषाः<BR>Ki. 9. 1; Śi. 1. 61; 4. 68;<BR>Pt. 5. 23.<BR>--3 Closing or concluding.<BR>--4<BR>Ved. Putting round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधानीयं|परिधानीय
परिधानीयं An undergarment.<BR>--या<BR>A concluding hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधायः|परिधाय
परिधायः<BR>1 Train, retinue,<BR>attendants collectively.<BR>--2 A receptacle,<BR>a reservoir.<BR>--3 The posteriors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधायकः|परिधायक
परिधायकः A hedge, fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधिः|परिधि
परिधिः<BR>1 A wall, fence, hedge,<BR>anything surrounding or enclosing<BR>another.<BR>--2 A misty halo round the<BR>sun or moon; परिधेर्मुक्त इवोष्णदीधितिः<BR>R. 8. 30; शशिपरिधिरिवोच्चैर्मंडलस्तेन<BR>तेने N. 2. 108.<BR>--3 A circle of light<BR>--4 The horizon.<BR>--5 The<BR>circumference or compass in general.<BR>--6<BR>The circumference of a circle.<BR>--7<BR>The periphery of a wheel.<BR>--8 A<BR>stick (of a sacred tree like पलाश)<BR>laid round the sacrificial fire;<BR>सप्तास्यासन् परिधयः त्रिःसप्त समिधः कृताः<BR>Rv. 10. 90. 15.<BR>--9 A circle<BR>surrounding the globe.<BR>--10 Epicycle.<BR>--11 A covering.<BR>--12 A branch of a<BR>sacred tree to which the sacrificial<BR>victim is tied.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिखेचरः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--स्थः {1} a guard.<BR>{2} an officer attendant on a king or<BR>general (modern ‘aide-de-camp’).<BR>{3} A number of sentinels posted<BR>in a circle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधारणं|परिधारण
परिधारणं Suffering, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधाव्
परिधाव् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To flow or<BR>stream round.<BR>--2 To go about.<BR>--3<BR>To run after, pursue. --Caus. To<BR>surround, encircle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधाविन्
परिधाविन् a. Running round. --m.<BR>N. of a year (संवत्सर)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधूपित
परिधूपित a. Richly perfumed<BR>or scented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधूसर
परिधूसर a. Quite grey; वसने<BR>परिधूसरे वसाना Ś. 7. 21; R. 11. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिधेयं|परिधेय
परिधेयं An under garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिध्वंसः|परिध्वंस
परिध्वंसः<BR>1 Distress, disaster,<BR>ruin, trouble.<BR>--2 Failure.<BR>--3<BR>Destruction.<BR>--4 Loss of caste.<BR>Ruining, destroying; H. 2. 125.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्वपणं|परिनिर्वपण
परिनिर्वपणं Distributing,<BR>giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्वाण
परिनिर्वाण a. Completely<BR>extinguished.<BR>--णं Final extinction (of<BR>the individual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिर्वृत्तिः
परिनिर्वृत्तिः f. Final liberation<BR>or complete emancipation of the<BR>soul from the body and exemption<BR>from future transmigration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिष्ठा
परिनिष्ठा<BR>1 Complete knowledge<BR>or acquaintance (of anything).<BR>--2<BR>Complete accomplishment.<BR>--3<BR>Extreme limit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिनिष्ठित
परिनिष्ठित p. p.<BR>1 Completely<BR>skilled in.<BR>--2 Not well fixed;<BR>अपरिनिष्ठितस्योपदेशस्यान्याय्यं प्रकाशनं M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिन्यासः|परिन्यास
परिन्यासः<BR>1 Completing the<BR>sense of a passage.<BR>--2 Alluding to<BR>the development of the origin of the<BR>dramatic plot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपक्व
परिपक्व p. p.<BR>1 Completely<BR>cooked.<BR>--2 Completely baked or burnt.<BR>--3 Quite ripe, mature, perfected<BR>(fig. also); प्रफुल्ललोभ्रः परिपक्वशालिः<BR>Rs. 4. 1; so परिपक्वबुद्धिः.<BR>--4 Highly<BR>cultivated, very sharp or shrewd.<BR>--5<BR>Fully digested.<BR>--6 Decaying, on the<BR>point of decay or death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपणं|परिपण
परिपणं(नं) Capital, principal,<BR>stock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपनं|परिपन
परिपणं(नं) Capital, principal,<BR>stock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपणनं|परिपणन
परिपणनं Plighting, promising;<BR>Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपणित
परिपणित p. p. Plighted, pledged,<BR>promised; Śi. 7. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपत्
परिपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fly round or<BR>about, wheel or whirl round, hover<BR>about; बिंदूत्क्षेपान् पिपासुः परिपतति<BR>शिखी भ्रांतिमद्वारियंत्रं M. 2. 13;<BR>Amaru. 48.<BR>--2 To spring down upon, attack,<BR>fall upon (as in battle).<BR>--3 To run<BR>in all directions; (हयाः)<BR>परिपेतुर्दिशो दश Mb.<BR>--4 To go to or fall into;<BR>Śi. 11. 41. --Caus. To shoot off or<BR>down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपतनं|परिपतन
परिपतनं Flying round or about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपतिः|परिपति
परिपतिः A protector (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपद्
परिपद् f. Ved.<BR>1 A snare, trap.<BR>--2 A living being.<BR>--3 Walking<BR>about.<BR>--4 A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपंथः|परिपन्थ|परिपन्थः
परिपंथः An antagonist, enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपथक
परिपथक An antagonist, adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपंथिन्|परिपन्थिन्
परिपंथिन् a. Standing in the way,<BR>obstructing, opposing, hindering<BR>(said by Pāṇini to be admissible<BR>only in the Veda, but see the<BR>quotations given below); अर्थपरिपंथी<BR>महानरातिः Mu. 5; नाभविष्यमहं तत्र<BR>यदि तत्परिपंथिनी Māl. 9. 50; so<BR>Bv. 1. 62, Bg. 3. 34; Ms. 7. 107, 1. 10.<BR>--m.<BR>1 An enemy, antagonist,<BR>opponent, a foe.<BR>--2 A robber, thief,<BR>highwayman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपरः|परिपर
परिपरः A tortuous or round-about<BR>way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपरिन्
परिपरिन् m. Ved. An<BR>antagonist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0676-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपवनः|परिपवन
परिपवनः<BR>1 Winnowing corn.<BR>--2<BR>A winnowing basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपा
परिपा {vI.v} {c1c} P. To drink;<BR>उपनिषदः परिपीताः Bv. 2. 40. {vII.v} {c2c} P.<BR>1<BR>To protect, preserve, guard, defend<BR>against; Y. 1. 335; Ms. 9. 251.<BR>--2<BR>To rule, govern; Māl. 10. 25.<BR>--3<BR>To bring up, nourish, support.<BR>--4<BR>To keep to, observe, adhere to,<BR>persevere in; अंगीकृतं सुकृतिनः<BR>परिपालयति Ch. P. 50.<BR>--5 To wait for,<BR>await; अथ मदनवधूरुपप्लवांतं<BR>व्यसनकृशा परिपालयांबभूव Ku. 4. 46. --Caus.<BR>1 To protect<BR>--2 To keep, maintain.<BR>--3 To wait for, expect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाकः|परिपाक
परि(री)पाकः<BR>1 Being<BR>completely cooked or dressed.<BR>--2<BR>Digestion, as in अन्नपरिपाक.<BR>--3 Ripening,<BR>maturing, development, perfection;<BR>Śi. 4. 48; Ku. 6. 10.<BR>--4 Fruit,<BR>result, consequence; प्रपन्नानां मूर्तः सुकृ<BR>तपरिपाको जनिमतां Mv. 4. 31;<BR>Bh. 2. 132, 3. 135.<BR>--5 Cleverness,<BR>shrewdness, skilfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीपाकः|परीपाक
परि(री)पाकः<BR>1 Being<BR>completely cooked or dressed.<BR>--2<BR>Digestion, as in अन्नपरिपाक.<BR>--3 Ripening,<BR>maturing, development, perfection;<BR>Śi. 4. 48; Ku. 6. 10.<BR>--4 Fruit,<BR>result, consequence; प्रपन्नानां मूर्तः सुकृ<BR>तपरिपाको जनिमतां Mv. 4. 31;<BR>Bh. 2. 132, 3. 135.<BR>--5 Cleverness,<BR>shrewdness, skilfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाटल
परिपाटल a. Pale red; R. 19. 10;<BR>Śi. 13. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाटिः|परिपाटि
परिपाटिः --टी f.<BR>1 Method,<BR>manner, course; पाटीर तव पटीयान्कः<BR>परिपाटीमिमामुरीकर्तुं Bv. 1. 12; कदंबानां<BR>वाटी रसिकपरिपाटीं स्फुटयति H. D. 24.<BR>--2 Arrangement, order, succession.<BR>--3 Arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाटी
परिपाटिः --टी f.<BR>1 Method,<BR>manner, course; पाटीर तव पटीयान्कः<BR>परिपाटीमिमामुरीकर्तुं Bv. 1. 12; कदंबानां<BR>वाटी रसिकपरिपाटीं स्फुटयति H. D. 24.<BR>--2 Arrangement, order, succession.<BR>--3 Arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपाठः|परिपाठ
परिपाठः Complete enumeration,<BR>detail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपार्श्व
परिपार्श्व a. Near, at the side,<BR>close or hard by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिपालनं|परिपालन
परिपालनं<BR>1 Protecting,<BR>defending, maintaining, keeping,<BR>sustaining; क्लिश्नति लब्धपरिपालनवृत्तिरेब<BR>Ś. 5. 6.<BR>--2 Nourishment, nurture;<BR>जातस्य परिपालनं Ms. 9. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

