परिबृंह्
परिबृं(वृं)ह् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To<BR>strengthen, fortify.<BR>--2 To increase.<BR>--3<BR>Ved. To encircle, surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंह्
परिबृं(वृं)ह् {c6c} U.<BR>1 To<BR>strengthen, fortify.<BR>--2 To increase.<BR>--3<BR>Ved. To encircle, surround.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबर्हः|परिबर्ह
परिब(व)र्हः<BR>1 Retinue, train,<BR>attendants; इयं प्रचुरपरिबर्हया भवत्या<BR>संवर्ध्यतां Dk. 108.<BR>--2 Furniture;<BR>परिवर्हवंति वेश्मानि R. 14. 15 ‘rooms<BR>properly furnished or provided with<BR>furniture’.<BR>--3 Royal insignia.<BR>--4<BR>The necessaries of life.<BR>--5 Property,<BR>wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्हः|परिवर्ह
परिब(व)र्हः<BR>1 Retinue, train,<BR>attendants; इयं प्रचुरपरिबर्हया भवत्या<BR>संवर्ध्यतां Dk. 108.<BR>--2 Furniture;<BR>परिवर्हवंति वेश्मानि R. 14. 15 ‘rooms<BR>properly furnished or provided with<BR>furniture’.<BR>--3 Royal insignia.<BR>--4<BR>The necessaries of life.<BR>--5 Property,<BR>wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबर्हणं|परिबर्हण
परिब(व)र्हणं<BR>1 Retinue, train.<BR>--2<BR>Attire, trim.<BR>--3 Growth.<BR>--4 Worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवर्हणं|परिवर्हण
परिब(व)र्हणं<BR>1 Retinue, train.<BR>--2<BR>Attire, trim.<BR>--3 Growth.<BR>--4 Worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबृंहणं|परिबृंहण
परिबृं(वृं)हणं<BR>1 Prosperity,<BR>welfare.<BR>--2 Appendix, supplement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंहणं|परिवृंहण
परिबृं(वृं)हणं<BR>1 Prosperity,<BR>welfare.<BR>--2 Appendix, supplement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिबृंहित
परिबृं(वृं)हित p. p.<BR>1 Increased,<BR>augmented.<BR>--2 Thriven, grown<BR>prosperous.<BR>--3 Accompanied by,<BR>furnished with.<BR>--तं The roar of an<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिवृंहित
परिबृं(वृं)हित p. p.<BR>1 Increased,<BR>augmented.<BR>--2 Thriven, grown<BR>prosperous.<BR>--3 Accompanied by,<BR>furnished with.<BR>--तं The roar of an<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभंगः|परिभङ्ग|परिभंग|परिभङ्गः
परिभंगः Shattering, breaking to<BR>pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभर्त्सनं|परिभर्त्सन
परिभर्त्सनं Threatening,<BR>menacing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाष्
परिभाष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To lay down a<BR>convention, speak conventionally.<BR>--2 To speak to, address.<BR>--3 To<BR>teach, explain, interpret, expound.<BR>--4 To exhort, encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषणं|परिभाषण
परिभाषणं<BR>1 Speaking, discourse,<BR>talking, chatting, gossiping.<BR>--2<BR>Expression of censure, admonition,<BR>reproof, abuse.<BR>--3 Rule, precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाषा
परिभाषा<BR>1 Speech, discourse.<BR>--2<BR>Censurc, reproof, blame, abuse.<BR>--3<BR>An explanation.<BR>--4 Terminology,<BR>technical phraseology, technical<BR>terms (used in a work); इति<BR>परिभाषाप्रकरणं Sk.; इको गुणवृद्धीत्यादिका<BR>परिभाषा Mbh.<BR>--5 (Hence) Any<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">Page0678-a+ 57</a>]<BR>general rule, precept, or definition<BR>which is applicable throughout (<BR>अनियमनिवारको न्यायविशेषः); परितः<BR>प्रमिताक्षरापि सर्वं विषयं प्राप्तवती गता प्रतिष्ठां ।<BR>न खलु प्रतिहन्यते कदाचित् परिभाषेव<BR>गरीयसी यदाज्ञा Śi. 16. 80.<BR>--6 A<BR>list of abbreviations or signs<BR>used in any work.<BR>--7 (In gram.)<BR>An explanatory Sūtra mixed up<BR>with the other Sūtras of Pāṇini,<BR>which teaches the method of<BR>applying them.<BR>--8 (In medicine)<BR>Prognosis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0677-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभिन्न
परिभिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Split open,<BR>cracked.<BR>--2 Deformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभुग्न
परिभुग्न a. Bowed, curved, bent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभुज्
परिभुज् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To eat.<BR>--2 To<BR>use, enjoy; न खलु च परिभेक्तुं नैव<BR>शक्नोमि ह तुं Ś. 5. 19; Ki. 5. 5; 8. 57.<BR>--3 To neglect to feed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभुक्त
परिभुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Eaten.<BR>--2 Used,<BR>enjoyed.<BR>--3 Possessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभोक्तृ
परिभोक्तृ a.<BR>1 Eating, enjoying,<BR>possessing.<BR>--2 Living at another's<BR>cost, using another's property<BR>illegally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभोगः|परिभोग
परिभोगः<BR>1 Enjoyment; R. 4. 45.<BR>--2 Especially, sexual enjoyment;<BR>R. 11. 52, 19. 21, 28, 30.<BR>--3<BR>IIlegal use of another's goods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभू
परिभू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To defeat, subdue,<BR>conquer, overcome; (hence) to<BR>surpass, excel; लग्नद्वि फं परिभूय पद्मं<BR>Ku. 7. 16; R. 10. 35.<BR>--2 To<BR>despise, slight, treat with contempt,<BR>disrespect, insult; मा मां महात्मन्<BR>परिभ्रः Bk. 1. 22; 4. 37.<BR>--3 To injure,<BR>destroy, ruin.<BR>--4 To afflict, grieve.<BR>--5 To humiliate, disgrace.<BR>--6 To<BR>disappear.<BR>--7 Ved. To surround,<BR>encircle.<BR>--8 To go or fly round.<BR>--9 To accompany.<BR>--10 To take care<BR>of.<BR>--11 To guide, govern. --Caus.<BR>1 To think of, reflect on, meditate,<BR>contemplate; U. 7. 20.<BR>--2 To<BR>contain, include.<BR>--3 To make known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभवः|परिभव
परि(री)भवः<BR>1 Insult, injury,<BR>humiliation, disrespect, degradation,<BR>disgrace; पराक्रमः परिभवे वैयात्यं<BR>सुरतेष्विव (भूषणं) Śi. 2. 44; R. 12. 37;<BR>Ve. 1. 25; U. 4. 23; Mu. 3. 4;<BR>Mv. 1. 40, 3. 17.<BR>--2 Defeat,<BR>discomfiture.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्पदं, --पदं {1} an<BR>object of contempt; H. 3. 51. {2} a<BR>disgrace or disgraceful situation.<BR>--विधिः humiliation; प्रायो मूर्खः<BR>परिभवविधौ नाभिमानं तनोति Ś. Til. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परीभवः|परीभव
परि(री)भवः<BR>1 Insult, injury,<BR>humiliation, disrespect, degradation,<BR>disgrace; पराक्रमः परिभवे वैयात्यं<BR>सुरतेष्विव (भूषणं) Śi. 2. 44; R. 12. 37;<BR>Ve. 1. 25; U. 4. 23; Mu. 3. 4;<BR>Mv. 1. 40, 3. 17.<BR>--2 Defeat,<BR>discomfiture.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्पदं, --पदं {1} an<BR>object of contempt; H. 3. 51. {2} a<BR>disgrace or disgraceful situation.<BR>--विधिः humiliation; प्रायो मूर्खः<BR>परिभवविधौ नाभिमानं तनोति Ś. Til. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभविन्
परिभविन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1<BR>Humiliating, treating with disrespect or<BR>contempt.<BR>--2 Suffering disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावः|परिभाव
परिभावः See परिभव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावनं|परिभावन
परिभावनं Union, cohesion.<BR>--नं,<BR>--ना Contemplation, meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावित
परिभावित p. p.<BR>1 Contained,<BR>included.<BR>--2 Pervaded.<BR>--3 Penetrated.<BR>--4<BR>Conceived.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभाविन्
परिभाविन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1<BR>Humiliating, despising, treating with<BR>contempt; Ś. 4.<BR>--2 Putting to shame,<BR>surpassing, excelling.<BR>--3 Setting at<BR>naught, defying; वैद्ययत्नपरिभाविनं गदं<BR>R. 19. 53 ‘defying medical<BR>remedies’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभावुक
परिभावुक a. Contemning,<BR>shaming &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूतिः|परिभूति
परिभूतिः f. Contempt, insult,<BR>disrespect, humiliation; Mu. 4. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूष्
परिभूष् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To decorate,<BR>adorn.<BR>--2 To serve, wait upon.<BR>--3<BR>To honour, worship.<BR>--4 To take<BR>care of.<BR>--5 To observe, follow.<BR>--6<BR>To prepare, equip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभूषणः|परिभूषण
परिभूषणः (scil. संधि) Peace<BR>obtained by the cession of the whole<BR>revenue of a land.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रंश्
परिभ्रंश् {c1c} A., {c4c} P.<BR>1 To fall or<BR>drop down, tumble, slip.<BR>--2 To<BR>stray from, go astray.<BR>--3 To fall<BR>away from, swerve, deviate.<BR>--4 To<BR>lose, be deprived of; Ms. 10. 20.<BR>--5 To escape.<BR>--6 To neglect, omit.<BR>--7 To disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रंशः|परिभ्रंश
परिभ्रंशः<BR>1 Escape.<BR>--2 Falling<BR>from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रंशनं|परिभ्रंशन
परिभ्रंशनं Falling from. --Losse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रष्ट
परिभ्रष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Fallen or<BR>dropped off.<BR>--2 Escaped.<BR>--3 Cast down,<BR>degraded.<BR>--4 Deprived of, devoid<BR>of (with abl. or instr.);<BR>Pt. 4. 93.<BR>--5 Neglecting.<BR>--6 Vanished.<BR>--7 Lost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रम्
परिभ्रम् {c1c} {c4c} P.<BR>1 To rove,<BR>wander about, ramble, move to and fro;<BR>परिभ्रमसि किं वृथा क्वचन चित्त<BR>विश्रम्यताम् Bh. 3. 137.<BR>--2 To hover, whirl<BR>round; परिभ्रमन्मूर्धजषट्पदाकुलैः<BR>Ki. 5. 14.<BR>--3 To revolve, rotate, move or<BR>turn round.<BR>--4 To wander or roam<BR>over (with acc.); भुवं परिबभ्राम.<BR>--5 To<BR>turn round (anything),<BR>circumambulate.<BR>--6 To encircle. --Caus. To<BR>bewilder, overwhelm, overpower;<BR>U. 3. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रमः|परिभ्रम
परिभ्रमः<BR>1 Wandering, going<BR>about.<BR>--2 Rambling discourse,<BR>circumlocution, periphrasis.<BR>--3 Error,<BR>delusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिभ्रमणं|परिभ्रमण
परिभ्रमणं<BR>1 Going about, roaming,<BR>wandering.<BR>--2 Revolving, turning<BR>round.<BR>--3 Circumference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमंडल|परिमण्डल|परिमण्डलं|परिमण्डलः
परिमंडल a.<BR>1 Globular, round,<BR>circular.<BR>--2 Of the measure of an<BR>atom.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A globe, sphere.<BR>--2<BR>A ball.<BR>--3 A circle.<BR>--4 An orb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमंथर|परिमन्थर
परिमंथर a. Extremely slow;<BR>Śi. 9. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमंद|परिमन्द
परिमंद a.<BR>1 Very dull or dim,<BR>quite faint; परिमंदसूर्यनयनो दिवसः<BR>Śi. 9. 3.<BR>--2 Very slow.<BR>--3 Very<BR>thin or weak; Śi. 2. 39.<BR>--4 Very<BR>little; Śi. 9. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमरः|परिमर
परिमरः<BR>1 Destruction;<BR>चिरात्क्षत्रस्यास्तु प्रलय इव घोरः परिमरः<BR>Mv. 3. 41.<BR>--2 The wind.<BR>--3 A magical<BR>rite for the destruction of enemies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमलः|परिमल
परिमलः<BR>1 Fragrance, perfume,<BR>scent; परिमलो गीर्वाणचेतोहरः<BR>Bv. 1. 63, 66, 70, 71; Me. 25.<BR>--2<BR>Pounding or trituration of fragrant<BR>substances.<BR>--3 A fragrant<BR>substance.<BR>--4 Copulation; अथ<BR>परिमलजामवाप्य लक्ष्मीं Ki. 10. 1.<BR>--5 A<BR>meeting of learned men.<BR>--6 A stain,<BR>spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमलित
परिमलित a.<BR>1 Perfumed.<BR>--2<BR>Soiled, despoiled of beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमा
परिमा {c2c} P., {c3c} {c4c} A.<BR>1 To<BR>measure.<BR>--2 To measure off, limit<BR>--3 To<BR>estimate, determine.<BR>--4 To fulfil (a<BR>period or course).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0678-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

परिमाणं|परिमाण
