पल्लः|पल्ल
पल्लः A large granary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवः|पल्लव|पल्लवं
पल्लवः --वं<BR>1 A sprout, sprig, twig<BR>करपल्लवः; लतेव संनद्धमनोज्ञपल्लवा<BR>R. 3. 7.<BR>--2 A bud, blossom.<BR>--3<BR>Expansion, spreading, dilating.<BR>--4 The red<BR>dye called Alakta, q. v.<BR>--5 Strength,<BR>power.<BR>--6 A blade of grass.<BR>--7 A<BR>bracelet, an armlet.<BR>--8 Love,<BR>amorous sport.<BR>--9 The end of a robe or<BR>garment.<BR>--10 Unsteadiness (चापलं).<BR>--वः A libertine.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकुरः<BR>--आधारः a branch.<BR>--अदः a deer.<BR>--अस्त्रः an epithet of the god of<BR>love.<BR>--आपीडित a. full of or laden<BR>with buds.<BR>--ग्राहिता {1} dealing with<BR>trifles. {2} superficial knowledge.<BR>--ग्राहिन् a. {1} putting forth sprouts.<BR>{2} dealing with trifles. {3}<BR>diffusive or superficial.<BR>--द्रुः the Aśoka<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवं|पल्लव|पल्लवः
पल्लवः --वं<BR>1 A sprout, sprig, twig<BR>करपल्लवः; लतेव संनद्धमनोज्ञपल्लवा<BR>R. 3. 7.<BR>--2 A bud, blossom.<BR>--3<BR>Expansion, spreading, dilating.<BR>--4 The red<BR>dye called Alakta, q. v.<BR>--5 Strength,<BR>power.<BR>--6 A blade of grass.<BR>--7 A<BR>bracelet, an armlet.<BR>--8 Love,<BR>amorous sport.<BR>--9 The end of a robe or<BR>garment.<BR>--10 Unsteadiness (चापलं).<BR>--वः A libertine.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकुरः<BR>--आधारः a branch.<BR>--अदः a deer.<BR>--अस्त्रः an epithet of the god of<BR>love.<BR>--आपीडित a. full of or laden<BR>with buds.<BR>--ग्राहिता {1} dealing with<BR>trifles. {2} superficial knowledge.<BR>--ग्राहिन् a. {1} putting forth sprouts.<BR>{2} dealing with trifles. {3}<BR>diffusive or superficial.<BR>--द्रुः the Aśoka<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवकः|पल्लवक
पल्लवकः<BR>1 A libertine.<BR>--2 A<BR>catamite.<BR>--3 The paramour of a harlot.<BR>--4 The Aśoka tree.<BR>--5 A kind of<BR>fish.<BR>--6 A sprout; (n. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवति
पल्लवति, पल्लवयति Den. P.<BR>1 To put<BR>forth sprouts, bud.<BR>--2 To expand,<BR>spread, make prolix or diffuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवयति
पल्लवति, पल्लवयति Den. P.<BR>1 To put<BR>forth sprouts, bud.<BR>--2 To expand,<BR>spread, make prolix or diffuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लविकः|पल्लविक
पल्लविकः<BR>1 A libertine, a gallant.<BR>--2 A catamite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लवित|पल्लवितं|पल्लवितः
पल्लवित a.<BR>1 Sprouting, having<BR>young shoots or sprouts.<BR>--2 Spread,<BR>extended; अलं पल्लवितेन ‘enough of<BR>further amplification or<BR>expatiation’.<BR>--3 Dyed red with lac.<BR>--तः<BR>Lac-dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लविन्
पल्लविन् a. (नी f.) Having young<BR>shoots or leaves; Ku. 3. 54. --m.<BR>A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लिः|पल्लि
पल्लिः --ल्ली f.<BR>1 A small village.<BR>--2 A hut.<BR>--3 A house, station.<BR>--4<BR>A city or town (at the end of<BR>names of towns); as त्रिशिरपल्ली.<BR>--5 A<BR>house-lizard.<BR>--6 A creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्ली
पल्लिः --ल्ली f.<BR>1 A small village.<BR>--2 A hut.<BR>--3 A house, station.<BR>--4<BR>A city or town (at the end of<BR>names of towns); as त्रिशिरपल्ली.<BR>--5 A<BR>house-lizard.<BR>--6 A creeping plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्लिका
पल्लिका<BR>1 A small village or<BR>station.<BR>--2 A house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पल्वलं|पल्वल
पल्वलं A small pool or pond,<BR>a puddle, tank (अल्पं सरः); स<BR>पल्वलजलेऽधुना… कथं वर्ततां Bv. 1. 3;<BR>R. 2. 17; 3. 3.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवासः a<BR>tortoise.<BR>--पंकः the mud of a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवः|पव|पवं
पवः [पू-भावे-अप्]<BR>1 Wind.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-a" target="_blank">Page0688-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Purification.<BR>--3 A marsh.<BR>--4<BR>Winnowing corn.<BR>--वा Purification.<BR>--वं<BR>Cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0687-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवन|पवनं|पवनः
पवन a. Clean, pure.<BR>--नः [<BR>पूल्यु]<BR>1 Air, wind; सर्पाः पिबंति पवन<BR>न च दुर्बलास्ते Subhāṣ.; पवनपदवी,<BR>पवनसुतः &c.<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 A<BR>householder's sacred fire.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Purification.<BR>--2 Winnowing.<BR>--3 A<BR>sieve, strainer.<BR>--4 Water.<BR>--5 A<BR>potter's kiln (m. also).<BR>--नी A broom.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अशनः, --भुज् m. a<BR>serpent.<BR>--आत्मजः {1} an epithet of<BR>Hanumat. {2} of Bhīma. {3} fire.<BR>--आशः a serpent, snake. ˚नाशः {1}<BR>an epithet of Garuḍa. {2} a peacock.<BR>--तनयः, --सुतः {1} epithets of<BR>Hanumat. {2} of Bhīma.<BR>--वाहनः fire.<BR>--व्याधिः {1} an epithet of Uddhava,<BR>a friend and counsellor of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>{2} rheumatism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवमानः|पवमान
पवमानः [पृ-ताच्छील्ये शानच्]<BR>1 Air,<BR>wind; पवमानः पृथिवीरुहानिव R. 8. 9.<BR>--2 One of the sacred fires,<BR>considered to be the same as गार्हपत्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित|पवितः
पवित a. Purified, cleansed.<BR>--तं<BR>Black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवाका
पवाका A whirl-wind, a<BR>hurricane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पविः|पवि
पविः<BR>1 The thunderbolt of<BR>Indra.<BR>--2 Ved. The tire of a wheel.<BR>--3 The point of a spear or arrow.<BR>--4 An arrow.<BR>--5 Speech.<BR>--6 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्र|पवित्रं|पवित्रः
पवित्र a. [पू करणे इत्र]<BR>1 Sacred,<BR>holy, sinless, sanctified (persons or<BR>things); त्रीणि श्राद्धे पवित्राणि दौहित्रः<BR>कुतपस्तिलाः Ms. 3. 235; पवित्रो नरः,<BR>पवित्रं स्थानं &c.<BR>--2 Purified by the<BR>performance of ceremonial acts<BR>(such as sacrifices &c.).<BR>--3<BR>Purifying, removing sin.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1 An<BR>instrument for cleansing or<BR>purifying, such as a sieve or strainer &c.<BR>--2 Two blades of Kuśa grass used<BR>at sacrifices in purifying and<BR>sprinkling ghee.<BR>--3 A ring of Kuśa<BR>grass worn on the fourth finger on<BR>certain religious occasions.<BR>--4 The<BR>sacred thread worn by members of<BR>the first three castes of the Hindus.<BR>--5 Copper.<BR>--6 Rain.<BR>--7 Water.<BR>--8<BR>Rubbing, cleansing.<BR>--9 A vessel<BR>in which the arghya is presented.<BR>--10 Clarified butter.<BR>--11 Honey.<BR>--त्रा<BR>1 The holy basil.<BR>--2 Turmeric.<BR>(पवित्रीकृ ‘to purify, sanctify’;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-b" target="_blank">Page0688-b+ 57</a>]<BR>पवित्रीभू ‘to become pure or holy’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आरोपणं, आरोहणं<BR>investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>--धान्यं barley.<BR>--पाणि a. holding darbha<BR>grass in the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रकं|पवित्रक|पवित्रकः
पवित्रकं A net or rope made of<BR>hemp or pack-thread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रयति
पवित्रयति Den. P., To purify,<BR>cleanse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रवत्|पवित्रवन्त्
पवित्रवत् a.<BR>1 Having a strainer<BR>or purifying instrument.<BR>--2<BR>Purifying, cleansing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवित्रिन्
पवित्रिन् a.<BR>1 Purifying.<BR>--2 Clean,<BR>pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पवीरं|पवीर
पवीरं Ved. A spear, lance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुः|पशु
पशुः [सर्वमविशेषेण पश्यति, दृश्-कु<BR>पशादेशः]<BR>1 Cattle (both singly and<BR>collectively); Ms. 9. 327, 331.<BR>--2<BR>An animal in general.<BR>--3 A<BR>sacrificial animal, such as a goat; an<BR>oblation, a victim.<BR>--4 A brute,<BR>beast; often added to words<BR>meaning ‘man’ to show contempt;<BR>पुरुषपशोश्च पशोश्च को विशेषः H. 1; cf.<BR>नृपशु, नरपशु &c.<BR>--5 N. of a<BR>subordinate deity and one of Śiva's<BR>followers.<BR>--6 An uninitiated person.<BR>--7 The soul, the Supreme spirit.<BR>--8<BR>A sacrifice in which an animal is<BR>killed.<BR>--9 Fire.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवदानं<BR>a sacrifice of animals.<BR>--क्रिया {1} the<BR>act of animal sacrifice. {2}<BR>copulation.<BR>--गायत्री a Mantra whispered<BR>into the ear of an animal which is<BR>about to be sacrificed; it is a parody<BR>of the celebrated Gāyatrī q. v.;<BR>पशुपाशाय विद्महे शिरश्छेदाय (विश्वकर्मणे)<BR>वीमहि । तन्नो जीवः प्रचोदयात्.<BR>--घातः<BR>slaughter of animals for sacrifice.<BR>--चर्या copulation.<BR>--देवता the deity<BR>to whom an animal is offered.<BR>--धर्मः {1} the nature or<BR>characteristics of cattle. {2} treatment of<BR>cattle. {3} promiscuous<BR>cohabitation; Ms. 9. 66. {4} the marrying of<BR>widows.<BR>--नाथः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--पः a herdsman.<BR>--पतिः {1} an<BR>epithet of Śiva; Me. 36, 56;<BR>Ku. 6. 95. {2} a herdsman, owner of cattle.<BR>{3} N. of a philosopher who taught<BR>the philosophical doctrine called<BR>पाशुपत; see Sarva. S. ad loc.<BR>--पालः,<BR>--पालकः a herdsman.<BR>--पालनं, --रक्षणं<BR>the tending or rearing of cattle.<BR>--पाशः {1} the cord with which the<BR>sacrificial animal is bound. {2} an<BR>animal-sacrifice. {3} the bonds which<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-c" target="_blank">Page0688-c+ 57</a>]<BR>enchain the individual soul.<BR>--पाशक<BR>kind of coitus or mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR>--प्रेरणं the driving of<BR>cattle.<BR>--बंधः an animal-sacrifice<BR>--मारं ind. according to the manner<BR>of slaughtering animals; इष्टिपशुमार<BR>मारितः Ś. 6.<BR>--यज्ञः, --यागः, --द्रव्यं an<BR>animal-sacrifice.<BR>--रज्जुः f. a cord for<BR>tethering cattle.<BR>--राजः a lion.<BR>--ष<BR>a. Ved. giving cattle.<BR>--समाम्नायः a<BR>collection of names for animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशव्य|पशव्यं
पशव्य a.<BR>1 Fit or suitable for<BR>cattle; Y. 1. 321.<BR>--2 Relating to<BR>cattle, or to a herd or drove.<BR>--3<BR>Possessed of cattle.<BR>--4 Brutish.<BR>--व्यं<BR>1 A herd of cattle.<BR>--2 A stall for<BR>cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुका
पशुका Any small animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पशुता
पशुता<BR>1 Brutality.<BR>--2 The sacrifice<BR>of an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्च
पश्च a.<BR>1 Being behind.<BR>--2<BR>Posterior, later.<BR>--3 Western.<BR>--श्चा ind.<BR>Ved.<BR>1 Behind, after.<BR>--2<BR>Afterwards.<BR>--3 Westward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चात्
पश्चात् ind. (Used by itself or<BR>with gen. or abl.)<BR>1 From behind,<BR>from the back; पश्चाद्वद्धपुरुषमादाय<BR>Ś. 6; पश्चा दुच्चैर्भवति हरिणः<BR>स्वांगमायच्छमानः Ś. 4 v. {1}<BR>--2 Behind, backwards,<BR>towards the back (opp. पुरः);<BR>गच्छति पुरः शरीरं धावति पश्चादसंरतुतं चेतः<BR>Ś. 1. 34; 3. 8.<BR>--3 After (in time or<BR>space), then, afterwards,<BR>subsequently; लध्वी पुरा वृद्धिमती च पश्चात्<BR>Bh. 2. 60; तस्य पश्चात् ‘after him’;<BR>R. 4. 30, 12. 7, 17, 39; 16. 29;<BR>Me. 36, 44.<BR>--4 At last, lastly, finally.<BR>--5<BR>From the west.<BR>--6 Towards the<BR>west, westward.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत a.<BR>left behind, surpassed, thrown into<BR>the back-ground; पश्चात्कृताः<BR>स्निग्धजनाशिषोपि Ku. 7. 28; R. 17. 18.<BR>तापः repentance, contrition; ˚पं कृ<BR>to repent.<BR>--बातः a west wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चार्धः|पश्चार्ध|पश्चार्द्धः
पश्चार्धः [अपरश्चासौ अर्धः]<BR>1 The<BR>hinder part or side (of the body);<BR>पश्चार्धेन प्रविष्टः शरपतनभयाद्भूयसा<BR>पूर्वकायं Ś. 1. 7.<BR>--2 The latter half.<BR>--3<BR>The western side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चिम|पश्चिमं
पश्चिम a. [पश्चाद्भवः डिमच्]<BR>1 Being<BR>behind, hindmost.<BR>--2 Last (in time<BR>or space); पाश्चिमे वयसि वर्तमानस्य<BR>K. 25; R. 19. 1, 54;<BR>पश्चिमाद्यामिनीयामात्प्रसादमिव चेतना R. 17. 1; स्मरंतः<BR>पश्चिमामाज्ञां 17. 8; पत पश्चिमयोः पितुः<BR>पादयोः Mu. 7; ˚क्रिया the last i. e.<BR>funeral rites; ˚अवस्था last state<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">Page0689-a+ 55</a>]<BR>(verging on death); Pt. 2.<BR>--3<BR>Western, westerly; Ms. 2. 22;<BR>5. 92. (पश्चिमेन is used adverbially in<BR>the sense of ‘in the west;’ or<BR>‘after, behind’; with acc. or gen.;<BR>so पश्चिमे ‘in the west’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्धः {1} the latter half. {2} the hinder<BR>part.<BR>--उत्तर a. north western.<BR>--रात्रः<BR>the latter part of the night, उपारताः<BR>पश्चिमरात्रगोचरात् Ki. 4. 10. v. {1}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0688-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्चिमा
पश्चिमा The west.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्तरा<BR>the north-west.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यत्
पश्यत् a. (न्ती f.) Seing,<BR>perceiving, beholding, looking at,<BR>observing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यतोहरः|पश्यतोहर
पश्यतोहरः A thief, robber,<BR>highwayman (one who steals before a<BR>person's eyes, or in the very sight of<BR>the possessor; as, for instance, a<BR>goldsmith).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पश्यंती
पश्यंती<BR>1 A harlot, courtezan.<BR>--2<BR>A particular sound; cf. Malli. on<BR>Ku. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पसस्
पसस् n. Ved. Membrum virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्त्यं|पस्त्य
पस्त्यं<BR>1 A house, habitation,<BR>abode; पस्त्यं प्रयातुमथ तं प्रभुरापपृच्छे<BR>Kīr. K. 9. 74.<BR>--2 Household,<BR>family.<BR>--3 Ved. Divine progeny.<BR>--4<BR>A man.<BR>--5 A priest.<BR>--स्त्या The<BR>goddess presiding over domestic<BR>affairs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्त्यावत्|पस्त्यावन्त्
पस्त्यावत्^1 m. Ved. A householder.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: changed according to the spelling of RV 1.151.2, 2.11.16, 4.54.5, 8.7.29, 9.97.18 - always with long ā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पस्पशः|पस्पश
पस्पशः<BR>1 N. of the first Āhnika<BR>of the first chapter of Patañjali's<BR>Mahābhāṣya; शब्दविद्येव नो भाति<BR>राजनीतिरपस्पशा Śi. 2. 112 (where<BR>अपस्पश also means ‘without spies’.)<BR>--2 (Fig.) An introductory chapter<BR>in general (उपोद्घात).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्नवाः
पह्न(ह्ल)वाः^1, पह्लिकाः (m. pl.)<BR>N. of a people; (the Persians?).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्लवाः
पह्न(ह्ल)वाः^1, पह्लिकाः (m. pl.)<BR>N. of a people; (the Persians?).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पह्लिकाः
पह्न(ह्ल)वाः^1, पह्लिकाः (m. pl.)<BR>N. of a people; (the Persians?).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
पा {vI.v} {c1c} P. (पिबति, पीत; pass.<BR>पीयते)<BR>1 To drink, quaff; पिब स्तन्यं<BR>पोत Bv. 1. 60; दुःशासनस्य रुधिरं न<BR>पिबाम्युरस्तः Ve. 1. 15; R. 3. 54;<BR>Ku. 3. 36; Māl. 8. 5; Bk. 14. 92;<BR>15. 6.<BR>--2 To kiss; पिबत्यसौ पाययते<BR>च सिंधूः R. 13. 9, Ś. 1. 24.<BR>--3 To<BR>drink in, inhale; R. 7. 63.<BR>--4 To<BR>drink in (with the eyes or ears),<BR>feast on, look at or listen to<BR>intently; समदुःखः पीयते नयनाभ्यां V. 1;<BR>निवातपद्मस्तिमितेन चक्षुषा नृपस्य कांतं<BR>पिबतः सुताननं R. 3. 17; 2. 19, 73;<BR>11. 36; 13. 30; Me. 16;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-b" target="_blank">Page0689-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Ku. 7. 64.<BR>--5 To absorb, drink or swallow<BR>up; (बाणैः) आयुर्देहातिगैः पीतं रुधिरं तु<BR>पतत्रिमिः R. 12. 48.<BR>--6 To drink<BR>intoxicating liquors. --Caus. (<BR>पाययति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to drink, give<BR>to drink; R. 13. 9;<BR>Bk. 8. 41, 62.<BR>--2 To water. --Desid. (<BR>पिपासति) To wish to drink &c.;<BR>हालाहलं खलु पिपासति कौतुकेन Bv. 1. 95.<BR>{vII.v} {c2c} P. (पाति, पात)<BR>1 To protect,<BR>guard, keep, defend, preserve; (oft.<BR>with abl.); पर्याप्तोसि प्रजाः पातुं<BR>R. 10. 25; पातु त्वा… … भूतेशस्य<BR>भुजंगवल्लिवलयस्रङ्नद्धजूटा जटाः Māl. 1. 2; जीवन्<BR>पुनः शश्वदुपप्लवेभ्यः प्रजाः प्रजानाथ पितेव<BR>पासि R. 2. 48.<BR>--2 To rule, govern;<BR>पातु पृथ्वीं…भूपाः Mk. 10. 60.<BR>--3<BR>To beware of.<BR>--4 Ved. To observe,<BR>notice.<BR>--5 To keep, observe, tend,<BR>take notice of. --Caus. (पालयति-ते)<BR>1 To protect, guard, keep, preserve;<BR>कथं दुष्ठुः स्वयं धर्मे प्रजास्त्वं पालयिष्यसि<BR>Bk. 6. 132; Ms. 9. 108; R. 9. 2.<BR>--2 To rule, govern; तां पुरीं पालयामास<BR>Rām.<BR>--3 To observe, keep, adhere<BR>to, fulfil (as a vow or promise);<BR>पालितसंगराय R. 13. 65.<BR>--4 To bring<BR>up, nourish, maintain.<BR>--5 To wait<BR>for; अत्रोपविश्य मुहूर्तमार्यः पालयतु<BR>कृष्णागमनं Ve. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पा
पा a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>1<BR>Drinking, quaffing; as in सोमपाः,<BR>अग्रेपाः &c.<BR>--2 Protecting, guarding,<BR>keeping; गोपा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुः|पांसु
पांसुः(शुः)<BR>1 Dust, dirt;<BR>crumbling soil; R. 2. 2; Rs. 1. 13;<BR>Y. 1. 150.<BR>--2 A particle of dust.<BR>--3 Dung,<BR>manure.<BR>--4 A kind of camphor.<BR>--5<BR>Landed property.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कासीसं<BR>sulphate of iron.<BR>--कुली a high-road,<BR>highway.<BR>--कूलं {1} a dust-heap. {2}<BR>a legal document not made out in<BR>any particular person's name (<BR>निरुपपदशासनं).<BR>--कृत a. covered with dust.<BR>--क्षारं-जं a kind of salt.<BR>--चत्वरं hail.<BR>--चंदनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--चामरः<BR>{1} a heap of dust. {2} a tent. {3} a<BR>bank covered with Dūrvā grass. {4}<BR>praise.<BR>--जालिकः an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--पटलं a mass or coating<BR>of dust.<BR>--मर्दनः an excavation for<BR>water round the root of a tree,<BR>a trench or basin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुः|पांशु
पांसुः(शुः)<BR>1 Dust, dirt;<BR>crumbling soil; R. 2. 2; Rs. 1. 13;<BR>Y. 1. 150.<BR>--2 A particle of dust.<BR>--3 Dung,<BR>manure.<BR>--4 A kind of camphor.<BR>--5<BR>Landed property.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कासीसं<BR>sulphate of iron.<BR>--कुली a high-road,<BR>highway.<BR>--कूलं {1} a dust-heap. {2}<BR>a legal document not made out in<BR>any particular person's name (<BR>निरुपपदशासनं).<BR>--कृत a. covered with dust.<BR>--क्षारं-जं a kind of salt.<BR>--चत्वरं hail.<BR>--चंदनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--चामरः<BR>{1} a heap of dust. {2} a tent. {3} a<BR>bank covered with Dūrvā grass. {4}<BR>praise.<BR>--जालिकः an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--पटलं a mass or coating<BR>of dust.<BR>--मर्दनः an excavation for<BR>water round the root of a tree,<BR>a trench or basin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसन|पांसनः
पांस(श)न a. (ना or नी f.)<BR>(Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>1<BR>Disgracing, dishonouring, defiling;<BR>पौलस्त्यकुलपांसन Mv. 5.<BR>--2 Vitiating<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">Page0689-c+ 57</a>]<BR>spoiling.<BR>--3 Wicked, contemptible.<BR>--4 Infamous.<BR>--नं Contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशन
पांस(श)न a. (ना or नी f.)<BR>(Usually at the end of comp.)<BR>1<BR>Disgracing, dishonouring, defiling;<BR>पौलस्त्यकुलपांसन Mv. 5.<BR>--2 Vitiating<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">Page0689-c+ 57</a>]<BR>spoiling.<BR>--3 Wicked, contemptible.<BR>--4 Infamous.<BR>--नं Contempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसव
पांस(श)व a. Consisting of dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशव|पांशवः
पांस(श)व a. Consisting of dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुका
पांसुका A menstruous woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुरः|पांसुर
पांसु(शु)रः<BR>1 A gad-fly.<BR>--2 A<BR>cripple moved about in a wheel-ehair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुरः|पांशुर
पांसु(शु)रः<BR>1 A gad-fly.<BR>--2 A<BR>cripple moved about in a wheel-ehair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांसुल|पांसुलः
पांसु(शु)ल a. [पांसुरस्त्यस्य सिध्मा˚ लच्]<BR>1 Dusty, covered with dust;<BR>Māl. 2. 4.<BR>--2 Polluted, defiled, sullied,<BR>stained; दारत्यागी भवाम्याहो<BR>परस्त्रीस्पर्शपांशुलः Ś. 5. 29.<BR>--3 Defiling,<BR>disgracing, dishonouring; as in<BR>कुलपांसुल.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A profligate or licentious<BR>person, libertine, gallant.<BR>--2 One of<BR>the weapons of Śiva.<BR>--3 An epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--ला<BR>1 A menstruous<BR>woman.<BR>--2 An unchaste or licentious<BR>woman; अ˚ a chaste woman;<BR>R. 2. 2.<BR>--3 The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांशुल|पांशुलः
पांसु(शु)ल a. [पांसुरस्त्यस्य सिध्मा˚ लच्]<BR>1 Dusty, covered with dust;<BR>Māl. 2. 4.<BR>--2 Polluted, defiled, sullied,<BR>stained; दारत्यागी भवाम्याहो<BR>परस्त्रीस्पर्शपांशुलः Ś. 5. 29.<BR>--3 Defiling,<BR>disgracing, dishonouring; as in<BR>कुलपांसुल.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A profligate or licentious<BR>person, libertine, gallant.<BR>--2 One of<BR>the weapons of Śiva.<BR>--3 An epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--ला<BR>1 A menstruous<BR>woman.<BR>--2 An unchaste or licentious<BR>woman; अ˚ a chaste woman;<BR>R. 2. 2.<BR>--3 The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक|पाकः
पाक a.<BR>1 Small.<BR>--2 Praiseworthy.<BR>--3 Of perfected or matured<BR>intellect.<BR>--4 Ved. Very young.<BR>--5<BR>Simple, genuine<BR>--6 Honest, sincere.<BR>--7 Ignorant.<BR>--कः<BR>1 [पच्-घञ्]<BR>Cooking, dressing, baking, boiling.<BR>--2 Burning (as bricks), baking;<BR>Ms. 5. 122; Y. 1. 187.<BR>--3 Digestion (as<BR>of food).<BR>--4 Ripeness; ओषध्यः<BR>फलपाकांताः Ms. 1. 46; पलमभिमुखपाकं<BR>राजजंबूद्रुमस्य V. 4. 13; Māl. 9. 31.<BR>--5 Maturity, full or perfect<BR>development; धी˚, मति˚<BR>--6 Completion,<BR>accomplishment, fulfilment; युयोज<BR>पाकाभिमुखैर्भृत्यान् विज्ञापनाफलैः<BR>R. 17. 40.<BR>--7 Result, consequence, fruit,<BR>fruition (fig also); आशीर्भिरेधयामासुः<BR>पुरःपाकाभिरंबिकां Ku. 6. 90;<BR>पाकाभिमुखस्य दैवस्य U. 7. 4; Mv. 4. 14.<BR>--8<BR>Development of the consequences of<BR>acts done.<BR>--9 Grain, corn;<BR>नीवारपाकादि R. 5. 9 (पच्यते इति पाकः धान्यं).<BR>--10 Ripeness, suppuration (as of a<BR>boil).<BR>--11 Greyness of hair caused<BR>by old age.<BR>--12 A domestic fire.<BR>--13 An owl.<BR>--14 A child, young<BR>one.<BR>--15 N. of a demon killed by<BR>Indra.<BR>--16 An abscess, ulcer.<BR>--17<BR>A vessel, cooking-utensil.<BR>--18<BR>General fear and panic such as causes a<BR>revolution or some national calamity.<BR>--19 The subversion of a country.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अगारः --रं, --आगारः --रं, --शाला,<BR>--स्थानं a kitchen.<BR>--अतीसारः chronic<BR>dysentery.<BR>--अभिमुख a. {1} ready for<BR>ripeness or development. {2}<BR>inclined to favour.<BR>--ज a. produced by<BR>heat. (जं) {1} black salt. {2}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">Page0690-a+ 55</a>]<BR>flatulence.<BR>--पात्रं, --भांडं a cooking-utensil.<BR>--पुटी a potter's kiln.<BR>--यज्ञः a simple<BR>or domestic sacrifice (for some<BR>varieties of it, see Kull. on<BR>Ms. 2. 143).<BR>--शुक्ला chalk.<BR>--शासनः, --द्विष्,<BR>--हंतृ m. epithets of Indra;<BR>Ku. 2. 63.<BR>--शासनिः {1} an epithet of<BR>Jayanta, son of Indra. {2} of Vāli. {3} of<BR>Arjuna.<BR>--स्थानं {1} a kitchen. {2} a<BR>potter's kiln.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0689-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकलः|पाकल|पाकलं
पाकलः<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 Wind.<BR>--3 A<BR>fever to which elephants are<BR>subject; cf. कूटपाकल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिन्
पाकिन् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>1 Becoming ripe, ripening.<BR>--2 Being<BR>digested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकिम|पाकिमं
पाकिम a.<BR>1 Cooked, dressed.<BR>--2<BR>Ripened (naturally or artificially).<BR>Got by boiling (as salt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकुः|पाकु
पाकुः, --पाकुकः A cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाकुकः|पाकुक
पाकुः, --पाकुकः A cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्य|पाक्यं|पाक्यः
पाक्य a. To be cooked, dressed,<BR>matured &c.<BR>--क्यः Salt-petre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्ष
पाक्ष a. (क्षी f.) [पक्षे भवः अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to a lunar fortnight,<BR>fortnightly.<BR>--2 Relating to a party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षपातिक
पाक्षपातिक a. (की f.) Partial,<BR>factious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाक्षिक|पाक्षिकः
पाक्षिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Belonging<BR>to a fortnight, fortnightly.<BR>--2<BR>Belonging to a bird.<BR>--3 Favouring<BR>a party of faction.<BR>--4 Belonging<BR>to an argument.<BR>--5 Optional,<BR>subject to an alternative, allowed but<BR>not specifically laid down; नियमः<BR>पाक्षेके सति.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A fowler.<BR>--2 An<BR>alternative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाखंडः|पाखण्ड|पाखंड|पाखण्डः
पाखंडः A heretic; पाखंडचंडालयोः<BR>पापारंभकयोर्मृगीव वृकयोर्भीरुर्गता गोचरं<BR>Māl. 5. 24; दुरात्मन् पाखंडचंडाल<BR>Māl. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पागल|पागलः
पागल a. Mad, demented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांक्त
पांक्त a. (क्ती f.) Ved.<BR>1 Consisting<BR>of five parts, fivefold.<BR>--2 Having ten<BR>limbs (as a man or beast).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांक्तेय|पाङ्क्तेय
पांक्तेय, पांक्त्य a.<BR>1 Fit to sit in<BR>the same row at a dinner-party.<BR>--2<BR>Fit to be associated with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांक्त्य|पाङ्क्त्य
पांक्तेय, पांक्त्य a.<BR>1 Fit to sit in<BR>the same row at a dinner-party.<BR>--2<BR>Fit to be associated with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांगुल्यं|पाङ्गुल्य
पांगुल्यं Limping, halting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचक|पाचकं|पाचकः
पाचक a. [पच्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 Cooking,<BR>baking.<BR>--2 Maturing, bringing to<BR>maturity.<BR>--3 Digestive, tonic.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A cook.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--कं Gall, bile.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्त्री a female cook.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचन|पाचनं|पाचनः
पाचन a. (नी f.) [पाचयति कर्तरि ल्युः<BR>पाच्यतेऽनेन करणे ल्युट् वा]<BR>1 Cooking.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">Page0690-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 Ripening.<BR>--3 Digestive.<BR>--4<BR>Softening, relaxing.<BR>--5 Suppurative.<BR>--नः<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 Sourness, acidity.<BR>--नं<BR>1 The act of cooking.<BR>--2 The<BR>act of ripening.<BR>--3 A dissolvent,<BR>digestive medicine.<BR>--4 Causing a<BR>wound to close.<BR>--5 Penance,<BR>expiation (प्रायश्चित्त).<BR>--6 Infusion,<BR>decoction.<BR>--7 Extracting extraneous<BR>substances from a wound.<BR>--8 A<BR>cataplasm.<BR>--9 A substance used in<BR>closing wounds or restraining<BR>bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनकः|पाचनक
पाचनकः Borax.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A sort<BR>of diet-drink.<BR>--2 Causing a wound<BR>to close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचनिका
पाचनिका Cooking, maturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचल|पाचलं|पाचलः
पाचल a. Cooking, ripening,<BR>causing digestion &c.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A cook.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 Wind.<BR>--4 A thing<BR>dressed without the aid of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचा
पाचा, पाचिः f. Cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाचिः|पाचि
पाचा, पाचिः f. Cooking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाजस्
पाजस् n. Ved. Strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचकपाल|पाञ्चकपाल|पाञ्चकपालः
पांचकपाल a. (ली f.) Relating<BR>to an oblation offered in five cups<BR>(कपाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचजन्यः|पाञ्चजन्य|पांचजन्य|पाञ्चजन्यः
पांचजन्यः N. of the conch of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; (दधानो) निध्वानमश्रूयत<BR>पांचजन्यः Śi. 3. 21; Bg. 1. 15.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धरः an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचदश|पाञ्चदश
पांचदश a. (शी f.) पांचदश्य<BR>(श्यी f.) Relating to the fifteenth<BR>day of a month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचदश्यं|पाञ्चदश्य
पांचदश्यं A collection of fifteen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचनद|पाञ्चनद|पाञ्चनदः
पांचनद a. (दी f.) Prevalent in the<BR>पंचनद or Punjab.<BR>--दः<BR>1 A prince of<BR>the Panjab.<BR>--2 (pl.) Its inhabitants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचभौतिक|पाञ्चभौतिक
पांचभौतिक a. (की f.)<BR>Composed of the five elements or<BR>containing them; पांचभौतिकी सृष्टिः Mv. 6;<BR>Y. 3. 175.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचयज्ञिक|पाञ्चयज्ञिक
