पांचाल|पाञ्चाल|पाञ्चालं|पाञ्चालः
पांचाल a. (ली f.) Belonging<BR>to or ruling over the Pañcālas.<BR>--लः<BR>1 The country of the Pañcālas.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">Page0690-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 A prince of the Pañcālas<BR>--लाः (m. pl.)<BR>1 The people of the<BR>Pañcālas.<BR>--2 An association of five<BR>guilds (i. e. of a car penter, weaver,<BR>barber, washerman, and shoe-maker).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचालक|पाञ्चालक|पाञ्चालकः
पांचालक a. Pelonging to the<BR>people of the Pañcālas.<BR>--कः A king<BR>of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचाली|पाञ्चाली
पांचाली<BR>1 A woman or princess of<BR>the Pañcālas.<BR>--2 N. of Draupadī,<BR>the wife of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>--3 A doll,<BR>puppet.<BR>--4 (In Rhet.) One of the<BR>four styles of composition. The<BR>S. D.thus defines it:<BR>--वर्णैः शेषैः (i. e.<BR>माधुर्यव्यंजकौजःप्रकांशकाभ्यां भिन्नैः) पुनर्द्वयोः<BR>समस्तपंचषपदो बंधः पांचालिको मतः ॥ 628.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांचालिका|पाञ्चालिका
पांचालिका A doll, puppet;<BR>स्तन्यत्यागात्प्रभृति सुमुखी दंतपांचालिकेव<BR>क्रीडायोगं तदनु विनयं प्रापिता वर्धिता च<BR>Māl. 10. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाट्
पाट् ind. An interjection used in<BR>calling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटः|पाट
पाटः<BR>1 Extension, breadth.<BR>--2<BR>(In geometry) The intersection of<BR>a prolonged side and perpendicular,<BR>or the figure formed by such<BR>intersection.<BR>--टा A series, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटकः|पाटक
पाटकः [पट्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A splitter,<BR>divider.<BR>--2 Part of a village.<BR>--3 The<BR>half of a village.<BR>--4 A kind of<BR>musical instrument.<BR>--5 A bank, shore.<BR>--6 A flight of steps leading to the<BR>water.<BR>--7 Loss of capital or stock.<BR>--8 A long span.<BR>--9 Throwing dice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटच्चरः|पाटच्चर
पाटच्चरः A thief, robber,<BR>pilferer; कुसुमरसपाटच्चर Ś. 6;<BR>पद्मिनीपरिमलालिपाटच्चरैः Bv. 2. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटनं|पाटन
पाटनं [पट्-भावे ल्युट्] Splitting,<BR>breaking, cleaving, destroying.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्रिया lancing an ulcer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटित|पाटितं
पाटित p. p.<BR>1 Torn, cleft, split,<BR>broken.<BR>--2 Pierced, pricked;<BR>R. 11. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल|पाटलं|पाटलः
पाटल a. [पट्-णिच् कलच्]<BR>1<BR>Palered, of a pink or pale-red colour;<BR>अग्रे स्त्रीनखपाटलं कुरबकं V. 2. 7;<BR>R. 1. 83; 2. 29; 7. 27;<BR>पाटलपाणिजांकितमुरः Gīt. 12.<BR>--लः The pale-red or<BR>pink colour; कपोलपाटलादेशि बभूव<BR>रघुचेष्टितं R. 4. 68.<BR>--2 The<BR>trumpetflower, Bignonia Suaveolens;<BR>पाटलसंसर्गसुरमिवनवाताः Ś. 1. 3.<BR>--लं<BR>1 The<BR>flower of this tree; R. 16. 52; 19. 46.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of rice ripening in the rains.<BR>--3 Saffron.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपलः a ruby.<BR>--द्रुमः the trumpet-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0690-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलक
पाटलक a. Of a pale-red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटला
पाटला<BR>1 The red lodhra.<BR>--2<BR>The trumpet-flower (the tree or<BR>its blossom).<BR>--3 An epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलावती
पाटलावती An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिः|पाटलि
पाटलिः f. The trumpet-flower.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुत्रं N. of an ancient city,<BR>the capital of Magadha, situated<BR>near the confluence of the Śoṇa and<BR>the Ganges, and identified by some<BR>with the modern Pātnā. It is<BR>also known by the names of पुष्पपुर,<BR>कुसुमपुर; see Mu. 2, 3, and 4. 16,<BR>and R. 6. 24 also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिमन्
पाटलिमन् m. Pale-red colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटल्या
पाटल्या A multitude of Pāṭala<BR>flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिक|पाटलिकः
पाटलिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Knowing<BR>the secrets of others.<BR>--2 Knowing<BR>time and place.<BR>--कः A pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटवं|पाटव
पाटवं [पटोर्भावः अण्]<BR>1<BR>Sharpness, acuteness.<BR>--2 Cleverness, skill,<BR>dexterity, proficiency; पाटवं<BR>संस्कृतोक्तिषु H. 1; Ki. 9. 54.<BR>--3 Energy<BR>--4 Quickness; rashness.<BR>--5 Health.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटविक|पाटविकः
पाटविक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Clever,<BR>sharp, skilful.<BR>--2 Cunning,<BR>fraudulent, crafty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटी
पाटी Arithmetic.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गणितं arithmetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटीरः|पाटीर
पाटीरः<BR>1 Sandal; पाटीर तव<BR>पटीयान् कः परिपाटीमिमामुरीकर्तुं<BR>Bv. 1. 12.<BR>--2 A field.<BR>--3 Tin.<BR>--4 A<BR>cloud.<BR>--5 A sieve.<BR>--6 A pungent<BR>root.<BR>--7 The manna of the bamboo.<BR>--8 Catarrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठः|पाठ
पाठः [पठ्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Reciting<BR>recitation, repeating.<BR>--2 Reading,<BR>perusal, study.<BR>--3 Studying or<BR>reciting the Vedas (ब्रह्मयज्ञ), one of<BR>the five daily Yajñas or sacrifices to<BR>be performed by Brāhmaṇas<BR>--4 The<BR>text of a book, a reading. variant;<BR>अत्र गंधवद्गंधमादनं इति आगंतुकः पाठः ।<BR>प्राचीनपाठस्तु सुगंधिर्गंधमादनः इति<BR>पुल्लिंगांतः Malli. on Ku. 6. 46.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरं another reading, a variant<BR>(v. l.).<BR>--छेदः a pause, cæsura.<BR>--दोषः a false reading.<BR>--निश्चयः<BR>determining the text of a passage.<BR>--भूः f. a place where the Vedas<BR>are learnt.<BR>--मंजरी, --शालिनी the<BR>Sārikā bird.<BR>--शाला a school, college,<BR>seminary.<BR>--शालिन् m. a pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठकः|पाठक
पाठकः [पठ्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A teacher,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-b" target="_blank">Page0691-b+ 56</a>]<BR>lecturer, preceptor.<BR>--2 A public<BR>reader of the Purāṇas or other sacred<BR>books.<BR>--3 A spiritual teacher.<BR>--4<BR>A pupil, student, scholar.<BR>--5 The<BR>text of a book.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठनं|पाठन
पाठनं Teaching, lecturing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठित
पाठित p. p. Taught, instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठिक
पाठिक a. Conformable to the text.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठिन्
पाठिन् a. [पठ्-णिनि]<BR>1 One who<BR>has read or studied any subject.<BR>--2<BR>Knowing or familiar with. --m.<BR>A Brāhmaṇa who has finished his<BR>studies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाठीनः|पाठीन
पाठीनः<BR>1 A public reader of the<BR>Purāṇas or other mythological<BR>books.<BR>--2 A kind of fish;<BR>विवृत्तपाठीनपराहतं पयः Ki. 4. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाडिनी
पाडिनी<BR>1 An earthen pot.<BR>--2 A<BR>boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणः|पाण
पाणः [पण् भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Trade,<BR>traffic.<BR>--2 A trader.<BR>--3 A game.<BR>--4<BR>A stake at play.<BR>--5 An agreement.<BR>--6 Praise.<BR>--7 The hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिः|पाणि
पाणिः [पण्-इण् आयाभावः; cf.<BR>Uṇ. 4. 132]<BR>1 The hand; दानेन पाणिर्न<BR>तु कंकणेन (विभाति) Bh. 2. 71; often<BR>at the end of comp. in the sense of<BR>‘carrying in the hand’; as चक्र˚,<BR>खड्ग˚ &c.; पाणिं ग्रह् or पीड् ‘to take<BR>the hand of, lead to the altar, marry.’<BR>पाणौ कृ to hold by the hand,<BR>marry; पाणौकरणं ‘marriage’.<BR>--2 Ved.<BR>A hoof.<BR>--णिः f. A market.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् m. {1} N. of Śiva. {2} one<BR>playing on a drum.<BR>--गृहीती<BR>‘espoused by the hand’, a wife.<BR>--ग्रहः,<BR>--ग्रहणं, --ग्राहः marrying, marriage;<BR>R. 7. 29; 8. 7; Ku. 7. 4.<BR>--ग्रहणिक,<BR>--ग्रहणीय a. matrimonial, nuptial.<BR>--(यं)<BR>a nuptial gift.<BR>--ग्रहीतृ m.,<BR>--ग्राहः<BR>a bridegroom, husband;<BR>ध्यायत्यनिष्टं यत्किंचित्पाणिग्राहस्य चेतसा<BR>Ms. 9. 21; बाल्ये पितुर्वशे तिष्ठेत्<BR>पाणिग्राहस्य यौवने 5. 148.<BR>--घः {1} a<BR>drummer. {2} a workman,<BR>handicraftsman.<BR>--घातः {1} a blow with the<BR>hand. {2} boxing. {3} a boxer.<BR>--चापल्यं<BR>snapping the fingers.<BR>--जः a<BR>fingernail; तस्याः पाटलपाणिजांकितमुरः<BR>Gīt. 12.<BR>--तलं the palm of the hand.<BR>--धर्मः due form of marriage.<BR>--पल्लवः<BR>{1} a sprout-like hand. {2} the fingers.<BR>--पात्र a. drinking by means of<BR>the hand.<BR>--पीडनं marriage;<BR>पाणिपीडनमहं दमयंत्याः कामयेमहि<BR>महीमहिकांशो N. 5. 99; पाणिपीडनविधेरनंतरं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">Page0691-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Ku. 8. 1; Māl. 8. 6.<BR>--प्रणयिनी a<BR>wife.<BR>--बंधः ‘union of the hands’,<BR>marriage.<BR>--भुज् m. the sacred<BR>fig-tree.<BR>--मुक्तं a missile thrown with<BR>the hand.<BR>--मुखाः m. pl. the manes.<BR>--रुह् m., रुहः a fingernail.<BR>--वादः {1}<BR>clapping the hands together. {2}<BR>playing on a drum.<BR>--सर्ग्या-र्या a rope.<BR>--स्वनिक a. playing musical<BR>instruments with the hands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिंधम|पाणिन्धम|पाणिन्धमः
पाणिंधम-य a.<BR>1 Blowing through the<BR>hands.<BR>--2 Chilly, as a road or<BR>journey.<BR>--3 Obscure, dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिंधय|पाणिन्धय|पाणिन्धयः
पाणिंधम-य a.<BR>1 Blowing through the<BR>hands.<BR>--2 Chilly, as a road or<BR>journey.<BR>--3 Obscure, dark.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिक|पाणिकः
पाणिक a. (की f.) Got by<BR>playing at stake.<BR>--कः A merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनिः|पाणिनि
पाणिनिः N. of a celebrated<BR>grammarian who is considered as an<BR>inspired muni, and is said to have<BR>derived the knowledge of his<BR>grammar from Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाणिनीय|पाणिनीयं|पाणिनीयः
पाणिनीय a. Relating to or<BR>composed by Pāṇini; Śi. 19. 75.<BR>--यः<BR>A follower of Pāṇini; अकृतव्यूहाः<BR>पाणिनीयाः.<BR>--यं The grammar of<BR>Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडर|पाण्डर|पाण्डरं|पाण्डरः
पांडर a. Whitish, pale-white.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Red-chalk.<BR>--2 The blossom of<BR>the jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडवः|पाण्डव|पांडव|पाण्डवः
पांडवः [पांडोरपत्यं पुमान् आरेञ्] ‘A<BR>son or descendant of Pāṇḍu’, N. of<BR>any one of the five sons of Pāṇḍu;<BR>i. e. युधिष्ठिर, भीम, अर्जुन, नकुल and<BR>सहदेव; हंसाः संप्रति पांडवा इव<BR>वनादज्ञातचर्यांगताः Mk. 5. 6.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आभीलः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--श्रेष्ठः N. of<BR>Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडवायनः|पाण्डवायन|पाण्डवायनः
पांडवायनः An epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडवीय|पाण्डवीय
पांडवीय a. Belonging to the<BR>Pāṇḍavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडवेयः|पाण्डवेय|पांडवेय|पाण्डवेयः
पांडवेयः = पांडव q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडित्यं|पाण्डित्य|पांडित्य|पाण्डित्यं
पांडित्यं<BR>1 Scholarship, profound<BR>learning, erudition; तदेव गमक<BR>पांडित्यवैदग्ध्ययोः Māl. 1. 7; Pt. 1. 19.<BR>--2 Cleverness, skill, dexterity,<BR>sharpness; नखानां पांडित्यं प्रकटयतु कस्मिन्<BR>मृगपतिः Bv. 1. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडु|पाण्डु|पाण्डुः
पांडु a. Pale-white, whitish, pale,<BR>yellowish; विकलकरणः पांडुच्छायः<BR>शुचा परिदुर्बलः U. 3. 22.<BR>--डुः<BR>1 The<BR>pale-white or yellowish-white colour.<BR>--2 Jaundice.<BR>--3 A white elephant.<BR>--4 N. of the father of the Pāṇḍavas.<BR>[He was begotten by Vyāsa on<BR>Ambālikā, one of the widows of<BR>Vichitravīrya. He was called Pāṇḍu,<BR>because he was born pale (पांडु) by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-a" target="_blank">Page0692-a+ 58</a>]<BR>reason of his mother having become quite<BR>pale with fear when in private with<BR>the sage Vyāsa; (यस्मात्पांडुत्वमापन्ना<BR>विरूपं प्रेक्ष्य ममिह । तस्मादेव सुतस्ते वै पांडुरेव<BR>भविष्यति Mb.). He was prevented by a<BR>curse from having progeny himself; so<BR>he allowed his first wife Kuntī to make<BR>use of a charm she had acquired<BR>from Durvāsas for the birth of sons.<BR>She gave birth to Yudhiṣṭhira,<BR>Bhīma and Arjuna; and Mādrī, his<BR>other wife, by the use of the same<BR>charm, gave birth to Nakula and<BR>Sahadeva. One day Pāṇḍu forgot the curse<BR>under which he was labouring, and made<BR>bold to embrace Mādrī, but he fell<BR>immediately dead in her arms.]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आमयः jaundice.<BR>--कंबलः<BR>{1} a white blanket. {2} a warm<BR>upper garment. {3} the housing of<BR>a royal elephant.<BR>--कंबलिन् m. {1} a<BR>carriage covered with a woollen<BR>blanket. {2} the housings of a<BR>royal elephant.<BR>--पुत्रः a son of<BR>Pāṇḍu, any one of the five<BR>Pāṇḍavas.<BR>--पृष्ठ a. ‘white-backed’, having<BR>no auspicious marks on the body,<BR>one from whom nothing great is<BR>to be expected.<BR>--भूमः a region full<BR>of chalky soil.<BR>--मृत्तिका {1} white or<BR>pale soil. {2} the opal.<BR>--मृद् f. chalk.<BR>--रागः whiteness, pallor.<BR>--रोगः<BR>jaundice.<BR>--लेखः a sketch made<BR>with chalk; a rough draft or sketch<BR>made on the ground, board &c.:<BR>पांडुलेखेन फलके भुमौ वा प्रथमं लिखंत् ।<BR>न्यूनाधिकं तु संशोध्य पश्चात्पत्रे निवेशयेत् ॥<BR>Vyāsa.<BR>--शर्करा light-coloured<BR>gravel (प्रमेहभेद)<BR>--शर्मिला an epithet<BR>of Draupadī.<BR>--सोपाकः N. of a<BR>mixed tribe;<BR>चांडालात्पांडुसोपाकस्त्वक्सारव्यवहारवान् Ms. 10. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0691-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडुकः|पाण्डुक|पाण्डुकः
पांडुकः<BR>1 The yellowish-white<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Jaundice.<BR>--3 N. of<BR>Pāṇḍu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडुकिन्|पाण्डुकिन्
पांडुकिन् a. Suffering from<BR>jaundice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडुर|पाण्डुर
पांडुर a. [पांडुवर्णोऽस्यास्ति र] Whitish,<BR>pale-white, yellowish-white, pale;<BR>छविः पांडुरा Ś. 3. 10; R. 14. 26;<BR>Ku. 3. 33.<BR>--रं The white leprosy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इक्षुः a species of sugar-cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांडुरिमन्|पाण्डुरिमन्
पांडुरिमन् m. Paleness, white or<BR>pale colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांड्याः
पांड्याः (m. pl.) N. of a<BR>country and its inhabitants; तस्यामेव रघोः<BR>पांड्याः प्रतापं न विषेहिरे R. 4. 49.<BR>--ड्यः<BR>A king of that country; R. 6. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांड्वं|पाण्ड्व
पांड्वं An uncoloured woollen<BR>garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाण्य|पाण्यः
पाण्य a. Praiseworthy,<BR>commendable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्
पात् a. Protecting, guarding. --m.<BR>1 Falling.<BR>--2 Sin.<BR>--3 A guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात|पातः
पात p. p. Protected, guarded<BR>&c.; See पा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातः|पात
पातः [पत्-घञ्]<BR>1 Flying, flight.<BR>--2 Alighting, descending, descent.<BR>--3 Falling down, fall, downfall (fig<BR>also); द्रुम˚, गृह˚; चग्णपातः ‘falling<BR>down at the feet’; R. 11. 92;<BR>पातोत्पातौ ‘rise and fall.’<BR>--4 Destruction.<BR>dissolution, ruin; Ku. 3. 44.<BR>--5 A<BR>blow, stroke; as in खड्गपातः.<BR>--6<BR>Shedding, discharging, emitting;<BR>असृक्पातैः Ms. 8. 44.<BR>--7 A cast,<BR>throw, shot; दृष्टि˚ R. 13. 18.<BR>--8<BR>An attack, inroad.<BR>--9 Happening,<BR>coming to pass, occurrence.<BR>--10 A<BR>failing, defect.<BR>--11 An epithet of<BR>Rāhu.<BR>--12 (In astr.) An<BR>inauspicious or malignant position or aspect.<BR>--13 The node in a planet's orbit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातन|पातनं
पातन a. [पत्-णिच् ल्यु ल्युट् वा] Felling.<BR>cutting down.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Causing to fall<BR>down, bringing or throwing down,<BR>knocking down.<BR>--2 Throwing,<BR>casting.<BR>--3 Humbling, lowering.<BR>--4<BR>Removing. N. B. पातनं may have<BR>different meanings according to the<BR>noun with which it is used; e. g.<BR>दडस्य पातनं ‘causing the rod to fall’,<BR>i. e. chastising; गर्भस्य पातनं ‘causing<BR>the fœtus to fall’, causing an<BR>abortion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातित
पातित p. p.<BR>1 Cast down, struck<BR>down.<BR>--2 Overthrown, humbled.<BR>--3<BR>Lowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिन्
पातिन् a. (नी f.) [पत्-णिनि]<BR>1<BR>Going to, descending, alighting on.<BR>--2 Falling, sinking. Being<BR>contained in.<BR>--3 Felling or throwing<BR>down.<BR>--4 Pouring forth,<BR>discharging, emitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातुक|पातुकः
पातुक a. (की f.) [पत्-उकञ्]<BR>1<BR>Falling habitually or frequently.<BR>--2<BR>Apt or disposed to fall.<BR>--3 Losing<BR>one's caste.<BR>--4 Going to hell.<BR>--कः<BR>1 The declivity of a mountain, a<BR>precipice.<BR>--2 The water-elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्य
पात्य a.<BR>1 To be caused to fall, to<BR>be felled or cut down.<BR>--2 To be<BR>imposed (as a fine); see पत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकः|पातक|पातकं
पातकः --कं [पातयति नरं, पत्-ण्वुल्]<BR>Sin, crime; (Hindu law-givers<BR>enumerate five great sins:<BR>--ब्रह्महत्या<BR>सरापानं स्तेयं गुर्वगनागमः । महांति पातकान्याहुः<BR>ससर्गश्चापि तैस्सह Ms. 11. 55).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकं|पातक|पातकः
पातकः --कं [पातयति नरं, पत्-ण्वुल्]<BR>Sin, crime; (Hindu law-givers<BR>enumerate five great sins:<BR>--ब्रह्महत्या<BR>सरापानं स्तेयं गुर्वगनागमः । महांति पातकान्याहुः<BR>ससर्गश्चापि तैस्सह Ms. 11. 55).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातकिन्
पातकिन् a. Sinful, guilty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातंगिः|पातङ्गि|पातंगि|पातङ्गिः
पातंगिः<BR>1 An epithet of Saturn.<BR>--2 Of Yama.<BR>--3 Of Karṇa.<BR>--4 Of<BR>Sugrīva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातंजल|पातञ्जल|पातञ्जलं
पातंजल a. (ली f.) Composed<BR>by Patañjali; पातंजले महाभाष्ये<BR>कृतभूरिपरिश्रमः Paribhāṣenduśekhara.<BR>--लं<BR>The Yoga system of philosophy<BR>taught by Patañjali. (It is<BR>generally believed that Patañjali, the<BR>author of the Mahābhāṣya, is the<BR>same as the author of the Yoga<BR>system: but it is a dubious point).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातालं|पाताल|पातालः
पातालं [पतत्यस्मिन्नधर्मेण पत्-आलञ्;<BR>cf. Uṇ. 1. 114]<BR>1 The last of the<BR>seven regions or worlds under the<BR>earth, said to be peopled by Nāgas;<BR>the seven regions are:<BR>--अतल. वितल,<BR>सुतल, रसातल, तलातल, महातल, and पाताल.<BR>--2 The lower regions or world in<BR>general; R. 15. 84; 1. 80.<BR>--3 An<BR>excavation, a hole.<BR>--4 Submarine<BR>fire.<BR>--5 (In astrol.^1) The fourth house<BR>or sign from that in which the sun<BR>is present.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A kind of<BR>instrument for distillation or the<BR>calcination and sublimation of metals.<BR>--2<BR>N. of Jupiter's year (of 361 days).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गंगा the Ganges of the<BR>lower world.<BR>--ओकस् m.,<BR>--निलयः,<BR>--निवासः, --वास्नि m. {1} a demon. {2}<BR>a Nāga or a serpent-demon.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिः|पाति
पातिः<BR>1 A master.<BR>--2 A bird.<BR>--3<BR>A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिकः|पातिक
पातिकः The Gangetic porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातित्यं|पातित्य
पातित्यं Loss of caste or position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिली
पातिली<BR>1 A snare, trap.<BR>--2 A<BR>small earthen vessel.<BR>--3 A woman<BR>of a particular class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पातिव्रत्यं|पातिव्रत्य
पातिव्रत्यं Fidelity to a husband,<BR>chastity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रं|पात्र|पात्त्रं|पात्रः
पात्रं [पाति रक्षत्याधेयं, पिबत्यनेन वा<BR>पाष्ट्रन् Tv.]<BR>1 A drinking-vessel, cup, jar.<BR>--2 A vessel or pot in general; पात्रे<BR>निधायार्ध्यं R. 5. 2, 12; any sacrificial<BR>vessel or utensil.<BR>--3 A receptacle of<BR>any kind, recipient; Pt. 2. 97.<BR>--4 A<BR>reservoir.<BR>--5 A fit or worthy<BR>person, a person fit or worthy to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">Page0693-a+ 57</a>]<BR>receive gifts; वित्तस्य पात्रं व्ययः<BR>Bh. 2. 82; Bg. 17. 22; Y. 1. 201;<BR>R. 11. 86.<BR>--6 An actor, a dramatis<BR>persona; तत्प्रतिपात्रमाधीयतां यत्नः<BR>Ś. 1; उच्यतां पात्रवर्गः V. 1. dramatis<BR>personae.<BR>--7 A king's minister.<BR>--8 The channel or bed of a river.<BR>--9 Fitness, propriety.<BR>--10 An order.<BR>command.<BR>--11 A leaf.<BR>--त्रः<BR>1 A kind<BR>of measure (अढक).<BR>--2 A preservative<BR>from sin.<BR>--त्री<BR>1 A vessel, plate, dish<BR>--2 A small furnace.<BR>--3 N. of Durgā.<BR>COMP.<BR>--पालः {1} a large paddle<BR>used as a rudder. {2} the rod of<BR>a balance (तृलाघट).<BR>--भृत् m. a<BR>servant.<BR>--संस्कारः {1} the cleaning<BR>or purification of a vessel. {2} the<BR>current of a river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0692-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रकं|पात्रक
पात्रकं A vessel, pot &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रट|पात्रटः
पात्रट a. Lean, emaciated.<BR>--टः<BR>1<BR>A cup. pot.<BR>--2 Rugged garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रटीरः|पात्रटीर
पात्रटीरः<BR>1 A competent<BR>minister.<BR>--2 A vessel of iron, brass or<BR>silver.<BR>--3 Fire.<BR>--4 A crow.<BR>--5 A<BR>heron.<BR>--6 Rust of iron.<BR>--7 Mucus<BR>running from the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रयति
पात्रयति Den. A. To use as a<BR>drinking-vessel; पाणिं पात्रयतां<BR>Bh. 3. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रसात्
पात्रसात् ind. In the possession of<BR>worthy persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिक
पात्रिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Measured<BR>out with any vessel or a measure<BR>called आढक.<BR>--2 Fit, adequate,<BR>appropriate.<BR>--कं, --की A vessel, cup,<BR>dish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रिन्
पात्रिन् a.<BR>1 Having or provided<BR>with a drinking-vessel.<BR>--2 Having<BR>fit or worthy persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीकृ
पात्रीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To make worthy;<BR>पात्रीकृतो दस्युरिवासि येन Ś. 5. 20.<BR>--2 To honour, dignify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीण
पात्रीण a. Measured, sown, or<BR>cooked with with a Pātra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीय|पात्रीयं
पात्रीय, पात्र्य a. Worthy to<BR>partake of a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्र्य
पात्रीय, पात्र्य a. Worthy to<BR>partake of a meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीयं|पात्रीय
पात्रीयं A sacrificial vessel or<BR>utensil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीरः|पात्रीर|पात्रीरं
पात्रीरः, --रं An oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रीरं|पात्रीर|पात्रीरः
पात्रीरः, --रं An oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रेबहुलः|पात्रेबहुल
पात्रेबहुलः --पात्रेसमितः<BR>1<BR>‘Constant at meals or dinner-time’, a<BR>parasite.<BR>--2 A treacherous or<BR>hypocritical fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पात्रेसमितः|पात्रेसमित
पात्रेबहुलः --पात्रेसमितः<BR>1<BR>‘Constant at meals or dinner-time’, a<BR>parasite.<BR>--2 A treacherous or<BR>hypocritical fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथः|पाथ|पाथं
पाथः [पीयतेऽदः पा-कर्मणि थ]<BR>1<BR>Fire.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--थं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथस्
पाथस् n. [पा-असुन् थुक् च]<BR>1<BR>Water; G. L. 26.<BR>--2 Air, wind.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-b" target="_blank">Page0693-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Food.<BR>--4 The sky.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं {1}<BR>a lotus. {2} a conch.<BR>--दः, --धरः a<BR>cloud.<BR>--धिः, --निधिः, --पतिः the<BR>ocean; N. 13. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथिस्
पाथिस् m.<BR>1 The sea.<BR>--2 The eye.<BR>--n. Scab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाथेयं|पाथेय
पाथेयं [पथि तद्व्यवहारे वा साधु ढञ्]<BR>1 Provender or provisions for a<BR>journey, viaticum; जग्राह<BR>पाथेयमिवेंद्रसूनुः Ki. 3. 37;<BR>बिसकिसलयच्छेदपाथेयवंतः Me. 11; V. 4. 15.<BR>--2 The<BR>sign virgo of the zodiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पादः|पाद
पादः [पद्यते गम्योऽनेन करणे कर्मणि<BR>वा घञ्]<BR>1 The foot (whether of<BR>men of animals); तयोर्जगृहतुः पादान्<BR>R. 1. 57; पादयोर्निपत्यः पादपतित<BR>&c. The word पाद at the end<BR>of comp. is changed to पाद्<BR>after सु and numerals; i. e. सुपाद्,<BR>द्विपाद्, त्रिपाद् &c.; and also when<BR>the first member is used as a<BR>standard of comparison, but is a word<BR>other than हस्ति &c.; see<BR>P. V. 4. 138-140 e. g. व्याघ्रपाद्. The nom. pl.<BR>of पाद is often added to names of<BR>persons or titles of address to show<BR>great respect or veneration; मृष्यंतु<BR>लवस्य बलिशतां तातपादाः U. 6;<BR>जीवत्सु तातपारेषु 1. 19; देवप दानां<BR>नास्माभिः प्रयोजनं Pt. 1; so<BR>एवमाराध्यपादा आज्ञापयंति Prab. 1; so<BR>कुमारिलपादाः &c.<BR>--2 A ray of light;<BR>बालस्यापि रवेः पादाः पतंत्युपरि भूभृतां<BR>Pt. 1. 328; Śi. 9. 34; R. 16. 53 (where<BR>the word has sense 1 also).<BR>--3 The<BR>foot or leg of an inanimate object,<BR>as of a bed stead.<BR>--4 The foot or<BR>root of a tree; as in पादप.<BR>--5 The<BR>foot of a mountain, a hill at the<BR>foot of a mountain (पादाः प्रत्यंतपर्वताः);<BR>Me. 19: Ś. 6. 16.<BR>--6 A quarter,<BR>fourth part; as in सपादो रूपंकः ‘one<BR>and one-fourth rupee’: Ms. 8. 241;<BR>Y. 2. 174.<BR>--7 The fourth part of a<BR>stanza, a line.<BR>--8 The fourth part<BR>of a chapter or book, as of the<BR>Adhyāyas of Pāṇini, or of the<BR>Brahma Sūtras.<BR>--9 A part in general.<BR>--10 A column, pillar.<BR>--11 A foot as<BR>a measure equal to twelve Aṅgulis.<BR>--12 The quadrant of a circle.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रं the point or<BR>extremity of the foot; Ratn. 1. 1.<BR>--अंकः<BR>a foot-mark.<BR>--अंगदं --दी an orna<BR>ment for the foot, an anklet.<BR>--अंगुलिः --ली f. a toe.<BR>--अंगुष्ठः the great<BR>toe.<BR>--अतः the point or extremity<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-c" target="_blank">Page0693-c+ 57</a>]<BR>of the feet.<BR>--अंतरं the interval of a<BR>step, the distance of a foot.<BR>--(रे)<BR>ind. {1} after the interval of a step.<BR>{2} close or near to.<BR>--अंबु n.<BR>butter milk containing a fourth part of<BR>water.<BR>--अंभस् n. water in which the<BR>feet (of revered persons) have been<BR>washed.<BR>--अरविंदं, --कमलं, --पंकजं,<BR>--पद्मं a lotus-like foot.<BR>--अर्घ्यं a gift<BR>to a Brāhmaṇa or a venerable<BR>person.<BR>--अलिन्दी a boat.<BR>--अवसेचनं {1}<BR>washing the feet. {2} the water<BR>used for washing the feet.<BR>--अष्ठीलः<BR>the ankle.<BR>--आघतः a kick.<BR>--आनत<BR>a. prostrate, fallen at the feet of;<BR>Ku. 3. 8.<BR>--आवर्तः {1} a wheel<BR>worked by the feet for raising up<BR>water from a well. {2} a square<BR>foot.<BR>--आसनं a foot-stool.<BR>--आस्फालनं trampling or motion of the feet,<BR>floundering.<BR>--आहत a. kicked.<BR>--आहति f. {1} treading or trampling.<BR>{2} a kick.<BR>--उदकं, --जलं {1} water<BR>for washing the feet. {2} water in<BR>which the feet of sacred and<BR>revered persons are washed, and which<BR>is thus considered holy.<BR>--उदरः a<BR>serpent.<BR>--कटकः --कं, --वीलिका an<BR>anklet.<BR>--क्षेपः a foot-step.<BR>--गंडीरः<BR>a morbid swelling of the legs and<BR>feet.<BR>--ग्रथिः the ankle.<BR>--ग्रहणं<BR>seizing or clasping the feet (as a<BR>mark of respectful salutation);<BR>Ku. 7. 27.<BR>--चतुरः, --चत्वरः {1} a<BR>slanderer. {2} a goat. {3} the fig-tree. {4}<BR>a sand-bank. {5} hail.<BR>--चापल्यं<BR>shuffling of the feet.<BR>--चारः going<BR>on foot, walking; यदि च विचरेत्<BR>पादच रेण गौरी Me. 60 ‘if Gaurī should<BR>walk on foot’; R. 11. 10. {2} the<BR>daily position of the planets.<BR>--चारिन्<BR>a. {1} walking or going on foot.<BR>{2} fighting on foot. (--m.) {1} a<BR>pedestrian. {2} a footsoldier.<BR>--जः<BR>a Śūdra.<BR>--जलं butter-milk mixed<BR>with one-fourth of water.<BR>--जाहं<BR>the tarsus.<BR>--तलं the sole of the foot.<BR>--त्रः, --त्रा, --त्राणं a boot or shoe.<BR>--दारी, --दारिका a chap in the feet.<BR>--दाहः a burning sensation in the<BR>feet.<BR>--धावनिका sand used for<BR>rubbing the feet.<BR>--नालिका an anklet.<BR>--न्यासः movement of the feet;<BR>M. 2. 9.<BR>--पः {1} a tree; निरस्तपादपे देश<BR>एरंडोऽपि द्रुमायते H. 1. 69;<BR>अनुभवति हि मूर्ध्ना पादपस्तीव्रमुष्णं<BR>Ś. 5. 7. {2} a foot-stool.<BR>--(पा) a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0694-a" target="_blank">Page0694-a+ 58</a>]<BR>shoe. ˚खंडः, --डं a grove of trees.<BR>˚रुहा a climbing plant.<BR>--पद्धतिः<BR>f. a track.<BR>--पालिका an anklet.<BR>--पाशः {1} a foot-rope for cattle. {2}<BR>an anklet of small bells &c.<BR>--(शी)<BR>{1} a fetter. {2} a mat. {3} a creeper.<BR>--पीठः --ठं a foot-stool; R. 17. 28;<BR>Ku. 3. 11.<BR>--पीठिका {1} a vulgar<BR>trade (as that of a barber). {2} white<BR>stone.<BR>--पूरणं {1} filling out a line. {2}<BR>an expletive; तु पादपूरणे भेदे समुच्चयेऽ<BR>वधारणे Viśva.<BR>--प्रक्षालनं washing the<BR>feet.<BR>--प्रणामः prostration (at the feet).<BR>--प्रतिष्ठानं a foot-stool.<BR>--प्रधारणं a<BR>shoe.<BR>--प्रहारः a kick.<BR>--बंधनं {1} a<BR>chain, fetter. {2} a stock of cattle.<BR>--भागः a quarter.<BR>--मुद्रा a foot-print.<BR>--मूलं {1} the tarsus. {2} the sole of<BR>the foot. {3} the heel. {4} the foot<BR>of a mountain. {5} a polite way of<BR>speaking of a person;<BR>देवपादमूलमागताहं K. 8.<BR>--रक्षः {1} a shoe. {2} a<BR>footguard.<BR>--रक्षणं {1} a cover for the feet.<BR>{2} a leather boot or shoe.<BR>--रजस्<BR>n. the dust of the feet.<BR>--रज्जुः f. a<BR>tether for the foot of an elephant.<BR>--रथी a shoe, boot.<BR>--रोहः, --रोहणः the<BR>(Indian) fig-tree.<BR>--वंदनं saluting<BR>the feet.<BR>--वल्मीकः elephantiasis.<BR>--विरजस् f. a shoe, boot. (--m.) a<BR>god.<BR>--शाखा a toe.<BR>--शैलः a hill at<BR>the foot of a mountain.<BR>--शोथः<BR>swelling of the foot.<BR>--शौचं cleaning the<BR>feet by washing, washing the<BR>feet; Pt. 1. 172.<BR>--सेवनं, --सेवा {1}<BR>showing respect by touching the<BR>feet. {2} service. स्फोटः ‘cracking<BR>of the feet’, chilblain.<BR>--हत a. kicked.<BR>--हर्षः numbness of the feet after<BR>pressure upon the crural nerves.<BR>--हीनात् ind. {1} without division or<BR>transition. {2} all at once.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0693-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

