पार्थवं Greatness, immensity,<BR>width.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिव|पार्थिवं|पार्थिवः
पार्थिव a. (वी f.) [पृथिव्याः ईश्ररः<BR>इदं वा अण्]<BR>1 Earthen, earthly,<BR>terrestrial, relating to the earth;<BR>यतो रजः पार्थिवमुज्जिहीते R. 13. 64.<BR>--2 Ruling the earth.<BR>--3<BR>Princely, royal.<BR>--वः<BR>1 An inhabitant of<BR>the earth.<BR>--2 A king, sovereign;<BR>R. 8. 1.<BR>--3 An earthen vessel.<BR>--4 The<BR>body.<BR>--वं An earthly substance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मजः --नंदनः, --सुतः a prince,<BR>the son of a king.<BR>--कंन्या, --नंदिनी,<BR>--सुता the daughter of a king, princess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्थिवी
पार्थिवी<BR>1 An epithet of Sītā,<BR>daughter of the earth;<BR>पार्थिवीमुदवहद्रघूद्वहः R. 11. 54.<BR>--2 An epithet of<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्परः|पार्पर
पार्परः<BR>1 A handful of rice.<BR>--2<BR>Consumption (क्षयरोग).<BR>--3 Ashes.<BR>--4<BR>A filament of Kadamba.<BR>--5 N. of<BR>Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्यंतिक|पार्यन्तिक|पार्य्यन्तिक
पार्यंतिक a. (की f.) Final, last,<BR>conclusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वण|पार्व्वण|पार्व्वणः
पार्वण a. (णी f.) [पर्वणि भवः अण्]<BR>1 Belonging or relating to a Parvan,<BR>falling on a Parva day, such as the<BR>full-moon, new-moon &c.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-a" target="_blank">Page0698-a+ 57</a>]<BR>R. 11. 82; Mu. 3. 10.<BR>--2 Waxing,<BR>increasing (as the moon).<BR>--णं The<BR>ceremony of offering oblations to all the<BR>Manes at a Parvan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0697-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वत|पार्व्वत|पार्व्वतः
पार्वत a. (ती f.) [पर्वते भवः अण्]<BR>1 Being or living on a mountain.<BR>--2<BR>Growing on or coming from a<BR>mountain.<BR>--3 Mountainous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतिकं|पार्वतिक
पार्वतिकं A multitude of mountains,<BR>a mountain-range.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वती|पार्व्वती
पार्वती [पर्वतस्यापत्यं स्त्री अण्]<BR>1 N.<BR>of Durgā, born as the daughter of<BR>the Himālaya mountain (she was<BR>Satī in her former birth; cf.<BR>Ku. 1. 21); तां पार्वतीत्याभिजनेन नाम्ना<BR>बंधुप्रियां बंधुजनो जुहाव Ku. 1. 26.<BR>--2 A<BR>female cowherd.<BR>--3 An epithet of<BR>Draupadī.<BR>--4 A mountain stream.<BR>--5 A kind of fragrant earth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नंदनः {1} an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>{2} of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतीय|पार्वतीयः|पार्व्वतीय
पार्वतीय a. (यी f.) Dwelling<BR>in a mountain.<BR>--यः<BR>1 A<BR>mountaineer.<BR>--2 N. of a particular<BR>mountain tribe (pl.); तत्र जन्यं<BR>रघोर्घोरं पार्वतीयैर्गणैरभूत् R. 4. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्वतेय|पार्व्वतेय|पार्व्वतेयं|पार्व्वतेयः
पार्वतेय a. (यी f.) [पर्वते भवं ढक्]<BR>Mountain-born.<BR>--यं Antimony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्शवः|पार्शव
पार्शवः A warrior armed with<BR>anaxe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्शुका
पार्शुका A rib.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्व|पार्श्वं|पार्श्वः
पार्श्व a. Near, proximate.<BR>--र्श्वः<BR>--र्श्वं [पर्शूनां समूहः]<BR>1 The part of<BR>the body below the arm-pit, the<BR>region of the ribs; शयने<BR>संनिषण्णैकपार्श्वा Me. 89.<BR>--2 The side, flank (in<BR>general) (of animate or inanimate<BR>objects); पिठरं क्वथदतिमात्रं<BR>निजपार्श्वानेव दहतितरां Pt. 1. 324.<BR>--3 Vicinity.<BR>--4 Ved. A curved knife.<BR>--र्श्वः An<BR>epithet of Jina.<BR>--र्श्वं<BR>1 A multitude<BR>of ribs.<BR>--2 A fraudulent expedient,<BR>a dishonourable means.<BR>--3 The<BR>extremity of the fore-axle of a wheel.<BR>(पार्श्वं is used adverbially in the sense<BR>of ‘near to,’ ‘by the side of,’<BR>‘towards’; Ś. 7. 8; so पार्श्वात् ‘from the<BR>side of, away, from’; पार्श्वे ‘near’,<BR>‘at hand’, ‘at the side’,; न मे<BR>दूरेकिंचित्क्षणमपि न पार्श्वे रथजवात् Ś. 1. 9,<BR>Bh. 3. 37).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुचरः an<BR>attendant, a servant; R. 2. 9.<BR>--अस्थि n. a rib.<BR>--आयात a. one who<BR>has come very near.<BR>--आसन्न a.<BR>standing by the side.<BR>--उदरप्रियः a<BR>crab.<BR>--ग, --गम, --चर, --स्थित a.<BR>being close to, standing by the side of.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">Page0698-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--गः an attendant, a servant;<BR>R. 11. 43.<BR>--गत a. {1} being at the side,<BR>being near or close to, attending<BR>upon. {2} sheltered.<BR>--चरः a servant,<BR>an attendant; R. 9. 72; 14. 29.<BR>--दः<BR>an attendant, a servant.<BR>--देशः the<BR>side (of the human body).<BR>--नाथः<BR>the Jaina pontiff.<BR>--परिवर्तनं {1}<BR>turning round from one side to the other<BR>in a bed. {2} N. of a festival on the<BR>eleventh day of the first half of<BR>Bhādrapada (when Viṣṇu is supposed<BR>to turn upon the other side in his<BR>sleep).<BR>--भागः the side or flank.<BR>--वक्रः an epithet of Mahādeva.<BR>--वर्तिन् a. {1} being by the side,<BR>attending, waiting upon. {2} adjacent.<BR>(--m.) {1} an attendant; R. 2. 46.<BR>{2} a companion, associate;<BR>Ku. 4. 29.<BR>--शय a. {1} sleeping on the side.<BR>{2} sleeping by the side.<BR>--शूलः --लं<BR>{1} a shooting pain in the side.<BR>{2} pleurisy.<BR>--सूत्रकः a kind of<BR>ornament.<BR>--स्थ a. being at the side,<BR>near, close, proximate.<BR>--(स्थः) {1} a<BR>companion. {2} an assistant of a<BR>stage-manager; cf. पारिपार्श्वक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वकः|पार्श्वक
पार्श्वकः (की f.) A swindler,<BR>pilferer, thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वतस्
पार्श्वतस् ind. Near, at hand, by<BR>the side, close to; R. 19. 31,<BR>Pt. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्वतीय|पार्श्वतीयः
पार्श्वतीय a. Being on or situated<BR>at the side.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्श्विक|पार्श्विकं|पार्श्विकः
पार्श्विक a. (की f.) [पार्श्वे भवः ठक्]<BR>Belonging to the side.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>sides-man, partisan.<BR>--2 A<BR>companion, an associate.<BR>--3 A juggler.<BR>--4 One who seeks money by<BR>fraudulent means, a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षत|पार्षतः
पार्षत a. (ती f.) Belonging to<BR>the spotted antelope; Ms. 3. 269;<BR>Y. 1. 257.<BR>--तः A patronymic of<BR>king Drupada, and of his son<BR>Dhṛṣṭadyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षती
पार्षती<BR>1 An epithet of Draupadī.<BR>--2 Of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद्
पार्षद् f. An assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षदः|पार्षद
पार्षदः [पार्षदमर्हति अण्]<BR>1 A<BR>companion, an associate, attendant.<BR>--2<BR>A train, retinue (of a god).<BR>--3<BR>One present at an assembly, a<BR>spectator, an assessor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्षद्यः|पार्षद्य
पार्षद्यः A member of an assembly,<BR>an assessor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पार्ष्णिः|पार्ष्णि
पार्ष्णिः m. f. [पृष्-नि नि˚ वृद्धिः;<BR>Uṇ. 4. 52]<BR>1 The heel;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-c" target="_blank">Page0698-c+ 57</a>]<BR>उद्वेजयत्यंगुलिपार्ष्णिभागान् Ku. 1. 11;<BR>पार्ष्णिप्रहार K. 119.<BR>--2 The rear of<BR>an army.<BR>--3 The back or rear in<BR>general; शुद्धपार्ष्णिरयान्वितः<BR>R. 4. 26 ‘with his rear cleared of foes.’<BR>--4 A kick.<BR>--5 Desire of<BR>conquering<BR>--6 Inquiry. --f.<BR>1 A licentious<BR>woman.<BR>--2 An epithet of Kuntī.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रहः a follower.<BR>--ग्रहणं<BR>attacking or threatening an enemy in<BR>the rear.<BR>--ग्राहः {1} an enemy in the<BR>rear. {2} a general commanding the<BR>rear of an army. {3} an ally who<BR>supports a prince; Ms. 7. 207.<BR>--घातः a kick; Ki. 17. 50.<BR>--त्रं a<BR>rear-guard, a body of forces in the<BR>rear, reserve.<BR>--वाहः an outside<BR>horse.<BR>--सारथिः a charioteer who<BR>drives one of the outside horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालः|पाल
पालः<BR>1 [पाल्-अच्] A protector<BR>guardian, keeper; as in गोपालः,<BR>वृष्णिपालः, &c.<BR>--2 A herdsman; विवादः,<BR>स्वामिपालयोः Ms. 8. 5, 229, 240.<BR>--3 A<BR>king.<BR>--4 A spitting-pot.<BR>--ली A<BR>herdsman's wife.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--घ्नः a<BR>mushroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालकः|पालक
पालकः [पाल्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A guardian,<BR>protector.<BR>--2 A prince, king, ruler,<BR>sovereign.<BR>--3 A groom, horse-keeper.<BR>--4 A horse.<BR>--5 The Citraka tree.<BR>--6 A foster-father.<BR>--7 Protection.<BR>--8 One who maintains or observes<BR>(as a promise &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालन|पालनं
पालन a. [पाल्-भावे ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>Protecting, guarding &c.; Ki. 1. 1.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Protecting, guarding,<BR>nourishing, cherishing, fostering; लब्ध˚<BR>R. 19. 3; so प्रजा˚, क्षिति˚, &c.<BR>--2<BR>Maintaining, observing, keeping<BR>(as a promise, vow &c.)<BR>--3 The<BR>milk of a cow that has recently<BR>calved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालनीय
पालनीय a.<BR>1 To be protected or<BR>guarded.<BR>--2 Fit to be protected,<BR>preserved or maintained.<BR>--3 To be<BR>kept or observed (as a promise, vow<BR>&c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालयितृ
पालयितृ m. A protector, guardian;<BR>R. 2. 69; 8. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालित|पालितः
पालित p. p.<BR>1 Protected, guarded,<BR>preserved.<BR>--2 Observed, fulfilled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालकाप्यः|पालकाप्य
पालकाप्यः N. of a sage, son of<BR>Kareṇu (who first taught the science<BR>of elephants).<BR>--प्यं The science of<BR>elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालंकः|पालङ्क|पालङ्कः
पालंकः<BR>1 The olibanum tree.<BR>--2<BR>A hawk.<BR>--की Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0698-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक्यः
पालक्यः --क्या Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालक्या
पालक्यः --क्या Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालल
पालल a. (ली f.) Made of the<BR>powdered sesamum-seed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालाश|पालाशं|पालाशः
पालाश a. (शी f.) [पलाश-अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to or coming from the<BR>Palāśa tree.<BR>--2 Made of the wood<BR>of the Palāśa tree; Ms. 2. 45.<BR>--3<BR>Green.<BR>--शः The green colour.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडः, --षंडः an epithet<BR>of the Magadha country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिः|पालि
पालिः --ली f.<BR>1 The tip of the ear;<BR>श्रवणपालिः Gīt. 3.<BR>--2 The edge,<BR>skirt, margin; Bh. 3. 55.<BR>--3 The<BR>sharp side, edge or point of<BR>anything (अश्रि); Bv. 2. 3.<BR>--4<BR>Boundary, limit.<BR>--5 A line, row;<BR>विपुलपुलकपाली Gīt. 6; Śi. 3. 51.<BR>--6 A<BR>spot, mark.<BR>--7 A causeway, bridge.<BR>--8 The lap or bosom.<BR>--9 An<BR>oblong pond.<BR>--10 Maintenance of a<BR>pupil by his teacher during the<BR>period of his studies.<BR>--11 A louse.<BR>--12 Praise, eulogium.<BR>--13 A<BR>woman with a beard.<BR>--14 The hip.<BR>--15 A measure of capacity (प्रस्थ).<BR>--16 A circumference.<BR>--ली A pot,<BR>boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाली
पालिः --ली f.<BR>1 The tip of the ear;<BR>श्रवणपालिः Gīt. 3.<BR>--2 The edge,<BR>skirt, margin; Bh. 3. 55.<BR>--3 The<BR>sharp side, edge or point of<BR>anything (अश्रि); Bv. 2. 3.<BR>--4<BR>Boundary, limit.<BR>--5 A line, row;<BR>विपुलपुलकपाली Gīt. 6; Śi. 3. 51.<BR>--6 A<BR>spot, mark.<BR>--7 A causeway, bridge.<BR>--8 The lap or bosom.<BR>--9 An<BR>oblong pond.<BR>--10 Maintenance of a<BR>pupil by his teacher during the<BR>period of his studies.<BR>--11 A louse.<BR>--12 Praise, eulogium.<BR>--13 A<BR>woman with a beard.<BR>--14 The hip.<BR>--15 A measure of capacity (प्रस्थ).<BR>--16 A circumference.<BR>--ली A pot,<BR>boiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिका
पालिका<BR>1 The tip of the ear.<BR>--2<BR>The sharp edge of a sword or of any<BR>cutting instrument.<BR>--3 A<BR>butterknife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालित्यं|पालित्य
पालित्यं Greyness of hair<BR>caused by old age, hoariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पालिंदः|पालिन्द|पालिन्दः
पालिंदः Incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्लवा
पाल्लवा A game with twigs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाल्वल
पाल्वल a. (ली f.) Coming from<BR>a pool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावक|पावकः
पावक a. [पू-ण्वुल्] Purifying.<BR>--कः<BR>1 Fire; पावकस्य महिमा स गण्यते<BR>कक्षवज्ज्वलति सागरेऽपि यः R. 11. 75,<BR>3. 9; 16. 87.<BR>--2 Agni or the god of<BR>fire.<BR>--3 The fire of lightning.<BR>--4<BR>The Citraka tree.<BR>--5 The number<BR>‘three’.<BR>--6 A person purified by<BR>religious abstraction, saint, sage.<BR>--7 Good conduct or behaviour.<BR>--8<BR>N. of Varuṇa.<BR>--की<BR>1 The wife of<BR>Agni.<BR>--2 Ved. N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मजः {1} an epithet of<BR>Kārtikeya. {2} N. of a sage called<BR>सुदर्शन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावकिः|पावकि
पावकिः<BR>1 An epithet of<BR>Kārtikeya.<BR>--2 Of the sage सुदर्शन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावन|पावनं|पावनः
पावन a. (नी f.) [पू-णिच् ल्बु]<BR>1<BR>Purifying, freeing from sin, purificatory,<BR>sanctifying; पादास्तामभितो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-b" target="_blank">Page0699-b+ 57</a>]<BR>निषण्णहरिणा गौरीगुरोः पावनाः Ś. 6. 16,<BR>R. 15. 101, 19. 53; Bg. 18. 5, Ms. 2. 26;<BR>Y. 3. 307.<BR>--2 Sacred, holy, pure,<BR>purified; Ku. 5. 17.<BR>--नः<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 Incense.<BR>--3 A kind of demi-god<BR>or Siddha.<BR>--4 N. of the poet Vyāsa.<BR>--5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Purifying,<BR>purification; पदनखनीरजनितजनपावन<BR>Gīt. 1.<BR>--2 Penance.<BR>--3 Water.<BR>--4<BR>Cow-dung.<BR>--5 A sectarial mark.<BR>--6<BR>Any means of purification; U. 1. 13.<BR>--7 Atonement, expiation.<BR>--8<BR>Incense (सिह्लक).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ध्वनिः a<BR>conch-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावनी
पावनी<BR>1 The holy basil.<BR>--2 A cow.<BR>--3 The river Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावमानी
पावमानी An epithet of particular<BR>Vedic hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पावरः|पावर
पावरः The side of a die which is<BR>marked with two points; or a<BR>particular throw of this die; पावरपतनाच्च<BR>शोषितशरीरः Mk. 2. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशः|पाश
पाशः [पश्यते बध्यतेऽनेन, पश्-करणे<BR>घञ्]<BR>1 A cord, chain,<BR>fetter, noose;<BR>पादाकृष्टव्रततिवलयासंगसंजातपाशः Ś. 1. 33; बाहुपाशेन<BR>व्यापादिता Mk. 9; R. 6. 84.<BR>--2 A snare, trap<BR>or net for catching birds and beasts.<BR>--3 A noose used as a weapon (as<BR>by Varuṇa); Ku. 2. 21.<BR>--4 A die,<BR>dice; Malli. on R. 6. 18.<BR>--5 The<BR>edge or border of anything woven.<BR>--6 (At the end of comp.) पाश<BR>expresses (a) contempt or<BR>depreciation; as in छत्रपाशः a bad pupil;<BR>वैयाकरण˚, भिषक्˚ &c. (b) beauty or<BR>admiration; as in सैवोष्ठमुद्रा स च<BR>कर्णपाशः U. 6. 27. (c) abundance, mass,<BR>or quantity (after a word signifying<BR>‘hair’); as in केशपाश q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः the back of a garment.<BR>--क्रीडा gambling, playing with dice.<BR>--धरः, --पाणिः an epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>--बद्ध a. entrapped, caught in a<BR>snare or net, noosed.<BR>--बंधः a noose,<BR>snare, halter.<BR>--बंधकः a<BR>birdcatcher.<BR>--बंधनं a snare.<BR>--भृत् m. {1}<BR>an epithet of Varuṇa; R. 2. 9. {2}<BR>one armed with a noose.<BR>--रज्जुः f.<BR>a fetter, rope.<BR>--हस्तः ‘holding a<BR>noose in hand’, an epithet of<BR>Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशकः|पाशक
पाशकः<BR>1 A die, dice.<BR>--2 (At the<BR>end of comp.) A snare, trap; as in<BR>कंठ˚ &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पीठं a gambling<BR>house or table.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशनं|पाशन
पाशनं<BR>1 A noose, snare, net, sling.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">Page0699-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 A cord, lash.<BR>--3 Ensnaring,<BR>entrapping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशयति
पाशयति Den. P. To bind, fetter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिकः|पाशिक
पाशिकः A bird-catcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशित|पाशितः
पाशित a. Bound, ensnared,<BR>fettered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशीकृत|पाशीकृतः
पाशीकृत a.<BR>1 Chained, fettered.<BR>--2 Snared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशिन्
पाशिन् m. [पाशोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>1 An<BR>epithet of Varuṇa.<BR>--2 Of Yama.<BR>--3 A deer-catcher, fowler, trapper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्या
पाश्या<BR>1 A net.<BR>--2 A collection of<BR>snares or ropes (पाशानां समूहः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशव
पाशव a. (वी f.) [पशोरिदं अण्]<BR>Relating to or derived from<BR>animals.<BR>--वं A flock, herd.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पालनं pasturage or meadow grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुक
पाशुक a. Ved. Belonging to<BR>cattle or a sacrificial animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपत|पाशुपतः
पाशुपत a. (ती f.) [पशुपतेरिदं अण्]<BR>Coming from or relating or sacred<BR>to Paśupati.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A follower<BR>and worshipper of Śiva.<BR>--2 A<BR>follower of the doctrines of<BR>Paśupati.<BR>--तं The Pāśupata<BR>doctrines; (for the Pāśupata<BR>doctrines, see Sarva. S.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अस्त्रं N. of a missile presided<BR>over by पशुपति or Śiva (which<BR>Arjuna acquired from Śiva).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुपाल्यं|पाशुपाल्य
पाशुपाल्यं The breeding or<BR>rearing of cattle, a herdsman's<BR>occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाशुबंधकः|पाशुबन्धक|पाशुबन्धकः
पाशुबंधकः A sacrifice.<BR>--का The<BR>sacrificial altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्चात्य|पाश्चात्यः
पाश्चात्य a. [पश्चाद्भवः त्यक्]<BR>1<BR>Hinder.<BR>--2 Western; R. 4. 62.<BR>--3<BR>Posterior, later.<BR>--4 Subsequent.<BR>--त्यं The hinder part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाश्या
पाश्या See under पाश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषंड|पाषण्ड|पाषण्डः
पाषंड a. Impious, heretical.<BR>--डः<BR>A heretic, an unbeliever, a hypocrite;<BR>Ms. 5. 90; 9. 225,<BR>--डः --डं Heresy<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषंडकः|पाषण्डक|पाषंडक|पाषण्डकः
पाषंडकः, पाषंडिन् m. पाखंडिकः A<BR>heretic, a religious hypocrite;<BR>Y. 1. 130; 2. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषंडिन्|पाषण्डिन्
पाषंडकः, पाषंडिन् m. पाखंडिकः A<BR>heretic, a religious hypocrite;<BR>Y. 1. 130; 2. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाषाणः|पाषाण
पाषाणः [पिनाष्टि पिष् संचूर्णने आनच्<BR>पृषो˚ Tv.] A stone.<BR>--णी<BR>1 A small<BR>stone used as a weight.<BR>--2 A spear.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गर्दभः a hard swelling on the<BR>maxillary joint.<BR>--चतुर्दशी N. of a<BR>festival on the 14th day of the month<BR>of Mārgaśīrṣa, in honour of Gaurī.<BR>--दारकः, --दारणः a stone-cutter's<BR>chisel.<BR>--संधिः a cave or chasm in a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-a" target="_blank">Page0700-a+ 55</a>]<BR>rock.<BR>--हृदय a. stone-hearted, cruel,<BR>relentless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0699-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पास्त्य
पास्त्य a. Ved. Dwelling in a<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पि
पि {c6c} P. (पियति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिंस्
पिंस् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (पिंसति,<BR>पिंसयति-ते)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>--2 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिकः|पिक
पिकः The(Indian) cuckoo;<BR>कुसुमशरासनशासनवंदिनि पिकनिकरे भज<BR>भावं Gīt. 11; or उन्मीलंति कुहूः<BR>कुहूरिति कलोत्तालाः पिकानां गिरः Gīt. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आनंदः, --बांधवः the<BR>spring.<BR>--वंधुः, --रागः, --वल्लभः the<BR>mango tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिक्कः|पिक्क
पिक्कः<BR>1 An elephant twenty<BR>years old.<BR>--2 A young elephant in<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिंग|पिङ्ग|पिङ्गं|पिङ्गः
पिंग a. [पिंज्-वर्णे अंच् न्यंक्व˚ कुत्वम्]<BR>Reddish-brown, tawny, yellow-red.<BR>अंतर्निविष्टामलपिंगतारं (विलोचनं)<BR>Ku. 7. 33.<BR>--गः<BR>1 The tawny colour.<BR>--2 A buffalo.<BR>--3 A rat.<BR>--गा<BR>1<BR>Turmeric.<BR>--2 Saffron.<BR>--3 A kind of<BR>yellow pigment.<BR>--4 An epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--5 A bow-string.<BR>--गं A<BR>young animal.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a.<BR>having reddish-brown eyes,<BR>redeyed.<BR>--(क्षः) {1} an ape. {2}<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--ईक्षणः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--ईशः an<BR>epithet of fire.<BR>--कपिशा a species<BR>of cock-roach.<BR>--चक्षुस् m. a crab.<BR>--जटः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--सारः<BR>yellow orpiment.<BR>--स्फटिकः ‘yellow<BR>crystal’, a kind of gem (गोमेद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिंगल|पिङ्गल|पिङ्गलं|पिङ्गलः
पिंगल a. [पिंग-सिध्मा˚ लच्, पिंगं<BR>लाति, ला-क वा Tv.] Reddish-brown,<BR>yellowish, brown, tawny;<BR>R. 12. 71; Ms. 3. 8.<BR>--लः<BR>1 The tawny<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 A monkey.<BR>--4<BR>An ichneumon.<BR>--5 A small owl.<BR>--6<BR>A kind of snake.<BR>--7 N. of an<BR>attendant on the sun.<BR>--8 N. of one<BR>of Kubera's treasures.<BR>--9 N. of a<BR>reputed sage, the father of<BR>Sanskrit prosody, his work being known<BR>as पिगलच्छंदःशास्त्र; छंदोज्ञानानंधिं जघान<BR>मकरो वेलातटे पिंगलं Pt. 2. 33.<BR>--लं<BR>1<BR>Brass.<BR>--2 Yellow orpiment.<BR>--ला<BR>1<BR>A kind of owl.<BR>--2 The Śiśu tree<BR>(शिंशपा).<BR>--3 A kind of metal.<BR>--4<BR>A particular vessel of the body.<BR>--5<BR>The female elephant of the south<BR>--6 N. of a courtezan who became<BR>remarkable for her piety and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-b" target="_blank">Page0700-b+ 56</a>]<BR>virtuous life; (the Bhāgavata<BR>mentions how she and Ajamīḍha were<BR>delivered from the trammels of the<BR>world).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--लौहं brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिंगलिका|पिङ्गलिका
पिंगलिका<BR>1 A kind of crane.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिंगलित|पिङ्गलित
पिंगलित a. Made reddish-brown,<BR>become tawny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिंगाशः|पिङ्गाश|पिंगाश|पिङ्गाशः
पिंगाशः<BR>1 The headman or<BR>proprietor of a village.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>fish.<BR>--शं Virgin gold.<BR>--शी The<BR>Indigo plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचंडः|पिचण्ड|पिचंड|पिचंडं|पिचण्डः
पिचंडः --डं, पिचिंडः --डं<BR>1 The<BR>belly.<BR>--2 A limb of an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0700-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पिचंडं|पिचण्ड|पिचंड|पिचंडः|पिचण्डः
