पृतना
पृतना<BR>1 An army (in general).<BR>--2 A division of an army consisting<BR>of 243 elephants, as many chariots,<BR>729 horse, and 1215 foot.<BR>--3 Battle,<BR>fight, encounter.<BR>--4 A hostile army.<BR>--5 (pl.) Men, mankind (Ved.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--साहः an epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतनायु
पृतनायु a. Ved. Hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतन्यति
पृतन्यति Den. P. To attack,<BR>encounter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृतन्या
पृतन्या An army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्
पृथ् {c10c} U. (पर्थयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>extend.<BR>--2 To throw, cast.<BR>--3 To send,<BR>direct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथः|पृथ
पृथः Ved.<BR>1 The palm of the<BR>hand.<BR>--2 A kind of measure.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्
पृथक् ind.<BR>1 Severally,<BR>separately, singly; शंखान् दध्मुः पृथक्<BR>पृथक् Bg. 1. 18; Ms. 3. 26;<BR>7. 57.<BR>--2 Different, separate,<BR>distinct; Bg. 5. 4; 13. 4; रचिता<BR>पृथगर्थता गिरां Ki. 2. 27.<BR>--3 Apart,<BR>aside. alone; V. 4. 20.<BR>--4 Apart<BR>from, except, with the<BR>exception of, without; (with acc.,<BR>instr., or abl.);<BR>पृथग्रामेण-रामात्-रामं वा Sk.; Bk. 8. 109. (पृथक्<BR>कृ<BR>1 to separate, divide, sever,<BR>analyse.<BR>--2 to keep off, avert.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मता {1} severalty,<BR>separateness. {2} distinction,<BR>difference. {3} discrimination,<BR>judgment.<BR>--आत्मन a. distinct,<BR>separate.<BR>--आत्मिका individual existence,<BR>individuality.<BR>--करणं, --क्रिया {1}<BR>separating, distinguishing. {2}<BR>analysing.<BR>--कुल a. belonging to a<BR>different family.<BR>--क्षत्राः (m. pl.)<BR>children of one father by different<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-c" target="_blank">Page0718-c+ 56</a>]<BR>wives, or by wives of different<BR>classes.<BR>--चर a. going alone or<BR>separately.<BR>--जनः {1} a low man,<BR>an unenlightened, vulgar man, the<BR>mob, low people; न पृथग्जनच्छुवो<BR>वशं वशिनामुतम गंतुमर्हसि R. 8. 90;<BR>Ki. 14. 24. {2} a fool, a<BR>blockhead, an ignorant man;<BR>Śi. 16. 9. {3} a wicked man, sinner.<BR>--पिंडः a distant relation who offers<BR>the funeral rice-ball separately and<BR>not together with other relations.<BR>--भावः separateness, individuality;<BR>(so पृथक्त्वं).<BR>--रूप a. of different<BR>shapes or kinds.<BR>--विध a. of<BR>different kinds, diverse, various.<BR>--शय्या sleeping apart.<BR>--स्यितिः f.<BR>separate existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथक्त्वं|पृथक्त्व
पृथक्त्वं Separateness, severalty.<BR>{2} Individuality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथवी
पृथवी See पृथिवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथा
पृथा N. of Kuntī, one of the<BR>two wives of Pāṇḍu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः<BR>तनयः, -सुतः, -सूनु an epithet of the<BR>first three Pāṇḍava princes, but<BR>generally applied only to Arjuna;<BR>अश्वत्थाना हत इति पृथासूनुना स्पष्टमुक्तवा<BR>Ve. 3. 9; अभितस्नं पृथासूनुः स्नेहेन<BR>परितस्तरे Ki. 11. 8.<BR>--पतिः an<BR>epithet of Pāṇḍu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिका
पृथिका A centipede.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथिवी
पृथिवी [cf. Uṇ. 1. 184]<BR>1 The<BR>earth; (sometimes written पृथिवि<BR>also)<BR>--2 Ground, soil.<BR>--3 The<BR>earth considered as one of the nine<BR>substances or five primary elements.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इंद्रः, --ईशः, --क्षित् m.,<BR>--पालः,<BR>--पालकः, --भुज् m.,<BR>--भुजः, --शुक्रः a king.<BR>--तलं the surface of the earth.<BR>--पतिः<BR>{1} a king. {2} Yama, the god of<BR>death.<BR>--भंडलः, --लं the circuit of<BR>the earth.<BR>--रुहः a tree: पवमानः<BR>पृथिवीरुहानिव R. 8. 9.<BR>--लोकः<BR>terrestrial world, the earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथु|पृथुः
पृथु a. (थु or थ्वी f., compar.<BR>प्रथीयस् superl. प्रथिष्ठ) [प्रथ् कुसंप्र˚<BR>Uṇ. 1. 28]<BR>1 Broad wide, spacious,<BR>expansive; पृथुनितंब q. v. below;<BR>सिंधोः पृथुमपि तनुं Me. 46.<BR>--2 Copious,<BR>abundant, ample; V. 4. 25.<BR>--3<BR>Large, great; दृशः पृथुतरीकृताः<BR>Ratn. 2. 15; Śi. 12. 48; R. 11. 25.<BR>--4<BR>Detailed, prolix.<BR>--5 Numerous.<BR>--6<BR>Smart, sharp, clever.<BR>--7 Important.<BR>--8 Various.<BR>--थुः<BR>1 N. of fire or<BR>Agni.<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 Of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-a" target="_blank">Page0719-a+ 63</a>]<BR>Mahādeva.<BR>--4 N. of a king. [Pṛthu<BR>was the son of Veṇa, son of Aṅga. He<BR>was called the first king, from whom<BR>the earth received her name Pṛthvī.<BR>The Viṣṇu Purāṇa relates that when<BR>Veṇa who was wicked by nature and<BR>prohibited worship and sacrifice, was<BR>beaten to death by the pious sages, and<BR>when consequently robbery and<BR>anarchy prevailed in the absence of a King,<BR>the Munis rubbed the right arm of the<BR>dead king to produce a son, and from<BR>it sprang the majestic Pṛthu, glowing<BR>like Agni. He was immediately<BR>declared King, and his subjects who had<BR>suffered from famine, besought the<BR>monarch for the edible fruits and plants<BR>which the earth withheld from them.<BR>In anger Pṛthu took up his bow to<BR>compel her to yield the supply so much<BR>needed by his subjects. She assumed<BR>the form of a cow and began to flee<BR>chased by the King. But she at last<BR>yielded and requested him to spare her<BR>life, and at the same time promised to<BR>restore all the needed fruits, plants &c.,<BR>‘if a calf were given to her through<BR>which she might be able to secrete<BR>milk’. Pṛthu thereupon made<BR>Svāyambhuva Manu the calf milked the<BR>earth, and received the milk into his<BR>own hand, from which proceeded all<BR>kinds of corn, vegetables, fruits &c.,<BR>for the maintenance of his subjects.<BR>The example of Pṛthu was afterwards<BR>followed by a variety of milkers-gods,<BR>men, Ṛṣis, mountains, Nāgas, Asuras<BR>&c., who found out the proper<BR>milkman and calf from their own number,<BR>and milked the earth of whatever they<BR>wanted; cf. Ku. 1. 2].<BR>--थु f. Opium<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदर a. big-bellied,<BR>corpulent.<BR>--(रः) a ram.<BR>--जघन, --नितंब<BR>a. having large or broad hips or<BR>slopes; पृथुनितंब नितंबवती तव<BR>V. 4. 26.<BR>--पत्रः-त्रं red garlic.<BR>--प्रथ,<BR>--यशस् a. far-famed, widely renowned<BR>--रोमन् m. a fish. ˚युग्म. the sign<BR>Pisces of the zodiac.<BR>--शेखरः a<BR>mountain.<BR>--श्री a. highly prosperous.<BR>--श्रोणि a. having large hips.<BR>--संपद्<BR>a. rich, wealthy.<BR>--स्कंधः a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0718-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुकः|पृथुक|पृथुकं
पृथुकः --कं Rice parched and<BR>flattened (Mar. पोहे).<BR>--कः A child;<BR>निन्युर्जनन्यः पृथुकान् पथिभ्यः Śi. 3. 30<BR>--का A girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुकं|पृथुक|पृथुकः
पृथुकः --कं Rice parched and<BR>flattened (Mar. पोहे).<BR>--कः A child;<BR>निन्युर्जनन्यः पृथुकान् पथिभ्यः Śi. 3. 30<BR>--का A girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथुल|पृथुलं
पृथुल a. Broad, large, wide;<BR>श्रोणिषु प्रियकर पृथुलासु स्पर्शमाप सकलेन<BR>तलेन Śi. 10. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वी
पृथ्वी [पृथु-ङीष्]<BR>1 The earth.<BR>--2<BR>The earth as one of the five<BR>elements.<BR>--3 Large cardamoms.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of a metre; (see App. I.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">Page0719-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--ईशः, --पतिः, --पालः, --भुज् m. a king,<BR>sovereign.<BR>--खातं a cavern.<BR>--गर्भः<BR>an epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR>--गृहं a cave,<BR>grotto.<BR>--जः {1} a tree. {2} the<BR>planet Mars.<BR>--धरः a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृथ्वीका
पृथ्वीका<BR>1 Large cardamoms.<BR>--2<BR>Small cardamoms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृदाकुः|पृदाकु
पृदाकुः<BR>1 A scorpion.<BR>--2 A tiger.<BR>--3 A serpent, adder<BR>--4 A tree<BR>--5<BR>An elephant.<BR>--6 A panther (चित्रक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृशन
पृशन a. Ved. Clinging,<BR>attached to<BR>--नं Clinging to, attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्नि|पृश्निः
पृश्नि(ष्णि) a. [स्पृअ-नि˚ किच्च<BR>पृषो˚ सलोपः; Uṇ. 4. 52]<BR>1 Short, small,<BR>dwarfish.<BR>--2 Delicate, feeble.<BR>--3<BR>Diversified, spotted.<BR>--4 Various,<BR>diverse (Ved.).<BR>--श्निः A dwarf.<BR>--श्नि f.<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>--2 The<BR>earth.<BR>--3 The starry sky.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>Devakī, mother of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--5 The<BR>earth.<BR>--6 A cloud.<BR>--7 Milk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गर्भः, --धरः, --भद्रः epithets of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--शृंगः {1} an epithet of Kṛ<BR>ṣṇa. {2} of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्णि|पृष्णिः
पृश्नि(ष्णि) a. [स्पृअ-नि˚ किच्च<BR>पृषो˚ सलोपः; Uṇ. 4. 52]<BR>1 Short, small,<BR>dwarfish.<BR>--2 Delicate, feeble.<BR>--3<BR>Diversified, spotted.<BR>--4 Various,<BR>diverse (Ved.).<BR>--श्निः A dwarf.<BR>--श्नि f.<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>--2 The<BR>earth.<BR>--3 The starry sky.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>Devakī, mother of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--5 The<BR>earth.<BR>--6 A cloud.<BR>--7 Milk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गर्भः, --धरः, --भद्रः epithets of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--शृंगः {1} an epithet of Kṛ<BR>ṣṇa. {2} of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्निका
पृश्नि(ष्णि)का, पृश्नी(ष्णी) N.<BR>of an aquatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्णिका
पृश्नि(ष्णि)का, पृश्नी(ष्णी) N.<BR>of an aquatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृश्नी
पृश्नि(ष्णि)का, पृश्नी(ष्णी) N.<BR>of an aquatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्णी
पृश्नि(ष्णि)का, पृश्नी(ष्णी) N.<BR>of an aquatic plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्
पृष् {c1c} A. (पर्षते)<BR>1 To sprinkle.<BR>--2 To hurt, injure.<BR>--3 To give.<BR>--4<BR>To vex, pain, weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत्|पृषन्त्
पृषत् a.<BR>1 Spotted, variegated.<BR>--2<BR>Sprinkling --m. The spotted ante<BR>lope. --n. A drop of water or of<BR>any other liquid; (said by some to<BR>be used only in pl.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः,<BR>अश्वः {1} wind, air. {2} an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--आज्यं ghee mixed with<BR>coagulated milk.<BR>--पतिः (पृषतांपतिः)<BR>wind.<BR>--बलः N. of the horse of<BR>Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत|पृषतः
पृषत a. [पृस्-अतच् किच्च] Spotted.<BR>--तः<BR>1 The spotted antelope.<BR>--2 A<BR>drop of water; पृषतैरपां शमयता च<BR>रजः Ki. 6. 27; R. 3. 3; 4. 27;<BR>6. 51.<BR>--3 A spot, mark.<BR>--4 An<BR>antelope considered as the vehicle of<BR>Vāyu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्वः air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषत्कः|पृषत्क
पृषत्कः An arrow; तदुपोढैश्च नभश्चरैः<BR>पृषत्कः Ki. 13. 23; Śi. 20. 18;<BR>Vb. 1. 1; धनुर्भृतां हस्तवतां पृषत्काः<BR>R. 7. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषंतिः|पृषन्ति|पृषंति|पृषन्तिः
पृषंतिः A drop of water;<BR>पयःपृषंतिभिः रपृष्टा वांति वाताःशनैःशनैः<BR>Bharata on Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषभाषा
पृषभाषा = पूषभसा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषाकरा
पृषाकरा A small stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषातकं|पृषातक
पृषातकं Mixture of ghee and<BR>coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृषोदरः|पृषोदर
पृषोदरः Wind, air. (The word<BR>is supposed to be compounded of<BR>पृषत् and उदर, the त् of पृषत् being<BR>dropped as an irregular case. The<BR>word is thus taken as the type of a<BR>whole class of such irregular<BR>compounds); पृषोदरादित्वात् साधुः, see<BR>Gaṇa to P. VI. 3. 109.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ट
पृष्ट p. p. [पृष्-प्रच्छ्-वा क्त]<BR>1 Asked,<BR>inquired, interrogated, questioned.<BR>--2 Sprinkled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्टिः|पृष्टि
पृष्टिः f.<BR>1 Inquiry, interrogation.<BR>--2 Ved. A rib.<BR>--3 Touch.<BR>--4 A ray<BR>of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्टहायनः|पृष्टहायन
पृष्टहायनः<BR>1 A species of grain.<BR>--2 An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठं|पृष्ठ
पृष्ठं [पृष् स्पृश्-वा थक् नि˚;<BR>Uṇ. 2. 12]<BR>1 The back, hinder part, rear.<BR>--2 The back of an animal;<BR>अश्वपृष्ठमारूढः &c.<BR>--3 The surface or upper<BR>side; R. 4. 31, 12. 67; Ku. 7. 51;<BR>so अवनिपृष्ठचारिणीं U. 3.<BR>--4 The<BR>back or the other side (of a letter,<BR>document &c.); Y. 2. 93.<BR>--5 The<BR>flat roof of a house.<BR>--6 The page of<BR>a book. (पृष्ठेन, पृष्ठे ‘behind, from<BR>behind’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुग, --गामिन्,<BR>यायिन् a. going behind, following;<BR>Pt. 1. 59.<BR>--अस्थि n. the back-bone.<BR>--उदय a. an epithet of particular<BR>signs of the zodiac, i. e. Aries,<BR>Taurus, Gemini, Sagittarius and<BR>Capricorn.<BR>--गोपः, --रक्षः a soldier who<BR>protects the rear of a warrior while he<BR>is fighting.<BR>--ग्रांथि a. hump-backed.<BR>--चक्षुस् m. a crab.<BR>--तल्पनं the<BR>exterior muscles on the back of an<BR>elephant.<BR>--दृष्टिः {1} a crab. {2} a bear.<BR>--पातिन् a. following.<BR>--फलं the<BR>superficial contents of a figure.<BR>--भागः the back.<BR>--मांसं {1} flesh on<BR>the back; प्राक् पादयोः पतति खादति<BR>पृष्ठमांसं H. 1. 81. {2} a fleshy<BR>protuberance on the back. ˚अद, ˚अदन्<BR>a. back-biter, slanderer,<BR>calumniator.<BR>--(दं --दनं) back-biting;<BR>पृष्ठमांसादनं तद्यत् परोक्षे दोषकीर्तनं<BR>Hemacandra; see पृष्ठमांस above.<BR>--यानं<BR>riding.<BR>--वंशः the back-bone.<BR>--वास्तु n. the upper story of a house.<BR>--वाह् m.,<BR>--वाह्यः a draught-ox.<BR>--शय a. sleeping on the back.<BR>--शृंगः a wild goat.<BR>--शृंगिन् m. {1} a ram.<BR>{2} a buffalo. {3} a eunuch. {4} an<BR>epithet of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0719-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठकं|पृष्ठक
पृष्ठकं The back. (पृष्ठके कृ {1} to put<BR>off, postpone. {2} to resign, give up,<BR>discard).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठतस्
पृष्ठतस् ind.<BR>1 Behind, behind the<BR>back, from behind, गच्छतः<BR>पृष्ठतोऽन्वियात् Ms. 4. 154; 8. 300;<BR>Bg. 11. 40.<BR>--2 Towards the back,<BR>backwards; गच्छ पृष्ठतः.<BR>--3 On the back.<BR>--4 Behind the back, secretly,<BR>covertly. (पृष्ठतः कृ means {1} to place<BR>on the back, leave behind. {2} to<BR>neglect, forsake, abandon. {3} to<BR>renounce, desist from, leave off,<BR>resign; येनाशाः पृष्ठतः कृत्वा<BR>नैराश्यमवलंबितं H. 1. 144; लज्जां पृष्ठतः कृत्वा K.;<BR>पृष्ठतो गम् to follow; पृष्ठतो भू {1} to<BR>stand at the back. {2} to be<BR>disregarded).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्ठ्य|पृष्ठ्यं|पृष्ठ्यः
पृष्ठ्य a. Relating to the back.<BR>--ष्ठ्यः A pack-horse.<BR>--ष्ठ्या<BR>1 A mare<BR>for draught.<BR>--2 An edge on the<BR>back of the altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पृष्णिः|पृष्णि
पृष्णिः f.<BR>1 The heel,<BR>--2 A ray<BR>of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पॄ
पॄ {c3c} {c9c} P. (पिर्पींत, पृणाति, पपार, अपारीत्,<BR>परि-री-ष्यति, परि-री-तुं, पूर्ण; pass. पूर्यते;<BR>caus. पूरयति-ते; desid. पिपरि-री-षति,<BR>पुपूर्षति)<BR>1 To fill, fill up, complete.<BR>--2<BR>To fulfil, gratify (as hopes &c.).<BR>--3 To fill with wind, blow (as a<BR>conch, flute &c.).<BR>--4 To satisfy,<BR>refresh, please; पितॄनपारित् Bk. 1. 2<BR>--5 To rear, bring up, nourish,<BR>nurture, cherish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचकः|पेचक
पेचकः<BR>1 An owl.<BR>--2 The root of<BR>an elephant's tail.<BR>--3 A couch, bed.<BR>--4 A cloud.<BR>--5 A louse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेचकिन्
पेचकिन् m., पेचिलः An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेंजूषः|पेञ्जूष|पेंजूष|पेञ्जूषः
पेंजूषः^1 The wax of the ear; see<BR>पिंजूषः<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: also pEMjUzaH -> piMjUzaH next line. cf AP and MW72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटः|पेट
पेटः (-टा-टी-टं also)<BR>1 A bag,<BR>basket.<BR>--2 A chest<BR>--3 A multitude.<BR>--4<BR>A retinue, train.<BR>--टः The open<BR>hand with the fingers extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटकः|पेटक|पेटकं
पेटकः --कं<BR>1 A basket, box, bag.<BR>--2<BR>A multitude, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटकं|पेटक|पेटकः
पेटकः --कं<BR>1 A basket, box, bag.<BR>--2<BR>A multitude, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटकः|पेटक|पेटकं
पेटकः A bag, basket, box.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटिका
पेटिका, पेटी A small bag, a basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेटी
पेटिका, पेटी A small bag, a basket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेडा
पेडा A large bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेण्
पेण् {c1c} P. (पेणति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2<BR>To grind.<BR>--3 To embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेत्वं|पेत्व|पेत्वः
पेत्वं<BR>1 Nectar.<BR>--2 Ghee.<BR>--त्वः A<BR>ram (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेय|पेयं
पेय a. [पा-पाने कर्मणि यत्]<BR>1<BR>Drinkable, fit to be quaffed or drunk.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">Page0720-b+ 54</a>]<BR>Sapid.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 Milk.<BR>--3 A<BR>drink, beverage.<BR>--या<BR>1 Rice gruel.<BR>--2 A drink mixed with a small<BR>quantity of boiled rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेयुः|पेयु
पेयुः<BR>1 The sea.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 The<BR>sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेयूषः|पेयूष|पेयूषं
पेयूषः --षं<BR>1 Nectar.<BR>--2 The milk<BR>of a cow that has calved within<BR>seven days; सप्तरात्रप्रसूतायाः क्षीरं<BR>पेयूषमुच्यते Hārāvalī; Ms. 5. 6.<BR>--3 Fresh<BR>ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेयूषं|पेयूष|पेयूषः
पेयूषः --षं<BR>1 Nectar.<BR>--2 The milk<BR>of a cow that has calved within<BR>seven days; सप्तरात्रप्रसूतायाः क्षीरं<BR>पेयूषमुच्यते Hārāvalī; Ms. 5. 6.<BR>--3 Fresh<BR>ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरा
पेरा A kind of musical<BR>instrument; Bk. 17. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेरुः|पेरु
पेरुः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3<BR>The occan.<BR>--4 The gold-mountain<BR>(Meru).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेल्
पेल् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (पेलति, पेलयति-ते)<BR>1 To go or move.<BR>--2 To shake or<BR>tremble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलः|पेल|पेलं
पेलः<BR>1 Going.<BR>--2 A small part.<BR>--लं, पेलकः A testicle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलव|पेलवं
पेलव a.<BR>1 Delicate, fine, soft,<BR>tender; धनुषः पेलवपुष्पपत्रिणः<BR>Ku. 4. 29; 5. 4; 7. 65.<BR>--2 Lean, thin,<BR>slender; कथमातपे गमिष्यसि परिबाधापेलवैरंगैः<BR>Ś. 3. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलिः|पेलि
पेलिः, पेलिन् m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेलिन्
पेलिः, पेलिन् m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशः|पेश
पेशः Form, shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशन
पेशन a.<BR>1 Ved. Well-formed.<BR>--2<BR>Adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशल|पेशलः
पेश(ष-स)ल a.<BR>1 Soft,<BR>tender, delicate; पुष्पचापमिव पेशलं स्मरः<BR>R. 11. 45; 9. 40; Me. 93.<BR>--2<BR>Thin, slender (as waist);<BR>R. 13. 34.<BR>--3 Lovely, beautiful,<BR>charming, good; Bv. 2. 2.<BR>--4<BR>Expert, clever, skilful; Bh. 3. 56;<BR>एकोन्मीलनपेशलः U. 6. 34.<BR>--5 Crafty,<BR>fraudulent.<BR>--6 Decorated, adorned.<BR>--लं Beauty.<BR>--लः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषल|पेषलः
पेश(ष-स)ल a.<BR>1 Soft,<BR>tender, delicate; पुष्पचापमिव पेशलं स्मरः<BR>R. 11. 45; 9. 40; Me. 93.<BR>--2<BR>Thin, slender (as waist);<BR>R. 13. 34.<BR>--3 Lovely, beautiful,<BR>charming, good; Bv. 2. 2.<BR>--4<BR>Expert, clever, skilful; Bh. 3. 56;<BR>एकोन्मीलनपेशलः U. 6. 34.<BR>--5 Crafty,<BR>fraudulent.<BR>--6 Decorated, adorned.<BR>--लं Beauty.<BR>--लः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेसल|पेसलः
पेश(ष-स)ल a.<BR>1 Soft,<BR>tender, delicate; पुष्पचापमिव पेशलं स्मरः<BR>R. 11. 45; 9. 40; Me. 93.<BR>--2<BR>Thin, slender (as waist);<BR>R. 13. 34.<BR>--3 Lovely, beautiful,<BR>charming, good; Bv. 2. 2.<BR>--4<BR>Expert, clever, skilful; Bh. 3. 56;<BR>एकोन्मीलनपेशलः U. 6. 34.<BR>--5 Crafty,<BR>fraudulent.<BR>--6 Decorated, adorned.<BR>--लं Beauty.<BR>--लः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशस्
पेशस् n.<BR>1 Form.<BR>--2 Gold.<BR>--3<BR>Brightness, lustre.<BR>--4 Decoration,<BR>ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशिः|पेशि
पेशिः --शी f.<BR>1 A piece of flesh.<BR>--2 A ball or mass of flesh.<BR>--3 An<BR>egg.<BR>--4 A muscle; Y. 3. 100.<BR>--5<BR>The fœtus shortly after conception.<BR>--6 A bud on the point of blowing.<BR>--7 The thunderbolt of Indra (said<BR>to be m. also).<BR>--8 A kind of<BR>musical instrument.<BR>--9 The shell or rind<BR>(of fruits).<BR>--10 A sheath,<BR>scabbard.<BR>--11 A shoe.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कोशः<BR>--षः a bird's egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेशी
पेशिः --शी f.<BR>1 A piece of flesh.<BR>--2 A ball or mass of flesh.<BR>--3 An<BR>egg.<BR>--4 A muscle; Y. 3. 100.<BR>--5<BR>The fœtus shortly after conception.<BR>--6 A bud on the point of blowing.<BR>--7 The thunderbolt of Indra (said<BR>to be m. also).<BR>--8 A kind of<BR>musical instrument.<BR>--9 The shell or rind<BR>(of fruits).<BR>--10 A sheath,<BR>scabbard.<BR>--11 A shoe.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कोशः<BR>--षः a bird's egg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेष्
पेष् {c1c} A. (पेषते) To resolve upon,<BR>strive diligently for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषः|पेष
पेषः [पिष्-घञ्] Grinding,<BR>pounding, crushing; Śi. 18. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषक
पेषक a. Pounding, grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषणं|पेषण
पेषणं [पिष्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Pounding,<BR>pulverizing.<BR>--2 A threshing-floor.<BR>--3 A stone and muller, any<BR>grinding or pounding apparatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषणिः|पेषणि
पेषणिः f. पेषणी, पेषाकः A<BR>millstone, a grind-stone, muller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेषिः|पेषि
पेषिः A thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेस्
पेस् {c1c} P. (पेसति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पेस्वर
पेस्वर a.<BR>1 Going, moving.<BR>--2<BR>Destructive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पै
पै {c1c} P. (पायति) To dry, wither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैंगिः|पैङ्गि|पैंगि|पैङ्गिः
पैंगिः A patronymic of Yāska.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैंजूषः|पैञ्जूष|पैंजूष|पैञ्जूषः
