पैंडिन्यं|पैण्डिन्य|पैंडिन्य|पैण्डिन्यं
पैंडिक्यं, पैंडिन्यं Living on alms,<BR>mendicity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतामह|पैतामहं
पैतामह a. (ही f.) [पितामह-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Relating to a paternal grandfather.<BR>--2 Inherited or derived from a<BR>paternal grandfather<BR>--3 Derived from,<BR>presided over by, or relating to,<BR>Brahmā; R. 15. 60.<BR>--हाः (pl.)<BR>Ancestors, forefathers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतामहिक
पैतामहिक a. (की f.) Relating to<BR>a paternal grandfather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृक|पैतृकं
पैतृक a. (की f.) [पितृत आगतं<BR>पितृरिदं वा ठञ्]<BR>1 Relating to a father.<BR>--2 Coming or derived from a father,<BR>ancestral, paternal; पदमृद्धमजंन पैतृकं<BR>विनयेनास्य नवं च यौवनं R. 8. 6;<BR>18. 40; Ms. 9. 104; Y. 2. 47.<BR>--3<BR>Sacred to the Manes.<BR>--कं A Śrāddha<BR>performed in honour of the Manes<BR>or deceased ancestors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृमत्यः|पैतृमत्य
पैतृमत्यः<BR>1 The son of an<BR>unmarried woman (पितृप्तत्याः पुत्रः).<BR>--2<BR>The son of an illustrious person<BR>(पितृमतः पुत्रः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृष्वसेयः|पैतृष्वसेय
पैतृष्वसेयः, पैतृष्वस्रीयः The son<BR>of a paternal aunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैतृष्वस्रीयः|पैतृष्वस्रीय
पैतृष्वसेयः, पैतृष्वस्रीयः The son<BR>of a paternal aunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्त|पैत्तः
पैत्त (त्ती f.), पैत्तिक a. (की f.)<BR>Bilious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्तल
पैत्तल a. (ली f.) Made of brass,<BR>brazen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैत्र|पैत्रं
पैत्र a. (त्री f.) [पितुरिदं अण्]<BR>1<BR>Relating to a father or ancestors<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">Page0721-a+ 55</a>]<BR>generally, paternal, ancestral.<BR>--2<BR>Sacred to the Manes.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1 The part<BR>of the hand between the forefinger<BR>and the thumb. (Also पैत्र्प in this<BR>sense).<BR>--2 A year, month, or day<BR>sacred to the Pitṛs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0720-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैप्पल
पैप्पल a. (ली f.) Made of the<BR>wood of the holy fig-tree U. 4. 20;<BR>Mv. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैलव
पैलव a. (वी f.) Made of the<BR>wood of the Pīlu tree; Ms. 2. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशल्यं|पैशल्य
पैशल्यं Mildness, affability,<BR>softness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाच|पैशाचः
पैशाच a. (ची f.) [पिशाचेन निर्वृत्तः<BR>अण्] Demoniacal, infernal.<BR>--चः<BR>1<BR>The eighth or lowest of the eight<BR>forms of marriage in Hindu law, in<BR>which a lover ravishes a maiden<BR>without her consent when she is<BR>sleeping, or intoxicated, or<BR>deranged in intellect; सुप्तां मत्तां प्रमत्तां वा<BR>रहो यत्रोपगच्छति । स पापिष्ठो विवाहानां<BR>पैशाचश्चाष्टमोऽधमः Ms. 3. 34;<BR>Y. 1. 61.<BR>--2 A kind of demon or पिशाच.<BR>--ची<BR>1 A present made at a<BR>religious ceremony.<BR>--2 Night.<BR>--3 A sort<BR>of gibberish spoken on the stage<BR>by demons, one of the lowest forms<BR>of Prākṛta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशाचिक
पैशाचिक a. (की f.) Infernal,<BR>demoniacal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुनं|पैशुन
पैशुनं --न्यं [पिशुनस्य भावः अण् ष्यञ्<BR>वा]<BR>1 Back-biting, slandering,<BR>talebearing, calumny; Ms. 7. 48;<BR>11. 56; Bg. 16. 2.<BR>--2 Roguery,<BR>depravity.<BR>--3 Wickedness, malignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैशुन्यं|पैशुन्य
पैशुनं --न्यं [पिशुनस्य भावः अण् ष्यञ्<BR>वा]<BR>1 Back-biting, slandering,<BR>talebearing, calumny; Ms. 7. 48;<BR>11. 56; Bg. 16. 2.<BR>--2 Roguery,<BR>depravity.<BR>--3 Wickedness, malignity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्ट|पैष्टः
पैष्ट a. (ष्टी f.) [पिष्टस्येदं अण्]<BR>Made of flour or meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्टिक|पैष्टिकं
पैष्टिक a. (की f.) Made of flour<BR>or meal.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A number of cakes.<BR>--2 A spirituous liquor distilled<BR>from meal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पैष्टी
पैष्टी A spirituous liquor distilled<BR>from meal; cf. गौडी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पो
पो a. Pure, clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोगंड|पोगण्ड|पोगण्डः
पोगंड a. [पौः शुद्धो गंड एकदेशो यस्य<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 Young, not adult or<BR>fullgrown.<BR>--2 Having a deficient or<BR>redundant member.<BR>--3 Deformed.<BR>--डः A boy, one from his 5th to his<BR>16th year; cf. अपोगंड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पोटः|पोट
पोटः<BR>1 The foundation of a<BR>house.<BR>--2 Putting together, uniting,<BR>mixing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गलः {1} a kind<BR>of reed (नल). {2} a kind of grass<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-b" target="_blank">Page0721-b+ 55</a>]<BR>(काश). {3} a kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0721-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

