पौत्तिकं|पौत्तिक
पौत्तिकं A kind of honey<BR>(palecoloured).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्र|पौत्त्रः|पौत्रः
पौत्र a. (त्री f.) [पृत्रस्यापत्यं अण्]<BR>1<BR>Relating to or derived from a son.<BR>--त्रः A grandson, son's son.<BR>--त्री {1} A<BR>grand-daughter.<BR>--2 An epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--त्रं The office of a Potṛ, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रिक
पौत्रिक a. (की f.) Belonging to a<BR>son or grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौत्रिकेयः|पौत्रिकेय
पौत्रिकेयः The son of a daughter<BR>appointed to raise issue for her<BR>father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुनिक|पौनःपुनिकः
पौनःपुनिक a. (की f.)<BR>Frequently repeated, recurring again and<BR>again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनःपुन्यं|पौनःपुन्य
पौनःपुन्यं Frequent or constant<BR>repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनरुक्तं|पौनरुक्त
पौनरुक्तं, पौनरुक्त्यं<BR>1 Repetition;<BR>अतिप्रियासीति पौनरुक्त्यं K. 237;<BR>R. 12. 40.<BR>--2 Superfluity, redundancy,<BR>uselessness; अभिव्यक्तायां चंद्रिक्राया<BR>किं दीपिकापौनरुक्त्येन V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनरुक्त्यं|पौनरुक्त्य
पौनरुक्तं, पौनरुक्त्यं<BR>1 Repetition;<BR>अतिप्रियासीति पौनरुक्त्यं K. 237;<BR>R. 12. 40.<BR>--2 Superfluity, redundancy,<BR>uselessness; अभिव्यक्तायां चंद्रिक्राया<BR>किं दीपिकापौनरुक्त्येन V. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौनर्भव|पौनर्भवः
पौनर्भव a. [पुनर्भू विदा˚ अपत्ये अञ्]<BR>1 Relating to a widow who has<BR>married a second husband.<BR>--2<BR>Repeated, superfluous.<BR>--वः<BR>1 The son<BR>of a widow remarried, one of the<BR>twelve sons recognised by the old<BR>Hindu law; Y. 2. 130; Ms. 3. 1. 55.<BR>--2 The second husband of a woman;<BR>Ms. 9. 176.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर|पौरं|पौरः
पौर a. (री f.) [पुरे वसति शैषिके<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Relating to a city or town,<BR>produced in a town, civic.<BR>--2 Ved.<BR>Filling one's own belly.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A<BR>townsman, citizen; (opp. जानपद);<BR>Ku. 6. 41; Me. 27; R. 2. 10, 74;<BR>12. 3; 16. 9.<BR>--2 A term applied to a<BR>prince engaged in war under<BR>particular circumstances.<BR>--3 A planet in a<BR>state of opposition to other planets.<BR>--री The language of the servants in<BR>a palace.<BR>--रं A sort of grass (रोहिष).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगना, --योषित् f.,<BR>--स्त्री a<BR>woman living in a town.<BR>--कार्यं<BR>public business; अर्थजातस्य<BR>गणनाबहुलतयैकभेव पौरकार्यमवेक्षितं Ś. 6.<BR>--जनः,<BR>--लोकः {1} a citizen. {2} citizens,<BR>burghers.<BR>--जानपद a. belonging to town<BR>and country. (--दाः pl.) citizens and<BR>rustics, townsmen and country<BR>people; कथं दुर्जनाः पौरजानपदाः U. 1.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">Page0722-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--वृद्धः an eminent citizen, an elder<BR>man.<BR>--सख्यं fellow-citizenship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरकं|पौरक|पौरकः
पौरकं<BR>1 A garden near a house.<BR>--2<BR>A garden near a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरिकः|पौरिक
पौरिकः<BR>1 A citizen.<BR>--2 A governor<BR>of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरेय
पौरेय a. (यी f.) Civic, town-bred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरंदर
पौरंदर a. (री) Derived from<BR>or sacred to, Indra.<BR>--रं The<BR>lunar mansion called ज्येष्ठा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरव|पौरवः
पौरव a. (वी f.) [पुरोर्गोत्रापत्यं<BR>अण्] Descended from Puru.<BR>--वः<BR>1 A descendant of Puru; Ś. 5.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a country or people in the<BR>north of India.<BR>--3 An<BR>inhabitant or ruler of that country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरवीय
पौरवीय a. (यी f.) Devoted to<BR>Paurava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरस्त्य|पौरस्त्यः
पौरस्त्य a. [पुरस् --भवार्ये त्यक् अण्<BR>च]<BR>1 Eastern: पौरस्त्यो वा सुखयति<BR>मरुत् साधुसंवाहनाभिः Māl. 9. 25<BR>पौरस्त्यझंझामरुत् 9. 17; R. 4. 34.<BR>--2<BR>Foremost.<BR>--3 Prior, first, preceding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराण
पौराण a. (णी f.) [पुराण-अण्]<BR>1<BR>{1} Belonging to the past, ancient,<BR>of the past, primeval.<BR>--2<BR>Relating to the Purāṇas or derived<BR>from them.<BR>--3 Former, previous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौराणिक|पौराणिकः
पौराणिक a. (की f.) [पुराण-ठक्]<BR>1 Belonging to the past, ancient.<BR>--2 Belonging to the Purāṇas or<BR>derived from them.<BR>--3 Versed in<BR>the legends of the past.<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>A Brāhmaṇa well-versed in the<BR>Purāṇas, a public reader of the<BR>Purāṇas.<BR>--2 A mythologist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुष|पौरुषं|पौरुषः
पौरुष a. (षी f.) [पुरुष-अण्]<BR>1 Relating to a man or man in<BR>general, human.<BR>--2 Manly, virile.<BR>--3 Sacred to Puruṣa.<BR>--षः A<BR>weight which can be carried by<BR>one man.<BR>--षी A woman.<BR>--षं<BR>1<BR>Human action, man's work, exer<BR>tion, effort; धिग्धिग्वृथा पौरुषं<BR>Bh. 2. 38; दैवं निहत्य कुरु पौरुषमात्मशक्त्या<BR>Pt. 1. 361; 2. 81.<BR>--2 (a)<BR>Heroism, prowess, valour, manliness,<BR>courage; पौरुषभूषणः R. 15. 28;<BR>8. 28. (b) Strength, power, vigour.<BR>--3 Virility; Bg. 7. 8.<BR>--4 Semen<BR>virile.<BR>--5 Penis.<BR>--6 The full height<BR>of a man, the height to which he<BR>reaches with both arms elevated<BR>and the fingers extended.<BR>--7<BR>Sundial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषिकः|पौरुषिक
पौरुषिकः A worshipper of<BR>Purusha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुषेय|पौरुषेयः
पौरुषेय a. (यी f.) [पुरुष-ठञ्]<BR>1<BR>Derived from or belonging to man,<BR>human, incidental to man; made,<BR>established or propounded by man;<BR>as in अपौरुषेया वै वेदाः.<BR>--2 Manly,<BR>virile.<BR>--3 Spiritual.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>Manslaughter (पुरुषवध).<BR>--2 A crowd of<BR>men.<BR>--3 A day labourer, hireling.<BR>--4 Human action, man's work.<BR>--5<BR>Law as affecting persons.<BR>--यं<BR>Human work, action of man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुष्यं|पौरुष्य
पौरुष्यं Manliness, courage,<BR>heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरुहूत
पौरुहूत a. (ती f.) Belonging to<BR>Indra; अस्याधिज्ये धनुषि विजयं<BR>पौरुह्वते च वज्रे Ś. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोगवः|पौरोगव
पौरोगवः A superintendent of<BR>the royal household; especially, of<BR>the royal kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोडाशः|पौरोडाश
