पौरोडाशिकः|पौरोडाशिक
पौरोडाशिकः A priest who<BR>repeats the above Mantra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोधसं|पौरोधस
पौरोधसं The office of a<BR>familypriest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोभाग्यं|पौरोभाग्य
पौरोभाग्यं<BR>1 Fault-finding,<BR>censoriousness; प्रियोपभोगचिह्नेषु<BR>पौरोभाग्यपिवाचरन् R. 12. 22.<BR>--2 Ill-will,<BR>envy, jealousy.<BR>--3 An ill natured<BR>act, mischievous deed; किमिदमनुष्ठितं<BR>पौरोभाग्यं Ś. 6.<BR>--4 Obtrusiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौरोहित्यं|पौरोहित्य
पौरोहित्यं The office of a<BR>family-priest; Pt. 2. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमास|पौर्णमासः
पौर्णमास a. (सी f.) Relating<BR>to the full moon.<BR>--सः A ceremony<BR>performed on the full moon day by<BR>one who maintains the sacred fire<BR>(अग्निहात्रिन्).<BR>--सं A day of full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमासी
पौर्णमासी, पौर्णमी A day of full<BR>moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमी
पौर्णमासी, पौर्णमी A day of full<BR>moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णमास्यं|पौर्णमास्य
पौर्णमास्यं A sacrifice performed on<BR>the full-moon day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णिमः|पौर्णिम
पौर्णिमः An ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्णिमा
पौर्णिमा A day of full moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्तिक|पौर्त्तिक
पौर्तिक a. (की f.) Relating to<BR>acts of pious charity; Ms. 3. 178;<BR>4. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्व|पौर्व्व
पौर्व a. (र्वी f.)<BR>1 Relating to the<BR>past.<BR>--2 Relating to the east,<BR>eastern.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वदेहिक|पौर्व्वदेहिक
पौर्वदे(दै)हिक a. (की f.)<BR>Relating to a former existence, done<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">Page0723-a+ 54</a>]<BR>in a former life; Bg. 6. 43;<BR>Y. 1. 349.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वदैहिक
पौर्वदे(दै)हिक a. (की f.)<BR>Relating to a former existence, done<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">Page0723-a+ 54</a>]<BR>in a former life; Bg. 6. 43;<BR>Y. 1. 349.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0722-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वपदिक|पौर्व्वपदिक
पौर्वपदिक a. (की f.) Relating<BR>to the first member of a compound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वापर्यं|पौर्वापर्य|पौर्वापर्य्य|पौर्व्वापर्य्य
पौर्वापर्यं<BR>1 The relation of prior<BR>and posterior.<BR>--2 Due order,<BR>succession, continuity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्वाह्णिक|पौर्व्वाह्णिक|पौर्व्वाह्णिकः
पौर्वाह्णिक a. (की f.) Relating to<BR>the forenoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौर्विक|पौर्व्विक
पौर्विक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Previous,<BR>former, prior; जातिं स्मरति पौर्विकीं<BR>Ms. 4. 148.<BR>--2 Ancestral.<BR>--3 Old,<BR>ancient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलस्त्यः|पौलस्त्य
पौलस्त्यः<BR>1 An epithet of<BR>Rāvaṇa; पौलस्त्यः कथमन्यदारहरणे दोषं न<BR>विज्ञ तवान् Pt. 2. 4; R. 4. 80; 10. 5;<BR>12. 72.<BR>--2 Of Kubera.<BR>--3 Of<BR>Bibhīṣaṇa<BR>--4 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलस्ती
पौलस्ती An epithet of<BR>Śūrpaṇakha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलिः|पौलि
पौलिः m. f. पौली f. A kind of<BR>cake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलोम|पौलोमः
पौलोम a. (मी f.) Relating to<BR>or descended from, Puloman or<BR>Pulomā.<BR>--मः N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौलोमी
पौलोमी Śacī, daughter of<BR>Puloman and wife of Indra; अ शीरन्या न<BR>ते यु का पौलोम्या सदृशी भव Ś. 7. 28.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संभवः an epithet of<BR>Jayanta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौषः|पौष
पौषः<BR>1 N. of a lunar month in<BR>which the moon is in the Puṣya<BR>asterism (corresponding to<BR>December-January).<BR>--षी The day of<BR>full moon in the month of Pauṣa;<BR>R. 18. 32.<BR>--षं {1} A festival.<BR>--2 A<BR>fight, combat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कर|पौष्करं
पौष्कर --रक (री-की f.),<BR>Relating to the blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्करक
पौष्कर --रक (री-की f.),<BR>Relating to the blue lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्करिणी
पौष्करिणी A lotus pool or pond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कलः|पौष्कल
पौष्कलः A species of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्कल्यं|पौष्कल्य
पौष्कल्यं<BR>1 Maturity, complete<BR>development, full growth.<BR>--2<BR>Abundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्टिक|पौष्टिकं
पौष्टिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Promoting<BR>growth or welfare.<BR>--2 Nourishing,<BR>nutritive, nutritious, invigorating.<BR>--3 Preservative.<BR>--कं A cloth worn<BR>during the tonsure ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्णं|पौष्ण
पौष्णं The lunar mansion called<BR>Revatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्प|पौष्पं
पौष्प a. (ष्पी f.) [पुष्प्-अण्]<BR>Relating to or coming from flowers,<BR>floral, flowery.<BR>--ष्पी<BR>1 N. of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">Page0723-b+ 55</a>]<BR>town पाटलिपुत्र q. v.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>spirituous liquor (made from<BR>flowers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पौष्पकं|पौष्पक
पौष्पकं Green vitriol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्याट्
प्याट् ind. A particle of calling<BR>(ho!, holla).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्याय्
प्याय् {c1c} A. (प्यायते, प्यान or पीन)<BR>To swell, grow; see प्यै below,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यान
प्यान a. Fat, grown fat; cf. पीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यायन
प्यायन a.<BR>1 Invigorating.<BR>--2<BR>Promoting strength or growth.<BR>--नं<BR>Increase, growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यायित
प्यायित a.<BR>1 Grown, increased.<BR>--2 Grown fat.<BR>--3 Refreshed,<BR>strengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्यै
प्यै {c1c} A. (प्यायते, पीन)<BR>1 To grow,<BR>increase, swell; Bk. 6. 33<BR>--2 To<BR>become full or exuberant.<BR>--3 To<BR>overfill, surcharge. --Caus. (प्या ययति<BR>ते)<BR>1 To increase, enlarge, make fat<BR>or comfortable; Ms. 9. 314.<BR>--2 To<BR>gratify, regale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्र
प्र ind.<BR>1 As a prefix to verbs it<BR>means ‘forward’, ‘forth’, ‘in<BR>front’, ‘onward’, ‘before’, ‘away’,<BR>as in प्रगम्, प्रस्या, प्रचर्, प्रय &c.<BR>--2<BR>With adjectives it means ‘very’,<BR>‘excessively’, ‘very much’ &c:<BR>प्रकृष्ट, प्रमत्त &c., see further on.<BR>--3 With<BR>nouns whether derived from verbs<BR>or not, it is used in the following<BR>senses according to G. M.:-- (a)<BR>beginning, commencement; (प्रमाणं,<BR>प्रस्थानं, प्रह्ण); (b) length; (<BR>प्रवालभूषिक); (c) power (प्रभु); (d)<BR>intensity, excess; (प्रवाद, प्रकर्ष, प्रच्छाय,<BR>प्रगुण); (e) source or origin; (प्रभव, प्रपौत्र);<BR>(f) completion, perfectness,<BR>satisfaction (प्रभुक्तमन्नं); (g) destitution,<BR>separation, being without; (प्रोषिता,<BR>प्रपर्णवृक्षः); (h) apart; (प्रज्ञु); (i)<BR>excellence; (प्राचार्यः): (j) purity<BR>(प्रसन्नं जलं); (k) wish (प्रार्थना); (l)<BR>cessation (प्रशम); (m.) adoration,<BR>respect; (प्रांजलिः who respectfully<BR>folds his hands together); (n.)<BR>prominence (प्रणस, प्रवाल). In the Veda<BR>it is often used as a separable<BR>adverb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकट|प्रकटं
प्रकट a<BR>1 Evident, plain, clear,<BR>apparent, manifest.<BR>--2 Undisguised,<BR>public.<BR>--3 Visible.<BR>--टं ind.<BR>1<BR>Clearly, manifestly; evidently.<BR>--2<BR>Publicly, openly, undisguisedly (<BR>प्रकटीकृ to manifest, unfold, display;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">Page0723-c+ 57</a>]<BR>गुह्यं च गूहति गुणान् प्रकटीकरोति<BR>Bh. 2 72; Pt. 1. 31; प्रकटीभू ‘to become<BR>manifest, appear’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रीतिवर्धनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटनं|प्रकटन
प्रकटनं The act of manifesting,<BR>disclosing, unfolding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटति
प्रकटति Den. P. To become<BR>manifest or visible, appear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटयति
प्रकटयति Den. P.<BR>1 To show,<BR>manifest, display, exhibit; Māl. 5. 11,<BR>N. 4. 151; Ratn. 4. 16<BR>--2 To<BR>proclaim, announce publicly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकटित|प्रकटितं
प्रकटित p. p.<BR>1 Manifested,<BR>displayed, unfolded.<BR>--2 Publicly<BR>exhibited.<BR>--3 Apparent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकथ्
प्रकथ् {c10c} U. To announce,<BR>proclaim, narrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकथनं|प्रकथन
प्रकथनं Announcing, narration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकंप्|प्रकम्प्
प्रकंप् {1} A<BR>1 To shake, quiver,<BR>tremble; प्राकंपत भुजः सव्यः Rām.;<BR>प्राकंपत महाशैलः Mb.<BR>--2 To vibrate<BR>(as sound).<BR>--3 To become loose, be<BR>loosened. --Caus. To shake, put in<BR>motion; Bk. 15. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकंपः|प्रकम्प|प्रकंप|प्रकम्पः
प्रकंपः Trembling, shaking,<BR>quivering, violent motion or tremour;<BR>बाला चाहं मनसिजवशात्प्र प्तग ढप्रकंपा<BR>Subhāṣ.; सशिरः प्रकंपं Śi. 13. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकंपन|प्रकम्पन|प्रकम्पनः
प्रकंपन a. Causing to shake.<BR>--नः<BR>1 Wind, violent wind or gust;<BR>प्रकंपनेनानुचकंपिरे सुराः Śi. 1. 61. 14. 43.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a hell.<BR>--नं Excessive or violent<BR>trembling, violent motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकंपिन्|प्रकम्पिन्
प्रकंपिन् a. Swinging, shaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्
प्रकल् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To pursue, go<BR>after.<BR>--2 To urge on, incite.<BR>--3 To<BR>hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकालन|प्रकालनः
प्रकालन a.<BR>1 Killing, hurting.<BR>--2<BR>Pursuing. chasing.<BR>--तः N. of a<BR>Nāga.<BR>--नं Hurting, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकला
प्रकला A minute portion<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विद् a ignorant. (--m.) a<BR>merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकांडः|प्रकाण्ड|प्रकांड|प्रकांडं|प्रकाण्डः
प्रकांडः, --डं<BR>1 The trunk of a tree<BR>from the root to the branches;<BR>Śi. 9. 45.<BR>--2 A branch, shoot.<BR>--3 (At<BR>the end of comp.) Anything excellent<BR>or pre-eminent of its kind;<BR>ऊरुप्रकांडद्वितयेन तस्याः N. 7. 93; क्षत्रप्रकांडः<BR>Mv. 4. 35; 5. 48.<BR>--डः The upper<BR>part of the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकांडं|प्रकाण्ड|प्रकांड|प्रकांडः|प्रकाण्डः
प्रकांडः, --डं<BR>1 The trunk of a tree<BR>from the root to the branches;<BR>Śi. 9. 45.<BR>--2 A branch, shoot.<BR>--3 (At<BR>the end of comp.) Anything excellent<BR>or pre-eminent of its kind;<BR>ऊरुप्रकांडद्वितयेन तस्याः N. 7. 93; क्षत्रप्रकांडः<BR>Mv. 4. 35; 5. 48.<BR>--डः The upper<BR>part of the arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकांडकः|प्रकाण्डक|प्रकांडक|प्रकाण्डकः
प्रकांडकः^1 See प्रकांड above;<BR>Bk. 5. 6.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: badly printed, lost anusvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकांडरः|प्रकाण्डर|प्रकांडर|प्रकाण्डरः
प्रकांडरः A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाम|प्रकामं|प्रकामः
प्रकाम a.<BR>1 Amorous.<BR>--2<BR>Excessive, much, to the heart's content,<BR>at pleasure; प्रकामविस्तार R. 2. 11;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-a" target="_blank">Page0724-a+ 55</a>]<BR>प्रकामालोकनीयतां Ku. 2. 24.<BR>--मः<BR>Desire, pleasure, satisfaction.<BR>--मं<BR>ind.<BR>1 Very much, exceedingly;<BR>जातो ममायं विशदः प्रकामं (अंतरोत्मा)<BR>Ś. 4. 21; R. 6. 44; Mk. 5. 25.<BR>--2<BR>Sufficiently, to the heart's content,<BR>according to the wish or desire.<BR>--3<BR>Voluntarily, willingly;<BR>Mu. 1. 25.<BR>--भुज् a. eating till satisfied or<BR>to the heart's content; R. 1. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0723-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकामतः
प्रकामतः ind.<BR>1 At will.<BR>--2 With<BR>pleasure, willingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाश्
प्रकाश् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To shine, gleam;<BR>look brilliant.<BR>--2 To become visible<BR>or manifest, come to light; to be<BR>apparent, appear; एषु सर्वेषु भूतेषु गूढोऽ<BR>ऽत्मा न प्रकाशते Kaṭh.<BR>--3 To look or<BR>appear like. --Caus.<BR>1 To show,<BR>display, manifest, discover;<BR>अवसरोऽयमात्मानं प्रकाशयितुं Ś. 1;<BR>Sāṅ. K. 59.<BR>--2 To disclose, unfold, reveal.<BR>--3 To bring to light, make public,<BR>proclaim, कदाचित्कुपितं मित्रं सर्वदोषं<BR>प्रकाशयेत् Chāṇ. 20.<BR>--4 To publish,<BR>bring out (as a work); प्रणीतः न तु<BR>प्रकाशितः U. 4.<BR>--5 To illuminate,<BR>lighten, irradiate; यथा<BR>प्रकाशयत्येकः कृत्स्नं लोकमिमं रविः Bg. 13. 33;<BR>5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाश|प्रकाशं|प्रकाशः
प्रकाश a.<BR>1 Bright, shining,<BR>brilliant; प्रकाशश्चाप्रकाशश्च लोकालोक<BR>इवाचलः R. 1. 68; 5. 2.<BR>--2 Clear,<BR>visible, manifest; Śi. 12. 56;<BR>Bg. 7. 25.<BR>--3 Vivid, perspicuous;<BR>Ki. 14. 4.<BR>--4 Famous, renowned,<BR>celebrated, noted; R. 3. 48.<BR>--5 Open,<BR>public.<BR>--6 Cleared of trees, open;<BR>R. 4. 31.<BR>--7 Blown, expanded.<BR>--8<BR>(At the end of comp.) Looking<BR>like, like, resembling.<BR>--शः<BR>1<BR>Light, lustre, splendour, brightness.<BR>--2 (Fig.) Light, elucidation,<BR>explanation (mostly at the end of<BR>titles of works); काव्यप्रकाश,<BR>भावप्रकाश; तर्कप्रकाश &c.<BR>--3 Sunshine.<BR>--4 Display, manifestation;<BR>Śi. 9. 5.<BR>--5 Fame, renown, celebrity;<BR>glory.<BR>--6 Expansion, diffusion.<BR>--7<BR>Open spot or air; प्रकाशं निर्गतोऽ<BR>वलोकय मि Ś. 4.<BR>--8 A golden mirror.<BR>--9 A chapter or section (of a book).<BR>--10 The gloss on the upper part of<BR>a horse's body.<BR>--शं Bell-metal<BR>brass.<BR>--शं ind.<BR>1 Openly, publicly;<BR>प्रतिभूर्दापितो यत्तु प्रकाशं धनिनो धनं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">Page0724-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Y. 2. 56; Ms. 8. 193; 9. 228.<BR>--2<BR>Aloud, audibly (used as a<BR>stagedirection in dramas; opp. आत्मगतं).<BR>--शे ind.<BR>1 Openly, publicly.<BR>--2<BR>Visibly.<BR>--3 In the presence of.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मक a. shining,<BR>brilliant.<BR>--आत्मन् a. bright, shining.<BR>(--m.) an epithet of (1) Viṣṇu.<BR>(2) of Śiva. (3) the sun.<BR>--इतर a.<BR>invisible.<BR>--कर्तृ, --कर्मन् N. of the<BR>sun.<BR>--क्रयः an open purchase.<BR>--नारी<BR>a public woman, prostitute, harlot;<BR>अलं चतुःशालमिमं प्रवेश्य<BR>प्रकाशनारीधृत एष यस्मात् Mk. 3. 7.<BR>--वंचकः<BR>an open cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशक|प्रकाशकः
प्रकाशक a. (शिका f.)<BR>1 Illuminating,<BR>giving light.<BR>--2 Making apparent,<BR>discovering, disclosing, evincing,<BR>betraying, displaying.<BR>--3<BR>Expressing, indicating.<BR>--4 Explaining,<BR>making clear, expounding.<BR>--5<BR>Bright, shining, brilliant.<BR>--6 Noted,<BR>celebrated, renowned.<BR>--कः<BR>1 The<BR>sun.<BR>--2 A discoverer.<BR>--3 An<BR>expounder.<BR>--4 A publisher.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञातृ<BR>m. a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशता
प्रकाशता --त्वं<BR>1 Brilliance,<BR>splendour.<BR>--2 Appearance, manifestation.<BR>--3 Renown, celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशत्वं|प्रकाशत्व
प्रकाशता --त्वं<BR>1 Brilliance,<BR>splendour.<BR>--2 Appearance, manifestation.<BR>--3 Renown, celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशन|प्रकाशनः
प्रकाशन a. Illuminating, making<BR>known &c.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Making known<BR>or manifest, bringing to light,<BR>disclosing.<BR>--2 Displaying, manifesting.<BR>--3 Illuminating, giving light,<BR>irradiating, making bright.<BR>--4<BR>Announcement, declaration.<BR>--नः<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--ना Explaining,<BR>teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशित|प्रकाशितं
प्रकाशित p. p.<BR>1 Made clear or<BR>manifest, displayed, manifested.<BR>--2<BR>Published; brought out (as a book)<BR>--3 Illuminated, irradiated,<BR>enlightened.<BR>--4 Visible, evident,<BR>apparent.<BR>--तं Light, clearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाश्य
प्रकाश्य a. To be illuminated,<BR>brought to light &c.<BR>--श्यं Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकाशिन्
प्रकाशिन् a. Clear, bright,<BR>shining &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुंचः|प्रकुञ्च|प्रकुंच|प्रकुञ्चः
प्रकुंचः A particular measure of<BR>capacity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुप्
प्रकुप् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be angry, to be<BR>enraged or provoked at: निमित्तमुविश्य<BR>हि यः प्रकुप्यति ध्रुवं स तस्यापगमे<BR>प्रसीदति Pt. 1. 283.<BR>--2 To be excited,<BR>gather strength, increase. --Caus.<BR>To provoke, irritate, exasperate;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">Page0724-c+ 56</a>]<BR>साधोः प्रकीपितस्यापि मनो नायाति<BR>विक्रियाम Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुपित
प्रकुपित p. p.<BR>1 Very angry,<BR>enraged, incensed.<BR>--2 Excited.<BR>--3<BR>Disordered, deranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपः|प्रकोप
प्रकोपः<BR>1 Wrath, fury, rage,<BR>violent anger.<BR>--2 Great excitement;<BR>provocation, irritation; उपदेशो हि<BR>मूर्खाणां प्रकोपाय न शांतये Pt. 1. 389.<BR>--3 Insurrection, rebellion, mutiny;<BR>as in प्रकृति˚ popular disturbance.<BR>--4<BR>An attack.<BR>--5 (Medic.) Excess,<BR>superabundance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपन
प्रकोपन --ण a. Irritating, exciting,<BR>provoking.<BR>--नं --णं Provocation,<BR>irritation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपण
प्रकोपन --ण a. Irritating, exciting,<BR>provoking.<BR>--नं --णं Provocation,<BR>irritation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोपित
प्रकोपित p. p. Provoked, enraged,<BR>incensed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकुलं|प्रकुल
प्रकुलं A handsome body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकूष्मांडी|प्रकूष्माण्डी
प्रकूष्मांडी An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृ
प्रकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To do, perform,<BR>commence (used much in the same<BR>sense as कृ); जानन्नपि नरो<BR>दैवात्प्रकरोति विगर्हितं Pt. 4. 35; Ki. 4. 30,<BR>Mv. 2. 13, Bk. 2. 36; Rs. 1. 6;<BR>Ms. 8. 54, 60; 8. 230; Amaru. 13.<BR>--2 To accomplish, achieve, effect.<BR>--3 To assault, outrage, insult;<BR>Bk. 8. 19.<BR>--4 To honor, worship.<BR>--5<BR>To express, utter.<BR>--6 To place in<BR>front, mention first.<BR>--7 To appoint<BR>(to a post, office &c.).<BR>--8 Ved. To<BR>induce.<BR>--9 To win, conquer.<BR>--10<BR>To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरः|प्रकर|प्रकरं
प्रकरः<BR>1 A heap, multitude,<BR>quantity, collection; मुक्ताफलप्रकरभांजि<BR>गुहागृहाणि Śi. 5. 12; बाष्पप्रकरकलुषां<BR>दृष्टिं Ś. 6. 8; R. 9. 56; Ku. 5. 68.<BR>--2 A nosegay, bunch of flowers.<BR>--3 Aid, assistance, friendship.<BR>--4<BR>Usage, practice.<BR>--5 Respect.<BR>--6<BR>Seduction, abduction.<BR>--रं<BR>Aloewood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरणं|प्रकरण
प्रकरणं<BR>1 Treating, explaining,<BR>discussing.<BR>--2 (a) A subject, topic,<BR>department, a subject (of<BR>representation); कतमत्प्रकरणमाश्रित्य<BR>Ś. 1. (b) A head or subject of<BR>treatment. (c) A province or<BR>department.<BR>--3 A section, chapter or<BR>any smaller division of a work.<BR>--4 An opportunity, occasion.<BR>--5<BR>An affair, a matter.<BR>--6 An<BR>introduction, prologue.<BR>--7 Relation.<BR>--8<BR>Doing much or well.<BR>--9 A<BR>species of drama with invented or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-a" target="_blank">Page0725-a+ 57</a>]<BR>fictitious plot; as the मृच्छकटिक,<BR>मालतीमाधव, पुष्पभूषित &c. The S. D.<BR>thus defines it:<BR>--भवेत् प्रकरणे वृत्तं<BR>लौकिकं कविकल्पितं । शृंगारोंऽगी नायकस्तु<BR>विप्रोऽमात्योऽथवा वणिक् । सापायधर्मकामार्थपरो<BR>धीरप्रशांतकः ॥ 511.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0724-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरणिका
प्रकरणिका, प्रकरणी A drama of the<BR>same character as the प्रकरण. The<BR>S. D. thus defines it:<BR>--नाटिकैव<BR>प्रकरणिका सार्थवाहादिनायिका । समानवंशजा<BR>नेतुर्भवेद्यत्र च नायिका ॥ 554.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरणी
प्रकरणिका, प्रकरणी A drama of the<BR>same character as the प्रकरण. The<BR>S. D. thus defines it:<BR>--नाटिकैव<BR>प्रकरणिका सार्थवाहादिनायिका । समानवंशजा<BR>नेतुर्भवेद्यत्र च नायिका ॥ 554.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरिका
प्रकरिका An interlude or episode<BR>inserted in a drama to explain<BR>what is to follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकरी
प्रकरी<BR>1 An interlude or episode<BR>inserted in a drama to explain what<BR>is to follow.<BR>--2 Theatrical dress.<BR>--3<BR>An open piece of ground.<BR>--4 A<BR>place where four roads meet.<BR>--5 A<BR>kind of song.<BR>--6 The proper site<BR>of any magical operations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकारः|प्रकार
प्रकारः<BR>1 Manner, mode, way,<BR>fashion; कः प्रकारः किमेतत् Māl. 5. 20.<BR>--2 Sort, kind, variety, species; oft.<BR>in comp.; बहुप्रकार manifold;<BR>त्रिप्रकार, नाना˚ &c.<BR>--3 Similitude.<BR>--4<BR>Speciality, special property or<BR>quality; तद्वति तत्प्रकारकोऽनुभवः प्रमा T.<BR>S.<BR>--5 Difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृत|प्रकृतः
प्रकृत p. p.<BR>1 Accomplished,<BR>completed.<BR>--2 Commenced, begun.<BR>--3<BR>Appointed, charged.<BR>--4 Genuine,<BR>real.<BR>--5 Forming the subject of<BR>discussion, that which is under<BR>consideration, the subject in hand<BR>(often used in works on Alaṃkāra<BR>for उपमेय); संभावनमथोत्प्रेक्षा प्रकृतस्य<BR>समेन यत् K. P. 10.<BR>--6 Important,<BR>interesting.<BR>--7 Wished, expected.<BR>--8 Original.<BR>--तं The original<BR>subject, the matter or subject in hand;<BR>यातु किमनेन प्रकृतमेव अनुसरामः ‘come<BR>to the point.’<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. {1}<BR>having the original sense. {2} true,<BR>real.<BR>--(र्थः) the original sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृतिः|प्रकृति
प्रकृतिः f.<BR>1 The natural condition<BR>or state of anything, nature,<BR>natural form (opp. विकृति which is a<BR>change or effect); प्रकृत्या यद्वक्रं<BR>Ś. 1. 9; उष्णत्वमग्न्यातपसंप्रयोगात् शैत्यं<BR>हि यत्सा प्रकृतिर्जलस्य R. 5. 54; मरणं<BR>प्रकृतिः शरीरिणां विकृतिर्जीवितमुच्यते<BR>बुधैः R. 8. 87; U. 7. 19; अपेहि रे<BR>अत्रभवान् प्रकृतिमापन्नः Ś. 2 ‘has<BR>resumed his wonted nature’;<BR>प्रकृतिमापट् or प्रतिपद् or प्रकृतौ स्था ‘to come<BR>to one's senses’, ‘regain one's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-b" target="_blank">Page0725-b+ 57</a>]<BR>consciousness’.<BR>--2 Natural disposition,<BR>temper, temperament, nature,<BR>constitution; प्रकृतिः खलु सा महीयसः<BR>सहते नान्यसमुन्नतिं यया Ki. 2. 21; कथं<BR>गत एव आत्मनः प्रकृतिं Ś. 7 ‘natural<BR>character’; so प्रकृतिकृपण, प्रकृतिसिद्ध<BR>see below.<BR>--3 Make, form, figure;<BR>महानुभावप्रकृतिः Māl. 1.<BR>--4<BR>Extraction, descent; गोपालप्रकृतिरार्यकोस्मि<BR>Mk. 7.<BR>--5 Origin, source, original<BR>or material cause, the material of<BR>which anything is made;<BR>प्रकृतिश्चोपादानकारणं च ब्रह्याभ्युपगंतव्यं Ś. B.<BR>(see the full discussion on<BR>Br. Sūt. I. 4. 23); यामाहुः सर्वभूतप्रकृतिरिति<BR>Ś. 1. 1.<BR>--6 (In Sān. phil.) Nature<BR>(as distinguished from पुरुष,) the<BR>original source of the material<BR>world, consisting of the three<BR>essential qualities सत्त्व, रजस् and<BR>तमस्.<BR>--7 (In gram.) The radical or<BR>crude form of a word to which<BR>caseterminations and other affixes are<BR>applied<BR>--8 A model, pattern,<BR>standard, (especially in ritualistic<BR>works).<BR>--9 A woman.<BR>--10 The<BR>personified will of the Supreme<BR>Spirit in the creation (identified<BR>with माया or illusion); Bg. 9. 10.<BR>--11 The male or female organ of<BR>generation.<BR>--12 A mother.<BR>--13 (In<BR>arith.) A co-efficient, or multiplier.<BR>--14 (In anatomy) Temperament<BR>of the humours.<BR>--15 An animal.<BR>--16 An artisan.<BR>--17 The Supreme<BR>Being. --pl.<BR>1 A king's ministers,<BR>the body of ministers or counsellors,<BR>ministry; R. 12. 12; Pt. 1. 48, 301.<BR>--2<BR>The subjects (of a king); प्रवर्ततां<BR>प्रकृतिहिताय पार्थिवः Ś. 7. 35; नृपतिः<BR>प्रकृतीरवेक्षितुं R. 8. 18, 10.<BR>--3 The<BR>constituent elements of the state (<BR>सप्तांगानि), i. e. 1. the king; 2. the<BR>minister; 3. the allies; 4.<BR>treasure; 5. army; 6. territory; 7.<BR>fortresses &c.; and the<BR>corporations of citizens (which is<BR>sometimes added to the 7);<BR>स्वाम्यमात्यसुहृत्कोशराष्ट्रदुर्गबलानि च Ak.<BR>--4 The<BR>various sovereigns to be considered<BR>in case of war; (for full<BR>explanation see Kull. on Ms. 7. 155 and<BR>157).<BR>--5 The eight primary<BR>elements out of which everything else<BR>is evolved according to the<BR>Sānkhyas; see Sāṅ. K. 3.<BR>--6 The five<BR>primary elements of creations (<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-c" target="_blank">Page0725-c+ 57</a>]<BR>पंचमहाभूतानि); i. e. पृथ्वी, अप्, तेजस्,<BR>वायु, and आकाश.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः a<BR>king or magistrate.<BR>--कृपण a.<BR>naturally slow or unable to discern;<BR>Me. 5.<BR>--गुणः one of the three<BR>constituent qualities of nature; see<BR>गुण.<BR>--ज a. innate, inborn, natural.<BR>--तरल a. fickle by nature, naturally<BR>inconsistent; Amaru. 27.<BR>--पुरुषः a<BR>minister, a functionary (of the<BR>state); Me. 6.<BR>--भाव a. natural,<BR>usual.<BR>--(वः) natural or original<BR>state.<BR>--मंडलं the whole territory or<BR>kingdom; R. 9. 2.<BR>--लयः<BR>absorption into the Prakṛti, dissolution of<BR>the universe.<BR>--सिद्ध a. inborn,<BR>innate, natural; Bh. 2. 52.<BR>--सुभग a.<BR>naturally lovely or agreeable.<BR>--स्थ<BR>a. {1} being in the natural state or<BR>condition, natural, genuine. {2}<BR>inherent, innate, incidental to nature;<BR>R. 8. 21. {3} healthy, in good<BR>health. {4} recovered. {5} come to<BR>oneself. {6} stripped of everything,<BR>bare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रिया
प्रक्रिया<BR>1 Way, manner,<BR>conduct.<BR>--2 A rite, ceremony.<BR>--3 The<BR>bearing of royal insignia.<BR>--4 High<BR>position, elevation.<BR>--5 A chapter<BR>or section (of a book); as in<BR>उणादिप्रक्रिया.<BR>--6 (In gram.) Etymological<BR>formation.<BR>--7 A privilege.<BR>--8 An<BR>introductory chapter of a work.<BR>--9<BR>Rules for the formation of words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्
प्रकृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To draw away, pull,<BR>attract.<BR>--2 To lead (as an army).<BR>--3 To bend (as a bow).<BR>--4 To<BR>increase.<BR>--5 To draw or stretch out,<BR>prolong.<BR>--6 To place before or in<BR>front.<BR>--7 To harass, disturb, afflict'<BR>trouble. --Pass. To be enhanced or<BR>increased; U. 7. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षः|प्रकर्ष
प्रकर्षः<BR>1 Excellence, eminence,<BR>superiority; वपुःप्रकर्षादजयद्गुरुं रघुः<BR>R. 3. 34; वर्णप्रकर्षे सति Ku. 3. 28.<BR>--2<BR>Intensity, high degree, excess;<BR>प्रकर्षगतेन शोकसंतानेन U. 3.<BR>--3<BR>Strength, power.<BR>--4 Absoluteness.<BR>--5<BR>Length, protraction.<BR>--6 Speciality.<BR>--7 Universality. (प्रकर्षेण and प्रकर्षात्<BR>are used adverbially in the sense of<BR>‘exceedingly’, ‘pre-eminently’, ‘in<BR>a high degree’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षकः|प्रकर्षक
प्रकर्षकः An epithet of the god of<BR>love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षण
प्रकर्षण a. Paining, harassing,<BR>troubling.<BR>--णं<BR>1 The act of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-a" target="_blank">Page0726-a+ 57</a>]<BR>drawing away; attracting.<BR>--2 Ploughing.<BR>--3 Duration, length, extension.<BR>--4<BR>Excellence, superiority.<BR>--5<BR>Distraction.<BR>--6 Realizing by the use of a<BR>pledge more than the interest of<BR>the money lent upon it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0725-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षित
प्रकर्षित a.<BR>1 Drawn out or forth.<BR>--2 Stretched out.<BR>--3 Exceeded in<BR>profit (as the interest of a loan).<BR>--तं Profit on a pledge exceeding<BR>the interest of the money lent upon<BR>it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकर्षिन्
प्रकर्षिन् a. Excellent, pre-eminent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकृष्ट|प्रकृष्टं
प्रकृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Drawn forth or out.<BR>--2 Protracted, long, lengthy.<BR>--3<BR>Superior, distinguished, excellent,<BR>eminent, exalted.<BR>--4 Chief,<BR>principal.<BR>--5 Distracted, disquieted.<BR>--6<BR>Violent, strong, excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॄ
प्रकॄ {c6c} P.<BR>1 To scatter, throw,<BR>pour out; प्रकीर्णः पुष्पाणां<BR>हरिचरणयोरंजलिरयं Ve. 1. 2.<BR>--2 To sow (as<BR>seed).<BR>--3 To issue forth, spring up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकिरणं|प्रकिरण
प्रकिरणं Scattering about, strewing<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्ण|प्रकीर्णं|प्रकीर्णः
प्रकीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Scattered about,<BR>scattered forth, thrown about,<BR>dispersed.<BR>--2 Spread, published,<BR>promulgated.<BR>--3 Waved,<BR>waving; Śi. 12. 17.<BR>--4 Disordered,<BR>loose, dishevelled.<BR>--5 Confused,<BR>incoherent; बह्वपि स्वेच्छया कामं<BR>प्रकीर्णमभिधीयते Śi. 2. 63.<BR>--6 Agitated,<BR>excited.<BR>--7 Miscellaneous, mixed; as the<BR>प्रकार्णिकांड of Bhaṭṭikāvya.<BR>--8<BR>Expanded, opened.<BR>--9 Standing alone.<BR>--र्णं<BR>1 A miscellany, any<BR>miscellaneous collection.<BR>--2 A chapter<BR>containing miscellaneous rules.<BR>--3<BR>A chapter or section of a book.<BR>--4<BR>Scattering or throwing about.<BR>--5<BR>Extent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केशी N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्णक|प्रकीर्णकं|प्रकीर्णकः
प्रकीर्णक a. Scattered or strewn<BR>about &c.<BR>--कः --क<BR>1 A chowrie,<BR>flyflap (चामर); Śi. 12. 17.<BR>--2 A tuft<BR>of hair used as an ornament for<BR>horses.<BR>--कः A horse.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A<BR>miscellany, any collection of<BR>miscellaneous things.<BR>--2 A miscellaneous<BR>chapter.<BR>--3 A section, chapter or<BR>division of a book.<BR>--4 A case not<BR>provided by the Śāstras and to be<BR>decided by the judge or king.<BR>--5<BR>Extent, length (of a book &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॄत्
प्रकॄत् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To announce,<BR>proclaim, mention.<BR>--2 To name, call.<BR>--3 To praise, extol, laud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्तनं|प्रकीर्तन|प्रकीर्त्तन
प्रकीर्तनं<BR>1 Proclaiming,<BR>announcing.<BR>--2 Praising, extolling, lauding.<BR>--ना Mentioning, naming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्तित|प्रकीर्त्तित|प्रकीर्त्तितं
प्रकीर्तित p. p.<BR>1 Proclaimed.<BR>--2<BR>Declared, said to be.<BR>--3 Named,<BR>called.<BR>--4 Celebrated.<BR>--5 Explained.<BR>--6 Revealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकीर्तिः|प्रकीर्ति|प्रकीर्त्ति
प्रकीर्तिः f.<BR>1 Celebration, praise.<BR>--2 Fame, celebrity.<BR>--3 Declaration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॢप्
प्रकॢप् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To be fit or<BR>suitable for.<BR>--2 To happen, occur.<BR>--3 To<BR>be successful. --Caus.<BR>1 To invent,<BR>devise, plan (schemes &c.).<BR>--2 To<BR>prepare, make ready, equip,<BR>accoutre.<BR>--3 To treat with respect.<BR>--4 To fix, settle.<BR>--5 To appoint,<BR>invest, install.<BR>--6 To fix, fasten, bind.<BR>--7 To further, advance, promote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्पना
प्रकल्पना Settlement, fixing,<BR>allotment; Ms. 8. 211.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकल्पित
प्रकल्पित p. p.<BR>1 Made, done,<BR>formed.<BR>--2 Settled, allotted.<BR>--3 Formed<BR>or shed (as a tear).<BR>--ता A kind<BR>of riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकॢप्त
प्रकॢप्त p. p. Prepared, made ready,<BR>arranged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकेत|प्रकेतः
प्रकेत a. Ved. One who knows.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Appearance.<BR>--2 Intelligence,<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोथः|प्रकोथ
प्रकोथः Putrefaction, putridity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोष्ठः|प्रकोष्ठ
प्रकोष्ठः<BR>1 The fore-arm, the part<BR>above the wrist; वामप्रकोष्ठार्पितहेमवेत्रः<BR>Ku. 3. 41; कनकवलयभ्रंशरिक्तप्रकोष्ठः<BR>Me. 2; R. 3. 59; Ś. 6. 6.<BR>--2 The room<BR>near the gate of a palace; Mu. 1.<BR>--3 A<BR>court in a house, a quadrangle or<BR>square (surrounded by buildings);<BR>इमं प्रथमं प्रकोष्ठ प्रविशत्वार्यः &c.<BR>Mk. 4.<BR>--4 A part of a door-frame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रकोष्ठकः|प्रकोष्ठक
प्रकोष्ठकः A room near the gate of<BR>a palace (= प्रकेष्ठ);<BR>तस्थुर्विनम्रक्षितिपालसंकुले तदंगनद्वारबहिःप्रकोष्ठके<BR>Ku. 15. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्खर|प्रक्खरः
प्रक्खर a. Very sharp or violent.<BR>--रः<BR>1 An armour for the defence<BR>of a horse or elephant.<BR>--2 A dog.<BR>--3 A mule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रम्
प्रक्रम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To go forward,<BR>proceed, walk on; Bk. 15. 23.<BR>--2<BR>To go, set out, march forth.<BR>--3 To issue forth, depart.<BR>--4<BR>To go across, pass.<BR>--5 To begin,<BR>commence (Atm.) (with inf.) प्रचक्रमे<BR>च प्रतिवक्तुमुत्तरं R. 3. 47; 2. 15;<BR>Ku. 3. 2; 5. 18.<BR>--6 To undertake, apply<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">Page0726-c+ 56</a>]<BR>oneself to.<BR>--7 To behave towards<BR>(with loc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रंतृ|प्रक्रन्तृ
प्रक्रंतृ a.<BR>1 A beginner.<BR>--2<BR>Conquering, overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रमः|प्रक्रम
प्रक्रमः<BR>1 A step, stride.<BR>--2 A pace<BR>considered as a measure of distance.<BR>--3 Commencement, beginning.<BR>--4<BR>(a) Stepping forward, proceeding.<BR>(b) Procedure, course;<BR>Māl. 5. 24.<BR>--5 The case in question.<BR>--6<BR>Leisure, opportunity.<BR>--7<BR>Regularity, order, method.<BR>--8 Degree,<BR>proportion, measure.<BR>--9 The reading of<BR>the Kramapāṭha.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भंगः<BR>want of symmetry or regularity, the<BR>breaking of arrangement, regarded<BR>as a fault of composition. It is the<BR>same as भग्नप्रक्रमता mentioned in<BR>K. P. 7, the break of symmetry being<BR>either in expression or<BR>construction; नाथे निशाया नियतेर्नियोगादस्तं गते<BR>हंत निशापि याता is an instance of the<BR>former, where गता निशापि would<BR>relieve the irregularity of expression;<BR>and विश्रब्धं क्रियतां वराहततिभिर्मुस्ताक्षतिः<BR>पल्वले is an instance of the latter,<BR>where the symmetry of the verse<BR>requires the active instead of the<BR>passive construction, and the fault may<BR>be removed by reading the line as<BR>विश्रब्धा रचयंतु शूकरवरा मुस्ताक्षतिं पल्वले;<BR>see K. P. 7 under भग्नप्रक्रमता for<BR>further details.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रमणं|प्रक्रमण
प्रक्रमणं<BR>1 Stepping forward,<BR>proceeding.<BR>--2 Issuing.<BR>--3 Beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रांत|प्रक्रान्त|प्रक्रान्तः
प्रक्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Commenced, begun,<BR>--2 Gone, proceeded.<BR>--3 In hand,<BR>under discussion.<BR>--4 Surpassed.<BR>--5<BR>Brave.<BR>--6 Previously mentioned.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The outset of a journey.<BR>--2<BR>The case or point in question.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्रीडः|प्रक्रीड
प्रक्रीडः Play, pastime, sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्लिन्न|प्रक्लिन्नः
प्रक्लिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Moist, humid, wet.<BR>--2 Satisfied (तृप्त).<BR>--3 Moved with<BR>pity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्लेदः|प्रक्लेद
प्रक्लेदः Moistness, wetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्लेदन
प्रक्लेदन a. Moistening, wetting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्वणः|प्रक्वण
प्रक्वणः, प्रक्वाणः The sound of a<BR>lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्वाणः|प्रक्वाण
प्रक्वणः, प्रक्वाणः The sound of a<BR>lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षर|प्रक्षरः
प्रक्षर See प्रक्खर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षरणं|प्रक्षरण
प्रक्षरणं Trickling out, oozing,<BR>flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षल्
प्रक्षल् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To wash, purify,<BR>cleanse; पादौ-मुखं-हस्त &c. प्रक्षालयति.<BR>--2 To wipe away; (अयशः)<BR>तेषामनुग्रहेणाद्य राजन् प्रक्षालयात्मनः Mb.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">Page0727-a+ 55</a>]<BR>To expiate, atone for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0726-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालनं|प्रक्षालन
प्रक्षालनं<BR>1 Washing, washing off;<BR>R. 6. 48.<BR>--2 Cleansing, cleaning,<BR>purifying.<BR>--3 Bathing.<BR>--4 Anything<BR>used for purifying.<BR>--5 Water for<BR>washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षालित|प्रक्षालितः
प्रक्षालित p. p.<BR>1 Washed, cleansed.<BR>--2 Purified.<BR>--3 Expiated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षि
प्रक्षि {c5c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To decay, wane.<BR>--2 To be emaciated or lean.<BR>--3 To<BR>injure, destroy, spoil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षयः|प्रक्षय
प्रक्षयः Ruin, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षीण
प्रक्षीण p. p.<BR>1 Decayed, wasting,<BR>declining.<BR>--2 Destroyed.<BR>--3<BR>Expiated.<BR>--4 Vanished, disappeared.<BR>--णं<BR>The spot where one has perished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्
प्रक्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To throw, fling at,<BR>hurl.<BR>--2 To put into, throw at or<BR>in; नामेध्यं प्रक्षिपेदग्नौ Ms. 4. 53; क्षारं<BR>क्षते प्रक्षिपन् Mk. 5. 18.<BR>--3 To insert,<BR>interpolate; इति सूत्रे कैश्चित्प्रक्षिप्तं<BR>Kaiyaṭa.<BR>--4 To put or lay before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षिप्त
प्रक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Thrown at, cast,<BR>hurled.<BR>--2 Thrown into;<BR>Māl. 5. 22.<BR>--3 Projected.<BR>--4 Interpolated,<BR>spurious; as in प्रक्षिप्तोयं श्लोकः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेपः|प्रक्षेप
प्रक्षेपः<BR>1 Throwing forward,<BR>projecting.<BR>--2 A throw, east.<BR>--3<BR>Scattering upon.<BR>--4 Spurious insertion,<BR>interpolation.<BR>--5 The box of a<BR>carriage.<BR>--6 The sum deposited by each<BR>member of a commercial company.<BR>--7 Anything added to drugs in<BR>decoetion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षेपणं|प्रक्षेपण
प्रक्षेपणं<BR>1 Throwing, casting,<BR>hurling.<BR>--2 Pouring upon, throwing<BR>into.<BR>--3 Settling, fixing (as price<BR>&c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षीवित
प्रक्षीवित a. Drunken,<BR>intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षुद्
प्रक्षुद् {c7c} U. To crush, bruise,<BR>pound; मित्रघ्नस्य प्रचुक्षोद गदयांगं<BR>बिभषिणः Bk. 14. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षुण्ण
प्रक्षुण्ण p. p.<BR>1 Crushed.<BR>--2<BR>Pierced through.<BR>--3 Incited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षुभ्
प्रक्षुभ् {c1c} A., {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be<BR>shaken or agitated.<BR>--2 To totter.<BR>--3 To<BR>be perplexed or confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्षोभणं|प्रक्षोभण
प्रक्षोभणं Exciting, agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेडनः|प्रक्ष्वेडन
प्रक्ष्वेडनः<BR>--ना<BR>1 An iron arrow.<BR>--2<BR>Clamour, hubbub.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रक्ष्वेडित
प्रक्ष्वेडित a. Clamorous, shouting,<BR>noisy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रखर|प्रखरः
प्रखर a.<BR>1 Very hot; as in<BR>प्रखरकिरण.<BR>--2 Very acrid or pungent,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">Page0727-b+ 56</a>]<BR>sharp.<BR>--3 Very hard or rough.<BR>--रः<BR>See प्रक्खर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्या
प्रख्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 To report, announce<BR>declare.<BR>--2 To praise, celebrate,<BR>--Pass. To be well-known or<BR>celebrated, be famous. --Caus. To<BR>celebrate proclaim, announce, declare<BR>publicly, publish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्य|प्रख्यः
प्रख्य a.<BR>1 Clear, visible, distinct.<BR>--2 Looking like, resembling (at the<BR>end of comp.); अमृत˚, शशांक˚ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्या
प्रख्या<BR>1 Perceptibility, visibility<BR>--2 Renown, fame, celebrity;<BR>न्यवसत्परमप्रख्यः संप्रत्येब पुरीमिमां Rām.<BR>--3<BR>Disclosure.<BR>--4 Resemblance,<BR>similitude (in comp.); Y. 3. 10.<BR>--5 Look,<BR>appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यात|प्रख्यातः
प्रख्यात p. p.<BR>1 Famous,<BR>celebrated, renowned, noted.<BR>--2 Forestalled,<BR>claimed by right of pre-emption.<BR>--3<BR>Happy, pleased.<BR>--4 Recognised,<BR>acknowledged.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भांडं a<BR>commodity the pre-emption of which is<BR>claimed by a king.<BR>--वप्तृक a. having<BR>a celebrated father.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यातिः|प्रख्याति
प्रख्यातिः f.<BR>1 Fame, renown,<BR>celebrity.<BR>--2 Praise, eulogium.<BR>--3<BR>Perceptibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यानं|प्रख्यान
प्रख्यानं<BR>1 Reporting.<BR>--2 A report,<BR>information.<BR>--3 Perception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रख्यापनं|प्रख्यापन
प्रख्यापनं<BR>1 Publishing, making<BR>public.<BR>--2 Communicating.<BR>--3<BR>Information.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगंडः|प्रगण्ड|प्रगंड|प्रगण्डः
प्रगंडः The upper part of the arm<BR>from the elbow to the shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगंडी
प्रगंडी The outer wall (of a city).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगम्
प्रगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To advance, proceed.<BR>--2 To set out.<BR>--3 To reach, attain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगत
प्रगत p. p.<BR>1 Gone forth or<BR>forward.<BR>--2 Separate, apart<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जानु, --जानुक a. bandy-legged,<BR>bow-legged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगमः|प्रगम
प्रगमः The first advance in<BR>courtship, first manifestation of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगमनं|प्रगमन
प्रगमनं<BR>1 Advance, progress.<BR>--2<BR>The first advance in courtship; see<BR>प्रगम above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगर्जनं|प्रगर्जन
प्रगर्जनं Roaring, shouting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगल्भ्
प्रगल्भ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To be bold or<BR>confident; या कथंचन सखीवचनेन<BR>प्रागभिप्रियतमं प्रजगल्भे Śi. 1. 18; न<BR>मौक्तिकच्छिद्रकरी शलाका प्रगल्भते कर्मणि<BR>टंकिकायाः Vikr. 1. 16 ‘cannot be bold<BR>(competent) enough to do the work<BR>of a hatchet’.<BR>--2 To be determined or<BR>resolute.<BR>--3 To be proud.<BR>--4 To be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">Page0727-c+ 58</a>]<BR>ready or able (with inf.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगल्भ|प्रगल्भः
प्रगल्भ a.<BR>1 Bold, confident.<BR>--2<BR>Daring, brave, intrepid, spirited,<BR>courageous; R. 2. 41.<BR>--3 Bold in<BR>speech, eloquent; पुंवत्प्रगल्भा<BR>प्रतिहाररक्षी R. 6. 20.<BR>--4 Ready-witted,<BR>prompt.<BR>--5 Resolute, energetic.<BR>--6<BR>Mature (as age); Ku. 1. 51.<BR>--7<BR>Matured, developed, full-grown,<BR>strong; प्रगल्भवाक् Ku. 5. 30 (<BR>प्रौढवाक्); Māl. 9. 29; U. 6. 35.<BR>--8<BR>Skilful; K. 12.<BR>--9 Audacious, arrogant,<BR>officious, proud.<BR>--10 Shameless,<BR>impudent; R. 13. 9.<BR>--11 Illustrious,<BR>eminent.<BR>--ल्भा<BR>1 A bold woman.<BR>--2 A shrew, scolding woman.<BR>--3 A<BR>bold or mature woman, one of the<BR>classes of heroines in poetic<BR>composition; she is versed in all kinds of<BR>caresses, lofty of demeanour,<BR>possessed of no great modesty; of<BR>mature age, and ruling her husband;<BR>see S. D. 101 and examples quoted<BR>ad loc.<BR>--4 An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगल्भता
प्रगल्भता<BR>1 Boldness.<BR>--2<BR>Resoluteness, energy.<BR>--3 Pride,<BR>arrogance.<BR>--4 Eminence.<BR>--5<BR>Perverseness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगल्भित
प्रगल्भित a.<BR>1 Arrogant.<BR>--2<BR>Eminent, illustrious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगाथः|प्रगाथ
प्रगाथः p. p.<BR>1 Dipped into,<BR>soaked, steeped.<BR>--2 Much, excessive,<BR>intense.<BR>--3 Firm, strong.<BR>--4 Hard,<BR>difficult.<BR>--ढं<BR>1 Privation.<BR>--2<BR>Penance, bodily mortification.<BR>--ढं ind.<BR>1 Very much, exceedingly.<BR>--2<BR>Firmly.<BR>--3 Forcibly.<BR>--4 Proportionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगातृ
प्रगातृ m. An excellent singer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगाढ|प्रगाढं
प्रगाढ A strophe, a combination<BR>of two verses (ऋच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगीत
प्रगीत a.<BR>1 Sung.<BR>--2 Singing.<BR>--3 Resonant with singing.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>A song.<BR>--2 A sing-song mode of<BR>reciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगीति
प्रगीति f. A variety of metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुण|प्रगुणः
प्रगुण a.<BR>1 Straight, honest,<BR>upright (lit. and fig.); बहिः<BR>सर्वाकारप्रगुणरमणीयं व्यवहरन् Māl. 1. 14.<BR>--2<BR>Being in the right state or<BR>condition, having excellent qualities;<BR>श्रमजयात्प्रगुणां च करोत्यसौ तनुमतोऽनुमतः<BR>सचिबैर्ययौ R. 9. 49.<BR>--3 (a)<BR>Worthy, suitable, meritorious;<BR>Māl. 1. 16. (b) Efficient; 9. 45.<BR>--4 Skilful,<BR>clever. (प्रगुणीकृ means<BR>1 To make<BR>straight, put in order, arrange.<BR>--2<BR>To make smooth.<BR>--3 To nourish,<BR>bring up).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0727-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुणनं|प्रगुणन
प्रगुणनं Putting straight,<BR>arranging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुणयति
प्रगुणयति Den. P. = प्रगुणीकृ above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुणित
प्रगुणित a.<BR>1 Made even or straight.<BR>--2 Made smooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगुण्य
प्रगुण्य a.<BR>1 More, exceeding.<BR>--2<BR>Excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगे
प्रगे ind. Early in the morning,<BR>at day-break; इत्थं रथाश्वेभानिषादिनां<BR>प्रगे गणो नृपाणामथ तोरणाद्बहिः<BR>Śi. 12. 1; सायं स्नायात्प्रगे तथा Ms. 6. 6;<BR>4. 62.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तन a. to be<BR>performed in the morning.<BR>--निश-शय a. who<BR>is asleep at day-break.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगोपनं|प्रगोपन
प्रगोपनं Protection, preservation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रथनं|प्रग्रथन
प्रग्रथनं Stringing together,<BR>weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रह्
प्रग्रह् {c9c} U.<BR>1 To take, hold, seize,<BR>grasp.<BR>--2 To receive, accept.<BR>--3<BR>To curb, restrain.<BR>--4 To stretch<BR>forth, extend.<BR>--5 To favour, behave<BR>friendly with.<BR>--6 To keep separate<BR>(as the प्रगृह्य vowels).<BR>--7 To offer.<BR>--8 To unite with. --Caus. To<BR>receive, accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगृहीत
प्रगृहीत p. p.<BR>1 Held forth or out.<BR>--2 Received, accepted.<BR>--3 Not<BR>subject to the rules of euphony (संधि);<BR>see प्रगृह्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रगृह्यं|प्रगृह्य
प्रगृह्यं<BR>1 A vowel which is not liable<BR>to the rules of Saṃdhi or euphony<BR>and which is allowed to be written<BR>and pronounced separately;<BR>ईदूदेद्द्बिवचनं प्रगृह्यं P. I. 1. 11 (i. e. the<BR>final ई, ऊ and ए of the dual<BR>terminations of a word or any grammatical<BR>form).<BR>--2 Remembrance.<BR>--3 A<BR>sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रहः|प्रग्रह
प्रग्रहः<BR>1 Holding or stretching<BR>forth, holding out.<BR>--2 Laying hold<BR>of, taking, grasping, seizing.<BR>--3<BR>The commencement of an eclipse.<BR>--4 (a) A rein, bridle; धृताः प्रग्रहाः<BR>अवतरत्वायुष्मान् Ś. 1; Śi. 12. 31.<BR>(b) A whip, lash, scourge.<BR>--5 A<BR>check, restraint.<BR>--6 Binding,<BR>confinement.<BR>--7 A prisoner, captive.<BR>--8<BR>Taming, breaking (as an animal).<BR>--9 A ray of light.<BR>--10 The string<BR>of a balance.<BR>--11 A vowel not<BR>subject to the rules of Saṃdhi or<BR>euphony; see प्रगृह्य.<BR>--12 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--13 The arm.<BR>--14 A leader, guide.<BR>--15 Kindness, favour.<BR>--16 The<BR>Karṇikāra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रहणं|प्रग्रहण
प्रग्रहणं<BR>1 Taking, seizing, grasping.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">Page0728-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 The commencement of an eclipse.<BR>--3 A rein, bridle.<BR>--4 A check,<BR>restraint.<BR>--5 Binding, confining.<BR>--6<BR>Offering.<BR>--7 Guiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्राहः|प्रग्राह
प्रग्राहः<BR>1 Seizing, taking.<BR>--2<BR>Bearing, carrying.<BR>--3 The string of a<BR>balance.<BR>--4 A rein, bridle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रीवः|प्रग्रीव
प्रग्रीवः --वम्<BR>1 A painted turret.<BR>--2 A wooden fence round a<BR>building.<BR>--3 A window.<BR>--4 A stable.<BR>--5<BR>The top of a tree.<BR>--6 A<BR>pleasurehouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रग्रीवम्
प्रग्रीवः --वम्<BR>1 A painted turret.<BR>--2 A wooden fence round a<BR>building.<BR>--3 A window.<BR>--4 A stable.<BR>--5<BR>The top of a tree.<BR>--6 A<BR>pleasurehouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघट्
प्रघट् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To be busy with, be<BR>occupied in; Bk. 21. 17.<BR>--2 To<BR>begin, commence; Bk. 14. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघटकः|प्रघटक
प्रघटकः, प्रघट्टकः A rule, doctrine,<BR>precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघट्टकः|प्रघट्टक
प्रघटकः, प्रघट्टकः A rule, doctrine,<BR>precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघटा
प्रघटा The first elements or<BR>rudiments of a science.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विद्<BR>m. a superficial reader, smatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघणः|प्रघण
प्रघणः(नः), प्रघाणः(नः)<BR>1 A<BR>porch before the door of a house,<BR>portico.<BR>--2 A copper-pot.<BR>--3 An<BR>iron mace, crow-bar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघनः|प्रघन
प्रघणः(नः), प्रघाणः(नः)<BR>1 A<BR>porch before the door of a house,<BR>portico.<BR>--2 A copper-pot.<BR>--3 An<BR>iron mace, crow-bar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघाणः|प्रघाण
प्रघणः(नः), प्रघाणः(नः)<BR>1 A<BR>porch before the door of a house,<BR>portico.<BR>--2 A copper-pot.<BR>--3 An<BR>iron mace, crow-bar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघानः|प्रघान
प्रघणः(नः), प्रघाणः(नः)<BR>1 A<BR>porch before the door of a house,<BR>portico.<BR>--2 A copper-pot.<BR>--3 An<BR>iron mace, crow-bar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघस|प्रघसः
प्रघस a. Voracious, gluttonous.<BR>--सः<BR>1 A demon.<BR>--2 Voracity,<BR>gluttony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघातः|प्रघात
प्रघातः<BR>1 Killing.<BR>--2 A combat,<BR>battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघुणः|प्रघुण
प्रघुणः A guest (v. l. for प्राघुण or<BR>प्राघूर्ण q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघूर्ण|प्रघूर्णः
प्रघूर्ण a.<BR>1 Wandering, roaming.<BR>--2 Turning round.<BR>--र्णः A guest;<BR>see प्राघूर्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रघोषः|प्रघोष
प्रघोषः<BR>1 Sound, noise.<BR>--2 Uproar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचक्रं|प्रचक्र
प्रचक्रं<BR>1 An army in motion.<BR>--2<BR>A foraging army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचक्ष्
प्रचक्ष् {c2c} A.<BR>1 To say, speak, lay<BR>down; स्वजनाश्रु किलातिसंततं दहति<BR>प्रेतमिति प्रचक्षते R. 8. 86.<BR>--2 To tell,<BR>relate.<BR>--3 To consider, regard, deem.<BR>--4 To name, call; योऽस्यात्ममः<BR>कारयिता तं क्षेत्रज्ञं प्रचक्षते Ms. 12. 12;<BR>2. 17; 3. 28; 10. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचक्षस्
प्रचक्षस् m.<BR>1 The planet<BR>Jupiter.<BR>--2 An epithet of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचंड|प्रचण्ड|प्रचण्डः
प्रचंड a.<BR>1 Vehement,<BR>excessively violent, impetuous.<BR>--2 Strong,<BR>powerful, fierce.<BR>--3 Very hot,<BR>stifling (as heat).<BR>--4 Furious,<BR>wrathful.<BR>--5 Bold, confident.<BR>--6 Terrible,<BR>terrific.<BR>--7 Intolerable, unbearable.<BR>--डः A species of oleander.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आतपः fierce heat.<BR>--घोण a.<BR>largenosed.<BR>--सूर्य a. having a hot or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">Page0728-c+ 56</a>]<BR>burning sun; Rs. 1. 1, 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचंडता|प्रचण्डता
प्रचंडता --त्वं<BR>1 Violence,<BR>impetuosity.<BR>--2 Boldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचंडत्वं
प्रचंडता --त्वं<BR>1 Violence,<BR>impetuosity.<BR>--2 Boldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचय|प्रचयः
प्रच(चा)य See under प्रचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचाय|प्रचायः
प्रच(चा)य See under प्रचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचर्
प्रचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To walk about,<BR>stalk forth.<BR>--2 To go or issue forth,<BR>appear.<BR>--3 To roam, wander over.<BR>--4 To reach, arrive at<BR>--5 To spread,<BR>circulate, be prevalent or current.<BR>--6 To prevail (as a custom).<BR>--7 To<BR>undertake, set about (anything),<BR>proceed to work; Ms. 9. 284.<BR>--8<BR>To do, perform.<BR>--9 To behave, act<BR>towards, treat.<BR>--10 To be engaged<BR>in.<BR>--11 To thrive, prosper. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause or allow to roam.<BR>--2 To<BR>turn out to graze.<BR>--3 To make<BR>public.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचरः|प्रचर
प्रचरः<BR>1 A road, path, way.<BR>--2 A<BR>custom, usage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचरणं|प्रचरण
प्रचरणं<BR>1 Going forth, proceeding.<BR>--2 Being current, circulating.<BR>--3<BR>Undertaking, beginning.<BR>--4<BR>Employing, using.<BR>--णी A wooden-ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचरित
प्रचरित p. p.<BR>1 Gone forth &c.<BR>--2<BR>Practised, followed, pursued (as a<BR>profession).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचारः|प्रचार
प्रचारः<BR>1 Going forth, ranging,<BR>walking about, wandering<BR>Ku. 3. 41.<BR>--2 Appearance, coming in,<BR>manifestation; U. 1; Mu. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Currency, prevalence, use, being<BR>used or applied; विलोक्य तैरप्यधुना<BR>प्रचारं Trik.<BR>--4 Conduct, behaviour.<BR>--5 Custom, usage.<BR>--6 A<BR>playground, place of exercise.<BR>--7 A<BR>pasture-ground, pasturage,<BR>Y. 2. 166.<BR>--8 A passage, path;<BR>Ms. 9. 219.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचारित
प्रचारित a.<BR>1 Allowed to wander.<BR>--2 Made public or known, become<BR>current.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचारिन्
प्रचारिन् a.<BR>1 Wandering.<BR>--2<BR>Showing itself, appearing.<BR>--3 Proceeding<BR>with, behaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचल्
प्रचल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To shake, move,<BR>tremble; Bh. 2. 4.<BR>--2 To go, walk,<BR>move on; set out, start off, depart.<BR>--3 To start up, spring up.<BR>--4 To<BR>be affected, disturbed or agitated.<BR>--5<BR>To prevail, be current.<BR>--6 To swerve,<BR>deviate from (abl.). --Caus.<BR>1 (चाल˚)<BR>To shake, stir up.<BR>--2 (चल˚)<BR>To move, set in motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचल|प्रचलः
प्रचल a.<BR>1 Trembling, shaking,<BR>tremulous; Ku. 5. 35; Māl. 1. 38.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">Page0729-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 Current, prevailing, customary.<BR>--3 Going well or widely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0728-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलनं|प्रचलन
प्रचलनं<BR>1 Shaking, trembling.<BR>--2<BR>Retreat, flight.<BR>--3 Circulation,<BR>currency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलित
प्रचलित(प्रचलत्) a.<BR>1 Shaken,<BR>moved, set in motion.<BR>--2 Moving<BR>about; U. 2. 29.<BR>--3 Wandering,<BR>roaming.<BR>--4 Having set out or<BR>proceeded.<BR>--5 Customary, recognized or<BR>received as authority.<BR>--6 Current,<BR>prevalent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलत्
प्रचलित(प्रचलत्) a.<BR>1 Shaken,<BR>moved, set in motion.<BR>--2 Moving<BR>about; U. 2. 29.<BR>--3 Wandering,<BR>roaming.<BR>--4 Having set out or<BR>proceeded.<BR>--5 Customary, recognized or<BR>received as authority.<BR>--6 Current,<BR>prevalent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचालनं|प्रचालन
प्रचालनं Stirring, shaking, a stir;<BR>किं वृथार्थप्रचालनेन Pt. 5 ‘why<BR>discuss this matter in vain.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलाकः|प्रचलाक
प्रचलाकः<BR>1 Archery.<BR>--2 A<BR>peacock's tail.<BR>--3 A snake.<BR>--का Ved.<BR>A violent shower of rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलाकिन्
प्रचलाकिन् m. A peacock;<BR>U. 2. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचलायित|प्रचलायितं
प्रचलायित a. Rolling about,<BR>tossing.<BR>--तं Nodding the head<BR>(while asleep in a sitting<BR>posture).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचालः|प्रचाल
प्रचालः The neck of the Indian<BR>lute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचि
प्रचि {c5c} U.<BR>1 To collect, gather.<BR>--2 To add to, increase, develop; to<BR>enhance, augment.<BR>--3 To cut down.<BR>--Pass.<BR>1 To grow, be developed;<BR>प्रचीयमानावयवा रराज सा R. 3. 7.<BR>--2 To increase, multiply, thrive,<BR>prosper; अपि प्रचीयंते वृद्धिलाभाः<BR>Mu. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचयः|प्रचय
प्रच(चा)यः<BR>1 Collecting,<BR>gathering (as flowers).<BR>--2 A multitude,<BR>quantity, collection, number;<BR>Mv. 2. 15.<BR>--3 Growth, increase.<BR>--4<BR>Slight union.<BR>--5 The neutral<BR>accentless tone (एकश्रुति).<BR>--6 The<BR>common difference of terms in a<BR>progression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचायः|प्रचाय
प्रच(चा)यः<BR>1 Collecting,<BR>gathering (as flowers).<BR>--2 A multitude,<BR>quantity, collection, number;<BR>Mv. 2. 15.<BR>--3 Growth, increase.<BR>--4<BR>Slight union.<BR>--5 The neutral<BR>accentless tone (एकश्रुति).<BR>--6 The<BR>common difference of terms in a<BR>progression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचयनं|प्रचयन
प्रचयनं Collecting, gathering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचायिका
प्रचायिका<BR>1 Gathering(flowers<BR>&c.) in turn.<BR>--2 A female who<BR>gathers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचित
प्रचित p. p.<BR>1 Gathered, collected,<BR>plucked.<BR>--2 Amassed, accumulated.<BR>--3 Covered, filled.<BR>--4 Accentless<BR>(अनुदात्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुद्
प्रचुद् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To impel, prompt,<BR>urge, incite; चापलाय प्रचोदितः<BR>R. 1. 9.<BR>--2 To drive or urge on, push on.<BR>--3 To excite, inspire, encourage,<BR>incite, stimulate.<BR>--4 To enjoin, direct,<BR>prescribe.<BR>--5 To request, ask.<BR>--6<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">Page0729-b+ 56</a>]<BR>To fix, settle, determine.<BR>--7 To<BR>proclaim, announce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदः|प्रचोद
प्रचोदः<BR>1 Driving onward, urging,<BR>inciting.<BR>--2 Instigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदनं|प्रचोदन
प्रचोदनं<BR>1 Driving onward, urging,<BR>inciting.<BR>--2 Instigating, setting on.<BR>--3 Ordering, enjoining, prescribing.<BR>--4 A rule, precept, order,<BR>commandment.<BR>--5 Saying.<BR>--6 Sending,<BR>despatching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदित|प्रचोदितः
प्रचोदित p. p.<BR>1 Urged, incited.<BR>--2<BR>Instigated.<BR>--3 Directed, ordered,<BR>prescribed; Ms. 2. 191.<BR>--4 Sent,<BR>despatched.<BR>--5 Decreed,<BR>determined.<BR>--6 Announced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचोदिन्
प्रचोदिन् a. Driving on, urging &c.<BR>--नी A prickly nightshade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुर|प्रचुरं|प्रचुरः
प्रचुर a.<BR>1 Much, ample,<BR>abundant, plentiful; नित्यव्यया<BR>प्रचुरनित्यधनागमा च Bh. 2. 47; Śi. 12. 72.<BR>--2 Great, large, extensive;<BR>प्रचुरपुरंदरधनुः Gīt. 2.<BR>--3 (At the end of<BR>comp.) Abounding in, filled or<BR>replete with.<BR>--रः A thief.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरुष a. populous.<BR>--(षः) a<BR>thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरता
प्रचुरता --त्वं<BR>1 Abundance, plenty,<BR>copiousness.<BR>--2 Multitude, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरत्वं|प्रचुरत्व
प्रचुरता --त्वं<BR>1 Abundance, plenty,<BR>copiousness.<BR>--2 Multitude, quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरीकरणं|प्रचुरीकरण
प्रचुरीकरणं Adding to,<BR>increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरीकृत
प्रचुरीकृत a. Augmented,<BR>increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचुरीभू
प्रचुरीभू {c1c} P. To become plentiful,<BR>increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेतस्
प्रचेतस् m.<BR>1 An epithet of<BR>Varuṇa; Ku. 2. 21.<BR>--2 N. of an<BR>ancient sage and law-giver,<BR>Ms. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेतृ
प्रचेतृ m. A charioteer,<BR>coachman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेलं|प्रचेल
प्रचेलं Yellow sandal-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रचेलकः|प्रचेलक
प्रचेलकः A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छ्|प्रछ्
प्रच्छ् {c6c} P. (पृच्छति, पप्रच्छ,<BR>अप्राक्षीत्, प्रक्ष्यति, प्रष्टुं, पृष्ट; caus. प्रच्छयति;<BR>pass. पृच्छ्यते; desid. पिप्रच्छिषति)<BR>1 To<BR>ask, question, interrogate, inquire of<BR>(with two acc.); पप्रच्छ रामां<BR>रमणोभिलाषं R. 14. 27; Bk. 6. 8;<BR>R. 3. 5; Bg. 2. 7; ब्राह्मणं कुशलं पृच्छेत्<BR>Ms. 2. 127; so महाश्वेता कादंबरीमनामयं<BR>पप्रच्छ K. 192; कुशलमबले पृच्छति<BR>त्वां वियुक्तः Me. 104; R. 1. 58.<BR>--2<BR>To ascertain, learn by inquiry.<BR>--3<BR>To seek, seek for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छनं|प्रच्छन
प्रच्छनं --ना A question, inquiry,<BR>interrogation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छना
प्रच्छनं --ना A question, inquiry,<BR>interrogation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छद्
प्रच्छद् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To cover, wrap<BR>up, veil, envelope; (वनं)<BR>प्राच्छादयदमेयात्मा नीहारेणेव चंद्रमाः Mb.<BR>--2<BR>To hide, conceal, disguise, keep<BR>secret; प्रच्छादय स्वान् गुणान्<BR>Bh. 2. 77; प्रदानं प्रच्छन्नं 2. 64;<BR>Ms. 4. 198; 10. 40; Ch. P. 4.<BR>--3 To<BR>clothe oneself, put on clothes.<BR>--4<BR>To stand in the way, become an<BR>obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छद्
प्रच्छद् n. Ved.<BR>1 Food.<BR>--2 A cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छदः|प्रच्छद|प्रछद
प्रच्छदः A cover, wrapper,<BR>coverlet, bed-clothes, bed-cover;<BR>R. 19. 22.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पटः bed-clothes,<BR>coverlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छन्न|प्रच्छन्नं
प्रच्छन्न p. p.<BR>1 Covered, wrapped,<BR>enveloped.<BR>--2 Private, secret;<BR>Bh. 2. 64.<BR>--3 Concealed, hidden.<BR>--4<BR>Clothed, clad.<BR>--न्रं<BR>1 A private door.<BR>--2 A loop-hole, lattice, window.<BR>--न्नं<BR>ind. Secretly, covertly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तस्करः an unseen thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादक|प्रच्छादकः
प्रच्छादक a. Concealing, covering<BR>(at the end of comp.).<BR>--कः The<BR>song of a wife deserted by her<BR>husband (containing a covert<BR>description of her sorrows).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादनं|प्रच्छादन
प्रच्छादनं<BR>1 Covering, concealing.<BR>--2 An upper garment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पटः a wrapper, cover, coverlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छादित|प्रच्छादितं
प्रच्छादित p. p.<BR>1 Covered,<BR>enveloped, clothed &c.<BR>--2 Hidden,<BR>concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छर्दनं|प्रच्छर्दन|प्रच्छर्द्दन
प्रच्छर्दनं<BR>1 Vomiting.<BR>--2<BR>Emitting, sending forth.<BR>--3 An emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छर्दिका|प्रच्छर्द्दिका
प्रच्छर्दिका Vomiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छानं|प्रच्छान
प्रच्छानं<BR>1 Scarifying.<BR>--2<BR>Making sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छायं|प्रच्छाय
प्रच्छायं [प्रकृष्टा छाया यत्र] Thick<BR>or dense shade, a shadowy place;<BR>गच्छायसुलभनिद्रा दिवसाः<BR>परिणामरमणीयाः Ś. 1. 3; M. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्छिल
प्रच्छिल a. Dry, waterless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यु
प्रच्यु {c1c} A.<BR>1 To move away, go<BR>away, withdraw, retreat.<BR>--2 To fall<BR>off from, drop down, fall down.<BR>--3<BR>To forsake, abandon (as religion).<BR>--4 To be ejected or driven, be<BR>dislodged, be deprived of, lose (with<BR>abl.).<BR>--5 To flow out, stream forth.<BR>--6 To drive, urge on. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>move, shake.<BR>--2 To displace,<BR>dislodge, eject, expel.<BR>--3 To cause to<BR>fall, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यवः|प्रच्यव
प्रच्यवः<BR>1 Fall, ruin,<BR>--2 Improve<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">Page0730-a+ 57</a>]<BR>ment, advancement, growth.<BR>--3<BR>Withdrawal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0729-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यवनं|प्रच्यवन
प्रच्यवनं<BR>1 Departing, retreating,<BR>withdrawal.<BR>--2 Loss, deprivation.<BR>--3 Oozing, dropping (क्षरण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्यावनं|प्रच्यावन
प्रच्यावनं<BR>1 Causing to give up.<BR>--2<BR>A means of removing, a sedative or<BR>palliative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्युत
प्रच्युत p. p.<BR>1 Fallen off or from.<BR>--2 Strayed, deviated.<BR>--3<BR>Dislodged, displaced, degraded.<BR>--4<BR>Displaced, ejected.<BR>--5 Banished,<BR>expelled.<BR>--6 Routed, put to flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रच्युतिः|प्रच्युति
प्रच्युतिः f.<BR>1 Departing,<BR>withdrawal.<BR>--2 Loss, deprivation, falling<BR>down from; नित्यं प्रच्युतिशंकया<BR>क्षणमपि स्वर्गे न मोदामहे Śānti. 4. 20.<BR>--3<BR>Fall, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजन्
प्रजन् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To be born or<BR>produced, come into existence.<BR>--2 To<BR>grow, arise, spring up.<BR>--3 To bring<BR>forth, be delivered of.<BR>--4 To beget,<BR>generate, produce in general. --Caus.<BR>1 To beget, generate.<BR>--2 To cause,<BR>produce.<BR>--3 To bring forth, bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजः|प्रज
प्रजः A husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनः|प्रजन
प्रजनः<BR>1 Impregnating, begetting,<BR>generating, production; Ms. 3. 61;<BR>9. 61.<BR>--2 The impregnation of<BR>cattle.<BR>--3 Bringing forth, bearing;<BR>Ms. 9. 96.<BR>--4 A generator, progenitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनन|प्रजननं
प्रजनन a. (नी f.) Producing,<BR>generating, procreative.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Procreation,<BR>generation, conception in the womb.<BR>--2 Production, birth, delivery.<BR>--3<BR>Semen.<BR>--4 The male or female<BR>organ of generation (penis or vulva).<BR>--5 Offspring.<BR>--6 Pregnancy of<BR>cattle (उपसर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनिका
प्रजनिका A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनिष्णु
प्रजनिष्णु a.<BR>1 Procreative,<BR>productive.<BR>--2 Growing, standing (as corn).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनुकः|प्रजनुक
प्रजनुकः The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजनूः
प्रजनूः f. The vulva (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजा
प्रजा^1 (Changed to प्रजस् at the<BR>end of a Bah. compound, when the<BR>first member is अ, सु or दुस्; see<BR>R. 8. 32, 18. 29.)<BR>1 Procreation,<BR>generation, propagation, birth,<BR>production.<BR>--2 Offspring, progeny, issue;<BR>children, brood (of animals);<BR>प्रजार्थव्रतकर्शितांगं R. 2. 73; प्रजायै<BR>गृहमेधिनां R. 1. 7; Ms. 3. 42;<BR>Y. 1. 269; so बकस्य प्रजा,<BR>सर्पप्रजा &c.<BR>--3 Posterity, descendants.<BR>--4 A creature.<BR>--5 Subjects, people,<BR>mankind; ननंदुः सप्रजाः प्रजाः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-b" target="_blank">Page0730-b+ 57</a>]<BR>R. 4. 3; प्रजाः प्रजाः स्वा इव तंत्रीयत्वा<BR>Ś. 5. 5 (where प्रजा has sense 2 also);<BR>R. 1. 7; 2. 73; Ms. 1. 8.<BR>--6<BR>Semen.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्यक्षः {1} an<BR>epithet of the sun. {2} of Dakṣa.<BR>--अंतकः Yama, the god of death;<BR>R. 8. 45.<BR>--ईप्सु a. desirous of<BR>progeny.<BR>--ईशः, --ईश्वरः the lord of men,<BR>a king, sovereign; R. 3. 68;<BR>5. 32; 18. 29.<BR>--उत्पत्तिः, f.<BR>--उत्पादनं the<BR>raising up of progeny.<BR>--काम a.<BR>desirous of progeny.<BR>--कारः author<BR>of the creation.<BR>--तंतुः a line<BR>of descendants, lineage, race.<BR>--द a.<BR>{1} granting progeny. {2} removing<BR>barrenness.<BR>--दानं silver.<BR>--द्वारं<BR>N. of the sun.<BR>--नायः {1} an<BR>epithet of Brahmā. {2} a king,<BR>sovereign, prince; R. 2. 48; 10. 83.<BR>--निषेकः impregnation, seed<BR>(implanted in the womb); R. 14. 60. {2}<BR>offspring.<BR>--पः a king.<BR>--पतिः {1} the<BR>god presiding over creation;<BR>Ms. 12. 121. {2} an epithet of Brahmā;<BR>अस्याः सर्गविधौ प्रजपतिरभूच्चंद्रो नु<BR>कांतिप्रदः V. 1. 9. {3} an epithet<BR>of the ten lords of created<BR>beings first created by Brahmā;<BR>(see Ms. 1. 34). {4} an epithet<BR>of Viśvakarman, the architect of<BR>gods. {5} the sun. {6} a king {7}<BR>a son-in-law {8} an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu. {9} a father, progenitor. {10}<BR>the penis. {11} a sacrifice.<BR>--पालः,<BR>पालकः a king, sovereign.<BR>--पालिः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--पाल्यं royal<BR>office<BR>--वृद्धिः f. increase of progeny.<BR>--सृज् m. an epithet of Brahmā;<BR>Śi. 1. 28.<BR>--हित a. beneficial to<BR>children or people.<BR>--(तं) water.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: wrong anusvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजात
प्रजात p. p. Born, produced &c.<BR>--ता A woman who has borne a<BR>child.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजातिः|प्रजाति
प्रजातिः f.<BR>1 Procreation, production,<BR>propagation.<BR>--2 Delivery.<BR>--3<BR>Procreative power.<BR>--4 Travail, labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजायिन्
प्रजायिन् a.<BR>1 Being about to<BR>produce or bring forth.<BR>--2 Bearing,<BR>bringing forth (अभिरूप˚, वीर˚ &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजावत्|प्रजावन्त्
प्रजावत् a.<BR>1 Having subjects or<BR>children.<BR>--2 Pregnant.<BR>--3<BR>Abounding in progeny, prolific.<BR>--ती<BR>1 A<BR>brother's wife (भ्र तृजाया); प्रजावती<BR>दोहदशंसिनी ते R. 14. 45; 15. 13.<BR>--2<BR>A matron, mother.<BR>--3 An elder<BR>brother's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्प्
प्रजल्प् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To speak, say, talk;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">Page0730-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Ku. 1. 45<BR>--2 To call.<BR>--3 To<BR>proclaim.<BR>--4 To prattle, chatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्पः|प्रजल्प
प्रजल्पः Prattle, gossip, heedless<BR>or frivolous words (used in<BR>greeting a lover); असूयेर्ष्यामदयुजा<BR>योवधीरणमुद्रया । प्रियस्य कौशलोद्गारः प्रजल्पः स तु<BR>कथ्यते ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्पनं|प्रजल्पन
प्रजल्पनं<BR>1 Talking, speaking.<BR>--2<BR>Prattle, gossip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजल्पित
प्रजल्पित a. Talked, prattled.<BR>--तं<BR>Talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजविन्
प्रजविन् See under प्रजू.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजागृ
प्रजागृ {c2c} P.<BR>1 To keep watch,<BR>be awake, wake.<BR>--2 To lie in wait<BR>for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजागरः|प्रजागर
प्रजागरः<BR>1 Lying awake at night,<BR>sleeplessness; स राजर्षिरिमानि दिवसानि<BR>प्रजागरकृशो लक्ष्यते Ś. 3;<BR>प्रजागरात्खिलीभूतस्तस्याः स्वप्ने समागमः Ś. 6. 21.<BR>--2 Vigilance, carefulness.<BR>--3 A<BR>guardian.<BR>--4 An epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजिनः|प्रजिन
प्रजिनः Wind, air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजीवनं|प्रजीवन
प्रजीवनं Livelihood, subsistence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजुष्ट
प्रजुष्ट a. Attached or devoted to,<BR>intent on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजू
प्रजू {c1c} U.<BR>1 To push or drive<BR>onward, impel, urge on.<BR>--2 To hasten<BR>forward. --Caus. To shoot, dart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजवः|प्रजव
प्रजवः Ved. Haste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजवन
प्रजवन a. Swift, fleet; U. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रजविन्
प्रजविन् a. Rapid, swift, speedy.<BR>--m. An express, a courier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञा
प्रज्ञा {c9c} U.<BR>1 To know, know<BR>about, be acquainted with.<BR>--2 To<BR>be aware of, find out.<BR>--3 To discern,<BR>distinguish. --Caus. (प्रज्ञपयति)<BR>1<BR>To show, point out (as way).<BR>--2<BR>To discover.<BR>--3 To call, summon,<BR>invite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञ|प्रज्ञः
प्रज्ञ a.<BR>1 Wise, intelligent,<BR>learned.<BR>--2 (At the end of comp.)<BR>conversant with.<BR>--ज्ञः A wise or<BR>learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञप्तिः|प्रज्ञप्ति
प्रज्ञप्तिः f.<BR>1 Agreement,<BR>engagement.<BR>--2 Teaching, informing,<BR>communicating.<BR>--3 A doctrine.<BR>--4<BR>Intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञा
प्रज्ञा<BR>1 Intelligence,<BR>understanding, intellect, wisdom;<BR>आकारसदृशप्रज्ञः प्रज्ञया सदृशागमः R. 1. 15; शस्त्रं<BR>निहंति पुरुषस्य शरीरमेकं प्रज्ञा कुलं च<BR>विभवं च यशश्च हंति ॥ Subhāṣ.<BR>--2<BR>Discernment, discrimination, judgment.<BR>--3 Device or design.<BR>--4 A wise or<BR>learned woman.<BR>--5 N. of the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">Page0731-a+ 55</a>]<BR>goddess Sarasvatī.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चक्षुस्<BR>a. blind; (lit. having<BR>understanding as the only eyes). (--m.) an<BR>epithet of Dhṛtarāṣṭra. (--n.) the<BR>mind's eye, mental eye, the mind;<BR>M. 1.<BR>--वादः a wise saying.<BR>--वृद्ध<BR>a. old in wisdom.<BR>--सहाय a.<BR>intelligent, wise,<BR>--हीन a. void of<BR>wisdom, silly, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0730-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञात
प्रज्ञात p. p.<BR>1 Known,<BR>understood.<BR>--2 Distinguished,<BR>discerned.<BR>--3 Distinct, clear.<BR>--4 Famous,<BR>well-known, renowned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञान|प्रज्ञानं
प्रज्ञान a. Prudent.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Intelligence, knowledge, wisdom.<BR>--2<BR>A mark, token, sign.<BR>--3<BR>Discernment, judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञाल
प्रज्ञाल, प्रज्ञिन् (नी f.), प्रज्ञिल a.<BR>Wise, intelligent, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञिन्
प्रज्ञाल, प्रज्ञिन् (नी f.), प्रज्ञिल a.<BR>Wise, intelligent, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञावत्|प्रज्ञावन्त्
प्रज्ञावत् a. Wise, intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्ञु|प्रज्ञुः
प्रज्ञु a. Bow legged,<BR>bandy-legged; (so प्रज्ञ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वल्
प्रज्वल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To burn brightly,<BR>blaze up, shine; रणांगानि प्रजज्वलुः<BR>Bk. 14. 98.<BR>--2 To catch fire, be in<BR>flames, blaze up.<BR>--3 To be<BR>kindled (as anger), to be incensed or<BR>wrathful. --Caus. (˚ज्व-ज्वा-लयति)<BR>1 To kindle, set on fire.<BR>--2 To<BR>brighten, illumine, irradiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वलनं|प्रज्वलन
प्रज्वलनं<BR>1 Blazing up, flaming,<BR>burning.<BR>--2 Kindling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रज्वलित|प्रज्वलितः
प्रज्वलित p. p.<BR>1 Being in flames,<BR>burning, flaming, blazing.<BR>--2 Bright,<BR>shining.<BR>--3 Burnt.<BR>--तं Burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रडीनं|प्रडीन
प्रडीनं<BR>1 Flying in every<BR>direction.<BR>--2 Flying forward; see under<BR>डीन.<BR>--3 Taking flight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रण|प्रणः
प्रण a. Old, ancient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणखः|प्रणख
प्रणखः The point of a nail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणद्
प्रणद् {c1c} P. To sound, resound,<BR>echo; क्रव्यादाः प्राणदन् घोराः Mb.;<BR>शिवाः प्रणदंति &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणदनं|प्रणदन
प्रणदनं Sounding, a sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणदित
प्रणदित a.<BR>1 Sounding.<BR>--2<BR>Humming, buzzing (as a bee).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणादः|प्रणाद
प्रणादः<BR>1 A loud noise, shout, cry.<BR>--2 Roaring, a roar.<BR>--3 Neighing,<BR>braying.<BR>--4 A murmur of rapture;<BR>a burst of applause; huzza.<BR>--5 A cry<BR>for help.<BR>--6 A particular disease<BR>of the ear (a buzzing sound in the<BR>ear).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणम्
प्रणम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bow down,<BR>salute, make a low obeisance to, be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-b" target="_blank">Page0731-b+ 56</a>]<BR>humble (with acc. or dative); न<BR>प्रणमंति देवताभ्यः K. 108; तां<BR>भक्तिप्रवणेन चेतसा प्रणनाम K. 228; Ku. 7. 27;<BR>Bg. 11. 44; R. 2. 21. (साष्टांगं प्रणम्<BR>‘to fall down on the eight limbs’;<BR>see अष्टांग; दंडवत् प्रणम् ‘to bow by<BR>throwing oneself down on the<BR>ground quite prostrate and flat like<BR>a stick placed horizontally,<BR>touching the ground at all points; cf.<BR>दंडप्रणाम). --Caus. (प्रणमयति) To<BR>cause to bow down; तामर्चिताभ्यः<BR>कुलदेवताभ्यः कुलप्रतिष्ठां प्रणमय्य माता<BR>Ku. 7. 27.<BR>--2 To bend, incline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणत|प्रणतः
प्रणत p. p.<BR>1 Bending, inclined,<BR>stooping.<BR>--2 Bowing to, saluting.<BR>--3 Humble.<BR>--4 Skilful, clever.<BR>--5<BR>Crooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणतिः|प्रणति
प्रणतिः f.<BR>1 A bow, salutation,<BR>obeisance; तव सर्वविधयवर्तिनः प्रणतिं<BR>बिभ्रति के न भूभृतः Śi. 16. 5; R. 4. 88.<BR>--2 Submissiveness, humility,<BR>courtesy; स ददर्श वेतसवनाचरितां<BR>प्रणतिं बलीयसि समृद्धिकरीं Ki. 6. 5;<BR>निर्जितेषु तरसा तरस्विनां शत्रुषु प्रणतिरेव<BR>कीर्तये R. 11. 89.<BR>--3 Inclination,<BR>bending, stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणामः|प्रणाम
प्रणामः<BR>1 Bending, bowing,<BR>stooping.<BR>--2 A reverential salutation,<BR>obeisance, prostration, bow (used<BR>with dat.); as in साष्टांगप्रणाम;<BR>Ku. 6. 91; मूर्ध्ना प्रणामं वृषभध्वजाय चंकार<BR>3. 62; अस्मै प्रणाममकरवम् K. 142.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजलिः a respectful<BR>salutation with the hands folded<BR>together; Ku. 4. 35; for अष्टांग˚ see<BR>अष्टांग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणश्
प्रणश् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To perish, die;<BR>स्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशो बुद्धिनाशात्प्रणश्यति<BR>Bg. 2. 63; Bk. 3. 14.<BR>--2 To vanish,<BR>disappear.<BR>--3 To escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशः|प्रणाश
प्रणाशः<BR>1 Cessation, loss,<BR>disappearance; Ki. 14. 9.<BR>--2 Death,<BR>destruction; भर्तुः प्रणाशादथ शोचंनीयं<BR>R. 14. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशन|प्रणाशनं
प्रणाशन a. Destroying,<BR>annihilating, removing.<BR>--नं Destruction,<BR>annihilation; प्रणाशनाय प्रबलस्य<BR>विद्विषः R. 3. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनष्ट|प्रनष्टः
प्रनष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Disappeared,<BR>vanished, not to be seen.<BR>--2 Lost;<BR>Pt. 4 35.<BR>--3 Perished, dead.<BR>--4 Ruined,<BR>destroyed, annihilated.<BR>--5 Escaped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणवः|प्रणव
प्रणवः<BR>1 The sacred syllable om.;<BR>आसन्मिहीक्षितामाद्यः प्रणवश्छंदसामिव<BR>R. 1. 11; Ms. 2. 74;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">Page0731-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Ku. 2. 12; Bg. 7. 8.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>musical instrument (drum or tabor).<BR>--3 An epithet of Viṣṇu or the<BR>Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणस
प्रणस a. Having a prominent<BR>nose, large-nosed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाडी
प्रणाडी<BR>1 Intervention,<BR>interposition, medium.<BR>--2 Ved. A<BR>watercourse, drain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाय्य|प्रणाय्यः
प्रणाय्य a.<BR>1 Dear, beloved.<BR>--2<BR>Upright, honest, straight-forward.<BR>--3 Disliked, disapproved;<BR>Bk. 6. 66.<BR>--4 Free from passion,<BR>indifferent to worldly attachments<BR>(विरक्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणालः|प्रणाल
प्रणालः --ली, प्रणालिका<BR>1 A<BR>channel, water-course, drain; कुर्वन्<BR>पूर्णा नयनपयसां चक्रवालैः प्रणालीः Ud.<BR>S. {2}; Śi. 3. 44.<BR>--2 Succession,<BR>uninterrupted series.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाली
प्रणालः --ली, प्रणालिका<BR>1 A<BR>channel, water-course, drain; कुर्वन्<BR>पूर्णा नयनपयसां चक्रवालैः प्रणालीः Ud.<BR>S. {2}; Śi. 3. 44.<BR>--2 Succession,<BR>uninterrupted series.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणालिका
प्रणालः --ली, प्रणालिका<BR>1 A<BR>channel, water-course, drain; कुर्वन्<BR>पूर्णा नयनपयसां चक्रवालैः प्रणालीः Ud.<BR>S. {2}; Śi. 3. 44.<BR>--2 Succession,<BR>uninterrupted series.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशः|प्रणाश
प्रणाशः --शनं See under प्रणश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणाशनं|प्रणाशन
प्रणाशः --शनं See under प्रणश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिंसित
प्रणिंसित a. Kissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधा
प्रणिधा {c2c} U.<BR>1 To place, put or<BR>lay down; prostrate; प्रणिहितशिरसं<BR>वा कांतमार्द्रापराधं M. 3. 12;<BR>तस्मात्प्रणम्य प्रणिधाय कायं Bg. 11. 44.<BR>--2 To<BR>set, put in, inlay or incase; यदि<BR>मणिस्त्रपुणि प्रणियीयते Pt. 1. 75. v. l.<BR>--3 To apply, fix upon, direct<BR>towards; भर्तृप्रणिहितेक्षणां R. 15. 84;<BR>Bk. 6. 142.<BR>--4 To stretch out,<BR>extend; मामाकाशप्रणिहितभुजं<BR>निर्दयाश्लेषहेतोः Me. 106; नीबीं प्रति प्रणिहिते तु<BR>करे प्रियेण सख्यः शपामि यदि किंचिदपि<BR>स्मरामि K. P. 4.<BR>--5 To send out (as<BR>spies).<BR>--6 To place or lay in<BR>the front.<BR>--7 To include, enclose.<BR>--8 To employ, use; U. 5. 13.<BR>--9 To resolve.<BR>--10 To think.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधानं|प्रणिधान
प्रणिधानं<BR>1 Applying, employing,<BR>application, use.<BR>--2 Great effort,<BR>energy.<BR>--3 Profound religious<BR>meditation, abstract contemplation;<BR>R. 1. 74; 8. 19; V. 2.<BR>--4<BR>Respectful behaviour towards (with loc.).<BR>--5 Renunciation of the fruit of<BR>actions (कर्मफलत्याग).<BR>--6 Entrance,<BR>access.<BR>--7 (With Buddhists) A<BR>prayer, an entreaty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधिः|प्रणिधि
प्रणिधिः<BR>1 Observing, spying out.<BR>--2 Sending out spies.<BR>--3 A spy, an<BR>emissary; Ku. 3. 6; R. 17. 48;<BR>Ms. 7. 153; 8. 182.<BR>--4 An<BR>attendant, a follower.<BR>--5 Care, attention.<BR>--6 Solicitation, entreaty, request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिधेयं|प्रणिधेय
प्रणिधेयं<BR>1 Sending spies.<BR>--2<BR>Employing, using.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0731-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिहित|प्रणिहितं
प्रणिहित p. p.<BR>1 Laid on, applied.<BR>--2 Deposited.<BR>--3 Outstretched,<BR>stretched forth; Me. 105.<BR>--4<BR>Consigned, delivered, entrusted.<BR>--5<BR>Having the attention fixed upon<BR>one object, with the mind<BR>concentrated, intent.<BR>--6 Determined,<BR>decided.<BR>--7 Cautious, wary.<BR>--8<BR>Obtained, attained.<BR>--9 Spied out.<BR>--10<BR>Acknowledged; admitted.<BR>--11<BR>Applied, directed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिनादः|प्रणिनाद
प्रणिनादः A deep sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपत्
प्रणिपत् {c1c} P. To bow down to, fall<BR>prostrate before, bow respectfully<BR>to, salute (with acc. or dat.);<BR>प्रणिपत्य सुरास्तस्मै शमयित्रे सुरद्विषां<BR>R. 10. 15; वागीशं वाग्भिरर्थ्याभिः<BR>प्रणिपत्योपतस्थिरे Ku. 2. 3; 3. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपतनं|प्रणिपतन
प्रणिपतनं, प्रणिपातः<BR>1 Falling at<BR>one's feet, prostration, submission;<BR>R. 4. 64.<BR>--2 Obeisance, salutation,<BR>reverential bow; Ku. 3. 61,<BR>4. 35; R. 3. 25.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरःसरं,<BR>--पूर्वकं ind. with an obeisance.<BR>--प्रतीकार a. averted or counteracted by<BR>prostration.<BR>--रसः a magical<BR>formula pronounced over weapons.<BR>--शिक्षा teaching (one) to salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणिपातः|प्रणिपात
प्रणिपतनं, प्रणिपातः<BR>1 Falling at<BR>one's feet, prostration, submission;<BR>R. 4. 64.<BR>--2 Obeisance, salutation,<BR>reverential bow; Ku. 3. 61,<BR>4. 35; R. 3. 25.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुरःसरं,<BR>--पूर्वकं ind. with an obeisance.<BR>--प्रतीकार a. averted or counteracted by<BR>prostration.<BR>--रसः a magical<BR>formula pronounced over weapons.<BR>--शिक्षा teaching (one) to salute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणी
प्रणी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To lead out or forth<BR>(as an army), conduct; वानरेंद्रेण<BR>प्रणीतेन (वलेन) Rām.<BR>--2 To offer,<BR>give, present; अर्घ्यं प्रणीय<BR>जनकात्मजा Bk. 5. 76.<BR>--3 To bring to, set<BR>(as fire); Pt. 3. 1.<BR>--4 To<BR>consecrate by reciting sacred Mantras,<BR>hallow, consecrate in general; त्रिधा<BR>प्रणीतो ज्वलनः Hariv.<BR>--5 To inflict<BR>(as punishment); Ms. 7. 20;<BR>8. 238.<BR>--6 To lay down, teach,<BR>promulgate, institute, prescribe; स एव<BR>धर्मो मनुना प्रणीतः R. 14. 67;<BR>भवत्प्रणीतमाचारमामनंति हि साधवः Ku. 6. 31.<BR>--7 To write, compose (as a work);<BR>प्रणीतः न तु प्रकाशितः U. 4; उत्तरं<BR>रामचरितं तत्प्रणीतं प्रयुज्यते U. 1. 3.<BR>--8<BR>To accomplish, effect, perform, bring<BR>about; N. 1. 15, 19; Bh. 3. 82.<BR>--9<BR>To lead or reduce to any condition.<BR>--10 To show, display.<BR>--11 To<BR>direct, fix or turn towards (as the<BR>eyes).<BR>--12 To show affection or<BR>love, love.<BR>--13 To throw, cast,<BR>discharge.<BR>--14 To remove, destroy.<BR>--15<BR>To draw in the breath (Atm.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयः|प्रणय
प्रणयः<BR>1 Espousing, seizing (as<BR>in marriage); Māl. 6. 14.<BR>--2 (a)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-b" target="_blank">Page0732-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Love, affection, fondness,<BR>attachment, liking, regard;<BR>साधारणोयमुभयोः प्रणयः स्मरस्य V. 2. 16;<BR>साधारणोयं प्रणयः Ś. 3; (where in both cases<BR>sense 6 may do as well); Ś. 6. 7; 5. 23;<BR>Me. 105; R. 6. 12; Bh. 2. 42. (b) A<BR>wish, desire, longing; Ku. 5. 85;<BR>Māl. 8. 7; Ś. 7. 16.<BR>--3 Friendly<BR>acquaintance or regard, friendship,<BR>intimacy; Māl. 1. 9.<BR>--4 Familiarity,<BR>confidence, trust; मया गृहीते सलिलेऽ<BR>नेन कृतः प्रणयः Ś. 5.<BR>--5 Favour, kindness,<BR>act of courtesy; अलंकृतोऽस्मि<BR>स्वयंग्राहप्रणयेन भवता Mk. 1; 1. 45.<BR>--6 An<BR>entreaty, request, solicitation;<BR>तद्भतताथानुग नार्हसि त्वं संबंधिनो मे प्रणयं<BR>विहंतु R. 2. 28; V. 4. 13.<BR>--7<BR>Reverence, obeisance.<BR>--8 Final beatitude.<BR>--9 A leader.<BR>--10 Conduct, guidance.<BR>(प्रणयेन confidentially, candidly;<BR>without reserve or ceremony;<BR>प्रणयात् openly, frankly).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपराधः<BR>an offence against friendship or love.<BR>--उन्मुख a. {1} disposed or about to<BR>declare one's love; M. 4. 13. {2}<BR>impatient through love.<BR>--उपेत a.<BR>candid, frank.<BR>--कलहः a lover's<BR>quarrel, a mock or feigned<BR>quarrel;<BR>नाप्यन्यस्मात्प्रणयकलहाद्विप्रयोगोपपत्तिः Me. (considered<BR>spurious by Malli.).<BR>--कुपित a. angry<BR>through love, feigning anger;<BR>Me. 105.<BR>--कोपः feigned anger of a<BR>mistress towards her lover,<BR>coquettish anger.<BR>--प्रकर्षः excessive love,<BR>intense attachment.<BR>--भंगः {1}<BR>breach of friendship. {2}<BR>faithlessness.<BR>--वचनं expression of love.<BR>--विमुख a. {1} averse from love. {2}<BR>disinclined to friendship; Me. 27.<BR>--विहतिः, --विघातः non-compliance,<BR>refusal (of a request &c.).<BR>--स्पृश् a.<BR>inspired by love; Māl. 5. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयनं|प्रणयन
प्रणयनं<BR>1 Bringing, fetching.<BR>--2<BR>Conducting, conveying.<BR>--3<BR>Carrying out, executing, performing;<BR>Ku. 6. 9.<BR>--4 Writing, composing.<BR>--5 Decreeing, sentencing, awarding;<BR>as दंडस्य प्रणयनं.<BR>--6 Bringing<BR>forward, adducing.<BR>--7 Distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयवत्|प्रणयवन्त्
प्रणयवत् a.<BR>1 Loving, fond,<BR>affectionate; R. 10. 57.<BR>--2 Candid,<BR>frank.<BR>--3 Earnestly desirous of,<BR>longing for; जातः सखे<BR>प्रणयवान्मृगतृष्णिकायां Ś. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयिता
प्रणयिता Love, attachment; (श्रीः)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">Page0732-c+ 57</a>]<BR>मूर्खान्द्वेष्टि न गच्छति,<BR>प्रणयितामत्यंतविद्वत्स्वपि Mu. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणयिन्
प्रणयिन् a.<BR>1 Loving, affectionate,<BR>kind, attached; Māl. 3. 9; 6. 30.<BR>--2 Beloved, dearly loved.<BR>--3<BR>Desirous of, longing for, fondly<BR>solicitous of; अंकाश्रयप्रणयिनस्तनयान्वहंतः<BR>Ś. 7. 17; Me. 3; R. 9. 55, 11. 3.<BR>--4<BR>Familiar, intimate. --m.<BR>1 A friend,<BR>companion, favourite; Ku. 5. 11.<BR>--2 A husband, lover.<BR>--3 A<BR>supplicant, humble petitioner, suitor;<BR>स्वार्थात् सतां गुरुतरा प्रणयिक्रियैव<BR>V. 4. 15; 1. 2.<BR>--4 A worshipper; devotee;<BR>Ku. 3. 66.<BR>--नी<BR>1 A mistress,<BR>beloved, wife.<BR>--2 A female friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणायकः|प्रणायक
प्रणायकः<BR>1 A leader or<BR>commander (of an army).<BR>--2 A guide,<BR>head, chief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीत|प्रणीतं|प्रणीतः
प्रणीत p. p.<BR>1 Put forward,<BR>advanced, presented.<BR>--2 Delivered,<BR>given, offered, presented.<BR>--3 Brought<BR>into, reduced to.<BR>--4 Executed,<BR>effected, performed.<BR>--5 Taught,<BR>prescribed.<BR>--6 Cast, sent,<BR>discharged.<BR>--7 Brought to, set.<BR>--8 Written,<BR>composed.<BR>--9 Set aside, removed.<BR>--10<BR>Agreeable or pleasing.<BR>--11 Inflicted<BR>(as punishment); see प्रणी above.<BR>--तः Fire consecrated by prayers.<BR>--ता A sacrificed vessel.<BR>--तं<BR>Anything cooked or dressed, such as a<BR>condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणीतिः|प्रणीति
प्रणीतिः f. Ved.<BR>1 Conduct,<BR>guidance.<BR>--2 Favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणेतृ
प्रणेतृ m.<BR>1 A leader.<BR>--2 A maker,<BR>creator.<BR>--3 The promulgator of a<BR>doctrine, expounder, teacher.<BR>--4 An<BR>author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणेय|प्रणेयः
प्रणेय a.<BR>1 To be guided or led,<BR>tractable, yielding, submissive,<BR>obedient.<BR>--2 To be executed or<BR>accomplished.<BR>--3 To be settled or<BR>fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणु
प्रणु {c2c} {c6c} P.<BR>1 To praise.<BR>--2 To<BR>mutter the sacred syllable om.<BR>--3<BR>To roar, bellow.<BR>--4 To resound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुत|प्रणुतं
प्रणुत p. p. Praised, lauded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुद्
प्रणुद् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To dispel, drive<BR>off, remove; Śi. 9. 71.<BR>--2 To push<BR>or thrust forward, push on.<BR>--3 To<BR>drive, stir, set in motion.<BR>--4 To<BR>scare way, frighten away. --Caus.<BR>1 To prompt, incite, urge forward.<BR>--2 To push away.<BR>--3 To request or<BR>ask any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुत्त
प्रणुत्त p. p.<BR>1 Driven away,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">Page0733-a+ 55</a>]<BR>repelled.<BR>--2 Scared away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0732-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणुन्न
प्रणुन्न p. p.<BR>1 Driven or sent away.<BR>--2 Set in motion.<BR>--3 Scared away.<BR>--4 Shaking, trembling.<BR>--5 Sent,<BR>despatched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणोदः|प्रणोद
प्रणोदः<BR>1 Driving.<BR>--2 Directing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणोदित
प्रणोदित a.<BR>1 Set in motion.<BR>--2<BR>Directed, ordered.<BR>--3 Driven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रणेजनं|प्रणेजन
प्रणेजनं<BR>1 Washing or wiping<BR>away.<BR>--2 Bathing.<BR>--3 Water for<BR>washing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतन्
प्रतन् {c8c} U.<BR>1 To spread abroad,<BR>diffuse; ख्यातस्त्वं विभवैर्यशांसि कवयो<BR>दिक्षु प्रतन्वंति नः Bh. 3. 24.<BR>--2 To<BR>spread, extend, stretch out.<BR>--3 To<BR>spread over, cover, fill.<BR>--4 To<BR>cause, produce, create.<BR>--5 To show,<BR>display, exhibit; तदूरीकृत्य<BR>कृतिभिर्वाचस्पत्यं प्रतायते Śi. 2. 30.<BR>--6 To<BR>perform, do (as a sacrifice).<BR>--7 To<BR>execute, complete, accomplish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतत
प्रतत p. p.<BR>1 Spread over,<BR>covered.<BR>--2 Stretched out, diffused.<BR>--तं<BR>ind. Continuously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रततिः|प्रतति
प्रततिः f.<BR>1 Extension, expansion,<BR>diffusion.<BR>--2 A creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतानः|प्रतान
प्रतानः<BR>1 A shoot, tendril;<BR>लताप्रतानोद्ग्रथितैः स केशैः R. 2. 8;<BR>Ś. 7. 11.<BR>--2 A creeper, low spreading<BR>plant.<BR>--3 Branching out,<BR>ramification.<BR>--4 Tetanus or epilepsy.<BR>--5<BR>Extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतानिन्
प्रतानिन् a.<BR>1 Spreading.<BR>--2<BR>Having shoots or tendrils.<BR>--नी A<BR>spreading creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतन|प्रतनः
प्रतन a. (नी f.) Old, ancient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतनु
प्रतनु a. (नु or न्वी f.)<BR>1 Very thin<BR>or minute, delicate: Me. 29.<BR>--2<BR>Very small, limited, narrow; प्रतनु<BR>तपसां K. 43; U. 1. 20; Me. 41.<BR>--3<BR>Slender, emaciated.<BR>--4<BR>Insignificant, trifling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतप्
प्रतप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To be hot, burn,<BR>glow.<BR>--2 To heat.<BR>--3 To kindle,<BR>illumine.<BR>--4 To bake, roast.<BR>--5 To feel<BR>pain, suffer.<BR>--6 To mortify the<BR>body, undergo penance.<BR>--7 To pain,<BR>distress, torment. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>warm, heat.<BR>--2 To set on fire,<BR>irradiate.<BR>--3 To torment, pain,<BR>distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतपनं|प्रतपन
प्रतपनं Warming, making warm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतप्त
प्रतप्त p. p.<BR>1 Heated.<BR>--2 Hot,<BR>ardent.<BR>--3 Tormented, tortured,<BR>pained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापः|प्रताप
प्रतापः<BR>1 Heat, warmth;<BR>Pt. 1. 107.<BR>--2 Radiance, glowing heat;<BR>Ku. 2. 24.<BR>--3 Splendour, brilliancy.<BR>--4 Dignity, majesty, glory;<BR>Mv. 2. 4.<BR>--5 Courage, valour, heroism;<BR>प्रतापस्तस्य भानोश्च युगपद् व्यानशे दिशः<BR>R. 4. 15 (where प्रताप means ‘heat’<BR>also); 4. 30.<BR>--6 Spirit, vigour,<BR>energy.<BR>--7 Ardour, zeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापन|प्रतापनं|प्रतापनः
प्रतापन a.<BR>1 Warming.<BR>--2<BR>Distressing.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Burning, heating,<BR>warming.<BR>--2 Paining, tormenting,<BR>inflicting punishment.<BR>--नः N. of<BR>a hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापवत्|प्रतापवन्त्
प्रतापवत् a.<BR>1 Glorious, dignified.<BR>--2 Valorous, powerful, mighty.<BR>--m.<BR>1 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--2 Of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतापिन्
प्रतापिन् a.<BR>1 Burning, scorching.<BR>--2 Splendid, brilliant.<BR>--3 Paining,<BR>distressing.<BR>--4 Glorious, dignified.<BR>--5 Powerful, mighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतम्
प्रतम् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To become<BR>exhausted or fatigued, faint.<BR>--2 To lose the<BR>breath, be beside oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतमकः|प्रतमक
प्रतमकः A kind of asthma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्क्
प्रतर्क् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To conclude,<BR>infer, guess.<BR>--2 To reason, reflect.<BR>--3<BR>To think, believe, consider,<BR>suppose; Bk. 2. 9.<BR>--4 To search,<BR>investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्कः|प्रतर्क
प्रतर्कः Conjecture, guess,<BR>supposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतर्कणं|प्रतर्कण
प्रतर्कणं<BR>1 Reasoning, discussion.<BR>--2 Doubt.<BR>--3 Logic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतलं|प्रतल|प्रतलः
प्रतलं One of the seven divisions<BR>of the lower world; see पाताल.<BR>--लः<BR>The open hand with the fingers<BR>extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रति
प्रति ind.<BR>1 As a prefix to verbs<BR>it means (a) towards, in the<BR>direction of; (b) back, in return, again;<BR>(c) in opposition to, against,<BR>counter; (d) upon, down upon; (see<BR>the several roots with this<BR>preposition).<BR>--2 As a prefix to nouns not<BR>directly derived from verbs it means<BR>(a) likeness, resemblance, equality;<BR>(b) opposite, of the opposite side;<BR>प्रतिबल Ve. 3. 5 ‘the opposing<BR>force’; so प्रतिद्विपाः Mu. 2. 13; (c)<BR>rivalry; as in प्रतिचंद्रः ‘a rival moon’;<BR>प्रतिपुरुषः &c.<BR>--3 As a separable<BR>preposition (with acc.) it means (a)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-c" target="_blank">Page0733-c+ 57</a>]<BR>towards, in the direction of, to; तौ<BR>दंपती स्वां प्रति राजधानीं प्रस्थापयामास<BR>वशी वसिष्ठः R. 2. 70; 1. 75; प्रत्यनिलं<BR>विचेरुः Ku. 3. 31; वृक्षं प्रति विद्योतते<BR>विद्युत् Sk.; (b) against, counter, in<BR>opposition to, opposite; तदा<BR>यायाद्रिपुं प्रति Ms. 7. 171; प्रदुद्रुवुस्तं प्रति<BR>राक्षसेंद्रं Rām.; ययावजः प्रत्यरिसैन्यमेव<BR>R. 7. 55; (c) in comparison with, on a<BR>par with, in proportion to, a match<BR>for; त्वं सहस्राणि प्रति Rv. 2. 1. 8; (d)<BR>near, in the vicinity of, by, at, in,<BR>on; समासेदुस्ततो गंगां शृंगवेरपुरं प्रति<BR>Rām.; गंगां प्रति; (e) at the time,<BR>about, during; आदित्यस्योदयं प्रति Mb.;<BR>फाल्गुनं वाथ चैत्रं वा मासौ प्रति<BR>Ms. 7. 182; (f) on the side of, in favour<BR>of, to the lot of; यदत्र मां प्रति स्यात्<BR>Sk.; हरं प्रति हलाहलं (अभवत्) Vop.;<BR>(g) in each, in or at every,<BR>severally (used in a distributive sense);<BR>वर्षं प्रति, प्रतिवर्षं; यज्ञं प्रति Y. 1. 110;<BR>वृक्षं वृक्षं प्रति सिंचति Sk.; (h) with<BR>regard or reference to, in<BR>relation to, regarding,<BR>concerning, about, as to; न हि मे<BR>संशीतिरस्या दिव्यतां प्रति K. 132; चंद्रोपरागं<BR>प्रति तु केनापि विप्रलब्धासि Mu. 1; धर्मं<BR>प्रति Ś. 5. 18; मंदौत्सुक्योस्मि नगरगमनं<BR>प्रति Ś. 1; Ku. 6. 27; 7. 83;<BR>त्वयैकमीशं प्रति साधु भाषितं 5. 81;<BR>Y. 1. 218; R. 6. 12; 10. 29; 12. 51;<BR>(i) according to, in conformity<BR>with; मां प्रति in my opinion; (j)<BR>before, in the presence of; (k) for,<BR>on account of.<BR>--4 As a separable<BR>preposition (with abl.) it means<BR>either (a) a representative of, in<BR>place of, instead of; प्रद्युम्नः<BR>कृष्णात्प्रति Sk., सं ग्रामे यो दारायणतः प्रति<BR>Bk. 8. 89; or (b) in exchange or<BR>return for; तिलेभ्यः प्रति यच्छति माषान्<BR>Sk.; भक्तेः प्रत्यमृतं शंभोः Vop.<BR>--5 As<BR>the first member of Avyayībhāva<BR>compounds it usually means (a)<BR>in or at every; as प्रतिसंवत्सरं ‘every<BR>year’; प्रतिक्षणं, प्रत्यहं &c.; (b)<BR>towards, in the direction of; प्रत्यग्नि<BR>शलभा डयंते.<BR>--6 प्रति is sometimes<BR>used as the last member of Avyayī.<BR>comp. in the sense of ‘a little’;<BR>सूपप्रति, शाकप्रति. (Note. In the<BR>compounds given below all words the<BR>second members of which are words<BR>not immediately connected with<BR>verbs, are included; other words<BR>will be found in their proper places)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0734-a" target="_blank">Page0734-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षरं ind. in every<BR>syllable or letter; प्रत्यक्षरश्लेषमयप्रबंध<BR>Vās.<BR>--आग्नि ind. towards the fire.<BR>--अंगं {1} a secondary or minor limb<BR>(of the body), as the nose. {2} a<BR>division, chapter, section. {3} every<BR>limb. {4} a weapon.<BR>--(गं) ind. {1}<BR>on or at every limb of the body; as<BR>in प्रत्यंगमालिंगितः Gīt. 1. {2} for<BR>every subdivision. {3} in each case<BR>(in grammar).<BR>--अनंतर a. {1} being<BR>in immediate neighbourhood. {2}<BR>standing nearest (as an heir). {3}<BR>immediately following, closely<BR>connected with; जीवेत् क्षत्रियधर्मेण स<BR>ह्यस्य (ब्राह्मणस्य) प्रत्यनं तरः<BR>Ms. 10. 82; 8. 185.<BR>--(रं) ind. {1}<BR>immediately after. {2} next in<BR>succession.<BR>--अनिलं ind. towards or<BR>against the wind.<BR>--अनीक a. {1}<BR>hostile, opposed, inimical. {2}<BR>resisting, opposing.<BR>--(कः) an enemy.<BR>--(कं) {1} hostility, enmity, hostile<BR>attitude or position; न शक्ताः<BR>प्रत्यनीकेषु स्थातुं मम सुरासुराः Rām. {2} a<BR>hostile army; यस्य शूरा महेष्वासाः<BR>प्रत्यनीकगता रणे Mb.; येऽवस्थिताः<BR>प्रत्यनीकेषु योधाः Bg. 11. 32 (प्र˚ may have<BR>here sense 1 also). {3} (in Rhet.) a<BR>figure of speech in which one tries<BR>to injure a person or thing<BR>connected with an enemy, who himself<BR>cannot be injured; प्रतिपक्षमशक्तेन<BR>प्रतिकर्तु तिरस्क्रिया । या तदीयस्य तत्स्तुत्यै<BR>प्रत्यनीकं तदुच्यते K. P. 10.<BR>--अनुमानं<BR>an opposite conclusion.<BR>--अंत a.<BR>contiguous, lying close to, adjacent,<BR>bordering.<BR>--(तः) {1} a border,<BR>frontier; R. 4. 26. {2} a bordering<BR>country; especially, a country<BR>occupied by barbarians or Mlecchas.<BR>˚देशः a bordering country.<BR>˚पर्वतः an adjacent hill; पादाः<BR>प्रत्यंतपर्वताः Ak.<BR>--अपकारः<BR>retaliation, injury in return; शाम्येत्<BR>प्रत्यपकारेण नोपकारेण दुर्जनः<BR>Ku. 2. 40.<BR>--अब्दं ind. every year.<BR>--अमित्र a. hostile.<BR>--(त्रः) an enemy.<BR>--(त्रं) ind. towards an enemy.<BR>--अर्कः a mock sun.<BR>--अवयवं ind.<BR>{1} in every limb. {2} in every<BR>particular, in detail.<BR>--अवर a. {1}<BR>lower, less honoured. {2} very<BR>low or degrading, very<BR>insignificant.<BR>--अश्मन् m. red chalk.<BR>--अहं<BR>ind. every day, daily; day by day;<BR>गिरिशमुपचचार प्रत्यहं सा सुकेशी<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0734-b" target="_blank">Page0734-b+ 58</a>]<BR>Ku. 1. 60.<BR>--आकारः a scabbard, sheath.<BR>--आघातः {1} a counter-stroke. {2}<BR>reaction.<BR>--आचारः suitable<BR>conduct or behaviour.<BR>--आत्मं ind.<BR>singly, severally.<BR>--आत्मक a.<BR>belonging to oneself.<BR>--आत्म्यं<BR>similarity with oneself.<BR>--आदित्यः a<BR>mock sun.<BR>--आरंभः {1}<BR>recommencement, second beginning. {2}<BR>prohibition.<BR>--आशा {1} hope,<BR>expectation; Māl. 9. 8. {2} trust,<BR>confidence.<BR>--उत्तरं a reply,<BR>rejoinder.<BR>--उलूकः {1} a crow. {2}<BR>a bird resembling an owl.<BR>--ऋचं<BR>ind. in each Ṛk.<BR>--एक a. each,<BR>each one, every single one.<BR>--(कं)<BR>ind. {1} one by one, one at a<BR>time, severally; singly, in every<BR>one, to every one; oft. with the<BR>force of an adjective; विवेश<BR>दंडकारण्यं प्रत्येकं च सतां मनः R. 12. 9<BR>‘entered the mind of every good<BR>man’; 12. 3, 7. 34; Ku. 2. 31.<BR>--कंचुकः an adversary.<BR>--कंठं ind.<BR>{1} severally, one by one. {2}<BR>near the throat.<BR>--कश a. not<BR>obeying the whip.<BR>--कायः {1} an effigy,<BR>image, picture, likeness. {2} an<BR>adversary; Ki. 13. 28. {3} a<BR>target, butt, mark.<BR>--कितवः an<BR>opponent in a game.<BR>--कुंजरः a hostile<BR>elephant.<BR>--कूपः a moat, ditch.<BR>--कूल<BR>a. {1} unfavourable, adverse, contrary,<BR>hostile, opposite, प्रतिकूलतामुपगते हि<BR>विधौ विफलत्वमेति बहुसाधनता Śi. 9. 6;<BR>Ku. 3. 24. {2} harsh, discordant,<BR>unpleasant, disagreeable;<BR>अप्यन्नपुष्टा प्रतिकूलशब्दा Ku. 1. 45. {3}<BR>inauspicious. {4} contradictory. {5}<BR>reverse, inverted. {6} perverse, cross,<BR>peevish, stubborn. ˚आचरणं ˚आचरितं<BR>any offensive or hostile action or<BR>conduct; R. 8. 81. ˚उक्तं -क्तिः f.<BR>a contradiction. ˚कारिन्, --कृत,<BR>--चारिन्, --वृंत्ति a. opposing. ˚दर्शन a.<BR>having an inauspicious or<BR>ungracious appearance. ˚प्रवर्तिन्, -वर्तिन् a.<BR>acting adversely, taking an adverse<BR>course. ˚भाषिन् a. opposing,<BR>contradicting. ˚वचनं disagreeable or<BR>unpleasant speech. ˚वादः<BR>contradiction. (प्रतिकूलता, -त्वं adverseness,<BR>opposition, hostility. प्रतिकूलयति<BR>‘to oppose’).<BR>--कूलं ind. {1}<BR>adversely, contrarily. {2} inversely, in<BR>inverted order.<BR>--क्षणं ind. at every<BR>moment or instant; constantly;<BR>Ku. 3. 56.<BR>--गजः a hostile<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0734-c" target="_blank">Page0734-c+ 57</a>]<BR>elephant<BR>--गात्रं ind. in very limb.<BR>--गिरिः {1} an opposite mountain.<BR>{2} an inferior mountain.<BR>--गृहं, --गेहं<BR>ind. in every house.<BR>--ग्रामं ind.<BR>in every village.<BR>--चंद्रः a mock<BR>moon.<BR>--चरणं ind. {1} in every<BR>(Vedic) school or branch. {2} at<BR>every foot-step.<BR>--छाया {1} a reflected<BR>image, reflection, shadow. {2} an<BR>image, picture.<BR>--जंघा the forepart<BR>of the leg.<BR>--जिह्वा, --जिह्विका the<BR>soft palate.<BR>--तंत्रं ind. according to<BR>each Tantra or opinion.<BR>--तंत्रसिद्धांतः a conclusion adopted by one<BR>of the disputants only; (<BR>वादिप्रतिवाद्येकतरमात्राभ्युपगतः).<BR>--इयहं ind. for<BR>three days at a time.<BR>--दंड a. Ved.<BR>disobedient.<BR>--दिनं ind. every day;<BR>Me. 58.<BR>--दिशं ind. in every<BR>direction, all round, everywhere.<BR>--देशं<BR>ind. in every country.<BR>--देहं ind.<BR>in every body.<BR>--दैवतं ind. for every<BR>deity.<BR>--द्वंद्वः {1} an antagonist,<BR>opponent, adversary, rival. {2} an<BR>enemy.<BR>--(द्वं) opposition, hostility.<BR>--द्वंद्बिन् a. {1} hostile, inimical. {2}<BR>adverse (प्रतिकूल); Ki. 16. 29. {3}<BR>rivalling, vying with; Ś. 4. 4. (--m.)<BR>an opponent, adversary, rival;<BR>R. 7. 37.; 15. 25.<BR>--द्वारं ind. at every<BR>gate.<BR>--धुरः a horse harnessed by<BR>the side of another.<BR>--नप्तृ m. a<BR>great-grandson.<BR>--नव a. {1} new,<BR>young, fresh. {2} newly blown or<BR>budded; Me. 36.<BR>--नाडी a<BR>branchvein.<BR>--नायकः the adversary of<BR>the hero of any poetic composition;<BR>as रावण in the Rāmāyaṇa, शिशुपाल<BR>in Māgha Kāvya &c.<BR>--पक्ष a. like,<BR>similar.<BR>--(क्षः) {1} the opposite side,<BR>party or faction, hostility. {2} an<BR>adversary, enemy, foe, rival;<BR>प्रतिपक्षकामिनी ‘a rival wife’; Bv. 2. 64;<BR>Vikr. 1. 70, 73; प्रतिपक्षमशक्तेन<BR>प्रतिकर्तुं K. P. 10; often used in comp.<BR>in the sense of ‘equal’ or<BR>‘similar’. {3} a defendant or<BR>respondent (in law). ˚ता {1} hostility,<BR>opposition. {2} obstacle.<BR>--पक्षित a.<BR>{1} containing a contradiction. {2}<BR>nullified by a contradictory premiss;<BR>(as a hetu in न्याय); cf. सत्प्रतिपक्ष.<BR>--पक्षिन् m. an opponent, adversary.<BR>--पथं ind. along the road, towards<BR>the way;<BR>प्रतिपथगतिरासीद्वेगदीर्घीकृतांगः Ku. 3. 76.<BR>--पदं ind. {1} at<BR>every stop. {2} at every place,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-a" target="_blank">Page0735-a+ 57</a>]<BR>everywhere. {3} expressly. {4} in<BR>every word.<BR>--पाणः {1} a stake. {2}<BR>a counter-pledge. {3} a counter-stake.<BR>--पादं ind. in each quarter.<BR>--पात्रं<BR>ind. with regard to each part, of<BR>each character; प्रतिपात्रमाधीयतां यत्नः<BR>Ś. 1 ‘let care be taken of each<BR>character’.<BR>--पादपं ind. in every<BR>tree.<BR>--पाप a. returning sin for sin,<BR>requiting evil for evil.<BR>--पु(पू)रुषः<BR>{1} a like or similar man. {2} a<BR>substitute, deputy. {3} a companion.<BR>{4} the effigy of a man pushed by<BR>thieves into the interior of a house<BR>before entering it themselves (to<BR>ascertain if any body is awake).<BR>{5} an effigy in general.<BR>--(बं) ind.<BR>man by man, for each man.<BR>--पुस्तकं a copy of an original manuscript.<BR>--पूर्वाह्णं ind. every forenoon.<BR>--प्रभातं ind. every morning.<BR>--प्राकारः an<BR>outer wall or rampart.<BR>--प्रियं a<BR>kindness or service in return;<BR>R. 5. 56.<BR>--बंधुः an equal in rank or<BR>station.<BR>--बल a. {1} able, powerful.<BR>{2} equal in strength, equally<BR>matched or powerful.<BR>--(लं) {1} a<BR>hostile army;<BR>अस्त्रज्वालाबलीढप्रतिबलजलधेरंतरौर्वायमाणे Ve. 3. 5. {2}<BR>strength.<BR>--बाहुः the forepart of the<BR>arm.<BR>--बिं(बिं)बः --बं {1} a reflection,<BR>reflected image; Ku. 6. 42;<BR>Śi. 9. 18. {2} an image, a picture.<BR>--बीजं<BR>a rotten seed.<BR>--भट a. vying with,<BR>rivalling; घटप्रतिभटस्तनि N. 13. 5.<BR>--(टः) {1} a rival, an opponent. {2}<BR>a warrior on the opposite side;<BR>सप्तालोक्याजौ त्वां विदधति विकल्पान्<BR>प्रतिभटाः K. P. 10.<BR>--भय a. {1} fearful,<BR>formidable, terrible, frightful. {2}<BR>dangerous; Pt. 2. 166.<BR>--(यं) a<BR>danger.<BR>--मंडलं {1} a secondary disc<BR>(of the sun &c.). {2} an eccentric<BR>orbit.<BR>--मंदिरं ind. in every house.<BR>--मल्लः an antagonist, a rival;<BR>N. 1. 63; पातालप्रतिमल्लगल्ल &c.<BR>Māl. 5. 22.<BR>--माया a counter-spell or charm.<BR>--मार्गं ind. back, backwards.<BR>--माला<BR>capping verses (Mar. भंडी).<BR>--मासं<BR>ind. every month, monthly.<BR>--मित्रं<BR>an enemy, adversary.<BR>--मुख a. {1}<BR>standing before the face, facing;<BR>प्रतिमुखागत Ms. 8. 291. {2} near,<BR>present.<BR>--(खं) a secondary plot or<BR>incident in a drama which tends<BR>either to hasten or retard the<BR>catastrophe; see S. D. 334 and 351-64<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-b" target="_blank">Page0735-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--(खं) ind. {1} towards. {2} in<BR>front, before.<BR>--मुद्रा a counter-seal.<BR>--मुहूर्तं ind. every moment.<BR>--मूर्तिः f.<BR>an image, a likeness.<BR>--यूथपः the<BR>leader of a hostile herd of elephants.<BR>--रथः an adversary in war (lit. in<BR>fighting in a war-chariot);<BR>दौष्यंतिमप्रतिरथं तनयं निवेश्य Ś. 4. 19.<BR>--राजः<BR>a hostile king.<BR>--रात्रं ind. every<BR>night.<BR>--रूप a. {1} corresponding,<BR>similar, having a counter-part in. {2}<BR>beautiful. {3} suitable, proper.<BR>--(पं)<BR>a picture, an image, a likeness.<BR>--रुपक a. resembling, similar (at<BR>the end of comp.); चेष्टाप्रतिरूपिका<BR>मनोवृत्तिः Ś. 1.<BR>--(कं) {1} a<BR>picture, an image. {2} a forged edict.<BR>{3} a reflection.<BR>--लक्षणं a mark,<BR>sign, token.<BR>--लिपिः f. a transcript,<BR>a written copy.<BR>--लोम a. {1}<BR>‘against the hair or grain’,<BR>contrary to the natural order, inverted,<BR>reverse (opp. अनुलोम). {2} contrary<BR>to easte (said of the issue of a<BR>woman who is of a higher caste than<BR>her husband). {3} hostile. {4} low,<BR>vile, base. {5} left (वाम). {6}<BR>obstinate, perverse; अपरिचितस्वापि<BR>तेऽप्रतिलोमः संवृत्तः Ś. 7. {7}<BR>disagreeable, unpleasant.<BR>--(मं) any<BR>injurious or unpleasant act.<BR>--(मं) ind.<BR>‘against the hair or grain’,<BR>inversely, invertedly. ˚ज a. born in the<BR>inverse order of the eastes; i. e.<BR>born of a mother who is of a higher<BR>caste than the father; cf. Ms. 10. 16,<BR>25.<BR>--लोमक a. reverse, inverted.<BR>--(कं)<BR>inverted order.<BR>--वत्सरं ind. every<BR>year.<BR>--वनं ind. in every forest.<BR>--वर्णिक a. similar, corresponding.<BR>--वर्धिन् a. being a match for.<BR>--वर्षं<BR>ind. every year.<BR>--वस्तु n. {1} an<BR>equivalent, a counter-part. {2}<BR>anything given in return. {3} a<BR>parallel. ˚उपमा a figure of speech thus<BR>defined by Mammaṭa:<BR>--प्रतिवस्तूपमा<BR>तु सा ॥ सामान्यस्य द्विरेकस्य यत्र वाक्यद्वये<BR>स्थितिः K. P. 10; e. g. तापेन भ्राजते<BR>सूर्यः शूरश्चापेन राजते Chandr. 5. 48.<BR>--बातः a contrary wind.<BR>--(तं) ind.<BR>against the wind; चीनांशुकमिव केतोः<BR>प्रतिवातं नीयमानस्य Ś. 1. 34.<BR>--वारणः<BR>a hostile elephant.<BR>--वासरं ind.<BR>every day.<BR>--विटपं ind. {1} on every<BR>branch. {2} branch by branch.<BR>--वेदं<BR>ind. in or for every Veda.<BR>--विषं an<BR>antidote.<BR>--(षा) a birch tree.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">Page0735-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--विष्णुकः a Mucukunda tree.<BR>--वीरः<BR>an opponent, antagonist.<BR>--वीर्यं<BR>being equal to or a match for.<BR>--वृषः<BR>a hostile bull.<BR>--वेलं ind. at each<BR>time, on every occasion.<BR>--वेशः {1} a<BR>neighbouring house, neighbourhood.<BR>{2} a neighbour.<BR>--वेशिन् a. a<BR>neighbour.<BR>--वेश्मन् n. a neighbour's house.<BR>--वेश्यः a neighbour.<BR>--वैरं requital<BR>of hostilities, revenge.<BR>--शब्दः {1}<BR>echo, reverberation;<BR>वसुधाधरकंदराभिसर्पी प्रतिशब्दोऽपि हरेर्भिनत्ति नागान्<BR>V. 1. 16; Ku. 6. 64; R. 2. 28. {2}<BR>a roar.<BR>--शशिन् m. a mock-moon.<BR>--शाखं ind. for every branch or<BR>school (of the Veda).<BR>--शाखा a<BR>side-branch.<BR>--संवत्सरं ind. every<BR>year.<BR>--सम a. equal to, a match for.<BR>--सव्य a. in an inverted order.<BR>--सामंतः an enemy.<BR>--सायं ind.<BR>every evening.<BR>--सूर्यः, --सूर्यकः {1} a<BR>mock-sun. {2} a lizard, chameleon;<BR>U. 2. 16.<BR>--सेना a hostile army.<BR>--स्थानं ind. in every place,<BR>everywhere.<BR>--स्रोतस् ind. against the<BR>stream.<BR>--हस्तः, --हस्तकः a deputy,<BR>an agent, substitute, proxy;<BR>आश्रितानां भृतौ स्वामिसेवायां धर्मसेवने ।<BR>पुत्रस्योत्पादने चैव न संति प्रति हस्तकाः H. 2. 33<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0733-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक|प्रतिकः
प्रतिक a. Worth or bought for<BR>a Kārṣāpaṇa, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकर्षः|प्रतिकर्ष
प्रतिकर्षः<BR>1 Aggregation,<BR>drawing together.<BR>--2 Anticipation (of a<BR>word) occurring later on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकषः|प्रतिकष
प्रतिकषः<BR>1 A leader.<BR>--2 An<BR>assistant.<BR>--3 A messenger (बार्ताहर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकाशः|प्रतिकाश
प्रति(ती)काशः<BR>1 A reflection.<BR>--2 Look, appearance, resemblance;<BR>oft. at the end of comp. in this<BR>sense and translated by ‘like’,<BR>‘resembling’; पुटपाकप्रतीकाशः U. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकाशः|प्रतीकाश
प्रति(ती)काशः<BR>1 A reflection.<BR>--2 Look, appearance, resemblance;<BR>oft. at the end of comp. in this<BR>sense and translated by ‘like’,<BR>‘resembling’; पुटपाकप्रतीकाशः U. 3. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकुंचित|प्रतिकुञ्चित
प्रतिकुंचित a. Bent, curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृ
प्रतिकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To requite, pay<BR>back, repay, return; पूर्वं कृतार्थो<BR>मित्राणां नार्यं प्रतिकरोति यः Rām.<BR>--2 To<BR>remedy, cure; व्याधिमिच्छानि ते ज्ञातुं<BR>प्रतिकुर्यां हि तत्र वै Mb.<BR>--3 To give<BR>back, restore, replace; Ms. 9. 225.<BR>--4 To retaliate; R. 12. 94.<BR>--5 To<BR>counteract.<BR>--6 To repair, mend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकरः|प्रतिकर
प्रतिकरः Requital, compensation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकर्तव्य
प्रतिकर्तव्य, --कार्य a.<BR>1 To be<BR>retaliated, returned or paid (as a debt.<BR>&c.).<BR>--2 To be counteracted.<BR>--3 To be<BR>cured or treated (by a physician).<BR>--र्यं Retribution, retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकार्य
प्रतिकर्तव्य, --कार्य a.<BR>1 To be<BR>retaliated, returned or paid (as a debt.<BR>&c.).<BR>--2 To be counteracted.<BR>--3 To be<BR>cured or treated (by a physician).<BR>--र्यं Retribution, retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0735-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकर्तृ
प्रतिकर्तृ a. (र्त्री f.) Requiting,<BR>recompensing. --m. An opponent,<BR>adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकर्मन्|प्रतिकर्म्मन्
प्रतिकर्मन् n.<BR>1 Requital,<BR>retaliation.<BR>--2 Redress, remedy,<BR>counteraction.<BR>--3 Personal decoration,<BR>dress, toilet; (अबलाः) प्रतिकर्म<BR>कर्तुमुपचक्रमिरे समये हि सर्वमुपकारि कृतं<BR>Śi. 9. 43; 5. 27; Ku. 7. 6.<BR>--4<BR>Opposition, hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकारः|प्रतिकार
प्रति(ती)कारः<BR>1 Requital, reward,<BR>return.<BR>--2 Revenge, retaliation,<BR>retribution.<BR>--3 Counter-action,<BR>obviating, prevention, remedy,<BR>application of a remedy; विकारं खंलु<BR>परमार्थतोऽज्ञात्वाऽनारंभः प्रतीकारस्य Ś. 3;<BR>प्रतीकारो व्याधेः सुखमिति विपर्यस्यति<BR>जनः Bh. 3. 92.<BR>--4 Opposition,<BR>obstruction.<BR>--5 Help.<BR>--6 A kind of<BR>treaty where one party requites the<BR>services of the other.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. making reparation or amends.<BR>--विधानं application of a remedy,<BR>medical treatment;<BR>प्रतिकारविधानमायुषः सति शेषे हि फलाय कल्पते<BR>R. 8. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकारः|प्रतीकार
प्रति(ती)कारः<BR>1 Requital, reward,<BR>return.<BR>--2 Revenge, retaliation,<BR>retribution.<BR>--3 Counter-action,<BR>obviating, prevention, remedy,<BR>application of a remedy; विकारं खंलु<BR>परमार्थतोऽज्ञात्वाऽनारंभः प्रतीकारस्य Ś. 3;<BR>प्रतीकारो व्याधेः सुखमिति विपर्यस्यति<BR>जनः Bh. 3. 92.<BR>--4 Opposition,<BR>obstruction.<BR>--5 Help.<BR>--6 A kind of<BR>treaty where one party requites the<BR>services of the other.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. making reparation or amends.<BR>--विधानं application of a remedy,<BR>medical treatment;<BR>प्रतिकारविधानमायुषः सति शेषे हि फलाय कल्पते<BR>R. 8. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकारिन्
प्रतिकारिन् a.<BR>1 Retaliating,<BR>opposing, counteracting.<BR>--2 Applying or<BR>using remedies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृत
प्रतिकृत p. p.<BR>1 Returned, repaid,<BR>requited, retaliated.<BR>--2<BR>Counteracted, remedied.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Recompense.<BR>--2 Opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृतिः|प्रतिकृति
प्रतिकृतिः f.<BR>1 Revenge,<BR>retaliation.<BR>--2 Return, requital.<BR>--3 A<BR>reflection, reflected image.<BR>--4 A<BR>likeness, picture, statue, an image;<BR>R. 8. 92; 14. 87; 18. 53.<BR>--5 A<BR>substitute.<BR>--6 Resistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रिया
प्रतिक्रिया<BR>1 Recompense, requital<BR>--2 Retaliation, revenge, retribution.<BR>--3 Counteracting, remedying,<BR>removal; अहेतुः पक्षपातो यस्तस्य नास्ति<BR>प्रतिक्रिया U. 5. 17; R. 15. 4.<BR>--4<BR>Opposition.<BR>--5 Personal decoration,<BR>embellishment, dress.<BR>--6<BR>Protection.<BR>--7 Help, succour.<BR>--8 A fence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकृष्ट|प्रतिकृष्टं
प्रतिकृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Twice ploughed.<BR>--2<BR>Repulsed, despised, rejected.<BR>--3<BR>Hidden, concealed.<BR>--4 Low, vile, abject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिकोपः|प्रतिकोप
प्रतिकोपः, प्रतिक्रोधः Anger against<BR>any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रोधः|प्रतिक्रोध
प्रतिकोपः, प्रतिक्रोधः Anger against<BR>any one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रमः|प्रतिक्रम
प्रतिक्रमः Inverted order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रमणं|प्रतिक्रमण
प्रतिक्रमणं Ved.<BR>1 Stepping towards.<BR>--2 (With Buddhists) A confession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्रुष्ट
प्रतिक्रुष्ट a. Miserable, poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षयः|प्रतिक्षय
प्रतिक्षयः A guard, an attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षिप्
प्रतिक्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To throw or cast<BR>into.<BR>--2 To hurt, injure.<BR>--3 To<BR>revile, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षिप्त|प्रतिक्षिप्तः
प्रतिक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Turned away,<BR>rejected, dismissed.<BR>--2 Repelled,<BR>resisted, repulsed, opposed.<BR>--3<BR>Abused, reviled, traduced.<BR>--4 Sent,<BR>despatched.<BR>--5 Hurt, injured.<BR>--6<BR>Despised, slighted.<BR>--7 Falsely accused.<BR>--प्तं Medicine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षेपः|प्रतिक्षेप
प्रतिक्षेपः, प्रतिक्षेपणं<BR>1 Not<BR>acknowledging, rejection.<BR>--2 Opposing,<BR>controverting, contradiction.<BR>--3<BR>Contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षेपणं|प्रतिक्षेपण
प्रतिक्षेपः, प्रतिक्षेपणं<BR>1 Not<BR>acknowledging, rejection.<BR>--2 Opposing,<BR>controverting, contradiction.<BR>--3<BR>Contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिक्षुतं|प्रतिक्षुत
प्रतिक्षुतं Sneezing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिख्यातिः|प्रतिख्याति
प्रतिख्यातिः f. Renown, fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगम्
प्रतिगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go towards,<BR>advance.<BR>--2 To return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगत|प्रतिगतं
प्रतिगत p. p. Flying backward<BR>and forward, wheeling about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगमनं|प्रतिगमन
प्रतिगमनं Returning, going back,<BR>return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगर्हित
प्रतिगर्हित p. p. Blamed, reviled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगर्ज्
प्रतिगर्ज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To roar at, to<BR>roar against.<BR>--2 (fig.) To resist,<BR>oppose; अयोहृदयः प्रतिगर्जतां R. 9. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगर्जना
प्रतिगर्जना Roaring against,<BR>answering roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रह्
प्रतिग्रह् {c9c} U.<BR>1 To hold, seize,<BR>take, support; वर्षधरप्रतिगृहीतमेनं<BR>M. 4; Ms. 2. 48.<BR>--2 To take, accept,<BR>receive; ददाति प्रतिगृह्णाति Pt. 2;<BR>अमोघाः प्रतिगृह्णंतावर्ध्यानुपदमाशिषः<BR>R. 1. 44; 2. 22.<BR>--3 To receive or accept<BR>as a present.<BR>--4 To receive<BR>inimically, oppose, encounter, resist; to<BR>attack, assault; प्रतिजग्राह<BR>कालिंगस्तमस्त्रैर्गजसाधनः R. 4. 40; 12. 47.<BR>--5<BR>To take in marriage, marry;<BR>Ms. 9. 72.<BR>--6 To obey, conform or listen<BR>to.<BR>--7 To resort to, betake oneself<BR>to.<BR>--8 To eclipse.<BR>--9 To assent to,<BR>admit.<BR>--10 To occupy, take<BR>possession of.<BR>--11 To deprive (one) of.<BR>--12 To welcome, receive.<BR>--13 To eat,<BR>drink. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to accept,<BR>give, present.<BR>--2 To allow to take<BR>or retain; मुष्टं प्रतिग्राहयता स्वमर्थं<BR>पात्रीकृतो दस्युरिवासि येन Ś. 5. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिगृहीत
प्रतिगृहीत p. p.<BR>1 Taken, received,<BR>accepted; त्वमवया पुत्र इति प्रतिगृहतिः<BR>Ś. 2; प्रतिगृहीतं ब्राह्मणवचनं V. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Admitted, assented to.<BR>--3 Married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रहः|प्रतिग्रह
प्रतिग्रहः<BR>1 Receiving, accepting.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">Page0736-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 Receiving or accepting a<BR>donation.<BR>--3 The right of receiving or<BR>accepting a donation.<BR>--4 The right<BR>of receiving gifts (which is a<BR>peculiar prerogative of Brāhmaṇas);<BR>Ms. 1. 88; 4. 86; Y. 1. 118.<BR>--5 A<BR>gift, present, donation; राज्ञः<BR>प्रतिग्रहोऽयं Ś. 1; Śi. 14. 35.<BR>--6 A<BR>receiver (of a gift).<BR>--7 Kind<BR>or friendly reception.<BR>--8<BR>Favour, grace.<BR>--9 Marrying.<BR>--10<BR>Listening to.<BR>--11 The rear of an army.<BR>--12 A spitting-pot.<BR>--13 The sun<BR>near the moon's node.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रहणं|प्रतिग्रहण
प्रतिग्रहणं<BR>1 Receiving presents.<BR>--2 Reception.<BR>--3 Marrying.<BR>--4 A<BR>vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रहिन्
प्रतिग्रहिन् m. A receiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्रहीतृ
प्रतिग्रहीतृ m.<BR>1 A receiver.<BR>--2 A<BR>husband, one who marries.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्राहः|प्रतिग्राह
प्रतिग्राहः<BR>1 Accepting gifts.<BR>--2 A<BR>spitting-pot, spittoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्राहक
प्रतिग्राहक --हिन् a. One who receives<BR>or accepts gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्राहिन्
प्रतिग्राहक --हिन् a. One who receives<BR>or accepts gifts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिग्राह्य
प्रतिग्राह्य a. Acceptable, admissible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघ|प्रतिघः
प्रतिघ a. Hostile, adverse.<BR>--घः<BR>1 Opposition, resistance.<BR>--2<BR>Fighting, combat, mutual beating.<BR>--3<BR>Anger, wrath.<BR>--4 Fainting.<BR>--5 An<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघातः|प्रतिघात
प्रति(ती)घातः<BR>1 Warding off,<BR>repulse.<BR>--2 Opposition, resistance.<BR>--3 A counterblow, blow in return.<BR>--4 Rebound, reaction; Ku. 2. 49.<BR>--5 Prohibiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीघातः|प्रतीघात
प्रति(ती)घातः<BR>1 Warding off,<BR>repulse.<BR>--2 Opposition, resistance.<BR>--3 A counterblow, blow in return.<BR>--4 Rebound, reaction; Ku. 2. 49.<BR>--5 Prohibiting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिघातक
प्रतिघातक, --घातिन् a.<BR>1 Hostile,<BR>inimical, opposed to.<BR>--2 Interrupting,<BR>obstructing; U. 5. 29. v. l.<BR>--3<BR>Repelling, warding off.<BR>--4<BR>Encroaching upon, disturbing.<BR>--5 Reacting.<BR>--6 Dazzling; Ku. 5. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0736-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

