प्रतिजागरणं|प्रतिजागरण
प्रतिजागरणं Watching, guarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिजीवनं|प्रतिजीवन
प्रतिजीवनं Resuscitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञा
प्रतिज्ञा {c9c} A.<BR>1 To promise, declare<BR>solemnly, engage, agree, vow;<BR>हरचापारोपणेन कन्यादानं प्रति जानीते<BR>P. R. 4.<BR>--2 To state, affirm, assert,<BR>maintain, allege.<BR>--3 To bring forward or<BR>introduce, adduce.<BR>--4 To admit,<BR>own, acknowledge.<BR>--5 To confirm.<BR>--6 To approve, consent.<BR>--7 To<BR>observe, learn, discern.<BR>--8 To<BR>propose.<BR>--9 To remember with regret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञा
प्रतिज्ञा<BR>1 Admission,<BR>acknowledgment.<BR>--2 A vow, promise,<BR>engagement, solemn declaration;<BR>दैवात्तीर्णप्रतिज्ञः Mu. 4. 12; तीर्त्वा जवेनैव<BR>नितांतदुस्तरां नदीं प्रतिज्ञामिब तां गरीयसीं<BR>Śi. 12. 74.<BR>--3 A statement, assertion,<BR>declaration, affirmation.<BR>--4 (In Nyāya<BR>phil.) A proposition, statement of<BR>the proposition to be proved,<BR>the first member of the<BR>fivemembered Indian syllogism; see<BR>under न्याय; (पर्वतो वह्निमान् is the<BR>usual instance).<BR>--5 A plaint, an<BR>indictment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरं (in<BR>logic) a subsequent proposition on<BR>failure of the first.<BR>--पत्रं, --पत्रकं a<BR>bond, written contract or<BR>document.<BR>--भंगः breach of promise.<BR>--बिरोधः {1} breaking an agreement,<BR>acting contrary to promise. {2}<BR>denial of a logical proposition.<BR>--विवाहित a. betrothed.<BR>--संन्यासः {1}<BR>breaking a promise. {2} (in logic)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">Page0737-b+ 55</a>]<BR>abandonment of the original<BR>preposition; also प्रतिज्ञाहानि in this<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञात|प्रतिज्ञातं
प्रतिज्ञात p. p.<BR>1 Declared, stated,<BR>asserted.<BR>--2 Promised, agreed.<BR>--3 Admitted, acknowledged.<BR>--4<BR>Agreeable, desirable.<BR>--तं A<BR>promise.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः a statement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञानं|प्रतिज्ञान
प्रतिज्ञानं<BR>1 Asserting, affirmation.<BR>--2 Agreement, promise.<BR>--3<BR>Admission.<BR>--4 Bringing forward or<BR>adducing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिज्ञेय|प्रतिज्ञेयः
प्रतिज्ञेय a. To be premised &c.<BR>--यः A panegyrist, bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतितरः|प्रतितर
प्रतितरः An oarsman, a sailor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिताली
प्रतिताली The key of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदर्शनं|प्रतिदर्शन
प्रतिदर्शनं Seeing, perceiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदा
प्रतिदा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To exchange,<BR>barter.<BR>--2 To give back, return,<BR>restore; Ch. P. 35.<BR>--3 To<BR>recompensate.<BR>--4 To give as a reward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदत्त
प्रतिदत्त p. p. Returned, restored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदानं|प्रतिदान
प्रतिदानं<BR>1 Restoration, giving back,<BR>restitution (as of a deposit).<BR>--2<BR>Barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदेय|प्रतिदेयं
प्रतिदेय a. To be returned &c.<BR>--यं<BR>1 A pawn, pledge.<BR>--2 An article<BR>purchased and given back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदारणं|प्रतिदारण
प्रतिदारणं<BR>1 Fighting, battle.<BR>--2 Splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदिवन्
प्रतिदिवन् m.<BR>1 A day.<BR>--2 The<BR>sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदृश्
प्रतिदृश् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To see, behold.<BR>--2 To know, become aware.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिदृष्ट
प्रतिदृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Beheld.<BR>--2 Come<BR>in sight, become visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधा
प्रतिधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To place or lay on.<BR>--2 To return, restore.<BR>--3 To fix<BR>(as an arrow).<BR>--4 To offer,<BR>present.<BR>--5 To use, employ.<BR>--6 To<BR>begin, commence.<BR>--7 To draw near,<BR>approach (as the night); (mostly<BR>Vedic in these senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधा
प्रतिधा A draught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधानं|प्रतिधान
प्रतिधानं<BR>1 Putting on.<BR>--2 Taking<BR>measures.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधिः|प्रतिधि
प्रतिधिः Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिधावनं|प्रतिधावन
प्रतिधावनं Assailing, attacking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वनिः|प्रतिध्वनि
प्रतिध्वनिः, --प्रतिध्वानः An echo,<BR>reverberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वानः|प्रतिध्वान|प्रतिध्वानं
प्रतिध्वनिः, --प्रतिध्वानः An echo,<BR>reverberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिध्वस्त
प्रतिध्वस्त p. p. Down-cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनद्
प्रतिनद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To resound, echo.<BR>--2 To answer with a shout. --Caus.<BR>To fill with noise, make resonant;<BR>Śānti. 2. 17; Rs. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनादः|प्रतिनाद
प्रतिनादः An echo, a reverberation;<BR>(also प्रतिनिनदः in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनादित
प्रतिनादित a. Resounding, echoing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनंद्|प्रतिनन्द्
प्रतिनंद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bless; तौ<BR>गुरुर्गुरुपत्नी च प्रीत्या प्रतिननंदतुः<BR>R. 1. 57; Ms. 7. 146; Ku. 7. 87.<BR>--2 To<BR>welcome, congratulate, hail with<BR>joy, receive gladly; प्रतिनंद्य स तां<BR>पूजां Mb.; Ms. 2. 54.<BR>--3 To accept<BR>cheerfully; Ku. 3. 2.<BR>--4 To<BR>address kindly, show devotion. --Caus.<BR>To delight, gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनंदनं|प्रतिनन्दन|प्रतिनंदन
प्रतिनंदनं<BR>1 Congratulating,<BR>welcoming.<BR>--2 Thanks-giving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनाहः|प्रतिनाह
प्रति(ती)नाहः A flag, banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीनाहः|प्रतीनाह
प्रति(ती)नाहः A flag, banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिधा
प्रतिनिधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To substitute,<BR>put in the place of.<BR>--2 To slight,<BR>disregard.<BR>--3 To order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिधिः|प्रतिनिधि
प्रतिनिधिः<BR>1 A representative,<BR>substitute; सोऽभवत्प्रतिनिधिर्न कर्मणा<BR>R. 11. 13, 1. 81; 4. 54; 5. 63; 9. 40.<BR>--2 A deputy, vicegerent.<BR>--3<BR>Substitution.<BR>--4 A surety,<BR>--5 An<BR>image, likeness, picture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनियत
प्रतिनियत a. Settled,<BR>predestined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनियमः|प्रतिनियम
प्रतिनियमः A general rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिर्जित
प्रतिनिर्जित p. p.<BR>1 Vanquished,<BR>subdued.<BR>--2 Rescinded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिर्देश्य
प्रतिनिर्देश्य a. That which,<BR>though before expressed, is repeated<BR>in order to state something more<BR>about it; cf. the instance given in<BR>K. P. 7; उदेति सविता ताम्रस्ताम्र<BR>एवास्तमेति च, where ताम्र is repeated to<BR>show that the sun that rises red<BR>sets also red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिर्यातनं|प्रतिनिर्यातन
प्रतिनिर्यातनं<BR>1 Retribution,<BR>retaliation.<BR>--2 Returning, giving back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिविष्ट
प्रतिनिविष्ट a. Perverse,<BR>obstinate, hardened.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मूर्खः a<BR>perverse fool, confirmed blockhead;<BR>न तु प्रतिनिविष्टमूर्खजनचित्तमाराधयेत्<BR>Bh. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनिवर्तनं|प्रतिनिवर्तन|प्रतिनिवर्त्तन
प्रतिनिवर्तनं<BR>1 Returning, return.<BR>--2 Turning away from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनुद्
प्रतिनुद् {c6c} U. To ward off, repel,<BR>repulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिनोदः|प्रतिनोद
प्रतिनोदः Repelling, repulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपद्
प्रतिपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To step or go<BR>towards, approach, resort or betake<BR>oneself to; उमामुखं तु प्रतिपद्य लोला<BR>द्विसंश्रयां प्रीतिमवाप लक्ष्मीः Ku. 1. 43.<BR>--2 To enter upon, step upon, take,<BR>follow (as a way &c.); इतः पंथानं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-a" target="_blank">Page0738-a+ 57</a>]<BR>प्रतिपद्यस्व Ś. 4; प्रतिपत्स्ये पदवीमहं तव<BR>Ku. 4. 10.<BR>--3 To arrive at, reach,<BR>attain; Śi. 6. 16.<BR>--4 To get, gain,<BR>obtain, share, partake, स हि तस्य न<BR>केवलां श्रियं प्रतिपेदे सकलान् गुणानपि<BR>R. 8. 5, 13; 4. 1, 41; 11. 34; 12. 7;<BR>19. 55; Bg. 14. 14; Śi. 10. 63.<BR>--5<BR>To accept, take to; Śi. 15. 22;<BR>16. 24.<BR>--6 To recover, reobtain, regain;<BR>receive; Ś. 6. 30; Ku. 4. 16;<BR>7. 22.<BR>--7 To admit, acknowledge;<BR>न मासे प्रतिपत्तासे मां चेन्मर्तासि मैथिलि<BR>Bk. 8. 95; Ś. 5. 23; प्रमदाः<BR>पतिवर्त्मगा इति प्रतिपन्नं हि विचेतनैरपि<BR>Ku. 4. 33.<BR>--8 To hold, grasp, seize;<BR>सुमंत्रप्रतिपन्नरश्मिभिः R. 14. 47.<BR>--9 To<BR>consider, regard, deem, look upon;<BR>तद्धनुर्ग्रहणमेव राघवः पत्यपद्यत समर्थमुत्तरं<BR>R. 11. 79.<BR>--10 To undertake, promise<BR>to do, take in hand; निर्वाहः<BR>प्रतिपन्नवस्तुषु सतामेतद्धि गोत्रव्रतं Mu. 2. 18;<BR>कार्यं त्वया नः प्रतिपन्नकल्पं Ku. 3. 14;<BR>R. 10. 40.<BR>--11 To assent or agree to,<BR>consent; तथेति मतिपन्नाय R. 15. 93.<BR>--12 To do, perform, practise,<BR>observe; आचारं प्रतिपद्यस्व Ś. 4; V. 2<BR>‘do the formal obeisance’;<BR>शासनमर्हतां प्रतिपद्यध्वं Mu. 4. 18 act up to or<BR>obey.’<BR>--13 To act or behave towards,<BR>deal, do anything to any one (with<BR>gen. or loc.); स कालयवनश्चापि किं<BR>कृष्णे प्रत्यपद्यत Hariv.; स भवान्<BR>मातृपितृवदस्मासु प्रतिपद्यतां Mb.; कयमहं<BR>प्रतिपत्स्ये Ś. 5; न युक्तं भवतास्मासु<BR>प्रतिपत्तुमसांप्रतं Mb.<BR>--14 To give or return<BR>(as a reply); कथं प्रतिवचनमपि न<BR>प्रतिपद्यसे Mu. 6; न जाने किं तातः<BR>प्रतिपत्स्यत इति Ś. 4.<BR>--15 To perceive,<BR>become aware of<BR>--16 To know,<BR>understand, become acquainted with,<BR>learn, discover.<BR>--17 To roam,<BR>wander.<BR>--18 To take place, occur.<BR>--19 To<BR>restore.<BR>--20 To permit, allow.<BR>--21<BR>To take place, happen.<BR>--22 To go<BR>back, return. (--Caus.)<BR>1 To give,<BR>present, bestow, confer upon,<BR>impart; अर्थिभ्यः प्रतिपाद्यमानमनिशं<BR>प्रप्नोति वृद्धिं परां Bh. 2. 16; Ms. 11. 4;<BR>गुणवते कन्या प्रतिपादनीया Ś. 4.<BR>--2 To<BR>substantiate, prove, establish by<BR>proof; उक्तमेवार्थमुदाहरणेन प्रतिपादयति.<BR>--3 To explain, expound.<BR>--4 To bring<BR>or lead back, convey or transport (to<BR>a place).<BR>--5 To regard, consider.<BR>--6<BR>To assert, declare to be, represent.<BR>--7 To procure.<BR>--8 To effect,<BR>accomplish.<BR>--9 To communicate, teach.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-b" target="_blank">Page0738-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--10 To appoint to, install (loc.).<BR>--11 To prepare, get ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0737-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिः|प्रतिपत्ति
प्रतिपत्तिः f.<BR>1 Getting,<BR>acquirement, gain; चंद्रलोकप्रतिपत्तिः; स्वर्ग˚<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Perception, observation,<BR>consciousness, (right) knowledge;<BR>वागर्थप्रतिपत्तये R. 1. 1;<BR>तयोरभेदप्रतिपत्तिरस्तिमे Bh. 3. 99; गुणिनांमपि<BR>निजरूपप्रतिपत्तिः परत एव संभवति Vās.<BR>--3<BR>Assent, compliance, acceptance;<BR>प्रतिपत्तिपराङ्मुखी Bk. 8. 95 ‘averse from<BR>compliance, unyielding’.<BR>--4<BR>Admission, acknowledgment.<BR>--5<BR>Assertion, statement.<BR>--6 Undertaking,<BR>beginning, commencement.<BR>--7<BR>Action, proceeding, course of action,<BR>procedure; वयस्य का प्रतिपत्तिरत्र<BR>M. 4; Ku. 5. 42; विषादलुप्तप्रतिपत्ति सैन्यं<BR>R. 3. 40 ‘which did not know what<BR>course of action to follow through<BR>dismay.’<BR>--8 Performance, doing,<BR>proceeding with; प्रस्तुतप्रतिपत्तये<BR>R. 15. 75.<BR>--9 Resolution,<BR>determination; व्यवसायः प्रतिपत्तिनिष्ठुरः<BR>R. 8. 65.<BR>--10 News, intelligence;<BR>कर्मसिद्धावाशु प्रतिपत्तिमानय Mu. 4; Ś. 6.<BR>--11 Honour, respect, mark of<BR>distinction, respectful behaviour;<BR>सामान्यप्रतिपत्तिपूर्वकमियं दारेषु दृश्या त्वया<BR>Ś. 4. 16; 7. 1; R. 14. 22; 15. 12.<BR>--12 A method, means.<BR>--13 Intellect,<BR>intelligence.<BR>--14 Use, application.<BR>--15 Promotion, preferment,<BR>exaltation.<BR>--16 Fame, renown, reputation.<BR>--17 Boldness, assurance, confidence.<BR>--18 Conviction, proof.<BR>--19 A rite<BR>from which no advantage accrues.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दक्ष a. knowing how to<BR>act.<BR>--पटहः a kind of kettle-drum.<BR>--भेदः difference of view.<BR>--विशारद<BR>a. knowing how to act, skilful,<BR>clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपत्तिमत्|प्रतिपत्तिमन्त्
प्रतिपत्तिमत् a.<BR>1 Intelligent.<BR>--2<BR>Active, prompt.<BR>--3 Celebrated,<BR>famous.<BR>--4 Noble, dignified.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपद्
प्रतिपद् f.<BR>1 Access, entrance, way.<BR>--2 Beginning, commencement.<BR>--3<BR>Intelligence, intellect.<BR>--4 The first<BR>day of a lunar fortnight.<BR>--5 A<BR>kettle-drum.<BR>--6 An introductory<BR>stanza.<BR>--7 Rank.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चंद्रः the new<BR>moon (the moon on the first day.)<BR>particularly revered and saluted by<BR>people; प्रतिपच्चंद्रनिभोयमात्मजः<BR>R. 8. 65.<BR>--तूर्यं a kind of kettle-drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपदा
प्रतिपदा --दी The first day of a lunar<BR>fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपदी
प्रतिपदा --दी The first day of a lunar<BR>fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपन्न|प्रतिपन्नं
प्रतिपन्न p. p.<BR>1 Gained, obtained.<BR>--2 Done, performed, effected,<BR>accomplished.<BR>--3 Undertaken,<BR>commenced.<BR>--4 Promised, engaged.<BR>--5<BR>Agreed to, assented to; admitted,<BR>acknowledged.<BR>--6 Known, learnt,<BR>understood.<BR>--7 Answered, replied.<BR>--8 Proved, demonstrated;<BR>Ku. 4. 33.<BR>--9 Approached, reached.<BR>--10<BR>Conquered, overcome.<BR>--11<BR>Conversant with, proficient in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादक|प्रतिपादकः
प्रतिपादक a. (दिका f.)<BR>1 Giving,<BR>granting, bestowing, imparting.<BR>--2<BR>Demonstrating, supporting, proving,<BR>establishing.<BR>--3 Treating of,<BR>explaining, illustrating.<BR>--4 Promoting,<BR>furthering, advancing.<BR>--5 Effective,<BR>accomplishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादनं|प्रतिपादन
प्रतिपादनं<BR>1 Giving, granting<BR>bestowing.<BR>--2 Demonstrating, proving,<BR>establishing.<BR>--3 Treating of,<BR>explaining, expounding, illustrating<BR>--4 Effecting, accomplishing,<BR>fulfilment.<BR>--5 Causing, producing.<BR>--6 Repeated action, practice^1.<BR>--7<BR>Commencement.<BR>--8 Giving back,<BR>restoring.<BR>--9 Entrusting, appointing.<BR>--10 Action, worldly conduct.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादयितृ
प्रतिपादयितृ m.<BR>1 A teacher,<BR>instructor.<BR>--2 A giver, bestower.<BR>--3 A demonstrator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादित
प्रतिपादित p. p.<BR>1 Given, bestowed,<BR>granted, presented.<BR>--2 Established<BR>proved, demonstrated.<BR>--3<BR>Explained, expounded.<BR>--4 Declared,<BR>asserted.<BR>--5 Caused, produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपादुक
प्रतिपादुक a.<BR>1 Producing,<BR>causing.<BR>--2 Ascertaining.<BR>--3 Making<BR>manifest or clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपाल्
प्रतिपाल् Caus.<BR>1 To protect,<BR>preserve, guard, defend.<BR>--2 To<BR>wait for, await.<BR>--3 To act up to,<BR>obey.<BR>--4 To nourish, foster, rear.<BR>--5 To keep, maintain, observe,<BR>follow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालकः|प्रतिपालक
प्रतिपालकः A protector, guardian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालनं|प्रतिपालन
प्रतिपालनं<BR>1 Guarding, protecting,<BR>defending.<BR>--2 Observance,<BR>following, practising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपालित
प्रतिपालित p. p.<BR>1 Protected,<BR>cherished.<BR>--2 Observed, practised,<BR>followed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपानं|प्रतिपान
प्रतिपानं Water for drinking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपीडनं|प्रतिपीडन
प्रतिपीडनं Oppressing,<BR>molesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूज्
प्रतिपूज् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To salute in<BR>return.<BR>--2 To honour, salute<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">Page0739-a+ 56</a>]<BR>respectfully, esteem.<BR>--3 To commend,<BR>approve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0738-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजनं|प्रतिपूजन
प्रतिपूजनं, --पूजा<BR>1 Doing homage,<BR>showing respect.<BR>--2 Mutual<BR>salutation, exchange of courtesies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजा
प्रतिपूजनं, --पूजा<BR>1 Doing homage,<BR>showing respect.<BR>--2 Mutual<BR>salutation, exchange of courtesies.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूजित
प्रतिपूजित p. p.<BR>1 Saluted in<BR>return.<BR>--2 Honoured, respectfully<BR>treated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपॄ
प्रतिपॄ Caus.<BR>1 To fill up, fill<BR>completely.<BR>--2 To satisfy, gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिपूरणं|प्रतिपूरण
प्रतिपूरणं<BR>1 Filling, filling up.<BR>--2<BR>Injecting (a fluid &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रणामः|प्रतिप्रणाम
प्रतिप्रणामः An obeisance in<BR>return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रदानं|प्रतिप्रदान
प्रतिप्रदानं<BR>1 Returning,<BR>restoring.<BR>--2 Giving in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रयाणं|प्रतिप्रयाण
प्रतिप्रयाणं Return, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रश्नः|प्रतिप्रश्न
प्रतिप्रश्नः<BR>1 A question asked in<BR>return.<BR>--2 An answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रसवः|प्रतिप्रसव
प्रतिप्रसवः<BR>1 A<BR>counter-exception, an exception to an exception<BR>(wherein the general rule is shown<BR>to be applicable to cases falling<BR>under the exception); तृजकाभ्यां<BR>कर्तरि इत्यस्य प्रतिप्रसवोऽयं (<BR>याजकादिभिश्च) Sk.<BR>--2 A contrary effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रस्थातृ
प्रतिप्रस्थातृ m. An epithet of a<BR>priest who assists the Adhvaryu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रस्थानं|प्रतिप्रस्थान
प्रतिप्रस्थानं Joining the<BR>opposite party, going over to the enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्रहारः|प्रतिप्रहार
प्रतिप्रहारः A counter-blow, a<BR>blow in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिप्लवनं|प्रतिप्लवन
प्रतिप्लवनं Leaping back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफल्
प्रतिफल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To be reflected.<BR>--2 To rebound, recoil.<BR>--3 To<BR>requite, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलः|प्रतिफल|प्रतिफलं
प्रतिफलः, --प्रतिफलनं<BR>1 A reflection,<BR>reflected image, an image or shadow.<BR>--2 Remuneration, requital.<BR>--3<BR>Retaliation, retribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलनं|प्रतिफलन
प्रतिफलः, --प्रतिफलनं<BR>1 A reflection,<BR>reflected image, an image or shadow.<BR>--2 Remuneration, requital.<BR>--3<BR>Retaliation, retribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफलित|प्रतिफलितं
प्रतिफलित a.<BR>1 Reflected.<BR>--2<BR>Returned, requited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिफुल्लक|प्रतिफुल्लकः
प्रतिफुल्लक a. Blossoming,<BR>fullblown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबंध्|प्रतिबन्ध्
प्रतिबंध् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To tie, fasten,<BR>bind (to); पीतप्रतिबद्धवत्सां (धेनुं)<BR>R. 2. 1.<BR>--2 To fix upon, direct<BR>towards; Ku. 7. 91.<BR>--3 To inlay,<BR>set, incase; यदि मणिस्त्रपुणि प्रतिबध्यते<BR>Pt. 1. 75;<BR>बहलानुरागकुरुविंददलप्रतिबद्धमध्यमिव दिग्वलयं Śi. 9. 8.<BR>--4 To<BR>obstruct, hinder, keep off or back,<BR>exclude, shut out; प्रतिबध्नाति हि श्रेयः<BR>पूज्यपूजाव्यतिक्रमः R. 1. 79.<BR>--5 To<BR>stop, interrupt; मैनमंतरा प्रतिबध्नीतं<BR>Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबद्ध|प्रतिबद्धः
प्रतिबद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Bound, tied,<BR>fastened to.<BR>--2 Connected with,<BR>--3 Hindered, obstructed,<BR>impeded.<BR>--4 Set, inlaid.<BR>--5<BR>Furnished with, possessing.<BR>--6<BR>Entangled, involved.<BR>--7 Kept at a<BR>distance.<BR>--8 Disappointed.<BR>--9 Fixed,<BR>directed.<BR>--10 Attached or hanging<BR>to.<BR>--11 Excluded, cut off.<BR>--12 (In<BR>phil.) Invariably and inseparably<BR>connected and implied (as fire in<BR>smoke).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबंधः|प्रतिबन्ध|प्रतिबंध|प्रतिबन्धः
प्रतिबंधः<BR>1 Binding or tying to.<BR>--2<BR>Obstruction, impediment, obstacle;<BR>स तपःप्रतिबंधमन्युना R. 8. 80;<BR>Mv. 5. 4.<BR>--3 Opposition, resistance.<BR>--4<BR>Investment, blockade, siege.<BR>--5<BR>Connection.<BR>--6 Cessation.<BR>--7<BR>Disappointment.<BR>--8 (In phil.)<BR>Invariable and inseparable connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबंधक|प्रतिबन्धक|प्रतिबन्धकः
प्रतिबंधक a. (धिका f.)<BR>1<BR>Binding, fastening.<BR>--2 Impeding,<BR>obstructing, hindering.<BR>--3 Resisting,<BR>opposing.<BR>--कः A branch, shoot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबंधनं|प्रतिबन्धन|प्रतिबंधन
प्रतिबंधनं<BR>1 Binding, tying.<BR>--2<BR>Confinement.<BR>--3 Obstructing,<BR>impeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबंधवत्
प्रतिबंधवत् a. Full of obstacles,<BR>beset with difficulties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबंधिन्|प्रतिबन्धिन्
प्रतिबंधिन् a.<BR>1 Fastening.<BR>--2<BR>Hindering, obstructing.<BR>--3 Impeded,<BR>obstructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबंधिः|प्रतिबन्धि|प्रतिबन्धिः
प्रतिबंधिः --धी f.<BR>1 An objection.<BR>--2<BR>An argument which equally affects<BR>the other side; (प्रतिबंधि m. also in<BR>this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबंधी
प्रतिबंधिः --धी f.<BR>1 An objection.<BR>--2<BR>An argument which equally affects<BR>the other side; (प्रतिबंधि m. also in<BR>this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाध्
प्रतिबाध् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To repel, ward<BR>or keep off.<BR>--2 To check, restrain.<BR>--3 To pain, distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाधक
प्रतिबाधक a.<BR>1 Repelling, keeping<BR>off.<BR>--2 Preventing, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाधनं|प्रतिबाधन
प्रतिबाधनं Repelling, keeping off,<BR>rejecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबाधिन्
प्रतिबाधिन्^1 a. Obstructing. --m.<BR>An adversary, opponent.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: wrong anusvara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिंबनं|प्रतिबिम्बन|प्रतिबिंबन
प्रतिबिंबनं<BR>1 Reflection.<BR>--2<BR>Comparison; दृष्टांतः पुनरेतेषां सर्वेषां<BR>प्रतिबिंबनं K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिंबयति
प्रतिबिंबयति Den. P. To reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबिंबित|प्रतिबिम्बित
प्रतिबिंबित a. Reflected, mirrored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबुध्
प्रतिबुध् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To wake, wake<BR>up, awaken; Ms. 1. 74; Y. 1. 330.<BR>--2 To perceive, be conscious, know.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To awaken, rouse from<BR>sleep; प्रियया प्रतिबोध्यमानमपि सुप्तं (<BR>हतहृदयं) Ś. 6. 6.<BR>--2 To inform,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">Page0739-c+ 56</a>]<BR>make known, acquaint with,<BR>communicate; भावितात्मा भुवो भर्तुरथैनं<BR>प्रत्यबोधयत् R. 1. 74; Śi. 6. 8.<BR>--3 To<BR>charge or entrust with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबुद्ध
प्रतिबुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Awakened,<BR>roused, wide awake; प्रतिबुद्धापि किं<BR>करेष्यामि Ś. 4; Māl. 4, Ms. 1. 74.<BR>--2<BR>Restored to consciousness.<BR>--3<BR>Opened, blown; अप्रतिबुद्धोऽपि चूतप्रसवोऽ<BR>त्रबंधनभंगसुरभिर्भवति Ś. 6.<BR>--4<BR>Illuminated, enlightened.<BR>--5 Great,<BR>exalted.<BR>--6 Recognized, observed.<BR>--7<BR>Celebrated, known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबुद्धिः|प्रतिबुद्धि
प्रतिबुद्धिः f.<BR>1 Awakening.<BR>--2<BR>Hostile purpose or intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधः|प्रतिबोध
प्रतिबोधः<BR>1 Waking, awaking,<BR>being awakened; तदपोहितुमर्हसि प्रिये<BR>प्रतिबोधेन विषादमाशु मे R. 8. 54;<BR>अप्रतिबोधशायिनी 58 ‘sleeping not to wake<BR>again’; Ki. 6. 12; 12. 48.<BR>--2 Perception, knowledge.<BR>--3<BR>Instruction.<BR>--4 Reason,<BR>reasoning faculty; किमुत याः<BR>प्रतिबोधवत्यः Ś. 5. 22.<BR>--5 Recollection;<BR>संमोहः खलु विस्मयनीयो न प्रतिबोधः<BR>Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधक|प्रतिबोधकः
प्रतिबोधक a.<BR>1 Awakening.<BR>--2<BR>Instructing, informing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधन
प्रतिबोधन a. Awakening.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Awakening.<BR>--2 Instructing,<BR>informing.<BR>--3 Knowledge, refinement,<BR>enlighten ment; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिबोधित
प्रतिबोधित p. p.<BR>1 Awakened.<BR>--2<BR>Instructed, taught.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभज्
प्रतिभज् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To receive back<BR>(as a share.).<BR>--2 To fall to one's<BR>share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभागः|प्रतिभाग
प्रतिभागः<BR>1 Division.<BR>--2 A share,<BR>portion (given to a king as a tax)<BR>of one's income, generally a sixth<BR>part; cf. Ś. 5. 4; Ms. 8. 307.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभा
प्रतिभा {c2c} P.<BR>1 To shine, appear<BR>bright or luminous; प्रतिभांत्यद्य<BR>वनानि केतकीनां Ghaṭ. 15.<BR>--2 To show<BR>oneself, become manifest.<BR>--3 To<BR>seem, appear; स्त्रीरत्नसृष्टिरपरा प्रतिभाति<BR>सा मे Ś. 2. 9; R. 2. 47;<BR>Ku. 5. 38; 6. 54.<BR>--4 To occur to, come<BR>into the mind of; as in नोत्तरं<BR>प्रतिभाति मे.<BR>--5 To fall to the lot or<BR>share of.<BR>--6 To seem fit or proper;<BR>Pt. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभा
प्रतिभा<BR>1 An appearance, a look.<BR>--2<BR>Light, splendour.<BR>--3 Intellect,<BR>understanding; Ki. 16. 27;<BR>Vikr. 1. 18, 23.<BR>--4 Genius, bright<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">Page0740-a+ 56</a>]<BR>conception, vivid imagination; (प्रज्ञा<BR>नवनवोन्मेषशालिनी प्रतिभा मता).<BR>--5 An<BR>image, reflection.<BR>--6 Audacity,<BR>impudence.<BR>--7 Suitableness,<BR>agreeableness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वित a. {1} endowed<BR>with genius, intelligent. {2}<BR>audacious, bold.<BR>--मुख a. bold, confident.<BR>--हानिः f. {1} darkness. {2} absence<BR>of intellect or genius.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0739-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभात
प्रतिभात p. p.<BR>1 Bright, luminous.<BR>--2 Known, understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभानं|प्रतिभान
प्रतिभानं<BR>1 Light, splendour.<BR>--2<BR>Intellect or understanding,<BR>brightness of conception; H. 3. 19.<BR>--3<BR>Readiness of wit, presence of mind;<BR>कालावबोधः प्रतिभानवत्त्वं Māl. 3. 11;<BR>दमघोषसुतेन कश्चन प्रतिशिष्टः प्रतिभानवानथ<BR>Śi. 16. 1.<BR>--4 Confidence, boldness,<BR>audacity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभानवत्|प्रतिभानवन्त्
प्रतिभानवत् a.<BR>1 Splendid, bright.<BR>--2 Ready-witted, prompt.<BR>--3 Bold.<BR>--4 Intelligent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभावत्|प्रतिभावन्त्
प्रतिभावत् a.<BR>1 Bright.<BR>--2<BR>Intelligent, shrewd.<BR>--3 Confident, bold.<BR>--m.<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 The moon.<BR>--3<BR>Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभावः|प्रतिभाव
प्रतिभावः Corresponding<BR>disposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाष्
प्रतिभाष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To speak in<BR>return, reply or answer; Bk. 5. 39.<BR>--2 To tell, relate.<BR>--3 To say after<BR>one, speak after hearing.<BR>--4 To<BR>name, call; कामिनि तामपगीतिं<BR>प्रतिभाषंते महाकवयः Śrut. 6.<BR>--5 To address<BR>or speak to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभाषा
प्रतिभाषा An answer, a reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभास्
प्रतिभास् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To shine.<BR>--2<BR>To appear or look like.<BR>--3 To<BR>become clear, manifest oneself.<BR>--4<BR>To be reflected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभासः|प्रतिभास
प्रतिभासः<BR>1 Occurring to, or flashing<BR>across, the mind at once, (sudden)<BR>perception; वाच्यवैचित्र्यप्रतिभासादेव<BR>K. P. 10.<BR>--2 A look, appearance.<BR>--3 Illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभासनं|प्रतिभासन
प्रतिभासनं Look, appearance,<BR>semblance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभिद्
प्रतिभिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To break<BR>through, pierce, penetrate.<BR>--2 To<BR>disclose, betray.<BR>--3 To reproach,<BR>abuse, censure; प्रतिभिद्य<BR>कांतमपराधकृतं Śi. 9. 58; R. 19. 22.<BR>--4 To<BR>reject, disown.<BR>--5 To touch, be in<BR>close contact with; Ku. 7. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभिन्न
प्रतिभिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Pierced through.<BR>--2 Closely connected with.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">Page0740-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभेदः|प्रतिभेद
प्रतिभेदः<BR>1 Splitting, dividing.<BR>--2<BR>Discovery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभेदनं|प्रतिभेदन
प्रतिभेदनं<BR>1 Piercing, penetrating.<BR>--2 Cutting, splitting, cleaving.<BR>--3<BR>Putting out (as the eyes).<BR>--4<BR>Dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभूः
प्रतिभूः A bail, surety, guarantee;<BR>सौभाग्यलाभप्रतिभूः पदानां Vikr. 1. 9;<BR>Y. 2. 10, 54; N. 14. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिभोगः|प्रतिभोग
प्रतिभोगः Enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमा
प्रतिमा {c3c} {c4c} A. To compare,<BR>liken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमा
प्रतिमा m. Ved. A creator, maker.<BR>--मा<BR>1 An image, a likeness,<BR>statue, figure, an idol; R. 16. 39.<BR>--2 Resemblance, similitude; oft.<BR>in comp. in the sense of ‘like,<BR>similar, or equal to’; देवप्रतिम,<BR>अप्रतिम &c.; गुगेः कृशानुप्रतिमात् R. 2. 49.<BR>--3 A reflection, reflected image;<BR>मुखमिंदुरुज्ज्वलकपोलमतः प्रतिमाच्छलेन<BR>सुदृशामविशत् Śi. 9. 48, 73; R. 7. 64;<BR>12. 100.<BR>--4 A measure, extent.<BR>--5<BR>The part of an elephant's head<BR>between the tusks.<BR>--6 A symbol.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गत a. present in an idol.<BR>--चंद्रः the reflected moon, reflection<BR>of the moon; R. 10. 65; so प्रतिमेंदुः,<BR>--प्रतिमाशशांकः.<BR>--परिचारकः an<BR>attendant upon an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमानं|प्रतिमान
प्रतिमानं<BR>1 A model, pattern.<BR>--2<BR>An image, idol.<BR>--3 Likeness,<BR>similitude, similarity; Māl. 9. 3.<BR>--4<BR>A weight.<BR>--5 The part of an<BR>elephant's head between the tusks;<BR>पृथुप्रतिमानभाग &c. Śi. 5. 36.<BR>--6 A<BR>reflection.<BR>--7 A picture.<BR>--8 Ved.<BR>An adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमित
प्रतिमित p. p.<BR>1 Imitated, copied.<BR>--2 Compared.<BR>--3 Reflected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुच्
प्रतिमुच् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To free, liberate,<BR>release, set free; गृहीतप्रतिमुक्तस्य<BR>R. 4. 43; अप्तुं तुरंगं प्रतिमोक्तुसर्हसि<BR>3. 46.<BR>--2 To put on, wear, accoutre<BR>or arm oneself with.<BR>--3 To quit,<BR>leave, abandon.<BR>--4 To throw, cast,<BR>or discharge at.<BR>--5 To pay off (a<BR>debt.).<BR>--6 To return, restore.<BR>--7<BR>To fasten, bind.<BR>--8 To assume a<BR>form. --Caus.<BR>1 To liberate, release.<BR>--2 To rescue, save, deliver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमुक्त|प्रतिमुक्तः
प्रतिमुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Put on, worn,<BR>applied.<BR>--2 Tied, bound, fastened.<BR>--3 Armed, accoutred.<BR>--4 Liberated,<BR>released.<BR>--5 Restored, returned.<BR>--6<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">Page0740-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Flung, hurled.<BR>--7 Thrown, cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमोक्षः|प्रतिमोक्ष
प्रतिमोक्षः, प्रतिमोक्षणं Liberation,<BR>deliverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमोक्षणं|प्रतिमोक्षण
प्रतिमोक्षः, प्रतिमोक्षणं Liberation,<BR>deliverance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिमोचनं|प्रतिमोचन
प्रतिमोचनं<BR>1 Loosening.<BR>--2<BR>Requital, retaliation, retribution;<BR>वैरप्रतिमोचनाय R. 14. 41.<BR>--3 Liberation,<BR>release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियत्
प्रतियत् {c1c} A. To try. --Caus.<BR>1 To restore, return.<BR>--2 To retaliate,<BR>requite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियत्न|प्रतियत्नः
प्रतियत्न a.<BR>1 Troubling about.<BR>--2<BR>Active, vigorous.<BR>--त्नः<BR>1 An effort,<BR>endeavour, exertion.<BR>--2<BR>Preparation, elaboration; Śi. 3. 54.<BR>--3<BR>Making complete or perfect.<BR>--4<BR>Imparting a new quality or virtue;<BR>सतो गुणांतराधानं प्रतियत्नः Kāśi. on<BR>P. II. 3. 53.<BR>--5 Wish, desire.<BR>--6<BR>Opposition, resistance.<BR>--7<BR>Retaliation, retribution, revenge.<BR>--8<BR>Making captive, taking prisoner.<BR>--9<BR>Favour.<BR>--10 Acting well or<BR>properly.<BR>--11 Comprehension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातनं|प्रतियातन
प्रतियातनं Requital, retaliation; as<BR>in वैरप्रतियातन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियातना
प्रतियातना A picture, an image,<BR>statue; Śi. 3. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिया
प्रतिया {c2c} P. To go back, return;<BR>R. 1. 72; 15. 18; 8. 91.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियात
प्रतियात a. Resisted, opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियानं|प्रतियान
प्रतियानं Return, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियुध्
प्रतियुध् {c4c} A. To encounter in<BR>fight, oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियुद्धं|प्रतियुद्ध
प्रतियुद्धं, प्रतियोधनं Fighting against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोधनं|प्रतियोधन
प्रतियुद्धं, प्रतियोधनं Fighting against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोधः|प्रतियोध
प्रतियोधः, प्रतियोधिन्, प्रतियोद्धृ m. An<BR>adversary, opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोधिन्
प्रतियोधः, प्रतियोधिन्, प्रतियोद्धृ m. An<BR>adversary, opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोद्धृ
प्रतियोधः, प्रतियोधिन्, प्रतियोद्धृ m. An<BR>adversary, opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगः|प्रतियोग
प्रतियोगः<BR>1 Being or forming a<BR>counter-part, of anything.<BR>--2<BR>Opposition, resistance.<BR>--3<BR>Contradiction.<BR>--4 Co-operation.<BR>--5 An<BR>antidote, a remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिक
प्रतियोगिक a. Antithetical,<BR>correlative, relative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिन्
प्रतियोगिन् a.<BR>1 Opposing,<BR>counteracting, impeding.<BR>--2 Related or<BR>corresponding to, being or forming<BR>a counter-part of (anything); often<BR>used in works on Nyāya; as a घट<BR>is the प्रतियोगी of घटाभाव; (यस्याभावो<BR>बिवक्ष्यते स प्रतियोगी).<BR>--3 Co-operating<BR>with.<BR>--4 Equally matched. --m.<BR>1 An adversary, opponent, enemy;<BR>दहत्यशेषं प्रतियोगिगर्वं Vikr. 1. 117.<BR>--2 A counter-part, match.<BR>--3 A<BR>partner, an associate.<BR>--4 An object<BR>dependent upon another.<BR>--5 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">Page0741-a+ 55</a>]<BR>counter-part, counter-entity;<BR>प्रतियोगिनानाधीनज्ञानविषयत्वमभावलक्षणम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0740-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगिता
प्रतियोगिता त्वं<BR>1 Opposition.<BR>--2<BR>Dependent existence<BR>--3 Being a<BR>counter-part.<BR>--4 Partnership,<BR>cooperation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतियोगित्वं|प्रतियोगित्व
प्रतियोगिता त्वं<BR>1 Opposition.<BR>--2<BR>Dependent existence<BR>--3 Being a<BR>counter-part.<BR>--4 Partnership,<BR>cooperation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरक्षणं|प्रतिरक्षण
प्रतिरक्षणं --रक्षा Safety,<BR>preservation, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरक्षा
प्रतिरक्षणं --रक्षा Safety,<BR>preservation, protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरंभः|प्रतिरम्भ|प्रतिरंभ|प्रतिरम्भः
प्रतिरंभः Passion, rage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरवः|प्रतिरव
प्रतिरवः<BR>1 Quarrel, contest.<BR>--2<BR>Echo.<BR>--3 Ved. Life (प्राण).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरुध्
प्रतिरुध् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To obstruct,<BR>stop; oppose, resist.<BR>--2 To<BR>blockade, besiege.<BR>--3 To impair disable.<BR>--4 To blame, accuse.<BR>--5 To hide,<BR>conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरुद्ध
प्रतिरुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Impeded,<BR>obstructed, hindered.<BR>--2 Interrupted.<BR>--3<BR>Impaired.<BR>--4 Disabled.<BR>--5<BR>Invested, blockaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधः|प्रतिरोध
प्रतिरोधः<BR>1 Impediment,<BR>obstruction, hindrance.<BR>--2 Siege, blockade.<BR>--3 An opponent.<BR>--4 Concealing.<BR>--5<BR>Theft, robbery.<BR>--6 Censure,<BR>despising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधक|प्रतिरोधकः
प्रतिरोधक, प्रतिरोधिन्-द्धृ a.<BR>1<BR>Obstructing.<BR>--2 Besieging. --m.<BR>1 An<BR>opponent.<BR>--2 A robber, thief;<BR>M. 5. 10.<BR>--3 An obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधिन्
प्रतिरोधक, प्रतिरोधिन्-द्धृ a.<BR>1<BR>Obstructing.<BR>--2 Besieging. --m.<BR>1 An<BR>opponent.<BR>--2 A robber, thief;<BR>M. 5. 10.<BR>--3 An obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोद्धृ
प्रतिरोधक, प्रतिरोधिन्-द्धृ a.<BR>1<BR>Obstructing.<BR>--2 Besieging. --m.<BR>1 An<BR>opponent.<BR>--2 A robber, thief;<BR>M. 5. 10.<BR>--3 An obstacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिरोधनं|प्रतिरोधन
प्रतिरोधनं Opposing, obstructing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलभ्
प्रतिलभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To recover,<BR>regain.<BR>--2 To get, obtain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलंभः|प्रतिलम्भ|प्रतिलम्भः
प्रतिलंभः<BR>1 Getting, obtaining,<BR>receiving.<BR>--2 Censure, abuse, reviling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिलाभः|प्रतिलाभ
प्रतिलाभः Taking or obtaining back,<BR>taking, getting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवच्
प्रतिवच् {c2c} P. To speak in reply,<BR>answer, reply to; न चेद्रहस्यं<BR>प्रतिवक्तुनर्हसि Ku. 5. 40; R. 3. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवचनं|प्रतिवचन
प्रतिवचनं<BR>1 An answer, reply;<BR>परभृतविरुतं कलं यथा<BR>प्रतिवचनीकृतमेभिरीदृशं Ś. 4. 9.<BR>--2 An echo.<BR>--3 A<BR>dependent or final clause in a sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवचस्
प्रतिवचस् n.<BR>1 An answer.<BR>--2 An<BR>echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाक्य|प्रतिवाक्यं
प्रतिवाक्य a. Answerable.<BR>--क्यं A<BR>reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाच्
प्रतिवाच् f.<BR>1 An answer, reply;<BR>प्रतिवाचमदत्त केशवः शपमानाय न चेदिभूभुजे<BR>Śi. 16. 25.<BR>--2 Calling out to.<BR>--3<BR>Barking in return (as a dog).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवद्
प्रतिवद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To speak in<BR>reply, answer; प्रियंवदः प्रत्यवदत्सुरेश्वरं<BR>R. 3. 64.<BR>--2 To speak, utter.<BR>--3 To<BR>repeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवादः|प्रतिवाद
प्रतिवादः<BR>1 An answer, a rejoinder,<BR>reply.<BR>--2 Refusal, rejection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवादिन्
प्रतिवादिन् a.<BR>1 Answering,<BR>replying.<BR>--2 Contradicting. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>defendant, respondent (in law).<BR>--2<BR>An opponent in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवप्
प्रतिवप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sow.<BR>--2 To<BR>plant or fix in, implant; U. 3. 46;<BR>Māl. 5. 10.<BR>--3 To set, stud (as with<BR>jewels); see प्रत्युप्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवापः|प्रतिवाप
प्रतिवापः Addition of substances<BR>to medicines either during or after<BR>decoction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवर्तनं|प्रतिवर्तन
प्रतिवर्तनं Returning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवसथः|प्रतिवसथ
प्रतिवसथः A village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवहनं|प्रतिवहन
प्रतिवहनं Leading back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवाणिः|प्रतिवाणि
प्रतिवाणिः f. An answer, reply.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवारः|प्रतिवार
प्रतिवारः, प्रतिवारणं Warding or<BR>keeping off, keeping back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवारणं|प्रतिवारण|प्रतिवारणः
प्रतिवारः, प्रतिवारणं Warding or<BR>keeping off, keeping back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवार्ता|प्रतिवार्त्ता
प्रतिवार्ता Account, information,<BR>news, tidings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवासिन्
प्रतिवासिन् a. (नी f.) Dwelling<BR>near, neighbouring. --m. A<BR>neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविघातः|प्रतिविघात
प्रतिविघातः Striking back,<BR>defending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविद्
प्रतिविद् {vI.v} {c2c} P. To acknowledge,<BR>receive. {vII.v} {c6c} P. To get, obtain.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To communicate, inform.<BR>--2 To deliver, give, grant.<BR>--3 To<BR>restore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधा
प्रतिविधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To counteract,<BR>correct, repair, retaliate, remedy,<BR>take steps against; अर्थवाद एषः । दोषं<BR>तु मे कंचित्कथय येन स प्रतिविधीयेत<BR>U. 1; क्षिप्रपेव कस्मान्न प्रतिविहितमार्येण<BR>Mu {3}<BR>--2 To dispose, arrange,<BR>prepare.<BR>--3 To despatch, send.<BR>--4 To<BR>doom, condemn; U. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधानं|प्रतिविधान
प्रतिविधानं<BR>1 Counteracting,<BR>counter-working, taking steps against.<BR>--2 Arrangement, array.<BR>--3<BR>Prevention.<BR>--4 Substituted<BR>ceremony, subsidiary rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविधिः|प्रतिविधि
प्रतिविधिः<BR>1 Retaliation.<BR>--2 A<BR>remedy, means of counteracting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिविशिष्ट
प्रतिविशिष्ट a. Most excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशः|प्रतिवेश
प्रतिवेशः<BR>1 A neighbour.<BR>--2 The<BR>residence of a neighbour, neighbour<BR>hood.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वासिन् a. living in<BR>the neighbourhood. (--m.) a<BR>neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेशिन्
प्रतिवेशिन् a. (नी f.) A neighbour;<BR>दृष्टिं हे प्रतिवोशिनि क्षणमिहाप्यस्मद्गृहे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">Page0741-c+ 54</a>]<BR>दास्यसि S. D.; Mk. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेश्यः|प्रतिवेश्य
प्रतिवेश्यः A neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिवेष्टित
प्रतिवेष्टित p. p. Rolled back,<BR>reverted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिव्यूढ
प्रतिव्यूढ p. p. Drawn out in<BR>battle-array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिव्यूहः|प्रतिव्यूह
प्रतिव्यूहः<BR>1 Arraying an army<BR>against an enemy.<BR>--2 A multitude,<BR>collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशमः|प्रतिशम
प्रतिशमः Cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशयनं|प्रतिशयन
प्रतिशयनं The act of lying down<BR>without food before a deity to secure<BR>some desired object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशयित
प्रतिशयित a. One who lies down<BR>without food before a deity to<BR>secure his desired object; अनया च<BR>किलास्मै प्रतिशयिताय स्वप्ने समादिष्टं<BR>Dk. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशापः|प्रतिशाप
प्रतिशापः A curse for curse, a<BR>curse in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशासनं|प्रतिशासन
प्रतिशासनं<BR>1 Giving orders,<BR>sending on an errand, ordering.<BR>--2<BR>Ordering or despatching an inferior<BR>after calling him to attend.<BR>--3<BR>Counter-manding.<BR>--4 A rival command<BR>or authority; अप्रतिशासनं जगत्<BR>R. 8. 27 ‘completely under the sway<BR>of one ruler’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशास्तिः|प्रतिशास्ति
प्रतिशास्तिः f. Sending on an<BR>errand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशिष्ट|प्रतिशिष्टं
प्रतिशिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Ordered, sent;<BR>Śi. 16. 1.<BR>--2 Dismissed, rejected.<BR>--3<BR>Famous, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिशीन
प्रतिशीन a. Fluid, dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्या
प्रतिश्या, प्रतिश्यानं, प्रतिश्यायः A<BR>catarrh or cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्यानं|प्रतिश्यान
प्रतिश्या, प्रतिश्यानं, प्रतिश्यायः A<BR>catarrh or cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्यायः|प्रतिश्याय
प्रतिश्या, प्रतिश्यानं, प्रतिश्यायः A<BR>catarrh or cold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रयः|प्रतिश्रय
प्रतिश्रयः<BR>1 A shelter, asylum.<BR>--2<BR>A house, dwelling, residence;<BR>Y. 1. 210; Ms. 10. 51.<BR>--3 An asembly.<BR>--4 A sacrificial hall.<BR>--5 Help,<BR>assistance.<BR>--6 A promise.<BR>--7 A receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रु
प्रतिश्रु {c5c} P. To promise (with<BR>dat. of person to whom the<BR>promise is made); तस्यै प्रतिश्रुत्य<BR>रघुप्रवीरस्तदीप्सितं R. 14. 29, 2. 65; 3. 67.<BR>15. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रवः|प्रतिश्रव
प्रतिश्रवः<BR>1 Assent, agreement,<BR>promise.<BR>--2 An echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रवणं|प्रतिश्रवण
प्रतिश्रवणं<BR>1 Listening to;<BR>Ms. 2. 195.<BR>--2 Promising, assenting;<BR>agreeing.<BR>--3 A promise.<BR>--4 Maintaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुत्
प्रतिश्रुत्, प्रतिश्रुतिः f.<BR>1 A promise.<BR>--2 An echo, reverberation;<BR>R. 13. 40; 16. 31; Śi. 17. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुतिः|प्रतिश्रुति
प्रतिश्रुत्, प्रतिश्रुतिः f.<BR>1 A promise.<BR>--2 An echo, reverberation;<BR>R. 13. 40; 16. 31; Śi. 17. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0741-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिश्रुत|प्रतिश्रुतः
प्रतिश्रुत p. p. Promised, agreed,<BR>assented to.<BR>--तं A promise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिध्
प्रतिषिध् {c1c} P. or Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>prevent, ward off, restrain; Ms. 2. 206;<BR>R. 8. 23.<BR>--2 To forbid, prohibit; नृपतेः<BR>प्रतिषिद्धमेव तत्कृतवान् पंक्तिरथो विलंघ्य<BR>यत् R. 9. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषिद्ध|प्रतिषिद्धः
प्रतिषिद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Forbidden,<BR>prohibited, disallowed, refused.<BR>--2<BR>Contradicted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधः|प्रतिषेध
प्रतिषेधः<BR>1 Keeping or warding off,<BR>driving away, expulsion; Vikr. 1. 8.<BR>--2 Prohibition; as in शास्त्रपतिषेधः.<BR>--3 Denial, refusal.<BR>--4 Negation,<BR>contradiction.<BR>--5 A negative particle.<BR>--6<BR>An exception.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षरं,<BR>--उक्तिः f. words of denial, refusal;<BR>Ś. 3. 25.<BR>--उपमा one of the several<BR>kinds of Upamā mentioned by<BR>Daṇḍin. It is thus explained:<BR>--न जातु<BR>शक्तिरिंदोस्ते मुखेन प्रतिगर्जिनुं । कलंकिनो<BR>जडस्येति प्रतिषेधापमैव सा ॥ Kāv. 2. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधक|प्रतिषेधकः
प्रतिषेधक, प्रतिषेद्धृ a.<BR>1 Warding<BR>off, prohibiting, preventing.<BR>--2<BR>Preventive. --m. A hinderer,<BR>prohibitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेद्धृ
प्रतिषेधक, प्रतिषेद्धृ a.<BR>1 Warding<BR>off, prohibiting, preventing.<BR>--2<BR>Preventive. --m. A hinderer,<BR>prohibitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिषेधनं|प्रतिषेधन
प्रतिषेधनं<BR>1 Keeping er warding<BR>off, preventing.<BR>--2 Prohibition.<BR>--3<BR>Denial, refusal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कः|प्रतिष्क
प्रतिष्कः, प्रतिष्कसः A spy,<BR>messenger, an emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कसः|प्रतिष्कस
प्रतिष्कः, प्रतिष्कसः A spy,<BR>messenger, an emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कशः|प्रतिष्कश
प्रतिष्कशः<BR>1 A spy, emissary.<BR>--2<BR>A whip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्कषः|प्रतिष्कष
प्रतिष्कषः A whip, leather-thong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्टब्ध
प्रतिष्टब्ध p. p. Obstructed,<BR>impeded, stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्टंभः|प्रतिष्टम्भ|प्रतिष्टंभ|प्रतिष्टम्भः
प्रतिष्टंभः Obstruction, impediment,<BR>resistance, opposition, obstacle;<BR>बाहुप्रतिष्टंभविवृद्धमन्युः R. 2. 32, 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठा
प्रतिष्ठा {c1c} P.<BR>1 To stand firm, be<BR>established.<BR>--2 To be supported.<BR>--3<BR>To rest or depend upon.<BR>--4 To stay,<BR>abide, be situated. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>place firmly on, station.<BR>--2 To set<BR>up, erect, establish.<BR>--3 To install,<BR>inaugurate (on a throne).<BR>--4 To<BR>entrust with, consign to.<BR>--5 To offer,<BR>present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठ|प्रतिष्ठः
प्रतिष्ठ a.<BR>1 Famous.<BR>--2 Standing<BR>firmly (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठा
प्रतिष्ठा<BR>1 Resting, remaining,<BR>situation, position; अपौरुषेयप्रतिष्ठं<BR>Māl. 9; Ś. 7. 6.<BR>--2 A house, residence,<BR>home, habitation; R. 6. 21; 14. 5.<BR>--3 Fixity, stability, strength,<BR>permanence, firm basis; अप्रतिष्ठे रघुज्येष्ठे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">Page0742-b+ 56</a>]<BR>का प्रतिष्ठा कुलस्य नः U. 5. 25; अत्र<BR>खलु मे वंशप्रतिष्ठा Ś. 7; वंशः प्रतिष्ठां नीतः<BR>K. 280; Śi. 2. 34.<BR>--4 Basis,<BR>foundation, site; as in गृहप्रतिष्ठा.<BR>--5 A prop,<BR>stay, support; (hence) an object<BR>of glory, a distinguished ornament;<BR>त्यक्ता मया नाम कुलप्रतिष्ठा Ś. 6. 23; द्वे<BR>प्रतिष्ठे कुलस्य नः 3. 21; Ku. 7. 27;<BR>Mv. 7. 21.<BR>--6 High position,<BR>preeminence, high authority;<BR>Mu. 2. 5.<BR>--7 Fame, glory, renown,<BR>celebrity; मा निषाद प्रतिष्ठां त्वमगमः शाश्वतीः<BR>समाः Rām. (= U. 2. 5.).<BR>--8<BR>Installation, inauguration; Mu. 1. 14.<BR>--9 Attainment of a desired object,<BR>accomplishment, fulfilment (of<BR>one's desire); औत्सुक्यमात्रमवसादयति<BR>प्रतिष्ठा Ś. 5. 6.<BR>--10 Tranquillity,<BR>rest, repose.<BR>--11 A receptacle.<BR>--12<BR>The earth.<BR>--13 The consecration of<BR>an idol or image.<BR>--14 A limit,<BR>boundary.<BR>--15 The foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठानं|प्रतिष्ठान
प्रतिष्ठानं<BR>1 Basis, foundation.<BR>--2<BR>Site, situation, position.<BR>--3 A<BR>resting-place.<BR>--4 The foundation of a<BR>city.<BR>--5 A leg, foot.<BR>--6 N. of a town<BR>at the confluence of the Ganges and<BR>Yamunā and capital of the early<BR>kings of the lunar race; cf. V. 2.<BR>--7 N. of a town on the Godāvarī<BR>and capital of Śālivāhana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठापनं|प्रतिष्ठापन
प्रतिष्ठापनं<BR>1 Placing, locating.<BR>--2<BR>Installation, inauguration.<BR>--3<BR>Consecrating or setting up of an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठापयितृ
प्रतिष्ठापयितृ m. A founder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठित|प्रतिष्ठितः
प्रतिष्ठित p. p.<BR>1 Set up, erected<BR>--2 Fixed, established.<BR>--3 Placed,<BR>situated; Pt. 1. 81.<BR>--4 Installed,<BR>inaugurated, consecrated.<BR>--5<BR>Completed, effected.<BR>--6 Prized, valued.<BR>--7 Famous, celebrated.<BR>--8 Settled,<BR>determined.<BR>--9 Comprised, included.<BR>--10 Established in life, married.<BR>--11<BR>Endowed.<BR>--12 Applied, applicable.<BR>--13 Conversant with.<BR>--14 Secured,<BR>got, acquired.<BR>--तः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठिति|प्रतिष्ठितिः
प्रतिष्ठिति f. Ved.<BR>1 Standing<BR>firmly.<BR>--2 A station, position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंविद्
प्रतिसंविद् f. An accurate<BR>knowledge of the particulars of anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंवेदक
प्रतिसंवेदक a. Giving detailed<BR>information about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंस्थानं|प्रतिसंस्थान
प्रतिसंस्थानं Setting in,<BR>entering into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहृ
प्रतिसंहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To draw back,<BR>withdraw, draw in; तत्साधुकृतसंधानं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">Page0742-c+ 55</a>]<BR>प्रतिसंहर सायकं Ś. 1. 11; R. 3. 64.<BR>--2 To retract, take back.<BR>--3 To<BR>compress, reduce in bulk.<BR>--4 To<BR>change.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहारः|प्रतिसंहार
प्रतिसंहारः<BR>1 Taking back,<BR>withdrawing.<BR>--2 Diminution,<BR>compression.<BR>--3 Comprehension, inclusion.<BR>--4 Yielding, giving up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंहृत
प्रतिसंहृत p. p.<BR>1 Taken back,<BR>withdrawn; एष प्रतिसंहृतः Ś. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Comprehended, included.<BR>--3<BR>Compressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंक्रमः|प्रतिसङ्क्रम|प्रतिसंक्रम
प्रतिसंक्रमः<BR>1 Reabsorption.<BR>--2<BR>Reflection (प्रतिच्छाया).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंख्या|प्रतिसङ्ख्या
प्रतिसंख्या Consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंगक्षिका|प्रतिसङ्गक्षिका
प्रतिसंगक्षिका A cloak to keep<BR>off dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंगिन्|प्रतिसङ्गिन्
प्रतिसंगिन् a. Clinging or<BR>adhering to, attached to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंचरः|प्रतिसञ्चर|प्रतिसंचर
प्रतिसंचरः<BR>1 Moving<BR>backwards.<BR>--2 Reabsorption.<BR>--3<BR>Especially, reabsorption (of the world)<BR>back into Prakṛti.<BR>--4 A place of<BR>resort, haunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंदेशः|प्रतिसन्देश|प्रतिसंदेश
प्रतिसंदेशः A message in return,<BR>an answer to a message.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंधा|प्रतिसन्धा
प्रतिसंधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To re-adjust.<BR>--2<BR>To aim at, direct<BR>--3 To conceive,<BR>comprehend.<BR>--4 To be, fasten.<BR>--5<BR>To put on, wear.<BR>--6 To restore,<BR>return.<BR>--7 To compose oneself.<BR>--8<BR>To fit (as an arrow to the<BR>bow-string.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंधानं|प्रतिसन्धान|प्रतिसंधान
प्रतिसंधानं<BR>1 Joining together,<BR>uniting.<BR>--2 The period of transition<BR>between two ages.<BR>--3 A means,<BR>remedy.<BR>--4 Self-command, restraint<BR>of feelings or passions.<BR>--5 Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसंधिः|प्रतिसन्धि|प्रतिसंधि
प्रतिसंधिः<BR>1 Reunion.<BR>--2 Entering<BR>into the womb.<BR>--3 The period of<BR>transition between two ages.<BR>--4<BR>Stop, cessation (उपरम).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसमाधानं|प्रतिसमाधान
प्रतिसमाधानं Cure, remedy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसमासनं|प्रतिसमासन
प्रतिसमासनं<BR>1 Coping with,<BR>being a match for.<BR>--2 Resisting,<BR>opposing, withstanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर|प्रतिसरः
प्रतिसर a. Dependent, subject.<BR>--रः --रं<BR>1 A cord or ribbon worn<BR>round the wrist or neck as an<BR>amulet.<BR>--2 An ornament.<BR>--3 A watch,<BR>guard.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A servant, follower.<BR>--2 A bracelet, marriage-string;<BR>स्रस्तोरगप्रतिसरेण करेण पाणिः (अगृह्यत)<BR>Ki. 5. 33 (= कौतुकसूत्र); Māl. 5. 18.<BR>--3 A garland, wreath.<BR>--4 Day-break.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">Page0743-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--5 The rear of an army.<BR>--6 A form of<BR>incantation.<BR>--7 Healing or<BR>dressing a wound.<BR>--रा<BR>1 A female servant.<BR>--2 A thread, fillet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0742-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसर्गः|प्रतिसर्ग
प्रतिसर्गः<BR>1 Secondary creation (as<BR>by the agents of one Supreme<BR>Being).<BR>--2 Dissolution.<BR>--3 Continued<BR>creation out of primitive matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसांधानिकः|प्रतिसान्धानिक|प्रतिसांधानिक|प्रतिसान्धानिकः
प्रतिसांधानिकः A bard,<BR>panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसृ
प्रतिसृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go back, return.<BR>--2 To go towards, rush upon,<BR>attack, assail; दैत्यः प्रत्यसरद्देवं मत्तो<BR>मत्तमिव द्विपं Hariv. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>push backwards, replace;<BR>कनकवलयं स्रस्तं स्रस्तं मया प्रतिसार्यते Ś. 3. 13.<BR>--2 To repel, drive away or back<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसरणं|प्रतिसरण
प्रतिसरणं Leaning or resting upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसारणं|प्रतिसारण
प्रतिसारणं<BR>1 Dressing the edges of<BR>a wound.<BR>--2 An instrument used<BR>for anointing a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसीरा
प्रतिसीरा A screen, curtain, wall<BR>of cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिसृष्ट|प्रतिसृष्टः
प्रतिसृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Sent out,<BR>despatched.<BR>--2 Celebrated.<BR>--3 Repulsed,<BR>rejected.<BR>--4 Intoxicated (प्रमत्त<BR>according to धरणि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्नात
प्रतिस्नात p. p. Bathed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्नेहः|प्रतिस्नेह
प्रतिस्नेहः Love in return,<BR>requital or reciprocation of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पंदनं|प्रतिस्पन्दन|प्रतिस्पंदन
प्रतिस्पंदनं Throbbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पर्धा
प्रतिस्पर्धा Rivalry, emulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्पर्धिन्
प्रतिस्पर्धिन् a. Rival, envious of.<BR>--m. A rival, competitor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्वनः|प्रतिस्वन
प्रतिस्वनः, प्रतिस्वरः<BR>1 An echo,<BR>reverberation; Śi. 13. 31.<BR>--2 A<BR>focus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिस्वरः|प्रतिस्वर
प्रतिस्वनः, प्रतिस्वरः<BR>1 An echo,<BR>reverberation; Śi. 13. 31.<BR>--2 A<BR>focus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहन्
प्रतिहन् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To strike back or<BR>in return; (तं) विध्यंतमुद्धृतसटाः<BR>प्रतिहंतुमीषुः R. 9. 60.<BR>--2 To ward off,<BR>keep off, prevent, oppose, resist;<BR>तोयस्येवाप्रतिहतरयः सैकतं सेतुमोघः<BR>U. 3. 36; प्रतिहतविघ्नाः क्रियाः सभवलोक्य<BR>Ś. 1. 13; Me. 20; Ku. 2. 48;<BR>V. 2. 1.<BR>--3 To repel, drive back,<BR>repulse.<BR>--4 To remove, destroy;<BR>यद्यत्पापं प्रतिजहि जगन्नाथ नम्रस्य तन्मे<BR>Māl. 1. 3.<BR>--5 To counter-act, remedy.<BR>--6 To disown, disavow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहत|प्रतिहतः
प्रतिहत p. p.<BR>1 Struck or beaten<BR>back; knocked back.<BR>--2 Driven<BR>away, repelled, repulsed; Ś. 7. 32.<BR>--3 Opposed, obstructed.<BR>--4 Sent,<BR>despatched,<BR>--5 Hated, disliked.<BR>--6<BR>Disappointed, frustrated.<BR>--7 Fallen,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">Page0743-b+ 56</a>]<BR>overthrown.<BR>--8 Tied, bound.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मति a. hating, disliking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहतिः|प्रतिहति
प्रतिहतिः f.<BR>1 Striking or<BR>knocking back, repelling.<BR>--2 Rebound,<BR>recoil; प्रतिहतिं ययुरर्जुनमुष्टयः<BR>Ki. 18. 5; Śi. 9. 49.<BR>--3<BR>Disappointment, frustration.<BR>--4 Anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहननं|प्रतिहनन
प्रतिहननं Striking or knocking<BR>back, returning a blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहासः|प्रतिहास
प्रतिहासः Returning a laugh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहिंसा
प्रतिहिंसा Retaliation, revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहिंसितं|प्रतिहिंसित
प्रतिहिंसितं Requital of an injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहित
प्रतिहित p. p. Fitted to, put<BR>close to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहृ
प्रतिहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To beat back.<BR>--2<BR>To avoid, shun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहरणं|प्रतिहरण
प्रतिहरणं<BR>1 Avoiding, shunning.<BR>--2<BR>Striking back, repelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहर्तृ|प्रतिहर्त्तृ
प्रतिहर्तृ m.<BR>1 One who beats back<BR>or removes, repeller, remover,<BR>averter, destroyer &c.<BR>--2 The assistant<BR>of the Udgātṛ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारः|प्रतिहार
प्रति(ती)हारः<BR>1 Striking back.<BR>--2 A door, gate.<BR>--3 A porter,<BR>doorkeeper.<BR>--4 A juggler.<BR>--5 Juggling,<BR>a juggling trick.<BR>--6 (In gram.) The<BR>hard contact of the tongue with the<BR>edge of the teeth in pronouncing<BR>dental letters.<BR>--री A female<BR>doorkeeper.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भूमिः f. the<BR>threshold (of a house &c.); Ku. 3. 58.<BR>--रक्षी a female doorkeeper; R. 6. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहारः|प्रतीहार
प्रति(ती)हारः<BR>1 Striking back.<BR>--2 A door, gate.<BR>--3 A porter,<BR>doorkeeper.<BR>--4 A juggler.<BR>--5 Juggling,<BR>a juggling trick.<BR>--6 (In gram.) The<BR>hard contact of the tongue with the<BR>edge of the teeth in pronouncing<BR>dental letters.<BR>--री A female<BR>doorkeeper.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भूमिः f. the<BR>threshold (of a house &c.); Ku. 3. 58.<BR>--रक्षी a female doorkeeper; R. 6. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारकः|प्रतिहारक
प्रतिहारकः A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारणं|प्रतिहारण
प्रतिहारणं Entrance, permission to<BR>enter a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहार्यं|प्रतिहार्य
प्रतिहार्यं Juggling, jugglery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रती
प्रती (प्रति-इ) {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go back<BR>to, return; प्रतीयाय गुरोः सकाशं<BR>R. 5. 35; Bk. 3. 19.<BR>--2 To go to,<BR>approach, turn to.<BR>--3 To fall to the<BR>lot of.<BR>--4 To reach, attain.<BR>--5<BR>To believe, trust, be certain or<BR>sure of, rely on; कः प्रत्येति<BR>सैवेयमिति U. 4; 1. 44.<BR>--6 To learn,<BR>understand, know, प्रतीयते धातुरिवे<BR>हितं फलैः Ki. 1. 20; Śi. 1. 69.<BR>--7<BR>To be well-known or celebrated; सोयं<BR>वटः श्याम इति प्रतीतः R. 13. 53.<BR>--8<BR>To be pleased or satisfied; प्रति<BR>प्रतीतः प्रसवोन्मुखीं प्रियां (ददर्श)<BR>R. 3. 12; 16. 23. --Pass.<BR>1 To be<BR>recognized or perceived.<BR>--2 To be<BR>proved, turn out to be true.<BR>--3 To<BR>follow from anything (as a<BR>necessary result). --Caus. (प्रत्याययति)<BR>1 To cause to believe; convince,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">Page0743-c+ 60</a>]<BR>inspire confidence; एष विवाद एव<BR>प्रत्याय यति Ś. 7; 5. 31; ताः<BR>स्वचारित्र्यमुद्दिश्य प्नत्याययतु मैथिली R. 15. 73.<BR>--2 To cause to perceive, bring to<BR>mind.<BR>--3 To prove, demonstrate,<BR>show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीत|प्रतीतः
प्रतीत p. p.<BR>1 Set forth, started.<BR>--2 Gone by, past, gone.<BR>--3 Believed,<BR>trusted.<BR>--4 Proved, established.<BR>--5 Acknowledged, recognised.<BR>--6<BR>Called, known as, named.<BR>--7<BR>Wellknown, renowned, famous.<BR>--8<BR>Firmly resolved.<BR>--9 (a) Convinced,<BR>of a firm conviction. (b) Believing,<BR>trusting, confident.<BR>--10 Pleased,<BR>delighted; R. 3. 12; 5. 26; 14. 47;<BR>16. 23.<BR>--11 Respectful.<BR>--12 Clever,<BR>learned, wise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीतिः|प्रतीति
प्रतीतिः f.<BR>1 Conviction, settled<BR>belief; Ś. 7. 31.<BR>--2 Belief.<BR>--3<BR>Knowledge, ascertainment, clear or<BR>distinct perception or apprehension;<BR>अपि तु वाच्यवैचित्र्यप्रतिभासादेव<BR>चारुताप्रतीतिः K. P. 10.<BR>--4 Fame, renown.<BR>--5 Respect.<BR>--6 Delight.<BR>--7 Going<BR>towards, approaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक|प्रतीकः
प्रतीक a.<BR>1 Directed or turned<BR>towards.<BR>--2 Inverted, reverse.<BR>--3<BR>Contrary, unfavourable, adverse.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A limb, member; Śi. 18. 79.<BR>--2 A part, portion.<BR>--कं<BR>1 An image.<BR>--2 Mouth, face.<BR>--3 The front (of<BR>anything).<BR>--4 The first word (of a<BR>verse, sentence &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकार|प्रतीकारः
प्रतीकार = प्रतिकारः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीकाश|प्रतीकाशः
प्रतीकाश = प्रतिकाश(ः) q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्ष्
प्रतीक्ष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To look at, observe,<BR>consider.<BR>--2 To look out for, expect.<BR>--3 To wait for, await; संपत्स्यते वः<BR>कामोयं कालः कश्चित्प्रतीक्ष्यतां<BR>Ku. 2. 54; 2. 37; Ms. 9. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्ष
प्रतीक्ष a. Expectant, waiting<BR>for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षक
प्रतीक्षक a. Expectant, waiting<BR>for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षिन्
प्रतीक्षिन् a. Expectant, waiting<BR>for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षण
प्रतीक्षण, प्रतीक्षा<BR>1 Waiting for.<BR>--2<BR>Expectation, hope.<BR>--3 Regard,<BR>consideration, attention.<BR>--4 Looking at,<BR>considering.<BR>--5 Fulfilment,<BR>observance (of a vow, promise &c).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षा
प्रतीक्षण, प्रतीक्षा<BR>1 Waiting for.<BR>--2<BR>Expectation, hope.<BR>--3 Regard,<BR>consideration, attention.<BR>--4 Looking at,<BR>considering.<BR>--5 Fulfilment,<BR>observance (of a vow, promise &c).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्षित
प्रतीक्षित p. p.<BR>1 Waited for,<BR>expected.<BR>--2 Considered.<BR>--3 Respected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीक्ष्य|प्रतीक्ष्यः
प्रतीक्ष्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be waited for.<BR>--2 Worthy of consideration or<BR>regard.<BR>--3 Venerable, respectable;<BR>R. 5. 14; Śi. 2. 108.<BR>--4 To be adhered<BR>to or maintained, to be fulfilled;<BR>Śi. 2. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0743-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीघात|प्रतीघातः
प्रतीघात = प्रतिघात q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीची
प्रतीची The west.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः<BR>N. of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीचीन|प्रतीचीनं
प्रतीचीन a.<BR>1 Western, westerly.<BR>--2 Future, subsequent, following.<BR>--3 Ved. Turned or directed towards.<BR>--4 Turning back, turned away<BR>from.<BR>--5 Coming from behind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीच्य|प्रतीच्यः
प्रतीच्य a.<BR>1 Living in the west,<BR>western, westerly.<BR>--2 Ved.<BR>Disappeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीच्छकः|प्रतीच्छक
प्रतीच्छकः A receiver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीत्त
प्रतीत्त a. Given back, restored.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतींधकः|प्रतीन्धक|प्रतींधक|प्रतीन्धकः
प्रतींधकः N. of a country called<BR>विदेह q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीनाहः|प्रतीनाह
प्रतीनाहः A flag, banner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीप|प्रतीपं|प्रतीपः
प्रतीप a. [प्रतिगताः आपो यत्र,<BR>प्रतिअप् अच्, अप ईप् च्]<BR>1 Contrary,<BR>unfavourable, adverse, opposite;<BR>तत्प्रतीपपवनादि वैकृतं R. 11. 62.<BR>--2<BR>Reverse, inverted, out of order.<BR>--3<BR>Backward, retrograde.<BR>--4<BR>Disagreeable, displeasing.<BR>--5 Refractory,<BR>disobedient, obstinate, perverse;<BR>Pt. 1. 424.<BR>--6 Turned away,<BR>averted.<BR>--7 Meeting, encountering.<BR>--8<BR>Hindering.<BR>--पः N. of a king,<BR>father of Saṃtanu and grand-father<BR>of Bhīṣma.<BR>--पं N. of a figure of<BR>speech in which the usual form of<BR>comparison is inverted, the उपमान<BR>being compared with the उपमेय;<BR>प्रतीपमुपमानस्याप्युपमेयत्वकल्पनं ।<BR>त्वल्लोचनसमं पद्मं त्वद्वक्त्रसदृशो विधुः ॥ Chandr. 5. 9;<BR>(for fuller definitions and<BR>explanation see K. P. 10 under प्रतीप).<BR>--पं<BR>ind.<BR>1 On the contrary.<BR>--2 In an<BR>inverted order.<BR>--3 Against, in<BR>opposition to; भर्तुर्विप्रकृतापि रोषणतया<BR>मा स्म प्रतीपं गमः Ś. 4. 17.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग a. {1} going against. {2} adverse,<BR>unfavourable; तस्य जातु मरुतः<BR>प्रतीपगाः R. 11. 58.<BR>--गमनं, गतिः f.<BR>retrograde motion; Ku. 2. 25.<BR>--तरणं<BR>going or sailing against the stream;<BR>V. 2. 5.<BR>--दर्शिनी a woman.<BR>--वचनं {1}<BR>contradiction. {2} a perverse or eva<BR>sive manner of speaking.<BR>--विपाकिन् a. producing the opposite result<BR>(recoiling on the doer); Māl. 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपक
प्रतीपक a. Hostile, opposed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपयति
प्रतीपयति Den. P.<BR>1 To cause to<BR>turn back, reverse, turn back;<BR>Ku. 5. 5.<BR>--2 To be against or hostile to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीपायते
प्रतीपायते Den. A. To be opposed<BR>or unfavourable, to dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीरं|प्रतीर
प्रतीरं A shore, bank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवापः|प्रतीवाप
प्रतीवापः<BR>1 Adding to,<BR>inserting (as an ingredient).<BR>--2 Calcining<BR>or fluxing metals.<BR>--3 An epidemic<BR>disease, a plague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवेश|प्रतीवेशः
प्रतीवेश, प्रतीहार, प्रतीहास &c. See<BR>प्रतिवेश &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहार|प्रतीहारः
प्रतीवेश, प्रतीहार, प्रतीहास &c. See<BR>प्रतिवेश &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहास|प्रतीहासः
प्रतीवेश, प्रतीहार, प्रतीहास &c. See<BR>प्रतिवेश &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीवेशिन्
प्रतीवेशिन् a. See प्रतिवेशिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीष्
प्रतीष् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To receive, accept;<BR>देवस्य शासनं प्रतीष्य Ś. 6.<BR>--2 To<BR>welcome, greet, receive, honour; एष<BR>माधवीमंडपः स्वागतेनैव नौ प्रतीच्छति Ś. 6.<BR>--3 To obey (as an order).<BR>--4 To<BR>wait for, expect; एष खलु त्वां प्रतीच्छति<BR>V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीष्ट
प्रतीष्ट p. p. Accepted, received &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहासः|प्रतीहास
प्रतीहासः A fragrant oleander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतीहारी
प्रतीहारी<BR>1 A female doorkeeper.<BR>--2 A doorkeeper in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुद्
प्रतुद् {c6c} P. To strike, hurt,<BR>wound. --Caus.<BR>1 To urge on, drive<BR>forward; (fig.) to press, urge<BR>repeatedly (to do a thing); प्रविश गृहमिति<BR>प्रतोद्यप्ताना न चलति भाग्यकृतां दशामवेक्ष्य<BR>Mk. 1. 56.<BR>--2 To pierce, cut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुदः|प्रतुद
प्रतुदः<BR>1 An epithet of a class of<BR>birds (such as hawks, parrots,<BR>crows &c.).<BR>--2 An instrument for<BR>pricking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोदः|प्रतोद
प्रतोदः<BR>1 A goad.<BR>--2 A long whip.<BR>--3 A pricking instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतुष्टिः|प्रतुष्टि
प्रतुष्टिः f., प्रतोषः Gratification,<BR>satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतूर्ण
प्रतूर्ण a. Speedy, quick, fleet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतॄ
प्रतॄ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To cross over.<BR>--2 To<BR>further, promote, advance.<BR>--3 To<BR>raise, elevate, enhance.<BR>--4 To<BR>lengthen, prolong (life).<BR>--5 To lead,<BR>conduct. --Caus.<BR>1 To cheat,<BR>deceive, take in; मां तथा प्रतार्य Ś. 5;<BR>किंत्वेवं कविभिः प्रतारितमनास्तत्त्वं<BR>विजानन्नपि Bh. 1. 78.<BR>--2 To mislead, lead<BR>astray.<BR>--3 To spread, extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतरः|प्रतर
प्रतरः Crossing, crossing or going<BR>over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारः|प्रतार
प्रतारः<BR>1 Carrying or bearing over,<BR>crossing.<BR>--2 Deceit, fraud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारकः|प्रतारक
प्रतारकः --प्रतारिन् A cheat, an<BR>impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारिन्
प्रतारकः --प्रतारिन् A cheat, an<BR>impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारणं|प्रतारण
प्रतारणं<BR>1 Carrying over.<BR>--2<BR>Deceiving, cheating, deception.<BR>--णा<BR>Fraud, deceit knavery, trickery,<BR>roguery, deception, hypocrisy;<BR>यदीच्छसि वशीकर्तुं जगदेकेन कर्मणा ।<BR>उपास्यतां कलौ कल्पलतादेवी प्रतारणा ॥;<BR>प्रतारणासमर्थस्य विद्यया किं प्रयोजनं Udb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतारित|प्रतारितः
प्रतारित a. Deceived, defrauded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतोली
प्रतोली A street, main road,<BR>principal street through a town;<BR>प्रापत्प्रतोलीमतुलप्रतापः Śi. 3. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्त|प्रत्तं
प्रत्त p. p.<BR>1 Given, given away,<BR>presented, offered.<BR>--2 Given in<BR>marriage, married. See प्रदा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्न|प्रत्नः
प्रत्न a.<BR>1 Old, ancient.<BR>--2<BR>Former.<BR>--3 Traditional, customary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्
प्रत्यक् ind.<BR>1 In an opposite<BR>direction, backwards.<BR>--2 Against.<BR>--3<BR>Westward, to the west of (with<BR>abl.).<BR>--4 In the interior, inwardly.<BR>--5 Formerly, in former times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्ष|प्रत्यक्षं
प्रत्यक्ष a. [अक्ष्णः प्रति]<BR>1 Perceptible<BR>(to the eye), visible; प्रत्यक्षाभिः<BR>प्रपन्नस्तनुभिरवतु वस्ताभिरष्टाभिरीशः Ś. 1. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Present, in sight, before the eye<BR>--3<BR>Cognizable by any organ of sense.<BR>--4 Distinct, evident, clear.<BR>--5 Direct,<BR>immediate.<BR>--6 Explicit, express.<BR>--7<BR>Corporeal.<BR>--क्षं<BR>1 Perception, ocular<BR>evidence, apprehension by the senses,<BR>considered as a प्रमाण or mode of<BR>proof; इंद्रियार्थसन्निकर्षजन्यं ज्ञानं<BR>त्यक्षं T. S.<BR>--2 Explicitness,<BR>distinctness. (The forms प्रत्यक्षं, प्रत्यक्षेण,<BR>प्रत्यक्षतः, प्रत्यक्षात् are used<BR>adverbially in the sense of<BR>1 Before, in the<BR>presence of, in the sight of.<BR>--2<BR>Openly, publicly.<BR>--3 Directly,<BR>immediately.<BR>--4 Personally.<BR>--5 At sight.<BR>--6<BR>Explicitly.<BR>--7 Distinctly, clearly.<BR>--8<BR>Literally. so प्रत्यक्षे in the sight of<BR>before the eyes of).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृता<BR>(i. e. ऋ क्) a hymn in which a deity is<BR>directly addressed.<BR>--ज्ञानं ocular<BR>evidence, knowledge obtained by direct<BR>perception.<BR>--दर्शनं ocular evidence.<BR>direct proof.<BR>--दर्शनः, --दर्शिन् m. an<BR>eye-witness.<BR>--दृष्ट a. personally seen.<BR>--परीक्षणं personal examination.<BR>--प्रम correct or certain knowledge, such<BR>as is obtained by direct perception<BR>through the senses.<BR>--प्रमाणं {1} ocular<BR>proof, evidence of the senses. {2} an<BR>organ of perception.<BR>--फल a. having<BR>evident or visible consequences.<BR>--भूत a. manifested.<BR>--भोगः enjoyment<BR>of anything with the knowledge of<BR>the owner.<BR>--वादिन् m. a Buddhist<BR>who admits no other evidence than<BR>ocular proof or perception.<BR>--विहित<BR>a. directly or explicitly enjoined.<BR>--सिद्ध a. determined by ocular<BR>proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0744-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षता
प्रत्यक्षता<BR>--त्वं<BR>1 Perceptibility,<BR>ocular proof.<BR>--2 Standing face to face.<BR>--3 Explicitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षयति
प्रत्यक्षयति Den. P. To make<BR>visible, show, manifest, display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षिन्
प्रत्यक्षिन् a. Witnessing in person.<BR>--m. An eye-witness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यक्षीकृ
प्रत्यक्षीकृ {c8c} U. To witness or see<BR>in person, ascertain or see with one's<BR>own eyes; राजर्षेरुदंतं प्रत्यक्षीकरिष्यामि<BR>Ś. 6; तद्देवः पत्रारूढं प्रत्यक्षीकरोतु ibid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यग्र|प्रत्यग्रः
प्रत्यग्र a.<BR>1 Fresh, young, new,<BR>recent; प्रत्यग्रहतानां मांसं Ve. 3;<BR>कुसुमशयनं न प्रत्यग्रं V. 3. 10; Me. 4;<BR>R. 10. 54; Ratn. 1. 21.<BR>--2 Repeated.<BR>--3 Pure.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वयस् a. young<BR>in age, in the prime of life,<BR>youthful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यंच्|प्रत्यञ्च्
प्रत्यंच्, प्रत्यच् a. (प्रतीची f. or<BR>according to Vopadeva प्रत्यंची also)<BR>1 Turned or directed towards.<BR>--2<BR>Being behind.<BR>--3 Following,<BR>subsequent.<BR>--4 Averted, turned sway,<BR>turning back; Pt. 3. 181.<BR>--5<BR>Western, westerly.<BR>--6 Inner, interior.<BR>--7 Equal to, a match for. --m.<BR>1<BR>The individual soul.<BR>--2 Future<BR>time.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षं (प्रत्यगक्ष)<BR>an inner organ.<BR>--आत्मन् m. (<BR>प्रत्यगात्मन्) the individual soul.<BR>--आनंद<BR>a. inwardly joyful.<BR>--आशापतिः<BR>(प्रत्यगाशापतिः) ‘the lord of the<BR>western direction’, an epithet of<BR>Varuṇa.<BR>--उदच् f. (प्रत्यगुदच्) the<BR>north-west.<BR>--चेतन a. {1} whose<BR>thoughts are turned upon himself<BR>{2} intelligent.<BR>--(नः) {1} the<BR>supreme soul. {2} the soul.<BR>--दक्षिणतः (प्रत्थग्दक्षिणतः) ind. towards<BR>the southwest.<BR>--दृश् f. (प्रत्यग्दृश्)<BR>an inward glance, a glance directed<BR>inwards.<BR>--धामन् a. internally<BR>illuminated.<BR>--मुख a. (प्रत्यङ्मुख) {1}<BR>facing the west. {2} having the<BR>face averted.<BR>--स्रोतस् (प्रत्यक्स्रोतस्)<BR>flowing towards the west; Malli.<BR>on Śi. 4. 66. (--f.) an epithet of<BR>the river Narmadā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यच्
प्रत्यंच्, प्रत्यच् a. (प्रतीची f. or<BR>according to Vopadeva प्रत्यंची also)<BR>1 Turned or directed towards.<BR>--2<BR>Being behind.<BR>--3 Following,<BR>subsequent.<BR>--4 Averted, turned sway,<BR>turning back; Pt. 3. 181.<BR>--5<BR>Western, westerly.<BR>--6 Inner, interior.<BR>--7 Equal to, a match for. --m.<BR>1<BR>The individual soul.<BR>--2 Future<BR>time.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षं (प्रत्यगक्ष)<BR>an inner organ.<BR>--आत्मन् m. (<BR>प्रत्यगात्मन्) the individual soul.<BR>--आनंद<BR>a. inwardly joyful.<BR>--आशापतिः<BR>(प्रत्यगाशापतिः) ‘the lord of the<BR>western direction’, an epithet of<BR>Varuṇa.<BR>--उदच् f. (प्रत्यगुदच्) the<BR>north-west.<BR>--चेतन a. {1} whose<BR>thoughts are turned upon himself<BR>{2} intelligent.<BR>--(नः) {1} the<BR>supreme soul. {2} the soul.<BR>--दक्षिणतः (प्रत्थग्दक्षिणतः) ind. towards<BR>the southwest.<BR>--दृश् f. (प्रत्यग्दृश्)<BR>an inward glance, a glance directed<BR>inwards.<BR>--धामन् a. internally<BR>illuminated.<BR>--मुख a. (प्रत्यङ्मुख) {1}<BR>facing the west. {2} having the<BR>face averted.<BR>--स्रोतस् (प्रत्यक्स्रोतस्)<BR>flowing towards the west; Malli.<BR>on Śi. 4. 66. (--f.) an epithet of<BR>the river Narmadā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यंचित|प्रत्यञ्चित
प्रत्यंचित a. Honoured,<BR>worshipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञा
प्रत्यभिज्ञा {c9c} U.<BR>1 To recognize.<BR>--2 To come to oneself, recover<BR>consciousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञा
प्रत्यभिज्ञा Knowing, recognition;<BR>सप्रत्यभिज्ञमिव मामवलोक्य Māl. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञानं|प्रत्यभिज्ञान
प्रत्यभिज्ञानं<BR>1 Recognition; see the<BR>word अभिज्ञान also.<BR>--2 A token of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">Page0745-b+ 54</a>]<BR>recognition (in return);<BR>प्रत्यभिज्ञानरत्नं च रामा यादर्श यत्कृती R. 12. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिज्ञात
प्रत्यभिज्ञात^1 p. p. Recognised.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: print vague.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिभूत
प्रत्यभिभूत p. p. Overcome,<BR>conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभियुक्त
प्रत्यभियुक्त p. p. Acoused in<BR>return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभियोगः|प्रत्यभियोग
प्रत्यभियोगः A counter-charge, an<BR>accusation in return; Y. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिवद्
प्रत्यभिवद् Caus. To salute or<BR>greet in return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिवादः|प्रत्यभिवाद
प्रत्यभिवादः, प्रत्यभिवादनं Returning<BR>a salutation; Ms. 2. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिवादनं|प्रत्यभिवादन
प्रत्यभिवादः, प्रत्यभिवादनं Returning<BR>a salutation; Ms. 2. 126.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यभिस्कंदनं|प्रत्यभिस्कन्दन|प्रत्यभिस्कंदन
प्रत्यभिस्कंदनं A counter-plaint<BR>or charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययः|प्रत्यय
प्रत्ययः<BR>1 Conviction, settled<BR>belief; मूढः परप्रत्ययनेयवुद्धिः M. 1. 2;<BR>संजातप्रत्ययः Pt. 4.<BR>--2 Trust, reliance,<BR>faith, confidence; बलवदपि<BR>शिक्षितानामात्मन्यप्रत्ययं चेतः Ś. 1. 2;<BR>Ku. 6. 20; Śi. 18. 63; Bh. 3. 60.<BR>--3<BR>Conception, idea, notion, opinion.<BR>--4 Surety, certainty.<BR>--5<BR>Knowledge, experience, cognition;<BR>स्थानप्रत्ययात् Ś. 7 ‘judging by the place’;<BR>so आकृतिप्रत्ययात् M. 1; Me. 8.<BR>--6<BR>A cause, ground, means of action;<BR>Ku. 3. 18.<BR>--7 Celebrity, fame,<BR>renown.<BR>--8 A termination, an affix<BR>or suffix; Śi. 14. 66.<BR>--9 An oath.<BR>--10 A dependant.<BR>--11 A usage,<BR>practice.<BR>--12 A hole.<BR>--13 Intellect,<BR>understanding (बुद्धि).<BR>--14 An<BR>assistant or associate.<BR>--15 An epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--16 (With Buddhists)<BR>A co-operating cause.<BR>--17 An<BR>instrument, a means of agency.<BR>--18<BR>Religious contemplation.<BR>--19 A<BR>house-holder who keeps a sacred<BR>fire.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारक --कारिन् a.<BR>producing assurance, convincing.<BR>--(णी)<BR>a seal, signet-ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययित|प्रत्ययितः
प्रत्ययित a.<BR>1 Relied upon,<BR>confided in.<BR>--2 Trusty, confidential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्ययिन्
प्रत्ययिन् a.<BR>1 Relying upon,<BR>trusting, believing.<BR>--2 Trustworthy,<BR>confidential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थ्
प्रत्यर्थ् {c10c} A.<BR>1 To challenge (to<BR>combat), encounter, seek as an<BR>opponent; एत सीताद्रुहः संख्ये प्रत्यर्थयत<BR>राघवं Bk. 6. 25.<BR>--2 To make an<BR>enemy of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थ
प्रत्यर्थ a. Useful, expedient.<BR>--र्थं<BR>1 A reply, an answer.<BR>--2 Hostility,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">Page0745-c+ 56</a>]<BR>opposition. --ind. At every object,<BR>in every case.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थकः|प्रत्यर्थक
प्रत्यर्थकः An opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्थिन्
प्रत्यर्थिन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Hostile,<BR>opposing, inimical to; नास्मि<BR>भवत्योरीश्वरनियोगप्रत्यर्थी V. 2.<BR>--2 Emulating.<BR>--3 Contradicting. --m.<BR>1 An<BR>opponent, adversary, enemy.<BR>--2 A<BR>rival, equal, match; चंद्रो मुखस्य<BR>प्रत्यर्थी.<BR>--3 (In law) A defendant;<BR>स धर्मस्थसखः शश्वदर्थिप्रत्यार्थिनां स्वयं<BR>R. 17. 39; Ms. 8. 79; Y. 2. 6.<BR>--4<BR>An obstacle or impediment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भूत a. coming in the way, become<BR>an obstacle; Ku. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्पणं|प्रत्यर्पण
प्रत्यर्पणं Giving back, restoring;<BR>सीताप्रत्यर्पणैषिणः R. 15. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यर्पित|प्रत्यर्पितं
प्रत्यर्पित p. p. Restored, given<BR>back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्शः|प्रत्यवमर्श
प्रत्यवमर्शः --र्षः<BR>1 Profound<BR>meditation or reflection.<BR>--2 Counsel,<BR>advice.<BR>--3 A counter-conclusion.<BR>--4 Patience, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवमर्षः|प्रत्यवमर्ष
प्रत्यवमर्शः --र्षः<BR>1 Profound<BR>meditation or reflection.<BR>--2 Counsel,<BR>advice.<BR>--3 A counter-conclusion.<BR>--4 Patience, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवरोधनं|प्रत्यवरोधन
प्रत्यवरोधनं Obstruction,<BR>hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवसानं|प्रत्यवसान
प्रत्यवसानं Eating, or drinking;<BR>P. I. 4. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवसित|प्रत्यवसितं
प्रत्यवसित a. Eaten, drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्कंदः|प्रत्यवस्कन्द|प्रत्यवस्कंद|प्रत्यवस्कन्दः
प्रत्यवस्कंदः --दनं (In law) A<BR>special plea; admitting a fact, but<BR>qualifying it in such a manner that<BR>it may not appear as a count of<BR>accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्कंदनं|प्रत्यवस्कन्दन|प्रत्यवस्कंदन|प्रत्यवस्कन्दनं
प्रत्यवस्कंदः --दनं (In law) A<BR>special plea; admitting a fact, but<BR>qualifying it in such a manner that<BR>it may not appear as a count of<BR>accusation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्था
प्रत्यवस्था {c1c} A.<BR>1 To stand<BR>separately.<BR>--2 To oppose, act hostilely,<BR>object to (in argument); अत्र<BR>केचित्पत्यवातेष्ठंते Ś. B.; Bv. 1. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्थातृ
प्रत्यवस्थातृ m. An opponent,<BR>adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवस्थानं|प्रत्यवस्थान
प्रत्यवस्थानं<BR>1 Removal.<BR>--2<BR>Hostility, opposition.<BR>--3 Status quo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवहारः|प्रत्यवहार
प्रत्यवहारः<BR>1 Withdrawal.<BR>--2<BR>Universal destruction, dissolution<BR>(of the world);<BR>सर्गस्थितिप्रत्यवहारहेतुः R. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवायः|प्रत्यवाय
प्रत्यवायः<BR>1 Decrease,<BR>diminution.<BR>--2 An obstacle, impediment;<BR>U. 1. 8.<BR>--3 A contrary or opposite<BR>course, contrariety; Ms. 4. 245.<BR>--4 A sin, an offence, sinfulness;<BR>अनुत्पत्तिं तथा चान्ये प्रत्यवायस्य मन्वते<BR>Jābāli.<BR>--5 Disappointment.<BR>--6<BR>Disappearance of an existing thing.<BR>--7 Non-production of what does not<BR>exist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्ष्
प्रत्यवेक्ष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To look into,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">Page0746-a+ 56</a>]<BR>inspect, examine; प्रत्यवेक्षिताः प्रमदवन<BR>भूमयः Ś. 6.<BR>--2 To investigate,<BR>inquire into, transact; प्रत्यवेक्षितं<BR>पौरकार्यमार्येण Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0745-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्षणं|प्रत्यवेक्षण
प्रत्यवेक्षणं, प्रत्यवेक्षा Taking care of,<BR>regard for, looking after;<BR>R. 17. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यवेक्षा
प्रत्यवेक्षणं, प्रत्यवेक्षा Taking care of,<BR>regard for, looking after;<BR>R. 17. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यस्तमयः|प्रत्यस्तमय
प्रत्यस्तमयः<BR>1 Setting(of the<BR>sun).<BR>--2 End, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याकलित
प्रत्याकलित a.<BR>1 Enumerated.<BR>--2<BR>Interposed, inserted.<BR>--3 Introduced<BR>(as a step in legal proceedings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याक्षेपक
प्रत्याक्षेपक a. (पिका f.)<BR>Jeering, derisive, deriding, treating<BR>scornfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्या
प्रत्याख्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 To deny (as a<BR>fact).<BR>--2 To decline, refuse, reject.<BR>--3 To forbid, prohibit.<BR>--4 To<BR>interdict.<BR>--5 To excel, surpass: M. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्यात|प्रत्याख्यातः
प्रत्याख्यात p. p.<BR>1 Refused,<BR>denied.<BR>--2 Prohibited, forbidden.<BR>--3<BR>Set aside, rejected.<BR>--4 Repulsed.<BR>--5<BR>Excelled, surpassed.<BR>--6 Informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याख्यानं|प्रत्याख्यान
प्रत्याख्यानं<BR>1 Repulse, rejection.<BR>--2 Denial, refusal, disavowal.<BR>--3<BR>Disregard.<BR>--4 Reproach.<BR>--5<BR>Refutation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागम्
प्रत्यागम् {c1c} P. To come back,<BR>return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागतिः|प्रत्यागति
प्रत्यागतिः f. Coming back, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागमः|प्रत्यागम
प्रत्यागमः, प्रत्यागमनं<BR>1 Return,<BR>coming back.<BR>--2 Arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यागमनं|प्रत्यागमन
प्रत्यागमः, प्रत्यागमनं<BR>1 Return,<BR>coming back.<BR>--2 Arrival.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादा
प्रत्यादा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To take back.<BR>--2 To recall, revoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादानं|प्रत्यादान
प्रत्यादानं^1 Receiving back,<BR>resumption.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: from verb pratyAdA.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादिश्
प्रत्यादिश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 (a) To reject,<BR>discard, shun; प्रत्यादिष्टविशेषमंडनविधिः<BR>Ś. 6. 5. (b) To repulse;<BR>प्रत्यादिदेशैनमभाषमाणा R. 6. 25.<BR>--2 To cast<BR>off, repudiate (as a person); कामं<BR>प्रत्यादिष्टां स्मरामि न परिग्रहं मुनेस्तनयां<BR>Ś. 5. 31.<BR>--3 To obscure, eclipse,<BR>defeat, throw into the shade or<BR>background; R. 1. 61; 10. 68.<BR>--4 To<BR>order back, countermand.<BR>--5 To<BR>direct, prescribe, enjoin.<BR>--6 To<BR>warn, caution.<BR>--7 To report to.<BR>--8<BR>To summon.<BR>--9 To conquer,<BR>overcome.<BR>--10 To remove, set aside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादिष्ट|प्रत्यादिष्टः
प्रत्यादिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Prescribed.<BR>--2<BR>Informed.<BR>--3 Rejected, repulsed.<BR>--4 Removed, set aside.<BR>--5<BR>Obscured, thrown into the shade.<BR>--6<BR>Warned, cautioned.<BR>--7 Declared.<BR>--8 Overcome, conquered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यादेशः|प्रत्यादेश
प्रत्यादेशः<BR>1 An order, a command.<BR>--2 Information, declaration.<BR>--3<BR>Refusal, denial, rejection, repulse,<BR>repudiation. प्रत्यादेशान्न खलु भवतो<BR>धीरतां कल्पयामि Me. 114; 95; Ś. 6. 8.<BR>--4 Obscuring, eclipsing, one that<BR>obscures, puts to shame or throws<BR>into shade; या प्रत्यादेशो रूपगर्वितायाः<BR>श्रियः V. 1; K. 5.<BR>--5 Caution,<BR>warning.<BR>--6 Particularly, divine<BR>caution, supernatural warning.<BR>--7<BR>Reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यानयनं|प्रत्यानयन
प्रत्यानयनं Bringing back,<BR>recovery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यापत्तिः|प्रत्यापत्ति
प्रत्यापत्तिः f.<BR>1 Return.<BR>--2<BR>Aversion from or indifference to<BR>worldly objects (वैराग्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याम्नायः|प्रत्याम्नाय
प्रत्याम्नायः<BR>1 The fifth member<BR>of a complete syllogism; i. e. निगमन<BR>(the repetition of the first<BR>proposition).<BR>--2 Contrary determination.<BR>--3 Ved. A substitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायः|प्रत्याय
प्रत्यायः<BR>1 A toll, tax.<BR>--2<BR>Revenue, income.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायक
प्रत्यायक a.<BR>1 Proving,<BR>explaining.<BR>--2 Convincing, producing<BR>assurance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायनं|प्रत्यायन
प्रत्यायनं<BR>1 Leading home (a bride),<BR>marrying.<BR>--2 Setting (of the sun).<BR>--नं --ना<BR>1 Producing confidence.<BR>--2<BR>Explaining.<BR>--3 Proving,<BR>demonstrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यायितः|प्रत्यायित
प्रत्यायितः A confidential agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यालीढं|प्रत्यालीढ
प्रत्यालीढं A particular attitude<BR>in shooting (opp. आलीढ q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यावर्तनं|प्रत्यावर्तन|प्रत्यावर्त्तन
प्रत्यावर्तनं Returning, coming<BR>back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याश्वस्त
प्रत्याश्वस्त p. p. Consoled,<BR>revived, refreshed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याश्वासः|प्रत्याश्वास
प्रत्याश्वासः Respiration, recovery<BR>(of breath).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याश्वासनं|प्रत्याश्वासन
प्रत्याश्वासनं Consolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासत्तिः|प्रत्यासत्ति
प्रत्यासत्तिः f.<BR>1 Close proximity<BR>or contiguity (in time or space).<BR>--2 Close, contact.<BR>--3 An<BR>analogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासन्न|प्रत्यासन्नः
प्रत्यासन्न p. p.<BR>1 Proximate near,<BR>contiguous.<BR>--2 Imminent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मरण, --मृत्यु a. at the point of death,<BR>about to die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासरः|प्रत्यासर
प्रत्यास(सा)रः<BR>1 The rear of an<BR>army.<BR>--2 A form of array, one array<BR>behind another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यासारः|प्रत्यासार
प्रत्यास(सा)रः<BR>1 The rear of an<BR>army.<BR>--2 A form of array, one array<BR>behind another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहत
प्रत्याहत a. Distracted, repelled;<BR>प्रत्याहतास्त्रो गिरिशप्रभावात् R. 2. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहृ
प्रत्याहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To take back<BR>again, bring back, recover.<BR>--2<BR>To withdraw, draw back.<BR>--3<BR>To utter (a speech).<BR>--4 To<BR>report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहरणं|प्रत्याहरण
प्रत्याहरणं<BR>1 Bringing or taking<BR>back, recovery.<BR>--2 Withholding.<BR>--3 Restraining the organs of<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहारः|प्रत्याहार
प्रत्याहारः<BR>1 Drawing back,<BR>marching back, retreat.<BR>--2 Keeping back,<BR>withholding.<BR>--3 Restraining the<BR>organs.<BR>--4 Dissolution of the world,<BR>--5 (In gram.) The comprehension<BR>of several letters or affixes into one<BR>syllable, effected by combining the<BR>first letter of a Sūtra with its final<BR>indicatory letter, or in the case of<BR>several Sūtras, with the final letter<BR>of the last member; thus अण् is the<BR>प्रत्याहार of the Sūtra अइउण्; अच्<BR>(vowels) of the four Sūtras अइउण्,<BR>ऋऌक्, एओङ्, ऐऔच्; हल् of the<BR>consonants; अल् of all letters.<BR>--6<BR>Abridgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्याहृत
प्रत्याहृत a.<BR>1 Got back, recovered.<BR>--2 Restrained, withheld, checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युक्त
प्रत्युक्त p. p. Answered, said in<BR>return, replied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युक्तिः|प्रत्युक्ति
प्रत्युक्तिः f. A reply, an answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युच्चारः|प्रत्युच्चार
प्रत्युच्चारः --च्चारणं Repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युच्चारणं|प्रत्युच्चारण
प्रत्युच्चारः --च्चारणं Repetition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युज्जीव्
प्रत्युज्जीव् {c1c} P. To revive, return<BR>to life. --Caus. To restore or bring<BR>to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युज्जीवनं|प्रत्युज्जीवन
प्रत्युज्जीवनं<BR>1 Reviving, restoring<BR>to life, resuscitation (fig. also).<BR>--2<BR>Coming to life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत
प्रत्युत ind.<BR>1 On the contrary;<BR>कृतमपि महोपकारं पय इव पीत्वा<BR>निरातंकः । प्रत्युत हंतुं यतते काकोदरमोदरः खलो<BR>जगति Bv. 1. 76.<BR>--2 Rather, even.<BR>--3 On the other hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्क्रमः|प्रत्युत्क्रम
प्रत्युत्क्रमः, --क्रमणं, --क्रांतिः f.<BR>1<BR>An undertaking.<BR>--2 Preparations<BR>for war.<BR>--3 Marching out to<BR>attack an enemy.<BR>--4 A secondary<BR>act or effort tending to a main<BR>object.<BR>--5 The first step in any<BR>business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्क्रमणं|प्रत्युत्क्रमण
प्रत्युत्क्रमः, --क्रमणं, --क्रांतिः f.<BR>1<BR>An undertaking.<BR>--2 Preparations<BR>for war.<BR>--3 Marching out to<BR>attack an enemy.<BR>--4 A secondary<BR>act or effort tending to a main<BR>object.<BR>--5 The first step in any<BR>business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्क्रांतिः|प्रत्युत्क्रान्ति|प्रत्युत्क्रांति|प्रत्युत्क्रान्तिः
प्रत्युत्क्रमः, --क्रमणं, --क्रांतिः f.<BR>1<BR>An undertaking.<BR>--2 Preparations<BR>for war.<BR>--3 Marching out to<BR>attack an enemy.<BR>--4 A secondary<BR>act or effort tending to a main<BR>object.<BR>--5 The first step in any<BR>business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्थानं|प्रत्युत्थान
प्रत्युत्थानं<BR>1 Rising against.<BR>--2<BR>Making preparations for war.<BR>--3<BR>Rising from one's seat (as a mark<BR>of respect) to welcome a visitor;<BR>Ms. 2. 210.<BR>--4 Making preparations<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">Page0747-a+ 54</a>]<BR>for, undertaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0746-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्थित
प्रत्युत्थित p. p. Risen to meet or<BR>encounter (a friend, foe &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युत्पन्न|प्रत्युत्पन्नः
प्रत्युत्पन्न p. p.<BR>1 Reproduced,<BR>regenerated.<BR>--2 Prompt, ready,<BR>quick.<BR>--3 (In math.) Multiplied.<BR>--4 Present, existing at present.<BR>--न्नं Multiplication.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मति<BR>a. {1} possessed of presence of mind,<BR>ready-witted. {2} bold, confident.<BR>{3} subtle, sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युदाहरणं|प्रत्युदाहरण
प्रत्युदाहरणं A<BR>counter-illustration, an example to the contrary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गम्
प्रत्युद्गम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go forth or<BR>advance towards to meet (as a mark<BR>of respect) प्रत्युज्जगामातिथिमातिथयः<BR>R. 5. 2: प्रत्युद्गच्छति मूर्छति<BR>स्थिरतमःपंजे निकुंजे प्रियः Gīt. 11; Bv. 3. 3.<BR>--2 To advance or march towards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गत
प्रत्युद्गत p. p.<BR>1 Risen from one's<BR>seat as a mark of respect to greet<BR>or welcome a guest; प्रत्युद्गतो मां भरतः<BR>ससैन्यः R. 13. 64; 12. 62.<BR>--2 Gone<BR>forth against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गतिः|प्रत्युद्गति
प्रत्युद्गतिः f., प्रत्युद्गमः, प्रत्युद्गमनं<BR>Going out or rising from one's seat to<BR>meet or greet a guest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्गमनीयं|प्रत्युद्गमनीय
प्रत्युद्गमनीयं A clean pair of<BR>garments; गृहीतप्रत्युद्गमनीयवस्त्रा<BR>Ku. 7. 11 (v. l. for ˚पत्युद्गमनीय˚); see<BR>उद्गमनीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्धरणं|प्रत्युद्धरण
प्रत्युद्धरणं<BR>1 Recovering,<BR>re-obtaining.<BR>--2 Raising up again.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्यम|प्रत्युद्यमः
प्रत्युद्यम<BR>1 Counterbalance,<BR>counterpoise.<BR>--2 An effort or measure<BR>against, counteraction; Bh. 3. 88<BR>v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युद्यात
प्रत्युद्यात a. See प्रत्युद्गत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युन्नमनं|प्रत्युन्नमन
प्रत्युन्नमनं Rising or springing up<BR>again, rebounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपकृ
प्रत्युपकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To requite a<BR>favour, render a service in return.<BR>--2 To repay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपकारः|प्रत्युपकार
प्रत्युपकारः<BR>1 Returning a<BR>service or kindness, requital of an<BR>obligation, service in return.<BR>--2<BR>Mutual assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपक्रिया
प्रत्युपक्रिया Return of a service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपदेशः|प्रत्युपदेश
प्रत्युपदेशः Advice in return;<BR>Ku. 1. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपपन्न
प्रत्युपपन्न a. See प्रत्युत्पन्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपमानं|प्रत्युपमान
प्रत्युपमानं<BR>1 A counterpart of<BR>a resemblance.<BR>--2 A pattern, model.<BR>--3 A counter-comparison; V. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपलब्ध
प्रत्युपलब्ध p. p. Got back,<BR>recovered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपवेशः|प्रत्युपवेश
प्रत्युपवेशः, --वेशनं Besetting any<BR>one in order to bring him to<BR>compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपवेशनं|प्रत्युपवेशन
प्रत्युपवेशः, --वेशनं Besetting any<BR>one in order to bring him to<BR>compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपस्थानं|प्रत्युपस्थान
प्रत्युपस्थानं Vicinity,<BR>neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युपहारः|प्रत्युपहार
प्रत्युपहारः<BR>1 A respectful<BR>offering.<BR>--2 Giving back, restoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युप्त
प्रत्युप्त p. p.<BR>1 Inlaid, set with,<BR>studded.<BR>--2 Sown.<BR>--3 Fixed,<BR>implanted. firmly fixed or lodged;<BR>Māl. 5. 10; U. 3. 35, 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युषः|प्रत्युष
प्रत्युषः, --प्रत्युषस् n. Morning,<BR>day-break, dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्युषस्
प्रत्युषः, --प्रत्युषस् n. Morning,<BR>day-break, dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषः|प्रत्यूष|प्रत्यूषं
प्रत्यूषः --षं Day-break, morning,<BR>dawn; प्रत्यूषेषु<BR>स्फुटितकमलामोदपैत्रीकषायः Me. 31; महत्येव प्रत्यूषे Ś. 2.<BR>--षः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 N. of one of<BR>the eight Vasus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषं|प्रत्यूष|प्रत्यूषः
प्रत्यूषः --षं Day-break, morning,<BR>dawn; प्रत्यूषेषु<BR>स्फुटितकमलामोदपैत्रीकषायः Me. 31; महत्येव प्रत्यूषे Ś. 2.<BR>--षः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 N. of one of<BR>the eight Vasus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूषस्
प्रत्यूषस् n. Day-break, morning,<BR>dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूह्
प्रत्यूह् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To oppose, resist.<BR>--2 To disturb, interrupt, impede.<BR>--3 To reject, refuse.<BR>--4 To excel,<BR>surpass.<BR>--5 To offer, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रत्यूहः|प्रत्यूह
प्रत्यूहः Impediment, obstacle,<BR>hindrance: विस्मयः सर्वथा हेयः<BR>प्रत्यूहसर्वकर्मणां H. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथ्
प्रथ् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (प्रथते, प्रथित)<BR>1 To<BR>increase (wealth &c.).<BR>--2 To<BR>spread abroad (as fame, rumour<BR>&c.); तथा यशोऽस्य प्रथते Ms. 11. 15.<BR>--3 To become famous or celebrated;<BR>भतस्तदख्यया तीर्थं पावनं भुवि पप्रथे<BR>R. 15. 101; अतोऽस्मि लोके वेदे च<BR>प्रथितः पुरुषोत्तमः Bg. 15. 18; Śi. 9. 16;<BR>15. 23; Ku. 5. 7; Me. 24;<BR>R. 5. 65; 9. 76.<BR>--4 To appear, arise, come<BR>to light; श्रमो नु तासां मदनो नु पप्रथे<BR>Ki. 8. 53.<BR>--5 To occur (to mind).<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} U. (प्रथयति-ते, प्रथित)<BR>1 To<BR>spread abroad, proclaim; सज्जना एव<BR>साधूनां प्रथयंति गुणोत्करं Dṛ. Ś. 12;<BR>Bk. 17. 107.<BR>--2 To show,<BR>manifest, display, evince, indicate; परमं<BR>वपुः प्रथयतीव जयं Ki. 6. 35; 5. 3;<BR>Śi. 10. 25; Ratn. 4. 13; Ś. 3. 15.<BR>--3 To increase, enlarge, enhance,<BR>augment, stretch; Bh. 2. 45.<BR>--4 To<BR>disclose.<BR>--5 To spread, extend<BR>--6 To throw, cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथनं|प्रथन
प्रथनं [प्रथ्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Spreading,<BR>extension.<BR>--2 Scattering.<BR>--3<BR>Throwing, projecting.<BR>--4 Showing,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-c" target="_blank">Page0747-c+ 57</a>]<BR>evincing, displaying.<BR>--5 A place where<BR>anything is spread.<BR>--6<BR>Celebrating, proclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथस्
प्रथस् n. Ved. Extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथम|प्रथमः
प्रथम [प्रथ्-अमच्] (Nom. pl., m.<BR>प्रथमे or प्रथमाः)<BR>1 First, foremost;<BR>R. 3. 44; H. 2. 39; Ki. 2. 44.<BR>--2<BR>First, chief, principal, most<BR>excellent or eminent, matchless,<BR>incomparable; Śi. 15. 42; Ms. 3. 147.<BR>--3<BR>Earliest, most ancient, primary.<BR>--4<BR>Prior, previous, former, earlier;<BR>प्रथमसुकृतापेक्षया Me. 17, R. 10. 67.<BR>--5 (In gram.) The first person<BR>(= third person according to<BR>European phraseology).<BR>--मः<BR>1 The first<BR>(third) person.<BR>--2 The first<BR>consonant of a class.<BR>--मा The<BR>nominative case.<BR>--मं ind.<BR>1 First,<BR>firstly, at first; Ku. 7. 24; R. 3. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Already, previously, formerly;<BR>प्रथमोदितं aforesaid; R. 3. 68.<BR>--3<BR>At once, immediately.<BR>--4 Before;<BR>यात्रायै चोदयामास तं शक्तेः प्रथमं शरत्<BR>R. 4. 24; उत्तिष्ठेत्यथमं चास्य चरमं चैव<BR>संविशेत् Ms. 2. 194.<BR>--5 Newly,<BR>recently. प्रथमं अनंतरं or ततः or पश्चात्<BR>first, afterwards; प्रथमात् firstly, for<BR>the first time; प्रथमतः<BR>1 At first,<BR>firstly;<BR>--2 previously.<BR>--3 immediately;<BR>--4 before, in preference to (gen.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्धः --र्धं the first half.<BR>--आगामिन् a. first mentioned.<BR>--आदेशः placing at the beginning.<BR>--आश्रमः the first of the four stages<BR>in the religious life of a Brāhmaṇa;<BR>i. e. Brahmacarya.<BR>--इतर a. ‘other<BR>than first’, the second.<BR>--उदित a.<BR>first uttered; उवाच धात्र्या<BR>प्रथमोदितं वचः R. 3. 25.<BR>--उत्पन्न a. firstborn.<BR>--कल्पः {1} the best course to adopt.<BR>{2} an excellent suggestion or idea.<BR>--कल्पित a. {1} first thought out. {2}<BR>first in rank or importance.<BR>--कुसुमः<BR>white marjoram.<BR>--गर्भ a. pregnant<BR>for the first time.<BR>--ज a. {1}<BR>firstborn. {2} original, primary.<BR>--दर्शनं<BR>first sight.<BR>--दिवसः the first day;<BR>Me. 2.<BR>--पुरुषः the first person (=the<BR>third person according to the<BR>English system of treating Sanskrit<BR>grammar).<BR>--मंगल a. highly<BR>auspicious.<BR>--यौवनं early youth or age,<BR>youthful state.<BR>--वयस् n. early age,<BR>youth.<BR>--विता Ved. a first wife.<BR>--विरहः separation for the first time.<BR>--वृत्तांतः antecedents, former<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">Page0748-a+ 57</a>]<BR>circumstances.<BR>--वैयाकरणः {1} the most<BR>distinguished grammarian. {2} a<BR>beginner in grammar.<BR>--साहसः the first<BR>or lowest of the three degrees of<BR>punishment or fine.<BR>--सुकृतं former<BR>kindness or service.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0747-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथमक
प्रथमक a. First, foremost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथा
प्रथा Fame, celebrity; Śi. 15. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथित|प्रथितः
प्रथित p. p.<BR>1 Increased, extended.<BR>--2 Published, proclaimed, spread,<BR>declared; प्रथितयशसां<BR>भासकविसोमिल्लकविमिश्रादीनां M. 1.<BR>--3 Shown,<BR>displayed, manifested, evinced.<BR>--4<BR>Famous, celebrated, renowned,<BR>wellknown; Pt. 1. 24; Ku. 5. 7.<BR>--5<BR>Intent upon, engaged in, devoted<BR>to.<BR>--6 Spread, stretched.<BR>--तंः N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथितिः|प्रथिति
प्रथितिः f. Celebrity, fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिमन्
प्रथिमन् m. Breadth, greatness,<BR>extension, magnitude; प्रथिमानं<BR>दधानेन जघनेन घनेन सा Bk. 4. 17; (गुणाः)<BR>प्रारंभसूक्ष्माः प्रथिमानमापुः R. 18. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिविः|प्रथिवि
प्रथिविः f. The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथिष्ठ|प्रथिष्ठः
प्रथिष्ठ a. Largest, widest,<BR>broadest; (superl. of पृथु q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथीयस्
प्रथीयस् a. (सी f.) Larger, wider,<BR>broader; (compar. of पृथु q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथु|प्रथुः
प्रथु a. Wide, wide-spread.<BR>--थुः<BR>An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथुकः|प्रथुक
प्रथुकः Rice parched and flattened<BR>(cf. पृथुक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रथम|प्रथमः
प्रथम See under प्रथ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदक्षिण|प्रदक्षिणं|प्रदक्षिणः
प्रदक्षिण a.<BR>1 Being placed or<BR>standing on the right, moving to<BR>the right.<BR>--2 Respectful,<BR>reverential.<BR>--3 Auspicious, of good omen.<BR>--णः, --णा, --णं Circumambulation<BR>from left to right, so that the right<BR>side is always turned towards the<BR>person or object circumambulated, a<BR>reverential salutation made by<BR>walking in this manner; Ku. 7. 79;<BR>Y. 1. 232.<BR>--णं ind.<BR>1 From left to<BR>right.<BR>--2 Towards the right side, so<BR>that the right side is always<BR>turned towards the person or object<BR>circumambulated.<BR>--3 In a<BR>southern direction, towards the south;<BR>Ms. 3. 87. (प्रदक्षिणीकृ or प्रदक्षिणयति<BR>Den. P. means ‘to go round from<BR>left to right’ as a mark of respect;<BR>प्रदक्षिणीकुरुष्व सद्योहुताग्नीन् Ś. 4; प्रद<BR>क्षिणीकृत्य हुतं हुताशनं R. 2. 71).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्चिस् a. flaming<BR>towards the right, having the flames<BR>turned towards the right;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">Page0748-b+ 55</a>]<BR>प्रदक्षिणार्चिर्हविरग्निराददे R. 3. 14. (--f.) flames<BR>turned towards the right; R. 4. 25.<BR>--आवर्त, --आवृत्क a. turned towards<BR>the right.<BR>--क्रिया going round from<BR>left to right, keeping the right side<BR>towards one as a mark of<BR>respect; R. 1. 76.<BR>--पट्टिका a yard,<BR>court-yard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदरः|प्रदर
प्रदरः<BR>1 Rending, tearing.<BR>--2 (a)<BR>A fracture, crack, cleft crevice,<BR>chasm; U. 2. 16. (b) Breach,<BR>hole.<BR>--3 The dispersion of an<BR>army.<BR>--4 An arrow.<BR>--5 A kind of<BR>disease of women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्पः|प्रदर्प
प्रदर्पः, प्रदृप्तिः f. Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदृप्तिः|प्रदृप्ति
प्रदर्पः, प्रदृप्तिः f. Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदलः|प्रदल
प्रदलः An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदवः|प्रदव
प्रदवः Burning, inflaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदव्यः|प्रदव्य
प्रदव्यः A forest conflagration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदह्
प्रदह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To burn.<BR>--2 To<BR>consume, destroy completely.<BR>--3 To pain,<BR>torment.<BR>--4 To trouble, tease. --Pass.<BR>To take or catch fire, be burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदग्ध
प्रदग्ध p. p. Burnt up, consumed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदा
प्रदा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To grant, give, offer.<BR>present; स्वं प्रागह प्रादिषि नामराय किं<BR>नाम तस्मै मनसा नराय N. 6. 95;<BR>Ms. 3. 99, 108, 273; Y. 2. 90.<BR>--2 To<BR>impart, teach (as learning);<BR>Bh. 2. 15<BR>--3 To give, give away; yield.<BR>--4 To give up, deliver.<BR>--5 To give<BR>away in marriage.<BR>--6 To sell;<BR>Pt. 1. 13.<BR>--7 To deliver up, restore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद|प्रदः
प्रद a.<BR>1 (At the end of comp.)<BR>Giving, bestowing, or conferring<BR>on, yielding; सुख˚, ताप˚, सस्य˚ &c.<BR>--2 Liberal, bountiful.<BR>--दा A gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदातृ
प्रदातृ m.<BR>1 A giver, donor.<BR>--2 A<BR>liberal man.<BR>--3 One who gives a<BR>daughter in marriage.<BR>--4 An<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदानं|प्रदान
प्रदानं<BR>1 Giving, granting,<BR>bestowing, offering; वर˚, अग्नि˚, काष्ठ˚ &c.<BR>--2 Giving away in marriage;<BR>वैखानसं किमनया<BR>व्रतमाप्रदानाद्व्यापाररोधि भदनस्य निषोवेतव्यं Ś. 1. 27.<BR>--3<BR>Imparting, instructing; विद्या˚.<BR>--4<BR>A gift, donation, present.<BR>--5 A<BR>goad.<BR>--6 An oblation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शूरः a very munificent man, donor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदानकं|प्रदानक
प्रदानकं An offering, a gift,<BR>donation, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदायं|प्रदाय
प्रदायं A present, gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदायिन्
प्रदायिन्, प्रदायक a. Granting,<BR>givin, bestowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदायक
प्रदायिन्, प्रदायक a. Granting,<BR>givin, bestowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिः|प्रदि
प्रदिः, प्रदेयः A present, gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेयः|प्रदेय
प्रदिः, प्रदेयः A present, gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेय|प्रदेयः
प्रदेय a.<BR>1 To be given, imparted,<BR>communicated &c. R. 5. 18, 31.<BR>--2<BR>To be given in marriage; इमे अपि<BR>प्रदेये Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिव्
प्रदिव् a. Ancient, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिश्
प्रदिश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To point out,<BR>indicate, show, assign;<BR>तस्याधिकारपुरुषैः प्रणतैः प्रदिष्टां R. 5. 63; 2. 39.<BR>--2 To tell, mention,<BR>communicate; Bg. 8. 28; Bk. 4. 5.<BR>--3 To<BR>give, grant, offer, bestow or<BR>confer upon; विद्ययोः पथि मुनिप्रदिष्टयोः<BR>R. 11. 9; 7. 35; निःशब्दोऽपि<BR>प्रदिशसि जलं याचितश्चातकेभ्यः Me. 114;<BR>Ms. 8. 265.<BR>--4 To direct, prescribe,<BR>ordain.<BR>--5 To signify, declare, make<BR>known.<BR>--6 To urge on, incite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिश्
प्रदिश् f.<BR>1 Pointing out.<BR>--2 An<BR>order, direction, command.<BR>--3 A<BR>direction, quarter.<BR>--4 An<BR>intermediate point of the compass; such<BR>as नैरृती, आग्नेयी, ऐशानी and वायवी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिष्ट
प्रदिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Shown, pointed<BR>out.<BR>--2 Directed, ordered.<BR>--3<BR>Fixed upon, ordained, appointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशः|प्रदेश
प्रदेशः<BR>1 Pointing out, indicating.<BR>--2 A place, region, spot, country,<BR>territory, district; पितुः प्रदेशास्तव<BR>देवभूमयः Ku. 5. 45; R. 5. 60; so<BR>कंठ˚, तालु˚, हृदय˚, &c.<BR>--3 A span<BR>measured from the tip of the<BR>thumb to that of the fore-finger.<BR>--4 Decision, determination.<BR>--5 A<BR>wall.<BR>--6 An example (in<BR>grammar).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशनं|प्रदेशन
प्रदेशनं<BR>1 Pointing out.<BR>--2 Advice,<BR>instruction.<BR>--3 A gift, present, an<BR>offering, especially to gods,<BR>superiors &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशनी
प्रदेश(शि)नी<BR>1 The fore-finger,<BR>the index finger.<BR>--2 The<BR>corresponding toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेशिनी
प्रदेश(शि)नी<BR>1 The fore-finger,<BR>the index finger.<BR>--2 The<BR>corresponding toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिह्
प्रदिह् {c2c} U. To besmear, daub,<BR>anoint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदिग्ध|प्रदिग्धं
प्रदिग्ध p. p. Besmeared,<BR>bedaubed, anointed.<BR>--ग्धं Meat fried in a<BR>particular way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदेहः|प्रदेह
प्रदेहः<BR>1 Anointing, plastering,<BR>unction.<BR>--2 A plaster, thick<BR>ointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्
प्रदीप् {c4c} A. To blaze, flame forth,<BR>shine brilliantly. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>kindle, inflame.<BR>--2 To excite,<BR>rouse, stimulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपः|प्रदीप
प्रदीपः<BR>1 A lamp, light (fig. also);<BR>अतैलपूराः सरतप्रदीपाः Ku. 1. 10;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">Page0749-a+ 57</a>]<BR>R. 2. 24; 16. 4; कुलप्रदीपो नृपतिर्दिलीपः<BR>R. 6. 74 ‘light or ornament of<BR>the family’; 7. 29.<BR>--2 That which<BR>enlightens or elucidates,<BR>elucidation; especially at the end of titles<BR>of works; as in महाभाष्यप्रदीपः,<BR>काव्यप्रदीपः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0748-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपक
प्रदीपक a.<BR>1 Illuminating.<BR>--2<BR>Explaining, illustrating.<BR>--कः,<BR>--प्रदीपिका A small lamp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीपन|प्रदीपनः
प्रदीपन a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Kindling.<BR>--2<BR>Illuminating.<BR>--3 Stimulating,<BR>exciting.<BR>--नं The act of kindling,<BR>lighting, stimulating &c.<BR>--नः A<BR>kind of mineral poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्त
प्रदीप्त p. p.<BR>1 Kindled, lighted,<BR>inflamed, illuminated.<BR>--2 Blazing,<BR>burning, shining.<BR>--3 Raised,<BR>expanded; प्रदीप्तशिरसमाशीविषं Dk.<BR>--4<BR>Stimulated, excited (hunger &c.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रज्ञ a. of a bright<BR>intellect, sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदीप्तिः|प्रदीप्ति
प्रदीप्तिः f. Lustre, splendour,<BR>brilliancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदुष्
प्रदुष् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To grow worse,<BR>deteriorate.<BR>--2 To be corrupted or<BR>spoiled, be vitiated; Y. 3. 19.<BR>--3<BR>To sin, err, commit an offence against,<BR>be faithless or unchaste; Bg. 1. 41;<BR>Ms. 9. 74; Pt. 4. 57. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>(a) To spoil, corrupt, soil, taint.<BR>(b) To pollute, contaminate, defile.<BR>--2 To blame, censure, find fault<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदुष्ट
प्रदुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Spoiled, corrupted.<BR>--2 Wicked, bad, sinful.<BR>--3<BR>Licentious, wanton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदूषणं|प्रदूषण
प्रदूषणं<BR>1 Corrupting, spoiling.<BR>--2<BR>Polluting, defiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदूषित
प्रदूषित p. p.<BR>1 Corrupted,<BR>vitiated, spoiled, depraved.<BR>--2<BR>Polluted, defiled, contaminated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोष|प्रदोषः
प्रदोष a. Bad, corrupt.<BR>--षः<BR>1 (a)<BR>A fault, defect, sin, offence. (b)<BR>Transgression, violation.<BR>--2<BR>Disordered condition, such as mutiny,<BR>rebellion.<BR>--3 Evening, nightfall,<BR>the first part of the night;<BR>तमःस्वभावास्तेऽप्यन्ये प्रदोषमनुयायिनः Śi. 2. 98<BR>(where प्रदोष primarily means<BR>‘corrupt’ or ‘bad’);<BR>व्रजसुंदरीजनमनस्तोषप्रदोषः Gīt. 5; Ku. 5. 44;<BR>R. 1. 93; Rs. 1. 12.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आगमः<BR>nightfall.<BR>--कालः --समयः --वेला<BR>evening-time, nightfall.<BR>--तिमिरं<BR>evening darkness, the dusk of early<BR>night; कामं प्रदोषतिमिरेण न दृश्यसे त्वं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">Page0749-b+ 58</a>]<BR>Mk. 1. 35.<BR>--रमणीय a. delightful<BR>in the evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोषक|प्रदोषकः
प्रदोषक a. Born in the evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदृश्
प्रदृश् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To see, behold.<BR>--2<BR>To look at, regard.<BR>--3 To foresee.<BR>--4 To observe, perceive, discern.<BR>--5<BR>To be intelligent.<BR>--6 To think,<BR>have an opinion.<BR>--7 To look at,<BR>look upon. --Pass.<BR>1 To become<BR>visible.<BR>--2 To look, appear. --Caus.<BR>1 To show, point out, discover,<BR>exhibit.<BR>--2 To make clear, prove,<BR>demonstrate, explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शः|प्रदर्श
प्रदर्शः<BR>1 Look, appearance.<BR>--2<BR>Direction, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शक|प्रदर्शकः
प्रदर्शक a.<BR>1 Showing,<BR>manifesting, exhibiting.<BR>--2 Foretelling.<BR>--3 Presenting.<BR>--4 Proclaiming.<BR>--5<BR>Teaching, informing, instructing.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A prophet.<BR>--2 A teacher,<BR>instructor.<BR>--3 A doctrine, principle,<BR>precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शनं|प्रदर्शन
प्रदर्शनं<BR>1 Look, appearance; as in<BR>घोरप्रदर्शनः.<BR>--2 Manifesting,<BR>displaying, show, exhibition.<BR>--3 Teaching,<BR>explaining.<BR>--4 An example.<BR>--5<BR>Prophesying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदर्शित|प्रदर्शितः
प्रदर्शित p. p.<BR>1 Shown forth,<BR>exhibited, manifested, evinced,<BR>displayed.<BR>--2 Made known.<BR>--3 Taught.<BR>--4 Explained, declared.<BR>--5 Foretold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रदोहः|प्रदोह
प्रदोहः Milking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युत्
प्रद्युत् {c1c} A. To shine forth.<BR>--Caus. To illumine, irradiate,<BR>light up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युतित
प्रद्युतित a. Illuminated, lighted<BR>up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योतः|प्रद्योत
प्रद्योतः<BR>1 Irradiating, lighting,<BR>illuminating.<BR>--2 Splendour, light,<BR>lustre.<BR>--3 A ray of light.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>a king of Ujjayinī, whose daughter<BR>Vatsa married; प्रद्योतस्य प्रियदुहितरं<BR>वत्सराजोऽत्र जह्ने Me. (considered as<BR>an interpolation by Malli.);<BR>Ratn. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्योतनं|प्रद्योतन|प्रद्योतनः
प्रद्योतनं<BR>1 Blazing, shining.<BR>--2<BR>Light.<BR>--नः The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्युम्नः|प्रद्युम्न
प्रद्युम्नः An epithet of Cupid, the<BR>god of love. [He was a son of Kṛṣṇa<BR>and Rukmiṇī. When only six years<BR>old, he was stolen away by the demon<BR>Śambara, for he was foretold that<BR>Pradyumna would be his destroyer.<BR>Śambara cast the child into the roaring sea,<BR>and a large fish swallowed it. This<BR>fish was caught by a fisherman and<BR>taken to the demon; and when it was<BR>cut up, a beautiful child came out from<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">Page0749-c+ 59</a>]<BR>the belly, and Māyāvatī, the<BR>mistress of Śambara's household, at the<BR>desire of Nārada, carefully reared him<BR>from childhood. As he grew up, she<BR>was fascinated by the beauty of his<BR>person, but Pradyumna reproved her for<BR>entertaining towards himself feelings so<BR>unbecoming a mother as he considered<BR>her. But when he was told that he was<BR>not her son, but of Viṣṇu and was cast<BR>into the sea by Śambara, he became<BR>enraged, and challenging him to fight,<BR>succeeded in killing him by the force of<BR>illusions. He and Māyāvatī afterwards<BR>repaired to the house of Kṛṣṇa, where<BR>Nārada told him and Rukmini that the<BR>boy was their own and that Māyāvatī<BR>was his wife].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्राणक
प्रद्राणक a. Sorely distressed,<BR>hard pressed, indigent, poor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्रु
प्रद्रु {c1c} P.<BR>1 To run, run away,<BR>retreat or fly to (with acc. or abl.)<BR>रणात्प्रद्रवंति बलानि Ve. 4;<BR>Bk. 15. 79.<BR>--2 To hasten away, rush<BR>towards.<BR>--3 To assail, fall upon,<BR>attack.<BR>--4 To attain. --Caus. To put<BR>to flight, rout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्रव|प्रद्रवः
प्रद्रव a. Fluid, liquid.<BR>--वः<BR>Running.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्रावः|प्रद्राव
प्रद्रावः<BR>1 Running away, flight,<BR>retreat, escape.<BR>--2 Going quickly or<BR>fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्राविन्
प्रद्राविन् a.<BR>1 Running away;<BR>fugitive.<BR>--2 Retreating, flying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वार्
प्रद्वार्, प्रद्वारं A place before a<BR>door or gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वारं|प्रद्वार
प्रद्वार्, प्रद्वारं A place before a<BR>door or gate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विष्
प्रद्विष् {c2c} U. To hate, dislike.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विष्
प्रद्विष्, प्राद्विषत्, a.<BR>1 Hating,<BR>disliking.<BR>--2 Hestile or opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्विषत्
प्रद्विष्, प्राद्विषत्, a.<BR>1 Hating,<BR>disliking.<BR>--2 Hestile or opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वेषः|प्रद्वेष
प्रद्वेषः, प्रद्वेषणं Dislike, hatred,<BR>aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रद्वेषणं|प्रद्वेषण
प्रद्वेषः, प्रद्वेषणं Dislike, hatred,<BR>aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधनं|प्रधन
प्रधनं<BR>1 A battle, fight, war,<BR>contest; प्रहितः प्रधनाय<BR>माधवानहमाकारयितुं महीभृता Śi. 16. 52; क्षेत्रं<BR>क्षत्रप्रधनपिशुनं कौरवं तद्भजेथाः Me. 48;<BR>R. 11. 77; Mv. 6. 33; U. 5. 1.<BR>--2 Spoil taken in battle.<BR>--3<BR>Destruction.<BR>--4 Tearing, rending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधमनं|प्रधमन
प्रधमनं<BR>1 Blowing in or into.<BR>--2<BR>A sternutatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधान|प्रधानं|प्रधानः
प्रधान a.<BR>1 Chief, principal,<BR>preeminent, main, best, most<BR>excellent; as in प्रधानामात्य, प्रधानपुरुष &c.<BR>Me. 7. 203.<BR>--2 Principally<BR>inherent, prevalent, predominant.<BR>--नं<BR>1 The chief thing or object,<BR>most important thing; head, chief;<BR>न परिचयो मलिनात्मनां प्रधानं Śi. 7. 61;<BR>G. L. 18; प्रयोगप्रधानं हि नाट्यशास्त्र<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-a" target="_blank">Page0750-a+ 58</a>]<BR>M. 1; शमप्रधानेषु तपोधनेषु Ś. 2. 7;<BR>गुणैश्च तैस्तैर्विनयप्रधानैः R. 6. 79.<BR>--2<BR>The first evolver, originator, or<BR>source of the material world, the<BR>primary germ out of which all<BR>material appearances are evolved,<BR>according to the Sāṃkhya<BR>philosophy; न पुनरपि प्रधानवादी अशब्दत्वं<BR>प्रधानस्यासिद्धमित्याह S. B; see प्रकृति<BR>also.<BR>--3 The Supreme Spirit.<BR>--4<BR>Intellect.<BR>--5 The principal<BR>member of a compound.<BR>--नः, --नं<BR>1 The<BR>principal attendant or companion<BR>of a king (his minister or<BR>confidant).<BR>--2 A noble, courtier.<BR>--3<BR>An elephant-driver.<BR>--4 The<BR>commander-in-chief.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं {1}<BR>the principal branch or part of<BR>anything. {2} the chief member<BR>of the body. {3} the principal or<BR>most eminent person in a state.<BR>--अमात्यः the prime-minister,<BR>premier.<BR>--आत्मन् m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--उत्तम a. {1} eminent, most<BR>illustrious. {2} warlike, brave.<BR>--कर्मन्<BR>n., कार्यं {1} the chief business. {2}<BR>(Medic.) the principal mode of<BR>treatment.<BR>--धातुः the chief element of the<BR>body; i. e. semen virile.<BR>--पुरुषः<BR>{1} the principal or most eminent<BR>person (in a state &c.);<BR>Pt. 3. 138. {2} an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--भाज्<BR>a. {1} most distinguished. {2}<BR>receiving the chief share.<BR>--मंत्रिन् m.<BR>the prime-minister.<BR>--वासस् n. a<BR>principal garment. (du.) the two<BR>chief garments.<BR>--वृष्टिः f. a heavy<BR>shower of rain.<BR>--शिष्ट a. taught<BR>or prescribed as of primary<BR>importance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0749-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानक
प्रधानक a. Chief, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानता
प्रधानता --त्वं = प्राधान्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधानत्वं|प्रधानत्व
प्रधानता --त्वं = प्राधान्य q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधाव्
प्रधाव् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To run forward,<BR>run away.<BR>--2 To set out, start.<BR>--3<BR>To become spread or diffused.<BR>--4<BR>To wash, cleanse.<BR>--5 To rub off,<BR>wipe out. --Caus. To cause to run<BR>away, drive away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधावनः|प्रधावन
प्रधावनः Air, wind.<BR>--नं<BR>Rubbing, rubbing or washing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधिः|प्रधि
प्रधिः<BR>1 The periphery of a<BR>wheel; Śi. 15. 79; 17. 27.<BR>--2<BR>A well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधी
प्रधी a. Pre-eminently intelligent.<BR>--f. Great intelligence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधूपित
प्रधूपित p. p.<BR>1 Fumigated,<BR>perfumed.<BR>--2 Heated, burned.<BR>--3<BR>Inflamed.<BR>--4 Afflicted, distressed.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">Page0750-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--ता<BR>1 A woman in trouble.<BR>--2 The<BR>quarter to which the sun proceeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधृ
प्रधृ {c10c} U. or Caus.<BR>1 To place<BR>or fix upon.<BR>--2 To direct the mind<BR>towards, determine, resolve.<BR>--3 To<BR>bear or keep in mind.<BR>--4 To think,<BR>consider, reflect.<BR>--5 To chastise,<BR>punish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधारण
प्रधारण a. (णी f.) Preserving,<BR>keeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधृष्
प्रधृष् {c5c} P.<BR>1 To assail, lay hands<BR>on.<BR>--2 To injure, harass.<BR>--3 To<BR>overpower overcome. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To assail, attack; overpower.<BR>--2<BR>To outrage, violate (a woman).<BR>--3<BR>To injure, hurt.<BR>--4 To devastate,<BR>lay waste, destroy completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षः|प्रधर्ष
प्रधर्षः<BR>1 Assaulting, attacking;<BR>an attack, assault.<BR>--2 Violation,<BR>outrage.<BR>--3 Ill-treatment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षक
प्रधर्षक a.<BR>1 Attacking, assailing.<BR>--2 Troubling, harassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षणं|प्रधर्षण
प्रधर्षणं --णा<BR>1 An assault, attack.<BR>--2<BR>An outrage, ill-treatment, insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षणा
प्रधर्षणं --णा<BR>1 An assault, attack.<BR>--2<BR>An outrage, ill-treatment, insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधर्षित
प्रधर्षित p. p.<BR>1 Assaulted,<BR>attacked.<BR>--2 Hurt, injured.<BR>--3 Haughty,<BR>arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रधृष्ट
प्रधृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Treated with<BR>contumely.<BR>--2 Proud, arrogant, haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्मा
प्रध्मा {c1c} P.<BR>1 To blow (as a conch);<BR>शंखौ प्रदध्मतुः Bg. 1. 14.<BR>--2 To blow<BR>away or into.<BR>--3 To destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्मापनं|प्रध्मापन
प्रध्मापनं A remedy for assisting<BR>respiration in any obstruction of the<BR>air-passages.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्यानं|प्रध्यान
प्रध्यानं<BR>1 Deep thought or<BR>reflection.<BR>--2 Reflection or thought in<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंस्
प्रध्वंस् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To fall in ruins,<BR>waste, decay.<BR>--2 To perish, be<BR>destroyed, --Caus. To cause to perish,<BR>destroy, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसः|प्रध्वंस
प्रध्वंसः Utter destruction,<BR>annihilation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभावः<BR>‘nonexistence caused by destruction’,<BR>one of the four kinds of अभाव or<BR>nonexistence, in which the<BR>non-existence of a thing is caused by<BR>destruction, as of an effect subsequently to<BR>its production.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसनः|प्रध्वंसन
प्रध्वंसनः Ved. A destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वंसिन्
प्रध्वंसिन् a.<BR>1 Transitory,<BR>perishable.<BR>--2 Destroying, annihilating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रध्वस्त
प्रध्वस्त p. p. Annihilated,<BR>completely destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनप्तृ
प्रनप्तृ m. The son of a grandson<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">Page0750-c+ 55</a>]<BR>a great-grand-son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनष्ट|प्रनष्टः
प्रनष्ट See under प्रणश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनायक
प्रनायक a.<BR>1 One whose leader<BR>is away.<BR>--2 Destitute of a leader<BR>or guide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनालः|प्रनाल
प्रनालः --ली f. See प्रणाल and प्रणाली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनाली
प्रनालः --ली f. See प्रणाल and प्रणाली<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनिघातनं|प्रनिघातन
प्रनिघातनं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनृत्
प्रनृत् {c4c} P. To dance. --Caus. To<BR>shake, cause to dance, set in motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनर्तित|प्रनर्त्तित
प्रनर्तित p. p.<BR>1 Set in motion,<BR>shaken.<BR>--2 Dandled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रनृत्त
प्रनृत्त a. Dancing.<BR>--त्तं A dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपक्षः|प्रपक्ष
प्रपक्षः The extremity of a wing<BR>(as of an army).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपंचः|प्रपञ्च|प्रपंच|प्रपञ्चः
प्रपंचः<BR>1 Display, manifestation;<BR>रागप्रायः प्रपंचः K. 151.<BR>--2<BR>Development, expansion, extension;<BR>Śi. 20. 44.<BR>--3 Amplification, expatiation,<BR>explanation, elucidation.<BR>--4<BR>Prolixity, diffuseness, copiousness; अलं<BR>प्रपंचेन.<BR>--5 Manifoldness, diversity.<BR>--6 Heap, abundance, quantity.<BR>--7<BR>An appearance, phenomenon.<BR>--8<BR>Illusion, fraud.<BR>--9 The visible world<BR>or universe, which is illusory and<BR>the scene of manifold action.<BR>--10<BR>Reciprocal false praise.<BR>--11<BR>Opposition, inversion.<BR>--12 Analysis.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बुद्धि a. cunning,<BR>deceitful.<BR>--वचनं a prolix discourse,<BR>diffuse talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपंचक|प्रपञ्चक
प्रपंचक a.<BR>1 Displaying, showing.<BR>--2 Developing.<BR>--3 Explaining fully,<BR>amplifying, expounding in detail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपंचनं|प्रपञ्चन|प्रपंचन
प्रपंचनं<BR>1 Display, development.<BR>--2 Copious exposition, detailed<BR>explanation or amplification.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपंचयति
प्रपंचयति Den. P.<BR>1 To show forth,<BR>display; प्रपंचय पंचमं Gīt. 10.<BR>--2<BR>To expand, amplify, explain in<BR>detail, dwell or dilate upon, treat at<BR>length.<BR>--3 To cause to appear in a<BR>false light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपंचित|प्रपञ्चित|प्रपञ्चितं
प्रपंचित p. p.<BR>1 Displayed.<BR>--2<BR>Expanded, amplified.<BR>--3 Dilated upon,<BR>fully explained, expatiated upon.<BR>--4 Erring, mistaken.<BR>--5 Deceived,<BR>tricked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपठ्
प्रपठ् {c1c} P. To repeat aloud.<BR>--Caus. To teach, explain,<BR>expound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाठकः|प्रपाठक
प्रपाठकः<BR>1 A lesson, lecture.<BR>--2 A<BR>chapter or subdivision of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपणः|प्रपण
प्रपणः Ved. Barter, exchange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपत्
प्रपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fly forth or away.,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-a" target="_blank">Page0751-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--2 To fly, fly or move about.<BR>--3 To<BR>fall down or upon, throw oneself<BR>down.<BR>--4 To hasten towards.<BR>--5 To<BR>be deprived of, fall from, lose,<BR>fall off or away from.<BR>--6 To come<BR>down, fall down, descend. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To throw down.<BR>--2 To rout, put to<BR>flight.<BR>--3 To chase, pursue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0750-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपतनं|प्रपतन
प्रपतनं<BR>1 Flying forth or away.<BR>--2<BR>Throwing oneself into, falling down.<BR>--3 Alighting.<BR>--4 Death,<BR>destruction.<BR>--5 A precipice, a steep crag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपतित
प्रपतित a.<BR>1 Flown away.<BR>--2<BR>Fallen, come down.<BR>--3 Decayed,<BR>wasted.<BR>--4 Dead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपातः|प्रपात
प्रपातः<BR>1 Going forth or away,<BR>departure.<BR>--2 Falling down or into, a<BR>fall; मनोरथानामतटप्रपातः Ś. 6. 9;<BR>Ku. 6. 57.<BR>--3 A sudden attack.<BR>--4 A<BR>cascade, waterfall, the place over<BR>which water falls down; R. 2. 26.<BR>--5 A bank, shore.<BR>--6 A precipice,<BR>steep rock.<BR>--7 Falling out or loss,<BR>as in केशप्रपात.<BR>--8 Emission,<BR>discharge, efflux, as in वीर्यप्रपात.<BR>--9<BR>Throwing oneself down from a rock.<BR>--10 A particular mode of flight.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंबु n. water falling from<BR>a rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपातनं|प्रपातन
प्रपातनं Causing to fall, throwing<BR>down (on the ground).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपातिन्
प्रपातिन् m. A precipitous mountain,<BR>cliff.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपथ|प्रपथः
प्रपथ a. Ved.<BR>1 Loose, relaxed.<BR>--2 Languid, enervated.<BR>--थः<BR>1 A long<BR>journey, a journey to a distant<BR>place.<BR>--2 A remote place.<BR>--3 A broad<BR>street.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपथ्य
प्रपथ्य a. Ved.<BR>1 Being in or on<BR>the road.<BR>--2 An epithet of Pūṣan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपद्
प्रपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To enter upon, set<BR>forward, set foot in.<BR>--2 (a) To go<BR>to or towards, approach, resort or<BR>attain to, reach; तां जन्मने शैलवधूं प्रपेदे<BR>Ku. 1. 21; (क्षितीशं) कौत्सः प्रपेदे<BR>वरतंतुशिष्यः R. 5. 1; Bk. 4. 1;<BR>Ki. 1. 9; 11. 16; R. 8. 11. (b) To take<BR>shelter or refuge with, flee to for<BR>safety, submit; शरणार्थमन्यां कथं<BR>प्रपत्स्ये त्वयि दीप्यमाने R. 14. 64.<BR>--3 To<BR>go or come to a particular state,<BR>arrive at, attain to, arrive at or be<BR>in a particular condition; रेणुः प्रपेदे<BR>पथि पंकभावं R. 16. 30;<BR>मुहूर्तकर्णोत्पलतां प्रपेदे Ku. 7. 81; बाल्यात्परं साथ<BR>वयः प्रपेदे Ku. 1. 31; 5. 24;<BR>ईदृशीमवस्थां प्रपन्नोस्मि Ś. 5: ऋषिनिकरौरिति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">Page0751-b+ 55</a>]<BR>संशयः प्रपेदे Bv. 4. 33; Amaru. 27.<BR>--4 To get, find, secure, obtain,<BR>attain to; partake of share in;<BR>सहकार न प्रपेदे मधुपेन भवत्समं जगति<BR>Bv. 1. 21; कांतं वपुर्व्योमचरं प्रपेदे R. 5. 51.<BR>--5 To behave or act towards, deal<BR>with; किं प्रपद्यते वैदर्भः M. 1 ‘what<BR>does he propose to do’; पश्यामो मयि<BR>किं प्रपद्यते Amaru. 20.<BR>--6 To admit,<BR>allow, agree or consent to;<BR>Y. 2. 40.<BR>--7 To draw near, come on,<BR>approach (as time &c.).<BR>--8 To be<BR>going on, to proceed.<BR>--9 To take effect,<BR>thrive, prosper.<BR>--10 To throw<BR>oneself down, fall down (at another's<BR>feet).<BR>--11 Ved. To attack, assault.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपदं|प्रपद
प्रपदं<BR>1 The forepart of the foot.<BR>--2 Tip of the toe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपदनं|प्रपदन
प्रपदनं Entrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपदीन
प्रपदीन a. Relating or extending to<BR>the forepart of the foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपन्न|प्रपन्नः
प्रपन्न p. p.<BR>1 Arriving at,<BR>reaching or going to.<BR>--2 Resorting to,<BR>betaking oneself to; इयं प्रपन्ना तपसे<BR>तपोवनं Ku. 5. 59; 3. 5.<BR>--3 Taking<BR>refuge with, seeking protection with,<BR>suppliant or submissive to; शिष्यस्तेहं<BR>शाधि मां त्वां प्रपन्नं Bg. 2. 7.<BR>--4 Adhering<BR>to.<BR>--5 Furnished or endowed with,<BR>possessed of; प्रत्यक्षाभिः प्रपन्नस्तुनुभिः<BR>Ś. 1. 1.<BR>--6 Promised.<BR>--7 Got,<BR>obtained.<BR>--8 Poor, distressed.<BR>--9 Effecting,<BR>producing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पालः an<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपादः|प्रपाद
प्रपादः Ved. Miscarriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपन्नाडः|प्रपन्नाड
प्रपन्नाडः See प्रपुनाट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपर्ण
प्रपर्ण a. Devoid of leaves (as a<BR>tree; प्रपतितानि पर्णानि यस्य).<BR>--र्णं<BR>A fallen leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायनं|प्रपलायन
प्रपलायनं Flight, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायित
प्रपलायित a.<BR>1 Run away.<BR>--2<BR>Routed, defeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपलायिन्
प्रपलायिन् a.<BR>1 Flying, escaping.<BR>--2 A fugitive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपा
प्रपा<BR>1 A place where water is<BR>distributed to travellers;<BR>व्याख्यास्थानान्यमलसलिला यस्य कूपाः प्रपाश्च<BR>Vikr. 18. 78.<BR>--2 A well, cistern;<BR>Ms. 8. 319.<BR>--3 A place for watering<BR>cattle.<BR>--4 A supply of water.<BR>--5 A<BR>draught.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पालिका a woman<BR>who distributes water to travellers;<BR>Vikr. 1. 89; 13. 10.<BR>--वनं a cool grove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाकः|प्रपाक
प्रपाकः<BR>1 Ripening(of a boil<BR>&c.).<BR>--2 Inflammation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाणिः|प्रपाणि
प्रपाणिः<BR>1 The forepart of the<BR>hand.<BR>--2 The palm of the extended<BR>hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपाथः|प्रपाथ
प्रपाथः A road, way.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपादिकः|प्रपादिक
प्रपादिकः A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपानं|प्रपान
प्रपानं<BR>1 Drinking.<BR>--2 The<BR>underpart of a horse's upper lip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपानकं|प्रपानक
प्रपानकं A kind of drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपालनं|प्रपालन
प्रपालनं Protecting, guarding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपालिन्
प्रपालिन् m. An epithet of<BR>Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपितामहः|प्रपितामह
प्रपितामहः<BR>1 A paternal<BR>greatgrandfather.<BR>--2 An epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa; Bg. 11. 39.<BR>--3 Of Brahman.<BR>--4 Of the Supreme spirit.<BR>--ही A<BR>paternal great-grandmother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपितृव्यः|प्रपितृव्य
प्रपितृव्यः A paternal grand-uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीड्
प्रपीड् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To press, squeeze.<BR>--2 To torture, torment, harass,<BR>afflict.<BR>--3 To check, suppress, restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीडनं|प्रपीडन
प्रपीडनं<BR>1 Pressing, squeezing.<BR>--2<BR>An astringent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीत
प्रपीत(न) a. Swollen up,<BR>distended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपीन
प्रपीत(न) a. Swollen up,<BR>distended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुत्रः|प्रपुत्र
प्रपुत्रः A grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुनाटः|प्रपुनाट
प्रपुना(न्ना)टः --डः N. of a<BR>tree (चक्रमर्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्नाटः|प्रपुन्नाट
प्रपुना(न्ना)टः --डः N. of a<BR>tree (चक्रमर्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुनाडः|प्रपुनाड
प्रपुना(न्ना)टः --डः N. of a<BR>tree (चक्रमर्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुन्नाडः|प्रपुन्नाड|प्रपुंनाड
प्रपुना(न्ना)टः --डः N. of a<BR>tree (चक्रमर्द).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूर्वगः|प्रपूर्वग
प्रपूर्वगः<BR>1 The Supreme being.<BR>--2 N. of the two Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपुष्पित
प्रपुष्पित a. Flowering, blooming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपृष्ठ
प्रपृष्ठ a. Having a prominent<BR>back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपॄ
प्रपॄ {c9c} P. To fill up, complete.<BR>--Pass. To be filled or completed;<BR>be fulfilled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरक
प्रपूरक a. Fulfilling, satisfying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरणं|प्रपूरण
प्रपूरणं<BR>1 Filling, filling up,<BR>completing.<BR>--2 Inserting, injecting.<BR>--3<BR>Satisfying; satiating.<BR>--4 Attaching<BR>to, affixing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपूरित
प्रपूरित p. p. Filled up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रपौत्रः|प्रपौत्र
प्रपौत्रः A great-grandson;<BR>Y. 1. 78.<BR>--त्री A great-grand-daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रप्यायनं|प्रप्यायन
प्रप्यायनं Swelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफर्वी
प्रफर्वी Ved. A woman having<BR>excellent hips or going in a graceful<BR>way; a lewd girl (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्त
प्रफुल्त p. p. Blooming,<BR>bloossomed, full-blown; लोध्रद्रुमं सानुमतः प्र<BR>फुल्तं R. 2. 29. (v. l. for प्रफुल्ल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्तिः|प्रफुल्ति
प्रफुल्तिः f. Blooming, expansion,<BR>blossoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0751-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रफुल्ल|प्रफुल्लः
प्रफुल्ल p. p.<BR>1 Full-blown,<BR>blossoming, blooming; न हि प्रफुल्लं सहकारमेत्य<BR>वृक्षांतरं काक्षति षट्पदाली R. 6. 69;<BR>2. 29; Ku. 3. 45; 7. 11.<BR>--2<BR>Expanded or dilated like a full-blown<BR>flower (as eyes).<BR>--3 Smiling.<BR>--4<BR>Shining.<BR>--5 Gay, cheerful, pleased.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नयन, --नेत्र, --लोचन a. with<BR>eyes expanded with joy.<BR>--वदन a.<BR>having a beaming or cheerful<BR>countenance, looking cheerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबंध्|प्रबन्ध्
प्रबंध् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To bind on, tie,<BR>fasten.<BR>--2 To stop, suppress, check.<BR>--3 To compose, put together, arrange.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबद्ध
प्रबद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Bound, tied,<BR>fastened.<BR>--2 Stopped, obstructed, checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबंद्धृ|प्रबन्द्धृ
प्रबंद्धृ m. An author.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबंधः|प्रबन्ध|प्रबंध|प्रबन्धः
प्रबंधः<BR>1 A bond, tie.<BR>--2<BR>Uninterruptedness, continuance,<BR>continuity, uninterrupted series or<BR>succession; विच्छेदमाप भुवि यस्तु कथाप्रबंधः<BR>K. 239; क्रियाप्रबंधादयमध्वराणां<BR>R. 6. 23; 3. 58; Māl. 6. 3.<BR>--3 A<BR>continued or connected narrative or<BR>discourse; अनुज्झितार्थसंबंधः प्रबंधो<BR>दुरुदाहरः Śi. 2. 73.<BR>--4 Any literary<BR>work or composition; प्रथितयशसां<BR>भासकविसौमिल्ल कविमिश्रादीनां<BR>प्रबंधानतिक्रम्य M. 1; प्रत्यक्षरश्लेषमयप्रबंध &c. Vās.<BR>--5 Arrangement, plan, scheme; as<BR>in कपटप्रबंधः<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः the<BR>subject matter of a composition or<BR>treatise.<BR>--कल्पना a feigned story,<BR>a work of imagination founded on<BR>a substratum of fact, प्रबंधकल्पनां<BR>स्तोकसत्यां प्राज्ञाः कथां विदुः.<BR>--वर्षः<BR>continuous or incessant rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबंधनं|प्रबन्धन|प्रबंधन
प्रबंधनं Bond, tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबभ्रः|प्रबभ्र
प्रबभ्रः An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबर्ह
प्रब(व)र्ह a. Most excellent,<BR>best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ह|प्रवर्हः
प्रब(व)र्ह a. Most excellent,<BR>best.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबल|प्रबलः
प्रबल a.<BR>1 Very strong or<BR>powerful, mighty, valorous (as a man);<BR>R. 3. 60; Rs. 3. 23.<BR>--2 Violent,<BR>strong, intense, excessive, very<BR>great; प्रबलतमसामेवं प्रायाः शुभेषु हि<BR>वृत्तयः Ś. 7. 24, प्रबलपुरोवातया वृष्ट्या<BR>M. 4. 2; प्रबलां वेदनां R. 8. 50.<BR>--3<BR>Important.<BR>--4 Abounding with.<BR>--5<BR>Dangerous, destructive.<BR>--लः<BR>1 N. of<BR>a Daitya.<BR>--2 A sprout (पल्लव).<BR>--लं<BR>ind. Exceedingly, much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबलति
प्रबलति Den. P. To become<BR>strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाध्
प्रबाध्^1 {c1c} A.<BR>1 To press hard upon,<BR>oppress.<BR>--2 To trouble, torment,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">Page0752-b+ 56</a>]<BR>harass, tease, hurt; समुच्छ्रितानेव<BR>तरून् प्रबाधते (प्रभंजनः) H. 1;<BR>Bk. 12. 2.<BR>--3 To drive away, remove, get<BR>over; कथं च दैवं शक्येत पौरुषेण<BR>प्रबाधितुं Mb.<BR>--4 To throw down,<BR>destroy.<BR>--5 To repel, repulse.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: prefix of root bAD.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाधक
प्रबाधक a.<BR>1 Repelling, repulsive.<BR>--2 Harassing, oppressive.<BR>--3<BR>Keeping off or back.<BR>--4 Refusing,<BR>rejecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाधनं|प्रबाधन
प्रबाधनं<BR>1 Oppressing, tormenting.<BR>--2 Refusing, denying.<BR>--3 Keeping<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाधित
प्रबाधित a.<BR>1 Molested, troubled,<BR>oppressed.<BR>--2 Pressed forward,<BR>driven onward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबह्लिका
प्रब(व)ह्लिका See प्रहेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लिका
प्रब(व)ह्लिका See प्रहेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालः|प्रबाल|प्रबालं
प्रबा(वा)लः --लं<BR>1 A sprout,<BR>shoot, new leaf; अपि…<BR>प्रवालमासामनुबंधि बीरुधां Ku. 5. 34; 1. 44; 3. 8;<BR>R. 6. 12; 13. 49.<BR>--2 Coral.<BR>--3 The<BR>neck of the Indian lute.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A<BR>pupil.<BR>--2 An animal.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्मंतकः {1} the red Aśmantaka tree.<BR>{2} the coral tree.<BR>--पद्मं a red<BR>lotus.<BR>--फलं red sandal-wood.<BR>--भस्मन्<BR>n. calx of coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवालः|प्रवाल|प्रवालं
प्रबा(वा)लः --लं<BR>1 A sprout,<BR>shoot, new leaf; अपि…<BR>प्रवालमासामनुबंधि बीरुधां Ku. 5. 34; 1. 44; 3. 8;<BR>R. 6. 12; 13. 49.<BR>--2 Coral.<BR>--3 The<BR>neck of the Indian lute.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A<BR>pupil.<BR>--2 An animal.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्मंतकः {1} the red Aśmantaka tree.<BR>{2} the coral tree.<BR>--पद्मं a red<BR>lotus.<BR>--फलं red sandal-wood.<BR>--भस्मन्<BR>n. calx of coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबालं|प्रबाल|प्रबालः
प्रबा(वा)लः --लं<BR>1 A sprout,<BR>shoot, new leaf; अपि…<BR>प्रवालमासामनुबंधि बीरुधां Ku. 5. 34; 1. 44; 3. 8;<BR>R. 6. 12; 13. 49.<BR>--2 Coral.<BR>--3 The<BR>neck of the Indian lute.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A<BR>pupil.<BR>--2 An animal.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्मंतकः {1} the red Aśmantaka tree.<BR>{2} the coral tree.<BR>--पद्मं a red<BR>lotus.<BR>--फलं red sandal-wood.<BR>--भस्मन्<BR>n. calx of coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवालं|प्रवाल|प्रवालः
प्रबा(वा)लः --लं<BR>1 A sprout,<BR>shoot, new leaf; अपि…<BR>प्रवालमासामनुबंधि बीरुधां Ku. 5. 34; 1. 44; 3. 8;<BR>R. 6. 12; 13. 49.<BR>--2 Coral.<BR>--3 The<BR>neck of the Indian lute.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A<BR>pupil.<BR>--2 An animal.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्मंतकः {1} the red Aśmantaka tree.<BR>{2} the coral tree.<BR>--पद्मं a red<BR>lotus.<BR>--फलं red sandal-wood.<BR>--भस्मन्<BR>n. calx of coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाहुः|प्रबाहु
प्रबाहुः The fore-arm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाहुक्
प्रबाहुक् ind.<BR>1 In an even line,<BR>to an equal height.<BR>--2 At the same<BR>time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबाहुकं|प्रबाहुक
प्रबाहुकं ind.<BR>1 On high.<BR>--2 At<BR>the same time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबुध्
प्रबुध् {c4c} A., {c1c} P.<BR>1 To awake,<BR>wake up, rise from sleep; प्रबुद्ध इव<BR>सुप्तं Ś. 5. 11; Śi. 9. 30.<BR>--2 To blow,<BR>expand, bloom, be blown; साभ्रेऽह्नीव<BR>स्थलकमलिनीं न प्रबुद्धां न सुप्तां Me. 90.<BR>--3 To perceive, observe, be aware<BR>of. --Caus.<BR>1 To awaken, waken,<BR>rouse; प्राबोधयन्नुषसि वाग्भिरुदारवाचः<BR>R. 5. 65; 6. 56.<BR>--2 To acquaint with,<BR>inform, make known; तमभ्यनंदत्प्रथमं<BR>प्रबोधितः R. 3. 68.<BR>--3 To cause to<BR>expand or open; (पद्मानि)<BR>प्रबोधयत्यूर्ध्वमुखैर्मयूखैः Ku. 1. 16.<BR>--4 To instruct,<BR>teach; explain.<BR>--5 To persuade,<BR>induce.<BR>--6 To stimulate, excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबुद्ध|प्रबुद्धः
प्रबुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Awakened, roused.<BR>--2 Wise, learned, clever; Pt. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Knowing, conversant with.<BR>--4<BR>Full-blown, expanded.<BR>--5<BR>Beginning to work or take effect (as a<BR>charm).<BR>--6 Enlivened, lively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबुधः|प्रबुध
प्रबुधः A great sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधः|प्रबोध
प्रबोधः<BR>1 Awaking(fig. also),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">Page0752-c+ 55</a>]<BR>awakening; regaining one's<BR>consciousness, consciousness; अप्रबोधाय सुष्वाप<BR>R. 12. 50; मोहाद्भूत्कष्टतरः प्रबोधः 14. 56.<BR>--2 Blowing, expanding (of flowers).<BR>--3 Wakefulness, sleeplessness;<BR>चिरप्रबोधान्न संभावितं धर्मासनमध्यासितुं<BR>Ś. 6.<BR>--4 Vigilance, watchfulness.<BR>--5<BR>Knowledge, understanding, wisdom,<BR>removal of delusion, real<BR>knowledge; as in प्रबोधचंद्रोदय; R. 5. 65.<BR>--6 Consolation.<BR>--7 Reviving the<BR>fragrance of a perfume.<BR>--8<BR>Explaining.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्सवः N. of a<BR>festival observed from the tenth to<BR>the day of full-moon in the month<BR>of Kārtika.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधकः|प्रबोधक
प्रबोधकः A minstrel whose duty<BR>it is to wake the king, bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधन|प्रबोधनं
प्रबोधन a. (नी f.) Awakening,<BR>rousing.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Waking.<BR>--2<BR>Awakening, rousing.<BR>--3 Regaining one's<BR>consciousness; recovery of senses;<BR>U. 6. 41.<BR>--4 Knowledge, wisdom.<BR>--5 Instructing, advising.<BR>--6<BR>Reviving the scent of a perfume.<BR>--7<BR>Refinement, enlightenment; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधनी
प्रबोध(धि)नी The eleventh day<BR>of the bright half of Kārtika on<BR>which Viṣṇu awakes from his four<BR>months' sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधिनी
प्रबोध(धि)नी The eleventh day<BR>of the bright half of Kārtika on<BR>which Viṣṇu awakes from his four<BR>months' sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रबोधित
प्रबोधित p. p.<BR>1 Awakened,<BR>roused.<BR>--2 Instructed, informed, taught,<BR>acquainted with.<BR>--3 Convinced,<BR>persuaded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रब्रू
प्रब्रू {c2c} P.<BR>1 To proclaim, announce.<BR>--2 To exclaim, shout.<BR>--3 To say,<BR>speak, tell; Bk. 8. 85.<BR>--4 To praise,<BR>laud.<BR>--5 To read before.<BR>--6 To<BR>describe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभंज्|प्रभञ्ज्
प्रभंज् {c7c} P.<BR>1 To break down,<BR>shatter.<BR>--2 To stop, arrest, suspend.<BR>--3 To frustrate, disappoint.<BR>--4 To<BR>defeat, conquer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभंगः|प्रभङ्ग|प्रभङ्गः
प्रभंगः<BR>1 Breaking, crushing.<BR>--2<BR>Destruction; complete defeat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभंजनं|प्रभञ्जन|प्रभंजन|प्रभञ्जनः
प्रभंजनं Breaking to pieces.<BR>--नः<BR>Wind, especially, stormy wind,<BR>hurricane; N. 1. 67; Pt. 1. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभद्रः|प्रभद्र
प्रभद्रः The Nimba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभा
प्रभा {c2c} P.<BR>1 To appear, seem.<BR>--2<BR>To shine forth, gleam.<BR>--3 To begin<BR>to become light, begin to dawn;<BR>ननु प्रभाता रजनी Ś. 4; प्रभातकल्पा<BR>शशिनेव शर्वरी R. 3. 2.<BR>--4 To<BR>illuminate, enlighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0752-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभा
प्रभा<BR>1 Light, splendour, lustre,<BR>effulgence, radiance; प्रभास्मि<BR>शशिसूर्थयोः Bg. 7. 8; प्रभा पतंगस्य<BR>R. 2. 15, 31; 6. 18; Rs. 1. 20; Me. 47.<BR>--2 A ray of light.<BR>--3 The shadow<BR>of the sun on a sun-dial.<BR>--4 An<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR>--5 N. of the city of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--6 N. of an Apsaras.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः {1} the sun;<BR>R. 10. 74. {2} the moon. {3} fire. {4} the<BR>ocean. {5} an epithet of Śiva. {6} N.<BR>of a learned writer, the founder of a<BR>school of Mīmāṃsā philosophy<BR>called after him.<BR>--कीटः a fire-fly.<BR>--तरल a. tremulously radiant, न<BR>प्रभातरलं ज्योतिरुदेति वसुधातलात् Ś. 1. 26.<BR>--पल्लवित a. overspread or glowing<BR>with lustre; V. 5. 3.<BR>--प्ररोहः a ray or<BR>flash of light.<BR>--मंडलं a circle or halo<BR>of light; स्फुरत्प्रभांमडलया च काशे<BR>Ku. 1. 24; 6. 4; R. 3. 60; 14. 14.<BR>--लेपिन् a. covered with lustre, emitting<BR>lustre; V. 4. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभात|प्रभातं
प्रभात p. p. Begun to become clear<BR>or light.<BR>--तं Day-break, dawn;<BR>अक्ष्णोः प्रभातमासीत Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभानं|प्रभान
प्रभानं Light, lustre, splendour,<BR>radiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावत्|प्रभावन्त्
प्रभावत् a. Luminous, radiant,<BR>splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभागः|प्रभाग
प्रभागः<BR>1 Division.<BR>--2 The<BR>fraction of a fraction (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाष्
प्रभाष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To speak to,<BR>address to; स्थितधीः किं प्रभाषेत<BR>Bg. 2. 54.<BR>--2 To proclaim; publish.<BR>--3 To<BR>disclose, reveal.<BR>--4 To expound,<BR>explain.<BR>--5 To prate, prattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाषणं|प्रभाषण
प्रभाषणं Explanation,<BR>interpretation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास्
प्रभास् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To shine.<BR>--2 To<BR>appear. --Caus. To illuminate,<BR>irradiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभासः|प्रभास
प्रभासः Splendour, beauty, lustre.<BR>--सः --सं N. of a well-known place<BR>of pilgrimage near Dvārakā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभासनं|प्रभासन
प्रभासनं Illumining, irradiating,<BR>brightening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभास्वर
प्रभास्वर a. Brilliant, bright,<BR>shining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिद्
प्रभिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To break, tear,<BR>break or tear asunder.<BR>--2 To exude<BR>(from the temples of an elephant);<BR>see प्रभिन्न. --Pass.<BR>1 To be broken<BR>to pieces.<BR>--2 To bud forth, open,<BR>expand (as flowers).<BR>--3 To split,<BR>divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभिन्न|प्रभिन्नः
प्रभिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Severed, split, cleft,<BR>divided.<BR>--2 Broken to pieces.<BR>--3<BR>Cut off, detached.<BR>--4 Budding,<BR>expanded, opened.<BR>--5 Changed,<BR>altered<BR>--6 Deformed, disfigured.<BR>--7<BR>Relaxed, loosened.<BR>--8 Intoxicated, in<BR>rut; Ku. 5. 80.<BR>--9 Pierced, bored.<BR>--10 Different, distinct.<BR>--न्नः An<BR>elephant in rut.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजनं a<BR>kind of collyrium or eye-salve<BR>mixed with oil.<BR>--करट a. ‘having the<BR>cheeks cleft,’ being in rut,<BR>intoxicated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेदः|प्रभेद
प्रभेदः<BR>1 Splitting, cleaving,<BR>opening.<BR>--2 Division, separation.<BR>--3<BR>The flowing of rut or ichor from<BR>the temples of an elephant;<BR>R. 3. 37.<BR>--4 Difference, distinction.<BR>--5<BR>A kind or sort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभेदक
प्रभेदक a.<BR>1 Tearing asunder,<BR>piercing &c.<BR>--2 Distinguishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभू
प्रभू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To arise, proceed,<BR>spring up, to be born or produced,<BR>originate (with abl.); लोभात् क्रोधः<BR>प्रभवति H. 1. 27; स्वायंभुवान्मरीचेर्यः<BR>प्रबभूव प्रजापतिः Ś. 7. 9; पुरुषः<BR>प्रबभूवाग्नेर्विस्मयेन सहर्त्विजां R. 10. 50;<BR>Bg. 8. 18.<BR>--2 To appear, become<BR>visible; H. 4. 84.<BR>--3 To multiply,<BR>increase; see प्रभूत.<BR>--4 To be strong<BR>or powerful, prevail, predominate,<BR>show one's power; प्रभवति हि महिम्ना<BR>स्वेन योगीश्वरीयं Māl. 9. 52; प्रभवति<BR>भगबान् विधिः K.; Pt. 1. 44.<BR>--5 To<BR>be able or equal, have power for<BR>(with inf.); कुसुमान्यपि<BR>गात्रसंगमात्प्रभवंत्यायुरपोहितुं यदि R. 8. 44;<BR>कोन्यो हुतवहाद्दग्धुं प्रभविष्यति Ś. 4;<BR>Ś. 6. 30; V. 1. 9; U. 2. 4; Pt. 1.<BR>--6 To have control or power over,<BR>prevail over, be master of (usually<BR>with gen., sometimes with dat. or<BR>loc.); यदि प्रभविष्याम्यात्मनः Ś. 1;<BR>प्रभवति निजस्य कन्यकाजनस्य महाराजः<BR>Māl. 4; तत्प्रभवति अनुशासने देवी Ve. 2;<BR>विधिरपि न येभ्यः प्रभवति Bh. 2. 94.<BR>--7 To be a match for (with dat.);<BR>प्रभवति मल्लो मल्लाय Mbh.<BR>--8 To be<BR>sufficient for, be able to contain;<BR>Ku. 6. 59.<BR>--9 To be contained in<BR>(wit loc.); गुरुः प्रहर्षः प्रबभूव<BR>नात्मनि R. 3. 17.<BR>--10 To be useful.<BR>--11<BR>To implore, beseech.<BR>--12 To<BR>extend beyond, surpass (Ved.)<BR>--13<BR>To profit, avail. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>increase, augment.<BR>--2 To provide<BR>more fully.<BR>--3 To recognize.<BR>--4 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">Page0753-c+ 57</a>]<BR>gain power or strength.<BR>--5 To<BR>make powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभव|प्रभवः
प्रभव a.<BR>1 Excellent,<BR>distinguished.<BR>--2 Superior, powerful.<BR>--वः<BR>1<BR>Source, origin; अनंतरत्नप्रभवस्य यस्य<BR>Ku. 1. 3; अकिंचनः सन् प्रभवः स<BR>संपदां 5. 77; R. 9. 75.<BR>--2 Birth,<BR>production.<BR>--3 The source of a river;<BR>तस्या एवं प्रभवमचलं प्राप्य गौरं तुषारैः<BR>Me. 52.<BR>--4 The operative cause, origin<BR>of being (as father, mother &c.);<BR>तमस्याः प्रभवमवगच्छ Ś. 1.<BR>--5 The<BR>author, creator; Ku. 2. 5.<BR>--6<BR>Birthplace.<BR>--7 Power, strength, valour,<BR>majestic dignity (= प्रभाब q. v.).<BR>--8<BR>An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--9 (At the<BR>end of comp.) Arising or<BR>originating from, derived from; सूर्यप्रभवो<BR>वंशः R. 1. 2; Ku. 3. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवनं|प्रभवन
प्रभवनं<BR>1 Production.<BR>--2 Source,<BR>origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभवितृ
प्रभवितृ m. A ruler, great lord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभविष्णु|प्रभविष्णुः
प्रभविष्णु a.<BR>1 Strong, mighty,<BR>powerful.<BR>--2 Pre-eminent,<BR>distinguished.<BR>--ष्णुः<BR>1 A lord, master<BR>यत्प्रभविष्णवे रोचते Ś. 2; Ku. 6. 62.<BR>--2 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावः|प्रभाव
प्रभावः<BR>1 Lustre, splendour,<BR>brilliance.<BR>--2 Dignity, glory, majesty<BR>grandeur, majestic lustre; प्रभाववानिव<BR>लक्ष्यते Ś. 1.<BR>--3 Strength, valour,<BR>power, efficacy; Pt. 1. 7.<BR>--4 Regal<BR>power (one of the three Śaktis q. v.).<BR>--5 A superhuman power or faculty,<BR>miraculous power; R. 2. 41, 62;<BR>3. 40, V. 1, 2, 5.<BR>--6 Magnanimity.<BR>--7<BR>Extension, circumference.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. proceeding from majesty or<BR>regal power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभाववत्|प्रभाववन्त्
प्रभाववत् a.<BR>1 Strong, powerful,<BR>mighty.<BR>--2 Majestic; Ś. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावक
प्रभावक, प्रभावन a. Prominent,<BR>influential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावन|प्रभावनः
प्रभावक, प्रभावन a. Prominent,<BR>influential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभावना
प्रभावना Disclosing, revealing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभु|प्रभुः
प्रभु a. (भु-भ्वी f.)<BR>1 Mighty, strong,<BR>powerful.<BR>--2 Able, competent,<BR>having power to (with inf. or in comp.);<BR>ऋषि प्रभावान्मयि नांतकोऽपि प्रभुः प्रहर्तुं<BR>किमुतान्यहिंस्राः R. 2. 62;<BR>समाधिभेदप्रभवो भवति Ku. 3. 40.<BR>--3 A match<BR>for; प्रभुर्मल्लो मल्लाय Mbh.<BR>--4<BR>Abundant.<BR>--5 Everlasting, eternal.<BR>--भुः<BR>1 A lord, master;<BR>प्रभुर्बुभूषुर्भुवनत्रयस्य यः Śi. 1. 49.<BR>--2 A governor,<BR>ruler, supreme authority.<BR>--3 An<BR>owner, proprietor.<BR>--4 Quick-silver.<BR>--5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--6 Of Śiva.<BR>--7<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">Page0754-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Of Brahmā.<BR>--8 Of Indra.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भक्त a. attached or devoted to<BR>one's lord, loyal.<BR>--(क्तः) a good<BR>horse.<BR>--भक्तिः f. devotion to one's<BR>lord, loyalty, faithfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0753-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुता
प्रभुता, --त्वं<BR>1 Lordship, supremacy,<BR>mastery, ascendancy, authority;<BR>Ś. 5. 26; V. 4. 12; Ś. 7. 32.<BR>--2<BR>Ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभुत्वं|प्रभुत्व
प्रभुता, --त्वं<BR>1 Lordship, supremacy,<BR>mastery, ascendancy, authority;<BR>Ś. 5. 26; V. 4. 12; Ś. 7. 32.<BR>--2<BR>Ownership.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूत|प्रभूतं
प्रभूत p. p.<BR>1 Sprung from,<BR>produced.<BR>--2 Much, abundant.<BR>--3<BR>Numerous, many.<BR>--4 Mature,<BR>perfect.<BR>--5 High, lofty.<BR>--6 Long.<BR>--7<BR>Presided over.<BR>--8 Abounding in.<BR>--9<BR>Gone up or upwards.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--यवसेंधन a. abounding in fresh grass<BR>and fuel.<BR>--वयस् a. advanced in<BR>age, old, aged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतता
प्रभूतता, --त्वं<BR>1 Abundance, plenty.<BR>--2 Multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतत्वं|प्रभूतत्व
प्रभूतता, --त्वं<BR>1 Abundance, plenty.<BR>--2 Multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूतिः|प्रभूति
प्रभूतिः f.<BR>1 Source, origin.<BR>--2<BR>Power, strength.<BR>--3 Sufficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभूष्णु|प्रभूष्णुः
प्रभूष्णु a. Able, powerful, strong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभृतिः|प्रभृति
प्रभृतिः f.<BR>1 Beginning,<BR>commencement; generally used in this<BR>sense as the last member of Bah.<BR>compounds; इंद्रप्रभृतयो देवाः &c.<BR>--2<BR>Ved. An oblation.<BR>--3 Throwing or<BR>casting (Ved.). --ind. From,<BR>ever since, beginning with (with<BR>abl.); शैशवात्प्रभृति पोषितां प्रियां<BR>U. 1. 45; Ku. 3. 26 R. 2. 38; अद्य<BR>प्रभृति henceforward; ततः प्रभृति, अतः<BR>प्रभृति &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंश्
प्रभ्रंश् {c1c} A., {c4c} P.<BR>1 To fall or drop<BR>down, slip; प्रभ्रश्यमानाभरणप्रसूना<BR>R. 14. 54.<BR>--2 To lose, be deprived of;<BR>प्रभ्रश्यते तेजसः Mk. 1. 14.<BR>--3 To<BR>escape or free oneself from. --Caus.<BR>To throw or bring down from, cause<BR>to fall down from; प्रभ्रंशयां यो नहुषं<BR>चकार R. 13. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशः|प्रभ्रंश
प्रभ्रंशः Fall, falling off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशथुः|प्रभ्रंशथु
प्रभ्रंशथुः A disease of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशित
प्रभ्रंशित p. p.<BR>1 Thrown or cast<BR>down.<BR>--2 Deprived of.<BR>--3<BR>Expelled, driven out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रंशिन्
प्रभ्रंशिन् a. Falling off or down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्ट
प्रभ्रष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Fallen off, fallen or<BR>dropped down.<BR>--2 Broken.<BR>--ष्टं A<BR>garland of flowers suspended from<BR>the lock on the crown of the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रभ्रष्टकं|प्रभ्रष्टक
प्रभ्रष्टकं See प्रभ्रष्टं above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमग्न
प्रमग्न p. p. Drowned, immersed,<BR>dipped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमणस्
प्रमण(न)स् a.<BR>1 Happy,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">Page0754-b+ 56</a>]<BR>cheerful, delighted.<BR>--2 Good-natured.<BR>--3 Attentive.<BR>--4 Kind, amiable<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमनस्
प्रमण(न)स् a.<BR>1 Happy,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">Page0754-b+ 56</a>]<BR>cheerful, delighted.<BR>--2 Good-natured.<BR>--3 Attentive.<BR>--4 Kind, amiable<BR>(Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत
प्रमत p. p.<BR>1 Thought out.<BR>--2<BR>Wise, prudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथ्
प्रमथ् --मंथ् {c1c} {c9c} P.,<BR>1 To churn;<BR>प्रमथ्यमानो (समुद्रो) गिरिणेव भूयः<BR>R. 13. 14.<BR>--2 To harass, trouble<BR>excessively, annoy, torment.<BR>--3 To<BR>strike down, bruise, hurt.<BR>--4 To<BR>tear off or cut.<BR>--5 To lay waste,<BR>devastate.<BR>--6 To kill, destroy;<BR>Māl. 4. 9, 9. 27.<BR>--7 To agitate, stir<BR>about.<BR>--8 Ved. To rob. --Caus. To<BR>harass, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमंथ्|प्रमन्थ्
प्रमथ् --मंथ् {c1c} {c9c} P.,<BR>1 To churn;<BR>प्रमथ्यमानो (समुद्रो) गिरिणेव भूयः<BR>R. 13. 14.<BR>--2 To harass, trouble<BR>excessively, annoy, torment.<BR>--3 To<BR>strike down, bruise, hurt.<BR>--4 To<BR>tear off or cut.<BR>--5 To lay waste,<BR>devastate.<BR>--6 To kill, destroy;<BR>Māl. 4. 9, 9. 27.<BR>--7 To agitate, stir<BR>about.<BR>--8 Ved. To rob. --Caus. To<BR>harass, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथः|प्रमथ
प्रमथः<BR>1 A horse.<BR>--2 N. of a class<BR>of Beings (said to be goblins)<BR>attending on Śiva; Ku. 7. 95.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः --नाथः --पतिः an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--आलयः hell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथनं|प्रमथन
प्रमथनं<BR>1 Hurting, injuring,<BR>tormenting.<BR>--2 Killing, slaughter.<BR>--3<BR>Churning, stirring about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथित|प्रमथितं
प्रमथित p. p.<BR>1 Tormented,<BR>distressed.<BR>--2 Trampled down.<BR>--3<BR>Slain, killed; Māl. 3. 18.<BR>--4<BR>Properly churned.<BR>--तं Butter-milk<BR>without water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमथिन्
प्रमथिन् a. Destroying; Mu. 2. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथः|प्रमाथ
प्रमाथः<BR>1 Excessive paining,<BR>tormenting, torturing.<BR>--2 Agitating,<BR>churning.<BR>--3 Killing, slaughter,<BR>destruction; सैनिकानां प्रमाथेन<BR>सत्यमोजायितं त्वया U. 5. 32; 4.<BR>--4<BR>Violence, outrage.<BR>--5 Rape, forcible<BR>abduction.<BR>--थाः m. pl. Epithet of the<BR>fiends attendant upon Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथित
प्रमाथित p. p.<BR>1 Forcibly attacked,<BR>roughly handled.<BR>--2 Ravished,<BR>seduced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाथिन्
प्रमाथिन् a.<BR>1 Tormenting,<BR>harassing, torturing, afflicting, harrowing;<BR>क्व रुजा हृदयप्रमाथिनी क्व च ते<BR>विश्वसनीयमायुधं M. 3. 2; Māl. 2. 1;<BR>Ki. 3. 14.<BR>--2 Killing, destroying.<BR>--3<BR>Agitating, setting in motion;<BR>Bg. 2. 60; 6. 34.<BR>--4 Tearing or<BR>pulling down, striking down;<BR>R. 11. 58.<BR>--5 Cutting down; Ki. 17. 31.<BR>--m. N. of a year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद्
प्रमद् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be intoxicated or<BR>drunk.<BR>--2 To be careless about, to<BR>be negligent or heedless, be<BR>regardless of or indifferent to (with loc.);<BR>अतोऽर्थान्न प्रमाद्यंति प्रमदासु विपश्चितः<BR>Ms. 2. 213.<BR>--3 To omit to do,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">Page0754-c+ 58</a>]<BR>swerve or deviate from (with abl.)<BR>स्वाधिकारात्प्रमत्तः Me. 1.<BR>--4 To make<BR>a mistake, err, go astray; Bk. 5. 8,<BR>17. 39; 18. 8.<BR>--5 To spend or while<BR>a way (time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्त|प्रमत्तः
प्रमत्त p. p.<BR>1 Intoxicated, drunk;<BR>कथां प्रमत्तः प्रथमं कृतामिव (न<BR>स्मरिष्यति) Ś. 4. 1.<BR>--2 Mad, insane.<BR>--3<BR>Careless, negligent, inattentive<BR>heedless, regardless (generally with<BR>loc.).<BR>--4 Swerving from, failing<BR>to do (with abl.)<BR>--5 Blundering.<BR>--6<BR>Wanton, lascivious.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गीत a.<BR>sung carelessly.<BR>--चित्त a. negligent,<BR>heedless, careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्तता
प्रमत्तता Inattention, carelessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमत्तवत्|प्रमत्तवन्त्
प्रमत्तवत् a. Inattentive, careless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद|प्रमदः
प्रमद a.<BR>1 Drunk, intoxicated (fig.<BR>also).<BR>--2 Impassioned.<BR>--3<BR>Careless.<BR>--4 Wanton, dissolute.<BR>--5<BR>Violent, strong.<BR>--दः<BR>1 Joy, pleasure,<BR>delight; Śi. 3. 54; 13 2; Māl. 9.<BR>--2 The Dhattūra plant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काननं, --वनं a pleasure-garden<BR>attached to the royal harem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदक
प्रमदक a. Licentious, sensual.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदनं|प्रमदन
प्रमदनं Amorous desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमदा
प्रमदा<BR>1 A young handsome<BR>woman; R. 9. 31; Ś. 5. 17.<BR>--2 A<BR>wife or woman in general;<BR>Ku. 4. 12; R. 8. 72.<BR>--3 The sign virgo of<BR>the zodiac.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काननं, --वनं a<BR>pleasure garden attached to the<BR>royal harem (for the use of the<BR>wives of a king).<BR>--जनः {1} a<BR>young woman. {2} womankind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमद्वर
प्रमद्वर a. Careless, inattentive,<BR>heedless^1.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादः|प्रमाद
प्रमादः<BR>1 Carelessness, negligence,<BR>inattention, inadvertence, oversight;<BR>ज्ञातुं प्रमादस्खलितं न शक्यं Ś. 6. 25;<BR>Ch. P. 1.<BR>--2 Intoxication, drun<BR>kenness.<BR>--3 (a) Fainting, swoon. (b)<BR>Insanity, madness.<BR>--4 A<BR>mistake, blunder, mistaken judgment;<BR>Pt. 1. 39.<BR>--5 An accident,<BR>mishap, calamity, danger; अहो प्रमादः<BR>Māl. 3; U. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादवत्|प्रमादवन्त्
प्रमादवत् a.<BR>1 Intoxicated.<BR>--2 Mad<BR>insane.<BR>--3 Careless, inattentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिका
प्रमादिका<BR>1 A careless woman.<BR>--2<BR>A deflowered girl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादित
प्रमादित a. Ridiculed, mocked,<BR>scoffed at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमादिन्
प्रमादिन् a.<BR>1 Careless, inattentive,<BR>negligent; सर्वत्र प्रमादी वैधेयः V. 2.<BR>--2 Insane, mad.<BR>--3 Intoxicated,<BR>drunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0754-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमनस्
प्रमनस् a. Delighted, happy,<BR>cheerful, in good spirits; R. 3. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमन्यु
प्रमन्यु a.<BR>1 Enraged, irritated,<BR>incensed against (with loc.);<BR>R. 7. 34.<BR>--2 Distressed, sorrowful,<BR>sorely grieved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमयः|प्रमय
प्रमयः<BR>1 Death.<BR>--2 Ruin,<BR>downfall.<BR>--3 Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमर्दनं|प्रमर्दन|प्रमर्दनः
प्रमर्दनं Crushing, destroying,<BR>trampling down.<BR>--नः An epithet<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमा
प्रमा {c2c} P., {c3c} A.<BR>1 To measure;<BR>त्रीणि पदानि प्रमाय.<BR>--2 To form, make,<BR>build.<BR>--3 To prove, establish,<BR>demonstrate.<BR>--4 To arrange, place in<BR>order.<BR>--5 To know, understand, get<BR>a correct idea of; न परोपहितन्न च स्वतः<BR>प्रमिमीतेऽनुभवादृतेऽल्पधीः Śi. 16. 40;<BR>अशक्योऽयमर्थः प्रमातुं H. 3.<BR>--6 To<BR>conjecture. --Caus. To afford or give<BR>proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमा
प्रमा<BR>1 Consciousness, perception.<BR>--2 (In logic) Correct notion or<BR>apprehension, true and certain<BR>knowledge, accurate conception;<BR>तद्वति तत्प्रकारकोऽनुभवः प्रमा यथा रजते<BR>इदं रजतमिति ज्ञानं T. S.<BR>--3 Ved.<BR>Basis, foundation.<BR>--4 A measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणं|प्रमाण|प्रमाणः
प्रमाणं<BR>1 A measure in general (of<BR>length, breadth &c.); R. 18. 38.<BR>--2 Size, extent, magnitude.<BR>--3<BR>Seale, standard; पृथिव्यां<BR>स्वामिभक्तानां प्रमाणे परमे स्थितः Mu. 2. 21.<BR>--4<BR>Limit, quantity.<BR>--5 Testimony,<BR>evidence, proof.<BR>--6 Authority, warrant;<BR>one who judges or decides, one<BR>whose word is an authority; श्रुत्वा<BR>देवः प्रमाणं Pt. 1 ‘having heard this<BR>your Majesty will decide (what to<BR>do)’; आर्यमिश्राः प्रमाणं M. 1;<BR>Mu. 1. 1; Ś. 1. 22; व्याकरणे पाणिनिः<BR>प्रमाणं; Ms. 2. 13; Pt. 1. 240;<BR>sometimes in pl.; वेदाः प्रमाणाः.<BR>--7<BR>A true or certain knowledge,<BR>accurate conception or notion.<BR>--8 A<BR>mode of proof, a means of arriving<BR>at correct knowledge; (the<BR>Naiyāyikas recognize only four kinds;<BR>प्रत्यक्ष, अनुमान, उपमान and शब्द, the<BR>Vedāntins and Mīmāṃsakas add<BR>two more अनुपलब्धि and अर्थापत्ति;<BR>while the Sāṃkhyas admit प्रत्यक्ष,<BR>अनुमान and शब्द only; cf. अनुभव<BR>also.)<BR>--9 Principal, capital.<BR>--10<BR>Unity.<BR>--11 Scripture, sacred<BR>authority.<BR>--12 Cause, reason.<BR>--13 Rule,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-b" target="_blank">Page0755-b+ 57</a>]<BR>sanction, precept.<BR>--14 The first term<BR>in a rule of three.<BR>--15 An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--16 Freedom from<BR>apprehension.<BR>--17 The prosodial length of<BR>a vowel.<BR>--णः -णी A rule, standard,<BR>authority.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिक a. more<BR>than ordinary, inordinate,<BR>excessive; Ś. 1. 30.<BR>--अंतरं another<BR>mode of proof.<BR>--अभावः absence of<BR>authority.<BR>--ज्ञ a. knowing the<BR>modes of proof, (as a logician).<BR>--(ज्ञः) an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--दृष्ट a.<BR>sanctioned by authority.<BR>--पत्रं a<BR>written warrant.<BR>--पुरुषः an<BR>arbitrator, a judge, an umpire.<BR>--भूत<BR>(˚णीभूत) a. authoritative.<BR>--(तः) an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--वचनं, --वाक्यं an<BR>an authoritative statement.<BR>--शास्त्रं<BR>{1} scripture. {2} the science of<BR>logic.<BR>--सूत्रं a measuring cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणक|प्रमाणकः
प्रमाणक a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Measuring, extending to, as far as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणयति
प्रमाणयति Den. P.<BR>1 To regard as<BR>an authority; दैवमबिद्वांसः प्रमाणयंति<BR>Mu. 3; H. 1. 10.<BR>--2 To hold up<BR>as a model.<BR>--3 To prove,<BR>demonstrate, show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणिक
प्रमाणिक a.<BR>1 Forming or being<BR>a measure.<BR>--2 Forming an<BR>authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमाणीकृ
प्रमाणीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To confide, believe.<BR>--2 To hold or regard as an<BR>authority; शासनं तरुभिरपि प्रमाणीकृतं<BR>Ś. 6.<BR>--3 To fix upon, dispense, deal or<BR>meet out; दैवेन प्रभुणा स्वयं जगति<BR>यद्यस्य प्रमाणीकृतं Bh. 2. 121.<BR>--4 To obey, conform to.<BR>--5<BR>To prove, to establish.<BR>--6 To<BR>consult, take the consent of;<BR>Ku. 6. 1.<BR>--7 To take into account;<BR>U. 7. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातृ
प्रमातृ a.<BR>1 Having a right notion,<BR>competent to judge or ascertain.<BR>--2 An authority, proof.<BR>--3<BR>Domonstrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापक|प्रमापकः
प्रमापक a. Furnishing authority<BR>or proof.<BR>--कः An authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमित|प्रमितः
प्रमित p. p.<BR>1 Measured.<BR>--2<BR>Measured off, limited, few, little;<BR>प्रमितविषयां शक्तिं विंदन् Mv. 1. 51;<BR>Śi. 16. 80.<BR>--3 Known, understood.<BR>--4<BR>Proved, demonstrated.<BR>--5 (At the end<BR>of comp.) Of such and such extent<BR>or measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमितिः|प्रमिति
प्रमितिः f.<BR>1 Measurement, a<BR>measure.<BR>--2 True or certain knowledge,<BR>accurate notion or conception.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">Page0755-c+ 55</a>]<BR>Knowledge obtained by any one of<BR>the Pramāṇas or means of<BR>knowledge.<BR>--4 True inference or analogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेय
प्रमेय a.<BR>1 Measurable, finite.<BR>--2<BR>To be proved, demonstrable.<BR>--यं<BR>1 An object of certain knowledge, a<BR>demonstrated conclusion, theorem.<BR>--2 The thing to be proved, the topic<BR>to be proved or discussed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमातामहः|प्रमातामह
प्रमातामहः A maternal<BR>greatgrandfather.<BR>--ही A maternal<BR>greatgrandmother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापणं|प्रमापण
प्रमापणं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमापयितृ
प्रमापयितृ m. A murderer, killer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमिद्
प्रमिद् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To grow fat.<BR>--2 To<BR>begin to show affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेदित
प्रमेदित a.<BR>1 Unctuous, greasy.<BR>--2<BR>Having begun to show affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमी
प्रमी {c9c} U.<BR>1 To destroy,<BR>annihilate, kill, slay.<BR>--2 To diminish.<BR>--3<BR>To surmount, get over.<BR>--4 To<BR>surpass, outstrip.<BR>--5 Ved. To<BR>transgress, infringe.<BR>--6 Ved. To lose or<BR>miss (one's way).<BR>--7 To perish, die.<BR>--Caus. To destroy, annihilate &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीत|प्रमीतः
प्रमीत p. p.<BR>1 Dead, deceased.<BR>--2<BR>Sacrificed (as an animal).<BR>--तः<BR>An animal immolated or killed at a<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीतिः|प्रमीति
प्रमीतिः f. Death, destruction,<BR>decease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीढ|प्रमीढः
प्रमीढ a.<BR>1 Thick, dense,<BR>compact.<BR>--2 Passed as urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीला
प्रमीला<BR>1 Sleepiness, lassitude,<BR>enervation of spirits.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>woman, sovereign of a kingdom of<BR>women. She fought with Arjuna<BR>when his horse entered her<BR>territory, but she was conquered and<BR>became his wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमीलित
प्रमीलित p. p. With closed eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुख|प्रमुखं|प्रमुखः
प्रमुख a.<BR>1 Facing, turning the<BR>face towards.<BR>--2 Chief, principal,<BR>foremost, first.<BR>--3 Respectable,<BR>honourable,.<BR>--4 (At the end of<BR>comp.) (a) Headed by, having as<BR>chief or at the head; वासुकिप्रमुखाः<BR>Ku. 2. 38. (b) Accompanied with;<BR>प्रीतिप्रमुखवचनं स्वागतं व्याजहार<BR>Me. 4.<BR>--खः<BR>1 A respectable man.<BR>--2<BR>A heap, multitude.<BR>--3 The tree<BR>called Punnāga.<BR>--खं<BR>1 The mouth<BR>--2 The beginning of a chapter or<BR>section.<BR>--3 The time being, the<BR>present. (प्रमुखतस् and प्रमुखे are used<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">Page0756-a+ 57</a>]<BR>adverbially in the sense of ‘in front<BR>of’, ‘before’ ‘opposite to’;<BR>Bg. 1. 25; Ś. 7. 22).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0755-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुच्
प्रमुच् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To set free, liberate,<BR>release.<BR>--2 To throw, cast, hurl.<BR>--3<BR>To shed, emit, send forth.<BR>--4 To<BR>abandon, forsake, give up, renounce.<BR>--5 To loosen, untie, unbind.<BR>--6<BR>To expel, drive away, banish.<BR>--7<BR>To utter.<BR>--8 To put on, wear (as a<BR>garland &c.). --Pass.<BR>1 To be<BR>loose or detached.<BR>--2 To leave off,<BR>cease.<BR>--3 To free oneself from.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To loosen, unbind.<BR>--2 To<BR>liberate, release.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुक्त
प्रमुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Loosened.<BR>--2<BR>Liberated, set free.<BR>--3 Resigned,<BR>renounced.<BR>--4 Cast, hurled.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठं ind. bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोक्षः|प्रमोक्ष
प्रमोक्षः<BR>1 Dropping, letting fall.<BR>--2 Discharging, liberating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोचनं|प्रमोचन
प्रमोचनं<BR>1 Liberating, setting free.<BR>--2 Emitting, shedding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुद्
प्रमुद् {c1c} A. To be extremely glad,<BR>be very much delighted; R. 6. 86;<BR>Māl. 5. 23. --Caus. To gladden,<BR>delight, exhilarate; प्रमोदय<BR>चातकान् Māl. 9. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुद्
प्रमुद् f. Extreme joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुदित|प्रमुदितः
प्रमुदित p. p. Delighted, glad,<BR>pleased, happy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हृदय a.<BR>delighted at heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदः|प्रमोद
प्रमोदः<BR>1 Joy, delight, rejoicing,<BR>pleasure; प्रमोदनृत्यैः सह वारयोषितां<BR>R. 3. 19; Ms. 3. 61.<BR>--2 One of the<BR>eight perfections in the Sāṃkhya<BR>philosophy.<BR>--3 A strong perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदनं|प्रमोदन|प्रमोदनः
प्रमोदनं<BR>1 Gladdening, delighting,<BR>making glad.<BR>--2 Gladness.<BR>--नः An<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदित|प्रमोदितः
प्रमोदित p. p. Pleased, delighted,<BR>joyful, happy.<BR>--तः An epithet of<BR>Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोदिन्
प्रमोदिन् a.<BR>1 Delighting, making<BR>happy.<BR>--2 Delighted, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुष्
प्रमुष् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To take away,<BR>obscure; Bk. 17. 60.<BR>--2 To steal<BR>away, rob.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुषित
प्रमुषित p. p.<BR>1 Stolen, taken away;<BR>Śi. 17. 11.<BR>--2 Distracted,<BR>unconscious.<BR>--ता A kind of riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुह्
प्रमुह् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be stupefied or<BR>infatuated.<BR>--2 To faint, swoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमुग्ध
प्रमुग्ध a.<BR>1 Fainting, unconscious.<BR>--2 Very lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमूढ
प्रमूढ p. p.<BR>1 Perplexed,<BR>bewildered, infatuated.<BR>--2 Stupid, foolish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोहः|प्रमोह
प्रमोहः<BR>1 Stupefaction,<BR>insensibility, stupor; तिरयति करणानां ग्राहकत्वं<BR>प्रमोहः Māl. 1. 41.<BR>--2 Infatuation,<BR>bewilderment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमोहित
प्रमोहित p. p. Infatuated,<BR>bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृत
प्रमृत p. p.<BR>1 Dead, deceased.<BR>--2 Covered, concealed.<BR>--3<BR>Withdrawn or gone out of sight.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Death.<BR>--2 Cultivation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृज्
प्रमृज् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To wipe off or out,<BR>cleanse (fig. also); स्वभावलोलेत्ययशः<BR>प्रमृष्टं R. 6. 41.<BR>--2 To wipe off, away<BR>or out, blow out, efface; Mu. 1. 20.<BR>--3 To remove, rid oneself of.<BR>--4 To<BR>atone for, make amends for, expiate;<BR>पणिपातलंघतं प्रसार्ष्टुकामा V. 3; सर्वथा<BR>प्रमार्जितं त्वया प्रत्यादेशदुःखं Ś. 6.<BR>--5<BR>To stroke or rub gently.<BR>--6 To<BR>prepare.<BR>--7 To mark useless, frustrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमार्जनं|प्रमार्जन
प्रमार्जनं Wiping off, rubbing or<BR>washing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमृष्ट
प्रमृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Rubbed off, washed<BR>or wiped off, cleared off; R. 6. 41,<BR>44.<BR>--2 Polished, bright, clear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रमेहः|प्रमेह
प्रमेहः A general name for a<BR>urinary disease (such as gleet,<BR>diabetes &c).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रम्लै
प्रम्लै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fade, wither.<BR>--2<BR>To be downcast, sad or dejected.<BR>--3<BR>To be languid or wearied.<BR>--4 To be<BR>dirty or foul, be soiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रम्लान
प्रम्लान a<BR>1 Faded, withered away.<BR>--2 Soiled, dirty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्
प्रयत् {c1c} A. To try, endeavour,<BR>strive, attempt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नः|प्रयत्न
प्रयत्नः<BR>1 Effort, exertion,<BR>endeavour; R. 2. 56; Mu. 5. 20.<BR>--2<BR>Persevering or continued effort;<BR>perseverance.<BR>--3 Labour, difficulty;<BR>प्रयत्नप्रेक्षणीयः संवृत्तः Ś. 1 ‘hardly<BR>visible’, ‘seen with difficulty’.<BR>--4 Great<BR>care, caution; कृतप्रयत्नोऽपि गृहे<BR>विनश्यति Pt. 1. 20.<BR>--5 (In gram.)<BR>Effort in uttering, effort of the mouth<BR>in the production of articulate<BR>sounds; see Sk. on P. VIII. 2. 1.<BR>--6 (In phil.) Active effort of three<BR>kinds; प्रवृत्तिश्च निवृत्तिश्च तथा<BR>जीवनकारणम् । एवं प्रथत्नत्र्यैविध्यं तांत्रिकैः<BR>परिदर्शितम्.<BR>--7 Activity, action in general. (<BR>प्रयत्नतः, प्रयत्नेन-त्नात् &c. ind.<BR>1 With<BR>great effort, diligently.<BR>--2<BR>Assiduously.<BR>--3 Hardly, scarcely.<BR>--4<BR>Particularly, specially).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत्नवत्|प्रयत्नवन्त्
प्रयत्नवत् a. Assiduous, diligent,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">Page0756-c+ 56</a>]<BR>persevering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयम्
प्रयम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To give, grant (with<BR>dat. of person).<BR>--2 To curb, check,<BR>restrain, control.<BR>--3 To deliver,<BR>restore.<BR>--4 To give in marriage.<BR>--5<BR>To pay, discharge (as a debt).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयत|प्रयतः
प्रयत p. p.<BR>1 Restrained,<BR>selfsubdued, holy, pious, devout,<BR>purified by austerities or religious<BR>observances; keeping the organs of<BR>sense under restraint; R. 1. 95;<BR>8. 11; 13. 70; Ku. 1. 58; 3. 16.<BR>--2<BR>Zealous, intent.<BR>--3 Submissive.<BR>--4<BR>Careful, prudent.<BR>--तः A holy or<BR>pious person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयतिः|प्रयति
प्रयतिः f. Ved.<BR>1 An offering,<BR>oblation.<BR>--2 A gift, present.<BR>--3 Effort,<BR>endeavour.<BR>--4 Will, intention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयामः|प्रयाम
प्रयामः<BR>1 Restraining, checking.<BR>--2<BR>Dearth, scarcity, dearness (of water,<BR>corn &c.).<BR>--3 Length.<BR>--4<BR>Competition of buyers on account of dearth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्
प्रयस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To strive,<BR>endeavour.<BR>--2 To toil, labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयासः|प्रयास
प्रयासः<BR>1 Effort, exertion,<BR>endeavour; R. 12. 53; 14. 41.<BR>--2 Labour,<BR>difficulty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्
प्रयस् n. Ved.<BR>1 Food.<BR>--2<BR>Pleasure, delight.<BR>--3 A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयस्त|प्रयस्तं
प्रयस्त p. p. Seasoned, dressed with<BR>condiments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रया
प्रया {c2c} P.<BR>1 To walk, go; त्रस्ताद्भुतं<BR>नगरदैवतवत्प्रचासि Mk. 1. 27.<BR>--2 To<BR>walk on, set out.<BR>--3 To depart, go<BR>forth or out.<BR>--4 To advance,<BR>progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणं|प्रयाण
प्रयाणं<BR>1 Setting out, starting<BR>departure.<BR>--2 A march, journey;<BR>मार्गं तावच्छृणु कथयतस्त्वत्प्रयाणानुरूपं<BR>Me. 13.<BR>--3 Progress, advance.<BR>--4<BR>The march (of an enemy), an<BR>attack, invasion, expedition; कामं<BR>पुरः शुक्रमिव प्रयाणे Ku. 3. 43;<BR>R. 6. 33.<BR>--5 Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--6 Death, departure (from<BR>the world); Bg. 7. 30.<BR>--7 The back<BR>of a horse.<BR>--8 The hinder part of<BR>any animal.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कालः,<BR>--समयः<BR>time of departure.<BR>--भंगः a break in<BR>a journey, halt; Pt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाणकं|प्रयाणक
प्रयाणकं<BR>1 A journey, march;<BR>K. 118; 305.<BR>--2 Going, motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयात|प्रयातः
प्रयात p. p.<BR>1 Advanced, gone<BR>forth, departed.<BR>--2 Deceased, dead.<BR>--तः<BR>1 An invasion.<BR>--2 A precipice,<BR>steep rock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0756-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापनं|प्रयापन
प्रयापनं(णं)<BR>1 Sending.<BR>--2<BR>Expelling, driving away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापणं|प्रयापण
प्रयापनं(णं)<BR>1 Sending.<BR>--2<BR>Expelling, driving away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयापित
प्रयापित p. p.<BR>1 Made to advance<BR>or go forward.<BR>--2 Made to go away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयागः|प्रयाग
प्रयागः<BR>1 A sacrifice.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>Indra.<BR>--3 A horse.<BR>--4 N. of a<BR>celebrated place of pilgrimage at the<BR>confluence of the Gaṅgā and<BR>Yamunā near the modern Allahabad;<BR>Ms. 2. 21; (said to be n. also in<BR>this sense).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भयः an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाचनं|प्रयाचन
प्रयाचनं Begging, requesting,<BR>imploring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयाजः|प्रयाज
प्रयाजः A principal sacrificial<BR>ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्
प्रयुज् {c7c} A.<BR>1 To use, employ.<BR>अयमपि च गिरं नस्त्वत्प्रबोधयुक्तां<BR>R. 5. 74; सद्भावे साधुभावे च<BR>सदित्येतत्प्रयुज्यते Bg. 17. 26.<BR>--2 To appoint,<BR>employ, direct, order; मा मां प्रयुंक्थाः<BR>कुलकीर्तिलोपे Bk. 3. 54; प्रायुक्त राज्ये<BR>बत दुष्करे त्वां 3. 51; Ku. 7. 85.<BR>--3<BR>To give, bestow, confer; आशिषं<BR>प्रयुयुजे न वाहिनीं R. 11. 6; 2. 70;<BR>5. 35, 15. 8.<BR>--4 To move, set in<BR>motion; मरुत्प्रयुक्ताः (बाललताः)<BR>R. 2. 10.<BR>--5 To excite, urge, prompt,<BR>drive on, अथावमानेन पितुः प्रयुक्ता<BR>Ku. 1. 21; Bg. 3. 36.<BR>--6 To<BR>perform, do; Ku. 7. 86; 17. 12.<BR>--7<BR>To represent on the stage, act, perform;<BR>उत्तरं रामचरितं तत्प्रणीतं<BR>प्रयोक्ष्यते U. 1. 2; Ku. 5. 35; परिषदि<BR>प्रयुंजानस्य मम Mu. 1.<BR>--8 To lend for use,<BR>put to interest (as money &c.,);<BR>Ms. 8. 146.<BR>--9 To harness, yoke.<BR>--10 To<BR>appoint, invest, install (in an office.)<BR>--11 To cast, hurl, throw (as a<BR>missile); direct; प्रयुक्तमप्यस्त्रनितो वृथा<BR>स्यात् R. 2. 34.<BR>--12 To be fit,<BR>become.<BR>--13 To impose, inflict (with<BR>loc. or gen. of person). --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To use, employ; Ms. 3. 112.<BR>--2 To<BR>exact (as, interest)<BR>--3 To perform,<BR>practise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्त|प्रयुक्तं
प्रयुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Yoked, harnessed<BR>--2 Used, employed (as a word &c.);<BR>Pt. 1. 202.<BR>--3 Applied.<BR>--4<BR>Appointed, nominated.<BR>--5 Acted,<BR>represented.<BR>--6 Arising or resulting from,<BR>produced by, consequent on;<BR>Pt. 1. 61.<BR>--7 Endowed with.<BR>--8 Lost in<BR>meditation, abstracted.<BR>--9 Lent or<BR>put to interest (as money).<BR>--10<BR>Prompted, instigated, urged;<BR>Ku. 1. 21.<BR>--11 Directed, hurled at.<BR>--12<BR>Shaken, set in motion.<BR>--13 Inflicted<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-b" target="_blank">Page0757-b+ 59</a>]<BR>upon.<BR>--14 Connected with.<BR>--15<BR>Thick, compact, closely united.<BR>--क्तं<BR>A cause.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संस्कार a.<BR>polished (as a gem).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुक्तिः|प्रयुक्ति
प्रयुक्तिः f.<BR>1 Use, employment,<BR>application.<BR>--2 Incitement,<BR>instigation.<BR>--3 Motive, main object or end.<BR>occasion.<BR>--4 Consequence, result,<BR>--5 Activity, effort, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुज्
प्रयुज् f. Ved.<BR>1 Impulse, motive,<BR>cause.<BR>--2 Acquisition, gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोक्तृ
प्रयोक्तृ a.<BR>1 One who uses or<BR>employs (as a means, word &c.).<BR>--2<BR>One who performs or directs, an<BR>executor.<BR>--3 One who prompts or<BR>instigates, an instigator.<BR>--4 An<BR>author, an agent; U. 3. 48.<BR>--5 One<BR>who acts or represents (a drama).<BR>--6<BR>One who lends money at interest, a<BR>money-lender.<BR>--7 One who shoots<BR>(an arrow).<BR>--8 The agent of an<BR>action.<BR>--9 A reciter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगः|प्रयोग
प्रयोगः<BR>1 Use, application,<BR>employment; as in शब्दप्रयोग; अयं शब्दो<BR>भूरिप्रयोगः -अल्पप्रयोगः ‘this word is<BR>generally or rarely used’.<BR>--2 A usual<BR>form, general usage.<BR>--3 Hurling,<BR>throwing, discharging (opp. संहारः);<BR>प्रयोगसंहारविभक्तमंत्रं R. 5. 57.<BR>--4<BR>Exhibition, performance, representation<BR>(dramatic), acting; देव प्रयोगप्रधानं<BR>हि नाट्यशास्त्रं M. 1; नाटिका न प्रयोगतो<BR>दृष्टा Ratn. 1 ‘not seen acted on<BR>the stage’.<BR>--5 Practice,<BR>experimental portion (of a subject); (opp.<BR>शास्त्र ‘theory’); तदत्रभवानिमं मां च<BR>शास्त्रे प्रयोगे च विमृशतु M. 1.<BR>--6<BR>Course of procedure, ceremonial<BR>form.<BR>--7 An act, action.<BR>--8<BR>Recitation, delivery.<BR>--9 Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--10 A plan,<BR>contrivance, device, scheme.<BR>--11 A means,<BR>instrument.<BR>--12 Consequence, result.<BR>--13 Combination, connection.<BR>--14<BR>Addition.<BR>--15 (In gram.) A usual<BR>form.<BR>--16 Offering, presenting.<BR>--17<BR>(a) Principal, loan bearing<BR>interest. (b) Lending money on usury.<BR>--18 Appointment.<BR>--19 A sacred<BR>text or authority.<BR>--20 A cause,<BR>motive.<BR>--21 An example.<BR>--22<BR>Application of magic, magical rites.<BR>--23<BR>A horse.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिशयः one<BR>of the five kinds of प्रस्तावना or<BR>prologue, in which a part or<BR>performance is superseded by another in<BR>such a manner that a character is<BR>suddenly brought on the stage; i. e.<BR>where the Sūtradhāra goes out<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">Page0757-c+ 59</a>]<BR>hinting the entrance of a character<BR>and thus performs a part<BR>superseding that which he has apparently<BR>intended for his own, viz. dancing;<BR>the S. D. thus defines it:<BR>--यदि<BR>प्रयोग एकस्मिन् प्रयोगोऽन्यः प्रयुज्यते । तेन<BR>पात्रप्रवेशश्चेत् प्रयोगातिशयस्तदा ॥ 291.<BR>--निपुण a. {1} skilled in practice; M. 3.<BR>{2} practically experienced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगतः
प्रयोगतः ind.<BR>1 By the use of,<BR>through the employment of.<BR>--2 In<BR>consequence of.<BR>--3 According to.<BR>--4<BR>In action, actually.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोगिन्
प्रयोगिन् a.<BR>1 Using, employing.<BR>--2 Having an object in view.<BR>--3<BR>Prompting, stimulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोग्यः|प्रयोग्य
प्रयोग्यः A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजक|प्रयोजकः
प्रयोजक a. Occasioning, causing.<BR>effecting, leading to; inciting,<BR>stimulating, deputing, appointing &c.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An employer, one who uses or<BR>employs.<BR>--2 An author.<BR>--3 A founder,<BR>an institutor.<BR>--4 A money-lender.<BR>--5 A law-giver, legislator.<BR>--6 An<BR>instigator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजनं|प्रयोजन
प्रयोजनं<BR>1 Use, employment,<BR>application.<BR>--2 Use, need, necessity<BR>(with instr. of that which is<BR>needed and gen. of the user); सर्बैरपि राज्ञां<BR>प्रयोजनं Pt. 1; बाले किमनेन पृष्टेन प्रयोजनं<BR>K. 144.<BR>--3 End, aim, object, purpose;<BR>प्रयोजनमनुद्दिश्य न मंदोऽपि प्रवर्तते;<BR>पुत्रप्रयोजना दाराः पुत्रः पिंडप्रयोजनः ।<BR>हितप्रयोजनं मित्रं धनं सर्वप्रयोजनं ॥<BR>Subhāṣ.; गुणवत्तापि परप्रयोजना<BR>R. 8. 31.<BR>--4 A means of attaining;<BR>Ms. 7. 100.<BR>--5 A cause, motive,<BR>occasion.<BR>--6 Profit, interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोजनवत्|प्रयोजनवन्त्
प्रयोजनवत् a.<BR>1 Having or done<BR>with a particular object.<BR>--2 Selfish.<BR>--3 Useful, serviceable.<BR>--4 Caused,<BR>produced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयोज्य|प्रयोज्यं|प्रयोज्यः
प्रयोज्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be used or<BR>employed.<BR>--2 To be practised.<BR>--3<BR>To be produced or caused.<BR>--4 To be<BR>appointed.<BR>--5 To be thrown or<BR>discharged (as a missile).<BR>--6 To be<BR>set to work.<BR>--ज्यः A servant, an<BR>employè.<BR>--ज्यं Capital, principal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुत|प्रयुतं
प्रयुत a.<BR>1 Joined, united.<BR>--2<BR>Separated.<BR>--तं A million.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुत्सुः|प्रयुत्सु
प्रयुत्सुः<BR>1 A warrior.<BR>--2 A ram.<BR>--3 Wind, air.<BR>--4 An ascetic.<BR>--5 N.<BR>of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रयुद्धं|प्रयुद्ध
प्रयुद्धं A battle, fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररक्षणं|प्ररक्षण
प्ररक्षणं Protection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुच्
प्ररुच् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To shine very much.<BR>--2 To be liked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोचन
प्ररोचन a. Exciting or enticing.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">Page0758-a+ 59</a>]<BR>--नं<BR>1 Exciting, or stimulating.<BR>--2 Illustration, explanation.<BR>--3<BR>Seduction.<BR>--4 Exhibition (of a<BR>person) for being seen and liked (by<BR>the people); अलोकसामान्यगुणस्तनूजः<BR>प्ररोचनार्थं प्रकटीकृतश्च Māl. 1. 10 (where<BR>Jagaddhara interprets प्ररोचनार्थं by<BR>प्रवृत्तिपाटवार्थं ‘in order to be<BR>thoroughly acquainted with the world’).<BR>--5<BR>Favourable description of that which<BR>is to follow in a play.<BR>--6<BR>Representation of the end as all but<BR>accomplished; see S. D. 388; (प्ररोचना also<BR>in the last two senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0757-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुदित
प्ररुदित p. p. Crying bitterly,<BR>weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुह्
प्ररुह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To grow, rise, shoot<BR>forth; न पर्वताग्रे नलिनी प्ररोहति<BR>Mk. 4. 17.<BR>--2 To heal up (as a wound).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररुह्
प्ररुह् f. Ved. A shoot, branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररूढ|प्ररूढः
प्ररूढ p. p.<BR>1 Full-grown,<BR>developed.<BR>--2 Born, sprung, produced;<BR>यस्यायमंगात् कृतिनः प्ररूढः Ś. 7. 19.<BR>--3<BR>Increased.<BR>--4 Gone deep, rooted;<BR>as in प्ररूढमूल.<BR>--5 Grown long; as in<BR>प्ररूढकेश, प्ररूढश्मश्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररूढिः|प्ररूढि
प्ररूढिः f. Growth, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोहः|प्ररोह
प्ररोहः<BR>1 Sprouting, shooting or<BR>growing up, germination; as in<BR>यवांकुरप्ररोहः.<BR>--2 A sprout, shoot (fig.<BR>also); प्लक्षप्ररोह इव सौधतलं बिभेद<BR>R. 8. 93; प्लक्षान् प्ररोहजटिलानिव मंत्रिवृद्धान्<BR>13. 71; Ku. 5. 60; 7. 17; 5. 60;<BR>U. 5. 2.<BR>--3 A scion, offspring; हा<BR>राधेयकुलप्ररोह Ve. 4; Mv. 6. 25;<BR>नंदवंशप्ररोहः Mu. 1. 11.<BR>--4 A shoot of<BR>light; कुर्वंति सामंतशिखामणीनां<BR>प्रभाप्ररोहास्तमयं रजांसि R. 6. 33.<BR>--5 A<BR>new leaf or branch, twig, spray.<BR>--6<BR>An excrescence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोहणं|प्ररोहण
प्ररोहणं<BR>1 Growing, shooting forth,<BR>germination.<BR>--2 Budding, sprouting.<BR>--3 A twig, sprout, shoot, spray.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्ररोहिन्
प्ररोहिन् a.<BR>1 Shooting up.<BR>--2<BR>Growing, propagated; Ms. 1. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलप्
प्रलप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To speak, talk;<BR>वचो वै देहीति (वैदेहीति) प्रतिपदमुदश्रु<BR>प्रलपितं S. D. 6.<BR>--2 To talk at ran<BR>dom or incoherently, prate, chatter<BR>talk wildly or nonsensically;<BR>प्रलपत्येष वैधेयः Ś. 2.<BR>--3 To lament,<BR>mourn, cry, bewail.<BR>--4 To call, invoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपनं|प्रलपन
प्रलपनं<BR>1 Talking, speaking, talk<BR>words, conversation.<BR>--2 Prating,<BR>prattle, raving, incoherent or<BR>nonsensical talk; इदं कस्यापि प्रलपितं.<BR>--3<BR>Lamentation, wailing; U. 3. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलपित|प्रलपितः
प्रलपित p. p. Talked, prated, &c.<BR>--तं Talk; see प्रलपन above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापः|प्रलाप
प्रलापः<BR>1 Talk, conversation,<BR>discourse.<BR>--2 Prating, prattling, an<BR>incoherent or nonsensical talk;<BR>Ms. 12. 6.<BR>--3 Lamentation, wailing;<BR>उत्तराप्रलापोपजनितकृपो भगवान्<BR>वासुदेवः K. 175; Ve. 5. 30.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हन् m. a sort of collyrium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलापिन्
प्रलापिन् a.<BR>1 Talking, speaking;<BR>हा असंबद्धप्रलापिन् Ve. 3.<BR>--2 Prating,<BR>prattling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलभ्
प्रलभ् {c1c} A. To cheat, deceive;<BR>cf. विप्रलभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलंभः|प्रलम्भ|प्रलंभ|प्रलम्भः
प्रलंभः<BR>1 Obtaining, gaining,<BR>attaining.<BR>--2 Deceiving, imposing upon,<BR>cheating, overreaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलंभनं|प्रलम्भन
प्रलंभनं Deceiving, cheating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलब्ध
प्रलब्ध p. p. Deceived, cheated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलंब|प्रलम्ब|प्रलम्बः
प्रलंब a.<BR>1 Pendulous, hanging<BR>down; as in प्रलंबकेश.<BR>--2 Prominent;<BR>as in प्रलंबनासिकः.<BR>--3 Slow, dilatory.<BR>--बः<BR>1 Hanging on or from,<BR>depending.<BR>--2 Anything hanging down.<BR>--3 A branch.<BR>--4 A garland worn<BR>round the neck.<BR>--5 A kind of<BR>necklace.<BR>--6 The female breast.<BR>--7 Tin<BR>or lead.<BR>--8 N. of a demon killed by<BR>Balarāma.<BR>--9 A shoot of the<BR>vinepalm.<BR>--10 A cucumber.<BR>--11 A<BR>verse (गाथा).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंडः a man<BR>with hanging testicles.<BR>--घ्नः, --मथनः,<BR>--हन् m. epithets of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलंबनं|प्रलम्बन|प्रलंबन
प्रलंबनं Hanging down, depending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलंबित|प्रलम्बित|प्रलम्बितः
प्रलंबित a. Pendulous, hanging<BR>down, suspended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलंबीकृ|प्रलम्बीकृ
प्रलंबीकृ {c8c} U. To cause to hang<BR>down, suspend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रललाट
प्रललाट a. Having a prominent<BR>forehead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलवः|प्रलव
प्रलवः<BR>1 A fragment, chip, bit.<BR>--2 The sheath of a leaf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलवित्रं|प्रलवित्र
प्रलवित्रं An instrument for cutting<BR>off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रली
प्रली {c4c} A.<BR>1 To become<BR>dissolved, melt away.<BR>--2 To be absorbed<BR>or dissolved in, be resolved into;<BR>आत्मना कृतिना च त्वमात्मन्येव प्रलीयसे<BR>Ku. 2. 10; रात्र्यागमे प्रलीयंते<BR>तत्रैवाव्यक्तसंज्ञके Bg. 8. 18; Ms. 1. 54.<BR>--3 To vanish, disappear; सह मेघेन<BR>तडित्प्रलीयते Ku. 4. 33.<BR>--4 To be<BR>destroyed, to perish, die;<BR>Māl. 9. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलयः|प्रलय
प्रलयः<BR>1 Destruction, annihilation,<BR>dissolution; स्यानानि किं हिमवतः<BR>प्रलयं गतानि Bh. 3. 70, 69; प्रलयं<BR>नीत्वा Śi. 11. 66 ‘causing to disappear’.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">Page0758-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 The destruction of the whole<BR>universe (at the end of a kalpa),<BR>universal destruction; Ku. 2. 8;<BR>Bg. 7. 6.<BR>--3 Any extensive<BR>destruction or devastation.<BR>--4 Death,<BR>dying, destruction; प्रारब्धाः प्रलयाय<BR>मांसवदहो विक्रेतुमेते वयं Mu. 5. 21;<BR>1. 14; Bg. 14. 14.<BR>--5 Swoon,<BR>fainting, loss of consciousness, syncope;<BR>प्रलयांतोन्मिषिते विलोचने Ku. 4. 2.<BR>--6 (In Rhet.) Loss of<BR>consciousness, considered as one of the 33<BR>subordinate feelings; प्रलयः<BR>सुखदुःखाद्यैर्गाढमिंद्रियमूर्छनं Pratāparudra.<BR>--7<BR>The mystic syllable om.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कालः the time of universal<BR>destruction.<BR>--जलधरः a cloud at the<BR>dissolution of the world.<BR>--दहनः the<BR>fire at the dissolution of the world.<BR>--पयोधिः the ocean at the<BR>dissolution of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलीन
प्रलीन p. p.<BR>1 Melted, dissolved.<BR>--2 Annihilated, destroyed.<BR>--3<BR>Insensible, unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलुठ्
प्रलुठ् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To roll along the<BR>ground, roll, wallow; प्रलुठितमवनौ<BR>विलोक्य कृत्तं Bk. 5. 108.<BR>--2 To be<BR>agitated, heave.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोठनं|प्रलोठन
प्रलोठनं<BR>1 Rolling(on the ground).<BR>--2 Heaving, tossing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलुभ्
प्रलुभ् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be greedy or<BR>desirous, be lustful.<BR>--2 To allure,<BR>seduce, entice.<BR>--3 To pollute<BR>(through lust). --Caus. To allure,<BR>attract, entice, seduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभः|प्रलोभ
प्रलोभः<BR>1 Cupidity, greediness,<BR>covetousness.<BR>--2 Allurement,<BR>seduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभनं|प्रलोभन
प्रलोभनं<BR>1 Attracting.<BR>--2 An<BR>allurement, seduction, temptation.<BR>--3<BR>A lure, bait.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभनी
प्रलोभनी Sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभिन्
प्रलोभिन् a.<BR>1 Greedy of, lusting<BR>after.<BR>--2 Alluring, enticing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोभ्य
प्रलोभ्य a. To be desired or coveted,<BR>attractive, alluring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलून
प्रलून p. p. Cut off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेपः|प्रलेप
प्रलेपः An unguent, an ointment,<BR>a salve; आलिंपन्नमृतमयैरिव प्रलेपैः<BR>U. 3. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेपक|प्रलेपकः
प्रलेपक a. Anointing, smearing.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An anointer, a plasterer.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of slow fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलेहः|प्रलेह
प्रलेहः A kind of broth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रलोल
प्रलोल a. Greatly agitated or<BR>tremulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0758-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवच्
प्रवच् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To speak, say,<BR>address; Pt. 1. 53.<BR>--2 To tell, relate,<BR>announce.<BR>--3 To explain.<BR>--4 To<BR>recite.<BR>--5 To celebrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवक्तृ
प्रवक्तृ m.<BR>1 One who declares or<BR>relates, a speaker, declarer.<BR>--2 A<BR>teacher, expounder; Ms. 8. 20;<BR>Pt. 3. 74.<BR>--3 An orator, eloquent<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवचनं|प्रवचन|प्रवचनः
प्रवचनं<BR>1 Speaking, declaration,<BR>announcement; Pt. 1. 190.<BR>--2<BR>Teaching, expounding.<BR>--3 Exposition,<BR>explanation, interpretation; Mv. 4. 25.<BR>--4 Eloquence.<BR>--5 A sacred treatise<BR>or writing; Ms. 3. 184.<BR>--6 An<BR>expression, a term.<BR>--7 A system of<BR>doctrines (in the form of a treatise).<BR>--8 The fundamental doctrine of the<BR>Buddhists.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पटु a. skilled<BR>in talking, eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवगः|प्रवग
प्रवगः, --प्रवंगः, --प्रवंगमः A monkey;<BR>see प्लवग, प्लवंगः, प्लवंगम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवंगः|प्रवङ्ग|प्रवङ्गः
प्रवगः, --प्रवंगः, --प्रवंगमः A monkey;<BR>see प्लवग, प्लवंगः, प्लवंगम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवंगमः|प्रवङ्गम|प्रवङ्गमः
प्रवगः, --प्रवंगः, --प्रवंगमः A monkey;<BR>see प्लवग, प्लवंगः, प्लवंगम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवटः|प्रवट
प्रवटः Wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवण|प्रवणः
प्रवण a.<BR>1 Sloping down, inclined,<BR>shelving, flowing downwards.<BR>--2<BR>Steep, abrupt, precipitous.<BR>--3<BR>Crooked, bent.<BR>--4 Inclined, disposed to,<BR>tending to (oft. at the end of<BR>comp.); भयेकप्रवणः Ki. 3. 19.<BR>--5<BR>Devoted or attached to, addicted to,<BR>intent on, prone to, full of; नृभिः<BR>प्राणत्राणप्रवणमतिभिः कैश्चिदधुना<BR>Bh. 3. 29; Śi. 8. 35; Mu. 5. 21;<BR>Ki. 2. 44.<BR>--6 Favourably inclined or<BR>disposed towards; Ku. 4. 42.<BR>--7<BR>Eager, ready; Ki. 2. 8.<BR>--8 Endowed<BR>with, possessed of.<BR>--9 Humbled,<BR>modestly humble, submissive.<BR>--10<BR>Decayed, wasted, waning.<BR>--11<BR>Generous.<BR>--णः A place where four<BR>roads meet.<BR>--णं<BR>1 A descent, a<BR>steep descent, precipice.<BR>--2 The side<BR>of a hill, slope, declivity.<BR>--3 The<BR>belly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवणता
प्रवणता<BR>1 Slope, inclination,<BR>declivity.<BR>--2 Propensity, tendency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवणायति
प्रवणायति Den. P. To feel inclined<BR>or disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवणीकृ
प्रवणीकृ {c8c} U. To incline<BR>favourably towards, overcome, win over;<BR>तपसा तत्प्रवणीकृतो हरः Ku. 4. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवत्|प्रवन्त्
प्रवत् f. Ved.<BR>1 A precipice,<BR>declivity.<BR>--2 Height, elevation.<BR>--3 A<BR>sloping path, easy passage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवत्स्यत्
प्रवत्स्यत् a. (ती or न्ती f.) About<BR>to go on a journey.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिका the wife of one who intends to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">Page0759-b+ 56</a>]<BR>go on a journey (one of the 8<BR>Nāyikās in erotic poetry).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवद्
प्रवद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To say, speak,<BR>utter.<BR>--2 To speak to, address;<BR>Bk. 7. 24.<BR>--3 To name, call.<BR>--4 To<BR>regard, consider.<BR>--5 To converse or<BR>talk with.<BR>--6 To proclaim, declare.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to speak.<BR>--2<BR>To play on (a musical<BR>instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवदनं|प्रवदन
प्रवदनं Ved. A proclamation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवादः|प्रवाद
प्रवादः<BR>1 Uttering a word or<BR>sound.<BR>--2 Expressing,<BR>mentioning, declaring.<BR>--3 Discourse,<BR>conversation.<BR>--4 Talk, report,<BR>rumour, popular saying or<BR>belief; अनुरागप्रवादस्तु बत्सयोः<BR>सार्वलौकिकः Māl. 1. 13; व्याघ्रो मानुषं<BR>खादतीति लोकप्रवादो दुर्निवारः H. 1;<BR>Ratn. 4. 15.<BR>--5 A fable or<BR>myth.<BR>--6 Litigious language.<BR>--7<BR>Words of challenge, mutual defiance;<BR>इत्थं प्रवादं युधि संप्रहारं प्रचक्रतू<BR>रामनिशाविहारौ Bk. 2. 36.<BR>--8 A base or<BR>crude form (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवादक
प्रवादक a. Playing on (a<BR>musical instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवादिन्
प्रवादिन् a. Uttering a sound;<BR>speaking, reporting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवप्
प्रवप् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To throw, cast,<BR>offer; Bk. 9. 98.<BR>--2 To scatter,<BR>strew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवप
प्रवप a. Very fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवपणं|प्रवपण
प्रवपणं Ved.<BR>1 Scattering forth.<BR>--2<BR>Shaving or shearing off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयणं|प्रवयण
प्रवयणं<BR>1 The upper part of a<BR>piece of woven cloth.<BR>--2 A goad;<BR>Śi. 13. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवयस्
प्रवयस् a.<BR>1 Advanced in age,<BR>aged, old; केप्येते प्रवयसस्त्वां दिदृक्षयः<BR>U. 4; R. 8. 18.<BR>--2 Ancient, old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर|प्रवरं|प्रवरः
प्रवर a.<BR>1 Chief, principal, most<BR>excellent or distinguished, best,<BR>exalted; संकेतके चिरयति प्रवरो विनोदः<BR>Mk. 3. 3; Ms. 10. 27; Ghaṭ. 16.<BR>--2 Eldest.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A call, summons.<BR>--2 A particular invocation<BR>addressed to Agni by a Brāhmaṇa at the<BR>consecration of his fire.<BR>--3 A line<BR>of ancestors.<BR>--4 A race, family,<BR>lineage.<BR>--5 An ancestor.<BR>--6 A Muni<BR>or noble ancestor who contributes<BR>to the credit of a particular gotra<BR>or family.<BR>--7 Offspring, descendants.<BR>--8 A cover, covering.<BR>--9 An upper<BR>garment.<BR>--10 One of the 42 Gotras,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">Page0759-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--रा N. of a river falling into<BR>Godāvarī.<BR>--रं Aloe-wood<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वाहनौ (du.) an epithet of the<BR>two Aśvins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवरणं|प्रवरण
प्रवरणं<BR>1 Call, summons &c.<BR>--2<BR>(with Buddhists) Festivities at the<BR>end of the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्गः|प्रवर्ग
प्रवर्गः<BR>1 The sacrificial fire.<BR>--2<BR>An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्ग्यः|प्रवर्ग्य
प्रवर्ग्यः A ceremony preliminary<BR>to the Soma sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्जनं|प्रवर्जन
प्रवर्जनं The performance of the<BR>प्रवर्ग्य ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवलाकिन्
प्रवलाकिन् m.<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>--2<BR>A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवस्
प्रवस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To live, dwell.<BR>--2<BR>To go abroad, sojourn, be absent<BR>from home, travel; विधाय वृत्तिं<BR>भार्यायाः प्रवसेत्कार्यवान्नरः Ms. 9. 74;<BR>R. 11. 4. --Caus. To banish, send into<BR>exile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवसनं|प्रवसन
प्रवसनं Going or journeying<BR>abroad, going on a journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासः|प्रवास
प्रवासः (a) Going or<BR>journeying abroad, being absent from one's<BR>home, foreign residence; कुशः<BR>प्रवासस्थकलत्रवेषां (बनितामपश्यत्)<BR>R. 16. 4; Ś. 4. 3; U. 6. 38; Pt. 1. 169;<BR>Bh. 3. 94. (b) A temporary sojourn;<BR>प्रवासादुपावृत्तेन काश्यपेनादिष्टोऽस्मि<BR>Ś. 4.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गत, --स्थ, --स्थित a.<BR>journeying abroad, being absent from<BR>home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासनं|प्रवासन
प्रवासनं<BR>1 Living abroad,<BR>temporary sojourn.<BR>--2 Exile, banishment.<BR>--3 Killing, slaughter.<BR>--4 Going from<BR>a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासित
प्रवासित a. Banished, exiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवासिन्
प्रवासिन् m. A traveller, wayfarer,<BR>sojourner; Ku. 4. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्
प्रवह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bear, carry, draw<BR>along.<BR>--2 To waft, carry or bear<BR>along; Bk. 8. 52.<BR>--3 To support,<BR>bear up (as a burden).<BR>--4 To<BR>flow, stream forth.<BR>--5 To blow.<BR>--6 To have, possess, feel.<BR>--7 To<BR>breathe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहः|प्रवह
प्रवहः<BR>1 Flowing or streaming<BR>forth.<BR>--2 Wind.<BR>--3 N. of one of<BR>the seven courses of wind (said to<BR>cause the motion of the planets).<BR>--4 A reservoir into which water is<BR>carried off.<BR>--5 Going forth, going<BR>from a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवहणं|प्रवहण
प्रवहणं<BR>1 A covered carriage or<BR>litter (for women).<BR>--2 A carriage,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">Page0760-a+ 57</a>]<BR>conveyance, vehicle in general.<BR>--3<BR>A ship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0759-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहः|प्रवाह
प्रवाहः<BR>1 Flowing or streaming<BR>forth.<BR>--2 A stream, course,<BR>current; प्रवाहस्ते वारां श्रियमयमपारां दिशतु<BR>नः G. L. 2; R. 5. 46; 13. 10, 48;<BR>Ku. 1. 54; Me. 46.<BR>--3 Flow,<BR>running water.<BR>--4 Continuous flow,<BR>unbroken succession, continuity.<BR>--5<BR>Course of events (rolling onward<BR>like a stream).<BR>--6 Activity, active<BR>occupation.<BR>--7 A pond, lake.<BR>--8<BR>Course or direction towards.<BR>--9 An<BR>excellent horse. (प्रवाहेमूत्रितं) means<BR>(lit.) making water in a stream;<BR>(fig.) doing a useless action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहक|प्रवाहकः
प्रवाहक a. Carrying off or<BR>forward.<BR>--कः A goblin, an imp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहनं|प्रवाहन
प्रवाहनं<BR>1 Driving forth.<BR>--2<BR>Evacuation by stool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहणी
प्रवाहणी The sphincter muscle<BR>which ejects the faces from the<BR>rectum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहिका
प्रवाहिका Diarrhœa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाहिन्
प्रवाहिन् a.<BR>1 Carrying forward,<BR>driving onward.<BR>--2 Carrying away.<BR>--3 Flowing, streaming forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाही
प्रवाही Sand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्लिः|प्रवह्लि
प्रवह्लिः --ह्ली See प्रहेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवह्ली
प्रवह्लिः --ह्ली See प्रहेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाकः|प्रवाक
प्रवाकः A proclaimer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाच्
प्रवाच् a.<BR>1 Eloquent, oratorical; (<BR>कुर्वते) जडानप्यनुलोमार्थान् प्रवाचः कृतिनां<BR>गिरः Śi. 2. 25.<BR>--2 Talkative,<BR>garrulous; Mu. 3. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाचक|प्रवाचकः
प्रवाचक a.<BR>1 Explanatory.<BR>--2<BR>Eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाचनं|प्रवाचन
प्रवाचनं<BR>1 Proclamation,<BR>promulgation, declaration.<BR>--2 A designation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाच्यं|प्रवाच्य
प्रवाच्यं A literary production or<BR>composition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाणं|प्रवाण
प्रवाणं The trimming or edging<BR>of a piece of woven cloth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाणिः|प्रवाणि
प्रवाणिः --णी f. A weaver's<BR>shuttle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाणी
प्रवाणिः --णी f. A weaver's<BR>shuttle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवात
प्रवात p. p. Exposed to stormy<BR>wind.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A current of air, fresh<BR>or free air; प्रवातशयनस्था देवी<BR>M. 4.<BR>--2 A strong or stormy wind; ननु<BR>प्रवातेऽपि निष्क्रंपा गिरयः Ś. 6.<BR>--3 An<BR>airy place; Ku. 1. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवारः|प्रवार
प्रवारः, प्रवारकः A cover, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवारकः|प्रवारक
प्रवारः, प्रवारकः A cover, covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवारणं|प्रवारण
प्रवारणं<BR>1 Satisfying(a desire).<BR>--2 Priority of choice.<BR>--3<BR>Prohibition, opposition.<BR>--4 A free-will<BR>offering (काम्यदान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवाल|प्रवालं|प्रवालः
प्रवाल See प्रबाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविकीर्ण
प्रविकीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Scattered or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">Page0760-b+ 54</a>]<BR>strewed about.<BR>--2 Dispersed,<BR>diffused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविख्यात
प्रविख्यात p. p.<BR>1 Named,<BR>called.<BR>--2 Famous, renowned,<BR>celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविख्यातिः|प्रविख्याति
प्रविख्यातिः f. Fame, renown,<BR>celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचयः|प्रविचय
प्रविचयः Examination,<BR>investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचर्
प्रविचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To roam about.<BR>--2<BR>To move onward, advance.<BR>--3 To<BR>wander through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचरः
प्रविचरः Discernment,<BR>discrimination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचल्
प्रविचल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To shake,<BR>tremble.<BR>--2 To deviate, swerve from, go<BR>astray; Bh. 2. 83.<BR>--3 To become<BR>confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचलित
प्रविचलित a. Moved, set in motion,<BR>shaken.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविचेतनं|प्रविचेतन
प्रविचेतनं Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवितत
प्रवितत p. p.<BR>1 Spread out,<BR>expanded.<BR>--2 Dishevelled,<BR>disordered (hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविदारः|प्रविदार
प्रविदारः Bursting asunder,<BR>opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविदारणं|प्रविदारण
प्रविदारणं<BR>1 Tearing, rending,<BR>breaking, bursting asunder.<BR>--2<BR>Budding.<BR>--3 Conflict, war, battle.<BR>--4<BR>Crowd, confusion, tumult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविद्ध
प्रविद्ध p. p. Cast away, thrown off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविद्रुत
प्रविद्रुत p. p. Dispersed, put to<BR>flight, scattered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविधा
प्रविधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To decide.<BR>--2 To<BR>do or make.<BR>--3 To meditate, think<BR>upon.<BR>--4 To place in front or at<BR>the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविधानं|प्रविधान
प्रविधानं<BR>1 Thinking upon.<BR>--2<BR>Doing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविध्वस्त
प्रविध्वस्त a.<BR>1 Thrown away.<BR>--2<BR>Agitated, disturbed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविपलः|प्रविपल|प्रविपलं
प्रविपलः --लं A small part of a<BR>vipala q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविपलं|प्रविपल|प्रविपलः
प्रविपलः --लं A small part of a<BR>vipala q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभज्
प्रविभज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sever, separate.<BR>--2 To divide, distribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभक्त
प्रविभक्त p. p.<BR>1 Severed,<BR>separated.<BR>--2 Apportioned, partitioned,<BR>divided, distributed; ज्योतींषि वर्तयति<BR>च प्रविभक्तरश्मिः Ś. 7. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविभागः|प्रविभाग
प्रविभागः Division, distribution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविरः|प्रविर
प्रविरः Yellow sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविरल
प्रविरल a.<BR>1 Separated by a<BR>great interval, isolated, separate.<BR>--2<BR>Very few or rare, very scanty; प्रवि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">Page0760-c+ 56</a>]<BR>रला इव मुग्धवधूकथाः R. 9. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविलयः|प्रविलय
प्रविलयः<BR>1 Melting away.<BR>--2<BR>Complete dissolution or absorption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविलुप्त
प्रविलुप्त p. p. Cut off, fallen or<BR>rubbed off, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविवादः|प्रविवाद
प्रविवादः Dispute, quarrel,<BR>wrangling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविविक्त
प्रविविक्त a.<BR>1 Very solitary.<BR>--2<BR>Separated, detached.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविश्
प्रविश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To enter into;<BR>Ku. 5. 51.<BR>--2 To enter upon, commence,<BR>--3 To appear. --Caus.<BR>1 To admit,<BR>introduce, usher; त्वरितं प्रवेशय U. 1.<BR>--2 To lay or store up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविष्ट|प्रविष्टः
प्रविष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Gone or entered<BR>into; पश्चार्धेन प्रविष्टः<BR>शरपतनभयाद्भूयसा पूर्वकायं Ś. 1. 7.<BR>--2<BR>Engaged in, occupied with.<BR>--3 Begun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविष्टकं|प्रविष्टक
प्रविष्टकं<BR>1 Fntrance on the stage.<BR>--2 Entering a room.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशः|प्रवेश
प्रवेशः<BR>1 Entrance, penetration;<BR>पुरप्रवेशाभिमुखो बभूव R. 7. 1;<BR>Ku. 3. 60.<BR>--2 Ingress, access, approach.<BR>--3 Entrance on the stage; तेन<BR>पात्रप्रवेशश्चेत् S. D. 6.<BR>--4 The entrance or<BR>door (of a house &c.).<BR>--5 Income,<BR>revenue.<BR>--6 Close application (to a<BR>pursuit), intentness of purpose.<BR>--7<BR>The entrance of the sun into a sign<BR>of the zodiac.<BR>--8 Coming on,<BR>setting in (of night).<BR>--9 The syringe<BR>of a clyster-pipe. (Proverb:<BR>--चंचुप्रवेशो मुसलप्रवेशः; cf. ‘the thin end of<BR>the wedge’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशकः|प्रवेशक
प्रवेशकः ‘The introducer,’ an<BR>interlude acted by inferior characters<BR>(such as servants, buffoon &c.)<BR>for the purpose of acquainting the<BR>audience with events not<BR>represented on the stage, but a knowledge<BR>of which is essential for the proper<BR>understanding of what follows;<BR>(like the Viṣkambhaka it<BR>connects the story of the drama and<BR>the subdivisions of the plot, by<BR>briefly referring to what has<BR>occurred in the intervals of the acts,<BR>or what is likely to happen at the<BR>end; it never occurs at the beginning<BR>of the first act or at the end of the<BR>last). S. D. thus defines it: --प्रवेशकोऽ<BR>नुदात्तोक्त्या नीचपात्रप्रयोजितः । अंकद्वयांतर्विज्ञेयः<BR>शेषं विष्कंभके यथा ॥ 308; see विष्कंभक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशनं|प्रवेशन
प्रवेशनं<BR>1 Entrance, penetration,<BR>going into.<BR>--2 Introducing, leading<BR>to, conducting.<BR>--3 An entrance to the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">Page0761-a+ 55</a>]<BR>main door of a house, gate.<BR>--4<BR>Sexual intercourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0760-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेशित
प्रवेशित p. p. Introduced, showed<BR>in, led or conducted to, brought in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेश्य
प्रवेश्य a.<BR>1 To be entered.<BR>--2 To<BR>be penetrated or pervaded.<BR>--3 To<BR>be played (as a musical instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविश्लेषः|प्रविश्लेष
प्रविश्लेषः Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविषण्ण
प्रविषण्ण^1 a. Dejected, spiritless.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविषा
प्रविषा A birch tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविस्तरः|प्रविस्तर
प्रविस्त(स्ता)रः Extent,<BR>circumference, compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रविस्तारः|प्रविस्तार
प्रविस्त(स्ता)रः Extent,<BR>circumference, compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीण|प्रवीणः
प्रवीण a. Clever, skilled or<BR>versed in, conversant with; आमोदानथ<BR>हरिदंतराणि नेतुं नैवान्यो जगति<BR>समीरणात्प्रवीणः Bv. 1. 15; Ku. 7. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवीर|प्रवीरः
प्रवीर a.<BR>1 Foremost, best, most<BR>excellent or distinguished;<BR>R. 14. 29; 16. 1; Bg. 11. 48.<BR>--2 Strong,<BR>powerful, heroic.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A brave<BR>person, hero, warrior.<BR>--2 A chief,<BR>distinguished personage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृ
प्रवृ {c5c} U.<BR>1 To cover, envelop;<BR>प्रावारिषुरिव क्षोणीं क्षिप्ता वृक्षाः समंततः<BR>Bk. 9. 25.<BR>--2 To wear, put on.<BR>--3<BR>To choose, select.<BR>--4 To keep or<BR>ward off (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत
प्रवृत p. p. Selected, picked, chosen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्
प्रवृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To go, forward,<BR>move on, proceed; स्वामिसेवकयोरेवं<BR>वृत्तिचक्रं प्रवर्तते Pt. 1. 81.<BR>--2 To arise,<BR>be produced, spring; Pt. 1. 6.<BR>--3<BR>To happen, come to pass, take place.<BR>--4 To begin, commence (usually<BR>with inf.); हंत प्रवृत्तं संगीतकं M. 1;<BR>Ku. 3. 25.<BR>--5 To strive, exert<BR>oneself; प्रवर्ततां प्रकृतिहिताय पार्थिवः<BR>Ś. 7. 35.<BR>--6 To act up to, follow;<BR>Pt. 1. 116.<BR>--7 To engage in, be occupied<BR>with; Ku. 5. 33.<BR>--8 To act, do;<BR>न पुनरेवं प्रवर्तितव्यं Ś. 6.<BR>--9 To act or<BR>behave towards.<BR>--10 To prevail,<BR>exist; राजन् प्रजासु ते कश्चिदपचारः<BR>प्रवर्तते R. 15. 47.<BR>--11 To hold good.<BR>--12 To proceed uninterruptedly,<BR>thrive; Bg. 17. 24; Ms. 3. 61.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To proceed with,<BR>continue; Mu. 2.<BR>--2 To introduce.<BR>--3<BR>To set on foot, establish, found.<BR>--4<BR>To drive, propel, urge, stimulate.<BR>--5 To promote, advance.<BR>--6 To<BR>throw, cast.<BR>--7 To produce, create.<BR>--8 To invent, devise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तः|प्रवर्त|प्रवर्त्त
प्रवर्तः<BR>1 Commencing,<BR>undertaking, engaging in.<BR>--2 Excitement,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-b" target="_blank">Page0761-b+ 57</a>]<BR>stimulus.<BR>--3 Ved. A round<BR>ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तक|प्रवर्तकः|प्रवर्त्तक|प्रवर्त्तकः
प्रवर्तक a. (र्तिका f.)<BR>1 Setting on<BR>foot, founding.<BR>--2 Advancing,<BR>promoting, furthering.<BR>--3 Producing,<BR>causing.<BR>--4 Prompting, urging,<BR>inducing, instigating (in a bad sense).<BR>--कः<BR>1 An originator, founder,<BR>author.<BR>--2 A prompter, instigator.<BR>--3 An arbiter, umpire.<BR>--कं The<BR>entrance of a character on the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तनं|प्रवर्तन|प्रवर्त्तन|प्रवर्त्तनं
प्रवर्तनं<BR>1 Going on, moving<BR>forward.<BR>--2 Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--3 Setting on foot, founding,<BR>establishing, instituting.<BR>--4<BR>Prompting, urging, stimulating, inciting.<BR>--5<BR>Engaging in, applying oneself to.<BR>--6 Happening, coming to pass.<BR>--7<BR>Activity, action.<BR>--8 Behaviour,<BR>conduct, procedure.<BR>--9 Directing,<BR>superintending.<BR>--10 Employment.<BR>--11 Exhortation.<BR>--ना Inciting or<BR>prompting to action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तयितृ
प्रवर्तयितृ a. One who sets in<BR>motion, urges, establishes, founds &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तित|प्रवर्त्तित|प्रवर्त्तितः
प्रवर्तित p. p.<BR>1 Caused to turn,<BR>made to go or roll onwards,<BR>revolving; R. 9. 66.<BR>--2 Founded, set up,<BR>established.<BR>--3 Prompted, incited,<BR>instigated.<BR>--4 Kindled; R. 5. 37.<BR>--5<BR>Caused, made.<BR>--6 Purified, rendered<BR>pure; Ms. 11. 196.<BR>--7 Informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्तिन्
प्रवर्तिन् a.<BR>1 Proceeding, moving<BR>onward.<BR>--2 Being active.<BR>--3<BR>Causing, effecting.<BR>--4 Using.<BR>--5 Arising<BR>from, flowing; Ś. 3. 14.<BR>--6<BR>Spreading &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्त|प्रवृत्तः
प्रवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Begun,<BR>commenced, proceeded with.<BR>--2 Set in;<BR>अचिरप्रवृत्तं ग्रीष्मसमयमधिकृत्य Ś. 1.<BR>--3<BR>Engaged in, occupied with.<BR>--4<BR>Going to, bound for.<BR>--5 Fixed, settled,<BR>determined.<BR>--6 Unimpeded,<BR>undisputed.<BR>--7 Round.<BR>--त्तः A round<BR>ornament.<BR>--त्तं An action,<BR>undertaking.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तकं|प्रवृत्तक
प्रवृत्तकं Entrance on the stage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृत्तिः|प्रवृत्ति
प्रवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Continued advance.<BR>--2 Rise, origin, source, flow (of<BR>words &c.); प्रवृत्तिरासीच्छब्दानां<BR>चरितार्था चतुष्टयी Ku. 2. 17.<BR>--3<BR>Appearance, manifestation;<BR>कुसुमप्रवृत्तिसमये Ś. 4. 17 v. l.; R. 11. 43; 14. 39;<BR>15. 4.<BR>--4 Advent, setting in,<BR>commencement; आकालिकीं वीक्ष्य<BR>मधुप्रवृत्तिं Ku. 3. 34.<BR>--5 Application or<BR>addiction to, tendency, inclination,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">Page0761-c+ 56</a>]<BR>predilection, propensity; सतां हि स<BR>देहपदेषु वस्तषु प्रमाणमंतः करणप्रवृत्तयः<BR>Ś. 1. 22.<BR>--6 Conduct; behaviour;<BR>R. 14. 73.<BR>--7 Employment, occupation,<BR>activity; Ku. 6. 26.<BR>--8 Use,<BR>employment, currency (as of a word).<BR>--9 Continued effort, perseverance.<BR>--10 Signification, sense, acceptation<BR>(of a word).<BR>--11 Continuance,<BR>permanence, prevalence.<BR>--12 Active<BR>life, taking an active part in<BR>worldly affairs (opp. निवृत्ति).<BR>--13 News,<BR>tidings, intelligence; जीमूतेन<BR>स्वकुशलमयीं हारयिष्यन् प्रवृत्तिं Me. 4;<BR>V. 4. 20.<BR>--14 Applicability or validity of<BR>a rule.<BR>--15 Fate, destiny, luck.<BR>--16<BR>Cognition, direct perception or<BR>apprehension.<BR>--17 Rutting juice, or<BR>ichor exuding from the temples of<BR>an elephant in rut.<BR>--18 N. of the<BR>city of उज्जयिनी q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञः<BR>a spy, secret emissary or agent.<BR>--निमित्तं a reason for the use of any<BR>term in a particular signification.<BR>--पराङ्मुख a. averse to giving news;<BR>V. 4. 20.<BR>--मार्गः active or worldly<BR>life, attachment to the business<BR>and pleasures of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृध्
प्रवृध् {c1c} A. To grow, increase, be<BR>augmented --Caus. To increase,<BR>augment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्धनं|प्रवर्धन|प्रवर्द्धनं
प्रवर्धनं Increasing, augmenting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृद्ध|प्रवृद्धः
प्रवृद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Full-grown.<BR>--2<BR>Increased, augmented, expanded,<BR>enlarged.<BR>--3 Full, deep.<BR>--4 Haughty,<BR>arrogant.<BR>--5 Violent.<BR>--6 Large.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृद्धिः|प्रवृद्धि
प्रवृद्धिः f.<BR>1 Increase, growth;<BR>R. 13. 71; 17. 71.<BR>--2 Rise, prosperity,<BR>preferment, promotion, elevation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवृष्
प्रवृष् {c1c} P. To begin to rain, rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्षः|प्रवर्ष
प्रवर्षः Heavy rain, heavy<BR>downpour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्षणं|प्रवर्षण
प्रवर्षणं<BR>1 Raining.<BR>--2 The first rain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवर्षिन्
प्रवर्षिन् a. Raining, causing to<BR>rain, showering or pouring down,<BR>discharging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेक|प्रवेकः
प्रवेक a. Best, chief, choicest,<BR>most excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेगः|प्रवेग
प्रवेगः Great speed, velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेटः|प्रवेट
प्रवेटः Barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणिः|प्रवेणि
प्रवेणिः --णी f.<BR>1 A braid of hair<BR>(in general); R. 15. 30.<BR>--2 The<BR>hair twisted and unadorned<BR>(worn by wives in the absence of<BR>their husbands).<BR>--3 The housings<BR>of an elephant.<BR>--4 A piece of colour<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">Page0762-a+ 55</a>]<BR>ed woollen cloth.<BR>--5 The current or<BR>stream (of a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेणी
प्रवेणिः --णी f.<BR>1 A braid of hair<BR>(in general); R. 15. 30.<BR>--2 The<BR>hair twisted and unadorned<BR>(worn by wives in the absence of<BR>their husbands).<BR>--3 The housings<BR>of an elephant.<BR>--4 A piece of colour<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">Page0762-a+ 55</a>]<BR>ed woollen cloth.<BR>--5 The current or<BR>stream (of a river).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0761-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेतृ
प्रवेतृ m. A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेदनं|प्रवेदन
प्रवेदनं Making known,<BR>announcing, proclaiming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपः|प्रवेप
प्रवेपः, प्रवेपकः, प्रवेपथुः, प्रवेपनं<BR>Trembling, quivering, shaking,<BR>tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपकः|प्रवेपक
प्रवेपः, प्रवेपकः, प्रवेपथुः, प्रवेपनं<BR>Trembling, quivering, shaking,<BR>tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपथुः|प्रवेपथु
प्रवेपः, प्रवेपकः, प्रवेपथुः, प्रवेपनं<BR>Trembling, quivering, shaking,<BR>tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेपनं|प्रवेपन
प्रवेपः, प्रवेपकः, प्रवेपथुः, प्रवेपनं<BR>Trembling, quivering, shaking,<BR>tremour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेरित
प्रवेरित a. Cast hither and<BR>thither, thrown about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेलः|प्रवेल
प्रवेलः A kind of kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रवेष्टः|प्रवेष्ट
प्रवेष्टः^1<BR>1 An arm.<BR>--2 The wrist<BR>or forearm.<BR>--3 The fleshy part of an<BR>elephant's back (where the rider<BR>sits).<BR>--4 An elephant's gums.<BR>--5<BR>An elephant's housings.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: alph. order and sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यक्त|प्रव्यक्तं
प्रव्यक्त p. p. Apparent, clear,<BR>manifest, evident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्यक्तिः|प्रव्यक्ति
प्रव्यक्तिः f. Manifestation,<BR>appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्याहारः|प्रव्याहार
प्रव्याहारः Prolongation of<BR>discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्
प्रव्रज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go into exile.<BR>--2 To renounce all worldly<BR>attachments, enter on the fourth stage in<BR>life, i. e. to become a Saṃnyāsin;<BR>Ms. 6. 38; 8. 363. --Caus. To<BR>banish, send into exile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजनं|प्रव्रजन
प्रव्रजनं<BR>1 Going abroad,<BR>sojourning.<BR>--2 Going into exile.<BR>--3<BR>Turning a recluse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रजित|प्रव्रजितः
प्रव्रजित p. p.<BR>1 Gone abroad or<BR>into exile.<BR>--2 Turned a recluse.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A religious mendicant or<BR>ascetic in general.<BR>--2 Especially, a<BR>Brāhmaṇa who has entered on the<BR>fourth (भिक्षु) order.<BR>--3 The pupil<BR>of a Jaina or Buddhist mendicant.<BR>--ता<BR>1 A female ascetic.<BR>--2 A<BR>spikenard.<BR>--तं Turning a recluse, the<BR>life of a religious mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रज्या
प्रव्रज्या<BR>1 Going abroad, migration.<BR>--2 Roaming, wandering about as a<BR>religious mendicant; Māl. 4. 6.<BR>--3<BR>The order of a religious mendicant,<BR>a mendicant's life, the fourth (or<BR>भिक्षु) order in the religious life of a<BR>Brāhmaṇa; प्रव्रज्यां कल्पवृक्षा इवाश्रिताः<BR>Ku. 6. 6 (where Malli. says प्रव्रज्या<BR>means the वानप्रस्थ or third order).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवसितः a religious<BR>mendicant who renounces his order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राज्
प्रव्राज् m. प्रव्राजकः A religious<BR>mendicant, recluse.<BR>--जिका A<BR>female ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्राजनं|प्रव्राजन
प्रव्राजनं Banishing, exile, sending<BR>into exile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रव्रश्चनः|प्रव्रश्चन
प्रव्रश्चनः A knife for cutting wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंस्
प्रशंस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To praise, extol,<BR>approve, speak approvingly of,<BR>commend; हरिणा युवतिः प्रशशंसे Gīt. 1;<BR>यच्च बाचा प्रशस्यते Ms. 5. 127;<BR>प्राशंसीत्तं निशाचरः Bk. 15. 65; R. 5. 25;<BR>17. 36.<BR>--2 To esteem, value.<BR>--3 To<BR>declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसक
प्रशंसक, प्रशंसिन् a. Praising,<BR>laudatory, eulogistic. --m. A panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसिन्
प्रशंसक, प्रशंसिन् a. Praising,<BR>laudatory, eulogistic. --m. A panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसनं|प्रशंसन
प्रशंसनं Praising, extolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसा
प्रशंसा<BR>1 Praise, eulogy,<BR>panegyric, applause; प्रशंसावचनं ‘a<BR>complimentary or laudatory remark.’<BR>--2<BR>Description, reference to; as in<BR>अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा q. v.<BR>--3 Glory, fame,<BR>reputation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपमा one of<BR>the several kinds of उपमा<BR>mentioned by Daṇḍin; ब्रह्मणोऽप्युद्भवः पद्मश्चंद्रः<BR>शंभुशिरोधृतः । तौ तुल्यौ त्वन्मुखेनेति सा<BR>प्रशंसोपमोच्यते ॥ Kāv. 2. 31.<BR>--मुखर a.<BR>loudly praising.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशंसित
प्रशंसित^1 p. p. Praised, extolled,<BR>applauded.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्त|प्रशस्तं
प्रशस्त p. p.<BR>1 Praised, lauded,<BR>commended, eulogised.<BR>--2<BR>Praiseworthy, commendable.<BR>--3 Best,<BR>excellent.<BR>--4 Blossed, happy,<BR>auspicious.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद्रिः N. of a<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्तिः|प्रशस्ति
प्रशस्तिः f.<BR>1 Praise, eulogy,<BR>laudation.<BR>--2 Description; U. 7.<BR>--3 A<BR>panegyric or small poem written in<BR>praise of any one (e. g. a patron.).<BR>--4 Excellence, eminence.<BR>--5<BR>Bonediction.<BR>--6 Guidance, instruction,<BR>rule for guidance; as in लेखप्रशस्तिः<BR>‘a form of writing’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशस्य|प्रशस्यः
प्रशस्य a. (Compar. श्रेयस् or ज्यायस्,<BR>superl. श्रेष्ठ or ज्येष्ठ) Praiseworthy,<BR>commendable, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशत्त्वन्
प्रशत्त्वन् m. The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशत्त्वरी
प्रशत्त्वरी A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशम्
प्रशम् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To become calm or<BR>tranquil.<BR>--2 To be soothed or<BR>appeased.<BR>--3 To stop, cease, terminate.<BR>--4 To be allayed, be quenched or<BR>extinguished; प्रशांतं पावकास्त्रं U. 6;<BR>Pt. 3. 56.<BR>--5 To decay, wither<BR>away. --Caus.<BR>1 To soothe, appease,<BR>pacify; Ms. 8. 391.<BR>--2 To allay,<BR>extinguish, quench, put down;<BR>त्वामासारप्रशमितवनोपप्लवं Me. 17.<BR>--3<BR>To remove, put an end to; तं (<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-c" target="_blank">Page0762-c+ 57</a>]<BR>अपचारं) अन्विष्य प्रशमयेः R. 15. 47.<BR>--4 To conquer, vanquish, subdue;<BR>Mk. 10. 60.<BR>--5 To settle, adjust,<BR>compose; प्रशमयसि विवादं कल्पसे<BR>रक्षणाय Ś. 5. 8.<BR>--6 To kill, destroy.<BR>--7<BR>To cure, heal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमः|प्रशम
प्रशमः<BR>1 Calmness, tranquillity,<BR>composure; प्रशमस्थित पूर्वपार्थिवं<BR>R. 8. 15; Ki. 2. 32.<BR>--2 Peace, rest.<BR>--3<BR>Extinction, abatement; Ku. 2. 20.<BR>--4 Cessation, end, destruction;<BR>Śi. 20. 73.<BR>--5 Pacification,<BR>appeasement; Śi. 16. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमन|प्रशमनं
प्रशमन a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Calming,<BR>tranquillizing, pacifying, removing &c.<BR>--2 Curing, healing.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Calming,<BR>tranquillizing, pacifying.<BR>--2<BR>Allaying, assuaging, soothing, mitigating;<BR>आपन्नार्तिप्रशमनफलाः संपदो ह्युत्तमानां<BR>Me. 53.<BR>--3 Curing, healing; as in<BR>ष्याधिप्रशमनं.<BR>--4 Quenching,<BR>extinguishing, suppressing, quelling.<BR>--5<BR>Cessation, abatement.<BR>--6<BR>Bestowing fitly or on fit objects;<BR>Ms. 7. 56; (सत्पात्रे प्रतिपादनं Kull.; but<BR>others give it the next sense).<BR>--7 Securing, guarding, keeping safe;<BR>लब्धप्रशप्ननस्वस्थमथैनं समुपस्थिता<BR>R. 4. 14.<BR>--8 Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशमित
प्रशमित p. p.<BR>1 Pacified, soothed,<BR>composed, appeased, allayed.<BR>--2<BR>Extinguished, quenched.<BR>--3 Atoned<BR>for, expiated; U. 1. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशांत|प्रशान्त|प्रशान्तः
प्रशांत p. p.<BR>1 Calmed,<BR>tranquillized, composed.<BR>--2 Calm, serene, quiet,<BR>sedate, still; अहो<BR>प्रशांतरमणीयतोद्यानस्य.<BR>--3 Tamed, subdued, quelled.<BR>--4 Ended, ceased, over;<BR>तत्सर्वमेकपद एव मम प्रशांतं Māl. 9. 36;<BR>प्रशांतमस्त्रं U. 6 ‘ceased to work or<BR>withdrawn.’<BR>--5 Dead, deceased; (see शम्<BR>with प्र).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>composed in mind, peaceful, calm.<BR>--ऊर्ज a. weakened, enervated,<BR>prostrated.<BR>--काम a. content.<BR>--चेष्ट a.<BR>resting, ceased to work.<BR>--बाध a.<BR>having all obstacles or calamities<BR>removed; Ki. 1. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशांतिः|प्रशान्ति|प्रशांति|प्रशान्तिः
प्रशांतिः f.<BR>1 Calmness,<BR>tranquillity, composure, quiet, repose.<BR>--2<BR>Rest, cessation, abatement.<BR>--3<BR>Allaying, quenching, extinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशामः|प्रशाम
प्रशामः<BR>1 Tranquillity, calm,<BR>composure.<BR>--2 Quenching, extinction,<BR>allaying.<BR>--3 Cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाख
प्रशाख a.<BR>1 Having many or<BR>spreading branches.<BR>--2 Being in the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">Page0763-a+ 55</a>]<BR>5th stage of formation (said of<BR>the embryo, when the hands and<BR>feet are formed).<BR>--खा A small<BR>branch or twig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0762-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशाखिका
प्रशाखिका A small branch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशास्
प्रशास् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To teach, instruct,<BR>advise; Bk. 19. 19.<BR>--2 To order,<BR>command; प्रशाधि यन्मया कार्यं Mārk.<BR>P.<BR>--3 To rule, govern, be lord of;<BR>द्यां प्रशाधि गलितावधिकालं N. 5. 24;<BR>R. 6. 76; 9. 1.<BR>--4 To punish,<BR>chastise.<BR>--5 To pray or ask for, seek<BR>for (Atm.); इदं कविभ्यः पूर्वेभ्यो<BR>नमोवाकं प्रशास्महे U. 1. 1 (used in the<BR>sense of शास् with आ q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासकः|प्रशासक
प्रशासकः<BR>1 A director, ruler.<BR>--2 A<BR>spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशासनं|प्रशासन
प्रशासनं<BR>1 Governing, ruling.<BR>--2<BR>Enjoining, exacting.<BR>--3<BR>Government.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशास्तृ
प्रशास्तृ m.<BR>1 A king, ruler,<BR>governor.<BR>--2 A director, adviser;<BR>Pt. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिष्ट
प्रशिष्ट p. p. Ruled over, governed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिष्टिः|प्रशिष्टि
प्रशिष्टिः, प्रशिस् f. Ved. Command,<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिस्
प्रशिष्टिः, प्रशिस् f. Ved. Command,<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिथिल
प्रशिथिल a. Very loose;<BR>Ś. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशिष्यः|प्रशिष्य
प्रशिष्यः The pupil of a pupil,<BR>the disciple of a disciple;<BR>शिष्यप्रशिष्यैरुपगीयमानमवेहि तन्मंडनमिश्रधाम<BR>Śāṅkaradigvijaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशुद्धिः|प्रशुद्धि
प्रशुद्धिः f. Clearness, purity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशोषः|प्रशोष
प्रशोषः Becoming dry, drying up,<BR>aridity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्चोतनं|प्रश्चोतन
प्रश्चोतनं Sprinkling, oozing;<BR>U. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नः|प्रश्न
प्रश्नः [प्रच्छ्-भावे नङ्]<BR>1 A<BR>question, query; an inquiry,<BR>interrogation (अविज्ञातप्रवचनं प्रश्न इत्यभिधीयते);<BR>अनामयप्रश्नपूर्वकं Ś. 5 ‘with an<BR>inquiry about (your) well-being or<BR>health’.<BR>--2 A judicial inquiry or<BR>investigation.<BR>--3 A point at issue,<BR>a subject of controversy,<BR>controverted or disputed point; इति प्रश्न<BR>उपस्थितः.<BR>--4 A problem for solution<BR>or calculation; अहं ते प्रश्नं दास्यामि<BR>Mk. 5.<BR>--5 Inquiry into the future.<BR>--6 A short section of a work.<BR>--7<BR>Basket-work.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपनिषद् n.<BR>N. of an Upaniṣad consisting of<BR>six questions and six answers.<BR>--दूतिः -ती f. a riddle, an enigma.<BR>--विवाकः an arbitrator, umpire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्नयति
प्रश्नयति Den. P. To inquire after,<BR>ask about (with two acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रथः|प्रश्रथ
प्रश्रथः Laxity, looseness,<BR>relaxation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रब्धिः|प्रश्रब्धि
प्रश्रब्धिः f. Trust, confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रयः|प्रश्रय
प्रश्रयः, --प्रश्रयणं<BR>1 Respect,<BR>courtesy, civility, politeness, respectful<BR>or courteous behaviour, humility;<BR>समागतैः प्रश्रयनम्रमूर्तिभिः Śi. 12. 33;<BR>R. 10. 70, 83; U. 6. 23; सप्रश्रयं<BR>respectfully, modestly.<BR>--2 Love,<BR>affection, regard; Pt. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रयणं|प्रश्रयण
प्रश्रयः, --प्रश्रयणं<BR>1 Respect,<BR>courtesy, civility, politeness, respectful<BR>or courteous behaviour, humility;<BR>समागतैः प्रश्रयनम्रमूर्तिभिः Śi. 12. 33;<BR>R. 10. 70, 83; U. 6. 23; सप्रश्रयं<BR>respectfully, modestly.<BR>--2 Love,<BR>affection, regard; Pt. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रयिन्
प्रश्रयिन्, प्रश्रित a. Civil, polite,<BR>courteous, humble, well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्रित|प्रश्रितः
प्रश्रयिन्, प्रश्रित a. Civil, polite,<BR>courteous, humble, well-behaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लथ|प्रश्लथः
प्रश्लथ a.<BR>1 Very loose or flaccid.<BR>--2 Spiritless, unnerved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लिष्ट|प्रश्लिष्टः
प्रश्लिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Twisted,<BR>entwined.<BR>--2 Reasonable, well-argued or<BR>reasoned (युक्तियुत).<BR>--ष्टः<BR>1 A term<BR>applied to the Saṃdhi of the vowel<BR>अ with a following vowel and of<BR>other vowels with other<BR>homegeneous ones.<BR>--2 The vowel resulting<BR>from this Saṃdhi.<BR>--3 The accent<BR>with which such substituted vowel<BR>is pronounced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्लेषः|प्रश्लेष
प्रश्लेषः<BR>1 Close contact, pressing<BR>hard against.<BR>--2 Euphonic coalition<BR>of vowels.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रश्वासः|प्रश्वास
प्रश्वासः Breath, respiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्टिः|प्रष्टि
प्रष्टिः Ved.<BR>1 A side-horse.<BR>--2<BR>A by-stander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठ|प्रष्ठः
प्रष्ठ a.<BR>1 Standing or being in<BR>front; R. 15. 10.<BR>--2 Chief,<BR>principal, foremost, best; a leader;<BR>पुलस्त्यप्रष्ठः Mv. 1. 30; 6. 30;<BR>Śi. 19. 30.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वाह् m. a young<BR>bull being trained for the plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रष्ठौही
प्रष्ठौही A cow for the first time<BR>with a calf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्
प्रस् {c1c} {c4c} A. (प्रस-स्य-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>bring forth young.<BR>--2 To spread,<BR>diffuse, expand, extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंख्या|प्रसङ्ख्या
प्रसंख्या<BR>1 Total number, sum.<BR>--2<BR>Reflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंख्यानः|प्रसङ्ख्यान
प्रसंख्यानः Payment, liquidation.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Enumeration.<BR>--2 Reflection,<BR>meditation; deep meditation,<BR>abstract contemplation हरः<BR>प्रसंख्यानपरो बभूव Ku. 3. 40.<BR>--3 Fame,<BR>reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंघः|प्रसङ्घ|प्रसंघ|प्रसङ्घः
प्रसंघः A great multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंज्|प्रसञ्ज्
प्रसंज् {c1c} P. To become attached<BR>to or fond of, feel affection for.<BR>--Pass.<BR>1 To cling to or adhere to.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-c" target="_blank">Page0763-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--2 To follow, apply or be<BR>applicable, hold good in the case of<BR>(active also in this sense);<BR>इतरेतराश्रयः प्रसज्येत, वैषम्यनैर्घृण्ये नेश्वरस्य<BR>प्रसज्येते Ś. B.<BR>--3 To be attached to;<BR>तस्यामसौ प्रासजत् Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्त|प्रसक्तं
प्रसक्त p. p.<BR>1 Attached to,<BR>connected with.<BR>--2 Excessively<BR>attached or fond; Pt. 1. 193.<BR>--3<BR>Adhering or sticking to.<BR>--4 Fixed<BR>or intent upon, devoted or addicted<BR>to, engaged in, applied to;<BR>Śi. 9. 63; so द्यूत˚, निद्रा˚ &c.<BR>--5<BR>Contiguous, near.<BR>--6 Constant,<BR>incessant, uninterrupted; Ki. 4. 18;<BR>R. 13. 40; Māl. 4. 6; M. 3. 1.<BR>--7<BR>Got, obtained, gained.<BR>--8 Expanded,<BR>opened.<BR>--क्तं ind. Incessantly,<BR>continuously; Ki. 16. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसक्तिः|प्रसक्ति
प्रसक्तिः f.<BR>1 Attachment,<BR>devotion, addiction, devotedness,<BR>adherence.<BR>--2 Connection, union,<BR>association.<BR>--3 Applicability, bearing,<BR>application; as in अतिप्रसक्ति (which<BR>is = अतिव्याप्ति q. v.)<BR>--4 Energy,<BR>perseverance; संतापे दिशतु शिवः शिवां<BR>प्रसक्तिं Ki. 5. 50.<BR>--5 Conclusion,<BR>deduction.<BR>--6 A topic or subject of<BR>discourse.<BR>--7 Occurrence of a<BR>possibility.<BR>--8 Acquisition, gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंगः|प्रसङ्ग|प्रसंग|प्रसङ्गः
प्रसंगः<BR>1 Attachment, devotion,<BR>addiction, devotedness; स्वरूपयोग्ये<BR>सुरतप्रसंगे Ku. 1. 19;<BR>तस्यात्यायतकोमलस्य सततं द्यूतप्रसंगेन किं Mk. 2. 11;<BR>Śi. 11. 22.<BR>--2 Union, intercourse,<BR>association, connection;<BR>निवर्ततामस्माद्गणिकाप्रसंगात् Mk. 4; Pt. 1. 251.<BR>--3 Illicit intercourse.<BR>--4<BR>Occupation, intentness, being engaged or<BR>occupied with; भ्रूविक्रियां<BR>विरतप्रसंगैः Ku. 3. 47.<BR>--5 A subject or<BR>topic (of discourse or controversy).<BR>--6 An occasion, incident;<BR>दिग्विजयप्रसंगेन K. 191; यात्राप्रसंगेन<BR>Māl. 1.<BR>--7 Conjuncture, time,<BR>opportunity; Ms. 9. 5.<BR>--8 A contingency,<BR>event, case, occurrence of a<BR>possibility; नेश्वरो जगतः कारणमुपपद्यते<BR>कुतः वैषम्यनैर्घृण्यप्रसंगात् Ś. B.; एवं<BR>चानवस्थाप्रसंगः ibid.; तस्याणुतरप्रसंगात्<BR>Tarka k.; Ku. 7. 16.<BR>--9 Connected<BR>reasoning or argument.<BR>--10 A<BR>conclusion, an inference.<BR>--11 Connected<BR>language.<BR>--12 Inseparable<BR>application or connection (= व्याप्ति q. v.).<BR>--13 Mention of parents.<BR>--14<BR>Introduction, insertion.<BR>--15 Gain.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-a" target="_blank">Page0764-a+ 57</a>]<BR>(प्रसंगेन, प्रसंगतः, प्रसंगात् are used<BR>adverbially in the sense of<BR>1 in<BR>relation to.<BR>--2 in consequence of, on<BR>account of, because of, by way of.<BR>--3 occasionally, incidentally.<BR>--4 in<BR>course of; as in कथाप्रसंगेन in course<BR>of conversation’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--निवारणं<BR>prevention or obviation of similar<BR>contingencies in future.<BR>--वशात् ind.<BR>according to the time, by the force<BR>of circumstances.<BR>--विनिवृत्तिः f.<BR>nonrecurrence of a contingency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0763-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंगिन्|प्रसङ्गिन्
प्रसंगिन् a.<BR>1 Fond of, attached or<BR>devoted to.<BR>--2 Dependent on,<BR>contingent on.<BR>--3 Occasional, incidental.<BR>--4 Secondary, subordinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसज्य
प्रसज्य a.<BR>1 To be attached to.<BR>--2<BR>Applicable, holding good.<BR>--3<BR>Contingent, possible.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रतिषेधः<BR>{1} negation of a possible case or<BR>contingency. {2} a simple prohibition of<BR>the particular matter specified<BR>without mentioning what is different<BR>(from it).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंजनं|प्रसञ्जन|प्रसंजन
प्रसंजनं<BR>1 Act of connecting,<BR>combining, uniting.<BR>--2 Applying,<BR>bringing to bear upon, bringing into use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसद्
प्रसद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To be pleased, be<BR>gracious or propitious (oft. with<BR>inf.); तमालपत्रास्तरणासु रंतुं प्रसीद<BR>शश्वन्मलयस्थलीषु R. 6. 64.<BR>--2 To be<BR>appeased or soothed, be satisfied;<BR>निमित्तमुद्द्विश्य हि यः प्रकुप्यति ध्रुवं स<BR>तस्यापगमे प्रसीदति Pt. 1. 283.<BR>--3 To be<BR>pure or clear, clear up, brighten up<BR>(lit. and fig.); दिशः प्रसेदुर्मरुतो ववुः<BR>सुखाः R. 3. 14; Ki. 16. 35;<BR>प्रससादोदयादम्भः कुम्भयोनेर्महौजसः 4. 21.<BR>--4<BR>To bear fruit, succeed, be successful;<BR>क्रिया हि वस्तूपहिता प्रसीदति R. 3. 29.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To propitiate, secure the<BR>favour of, pray, beseech;<BR>तस्मात्प्रणम्य प्रणिधाय कायं प्रसादये<BR>त्वामहमीशमीड्यं Bg. 11. 44; R. 1. 88;<BR>Y. 3. 283.<BR>--2 To beg pardon, pray for<BR>grace.<BR>--3 To purify, make clear or<BR>pure; चेतः प्रसादयति Bh. 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसत्तिः|प्रसत्ति
प्रसत्तिः f.<BR>1 Favour, graciousness,<BR>complacency.<BR>--2 Clearness, purity,<BR>transparency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसन्न|प्रसन्नः
प्रसन्न p. p.<BR>1 Pure, clear, bright,<BR>limpid, pellucid, transparent;<BR>Ku. 1. 23; 7. 74; Ś. 5. 21.<BR>--2 Pleased,<BR>delighted, propitiated, soothed;<BR>गंगां शरन्नयति सिंधुपतिं प्रसन्नां Mu. 3. 9;<BR>गंभीरायाः पयसि सरितश्चेतसीव प्रसन्ने<BR>Me. 40 (where the first sense is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-b" target="_blank">Page0764-b+ 57</a>]<BR>also intended); Ku. 5. 35;<BR>R. 2. 68.<BR>--3 Kind, kindly disposed,<BR>gracious, propitious; अवेहि मां कामदुघां<BR>प्रसन्नां R. 2. 63.<BR>--4 Plain, open, clear,<BR>easily intelligible (as meaning).<BR>--5<BR>True, correct; प्रसन्नस्ते तर्कः V. 2;<BR>प्रसन्नप्रायस्ते तर्कः Māl. 1.<BR>--6 Settled<BR>down, tranquil.<BR>--न्ना<BR>1 Propitiation,<BR>pleasing.<BR>--2 Spirituous liquor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>gracious-minded, propitious. (--m.) N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--ईरा spirituous liquor.<BR>--कल्प a. {1} almost calm. {2} almost<BR>true.<BR>--मुख, --वदन a.<BR>gracious-looking, with a pleased countenance,<BR>smiling.<BR>--सलिल a. having clear<BR>water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादः|प्रसाद
प्रसादः<BR>1 Favour, kindness,<BR>condescension, propitiousness; कुरु<BR>दृष्टिप्रसादं ‘be pleased to show<BR>yourself’; इत्याप्रसादादस्यास्त्वं परिचर्यापरो<BR>भव R. 1. 91; 2. 22.<BR>--2 Good<BR>temper, graciousness of disposition.<BR>--3 Calmness, tranquillity,<BR>composure, serenity, sedateness, absence of<BR>excitement; Bg. 2. 64.<BR>--4<BR>Clearness, limpidness, brightness,<BR>transparency, purity (as of water, mind<BR>&c.); गंगा रोधः पतनकलुषा गृह्णतीव<BR>प्रसादं V. 1. 8; Ś. 7. 32;<BR>प्राप्तबुद्धिप्रसादाः Śi. 11. 6; R. 17. 1;<BR>Ki. 9. 25.<BR>--5 Perspicuity, clearness of style,<BR>one of the three Guṇas according to<BR>Mammaṭa, who thus defines it;<BR>शुष्केंधनाग्निबत् स्वच्छजलबत्सहसैव यः ।<BR>व्याप्नोत्यन्यत्प्रसादोसौ सर्वत्र विहितस्थितिः<BR>K. P. 8; यावदर्थकपदत्वरूपमर्थवैमल्यं प्रसादः<BR>or श्रुतमात्रा वाक्यार्थं करतलबदरमिव<BR>निवेदयंती घटना प्रसादस्य R. G.; see<BR>Kāv. 1. 44; S. D. 611 also.<BR>--6 Food<BR>offered to idols &c., or the remnants<BR>of such food.<BR>--7 A free gift, gratuity.<BR>--8 Any propitiatory offering.<BR>--9<BR>Wellbeing, welfare.<BR>--Comp. उन्मुख a.<BR>disposed to favour.<BR>--दानं a propitiatory<BR>gift.<BR>--पट्टः a turban of honour.<BR>--पराङ्मुख a. {1} withdrawing<BR>favour from any one. {2} not caring<BR>for any body's favour.<BR>--पात्रं an<BR>object of favour.<BR>--स्थ a. {1} kind,<BR>propitious. {2} serene, pleased, happy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादक
प्रसादक, प्रसादिन् a. (दिका f.)<BR>1<BR>Purifying, clearing, making pellucid.<BR>--2 Soothing, calming.<BR>--3<BR>Gladdening, cheering.<BR>--4 Courting favour,<BR>propitiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादिन्
प्रसादक, प्रसादिन् a. (दिका f.)<BR>1<BR>Purifying, clearing, making pellucid.<BR>--2 Soothing, calming.<BR>--3<BR>Gladdening, cheering.<BR>--4 Courting favour,<BR>propitiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादन|प्रसादनं|प्रसादनः
प्रसादन a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Purifying,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">Page0764-c+ 55</a>]<BR>clearing, rendering pure or clear;<BR>फलं कतकवृक्षस्य यद्यप्यंबुप्रसादनं<BR>Ms. 6. 67.<BR>--2 Soothing, calming.<BR>--3<BR>Cheering, gladdening.<BR>--नः A royal tent.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Clearing from impurities,<BR>purifying.<BR>--2 Soothing, calming,<BR>tranquillizing, composing.<BR>--3<BR>Pleasing, gratifying.<BR>--4 Propitiating,<BR>courting favour.<BR>--ना<BR>1 Service,<BR>worship.<BR>--2 Purifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादित
प्रसादित p. p.<BR>1 Purified, cleared.<BR>--2 Appeased, propitiated.<BR>--3<BR>Worshipped.<BR>--4 Calmed, soothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसादीकृ
प्रसादीकृ {c8c} U. To bestow as a<BR>favour, give as a present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसंधानं|प्रसन्धान|प्रसंधान
प्रसंधानं Combination, union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसभः|प्रसभ
प्रसभः Force, violence,<BR>impetuosity; प्रसभोद्धृतारिः R. 2. 30.<BR>--भं<BR>ind.<BR>1 Violently, forcibly, perforce;<BR>इंद्रियाणि प्रमाथीनि हरंति प्रसभं मनः<BR>Bg. 2. 60; Ms. 8. 332.<BR>--2 Very much,<BR>exceedingly; तवास्मि गीतरागेण हारिणा<BR>प्रसभं हृतः Ś. 1. 5; Rs. 6. 25.<BR>--3<BR>Importunately; Bg. 11. 41.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दमनं subduing by force;<BR>Ś. 7. 33.<BR>--हरणं forcible abduction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्षणं|प्रसमीक्षण
प्रसमीक्षणं, प्रसमीक्षा<BR>Consideration, deliberation, judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसमीक्षा
प्रसमीक्षणं, प्रसमीक्षा<BR>Consideration, deliberation, judgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसयनं|प्रसयन
प्रसयनं<BR>1 Binding, fastening.<BR>--2<BR>A net.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्गः|प्रसर्ग
प्रसर्गः Ved.<BR>1 Pouring or<BR>flowing forth.<BR>--2 Emission, discharge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसलः|प्रसल
प्रस(श)लः The cold season<BR>(हेमंत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रशलः|प्रशल
प्रस(श)लः The cold season<BR>(हेमंत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसव्य|प्रसव्यं
प्रसव्य a.<BR>1 Contrary, inverted,<BR>reverse.<BR>--2 Turned towards the left<BR>--3 Favourable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्
प्रसह् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To bear, endure; न<BR>तेजस्तेजस्वी प्रसृतमपरेषां प्रसहते<BR>U. 6. 14.<BR>--2 To withstand, resist,<BR>overpower; संयुगे सायुगीनं तमुद्यतं प्रसहेत<BR>कः Ku. 2. 57.<BR>--3 To exert oneself,<BR>attempt.<BR>--4 To dare, venture, be<BR>able.<BR>--5 To have power or energy;<BR>see प्रसह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्
प्रस(सा)ह् m. Ved.<BR>1 Force,<BR>violence.<BR>--2 An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाह्
प्रस(सा)ह् m. Ved.<BR>1 Force,<BR>violence.<BR>--2 An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह|प्रसहः
प्रसह a. Withstanding, enduring,<BR>bearing up.<BR>--हः<BR>1 A beast or bird<BR>of prey.<BR>--2 Resistance, endurance,<BR>opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसहनः|प्रसहन
प्रसहनः A beast or bird of prey.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Withstanding, resisting.<BR>--2<BR>Enduring, bearing up.<BR>--3 Defeating,<BR>overcoming.<BR>--4 Embracing, an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">Page0765-a+ 56</a>]<BR>embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0764-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसह्य
प्रसह्य ind.<BR>1 Forcibly, violently,<BR>by force; प्रसह्य<BR>मणिमुद्धरेन्मकरवक्त्रदंष्ट्रांकुरात् Bh. 2. 4; Śi. 1. 27.<BR>--2 Exceedingly, much.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चौरः a plunderer, highwayman.<BR>--हरणं violent or forcible seizure,<BR>plundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाहः|प्रसाह
प्रसाहः Overpowering, defeating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसातिका
प्रसातिका A kind of rice (with<BR>small grains).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाध्
प्रसाध् Caus.<BR>1 To advance,<BR>promote.<BR>--2 To accomplish, effect;<BR>perfect, complete.<BR>--3 To gain, obtain;<BR>Pt. 1. 2.<BR>--4 To overcome, subdue.<BR>--5 To dress, decorate, adorn,<BR>embellish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधक|प्रसाधकः
प्रसाधक a. (धिका f.)<BR>1<BR>Accomplishing, or perfecting.<BR>--2 Purifying,<BR>cleansing.<BR>--3 Decorating,<BR>ornamenting.<BR>--कः A valet-de-chambre, an<BR>attendant who dresses his master;<BR>R. 17. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधनं|प्रसाधन|प्रसाधनः
प्रसाधनं<BR>1 Accomplishing, effecting,<BR>bringing about.<BR>--2 Setting in order,<BR>arranging.<BR>--3 Decorating,<BR>ornamenting, embellishing; toilet, dress;<BR>Ku. 4. 18.<BR>--4 A decoration,<BR>ornament, means of decoration or<BR>ornament; Ku. 7. 13, 30.<BR>--नः, --नं, --नी<BR>A comb.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विधिः<BR>decoration, embellishment.<BR>--विशेषः the<BR>highest decoration; प्रसाधनविधेः<BR>प्रसाधनविशेषः V. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधिका
प्रसाधिका<BR>1 A lady's maid, a female<BR>attendant who looks to the toilet of<BR>her mistress;<BR>प्रसधिकालंबितमग्रपादमाक्षिप्य R. 7. 7.<BR>--2 Wild rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसाधित|प्रसाधितः
प्रसाधित p. p.<BR>1 Accomplished,<BR>completed, perfected.<BR>--2<BR>Ornamented, decorated.<BR>--3 Proved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसित|प्रसितं
प्रसित p. p.<BR>1 Bound, fastened.<BR>--2 Devoted to, engaged in,<BR>occupied with.<BR>--3 Intent on, longing for,<BR>craving after (with instr. or loc.);<BR>लक्ष्म्या लक्ष्म्यां वा प्रसितः Sk;. R. 8. 23.<BR>--4 Very clear.<BR>--तं Pus, matter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसितिः|प्रसिति
प्रसितिः f.<BR>1 A net.<BR>--2 A ligament.<BR>--3 A tie, fetter.<BR>--4 An attack,<BR>assault.<BR>--5 A throw, shot.<BR>--6 Reach,<BR>extent.<BR>--7 A series, succession.<BR>--8<BR>Power, authority, influence.<BR>--9 Ved.<BR>A flame.<BR>--10 A track, path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिध्
प्रसिध् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be<BR>accomplished or effected.<BR>--2 To succeed.<BR>--3<BR>To be made known.<BR>--4 To be got or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">Page0765-b+ 58</a>]<BR>obtained.<BR>--5 To be established.<BR>--6<BR>To be decorated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्ध|प्रसिद्धः
प्रसिद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Renowned, famous,<BR>celebrated.<BR>--2 Decorated,<BR>ornamented, adorned; R. 18. 41; Ku. 5. 9;<BR>7. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसिद्धि|प्रसिद्धिः
प्रसिद्धिः f.<BR>1 Fame, celebrity,<BR>publicity, renown.<BR>--2 Success,<BR>accomplishment, fulfilment; Ki. 3. 39;<BR>Ms. 4. 3.<BR>--3 Ornament, decoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसीदिका
प्रसीदिका A small garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसुप्त
प्रसुप्त p. p.<BR>1 Asleep, sleepy.<BR>--2<BR>Fast asleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसुप्तिः|प्रसुप्ति
प्रसुप्तिः f.<BR>1 Sleepiness.<BR>--2<BR>Paralysis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसु
प्रसु-सू {c1c} P., {c2c} {c4c} A.<BR>1 To beget,<BR>generate, produce.<BR>--2 To bring forth,<BR>be delivered of; पुत्ररत्नं प्रासोष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसू
प्रसु-सू {c1c} P., {c2c} {c4c} A.<BR>1 To beget,<BR>generate, produce.<BR>--2 To bring forth,<BR>be delivered of; पुत्ररत्नं प्रासोष्ट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवः|प्रसव
प्रसवः<BR>1 Begetting, generation,<BR>procreation, birth, production.<BR>--2<BR>Child-birth, delivery, confinement;<BR>as in आसन्नप्रसवा.<BR>--3 Offspring,<BR>progeny, young ones, children;<BR>oft. at the end of comp.; केवलं<BR>वीरप्रसवा भूयाः U. 1; Ku. 7. 87.<BR>--4<BR>Source, origin, birth-place (fig.<BR>also); Ki. 2. 43.<BR>--5 Flower,<BR>blossom; प्रसवविभूतिषु भूरुहां विरक्तः<BR>Śi. 7. 42; नीता लोध्रप्रसवरजसा पांडुतामानने<BR>श्रीः Me. 65; कुंदप्रसवशिथिलं जीवितं<BR>113; R. 9. 28; Ku. 1. 55; 4. 14;<BR>Ś. 5. 9; Māl. 9. 27, 31; U. 2. 20.<BR>--6 A fruit, product<BR>--7 Ved.<BR>Extracting Soma juice.<BR>--8 Setting in<BR>motion.<BR>--9 A current, stream.<BR>--10<BR>Excitement, animation.<BR>--11<BR>Enjoining, ordering<BR>--12 Assistance, help.<BR>--13 Pursuit, acquisition.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उन्मुख a. about to be delivered or<BR>confined; पतिः प्रतीतः प्रसवोन्मुखीं प्रियां<BR>ददर्श R. 3. 12.<BR>--गृहं a<BR>lying-inchamber.<BR>--धर्मिन् a. productive,<BR>prolific.<BR>--बंधनं the foot-stalk of a<BR>leaf or flower, peduncle.<BR>--वेदना<BR>--व्यथा pangs of child-birth, throes.<BR>--स्थली a mother.<BR>--स्थानं {1} a place<BR>for delivery. {2} a nest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवकः|प्रसवक
प्रसवकः The Piyāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवनं|प्रसवन
प्रसवनं<BR>1 Bringing forth.<BR>--2<BR>Bearing children, fecundity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवंती
प्रसवंती^1 f. A woman in labour.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170131. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: f. of pres. participle ends in I not iH.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवितृ
प्रसवितृ m. A father, procreator;<BR>Pt. 4. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसवित्री
प्रसवित्री A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसू
प्रसू a. Bringing forth, bearing,<BR>giving birth to; स्त्रीप्रसूश्चाधिवेत्तव्या<BR>Y. 1. 73. --f.<BR>1 A mother;<BR>मातरपितरौप्रसूजनयितारौ Ak. ‘parents’.<BR>--2 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-c" target="_blank">Page0765-c+ 57</a>]<BR>mare.<BR>--3 A spreading creeper.<BR>--4 A<BR>young shoot, tender grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूका
प्रसूका A mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूत|प्रसूतं|प्रसूतः
प्रसूत p. p.<BR>1 Begotten,<BR>engendered.<BR>--2 Brought forth, born,<BR>produced.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A flower.<BR>--2 Any<BR>productive source.<BR>--ता A woman<BR>recently delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिः|प्रसूति
प्रसूतिः f.<BR>1 Procreation, begetting,<BR>generation.<BR>--2 Bringing forth,<BR>bearing, delivering, giving birth to;<BR>R. 14. 66.<BR>--3 Calving.<BR>--4 Laying eggs;<BR>N. 1. 135.<BR>--5 Birth, production, generation;<BR>R. 10. 53.<BR>--6 Appearance, coming<BR>forth, growth (of flowers &c.);<BR>R. 5. 15; Ku. 1. 42.<BR>--7 A product,<BR>production.<BR>--8 Offspring, progeny,<BR>issue; R. 1. 25, 77; 2. 4; 5. 7;<BR>Ku. 2. 7, Ś. 6. 24.<BR>--9 A producer,<BR>generator, procreator; R. 2. 63.<BR>--10 A<BR>mother.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं pain<BR>resulting as a necessary consequence of<BR>birth.<BR>--वायुः wind produced in the<BR>womb during the pangs of travail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूतिका
प्रसूतिका A woman recently<BR>delivered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसून|प्रसूनं
प्रसून p. p. Produced, born.<BR>--नं.<BR>1 A flower; लतायां पूर्वलूतायां<BR>प्रसूनस्यागमः कुतः U. 5. 20, R. 2. 10.<BR>--2 A<BR>bud, blossom.<BR>--3 A fruit.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इषुः, --बाणः, --वाणः epithets of the<BR>god of love.<BR>--वर्षः a shower of<BR>flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसूनकं|प्रसूनक|प्रसूनकः
प्रसूनकं<BR>1 A flower.<BR>--2 A bud,<BR>blossom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृ
प्रसृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To flow forth, spring,<BR>arise, proceed; लोहिताद्या महानद्यः<BR>प्रसस्रुस्तत्र चासकृत् Mb.<BR>--2 To go<BR>forth, advance; वेलानिलायप्रमृता<BR>भुजंगाः R. 13. 12; अन्वेषणप्रसृते च<BR>मित्रगणे Dk.<BR>--3 To spread, spread<BR>round; कृशानुः किं साक्षात्प्रसरति दिशो<BR>नैष नियतं K. P. 10; प्रसरति तृणमध्ये<BR>लब्धवृद्धिः क्षणेन (दवाग्निः) Rs. 1. 25.<BR>--4 To spread, prevail, pervade;<BR>प्रसरति परिमाथी कोप्ययं देहदाहः<BR>Māl. 1. 41; भित्त्वा भित्त्वा प्रसरति बलात्कोपि<BR>चेतोविकारः U. 3. 36.<BR>--5 To be<BR>stretched, to extend; न मे हस्तौ<BR>प्रसरतः Ś. 2.<BR>--6 To be disposed or<BR>inclined to (do a thing), move;<BR>न मे उचितेषु करणीयेषु हस्तपादं प्रसरति<BR>Ś. 4; प्रसरति मनः कार्यारंभे<BR>Pt. 3. 180.<BR>--7 To prevail, begin,<BR>commence; प्रससार चोत्सवः Ks. 16. 85.<BR>--8 To be long, be lengthened;<BR>V. 3. 22.<BR>--9 To grow strong or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-a" target="_blank">Page0766-a+ 57</a>]<BR>intense; प्रसृततरं सख्यं Dk.<BR>--10 To<BR>pass away (as time).<BR>--11 To break<BR>forth or out (as fire). --Caus.<BR>1 To spread, stretch; Bk. 10. 44.<BR>--2 To stretch forward, extend, hold<BR>out (as the hand); कालः सर्वजनान्<BR>प्रसारितकरो गृह्णाति दूरादपि Pt. 2. 20.<BR>--3 To spread out or expose for<BR>sale; क्रेतारः क्रीणीयुरिति बुद्ध्या<BR>आपणे प्रसारितं क्रय्यं Sk.; Ms. 5. 129.<BR>--4 To open wide, expand (as eyes).<BR>--5 To publish, promulgate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0765-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरः|प्रसर
प्रसरः<BR>1 Going forward,<BR>advancing; Ś. 1. 29.<BR>--2 Free or<BR>unimpeded motion, free scope; access or<BR>course; R. 8. 23; 16. 20;<BR>Mu. 3. 5; H. 1. 186.<BR>--3 Spreading,<BR>diffusion, extension, expansion, dilation;<BR>Śi. 9. 71.<BR>--4 Extent, dimension,<BR>great quantity; Śi. 3. 35.<BR>--5<BR>Prevalence, influence; Ś. 3. 10.<BR>--6 A<BR>stream, flow, torrent, flood; पपात<BR>स्वेदांबुप्रसर इव हर्ष श्रुनिकरः Gīt. 11.<BR>--7 A group, multitude.<BR>--8 War,<BR>battle.<BR>--9 An iron arrow.<BR>--10 Speed.<BR>--11 Affectionate solicitation.<BR>--12<BR>(In medicine) Morbid<BR>displacement of the humours of the body.<BR>--13 Destruction, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरणं|प्रसरण
प्रसरणं<BR>1 Going forth, running<BR>or streaming forth.<BR>--2<BR>Escaping, running away.<BR>--3 Spreading<BR>forth or abroad.<BR>--4 Surrounding an<BR>enemy.<BR>--5 Amiability.<BR>--6 Morbid<BR>displacement of the humours of the<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरणिः|प्रसरणि
प्रसरणिः --णी f. Surrounding an<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसरणी
प्रसरणिः --णी f. Surrounding an<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारः|प्रसार
प्रसारः<BR>1 Spreading, extending.<BR>--2 Spread, diffusion, extension,<BR>expansion.<BR>--3 Stretching out.<BR>--4<BR>Spreading over the country to<BR>forage.<BR>--5 Opening (the mouth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारणं|प्रसारण
प्रसारणं<BR>1 Spreading abroad,<BR>extending, increase, diffusing,<BR>expanding.<BR>--2 Stretching out; as<BR>in बाहुप्रसारणं.<BR>--3 Surrounding<BR>an enemy.<BR>--4 Spreading over the<BR>country for fuel and grass.<BR>--5 The<BR>change of a semivowel (य् र् and व्)<BR>into a vowel; see संप्रसारण.<BR>--6<BR>Displaying, unfolding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारिणी
प्रसारिणी Surrounding an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसारित
प्रसारित p. p.<BR>1 Expanded, spread,<BR>diffused, extended.<BR>--2 Stretched<BR>out (as hands.).<BR>--3 Exhibited, laid<BR>out, exposed (for sale).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृत|प्रसृतं|प्रसृतः
प्रसृत p. p.<BR>1 Gone forward.<BR>--2<BR>Stretched out, extended.<BR>--3 Spread,<BR>diffused.<BR>--4 Long, lengthened.<BR>--5<BR>Engaged in, attached to.<BR>--6 Swift,<BR>or quick.<BR>--7 Manifested,<BR>displayed; U. 6. 14.<BR>--8 Modest,<BR>humble.<BR>--तः The palm of the hand<BR>stretched out and hollowed.<BR>--तः,<BR>--तं A measure equal to two palas.<BR>--ता The leg.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः a<BR>particular class of sons, an adulterine<BR>(कुंडगोलकरूप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृतिः|प्रसृति
प्रसृतिः f.<BR>1 Advance, progress.<BR>--2<BR>Flowing.<BR>--3 The palm of the hand<BR>stretched out and hollowed.<BR>--4 A<BR>handful (considered as a measure<BR>equal to two palas.); परिक्षीणः<BR>काश्चित्स्पृहयति यवानां प्रसृतये Bh. 2. 45,<BR>Y. 2. 112.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृत्वर
प्रसृत्वर a. Spreading about;<BR>Bv. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृमर
प्रसृमर a. Flowing forth,<BR>dropping, distilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृज्
प्रसृज् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To leave, abandon.<BR>--2 To let loose.<BR>--3 To sow, scatter.<BR>--4 To injure, hurt.<BR>--5 To dismiss,<BR>set aside.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृष्ट
प्रसृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Laid aside,<BR>dismissed.<BR>--2 Hurt, injured.<BR>--ष्टा A finger<BR>stretched forth or extended; (<BR>अंगुल्यः प्रसृता यास्तु ताः प्रसृष्टा उदीरिताः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसृप्
प्रसृप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go forth,<BR>proceed; Bk. 14. 20.<BR>--2 To spread,<BR>circulate (fig.); रुधिरेण प्रसर्पता Mb.;<BR>आलर्कं विषमिव सर्वतः प्रसृप्तं U. 1. 40.<BR>--3 To creep or crawl forth or along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पः|प्रसर्प
प्रसर्पः Going to the part of the<BR>sacrificial enclosure called सदस् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पणं|प्रसर्पण
प्रसर्पणं<BR>1 Going or moving<BR>forward, advancing.<BR>--2<BR>Pervading, spreading in all<BR>directions.<BR>--3 Entering the सदस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसर्पिन्
प्रसर्पिन् a.<BR>1 Going forth,<BR>progressing, advancing.<BR>--2 Creeping along.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेकः|प्रसेक
प्रसेकः<BR>1 Flowing forth, oozing,<BR>dropping.<BR>--2 Sprinkling, wetting.<BR>--3 Emission, discharge; Rs. 3. 6.<BR>--4 Vomiting.<BR>--5 Watering of the<BR>mouth or nose.<BR>--6 The bowl of a<BR>spoon or ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेदिका
प्रसेदिका A small garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेवः|प्रसेव
प्रसेवः, --प्रसेवकः<BR>1 A sack, bag<BR>for grain.<BR>--2 A leathern bottle.<BR>--3<BR>A small instrument of wood placed<BR>under the neck of the lute to make<BR>the sound deeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रसेवकः|प्रसेवक
प्रसेवः, --प्रसेवकः<BR>1 A sack, bag<BR>for grain.<BR>--2 A leathern bottle.<BR>--3<BR>A small instrument of wood placed<BR>under the neck of the lute to make<BR>the sound deeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कंद्|प्रस्कन्द्
प्रस्कंद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To leap forward.<BR>--2 To fall upon, attack. --Caus.<BR>To cross (a river &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कंदनं|प्रस्कन्दन|प्रस्कंदन|प्रस्कन्दनं|प्रस्कन्दनः
प्रस्कंदनं<BR>1 Springing across or<BR>leaping over.<BR>--2 Evacuation by<BR>stool, diarrhœa.<BR>--नः An epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कंदिका|प्रस्कन्दिका
प्रस्कंदिका Dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कन्न|प्रस्कन्नः
प्रस्कन्न p. p.<BR>1 Sprung forth.<BR>--2<BR>Fallen, dropped.<BR>--3 Defeated.<BR>--न्नः<BR>1 An outcast.<BR>--2 A sinner,<BR>transgressor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्कुंदः|प्रस्कुन्द|प्रस्कुंद|प्रस्कुन्दः
प्रस्कुंदः An altar of a circular<BR>shape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्खल्
प्रस्खल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To jostle; रथाः<BR>प्रचस्खलुश्चाश्वाः Bk. 14. 98.<BR>--2 To<BR>stagger, stumble, reel, totter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्खलनं|प्रस्खलन
प्रस्खलनं<BR>1 Staggering.<BR>--2<BR>Stumbling, falling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तरः|प्रस्तर
प्रस्तरः<BR>1 A couch of leaves and<BR>flowers.<BR>--2 A couch or bed in<BR>general.<BR>--3 A flat surface or top,<BR>level plain.<BR>--4 A stone, rock.<BR>--5<BR>A precious stone, gem.<BR>--6 A<BR>paragraph, section of a work.<BR>--7 A<BR>handful of darbha grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तरणं|प्रस्तरण
प्रस्तरणं --णा<BR>1 A bed, couch.<BR>--2<BR>A seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तरणा
प्रस्तरणं --णा<BR>1 A bed, couch.<BR>--2<BR>A seat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तारः|प्रस्तार
प्रस्तारः<BR>1 Strewing, spreading out,<BR>covering with.<BR>--2 A bed of leaves<BR>and flowers.<BR>--3 A bed or couch in<BR>general.<BR>--4 A flat surface, level,<BR>plain.<BR>--5 A thicket, wood.<BR>--6 (In<BR>prosody) A tabular representation<BR>of the long and short vowels of<BR>a metre with all possible varieties.<BR>--7 A process in preparing minerals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तिरः|प्रस्तिर
प्रस्तिरः A bed of leaves and<BR>flowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तीत|प्रस्तीतः
प्रस्तीत --म a.<BR>1 Making a noise,<BR>sounded.<BR>--2 Crowded together,<BR>swarming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तीम
प्रस्तीत --म a.<BR>1 Making a noise,<BR>sounded.<BR>--2 Crowded together,<BR>swarming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तु
प्रस्तु {c2c} U.<BR>1 To praise.<BR>--2 To<BR>begin, commence; प्रस्तूयतां विवादवस्तु<BR>M. 1.<BR>--3 To cause, produce;<BR>Māl. 5. 9.<BR>--4 To say, relate, propound.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To relate, allude to, tell;<BR>Māl. 3. 3.<BR>--2 To begin, commence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तवः|प्रस्तव
प्रस्तवः<BR>1 A song or hymn of praise.<BR>--2 A fit time or opportunity; see<BR>प्रस्ताव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावः|प्रस्ताव
प्रस्तावः<BR>1 Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--2 An introduction.<BR>--3<BR>Mention, allusion, reference;<BR>नाममात्रप्रस्तावः Ś. 7.<BR>--4 An occasion,<BR>opportunity, time, season; fit<BR>or proper time; त्वराप्रस्तावोयं न ख<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-a" target="_blank">Page0767-a+ 56</a>]<BR>परिहासस्य समयः Māl. 9. 44;<BR>शिष्याय बृहतां पत्युः प्रस्तावमदिशद् दृशा<BR>Śi. 2. 68.<BR>--5 The occasion of a discourse,<BR>subject, topic.<BR>--6 The prologue of a<BR>drama; see प्रस्तावना below.<BR>--7 The<BR>prelude or introductory words of a<BR>Sāman.<BR>--8 An introductory praise.<BR>(प्रस्तावे ind. on a suitable occasion,<BR>seasonably. प्रस्तावेन {1}<BR>incidentally, occasionally. {2} suitably).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--यज्ञः a conversation in<BR>which each interlocutor takes a part<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0766-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावना
प्रस्तावना<BR>1 Causing to be praised<BR>or mentioned, praising, praise.<BR>--2<BR>Beginning, commencement; आर्य<BR>बालचरितप्रस्तावनाडिंडमः Mv. 1. 54.<BR>--3 An introduction, preface,<BR>exordium (in general); प्रस्तावना इयं<BR>कपटनाटकस्य Māl. 2.<BR>--4 Sounding forth.<BR>--5 An introductory dialogue (the<BR>prologue) at the beginning of a<BR>drama between the manager and<BR>one of the actors, which, after<BR>giving an account of the author and<BR>his qualifications &c., introduces<BR>the audience to the incidents of<BR>the drama; (for definition, see<BR>आमुख).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तावित
प्रस्तावित a.<BR>1 Begun, commenced.<BR>--2 Mentioned, referred to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तुत|प्रस्तुतः
प्रस्तुत p. p.<BR>1 Praised, eulogized.<BR>--2 Begun, commenced.<BR>--3<BR>Accomplished, done, effected.<BR>--4<BR>Happened.<BR>--5 Approached.<BR>--6<BR>Proposed, declared, under discussion,<BR>taken in hand.<BR>--7 Expected,<BR>desired.<BR>--8 Ready, prepared.<BR>--9<BR>Executed with effort or energy.<BR>--10<BR>Made or consisting of.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The<BR>matter in hand, the subject under<BR>discussion or consideration; अधुना<BR>प्रस्तुतमनुस्रियतां.<BR>--2 (In Rhet.)<BR>Forming the subject of discussion,<BR>the उपमेय; see प्रकृत;<BR>अप्रस्तुतप्रशंसा सा या सैव प्रस्तुताश्रया<BR>K. P. 10.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकुरः a figure of<BR>speech in which a reference is made<BR>to a passing circumstance to bring<BR>out something latent in the hearer's<BR>mind; see Chandr. 5. 64 and Kuval.<BR>under प्रस्तुतांकुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्तुतिः|प्रस्तुति
प्रस्तुतिः f. Ved. Praise, eulogium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्था
प्रस्था {c1c} A.<BR>1 To set out, depart;<BR>पारसीकांस्ततो जेतुं प्रतस्थे स्थलवर्त्मना<BR>R. 4. 60; Ku. 3. 22.<BR>--2 To advance,<BR>march towards.<BR>--3 To walk, move;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">Page0767-b+ 56</a>]<BR>R. 1. 89.<BR>--4 To stand firmly.<BR>--5<BR>To be established.<BR>--6 To approach,<BR>come near. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to<BR>retire.<BR>--2 To send away, dismiss,<BR>despatch; तौ दंपती स्वां प्रति राजधानीं<BR>प्रस्थापयामास वशी वशिष्ठः R. 2. 70.<BR>--3<BR>To drive away, banish, expel;<BR>Ku. 6. 7.<BR>--4 To urge forwards, push on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थ|प्रस्थः
प्रस्थ a.<BR>1 Going to, visiting,<BR>abiding in; as in वानप्रस्थ.<BR>--2 Going on<BR>a journey.<BR>--3 Spreading, expanding.<BR>--4 Firm, stable.<BR>--स्थः, --स्थं<BR>1 A<BR>level expanse, level plain; as in<BR>ओषधिप्रस्थ, इंद्रप्रस्थ &c.<BR>--2 Table-land<BR>on the top of a mountain; प्रस्थं<BR>हिमाद्रेर्मृगनाभिगंधि किंचित्<BR>क्वणतकिन्नरमध्युवास Ku. 1. 54; Me. 58.<BR>--3 The<BR>top or peak of a mountain;<BR>Śi. 4. 11 (where it has sense 4 also).<BR>--4 A particular measure of capacity<BR>equal to thirty-two palas.<BR>--5<BR>Anything measuring a Prastha.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुष्पः a variety of holy basil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थंपच
प्रस्थंपच a. Cooking a Prastha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थानं|प्रस्थान
प्रस्थानं<BR>1 Going or setting forth,<BR>departure, moving, walking;<BR>प्रस्थानविक्लवगतेरवलंबनार्थं Ś. 5. 3; R. 4. 88;<BR>Me. 41; Amaru. 31.<BR>--2 Coming to;<BR>Ku. 6. 61.<BR>--3 Sending away,<BR>despatching.<BR>--4 Procession, march.<BR>--5 A<BR>march, the march of an army or<BR>assailant.<BR>--6 A method, system.<BR>--7<BR>Death, dying.<BR>--8 An inferior kind<BR>of drama; see S. D. 276, 544<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थापनं|प्रस्थापन
प्रस्थापनं<BR>1 Sending away,<BR>dismissing, despatching.<BR>--2 Appointment<BR>to an embassy.<BR>--3 Proving,<BR>demonstrating.<BR>--4 Using, employing.<BR>--5<BR>Carrying off cattle.<BR>--ना Sending<BR>away, despatching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थापित|प्रस्थापितः
प्रस्थापित p. p.<BR>1 Sent away,<BR>despatched.<BR>--2 Established, proved.<BR>--3<BR>Urged, pushed on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थायिन्
प्रस्थायिन् a.<BR>1 Departing, going<BR>forth.<BR>--2 Travelling, marching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थित
प्रस्थित p. p. Set out, gone forth,<BR>departed, gone on a journey; (see<BR>स्था with प्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्थितिः|प्रस्थिति
प्रस्थितिः f.<BR>1 Going forth,<BR>departure.<BR>--2 A march, journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नः|प्रस्न
प्रस्नः A vessel for bathing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्निग्ध
प्रस्निग्ध a. Very oily or greasy;<BR>Ś. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नु
प्रस्नु {c2c} P. To distil, pour forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नवः|प्रस्नव
प्रस्नवः<BR>1 Flowing, pouring forth,<BR>exudation; U. 6. 22.<BR>--2 A stream<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">Page0767-c+ 55</a>]<BR>or flow (as of milk); R. 1. 84.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नुत
प्रस्नुत p. p. Dropping, oozing,<BR>pouring forth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्तनी one<BR>whose breasts distil milk (through<BR>excess of maternal love); U. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्नुषा
प्रस्नुषा The wife of a grandson.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्पंदनं|प्रस्पन्दन|प्रस्पंदन
प्रस्पंदनं Palpitating, vibrating,<BR>trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फुट्
प्रस्फुट् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To pierce through,<BR>cleave, split.<BR>--2 To expand, open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फुट|प्रस्फुटः
प्रस्फुट a.<BR>1 Blown, opened,<BR>expanded (as a flower).<BR>--2 Divulged,<BR>published, spread abroad (as a<BR>report).<BR>--3 Plain, clear, manifest,<BR>evident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फोटनं|प्रस्फोटन
प्रस्फोटनं<BR>1 Expanding, blooming,<BR>opening.<BR>--2 Making clear or<BR>manifest, disclosing, revealing.<BR>--3<BR>Splitting.<BR>--4 Causing to bloom or blow.<BR>--5 Threshing corn.<BR>--6 A<BR>winnowing basket.<BR>--7 Striking, beating.<BR>--8<BR>Wiping away, rubbing out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फुर्
प्रस्फुर् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To quiver, tremble.<BR>--2 To expand, be dilated;<BR>प्रास्फुरन्नयनं Mb.<BR>--3 To spread far and wide;<BR>संस्थितस्य गुणोत्कर्षः प्रायः प्रस्फुरति स्फुटं<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्फुरित
प्रस्फुरित p. p. Quivering,<BR>trembling, vibrating, tremulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्मृतिः|प्रस्मृति
प्रस्मृतिः f. Forgetfulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्यंद्|प्रस्यन्द्
प्रस्यंद् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To flow forth,<BR>exude.<BR>--2 To move rapidly, fly away,<BR>run.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्यंदः|प्रस्यन्द|प्रस्यंद|प्रस्यन्दः
प्रस्यंदः --दनं Flowing forth,<BR>exudation; trickling out, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्यंदनं|प्रस्यन्दन|प्रस्यंदन
प्रस्यंदः --दनं Flowing forth,<BR>exudation; trickling out, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रंसिन्
प्रस्रंसिन् a. Miscarrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रु
प्रस्रु {c1c} P.<BR>1 To flow forth or out,<BR>gush forth, ooze out.<BR>--2 To pour<BR>out, let flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रवः|प्रस्रव
प्रस्रवः<BR>1 Trickling forth, gushing,<BR>flowing or oozing out.<BR>--2 A flow,<BR>stream.<BR>--3 Milk flowing from the<BR>breast or udder; प्रस्रवेण (v. l. for<BR>प्रस्नवेन) अभिवर्षंती वत्सालोकप्रवर्तिना<BR>R. 1. 84.<BR>--4 Urine.<BR>--5 The overflowing<BR>scum of boiling rice.<BR>--वाः (pl.)<BR>Falling or gushing tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रवणं|प्रस्रवण|प्रस्रवणः
प्रस्रवणं<BR>1 Flowing or gushing forth,<BR>trickling, oozing, dripping.<BR>--2 Flow<BR>or discharge of milk from the<BR>breast or udder; (वृक्षकान्)<BR>घटस्तनप्रस्रवणैर्व्यवर्धयत् Ku. 5. 14.<BR>--3 A.<BR>fall of water, cascade, cataract.<BR>--4<BR>A spring, fountain; समाचिता प्रस्रवणैः<BR>समंततः Rs. 2. 16; Ms. 8. 248;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">Page0768-a+ 55</a>]<BR>Y. 1. 159.<BR>--5 A spout.<BR>--6 A pool formed<BR>by the mountain streams.<BR>--7 Sweat,<BR>perspiration.<BR>--8 Voiding urine.<BR>--णः<BR>N. of a mountain; जनस्थानमध्यगो<BR>गिरिः प्रस्रवणो नाम U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0767-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रविन्
प्रस्रविन् a.<BR>1 Pouring forth.<BR>--2<BR>Yielding milk; R. 2. 61.<BR>--3 Rich in<BR>milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रावः|प्रस्राव
प्रस्रावः<BR>1 Flowing, oozing.<BR>--2<BR>Urine.<BR>--3 = प्रस्रव (5) q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्रुत
प्रस्रुत p. p. Oozed, trickled,<BR>dropped, issued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वनः|प्रस्वन
प्रस्व(स्वा)नः A loud noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वानः|प्रस्वान
प्रस्व(स्वा)नः A loud noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वापः|प्रस्वाप
प्रस्वापः<BR>1 Sleep.<BR>--2 A dream.<BR>--3<BR>A missile which induces sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वापक
प्रस्वापक a.<BR>1 Causing to fall<BR>asleep, soporific.<BR>--2 Causing to die,<BR>slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वापनं|प्रस्वापन
प्रस्वापनं<BR>1 Causing or inducing<BR>sleep.<BR>--2 A missile which induces<BR>sleep in the person attacked; R. 7. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वादस्
प्रस्वादस् a. Ved. Agreeable,<BR>pleasant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वारः|प्रस्वार
प्रस्वारः Ved. An epithet of the<BR>sacred syllable om (repeated at the<BR>beginning of a Pāṭha or lesson).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्विन्न
प्रस्विन्न p. p. Sweated, perspired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वेदः|प्रस्वेद
प्रस्वेदः Excessive perspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रस्वेदित
प्रस्वेदित p. p.<BR>1 Covered with<BR>sweat, perspired, sweating.<BR>--2<BR>Causing perspiration, hot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहन्
प्रहन् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To kill, slay;<BR>प्राघानिषत रक्षांसि येनाप्तानि वने मम । न प्रहण्मः<BR>कथं पापं वद पूर्वापकारिणं Bk. 9. 102.<BR>--2 To strike, beat, hit; गदाप्रहततनुः<BR>--3 To strike, beat (a drum &c.);<BR>see प्रहत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहणनं|प्रहणन
प्रहणनं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहत|प्रहतं
प्रहत p. p.<BR>1 Wounded, killed,<BR>slain.<BR>--2 Beaten, struck (as a drum);<BR>स स्वयं प्रहतपुष्करः कृती R. 19. 14;<BR>Me. 64.<BR>--3 Repulsed, overcome,<BR>defeated.<BR>--4 Spread, expanded.<BR>--5<BR>Contiguous.<BR>--6 Beaten, frequented<BR>(as a track).<BR>--7 Accomplished,<BR>learned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहणेमिः|प्रहणेमि
प्रहणे(ने)मिः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहनेमिः|प्रहनेमि
प्रहणे(ने)मिः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहस्
प्रहस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To laugh, smile;<BR>ततः प्रहस्यापभयः पुरंदरं R. 3. 51.<BR>--2<BR>To deride, ridicule, mock; हसंतं<BR>प्रहसंत्येता रुदंतं प्ररुदंति च Subhāṣ.<BR>--3<BR>To brighten up, look splendid, cheer<BR>up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसनं|प्रहसन
प्रहसनं<BR>1 Loud or violent<BR>laughter, laughing, mirth.<BR>--2 Ridicule,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">Page0768-b+ 57</a>]<BR>mockery, irony, joke; धिक् प्रहसनं<BR>U. 4.<BR>--3 Satire, satirical writing.<BR>--4<BR>A farce, a kind of low comedy;<BR>S. D.thus defines it:<BR>--भाणवत्संधिसंध्यंगलास्यांगांकौर्विनिमर्तिं । भवेत् प्रहसनं वृत्तं निंद्यानां<BR>कविकल्पितं ॥ 533 et seq.; e. g.<BR>कंदर्पकेलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसंती|प्रहसन्ती
प्रहसंती<BR>1 A kind of jasmine(<BR>पृथिका or वासंती q. v.).<BR>--2 A large<BR>firepan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहसित
प्रहसित p. p. Laughing.<BR>--तं<BR>Laughter, mirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहासः|प्रहास
प्रहासः<BR>1 Violent or loud laughter.<BR>--2 Ridicule, derision.<BR>--3 Irony,<BR>satire.<BR>--4 A dancer, an actor.<BR>--5<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--6 Appearance, display;<BR>Ve. 2. 28.<BR>--7 N. of a place of<BR>pilgrimage; cf. प्रभास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहासकः|प्रहासक
प्रहासकः A jester, buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहासिन्
प्रहासिन् a.<BR>1 Causing laughter,<BR>amusing, diverting.<BR>--2 Joking,<BR>jesting.<BR>--3 Smiling with;<BR>Māl. 9. 15.<BR>--4 Shining, resplendent;<BR>Ku. 5. 37.<BR>--5 Satirical. --m. A jester,<BR>buffoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहस्तः|प्रहस्त
प्रहस्तः<BR>1 The open hand with<BR>the fingers extended.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>general of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहा
प्रहा {c3c} P.<BR>1 To give up, forsake,<BR>abandon, relinquish; प्रजहाति यदा<BR>कामान् Bg. 2. 55, 39; मादेमेतौ प्रहास्येते<BR>Rām.<BR>--2 To let go, cast, discharge;<BR>प्रजहुः शूलपट्टिशान् Bk. 14. 23.<BR>--3<BR>To depart from. --Pass.<BR>1 To be<BR>forsaken or neglected.<BR>--2 To be<BR>lost, to perish.<BR>--3 To vanish, cease,<BR>disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहा
प्रहा Ved. A good throw at dice,<BR>gain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहाणं|प्रहाण
प्रहाणं Abandoning, omitting,<BR>quitting; Śi. 4. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहाणिः|प्रहाणि
प्रहाणिः f.<BR>1 Abandoning.<BR>--2<BR>Deficiency, want.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहीण|प्रहीणः
प्रहीण^1 p. p. Left, quitted,<BR>abandoned.<BR>--णं Destruction, removal,<BR>loss.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: mis-aligned diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहि|प्रहिः
प्रहि {c5c} P.<BR>1 To send forth,<BR>propel.<BR>--2 To throw, discharge, shoot;<BR>विनाशात्तस्य वृक्षस्य रक्षस्तस्मै महोपलं<BR>प्रजिघाय R. 15. 21; Bk. 15. 121.<BR>--3 To send, despatch; हरिरस्मै हरिणीं<BR>सुरांगनां प्रजिघाय R. 8. 79; 11. 49;<BR>12. 84; Bk. 15. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहाय्यः|प्रहाय्य
प्रहाय्यः Ved. A messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहिः|प्रहि
प्रहिः A well.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहित|प्रहितं
प्रहित p. p.<BR>1 Placed, put forth.<BR>--2 Extended, stretched out.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">Page0768-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Sent, despatched, directed;<BR>विचारमार्गप्रहितेन चेतसा Ku. 5. 42.<BR>--4<BR>Discharged, shot (as an arrow).<BR>--5<BR>Appointed.<BR>--6 Appropriate, suitable.<BR>--तं A sauce, condiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहुतः|प्रहुत|प्रहुतं
प्रहुतः --तं An offering of food to<BR>all created beings (भूतयज्ञ), one of<BR>the five daily Yajñas to be<BR>performed by a householder; cf. Ms. 3. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहुतं|प्रहुत|प्रहुतः
प्रहुतः --तं An offering of food to<BR>all created beings (भूतयज्ञ), one of<BR>the five daily Yajñas to be<BR>performed by a householder; cf. Ms. 3. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहुतिः|प्रहुति
प्रहुतिः f. Ved. An excellent<BR>oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृ
प्रहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To strike, strike at,<BR>beat; लत्तया प्रहरति ‘kicks’;<BR>R. 5. 58; Ku. 3. 70; Bk. 9. 7.<BR>--2 To<BR>hurt, injure, wound (with loc.);<BR>आर्तत्राणाय वः शस्त्रं न प्रहर्तुमनागसि<BR>Ś. 1. 11; R. 2. 62; 7. 59; 11. 84;<BR>15. 3.<BR>--3 To attack, assault.<BR>--4 To<BR>throw, cast, hurl (with loc. or dat.).<BR>--5 To seize upon.<BR>--6 To offer,<BR>present (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरः|प्रहर
प्रहरः The eighth part of a whole day,<BR>a watch (a period roughly reckoned<BR>at {3} hours); प्रहरे प्रहरेऽसहोच्चारितानि<BR>गामानयेत्यादिपदानि न प्रमाणं T. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरकः|प्रहरक
प्रहरकः<BR>1 A watch.<BR>--2 Striking the<BR>hours.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरणं|प्रहरण
प्रहरणं<BR>1 Striking, beating.<BR>--2<BR>Casting, throwing.<BR>--3 Assailing,<BR>attacking.<BR>--4 Hurting.<BR>--5 Removing,<BR>expelling.<BR>--6 A weapon, missile; या<BR>(उर्वशी) सुकुमारं प्रहरणं महेंद्रस्य V. 1;<BR>R. 13. 73; Mk. 5. 12; Bg. 1. 9;<BR>Māl. 8. 9.<BR>--7 War, battle, fight.<BR>--8<BR>A covered litter or car.<BR>--9 The box<BR>of a carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरणीयं|प्रहरणीय
प्रहरणीयं A missile, weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहरिन्
प्रहरिन् m.<BR>1 A watchman.<BR>--2 A<BR>bellman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्तृ|प्रहर्त्तृ
प्रहर्तृ a. or s.<BR>1 One who strikes<BR>or beats, an assailant.<BR>--2 Fighting,<BR>a combatant, fighter.<BR>--3 Shooting,<BR>a shooter, an archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारः|प्रहार
प्रहारः<BR>1 Striking, beating,<BR>hitting; Y. 3. 248.<BR>--2 Wounding,<BR>killing.<BR>--3 A stroke, blow, hit, knock,<BR>thump; R. 7. 44; मुष्टिप्रहार,<BR>तलप्रहार &c.<BR>--4 A cut or thrust, as in<BR>खड्गप्रहार.<BR>--5 A kick; as in पादप्रहार;<BR>लत्ताप्रहार.<BR>--6 Shooting.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आर्त a. wounded by a blow.<BR>--(र्तं)<BR>acute pain caused by a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहारणं|प्रहारण
प्रहारणं A desirable gift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृत
प्रहृत p. p.<BR>1 Beaten, struck, hit,<BR>wounded.<BR>--2 Seized.<BR>--तं A blow,<BR>stroke, hit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0768-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्
प्रहृष् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be glad, to rejoice;<BR>न प्रहृष्येत् प्रियं प्राप्य Bg. 5. 20;<BR>11. 36.<BR>--2 To stand on end, bristle (as<BR>hair of the body).<BR>--3 To rejoice before<BR>hand, anticipate pleasure. --Caus.<BR>To gladden, exhilarate, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षः|प्रहर्ष
प्रहर्षः<BR>1 Extreme joy, exultation,<BR>rapture; गुरुः प्रहर्षः प्रबभूव नात्मनि<BR>R. 3. 17.<BR>--2 Erection of the male<BR>organ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षणं|प्रहर्षण|प्रहर्षणः
प्रहर्षणं Enrapturing, making<BR>extremely glad.<BR>--णः The planet<BR>Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षणी
प्रहर्ष(र्षि)णी<BR>1 Turmeric.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a metre; see App. I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षिणी
प्रहर्ष(र्षि)णी<BR>1 Turmeric.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a metre; see App. I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहर्षुलः|प्रहर्षुल
प्रहर्षुलः The planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्ट
प्रहृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Delighted, pleased,<BR>glad, overjoyed.<BR>--2 Thrilling,<BR>bristling (as hair).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन्,<BR>--चित्त, --मनस् a. delighted in soul,<BR>rejoiced at heart.<BR>--रूप a. looking<BR>pleased. {2} of a pleasing form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहृष्टकः|प्रहृष्टक
प्रहृष्टकः A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेणकं|प्रहेणक
प्रहेणकं<BR>1 A kind of pastry (पिष्टक).<BR>--2 Sweetmeats distributed at<BR>festivals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलकः|प्रहेलक|प्रहेलकं
प्रहेलकः<BR>1 A kind of cake or<BR>sweetmeat.<BR>--2 A riddle; see प्रहेलिका<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेला
प्रहेला Free or unrestrained<BR>behaviour, loose conduct, playful<BR>dalliance; Pt. 2. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रहेलिः|प्रहेलि
प्रहेलिः f., प्रहेलिका A riddle, an<BR>enigma, a conundrum. It is thus<BR>defined in the विदग्धमुखमंडनः -<BR>व्यक्तीकृत्य कमप्यर्थं स्वरूपार्थस्य गोपनात् । यत्र<BR>बाह्यांतरावर्थौ कथ्येते सा प्रहेलिका. It is<BR>आर्थी or शाब्दी; तरुण्यालिंगितः कंठे<BR>नितंबस्थलमाश्रितः । गुरूणां सन्निधानेऽपि कः<BR>कूजति मुहुर्मुहुः (where the answer is<BR>ईषदूनजलपूर्णकुंभः) is an instance of the<BR>former kind; सदारि मध्यापि न वैरियुक्ता<BR>नितांतरक्ताप्यसितैव नित्यं । यथोक्तवादिन्यपि<BR>नैव दूती का नाम कांतेति निवेदयाशु ॥<BR>(where the answer is सारिका), of the<BR>latter. Daṇḍin, however, mentions<BR>16 different kinds of प्रलेहिका; see<BR>Kāv. 3. 96-124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्रासः|प्रह्रास
प्रह्रासः<BR>1 Diminution, decrease.<BR>--2 Languishing, fading away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लाद्
प्रह्लाद् {c1c} A. To be greatly<BR>delighted, rejoice. --Caus. To delight,<BR>exhilarate, gladden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लन्न|प्रह्लन्नः
प्रह्लन्न p. p. Delighted, joyful,<BR>pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लन्निः|प्रह्लन्नि
प्रह्लन्निः f. Pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्रादः|प्रह्राद
प्रह्रा(ह्ला)दः<BR>1 Great joy, pleasure,<BR>delight, happiness.<BR>--2 Sound.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a son of the demon<BR>HiraṇyaKaśipu. [According to the<BR>PadmaPurāṇa, he was a Brāhmaṇa in his<BR>previous existence, and when born as son<BR>of Hiraṇya-Kaśipu, he still retained his<BR>ardent devotion to Viṣṇu. His father,<BR>of course, did not like that his own son<BR>should be such a devout worshipper of<BR>his mortal enemies, the gods, and with<BR>the object of getting rid of him, he<BR>subjected him to a variety of cruelties;<BR>but Prahlāda, by the favour of Viṣṇu,<BR>was quite unscathed, and began to<BR>preach with even greater earnestness<BR>than before the doctrine that Viṣṇu<BR>filled all space and was omni-present,<BR>omni-scient, omni-potent.<BR>Hiraṇya-Kaśipu in a fit of exasperation asked him<BR>“If Viṣṇu is omni-present how do I<BR>not see him in the pillar of this hall”?<BR>Whereupon Prahlāda struck the pillar<BR>with his fist (according to another<BR>account, Hiraṇya-Kaśipu himself<BR>angrily kicked the pillar to convince his<BR>son of the absurdity of his faith), when<BR>Viṣṇu came out half-man and half-lion,<BR>and tore Hiraṇya-Kaśipu to pieces.<BR>Prahlāda succeeded his father, and reigned<BR>wisely and righteously.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लादः|प्रह्लाद
प्रह्रा(ह्ला)दः<BR>1 Great joy, pleasure,<BR>delight, happiness.<BR>--2 Sound.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a son of the demon<BR>HiraṇyaKaśipu. [According to the<BR>PadmaPurāṇa, he was a Brāhmaṇa in his<BR>previous existence, and when born as son<BR>of Hiraṇya-Kaśipu, he still retained his<BR>ardent devotion to Viṣṇu. His father,<BR>of course, did not like that his own son<BR>should be such a devout worshipper of<BR>his mortal enemies, the gods, and with<BR>the object of getting rid of him, he<BR>subjected him to a variety of cruelties;<BR>but Prahlāda, by the favour of Viṣṇu,<BR>was quite unscathed, and began to<BR>preach with even greater earnestness<BR>than before the doctrine that Viṣṇu<BR>filled all space and was omni-present,<BR>omni-scient, omni-potent.<BR>Hiraṇya-Kaśipu in a fit of exasperation asked him<BR>“If Viṣṇu is omni-present how do I<BR>not see him in the pillar of this hall”?<BR>Whereupon Prahlāda struck the pillar<BR>with his fist (according to another<BR>account, Hiraṇya-Kaśipu himself<BR>angrily kicked the pillar to convince his<BR>son of the absurdity of his faith), when<BR>Viṣṇu came out half-man and half-lion,<BR>and tore Hiraṇya-Kaśipu to pieces.<BR>Prahlāda succeeded his father, and reigned<BR>wisely and righteously.]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्रादन
प्रह्रा(ह्ला)दन a. Gladdening,<BR>delighting; R. 13. 4.<BR>--नं Causing<BR>joy or delight, gladdening,<BR>delighting; यथा प्रह्ळादनाच्चंद्रः R. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्लादन
प्रह्रा(ह्ला)दन a. Gladdening,<BR>delighting; R. 13. 4.<BR>--नं Causing<BR>joy or delight, gladdening,<BR>delighting; यथा प्रह्ळादनाच्चंद्रः R. 4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्व|प्रह्वः
प्रह्व a.<BR>1 Sloping, slanting,<BR>inclined; Śi. 12. 56.<BR>--2 Stooping,<BR>bent down; bowing humbly down;<BR>एष प्रह्वोस्मि भगवन् एषा विज्ञापना च नः<BR>Mv. 1. 47; 6. 37.<BR>--3 Submissive,<BR>humble, modestly submitting;<BR>प्रह्वेष्वनिर्बंधरुषो हि संतः R. 16. 80.<BR>--4 Devoted or attached to,<BR>engaged in, engrossed by.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजलि a. bowing with the palms<BR>of the hand joined and put to the<BR>forehead as a mark of respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वयति
प्रह्वयति Den. P. To make humble,<BR>subdue; तदौद्धत्यं क्वापि व्रजति विनयः<BR>प्रह्वयति मां U. 6. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वलिका
प्रह्वलिका See प्रहेलिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रह्वायः|प्रह्वाय
प्रह्वायः A call, summons,<BR>invitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांशु|प्रांशुः
प्रांशु a. [प्रकृष्टाः अंशवोऽत्र]<BR>1 High,<BR>tall, lofty, of lofty or great stature<BR>(as a man); शालप्रांशुर्महाभुजः<BR>R. 1. 13; 15. 19.<BR>--2 Long, extended;<BR>Ś. 2. 15.<BR>--शुः A tall man, a man of<BR>great stature; प्रांशुलभ्ये फले<BR>मोहादुद्बाहुरिव वामनः R. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्
प्राक् ind.<BR>1 Before(usually<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">Page0769-c+ 55</a>]<BR>with abl.), सफलानि निमित्तानि<BR>प्राक्प्रभाता त्ततो मम Bk. 8. 106; प्राक्<BR>सृष्टेः केवलात्मने Ku. 2. 4; R. 14. 78<BR>Ś. 5. 21.<BR>--2 At first, already;<BR>प्रमन्यवः प्रागपि कोशलेंद्रे R. 7. 34.<BR>--3<BR>Before, previously, in a previous<BR>portion (as of a book); इति प्रागेव<BR>निर्दिष्टं; Ms. 1. 71.<BR>--4 In the east, to<BR>the east of; ग्रामात्प्राक् पर्वतः.<BR>--5 In<BR>front.<BR>--6 As far as, up to; प्राक्<BR>कडारात्.<BR>--7 At dawn or daybreak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकट्यं|प्राकट्य
प्राकट्यं Manifestation,<BR>publicity, notoriety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकरणिक
प्राकरणिक a. (की f.)<BR>Pertaining to the subject of discussion,<BR>relevant to the matter in hand<BR>(often used in the sense of उपमेय in<BR>works on Rhetoric);<BR>अप्राकरणिकस्याभिधानेन प्राकरणिकस्याक्षेपोऽ<BR>प्रस्तुतप्रशंसा K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकर्षिक
प्राकर्षिक a. (की f.) Entitled<BR>to preference or superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकषिकः|प्राकषिक
प्राकषिकः<BR>1 A catamite.<BR>--2 A<BR>man supported by another's wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाम्यं|प्राकाम्य
प्राकाम्यं<BR>1 Freedom of will;<BR>प्राकाम्यं ते विभूतिषु Ku. 2. 11.<BR>--2<BR>Wilfulness.<BR>--3 Irresistible will,<BR>considered as one of the eight<BR>attributes or siddhis of Śiva or the<BR>Supreme Being; see सिद्धि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकारः|प्राकार
प्राकारः<BR>1 A fence, a wall, an<BR>enclosure.<BR>--2 An encircling or<BR>surrounding wall, rampart; द्वितीयं<BR>हेमप्राकारं कुर्वद्भिरिव वानरैः R. 12. 71;<BR>Pt. 1. 229.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकारीय
प्राकारीय a.<BR>1 Fit for a wall.<BR>--2<BR>Enclosed by a wall, walled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाशः|प्राकाश
प्राकाशः Ved.<BR>1 A metallic<BR>mirror.<BR>--2 A kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकाश्यं|प्राकाश्य
प्राकाश्यं<BR>1 Being known,<BR>evident or clear, publicity.<BR>--2 Fame,<BR>celebrity, renown; प्राकाश्यं<BR>स्वगुणोदयेन गुणिनो गच्छति किं जम्मना<BR>Pt. 1. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृत|प्राकृतः
प्राकृत a. (ता-ती f.) [प्रकृतेरयं<BR>प्रकृत्या निर्वृत्तो वा अण्]<BR>1 Original,<BR>natural, unaltered, unmodified;<BR>स्याताममित्रौ मित्रे च सहजप्राकृतावपि Śi. 2. 36<BR>(see Malli. thereon).<BR>--2 Usual,<BR>common, ordinary.<BR>--3<BR>Uncultivated, vulgar, unrefined, illiterate;<BR>प्राकृत इव परिभूयमानमात्मानं न रुणत्सि<BR>K. 146; Bg. 18. 28.<BR>--4<BR>Insignificant, unimportant, trifling; Mu. 1.<BR>--5 Derived from Prakṛti, q. v.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-a" target="_blank">Page0770-a+ 56</a>]<BR>प्राकृतो लयः ‘reabsorption into<BR>Prakṛti.’<BR>--6 Provincial, vernacular (as<BR>a dialect); see below.<BR>--तः A low<BR>man, an ordinary or vulgar man.<BR>--तं A vernacular or provincial<BR>dialect derived from and akin to<BR>Sanskrit; प्रकृतिः संस्कृतं तत्र भवं तत<BR>आगतं च प्राकृतं Hemacandra. (Many<BR>of these dialects are spoken by the<BR>female characters and inferior<BR>personages of Sanskrit plays);<BR>तद्भवस्तत्समो देशीत्यनेकः प्राकृतक्रमः<BR>Kāv. 1. 33; also 34, 35;<BR>त्वमप्यस्मादृशजनयोग्ये प्राकृतमार्गे प्रवृत्तोऽसि Vb. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः a natural enemy, i. e. the<BR>ruler of an adjacent country; see<BR>Malli. on Śi. 2. 36.<BR>--उदासीनः a<BR>natural neutral; i. e. a ruler whose<BR>dominions lie beyond those of the<BR>natural ally.<BR>--ज्वरः a common or<BR>ordinary fever.<BR>--प्रलयः complete<BR>dissolution of the universe.<BR>--मित्रं<BR>a natural ally; i. e. a ruler whose<BR>dominions lie immediately beyond<BR>those of the natural enemy (i. e.<BR>whose country is separated from<BR>the country with which he is<BR>allied by that of another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0769-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राकृतिक|प्राकृतिकः
प्राकृतिक a. (की f.) [प्रकृत्या निर्वृत्तः<BR>ठञ्]<BR>1 Natural, derived from nature;<BR>Mv. 7. 39.<BR>--2 Illusory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राक्तन|प्राक्तनः
प्राक्तन a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Former,<BR>previous, antecedent; प्रपेदिरे<BR>प्राक्तनजन्मविद्याः Ku. 1. 30.<BR>--2 Old, ancient,<BR>early.<BR>--3 Relating to a former life<BR>or acts in a former life; संस्काराः<BR>प्राक्तना इव R. 1. 20; Ku. 6. 10.<BR>--नं<BR>(or प्राक्तनकर्मन्) n. Fate, destiny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राखर्यं|प्राखर्य|प्राखर्य्य|प्राखर्य्यं
प्राखर्यं<BR>1 Sharpness.<BR>--2 Pungency.<BR>--3 Wickedness.<BR>--4 Ardour, zeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागल्भ्यं|प्रागल्भ्य
प्रागल्भ्यं<BR>1 Boldness, confidence;<BR>निःसाध्वसत्वं प्रागल्भ्यं S. D.<BR>--2 Pride,<BR>arrogance.<BR>--3 Proficiency, skill.<BR>--4<BR>Development, greatness, maturity;<BR>बुद्धिप्रागल्भ्य, तमःप्रागल्भ्य &c.<BR>--5<BR>Manifestation, appearance; अवाप्तः<BR>प्रागल्म्यं परिणतरुचः शैलतनये K. P. 10<BR>‘which has appeared’.<BR>--6<BR>Eloquence, प्रागल्भ्यहीनस्य नरस्य विद्या<BR>शस्त्रं यथा कापुरुषस्य हस्ते (where प्रा˚<BR>may mean ‘boldness’ also);<BR>Māl. 3. 11.<BR>--7 Pomp, rank.<BR>--8<BR>Resoluteness, determination.<BR>--9 Impudence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रागारः|प्रागार
प्रागारः A house, building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्रं|प्राग्र
प्राग्रं The highest point.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सर a. first, fore most; त्वमर्हतां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">Page0770-b+ 55</a>]<BR>प्राग्रसरः स्मृतोऽसि नः Ś. 5. 15.<BR>--हर a.<BR>chief, principal; विश्वावसु प्राग्रहरैः<BR>प्रवीणैः Ku. 7. 48; R. 16. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्राटः|प्राग्राट|प्राग्राटं
प्राग्राटः Thin coagulated milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राग्र्य|प्राग्र्यं
प्राग्र्य a. Chief, foremost, best,<BR>most excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघातः|प्राघात
प्राघातः War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघारः|प्राघार
प्राघारः Trickling out, dropping,<BR>oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघुणः|प्राघुण
प्राघुणः, प्राघुणकः, प्राघुणिकः, प्राघूर्णकः, प्राघूर्णिकः<BR>A guest, visitor;<BR>चिरापराधस्मृतिमांसलोऽपि रोषः<BR>क्षणप्राघुणिको बभूव Bv. 2. 66; श्रवणप्राघुणिकी<BR>कृता जनैः (कथा) N. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघुणकः|प्राघुणक
प्राघुणः, प्राघुणकः, प्राघुणिकः, प्राघूर्णकः, प्राघूर्णिकः<BR>A guest, visitor;<BR>चिरापराधस्मृतिमांसलोऽपि रोषः<BR>क्षणप्राघुणिको बभूव Bv. 2. 66; श्रवणप्राघुणिकी<BR>कृता जनैः (कथा) N. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघुणिकः|प्राघुणिक
प्राघुणः, प्राघुणकः, प्राघुणिकः, प्राघूर्णकः, प्राघूर्णिकः<BR>A guest, visitor;<BR>चिरापराधस्मृतिमांसलोऽपि रोषः<BR>क्षणप्राघुणिको बभूव Bv. 2. 66; श्रवणप्राघुणिकी<BR>कृता जनैः (कथा) N. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघूर्णकः|प्राघूर्णक
प्राघुणः, प्राघुणकः, प्राघुणिकः, प्राघूर्णकः, प्राघूर्णिकः<BR>A guest, visitor;<BR>चिरापराधस्मृतिमांसलोऽपि रोषः<BR>क्षणप्राघुणिको बभूव Bv. 2. 66; श्रवणप्राघुणिकी<BR>कृता जनैः (कथा) N. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राघूर्णिकः|प्राघूर्णिक
प्राघुणः, प्राघुणकः, प्राघुणिकः, प्राघूर्णकः, प्राघूर्णिकः<BR>A guest, visitor;<BR>चिरापराधस्मृतिमांसलोऽपि रोषः<BR>क्षणप्राघुणिको बभूव Bv. 2. 66; श्रवणप्राघुणिकी<BR>कृता जनैः (कथा) N. 2. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांगं|प्राङ्ग|प्रांग|प्राङ्गः
प्रांगं A small kind of drum (<BR>पणव).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांगणं|प्राङ्गण|प्रांगण|प्राङ्गणं
प्रांगणं(नं)<BR>1 A court,<BR>courtyard.<BR>--2 A floor (as of the house).<BR>--3 A kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांगनं|प्राङ्गन|प्रांगन
प्रांगणं(नं)<BR>1 A court,<BR>courtyard.<BR>--2 A floor (as of the house).<BR>--3 A kind of drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्
प्राच्, प्रांच् a. (ची f.)<BR>1 Turned<BR>towards the front, in front,<BR>foremost.<BR>--2 Eastern, easterly.<BR>--3 Prior,<BR>previous, former. --m. (pl.)<BR>1 The<BR>people of the east.<BR>--2 Eastern<BR>grammarians.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्र a. (प्रागग्र)<BR>having the point turned towards the<BR>east.<BR>--अभावः (प्रागभावः) {1}<BR>antecedent non-existence, non-existence of<BR>a thing previous to its production,<BR>as of an effect previous to its<BR>production. {2} (in law)<BR>non-possession of property (that may be<BR>possessed).<BR>--अभिहित (प्रागभिहित) a.<BR>mentioned before.<BR>--अवस्था (<BR>प्रागग्रस्था) the former state; न तर्हि<BR>प्रागवस्थायाः परिहीयसे Māl. 4 ‘you are<BR>none the worse for it’.<BR>--आयत (<BR>प्रागायत) a. extending towards the<BR>east.<BR>--उक्तिः f. (प्रागुक्तिः) previous<BR>utterance.<BR>--उत्तर (प्रागुत्तर) a.<BR>northeastern.<BR>--उदंच् a. (प्रागुदंच्)<BR>northeastern.<BR>--उदीची (प्रागुदीची) f. the<BR>northeast.<BR>--कर्मन् (प्राक्कर्मन्) n. {1}<BR>an action done in a former life. {2}<BR>a preliminary medical treatment. {3}<BR>a preliminary action in general.<BR>--कालः (प्राक्कालः) a former age.<BR>--कालीन (प्राक्कालीन) a. belonging to the<BR>former times, old, ancient.<BR>--कूल<BR>(प्राक्कूल) a. having the points<BR>turned towards the east (said of Kuśa<BR>grass); Ms. 2. 75.<BR>--(लं) the point<BR>of a blade of such Kuśa grass.<BR>--कृतं<BR>(प्राक्कृतं) an act done in a former<BR>life.<BR>--केवल a. (प्राक्केवल)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-c" target="_blank">Page0770-c+ 57</a>]<BR>manifested from the first in a<BR>distinct form.<BR>--गामिन् a. (प्राग्गामिन्)<BR>{1} going before, preceding. {2} a<BR>precursor, forerunner. {3} going<BR>eastward.<BR>--चरणा (प्राक्चरणा) the<BR>female organ of generation.<BR>--चिरं (<BR>प्राक्चिरं) ind. in due or good time,<BR>before too late.<BR>--जन्मन् (प्राग्जन्मन्)<BR>n.,<BR>--जातिः (प्राग्जातिः) f. a former<BR>birth.<BR>--ज्योतिषः (प्राग्योतिषः) {1} N.<BR>of country, also called Kāmarūpa. {2}<BR>the people of this country (pl.)<BR>--(षं) N. of a city. ˚ज्येष्ठः an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--दक्षिण a. (<BR>प्राग्दक्षिण) south-eastern.<BR>--देशः (प्राग्देशः)<BR>the eastern country.<BR>--द्वार, --द्वारिक<BR>a. (प्राग्द्वार &c.) having doors facing<BR>the east.<BR>--न्यायः (प्राङ्न्यायः) the<BR>plea of a former trial, res judicata;<BR>आचारेणावसन्नोपि पुतर्लेखय ते यदि ।<BR>सोभिधेयोजितः पूर्वं प्राङ्न्यायस्तु स उच्यते ॥<BR>--पदं (प्राक्पदं) the first member of<BR>a compound.<BR>--प्रहारः (<BR>प्राक्प्रहारः) the first blow.<BR>--फलः (<BR>प्राक्फलः) the bread-fruit tree.<BR>--फ<BR>(फा) ल्गुनी (प्राक्फल्गुनी) the<BR>eleventh lunar mansion, (पूर्वा). ˚भवः<BR>{1} the planet Jupiter. {2} N. of<BR>Bṛhaspati.<BR>--फाल्गुनः, --फाल्गुनेयः<BR>(प्राक्फाल्गुनः &c.) the planet<BR>Jupiter.<BR>--भक्तं (प्राग्भक्तं) taking<BR>medicine before meals.<BR>--भागः (<BR>प्राग्भागः) {1} the front. {2} the forepart.<BR>--भारः (प्राग्भारः) {1} the top or<BR>summit of a mountain; Māl. 9. 15.<BR>{2} the front part, forepart or end<BR>(of anything);<BR>क्रंदत्फेरवचंडडात्कृतिभृतप्राग्भारभीमैस्तटैः Māl. 5. 19. {3}<BR>a large quantity, heap, multitude,<BR>flood; Bh. 3. 129; Māl. 5. 29.<BR>--भावः (प्राग्भावः) {1} previous<BR>existence. {2} excellence, superiority.<BR>--मुख (प्राङ्मुख) a. {1} turned towards<BR>or facing the east; Ku. 7. 13;<BR>Ms. 2. 51; 8. 87. {2} inclined towards,<BR>wishing, desirous of.<BR>--वंशः (<BR>प्राग्वंशः) {1} a kind of sacrificial room<BR>having its columns turned towards<BR>the east; R. 15. 61 (प्राचीनस्थूणो<BR>यज्ञशालाविशेषः Malli.; but some<BR>interpret the word to mean ‘a room in<BR>which the friends and family of the<BR>sacrificer assemble’). {2} a former<BR>dynasty or generation.<BR>--वृत्तं =<BR>प्राङ्न्यायः q. v.<BR>--वृत्तांतः (प्राग्वृत्तांतः)<BR>a former event.<BR>--शिरस् --स, --शिरस्क<BR>(प्राक्शिरस् &c.) a. having the head<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">Page0771-a+ 56</a>]<BR>turned towards the east.<BR>--संध्या<BR>(प्राक्संध्या) the morning twilight.<BR>--सवनं (प्राक्सवनं) a morning<BR>libation or sacrifice.<BR>--स्रोतस् (<BR>प्राक्स्रोतस्) a. flowing eastward. (--f.) a<BR>river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांच्|प्राञ्च्
प्राच्, प्रांच् a. (ची f.)<BR>1 Turned<BR>towards the front, in front,<BR>foremost.<BR>--2 Eastern, easterly.<BR>--3 Prior,<BR>previous, former. --m. (pl.)<BR>1 The<BR>people of the east.<BR>--2 Eastern<BR>grammarians.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्र a. (प्रागग्र)<BR>having the point turned towards the<BR>east.<BR>--अभावः (प्रागभावः) {1}<BR>antecedent non-existence, non-existence of<BR>a thing previous to its production,<BR>as of an effect previous to its<BR>production. {2} (in law)<BR>non-possession of property (that may be<BR>possessed).<BR>--अभिहित (प्रागभिहित) a.<BR>mentioned before.<BR>--अवस्था (<BR>प्रागग्रस्था) the former state; न तर्हि<BR>प्रागवस्थायाः परिहीयसे Māl. 4 ‘you are<BR>none the worse for it’.<BR>--आयत (<BR>प्रागायत) a. extending towards the<BR>east.<BR>--उक्तिः f. (प्रागुक्तिः) previous<BR>utterance.<BR>--उत्तर (प्रागुत्तर) a.<BR>northeastern.<BR>--उदंच् a. (प्रागुदंच्)<BR>northeastern.<BR>--उदीची (प्रागुदीची) f. the<BR>northeast.<BR>--कर्मन् (प्राक्कर्मन्) n. {1}<BR>an action done in a former life. {2}<BR>a preliminary medical treatment. {3}<BR>a preliminary action in general.<BR>--कालः (प्राक्कालः) a former age.<BR>--कालीन (प्राक्कालीन) a. belonging to the<BR>former times, old, ancient.<BR>--कूल<BR>(प्राक्कूल) a. having the points<BR>turned towards the east (said of Kuśa<BR>grass); Ms. 2. 75.<BR>--(लं) the point<BR>of a blade of such Kuśa grass.<BR>--कृतं<BR>(प्राक्कृतं) an act done in a former<BR>life.<BR>--केवल a. (प्राक्केवल)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-c" target="_blank">Page0770-c+ 57</a>]<BR>manifested from the first in a<BR>distinct form.<BR>--गामिन् a. (प्राग्गामिन्)<BR>{1} going before, preceding. {2} a<BR>precursor, forerunner. {3} going<BR>eastward.<BR>--चरणा (प्राक्चरणा) the<BR>female organ of generation.<BR>--चिरं (<BR>प्राक्चिरं) ind. in due or good time,<BR>before too late.<BR>--जन्मन् (प्राग्जन्मन्)<BR>n.,<BR>--जातिः (प्राग्जातिः) f. a former<BR>birth.<BR>--ज्योतिषः (प्राग्योतिषः) {1} N.<BR>of country, also called Kāmarūpa. {2}<BR>the people of this country (pl.)<BR>--(षं) N. of a city. ˚ज्येष्ठः an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--दक्षिण a. (<BR>प्राग्दक्षिण) south-eastern.<BR>--देशः (प्राग्देशः)<BR>the eastern country.<BR>--द्वार, --द्वारिक<BR>a. (प्राग्द्वार &c.) having doors facing<BR>the east.<BR>--न्यायः (प्राङ्न्यायः) the<BR>plea of a former trial, res judicata;<BR>आचारेणावसन्नोपि पुतर्लेखय ते यदि ।<BR>सोभिधेयोजितः पूर्वं प्राङ्न्यायस्तु स उच्यते ॥<BR>--पदं (प्राक्पदं) the first member of<BR>a compound.<BR>--प्रहारः (<BR>प्राक्प्रहारः) the first blow.<BR>--फलः (<BR>प्राक्फलः) the bread-fruit tree.<BR>--फ<BR>(फा) ल्गुनी (प्राक्फल्गुनी) the<BR>eleventh lunar mansion, (पूर्वा). ˚भवः<BR>{1} the planet Jupiter. {2} N. of<BR>Bṛhaspati.<BR>--फाल्गुनः, --फाल्गुनेयः<BR>(प्राक्फाल्गुनः &c.) the planet<BR>Jupiter.<BR>--भक्तं (प्राग्भक्तं) taking<BR>medicine before meals.<BR>--भागः (<BR>प्राग्भागः) {1} the front. {2} the forepart.<BR>--भारः (प्राग्भारः) {1} the top or<BR>summit of a mountain; Māl. 9. 15.<BR>{2} the front part, forepart or end<BR>(of anything);<BR>क्रंदत्फेरवचंडडात्कृतिभृतप्राग्भारभीमैस्तटैः Māl. 5. 19. {3}<BR>a large quantity, heap, multitude,<BR>flood; Bh. 3. 129; Māl. 5. 29.<BR>--भावः (प्राग्भावः) {1} previous<BR>existence. {2} excellence, superiority.<BR>--मुख (प्राङ्मुख) a. {1} turned towards<BR>or facing the east; Ku. 7. 13;<BR>Ms. 2. 51; 8. 87. {2} inclined towards,<BR>wishing, desirous of.<BR>--वंशः (<BR>प्राग्वंशः) {1} a kind of sacrificial room<BR>having its columns turned towards<BR>the east; R. 15. 61 (प्राचीनस्थूणो<BR>यज्ञशालाविशेषः Malli.; but some<BR>interpret the word to mean ‘a room in<BR>which the friends and family of the<BR>sacrificer assemble’). {2} a former<BR>dynasty or generation.<BR>--वृत्तं =<BR>प्राङ्न्यायः q. v.<BR>--वृत्तांतः (प्राग्वृत्तांतः)<BR>a former event.<BR>--शिरस् --स, --शिरस्क<BR>(प्राक्शिरस् &c.) a. having the head<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">Page0771-a+ 56</a>]<BR>turned towards the east.<BR>--संध्या<BR>(प्राक्संध्या) the morning twilight.<BR>--सवनं (प्राक्सवनं) a morning<BR>libation or sacrifice.<BR>--स्रोतस् (<BR>प्राक्स्रोतस्) a. flowing eastward. (--f.) a<BR>river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0770-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राची
प्राची The east; तनयमचिरात्<BR>प्राचीवार्कं प्रसूयं च पावनं Ś. 4. 18.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिः an epithet of Indra.<BR>--मूलं<BR>the eastern horizon; प्राचीमूले<BR>तनुमिव कलामात्रशेषां हिमांशोः Me. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीन|प्राचीनः
प्राचीन a. [प्रच् भवार्थे ख]<BR>1<BR>Turned towards the front or east,<BR>eastern, easterly.<BR>--2 Previous,<BR>former, previously mentioned.<BR>--3 Old,<BR>ancient.<BR>--नः -नं A fence, wall.<BR>--नं ind.<BR>1 In front.<BR>--2 Eastward<BR>(abl.).<BR>--3 Before.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्र a.<BR>= प्रागग्र q. v.<BR>--आवीतं the sacred<BR>thread (यज्ञोपवीत) worn over the<BR>right shoulder and passed under<BR>the left arm, as at a Śrāddha.<BR>--आवीतिन्, --उपवीत a. wearing the<BR>sacred thread over the right<BR>shoulder and under the left arm;<BR>Ms. 2. 63.<BR>--कल्पः a former kalpa q. v.<BR>--गाथा an ancient story.<BR>--तिलकः<BR>the moon.<BR>--पनसः the Bilva tree.<BR>--बर्हिस् m. an epithet of Indra.<BR>--मतं an ancient opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्य|प्राच्यः
प्राच्य a. [प्राचि भवः यत्]<BR>1 Being<BR>or situated in front.<BR>--2 Being or<BR>living in the east, eastern, easterly.<BR>--3 Prior, preceding, previous.<BR>--4<BR>Ancient, old.<BR>--च्याः (pl.)<BR>1 ‘The<BR>eastern country’, the country south<BR>or east of the river Sarasvatī.<BR>--2<BR>The people of this country.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भांषा the eastern dialect, language<BR>spoken in the east of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राच्यक
प्राच्यक a. Eastern, easterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचंड्यं|प्राचण्ड्य|प्राचंड्य
प्राचंड्यं<BR>1 Vehemence, passion.<BR>--2 Fierceness, horrible look;<BR>प्राचंड्यं वहति नखायुधस्य मार्गः<BR>Māl. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचिका
प्राचिका<BR>1 A mosquito.<BR>--2 A<BR>female falcon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचीरं|प्राचीर
प्राचीरं An enclosure, fence, wall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचुर्यं|प्राचुर्य
प्राचुर्यं<BR>1 Abundance,<BR>copiousness, plenty.<BR>--2 Multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राचेतसः|प्राचेतस
प्राचेतसः<BR>1 A patronymic of<BR>Manu.<BR>--2 Of Dakṣa.<BR>--3 Of<BR>Vālmīki.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राछ्|प्राच्छ्
प्राछ् a. (Nom. sing. प्राट्-ड्)<BR>Asking, inquiring, questioning; as<BR>in शब्दप्राट्.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विवाकः (<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">Page0771-b+ 56</a>]<BR>प्राड्विवाकः) a judge, the presiding<BR>officer in a court of law; Ms. 8. 79,<BR>181; 9. 234.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजकः|प्राजक
प्राजकः A charioteer, driver,<BR>coachman; Ms. 8. 293.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजनः|प्राजन|प्राजनं
प्राजनः --नं A whip, goad;<BR>त्यक्तप्राजनरश्मिरंकिततनुः पार्थांकितैर्मार्गणैः<BR>Ve. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजनं|प्राजन|प्राजनः
प्राजनः --नं A whip, goad;<BR>त्यक्तप्राजनरश्मिरंकिततनुः पार्थांकितैर्मार्गणैः<BR>Ve. 5. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजहितः|प्राजहित
प्राजहितः The Gārhapatya fire,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजापत्य|प्राजापत्यं|प्राजापत्यः
प्राजापत्य a. [प्रजापतिर्देवताऽस्य यक्]<BR>1 Sacred to Prajāpati.<BR>--2 Born of<BR>Prajāpati (Brahmā); Ku. 6. 34.<BR>--3<BR>Belonging to Prajāpati; R. 10. 52.<BR>--त्यः<BR>1 One of the eight forms of<BR>marriage in Hindu law, in which<BR>the father gives his daughter to<BR>the bridegroom without receiving<BR>any present from him in order that<BR>the two may live happily and<BR>faithfully together; सहोभौ चरतां धर्ममिति<BR>वाचानुभाष्य च । कन्याप्रदानमभ्यर्च्यं प्राजापत्यो<BR>विधिः स्मृतः ॥ Ms. 3. 30; or इत्युक्त्वा<BR>चरतां धर्मं सह या दीयतेऽर्थिने । स कायः (i. e.<BR>प्राजापत्यः) पावयेत्तज्जः षट्<BR>षड्वंश्यान्सहात्मना Y. 1. 60.<BR>--2 N. of the<BR>confluence of the Ganges and Yamunā<BR>(प्रयाग); (also n.).<BR>--3 (with तिथि)<BR>The eighth day in the dark half<BR>of the month of Pauṣa.<BR>--4 N of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--5 A kind of fast or<BR>penance; त्र्यहं प्रातस्त्र्यहं सायं<BR>त्र्यहमद्यादयाचितम् । त्र्यहं परं च न श्नयीत्<BR>प्राजापत्पमिति स्मृतम् ॥.<BR>--6 The heaven of the<BR>Manes (पितृलोक).<BR>--त्यं Giving<BR>away the whole of one's property<BR>before entering upon the life of an<BR>ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजिकः|प्राजिक
प्राजिकः --प्राजिन् m. A hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजिन्
प्राजिकः --प्राजिन् m. A hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजितृ
प्राजितृ m. A charioteer, driver,<BR>coachman; Śi. 18. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राजेशं|प्राजेश
प्राजेशं The constellation Rohiṇī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्ञ|प्राज्ञः
प्राज्ञ a. (ज्ञा or ज्ञी f.)<BR>[प्रज्ञ एव स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>1<BR>Intellectual.<BR>--2 Wise, learned, clever;<BR>किमुच्यते प्राज्ञः खलु कुमारः U. 4.<BR>--ज्ञः<BR>1 A wise or learned man; तेभ्यः<BR>प्राज्ञा न बिभ्यति Ve. 2. 14;<BR>Bg. 17. 14.<BR>--2 A kind of parrot.<BR>--ज्ञा<BR>1<BR>Intelligence, understanding.<BR>--2 A<BR>clever or intelligent woman.<BR>--ज्ञी<BR>1 A clever or learned woman.<BR>--2<BR>The wife of a learned man.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a wife of the sun (सूर्यपत्नी).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कथा a story about a wise<BR>man.<BR>--मन्य, --मानिन् or प्राज्ञंमामिन् a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-c" target="_blank">Page0771-c+ 56</a>]<BR>fancying oneself to be wise,<BR>conceited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राज्य|प्राज्यं
प्राज्य a.<BR>1 Abundant, copious,<BR>plentiful, much, many; तव भवतु<BR>बिडौजाः प्राज्यवृष्टिः प्रजासु Ś. 7. 34;<BR>R. 13. 62; Śi. 14. 25.<BR>--2 Great, large,<BR>important; प्राज्यविक्रमाः Ku. 2. 18;<BR>अपि प्राज्यं राज्यं तृणामिव परित्यज्य सहसा<BR>G. L. 5.<BR>--3 Lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांजल|प्राञ्जल|प्राञ्जलः
प्रांजल a.<BR>1 Straightforward,<BR>candid, honest, sincere.<BR>--2 Straight,<BR>erect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांजलि|प्राञ्जलि
प्रांजलि a. [प्रसृतौ अंजली येन]<BR>Folding the hands in supplication, as a<BR>mark of respect or humility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांजलिक|प्राञ्जलिक
प्रांजलिक, प्रांजलिन् See प्रांजलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांजलिन्|प्राञ्जलिन्
प्रांजलिक, प्रांजलिन् See प्रांजलि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण्
प्राण् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To breathe, respire,<BR>inhale air.<BR>--2 To live, be alive; यदहं<BR>पुनरेव प्राणिमि K. 35; प्राणिमस्तव मानार्थं<BR>Bk. 4. 38.<BR>--3 Ved. To blow (as the<BR>wind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राण्
प्राण् m. = प्राण below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणः|प्राण
प्राणः<BR>1 Breath, respiration.<BR>--2 The<BR>breath of life, vitality, life, vital air,<BR>principle of life (usually pl. in this<BR>sense, the Prāṇas being five; प्राण,<BR>अपान, समान, व्यान and उदान);<BR>प्राणैरुपक्रोशमलमिसैर्वा R. 2. 53; 12. 54; (हदि<BR>प्राणो गुदेऽपानः समानो नाभिसंस्थितः । उदानः<BR>कंठदेशस्थो व्यानः सर्वशरीरगः ॥).<BR>--3 The<BR>first of the five life-winds or vital<BR>airs (which has its seat in the<BR>lungs); Bg. 4. 29.<BR>--4 Wind, air<BR>inhaled.<BR>--5 Energy, vigour, strength,<BR>power; as in प्राणसार q. v.<BR>--6 The<BR>spirit or soul (opp. शरीर).<BR>--7 The<BR>Supreme Spirit.<BR>--8 An organ of<BR>sense; Ms. 4. 143.<BR>--9 Any person<BR>or thing as dear and necessary as<BR>life, a beloved person or object;<BR>कोशः कोशवतः प्राणाः प्राणाः प्राणा न<BR>भूपतेः H. 2. 92; अर्थपतेर्विमर्दको<BR>बहिश्चराः प्राणाः Dk.<BR>--10 The life or essence<BR>of poetry, poetical talent or genius;<BR>inspiration.<BR>--11 Aspiration; as in<BR>महाप्राण or अल्पप्राण q. v.<BR>--12<BR>Digestion.<BR>--13 A breath as a measure of<BR>time.<BR>--14 Gum-myrrh.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिपातः killing a living being, taking<BR>away life.<BR>--अत्ययः loss of life.<BR>--अधिक a. {1} dearer than life. {2} superior<BR>in strength or vigour.<BR>--अधिनाथः a<BR>husband.<BR>--अधिपः the soul.<BR>--अंतः<BR>death.<BR>--अंतिक a. {1} fatal, mortal.<BR>{2} lasting to the end of life, ending<BR>with life. {3} dangerous. {4} capital<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-a" target="_blank">Page0772-a+ 57</a>]<BR>(as a sentence).<BR>--(कं) murder.<BR>--अपहारिन् a. fatal, destructive to<BR>life.<BR>--अपानं --नौ air inhaled and<BR>exhaled.<BR>--अयनं an organ of sense.<BR>--आघातः destruction of life, killing<BR>a living being; Bh. 3. 63.<BR>--आचार्यः a<BR>physician to a king.<BR>--आत्मन् m. the<BR>vital or animal soul.<BR>--आद a. fatal,<BR>mortal, causing death.<BR>--आबाधः injury<BR>to life.<BR>--आयामः restraining or<BR>suspending the breath during the<BR>mental recitation of the names or<BR>attributes of a deity.<BR>--आहुतिः f. an<BR>oblation to the five Prāṇas.<BR>--ईशः,<BR>--ईश्वरः {1} a lover, husband;<BR>Amaru. 67; Bv. 2. 57. {2} wind.<BR>--ईशा,<BR>--ईश्वरी a wife, beloved, mistress.<BR>--उत्क्रमणं, --उत्सर्गः departure of the soul,<BR>death.<BR>--उपहारः food.<BR>--कर a.<BR>refreshing or reviving the spirits.<BR>--कृच्छ्रं, --बाधा peril of life, a danger to<BR>life.<BR>--ग्रहः the nose.<BR>--घातक a.<BR>destructive to life.<BR>--घ्न a. fatal,<BR>lifedestroying.<BR>--छिद् a. {1} murderous.<BR>{2} destructive.<BR>--छेदः murder.<BR>--त्यागः {1} suicide; वरं प्राणत्यागो<BR>न च पिशुनवाक्येष्वभिरुचिः H. 1. {2}<BR>death.<BR>--द a. life-giving.<BR>--(दं) {1}<BR>water. {2} blood.<BR>--(दः) Viṣṇu.<BR>--दक्षिणा gift of life; प्राणदक्षिणां दा ‘to<BR>grant one his life’.<BR>--दंडः capital<BR>punishment.<BR>--दयितः a husband.<BR>--दातृ<BR>a. ‘life-giver’, saviour, deliverer.<BR>--दानं {1} resigning life. {2} the gift of<BR>life, saving one's life.<BR>--दुरोदरं, --द्यूतं<BR>fighting for life.<BR>--द्रोहः an attempt<BR>upon any body's life.<BR>--धार a.<BR>living, animate.<BR>--(रः) a living being.<BR>--धारणं {1} maintenance or<BR>support of life. {2} vitality. {3}<BR>a means of supporting life.<BR>--नाथः {1} a lover, husband. {2} an<BR>epithet of Yama.<BR>--निग्रहः restraint<BR>of breath, checking the breath.<BR>--पतिः {1} a lover, husband. {2}<BR>the soul.<BR>--पत्नी the voice.<BR>--परिक्रयः<BR>staking one's life.<BR>--परिग्रहः<BR>possession of life, life, existence.<BR>--प्रद,<BR>--दायक, --दायिन् a. restoring or saving<BR>life.<BR>--प्रयाणं departure of life, death.<BR>--प्रियः ‘as dear as life’, a lover,<BR>husband.<BR>--भक्ष a. feeding on air<BR>only.<BR>--भास्वत् m. the ocean.<BR>--भृत्<BR>a. possessed of life, living, animate,<BR>sentient. (--m.) a living being;<BR>अंतर्गतं प्राणभृतां हि वेद R. 2. 43. {2} N.<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--मोक्षणं {1} departure of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">Page0772-b+ 56</a>]<BR>life, death. {2} suicide.<BR>--यमः =<BR>प्राणायाम q. v.<BR>--यात्रा {1} support of life;<BR>maintenance, livelihood;<BR>पिंडपातमात्रप्राणयात्रां भगवतीं Māl. 1. {2} the<BR>act of breathing.<BR>--योनिः {1} the<BR>Supreme being. {2} wind. (--f.) the<BR>source of life.<BR>--रंध्रं {1} the mouth.<BR>{2} a nostril.<BR>--रोधः {1} suppressing<BR>the breath. {2} danger to life.<BR>--विनाशः, --विप्लवः loss of life, death.<BR>--वियोगः separation of the soul from the<BR>body, death.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. a vital<BR>function.<BR>--व्ययः cost or sacrifice of life.<BR>--शरीरः the Supreme being.<BR>--संयमः<BR>suspension of breath.<BR>--संशयः,<BR>--संकटं, --संदेहः risk or danger to<BR>life, peril of life, a very great<BR>peril.<BR>--संहिता a manner of reciting<BR>the Vedic text.<BR>--सद्मन् n. the body.<BR>--सम a. as dear as life<BR>--(मः) a<BR>husband, lover.<BR>--(मा) a wife.<BR>--सार<BR>a. ‘having life as the essence’,<BR>full of strength and vigour,<BR>muscular; गिरिचर इव नागः प्राणसारं (गात्रं)<BR>बिभर्ति Ś. 2. 4.<BR>--हर --हारिन् a. {1}<BR>causing death, taking away life,<BR>fatal; पुरो मम प्राणहरो भविष्यसि<BR>Gīt. 7. {2} capital.<BR>--हारक a. fatal.<BR>--(कं)<BR>a kind of deadly poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0771-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणकः|प्राणक
प्राणकः<BR>1 A living being, an<BR>animate or sentient being.<BR>--2 Myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणथ|प्राणथः
प्राणथ a. Strong, powerful.<BR>--थः<BR>1 Breathing.<BR>--2 Air, wind.<BR>--3 A<BR>sacred bathing place.<BR>--4 The lord<BR>of created beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणनः|प्राणन|प्राणनं
प्राणनः<BR>1 The throat.<BR>--2 Water<BR>--नं<BR>1 Respiration, breathing.<BR>--2<BR>Life, living.<BR>--3 Producing life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणंतः|प्राणन्त|प्राणंत|प्राणन्तः
प्राणंतः Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणंती
प्राणंती<BR>1 Hunger.<BR>--2 Sobbing.<BR>--3<BR>Hic-cough (हिक्का).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणमय
प्राणमय a. Living, breathing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कोशः the vesture of the<BR>vital airs; see कोश.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणवत्|प्राणवन्त्
प्राणवत् a.<BR>1 Furnished with or<BR>having breath, living, animated;<BR>यया प्राणिनः प्राणवंतः Ś. 1. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणित
प्राणित a. Kept alive, animated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणिन्
प्राणिन् a. Breathing, living, alive.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A living or sentient<BR>being, a living creature; यया<BR>प्राणिनः प्राणवंतः Ś. 1. 1; Me. 5.<BR>--2 A<BR>man.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं a limb of an<BR>animal.<BR>--जातं a whole class of<BR>animals.<BR>--द्यूतं gambling with fighting<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">Page0772-c+ 56</a>]<BR>animals, (cock-fighting,<BR>ram-fighting^1 &c.).<BR>--पीडा cruelty to animals.<BR>--हिंसा injury to life, doing harm<BR>to living creatures.<BR>--हिता a shoe,<BR>boot.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणाय्य
प्राणाय्य a. (य्यी f.) Proper, fit,<BR>suited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राणीत्यं|प्राणीत्य
प्राणीत्यं Debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातर्
प्रातर् ind.<BR>1 At day-break, at<BR>dawn, early, in the morning.<BR>--2<BR>Early on the morrow, the next or<BR>tomorrow morning^1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अह्नः<BR>the early part of the day, forenoon.<BR>--आशः morning meal, breakfast;<BR>अन्यथा प्रातराशाय कुर्याम त्वामलं वयं<BR>Bk. 8. 98.<BR>--आशिन् m. one who<BR>has breakfasted or taken his<BR>morning meal.<BR>--कर्मन् n.<BR>--कार्यं, --कृत्यं<BR>(प्रातःकर्म &c.) a morning<BR>ceremony; a morning duty or rite<BR>(worship, prayer &c.).<BR>--कालः<BR>(प्रातःकालः) morning time.<BR>--गेयः<BR>a bard whose duty it is to wake<BR>the king or any great personage in<BR>the morning with appropriate songs.<BR>--त्रिवर्गा (प्रातस्त्रिवर्गा) the river<BR>Ganges.<BR>--दिनं forenoon.<BR>--दोहः<BR>morning milk.<BR>--प्रहरः (प्रातःप्रहरः) the first<BR>watch of the day.<BR>--भोक्तृ m. a crow.<BR>--भोजनं morning meal, breakfast.<BR>--संध्या (प्रातःसंध्या) {1} the morning<BR>twilight. {2} the morning devotions<BR>or Saṃdhyā adoration of a<BR>Brāhmaṇa<BR>--समयः (प्रातःसमयः)<BR>morningtime, day-break.<BR>--सवः, --सवनं (<BR>प्रातःसवः &c.) the morning libation of<BR>Soma.<BR>--स्नानं (प्रातःस्नानं) morning<BR>ablution<BR>--होमः morning sacrifice.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20171110.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातस्तन
प्रातस्तन a. (नी f.) Relating to<BR>the morning, matutinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातस्तरां
प्रातस्तरां ind. Very early in the<BR>morning; प्रातस्तरां पतत्रिभ्यः प्रबुद्धः<BR>प्रणमन् रविं Bk. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातस्त्य
प्रातस्त्य a. Matutinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिः|प्राति
प्रातिः f.<BR>1 The span of the<BR>thumb and the forefinger.<BR>--2<BR>Filling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिका
प्रातिका The China rose (जवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकूलिक
प्रातिकूलिक a. (की f.)<BR>Opposed, opposing, contrary; आः<BR>प्रातिकूलिकः संवृत्तः Mv. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिकूल्यं|प्रातिकूल्य
प्रातिकूल्यं Adverseness, opposition,<BR>hostility, unfavourableness,<BR>unfriendliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिजनीन
प्रातिजनीन (नी f.) Suitable<BR>against an adversary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0772-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिज्ञं|प्रातिज्ञ
प्रातिज्ञं The subject under<BR>discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिदैवसिक
प्रातिदैवसिक a. (की f.)<BR>Occurring daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपक्ष
प्रातिपक्ष a. (क्षी f.)<BR>1 Contrary,<BR>adverse.<BR>--2 Hostile, inimical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपक्ष्यं|प्रातिपक्ष्य
प्रातिपक्ष्यं Enmity, hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपद
प्रातिपद a. (दी f.)<BR>1 Forming<BR>the commencement.<BR>--2 Produced<BR>in, or belonging to, the day called<BR>प्रतिपद् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपदिक|प्रातिपदिकः
प्रातिपदिक a. Express, explicit.<BR>--कः Fire.<BR>--कं The crude form<BR>of a substantive, a noun in<BR>its uninflected state (before<BR>receiving the case-terminations);<BR>अर्थवदधातुरप्रत्ययः प्रातिपदिकं P. I. 2. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिपौरुषिक
प्रातिपौरुषिक a. (की f.)<BR>Relating to manliness or valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभ
प्रातिभ a. (भी f.)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>divination or genius.<BR>--2<BR>Intellectual, mental.<BR>--भं Genius or vivid<BR>imagination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभाव्यं|प्रातिभाव्य
प्रातिभाव्यं Becoming bail or<BR>security, suretiship, becoming<BR>answerable for the appearance of a<BR>debtor, for his being trustworthy,<BR>and for paying his debt;<BR>श्रेणीप्रातिभाव्येनातिष्ठत् Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिभासिक
प्रातिभासिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Existing only in appearance, not real.<BR>--2 Looking like.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिलोमिक
प्रातिलोमिक a. (की f.) Against<BR>the grain, adverse, hostile,<BR>disagreeable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिलोम्यं|प्रातिलोम्य
प्रातिलोम्यं<BR>1 Inversion, inverted or<BR>reverse order; Ms. 10. 13.<BR>--2<BR>Hostility, opposition, hostile feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेशिकः|प्रातिवेशिक
प्रातिवेशिकः, प्रातिवेश्मकः, प्रातिवेश्यकः<BR>A neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेश्मकः|प्रातिवेश्मक
प्रातिवेशिकः, प्रातिवेश्मकः, प्रातिवेश्यकः<BR>A neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेश्यकः|प्रातिवेश्यक
प्रातिवेशिकः, प्रातिवेश्मकः, प्रातिवेश्यकः<BR>A neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिवेश्यः|प्रातिवेश्य
प्रातिवेश्यः<BR>1 A neighbour (in<BR>general).<BR>--2 A next-door<BR>neighbour (निरंतरगृहवासी Kull.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिशाख्यं|प्रातिशाख्य
प्रातिशाख्यं A grammatical<BR>treatise laying down rules for the<BR>phonetic changes which words in<BR>any Śākhā of the Vedas undergo,<BR>and teaching the mode of<BR>pronouncing the accents &c. (There exist four<BR>Prātiśākhyas, one for the Śākala<BR>branch of Ṛgveda, one for each of<BR>the two branches of the Yajurveda,<BR>and one for the Atharvaveda).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिस्विक|प्रातिस्विकं
प्रातिस्विक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Peculiar,<BR>not common to others, one's own.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">Page0773-b+ 54</a>]<BR>--2 Granting to every one what is<BR>his due.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहंत्रं|प्रातिहन्त्र|प्रातिहंत्र
प्रातिहंत्रं Vengeance, revenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहारः|प्रातिहार
प्रातिहारः, प्रतिहारकः, प्रातिहारिकः<BR>A juggler, conjurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिहारकः|प्रतिहारक
प्रातिहारः, प्रतिहारकः, प्रातिहारिकः<BR>A juggler, conjurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहारिकः|प्रातिहारिक
प्रातिहारः, प्रतिहारकः, प्रातिहारिकः<BR>A juggler, conjurer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातिहार्यं|प्रातिहार्य
प्रातिहार्यं<BR>1 Juggling, conjuring,<BR>legerdemain.<BR>--2 Working miracles.<BR>--3 A miracle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीतिक
प्रातीतिक a. (की f.) Mental,<BR>existing in the mind or<BR>imagination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीपः|प्रातीप
प्रातीपः A patronymic of<BR>Śantanu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रातीपिक
प्रातीपिक a. (की f.) Roverse,<BR>contrary, retrograde.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्यंतिकः|प्रात्यन्तिक|प्रात्यंतिक|प्रात्यन्तिकः
प्रात्यंतिकः A prince of the<BR>Pratyantas, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्ययिक
प्रात्ययिक a. (क्री f.)<BR>1<BR>Confidential, trusty.<BR>--2 Standing bail for<BR>the trustworthiness of a debtor (as<BR>a प्रतिभू or surety).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रात्यहिक
प्रात्यहिक a. (की f.) Occurring<BR>every day, daily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमकल्पिकः|प्राथमकल्पिक
प्राथमकल्पिकः^1<BR>1 A student who<BR>has just entered on the study of the<BR>Vedas (शैक्ष).<BR>--2 A Yogin just<BR>commencing his course.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथमिक|प्राथमिकः
प्राथमिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Primary,<BR>first, initial.<BR>--2 Former, previous.<BR>--3 Happening for the first time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राथम्यं|प्राथम्य
प्राथम्यं Being first, precedence,<BR>priority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादक्षिण्यं|प्रादक्षिण्य
प्रादक्षिण्यं Going round a person<BR>or object from left to right keeping<BR>the right side towards the object<BR>circumambulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुस्
प्रादुस् ind. Visibly, evidently,<BR>manifestly, in sight (used chiefly<BR>with भू, कृ and अस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुरस्
प्रादुरस् {c2c} P. To appear, spring up;<BR>प्रादुरासीत्तमोनुदः Ms. 1. 6; R. 11. 15;<BR>प्रादुःष्यात्क इव जित पुरः परेण Śi. 8. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुर्भू
प्रादुर्भू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To become manifest<BR>or visible, show oneself, appear.<BR>--2<BR>To arise, come to light.<BR>--3 To<BR>become audible, be heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुर्भावः|प्रादुर्भाव
प्रादुर्भावः<BR>1 Coming into existence,<BR>arising; वपुःप्रादुर्भावात् K. P. 10.<BR>--2<BR>Becoming visible, evident or<BR>manifest, manifestation, appearance.<BR>--3<BR>Becoming audible.<BR>--4 The<BR>appearance of a deity on earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुर्भूत
प्रादुर्भूत a. Appeared, become<BR>visible or manifest, manifested,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">Page0773-c+ 55</a>]<BR>displayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुष्करणं|प्रादुष्करण
प्रादुष्करणं Manirestation, making<BR>visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादुष्यं|प्रादुष्य
प्रादुष्यं Manifestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशः|प्रादेश
प्रादेशः<BR>1 The span of the thumb<BR>and forefinger.<BR>--2 A spot, place,<BR>region.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशनं|प्रादेशन
प्रादेशनं A gift, donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशिक|प्रादेशिकः
प्रादेशिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Having<BR>precedents, precedented.<BR>--2 Limited,<BR>local.<BR>--3 Significant.<BR>--कः The<BR>owner of a district.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशिन्
प्रादेशिन् a. A span long.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादेशिनी
प्रादेशिनी The forefinger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रादोष|प्रादोषः
प्रादोष a. (षी f.), प्रादोषिक a.<BR>(की f.), Relating to the evening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधनिकं|प्राधनिक
प्राधनिकं A destructive weapon,<BR>any war implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधानिक
प्राधानिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Most<BR>eminent or excellent, pre-eminent,<BR>supreme, most distinguished.<BR>--2<BR>Relating to or derived from<BR>Pradhāna, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधान्यं|प्राधान्य
प्राधान्यं<BR>1 Pre-eminence,<BR>superiority, predominance, prominence.<BR>--2 Ascendancy, supremacy.<BR>--3 A<BR>chief or principal cause. (प्रावान्येन,<BR>प्राधान्यात्, प्राधान्यतः ‘chiefly’,<BR>‘especially’, ‘principally’; Bg. 10. 19).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राधीत
प्राधीत a. Well-read, highly<BR>educated (as a Brāhmaṇa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्ययनं|प्राध्ययन
प्राध्ययनं Reading, studying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राध्व|प्राध्वं|प्राध्वः
प्राध्व a. [प्रकृष्टोऽध्वा अच् समासः]<BR>1 Distant, remote, long.<BR>--2 Bent,<BR>inclined.<BR>--3 Fastened, bound (बद्ध).<BR>--4 Favourable.<BR>--ध्वः A carriage.<BR>--ध्वं ind.<BR>1 Favourably, agreeably<BR>or conformably, suitably; सभाजने<BR>मे भुजमूर्ध्वबाहुः सव्येतरं प्राध्वमितः प्रयुंक्ते<BR>R. 13. 43.<BR>--2 Crookedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांतः|प्रान्त|प्रांत|प्रान्तः
प्रांतः [प्रकृष्टोंऽतः]<BR>1 Edge,<BR>margin, border, skirt, verge;<BR>प्रांतसंस्तीर्णदर्भाः Ś. 4. 7.<BR>--2 Corner (as of the<BR>lips, eyes &c.); Māl. 4. 2; ओष्ठ˚,<BR>नयन˚.<BR>--3 Boundary, extremity.<BR>--4<BR>Extreme verge, end; यौवनप्रांत<BR>Pt. 4.<BR>--5 A point, tip.<BR>--6 The back<BR>part.<BR>--Comp. A<BR>--ग a. living close<BR>by.<BR>--दुर्गं a suburb outside the<BR>walls of a town, a town near a fort.<BR>--विरस a. tasteless in the end.<BR>--शून्य a. see प्रांतरशून्य.<BR>--स्थ a. one<BR>who inhabits the borders.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांततः
प्रांततः ind. Marginally, along the<BR>border or edge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0773-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रांतरं|प्रान्तर|प्रांतर|प्रान्तरं
प्रांतरं [प्रकृष्टमंतंर यत्र]<BR>1 A long,<BR>lonesome or solitary path, desolate<BR>road.<BR>--2 A road without shade,<BR>dreary tract of land.<BR>--3 A forest,<BR>wilderness.<BR>--4 The hollow of a<BR>tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शून्यः a long<BR>dreary road (without trees, shade<BR>&c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्
प्राप् {c5c} P.<BR>1 To get, obtain, gain,<BR>acquire; R. 17. 1.<BR>--2 To attain to,<BR>go to, reach; यथा महाहदं प्राप्य क्षिप्तं<BR>लोष्टं विनश्यति Ms. 11. 264;<BR>R. 1. 48; Bk. 15. 106; so आश्रमं, नदीं,<BR>वनं &c.; प्राप्यावंतीन् Me. 30.<BR>--3 To<BR>stretch, extend.<BR>--4 To meet with,<BR>find, light upon, overtake;<BR>Bk. 5. 96.<BR>--5 To result or follow (as a<BR>conclusion); परिच्छिन्नस्तावज्जीव इति<BR>प्राप्नोति Ś. B.<BR>--6 To incur, bring<BR>upon oneself (दोष, दंड &c.).<BR>--7<BR>To suffer, endure.<BR>--8 To be changed<BR>into (in gram.).<BR>--9 To be<BR>present, be at hand (Ved.). --Caus.<BR>1 To lead or bring to, take to,<BR>convey; सपत्नीः प्रापयंत्याब्ध सिंधवो<BR>नगनिम्नगाः Śi. 2. 104; वसतिं प्रिय<BR>कामिनां प्रियास्त्वदृते प्रापायितुं क ईश्वरः<BR>Ku. 4. 11, 32; Ve. 3. 7, R. 14. 45, 60.<BR>--2 To cause to obtain, give,<BR>provide; अभिमन्युतनयमसून्प्रापितवान्<BR>K. 175 ‘restored to life, revived’.<BR>--3<BR>To promote or advance, appoint<BR>to (an office).<BR>--4 To tell,<BR>communicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप
प्राप a. Arriving at, reaching,<BR>obtaining &c., as in दुष्प्राप.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापक|प्रापकः
प्रापक (पिका f.) [प्राप्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1<BR>Leading to, conveying.<BR>--2 Procuring,<BR>providing with.<BR>--3<BR>Establishing, making valid.<BR>--4 Obtaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापणं|प्रापण
प्रापणं<BR>1 Reaching, extending to.<BR>--2 Obtaining, acquisition,<BR>attainment.<BR>--3 Bringing to, conveying,<BR>leading to.<BR>--4 Procuring.<BR>--5<BR>Reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापित
प्रापित p. p.<BR>1 Conveyed,<BR>conducted.<BR>--2 Led to, promoted or<BR>advanced to.<BR>--3 Caused to obtain.<BR>--4<BR>Procured, got.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्त|प्राप्तः
प्राप्त p. p.<BR>1 Got, obtained, won,<BR>acquired.<BR>--2 Reached, attained to.<BR>--3 Met with, found.<BR>--4 Incurred,<BR>suffered, endured.<BR>--5 Arrived, come,<BR>present.<BR>--6 Completed.<BR>--7 Proper,<BR>right.<BR>--8 Following from a rule.<BR>--9<BR>Described (as a symptom).<BR>--10<BR>Fixed, placed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुज्ञ a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-b" target="_blank">Page0774-b+ 57</a>]<BR>one who has got permission to go,<BR>allowed to depart.<BR>--अपराध a. guilty<BR>of an offence.<BR>--अर्थ a. successful.<BR>--(र्थः) an object gained.<BR>--अवसर<BR>a. {1} finding occasion or<BR>opportunity. {2} timely, seasonable.<BR>--(रः) a<BR>fit or suitable time.<BR>--उदय a. one<BR>who has attained rise or exaltation.<BR>--कारिन् a. doing what is right.<BR>--काल<BR>a. {1} opportune, seasonable;<BR>suitable, see अप्राप्तकाल. {2} marriageable.<BR>{3} fated, destined.<BR>--(लः) a fit time,<BR>suitable or favourable moment.<BR>--(लं)<BR>ind. seasonably, opportunely,<BR>timely; Pt. 1. 63.<BR>--जीवन a. revived,<BR>restored to life.<BR>--दोष a. guilty.<BR>--पंचत्व a. resolved into the five<BR>elements, i. e. dead; cf. पंचत्व.<BR>--प्रसव<BR>a. {1} delivered of a child. {2} near<BR>her confinement; U. 7. 2.<BR>--बुद्धि<BR>a. {1} recovering, regaining one's<BR>consciousness. {2} instructed,<BR>enlightened.<BR>--भारः a beast of burden.<BR>--मनोरथ a. one who has obtained<BR>his desired object.<BR>--यौवन a. being<BR>in the bloom of youth, arrived at<BR>the age of puberty, youthful.<BR>--रूप<BR>a. {1} handsome, beautiful. {2} wise,<BR>learned. {3} charming, attractive. {4}<BR>fit, proper, worthy.<BR>--व्यवहार a. come<BR>of age, being able and legally<BR>authorised to manage his own affairs<BR>(opp. ‘minor’).<BR>--श्री a. one who<BR>owes his rise (to another);<BR>Ku. 2. 55; Pt. 1. 245.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तिः|प्राप्ति
प्राप्तिः f.<BR>1 Obtaining, acquisition<BR>gain, attainment, profit; द्रव्य˚,<BR>यशः˚, सुख˚ &c.<BR>--2 Reaching or<BR>attaining to.<BR>--3 Arrival, coming to.<BR>--4 Finding, meeting with.<BR>--5 Range,<BR>reach.<BR>--6 A guess, conjecture.<BR>--7<BR>Lot, share, portion.<BR>--8 Fortune, luck.<BR>--9 Rise, production.<BR>--10 The power<BR>of obtaining anything (one of the<BR>eight Siddhis q. v.).<BR>--11 Union,<BR>collection (संहति).<BR>--12 The result of<BR>actions done in a former life.<BR>--13<BR>Fate, destiny; Pt. 2. 123.<BR>--14 Being<BR>valid, holding good, application (as<BR>of a rule).<BR>--15 The successful<BR>termination of a plot (सुखागम).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशा the hope of obtaining<BR>anything (regarded as part of the<BR>development of the plot of a play);<BR>उपायापायशंकाभ्यां प्राप्त्याशा प्राप्तिसंभवा<BR>S. D. 6.<BR>--समं a particular Jāti in<BR>Nyāya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्य|प्राप्यं
प्राप्य, प्राप्तव्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be got or<BR>obtained.<BR>--2 Attainable, procurable;<BR>destined to be got; प्राप्तत्वमर्थं लभते<BR>म्नुष्यः Pt. 2. 105.<BR>--3 To be reached,<BR>attainable.<BR>--4 To be met with or<BR>found.<BR>--5 Proper, fit, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राप्तव्य|प्राप्तव्यं
प्राप्य, प्राप्तव्य pot. p.<BR>1 To be got or<BR>obtained.<BR>--2 Attainable, procurable;<BR>destined to be got; प्राप्तत्वमर्थं लभते<BR>म्नुष्यः Pt. 2. 105.<BR>--3 To be reached,<BR>attainable.<BR>--4 To be met with or<BR>found.<BR>--5 Proper, fit, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रापणिकः|प्रापणिक
प्रापणिकः A merchant, trader;<BR>आढ्यादिव प्रापणिकादजस्रं Śi. 4. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबल्यं|प्राबल्य
प्राबल्यं<BR>1 Ascendancy,<BR>superiority, predominance.<BR>--2 Power, force,<BR>might.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबालिकः|प्राबालिक
प्राबा(वा)लिकः A dealer in<BR>coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावालिकः|प्रावालिक
प्राबा(वा)लिकः A dealer in<BR>coral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबोधकः|प्राबोधक
प्राबोध(धि)कः<BR>1 Dawn,<BR>daybreak.<BR>--2 A minstrel whose duty it<BR>is to wake the king in the morning<BR>by singing appropriate songs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राबाधिकः
प्राबोध(धि)कः<BR>1 Dawn,<BR>daybreak.<BR>--2 A minstrel whose duty it<BR>is to wake the king in the morning<BR>by singing appropriate songs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभंजनं|प्राभञ्जन|प्राभंजन
प्राभंजनं The lunar mansion Svāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभंजनिः|प्राभञ्जनि|प्राभंजनि|प्राभञ्जनिः
प्राभंजनिः<BR>1 An epithet of<BR>Hanumat.<BR>--2 Of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभवं|प्राभव
प्राभवं Superiority, supremacy,<BR>predominance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभवत्यं|प्राभवत्य
प्राभवत्यं Supremacy, authority,<BR>power; Ms. 8. 412.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभाकरः|प्राभाकर
प्राभाकरः ‘A follower of<BR>Prabhākara’, a follower of that school<BR>of Mīmāṃsā philosophy which is<BR>known as प्राभाकर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभातिक
प्राभातिक a. (की f.) Relating<BR>to the morning, matutinal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभृतं|प्राभृत
प्राभृतं, प्राभृतकं<BR>1 A present, gift.<BR>--2 An offering to a deity or to a<BR>king (Nazerāṇā).<BR>--3 A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राभृतकं|प्राभृतक
प्राभृतं, प्राभृतकं<BR>1 A present, gift.<BR>--2 An offering to a deity or to a<BR>king (Nazerāṇā).<BR>--3 A bribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाणिक|प्रामाणिकः
प्रामाणिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Established by proof, founded or resting<BR>on authority.<BR>--2 Founded on the<BR>authority of scriptures (शास्त्रसिद्ध).<BR>--3 Authentic, credible.<BR>--4 Relating<BR>to a प्रमाण q. v.<BR>--कः<BR>1 One who<BR>accepts proof.<BR>--2 One who is<BR>conversant with the Pramāṇas of<BR>the Naiyāyikas, a logician.<BR>--3 The<BR>head of a trade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाण्यं|प्रामाण्य
प्रामाण्यं<BR>1 Being a proof or<BR>resting on authority.<BR>--2 Credibility,<BR>authenticity.<BR>--3 Proof, evidence,<BR>authority.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वादिन् a. one<BR>who affirms or believes in proof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामादिक
प्रामादिक a. (की f.) Due to<BR>carelessness or error, wrong, faulty,<BR>incorrect; इति प्रामादिकः प्रयोगः or<BR>पाठः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामाद्यं|प्रामाद्य|प्रामाद्यः
प्रामाद्यं<BR>1 Error, fault, blunder,<BR>mistake.<BR>--2 Madness, frenzy.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-a" target="_blank">Page0775-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Intoxication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0774-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामीत्यं|प्रामीत्य
प्रामीत्यं<BR>1 Debt.<BR>--2 Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामोदक
प्रामोद(दि)क a. (की f.)<BR>Charming, enchanting, delightful; अहो<BR>प्रामोदिकं रूपं U. 6. 20 v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रामोदिक
प्रामोद(दि)क a. (की f.)<BR>Charming, enchanting, delightful; अहो<BR>प्रामोदिकं रूपं U. 6. 20 v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायः|प्राय
प्रायः [प्र-अय् घञ्, इ-अच् वा]<BR>1<BR>Going away, departure, departure<BR>from life.<BR>--2 Seeking death by<BR>fasting, fasting, sitting down and<BR>abstaining from food with some object<BR>in view (generally with words like<BR>आस्, उपविश् &c.); see प्रायोपवेशन<BR>below.<BR>--3 The largest portion,<BR>majority, plurality; majority of cases.<BR>--4 Excess, abundance, plenty.<BR>--5<BR>A condition of life. N. B. At the<BR>end of comp. प्राय may be translated<BR>by (a) for the most part, generally,<BR>mostly, almost, nearly; पतनप्रायौ<BR>‘about to fall;’ मृतप्रायः ‘almost dead,<BR>a little less than dead, nearly dead’;<BR>or (b) abounding or rich in, full<BR>of, excessive, abundant; कष्टप्रायं<BR>शरीरं U. 1; शालिप्रायो देशः Pt. 3;<BR>कमलामोदप्राया वनानिलाः U. 3. 24 ‘full<BR>of the fragrance’ &c., or (c) like,<BR>resembling; वर्षशतप्रायं दिनं,<BR>अमृतप्रायं वचनं &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपगमनं,<BR>--उपवेशः, --उपवेशनं, --उपवेशनिका sitting<BR>down and abstaining from food and<BR>thus preparing oneself for death,<BR>fasting oneself to death; मया<BR>प्रायोपवेशनं कृतं विद्धि Pt. 4;<BR>प्रायोपवेशनमतिर्नृपतिर्बभूव R. 8. 94;<BR>प्रायोपवेशसदृशं व्रतमास्थितस्य Ve. 3. 10.<BR>--उपेत<BR>a. abstaining from food and thus<BR>awaiting the approach of death.<BR>--उपविष्ट, --उपवेशिन् a. fasting oneself<BR>to death, who sits without food at<BR>the door of another to exact<BR>compliance with his demands.<BR>--दर्शनं<BR>an ordinary phenomenon.<BR>--भव a.<BR>common, usually met with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायणं|प्रायण
प्रायणं<BR>1 Entrance, beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--2 The path of life.<BR>--3 Voluntary death; Ms. 9. 323.<BR>--4 Taking refuge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायणीय|प्रायणीयः
प्रायणीय a. Introductory, initial,<BR>initiatory.<BR>--यं The first.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>An introductory libation at a Soma<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--2 The first day of a Soma<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायशस्
प्रायशस् ind. Generally, mostly,<BR>for the most part, in all probability;<BR>आशाबंधः कुसुमसदृशं प्रायशो ह्यंगनानां<BR>सद्यःपाति प्रणयि हृदयं विप्रयोगे रुणद्धि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">Page0775-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Me. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्तं|प्रायश्चित्त
प्रायश्चित्तं, प्रायश्चित्तिः f.<BR>1<BR>Atonement, expiation, indemnification,<BR>a religious act to atone for sin;<BR>मातुः पापस्य भरतः प्रायश्चितमिवाकरोत्<BR>R. 12. 19. (प्रायो नाम तपः प्रोक्तं चित्तं निश्चय<BR>उच्यते । तपोनिश्चयसंयोगात् प्रायश्चितमितीर्यते ॥<BR>Hemādri).<BR>--2 Satisfaction, amends<BR>(in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्तिः|प्रायश्चित्ति
प्रायश्चित्तं, प्रायश्चित्तिः f.<BR>1<BR>Atonement, expiation, indemnification,<BR>a religious act to atone for sin;<BR>मातुः पापस्य भरतः प्रायश्चितमिवाकरोत्<BR>R. 12. 19. (प्रायो नाम तपः प्रोक्तं चित्तं निश्चय<BR>उच्यते । तपोनिश्चयसंयोगात् प्रायश्चितमितीर्यते ॥<BR>Hemādri).<BR>--2 Satisfaction, amends<BR>(in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्तिक
प्रायश्चित्तिक a.<BR>1 Expiating,<BR>expiatory.<BR>--2 Expiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चित्तिन्
प्रायश्चित्तिन् a. One who makes an<BR>atonement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायश्चितीय
प्रायश्चितीय a. Expiatory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायस्
प्रायस् ind.<BR>1 Mostly, generally,<BR>as a general rule, for the most part;<BR>प्रायः प्रत्ययमाधत्ते स्वगुणेषूत्तमादरः<BR>Ku. 6. 20; प्रायो भृत्यास्त्यजंति प्रचलितविभवं<BR>स्वामिनं सेवमानाः Mu. 4. 21; or प्रायो<BR>गच्छति यत्र भाग्यरंहितस्तत्रैव यांत्यापदः<BR>Bh. 2. 90.<BR>--2 In all probability,<BR>most likely, probably, perhaps;<BR>तव प्राज्ञाप्रसादाद्धि प्रायः प्राप्स्याभि<BR>जीवितं Mb.<BR>--3 Abundantly, largely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायेण
प्रायेण ind.<BR>1 Mostly, as a general<BR>rule; प्रायेणैते रमणविरहेष्वंगनानां विनोदाः<BR>Me. 87; प्रायेण सत्यपि हितार्थकरे विधौ<BR>हि श्रेयांसि लब्धुमसुखानि विनांतरायैः<BR>Ki. 5. 49; Ku. 3. 28; Rs. 6. 24.<BR>--2<BR>Probably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायाणिक
प्रायाणिक, प्रायात्रिक a. (की f.)<BR>Necessary or suitable for a journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायात्रिक
प्रायाणिक, प्रायात्रिक a. (की f.)<BR>Necessary or suitable for a journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायिक|प्रायिकं
प्रायिक a. (की f.) Usual,<BR>common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायुद्धेषिन्
प्रायुद्धेषिन् m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायत्यं|प्रायत्य
प्रायत्यं Purity, cleanliness, piety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रायोगिक
प्रायोगिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Applied.<BR>--2 Applicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारभ्
प्रारभ् {c1c} A. To begin, commence;<BR>प्रारभ्यते न खलु विघ्नभेयन नीचैः<BR>Bh. 2. 27; see आरभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारब्ध|प्रारब्धं
प्रारब्ध p. p. Begun, commenced.<BR>--ब्धं<BR>1 What is begun, an<BR>undertaking.<BR>--2 Fate, destiny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारब्धिः|प्रारब्धि
प्रारब्धिः f.<BR>1 Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--2 A post to which an<BR>elephant is fastened; or a rope for<BR>fastening him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारंभः|प्रारम्भ|प्रारंभ|प्रारम्भः
प्रारंभः<BR>1 Beginning,<BR>commencement; प्रारंभेपि त्रियामा तरुणयति निजं<BR>नीलिमानं वनेषु Māl. 5. 6; R. 10. 9;<BR>18. 49.<BR>--2 An undertaking, deed,<BR>enterprize; फलानुमेयाः प्रारंभाः संस्काराः<BR>प्राक्तना इव R. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारंभणं|प्रारम्भण|प्रारंभण
प्रारंभणं Commencing, beginning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रारोहः|प्रारोह
प्रारोहः A shoot, sprout, new<BR>leaf; see प्ररोह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्णं|प्रार्ण
प्रार्णं A chief debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थ्
प्रार्थ् {c10c} A.<BR>1 To ask or pray<BR>for, beg, request; तेन भवंतं प्रार्थयंते<BR>Ś. 2.<BR>--2 To demand in marriage.<BR>--3 To wish or long for, desire,<BR>want; अहो विघ्नवत्यः प्रार्थितार्थसिद्धयः<BR>Ś. 3; स्वर्गतिं प्रार्थयंते Bg. 9. 20;<BR>Bk. 7. 48; R. 7. 53, 67;<BR>Ku. 5. 45.<BR>--4 To look for, search, be in<BR>search of; प्रार्थयध्वं तथा सीतां<BR>Bk. 7. 48.<BR>--5 To attack, seize or fall<BR>upon; असौ अश्वानीकेन यवनानां<BR>प्रार्थितः M. 5; दुर्जयो लवणः शूली विशूलः<BR>प्रार्थ्यतामिति R. 15. 5; 9. 56.<BR>--6<BR>To petition, file a suit against.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थक|प्रार्थकः
प्रार्थक a. (र्थिका f.) Asking,<BR>begging, requesting, soliciting,<BR>entreating, desiring, wishing &c.<BR>--कः<BR>A suitor, petitioner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थनं|प्रार्थन
प्रार्थनं --ना<BR>1 A request, entreaty,<BR>prayer, solicitation; ये वर्धते<BR>धनपतिपुरःप्रार्थनादुःखभाजः Bh. 3. 47.<BR>--2 A<BR>wish, desire; लब्धावकाशा मे प्रार्थना<BR>or न दुरवापेयं खलु प्रार्थन Ś. 1; 2. 1;<BR>उत्सर्पिणी खलु महतां प्रार्थना Ś. 7; 7.<BR>{2}<BR>--3 A suit, petition,<BR>supplication, a love-suit;<BR>कदाचिदस्मत्प्रार्थनामंतःपुरेभ्यः कथयेत् Ś {2} (the object<BR>is expressed by the loc.; as in<BR>शकुंतलायां प्रार्थना).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भंगः<BR>refusal of a request^1.<BR>--सिद्धिः f.<BR>fulfilment of a desire;<BR>प्रार्थनासिद्धिशंसिनः R. 1. 42.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20180518.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थना
प्रार्थनं --ना<BR>1 A request, entreaty,<BR>prayer, solicitation; ये वर्धते<BR>धनपतिपुरःप्रार्थनादुःखभाजः Bh. 3. 47.<BR>--2 A<BR>wish, desire; लब्धावकाशा मे प्रार्थना<BR>or न दुरवापेयं खलु प्रार्थन Ś. 1; 2. 1;<BR>उत्सर्पिणी खलु महतां प्रार्थना Ś. 7; 7.<BR>{2}<BR>--3 A suit, petition,<BR>supplication, a love-suit;<BR>कदाचिदस्मत्प्रार्थनामंतःपुरेभ्यः कथयेत् Ś {2} (the object<BR>is expressed by the loc.; as in<BR>शकुंतलायां प्रार्थना).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भंगः<BR>refusal of a request^1.<BR>--सिद्धिः f.<BR>fulfilment of a desire;<BR>प्रार्थनासिद्धिशंसिनः R. 1. 42.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20180518.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थनीय|प्रार्थनीयं
प्रार्थनीय pot. p.<BR>1 To be prayed<BR>for or solicited.<BR>--2 To be wished<BR>or desired.<BR>--यं The third or<BR>Dvāpara age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थयितृ
प्रार्थयितृ^1 m.<BR>1 One who asks for,<BR>a solicitor, beggar.<BR>--2 A suitor,<BR>woeer, lover (of a lady); लभेत वा<BR>प्रार्थंयिता न वा श्रियं Ś. 3. 14;<BR>Pt. 1. 138; एवं प्रार्थयिता विडंब्यते Ś. 2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थित|प्रार्थितः
प्रार्थित p. p.<BR>1 Begged, requested,<BR>asked for, solicited.<BR>--2 Wished,<BR>desired.<BR>--3 Attacked, opposed by<BR>an enemy; R. 9. 56.<BR>--4 Killed,<BR>hurt.<BR>--5 Required, wanted; sought<BR>for; Ku. 5. 46.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रार्थिन्
प्रार्थिन् a.<BR>1 Begging, requesting.<BR>--2 Wishing, desiring; मंदः<BR>कवियशःप्रार्थी गमिष्यामुपहास्यतां R. 1. 3.<BR>--3<BR>Attacking, assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालंब|प्रालम्ब|प्रालम्बं|प्रालम्बः
प्रालंब a. Pendent, hanging<BR>down; प्रालबद्विगुणितचामरप्रहासः<BR>Ve. 2. 28.<BR>--बः<BR>1 A kind of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">Page0776-a+ 55</a>]<BR>pearl-ornament.<BR>--2 A female breast.<BR>--बं A<BR>garland worn round the neck and<BR>reaching to the breast; प्रालंबमुत्कृष्य<BR>यथावकाशं निनाय साचीकृतचारुक्त्रः<BR>R. 6. 14; मुक्ताप्रालंबेषु K. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0775-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालंबकं|प्रालम्बक|प्रालंबक
प्रालंबकं See प्रालंबं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालंबिका|प्रालम्बिका
प्रालंबिका A kind of golden<BR>necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रालेयं|प्रालेय
प्रालेयं Snow, frost, hoar frost,<BR>dew, ईशाचलप्रालेयप्लवमेच्छया Gīt. 1;<BR>प्रालेयशीतमचलेश्वरमीश्वरोऽपि (अधिशेते)<BR>Śi. 4. 64; Me. 39.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद्रिः,<BR>--शैलः ‘the snowy mountain’, the<BR>Himālaya; Me. 57.<BR>--अंशुः, --करः,<BR>--रश्मिः {1} the moon. {2} camphor.<BR>--लेशः a hail-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावटः|प्रावट
प्रावटः Barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावणं|प्रावण
प्रावणं A spade, hoe, shovel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावास
प्रावास a. (सी f.) Relating to<BR>a journey, to be done or given in a<BR>journey,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावासिक
प्रावासिक a, (की f.) Suitable or<BR>fit for a journey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावीण्यं|प्रावीण्य
प्रावीण्यं Cleverness, skilfulness,<BR>proficiency, dexterity; आविष्कृतं<BR>कथाप्रावीण्यं वत्सेन U. 4; R. 15. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृ
प्रावृ {c5c} U.<BR>1 To put on, dress or<BR>clothe oneself in.<BR>--2 To surround,<BR>encompass, enclose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरः|प्रावर
प्रावरः<BR>1 A fence, an enclosure.<BR>--2 An upper garment (according<BR>to Hemacandra).<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरणं|प्रावरण
प्रावरणं A garment, covering;<BR>especially, an upper garment, cloak,<BR>mantle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावरणीयं|प्रावरणीय
प्रावरणीयं An upper garment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावारः|प्रावार
प्रावारः<BR>1 An upper garment, a<BR>cloak, mantle.<BR>--2 N. of a district.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीटः a kind of white<BR>ant or moth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावारकः|प्रावारक
प्रावारकः An upper garment,<BR>mantle; यदीच्छसि लंबदशाविशालं प्रावारकं<BR>सूत्रशतैर्हि युक्तं Mk. 8. 22;<BR>जातीकुसुमवासितः प्रावारकोऽनुप्रेषितः Mk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावारिकः|प्रावारिक
प्रावारिकः A maker of upper<BR>garments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृत|प्रावृतं|प्रावृतः
प्रावृत p. p. Enclosed, surrounded,<BR>covered, screened.<BR>--तः, तं A veil,<BR>mantle, wrapper (f. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृतिः|प्रावृति
प्रावृतिः f.<BR>1 An enclosure, a hedge,<BR>fence.<BR>--2 Spiritual darkness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृत्तिक|प्रावृत्तिकः
प्रावृत्तिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Secondary.<BR>--2 Well-informed.<BR>--कः A<BR>messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृष्
प्रावृष् f. The rainy season,<BR>monsoon, rains, (the months आषाढ and<BR>श्रावण); कलापिनां प्रावृषि पश्य नृत्यं<BR>R. 6. 51; 19. 37; प्रावृट् प्रावृडिति<BR>ब्रवीति शठधीः क्षारं क्षते प्रक्षिपन् Mk. 5. 18;<BR>Me. 115.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अत्ययः (<BR>प्रावृडत्ययः) end of the rainy season.<BR>--कालः (प्रावृट्कालः) the rainy season.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषः|प्रावृष
प्रावृषः --षा The rainy season,<BR>monsoons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषा
प्रावृषः --षा The rainy season,<BR>monsoons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषिक|प्रावृषिकः
प्रावृषिक, प्रावृषीण a. (की f.)<BR>Produced in the rainy season.<BR>--कः A<BR>peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषीण
प्रावृषिक, प्रावृषीण a. (की f.)<BR>Produced in the rainy season.<BR>--कः A<BR>peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषिज|प्रावृषिजः
प्रावृषिज a. Produced in the rainy<BR>season.<BR>--जः A storm, stormy gale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृषेण्य|प्रावृषेण्यः
प्रावृषेण्य a.<BR>1 Produced in,<BR>relating to, the rainy season; सा किं<BR>शक्या जनयितुमिह प्रावृषेण्येन… वारिदेन<BR>Bv. 1. 30; 4. 6; R. 1. 36.<BR>--2<BR>Abundant, copious, much (lit. coming<BR>in showers).<BR>--3 To be paid in the<BR>rainy season (as a debt &c.).<BR>--ण्यः<BR>1 The Kadamba tree.<BR>--2 The Kuṭaja<BR>tree.<BR>--ण्यं Numerousness,<BR>abundance, plenty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावृष्यः|प्रावृष्य|प्रावृष्यं
प्रावृष्यः<BR>1 A kind of Kadamba<BR>tree.<BR>--2 The Kuṭaja tree.<BR>--प्यं<BR>Lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेण्यं|प्रावेण्य
प्रावेण्यं A fine woollen covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशन
प्रावेशन a. (ना f.) To be given<BR>or done on entering.<BR>--नं A<BR>workshop, manufactory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रावेशिक
प्रावेशिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>or connected with entrance (into<BR>a house or upon the stage).<BR>--2 In<BR>the habit of entering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राव्रज्यं|प्राव्रज्य
प्राव्रज्यं, प्राव्राज्यं<BR>1 The life of a<BR>religious mendicant or recluse.<BR>--2<BR>Vagrancy, wandering habit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राव्राज्यं|प्राव्राज्य
प्राव्रज्यं, प्राव्राज्यं<BR>1 The life of a<BR>religious mendicant or recluse.<BR>--2<BR>Vagrancy, wandering habit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्
प्राश् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To eat, consume,<BR>devour, feed upon.<BR>--2 To taste;<BR>Ms. 2. 62.<BR>--3 To enjoy, sport with.<BR>--4<BR>To drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्
प्राश् f. Ved. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशः|प्राश
प्राशः<BR>1 Eating, tasting, living or<BR>feeding on; Ms. 11. 144; धूम˚ &c.<BR>--2 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशकः|प्राशक
प्राशकः An eater.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशनं|प्राशन
प्राशनं<BR>1 Eating, feeding upon,<BR>tasting.<BR>--2 Causing to eat, or taste;<BR>Ms. 2. 29.<BR>--3 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशनीय
प्राशनीय a. Eatable, serving as<BR>food.<BR>--यं Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशित|प्राशितं
प्राशित p. p. Eaten, tasted,<BR>consumed.<BR>--तं<BR>1 An offering of rice<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">Page0776-c+ 55</a>]<BR>and water to the Manes of deceased<BR>ancestors, daily obsequies to the<BR>Manes; प्राशितं पितृतर्पणं Ms. 3. 74.<BR>--2 Eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशित्रं|प्राशित्र
प्राशित्रं<BR>1 The portion of oblation<BR>partaken by Brahman at a sacrifice.<BR>--2 The vessel in which this oblation<BR>is placed.<BR>--3 Anything eatable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशस्त्यं|प्राशस्त्य
प्राशस्त्यं Excellence,<BR>praiseworthiness, pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशास्त्रं|प्राशास्त्र
प्राशास्त्रं<BR>1 The office of a Praśāstṛ.<BR>--2 Government, rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राशु|प्राशुः
प्राशु a. Ved. Exceedingly quick<BR>or swift.<BR>--शुः<BR>1 Eating.<BR>--2 One<BR>who eats Soma.<BR>--3 An enemy of<BR>Vṛtra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राश्निक|प्राश्निकः
प्राश्निक a. Containing questions.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An examiner.<BR>--2 An umpire,<BR>an arbitrator, a judge; अहो<BR>प्रयोगाभ्यंतरः प्राशिनकः M. 2; तद्भगवत्या<BR>प्राश्निकपदमध्यासितव्यं M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्
प्रास् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To throw, hurl or<BR>fling.<BR>--2 To discharge, cast (as a<BR>missile).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासः|प्रास
प्रासः<BR>1 Throwing, casting,<BR>discharging.<BR>--2 A dart, a barbed<BR>missile; Ms. 6. 32; Ki. 16. 4.<BR>--3<BR>Insertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासकः|प्रासक
प्रासकः<BR>1 A dart, barbed missile.<BR>--2 A die.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासनं|प्रासन
प्रासनं<BR>1 Throwing, hurling,<BR>casting.<BR>--2 Throwing down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासिक|प्रासिकः
प्रासिक a. Armed with a dart.<BR>--कः<BR>A lancer, spearman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्त
प्रास्त p. p.<BR>1 Thrown, darted,<BR>hurled, cast, discharged.<BR>--2<BR>Expelled, turned out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासंगः|प्रासङ्ग|प्रासंग|प्रासङ्गः
प्रासंगः A yoke for cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासंगिक|प्रासङ्गिक
प्रासंगिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Derived<BR>from close connection.<BR>--2<BR>Connected with, innate.<BR>--3 Incidental,<BR>casual, occasional; प्रासंगिकीनां विषयः<BR>कथानां U. 2. 6.<BR>--4 Relevant.<BR>--5<BR>Seasonable, opportune.<BR>--6<BR>Episodical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासंग्यः|प्रासङ्ग्य|प्रासंग्य|प्रासङ्ग्यः
प्रासंग्यः A draught-ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादः|प्रासाद
प्रासादः [प्रसीदत्यास्मिन् प्र + सद् आधारे<BR>घञ् दीर्घः]<BR>1 A palace, mansion, any<BR>large palatial building; भिक्षुः<BR>कुटीयति प्रासादे Sk.; Me. 64.<BR>--2 A royal<BR>mansion.<BR>--3 A temple, shrine.<BR>--4<BR>A raised platform for spectators.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगनं the court-yard of<BR>a palace or temple.<BR>--आरोहणं<BR>entering or going up into a palace.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">Page0777-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--कुक्कुटः a tame pigeon.<BR>--तलं the<BR>surface or flat roof of a palace.<BR>--पृष्ठः a balcony on the top of a<BR>palace.<BR>--प्रतिष्ठा the consecration of<BR>atemple.<BR>--प्रस्तरः the flat roof of a<BR>house.<BR>--मंडना a kind of orpiment.<BR>--शायिन् a. sleeping in a palace.<BR>--शृंगं the spire or pinnacle of a<BR>palace or temple, a turret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0776-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादीय
प्रासादीय a. Palatial, splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादीयति
प्रासादीयति Den. P. To look upon<BR>(a hut &c.) as a palace; प्रासादीयति<BR>कुट्यां Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासादिक
प्रासादिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Given as<BR>a favour.<BR>--2 Kind, friendly,<BR>amiable; U. 6. 20.<BR>--3 Beautiful, lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रासूतिक
प्रासूतिक a. (की f.) Relating to<BR>delivery or child-birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्ताविक
प्रास्ताविक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Serving as an introduction,<BR>introductory, prefatory; as in<BR>प्रास्ताविकविलास (the first or introductory part<BR>of Bhāminīvilāsa); प्रास्ताविकं वचनं<BR>‘prefatory remarks.’<BR>--2 Seasonable,<BR>opportune, timely.<BR>--3 Pertinent,<BR>relevant (to the matter in hand);<BR>अप्रास्ताविकी महत्येषा कथा Māl. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्तुत्यं|प्रास्तुत्य
प्रास्तुत्यं Being under discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्थानिक
प्रास्थानिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Relating to or proper at the time of<BR>departure; R. 2. 70.<BR>--2 Favourable<BR>to a departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्थिक|प्रास्थिकः
प्रास्थिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Weighing a Prastha q. v.<BR>--2 Bought for<BR>a Prastha.<BR>--3 Containing a<BR>Prastha.<BR>--4 Sown with a Prastha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रास्रवण
प्रास्रवण a. (णी f.) Derived<BR>from a spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राहः|प्राह
प्राहः Instruction in the art of<BR>dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णः|प्राह्ण
प्राह्णः The forenoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णेतन|प्राह्णेतनः
प्राह्णेतन a. (नी f.) Relating to, or<BR>happening in, the forenoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णेतरां
प्राह्णेतरां --मां ind. Very early in<BR>the morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्राह्णेतमां
प्राह्णेतरां --मां ind. Very early in<BR>the morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रिय|प्रियः
प्रिय a. [प्रीणाति प्री-तर्पणे क]<BR>(compar. प्रेयस्, superl. प्रेष्ठ)<BR>1 Dear,<BR>beloved, liked, welcome, favourite;<BR>बंधुप्रियां Ku. 1. 26; प्रकृत्यैव प्रिया<BR>सीता रामस्यासीन्महात्मनः Rām; R. 3. 29.<BR>--2 Pleasing, agreeable; तामूचतुस्ते<BR>प्रियमप्यमिथ्या R. 14. 6.<BR>--3 Fond of,<BR>liking, loving, devoted or attached<BR>to; प्रियमंडना Ś. 4. 8.; प्रियारामा वैदेही<BR>U. 2.<BR>--4 Dear, expensive.<BR>--5 Ved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-b" target="_blank">Page0777-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Customary, familiar, usual.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>A lover, husband; स्त्रीणामाद्यं<BR>प्रणयवचनं विभ्रमो हि प्रियेषु Me. 28.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of deer.<BR>--या<BR>1 A beloved<BR>(wife), wife, mistress; प्रिये<BR>चारुशीले प्रिये रम्यशीले प्रिये Gīt. 10.<BR>--2 A<BR>woman in general.<BR>--3 Small<BR>cardamoms.<BR>--4 News, information.<BR>--5<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>--6 A kind of<BR>jasmine.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Love.<BR>--2 Kindness,<BR>service, favour; प्रियमाचरितं लते त्वया<BR>मे V. 1. 16; मत्प्रियार्थं यियासोः<BR>Me. 22; प्रियं मे प्रियं मे ‘a good service<BR>done to me’; Bg. 1. 23; U. 3. 26;<BR>Pt. 1. 365, 193.<BR>--3 Pleasing or<BR>gladsome news; R. 12. 91;<BR>प्रियनिवेदयितारं Ś. 4.<BR>--4 Pleasure.<BR>--यं ind.<BR>In a pleasing or agreeable manner.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिथि a. hospitable.<BR>--अन्नं dear food or provisions.<BR>--अपायः absence or loss of a<BR>beloved object.<BR>--अप्रिय a. pleasant<BR>and unpleasant, agreeable and<BR>disagreeable (feelings &c.).<BR>--(यं)<BR>service and disservice, favour and<BR>injury.<BR>--अंबुः the mango tree.<BR>--अर्ह a. {1} deserving love or<BR>kindness; U. 3. {2} amiable.<BR>--(र्हः) N.<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--असु a. fond of life.<BR>--आख्य a. announcing good news.<BR>--आख्यानं agreeable news.<BR>--आत्मन्<BR>a. amiable, pleasant, agreeable.<BR>--उक्तिः f.,<BR>--उदितं a kind or friendly<BR>speech, flattering remarks.<BR>--उपपत्तिः f. a happy or pleasant<BR>occurrence.<BR>--उपभोगः enjoyment of a<BR>lover or mistress; R. 12. 22.<BR>--एषिन् a. {1} desirous of pleasing or<BR>doing service. {2} friendly,<BR>affectionate.<BR>--कर a. giving or causing<BR>pleasure.<BR>--कर्मन् a. acting in a kind<BR>or friendly manner.<BR>--कलत्रः a<BR>husband who is fond of his wife, who<BR>loves her dearly.<BR>--काम a. friendly<BR>disposed, desirous of rendering<BR>service.<BR>--कार a. {1} acting kindly,<BR>doing good to. {2} favourable,<BR>suitable.<BR>--कारक, --कारिन्, a. acting<BR>or treating kindly. (--m.) a<BR>friend, benefactor; Pt. 4. 76.<BR>--कृत् m. {1} one who does good,<BR>a friend, benefactor. {2} N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--जनः a beloved or dear<BR>person.<BR>--जानिः a husband who<BR>dearly loves his wife.<BR>--जीव a. living<BR>long, long-lived.<BR>--तोषणः a kind of<BR>coitus or mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-c" target="_blank">Page0777-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--दर्श a. pleasant to look at.<BR>--दर्शन<BR>a. pleasing to look at, of pleasing<BR>appearance, good-looking,<BR>lovely, handsome; अहो प्रियदर्शनः कुमारः<BR>U. 5; R. 1. 47; Ś. 3. 10;<BR>एवमुत्सुकोऽपि प्रियदर्शनो देवः Ś. 6.<BR>--(नः) {1} a<BR>parrot. {2} a kind of date tree. {3}<BR>N. of a prince of the Gandharvas;<BR>R. 5. 53.<BR>--(नं) the sight of a beloved<BR>object; Pt. 1. 128.<BR>--दर्शिन् a.<BR>looking kindly upon anything. (--m.) an<BR>epithet of king Aśoka.<BR>--देवन a.<BR>fond of gambling.<BR>--धन्वः an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--पुत्रः a kind of bird.<BR>--प्रसादनं propitiation of a husband.<BR>--प्राय a. exceedingly kind or courteous;<BR>प्रियप्राया वृत्तिः U. 2. 2.<BR>--(यं)<BR>eloquence in language.<BR>--प्रायस् n. a very<BR>agreeable speech, as of a lover to his<BR>mistress.<BR>--प्रेप्सु a. wishing to<BR>secure one's desired object.<BR>--भावः<BR>feeling of love; U. 6. 31.<BR>--भाषणं<BR>kind or agreeable words.<BR>--भाषिन् a.<BR>speaking sweet words.<BR>--मंडन a.<BR>fond of ornaments; Ś. 4. 8.<BR>--मधु<BR>a. fond of liquor.<BR>--(धुः) an epithet<BR>of Balarāma.<BR>--रण a. warlike, heroic.<BR>--वक्तृ a. flattering, a flatterer.<BR>--वचन a. speaking kind or agreeable<BR>words.<BR>--(नं) kind, coaxing or<BR>endearing words; V. 2. 22.<BR>--वयस्यः a<BR>dear friend.<BR>--वर्णी the plant called<BR>प्रियंगु.<BR>--वस्तु n. a beloved object.<BR>--वाच् a. speaking kindly, affable<BR>in address. (--f.) kind or agreeable<BR>words.<BR>--वादिका a kind of musical<BR>instrument.<BR>--वादिन् a. speaking kind<BR>or pleasing words, a flatterer;<BR>सुलभाः पुरुषा राजन् सततं प्रियवादिनः Rām.<BR>--(नी) a kind of bird.<BR>--श्रवस् m. an<BR>epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--संबासः the<BR>society of a beloved person.<BR>--सखः {1}<BR>a dear friend. {2} the tree Khadira.<BR>(--खी f.) a female friend, a<BR>lady's confidante.<BR>--सत्य a. {1} a<BR>lover of truth. {2} pleasant though<BR>true.<BR>--संदेशः {1} a friendly message,<BR>the message of a lover. {2} the tree<BR>called चंपक.<BR>--समागमः union with a<BR>beloved object or person.<BR>--सहचरी<BR>a beloved wife.<BR>--सुहृद् m. a dear or<BR>bosom friend.<BR>--स्वप्न a. fond of<BR>sleep; R. 12. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंवद|प्रियंवदः
प्रियंवद a. Sweet-speaking,<BR>speaking kindly, affable in address,<BR>agreeable; Ku. 5. 28; R. 3. 64.<BR>--दः<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">Page0778-a+ 57</a>]<BR>A kind of bird.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0777-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियकः|प्रियक
प्रियकः<BR>1 A kind of deer;<BR>Śi. 4. 32.<BR>--2 The tree called नीप.<BR>--3 The<BR>creeper प्रियंगु.<BR>--4 A bee.<BR>--5 A kind<BR>of bird.<BR>--6 Saffron.<BR>--कं A flower of<BR>the asana tree; Śi. 8. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंकर|प्रियङ्कर|प्रियङ्करः
प्रियंकर, प्रियंकरण, प्रियंकार a.<BR>1<BR>Showing kindness to, acting kindly<BR>or affectionately; प्रियंकरो मे प्रिय<BR>इत्यनंदत् R. 14. 48.<BR>--2 Agreeable.<BR>--3<BR>Amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंकरण|प्रियङ्करण
प्रियंकर, प्रियंकरण, प्रियंकार a.<BR>1<BR>Showing kindness to, acting kindly<BR>or affectionately; प्रियंकरो मे प्रिय<BR>इत्यनंदत् R. 14. 48.<BR>--2 Agreeable.<BR>--3<BR>Amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंकार
प्रियंकर, प्रियंकरण, प्रियंकार a.<BR>1<BR>Showing kindness to, acting kindly<BR>or affectionately; प्रियंकरो मे प्रिय<BR>इत्यनंदत् R. 14. 48.<BR>--2 Agreeable.<BR>--3<BR>Amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंगुः|प्रियङ्गु|प्रियंगु|प्रियङ्गुः
प्रियंगुः<BR>1 N. of a creeper (said to<BR>put forth blossoms at the touch of<BR>women); प्रियंगुश्यामांगप्रकृतिरपि<BR>Māl. 3. 9. (For some of the conventions<BR>of poets about the blossoming of<BR>trees, see the quotation under अशोक).<BR>--2 Long pepper.<BR>--गु n. Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियतम|प्रियतमः
प्रियतम a. Most beloved, dearest.<BR>--मः A lover, husband; शिप्रावातः<BR>प्रियतम इव प्रार्थनाचाटुकारः Me. 31, 70.<BR>--मा A wife, mistress, beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियतर|प्रियतरः
प्रियतर a. Dearer, more beloved &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियता
प्रियता, --त्वं<BR>1 Being dear, dearness.<BR>--2 Love, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियत्वं|प्रियत्व
प्रियता, --त्वं<BR>1 Being dear, dearness.<BR>--2 Love, affection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंभविष्णु|प्रियम्भविष्णु
प्रियंभविष्णु, प्रियंभावुक a. Become<BR>an object of affection, amiable,<BR>dearly loved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियंभावुक|प्रियम्भावुक
प्रियंभविष्णु, प्रियंभावुक a. Become<BR>an object of affection, amiable,<BR>dearly loved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रियालः|प्रियाल
प्रियालः The tree called Piyāl; see<BR>पियाल.<BR>--ला A vine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्री
प्री {vI.v} {c9c} U. (प्रीणाति, प्रीणीते, प्रीत)<BR>1<BR>To please, delight, satisfy, gladden;<BR>प्रीणातियः सुचरितैः पितरं स पुत्रः<BR>Bh. 2. 68; सस्नुः पितॄन् पिप्रियुरापगासु<BR>Bk. 3. 38; 5. 104; 7. 64.<BR>--2 To be<BR>pleased, take delight in; कच्चिन् मनस्ते<BR>प्रीणाति वनवासे Mb.<BR>--3 To act kindly<BR>towards, show kindness towards.<BR>--4<BR>To be cheerful or gay. --Caus. (<BR>प्रीणयति-ते) To please, satisfy &c. {vII.v}<BR>{c4c} A. (प्रीयते, strictly a passive voice<BR>of the root प्री)<BR>1 To be satisfied or<BR>pleased, be gratified; प्रकाममप्रीयत<BR>यज्वनां प्रियः Śi. 17; R. 15. 30; 19. 30;<BR>Y. 1. 245.<BR>--2 To feel affection for,<BR>love.<BR>--3 To assent, be satisfied. {vIII.v}<BR>{c1c} P. To please, gratify &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीण|प्रीणः
प्रीण a.<BR>1 Pleased, satisfied,<BR>gratified.<BR>--2 Old, ancient.<BR>--3 Previous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीणन|प्रीणनं
प्रीणन^1 a. Pleasing, gratifying.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Pleasing, satisfying.<BR>--2 That<BR>which pleases or satisfies.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170203. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/335. note: adjective.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीणित
प्रीणित a. Pleased, delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीत|प्रीतः
प्रीत p. p. [प्री-कर्तरि क्त]<BR>1 Pleased.<BR>delighted, rejoiced, gladdened;<BR>प्रीतास्मि ते पुत्र वरं वृणीष्व R. 2. 63;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-b" target="_blank">Page0778-b+ 57</a>]<BR>1. 81, 12. 94.<BR>--2 Glad, happy, joyful;<BR>Me. 4.<BR>--3 Content.<BR>--4 Dear,<BR>beloved.<BR>--5 Kind, affectionate.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन्, --चित्त, --मनस् a. delighted<BR>at heart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिः|प्रीति
प्रीतिः [प्री भावे क्तिच्]<BR>1 f. Pleasure,<BR>happiness, satisfaction, delight,<BR>gladness, joy, gratification;<BR>भुवनालोकनप्रीतिः Ku. 2. 45, 6. 21;<BR>R. 2. 51; Me. 62.<BR>--2 Favour, kindness.<BR>--3 Love, affection, regard; Me. 4,<BR>16; R. 1. 57; 12. 54.<BR>--4 Liking<BR>or fondness for, delight in,<BR>addiction to; द्यूत˚, मृगया˚.<BR>--5<BR>Friendliness, amity.<BR>--6 Conciliation.<BR>--7 A<BR>symbolical expression for the letter<BR>ध.<BR>--8 N. of a wife of Cupid and<BR>rival of Rati; (सपत्नी संजाता रत्याः<BR>प्रीतिरिति श्रुता).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a.<BR>producing love, kind, agreeable.<BR>--कर्मन् n.<BR>an act of friendship or love, a kind<BR>action.<BR>--जुषा N. of the wife of<BR>अनिरुद्ध.<BR>--तृष् m. N. of cupid.<BR>--द a.<BR>inspiring love; giving pleasure,<BR>pleasing.<BR>--(दः) a jester or buffoon<BR>in a play.<BR>--दत्त a. given through<BR>affection.<BR>--(त्तं) property given to<BR>a female by her relatives,<BR>particularly by her father-in-law or<BR>motherin-law at the time of marriage.<BR>--दानं, --दायः a gift of love, a<BR>friendly present; तदवसरोऽयं प्रीतिदायस्य<BR>Māl. 4; R. 15. 68.<BR>--धनं money<BR>given through love or friendship.<BR>--पात्रं an object of love, any<BR>beloved person or object.<BR>--पुरोग a.<BR>affectionate, loving.<BR>--पूर्वं, पूर्वकं ind.<BR>kindly, affectionately.<BR>--प्रमुख a.<BR>friendly, affectionate, full of love,<BR>kind; Me. 4.<BR>--भाज् a. enjoying<BR>friendship, loved.<BR>--मनस् a. {1}<BR>delighted in mind, pleased, happy.<BR>{2} kind, affectionate.<BR>--मय a.<BR>arising from love or joy.<BR>--युज् a. dear,<BR>affectionate, beloved; Ki. 1. 10.<BR>--वचस् n.,<BR>--वचनं a friendly or kind<BR>speech.<BR>--वर्धन a. increasing love<BR>or joy.<BR>--(नः) an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--वादः a friendly discussion.<BR>--विवाहः a love-marriage, love-match<BR>(based purely on love).<BR>--श्राद्धं a<BR>sort of Śrāddha or obsequial<BR>ceremony performed in honour of<BR>the Manes of both parents.<BR>--स्निग्ध<BR>a. moist or wet through love (as<BR>the eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रीतिमत्|प्रीतिमन्त्
प्रीतिमत् a.<BR>1 Full of love or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-c" target="_blank">Page0778-c+ 56</a>]<BR>affection, loving, fond, affectionate^1.<BR>--2<BR>Pleased, satisfied.<BR>--3 Content, glad.<BR>--4 Favourable.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रु
प्रु {c1c} A. (प्रवते)<BR>1 To go, move.<BR>--2 To jump, spring. --Caus. To<BR>extend, reach as far as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्
प्रुष् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (प्रोषति, प्रुष्ट)<BR>1 To burn<BR>consume.<BR>--2 To reduce to ashes.<BR>{vII.v} {c9c} P. (प्रुष्णाति)<BR>1 To become wet<BR>or moist.<BR>--2 To pour out, sprinkle.<BR>--3 To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुषित
प्रुषित a.<BR>1 Sprinkled, wetted.<BR>--2<BR>Burning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्ट|प्रुष्टः
प्रुष्ट p. p. Burnt, consumed,<BR>reduced to ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रुष्वः|प्रुष्व
प्रुष्वः<BR>1 The rainy season.<BR>--2<BR>The sun.<BR>--3 A drop of water (Sk.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रे
प्रे (प्र-इ) {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go forward.<BR>--2<BR>To arrive at, reach.<BR>--3 To go out of,<BR>depart from; धीराः प्रेत्यास्माल्लोकादमृता<BR>भवंति Ken.<BR>--4 (Hence) to die,<BR>depart life; प्रेत्य ‘after death; see<BR>प्रेत्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत|प्रेतः
प्रेत p. p. [प्र-इ-क्त] Departed<BR>from this world, dead, deceased;<BR>स्वजनाश्रु किलातिसंततं दहति प्रेतमिति<BR>प्रचक्षते R. 8. 86.<BR>--तः<BR>1 The<BR>departed spirit, the spirit before obsequial<BR>rites are performed.<BR>--2 A ghost,<BR>evil spirit, Bg. 17. 4; Ms. 12. 71.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः an epithet of<BR>Yama.<BR>--अन्नं food offered to the<BR>Manes.<BR>--अस्थि n. the bone of a<BR>dead man. ˚धारिन् an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--आवासः a burial-ground,<BR>cemetery.<BR>--ईशः, --ईश्वरः an epithet of<BR>Yama.<BR>--उद्देशः an offering to the<BR>Manes.<BR>--कर्मन् n.,<BR>--कृत्यं, --कृत्या<BR>obsequial or funeral rites.<BR>--गत a.<BR>dead.<BR>--गृहं a cemetery.<BR>--गोपः the<BR>keeper of the dead.<BR>--चारिन् m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--दाहः the burning<BR>of the dead, cremation.<BR>--धूमः the<BR>smoke issuing from a funeral pile.<BR>--नदी the river वैतरिणी.<BR>--तरः a<BR>goblin, ghost.<BR>--निर्यातकः, --निहार्रकः a<BR>man employed to carry out dead<BR>bodies.<BR>--पक्षः ‘the fortnight of the<BR>Manes’, N. of the dark half of<BR>Bhādrapada when offerings in<BR>honour of the Manes are usually<BR>performed; cf. पितृपक्ष.<BR>--पटहः a drum<BR>beaten at a funeral.<BR>--पतिः Yama<BR>(the Indian ‘Pluto’).<BR>--पुरं the<BR>city of Yama.<BR>--भावः death.<BR>--भूमिः<BR>f. a cemetery.<BR>--मेघः a funeral<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">Page0779-a+ 57</a>]<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--राक्षसी the holy basil<BR>(तुलसी).<BR>--राजः an epithet of<BR>Yama.<BR>--लोकः the world of the<BR>dead.<BR>--वनं a cemetery.<BR>--वाहित a.<BR>possessed by a ghost.<BR>--शरीरं the<BR>body of the departed spirit.<BR>--शुद्धिः<BR>f.,<BR>--शौचं purification after the<BR>death of a relative.<BR>--श्राद्धं an<BR>obsequial offering made to a departed<BR>relative during the year of his<BR>death.<BR>--हारः {1} one who carries<BR>out a dead body. {2} a near<BR>relative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0778-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतिः|प्रेति
प्रेतिः f.<BR>1 Death, dying.<BR>--2<BR>Departure, flight.<BR>--3 Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेतिकः|प्रेतिक
प्रेतिकः A ghost, spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्य
प्रेत्य ind. Having departed (from<BR>this world), after death, in the next<BR>world; न च तत्प्रेत्य नो इह<BR>Bg. 17. 28; Ms. 2. 9, 26.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जातिः<BR>f. position in the world to come.<BR>--भाज् a. enjoying the fruits of<BR>actions in the next world.<BR>--भावः<BR>the condition of soul after death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्ष्
प्रेक्ष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To see, behold, look<BR>at, perceive; तमायांतं प्रेक्ष्य Pt. 1;<BR>R. 12. 44; Ku. 6. 47; Ms. 8. 147.<BR>--2 To look on, be a spectator, युष्माकं<BR>प्रेक्षमाणानां Ve. 3.<BR>--3 To allow, suffer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षकः|प्रेक्षक
प्रेक्षकः A spectator, looker on, be<BR>holder, sight-seer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणं|प्रेक्षण
प्रेक्षणं<BR>1 Viewing, seeing.<BR>--2 A<BR>view, look, appearance.<BR>--3 The eye;<BR>चकितहरिणीप्रेक्षणा Me. 82.<BR>--4 Any<BR>public show or spectacle, sight,<BR>show.<BR>--5 A dramatic representation;<BR>प्रेक्षणावसाने V. 3.<BR>--6 A place where<BR>public exhibitions are held.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कूटं the eye-ball.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणकं|प्रेक्षणक
प्रेक्षणकं A show, spectacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणिका
प्रेक्षणिका A woman fond of<BR>seeing shows.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणीय
प्रेक्षणीय pot. p.<BR>1 To bee seen,<BR>viewed, or gazed at; visible,<BR>apparent.<BR>--2 Fit to be seen, lovely to<BR>the sight, beautiful to look at;<BR>Me. 2; R. 14. 9.<BR>--3 To be<BR>considered or regarded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षणीयकं|प्रेक्षणीयक
प्रेक्षणीयकं A show, sight,<BR>spectacle; Śi. 10. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षा
प्रेक्षा<BR>1 Viewing, seeing,<BR>beholding.<BR>--2 A look, view, sight,<BR>appearance.<BR>--3 Being a looker-on.<BR>--4 Any<BR>public spectacle or show, sight.<BR>--5<BR>Particularly, a theatrical show,<BR>dramatic performance, play.<BR>--6<BR>Intellect, understanding.<BR>--7<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">Page0779-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Reflection, consideration, deliberation.<BR>--8<BR>The branch of a tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अ<BR>(आ) गारः --रं, --गृहं, --स्थानं {1} a<BR>theatre, or play-house. {2} a<BR>councilchamber.<BR>--कारिन् a. wise, prudent,<BR>circumspect; प्रेक्षाकारी याति पदं<BR>मुक्तमपायैः Ki. 18. 28.<BR>--समाजः an<BR>audience, a crowd of spectators,<BR>asembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षावत्|प्रेक्षावन्त्
प्रेक्षावत् a. Considerate, wise,<BR>learned (as a man).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षित
प्रेक्षित p. p. Seen, viewed, behold,<BR>gazed or looked at.<BR>--तं A look,<BR>glance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्षिन्
प्रेक्षिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>1 Looking at,<BR>viewing.<BR>--2 Watching narrowly,<BR>observing carefully.<BR>--3 Having the<BR>eyes or glance of, looking like, as in<BR>मृगप्रेक्षिणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेक्ष्य
प्रेक्ष्य = प्रेक्षणीय q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेंख्|प्रेङ्ख्
प्रेंख् {c1c} P. To vibrate, shake,<BR>tremble, swing to and fro, oscillate.<BR>--Caus. To shake, swing, rock to<BR>and fro.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेंखः|प्रेङ्ख|प्रेंखं|प्रेङ्खः
प्रेंखः, --खं A swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेंखं|प्रेङ्ख|प्रेंखः|प्रेङ्खः
प्रेंखः, --खं A swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेंखण|प्रेङ्खण
प्रेंखण a. Wandering, moving,<BR>going towards, entering;<BR>Bk. 9. 106.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Swinging.<BR>--2 A swing.<BR>--3 A minor drama in one act,<BR>having no Sūtradhāra, hero &c; S. D.<BR>thus defines it: --गर्भावमर्षरहितं प्रेंखणं<BR>हीननायकं । असूत्रधारमेकांकमविष्कंभप्रवेशकम् ।<BR>नियुद्धसंफेटयुतं सर्ववृत्तिसमाश्रितं ॥ 547; e. g.<BR>वालिवध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेंखा|प्रेङ्खा
प्रेंखा<BR>1 A swing.<BR>--2 Dancing.<BR>--3<BR>Roaming about, wandering,<BR>travelling.<BR>--4 A kind of building or<BR>house.<BR>--5 A particular pace of a<BR>horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेंखित|प्रेङ्खित|प्रेङ्खितं
प्रेंखित p. p. Swung, shaken,<BR>oscillated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेंखोल्|प्रेङ्खोल्
प्रेंखोल् {c10c} U. (प्रेंखोलयति-ते) To<BR>swing, shake, oscillate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेंखोलः|प्रेङ्खोल|प्रेङ्खोलः
प्रेंखोलः, --प्रेंखोलनं<BR>1 Swinging,<BR>shaking, oscillating; Māl. 9. 17.<BR>--2 A<BR>swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेंखोलनं|प्रेङ्खोलन|प्रेङ्खोलनं
प्रेंखोलः, --प्रेंखोलनं<BR>1 Swinging,<BR>shaking, oscillating; Māl. 9. 17.<BR>--2 A<BR>swing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत|प्रेतः
प्रेत, प्रेति, प्रेत्य &c. See under प्रे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेति|प्रेतिः
प्रेत, प्रेति, प्रेत्य &c. See under प्रे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्य
प्रेत, प्रेति, प्रेत्य &c. See under प्रे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेत्वन्
प्रेत्वन् m.<BR>1 Wind.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेप्सा
प्रेप्सा<BR>1 Desire of obtaining.<BR>--2<BR>Desire (in general).<BR>--3<BR>Supposition, assumption.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेप्सु
प्रेप्सु a.<BR>1 Desirous of obtaining,<BR>wishing, seeking, longing for.<BR>--2<BR>Aiming at.<BR>--3 Supposing, assuming.<BR>--4 Anxious to deliver.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमन्
प्रेमन् m., n. [प्रियस्य भावः इमनिच<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">Page0779-c+ 56</a>]<BR>प्रादेशः एकाच्कत्वात् न टिलोपः Tv.]<BR>1<BR>Love, affection; तत्प्रेमहेमनिकषोपलतां<BR>तनोति Gīt. 11; Me. 44.<BR>--2 Favour,<BR>kindness, kind or tender regard.<BR>--3<BR>Sport, pastime.<BR>--4 Joy, delight,<BR>gladness. --m.<BR>1 A jest, joke.<BR>--2<BR>Wind, air.<BR>--3 An epithet of Indra.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्रु n. a tear of joy or<BR>affection.<BR>--ऋद्धिः f. increase of<BR>affection, ardent love.<BR>--पर a.<BR>affectionate, loving.<BR>--पातनं {1} tears<BR>(of joy). {2} the eye (that sheds<BR>them).<BR>--पात्रं ‘an object of love,<BR>any beloved person or thing.<BR>--बंधः<BR>बं धनं a bond or tie of affection,<BR>--भावः affection, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमवती
प्रेमवती A mistress or beloved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेमिन्
प्रेमिन् a. (णी f.) Loving,<BR>affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेयस्
प्रेयस् a. (सी f.) Dearer, more<BR>beloved or agreeable &c. (comper.<BR>of प्रिय q. v.). --m.<BR>1 A lover,<BR>husband.<BR>--2 A dear friend;<BR>Māl. 10. 24. --m. --n. Flattery.<BR>--सी A wife,<BR>mistress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेयोपत्यः|प्रेयोपत्य
प्रेयोपत्यः A heron (fond of<BR>offspring).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेर्
प्रेर् Caus.<BR>1 To set in motion,<BR>move.<BR>--2 To push or urge on,<BR>propel, impel, send forth; R. 4. 24. v. l.<BR>--3 To incite, instigate, set on<BR>--4<BR>To cast, direct (as eyes); नयने<BR>यत्प्रेरयंत्या तया Ś. 2. 2.<BR>--5 To throw,<BR>hurl.<BR>--6 To send forth, despatch.<BR>--7 To utter.<BR>--8 To ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरक
प्रेरक a. (रिका f.)<BR>1 Impelling,<BR>urging, stimulating.<BR>--2 Sending,<BR>directing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरणं|प्रेरण
प्रेरणं, --णा<BR>1 Driving or urging on,<BR>impelling, inciting, instigation.<BR>--2<BR>Impulse, passion.<BR>--3 Throwing,<BR>casting; ह्नीमूढानां भवति विफलप्रेरणा<BR>चूर्णमुष्टिः Me. 68.<BR>--4 Sending,<BR>despatching.<BR>--5 Order, direction.<BR>--6 (In<BR>gram.) The sense of the causal<BR>form.<BR>--7 Activity, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरणा
प्रेरणं, --णा<BR>1 Driving or urging on,<BR>impelling, inciting, instigation.<BR>--2<BR>Impulse, passion.<BR>--3 Throwing,<BR>casting; ह्नीमूढानां भवति विफलप्रेरणा<BR>चूर्णमुष्टिः Me. 68.<BR>--4 Sending,<BR>despatching.<BR>--5 Order, direction.<BR>--6 (In<BR>gram.) The sense of the causal<BR>form.<BR>--7 Activity, exertion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेरित|प्रेरितः
प्रेरित p. p.<BR>1 Impelled, urged,<BR>instigated.<BR>--2 Excited, stimulated,<BR>prompted; Pt. 2. 144.<BR>--3 Sent,<BR>despatched.<BR>--4 Ordered.<BR>--5 Directed,<BR>cast; ततस्ततः प्रेरितलोललोचना<BR>Ś. 1. 23.<BR>--6 Touched.<BR>--तः An envoy, a<BR>messenger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेर्त्वन्
प्रेर्त्वन् m. Ved. The ocean. --f.<BR>(प्रेर्त्वरी) A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्
प्रेष् {vI.v} {c4c} P.<BR>1 To drive forward,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">Page0780-a+ 56</a>]<BR>drive on.<BR>--2 To send forth, utter.<BR>--3 To fling, cast. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>send forth, cast, hurl, Bk. 15. 77.<BR>--2 To send, despatch; किमर्थमृषयः<BR>प्रेषिताः स्युः Ś. 5.<BR>--3 To send away,<BR>dismiss.<BR>--4 To banish.<BR>--5 To turn<BR>or direct (the eyes). {vII.v} {c1c} U.<BR>(प्रेषति ते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0779-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषः|प्रेष
प्रेषः<BR>1 Urging on.<BR>--2 Affliction,<BR>pain, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषक
प्रेषक a.<BR>1 Despatching, sending.<BR>--2 Ordering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषणं|प्रेषण
प्रेषणं, --णा<BR>1 Sending, despatching.<BR>--2 Sending on a mission, directing,<BR>commissioning.<BR>--3 Executing a<BR>commission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषणा
प्रेषणं, --णा<BR>1 Sending, despatching.<BR>--2 Sending on a mission, directing,<BR>commissioning.<BR>--3 Executing a<BR>commission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेषित|प्रेषितं
प्रेषित p. p.<BR>1 Despatched (on<BR>an errand).<BR>--2 Ordered, directed.<BR>--3 Turned, fixed upon, directed<BR>towards, cast (as eyes).<BR>--4 Banished.<BR>--5 Sent away, dismissed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्य|प्रेष्यः
प्रेष्य a. To be ordered, sent,<BR>despatched &c.<BR>--ष्यः<BR>1 A servant,<BR>menial, slave; Pt. 1. 424.<BR>--2 A<BR>messenger.<BR>--ष्या A female servant,<BR>hand-maid.<BR>--ष्यं<BR>1 Sending on a<BR>mission.<BR>--2 Servitude.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जवः servants taken collectively.<BR>--भावः capacity of a servant,<BR>servitude, bondage; M. 5. 12.<BR>--वध्रः {1}<BR>the wife of a servant. {2} a female<BR>servant, hand-maid.<BR>--वर्गः the body<BR>of servants, suite, train.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेष्ठ|प्रेष्ठः
प्रेष्ठ p. p. Dearest, most<BR>beloved &c. (superl. of प्रिय q. v.).<BR>--ष्ठः<BR>A lover, husband.<BR>--ष्ठा<BR>1 A wife,<BR>mistress.<BR>--2 A leg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रेहि
प्रेहि (Second person sing. of the<BR>imperative of इ with प्र q. v.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कटा a rite in which no<BR>mats are allowed.<BR>--कर्दमा a rite in<BR>which no impurity is allowed.<BR>--द्वितीया a rite at which no second<BR>person is allowed to be present.<BR>--वाणिजा a rite at which no merchants<BR>are allowed to be present. (See Gaṇa<BR>to P. II. 1. 72).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैयं|प्रैय
प्रैयं Being kind, kindness, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैषः|प्रैष
प्रैषः<BR>1 Sending, directing.<BR>--2 An<BR>order, command, invitation.<BR>--3<BR>Affliction, distress.<BR>--4 Madness, frenzy.<BR>--5 Crushing, pressing, squeezing<BR>(मर्दन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैषणिक
प्रैषणिक a. Executing orders or<BR>commissions (as a servant).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रैष्यः|प्रैष्य
प्रैष्यः A servant, menial, slave;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">Page0780-b+ 54</a>]<BR>Ku. 6. 58.<BR>--ष्या A female servant.<BR>--ष्यं Servitude, slavery.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भावः the capacity of a servant,<BR>being used as servant, servitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्ष्
प्रोक्ष् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To sprinkle upon or<BR>with.<BR>--2 To consecrate by<BR>sprinkling holy water; प्राणात्यये तथा श्राद्धे<BR>प्रोक्षितं द्विजकाम्यया Y. 1. 179;<BR>Ms. 5. 27.<BR>--3 To slay, kill. --Caus. To<BR>sprinkle, sprinkle with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षणं|प्रोक्षण
प्रोक्षणं<BR>1 Sprinkling, sprinkling<BR>with water; Ms. 5. 118; Y. 1. 184.<BR>--2 Consecration by sprinkling.<BR>--3<BR>Immolation (of animals) at a<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--4 A text to be repeated at<BR>an animal-sacrifice.<BR>--णी, --प्रोक्षणिः<BR>f. Water used for sprinkling or<BR>consecrating, holy water (used in pl.,<BR>and sometimes used to denote ‘the<BR>vessel containing holy water,’ in<BR>which sense the word generally used<BR>is प्रोक्षणीपात्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षणीयं|प्रोक्षणीय
प्रोक्षणीयं Water for consecrating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोक्षित|प्रोक्षितं
प्रोक्षित p. p.<BR>1 Purified or<BR>consecrated by sprinkling.<BR>--2 Immolated<BR>at a sacrifice.<BR>--3 Offered in sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चंड|प्रोच्चण्ड
प्रोच्चंड a. Exceedingly frightful or<BR>terrible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चारित
प्रोच्चारित a. Sounding loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्चैस्
प्रोच्चैस् ind.<BR>1 Very loudly, aloud.<BR>--2 In a very high degree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छून
प्रोच्छून a.<BR>1 Dilated.<BR>--2 Swollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोच्छ्रित
प्रोच्छ्रित p. p. High, lofty,<BR>elevated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्जासनं|प्रोज्जासन
प्रोज्जासनं Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झ्
प्रोज्झ् {c6c} P. = उज्झ् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झनं|प्रोज्झन
प्रोज्झनं Abandoning, quitting,<BR>leaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोज्झित|प्रोज्झितं
प्रोज्झित p. p. Abandoned,<BR>quitted, forsaken, avoided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोंछनं|प्रोञ्छन|प्रोंछन|प्रोञ्छनं
प्रोंछनं<BR>1 Wiping away, wiping<BR>out, effacing; N. 5. 36.<BR>--2 Picking<BR>up the remnants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोड्डीन
प्रोड्डीन a. Flown up or away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढ
प्रोढ, प्रोढि See प्रौढ, प्रौढि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोढि|प्रोढिः
प्रोढ, प्रोढि See प्रौढ, प्रौढि<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोंठः|प्रोण्ठ|प्रोण्ठः
प्रोंठः A spitting-pot, spittoon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत|प्रोतं
प्रोत p. p. [प्र-वे-स्यूतौ-क्त संप्रसारणं]<BR>1<BR>{1} Sewn, stitched; Ku. 7. 49.<BR>--2<BR>Extended lengthwise or<BR>perpendicularly (opp. ओत).<BR>--3 Tied, bound,<BR>fastened; Mv. 6. 33.<BR>--4 Pierced,<BR>transfixed; R. 9. 75.<BR>--5 Passed or<BR>come through; तरुछिद्रप्रोतान् i. e.<BR>(चंद्रोकरणान्) बिसमिति करी<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">Page0780-c+ 54</a>]<BR>संकलयति K. P. 10.<BR>--6 Set, inlaid;<BR>Mv. 1. 35.<BR>--7 Joined, connected.<BR>--तं<BR>A garment, woven cloth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्सादनं {1} an umbrella. {2} a<BR>cloth house, tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोतयति
प्रोतयति Den. P. To insert, infix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कट
प्रोत्कट (i. e. भृत्यः) A favourite<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कंठ|प्रोत्कण्ठ
प्रोत्कंठ a. Lifting up or<BR>stretching out the neck.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्कर्षः|प्रोत्कर्ष
प्रोत्कर्षः Pre-eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्क्रुष्टं|प्रोत्क्रुष्ट
प्रोत्क्रुष्टं A loud noise or uproar<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्तुंग|प्रोत्तुङ्ग
प्रोत्तुंग a. Very high or lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्फुल्ल|प्रोत्फुल्लं
प्रोत्फुल्ल a.<BR>1 Full-blown,<BR>expanded.<BR>--2 Fully dilated, wide open<BR>(eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्सारणं|प्रोत्सारण
प्रोत्सारणं Getting rid of,<BR>clearing away, removing, expelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्सारित
प्रोत्सारित p. p.<BR>1 Removed, got<BR>rid of, expelled.<BR>--2 Urged<BR>forward, incited.<BR>--3 Relinquished.<BR>--4<BR>Granted, given.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहः|प्रोत्साह
प्रोत्साहः<BR>1 Zeal, ardour.<BR>--2 An<BR>incentive, a stimulus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहकः|प्रोत्साहक
प्रोत्साहकः<BR>1 An inciter,<BR>instigator.<BR>--2 (In law) An instigator of a<BR>crime, an abettor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोत्साहनं|प्रोत्साहन
प्रोत्साहनं Inciting, stimulating,<BR>instigating, prompting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथ्
प्रोथ् {c1c} U. (प्रोथति-ते)<BR>1 To be<BR>equal to, be a match for, withstand<BR>(with dat.); पुप्रोथास्मै न कश्चत<BR>Bk. 14. 84; 15. 40.<BR>--2 To be able,<BR>adequate or competent.<BR>--3 To be full<BR>or complete.<BR>--4 To subdue,<BR>overpower.<BR>--5 To destroy, slay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथ|प्रोथः
प्रोथ a.<BR>1 Famous, well-known.<BR>--2 Placed, fixed.<BR>--3 Travelling,<BR>going out on a journey, wayfaring;<BR>वृक्षांतमुदकांतं च प्रियं प्रोथमनुव्रजेत् Tv.<BR>--थः --थं<BR>1 The nose or nostrils of<BR>a horse; N. 1. 60; Śi. 11. 11,<BR>12. 73.<BR>--2 The snout of a hog.<BR>--थः<BR>1<BR>The hip, buttocks.<BR>--2 An<BR>excavation.<BR>--3 A garment, old clothes.<BR>--4 Embryo.<BR>--5 Terror, fright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोथिन्
प्रोथिन् m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्गत
प्रोद्गत a. Projecting, prominent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्घुष्
प्रोद्घुष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sound forth.<BR>--2 To fill with sounds or cries.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to resound.<BR>--2<BR>To proclaim loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्घुष्ट
प्रोद्घुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Resounding,<BR>resonant.<BR>--2 Making a loud noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0780-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्घोषणं|प्रोद्घोषण
प्रोद्घोषणं, --णा<BR>1 Proclaiming,<BR>proclamation.<BR>--2 Sounding aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्घोषणा
प्रोद्घोषणं, --णा<BR>1 Proclaiming,<BR>proclamation.<BR>--2 Sounding aloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्दीप्त
प्रोद्दीप्त p. p. Set on fire, burning,<BR>blazing; Bh. 3. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्बोधः|प्रोद्बोध
प्रोद्बोधः Awaking, appearing,<BR>manifestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रोद्भिन्न
प्रोद्भिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Germinated,<BR>shot up.<BR>--2 Burst forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0781-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

