मातंगः|मातङ्ग|मातंग|मातङ्गः
मातंगः [मतंगस्य मुनेरयं अण्]<BR>1<BR>An elephant; मातंगाः किमु वल्गितैः<BR>K. P. 7; Śi. 1. 64.<BR>--2 A man of the<BR>lowest caste, a Cāṇḍāla.<BR>--3 A<BR>Kirāta, a mountaineer or barbarian.<BR>--4 (At the end of comp.) Any<BR>thing the best of its kind; e. g.<BR>बलाहकमातंगः.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दिवाकरः N.<BR>of a poet.<BR>--तक्रः a crocodile as large<BR>as an elephant; R. 13. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातरिपुरुषः|मातरिपुरुष
मातरिपुरुषः ‘One who can act<BR>like a man only against his mother’,<BR>a poltroon, cowardly boaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातरिश्वन्
मातरिश्वन् [मातरि अंतरीक्षे श्वयति<BR>वर्वते श्वि-कनिन् डिच्च अलुक् स<BR>Uṇ. 1. 156] Wind; पुनरुषसि<BR>विविक्तैर्मातरिश्वावचूर्ण्य ज्वलयति मदनाग्निं मालतीनां<BR>रजोभिः Śi. 11. 17; Ki. 5. 36;<BR>मातरिश्वा वायुर्मातर्यंतरिक्षे श्वसिति मातर्वाशु<BR>अनिति वा Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातलिः|मातलि
मातलिः N. of the charioteer of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">Page0857-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Indra.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--साराथिः an epithet of<BR>Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माता
माता A mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातामहः|मातामह
मातामहः A maternal<BR>grandfather.<BR>--हौ (dual) The maternal<BR>grand-father and grand-mother.<BR>--ही<BR>The maternal grand-mother.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातिः|माति
मातिः f.<BR>1 Measure.<BR>--2 A<BR>thought, idea, conception.<BR>--3<BR>Accurate knowledge or<BR>determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलः|मातुल
मातुलः [मातुर्भ्राता मातृ-डुलच्]<BR>1 A<BR>maternal uncle; Bg. 1. 26;<BR>Ms. 2. 130, 5. 81.<BR>--2 The Dhattūra plant.<BR>--3 An epithet of the solar year.<BR>--4<BR>A kind of rice.<BR>--5 A kind of snake.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुत्रकः {1} the son of a<BR>maternal uncle. {2} the fruit of the<BR>Dhattūra plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलकः|मातुलक
मातुलकः<BR>1 A maternal uncle (as a<BR>term of endearment).<BR>--2 The<BR>thornapple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुला
मातुला, मातुलानी, मातुली<BR>1 The wife<BR>of a maternal uncle; Ms. 2. 131;<BR>Y. 3. 232.<BR>--2 Hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलानी
मातुला, मातुलानी, मातुली<BR>1 The wife<BR>of a maternal uncle; Ms. 2. 131;<BR>Y. 3. 232.<BR>--2 Hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुली
मातुला, मातुलानी, मातुली<BR>1 The wife<BR>of a maternal uncle; Ms. 2. 131;<BR>Y. 3. 232.<BR>--2 Hemp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलेयः|मातुलेय
मातुलेयः (यी f.) The son of a<BR>maternal uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलिंगः|मातुलिङ्ग|मातुलिंग|मातुलिङ्गः
मातुलिंगः, मातुलुंगः A kind of<BR>citron tree; (भुवो) भागाः प्रेंखितम<BR>तुलुगवृतयः प्रेयो विधास्यति वां<BR>Māl. 6. 19.<BR>--गं The fruit of this tree, a<BR>citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातुलुंगः|मातुलुङ्ग|मातुलुंग|मातुलुङ्गः
मातुलिंगः, मातुलुंगः A kind of<BR>citron tree; (भुवो) भागाः प्रेंखितम<BR>तुलुगवृतयः प्रेयो विधास्यति वां<BR>Māl. 6. 19.<BR>--गं The fruit of this tree, a<BR>citron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृ
मातृ f. [मान् पूजायां तृच् नलोपः<BR>Uṇ. 2. 94]<BR>1 A mother; मातृवत्परदारेषु या<BR>पश्यति स पश्यति; सहस्रं तु पितॄन् मातः<BR>गौर वेणातिरिच्यते Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Mother<BR>as a term of respect or endearment;<BR>मातर्लक्ष्मि भजस्व कंचिदपरं Bh. 3. 64,<BR>87; अयि मातर्देवयजनसंभवे देवि सीते<BR>U. 4<BR>--3 A cow.<BR>--4 An epithet of<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR>--5 An epithet of Durgā.<BR>--6<BR>Ether, sky.<BR>--7 The earth.<BR>--8 A<BR>divine mother; मातृभ्यो बलिमुपहर<BR>Mk. 1.<BR>--9 An epithet of Revatī.<BR>--10 N. of several plants आखुकर्णी,<BR>इंद्रवारुणी and जटामांसी &c. --pl.<BR>1 An epithet of the divine<BR>mothers, said to attend on<BR>Śiva, but usually on Skanda. They<BR>are usually said to be 8; ब्र ह्मी<BR>माहेश्वरी चंडी वाराही वैष्णवी तथा । कौमारी चैव<BR>चामुंडाचर्चिंकेत्यष्ट मातरः ॥ or, according to<BR>some, only seven; ब्राह्मी माहेश्वरी चैव<BR>कौमारी वैष्णवी तथा । माहेंद्री चैव वाराही<BR>चामुंडा-सप्त मातरः ॥ Some increase the<BR>umber to sixteen.<BR>--2 N. of eight<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-a" target="_blank">Page0858-a+ 58</a>]<BR>classes of female ancestors or<BR>Manes. --m.<BR>1 A measurer.<BR>--2 Ved.<BR>A maker, builder, creator.<BR>--3 A<BR>knower, one having true<BR>knowledge.<BR>--4 Life, or soul (जीव)<BR>[cf. L. Mater.]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केशटः a maternal uncle.<BR>--गणः the<BR>collection of the divine mothers.<BR>--गंधिनी an unnatural mother.<BR>--गोमिन् m. one who has committed<BR>incest with his mother.<BR>--गोत्रं a mother's family.<BR>--ग्रामः the<BR>female sex, womankind.<BR>--घातः,<BR>--घातकः, --घातिन् m.<BR>--घ्नः a matricide<BR>--घातुकः {1} a matricide. {2} an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>--चक्रं the group of<BR>divine mothers.<BR>--देव a. having a<BR>mother for one's god, adoring<BR>mother like a god.<BR>--नंदनः an epithet<BR>of Kārtikeya.<BR>--पक्ष a. belonging to<BR>the mother's side or line.<BR>--(क्षः)<BR>maternal kinsmen.<BR>--पितृ m. (dual)<BR>(forming मातापितरौ or मातरपितरौ)<BR>parents.<BR>--पुत्रौ (मातापुत्रौ) a mother<BR>and son.<BR>--पूजनं worship of the<BR>divine mothers<BR>--बंधुः, --बांधवः a<BR>maternal kinsman; R. 12. 12.<BR>(--pl.) a class of relatives on the<BR>mother's side; they are thus<BR>specified: --मातुः पितुः स्वसुः पुत्रा मातुर्मातुः<BR>स्वसुः सुताः । मातुर्मातुलपुत्राश्च विज्ञेया मातृबंधवः ॥<BR>--भोगीण a. fit to be enjoyed or<BR>possessed by a mother.<BR>--मंडलं the<BR>collection of the divine mothers.<BR>--मातृ f. an epithet of Pārvatī.<BR>--मुखः, --शासितः a foolish fellow.<BR>simpleton.<BR>--यज्ञः a sacrifice offered<BR>to the divine mothers.<BR>--वत्सलः an<BR>epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>--स्वसृ f.<BR>(मातृष्वसृ or मातुःस्वसृ) a mother's<BR>sister, a maternal aunt.<BR>--स्वसेयः<BR>(मातृष्वसेयः) a mother's sister's son.<BR>--(यी) the daughter of a maternal<BR>aunt so मातृष्वस्रीयः --या.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0857-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मातृक|मातृकः
मातृक a.<BR>1 Coming or inherited<BR>from a mother; मातृकं च धनुरूर्जितं<BR>दधत् R. 11. 64, 90.<BR>--2 Maternal.<BR>--कः A maternal uncle.<BR>--का<BR>1 A<BR>mother.<BR>--2 A grand-mother.<BR>--3 A<BR>nurse.<BR>--4 A source, origin.<BR>--5 A<BR>divine mother.<BR>--6 N of certain<BR>diagrams written in characters<BR>supposed to have a magical<BR>power.<BR>--7 The character or<BR>alphabet so used (pl.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्र|मात्रं|मात्रः
मात्र a. (त्रा, --त्री f.) [मा-त्रन्] An<BR>affix added to nouns in the sense<BR>of ‘measuring as much as’, ‘as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-b" target="_blank">Page0858-b+ 57</a>]<BR>high or long, or broad as,’<BR>‘reaching as far as;’ as in ऊरुमात्री भित्तिः<BR>पंचदशयोजनमात्रमध्वानमतिचक्राम K.;<BR>(in this sense the word may as<BR>well be considered to be मात्रा at the<BR>end of comp. q. v. below).<BR>--त्रं<BR>1<BR>A measure, whether of length,<BR>breadth, height, size, space,<BR>distance or number; usually at the<BR>end of comp. i. e. अंगुलिमात्रं a<BR>‘finger's breadth’; किंचिन्मात्रं गत्वा ‘to<BR>some distance’; क्रोशमात्रे ‘at the<BR>distance of a Krośa’, रेखामात्रमपि<BR>‘even the breadth of a line, as much<BR>as a line’; R. 1. 17; so क्षणमात्र, नि<BR>मिषमात्रं ‘the space of an instant;’<BR>शतमात्र ‘a hundred in number’; so<BR>गजमात्र ‘as high or big as an<BR>elephant’; तालम त्र, यवमात्र &c.<BR>--2 The<BR>full measure of anything, the whole<BR>or entire class of things, totality;<BR>जीवमात्र or प्राणिमात्रं ‘the entire<BR>class of living beings’; मनुष्यमात्रो<BR>मर्त्यः ‘every man is mortal’;<BR>वस्तुमात्रपक्षकोऽनुप पंहारी (हेतुः) Tarka K.;<BR>मानुषमात्रदुष्करं कर्मानुष्ठितं Dk.<BR>--3 The<BR>simple measure of anything, the<BR>one thing and no more, often<BR>translateable by ‘mere,’ ‘only’, ‘even’;<BR>जातिमात्रेण H. 1. 58 ‘by mere caste’;<BR>टिट्टिभमात्रेण समुद्रो व्याकुलीकृतः 2. 149.<BR>‘by a mere wag-tail’, वाचामात्रेण<BR>जाप्यसे Ś. 2 ‘merely by words’; so<BR>अर्थमात्रं, संमानमात्रं Pt. 1. 83; used<BR>with past participles मात्र may be<BR>translated by ‘as soon as’, ‘no<BR>sooner than’, ‘just’; विद्धमात्रः<BR>R. 5. 51 ‘as soon as pierced’, ‘when just<BR>pierced’; भुक्तामात्रे ‘just after eating’;<BR>प्रविष्टमात्र एव तत्रमवति Ś. 3. &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्रा
मात्रा<BR>1 A measure; see मात्रं above.<BR>--2 A standard of measure, standard,<BR>rule.<BR>--3 The correct measure.<BR>--4 A<BR>unit of measure, a foot.<BR>--5 A moment.<BR>--6 A particle, an atom.<BR>--7 A part,<BR>portion: सुरेंद्रमात्राश्रितगौरवत्वात्<BR>R. 3. 11.<BR>--8 A small portion, a little,<BR>trifle, a little quantity, a small<BR>measure only, see मात्र (3).<BR>--9 Account,<BR>consideration; राजेति कियती मात्रा<BR>Pt. 1. 40 ‘of what account or<BR>consideration is a king’, i. e. I hold him<BR>of no account; कायस्थ इति लघ्वी मात्रा<BR>Mu. 1.<BR>--10 Money, wealth; property.<BR>शून्यमठिकायां मात्राः समवतार्य Dk.;<BR>नक्तदिनं कक्षांतरात्तां मात्रां न मुंचति<BR>Pt. 1; कथमस्यार्थमात्रा हर्तव्या ibid.<BR>--11<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">Page0858-c+ 56</a>]<BR>(In prosody) A prosodial or<BR>syllabic instant, the time required to<BR>pronounce a short vowel.<BR>--12 An<BR>element.<BR>--13 The material world,<BR>matter.<BR>--14 The upper part of the<BR>Nāgarī characters.<BR>--15 An ear-ring.<BR>--16 An ornament; a jewel.<BR>--17 A<BR>measure of time (in music).<BR>--18<BR>Function of the organs (इंद्रियवृत्ति).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्वं half of a prosodial<BR>instant.<BR>--च्युतकं a kind of artificial<BR>composition, getting out another<BR>meaning by the omission of a<BR>Mātrā; e. g. मूलस्यितिपधः कुर्वन् पात्रैर्जष्टो<BR>गताक्षरैः । विटसेव्यः कुलीनस्य तिष्ठतः<BR>पथिकस्य सः ॥ (where the omission of the<BR>Mātrā in विट makes the sense<BR>applicable to a वट).<BR>--छंदस्, --वृत्तं a<BR>metre regulated by the number of<BR>prosodial instants it contains, e. g.<BR>the Āryā.<BR>--भस्त्रा a money-bag.<BR>--वस्तिः an oily clyster.<BR>--संगः<BR>attachment to or regard for<BR>household possessions or property;<BR>Ms. 6. 57.<BR>--समकः N. of a class of<BR>metres, see App. {1}<BR>--स्पंर्शः material<BR>contact, contact with material<BR>elements; Bg. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्रिका
मात्रिका A syllable or prosodial<BR>instant (= मात्रा above.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर
मात्सर a. (री f.), मात्सरिक a.<BR>(की f.) Jealous, envious,<BR>malicious, spiteful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्सर्यं|मात्सर्य|मात्सर्य्य|मात्सर्य्यं
मात्सर्यं<BR>1 Envy, jealousy, spite,<BR>malice; अहो वस्तुनि मात्सर्यं<BR>Ks. 21. 49; Ki. 3. 53.<BR>--2 Displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मात्स्यिकः|मात्स्यिक
मात्स्यिकः A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथः|माथ
माथः [मथ्-घञ्]<BR>1 Stirring,<BR>churning, shaking about.<BR>--2 Killing,<BR>destruction.<BR>--3 A way, road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माथुर|माथुरः
माथुर a. (री f.) [मथुरायां भवो<BR>मथुराया आगतो वा अण्]<BR>1 Coming from<BR>Mathurā.<BR>--2 Produced in Mathurā.<BR>--3 Dwelling in Mathurā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादः|माद
मादः [मद्-घञ्]<BR>1 Intoxication,<BR>drunkenness.<BR>--2 Joy, delight.<BR>--3<BR>Pride, arrogance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादक|मादकः
मादक a. (दिका f.) [मद्-णिच् ण्वुत्]<BR>1 Intoxicating, maddening,<BR>stupefying.<BR>--2 Gladdening.<BR>--कः A<BR>gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादन|मादनं|मादनः
मादन a. (नी f.) [मद् णिच् ल्यु-ल्युट्<BR>वा] Intoxicating &c.; see मादक.<BR>--नः<BR>1 The god of love.<BR>--2 The<BR>thornapple.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Intoxication.<BR>--2<BR>Delighting, exhilaration.<BR>--3 Cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0858-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादनीयं|मादनीय
मादनीयं An intoxicating drink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मादृक्ष
मादृक्ष a. (क्षी f.), म दृश् a., मादृश<BR>a. (शी f.) Like-me, resembling me;<BR>प्रवृत्तिसाराः खलु माट्टशां गिरः<BR>Ki. 1. 25; U. 2; उपचारो नैव कल्प्य इति तु<BR>मादृशाः R. G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रकः|माद्रक
माद्रकः A prince of the Madras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रवती
माद्रवती N. of the second wife of<BR>Pāṇḍu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्री
माद्री N. of the second wife of<BR>Pāṇḍu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नंदनः an epithet<BR>of Nakula and Sahadeva.<BR>--पतिः an<BR>epithet of Pāṇḍu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माद्रेयः|माद्रेय
माद्रेयः An epithet of Nakula and<BR>Sahadeva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधव|माधवः
माधव a. (वी f.) [मधु-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Honey-like sweet.<BR>--2 Made of honey.<BR>--3 Vernal, relating to the spring;<BR>सावज्ञेव मुखप्रसाधनविधौ श्रीमाधवी<BR>योषितां M. 3. 5.<BR>--4 Relating to the<BR>descendants of Madhu.<BR>--वः [माया लक्ष्म्या<BR>धवः]<BR>1 N. of Kṛṣṇa;<BR>राधामाधवयोर्जयंति यमुनाकूले रहःकेलयः Gīt. 1;<BR>माधवे मा कुरु मानिनि मानमये 9.<BR>--2 he<BR>spring season, a friend of Cupid;<BR>स्मर पर्युत्सुक एष माधवः Ku. 4. 28;<BR>म माधवेनाभिमतेन सख्या (अनुप्रयातः)<BR>3. 23.<BR>--3 The month called Vaiśākha;<BR>भास्करस्य मधुमाधवाविव R. 11. 7.<BR>--4<BR>N. of Indra.<BR>--5 N. of Paraśurāma.<BR>--6 N. of the Yādavas (pl.);<BR>Śi. 16 52.<BR>--7 N. of a celebrated author,<BR>son of Māyaṇa and brother of<BR>Sāyaṇa and Bhoganātha, and<BR>supposed to have lived in the<BR>fifteenth century. He was a very<BR>reputed scholar, numerous important<BR>works being ascribed to him; he<BR>and Sāyaṇa are supposed to have<BR>jointly written the commentary on<BR>the Ṛgveda; श्रुतिस्मृतिसदाचारपालको<BR>माधवो बुध । स्मार्तं व्याख्याय सर्वार्थं<BR>द्विज र्थ श्रोत उद्यतः । J. N. V.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उचित a kind of perfume (कक्कंल)<BR>--वल्ली = माधवी q. v.<BR>--श्री vernal<BR>beauty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवकः|माधवक
माधवकः A kind of intoxicating<BR>liquor (produced from honey).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधविका
माधविका N. of a creeper; माधवि<BR>कापरिमलललिते Gīt {1}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवी
माधवी<BR>1 Candied sugar.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of drink made from honey.<BR>--3 The spring-creeper (वासंती), with<BR>white fragrant flowers: पत्राणामिव<BR>शोषणेन मरुता स्पृष्टा लता माधवी<BR>Ś. 3. 10; Me. 78.<BR>--4 The sacred basil.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">Page0859-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--5 A procuress, bawd.<BR>--6 Affluence<BR>in cattle<BR>--Comp.<BR>--लता the spring<BR>creeper.<BR>--वनं a grove of Mādhavī<BR>creepers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधवीय
माधवीय a. Relating to Mādhava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुकर
माधुकर a. (री f.) [मधुकर-अण्]<BR>Relating to or resembling a bee;<BR>as in माधुकरी वृत्ति.<BR>--री<BR>1 Collecting<BR>alms by begging from door to door,<BR>as a bee collects honey by moving<BR>from flower to flower.<BR>--2 Alms<BR>obtained from five different places.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुपर्किक
माधुपर्किक a. (की f.) Offered<BR>to a guest as a token of respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुरं|माधुर
माधुरं [मधुर-अण्] Tho flower<BR>of the Mallikā creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुरी
माधुरी<BR>1 Sweetness, sweet or<BR>savoury taste; वदने तव यत्र माधुरी सा<BR>Bv. 2. 161:<BR>कामालसस्वर्वामाधरमाधुरीमधरयन् वाचां विपाको मम 4. 42,<BR>37, 43; वाङ्माधुरीविरसीकृतकलकंठा<BR>Dk.<BR>--2 Spirituous liquor.<BR>--3<BR>Mead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधुर्यं|माधुर्य|माधुर्य्य|माधुर्य्यं
माधुर्यं [मधुरस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Sweetness. pleasantness; माधुर्यपीष्टे<BR>हरिणान् ग्रहीतुं R. 18. 13, Bh. 2. 6.<BR>--2 Attractive beauty. exquisite<BR>beauty; रूपं किमप्यनिर्वाच्य<BR>तनोर्माधुर्यमुच्यते.<BR>--3 (In Rhet.)<BR>Sweetness, one of the three (accord<BR>ing to Mammaṭa) chief Guṇas<BR>in poetic compositions;<BR>चितद्रवीभावमयो ह्लादो माधुर्यपुच्यते S. D. 606:<BR>see K. P. 8 also.<BR>--4 Kindness,<BR>amiability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माधूक
माधूक a. Sweet-speaking,<BR>amiable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्य
माध्य a. [मध्य आण्] Central,<BR>middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यंदिन|माध्यन्दिन|माध्यन्दिनं|माध्यंदिनः
माध्यंदिन a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Midday,<BR>meridional.<BR>--2 Middle, central<BR>--नः<BR>N. of a branch of Vājasaneyins.<BR>--नं A branch of the शुक्ल or white<BR>Yajurveda (followed by the<BR>Mādhyandinas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यम|माध्यमं
माध्यम a. (मी f.) [मध्यम-अण्] Be<BR>longing to the middle portion,<BR>central, middle, middlemost.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यमक
माध्यमक a. (मिका f.) माध्यमिक a.<BR>(की f.) Middle, central.<BR>--काः (m.<BR>pl.) N. of a people or their country<BR>in the central part of India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्य
माध्यस्य a. Indifferent, impartial,<BR>neutral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थं|माध्यस्थ
माध्यस्थं, माध्यस्थ्यं<BR>1 Impartiality.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-c" target="_blank">Page0859-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 Indifference, unconcern;<BR>अभ्यर्थनाभंगभयेन साधुर्माध्यस्थ्यमिष्टेऽप्यवलंबतेर्थे<BR>Ku. 1. 52.<BR>--3 Intercession,<BR>mediation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्यस्थ्यं|माध्यस्थ्य
माध्यस्थं, माध्यस्थ्यं<BR>1 Impartiality.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-c" target="_blank">Page0859-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 Indifference, unconcern;<BR>अभ्यर्थनाभंगभयेन साधुर्माध्यस्थ्यमिष्टेऽप्यवलंबतेर्थे<BR>Ku. 1. 52.<BR>--3 Intercession,<BR>mediation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्याह्निक
माध्याह्निक a. (की f.) Belonging<BR>to noon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्व|माध्वः
माध्व a. (ध्वी f.) Sweet.<BR>--ध्वः A<BR>follower of Madhva.<BR>--ध्वी<BR>1 A kind<BR>of liquor (made from honey).<BR>--2<BR>The creeper called Mādhavī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वकं|माध्वक
माध्वकं An intoxicating drink<BR>prepared from honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्विकः|माध्विक
माध्विकः A person who collects<BR>honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माध्वीकं|माध्वीक
माध्वीकं [मधुना मधूकपुऽपेण निर्वृत्तं ईकक्]<BR>1 A kind of spirituous liquor,<BR>distilled from the flowers of the tree<BR>called Madhūka; चचाम मधु माध्वीकं<BR>Bk. 14. 94.<BR>--2 Wine distilled from<BR>grapes; साध्वी माध्वीक चिंता न भवति<BR>भवतः Gīt. 12 (= मधो Com.).<BR>--3 A<BR>grape.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फलं a kind of<BR>cocoa-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्
मान् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (मीमांसते = desid. of<BR>मन् q. v.). {vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U. = Caus.<BR>of मन् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानः|मान|मानं
मानः [मन्-घञ्]<BR>1 Respect, honour,<BR>regard, respectful consideration;<BR>दारिद्र्यस्य परा मूर्तिर्यन्मानद्रविणाल्पता<BR>Pt. 2. 159: Bg. 6. 7; so मानधन &c.<BR>--2<BR>Pride (in a good sense),<BR>self-reliance, self respect; जन्मिनो मानहीनस्य<BR>तृणस्य च समा गतिः Pt. 1. 106;<BR>R. 16. 81.<BR>--3 Haughtiness, pride,<BR>conceit, self-confidence.<BR>--4 A<BR>wounded sense of honour.<BR>--5<BR>Jealous anger, anger excited by jealousy<BR>(especially in women); anger in<BR>general. मुच मयि मानमनिदानं Gīt. 10;<BR>माधवे मा कुरु मानिनि मानमये 9; त्यजत<BR>मानमलं बत विग्रहैः R. 9. 47;<BR>Śi. 9. 84; Bv. 2. 56.<BR>--6 Opinion,<BR>conception.<BR>--7 Ved. Object, purpose.<BR>--नं<BR>[मा-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Measuring.<BR>--2 A<BR>measure, standard<BR>--3 Dimension,<BR>computation.<BR>--4 A standard of measure,<BR>measuring-rod, rule.<BR>--5 Proof,<BR>authority, means of proof or<BR>demonstration: येऽमी माधुर्यौजः प्रमादा<BR>रसमात्रवर्मतयोक्तास्तपां रसधर्मत्वे किं मानं<BR>R. G.; मानाभावात् (frequently occurring<BR>in controversial language) Pad. D. 4. 3.<BR>--6 Likeness, resemblance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आसक a. given to pride, haughty,<BR>proud.<BR>--उत्साहः energy arising from<BR>self-confidence; Pt. 1. 226.<BR>--उन्नतिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-a" target="_blank">Page0860-a+ 57</a>]<BR>f. great respect or honour:<BR>Bh. 2. 23.<BR>--उन्मादः infatuation of pride.<BR>--कलहः, --कलिः a quarrel caused by<BR>jealous anger.<BR>--क्षितिः f.,<BR>--भंगः, --हानिः<BR>f. injury to reputation or honour,<BR>humiliation, mortification, insult,<BR>indignity.<BR>--ग्रथिः injury to honour<BR>or pride.<BR>--द a. {1} showing respect.<BR>{2} proud. {3} destroying pride. {4}<BR>a giver of honour (a mode of<BR>addressing lovers &c.).<BR>--(दः) a mystical<BR>name for the letter आ.<BR>--(दा) N. of<BR>the second digit of the moon.<BR>--दंडः<BR>a measuring-rod; स्थितः पृथिव्या इव<BR>मानदंडः Ku. 1. 1.<BR>--धत a. rich in<BR>honour; महौजसो मानधना धनार्चिताः<BR>Ki. 1. 19;<BR>--धानिका a cucumber.<BR>--परिखंडनं mortification, humiliation.<BR>--भंग see मानक्षति.<BR>--भृत्, पर a.<BR>possessing pride, extremely proud; प्रथमे<BR>मानभृतां न वृष्णयः Ki. 2. 44.<BR>--महत् a.<BR>rich or great in pride, greatly proud;<BR>किं जीर्णं तृणमत्ति मानमहतामग्रेसरः केसरी<BR>Bh. 2. 29.<BR>--योगः the correct mode<BR>of measuring or weighing;<BR>Ms. 9. 330.<BR>--रंध्रा a sort of clepsydra, a<BR>perforated water-vessel, which,<BR>placed in water and gradually filling,<BR>serves to measure time.<BR>--वर्जित a.<BR>{1} disgraced, dishonoured. {2}<BR>humble, lowly. {3} slanderous, libellous.<BR>--सूत्रं {1} a measuring-cord. {2} a<BR>chain (of gold &c.) worn round the<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0859-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानयितृ
मानयितृ m. One who honours,<BR>honourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माननं|मानन
माननं --ना<BR>1 Honouring, respecting.<BR>--2 Killing; Śi. 16. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानना
माननं --ना<BR>1 Honouring, respecting.<BR>--2 Killing; Śi. 16. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माननीय|माननीयं
माननीय a. Fit to be honoured,<BR>worthy of honour, deserving to be<BR>honoured (with gen); मेनां मुनीनामपि<BR>माननीयां Ku. 1. 18 R. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवत्|मानवन्त्
मानवत् a. Proud, arrogant,<BR>haughty or high-spirited.<BR>--ती A<BR>haughty or high-spirited woman<BR>angry through jealous pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानित
मानित p. p. [मन्-णिच् क्त]<BR>Honoured, respected, esteemed.<BR>--तं<BR>Showing honour or respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिन्
मानिन् a. [मान-इनि, मन्-णिनि वा]<BR>1 Fancying, considering, regarding<BR>(at the end of comp.); as in<BR>पंडितमानिन्.<BR>--2 Honouring, respecting,<BR>(at the end of comp.)<BR>--3 Haughty,<BR>proud, possessed of self-respect;<BR>पराभवोऽप्युत्सव एव मानिनां Ki. 1. 41;<BR>परवृद्धिमत्सरि मनो हि मानिनां<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-b" target="_blank">Page0860-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Śi. 15. 1.<BR>--4 Entitled to respect, highly<BR>honoured; Bk. 19. 24.<BR>--5<BR>Disdainful, angry, sulky.<BR>--6 Being<BR>regarded or considered as. --m. A<BR>lion.<BR>--नी<BR>1 A woman possessed of<BR>self-respect, a strong-minded,<BR>resolute, or proud woman, (in a good<BR>sense): चतुर्दिगीशानवमत्य मानिनी<BR>Ku. 5. 53; R. 13. 38.<BR>--2 An angry woman,<BR>or one offended with her husband<BR>(through jealous pride); माधवे<BR>मा कुरु मानिनि मानमये Gīt. 9;<BR>Ki. 9. 36.<BR>--3 A kind of odoriferous<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिता
मानिता --त्वं<BR>1 Haughtiness, pride.<BR>--2 Honouring, respect.<BR>--3 Being<BR>respected or honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानित्वं|मानित्व
मानिता --त्वं<BR>1 Haughtiness, pride.<BR>--2 Honouring, respect.<BR>--3 Being<BR>respected or honoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानःशिल
मानःशिल a. Consisting of red<BR>arsenic (मनःशिला).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव|मानवः
मानव a. (वी f.) [मनोरपत्यं अण्]<BR>1 Relating to or descended from<BR>Manu; मानवस्य राजर्षिवंशस्य<BR>प्रसवितारं सवितारं U. 3; Ms. 12. 107.<BR>--2<BR>Human.<BR>--वः<BR>1 A man, human<BR>being; मनोर्वंशो मानवानां ततोयं<BR>प्रथिनोऽभवत् । ब्रह्मक्षत्रादयस्तस्मान्मनोर्जातास्तु<BR>मानवाः Mb.; Ms. 2. 9; 5. 35.<BR>--2<BR>A lad, boy.<BR>--3 Mankind (pl.).<BR>--4<BR>The subjects of a king (pl.).<BR>--वी<BR>A woman.<BR>--वं A particular fine.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इंद्रः, --देवः --पतिः a lord of<BR>men, king, sovereign; R. 14. 32.<BR>--धर्मशास्त्रं the institutes of Manu.<BR>--राक्षसः a demon or fiend in the<BR>form of a man; तेऽमी मानवराक्षसाः<BR>परहितं स्वार्थाय निघ्नंति ये Bh. 2. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानवीय
मानवीय a. Descended or derived<BR>from Manu.<BR>--यं A particular fine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानव्यं|मानव्य
मानव्यं A number of boys or<BR>youths (माणव्यं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस|मानसं|मानसः
मानस a. (सी f.) [मन एव, मनस<BR>इदं वा अण्]<BR>1 Pertaining to the<BR>mind, mental, spiritual (opp. शारीर).<BR>--2 Produced from the mind,<BR>sprung at will; ब्रह्मणो मानसपुत्राः;<BR>किं मानसी सृष्टिः Ś. 4; Ku. 1. 18;<BR>Bg. 10. 6.<BR>--3 Only to be conceived<BR>in the mind, conceivable.<BR>--4 Tacit,<BR>implied.<BR>--5 Dwelling on the lake<BR>Mānasa.<BR>--सः A form of Viṣṇu.<BR>--सं<BR>1 The mind, heart, soul; सपदि<BR>मदनानलो दहति मम मानसं Gīt. 10;<BR>अपि च मानसमंबुनिधिः Bv. 1. 113;<BR>मानसं विषयैर्विना (भाति) 116.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a sacred lake on the mountain<BR>Kailāsa; (कैलासशिखरे राम मनसा निर्मितं<BR>सरः । ब्रह्मणा प्रागिदं यस्मात्तदभून्मानसं सरः ॥<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">Page0860-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Rām.; it is said to be the native<BR>place of swans, who are described<BR>as migrating to its shores every<BR>year at the commencement of the<BR>breeding season or the monsoons;<BR>मेघश्यामा दिशो दृष्ट्वा मानसोत्सुकचेतसां ।<BR>कूजितं राजहंसानां नेदं नूपुरशिंजितं<BR>V. 4. 14, 15; यस्यास्तोये कृतवसतयो मानसं<BR>संनिकृष्टं नाध्यास्यंति व्यपगतशुच त्वामपि प्रेक्ष्य<BR>हंसः Me. 76; see Me. 11;<BR>Ghaṭ. 9 also); R. 6. 26; Me. 62.<BR>Bv. 1. 3.<BR>--3 (In law) Tacit or implied<BR>consent.<BR>--4 A kind of salt.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आलयः a swan, goose.<BR>--उत्क a.<BR>eager to go to Mānasa; Me. 11.<BR>--ओकस्, --चारिन् m. a swan.<BR>--जन्मन् m. {1} the god of love. {2}<BR>a swan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानसिक|मानसिकं|मानसिकः
मानसिक a. (की f.) Mental,<BR>spiritual.<BR>--कः An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानिका
मानिका<BR>1 A kind of spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>--2 A kind of weight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष|मानुषः
मानुष a. (षी f.) [मनोरयं अण्<BR>सुक् च]<BR>1 Human; मानुषी तनुः, मानुषी<BR>वाक् &c.; R. 1. 60, 16. 22;<BR>Bg. 4. 12; 9. 11; Ms. 4. 124.<BR>--2<BR>Humane, kind.<BR>--षः<BR>1 A man,<BR>human being.<BR>--2 An epithet of the<BR>three signs of the zodiac, Gemini,<BR>Virgo, and Libra.<BR>--षी<BR>1 A woman.<BR>--2 A branch of medicine,<BR>administering drugs and herbs.<BR>--षं<BR>1<BR>Humanity.<BR>--2 Human effort or<BR>action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषक
मानुषक a. (की f.) Human,<BR>mortal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषता
मानुषता --त्वं<BR>1 Humanity.<BR>--2 State<BR>or condition of man, human nature;<BR>मानुषतासुलभो लघिमा K.<BR>--3 Manhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुषत्वं|मानुषत्व
मानुषता --त्वं<BR>1 Humanity.<BR>--2 State<BR>or condition of man, human nature;<BR>मानुषतासुलभो लघिमा K.<BR>--3 Manhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्यं|मानुष्य
मानुष्यं, मानुष्यकं<BR>1 Human nature,<BR>humanity; किं पुनर्मानुष्यं विडंब्यते<BR>V. 2; यावन्मानुष्यके शक्यमुपपादयितुं<BR>तावत्सर्वमुपपाद्यतां K. 62.<BR>--2 A mortal<BR>frame, human body; प्राप्यापि<BR>मानुष्यकमनेकसाधारणीभव Dk.<BR>--3 Mankind,<BR>the race of human beings.<BR>--4 A<BR>collection of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानुष्यकं|मानुष्यक
मानुष्यं, मानुष्यकं<BR>1 Human nature,<BR>humanity; किं पुनर्मानुष्यं विडंब्यते<BR>V. 2; यावन्मानुष्यके शक्यमुपपादयितुं<BR>तावत्सर्वमुपपाद्यतां K. 62.<BR>--2 A mortal<BR>frame, human body; प्राप्यापि<BR>मानुष्यकमनेकसाधारणीभव Dk.<BR>--3 Mankind,<BR>the race of human beings.<BR>--4 A<BR>collection of men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानोज्ञकं|मानोज्ञक
मानोज्ञकं Beauty, loveliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांत्रिकः|मान्त्रिक|मांत्रिक|मान्त्रिकः
मांत्रिकः One who is conversant<BR>with charms or spells, a conjurer,<BR>sorcerer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांथ्|मान्थ्
मांथ् {c1c} P. (मांथति) To hurt, in<BR>jure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांथर्यं|मान्थर्य|मांथर्य
मांथर्यं<BR>1 Slowness, dulness,<BR>tardiness.<BR>--2 Weakness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांदारः|मान्दार|मांदार|मान्दारः
मांदारः, मांदारवः A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांदारवः|मान्दारव|मांदारव|मान्दारवः
मांदारः, मांदारवः A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0860-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांद्यं|मान्द्य|मांद्य|मान्द्यं
मांद्यं [मंद-ष्यञ्]<BR>1 Dulness,<BR>laziness, slowness,<BR>--2 Stupidity.<BR>--3<BR>Weakness, feeble state; अग्निमांद्यं.<BR>--4 Apathy.<BR>--5 Sickness, illness,<BR>indisposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मांधातृ|मान्धातृ
मांधातृ m. N. of a king of the<BR>solar race, son of Yuvanāśva<BR>(being born from his own belly). As<BR>soon as he came out of the belly,<BR>the sages said ‘कं एष धास्यति’;<BR>whereupon Indra came down and said<BR>‘मां धास्यति’; the boy was, therefore,<BR>called Māndhātṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्मथ
मान्मथ a. (थी f.) [मन्मथ-अण्]<BR>Relating to or caused by love;<BR>आचार्यकंविजयि मान्मथमाविरासीत् Māl. 1. 16;<BR>2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मान्य|मान्यः
मान्य pot. p. [मान् अर्चायां कर्मणि<BR>ण्यत्]<BR>1 To be revered or respected;<BR>अहमपि तव मान्या हेतुभिस्तैश्च तैश्च<BR>Māl. 6. 26.<BR>--2 Respectable, honourable,<BR>venerable: R. 2. 44; Y. 1. 111.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापनं|मापन|मापनः
मापनं --ना<BR>1 Measuring.<BR>--2<BR>Forming, making.<BR>--नः A balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापना
मापनं --ना<BR>1 Measuring.<BR>--2<BR>Forming, making.<BR>--नः A balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मापत्यः|मापत्य
मापत्यः The god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माम
माम a. (मी f.)<BR>1 My, mine.<BR>--2<BR>Uncle (used in voc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामक|मामकं|मामकः
मामक a. (मिका f.)<BR>1 My, mine,<BR>belonging to my side; मामकाः<BR>पांडवाश्चैव किमकुर्वत संजय Bg. 1. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Selfish, covetous, greedy.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>miser.<BR>--2 A maternal uncle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मामकीन|मामकीनं
मामकीन a. My, mine: यो<BR>मामकीनस्य मनसो द्वितीयं निबंधनं Māl. 2;<BR>सा मामकीनकवितेव मनोभिरामा<BR>Bv. 3. 6, 2. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माय|मायः
माय a. Possessing magical power.<BR>--यः<BR>1 A conjurer, juggler.<BR>--2 A<BR>demon, an evil spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माया
माया [मा-यः बा˚ नेत्वम्]<BR>1 Deceit,<BR>fraud, trick, trickery; a device, an<BR>artifice; Pt. 1. 359.<BR>--2 Jugglery,<BR>witchcraft, enchantment, an illusion<BR>of magic; स्वप्नो नु माया नु मतिभ्रमो नु<BR>Ś. 6. 9.<BR>--3 (Hence) An unreal or<BR>illusory image, a phantom, illusion,<BR>unreal apparition; मायां मयोद्भाव्य<BR>परीक्षितोऽसि R. 2. 62; विकृतिः किन्नु<BR>भवेदियं नु माया Ki. 13. 4, R. 12. 74;<BR>oft. as the first member of comp.<BR>in the sense of ‘false’, ‘phantom’,<BR>‘illusory’; e. g. मायावचनं false words;<BR>मायामृग &c.<BR>--4 A political trick or<BR>artifice, diplomatic feat.<BR>--5 (In<BR>Vedānta phil.) Unreality, the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-b" target="_blank">Page0861-b+ 57</a>]<BR>illusion by virtue of which one<BR>considers the unreal universe as really<BR>existent and as distinct from the<BR>Supreme Spirit.<BR>--6 (In Sān. phil.)<BR>The Pradhāna or Prakṛti.<BR>--7<BR>Wickedness.<BR>--8 Pity, compassion.<BR>--9 N. of the mother of Buddha.<BR>--10 Ved. Extraordinary power,<BR>wisdom (प्रज्ञा).<BR>--11 (With Śaivas)<BR>One of the four snares (पाश) which<BR>entangle the soul.<BR>--12 N. of the<BR>city Gayā.<BR>--13 N. of Lakṣmī.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचर a. acting<BR>deceitfully.<BR>--आत्मक a. false, illusory.<BR>--उपजीविन् a. living by fraud;<BR>Pt. 1. 288.<BR>--कारः, --कृत्, --जीविन् m. a<BR>conjurer, juggler.<BR>--चण a. {1} noted<BR>for juggling. {2} deceptive.<BR>--दः a<BR>crocodile.<BR>--देवी N. of the mother<BR>of Buddha. ˚सुतः Buddha.<BR>--धर a.<BR>deceitful, illusive.<BR>--पटु a. skilled<BR>in deception, fraudulent, deceitful.<BR>--प्रयोगः {1} deceitfulness,<BR>employment of tricks or fraud; Pt. 1. 190.<BR>{2} employment of magic.<BR>--फलं a<BR>gall nut.<BR>--मृगः a phantom deer, an<BR>illusory or false deer.<BR>--यंत्रं an<BR>enchantment.<BR>--योगः employment of<BR>magic.<BR>--योधिन् a. fighting<BR>deceitfully.<BR>--वचनं false or deceitful<BR>words.<BR>--वादः the doctrine of<BR>illusion, (a term applied to Buddhism).<BR>--विद् a. skilled in deception or<BR>magical arts.<BR>--सुतः an epithet of<BR>Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायामय
मायामय a. (यी f.)<BR>1 Illusive,<BR>illusory, deceitful.<BR>--2 False, unreal.<BR>--3 Magical.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायावत्|मायावन्त्
मायावत् a.<BR>1 Deceitful, fraudulent.<BR>--2 Illusory, unreal, deceptive.<BR>--3 Skilled in magical arts,<BR>employing magical powers. --m. An<BR>epithet of Kaṃsa.<BR>--ती N. of the wife<BR>of Pradyumna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायाविन्
मायाविन् a. [माया-अस्त्यर्थे विनि]<BR>1<BR>Using deceit or tricks, employing<BR>stratagems, deceitful, fraudulent;<BR>व्रजंति ते मूढधियः पराभवं भवंति मायाविषु<BR>ये न मायिनः Ki. 1. 30; R. 10. 45.<BR>--2 Skilled in magic.<BR>--3 Unreal,<BR>illusory. --m.<BR>1 A magician, conjurer.<BR>--2 A cat. --n. A gall-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिक|मायिकं|मायिकः
मायिक a. [माया-ठन्]<BR>1 Deceitful,<BR>fraudulent.<BR>--2 Illusory, unreal.<BR>--कः<BR>A juggler.<BR>--कं A gall-unt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायिन्
मायिन् [माय-इनि] See मायाविन्.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A conjurer.<BR>--2 A rogue,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">Page0861-c+ 56</a>]<BR>cheat.<BR>--3 A deceitful or treacherous<BR>person; Ku. 2. 46.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--5 Of Kāma.<BR>--6 Of Agni.<BR>--7<BR>Śiva. --n. Magic, magical art.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायातिः|मायाति
मायातिः The sacrifice to men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायुः|मायु
मायुः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 Bile, bilious<BR>humour; (n. also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूर|मायूरं
मायूर a. (री f.) [मयूर-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Belonging to or arising from a peacock;<BR>मायूरी मदयति मार्जना मनांसि M. 1. 21.<BR>--2 Made of the feathers of a<BR>peacock.<BR>--3 Drawn by a peacock<BR>(as a car).<BR>--4 Dear to a peacock.<BR>--रं A flock of peacocks.<BR>--री N. of<BR>a plant (अजमोदा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरकः|मायूरक
मायूरकः, --मायूरिकः A<BR>peacockcatcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मायूरिकः|मायूरिक
मायूरकः, --मायूरिकः A<BR>peacockcatcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारः|मार
मारः [मृ-घञ्]<BR>1 Killing,<BR>slaughter, slaying; अशेषप्राणिनामासीदमारो<BR>दश वत्सरान् Rāj. T. 5. 64.<BR>--2 An<BR>obstacle, hinderance, opposition.<BR>--3<BR>The god of love; श्यामात्मा कुटिलः<BR>करोतु कब रीभारोपि मारोद्यमं Gīt. 3;<BR>(where मार primarily means<BR>‘killing’); Nāg. 1. 1.<BR>--4 Love,<BR>passion.<BR>--5 The thorn-apple (धत्तूर).<BR>--6 An evil one, a destroyer;<BR>(according to Buddhists).<BR>--7 Death.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंक a. ‘marked by love’,<BR>displaying signs of love; मारांके<BR>रतिकेलिसंकुलरणारंभे Gīt. 12.<BR>--अभिभूः (भुः ?)<BR>an epithet of a Buddha.<BR>--अरिः,<BR>--रिपुः Śiva.<BR>--आत्मक a. murderous;<BR>कथं मारात्मके त्वयि विश्वासः कर्तव्यः<BR>H. 1.<BR>--जित् m. an epithet of Śiva. {2}<BR>of a Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारक|मारकः
मारक a. [मृ-णिच् ण्वुल्] (At the<BR>end of comp.) Killing, destroying,<BR>slaying.<BR>--कः<BR>1 Any pestilential<BR>disease, plague, epidemic.<BR>--2 The god of<BR>love.<BR>--3 A murderer, destroyer in<BR>general.<BR>--4 A hawk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारणं|मारण
मारणं [मृ-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>1 Killing, slaying,<BR>slaughter, destruction;<BR>पशुमारणकर्मदारुणः Ś. 6. 1.<BR>--2 A magical ceremony<BR>performed for the purpose of<BR>destroying an enemy.<BR>--3 Calcination.<BR>--4 A kind of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिः|मारि
मारिः f. [मृ-णिच्-इनि]<BR>1 A<BR>pestilence, plague.<BR>--2 Killing, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिका
मारिका A plague, pestilence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारित|मारितः
मारित p. p.<BR>1 Slain, killed.<BR>--2<BR>Destroyed, ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिन्
मारिन् a.<BR>1 Dying.<BR>--2 Killing,<BR>slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारी
मारी<BR>1 Plague, pestilence, an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-a" target="_blank">Page0862-a+ 54</a>]<BR>epidemic.<BR>--2 Pestilence personified<BR>(the goddess presiding over plagues<BR>and identified with Durgā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0861-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारकत
मारकत a. (ती f.) Belonging to<BR>an emerald; काचः कांचनसंसर्गाद्धत्ते<BR>मारकतीं द्युतिं H. Pr. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारव
मारव a. (वी f.) Desert, belonging<BR>to a wilderness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिच
मारिच a. (ची f.) Made of<BR>pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिचिक|मारिचिकं
मारिचिक a. Peppered, seasoned<BR>with pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारिषः|मारिष
मारिषः A respectable, worthy or<BR>venerable man, (used in dramas in<BR>the voc. as a respectful mode of<BR>address by the Sūtradhāra to one of<BR>the principal actors; see U. 1;<BR>Māl. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारीच|मारीचः
मारीच a. (ची f.) Belonging to<BR>or composed by Marīci.<BR>--चः<BR>1 N.<BR>of a demon, son of Sunda and<BR>Tāḍakā. He assumed the form of<BR>a golden deer, and thus enticed<BR>Rāma to a considerable distance<BR>from Sītā, so that Rāvaṇa found a<BR>good opportunity to carry her off.<BR>--2 A large or royal elephant.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of plant.<BR>--4 N. of the sage<BR>Kaśyapa; Ś. 7. 9.<BR>--5 A sacrificing<BR>priest.<BR>--ची N. of the mother of<BR>Śākyamuni.<BR>--चं A collection of<BR>pepper shrubs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुंडः|मारुण्ड|मारुंड|मारुण्डः
मारुंडः<BR>1 A serpent's egg.<BR>--2<BR>Cow-dung.<BR>--3 A way, road.<BR>--4 A<BR>place covered with cowdung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुत|मारुतः
मारुत a. (ती f.) [मरुत इदं अण्]<BR>1 Relating to or arising from the<BR>Maruts.<BR>--2 Relating to wind, aerial,<BR>windy.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Wind; R. 2. 12,<BR>34; 4. 55; Ms. 4. 122.<BR>--2 The<BR>god of wind, the deity presiding<BR>over wind.<BR>--3 Breathing.<BR>--4 Vital<BR>air, one of the three essential<BR>humours of the body.<BR>--5 The trunk of<BR>an elephant.<BR>--6 Ved. A son of<BR>the Maruts.<BR>--ती The north-west<BR>quarter.<BR>--तं The lunar<BR>mansion called Svāti.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अशनः a snake.<BR>--आत्मजः, --सुतः, --सूनुः<BR>{1} epithets of Hanumat. {2} of<BR>Bhīma.<BR>--व्रतं ‘penetrating everywhere’,<BR>one of the duties of a king<BR>(who is able to penetrate<BR>everywhere by means of spies); cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-b" target="_blank">Page0862-b+ 56</a>]<BR>प्रविश्य सर्वभूतानि यथा चरति मारुतः । तथा चरैः<BR>प्रवेष्टव्यं व्रतमेतद्धि मारुतं ॥ Ms. 9. 306.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मारुतिः|मारुति
मारुतिः [मरुतोऽपत्यं इञ्]<BR>1 An<BR>epithet of Hanumats; R. 12. 60.<BR>--2<BR>Of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कंडः|मार्कण्ड|मार्कंड|मार्कण्डः
मार्कंडः, मार्कंडेयः [मृकंडोरपत्यं अण्<BR>ढक्] N. of an ancient sage.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुराणं N. of one of the eighteen<BR>Purāṇas (composed by this sage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्कंडेयः|मार्कण्डेय|मार्कंडेय|मार्कण्डेयः
मार्कंडः, मार्कंडेयः [मृकंडोरपत्यं अण्<BR>ढक्] N. of an ancient sage.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुराणं N. of one of the eighteen<BR>Purāṇas (composed by this sage).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ग्
मार्ग् {vI.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (मार्गति,<BR>मार्गयति-ते)<BR>1 To seek, seek for.<BR>--2 To<BR>hunt after, chase.<BR>--3 To strive to<BR>attain, strive after; आत्मोत्कर्षं न मार्गेत<BR>परेषां परिनिंदया । स्वगुणैरेव मार्गेत<BR>विप्रकर्षं पृथग्जनात् Subhāṣ.<BR>--4 To<BR>solicit, beg, ask for; वरं वरेण्यो नृपतेरमा<BR>र्गीत् Bk. 1. 12; Y. 2. 66.<BR>--5 To ask<BR>in marriage.<BR>--6 To seek through,<BR>trace out. {vII.v} {c10c} U. (मार्गयति-ते)<BR>1<BR>To go, move.<BR>--2 To decorate, adorn.<BR>--WITH परि to seek, look out for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गः|मार्ग
मार्गः [मृज्-शुद्धौ, मार्ग्-अन्वेषणे घञ् वा]<BR>1 A way, road, path (fig. also);<BR>अग्निशरणमार्गमादेशय Ś. 5; so<BR>विचारमार्गप्रहितेन चेतसा Ku. 5. 42; R. 2. 72.<BR>U. 3. 37.<BR>--2 A course, passage, the<BR>tract passed over; वायोरिमं परिवहस्य<BR>वदंति मार्गं Ś. 7. 6.<BR>--3 Reach, range;<BR>Ki. 18. 40.<BR>--4 A scar, mark (left<BR>by a wound &c.); R. 4. 48; 14. 4.<BR>--5 The path or course of a planet.<BR>--6 Search, inquiry, investigation.<BR>--7<BR>A canal, channel, passage.<BR>--8 A<BR>means, way.<BR>--9 The right way or<BR>course, proper course; सुमार्ग, अमार्ग.<BR>--10 Mode, manner, method, course;<BR>शांति˚ R. 7. 71.<BR>--11 Style, direction;<BR>इति वैदर्भमार्गस्य प्राणा दश गुणाः स्मृताः<BR>Kāv. 1. 41; वाचां विचित्रमार्गाणां {1}<BR>{9}<BR>--12 Custom, usage, practice;<BR>कुल˚, शास्त्र˚, धर्म˚ &c.<BR>--13<BR>Hunting or tracing out game.<BR>--14 A title<BR>or head in law, ground for litigation.<BR>--15 A high style of acting, dancing,<BR>and singing.<BR>--16 (In dramaturgy)<BR>Hinting or indicating how<BR>anything is to happen.<BR>--17 (In geom.)<BR>A section.<BR>--18 The anus.<BR>--19 Musk.<BR>--20 The constellation called मृगशिरस्.<BR>--21 The month called मार्गशीर्ष.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आगतः a traveller.<BR>--उपदेशकः a guide, leader.<BR>--तोरणं a<BR>triumphal arch erected on a road;<BR>R. 11. 5.<BR>--दर्शकः a guide.<BR>--द्रगः<BR>a city or town on the road.<BR>--धेनुः,<BR>--धेनुकं a measure of distance equal<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">Page0862-c+ 56</a>]<BR>to 4 krośas.<BR>--बंधनं a barricade.<BR>--रक्षकः a road-keeper, guard.<BR>--वटी<BR>an epithet of the tutelary deity of<BR>travellers.<BR>--शोधकः a pioneer.<BR>--स्थ<BR>a. travelling, way-faring.<BR>--हर्म्यं a<BR>palace on a high road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गकः|मार्गक
मार्गकः The month called मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गण|मार्गणं|मार्गणः
मार्गण a. [मार्ग्-ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>1<BR>Seeking, searching or looking out for.<BR>--2<BR>Inquiring.<BR>--3 Asking, begging.<BR>--णं,<BR>--णा<BR>1 Begging, requesting,<BR>soliciting.<BR>--2 Seeking, looking out for,<BR>searching.<BR>--3 Investigating, inquiry,<BR>examination.<BR>--णः<BR>1 A beggar,<BR>supplicant, mendicant.<BR>--2 An arrow;<BR>दुर्वाराः स्मरमार्गणाः K. P. 10; अभेदि<BR>तत्तादृगनंग मार्गणैर्यदस्य पौष्पैरपि<BR>धैयर्कंचुकं N. 1. 46; Vikr. 1. 77;<BR>R. 9. 17, 65.<BR>--3 The number ‘five’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गणकः|मार्गणक
मार्गणकः A beggar, supplicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशिरः|मार्गशिर
मार्गशिरः, मार्गशिरस् m., मार्गशीर्षः<BR>N. of the ninth month of the Hindu<BR>year (corresponding to<BR>NovemberDecember) in which the full-moon<BR>is in the constellation मृगशिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशिरस्
मार्गशिरः, मार्गशिरस् m., मार्गशीर्षः<BR>N. of the ninth month of the Hindu<BR>year (corresponding to<BR>NovemberDecember) in which the full-moon<BR>is in the constellation मृगशिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशिरी
मार्गशिरी, मार्गशीर्षी The full-moon<BR>day in the month of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गशीर्षी
मार्गशिरी, मार्गशीर्षी The full-moon<BR>day in the month of मार्गशीर्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गिकः|मार्गिक
मार्गिकः<BR>1 A traveller.<BR>--2 A<BR>hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गित|मार्गितं
मार्गित p. p.<BR>1 Sought, searched,<BR>inquired after.<BR>--2 Hunted after,<BR>desired, solicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्गिन्
मार्गिन् m.<BR>1 A pioneer.<BR>--2 A guide,<BR>leader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ज्
मार्ज् {c10c} U. (मार्जयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>purify, cleanse, wipe; cf. मृज्.<BR>--2<BR>To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जः|मार्ज|मार्ज्ज|मार्ज्जः
मार्जः [मृज् मार्ज् वा घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Cleansing, purifying, scouring.<BR>--2 A<BR>washerman.<BR>--3 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जक
मार्जक a. (र्जिका f.) [मृज्-ण्वुल्]<BR>Cleansing, purifying, scouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जन|मार्जनः|मार्ज्जन|मार्ज्जनं|मार्ज्जनः
मार्जन a. (नी f.) [मृज्-ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>Cleansing, purifying.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Cleansing, cleaning, purifying.<BR>--2 Wiping<BR>or rubbing off.<BR>--3 Effacing, wiping<BR>away.<BR>--4 Cleansing the person by<BR>rubbing it with unguents.<BR>--5<BR>Sprinkling the person with water by<BR>means of the hand, a blade of Kuśa<BR>grass &c.<BR>--नः The tree called Lodhra.<BR>--ना<BR>1 Cleansing, purifying,<BR>cleaning.<BR>--2 The sound of a drum;<BR>मायूरीमदयति मार्जना मनांसि M. 1. 21.<BR>--नी<BR>A broom, brush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारः|मार्जार|मार्ज्जार
मार्जारः(लः) [मृज्-आरन् वा रस्य लः]<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">Page0863-a+ 54</a>]<BR>A cat; कपाले मार्जारः पय इति<BR>कराँल्लेढि शशिनः K. P. 10.<BR>--2 A pole-cat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठः a peacock.<BR>--करणं a<BR>kind of coitus or mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR>--कर्णिका, --कर्णी N. of<BR>Cāmuṇḍā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जालः|मार्जाल|मार्ज्जाल
मार्जारः(लः) [मृज्-आरन् वा रस्य लः]<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">Page0863-a+ 54</a>]<BR>A cat; कपाले मार्जारः पय इति<BR>कराँल्लेढि शशिनः K. P. 10.<BR>--2 A pole-cat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठः a peacock.<BR>--करणं a<BR>kind of coitus or mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR>--कर्णिका, --कर्णी N. of<BR>Cāmuṇḍā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0862-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारकः|मार्जारक|मार्ज्जारक
मार्जारकः<BR>1 A cat.<BR>--2 A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारी|मार्ज्जारी
मार्जारी<BR>1 A female cat.<BR>--2 A<BR>civetcat.<BR>--3 Musk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जारीयः|मार्जारीय|मार्ज्जारीय
मार्जारीयः<BR>1 A cat.<BR>--2 A Śūdra.<BR>--3<BR>One who cleanses his body (<BR>कायशोधन).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जित|मार्ज्जित
मार्जित p. p.<BR>1 Cleansed, scoured,<BR>purified.<BR>--2 Swept, brushed.<BR>--3<BR>Clean, bright.<BR>--4 Rubbed, smeared.<BR>--5 Washed away, removed.<BR>--6<BR>Adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्जिता|मार्ज्जिता
मार्जिता Curds with sugar and<BR>spices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्तंडः|मार्तण्ड|मार्तंड|मार्तण्डः|मार्त्तण्ड|मार्त्तण्डः
मार्तंडः [मृतादंडाज्ज यते अण् शकं˚]<BR>1 The sun; अयं मार्तंडः किं स खलु<BR>तुरगैः सप्तभिरितः K. P. 10; U. 6. 3.<BR>--2 The Arka tree.<BR>--3 A hog.<BR>--4<BR>The number twelve. (Also मार्तांड).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्तिक|मार्त्तिक|मार्त्तिकः
मार्तिक a. (की f.) [मृत्तिकया निर्मितं<BR>अण्] Made of clay, earthen.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A kind of pitcher.<BR>--2 The lid of a<BR>pitcher.<BR>--कं A clod or lump of<BR>earth; गुरुमध्ये हरिणाक्षी<BR>मार्तिकशकलैर्निहंतुकामं मां Bv. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्त्य
मार्त्य a. Mortal.<BR>--र्त्यं Mortality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दंगः|मार्दङ्ग|मार्दंग|मार्दङ्गः|मार्द्दङ्ग|मार्द्दङ्गं
मार्दंगः A drummer.<BR>--गं A city,<BR>town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दंगिकः|मार्दङ्गिक|मार्दंगिक|मार्दङ्गिकः|मार्द्दङ्गिक|मार्द्दङ्गिकः
मार्दंगिकः A drummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्दवं|मार्दव|मार्द्दव|मार्द्दवं|मार्द्दवः
मार्दवं [मृदोर्भावः अण्]<BR>1 Softness<BR>(lit. and fig.), pliancy, weakness;<BR>अभितप्तमयोऽपि मार्दवं भजते कैव कथा<BR>शरीरिषु R. 8. 43 ‘becomes soft’;<BR>स्वशरीरमार्दवं Ku. 5. 18.<BR>--2 Mildness,<BR>indulgence, gentleness, leniency;<BR>Bg. 16. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्द्वीक
मार्द्वीक a. (की f.) Made of<BR>grapes.<BR>--कं Wine; Śi. 8. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्मिक
मार्मिक a. [मर्म जानाति ठञ्]<BR>Having a deep insight into, fully<BR>conversant with the essence, beauty<BR>&c.; (= मर्मज्ञ q. v.); मार्मिकः को<BR>मरंदानामंतरेण मधुव्रतं Bv. 1. 117;<BR>परिणतमकरंदमार्मिकास्ते जगति भवंतु चिरायुषो<BR>मिलिंदाः 1. 8, 4. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0863-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मार्ष|मार्षः
