मुस्त्
मुस्त् {c10c} U. (मुस्तयति--ते) To heap<BR>up, gather, collect, accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0872-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तः|मुस्त|मुस्तं
मुस्तः --स्ता --स्तं A kind of grass;<BR>विस्रब्धं क्रियतां वराहततिभिर्मुःताक्षतिः<BR>पल्वले Ś. 2. 6; R. 9. 59; 15. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदः, --आदः a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0872-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्ता
मुस्तः --स्ता --स्तं A kind of grass;<BR>विस्रब्धं क्रियतां वराहततिभिर्मुःताक्षतिः<BR>पल्वले Ś. 2. 6; R. 9. 59; 15. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदः, --आदः a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0872-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्तं|मुस्त|मुस्तः
मुस्तः --स्ता --स्तं A kind of grass;<BR>विस्रब्धं क्रियतां वराहततिभिर्मुःताक्षतिः<BR>पल्वले Ś. 2. 6; R. 9. 59; 15. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदः, --आदः a hog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0872-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुस्रं|मुस्र
मुस्रं<BR>1 A pestle.<BR>--2 A tear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0872-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुह्
मुह् {c4c} P. (मुह्यति, मुग्ध or मूढ)<BR>1<BR>To faint, swoon, lose consciousness,<BR>become senseless; इहाहं द्रष्टुमाह्नं तां<BR>स्मरन्नेवं मुमोह सः Bk. 6. 21, 1. 20;<BR>15. 16.<BR>--2 To be perplexed or<BR>bewilddered, to be disturbed in mind,<BR>be at a loss; आपत्स्वपि न मुह्यंति नराः<BR>पंडितबुद्धयः H. 1. 166, Ki. 18. 9.<BR>--3 To be foolish, stupid, or<BR>infatuated.<BR>--4 To fail.<BR>--5 To err,<BR>mistake. --Caus. (मोहयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>stupefy, infatuate; मा मूमुहत्खलु<BR>भवंतमनन्यजन्मा Māl. 1. 32.<BR>--2 To<BR>confound, bewilder, perplex;<BR>Bg. 3. 2, 4. 16.<BR>--3 To throw into<BR>confusion.<BR>--4 To cause to err or<BR>mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0872-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढ|मूढः
मूढ p. p. [मुह-क्त]<BR>1 Stupefied,<BR>infatuated; Pt. 2. 4.<BR>--2 Perplexed,<BR>bewildered; confounded, at a loss;<BR>किंकर्तव्यतामूढः ‘being at a loss what<BR>to do’; so ह्रीमूढ Me. 68.<BR>--3 Foolish,<BR>silly, dull, stupid, ignorant; अल्पस्य<BR>हेतेर्बहु हातुमिच्छन्विचारमूढः प्रतिभासि<BR>मे त्वं R. 2. 47.<BR>--4 Mistaken, erring,<BR>deceived, gone astray.<BR>--5 Abortive.<BR>--6 Confounding.<BR>--ढः A fool,<BR>blockhead, dolt, an ignorant person;<BR>मूढः परपत्ययनेयबुद्धिः M. 1. 2.<BR>--ढाः<BR>(m. pl.) An epithet of the<BR>elements in the Sāṃkhya philosophy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a. {1}<BR>stupefied in mind. {2} foolish, stupid,<BR>silly.<BR>--गर्भः {1} a dead fœtus. {2}<BR>difficult delivery.<BR>--ग्राह. {1} a wrong<BR>notion, misconception,<BR>misapprehension. {2} infatuation.<BR>--चेतन,<BR>चेतस् a. foolish, silly, ignorant;<BR>अवगच्छति मूढचेतनः प्रियनाशं हृदि शल्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">Page0873-a+ 55</a>]<BR>मर्पितं R. 8. 88.<BR>--धी, --बुद्धि, मति a.<BR>foolish, stupid, silly, simple;<BR>Ki. 1. 30<BR>--प्रभुः --श्रेष्ठः the greatest<BR>block-head.<BR>--सत्त्व a. infatuated,<BR>insane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0872-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढता
मूढता --त्वं<BR>1 Confusion,<BR>bewilderment.<BR>--2 Folly, stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूढत्वं|मूढत्व
मूढता --त्वं<BR>1 Confusion,<BR>bewilderment.<BR>--2 Folly, stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहिर|मुहिरः
मुहिर a. [मुह्-किरच्] Silly, foolish,<BR>stupid.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The god of love.<BR>--2<BR>A fool, block-head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहु|मुहुः
मुहु ind. = मुहस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुकं|मुहुक
मुहुकं Ved. A moment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहुस्
मुहुस् ind.<BR>1 Often, constantly,<BR>repeatedly, frequently;<BR>ग्रीवाभगाभिरामं मुहुरनुपतति स्यंदने दत्तदृष्टिः Ś. 1. 7,<BR>2. 6; generally repeated in this sense;<BR>मुहुर्मुहुः over and over again, often<BR>and often; गुरुणा सन्निधानेऽपि कः<BR>कूजति मुहुर्मुहुः.<BR>--2 For a time or moment,<BR>awhile; Me. 105; generally used<BR>with successive clauses in the sense<BR>of ‘now now’, ‘at one time-at<BR>another time’; मुहुरुत्पतते बाला मुहुः<BR>पतति विह्वला । मुहुरालीयते भीता मुहुः<BR>क्रोशति रोदिति ॥ Subhāṣ.; Mu. 5. 3;<BR>मुहुर्तुहुः ‘again and again, repeatedly.’<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भाषा, --वचस् n.<BR>repetition, tautology.<BR>--भुज् m. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहूर्तः|मुहूर्त|मुहूर्तं|मुहूर्त्त|मुहूर्त्तः
मुहूर्तः --र्तं [हुर्छ् क्त ध तोः पूर्वं मुट् च<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 A moment, any short portion<BR>of time, an instant:<BR>नवांबुदानीकमुहूर्तलांछने R. 3. 53; संध्याभ्ररेखव<BR>मुहूर्तरागाः Pt. 1. 194; Me. 19; Ku. 7. 50.<BR>--2 A period, time (auspicious or<BR>otherwise).<BR>--3 A period of 48<BR>minutes.<BR>--र्तः An astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहूर्तं|मुहूर्त|मुहूर्तः|मुहूर्त्त|मुहूर्त्तः
मुहूर्तः --र्तं [हुर्छ् क्त ध तोः पूर्वं मुट् च<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 A moment, any short portion<BR>of time, an instant:<BR>नवांबुदानीकमुहूर्तलांछने R. 3. 53; संध्याभ्ररेखव<BR>मुहूर्तरागाः Pt. 1. 194; Me. 19; Ku. 7. 50.<BR>--2 A period, time (auspicious or<BR>otherwise).<BR>--3 A period of 48<BR>minutes.<BR>--र्तः An astrologer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहूर्तकः|मुहूर्तक
मुहूर्तकः<BR>1 An instant, a moment.<BR>--2 A period of 48 minutes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुहेरः|मुहेर
मुहेरः A block-head, fool.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मू
मू {c1c} A. (मवते) To bind, fasten,<BR>tie.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूक|मूकः
मूक a. [मू-कक्]<BR>1 Dumb, silent,<BR>mute, speechless: मूकं कराति वाचालंः<BR>मूकांडजं (काननं) Ku. 3. 42; सखामयं<BR>वीक्ष्य विषादमूकां Gīt. 7;<BR>मूकीभूतघंटास्वरास्वंतः पुरदोलासु K. 97;<BR>मूकीभूतवीणा K. 132.<BR>--2 Poor, miserable,<BR>wretched.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A mute; मौनान्मूकः<BR>H. 2. 26 v. l.; Ms. 7. 149.<BR>--2 A<BR>poor or miserable man<BR>--3 A fish.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंबा a form of Durgā.<BR>--भावः silence, muteness, dumb.<BR>ness (also मूकता --त्वं in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूकिमन्
मूकिमन् m. Muteness, dumbness,<BR>silence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत|मूतः
मूत a. [मू-क्त]<BR>1 Bound, tied<BR>--2 Confined.<BR>--3 Woven.<BR>--तः --तं<BR>1 A woven basket (Ved.).<BR>--2 A<BR>woven band of cloth.<BR>--3 A lump,<BR>collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रं|मूत्र
मूत्रं Urine; नाप्सु मूत्रं समूत्सृजेत्<BR>Ms. 4. 56; मूत्रं चकार ‘made water’.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आघातः a urinary disease.<BR>--आशयः the lower belly.<BR>--उत्संग<BR>see मूत्रसंग --कृच्छ्र painful discharge<BR>of urine, strangury.<BR>--कोशः the<BR>scrotum.<BR>--क्षयः insufficient<BR>secretion of urine.<BR>--ग्रथिः a knot or<BR>induration on the neck of the<BR>bladder.<BR>--जठरः --रं the swelling of the<BR>belly caused by retention of urine.<BR>--दोषः a urinary disease.<BR>--निरोधः<BR>retention of urine.<BR>--पतनः a<BR>civetcat.<BR>--पथः the urinary passage.<BR>--परीक्षा uroscopy or examination<BR>of urine.<BR>--पुटं the lewer belly<BR>--मार्गः, --प्रसेकः the urethra.<BR>--वर्धक<BR>a. diuretic.<BR>--वृद्धिः f. copious<BR>secretion of urine.<BR>--शकृत् n. urine<BR>and excrement.<BR>--शुक्रं a disease in<BR>which semen is discharged along<BR>with urine.<BR>--शूलः --लं urinary colic.<BR>--संगः urinary obstruction, a<BR>painful and bloody discharge of urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रयति
मूत्रयति Den. P. To make<BR>water; तिष्ठन्मूत्रयति Mbh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रल|मूत्रलं
मूत्रल a. Promoting the secretion<BR>of urine, diuretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूत्रित|मूत्रितः
मूत्रित a.<BR>1 Discharged or voided<BR>as urine.<BR>--2 Soiled with urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर
मूर a. Ved.<BR>1 Stupefied,<BR>bewildered.<BR>--2 Foolish, silly stupid.<BR>--3<BR>Destroying, killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ख|मूर्खः
मूर्ख a. Stupid, dull-headed,<BR>foolish, silly.<BR>--र्खः<BR>1 A fool,<BR>blockhead; न तु<BR>प्रातनिविष्टमूर्खजनचित्तमाराधयत् Bh. 2. 5, 8;<BR>मूर्ख बलादपगाधिनं मां प्रतिपादायष्यसि<BR>V. 2.<BR>--2 A kind of bean.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पंडितः a learned fool; Pt. 5. 40.<BR>--भूयं folly, stupidity, ignorance.<BR>--भ्रातृक a. one who has a foolish<BR>brother.<BR>--मंडलं an assembly of<BR>fools.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खता
मूर्खता --त्वं, मूर्खिमन् m. Stupidity,<BR>folly, silliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खत्वं|मूर्खत्व
मूर्खता --त्वं, मूर्खिमन् m. Stupidity,<BR>folly, silliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्खिमन्
मूर्खता --त्वं, मूर्खिमन् m. Stupidity,<BR>folly, silliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छन
मूर्च्छन a. (नी f.)<BR>1<BR>Stupefying, producing insensibility or<BR>stupor (an epithet applied to<BR>one of the five arrows of Cupid).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-c" target="_blank">Page0873-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--2 Increasing, augmenting,<BR>strengthening.<BR>--नं, --ना [मुर्च्छ् युच्]<BR>1<BR>Fainting, swooning.<BR>--2 Prevalence,<BR>growth, increase (usually n. in this<BR>sense).<BR>--3 A process in metallic<BR>preparation, calcining quicksilver<BR>with sulphur; cf. मूर्च्छा (3) also.<BR>--4 (In music) The rising of sounds,<BR>an intonation, a duly<BR>regulated rise and fall of sounds<BR>conducting the air and the harmony<BR>through the keys in a pleasing<BR>manner, changing the key or<BR>passing from the key to another;<BR>modulation, melody;<BR>स्फुटीभवद्ग्रामविशेषमूर्च्छनां Śi. 1. 10; भूयो भूयः<BR>स्वयमपि कृतां मूर्च्छनां विस्मरंती Me. 86;<BR>वर्णानामपि मूर्च्छनांतरगतं तारं विरामे<BR>मृदु Mk. 3. 5; सप्त स्वरास्त्रयो ग्रामा<BR>मूर्च्छनाश्चैकबिंशतिः Pt. 5. 54; (a मूर्च्छ or<BR>मूर्च्छना is thus defined:<BR>--क्रमात्स्वराणां<BR>सप्तानामारोहश्चावरोहणम । सा मूर्च्छेत्युच्यते<BR>ग्रामस्था एताः सप्त सप्त च ॥ see Malli. on<BR>Śi. 1. 10 for further information).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छा
मूर्च्छा [मुर्च्छ् --भावे अङ्]<BR>1<BR>Fainting, swooning; R. 7. 44.<BR>--2<BR>Spiritual ignorance or delusion.<BR>--3 A<BR>process in calcining metals; मूर्च्छां गतो<BR>मृतो वा निदर्शनं पारदोऽत्र रसः<BR>Bv. 1. 82.<BR>--4 The rising of sounds &c.; see<BR>मूर्च्छन (4) above.<BR>--5 Growth,<BR>increase<BR>--Comp. आक्षेपः (in Rhet.)<BR>expressing strong dissent by a swoon.<BR>--पगीत a. unconscious, fainted away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छाल
मूर्च्छाल a. Fainted, in sensible,<BR>senseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्च्छित
मूर्च्छित p. p. [मूर्च्छा जाता अस्य तार˚<BR>इतच्, मुर्छ् क्त वा]<BR>1 Fainted, swooning,<BR>insensible.<BR>--2 Foolish, stupid, silly.<BR>--3 Increased, augmented.<BR>--4 Made<BR>violent, intensified.<BR>--5 Perplexed,<BR>bewildered.<BR>--6 Filled.<BR>--7 Calcined.<BR>--8 Rising upwards, lofty.<BR>--तं A<BR>kind of song or air.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्त|मूर्त्त|मूर्त्तः
मूर्त a. [मुर्च्छ्-क्त]<BR>1 Fainted,<BR>insensible.<BR>--2 Stupid, foolish.<BR>--3<BR>Embodied, incarnate; मूर्तो<BR>विघ्नस्तपस इव नो भिन्न मारंगयूथः Ś. 1. 33;<BR>प्रसाद इव मूर्तस्ते स्पर्शः स्नेहार्द्रशतिलः<BR>U. 3. 14; R. 2. 69; 7. 70;<BR>Ku. 7. 42; Pt. 2. 99.<BR>--4 Material,<BR>corporeal.<BR>--5 Solid, hard.<BR>--6 Real.<BR>--7<BR>Thickened, coagulated (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तत्वं|मूर्तत्व
मूर्तत्वं<BR>1 Embodiment, materiality.<BR>--2 (In phil.) Having a finite or<BR>fixed measure or motion;<BR>परिच्छिन्नपरिमाणवत्त्वं क्रियावत्त्वं वा मूर्तत्वम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0873-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिः|मूर्ति|मूर्त्ति|मूर्त्तिः
मूर्तिः f. [मुर्च्छ्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Anything<BR>which has definite shape and limits,<BR>material element, matter,<BR>substance.<BR>--2 A form, visible shape,<BR>body, figure; Mu. 2. 2; R. 3. 27;<BR>14. 54.<BR>--3 An embodiment,<BR>incarnation, personification, manifestation;<BR>करुणस्य मूर्तिः U. 3. 4; Pt. 2. 159.<BR>--4 An image, idol, a statue.<BR>--5<BR>Beauty.<BR>--6 Solidity, hardness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धर, --संचर a. embodied, incarnate;<BR>धर्मो बा मूर्तिसंचरः Mv. 1. 10;<BR>U. 6. 10.<BR>--पः a worshipper of an image,<BR>one who is in charge of an idol.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तित्वं|मूर्तित्व
मूर्तित्वं Embodiment, materiality,<BR>incarnation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्तिमत्|मूर्तिमन्त्|मूर्त्तिमत्
मूर्तिमत् a.<BR>1 Material, corporeal.<BR>--2<BR>Embodied, incarnate, personified;<BR>शकुंतला मूर्तिमती च सत्क्रिया Śi. 5. 15;<BR>तव मूर्तिमानिव महोत्सवः करः U. 1. 18;<BR>R. 12. 64; Māl. 9. 9.<BR>--3 Hard,<BR>solid. --m. The body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धन्
मूर्धन् m. [मुह्यंत्यस्मिन्नाहते इति मूर्धा, cf.<BR>Uṇ. 1. 156]<BR>1 The forehead, brow.<BR>--2 The head in general; नतेन मूर्ध्ना<BR>हरिरग्रहीदपः Śi. 1. 18; R. 16. 81;<BR>नैसर्गिकी सुरभिणः कुसुमस्य सिद्धा मूर्ध्नि<BR>स्थितिर्न चरणैरवताडनानि U. 1. 14;<BR>Ku. 3. 22.<BR>--3 The highest or most<BR>prominent part, top, summit, peak,<BR>head; अतिष्ठन्मनुजेंद्राणां मूर्ध्नि<BR>देवपतिर्यथा Mb. ‘stood at the head of all<BR>kings’ &c.; भूम्यां पर्वतमूर्धनि;<BR>Ś. 5. 7; Me. 17.<BR>--4 (Hence) A leader,<BR>head, chief, foremost, prominent.<BR>--5<BR>Front, van, forepart; स किल<BR>संयुगमूर्ध्नि सहायतां मघवतः प्रतिपद्य महारथः<BR>R. 9. 19.<BR>--6 (In geom.) The base.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः the crown of the<BR>head.<BR>--अभिषिक्त a. f. consecrated,<BR>crowned, inaugurated; R. 16. 81.<BR>{2} common, stock (as an instance);<BR>उत्कृत्योत्कृत्य कृत्तिं इति बीभत्सस्य<BR>मूर्धाभिषिक्तमुदाहरणम्.<BR>--(क्तः) {1} a<BR>consecrated king. {2} a man of the<BR>Kṣatriya caste. {3} a minister. {4} =<BR>मूर्धावसिक्त (1) q. v.<BR>--अभिषेकः<BR>censecration, inauguration.<BR>--अवसिक्तः {1} N.<BR>of a particular mixed tribe sprung<BR>from a Brāhmaṇa father and<BR>Kṣatriya mother. {2} a consecrated king.<BR>--कर्णी, --कर्परी f. an umbrella.<BR>--जः<BR>{1} the hair (of the head); पर्याकुला<BR>मूर्धजाः Ś. 1. 30; विललाप<BR>विकीर्णमूर्धजा Ku. 4. 4 ‘she tore her hair for<BR>grief’. {2} the mane.<BR>--ज्योतिस् n.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-b" target="_blank">Page0874-b+ 56</a>]<BR>see ब्रह्मरंध्र or मुद्रामार्ग.<BR>--पिंडः a lump<BR>upon the head (of an elephant in<BR>rut).<BR>--पुष्पः the Śirīṣa tree.<BR>--रसः<BR>the scum of boiled rice.<BR>--वेष्टनं a<BR>turban, diadem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्धन्य|मूर्द्धन्यः
मूर्धन्य a. [मूर्ध्नि भवः यत्]<BR>1 Being<BR>in or on the head.<BR>--2 Cerebral or<BR>lingual, a term applied to the letters<BR>ऋ, ॠ, ट्, ठ्, ड्, ढ्, ण्, र्, and ष्; ऋटुरषाणां<BR>मूर्धा.<BR>--3 Chief, pre-eminent, most<BR>excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्ध्वन्
मूर्ध्वन् See मूर्धन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्वा|मूर्व्वा
मूर्वा --र्वी, मूर्विका A kind of<BR>creeper (from the fibres of which<BR>bow-strings and the girdle of Kṣatriyas<BR>are made).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्वी
मूर्वा --र्वी, मूर्विका A kind of<BR>creeper (from the fibres of which<BR>bow-strings and the girdle of Kṣatriyas<BR>are made).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूर्विका
मूर्वा --र्वी, मूर्विका A kind of<BR>creeper (from the fibres of which<BR>bow-strings and the girdle of Kṣatriyas<BR>are made).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्
मूल् {vI.v} {c1c} U. (मूलति-ते) To take or<BR>strike root, be firm, stand fast. {vII.v}<BR>{c10c} U. (मूलयति-ते, मूलित)<BR>1 To plant,<BR>cause to grow, rear.<BR>--2 To grow,<BR>sprout, germinate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलं|मूल|मूलः
मूलं [मूल्-क]<BR>1 A root (fig. also);<BR>तरुमूलानि गृहीभवति तेषां Ś. 7. 20; or<BR>शाखिनो धौतमूलाः 1. 15; मूलं बंध् to<BR>take or strike root; बद्धमूलस्य मूलं हि<BR>महद्वैरतरोः स्त्रियः Śi. 2. 38.<BR>--2 The<BR>root, lowest edge or extremity of<BR>anything; कस्याश्चिदासिद्रशना<BR>तदानीमंगुष्ठमूलार्पितसूत्रशेषा R. 7. 10; so<BR>प्राचीमूले Me. 89.<BR>--3 The lower part or<BR>end, base, the end of anything by<BR>which it is joined to something<BR>else; बाह्वोर्मूलं Śi. 7. 32; so पादमूलं,<BR>कर्णमूलं, ऊरुमूलं &c.<BR>--4 Beginning,<BR>commencement; आमूलाच्छ्रोतुमिच्छामि<BR>Ś. 1.<BR>--5 Basis, foundation, source,<BR>origin, cause; सर्वे गार्हस्थ्यमूलकाः Mb.;<BR>रक्षोगृहे स्थितिर्मूलं U. 1. 6; इति<BR>केनाप्युक्तं तत्र मूलं मृग्यं ‘the source or<BR>authority should be found out’.<BR>--6<BR>The foot or bottom of anything;<BR>पर्वतमूलं, गिरिमूलं &c.<BR>--7 The text, or<BR>original passage (as distinguished<BR>from the commentary or gloss).<BR>--8<BR>Vicinity, neighbourhood.<BR>--9 Capital,<BR>principal, stock.<BR>--10 A hereditary<BR>servant.<BR>--11 A square root.<BR>--12 A<BR>king's own territory; स गुप्तमूलप्रत्यंतं:<BR>R. 4. 26; Ms. 7. 184.<BR>--13 A vender<BR>who is not the true owner;<BR>Ms. 8. 202 (अस्वामिविक्रेता Kull.).<BR>--14 The<BR>nineteenth lunar mansion<BR>containing 11 stars.<BR>--15 A thicket, copse.<BR>--16 The root of long pepper.<BR>--17 A<BR>particular position of the fingers.<BR>--18 A chief or capital city.<BR>--19 An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-c" target="_blank">Page0874-c+ 57</a>]<BR>aboriginal inhabitant.<BR>--20 A bower,<BR>an arbour (निकुंज).<BR>--21 N. of several<BR>roots. पिप्यली, पुष्कर, शूरण &c. (In<BR>comp. मुल may be translated by<BR>‘first, prime, original, chief,<BR>principal’; e. g. मूलकारणं ‘prime cause’ &c.<BR>&c.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आधारं {1} the navel.<BR>{2} a mystical circle above the<BR>organs of generation.<BR>--आभं a<BR>radish.<BR>--भायतनं the original abode.<BR>--आशिन् a. living upon roots.<BR>--आह्वं a radish.<BR>--उच्छेदः utter<BR>destruction, total eradication.<BR>--कर्मन्<BR>n. magic.<BR>--कारः the author of an<BR>original work.<BR>--कारणं the original<BR>or prime cause; Ku. 6. 13.<BR>--कारिका<BR>a furnace, an oven.<BR>--कृच्छ्रः --च्छ्रं a<BR>kind of penance, living only upon<BR>roots.<BR>--केशरः a citron.<BR>--गुणः the<BR>co-efficient of a root.<BR>--ग्रंथः {1} an<BR>original text. {2} the very words<BR>uttered by Śākyamuni.<BR>--छेदः<BR>uprooting.<BR>--ज a. {1} radical. {2}<BR>growing at the roots of trees (as an<BR>anthill). {3} born under the<BR>constellation Mūla.<BR>--(जः) plant growing<BR>from a root.<BR>--(जं) a green ginger.<BR>--देवः an epithet of Kaṃsa.<BR>--द्रव्यं,<BR>--धनं principal, stock, capital.<BR>--धातुः<BR>lymph.<BR>--निकृंतन a. destroying root<BR>and branch.<BR>--पुरुषः ‘the stock-man’,<BR>the male representative of a family.<BR>--प्रकृतिः f. the Prakṛti or<BR>Pradhāna of the Sāṃkhyas (q. v.). --(pl.)<BR>the four principal sovereigns to be<BR>considered at the time of war (<BR>विजिगीषु, अरि, मध्यम, and उदासीन); see<BR>Ms. 7. 155.<BR>--फलदः the bread-fruit tree.<BR>--बर्हणं the act of uprooting,<BR>extermination.<BR>--भद्रः an epithet of<BR>Kaṃsa.<BR>--भृत्यः an old or hereditary<BR>servant.<BR>--वचनं an original text.<BR>--वापः one who plants roots.<BR>--वित्तं<BR>capital, stock.<BR>--विभुजः a chariot.<BR>--व्यसनवृत्तिः the hereditary<BR>occupation of executing criminals;<BR>Ms. 10. 38.<BR>--व्रतिन् a. living exclusively on<BR>roots.<BR>--शकुनः (in augury) the<BR>first bird.<BR>--शाकटः, --शाकिनं a field<BR>planted with edible roots.<BR>--संघः a<BR>society, sect.<BR>--स्थानं {1} base, foundation.<BR>{2} the Supreme Spirit. {3} wind,<BR>air. {4} Mooltan.<BR>--(नी) N. of Gaurī.<BR>--स्थायिन् m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--स्रोतस् n. the principal current or<BR>fountain-head of a river.<BR>--हर a.<BR>uprooting completely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0874-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलक|मूलकं|मूलकः
मूलक a.<BR>1 (At the end of comp.)<BR>Rooted in, springing from, founded<BR>or based on; भ्रांतिमूलक ‘based on<BR>error.<BR>--2 Born under the<BR>constellation Mūla.<BR>--कः, --कं<BR>1 A radish.<BR>--2<BR>An esculent root.<BR>--3 A sort of Yam.<BR>--कः A kind of poison.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पणः a handful of radishes &c. (for<BR>sale).<BR>--पोतिका a radish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूला
मूला<BR>1 N. of a plant.<BR>--2 The<BR>asterism Mūla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिक|मूलिकः
मूलिक a.<BR>1 Radical, original.<BR>--2<BR>Primary, principal.<BR>--3 Living on<BR>roots.<BR>--कः A devotee, an ascetic.<BR>--का<BR>1 A root.<BR>--2 A collection of<BR>roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिन्
मूलिन् m. A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलिन|मूलिनः
मूलिन a. Growing from a root.<BR>--नः A plant, tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूली
मूली A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूलेरः|मूलेर
मूलेरः<BR>1 A king.<BR>--2 The Indian<BR>spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूल्य|मूल्यं
मूल्य a.<BR>1 To be eradicated.<BR>--2<BR>Being at the root.<BR>--3 Purchasable.<BR>--ल्यं<BR>1 Price, worth, cost; क्रीणंति<BR>स्म प्राणमूल्यैर्यशांसि Śi. 18. 15,<BR>Śānti. 1. 12.<BR>--2 Wages, hire, salary.<BR>--3<BR>Gain.<BR>--4 Capital, principal.<BR>--5<BR>Original value.<BR>--6 An article<BR>purchased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूष्
मूष् {c1c} A. (मूषति, मूषित) To steal,<BR>rob, plunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषः|मूष
मूषः<BR>1 A rat, mouse.<BR>--2 A round<BR>window, an air-hole.<BR>--3 A crucible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषकः|मूषक
मूषकः<BR>1 A rat, mouse.<BR>--2 A thief.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरातिः a cat.<BR>--वाहनः an<BR>epithet of Gaṇeśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषणं|मूषण
मूषणं Stealing, pilfering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषा
मूषा, मूषिका<BR>1 A female rat.<BR>--2 A<BR>crucible<BR>--3 An air-hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिका
मूषा, मूषिका<BR>1 A female rat.<BR>--2 A<BR>crucible<BR>--3 An air-hole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकः|मूषिक
मूषिकः<BR>1 A rat.<BR>--2 A thief.<BR>--3<BR>The Śirīṣa tree.<BR>--4 N. of a<BR>country.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः, --अंचनः, --रथः<BR>epithets of Gaṇeśa.<BR>--अदः a cat.<BR>--अरातिः a cat.<BR>--उत्करः, --स्थलं a<BR>molehill.<BR>--विषाणं ‘the horn of a<BR>mouse’, i. e. an impossibility; cf.<BR>शशवषिण, खपुष्प &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषिकारः|मूषिकार
मूषिकारः A male rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषी
मूषी, मूषीकः, मूषीका A rat, mouse<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषीकः|मूषीक
मूषी, मूषीकः, मूषीका A rat, mouse<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषीका
मूषी, मूषीकः, मूषीका A rat, mouse<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मूषीकरणं|मूषीकरण
मूषीकरणं Melting in a crucible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृ
मृ {c6c} A. (but P. in the Perfect,<BR>the two Futures and the<BR>Conditional) (म्रियते, ममार, अमृत, मरिष्यति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-b" target="_blank">Page0875-b+ 57</a>]<BR>मर्तुं, मृत) To die, perish, decease,<BR>depart from life. --Caus. (मारयति-ते)<BR>To kill, slay. --Desid. (मुमूर्षति)<BR>1<BR>To wish to die.<BR>--2 To be about to<BR>die, be on the point of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृक्ष्
मृक्ष् See म्रक्ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृग्
मृग् {c4c} P., {c10c} A. (मृग्यति, मृगयते<BR>मृगित)<BR>1 To seek, search for, seek<BR>after; न रत्नमन्विष्यति मृग्यते हि तत्<BR>Ku. 5. 45; गता दूता दूरं क्वचिदपि<BR>परेतान् मृगयितुं G. L. 25.<BR>--2 To hunt,<BR>chase, pursue.<BR>--3 To aim at, strive<BR>after.<BR>--4 To examine, investigate;<BR>अबिचलितमनोभिः साधकैर्मृग्यमाणः<BR>Māl. 5. 1; अंतर्यश्च<BR>मुमुक्षुभिर्नियमितप्राणादिभिर्मृग्यते V. 1. 1 ‘inwardly sought or<BR>investigated’.<BR>--5 To ask for, beg of<BR>one; एतावदेव मृगये प्रतिपक्षहेतोः<BR>M. 5. 20.<BR>--6 To visit, frequent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मृगः|मृग
मृगः [मृग्-क]<BR>1 (a) A quadruped, an<BR>animal in general; नाभिषेको न<BR>संस्कारः सिंहस्य क्रियते मृगैः ।<BR>विक्रमार्जितराज्यस्य स्वयमेव मृगेंद्रता; see मृगाधिप below.<BR>(b) A wild beast.<BR>--2 A deer, an<BR>antelope; विश्वासोपगमादभिन्नगतयः शब्दं<BR>सहंते मृगाः Ś. 1. 14; R. 1. 40, 50;<BR>आश्रममृगोयं न हंतव्यः Ś. 1.<BR>--3 Game<BR>in general.<BR>--4 The spots on the<BR>moon represented as an antelope.<BR>--5 Musk.<BR>--6 Seeking, search.<BR>--7<BR>Pursuit, chase, hunting.<BR>--8 Inquiry,<BR>investigation.<BR>--9 Asking, soliciting.<BR>--10 A kind of elephant.<BR>--11 N. of<BR>a particular class of men; मृगे तुष्टा<BR>च चित्रिणी; वदति मधुरवाणीं दीर्घनेत्रोऽ<BR>तिभीरुश्चपलमतिसुदेहः शीघ्रवेगो मृगोऽयम्<BR>Śabdak.<BR>--12 The lunar mansion<BR>called मृगशिरश्<BR>--13 The lunar month<BR>called मार्गशीर्ष.<BR>--14 The sign<BR>Capricornus of the zodiac.<BR>--15 N. of a<BR>district in Śākadvīpa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षी a fawn-eyed or deer-eyed<BR>woman.<BR>--अंकः {1} the moon. {2}<BR>camphor. {3} the wind.<BR>--अंगना a<BR>doe.<BR>--अजिनं a deer's skin.<BR>--अंडजा<BR>musk.<BR>--अद् m.,<BR>--अदनः, --अंतकः a small<BR>tiger or hunting leopard, hyena<BR>--अधिपः, --अधिराजः a lion; केसरी<BR>निष्ठुरक्षिप्तमृगयूथो मृगाधिपः Śi. 2. 53;<BR>मृगाधिराजस्य वचो निशम्य R. 2. 41.<BR>--अरातिः {1} a lion. {2} a dog.<BR>--अरिः<BR>{1} a lion. {2} a dog. {3} a tiger. {4}<BR>N. of a tree.<BR>--अशनः a lion.<BR>--आजीवः {1} a hunter. {2} a hyena.<BR>--आविध् m. a hunter.<BR>--आस्यः the sign<BR>Capricornus of the zodiac.<BR>--इंद्रः {1}<BR>a lion; ततो मृगेंद्रस्य मृगेंद्रगामी<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-c" target="_blank">Page0875-c+ 56</a>]<BR>R. 2. 30. {2} a tiger. {3} the sign Leo O<BR>the zodiac. ˚आसनं a throne. ˚आस्यः<BR>an epithet of Śiva. ˚चटकः a hawk.<BR>--इष्टः a variety of jasmine.<BR>--ईक्षणा<BR>a fawn-eyed woman.<BR>--ईश्वरः {1} a lion.<BR>{2} the sign Leo of the zodiac.<BR>--उत्तमः the best antelope.<BR>--उत्तमं,<BR>--उत्तमांगं the constellation मृगशिरस्.<BR>--काननं {1} a park. {2} a forest<BR>abounding in game.<BR>--गामिनी a kind<BR>of medicinal substance.<BR>--चारिन् a.<BR>acting like a deer (as a devotee);<BR>leading a deer's life; V. 4.<BR>--जलं<BR>mirage. ˚स्नानं bathing in the waters<BR>of the mirage; i. e. an impossibility.<BR>--जीवनः a hunter, fowler.<BR>--तृष्,<BR>--तृषा, --तृष्णा, --तृष्णि, --तृष्णिका, f.<BR>mirage; मृगतृष्णांभसि स्नातः; see खपुष्प;<BR>जातः सखे प्रणयवान्मृगतृष्णिकायां<BR>Ś. 6. 15.<BR>--दंशः, --दंशकः a dog.<BR>--दावः a<BR>park, preserve.<BR>--दृश् f. a fawn-eyed<BR>woman; तदीषद्विस्तारि<BR>स्तनयुगलमासीन्मृगदृशः U. 6. 35. (--m.) the sign<BR>Capricornus of the zodiac.<BR>--द्युः a<BR>hunter.<BR>--द्विष् m. a lion.<BR>--धरः the<BR>moon.<BR>--धूर्तः, धूर्तकः a jackal.<BR>--नयना<BR>a fawn-eyed woman.<BR>--नाभिः {1}<BR>musk; Ku. 1. 54; Rs. 6. 13;<BR>Ch. P. 8; R. 17. 24. {2} the musk-deer;<BR>R. 4. 74. ˚जा musk.<BR>--पतिः {1} a<BR>lion. {2} a roe-buck. {3} a tiger.<BR>--पालिका the musk-deer.<BR>--पिप्लुः the<BR>moon.<BR>--पोतः --पोतकः a fawn.<BR>--प्रभुः<BR>a lion.<BR>--प्रियं grass growing on<BR>mountains.<BR>--ब (व) धाजीवः a hunter.<BR>--बंधिनी a net for catching deer.<BR>--भोजना bitter apple.<BR>--मदः musk;<BR>कुचतटीगतो यावन्मातर्मिलति तव<BR>तोयैर्मृगमदः G. L. 7; मृगमदतिलकं लिखति<BR>सपुलकं मृगमिव रजनीकरे Gīt. 7. ˚वासा<BR>a musk-bag<BR>--मंद्रः N. of a class of<BR>elephants.<BR>--मांसं venison.<BR>--मातृका<BR>a doe.<BR>--मासः the month of<BR>Mārgaśīrsha.<BR>--मुखः the sign Capricornus<BR>of the zodiac.<BR>--यूथं a herd of deer.<BR>--राज् m. {1} a lion; Śi. 9. 18. {2} a<BR>tiger. {3} the sign Leo of the zodiac.<BR>--राजः {1} a lion; R. 6. 3. {2} the<BR>sign Leo of the zodiac. {3} a tiger.<BR>{4} the moon. ˚धारिन्, ˚लक्ष्मन् m. the<BR>moon.<BR>--रिपुः a lion.<BR>--रोमं wool. ˚जं<BR>a woollen cloth.<BR>--रोचना yellow<BR>pigment.<BR>--लांछंनः --लक्ष्मन् m. the moon;<BR>अंकधिरोवितमृगश्चंद्रमा भृगलांछनः<BR>Śi. 2. 53. ˚जः the planet Mercury.<BR>--लेखा<BR>the deer-like streak on the moon;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0876-a" target="_blank">Page0876-a+ 57</a>]<BR>मृगलेखामुषसीव चंद्रमाः R. 8. 42.<BR>--लोचनः the moon.<BR>--(न, --नी) a<BR>fawneyed woman.<BR>--वल्लभः a kind of grass<BR>(कुंदर).<BR>--वाहनः wind.<BR>--व्याधः {1}<BR>a hunter. {2} Sirius or the<BR>dogstar. {3} an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--शायिका the reclining posture of a<BR>deer.<BR>--शावः a fawn; मृगशावैः<BR>सममेधितो जनः Ś. 2. 18.<BR>--शिरः, शिरस्<BR>n.<BR>--शिरा N. of the fifth lunar<BR>mansion consisting of three stars.<BR>--शीर्षं the constellation मृगशिरस्<BR>--(र्षः)<BR>the lunar month Mārgaśīrṣa.<BR>--शीर्षन् m. the constellation<BR>मृगशिरस्.<BR>--श्रेष्ठः a tiger.<BR>--हन् m. a<BR>hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0875-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

