वाधूक्यं|वाधूक्य
वाधु(धू)क्यं Marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाध्रीणसः|वाध्रीणस
वाध्रीणसः Arhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान|वानं|वानः
वान a.<BR>1 Blown.<BR>--2 Dried(by<BR>wind) dried up.<BR>--3 Belonging to<BR>a forest.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Dry or dried fruit<BR>(m. also).<BR>--2 Blowing.<BR>--3<BR>Living.<BR>--4 Rolling, moving, (as of<BR>waters &c.).<BR>--5 A perfume,<BR>fragrance.<BR>--6 A number of groves or<BR>thickets.<BR>--7 Weaving.<BR>--8 A mat of<BR>straw.<BR>--9 A hole in the wall of a<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानप्रस्थः|वानप्रस्थ
वानप्रस्थः [वाने वनसमूहे प्रतिष्ठते<BR>स्थाक]<BR>1 A Brāhmaṇa in the third<BR>stage of his religious life.<BR>--2 An<BR>anchorite, a hermit.<BR>--3 The<BR>Madhuka tree.<BR>--4 The Palāśa<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानरः|वानर
वानरः [वानं वनसंबंधि फलादिकं<BR>रातिगृह्णति रा-क; वा किकल्पेन नरो वा] A<BR>monkey, an ape.<BR>--री A female<BR>monkey.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः a wild goat.<BR>--आघातः the tree called Lodhra.<BR>--इंद्रः N. of Sugrīva or of<BR>Hanumat.<BR>--प्रियः the tree called क्षीरिन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानलः|वानल
वानलः A kind of holy basil<BR>(the black variety).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानस्पत्यः|वानस्पत्य
वानस्पत्यः A tree the fruit of<BR>which is produced from flower;<BR>e. g. the mango.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाना
वाना<BR>1 A quail.<BR>--2 Dry or dried<BR>fruit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानायुः|वानायु
वानायुः N. of a country to the<BR>north-west of India.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः<BR>a Vanāyu horse, i. e. a horse<BR>produced in the Vanāyu country.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीरः|वानीर
वानीरः A sort of cane or ratan;<BR>स्मरामि वानीरगृहेषु सुप्तः R. 13. 35;<BR>Me. 41; Māl. 9. 15; R. 13. 30,<BR>16. 21; U. 2. 20; Mv. 5. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानीरकः|वानीरक
वानीरकः The Munja grass, a<BR>kind of rush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वानेयं|वानेय
वानेयं N. of a fragrant grass<BR>(मुस्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांत|वान्त|वान्तः
वांत p. p. [वम्-क्त]<BR>1 Vomited,<BR>spitted out.<BR>--2 Emitted, ejected,<BR>effused.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदः a dog.<BR>--अ-आ--शिन् m. a foul-feeding demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वांति|वान्ति|वान्तिः
वांति f.<BR>1 Vomiting.<BR>--2 Ejecting,<BR>emitting.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत्, --द a.<BR>emetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वान्या
वान्या A multitude of groves or<BR>woods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापः|वाप
वापः [वप्-घञ्]<BR>1 Sowing seed.<BR>--2 Weaving.<BR>--3 Shaving, shearing;<BR>Ms. 11. 109.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंडः a<BR>weaver's loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापनं|वापन
वापनं<BR>1 Causing to sow.<BR>--2<BR>Shaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापित|वापितं
वापित p. p.<BR>1 Sown.<BR>--2 Shaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापिः|वापि
वापिः --पी f. [वप्-इञ् वा ङीप्;<BR>Uṇ. 4. 125] A well, any large oblong<BR>or circular reservoir of water;<BR>वापी चास्मिन्मरकतशिलाबद्धसोपानमार्गा<BR>Me. 76.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हः the Cātaka<BR>bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वापी
वापिः --पी f. [वप्-इञ् वा ङीप्;<BR>Uṇ. 4. 125] A well, any large oblong<BR>or circular reservoir of water;<BR>वापी चास्मिन्मरकतशिलाबद्धसोपानमार्गा<BR>Me. 76.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हः the Cātaka<BR>bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाम|वामं|वामः
वाम a.<BR>1 Left(opp. दक्षिण);<BR>विलोचनं दक्षिणमंजनेन संभाव्य<BR>तद्वंचितवामनेत्रा R. 7. 8; Me. 78, 96.<BR>--2<BR>Being or situated on the left side;<BR>वामश्चायं नदति मधुरं चातकस्ते सगंधः<BR>Me. 9; (वामेन is used adverbially in<BR>the same sense; e. g. वामेनात्र<BR>वटस्तमध्वगजनः सर्वात्मना सेवते K. P. 10).<BR>--3 (a) Reverse, contrary,<BR>opposite, adverse, unfavourable; तदहो<BR>कामस्य वामा गतिः Gīt. 12;<BR>Māl. 9. 8, Bk. 6. 17. (b) Acting contrary,<BR>of an opposite nature; यांत्येवं<BR>गृहिणीपदं युवतयो वामाः कुलस्यावयः Ś. 4. 17.<BR>(e) Perverse, crooked-natured,<BR>refractory; Ś. 6.<BR>--4 Vile, wicked,<BR>base, low, bad; Ki. 11. 24.<BR>--5<BR>Lovely, beautiful, charming; as in<BR>वामलोचना q. v.<BR>--6 Short.<BR>--मः<BR>1 A<BR>sentient being, an animal.<BR>--2<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--3 Of Cupid, the god<BR>of love.<BR>--4 A snake.<BR>--5 An udder,<BR>a breast.<BR>--6 Prohibited or forbidden<BR>act or practice (as drinking wine).<BR>--मं Wealth, possessions.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचारः --मार्गः the left-hand<BR>ritual or doctrine of the Tantras.<BR>--आपीडनः the Pīlu tree.<BR>--आवर्तः<BR>{1} a conch-shell, the spiral<BR>of which runs from right to left.<BR>--ऊरु, --ऊरू f. a woman with<BR>handsome thighs; तदिदं विषहिष्यते कथं<BR>वद वामोरु चिताधिराहेणं R. 8. 57.<BR>--दृश् f. a woman (with lovely<BR>eyes).<BR>--देवः {1} N. of a sage. {2}<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--भ्रूः f. a<BR>beautifuleye-browed woman; Pt. 1. 136.<BR>--लोचना a woman with lovely eyes;<BR>विरूपाक्षस्य जयिनीस्ताः स्तुवे वामलोचनाः<BR>K. P. 10; R. 19. 13.<BR>--शील a. of<BR>a perverse or crooked nature;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">Page0960-a+ 55</a>]<BR>crosstempered: तदेहि वामशीलां मालतीं<BR>निर्भर्त्सयामः Māl. 7.<BR>--(लः) an epithet<BR>of the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0959-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामक|वामकः
वामक a.<BR>1 Left.<BR>--2 Adverse,<BR>contrary; स्फुरता वामकेनापि<BR>दाक्षिण्यमवलंब्यते Māl. 8 (where both senses are<BR>intended).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामन|वामनः
वामन a.<BR>1 (a) Short in stature,<BR>dwarfish, pigmy; छलवामनं<BR>Śi. 13. 12. (b) (Hence) Small, short,<BR>little, reduced in length;<BR>वामनार्चिरिव दीपभाजनं R. 19. 51; कथं कथं<BR>तानि (दिनानि) च वामनानि N. 22. 57.<BR>--2 Bent down, bent low (नम्र);<BR>शिरसि स्म जिघ्रति सुरारिबंधने छलवामनं<BR>विनयवामनं तदा Śi. 13. 12.<BR>--3 Vile,<BR>low, base.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A dwarf, pigmy;<BR>प्रांशुलभ्ये फले मोहादुद्वाहुरिव वामनः<BR>R. 1. 3, 10. 60.<BR>--2 N. of Viṣṇu in<BR>his fifth incarnation, when he was<BR>born as a dwarf to humble the<BR>demon Bali, (see बलि); छलयसि<BR>विक्रमणे बलिमद्भुतवामन<BR>पदनखनीरजनितजतपावन । केशव धृतवामनरूप जय<BR>जगदीश हरे Gīt. 1; Śi. 13. 12.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of the elephant that presides over<BR>the south.<BR>--4 N. of the author of<BR>the Kāśikāvṛtti, a commentary on<BR>Pāṇini's Sūtras.<BR>--5 The tree called<BR>अंकोट.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आकृति a.<BR>dwarfish.<BR>--पुराणं N. of one of the 18<BR>Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनिका
वामनिका A female dwarf.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामनी
वामनी<BR>1 A female dwarf.<BR>--2 A<BR>mare.<BR>--3 A kind of woman.<BR>--4 A<BR>disease of the vagina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामलूरः|वामलूर
वामलूरः An ant-hill, a mole-hill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामा
वामा<BR>1 A woman.<BR>--2 A lovely<BR>woman; Bv. 4. 39, 42.<BR>--3 N. of<BR>Gaurī.<BR>--4 Of Lakṣmī.<BR>--5 Of<BR>Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामिल|वामिलः
वामिल a.<BR>1 Beautiful,<BR>handsome.<BR>--2 Proud, haughty.<BR>--3<BR>Cunning, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामिका
वामिका An epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वामी
वामी<BR>1 A mare;<BR>अथोष्ट्रमामीशतवाहितार्थं R. 5. 32.<BR>--2 A she-ass.<BR>--3 A female elephant.<BR>--4 The<BR>female of the jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायः|वाय
वायः [वे-घञ्] Weaving,<BR>sewing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दंडः a weaver's loom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायकः|वायक
वायकः<BR>1 A weaver.<BR>--2 A heap,<BR>multitude, collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायनं|वायन
वायनं, --वायनकं A present of<BR>sweetmeats made to a deity,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-b" target="_blank">Page0960-b+ 56</a>]<BR>particularly to a Brāhmaṇa, on festive<BR>occasions, observance of fasts &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायनकं|वायनक
वायनं, --वायनकं A present of<BR>sweetmeats made to a deity,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-b" target="_blank">Page0960-b+ 56</a>]<BR>particularly to a Brāhmaṇa, on festive<BR>occasions, observance of fasts &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव
वायव a. (वी f.)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>or given by the wind or Vāyu.<BR>--2<BR>Aerial.<BR>--वी The north-west<BR>quarter (presided over by Vāyu).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायवीय
वायवीय, वायव्य a. Relating to<BR>the wind, aerial.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुराणं N. of a Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायव्य|वायव्यं
वायवीय, वायव्य a. Relating to<BR>the wind, aerial.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुराणं N. of a Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायसः|वायस
वायसः [वय एव अण् Uṇ. 3. 120]<BR>1 A crow; बलिमिव परिभोक्तु<BR>वायसास्तर्कयंति Mk. 10. 3.<BR>--2 Fragrant<BR>aloe-wood, agallochum.<BR>--3<BR>Turpentine.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरातिः, --अरिः an owl.<BR>--आह्वा a kind of esculent<BR>vegetable.<BR>--इ क्षुः a kind of long grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वायुः|वायु
वायुः [वा-उण् युक च Uṇ. 1. 1]<BR>1 Air,<BR>wind; वायुर्विधुनयति चंपकपुष्परेणून् K.R.;<BR>आकाशात्तु विकुर्वाणात्सर्वगंधवहः शुचिः ।<BR>बलवाञ्जायते वायुः स वै स्पर्शगुणो मतः ॥<BR>Ms. 1. 76. (There are seven courses of<BR>wind one above the other:<BR>--आवहः<BR>प्रवहश्चैव संवहश्चोद्वहस्तथा । विवहाख्यः परिवहः<BR>परावह इति क्रमात्).<BR>--2 The god of wind,<BR>the deity supposed to preside over<BR>wind, (who is the regent of the<BR>north-west quarter.).<BR>--3 A<BR>lifewind or vital air, of which five<BR>kinds are enumerated:<BR>--प्राण, अपान,<BR>समान, व्यान, and उदान.<BR>--4 Morbid<BR>affection or vitiation of the windy<BR>humour.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्पदं the sky,<BR>atmosphere.<BR>--केतुः dust.<BR>--कोणः<BR>the north-west.<BR>--गंडः flatulence<BR>(caused by indigestion).<BR>--गति a.<BR>swift as wind, very fleet.<BR>--गुल्मः<BR>{1} a hurricane, storm. {2} a<BR>whirlpool.<BR>--गोचरः the range of the<BR>wind.<BR>--ग्रस्त a. {1} affected by wind,<BR>flatulent. {2} gouty.<BR>--जातः, --तनयः,<BR>नंदनः, --पुत्रः, --सुतः, --सूनुः epithets of<BR>Hanumat or Bhīma.<BR>--दारुः a cloud.<BR>--निघ्न a. affected by wind, crazy,<BR>mad, frantic.<BR>--निवृत्तिः f. {1} a lull,<BR>calm. {2} cure of windy distempers<BR>(such as gout &c.).<BR>--पुराणं N. of<BR>one of the 18 Purāṇas.<BR>--फलं {1}<BR>hail. {2} the rainbow.<BR>--भक्षः, --भक्षणः,<BR>--भुज् m. {1} one who feeds only on<BR>air, as an ascetic. {2} a snake; cf.<BR>पवनाशन.<BR>--रोषा night.<BR>--रुग्ण a.<BR>broken down by wind; R. 9. 63.<BR>--वर्त्मन् m., n. the sky, atmosphere.<BR>--वाहः smoke.<BR>--वाहिनी a vein, an<BR>artery, a vessel of the body.<BR>--वेग,<BR>सम a. swift as wind.<BR>--सखः,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-c" target="_blank">Page0960-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--सखिः m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्
वार् n. Water; Bv. 1. 30.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आसनं a reservoir of water.<BR>--किटिः (वाःकिटिः) a porpoise.<BR>--चः {1}<BR>a goose, gander.<BR>--दः a cloud.<BR>--दरं<BR>{1} water. {2} silk. {3} speech. {4} the<BR>seed of the mango. {5} a curl on a<BR>horse's neck. {6} a conch-shell.<BR>--धिः the ocean. ˚भवं a kind of<BR>salt.<BR>--पुष्पं (वाःपुष्पं) cloves.<BR>--भटः<BR>an alligator.<BR>--मुच् m. a cloud.<BR>--राशिः the ocean.<BR>--वटः a ship,<BR>boat.<BR>--सदनं (वाःसदनं) a<BR>reservoir of water, a cistern.<BR>--स्थ a. (वाःस्थ) being in water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारः|वार|वारं
वारः [वृ-घञ्]<BR>1 That which<BR>covers, a cover.<BR>--2 A multitude,<BR>large number; as in वारयुवति.<BR>--3 A<BR>heap; quantity.<BR>--4 A herd, flock;<BR>Śi. 18. 56.<BR>--5 A day of the week;<BR>as in बुधवार, शनिवार.<BR>--6 Time,<BR>turn; शशकस्य वारः समायातः Pt. 1;<BR>अप्सरावारपर्यायेण V. 5; R. 19. 18;<BR>often used in pl. like the English<BR>‘times’; बहुवारान् ‘many times’<BR>कतिवारान् ‘how many times’.<BR>--7 A<BR>An occasion, opportunity.<BR>--8 A<BR>door, gate.<BR>--9 The opposite bank<BR>of a river.<BR>--10 N. of Śiva.<BR>--11<BR>Ved. A tail.<BR>--रं<BR>1 A vessel for<BR>holding spirituous liquor.<BR>--2 A<BR>mass of water (जलसंघ).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगना, --नारी, --युवति f., योप्रित् f.,<BR>--वनिता, विलासिनी, --सुंदरी, --स्त्री ‘a woman<BR>of the multitude’, a common woman,<BR>harlot, courtezan, prostitute;<BR>Ratn. 1. 26; Ś. Til. 16.<BR>--कीरः {1} a wife's<BR>brother (according to Trik.). {2}<BR>the submarine fire. {3} a<BR>hairdresser or comb. {4} a louse. {5}<BR>a courser. {6} a carrier, porter;<BR>(these meanings are given in<BR>Medinī).<BR>--बु (बू) षा the plantain<BR>tree.<BR>--मुख्या the chief of a number<BR>of harlots.<BR>--बा (वा) णः, --णं<BR>armour, a coat of mail; अगमत्कैतकं रजः ।<BR>तद्याघेवारवाणानामयत्नपटवासतां<BR>R. 4. 55; Śi. 15. 118.<BR>--वाणिः {1} a piper,<BR>player on a flute. {2} a<BR>musician. {3} a year. {4} a judge.<BR>(--णिः f.) a harlot.<BR>--वाणी a harlot.<BR>--वृषा {1} corn. {2} the plantain tree.<BR>--वेला a time or period of the day<BR>when no act is performed.<BR>--सेवा<BR>{1} harlotry, prostitution. {2} a<BR>number of harlots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारक|वारकं|वारकः
वारक a. [वृ-णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">Page0961-a+ 54</a>]<BR>Obstructing, opposing.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A kind of<BR>horse.<BR>--2 A horse in general.<BR>--3<BR>One of the paces of a horse.<BR>--कं<BR>1 The seat of pain.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>perfume (वाल or थीवेर.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0960-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारकिन्
वारकिन् m.<BR>1 An opposer, enemy.<BR>--2 The ocean.<BR>--3 A kind of horse,<BR>one with good marks.<BR>--4 An<BR>ascetic living on leaves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारंकः|वारङ्क|वारंक|वारङ्कः
वारंकः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारंगः|वारङ्ग|वारंग|वारङ्गः
वारंगः<BR>1 The handle of a sword,<BR>knife &c.<BR>--2 The narrow end to<BR>which the handle is fastened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारटं|वारट
वारटं<BR>1 A field.<BR>--2 A number<BR>of fields.<BR>--टा A goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारण|वारणं|वारणः
वारण a. (णी f.) [वृ-ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>Warding off, resisting, opposing.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Warding off, restraining,<BR>obstructing; न भवति बिसतंतुर्वारणं<BR>वारणानां Bh. 2. 17.<BR>--2 An obstacle,<BR>impediment.<BR>--3 Resistance,<BR>opposition.<BR>--4 Defending, guarding,<BR>protecting.<BR>--णः<BR>1 An elephant; न<BR>भवति बिसतंतुर्वारणं वारणानां Bh. 2. 17;<BR>Ku. 5. 70; R. 12. 93; Śi. 18. 56.<BR>--2 An armour, mail-coat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बुषा, --सा, --वल्लभा the plantain tree.<BR>--साह्वयं N. of Hastināpura.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणसी
वारणसी See वाराणसी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणावतः|वारणावत|वारणावतं
वारणावतः --तं N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारणावतं|वारणावत|वारणावतः
वारणावतः --तं N. of a town.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारत्रं|वारत्र
वारत्रं A leather thong.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारंवारं
वारंवारं ind. Often times,<BR>repeatedly, again and again; वारंवारं<BR>तिरयति दृशोरुद्गमं बाष्पपूरः Māl. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारला
वारला<BR>1 A wasp.<BR>--2 A goose;<BR>cf. वरटा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराणसी
वाराणसी The holy city of<BR>Benares.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारांनिधिः|वारान्निधि
वारांनिधिः The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराह|वाराहः
वाराह a. (ही f.) [वराहस्येदं<BR>प्रियत्वात् अण्] Relating to a boar;<BR>वराहीमात्मयोनेस्तनुमवनविधावास्थितस्यानुरूपां<BR>Mu. 7. 19; Y. 1. 259.<BR>--हः<BR>1 A<BR>boar.<BR>--2 A kind of tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कल्पः N. of the present Kalpa<BR>(that in which we are at present<BR>living).<BR>--पुराणं N. of one of the<BR>18 Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाराही
वाराही<BR>1 A sow.<BR>--2 The earth.<BR>--3 The Śakti of Viṣṇu in the form<BR>of a boar.<BR>--4 A measure.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंदः N. of a bulbous plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारि|वारिः
वारि n. [वृ-इण् Uṇ. 4. 124]<BR>1<BR>Water; यथा खनन् खनित्रेण नरो<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-b" target="_blank">Page0961-b+ 56</a>]<BR>वार्यधिगच्छति Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 A fluid.<BR>--3<BR>A kind of perfume (वाल or ह्रीवेर).<BR>--रिः<BR>--री f.<BR>1 A place for fastening<BR>an elephant; वारी वारैः सस्मरे वारणानां<BR>Śi. 18. 56; R. 5. 45.<BR>--2 A rope for<BR>fastening an elephant.<BR>--3 A hole or<BR>trap for catching elephants.<BR>--4 A<BR>captive, prisoner.<BR>--5 A water-pot.<BR>--6 N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>--7 Speech.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः {1} the ocean. {2} N.<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--उद्भवं a lotus.<BR>--ओकः<BR>a leech.<BR>--कर्पूरः a kind of fish (इलीश).<BR>--कुब्जकः the plant शृंगाटक.<BR>--क्रिमिः<BR>a leech.<BR>--चत्वरः a piece of water.<BR>--चर a. aquatic.<BR>--(रः) {1} a fish. {2}<BR>any aquatic animal.<BR>--चामरं moss.<BR>--ज a. produced in water.<BR>--(जः)<BR>{1} a conch-shell; Śi. 15. 72. {2} any<BR>bivalve shell.<BR>--(जं) {1} a lotus;<BR>Śi. 4. 66. {2} a kind of salt. {3} a kind<BR>of plant (गौरसुवर्ण). {4} cloves.<BR>--तस्क्ररः {1} a cloud. {2} the sun.<BR>--त्रा<BR>an umbrella.<BR>--दः a cloud; वितर<BR>वारिद वारि दवातुरे Subhāsh; Bv. 1. 30.<BR>--(दः) a kind of perfume.<BR>--द्रः the<BR>Cātaka bird.<BR>--धरः a cloud;<BR>नववारिधरोदयादहोभेर्भवितव्यं च<BR>निरातपत्वरम्यैः V. 4. 3.<BR>--धारा a shower of<BR>rain.<BR>--धिः {1} the ocean;<BR>वारिधिसुतामक्ष्णां दिदृक्षुः शतैः Gīt. 12. {2} a<BR>jar or pot.<BR>--नाथः {1} the ocean. {2}<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu. {3} a cloud.<BR>{4} the habitation of the<BR>serpentrace.<BR>--निधिः the ocean.<BR>--पथः, --थं<BR>‘journey by sea’, a voyage.<BR>--प्रवाहः<BR>a cascade, water-fall.<BR>--मसिः, --मुच् m.,<BR>--रः a cloud.<BR>--यंत्रं a water-wheel, a<BR>machine for drawing up water;<BR>M. 2. 13.<BR>--रथः a raft, boat, float.<BR>--राशिः {1} the ocean. {2} a lake.<BR>--रुहं a<BR>lotus.<BR>--लोमन् m. N. of Varuṇa.<BR>--वासः a dealer in spirituous liquors.<BR>--वाहः, --वाहनः a cloud; Pt. 2. 142.<BR>--शः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--संभवः {1} cloves.<BR>{2} a kind of antimony. {3} the<BR>fragrant root called उशीर q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारी
वारी See वारि (f.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारीटः|वारीट
वारीटः An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुः|वारु
वारुः A war-elephant(विजयकुंजर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुठः|वारुठ
वारुठः A bier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुण|वारुणं|वारुणः
वारुण a. (णी f.) [वरुणस्येदं अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to Varuṇa; साक्ष्येऽनृतं<BR>वदन् पाशैर्बध्यते वारुणैर्भृशं Ms. 8. 82.<BR>--2 Dedicated or sacred to Varuṇa<BR>--3 Given to Varuṇa.<BR>--णः N. of<BR>one of the nine divisions of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-c" target="_blank">Page0961-c+ 55</a>]<BR>Bhāratavarṣa.<BR>--णं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुणिः|वारुणि
वारुणिः<BR>1 N. of Agastya.<BR>--2 Of<BR>Bhṛgu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुणी
वारुणी<BR>1 The west (the quarter<BR>presided over by Varuṇa).<BR>--2 Any<BR>spirituous liquor; पयोपि शौडिकीहस्ते<BR>वारुणीत्यभिधीयते H. 3. 11;<BR>Pt. 1. 178 (where both senses are<BR>intended); Ku. 4. 12.<BR>--3 The asterism<BR>शतभिषज्.<BR>--4 Dūrvā grass.<BR>--5 N. of<BR>the wife of Varuṇa.<BR>--6 A kind of<BR>Dūrvā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वल्लभः an epithet<BR>of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारुंडः|वारुण्ड|वारुंड|वारुण्डः
वारुंडः The chief of the<BR>serpentrace.<BR>--डः, --डं<BR>1 The rheum or<BR>excretion of the eyes.<BR>--2 The ear-wax.<BR>--3 A vessel for baling water out of<BR>a boat.<BR>--डी A door-step.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वारेंद्री|वारेन्द्री
वारेंद्री N. of a part of Bengal<BR>(and Behar) now called राजशाही.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्क्ष
वार्क्ष a. (र्क्षी f.) [वृक्ष-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Consisting of trees.<BR>--2 Made of or<BR>belonging to a tree.<BR>--3 Made of<BR>bark.<BR>--र्क्षं A forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्क्ष्य|वार्क्ष्यं
वार्क्ष्य a. Made of trees.<BR>--र्क्ष्यं An<BR>enclosure made of trees &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्णिकः|वार्णिक
वार्णिकः A scribe, writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वार्ताकः|वार्ताक|वार्त्ताक|वार्त्ताकः
वार्ताकः, वार्ताकिः f., वार्ताकिन् m., वार्ताकी f., वार्ताकुः m. f.<BR>{ The<BR>eggplant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0961-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

