विकट|विकटः
विकट a.<BR>1 Hideous, ugly.<BR>--2 (a)<BR>Formidable, frightful, horrible,<BR>dreadful;<BR>पृथुललाटतटवटितविकटभ्रूकुटिना Ve. 1; विधुमिव<BR>विकटविधुंतुददंतदलनगलितामृतधारं Gīt. 4. (b) Fierce,<BR>savage.<BR>--3 Great, large, broad, spacious,<BR>wide; जृंभाविडंबि विकटोदरमस्तु चापं<BR>U. 4. 30; आवरिष्ट विकटेन<BR>विवोढुर्वक्षसैव कुचमंडलमन्या Śi. 10. 42,<BR>13. 10; Māl. 7.<BR>--4 Proud, haughty;<BR>विकटं परिक्रामति U. 6; Mv. 6. 32.<BR>--5 Beautiful; Mk. 2.<BR>--6 Frowning.<BR>--7 Obscure.<BR>--8 Changed in<BR>appearance.<BR>--9 Large-toothed.<BR>--टं A boil,<BR>tumour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थ्
विकत्थ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To boast, vaunt;<BR>का खल्वनेन प्रार्थ्यमाना विकत्थते V. 2.<BR>--2 To depreciate, speak ill of,<BR>disparage; सदा भवान् फाल्गुनस्य<BR>गुणैरस्मान् विकत्थते Mb.<BR>--3 To humiliate.<BR>--4 To proclaim loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्थन|विकत्थनं
विकत्थन a.<BR>1 Boasting,<BR>swaggering, vaunting, bragging;<BR>विद्वांसोप्यविकत्थना भवंति Mu. 3; R. 14. 73.<BR>--2 Praising ironically.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Vaunting, boasting.<BR>--2 Irony, false praise.<BR>--3 Praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकत्था
विकत्था<BR>1 Boasting, vaunt, brag,<BR>boast.<BR>--2 Praise.<BR>--3 False praise,<BR>irony.<BR>--4 Proclaiming loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकंप्|विकम्प्
विकंप् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To shake, tremble;<BR>किं यासि बालकदलीव विकंपमाना<BR>Mk. 1. 20; स्फुरति नयनं वामो बाहुर्मुहुश्च<BR>विकंपते 9. 13; Bg. 2. 31.<BR>--2 To<BR>become changed or deformed.<BR>--3 To<BR>shrink or retreat from. --Caus. To<BR>shake; R. 11. 19; Rs. 2. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकंप|विकम्प
विकंप a.<BR>1 Heaving.<BR>--2 Unsteady,<BR>fickle, inconstant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकंपित|विकम्पित|विकम्पितः
विकंपित p. p.<BR>1 Shaken, trembling,<BR>tremulous.<BR>--2 Palpitating, heaving.<BR>--3 Unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकरः|विकर
विकरः Sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकरणः|विकरण
विकरणः The inserted<BR>conjugational affix, the conjugational sign<BR>placed between the root and the<BR>terminations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकराल|विकरालः
विकराल a. Very dreadful or<BR>formidable, frightful; U. 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्णः|विकर्ण
विकर्णः N. of a Kuru prince;<BR>Bg. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्तनः|विकर्तन|विकर्त्तन|विकर्त्तनः
विकर्तनः<BR>1 The sun; U. 5.<BR>--2<BR>The Arka plant.<BR>--3 A son who has<BR>usurped his father's kingdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्मन्|विकर्म्मन्
विकर्मन् a. Acting wrongly. --n.<BR>1 An unlawful or prohibited act, an<BR>impious act; Bg. 4. 17; Ms. 9. 226.<BR>--2 Various or divergent duty.<BR>--3<BR>Retiring from business.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्रिया an illegal act, irreligious<BR>conduct.<BR>--स्थ a. doing prohibited<BR>acts, addicted to vice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्मिक|विकर्मिकः|विकर्म्मिक
