विकालिका A perforated<BR>coppervessel which, placed in water,<BR>marks the time by gradually filling;<BR>cf. मानरंध्रा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाश्
विकाश् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To appear,<BR>become visible.<BR>--2 To bloom, open.<BR>--3 To shine. --Caus.<BR>1 To display,<BR>manifest.<BR>--2 To illuminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशः|विकाश
विकाशः<BR>1 Manifestation, display,<BR>exhibition.<BR>--2 Blowing, expanding<BR>(usually written विकास in this sense);<BR>Ku. 3. 29.<BR>--3 An open or direct<BR>course; विकाशमीयुर्जगतीशमार्गणाः<BR>Ki. 15. 52.<BR>--4 An oblique course;<BR>Ki. 15. 52.<BR>--5 Joy, pleasure; Ki. 15. 52.<BR>--6 Sky, heaven (आकाश);<BR>Ki. 15. 52.<BR>--7 Eagerness, ardent desire;<BR>Śi. 9. 41 (where it means ‘blowing’<BR>also).<BR>--8 Retreat, solitude, privacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशक
विकाशक a. (शिका f.)<BR>1 Displaying.<BR>--2 Opening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशनं|विकाशन
विकाशनं<BR>1 Manifestation, display,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">Page0966-a+ 55</a>]<BR>exhibition.<BR>--2 Blowing, expanding<BR>(of flowers &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0965-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकाशिन्
विकाशि(सि)न् a. (नी f.)<BR>1<BR>Becoming visible, shining forth.<BR>--2<BR>Expanding, opening, blowing.<BR>--3<BR>Shining, resplendent; Pt. 3. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकासिन्
विकाशि(सि)न् a. (नी f.)<BR>1<BR>Becoming visible, shining forth.<BR>--2<BR>Expanding, opening, blowing.<BR>--3<BR>Shining, resplendent; Pt. 3. 147.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुंठ|विकुण्ठ
विकुंठ N. of Viṣṇu's heaven.<BR>--ठा N. of the mother of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुंठित|विकुण्ठित
विकुंठित a.<BR>1 Obtuse, blunt.<BR>--2<BR>Weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुस्रः|विकुस्र
विकुस्रः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूजनं|विकूजन
विकूजनं<BR>1 Cooing, humming.<BR>--2<BR>Rumbling (as of the bowels).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणनं|विकूणन
विकूणनं A side-glance, leer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकूणिका
विकूणिका The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृ
विकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To alter, change,<BR>affect; विकारहेतौ सति विक्रियंते येषां न<BR>चेतांसि त एव धीराः Ku. 1. 59;<BR>R. 13. 42.<BR>--2 To disfigure, deform;<BR>विकृताकृति Ms. 9. 52.<BR>--3 To create,<BR>produce, effect; Ms. 1. 75; नास्य विघ्नं<BR>विकुर्विंति दानवाः Mb.<BR>--4 To disturb,<BR>harm, injure (A.);<BR>हीनान्यनुपकर्तॄणि प्रवृद्धानि विकुर्वते R. 17. 58.<BR>--5 To<BR>utter (a sound); विकुर्वाणः स्वरानद्य<BR>Bk. 8. 20.<BR>--6 To be faithless (as a<BR>wife).<BR>--7 To deprave, pervert,<BR>spoil.<BR>--8 To display.<BR>--9 To change<BR>for the worse, deteriorate (A.).<BR>--10 To<BR>rejoice (A.).<BR>--11 To feel aversion<BR>(A.).<BR>--12 To act in various ways<BR>(A.).<BR>--13 To decorate in various<BR>ways.<BR>--14 To exercise.<BR>--15 To<BR>distribute.<BR>--16 To destroy, ruin.<BR>--17<BR>To spread, extend.<BR>--18 To become<BR>restless; move to and fro.<BR>--19 To<BR>act in a hostile manner.<BR>--20 To<BR>contend together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारः|विकार
विकारः<BR>1 Change of form or<BR>nature, transformation, deviation from<BR>the natural state; cf. विकृति.<BR>--2 A<BR>change, alteration, a modification;<BR>Pt. 1. 44; Ś. 7.<BR>--3 Sickness,<BR>disease, malady; विकारं खलु<BR>परमार्थतोऽज्ञात्वाऽनारंभः प्रतीकारस्य Ś. 4;<BR>Ku. 2. 48.<BR>--4 Change of mind or<BR>purpose; मूर्छंत्यमी विकाराः प्रायेणैश्वर्यमत्तेषु<BR>Ś. 5. 18.<BR>--5 A feeling, an emotion;<BR>विकारश्चैतन्यं भ्रमयति च संमीलयति च<BR>U. 1. 35, 3. 25, 36; Māl. 1. 30.<BR>--6<BR>Agitation, excitement, perturbation;<BR>Ki. 17. 23.<BR>--7 Contortion, contraction (as<BR>of the features of the face);<BR>प्रमथमुखबिकारैर्हासयामास गूढं Ku. 7. 95.<BR>--8 (In Sān, phil.) That which is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">Page0966-b+ 56</a>]<BR>evolved from a previous source or<BR>Prakṛti.<BR>--9 A wound.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हेतुः a temptation, seduction,<BR>cause of perturbation; विकारहेतौ<BR>सति विक्रियंते येषां न चेतांसि त एव धीराः<BR>Ku. 1. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारित
विकारित a. Changed, perverted,<BR>corrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकारिन्
विकारिन् a.<BR>1 Liable to change,<BR>susceptible of emotions or<BR>impressions; भ्रमति भुवने कंदर्पाज्ञा विकारि च<BR>यौवनं Māl. 1. 17.<BR>--2 Changing,<BR>modifying.<BR>--3 Spoiling, corrupting.<BR>--4<BR>Affected by love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकुर्वाण|विकुर्व्वाण|विकुर्व्वाणः
विकुर्वाण a.<BR>1 Undergoing or<BR>causing a change.<BR>--2 Feeling glad,<BR>delighted, rejoiced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृत|विकृतं
विकृत p. p.<BR>1 Changed, altered,<BR>modified.<BR>--2 Sick, diseased.<BR>--3<BR>Mutilated, deformed, disfigured.<BR>--4<BR>Incomplete, imperfect.<BR>--5 Affected<BR>by passion or emotion.<BR>--6 Averse<BR>from, disgusted with.<BR>--7 Loathsome.<BR>--8 Strange, extraordinary.<BR>--9<BR>Unnatural.<BR>--10 Perverted,<BR>spoiled; see विकृ above.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Change, modification.<BR>--2 Change for<BR>the worse, sickness.<BR>--3 Aversion,<BR>disgust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृतिः|विकृति
विकृतिः f.<BR>1 Change(as of<BR>purpose, mind, form &c.);<BR>चित्तविकृतिः, अंगुलीयकं सुवर्णस्य विकृतिः &c.<BR>--2<BR>An unnatural or accidental<BR>circumstance, an accident; मरणं प्रकृतिः<BR>शरीरिणां विकृतिर्जीवितमुच्यते बुधैः<BR>R. 8. 87.<BR>--3 Sickness.<BR>--4<BR>Excitement, perturbation, anger, rage;<BR>Ki. 13. 56; U. 5. 29;<BR>Śi. 15. 11, 40.<BR>--5 Emotion;<BR>Ś. 2. 5.<BR>--6 A sudden seizure or<BR>affection.<BR>--7 Fermented liquor; see<BR>विकार and विक्रिया also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृष्
विकृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To draw, pull.<BR>--2<BR>To bend (as a bow); शरासनं तेषु<BR>विकृष्यतामिदं Ś. 6. 28.<BR>--3 To deprive of,<BR>withhold, keep back.<BR>--4 To destroy,<BR>ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्षः|विकर्ष
विकर्षः<BR>1 Drawing asunder,<BR>pulling apart.<BR>--2 An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकर्षणः|विकर्षण|विकर्षणं
विकर्षणः N. of one of the five<BR>arrows of Cupid.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Drawing,<BR>dragging, pulling asunder.<BR>--2 A<BR>cross throw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकृष्ट|विकृष्टः
विकृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Dragged asunder,<BR>pulled hither and thither.<BR>--2<BR>Drawn, pulled, drawn towards or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-c" target="_blank">Page0966-c+ 56</a>]<BR>attracted.<BR>--3 Extended, protracted.<BR>--4 Making a noise; (see कृष् with<BR>वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकॄ
विकॄ^1 {c6c} P.<BR>1 To scatter, throw<BR>about; strew or spread about;<BR>Ku. 3. 61; Ki. 2. 59; Bk. 1. 3;<BR>14. 25.<BR>--2 To split, cut to pieces;<BR>असिर्गात्रं गात्रं सपदि लवशस्ते विकिरतु<BR>Māl. 5. 34.<BR>--3 To pollute, contaminate.<BR>--4 To dissolve.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: print vague; by sense must be vikF.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिरः|विकिर
विकिरः<BR>1 A scattered portion or<BR>fallen bit.<BR>--2 One who tears or<BR>scatters, a bird;<BR>कंकोलीफलजग्धिमुग्धविकिरव्याहारिणस्तद्भुवो भागाः<BR>Māl. 6. 19.<BR>--3 A well.<BR>--4 A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकिरणं|विकिरण|विकिरणः
विकिरणं<BR>1 Scattering, throwing<BR>about, dispersing.<BR>--2 Spreading<BR>abroad.<BR>--3 Tearing up.<BR>--4 Killing<BR>(हिंसन).<BR>--5 Knowledge.<BR>--णः The<BR>Arka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकीर्ण|विकीर्णः
विकीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Scattered,<BR>dispersed.<BR>--2 Diffused.<BR>--3 Celebrated.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केश, --मूर्धज a. tearing<BR>the hair, having dishevelled hair;<BR>विललाप विकीर्णमूर्वजा Ku. 4. 4.<BR>--ज्ञं<BR>a kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकॢप्
विकॢप् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To doubt, be<BR>doubtful; Pt. 1. 339.<BR>--2 To be<BR>optional. --Caus.<BR>1 To doubt,<BR>question.<BR>--2 To consider, reflect<BR>upon; सखीनियोगोऽपि विकल्प्यते Ś. 3.<BR>--3 To presume, conjecture.<BR>--4 To<BR>prepare or arrange differently.<BR>--5<BR>To make, form.<BR>--6 To exchange.<BR>--7<BR>To admit as optional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पः|विकल्प
विकल्पः<BR>1 Doubt, uncertainty,<BR>indecision, hesitation; तत्सिषेवे<BR>नियोगेन स विकल्पपराङ्मुखः R. 17. 49.<BR>--2<BR>Suspicion; Mu. 1.<BR>--3 Contrivance,<BR>art; मायाविकल्परचितैः R. 13. 75.<BR>--4<BR>Option, alternative (in gram.).<BR>--5<BR>Sort, variety.<BR>--6 An error, a<BR>mistake, ignorance.<BR>--7 Distinction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपहारः an optional<BR>offering.<BR>--जालं a net-like indecision,<BR>a dilemma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकल्पनं|विकल्पन
विकल्पनं<BR>1 Admitting of a doubt.<BR>--2 Allowing an option.<BR>--3<BR>Indecision.<BR>--4 Inconsideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकेश
विकेश a. (शी f.)<BR>1 Having<BR>loose hair.<BR>--2 Having no hair, bald<BR>(as head).<BR>--शी<BR>1 A woman with<BR>loose hair.<BR>--2 A woman without<BR>hair.<BR>--3 A small tress of hair tied<BR>up separately and then collected<BR>into the larger braid or Veṇi.<BR>--4<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">Page0967-a+ 56</a>]<BR>N. of the wife of Śiva in the form<BR>of the Earth (one of the 8 forms of<BR>Śiva; cf. यामाहुः सर्वभूतप्रकृतिः Ś. 1. 1.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0966-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकोश
विकोश --ष a.<BR>1 Without husk.<BR>--2 Unsheathed, uncovered;<BR>Ki. 17. 45; R. 7. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विकोष|विकोषः
विकोश --ष a.<BR>1 Without husk.<BR>--2 Unsheathed, uncovered;<BR>Ki. 17. 45; R. 7. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्कः|विक्क
विक्कः A young elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रम्
विक्रम् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To walk along or<BR>through; विष्णुस्त्रेधा विचक्रमे ‘took<BR>{3} steps’; Bk. 1. 24.<BR>--2 To assail,<BR>overcome, conquer.<BR>--3 To cleave;<BR>split open (P.)<BR>--4 To advance,<BR>proceed.<BR>--5 To show prowess or<BR>valour; Māl. 8. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमः|विक्रम
विक्रमः<BR>1 A step, stride, pace;<BR>गतेषु लीलांचितविक्रमेषु Ku. 1. 34;<BR>Ś. 7. 6; cf. त्रिविक्रम.<BR>--2 Stepping<BR>over, walking.<BR>--3 Overcoming,<BR>overpowering.<BR>--4 Heroism, prowess,<BR>heroic valour; अनुत्सेकः खलु<BR>विक्रमालंकारः V. 1; R. 12. 87, 93.<BR>--5 N.<BR>of a celebrated king of Ujjayinī;<BR>see App. II.<BR>--6 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--7<BR>Strength, power.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्कः,<BR>--आदित्यः see विक्रम.<BR>--कर्मन् n. a<BR>heroic deed, feat of valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमणं|विक्रमण
विक्रमणं A stride (of Viṣṇu);<BR>छलयसि विक्रमणे बलिमद्भुतवामन Gīt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रमिन्
विक्रमिन्^1 a.<BR>1 Chivalrous, heroic.<BR>--2 Powerful, strong. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>lion.<BR>--2 A hero.<BR>--3 An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: print vague; 'mit' not valid ending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रांत|विक्रान्त|विक्रान्तं|विक्रान्तः
विक्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Stepped or<BR>passed beyond.<BR>--2 Powerful, heroic,<BR>valiant, chivalrous.<BR>--3 Victorious,<BR>overpowering (one's enemies).<BR>--तः<BR>1 A hero, warrior.<BR>--2 A lion.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>A pace, stride.<BR>--2 Heroism, valour,<BR>prowess.<BR>--3 The jewel called वैक्रात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रांतिः|विक्रान्ति|विक्रांति|विक्रान्तिः
विक्रांतिः f.<BR>1 Stepping, striding.<BR>--2 A horse's gallop or canter.<BR>--3<BR>Heroism, valour, prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रांतृ|विक्रान्तृ
विक्रांतृ a. Valiant, victorious. --m.<BR>1 A lion.<BR>--2 A hero, victor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रस्रः|विक्रस्र
विक्रस्रः The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रिया
विक्रिया<BR>1 Change, modification,<BR>alternation;<BR>श्मश्रुप्रवृद्धिजनिताननविक्रियान् R. 13. 71, 10. 17.<BR>--2 Agitation,<BR>excitement, perturbation, excitement of<BR>passion; अथ तेन निगृह्य विक्रियामभिशप्तः<BR>फलमेतदन्वभूत् Ku. 4. 41, 3. 34.<BR>--3<BR>Anger, wrath, displeasure; साधोः<BR>प्रकोपितस्यापि मनो नायाति विक्रियां<BR>Subhāṣ.; लिंगैर्मुदः संवृतविक्रियास्ते<BR>R. 7. 30.<BR>--4 Reverse, evil;<BR>Ku. 6. 29 (वैकल्यं Malli. ‘defect’.)<BR>--5<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">Page0967-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Knitting, contraction (of the<BR>eyebrows); भ्रूविक्रियायां विरतप्रसंगैः<BR>Ku. 3. 47.<BR>--6 Any sudden movement, as in<BR>रोमविक्रिया V. 1. 12 ‘thrill’.<BR>--7 A sudden<BR>affection or seizure, disease.<BR>--8<BR>Violation, vitiation (of the proper<BR>duties); R. 15. 48.<BR>--9 A preparation<BR>or dish of rice &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपमा<BR>a kind of Upamā mentioned by<BR>Daṇḍin; see Kāv. 2. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्री
विक्री {c9c} A.<BR>1 To sell (Atm. in<BR>this sense); गवां शतसहस्रेण<BR>विक्रीणीषे सुतं यदि Rām; विक्रीणीत तिलाञ्<BR>शुद्धान् Ms. 10. 90; 8. 197, 222;<BR>Śānti. 1. 12.<BR>--2 To barter, exchange;<BR>नाक्रस्माच्छांडिलीमाता विक्रीणाति<BR>तिलैस्तिलान् Pt. 2. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयः|विक्रय|विक्रयं
विक्रयः Sale, selling: Ms. 3. 54.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुशयः rescission of a<BR>sale.<BR>--पत्रं a bill of sale, sale-deed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयिकः|विक्रयिक
विक्रयिकः, विक्रयिन् m. A dealer,<BR>seller, vendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रयिन्
विक्रयिकः, विक्रयिन् m. A dealer,<BR>seller, vendor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रेय|विक्रेयं
विक्रेय a. Saleable, vendible (as<BR>an article).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रुश्
विक्रुश् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To call aloud,<BR>cry out loudly; आक्रोश विक्रोश<BR>लपाधिचंडं Mk. 1. 41; Bk. 14. 42;<BR>16. 32.<BR>--2 To utter (with acc.).<BR>--3 To<BR>call out to (with acc.).<BR>--4 To<BR>resound.<BR>--5 To abuse, revile, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रुष्ट|विक्रुष्टं
विक्रुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Exclaimed, cried<BR>out.<BR>--2 Harsh, cruel, unkind.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 A cry for help.<BR>--2 Abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रोशनं|विक्रोशन
विक्रोशनं<BR>1 Calling out,<BR>exclaiming.<BR>--2 Abusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लव|विक्लवः
विक्लव a.<BR>1 Overcome with fear,<BR>startled, alarmed, frightened;<BR>आचकांक्ष घनशब्दविक्लवाः R. 19. 38;<BR>Ku. 4. 11.<BR>--2 Timid; Śi. 7. 43;<BR>Me. 37.<BR>--3 Affected by, overcome with;<BR>निसर्गदुर्बोधमबोधविक्लवाः क्व भूपतीनां<BR>चरितं क्व जतवः Ki. 1. 6.<BR>--4 Agitated,<BR>excited, confused, bewildered;<BR>Ś. 3. 25.<BR>--5 Distressed, afflicted; grieved;<BR>निराकरणविक्लवायाः प्रियायाः Ś. 6;<BR>Śi. 12. 63; Ku. 4. 39.<BR>--6 Disgusted<BR>with, averse from; मृगयाविक्लवं चेतः<BR>Ś. 2.<BR>--7 Faltering; प्रस्थानाविक्लव<BR>गतेरवलंबनार्थं Ś. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लिन्न|विक्लिन्नः
विक्लिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Very moist,<BR>thoroughly wetted.<BR>--2 Decayed,<BR>withered up.<BR>--3 Old.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लिष्ट
विक्लिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Excessively<BR>afflicted, distressed.<BR>--2 Injured,<BR>destroyed.<BR>--ष्टं A fault in<BR>pronunciation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लेदः|विक्लेद
विक्लेदः<BR>1 Wetting thoroughly.<BR>--2<BR>Dissolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्लेशः|विक्लेश
विक्लेशः An incorrect<BR>pronunciation of the dentals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षत|विक्षतः
विक्षत p. p. Torn asunder,<BR>wounded, hurt, struck.<BR>--तं<BR>Wounding, a wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षावः|विक्षाव
विक्षावः<BR>1 Cough, sneezing.<BR>--2<BR>A sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षिप्
विक्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To throw about,<BR>scatter.<BR>--2 To throw, cast.<BR>--3<BR>To divert.<BR>--4 To distract.<BR>--5 To<BR>extend, stretch out.<BR>--6 To<BR>reject, discard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षिप्त|विक्षिप्तः
विक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Scattered, thrown<BR>about, dispersed, cast about.<BR>--2<BR>Discarded, dismissed.<BR>--3 Sent,<BR>despatched.<BR>--4 Distracted,<BR>bewildered, agitated; Māl. 9. 8.<BR>--5<BR>Refuted; (see क्षिप् with वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपः|विक्षेप
विक्षेपः<BR>1 Throwing away or<BR>asunder, scattering about.<BR>--2 Casting,<BR>throwing, discharging (opp. संहार);<BR>R. 5. 45.<BR>--3 Waving, moving about,<BR>shaking, moving to and fro; लांगूल˚<BR>Ku. 1. 13.<BR>--4 Sending,<BR>despatching.<BR>--5 Distraction, confusion,<BR>perplexity; Māl. 1.<BR>--6 Alarm, fear.<BR>--7 Refutation of an argument.<BR>--8<BR>Polar latitude.<BR>--9 Looking about<BR>vaguely or wildly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ध्रुवः<BR>(in astr.) the greatest inclination<BR>of a planet's orbit.<BR>--शक्ति f. (in<BR>Vedānta phil.) the power of Māyā<BR>(अविद्या).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षेपणं|विक्षेपण
विक्षेपणं<BR>1 Throwing, casting,<BR>discharging.<BR>--2 Despatching, sending.<BR>--3 Scattering, dispersing.<BR>--4<BR>Confusion, perplexity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षीणकः|विक्षीणक
विक्षीणकः<BR>1 N. of the chief of<BR>a class of beings attending on Śiva.<BR>--2 An assembly of the gods.<BR>--3<BR>A destroyer.<BR>--4 A place from which<BR>flesh-eaters are excluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षीरः|विक्षीर
विक्षीरः The Arka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षुभ्
विक्षुभ् {c1c} A., {c4c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To be<BR>greatly agitated or disturbed.<BR>--2<BR>To confuse, disturb, perplex.<BR>--Caus. To agitate, disturb, confuse<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्षोभः|विक्षोभ
विक्षोभः<BR>1 Shaking. agitation,<BR>movement; वीचि˚ R. 1. 43.<BR>--2<BR>Agitation of mind, distraction, alarm.<BR>--3 Conflict, struggle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0967-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख|विखः
विख a. Noseless.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नस् m. an epithet<BR>of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखु|विखुः
विखु a. Noseless.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नस् m. an epithet<BR>of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्य|विख्यः
विख्य a. Noseless.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नस् m. an epithet<BR>of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्र|विख्रः
विख्र a. Noseless.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नस् m. an epithet<BR>of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्रु|विख्रुः
विख्रु a. Noseless.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नस् m. an epithet<BR>of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्र|विग्रः
विग्र a. Noseless.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नस् m. an epithet<BR>of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखंडित|विखण्डित
विखंडित p. p.<BR>1 Broken up,<BR>divided.<BR>--2 Cleft in two.<BR>--3<BR>Disfigured, mutilated; Pt. 4. 89.<BR>--4<BR>Refuted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखानसः|विखानस
विखानसः A kind of hermit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखासा
विखासा The tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विखुरः|विखुर
विखुरः<BR>1 A demon, goblin.<BR>--2<BR>A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्या
विख्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 To be well-known<BR>or famous.<BR>--2 To look at, see.<BR>--3<BR>To call, name.<BR>--4 To celebrate.<BR>--5<BR>To make visible, illuminate. --Caus.<BR>To proclaim, announce, publish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यात|विख्यातः
विख्यात p. p.<BR>1 Renowned,<BR>wellknown, celebrated, famous.<BR>--2<BR>Called, named.<BR>--3 Avowed,<BR>confessed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यातिः|विख्याति
विख्यातिः f. Celebrity, fame,<BR>reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विख्यापनं|विख्यापन
विख्यापनं<BR>1 Publishing,<BR>proclaiming.<BR>--2 Explanation, exposition.<BR>--3<BR>Confessing, acknowledging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगण्
विगण् {c10c} P.<BR>1 To number,<BR>compute; Y. 3. 104.<BR>--2 To regard,<BR>consider; Me. 109; R. 1. 87.<BR>--3 To<BR>disregard, not to mind.<BR>--4 To<BR>reflect, think; Pt. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगणनं|विगणन
विगणनं<BR>1 Reckoning, computing,<BR>calculation.<BR>--2 Considering,<BR>deliberating.<BR>--3 Paying off a debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगंधकः|विगन्धक|विगंधक|विगन्धकः
विगंधकः The tree called इंगुदी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगम्
विगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To pass away (as<BR>time &c.); संध्ययापि सपदि व्यगमि<BR>Śi. 9. 17.<BR>--2 To go away, depart.<BR>--3<BR>To vanish; disappear; सलज्जाया<BR>लज्जा व्यगमदिव दूरं मृगदृशः Gīt. 11;<BR>Bg. 11. 1.<BR>--4 To die. --Caus. To<BR>spend, pass; विगमयत्युन्निद्र एव क्षपाः<BR>Ś. 6. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगत|विगतः
विगत p. p.<BR>1 Departed, gone<BR>away, disappeared.<BR>--2 Parted,<BR>separated.<BR>--3 Dead.<BR>--4 Destitute or<BR>devoid of, free from (in comp.).<BR>विगतमदः.<BR>--5 Lost.<BR>--6 Dark,<BR>obscurd.<BR>--तं The flight of birds.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आर्तवां a woman past<BR>child-bearing (in whom the menstrual<BR>discharge has ceased).<BR>--कल्मष a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">Page0968-b+ 56</a>]<BR>sinless, pure.<BR>--भी a. fearless, intrepid.<BR>--लक्षण a. unlucky, inauspicious.<BR>--स्पृह a. indifferent, void of desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगमः|विगम
विगमः<BR>1 Departure,<BR>disappearance, cessation, end; चारुनृत्यविगमे<BR>च तन्मुखं R. 19. 15; ईतिविगम<BR>M. 5. 20; Rs. 6. 23.<BR>--2 Abandoning;<BR>करणविगमात् Me. 55 (देहत्यागात्).<BR>--3<BR>Loss, destruction.<BR>--4 Death.<BR>--5<BR>Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगरः|विगर
विगरः<BR>1 A naked ascetic.<BR>--2 A<BR>mountain.<BR>--3 An abstemious man<BR>(abstaining from eating).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्ह्
विगर्ह् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To blame, censure,<BR>reproach; तं विगर्हंति साधवः<BR>Ms. 9. 68; 3. 46; 11. 53.<BR>--2 To despise,<BR>contemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हणं|विगर्हण
विगर्हणं, --णा Censure, blame,<BR>reproach, abuse; Ve. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हणा
विगर्हणं, --णा Censure, blame,<BR>reproach, abuse; Ve. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगर्हित|विगर्हितः
विगर्हित p. p.<BR>1 Censured, reviled,<BR>abused.<BR>--2 Disdained.<BR>--3<BR>Condemned, reprobated, prohibited.<BR>--4 Low,<BR>vile.<BR>--5 Bad, wicked.<BR>--तं Censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगल्
विगल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To drop down, get<BR>loose; रतिविगलितवंधे केशहस्ते सुकेश्याः<BR>V. 4. 10.<BR>--2 To ooze or trickle.<BR>--3 To<BR>vanish, disappear.<BR>--4 To melt away,<BR>be dissolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगलित|विगलितः
विगलित p. p.<BR>1 Trickled, oozed.<BR>--2 Disappeared, gone away.<BR>--3<BR>Fallen or dropped down.<BR>--4<BR>Melted away, dissolved.<BR>--5 Dispersed.<BR>--6 Slackened. untied.<BR>--7 Loose,<BR>dishevelled, disordered (as hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाह्
विगाह् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To plunge or dive<BR>into, bathe; (दीर्घिकाः) स व्यगाहत<BR>विगाढमन्मथः R. 19. 9.<BR>--2 To enter,<BR>penetrate into, pervade (fig. also);<BR>विषमोऽपि विगाह्यते नयः कृततीर्थः<BR>पयसामिवाशयः Ki. 2. 3; R. 13. 1,<BR>Mu. 1. 26.<BR>--3 To stir about, agitate;<BR>विगाह्यमानां सरयूं च नौभिः R. 14. 30.<BR>--4 To follow, practise; तया मुनीनां<BR>चरितं व्यगाह्यत Ku. 5. 19.<BR>--5 To<BR>approach, set in (as season &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाढ|विगाढः
विगाढ p. p.<BR>1 Plunged into,<BR>bathed, immersed.<BR>--2 Deep,<BR>excessive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगाहः|विगाह
विगाहः Plunging into, bathing,<BR>diving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगुण|विगुणः
विगुण a.<BR>1 Destitute of merits,<BR>worthless, bad; श्रेयान्स्वधर्मो विगुणः<BR>परधर्मात्स्वनुष्ठितात् Bg. 3. 35;<BR>Śi. 9. 12, Mu. 6. 11.<BR>--2 Destitute of<BR>qualities.<BR>--3 Having no string;<BR>Mu. 7. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगूढ|विगूढः
विगूढ p. p.<BR>1 Secret, concealed,<BR>hidden.<BR>--2 Reproached, censured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगै
विगै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To censure, reproach,<BR>blame; विगीयसे मन्मथदेहदाहिना<BR>N. 1. 79.<BR>--2 To sing in a<BR>discordant tone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगानं|विगान
विगानं<BR>1 Censure, reproach,<BR>defamation, scandal.<BR>--2 A<BR>contradictory statement, contradiction,<BR>inconsistency; यत्पुनः कारणविषयं विगानं<BR>दर्शितं तत्परिहर्तव्यं Ś. B. (and in<BR>several other places of the same work).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगीत
विगीत p. p.<BR>1 Censured, abused,<BR>reviled.<BR>--2 Contradictory,<BR>inconsistent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगीतिः|विगीति
विगीतिः f.<BR>1 Censure, abuse,<BR>reproach.<BR>--2 Contradictory statement,<BR>contradiction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रह्
विग्रह् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To hold or seize,<BR>catch hold of; विजगृहे तिसृणां जयिनं<BR>पुरां Ki. 18. 12.<BR>--2 To quarrel,<BR>fight, contend; विगृह्य चक्रे नमुचिद्विषा<BR>बली य इत्थमस्वास्थ्यमहर्दिवं दिवः<BR>Śi. 1. 51; Bk. 6. 86; 17. 23, Ki. 14. 24.<BR>--3 To divide into parts, separate<BR>(into constituent members).<BR>--4<BR>To dissolve, analyse, resolve in<BR>general.<BR>--5 To receive, welcome (as<BR>a guest).<BR>--6 To perceive, observe.<BR>--7 To stretch or spread out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विगृहीत
विगृहीत p. p.<BR>1 Divided,<BR>dissolved, analysed, resolved (as a<BR>compound).<BR>--2 Seized.<BR>--3<BR>Encountered, opposed.<BR>--4 Obstructed, stopped;<BR>see विग्रह् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहः|विग्रह
विग्रहः<BR>1 Stretching out,<BR>extension, expansion.<BR>--2 Form, figure,<BR>shape.<BR>--3 The body; त्रयी<BR>विग्रहवत्येव सममध्यात्मविद्यया M. 1. 14; गूढविग्रहः<BR>R. 3. 39, 9. 52; Ki. 4. 11, 12. 43.<BR>--4 Resolution, dissolution,<BR>analysis, separation (as of a compound<BR>word into its component parts);<BR>वृत्त्यर्थ (समासार्थ) बोधकं वाक्यं विग्रहः.<BR>--5 Quarrel, strife (often,<BR>lovequarrel or प्रणयकलह); विग्रहाच्च शयने<BR>पराङ्मुखीर्नानुनेतुमबलाः स तत्वरे<BR>R. 19. 38, 9. 47; Śi. 11. 35.<BR>--6 War,<BR>hostilities, fighting, battle (opp.<BR>संधि), one of the six Guṇas or<BR>modes of policy; see गुण.<BR>--7<BR>Disfavour.<BR>--8 A part, portion, division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रहवत्|विग्रहवन्त्
विग्रहवत् a. having, body,<BR>incarnate, embodied; M. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्रीव
विग्रीव a. Decapitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0968-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्
विघट् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To be disunited<BR>or separated.<BR>--2 To be spoiled or<BR>ruined.<BR>--3 To be stopped, break<BR>down.<BR>--4 To assume various shapes;<BR>Māl. 9. 24. --Caus.<BR>1 To separate,<BR>disperse, tear apart;<BR>विघटयंत्यग्रेनभोंऽभोमुचः Māl. 5. 2.<BR>--2 To remove,<BR>displace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटनं|विघटन
विघटनं Beaking up, ruin,<BR>destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटित
विघटित p. p.<BR>1 Separated,<BR>severed.<BR>--2 Divided.<BR>--3 Broken,<BR>shattered; U. 3. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघटिका
विघटिका A measure of time<BR>equal to one-sixtieth part of<BR>a Ghaṭikā (or nearly equal<BR>to 24 seconds).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्ट्
विघट्ट् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To strike down,<BR>disperse, scatter, scare away;<BR>Śi. 1. 64; Bh. 3. 54.<BR>--2 To rub, strike,<BR>rub against;<BR>कारंडवाननविघट्टितवीचिमालाः Rs. 3. 8; 4. 9; विघटृइतानां<BR>सरलद्रुमाणां Ku. 1. 9 Ki. 8. 45; Śi. 8. 24,<BR>13. 41.<BR>--3 To break, violate (as an<BR>agreement).<BR>--4 To break asunder,<BR>burst open (as a door).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टनं|विघट्टन
विघट्टनं --ना<BR>1 Striking asunder.<BR>--2<BR>Striking against, friction.<BR>--3<BR>Separating, undoing, untying.<BR>--4<BR>Offending, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टना
विघट्टनं --ना<BR>1 Striking asunder.<BR>--2<BR>Striking against, friction.<BR>--3<BR>Separating, undoing, untying.<BR>--4<BR>Offending, hurting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघट्टित|विघट्टितं
विघट्टित p. p.<BR>1 Struck apart,<BR>severed, separated, dispersed;<BR>Bh. 3. 54.<BR>--2 Untied, loosened, opened.<BR>--3 Rubbed, touched.<BR>--4 Shaken<BR>about, churned.<BR>--5 Hurt, offended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघनः|विघन
विघनः<BR>1 A mallet, hammer.<BR>--2<BR>One who destroys, subdues or<BR>overpowers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघसः|विघस|विघसं
विघसः<BR>1 Half-chewed morsel,<BR>the residue or leavings of food<BR>eaten; विघसो भुक्तशेषं तु Ms. 3. 285;<BR>तृप्यत्कालकरालवक्त्रविघसव्याकीर्यमाणा<BR>इव U. 5. 6; Māl. 5. 14.<BR>--2 Food in<BR>general.<BR>--सं Bees'-wax.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशः, --आशिन् m. one who eats<BR>the remains of an offering or of<BR>food eaten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघातः|विघात
विघातः<BR>1 Destruction,<BR>removing, warding off; क्रियादवानां मघवा<BR>विघातं Ki. 3. 52.<BR>--2 Killing, slaying.<BR>--3 An obstacle, impediment,<BR>interruption; opposition, prevention;<BR>क्रियाविघाताय कथं प्रवर्तसे R. 3. 44;<BR>अध्वरविघातशांतये 11. 1.<BR>--4 A blow,<BR>stroke.<BR>--5 Abandoning, leaving.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">Page0969-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सिद्धिः f. the removal of<BR>obstacles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघूर्णित
विघूर्णित p. p. Rolled, shaken<BR>about, rolling (as eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघृष्ट
विघृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Rubbed<BR>excessively.<BR>--2 Sore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नः|विघ्न
विघ्नः [विहन्-क] (rarely n.)<BR>1<BR>An obstacle, interruption,<BR>impediment, a hindrance; कुतो धर्मक्रियाविघ्नः<BR>सतां रक्षितरि त्वयि Ś. 5. 14; मूर्तो<BR>विघ्नस्तपस इव नः Ś. 1. 33; हुंकारेणेव धनुषः<BR>स हि विघ्नानपोहति Ś. 3. 1; Ku. 3. 40.<BR>--2 Difficulty, trouble.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः, --ईशानः, --ईश्वरः epithets of Gaṇeśa.<BR>˚वाहनं a rat.<BR>--कर, --कर्तृ, --कारिन् a.<BR>opposing, obstructing.<BR>--ध्वंसः,<BR>--विघातः removal of obstacles.<BR>--नायकः,<BR>--नाशकः, --नाशनः epithets of Gaṇeśa.<BR>--प्रतिक्रिया removal of impediments;<BR>R. 15. 4.<BR>--राजः --विनायकः, --हारिन्<BR>m. epithets of Gaṇeśa.<BR>--सिद्धिः f.<BR>removal of obstacles.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नयति
विघ्नयति Den. P. To obstruct,<BR>hinder, impede, oppose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विघ्नित|विघ्नितः
विघ्नित a.<BR>1 Impeded, hindered,<BR>obstructed, opposed; Pt. 1. 387.<BR>--2 Obscured, blinded; Ku. 3. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंखः|विङ्ख|विंख|विङ्खः
विंखः A horse's hoof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्
विच् {c3c} {c7c} U. (वेवोक्ति, वेविक्ते,<BR>विनक्ति, विंक्ते, विक्त)<BR>1 To separate, divide,<BR>sever.<BR>--2 To discriminate,<BR>distinguish, discern.<BR>--3 To deprive of,<BR>remove from (with instr.); शशास स<BR>बहून्योधान् जीवितेन विवेच च<BR>Bk. 14. 103.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचकिलः|विचकिल
विचकिलः<BR>1 A kind of jasmine.<BR>--2 N. of the tree called Madana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचक्षण|विचक्षणः
विचक्षण a.<BR>1 Clear sighted,<BR>far-seeing, circumspect.<BR>--2 Wise, clever,<BR>learned; विचक्षणः प्रस्तुतमाचचक्षे<BR>R. 5. 19.<BR>--3 Expert, skilful, able;<BR>R. 13. 69.<BR>--णः A learned man, wise<BR>man; न दत्वा कस्यचित्कन्यां<BR>पुनर्दद्याद्विचक्षणः Ms. 9. 71.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचक्षस्
विचक्षस् m. A spiritual teacher,<BR>preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचक्षुस्
विचक्षुस् a.<BR>1 Blind, sightless.<BR>--2 Perplexed, sad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचर्
विचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To wander about,<BR>roam over (oft. with acc.);<BR>इष्टान्देशान् विचर जलद Me. 115; विचचार दावं<BR>R. 2. 8; Ku. 3. 31.<BR>--2 To do,<BR>perform, practise.<BR>--3 To act, deal,<BR>behave.<BR>--4 To deviate from the right<BR>path, go about wantonly;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">Page0969-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Ms. 9. 20.<BR>--5 To pass through, pervade.<BR>--6 To attack, march against.<BR>--7 To<BR>associate or have intercourse with.<BR>--8 To go badly, fail. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>think, reflect or meditate upon.<BR>--2<BR>To discuss, call in question, debate;<BR>आज्ञा गुरूणां ह्यविचारणीया R. 14. 46.<BR>--3 To calculate, estimate; take into<BR>account, consider; परेषामात्मनश्चैव यो<BR>विचार्य बलाबलं Pt. 3; सुविचार्य यत्कृतं<BR>H. 1. 22.<BR>--4 To hesitate, doubt.<BR>--5<BR>To examine, investigate.<BR>--6 To<BR>seduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचरितं|विचरित
विचरितं Wandering, roaming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारः|विचार
विचारः<BR>1 Reflection,<BR>deliberation, thought, consideration;<BR>विचारमार्गप्रहितेन चक्षुषा<BR>Ku. 5. 42.<BR>--2 Examination, discussion,<BR>investigation; तत्वार्थविचार.<BR>--3 Trial,<BR>(of a case);<BR>विषसलिलतुलाग्निप्रार्थिते मे विचारे Mk. 9. 43.<BR>--4 Judgment,<BR>discrimination, discernment,<BR>exercise of reason; विचारमूढः प्रतिभासि मे<BR>त्वं R. 2. 47.<BR>--5 Decision,<BR>determination.<BR>--6 Selection.<BR>--7 Doubt,<BR>hesitation.<BR>--8 Prudence,<BR>circumspection.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञ a. able to<BR>decide, a judge.<BR>--भूः f. {1} a<BR>tribunal, seat of justice. {2}<BR>particularly, the judgment-seat of Yama.<BR>--शील a. thoughtful, considerate,<BR>prudent.<BR>--स्थलं {1} a tribunal. {2}<BR>logical discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारकः|विचारक
विचारकः An investigator, a judge,<BR>an examiner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारणं|विचारण
विचारणं<BR>1 Discussion,<BR>consideration, examination, deliberation,<BR>investigation.<BR>--2 Doubt, hesitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारणा
विचारणा<BR>1 Examination,<BR>discussion, investigation.<BR>--2 Reflection,<BR>consideration, thought.<BR>--3<BR>Hesitation, doubt.<BR>--4 The Mīmāṃsā<BR>system of philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारित|विचारितः
विचारित p. p.<BR>1 Considered,<BR>inquired into, examined, discussed.<BR>--2<BR>Decided, determined.<BR>--तं<BR>Deliberation, thought.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचारिन्
विचारिन् a.<BR>1 Roaming, wandering.<BR>--2 Dissolute, wanton.<BR>--3<BR>Deliberating, judging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचर्चिका|विचर्च्चिका
विचर्चिका Itch, scab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचर्चित
विचर्चित a. Anointed, smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचल्
विचल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To shake, tremble,<BR>move; पतति पतत्रे विचलति पत्रे<BR>शंकितभवदुपयानं Gīt. 5.<BR>--2 To go,<BR>proceed, set out.<BR>--3 To be agitated or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">Page0970-a+ 57</a>]<BR>disturbed, be rough (as the sea);<BR>व्यचालीदंभसां पतिः Bk. 15. 70.<BR>--4<BR>To deviate, swerve; Y. 1. 358.<BR>--5<BR>To fall off or down. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>shake, move, wave,<BR>--2 To cause to<BR>swerve, lead away from.<BR>--3 To<BR>excite, agitate, stir up.<BR>--4 To destroy,<BR>rescind, annul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0969-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचल|विचलः
विचल a.<BR>1 Moving about, shaking,<BR>wavering, tottering, unsteady (fig.<BR>also).<BR>--2 Conceited, proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचलनं|विचलन
विचलनं<BR>1 Moving.<BR>--2 Deviation.<BR>--3 Unsteadiness, fickleness.<BR>--4<BR>Conceit, pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचि|विचिः
विचि {c5c} U.<BR>1 To collect, gather,<BR>bring together, store up; Pt. 1. 45,<BR>36.<BR>--2 To search for, look out for;<BR>विचितश्चैष समंतात् श्मशानवाटः Māl. 5;<BR>R. 12. 61, 13. 23; प्रियतमां विचिन्वन्<BR>V. 4.<BR>--3 To seek, investigate,<BR>examine, reflect upon; R. 10. 23;<BR>Ki. 16. 1.<BR>--4 To separate, discern,<BR>distinguish.<BR>--5 To disarrange.<BR>--6 To<BR>select, choose.<BR>--7 To destroy, efface.<BR>--8 Ved. To clear, prepare (as a way).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचयः|विचय
विचयः<BR>1 Search, seeking, looking<BR>out for; तुरगविचयव्यग्रान् U. 1. 23.<BR>--2 Investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचयनं|विचयन
विचयनं Searching, seeking &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित
विचित p. p. Searched, searched<BR>through.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचितिः|विचिति
विचितिः f.<BR>1 Searching, search,<BR>seeking for.<BR>--2 Inquiry,<BR>investigation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिः|विचि
विचिः m. f., विची f. A wave; cf.<BR>वीचि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिकित्सा
विचिकित्सा<BR>1 Doubt, hesitation,<BR>uncertainty.<BR>--2 Mistake, error.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्र|विचित्रं|विचित्रः
विचित्र a.<BR>1 Diversified,<BR>variegated, spotted, speckled;<BR>Mu. 1. 4.<BR>--2 Various, varied.<BR>--3 Painted.<BR>--4 Beautiful, lovely; क्वचिद्विचित्रं<BR>जलयंत्रमंदिरं Rs. 1. 2.<BR>--5 Wonderful,<BR>surprising, strange; हतविधिलसितानां<BR>ही विचित्रो विपाकः Śi. 11. 64.<BR>--त्रा<BR>A white deer.<BR>--त्रं<BR>1 Variegated<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Surprise.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग<BR>a. having a spotted body.<BR>--(गः) {1}<BR>a peacock. {2} tiger.<BR>--देह a. having a<BR>lovely body.<BR>--(हः) a cloud.<BR>--रूप a.<BR>diverse.<BR>--वीर्यः N. of a king of the<BR>lunar race. [He was a son of Śantanu by<BR>his wife Satyavatī and so half-brother<BR>of Bhīṣma. When he died childless,<BR>his mother called Vyāsa (her own son<BR>before her marriage), and requested<BR>him to raise up issue to Vicitravīrya in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">Page0970-b+ 56</a>]<BR>accordance with the practice of Niyoga.<BR>He complied with the request, and<BR>begot on Ambikā and Ambālikā, the two<BR>widows of his brother, two sons<BR>Dhṛtarāṣṭra and Pāṇḍu respectively].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचित्रकः|विचित्रक
विचित्रकः The birch tree.<BR>--कं<BR>Wonder, astonishment, surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिंत्|विचिन्त्
विचिंत् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To think,<BR>consider.<BR>--2 To think of, ponder over,<BR>call to mind; विचिंतयंती<BR>यमनन्यमानसा Ś. 4. 1.<BR>--3 To take into<BR>consideration, have regard to, regard;<BR>अस्मान्साधु विचिंत्य संमयधनानुच्चैःकुलं<BR>चात्मनः Ś. 4. 16.<BR>--4 To intend, fix<BR>upon, determine.<BR>--5 To devise, find<BR>out, discover.<BR>--6 To imagine.<BR>--7<BR>To perceive, observe (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचिन्वत्कः|विचिन्वत्क
विचिन्वत्कः^1<BR>1 Search.<BR>--2<BR>Investigation.<BR>--3 A hero.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: cf AP and MW.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचीर्ण
विचीर्ण a.<BR>1 Occupied by,<BR>wandered through.<BR>--2 Entered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेतन
विचेतन a.<BR>1 Senseless, lifeless,<BR>unconscious, dead.<BR>--2 Inanimate;<BR>Ku. 4. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेतस्
विचेतस् a.<BR>1 Senseless, stupid,<BR>ignorant.<BR>--2 Perplexed, confounded,<BR>sad.<BR>--3 Malevolent, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेष्ट्
विचेष्ट् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To stir, move, be<BR>in motion, move about.<BR>--2 To act,<BR>behave.<BR>--3 To exert oneself, strive,<BR>try.<BR>--4 To roll, wallow, struggle,<BR>writhe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेष्टा
विचेष्टा<BR>1 Effort, exertion.<BR>--2<BR>Movement.<BR>--3 Conduct,<BR>behaviour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विचेष्टित|विचेष्टितः
विचेष्टित p. p.<BR>1 Striven, tried,<BR>struggled.<BR>--2 Examined,<BR>investigated.<BR>--3 Misdone, done foolishly.<BR>--तं<BR>1 An act, a deed.<BR>--2 Effort,<BR>movement, undertaking, enterprise.<BR>--3 Gesture.<BR>--4 Working, sensation,<BR>play; किमपि चेदमनंगविचेष्टितं<BR>V. 2. 9.<BR>--5 Machination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छ्|विछ्
विच्छ् {vI.v} {c6c} P. (विच्छति, also<BR>विच्छायति-ते) To go, move. {vII.v} {c10c} U.<BR>(विच्छयति-ते)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>--2 To<BR>speak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छंदः|विच्छन्द|विच्छंद|विच्छन्दः|विछन्द
विच्छंदः, विच्छंदकः A palace, a<BR>large building having several<BR>stories (ईश्वरगृह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छंदकः|विच्छन्दक|विच्छंदक|विच्छन्दकः
विच्छंदः, विच्छंदकः A palace, a<BR>large building having several<BR>stories (ईश्वरगृह).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छर्दकः|विच्छर्दक|विच्छर्द्दक|विच्छर्द्दकः|विछर्द्दक
विच्छर्दकः A palace; see विच्छंद<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छर्दनं|विच्छर्दन|विच्छर्द्दन|विछर्द्दन
विच्छर्दनं Vomiting, ejecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छर्दित|विच्छर्द्दित|विछर्द्दित
विच्छर्दित p. p.<BR>1 Vomited, ejected.<BR>--2 Neglected, disregarded.<BR>--3<BR>Given up, abandoned, left;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-c" target="_blank">Page0970-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Māl. 7, U. 1.<BR>--4 Marred, impaired,<BR>lessened; Māl. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छाय|विच्छायं|विच्छायः|विछाय
विच्छाय a. Pale, dim;<BR>Ratn. 1. 26.<BR>--यः A gem, jewel.<BR>--यं The<BR>shadow of a flock of birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिद्
विच्छिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To cut off, break,<BR>tear asunder, divide; यदर्धे<BR>विच्छिन्नं भवति कृतसंधानमिव तत् Ś. 1. 9;<BR>R. 16. 20; Bh. 1. 96.<BR>--2 To<BR>interrupt, break off, terminate, end,<BR>destroy, make extinct (as a family);<BR>विच्छिद्यमानेऽपि कुले परस्य Bk. 3. 52;<BR>Amaru. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छित्तिः|विच्छित्ति
विच्छित्तिः f.<BR>1 (a) Cutting off or<BR>asunder, tearing off; Bh. 3. 11.<BR>(b) Breaking off, fracture.<BR>--2<BR>Dividing, separating.<BR>--3<BR>Disappearance, absence, loss.<BR>--4<BR>Cessation.<BR>--5 Colouring the body with<BR>paints and unguents, painting<BR>colours, rouge; विच्छित्तिशेषैः सुरसुंदरीणां<BR>Ś. 7. 5; Śi. 16. 84.<BR>--6 Limit,<BR>boundary (of a house &c.).<BR>--7 A<BR>pause in a verse, cæsura.<BR>--8 A<BR>particular kind of amorous gesture,<BR>consisting in carelessness in dress<BR>and decoration (through pride of<BR>personal beauty);<BR>स्तोकाप्याकल्परचना विच्छित्तिः कांतिपोषकृत् S. D. 138.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छिन्न|विच्छिन्नः
विच्छिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Torn asunder,<BR>cut off.<BR>--2 Broken, severed,<BR>divided, separated; Ś. 1. 9.<BR>--3<BR>Interrupted, prevented.<BR>--4 Ended,<BR>ceased, terminated.<BR>--5 Variegated.<BR>--6 Hidden.<BR>--7 Smeared or painted<BR>with unguents.<BR>--8 Crooked, curved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदः|विच्छेद
विच्छेदः<BR>1 Cutting asunder,<BR>cutting, dividing, separation;<BR>Māl. 6. 11.<BR>--2 Breaking; Śi. 8. 51.<BR>--3<BR>Break, interruption, cessation,<BR>discontinuance; विच्छेदमाप भुवि यस्तु<BR>कथाप्रबंधः K.; पिंडविच्छेददर्शिनः<BR>R. 1. 66.<BR>--4 Removal, prohibition.<BR>--5<BR>Dissension.<BR>--6 A section, or<BR>division of a book.<BR>--7 Interval, space.<BR>--8 Interruption in family succession,<BR>failure of issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छेदनं|विच्छेदन
विच्छेदनं Cutting off, breaking &c.;<BR>see विच्छेद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छुर्
विच्छुर् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To smear, anoint,<BR>cover, coat; मनःशिलाविच्छुरिता निषेदुः<BR>Ku. 1. 55; Ch. P. 11; V. 4. 42.<BR>--2 To set, inlay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्छुरित|विछुरित
विच्छुरित p. p.<BR>1 Covered,<BR>overspread, coated.<BR>--2 Inlaid.<BR>--3<BR>Besmeared, anointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0970-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्यु
विच्यु {c1c} A.<BR>1 To deviate or<BR>swerve from.<BR>--2 To fall to pieces,<BR>--3 To err, make mistake. --Caus.<BR>To throw down or destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्युत|विच्युतः
विच्युत p. p.<BR>1 Fallen down,<BR>slipped off.<BR>--2 Displaced, thrown down<BR>from.<BR>--3 Deviated or swerving from.<BR>--4 Separated from the living part,<BR>sloughed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विच्युतिः|विच्युति
विच्युतिः f.<BR>1 Falling down from,<BR>severance, separation.<BR>--2 Decline,<BR>decay, downfall.<BR>--3 Deviation.<BR>--4<BR>Miscarriage, failure; as in<BR>गर्भविच्युतिः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्
विज् {vI.v} {c3c} U. (वेवेक्ति, वेविक्ते, विक्त)<BR>1 To separate, divide.<BR>--2 To<BR>distinguish, discern, discriminate (usually<BR>with वि and allied to विच् with वि<BR>q. v.) {vII.v} {c6c} A., {c7c} P. (विजते, विनाक्ति,<BR>विग्न)<BR>1 To shake, tremble.<BR>--2 To be<BR>agitated, tremble with fear.<BR>--3 To<BR>fear, be afraid; चक्रंद विग्ना कुररीव<BR>भूयः R. 14. 68.<BR>--4 To be distressed<BR>or afflicted. --Caus. (वेजयति-ते) To<BR>terrify, frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विग्न
विग्न p. p.<BR>1 Trembling, agitated.<BR>--2 Frightened, alarmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्
विज् m. A bird; a die (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितृ
विजितृ m.<BR>1 A discriminator, judge.<BR>--2 A partner, coheir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्
विजन् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To be born or<BR>produced.<BR>--2 To generate, produce.<BR>--3 To grow, arise, spring.<BR>--4 To<BR>be changed or transformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन|विजनः
विजन a. Lonely, retired, solitary.<BR>--नं A solitary place, retreat (विजने<BR>means ‘privately’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजननं|विजनन
विजननं Birth, procreation,<BR>delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजन्मन्
विजन्मन् a. or m. A bastard, one<BR>born illegitimately. --n. Birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजात|विजातः
विजात p. p.<BR>1 Base-born, of<BR>mixed origin.<BR>--2 Born, produced.<BR>--3<BR>Transformed.<BR>--ता A mother,<BR>matron, a woman who has given birth<BR>to children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजातिः|विजाति
विजातिः f.<BR>1 Different origin,<BR>--2<BR>Different kind, species or tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजातीय|विजातीयः
विजातीय a.<BR>1 Of a different kind<BR>or species, dissimilar, unlike.<BR>--2 Of<BR>different caste or tribe.<BR>--3 Of mixed<BR>origin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजपिलं|विजपिल
विजपिलं Mud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयंतः|विजयन्त|विजयंत|विजयन्तः
विजयंतः N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजर|विजरः
विजर a. Young, fresh.<BR>--रं A<BR>stalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल्पः|विजल्प
विजल्पः<BR>1 Prattle, idle or foolish<BR>talk.<BR>--2 Talk or speech in general.<BR>--3 A malignant or spiteful speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजल्पित
विजल्पित p. p.<BR>1 Spoken, talked;<BR>परिहासविजल्पितं सखे (वचः) Ś. 2. 18.<BR>--2 Prated, babbled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजि
विजि {c1c} A.<BR>1 To conquer,<BR>defeat, overcome, subdue; व्यजेष्ट<BR>षड्वर्गं Bk. 1. 2; प्रायस्त्वन्मुखसेवया<BR>विजयते विश्वं स पुष्पायुधः Gīt. 10;<BR>Bk. 2. 39; 15. 39.<BR>--2 To surpass,<BR>excel; चक्षुर्मेचकमंबुजं विजयते<BR>Vb. 1. 33.<BR>--3 To win, acquire by conquest;<BR>भुजविजितविमान R. 12. 104;<BR>विजितारिपुरः 1. 59; Śānti. 2. 14.<BR>--4 To be<BR>victorious, be supreme or<BR>pre-eminent; विजयतां देवः Ś. 5; रहस्यं<BR>साधूनामनुपधि विशुद्धं विजयते U. 2. 2;<BR>Māl. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयः|विजय
विजयः<BR>1 Overcoming,<BR>vanquishing, defeating.<BR>--2 Conquest, victory,<BR>triumph; दिग्विजयादारभ्य ‘conquest<BR>of the world;’ Ki. 10. 35;<BR>R. 12. 44; Ku. 3. 19; Ś. 2. 14.<BR>--3 A chariot<BR>of the gods, celestial chariot.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of Arjuna; the Mb. thus explains<BR>the name: --अभिप्रयामि संग्रामे यदहं<BR>युद्धदुमदान् । नाजित्वा विनिवर्तामि तेन मांविजयं<BR>विदुः ॥.<BR>--5 An epithet of Yama.<BR>--6<BR>N. of the first year of Jupiter's<BR>cycle.<BR>--7 N. of an attendant of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभ्युपायः a<BR>means of victory.<BR>--ईशः N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--कुंजरः a war-elephant.<BR>--छंदः a necklace of 500 strings.<BR>--डिंडिभः a large military drum.<BR>--नगरं N. of a town.<BR>--मर्दलः a large<BR>military drum.<BR>--सिद्धिः f. success,<BR>victory, triumph.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजया
विजया<BR>1 N. of Durgā.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>one of her female attendants;<BR>Mu. 1. 1.<BR>--3 N. of a lore taught by<BR>Viśvāmitra to Rāma; Bk. 2. 21.<BR>--4<BR>Hemp.<BR>--5 N. of a festival = विजयोत्सव,<BR>see below.<BR>--6 Yellow myrobalan.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्सवः a festival in<BR>honour of Durgā held on the 10th<BR>day of the bright half of Āśvina.<BR>--दशमी the tenth day of the bright<BR>half of Āśvina, observed as a great<BR>holiday and commonly known as<BR>Daśarā.<BR>--सप्तमी the seventh day of<BR>the bright half of a month falling<BR>on a Sunday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजयिन्
विजयिन् m. A conqueror, victor.<BR>विजिगीषा<BR>1 Desire to conquer or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">Page0971-c+ 56</a>]<BR>overcome.<BR>--2 Desire to surpass<BR>emulation, competition, ambition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिगीषु|विजिगीषुः
विजिगीषु a.<BR>1 Desirous of victory,<BR>wishing to conquer; यशसे<BR>विजिगीषूणां R. 1. 7.<BR>--2 Emulous,<BR>ambitious.<BR>--षुः<BR>1 A warrior, a hero.<BR>--2<BR>Antagonist, a disputant, an<BR>opponent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजित|विजितः
विजित p. p. Subdued, conquered,<BR>overcome, defeated.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a. self-subdued,<BR>selfcontrolled.<BR>--इंद्रिय a. having the<BR>organs of sense subdued or<BR>controlled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजितिः|विजिति
विजितिः f. Conquest, victory,<BR>triumph; Kāv. 3. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिनः|विजिन|विजिनं
विजिनः --नं(लः, --लं) A sauce<BR>(mixed with gruel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिनं|विजिन|विजिनः
विजिनः --नं(लः, --लं) A sauce<BR>(mixed with gruel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिलः|विजिल|विजिलं
विजिनः --नं(लः, --लं) A sauce<BR>(mixed with gruel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिलं|विजिल|विजिलः
विजिनः --नं(लः, --लं) A sauce<BR>(mixed with gruel).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजिह्म|विजिह्मः
विजिह्म a.<BR>1 Crooked, bent,<BR>turned away; कृतं न वा कोपविजिह्ममाननं<BR>Ki. 1. 21; R. 19. 35.<BR>--2<BR>Dishonest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजुलः|विजुल
विजुलः The silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृंभ्|विजृम्भ्
विजृंभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To yawn, gape,<BR>open the mouth; व्यजृंभिषत चापरे<BR>Bk. 15. 108; विजृंभितमिवांतरिक्षेण<BR>Mk. 5.<BR>--2 To open, expand (as a flower)<BR>--3 To spread everywhere, pervade,<BR>fill; सुखश्रवा मंगलतूर्यनिस्वनाः… न<BR>केवलं सद्मनि मागधीपतेः पथि व्यजृंभंत<BR>दिवौकसामपि R. 3. 19; 12. 72;<BR>रजोंधकारस्य विजृंभितस्य 7. 42.<BR>--4 To<BR>rise, appear, show, manifest oneself;<BR>तत्खल्विदं विजृंभते Māl. 7.<BR>--5 To<BR>spring back (as a bow).<BR>--6 To<BR>display activity.<BR>--7 To become<BR>increased or developed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृंभणं|विजृम्भण|विजृंभण|विजृम्भणं
विजृंभणं<BR>1 Gaping, yawning.<BR>--2<BR>Blossoming, budding, blowing,<BR>opening; वनेषु सायंतनमल्लिकानां<BR>विजृंभणोद्गंधिषु कुड्मलेषु R. 16. 47.<BR>--3<BR>Exhibiting, displaying,<BR>unfolding.<BR>--4 Expanding.<BR>--5 Pastime,<BR>amorous sport.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजृंभित|विजृम्भित|विजृम्भितं|विजृम्भितः
विजृंभित p. p.<BR>1 Gaped, yawned;<BR>Mk. 5. 51.<BR>--2 Opened, blown,<BR>expanded.<BR>--3 Displayed,<BR>exhibited, manifested; R. 7. 42;<BR>U. 6. 2.<BR>--4 Appeared.<BR>--5 Sported.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Sport, pastime.<BR>--2 Wish,<BR>desire.<BR>--3 Display, exhibition;<BR>अज्ञानविजृंभितमेतत्.<BR>--4 An act, action,<BR>conduct; Māl. 10. 21.<BR>--5 Fruit,<BR>result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जनं|विज्जन
विज्जनं --लं<BR>1 A kind of sauce;<BR>see विजुल.<BR>--2 An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जलं|विज्जल
विज्जनं --लं<BR>1 A kind of sauce;<BR>see विजुल.<BR>--2 An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0971-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जिल|विज्जिलं
विज्जिल = विजिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्जुलं|विज्जुल
विज्जुलं Cinnamon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञा
विज्ञा {c9c} U.<BR>1 To know, be aware<BR>of; Bh. 3. 21.<BR>--2 To learn,<BR>comprehend, understand.<BR>--3 To<BR>ascertain, find out, learn from.<BR>--4 To<BR>regard, know to be, consider as.<BR>--5<BR>To discern, discriminate,<BR>distinguish.<BR>--6 To be familiar with.<BR>--7<BR>To become wise or learned;<BR>Ms. 4. 20. --Caus. (विज्ञापयति)<BR>1 To<BR>request, beg (opp. आज्ञापयति);<BR>सीता-आर्यपुत्र अस्ति मे विज्ञाप्यं;<BR>रामः-नन्वाज्ञापय U. 1; R. 5. 20.<BR>--2 To<BR>communicate, inform.<BR>--3 To say,<BR>speak in general.<BR>--4 To teach,<BR>instruct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञ|विज्ञः
विज्ञ, विजानत् a.<BR>1 Knowing,<BR>intelligent, wise, learned.<BR>--2 Clever,<BR>skilful, proficient.<BR>--ज्ञः A wise or<BR>learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विजानत्
विज्ञ, विजानत् a.<BR>1 Knowing,<BR>intelligent, wise, learned.<BR>--2 Clever,<BR>skilful, proficient.<BR>--ज्ञः A wise or<BR>learned man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्त
विज्ञप्त p. p.<BR>1 Respectfully told,<BR>requested.<BR>--2 Made known,<BR>informed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञप्तिः|विज्ञप्ति
विज्ञप्तिः f.<BR>1 A respectful<BR>statement or communication, a request,<BR>an entreaty.<BR>--2 An announcement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञात|विज्ञातः
विज्ञात p. p.<BR>1 Known,<BR>understood, perceived.<BR>--2 Well-known,<BR>celebrated, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानं|विज्ञान
विज्ञानं<BR>1 Knowledge, wisdom,<BR>intelligence, understanding; Pt. 1. 24;<BR>5. 3; विज्ञानमयः कोशः ‘the sheath of<BR>intelligence’ (the first of the five<BR>sheaths of the soul).<BR>--2<BR>Discrimination, discernment.<BR>--3 Skill,<BR>proficiency; प्रयोगविज्ञानं Ś. 1. 2.<BR>--4 Worldly<BR>or profane knowledge, knowledge<BR>derived from worldly experience (opp.<BR>ज्ञान which is ‘knowledge of Brahma<BR>or Supreme Spirit’); ज्ञानं तेहं<BR>सविज्ञानमिदं वक्ष्याम्यशेषतः Bg. 7. 2, 3. 41;<BR>(the whole of the 7th Adhyāya of<BR>Bg. explains ज्ञान and विज्ञान).<BR>--5<BR>Business, employment.<BR>--6 Music.<BR>--7 Knowledge of the fourteen lores.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईश्वरः N. of the author of<BR>the Mitākṣarā, a commentary on<BR>Yājñavalkya's Smṛti.<BR>--पादः N. of<BR>Vyāsa.<BR>--मातृकः an epithet of<BR>Buddha.<BR>--वादः the theory of<BR>knowledge, the doctrine taught by<BR>Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञानिक|विज्ञानिकः
विज्ञानिक a. Wise, learned; see<BR>विज्ञ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापकः|विज्ञापक
विज्ञापकः<BR>1 An informant.<BR>--2 A<BR>teacher, an instructor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापनं|विज्ञापन
विज्ञापनं --ना<BR>1 Respectful statement<BR>or communication, a request, an<BR>entreaty; कालप्रयुक्ता खलु<BR>कार्यविद्भिर्विज्ञापना भर्तृषु सिद्धिमेति Ku. 7. 93;<BR>R. 17. 40.<BR>--2 Information,<BR>representation.<BR>--3 Instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापना
विज्ञापनं --ना<BR>1 Respectful statement<BR>or communication, a request, an<BR>entreaty; कालप्रयुक्ता खलु<BR>कार्यविद्भिर्विज्ञापना भर्तृषु सिद्धिमेति Ku. 7. 93;<BR>R. 17. 40.<BR>--2 Information,<BR>representation.<BR>--3 Instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञापित
विज्ञापित p. p.<BR>1 Respectfully told<BR>or communicated.<BR>--2 Requested.<BR>--3<BR>Informed.<BR>--4 Instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञाप्ति|विज्ञाप्तिः
विज्ञाप्ति See विज्ञप्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्ञाप्यं|विज्ञाप्य
विज्ञाप्यं A request; U. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विज्वर
विज्वर a. Free from fever,<BR>anxiety or distress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंजामरं|विञ्जामर|विंजामर|विञ्जामरं
विंजामरं The white of the eye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंजोलि
विंजोलि --ली f. A line, row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंजोली|विञ्जोली
विंजोलि --ली f. A line, row.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्
विट् {c1c} P. (वेटति)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>--2<BR>To curse, rail at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटः|विट
विटः [विट्-क]<BR>1 A paramour;<BR>त्वद्वत्सलः क्व स तपस्विजनस्य हंता<BR>कन्याविटः पतिरसौ परिरक्षतु त्वां Māl. 8. 8;<BR>Śi. 4. 48.<BR>--2 A voluptuary, sensualist.<BR>--3 (In dramas) The companion of a<BR>prince or dissolute young man, or of a<BR>courtezan (who is described as<BR>being skilled in the arts of singing,<BR>music, and poetry and as a parasite<BR>on familiar terms with his associate<BR>to whom he nearly serves the<BR>purpose of the Vidūṣaka; see inter<BR>alia Mk. acts 1, 5, and 8); for<BR>definition, see S. D. 78.<BR>--4 A<BR>rogue, cheat.<BR>--5 A catamite.<BR>--6 A<BR>rat.<BR>--7 The Khadira tree.<BR>--8 The<BR>orange tree.<BR>--9 A branch together<BR>with its shoot.<BR>--10 A mineral salt.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--माक्षिकं a kind of<BR>mineral.<BR>--लवणं a medicinal salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटंकः|विटङ्क|विटंक|विटङ्कः
विटंकः<BR>1 An aviary, dove-cot.<BR>--2 The loftiest point, pinnacle,<BR>elevation; अयमेव महीधरविटंकः<BR>Māl. 10; Vikr. 5. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटंकक
विटंकक See विटंक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटंकित|विटङ्कित
विटंकित a. Marked, stamped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटपः|विटप
विटपः [विटं विस्तारं वा पाति पिबति<BR>पा˚ क Tv.]<BR>1 A branch, bough (of a<BR>creeper or tree);<BR>कोमलविटपानुकारिणौ बाहू Ś. 1. 21, 32; यदनेन तरुर्त<BR>पातितः क्षपिता तद्विटपाश्रिता लता<BR>R. 8. 47; Śi. 4. 48; Ku. 6. 41.<BR>--2 A<BR>bush.<BR>--3 A new shoot or sprout;<BR>Śi. 7. 53.<BR>--4 A cluster, clump, thicket.<BR>--5 Extension.<BR>--6 The septum of<BR>the scrotum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटपिन्
विटपिन् m. [विटप-अस्त्यर्थे इनि]<BR>1<BR>A tree; परितो दृष्टाश्च विटपिनः सर्वे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">Page0972-c+ 54</a>]<BR>Bv. 1. 21, 29.<BR>--2 The fig-tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मृगः a monkey, an ape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटिः|विटि
विटिः --टी f. Yellow sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विटी
विटिः --टी f. Yellow sandal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विट्ठलः|विट्ठल
विट्ठ(ठ्ठ)लः N. of a form of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (worshipped at<BR>Pandharpur in the Bombay<BR>presidency).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठ्ठलः
विट्ठ(ठ्ठ)लः N. of a form of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa (worshipped at<BR>Pandharpur in the Bombay<BR>presidency).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठंक|विठङ्क
विठंक a. Bad, vile, base, low.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विठरः|विठर
विठरः N. of Bṛhaspati.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विड्
विड् {c1c} P. (वेडति)<BR>1 To curse,<BR>rail at, revile.<BR>--2 To cry out loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडं|विड|विडः
विडं A kind of artificial salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडंग|विडङ्ग|विडङ्गं|विडङ्गः
विडंग a. Clever, skilful.<BR>--गः,<BR>--गं N. of a vegetable and medicinal<BR>substance (largely used as a<BR>vermifuge).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडंब्|विडम्ब्
विडंब् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To imitate, copy,<BR>resemble; (तं) ऋतुर्विडंबयामास न<BR>पुनः प्राप तच्छ्रियं R. 4. 17;<BR>वपुःप्रकर्षेण विडंबितेश्वरः 3. 52; 13. 29; 16. 11;<BR>Ki. 5. 46; 12. 38; Śi. 1. 6;<BR>12. 5; 16. 58.<BR>--2 To ridicule, deride,<BR>mock; संमोहयंति मदयंति विडंबयंति<BR>निभर्त्सयंति रमयंति विषादयंति<BR>Bh. 1. 22; यथा न विडंब्यसे जनैः K. 109.<BR>--3<BR>To cheat, deceive;<BR>एवमात्माभिप्रायसंभावितेष्टजनचित्तवृत्तिः प्रार्थयिता विडंब्य.<BR>ते Ś. 2.<BR>--4 To afflict, pain, molest.<BR>--5 To transform, distort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडंबः|विडम्ब|विडंब|विडम्बः
विडंबः<BR>1 Imitation.<BR>--2<BR>Distressing, afflicting, molesting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडंबनं|विडम्बन|विडंबन|विडम्बनं
विडंबनं --ना<BR>1 Imitation.<BR>--2<BR>Disguise, imposture.<BR>--3 Deception,<BR>fraud.<BR>--4 Vexation, mortification.<BR>--5 Paining, distressing.<BR>--6<BR>Disappointing.<BR>--7 Ridiculousness,<BR>mockery, a matter for laughter; इयं च<BR>तेऽन्या पुरतो विडंबना Ku. 5. 70; असति<BR>त्वयि वारुणीमदः प्रमदानामधुना विडंबना<BR>4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडंबना
विडंबनं --ना<BR>1 Imitation.<BR>--2<BR>Disguise, imposture.<BR>--3 Deception,<BR>fraud.<BR>--4 Vexation, mortification.<BR>--5 Paining, distressing.<BR>--6<BR>Disappointing.<BR>--7 Ridiculousness,<BR>mockery, a matter for laughter; इयं च<BR>तेऽन्या पुरतो विडंबना Ku. 5. 70; असति<BR>त्वयि वारुणीमदः प्रमदानामधुना विडंबना<BR>4. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडंबित|विडम्बित|विडम्बितः
विडंबित p. p.<BR>1 Imitated, copied.<BR>--2 Mocked, ridiculed.<BR>--3 Deceived.<BR>--4 Vexed, mortified.<BR>--5<BR>Frustrated.<BR>--6 Low, abject, poor.<BR>--तं An<BR>object of ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडारकः|विडारक
विडारकः A cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडाल|विडालः
विडाल, विडालक See बिडाल,<BR>बिडालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडालक|विडालकं|विडालकः
विडाल, विडालक See बिडाल,<BR>बिडालक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडीनं|विडीन
विडीनं One of the several modes<BR>of flight of birds; see डीन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडुलः|विडुल
विडुलः A sort of cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडूरजं|विडूरज
विडूरजं Lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडोजस्
विडो(डौ)जस् m. N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विडौजस्
विडो(डौ)जस् m. N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितंसः|वितंस
वितंसः<BR>1 A bird-cage.<BR>--2 A rope,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">Page0973-a+ 57</a>]<BR>chain, fetter &c. to confine beasts<BR>or birds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0972-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितंडः|वितण्ड|वितण्डः
वितंडः<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>--2 A<BR>sort of lock or bolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितंडा|वितण्डा
वितंडा<BR>1 A captious objection,<BR>idle carping, a frivolous or<BR>fallacious argument or controversy (one<BR>of the sixteen padārthas or<BR>categories in Nyāya philosophy); स<BR>(जल्पः) प्रतिपक्षस्थापनाहीनो वितंडा<BR>Gaut. S.<BR>--2 Wrangling, captious<BR>criticism in general.<BR>--3 A spoon,<BR>ladle.<BR>--4 Benzoin.<BR>--5 The oleander<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथ|वितथं
वितथ a.<BR>1 Untrue, false;<BR>आजन्मनो न भवता वितथं किलोक्तं<BR>Ve. 3. 13, 5. 41; R. 9. 8.<BR>--2 Vain, futile;<BR>as in वितथप्रयत्न R. 2. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथ्य|वितथ्यं
वितथ्य a. False; see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितथयति
वितथयति Den. P. To make false;<BR>Śi. 7. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितद्रुः|वितद्रु
वितद्रुः f. N. of a river in the<BR>Panjāb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितन्
वितन् {c8c} U.<BR>1 To spread, stretch;<BR>स्फुरितविततजिह्वः Mk. 9. 12;<BR>Ki. 15. 53, Śi. 5. 38, 14. 53.<BR>--2 To cover,<BR>fill; प्रस्वेदबिंदुविततं वदनं प्रियायाः<BR>Ch. P. 9; यो वितत्व स्थितः खं Me. 58.<BR>--3<BR>To form, make;<BR>श्रेणीबंधाद्वितन्वद्धिरस्तंभां तोरणस्रजं R. 1. 41;<BR>Ki. 16. 51.<BR>--4 To stretch, string<BR>(as a bow); U. 6. 1;<BR>Bk. 3. 47.<BR>--5 To cause, produce,<BR>create, give, bestow; V. 1. 4.<BR>--6<BR>To write or compose (as a work);<BR>विराटपर्वप्रद्योती भावदीपो वितन्यते.<BR>--7<BR>To do or perform (as a sacrifice or<BR>any other rite); Ku. 2. 46.<BR>--8 To<BR>unfold, manifest, exhibit, show;<BR>Māl. 9. 11.<BR>--9 To perform, carry<BR>out, accomplish.<BR>--10 To prepare,<BR>make ready.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितत|विततं
वितत p. p.<BR>1 Spread out,<BR>extended, stretched.<BR>--2 Elongated, large,<BR>broad.<BR>--3 Performed,<BR>accomplished, effected; विततयज्ञः Ś. 7. 34.<BR>--4<BR>Covered.<BR>--5 Diffused; (see तन् with<BR>वि).<BR>--तं Any stringed instrument,<BR>such as a lute &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धन्वन्<BR>a. one who has fully drawn or<BR>stretched his bow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विततिः|वितति
विततिः f.<BR>1 Extension,<BR>expansion.<BR>--2 Quantity, collection,<BR>cluster, clump.<BR>--3 A line, row;<BR>Māl. 9. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितनु|वितनुः
वितनु a.<BR>1 Delicate.<BR>--2<BR>Beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितंतुः|वितन्तु|वितन्तुः
वितंतुः A good horse. --f. A<BR>widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितंत्री
वितंत्री A disordered or<BR>discordant lute; Ku. 1. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितप्
वितप्<BR>1 A. To shine;<BR>रविर्बितपतेऽत्यर्थं Bk. 8. 14.<BR>--2 To warm,<BR>heat.<BR>--3 To warm oneself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितमस्
वितमस् a.<BR>1 Light.<BR>--2 Free<BR>from darkness or the quality of<BR>ignorance (तमस्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्क्
वितर्क् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To guess,<BR>conjecture.<BR>--2 To think, suppose,<BR>believe.<BR>--3 To reflect, reason.<BR>--4 To<BR>expect, anticipate.<BR>--5 To find out,<BR>discover, ascertain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्कः|वितर्क
वितर्कः<BR>1 Argument, reasoning,<BR>inference.<BR>--2 Guess, conjecture,<BR>supposition, belief;<BR>शिरीषपुष्पाधिकसौकुमार्यौ बाहू तदीयाविति मे वितर्कः<BR>Ku. 1. 41.<BR>--3 Fancy, thought;<BR>Bh. 3. 45.<BR>--4 Doubt; Ki. 4. 5, 13. 2.<BR>--5 Deliberation, discussion.<BR>--6 A<BR>teacher in divine knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्कणं|वितर्कण
वितर्कणं<BR>1 Reasoning.<BR>--2<BR>Conjecturning, guessing.<BR>--3 Doubt.<BR>--4<BR>Discussion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्दिः|वितर्दि|वितर्द्दिः
वितर्दिः, --र्दी, वितर्दिका f.<BR>1 A<BR>raised seat of a quadrangular shape in<BR>a court-yard.<BR>--2 A balcony, verandah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्दी|वितर्द्दी
वितर्दिः, --र्दी, वितर्दिका f.<BR>1 A<BR>raised seat of a quadrangular shape in<BR>a court-yard.<BR>--2 A balcony, verandah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्दिका|वितर्द्दिका
वितर्दिः, --र्दी, वितर्दिका f.<BR>1 A<BR>raised seat of a quadrangular shape in<BR>a court-yard.<BR>--2 A balcony, verandah.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्द्धिः|वितर्धि
वितर्द्धिः --र्द्धी, वितर्द्धिका f. See वितर्दि<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्द्धी
वितर्द्धिः --र्द्धी, वितर्द्धिका f. See वितर्दि<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितर्द्धिका
वितर्द्धिः --र्द्धी, वितर्द्धिका f. See वितर्दि<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितलं|वितल
वितलं The second of the seven<BR>lower regions under the earth, see<BR>पाताल or लोक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्ता
वितस्ता N. of a river in the<BR>Punjab called Hydaspes by the<BR>Greeks and now called Jhelum or<BR>Betustā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितस्तिः|वितस्ति
वितस्तिः [cf. Uṇ. 4. 181] A<BR>measure of length equal to 12<BR>angulas (being the distance between the<BR>extended thumb and the little<BR>finger).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितान|वितानं|वितानः
वितान a.<BR>1 Vacant, empty.<BR>--2<BR>Pithless.<BR>--3 Dismayed, sad;<BR>क्षितिपतिमंडलमन्यतो वितानं R. 6. 86.<BR>--4<BR>Dull, stupid.<BR>--5 Wicked,<BR>abandoned.<BR>--नः, --नं<BR>1 Spreading out,<BR>expansion, extension; Śi. 11. 28.<BR>--2 An<BR>awning, a canopy;<BR>विद्युल्लेखाकनकरुचिरश्रीर्वितानं ममाब्दः V. 4. 4;<BR>R. 19. 39; Ki. 3. 42; Śi. 3. 50.<BR>--3 A<BR>cushion.<BR>--4 A collection, quantity,<BR>an assemblage; प्रस्तारस्पगिता<BR>इवोन्मुखमणिज्योतिर्वितानैर्दिशः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">Page0973-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Māl. 6. 5; Ki. 17. 61.<BR>--5 A sacrifice; an<BR>oblation; वितानेष्वप्ये वं तव मम च सोमे<BR>विधिरभूत Ve. 6. 30, 3. 16,<BR>Śi. 14. 10.<BR>--6 The sacrificial hearth or<BR>altar.<BR>--7 Season, opportunity.<BR>--नं<BR>Leisure, rest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानकः|वितानक|वितानकं
वितानकः --कं<BR>1 An expanse.<BR>--2 A<BR>heap, quantity, collection, mass;<BR>Śi. 3. 6.<BR>--3 An awning, a canopy.<BR>--4 The tree called Māda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानकं|वितानक|वितानकः
वितानकः --कं<BR>1 An expanse.<BR>--2 A<BR>heap, quantity, collection, mass;<BR>Śi. 3. 6.<BR>--3 An awning, a canopy.<BR>--4 The tree called Māda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानायते
वितानायते Den. A. To act or serve<BR>as an awning; Māl. 9. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितानीकृ
वितानीकृ {c8c} U. To spread or extend<BR>over (as a canopy), overshadow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्नं|वितुन्न
वितुन्नं<BR>1 The potherb called<BR>सुनिषण्णक.<BR>--2 The plant called शैवाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुन्नकं|वितुन्नक|वितुन्नकः
वितुन्नकं<BR>1 Coriander-seed.<BR>--2<BR>Blue vitriol.<BR>--कः The plant called<BR>तामलकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितुष्ट
वितुष्ट p. p. Dissatisfied,<BR>displeased, discontented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितृष्ण
वितृष्ण a. Free from desire,<BR>content.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितॄ
वितॄ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To cross or pass<BR>over, go beyond; R. 6. 77.<BR>--2 To<BR>give, grant, impart, confer or<BR>bestow on, vouchsafe, favour with;<BR>भगवान् मारचिस्ते दर्शनं वितरति Ś. 7;<BR>वितरति गुरुः प्राज्ञे विद्यां यथैव तथा जडे<BR>U. 2. 4; वितरति नृपो नोचितमहा Pt. 1. 11;<BR>U. 3. 48; निवासहेतोरुटजं वितेरुः<BR>R. 14. 81; Māl. 1. 3; 6. 7; 9. 5, 44.<BR>--3<BR>To cause, produce; ज्योत्स्नाशंकामिह<BR>वितरति हंसश्रेणी Ki. 5. 31.<BR>--4 To<BR>carry over, ferry over.<BR>--5 To give<BR>(as medicine), apply a remedy.<BR>--6<BR>To do, perform.<BR>--7 To forgive,<BR>pardon.<BR>--8 To increase, enhance.<BR>--Caus. To carry through,<BR>accomplish (fig. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितरणं|वितरण
वितरणं<BR>1 Crossing over.<BR>--2 A<BR>gift, donation, present; पूर्णाशा वहवः<BR>कृता वितरणैर्येन त्वया याचकाः<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--3 Giving up, leaving,<BR>abandoning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वितीर्ण
वितीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Crossed or passed<BR>over.<BR>--2 Given, bestowed, imparted;<BR>U. 3. 25, Śi. 7. 67, 17. 15.<BR>--3 Gone<BR>down, descended, R. 6. 77.<BR>--4<BR>Conveyed.<BR>--5 Subdued, overcome (see<BR>तॄ with वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त्
वित्त् {c10c} U. (वित्तयति-ते;<BR>वित्तापयति-ते also according to some) To give<BR>away, give as alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्त|वित्तं|वित्तः
वित्त p. p. [विद् लाभे क्त]<BR>1<BR>Found, discovered.<BR>--2 Gained,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-a" target="_blank">Page0974-a+ 55</a>]<BR>acquired.<BR>--3 Examined, investigated.<BR>--4 Known, famous.<BR>--त्तं<BR>1 Wealth,<BR>possessions, property, substance.<BR>--2 Power.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आगमः,<BR>--उपार्जनं acquisition of wealth.<BR>--ईशः an<BR>epithet of Kubera; Bg. 10. 23;<BR>Ms. 7. 4.<BR>--जानि a. one who has married<BR>a wife.<BR>--दः a donor, benefactor.<BR>--मात्रा property.<BR>--वर्धन a.<BR>profitable, lucrative.<BR>--समागमः acquisition<BR>of wealth, income; Pt. 1. 425.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0973-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तवत्|वित्तवन्त्
वित्तवत् a. Rich, wealthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्तिः|वित्ति
वित्तिः f. [विद्-क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>Knowledge.<BR>--2 Judgment, discrimination,<BR>thought.<BR>--3 Gain, acquisition.<BR>--4<BR>Likelihood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रस्
वित्रस् {c1c} {c4c} P. To be<BR>frightened or terrified;<BR>वित्रस्तमुग्धहरिणीसदृशैः कटाक्षैः Bh. 1. 9. --Caus. To<BR>terrify, frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्रासः|वित्रास
वित्रासः Fear, alarm, terror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वित्सनः|वित्सन
वित्सनः An ox, a bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथ्
विथ् {c1c} A. (वेथते) To beg, ask.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विथुरः|विथुर
विथुरः<BR>1 A demon.<BR>--2 A thief.<BR>--रा A widow; cf. विधुरा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्
विद् {vI.v} {c2c} P. (वेत्ति or वेद, विवेद;<BR>विदांचकार, अवेदीत्, वेत्स्यति, वेत्तुं, विदित;<BR>desid. विविदिषति)<BR>1 To know,<BR>understand, learn, find out, ascertain,<BR>discover; न चैतद्विद्मः कतरन्नो गरीयो<BR>यद्वा जयेम यदि वा नो जयेयुः Bg. 2. 5;<BR>त मोहांधः कथमयममुं वेत्तु देवं पुराणं<BR>Ve. 1. 23, 3. 39; Ś. 5. 27, R. 3. 43;<BR>Bg. 4. 34, 18. 1.<BR>--2 To feel,<BR>experience; Mu. 3. 4.<BR>--3 To look<BR>upon, regard, consider, know or<BR>take to be; य एनं वेत्ति हंतांर<BR>Bg. 2. 19; विद्धि व्याधिव्यालग्रस्तं लोक<BR>शोकहतं च समस्तं Moha M. 5;<BR>Bg. 2. 17; Ms. 1. 33; Ku. 6. 30. --Caus.<BR>(वेदयति-ते)<BR>1 To make known,<BR>communicate, inform, apprise, tell.<BR>--2<BR>To teach, expound; वेदार्थं<BR>स्वानवेदयत् Sk.<BR>--3 To feel, experience;<BR>Ms. 12. 13. {vII.v} {c4c} A. (विद्यते, वित्त)<BR>1<BR>To be, to exist; अपापानां कुले जाते<BR>मयि पापं न विद्यते Mk. 9. 37; नासतो<BR>विद्यते भावो नाभावो विद्यते सतः<BR>Bg. 2. 16; (cf. the root 1 अस्).<BR>--2 To<BR>happen. {vIII.v} {c6c} U. (विंदति-ते, वित्त)<BR>1 To get, obtain, acquire, gain;<BR>एकमप्यास्थितः सम्यगुभयोर्विदंते फलं<BR>Bg. 5. 4; Y. 3. 192.<BR>--2 To find,<BR>discover, recognise; यथा धेनुसहस्रेषु<BR>वत्सो विंदति मातरं Subhāṣ.;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-b" target="_blank">Page0974-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Ms. 8. 109.<BR>--3 To feel, experience;<BR>R. 14. 56; Bg. 5. 21, 11. 24, 18. 45.<BR>--4<BR>To marry; Ms. 9. 69. {vIV.v} {c7c} A.<BR>(विंत्ते, वित्त or विन्न)<BR>1 To know,<BR>understand.<BR>--2 To consider, regard,<BR>take for; न तृणेह्मीति लोकोयं विंत्ते मां<BR>निष्पराक्रमं Bk. 6. 39.<BR>--3 To find,<BR>meet with.<BR>--4 To reason, reflect.<BR>--5 To examine, inquire into. {vV.v}<BR>{c10c} A. (वेदयते)<BR>1 To tell, declare,<BR>announce, communicate.<BR>--2 To feel,<BR>experience.<BR>--3 To dwell. (The<BR>following verse illustrates the root<BR>in some of its conjugations:<BR>--वेत्ति सर्वाणि शास्त्राणि गर्वस्तस्य न विद्यते ।<BR>विंत्ते धर्मं सदा सद्भिस्तेषु पूजां च विंदति ॥; cf.<BR>also: --सत्तायां विद्यते ज्ञाने वेत्ति विंत्ते<BR>विचारणे । विंदते विंदति प्राप्तौ श्यन्लुक्<BR>श्नम्शेष्विदं क्रमात् ॥). [cf. L. video; A. S. witan;<BR>Goth. vait].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्
विद् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Knowing, conversant with; वेदविद्<BR>&c. --m.<BR>1 The planet Mercury.<BR>--2<BR>A learned man, wise man. --f.<BR>1<BR>Knowledge.<BR>--2 Understanding,<BR>intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदः|विद
विदः<BR>1 A learned man, wise man<BR>or Paṇḍita.<BR>--2 The planet Mercury.<BR>--दा<BR>1 Knowledge, learning.<BR>--2<BR>Understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदित|विदितं|विदितः
विदित p. p.<BR>1 Known, understood,<BR>learnt; अविदितगतयामा रात्रिरेव व्यरंसीत्<BR>U. 1. 27.<BR>--2 Informed.<BR>--3<BR>Renowned, celebrated, well-known;<BR>भुवनविदिते वंशे Me. 6.<BR>--4 Promised, agreed<BR>to.<BR>--तः A learned man, scholar.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Knowledge, information.<BR>--2<BR>Celebrity, fame.<BR>--3 Acquisition,<BR>gaining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदंशः|विदंश
विदंशः Pungent food such as<BR>excites thirst.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्ध|विदग्धः
विदग्ध p. p.<BR>1 Burnt up,<BR>consumed by fire.<BR>--2 Cooked.<BR>--3<BR>Digested.<BR>--4 Destroyed, decomposed.<BR>--5 Clever, shrewd, sharp, subtle;<BR>Pt. 1. 164; U. 4. 21.<BR>--6 Crafty,<BR>artful, intriguing.<BR>--7 Unburnt or<BR>ill-digested.<BR>--8 Lovely, charming.<BR>--9 Respectable (as dress &c.).<BR>--ग्धः<BR>1 A wise or learned man,<BR>scholar.<BR>--2 A libertine.<BR>--ग्धा A<BR>shrewd and clever woman, an artful<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धता
विदग्धता --त्वं Shrewdenss,<BR>cleverness; skill, elegance &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदग्धत्वं|विदग्धत्व
विदग्धता --त्वं Shrewdenss,<BR>cleverness; skill, elegance &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदथः|विदथ
विदथः<BR>1 A learned man,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">Page0974-c+ 55</a>]<BR>scholar.<BR>--2 An ascetic, a sage.<BR>--3 Ved.<BR>A sacrifice.<BR>--थं Ved.<BR>1 Knowledge.<BR>--2 A sacrifice.<BR>--3 A battle (?)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदरः|विदर|विदरं
विदरः Breaking, bursting,<BR>rending.<BR>--रं The prickly pear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भाः
विदर्भाः (m. pl.) [विगताः दर्भाः<BR>कुशा यतः Tv.]<BR>1 N. of a district,<BR>the modern Berar; अस्ति विदर्भो<BR>नाम जनपदः Dk.; अस्ति विदर्भेषु पद्मपुरं<BR>नाम नगरं Māl. 1; R. 5. 40, 60;<BR>N. 1. 50.<BR>--2 The natives of Vidarbha.<BR>--र्भः<BR>1 A king of the Vidarbhas.<BR>--2 Any dry or desert soil.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जा, --तनया, --राजतनया, --सुभ्रूः epithets<BR>of Damayantī, daughter of the<BR>king of the Vidarbhas.<BR>--जा N. of<BR>the wife of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदल्
विदल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To break, split,<BR>crack; त्वदिषुभिर्व्यदलिष्यदसावपि<BR>N. 4. 88.<BR>--2 To dig up.<BR>--3 To open,<BR>expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदल|विदलं|विदलः
विदल a.<BR>1 Split, rent asunder.<BR>--2<BR>Opened, blown (as a flower &c.).<BR>--लः<BR>1 Dividing, separating.<BR>--2<BR>Rending, splitting.<BR>--3 A cake.<BR>--4<BR>Mountain ebony.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A basket<BR>of split bamboos or any vessel<BR>of wicker-work.<BR>--2 The bark of<BR>pomegranate.<BR>--3 A twig.<BR>--4 The<BR>chips of a substance.<BR>--5 Split peas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदलनं|विदलन
विदलनं Splitting, rending asunder,<BR>cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारुः|विदारु
विदारुः A lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदाहः|विदाह
विदाहः<BR>1 Burning.<BR>--2 Great<BR>heat, inflammation.<BR>--3 Pungency,<BR>sharpness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदाहिन्
विदाहिन् m. A substance causing<BR>inflammation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिश्
विदिश् f. An intermediate point<BR>of the compass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिशा
विदिशा<BR>1 N. of the capital of<BR>the district called दशार्ण; तेषां (<BR>दशार्णानां) दिक्षु प्रथितविदिशालक्षणां राजधानीं<BR>Me. 24.<BR>--2 N. of a river in Mālvā.<BR>--3 = विदिश् q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुः|विदु
विदुः<BR>1 The middle of the<BR>frontal globes on an elephant's forehead<BR>(हस्तिकुंभमध्यभागः).<BR>--2 A hippopotamus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुर|विदुरः
विदुर a. [विद्-कुरच् P. III. 2. 162]<BR>Wise, intelligent.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A wise or<BR>learned man.<BR>--2 A crafty man, an<BR>intriguer.<BR>--3 N. of the younger<BR>brother of Pāṇḍu. [When Satyavat;<BR>found that both the sons begotten by<BR>Vyāsa upon her two daughters-in-law<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-a" target="_blank">Page0975-a+ 58</a>]<BR>were physically incapacitated for the<BR>throne-Dhṛtarāṣṭra being blind and<BR>Pāṇḍu pale and sickly-she asked them<BR>to seek the assistance of Vyāsa once<BR>more. But being frightened by the<BR>austere look of the sage, the elder widow<BR>sent one of her slave-girls dressed in her<BR>own clothes, and this girl became the<BR>mother of Vidura. He is remarkable for<BR>his great wisdom, righteousness, and<BR>strict impartiality. He particularly loved<BR>the Pāṇḍavas, and saved them from<BR>several critical dangers].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0974-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदुलः|विदुल
विदुलः<BR>1 A kind of reed or<BR>ratan.<BR>--2 Gum-myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदून
विदून p. p. Afflicted, tormented,<BR>distressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूर|विदूरः
विदूर a. Remote, distant;<BR>सरिद्विदूरांतरभावतन्वी R. 13. 48;<BR>U. 6. 39.<BR>--रः N. of a mountain or city<BR>from which the Vaidūrya jewel or<BR>lapis lazuli is brought;<BR>विदूरभूमिर्नवमेघशब्दादुद्भिन्नया रत्नशलाकयेव<BR>Ku. 1. 24; see Malli thereon, as well as<BR>on Śi. 3. 45. (The forms विदूरं,<BR>विदूरेण, विदूरतस् or विदूरात् are often<BR>used adverbially in the sense of<BR>‘from a distance,’ ‘from afar’, ‘at<BR>a distance’, ‘far off’; Māl. 3. 18.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग a. spreading far and<BR>wide.<BR>--जं the lapis lazuli.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूषक|विदूषकः
विदूषक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Defiling,<BR>polluting, contaminating,<BR>corrupting.<BR>--2 Detracting, abusing.<BR>--3<BR>Witty, humorous, jocular.<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>A jester, buffoon.<BR>--2<BR>Particularly, the humorous companion and<BR>confidential friend of the hero in<BR>a play, who excites mirth by his<BR>quaint dress, speeches, gestures,<BR>appearances &c., and by allowing<BR>himself to be made the butt of<BR>ridicule by almost every body; the<BR>S. D. thus defines him:<BR>--कुसुमवसंताद्यभिधः कर्मवपुर्वेशभाषाद्यैः । हास्यकरः<BR>कलहरतिर्विदूषकः स्यात्स्वकर्मज्ञः ॥ 79.<BR>--3 A<BR>libertine, lecher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदूषणं|विदूषण
विदूषणं<BR>1 Pollution, corruption.<BR>--2 Abuse, reproach, detraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदृतिः|विदृति
विदृतिः A seam.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदॄ
विदॄ {c9c} P. or {c10c} U.<BR>1 To split,<BR>tear asunder, divide, cut to pieces;<BR>ऐंद्रिः किल नखैस्तस्या विददार स्तनौ द्विज<BR>R. 12. 22; न विदीर्ये कठिनाः खलु स्त्रियः<BR>Ku. 4. 5; R. 15. 33.<BR>--2 To rend<BR>(fig.); चित्तं विदारयति कस्य न<BR>कोविदारः Rs. 3. 6. स घोषो धार्तराष्ट्राणां<BR>हृदयानि व्यदारयत् Bg. 1. 19. --Pass.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">Page0975-b+ 56</a>]<BR>To be rent or torn (with grief &c.)<BR>--Caus. To rend, tear in pieces,<BR>tear or rip up; Māl. 5. 15; 10. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारः|विदार
विदारः<BR>1 Rending or cutting<BR>asunder, splitting.<BR>--2 War, battle.<BR>--3 An inundation, overflowing (of<BR>a tank, river &c.).<BR>--री A swelling<BR>in the groin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारकः|विदारक|विदारकं
विदारकः<BR>1 A tearer, divider.<BR>--2<BR>A tree or rock in the middle of a<BR>stream (which divides its course).<BR>--3 A hole sunk in water in the bed<BR>of a dry river.<BR>--कं Alkaline earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदारणः|विदारण|विदारणं
विदारणः<BR>1 A tree or rock in the<BR>middle of a stream (to which a<BR>boat is fastened).<BR>--2 War, battle.<BR>--3 The Karṇikāra tree.<BR>--णा War,<BR>battle.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Rending, splitting,<BR>tearing, ripping up, breaking, (often<BR>with the force of an adj. at the<BR>end of comp.); श्रुतं सखे श्रवणविदारणं<BR>वचः Mu. 5. 6;<BR>युवजनहृदयविदारणमनसिजनखरुचिक्रिंशुक्रजाले Gīt. 1,<BR>Ki. 14. 54.<BR>--2 Afflicting, tormenting.<BR>--3<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदीर्ण|विदीर्णः
विदीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Torn, split, rent<BR>asunder, split open.<BR>--2 Opened,<BR>expanded; (see दॄ with वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशः|विदेश
विदेशः Another country, foreign<BR>land or country; भजते विदेशमधिकेन<BR>जितस्तदनुप्रवेशमथवा कुशलः Śi. 9. 48;<BR>को वीरस्य मनस्विनः स्वविषयः को बा<BR>विदेशस्तथा H. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a.<BR>exotic, foreign.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशिन्
विदेशिन्, विदेशीय a. Foreign,<BR>exotic. --m. A foreigner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेशीय
विदेशिन्, विदेशीय a. Foreign,<BR>exotic. --m. A foreigner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेह|विदेहः
विदेह a.<BR>1 Bodiless; incorporeal.<BR>--2 Trunkless.<BR>--हाः (m. pl.)<BR>1 N.<BR>of a country, the ancient Mithilā<BR>(see App. III.); R. 11. 36,<BR>12. 26.<BR>--2 The natives of this country.<BR>--हः<BR>1 The district Videha.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of Janaka.<BR>--हा The same as विदेह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्ध|विद्धः
विद्ध p. p. [व्यध्-क्त]<BR>1 Pierced,<BR>penetrated; wounded, stabbed.<BR>--2<BR>Beaten, whipped, lashed.<BR>--3 Thrown,<BR>directed, sent.<BR>--4 Opposed.<BR>--5<BR>Resembling.<BR>--द्धं A wound.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्ण a. having bored ears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्मन्
विद्मन् n. Ved. Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्यमान|विद्यमानः
विद्यमान a.<BR>1 Being, existing.<BR>--2<BR>Present.<BR>--3 Actual, real.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्या
विद्या [विद्-क्यप्]<BR>1 Knowledge,<BR>learning, lore, science; (तां)<BR>विद्यामभ्यसनेनेव प्रसादयितुमर्हसि R. 1. 88;<BR>विद्या नाम नरस्य रूपमधिकं प्रच्छन्नगुप्तं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-c" target="_blank">Page0975-c+ 57</a>]<BR>धनं &c. Bh. 2. 20. (According to<BR>some Vidyās are four:<BR>--आन्वीक्षिकी<BR>त्रयी वार्ता दंडनीतिश्च शाश्वती Kāmandaka);<BR>चतसृष्वपि ते विवेकिनी नृप विद्यासु<BR>निरूढिमागता Ki. 2. 6; to these four<BR>Manu adds a fifth आत्मविद्या; see<BR>Ms. 7. 43. But the usual number of<BR>Vidyās is stated to be fourteen, i. e.<BR>the four Vedas, the six Aṅgas,<BR>Dharma, Mīmāṃsā, Tarka or<BR>Nyāya and the Purāṇas; see चतुर्दशविद्या<BR>under चतुर्; and N. 1. 4.<BR>--2 Right<BR>knowledge, spiritual knowledge;<BR>U. 6. 6; cf. अविद्या.<BR>--3 A spell, an<BR>incantation.<BR>--4 The goddess Durgā.<BR>--5 Magical skill.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुपालिन्, --अनुसेविन् a. acquiring<BR>knowledge.<BR>--अभ्यासः, --अर्जनं,<BR>--आगमः acquisition of knowledge,<BR>pursuit of learning, study.<BR>--अर्थः<BR>seeking for knowledge.<BR>--अर्थिन् m. a<BR>student, scholar, pupil.<BR>--आधारः a<BR>receptacle of learning; Māl. 2. 11.<BR>--आरंभः introduction of a boy to<BR>learning.<BR>--आलयः a school, college,<BR>any place of learning.<BR>--उपार्जनं =<BR>विद्यार्जनं q. v.<BR>--करः a learned man.<BR>--चण, --चंचु a. famous for one's<BR>learning.<BR>--दलः the Bhūrja tree.<BR>--दातृ m. a teacher, an instructor.<BR>--दानं teaching, imparting<BR>instruction.<BR>--देवी the goddess of learning.<BR>--धनं {1} wealth in the form of<BR>learning. {2} wealth acquired by<BR>learning.<BR>--धरः, (--री f.) a class of<BR>demigods or semi-divine beings;<BR>विद्याधराध्युषितचारुशिलातलानि स्थानानि<BR>Bh. 3. 70.<BR>--प्राप्तिः = विद्यार्जन q. v.<BR>--लाभः<BR>{1} acquisition of learning. {2}<BR>wealth or any other acquisition made<BR>by learning.<BR>--विशिष्ट a.<BR>distinguished by learning.<BR>--विहीन a. illiterate,<BR>ignorant; Pt. 1. 35.<BR>--वृद्ध a. old<BR>in knowledge, advanced in learning.<BR>--व्यसनं, --व्यवसायः pursuit of<BR>knowledge.<BR>--व्रतस्नातक, --स्नातकः a<BR>Brāhmaṇa who has finished his course of<BR>religious studentship (ब्रह्मचारिव्रत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्
विद्युत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To shine, sparkle,<BR>be bright; व्यद्योतिष्ट सभावेद्यामसौ<BR>नरशिखित्रयी Śi. 2. 3; 1. 20.<BR>--2 To<BR>light, illuminate (usually caus. in<BR>this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्
विद्युत् f.<BR>1 Lightning; वाताय<BR>कपिला विद्युत् Mbh.; Me. 38, 115.<BR>--2<BR>A thunderbolt.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उन्मेषः a flash of lightning.<BR>--जिह्वः a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">Page0976-a+ 55</a>]<BR>kind of demon or Rākṣasa.<BR>--ज्वाला,<BR>--द्योतः a flash or lustre of lightning.<BR>--दामन् n. a flash of zigzag or<BR>forked lightning.<BR>--पातः falling<BR>or stroke of lightning.<BR>--प्रियं<BR>bellmetal.<BR>--लता, --लेखा (विद्युल्लता,<BR>विद्युल्लेखा) {1} a streak of lightning.<BR>{2} forked or zigzag lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0975-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्युत्वत्|विद्युत्वन्त्
विद्युत्वत् a. Having lightning;<BR>Me. 64. --m. A cloud; विद्युत्वानिव<BR>चातकैः Ku. 6. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्योतन
विद्योतन a. (नी f.)<BR>1<BR>Illuminating, irradiating.<BR>--2 Illustrating,<BR>elucidating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रः|विद्र|विद्रं
विद्रः<BR>1 Tearing, splitting,<BR>piercing.<BR>--2 A fissure, hole, cavity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रधिः|विद्रधि
विद्रधिः An abscess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्राण
विद्राण a. Roused from sleep,<BR>awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रु
विद्रु {c1c} P.<BR>1 To run, run away,<BR>retreat; जलसंवात इवासि विद्रुतः<BR>Ku. 4. 6.<BR>--2 To melt, dissolve.<BR>--3 To<BR>become divided, burst asunder.<BR>--Caus. To put to flight, rout,<BR>scare away, disperse, scatter;<BR>प्रतिरवाभोगभीषितनष्टविद्राविताशेषजननिवहः<BR>Māl. 3; असौ कुंभिभ्रात्या<BR>खरनखरविद्रावितमहागुरुग्रावग्रामः स्वपिति गिरिगर्भे<BR>हरिपतिः Bv. 1. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रवः|विद्रव
विद्रवः<BR>1 Running away, flight,<BR>retreat.<BR>--2 Panic.<BR>--3 Flowing out.<BR>--4 Melting, liquefaction.<BR>--5<BR>Censure, abuse.<BR>--6 Intellect,<BR>understanding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्राव|विद्रावः
विद्राव = विद्रवः q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावणं|विद्रावण
विद्रावणं<BR>1 Driving or scaring away,<BR>putting to flight, defeating.<BR>--2<BR>Liquefying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रावित|विद्रावितं
विद्रावित a.<BR>1 Put to flight,<BR>routed, chased away.<BR>--2 Scattered,<BR>dispersed: torn asunder.<BR>--3 Liquefied,<BR>fused, melted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुत|विद्रुतः
विद्रुत p. p.<BR>1 Flown, fled away,<BR>(in panic).<BR>--2 Agitated, frightened,<BR>alarmed.<BR>--3 Liquid, fluid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्रुमः|विद्रुम
विद्रुमः<BR>1 The coral tree<BR>(bearing reddish precious gems called<BR>corals).<BR>--2 A coral; तवाधरस्पर्धिषु<BR>विद्रुमेषु R. 13. 13; Ku. 1. 44.<BR>--3<BR>A young shoot or sprout.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--लता {1} a branch of coral. {2} a<BR>kind of perfume.<BR>--लतिका a kind<BR>of perfume (नलिका).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वस्
विद्वस् a. [विद्-क्वसु] (Nom. sing.<BR>m. विद्वान्; f. विदुषी; n. विद्वत्)<BR>1<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">Page0976-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Knowing (with acc.); आनंदं<BR>ब्रह्मणो विद्वान् न बिभेति कदाचन; तव<BR>विद्वानपि तापकारणं R. 8. 76;<BR>Ki. 11. 30.<BR>--2 Wise, learned. --m. A<BR>learned or wise man, scholar; किं<BR>वस्तु विद्वन् गुरवे प्रदेयं R. 5. 18.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कल्प, --देशीय, --देश्य a.<BR>(विद्वत्कल्प, विद्वद्देशीय, विद्वद्देश्य)<BR>slightly learned, a little learned.<BR>--जनः (विद्वज्जनः) a learned or wise<BR>man, sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष्
विद्विष् m., विद्वषः An enemy, a<BR>foe; विद्विषोऽप्यनुनय Bh. 2. 77;<BR>R. 3. 60; Y. 1. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्विष्ट
विद्विष्ट p. p. Hated, disliked,<BR>odious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषः|विद्वेष
विद्वेषः<BR>1 Enmity, hatred, odium;<BR>Ms. 8. 346.<BR>--2 Disdainful pride,<BR>contempt; विद्वेषोऽभिमतप्राप्तावपि<BR>गवार्दनादरः Bharata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषणः|विद्वेषण|विद्वेषणं
विद्वेषणः A hater, an enemy.<BR>--णी<BR>A woman of a resentful temper.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Causing hatred or enmity.<BR>--2<BR>Enmity, hatred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेषिन्
विद्वेषिन्, विद्वेष्टृ a. Hating, inimical.<BR>--m. A hater, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विद्वेष्टृ
विद्वेषिन्, विद्वेष्टृ a. Hating, inimical.<BR>--m. A hater, an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्
विध् {vI.v} {c6c} P. (विधति)<BR>1 To pierce,<BR>cut.<BR>--2 To honour, worship.<BR>--3 To<BR>rule, govern, administer. {vII.v} {c1c} A.<BR>(वेधते) To ask, beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधः|विध
विधः [विध-क अच् वा]<BR>1 Kind,<BR>sort; as in बहुविध, नानाविध.<BR>--2 Mode,<BR>manner, form.<BR>--3 Fold (at the end<BR>of comp., especially after numerals);<BR>त्रिविध, अष्टविध &c.<BR>--4 The food of<BR>elephants.<BR>--5 Prosperity.<BR>--6<BR>Penetration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवनं|विधवन
विधवनं<BR>1 Shaking, agitating.<BR>--2<BR>Tremor, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधव्यं|विधव्य
विधव्यं Tremor, agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधवा
विधवा [विगतो धवो यस्याः सा] A<BR>widow; सा नारी विधवा जाता गृहे<BR>रोदिति तत्पतिः Subhāṣ.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवेदनं marrying a widow.<BR>--गामिन् m. one who has sexual intercourse<BR>with a widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधस्
विधस् m. N. of Brahman, the<BR>creator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधा
विधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To do, make, bring<BR>about, effect, accomplish, perform,<BR>cause, produce, occasion; यथाक्रमं<BR>पुंसवनादिकाः क्रिया धृतेश्च धीरः<BR>सदृशीर्व्यधत्त सः R. 3. 10; तन्नो देवा विधेयासुः<BR>Bk. 19. 2; विधेयासुर्देवाः परमरमणीयां<BR>परिणतिं Māl. 6. 7; प्रायः शुभं च<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-c" target="_blank">Page0976-c+ 57</a>]<BR>विदधात्यशुभं च जंतोः सर्वंकषा भगवती<BR>भवितव्यतैव 1. 23; ये द्वे कालं विधत्तः Ś. 1. 1<BR>‘cause, produce, or regulate time’;<BR>तस्य तस्याचलां श्रद्धां तामेव विदधाम्यहं<BR>Bg. 7. 21; R. 2. 38, 3. 66, Ve. 1. 1,<BR>Ki. 1. 3, 16. 62, 18. 28; (these<BR>senses may be further modified<BR>according to the noun with which विधा<BR>is used; cf. कृ).<BR>--2 To lay down,<BR>ordain, prescribe, fix, settle,<BR>command, enjoin; प्राङ्नाभिवर्धनात्पुंसो<BR>जातकर्म विधीयते Ms. 2. 29, 3. 19;<BR>Y. 1. 72; शूद्रस्य तु सवर्णैव नान्या भार्या<BR>विधीयते Ms. 9. 157, 3. 118;<BR>पाणिनिश्च क्रियाफलस्य कर्तृगामित्वे<BR>सत्यात्मनेपदं विदधाति J. N. V.<BR>--3 To make, form,<BR>shape, create, manufacture; तं वेधा<BR>विदधे नूनं सहाभूतसमाधिना R. 1. 29;<BR>अंगानि चंपकदलैः स विधाय नूनं कांते<BR>कथं घटितवानुपलेन चेतः Ś. Til. 3.<BR>--4<BR>To appoint, depute (as a minister).<BR>--5<BR>To put on, wear; Pt. 1.<BR>--6 To fix upon,<BR>direct towards (as mind &c.); योगे<BR>धैर्यसमाधिसिद्धिसुलभे बुद्धिं विधद्ध्वं बुधाः<BR>Bh. 3. 54, Bg. 2. 44.<BR>--7 To<BR>arrange, put in order.<BR>--8 To make<BR>ready, prepare.<BR>--9 To settle, fix,<BR>establish.<BR>--10 To give, grant;<BR>Ki. 14. 10.<BR>--11 To procure, furnish.<BR>--12 To<BR>place, put, lay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधा
विधा<BR>1 Mode, manner, form.<BR>--2<BR>Kind, sort.<BR>--3 Prosperity, affluence.<BR>--4 The food of elephants, horses &c.<BR>--5 Penetration.<BR>--6 Hire, wages.<BR>--7<BR>Act, action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधातृ
विधातृ m.<BR>1 A maker, creator;<BR>Ku. 7. 36.<BR>--2 The creator, N.<BR>of Brahman; विधाता भद्रं नो वितरतु<BR>मनोज्ञाय विधये Māl. 6. 7; R. 1. 35,<BR>6. 11; 7. 25.<BR>--3 A granter, giver,<BR>bestower; Ku. 1. 57.<BR>--4 Fate,<BR>destiny; H. 1. 40.<BR>--5 N. of<BR>Viśvakarman.<BR>--6 N. of Kāma, the god<BR>of love.<BR>--7 Spirituous liquor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आयुस् m. {1} sunshine. {2} the<BR>sun-flower.<BR>--भूः an epithet of<BR>Nārada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधात्री
विधात्री Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानं|विधान
विधानं<BR>1 Arranging, disposing.<BR>--2<BR>Performing, making, doing,<BR>executing; नेपथ्यविधानं Ś. 1; आज्ञा˚, यज्ञ˚<BR>&c.<BR>--3 Creation, creating; R. 6. 11,<BR>7. 14; Ku. 7. 66.<BR>--4 Employment,<BR>use, application; प्रतिकारविधानं<BR>R. 8. 40.<BR>--5 Prescribing, enjoining,<BR>ordering.<BR>--6 A rule, precept, ordinance,<BR>sacred rule or precept, sacred<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-a" target="_blank">Page0977-a+ 57</a>]<BR>injunction; Ms. 9. 148; Bg. 16. 24,<BR>17. 24.<BR>--7 Mode, manner.<BR>--8 A means<BR>or expedient.<BR>--9 Performance of<BR>prescribed acts or rites.<BR>--10 A rite,<BR>ceremony.<BR>--11 Gaining, obtaining.<BR>--12 Affixing, prefixing (as<BR>terminations, suffixes &c.).<BR>--13 The food<BR>given to elephants (to make them<BR>intoxicated);<BR>विधानसंपादितदानशोभितैः K. (where विधान means ‘rule’<BR>also);<BR>उत्क्षिप्तहस्ततलदत्तविधानपिंडस्नेहस्रुतिस्नपितबाहुरिभाधिराजं Śi. 5. 51.<BR>--14 Wealth.<BR>--15 Pain, agony,<BR>torment, distress.<BR>--16 An act of<BR>hostility.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गः, --ज्ञः a wise or<BR>learned man.<BR>--युक्त a. in<BR>accordance with or conformable to sacred<BR>precept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0976-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधानकं|विधानक
विधानकं Distress, affliction, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधायक|विधायकः
विधायक a. (यिका f.,) विधायिन् a.<BR>1 Arranging, disposing.<BR>--2 Doing,<BR>making, performing, executing.<BR>--3<BR>Creating.<BR>--4 Enjoying, prescribing,<BR>laying down<BR>--5 Consigning,<BR>committing, delivering (to the care<BR>of).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिः|विधि
विधिः [विधा-कि]<BR>1 Doing,<BR>performance, practice, an act or action;<BR>ब्रह्मध्यानाभ्यसनविधिना योगनिद्रां गतस्य<BR>Bh. 3. 41; योगविधि R. 8. 22; अस्याः<BR>सर्गविधौ V. 1. 8; लेत्वाविधि<BR>Māl. 1. 35.<BR>--2 Method, manner, way, means,<BR>mode; Pt. 1. 376.<BR>--3 A rule,<BR>commandment, any precept which<BR>enjoins something for the first time<BR>(as distinguished from नियम and<BR>परिसंख्या q.q. v.v.); विधिरत्यंतमप्राप्तौ;<BR>चि कीर्षाकृतिसाध्यत्वहेतुधीविषयो विधिः,<BR>वहति विधिहुतं या हविः Ś. 1. 1.<BR>--4 A sacred<BR>precept or rule, ordinance, injunction,<BR>law, a sacred command, religious<BR>commandment (opp. अर्थवाद which means<BR>‘an explanatory statement coupled<BR>with legends and illustrations’; see<BR>अर्थवाद); प्रवृत्तिपरं वाक्यं विधिः, as<BR>ज्योतिष्टोमेन स्वर्गकामो यजेत; श्रद्धा वित्तं<BR>विधिश्चेति त्रितयं तत्समागतं Ś. 7. 29;<BR>R. 2. 16.<BR>--5 Any religious act or<BR>ceremony, a rite, ceremony; स चेत् स्वयं<BR>कर्मसु धर्मचारिणां त्वमंतरायो भवसि च्युतो<BR>विधिः R. 3. 45, 1. 34.<BR>--6 Behaviour,<BR>conduct.<BR>--7 Condition; V. 4.<BR>--8<BR>Creation, formation; सामग्र्यविधौ<BR>Ku. 3. 28; कल्याणी विधिषु विचित्रता<BR>विधातुः Ki. 7. 7.<BR>--9 The creator.<BR>--10<BR>Fate, destiny, luck; विधौ वामारंभे<BR>मन समुचितैषा परिणतिः Māl. 4. 4.<BR>--11<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-b" target="_blank">Page0977-b+ 57</a>]<BR>The food of elephants.<BR>--12 Time.<BR>--13 A physician.<BR>--14 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--घ्न a. disregarding<BR>prescribed rites or rules.<BR>--ज्ञ a.<BR>knowing the ritual.<BR>--(ज्ञः) a Brāhmaṇa<BR>versed in the ritual, a ritualist.<BR>--दर्शकः a priest at a sacrifice who<BR>sees that everything is done<BR>according to the precepts, and corrects<BR>any deviation from them.<BR>--दुष्ट,<BR>--विहित a. prescribed by rule, enjoined<BR>by law.<BR>--देशकः {1} = विधिदर्शक above.<BR>{2} a preceptor, teacher.<BR>--द्वैधं<BR>diversity of rules, variance of precept or<BR>commandment.<BR>--पूर्वकं ind.<BR>according to rule.<BR>--प्रयोगः application of a<BR>rule.<BR>--योगः the force or influence<BR>of fate.<BR>--वधूः f. an epithet of<BR>Sarasvatī.<BR>--हीन a. devoid of rule,<BR>unauthorised, irregular.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सा
विधित्सा<BR>1 Desire to do or perform.<BR>--2 Design, purpose, desire in<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधित्सित
विधित्सित a. Intended to be done.<BR>--तं Intention, design.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधिवत्
विधिवत्, विधितः ind. According to<BR>law, agreeably to precept or rule,<BR>in conformity to prescribed rules,<BR>in due form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधितः
विधिवत्, विधितः ind. According to<BR>law, agreeably to precept or rule,<BR>in conformity to prescribed rules,<BR>in due form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधेय|विधेयः
विधेय pot. p.<BR>1 To be done or<BR>performed.<BR>--2 To be enjoyed or<BR>prescribed.<BR>--3 (a) Dependent on.<BR>at the disposal of; अथ विधिविधेयः<BR>परिचयः Māl. 2. 13. (b) Subject<BR>to, influenced or controlled by,<BR>subdued or overpowered by (usually<BR>in comp.); तिद्राविधेयं नरदेवसैन्यं<BR>R. 7. 62; संभाव्यमानस्नेहरसेनाभिसंधिना<BR>विधेयीकृतोऽपि Māl. 1. Bg. 2. 64;<BR>भ्रातुः सौहार्देन विधेयीकृतोस्मि Mv. 7;<BR>Mu. 3. 1; Śi. 3. 20; R. 19. 4.<BR>--4 Obedient, tractable, compliant,<BR>submissive; अविधेयेंद्रियः पुंसां<BR>गौरिवैति विधेयतां Ki. 11. 33.<BR>--5 To be<BR>predicated (in gram &c.); अत्र<BR>मिथ्यामहिमत्वं नानुवाद्यं अपि तु विधेयं<BR>K. P. 7.<BR>--यं<BR>1 What ought to be<BR>done, a duty; Ki. 1. 25, 16. 62.<BR>--2 The predicate of a proposition.<BR>--यः A servant, dependant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अविमर्शः a fault of composition<BR>which consists in assigning to the<BR>predicate a subordinate position or<BR>in expressing it imperfectly (<BR>अविमृष्टः प्राधान्येनानिर्दिष्टो विधेयांशो यत्र<BR>K. P. 7: see examples ad loc.).<BR>--आत्मन्<BR>m. N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--ज्ञ a. one who<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-c" target="_blank">Page0977-c+ 56</a>]<BR>knows one's duty; स भृत्यो यो<BR>विधेयज्ञः Pt. 1. 337.<BR>--पदं {1} the<BR>object to be accomplished. {2} the<BR>predicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुः|विधु
विधुः [व्यध्-कु; Uṇ. 1. 23]<BR>1 The<BR>moon; सविता विधवति विधुरपि<BR>सवितरति दिनंति यामिन्यः K. P. 10.<BR>--2<BR>Camphor.<BR>--3 A demon, fiend.<BR>--4 An<BR>expiatory oblation.<BR>--5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--6 N. of Brahman.<BR>--7 N. of Śiva.<BR>--8 Wind.<BR>--9 War, battle.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्षयः waning of the moon, the<BR>period of the dark fortnight of a<BR>month.<BR>--पंजरः (also पिंजरः) a<BR>scimitar, sabre.<BR>--प्रिया a Nakṣatra or<BR>lunar mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुत|विधुतः
विधुत See विधूत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुतिः|विधुति
विधुतिः f. Shaking, trepidation,<BR>tremor; वैनायक्यश्चिरं वो वदनविधुतयः<BR>पांतु चीत्कारवत्यः Māl. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुननं|विधुनन
विधुननं<BR>1 Shaking or tossing<BR>about, agitating.<BR>--2 Trembling,<BR>tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुंतुदः|विधुन्तुद|विधुंतुद|विधुन्तुदः
विधुंतुदः N. of Rāhu; विधुमिव<BR>विकटविधुंतुददंतदलनगलितामृतधारं<BR>Gīt. 4; आभिमुख्यं शशांकस्य यथाद्यापि<BR>विधुंतुदः Pt. 1. 326; N. 4. 71;<BR>Śi. 2. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुर|विधुरं|विधुरः
विधुर a. [विगता धूर्यस्य अच् समा˚]<BR>1 Distressed, troubled, afflicted,<BR>overwhelmed with grief, miserable;<BR>Māl. 2. 3, 9. 11, U. 3. 38, 6. 41,<BR>Ki. 11. 26; Śi. 9. 77, 17. 66,<BR>Bh. 3. 8, 114.<BR>--2 Love-lorn,<BR>bereaved, suffering separation from a wife<BR>or husband; मयि च विधुरे भावः<BR>कांताप्रवृत्तिपराङ्मुखः V. 4. 20; विधुरां<BR>ज्वलनातिसर्जनान्ननु मां प्रापय पत्युरंतिकं<BR>Ku. 4. 32; विधुरबंधुरबंधुरमैक्षत Śi. 6. 29,<BR>12. 8.<BR>--3 Devoid, deprived, or<BR>destitute of, free from; सा बै कलंकविधुरा<BR>मधुराननश्रीः Bv. 2. 5.<BR>--4 Adverse,<BR>hostile, unfriendly; Pt. 2. 81.<BR>--रः<BR>A widower.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Alarm, fear,<BR>anxiety.<BR>--2 Separation from a wife<BR>or husband, bereavement suffered<BR>by a lover or mistress.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दर्शनं {1} the sight of danger or<BR>alarm; विना विधुरदर्शनं स्वामिनो<BR>मंदादरा भवंति H. 2. {2} a feeling of<BR>agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुरा
विधुरा Curds mixed with sugar<BR>and spices.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधू
विधू {5} {c10c} U., {c6c} P.<BR>1 To shake,<BR>move, cause to tremble;<BR>वायुर्विधूनयति चंपकपुष्परेणून् Kavirahasya;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">Page0978-a+ 57</a>]<BR>मृदुपवनविधूतान् Rs. 6. 29; 3. 10;<BR>दीर्घां वेणीं विधुन्वाना Mb.<BR>--2 To shake<BR>off, destroy, expel, drive away;<BR>कपेर्विधवितुं द्युतिं Bk. 9. 28; R. 9. 72<BR>v. l.<BR>--3 To spurn, despise, treat<BR>with contempt; R. 11. 40.<BR>--4 To<BR>leave, give up, abandon;<BR>N. 1. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0977-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधुवनं|विधुवन
विधुवनं Shaking, trembling,<BR>tremor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूत|विधूतं
विधूत p. p.<BR>1 Shaken or tossed<BR>about, waved.<BR>--2 Tremulous.<BR>--3<BR>Shaken off, dispelled, removed.<BR>--4<BR>Unsteady.<BR>--5 Abandoned.<BR>--तं<BR>Repugnance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कल्मष a.<BR>free from sin.<BR>--केश a. one who<BR>has tossed about the hair;<BR>Ki. 8. 33.<BR>--निद्र a. awakened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूतिः|विधूति
विधूतिः f., विधूननं Shaking, tremor,<BR>agitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधूनित|विधूनितं
विधूनित a.<BR>1 Agitated, alarmed.<BR>--2<BR>Harassed, annoyed, molested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृ
विधृ {c10c} U.<BR>1 To seize, catch,<BR>catch or take hold of; अंशुकपल्लवेन<BR>विधृतः Amaru. 79, 85.<BR>--2 To put<BR>on, wear, use; R. 12. 40.<BR>--3 To<BR>maintain, bear, support, hold up;<BR>शिरसा विधृता नित्यं Pt. 1. 82 (where<BR>sense 2 is also intended); Bh. 3. 23.<BR>--4 To fix upon, direct towards.<BR>--5<BR>To separate, divide.<BR>--6 To arrange;<BR>manage.<BR>--7 To with hold, obstruct,<BR>restrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृत|विधृतं
विधृत p. p.<BR>1 Seized, held,<BR>grasped.<BR>--2 Separated, kept asunder or<BR>separate.<BR>--3 Assumed, possessed.<BR>--4 Checked, restrained.<BR>--5<BR>Supported, protected, borne up; (see धृ<BR>with वि).<BR>--तं<BR>1 Disregard of a<BR>command.<BR>--2 Dissatisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विधृतिः|विधृति
विधृतिः f. Arrangement,<BR>regulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंस्
विध्वंस् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To fall to pieces.<BR>--2 To be dispersed or scattered.<BR>--3 To perish, be destroyed or<BR>ruined. --Caus.<BR>1 To destroy,<BR>crush, annihilate.<BR>--2 To injure,<BR>hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसः|विध्वंस
विध्वंसः<BR>1 Ruin, destruction.<BR>--2<BR>Enmity, aversion; dislike.<BR>--3 An<BR>insult, offence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वंसिन्
विध्वंसिन् a.<BR>1 Being ruined,<BR>falling to pieces.<BR>--2 Hostile, adverse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विध्वस्त
विध्वस्त p. p.<BR>1 Ruined, destroyed;<BR>Pt. 2. 113.<BR>--2 Scattered about,<BR>tossed up.<BR>--3 Obscured, darkened.<BR>--4 Eclipsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनद्
विनद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sound, resound;<BR>Bg. 1. 12.<BR>--2 To roar, cry out.<BR>--3<BR>To fill with cries. --Caus. To cause<BR>to cry or utter notes; अंबुदैः<BR>शिखिगणो विनाद्यते Ghaṭ. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनदः|विनद
विनदः<BR>1 Sound, noise.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्
विनम् {c1c} P. To bend oneself,<BR>stoop, be bent; विनमंति चास्य तरवः<BR>प्रचये Ki. 6. 34; Bh. 1. 67;<BR>Bk. 7. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनत|विनतः
विनत p. p.<BR>1 Bent down, bowed.<BR>--2 Stooping, drooping, inclined;<BR>Ś. 3. 10.<BR>--3 Sunk down, depressed.<BR>--4 Bent, crooked, curved.<BR>--5<BR>Humble, modest.<BR>--6 Changed into a<BR>lingual letter; see विनाम.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आनन a. with downcast face,<BR>dejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनता
विनता<BR>1 N. of the mother of<BR>Aruṇa and Garuḍa, said to be one<BR>of the wives of Kaśyapa; see गरुड.<BR>--2 A kind of basket.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नंदनः, --सुतः, --सूनुः epithets of<BR>Garuḍa or Aruṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनतिः|विनति
विनतिः f.<BR>1 Bowing down,<BR>bending, stooping.<BR>--2 Modesty,<BR>humility.<BR>--3 A request.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनमनं|विनमन
विनमनं Bending, bowing,<BR>stooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्र
विनम्र a.<BR>1 Bent down, stooping;<BR>Ki. 4. 2.<BR>--2 Depressed, sunk down.<BR>--3 Modest, humble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनम्रकं|विनम्रक
विनम्रकं The flower of the Tagara<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनश्
विनश् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be destroyed,<BR>perish, die.<BR>--2 To disappear, vanish.<BR>--3 To be lost or ruined.<BR>--4 To be<BR>frustrated or foiled. --Caus. To<BR>destroy, annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनशनं|विनशन|विनशनः
विनशनं Perishing, loss,<BR>destruction, disappearance.<BR>--नः N. of the<BR>place where the river Sarasvatī is<BR>lost in the sand; cf. Ms. 2. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्ट|विनष्टः
विनष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Perished,<BR>destroyed, ruined.<BR>--2 Disappeared, lost.<BR>--3<BR>Spoiled, corrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनष्टिः|विनष्टि
विनष्टिः f.<BR>1 Utter ruin or<BR>destruction.<BR>--2 Disappearance, vanishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशः|विनाश
विनाशः<BR>1 Destruction, ruin, utter<BR>loss, decay.<BR>--2 Removal.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उन्मुख a. about to perish, ripe to<BR>meet one's doom.<BR>--धर्मन्, --धर्मिन् a.<BR>subject to decay, perishable,<BR>transient; विषयेषु विनाशधर्मसु<BR>त्रिदिवस्थेष्वपि निःस्पृहोऽभवत् R. 8. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाशनं|विनाशन|विनाशनः
विनाशनं Destruction, ruin,<BR>annihilation.<BR>--नः A destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनस|विनसः
विनस a. (सा --सी f.) Noseless;<BR>Bk. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विना
विना ind. Without, except (with<BR>acc., instr. or abl.); यथा तानं विना<BR>रागो यथा मानं विना नृपः । यथा दानं<BR>विना हस्ती तथा ज्ञानं विना यतिः<BR>Bv. 1. 119; पंकैर्विना सरो भाति सदः<BR>खलजनैर्विना । कटुवर्णैर्विना काव्यं मानसं<BR>विषयैर्विना 1. 116; विना वाहनहस्तिभ्यः क्रियतां<BR>सर्वमोक्षः Mu. 7; Śi. 2. 9. (विनाकृ<BR>means ‘to leave, abandon, bereave,<BR>deprive of’; मदनेन विनाकृता रतिः<BR>Ku. 4. 21 ‘bereft of Cupid’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः f. a figure of speech<BR>in which विना is used in a poetically<BR>charming way; विनार्थसंबंध एव<BR>विनोक्तिः R. G.; see K. P. 10 also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाडिः|विनाडि
विनाडिः, विनाडिका A measure<BR>of time equal to one-sixtieth part<BR>of a Ghaṭikā or equal to 24 seconds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाडिका
विनाडिः, विनाडिका A measure<BR>of time equal to one-sixtieth part<BR>of a Ghaṭikā or equal to 24 seconds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनामः|विनाम
विनामः (In gram.). Change<BR>into a lingual or cerebral letter, the<BR>substitution of ष् for स् and ण् for न्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनायकः|विनायक
विनायकः<BR>1 A remover (of<BR>obstacles).<BR>--2 N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR>--3 A<BR>Buddhist deified teacher.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>Garuḍa.<BR>--5 An obstacle, impediment.<BR>--6 A spiritual preceptor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनायिका
विनायिका The wife of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनासक|विनासकः
विनास(सि)क a. Noseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनासिक
विनास(सि)क a. Noseless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनाहः|विनाह
विनाहः A cover for the mouth<BR>of a well; cf. वीनाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकॄ
विनिकॄ {c6c} A.<BR>1 To throw,<BR>abandon, cast off; Ku. 4. 6.<BR>--2 To<BR>throw about, scatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिकीर्ण
विनिकीर्ण p. p. Scattered, thrown<BR>about.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षिप्
विनिक्षिप् {c6c} A.<BR>1 To entrust,<BR>deliver over.<BR>--2 To place in or upon.<BR>--3 To throw down, overthrow.<BR>--4<BR>To engage in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिक्षेपः|विनिक्षेप
विनिक्षेपः Throwing down, sending<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिगड
विनिगड a. Without fetters,<BR>unrestrained, free.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिग्रह्
विनिग्रह् {c9c} U.<BR>1 To restrain,<BR>check; obstruct, impede.<BR>--2 To lay<BR>hold of, seize.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिग्रहः|विनिग्रह
विनिग्रहः<BR>1 Restraining, curbing,<BR>subduing; Bg. 13. 7, 17. 16;<BR>Ms. 9. 263.<BR>--2 Mutual opposition or<BR>antithesis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिद्र|विनिद्रः
विनिद्र a.<BR>1 Sleepless, awake<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">Page0979-a+ 56</a>]<BR>(fig. also); तामेकतस्तव बिभार्त्ति<BR>गुरुर्विनिद्रः R. 5. 66.<BR>--2 Budded,<BR>opened, full-blown, expanded;<BR>विनिद्रमंदाररजोरुणांगुली Ku. 5. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0978-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपत्
विनिपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To fly at, fall<BR>down, descend; Rs. 4. 19.<BR>--2 To<BR>attack, assail. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to<BR>fall down, ruin, destroy; कटेन<BR>विनिपातितो यामि Mk. 2. 8.<BR>--2 To throw<BR>or pull down.<BR>--3 To kill, deprive of<BR>life.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिपातः|विनिपात
विनिपातः<BR>1 Falling down, a fall.<BR>--2 A great fall, calamity, an<BR>evil, loss, ruin, destruction;<BR>विवेकभ्रष्टानां भवति विनिपातः शतमुखः<BR>Bh. 2. 10 (where it has sense 1 also);<BR>विधिहेतुरहेतुरागसां विनिपातोपि समः<BR>समुन्नतेः Ki. 2. 34.<BR>--3 Decay, death.<BR>--4 Hell, perdition; Ś. 5.<BR>--5<BR>Occurrence, happening.<BR>--6 Pain,<BR>distress.<BR>--7 Disrespect.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शंसिन् a. portentous, foreboding ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमयः|विनिमय
विनिमयः<BR>1 Exchange, barter;<BR>कार्यविनिमयेन M. 1; संपद्विनिमयेनोभौ<BR>दधतुर्भुवनद्वयं R. 1. 26.<BR>--2 A pledge,<BR>deposit, security.<BR>--3 Transmutation<BR>(of letters).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिमेषः|विनिमेष
विनिमेषः Twinkling(of the<BR>eyes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियम्
विनियम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To restrain,<BR>check, curb; Bg. 6. 24.<BR>--2 To limit,<BR>restrict.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियत
विनियत p. p. Controlled, checked,<BR>restrained, regulated; as in<BR>विनियताहार, विनियतवाच् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियमः|विनियम
विनियमः Control, restraint, check.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियुज्
विनियुज् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To use, expend.<BR>--2 To appoint, employ.<BR>--3 To<BR>divide, apportion, distribute; प्रत्येकं<BR>विनियुक्तात्मा कथं न ज्ञास्यसि प्रभो<BR>Ku. 2. 31.<BR>--4 To disconnect, separate.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To appoint, employ.<BR>--2<BR>To enjoin, order, command.<BR>--3 To<BR>offer, present, give.<BR>--4 To perform,<BR>do, dispose of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियुक्त
विनियुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Separated,<BR>loosed, detached.<BR>--2 Attached to,<BR>appointed.<BR>--3 Applied to.<BR>--4<BR>Commanded, enjoined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनियोगः|विनियोग
विनियोगः<BR>1 Separation, parting,<BR>detachment.<BR>--2 Leaving, giving up,<BR>abandoning.<BR>--3 Employment, use,<BR>application, disposal; बभूव<BR>विनियोगज्ञः साधनीयेषु वस्तुषु R. 17. 67;<BR>प्राणायामे विनियागेः &c.<BR>--4 Appointment<BR>to a duty, commission, charge;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">Page0979-b+ 55</a>]<BR>विनियोगप्रसादा हि किंकराः प्रभविष्णुषु<BR>Ku. 6. 62.<BR>--5 An obstacle,<BR>impediment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्गम्
विनिर्गम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go out.<BR>--2<BR>To disappear, vanish.<BR>--3 To go<BR>away, depart.<BR>--4 To escape from,<BR>liberate oneself from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्गमः|विनिर्गम
विनिर्गमः Disappearance. = {9}<BR>Departure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्जि
विनिर्जि {c1c} P.<BR>1 To conquer<BR>completely.<BR>--2 To subdue, overpower,<BR>master.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्जयः|विनिर्जय
विनिर्जयः Complete victory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्णी
विनिर्णी = निर्णी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्णयः|विनिर्णय
विनिर्णयः<BR>1 Complete settlement<BR>or ascertainment, full decision.<BR>--2<BR>Certainty.<BR>--3 A settled rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्बंधः|विनिर्बन्ध|विनिर्बंध|विनिर्बन्धः
विनिर्बंधः Persistence,<BR>pertinacity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मा
विनिर्मा See निर्मा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मित
विनिर्मित p. p.<BR>1 Formed or made<BR>of.<BR>--2 Made, created.<BR>--3<BR>Celebrated, observed (as a feast).<BR>--4<BR>Determined, destined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मुच्
विनिर्मुच् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To loosen, free<BR>from.<BR>--2 To set free, release,<BR>liberate.<BR>--3 To discharge, shoot off.<BR>--4<BR>To abandon, give up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्मुक्तिः|विनिर्मुक्ति
विनिर्मुक्तिः f. Release, liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिर्वृत्
विनिर्वृत् See निवृत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिविद्
विनिविद् See निविद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिविश्
विनिविश् {c6c} P. To be placed or<BR>be seated in. --Caus.<BR>1 To fix,<BR>place; Ku. 1. 49; R. 5. 63; मदुरसि<BR>कुचकलशं विनिवेशय Gīt. 12.<BR>--2 To<BR>populate or colonize.<BR>--3 To<BR>introduce.<BR>--4 To add, insert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवेशः|विनिवेश
विनिवेशः<BR>1 Entrance, settling down<BR>in a place.<BR>--2 An impression; Ś. 6. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृ
विनिवृ {c10c} U. or --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>prevent, ward off, suppress; विनयं<BR>विनिवार्य Māl. 1. 18.<BR>--2 To prohibit,<BR>forbid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्
विनिवृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To turn back,<BR>return.<BR>--2 To cease, come to an<BR>end; सपिंडता तु पुरुषे सप्तमे विनिवर्तते<BR>Ms. 5. 60; Bg. 2. 59.<BR>--3 To desist, turn away,<BR>abstain (from); देवनात्, युद्धात् &c.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to cease or step,<BR>withdraw; Ś. 7. 26.<BR>--2 To restrain,<BR>withhold.<BR>--3 To renounce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्त|विनिवृत्तः
विनिवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Returned,<BR>turned away.<BR>--2 Stopped, ceased,<BR>desisted from.<BR>--3 Retired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिवृत्तिः|विनिवृत्ति
विनिवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Cessation, stopping,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-c" target="_blank">Page0979-c+ 56</a>]<BR>removing; शक्राभ्यसूयाविनिवृत्तये<BR>R. 6. 74.<BR>--2 End, stop, termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चि
विनिश्चि {c5c} U. To determine,<BR>resolve, ascertain; विनिश्चेतुं शक्यो न<BR>सुखमिति वा दुःखमिति वा U. 1. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्चयः|विनिश्चय
विनिश्चयः<BR>1 Fixing, settling,<BR>ascertainment.<BR>--2 A decision, resolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिश्वासः|विनिश्वास
विनिश्वासः Hard breathing or<BR>respiration, sighing, a sigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिष्पेषः|विनिष्पेष
विनिष्पेषः Bruising, crushing,<BR>grinding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनिहत|विनिहतः
विनिहत p. p.<BR>1 Struck down,<BR>wounded.<BR>--2 Killed.<BR>--3<BR>Completely overcome.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Any great or<BR>unavoidable calamity, such as that<BR>inflicted by fate or heaven.<BR>--2 A<BR>portent, comet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनी
विनी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To remove, take<BR>away, destroy (said to be Atm.<BR>only except where it has ‘a part of<BR>the body’ for its object);<BR>पटुपटहध्वनिभिर्विनीतनिद्रः R. 9. 71; विनीतखेदः<BR>13. 35, 46; 15. 48; Śi. 10. 62,<BR>Ki. 7. 30, Ku. 1. 9, 5. 32.<BR>--2 To teach,<BR>instruct, educate, train; विनिन्युरेनं<BR>गुरवो गुरुप्रियं R. 3. 29; 5. 101.<BR>15. 69; 18. 51; Y. 1. 311; Ku. 1. 34.<BR>--3 To tame, subdue, govern,<BR>control (fig. also); वन्यान्विनेष्यन्निव दुष्ट<BR>सत्वान् R. 2. 8; 6. 27, 14. 75;<BR>Ki. 2. 41; वनगज इव<BR>तस्मात्सोभ्युपायैर्विनेयः Mu. 3. 25.<BR>--4 To appease, pacify<BR>(anger) (Atm.); R. 2. 49.<BR>--5<BR>To pass away, spend (as time);<BR>कथमपि यामिनीं विनीय Gīt. 8.<BR>--6 To<BR>carry through, perform, complete,<BR>finish.<BR>--7 To spend, apply to use<BR>(Atm.). शतं विनयते Sk.<BR>--8 To give,<BR>present, pay, pay off (as tribute)<BR>(Atm.); करं विनयते Sk.<BR>--9 To<BR>lead or conduct towards;<BR>Ku. 7. 9.<BR>--10 To bid, direct, order;<BR>Ku. 3. 41.<BR>--11 To bend down, incline.<BR>--12 To spread, stretch out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनय|विनयः
विनय a.<BR>1 Cast, thrown.<BR>--2<BR>Secret.<BR>--3 Ill-behaved.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>Guidance, discipline, instruction (in<BR>one's duties), moral training;<BR>प्रजानां विनयाधानात् R. 1. 24;<BR>Māl. 10. 5.<BR>--2 Sense of propriety,<BR>decorum, decency; अनुयास्यन्मुनितनयां<BR>सहसा विनयेन वारितप्रसरः Ś. 1. 29.<BR>--3 Polite conduct, gentleman-like<BR>bearing, good breeding or manners;<BR>R. 6. 79; Māl. 1. 18.<BR>--4 Modesty,<BR>humility; सुष्ठु शोभसे आर्यपुत्र एतेन<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-a" target="_blank">Page0980-a+ 56</a>]<BR>विनयमाहात्म्येन U. 1; विद्या ददाति वि<BR>नयम्; तथापि नीचैर्विनयाददृश्यत<BR>R. 3. 34; 10. 71 (where Malli. renders<BR>विनय by इंद्रियजय or restraint of<BR>passions, unnecessarily in our opinion^1).<BR>--5 Reverence, courtesy, obeisance.<BR>--6 Conduct in general.<BR>--7 Drawing<BR>off, taking away, removing;<BR>Śi. 10. 42.<BR>--8 A man who has subdued his<BR>senses.<BR>--9 A trader, merchant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवनत a. stooping<BR>humbly.<BR>--ग्राहिन् a. tractable, obedient,<BR>submissive.<BR>--भाज् a. modest,<BR>wellbehaved.<BR>--वाच् a. speaking mildly<BR>or affably.<BR>--स्थ a. modest.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0979-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनयनं|विनयन
विनयनं<BR>1 Removing, taking away;<BR>Me. 52.<BR>--2 Education, instruction,<BR>training, discipline.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीत|विनीतः
विनीत p. p.<BR>1 Taken away,<BR>removed.<BR>--2 Well-trained, educated,<BR>disciplined.<BR>--3 Refined,<BR>well-behaved.<BR>--4 Modest, humble, meek,<BR>gentle.<BR>--5 Decent, decorous,<BR>gentlemanly.<BR>--6 Sent away, dismissed.<BR>--7<BR>Tamed, broken in.<BR>--8 Plain,<BR>simple, (as a dress).<BR>--9 Having<BR>the passions under control,<BR>selfsubdued.<BR>--10 Chastised, punished.<BR>--11 Tractable, governable.<BR>--12<BR>Lovely, handsome. (See नी with<BR>वि also).<BR>--तः<BR>1 A trained horse.<BR>--2 A<BR>trader.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a. humble,<BR>lowly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतकं|विनीतक
विनीतकं<BR>1 A vehicle or<BR>conveyance (a litter &c.).<BR>--2 A carrier,<BR>bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीतिः|विनीति
विनीतिः f.<BR>1 Training, good<BR>behaviour.<BR>--2 Respect, reverence,<BR>esteem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनीयः|विनीय
विनीयः<BR>1 Sediment, dregs.<BR>--2 Sin,<BR>crime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनेतृ
विनेतृ m.<BR>1 A leader, guide.<BR>--2 A<BR>teacher, an instructor; स तथेति<BR>विनेतुरुदारमतेः प्रतिगृह्य वचो विससर्ज मुनिं<BR>R. 8. 91.<BR>--3 A king, ruler.<BR>--4 A<BR>chastiser, punisher; अयं विनेता<BR>दृप्तानां Mv. 3. 46, 4. 1, R. 6. 39,<BR>14. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनुद्
विनुद् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To strike, pierce.<BR>--2 To play on a musical<BR>instrument (वीणां, आतोद्यं &c.).<BR>--3 To<BR>remove, drive away, dispel. --Caus.<BR>1 To remove, drive away, dispel,<BR>cast off; तापं विनोदय दृष्टिभिः<BR>Gīt. 10; Śi. 4. 66; Ś. 3. 21;<BR>Māl. 9. 41.<BR>--2 To pass, spend (as time).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-b" target="_blank">Page0980-b+ 60</a>]<BR>--3 To divert, amuse, entertain;<BR>क्व नु खल्वात्मानं विनोदयामि Ś. 3;<BR>लतासु दृष्टिं विनोदयामि Ś. 6; R. 14. 77.<BR>--4 To amuse oneself with;<BR>लक्ष्मीर्विमोदयाति येन दिगंतलंबी सोपि<BR>त्वदाननरुचिं विजहाति चंद्रः R. 5. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदः|विनोद
विनोदः<BR>1 Removing, driving away;<BR>श्रमविनोद.<BR>--2 A diversion, an<BR>amusement, any interesting or amusing<BR>pursuit or occupation; प्रायेणैते<BR>रमणविरहेष्वंगनानां विनोदाः Me. 87; मिथ्यैव<BR>व्यसनं वदंति मृगयामीदृग्विनोदः कुतः<BR>Ś. 2. 5.<BR>--3 Play, sport, pastime.<BR>--4<BR>Eagerness, vehement desire.<BR>--5<BR>Pleasure, happiness, gratification;<BR>विलपनवितोदोप्यसुलभः U. 3. 30;<BR>जनयतु रसिकजनेषु मनोरमरतिरसभावविनोदं<BR>Gīt. 12.<BR>--6 A particular mode of<BR>sexual enjoyment.<BR>--7 A kind of<BR>house.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विनोदनं|विनोदन
विनोदनं<BR>1 Removing.<BR>--2 A<BR>diversion &c.; see विनोद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंदु|विन्दु|विन्दुः
विंदु a.<BR>1 Intelligent, wise.<BR>--2<BR>Liberal.<BR>--दुः A drop; see बिंदु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंध्यः|विन्ध्य|विन्ध्यः
विंध्यः<BR>1 N. of a range of<BR>mountains which separates Hindustān<BR>proper from the Deccan or south;<BR>it is one of the seven Kulaparvatas<BR>q. v., and forms the southern limit<BR>of Madhyadeśa; see Ms. 2. 21.<BR>[According to a legend, the Vindhya<BR>mountain, being jealous of the mount<BR>Meru (or Himālaya) demanded that<BR>the sun should revolve round himself<BR>as about Meru, which the sun declined<BR>to do; whereupon the Vindhya began<BR>to rise higher and higher so as to<BR>obstruct the path of the sun and moon.<BR>The gods being alarmed sought the aid<BR>of the sage Agastya, who approached<BR>the mountain and requested that by<BR>bending down he would give him an<BR>easy passage to the south, and that he<BR>would retain the same position till his<BR>return. This Vindhya consented to do<BR>(because according to one account, he<BR>regarded Agastya as his teacher); but<BR>Agastya never returned from the south,<BR>and Vindhya never attained the height<BR>of Meru].<BR>--2 A hunter.<BR>--ध्या<BR>1<BR>N. of a plant (लवली).<BR>--2 Small<BR>cardamoms.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अटवी<BR>the great Vindhya forest.<BR>--कूटः,<BR>--कूटनं epithets of the sage Agastya.<BR>--वासिन् m. an epithet of the<BR>grammarian व्याडि.<BR>--(नी) an epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्न|विन्नः
विन्न p. p. [विद् कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Known.<BR>--2 Got, obtained.<BR>--3<BR>Discussed, investigated.<BR>--4 Placed,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">Page0980-c+ 57</a>]<BR>fixed.<BR>--5 Married; (See विद्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्नकः|विन्नक
विन्नकः N. of Agastya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्
विन्यस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To put down,<BR>deposit, place; विन्यस्यंती भुवि गणनया<BR>देहलीदत्तषुष्पैः Me. 87; Bk. 3. 3.<BR>--2<BR>To fix in or on, direct towards; रामे<BR>विन्यस्तमानसाः Rām.<BR>--3 To deliver<BR>or make over, commit to the care of,<BR>entrust; सुतविन्यस्तपत्नीकः Y. 3. 45.<BR>--4 To arrange, dispose, adjust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यस्त|विन्यस्तः
विन्यस्त p. p.<BR>1 Placed or put<BR>down.<BR>--2 Inlaid, paved.<BR>--3 Fixed.<BR>--4 Arranged.<BR>--5 Delivered.<BR>--6<BR>Presented, offered.<BR>--7 Deposited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विन्यासः|विन्यास
विन्यासः<BR>1 Entrusting,<BR>depositing.<BR>--2 A deposit.<BR>--3<BR>Arrangement, adjustment, disposition;<BR>अक्षरविन्यासः ‘inscribing letters’;<BR>प्रत्यक्षरश्लेषमयप्रबंधविन्यासवैदग्धनिधिः Vās.<BR>‘composition of a work &c.’<BR>--4 A<BR>collection, an assemblage.<BR>--5 A site<BR>or receptacle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्
विप् {c10c} A. (वेपयति-ते) To throw,<BR>cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्
विप् m.<BR>1 A praiser, singer of<BR>hymns.<BR>--2 A wise man. --f.<BR>1<BR>Praise, a hymn.<BR>--2 A finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्ष|विपक्षः
विपक्ष a. Hostile, inimical,<BR>adverse, contrary.<BR>--क्षः<BR>1 An enemy,<BR>adversary, opponent; गुणास्तस्य<BR>विपक्षेपि गुणिनो लेभिरेंतरं R. 17. 75;<BR>Śi. 11. 59.<BR>--2 A rival or fellow wife;<BR>R. 19. 20.<BR>--3 A disputant;<BR>Ki. 17. 43.<BR>--4 (In logic) A<BR>negative instance, an instance<BR>on the opposite side, (i. e.<BR>that in which the साध्य or major term<BR>is not found); निश्चितसाध्याभाववान्<BR>विपक्षः T. S.; Mu. 5. 10.<BR>--5 (In<BR>gram.) An exception.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भावः, --वृत्ति f. hostility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षता
विपक्षता --त्वं Hostility, enmity,<BR>opposition; R. 3. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्षत्वं|विपक्षत्व
विपक्षता --त्वं Hostility, enmity,<BR>opposition; R. 3. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपच्
विपच् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To mature,<BR>develop, ripen; bear fruit; (समारंभाः)<BR>गर्भशालिसधर्माणस्तस्य गूढं विपेचिरे<BR>R. 17. 53.<BR>--2 To digest.<BR>--3 To cook<BR>thoroughly.<BR>--4 To melt, dissolve,<BR>liquefy.<BR>--5 To roast. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>cook thoroughly.<BR>--2 To melt, liquefy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्त्रिम
विपक्त्रिम a.<BR>1 Fully ripened or<BR>matured.<BR>--2 Developed, fulfilled<BR>(as the consequences of former acts).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपक्व
विपक्व a.<BR>1 Fully ripened or<BR>matured.<BR>--2 Developed, fulfilled; यच्च<BR>तप्तं तपस्तस्य विपक्वं फलमद्य नः<BR>Ku. 6. 10.<BR>--3 Cooked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0980-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपंचिका|विपञ्चिका
विपंचिका, विपंची<BR>1 A lute.<BR>--2 Play, sport, pastime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपंची|विपञ्ची
विपंचिका, विपंची<BR>1 A lute.<BR>--2 Play, sport, pastime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपट्
विपट् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To tear up or<BR>out; (केतकबर्हं) विपाटयामास युवा<BR>नखाग्रैः R. 6. 17.<BR>--2 To pull or<BR>draw out, extract.<BR>--3 To root up,<BR>eradicate.<BR>--4 To open, unfold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाटनं|विपाटन
विपाटनं<BR>1 Tearing open, splitting.<BR>--2 Eradication.<BR>--3 Spoliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपण्
विपण् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To sell, barter;<BR>आभीरदेशे किल चंद्रकांतं<BR>त्रिभिर्वराटैर्विपणंति गोपाः Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 To bet,<BR>stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणः|विपण
विपणः, विपणनं<BR>1 Sale; Ms. 3. 152.<BR>--2 Petty trade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणनं|विपणन
विपणः, विपणनं<BR>1 Sale; Ms. 3. 152.<BR>--2 Petty trade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणिः|विपणि
विपणिः, --णी f.<BR>1 A market,<BR>market-place, stall; हा हा नश्यति<BR>मन्मथस्य विपणिः सौभाग्यपण्याकरः<BR>Mk. 8. 38; Śi. 5. 24; R. 16. 41.<BR>--2 An<BR>article or commodity for sale.<BR>--3<BR>Trade, traffic; Ms. 10. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणी
विपणिः, --णी f.<BR>1 A market,<BR>market-place, stall; हा हा नश्यति<BR>मन्मथस्य विपणिः सौभाग्यपण्याकरः<BR>Mk. 8. 38; Śi. 5. 24; R. 16. 41.<BR>--2 An<BR>article or commodity for sale.<BR>--3<BR>Trade, traffic; Ms. 10. 116.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपणिन्
विपणिन् m. A trader, merchant,<BR>shop-keeper; Śi. 5. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपथः|विपथ
विपथः A wrong road, bad way<BR>(lit. and fig.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्
विपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To go badly; fail,<BR>miscarry (as a business &c.).<BR>--2<BR>To fall into misfortune or bad<BR>state; स बंधुर्यो विपन्नानामापदुद्धरणक्षमः<BR>H. 1. 31.<BR>--3 To be disabled or<BR>incapacitated.<BR>--4 To die, perish;<BR>नाथवंतस्त्वया लोकास्त्वमनाथा विपत्स्यसे<BR>U. 1. 44; हा तात एष ते<BR>नरेंद्रचित्ताराधनोपकरणं जनो विपद्यते Māl. 5;<BR>Mk. 1. 38.<BR>--5 To obstruct. --Caus. To<BR>destroy, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपत्तिः|विपत्ति
विपत्तिः f.<BR>1 A calamity,<BR>misfortune, disaster, mishap, adversity;<BR>संपत्तौ च विपत्तौ च महतामेकरूपता<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Death, destruction;<BR>अतिरभसकृतानां कर्मणामाविपत्तेर्भवति<BR>हृदयदाही शल्यतुल्यो विपाकः Bh. 2. 99;<BR>R. 19. 56; Ve. 4. 6; हिमसेकविपत्तिः<BR>नलिनी R. 8. 45.<BR>--3 Agony,<BR>torment (यातना).<BR>--त्तिः (m.) An<BR>excellent or distinguished<BR>footsoldier; Ki. 15. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपद्
विपद् f.<BR>1 A calamity, misfortune,<BR>adversity, distress; तत्त्वनिकषग्रावा तु<BR>तेषां (मित्राणां) विपद् H. 1. 210.<BR>--2<BR>Death; सिंहादवापद्विपदं नृसिंहः<BR>R. 18. 35.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्धरणं, --उद्धारः relieving<BR>or extricating (one) from<BR>misfortune.<BR>--कालः times of need,<BR>season of calamity, adversity.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">Page0981-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--ग्रस्त, --युक्त a. overtaken by or<BR>involved in calamity, unhappy,<BR>unfortunate.<BR>--सागरः ‘sea of<BR>misery’ a very heavy calamity or<BR>disaster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपदा
विपदा See विपद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपन्न|विपन्नः
विपन्न p. p.<BR>1 Dead.<BR>--2 Lost,<BR>destroyed.<BR>--3 Unfortunate, afflicted,<BR>distressed, fallen into adversity.<BR>--4<BR>Declined.<BR>--5 Disabled,<BR>incapacitated.<BR>--न्नः A snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणम्
विपरिणम् Caus. To change or<BR>transform into. --Pass.<BR>1 To be<BR>changed into.<BR>--2 To undergo a<BR>change for the worse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणमनं|विपरिणमन
विपरिणमनं, विपरिणामः<BR>1 A change,<BR>an alteration.<BR>--2 Change of form,<BR>transformation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिणामः|विपरिणाम
विपरिणमनं, विपरिणामः<BR>1 A change,<BR>an alteration.<BR>--2 Change of form,<BR>transformation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवृत्
विपरिवृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To turn round,<BR>revolve (fig. also); Bg. 9. 10.<BR>--2<BR>To roll about.<BR>--3 To wander about,<BR>move to and fro.<BR>--4 To return.<BR>--5<BR>To surround; attend upon (with<BR>acc.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरिवर्तनं|विपरिवर्तन|विपरिवर्त्तन
विपरिवर्तनं Turning about,<BR>rolling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरी
विपरी (विपरि + इ) {c2c} P.<BR>1 To turn<BR>in an opposite direction.<BR>--2 To be<BR>otherwise, fail, prove fruitless;<BR>कल्याणं विदधातु वा भगवतीनीतिर्विपर्येतु वा<BR>Māl. 6. 3.<BR>--3 To change for the<BR>worse.<BR>--4 To go round, return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीत|विपरीतः
विपरीत a.<BR>1 Reversed, inverted.<BR>--2 Contrary, opposite, reverse,<BR>inverse; R. 2. 53.<BR>--3 Wrong, contrary<BR>to rule.<BR>--4 False, untrue;<BR>Bv. 2 177.<BR>--5 Unfavourable, adverse.<BR>--6<BR>Cross, acting in an opposite manner.<BR>--7 Disagreeable, inauspicious.<BR>--तः<BR>A particular mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR>--ता<BR>1 An unchaste or<BR>faithless wife.<BR>--2 A perverse woman.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर, --कारक, --कारिन्, --कृत्,<BR>a. perverse, acting in a contrary<BR>manner; Śi. 14. 66.<BR>--चेतस्,--मति<BR>a. having a perverted mind.<BR>--रतं<BR>inverted sexual intercourse; cf.<BR>पुरुषायित.<BR>--लक्षणा ironical description<BR>of a thing by mentioning its contrary<BR>properties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतता
विपरीतता --त्वं Contrariety,<BR>inversion, opposition; लोके गुरुत्वं<BR>विपरीततां वा स्वचेष्टितान्येव नरं नयतिं<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपरीतत्वं|विपरीतत्व
विपरीतता --त्वं Contrariety,<BR>inversion, opposition; लोके गुरुत्वं<BR>विपरीततां वा स्वचेष्टितान्येव नरं नयतिं<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्ययः|विपर्यय|विपर्य्यय|विपर्य्ययः
विपर्ययः<BR>1 Contrariety, reverse,<BR>inversion; आहितो जयविपर्ययोपि मे<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-c" target="_blank">Page0981-c+ 57</a>]<BR>श्लाध्य एव परमेष्ठिना त्वया R. 11. 86;<BR>स्वशरीरशरीरिणावपि श्रुतसंयोगविपर्ययौ यदा<BR>8. 89; नभसः स्फुटतारस्य रात्रेरिव<BR>विपर्ययः (न भाजनं) Ki. 11. 44;<BR>विपर्यये तु Ś. 5. ‘if it be otherwise’, if<BR>contrary be the case; विपर्यये<BR>त्वस्याधिपतेरुल्लंधितः क्षात्रधर्मः स्यात् Ve. 5.<BR>--2<BR>Change (of purpose, dress &c.);<BR>कथमेत्य मतिर्विपर्ययं करिणी<BR>पंकमिवावसीदति Ki. 2. 6; so वेषविपर्ययः Pt. 1.<BR>--3 Absence or non-existence;<BR>समुद्रगारूपविपर्ययेऽपि Ku. 7. 42; त्यागे<BR>श्लाघाविपर्ययः R. 1. 22.<BR>--4 Loss; निद्रा<BR>संज्ञाविपर्ययः Ku. 6. 44 ‘loss of<BR>consciousness’.<BR>--5 Complete<BR>destruction, annihilation.<BR>--6 Exchange,<BR>barter.<BR>--7 Error, trespass, mistake,<BR>misapprehension.<BR>--8 A calamity,<BR>misfortune, adverse fate.<BR>--9<BR>Hostility, enmity.<BR>--10 Perverseness,<BR>opposition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यायः|विपर्याय|विपर्य्याय|विपर्य्यायः
विपर्यायः Reverse, contrariety;<BR>V. 4; see विपर्यय above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यस्
विपर्यस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To overturn,<BR>reverse, invert.<BR>--2 To change, alter.<BR>--3<BR>To take wrongly, misunderstand;<BR>प्रतीकारो व्याधेः सुखमिति विपर्यस्यति<BR>जनः Bh. 3. 92.<BR>--4 To undergo change,<BR>be affected, (intrans.);<BR>दैवेनोपहतस्य बुद्धिरथवा सर्वा विपर्यस्यति<BR>Mu. 6. 8; (cf. the Latin adage ‘quem deus<BR>vult perdere prius dementat’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यस्त|विपर्य्यस्त
विपर्यस्त p. p.<BR>1 Changed,<BR>inverted, reversed; हंत विपर्यस्तः संप्रति<BR>जीवलोकः U. 1.<BR>--2 Opposite, contrary.<BR>--3 Wrongly considered to be real.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुत्रा a woman bearing no<BR>male children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपर्यासः|विपर्यास|विपर्य्यास|विपर्य्यासः
विपर्यासः<BR>1 Change, contrariety,<BR>reverse; विपर्यासं यातो घनविरलभावः<BR>क्षितिरुहां U. 2. 27.<BR>--2 Adverseness,<BR>unfavourableness; as in दैवविपर्यासात्.<BR>--3 Interchange, exchange;<BR>प्रवहणविपर्यासेनागता Mk. 8.<BR>--4 An error, a<BR>mistake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलं|विपल
विपलं A moment, an extremely<BR>small division of time (said to be<BR>equal to one-sixth or one-sixtieth<BR>part of a pala).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपलायनं|विपलायन
विपलायनं Running away,<BR>fleeing in different directions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपश्चित्
विपश्चित् a. Learned, wise;<BR>विपश्चितो विनिन्युरेनं गुरवो गुरुप्रियं<BR>R. 3. 29. --m. A learned or wise man<BR>sage; भवंति ते सभ्यतमा विपश्चितां<BR>मनोगतं वाचि निवेशयंति ये Ki. 14. 4;<BR>Pt. 1. 100.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0981-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाकः|विपाक
विपाकः<BR>1 Cooking, dressing.<BR>--2<BR>Digestion.<BR>--3 Ripening, ripeness,<BR>maturity, development (fig. also);<BR>अमी पृथुस्तंबभृतः पिशंगतां गता<BR>विपाकेन फलस्य शालयः Ki. 4. 26;<BR>वाचां विपाको मम Bv. 4. 42<BR>‘my mature, full-developed, or<BR>dignified words’.<BR>--4 Consequence,<BR>fruit, result, the result of actions<BR>either in this or in a former birth;<BR>अहो मे दारुणतरः कर्मणां विपाकः K. 354;<BR>ममैव जन्मांतरपातकानां<BR>विपाकविस्फूर्जथुरषसह्यः R. 14. 62; Bh. 2. 99;<BR>Mv. 5. 56.<BR>--5 (a) Change of state;<BR>कष्टं बतान्यदिव दैववशेन जाता<BR>दुःखात्मकं किमपि भूतमहो विपाकः U. 4. 6.<BR>(b) An unexpected event or<BR>occurrence, a reverse, adverse turn of<BR>fate, distress, calamity; रिदृशानां<BR>विपाकोऽपि जायते परमाद्भुतः U. 3. 3;<BR>विपाके घोरेऽस्मिन्नथ खलु विमूढा तव<BR>सखी 4. 12.<BR>--6 Difficulty,<BR>embarrassment.<BR>--7 Flavour, taste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाठः|विपाठ
विपाठः A kind of large arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपांडु|विपाण्डु
विपांडु a. Pale, pallid; परितो<BR>विपांडु दधदभ्रशिरः Śi. 9. 3; Ki. 5. 6;<BR>so विपांडुर Śi. 4. 5; Ratn. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादनं|विपादन
विपादनं Destroying, killing,<BR>destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपादिका
विपादिका<BR>1 A sore or tumour<BR>on the foot.<BR>--2 An enigma, a riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाश्
विपाश्, विपाशा f. N. of one<BR>of the five rivers in the Panjab (now<BR>called Beas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपाशा
विपाश्, विपाशा f. N. of one<BR>of the five rivers in the Panjab (now<BR>called Beas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपिनं|विपिन
विपिनं [वप्-इनन् पृषो˚; cf.<BR>Uṇ. 2. 52] A wood, forest, grove, thicket;<BR>वृंदावनविपिने ललितं वितनोतु शुभानि<BR>यशंस्यं Gīt. 1; विपिनानि प्रकाशानि<BR>शक्तिमत्वाच्चकार सः R. 4. 31; Māl. 9. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुल|विपुलः
विपुल a.<BR>1 Large, extensive,<BR>capacious, broad, wide, spacious;<BR>विपुलं नितंबदेशे M. 3. 7; शिरसि<BR>तनुर्विपुलश्च मध्यदेशे Mk. 3. 22; कालो ह्ययं<BR>निरवधिर्विपुला च पृथ्वी Māl. 1. 6;<BR>so विपुलं पृष्ठं, विपुलः कुक्षिः &c.<BR>--2<BR>Much, ample, copious, abundant;<BR>Ki. 18. 14.<BR>--3 Deep, profound;<BR>Mv. 1. 2.<BR>--4 With the hair<BR>standing on end, thrilling; Śi. 16. 3 (where<BR>it has sense 1 also).<BR>--लः<BR>1 N. of<BR>the mountain Meru.<BR>--2 Of<BR>Himālaya.<BR>--3 A respectable man.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--छाय a. shady, umbrageous.<BR>--जघना a woman with large hips.<BR>--मति a. endowed with great talents<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">Page0982-b+ 55</a>]<BR>or understanding.<BR>--रसः the<BR>sugarcane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुला
विपुला The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपुष्ट
विपुष्ट a. Ill-fed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विपूयः|विपूय
विपूयः The Munja grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रः|विप्र
विप्रः [वप्-रन् पृषो ˚अत इत्वम्;<BR>Uṇ. 2. 28]<BR>1 A Brāhmaṇa; see the<BR>quotations under ब्राह्मण.<BR>--2 A sage, wise<BR>man.<BR>--3 The Aśvattha tree.<BR>--4 (In<BR>prosody) A foot of four short<BR>syllables.<BR>--5 A singer of hymns, praiser.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ऋषिः = ब्रह्मषिंः q. v.<BR>--काष्ठं<BR>the cotton-plant.<BR>--प्रियः the Palāśa<BR>tree.<BR>--समागमः a concourse or<BR>synod of Brāhmaṇas.<BR>--स्वं the<BR>property of a Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकीर्ण
विप्रकीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Spread about,<BR>dispersed, scattered.<BR>--2 Loose,<BR>dishevelled (as hair).<BR>--3 Expanded,<BR>outstretched.<BR>--4 Wide, broad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृ
विप्रकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 (a) To tease,<BR>trouble, harass, harm; किं सत्त्वानि<BR>विप्रकरोषि Ś. 7; (b) To oppress;<BR>तस्मिन् विप्रकृताः काले तारकेण दिवौकसः<BR>Ku. 2. 1.<BR>--2 To wrong, ill-treat,<BR>offend; Ś. 4. 17.<BR>--3 To affect, cause<BR>a change in; कमपरमवशं<BR>नविप्रकुर्युर्विभुमपि तं यदमी स्पृशंति भावाः Ku. 6. 95.<BR>--4 To disfigure, deform;<BR>आभरणोचितं रूपमाश्रमसुलभैः प्रसाधनैर्विप्रकार्यते<BR>Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकारः|विप्रकार
विप्रकारः<BR>1 Insult, contumely,<BR>abuse, treating with disrespect;<BR>Ki. 3. 55.<BR>--2 Injury, offence.<BR>--3<BR>Wickedness.<BR>--4 Opposition,<BR>counteraction.<BR>--5 Retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृत|विप्रकृतः
विप्रकृत p. p.<BR>1 Hurt, offended,<BR>injured.<BR>--2 Insulted, abused, treated<BR>with contumely.<BR>--3 Opposed.<BR>--4<BR>Retaliated, requited.<BR>--5 Oppressed,<BR>troubled, disturbed.<BR>--6 Irritated,<BR>provoked; विप्रकृतः पन्नगः फणां कुरुते<BR>Ś. 6. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृतिः|विप्रकृति
विप्रकृतिः f.<BR>1 Injury, offence.<BR>--2<BR>An insult, abuse, contumely.<BR>--3<BR>Retaliation, retort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्
विप्रकृष् {c1c} P. To draw away,<BR>remove, counteract; U. 5. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकर्षः|विप्रकर्ष
विप्रकर्षः Distance, remoteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्ट|विप्रकृष्टः
विप्रकृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Drawn away,<BR>removed.<BR>--2 Distant, remote.<BR>--3<BR>Protracted, lengthened, extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रकृष्टक|विप्रकृष्टकं
विप्रकृष्टक a. Remote, distant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रणश्
विप्रणश् See प्रणश्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिकारः|विप्रतिकार
विप्रतिकारः<BR>1 Counteraction,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">Page0982-c+ 56</a>]<BR>opposition, contradiction.<BR>--2<BR>Retaliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपद्
विप्रतिपद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To differ, be<BR>mutually opposed, conflict.<BR>--2 To<BR>waver, vacillate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपत्तिः|विप्रतिपत्ति
विप्रतिपत्तिः f.<BR>1 Mutual<BR>discrepancy, contest, conflict, dispute,<BR>opposition (as of opinions or<BR>interests).<BR>--2 Dissent, objection.<BR>--3<BR>Perplexity, confusion.<BR>--4 Mutual<BR>relation.<BR>--5 Conversancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिपन्न
विप्रतिपन्न p. p.<BR>1 Mutually<BR>opposed, opposite, dissentient.<BR>--2<BR>Confused, bewildered, perplexed.<BR>--3 Contested, disputed.<BR>--4<BR>Mutually connected or related.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिषेधः|विप्रतिषेध
विप्रतिषेधः<BR>1 Keeping under<BR>control, controlling; क्रव्याद्भ्य इव<BR>भूतानामदांतेभ्यः सदा भयम् । तेषां<BR>विप्रतिषेधार्थं राजा सृष्टः स्वयंभुवा Mb.<BR>--2 The<BR>opposition of two courses of action<BR>which are equally important, the<BR>conflict of two even-matched<BR>interests; हरिर्विप्रतिषेधं तमाच चक्षे<BR>विचक्षणः Śi. 2. 6 (तुल्यबलविरोधो विप्रतिषेधः<BR>Malli.).<BR>--3 (In gram.) The<BR>conflict of two different grammatical<BR>operations become possible<BR>according to two different rules, conflict<BR>of two equally important rules;<BR>विप्रतिषेधे परं कार्यं P. I. 4. 2; विरोधो<BR>विप्रतिषेधः । यत्र द्वौ<BR>प्रसंगावन्यार्थावेकस्मिन् प्राप्नुतः स विप्रतिषेधः Kāśikā.;<BR>See Mbh. also.<BR>--4 Prohibition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतिसारः|विप्रतिसार
विप्रति(ती)सारः<BR>1<BR>Repentance; Śi. 10. 20.<BR>--2 Anger, rage,<BR>wrath.<BR>--3 Wickedness, evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रतीसारः|विप्रतीसार
विप्रति(ती)सारः<BR>1<BR>Repentance; Śi. 10. 20.<BR>--2 Anger, rage,<BR>wrath.<BR>--3 Wickedness, evil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रदुष्ट
विप्रदुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Vitiated, spoiled,<BR>dissolute.<BR>--2 Corrupt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रनष्ट
विप्रनष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Lost.<BR>--2 Vain,<BR>useless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमुच्
विप्रमुच् See प्रमुच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रमुक्त
विप्रमुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Set free,<BR>liberated, loosened.<BR>--2 Shot,<BR>discharged.<BR>--3 Free from (in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयुज्
विप्रयुज् {c7c} A. To separate,<BR>disjoin; to deprive (one) of --Pass.<BR>To be separated from (with instr.).<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To deprive of, free from.<BR>--2 To separate, disjoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयुक्त|विप्रयुक्तः
विप्रयुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Separated,<BR>severed, detached.<BR>--2 Separated from,<BR>being absent or away from (with<BR>instr. or in comp.); अबलाविप्रयुक्तः<BR>स कामी Me. 2.<BR>--3 Freed or<BR>released from.<BR>--4 Deprived or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-a" target="_blank">Page0983-a+ 56</a>]<BR>destitute of, without (in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0982-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रयोगः|विप्रयोग
विप्रयोगः<BR>1 Disunion, severance,<BR>separation, dissociation; as प्रिय˚.<BR>--2 Especially, separation of lovers;<BR>मा भूदेवं क्षणमपि च ते विद्युता विप्रयोगः<BR>Me. 115, 10; सद्यस्त्वया सह कृशोदरि<BR>विप्रयोगः V. 5. 16; R. 13. 26,<BR>14. 66.<BR>--3 Quarrel, disagreement.<BR>--4<BR>Being fit or deserved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलप्
विप्रलप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To dispute,<BR>contradict, wrangle, quarrel.<BR>--2 To<BR>discuss, debate.<BR>--3 To lament,<BR>bewail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलप्तं|विप्रलप्त
विप्रलप्तं<BR>1 Discussion, debate,<BR>controversy.<BR>--2 Bewailing,<BR>lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलापः|विप्रलाप
विप्रलापः<BR>1 Idle or unmeaning talk,<BR>prattle, gibberish, nonsense.<BR>--2<BR>Mutual contradiction,<BR>contradictory statement.<BR>--3 A dispute,<BR>wrangling.<BR>--4 Violation of one's<BR>promise, breaking one's word.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलभ्
विप्रलभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To cheat,<BR>deceive, impose upon.<BR>--2 To recover,<BR>regain.<BR>--3 To insult, disrespect.<BR>--4<BR>To violate, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलब्ध|विप्रलब्धः
विप्रलब्ध p. p.<BR>1 Deceived, cheated.<BR>--2 Disappointed.<BR>--3 Hurt, injured.<BR>--ब्धा A woman disappointed by<BR>her lover's breaking his<BR>appointment; (one of the several classes<BR>of a Nāyikā in poetic<BR>composition); she is thus defined in<BR>S. D. : --प्रियः कृत्वापि संकेतं यस्या नायाति<BR>संनिधिम् । विप्रलब्धेति सा ज्ञेया<BR>नितांतमवमानिता ॥ 118.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलंभः|विप्रलम्भ|विप्रलंभ|विप्रलम्भः
विप्रलंभः<BR>1 (a) Deceiving, deceit,<BR>tricking; Ki. 11. 27. (b)<BR>Delusion; अतिक्लामिता खलु प्रियसखी<BR>अनेनानुकूलविप्रलंभेन Māl. 6.<BR>--2<BR>Especially, deceiving by false<BR>statement or by not keeping<BR>promises.<BR>--3 Quarrel, disagreement.<BR>--4 Disunion, separation,<BR>disjunction.<BR>--5 The separation of lovers;<BR>शुश्रुवे प्रियजनस्य कातरं<BR>विप्रलंभपरिशंकिनो वचः R. 19. 18; Ve. 2. 12.<BR>--6 (In Rhet.) The feeling or<BR>sentiment of love in separation, one of<BR>the two main kinds of शृंगार (opp.<BR>संभोग); अपरः (विप्रलंभः)<BR>अभिलाषविरहेर्ष्याप्रवासशापहेतुक इति पंचविधः<BR>K. P. 4; यूनोरयुक्तयोर्भावो युक्तयोर्वाथवा मिथः ।<BR>अभीष्टालिंगनादीनामनवाप्तौ प्रहृष्यते । विप्रलंभः<BR>स विज्ञेयः -उज्ज्वलमणिः; cf.<BR>S. D. 212 et seq.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलंभनं|विप्रलम्भन
विप्रलंभनं Deception, fraud, trick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलयः|विप्रलय
विप्रलयः Complete destruction<BR>or dissolution, annihilation;<BR>विद्याकल्पेन मरुता मेघानां भूयसामपि ।<BR>ब्रह्मणीव विवर्तानां क्वापि विप्रलयः कृतः<BR>U. 6. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रलुप्त
विप्रलुप्त p. p.<BR>1 Carried away,<BR>snatched away.<BR>--2 Disturbed,<BR>interrupted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवस्
विप्रवस् {c1c} P. To sojourn, be<BR>absent from (one's home);<BR>R. 12. 11. --Caus.<BR>1 To banish, expel.<BR>--2<BR>To remove, take away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवासः|विप्रवास
विप्रवासः Staying abroad,<BR>dwelling in a foreign country (away<BR>from one's home).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रवासनं|विप्रवासन
विप्रवासनं<BR>1 Banishment.<BR>--2<BR>Staying abroad, sojourn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रोषित|विप्रोषितः
विप्रोषित p. p.<BR>1 Staying abroad,<BR>away from, absent.<BR>--2 Banished,<BR>being in exile.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भर्तृका a<BR>woman whose husband is absent<BR>from home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रश्निका
विप्रश्निका A female<BR>fortune-teller; Ak. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रहीण
विप्रहीण a. Deprived or<BR>destitute of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रिय|विप्रियः
विप्रिय a. Disagreeable,<BR>disliked, unpleasant, distasteful.<BR>--यं;<BR>Offence, wrong, a disagreeable act;<BR>मनसापि न विप्रियं मया कृतपूर्वं तव किं<BR>जहासि मां R. 8. 52, Ku. 4. 7;<BR>Ki. 9. 39; Śi. 15. 11; U. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्रुष्
विप्रुष् f.<BR>1 A drop (of water or<BR>any other liquid); संतापं<BR>नवजलविप्रुषो गृहीत्वा Śi. 8. 40; स्वेदविप्रुषः 2. 18.<BR>--2 A mark, dot, spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लु
विप्लु {c1c} A.<BR>1 To float about, swing<BR>to and fro, fluctuate.<BR>--2 To drift (in<BR>the sea), be scattered; यदि न<BR>स्यान्नरपतिः सम्यङ् नेता ततः प्रजा । अकर्णधारा<BR>जलधौ विप्लवेतेह नैरिव H. 3. 2,<BR>Pt. 3. 73.<BR>--3 To be confused (as mind).<BR>--4 To be ruined or destroyed.<BR>--5<BR>To fail. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to float<BR>or swim.<BR>--2 To divulge, spread<BR>abroad.<BR>--3 To teach (to unworthy<BR>persons); Ms. 11. 199.<BR>--4 To cause<BR>to fail, spoil, mar;<BR>गुणानामायथातर्थ्यादर्थं विप्लावयंति ये Śi. 2. 56.<BR>--5 To<BR>confound, bewilder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लवः|विप्लव
विप्लवः<BR>1 Floating or drifting<BR>about, floating in different directions.<BR>--2 Opposition, contrariety.<BR>--3<BR>Confusion, perplexity.<BR>--4 Tumult, scuffle,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">Page0983-c+ 55</a>]<BR>affray; M. 1.<BR>--5 Devastation,<BR>predatory warfare; danger from an<BR>enemy.<BR>--6 Extortion.<BR>--7 Loss,<BR>destruction; सत्त्वविप्लवात् R. 8. 41.<BR>--8<BR>Adverseness, evil turn; अथवा मम<BR>भाग्यविप्लवात् R. 8. 47.<BR>--9 The rust<BR>on a mirror (dust accumulating on<BR>its surface); अपवर्जितविप्लवे शुचौ…<BR>मतिरादर्श इवाभिदृश्यते Ki. 2. 26 (where<BR>विप्लव also means प्रमाणबाधः ‘absence of<BR>reasoning’).<BR>--10 Transgression,<BR>violation; Ki. 1. 13.<BR>--11 An evil, a<BR>calamity.<BR>--12 Sin, wickedness,<BR>sinfulness.<BR>--13 Terrifying an enemy by<BR>shouts and gestures.<BR>--14 Divulging,<BR>making public.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लावः|विप्लाव
विप्लावः<BR>1 Deluging, inundating.<BR>--2<BR>Causing tumult.<BR>--3 A horse's canter<BR>or gallop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुत|विप्लुतः
विप्लुत p. p.<BR>1 Drifted about.<BR>--2<BR>Drowned, submerged, deluged,<BR>overflowed.<BR>--3 Confounded, disturbed.<BR>--4 Ravaged, devastated.<BR>--5 Lost,<BR>disappeared.<BR>--6 Disgraced,<BR>dishonoured.<BR>--7 Ruined.<BR>--8 Obscured,<BR>disfigured.<BR>--9 Depraved, dissolute,<BR>profligate, guilty of lewdness.<BR>--10<BR>Contrary, reverse.<BR>--11 Turning out<BR>false; नैते वाचं विप्लुतां व्याहरंति U. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्लुष्
विप्लुष् See विप्रुष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विप्सा
विप्सा See वीप्सा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफल|विफलं
विफल a.<BR>1 Fruitless, useless<BR>vain, ineffectual, unprofitable; मम<BR>विफलमेतदनुरूपमपि यौवनं Gīt. 7;<BR>जगता वा विफलेन किं फलं R. G.;<BR>Śi. 9. 6; Ku. 7. 66; Me. 68.<BR>--2 Idle,<BR>unmeaning.<BR>--ला N. of a plant (<BR>केतकी).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीकृ
विफलीकृ {c8c} U. To frustrate, defeat,<BR>foil, render fruitless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विफलीभू
विफलीभू {c1c} P. To become useless<BR>or unprofitable, be foiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबंध्|विबन्ध्
विबंध् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To bind or fasten<BR>(on different sides).<BR>--2 To stretch<BR>out, extend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबद्ध
विबद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Fastened, tied.<BR>--2<BR>Obstructed, stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबंधः|विबन्ध|विबंध|विबन्धः
विबंधः<BR>1 Constipation.<BR>--2<BR>Obstruetion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबाध्
विबाध् See बाध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबाधा
विबाधा Pain, anguish, torment,<BR>agony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुध्
विबुध् {c1c} P., {c4c} A.<BR>1 To wake up,<BR>awake; निमील्य नेत्रे सहसा व्यबुध्यत<BR>Ku. 5. 57.<BR>--2 To become conscious.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-a" target="_blank">Page0984-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--3 To observe, perceive; find out.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To awaken, rouse.<BR>--2 To<BR>restore to consciousness; अथ<BR>मोहपरायणा सती विवशा कामपधूर्विबोधिता<BR>Ku. 4. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0983-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुद्ध
विबुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Aroused, awakened,<BR>wide awake; Ś. 2.<BR>--2 Expanded,<BR>blossomed, full-blown.<BR>--3 Clever,<BR>skilful.<BR>--4 Unconscious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधः|विबुध
विबुधः<BR>1 A wise or learned man,<BR>sage; सख्यं साप्तपदीनं भो इत्याहुर्विबुधा<BR>जनाः Pt. 2. 43.<BR>--2 A god, deity;<BR>अभून्नृपो विबुधसखः परंतपः Bk. 1. 1;<BR>गोप्तारं न निधीनां महयंति महेश्वरं विबुधाः<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--3 The moon.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपतिः, --इंद्रः, --ईश्वरः epithets of<BR>Indra.<BR>--द्विष्, --शत्रुः a demon; V. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबुधानः|विबुधान
विबुधानः<BR>1 A learned man.<BR>--2 A<BR>teacher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विबोधः|विबोध
विबोधः<BR>1 Awakening, being<BR>awake.<BR>--2 Perceiving, discovering.<BR>--3 Intelligence.<BR>--4 Awaking,<BR>becoming conscious, one of the 33 or<BR>34 subordinate feelings (or<BR>व्यभिचारिभाव) in Rhetoric; निद्रानाशोत्तरं<BR>जायमानो बोधो विबोधः R. G.<BR>--5<BR>Inattention, absence of mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विब्बोकः|विब्बोक
विब्बोकः^1 See बिब्बोकः.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: Also bibbokaH; since bibbokaH is an entry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विब्रू
विब्रू^1 {c2c} U.<BR>1 To say, speak.<BR>--2<BR>To speak of or about.<BR>--3 To speak<BR>falsely or wrongly.<BR>--4 To explain,<BR>expound, interpret.<BR>--5 To quarrel,<BR>dispute, contend about.<BR>--6 To<BR>disagree with, contradict.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: print missing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभज्
विभज् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To divide,<BR>distribute; विभज्य मेरुर्न यदर्थिसात्कृतः<BR>N. 1. 16; पत्रिणां व्यभजदाश्रमाद्बहिः<BR>R. 11. 29; 10. 54; वपुर्विभक्तावयवं<BR>पुमानिति Śi. 1. 3; संध्यामंगलदीपिका<BR>विभजते शुद्धांतवृद्धो जनः V. 3. 2.<BR>‘distributes or places’.<BR>--2 To divide<BR>(as property, patrimony &c.);<BR>विभक्ता भ्रातरः ‘divided brothers’.<BR>--3 To<BR>distinguish, discriminate.<BR>--4 To<BR>honour, worship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्त|विभक्तः
विभक्त p. p.<BR>1 Divided,<BR>partitioned (as property &c.).<BR>--2 Divided,<BR>separated in interest, as in विभक्ता<BR>भ्रातरः<BR>--3 Parted, separated, made<BR>distinct; Śi. 1. 3.<BR>--4 Different,<BR>multifarious.<BR>--5 Retired, secluded.<BR>--6 Regular, symmetrical.<BR>--7<BR>Ornamented.<BR>--8 Measured.<BR>--क्तः N. of<BR>Kārtikeya.<BR>--क्तं<BR>1 Solitude,<BR>retirement.<BR>--2 A share.<BR>--3 Property<BR>(divided).<BR>--4 Separation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">Page0984-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--जः a son born after partition of<BR>the family-property (between his<BR>parents and brothers).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभक्तिः|विभक्ति
विभक्तिः f.<BR>1 Separation, division,<BR>partition, apportionment.<BR>--2<BR>Division, separation in interest.<BR>--3 A<BR>portion or share of inheritance.<BR>--4<BR>(In gram.) Inflection of nouns, a<BR>case or case-termination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभंज्|विभञ्ज्
विभंज् {c7c} P. To break asunder,<BR>break to pieces, shatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभंगः|विभङ्ग|विभंग|विभङ्गः
विभंगः<BR>1 Breaking, fracture.<BR>--2<BR>Stopping, obstruction, stoppage;<BR>Bg. 2. 26.<BR>--3 Bending,<BR>contraction (as of the eyebrows);<BR>भ्रूविभंगकुटिलं च वीक्षितं R. 19. 17.<BR>--4 A<BR>fold, wrinkle.<BR>--5 A step, stair;<BR>R. 6. 3.<BR>--6 Breaking out,<BR>manifestation; विविधविकारविभंगं Gīt. 11.<BR>--7<BR>Division.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभवः|विभव
विभवः<BR>1 Wealth, riches,<BR>property; अतनुषु विभवेषु ज्ञातयः संतु नाम<BR>Ś. 5. 8; R. 8. 69.<BR>--2 Might,<BR>power, prowess, greatness;<BR>एतावान्मम मतिविभवः V. 2; वाग्विभवः<BR>Māl. 1. 26, R. 1. 9; Ki. 5. 21.<BR>--3<BR>Exalted position, rank, dignity.<BR>--4<BR>Magnanimity.<BR>--5 Final beatitude,<BR>absolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभा
विभा {c2c} P.<BR>1 To shine; पयसा<BR>कमलेन विभाति सरः; Bh. 2. 71.<BR>--2<BR>To seem, appear.<BR>--3 To become<BR>visible, come to light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभा
विभा<BR>1 Light, lustre.<BR>--2 A ray of<BR>light.<BR>--3 Beauty; splendour.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः {1} the sun; बत बत<BR>लसत्तेजःपुंजो विभाति विभाकरः K. P. 10. {2}<BR>the arka plant. {3} the moon. {4}<BR>fire.<BR>--वसुः {1} the sun. {2} fire;<BR>रचयिष्यामि तनुं विभावसौ Ku. 4. 34;<BR>R. 3. 37, 10. 82; Bg. 7. 9. {3} the<BR>moon. {4} a kind of necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभातं|विभात
विभातं --ती Day-break, dawn;<BR>Ś. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाती
विभातं --ती Day-break, dawn;<BR>Ś. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागः|विभाग
विभागः<BR>1 Division, partition,<BR>apportionment (as of inheritance);<BR>समस्तत्र विभागः स्यात् Ms. 9. 120,<BR>210; Y. 2. 114.<BR>--2 The share of<BR>an inheritance.<BR>--3 A part or share<BR>in general<BR>--4 Division, separation,<BR>disjunction (regarded in Nyāya<BR>phil. as a Guṇa); Ku. 2. 4;<BR>Bg. 3. 28.<BR>--5 The numerator of a<BR>fraction.<BR>--6 A section.<BR>--7 Arrangement.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कल्पना allotment of<BR>shares; Y. 2. 149.<BR>--धर्मः the law<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">Page0984-c+ 56</a>]<BR>of inheritance.<BR>--पत्रिका a deed of<BR>partition.<BR>--भाज् m. one who shares<BR>in a property already distributed;<BR>Y. 1. 122.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागतः
विभागतः ind. Proportionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभागशः
विभागशः ind. Part by part, share<BR>by share, proportionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाजनं|विभाजन
विभाजनं Dividing, distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाज्य|विभाज्यं
विभाज्य a.<BR>1 Portionable, to be<BR>divided.<BR>--2 Divisible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावरी
विभावरी<BR>1 Night; अपर्वाणि<BR>ग्रहकलुषेंदुमंडला विभावरी कथय कथं भविष्यति<BR>M. 4. 15, 5. 7; Ku. 5. 44.<BR>--2<BR>Turmeric.<BR>--3 A bawd.<BR>--4 A harlot.<BR>--5 A perverse woman.<BR>--6 A<BR>talkative woman (मुखरस्त्री).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाष्
विभाष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To lay down as<BR>an optional rule.<BR>--2 To abuse, revile,<BR>defame, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभाषा
विभाषा<BR>1 An option, alternative.<BR>--2 Optionality of a rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभासा
विभासा Light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिद्
विभिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To break, tear<BR>down.<BR>--2 To pierce, penetrate.<BR>--3<BR>To divide, separate.<BR>--4 To<BR>interrupt.<BR>--5 To scatter, unbind,<BR>disperse.<BR>--6 To loosen, untie.<BR>--7 To alienate, estrange. --Pass.<BR>To change, become changed.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To divide, separate.<BR>--2<BR>To alienate, estrange.<BR>--3 To<BR>dispel, remove, drive away or off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभिन्न|विभिन्नः
विभिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Broken asunder,<BR>divided, split.<BR>--2 Pierced,<BR>wounded.<BR>--3 Dispelled, driven away,<BR>dispersed.<BR>--4 Perplexed, bewildered.<BR>--5 Moved to and fro.<BR>--6<BR>Disappointed.<BR>--7 Different, various.<BR>--8<BR>Mixed, blended, variegated;<BR>विभिन्नवर्णा गरुडाग्रजेन सूर्यस्य रथ्याः परितः<BR>स्फुरंत्या Śi. 4. 14.<BR>--9 Manifested,<BR>displayed.<BR>--10 Become faithless.<BR>--न्नः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभेदः|विभेद
विभेदः<BR>1 Breaking asunder,<BR>dividing.<BR>--2 Division, separation.<BR>--3<BR>Wounding.<BR>--4 Perplexing,<BR>bewildering.<BR>--5 Contradiction.<BR>--6<BR>Enmity, opposition.<BR>--7 Variety,<BR>distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतः|विभीत|विभीतं
विभीतः, -तं, विभीतकः -कं,<BR>विभीतकी, विभीता N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR>Belerica, one of the three<BR>myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतं|विभीत|विभीतः
विभीतः, -तं, विभीतकः -कं,<BR>विभीतकी, विभीता N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR>Belerica, one of the three<BR>myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतकः|विभीतक|विभीतकं
विभीतः, -तं, विभीतकः -कं,<BR>विभीतकी, विभीता N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR>Belerica, one of the three<BR>myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतकं|विभीतक|विभीतकः
विभीतः, -तं, विभीतकः -कं,<BR>विभीतकी, विभीता N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR>Belerica, one of the three<BR>myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीतकी
विभीतः, -तं, विभीतकः -कं,<BR>विभीतकी, विभीता N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR>Belerica, one of the three<BR>myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीता
विभीतः, -तं, विभीतकः -कं,<BR>विभीतकी, विभीता N. of a tree, Terminalia<BR>Belerica, one of the three<BR>myrobalans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषक
विभीषक a. Frightening,<BR>terrifying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभीषिका
विभीषिका<BR>1 Terror.<BR>--2 A means<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-a" target="_blank">Page0985-a+ 57</a>]<BR>of terrifying, a scare (a scare-crow);<BR>यदि ते संति संत्वेव केयमन्या विभीषिका<BR>U. 4. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0984-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभु|विभुः
विभु a. (भू-भ्वी f.)<BR>1 Mighty,<BR>powerful.<BR>--2 Eminent, supreme.<BR>--3 Able to, capable of (with inf.);<BR>(धनुः) पूरयितुं भवंति विभवः<BR>शिखरमणिउचः Ki. 5. 43.<BR>--4 Self-subdued,<BR>firm, self-controlled; कमपरमवशं न<BR>विप्रकुर्यर्विभुमपि तं यदमी स्पृशति भावाः<BR>Ku. 6. 95.<BR>--5 (In Nyāya phil.)<BR>Eternal, existing everywhere,<BR>all-pervading, pervading all material<BR>things; सर्वमूर्तद्रव्यसंयोगित्वं विभुत्वम्.<BR>--6 Firm, hard.<BR>--भुः<BR>1 Ether.<BR>--2<BR>Space.<BR>--3 Time.<BR>--4 The soul.<BR>--5<BR>A lord, ruler, master, sovereign,<BR>king.<BR>--6 The supreme ruler;<BR>Bg. 5. 15; 10. 12.<BR>--7 A servant.<BR>--8 N. of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--9 Of Śiva; Ku. 6. 95;<BR>7. 31; Mu. 1. 1.<BR>--10 Of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभू
विभू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To appear, become<BR>manifest.<BR>--2 To be equal to, suffice<BR>for.<BR>--3 To pervade.<BR>--4 To be able,<BR>be capable of, prevail. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To think of, reflect, contemplate.<BR>--2 To be aware of, know, perceive,<BR>discover, see; Māl. 1. 18; 5. 21;<BR>Pt. 5. 7; U. 2. 24.<BR>--3 To see or<BR>observe minutely, perceive carefully;<BR>V. 4.<BR>--4 To decide, settle, make<BR>clear.<BR>--5 To manifest, show,<BR>reveal.<BR>--6 To separate.<BR>--7 To<BR>suppose, imagine.<BR>--8 To convince.<BR>--9<BR>To establish, prove; Ś. 6. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावः|विभाव
विभावः<BR>1 (In Rhet.) Any<BR>condition which produces or<BR>develops a particular state of<BR>body or mind; (one of the three<BR>main divisions of Bhāvas, the other<BR>two being अनुभाव and ब्याभिचारिभाव<BR>q. v.); रत्याद्युद्वोधका लोके विभावाः<BR>काव्यनाट्ययोः S. D. 62; its chief<BR>subdivisions are आलंबन and उद्दीपक;<BR>see आलंबन.<BR>--2 A friend, an<BR>acquaintance.<BR>--3 Any exciting<BR>circumtance, (as dress &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावक
विभावक a.<BR>1 Manifesting,<BR>showing.<BR>--2 Discussing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावनं|विभावन
विभावनं --ना<BR>1 Clear perception or<BR>ascertainment, discrimination,<BR>judgment.<BR>--2 Discussion, investigation,<BR>examination.<BR>--3 Conception,<BR>imagination.<BR>--ना (In Rhet.) A<BR>figure of speech in which effects are<BR>represented as taking place though<BR>their usual causes are absent;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">Page0985-b+ 56</a>]<BR>क्रियायाः प्रतिषेधेपि फलव्यक्तिर्विभावना<BR>K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावना
विभावनं --ना<BR>1 Clear perception or<BR>ascertainment, discrimination,<BR>judgment.<BR>--2 Discussion, investigation,<BR>examination.<BR>--3 Conception,<BR>imagination.<BR>--ना (In Rhet.) A<BR>figure of speech in which effects are<BR>represented as taking place though<BR>their usual causes are absent;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">Page0985-b+ 56</a>]<BR>क्रियायाः प्रतिषेधेपि फलव्यक्तिर्विभावना<BR>K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभावित|विभावितः
विभावित p. p.<BR>1 Manifested,<BR>made clearly visible.<BR>--2 Known,<BR>understood, ascertained.<BR>--3 Seen,<BR>conceived.<BR>--4 Judged,<BR>discriminated.<BR>--5 Inferred, indicated.<BR>--6<BR>Proved, established.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--एकदेश a. ‘with whom a part has been<BR>discovered’, who has been found<BR>guilty with regard to a part (of<BR>what is in dispute); विभावितैकदशेने<BR>देयं यदभियुज्यते V. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूत
विभूत p. p.<BR>1 Arisen, produced.<BR>--2<BR>Appeared, manifested.<BR>--3 Great,<BR>mighty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूतिः|विभूति
विभूतिः f.<BR>1 Mighty, power,<BR>greatness; Śi. 14. 5; Ku. 2. 61.<BR>--2<BR>Prosperity, welfare.<BR>--3 Dignity,<BR>exalted rank.<BR>--4 Riches, plenty,<BR>magnificence, splendour; अहो<BR>राजाधिराजमंत्रिणो विभूतिः Mu. 3;<BR>R. 8. 36.<BR>--5 Wealth, riches; R. 4. 19,<BR>6. 76, 17. 43.<BR>--6 Superhuman power<BR>(which consists of eight faculties,<BR>अणिमन्, लघिमन्, प्राप्ति, प्राकाम्य, महिमन्,<BR>रिशिता, वशिता and कामावसायिता);<BR>Ku. 2. 11.<BR>--7 Ashes of cow-dung.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूष्
विभूष् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To adorn,<BR>decorate; केयूरा न विभूषयंति पुरुषं<BR>Bh. 2. 19; Śi. 9. 33; Ku. 1. 28.<BR>--2<BR>Ved. To shine forth, appear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषणं|विभूषण
विभूषणं Ornament, decoration;<BR>विशेषतः सर्वविदां समाजे विभूषणं<BR>मौनमपंडितानां Bh. 2. 7; R. 16. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषा
विभूषा<BR>1 Ornament, decoration;<BR>संपेदे श्रमसालिलोद्गमो विभूषा Ki. 7. 5,<BR>R. 4. 54.<BR>--2 Light, lustre.<BR>--3 Beauty,<BR>splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभूषित|विभूषितः
विभूषित p. p. Adorned, decorated,<BR>ornamented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभृत|विभृतः
विभृत p. p. Upheld, supported,<BR>maintained.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंश्
विभ्रंश् {c1c} A., {c4c} P.<BR>1 To drop or<BR>fall down.<BR>--2 To go to ruin, decay.<BR>--3 To fall stray from, go astray.<BR>--4 To lose.<BR>--5 To disappear,<BR>vanish.<BR>--6 To fail. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>strike off, knock down.<BR>--2 To lead<BR>astray, seduce.<BR>--3 To destroy, ruin,<BR>annihilate.<BR>--4 To deprive (one) of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंशः|विभ्रंश
विभ्रंशः<BR>1 Falling away or off.<BR>--2<BR>Decay, decline, ruin.<BR>--3 A precipice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रंशित
विभ्रंशित p. p.<BR>1 Led astray, seduced.<BR>--2 Deprived of.<BR>--3 Destroyed;<BR>ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रष्ट
विभ्रष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Fallen off or away,<BR>separated.<BR>--2 Decayed, lost, fallen.<BR>ruined.<BR>--3 Disappeared. vanished.<BR>--4 Deprived or devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रम्
विभ्रम् {c1c} {c4c} P.<BR>1 To roam,<BR>wander about.<BR>--2 To hover, whirl or<BR>wheel round.<BR>--3 To scare away,<BR>disperse, scatter about.<BR>--4 To be<BR>confused or disordered, be<BR>bewildered or perplexed; Bg. 16. 16.<BR>--Caus. To confuse, confound;<BR>प्रभामत्तश्चंद्रो जगादिदमहो विभ्रमयति<BR>K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रमः|विभ्रम
विभ्रमः<BR>1 Roaming or wandering<BR>about.<BR>--2 Whirling or going round,<BR>rolling about.<BR>--3 Error, mistake,<BR>blunder.<BR>--4 Hurry, confusion,<BR>flurry, perturbation; especially, the<BR>flurry of mind caused by love;<BR>चित्तवृत्त्यनवस्थानं शृंगाराद्बिभ्रमो भवेत्.<BR>--5<BR>(Hence) Putting on of ornaments<BR>&c. in wrong places through flurry;<BR>विभ्रमस्त्वरयाऽकाले भूषास्थानाविपर्ययः;<BR>यश्चाप्सरोविभ्रममंडनानां संपादयित्रीं<BR>शिखरैर्बिभर्त्ति Ku. 1. 4. (see Malli.<BR>thereon).<BR>--6 Any amorous or<BR>sportive action, amorous play or<BR>movement; Māl. 1. 26, 9. 38.<BR>--7 Beauty,<BR>grace, charm; N. 15. 25, U. 1. 20,<BR>34, 6. 4; Śi. 6. 46, 7. 15, 16. 64,<BR>Māl. 7.<BR>--8 Doubt, apprehension.<BR>--9<BR>Caprice, whim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रमा
विभ्रमा Old age.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रांत|विभ्रान्त|विभ्रान्तः
विभ्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Whirled about.<BR>--2<BR>Agitated, bewildered, confused,<BR>flurried.<BR>--3 Mistaken, erring.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नयन a. with rolling eyes.<BR>--शील<BR>a. {1} confused in mind. {2}<BR>intoxicated, drunk.<BR>--(लः) {1} a monkey.<BR>{2} the disc of the sun or moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्रांतिः|विभ्रान्ति|विभ्रांति|विभ्रान्तिः
विभ्रांतिः f.<BR>1 Whirling, going<BR>round.<BR>--2 Flurry, error, confusion.<BR>--3 Hurry, precipitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राज्
विभ्राज् {c1c} A. To shine<BR>brilliantly or intensely; विभ्राजसे<BR>मकरकेतनमर्चयंती Ratn. 1. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विभ्राज्
विभ्राज् a. Shining, splendid, bright,<BR>luminous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत्सर
विमत्सर a. Free from jealousy,<BR>unenvious; Bg. 4. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमथ्
विम(मं)थ् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To<BR>disperse, scatter.<BR>--2 To destroy,<BR>annihilate.<BR>--3 To confound,<BR>confuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमंथ्|विमन्थ्
विम(मं)थ् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To<BR>disperse, scatter.<BR>--2 To destroy,<BR>annihilate.<BR>--3 To confound,<BR>confuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमाथः|विमाथ
विमाथः Utter ruin or destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमद्
विमद् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To become<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">Page0986-a+ 57</a>]<BR>perplexed or confused.<BR>--2 To be<BR>intoxicated or mad. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>confound, perplex.<BR>--2 To intoxicate,<BR>madden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0985-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत्त
विमत्त p. p.<BR>1 Intoxicated.<BR>--2<BR>Ruttish; furious, in rut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमद
विमद a.<BR>1 Free from intoxication;<BR>Pt. 1. 238.<BR>--2 Devoid of joy, sad,<BR>cheerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमन्
विमन् Caus. To disrespect,<BR>dishonour, insult; त्वया नाम मुनिर्विमान्यः<BR>Ś. 5. 20; स्त्रीभिर्विमानितानां कापुरुषाणां<BR>विवधते मदनः Mk. 8. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमत|विमतः
विमत p. p.<BR>1 Disagreeing,<BR>dissenting, differing in opinion.<BR>--2<BR>At variance, inconsistent.<BR>--3<BR>Slighted, despised, neglected.<BR>--4<BR>Dubious, doubtful.<BR>--तः An<BR>enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमति|विमतिः
विमति a. Stupid, devoid of<BR>intelligence, foolish.<BR>--तिः f.<BR>1<BR>Dissent, disagreement, difference<BR>of opinion.<BR>--2 Dislike.<BR>--3<BR>Stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानः|विमान|विमानं
विमानः --नं<BR>1 Disrespect, dishonour.<BR>--2 A measure.<BR>--3 A balloon, a<BR>heavenly car (moving through the<BR>skies); पदं विमानेन विगाहमानः<BR>R. 13. 1, 7. 51; विमानीकृतराजहंसमंडलः<BR>K.; R. 12. 104; Ku. 2. 45, 7. 40;<BR>V. 4. 43; Ki. 7. 11.<BR>--4 A vehicle or<BR>conveyance in general; R. 16. 68.<BR>--5 A palace (with seven stories);<BR>नेत्रा नीताः सततगतिना यद्विमानाग्रभूमीः<BR>Me. 69.<BR>--6 A horse.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चारिन्, --यान a. moving in a balloon.<BR>--राजः {1} an excellent heavenly<BR>car; U. 3. {2} the driver of a<BR>heavenly car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानं|विमान|विमानः
विमानः --नं<BR>1 Disrespect, dishonour.<BR>--2 A measure.<BR>--3 A balloon, a<BR>heavenly car (moving through the<BR>skies); पदं विमानेन विगाहमानः<BR>R. 13. 1, 7. 51; विमानीकृतराजहंसमंडलः<BR>K.; R. 12. 104; Ku. 2. 45, 7. 40;<BR>V. 4. 43; Ki. 7. 11.<BR>--4 A vehicle or<BR>conveyance in general; R. 16. 68.<BR>--5 A palace (with seven stories);<BR>नेत्रा नीताः सततगतिना यद्विमानाग्रभूमीः<BR>Me. 69.<BR>--6 A horse.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चारिन्, --यान a. moving in a balloon.<BR>--राजः {1} an excellent heavenly<BR>car; U. 3. {2} the driver of a<BR>heavenly car.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानना
विमानना Disrespect, dishonour,<BR>contempt, humiliation;<BR>विमानना सुभ्रु कुतः पितुर्गृहे Ku. 5. 43;<BR>अभवन्नास्य विमानना क्वचित् R. 8. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमानित
विमानित p. p. Disrespected,<BR>dishonoured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्
विमनस्, --विमनस्क a.<BR>1 Sad,<BR>disconsolate, depressed in mind or<BR>spirits, sorry, discomposed;<BR>U. 1. 7.<BR>--2 Absent-minded.<BR>--3<BR>Perplexed, bewildered.<BR>--4 Displeased.<BR>--5 Changed in mind or feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनस्क|विमनस्कः
विमनस्, --विमनस्क a.<BR>1 Sad,<BR>disconsolate, depressed in mind or<BR>spirits, sorry, discomposed;<BR>U. 1. 7.<BR>--2 Absent-minded.<BR>--3<BR>Perplexed, bewildered.<BR>--4 Displeased.<BR>--5 Changed in mind or feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमनीकृत
विमनीकृत a.<BR>1 Displeased.<BR>--2<BR>Changed in mind or feeling.<BR>--3 Sad,<BR>discomposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमन्यु
विमन्यु a.<BR>1 Free from anger.<BR>--2<BR>Free from grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमयः|विमय
विमयः Exchange, barter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्षः|विमर्ष
विमर्षः<BR>1 Thought, deliberation.<BR>--2 Impatience, non-forbearance.<BR>--3<BR>Dissatisfaction, displeasure.<BR>--4 (In<BR>dramas) A change in the successful<BR>progress of a dramatic plot, a<BR>change in the prosperous course of<BR>a love-story caused by some<BR>unforeseen reverse or accident, one of<BR>the five Saṃdhis in a drama; it is<BR>thus defined in S. D.; यत्र<BR>मुख्यफलोपाय उद्भिन्नो गर्भतोऽधिकः । शापाद्यैः<BR>सांतरायश्च स विमर्ष इति स्मृतः 336;<BR>see Mu. 4. 3; (often written विमर्श<BR>in all these senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमल|विमलं|विमलः
विमल a.<BR>1 Pure, stainless,<BR>spotless, clean (fig. also).<BR>--2 Clear,<BR>limpid, pellucid, transparent (as<BR>water); विमलं जलं.<BR>--3 White,<BR>bright.<BR>--लः An Arhat.<BR>--लं<BR>1<BR>Silver-gilt.<BR>--2 Talc.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद्रिः<BR>the mountain Girnār in Gujerāt<BR>(famous for its inscriptions).<BR>--दानं an offering to a deity.<BR>--मणिः<BR>a crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमांसः|विमांस|विमांसं
विमांसः --सं Unclean meat (as<BR>of dogs),<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमांसं|विमांस|विमांसः
विमांसः --सं Unclean meat (as<BR>of dogs),<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमातृ
विमातृ f. A step-mother.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः a step-mother's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गः|विमार्ग
विमार्गः<BR>1 A bad road.<BR>--2 A<BR>wrong road, evil conduct or course,<BR>immorality.<BR>--3 A broom.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गा an unchaste woman;<BR>विमार्गगायाश्च रुचिः स्वकाते Bv. 1. 125.<BR>--गामिन्, --प्रस्थित a. following evil courses;<BR>नियमयसिविमार्गप्रस्थितानात्तदंडः Ś. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमार्गणं|विमार्गण
विमार्गणं Searching, looking out<BR>for, seeking for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिश्र
विमिश्र, विमिश्रित a. Mixed,<BR>blended, mingled (with instr. or<BR>in comp.); पुंभिर्विमिश्रा नार्यश्च Mb.;<BR>दंपत्योरिह को न को न तमसि<BR>व्रीडाविमिश्रो रसः Gīt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमिश्रित
विमिश्र, विमिश्रित a. Mixed,<BR>blended, mingled (with instr. or<BR>in comp.); पुंभिर्विमिश्रा नार्यश्च Mb.;<BR>दंपत्योरिह को न को न तमसि<BR>व्रीडाविमिश्रो रसः Gīt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुख|विमुखः
विमुख a. (खी f.)<BR>1 With the<BR>face averted or turned away from.<BR>--2 Averse, disinclined, opposed;<BR>न क्षुद्रेपि प्रथमसुकृतापेक्षया संश्रयाय<BR>प्राप्ते मित्रे भवति विमुखः किं पुनर्यस्तथोच्चैः<BR>Me. 17; 27; Mu. 2. 7; (रघूणां) मनः<BR>परस्त्रीविमुखप्रवृति R. 16. 8, 19. 47.<BR>--3 Adverse; H. 1. 130.<BR>--4<BR>Without, devoid of (in comp.);<BR>करुणाविमुखेन मृत्युना हरता त्वां वद किं न मे<BR>हृतं R. 8. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुच्
विमुच् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To free, liberate.<BR>--2<BR>To loosen, unbind, unfasten, untie<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">Page0986-c+ 57</a>]<BR>आसीद्विवृत्तवदना च विमोचयंती (<BR>वल्कलं) Ś. 2. 12.<BR>--3 To give up, lay aside,<BR>abandon, quit; विमुच्य वासांसि<BR>गुरूनि सांप्रतं Rs. 1. 7.<BR>--4 To let go,<BR>let loose; Bk. 7. 50.<BR>--5 To except,<BR>set aside, set apart; Ku. 4. 31.<BR>--6<BR>To shed, pour down (te ars);<BR>चिरमश्रूणि विमुच्य राघवः R. 8. 25.<BR>--7 To<BR>throw, cast.<BR>--8 To take off (clothes),<BR>undress oneself.<BR>--9 To stop, cease.<BR>--10 To take, assume. --Pass. To<BR>be deprived of, be freed from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्त|विमुक्तः
विमुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Set free, released,<BR>liberated.<BR>--2 Abandoned, given<BR>up, quitted, left.<BR>--3 Freed from.<BR>--4 Hurled, discharged.<BR>--5 Given<BR>vent to.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठ a. raising a<BR>loud cry, weeping bitterly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुक्तिः|विमुक्ति
विमुक्तिः f.<BR>1 Release, liberation.<BR>--2 Separation.<BR>--3 Absolution, final<BR>liberation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुद्र|विमुद्रः
विमुद्र a.<BR>1 Unsealed.<BR>--2<BR>Opened, budded, blown (as a flower &c).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुह्
विमुह् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be confused,<BR>bewildered, or perplexed, be<BR>embarrassed; Bg. 2. 72; 3. 6, 27.<BR>--2 To be foolish or infatuated.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To infatuate, bewilder.<BR>--2 To allure, tempt, seduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमुग्ध
विमुग्ध a. Confused, confounded,<BR>bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमूढ|विमूढः
विमूढ p. p.<BR>1 Confounded,<BR>bewildered.<BR>--2 Seduced, tempted,<BR>beguiled.<BR>--3 Stupid.<BR>--4 Wise, learned.<BR>--ढः A kind of divine being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृद्
विमृद् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To press, squeeze.<BR>--2 To bruise, crush, pound.<BR>--3 To<BR>kill, destroy.<BR>--4 To lay waste,<BR>devastate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दः|विमर्द|विमर्द्द|विमर्द्दः
विमर्दः<BR>1 Pounding, crushing,<BR>bruising.<BR>--2 Rubbing together,<BR>trituration (as of perfumes),<BR>friction; विमर्दसुरभिर्बकुलावलिका खल्वहं<BR>M. 3; R. 5. 65; कस्तूरिका<BR>मृगविमर्दसुगंधिरेति Śi. 4. 61, 11. 28.<BR>--3<BR>Pressing together (as in embrace).<BR>--4 Spoiling, marring;<BR>कुतूहलविमर्दकारिणा परिश्रमेण Mk. 1.<BR>--5 Touch;<BR>contact.<BR>--6 Rubbing the person<BR>with saffron or other unguents.<BR>--7<BR>War, battle, fight, encounter;<BR>विमर्दक्षमां भूमिमवतरावः U. 5, 3. 44.<BR>--8<BR>Destruction, devastation; R. 6. 62.<BR>--9 Conjunction of the sun and<BR>moon.<BR>--10 An eclipse.<BR>--11<BR>Weariness, tediousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दकः|विमर्दक|विमर्द्दकः
विमर्दकः<BR>1 Grinding, pounding<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">Page0987-a+ 55</a>]<BR>bruising.<BR>--2 The trituration of<BR>perfumes.<BR>--3 An eclipse.<BR>--4 The<BR>conjunction of the sun and moon.<BR>--5 Destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0986-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दनं|विमर्दन|विमर्द्दन|विमर्द्दनं
विमर्दनं, --ना<BR>1 Pounding, crushing,<BR>trampling.<BR>--2 Rubbing together,<BR>friction.<BR>--3 Destruction, killing.<BR>--4 An eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दना
विमर्दनं, --ना<BR>1 Pounding, crushing,<BR>trampling.<BR>--2 Rubbing together,<BR>friction.<BR>--3 Destruction, killing.<BR>--4 An eclipse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्दित
विमर्दित, --विमृदित p. p.<BR>1 Pounded,<BR>crushed, ground.<BR>--2 Rubbed.<BR>--3<BR>Anointed, smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृदित
विमर्दित, --विमृदित p. p.<BR>1 Pounded,<BR>crushed, ground.<BR>--2 Rubbed.<BR>--3<BR>Anointed, smeared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृश्
विमृश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To touch, feel.<BR>--2 To stroke, rub.<BR>--3 To think,<BR>consider, reflect, ponder (over);<BR>वृणते हि विमृश्यकारिणं गुणलुब्धाः<BR>स्वयमेव संपदः Ki. 2. 30; रामप्रवासे<BR>व्यमृशन्न दोषं जनापवादं स नरद्रेंमृत्युं<BR>Bk. 3. 7; 12. 24; Ku. 6. 87; Bg. 18. 63;<BR>Śi. 10. 56.<BR>--4 To perceive, observe.<BR>--5 To examine, test;<BR>तदत्रभवानिमं मां च शास्त्रे प्रयोगे च विमृशतु M. 1.<BR>--6 To hesitate, doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शः|विमर्श
विमर्शः --र्शनं<BR>1 Deliberation,<BR>consideration, examination, discussion.<BR>--2 Reasoning.<BR>--3 A conflicting<BR>judgment.<BR>--4 Hesitation, doubt.<BR>--5<BR>The impression left on the mind<BR>by past good or bad actions; see<BR>वासना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमर्शनं|विमर्शन
विमर्शः --र्शनं<BR>1 Deliberation,<BR>consideration, examination, discussion.<BR>--2 Reasoning.<BR>--3 A conflicting<BR>judgment.<BR>--4 Hesitation, doubt.<BR>--5<BR>The impression left on the mind<BR>by past good or bad actions; see<BR>वासना.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमृष्ट
विमृष्ट p. p. Considered, reflected<BR>upon, pondered over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षः|विमोक्ष
विमोक्षः<BR>1 Release, liberation,<BR>freeing.<BR>--2 Discharging, shooting.<BR>--3 Final emancipation or beatitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षणं|विमोक्षण
विमोक्षणं --णा<BR>1 Liberating,<BR>releasing, setting free.<BR>--2 Discharging.<BR>--3<BR>Quitting, leaving, abandoning.<BR>--4<BR>Laying (as eggs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोक्षणा
विमोक्षणं --णा<BR>1 Liberating,<BR>releasing, setting free.<BR>--2 Discharging.<BR>--3<BR>Quitting, leaving, abandoning.<BR>--4<BR>Laying (as eggs).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोचनं|विमोचन
विमोचनं<BR>1 Unloosing, unyoking.<BR>--2 Release, freedom.<BR>--3 Liberation,<BR>emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विमोहन|विमोहनं|विमोहनः
विमोहन a. (ना or नी f.)<BR>Alluring, tempting, fascinating.<BR>--नः --नं<BR>N. of a division of Hell.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Seducing, tempting, fascinating.<BR>--2<BR>Infatuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विम्लापनं|विम्लापन
विम्लापनं<BR>1 Refreshing,<BR>reviving.<BR>--2 Cleaning, wiping.<BR>--3<BR>Causing to wither or fade away, wasting<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंबः|विम्ब|विंब|विंबं|विम्बं|विम्बः
विंबः --बं See बिंब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंबं|विम्ब|विंब|विम्बं|विंबः|विम्बः
विंबः --बं See बिंब.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंबक|विम्बक|विम्बकं
विंबक See बिंबक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंबटः|विम्बट|विंबट|विम्बटः
विंबटः The mustard plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंबा
विंबा --बी f. N. of a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंबी
विंबा --बी f. N. of a creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंबिका|विम्बिका
विंबिका See बिंबिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विंबुः|विम्बु|विंबु|विम्बुः
विंबुः The betel-nut tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियत्|वियन्त्
वियत् n. The sky^1, atmosphere,<BR>ether; पश्योदग्रवतत्वाद्बियति बहुतरं<BR>स्तोकमुर्व्यां प्रयाति Ś. 1. 7; R. 13. 40.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गंगा {1} the heavenly<BR>Ganges. {2} the galaxy.<BR>--चारिन् (<BR>वियच्चारिन्) m. a kite.<BR>--भूतिः f. darkness.<BR>--मणिः (वियन्मणिः) the sun.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by User saurabh.kapoor on 20200617. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/291. note: 1957 edition has 'sky'.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियतिः|वियति
वियतिः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियम्
वियम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To spread out,<BR>extend.<BR>--2 To curb, restrain.<BR>--3 To<BR>give, grant, bestow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियमः|वियम
वियमः<BR>1 Restraint, check,<BR>control.<BR>--2 Distress, pain, affliction.<BR>--3<BR>Cessation, stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियात|वियातः
वियात a.<BR>1 Bold(धृष्ट).<BR>--2<BR>Audacious, shameless, impudent.<BR>--3<BR>Abandoned, wretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियाम|वियामः
वियाम See वियम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियु
वियु {c3c} P.<BR>1 To be separated or<BR>dissolved (intran.).<BR>--2 To lose or<BR>be deprived of.<BR>--3 To exclude,<BR>deprive of.<BR>--4 To keep or ward off,<BR>prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुत
वियुत p. p.<BR>1 Deprived of,<BR>separated from; V. 4. 18.<BR>--2 Without,<BR>devoid of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुज्
वियुज् {c7c} A.<BR>1 To leave, abandon;<BR>part with, forsake; मदमानसमुद्धतं नृपं<BR>न वियुंक्ते नियमेन मूढता Ki. 2. 49;<BR>R. 13. 63.<BR>--2 To separate; पुरो वियुक्ते<BR>मिथुने कृपावती Ku. 5. 26.<BR>--3 To<BR>relax, slacken.<BR>--4 To disjoin, divide,<BR>sever.<BR>--5 To free or deliver from,<BR>deprive of (with instr.); प्राणैर्न<BR>वियोजयति Pt. 1; असुभिर्न वियुज्यते<BR>K. 38. --Caus.<BR>1 To separate.<BR>--2<BR>To free from, deprive of; अजानता<BR>मया सैव पत्रैः शाखा वियोजिता<BR>Mk. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियुक्त|वियुक्तः
वियुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Detached, severed,<BR>separated.<BR>--2 Separated from,<BR>deserted by.<BR>--3 Free from, deprived of<BR>(with instr. or in comp.).<BR>--4<BR>Failing, deficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगः|वियोग
वियोगः<BR>1 Separation, disunion;<BR>अयमेकपदे तया वियोगः सहसा चोपनतः<BR>सुदुःसहो मे V. 4. 3;<BR>त्वयोपस्थितवियोगस्य तपोवनस्यापि समवस्था दृश्यते Ś. 4;<BR>संधत्ते भृशमरतिं हि सद्वियोगः Ki. 5. 51;<BR>R. 12. 10; Me. 88; Śi. 12. 63.<BR>--2<BR>Absence, loss.<BR>--3 Subtraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगिन्
वियोगिन् a.<BR>1 Separated.<BR>--2<BR>Absent, apart. --m. The ruddy goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोगिनी
वियोगिनी<BR>1 A woman separated<BR>from her lover or husband;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">Page0987-c+ 56</a>]<BR>गुरुनिःश्वसितैः कपिर्मनीषी निरणैषीदथ तां<BR>वियोगिनीति Bv. 4. 35.<BR>--2 N. of a metre;<BR>(see App. I).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोजित|वियोजितः
वियोजित p. p.<BR>1 Separated.<BR>--2<BR>Separated from, deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोनिः|वियोनि
वियोनिः --नी f.<BR>1 Manifold birth.<BR>--2 The womb of animals (Kull. on<BR>Ms. 12. 77).<BR>--3 A debased or<BR>ignominious birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वियोनी
वियोनिः --नी f.<BR>1 Manifold birth.<BR>--2 The womb of animals (Kull. on<BR>Ms. 12. 77).<BR>--3 A debased or<BR>ignominious birth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरच्
विरच् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To arrange;<BR>Ki. 7. 94.<BR>--2 To compose, put together,<BR>write; R. 5. 75, Me. 86, 103.<BR>--3<BR>To effect, produce, cause, make;<BR>Bv. 1. 30.<BR>--4 To put on.<BR>--5 To set, inlay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचनं|विरचन
विरचनं --ना<BR>1 Arrangement,<BR>disposition; Śi. 5. 21.<BR>--2 Contriving,<BR>constructing.<BR>--3 Formation, creation.<BR>--4 Composition, compilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचना
विरचनं --ना<BR>1 Arrangement,<BR>disposition; Śi. 5. 21.<BR>--2 Contriving,<BR>constructing.<BR>--3 Formation, creation.<BR>--4 Composition, compilation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरचित|विरचितः
विरचित p. p.<BR>1 Arranged, made,<BR>formed, prepared.<BR>--2 Contrived,<BR>constructed.<BR>--3 Written, composed.<BR>--4 Trimmed, dressed, embellished,<BR>ornamented.<BR>--5 Put on, worn.<BR>--6 Set,<BR>inlaid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरज|विरजः
विरज a. Free from dust or<BR>passion.<BR>--जः An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--जा<BR>1 Dūrvā grass.<BR>--2 N. of the<BR>wife of Nahuṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्
विरजस्, विरजस्क a.<BR>1 Free from<BR>dust.<BR>--2 Free from passion;<BR>Śi. 20. 80.<BR>--3 Free from menstrual<BR>excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्क
विरजस्, विरजस्क a.<BR>1 Free from<BR>dust.<BR>--2 Free from passion;<BR>Śi. 20. 80.<BR>--3 Free from menstrual<BR>excretion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजस्का
विरजस्का A woman in whom<BR>the menstrual secretion has ceased<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीकृ
विरजीकृ {c8c} U. To render free from<BR>dust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरजीभू
विरजीभू {c1c} P. To become free from.<BR>dust, be pure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरंचः|विरञ्च|विरंच|विरञ्चः
विरंचः, --चिः N. of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरंचिः|विरञ्चि|विरंचि|विरञ्चिः
विरंचः, --चिः N. of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरंज्|विरञ्ज्
विरंज् {c1c} {c4c} U.<BR>1 To grow<BR>discoloured or soiled, be coarse or<BR>rough; केशा अपि विरज्यंते निःस्नेहाः<BR>किं न सेवकाः Pt. 1. 82 (where it<BR>has sense 2 also).<BR>--2 To be<BR>discontented or disaffected, to dislike,<BR>hate; चिरानुरक्तोऽपि विरज्यते जनः<BR>Mk. 1. 53; यां चिंतयामि सततं मयि सा<BR>विरक्ता Bh. 2. 2; Bk. 18. 22.<BR>--3 To<BR>become disgusted with the world<BR>and hence to renounce all worldly<BR>attachments. --Caus. To colour,<BR>dye.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्त|विरक्तः
विरक्त p. p.<BR>1 Very red, ruddy,<BR>R. 13. 64.<BR>--2 Discoloured.<BR>--3<BR>Changed in mind, disaffected, displeased;<BR>Bh. 2. 2.<BR>--4 Free from passion or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">Page0988-a+ 56</a>]<BR>worldly attachment, indifferent.<BR>--5<BR>Impassioned.<BR>--क्ता An unfortunate<BR>or unhappy woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0987-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरक्तिः|विरक्ति
विरक्तिः f.<BR>1 Change of disposition,<BR>dissatisfaction, discontent,<BR>disaffection.<BR>--2 Estrangement.<BR>--3<BR>Indifference, absence of desire, freedom<BR>from passion or worldly<BR>attachment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरटः|विरट
विरटः A kind of black<BR>agallochum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरणं|विरण
विरणं A kind of fragrant grass;<BR>cf. वीरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरम्
विरम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To end, terminate,<BR>come to an end; अविदितगतयामा<BR>रात्रिरेव व्यरंसीत् U. 1. 27; 6. 33.<BR>--2<BR>To cease, desist, stop, leave off<BR>(speaking &c.); एतावदुक्त्वा विरते<BR>मृगेंद्रे R. 2. 51; Śi. 2. 13; oft. with<BR>abl.; हा हंत किमिति चित्तं विरमति<BR>नाद्यपि विषयेभ्यः Bv. 4. 25; न स्थिरकर्मा<BR>विरराम कर्मणः R. 8. 22;<BR>वत्सैतस्माद्विरम विरमातः परं न क्षमोस्मि U. 1. 33;<BR>Bh. 2. 80.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरत|विरतः
विरत p. p.<BR>1 Ceased or desisting<BR>from (with abl.).<BR>--2 Rested,<BR>stopped, ceased.<BR>--3 Ended, concluded,<BR>at an end; विरतं गेयमृतुर्निरुत्सवः<BR>R. 8. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरतिः|विरति
विरतिः f.<BR>1 Cessation, stop,<BR>discontinuance.<BR>--2 Rest, end, pause.<BR>--3 Indifference to worldly<BR>attachments; विरतिवनितासंगमुदितः Bh. 3. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरमः|विरम
विरमः<BR>1 Cessation, stop.<BR>--2<BR>Sunset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरामः|विराम
विरामः<BR>1 (a) Cessation,<BR>discontinuance; सुधां विना न प्रययुर्विरामं<BR>Bh. 2. 80; प्रवृत्तस्याविरामे भवंती शासितव्या<BR>Mbh. (b) Rest, repose.<BR>--2 End,<BR>termination, conclusion;<BR>रजनिरिदानीमियमपि याति विरामं Gīt. 5;<BR>U. 3. 16, Māl. 9. 34.<BR>--3 Pause, stop.<BR>--4<BR>The stop or pause of the voice;<BR>Mk. 3. 5.<BR>--5 A small oblique stroke<BR>placed under a consonant, usually<BR>at the end of a sentence.<BR>--6 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरल|विरलं|विरलः
विरल a.<BR>1 Having interstices,<BR>separated by intervals, thin, not<BR>thick or compact; विपर्यासं यातो<BR>घनविरलभावः क्षितिरुहां U. 2. 27; 1. 20;<BR>भवति विरलभक्तिर्म्लानपुष्पापहारः<BR>R. 5. 74.<BR>--2 Fine, delicate.<BR>--3 Loose,<BR>wide apart.<BR>--4 Rare, scarcely found,<BR>unfrequent; विरला हि तेषामुपदेष्टारः<BR>K.; Pt. 1. 29.<BR>--5 Few, little<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">Page0988-b+ 56</a>]<BR>(referring to number or quantity);<BR>तत्त्वं किमपि काव्यानां जानाति विरलो<BR>भुवि Bv. 1. 117; विरलातपच्छविः<BR>Śi. 9. 3.<BR>--6 Remote, distant, long (as<BR>time, distance &c.).<BR>--लं Curds,<BR>coagulated milk.<BR>--लं ind. Scarcely,<BR>rarely, not frequently.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जानुक a. bandy-legged,<BR>bowkneed.<BR>--द्रवा a kind of gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरस|विरसः
विरस a.<BR>1 Tasteless, insipid,<BR>flavourless.<BR>--2 Unpleasant,<BR>disagreeable, painful; तावत्कोकिल विरसान्<BR>यापय दिवसान् वनांतरे निवसन्<BR>Bv. 1. 7; Māl. 1. 31; 6. 10.<BR>--3 Cruel,<BR>unfeeling.<BR>--सः Pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहः|विरह
विरहः<BR>1 Parting with,<BR>separation.<BR>--2 Especially, the separation<BR>of lovers; सा विरहे तव दीना Gīt. 4;<BR>क्षणमपि विरहः पुरा न सेहे ibid.;<BR>Me. 8, 12, 29, 85, 87.<BR>--3 Absence.<BR>--4<BR>Want.<BR>--5 Desertion, abandonment,<BR>relinquishment.<BR>--6 The feeling of<BR>love in separation; see विप्रलंभ (6).<BR>--7<BR>Loneliness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनलः the fire<BR>of separation.<BR>--अवस्था the state<BR>of separation.<BR>--आर्त, --उत्कंठ,<BR>--उत्सुक a. suffering from separation,<BR>pining away in separation.<BR>--उत्कंठिता a woman distressed by the<BR>absence of her lover or husband,<BR>one of the several classes of a<BR>Nāyikā in poetic compositions; see<BR>S. D. 121.<BR>--ज्वरः the fever or<BR>anguish of separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिणी
विरहिणी<BR>1 A woman separated<BR>from her lover or husband.<BR>--2<BR>Wages, hire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहित|विरहितः
विरहित p. p.<BR>1 Deserted,<BR>abandoned, forsaken.<BR>--2 Separated from.<BR>--3 Lonely, solitary.<BR>--4 Bereft<BR>of, devoid or destitute of, free from<BR>(mostly in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरहिन्
विरहिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>1 Absent<BR>from, being separated from a<BR>mistress or lover; नृत्यति युवतिजनेन समं<BR>सखि विरहिजनस्य दुरंते Gīt. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Lonely, solitary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरागः|विराग
विरागः<BR>1 Change of colour.<BR>--2<BR>Change of disposition, disaffection,<BR>discontent, dissatisfaction;<BR>विरागकारणेषु परिहृतेषु Mu. 1.<BR>--3 Aversion,<BR>disinclination.<BR>--4 Indifference to<BR>worldly attachments, freedom from<BR>passion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज्
विराज् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To shine, glitter;<BR>Bv. 1. 88.<BR>--2 To appear or look<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">Page0988-c+ 56</a>]<BR>like; R. 2. 20.<BR>--3 To be eminent<BR>or illustrious. --Caus. To brighten,<BR>illuminate, irradiate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज्
विराज् m.<BR>1 Beauty, splendour.<BR>--2 A man of the Kṣatriya or<BR>warrior tribe.<BR>--3 The first progeny<BR>of Brahman; cf. Ms. 1. 32;<BR>तस्मात् विराडजायत Rv. 10. 90. 5<BR>(where विराज् is represented as born<BR>from Puruṣa).<BR>--4 The body.<BR>--5<BR>(In Vedānta phil.) N. of<BR>‘intellect’ considered as ruling over the<BR>aggregate of bodies. --f. N. of a<BR>Vedic metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराज|विराजः
विराज See विराज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराजित|विराजितः
विराजित p. p.<BR>1 Irradiated,<BR>illuminated.<BR>--2 Displayed,<BR>manifested.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटः|विराट
विराटः<BR>1 N. of a district in<BR>India.<BR>--2 N. of a king of the<BR>Matsyas. The Pāṇḍavas lived<BR>incognito in the service of this king<BR>for one year, (the thirteenth of their<BR>exile) having assumed different<BR>disguises. His daughter Uttarā was<BR>married to Abhimanyu and was mother<BR>of Parīkṣit who succeeded<BR>Yudhisṭhira to the throne of Hastināpura.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः a sort of inferior<BR>diamond.<BR>--पर्वन् n. the fourth book<BR>of the Mahābhārata.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराटकः|विराटक
विराटकः A sort of inferior<BR>diamond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराणिन्
विराणिन् m. An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराध्
विराध् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To hurt, injure,<BR>offend, wrong; क्रियासमभिहारेण<BR>विराध्यंतं क्षमेत कः Śi. 2. 43; विराद्ध एवं<BR>भवता विरा द्धा बहुधा च नः 2. 41.<BR>--2 To<BR>lose, be deprived of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराद्ध
विराद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Opposed,<BR>counteracted.<BR>--2 Offended, injured,<BR>treated with contempt; see the<BR>quotations under राध् with वि above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधः|विराध
विराधः<BR>1 Opposition.<BR>--2<BR>Annoyance, vexation, molestation.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a powerful Rākṣasa slain by<BR>Rāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराधनं|विराधन
विराधनं<BR>1 Opposing.<BR>--2 Hurting,<BR>injuring, offending.<BR>--3 Pain, anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराल|विरालः
विराल See बिडाल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिंचः|विरिञ्च|विरिंच|विरिञ्चः
विरिंचः, विरिंचनः<BR>1 N. of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--2 Of Śiva.<BR>--3 Of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिंचनः|विरिञ्चन|विरिंचन|विरिञ्चनः
विरिंचः, विरिंचनः<BR>1 N. of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--2 Of Śiva.<BR>--3 Of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिंचिः|विरिञ्चि|विरिंचि|विरिञ्चिः
विरिंचिः<BR>1 N. of Brahman;<BR>Vikr. 1. 46; N. 3. 44; Śi. 9. 9.<BR>--2 Of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 Of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0988-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरिब्धः|विरिब्ध
विरिब्धः A note, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरु
विरु {c2c} P.<BR>1 To cry, bewail,<BR>lament; ननु सहवरीं दूरे मत्वा विरौषि<BR>समुत्सुकः V. 4. 20; Bk. 5. 54;<BR>Rs. 6. 27.<BR>--2 To make a sound, sound in<BR>general; न स विरौति न चापि स शोभते<BR>Pt. 1. 75; जीर्णत्वाद गृहस्य विरौति<BR>कपाटं Mk. 3; एते त एव गिरयो<BR>विरुवन्मयूराः U. 2. 23.<BR>--3 To cry out, shout,<BR>scream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरावः|विराव
विरावः Clamour, noise, sound;<BR>आलोकशब्दं वयसां विरावैः R. 2. 9,<BR>16. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराविन्
विराविन् a.<BR>1 Weeping, crying,<BR>shouting.<BR>--2 Lamenting.<BR>--णी<BR>1<BR>Weeping, crying.<BR>--2 A broom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुत
विरुत p. p.<BR>1 Screamed,<BR>shouted.<BR>--2 Resounding, filled with<BR>cries.<BR>--त<BR>1 Crying, shrieking,<BR>roaring &c.<BR>--2 Cry, sound, noise,<BR>clamour, din.<BR>--3 Singing,<BR>humming, chirping, buzzing; परभृतविरुतं<BR>कलं यथा प्रतिवचनीकृतमेभिरीदृशं Ś. 4. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुग्ण
विरुग्ण p. p.<BR>1 Broken to pieces,<BR>shattered.<BR>--2 Destroyed.<BR>--3 Bent.<BR>--4 Blunted, dulled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुच्
विरुच् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To shine, be<BR>resplendent; R. 6. 5; 17. 14;<BR>Bk. 8. 66.<BR>--2 To be eminent or<BR>conspicuous.<BR>--3 To become visible,<BR>appear.<BR>--4 To illuminate, brighten<BR>(P.).<BR>--5 To please, delight.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To irradiate, illuminate.<BR>--2 To delight in.<BR>--3 To sport with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुक्मत्|विरुक्मन्त्
विरुक्मत् m. A bright weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुदः|विरुद|विरुदं
विरुदः --दं<BR>1 Proclaiming.<BR>--2<BR>Crying aloud.<BR>--3 A panegyric,<BR>laudatory poem; गद्यपद्यमयी<BR>राजस्तुतिर्बिरुदमुच्यते S. D. 570; नदंति<BR>मददंतिनः परिलसंति वाजिव्रजाः पठंति<BR>विरुदावलीमहितमंदिरे वंदिनः ॥ R. G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुदं|विरुद|विरुदः
विरुदः --दं<BR>1 Proclaiming.<BR>--2<BR>Crying aloud.<BR>--3 A panegyric,<BR>laudatory poem; गद्यपद्यमयी<BR>राजस्तुतिर्बिरुदमुच्यते S. D. 570; नदंति<BR>मददंतिनः परिलसंति वाजिव्रजाः पठंति<BR>विरुदावलीमहितमंदिरे वंदिनः ॥ R. G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुदितं|विरुदित
विरुदितं Loud cry or<BR>lamentation; U. 3. 30 v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुध्
विरुध् {c7c} U. To oppose,<BR>obstruct, hinder, prevent. --Pass.<BR>1<BR>To be opposed to, be inconsistent<BR>or at variance with.<BR>--2 To contend<BR>or quarrel with; Pt. 4. 116.<BR>--3 To<BR>fail.<BR>--4 To be kept back or<BR>withheld.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुद्ध|विरुद्धः
विरुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Hindered, checked,<BR>opposed, obstructed.<BR>--2 Blocked<BR>up, confined or shut up.<BR>--3<BR>Besieged, blockaded.<BR>--4 Opposed to,<BR>inconsistent with, incongruous,<BR>inconsistent.<BR>--5 Contrary, opposite,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-b" target="_blank">Page0989-b+ 56</a>]<BR>opposed in quality.<BR>--6<BR>Contradictory, proving the reverse, (as a<BR>hetu in Logic); साध्याभवव्याप्तो<BR>हेतुर्विरुद्धः Tarka K.: e. g. शब्दो नित्यः<BR>कृतकत्वात् T. S.<BR>--7 Hostile, adverse,<BR>inimical.<BR>--8 Unfavourable,<BR>unpropitious.<BR>--9 Prohibited, forbidden<BR>(as food).<BR>--10 Wrong, unlawful,<BR>improper.<BR>--11 Excluded.<BR>--12<BR>Uncertain, doubtful.<BR>--द्धं<BR>1<BR>Opposition, contrariety, hostility.<BR>--2<BR>Discord, disagreement.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धी<BR>a. evil-minded, wicked<BR>--मतिकृत् m.<BR>a fault or defect in composition;<BR>विपरीतार्थधीयर्स्मात् विरुद्धमतिकृन्मतम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधः|विरोध
विरोधः<BR>1 Opposition, obstruction,<BR>impediment.<BR>--2 Blockade, siege,<BR>investment.<BR>--3 Restraint, check.<BR>--4 Inconsistency, incongruity,<BR>contradiction.<BR>--5 Antithesis,<BR>contrast.<BR>--6 Enmity, hostility;<BR>विरोधो विश्रांतः U. 6. 11; Pt. 1. 332;<BR>R. 10. 13.<BR>--7 A quarrel,<BR>disagreement.<BR>--8 A calamity, misfortune.<BR>--9 (In Rhet.) An apparent<BR>incongruity which is merely verbal and<BR>is explained away by properly<BR>construing the passage; it consists in<BR>representing objects as antithetical<BR>to one another though in the<BR>nature of things they are not so:<BR>representing things as being<BR>together though really they cannot<BR>be together; (this figure is<BR>largely used by Bāṇa and Subandhu;<BR>पुष्पवत्यपि पवित्रा, कृष्णोप्यसुदर्शनः, भरतोपि<BR>शत्रुघ्नः being familiar instances); it<BR>is thus defined by Mammaṭa:<BR>--विरोध सोऽविरोधेऽपि विरुद्धत्वेन यद्वचः<BR>K. P. 10; this figure is also<BR>called विरोधाभास.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः<BR>f.,<BR>--वचनं contradiction, opposition.<BR>--कारिन् a. fomenting quarrels.<BR>--कृत् a. opposing. (--m.) an enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधनं|विरोधन
विरोधनं<BR>1 Hindering, opposing,<BR>obstructing.<BR>--2 Besieging,<BR>blockading.<BR>--3 Opposition, resistance.<BR>--4<BR>Contradiction, inconsistency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोधिन्
विरोधिन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Resisting,<BR>opposing, obstructing.<BR>--2<BR>Besieging.<BR>--3 Contradictory, opposed to,<BR>inconsistent with; तपोवन˚ Ś. 1.<BR>--4 Hostile, inimical, adverse;<BR>विरोधिसत्त्वोज्झितपूर्वमत्सरं Ku. 5. 17.<BR>--5<BR>Quarrelsome. --m. An enemy;<BR>Śi. 16. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरुह्
विरुह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To grow, shoot up;<BR>R. 2. 26; Mk. 1. 19.<BR>--2 To mount,<BR>ascend.<BR>--3 To arise, proceed. --Caus.<BR>1 To heal (as a wound).<BR>--2 To<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूढ|विरूढः
विरूढ p. p.<BR>1 Grown, germinated,<BR>shot up; Mk. 1. 9.<BR>--2 Produced,<BR>born, arisen.<BR>--3 Grown, increased.<BR>--4 Budded, blossomed.<BR>--5<BR>Ascended, mounted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोपणं|विरोपण
विरोप(ह)णं<BR>1 Healing (as<BR>a sore); व्रणविरोपणं तैलं Ś. 4. 13.<BR>--2 Planting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोहणं|विरोहण
विरोप(ह)णं<BR>1 Healing (as<BR>a sore); व्रणविरोपणं तैलं Ś. 4. 13.<BR>--2 Planting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोहः|विरोह
विरोहः Growing, shooting forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूक्षणं|विरूक्षण
विरूक्षणं<BR>1 Roughening.<BR>--2<BR>Acting as an astringent.<BR>--3 Blame,<BR>censure.<BR>--4 A curse, an<BR>imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूप|विरूपं|विरूपः
विरूप a. (पा or पी f.)<BR>1<BR>Deformed, ugly, misshapen,<BR>disfigured; Pt. 1. 143.<BR>--2 Unnatural,<BR>monstrous.<BR>--3 Multiform, diverse.<BR>--पं<BR>1 Deformity, ugliness.<BR>--2<BR>Variety of form, nature, or character.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a. having deformed<BR>eyes: वपुर्विरूपाक्षं Ku. 5. 72.<BR>--(क्षः)<BR>N. of Śiva (having an unusual<BR>number of eyes); दृशा दग्धं मनसिजं<BR>जीवयंति दृशैव याः । विरूपाक्षस्य<BR>जयिनीस्ताः स्तुवे वामलोचनाः Vb. 1. 2;<BR>Ku. 6. 21.<BR>--करणं {1} disfiguring.<BR>{2} injuring.<BR>--चक्षुस् m. an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--रूप a. deformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपक|विरूपकः
विरूपक a.<BR>1 Deformed, ugly.<BR>--2<BR>Hideous, frightful, monstrous.<BR>--कः<BR>A nickname.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरूपिन्
विरूपिन् a. (णी f.) Deformed,<BR>ugly, disfigured. --m. A pole-cat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेकः|विरेक
विरेकः<BR>1 Evacuation of the<BR>bowels, purging.<BR>--2 A purgative.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचनं|विरेचन|विरेचनः
विरेचनं See विरेक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेचित
विरेचित a. Purged, evacuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरेफः|विरेफ
विरेफः<BR>1 A river, stream.<BR>--2<BR>Absence of the letter र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोकः|विरोक|विरोकं
विरोकः --कं A hole, pit, chasm;<BR>Śi. 5. 54.<BR>--कः A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोकं|विरोक|विरोकः
विरोकः --कं A hole, pit, chasm;<BR>Śi. 5. 54.<BR>--कः A ray of light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विरोचनः|विरोचन
विरोचनः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 The<BR>moon.<BR>--3 Fire.<BR>--4 N. of the son<BR>of Prahrāda and father of Bali;<BR>Śi. 14. 74.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सुतः an<BR>epithet of Bali.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्
विल् {vI.v} {c6c} P. (विलति)<BR>1 To cover,<BR>conceal.<BR>--2 To break, divide. {vII.v}<BR>{c10c} U. (वेलयति-ते) To throw, send<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0989-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलं|विल|विलः
विलं See बिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष्
विलक्ष् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To see, observe,<BR>perceive, notice.<BR>--2 To characterize,<BR>distinguish.<BR>--3 To be confused, be<BR>bewildered; निर्व्यापारविलक्षितानि<BR>सांत्वय बलानि U. 6; see विलक्ष below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्ष|विलक्षः
विलक्ष a.<BR>1 Having no<BR>characteristic or distinguishing marks.<BR>--2 Bewildered, embarrassed.<BR>--3<BR>Surprised, astonished.<BR>--4 Ashamed,<BR>abashed, disconcerted; गोत्रेषु<BR>स्खलितस्तदा भवति च व्रीडाविलक्षश्चिरं<BR>Ś. 6. 4.<BR>--5 Forced, unnatural,<BR>embarrassed (as a smile);<BR>विलक्षस्मितस्फुरितैर्दशनांशुभिः K. 233; Ratn. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षण|विलक्षणं|विलक्षणः
विलक्षण a.<BR>1 Having no<BR>characteristic or distinguishing marks.<BR>--2 Different, other.<BR>--3 Strange,<BR>extraordinary, unusual.<BR>--4 Possessed<BR>of inauspicious marks.<BR>--णं<BR>1 A<BR>vain or useless state.<BR>--2 Perceiving,<BR>observing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलक्षित
विलक्षित p. p.<BR>1 Distinguished,<BR>perceived, seen, discovered.<BR>--2<BR>Discernible by.<BR>--3 Dismayed, perplexed,<BR>embarrassed, puzzled.<BR>--4 Vexed,<BR>annoyed.<BR>--5 Undistinguished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्
विलग् {c1c} P. To stick or adhere to,<BR>cling to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलग्न|विलग्नं
विलग्न a.<BR>1 Clinging or sticking<BR>to, resting on, fastened on;<BR>आकुटिलपक्ष्मविलग्नं Ś. 7. 25; Śi. 9. 20.<BR>--2<BR>Cast, fixed, directed; Ku. 7. 50<BR>--3 Gone by, elapsed (as time).<BR>--4<BR>Thin, slender, delicate; मध्येन सा<BR>वेदिविलग्नमध्या Ku. 1. 39; V. 4. 37.<BR>--ग्नं<BR>1 The waist.<BR>--2 The hips.<BR>--3<BR>The rising of constellations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंघ्|विलङ्घ्
विलंघ् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To pass or spring<BR>over, traverse; निवेशयमास<BR>विलंघिताध्वा R. 5. 42; 16. 32; Śi. 12. 24,<BR>8. 26.<BR>--2 To violate, transgress,<BR>overstep, disregard, neglect; गतुं प्रवृत्ते<BR>समयं विलंध्य Ku. 3. 25; R. 5. 48,<BR>Ki. 2. 45, Śi. 17. 12.<BR>--3 To violate<BR>the limits of propriety; R. 9. 74.<BR>--4 To rise towards, ascend or go<BR>up to; Ki. 5. 1; N. 5. 2.<BR>--5 To<BR>give up, abandon, leave aside; मनो<BR>बबंधान्यरसान् विलंघ्य सा R. 3. 4.<BR>--6<BR>To surpass, excel; इति कर्णोत्पलं<BR>प्रायस्तव दृष्ट्या विलंघ्यते Kāv. 2. 224.<BR>--7<BR>To cause to fast.<BR>--8 To overcome,<BR>surmount.<BR>--9 To offend, insult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंघनं|विलङ्घन|विलंघन
विलंघनं<BR>1 Transgressing,<BR>overstepping.<BR>--2 Offence, transgression,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">Page0990-b+ 56</a>]<BR>injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंघित|विलङ्घित
विलंघित p. p.<BR>1 Passed over or<BR>beyond, gone over.<BR>--2 Transgressed.<BR>--3 Surpassed, excelled.<BR>--4<BR>Overcome, defeated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्ज्
विलज्ज् {c6c} A. To be bashful or<BR>modest, to blush, feel ashamed;<BR>यत्रांशुकाक्षेपविलज्जितानां Ku. 1. 14;<BR>R. 14. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलज्ज|विलज्जः
विलज्ज a. Shameless, unabashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलप्
विलप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To say, speak.<BR>--2 To<BR>lament, moan, bewail, cry, weep;<BR>विललाप विकीर्णमूर्घजा Ku. 4. 4;<BR>विललाप स बाष्पगद्गदं R. 8. 43, 70;<BR>Bk. 6. 11; तमिह वृथा किं विलपामि Gīt {3}<BR>--3 To prattle, talk idly, babble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपनं|विलपन
विलपनं<BR>1 Talking.<BR>--2 Talking<BR>idly, chattering, prattle<BR>--3<BR>Lamenting, wailing; विलपनविनोदोप्यसुलभः<BR>U. 3. 30.<BR>--4 The sediment of any<BR>oily substance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलपितं|विलपित
विलपितं<BR>1 Lamentation, wailing.<BR>--2 A wail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलापः|विलाप
विलापः Wailing, lamentation, a<BR>wail, moan; लंकास्त्रीणां पुनश्चक्रे<BR>विलापाचार्यकं शरैः R. 12. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंब्|विलम्ब्
विलंब् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To hang down,<BR>hang from, be suspended from;<BR>R. 10. 62.<BR>--2 To set, decline (as the<BR>sun &c.).<BR>--3 To stay or lag behind,<BR>stay or remain, wait, stand still,<BR>तां प्राङ्मुखीं तत्र निवेश्य तन्वीं क्षणं<BR>व्यलबंत पुरो निषण्णाः Ku. 7. 13.<BR>--4 To<BR>delay, be retarded; विलांबितफलैः<BR>कालं निनाय स मनोरथैः R. 1. 33; किं<BR>विलंव्यते त्वरितं तं प्रवेशय U. 1. --Caus.<BR>1 To delay, detain.<BR>--2 To put off,<BR>retard, procrastinate, postpone.<BR>--3<BR>To waste, lose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंबः|विलम्ब|विलंब|विलम्बः
विलंबः<BR>1 Hanging over,<BR>pendulousness.<BR>--2 Tardiness, delay,<BR>procrastination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंबनं|विलम्बन|विलंबन|विलम्बनं
विलंबनं<BR>1 Hanging down,<BR>depending.<BR>--2 Delay, procrastination; न<BR>करु नितंबिनि गमनविलंबनं Gīt. 5; or<BR>तन्मुग्धे विफलं विलंबनमसौ रम्योऽ<BR>भिसारक्षणः ibid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंबिका|विलम्बिका
विलंबिका Constipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंबित|विलम्बित|विलम्बितं
विलंबित p. p.<BR>1 Hanging,<BR>depending.<BR>--2 Pendent, pendulous.<BR>--3<BR>Depending on, closely connected<BR>with.<BR>--4 Tardy, delayed, retarded.<BR>--5 Slow (as time in music).<BR>--तं<BR>Delay.<BR>--तं ind. Slowly, tardily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंबिन्|विलम्बिन्
विलंबिन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Hanging<BR>down, depending, pendent;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-c" target="_blank">Page0990-c+ 56</a>]<BR>नवांबुभिर्भूरिबिलंबिनो घनाः Ś. 5. 12.<BR>शिरीषम गंडविलंबि केशरं 6. 17;<BR>अलघुविलंबिपयोधरोपरुद्धाः Śi. 4. 29, 59;<BR>Ku. 1. 14; Ki. 5. 6; R. 16. 14, 18. 26;<BR>Mk. 5. 13.<BR>--2 Delaying, dilatory,<BR>being slow; भवति विलंबिनि<BR>विगलितलज्जा विलपति रोदिति वासकसज्जा Gīt. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलंभः|विलम्भ|विलंभ|विलम्भः
विलंभः<BR>1 Liberality.<BR>--2 A gift,<BR>donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलयः|विलय
विलयः<BR>1 Dissolution,<BR>liquefaction.<BR>--2 Destruction, death, end;<BR>नयतु मामात्ममोंऽगेषु विलयमंबा U. 7.<BR>--3 Destruction or dissolution of the<BR>world; (विलयं गम् to be dissolved,<BR>to end, to be terminated, दिवसोऽ<BR>नुमित्रमगपद्विलयं Śi. 9. 17).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलयनं|विलयन
विलयनं<BR>1 Dissolving, liquefying,<BR>dissolution.<BR>--2 Corroding.<BR>--3<BR>Removing, taking away.<BR>--4<BR>Attenuating.<BR>--5 An attenuant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलस्
विलस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To shine, flash,<BR>glitter; वियति च विलिलास<BR>तद्वदिंदुर्विलसति चंद्रमसो न यद्वदन्यः Bk. 10. 68;<BR>Me. 47; R. 13. 76.<BR>--2 To appear,<BR>arise, become manifest; प्रेम विलसति<BR>महत्तदहो Śi. 15. 14; 9. 87.<BR>--3 To<BR>sport, amuse oneself, play, frolic<BR>about sportively; कापि चपला<BR>मधुरिपुणा विलसति युवतिरधिकगुणा Gīt. 7;<BR>or हरिरिह मुग्धवधूनिकरे विलासिनि<BR>विलसाति केलिपरे Gīt. 1; पर्यंके तया सह<BR>विललास H. 1.<BR>--4 To sound, echo,<BR>reverberate.<BR>--5 To act upon, work<BR>upon, show oneself; (खेदः)<BR>त्वयि विलसति तुल्यं वल्लभालोकनेन<BR>Māl. 3. 8.<BR>--6 To move about, dart, shoot<BR>up wards.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसत्|विलसन्त्
विलसत् pres. a. (न्ती f.)<BR>1<BR>Glittering, shining, bright.<BR>--2<BR>Flashing, darting.<BR>--3 Waving.<BR>--4<BR>Sportive, playful; see विलस् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसनं|विलसन
विलसनं<BR>1 Glittering, flashing,<BR>gleaming.<BR>--2 Sporting, dallying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलसित
विलसित p. p.<BR>1 Glittering,<BR>shining, gleaming.<BR>--2 Appeared,<BR>manifested.<BR>--3 Sportive, wanton.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Glittering, gleaming.<BR>--2 A gleam,<BR>flash; रोधोभुवां मुहुग्मुत्र हिरण्मयीनां<BR>भासस्तडिद्विलसितानि विडंबयंति Ki. 5. 46.<BR>Me. 81, V. 4.<BR>--3 Appearance,<BR>manifestation; as in अज्ञानविलसितं &c.<BR>--4 Sport, play, dalliance, amorous<BR>or wanton gesture (fig. also);<BR>अतिपिशुनानि चैकांतनिष्टुरस्य दवैह कस्य<BR>विलसितानि K.<BR>--5 Action or gesture<BR>in general.<BR>--6 Effect, fruit, result;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">Page0991-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Māl. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0990-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासः|विलास
विलासः<BR>1 Sport, play, pastime.<BR>--2 Amorous pastime, diversion,<BR>pleasure; as in विलासमेखला R. 8. 64;<BR>so विलासकाननं, विलासमंदिरं &c.<BR>--3<BR>Coquetry, dalliance, affectation,<BR>wantonness, graceful movement or play,<BR>any feminine gesture indicative of<BR>amorous sentiment; Ś. 2. 2;<BR>कविकुलगुरुः कालिदासो विलासः<BR>P. R. 1. 22; Śi. 9. 26.<BR>--4 Grace, beauty,<BR>elegance, charm; Māl. 2. 6.<BR>--5 Flash,<BR>gleam.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काननं a<BR>pleasuregrove.<BR>--मंदिर a pleasure-house.<BR>--चेष्टितं amorous movement; Ku. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासनं|विलासन
विलासनं<BR>1 Sport, play, pastime.<BR>--2 Wantonness, dalliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासवती
विलासवती A wanton or amorous<BR>woman; R. 9. 48; Rs. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिका
विलासिका A drama in one act<BR>full of love-incidents; it is<BR>thus defined in S. D.:<BR>--शृंगारबहुलैकांका<BR>दशलास्यांगसंयुता । विदूषकविटभ्यां च<BR>पीठमर्देन भूषिता । हीना गर्भविमर्षाभ्यां संधिभ्यां<BR>हीननायका । स्वल्पवृत्ता सुमेपथ्या विख्याता सा<BR>विलासिका 552.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिन्
विलासिन् a. (नीं f.) Sportive,<BR>playful, dallying, wanton, coquettish;<BR>R. 6. 14. --m.<BR>1 A sensualist,<BR>voluptuary, an amorous person;<BR>उपमानमभूद्विलासिनां करणं यत्तव कांतिमतया<BR>Ku. 4. 5.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 The moon.<BR>--4 A snake.<BR>--5 An epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa or Viṣṇu.<BR>--6 Of Śiva.<BR>--7 Of<BR>the god of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलासिनी
विलासिनी<BR>1 A woman (in general).<BR>--2 A coquettish or wanton woman;<BR>हरिघि मग्धवधूनि करे विलासिनि विलसति<BR>केलिपरे Gīt. 1; Ku. 7. 69; Śi. 8. 10,<BR>R. 6. 17.<BR>--3 A wanton, harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलालः|विलाल
विलालः<BR>1 A cat (= बिडाल).<BR>--2<BR>An instrument, a machine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिख्
विलिख् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To write, inscribe.<BR>--2 To draw, paint, delineate, portray;<BR>विलिखति रहसि कुरंगमदेन<BR>भवंतमसमशरभूतं Gīt. 4.<BR>--3 To scratch, scrape,<BR>tear up; मंदं शब्दायमानो विलिखति<BR>शयनादुत्थितः क्ष्मां खुरण K. P. 10;<BR>व्यलिखच्चचुपुटेन पक्षती N. 2. 2; पादेन हैमं<BR>विलिलेख पीठं R. 6. 15; Ku. 2. 23.<BR>--4<BR>To implant, infix; तावंतोपि<BR>विलिख्यंते हृदये शाकशकवः H. 4. 72 v. l.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिखनं|विलिखन
विलिखनं Scratching, scraping,<BR>writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेखनं|विलेखन
विलेखनं<BR>1 Scratching, scraping,<BR>making a mark or furrow.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">Page0991-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Digging.<BR>--3 Uprooting.<BR>--4 Dividing,<BR>splitting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्
विलिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To smear, anoint.<BR>rub on; तथाहि नृत्याभिनयक्रियाच्युतं<BR>विलिप्यते मौलिभिरंबरौकसां Ku. 5. 79;<BR>Bk. 3. 20; 15. 6; Śi. 16. 62.<BR>--2 To<BR>pollute, defile, taint, contaminate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलिप्त
विलिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Anointed,<BR>besmeared, smeared over.<BR>--2 Polluted,<BR>stained, defiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपः|विलेप
विलेपः<BR>1 An unguent, an ointment.<BR>--2 Mortar.<BR>--3 Plaster (in general).<BR>--4 Anointing, plastering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपनं|विलेपन
विलेपनं<BR>1 Smearing, anointing.<BR>--2<BR>An ointment, unguent, any<BR>cosmetic or perfume for the body (such<BR>as saffron, sandal &c); न स्नानं न<BR>विलेपनं न कुसुमं नालंकृता मूर्धजाः<BR>Bh. 2. 19; यान्येव सुरभिकुसुमधूपावलेपनादीनि K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपनी
विलेपनी<BR>1 A woman scented with<BR>perfumes<BR>--2 A woman beautifully<BR>dressed or attired (सुवेशा).<BR>--3<BR>Ricegruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपिका
विलेपिका, विलेपी, विलेप्यः<BR>Ricegruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेपी
विलेपिका, विलेपी, विलेप्यः<BR>Ricegruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलेप्यः|विलेप्य
विलेपिका, विलेपी, विलेप्यः<BR>Ricegruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विली
विली {vI.v} {c4c} A.<BR>1 To cling or stick<BR>to, adhere to.<BR>--2 To rest on, settle<BR>down or alight on; पुरोऽस्य यावन्न<BR>भुविव्यलीयत Śi. 1. 12.<BR>--3 To be<BR>dissolved, to melt away, be absorbed<BR>in; विलिल्ये यत्कुक्षिस्थितशिखिनि<BR>वातापिवपुषा Mv. 6. 60; 7. 14.<BR>--4 To<BR>vanish, disappear.<BR>--5 To perish. {vII.v}<BR>{c9c} P. To melt, liquefy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलीन|विलीनः
विलीन p. p.<BR>1 Sticking to, clung<BR>or attached to.<BR>--2 Perched or<BR>settled on, alighting on.<BR>--3 Contiguous<BR>to, in contact with.<BR>--4 Melted,<BR>dissolved, liquefied.<BR>--5 Disappeared,<BR>vanished.<BR>--6 Dead, perished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुंचनं|विलुञ्चन
विलुंचनं Tearing off, peeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुड्
विलुड् Caus.<BR>1 To agitate, stir<BR>up, toss about.<BR>--2 To disturb,<BR>confuse.<BR>--3 To turn over, upset.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडनं|विलोडन
विलोडनं Agitating, shaking about,<BR>stirring up, churning; Śi. 14. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोडित|विलोडितं
विलोडित p. p.<BR>1 Shaken,<BR>churned, stirred, agitated.<BR>--2 Rolling on<BR>the ground.<BR>--तं Butter-milk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुंठनं|विलुण्ठन|विलुंठन
विलुंठनं Robbing, plundering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुप्
विलुप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To break off, pull<BR>out, cut off.<BR>--2 To seize, plunder,<BR>rob, carry off.<BR>--3 To mar, spoil,<BR>impair.<BR>--4 (a) To destroy, ruin,<BR>cause to disappear;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">Page0991-c+ 55</a>]<BR>प्रियमत्यंतविलुप्तदर्शनं Ku. 4. 2 ‘for ever lost to view’.<BR>(b) To eat up; क्रव्याद्भिरंगलतिका<BR>नियतं विलुप्ता U. 3. 28, Mk. 1. 9.<BR>--5<BR>To wipe or rub off. --Pass. To be<BR>destroyed or lost, to perish,<BR>disappear; जराविलुप्तमानावमानचिंतः Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुप्त
विलुप्त p. p.<BR>1 Broken or torn off;<BR>Pt. 2. 2.<BR>--2 Seized, snatched away,<BR>carried off<BR>--3 Robbed, plundered.<BR>--4 Destroyed, ruined.<BR>--5 Impaired,<BR>mutilated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुंपकः|विलुम्पक|विलुंपक|विलुम्पकः
विलुंपकः^1 A thief, robber, ravisher^2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: per AP quote from Bhag. Pur. 1.18.44.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोपः|विलोप
विलोपः<BR>1 Taking away, carrying<BR>off, seizure, plunder.<BR>--2 Loss,<BR>destruction, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोपनं|विलोपन
विलोपनं<BR>1 Cutting off.<BR>--2 Carrying<BR>away.<BR>--3 Destroying, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुभ्
विलुभ् {c4c} P. To be disturbed or<BR>deranged; be disordered;<BR>Bk. 9. 40. --Caus.<BR>1 To allure, entice,<BR>attract; स्मर यावन्न विलाभ्यसे दिवि<BR>Ku. 4. 20; अंगनास्तमधिकं व्यलोभयन्<BR>(मुखैः) R. 19. 10.<BR>--2 To divert, amuse,<BR>entertain; क्वदृष्टिं विलोभयामि Ś. 6;<BR>ललितलताविलोभ्यमाननयनो भवानुत्कठां<BR>विनोदयतु V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभः|विलोभ
विलोभः Attraction, seduction,<BR>allurement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोभनं|विलोभन
विलोभनं<BR>1 Enticing, alluring.<BR>--2<BR>An allurement, a temptation,<BR>seduction; प्रयुज्य सामाचरितं विलोभनं भयं<BR>विभेदाय धियः प्रदर्शितं Ki. 14. 7;<BR>R. 8. 60.<BR>--3 Praise, flattery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुल्
विलुल् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To move to and<BR>fro.<BR>--2 To shake, make tremulous.<BR>--3 To disorder, derange, dishevel<BR>(as hair). --Caus. To agitate, stir,<BR>disturb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलुलित
विलुलित p. p.<BR>1 Moving to and fro,<BR>unsteady, shaken, tossed about,<BR>tremulous; U. 3. 23.<BR>--2 Disordered,<BR>disarranged;<BR>गलितकुसुमदलविलुलितकेशा Gīt. 7.<BR>--3 Waving, fickle,<BR>unsteady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलून
विलून p. p. Cut off, lopped off,<BR>clipt, cut asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोक्
विलोक् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To see, behold,<BR>look at, perceive; विलोक्य<BR>वृद्धोक्षमधिष्ठितं त्वया महाजनः स्मेरमुखो भविष्यति<BR>Ku. 5. 70; R. 2. 11; 6. 59.<BR>--2 To<BR>search for, look out for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकनं|विलोकन
विलोकनं<BR>1 Seeing, looking at,<BR>observing; Ki. 5. 16.<BR>--2 Sight,<BR>observation; Śi. 1. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोकित|विलोकितं
विलोकित p. p.<BR>1 Seen, observed,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">Page0992-a+ 57</a>]<BR>viewed, beheld.<BR>--2 Examined,<BR>thought about.<BR>--तं A look, glance;<BR>Ś. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0991-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोचनं|विलोचन
विलोचनं The eye; R. 7. 8;<BR>Ku. 4. 1, 3. 67.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंबु n.<BR>tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोम|विलोमं|विलोमः
विलोम a. (मी f.)<BR>1 Inverted,<BR>reverse, inverse, contrary, opposite.<BR>--2 Produced in the reverse order.<BR>--3<BR>Backward.<BR>--मः<BR>1 Reverse order,<BR>inversion.<BR>--2 A dog.<BR>--3 A snake.<BR>--4<BR>N. of Varuṇa.<BR>--मं A waterwheel,<BR>machine for raising water from<BR>a well.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्पन्न, --ज, --जात,<BR>--वर्ण a. ‘born in the reverse order’;<BR>i. e. born of a mother whose caste<BR>is superior to the father's; cf.<BR>प्रतिलोमज also.<BR>--क्रिया, --विधिः {1} a reverse<BR>action. {2} a rule of inversion (in<BR>math.).<BR>--जिह्वः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोमी
विलोमी The emblic myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोल|विलोलः
विलोल a.<BR>1 Shaking about,<BR>trembling, tremulous, unsteady,<BR>rolling, waving, tossing about;<BR>पृषतीषु विलोलमीक्षितं R. 8. 59;<BR>Ku. 5. 8; Śi. 8. 8, 15. 62, 20. 42;<BR>Ve. 2. 28, 24; R. 7. 41, 16. 68.<BR>--2 Loose,<BR>disordered, dishevelled (as hair);<BR>दधती विलोलकबरीकमाननं U. 3. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोलनं|विलोलन
विलोलनं<BR>1 Shaking.<BR>--2 Stirring,<BR>agitating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विलोहित|विलोहितः
विलोहित a.<BR>1 Of a purple<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Reddish, red; धनुर्धरः<BR>कोपविलोहिताक्षः R. 16. 77.<BR>--तः N. of<BR>Rudra.<BR>--ता One of the tongues of<BR>fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्ल|विल्लं
विल्ल See बिल्ल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विल्व|विल्वं|विल्वः
विल्व See बिल्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षा
विवक्षा<BR>1 A desire to speak.<BR>--2<BR>Wish, desire.<BR>--3 Meaning, sense.<BR>--4 Intention, purpose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षित|विवक्षितः
विवक्षित a.<BR>1 Intended to be said<BR>or spoken; विवक्षितं ह्यनुक्तमनुतापं<BR>जनयति Ś. 3.<BR>--2 Meant, intended,<BR>purposed.<BR>--3 Wished, desired.<BR>--4<BR>Favourite.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Purpose,<BR>intention.<BR>--2 Sense, meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवक्षु
विवक्षु a. Wishing or about to<BR>speak; पुनर्विवक्षुः स्फुरितोत्तराधरः<BR>Ku. 5. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवंचिषु|विवञ्चिषु
विवंचिषु a. Crafty, deceitful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवद्
विवद् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To quarrel,<BR>dispute; परस्परं विवदमानौ भ्रातरौ.<BR>--2<BR>To be at variance, to conflict, be in<BR>opposition; परस्परंविवदमानानां शास्त्राणां<BR>H. 1.<BR>--3 To contend (as in a court<BR>of law).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादः|विवाद
विवादः<BR>1 (a) A dispute, contest,<BR>contention, controversy, discussion,<BR>debate, quarrel, strife; अलं विवादेन<BR>Ku. 5. 82; एतयोर्विवाद एव मे न रोचते<BR>M. 1; एकप्सरःप्रार्थितयार्विवादः<BR>R. 7. 53. (b) Argument, argumentation,<BR>discussion.<BR>--2 Contradiction; एष<BR>विवाद एव प्रत्याययति Ś. 7.<BR>--3 A<BR>litigation, law-suit, contest at law;<BR>सीमाविवादः, विवादपदं &c.; (it is thus<BR>defined: --ऋणादिदायकलहे द्वयोर्बहुतरस्य वा<BR>विवादो व्यवहरश्च); see व्यवहर also.<BR>--4<BR>Crying aloud, sounding.<BR>--5 An<BR>order, a command; तस्याननादुच्चरितो<BR>विवादश्चस्खाल वेलास्वपि नार्णवानां<BR>R. 18. 43.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आर्यिन् m. {1} a<BR>litigant. {2} a plaintiff, complainant,<BR>prosecutor.<BR>--पदं a title of dispute.<BR>--वस्तु n. the subject of dispute, the<BR>matter at issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवादिन्
विवादिन् a.<BR>1 Disputing,<BR>contending, disputatious, quarrelling.<BR>--2<BR>Litigating. --m. A litigant, party<BR>in a law suit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवत्सा
विवत्सा A calfless cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवधः|विवध
विवधः<BR>1 A yoke for carrying<BR>burdens.<BR>--2 A road, high-way.<BR>--3<BR>A load, burden.<BR>--4 Storing grain.<BR>--5 A pitcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवधिकः|विवधिक
विवधिकः<BR>1 A carrier of loads,<BR>porter.<BR>--2 A pedlar, hawker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरं|विवर|विवरः
विवरं<BR>1 A fissure, hole, cavity,<BR>hollow, vacuity; यच्चकार विवरं<BR>शिलाघने ताडकोरसि स रामसायकः<BR>R. 11. 18, 9. 61, 19. 7; धीरनादभरितकर्णविवरं<BR>प्रिये मदयंतिके इति व्याहरति Māl. 7.<BR>--2<BR>An interstice, interval, intervening<BR>space; Ś. 7. 7.<BR>--3 A solitary place;<BR>Ki. 12. 37.<BR>--4 A fault, flaw, defect, weak<BR>point.<BR>--5 A breach, wound.<BR>--6 The<BR>number ‘nine’.<BR>--रः Expansion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नालिका a flute, fife<BR>--प्रवेशः entrance into a chasm (one<BR>of the means of getting one's<BR>desired object); Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्ण|विवर्णः
विवर्ण a.<BR>1 Colourless, pale, wan,<BR>pallid; नरेंद्रमार्गट्ट इव प्रपेदे विवर्णभावं<BR>स स भूमिपालः R. 6. 67.<BR>--2<BR>Discoloured, deprived of water (as a<BR>gem.); विवर्णमणीकृतं (कनकवलयं)<BR>Ś. 3. 13.<BR>--3 Low, vile.<BR>--4 Ignorant,<BR>stupid, unlettered.<BR>--र्णः An<BR>outcast, a man belonging to low caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवश|विवशः
विवश a.<BR>1 Uncontrolled,<BR>independent, unsubdued.<BR>--2 Having<BR>lost control over oneself, dependent,<BR>subject, under control (of another),<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">Page0992-c+ 56</a>]<BR>helpless; परीता रक्षोभिः श्रयति विवशा<BR>कामपि दशां Bv. 1. 83;<BR>मित्रस्नेहाद्विवशमधुना साहसे मां नियुंक्ते Mu. 6. 18;<BR>जातं जातमवश्यमाशु विवशं मृत्युः<BR>करोत्यात्मसात् Bh. 3. 105; Śi. 20. 58;<BR>H. 1. 172; Mv. 6. 32, 63.<BR>--3<BR>Insensible, not master of oneself; विवशा<BR>कामवधूर्विबोधिता Ku. 4. 1.<BR>--4 Dead,<BR>perished; उपलब्धवती दिवश्च्युतं<BR>विवशा शापनिवृत्तिकारणं R. 8. 82.<BR>--5<BR>Desirous or apprehensive of death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्
विवस् {vI.v} {c1c} P.<BR>1 To dwell abroad.<BR>--2 To live, dwell.<BR>--3 To spend,<BR>pass (time).<BR>--4 To retire,<BR>withdraw. --Caus. To banish, send into<BR>exile; Bk. 4. 35. {vII.v} {c2c} A.<BR>1<BR>To exchange clothes.<BR>--2 To wear,<BR>put on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासः|विवास
विवासः, विवासनं Banishment,<BR>sending into exile, expulsion; रामस्य<BR>गात्रमसि दुर्वहगर्भाखन्नसीताविवासनपटोः<BR>करुणा कुतस्ते U. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासनं|विवासन
विवासः, विवासनं Banishment,<BR>sending into exile, expulsion; रामस्य<BR>गात्रमसि दुर्वहगर्भाखन्नसीताविवासनपटोः<BR>करुणा कुतस्ते U. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवासित
विवासित p. p. Banished, exiled,<BR>expelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवसन|विवसनः
विवसन a. Naked, unclothed.<BR>--नः A Jaina mendicant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवस्वत्|विवस्वन्त्
विवस्वत् m.<BR>1 The sun; त्वष्टा<BR>विवस्वतमिवोल्लिलेख Ki. 17. 48, 5. 48;<BR>R. 10. 30, 17. 48.<BR>--2 N. of Aruṇa.<BR>--3<BR>N. of the present Manu.<BR>--4 A god.<BR>--5 The Arka plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवह्
विवह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To remove, take<BR>away, drive off.<BR>--2 To marry.<BR>--Caus. To give in marriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवहः|विवह
विवहः N. of one of the seven<BR>tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहः|विवाह
विवाहः Marriage; (Hindu<BR>lawgivers enumerate eight forms of<BR>marriage; ब्राह्म दैवस्तथै वार्षः<BR>प्राजापत्यस्तथासुरः । गांधर्वे राक्षसश्चैव पैशाचश्च ष्टमोऽधमः<BR>Ms. 3. 21; see Y. 1. 58-61 also;<BR>for explanation of these forms see<BR>s. v.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चतुष्टयं<BR>marrying four wives.<BR>--दीक्षा the<BR>marriage ceremony or rite; R. 3. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाहित|विवाहितः
विवाहित p. p. Married.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाह्यः|विवाह्य
विवाह्यः<BR>1 A son-in-law.<BR>--2 A<BR>bridegroom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवाकः|विवाक
विवाकः A judge; cf. प्रडविवाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवारः|विवार
विवारः<BR>1 Opening, expansion.<BR>--2 Expansion of the throat in the<BR>articulation of letters, (one of the<BR>Ābhyantara Prayatnas, opp. संवार);<BR>cf. विवृतमूष्मणां स्वराणां च Sk. on<BR>P. I. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविग्न
विविग्न a.<BR>1 Very much agitated<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-a" target="_blank">Page0993-a+ 56</a>]<BR>or terrified; R. 18. 13; Ku. 1. 56.<BR>--2 Very angry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0992-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविच्
विविच् {c3c} {c7c} U.<BR>1 To separate,<BR>divide, remove from; विविनच्मि दिवः<BR>सुरान् Bk. 6. 36.<BR>--2 To discern,<BR>discriminate.<BR>--3 To judge, ascertain,<BR>determine; रे खल तव खलु चरितं<BR>विदुषामग्रे विविच्य वक्ष्यामि Bv. 1. 108.<BR>--4<BR>To describe, treat of.<BR>--5 To tear up,<BR>rend asunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविक्त|विविक्तं
विविक्त p. p.<BR>1 Separated, detached,<BR>disjoined, abstracted.<BR>--2 Lonely,<BR>solitary, retired, sequestered.<BR>--3 Single,<BR>alone.<BR>--4 Distinguished,<BR>discriminated.<BR>--5 Judicious<BR>--6 Pure, faultless;<BR>Ratn. 1. 21.<BR>--7 Profound (as a<BR>judgment or thought).<BR>--8 Intent<BR>on.<BR>--9 Devoid of, free from;<BR>Ku. 1. 23.<BR>--क्तं<BR>1 A lonely or solitary<BR>place; विविक्तादृते नान्यदुत्सुकस्य<BR>शरणमस्ति V. 2, Ś. 5. 5, Śi. 8. 70.<BR>--2<BR>Loneliness, privacy, seclusion.<BR>--क्ता<BR>An unlucky or ill-fated woman,<BR>one disliked by her husband (<BR>दुर्भगा).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सेविन् a. seeking<BR>solitude, lonely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विविध|विविधं
विविध a. Various, diverse,<BR>manifold, multiform, sundry;<BR>Ms. 1. 8, 39.<BR>--धं A variety of action or<BR>gesture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवीतः|विवीत
विवीतः An enclosed or preserved<BR>spot of ground, such as<BR>pastureland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृ
विवृ {5} {c9c} U.<BR>1 To cover up, stop.<BR>--2 To open; Ku. 4. 26.<BR>--3 To<BR>unfold, disclose, reveal, show, display;<BR>द्वंद्वानि भावं क्रियया विवव्रुः Ku. 3. 35;<BR>N. 9. 1; Bk. 7. 73, Śi. 16. 30.<BR>--4<BR>To speak, utter; श्रवणकटु<BR>नृपाणामेकवाक्यं विवव्रुः R. 6. 85.<BR>--5 To teach,<BR>explain, expound; Mv. 2. 43.<BR>--6 To<BR>spread; Bv. 1. 5.<BR>--7 To choose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवरणं|विवरण
विवरणं<BR>1 Displaying, expressing,<BR>unfolding, opening.<BR>--2 Exposing,<BR>laying bare or open.<BR>--3 Exposition,<BR>explanation, gloss, comment,<BR>interpretation.<BR>--4 Describing,<BR>description.<BR>--5 A sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत|विवृतं
विवृत p. p.<BR>1 Displayed,<BR>manifested, expressed.<BR>--2 Evident, clear, open.<BR>--3 Uncovered, exposed, laid bare.<BR>--4 Opened, unclosed; bare, open.<BR>--5 Proclaimed.<BR>--6 Expounded,<BR>explained, commented upon.<BR>--7<BR>Expanded, spread out.<BR>--8 Extensive,<BR>large, spacious.<BR>--9 Bare, barren (as<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-b" target="_blank">Page0993-b+ 57</a>]<BR>ground).<BR>--तं Open articulation.<BR>--तं ind. Openly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a.<BR>large-eyed.<BR>--(क्षः) a cock.<BR>--द्वार a.<BR>with the gates thrown open;<BR>Ku. 4. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृतिः|विवृति
विवृतिः f.<BR>1 Display,<BR>manifestation.<BR>--2 Expansion.<BR>--3 Exposure,<BR>discovery.<BR>--4 Exposition, comment,<BR>interpretation, gloss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृज्
विवृज् {c10c} U. or Caus.<BR>1 To shun,<BR>avoid.<BR>--2 To make destitute of,<BR>deprive of.<BR>--3 To exclude.<BR>--4 To<BR>distribute, give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्जनं|विवर्जन|विवर्ज्जन
विवर्जनं Leaving, excluding,<BR>abandoning; Y. 1. 181.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्जित|विवर्ज्जित
विवर्जित p. p.<BR>1 Left, abandoned.<BR>--2 Shunned.<BR>--3 Deprived of,<BR>destitute of, without (usually in comp);<BR>Pt. 1. 34.<BR>--4 Given, distributed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृक्त
विवृक्त p. p. Left, abandoned,<BR>deserted.<BR>--क्ता A woman disliked by<BR>her husband; cf. विविक्ता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्
विवृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To turn round,<BR>roll, revolve, move round;<BR>Māl. 1. 40.<BR>--2 To turn or move about.<BR>--3<BR>To turn aside, bend;<BR>कश्चिद्विवृत्तत्रिकभिन्नहारः R. 6. 16; Ś. 2. 12.<BR>--4 To<BR>become.<BR>--5 To turn away from,<BR>depart from, return.<BR>--6 To descend.<BR>--7<BR>To attack, fall upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तः|विवर्त|विवर्त्त|विवर्त्तः
विवर्तः<BR>1 Turning round,<BR>revolving, whirling.<BR>--2 Rolling onward,<BR>moving about; Mv. 6. 26.<BR>--3<BR>Rolling back, returning.<BR>--4 Dancing.<BR>--5<BR>Alteration, modification, change of<BR>form, altered condition or state;<BR>शब्दब्रह्मणस्तादृशं विवर्तमितिहासं रामायणं<BR>प्रणिनाय U. 2; एको रसः करुण एव<BR>निमित्तभेदाद्भन्नः पृथक् पृथगिवाश्रयते<BR>विवर्तान् U. 3. 47;<BR>अकांडशुष्काशनिपातरौद्रः क एष धातुर्विषमो विवर्तः<BR>Mv. 5. 57.<BR>--6 (In Vedānta phil.) An<BR>apparent or illusory form, an unreal<BR>appearance caused by अविद्या or<BR>human error; (this is a favourite<BR>doctrine of the Vedāntins according to<BR>whom the whole visible world is a<BR>mere illusion-an unreal and<BR>illusory appearance-while Brahman or<BR>Supreme Spirit is the only real<BR>entity; as a serpent (सर्प) is a vivarta<BR>of a rope (रज्जु), so is the world a<BR>vivarta of the real entity Brahman,<BR>and the illusion is removed by<BR>Vidyā or true knowledge; cf.<BR>Bhavabhūti: --विद्याकल्पेन मरुता भेघानां<BR>भूयसामपि । ब्रह्मणीव विवर्तानां क्वापि विप्रलयः कृतः ॥<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">Page0993-c+ 56</a>]<BR>U. 6. 6).<BR>--7 A heap, multitude,<BR>collection, an assemblage.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वादः the doctrine of the<BR>Vedāntins that the visible world is<BR>illusory and Brahman alone is the real<BR>entity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तनं|विवर्तन|विवर्त्तन|विवर्त्तनं
विवर्तनं<BR>1 Revolving, revolution,<BR>whirling round.<BR>--2 Rolling about,<BR>turning round;<BR>शय्याप्रांतविवर्तनैर्विगमयत्युन्निद्र एव क्षपाः Ś. 6. 4; Ve. 2. 8,<BR>5. 40: Mv. 7. 5.<BR>--3 Rolling back,<BR>returning.<BR>--4 Rolling down,<BR>descending.<BR>--5 Existing, abiding.<BR>--6<BR>Reverential salutation.<BR>--7 Passing<BR>through various states or existences.<BR>--8 An altered condition;<BR>पुनरकांडविवर्ननदारुणो प्रविशितष्टि विधिर्तनसो रुजं<BR>U. 4. 15; Māl. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्तित|विवर्त्तित
विवर्तित p. p.<BR>1 Turned or<BR>whirled round, revolved.<BR>--2 Moved round<BR>or about, rolling; विवर्तितभ्रूरियमद्य<BR>शिक्षते Ś. 1. 23.<BR>--3 Mangled,<BR>hacked, cut to pieces; Māl. 3. 17.<BR>--4<BR>Unfolded.<BR>--5 Distorted, bent down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्त|विवृत्तं
विवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Turned round.<BR>--2<BR>Turning round, revolving, rolling,<BR>whirling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृत्तिः|विवृत्ति
विवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Turning round,<BR>whirling, revolution.<BR>--2 (In gram.) A<BR>hiatus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृध्
विवृध् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To grow, increase.<BR>--2 To thrive, prosper.<BR>--3 To spring<BR>up, arise. --Caus.<BR>1 To increase,<BR>augment.<BR>--2 To promote, advance,<BR>further.<BR>--3 To raise, elevate.<BR>--4 To<BR>gratify, exhilarate.<BR>--5 To<BR>congratulate (one) upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धनं|विवर्धन
विवर्धनं<BR>1 Increasing.<BR>--2 Increase,<BR>augmentation, growth.<BR>--3<BR>Enlargement, aggrandisement.<BR>--4<BR>Cutting, dividing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवर्धित
विवर्धित p. p.<BR>1 Increased,<BR>augmented.<BR>--2 Advanced, promoted,<BR>furthered.<BR>--3 Gratified, satisfied.<BR>--4<BR>Cut, divided.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्ध
विवृद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Grown up.<BR>--2<BR>Increased, augmented, heightened,<BR>enhanced, intensified (as grief, joy<BR>&c.).<BR>--3 Copious, large, plentiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवृद्धिः|विवृद्धि
विवृद्धिः f.<BR>1 Growth, increase,<BR>augmentation, development; ययुः<BR>शरीरावयवा विवृद्धिं R. 18. 49;<BR>विवृद्धिमत्राश्नुवते व सूनि 13. 4; so शोक˚, हर्ष˚<BR>&c.<BR>--2 Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकः|विवेक
विवेकः<BR>1 Discrimination,<BR>judgment, discernment, discretion;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-a" target="_blank">Page0994-a+ 56</a>]<BR>काश्यपि यातस्तवापि च विवेकः Bv. 1. 68,<BR>66; ज्ञातोयं जलधर तावको विवेकः 96;<BR>विवेकभ्रष्टानां भवति विनितः शतमुखः<BR>Bh. 2. 10.<BR>--2 Consideration,<BR>discussion, investigation;<BR>यच्छृगारविवेकतत्त्वमपि यत्काव्येषु लीलायित Gīt. 12,<BR>so द्वैत,˚ धर्म˚<BR>--3 Distinction,<BR>difference, discriminating (between two<BR>things); नीरक्षीरविवेके हंसालस्यं त्वमेव<BR>तनुषे चेत् Bv. 1. 13; Bk. 17. 60.<BR>--4 (In Vedānta phil.) The power<BR>of distinguishing between the<BR>visible world and the invisible spirit, or<BR>of separating reality from mere<BR>semblance or illusion.<BR>--5 True<BR>knowledge.<BR>--6 A receptacle for<BR>water, basin, reservoir.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञ a. judicious, discriminative;<BR>Pt. 1. 262, 387.<BR>--ज्ञानं the faculty<BR>of discrimination.<BR>--दृशान् m. a<BR>discerning man.<BR>--पदवी reflection,<BR>consideration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0993-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेकिन्
विवेकिन् a. Discriminating,<BR>discreet, judicious; Pt. 1. 418. --m.<BR>1<BR>A judge, discriminator.<BR>--2 A<BR>philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेक्तृ
विवेक्तृ m.<BR>1 A judge.<BR>--2 A sage,<BR>philosopher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचनं|विवेचन
विवेचनं --ना<BR>1 Discrimination.<BR>--2<BR>Discussion, consideration.<BR>--3 Settle.<BR>ment, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवेचना
विवेचनं --ना<BR>1 Discrimination.<BR>--2<BR>Discussion, consideration.<BR>--3 Settle.<BR>ment, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विवोढृ
विवोढृ m.<BR>1 A bridegroom,<BR>husband.<BR>--2 A son-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विव्वोक|विव्वोकः
विव्वोक See बिब्बोकः विव्वोकस्ते<BR>मुरविजयिनो वर्त्मपाती बभूव Ud. S. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
विश् {c6c} P. (विशति, विवेश, अविक्षत्,<BR>वेक्ष्यति, वेष्टुं, विष्ट)<BR>1 To enter, go or<BR>enter into; विवेश कश्चिज्जटिलस्तपोवनं<BR>Ku. 5. 30; R. 6. 10, Me. 102;<BR>Bg. 11. 29; so दोलायमानेत चेतसा विंतां<BR>विवेश K. 199 ‘fell a-thinking’.<BR>--2<BR>To go or come to, come into the<BR>possession of, fall to the share of;<BR>उपदा विविशुः शश्वन्नात्सेकाः कोशलेश्वरं<BR>R. 4. 70.<BR>--3 To sit or settle down<BR>upon.<BR>--4 To penetrate, pervade.<BR>--5<BR>To enter upon, undertake. --Caus.<BR>(वेशयति-ते) To cause to enter.<BR>--Desid. (विपिक्षति) To wish to<BR>enter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्
विश् m.<BR>1 A man of the third<BR>caste, a Vaiśya.<BR>--2 A man in general.<BR>--3 People. --f.<BR>1 People, subjects.<BR>--2 A daughter.<BR>--3 Ved. Entrance.<BR>--4 A family, tribe, race.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पण्यं goods, merchandise.<BR>--पतिः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">Page0994-b+ 55</a>]<BR>(also विशांपतिः) {1} a king, lord of<BR>subjects. {2} a son-in-law. {3} a<BR>head-merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशं|विश
विशं The fibres of the stalk of a<BR>lotus; cf. बिस.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आकरः a<BR>kind of plant (भद्रवूड).<BR>--कठा a<BR>crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशंक्|विशङ्क्
विशंक् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To suspect, fear,<BR>have doubts or suspicions about;<BR>विशंकसे भीरु यताऽवधीरणां Ś. 3. 14.<BR>सतीमपि ज्ञातिकुलैकसंश्रयां जनोऽन्यथा<BR>भर्तृमतीं विशकते 5. 17.<BR>--2 To think to<BR>be, fancy, imagine, विशंकमाना रमितं<BR>कयापि जनार्दनं दृष्टवदेतदाह Gīt. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशंक|विशङ्क|विशङ्कः
विशंक a. Fearless.<BR>--का Fear,<BR>suspicion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशंकट|विशङ्कट|विशङ्कटः
विशंकट a. (टा-टी f.)<BR>1 Great,<BR>large, big; विशंकटो वक्षासि बाण<BR>पाणिः Bk. 2. 50, Śi. 13. 34.<BR>--2<BR>Strong, vehement, powerful.<BR>--टं<BR>ind. Vehemently, intensely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशद|विशदः
विशद a.<BR>1 Clear, pure, pellucid,<BR>clean, spotless; योगनिद्रातविशदैः<BR>पावनैरवलोकनैः R. 10. 14, 19. 39; 8. 3<BR>प्रणयविशदा दृष्टिं वक्त्रे ददाति न शंकि<BR>ता Ratn. 3. 9. Ki. 5. 12.<BR>--2<BR>White, of a pure, white colour;<BR>निर्धौतहारगुलिकाविशदं हिमांभः<BR>R. 5. 70; Ku. 1. 44. 6. 25, Śi. 9. 26,<BR>Ki. 4. 23.<BR>--3 Bright, shining,<BR>beautiful; Ku. 3. 33; Śi. 8. 70.<BR>--4 Clear, evident, manifest.<BR>--5<BR>Calm, free from anxiety, at ease:<BR>जातो ममायं विशदः प्रकामं (अंतरात्मा)<BR>Ś. 4. 21, V. 3.<BR>--दः The white<BR>colour. (विशदीकृ {c8c} U. ‘to<BR>explain make clear, illustrate’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशयः|विशय
विशयः<BR>1 Doubt, uncertainty,<BR>the second of the five members of<BR>an Adhikaraṇa, q. v.<BR>--2 Refuge,<BR>asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशरः|विशर
विशरः<BR>1 Splitting, bursting.<BR>--2<BR>Slaughter, killing, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशल्य|विशल्यः
विशल्य a.<BR>1 Free from trouble<BR>or anxiety, secure.<BR>--2 Free from<BR>thorns or darts.<BR>--ल्या N. of<BR>several plants:<BR>--दंती, गुडूवी, अजमोदा &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्
विशस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To cut up, kill;<BR>U. 4.<BR>--2 To immolate, sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशसनं|विशसन|विशसनः
विशसनं<BR>1 Killing, slaughter,<BR>immolation; तस्यास्त्वं दुहितुस्तथा<BR>विशसनं किं दारुणेऽमृष्यथाः U. 4. 5.<BR>--2<BR>Ruin.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A sabre, crooked<BR>sword.<BR>--2 A sword in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त|विशस्तः
विशस्त p. p.<BR>1 Cut up, hacked.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">Page0994-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 Rude, ill-mannered.<BR>--3 Praised,<BR>celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्तृ
विशस्तृ m.<BR>1 An immolator.<BR>--2 A<BR>Cāṇḍāla.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशस्त्र
विशस्त्र a. Weaponless, unarmed,<BR>defenceless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखः|विशाख
विशाखः<BR>1 N. of Kārtikeya.<BR>Mv. 2. 38.<BR>--2 An attitude in<BR>shooting (in which the archer stands<BR>with the feet a span apart).<BR>--3 A<BR>beggar, petitioner.<BR>--4 A spindle,<BR>--5 N. of Śiva.<BR>--6 N. of a god,<BR>frequently mentioned by Pāṇini<BR>and Patañjali along with Skanda;<BR>e. g. see Mbh. on P. VI. 3. 26,<BR>VIII. 1. 15.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः the<BR>orange tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखल|विशाखलं
विशाखल See विशाख (2).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखा
विशाखा (usually in the dual)<BR>N. of the 16th lunar mansion<BR>consisting of two stars; किमत्र<BR>चित्रं यदि विशाखे शशांकलेखामनुवर्तेते<BR>Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशातनं|विशातन|विशातनः
विशातनं<BR>1 Rending asunder,<BR>cutting off.<BR>--2 Setting free, delivering,<BR>releasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशायः|विशाय
विशायः Sleeping in rotation,<BR>the rest enjoyed in rotation by the<BR>sentinels on watch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारणं|विशारण
विशारणं<BR>1 Splitting, rending.<BR>--2 Killing, slaughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशारद|विशारदः
विशारद a.<BR>1 Clever, skilful or<BR>proficient in, versed in, conversant<BR>with (usually in comp.);<BR>मधुदानविशारदाः R. 9. 29, 8. 17.<BR>--2<BR>Learned, wise.<BR>--3 Famous, celebrated.<BR>--4 Bold, confident.<BR>--दः The<BR>Bakula tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाल|विशालः
विशाल a.<BR>1 Large, great,<BR>extensive, spacious, broad, wide;<BR>गृहैर्विशालैरपि भूरिशालैः Śi. 3. 50;<BR>रथचरणविशालश्र णिलोलेक्षणेन 11. 23, 17. 47;<BR>R. 2. 21. 6. 32, Bg. 9. 21.<BR>--2 Rich or abounding in: श्रीविशालां<BR>विशालां Me. 30.<BR>--3 Eminent,<BR>illustrious, great, noble, celebrated.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A kind of deer.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of bird.<BR>--ला<BR>1 N. of the town<BR>Ujjayinī; पूर्वोद्दिष्टामनुसर पुरीं श्रीविशालां<BR>विशालां Me. 30.<BR>--2 N. of a river.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a. large-eyed.<BR>--(क्षः) {1} N. of Viṣṇu. {2} of<BR>Garuḍa. {3} an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--(क्षी) an epithet of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालता
विशालता --त्वं<BR>1 Greatness,<BR>magnitude.<BR>--2 Eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशालत्वं|विशालत्व
विशालता --त्वं<BR>1 Greatness,<BR>magnitude.<BR>--2 Eminence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0994-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिख|विशिखः
विशिख a. Crownless, crestless,<BR>pointless.<BR>--खः<BR>1 An arrow; माधव<BR>मनसिजविशिखभयादिव भावनया त्वयि<BR>लीना Gīt. 4; R. 5. 50; Mv. 2. 38.<BR>--2 A kind of reed.<BR>--3 An iron<BR>crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिखा
विशिखा<BR>1 A spade.<BR>--2 A spindle.<BR>--3 A needle or pin.<BR>--4 A minute<BR>arrow.<BR>--5 A highway.<BR>--6 A barber's<BR>wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशित
विशित a. Sharp, acute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिपं|विशिप
विशिपं<BR>1 A temple.<BR>--2 An<BR>abode, a house.<BR>--3 A palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्
विशिष् {c7c} P.<BR>1 To particularize,<BR>individualize, specify, define.<BR>--2<BR>To distinguish, discriminate.<BR>--3<BR>To aggravate, heighten, enhance,<BR>intensify; पुनरकांडविवर्तनदारुणो<BR>विधिरहो विशिनाष्टि मनोरुजं Māl. 4. 7;<BR>U. 4. 15.<BR>--4 To surpass, excel;<BR>विशेषको वा विशिशेष यस्याः श्रियं<BR>त्रिलोकीतिलकः स एव Śi. 3. 63. --Pass.<BR>1 To be different from R. 17. 62.<BR>--2 To be better or higher than,<BR>surpass, excel, be preferable or<BR>superior to (often with abl.); तस्माद्दुर्गं<BR>विशिष्यते H. 3. 50; Mv. 7. 39;<BR>मौनात् सत्यं विशिष्यते Ms. 2. 83;<BR>3. 203; (also with instr and gen.);<BR>सर्वेषामेव दानानां ब्रह्मदानं विशिष्यते<BR>Ms. 4. 233. --Caus.<BR>1 To distinguish,<BR>particularize.<BR>--2 To surpass, excel.<BR>मदनमपि गुणैर्विशेषयंती Mk. 4. 4;<BR>M. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्ट|विशिष्टः
विशिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Distinguished,<BR>distinct.<BR>--2 Particular, special,<BR>peculiar, distinctive.<BR>--3 Characterized<BR>by, endowed with, possessed of,<BR>having.<BR>--4 Superior, best (of all),<BR>eminent, excellent, choice; विशिष्टाया<BR>विशेषेण संगमो गुणवान् भवेत् Mb.<BR>--ष्टः<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद्वैतवादः a doctrine of Rāmānuja which<BR>regards Brahman and Prakṛti<BR>as identical and real entities.<BR>--बुद्धिः f. a distinguishing<BR>knowledge, differentiation.<BR>--वर्ण a. of<BR>an eminent or excellent colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशिष्टता
विशिष्टता<BR>1 Distinction,<BR>speciality.<BR>--2 Excellence, superiority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष|विशेषः
विशेष a.<BR>1 Peculiar.<BR>--2<BR>Copious, abundant; आसीद्विशेषा<BR>फलपुष्पवृष्टिः R. 2. 14.<BR>--षः<BR>1<BR>Discrimination, distinguishing between.<BR>--2<BR>Distinction, difference; निर्विशेषो<BR>विशेषः Bh. 3. 50.<BR>--3 Characteristic<BR>difference, peculiar mark, special<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-b" target="_blank">Page0995-b+ 57</a>]<BR>property, speciality, differentia; oft.<BR>in comp. and translated by ‘special’<BR>‘peculiar’ &c.; Ś. 6. 5.<BR>--4 A<BR>favourable turn or crisis in sickness,<BR>a change for the better; अस्ति मे<BR>विशेषः Ś. 3 ‘I feel better’.<BR>--5 A<BR>limb, member; पुपोष लावण्यमयान्<BR>विशेष न् Ku. 1. 25.<BR>--6 A species,<BR>sort, variety, kind, mode (usually<BR>at the end of comp.); भूतविशेषः<BR>U. 4. परिमलविशेषान् Pt. 1: कदलीविशेषाः<BR>Ku. 1. 36.<BR>--7 A different or<BR>various object, various particulars (pl.);<BR>प्रामादस्त्वां तुलयितुमलं यत्र तैस्तैर्विशेषैः<BR>Me. 64, 57.<BR>--8 Excellence,<BR>superiority, distinction; usually at the<BR>end of comp. and translated by<BR>‘excellent’, ‘distinguished’,<BR>‘pre-eminent’, ‘choice’, &c.; अनुभावविशेषात्तु<BR>R. 1. 37; वपुर्विशेषेषु Ku. 5. 31;<BR>R. 2. 7, 6. 5; Ki. 9. 58; so<BR>आकृतिविशेषाः ‘excellent forms’, अतिथिविशेषः<BR>‘a distinguished guest’ &c.<BR>--9 A<BR>peculiar attribute, the eternal<BR>distinguishing nature of each of the<BR>nine dravyas; अयमस्माद् व्यावृत्त इति<BR>व्यावृत्तिबुद्धिमात्रहंतुर्विशेषः Tarka K.<BR>(these viśeshas are said to inhere in<BR>the atoms of the Earth, Water,<BR>Lignt, and Air and the five eternal<BR>substances, Ether, Time, Space, Soul<BR>and Mind.).<BR>--10 (a)<BR>Individuality, particularity. (b) A particular<BR>instance; उक्तिरर्थांतरन्यासः<BR>स्यात्सामान्यविशेषयोः.<BR>--11 A category,<BR>predicament.<BR>--12 A mark on the forehead<BR>with sandal, saffron &c.<BR>--13 A<BR>word which limits or qualifies the<BR>sense of another; see विशेषण.<BR>--14 N.<BR>of the mundane egg.<BR>--15 (In Rhet.)<BR>A figure of speech, said to be of<BR>three kinds; it is thus defined by<BR>Mammaṭa: --विना प्रसिद्धमाधारमाधेयस्य<BR>व्यवस्थितिः । एकात्मा युगपद्वृत्तिरेकस्मानेकगोच<BR>रा । अन्यत्प्रकुर्वतः कार्यमशक्यान्यस्य वस्तुनः ।<BR>तथैव करणं चेति विशेषस्त्रिविधः स्मृतः ॥<BR>K. P. 10.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिदेशः a special<BR>supplementary rule, special<BR>extended application.<BR>--उक्तिः f. a figure<BR>of speech in which an effect is<BR>represented as not taking place though<BR>the usual necessary causes exist;<BR>विशेषोक्तिरखंडेषु का णेषु फलावचः<BR>K. P. 10; e. g. हृदि स्नेहक्षयो नाभूत् स्मरदीपे<BR>ज्वलत्यपि.<BR>--गुणः {1} a special or<BR>distinguishing property. {2} (in phil.) such guṇa<BR>as is not produced (like संयोग, पृथक्त्व<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">Page0995-c+ 57</a>]<BR>&c). by the union of two things.<BR>--ज्ञ<BR>विद् a. {1} knowing distinctions,<BR>critical, connoisseur. {2} learned,<BR>wise; Bh. 2. 3.<BR>--लक्षणं, --लिंगं a<BR>special or characteristic mark.<BR>--वचनं<BR>a special text or precept.<BR>--विधिः,<BR>शास्त्रं a special rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषक|विशेषकः
विशेषक a. Distinguishing,<BR>distinctive.<BR>--कः, --कं<BR>1 A<BR>distinguishing feature or characteristic, an<BR>attribute.<BR>--2 A discriminative or<BR>distinguishing quality.<BR>--3 A mark<BR>on the forehead with sandal,<BR>saffron &c.; M. 3. 5.<BR>--4 Drawing<BR>lines of painting on the face and<BR>person with coloured unguents and<BR>cosmetics; स्वेदोद्गमः किंपुरुषांगनानां<BR>चक्र पदं पत्रविशेषकेषु Ku. 3. 33,<BR>R. 9. 29, Śi. 3. 63, 10. 84.<BR>--कं A<BR>group of three stanzas forming one<BR>grammatical sentence; द्वाभ्यां युग्ममिति<BR>प्राक्तं त्रिभिः श्लोकैर्विशेषकम् । कलापकं<BR>चतुर्भिः स्यात्तदूर्ध्वं कुलकं स्मृतम् ॥.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषण|विशेषणं
विशेषण a.<BR>1 Attributive.<BR>--2<BR>Distinctive.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Distinguishing,<BR>discrimination.<BR>--2 Distinction,<BR>difference.<BR>--3 A word which<BR>particularizes, qualifies, or defines<BR>another, an adjective, attribute,<BR>epithet (opp. विशेष्य); उपपन्नमिदं<BR>विशेषणं वायोः V. 3;<BR>विशेषणैर्यत्साकूतैरुक्तिः परिकरस्तु सः K. P. 10. (विशेषण<BR>is said to be of three kinds व्यावर्तक,<BR>विधेय, and हेतुगर्भ).<BR>--4 A<BR>distinguishing feature or mark.<BR>--5 Species,<BR>kind.<BR>--6 Surpassing, excelling;<BR>अस्य काव्यस्य कवयो न समर्था विशेषणे<BR>Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषतस्
विशेषतस्, विशेषेण, विशेषात् ind.<BR>Especially, particularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषेण
विशेषतस्, विशेषेण, विशेषात् ind.<BR>Especially, particularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषात्
विशेषतस्, विशेषेण, विशेषात् ind.<BR>Especially, particularly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषित|विशेषितं
विशेषित p. p.<BR>1 Distinguished.<BR>--2 Defined, particularized.<BR>--3<BR>Distinguished by an attribute.<BR>--4<BR>Superior, excellent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेष्य|विशेष्यः
विशेष्य, विशेषणीय a.<BR>1 To be<BR>distinguished.<BR>--2 Chief, superior.<BR>--ष्यं The word qualified or limited<BR>by an adjective, the object to be<BR>defined or particularized by<BR>another word; a noun; विशेष्यं नाभिधा<BR>गच्छेत्क्षीणशक्तिर्विशेषणे K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशेषणीय
विशेष्य, विशेषणीय a.<BR>1 To be<BR>distinguished.<BR>--2 Chief, superior.<BR>--ष्यं The word qualified or limited<BR>by an adjective, the object to be<BR>defined or particularized by<BR>another word; a noun; विशेष्यं नाभिधा<BR>गच्छेत्क्षीणशक्तिर्विशेषणे K. P. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशील
विशील a. Ill-behaved, immoral,<BR>wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुध्
विशुध् {c4c} P. To be purified.<BR>--Caus. To purify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्ध|विशुद्धं
विशुद्ध a.<BR>1 Purified, cleansed.<BR>--2 Pure, free from vice, sin, or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">Page0996-a+ 55</a>]<BR>imperfection.<BR>--3 Spotless, stainless.<BR>--4 Correct, accurate.<BR>--5 Virtuous,<BR>pious, straightforward; विशुद्धमुग्धः<BR>कुलकन्यकाजनः Māl. 7. 1.<BR>--6<BR>Humble<BR>--द्धं A kind of mystical circle<BR>(चक्र) in the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0995-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशुद्धिः|विशुद्धि
विशुद्धिः f.<BR>1 Purification;<BR>तदंगसंसर्गमवाप्य कल्पते ध्रुवं चिताभस्मग्जो<BR>विशुद्धये Ku. 5. 79, Bg. 6. 12;<BR>Ms. 6. 69, 11. 54.<BR>--2 Purity, complete<BR>purity; हेम्नः संलक्ष्यते ह्यग्नौ विशुद्धिः<BR>श्यामिकापि वा R. 1. 10, 12. 48.<BR>--3<BR>Correctness, accuracy.<BR>--4<BR>Rectification, removal of error.<BR>--5<BR>Similarity, equality.<BR>--6 (In alg.) A<BR>subtractive quantity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोधनं|विशोधन
विशोधनं<BR>1 Cleaning, clearing<BR>(fig. also); राज्यकंटकविशोधनोद्यतः<BR>Vikr. 5. 1.<BR>--2 Purifying, freeing<BR>from sin, defect &c.<BR>--3 Expiation,<BR>atonement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोध्य
विशोध्य a. To be purified,<BR>cleansed or corrected.<BR>--ध्यं A debt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशूल
विशूल a. Without(i. e. not<BR>possessing) a spear; दुर्जपो लवणः<BR>शूली विशूलः प्रार्थ्यतामिति R. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशृंखल|विशृङ्खल|विशृङ्खलः
विशृंखल a.<BR>1 Without fetters<BR>(lit.).<BR>--2 Unfettered, unchecked,<BR>unrestrained, uncurbed (fig.);<BR>Śi. 12. 7; Bv. 2. 177.<BR>--3 Free from all<BR>moral bonds, dissolute, Bh. 2. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशॄ
विशॄ Pass.<BR>1 To be split in<BR>pieces, be shattered, विशीर्येत वनेऽथ<BR>वा.<BR>--2 To crumble to pieces, be<BR>dissolved, decay.<BR>--3 To waste away,<BR>become emaciated.<BR>--4 To vanish,<BR>disappear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशीर्ण|विशीर्णः
विशीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Shattered, broken<BR>to pieces.<BR>--2 Decayed, withered.<BR>--3 Dropped or fallen down;<BR>Ku. 5. 28.<BR>--4 Shrunk, shrivelled.<BR>--5<BR>Impaired, wasted, spoiled.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पर्णः the Nimba tree.<BR>--मूर्ति a.<BR>having the body destroyed;<BR>Ku. 5. 54.<BR>--(र्तिः) an epithet of the god<BR>of love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोक|विशोकः
विशोक a. Free from grief,<BR>happy.<BR>--कः The Aśoka tree.<BR>--का<BR>Exemption from grief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशोषणं|विशोषण
विशोषणं Drying up,<BR>dessication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्चकद्रः|विश्चकद्र
विश्चकद्रः Ved.<BR>1 A dog-dealer.<BR>--2 A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्नः|विश्न
विश्नः Lustre, splendour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रण्
विश्रण् {c10c} U. To give away,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">Page0996-b+ 56</a>]<BR>bestow; निःशेषविश्राणितकोशजातं R. 5. 1;<BR>14. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रणनं|विश्रणन
विश्रणनं, विश्राणतं Giving away,<BR>bestowing, grant, gift, donation;<BR>विश्राणनाच्चान्यपयस्विनीनां R. 2. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्राणतं
विश्रणनं, विश्राणतं Giving away,<BR>bestowing, grant, gift, donation;<BR>विश्राणनाच्चान्यपयस्विनीनां R. 2. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रम्
विश्रम् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To take rest,<BR>repose, stop; Ku. 3. 9.<BR>--2 To cease,<BR>stop, come to an end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रमः|विश्रम
विश्रमः<BR>1 Rest, repose.<BR>--2<BR>Relaxation, cessation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रांत|विश्रान्त|विश्रान्तः
विश्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Ceased, stopped;<BR>V. 4. 38.<BR>--2 Rested, reposed<BR>--3<BR>Calm, tranquil, composed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रांतिः|विश्रान्ति|विश्रांति|विश्रान्तिः
विश्रांतिः f.<BR>1 Rest, repose.<BR>--2<BR>Cessation, stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रामः|विश्राम
विश्रामः<BR>1 Cessation, stop.<BR>--2 Rest,<BR>repose; विश्रामो हृदयस्य यत्र<BR>U. 1. 39.<BR>--3 Tranquillity, calm,<BR>composure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रंभ्|विश्रम्भ्
विश्रंभ् {c1c} A. To confide, place<BR>confidence in; see विश्रब्ध below.<BR>--Caus. To inspire confidence in (a<BR>person), console, encourage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रब्ध|विश्रब्धः
विश्रब्ध p. p. (also written<BR>विस्रब्ध)<BR>1 Confided in, confided to,<BR>entrusted.<BR>--2 Confident, fearless,<BR>confiding; Mu. 3. 3.<BR>--3 Trusty,<BR>confidential.<BR>--4 Quiet, calm,<BR>tranquil, free from anxiety.<BR>--5 Firm,<BR>steady.<BR>--6 Meek, lowly.<BR>--7<BR>Excessive, exceeding.<BR>--ब्धं ind.<BR>Confidently, fearlessly, without reserve,<BR>fear, or hesitation; विश्रब्धं क्रियतां<BR>वराहततिभिर्मुस्ताक्षतिः पल्ले Ś. 2. 6;<BR>वृषल विश्रब्धं पृच्छ ममापि वह्वाख्येयमत्र<BR>Mu. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रंभः|विश्रम्भ|विश्रंभ|विश्रम्भः
विश्रंभः<BR>1 Trust, confidence,<BR>familiar confidence, perfect intimacy or<BR>familiarity; विश्रंमादुरसि निपत्य<BR>लब्धनिद्रां U. 1. 49; Māl. 3. 1.<BR>--2 A<BR>confidential matter, secret;<BR>विश्रभेष्वभ्यंतरीकरणीया K.<BR>--3 Rest,<BR>relaxation.<BR>--4 An affectionate inquiry.<BR>--5<BR>A love-quarrel, an amorous dispute.<BR>--6 Killing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आलापः,<BR>--भाषणं confidential or familiar<BR>conversation.<BR>--पात्रं, --भूमिः, --स्थानं an<BR>object of confidence, a confidant,<BR>trusty person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रंभिन्|विश्रम्भिन्
विश्रंभिन् a.<BR>1 Trusting, confiding.<BR>--2 Trustworthy, faithful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रंभणं|विश्रम्भण
विश्रंभणं Winning confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रयः|विश्रय
विश्रयः A shelter, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रवस्
विश्रवस् m. N. of a son of<BR>Pulastya, and father of Rāvaṇa,<BR>Kumbhakarṇa, Bibhīṣaṇa and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">Page0996-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Śūrpaṇakhā by his wife Kaikasī, and of<BR>Kubera by his wife Iḍaviḍā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रावः|विश्राव
विश्रावः<BR>1 Dropping, flowing<BR>forth (for विस्राव q. v.).<BR>--2<BR>Celebrity, renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुत|विश्रुतः
विश्रुत p. p.<BR>1 Well-known,<BR>renowned, celebrated.<BR>--2 Pleased,<BR>delighted, happy.<BR>--3 Flowing<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्रुतिः|विश्रुति
विश्रुतिः f.<BR>1 Fame, celebrity.<BR>--2<BR>Flowing, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लथ
विश्लथ a.<BR>1 Loose, relaxed,<BR>untied; R. 6. 73.<BR>--2 Languid.<BR>drooping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लिष्
विश्लिष् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be separated,<BR>to be away from.<BR>--2 To burst, fly<BR>asunder; R. 12. 76; Bk. 14. 67.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 to separate; Me. 7.<BR>--2 To<BR>deprive of (instr.); बुद्ध्या<BR>विश्लेषयंति ते Pt. 3. 183.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लिष्ट
विश्लिष्ट p. p. Disjoined, separated,<BR>disunited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषः|विश्लेष
विश्लेषः<BR>1 Disunion, disjunction.<BR>--2 Especially separation of lovers,<BR>or of husband and wife.<BR>--3<BR>Separation (in general); तनयाविश्लेषदुःखैः<BR>Ś. 4. 5; चरणारविंदविश्लेष R. 13. 23.<BR>--4 Absence, loss, bereavement.<BR>--5<BR>A chasm.<BR>--6 (In arith.) The<BR>converse of addition.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जातिः<BR>f. the reduction of fractional<BR>difference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्लेषित
विश्लेषित p. p. Severed, separated,<BR>disunited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्व|विश्वं|विश्वः
विश्व pron. a. [विश्-व Uṇ. 1. 151]<BR>1 All, whole, entire, universal.<BR>--2<BR>Every, every one. --m. pl. N. of a<BR>particular group of deities, ten in<BR>number and supposed to be sons of<BR>विश्वा; their names are:<BR>--वसुः सत्यः<BR>क्रतुर्दक्षः कालः कामो धृतिः कुरुः । पुरूरवा<BR>माद्रायाश्च विश्वेदेवाः प्रकीर्तिताः ॥.<BR>--श्वं<BR>1 The<BR>universe, the (whole) world; इदं<BR>विश्वं पाल्यं U. 3. 30; विश्वस्मिन्नधुनान्यः<BR>कुलव्रतं पालयिष्यति कः Bv. 1. 13.<BR>--2<BR>Dry ginger.<BR>--3 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--श्वः<BR>1 The soul.<BR>--2 A citizen (नागर).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् m. {1} the Supreme<BR>Being (soul of the universe). {2}<BR>an epithet of Brahman. {3} of Śiva;<BR>अथ विश्व त्मने गौरी संदिदेश मिथः सखीं<BR>Ku. 6. 1. {4} of Viṣṇu.<BR>--ईशः --ई<BR>श्वरः {1} the Supreme Being, lord of the<BR>universe. {2} an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--कद्रु<BR>a. wicked, low, vile.<BR>--(द्रुः) {1} a hound,<BR>dog trained for the chase. {2} sound.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-a" target="_blank">Page0997-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--कर्मन् m. {1} N. of the architect<BR>of gods; cf. त्वष्टृ. {2} an epithet of<BR>the sun. {3} one of the seven<BR>principal rays of the sun. {4} a great<BR>saint. {5} the supreme being. ˚जा,<BR>˚सुता an epithet of संज्ञा, one of the<BR>wives of the sun.<BR>--कार्यः one of the<BR>rays of the sun.<BR>--कृत् m. {1} the<BR>creator of all beings. {2} an epithet<BR>of Viśvakarman.<BR>--केतुः an epithet<BR>of Aniruddha.<BR>--गः N. of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--गंधः an onion.<BR>--(धं) myrrh.<BR>--गंधा the earth.<BR>--गोप्तृ m. {1} N. of<BR>Viṣṇu. {2} Indra.<BR>--ग्रंथिः the plant<BR>called हंसपदी.<BR>--चक्रं a kind of<BR>valuable gift (महादान) of pure gold.<BR>--चर्षणि a. Ved. all-pervading,<BR>world-wide, extending everywhere.<BR>--जनं mankind.<BR>--जनीन, --जन्य,<BR>--जनीय a. good for all men, suitable to<BR>all mankind, beneficial to all men;<BR>Bk. 2. 41, 21. 17.<BR>--जित् m. {1} N.<BR>of a particular sacrifice; R. 5. 1.<BR>{2} the noose of Varuṇa. {3} N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--देव see under विश्व m. above.<BR>--धारिणी the earth.<BR>--धारिन् m. a<BR>deity.<BR>--धेना Ved. the earth.<BR>--नाथः<BR>lord of the universe, an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--मा m. {1} the protector of all.<BR>{2} the sun. {3} the moon. {4} fire.<BR>--पावनी, --पूजिता holy basil.<BR>--प्सन्<BR>m. {1} a god. {2} the sun. {3} the<BR>moon. {4} an epithet of Agni. {5}<BR>N. of Viśvakarman.<BR>--बोधः a<BR>Buddha.<BR>--भावनः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--भुज<BR>a. all enjoying, all-eating. (--m.) an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>--भेषजं dry ginger.<BR>--(जः) a universal remedy.<BR>--मूर्ति<BR>a. existing in all forms,<BR>all-pervading, omnipresent; Māl. 1. 3.<BR>--(र्तिः)<BR>{1} the supreme being. {2} N. of<BR>Śiva<BR>--योनिः {1} an epithet of<BR>Brahman. {2} of Viṣṇu.<BR>--राज् m.<BR>--राजः a<BR>universal sovereign.<BR>--रुची one of<BR>the seven tongues of fire.<BR>--रूप a.<BR>omnipresent, existing everywhere.<BR>--(पः) an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--(पं)<BR>agallochum.<BR>--रेतस् m. an epithet of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--वाह् a. (विश्वौही f.)<BR>allsustaining.<BR>--वेदस् a. {1}<BR>all-knowing, omniscient. {2} a saint, sage.<BR>--व्यचस् f. N. of Aditi.<BR>--व्यापक,<BR>व्यपिन् a. all-pervading.<BR>--सहा {1} the<BR>earth. {2} one of the tongues of fire.<BR>--सारकं the prickly pear.<BR>--सृज् m.<BR>an epithet of Brahman, the creator;<BR>प्रायेण सामग्र्यविधौ गुणानां पराङ्मुखी<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">Page0997-b+ 56</a>]<BR>विश्वसृजः प्रवृत्तिः Ku. 3. 28; 1. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0996-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वंकरः|विश्वङ्कर|विश्वंकर|विश्वङ्करः
विश्वंकरः The eye (n. according<BR>to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वतस्
विश्वतस् ind. On all sides, all<BR>round, everywhere; Bv. 1. 30.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुख a. having a face on<BR>every side; Bg. 9. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वथा
विश्वथा ind. Everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वदानीं
विश्वदानीं ind. Ved. At all times.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वंभर|विश्वम्भर|विश्वंभरः|विश्वम्भरः
विश्वंभर a. All-sustaining.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>The all-pervading being, the<BR>Supreme Spirit<BR>--2 An epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 Of Indra.<BR>--रा The earth;<BR>विश्वंभरा भगवती भवतीमसूत U. 1. 9;<BR>विश्वंभराप्यतिलघुनर्रनाथ तवांतिके नियतं<BR>K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वयुः|विश्वयु
विश्वयुः Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वह
विश्वह ind. At all times.<BR>--हा ind.<BR>Everywhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वस्
विश्वस् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To confide in,<BR>trust, rely on, place confidence in<BR>(usually with loc.); पुंसि<BR>विश्वसिति कुव कुमरी N. 5. 110; न जानामि<BR>केनापि कारणेनापहस्तितसकलसखीजनं<BR>त्वयि विश्वसिति मे हृदयं K. 233;<BR>Ku. 5. 15; (sometimes with gen. also).<BR>--2 To rest secure, be fearless or<BR>confident; विशश्वसे पक्षिगणैः समंतात्<BR>Bk. 2. 25. --Caus. To cause to believe,<BR>inspire confidence in; ऋते<BR>क्रौर्यात्समायातो मां विश्वासयितुं नु किं<BR>Bk. 8. 105; Pt. 1. 192.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वसनीय
विश्वसनीय pot. p.<BR>1 To be relied<BR>upon, trustworthy, reliable.<BR>--2 Capable of<BR>inspiring confidence; अहो दोप्तिमतोऽपि<BR>विश्वसनीयतास्य वपुषः Ś. 2; M. 3. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वस्त|विश्वस्तः
विश्वस्त p. p.<BR>1 Believed in,<BR>trusted, relied on.<BR>--2<BR>Confiding, relying on.<BR>--3 Fearless,<BR>confident.<BR>--4 Trustworthy, reliable.<BR>--स्ता A widow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासः|विश्वास
विश्वासः<BR>1 Trust, confidence, faith,<BR>reliance; दुर्जनः प्रियवादीति<BR>नैतद्विश्वासकारणं; Ś. 1. 14; R. 1. 51, H. 4. 103.<BR>--2 A secret, confidential<BR>communication.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--घातः, --भंगः breach of<BR>faith, treachery, perfidy.<BR>--घातकः,<BR>--घातिन् m. a treacherous fellow,<BR>traitor.<BR>--पात्रं, --भूमिः --स्थानं an object<BR>of confidence, a reliable or trusty<BR>person, a confidant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वासनं|विश्वासन
विश्वासनं Producing confidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वाधायस्
विश्वाधायस् m. A god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वानरः|विश्वानर
विश्वानरः An epithet of Savitṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वामित्रः|विश्वामित्र
विश्वामित्रः [विश्वं मित्रं यस्य,<BR>विश्वस्य मित्रं वा पूर्वपददीर्घः; P. VI. 3. 130]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-c" target="_blank">Page0997-c+ 61</a>]<BR>N. of a celebrated sage. [He was<BR>originally a Kṣatriya, being the king<BR>of Kanyakubja and son of Gādhi. One<BR>day while out hunting, he went to the<BR>hermitage of the great sage Vasiṣṭha,<BR>and seeing there the cow of plenty,<BR>offered him untold treasures in<BR>exchange for it, but being refused he<BR>tried to take it by force. A long<BR>contest thereupon ensued, in which king<BR>Viśvāmitra was signally defeated; and<BR>so great was his vexation, and withal<BR>so greatly was he impressed with the<BR>power inherent in Brāhmanism that he<BR>devoted himself to the most rigorous<BR>austerities till he successively got the<BR>titles Rājarṣi, Ṛṣi, Maharṣi, and<BR>Brahmarṣi, but he was not<BR>contented till Vasiṣṭha himself called him by<BR>the name Brahmarṣi, which, however,<BR>took place after several thousands of<BR>years. Viśvāmitra several times tried<BR>to excite Vasiṣṭha-for example by<BR>killing his one hundred sons-but the<BR>great sage was not in the least<BR>perturbed. His power, even before he<BR>finally became a Brahmarṣi, was very great,<BR>as was seen in his transporting<BR>Triśanku to the skies, in saving<BR>Śunahśepha from the hands of Indra, in<BR>creating things after the style of<BR>Brahman &c. &c. He was the companion<BR>and counsellor of young Rāma to whom<BR>he gave several miraculous missiles].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वाराज्
विश्वाराज् m. [विश्वस्य राजा] A<BR>king of the universe, universal<BR>monarch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विश्वावसुः|विश्वावसु
विश्वावसुः N. of a Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
विष् {vI.v} {c3c} U. (वेवेष्टि, वेविष्टे, --विष्ट)<BR>1<BR>To surround.<BR>--2 To spread through,<BR>extend, pervade.<BR>--3 To embrace.<BR>--4<BR>To accomplish, effect, perform.<BR>--5<BR>To eat.<BR>--6 To go to, go against,<BR>encounter; (not generally used in<BR>classical literature). {vII.v} {c9c} P. (<BR>विष्णाति) To separate, disjoin. {vIII.v} {c1c} P.<BR>(वेषति) To sprinkle, pour out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विष्
विष् f.<BR>1 Feces, excrement,<BR>ordure.<BR>--2 Spreading, diffusion.<BR>--3 A<BR>girl, as in विट्पति.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारिका<BR>(विट्कारिका) a kind of bird.<BR>--ग्रहः<BR>(विड्ग्रहः) constipation.<BR>--चरः,<BR>--वराहः (विट्चरः, विड्वराहः) a tame or<BR>village hog (eating ordure).<BR>--पतिः a<BR>son-in-law.<BR>--लवणं (विड्लवणं) a<BR>kind of medicinal salt.<BR>--संगः (<BR>विट्संगः) constipation.<BR>--सारिका (<BR>विट्सारिका) a kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषं|विष|विषः
विषं [विष्-क]<BR>1 Poison, venom<BR>(said to be m. also in this sense);<BR>विषं भवतु मा भूद्वा फटाटोपो भयंकरः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-a" target="_blank">Page0998-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Pt. 1. 204.<BR>--2 Water; विषं जलधरैः पीतं<BR>मूर्छिताः पथिकांगनाः Chandr. 5. 82<BR>(where both senses are intended).<BR>--3<BR>The fibres of a lotus-stalk.<BR>--4<BR>Gummyrrh.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्त, --दिग्ध a.<BR>poisoned, envenomed.<BR>--अंकुरः {1} a spear.<BR>{2} a poisoned arrow.<BR>--अंतक a.<BR>antidotal.<BR>--(कः) an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--अपह, --घ्न a. repelling poison,<BR>antidotal.<BR>--आननः, --आयुधः, --आस्यः<BR>a snake.<BR>--आस्या the marking-nut<BR>plant.<BR>--आस्वाद a. tasting poison.<BR>--कंठः N. of Śiva.<BR>--कुंभः a jar<BR>filled with poison.<BR>--कृमिः a worm<BR>bred in poison. ˚न्याय see under<BR>न्याय.<BR>--घातिन् m. the Śirīṣa tree.<BR>--घ्न<BR>a. antidotal, serving as an antidote;<BR>इति चिंताविषघ्नोयमगदः किं न पीयते<BR>H. 1.<BR>--(घ्नः) {1} an antidote. {2} the<BR>शिरीष and चंपक trees.<BR>--(घ्नी) {1}<BR>turmeric. {2} colocynth.<BR>--जुष्ट a. {1}<BR>poisonous. {2} poisoned, affected by<BR>poison.<BR>--ज्वरः a buffalo.<BR>--दः a<BR>cloud.<BR>--(दं) green vitriol.<BR>--दंतकः<BR>a snake.<BR>--दर्शनमृत्युकः, --मृत्युः a kind<BR>of bird (said to be Cakora).<BR>--द्रुमः = ˚वृक्ष. q. v.<BR>--धरः a snake;<BR>Bv. 1. 74. ˚निलयः the lower regions, the<BR>abode of snakes.<BR>--पुष्पं the blue<BR>lotus.<BR>--पुष्पकः a disease caused by<BR>eating poisonous flowers.<BR>--प्रयोगः use of<BR>poison, administering poison.<BR>--भिषज् m.,<BR>--वैद्यः a dealer in antidotes,<BR>a curer of snake-bites; संप्रति<BR>विषवैद्यानां कर्म M. 4.<BR>--मंत्रः {1} a spell<BR>for curing snake-bites, {2} a<BR>snakecharmer, conjurer.<BR>--रसः a<BR>poisoned potion, poison-liquid; U. 2. 26.<BR>--विद्या cure of poison.<BR>--वृक्षः, --द्रुमः<BR>a poisonous tree; विषवृक्षोपि संवर्ध्य<BR>स्वयं छेत्तुमसांप्रतं Ku. 2. 55;<BR>श्रिनासि चंदनभ्रांत्या दुर्विपाकं विषद्रुमं U. 1. 46.<BR>˚न्याय see under न्याय.<BR>--वेगः the<BR>circulation or effect of poison.<BR>--शालूकः the root of the lotus.<BR>--शूकः,<BR>--शृंगिन्, --सृक्कन् m. a wasp.<BR>--सूचकः<BR>the Cakora bird.<BR>--हृदय a.<BR>‘poisonhearted’, malicious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0997-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषंज्|विषञ्ज्
विषंज् {c1c} P. To attach or stick to,<BR>to hang or suspend upon, (usually<BR>in p. p.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषक्त
विषक्त p. p.<BR>1 Fixed firmly or<BR>closely.<BR>--2 Adhering or clinging<BR>closely to.<BR>--3 Hung or suspended<BR>on; Ś. 1. 32.<BR>--4 Caused,<BR>produced; U. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषंडं|विषण्ड|विषंड|विषण्डं
विषंडं The fibres of the<BR>lotusstalk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषद्
विषद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To sink down, be<BR>exhausted.<BR>--2 To be dispirited or<BR>cast down, be afflicted or sorrowful,<BR>despond, despair; विलपति हसति<BR>विषीदति रोदिति चंचति मुंचति तापं<BR>Gīt. 4; बालसूनुरवलोक्य भार्गवं स्वां<BR>दशां च विषसाद पर्थिवः R. 11. 67;<BR>Bg. 2. 1; Bk. 7. 89; R. 9. 75.<BR>--3<BR>To be afraid. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause<BR>to despond or despair, discourage.<BR>--2 To make afflicted, pain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषण्ण|विषण्णः
विषण्ण p. p. Dejected, cast down,<BR>sad, sorrowful, spiritless,<BR>despondent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुख, --वदन a.<BR>looking sad.<BR>--रूप a. in a sad<BR>mood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषादः|विषाद
विषादः<BR>1 Dejection, sadness,<BR>depression of spirits, grief, sorrow;<BR>मद्वाणि मा कुरु विषादं Bv. 4. 41; विषादे<BR>कर्तव्ये विदधति जडाः प्रत्युत मुदं<BR>Bh. 3. 25, R. 8. 54; Ś. 4. 15.<BR>--2<BR>Disappointment, despondency, despair;<BR>विषादलुप्तप्रतिपत्ति सैन्यं R. 3. 40;<BR>(विषादश्चेतसो भंग उपायाभावनाशयोः).<BR>--3<BR>Languor, drooping state; दोर्विषादः<BR>Māl. 2. 5.<BR>--4 Dulness, stupidity,<BR>insensibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषादिन्
विषादिन् a. Dejected, dismayed,<BR>sad, disconsolate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषम|विषमं|विषमः
विषम a. [विगतो विरुद्धो वा समः]<BR>1<BR>Uneven, rough, rugged; पथिषु<BR>विषमेष्वप्यचलता Mu. 3. 3;<BR>व्यालाकीर्णाः सुविषमाः Pt. 1. 64; Me. 19.<BR>--2<BR>Irregular, unequal; Māl. 9. 43.<BR>--3<BR>Odd, not even.<BR>--4 Difficult, hard<BR>to understand, mysterious;<BR>Ki. 2. 3; विषमाः कर्मगतयः Pt. 4. 50.<BR>--5 Impassable, inaccessible;<BR>Ki. 2. 3, Bh. 3. 5.<BR>--6 Coarse, rough.<BR>--7<BR>Oblique; Māl. 4. 2.<BR>--8 Painful,<BR>troublesome;<BR>कांताविश्लेषदुःखव्यतिकरविषमे यौवने विप्रयोगः Bh. 3. 106;<BR>H. 4. 3.<BR>--9 Very strong, vehement;<BR>Māl. 3. 9.<BR>--10 Dangerous, fearful;<BR>Mv. 5. 56, Mk. 8. 1, 27,<BR>Mu. 1. 18, 2. 20.<BR>--11 Bad, adverse,<BR>unfavourable; Pt. 4. 16.<BR>--12 Odd,<BR>unusual, unparalleled.<BR>--13<BR>Dishonest, artful.<BR>--14 Intermittent, (as<BR>fever).<BR>--15 Wicked.<BR>--16 Different.<BR>--मः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--मं<BR>1<BR>Unevenness.<BR>--2 Oddness.<BR>--3 An<BR>inaccessible place, precipice, pit &c.<BR>--4 A<BR>difficult or dangerous position,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-c" target="_blank">Page0998-c+ 57</a>]<BR>difficulty, misfortune; सुप्तं प्रमत्तं<BR>विषमस्थितं वा रक्षंति पुण्यानि पुरा कृतानि<BR>Bh. 2. 97; Bg. 2. 2.<BR>--5 Rough or<BR>uneven ground.<BR>--6 N. of a figure of<BR>speech in which some unusual or<BR>incompatible relation between cause<BR>and effect is described; (said to be<BR>of four kinds; see K. P. Kārikās<BR>126 and 127).<BR>--7 A kind of stanza<BR>or verse; भिन्नचिह्न चतुष्पादं विषमं<BR>परिकीर्तितम्.<BR>--मं ind. Unequally,<BR>unevenly, unfairly, dangerously &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः, --ईक्षणः, --नयनः, --नेत्रः,<BR>--लोचनः epithets of Śiva.<BR>--अन्नं unusual<BR>or irregular food.<BR>--अवतारः descent<BR>on uneven ground, perhaps also<BR>‘undertaking or embarking in an<BR>adventure’; V. 1.<BR>--आयुधः, --इषुः,<BR>--शरः epithets of the god of love.<BR>--कर्णः {1} a quadrangle or tetragon<BR>with unequal diagonals. {2} the<BR>hypotenuse of a right-angled<BR>triangle.<BR>--कर्मन् (in math.) the<BR>finding of two quantities when the<BR>difference of their squares is given<BR>and either the sum or the difference<BR>of the quantities (Colebrooke.)<BR>--कालः an unfavourable season.<BR>--चतुरस्रःचतुर्भुजः an unequal quadrilateral<BR>figure.<BR>--छदः the tree सप्तपर्ण q. v.<BR>--छाया the shadow of the gnomon<BR>at noon.<BR>--ज्वरः remittent fever.<BR>--त्रिभुजः a scalene triangle.<BR>--लक्ष्मी<BR>f. ill-luck.<BR>--विभागः unequal<BR>distribution (of property).<BR>--शील a.<BR>cross-tempered, peevish, perverse.<BR>--स्थ a. {1} being in an<BR>inaccessible position. {2} being in difficulty<BR>or misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमित
विषमित a.<BR>1 Made rough, uneven<BR>or crooked.<BR>--2 Contracted,<BR>frowning.<BR>--3 Made difficult or<BR>inaccessible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषमीभू
विषमीभू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To become uneven.<BR>--2 To stumble, fall unevenly;<BR>Ś. 4. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयः|विषय
विषयः<BR>1 An object of sense;<BR>(these are five, corresponding to<BR>the five organs of sense; रूप, रस, गंध,<BR>स्पर्श and शब्द corresponding to the<BR>eye, tongue, nose, skin, and ear);<BR>श्रुतिविषयगुणा या स्थिता व्याप्य विश्वं<BR>Ś. 1. 1.<BR>--2 A worldly object or<BR>concern, an affair, a transaction.<BR>--3<BR>The pleasures of sense, worldly or<BR>sensual objects (usually in pl.)<BR>यौवने विषयैषिणां R. 1. 8; शब्दादीन्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-a" target="_blank">Page0999-a+ 57</a>]<BR>विषयान्भोक्तुं 10. 25; विषयव्यावृत्तकौतूहलः<BR>V. 1. 9; निर्विष्टविषयस्नेहः 12. 1, 3. 70,<BR>8. 10, 19. 49; Bg. 2. 59.<BR>--4 An<BR>object, a thing, matter; नार्यो न<BR>जग्मुर्विषयांतराणि R. 7. 12, 8. 89.<BR>--5<BR>An object or thing aimed at, mark,<BR>object; भूयिष्ठमन्यविषया न तु दृष्टिरस्याः<BR>Ś. 1. 31; Śi. 9. 40.<BR>--6 Scope,<BR>range, reach, compass; सौमित्रेरपि<BR>पत्रिणामविषये तत्र प्रिये क्वासि भोः<BR>U. 3. 45; यस्मिन्नीश्वर इत्यनन्यविषयः शब्दो<BR>यथार्थाक्षरः V. 1. 1;<BR>सकलवचनानामविषयः Māl. 1. 30, 36; U. 5. 19;<BR>Ku. 6. 17.<BR>--7 Department, sphere,<BR>province, field, element;<BR>सर्वत्रौदरिकस्याभ्यवहार्यमेव विषयः V. 3.<BR>--8 A<BR>subject, subject matter, topic; अयि<BR>मलयज महिमायं कस्य गिरामस्तु विषयस्ते<BR>Bv. 1. 11; so शृंगारविषयको ग्रंथः<BR>‘treating of love’.<BR>--9 The topic or<BR>subject to be explained, general<BR>head; the first of the five members<BR>of an Adhikaraṇa q. v.<BR>--10 A<BR>place, spot; परिसरविषयेषु लीढमुक्ताः<BR>Ki. 5. 38.<BR>--11 A country, realm,<BR>domain, territory, district,<BR>kingdom; Pt. 2. 2.<BR>--12 A refuge, an<BR>asylum.<BR>--13 A collection of<BR>villages.<BR>--14 A lover, husband.<BR>--15<BR>Semen virile.<BR>--16 A religious<BR>observance.<BR>--17 A symbolical expression<BR>for the number ‘five.’ (विषये means<BR>‘with regard or reference to,’ ‘in<BR>respect of’, ‘in the case of’,<BR>‘regarding’, ‘cancerning’; या तत्रास्ते<BR>युवतिविषये सृष्टिराद्येव धातुः Me. 82; स्त्रीणा<BR>विषये; धनविषये &c.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभिरतिः {1} attachment to objects of<BR>sense or worldly pleasures;<BR>Ki. 6. 44; so ˚अभिलाषः Ki. 3. 13.<BR>--आत्मक a. {1} consisting of worldly<BR>objects. {2} carnal, sensual.<BR>--आसक्त,<BR>--निरत a. addicted to sensual objects,<BR>sensualist, worldly-minded.<BR>--आसक्तिः --उपसेवा, --निरतिः f.<BR>--प्रसंगः<BR>addiction to pleasures of sense,<BR>sensuality.<BR>--एषिन् a. addicted to<BR>worldly objects; R. 1. 8.<BR>--ग्रामः the<BR>collection of the objects of sense.<BR>--सुखं the pleasures of sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0998-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयक
विषयक a.<BR>1 Relating to an<BR>object.<BR>--2 (At the end of comp.).<BR>Having for an object, treating of,<BR>relating to, as in दानविषयको ग्रंथः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयायिन्
विषयायिन् m.<BR>1 One addicted to<BR>pleasures of sense, a sensualist.<BR>--2<BR>A man of the world.<BR>--3 The god<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">Page0999-b+ 55</a>]<BR>of love.<BR>--4 A king.<BR>--5 An organ of<BR>sense.<BR>--6 A materialist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषयिन्
विषयिन् a. Sensual, carnal. --m.<BR>1 A man of the world, worldling.<BR>--2 A king.<BR>--3 The god of love.<BR>--4 A sensualist, voluptuary;<BR>विषयिणः कस्यापदोऽस्तं गताः Pt. 1. 146;<BR>Ś. 5. --n.<BR>1 An organ of sense.<BR>--2<BR>Knowledge (ज्ञान).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषह्
विषह् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To bear, suffer,<BR>endure; दुर्वारं सा कथमपि परित्यागदुःखं<BR>विषेहे R. 14. 87, 3. 63, 8. 57.<BR>--2<BR>To resist, oppose, withstand, be<BR>able to resist; तस्यामेव रघोः पांड्याः<BR>प्रतापं न विषेहिरे R. 4. 49.<BR>--3 To be<BR>able; Śi. 14. 29, 17. 10.<BR>--4 To<BR>allow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषह्य
विषह्य a.<BR>1 Endurable, bearable;<BR>अविषह्यव्यसनेन धूमितां Ku. 4. 30,<BR>R. 6. 47.<BR>--2 Possible to be settled<BR>or determined; Ms. 8. 265.<BR>--3<BR>Possible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषलः|विषल|विषलं
विषलः Poison, venom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषा
विषा<BR>1 Ordure, feces.<BR>--2<BR>Intellect, understanding.<BR>--3 A tree (<BR>अतिविषा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणः|विषाण|विषाणं
विषाणः --णं, --णी [विष्-बा˚ कानच्]<BR>1 A horn; साहित्यसंगीतकलाविहीनः<BR>साक्षात्पशुः पुच्छविषाणहीनः Bh. 2. 12;<BR>कदाचिदपि पर्यटञ् शशविषाणमासादयेत्<BR>2. 5.<BR>--2 The tusk of an elephant<BR>or boar; तप्तानामुपदधिरे विषाणभिन्नाः<BR>प्रह्लादं सुरकरिणां घनाः क्षरंतः Ki. 7. 13;<BR>Śi. 1. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणं|विषाण|विषाणः
विषाणः --णं, --णी [विष्-बा˚ कानच्]<BR>1 A horn; साहित्यसंगीतकलाविहीनः<BR>साक्षात्पशुः पुच्छविषाणहीनः Bh. 2. 12;<BR>कदाचिदपि पर्यटञ् शशविषाणमासादयेत्<BR>2. 5.<BR>--2 The tusk of an elephant<BR>or boar; तप्तानामुपदधिरे विषाणभिन्नाः<BR>प्रह्लादं सुरकरिणां घनाः क्षरंतः Ki. 7. 13;<BR>Śi. 1. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणी
विषाणः --णं, --णी [विष्-बा˚ कानच्]<BR>1 A horn; साहित्यसंगीतकलाविहीनः<BR>साक्षात्पशुः पुच्छविषाणहीनः Bh. 2. 12;<BR>कदाचिदपि पर्यटञ् शशविषाणमासादयेत्<BR>2. 5.<BR>--2 The tusk of an elephant<BR>or boar; तप्तानामुपदधिरे विषाणभिन्नाः<BR>प्रह्लादं सुरकरिणां घनाः क्षरंतः Ki. 7. 13;<BR>Śi. 1. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विषाणिन्
विषाणिन् a. Having horns or<BR>tusks. --m.<BR>1 Any animal having<BR>horns or tusks.<BR>--2 An elephant;<BR>भग्नो निवासोऽयमिहास्य पुष्पैः सदानतो<BR>येन विषाणिनागः Śi. 4. 63, 12. 77.<BR>--3 A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=0999-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

