वैयाकरण a. (णी f.) [व्याकरणं वेत्त्यधीते<BR>वा अण्] Grammatical.<BR>--णः A<BR>grammarian; वैयाकरणकिरातादपशब्दमृगाः क्व यांतु<BR>संत्रस्ताः Subhāṣ.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पाशः a<BR>bad grammarian.<BR>--भार्यः one whose<BR>wife is a grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयाघ्र|वैयाघ्रः
वैयाघ्र a. (घ्री f.)<BR>1 Tiger-like.<BR>--2 Covered with a tiger's skin.<BR>--घ्रः A cart covered with a tiger's<BR>skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयात्यं|वैयात्य
वैयात्यं<BR>1 Boldness, immodesty,<BR>absence of shame; अन्यदा भूषणं<BR>पुंसां क्षमा लज्जेव योषितां । पराक्रमः<BR>परिभवे वैयात्यं सुरतेष्विव Śi. 2. 44.<BR>--2<BR>Rudeness in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयासिकः|वैयासिक
वैयासिकः A son of Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैयुष्ट|वैयुष्टः
वैयुष्ट a. Early, occurring at<BR>daybreak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरं|वैर
वैरं [वीरस्य भावः अण्]<BR>1<BR>Hostility, enmity, animosity, spite, grudge,<BR>opposition, quarrel; दानेन वैराण्यपि<BR>यांति नाशं Subhāṣ.; अज्ञातहृदयेष्वेवं<BR>वैरीभवति सौहृदं Ś. 5. 24 ‘turns into<BR>enmity’; विधाय वैरं सामर्षे नरोऽरौ य<BR>उदासते । प्राक्षिण्योदर्चिषं कक्षे शेरते<BR>तेऽभिमारुतं Śi. 2. 42.<BR>--2 Hatred,<BR>revenge.<BR>--3 Heroism, prowess.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुबंधः commencement of<BR>hostilities.<BR>--अनुबंधिन् a. leading to<BR>enmity. (--m.) {1} the heating solar<BR>ray. {2} N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--आतंकः<BR>the Arjuna tree.<BR>--आनृण्यं, --उद्धारः,<BR>निर्यातनं, --प्रतिक्रिया, --प्रतीकारः,<BR>--यातना, --शुद्धिः f.,<BR>--साधनं requital of<BR>enmity, taking revenge, retaliation.<BR>--करः, --कारः, --कृत् m. an enemy.<BR>--भावः hostile attitude.<BR>--रक्षिन् a.<BR>guarding against hostilities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरायते
वैरायते Den. A. To act inimically,<BR>become hostile towards, contend<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरक्तं|वैरक्त
वैरक्तं --क्त्यं [विरक्तस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Indifference to worldly attachments,<BR>absence of desire.<BR>--2 Displeasure,<BR>dislike, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरक्त्यं|वैरक्त्य
वैरक्तं --क्त्यं [विरक्तस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Indifference to worldly attachments,<BR>absence of desire.<BR>--2 Displeasure,<BR>dislike, aversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरंगिकः|वैरङ्गिक|वैरङ्गिकः
वैरंगिकः [विरंगं विरागं नित्यमर्हति ठक्]<BR>One who has subdued all his<BR>passions and desires, an ascetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरल्यं|वैरल्य
वैरल्यं<BR>1 Scarceness, rareness.<BR>--2 Looseness.<BR>--3 Fineness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1014-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागं|वैराग
वैरागं See वैराग्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागिकः|वैरागिक
वैरागिकः, वैरागिन् m. An ascetic who<BR>has subdued all his passions and<BR>desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरागिन्
वैरागिकः, वैरागिन् m. An ascetic who<BR>has subdued all his passions and<BR>desires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराग्यं|वैराग्य
वैराग्यं [विरागस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Absence of worldly desires or passions,<BR>indifference to the world, asceticism;<BR>अभ्यासेन च कौंतेय वैराग्येण च गृह्यते<BR>Bg. 6. 35, 13. 8.<BR>--2 Dissatistaction,<BR>displeasure, discontent; कामं<BR>प्रकृतिवैराग्यं सद्यः शमयितुं क्षमः R. 17. 55.<BR>--3<BR>Aversion, dislike.<BR>--4 Grief, sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराज|वैराजः
वैराज a. (जी f.) Belonging to<BR>Brahman; U. 2. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैराट|वैराटः
वैराट a. (टी f.) [विराटस्येदं अण्]<BR>Belonging to Virāṭa.<BR>--टः A kind of<BR>earth-worm (इंद्रगोप).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरिन्
वैरिन् a. [वैरमस्त्यस्य इनि] Hostile,<BR>inimical. --m.<BR>1 An enemy; शौर्ये<BR>वैरिणि वज्रमाशु निपतत्वर्थोऽस्तु नः केवलं<BR>Bh. 2. 39; Bg. 3. 37; R. 12. 104.<BR>--2 A hero, brave person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरूप्यं|वैरूप्य
वैरूप्यं [विरूपस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Deformity, ugliness; R. 12. 40.<BR>--2<BR>Difference or diversity of form.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचनः|वैरोचन
वैरोचनः, वैरोचनिः, वैरोचिः<BR>1<BR>Epithets of the demon Bali, son of<BR>Virocana.<BR>--2 Of the son of Agni.<BR>--3 Of the son of Sūrya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचनिः|वैरोचनि
वैरोचनः, वैरोचनिः, वैरोचिः<BR>1<BR>Epithets of the demon Bali, son of<BR>Virocana.<BR>--2 Of the son of Agni.<BR>--3 Of the son of Sūrya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैरोचिः|वैरोचि
वैरोचनः, वैरोचनिः, वैरोचिः<BR>1<BR>Epithets of the demon Bali, son of<BR>Virocana.<BR>--2 Of the son of Agni.<BR>--3 Of the son of Sūrya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलक्षण्यं|वैलक्षण्य
वैलक्षण्यं [विलक्षणस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Strangeness.<BR>--2 Contrariety,<BR>opposition.<BR>--3 Difference, disparity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलक्ष्यं|वैलक्ष्य
वैलक्ष्यं [विलक्षस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Embarrassment, confusion.<BR>--2<BR>Unnaturalness, affectation; वैलक्ष्यस्मितं ‘a<BR>forced or affected smile’.<BR>--3 Shame.<BR>--4 Absence of any mark or<BR>characteristic.<BR>--5 Contrariety, inversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैलोम्यं|वैलोम्य
वैलोम्यं Opposition, inversion,<BR>contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैल्व|वैल्वं
वैल्व a. See बैल्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवधिकः|वैवधिक
वैवधिकः<BR>1 A pedlar, hawker.<BR>--2<BR>A carrier of loads on a pole.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्ण्यं|वैवर्ण्य
वैवर्ण्यं [विवर्णस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Change of colour or complexion,<BR>paleness.<BR>--2 Difference, diversity.<BR>--3 Deviation from caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवर्तं|वैवर्त
वैवर्तं Revolution, change of<BR>existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वतः|वैवस्वत
वैवस्वतः [विवस्वतोऽपत्यं अण्]<BR>1 N. of<BR>the seventh Manu who is supposed<BR>to preside over the present age; see<BR>under Manu; वैवस्वतो मनुर्नाम माननीयो<BR>मनीषिणां R. 1. 11; U. 6. 18.<BR>--2 N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">Page1015-b+ 58</a>]<BR>of Yama; R. 15. 45.<BR>--3 N. of<BR>Agni.<BR>--4 One of the eleven Rudras.<BR>--5 The planet Saturn.<BR>--तं The<BR>present age or Manvantara, as<BR>presided over by Manu Vaivasvata or<BR>the seventh Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवस्वती
वैवस्वती<BR>1 The southern quarter.<BR>--2 N. of Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैवाहिक|वैवाहिकः
वैवाहिक a. (की f.) [विवाहाय<BR>हितं सधु वा ठक्] Relating to<BR>marriage, matrimonial, nuptial;<BR>Ku. 7. 2.<BR>--कः --कं A marriage, wedding.<BR>--कः The father of a son's wife or<BR>daughter's husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशद्यं|वैशद्य
वैशद्यं<BR>1 Clearness, purity (fig.<BR>also).<BR>--2 Perspicuity; as in शिष्यबु<BR>द्धिवैशद्यार्थं.<BR>--3 Whiteness.<BR>--4 Calmness,<BR>composure (of mind).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशंपायनः|वैशम्पायन|वैशंपायन|वैशम्पायनः
वैशंपायनः N. of a celebrated<BR>pupil of Vyāsa. [It was he who<BR>made Yājñavalkya disgorge the whole<BR>of the Yajurveda he had learnt from him<BR>which was picked up by his other<BR>pupils in the form of Tittiris or partridges;<BR>and hence the Veda was called<BR>‘Taittirīya’. Vaiśampāyana was celebrated<BR>for his great skill in narrating Purāṇas,<BR>and is said to have recounted the<BR>whole of the Mahābhārata to king<BR>Janamejaya].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशसं|वैशस
वैशसं<BR>1 Destruction, slaughter,<BR>butchery; विधिना कृतमर्धवैशसं<BR>Ku. 4. 31; U. 4. 24, 6. 40.<BR>--2 Distress,<BR>torment, pain, suffering, hardship;<BR>उपराधवैशसं Mu. 2;<BR>धिगुच्छ्वसितवैशसं Māl. 9. 35.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशस्त्रं|वैशस्त्र
वैशस्त्रं<BR>1 Defencelessness.<BR>--2<BR>Government, rule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशाखः|वैशाख|वैशाखं
वैशाखः<BR>1 N. of the second<BR>lunar month (corresponding to<BR>AprilMay).<BR>--2 A churning-stick;<BR>द्रुततरकरदक्षाः क्षिप्तवैशाखशैले…<BR>कलशिमुदधिगुर्वी वल्लवा लोडयति Śi. 11. 8.<BR>--खं<BR>A kind of attitude in shooting; see<BR>विशख.<BR>--खी The full-moon day in<BR>the month of Vaiśākha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशारद्यं|वैशारद्य
वैशारद्यं Skill, cleverness,<BR>proficiency.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिक|वैशिकः
वैशिक a. Practised by harlots;<BR>वैशिकीं कलां Mk. 1. 4 ‘arts<BR>practised by harlots’.<BR>--कः A person<BR>who associates with harlots; a kind<BR>of hero in erotic works.<BR>--कं<BR>Harlotry, arts of harlots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिष्टं|वैशिष्ट
वैशिष्टं = वैशिष्ट्य below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशिष्ट्यं|वैशिष्ट्य
वैशिष्ट्यं<BR>1 Distinction, difference.<BR>--2 Peculiarity, speciality,<BR>particularity; वैञ्चिष्ट्यादन्यमर्थं याबोधयेत्सार्थसंभवा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-c" target="_blank">Page1015-c+ 57</a>]<BR>S. D. 27.<BR>--3 Excellence; S. D. 78.<BR>--4 Possession or endowment with<BR>some characteristic attribute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेषिक|वैशेषिकः
वैशेषिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Characteristic.<BR>--2 Belonging to the<BR>Vaiśeshika doctrine.<BR>--कः A follower of<BR>the Vaiśeṣika doctrine.<BR>--कं [<BR>विशेषं पदार्थमेदमधिकृत्य कृतो ग्रंथः ठञ्] One<BR>of the six principal Darśanas or<BR>systems of Hindu philosophy founded<BR>by Kaṇāda; it differs from the<BR>Nyāya philosophy of Gautama in that it<BR>recognizes only seven instead of<BR>sixteen categories or heads of<BR>predicables (the earlier writers, e. g.<BR>Kaṇāda recognizing only six), and<BR>lays particular stress upon Viśeṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैशेष्यं|वैशेष्य
वैशेष्यं<BR>1 Excellence, pre-eminence,<BR>superiority.<BR>--2 Specific or generic<BR>distinction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्यः|वैश्य
वैश्यः A man of the third tribe,<BR>his business being trade and<BR>agriculture; विशत्याशु पशुभ्यश्च कृष्यादावरुचिः<BR>शुचिः । वेदाध्ययनसंपन्नः स वैश्य इति<BR>संज्ञितः Padma Purāṇa. (He is<BR>supposed to have sprung from the thighs<BR>of Puruṣa; cf. ऊरू तदस्य यद्वैश्यः<BR>Rv. 10. 90).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n.<BR>--वृत्तिः f.<BR>the business or occupation of a<BR>Vaiśya; trade, agriculture &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्रवणः|वैश्रवण
वैश्रवणः<BR>1 N. of Kubera, the god<BR>of wealth; विभाति यस्यां<BR>ललितालकायां मनोहरा वैश्रवणस्य लक्ष्मीः Bv. 2. 10.<BR>--2 N. of Rāvaṇa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आलयः,<BR>--आवासः {1} the abode of Kubera. {2}<BR>the fig-tree.<BR>--उदयः the fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वदेव|वैश्वदेवः
वैश्वदेव a. (वी f.) Belonging to<BR>the Viśvedevas, q. v.<BR>--वं [विश्वेभ्यो<BR>देवेभ्यो देयो बलिः अण्]<BR>1 An offering<BR>made to the Viśvedevas.<BR>--2 An<BR>offering to all deities (made by<BR>presenting oblations to fire before meals).<BR>--वी The eighth day of the second<BR>half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वानर|वैश्वानरः
वैश्वानर a. (री f.) Relating or<BR>common to all mankind, fit for all<BR>men.<BR>--रः<BR>1 An epithet of fire; त्वत्तः<BR>खांडवरंगतांडवनटो दूरेऽस्तु वैश्वानरः<BR>Bv. 1. 57.<BR>--2 The fire of digestion (in<BR>the stomach); अहं वैश्वानरो भूत्वा<BR>प्राणिनां देहमाश्रितः । प्राणापानसमायुक्तः<BR>पचाम्यन्नं चतुर्बिधं Bg. 15. 14.<BR>--3<BR>General consciousness (in Vedānta phil.).<BR>--4 The Supreme Being.<BR>--5 The<BR>Chitraka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैश्वासिक
वैश्वासिक a. (की f.) Trusty,<BR>confidential.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1015-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषम्यं|वैषम्य
वैषम्यं [विषमस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Unevenness.<BR>--2 Roughness, harshness.<BR>--3 Inequality.<BR>--4 Injustice.<BR>--5<BR>Difficulty, misery, calamity.<BR>--6<BR>Solitariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषयिक|वैषयिकः
वैषयिक a. (की f.) [विषयेण निर्वृत्तः<BR>ठक्]<BR>1 Relating to an object.<BR>--2<BR>Pertaining to objects of sense, sensual,<BR>carnal.<BR>--कः A sensualist,<BR>voluptuary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैषुवत्
वैषुवत् a. (ती f.) Relating to the<BR>equinox, equinoctial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्टुतं|वैष्टुत
वैष्टुतं The ashes of a burnt<BR>offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्ट्रः|वैष्ट्र|वैष्ट्रं
वैष्ट्रः<BR>1 Heaven, sky.<BR>--2 Air, wind.<BR>--3 A world, a division of the<BR>universe.<BR>--4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैष्णव|वैष्णवं|वैष्णवः
वैष्णव a. (वी f.) [विष्णुर्देवतास्य<BR>तस्येदं वा अण्]<BR>1 Relating to Viṣṇu;<BR>गां गतस्य तव धाम वैष्णवं R. 11. 85.<BR>--2<BR>Worshipping Viṣṇu.<BR>--वः<BR>1 One<BR>of the three important modern<BR>Hindu sects, the other two being Śaiva<BR>and Śākta sects.<BR>--2 N. of the<BR>asterism Śravaṇa.<BR>--वी<BR>1 The<BR>personified Śakti or energy of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2<BR>N. of Durgā.<BR>--वं<BR>1 The residence of<BR>Viṣṇu; i. e. वैकुंठ.<BR>--2 The ashes of<BR>a burnt offering.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुराणं N.<BR>of one of the 18 Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैसारिणः|वैसारिण
वैसारिणः A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैसूचनं|वैसूचन
वैसूचनं Assuming the part of a<BR>female by a man (in dramas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहायस|वैहायसं
वैहायस a. (सी f.) Being in the<BR>air, aerial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहार्य|वैहार्य्य|वैहार्य्यः
वैहार्य a. To be sported with, to<BR>be made the subject of jokes or<BR>pleasantry (said of the brother of<BR>one's wife or of the wife's relatives<BR>in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वैहासिकः|वैहासिक
वैहासिकः<BR>1 A jester, buffoon.<BR>--2<BR>An actor in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोड्रः|वोड्र
वोड्रः<BR>1 A kind of snake.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोड्री
वोड्री The fourth part of a Paṇa,<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोढृ
वोढृ m.<BR>1 A bearer, porter.<BR>--2 A<BR>leader.<BR>--3 A husband.<BR>--4 A bull.<BR>--5<BR>A charioteer.<BR>--6 A draught-horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोंटः|वोण्ट|वोंट|वोण्टः
वोंटः A stalk, stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोद|वोदः
वोद a. Moist, wet, damp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोदालः|वोदाल
वोदालः The sheat-fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरकः|वोरक
वोर(ल)कः A scribe, writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोलकः|वोलक
वोर(ल)कः A scribe, writer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोरटः|वोरट
वोरटः A kind of jasmine (कुंद).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोलः|वोल|वोलं
वोलः Gum-myrrh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वोल्लाहः|वोल्लाह
वोल्लाहः A kind of horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वौद्ध|वौद्धं
वौद्ध a. See बौद्ध.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वौषट्
वौषट् ind. An exclamation or<BR>formula used in offering an<BR>oblation to the gods or Manes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्य|व्यः
व्य A technical term for<BR>indeclinables such as नि, चित् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यः|व्य
व्यः A cover, veil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंशक|व्यंशकः
व्यंशक a. Undressed, naked;<BR>Ki. 9. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंशुकः|व्यंशुक
व्यंशुकः A mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंस्
व्यंस् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To divide,<BR>distribute.<BR>--2 To foil, ward off.<BR>--3 To<BR>deceive, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसकः|व्यंसक
व्यंसकः A rogue, cheat; as in<BR>मयूरव्यंसकः ‘a roguish peacock’, ‘a<BR>rogue of a peacock’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंसनं|व्यंसन
व्यंसनं<BR>1 Cheating, deceiving.<BR>--2<BR>Distributing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यग्र|व्यग्रः
व्यग्र a. [विगतमग्रं यस्य]<BR>1<BR>Bewildered, perplexed, distracted.<BR>--2<BR>Alarmed, frightened.<BR>--3 Eagerly or<BR>intently occupied (with loc., instr.<BR>or in comp.); स<BR>राजककुदव्यग्रपाणिभिः पार्श्ववर्तिभिः R. 17. 27,<BR>Mv. 1. 13, 4. 28, Ku. 7. 2, U. 1. 23<BR>Bv. 1. 123; Śi. 2. 79.<BR>--ग्रः N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंग|व्यङ्ग|व्यङ्गः
व्यंग a. [विगतमंगं यस्य]<BR>1<BR>Bodiless.<BR>--2 Wanting a limb, deformed,<BR>mutilated, maimed, crippled.<BR>--3<BR>Illarranged.<BR>--4 Lame.<BR>--गः<BR>1 A<BR>cripple.<BR>--2 A frog.<BR>--3 Dark spots<BR>on the cheek.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः<BR>suggested or implied sense; cf व्यंग्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंगयति
व्यंगयति Den. P. To mutilate,<BR>cripple, maim.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंगिता
व्यंगिता Mutilation; Pt. 1. 201.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंगुलं|व्यङ्गुल|व्यंगुल
व्यंगुलं An extremely small mea<BR>sure of length equal to one-sixtieth<BR>part of an angula.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंग्य|व्यङ्ग्य|व्यङ्ग्यः
व्यंग्य a.<BR>1 Indicated by<BR>implication, indicated by covert or indirect<BR>allusion.<BR>--2 Suggested (as sense).<BR>--ग्यं Suggested sense, insinuation,<BR>the meaning hinted at (opp. वाच्य<BR>‘the primary or expressed meaning’,<BR>and लक्ष्य ‘the secondary or indicated<BR>meaning’); इदमुत्तममतिशयिनि व्यंग्ये<BR>वाच्याद् ध्वनिर्बुधैः कथितः K. P. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः f. covert<BR>expression, insinuation, inuendo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यच्
व्यच् {c6c} P. (विचति, pass. विच्यते)<BR>1 To cheat, deceive, trick.<BR>--2 To<BR>surround, encompass, pervade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यचस्
व्यचस् n. Ved. Expanse, vastness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यजः|व्यज
व्यजः A fan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यजनं|व्यजन
व्यजनं A fan; निर्वाते व्यजनं<BR>H. 2. 165; R. 8. 40, 10. 62; cf. बालव्यजन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंज्|व्यञ्ज्
व्यंज् {c7c} P.<BR>1 To reveal, manifest,<BR>show; अकिंचनत्वं मखजं व्यनक्ति<BR>R. 5. 16; Śi. 1. 26.<BR>--2 To indicate,<BR>denote.<BR>--3 Ved. To anoint<BR>thoroughly.<BR>--4 Ved. To decorate, adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्त|व्यक्तः
व्यक्त p. p.<BR>1 Manifested,<BR>displayed.<BR>--2 Developed, created;<BR>Ku. 2. 11.<BR>--3 Evident, manifest, clear,<BR>plain, distinct, clearly visible;<BR>Pt. 2. 92.<BR>--4 Specified, known,<BR>distinguished.<BR>--5 Individual.<BR>--6 Wise,<BR>learned.<BR>--7 Ved. Adorned,<BR>decorated.<BR>--क्तः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--क्तं<BR>That which is developed as the<BR>product of अव्यक्त q. v.<BR>--क्तं ind.<BR>Clearly, evidently, certainly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गणितं arithmetic.<BR>--दृष्टार्थः an<BR>eye-witness, a witness in general.<BR>--राशिः<BR>a known quantity.<BR>--रूपः an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--विक्रम a.<BR>displaying valour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तिः|व्यक्ति
व्यक्तिः f.<BR>1 Manifestation,<BR>visibility; clear perception; राज्ञः<BR>समक्षमेवाधगोत्तरव्यक्तिर्भविष्यति M. 1;<BR>स्तेहव्याक्तिः Me. 12.<BR>--2 Visible<BR>appearance, clearness, distinctness;<BR>व्यक्तिं भजंत्यापगाः Ś. 7. 8.<BR>--3<BR>Distinction, discrimination; तं संतः<BR>श्रोतुमर्हंति सदसद्व्यक्तिहेतवः R. 1. 10.<BR>--4 Real form or nature, true<BR>character; न हि ते भगवन् व्यक्तिं विदुर्देवा<BR>न दानवाः Bg. 10. 14.<BR>--5 An<BR>individual (opp. जाति), as in जातिव्यक्ती;<BR>Bg. 8. 18.<BR>--6 Gender (in gram.).<BR>--7 Inflection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तीकृ
व्यक्तीकृ {c8c} U. To make clear,<BR>show, manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यक्तीभू
व्यक्तीभू {c1c} P. To become distinct<BR>or clear, become clearly visible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंजक|व्यञ्जक|व्यञ्जकः
व्यंजक a. (जिका f.)<BR>1 Making<BR>clear, indicating, showing,<BR>manifesting.<BR>--2 Suggesting or insinuating<BR>a meaning (as a word, opp. वाचक<BR>and लाक्षणिक q.q. v.v.).<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>Dramatic action or gesture,<BR>external indication of an internal<BR>feeling by suitable gesticulation.<BR>--2<BR>A sign, symbol.<BR>--3 Figurative<BR>expression or insinuation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंजनं|व्यञ्जन|व्यंजन|व्यञ्जनं
व्यंजनं<BR>1 Making clear,<BR>indicating, manifesting.<BR>--2 A mark, token,<BR>sign.<BR>--3 A reminder; Māl. 9.<BR>--4<BR>Disguise, garb; नानाव्यंजनाः प्रणिधयः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">Page1017-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Mu. 1; Śi. 2. 56; तपस्विव्यंजनोपेताः<BR>&c.<BR>--5 A consonant.<BR>--6 A mark of<BR>the sex, i. e. the male or female<BR>organ.<BR>--7 Insignla.<BR>--8 A mark or sign<BR>of puberty.<BR>--9 The beard.<BR>--10 A<BR>limb, member.<BR>--11 (a) A<BR>condiment, sauce, a seasoned article;<BR>N. 16. 104. (b) An article used in<BR>seasoning food, spices &c.<BR>--12<BR>The last of the three powers of a<BR>word by virtue of which it suggests<BR>or insinuates a sense; see अंजन-ना<BR>(8) (written व्यंजना also in this<BR>sense).<BR>--13 A day.<BR>--14 A privy part.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदय a. followed by a<BR>consonant.<BR>--संधिः the junction or<BR>coalition of consonants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1016-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंजना
व्यंजना<BR>1 See व्यंजन (12) above.<BR>--2<BR>Irony, sarcasm.<BR>--3 Insinuation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. insinuation,<BR>figurative or elliptical mode of expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंजित|व्यञ्जित
व्यंजित p. p.<BR>1 Made clear,<BR>manifested, indicated.<BR>--2 Marked,<BR>distinguished, characterized.<BR>--3<BR>Suggested, insinuated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यडंबकः|व्यडम्बक|व्यडंबक|व्यडम्बकः
व्यडंबकः, व्यडंबनः The castor-oil<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यडंबनः|व्यडम्बन|व्यडंबन|व्यडम्बनः
व्यडंबकः, व्यडंबनः The castor-oil<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकॄ
व्यतिकॄ {c6c} P. To mix, blend,<BR>scatter (usually in pass.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकर|व्यतिकरः
व्यतिकर a.<BR>1 Reciprocal.<BR>--2<BR>Spreading, pervading.<BR>--3<BR>Contiguous, near.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Mixture,<BR>intermixture, mixing,<BR>blending together; तीर्थे तोयव्यतिकरभवे<BR>जह्नुकन्यासरय्वोः R. 8. 95; व्यतिकर इव<BR>भीमस्तामसो वैद्युतश्च U. 5. 13;<BR>Māl. 9. 52.<BR>--2 Contact, union,<BR>combination; रुद्रेणेदमुमाकृतव्यतिकरे स्वांगे<BR>विभक्तं द्विधा M. 1. 4; Māl. 7, Śi. 4. 53,<BR>7. 28.<BR>--3 Striking against; Māl. 5. 34.<BR>--4 Obstruction; Ku. 5. 85.<BR>--5 An<BR>incident, occurrence, affair, a thing,<BR>matter; एवंविधे व्यतिकरे ‘such being<BR>the case.’<BR>--6 An opportunity.<BR>--7<BR>Misfortune, calamity.<BR>--8 Mutual<BR>relation, reciprocity.<BR>--9 Exchange,<BR>interchange.<BR>--10 Alternation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकरित
व्यतिकरित a. Pervaded, filled;<BR>Māl. 2. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिकीर्ण
व्यतिकीर्ण^1 p. p.<BR>1 Mixed or<BR>blended together.<BR>--2 United.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रम्
व्यतिक्रम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To transgress,<BR>violate, offend against; Pt. 1. 56.<BR>--2 To neglect, omit.<BR>--3 To pass,<BR>spend (time).<BR>--4 To pass over or<BR>beyond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतियु
व्यतियु {c2c} P. To mix; अन्योन्यं<BR>स्म व्यतियुतः शब्दाञ् शब्दैस्तु भीषणान्<BR>Bk. 8. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रमः|व्यतिक्रम
व्यतिक्रमः<BR>1 Transgressing,<BR>deviating, swerving.<BR>--2 Violation, breach,<BR>non-performance; as in<BR>सांविद्व्यतिक्रमः; प्रतिबघ्नाति हि श्रेयः<BR>पूज्यपूजाव्यतिक्रमः R. 1. 79.<BR>--3 Disregard, neglect,<BR>omission.<BR>--4 Contrariety, inversion,<BR>reverse.<BR>--5 Sin, vice, crime.<BR>--6<BR>Adversity, misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिक्रांत|व्यतिक्रान्त
व्यतिक्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Passed over,<BR>transgressed, violated, neglected.<BR>--2<BR>Inverted, reversed.<BR>--3 Elapsed,<BR>passed away (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरिच्
व्यतिरिच् Pass.<BR>1 To differ or be<BR>separate from.<BR>--2 To surpass, excel;<BR>lie beyond; स्तुतिभ्यो व्यतिरिच्यंते दूराणि<BR>चरितानि ते R. 10. 30. See व्यतिरिक्त<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरिक्त|व्यतिरिक्तः
व्यतिरिक्त p. p.<BR>1 Separated or<BR>distinct from; अव्यतिरिक्तेयमस्मच्छरीरात्<BR>K., Ku. 1. 31, 5. 22.<BR>--2<BR>Surpassing, excelling, going beyond.<BR>--3<BR>Withdrawn, withheld.<BR>--4 Excepted<BR>--क्तं ind. With the exception of,<BR>except, without.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेकः|व्यतिरेक
व्यतिरेकः<BR>1 Distinction,<BR>difference.<BR>--2 Separation from.<BR>--3<BR>Exclusion, exception.<BR>--4<BR>Excellence, surpassing, excelling.<BR>--5<BR>Contrast, dissimilarity.<BR>--6 (In<BR>logic) Logical discontinuance (opp.<BR>अन्वय q. v.); यत्र साध्याभावस्तत्र<BR>हेत्वभाव इति व्यतिरेकव्याप्तिः (e. g. यत्र<BR>वह्निर्नास्ति तत्र धूमो नास्ति is an instance of<BR>व्यतिरेकव्याप्ति).<BR>--7 (In Rhet.) A<BR>figure of speech which consists in<BR>representing the Upameya as<BR>superior to the Upamāna in some<BR>particular respects; उपमानाद्यदन्यस्य<BR>व्यतिरेकः स एव सः K. P. 10. (व्यतिरेकेण<BR>means ‘except, without’; व्यतिरेके ‘on<BR>the contrary supposition.’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--व्याप्ति see व्यतिरेक (6) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिरेकिन्
व्यतिरेकिन् a.<BR>1 Different.<BR>--2<BR>Surpassing, excelling.<BR>--3 Excluding,<BR>excepting.<BR>--4 Showing negation or<BR>non-existence; as in व्यतिरोकिलिंगं;<BR>see व्यतिरेक (6) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषंज्|व्यतिषञ्ज्
व्यतिषंज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To link<BR>together, connect mutually;<BR>व्यतिषजति पदार्थानांतरः कोऽपि हेतुः U. 6. 12.<BR>--2 To change (Atm.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषक्त
व्यतिषक्त p. p.<BR>1 Mutually<BR>connected or related, linked or joined<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">Page1017-c+ 56</a>]<BR>together.<BR>--2 Intermixed.<BR>--3 Inter<BR>marrying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिषंगः|व्यतिषङ्ग|व्यतिषंग|व्यतिषङ्गः
व्यतिषंगः<BR>1 Mutual relation,<BR>reciprocal connection.<BR>--2<BR>Intermixture.<BR>--3 Union, junction in general.<BR>--4 Fastening or tying together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतिहारः|व्यतिहार
व्यति(ती)हारः<BR>1 Exchange,<BR>barter.<BR>--2 Reciprocity, interchange;<BR>R. 12. 93.<BR>--3 Exchange of blows,<BR>abuse, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीहारः|व्यतीहार
व्यति(ती)हारः<BR>1 Exchange,<BR>barter.<BR>--2 Reciprocity, interchange;<BR>R. 12. 93.<BR>--3 Exchange of blows,<BR>abuse, &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यती
व्यती {c2c} P. (व्यति-इ)<BR>1 To go<BR>out of, swerve from, transgress;<BR>रेखामात्रमपि क्षुण्णादा मनोर्वर्त्मनः परं । न<BR>व्यतीयुः प्रजास्तस्य नियंतुर्नेमिवृत्तयः ॥<BR>R. 1. 17.<BR>--2 To pass, elapse (as time);<BR>सप्त व्यतीयुस्त्रिगुणानि तस्य (दिनानि)<BR>R. 2. 25; व्यतीते काले &c<BR>--3 To pass<BR>beyond, leave behind; यं यं<BR>व्यतीयाय पतिंवरा सा R. 6. 67.<BR>--4 To<BR>surpass, excel.<BR>--5 To neglect, omit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीत|व्यतीतः
व्यतीत p. p.<BR>1 Passed, gone,<BR>elapsed, passed over; R. 5. 14.<BR>--2 Dead.<BR>--3 Left, abandoned, departed from.<BR>--4 Disregarded, omitted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्ययः|व्यत्यय
व्यत्ययः<BR>1 Passing over.<BR>--2<BR>Opposition, contrariety.<BR>--3 Inverted<BR>order, inversion.<BR>--4 Interchange,<BR>transmutation.<BR>--5 Obstruction,<BR>hindrance; Pt. 4. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यतीपातः|व्यतीपात
व्यतीपातः<BR>1 Total departure,<BR>complete deviation.<BR>--2 Any great<BR>portentous calamity, or a portent<BR>foreboding a great calamity.<BR>--3<BR>Disrespect, contempt.<BR>--4 The<BR>seventeenth of the astronomical Yogas.<BR>--5 The day of full-moon (when it<BR>falls on a Monday).<BR>--6 A malignant<BR>or evil aspect of the sun and moon<BR>(considered to be inauspicious for<BR>the performance of any action).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यस्
व्यत्यस् {vI.v} {c2c} A. (व्यतिहे, व्यतिसे,<BR>व्यतिस्ते) To excel, surpass, be above or<BR>superior to, outweigh; अन्यो व्यतिस्ते<BR>तु ममापि धर्मः Bk. 2. 35. {vII.v} {c4c} P.<BR>To invert, reverse, change upside<BR>down; see व्यत्यस्त below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यस्त
व्यत्यस्त p. p.<BR>1 Reversed,<BR>inverted.<BR>--2 Contrary, opposite.<BR>--3<BR>Incoherent; व्यत्यस्तं लपति<BR>Bv. 2. 84.<BR>--4 Crossed, placed<BR>crosswise; व्यत्यस्तपादः, व्यत्यस्तभुजः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यत्यासः|व्यत्यास
व्यत्यासः<BR>1 Inverted position or<BR>order.<BR>--2 Opposition, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथ्
व्यथ् {c1c} A. (व्यथते, व्यथित)<BR>1 To<BR>be sorry, to be pained, vexed or<BR>afflicted, be agitated or disquieted;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">Page1018-a+ 57</a>]<BR>विश्वंभरापि नाम व्यथते इति<BR>जितमपत्यस्नेहेन U. 7; न विव्यथे तस्य मनः<BR>Ki. 1. 2, 24.<BR>--2 To be disturbed, be<BR>ruffled or agitated; व्यथितसिंधुमनीरशनैः<BR>शनैः Ki. 5. 11.<BR>--3 To tremble.<BR>--4<BR>To be afraid.<BR>--5 To dry, become<BR>dry. --Caus. (व्यथयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>pain, distress, vex, annoy;<BR>U. 1. 28.<BR>--2 To frustrate, mar.<BR>--3 To<BR>frighten, terrify.<BR>--4 To lead or turn<BR>away. --WITH प्र to be excessively<BR>vexed; Bg. 11. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1017-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथक|व्यथकः
व्यथक a. (थिका f.) Painful,<BR>distressing; Ki. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथनं|व्यथन
व्यथनं<BR>1 Giving pain, tormenting.<BR>--2 (In Ved. gram.) Change,<BR>variation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथा
व्यथा [व्यथ्-भावे-अङ्]<BR>1 Pain,<BR>agony, anguish; तां च व्यथां<BR>प्रसवकालकृतामवाप्य U. 4. 23, 1. 12.<BR>--2<BR>Fear, alarm, anxiety:<BR>स्वंतमित्यलघयत्स तद्व्यथां R. 11. 62.<BR>--3 Agitation,<BR>disquietude.<BR>--4 Disease.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a. painful, troublesome,<BR>hurtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यथित|व्यथितः
व्यथित p. p.<BR>1 Afflicted,<BR>distressed, pained.<BR>--2 Alarmed.<BR>--3<BR>Agitated, disquieted, troubled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्
व्यध् {c4c} P. (विध्यति, विद्ध)<BR>1 To<BR>pierce, hurt, strike, stab, kill;<BR>यूनां मनांसि विव्याध दृष्ट्वा दृष्ट्वा मनोभवः<BR>H. 2. 111; अक्षितारासु विव्याध द्विषतः स<BR>तनुत्रिणः Śi. 19. 99; विद्धमात्रः<BR>R. 5. 51, 9. 60, 14. 70; Bk. 5. 52,<BR>9. 66, 15. 69.<BR>--2 To bore,<BR>perforate, pierce through.<BR>--3 To pick.<BR>--4 To wave or brandish in triumph<BR>(as the tail &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यधः|व्यध
व्यधः [व्यध्-अच्]<BR>1 Piercing,<BR>splitting, hitting; Śi. 7. 24.<BR>--2<BR>Smiting, wounding, striking.<BR>--3<BR>Perforating.<BR>--4 A stroke, wound.<BR>--धा<BR>Bleeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यधिकरणं|व्यधिकरण
व्यधिकरणं Subsisting in<BR>different receptacles or substrata; (as<BR>in व्यधिकरणबहुव्रीहि which means<BR>‘a Bahuvrīhi compound, the first<BR>member of which is not in<BR>apposition, or stands in a different<BR>caserelation, to the second, in the<BR>dissolution of the compound; e. g.<BR>चक्रपाणिः, चंद्रमौलिः &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्यः|व्यध्य
व्यध्यः A butt, target, a mark<BR>to aim at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यध्वः|व्यध्व
व्यध्वः A bad or wrong road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यनुनादः|व्यनुनाद
व्यनुनादः Reverberation, loud<BR>echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यंतरः|व्यन्तर|व्यन्तरः
व्यंतरः A spirit, a kind of<BR>supernatural being; अस्माकं कश्चिद् व्यंतरः<BR>सिद्धः Pt. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यप्
व्यप् {c10c} U. (व्यापयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>throw.<BR>--2 To diminish, waste,<BR>decrease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपकृष्
व्यपकृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To draw away.<BR>--2 To lead astray, seduce.<BR>--3 To<BR>remove, take away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपकृष्ट
व्यपकृष्ट p. p. Drawn aside, taken<BR>away, removed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगम्
व्यपगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go away,<BR>retire, retreat.<BR>--2 To disappear,<BR>vanish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगत
व्यपगत p. p.<BR>1 Gone away,<BR>departed, disappeared; मदो मे व्य गतः<BR>Bh. 2. 8; Me. 76.<BR>--2 Removed.<BR>--3 Fallen away from, deprived of,<BR>free from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपगमः|व्यपगम
व्यपगमः Departure, disappearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपत्रप्
व्यपत्रप् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To turn away<BR>through shame.<BR>--2 To be ashamed,<BR>feel ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपत्रप
व्यपत्रप a. Shameless, impudent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदिश्
व्यपदिश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To name, call;<BR>व्यपदिश्यसे जगति विक्रमीत्यतः<BR>Śi. 15. 28.<BR>--2 To name or call falsely;<BR>मित्रं च मां व्यपदिशस्यपरं च यासि<BR>Mk. 4. 9.<BR>--3 To speak of, profess;<BR>जन्मेंदोर्विमले कुले व्यपदिशसि Ve. 6. 7.<BR>--4<BR>To pretend, feign; Mv. 2. 11.<BR>--5<BR>To indicate, show.<BR>--6 To signify,<BR>mean, denote.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदिष्ट
व्यपदिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Named.<BR>--2 Shown,<BR>represented, signified.<BR>--3 Pleaded<BR>as a pretext or excuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदेशः|व्यपदेश
व्यपदेशः<BR>1 Representation,<BR>information, notice.<BR>--2 Designation by<BR>name, naming.<BR>--3 A name, an<BR>appellation, a title; एवंव्यपदेशभाजः<BR>U. 6.<BR>--4 A family, race; अथ कोस्य<BR>व्यपदेशः Ś. 7; व्यपदेशमाविलयितुं<BR>किमीहसे जनमिमं च पातयितुं Ś. 5. 21.<BR>--5 Fame, reputation, renown.<BR>--6<BR>A trick, pretext, excuse, device.<BR>--7<BR>Fraud, craft.<BR>--8 Concealment,<BR>dissimulation; Mal. {7}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपदेष्टृ
व्यपदेष्टृ m. A cheat, an impostor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरुह्
व्यपरुह् Caus.<BR>1 To eradicate,<BR>extirpate.<BR>--2 To remove.<BR>--3 To<BR>deprive of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपरोपणं|व्यपरोपण
व्यपरोपणं<BR>1 Extirpating,<BR>uprooting.<BR>--2 Expelling, removing,<BR>driving away.<BR>--3 Cutting off, tearing<BR>out, plucking; चुकोप तस्मै स भृशं<BR>सुरस्त्रियः प्रसह्यकेशव्यपरोपणादिव R. 3. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपवृत्
व्यपवृत् {1} A<BR>1 To return, turn<BR>back; चेतः कथं कथमपि व्य पवर्तते मे<BR>Māl. 1. 18.<BR>--2 To desist from,<BR>leave; U. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपवर्तनं
व्यपवर्तनं Return.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाकृतिः|व्यपाकृति
व्यपाकृतिः f.<BR>1 Expelling,<BR>driving away.<BR>--2 Denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपायः|व्यपाय
व्यपायः End, disappearance,<BR>close; Ku. 3. 33, R. 3. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपाश्रयः|व्यपाश्रय
व्यपाश्रयः<BR>1 Succession.<BR>--2<BR>Taking refuge with, having recourse to,<BR>trusting to; Bg. 3. 18.<BR>--3<BR>Depending on; धर्मो रामव्यपाश्रयः Rām.<BR>--4<BR>Expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपे
व्यपे {c2c} P.<BR>1 To depart or deviate<BR>from, be free from; व्यपेतमदमत्सरः<BR>Y. 1. 268; स्मृत्याचारव्यपेतेन मार्गेण<BR>2. 5.<BR>--2 To go away, separate, part<BR>asunder; समेत्य च व्यपेयातां<BR>H. 4. 69; Ms. 9. 142; 11. 98.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेत
व्यपेत p. p.<BR>1 Separated, severed.<BR>--2 Gone away, departed; oft. in<BR>comp.; व्यपेतकल्मष, व्यपेतभी, व्यपेतहर्ष<BR>&c.<BR>--3 Contrary, opposed to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्ष्
व्यपेक्ष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To mind, care for,<BR>regard; न व्यपैक्षत समुत्सुकाः प्रजाः<BR>R. 19. 6.<BR>--2 To expect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्ष
व्यपेक्ष a.<BR>1 Expecting, expectant.<BR>--2 Eager, attentive.<BR>--3 Regarding,<BR>minding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षा
व्यपेक्षा<BR>1 Expectation, hope.<BR>--2<BR>Regard, consideration; R. 8. 24.<BR>--3 Mutual relation,<BR>inter-dependence.<BR>--4 Mutual regard.<BR>--5<BR>Application.<BR>--6 (In gram.) The mutual<BR>application of two rules.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षणं|व्यपेक्षण
व्यपेक्षणं Expecting, expectation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपेक्षित
व्यपेक्षित p. p.<BR>1 Hoped,<BR>expected.<BR>--2 Regarded, minded.<BR>--3<BR>Mutually connected.<BR>--4 Employed,<BR>applied, used.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोढ
व्यपोढ p. p.<BR>1 Expelled, removed.<BR>--2 Contrary, opposite; Ki. 4. 15.<BR>--3 Manifested, displayed, shown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोह्
व्यपोह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To atone for,<BR>expiate.<BR>--2 To heal, cure.<BR>--3 To<BR>drive away, remove, keep off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यपोहः|व्यपोह
व्यपोहः Expelling, driving a way,<BR>keeping off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचर्
व्यभिचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go astray,<BR>deviate from; as in अव्यभिचरित<BR>साध्यसामान्याधिकरण्यं व्यप्तिः Tarka K.<BR>--2<BR>To transgress against, be faithless to.<BR>--3 To act crookedly.<BR>--4 To offend,<BR>injure.<BR>--5 To fail, miscarry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारः|व्यभिचार
व्यभि(भी)चारः<BR>1 Going away<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-a" target="_blank">Page1019-a+ 57</a>]<BR>from, deviation, leaving the right<BR>course, following improper courses;<BR>मंत्रज्ञमव्यसनिनं व्यभिचाराविवार्जित<BR>H. 3. 16, Bg. 14. 26.<BR>--2 Transgression,<BR>violation; Ms. 10. 24.<BR>--3 Error,<BR>crime, sin.<BR>--4 Separableness.<BR>--5<BR>Infidelity, faithlessness (of a wife<BR>or husband), unchastity;<BR>व्यभिचारात्तु भर्तुः स्त्री लोके प्राप्नोति गर्ह्यतां<BR>Ms. 5. 164; वाङ्मनः कर्मभिः पत्यौ<BR>व्यभिचारोयथा न मे R. 15. 81; Y. 1. 72.<BR>--6<BR>An anomaly, irregularity,<BR>exception (to a rule.)<BR>--7 (In logic)<BR>A fallacious hetu, the presence of<BR>the hetu without the sādhya; हेतोः<BR>साध्याभाववद्वृत्तित्वं व्यभिचारः Tarka K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभीचारः|व्यभीचार
व्यभि(भी)चारः<BR>1 Going away<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-a" target="_blank">Page1019-a+ 57</a>]<BR>from, deviation, leaving the right<BR>course, following improper courses;<BR>मंत्रज्ञमव्यसनिनं व्यभिचाराविवार्जित<BR>H. 3. 16, Bg. 14. 26.<BR>--2 Transgression,<BR>violation; Ms. 10. 24.<BR>--3 Error,<BR>crime, sin.<BR>--4 Separableness.<BR>--5<BR>Infidelity, faithlessness (of a wife<BR>or husband), unchastity;<BR>व्यभिचारात्तु भर्तुः स्त्री लोके प्राप्नोति गर्ह्यतां<BR>Ms. 5. 164; वाङ्मनः कर्मभिः पत्यौ<BR>व्यभिचारोयथा न मे R. 15. 81; Y. 1. 72.<BR>--6<BR>An anomaly, irregularity,<BR>exception (to a rule.)<BR>--7 (In logic)<BR>A fallacious hetu, the presence of<BR>the hetu without the sādhya; हेतोः<BR>साध्याभाववद्वृत्तित्वं व्यभिचारः Tarka K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1018-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारिणी
व्यभिचारिणी An unchaste wife,<BR>adulteress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यभिचारिन्
व्यभिचारिन् a.<BR>1 Straying or<BR>deviating from, going astray, erring,<BR>trespassing.<BR>--2 Irregular,<BR>anomalous.<BR>--3 Untrue, false; see अव्याभचारन्.<BR>--4 Faithless, unchaste, adulterous.<BR>--5 Profligate, wanton.<BR>--6<BR>Departing from its usual meaning, having<BR>several secondary meanings (as a<BR>word) --m. व्यभिचारिभावः A<BR>transitory feeling. an accessory (opp.<BR>स्थायन or स्थायिभाव q. v.). (Though like<BR>the Sthāyibhāvas these<BR>accessories do not form a necessary<BR>substratum of any rasa, still they<BR>act as feeders to the prevailing<BR>sentiment, and strengthen it in<BR>various ways, whether openly or<BR>covertly. They are said to be 33 or 34<BR>in number; for an enumeration<BR>of these, see K. P. 4 Kārikās 31-34,<BR>S. D. 169; or R. G. first Ānana;<BR>cf. विभाव and स्थायिभाव also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय्
व्यय् {vI.v} {c10c} U. (व्यययति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>go, move.<BR>--2 To expend, give<BR>away, bestow. {vII.v} {c1c} U. (व्ययति-ते)<BR>To go, move. {vIII.v} {c10c} U. (व्याययति-ते,<BR>also व्यापयति-ते)<BR>1 To throw, cast.<BR>--2<BR>To drive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यय|व्ययं|व्ययः
व्यय a. Liable to change,<BR>mutable, perishable; cf. अव्यय.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>(a) Loss, disappearance,<BR>destruction; आपाद्यते न व्ययमंतरायैः<BR>कच्चिन्महर्षेस्त्रविधं तपस्पत् R. 5. 5, 12. 23.<BR>(b) Cost, sacrifice; प्राणव्ययेनापि<BR>मया विधेयः Māl. 4. 5. Ku. 3. 23.<BR>--2 Hindrance, obstacle;<BR>भूयस्तपोव्ययो मा भूत् R. 15. 37.<BR>--3 Decay,<BR>decline, overthrow, downfall.<BR>--4<BR>Expenditure, expense, outlay,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">Page1019-b+ 56</a>]<BR>spending, applying to use (opp. आय);<BR>आये दुःख व्यये दुःख धिगर्थाः<BR>कष्टसंश्रयाः Pt. 1. 163; आयधिकं व्ययं<BR>करोति ‘he lives beyond his means’;<BR>R. 5. 12, 15. 3; Ms. 9. 11.<BR>--5<BR>Extravagance, prodigality.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पर a. lavish in expenditure;<BR>Pt. 5. 61.<BR>--पराङ्मुख a. stingy,<BR>niggardly.<BR>--शील a. spendthrift, prodigal.<BR>--शुद्धिः f. defraying^1 of expenses.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययनं|व्ययन
व्ययनं<BR>1 Spending.<BR>--2 Wasting,<BR>destroying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ययित|व्ययितः
व्ययित p. p.<BR>1 Expended, spent.<BR>--2 Wasted, fallen into decay.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थ|व्यर्थं
व्यर्थ a. [विगतोऽर्थः प्रयोजनं वाऽस्य]<BR>1<BR>Useless, vain, fruitless,<BR>unprofitable; व्यर्थं यत्र कपींद्रसख्यमपि मे<BR>U. 3. 45.<BR>--2 Meaningless, unmeaning,<BR>idle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यर्थक
व्यर्थक = व्यर्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यलीक|व्यलीकं|व्यलीकः
व्यलीक a.<BR>1 False, untrue.<BR>--2<BR>Offensive, disagreeable, displeasing.<BR>--3 Not false; Śi. 5. 1.<BR>--4 Unfit to<BR>be done.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A libertine.<BR>--2 A<BR>catamite.<BR>--कं<BR>1 Anything<BR>disagreeable or displeasing,<BR>disagreeableness; इत्थं गिरः प्रिवतमा इव रोऽ<BR>व्यलीकाः शुश्राव सूततनयस्य तदा व्यलीकाः<BR>Śi. 5. 1.<BR>--2 Any cause of grief or<BR>uneasiness, pain, sorrow, grief;<BR>सुतनु हृदयात्प्रत्यादेशव्यलीकमपैतु ते<BR>Ś. 7. 24; यस्मिन्ननैश्वर्यकृतव्यलीकः पराभवं<BR>प्राप इवांतकोपि Ki. 3. 19; Ku. 3. 25;<BR>R. 4. 87.<BR>--3 A fault, an offence, a<BR>transgression, any improper act;<BR>सव्यलीकमवधीरितखिन्नं प्रस्थितं सपदि<BR>कोपपदेन Ki. 9. 45; Śi. 9. 85; एवं<BR>प्रत्यक्षदृष्टव्यलीकः किं ब्रवीमि Ratn. 3, 3. 15.<BR>--4 Fraud, trick, deception;<BR>Pt. 1. 120, 242.<BR>--5 Falsehood.<BR>--6<BR>Inversion, contrariety.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवकलनं|व्यवकलन
व्यवकलनं<BR>1 Separation.<BR>--2 (In<BR>math.) Subtraction, deduction (<BR>व्यवकलितं also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवक्रोशनं|व्यवक्रोशन
व्यवक्रोशनं<BR>1 Wrangling, mutual<BR>abuse.<BR>--2 Abuse in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छिद्
व्यवच्छिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To cut off,<BR>separate, detach from.<BR>--2 To<BR>interrupt.<BR>--3 To particularize, specify,<BR>distinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छिन्न|व्यवच्छिन्नं|व्यवछिन्न
व्यवच्छिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Cut off, rent<BR>asunder, torn off.<BR>--2 Separated,<BR>divided.<BR>--3 Particularized, specified.<BR>--4<BR>Marked, distinguished; शरीरं<BR>तावदिष्टार्थव्यवच्छिन्ना पदावली Kāv. 1. 10.<BR>--5 Interrupetd.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवच्छेदः|व्यवच्छेद|व्यवछेद
व्यवच्छेदः<BR>1 Cutting off, rending<BR>asunder.<BR>--2 Dividing, separating.<BR>--3 Dissection.<BR>--4 Particularizing.<BR>--5 Distinguishing.<BR>--6 Contrast,<BR>distinction.<BR>--7 Determination.<BR>--8<BR>Shooting, letting fly (as an arrow).<BR>--9 A chapter or section of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधा
व्यवधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To place<BR>between, interpose, intervene; प्रेक्ष्य<BR>स्थितां सहचरीं व्यवधाय देहं R. 9. 57,<BR>--2 To hide, conceal, screen;<BR>शापव्यवहितस्मृतिः Ś. 5.<BR>--3 To separate,<BR>divide.<BR>--4 To obstruct, interrupt.<BR>--5 To neglect, omit, pass over; see<BR>व्यवहित also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधा
व्यवधा<BR>1 That which intervenes.<BR>--2 A cover, screen, partition.<BR>--3<BR>Concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधानं|व्यवधान
व्यवधानं<BR>1 Intervention,<BR>interposition, separation.<BR>--2<BR>Obstruction, hiding from view; दृष्टिं<BR>विमानव्यवधानमुक्तां पुनः सहस्रार्चिषि संनिधत्ते<BR>R. 13. 44.<BR>--3 Concealment,<BR>disappearance.<BR>--4 A screen, partition.<BR>--5 A cover, covering;<BR>शार्दूलचर्मव्यवधानवत्यां Ku. 3. 44.<BR>--6 Interval,<BR>space.<BR>--7 (In gram.) The<BR>intervention of a syllable or letter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधायक|व्यवधायकः
व्यवधायक a. (यिका f.)<BR>1<BR>Intervening, screening, covering.<BR>--2<BR>Obstructing, hiding.<BR>--3 Intermediate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवधिः|व्यवधि
व्यवधिः Covering, intervention<BR>&c.; see व्यवधान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहित|व्यवहितः
व्यवहित p. p.<BR>1 Placed apart.<BR>--2<BR>Separated by anything intervening;<BR>Śi. 2. 85.<BR>--3 Interrupted, stopped,<BR>obstructed, impeded.<BR>--4 Screened<BR>from view, hidden, concealed.<BR>--5<BR>Not immediately connected.<BR>--6 Done,<BR>performed.<BR>--7 Passed over, omitted.<BR>--8 Surpassed, excelled.<BR>--9 Hostile;<BR>opposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसो
व्यवसो {c4c} P.<BR>1 To strive,<BR>endeavour, try, seek, attempt, set<BR>about; ध्रुवं स नीलोत्पलपत्रधारया<BR>शमीलतां छेत्तुमृषिर्व्यवस्यति Ś. 1. 18; V. 4.<BR>--2 To think of, wish, desire; पातुं<BR>न प्रथमं व्यवस्यति जलं युष्मास्वपीतेषु या<BR>Ś. 4. 8.<BR>--3 To exert strenuously,<BR>be industrious or diligent.<BR>--4 To<BR>resolve, determine, settle, decide;<BR>Ś. 5. 19.<BR>--5 To accept, undertake;<BR>कच्चित्सौम्य व्यवसितमिदं बंधुकृत्यं त्वया<BR>मे Me. 114.<BR>--6 To be convinced or<BR>persuaded.<BR>--7 To reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसायः|व्यवसाय
व्यवसायः<BR>1 Effort, exertion,<BR>energy, industry, perseverance; करोतु<BR>नाम नीतिज्ञो व्यवसायमितस्ततः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-a" target="_blank">Page1020-a+ 57</a>]<BR>H. 2. 14.<BR>--2 Resolve, resolution,<BR>determination; मंदीचकार मरणव्यवसायबुद्धिं<BR>Ku. 4. 45 ‘the thought of<BR>resolving to die’; Bg. 2. 41, 10. 36.<BR>--3 An act, action, performance;<BR>व्यवसायः प्रतिपत्तिनिष्टुरः R. 8. 65.<BR>--4<BR>(a) Business, employment, trade.<BR>(b) Following a particular<BR>profession or trade.<BR>--5 Conduct,<BR>behaviour.<BR>--6 Device, stratagem, artifice.<BR>--7 Boasting.<BR>--8 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--9<BR>Of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1019-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसायिन्
व्यवसायिन् a.<BR>1 Energetic,<BR>industrious, diligent; Pt. 2. 51.<BR>--2<BR>Resolute. persevering; Pt. 1. 248.<BR>--3 Performing, doing, undertaking.<BR>--4 Engaged in any business or<BR>profession. --m. A tradesman,<BR>merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवसित|व्यवसितः
व्यवसित p. p.<BR>1 Endeavoured,<BR>attempted; Ś. 6. 8.<BR>--2 Undertaken.<BR>--3 Resolved, determined settled.<BR>--4 Devised, planned.<BR>--5<BR>Endeavouring, resolving.<BR>--6 Persevering,<BR>energetic.<BR>--7 Cheated, deceived.<BR>--तं Ascertainment, determination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्था
व्यवस्था {c1c} A.<BR>1 To be placed<BR>asunder.<BR>--2 To be arranged in due<BR>order.<BR>--3 To be settled or fixed,<BR>become permanent, वचतीयमिदं<BR>व्यवस्थितं Ku. 4. 21.<BR>--4 To rest or<BR>depend upon. --Caus.<BR>1 To place or<BR>rest upon, direct towards;<BR>Ku. 7. 75.<BR>--2 To arrange, manage, adjust.<BR>--3 To settle, resolve, decree.<BR>--4<BR>To separate, place apart.<BR>--5 To do,<BR>perform.<BR>--6 To lay down a rule or<BR>law, enact a law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्था
व्यवस्था<BR>1 Adjustment,<BR>arrangement, settlement; as in<BR>वर्णाश्रमव्यवस्था.<BR>--2 Fixity,<BR>definiteness; R. 7. 54.<BR>--3 Fixity,<BR>firm basis; आजहतुस्तच्चरणौ<BR>पृथिव्यां स्थलारविंदश्रियमव्यवस्थां<BR>Ku. 1. 33.<BR>--4 Relative position.<BR>--5 A<BR>settled rule, law, statute, decree,<BR>decision, legal opinion, written<BR>declaration of the law (especially<BR>on doubtful points or where<BR>contradictory texts have to be properly<BR>adjusted).<BR>--6 An agreement, a<BR>contract.<BR>--7 State, condition.<BR>--8<BR>State or order of things.<BR>--9<BR>Separation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थानं|व्यवस्थान|व्यवस्थानः
व्यवस्थानं, व्यवस्थितिः f.<BR>1<BR>Arrangement, settlement, determination,<BR>decision.<BR>--2 A rule, statute,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">Page1020-b+ 57</a>]<BR>decision.<BR>--3 Steadiness, constancy<BR>--4 Firmness, perseverance.<BR>--5<BR>Separation.<BR>--नः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थितिः|व्यवस्थिति
व्यवस्थानं, व्यवस्थितिः f.<BR>1<BR>Arrangement, settlement, determination,<BR>decision.<BR>--2 A rule, statute,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">Page1020-b+ 57</a>]<BR>decision.<BR>--3 Steadiness, constancy<BR>--4 Firmness, perseverance.<BR>--5<BR>Separation.<BR>--नः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापक
व्यवस्थापक a. (पिका f.)<BR>1<BR>Arranging, putting in proper order,<BR>adjusting, settling, establishing,<BR>deciding.<BR>--2 One who gives a<BR>legal opinion.<BR>--3 A manager<BR>(modern use).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापनं|व्यवस्थापन
व्यवस्थापनं<BR>1 Arranging, proper<BR>adjustment.<BR>--2 Fixing,<BR>determining, settling, deciding.<BR>--3 Fixing,<BR>placing (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थापित
व्यवस्थापित p. p. Arranged,<BR>settled &c.; कथचिदद्रेस्ततया मिताक्षरं<BR>चिरव्यवस्थापितवागभाषत Ku. 5. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थित|व्यवस्थितः
व्यवस्थित p. p.<BR>1 Placed in order,<BR>adjusted, arranged.<BR>--2 Settled,<BR>fixed; किं व्यवस्थितविषयाः क्षात्रधर्माः<BR>U. 5.<BR>--3 Decided, determined,<BR>declared by law.<BR>--4 Stood aside,<BR>separated.<BR>--5 Extracted.<BR>--6 Based<BR>on, resting on.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विभाषा a<BR>fixed option; व्यवस्थितविमाषया<BR>साधुः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवस्थिति|व्यवस्थितिः
व्यवस्थिति See व्यवस्थान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहित|व्यवहितः
व्यवहित See under व्यवधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहृ
व्यवहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To deal in any<BR>transaction or business.<BR>--2 To act,<BR>behave, deal with (with loc. or by<BR>itself); कथं कार्यविनिमयेत व्यवहरति<BR>मय्यनात्मज्ञः M. 1;<BR>बहिःसर्वाकारप्रगुणरमणीयं व्यवहरन् Māl. 1. 14.<BR>--3 To<BR>go to law, sue (one) in a court of<BR>law;<BR>अर्थपतिर्व्यवहर्तुमर्थगौरवादभियोक्ष्यते Dk.<BR>--4 To manage, transact<BR>business; U. 1. 5.<BR>--5 To regain,<BR>recover.<BR>--6 To distinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहर्तृ|व्यवहर्त्तृ
व्यवहर्तृ^1 m.<BR>1 The manager of a<BR>business.<BR>--2 A suer, litigant,<BR>plaintiff.<BR>--3 A judge.<BR>--4 An associate.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारः|व्यवहार
व्यवहारः<BR>1 Conduct, behaviour,<BR>action.<BR>--2 Affair, business, work.<BR>--3 Profession, occupation.<BR>--4<BR>Dealing, transaction.<BR>--5 Commerce,<BR>trade, traffic.<BR>--6 Dealing in money,<BR>usury.<BR>--7 Usage, custom, an<BR>established rule or practice.<BR>--8 Relation,<BR>connection; Pt. 1. 79.<BR>--9 Judicial<BR>procedure, trial or investigation of<BR>a case, administration of justice;<BR>व्यवहारस्तमाह्वयति; अलं लज्जया<BR>व्यवहारस्त्वां पृच्छति Mk. 9.<BR>--10 A legal<BR>dispute, complaint, suit, law-suit,<BR>litigation; व्यवहारोऽयं<BR>चारुदत्तप्तवलंबते, इति लिख्यतां व्यवहारस्य प्रथमः पा<BR>दः, केन सह मम व्यवहारः Mk. 9;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-c" target="_blank">Page1020-c+ 57</a>]<BR>R. 17. 39.<BR>--11 A title of legal<BR>procedure, any occasion of litigation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं the body of civil<BR>and criminal law.<BR>--अभिशस्त a.<BR>prosecuted, charged.<BR>--अयग्येः a minor<BR>(in law).<BR>--आसनं the tribunal of<BR>justice, judgment-seat;<BR>व्यवहारासनमाददे युवा R. 8. 18.<BR>--ज्ञः {1} one who<BR>understands business. {2} a youth<BR>come of age, one who is no longer<BR>a minor. {3} one who is<BR>acquainted with judicial procedure.<BR>--तंत्रं<BR>course of conduct; वाक्प्रतिष्ठानिबंधनानि<BR>देहिनां व्यवहारतत्रांणि Māl. 4.<BR>--दर्शनं<BR>trial, judicial investigation.<BR>--पदं =<BR>व्यवहारविषय q. v.<BR>--पादः {1} any one<BR>of the four stages of a legal<BR>proceeding; these are four: --(1) पूर्वपक्ष,<BR>the plaint; (2) उत्तरपक्ष the defence;<BR>(3) क्रियापाद adducing evidence, oral<BR>or written; (4) निर्णयपाद, the decision<BR>or verdict. {2} the fourth stage;<BR>i. e. निर्णयपाद, that part which<BR>concerns the verdict or decision.<BR>--मातृका {1} a legal process in general. {2}<BR>any act or subject relating to the<BR>administration of justice or<BR>formation of courts (of which thirty<BR>heads are enumerated).<BR>--विधिः a<BR>rule of law, any code of law.<BR>--विषयः (so<BR>--पदं, --मार्गः, --स्थानं) a<BR>subject or head of legal procedure,<BR>an actionable business, a matter<BR>which may be made the subject of<BR>litigation (these are eighteen; for<BR>an enumeration of their names,<BR>see Ms. 8. 4-7).<BR>--स्थितिः f. judicial<BR>procedure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारकः|व्यवहारक
व्यवहारकः A dealer, trader,<BR>merchant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिक|व्यवहारिकः
व्यवहारिक a. (का or की f.)<BR>1<BR>Relating to business.<BR>--2 Engaged<BR>in business, practical.<BR>--3 Judicial,<BR>legal.<BR>--4 Litigant.<BR>--5 Usual,<BR>customary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिका
व्यवहारिका<BR>1 Usage, custom.<BR>--2 A<BR>broom.<BR>--3 The Iṅgudī plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहारिन्
व्यवहारिन् a.<BR>1 Transacting<BR>business, acting, practising.<BR>--2<BR>Engaged in a law suit, litigant.<BR>--3 Usual,<BR>customary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहार्य|व्यवहार्य्य|व्यवहार्य्यः
व्यवहार्य a.<BR>1 Usual, customary.<BR>--2<BR>Liable to be sued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवहृतिः|व्यवहृति
व्यवहृतिः f.<BR>1 Practice, process.<BR>--2<BR>Action, performance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवे
व्यवे {c2c} P.<BR>1 To divide, separate.<BR>--2 To dissolve, decompose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1020-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवायः|व्यवाय|व्यवायं
व्यवायः<BR>1 Separation,<BR>decomposition, resolution (into components).<BR>--2 Dissolution.<BR>--3 Covering,<BR>concealment.<BR>--4 Intervention, interval;<BR>अट्कुप्वाङ्नुम्व्यवायेऽपि.<BR>--5 An<BR>impediment, obstacle.<BR>--6 Copulation,<BR>sexual intercourse.<BR>--7 Purity.<BR>--यं<BR>Light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवायिन्
व्यवायिन् a.<BR>1 Resolving,<BR>decomposing.<BR>--2 Lustful, dissolute. --m.<BR>1<BR>A sensualist, libertine.<BR>--2 An<BR>aphrodisiac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यवेत
व्यवेत p. p.<BR>1 Separated,<BR>decomposed.<BR>--2 Different.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यश्
व्यश् {c5c} A.<BR>1 To fill completely,<BR>pervade, occupy; प्रतापस्तस्य भानोश्च<BR>युगपद् व्यानशे दिशः R. 4. 15;<BR>Bk. 9. 4; 14. 96.<BR>--2 To obtain, attain to,<BR>reach.<BR>--3 To possess, gain.<BR>--4 To<BR>fall to one's share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यष्टि
व्यष्टि f.<BR>1 Individuality,<BR>singleness.<BR>--2 Distributive pervasion.<BR>--3 (In Vedānta phil.) An<BR>aggregate or whole viewed as made up<BR>of many separate bodies (opp. समष्टि<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्
व्यस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To toss about,<BR>scatter, cast or throw asunder; dispel,<BR>destroy; प्राप्तो व्यालतमान् व्यस्यन्<BR>भुजंगेभ्योऽपि राक्षसान् Bk. 8. 116, 9. 31.<BR>--2 To divide into parts, separate,<BR>arrange; स्वयं वेदान् व्यस्यन् Pt. 4. 50;<BR>विव्यात वेदान् यस्मात्स तस्माद् व्यास इति<BR>स्मृतः Mb.; R. 10. 84.<BR>--3 To take<BR>separately or singly; see व्यस्त<BR>below.<BR>--4 To throw over, overturn,<BR>upset.<BR>--5 To expel, remove, drive<BR>away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनं|व्यसन
व्यसनं<BR>1 Casting away, dispelling.<BR>--2<BR>Separating, dividing.<BR>--3 Violation,<BR>infraction.<BR>--4 Loss, destruction, defeat,<BR>fall; defection, weak point;<BR>अमात्यव्यसनं Pt. 3; स्वबलव्यसने<BR>Ki. 13. 15; Śi. 2. 57.<BR>--5 (a) A calamity,<BR>misfortune, distress, evil, disaster'<BR>ill-luck; अज्ञातभर्तृव्यसना मुहूर्तं<BR>कृतोपकारेव रतिर्बभूव Ku. 3. 73,<BR>4. 30; R. 12. 57. (b) Adversity’<BR>need; स सुहृद् व्यसने यः स्यात्<BR>Pt. 1. 337 ‘a friend in need is a friend<BR>indeed’.<BR>--6 Setting (as of the sun<BR>&c.); तेजोद्वयस्य<BR>युगपद्व्यसनोदयाभ्यां Ś. 4. 1 (where व्यसन<BR>means ‘a fall’ also).<BR>--7 Vice, bad<BR>practice, evil habit; मिथ्यैव व्यसनं<BR>वदंति मृगयामीदृग् विनोदः कुतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-b" target="_blank">Page1021-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Ś. 2. 5, R. 18. 14; Y. 1. 310; (these<BR>vices are usually said to be ten;<BR>see Ms. 7. 47-48);<BR>समानशीलव्यसनेषु सख्यं Subhāṣ.<BR>--8 Close or<BR>intent application, assiduous<BR>devotion; विद्यायां व्यसनं Bh. 2. 62, 63.<BR>--9 Inordinate addiction.<BR>--10 Crime,<BR>sin.<BR>--11 Punishment.<BR>--12<BR>Inability, incompetency.<BR>--13 Fruitless<BR>effort.<BR>--14 Air, wind.<BR>--15<BR>Individuality.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिभारः heavy<BR>calamity or distress; R. 14. 68.<BR>--अन्वित, --आर्त, --पीडित a. overtaken<BR>by calamity, involved in distress.<BR>--प्रहरिन् a. {1} hurting, attacking,<BR>giving trouble. {2} striking (an<BR>enemy) in his weak point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसनिन्
व्यसनिन् a.<BR>1 Addicted to any<BR>vice, vicious.<BR>--2 Unlucky,<BR>unfortunate.<BR>--3 Intently attached or<BR>excessively devoted to anything, fond<BR>of (usually in comp.); किं<BR>भूमृत्कटकस्थितिव्यसनिना व्यर्थं खुराः शातिताः<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्त|व्यस्तः
व्यस्त p. p.<BR>1 Cast or thrown<BR>asunder, tossed about; Māl. 5. 23.<BR>--2 Dispersed, scattered; U. 5. 14.<BR>--3 Dispelled, cast away.<BR>--4<BR>Separated, divided, severed; हिमवति<BR>जलधौ च व्यस्ततोयेव गंगा V. 5. 22.<BR>--5 Taken or considered separately,<BR>taken singly (opp. समस्त); एभिः<BR>समस्तैरपि किमस्य किं पुतर्व्यस्तैः U. 5;<BR>तदस्ति किं व्यस्तमपि त्रिलोचने<BR>Ku. 5. 72.<BR>--6 Simple, uncompounded (as<BR>a word).<BR>--7 Manifold, different.<BR>--8 Removed, expelled.<BR>--9 Agitated,<BR>troubled, confused.<BR>--10 Disordered,<BR>out of order, disarranged.<BR>--11<BR>Reversed, upset.<BR>--12 Inverse (as<BR>ratio).<BR>--13 Pervading, inherent<BR>in.<BR>--स्तं ind. Severally,<BR>separately, singly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केश a. with<BR>disordered or dishevelled hair.<BR>--त्रैराशिकं the rule of three inverted.<BR>--पदं {1} (in law) a confused<BR>statement (of a case). {2} an<BR>uncompounded or simple word.<BR>--वृत्ति<BR>a. the meaning of which is<BR>changed, which has lost its force<BR>(as a word); R. 11. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यसु
व्यसु a. Lifeless, dead; Śi. 20. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यस्तारः|व्यस्तार|व्यस्तारं
व्यस्तारः The issue of rut or<BR>ichor from the temples of an<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकीर्ण
व्याकीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Scattered or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">Page1021-c+ 56</a>]<BR>thrown about.<BR>--2 Disordered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुल|व्याकुलः
व्याकुल a.<BR>1 Agitated,<BR>perplexed, bewildered, distracted;<BR>शोकव्याकुल, बाष्प˚.<BR>--2 Alarmed, troubled,<BR>frightened; वृष्टिव्याकुलगोकुल<BR>Gīt. 4.<BR>--3 Full of, overtaken by.<BR>--4<BR>Intently engaged in, busy with;<BR>आलोके ते निपतति पुरा सा बलिव्याकुला<BR>वा Me. 85.<BR>--5 Flashing, moving<BR>about; U. 3. 43.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन,<BR>चित्त, -चेतस्, -मनस् a. bewildered in<BR>mind, having a perplexed or<BR>distracted mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलयति
व्याकुलयति Den. P. To agitate,<BR>confuse, frighten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलित
व्याकुलित a. Agitated, distracted,<BR>confounded, perplexed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलीकृ
व्याकुलीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To confound,<BR>bewilder, perplex.<BR>--2 To alarm,<BR>trouble.<BR>--3 To agitate, perturb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकुलीभू
व्याकुलीभू {c1c} P. To become<BR>perplexed or confused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकूतिः|व्याकूति
व्याकूतिः f. Fraud, disguise,<BR>deception.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृ
व्याकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To make manifest,<BR>clear up; नामरूपे व्याकरवाणि Ch. Up.<BR>--2 To propound, explain.<BR>--3 To<BR>tell, narrate; तन्मे सर्वं भगवान्<BR>व्याकरोतु Mb.<BR>--4 To separate, divide,<BR>decompose.<BR>--5 To analyse in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकरणं|व्याकरण
व्याकरणं<BR>1 Analysis,<BR>decomposition.<BR>--2 Grammatical analysis,<BR>grammar, one of the six Vedāṅgas<BR>q. v.; सिंहो व्याकरणस्य कर्तुरहरत् प्राणान्<BR>प्रियान् पाणिनेः Pt. 2. 33.<BR>--3<BR>Explaining, expounding.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रक्रिया etymology, derivation (of a<BR>word).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकारः|व्याकार
व्याकारः<BR>1 Transformation, change<BR>of form.<BR>--2 Deformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृत
व्याकृत p. p.<BR>1 Analysed,<BR>separated.<BR>--2 Explained, expounded.<BR>--3<BR>Disfigured, distorted, deformed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकृतिः|व्याकृति
व्याकृतिः f.<BR>1 Analysis.<BR>--2<BR>Exposition, explanation.<BR>--3 Change of<BR>form, development.<BR>--4 Grammar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकोश|व्याकोशः
व्याकोश(ष) a.<BR>1 Expanded,<BR>blown, blossomed; व्याकोशकोकनदतां<BR>दधते नलिन्यः Śi. 4. 46.<BR>--2<BR>Developed; विवेकव्याकोशे विकसति शमे<BR>शाम्यति तृषा Bh. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याकोष|व्याकोषः
व्याकोश(ष) a.<BR>1 Expanded,<BR>blown, blossomed; व्याकोशकोकनदतां<BR>दधते नलिन्यः Śi. 4. 46.<BR>--2<BR>Developed; विवेकव्याकोशे विकसति शमे<BR>शाम्यति तृषा Bh. 3. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षिप्
व्याक्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To toss or throw<BR>about.<BR>--2 To stretch out or forth,<BR>open.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षिप्त
व्याक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Tossed about.<BR>--2<BR>Torn asunder, distracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1021-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षेपः|व्याक्षेप
व्याक्षेपः<BR>1 Tossing about.<BR>--2<BR>Obstruction, hindrance.<BR>--3 Delay;<BR>अव्याक्षेपो भविष्यंत्याः कार्यसिद्धेर्हि लक्षणं<BR>R. 10. 6.<BR>--4 Distraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याक्षोभः|व्याक्षोभ
व्याक्षोभः Agitation,<BR>perturbation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्या
व्याख्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 To tell,<BR>communicate, declare; Bk. 14. 113.<BR>--2<BR>To explain, relate; रावणस्यापि ते जन्म<BR>व्याख्यास्यामि Mb.<BR>--3 To name,<BR>call; विद्वद्वृंदैर्वीणावाणि व्याख्याता सा<BR>विद्युन्माला Śrut. 13.<BR>--4 To dwell at<BR>large, dilate or enlarge upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्या
व्याख्या<BR>1 Relation, narration.<BR>--2<BR>Explanation, exposition, comment,<BR>gloss.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यात|व्याख्यातः
व्याख्यात p. p.<BR>1 Related, narrated.<BR>--2 Explained, expounded,<BR>commented upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यातृ
व्याख्यातृ m. An expounder, a<BR>commentator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याख्यानं|व्याख्यान
व्याख्यानं<BR>1 Communication,<BR>narration.<BR>--2 Speech, lecture.<BR>--3<BR>Explanation, exposition,<BR>interpretation, comment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघट्टनं|व्याघट्टन
व्याघट्टनं<BR>1 Churning.<BR>--2<BR>Rubbing together, friction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघातः|व्याघात
व्याघातः<BR>1 Striking against.<BR>--2<BR>A blow, stroke.<BR>--3 An impediment,<BR>obstacle.<BR>--4 Contradiction.<BR>--5<BR>Disobedience; प्रथमं तावन्ममाज्ञाव्याघातः<BR>Mu. 3.<BR>--6 A figure of speech in<BR>which opposite effects are shown to<BR>be produced from the same cause or<BR>by the same agency; it is thus<BR>defined by Mammaṭa:<BR>--तद्यथा साधितं<BR>केनाप्यपरेण तदन्यथा । तथैव यद्विधीयेत स<BR>व्याघात इति स्मृतः K. P. 10; e. g. see<BR>Vb. 1. 2, or the quotation under विरूपाक्ष.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघातक
व्याघातक a.<BR>1 Striking against.<BR>--2 Opposing, resisting, thwarting,<BR>hindering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याघ्रः|व्याघ्र
व्याघ्रः [व्याजिघ्रति, व्याघ्रा-क]<BR>1 A<BR>tiger.<BR>--2 (At the end of comp.)<BR>Best, pre-eminent, chief; as in<BR>नरव्याघ्र, पुरुषव्याघ्र.<BR>--3 The red variety<BR>of the castor-oil plant.<BR>--घ्री A<BR>tigress; व्याघ्रीव तिष्ठति जरा परितर्जयंती<BR>Bh. 3. 109.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अटः a<BR>skylark.<BR>--आस्यः a cat.<BR>--दलः, --पुच्छः<BR>the castor-oil plant.<BR>--नखः -खं {1} a<BR>tiger's claw. {2} a kind of perfume.<BR>{3} a scratch, the impression of a<BR>fingernail.<BR>--नायकः a jackal.<BR>--पाद<BR>(द्) a. tiger-footed.<BR>--श्वन् m. a<BR>tiger-like dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याजः|व्याज
व्याजः<BR>1 Deceit, trick, deception.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">Page1022-b+ 55</a>]<BR>fraud.<BR>--2 Art, cunning;<BR>अव्याजमनोहरं वपुः Ś. 1. 18 ‘artlessly lovely.’<BR>--3 A<BR>pretext, pretence, semblance;<BR>ध्यानव्याजमुपेत्य Nāg. 1. 1; R. 4. 25, 58;<BR>10. 76; 11. 66.<BR>--4 An artifice, a device,<BR>contrivance; व्याजार्धसंदर्शितमेखलानि<BR>R. 13. 42.<BR>--5 Wickedness,<BR>depravity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः f. {1} a figure of<BR>speech in which what is<BR>apparently the effect of one cause is<BR>intentionally ascribed to another; in<BR>other words, where a feeling is<BR>dissembled by being attributed<BR>to a different cause; see K. P. 10<BR>under व्याजोक्ति. {2} covert allusion,<BR>insinuation.<BR>--निंदा artful censure.<BR>--सुप्त a. feigning to be asleep.<BR>--स्तुतिः f. a figure of speech resembling<BR>the English ‘irony’, wherein<BR>censure is implied by apparent praise,<BR>or praise by apparent censure;<BR>व्याजस्तुतिर्मुखे निंदा स्तुतिर्वा रूढिरन्यथा<BR>K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याडः|व्याड
व्याडः<BR>1 A carnivorous animal,<BR>such as a tiger.<BR>--2 A villain, rogue.<BR>--3 A snake.<BR>--4 N. of Indra; cf.<BR>व्याल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याडिः|व्याडि
व्याडिः N. of a celebrated<BR>grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यात्युक्षी
व्यात्युक्षी Mutual splashing and<BR>sporting in water; ताः कांतैः सह<BR>करपुष्क<BR>रेरितांबुव्यात्युक्षीमभिसरणग्लहामदीव्यन् Śi. 8. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादा
व्यादा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To open, break<BR>open; न व्याददात्याननमत्र मृत्युः<BR>Ki. 16. 16; नदी कूलं व्यादद ति, or व्याददते<BR>पिपीलिकाः पतंगस्य मुखं Mbh.<BR>--2 To make<BR>large, broaden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यात्त|व्यात्तं
व्यात्त p. p. Opened, spread,<BR>expanded.<BR>--त्तं The open mouth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादानं|व्यादान
व्यादानं Opening; Māl. 5. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादिश्
व्यादिश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To order,<BR>command; समीरणो नोदयिता भवेति<BR>व्यादिश्यते केन हुताशनस्य Ku. 3. 21, 13.<BR>--2<BR>To assign or appoint to (a duty).<BR>--3 To divide, distribute.<BR>--4 To point,<BR>indicate, show.<BR>--5 To teach, instruct.<BR>--6 To foretell, declare beforehand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यादिशः|व्यादिश
व्यादिशः An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधः|व्याध|व्याधं
व्याधः [व्यध्-ण]<BR>1 A hunter,<BR>fowler (by caste or profession).<BR>--2<BR>A wicked or low man.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भीतः a deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिन्
व्याधिन् a. Piercing, wounding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधामः|व्याधाम
व्याधामः, व्याधावः Indra's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">Page1022-c+ 56</a>]<BR>thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधावः|व्याधाव
व्याधामः, व्याधावः Indra's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">Page1022-c+ 56</a>]<BR>thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधिः|व्याधि
व्याधिः<BR>1 Sickness, ailment,<BR>disease, illness (usually physical, and<BR>opp. आधि which means ‘mental<BR>distress or anxiety’);<BR>रिपुरुन्नतधीरचेतसः सततव्याधिरनीतिरस्तु ते Śi. 16. 11<BR>(where व्याधि means ‘free from आधि’<BR>also); cf. आधि.<BR>--2 Leprosy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a. unwholesome.<BR>--ग्रस्त a.<BR>seized with disease, diseased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधित|व्याधितः
व्याधित a. Diseased, sick.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याधूत|व्याधूतः
व्याधूत p. p. Shaken about,<BR>trembling, tremulous; U. 1. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानः|व्यान
व्यानः One of the five life-winds<BR>or vital airs in the body, that which<BR>is diffused through the whole body;<BR>व्यानः सर्वशरीरगः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यानतं|व्यानत
व्यानतं A particular kind of<BR>coitus or mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्
व्याप् {c5c} P.<BR>1 To fill completely,<BR>pervade; श्रुतिविषयगुणा या स्थिता<BR>व्याप्य विश्वं Ś. 1. 1; V. 1. 1; स्वेदापूरो<BR>युवतिसरितां व्याप गंडस्थलानि Śi. 7. 74;<BR>Bg. 10. 16; R. 13. 5, 18. 40;<BR>Bk. 7. 56.<BR>--2 To reach as far, extend to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापक|व्यापकः
व्यापक a. (पिका f.)<BR>1<BR>Pervading, comprehensive, diffusive,<BR>widely spread, extending over the whole<BR>of anything; तिर्यगूर्ध्वमधस्ताच्च व्यापको<BR>महिमा हरेः Ku. 6. 71.<BR>--2 (In law)<BR>Comprehending all the points of an<BR>argument.<BR>--3 Invariably<BR>concomitant.<BR>--4 That which is more<BR>extensive than the व्याप्य; e. g. in the<BR>instance मनुष्यो मर्त्यः; मर्त्यं is व्यापक as<BR>it includes मनुष्य, and is more<BR>extensive than it.<BR>--कः An attribute<BR>which is invariably concomitant<BR>or inherent.<BR>--कं An invariably<BR>concomitant or inherent property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापनं|व्यापन
व्यापनं<BR>1 Pervading,<BR>comprehending, penetrating.<BR>--2 Covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापिन्
व्यापिन् a.<BR>1 Pervading, filling,<BR>occupying (at the end of comp.).<BR>--2<BR>All-pervading, co-extensive,<BR>invariably concomitant.<BR>--3 Covering. --m.<BR>1 An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 A<BR>pervading property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्त|व्याप्तं
व्याप्त p. p.<BR>1 Spread through,<BR>penetrated, pervaded, extended<BR>over, permeated, covered.<BR>--2<BR>Pervading, extending over all.<BR>--3<BR>Filled with, full of.<BR>--4 Encompassed,<BR>surrounded.<BR>--5 Placed, fixed.<BR>--6<BR>Obtained, possessed.<BR>--7<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">Page1023-a+ 58</a>]<BR>Comprehended, included.<BR>--8 Invariably<BR>accompanied (in logic); as in<BR>धूमो वह्निना व्याप्तः.<BR>--9 Famous,<BR>celebrated.<BR>--10 Expanded, stretched<BR>out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1022-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्तिः|व्याप्ति
व्याप्तिः f.<BR>1 Pervasion,<BR>permeation.<BR>--2 (In logic) Universal<BR>pervasion, invariable concomitance,<BR>universal accompaniment of the<BR>middle term by the major; यत्र यत्र<BR>धूमस्तत्र तत्राग्निरिति साहचर्यनियमो<BR>व्याप्तिः T. S.;<BR>अव्यभिचरितसाध्यसामानाधिकरण्यं व्याप्तिः Tarka K.; व्याप्तिः<BR>साध्यवदन्यस्मिन्नसंबंध उदाहृतः ।<BR>अथवा हेतुमन्निष्ठविरहाप्रतियोगिना ।<BR>साध्येन हेतोरैकाधिकरण्यं व्याप्तिरुच्यते<BR>Bhāṣā P. 67-68.<BR>--3 A universal<BR>rule, universality.<BR>--4 Fulness.<BR>--5<BR>Obtaining.<BR>--6 Omnipresence,<BR>ubiquity (as a divine attribute).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रहः apprehension of<BR>universal concomitance.<BR>--ज्ञानं<BR>knowledge of invariable or<BR>universal concomitance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्य|व्याप्यं|व्याप्यः
व्याप्य a. To be pervaded, filled,<BR>&c.<BR>--ण्यं The sign or middle term<BR>of a syllogism (= हेतु, साधन q. v.)<BR>(in logic.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याप्यत्वं|व्याप्यत्व
व्याप्यत्वं Invariableness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--असिद्धिः f. imperfect inference,<BR>where the हेतु itself is false or<BR>nonexistent; as in the argument<BR>पर्वतो वह्निमान् कांचनमयधूमात्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापद्
व्यापद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To die, perish.<BR>--2 To come down (to the earth),<BR>fall down.<BR>--3 To be inaudible (as<BR>a sound). --Caus.<BR>1 To kill, slay.<BR>--2 To hurt, injure, spoil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापत्तिः|व्यापत्ति
व्यापत्तिः f.<BR>1 Ruin, calamity,<BR>misfortune; Mu. 6. 20; Mk. 6. 1.<BR>--2 Substitution of one thing for<BR>another.<BR>--3 Death; R. 12. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापद्
व्यापद् f.<BR>1 Calamity,<BR>misfortune, affliction; Māl. 9. 36;<BR>Bh. 3. 105.<BR>--2 Disease.<BR>--3 Derangement.<BR>--4 Death, decease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापन्न|व्यापन्नः
व्यापन्न p. p.<BR>1 Fallen into<BR>misfortune, ruined.<BR>--2 Failed,<BR>miscarried.<BR>--3 Hurt, injured.<BR>--4 Dead,<BR>expired, deceased; as in अव्यापन्न<BR>q. v.<BR>--5 Deranged, disordered.<BR>--6<BR>Substituted, changed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादः|व्यापाद
व्यापादः, व्यापादनं<BR>1 Killing,<BR>slaying.<BR>--2 Ruin, destruction.<BR>--3 Evil<BR>design, malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादनं|व्यापादन
व्यापादः, व्यापादनं<BR>1 Killing,<BR>slaying.<BR>--2 Ruin, destruction.<BR>--3 Evil<BR>design, malice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादक
व्यापादक a. Destructive,<BR>murderous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापादित|व्यापादितः
व्यापादित p. p.<BR>1 Killed, slain,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">Page1023-b+ 56</a>]<BR>destroyed.<BR>--2 Ruined, injured, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापृ
व्यापृ {c6c} A.<BR>1 To be engaged in<BR>or occupied with, be busy about<BR>(with loc.).<BR>--2 To be employed or<BR>placed (in any office). --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To cause to work, engage upon,<BR>entrust with, appoint to (usually<BR>with loc.); व्यापारितः शूलभृता<BR>विधाय सिंहत्वमंकागतसत्ववृत्ति R. 2. 38;<BR>आत्मजनानुष्ठेये कर्मणि त्वां<BR>व्यापारयितुमिच्छामि Mu. 1.<BR>--2 To place, sot,<BR>fix, direct, cast; व्यापारयामास करं<BR>किरीटे R. 6. 19; उमामुख…<BR>व्यापारयामास विलोचनानि Ku. 3. 67;<BR>व्यापारितं शिरसि शस्त्रमशस्त्रपाणेः Ve. 3. 19;<BR>R. 13. 25; M. 3. 4.<BR>--3 To use,<BR>employ; Mu. 7. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारः|व्यापार
व्यापारः<BR>1 Employment,<BR>engagement, business, occupation; ततः<BR>प्रविशति यथोक्तव्यापारा शकुंतला Ś. 1;<BR>Ku. 2. 54.<BR>--2 Application,<BR>employment; Mu. 2. 4.<BR>--3 Profession,<BR>trade, practice, exercise; as in<BR>शस्त्रव्यापार.<BR>--4 An act, doing,<BR>performance.<BR>--5 Working, operation,<BR>action, influence; (व्रतं) व्यापाररोधि<BR>मदनस्य निषेवितव्य Ś. 1. 27;<BR>तस्यानुमेने भगवान् विमन्युर्व्यापारमात्मन्यपि<BR>सायकानां Ku. 7. 93; V. 3. 17.<BR>--6<BR>Being placed on; M. 4. 14.<BR>--7 Exertion,<BR>effort; आर्याप्यरुंधती तत्र व्यापारं<BR>कर्तुमर्हति Ku. 6. 32 ‘will be pleased to<BR>exert herself in that behalf;’ न<BR>व्यापारशतेनापि शुकवत्पाठ्यते बकः<BR>H. Pr. 43. (व्यापारं कृ {1} to take part in. {2}<BR>to have effect on. {3} to meddle; as<BR>in अव्यापारेषु व्यापारं यो नरः<BR>कर्तुमिच्छति Pt. 1. 21).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारित
व्यापारित p. p.<BR>1 Engaged,<BR>occupied, employed, appointed;<BR>R. 2. 38.<BR>--2 Placed, fixed, set.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापारिन्
व्यापारिन् m.<BR>1 A dealer, trader.<BR>--2 One who exercises or practises<BR>anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापृत|व्यापृतः
व्यापृत p. p.<BR>1 Engaged in,<BR>occupied or busy with, employed in<BR>(with loc.); अन्यस्मिन्कर्मणि व्यापृतं<BR>धनुः Ś. 6. 31.<BR>--2 Placed, fixed. --m.<BR>An employé, a minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यापृतिः|व्यापृति
व्यापृतिः f.<BR>1 Employment,<BR>engagement, business;<BR>स्वस्वव्यापृतिमग्नमानसतया Bv. 1. 58.<BR>--2 Operation,<BR>action.<BR>--3 Exertion.<BR>--4 Profession,<BR>practice; see व्यापार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याभ्युक्षी
व्याभ्युक्षी = व्यात्युक्षी q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामः|व्याम
व्यामः, व्यामनं A measure of length<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">Page1023-c+ 57</a>]<BR>equal to the space between the<BR>tips of the fingers of either hand<BR>when the arms are extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामनं|व्यामन
व्यामः, व्यामनं A measure of length<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">Page1023-c+ 57</a>]<BR>equal to the space between the<BR>tips of the fingers of either hand<BR>when the arms are extended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामर्षः|व्यामर्ष
व्यामर्षः<BR>1 Impatience.<BR>--2<BR>Erasure, wiping out.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामिश्र|व्यामिश्रं
व्यामिश्र a. Mingled, intermixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यामोहः|व्यामोह
व्यामोहः<BR>1 Infatuation.<BR>--2<BR>Bewilderment, embarrassment,<BR>perplexity; कंसस्यालमभूज्जितं जितमिति<BR>व्यामोहकोलाहलः Gīt. 10; Kāv. 3. 101.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायम्
व्यायम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To stretch out,<BR>extend.<BR>--2 To struggle, contend,<BR>fight.<BR>--3 To try, strive, endeavour.<BR>--4 To sport, dally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायत|व्यायतं
व्यायत p. p.<BR>1 Long, extended;<BR>युवा युगव्यायतबाहुरंसलः R. 3. 34.<BR>--2<BR>Expanded, wide open.<BR>--3<BR>Exercised, disciplined.<BR>--4 Busy, engaged,<BR>occupied.<BR>--5 Hard, firm.<BR>--6 Strong,<BR>intense, excessive.<BR>--7 Mighty,<BR>powerful.<BR>--8 Deep;<BR>व्यायतपातमाक्षिणोत् Ku. 5. 54.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायतत्वं|व्यायतत्व
व्यायतत्वं Muscular development;<BR>Ś. 2. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायामः|व्यायाम
व्यायामः<BR>1 Extending, stretching<BR>out.<BR>--2 Exercise, gymnastic or<BR>athletic exercise; स्थाने शमवतां<BR>शक्त्या व्यायामे वृद्धिरंगिनां Śi. 2. 94.<BR>--3<BR>Fatigue, labour.<BR>--4 Effort, exertion.<BR>--5 Contention, struggle.<BR>--6<BR>Business, occupation.<BR>--7 A difficulty.<BR>--8<BR>A measure of distance (= व्याम q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायामिक
व्यायामिक a. (की f.), व्यायामिन् a.<BR>Athletic, gymnastic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यायोगः|व्यायोग
व्यायोगः A kind of dramatic<BR>composition in one act; it is thus<BR>described by S. D.:<BR>--ख्यातेतिवृत्तो व्यायोगः<BR>स्वल्पस्त्रीजनसंयुतः । हीनो गर्भविमर्षाभ्यां<BR>नरैर्बहुभिराश्रितः । एकांकश्च<BR>भवेदस्त्रीनिमित्तसमरोदयः । कौशिकीवृत्तिरहितः प्रख्यातस्तत्र नायकः ।<BR>राजर्षिरथ दिव्यो वा भवेद्धीरोद्धतश्च सः ।<BR>हास्यशृंगारशांतेभ्य इतरेऽत्रांगिनो रसाः ॥ 514.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याल|व्यालः
व्याल a.<BR>1 Wicked, vicious;<BR>व्यालद्विपा यंतृभिरुन्मदिष्णवः Śi. 12. 28;<BR>यंता गजं व्यालमिवापराद्धः Ki. 17. 25.<BR>--2 Bad, villainous.<BR>--3 Cruel, fierce,<BR>savage; Ki. 13. 4.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A vicious<BR>elephant; व्यालं बालमृणालतंतुभिरसौ<BR>रोद्धुं समुज्जृंभते Bh. 2. 6.<BR>--2 A beast of<BR>prey; वर्नं व्यालनिषेवितं Rām.<BR>--3 A<BR>snake; H. 3. 29.<BR>--4 A tiger; Māl. 3.<BR>--5 A leopard.<BR>--6 A king.<BR>--7 A cheat,<BR>rogue.<BR>--8 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खड्गः, --नखः a kind of herb.<BR>--ग्राहः, --ग्राहिन् m. a snake-catcher.<BR>--मृगः<BR>{1} a wild animal. {2} a hunting<BR>leopard.<BR>--रूपः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1023-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालकः|व्यालक
व्यालकः A vicious or wicked<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालंबः|व्यालम्ब|व्यालंब|व्यालम्बः
व्यालंबः A kind of castor-oil<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालीन
व्यालीन a. Thick, dense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यालोल
व्यालोल a.<BR>1 Shaking about,<BR>tremulous.<BR>--2 Disordered,<BR>dishevelled; व्यालोलः केशपाशः Gīt. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावकलनं|व्यावकलन
व्यावकलनं Subtraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावक्रोशी
व्यावक्रोशी, व्यावभाषी Mutual<BR>abuse, reciprocal imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावभाषी
व्यावक्रोशी, व्यावभाषी Mutual<BR>abuse, reciprocal imprecation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावल्गित
व्यावल्गित p. p. Moved, agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहारिक|व्यावहारिकः
व्यावहारिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Relating to business, practical.<BR>--2<BR>Legal, judicial.<BR>--3 Customary,<BR>usual.<BR>--4 Relating to the world<BR>of illusion; cf. प्रातिभासिक.<BR>--कः<BR>A counsellor, minister.<BR>--कं Use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहारी
व्यावहारी Mutual seizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावहासी
व्यावहासी Mutual derision or<BR>laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृ
व्यावृ {c5c} U.<BR>1 To select, choose.<BR>--2 To hide, conceal.<BR>--3 To obstruct,<BR>impede.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत
व्यावृत p. p.<BR>1 Covered, hid,<BR>screened.<BR>--2 Impeded, obstructed.<BR>--3 Opened.<BR>--4 Excepted, excluded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृतिः|व्यावृति
व्यावृतिः f. Covering, screening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्
व्यावृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To turn away<BR>from, turn back; सहभुवा<BR>व्यावर्तमाना ह्निया Ratn. 1. 2.<BR>--2 To be turned<BR>or withdrawn from, to be averse<BR>to; विषयव्यावृत्तकौतूहलः V. 1. 8.<BR>--3 To become separate or distinct<BR>from.<BR>--4 To turn round, revolve.<BR>--5 To go down, set (as the sun).<BR>--6 To cease to exist, perish.<BR>--7 To<BR>be opened or split asunder. --Caus.<BR>1 To restrict, limit, exclude, arrest;<BR>overrule, annul, (as a rule &c.); तुशब्दः<BR>पूर्वपक्षं व्यावर्तयति Ś. B.; अपवाद<BR>इवोत्सर्गं व्यावर्तयितुमश्विरः R. 15. 7.<BR>--2<BR>To dissuade from, cause to turn<BR>away from;<BR>नेयमस्माद्व्यवसायात्कथंचिदपि शक्यते व्यावर्तयितुं K. 172.<BR>--3 To destroy, remove; V. 5. 16.<BR>--4 To turn round, cause to revolve.<BR>--5 To separate from.<BR>--6 To scatter,<BR>strew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्तः|व्यावर्त|व्यावर्त्त|व्यावर्त्तः
व्यावर्तः<BR>1 Surrounding,<BR>encompassing.<BR>--2 Revolution, going round.<BR>--3 Ruptured navel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्तक|व्यावर्त्तक
व्यावर्तक a. (र्तिका f.)<BR>1<BR>Encompassing, surrounding.<BR>--2 Excluding,<BR>separating, restricting.<BR>--3 Turning<BR>away from.<BR>--4 Turning round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावर्तनं|व्यावर्तन|व्यावर्त्तन
व्यावर्तनं<BR>1 Surrounding,<BR>encompassing.<BR>--2 Revolving, turning round;<BR>Ki. 5. 30.<BR>--3 A fold, band.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्त|व्यावृत्तः
व्यावृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Turned a way from,<BR>withdrawn from; व्यावृत्ता यत्परस्वेभ्यः<BR>श्रुतौ तस्करता स्थिता R. 1. 27;<BR>V. 1. 8.<BR>--2 Separated from, singled<BR>out.<BR>--3 (a) Excluded, set aside;<BR>different from; अयमर्थोऽस्माद् व्यावृत्तः<BR>Tarka K. (b) Not being found or<BR>existing in, absent from (frequently<BR>used in phil. in this sense); धूमो<BR>जलहदादेर्व्यावृत्तः Tarka K.;<BR>Mu. 5. 10.<BR>--4 Revolved, turned round.<BR>--5<BR>Encompassed, surrounded.<BR>--6<BR>Desisting, ceased from; Ku. 2. 35.<BR>--7 Split asunder.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गति<BR>a. desisting from any course of<BR>action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यावृत्तिः|व्यावृत्ति
व्यावृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Covering, screening.<BR>--2 Exclusion, separation.<BR>--3 Not<BR>being found in, absence from;<BR>विपक्षाद्व्यावृत्तिः Tarka K.<BR>--4<BR>Surrounding.<BR>--5 Rolling backwards.<BR>--6<BR>Praise, eulogium.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बुद्धि<BR>f. the notion of exclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासः|व्यास
व्यासः<BR>1 Distribution, separation<BR>into parts.<BR>--2 Dissolution or<BR>analysis of a compound.<BR>--3 Severalty,<BR>distinction.<BR>--4 Diffusion, extension.<BR>--5 Width, breadth.<BR>--6 The<BR>diameter of a circle.<BR>--7 A fault in<BR>pronunciation.<BR>--8 Arrangement,<BR>compilation.<BR>--9 An arranger, a<BR>compiler.<BR>--10 N. of a celebrated sage.<BR>[He was the son of the sage Parāśara<BR>by Satyavatī (born before her marriage<BR>with Śantanu q. v.); but he retired to<BR>the wilderness as soon as he was born,<BR>and there led the life of a hermit,<BR>practising the most rigid austerities<BR>until he was called by his mother<BR>Satyavatī to beget sons on the widows<BR>of her son Vicitravīrya. He was thus<BR>the father of Pāṇḍu and Dhṛtarāṣṭra<BR>and also of Vidura; q.q. v.v. He<BR>was at first called ‘Kṛṣṇadvaipāyana’<BR>from his dark complexion and from<BR>his having been brought forth by<BR>Satyavatī on a Dvīpa or island; but he<BR>afterwards came to be called<BR>Vyāsa or ‘the arranger’, as he was<BR>supposed to have arranged the<BR>Vedas in their present form;<BR>विव्यास वेदान् यस्मात्स तस्माद् व्यास इति स्मृतः.<BR>He is believed to be the author of the<BR>great epic the Mahābhārata which he<BR>is said to have composed with<BR>Gaṇapati for his scribe. The eighteen<BR>Purāṇas, as also the Brahma-sūtras and<BR>several other works are also ascribed<BR>to him. He is one of the seven<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">Page1024-c+ 56</a>]<BR>chirajīvins or deathless persons; cf.<BR>चिरजीविन्].<BR>--11 A Brāhmaṇa who<BR>recites or expounds the Purāṇas in<BR>public.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासंज्|व्यासञ्ज्
व्यासंज् {c1c} P. To attach firmly to,<BR>fasten on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासक्त|व्यासक्तः
व्यासक्त p. p.<BR>1 Closely adhering<BR>to.<BR>--2 Attached or devoted to,<BR>intent on, occupied or busy with<BR>(with loc.).<BR>--3 Separated, detached,<BR>disjoined.<BR>--4 Confused, bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासंगः|व्यासङ्ग|व्यासंग|व्यासङ्गः
व्यासंगः<BR>1 Close adherence, intent<BR>attachment or application.<BR>--2<BR>Intentness, devotion; Bv. 1. 79.<BR>--3<BR>Diligent study.<BR>--4 Attention;<BR>Māl. 9. 33.<BR>--5 Detachment, separation.<BR>--6<BR>Perplexity, confusion.<BR>--7 Addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासिद्ध|व्यासिद्धः
व्यासिद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Prohibited,<BR>forbidden.<BR>--2 Contraband (said of<BR>goods &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यासेधः|व्यासेध
व्यासेधः Restraint, prohibition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहन्
व्याहन् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To obstruct,<BR>thwart, oppose, impede.<BR>--2 To<BR>repel, drive back.<BR>--3 To strike<BR>excessively.<BR>--4 To violate, transgress,<BR>disobey; R. 19. 57.<BR>--5 To foil, frustrate,<BR>disappoint.<BR>--6 To trouble, vex, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहत|व्याहतः
व्याहत p. p.<BR>1 Obstructed,<BR>impeded.<BR>--2 Repelled, repulsed.<BR>--3<BR>Foiled, disappointed; Śi. 3. 40.<BR>--4<BR>Confused, bewildered, alarmed.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थता one of the faults of<BR>composition; see K. P. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहावः|व्याहाव
व्याहावः A distinct call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृ
व्याहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To speak, say,<BR>utter, tell, narrate, declare; व्याजहार<BR>हरसूनुसंनिभः R. 11. 83; Ku. 2. 62;<BR>6. 2.<BR>--2 To explain.<BR>--3 To cry,<BR>scream, shout.<BR>--4 To answer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहरणं|व्याहरण
व्याहरणं<BR>1 Utterance,<BR>pronunciation.<BR>--2 Speech, narration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहारः|व्याहार
व्याहारः<BR>1 Speech, utterance, words;<BR>U. 4. 18, 5. 29.<BR>--2 Voice, note,<BR>sound; M. 5. 1.<BR>--3 Jest, joke,<BR>humorous speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृत
व्याहृत p. p. Said, spoken, uttered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्याहृतिः|व्याहृति
व्याहृतिः f.<BR>1 Utterance, speech,<BR>words; न हीश्वरव्याहृतयः<BR>कदाचित्पुष्णंति लोके विपरीतमर्थं Ku. 3. 63.<BR>--2<BR>Statement, expression; भूतार्थव्याहृतिः<BR>सा हि न स्तुतिः परमोष्ठिनः R. 10. 33.<BR>--3<BR>A mystic word uttered by every<BR>Brāhmaṇa in performing his daily<BR>Saṃdhyā adoration; (these<BR>Vyāhṛtis are three भूर्, भुवस् and स्वस् or<BR>स्वर् usually repeated after om; cf.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">Page1025-a+ 55</a>]<BR>Ms. 2. 76; according to some they<BR>are seven in number).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1024-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्चर्
व्युच्चर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To transgress,<BR>offend against, violate.<BR>--2 To be<BR>faithless to.<BR>--3 To commit adultery with.<BR>--4 To deviate from the right path.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्चरणं
व्युच्चरणं Transgression; deviation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युच्छित्तिः|व्युच्छित्ति
व्युच्छित्तिः f., व्युच्छेदः Cutting<BR>off, extermination, complete<BR>destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रम्
व्युत्क्रम् See उत्क्रम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रमः|व्युत्क्रम|व्युत्क्रमं
व्युत्क्रमः<BR>1 Transgression, going<BR>astray.<BR>--2 Inverted order,<BR>contrariety.<BR>--3 Confusion, disorder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्क्रांत|व्युत्क्रान्त
व्युत्क्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Transgressed,<BR>overstepped.<BR>--2 Departed, left, gone<BR>forth.<BR>--3 Neglected.<BR>--ता A kind of<BR>riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्था
व्युत्था {c1c} A.<BR>1 To get up, rise.<BR>--2<BR>To increase in strength or power,<BR>grow strong. --Caus. To excite,<BR>instigate, rouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्थानं|व्युत्थान
व्युत्थानं, व्युत्थितिः f.<BR>1 Great<BR>activity.<BR>--2 Rising up against,<BR>opposition, obstruction.<BR>--3 Independent<BR>action, following one's own bent of<BR>mind.<BR>--4 The completion of religious<BR>abstraction or abstract meditation<BR>(in Yoga phil.).<BR>--5 A kind of dance.<BR>--6 Causing (an elephant) to rise;<BR>Śi. 18. 26.<BR>--7 Contradicting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्थितिः
व्युत्थानं, व्युत्थितिः f.<BR>1 Great<BR>activity.<BR>--2 Rising up against,<BR>opposition, obstruction.<BR>--3 Independent<BR>action, following one's own bent of<BR>mind.<BR>--4 The completion of religious<BR>abstraction or abstract meditation<BR>(in Yoga phil.).<BR>--5 A kind of dance.<BR>--6 Causing (an elephant) to rise;<BR>Śi. 18. 26.<BR>--7 Contradicting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पद्
व्युत्पद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To be produced<BR>from, originate in.<BR>--2 To be<BR>derived from (a root &c.).<BR>--3 To become<BR>proficient in or conversant^1 with.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To produce, cause.<BR>--2 To<BR>derive, trace to a root (as a word);<BR>ब्रह्मशब्दस्य व्युत्पाद्यमानस्य Ś. B.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पत्तिः|व्युत्पत्ति
व्युत्पत्तिः f.<BR>1 Origin, production.<BR>--2 Derivation, etymology.<BR>--3<BR>Perfect proficiency, conversancy.<BR>--4<BR>Scholarship, learning;<BR>व्युत्पत्तिरावर्जितकोविदापि न रंजनाय क्रमते जडानां<BR>Vikr. 1. 16, 18. 108.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्पन्न|व्युत्पन्नः
व्युत्पन्न p. p.<BR>1 Produced,<BR>begotten.<BR>--2 Formed by derivation.<BR>--3<BR>Derived, traced to its etymology, as<BR>a word (opp. अव्युत्पन्न or ‘primitive’).<BR>--4 Completed, perfected; Mv. 4. 57.<BR>--5 Thoroughly proficient in, learned,<BR>erudite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युत्त
व्युत्त p. p. Wetted, drenched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदस्
व्युदस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To throw or<BR>scatter about.<BR>--2 To throw off, cast<BR>away.<BR>--3 To set or lay aside.<BR>--4 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">Page1025-b+ 55</a>]<BR>give up, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदस्त
व्युदस्त p. p. Thrown aside,<BR>rejected, cast off.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदासः|व्युदास
व्युदासः<BR>1 Throwing aside,<BR>rejection.<BR>--2 Exclusion (in gram.).<BR>--3<BR>Prohibition.<BR>--4 Disregard,<BR>indifference.<BR>--5 Killing, destruction;<BR>Śi. 15. 37.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युदित
व्युदित a. Disputed, discussed,<BR>debated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपदेशः|व्युपदेश
व्युपदेशः Pretext, pretence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपरमः|व्युपरम
व्युपरमः Cessation, stop, close.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युपशमः|व्युपशम
व्युपशमः<BR>1 Non-cessation.<BR>--2<BR>Inquietude.<BR>--3 Complete cessation<BR>(where वि shows intensity).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्ट|व्युष्टं|व्युष्टः
व्युष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Burnt.<BR>--2 Dawned,<BR>become day-light.<BR>--3 Become bright<BR>or clear.<BR>--4 Dwelt.<BR>--5 Passed.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>1 Day-break, dawn; Śi. 12. 4.<BR>--2<BR>Day.<BR>--3 Fruit, result.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्युष्टिः|व्युष्टि
व्युष्टिः f.<BR>1 Dawn.<BR>--2 Prosperity.<BR>--3 Praise.<BR>--4 Fruit, consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूत|व्यूतं
व्यूत a. Interwoven, sewn,<BR>interlaced.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूतिः|व्यूति
व्यूतिः<BR>1 Weaving, sewing.<BR>--2 The<BR>wages of weaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूह्
व्यूह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To arrange troops in<BR>battle array; सूच्या वज्रेण चैवेतान्<BR>व्यूहेन व्यूह्य योधयेत् Ms. 7. 191.<BR>--2 To<BR>arrange, put or place in order,<BR>dispose.<BR>--3 To separate, divide.<BR>--4 To<BR>alter, transpose, disarrange.<BR>--5 To<BR>resolve (vowels, syllables &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढ|व्यूढः
व्यूढ p. p.<BR>1 Expanded, developed,<BR>broad, wide; व्यूढोरस्को वृषस्कंधः<BR>R. 1. 13.<BR>--2 Firm, compact.<BR>--3 Placed<BR>in order, arranged, marshalled (as<BR>an army); Bg. 1. 3.<BR>--4<BR>Disarranged, placed out of order.<BR>--5 Married.<BR>--6 Large, great.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंकट a.<BR>mailed, clad in armour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूढिः|व्यूढि
व्यूढिः f. Orderly arrangement,<BR>array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहः|व्यूह
व्यूहः<BR>1 A military array;<BR>Ms. 7. 187.<BR>--2 An army, a host, squadron;<BR>व्यूहावुभौ तावितरेतरस्मात् भंगं जयं<BR>चापतुरव्यवस्थं R. 7. 54.<BR>--3 A large<BR>quantity, an assemblage, a multitude,<BR>collection.<BR>--4 A part, portion,<BR>subhead.<BR>--5 The body.<BR>--6 Structure,<BR>formation.<BR>--7 Reasoning, logic.<BR>--8<BR>Separation, distribution.<BR>--9 (In<BR>phil.) A peculiar arrangement of<BR>the senses.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पार्प्णिः f. the<BR>rear of an army.<BR>--भंगः, --भेदः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">Page1025-c+ 56</a>]<BR>breaking an array.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यूहनं|व्यूहन
व्यूहनं<BR>1 Arraying of troops,<BR>marshalling.<BR>--2 Structure of the<BR>members of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृद्ध
व्यृद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Deprived of<BR>prosperity, unlucky, unfortunate.<BR>--2<BR>Deprived of or excluded from.<BR>--3<BR>Nullified.<BR>--4 Imperfect, deficient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्यृद्धिः|व्यृद्धि
व्यृद्धिः f. Non-prosperity, ill-luck,<BR>misfortune (विगता ऋद्धिर्व्यृद्धिः); as in<BR>यवनानां व्यृद्धिर्दुर्यवनं Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ये
व्ये {c1c} U. (व्ययति-ते, ऊत; caus.<BR>व्याययति-ते; desid. विव्यासति)<BR>1 To cover.<BR>--2 To sew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योकारः|व्योकार
व्योकारः A blacksmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योमन्
व्योमन् n. [व्ये-मनिन् पृषो˚<BR>Uṇ. 4. 150]<BR>1 The sky, atmosphere;<BR>अस्त्वेवं जडधामता तु भवतो यद् व्योम्नि<BR>विस्फूर्जसे K. P. 10, Me. 51;<BR>R. 12. 67; N. 22. 54.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--3 A<BR>temple sacred to the sun.<BR>--4 Talc.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदकं rain-water, dew.<BR>--केशः, --केशिन् m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--गंगा the heavenly Ganges.<BR>--चारिन् m. {1} a god. {2} a bird. {3}<BR>a saint. {4} a Brāhmaṇa. {5} a<BR>heavenly body.<BR>--धूमः a cloud.<BR>--देवः N. of Śiva.<BR>--नाशिका a kind of<BR>quail.<BR>--मंजरं, --मंडलं a flag, banner.<BR>--माय a. reaching to the sky.<BR>--मुद्गरः a gust of wind.<BR>--यानं a<BR>celestial car.<BR>--सद् m. {1} a deity, god. {2}<BR>a Gandharva. {3} a spirit.<BR>--स्थली<BR>the earth.<BR>--स्पृश् a. ‘sky-touching’,<BR>very lofty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्योषं|व्योष
व्योषं An aggregate of three<BR>spices (black and long pepper, and<BR>dry ginger.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्
व्रज् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (व्रजति)<BR>1 To go,<BR>walk, proceed; नाविनीतैर्व्रजेद् धुर्यैः<BR>Ms. 4. 67.<BR>--2 To go to, approach,<BR>visit; मामेकं शरणं व्रज Bg. 18. 66.<BR>--3 To depart, retire, withdraw.<BR>--4<BR>To pass away (as time); इयं व्रजति<BR>यामिनी त्यज नरेंद्र निद्रारसं<BR>Vikr. 11. 74.<BR>--5 To attain to, go to the state<BR>of.<BR>--6 To obtain, gain. {vII.v} {c10c} U.<BR>(व्राजयति-ते)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To prepare,<BR>decorate. (This root is used much<BR>in the same way as गम् or या q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजः|व्रज|व्रजं
व्रजः [व्रज्-घञर्थे क]<BR>1 A<BR>multitude, collection, flock, group;<BR>नेत्रव्रजाः पौरजनस्य तास्मिन् विहाय<BR>सर्वान्नृपतीन्निपेतुः R. 6. 7; 7. 60; Śi. 6. 6,<BR>14. 33.<BR>--2 A station of cowherds.<BR>--3 A cow-pen, cow-shed; Śi. 2. 64.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">Page1026-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--4 An abode, a resting-place.<BR>--5 A<BR>road.<BR>--6 A cloud.<BR>--7 N. of a<BR>district near Mathurā.<BR>--जं<BR>Wandering, going.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगना, --युवतिः<BR>f. a woman of Vraja, a cowherdess;<BR>Bv. 2. 165.<BR>--अजिरं a cow-pen.<BR>--किशोरः, --नाथः, --मोहनः, --वरः,<BR>--वल्लभः epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1025-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजकः|व्रजक
व्रजकः A religious mendicant<BR>wandering about for alms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रजनं|व्रजन
व्रजनं<BR>1 Roaming, wandering,<BR>travelling.<BR>--2 Exile.<BR>--3 Ved. A<BR>way, road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रज्या
व्रज्या<BR>1 Wandering about as a<BR>religious mendicant.<BR>--2 An attack,<BR>invasion, a march.<BR>--3 A flock,<BR>multitude, tribe, class.<BR>--4 A theatre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रण्
व्रण् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (व्रणति) To sound.<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} U. (व्रणयति-ते) To hurt;<BR>wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणः|व्रण|व्रणं
व्रणः --णं [व्रण्-अच्]<BR>1 A wound,<BR>sore, bruise, hurt; R. 12. 55.<BR>--2 A<BR>boil, an ulcer; U. 2. 26.<BR>--3 A<BR>fracture, scar.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः<BR>gummyrrh.<BR>--कृत् a. {1} wounding. {2}<BR>corroding. (--m.) the marking-nut<BR>tree.<BR>--विरोपण a. sore-healing;<BR>Ś. 4. 13.<BR>--शोधनं the cleansing or<BR>dressing of a wound.<BR>--हः the<BR>castoroil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणं|व्रण|व्रणः
व्रणः --णं [व्रण्-अच्]<BR>1 A wound,<BR>sore, bruise, hurt; R. 12. 55.<BR>--2 A<BR>boil, an ulcer; U. 2. 26.<BR>--3 A<BR>fracture, scar.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः<BR>gummyrrh.<BR>--कृत् a. {1} wounding. {2}<BR>corroding. (--m.) the marking-nut<BR>tree.<BR>--विरोपण a. sore-healing;<BR>Ś. 4. 13.<BR>--शोधनं the cleansing or<BR>dressing of a wound.<BR>--हः the<BR>castoroil plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रणित
व्रणित a. Wounded, bruised;<BR>U. 4. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतः|व्रत|व्रतं
व्रतः --तं [व्रज्-घ जस्य तः]<BR>1 A<BR>religious act of devotion or austerity,<BR>vowed observance, a vow in general;<BR>अभ्यस्यतीव व्रतमासिधारं R. 13. 67,<BR>2. 4, 25; (there are several vratas<BR>enjoined in the different Purāṇas;<BR>but their number cannot be said to<BR>be fixed, as new ones, e. g.<BR>सत्यनारायणव्रत, are being added every day.)<BR>--2 A vow, promise, resolve; सोऽभूद्<BR>भग्नव्रतः शत्रूनुद्धृत्य प्रतिरोपयन्<BR>R. 17. 42; so सत्यव्रत, पुण्यव्रत, दृढव्रत &c.<BR>--3<BR>Object of devotion or faith,<BR>devotion; as in पतिव्रता (पतिर्व्रतं यस्याः सा);<BR>यांति देवव्रता देवान् पितॄन् यांति पितृव्रताः<BR>Bg. 9. 25.<BR>--4 A rite, an observance,<BR>practice, as in अर्कव्रत q v.<BR>--5 Mode<BR>of life, course of conduct; Ś. 5. 27.<BR>--6 An ordinance, a law, rule.<BR>--7<BR>Sacrifice.<BR>--8 An act, a deed, work.<BR>--9<BR>A design, plan.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचरणं the<BR>observance of a vow.<BR>--आदेशः<BR>investiture of a youth (of any one<BR>of the three classes) with the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">Page1026-b+ 56</a>]<BR>sacred thread.<BR>--उपवासः a fast for a<BR>vow.<BR>--ग्रहणं initiation into a vow<BR>for a religious performance.<BR>--चर्यः<BR>a religious student; see ब्रह्मचारिन्.<BR>--चर्या observance or practice of a<BR>religious vow.<BR>--पारणं, --णा<BR>conclusion of a vow or fast, eating after a<BR>fast.<BR>--प्रतिष्ठा performance of a<BR>religious vow voluntarily undertaken.<BR>--भंगः {1} breach of a vow. {2} breach<BR>of a promise.<BR>--भिक्षा begging alms<BR>as part of the ceremony of<BR>investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>--लोपनं<BR>breaking a vow.<BR>--वैकल्यं the<BR>incompletion of a religious vow.<BR>--संग्रहः initiation into a vow.<BR>--स्थ a.<BR>practising any vow.<BR>--स्नातकः a<BR>Brāhmaṇa who has completed the<BR>first stage of his religious life, i. e.<BR>that of a Brahmacārin or religious<BR>student; see स्नातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतं|व्रत|व्रतः
व्रतः --तं [व्रज्-घ जस्य तः]<BR>1 A<BR>religious act of devotion or austerity,<BR>vowed observance, a vow in general;<BR>अभ्यस्यतीव व्रतमासिधारं R. 13. 67,<BR>2. 4, 25; (there are several vratas<BR>enjoined in the different Purāṇas;<BR>but their number cannot be said to<BR>be fixed, as new ones, e. g.<BR>सत्यनारायणव्रत, are being added every day.)<BR>--2 A vow, promise, resolve; सोऽभूद्<BR>भग्नव्रतः शत्रूनुद्धृत्य प्रतिरोपयन्<BR>R. 17. 42; so सत्यव्रत, पुण्यव्रत, दृढव्रत &c.<BR>--3<BR>Object of devotion or faith,<BR>devotion; as in पतिव्रता (पतिर्व्रतं यस्याः सा);<BR>यांति देवव्रता देवान् पितॄन् यांति पितृव्रताः<BR>Bg. 9. 25.<BR>--4 A rite, an observance,<BR>practice, as in अर्कव्रत q v.<BR>--5 Mode<BR>of life, course of conduct; Ś. 5. 27.<BR>--6 An ordinance, a law, rule.<BR>--7<BR>Sacrifice.<BR>--8 An act, a deed, work.<BR>--9<BR>A design, plan.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचरणं the<BR>observance of a vow.<BR>--आदेशः<BR>investiture of a youth (of any one<BR>of the three classes) with the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">Page1026-b+ 56</a>]<BR>sacred thread.<BR>--उपवासः a fast for a<BR>vow.<BR>--ग्रहणं initiation into a vow<BR>for a religious performance.<BR>--चर्यः<BR>a religious student; see ब्रह्मचारिन्.<BR>--चर्या observance or practice of a<BR>religious vow.<BR>--पारणं, --णा<BR>conclusion of a vow or fast, eating after a<BR>fast.<BR>--प्रतिष्ठा performance of a<BR>religious vow voluntarily undertaken.<BR>--भंगः {1} breach of a vow. {2} breach<BR>of a promise.<BR>--भिक्षा begging alms<BR>as part of the ceremony of<BR>investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>--लोपनं<BR>breaking a vow.<BR>--वैकल्यं the<BR>incompletion of a religious vow.<BR>--संग्रहः initiation into a vow.<BR>--स्थ a.<BR>practising any vow.<BR>--स्नातकः a<BR>Brāhmaṇa who has completed the<BR>first stage of his religious life, i. e.<BR>that of a Brahmacārin or religious<BR>student; see स्नातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतयति
व्रतयति Den. P.<BR>1 To observe a<BR>vow.<BR>--2 To fast in consequence of a<BR>vow.<BR>--3 To eat together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतिन्
व्रतिन् a. Observing a vow,<BR>practising penance, devout, pious;<BR>Pt. 1. 416. --m.<BR>1 A religious student.<BR>--2 An ascetic, a devotee; Ś. 5. 9.<BR>--3 One who institutes a sacrifice;<BR>cf. यजमान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रततिः|व्रतति
व्रततिः, --ती f.<BR>1 A creeper;<BR>पादाकृष्टव्रततिवलयासंगसंजातपाशः Ś. 1. 33,<BR>R. 14. 1.<BR>--2 Expansion, extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रतती
व्रततिः, --ती f.<BR>1 A creeper;<BR>पादाकृष्टव्रततिवलयासंगसंजातपाशः Ś. 1. 33,<BR>R. 14. 1.<BR>--2 Expansion, extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रध्न
व्रध्न See ब्रध्न.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रह्मन्
व्रह्मन् See ब्रह्मन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्च्
व्रश्च् {c6c} P. (वृश्चति, वृक्ण; caus.<BR>व्रश्चयति-ते; desid. विव्रश्चिषति or विव्रक्षति)<BR>1<BR>To cut, cut up or asunder, tear,<BR>lacerate.<BR>--2 To wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रश्चनः|व्रश्चन|व्रश्चनं
व्रश्चनः<BR>1 A small saw.<BR>--2 A fine<BR>file used by goldsmiths.<BR>--3 The<BR>juice trickling from an incision in a<BR>tree.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Cutting, tearing,<BR>wounding.<BR>--2 A cut, an incision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राजः|व्राज
व्राजः<BR>1 Going, motion.<BR>--2 A<BR>multitude (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्राजिः|व्राजि
व्राजिः f. A gust or gale of wind,<BR>stormy wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातः|व्रात
व्रातः A multitude, group, flock,<BR>an assemblage; श्वपाकानां व्रातैः<BR>G. L. 29; R. 12. 94; Śi. 4. 35.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Bodily or manual labour.<BR>--2<BR>Daylabour.<BR>--3 Casual employment.<BR>--4<BR>The company or attendants at a<BR>marriage feast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रातीन|व्रातीनः
व्रातीन a.<BR>1 Living by day-labour,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">Page1026-c+ 54</a>]<BR>a hired labourer, coolie.<BR>--2 One<BR>living by violence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रात्यः|व्रात्य
व्रात्यः [व्रातात् समूहात च्यवति यत्]<BR>1 A man of the first three<BR>classes who has lost his caste<BR>owing to the non-performance of<BR>the principal Saṃskāras or<BR>purificatory rites (especially investiture<BR>with the sacred thread) over him,<BR>an outcast; भवत्या हि व्र<BR>त्याधमपतितपाखंडपरिषत्परित्राणस्नेहः G. L. 37.<BR>--2<BR>A low or vile person in general.<BR>--3 A man of a particular inferior<BR>tribe (the descendant of a Śūdra<BR>father and Kṣatriya mother).<BR>--त्या<BR>The daughter of an outcast.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ब्रुवः one who calls himself a<BR>Vrātya.<BR>--स्तोमः N. of a sacrifice<BR>performed to rec over the rights<BR>forfeited by the non-performance<BR>of the due Saṃskāras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्री
व्री {vI.v} {c9c} P. (व्रिणाति-व्राणीति) To<BR>choose, select; cf. वृ. {vII.v} {c4c} A. (<BR>व्रीयते, व्रीण)<BR>1 To go, move.<BR>--2 To be<BR>chosen.<BR>--3 To cover, screen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीड्
व्रीड् {c4c} P. (व्रीड्यति)<BR>1 To be<BR>ashamed, feel shame.<BR>--2 To throw,<BR>cast, send forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडः|व्रीड
व्रीडः --डा<BR>1 Shame;<BR>व्रीडादिवाभ्यासगतैर्विलिल्ये Śi. 3. 40; व्रीडमावहति<BR>मे स (शब्दः) संप्रति R. 11. 73.<BR>--2<BR>Modesty, bashfulness; Śi. 10. 18.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आनत, --आन्वित a. modest,<BR>bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडा
व्रीडः --डा<BR>1 Shame;<BR>व्रीडादिवाभ्यासगतैर्विलिल्ये Śi. 3. 40; व्रीडमावहति<BR>मे स (शब्दः) संप्रति R. 11. 73.<BR>--2<BR>Modesty, bashfulness; Śi. 10. 18.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आनत, --आन्वित a. modest,<BR>bashful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडनं|व्रीडन
व्रीडनं<BR>1 Shame.<BR>--2 Modesty.<BR>--3<BR>Lowering, depression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीडित
व्रीडित p. p. Put to shame,<BR>ashamed, abashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीस्
व्रीस् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (व्रीसति,<BR>व्रीसयति-ते) To injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रीहिः|व्रीहि
व्रीहिः [व्री-हि किच्च]<BR>1 Rice; as<BR>in बहुव्रीहि q. v.<BR>--2 A grain of<BR>rice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अगारं a granary.<BR>--कांचनं a kind of pulse.<BR>--राजिकं<BR>panic seed (= कंगू q. v.).<BR>--श्रेष्ठः a<BR>kind of rice (शलिधान्य).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रुड्
व्रुड् {c6c} P. (व्रुडति)<BR>1 To cover.<BR>--2<BR>To be heaped or gathered.<BR>--3 To<BR>heap, accumulate.<BR>--4 To sink, go<BR>down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रूस्
व्रूस् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. See व्रीस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्रैहेय|व्रैहेयः
व्रैहेय a. (यी f.) [व्रीहि-ठक्]<BR>1<BR>Fit for rice.<BR>--2 Sown with rice.<BR>--यं A field of rice, one fit for<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-a" target="_blank">Page1027-a+ 2</a>]<BR>growing rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1026-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्ली
व्ली {c9c} P. (व्लिनाति, rarely व्लीनाति,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-b" target="_blank">Page1027-b+ 2</a>]<BR>caus. व्लेपयति)<BR>1 To go, move.<BR>--2 To<BR>support, hold, maintain.<BR>--3 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">Page1027-c+ 2</a>]<BR>choose, select.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

व्लेक्ष्
व्लेक्ष् {c10c} U. (व्लेक्षयति-ते) To see.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शः|श|शं
शः<BR>1 A cutter, destroyer;<BR>Ki. 15. 45.<BR>--2 A weapon.<BR>--3 N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--शं Happiness; Bh. 2. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंयु|शंयुः
शंयु a. Happy, prosperous;<BR>Bk. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंवः|शंव
शंवः<BR>1 Ploughing in the<BR>regular direction.<BR>--2 The thunderbolt<BR>of Indra.<BR>--3 The iron head of a<BR>pestle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्
शंस् {c1c} P. (शंसति, शस्त; pass.<BR>शस्यते)<BR>1 To praise, extol, approve<BR>of; साधु साध्विति भूतानि<BR>शशंसुर्मारुतात्मजं Rām.; Bg. 5. 1.<BR>--2 To tell,<BR>relate, express, declare,<BR>communicate, announce, report (with dat.<BR>or sometimes gen. of person or by<BR>itself); शशंस सीता परिदेवनांतमनुष्ठितं<BR>शासनमग्रजाय R. 14. 83; न मे ह्रिया<BR>शंसति किंचिदीप्सितं 3. 5, 2. 68, 4. 72,<BR>9. 77, 11. 84; Ku. 3. 60, 5. 51.<BR>--3 To indicate, bespeak, show; यः<BR>(अशोकः) सावज्ञो माधवश्रीनियोगे पुष्पैः<BR>शंसत्यादरं त्वत्प्रयत्ने M. 5. 8;<BR>Ki. 5. 23, Ku. 2. 22.<BR>--4 To repeat,<BR>recite.<BR>--5 To hurt injure.<BR>--6 To revile,<BR>traduce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसः|शंस
शंसः Ved.<BR>1 Praise.<BR>--2<BR>Recitation.<BR>--3 Calling, invocation.<BR>--4 A<BR>charm, spell.<BR>--5 Wishing well,<BR>to.<BR>--6 A blessing.<BR>--7 A curse.<BR>--8<BR>Calumny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसनं|शंसन
शंसनं [शंस्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Praising.<BR>--2<BR>Telling, relating.<BR>--3 Reciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसा
शंसा [शंस्-अ]<BR>1 Praise.<BR>--2 Wish,<BR>desire, hope.<BR>--3 Repeating,<BR>narrating.<BR>--4 Reciting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसित|शंसितः
शंसित p. p. [शंस्-क्त]<BR>1 Prsised,<BR>extolled.<BR>--2 Told, said, spoken,<BR>declared.<BR>--3 Wished, desired.<BR>--4<BR>Ascertained, established,<BR>determined.<BR>--5 Falsely accused,<BR>ealumniated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंसिन्
शंसिन् a. (Usually at the end of<BR>comp.)<BR>1 Praising.<BR>--2 Telling,<BR>announcing, communicating;<BR>प्रजावती दोहदशंसिनी ते R. 14. 45.<BR>--3<BR>Indicating, bespeaking; मूर्धानः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1b" target="_blank">Page1027-1b+ 47</a>]<BR>क्षतहुंकारशंसिनः Ku. 2. 26;<BR>अभिमतफलशंसी चारु पुस्फोर बाहुः Bk. 1. 27;<BR>प्रार्थनासिद्धिशंसिनः R. 1. 42, Śi. 9. 77.<BR>--4 Presaging, foretelling;<BR>R. 3. 14, 12. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंस्तृ
शंस्तृ m.<BR>1 A praiser, panegyrist,<BR>--2 A reciter of hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्
शक् {vI.v} {c5c} P. (शक्नोति, शक्त)<BR>1 To<BR>be able, be competent for, have<BR>power to, effect (usually with an<BR>inf. and translateable by ‘can’);<BR>अदर्शयन् वक्तुमशक्नुवत्यः<BR>शाखाभिरावर्जितपल्लवांभिः R. 13. 24, Bk. 3. 6;<BR>Me. 20; sometimes, with acc. or<BR>dat.; Ms. 11. 139; with gen.<BR>also; see शक्त.<BR>--2 To bear,<BR>endure.<BR>--3 To be powerful.<BR>--Pass. To be able, be possible or<BR>practicable (giving a passive sense<BR>to a following infinitive); तत्कर्तुं<BR>शक्यते ‘it can be done’. --Desid.<BR>(शिक्षति)<BR>1 To wish to be able.<BR>--2<BR>To learn. {vII.v} {c4c} U. (शक्यति-ते, शक्त)<BR>1 To be able, have power to effect.<BR>--2 To bear, endure.<BR>--3 To give.<BR>--4 To<BR>aid.<BR>--5 To know (mostly Ved. in<BR>these senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकः|शक
शकः<BR>1 N. of a king (especially<BR>applied to Śālivāhana; but<BR>scholars do not seem to have yet agreed<BR>as to the precise meaning and scope<BR>of the word).<BR>--2 An epoch, era (the<BR>term is especially applied to the era<BR>of Śālivāhana which commences 78<BR>years after the Christian era).<BR>--काः (m. pl.)<BR>1 N. of a country.<BR>--2 N. of a particular tribe or race<BR>of people (mentioned in Ms. 10. 44<BR>along with the Pauṇḍrakas, &c.;<BR>see Mu. 5. 11 also.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतकः, --अरिः epithets of king<BR>Vikramāditya who is said to have<BR>exterminated the Śakas.<BR>--अब्दः a<BR>year of the Śaka era.<BR>--कर्तृ, --कृत्<BR>m. the founder of an era.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटः|शकट|शकटं
शकटः --टं [शक्-अटन् Uṇ. 4. 81]<BR>A cart, carriage, waggon;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1c" target="_blank">Page1027-1c+ 48</a>]<BR>रोहिणीशकटं Pt. 1. 213, 211, 212; Y. 3. 42.<BR>--टः<BR>1 A form of military array<BR>resembling a wedge; Ms. 7. 187.<BR>--2<BR>A measure of capacity, cart-load<BR>equal to 2000 palas.<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>demon slain by Kṛṣṇa when quite a<BR>boy.<BR>--4 N. of a tree (तिनिश).<BR>--5<BR>An implement for preparing grain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः the axle of a cart.<BR>--अरिः, --हन् m. epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--आह्वा the lunar asterism Rohiṇī<BR>(so called because it is figured by a<BR>cart).<BR>--भेदः the division of<BR>Rohiṇī by a planet passing through it.<BR>--बिलः a gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटं|शकट|शकटः
शकटः --टं [शक्-अटन् Uṇ. 4. 81]<BR>A cart, carriage, waggon;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1c" target="_blank">Page1027-1c+ 48</a>]<BR>रोहिणीशकटं Pt. 1. 213, 211, 212; Y. 3. 42.<BR>--टः<BR>1 A form of military array<BR>resembling a wedge; Ms. 7. 187.<BR>--2<BR>A measure of capacity, cart-load<BR>equal to 2000 palas.<BR>--3 N. of a<BR>demon slain by Kṛṣṇa when quite a<BR>boy.<BR>--4 N. of a tree (तिनिश).<BR>--5<BR>An implement for preparing grain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः the axle of a cart.<BR>--अरिः, --हन् m. epithets of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--आह्वा the lunar asterism Rohiṇī<BR>(so called because it is figured by a<BR>cart).<BR>--भेदः the division of<BR>Rohiṇī by a planet passing through it.<BR>--बिलः a gallinule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकटिका
शकटिका A small cart, a toy-cart;<BR>as in मच्छकटिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकन्
शकन् n. Ordure, feces,<BR>especially of animals; (this word has no<BR>forms for the first five inflections,<BR>and is optionally substituted for<BR>शकृत् after acc. dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलः|शकल|शकलं
शकलः --लं [शक्-कलक्<BR>Uṇ. 1. 109] A part, portion, piece,<BR>fragment, bit; उपलशकलमेतद्भेदकं<BR>गोमयानां Mu. 3. 15; R. 2. 46, 5. 73.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Bark.<BR>--2 The scales (of a<BR>fish).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलं|शकल|शकलः
शकलः --लं [शक्-कलक्<BR>Uṇ. 1. 109] A part, portion, piece,<BR>fragment, bit; उपलशकलमेतद्भेदकं<BR>गोमयानां Mu. 3. 15; R. 2. 46, 5. 73.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Bark.<BR>--2 The scales (of a<BR>fish).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलित
शकलित a. Reduced to fragments,<BR>shattered to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलिन्
शकलिन् m. A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकलीकृ
शकलीकृ {c8c} U. To reduce to<BR>fragments or pieces, cut to pieces,<BR>divide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकारः|शकार
शकारः The brother of a king's<BR>concubine, the brother-in-law of a<BR>king by a wife not regularly<BR>married (अनूढाभ्रातृ); (he is usually<BR>represented as a strange mixture of<BR>pride, folly, and vanity, of low<BR>family, and raised to power by reason<BR>of his relation to the king. In the<BR>Mṛcchakaṭikā of Śūdraka where<BR>he plays a prominent part, his<BR>character is well exhibited in his<BR>lightness and frivolity of spirit,<BR>vain-glory, constant references to<BR>his high connection, his<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-a" target="_blank">Page1028-a+ 57</a>]<BR>blundering and ludicrous folly, but withal<BR>cruelty enough to throttle the<BR>heroine when she refused to yield to<BR>his desire; S. D. thus defines him:<BR>--मदमूर्खताभिमानी दुष्कुलतैश्वर्यसंयुक्तः ।<BR>सोयमनूढाभ्राता राज्ञः श्यालः शकार इत्युक्तः ॥<BR>81).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1027-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनः|शकुन|शकुनं
शकुनः [शक्-उनन् Uṇ. 3. 49]<BR>1<BR>A bird (in general); शकुनोच्छिष्टं<BR>Y. 1. 168.<BR>--2 A kind of bird, a<BR>vulture or kite.<BR>--3 A kind of song<BR>(sung at festivals).<BR>--नं<BR>1 An<BR>omen, a prognostic, any omen<BR>presaging good or evil; Śi. 9. 83.<BR>--2<BR>An auspicious omen.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञ<BR>a. knowing omens.<BR>--(ज्ञा) a small<BR>house-lizard.<BR>--ज्ञानं knowledge of<BR>omens, augury.<BR>--शास्त्रं ‘the science<BR>of omens’, N. of a work.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनिः|शकुनि
शकुनिः [शक्-उनि]<BR>1 A bird;<BR>तरुशकुनिकुरंगान् मैथिली यानपुष्यत्<BR>U. 3. 25; Ms. 12. 63.<BR>--2 A vulture,<BR>kite or eagle.<BR>--3 A cock.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>a son of Subala, king of Gāndhāra<BR>and brother of Gāndhārī, wife of<BR>Dhṛtarāṣṭra; he was thus the<BR>maternal uncle of Duryodhana whom<BR>he assisted in many of his wicked<BR>schemes to exterminate the<BR>Pāṇḍavas. The name is now<BR>usually applied to an old wicked-minded<BR>relative whose counsels tend to<BR>ruin.<BR>--5 N. of a demon killed by<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईश्वरः N. of<BR>Garuḍa.<BR>--प्रपा a trough for<BR>watering birds.<BR>--वादः {1} the cry or<BR>sound of a bird. {2} the crowing of<BR>a cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुनी
शकुनी<BR>1 A hen-sparrow.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुंतः|शकुन्त|शकुंत|शकुन्तः
शकुंतः [शक्-उंत]<BR>1 A bird in<BR>general; अंसव्यापिशकुंतनीडनिचितं<BR>बिभ्रज्जटामंडलं Ś. 7. 11.<BR>--2 The blue<BR>jay.<BR>--3 A kind of bird.<BR>--4 A sort<BR>of insect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुंतकः|शकुन्तक|शकुंतक|शकुन्तकः
शकुंतकः A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुंतला|शकुन्तला
शकुंतला [शकुंतैः लायते ला-घञर्थे<BR>क] N. of the daughter of<BR>Viśvāmitra by the nymph Menakā who<BR>was sent down by Indra to<BR>disturb the sage's austerities. [When<BR>Menakā went up to the heaven she left<BR>the child in a solitary forest where she<BR>was taken care of by ‘Śakuntas’ or<BR>birds, whence she was called<BR>“Śakuntalā”. She was afterwards found by<BR>the sage Kaṇva and brought up as his<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">Page1028-b+ 57</a>]<BR>own daughter. When Duṣyanta in the<BR>course of his hunting came to the sage's<BR>hermitage, he was fascinated by her<BR>charms and prevailed on her to become<BR>his wife by the Gandharva form of<BR>marriage; (see Duṣyanta). She bore to<BR>him a son named Bharata, who became<BR>a universal monarch, and gave his name<BR>to India which came to be called<BR>Bharatavarsha].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुंतिः|शकुन्ति|शकुंति|शकुन्तिः
शकुंतिः A bird; कलमविरलं<BR>रत्युत्कंठाः क्वणंतु शकुंतयः U. 3. 24.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुंतिका|शकुन्तिका
शकुंतिका<BR>1 A bird; छद्मना<BR>परिददामि मृत्यवे सौनिको गृहशकुंतिकामिव<BR>U. 1. 45.<BR>--2 A kind of bird.<BR>--3 A<BR>locust, cricket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुलः|शकुल
शकुलः, --ली A kin of fish.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदनी {1} a kind of<BR>medicinal plant (called Kaṭki). {2}<BR>an earthworm.<BR>--अर्भकः a kind of<BR>fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकुली
शकुलः, --ली A kin of fish.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदनी {1} a kind of<BR>medicinal plant (called Kaṭki). {2}<BR>an earthworm.<BR>--अर्भकः a kind of<BR>fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शकृत्
शकृत् n. [शक्-ऋतन् Uṇ. 4. 58]<BR>Ordure, excrement, especially of<BR>animals.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करिः m. f.,<BR>--करी a<BR>calf; शकृत्करिर्वत्सः Sk.<BR>--द्वारं the<BR>anus.<BR>--पिंडः --पिंडकः a ball or lump<BR>of dung; शष्पाण्यत्ति प्रकिरति<BR>शकृत्पिंडकानाम्रमात्रान् U. 4. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्करः|शक्कर
शक्करः, शक्करिः A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्करिः|शक्करि
शक्करः, शक्करिः A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्करी
शक्करी<BR>1 A river.<BR>--2 A girdle,<BR>zone.<BR>--3 A woman of impure caste.<BR>--4 A finger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्त|शक्तः
शक्त p. p. [शक्-क्त]<BR>1 Able,<BR>capable, competent (with gen. or loc. or<BR>inf.); बहवोऽस्य कर्मणः शक्ताः Ve. 3;<BR>तस्योपकारे शक्तस्त्वं किं जीवन्<BR>किमुतान्यथा ibid.<BR>--2 Strong, mighty,<BR>powerful.<BR>--3 Rich, opulent; Ms. 11. 9.<BR>--4 Significant, expressive,<BR>conveying a meaning by denotation (<BR>अभिधा or शक्ति) and not by indication<BR>(लक्षणा) (as a word).<BR>--5 Clever,<BR>intelligent.<BR>--6 Speaking kindly or<BR>agreeably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिः|शक्ति
शक्तिः f. [शक्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 (a)<BR>Power, ability, capacity, strength,<BR>energy, prowess; दैवं निहत्य कुरु<BR>पौरुषमात्मशक्त्या Pt. 1. 361; ज्ञानि मौनं क्षमा<BR>शक्तौ R. 1. 22; so यथाशक्ति, स्वशक्ति<BR>&c. (b) Faculty, capacity;<BR>स्मरणशक्ति ‘retentive faculty or memory’.<BR>--2 Regal power; (it has three parts<BR>or elements; प्रभुशक्ति or प्रभावशक्ति<BR>‘the majesty or pre-eminent<BR>position of the king himself’; {2} मंत्रशक्ति<BR>‘the power of good counsel’, and<BR>{3} उत्साहशक्ति ‘the power of energy’);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-c" target="_blank">Page1028-c+ 57</a>]<BR>राज्यं नाम शक्तित्रयायत्तं Dk.;<BR>त्रिसाधना शक्तिरिवार्थसंचयं R. 3. 13, 6. 33,<BR>17. 63; Śi. 2. 26.<BR>--3 The power of<BR>composition, poetic power or genius;<BR>शक्तिर्निपुणता लोकशास्त्रकाव्याद्यवेक्षणात्<BR>K. P. 1; see explanation ad loc.<BR>--4 The active power of a deity,<BR>regarded as his wife, female divinity;<BR>(these are variously enumerated, 8,<BR>9 or even 50 being mentioned); स<BR>जयति परिणद्धः शक्तिभिः शक्तिनाथः<BR>Māl. 5. 1; Ś. 7. 35.<BR>--5 A kind of<BR>missile; शक्तिखंडामर्षितेन गांडीविनोक्तं<BR>Ve. 3; ततो बिभेद पौलस्त्यः शक्त्या<BR>वक्षसि लक्ष्मणं R. 12. 77.<BR>--6 A spear,<BR>dart, pike, lance.<BR>--7 (In phil.) The<BR>relation of a term to the thing<BR>designated.<BR>--8 The power inherent in<BR>cause to produce its necessary effect.<BR>--9 (In Rhet.) The power or<BR>signification of a word; (these are three<BR>अभिधा, लक्षणा and व्यंजना); तिस्रः<BR>शब्दस्य शक्तयः S. D. 11.<BR>--10 The<BR>expressive power or denotation of a<BR>word (opp. लक्षणा and व्यंजना); it is<BR>thus defined:<BR>--अस्माच्छब्दादयमर्थो<BR>बोद्धव्य इत्याकारकोऽनादिसंकेतः शक्तिः<BR>Tarka K.<BR>--11 The female organ, the<BR>counterpart of the Phallus of Śiva<BR>worshipped by a sect of people<BR>called Śāktas.<BR>--12 A sword.<BR>--13 An<BR>implement in gambling.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्धः perspiring and panting through<BR>fatigue or exertion.<BR>--अपेक्ष,<BR>--अपेक्षिन् a. having regard to strength;<BR>Śi. 2. 93.<BR>--कुंठनं the deadening of a<BR>power.<BR>--ग्रह a. {1} apprehending the<BR>force or meaning. {2} armed with a<BR>spear.<BR>--(हः) {1} apprehension of the<BR>force, meaning, or acceptation of a<BR>word. {2} a spearman, lancer. {3} an<BR>epithet of Śiva. {4} of Kārtikeya.<BR>--ग्राहक a. determining or<BR>establishing the meaning of a word.<BR>--(कः)<BR>an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>--त्रयं the<BR>three constituent elements of regal<BR>power; see शक्ति (2) above.<BR>--धर a.<BR>strong, powerful.<BR>--(रः) {1} a<BR>spearman. {2} an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>--पाणिः, --भृत् m. {1} a spearman. {2}<BR>an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>--पातः<BR>prostration of strength.<BR>--पूजकः a<BR>Śākta q. v.<BR>--पूजा the worship of<BR>Śakti.<BR>--पूर्वः an epithet of Parāśara.<BR>--कल्यं loss of strength, debility,<BR>incapacity.<BR>--हनि a. powerless, weak,<BR>impotent.<BR>--हेतिकः a lancer, spearman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1028-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तितस्
शक्तितस् ind. According to power,<BR>to the best of one's power or<BR>ability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तिमत्|शक्तिमन्त्
शक्तिमत् a.<BR>1 Strong, able,<BR>powerful, mighty.<BR>--2 Possessing a<BR>competence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्मन्
शक्मन् n. Ved. Power, strength,<BR>energy. --m. N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्य|शक्यः
शक्य pot. p.<BR>1 Possible,<BR>practicable, capable of being done or<BR>effected (usually with an inf.); श<BR>क्यो वारयितुं जलेन हुतभुक् Bh. 2. 11,<BR>R. 2. 49, 54.<BR>--2 Fit to be<BR>effected.<BR>--3 Easy to be effected.<BR>--4 Directly conveyed or<BR>expressed (as the meaning of a word);<BR>शक्योऽर्थोऽभिधया ज्ञेयः S. D. 10.<BR>--5<BR>Potential. (The form शक्यं is some<BR>times used as a predicative word<BR>with an inf. in a passive sense, the<BR>real object of the infinitive being<BR>in the nom. case; एवं हि प्रणय<BR>वती सा शक्यमुपेक्षितुं कुपिता<BR>M. 3. 22; शक्यं…अविरलमालिंगितु पवनः<BR>Ś. 3. 7, विभूतयः शक्यमव प्तुमूर्जिताः<BR>Subhāṣ.; Bg. 18. 11.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः the meaning directly<BR>expressed.<BR>--प्रतीकार a. remediable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्तु|शक्तुः
शक्तु m. n. The flour or meal of<BR>barley, barley-meal; see सक्तु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्न|शक्नः
शक्न, शक्नु , a. Speaking kindly or<BR>agreeably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्नु|शक्नुः
शक्न, शक्नु , a. Speaking kindly or<BR>agreeably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रः|शक्र
शक्रः [शक्-रक्]<BR>1 N. of Indra;<BR>एकः कृती शकुतेषु योऽन्यं शक्रान्न याचते<BR>Kuval.<BR>--2 The Arjuna tree.<BR>--3<BR>The Kuṭaja tree.<BR>--4 An owl.<BR>--5<BR>The asterism ज्येष्ठा.<BR>--6 The number<BR>‘fourteen’.<BR>--7 N. of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अशनः the Kuṭaja tree.<BR>--(नं) an<BR>intoxicating drink prepared from<BR>hemp.<BR>--आख्यः an owl.<BR>--आत्मजः<BR>{1} Jayanta, son of Indra. {2}<BR>Arjuna.<BR>--उत्थानं, --उत्सवः a festival in<BR>honour of Indra on the 12th day of<BR>the bright half of Bhādrapada.<BR>--गोपः a kind of red insect; cf<BR>इंद्रगोप,<BR>--जः, --जातः a crow.<BR>--जित्,<BR>--भिद् m. epithets of Meghanāda, son<BR>of Rāvaṇa.<BR>--द्रुमः the Devadāru tree.<BR>--धनुस् n., शरासनं the rainbow.<BR>--ध्वजः a flag set up in honour of<BR>Indra.<BR>--पर्यायः the Kuṭaja tree.<BR>--पादपः {1} the Kuṭaja tree. {2}<BR>the Devadāru tree.<BR>--प्रस्थं = इंद्रप्रस्थ<BR>q. v.<BR>--भवनं, --भुवनं, वासः heaven,<BR>paradise.<BR>--भूभवा colocynth.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-b" target="_blank">Page1029-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--मातृका a wooden post for supporting<BR>Indra's banner.<BR>--मूर्धन् m.,<BR>--शिरस्<BR>n. an ant-hill, a hillock.<BR>--लोकः the<BR>world of Indra.<BR>--वल्ली colocynth<BR>(इंद्रवारुणी).<BR>--वाहनं a cloud.<BR>--शाखिन् m. the Kuṭaja tree.<BR>--शाला a<BR>sacrificial ground.<BR>--सारथिः ‘the<BR>charioteer of Indra’, an epithet of<BR>Mātali.<BR>--सुतः {1} an epithet of<BR>Jayanta. {2} of Arjuna. {3} of Vāli.<BR>--सृष्टा yellow myrobalan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्राणी
शक्राणी N. of Sacī, wife of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्रिः|शक्रि
शक्रिः<BR>1 A cloud.<BR>--2 The<BR>thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>--3 A mountain.<BR>--4 An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वः|शक्व
शक्वः An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वन्
शक्वन् a. Ved. Strong, powerful.<BR>--m. An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक्वरः|शक्वर
शक्वरः A bull, an ox.<BR>--री<BR>1 A<BR>finger.<BR>--2 A finger-ring.<BR>--3 A girdle,<BR>zone.<BR>--4 A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंक्|शङ्क्
शंक् {c1c} A. (शंकते, शंकित)<BR>1 To<BR>doubt, be uncertain, hesitate, be<BR>doubtful; शंके जीवति वा न वा Rām.<BR>--2 To dread, fear, be afraid (with<BR>abl.); नाशंकिष्ट विवस्वतः Bk. 15. 39;<BR>अशकितेभ्यः शकेत शंकितेभ्यश्च सर्वतः<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--3 To suspect, mistrust,<BR>distrust; स्वैर्दोषैर्भवति हि शंकितो<BR>मनुष्यः Mk. 4. 2.<BR>--4 To think, believe,<BR>fancy, imagine, think probable,<BR>suspect, fear; त्वय्यासन्ने नयनमुपरिस्पंदि<BR>शंके मृगाक्ष्याः Me. 95; नाहं पुनस्तथा<BR>त्वायि यथा हि मां शंकसे भीरु V. 3. 14;<BR>Bk. 3. 26, N. 22. 42.<BR>--5 To start<BR>an objection, raise a doubt or<BR>objection (about); अत्रेदं शंक्यते (often<BR>used in controversial language);<BR>न च ब्रह्मणः प्रमाणांतरगम्यत्वं शंकितुं<BR>शक्यं Sarva S. --Caus. To frighten,<BR>terrify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकनीय|शङ्कनीय
शंकनीय a.<BR>1 Doubtful,<BR>questionable.<BR>--2 Fit to be suspected;<BR>शंकनीया हि लोकेस्मिन्निष्प्रतापा दरिद्रता<BR>Mk. 3. 24.<BR>--3 To be supposed or imagined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंका|शङ्का
शंका [शंक्-अ]<BR>1 Doubt,<BR>uncertainty.<BR>--2 Hesitation, scruple.<BR>--3<BR>Suspicion, distrust misgiving;<BR>अपायशंका; अरिष्टशंका &c.<BR>--4 Fear,<BR>apprehension, dread, alarm;<BR>जातशंकैर्देवेर्मेनका नामाप्सराः प्रेषिता Ś. 1;<BR>कैकेयीशंकयेवाह R. 12. 2; 13. 42;<BR>Me. 69.<BR>--5 Hope, expectation.<BR>--6<BR>(Mistaken) belief, suspicion, (wrong)<BR>impression; स्रजमपि शिरस्यंधः क्षिप्तां<BR>धुनं त्यहिशकया Ś. 7. 24; कुर्वन्<BR>वधूजनमनःसु शशांकशंकां Ki. 5. 42;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-c" target="_blank">Page1029-c+ 57</a>]<BR>हरिततृणोद्गमशंकया 5. 38.<BR>--7 An<BR>objection started in disputation.<BR>--8<BR>Presumption.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वित,<BR>आकुल a filled with fear or doubt,<BR>doubtful, afraid.<BR>--अभियोगः a<BR>charge on suspicion.<BR>--आस्पदं a<BR>matter of doubt.<BR>--निवृत्तिः f. solving<BR>or clearing a doubt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकित|शङ्कित|शङ्कितः
शंकित p. p.<BR>1 Doubted,<BR>suspected, feared.<BR>--2 Suspicious,<BR>suspecting, distrustful.<BR>--3 Uncertain,<BR>doubtful.<BR>--4 Fearful, apprehensive,<BR>alarmed; Pt. 1. 197.<BR>--5 Weak,<BR>unsteady; (see शंक्).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चित,<BR>--मनस् a. {1} timid, faint-hearted. {2}<BR>suspicious, distrustful. {3} doubtful.<BR>--वर्णः a thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकिन्|शङ्किन्
शंकिन् a.<BR>1 Doubting, suspecting,<BR>fearing, believing (at the end of<BR>comp); त्वदुपावर्तमशंकि मे मनः<BR>R. 8. 53; अतिस्नेहः पापशंकी Ś. 4.<BR>--2 Full<BR>of danger; तस्मादंबुपतेरिवावनिपतेः सेवा<BR>सदा शंकिनी Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकुर|शङ्कुर|शङ्कुरः
शंकुर a. Fearful, frightful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकः|शङ्क|शंक|शङ्कः
शंकः A draught-ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकर|शङ्कर|शंकरः|शङ्करः
शंकर a. (रा --री f.) [शं सुखं करोति<BR>कृ-अच्] Conferring happiness or<BR>prosperity, auspicious, propitious.<BR>--रः<BR>1 N. of Śiva.<BR>--2 N. of a celebrated<BR>teacher and author; see App. II.<BR>--री<BR>1 N. of Pārvatī, wife of Śiva.<BR>--2 Bengal madder.<BR>--3 The Śamī<BR>tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवासः the<BR>Kailāsa. {2} camphor.<BR>--प्रियः the<BR>francoline partridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकुः|शङ्कु|शंकु|शङ्कुः
शंकुः [शंक्-उण् Uṇ. 1. 36]<BR>1 A<BR>dart, spear, spike, javelin, dagger;<BR>oft. at the end of comp.; शोकशंकुः<BR>‘the dart of grief’, i. e. sharp or<BR>poignant grief; U. 3. 35; R. 8. 93.<BR>--2 A stake, pillar, post, pale.<BR>--3 A<BR>nail, pin, peg; R. 12. 95.<BR>--4 The<BR>sharp head or point of an arrow,<BR>barb.<BR>--5 The trunk (of a lopped<BR>tree), stump, pollard.<BR>--6 The pin<BR>of a dial.<BR>--7 A measure of twelve<BR>fingers.<BR>--8 A measuring-rod<BR>--9 The<BR>sine of altitude (in astr.).<BR>--10 Ten<BR>billions.<BR>--11 The fibres of a leaf.<BR>--12 An ant-hill.<BR>--13 The penis.<BR>--14<BR>The skate-fish.<BR>--15 A demon.<BR>--16 Poison.<BR>--17 Sin; crime.<BR>--18<BR>An aquatic animal, particularly,<BR>a goose.<BR>--19 N. of Śiva.<BR>--20<BR>The sāla tree.<BR>--21 A kind of<BR>perfume (नखी).<BR>--22 N. of Kāma, the<BR>god of love.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्ण a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">Page1030-a+ 57</a>]<BR>spikecared.<BR>--(र्णः) an ass.<BR>--जीवा (in<BR>astr.) the gnomon sine.<BR>--तरुः, --वृक्षः<BR>the Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1029-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकव्यं|शङ्कव्य
शंकव्यं Anything fit for a stake<BR>(as wood &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकुचिः|शङ्कुचि|शङ्कुचिः
शंकुचिः, शंकोचः(चिः) A<BR>skatefish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकोचः|शङ्कोच|शङ्कोचः
शंकुचिः, शंकोचः(चिः) A<BR>skatefish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकोचिः|शङ्कोचि|शङ्कोचिः
शंकुचिः, शंकोचः(चिः) A<BR>skatefish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकुला|शङ्कुला
शंकुला<BR>1 A kind of knife or<BR>lancet.<BR>--2 A pair of scissors.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडः a piece cut off with a pair of<BR>scissors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंखः|शङ्ख|शंख|शंखं|शङ्खः
शंखः --खं [शम्-ख Uṇ. 1. 102]<BR>1 The conch-shell, a shell; न<BR>श्वेतभावमुज्झति शखः शिखिभुक्तमुक्तोपि<BR>Pt. 4. 110; शंखान् दध्मुः पृथक् पृथक्<BR>Bg. 1. 18.<BR>--2 The bone on the forehead;<BR>शंखांतरद्योति विलोचनं यत् Ku. 7. 33.<BR>--3 The temporal bone.<BR>--4 The part<BR>between the tusks of an elephant.<BR>--5 A hundred billions.<BR>--6 A<BR>military drum or other martial<BR>instrument.<BR>--7 A kind of perfume (नर्खा).<BR>--8 One of the nine treasures of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--9 N. of a demon slain by<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--10 N. of the author of a<BR>Smṛti (mentioned in conjunction<BR>with लिखित q. v.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदकं<BR>the water poured into a conch-shell.<BR>--कारः, --कारकः a shell-cutter,<BR>described as a kind of mixed caste<BR>--क्षीरं an impossibility; cf. खपुष्प.<BR>--चरी, --चर्ची a mark made with<BR>sandal (on the forehead.).<BR>--चूर्णं<BR>powder produced from shells.<BR>--जः a<BR>large pearl (of the shape of a<BR>pigeon's egg).<BR>--द्रावः, --द्रावकः a<BR>solvent for dissolving shells.<BR>--ध्मः,<BR>--ध्मा m. a shell-blower;<BR>conch-blower.<BR>--ध्वनिः the sound of a conch<BR>(sometimes, but erroneously, used<BR>to denote a cry of alarm or despair).<BR>--पालः an epithet of the sun.<BR>--प्रस्थः<BR>a spot on the moon.<BR>--भृत् m. an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--मुखः an alligator.<BR>--मुक्ता the mother of pearls.<BR>--लिखितः a righteous or just king. (-dual)<BR>N. of two writers of Smṛtis.<BR>--स्वनः<BR>the sound of a conch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंखं|शङ्ख|शंख|शंखः|शङ्खः
शंखः --खं [शम्-ख Uṇ. 1. 102]<BR>1 The conch-shell, a shell; न<BR>श्वेतभावमुज्झति शखः शिखिभुक्तमुक्तोपि<BR>Pt. 4. 110; शंखान् दध्मुः पृथक् पृथक्<BR>Bg. 1. 18.<BR>--2 The bone on the forehead;<BR>शंखांतरद्योति विलोचनं यत् Ku. 7. 33.<BR>--3 The temporal bone.<BR>--4 The part<BR>between the tusks of an elephant.<BR>--5 A hundred billions.<BR>--6 A<BR>military drum or other martial<BR>instrument.<BR>--7 A kind of perfume (नर्खा).<BR>--8 One of the nine treasures of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--9 N. of a demon slain by<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--10 N. of the author of a<BR>Smṛti (mentioned in conjunction<BR>with लिखित q. v.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदकं<BR>the water poured into a conch-shell.<BR>--कारः, --कारकः a shell-cutter,<BR>described as a kind of mixed caste<BR>--क्षीरं an impossibility; cf. खपुष्प.<BR>--चरी, --चर्ची a mark made with<BR>sandal (on the forehead.).<BR>--चूर्णं<BR>powder produced from shells.<BR>--जः a<BR>large pearl (of the shape of a<BR>pigeon's egg).<BR>--द्रावः, --द्रावकः a<BR>solvent for dissolving shells.<BR>--ध्मः,<BR>--ध्मा m. a shell-blower;<BR>conch-blower.<BR>--ध्वनिः the sound of a conch<BR>(sometimes, but erroneously, used<BR>to denote a cry of alarm or despair).<BR>--पालः an epithet of the sun.<BR>--प्रस्थः<BR>a spot on the moon.<BR>--भृत् m. an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--मुखः an alligator.<BR>--मुक्ता the mother of pearls.<BR>--लिखितः a righteous or just king. (-dual)<BR>N. of two writers of Smṛtis.<BR>--स्वनः<BR>the sound of a conch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंखकः|शङ्खक|शंखक|शंखकं|शङ्खकं|शङ्खकः
शंखकः --कं A conch-shell.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A disease of the head.<BR>--2 The<BR>temporal bone.<BR>--कं A bracelet<BR>(made of conch-shell); Śi. 13. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंखकं|शङ्खक|शंखक|शङ्खकं|शंखकः|शङ्खकः
शंखकः --कं A conch-shell.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A disease of the head.<BR>--2 The<BR>temporal bone.<BR>--कं A bracelet<BR>(made of conch-shell); Śi. 13. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंखनकः|शङ्खनक|शंखनक|शङ्खनकः
शंखनकः(खः) A small conch or<BR>shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंखनखः|शङ्खनख|शंखनख|शङ्खनखः
शंखनकः(खः) A small conch or<BR>shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंखिन्|शङ्खिन्
शंखिन् m.<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>--2 An<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--3 A conch-blower.<BR>--4 A worker in shells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंखिनी
शंखिनी<BR>1 A woman of one of the<BR>four classes into which writers on<BR>erotic science divide women; the<BR>Ratimañjarī thus describes her:<BR>--दीर्घातिदीर्घनयना वरसुंदरी या<BR>कामोपभोगरसिका गुणशीलयुक्ता । रेखात्रयेण च<BR>विभूषितकंठदेशा सभोगकेलिर संका किल शंखिनी सा ॥<BR>cf. चित्रिणी, हस्तिनी, and पद्मिनी also.<BR>--2<BR>A female spirit, or a kind of fairy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फलः the Śirīṣa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शच्
शच् {c1c} A. (शचते) To speak,<BR>say, tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शचिः|शचि
शचिः --ची f. N. of the wife of<BR>Indra; R. 3. 13, 23.<BR>--ची Ved.<BR>1<BR>Speech, eloquence.<BR>--2 Activity,<BR>energy.<BR>--3 Power, strength,<BR>--4 A<BR>holy or pious act; devotion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिः, --भर्तृ m. epithets of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शची
शचिः --ची f. N. of the wife of<BR>Indra; R. 3. 13, 23.<BR>--ची Ved.<BR>1<BR>Speech, eloquence.<BR>--2 Activity,<BR>energy.<BR>--3 Power, strength,<BR>--4 A<BR>holy or pious act; devotion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतिः, --भर्तृ m. epithets of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंच्|शञ्च्
शंच् {c1c} A. (शंचते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट्
शट् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (शटति)<BR>1 To be sick.<BR>--2 To divide, separate.<BR>--3 To be<BR>dissolved.<BR>--4 To be weary or<BR>dejected.<BR>--5 To go. {vII.v} {c10c} A.<BR>(शाटयते) To praise, flatter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट|शटः
शट a. Sour, acid, astringent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटा
शटा The matted hair of an<BR>ascetic; cf. जटा, सिंहकेशर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शटिः|शटि
शटिः f. The plant called Zedoary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शट्टकं|शट्टक
शट्टकं Flour of rice mixed with<BR>water and ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ्
शठ् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (शठति)<BR>1 To<BR>deceive, cheat, defraud.<BR>--2 To hurt,<BR>kill.<BR>--3 To suffer pain. {vII.v} {c10c} P.<BR>(शठयति)<BR>1 To finish.<BR>--2 To leave<BR>unfinished.<BR>--3 To go, move.<BR>--4 To<BR>be idle or lazy (शठयति).<BR>--5 To<BR>deceive, cheat.<BR>--6 To speak ill of.<BR>--7<BR>To speak well or elegantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शठ|शठं|शठः
शठ a. [शठ् अच्]<BR>1 Crafty,<BR>deceitful, fraudulent, dishonest,<BR>perfidious.<BR>--2 Wicked, depraved.<BR>--ठः<BR>1 A rogue, cheat, knave, swindler;<BR>Ms. 4. 30, Bg. 18. 28.<BR>--2 A false<BR>or deceitful lover (who pretends to<BR>love one woman while his heart is<BR>fixed on another); ध्रुवमस्मि शटः<BR>शुचिस्मिते विदितः कैतबवत्सलस्तव<BR>R. 8. 49, 19. 31; शठ इति मयि तावदस्तु ते<BR>परिचयवत्यवधीरणाप्रिये M. 3. 19. (the<BR>S. D. thus defines a शठः --शठोयमेकत्र<BR>बद्धभावो यः । दर्शिंतबहिरनुरागा विप्रियमन्यत्र<BR>गूढभाचरति ॥ 74).<BR>--3 A fool, blockhead.<BR>--4<BR>A mediator, arbitrator.<BR>--5 The<BR>Dhattūra plant.<BR>--6 An idler, a lazy<BR>fellow.<BR>--ठं<BR>1 Iron.<BR>--2 Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शण्
शण् {c1c} P. (शणति) To give.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणं|शण|शणः
शणं Hemp.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सूत्रं {1} a<BR>hempen cord or string. {2} a net<BR>made of hemp. {3} cordage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शणीरं|शणीर
शणीरं A bank or alluvial island<BR>in the middle of the river Śoṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंठः|शण्ठ
शंठः A eunuch (= शंढ q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंड्|शण्ड्
शंड् {c1c} P. (शंडति)<BR>1 To heap,<BR>collect.<BR>--2 To hurt, wound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंडः|शण्ड|शंड|शण्डं|शण्डः
शंडः [शंड् अच् Uṇ. 1. 113.]<BR>1<BR>An impotent man, a eunuch.<BR>--2 A<BR>bull.<BR>--3 A bull at liberty to move.<BR>--डं A collection, multitude; cf. षंड<BR>or खंड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंढः|शण्ढ|शंढ|शण्ढः
शंढः<BR>1 A eunuch, an impotent<BR>man.<BR>--2 A male attendant in the<BR>women's apartments (chosen from<BR>the class of eunuchs or emasculated<BR>persons).<BR>--3 A bull.<BR>--4 A bull at<BR>liberty to move.<BR>--5 A mad-man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतं|शत
शतं<BR>1 A hundred; निःस्वो वष्टि शतं<BR>Śānti. 2. 6; शतमेकोपि संधत्ते<BR>प्राकारस्थो धनुर्धरः Pt. 1. 229; (शत is used<BR>in the singular with a plural noun<BR>of any gender; शतं नराः; शतं गावः; or<BR>शतं गृहाणि, in which case it is<BR>treated as a numeral adjective; but<BR>sometimes in dual and plural also; द्वे शते;<BR>दश शतानि &c. It is also used with a<BR>noun in the genitive; गवां शतं,<BR>वर्षाणां शतं ‘a century of cows, years’<BR>&c At the end of comp., it may<BR>remain unchanged; भव भर्ता शरच्छतं, or<BR>may be changed into शती; as in<BR>आर्यासप्तशती a work of<BR>Govardhanāchārya.)<BR>--2 Any large number; as in<BR>शतपत्र q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षी {1} night.<BR>{2} the goddess Durgā.<BR>--अंगः {1} a<BR>car, carriage; especially, a war-c<BR>hariot. {2} N. of a tree (तिनिश).<BR>--अनीकः an old man.<BR>--अब्दं a century.<BR>--अरं, --आरं the thunderbolt of<BR>Indra.<BR>--अरुस् n., अरुषी a leprous<BR>disease of the skin.<BR>--अवरः a fine of a<BR>hundred.<BR>--(री) {1} N of a plant. {2}<BR>N. of the wife or Indra.<BR>--आनकं a<BR>cemetery.<BR>--आनंदः {1} N. of<BR>Brahman. {2} of Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa. {3}<BR>of the car of Viṣṇu. {4} of a son of<BR>Gautama and Ahalyā, the<BR>familypriest of Janaka; U. 1. 16.<BR>--आयुस् a. lasting or living for a<BR>hundred years.<BR>--आवर्तः, --आवर्तिन् m. N.<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--ईशः {1} the ruler of a<BR>hundred. {2} the ruler of a<BR>hundred villages, Ms. 7. 115.<BR>--कुंभः<BR>N. of a mountain (where gold is<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-a" target="_blank">Page1031-a+ 56</a>]<BR>said to be found).<BR>--(भं) gold.<BR>--कृत्वस् ind. a hundred times<BR>--कोटि a. hundred-edged.<BR>--(टिः)<BR>Indra's thunderbolt. (--f.) a<BR>hundred crores.<BR>--क्रतुः an epithet of<BR>Indra; R. 3. 38.<BR>--खंडं gold.<BR>--गु<BR>a. possessed of a hundred cows.<BR>--गुण, --गुणित a. a<BR>hundredfold, increased a hundred times;<BR>V. 3. 22.<BR>--ग्रंथिः f. the Dūrvā<BR>grass.<BR>--घ्नः N. of Śiva.<BR>--घ्नी {1} a<BR>kind of weapon used as a missile<BR>(supposed by some to be a sort of<BR>rocket, but described by others as a<BR>huge stone studded with iron spikes<BR>and four tālas in length; शतघ्नी च<BR>चतुस्ताला लोहकंटकसंचिता; or<BR>अयःकंटकसंच्छन्ना शतघ्नी महती शिला);<BR>R. 12. 95. {2} a female scorpion. {3} a<BR>disease of the throat. {4} N. of a<BR>plant (करंज).<BR>--छदः a kind of<BR>wood-pecker.<BR>--जिह्वः an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--तारका, --भिषज --भिषा f.<BR>N. of the 24th lunar mansion<BR>containing one hundred stars.<BR>--दला<BR>the white rose.<BR>--द्रुः f. {1} N. of a<BR>river in the Panjab now called<BR>Sutlej. {2} N. of the Ganges.<BR>--धामन्<BR>m. an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--धार a.<BR>{1} flowing in a hundred streams. {2}<BR>having a hundred edges.<BR>--(रं) the<BR>thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>--धृतिः {1} an<BR>epithet of Indra. {2} of Brahman.<BR>{3} heaven or Svarga.<BR>--पत्रः {1} a<BR>peacock. {2} the (Indian) crane.<BR>{3} a wood-pecker. {4} a parrot or<BR>a species of it.<BR>--(त्रा) a woman.<BR>--(त्रं) a lotus; आवृत्तवृंतशतपत्रनिभं<BR>(आननं) वहंत्या Māl. 1. 22. ˚योनिः<BR>an epithet of Brahman; कंपेन मूर्ध्नः<BR>शतपत्रयोनिं (संभावयामास);<BR>Ku. 7. 46.<BR>--पत्रकः the wood-pecker.<BR>--पत्री, --पत्रिका the white rose.<BR>--पथब्राह्मणं N. of a well-known Brāhmaṇa<BR>attached to the Śukla Yajurveda.<BR>--पद, --पाद् a. having a<BR>hundred feet.<BR>--पदी, --पाद् f. a<BR>centipede.<BR>--पद्मं {1} a lotus<BR>with a hundred petals. {2} the<BR>white lotus.<BR>--पर्वन् m. a bamboo.<BR>(f.) {1} the full-moon day in the<BR>month of Āśvina. {2} Dūrvā grass.<BR>{3} the plant Kaṭukā. {4} orris root.<BR>{5} the wife of Bhārgava or Śukra.<BR>˚ईशः the planet Venus.<BR>--पर्बिका {1}<BR>Dūrvā grass. {2} orris root. {3}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-b" target="_blank">Page1031-b+ 56</a>]<BR>barley.<BR>--पादः, --पाद् m.,<BR>--पादां,<BR>--पादिका a centipede.<BR>--पुष्पः epithet of<BR>the poet Bhāravi.<BR>--प्रासः the<BR>Karavīra tree.<BR>--भिषज् see ˚तारका.<BR>--भीरुः<BR>f. the Arabian jasmine.<BR>--मखः, --मन्युः<BR>{1} epithets of Indra; Ki. 2. 23;<BR>Bk. 1. 5; Ku. 2. 64; R. 9. 13. {2} an<BR>owl.<BR>--मानः, --नं {1} a Pala of silver.<BR>{2} an Āḍhaka q. v.<BR>--पार्जः an<BR>armourer.<BR>--मुख a. {1} having a<BR>hundred ways. {2} having a hundred<BR>outlets, mouths, or openings;<BR>विवेकभ्रष्टानां भवति विनिपानः शतमुखः<BR>Bh. 2. 10 (where the word has sense 1.<BR>also).<BR>--(खं) a hundred ways or<BR>openings.<BR>--(खी) a brush, broom.<BR>--मूला the Dūrvā grass.<BR>--यज्वन् m.<BR>an epithet of Indra.<BR>--यष्टिकः a<BR>necklace of one hundred strings.<BR>--रूपा<BR>N. of a daughter of Brahman (who<BR>is supposed to be also his wife, from<BR>whose incestuous connection with<BR>her father is said to have sprung<BR>Manu Svāyambhuva).<BR>--लुपः,<BR>--लुपकः an epithet of the poet Bhāravi.<BR>--वर्ष a. {1} a century old. {2} lasting<BR>for a hundred years.<BR>--(र्षं) one<BR>hundred years, a century.<BR>--वीर्या {1}<BR>whiteflowering Dūrvā. {2} the plant<BR>Śatāvarī.<BR>--वेधिन m. a kind of sorrel.<BR>--शाख<BR>a. {1} various, multiform. {2} having<BR>hundred, i. e. many branches.<BR>--सहस्रं {1} a hundred thousand. {2}<BR>several hundreds, i. e. a large number.<BR>--साहस्र a. {1} consisting of or<BR>containing a hundred thousand {2}<BR>bought with a hundred thousand.<BR>--ह्रदा {1} lightning; Ku. 7. 39;<BR>Mk. 5. 48; V. 4. {2} the thunderbolt of<BR>Indra.<BR>--ह्रादा the thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1030-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतक|शतकः
शतक a.<BR>1 A hundred.<BR>--2<BR>Containing a hundred.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A century.<BR>--2 A collection of one hundred<BR>stanzas; as in नीति˚, वैराग्य˚, शृंगार˚ a<BR>collection of one hundred stanzas<BR>on Nīti’ &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शततम|शततमः
शततम a. (मी f.) One-hundredth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतधा
शतधा ind.<BR>1 In a hundred ways.<BR>--2 Into a hundred parts or pieces<BR>--3 A hundred-fold. --f. The Dūrvā<BR>grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतशस्
शतशस् ind.<BR>1 By hundreds.<BR>--2<BR>A hundred times; शतशः शपे<BR>Prab. 3; Ms. 12. 58.<BR>--3 A hundred-fold,<BR>variously, multifariously; Bg. 11. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतिक|शतिकः
शतिक a. (की f.), शत्य a. [शतेन क्रोतः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">Page1031-c+ 56</a>]<BR>शतस्य विकारः तस्यायं वा इति ठन् यत् वा]<BR>1<BR>Containing or consisting of a<BR>hundred; Y. 2. 208.<BR>--2 Relating to a<BR>hundred.<BR>--3 Effected with a<BR>hundred.<BR>--4 Bought with a hundred.<BR>--5<BR>Changed with or for a hundred.<BR>--6<BR>Bearing tax or interest per<BR>hundred.<BR>--7 Indicative of (the<BR>acquisition of) a hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतिन्
शतिन् a.<BR>1 A hundred-fold.<BR>--2<BR>Numerous. --m. The owner of a<BR>hundred; निःस्वो वष्टि शतं शती<BR>दशशतं Śānti. 2. 6; Pt. 5. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोनः|शतपोन
शतपोनः A sieve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतपोनकः|शतपोनक
शतपोनकः Fistula in the anus<BR>(with many external openings).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतृ
शतृ A technical term used by<BR>Pāṇini to denote the Kṛt affix अत्<BR>used in forming present participles<BR>of the Parasmaipada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शतेरः|शतेर
शतेरः<BR>1 An enemy.<BR>--2 Injury,<BR>hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्त्रिः|शत्रि
शत्त्रिः An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुः|शत्रु
शत्रुः [शद्-त्रुन् Uṇ. 4. 103]<BR>1 An<BR>overthrower, a destroyer, conqueror.<BR>--2 An enemy, a foe, an adversary;<BR>क्षमा शत्रौ च मित्रे च यतीनामेव भूषणं<BR>Subhāṣ.: ऋणकर्ता पिता शत्रुर्माता च<BR>व्यभिचारिणी । भार्या रूपवती शत्रुः पुत्रः<BR>शत्रुरपंडितः Subhāṣ.<BR>--3 A political<BR>rival, a rival neighbouring king.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपजापः the secret<BR>whisperings of a foe, treacherous<BR>overtures of an enemy.<BR>--कर्षण, --दमन,<BR>--निबर्हण a. subduing, overpowering,<BR>or destroying enemies.<BR>--घ्नः<BR>‘destroyer of enemies’, an epithet of<BR>a brother of Rāma and twin brother<BR>of Lakṣmaṇa, being a son of<BR>Sumitrā. He killed the demon Lavaṇa<BR>and colonized Mathurā. He had<BR>two sons named Subāhu and<BR>Bahuśruta; see R. 15.<BR>--पक्षः {1} the<BR>party or side of an enemy. {2} an<BR>opponent, antagonist.<BR>--मर्शनः an<BR>epithet of Śatrughna.<BR>--विग्रहः a<BR>hostile invasion.<BR>--विनाशनः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--सह, --साह a.<BR>withstanding an enemy.<BR>--सेविन् a.<BR>serving a hostile prince; Ms. 7. 186.<BR>--हत्या foe-slaughter.<BR>--हन् a.<BR>foeslayer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुंजयः|शत्रुञ्जय|शत्रुंजय|शत्रुञ्जयः
शत्रुंजयः {1} An elephant. {2} N.<BR>of a mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्रुंतप|शत्रुन्तप|शत्रुन्तपः
शत्रुंतप a. Overcoming or<BR>destroying one's foes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1031-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शत्वरी
शत्वरी Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्
शद् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (but A. in<BR>conjugational tenses) शीयते, शन्न<BR>1 To fall,<BR>perish, decay, wither.<BR>--2 To go.<BR>--Caus. शादयति-ते<BR>1 To cause to<BR>go, impel.<BR>--2 शातयति-ते (a) To<BR>fell, throw down, cut down; किं<BR>भूभृत्कटकस्थितिव्यसनिना व्यर्थं खुराः<BR>शातिताः Subhāṣ.; Śi. 14. 80, 15. 24,<BR>(b) To kill, destroy. {vII.v} {c1c} P. (<BR>शदति) To go (usually with आ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शदः|शद
शदः An eatable vegetable product<BR>(fruit, root &c.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रिः|शद्रि
शद्रिः<BR>1 An elephant.<BR>--2 Cloud.<BR>--3<BR>N. of Arjuna.<BR>--द्रिः f.<BR>1 Lightning.<BR>--2 Candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शद्रु|शद्रुः
शद्रु a.<BR>1 Going, moving.<BR>--2<BR>Falling, perishing, decaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शन्न
शन्न p. p. Fallen, decayed,<BR>withered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनकैस्
शनकैस् ind. Slowly; see शनैस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनिः|शनि
शनिः [शो-अनि किच्च Tv.]<BR>1 The<BR>planet Saturn (the son of the sun<BR>and represented as of a black colour<BR>or dressed in dark-coloured clothes).<BR>--2 Saturday.<BR>--3 N. of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं black pepper.<BR>--प्रदोषः a term<BR>for the (evening) worship of Śiva<BR>performed on the thirteenth day of<BR>a lunar fortnight when it falls on<BR>a Saturday.<BR>--प्रसूः f. an epithet of<BR>Chāyā, wife of the sun; cf. संज्ञा.<BR>--प्रियं a sapphire.<BR>--वारः, --वासरः<BR>Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शनैस्
शनैस् ind.<BR>1 Slowly, gently,<BR>quietly.<BR>--2 Gradually, by degrees, little<BR>by little; धर्मं संचिनुय च्छनैः;<BR>Ku. 3. 59; Ms. 3. 217.<BR>--3 Successively,<BR>in due order, Ms. 1. 15.<BR>--4<BR>Mildly, softly.<BR>--5 Tardily, sluggishly.<BR>--6<BR>Independently. (शनैः शनैः slowly, by<BR>slow degrees).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चर a.<BR>going or moving slowly; शनैश्वराब्यां<BR>पादाब्यां रेजे ग्रहमयीव सा Bh. 1. 17.<BR>(where it means ‘Saturn’ also).<BR>--रः the planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंतनुः|शन्तनु|शंतनु|शन्तनुः
शंतनुः N. of a king of the lunar<BR>race. He married Gaṅgā and<BR>Satyavatī; by the former wife he had a son<BR>named Bhīṣma, and by the latter<BR>Citrāṅgada and Vicitravīrya.<BR>Bhīṣma remained a celibate all his<BR>life, and his younger brothers died<BR>childless; cf. भीष्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् A technical term used by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-b" target="_blank">Page1032-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Pāṇini for the conjugational sign<BR>अ inserted between the root and<BR>the terminations of the<BR>conjugational tenses in the first class of<BR>roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् ind. A particle and prefix<BR>implying assent or compliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्
शप् {c1c} {c4c} U. (शपति-ते, शप्यति-ते, शप्त)<BR>1 To curse, execrate; अशपद्भव<BR>मानुषीति तां R. 8. 80; सोऽभूत्परासुरथ<BR>भूमिपतिं शशाप (वृद्धः) 9. 78, 1. 77.<BR>--2 To<BR>swear, take an oath, promise by<BR>oath, say on oath, (usually with<BR>dat. of the person to whom a<BR>promise &c. is made and instr. of the<BR>object by which it is made);<BR>भरतेनात्पना चाहं शपे ते मनुजाधिप । यथा<BR>नान्येन तुष्येयमृते रामविवासनात् Rām;<BR>when used without an object it<BR>generally governs the instr. of the<BR>thing and dat. of the person by<BR>which or whom the oath is taken;<BR>सत्यं शपामि ने पादपंकजस्पर्शेन K.;<BR>Ghaṭ. 22; अशप्त निह्नुवानाऽसौ सीतायै<BR>स्मरमोहितः Bk. 8. 74; प्रेम<BR>जिज्ञासमानाब्यस्ताब्योऽशप्सत कामिनः 8. 33;<BR>sometimes शप् governs a cognate<BR>accusative सहत्रशोऽसौ शपथानशप्यत्<BR>Bk. 3. 32.<BR>--3 To blame, scold, revile, abuse<BR>(with dat or by itself);<BR>द्विषद्भ्यश्चाशपस्तया Bk. 17. 4. प्रतिवाचमदत्त<BR>केशवः शपमानाय न चेदिभूभुजे<BR>Śi. 16 25. --Caus. (शापयति-ते) To bind by<BR>an oath, conjure; शापितोऽसि<BR>गोब्राह्मणकाम्यया Mk. 3; शापितासि मम<BR>लवंगिकावलोकितयोश्व जीवितेन यदि वाचा न<BR>कथयसि Māl. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपः|शप
शपः शप्-अच्<BR>1 A curse, an<BR>imprecation.<BR>--2 An oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपथः|शपथ
शपथः [शप्-अथन्]<BR>1 Cursing.<BR>--2 A<BR>curse, an imprecation, anathema.<BR>--3 An oath, swearing, taking or<BR>administering an oath, asseveration<BR>by oath or ordeal; आमोदो न हि<BR>कस्तूर्याः शपथेनानुभ व्यते Bv. 1. 120;<BR>Ms. 8. 109.<BR>--4 Conjuration, binding by<BR>oaths; Māl. 3. 2.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रं an<BR>affidavit, a statement on oath.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शपनं|शपन
शपनं<BR>1 See शपथ.<BR>--2 Reviling;<BR>abuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शप्त|शप्तः
शप्त p. p.<BR>1 Cursed.<BR>--2 Sworn.<BR>--3<BR>Reviled, abused; (see शप्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफः|शफ|शफं
शफः --फं [शम्-अच् पृषो˚ पस्यफः]<BR>1<BR>A hoof.<BR>--2 The root of a tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ऊरुः f. a woman having<BR>thighs resembling the two divisions<BR>of a cow's hoof; see P. IV. 1. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफं|शफ|शफः
शफः --फं [शम्-अच् पृषो˚ पस्यफः]<BR>1<BR>A hoof.<BR>--2 The root of a tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ऊरुः f. a woman having<BR>thighs resembling the two divisions<BR>of a cow's hoof; see P. IV. 1. 70.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शफरः|शफर
शफरः (री f.) [शफं राति रा-क Tv.]<BR>A kind of small glittering fish;<BR>मोघीकर्तुं चटुलशफरोद्वर्तनप्रेक्षितानि Me. 40;<BR>Śi. 8. 24; Ku. 4. 39.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिपः the fish called Ilīśa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबरः|शबर
शब(व)रः<BR>1 A mountaineer,<BR>barbarian, savage; राजन् गुंजाफलानां<BR>स्त्रज इति शवरा नैव हारं हरांति K. P. 10.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva.<BR>--3 The hand.<BR>--4<BR>Water.<BR>--5 N. of a celebrated<BR>commentator and writer on<BR>Mīmāmsā<BR>--री<BR>1 A Śabara female.<BR>--2<BR>A female Kirāta who was an ardent<BR>devotee of Rāma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आलयः<BR>the abode of wild mountaineers or<BR>barbarians.<BR>--लोध्रः the wild Lodhra<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवरः|शवर
शब(व)रः<BR>1 A mountaineer,<BR>barbarian, savage; राजन् गुंजाफलानां<BR>स्त्रज इति शवरा नैव हारं हरांति K. P. 10.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva.<BR>--3 The hand.<BR>--4<BR>Water.<BR>--5 N. of a celebrated<BR>commentator and writer on<BR>Mīmāmsā<BR>--री<BR>1 A Śabara female.<BR>--2<BR>A female Kirāta who was an ardent<BR>devotee of Rāma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आलयः<BR>the abode of wild mountaineers or<BR>barbarians.<BR>--लोध्रः the wild Lodhra<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शबल|शबलः
शब(व)ल a.<BR>1 Spotted,<BR>brindled, variegated; क्वचित्प्रभा चांद्रमसी<BR>तमोभिश्र्छायाविलीनैः शबलीकृतेव<BR>R. 13. 56, 5. 44; Mv. 7. 26.<BR>--2 Varied,<BR>divided into various parts.<BR>--3<BR>Articulate; imitative.<BR>--लः A<BR>variegated colour.<BR>--ला, --ली<BR>1 A spotted or<BR>brindled cow.<BR>--2 The cow of plenty<BR>or Kāmadhenu q. v.<BR>--लं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवल|शवलः
शब(व)ल a.<BR>1 Spotted,<BR>brindled, variegated; क्वचित्प्रभा चांद्रमसी<BR>तमोभिश्र्छायाविलीनैः शबलीकृतेव<BR>R. 13. 56, 5. 44; Mv. 7. 26.<BR>--2 Varied,<BR>divided into various parts.<BR>--3<BR>Articulate; imitative.<BR>--लः A<BR>variegated colour.<BR>--ला, --ली<BR>1 A spotted or<BR>brindled cow.<BR>--2 The cow of plenty<BR>or Kāmadhenu q. v.<BR>--लं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्द्
शब्द् {c10c} U. (शब्दयति ते, शब्दित)<BR>1<BR>To sound, make a noise.<BR>--2 To<BR>speak, call out, call out to;<BR>विततमृदुकराग्रः शब्दयंत्या वयोभिः परिपतति<BR>दिवोंऽके हेलया बालसूर्यः Śi. 11. 47.<BR>--3 To<BR>name, call; अत एव सागरिकेति शब्द्यते<BR>Ratn. 4. --WITH अभि to name.<BR>--प्र<BR>to explain.<BR>--सं to call out to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दः|शब्द
शब्दः [शब्द्-घञ्]<BR>1 Sound (the<BR>object of the sense of hearing and<BR>property of आकाश); अथात्मनः<BR>शब्दगुणं गुणजः पदं विमानेन विगाहमानः<BR>R. 13. 1.<BR>--2 Sound, note (of birds;<BR>men &c.), noise in general;<BR>विश्वासोपगमादभिन्नगतयः शब्दं सहंते मृगाः<BR>Ś. 1. 14; Bg. 1. 13; Ś. 3. 1; Ms. 4. 31;<BR>Ku. 1. 45.<BR>--3 The sound of a musical<BR>instrument; वाद्यशब्दः Pt. 2;<BR>Ku. 1. 45.<BR>--4 A word, sound, significant<BR>word (for def. &c. see Mbh.<BR>introduction); एकः शब्दः सम्यगधीतः<BR>सम्यक् प्रयुक्तः स्वर्गे लोके कामधुग्भवति;<BR>so शब्दार्थौ.<BR>--5 A declinable word, a<BR>noun, substantive.<BR>--6 A title, an<BR>epithet; यस्यार्थयुक्तं गिरिराजशब्दं<BR>कुर्वंति ब लव्यजनैश्चमर्यः Ku. 1. 13;<BR>Ś. 2. 14; नृपेण चक्रे युवराजशब्दभाक्<BR>R. 3. 35, 2. 53, 64, 3. 49, 5. 22; 18. 42;<BR>V. 1. 1.<BR>--7 The name, mere-name;<BR>as in शब्दपति q. v.<BR>--8 Verbal<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1033-a" target="_blank">Page1033-a+ 57</a>]<BR>authority (regarded by the Naiyāyikas<BR>as a Pramāṇa).<BR>--9 Grammar.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतीत a. beyond the<BR>power or reach of words,<BR>indescribable.<BR>--अधिष्ठानं the ear.<BR>--अध्याहारः<BR>supplying a word (to complete an<BR>ellipsis).<BR>--अनुरूप a. proportionate<BR>or corresponding to the sound;<BR>शबदानुरूपेण पाक्रमेण भवितव्यं Pt. 1.<BR>--अनुशासनं the science of words;<BR>i. e. grammar.<BR>--अर्थः the meaning<BR>of a word. (--र्थौ dual) a word and<BR>its meaning; अदोषौ शब्दार्थौ<BR>K. P. 1.<BR>--अलंकारः a figure of speech<BR>depending for its charmingness on<BR>sound or words and disappearing as<BR>soon as the words which constitute<BR>the figure are replaced by others of<BR>the same meaning (opp. अर्थालंकार);<BR>e. g. see K. P. 9<BR>--आखयय a. to be<BR>communicated in words; Me. 103.<BR>--(यं) an oral or verbal<BR>communication.<BR>--आडबरः bombast, verbosity,<BR>high-sounding or grandiloquent<BR>words.<BR>--आदि a. beginning with<BR>शब्द (as the objects of sense);<BR>R. 10. 25.<BR>--कार a. sounding sonorous.<BR>--कोशः a lexicon, dictionary.<BR>--गत<BR>a. inherent or residing in a word.<BR>--गुण a. having sound for its<BR>quality; R. 13. 1.<BR>--ग्रहः {1} catching the<BR>sound. {2} the ear.<BR>--ग्रामः the range or<BR>reach of sound.<BR>--चातुर्यं cleverness<BR>of style, eloquence.<BR>--चित्रं one of<BR>the two subdivisions of the last<BR>(अवर or अधम) class of poetry<BR>(wherein the charm lies in the use<BR>of words which please the ear<BR>simply by their sound; see the example<BR>given under the word चित्र).<BR>--चोरः<BR>'a word-thief,’ a plagiarist.<BR>--तन्मात्रं<BR>the subtle element of sound.<BR>--पतिः<BR>a lord in name only, nominal lord;<BR>ननु शब्दपतिः क्षितेरहं त्वायि मे<BR>भावनिबंधना रतिः R. 8. 52.<BR>--पातिन् a.<BR>hitting an invisible mark the sound<BR>of which is only heard, tracing a<BR>sound; शब्दपातिनमिषुं विससर्ज<BR>R. 9. 73.<BR>--प्रमाणं verbal or oral<BR>evidence.<BR>--बोधः knowledge derived<BR>from verbal testimony.<BR>--ब्रह्मन् n.<BR>{1} the Vedas. {2} spiritual<BR>knowledge consisting in words,<BR>knowledge of the Supreme Spirit or<BR>the Spirit itself; शब्दब्रह्मणस्तादृशं<BR>विवर्तमितिहासं U. 2, 7. 20. {3} a<BR>property of words called स्फोट q. v.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1033-b" target="_blank">Page1033-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--भेदिन् a. hitting a mark merely<BR>by its sound. (--m.) {1} an epithet<BR>of Arjuna. {2} the anus. {3} a<BR>kind of arrow.<BR>--योमिः f. a root,<BR>radical word.<BR>--विद्या, शास्त्रं the<BR>science of words; i. e. grammar;<BR>अनंतपारं किल शब्दशास्त्रं Pt. 1;<BR>Śi. 2. 112; 14. 24.<BR>--विरोधः<BR>opposition of words (in a sentence).<BR>--विशेषः a variety of sound.<BR>--विशेषणं (in gram.) an adjective,<BR>adjectival word.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. the<BR>function of a word (in Rhet.).<BR>--वेधिन् a. hitting an invisible<BR>mark the sound of which is only<BR>heard; see शब्दपातिन्. (--m.) {1} a<BR>kind of arrow. {2} an archer. {3}<BR>a warrior who pierces his enemies<BR>by mere sounds. {4} an epithet of<BR>king Daśaratha. {5} an epithet<BR>of Arjuna.<BR>--शक्तिः f. the force or<BR>expressive power of a word;<BR>signification of a word; see शक्ति.<BR>--शासनं<BR>{1} a rule of grammar. {2} the<BR>science of grammar.<BR>--शुद्धिः f. {1}<BR>purity of words. {2} the correct use<BR>of words.<BR>--श्लेषः a play or pun<BR>upon words, a verbal equivoque;<BR>(it differs from अर्थश्लेष in-as-much<BR>as the pun disappears as soon as<BR>the words which constitute it are<BR>replaced by others of the same<BR>signification, whereas in अर्थश्लष the<BR>pun remains unchanged; शब्दपरि<BR>वृत्तिसहत्वमर्थश्र्लेषः)<BR>--संग्रहः a<BR>vocabulary, lexicon.<BR>--सौष्ठवं elegance<BR>of words, a graceful or elegant<BR>style.<BR>--सौकर्यं ease of<BR>expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1032-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दन|शब्दनः
शब्दन a. [शब्द् ल्यु ल्युट् वा] Sounding,<BR>making a sound.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Sounding,<BR>making a noise, uttering a sound<BR>--2 A sound, noise.<BR>--3 Calling out,<BR>calling.<BR>--4 Naming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दायते
शब्दायते Den. A.<BR>1 To make a<BR>noise, sound; शब्दायंते मधुरमनिलैः<BR>कीचकाः पूर्यमाणाः Me. 56.<BR>--2 To<BR>cry, roar, scream, yell; Bk. 5. 52;<BR>17. 91.<BR>--3 To call, call out to;<BR>एते हस्तिनापुरगामिन ऋषयः शब्दाय्यंते<BR>Ś. 4; Mu. 1; भवतु शब्दायिष्ये तावत्<BR>Ve. 3; Mk. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शब्दित
शब्दित p. p.<BR>1 Sounded, made<BR>to give out a sound, played upon<BR>(as a musical instrument).<BR>--2<BR>Uttered, articulated.<BR>--3 Called, called<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1033-c" target="_blank">Page1033-c+ 57</a>]<BR>out to.<BR>--4 Named; designated.<BR>--5<BR>Explained.<BR>--6 Made public,<BR>manifested.<BR>--तं Noise, cry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1033-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
शम् ind. A particle meaning<BR>welfare, happiness, prosperity,<BR>health, and generally used to<BR>express a blessing or pious wish,<BR>(with dat. or gen.); शं देवदत्ताय<BR>or देवदत्तस्य (often used in modern<BR>letters as an auspicious conclusion;<BR>इति शम्).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर see s. v.<BR>--ताति a. conferring happiness,<BR>propitious, auspicious.<BR>--पाकः {1}<BR>lac, red dye. {2} cooking,<BR>maturing.<BR>--भु see s. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्
शम् {vI.v} {c4c} P. (शाम्यति, शांत)<BR>1 To<BR>be calm, quiet or tranquil, be<BR>appeased or pacified; (as a<BR>person); शाम्येत्प्रत्यपकारेण नोपकारेण<BR>दुर्जनः Ku. 2. 40; काकुत्स्थमुद्दिश्य<BR>समत्सरोऽपि शशाम तेत क्षितिपाललोकः<BR>R. 7. 3; शांतो लवः U. 6. 7.<BR>--2 To<BR>cease, stop, come to an end; चिंता<BR>शशाम सकलाऽपि सरोरुहाणां Bv. 3. 7; न<BR>जातु कामः कामानामुपभोगेन शाम्यति<BR>Ms. 2. 94 ‘is not satisfied’.<BR>--3 To be<BR>quelled, be extinguished or<BR>quenched; शशाम वृष्ट्र्यापि विना दवाग्निः R. 2. 14,<BR>U. 5. 7.<BR>--4 To desist, leave off<BR>(speaking &c.).<BR>--5 To put an end<BR>to, destroy, kill (also {c9c} P. in this<BR>sense). --Caus. (शमयति-ते, but<BR>शामयति-ते in the sense of ‘seeing’, see शम्<BR>II).<BR>1 To appease, allay, calm,<BR>tranquillize, pacify, soothe; कः शीतलैः<BR>शमयिता वचनैस्तवाधिं Bv. 3. 1; संरंभं<BR>शमयामास R. 15. 85, 17. 55; Ś. 5. 7.<BR>--2 To put an end, to stop;<BR>Ku. 2. 56.<BR>--3 To remove, avert; प्रतिकूलं<BR>दैवं शमयितुं Ś. 1.<BR>--4 To subdue, tame,<BR>defeat, conquer, vanquish; शमयति<BR>गजानन्यान् गंधद्विपः कलभोऽपि सन्<BR>V. 5. 18; R. 9. 12, 11. 59.<BR>--5 To kill,<BR>destroy, slay; Ve. 5. 5.<BR>--6 To<BR>quench, extinguish; सुतप्तमपि पानीयं<BR>शमयत्येव पावकं H. 1. 88, Me. 53.<BR>--7 To leave off, desist, cease. {vII.v}<BR>{c10c} U. शामयति-ते<BR>1 To see,<BR>look at, inspect.<BR>--2 To show,<BR>display.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमः|शम
शमः [शम्-घञ्]<BR>1 Quiet,<BR>tranquillity, calmness.<BR>--2 Rest, calm, repose,<BR>cessation.<BR>--3 Absence or restraint<BR>of passions, mental quietness,<BR>quietism; शमरतेऽमरतेजसि पार्थिवे<BR>R. 9. 4; Ki. 10. 10; 16. 48, Śi. 2. 94;<BR>Bg. 10. 4.<BR>--4 Allayment, mitigation,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-a" target="_blank">Page1034-a+ 56</a>]<BR>alleviation, satisfaction, pacification<BR>(of grief, thirst, hunger &c.);<BR>शममुपयातु ममापि चित्तदाहः U. 6. 8;<BR>शममेष्यति मम शोकः कथं नु वत्से Ś. 4. 20.<BR>--5 Peace; as in शमोपन्यास Ve. 5.<BR>--6 Final emancipation (from all<BR>worldly illusions and attachments).<BR>--7 The hand.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतकः the<BR>god of love (a destroyer of mental<BR>tranquillity).<BR>--पर a. tranquil,<BR>quiet, stoical.<BR>--प्रधान a. in whom<BR>tranquillity or quietism<BR>predominates; शमप्रधानेषु तपोधनेषु Ś. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1033-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमथः|शमथ
शमथः शम्-अथच्<BR>1 Tranquillity,<BR>calmness; especially mental<BR>calmness, absence of passion.<BR>--2 A<BR>counsellor, minister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमन|शमनं|शमनः
शमन a. नी f. [शम् णिच् ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>Quelling, allaying, subduing &c.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Appeasing, allaying,<BR>soothing, conquering, alleviating, &c.<BR>--2<BR>Calmness, tranquillity.<BR>--3 End,<BR>stop, cessation, destruction.<BR>--4<BR>Hurting, injuring.<BR>--5 Killing animals<BR>for sacrifice, immolation.<BR>--6<BR>Swallowing, chewing.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A kind of<BR>deer, an antelope.<BR>--2 N of Yama,<BR>the god of death.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्वसृ f.<BR>'Yama's sister', epithet of the river<BR>Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमनी
शमनी Night.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सदः (--षदः)<BR>a demon, goblin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमलं|शमल
शमलं [शम्-कलच्]<BR>1 Feces, ordure,<BR>excrement.<BR>--2 Impurity, sediment<BR>--3 Sin, moral impurity.<BR>--4 A<BR>calamity, misfortune.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमित|शमितः
शमित p. p.<BR>1 Appeased, allayed,<BR>soothed, calmed.<BR>--2 Alleviated,<BR>cured, relieved.<BR>--3 Relaxed.<BR>--4<BR>Calm, sedate.<BR>--5 Moderated,<BR>tempered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिन्
शमिन् a.<BR>1 Calm, tranquil, pacific.<BR>--2 One who has subdued his<BR>passions, self-controlled; Bk. 7. 5,<BR>Mk. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमी
शमी [शम्-इन् वा ङीप्] (शमि<BR>sometimes)<BR>1 N. of a tree (said<BR>to contain fire); अग्निगर्भां शमीमिव<BR>Ś. 4. 3; Ms. 8. 247; ध्रुवं स<BR>नीलोत्पलपत्रधारया शमीलतां छेत्तुमृषिर्व्यवस्यति<BR>Ś. 1. 18; Y. 1. 302.<BR>--2 A pod, legume.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गर्भः {1} an epithet of fire.<BR>{2} a Brāhmaṇa, one belonging to<BR>the sacerdotal or priestly class.<BR>--धान्यं any pulse or grain growing<BR>in pods, leguminous grain.<BR>--रोहः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">Page1034-b+ 55</a>]<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमीरः|शमीर
शमी(मि)रः A small variety of<BR>the Śamī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शमिरः|शमिर
शमी(मि)रः A small variety of<BR>the Śamī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंपा|शम्पा
शंपा Lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंब्|शम्ब्
शंब् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (शंबति) To go, move.<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} P. (शंबयति) To collect, heap<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंब|शम्ब|शम्बः
शंब(व)^1 a [शंब्-अच्]<BR>1 Happy,<BR>fortunate.<BR>--2 Poor, unfortunate.<BR>--बः<BR>1 The thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>--2 The iron head of a pestle.<BR>--3 An<BR>iron chain worn round the loins.<BR>--4 Ploughing ‘with the grain’ or in<BR>the regular direction.<BR>--5 The second<BR>ploughing of a field. (शंबाकृ means<BR>‘to plough twice’).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20161106. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/alternateheadwords/issues/7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंव|शंवः
शंब(व)^1 a [शंब्-अच्]<BR>1 Happy,<BR>fortunate.<BR>--2 Poor, unfortunate.<BR>--बः<BR>1 The thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>--2 The iron head of a pestle.<BR>--3 An<BR>iron chain worn round the loins.<BR>--4 Ploughing ‘with the grain’ or in<BR>the regular direction.<BR>--5 The second<BR>ploughing of a field. (शंबाकृ means<BR>‘to plough twice’).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20161106. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/alternateheadwords/issues/7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंबर|शम्बर|शम्बरं|शम्बरः
शंबर a. [शंब्-अरच्] Best,<BR>excellent.<BR>--रः<BR>1 N. of a demon slain<BR>by Pradyumna, q v.<BR>--2 A<BR>mountain.<BR>--3 A kind of deer.<BR>--4 A Jina.<BR>--5 N. of the trees चित्रक, लोध्र, and<BR>अर्जुन.<BR>--6 A kind of fish.<BR>--7 War.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 A cloud.<BR>--3 Wealth.<BR>--4 A rite or religious observance<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः, सदनः epithets of<BR>Pradyumna or the god of love.<BR>--असुरः the demon Sambara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंबरी
शंबरी<BR>1 Illusion, jugglery.<BR>--2 A<BR>female juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंबलः|शम्बल|शंबल|शंबलं|शम्बलः
शंबलः --लं [शंब्-कलच्]<BR>1 A bank,<BR>shore.<BR>--2 Provisions for a journey,<BR>viaticum.<BR>--3 Envy, jealousy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंबलं|शम्बल|शंबल|शंबलः|शम्बलः
शंबलः --लं [शंब्-कलच्]<BR>1 A bank,<BR>shore.<BR>--2 Provisions for a journey,<BR>viaticum.<BR>--3 Envy, jealousy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंबली
शंबली A procuress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंबुः|शम्बु|शंबु|शम्बुः
शंबुः, शंबुकः, शंबुक्कः A bivalve<BR>shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंबुकः|शम्बुक|शंबुक|शम्बुकः
शंबुः, शंबुकः, शंबुक्कः A bivalve<BR>shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंबुक्कः|शम्बुक्क|शंबुक्क|शम्बुक्कः
शंबुः, शंबुकः, शंबुक्कः A bivalve<BR>shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंबूकः|शम्बूक|शंबूक|शम्बूकः
शंबूकः<BR>1 A bivalve shell<BR>(शंबूका also in this sense).<BR>--2 A small<BR>conch-shell.<BR>--3 A snail.<BR>--4 The<BR>edge of the frontal protuberance of<BR>an elephant.<BR>--5 N. of a Śūdra (who<BR>practised penance though forbidden<BR>to his caste and was in consequence<BR>slain by Rāma; see inter alia U. 2.<BR>and R. 15).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंभः|शम्भ|शंभ|शम्भः
शंभः<BR>1 A happy man.<BR>--2 The<BR>thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>--3 The<BR>ironhead of a pestle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंभली|शम्भली
शंभली A bawd, procuress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंभु|शम्भु|शंभुः|शम्भुः
शंभु a. [शं-भू-डु] Causing<BR>happiness, granting prosperity.<BR>--भुः<BR>1 N. of Śiva.<BR>--2 Brahman.<BR>--3 A<BR>sage, venerable man.<BR>--4 A kind of<BR>Siddha.<BR>--5 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तनयः, --नंदनः, --सुतः epithets of<BR>Kārtikeya or Gaṇesa.<BR>--प्रिया N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">Page1034-c+ 56</a>]<BR>of Durgā. {2} emblic myrobalan<BR>आमलकी<BR>--वल्लभं the white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शम्या
शम्या [शम्-यत् टाप्]<BR>1 A<BR>wooden stick or post.<BR>--2 A staff.<BR>--3 The<BR>pin of a yoke.<BR>--4 A kind of cymbal.<BR>--5 A sacrifical vessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय|शयः
शय a. (या, --यी f.) [शी-अच्]<BR>Lying down, sleeping (usually at<BR>the end of comp.); रात्रिजागरपरो<BR>दिवाशयः R. 19. 34; so उत्तानशय,<BR>पार्श्वशय, वृक्षेशय, बिलेशय &c.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>Sleep.<BR>--2 A bed, couch.<BR>--3 A<BR>hand.<BR>--4 A snake, especially the<BR>boa.<BR>--5 Abuse, imprecation, curse.<BR>--6 A stake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयंड|शयण्ड|शयण्डः
शयंड a. Sleepy, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयथ|शयथः
शयथ a. [शी-अथच्] Sleepy,<BR>asleep.<BR>--थः<BR>1 Death.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>snake, the boa-constrictor.<BR>--3 A<BR>boar.<BR>--4 A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनं|शयन
शयनं [शी-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Sleeping, sleep,<BR>lying down.<BR>--2 A bed, couch;<BR>शयनस्थो न भुंजीत Ms. 4. 74, R. 1. 95;<BR>V. 3. 10.<BR>--3 Copulation, sexual<BR>union.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अ (आ) गारः --रं,<BR>--गृहं a bed-chamber, sleeping<BR>apartments.<BR>--एकादशी the eleventh day<BR>of the bright half of Āṣāḍha when<BR>Viṣṇu lies down to enjoy his four<BR>months’ repose.<BR>--सखी a bed-fellow.<BR>--स्थानं a sleeping apartment,<BR>bedchamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयनीयं|शयनीय
शयनीयं [शी-आधरे अनीयर्] A bed,<BR>couch; परिशून्यं शयनीयमद्य मे R. 8. 66;<BR>कांतासखस्य शयनीयशिलातलं ते<BR>U. 3. 21; (शयनीयकं in the same sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयानकः|शयानक
शयानकः<BR>1 A chameleon.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of snake, the boa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयालु|शयालुः
शयालु a. [शी-आलुच्] Sleepy,<BR>slothful; हंति नोपशयस्थोपि<BR>शयालुर्मृगयुर्मृगान् Śi. 2. 80.<BR>--लुः<BR>1 A kind<BR>of snake, the boa-constrictor.<BR>--2<BR>A dog.<BR>--3 A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयित|शयितः
शयित p. p. [शी-कर्तरि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Sleeping, reposed, asleep.<BR>--2 Lying down.<BR>--तं Sleep, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयुः|शयु
शयुः, शयुनः A large snake, the<BR>boa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शयुनः|शयुन
शयुः, शयुनः A large snake, the<BR>boa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शय्या
शय्या [शी-आधारे क्यप्]<BR>1 A bed,<BR>couch; शय्या भूमितलं Śānti. 4. 9;<BR>मही रम्या शय्या Bh. 3. 79; R. 5. 66.<BR>--2 Sleeping.<BR>--3 Tying, stringing<BR>together.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्यक्षः, --पालः,<BR>the superintendent or guardian of<BR>a king's bed-chamber.<BR>--उत्संगः the<BR>side of a bed.<BR>--गत a. {1} lying in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-a" target="_blank">Page1035-a+ 56</a>]<BR>a bed. {2} confined to a bed.<BR>--गृहं<BR>a bed-chamber; R. 16. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1034-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरः|शर|शरं
शरः [शॄ-अच्]<BR>1 An arrow, a<BR>shaft; क्व च निशितनिपाता वज्रसाराः<BR>शरास्ते Ś. 1. 10.<BR>--2 A kind of white<BR>reed or grass; शरकांडपांडुगंडस्थला<BR>M. 3. 8; मुखंन सीता शरपाडुरेण<BR>R. 14. 26: Śi. 11. 30.<BR>--3 The cream of<BR>slightly curdled milk, cream<BR>--4 Hurt,<BR>injury, wound.<BR>--5 The number<BR>‘five.’<BR>--रं Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्र्यः<BR>an excellent arrow.<BR>--अब्यासः,<BR>--आघातः archery.<BR>--असनं, --आस्यं an<BR>arrow shooter, a bow; शरासनं नेषु<BR>विकृष्यतामिदं Ś. 6. 28; R. 3. 52;<BR>Ku. 3. 64.<BR>--अक्षेपः flight of arrows.<BR>--आरोपः, --आवापः a bow.<BR>--आश्रयः a<BR>quiver.<BR>--अहत a. struck by an arrow.<BR>--इषीका an arrow.<BR>--इष्टः the<BR>mango tree.<BR>--अओघः a shower or multi<BR>tude of arrows.<BR>--कांडः {1} a<BR>reedstalk. {2} a shaft of an arrow.<BR>--घातः shooting with arrows, archery.<BR>--जं fresh butter.<BR>--जः N. of<BR>Kārtikeya.<BR>--जन्मन् m. an epithet of<BR>Kārtikeya; R. 3. 23.<BR>--जालं a<BR>multitude or dense mass of arrows.<BR>--धिः a quiver.<BR>--पातः an arrow's<BR>flight. ˚स्थानं a bow-shot.<BR>--पुंखः,<BR>पुंखा the feathered end of an<BR>arrow.<BR>--प्रवेगः a swift arrow.<BR>--फलं the blade or barb of an<BR>arrow.<BR>--भंगः N. of a sage whom<BR>Rāma visited in the Daṇḍaka<BR>forest; R. 13. 45.<BR>--भूः N. of<BR>Kārtikeya.<BR>--भृष्टिः f. the point of<BR>an arrow.<BR>--मल्लः a bow-man, an<BR>archer.<BR>--वनं (वणं) a thicket of<BR>reeds; Me. 45. ˚उद्भवः, ˚भवः<BR>epithets of Kārtikeya.<BR>--वर्षः a shower<BR>or volley of arrows.<BR>--वाणिः {1} the<BR>head of an arrow. {2} an archer.<BR>{3} a maker of arrows. {4} a<BR>footsoldier.<BR>--वृष्टिः f. a shower of<BR>arrows.<BR>--व्रातः a mass or multitude<BR>of arrows.<BR>--संधानं taking aim with<BR>an arrow; शरसंधानं नाटयति Ś. 1.<BR>--सबाध a. covered with arrows:<BR>U. 4. 29.<BR>--स्तंचः a clump of reeds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरटः|शरट
शरटः [शॄ-अटन्]<BR>1 A chameleon.<BR>--2 A safflower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणं|शरण
शरणं [शॄ-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Protection,<BR>help, succour, defence; भूत्वा शरण्या<BR>शरणार्थमन्यं कथं प्रपत्त्ये त्वयि<BR>दीप्यमाने R. 14. 64, V. 1. 3; U. 4. 23.<BR>--2 Refuge, shelter; Ku. 3. 8;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-b" target="_blank">Page1035-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Pt. 2.<BR>--3 A place of refuge, resort,<BR>asylum (applied to persons also);<BR>स सुरासुरस्य जगतः शरणं Ki. 18. 22;<BR>संतप्तानां त्वमसि शरणं Me. 7; शरणं<BR>गमइ-या &c. ‘to go to for protection,<BR>take shelter with, to submit to’;<BR>यामि ह कमिह शरणं Gīt. 7.<BR>--4 A<BR>sanctuary, closet, an apartment;<BR>अग्निशरणमार्गमादंशय Ś. 5.<BR>--5 An<BR>abode, a house, habitation;<BR>Mu. 3. 15; Bk. 6. 9.<BR>--6 Lair,<BR>restingplace.<BR>--7 Injuring, killing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्यिन् a.<BR>--एषिन् a. {1} seeking<BR>refuge or protection; Bh. 2. 76. {2}<BR>unfortunate.<BR>--आगत, --आपन्न a.<BR>gone to for refuge or protection,<BR>taking shelter with, fugitive.<BR>--उन्तुख<BR>a. looking up to for protection;<BR>R. 6. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्य|शरण्यः
शरण्य a. [शरणे साधुः यत्]<BR>1<BR>Fit to protect, yielding<BR>protection, a protector, refuge;<BR>असौ शरण्यः शरणोन्मुखानां R. 6. 21;<BR>शरण्यो लोकानां Mv. 4. 1;<BR>R. 2. 30; 14. 64, 15. 2; Ku. 5. 76.<BR>--2<BR>Needing protection, poor,<BR>miserable.<BR>--ण्यः An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--ण्यं<BR>1 A place of refuge, shelter.<BR>--2 A<BR>protector, who or what affords<BR>protection; U. 1. 50 v. l.<BR>--3 Protection,<BR>defence.<BR>--4 Injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरणी
शरणी (णिः f.)<BR>1 A road, path.<BR>--2 The earth.<BR>--3 A row, line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरण्युः|शरण्यु
शरण्युः<BR>1 A protector.<BR>--2 A<BR>cloud.<BR>--3 Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरंडः|शरण्ड|शरंड|शरण्डः
शरंडः<BR>1 A bird.<BR>--2 A<BR>chameleon.<BR>--3 A cheat, rogue.<BR>--4 A lecher,<BR>libertine.<BR>--5 A kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरद्
शरद् f. [शॄ-अदि Uṇ. 1. 129]<BR>1<BR>The autumn, autumnal season<BR>(comprising the two months आश्विन<BR>and कार्तिक); यात्रायै चोदयामास तं<BR>शक्तेः प्रथमं शरद् R. 4. 24.<BR>--2 A year;<BR>त्वं जीव शरदः शतं; R. 10. 1;<BR>U. 1. 15; धारिणीभूतधारिण्यार्भव भर्ता शरच्छतं<BR>M. 1. 15.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः the end<BR>of autumn, winter.<BR>--अंबुधरः an<BR>autumnal cloud.<BR>--उदाशयः an<BR>autumnal lake.<BR>--कामिन् m. a dog.<BR>--कालः the autumnal season.<BR>--घनः,<BR>--मेघः an autumnal cloud.<BR>--चंद्रः<BR>(शरच्चंद्रः) the autumnal moon<BR>--त्रियामा an autumnal night<BR>--पद्मः,<BR>--द्मं the white lotus.<BR>--पर्वन् n. the<BR>festival called Kojāgara; q. v.<BR>--मुखं the commencement of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">Page1035-c+ 56</a>]<BR>autumn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरदा
शरदा<BR>1 Autumn.<BR>--2 A year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरदिज|शरदिजं
शरदिज a. Autumnal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरभः|शरभ
शरभः [शॄ-अभच् Uṇ. 3. 122]<BR>1<BR>A young elephant.<BR>--2 A fabulous<BR>animal said to have {8} legs and to<BR>be stronger than a lion;<BR>शरभकुलमजिह्मं प्रोद्धरत्यंबु कूपात् Rs. 1. 23;<BR>अष्टपादः शरभः सिंहघाती Mb.<BR>--3 A<BR>camel.<BR>--4 A grass-hopper.<BR>--5 A<BR>locust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरयुः|शरयु
शरयुः(यूः) f. N. of a river;<BR>see सरयु (यू)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरयूः
शरयुः(यूः) f. N. of a river;<BR>see सरयु (यू)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरल|शरलः
शरल a.<BR>1 See सरल.<BR>--2 Crooked;<BR>fraudulent (according to Śabdak.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरलकं|शरलक
शरलकं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरव्यं|शरव्य
शरव्यं [शरवे शरशिक्षायै हितं शरु-यत्]<BR>A butt or mark (for arrows), target<BR>(fig. also); तौ शरव्यमकरोत्स नेतरान्<BR>R. 11. 27; कृताः शरव्यं हरिणा<BR>तवासुराः Ś. 6. 28; R. 7. 45; Śi. 7. 24;<BR>व्यसनशतशरव्यतां गताः K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शराटिः|शराटि
शराटिः<BR>--(डिः तिः --रिः --लिः) A<BR>kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरारु|शरारुः
शरारु a. Noxious, hurtful,<BR>injurious.<BR>--रुः A mischievous animal;<BR>शरारुचकचारभीषणायां महाटव्यां Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरावः|शराव|शरावं
शरावः --वं [शरं दध्यादिसारमवति<BR>अव-अण् Tv.]<BR>1 A shallow dish, platter,<BR>an earthenware vessel, tray;<BR>मोदकशरावं ग्टहीत्वा V. 3; Ms. 6. 56.<BR>--2<BR>A cover, lid.<BR>--3 A measure equal to<BR>{2} Kuḍavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरावं|शराव|शरावः
शरावः --वं [शरं दध्यादिसारमवति<BR>अव-अण् Tv.]<BR>1 A shallow dish, platter,<BR>an earthenware vessel, tray;<BR>मोदकशरावं ग्टहीत्वा V. 3; Ms. 6. 56.<BR>--2<BR>A cover, lid.<BR>--3 A measure equal to<BR>{2} Kuḍavas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरावती
शरावती N. of a town of which<BR>Lava was made ruler by Rāma;<BR>R. 15. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरिमन्
शरिमन् m. Bearing, bringing<BR>forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरं|शरीर
शरीरं [शॄ-ईरन्]<BR>1 The-body (of<BR>animate or inanimate objects);<BR>शरोरमाद्यं खलु धर्मसाधनं Ku. 5. 33.<BR>--2 The constituent element; शरीरं<BR>तावदिष्टार्थव्यवच्छिन्ना पदावली<BR>Kāv. 1. 10; शरीरमसि संसारस्य U. 7.<BR>--3<BR>Bodily strength.<BR>--4 A dead body.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरं {1} the interior<BR>of the body. {2} another body.<BR>--आवरणं the skin.<BR>--कर्तृ m.<BR>a father.<BR>--कर्षणं emaciation of<BR>the body.<BR>--जः {1} sickness. {2}<BR>lust, passion. {3} the god of love.<BR>{4} a son, offspring; Ki. 4. 31.<BR>--तुल्य a. equal to, i. e. as dear as,<BR>one's own person.<BR>--दंडः {1} corporal<BR>punishment. {2} mortification of<BR>the body (as in penance).<BR>--धृक्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1036-a" target="_blank">Page1036-a+ 56</a>]<BR>a. having a body.<BR>--पतनं, --पातः<BR>shuffling off the mortal coil', death.<BR>--पाकः emaciation (of the body).<BR>--बद्ध a. endowed with a body,<BR>embodied, incarnate; शरीरबद्धः<BR>प्रथमाश्रमो यथा Ku. 5. 30.<BR>--बंधः {1} the<BR>bodily frame; शरीरबधेन तिरोबभूव<BR>R. 16. 23. {2} being endowed with a<BR>body; i. e. birth as an embodied<BR>being; R. 13. 58.<BR>--बधंकः a<BR>hostage.<BR>--भाज् a. embodied, incarnate.<BR>(--m.) a creature, an embodied<BR>being.<BR>--भेदः separation of the body<BR>(from the soul), death.<BR>--यष्टिः f.<BR>a slender body, slim or delicate<BR>figure.<BR>--यात्रा means of bodily<BR>sustenance.<BR>--विमोक्षणं the<BR>emancipation of the soul from the body.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. maintenance or support<BR>of the body; R. 2. 45.<BR>--वैकल्यं<BR>bodily ailment, sickness, disease.<BR>--शुश्रूषा personal attendance.<BR>--संस्कारः {1} decoration of the person.<BR>{2} purification of the body by the<BR>performance of the several<BR>purificatory Saṃskāras.<BR>--संपत्तिः f. the<BR>prosperity of body, (good) health.<BR>--संबंधः relation by marriage.<BR>--सादः<BR>leanness of body, emaciation;<BR>R. 3. 2.<BR>--स्थितिः f. {1} the maintenance<BR>or support of the body; R. 5. 9.<BR>{2} taking one's meals, eating<BR>(frequently used in Kādambarī).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1035-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरकं|शरीरक|शरीरकः
शरीरकं<BR>1 The body.<BR>--2 A small<BR>body.<BR>--कः The soul.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरीरिन्
शरीरिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>1 Embodied,<BR>corporeal, incarnate; करुणस्य<BR>मूर्तिरथवा शरीरिणी बिरहव्यथैव वनमेति<BR>जानकी U. 3. 4; भावाविव शरीरिणौ M. 1. 10.<BR>--2 Living. --m.<BR>1 Anything endowed<BR>with a body (whether animate or<BR>inanimate); शरीरिणां स्थावरजंगमानां<BR>सुखाय तज्जन्मदिनं बभूव Ku. 1. 23;<BR>मरणं प्रकृतिः शरीरिणां R. 8. 87, 43.<BR>--2 A sentient being.<BR>--3 A man.<BR>--4<BR>The soul (clad with the body);<BR>R. 8. 89; Bg. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शरुः|शरु
शरुः<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>--2 A weapon.<BR>--3<BR>The thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>--4 Anger,<BR>passion.<BR>--5 Practice of archery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करा
शर्करा [शॄ-करन् कस्य नेत्वम्<BR>Uṇ. 4. 3]<BR>1 Candied sugar.<BR>--2 A<BR>pebble, gravel, small stone;<BR>पादुकांतरप्रविष्टिव शर्करा Mk. 5.<BR>--3 Gravelly<BR>mould.<BR>--4 Soil abounding in stony<BR>fragments, sand.<BR>--5 A piece,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1036-b" target="_blank">Page1036-b+ 54</a>]<BR>fragment.<BR>--6 A potsherd.<BR>--7 Any hard<BR>particle, as in जलशर्करा a nodule of<BR>water, i. e. hail.<BR>--8 The disease<BR>called gravel.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदक<BR>sugar-water, water sweetened with<BR>sugar.<BR>--सप्तमी N. of an observance<BR>on the 7th day in the bright half of<BR>VaiŚākha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1036-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करकः|शर्करक
शर्करकः A kind of citron or lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करजा
शर्करजा Candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1036-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शर्करिक|शर्करिकः
