शलालुः|शलालु
शलालुः A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्कं|शल्क
शल्कं, शल्कलं [शल्-क कस्य नेत्वम्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 43]<BR>1 The scale of a fish;<BR>Ms. 5. 16; Y. 1. 178.<BR>--2 Bark, rind.<BR>(of trees).<BR>--3 A part, portion,<BR>fragment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्कलं|शल्कल
शल्कं, शल्कलं [शल्-क कस्य नेत्वम्<BR>Uṇ. 3. 43]<BR>1 The scale of a fish;<BR>Ms. 5. 16; Y. 1. 178.<BR>--2 Bark, rind.<BR>(of trees).<BR>--3 A part, portion,<BR>fragment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्कलिन्
शल्कलिन्, शल्किन् m. A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्किन्
शल्कलिन्, शल्किन् m. A fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्भ्
शल्भ् {c1c} A. (शल्भते) To praise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्मलिः|शल्मलि
शल्मलिः --ली f. The silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्मली
शल्मलिः --ली f. The silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यं|शल्य|शल्यः
शल्यं [शल्-यत्]<BR>1 A spear, javelin,<BR>dart.<BR>--2 An arrow, a shaft; शल्यं<BR>निखातमुदहारयतामुरस्तः R. 9. 78; शल्यप्रोतं<BR>9. 75; अवगच्छति मूढचेतनः प्रियनाशं<BR>हृदि शल्यमर्पितं R. 8. 88, Ś. 6. 8,<BR>V. 2. 10.<BR>--3 A thorn, splinter.<BR>--4 A<BR>pin, peg, stake (said to be m. also<BR>in these four senses).<BR>--5 Any<BR>extraneous substance lodged in the<BR>body and giving it very great pain;<BR>अलातशल्यं U. 3. 35; अपनीताशेषशल्यः<BR>Dk.<BR>--6 (Fig) Any cause of<BR>poignant or heart-rending grief;<BR>उद्धृतविषादशल्यः कथयिष्यामि Ś. 7.<BR>--7 A<BR>bone.<BR>--8 Difficulty, distress.<BR>--9 Sin,<BR>crime<BR>--10 Poison.<BR>--11 Abuse,<BR>defamation.<BR>--ल्यः<BR>1 A porcupine,<BR>hedge-hog.<BR>--2 The thorny shrub.<BR>--3<BR>Extraction of splinters.<BR>--4 A fence,<BR>boundary.<BR>--5 The Bilva and<BR>Madana trees.<BR>--6 A kind of fish.<BR>--7 N.<BR>of a king of Madra and brother of<BR>Mādrī, the second wife of Pāṇḍu,<BR>and thus maternal uncle of Nakula<BR>and Sahadeva. [In the great war<BR>he at first intended to fight on the side<BR>of the Pāṇḍavas, but he was artfully<BR>won over by Duryodhana and<BR>subsequently fought in his behalf. He<BR>acted as charioteer to Karṇa when he was<BR>generalissimo of the Kaurava forces,<BR>and after his death was appointed<BR>commander. He maintained the field for<BR>one day, but was at last slain by<BR>Yudhiṣṭhira].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः an<BR>epithet of Yudhiṣṭhira.<BR>--आहरणं,<BR>--उद्धरणं, --उद्धारः, --क्रिया, --शास्त्रं<BR>extraction of thorns or splinters, or that<BR>part of surgery which relates to the<BR>extraction of extraneous matter<BR>from the body.<BR>--कंठः a porcupine.<BR>--लोमन् n. the quill of a porcupine.<BR>--हर्तृ m. a weeder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यकः|शल्यक
शल्यकः<BR>1 A dart, javelin, spike.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">Page1037-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--2 A splinter, thorn.<BR>--3 A<BR>porcupine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्यित
शल्यित a. Pierced(as with a<BR>dart); निष्कारणपरित्यागशल्यित U. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्ल्
शल्ल् {c1c} P. (शल्लति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्लः|शल्ल|शल्लं
शल्लः [शल्ल्-अच्] A frog.<BR>--ल्लं<BR>Bark, rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्लकः|शल्लक|शल्लकं
शल्लकः N. of a tree.<BR>--कं Bark,<BR>rind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्लकी
शल्लकी<BR>1 A porcupine.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of tree (of which elephants are<BR>very fond); अभिलेढु<BR>तावदासवसुरभिरसं शल्लकीभंगं V. 4. 23; U. 2. 21;<BR>3. 6; Māl. 9. 6.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द्रवः<BR>incense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शल्वः|शल्व
शल्वः N. of a country; see शाल्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शव्
शव् {c1c} P. (शवति)<BR>1 To go,<BR>approach.<BR>--2 To alter, change,<BR>transform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवः|शव|शवं
शवः --वं [शव्-अच्] A corpse, dead<BR>body; Ms. 10. 55.<BR>--वं Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आच्छादनं covering of a<BR>corpse, shroud.<BR>--आश a feeding<BR>on corpses; Bk. 12. 75.<BR>--काम्यः a<BR>dog.<BR>--दाहः cremation (of dead<BR>bodies).<BR>--यानं, --रथः a hearse, bier,<BR>a sort of litter for carrying a corpse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवं|शव|शवः
शवः --वं [शव्-अच्] A corpse, dead<BR>body; Ms. 10. 55.<BR>--वं Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आच्छादनं covering of a<BR>corpse, shroud.<BR>--आश a feeding<BR>on corpses; Bk. 12. 75.<BR>--काम्यः a<BR>dog.<BR>--दाहः cremation (of dead<BR>bodies).<BR>--यानं, --रथः a hearse, bier,<BR>a sort of litter for carrying a corpse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवर|शवरः
शवर See शबर, शबल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवल|शवलः
शवल See शबर, शबल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शवसानः|शवसान
शवसानः<BR>1 A traveller.<BR>--2 A<BR>way, road.<BR>--नं A cemetery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्
शश् {c1c} P. (शशति) To leap,<BR>bound, jump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशः|शश
शशः<BR>1 A hare, rabbit;<BR>Ms. 3. 270, 5. 18.<BR>--2 The spots on the<BR>moon (which are popularly<BR>considered to resemble the form of a<BR>hare).<BR>--3 One of the four classes<BR>into which men are divided by<BR>erotic writers; thus defined:<BR>--मृदुवचनसुशीलः कोमलांगः सुकेशः<BR>सकलगुणनिधानं सत्यवादी शशोऽयं Śabdak.; see<BR>Ratimañjarī 35 also.<BR>--4 The<BR>Lodhra tree.<BR>--5 Gum-myrrh.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः {1} the moon. {2} camphor.<BR>˚अर्धमुख a. crescent-headed (as an<BR>arrow). ˚मूर्तिः an epithet of the moon.<BR>˚लेखा the digit of the moon, lunar<BR>crescent.<BR>--अदः {1} a hawk, falcon.<BR>{2} N. of a son of Ikṣvāku, father<BR>of पुरंजय.<BR>--अदनः a hawk, falcon.<BR>--ऊर्णं, --लोमन् n. the hair of a rabbit,<BR>hair-skin.<BR>--धरः {1} the moon;<BR>प्रसरति शशधरविंबे Gīt. 7. {2} camphor.<BR>˚मौलिः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--प्लुतकं<BR>a scratch with a fingernail.<BR>--भृत् m.<BR>the moon. ˚भृत् m. an epithet of Śiva<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">Page1037-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--लक्ष्मणः an epithet of the moon.<BR>--लंछनः {1} the moon;<BR>Ku. 7. 6. {2} camphor.<BR>--विं(विं)दुः<BR>{1} the moon. {2} an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--विषाणं, --शृंगं a hair's horn;<BR>used to denote anything impossible,<BR>an utter impossibility; कदाचिदपि<BR>पर्यटञ् शशविषाणमासादयेत् Bh. 2. 5;<BR>शशशृंगधनुर्धरः; see खपुष्प.<BR>--स्थली the<BR>country between the Ganges and<BR>Yamunā, the Doab.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशकः|शशक
शशकः<BR>1 A hare, rabbit.<BR>--2 = शश<BR>(3) q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिन्
शशिन् m. [शशोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>1<BR>The moon; शशिनं पुनरेति शर्वरी<BR>R. 8. 56, 6. 85; Me. 41.<BR>--2 Camphor,<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--कला a digit of the moon;<BR>Mu. 1. 1.<BR>--कांतः the moon-gem.<BR>--(तं) a<BR>lotus.<BR>--कोटिः a horn of the moon.<BR>--ग्रहः an eclipse of the moon.<BR>--जः<BR>an epithet of Budha or Mercury<BR>(son of the moon).<BR>--प्रभ a. having<BR>the lustre of the moon, as bright<BR>and white as the moon; R. 3. 16.<BR>--भं {1} a water-lily. {2} a pearl.<BR>--प्रभा moonlight.<BR>--भूषणः, --भृत् m.,<BR>--मौलिः, --शेखरः epithets of Śiva.<BR>--लेखा a digit of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शशिनी
शशिनी N. of one of the sixteen<BR>digits of the moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शश्वत्|शश्वन्त्
शश्वत् ind.<BR>1 Perpetually,<BR>eternally, for ever.<BR>--2 Constantly,<BR>repeatedly, always, frequently, again<BR>and again; R. 2. 48, 4. 70;<BR>Me. 55. (In comp. शश्वत् may be<BR>translated by ‘lasting, eternal’; as<BR>शश्वच्छांति eternal tranquillity.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्
शष् {c1c} P. (शषति) To hurt,<BR>injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्कुली
शष्कु(स्कु)ली<BR>1 The orifice<BR>of the ear, auditory passage;<BR>तथापि कर्णशष्कुल्ववच्छिन्नः सन् (आकाशः)<BR>शब्दग्राहकश्रोत्रेंद्रियात्मकः Tarka K.;<BR>अवलींबतकर्णशष्कुलीकलसीकं<BR>रचयन्नवोचत N. 2. 8; Y. 3. 96.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of baked cake; Y. 1. 173.<BR>--3<BR>Ricegruel.<BR>--4 A disease of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्कुली
शष्कु(स्कु)ली<BR>1 The orifice<BR>of the ear, auditory passage;<BR>तथापि कर्णशष्कुल्ववच्छिन्नः सन् (आकाशः)<BR>शब्दग्राहकश्रोत्रेंद्रियात्मकः Tarka K.;<BR>अवलींबतकर्णशष्कुलीकलसीकं<BR>रचयन्नवोचत N. 2. 8; Y. 3. 96.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of baked cake; Y. 1. 173.<BR>--3<BR>Ricegruel.<BR>--4 A disease of the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शष्पः|शष्प|शष्पं
शष्पः(स्पः) Loss of intellect or<BR>presence of mind (प्रतिभाक्षय).<BR>--ष्पं<BR>Young grass; U. 4. 27; R. 2. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्पः|शस्प|शस्पं
शष्पः(स्पः) Loss of intellect or<BR>presence of mind (प्रतिभाक्षय).<BR>--ष्पं<BR>Young grass; U. 4. 27; R. 2. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (शसति) To cut up, kill,<BR>destroy. {vII.v} {c2c} P. (शस्ति) To sleep.<BR>Cf. शंस् also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शसनं|शसन
शसनं [शस्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Wounding,<BR>killing.<BR>--2 Immolation (of an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-a" target="_blank">Page1038-a+ 56</a>]<BR>animal at sacrifice).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1037-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त|शस्तं|शस्तः
शस्त p. p. [शंस्-क्त]<BR>1 Praised,<BR>extolled.<BR>--2 Auspicious, happy.<BR>--3 Right,<BR>best.<BR>--4 Repeated. recited<BR>--5 Best,<BR>excellent.<BR>--6 Wounded, injured.<BR>--7<BR>Killed.<BR>--स्तं<BR>1 Happiness, welfare.<BR>--2 Excellence, auspiciousness.<BR>--3<BR>The body.<BR>--4 A finger-guard<BR>(अंगुलित्राण q. v.; also शस्तकं in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्तिः|शस्ति
शस्तिः f.<BR>1 Praise, eulogy.<BR>--2 A<BR>hymn of praise (स्तोत्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्
शस्<BR>1 A technical name for the<BR>termination of the acc. plural.<BR>--2 A<BR>Taddhita affix forming adverbs from<BR>nouns, especially from numerals; as<BR>द्विशः, शतशः, बहुशः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रं|शस्त्र|शस्त्रः
शस्त्रं [शस्-ष्ट्र्न्]<BR>1 A weapon, arms;<BR>क्षमाशस्त्रं करे यस्य दुर्जनः किं करिष्यति<BR>Subhāṣ., R. 2. 40, 3. 51, 62; 5. 28.<BR>--2<BR>An instrument, a tool in general.<BR>--3<BR>Iron.<BR>--4 Steel.<BR>--5 A hymn of praise<BR>(स्तोत्र).<BR>--6 Repetition, recitation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अब्यासः the practice of<BR>arms. military exercise.<BR>--अयसं {1}<BR>steel. {2} iron.<BR>--अस्त्रं {1} weapons for<BR>striking and throwing, arms and<BR>missiles. {2} arms or weapons<BR>generally.<BR>--आजीवः, --उपजीविन् m. a<BR>professional soldier.<BR>--उद्यमः lifting up<BR>a weapon (to strike).<BR>--उपकरणं<BR>arms or instruments of war,<BR>military apparatus.<BR>--कारः an armourer.<BR>--कोषः the sheath or scabbard of<BR>any weapon.<BR>--ग्राहिन् a. taking up<BR>or wearing arms (for battle);<BR>शस्त्रग्राही ब्राह्नणो जामदग्नयः U. 5. 33.<BR>--जीविन्, --वृत्ति m. one living by the<BR>use of arms, a professional soldier.<BR>--देवता the deity presiding over<BR>weapons.<BR>--धरः = शस्त्रभृत् q. v.<BR>--न्यासः<BR>laying down arms; so शस्त्र (परि)<BR>त्यागः.<BR>--पणि a. bearing arms, arm.<BR>ed. (--m.) an armed warrior.<BR>--पूत<BR>a. ‘purified by arms’, rendered<BR>pure or absolved from guilt by<BR>being killed with a weapon on the<BR>battle-field; अशस्त्रपूतं निर्व्याजं (<BR>महामांसं) Māl. 5. 12; (see Jagaddhara's<BR>explanation of the word); अहमपि<BR>तस्य मिथ्याप्रतिज्ञौवलक्ष्यसंपादितमशस्त्रपूतं<BR>मरणमुपदिशामि Ve. 2.<BR>--प्रहारः a<BR>wound inflicted with a weapon.<BR>--भृत् m. {1} a soldier, warrior;<BR>R. 2. 40. {2} an armed man.<BR>--मार्जः<BR>a weapon-cleaner, an armourer, a<BR>furbisher.<BR>--विद्या, --शास्त्रं the science of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">Page1038-b+ 57</a>]<BR>arms.<BR>--संहतिः f. {1} a collection of<BR>arms. {2} an arsenal.<BR>--संपातः a<BR>sudden fall of a number of weapons.<BR>--हत a. killed by a weapon.<BR>--हस्त<BR>a. armed.<BR>--(स्तः) an armed man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रकं|शस्त्रक
शस्त्रकं<BR>1 Steel.<BR>--2 Iron.<BR>--3 An<BR>instrument, a tool, weapon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिका
शस्त्रिका A knife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्रिन्
शस्त्रिन् a. Bearing arms or<BR>weapons, armed, accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्त्री
शस्त्री A knife; पण्यस्त्रीषु<BR>विवेककल्पलतिकाशस्त्रीषु रज्यत कः Subhāṣ.;<BR>Śi. 4. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्य|शस्यं
शस्य a. (from शंस्)<BR>1 Best,<BR>excellent.<BR>--2 Praiseworthy, laudable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शस्यं|शस्य
शस्यं [शस्-यत्]<BR>1 Corn or grain<BR>in general; दुदोह गां स यज्ञाय<BR>शस्याय मघवा दिवं R. 1. 26.<BR>--2 The<BR>produce or fruit of a plant or tree;<BR>शस्यं क्षेत्रगतं प्राहुः सतुषं धान्यमुच्यते;<BR>see तंडुल also.<BR>--3 A merit.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्षेत्रं a corn-field.<BR>--भक्षक a.<BR>granivorous.<BR>--मंजरी {1} an ear of<BR>corn. {2} a fruit-stalk.<BR>--मालिन् a.<BR>crowned with harvests.<BR>--शालिन्,<BR>--संपन्न a. abounding in corn.<BR>--शूकं<BR>a beard of corn.<BR>--संपद् f.<BR>abundance of corn.<BR>--संब (व) रः the<BR>Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकः|शाक|शाकं
शाकः --कं [शक्-घञ्]<BR>1 A vegetable,<BR>potherb, herb, any edible leaf, fruit<BR>or root used as a vegetable; दिल्लीश्वरो<BR>वा जगदीश्वरो वा मनोरथान् पूरयितुं समर्थः ।<BR>अन्यैर्नृपालैः परिदीयमानं शाकाय वा<BR>स्याल्लवणाय वा स्यात् Jag.<BR>--कः {1}<BR>Power, strength, energy.<BR>--2 The<BR>teak tree.<BR>--3 The Śirīṣa tree.<BR>--4<BR>N. of a people; see शक.<BR>--5 An era;<BR>especially the era of Sālivāhana.<BR>--6<BR>N. of the sixth Dvīpa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं<BR>pepper.<BR>--अम्लं hog-plum. ˚भेदनं sorrel.<BR>--आखयः the teak tree.<BR>--(खयं) a<BR>vegetable.<BR>--आहारः a vegetarian<BR>(living only on herbs &c.)<BR>--चुक्रिका the tamarind.<BR>--तरुः the teak<BR>tree.<BR>--पणः {1} a measure equal to a<BR>handful. {2} a handful of<BR>vegetables.<BR>--पत्रः the Śigru tree.<BR>--पार्थिवः<BR>a king fond of an era; see<BR>मध्यमपदलोपिन्.<BR>--प्रति ind. a little of herbs.<BR>--योग्यः coriander.<BR>--वृक्षः the teak<BR>tree.<BR>--शाकटं, शाकितं a field of<BR>vegetables, a kitchen-garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकं|शाक|शाकः
शाकः --कं [शक्-घञ्]<BR>1 A vegetable,<BR>potherb, herb, any edible leaf, fruit<BR>or root used as a vegetable; दिल्लीश्वरो<BR>वा जगदीश्वरो वा मनोरथान् पूरयितुं समर्थः ।<BR>अन्यैर्नृपालैः परिदीयमानं शाकाय वा<BR>स्याल्लवणाय वा स्यात् Jag.<BR>--कः {1}<BR>Power, strength, energy.<BR>--2 The<BR>teak tree.<BR>--3 The Śirīṣa tree.<BR>--4<BR>N. of a people; see शक.<BR>--5 An era;<BR>especially the era of Sālivāhana.<BR>--6<BR>N. of the sixth Dvīpa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं<BR>pepper.<BR>--अम्लं hog-plum. ˚भेदनं sorrel.<BR>--आखयः the teak tree.<BR>--(खयं) a<BR>vegetable.<BR>--आहारः a vegetarian<BR>(living only on herbs &c.)<BR>--चुक्रिका the tamarind.<BR>--तरुः the teak<BR>tree.<BR>--पणः {1} a measure equal to a<BR>handful. {2} a handful of<BR>vegetables.<BR>--पत्रः the Śigru tree.<BR>--पार्थिवः<BR>a king fond of an era; see<BR>मध्यमपदलोपिन्.<BR>--प्रति ind. a little of herbs.<BR>--योग्यः coriander.<BR>--वृक्षः the teak<BR>tree.<BR>--शाकटं, शाकितं a field of<BR>vegetables, a kitchen-garden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकट|शाकटं|शाकटः
शाकट a. (टी f.) [शकटाय हितं<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Relating to a cart.<BR>--2<BR>Going in a cart.<BR>--टः<BR>1 A draught-ox.<BR>--2 The tree called श्लेष्मातक.<BR>--टं A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-c" target="_blank">Page1038-c+ 55</a>]<BR>field; cf. शाकशाकट.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटायनः|शाकटायन
शाकटायनः N. of a philologist<BR>and grammarian often referred to<BR>by Pāṇini and Yāska; cf. व्याकरणे<BR>शकटस्य च तोकं Nir.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1038-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाकटिक|शाकटिकः
