शाठ्यं|शाठ्य
शाठ्यं [शठस्य भावः ष्यञ्] (a)<BR>Dishonesty, perfidy, guile, trickery,<BR>fraud, villainy; आजन्मनः<BR>शाठ्यमशिक्षितो यः Ś. 5. 25; (b) Art, skill,<BR>cunning; देव्या निह्नोतुमिच्छोरिति<BR>सुरसरितं शाठ्यमव्याद्विभोर्वः Mu. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाण|शाणं|शाणः
शाण a. (णी f.) [शणेन निर्वृत्तं अण्]<BR>Hempen, flaxen.<BR>--णः<BR>1 A<BR>touchstone; मणिः शाणो ल्लीढः Bh. 2. 44;<BR>Bv. 1. 73.<BR>--2 A whetstone.<BR>--3 A<BR>saw.<BR>--4 A weight of four Māṣas.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Sack-cloth, coarse cloth.<BR>--2 A<BR>hempen garment; Ms. 2. 41,<BR>10. 87.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आजीवः an armourer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणिः|शाणि
शाणिः A plant from the fibres of<BR>which a coarse cloth is prepared.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणित|शाणितः
शाणित p. p. Whetted, ground,<BR>sharpened (on a whetstone).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणी
शाणी<BR>1 A touchstone.<BR>--2 A<BR>whetstone.<BR>--3 A saw.<BR>--4 A hempen<BR>garment.<BR>--5 A ragged garment.<BR>--6 A<BR>small screen or tent.<BR>--7 Gesticulation,<BR>a sign made with the hands or eyes.<BR>--8 A weight of four Māṣas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाणीरं|शाणीर
शाणीरं A bank or spot of ground<BR>in the Śoṇa river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांडिल्यः|शाण्डिल्य|शांडिल्य|शाण्डिल्यः
शांडिल्यः<BR>1 N. of a sage, the<BR>author of a law-book.<BR>--2 The Bilva<BR>tree.<BR>--3 A form of Agni.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गोत्रं the family of Śāṇḍilya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात|शातं|शातः
शात p. p. शे-क्त<BR>1<BR>Sharpened, whetted.<BR>--2 Thin, slender.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">Page1039-c+ 54</a>]<BR>Weak, feeble.<BR>--4 Beautiful,<BR>handsome.<BR>--5 Cut down.<BR>--6 Happy,<BR>thriving.<BR>--तः The Dhattūra plant.<BR>--तं Happiness, pleasure, delight;<BR>मानिनीजनजनितशातं Gīt. 10.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदरी a woman with; a slender<BR>waist; Śi. 5. 23; R. 10. 69.<BR>--शिख<BR>a. sharp-pointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकुंभं|शातकुम्भ|शातकुंभ|शातकुम्भं|शातकुम्भः
शातकुंभं<BR>1 Gold; Śi. 9. 9;<BR>N. 16. 34.<BR>--2 The thorn-apple (धत्तूर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातकौंभं|शातकौम्भ|शातकौंभ|शातकौम्भं
शातकौंभं Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातनं|शातन
शातनं<BR>1 Whetting, sharpening.<BR>--2 Cutting down, destroyer; as in<BR>पर्वतपक्षशातनं R. 3. 42.<BR>--3<BR>Causing to fall or perish.<BR>--4 Causing<BR>to decay or wither.<BR>--5 Becoming<BR>thin or small, thinness.<BR>--6<BR>Withering, decaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातपत्रकः|शातपत्रक
शातपत्रकः --की Moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातपत्रकी
शातपत्रकः --की Moonlight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातभीरुः|शातभीरु
शातभीरुः A kind of Mallikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शातमान|शातमानं
शातमान a. (नी f.) Bought for<BR>one hundred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रव|शात्रवं|शात्रवः
शात्रव a. (वी f.) [शत्रुरेव शत्रोरिदं<BR>वा अण्]<BR>1 Relating to an enemy;<BR>R. 4. 42.<BR>--2 Hostile, inimical.<BR>--वः<BR>An enemy; तत्र नाभवदसौ महाहवे<BR>शात्रवादिव पराङ्मुखोऽर्थिनः Śi. 14. 44,<BR>18. 20; Ve. 5. 1; Bk. 5. 81;<BR>Ki. 14. 2; Mu. 2. 5.<BR>--वं<BR>1 A<BR>collection of enemies.<BR>--2 Enmity,<BR>hostility; त्रयीशात्रवशत्रवे R. G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शात्रवीय
शात्रवीय a.<BR>1 Relating to an<BR>enemy.<BR>--2 Hostile, inimical,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शादः|शाद
शादः [शद्-घञ्]<BR>1 Young grass.<BR>--2 Mud.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हरितः -तं a<BR>place green with young grass, a<BR>place clad in verdure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाद्वल|शाद्वलः
शाद्वल a. [शादाः संत्यत्र वलच्]<BR>1<BR>Grassy.<BR>--2 Abounding in young<BR>green grass.<BR>--3 Green, verdant.<BR>--लः<BR>--लं A grass-plot, green, meadow;<BR>शय्या शाद्वलं Śānti. 2. 21; R. 2. 17;<BR>Ki. 5. 37, Y. 3. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शान्
शान् {c1c} U. (शीशांसति-ते, strictly<BR>a desiderative of शान् used in a<BR>primitive sense) To sharpen, whet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानः|शान
शानः<BR>1 A touch-stone.<BR>--2 A<BR>whet-stone.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पादः {1} a<BR>stone for grinding sandal. {2}<BR>the Pāriyātra mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानच्
शानच् (In gram.) A technical<BR>term used by Pāṇini for the Kṛt<BR>affix आन or मान् used in forming<BR>present participles of the Atm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1039-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शानैश्चर
शानैश्चर a. (री f.)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>Saturn.<BR>--2 Falling on a Saturday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांत|शान्त|शान्तं|शान्तः
शांत p. p. [शम्-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Appeased, allayed, calmed, satisfied,<BR>pacified; R. 12, 20.<BR>--2 Cured,<BR>alleviated; शांतरोगः.<BR>--3 Abated,<BR>subsided, put an end to, removed,<BR>extinguished; शांतरथक्षोभपरिश्रमं<BR>R. 1. 58; 5. 47; शांतार्चिषं दीपमिव<BR>प्रकाशः Ki. 17. 16.<BR>--4 Ceased,<BR>stopped; शांतमृगप्रचारं Ku. 3. 42.<BR>--5<BR>Dead, deceased.<BR>--6 Stilled,<BR>hushed.<BR>--7 Calm, quiet, undisturbed,<BR>tranquil, still; शांतमिदमाश्रमपदं<BR>Ś. 1. 16; 4. 19.<BR>--8 Tamed;<BR>R. 14. 79.<BR>--9 Free from passions, at ease,<BR>contented.<BR>--10 Shaded.<BR>--11 Gentle;<BR>शांतानुकूलपवनश्च शिवश्च पंथाः<BR>Ś. 4. 10.<BR>--12 Purified.<BR>--13 Meek,<BR>humble.<BR>--14 Auspicious (in augury);<BR>(the phrase शांतं पापं, which is<BR>sometimes repeated, means ‘oh, no!’<BR>'how can it be’, ‘God forbid such<BR>an untoward or unlucky event’;<BR>Ś. 5; Mu. 1).<BR>--तः<BR>1 A man who has<BR>subdued his passions, an ascetic.<BR>--2 Tranquillity, quietism, the<BR>sentiment of quietism, the<BR>predominant feeling of which is indifference<BR>to worldly objects and pleasures; see<BR>निर्वेद and रस.<BR>--तं Appeasing,<BR>pacifying.<BR>--तं ind. Enough, no more,<BR>not so, for shame, hush!, god<BR>(heaven) forbid!; शांतं कथं दुर्जनाः<BR>पौरजानपदाः U. 1; तामेव शांतमथवा<BR>किमिहोत्तरेण 3. 26.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन्,<BR>--चेतस् a. calm, tranquil-minded,<BR>sedate or composed in mind.<BR>--तोय<BR>a. having still waters.<BR>--रसः<BR>the sentiment of quietism; see शांत<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांतनवः|शान्तनव|शांतनव|शान्तनवः
शांतनवः ‘The son of Saṃtanu’,<BR>N. of Bhīṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांता
शांता N. of the daughter of<BR>Daśaratha, adopted by the sage<BR>Lomapāda and subsequently married<BR>by Ṛṣyaśṛṅga; see U. 1. 4. and<BR>ऋष्यश्टंग also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांतिः|शान्ति|शांति|शान्तिः
शांतिः f. [शम्-क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>Pacification, allayment, alleviation,<BR>removal; अध्वरविघातशांतये R. 11. 1,<BR>62.<BR>--2 Calmness, tranquillity, quiet,<BR>ease, rest, repose; स्मर संस्मृत्य न<BR>शांतिरस्ति मे Ku. 4. 17; Māl. 6. 1.<BR>--3 Cessation of hostility;<BR>Bv. 1. 125.<BR>--4 Cessation, stop.<BR>--5 Absence<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">Page1040-b+ 55</a>]<BR>of passion, quietism, complete<BR>indifference to all worldly enjoyments;<BR>तदुपहितकुटुंबः शांतिमार्गोत्सुकोऽभूत्<BR>R. 7. 71.<BR>--6 Consolation, solace.<BR>--7<BR>Settlement of differences,<BR>reconciliation.<BR>--8 Satisfaction of hunger.<BR>--9 An expiatory rite, a propitiatory<BR>rite for averting evil.<BR>--10 Good<BR>fortune, felicity, auspiciousness.<BR>--11<BR>Exculpation or absolution from<BR>blame.<BR>--12 Preservation.<BR>--13 N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदं, --उदकं, --जलं<BR>soothing or propitiatory water; Ś. 3.<BR>--कर, --कारिन् a. soothing, pacifying.<BR>--गृहं a room for rest or retirement.<BR>--होमः a sacrifice or burnt offering<BR>to avert or remove an evil; Ms. 4. 150.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांतिक|शान्तिक
शांतिक a. की f. Expiatory,<BR>propitiatory.<BR>--कं Observances or<BR>ceremonies calculated to remove<BR>calamities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांत्व्|शान्त्व्
शांत्व् &c. See सांत्व् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापः|शाप
शापः [शप्-घञ्]<BR>1 A curse, an<BR>imprecation, anathema; शापेनास्तं<BR>गमितमहिमा वर्षभोग्येण भर्तुः Me. 1, 92;<BR>R. 1. 78, 5. 56, 59; 11. 14.<BR>--2 An<BR>oath, asseveration.<BR>--3 Abuse,<BR>calumny.<BR>--4 An interdiction, a ban.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः, --अवसानं, --निवृत्तिः f.<BR>the end of a curse; Me. 110;<BR>R. 8. 82.<BR>--अस्त्रः ‘having a curse for a<BR>weapon', a sage, saint; R. 15. 3.<BR>--उत्सर्गः the utterance of a curse.<BR>--उद्धारः, --माक्तिः f.,<BR>--मोक्षः release or<BR>deliverance from a curse.<BR>--ग्रस्त a.<BR>labouring under a curse.<BR>--मुक्त a.<BR>released from a curse.<BR>--यंत्रित a.<BR>restrained by a curse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापित
शापित p. p.<BR>1 Bound by an oath,<BR>conjured.<BR>--2 Sworn, adjured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शापठिकः|शापठिक
शापठिकः A peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाफरिकः|शाफरिक
शाफरिकः A fisherman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाबर|शाबरः
शाब(व)र a. (री f.)<BR>[शब(व) र-अण्]<BR>1 Savage, barbarous.<BR>--2<BR>Low, vile, base.<BR>--रः<BR>1 An offence, a<BR>fault.<BR>--2 Sin, wickedness.<BR>--3 The<BR>tree called Lodhra.<BR>--री A low form<BR>of the Prākṛta dialect (spoken<BR>by mountaineers &c.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भेदाख्यं (also भेदाक्षं) copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावर|शावरः
शाब(व)र a. (री f.)<BR>[शब(व) र-अण्]<BR>1 Savage, barbarous.<BR>--2<BR>Low, vile, base.<BR>--रः<BR>1 An offence, a<BR>fault.<BR>--2 Sin, wickedness.<BR>--3 The<BR>tree called Lodhra.<BR>--री A low form<BR>of the Prākṛta dialect (spoken<BR>by mountaineers &c.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भेदाख्यं (also भेदाक्षं) copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्द|शाब्दः
शाब्द a. (ब्दी f.) [शब्द-अण्]<BR>1 Relating to or derived from a<BR>word.<BR>--2 Relating to or depending<BR>on sound (opp. आर्थ.).<BR>--3 Verbal,<BR>oral.<BR>--4 Sounding, sonorous.<BR>--5<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">Page1040-c+ 54</a>]<BR>Nominal (as inflection).<BR>--ब्दः A<BR>grammarian.<BR>--ब्दी N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बोधः perception or<BR>apprehension of the sense of words.<BR>--व्यंजना<BR>insinuation founded on words.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाब्दिक|शाब्दिकः
शाब्दिक a. (की f.) [शब्द-ठक्]<BR>1<BR>Verbal, oral.<BR>--2 Relating to sounds<BR>or words.<BR>--3 Sounding.<BR>--कः A<BR>grammarian.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामन्
शामन् n. Appeasing,<BR>conciliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामनः|शामन|शामनं
शामनः N. of Yama.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Killing, slaughter.<BR>--2 Tranquillity,<BR>peace.<BR>--3 End.<BR>--नी The southern<BR>direction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामित्रं|शामित्र
शामित्रं<BR>1 Sacrificing.<BR>--2<BR>Immolating, killing animals at a<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--3 Tying up cattle for<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--4 A sacrificial vessel.<BR>--5 A<BR>deadly blow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामिली
शामिली A sacrificial ladle; (स्त्रच्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामीनं|शामीन
शामीनं<BR>1 Ashes.<BR>--2 A sacrificial<BR>ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामीलं|शामील
शामीलं Ashes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शामीली
शामीली A chaplet, garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांबः|शाम्ब|शाम्बः
शांबः N. of a son of Kṛṣṇa and<BR>Jāmbavatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांबरी|शाम्बरी
शांबरी<BR>1 Jugglery, sorcery.<BR>--2<BR>A sorceress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांबविकः|शाम्बविक|शांबविक|शाम्बविकः
शांबविकः A dealer in shells.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांबुकः|शाम्बुक|शांबुक|शाम्बुकः
शांबु(बू)कः A bivalve-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांबूकः|शाम्बूक|शांबूक|शाम्बूकः
शांबु(बू)कः A bivalve-shell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांभव|शाम्भव|शाम्भवं|शाम्भवः
शांभव a. (वी f.) [शंभोरिदं अण्]<BR>Belonging to Śiva; अत्तुं वांछति शांभबो<BR>गणपतेराखुं क्षुधार्तः फणी Pt. 1. 159.<BR>--वः<BR>1 A worshipper of Śiva.<BR>--2 A son of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--3 Camphor.<BR>--4 Bdellium.<BR>--5 A kind of poison.<BR>--वं The<BR>Devadāru tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शांभवी
शांभवी<BR>1 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>plant (नीलदूर्वा).<BR>--3 The opening in<BR>the crown of the head through<BR>which the soul is said to escape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायः|शाय
शायः Lying, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिका
शायिका Repose, sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायिन्
शायिन् a. Reclining, sleeping,<BR>resting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शायकः|शायक
शायकः<BR>1 An arrow.<BR>--2 A sword;<BR>cf. सायक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्
शार् {c10c} U. (शारयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>weaken.<BR>--2 To be weak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार|शारं|शारः
शार a. [शार्-अच् शॄ-घञ् वा]<BR>1<BR>Variegated, speckled, mottled,<BR>spotted.<BR>--2 Yellow.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A variegated<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Green colour.<BR>--3 Air, wind.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">Page1041-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--4 A piece used at chess, a chessman;<BR>कालः काल्या भुवनफलके त्रीडति<BR>प्रणिशारैः Bh. 3. 39.<BR>--5 Injuring, hurting<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1040-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारंगः|शारङ्ग|शारंग|शारङ्गः
शारंगः<BR>1 The Cātaka bird.<BR>--2<BR>A peacock.<BR>--3 A bee.<BR>--4 A deer.<BR>--5<BR>An elephant; cf. सारंग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारंगी
शारंगी A particular musical<BR>instrument (played with a bow);<BR>cf. सारंगी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारद|शारदं|शारदः
शारद a. [शरदि भवं अण्]<BR>1<BR>Belonging to autumn, autumnal; (the f.<BR>is शारदी in this sense);<BR>विमलशारदचंदिरचंद्रिका Bv. 1. 113; R. 10. 9;<BR>Ms. 6. 11; मेघः शारद एव काशघवलः<BR>पानीयरिक्तोदरः Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Annual.<BR>--3 New,<BR>recent.<BR>--4 Young, fresh.<BR>--5 Modest,<BR>shy, bashful.<BR>--6 Diffident, not<BR>bold.<BR>--दः<BR>1 A year.<BR>--2 An<BR>autumnal sickness.<BR>--3 Autumnal sunshine.<BR>--4 A kind of kidney-bean.<BR>--5 The<BR>Bakula tree.<BR>--दी The full-moon<BR>day in the month of Kārtika.<BR>--दं<BR>1 Corn, grain.<BR>--2 The white lotus.<BR>--दा<BR>1 A kind of Vīṇā or lute.<BR>--2<BR>N. of Durgā.<BR>--3 Of Sarasvatī; (<BR>शरत्काले पुरा यस्मान्नवम्यां बोधिता सुरैः । शारदा<BR>सा समाख्याता पींठे लोके च नामतः).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदिकः|शारदिक|शारदिकं
शारदिकः<BR>1 Autumnal sickness.<BR>--2 Autumnal sunshine or heat.<BR>--कं An autumnal or annual<BR>Srāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारदीय
शारदीय a. Autumnal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिः|शारि
शारिः<BR>1 A chessman, a piece at<BR>chess &c.<BR>--2 A small round ball.<BR>--3<BR>A kind of die.<BR>--रिः f.<BR>1 The bird<BR>called Sārikā.<BR>--2 Fraud, trick.<BR>--3 An<BR>elephant's housings.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पट्टः,<BR>--फलं, --फलकः --कं a chequered cloth<BR>for playing at chess, draughts &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारिका
शारिका<BR>1 A kind of bird.<BR>--2 A<BR>bow or stick for playing any<BR>stringed instrument.<BR>--3 Playing at chess<BR>&c.<BR>--4 A chessman, a piece at<BR>chess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारी
शारी<BR>1 A kind of bird.<BR>--2 Ved.<BR>An arrow.<BR>--3 Kuśa grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीर|शारीरं|शारीरः
शारीर a. (री f.) [शरोंरस्येदं अण्]<BR>1 Relating to the body, bodily,<BR>corporeal.<BR>--2 Incorporate, embodied.<BR>--रः<BR>1 The incorporate or embodied<BR>spirit (जीवात्मन्); human or<BR>individual soul.<BR>--2 A bull.<BR>--3 A kind of<BR>drug.<BR>--4 Excrement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरक|शारीरकं
शारीरक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>the body, corporeal.<BR>--2 Incorporate,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">Page1041-b+ 55</a>]<BR>embodied (as the soul).<BR>--कं<BR>1 The<BR>embodied spirit.<BR>--2 The inquiry into<BR>the nature of that spirit (a term<BR>applied to the Bhāṣya of<BR>Śankarāchārya on the Brahma-sūtras).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सूत्रं the aphorisms of the<BR>Vedānta philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरकीय
शारीरकीय a. Corporeal; embodied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारीरिक|शारीरिकः
शारीरिक a. की f. Bodily,<BR>corporeal, material.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शारुक|शारुकः
शारुक a. (की f.) Noxious,<BR>hurtful, mischievous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कः|शार्क
शार्कः Candied sugar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ककः|शार्कक
शार्ककः<BR>1 Candied sugar.<BR>--2 A<BR>lump of sugar.<BR>--3 The froth of<BR>milk.<BR>--4 Cream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्कर|शार्करः
शार्कर a. (री f.) [शर्करा-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Made of sugar, sugary.<BR>--2 Stony,<BR>gravelly.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A gravelly place.<BR>--2 The froth or scum^1 of milk.<BR>--3<BR>Cream.<BR>--4 Molasses.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्करक|शार्करकः
शार्करक --रिक --रीय a. Gravelly, stony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्करिक|शार्करिकः
शार्करक --रिक --रीय a. Gravelly, stony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्करीय|शार्करीयः
शार्करक --रिक --रीय a. Gravelly, stony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ंग|शार्ङ्ग|शार्ङ्गं|शार्ङ्गः
शार्ंग a. (शार्ङ्ग strictly)<BR>1 Made<BR>of horn, horny.<BR>--2 Having a bow,<BR>armed with a bow; Bk. 8. 123.<BR>--र्गः --र्गं<BR>1 A bow (in general).<BR>--2<BR>The bow of Viṣṇu.<BR>--र्गं Wet ginger.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धन्वन् m.,<BR>--धरः, --पाणिः,<BR>--भृत् m. epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्ंगिन्|शार्ङ्गिन्
शार्ंगिन् m.<BR>1 An archer, a bowman.<BR>--2 An epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>धर्मसंरक्षणार्थैव प्रवृत्तिर्भुवि शांर्गिणः R. 15. 4. 12. 70;<BR>Me. 46.<BR>--3 Of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्दूलः|शार्दूल|शार्द्दूलः
शार्दूलः [शॄ-ऊलल् दुक् च]<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>--2 A leopard or panther.<BR>--3 A<BR>demon, Rākṣasa.<BR>--4 A kind of bird.<BR>--5 A kind of animal called श भ.<BR>(at the end of comp.) An<BR>eminent or distinguished person,<BR>foremost; as in नरशार्दूलः; cf. कुंजर.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चर्मन् n. a tiger's skin.<BR>--विक्रीडितं {1} a tiger's play;<BR>कंदर्पोऽपि यमायते विरचयन् शार्दूलविक्रीडितं<BR>Gīt. 4. {2} N. of a metre; see<BR>App. {1}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शार्वर|शार्व्वरं
शार्वर a. (री f.) [शर्वर्यां भवं अण]<BR>1<BR>Nocturnal; शार्वरांधकारपूर &c. Dk.;<BR>Ku. 8. 58.<BR>--2 Mischievous,<BR>pernicious.<BR>--रं Darkness, thick gloom.<BR>--री Night.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्
शाल् {c1c} A. (शालते)<BR>1 To praise,<BR>flatter.<BR>--2 To shine.<BR>--3 To be<BR>endowed with; Malli. on Ki. 5. 44.<BR>--4 To tell.<BR>--5 To boast, vaunt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालः|शाल
शालः<BR>1 N. of a tree (very tall<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-c" target="_blank">Page1041-c+ 55</a>]<BR>and stately), Shorea Robusta;<BR>R. 1. 38; Śi. 3. 40.<BR>--2 A tree in<BR>general; R. 1. 13; Ve. 4. 3.<BR>--3 An enclosure, a fence.<BR>--4<BR>A kind of fish.<BR>--5 N. of king<BR>Sālivāhana.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रामः a kind<BR>of sacred stone said to be typical<BR>of Viṣṇu, as the Phallus is of<BR>Śiva. ˚गिरि N. of a mountain. ˚शिला<BR>the Sālagrāma stone.<BR>--जः,<BR>--निर्यास; exudation of the Sāla tree, resin;<BR>R. 1. 38.<BR>--भंजिका {1} a doll,<BR>puppet, statue; Vb. 1; N. 2. 83. {2}<BR>a courtezan, harlot.<BR>--भंजी a doll,<BR>puppet.<BR>--वेष्ट्रः the resin of the<BR>Sāla tree.; cf. साल.<BR>--सारः {1} a<BR>superior tree. {2} asa foetida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालवः|शालव
शालवः The Lodhra tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाला
शाला [शाल्-अच्]<BR>1 An<BR>apartment, a room, saloon, hall;<BR>गृहैर्विशालैरपि भूरिशालैः Śi. 3. 50; so<BR>संगीतशाला, रंगशाला &c.<BR>--2 A house, an<BR>abode; R. 16. 41.<BR>--3 The upper<BR>or main branch of a tree.<BR>--4 The<BR>trunk of a tree.<BR>--5 A stable, stall; as<BR>in वाजिशाला, गर्दभशाला &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अजिरः --रं a hollow earthen cup.<BR>--मृगः a jackal.<BR>--वृकः {1} a dog;<BR>सिंहानां च सुखेन मूर्घसु पदं धास्यंति<BR>शालावृकाः Bv. 1. 72. {2} a wolf. {3}<BR>a deer. {4} a cat. {5} a jackal. {6}<BR>a monkey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाकः|शालाक
शालाकः N. of Pāṇini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाकिन्
शालाकिन् m.<BR>1 A lancer,<BR>spearman.<BR>--2 A surgeon.<BR>--3 A barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालाक्यं|शालाक्य|शालाक्यः
शालाक्यं A branch of surgery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालातुरीयः|शालातुरीय
शालातुरीयः An epithet of<BR>Pāṇini (written also शालोत्तरीय; so called<BR>from शलातुर the place of his birth).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालारं|शालार
शालारं<BR>1 A flight of steps, ladder.<BR>--2 A bird-cage.<BR>--3 The claw of an<BR>elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिः|शालि
शालिः<BR>1 Rice; न शालेः स्तंबकरिता<BR>वप्तुर्गुणमपेक्षते Mu. 1. 3; यवाः<BR>प्रकीर्णा न भवंति शालयः Mk. 4. 17.<BR>--2<BR>The civet-cat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ओदनः --नं<BR>boiled rice (of a superior kind).<BR>--गोपी a female appointed to watch<BR>a rice-field; इक्षुच्छायनिषदिन्यः<BR>शालिगोप्यो जगुर्यशः R. 4. 20.<BR>--चूर्णः --र्णं<BR>rice-flour.<BR>--पिष्ट्रं a crystal.<BR>--भवनं<BR>a rice-field.<BR>--वाहनः N. of a<BR>celebrated sovereign of India whose<BR>era commences with 78 A. D.<BR>--होत्रः {1} N. of a writer on<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">Page1042-a+ 55</a>]<BR>veternary subjects. {2} a horse.<BR>--होत्रिन्<BR>m. a horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1041-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिकः|शालिक
शालिकः<BR>1 A weaver.<BR>--2 A toll,<BR>tax.<BR>--3 A village of artisans.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिन्
शालिन् a. (नी f.) (usually at<BR>the end of comp.)<BR>1 Endowed with,<BR>possessed of, possessing, shining or<BR>resplendent with;<BR>अलघूपलपक्तिंशालिनी Śi. 16. 76, Ki. 2. 31, 7. 28,<BR>55; 8. 17, Rs. 4. 2.<BR>--2 Domestic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालिनी
शालिनी<BR>1 A mistress of the house,<BR>housewife.<BR>--2 N. of a metre; see<BR>App. I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीन|शालीनः
शालीन a. [शालाप्रवेशमर्हति, शाला-ख]<BR>1 Modest, bashful, shy, retiring;<BR>निसर्गशालीनः स्त्रीजनः M. 4; R. 6. 81,<BR>18. 17; Śi. 16. 83.<BR>--2 Like,<BR>resembling<BR>--नः A householder. (<BR>शालीनीकृ ‘to make humble, humiliate’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनता
शालीनता --त्वं Bashfulness, modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालीनत्वं|शालीनत्व
शालीनता --त्वं Bashfulness, modesty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुः|शालु
शालुः [शाल्-उण्]<BR>1 A frog.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of perfume.<BR>--3 A kind of<BR>astringent substance.<BR>--लु n. The<BR>root of the water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुकं|शालुक|शालुकः
शालु(लू)कं<BR>1 The root of the<BR>water-lily.<BR>--2 Nutmeg.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>frog.<BR>--2 The root of the<BR>waterlily (शालूक only in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूकं|शालूक|शालूकः
शालु(लू)कं<BR>1 The root of the<BR>water-lily.<BR>--2 Nutmeg.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>frog.<BR>--2 The root of the<BR>waterlily (शालूक only in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालुरः|शालुर
शालु(लू)रः A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालूरः|शालूर
शालु(लू)रः A frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालेयं|शालेय|शालेयः
शालेयं A field of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शालोत्तरीयः|शालोत्तरीय
शालोत्तरीयः An epithet of<BR>Pāṇini; see शालातुरीय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलः|शाल्मल
शाल्मलः [शाल्-मलच्]<BR>1 The<BR>silk-cotton tree.<BR>--2 One of the seven<BR>great divisions of the earth.<BR>--3 The<BR>gum of the cotton-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिः|शाल्मलि
शाल्मलिः<BR>1 The silk-cotton tree;<BR>Bv. 1. 115; Ms. 8. 246.<BR>--2 One of<BR>the seven great divisions of the earth.<BR>--3 N. of a kind of hell.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्थः an epithet of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिकं|शाल्मलिक|शाल्मलिकः
शाल्मलिकं An inferior kind of<BR>Śālmali tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिन्
शाल्मलिन् m. N. of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मलिनी
शाल्मलिनी The silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्मली
शाल्मली<BR>1 The silk-cotton tree.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a river in Pātāla.<BR>--3 A kind<BR>of hell.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वेष्टः, --वेष्टकः the<BR>gum of the silk-cotton tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाल्वः|शाल्व
शाल्वः<BR>1 N. of a country.<BR>--2 A<BR>king of Sālva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाव|शावः
शाव a. (वी f.) [शव-अण्]<BR>1 Relating to a dead body;<BR>caused by the death (of a<BR>relative); दशाहं शावमाशौचं सपिंडेषु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">Page1042-b+ 56</a>]<BR>विधीयते Ms. 5. 59, 61.<BR>--2 Tawny,<BR>dark-yellowish.<BR>--वः<BR>1 The young<BR>of any animal, a fawn, cub; क्व वयं<BR>क्व परोक्षमन्मथो मृगशावैः सममेधितो जनः<BR>Ś. 2. 18; मृगराजशावः R. 6. 3,<BR>18. 37.<BR>--2 A dark-yellowish colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावकः|शावक
शावकः The young of any animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शावर|शावरः
शावर See शाबर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वत|शाश्वतं|शाश्वतः
शाश्वत a. (ती f.) [शश्वद् भवः<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Eternal, perpetual,<BR>everlasting; शाश्वतीः समाः Rām. (=<BR>U. 2. 5) ‘for eternal years’, ‘ever more’<BR>'for all time to come'; U. 5. 27;<BR>R. 14. 14.<BR>--2 All.<BR>--तः<BR>1 N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--2 Of Vyāsa.<BR>--3 The sun.<BR>--तं<BR>Heaven.<BR>--तं ind. Eternally,<BR>perpetually, for ever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वतिक
शाश्वतिक a. (की f.) Eternal,<BR>permanent, perpetual, constant;<BR>शाश्वतिको विरोधः ‘natural antipathy’;<BR>शाश्वतिकं बिरोधमपहाय K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाश्वती
शाश्वती The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुल
शाष्कुल a. (ली f.) Eating flesh<BR>(or fish).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शाष्कुलिकं|शाष्कुलिक
शाष्कुलिकं A quantity of baked<BR>cakes (शष्कुली).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्
शास् {c2c} P. (शास्ति, शशास, अशिषत्,<BR>शासिष्यति, शासितुं, शिष्ट)<BR>1 To teach,<BR>instruct, train (governing two<BR>accusatives in this sense); माणवकं धंर्म<BR>शास्ति Sk.; Bk. 6. 10; शिष्यस्तेऽहं<BR>शाधि मां त्वां प्रपन्नं Bg. 2. 7.<BR>--2 To rule,<BR>govern; अनन्यशासनामुर्वी<BR>शशासैकपुरीमिव R. 1. 30; 10. 1. 14. 85, 19. 57;<BR>Ś. 1. 25; Bk. 3. 53.<BR>--3 To order,<BR>command, direct, enjoin; R. 12. 34;<BR>Mv. 6. 20; Ku. 6. 24; Bk. 9. 68.<BR>--4 To tell. communicate, inform<BR>(with dat.); तस्मिन्नायोधनं वृत्तं<BR>लक्ष्मणायाशिषन्महत् Bk. 6. 27;<BR>Ms. 11. 83.<BR>--5 To advise; स किंसखा साधु न<BR>शास्ति योऽधिपं Ki. 1. 5.<BR>--6 To decree,<BR>enact.<BR>--7 To punish, chastise,<BR>correct; ताञ् शिष्याच्चोरदंडेन धार्मिकः<BR>पृथिवीपतिः Ms. 8. 29, 4. 175, V. 5.<BR>--8 To<BR>tame, subdue; Mv. 6. 20.<BR>--9 To<BR>wish, desire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्
शास् m. A reciter; as in उक्थशास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासः|शास
शासः Ved.<BR>1 An order, command.<BR>--2 Praise (स्तुति).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासकः|शासक
शासकः [शास्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A ruler.<BR>--2 A chastiser, punisher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनं|शासन
शासनं [शास्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Instruction,<BR>teaching, discipline.<BR>--2 Rule, sway,<BR>government; अनन्यशासनामुर्वी<BR>R. 1. 30; so अप्रतिशासन.<BR>--3 An order, a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-c" target="_blank">Page1042-c+ 57</a>]<BR>command, direction; तरुभिरपि देवस्य<BR>शासनं प्रप्ताणीकृतं Ś. 6; R. 3. 69,<BR>14. 83, 18. 28.<BR>--4 An edict, enactment,<BR>a decree.<BR>--5 A precept, rule.<BR>--6 A<BR>royal grant (of land &c.),<BR>charter; अहं त्वां शासनशतेन योज यिष्यामि<BR>Pt. 1; Y. 2. 240, 295.<BR>--7 A deed,<BR>writing, written agreement.<BR>--8<BR>Control of passions.<BR>--9 A written book<BR>of authority. (At the end of comp.<BR>शासन often means ‘punisher,<BR>destroyer, killer’; as in स्मरशासनः,<BR>पाकशासनः).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिवृत्तिः f.<BR>violation of commands, disobedience.<BR>--पत्रं {1} a plate (usually of copper)<BR>on which a grant of land &c. is<BR>inscribed. {2} a sheet of paper on<BR>which an order is written.<BR>--हरः a<BR>royal messenger.<BR>--हारिन् m. an<BR>envoy, a messenger; R. 3. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासनीय
शासनीय a.<BR>1 To be ruled,<BR>governed or directed.<BR>--2 Punishable; V. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासित|शासितः
शासित p. p.<BR>1 Ruled,<BR>governed.<BR>--2 Punished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शासितृ
शासितृ m. [शास्-तृच्]<BR>1 A ruler,<BR>governor.<BR>--2 A chastiser; Ś. 1. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तिः|शास्ति
शास्तिः f. [शास्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Governing,<BR>ruling.<BR>--2 An order, a command.<BR>--3<BR>Correction, chastisement, punishment,<BR>especially the punishment<BR>inflicted by command of the king.<BR>--4 A<BR>sceptre, rod (of authority).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्तृ
शास्तृ m. [शास्-तृच् इडभावः]<BR>1 A<BR>teacher, an instructor.<BR>--2 A ruler,<BR>king, sovereign.<BR>--3 A father.<BR>--4<BR>A Buddha or Jina; or a deified<BR>teacher of the Bauddhas or Jainas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रं|शास्त्र
शास्त्रं [शिष्यतेऽनेन शास्-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>1 An<BR>order, a command, rule, precept.<BR>--2 A sacred precept or rule,<BR>scriptural injunction.<BR>--3 A religious or<BR>sacred treatise, sacred book,<BR>scripture; see comps. below.<BR>--4 Any<BR>department of knowledge, science;<BR>इति गुह्यतमं शास्त्रं Bg. 15. 20;<BR>शास्त्रेष्वकुंठिता बुद्धिः R. 1. 19; often at<BR>the end of comp. after the word<BR>denoting the subject, or applied<BR>collectively to the whole body of<BR>teaching on that subject; वेदांतशास्त्र,<BR>न्यायशास्त्र, तर्कशास्त्र, अलंकारशास्त्र &c.<BR>--5 What is learnt, knowledge;<BR>Śi. 5. 47.<BR>--6 A work, treatise; तंत्रैः<BR>पंचभिरेतच्चकार सुमनोहरं शास्त्रं Pt. 1.<BR>--7<BR>Theory (opp. प्रयोग or practice); इमं<BR>मां च शास्त्रे प्रयोगे च विमृशतु M. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिक्रमः, --अननुष्ठानं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-a" target="_blank">Page1043-a+ 56</a>]<BR>violation of sacred precepts, disregard<BR>of religious authority.<BR>--अनुष्ठानं<BR>--अनुसारः conformity to or observance<BR>of sacred precepts.<BR>--अभिज्ञ a.<BR>versed in the Śāstras.<BR>--अर्थः {1} the<BR>meaning of a sacred precept. {2}<BR>a scriptural precept or statement.<BR>--आचरणं {1} observance of sacred<BR>precepts. {2} the study of Śāstras.<BR>--(णः) {1} one versed in scriptures.<BR>{2} a student of the Vedas.<BR>--उक्त a. prescribed by sacred<BR>laws, enjoined by the Śāstras,<BR>lawful, legal.<BR>--कारः --कृत m.<BR>{1} the author of a Śāstra or<BR>sacred book. {2} an author in general.<BR>{3} a sage, saint.<BR>--कोविद् a. versed<BR>in the Śāstras.<BR>--गंडः a superficial<BR>reader of books, superficial scholar.<BR>--चक्षुस् n. grammar (as being the<BR>'eye', as it were, with which to<BR>understand any Śāstra).<BR>--चारणः<BR>one who deserves sacred precepts.<BR>--ज्ञ, --विद् a. {1} well versed in the<BR>Śāstras. {2} a mere theorist.<BR>--ज्ञानं<BR>knowledge of sacred books,<BR>conversancy with scriptures.<BR>--तत्त्वं truth<BR>as taught in the Śāstras, scriptural<BR>truth. ˚ज्ञः an astronomer.<BR>--दर्शिन् a.<BR>stated or enjoined in sacred books.<BR>--दृष्ट्रिः f. scriptural point of view.<BR>--प्रसंगः {1} the subject of the<BR>Śāstras. {2} any discussion on<BR>scriptural points.<BR>--योनिः the source of<BR>the Śāstras.<BR>--विधानं, --विधिः a sacred<BR>precept, scriptural injunction.<BR>--विप्रतिपेधः, --विरोधः {1} mutual<BR>contradiction of sacred precepts,<BR>inconsistency of precepts. {2} any act<BR>contrary to sacred precepts.<BR>--विमुख a.<BR>averse from study; Pt. 1.<BR>--विरुद्ध<BR>a. contrary to the Śāstras, illegal,<BR>unlawful.<BR>--व्युत्पत्तिः f. intimate<BR>knowledge of the sacred writings,<BR>proficiency in the Śāstras.<BR>--शिल्पिन्<BR>m. the country of Kāshmīra.<BR>--सिद्ध a. established by sacred authority.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1042-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रिन्
शास्त्रिन् a. (णी f.) [शास्त्रं वेत्त्यधीते<BR>वा इनि] Versed or skilled in the<BR>Śāstras. --m.<BR>1 One who has<BR>mastered the Śāstras, a learned man, a<BR>great Paṇḍita.<BR>--2 A teacher of<BR>sacred science.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्त्रीय
शास्त्रीय a. [शास्त्रेण विहितः छ]<BR>1<BR>Scriptural.<BR>--2 Scientific.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शास्य|शास्यः
शास्य a. [शास्-ण्यत्]<BR>1 To be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">Page1043-b+ 55</a>]<BR>taught or advised.<BR>--2 To be<BR>regulated or governed.<BR>--3 Deserving<BR>punishment, punishable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शि|शिः
शि {c5c} U. शिनोति, शिनुते<BR>1 To<BR>whet, sharpen,<BR>--2 To attenuate,<BR>make thin.<BR>--3 To excite.<BR>--4 To be<BR>attentive.<BR>--5 To be sharp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिः|शि
शिः<BR>1 Auspiciousness, good<BR>fortune.<BR>--2 Composure, calm,<BR>tranquillity, peace.<BR>--3 An epithet^1 of Śiva.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंशपा
शिंशपा<BR>1 N. of a tree शिशु<BR>--2 The Aśoka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्कु|शिक्कुः
शिक्कु a. Idle, lazy, indolent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्थं|शिक्थ
शिक्थं Bee's-wax; cf. सिक्थ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्यं|शिक्य
शिक्यं, --क्या<BR>1 A loop or swing<BR>(made of rope).<BR>--2 A burden or<BR>load carried in a sling.<BR>--3 The strings<BR>of a balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्या
शिक्यं, --क्या<BR>1 A loop or swing<BR>(made of rope).<BR>--2 A burden or<BR>load carried in a sling.<BR>--3 The strings<BR>of a balance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्यित|शिक्यितं
शिक्यित a. Suspended or carried<BR>in a loop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्ष्
शिक्ष् {c1c} A. (शिक्षते, शिक्षित)<BR>1 To<BR>learn, study, acquire knowledge of;<BR>अशिक्षतास्त्रं पितुरेव मंत्रवत् R. 3. 31.<BR>--2<BR>To teach (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षकः|शिक्षक
शिक्षकः (शिक्षका or शिक्षिका f.)<BR>[शिक्ष् ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A learner.<BR>--2 A<BR>teacher, instructor; यस्योभयं (i. e. क्रिया<BR>and संक्रांति) साधु स शिक्षकाणां धुरि<BR>प्रतिष्ठापयितव्य एव M. 1. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षणं|शिक्षण
शिक्षणं [शिक्ष्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Learning,<BR>acquiring knowledge.<BR>--2 Teaching,<BR>instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षा
शिक्षा [शिक्ष्-भाबे अ]<BR>1 Learning,<BR>study, acquisition of knowledge;<BR>शिक्षाविशेषलघुहस्ततया निमेषात्<BR>R. 9. 63.<BR>--2 Desire of being able to do<BR>anything, wish to prevail;<BR>Ki. 15. 37.<BR>--3 Teaching, instruction,<BR>training; काव्यजशिक्षयाऽब्यासः K. P. 1;<BR>अभूच्च नम्रः प्रणिपातशिक्षया R. 3. 25;<BR>M. 4. 9.<BR>--4 One of the six<BR>Vedāngas, the science which teaches the<BR>proper pronunciation of words and<BR>laws of euphony.<BR>--5 Modesty,<BR>humility.<BR>--6 Science; रणशिक्षा<BR>‘military science'.<BR>--7 Giving, bestowing<BR>(Ved.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः {1} a teacher,<BR>an instructor. {2} N. of Vyāsa.<BR>--गुरुः<BR>a religious preceptor.<BR>--नरः an<BR>epithet of Indra.<BR>--शक्तिः f. skill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षित|शिक्षितः
शिक्षित p. p. [शिक्षा जाताऽस्य तार,<BR>इतच्, शिक्ष-क्त वा]<BR>1 Learnt, studied.<BR>--2 Taught, instructed; अशिक्षितपदुत्वं<BR>Ś. 5. 22.<BR>--3 Trained, disciplined.<BR>--4 Tame, docile.<BR>--5 Skilful, clever.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">Page1043-c+ 60</a>]<BR>--6 Modest, diffident.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षरः {1} a teacher. {2} a pupil.<BR>--आयुध a. versed in the use of weapons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिक्षमाणः|शिक्षमाण
शिक्षमाणः A pupil, scholar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखंडः|शिखण्ड|शिखंड|शिखण्डः
शिखंडः [शिखाममति अम्-ड् तस्य<BR>नेत्वम् Tv.]<BR>1 A lock of hair left on the<BR>crown or sides of the head at tonsure.<BR>--2 A peacock's tail.<BR>--3 A crest;<BR>V. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखंडकः|शिखण्डक|शिखंडक|शिखण्डकः
शिखंडकः [शिखंड इव-कन्]<BR>1 A lock<BR>of hair left on the crown of the head<BR>at tonsure.<BR>--2 Locks or tufts of hair<BR>left on the sides of the head; (these<BR>are three or five in the case of the<BR>Kṣatriyas); कुवलयदलश्यामास्निग्धः<BR>शिखंडकमंडनः U. 4. 19.<BR>--3 A crest,<BR>tuft. plume.<BR>--4 A peacock's tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखंडिकः|शिखण्डिक|शिखंडिक|शिखण्डिकः
शिखंडिकः A cock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखंडिका
शिखंडिका See शिखंड (1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखंडिन्|शिखण्डिन्
शिखंडिन् a. [शिखंडोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>Crested, tufted. --m.<BR>1 A peacock;<BR>नदति स एष वधूसखः शिखंडी U. 3. 18;<BR>R. 1. 39; Ku. 1. 15.<BR>--2 A cock.<BR>--3<BR>An arrow.<BR>--4 A peacock's tail.<BR>--5<BR>A kind of jasmine.<BR>--6 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--7 N. of a son of Drupada.<BR>[Śikhaṇḍin was originally a female,<BR>being Amba born in the family of<BR>Drupada for wreaking her revenge upon<BR>Bhishma; (see Amba). But from her very<BR>birth the girl was given out as a male<BR>child and brought up as such. In due<BR>course she was married to the daughter<BR>of Hiraṇyavarman, who was extremely<BR>sorry to find that she had got a veritable<BR>woman for her husband. Her father,<BR>therefore, resolved to attack the kingdom<BR>of Drupada for his having deceived him;<BR>but Śikhaṇḍin contrived, by<BR>practising austere penance in a forest, to<BR>exchange her sex with a Yakṣa, and thus<BR>averted the calamity which threatened<BR>Drupada. Afterwards in the great<BR>Bhāratī war he proved a means of killing<BR>Bhīshma, who declined to fight with a<BR>woman, when Arjuna put him forward as<BR>his hero. He was afterwards killed by<BR>Aśvatthāman].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखंडिनी
शिखंडिनी<BR>1 A pea-hen.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of jasmine.<BR>--3 N. of the daughter<BR>of Drupada; see शिखंडिन् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरः|शिखर|शिखरं
शिखरः --रं [शिखा अस्त्यस्य-अरच्<BR>आलोपः]<BR>1 The top, summit, or peak<BR>of a mountain; जगाम गौरी शिखरं<BR>शिखडिमत् Ku. 5. 7, 4; Me. 18.<BR>--2<BR>The top of a tree.<BR>--3 Crest, tuft.<BR>--4 The point or edge of a sword.<BR>--5 Top, peak, point in general.<BR>--6<BR>The arm-pit.<BR>--7 Bristling of the<BR>hair.<BR>--8 The bud of the Arabian<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-a" target="_blank">Page1044-a+ 57</a>]<BR>jasmine.<BR>--9 A kind of ruby-like<BR>gem.<BR>--रा N. of a plant (मूर्वा).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वासिनी an epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरं|शिखर|शिखरः
शिखरः --रं [शिखा अस्त्यस्य-अरच्<BR>आलोपः]<BR>1 The top, summit, or peak<BR>of a mountain; जगाम गौरी शिखरं<BR>शिखडिमत् Ku. 5. 7, 4; Me. 18.<BR>--2<BR>The top of a tree.<BR>--3 Crest, tuft.<BR>--4 The point or edge of a sword.<BR>--5 Top, peak, point in general.<BR>--6<BR>The arm-pit.<BR>--7 Bristling of the<BR>hair.<BR>--8 The bud of the Arabian<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-a" target="_blank">Page1044-a+ 57</a>]<BR>jasmine.<BR>--9 A kind of ruby-like<BR>gem.<BR>--रा N. of a plant (मूर्वा).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वासिनी an epithet of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1043-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरिणी
शिखरिणी<BR>1 An excellent woman.<BR>--2 A dish of curds and sugar with<BR>spices.<BR>--3 A line of hair extending<BR>across the navel.<BR>--4 A kind of vine.<BR>--5 N. of a plant (मूर्वा)<BR>--6<BR>Arabian jasmine.<BR>--7 N. of a metre;<BR>see App. I.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखरिन्
शिखरिन् a. (णी f.) [शिखरं अस्त्यस्य<BR>इनि]<BR>1 Crested, tufted.<BR>--2 Pointed,<BR>peaked; शिखरिदशना Me. 82. --m.<BR>1 A mountain; इतश्व शरणर्थिनां<BR>शिखरिणां गणाः शेरते Bh. 2. 76;<BR>Me. 13; R. 9. 12, 17.<BR>--2 A hill-fort.<BR>--3 A tree.<BR>--4 The lapwing.<BR>--5 The<BR>plant अपामार्ग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखा
शिखा [शी-खक् तस्य नेत्वम् पृषो˚;<BR>Uṇ. 5. 24]<BR>1 A lock of hair left on<BR>the crown of the head; Mu. 3. 30;<BR>Śi. 4. 50; Māl. 10. 6.<BR>--2 A crest,<BR>top-knot.<BR>--3 Tuft, plume.<BR>--4 Top,<BR>summit, peak; Ki. 6. 17.<BR>--5 Sharp<BR>end, edge, point or end in general;<BR>Ś. 1. 4; Bv. 1. 2.<BR>--6 The end of<BR>a garment; तोयाधारपथाश्च वल्कलशि<BR>खानिष्यंदरेखंकिता; Ś. 1. 14.<BR>--7 A<BR>flame; प्रभामहत्या शिखयेव दीपः<BR>Ku. 1. 28; R. 17. 34.<BR>--8 A ray of<BR>light; Ku. 2. 38.<BR>--9 A peacock's<BR>crest or comb.<BR>--10 A fibrous root.<BR>--11 A branch in general,<BR>especially one taking root.<BR>--12 The head<BR>or chief of anything.<BR>--13 The<BR>fever of love.<BR>--14 The point of the<BR>foot.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंदं a kind of<BR>turnip.<BR>--तरुः a lamp-stand.<BR>--दामन् n. a garland worn on the top of<BR>the head.<BR>--धर a. pointed, crested.<BR>--रः {1} a peacock. {2} a Jaina<BR>deified saint. ˚जं a peacock's<BR>feather.<BR>--धारः a peacock.<BR>--मणिः a<BR>crest-jewel.<BR>--मूलं {1} a carrot. {2}<BR>a root having a tuft of leaves.<BR>{3} a turnip.<BR>--वरः the jack-fruit<BR>tree.<BR>--वल a. pointed, crested.<BR>--(लः)<BR>a peacock.<BR>--वृक्षः a lamp-stand.<BR>--वृद्धिः f. a kind of usurious interest<BR>daily increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखालुः|शिखालु
शिखालुः The crest of a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखावत्|शिखावन्त्
शिखावत् a.<BR>1 Crested.<BR>--2<BR>Flaming. --m.<BR>1 A lamp.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 The descending node.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिखिन्
शिखिन् a. [शिखा अस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>1<BR>Pointed.<BR>--2 Crested, tufted.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">Page1044-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Proud. --m.<BR>1 A peacock;<BR>उष्णालुः शिशिरे निषोदति तरोर्मूलालवाले<BR>शिखी V. 2. 23, 4. 8; Pt. 1. 151;<BR>Śi. 4. 5.<BR>--2 Fire; रिपुरिव सखी<BR>संवासोयं शिखीव हिमानिलः Gīt. 7;<BR>Pt. 4. 110; R. 19. 54; Śi. 15. 7.<BR>--3<BR>A cock.<BR>--4 An arrow.<BR>--5 A tree.<BR>--6<BR>A lamp.<BR>--7 A bull.<BR>--8 A horse.<BR>--9<BR>A mountain.<BR>--10 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--11<BR>A religious mendicant.<BR>--12 N. of<BR>Ketu.<BR>--13 The number ‘three’.<BR>--14<BR>The Citraka tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठं,<BR>--ग्रीवं blue vitriol.<BR>--ध्वजः {1} an<BR>epithet of Kārtikeya. {2} smoke.<BR>--पिच्छं, --पुच्छं a peacock's tail.<BR>--यूपः an antelope.<BR>--वर्वकः a gourd.<BR>--वाहनः an epithet of Kārtikeya.<BR>--शिखा {1} a flame. {2} a peacock's<BR>crest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिग्रुः|शिग्रु
शिग्रुः [शि-रुक् गुक् च]<BR>1 A<BR>potherb.<BR>--2 A kind of tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंख्|शिङ्ख्
शिंख् {c1c} P. (शिंखति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंघ्|शिङ्घ्
शिंघ् {c1c} P. (शिंघति) To smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंघाणः|शिङ्घाण|शिंघाण|शिङ्घाणं|शिङ्घाणः
शिंघाणः<BR>1 Froth, foam.<BR>--2<BR>Phlegm.<BR>--णं<BR>1 The mucus of the<BR>nose.<BR>--2 Rust of iron.<BR>--3 A<BR>glassvessel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंघाणकः|शिङ्घाणक|शिंघाणक|शिंघाणकं|शिङ्घाणकः
शिंघाणकः --कं The mucus of the<BR>nose.<BR>--कः Phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंघाणकं|शिङ्घाणक|शिंघाणक|शिंघाणकः|शिङ्घाणकः
शिंघाणकः --कं The mucus of the<BR>nose.<BR>--कः Phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंघित|शिङ्घित|शिङ्घितं
शिंघित a. Smelled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिच्
शिच् f. The string of a yoke<BR>(for carrying burdens).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंज्|शिञ्ज्
शिंज् {c1c} {c2c} A., {c10c} U. (शिंजते,<BR>शिंक्ते, शिंजयति-ते, शिंजित)<BR>1 To tinkle,<BR>jingle, rattle; Śi. 10. 62.<BR>--2 To<BR>roar, sound, bellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंजः|शिञ्ज|शिंज|शिञ्जः
शिंजः Tinkle, jingle, tinkling or<BR>jingling sound; especially of<BR>ornaments such as anklets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंजंजिका|शिञ्जञ्जिका
शिंजंजिका A chain worn round<BR>the loins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंजा
शिंजा<BR>1 Tinkle, jingle &c.<BR>--2 A<BR>bow-string.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंजित|शिञ्जित|शिञ्जितं
शिंजित p. p. Tinkling, jingling.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Tinkling, jingling (of anklets<BR>&c.); कूजितं राजहंसानां नेदं<BR>नूपुरशिंजितं V. 4. 14.<BR>--2 Clanking (of<BR>chains).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंजिनी
शिंजिनी<BR>1 A bow-string.<BR>--2 An<BR>anklet (worn round the feet).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिट्
शिट् {c1c} P. (शिटति) To slight,<BR>depise, disregard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शित|शितं
शित p. p. [शो-क्त]<BR>1 Sharpened,<BR>whetted.<BR>--2 Thin, emaciated.<BR>--3<BR>Wasted, declined.<BR>--4 Weak, feeble,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-c" target="_blank">Page1044-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रः a thorn.<BR>--धार a.<BR>sharp-edged.<BR>--शूकः {1} barley. {2}<BR>wheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शितद्रुः|शितद्रु
शितद्रुः f. The river Sutlej; see<BR>शतद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिति|शितिः
शिति a. [शि-क्तिच्]<BR>1 White.<BR>--2<BR>Black;<BR>शितितारकानुमितताम्रनयनमरुणीकृतं क्रुधा Śi. 15. 48.<BR>--तिः The birch<BR>tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठः {1} an epithet<BR>of Śiva; तस्यात्मा शितिकंठस्य<BR>सैनापत्यमुपेत्य वः Ku. 2, 61, 6. 81. {2} a<BR>peacock; अवनतशितिकंठकंठलक्ष्मीमिह<BR>दधति स्फुरिताणुरेणुजालाः Śi. 4. 56. {3}<BR>a gallinule.<BR>--छदः, --पक्षः a goose.<BR>--रत्नं a sapphire.<BR>--वासस् m. an<BR>epithet of Balarāma; विडंबयंतं<BR>शितिवाससस्तनुं Śi. 1. 6.<BR>--सारकः a kind of<BR>ebony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिल|शिथिलं
शिथिल a. [श्लथ्-किलच् पृषो˚<BR>Uṇ. 1. 53]<BR>1 Loose, loosened, slackened,<BR>relaxed.<BR>--2 Untied, unfastened;<BR>Ś. 2. 6.<BR>--3 Severed, fallen from the<BR>stalk; अर्कस्योपरि शिथिलं च्युतमिव<BR>नवमल्लिकाकुसुमं Ś. 2. 8.<BR>--4 Languid,<BR>enfeebled, unnerved.<BR>--5 Weak,<BR>feeble; अशिथिलपरिरंभ U. 1. 24, 27<BR>'fast or close embrace'.<BR>--6 Flaccid,<BR>flabby.<BR>--7 Dissolved.<BR>--8 Decayed.<BR>--9 Ineffective, futile, vain.<BR>--10<BR>Inattentive, careless; Pt. 4. 116.<BR>--11<BR>Loosely done, not strictly or rigidly<BR>performed.<BR>--12 Cast off, abandoned.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Laxity, looseness.<BR>--2<BR>Slowness. (शिथिलीकृ means {1} to loosen,<BR>unfasten, untie. {2} to relax,<BR>slacken. {3} to weaken, impair, enfeeble.<BR>--4 to give up, abandon; R. 2. 41.<BR>शिथिलीभू {1} to be slackened or<BR>relaxed. {2} to fall off from; Mk. 1. 13).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलयति
शिथिलयति Den. P.<BR>1 To<BR>relaxslacken, loosen, Ratn. 1. 14.<BR>--2 To<BR>give up, abandon; शिथिलय क्षणमात्रं<BR>बाष्पमोक्ष Ve. 5.<BR>--3 To lessen, allow<BR>to cool down; न सा इतोगतमनुरागं<BR>शिथिलयति V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलायते
शिथिलायते Den. A. To become<BR>loose or flaccid; Bh. 3. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिथिलित
शिथिलित a.<BR>1 Loosed.<BR>--2 Relaxed,<BR>loosened.<BR>--3 Dissolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिनिः|शिनि
शिनिः N. of a warrior<BR>belonging to the side of the Yādavas.<BR>(शिनेर्नप्तृ m. N. of Sātyaki).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिपिः|शिपि
शिपिः A ray of light. --f. Skin,<BR>leather. --n. Water;<BR>शैत्याच्छयनयागोच्च शिपि वारि प्रचक्षते Vyāsa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">Page1045-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--विष्ट a. (written शिपविपष्ट or शिविपष्ट<BR>also) {1} pervaded by rays. {2} bald,<BR>bald-headed. {3} leprous.<BR>--(ष्टः) {1}<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu. {2} of Śiva.<BR>{3} a bald man. {4} a man without<BR>prepuce. {5} a leper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1044-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिप्रः|शिप्र
शिप्रः N. of a lake on the<BR>Himālaya.<BR>--प्रं Ved.<BR>1 A cheek; jaw.<BR>--2<BR>The chin.<BR>--3 The nose.<BR>--4 A<BR>helmet or visor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिप्रा
शिप्रा<BR>1 N. of a river which issues<BR>from the Sipra lake and on the bank<BR>of which stands Ujjayinī;<BR>शिप्रावातः प्रियतम इव प्रार्थनाच टुकारः Me. 81.<BR>--2 A visor or helmet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफः|शिफ
शिफः See शिफा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफा
शिफा<BR>1 A fibrous root.<BR>--2 The root<BR>of a water-lily.<BR>--3 A root in general.<BR>--4<BR>A stroke with a whip.<BR>--5 A mother.<BR>--6 A river.<BR>--7 Turmeric.<BR>--8<BR>Spikenard.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंदः --दं the root of a<BR>water-lily.<BR>--धरः a branch.<BR>--रुहः<BR>the (Indian) fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिफाकः|शिफाक
शिफाकः The root of a water-lily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिबिः|शिबि
शिबिः(विः)<BR>1 A beast of prey.<BR>--2<BR>The birch tree.<BR>--3 N. of a country<BR>(pl).<BR>--4 N. of a king (who is said<BR>to have saved Agni in the form of<BR>a dove from Indra in the form of a<BR>hawk by offering an equal quantity<BR>of his own flesh weighed in a<BR>balance); Mu. 6. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविः|शिवि
शिबिः(विः)<BR>1 A beast of prey.<BR>--2<BR>The birch tree.<BR>--3 N. of a country<BR>(pl).<BR>--4 N. of a king (who is said<BR>to have saved Agni in the form of<BR>a dove from Indra in the form of a<BR>hawk by offering an equal quantity<BR>of his own flesh weighed in a<BR>balance); Mu. 6. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिबिका
शिबि(वि)का<BR>1 A palanquin,<BR>litter.<BR>--2 A bier.<BR>--3 A raised<BR>platform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविका
शिबि(वि)का<BR>1 A palanquin,<BR>litter.<BR>--2 A bier.<BR>--3 A raised<BR>platform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिबिरं|शिबिर
शिबि(वि)रं<BR>1 A camp;<BR>धृष्ट्रद्युम्नः स्वशिबिरमयं याति सर्वे सहध्वं<BR>Ve. 3. 18; Śi. 5. 68.<BR>--2 A royal camp<BR>or residence.<BR>--3 An intrenchment<BR>for the protection of an army.<BR>--4<BR>A kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविरं|शिविर
शिबि(वि)रं<BR>1 A camp;<BR>धृष्ट्रद्युम्नः स्वशिबिरमयं याति सर्वे सहध्वं<BR>Ve. 3. 18; Śi. 5. 68.<BR>--2 A royal camp<BR>or residence.<BR>--3 An intrenchment<BR>for the protection of an army.<BR>--4<BR>A kind of grain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिबिरथः
शिबि(वि)रथः A palanquin,<BR>litter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविरथः
शिबि(वि)रथः A palanquin,<BR>litter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंबः|शिम्ब|शिम्बः
शिंबः A kind of large shrub<BR>(चकमर्द).<BR>--बा A pod, legume; (also<BR>शिंबिः f. in this sense); Māl. 9. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंबिका
शिंबिका<BR>1 A pod, legume.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of kidney-bean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिंबी|शिम्बी
शिंबी<BR>1 A pod, legume.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरं|शिर|शिरः
शिरं<BR>1 The head.<BR>--2 The root<BR>of the pepper plant (m. also<BR>according to some, in these senses).<BR>--रः<BR>1 A bed.<BR>--2 A large serpent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्
शिरस् n. [शॄ-असुन् निपातः<BR>Uṇ. 4. 193]<BR>1 The head; शिरसा श्लाघते<BR>पूर्वं (गुणं) परं (दोषं) कंठे नियच्छति<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Skull.<BR>--3 A peak,<BR>summit, top (as of a mountain);<BR>हिमगौरैरचलाधिपः शिरोभिः Ki. 5. 17;<BR>Śi. 4. 54.<BR>--4 The top of a tree.<BR>--5<BR>The head or top of anything;<BR>शिरसि मपीपटलं दधाति दीपः Bv. 1. 74.<BR>--6 Pinnacle, acme, highest point.<BR>--7<BR>Front, forepart, van (as of an army);<BR>पुत्रस्य ते रणशिरस्ययमग्रयायी Ś. 7. 26;<BR>U. 5. 3.<BR>--8 Chief, principal, head<BR>(usually at the end of comp.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अस्थि n. (शिरोस्थि) the skull.<BR>--कपालिन् m. an ascetic who carries<BR>about a human skull.<BR>--गृहं (<BR>शिरोगृहं) a room on the top of a house,<BR>turret, garret.<BR>--ग्रहः (शिरोग्रहः)<BR>affection of the head, head-ache.<BR>--छदः, --छेदनं (शिरश्छेदः &c.)<BR>beheading, decapitation.<BR>--तापिन् m.<BR>an elephant.<BR>--त्रं, --त्राणं {1} a helmet;<BR>च्युतैः शिरस्त्रैश्चषकोत्तरेव R. 7. 49, 66;<BR>अपनीतशिरस्त्राणाः 4. 64. {2} a<BR>headdress.<BR>--धरा, --धिः (शिरोधरा --धि) the<BR>neck; Śi. 4. 52, 5. 65.<BR>--पीडा<BR>headache.<BR>--प्रणामः bending the head.<BR>--प्रावरणं a turban.<BR>--फठः the<BR>cocoanut tree.<BR>--भूषणं (शिरोभूषणं) an<BR>ornament for the head.<BR>--मणिः<BR>(शिरोमणिः) {1} a jewel worn on the<BR>head. {2} a crest-jewel. {3} a title of<BR>respect conferred on learned men.<BR>--मर्मन् m. (शिरोमर्मन्) a hog.<BR>--मालिन् m. (शिरोमालिन्) an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--रत्नं (शिरोरत्नं) a jewel worn<BR>on the head.<BR>--रुजा (शिरोरुजा)<BR>head-ache.<BR>--रुह् m.<BR>--रुहः (<BR>शिरोरुह्रुहः) (also शिरसिरुह्-हः) the hair of<BR>the head; Rs. 1. 4, Ku. 5. 9;<BR>R. 15. 16.<BR>--वर्तिन् a. (शिरोवर्तिन्)<BR>being at the head. (--m.) a chief, any<BR>one at the head of affairs.<BR>--वल्ली (<BR>शिरोवल्ली) the crest of a peacock.<BR>--वृत्तं<BR>(शिरोवृत्तं) pepper.<BR>--वेष्टः, वेष्टनं (<BR>शिरोवेष्ट्रः-ष्टनं) a head-dress, turban.<BR>--शूलं<BR>head-ache.<BR>--स्थः leader, chief.<BR>--हारिन्<BR>m. (शिरोहारिन्) an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरसिजः|शिरसिज
शिरसिजः The hair of the head;<BR>Śi. 7. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्कं|शिरस्क
शिरस्कं<BR>1 A helmet.<BR>--2 A turban,<BR>head-dress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्का
शिरस्का A palanquin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्तस्
शिरस्तस् ind. From the head;<BR>Ku. 3. 49; Bh. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरस्य|शिरस्यः
शिरस्य a. [शिरसि भवः यत्]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-c" target="_blank">Page1045-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Belonging to, or being on, the head.<BR>--स्यः<BR>Clean hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरा
शिरा Any tubular vessel of the<BR>body, a nerve, vein, artery,<BR>bloodvessel.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रः the<BR>woodapple.<BR>--मोक्षः bleeding.<BR>--वृत्तं lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिराल|शिरालं
शिराल a. Sinewy, tendinous, veiny.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरिः|शिरि
शिरिः [शॄ-कि]<BR>1 A sword.<BR>--2<BR>A killer, murderer.<BR>--3 An arrow.<BR>--4 A locust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिरीषः|शिरीष
शिरीषः [शॄ-ईषन् किच्च] N. of a<BR>tree.<BR>--षं A flower of this tree<BR>(regarded as the type of delicacy);<BR>शिरीषपुष्पाधिकसौकुमार्यौ बाहू<BR>तदीयाविति मे वितर्कः Ku. 1. 41; so पदं सहेत<BR>भ्रमरस्य पेलवं शिरीषपुष्पं न पुनः पतात्रिणः<BR>5. 4, R. 16. 48; Me. 65.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्
शिल् {c6c} P. (शिलति) To glean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलः|शिल|शिलं
शिलः --लं Gleaning ears of corn<BR>(more than one at a time); see<BR>Kull. on Ms. 10. 112.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उंछः {1} gleaning ears of corn. {2}<BR>an irregular occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलं|शिल|शिलः
शिलः --लं Gleaning ears of corn<BR>(more than one at a time); see<BR>Kull. on Ms. 10. 112.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उंछः {1} gleaning ears of corn. {2}<BR>an irregular occupation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिला
शिला<BR>1 A stone, rock.<BR>--2 A<BR>grindstone.<BR>--3 The lower timber of a<BR>door.<BR>--4 The top of a column.<BR>--5<BR>A tendon, vein (for शिरा).<BR>--6 Red<BR>arsenic.<BR>--7 Camphor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अटकः {1} a hole. {2} a fence, an<BR>enclosure. {3} a room on the top of a<BR>house.<BR>--आत्मजं iron.<BR>--आत्मिका a<BR>crucible.<BR>--आरंभा the wild plantain.<BR>--आसनं {1} a slab of stone used as a<BR>seat. {2} benzoin.<BR>--आह्वं bitumen.<BR>--उच्चयः a mountain; huge rock;<BR>R. 2. 34.<BR>--उत्थं benzoin.<BR>--उधवं {1}<BR>benzoin. {2} a superior kind of<BR>sandal-wood.<BR>--अओकस् m. an epithet of<BR>Garuḍa.<BR>--कुद्दकः a stone-cutter's<BR>chisel.<BR>--कुसुमं, --पुष्पं benzoin.<BR>--ज<BR>a. fossil, mineral.<BR>--जं {1} bitumen.<BR>{2} benzoin. {3} petroleum. {4} iron.<BR>{5} any fossil production.<BR>--जतु n. {1}<BR>bitumen. {2} red chalk.<BR>--जित f.,<BR>--दद्रुः bitumen.<BR>--धातुः {1} chalk. {2} red<BR>chalk. {3} a white fossil substance.<BR>--पट्टः --पट्टकः {1} a flat-stone for<BR>grinding &c. {2} a slab (of stone)<BR>used as a seat, stone seat.<BR>--पुत्रः,<BR>--पुत्रकः a small flat stone for<BR>grinding condiments upon.<BR>--प्रतिकृतिः f.<BR>an image of stone.<BR>--फलकं a stone<BR>slab.<BR>--भवं benzoin.<BR>--भेदः a stone<BR>cutter's chisel.<BR>--रसः {1} benzoin. {2}<BR>incense.<BR>--वल्कलः --लं, --वल्का a kind<BR>of moss.<BR>--वृष्ट्रिः f. {1} a shower of<BR>stones. {2} hail.<BR>--वेश्मन् n. a grotto<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">Page1046-a+ 55</a>]<BR>rocky recess.<BR>--व्याधिः bitumen.<BR>--सारं<BR>iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1045-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलिः|शिलि
शिलिः The birch tree.<BR>--लि f. The<BR>lower timber of a door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलिंदः|शिलिन्द|शिलिंद|शिलिन्दः
शिलिंदः A kind of fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिली
शिली<BR>1 The lower timber of a<BR>door.<BR>--2 A kind of earthworm.<BR>--3<BR>The top of a pillar.<BR>--4 A dart.<BR>--5 An<BR>arrow.<BR>--6 A female frog.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुखः<BR>{1} a bee;<BR>मिलितशिलीमुखपाटलिपटलकृतस्मरतूणविलासे Gīt. 1.;<BR>R. 4. 57. {2} an arrow; सा<BR>कुसुमघटितशिलीमुखमतोहरान्मदतचापादिव<BR>प्रमदवनास्त्रस्यति K. 225; or<BR>युगपद्विकाशमुदयाद्गमिते शशिनः शिलीमुखगणोऽ<BR>लभत Śi. 9. 41 (in both passages the<BR>word is used in senses {1} and {2}). {3}<BR>a fool. {4} war, fight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलींध्रः|शिलीन्ध्र|शिलींध्र|शिलीन्ध्रं|शिलीन्ध्रः
शिलींध्रः [शिलीं धरति धृ क पृषो˚<BR>मुम्]<BR>1 A kind of fish.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of tree.<BR>--ध्रं<BR>1 A mushroom, fungus,<BR>as in उच्छिलींध्र q. v.<BR>--2 The flower<BR>of the plantain tree; अधिपुरंध्रि<BR>शिलींध्रसुगंधिभिः Śi. 6. 32, or<BR>अलिनारमतालिनी शिलींध्र 72.<BR>--3 Hail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलींध्रक|शिलीन्ध्रक|शिलीन्ध्रकं
शिलींध्रक A mushroom, fungus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलींध्री
शिलींध्री<BR>1 Earth, clay.<BR>--2 A small<BR>earthworm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिलेय|शिलेयं
शिलेय a. Rocky, stony.<BR>--यं<BR>1<BR>Benzoin.<BR>--2 Bitumen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पं|शिल्प
शिल्पं [शिल्-पक्]<BR>1 An art, a<BR>fine or mechanical art; (64 such arts<BR>are enumerated).<BR>--2 Skill (in any<BR>art); craft; पात्रविशेषन्यस्तं गुणांतरं<BR>व्रजति शिल्पमाधातुः M. 1. 6.<BR>--3<BR>Ingenuity, cleverness.<BR>--4 Work,<BR>manual work or labour.<BR>--5 A rite,<BR>ceremony.<BR>--6 A kind of ladle or<BR>spoon used at sacrifices.<BR>--7 Form,<BR>shape.<BR>--8 Creation, procreation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन्, n.,<BR>--क्रिया any<BR>manual labour, handicraft.<BR>--कारः,<BR>--कारकः, --कारिन् m. an artisan, a<BR>mechanic.<BR>--विद्या {1} mechanical science.<BR>{2} any manual skill, handicraft.<BR>--शालं, --ला a workshop,<BR>manufactory (a technical school).<BR>--शास्त्रं<BR>{1} a book on any art, fine or<BR>mechanical. {2} mechanics.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पकं|शिल्पक
शिल्पकं A kind of drama<BR>(exhibiting magical and mystical rites).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिक
शिल्पिक a. Manual, mechanical.<BR>--कं<BR>1 Any handicraft or<BR>mechanical art.<BR>--2 = शिल्पकं q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिल्पिन्
शिल्पिन् a.<BR>1 Relating to a fine or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-b" target="_blank">Page1046-b+ 56</a>]<BR>mechanical art.<BR>--2 Mechanical.<BR>--m.<BR>1 An artisan, artist, a<BR>mechanic.<BR>--2 One who is skilled in<BR>any art.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिव|शिवं|शिवः
शिव a. [श्यति पापं शो-वन् पृषो˚]<BR>1 Auspicious, propitious, lucky;<BR>इयं शिवाया नियतेरिवायतिः Ki. 4. 21;<BR>1. 38; R. 11. 33.<BR>--2 In good health<BR>or condition, happy, prosperous,<BR>fortunate; शिवाति वस्तीर्थज लानि<BR>कच्चित् R. 5. 8 (= अतुपप्लवानि<BR>‘undisturbed’); शिवास्त पंथानः संतु ‘a<BR>happy journey to you’, ‘God bless<BR>(or speed) you on your journey’.<BR>--वः<BR>1 N. of the third god of the<BR>sacred Hindu Trinity, who is<BR>entrusted with the work of destruction,<BR>as Brahman and Viṣṇu are with<BR>the creation and preservation, of<BR>the world; एको दवः केशवो वा शिवो<BR>वा Bh. 2. 115.<BR>--2 The male organ<BR>of generation, penis.<BR>--3 An<BR>auspicious planetary conjunction.<BR>--4<BR>The Veda.<BR>--5 Final beatitude.<BR>--6<BR>A post to which cattle are tied<BR>--7 A god, deity,<BR>--8 Quick-silver.<BR>--9 Bdellium.<BR>--10 The black variety<BR>of thorn-apple.<BR>--वौ (m. dual) Śiva<BR>and Pārvatī कथयति शिवयोः<BR>शरीरयोगं विषमपदा पदवी विवर्तनेषु<BR>Ki. 5. 40.<BR>--वं<BR>1 Prosperity, welfare,<BR>wellbeing, happiness; तव वर्त्मान वर्ततां<BR>शिवं N. 2. 62; Ratn. 1. 2; R. 1. 60.<BR>--2 Bliss, auspiciousness.<BR>--3 Final<BR>beatitude.<BR>--4 Water.<BR>--5 Sea-salt.<BR>--6 Rock-salt<BR>--7 Refined borax.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षं = रुद्राक्ष q. v.<BR>--अरातिः a heretic (lit. a disbeliever in<BR>Śiva).<BR>--आत्मकं rock-salt.<BR>--आदेशकः {1} the bearer of auspicious news.<BR>{2} a fortune-teller.<BR>--आलयः {1}<BR>Śiva's abode. {2} the red basil.<BR>--(यं)<BR>{1} a temple of Śiva. {2} a cemetery.<BR>--इतर a. inauspicious, unlucky;<BR>शिवेतरक्षतये K. P. 1.<BR>--इष्ट्रा Dūrvā<BR>grass.<BR>--कर (शिवंकर also) a.<BR>conferring happiness, auspicious.<BR>--कीर्तनः N. of Bhṛṅgi.<BR>--गति a.<BR>prosperous, happy.<BR>--घर्मजः the planet<BR>Mars.<BR>--चतुर्दशी the fourteenth day<BR>of the dark half of Māgha; see<BR>शिवरात्र. ज्ञा a female devotee of the<BR>Śaiva sect.<BR>--ताति a. {1} having an<BR>auspicious end, conferring or<BR>conducive to happiness, propitious;<BR>प्रयत्न. कृत्स्नोयं फलतु शिवतातिश्च भवतु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-c" target="_blank">Page1046-c+ 55</a>]<BR>Māl. 6. 7. {2} tender, merciful, not<BR>demoniacal; मा पूतनात्वमुपगाः<BR>शिवतातिरेधि 9. 49.<BR>--(तिः) auspiciousness,<BR>happiness.<BR>--दत्तं the discus of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--दारु n. the Devadāru tree.<BR>--दूती epithet of Durgā.<BR>--द्रुमः<BR>theBilva tree.<BR>--द्विष्ट्रा the Ketaka tree.<BR>--धातुः {1} quick-silver. {2} milk.<BR>stone.<BR>--पुरं, पुरी N. of Benares.<BR>--पुराण<BR>N. of one of the eighteen Purāṇas<BR>--प्रियः {1} a crystal. {2} the Baka<BR>tree. {3} the thorn-apple.<BR>--(यं)<BR>= रुद्रक्ष q. v.<BR>--(या) the goddess<BR>Durgā.<BR>--मल्लकः the Arjuna tree.<BR>--रसः<BR>the water of boiled rice.<BR>--राजधानी N. of Benares.<BR>--रात्रिः f.<BR>the fourteenth day of the<BR>dark half of Māgha on which a<BR>rigorous fast is observed in honour<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--लिंगं {1} Śiva,<BR>worshipped in the form of a Phallus. {2}<BR>a temple dedicated to the worship<BR>of the Liṅga.<BR>--लोकः the world of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--वल्लभः the mango tree.<BR>--(भा)<BR>{1} white rose. {2} Pārvatī.<BR>--वाहनः a bull.<BR>--वीजं quick-silver.<BR>--शेखाः {1} the moon. {2} the<BR>thorn-apple.<BR>--सायुज्यं final<BR>emancipation (lit. unification with Śiva).<BR>--सुंदरी an epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवकः|शिवक
शिवकः<BR>1 A post to which cows<BR>or cattle in general are tied.<BR>--2<BR>A post for cattle to rub against,<BR>scratching-post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवा
शिवा<BR>1 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>--2 A<BR>jackal (in general); जहासि निद्रामशिवैः<BR>शिवारुतैः Ki. 1. 38; हरेरद्य द्वारे शिव<BR>शिव शिवानां कलकलः Bv. 1. 32;<BR>R. 7. 50, 11. 61, 12. 39.<BR>--3 A<BR>fortunate woman.<BR>--4 Final beatitude.<BR>--5 The Śamī tree.<BR>--6 The yellow<BR>myrobalan.<BR>--7 Dūrvā grass.<BR>--8<BR>A kind of yellow pigment.<BR>--9<BR>Turmeric.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरातिः a dog<BR>--प्रियः a goat.<BR>--फला the Śamī<BR>tree.<BR>--रुतं the howling of a jackal<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवानी
शिवानी Pārvatī, wife of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिवालुः|शिवालु
शिवालुः A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविः|शिवि
शिविः<BR>1 A beast of prey.<BR>--2 The<BR>birch tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविका
शिविका, शिविर See शिबिका,<BR>शिबर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिविर|शिविरं
शिविका, शिविर See शिबिका,<BR>शिबर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशिर|शिशिरः
शिशिर a. [शश्-किरच् नि.<BR>Uṇ. 1. 53] Cool, cold, chill, frigid;<BR>कुरु यदुनंदनचदनशिशिरतरेण करेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-a" target="_blank">Page1047-a+ 59</a>]<BR>पयोधरे Gīt. 12; R. 14. 3, 16. 49.<BR>--रः, --रं<BR>1 Dew, hoar-frost; पझानां<BR>शिशिराद्भयं; जातां मन्ये शिशिरमथितां पद्मिनीं<BR>वान्यरूपां Me. 83.<BR>--2 The cold season<BR>(comprising the two months Māgha<BR>and Phālguna); कंठेषु स्खलितं गतेऽपि<BR>शिशिरे पुंस्कोकिलानां रुतं Ś. 6. 3,<BR>Pt. 1. 128<BR>--3 Coldness, frigidity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुः, --करः, --किरणः, --दीधितिः, --रश्मिः<BR>the moon; बुव इव शिशिरांशोः<BR>V. 5. 21; शिशिरकिरणकांतं वासरातेऽभिसार्य<BR>Śi. 11. 21; शिशिरदीधितिना रजन्यः<BR>Rs. 3. 2.<BR>--अत्ययः, --अपगमः ‘the close of<BR>the cold season’, the spring season;<BR>स्वहस्तलूनः शिशिरात्ययस्य (पुष्पच्चियः)<BR>Ku. 3. 61; उपहित शिशिरापगमश्रिया<BR>R. 9. 31.<BR>--कालः, --समयः the cold season.<BR>--घ्नः an epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1046-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुः|शिशु
शिशुः [शो-कु सन्वद्भावः द्वित्वम्; cf.<BR>Uṇ. 1. 20]<BR>1 A child, an infant; शिशुर्वा<BR>शिष्या वा U. 4. 11.<BR>--2 The young<BR>of any animal (as a calf, puppy,<BR>fawn &c.); Ś. 1. 15; 7. 14, 18.<BR>--3<BR>A boy under eight or sixteen years<BR>of age.<BR>--4 A pupil, scholar.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्रंदः, --क्रंदनं the cry or weeping of<BR>a child.<BR>--क्रंदीयः (i. e. ग्रथः) a<BR>work treating of the complaints of<BR>children.<BR>--गंधा a kind of jasmine<BR>(double jasmine).<BR>--चाद्रायणं a<BR>lunar penance of children; (चतुरः<BR>प्रातरश्नीयींत्पडान् विप्रः समाहितः । चतुरोऽ<BR>स्तमिते सूर्ये शिशुचांद्रायणं स्मृतं ॥<BR>Ms. 11. 220).<BR>--नागः a young elephant.<BR>--पालः N. of a king of the Cedis<BR>and son of Damaghoṣa. [According<BR>to the Viṣṇu Purāṇa this monarch was,<BR>in a previous existence, the<BR>unrighteous Hiraṇyakaśipu, king of the Asuras<BR>who was killed by Viṣṇu in the form<BR>of Narasiṃha. He was next born as<BR>the ten-he added Rāvaṇa who was killed<BR>by Rāma. Then he was born as the<BR>son of Damaghoṣa, and continued his<BR>enmity to Kṛṣṇa, the eighth<BR>incarnation of Viṣṇu, with even greater<BR>implacability; (see Śi. 1.) He<BR>denounced Kṛṣṇa when they met at the<BR>Rajasuya sacrifice of Yudhiṣṭhira, but his<BR>head was cut off by Kṛṣṇa with his<BR>discus. His death forms the subject<BR>of a celebrated poem by Māgha].<BR>˚हन् m. an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--मारः the Gangetic porpoise. ˚शिरसु<BR>n. the northeast quarter.<BR>--वाहकः,<BR>वाह्यकः a wild goat.<BR>--हत्या<BR>childmurder, infanticide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुकः|शिशुक
शिशुकः<BR>1 A child, an infant.<BR>--2<BR>The young of any animal.<BR>--3 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">Page1047-b+ 55</a>]<BR>tree.<BR>--4 A porpoise.<BR>--5 A fish<BR>resembling a porpoise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशुलः|शिशुल
शिशुलः Ved.<BR>1 A child.<BR>--2 The<BR>young of an animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिश्नं|शिश्न|शिश्नः
शिश्नं, शिस्तं [शअ-नक् नि.] The<BR>penis or male organ of generation;<BR>Y. 1. 17; Ms. 11. 105.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--देवः a lustful or unchaste man<BR>(sporting with the penis).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिस्तं|शिस्त
शिश्नं, शिस्तं [शअ-नक् नि.] The<BR>penis or male organ of generation;<BR>Y. 1. 17; Ms. 11. 105.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--देवः a lustful or unchaste man<BR>(sporting with the penis).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिशिवदान
शिशिवदान a.<BR>1 Pious in<BR>conduct, virtuous, holy.<BR>--2 Wicked,<BR>sinful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्
शिष् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (शेषति) To hurt,<BR>kill. {vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U., (शेषति,<BR>शेषयति-ते) To leave as a remainder,<BR>spare. {vIII.v} {c7c} P. (शिनष्टि, शिष्ट)<BR>1<BR>To leave as a remainder, leave,<BR>leave remaining.<BR>--2 To distinguish<BR>or discriminate from others. --Caus.<BR>(शेषयति-ते) To leave &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्ट|शिष्टः
शिष्ट p. p. [शास् क्त शिष-क्त वा]<BR>1<BR>Left, remaining^1, residual, rest.<BR>--2<BR>Ordered, commanded.<BR>--3 Trained,<BR>educated, disciplined.<BR>--4 Tamed,<BR>docile, tractable.<BR>--5 Wise, learned;<BR>Śi. 2. 10; Pt. 1. 234.<BR>--6<BR>Virtuous, respectable.<BR>--7 Civil, polite.<BR>--8 Chief, principal, superior,<BR>excellent, distinguished, eminent;<BR>R. 1. 28.<BR>--ष्ट्रः<BR>1 An eminent or<BR>distinguished person.<BR>--2 A wise<BR>man.<BR>--3 A counsellor.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचारः {1} the practice of wise<BR>men. {2} good manners, good<BR>breeding.<BR>--सभा an assembly of chief<BR>or learned men, a council of state.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्टिः|शिष्टि
शिष्टिः f. [शास्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Rule,<BR>government.<BR>--2 Order, command.<BR>--3 Chastisement, punishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिष्यः|शिष्य
शिष्यः [शस् --क्यप्]<BR>1 A pupil,<BR>disciple, scholar; शिष्यस्तेऽहं शाधि मा<BR>त्वां प्रपन्नं Bg. 2. 7.<BR>--2 Anger, passion^1.<BR>--3 Violence, force.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--परंपरा a<BR>succession of pupils.<BR>--पुत्रः a pupil<BR>regarded as a son.<BR>--शिष्ट्रिः f. the<BR>correction of a pupil.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिह्लः|शिह्ल
शिह्लः, शिह्लकः Benzoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शिह्लकः|शिह्लक
शिह्लः, शिह्लकः Benzoin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शी
शी {c2c} A. (शेते, शयित; pass. शय्यते;<BR>desid. शिशयिषते)<BR>1 To lie, lie down,<BR>recline, rest; इतश्च शरणर्थिनः<BR>शिखरिणां गणाः शेरते Bh. 2. 76.<BR>--2 To<BR>sleep (fig. also); किं निःशंके शेषे<BR>शेषेवयसः समागतो मृत्युः । अथवा सुखं<BR>शयीथा निकटे जागर्ति जाहवी जननी<BR>Bv. 4. 30; Bh. 3. 79; Ku. 5. 12.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">Page1047-c+ 57</a>]<BR>To rest, repose. --Caus. (शाययति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to sleep or lie down;<BR>पार्श्वे शायय रावणं Bk. 8. 83.<BR>--2 To<BR>allow to rest or repose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शी
शी<BR>1 Sleep, repose.<BR>--2 Tranquillity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीक्
शीक् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (शीकते)<BR>1 To wet,<BR>sprinkle.<BR>--2 To go or move gently.<BR>{vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (शीकति, शीकयति-ते)<BR>1 To be angry.<BR>--2 To moisten,<BR>wet.<BR>--3 To be patient.<BR>--4 To speak.<BR>--5 To shine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीकरः|शीकर|शीकरं
शीकरः [शीक्-अरन्]<BR>1 Spray,<BR>thin rain, drizzle, mist; Ku. 1. 15,<BR>2. 42; R. 5. 42, 9. 68; Ki. 5. 15.<BR>--2 A drop of water or rain;<BR>गतमुपरि घनानां वारिगर्भोदराणां पिशुनयति<BR>रथस्ते शीकरक्लिन्ननमिः Ś. 7. 7;<BR>R. 16. 62.<BR>--रं<BR>1 The Sarala tree.<BR>--2 The<BR>resin of this tree.<BR>--3 Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीकरिन्
शीकरिन् a. Sprinkling, drizzling,<BR>pouring forth a spray of water;<BR>U. 3. 16; Māl. 9. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्र|शीघ्रं
शीघ्र a. Quick, rapid, speedy;<BR>बिब्रन्मणिं मंडलचारशीघ्रः V. 5. 2;<BR>शीघ्रकृत्यं ‘urgent business’;<BR>Pt. 3. 170.<BR>--घ्रः Conjunction (in astr.).<BR>--घ्रं ind. Quickly, swiftly, rapidly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उच्चः conjunction (in<BR>astr.).<BR>--कारिन् a. expeditions,<BR>quick.<BR>--कोपिन् a. choleric, irascible.<BR>--चेतनः a dog.<BR>--बुद्धि a. acute,<BR>sharp-witted.<BR>--लंघन a. going<BR>rapidly, swift of foot; Ghaṭ. 8.<BR>--वेधिन<BR>m. a good archer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रायते
शीघ्रायते Den. A.<BR>1 To become<BR>quick or rapid.<BR>--2 To hasten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रिन्
शीघ्रिन् a.<BR>1 Speedy, expeditious.<BR>--2 Making haste in pronunciation,<BR>pronouncing very rapidly; Śik. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रिय|शीघ्रियः
शीघ्रिय a. Quick.<BR>--यः<BR>1 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 Of Śiva.<BR>--3 The<BR>fighting of cats.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्रीय|शीघ्रीयं
शीघ्रीय a. Quick, swift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीघ्र्यं|शीघ्र्य
शीघ्र्यं Quickness, rapidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्
शीत् ind. A sound made to<BR>express a sudden thrill of pleasure or<BR>pain, (particularly applied to the<BR>sound of pleasure during sexual<BR>enjoyment).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः, --कृत्<BR>m. the above sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत|शीतं|शीतः
शीत a. [श्यै-क्त]<BR>1 Cool, cold,<BR>frigid; तव कुसुमशरत्वं शीतरश्मित्वमिंदोः<BR>Ś. 3. 2.<BR>--2 Dull, sluggish, apathetic,<BR>sleepy.<BR>--3 Dull, lazy, stupid.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A kind of reed.<BR>--2 The Nimba tree.<BR>--3 The cold season (n. also).<BR>--4<BR>Camphor.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Cold, coldness<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-a" target="_blank">Page1048-a+ 57</a>]<BR>chillness; आः शीतं तुहिनाचलस्य करयोः<BR>K. P. 10.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--3 Cinnamon.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुः {1} the moon:<BR>वक्त्रेदौ तव सत्ययं यदपरः<BR>शीतांशुरुज्जृंभते K. P. 10. {2} camphor.<BR>--अदः<BR>a kind of affection or diseased state<BR>of the gums.<BR>--अद्रिः the<BR>Himālaya mountain.<BR>--अश्मन् m. the<BR>moonstone.<BR>--आकुल, --आर्त a. pinched<BR>or benumbed with cold, shivering.<BR>--उत्तमं water.<BR>--करः {1} the moon.<BR>{2} camphor.<BR>--कालः the cold season,<BR>winter.<BR>--कालीन a. wintry.<BR>--कुंभः<BR>the fragrant oleander.<BR>--कृच्छ्रः, --च्छ्रं<BR>a kind of religious penance.<BR>--क्षारः<BR>refined borax.<BR>--गंधः white sandal.<BR>--गुः {1} the moon. {2} camphor.<BR>--चंपकः {1} a lamp. {2} a mirror.<BR>--दीधितिः the moon.<BR>--पुष्पः the<BR>Sirīsha tree.<BR>--पुष्पकं benzoin.<BR>--प्रभः<BR>camphor.<BR>--भानुः the moon.<BR>--भीरुः<BR>a kind of jasmine (Arabian)<BR>--मयूखः,<BR>--मरीचिः, --रश्मिः {1} the moon. {2}<BR>camphor.<BR>--मूलकं the root of the<BR>Uśīra q. v.<BR>--रम्यः a lamp.<BR>--रुच् m. the moon.<BR>--वल्कः the<BR>Udumbara tree.<BR>--वीर्यकः the fig-tree.<BR>--शिवः the Śamī tree.<BR>--(वं) {1}<BR>rocksalt. {2} borax.<BR>--शूकः barley.<BR>--सहः<BR>the Pīlu tree.<BR>--स्पर्श a. cooling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1047-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतक|शीतकः
शीतक a. Cold; see शीत.<BR>--कः<BR>1 Any cold thing.<BR>--2 Winter, the<BR>cold season.<BR>--3 A dull or dilatory<BR>person.<BR>--4 A happy man, one free<BR>from cares or anxieties.<BR>--5 A<BR>scorpion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतल|शीतलं|शीतलः
शीतल a. [शीतं लाति ला-क,<BR>शीतमस्त्यस्य लच्-वा] (a) Cool, cold,<BR>chill, frigid; अतिशीतलमप्यभः<BR>किं भिनात्ति न भूभृतः Subhāṣ.<BR>(b) Cool, bearable; महदपि पग्दुःखं<BR>शी तलं सब्यगाहुः V. 4. 13.<BR>--लः<BR>1<BR>The moon.<BR>--2 A kind of camphor.<BR>--3 Turpentine.<BR>--4 The Campaka<BR>tree.<BR>--5 A kind of religious<BR>observance (observed upon the sun's<BR>entering the sign Aries).<BR>--लं<BR>1 Cold,<BR>coolness.<BR>--2 The cold season.<BR>--3<BR>Benzoin.<BR>--4 White sandal, or sandal<BR>in general.<BR>--5 A pearl.<BR>--6 Green<BR>sulphate of iron.<BR>--7 A lotus.<BR>--8<BR>The root called वीरण q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--छदः the Campaka tree.<BR>--जलं<BR>a lotus.<BR>--प्रदः --दं sandal.<BR>--वातः a<BR>cool breeze.<BR>--षष्ठी the sixth day of<BR>the bright half of Māgha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतलकं|शीतलक|शीतलकः
शीतलकं A white lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतला
शीतला<BR>1 Small-pox.<BR>--2 The<BR>goddess presiding over small-pox.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पूजा worship of the<BR>goddess Śītalā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतली
शीतली Small-pox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीता
शीता See सीता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीतालु|शीतालुः
शीतालु a. [शीतं न सहते शीत-आलुच्]<BR>Suffering from or shivering with<BR>cold, chilled, pinched; शीतालुः<BR>सलिलगतेन सिच्यते स्प्त Śi. 8. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीत्य|शीत्यं
शीत्य See सीत्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीधु|शीधुः
शीधु m., n.<BR>1 Any spirituous<BR>liquor, rum.<BR>--2 Wine.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गंधः<BR>the Bakula tree.<BR>--पः a drinker of<BR>spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीन|शीनं|शीनः
शीन a. [श्यै-क्त] Thick,<BR>congealed.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A dolt, blockhead.<BR>--2 A<BR>large snake (अजणर).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ्
शीभ् {c1c} A. (शीभते)<BR>1 To boast.<BR>--2 To tell, say, speak (कयने?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीभ्यः|शीभ्य
शीभ्यः<BR>1 A bull.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीरः|शीर
शीरः A large snake; see सीर<BR>also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्ण|शीर्णं
शीर्ण [शॄ-क्त] p. p.<BR>1 Withered,<BR>decayed, rotten.<BR>--2 Dry, sere.<BR>--3<BR>Shattered, torn; shivered.<BR>--4 Thin,<BR>emaciated; (see शॄ).<BR>--5 Small,<BR>slender.<BR>--र्णं A kind of perfume.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंघ्रिः, --पादः {1} epithets of Yama.<BR>{2} of the planet Saturn.<BR>--पर्णं a<BR>withered leaf; (so शीर्णपत्रं).<BR>--(र्णः)<BR>the Nimba tree.<BR>--वृतं a water-melon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्वि|शीर्व्वि|शीर्व्विः
शीर्वि a.<BR>1 Destructive, hurtful,<BR>noxious, injurious.<BR>--2 Savage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षं|शीर्ष
शीर्षं [शिरस्-पृषो˚ शीर्षदेशः, शॄ-क सुक्<BR>च वा]<BR>1 The head; शीर्षे सर्पो देशांतरे<BR>वैद्यः Karpūr., Mu. 1. 21.<BR>--2 The black<BR>variety of aloe-wood.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवशेषः the head only as the remainder.<BR>--आमयः any affection or disease of<BR>the head.<BR>--उदयः an epithet of the<BR>zodiacal signs, Gemini, Leo, Virgo,<BR>Libra, Scorpio, Aquarius, and<BR>Pisces.<BR>--छेदः decapitation.<BR>--छेद्य a.<BR>fit to be beheaded, deserving death<BR>by decapitation; शीर्षच्छेद्यः स ते राम<BR>तं हत्वा जीबय द्विजं U. 2. 8;<BR>R. 15. 51.<BR>--रक्षं a helmet.<BR>--शोकः pain in<BR>the head.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षकः|शीर्षक|शीर्षकं
शीर्षकः An epithet of Rāhu.<BR>--कं<BR>1 The head.<BR>--2 Skull.<BR>--3 A helmet.<BR>--4 A head-dress, (cap, hat &c.).<BR>--5<BR>Verdict, judgment, judicial<BR>sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षण्यः|शीर्षण्य
शीर्षण्यः [शीर्षन्-यत्] Clean or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-c" target="_blank">Page1048-c+ 56</a>]<BR>unentangled hair.<BR>--ण्यं<BR>1 A helmet.<BR>--2 A head-dress (hat, cap &c.).<BR>--3<BR>Ved. A headrope.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीर्षन्
शीर्षन् n. The head. (This word<BR>has no forms for the first five<BR>inflections, and is optionally substituted<BR>for शिरस् or शीर्ष after acc. dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शील्
शील् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (शीलति)<BR>1 To<BR>meditate, contemplate.<BR>--2 To serve,<BR>honour, worship.<BR>--3 To do, practise.<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} U. (शीलयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>honour, worship.<BR>--2 To practise<BR>repeatedly, exercise, study, think of,<BR>ponder over; श्रुतिशतमपि भूयः<BR>शीलितं भारतं वा Bv. 2. 35; शीलयति मुनयः<BR>सुशीलतां Ki. 13. 43.<BR>--3 To put on,<BR>wear; चल सखि कुजं सतिमिरपुंजं<BR>शीलय नीलनिचीलं Gīt. 5.<BR>--4 To go to,<BR>visit, frequent; यदनुगमनाय निशि<BR>गहनमपि शीलितं Gīt. 7; स्मेरानता सपदि शीलय<BR>सौधमौलिं Bv. 2. 4. --WITH अनु, --परि<BR>to practise repeatedly, cultivate,<BR>think of; शश्वच्छ्रुतोऽसि मनसा<BR>परिशीलितोऽपि Rāj. P.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलः|शील
शीलः [शील् अच्] A large<BR>serpent (the boa)<BR>--लं<BR>1 Disposition,<BR>nature, character, tendency,<BR>inclination, habit, custom;<BR>समानशीलव्यसनेषु सख्यं Subhāsh; frequently at<BR>the end of comp. in the sense of<BR>‘disposed or habituated to’,<BR>‘indulging in’, ‘prone to’,<BR>‘addicted to’, ‘attached to’ &c; as<BR>कलहशील ‘disposed to quarrel’,<BR>‘quarrelsome’; भावनशील ‘disposed or<BR>apt to think'; so दात˚, मृगया˚, दया˚,<BR>पुण्य˚, आश्वासन˚ &c.<BR>--2 Conduct,<BR>behaviour in general.<BR>--3 Good<BR>disposition or character; good nature;<BR>शीलं परं भूषणं Bh. 2. 82; Pt. 5. 2.<BR>--4 Virtue; morality, good conduct,<BR>virtuous life, chastity, uprightness;<BR>दैर्भंव्यान्नृपतिर्विनश्यति… शीलं<BR>खलोपासनात् Bh. 2. 42, 39; तथा हि ते<BR>शीलमुदारदर्शने तपस्विन मप्युपदशेतां गतं<BR>Ku. 5. 36. Ki. 11. 25; Pt. 1. 169;<BR>R. 10. 70.<BR>--5 Beauty, good form.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडनं violation of<BR>morality or chastity; Pt. 1.<BR>--धारिन् m.<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--वंचना<BR>violation of chastity; ग्राप्तेयं<BR>शीलवंचना Mk. 1. 44.<BR>--वृत्त a.<BR>wellbehaved, virtuous.<BR>--(त्त) good or<BR>virtuous conduct, good breeding.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. virtue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलनं|शीलन
शीलनं [शील्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Repeated<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-a" target="_blank">Page1049-a+ 58</a>]<BR>practice, exercise, study, cultivation.<BR>--2<BR>Constant application.<BR>--3<BR>Honouring, serving.<BR>--4 Wearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1048-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीलित|शीलितं
शीलित p. p.<BR>1 Practised,<BR>exercised.<BR>--2 Put on.<BR>--3 Frequented,<BR>visited.<BR>--4 Skilled in.<BR>--5 Endowed<BR>with, possessed of.<BR>--तं Practice,<BR>conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शीवन्
शीवन् m. A large snake (boa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंशुमारः|शुंशुमार
शुंशुमारः A porpoise, (a<BR>corruption of शिशुमार q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्
शुक् {c1c} P. (शोकति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकः|शुक|शुकं
शुकः [शक्-क]<BR>1 A parrot; आत्मनो<BR>मुखदे षेण बध्यंते शुकसारिकाः Subhāṣ.;<BR>तुंडैराताब्रकुटिलैः पक्षैर्हरितकोमलैः ।<BR>त्रिवर्णराजिभिः कण्ठैरेते^1 मजुगिरः शुकाः ॥<BR>Kāv. 2. 9.<BR>--2 The Śirīṣa tree.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a son of Vyāsa. [He is said to<BR>have been born from the seed of Vyāsa<BR>which fell at the sight of the heavenly<BR>nymph Ghṛtācī while roaming over<BR>the earth in the form of a female<BR>parrot. Śuka was a born philosopher, and<BR>by his moral eloquence successfully<BR>resisted all the attempts of the nymph<BR>Rambha to win him over to the path of love.<BR>He is said to have narrated the<BR>Bhāgavata Purāṇa to king Parīkṣit. His<BR>name has become proverbial for the most<BR>rigid observer of continence].<BR>--कं<BR>1<BR>Cloth, clothes.<BR>--2 A helmet.<BR>--3 A<BR>turban<BR>--4 The end or hem of a<BR>garment.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अदतः the<BR>pomegranate tree.<BR>--तरुः, --द्रुमः the<BR>Sirīsha tree.<BR>--देवः N. of Suka.<BR>--नास<BR>a. having an aquiline nose.<BR>--(सः)<BR>N. of the minister of Tārāpīḍa.<BR>--नासिका an aquiline nose.<BR>--पुच्छः<BR>sulphur.<BR>--पुष्पः, --प्रियः the Śirīṣa<BR>tree.<BR>--(या) the rose-apple.<BR>--वल्लभः<BR>the pomegranate.<BR>--वाहः an epithet<BR>of Cupid.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dhaval Patel on 20161231. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/329. note: cf. AP.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्त|शुक्तं
शुक्त p. p. [शुच्-क्त]<BR>1 Bright,<BR>pure, clean.<BR>--2 Acid, sour<BR>--3 Harsh,<BR>rough, hard, severe.<BR>--4 United,<BR>joined.<BR>--5 Deserted, lonely.<BR>--क्तं<BR>1<BR>Flesh.<BR>--2 Sour gruel.<BR>--3 A kind of<BR>acid liquid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तकं|शुक्तक
शुक्तकं Sour eructation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिः|शुक्ति
शुक्तिः f. [शच्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 An oyster.<BR>shell, pearl-oyster; पात्रविशेषन्यस्तं<BR>गुणांतरं व्रजति शिल्पमाधातुः । जलमिव<BR>समुद्रशुक्तौ मुक्ताफलतां पयोदस्य M. 1. 6;<BR>Bh. 2. 67; R. 13. 17.<BR>--2 A<BR>conchshell.<BR>--3 A small shell, muscle.<BR>--4<BR>A portion of the skull.<BR>--5 A curl of<BR>hair^1 on a horse's breast (or neck);<BR>Śi. 5. 4; see Malli. thereon.<BR>--6 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-b" target="_blank">Page1049-b+ 58</a>]<BR>kind of perfume.<BR>--7 A particular<BR>weight equal to two Karṣas.<BR>--8<BR>Hemorrhoids.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्भवं, --जं<BR>a pearl.<BR>--पुटं, --पेशी a pearl-oyster<BR>shell.<BR>--वधूः the pearl-oyster.<BR>--वीजं<BR>a pearl.<BR>--स्पर्शः dusky spots on a<BR> pearl^2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिका
शुक्तिका A pearl-oyster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्र|शुक्रं|शुक्रः
शुक्र a. [शुच्-रक नि˚ कुत्वम्] Ved.<BR>1 Bright, radiant, shining.<BR>--2<BR>White, pure.<BR>--क्रः<BR>1 The planet<BR>Venus.<BR>--2 N. of the preceptor of<BR>the Asuras, who, by means of his<BR>magical charm, restored to life the<BR>demons killed in battle; see कच,<BR>देवयानी, and ययाति.<BR>--3 The month<BR>of Jyeṣṭha.<BR>--4 N. of Agni or fire.<BR>--5 N. of the plant Citraka.<BR>--क्रं<BR>1 Semen virile; पुमान् पुंसोऽधिक<BR>शुक्रे स्त्री भवत्यधिके स्त्रियाः<BR>Ms. 3. 49, 5. 63.<BR>--2 The essence of<BR>anything.<BR>--3 Male and female energy.<BR>--4 Ved. Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः a<BR>peacock.<BR>--कर a. spermatic.<BR>--(रः)<BR>the marrow of the bones.<BR>--भुज् f.<BR>a pea-hen.<BR>--भूः m. the marrow of<BR>the bones.<BR>--वरः, --वासरः Friday<BR>--शिष्यः a demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्रल
शुक्रल, शुकिय a.<BR>1 Seminal.<BR>--2<BR>Increasing the seminal flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुकिय
शुक्रल, शुकिय a.<BR>1 Seminal.<BR>--2<BR>Increasing the seminal flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ल|शुक्लं|शुक्लः
शुक्ल a. [शुच्-लुक् कुत्वम्] White,<BR>pure, bright; as in शुक्लापांग q. v.<BR>--क्लः<BR>1 A white colour.<BR>--2 The<BR>bright or light half of a lunar<BR>month.<BR>--3 N. of Śiva.<BR>--क्लं<BR>1 Silver.<BR>--2 A disease of the white part of<BR>the eye.<BR>--3 Fresh butter.<BR>--4 Sour<BR>gruel<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः, --अपांगः a<BR>peacock (having white corners of<BR>the eye); शुक्लापांगैः सजलनयनैः<BR>स्वागतीकृत्य केकाः Me. 22.<BR>--अब्लं a<BR>kind of sorrel.<BR>--अर्मन् n. a kind of<BR>disease of the eyes.<BR>--उपला candied<BR>sugar.<BR>--कंठकः a kind of gallinule.<BR>--कर्मन् a pure in conduct, virtuous.<BR>--कष्ठं white leprosy.<BR>--धातुः chalk.<BR>--पक्षः the bright half of a month.<BR>--मंडलं the corner of the eye.<BR>--वस्त्र<BR>a. dressed in white.<BR>--वायसः a<BR>crane.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. {1} a pure mode of<BR>life. {2} the maintenance derived by a<BR>Brāhmaṇa from other Brāhmaṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लक|शुक्लकः
शुक्लक a. White.<BR>--कः<BR>1 White<BR>colour.<BR>--2 The bright half of a<BR>lunar month.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लल
शुक्लल a. White.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्ला
शुक्ला<BR>1 N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>--2<BR>Candied sugar.<BR>--3 A woman having a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">Page1049-c+ 58</a>]<BR>white complexion.<BR>--4 The plant<BR>Kākolī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्लिमन्
शुक्लिमन् m. Whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्षिः|शुक्षि
शुक्षिः<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>--2 Light,<BR>lustre.<BR>--3 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंगः|शुङ्ग|शुंग|शुङ्गः
शुंगः<BR>1 The(Indian) fig-tree.<BR>--2 The hog-plum.<BR>--3 The awn of<BR>corn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंगा
शुंगा<BR>1 The sheath of a young<BR>bud.<BR>--2 The awn of barley or corn.<BR>--3 The waved-leaf fig.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंगिन्|शुङ्गिन्
शुंगिन् m.<BR>1 The(Indian) fig-tree.<BR>--2 The Plakṣa tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
शुच् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (शोचति)<BR>1 To be<BR>sorry, grieve for, bewail, mourn;<BR>अरोदीद्रावणोऽशोचीन्मोहं चाशिश्रियत्परं<BR>Bk. 15. 71; 21. 6; Bg. 16. 5.<BR>--2<BR>To regret, repent. {vII.v} {c4c} U. (<BR>शुच्यति-ते)<BR>1 To be sorry or afflicted.<BR>--2 To be wet.<BR>--3 To shine.<BR>--4 To<BR>be pure or clean.<BR>--5 To decay;<BR>become fetid.<BR>--6 To brighten,<BR>illuminate.<BR>--7 To burn, consume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्
शुच्, शुचा f. [शुच्-क्विप् टाप् वा]<BR>Grief, sorrow, affliction, distress;<BR>विकलकरणः पांडुच्छायः शुचा परिदुर्बलः<BR>U. 3. 22; कामं जीवति मे नाथ इति सा<BR>विजहौ शुचं R. 12. 75, 8. 72;<BR>Me. 88, Ś. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचा
शुच्, शुचा f. [शुच्-क्विप् टाप् वा]<BR>Grief, sorrow, affliction, distress;<BR>विकलकरणः पांडुच्छायः शुचा परिदुर्बलः<BR>U. 3. 22; कामं जीवति मे नाथ इति सा<BR>विजहौ शुचं R. 12. 75, 8. 72;<BR>Me. 88, Ś. 4. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचि|शुचिः
शुचि a. [शच्-कि]<BR>1 Clean, pure,<BR>clear; सकलहंसगुणं शुचि मानसं<BR>Ki. 5. 13.<BR>--2 White; Ki. 18. 15.<BR>--3<BR>Bright, resplendent; प्रभवति<BR>शुचिर्बिबोद्ग्राहे मणिर्न मृदां चयः U. 2. 4.<BR>--4<BR>Virtuous, pious, holy, undefiled,<BR>unsullied, अथ तु वेत्सि शुचिव्रतमात्मनः<BR>Ś. 5. 27; पथः शुचेर्दर्शयितार ईश्वराः R. 3. 46<BR>Ki. 5. 13.<BR>--5 Purified, cleansed<BR>hallowed; R. 1. 81; Ms. 4. 71.<BR>--6<BR>Honest, upright, faithful, true,<BR>guileless; सभायां वक्ति सामर्षः<BR>सावष्ट्रंभो नरः शुचिः Pt. 1. 200.<BR>--7<BR>Correct, accurate.<BR>--चिः<BR>1 The white<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Purity, purification.<BR>--3<BR>Innocence, virtue, goodness,<BR>uprightness.<BR>--4 Correctness, accuracy<BR>--5 The condition of a religious<BR>student.<BR>--6 A pure man.<BR>--7 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--8 The hot season; उपयर्या विदध.<BR>न्नवमल्लिकाः शुचिरसौ चिरसौरभ संपदः<BR>Śi. 6. 22, 1. 58; R. 3. 3;<BR>Ku. 5. 20.<BR>--9 The months of<BR>Jyeṣṭha and Aṣāḍha.<BR>--10 A<BR>faithful or true friend.<BR>--11 The sun<BR>--12 The moon.<BR>--13 Fire.<BR>--14 The<BR>sentiment of love (शृंगार).<BR>--15 The<BR>planet Venus.<BR>--16 The Citraka<BR>tree.<BR>--17 Acquittal.<BR>--18 An oblation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">Page1050-a+ 55</a>]<BR>made to fire at the first feeding of<BR>an infant.<BR>--19 N. of Śiva.<BR>--20<BR>The Arka plant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द्रुमः<BR>the sacred fig-tree.<BR>--प्रणी a.<BR>sipping water.<BR>--मणिः {1} a crystal.<BR>{2} a jewel worn on the head.<BR>--मल्लिका a kind of jasmine (Arabian)<BR>--रोचिस् m. the moon.<BR>--व्रत a.<BR>holy, virtuous.<BR>--स्मित a. having<BR>sweet or pleasant smile; Ku. 5. 20,<BR>R. 8. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1049-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिष्मत्|शुचिष्मन्त्
शुचिष्मत् a. Bright. --m. An<BR>epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचिस्
शुचिस् n. Light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुचीयति
शुचीयति Den. P., शुचीभू {c1c} P.<BR>1 To<BR>become pure.<BR>--2 To be bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुच्य्
शुच्य् {c1c} P. (शुच्यति)<BR>1 To bathe,<BR>perform ablutions<BR>--2 To squeeze,<BR>express (as juice).<BR>--3 To distil.<BR>--4<BR>To churn; (these senses may belong<BR>to शुच् {c4c} P. also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीरः|शुटीर
शुटीरः A hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुटीर्यं|शुटीर्य|शुटीर्य्य|शुटीर्य्यं
शुटीर्यं Valour, heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुठ्
शुठ् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (शोठति)<BR>1 To be<BR>impeded or hindered.<BR>--2 To limp, be<BR>lame.<BR>--3 To resist. {vII.v} {c10c} U. (<BR>शोठयति-ते) To be idle, lazy, or dull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंठ्|शुण्ठ्
शुंठ् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (शुंठति,<BR>शुंठयति-ते)<BR>1 To purify.<BR>--2 To become dry;<BR>see शुठ् I. also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंठिः|शुण्ठि|शुंठि|शुण्ठिः
शुंठिः --ठी f., शुंट्यं Dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंठी
शुंठिः --ठी f., शुंट्यं Dry ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंड्|शुण्ड्
शुंड् {c1c} P. (शुंडति)<BR>1 To break.<BR>--2<BR>To molest, vex, trouble, annoy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंडः|शुण्ड|शुंड|शुण्डः
शुंडः<BR>1 The juice issuing from the<BR>temples of an elephant in rut.<BR>--2<BR>An elephant's trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंडकः|शुण्डक|शुंडक|शुण्डकः
शुंडकः<BR>1 Distiller.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>military music or musical<BR>instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंडा
शुंडा<BR>1 An elephant's trunk.<BR>--2<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>--3 A tavern,<BR>dramshop.<BR>--4 The stalk of the lotus.<BR>--5<BR>A courtezan, harlot.<BR>--6 A bawd,<BR>procuress.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पानं a tavern,<BR>dram-shop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंडारः|शुण्डार|शुंडार|शुण्डारः
शुंडारः<BR>1 A distiller.<BR>--2 An<BR>elephant's trunk or proboscis;<BR>Mv. 1. 53.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंडालः|शुण्डाल|शुंडाल|शुण्डालः
शुंडालः An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंडिका|शुण्डिका
शुंडिका See शुंडा.<BR>1 The uvula or<BR>soft palate.<BR>--2 A swelling of a gland<BR>(also शुंडी in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंडिन्|शुण्डिन्
शुंडिन् m.<BR>1 A distiller.<BR>--2 An<BR>elephant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मूषिका the<BR>musk-rat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रिः|शुतुद्रि
शुतुद्रिः --द्रूः f. The river Sutlej;<BR>cf. शतद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुतुद्रूः
शुतुद्रिः --द्रूः f. The river Sutlej;<BR>cf. शतद्रु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुध्
शुध् {c4c} P. (शुध्यति, शुद्ध)<BR>1 To<BR>become pure or purified; (fig. also);<BR>मृतोयैः शुध्यते शोध्यं नदी वेगेन शुध्यति ।<BR>अद्भिर्गात्राणि शुध्यंति मनः सत्येन शुध्यति<BR>Ms. 5. 108-9.<BR>--2 To be<BR>auspicious, favourable, or eligible;<BR>तिथिरेव तावन्न शुध्यति Mu. 5.<BR>--3 To be<BR>made clear, have the doubts<BR>removed; न शुध्यति मेंऽतरात्मा Mk. 8.<BR>--4 To be defrayed or cleared; व्ययः<BR>शुध्यति Pt. 5. --Caus. (शोधयति-ते)<BR>1 To purify, cleanse, wash off.<BR>--2<BR>To clear, pay off (as a debt).<BR>--3<BR>To refine, filter.<BR>--4 To correct.<BR>--5<BR>To acquit.<BR>--6 To examine,<BR>investigate, inquire into. --WITH परि, --वि,<BR>सं to be purified; R. 12. 104;<BR>Ms. 5. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्ध|शुद्धं|शुद्धः
शुद्ध p. p. [शुध्-क्त]<BR>1 Pure, clean,<BR>purified; अंतःशुद्धस्त्वमपि भविता<BR>वर्णमात्रेण कृष्णः Me. 49.<BR>--2 Holy, undefiled,<BR>chaste, innocent; अन्वमीयत शुद्धोति<BR>शांतेन वपुषैव सा R. 15. 77, 14. 14,<BR>--3 White, bright.<BR>--4 Stainless,<BR>spotless.<BR>--5 Innocent, simple,<BR>guileless.<BR>--6 (a) Genuine, true. (b)<BR>Honest, upright.<BR>--7 Correct,<BR>faultless, upright.<BR>--8 Cleared, acquitted.<BR>--9 Mere, only.<BR>--10 Simple, pure,<BR>unmixed; (opp. मिश्र).<BR>--11<BR>Unequalled.<BR>--12 Authorized.<BR>--13<BR>Whetted, sharpened.<BR>--14 Not nasal.<BR>--द्धः<BR>An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--द्धं<BR>1<BR>Anything pure.<BR>--2 The pure spirit.<BR>--3<BR>Rock-salt.<BR>--4 Black pepper.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः a king's female apartments,<BR>harem, seraglio; शुद्धांतदुर्लभमिदं<BR>वपुराश्रमवासिनो यदि जनस्य Ś. 1. 17;<BR>Ku. 6. 52. {2} a king's wife. ˚चारिन्<BR>m. an attendant in the harem, a<BR>chamberlain; U. 1. ˚पालकः, --˚रक्षकः<BR>a guard of the harem.<BR>--अंता a<BR>king's wife, queen.<BR>--अपह्नुतिः f. a<BR>figure of speech; it is thus defined:<BR>--शुधापह्नुतिरन्यस्यारोपार्थो धर्मनिह्नवः.<BR>--आत्मन्<BR>a. pure-minded, honest. (--m.) {1} the<BR>pure spirit. {2} N. of Śiva.<BR>--ओदनः<BR>(शुद्धोदनः) N. of the father of the<BR>celebrated Buddha. ˚सुतः N. of<BR>the celebrated Buddha.<BR>--कर्मन् a.<BR>pure in deeds, holy.<BR>--कोटिः f.<BR>one of the sides of a right-angled<BR>triangle.<BR>--चैतन्यं pure<BR>intelligence.<BR>--जंघः an ass.<BR>--धी, --भाव,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">Page1050-c+ 58</a>]<BR>--मति a. pure-minded, guileless,<BR>honest.<BR>--वधः killing in a simple<BR>or ordinary way.<BR>--वंश्य a. born of<BR>a pure family; R. 1. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुद्धिः|शुद्धि
शुद्धिः [शुध्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Purity,<BR>cleanness.<BR>--2 Brightness, lustre;<BR>मुक्तागुणशुद्धयोपि (चंद्रपादाः) R. 16. 18.<BR>--3 Sanctity, holiness; तीर्थभिषेकजां<BR>शुद्धिमादधाना महीक्षितः R. 1. 85<BR>--4<BR>Purification expiation, atonement,<BR>expiatory act; शरीरत्यागमात्रणे<BR>शुद्धिलाभममन्यत R. 12. 10.<BR>--5 A<BR>purificatory or expiatory rite.<BR>--6<BR>Paying off or clearing (of expenses).<BR>--7 Retaliation, requital.<BR>--8<BR>Acquittal, innocence (established by trial).<BR>--9 Truth, accuracy, correctness.<BR>--10 Rectification, correction.<BR>--11<BR>Subtraction.<BR>--12 N. of Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a. purifying,<BR>correctng.<BR>--पत्रं {1} a list of errata or<BR>corrigenda. {2} a certificate of purification<BR>by penance or atonement.<BR>--भृत् a.<BR>{1} clear, clean. {2} pious, virtuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्
शुन् {c6c} P. (शुतति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनःशेपः|शुनःशेप
शुनःशेपः(फः) N. of a Vedic<BR>sage, son of Ajīgarta. [In the<BR>Aitareya Brāhmaṇa it is related that king<BR>Hariścandra, being childless, made a<BR>vow that on obtaining a son he would<BR>sacrifice him to the god Varuṇa. A son<BR>was born who was named Rohita, but<BR>the king put off the fulfilment of the<BR>vow under various pretexts. At last<BR>Rohita purchased for one hundred cows<BR>Śunaḥśepha, the middle son of<BR>Ajīgarta, as a substitute for himself to be<BR>offered to Varuṇa. But the boy<BR>praised Viṣṇu, Indra, and other deities, and<BR>escaped death. He was then adopted<BR>by Viśvāmitra in his own family and<BR>called by the name Devarāta].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनःशेफः|शुनःशेफ
शुनःशेपः(फः) N. of a Vedic<BR>sage, son of Ajīgarta. [In the<BR>Aitareya Brāhmaṇa it is related that king<BR>Hariścandra, being childless, made a<BR>vow that on obtaining a son he would<BR>sacrifice him to the god Varuṇa. A son<BR>was born who was named Rohita, but<BR>the king put off the fulfilment of the<BR>vow under various pretexts. At last<BR>Rohita purchased for one hundred cows<BR>Śunaḥśepha, the middle son of<BR>Ajīgarta, as a substitute for himself to be<BR>offered to Varuṇa. But the boy<BR>praised Viṣṇu, Indra, and other deities, and<BR>escaped death. He was then adopted<BR>by Viśvāmitra in his own family and<BR>called by the name Devarāta].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनकः|शुनक
शुनकः<BR>1 N. of a sage,<BR>descendant of Bhṛgu.<BR>--2 A dog.<BR>--3 A<BR>young dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनाशीरः|शुनाशीर
शुनाशी(सी)रः<BR>1 An epithet<BR>of Indra.<BR>--2 An owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनासीरः|शुनासीर
शुनाशी(सी)रः<BR>1 An epithet<BR>of Indra.<BR>--2 An owl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनिः|शुनि
शुनिः A dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनी
शुनी f. A female dog, a bitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुनीरः|शुनीर
शुनीरः A number of female dogs.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंध्|शुन्ध्
शुंध्^1 {c1c} {c10c} U. (शुंधति-ते, शुंधयति-ते)<BR>1 To be purified or cleansed.<BR>--2 To<BR>cleanse, purify.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंध्युः|शुन्ध्यु|शुन्ध्युः
शुंध्युः<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>Agni (Ved.). --f. A mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुन्य|शुन्यं
शुन्य a. Empty.<BR>--न्यं<BR>1 A<BR>number of bitches.<BR>--2 A cypher; (more<BR>properly शून्य q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1050-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुप्
शुप् A technical term used by<BR>Pāṇini for उ the sign of the eighth<BR>class of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
शुभ् {c1c} A. शोभते<BR>1 To shine, be<BR>splendid, look beautiful or<BR>handsome; सुष्ठु शोभसे एतेन विनयमाहात्म्येन<BR>U. 1; R. 8. 6.<BR>--2 To appear to<BR>advantage; सुखं हि दुःखान्यनुभूय शोभते<BR>Mk. 1. 10.<BR>--3 To suit, become, befit<BR>(with gen.); रामभद्र इत्येवोपचारः<BR>शोभते तातपरिजनस्य U. 1.<BR>--4 To be gay<BR>or happy.<BR>--5 To be victorious. --Caus.<BR>(शोभयनि-ते) To decorate, adorn,<BR>grace. --WITH परि, -वि to shine,<BR>look splendid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्
शुभ् f. Ved.<BR>1 Beauty, splendour.<BR>--2 Radiance, lustre.<BR>--3 Happiness.<BR>--4 Victory.<BR>--5 An ornament.<BR>--6 An<BR>auspicious offering.<BR>--7 Water.<BR>--8<BR>A brilliant chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ|शुभं|शुभः
शुभ a. [शुभ्-क]<BR>1 Shining, bright.<BR>--2 Beautiful, handsome; जंघे शुभे<BR>सृष्ट्रवतस्तदीये Ku. 1. 35.<BR>--3<BR>Auspicious, lucky, happy, fortunate.<BR>--4<BR>Eminent, good, virtuous,<BR>Pt. 1. 358.<BR>--5 Learned, versed in the<BR>Vedas.<BR>--भं<BR>1 Auspiciousness,<BR>welfare, good fortune, happiness, good,<BR>prosperity. प्रायः शुभं च विदधात्यशुभं<BR>च जंतोः सर्वंकषा भगवती भवितव्यतैव<BR>Māl. 1. 23.<BR>--2 An ornament.<BR>--3<BR>Water.<BR>--4 A kind of fragrant wood.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--अंग a. handsome.<BR>--(गी) {1} a<BR>handsome woman. {2} N. of Rati,<BR>wife of Cupid. {3} of the wife of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--अपांगा a beautiful woman.<BR>--अशुभं weal and woe, good and<BR>evil.<BR>--आचार a. virtuous.<BR>--आनना<BR>a handsome woman.<BR>--आवह a.<BR>tending to welfare, conducive to good.<BR>इतर a {1} evil, bad. {2}<BR>inauspicious.<BR>--उदर्क a. having a happy end<BR>--कर a. auspicious, propitious.<BR>--कर्मन् n. {1} a virtuous act. {2} an<BR>honourable occupation.<BR>--ग a. {1}<BR>elegant, graceful. {2} propitious,<BR>fortunate.<BR>--गंधकं gum-myrrh.<BR>--ग्रहः an auspicious planet.<BR>--दः the<BR>sacred fig-tree.<BR>--दंती a woman with<BR>good teeth.<BR>--लग्नः -ग्नं a lucky or<BR>auspicious moment.<BR>--वार्ता good<BR>news.<BR>--वासनः perfume for the<BR>mouth.<BR>--शंसिन् a. presaging good,<BR>indicative of auspiciousness;<BR>R. 3. 14.<BR>--स्थली {1} a hall in which<BR>sacrifices are performed. {2} an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">Page1051-b+ 55</a>]<BR>auspicious place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंयु|शुभंयुः
शुभंयु a. [शुभं अस्यास्ति युस्]<BR>Auspicious, lucky, fortunate, blessed;<BR>अधिकं शुशुभे शुभंयुना द्वितयेन द्व्यमेव संग<BR>तं R. 8. 6; Bk. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंकर|शुभङ्कर|शुभङ्करः
शुभंकर a.<BR>1 Auspicious.<BR>--2<BR>Promoting happiness.<BR>--री N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभंभावुक
शुभंभावुक a. Decorated,<BR>ornamented, bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभा
शुभा<BR>1 Lustre, light.<BR>--2 Beauty.<BR>--3 Desire.<BR>--4 Yellow pigment.<BR>--5<BR>The Śamī tree.<BR>--6 An assembly of<BR>gods.<BR>--7 Dūrvā grass.<BR>--8<BR>Bamboomanna.<BR>--9 The Priyaṅgu creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्र|शुभ्रं|शुभ्रः
शुभ्र a. [शुभ-रक्]<BR>1 Shining,<BR>bright, radiant.<BR>--2 White; पश्यति<BR>पित्तोपहतः शशिशुभ्रं शंखपपि पीतं K. P. 10;<BR>R. 2. 69.<BR>--ब्रः<BR>1 The white colour.<BR>--2 Sandal (said to be n.).<BR>--ब्रं<BR>1<BR>Silver.<BR>--2 Talc.<BR>--3 Rock-salt.<BR>--4<BR>Green vitriol.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुः, --करः {1}<BR>the moon. {2} camphor.<BR>--दतिन् n.<BR>the elephant presiding over the<BR>north-west quarter.<BR>--रशिमः the<BR>moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रा
शुभ्रा<BR>1 The Ganges.<BR>--2 A crystal.<BR>--3 Bamboo-manna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुभ्रिः|शुभ्रि
शुभ्रिः An epithet of Brahman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंभ्|शुम्भ्
शुंभ् {c1c} P. (शुंभति)<BR>1 To shine.<BR>--2 To speak.<BR>--3 To hurt, injure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुंभः|शुम्भ|शुंभ|शुम्भः
शुंभः N. of a demon killed by<BR>Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--घातिनी, --मर्दिनी an<BR>epithet of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुर्
शु(शू)र् {c4c} A. (शूर्यते)<BR>1 To<BR>hurt, kill.<BR>--2 To make firm or<BR>steady, stop.<BR>--3 To be firm or fixed.<BR>--4<BR>To be senseless, to faint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर|शूरः
शु(शू)र् {c4c} A. (शूर्यते)<BR>1 To<BR>hurt, kill.<BR>--2 To make firm or<BR>steady, stop.<BR>--3 To be firm or fixed.<BR>--4<BR>To be senseless, to faint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्क्
शुल्क् {c10c} U. (शुल्कय ति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>gain.<BR>--2 To pay, give.<BR>--3 To create.<BR>--4 To tell, narrate.<BR>--5 To leave,<BR>forsake, abandon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्कः|शुल्क|शुल्कं
शुल्कः, --ल्कं [शुल्क्यते अतिसृज्यते<BR>कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>1 A toll, tax, customs,<BR>duty; particularly^1 levied at ferries,<BR>passes, roads &c.; कः सुधीः<BR>संत्यजेद्रांडं शुल्कस्यैवातिसाध्वसात् H. 3. 125;<BR>Ms. 8. 159; Y. 2. 47.<BR>--2 Gain,<BR>profit.<BR>--3 Money advanced to ratify a<BR>bargain.<BR>--4 Purchase-price (of a<BR>girl); money given to the parents<BR>of a bride; पीडिवो दुंहितृशुल्कसंस्थया<BR>R. 11. 38; न कन्याया पिता विद्वान्<BR>गृह्णीयाच्छुल्कमण्वपि Ms. 3. 51, 8. 204,<BR>9. 93, 98.<BR>--5 A nuptial present.<BR>--6<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">Page1051-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Marriage settlement or dowry.<BR>--7<BR>Present given by the bride-groom<BR>to his bride.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडनं<BR>defrauding (government) of its due<BR>revenue.<BR>--ग्राहक, --ग्राहिन् m. a<BR>toll-collector.<BR>--दः {1} the giver of a<BR>nuptial present. {2} an affianced suitor.<BR>--शाला --स्थानं a toll-station,<BR>customhouse^2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्कं|शुल्क|शुल्कः
शुल्कः, --ल्कं [शुल्क्यते अतिसृज्यते<BR>कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>1 A toll, tax, customs,<BR>duty; particularly^1 levied at ferries,<BR>passes, roads &c.; कः सुधीः<BR>संत्यजेद्रांडं शुल्कस्यैवातिसाध्वसात् H. 3. 125;<BR>Ms. 8. 159; Y. 2. 47.<BR>--2 Gain,<BR>profit.<BR>--3 Money advanced to ratify a<BR>bargain.<BR>--4 Purchase-price (of a<BR>girl); money given to the parents<BR>of a bride; पीडिवो दुंहितृशुल्कसंस्थया<BR>R. 11. 38; न कन्याया पिता विद्वान्<BR>गृह्णीयाच्छुल्कमण्वपि Ms. 3. 51, 8. 204,<BR>9. 93, 98.<BR>--5 A nuptial present.<BR>--6<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">Page1051-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Marriage settlement or dowry.<BR>--7<BR>Present given by the bride-groom<BR>to his bride.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडनं<BR>defrauding (government) of its due<BR>revenue.<BR>--ग्राहक, --ग्राहिन् m. a<BR>toll-collector.<BR>--दः {1} the giver of a<BR>nuptial present. {2} an affianced suitor.<BR>--शाला --स्थानं a toll-station,<BR>customhouse^2.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR>[2] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्लं|शुल्ल
शुल्लं<BR>1 A cord, rope, string.<BR>--2<BR>Copper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्व्
शुल्व्(ल्ब्) {c10c} U.<BR>(शुल्व-ल्ब-यति-ते)<BR>1 To give, bestow.<BR>--2 To send<BR>away, dismiss.<BR>--3 To measure.<BR>--4<BR>To create, produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्ब्
शुल्व्(ल्ब्) {c10c} U.<BR>(शुल्व-ल्ब-यति-ते)<BR>1 To give, bestow.<BR>--2 To send<BR>away, dismiss.<BR>--3 To measure.<BR>--4<BR>To create, produce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुल्वं|शुल्व
शुल्वं (ल्बं) [शुला-अच्]<BR>1 A rope,<BR>string.<BR>--2 Copper.<BR>--3 A sacrifical<BR>rite or act.<BR>--4 The proximity of<BR>water, a place near it.<BR>--5 A rule,<BR>law, an institute.<BR>--ल्वा, --ल्वी See<BR>above.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः sulphur.<BR>--जं brass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

