शुश्रूषक|शुश्रूषकः
शुश्रूषक a. Attentive, obedient.<BR>--कः A servant, an attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषणं|शुश्रूषण
शुश्रूषणं, --णा [श्रु-सन् ल्युट]<BR>1<BR>Desire to hear.<BR>--2 Service, attendance.<BR>--3 Obedience, dutifulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषणा
शुश्रूषणं, --णा [श्रु-सन् ल्युट]<BR>1<BR>Desire to hear.<BR>--2 Service, attendance.<BR>--3 Obedience, dutifulness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषा
शुश्रूषा<BR>1 Desire to hear; अत एव<BR>शुश्रूषा मां मुखरयति Mu. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Service, attendance.<BR>--3 Dutifulness,<BR>obedience.<BR>--4 Reverence.<BR>--5<BR>Telling, saying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुश्रूषु
शुश्रूषु a.<BR>1 Desirous to hear.<BR>--2<BR>Desirous of serving or attending.<BR>--3<BR>Obedient, attentive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्
शुष् {c4c} P. (शुष्यति, शुष्क)<BR>1 To be<BR>dried, become dry or parched up;<BR>तृषा शुष्यत्यास्ये पिबति सलिलं स्वादु<BR>सुरभि Bh. 3. 92.<BR>--2 to be withered.<BR>--3<BR>To languish, become emaciated;<BR>Pt. 1. 49.<BR>--4 To be afflicted or<BR>distressed. --Caus. (शोषयति-ते)<BR>1 To dry<BR>up, wither, parch; न शोषयति मारुतः<BR>Bg. 2. 23.<BR>--2 To emaciate.<BR>--3 To<BR>destroy.<BR>--4 To extinguish.<BR>--5 To<BR>drain, suck up, absorb.<BR>--6 To<BR>exhaust, empty. --WITH उद --परि<BR>1<BR>to be dried up, dry up; Bk. 10. 41;<BR>Bg. 1. 29.<BR>--2 to pine, decay, wither.<BR>-वि, -सं to be dried up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषः|शुष
शुषः, --शुषी<BR>1 Drying, drying up.<BR>--2 A hole in the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषी
शुषः, --शुषी<BR>1 Drying, drying up.<BR>--2 A hole in the ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिः|शुषि
शुषिः f.<BR>1 Drying up.<BR>--2 A hole.<BR>--3 The hollow in the fang of a<BR>snake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1051-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिर|शुषिरं|शुषिरः
शुषिर a. [शुष् किरच्] Full of<BR>holes, perforated.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Fire.<BR>--2 A<BR>rat or mouse.<BR>--रं<BR>1 A hole.<BR>--2 The<BR>atmosphere.<BR>--3 A<BR>wind-instrument.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिरा
शुषिरा<BR>1 A river.<BR>--2 A sort of<BR>perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुषिलः|शुषिल
शुषिलः Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्क|शुष्कः
शुष्क p. p. [शुष्-क्त]<BR>1 Dry,<BR>dried up; शाखायां शुष्कं करिष्यामि<BR>Mk. 8.<BR>--2 Parched up, sear.<BR>--3<BR>Shrivelled, shrunk up, emaciated.<BR>--4<BR>Feigned, pretended, mock; कामिनः<BR>स्म कुरुते करभोरूर्हारि शुष्करुदितं च<BR>सुखेऽपि Śi. 10. 69.<BR>--5 Empty, vain,<BR>useless, unproductive; M. 2.<BR>--6<BR>Groundless, causeless.<BR>--7 Offensive,<BR>harsh; तस्मै नाकुशलं ब्रूयान्न शुष्कां<BR>गिरमीरयेत् Ms. 11. 35.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. emaciated.<BR>--(गी) a lizard.<BR>--अन्नं rice in the husk.<BR>--आर्द्रं dry<BR>ginger.<BR>--कलहः {1} a vain or<BR>groundless quarrel. {2} a mock quarrel;<BR>Mu. 3.<BR>--वैरं groundless enmity.<BR>--व्रणं a<BR>healed wound, scar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कलः|शुष्कल|शुष्कलं
शुष्कलः, --लं<BR>1 Dried flesh.<BR>--2<BR>Flesh in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्कलं|शुष्कल|शुष्कलः
शुष्कलः, --लं<BR>1 Dried flesh.<BR>--2<BR>Flesh in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्णः|शुष्ण
शुष्णः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मः|शुष्म|शुष्मं
शुष्मः [शुष् --मन् किच्च]<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 Fire.<BR>--3 Air, wind.<BR>--4 A bird.<BR>--ष्मं<BR>1 Prowess, strength.<BR>--2 Light,<BR>lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मन्
शुष्मन् m.<BR>1 Fire; Śi. 14. 22.<BR>--2<BR>The Citraka tree. --n.<BR>1 Strength,<BR>prowess.<BR>--2 Light, lustre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुष्मिन्
शुष्मिन् a.<BR>1 Powerful, strong.<BR>--2<BR>Fiery, high-mettled (as a horse)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकः|शूक|शूकं
शूकः, --कं<BR>1 The awn of barley<BR>&c., beard.<BR>--2 A bristle; वृतं च<BR>खलु शूकैः Bv. 1. 24.<BR>--3 Point, tip,<BR>sharp end.<BR>--4 Tenderness,<BR>compassion.<BR>--5 A kind of poisonous<BR>insect.<BR>--6 The bristle or sharp hair<BR>of insects.<BR>--का A cowach.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीटः, --कीटकः a kind of insect or<BR>worm covered with bristles.<BR>--धान्यं<BR>any awned grain, (as barely).<BR>--पिंडिः, --डी, --शिंबा, --शिंबिका, --शिंबी<BR>cowach (कपिकच्छु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकं|शूक|शूकः
शूकः, --कं<BR>1 The awn of barley<BR>&c., beard.<BR>--2 A bristle; वृतं च<BR>खलु शूकैः Bv. 1. 24.<BR>--3 Point, tip,<BR>sharp end.<BR>--4 Tenderness,<BR>compassion.<BR>--5 A kind of poisonous<BR>insect.<BR>--6 The bristle or sharp hair<BR>of insects.<BR>--का A cowach.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीटः, --कीटकः a kind of insect or<BR>worm covered with bristles.<BR>--धान्यं<BR>any awned grain, (as barely).<BR>--पिंडिः, --डी, --शिंबा, --शिंबिका, --शिंबी<BR>cowach (कपिकच्छु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूककः|शूकक
शूककः<BR>1 A kind of grain.<BR>--2<BR>Tenderness, compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकवत्|शूकवन्त्
शूकवत्, शूकिन् a. Awned, bearded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकिन्
शूकवत्, शूकिन् a. Awned, bearded.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकरः|शूकर
शूकरः A hog; गच्छ शूकर भद्रं ते<BR>वद सिंहो मया हतः । पंडिता एव जानंति<BR>सिंहशूकरयोर्बलम् Subhāṣ.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इष्टः a kind of grass (मुस्ता).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूकलः|शूकल
शूकलः A restive horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूतिः|शूति
शूतिः f. Growing, increasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रः|शूद्र
शूद्रः [शुच्-रक् पृषो˚ चस्य दः दीर्घः<BR>Uṇ. 2. 19] A man of the fourth<BR>or the last of the four principal<BR>tribes of the Hindus; he is said<BR>to have been born from the feet of<BR>Puruṣa; पद्भ्यां शूद्रो अजायत<BR>Rv. 10. 90. 12, or of Brahman;<BR>Ms. 1. 87, and his principal business<BR>was to serve the three higher castes;<BR>cf. Ms. 1. 91.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आर्ता<BR>the Priyaṅgu plant.<BR>--अह्निकं the<BR>daily ceremonies or observances of<BR>a Śūdra.<BR>--उदकं water polluted by<BR>the touch of a Śūdra.<BR>--कृत्यं, --धर्मः<BR>the duties of a Śūdra.<BR>--प्रियः an<BR>onion.<BR>--प्रेष्यः a man of any of<BR>the three higher castes who has<BR>become a servant to a Śūdra.<BR>--भूयिष्ठ a. consisting mostly of<BR>Śūdras.<BR>--याजकः one who conducts<BR>a sacrifice for a Śūdra.<BR>--वर्गः the<BR>Śūdra or servile class.<BR>--सेवनं<BR>serving a Śūdra, being the servant of<BR>a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रा
शूद्रा A woman of the Śūdra tribe.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भार्यः one who has a<BR>Śūdra woman for his wife.<BR>--वेदनं<BR>marrying a Śūdra woman.<BR>--सुतः<BR>the son of a Śūdra woman. (the<BR>father being of any caste).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्राणी
शूद्राणी, शूद्री The wife of a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्री
शूद्राणी, शूद्री The wife of a Śūdra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूद्रकः|शूद्रक
शूद्रकः N of a king, the reputed<BR>author of the Mṛcchakaṭikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून|शूनः
शून p. p. [श्वि-क्त]<BR>1 Swollen.<BR>--2 Increased, grown, prospered.<BR>--3<BR>Morbidly swollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूना
शूना [श्वि अधिकरणे --क्त संप्र० दीर्घः<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 The soft palate, uvula.<BR>--2<BR>A slaughter house in general.<BR>--3<BR>Anything (such as a piece of<BR>household furniture), whereby<BR>life is likely to be<BR>destroyed; (these are five; a fire place,<BR>a grind-stone, a broom, a mortar,<BR>and a water-pot; पंच शूना गृहस्थस्य चुल्ली<BR>पेषण्युपस्करः । कंडनी चोदकुंभश्च वध्यते यास्तु<BR>वाहयन् Ms. 3. 68.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्य|शून्यं|शून्यः
शून्य a. [शूनायै प्राणिवधाय हिंतं<BR>रहस्यस्थानत्वात् यत् Tv.]<BR>1 Empty, void^1.<BR>--2 Vacant (applied also to the heart,<BR>glances &c.), absent, listless;<BR>गमनमलसं शून्या दृष्टिः Māl. 1. 17; see<BR>शून्यहृदय below.<BR>--3 Non-existent.<BR>--4<BR>Lonely, desolate, secluded,<BR>deserted; शून्येषु शूरा न के K. P. 7;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-c" target="_blank">Page1052-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Bk. 6. 9; शून्यं मन्ये जगदविरतज्वालमंतर्ज्वलामि<BR>U. 3. 38; Māl. 9. 20.<BR>--5 Dejected,<BR>downcast, dispirited; शून्या जगाम<BR>भवनाभिमुखी कथंचित Ku. 3. 75;<BR>Ki. 17. 39<BR>--6 Utterly devoid or<BR>deprived of, without, wanting in (with<BR>instr. or in comp.); अंगुलयिकशून्या<BR>मे अंगुलि; Ś. 5; दया˚, ज्ञान˚, &c.<BR>--7<BR>Indifferent.<BR>--8 Guileless.<BR>--9<BR>Nonsensical, unmeaning; Śi. 11. 4.<BR>--10<BR>Bare, naked.<BR>--न्यं<BR>1 A vacuum, void,<BR>blank.<BR>--2 The sky, space,<BR>atmosphere.<BR>--3 A cipher, dot.<BR>--4<BR>Non-entity, (absolute) non-existence;<BR>दूषणशून्यबिंदवः N. 1. 21.<BR>--5 N. of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पदवी the passage<BR>of the soul.<BR>--मध्यः a hollow<BR>reed.<BR>--मनस्, --मनस्क a.<BR>absent-minded, listless.<BR>--मुख, --वदन a. with a<BR>blank face, with a downcast<BR>countenance.<BR>--वादः the doctrine of the<BR>non-existence of anything, the<BR>doctrine of a Buddhist sect.<BR>--वादिन्<BR>m. {1} an atheist. {2} a Buddhist.<BR>--हृदय a. {1} absent-minded; V. 2;<BR>Ś. 4. {2} open-hearted, unsuspecting.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20221222. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/1003. note: cf. AP57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शून्या
शून्या<BR>1 A hollow reed.<BR>--2 A<BR>barren woman.<BR>--3 The prickly pear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्
शूर् {c10c} U. (शूरयति-ते)<BR>1 To act<BR>the hero, be powerful.<BR>--2 To make<BR>vigorous exertions; see शुर् also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर|शूरः
शूर a. [शूर्-अच्] Brave, heroic,<BR>valiant, mighty; शून्येषु शूरा न के<BR>K. P. 7.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A hero, warrior, valiant<BR>man.<BR>--2 A lion.<BR>--3 A boar.<BR>--4 The<BR>sun.<BR>--5 The Śāla tree.<BR>--6 N. of a<BR>Yādava, the grandfather of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--7 The Arka plant.<BR>--8 The Citraka<BR>tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कीटः a contemptible<BR>warrior; Mv. 6. 32.<BR>--मानं arrogance,<BR>vaunting.<BR>--मानिन् m. a boaster,<BR>braggart.<BR>--संन m. pl. N. of the<BR>country about Mathurā or the<BR>inhabitants of that country; R. 6. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरणः|शूरण
शूरणः [शूर्-ल्यु] A kind of esculent<BR>root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूरंमन्य|शूरम्मन्य
शूरंमन्य a. One who fancies<BR>himself to be a hero.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्प्
शूर्प् {c10c} U. (शूर्पयति-ते) To<BR>measure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्पः|शूर्प|शूर्पं|शूर्प्प
शूर्पः --र्पं A winnowing-basket.<BR>--र्पः<BR>A measure of two Droṇas.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्णः an elephant.<BR>--णखा (for<BR>नखा) ‘having fingernails like<BR>winnowing-baskets’, N. of a sister of<BR>Rāvaṇa. [She was attracted by the beauty<BR>of Rāma, and solicited him to marry<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">Page1053-a+ 58</a>]<BR>her. But he said that as he had already<BR>got a wife she had better go to<BR>Lakṣmaṇa and try him. But he too rejected<BR>her, and back she came to Rāma. This<BR>circumstance excited Sītā's laughter,<BR>and the revengeful demoness, feeling<BR>herself grossly insulted, assumed a<BR>hideous form and threatened to eat her up.<BR>But Lakṣmaṇa cut off her ears and<BR>nose, and thus doubly deformed her; see<BR>R. 12. 32-40].<BR>--वातः wind produced<BR>by shaking a winnowing-basket.<BR>--श्रुतिः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्पं|शूर्प|शूर्पः|शूर्प्प
शूर्पः --र्पं A winnowing-basket.<BR>--र्पः<BR>A measure of two Droṇas.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्णः an elephant.<BR>--णखा (for<BR>नखा) ‘having fingernails like<BR>winnowing-baskets’, N. of a sister of<BR>Rāvaṇa. [She was attracted by the beauty<BR>of Rāma, and solicited him to marry<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">Page1053-a+ 58</a>]<BR>her. But he said that as he had already<BR>got a wife she had better go to<BR>Lakṣmaṇa and try him. But he too rejected<BR>her, and back she came to Rāma. This<BR>circumstance excited Sītā's laughter,<BR>and the revengeful demoness, feeling<BR>herself grossly insulted, assumed a<BR>hideous form and threatened to eat her up.<BR>But Lakṣmaṇa cut off her ears and<BR>nose, and thus doubly deformed her; see<BR>R. 12. 32-40].<BR>--वातः wind produced<BR>by shaking a winnowing-basket.<BR>--श्रुतिः an elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1052-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्पी
शूर्पी^1<BR>1 A small winnowing-basket<BR>or fan.<BR>--2 N. of Śūrpaṇakhā.<BR>--3 A<BR>toy for children.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: print unclear; cf AP; N. of Śūrpaṇakhā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्मः|शूर्म|शूर्म्म|शूर्म्मः
शूर्मः, शूर्मिः m. f., शूर्मिका, शूर्मी<BR>1 An<BR>iron-image.<BR>--2 An anvil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूर्मिः|शूर्मि|शूर्म्मि|शूर्म्मिः
शूर्मः, शूर्मिः m. f., शूर्मिका, शूर्मी<BR>1 An<BR>iron-image.<BR>--2 An anvil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल्
शूल् {c1c} P. (शूलति)<BR>1 To be ill.<BR>--2 To make a loud noise.<BR>--3 To<BR>make ill, disorder.<BR>--4 To pierce,<BR>impale.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलः|शूल|शूलं
शूलः --लं [शूल्-क]<BR>1 A sharp or<BR>pointed weapon, pike, dart, spear,<BR>lance.<BR>--2 The trident of Śiva.<BR>--3<BR>An iron-spit (for roasting meat<BR>upon); शूले संस्कृतं शूल्यम्; cf. अयः शूल.<BR>--4 A stake for impaling criminals;<BR>(बिभ्रत्) स्कंधेन शूलं हृदयेन शोकं<BR>Mk. 10. 21, Ku. 5. 73.<BR>--5 Any acute or<BR>sharp pain.<BR>--6 Colic.<BR>--7 Gout,<BR>rheumatism.<BR>--8 Death.<BR>--9 A banner,<BR>an ensign. (शूलाकृ ‘to roast on an<BR>iron-spit’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रं the point<BR>of a pike.<BR>--ग्रंथिः f. a kind of Dūrvā<BR>grass.<BR>--घातनं iron-filings.<BR>--घ्न a.<BR>sedative, anodyne.<BR>--द्विष् m. asa<BR>fœtida.<BR>--धन्वन्, --धर, --धारिन्,<BR>--धृक्, --पाणि, --भृत् m. epithets of<BR>Śiva; अधिगतधवलिम्नः<BR>शूलपाणेरभिख्यां Śi. 4. 65; R. 2. 38.<BR>--नाशनं<BR>white sochal salt.<BR>--शत्रुः the<BR>castor-oil plant.<BR>--स्थ a. impaled.<BR>--हंत्री a kind of barley.<BR>--हस्तः a<BR>lancer.<BR>--हृत् m. asa Fœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलं|शूल|शूलः
शूलः --लं [शूल्-क]<BR>1 A sharp or<BR>pointed weapon, pike, dart, spear,<BR>lance.<BR>--2 The trident of Śiva.<BR>--3<BR>An iron-spit (for roasting meat<BR>upon); शूले संस्कृतं शूल्यम्; cf. अयः शूल.<BR>--4 A stake for impaling criminals;<BR>(बिभ्रत्) स्कंधेन शूलं हृदयेन शोकं<BR>Mk. 10. 21, Ku. 5. 73.<BR>--5 Any acute or<BR>sharp pain.<BR>--6 Colic.<BR>--7 Gout,<BR>rheumatism.<BR>--8 Death.<BR>--9 A banner,<BR>an ensign. (शूलाकृ ‘to roast on an<BR>iron-spit’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्रं the point<BR>of a pike.<BR>--ग्रंथिः f. a kind of Dūrvā<BR>grass.<BR>--घातनं iron-filings.<BR>--घ्न a.<BR>sedative, anodyne.<BR>--द्विष् m. asa<BR>fœtida.<BR>--धन्वन्, --धर, --धारिन्,<BR>--धृक्, --पाणि, --भृत् m. epithets of<BR>Śiva; अधिगतधवलिम्नः<BR>शूलपाणेरभिख्यां Śi. 4. 65; R. 2. 38.<BR>--नाशनं<BR>white sochal salt.<BR>--शत्रुः the<BR>castor-oil plant.<BR>--स्थ a. impaled.<BR>--हंत्री a kind of barley.<BR>--हस्तः a<BR>lancer.<BR>--हृत् m. asa Fœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलकः|शूलक
शूलकः A restive horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूला
शूला<BR>1 A stake for impaling<BR>criminals.<BR>--2 A harlot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलाकृतं|शूलाकृत
शूलाकृतं Roasted meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिक|शूलिकं|शूलिकः
शूलिक a. [शूल-ठन्]<BR>1 Having a<BR>pike.<BR>--2 Roasted on a spit.<BR>--कः<BR>A hare.<BR>--कं Roasted meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिन्
शूलिन् a. [शूलमस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>1<BR>Armed with a spear; दुर्जयो लवणः शूली<BR>R. 15. 5.<BR>--2 Suffering from colic.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A spearman.<BR>--2 A hare.<BR>--3<BR>N. of Śiva; कुर्वन्संध्याबलिपटहतां<BR>शूलिनः श्लाघनीयां Me. 34; Ku. 3. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूलिनः|शूलिन
शूलिनः The(Indian) fig-tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूल्य|शूल्यं
शूल्य a. [शूले संस्कृतं यत्]<BR>1<BR>Roasted on a spit; शूल्यमांसभूयिष्ठ<BR>आहारोऽश्यते Ś. 2.<BR>--2 Deserving<BR>impalement.<BR>--ल्यं Roasted meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शूष्
शूष् {c1c} P. (शूषति)<BR>1 To produce,<BR>beget.<BR>--2 To bring forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृकालः|शृकाल
शृकालः A jackal; see शृगाल<BR>below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालः|शृगाल
शृगालः [असृजं लाति ला-क पृषो०]<BR>1 A jackal.<BR>--2 A cheat, rogue,<BR>swindler.<BR>--3 A coward.<BR>--4<BR>An ill-natured man, one using<BR>harsh words.<BR>--5 N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केलिः a kind of jujube.<BR>--जंबुः --बूः f. a kind of cucumber.<BR>--योनिः birth in a future life as a<BR>jackal.<BR>--रूपः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगालिका
शृगालिका, शृगाली<BR>1 A female<BR>jackal.<BR>--2 A fox.<BR>--3 Flight, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृगाली
शृगालिका, शृगाली<BR>1 A female<BR>jackal.<BR>--2 A fox.<BR>--3 Flight, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंखलः|शृङ्खल|शृंखल|शृंखलं|शृङ्खलः
शृंखलः --ला --लं [शृंगात् प्राधान्यात्<BR>स्खल्यते अमेन पृषो० Tv.]<BR>1 An<BR>ironchain, fetter.<BR>--2 A chain, fetter in<BR>general (fig. also); Bk. 9. 90;<BR>लीलाकटाक्षमालाशृंखलाभिः Dk.;<BR>संसारवासनाबद्धशृंखलां Gīt. 3.<BR>--3 A chain<BR>for tying the feet of an elephant;<BR>स्तंबेरमा मुखरशृंखलकर्षिणस्ते R. 5. 72;<BR>Ki. 7. 31.<BR>--4 A chain or belt worn<BR>round the waist.<BR>--5 A measuring<BR>chain.<BR>--6 A chain, series,<BR>succession.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--यमकं a variety of<BR>Yamaka; see Ki. 15. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंखला
