शृंखलं|शृङ्खल|शृंखल|शृंखलः|शृङ्खलः
शृंखलः --ला --लं [शृंगात् प्राधान्यात्<BR>स्खल्यते अमेन पृषो० Tv.]<BR>1 An<BR>ironchain, fetter.<BR>--2 A chain, fetter in<BR>general (fig. also); Bk. 9. 90;<BR>लीलाकटाक्षमालाशृंखलाभिः Dk.;<BR>संसारवासनाबद्धशृंखलां Gīt. 3.<BR>--3 A chain<BR>for tying the feet of an elephant;<BR>स्तंबेरमा मुखरशृंखलकर्षिणस्ते R. 5. 72;<BR>Ki. 7. 31.<BR>--4 A chain or belt worn<BR>round the waist.<BR>--5 A measuring<BR>chain.<BR>--6 A chain, series,<BR>succession.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--यमकं a variety of<BR>Yamaka; see Ki. 15. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंखलकः|शृङ्खलक|शृंखलक|शृङ्खलकः
शृंखलकः<BR>1 A chain.<BR>--2 A camel<BR>in general.<BR>--3 An animal with clogs<BR>on his feet (to prevent him from<BR>straying).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंखलित|शृङ्खलित|शृङ्खलितः
शृंखलित a. Chained, fettered,<BR>bound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगं|शृङ्ग|शृंग|शृङ्गं|शृङ्गः
शृंगं [शॄ-गन् पृषो˚ मुम् थस्वश्च<BR>Uṇ. 1. 123]<BR>1 A horn वन्यैरिदानीं<BR>महिषैस्तदंभः शृंगाहतं क्रोशति दीर्घिकाणां<BR>R. 16. 13; गाहतां महिषां निपानसलिलं<BR>शृंगैर्नुहुस्ताडितं Ś. 2. 6.<BR>--2 The top or<BR>summit of a mountain; अद्रेः शृंगं<BR>हरति पवनः किं स्विदित्युन्मुखीभिः Me. 14,<BR>52; Ki. 5. 42; R. 13. 26.<BR>--3 The<BR>top of a building, turret.<BR>--4<BR>Elevation, height.<BR>--5 Lordship,<BR>sovereignty, supremacy; eminence;<BR>शृंगं स दृप्तविनयाधिकृतः परेषामत्युच्छ्रित<BR>न ममृषे न तु दीर्घमायुः R. 9. 62 (where<BR>the word means a ‘horn’ also).<BR>--6<BR>A cusp or horn of the moon.<BR>--7<BR>Any peak, point or projection in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-c" target="_blank">Page1053-c+ 57</a>]<BR>general.<BR>--8 A horn (of a buffalo<BR>&c.) used for blowing.<BR>--9 A<BR>syringe; वर्णेदैकः कांचनशृंगमुक्तैः<BR>R. 16. 70.<BR>--10 Excess of love,<BR>rising of desire.<BR>--11 A mark, sign.<BR>--12 A lotus.<BR>--13 A fountain of<BR>water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरं space or<BR>interval between the horns (of a<BR>cow &c.).<BR>--उच्चयः a lofty summit.<BR>--जः an arrow.<BR>--(जं) aloe-wood.<BR>--प्रहारिन् a. butting.<BR>--प्रियः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--मोहिन् m. the<BR>Campaka tree.<BR>--वेरं {1} N. of a<BR>town on the Ganges near the<BR>modern Mirzāpura; U. 1. 21. {2}<BR>ginger.<BR>--वेरकं ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगकः|शृङ्गक|शृंगक|शृंगकं|शृङ्गकः
शृंगकः --कं<BR>1 A horn.<BR>--2 A horn<BR>of the moon.<BR>--3 Any pointed<BR>thing.<BR>--4 A syringe; Ratn. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगकं|शृङ्गक|शृंगक|शृंगकः|शृङ्गकः
शृंगकः --कं<BR>1 A horn.<BR>--2 A horn<BR>of the moon.<BR>--3 Any pointed<BR>thing.<BR>--4 A syringe; Ratn. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगवत्|शृङ्गवत्|शृङ्गवन्त्
शृंगवत् a. Peaked. --m. A<BR>mountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगाटः|शृङ्गाट|शृंगाट|शृङ्गाटं|शृङ्गाटः
शृंगाटः<BR>1 N. of a mountain.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a plant.<BR>--टं A place where<BR>four roads meet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगाटकः|शृङ्गाटक|शृंगाटक|शृङ्गाटकं|शृङ्गाटकः
शृंगाटकः A mountain with three<BR>peaks.<BR>--कं<BR>1 A place where four<BR>roads meet.<BR>--2 A kind of pastry.<BR>--3 A door.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगारः|शृङ्गार|शृंगार|शृङ्गारं|शृङ्गारः
शृंगारः [शृंगं कामोद्रेकमृच्छत्यनेन<BR>ऋअण्]<BR>1 The sentiment of love or<BR>sexual passion, the erotic<BR>sentiment (the first of the eight or<BR>nine sentiments in poetical<BR>compositions; it is of two kinds:<BR>--संमोगशृंगार and बिप्रलंभशृंगार q.q. v.v.);<BR>शृंगारः सखि मूर्तिमानिव मधौ मुग्धो<BR>हरिः क्रीडति Gīt. 1; (it is thus<BR>defined: --पुंसः स्त्रियां स्त्रियाः पुंसि<BR>संभोगं प्रति या स्पृहा । स शृंगार इति ख्यातः<BR>क्रीडारत्यादिकारकः ॥ see S. D. 210<BR>also).<BR>--2 Love, passion, sexual<BR>love; V. 1. 8.<BR>--3 A dress suited<BR>to amorous interviews, an elegant<BR>dress.<BR>--4 Coition, sexual union.<BR>--5 Marks made with red-lead on<BR>the body of an elephant.<BR>--6 A<BR>mark in general.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Cloves.<BR>--2<BR>Red-lead.<BR>--3 Undried ginger.<BR>--4<BR>A fragrant powder for the dress or<BR>body.<BR>--5 Agallochum.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चेष्टा an amorous or love-gesture;<BR>शृंगारचेष्टा विविधा बभूबुः R. 6. 12.<BR>--भाषितं amorous talk.<BR>--भूषणं<BR>redlead.<BR>--योनिः an epithet of the god<BR>of love.<BR>--रसः the sentiment of<BR>love.<BR>--विधिः --वेशः a dress suited<BR>to amorous interviews and other<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">Page1054-a+ 56</a>]<BR>purposes.<BR>--सहायः an assistant in<BR>love-affairs, a confidant of the hero<BR>of a play; cf. नर्मसचिव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1053-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगारकः|शृङ्गारक|शृङ्गारकं|शृङ्गारकः
शृंगारकः Love.<BR>--कं Red-lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगारित|शृङ्गारित
शृंगारित a.<BR>1 Impassioned, affected<BR>by love.<BR>--2 Reddened.<BR>--3<BR>Adorned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगारिन्|शृङ्गारिन्
शृंगारिन् a.<BR>1 Amorous,<BR>impassioned, enamoured,<BR>--2 Relating to love.<BR>--3 Stained with red-lead. --m.<BR>1<BR>An impassioned lover.<BR>--2 A ruby.<BR>--3 An elephant.<BR>--4 Dress,<BR>decoration.<BR>--5 The betel-nut tree.<BR>--6 A<BR>preparation of betel-leaves and<BR>pieces of areca-nut, see तांबूल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगिः|शृङ्गि|शृंगि|शृङ्गिः
शृंगिः Gold for ornaments. --f.<BR>The sheat-fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगिकं|शृङ्गिक|शृंगिक|शृङ्गिकं
शृंगिकं A kind of poison.<BR>--का<BR>A kind of birch tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगिणः|शृङ्गिण|शृंगिण|शृङ्गिणः
शृंगिणः A ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगिणी
शृंगिणी<BR>1 A cow.<BR>--2 The Arabian<BR>jasmine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगिन्|शृङ्गिन्
शृंगिन् a. (णी f.) [शृंगमस्त्यम्य<BR>इनि]<BR>1 Horned.<BR>--2 Crested,<BR>peaked. --m.<BR>1 A mountain.<BR>--2 An<BR>elephant.<BR>--3 A ram.<BR>--4 A tree.<BR>--5 N. of Śiva.<BR>--6 N. of one of Śiva's<BR>attendants; शृणी भृंगी रिटिस्तुंडी Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृंगी|शृङ्गी
शृंगी<BR>1 Gold used for ornaments.<BR>--2 A kind of medicinal root.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of poison.<BR>--4 The sheat-fish.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कनकं gold used for<BR>ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृणिः|शृणि
शृणिः f. A hook for pricking an<BR>elephant, a goad; मदांधकरिणां<BR>दर्पोपशांत्यै शृणिः H. 2. 165.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृत|शृतं
शृत p. p.<BR>1 Cooked.<BR>--2 Boiled<BR>(water, milk &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृध्
शृध् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (but Paras. also in<BR>the Second Future, Aorist, and<BR>Conditional) (शर्धते) To break wind<BR>downwards. {vII.v} {c1c} U. (शर्धति-ते)<BR>1<BR>To moisten, wet.<BR>--2 To cut off.<BR>{vIII.v} {c10c} U. (शर्धयति ते)<BR>1 To strive.<BR>--2 To take, grasp.<BR>--3 To insult (as<BR>by breaking wind), mock, ridicule.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृद्ध
शृद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Expelled from the<BR>body (as wind).<BR>--2 Moistened,<BR>wetted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शृधुः|शृधु
शृधुः<BR>1 Intellect (बुद्धि).<BR>--2 The<BR>anus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शॄ
शॄ {c9c} P. (शृणाति, शीर्ण)<BR>1 To tear<BR>asunder, tear to pieces.<BR>--2 To hurt,<BR>injure.<BR>--3 To kill, destroy; वनाश्रयाः<BR>कस्य मृगाः परिग्रहाः शृणाति यस्तान्<BR>प्रसभेन तस्य ते Ki. 14. 13. --Pass. (<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-b" target="_blank">Page1054-b+ 55</a>]<BR>शीर्यते)<BR>1 To be shattered.<BR>--2 To wither,<BR>decay, waste away. --WITH अव or वि<BR>to seize away. (--Pass.) to fade or<BR>wither; मूर्ध्नि वा सर्वलोकस्य विशीर्येत<BR>वनेऽथवा Bh. 2. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखरः|शेखर|शेखरं
शेखरः<BR>1 A crest, chaplet, tuft,<BR>a garland of flowers worn on the<BR>head; कपालि वा स्यादथर्वेदुशेखरं<BR>Ku. 5. 78, 7. 42; नवकरनिकरेण स्पष्टबधूक<BR>सूनस्तब करचितमेते शेखरं बिभ्रतीव<BR>Śi. 11. 46, 4, 50; मग धदेशशेखरीभूता<BR>पुष्पपुरी नाम नगरी Dk.<BR>--2 A diadem,<BR>crown.<BR>--3 A peak, summit.<BR>--4 The<BR>best or most distinguished of a class<BR>(at the end of comp.).<BR>--5 A kind<BR>of Dhruva or burden of a song.<BR>--रं<BR>Cloves.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेखरित
शेखरित a. Crested, tufted, peaked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपः|शेप
शेपः, शेपस् n., शेफः --फं, शेफस् n.<BR>1 The penis.<BR>--2 A testicle.<BR>--3 A<BR>tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेपस्
शेपः, शेपस् n., शेफः --फं, शेफस् n.<BR>1 The penis.<BR>--2 A testicle.<BR>--3 A<BR>tail.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1054-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शेफालिः|शेफालि
