शैन्याः
शैन्याः (m. pl.) The descendants<BR>of Śini.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैब्य
शैब्य See शैब्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल|शैलं|शैलः
शैल a. (ली f.) [शिलाः संत्यस्य प्रज्ञा˚<BR>अण्] Rocky, craggy, stony.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A mountain, hill; शैले शैले न<BR>माणिक्यं मौक्तिकं न गजे गजे Chāṇ. 55;<BR>शैलौ मलयदर्दुरौ R. 4. 51.<BR>--2 A dike,<BR>dam.<BR>--3 A rock, big stone.<BR>--लं<BR>1<BR>Borax, benzoin.<BR>--2 Bitumen.<BR>--3 A<BR>kind of collyrium.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः<BR>N. of a country.<BR>--अग्रं the peak of a<BR>mountain.<BR>--अटः {1} a mountaineer, a<BR>barbarian. {2} an attendant on an<BR>idol. {3} a lion. {4} a crystal.<BR>--अधिपः, --अधिराजः, --इंद्रः, --पतिः, --राजः<BR>epithets of the Himālaya.<BR>--आख्यं<BR>{1} benzoin. {2} a fragrant resinous<BR>substance.<BR>--इंद्रस्थः the birch tree.<BR>--कटकः the side or slope of a<BR>mountain.<BR>--गंधं a kind of sandal.<BR>--जं {1}<BR>benzoin. {2} bitumen.<BR>--जनः a<BR>mountaineer.<BR>--जा, --तनया, --पुत्री, --सुता<BR>epithets of Pārvatī; अवाप्तः प्रागल्भ्यं<BR>परिणतरुचः शैलतनये K. P. 10;<BR>Ku. 3. 68.<BR>--धन्वन् m. an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--धरः an epithet of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--निर्यासः benzoin.<BR>--पत्रः the Bilva tree.<BR>--भित्तिः f. an instrument for cutting<BR>stones, a stone cutter's chisel.<BR>--रंध्रं<BR>a cave, cavern.<BR>--वीजं the<BR>markingnut plant.<BR>--शिबिरं the ocean.<BR>--सार<BR>a. as strong as a mountain, firm as<BR>a rock; Ki. 10. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलकं|शैलक
शैलकं<BR>1 Benzoin.<BR>--2 Bitumen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलादिः|शैलादि
शैलादिः N. of Nandin, Śiva's<BR>attendant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलालिन्
शैलालिन् m. An actor, a dancer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलिक्यः|शैलिक्य
शैलिक्यः A hypocrite, an<BR>impostor, a cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैली
शैली [शीलमेव स्वार्थे ष्यञ् ङीपि<BR>यलोपः]<BR>1 A short explanation of a<BR>grammatical aphorism.<BR>--2 A mode of<BR>expression or interpretation;<BR>प्रायेणाचार्याणामियं शैली यत्स्वाभिप्रायमपि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">Page1055-b+ 54</a>]<BR>परोपदेशपिव वर्णयंति Kull. on Ms. 1. 4;<BR>आचार्याणामियं शैली यत्सामान्येनाभिधाय<BR>विशेषेण विवृणोति.<BR>--3 Behaviour,<BR>manner of acting, conduct, course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूषः|शैलूष
शैलूषः [शिलूप्रस्य अपत्यं अण् Tv.]<BR>1 An actor, a dancer; आःशैलूषापसद<BR>Ve. 1; एते पुरुषाः सर्वमेव<BR>शैलूषजनंव्याहरंति ibid.; अवाप्य शैलूष इवैष भूमिकां<BR>Śi. 1. 69.<BR>--2 A musician, leader of a<BR>band.<BR>--3 One who beats time at a<BR>concert.<BR>--4 A rogue.<BR>--5 The Bilva<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलूषिकः|शैलूषिक
शैलूषिकः One who follows the<BR>profession of an actor.<BR>--की An actress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैलेय|शैलेयं|शैलेयः
शैलेय a. (यी f.) [शिलायां भवः<BR>ढक]<BR>1 Mountainous;<BR>शैलेयस्थलीपाषाणनिषण्णः V. 4.<BR>--2 Produced<BR>from rocks.<BR>--3 Mountain-like, hard,<BR>stony.<BR>--यः<BR>1 A lion.<BR>--2 A bee.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Benzoin; शैलेयगंधीनि<BR>शिलातलानि R. 6. 51; शैलेयनद्धेषु शिलातलेषु<BR>Ku. 1. 55.<BR>--2 Fragrant resin.<BR>--3<BR>Rock-salt.<BR>--यी N. of Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैल्य|शैल्यं
शैल्य a. (ली f.) Stony.<BR>--ल्यं<BR>Rockiness, hardness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव|शैवं|शैवः
शैव a. (वी f.) [शिवो देवताऽस्य अण्]<BR>Relating to the god Śiva.<BR>--वः<BR>1 N.<BR>of one of the three principal Hindu<BR>sects.<BR>--2 A member of the Śaiva<BR>sect.<BR>--3 The thorn-apple.<BR>--वं N. of<BR>one of the eighteen Purāṇas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवलः|शैवल|शैवलं
शैवलः [शी-वलच् Uṇ. 4. 38] A<BR>kind of aquatic plant, moss;<BR>सरसिजमनुविद्धं शैवलेनापि रम्यं Ś. 1. 20; न<BR>षट्पदश्रेणिभिरेव पंकजं सशैवलासंगमपि<BR>प्रकाशते Ku. 5. 9.<BR>--लं A kind of<BR>fragrant wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवलिनी
शैवलिनी A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैवाल|शैवालं
शैवाल See शैवल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैव्यः|शैव्य
शैव्यः<BR>1 N. of one of the four<BR>horses of Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--2 N. of a king<BR>and warrior in the Pāṇḍava army.<BR>--3 A horse (in general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशवं|शैशव
शैशवं [शिशोर्भावः अण्] Childhood,<BR>infancy (period under sixteen);<BR>शैशवात्प्रभृति पाषितां प्रिया U. 1. 45;<BR>शैशवेऽभ्यस्तविद्यानां R. 1. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैशिर|शैशिरः
शैशिर a. (री f.) [शिशिर-अण्]<BR>Belonging to the cold or dewy<BR>season.<BR>--रः A black kind of the<BR>Cnātaka bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शैष्योपाध्यायिका
शैष्योपाध्यायिका Instruction or<BR>tuition of young pupils.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शो
शो {c4c} P. (श्यति, शात or शित, pass.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">Page1055-c+ 56</a>]<BR>शायते; caus. शाययति; desid. शिशासातं)<BR>1 To sharpen, whet.<BR>--2 To make<BR>thin, attenuate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकः|शोक
शोकः [शुच्-घञ्] Sorrow, grief,<BR>distress, affliction, lamentation,<BR>wailing, deep anguish; श्लाकत्वमापद्यत<BR>यस्य शोकः R. 14. 70.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः,<BR>--अनलः the fire of grief.<BR>--अपनोदः<BR>removal of grief.<BR>--अभिभूत.<BR>--आकुल,<BR>--आविष्ट, --उपहत, --विह्वल a. afflicted or<BR>agonized by grief.<BR>--अरिः the<BR>Kadamba tree.<BR>--कर्षित a. afflicted or<BR>agonized with grief.<BR>--चर्वा<BR>indulgence in grief.<BR>--नाशः the Aśoka<BR>tree.<BR>--परायण, --लासक a. engrossed<BR>in grief, wholly given up to grief.<BR>--विकल a. overwhelmed with grief.<BR>--स्थानं any cause of sorrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोकिन्
शोकिन् a. Sorrowful, dejected,<BR>sad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचक
शोचक a. Distressing, afflicting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचनं|शोचन
शोचनं Grief, sorrow, lamentation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचनीय
शोचनीय a. Lamentable, deplorable,<BR>mournful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोच्य
शोच्य a.<BR>1 To be lamented or<BR>mourned. deplorable, pitiable;<BR>Ś. 3. 10.<BR>--2 Vile, wicked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोचिस्
शोचिस् n. [शुच्-इसि]<BR>1 Light,<BR>lustre, radiance.<BR>--2 A flame.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--केशः (शोचिष्केशः) an epithet of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोटीर्यं|शोटीर्य|शोटीर्य्य|शोटीर्य्यं
शोटीर्यं Valour, heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोठ|शोठः
शोठ a. [शुठ्-अच्]<BR>1 Foolish.<BR>--2 Low, wicked.<BR>--3 Idle, lazy.<BR>--ठः<BR>1 A fool.<BR>--2 An idler, sluggard.<BR>--3<BR>A low or wicked man.<BR>--4 A rogue,<BR>cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण्
शोण् {c1c} P. (शोणति)<BR>1 To go,<BR>move.<BR>--2 To become red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोण|शोणं|शोणः
शोण a. (णा or णी f.) [शोण्-अच्]<BR>1 Red, crimson, tinged red;<BR>स्त्यानावनद्धघतशोणितशोणपाणिरुत्तंसयिष्यति<BR>कचांस्तव देवि भीमः Ve. 1. 21;<BR>आस्वादितद्वि दशोणि तशोणशोभां Mu. 1. 8;<BR>Ku. 1. 7.<BR>--2 Bay, reddish-brown.<BR>--3 Yellow.<BR>--णः<BR>1 Crimson, the red colour.<BR>--2<BR>Fire<BR>--3 A kind of red sugar-cane.<BR>--4<BR>A bay horse.<BR>--5 N. of a male river,<BR>rising in Goṇḍavana and falling<BR>into the Ganges near Pātaliputra<BR>q. v.; प्रत्यग्रहीत्पार्थिववाहिनीं तां<BR>भागीरथीं शोण इवोत्तरंगः R. 7. 36.<BR>--6<BR>The planet Mars; cf. लोहित.<BR>--णं<BR>1<BR>Blood.<BR>--2 Red lead.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंबुः<BR>N. of a cloud which is said to rise<BR>at the destruction of the world.<BR>--अश्मन् m.,<BR>--उपलः {1} a red stone.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">Page1056-a+ 56</a>]<BR>{2} a ruby.<BR>--पद्मं a red lotus.<BR>--पुष्पकः the Kovidāra tree.<BR>--रत्नं a<BR>ruby.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1055-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणित|शोणितं
शोणित a. [शोण्-इतच्] Red,<BR>purple, crimson.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Blood;<BR>उपस्थिता शोणितपारणा मे R. 2. 39;<BR>Ve. 1. 21; Mu. 1. 8.<BR>--2 Saffron.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आह्वयं saffron.<BR>--उक्षित a.<BR>bloodstained.<BR>--उपलः a ruby.<BR>--चंदनं<BR>red sandal.<BR>--प a. blood-sucking.<BR>--पारणा a meal of blood or<BR>fleshmeat.<BR>--पुरं N. of the city of the<BR>demon Bāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोणिमन्
शोणिमन् m. Redness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोथः|शोथ
शोथः [Uṇ. 2. 4] Swelling,<BR>intumescence.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--घ्न, --जित् a.<BR>removing swellings, discutient.<BR>--जिह्मः<BR>hog-weed.<BR>--रोगः dropsy.<BR>--हृत् a.<BR>discutient. (--m.) the marking-nut<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधः|शोध
शोधः [शुध्-घञ्]<BR>1 Purification.<BR>--2 Correction, rectification.<BR>--3<BR>Acquittance, paying off (as of debts).<BR>--4 Retaliation, requital.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधक|शोधकः
शोधक a. (का or धिका f.) [<BR>शुध्णिच् ण्वुल्]<BR>1 Purificatory.<BR>--2<BR>Purgative.<BR>--3 Corrective.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>purifier.<BR>--2 (In arith. and alg.) The<BR>subtrahend.<BR>--कं A kind of earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधन|शोधनं|शोधनः
शोधन a. (नी f.) [शुध्-णिच्-ल्यु ल्युट्<BR>वा] Purifying, cleansing &c.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>(a) Purifying, cleansing. (b)<BR>Cleansing or washing of a wound.<BR>--2<BR>Correction, clearing away errors.<BR>--3<BR>Exact determination.<BR>--4 Payment,<BR>discharge, acquittance.<BR>--5 Expiation,<BR>atonement.<BR>--6 Refining of metals.<BR>--7 Retaliation, requital,<BR>punishment.<BR>--8 Subtraction (in math.).<BR>--9 Green vitriol.<BR>--10 Feces, ordure.<BR>--नः The lime.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधनकः|शोधनक
शोधनकः An officer in a criminal<BR>court; Mk. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधनी
शोधनी A broom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोधित|शोधितं
शोधित p. p. [शुध्-णिच्-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Purified, cleansed.<BR>--2 Refined.<BR>--3<BR>Filtered.<BR>--4 Corrected, rectified.<BR>--5 Paid<BR>off, discharged.<BR>--6 Requited,<BR>retaliated.<BR>--7 Acquitted, absolved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोध्य|शोध्यः
शोध्य a. [शुध्-णिच् ण्य] To be<BR>purified, refined, paid off &c.<BR>--ध्यः An<BR>accused person, one who has to clear<BR>himself of the charge brought<BR>against him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोफः|शोफ
शोफः [शु-फन्] Swelling,<BR>tumour, intumescence.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जित्,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">Page1056-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--हृत् m. the marking-nut plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभन|शोभनं|शोभनः
शोभन a. (नी f.) [शोभते शुभू-ल्यु]<BR>1 Shining, splendid.<BR>--2 Handsome,<BR>beautiful, lovely.<BR>--3 Good,<BR>auspicious, fortunate.<BR>--4 Richly decorated.<BR>--5 Moral, virtuous.<BR>--नः<BR>1 N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--2 A planet.<BR>--3 A burnt<BR>offering for the production of happy<BR>results.<BR>--ना<BR>1 Turmeric.<BR>--2 A<BR>beautiful or virtuous woman; तदिदं<BR>परिरक्ष शोभने भवितव्यप्रियसंगमं वपुः<BR>Ku. 4. 44.<BR>--3 A sort of yellow pigment<BR>(= गोरोचना q. v.).<BR>--नं<BR>1 Beauty,<BR>lustre, brilliance.<BR>--2 A lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभनकः|शोभनक
शोभनकः The Śobhāñjana tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभा
शोभा [शुभ्-अ]<BR>1 Light, lustre,<BR>brilliance, radiance.<BR>--2 (a) Splendour,<BR>beauty, elegance, grace, loveliness;<BR>वपुरभिनवमस्याः पुष्यति स्वां न शोभां<BR>Ś. 1. 19; Me. 52, 59. (b) Natural beauty,<BR>grandeur (as of a mountain);<BR>अद्रिशोभा R. 2. 27.<BR>--3 An ornament,<BR>graceful expression; शोभैव मंदरक्षु<BR>ब्धक्षुभितांभोधिवर्णना Śi. 2. 107.<BR>--4<BR>Turmeric.<BR>--5 A kind of pigment<BR>(= गोरोचना q. v.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजनः<BR>N. of a very useful tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभित
शोभित p. p.<BR>1 Adorned, graced,<BR>decorated.<BR>--2 Beautiful, lovely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोभिन्
शोभिन् a.<BR>1 Shining;<BR>Ku. 5. 44; R. 8. 12.<BR>--2 Beautiful, lovely,<BR>handsome.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषः|शोष
शोषः [शुष्-घञ्]<BR>1 Drying up,<BR>dryness; ह्रदशोषविक्लवां Ku. 4. 39;<BR>so आस्यशोषः, कंठशोषः &c.<BR>--2<BR>Emaciation, withering up; शरीरशोषः,<BR>कुसुमशोषः &c.<BR>--3 Pulmonary<BR>consumption or consumption in general;<BR>संशोषणाद्रसादीनां शोष इत्यभिधीयते Suśr.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संभवं the root of long<BR>pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषण|शोषणं|शोषणः
शोषण a. (णी f.) [शुष्-ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>1 Drying up, desiccating.<BR>--2<BR>Causing to wither up, emaciating;<BR>Ś. 3. 10.<BR>--णः N. of one of the<BR>arrows of Cupid.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Drying up,<BR>desiccation.<BR>--2 Suction, sucking<BR>up, absorption.<BR>--3 Exhaustion.<BR>--4<BR>Emaciation, withering up.<BR>--5 Dry<BR>ginger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषित|शोषितः
शोषित p. p.<BR>1 Dried up;<BR>शोषितसरसि निदाघे नितरामेवोद्धतः सिंधुः<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Emaciated, withered up.<BR>--3 Exhausted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शोषिन्
शोषिन् a. (णी f.) Drying up,<BR>withering, emaciating; हुदयकुसुमशोषी<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">Page1056-c+ 53</a>]<BR>दारुणो दीर्घशोकः U. 3. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौकं|शौक
शौकं A flock of parrots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तं|शौक्त
शौक्तं a. (क्ती f.) Acid, acetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तिक
शौक्तिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Relating<BR>to a pearl.<BR>--2 Acid, acetic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तिकेयं|शौक्तिकेय
शौक्तिकेयं, शौक्तेयं A pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्तेयं|शौक्तेय
शौक्तिकेयं, शौक्तेयं A pearl.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्र
शौक्र a. (क्री f.) [शुक्र-अण्]<BR>Seminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्लिकेयः|शौक्लिकेय
शौक्लिकेयः A sort of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौक्ल्यं|शौक्ल्य
शौक्ल्यं Whiteness, clearness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचं|शौच
शौचं [शुचेर्भावः अण्]<BR>1 Purity,<BR>clearness; काके शौचं द्यूतकारे च सत्यं<BR>Pt. 1. 147.<BR>--2 Purification from<BR>personal defilement caused by<BR>voiding excrement, but<BR>particularly by the death of a<BR>relative.<BR>--3 Cleansing, purifying.<BR>--4 Voiding of excrement.<BR>--5<BR>Uprightness, honesty.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचारः, --कर्मन् n.<BR>--कल्पः a purificatory<BR>rite.<BR>--कूपः a privy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचिकः|शौचिक
शौचिकः<BR>1 A cleanser.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>mixed tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौचेयः|शौचेय
शौचेयः A washerman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौट्
शौट् {c1c} P. (शौटति) To be proud<BR>or haughty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर|शौटीरः
शौटीर a. Proud, haughty.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A hero, champion.<BR>--2 A proud<BR>man.<BR>--3 An ascetic.<BR>--4 An upstart.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौटीर्यं|शौटीर्य|शौटीर्य्य|शौटीर्य्यं
शौटीर्यं<BR>1 Pride, arrogance,<BR>haughtiness.<BR>--2 Prowess, heroism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौड्
शौड् {c1c} P. (शौडति) See शौट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौंड|शौण्ड|शौण्डः
शौंड a. (डी f.) [शुंडायां सुरायां<BR>अभिरतः अण्]<BR>1 Addicted to drinking,<BR>fond of liquor.<BR>--2 Excited,<BR>intoxicated, drunk &c. (fig);<BR>अनिकृतिनिपुणं ते चेष्टितं मानशौंड Ve. 5. 21<BR>‘drunk with pride or very proud’.<BR>--3 Skilled in (with loc. or in comp.);<BR>अक्षशौंड, दानशौंड &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौंडिकः|शौण्डिक|शौंडिक|शौण्डिकः
शौंडिकः, शौंडिन् m. [शुंडा सुरा पण्यमस्य<BR>ठक् इनि वा] A distiller and seller of<BR>spirituous liquors, a vintner.<BR>--की<BR>--नी A female vintner; पयोपि<BR>शौंडिकीहस्ते वारुणीत्यभिधीयते H. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौंडिन्|शौण्डिन्
शौंडिकः, शौंडिन् m. [शुंडा सुरा पण्यमस्य<BR>ठक् इनि वा] A distiller and seller of<BR>spirituous liquors, a vintner.<BR>--की<BR>--नी A female vintner; पयोपि<BR>शौंडिकीहस्ते वारुणीत्यभिधीयते H. 3. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौंडिकेयः|शौण्डिकेय|शौंडिकेय|शौण्डिकेयः
शौंडिकेयः A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौंडी
शौंडी Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौंडीर|शौण्डीर|शौण्डीरः
शौंडीर a.<BR>1 Proud, haughty.<BR>--2<BR>Elevated, raised up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौद्धोदनिः|शौद्धोदनि
शौद्धोदनिः An epithet of<BR>Buddha, son of शुद्धोदन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौद्र|शौद्रः
शौद्र a. (द्री f.) [शूद्र-अण्]<BR>Relating to a Śūdra or his tribe.<BR>--द्रः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">Page1057-a+ 53</a>]<BR>The son of a man of any of the first<BR>three castes by a Śūdra woman; see<BR>Ms. 9. 160.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1056-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनं|शौन
शौनं Meat kept at a<BR>slaughterhouse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनकः|शौनक
शौनकः N. of a great sage, the<BR>reputed author of the Ṛgveda<BR>Prātiśākhya and various other Vedic<BR>compositions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौनिकः|शौनिक
शौनिकः [शुना प्राणिवधस्यानं<BR>प्रयोजनमस्य ठक्]<BR>1 A butcher; छद्मना<BR>परिददामि मृत्यवे शौनिको गृहशकुंतिकामिव<BR>U. 1. 5.<BR>--2 A bird-catcher, hunter.<BR>--3 Hunting, chase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभः|शौभ|शौभं
शौभः<BR>1 God, divinity.<BR>--2 The<BR>betel-nut tree.<BR>--भं The city of<BR>Hariścandra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभांजनः|शौभाञ्जन|शौभांजन|शौभाञ्जनः
शौभांजनः N. of a tree; see<BR>शोभांजन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौभिकः|शौभिक
शौभिकः<BR>1 A juggler, conjurer.<BR>--2 A hunter, fowler; इति चिंतयतो<BR>हृदये पिकस्य समधायि शौभिकेन शरः<BR>Bv. 1. 114.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौरसेनी
शौरसेनी N. of a Prākṛta<BR>dialect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौरिः|शौरि
शौरिः<BR>1 N. of Viṣṇu or<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR>--2 Of Balarāma.<BR>--3 The<BR>planet Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्प|शौर्पः|शौर्प्प
शौर्प a. (र्पी f.) Measured by<BR>or belonging to a शूर्प or<BR>winnowingbasket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौर्यं|शौर्य|शौर्य्य|शौर्य्यं
शौर्यं [शूरस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Prowess, heroism, valour; शौर्ये वैरिणि<BR>वज्रमाशु निपतत्वर्थोऽस्तु नः केवलं<BR>Bh. 2. 39; नये च शौर्ये च वसंति संपदः<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Strength, power, might.<BR>--3 Representation of war and<BR>supernatural events on the stage; cf.<BR>आरभटी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्कः|शौल्क|शौल्कं
शौल्कः, शौल्किकः [शुल्के<BR>तदादानेऽधिकृतः अण् ठक् वा] A<BR>superintendent of tolls, custom-officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्किकः|शौल्किक
शौल्कः, शौल्किकः [शुल्के<BR>तदादानेऽधिकृतः अण् ठक् वा] A<BR>superintendent of tolls, custom-officer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्विकः|शौल्विक
शौल्वि(ल्बि)कः A<BR>coppersmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौल्बिकः|शौल्बिक
शौल्वि(ल्बि)कः A<BR>coppersmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौव|शौवं
शौव a. (वी f.) [श्वन्-अण् टिलोपः]<BR>Relating to dogs, canine.<BR>--वं<BR>1 A<BR>pack of dogs.<BR>--2 The state or<BR>nature of a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवन|शौवनं
शौवन a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Canine.<BR>--2<BR>Having the qualities of a dog.<BR>--नं<BR>1 The nature of a dog.<BR>--2 The<BR>progeny of a dog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवस्तिक|शौवस्तिकं
शौवस्तिक a. (की f.) [श्वस्-ठक्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">Page1057-b+ 55</a>]<BR>तुट् च] Belonging to or lasting till<BR>to-morrow, ephemeral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौवापद|शौवापदं
शौवापद a. (दी f.) [श्वापद-अण्]<BR>1 Relating to a wild beast.<BR>--2<BR>Savage, fierce, wild.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शौष्कलः|शौष्कल
शौष्कलः<BR>1 A vendor of flesh.<BR>--2<BR>A habitual eater of flesh.<BR>--लं The<BR>price of dried meat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चुत्
श्चुत् See श्च्युत् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्युत्
श्च्युत् {c1c} P. (श्च्योतति)<BR>1 To trickle,<BR>ooze, flow, exude; एतास्ता<BR>मधुतोधाराश्श्च्योतंति सविषास्त्वयि U. 3. 34;<BR>Śi. 8. 63; Ki. 5. 29<BR>--2 To shed,<BR>pour out, diffuse, scatter. --WITH<BR>नि to flow, ooze, trickle; निश्च्योतंते<BR>सुतनु कवरीबिंदवो यावदेते<BR>Māl. 8. 2. v. {1}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्योतः|श्च्योत
श्च्यो(श्चो)तः, श्चो(श्च्यो)तनं<BR>Oozing, flowing, exuding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चोतः|श्चोत
श्च्यो(श्चो)तः, श्चो(श्च्यो)तनं<BR>Oozing, flowing, exuding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्चोतनं|श्चोतन
श्च्यो(श्चो)तः, श्चो(श्च्यो)तनं<BR>Oozing, flowing, exuding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्च्योतनं|श्च्योतन
श्च्यो(श्चो)तः, श्चो(श्च्यो)तनं<BR>Oozing, flowing, exuding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्नम्
श्नम् A technical term used by<BR>Pāṇini for न, the sign of the 7th<BR>class of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्ना
श्ना A technical term used by<BR>Pāṇini for ना, the sign of the 9th class<BR>of ruts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्नु
श्नु A technical term used by<BR>Pāṇini for नु, the sign of the 5th class<BR>of roots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मन्
श्मन् n.<BR>1 The mouth, face.<BR>--2<BR>The body.<BR>--3 A dead body (m.;<BR>also in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मशानं|श्मशान
श्मशानं [श्मानः शवाः शेरतेऽत्र<BR>शी-आनच् डिच्च Tv.] A cemetery, a burial<BR>or burning ground; राजद्वारे श्मशाने<BR>च यस्तिष्ठति स बांधवः Subhāṣ.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः the fire of a<BR>burning ground.<BR>--आलयः a cemetery.<BR>--गोचर a. frequenting burning<BR>grounds; Ms. 10. 39.<BR>--निवासिन्,<BR>--वर्तिन्, --वासिन् m. a ghost.<BR>--भाज्,<BR>--वासिन् m. epithets of Śiva.<BR>--वाटः an<BR>enclosure of the cemetery; Māl. 5.<BR>--वेश्मन् m. {1} an epithet of Śiva. {2}<BR>a spirit, ghost.<BR>--वैराग्यं temporary<BR>despondency, momentary<BR>renunciation of the world as at the sight<BR>of a cemetery.<BR>--शूलः --लं an<BR>impaling stake in a cemetery;<BR>Ku. 5. 73.<BR>--साधनं performance of magical<BR>rites in a cemetery to acquire<BR>control over ghosts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रु
श्मश्रु n. [श्म मुखं श्रूयते लक्ष्यतेऽनेन<BR>श्रु ङु; Uṇ. 5. 28] The beard;<BR>ज्योतिष्कणाहतश्मश्रु कंठनालादपातयत्<BR>R. 15. 52.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रवृद्धि f. the growth of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">Page1057-c+ 56</a>]<BR>a beard; R. 13. 71.<BR>--मुखी a woman<BR>with a beard.<BR>--वर्धकः a barber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मश्रुल
श्मश्रुल a. [श्मश्रु विद्यतेऽस्य लच्]<BR>Having a beard, bearded;<BR>भल्लापवर्जितेस्तेषां शिरोभिः श्मश्रुलैर्महीं (तस्तार)<BR>R. 4. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मील्
श्मील् {c1c} P. (श्मीलति) To wink,<BR>contract the eyelids, twinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मीलनं|श्मीलन
श्मीलनं Winking, twinkling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्मीलितं|श्मीलित
श्मीलितं A wink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यान|श्यानः
श्यान p. p. [श्यै क्त]<BR>1 Gone.<BR>--2<BR>Coagulated, congealed.<BR>--3 Thick,<BR>sticky, viscous.<BR>--4 Shrunk, dry;<BR>शरदि सरितः श्यानपुलिनाः Bh. 2. 44.<BR>--नं<BR>Smoke.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याम|श्यामः
श्याम a. [श्यै-मक]<BR>1 Black, dark-blue,<BR>dark-coloured; प्रत्याख्यात विशेषकं<BR>कुरबकं श्यामावदातारुणं M. 3. 5; श्यामं<BR>द्रुयोर्भागयोः V. 2. 7;<BR>कुवलयदलश्यामस्निग्धः U. 4. 19; Me. 15, 23.<BR>--2 Brown.<BR>--3 Shady, dusky.<BR>--4 Dark-green.<BR>--नः<BR>1 The black colour.<BR>--2 The<BR>green colour.<BR>--3 A cloud.<BR>--4 The<BR>cuckoo.<BR>--5 N. of a sacred fig-tree at<BR>Allahabad on the bank of the<BR>Yamunā; अयं च कालिंदीतटे वटः श्यामो<BR>नाम U. 1; सोयं वटः श्याम इति प्रतीतः<BR>R. 13. 53.<BR>--6 The thorn<BR>apple.<BR>--मं<BR>1 Sea-salt.<BR>--2 Black<BR>pepper.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. dark.<BR>--(गः) the planet Mercury.<BR>--कंठः<BR>{1} an epithet of Śiva; (नीलकंठ).<BR>{2} a peacock.<BR>--कर्णः a horse<BR>suitable for a horse sacrifice.<BR>--पत्रः the<BR>tamāla tree.<BR>--भास्, --रुचि a.<BR>glossy-black.<BR>--शबलौ the two four-eyed<BR>watch-dogs of Yama; cf.<BR>Rv. 10. 14. 10.<BR>--सुंदरा an epithet of<BR>Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामकः|श्यामक|श्यामकं
श्यामकः<BR>1 A kind of edible grain<BR>(कंगु).<BR>--2 A gramineous plant.<BR>--कं<BR>A kind of grass; cf. श्यामाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामल|श्यामलः
श्यामल a. Black, dark-blue,<BR>blackish; निशितश्यामलस्निग्धमुखी शक्तिः<BR>Ve. 4; Śi. 18. 36; श्यामलानोकहश्रीः<BR>U. 2. 25.<BR>--लः<BR>1 Black colour.<BR>--2<BR>Black pepper.<BR>--3 A large bee.<BR>--4<BR>The sacred fig-tree.<BR>--ला N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामलिका
श्यामलिका The indigo plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामलिमन्
श्यामलिमन् m. Blackness,<BR>darkness; श्यामां श्यामलिमानमान यत भोः<BR>सांद्रैर्मषीकूर्त्रकैः Vb. 3. 1; तदीयधूमैरिव<BR>धूसरागाः क्षोणीभुजः श्यामलिमानमापुः<BR>Vikr. 10. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामा
श्यामा<BR>1 Night, particularly a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">Page1058-a+ 56</a>]<BR>dark night; श्मामां श्यामलिमानमानयत<BR>भोः सांद्रैर्मषीकूर्चकैः Vb. 3. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Shade, shadow.<BR>--3 A dark<BR>woman.<BR>--4 A kind of woman<BR>(यौवनमध्यस्था according to Malli. on<BR>N. 3. 8, Śi. 8. 36; Me. 82; or<BR>शीते सुखोष्णसर्वांगी ग्रीष्मे या सुखशीतला ।<BR>तप्तकांचनवर्णाभा सा स्री श्यामोति कथ्यते<BR>according to one commentator on<BR>Bk. 5. 18 and 8. 100).<BR>--5 A<BR>woman who has borne no children.<BR>--6<BR>A cow.<BR>--7 Turmeric.<BR>--8 The<BR>female cuckoo.<BR>--9 The Priyaṅgu<BR>creeper; M. 2. 7; Me. 104.<BR>--10<BR>The indigo plant.<BR>--11 The holy<BR>basil.<BR>--12 The seed of the lotus.<BR>--13<BR>N. of the Yamunā.<BR>--14 N. of<BR>several plants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1057-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामाकः|श्यामाक
श्यामाकः A kind of grain or corn;<BR>(न) श्यामाकमुष्टिपरिवर्धितको जहाति<BR>Ś. 4. 13 (also श्यामक).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामायते
श्यामायते Den. A. To become<BR>black, to prove impure (as gold<BR>&c.); श्यामायते न युष्मासु यः<BR>काचनभिवाग्निषु M. 2. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामिका
श्यामिका<BR>1 Blackness, darkness;<BR>अपांगयोः केवलमस्य दीर्घयोः शनैःशनैः<BR>श्यामिकया कृतं पदं Ku. 5. 21.<BR>--2<BR>Impurity, alloy, (of metals &c.); हेम्नः<BR>संलक्ष्यते ह्यग्नौ विशुद्धिः श्यामिकापि बा<BR>R. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यामित
श्यामित a. Blackened, darkened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालः|श्याल
श्यालः [श्यै-कालन्] A wife's<BR>brother, brother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालकः|श्यालक
श्यालकः<BR>1 A wife's brother.<BR>--2<BR>A wretched brother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालकी
श्यालकी, श्यालिका, श्याली A wife's<BR>sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यालिका
श्यालकी, श्यालिका, श्याली A wife's<BR>sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याली
श्यालकी, श्यालिका, श्याली A wife's<BR>sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्याव|श्यावः
श्याव a. (वा or वी f.) [श्यै-वन्]<BR>1 Dark-brown, dark, dusky.<BR>--2 Bay,<BR>brown.<BR>--वः The brown colour.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तैलः the mango tree.<BR>--दत्, --दंत a. brown-toothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येत|श्येतः
श्येत a. (ता or ना f.) White.<BR>--तः<BR>The white colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्येनः|श्येन
श्येनः [श्यै-इनन्]<BR>1 The white<BR>colour.<BR>--2 Whiteness.<BR>--3 A hawk,<BR>falcon.<BR>--4 Violence.<BR>--5 Ved. A<BR>horse.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवपातः the swoop<BR>of a hawk; Māl. 8. 8.<BR>--करणं,<BR>--करणिका {1} burning on a separate<BR>funeral pile. {2} a hawk-like, i. e. rash<BR>and desperate, act.<BR>--चित्, --जीविन्<BR>m. a falconer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यै
श्यै {c1c} A. (श्यायते, श्यान, शीत or<BR>शीन)<BR>1 To go, move.<BR>--2 To be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">Page1058-b+ 55</a>]<BR>congealed or coagulated.<BR>--3 To dry up,<BR>wither.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्यैनंपाता|श्यैनम्पाता
श्यैनंपाता [श्येनस्य पातोऽत्र अण् मुम्<BR>च] Hawking. hunting, chase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्योणाकः|श्योणाक
श्योणाकः, श्योनाकः N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्योनाकः|श्योनाक
श्योणाकः, श्योनाकः N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रंक्|श्रङ्क्
श्रंक् {c1c} A. (श्रंकते) To go, creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रंग्|श्रङ्ग्
श्रंग् {c1c} P. (श्रगति) To go, move,<BR>creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रण्
श्रण् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (श्रणति, श्राणयति<BR>ते) To give, give away, bestow<BR>usually with वि; R. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रत्
श्रत् ind. A prefix used with the<BR>root धा; see श्रद्धा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथ्
श्रथ् {vI.v} {c1c} {c9c} P. (श्रथति, श्रथ्नाति) To<BR>hurt, injure, kill. {vII.v} {c1c} P., {c10c} U.<BR>(श्रथति, श्राथयति-ते)<BR>1 To hurt, kill.<BR>--2<BR>To untie, loosen, liberate, release.<BR>{vIII.v} {c10c} U. (श्रथयति-ते)<BR>1 To make<BR>efforts, be occupied or busy.<BR>--2 To<BR>be weak or infirm.<BR>--3 To be glad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रथनं|श्रथन
श्रथनं<BR>1 Killing, destruction.<BR>--2<BR>Untying, loosening, release.<BR>--3 Ef.<BR>fort, exertion.<BR>--4 Tying, binding.<BR>--5 Delighting repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धा
श्रद्धा {c3c} U. To confide, believe,<BR>put faith in (with acc. of thing);<BR>कः श्रद्धास्यति भूतार्थं Mk. 3. 24;<BR>कामिन्यः श्रदधुरनार्जवं नरेषु Śi. 8. 11,<BR>9. 69; U. 7. 6; श्रद्दये त्रिदशगोपमात्रके<BR>दाहशक्तिमिव कृष्णवर्त्मनि R. 11. 42.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्ध
श्रद्ध a. Believing, trusting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धा
श्रद्धा<BR>1 Trust, faith, belief,<BR>confidence.<BR>--2 Belief in divine<BR>revelation, religious faith; श्रद्धा<BR>वित्तं विधिश्चेति त्रितयं तत्समागतं<BR>Ś. 7. 29; R. 2. 16; Bg. 6. 37; 17. 3.<BR>--3 Sedateness, composure of mind.<BR>--4 Intimacy, familiarity.<BR>--5 Respect,<BR>reverence.<BR>--6 Strong or vehement<BR>desire; तथापि वैचिव्यरहस्यलुब्याः<BR>श्रद्धां विधास्यंति सचेतसोऽत्र Vikr. 1. 13,<BR>युद्धश्रद्धापुलकित इव प्राप्तसख्यः<BR>करेण Mu. 6. 18.<BR>--7 The longing of a<BR>pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रद्धालु|श्रद्धालुः
श्रद्धालु a. [श्रद्धा --आलुच्]<BR>1<BR>Believing, full of faith.<BR>--2 Desirous,<BR>longing or wishing for (anything);<BR>अकालकुसुमसमुद्गमश्रद्धालुता भर्त्रा<BR>Ratn. 1.<BR>--लुः f. A pregnant woman longing<BR>for anything.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रंथ्|श्रन्थ्
श्रंथ् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (श्रंथते)<BR>1 To be weak.<BR>--2 To be loose or relaxed.<BR>--3 To<BR>loosen, relax. {vII.v} {c9c} P. (श्रथ्नाति)<BR>1 To<BR>loosen, liberate, release.<BR>--2 To<BR>delight repeatedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रंथः|श्रन्थ|श्रंथ|श्रन्थः
श्रंथः<BR>1 Loosening, liberating.<BR>--2<BR>Looseness.<BR>--3 Binding, tying<BR>together.<BR>--4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रंथनं|श्रन्थन|श्रंथन|श्रन्थनं
श्रंथनं<BR>1 Loosing, untying.<BR>--2<BR>Hurting, killing, destroying.<BR>--3<BR>Tying, binding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रंथित|श्रन्थित|श्रन्थितः
श्रंथित p. p.<BR>1 Loosed, liberated,<BR>let loose.<BR>--2 Connected; strung or<BR>bound together.<BR>--3 Hurt,<BR>injured.<BR>--4 Overcome, overpowered.<BR>--5<BR>Delighted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपणं|श्रपण|श्रपणः
श्रपणं --णा Causing to boil,<BR>boiling, seething.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपणा
श्रपणं --णा Causing to boil,<BR>boiling, seething.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रपित|श्रपितं
श्रपित p. p.<BR>1 Boiled or caused to<BR>be boiled.<BR>--2 Seethed.<BR>--तं Boiled<BR>meat &c.<BR>--ता Rice gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रम्
श्रम् {c4c} P. (श्राम्यति, श्रांत)<BR>1 To exert<BR>oneself, take pains, toil, labour.<BR>--2<BR>To perform austerities, mortify the<BR>body (by acts of penance); कियच्चिरं<BR>श्राम्यसि गौरि Ku. 5. 50.<BR>--3 To be<BR>wearied or fatigued, be exhausted;<BR>रतिश्रांता शेते रजानिरमणी गाढमुरमि<BR>K. P. 10; Śi. 14. 38; Bk. 14. 110.<BR>--4<BR>To be afflicted or distressed; यो<BR>वृंदानि त्वरयति पथि श्राम्यतां प्रोषितानां<BR>Me. 99. --Caus. (श्र श्रा-मयति-ते)<BR>To cause to be fatigued &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमः|श्रम
श्रमः [श्रम्-घञ्-न वृद्धिः]<BR>1 Toil,<BR>labour, exertion, effort; अलं महीपाल<BR>तव श्रमेण R. 2. 34; जानाति हि पुनः<BR>सम्यक् कविरेव कवेः श्रमं Subhāṣ.;<BR>R. 16. 75; Ms. 9. 208.<BR>--2 Weariness,<BR>fatigue, exhaustion; विनयंते स्म<BR>तद्योधा मधुभिर्विजयश्रमं R. 4. 65, 67;<BR>Me. 17, 52; Ki. 5. 28.<BR>--3 Affliction,<BR>distress.<BR>--4 Penance, austerity,<BR>mortification of the body; दिवं यदि<BR>प्रार्थयसे वृथा श्रमः Ku. 5. 45.<BR>--5 (a)<BR>Exercise; अयोदंडेन च श्रममकरोत्<BR>K. 76. (b) Especially, military<BR>exercise, drill.<BR>--6 Hard study.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंबु n.,<BR>--जलं perspiration, sweat.<BR>--कर्षित a. worn out by fatigue.<BR>--साध्य a. to be accomplished by<BR>dint of labour.<BR>--स्थानं a drill-ground,<BR>gymnasium &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमण|श्रमणः
श्रमण a. (णा --णी f.) [श्रम्-युच्]<BR>1 Labouring, toiling.<BR>--2 Low, base,<BR>vile.<BR>--णः<BR>1 An ascetic, a devotee,<BR>religious mendicant in general.<BR>--2<BR>A Buddhist ascetic.<BR>--3 A beggar.<BR>--णा-णी<BR>1 A female devotee or<BR>mendicant.<BR>--2 A lovely woman.<BR>--3<BR>A woman of low caste.<BR>--4 Bengal<BR>madder.<BR>--5 The spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमणायते
श्रमणायते Den. A. To become a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">Page1059-a+ 55</a>]<BR>beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1058-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रमिन्
श्रमिन् a.<BR>1 Laborious, toiling,<BR>diligent.<BR>--2 Undergoing fatigue or<BR>exertions.<BR>--3 Tiring, fatiguing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रंभ्|श्रम्भ्
श्रंभ् {c1c} A. (श्रंभते, श्रब्ध)<BR>1 To be<BR>careless or inattentive, be<BR>negligent.<BR>--2 To err.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयः|श्रय
श्रयः, श्रयणं [श्रि-घञ् ल्युट् वा]<BR>Refuge, shelter, protection, asylum;<BR>Mv. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रयणं|श्रयण
श्रयः, श्रयणं [श्रि-घञ् ल्युट् वा]<BR>Refuge, shelter, protection, asylum;<BR>Mv. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवः|श्रव
श्रवः [शृणोत्यनेन श्रु-अप्]<BR>1<BR>Hearing; as in सुखश्रव.<BR>--2 The ear.<BR>--3<BR>The hypothenuse of a triangle.<BR>--4<BR>Flowing, oozing (for स्रव).<BR>--5<BR>Fame, glory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणः|श्रवण|श्रवणं
श्रवणः, --णं [शृणोत्यनेन श्रु-करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 The ear. ध्वनति मधुपसमूहे<BR>श्रवणमपिदधाति Gīt. 5.<BR>--2 The hypothenuse<BR>of a triangle.<BR>--णः --णा N. of a<BR>lunar mansion containing three<BR>stars.<BR>--णं<BR>1 The act of hearing;<BR>श्रवणसुभगं Me. 11.<BR>--2 Study.<BR>--3 Fame,<BR>glory.<BR>--4 That which is heard or<BR>revealed, the Veda; इति श्रबणात्<BR>‘because of such a Vedic text’.<BR>--5<BR>Wealth.<BR>--6 Flowing, oozing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इंद्रियं the sense of hearing, the<BR>ear.<BR>--उत्पलं a lotus fastened in the<BR>ear.<BR>--उदरं the hollow of the outer<BR>ear.<BR>--गोचर a. within the range of<BR>hearing.<BR>--(रः) ear-shot; as in<BR>श्रवणगोचरे तिष्ठ ‘be within ear-shot’.<BR>--पथः, --विषयः the reach or range<BR>of the ear; वृत्तांतेन श्रवणविषयप्रापिणा<BR>R. 14. 87.<BR>--पालः-ली f. the tip of the<BR>ear.<BR>--पाशः a beautiful ear.<BR>--सुमग<BR>a. pleasing to the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवणं|श्रवण|श्रवणः
श्रवणः, --णं [शृणोत्यनेन श्रु-करणे ल्युट्]<BR>1 The ear. ध्वनति मधुपसमूहे<BR>श्रवणमपिदधाति Gīt. 5.<BR>--2 The hypothenuse<BR>of a triangle.<BR>--णः --णा N. of a<BR>lunar mansion containing three<BR>stars.<BR>--णं<BR>1 The act of hearing;<BR>श्रवणसुभगं Me. 11.<BR>--2 Study.<BR>--3 Fame,<BR>glory.<BR>--4 That which is heard or<BR>revealed, the Veda; इति श्रबणात्<BR>‘because of such a Vedic text’.<BR>--5<BR>Wealth.<BR>--6 Flowing, oozing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इंद्रियं the sense of hearing, the<BR>ear.<BR>--उत्पलं a lotus fastened in the<BR>ear.<BR>--उदरं the hollow of the outer<BR>ear.<BR>--गोचर a. within the range of<BR>hearing.<BR>--(रः) ear-shot; as in<BR>श्रवणगोचरे तिष्ठ ‘be within ear-shot’.<BR>--पथः, --विषयः the reach or range<BR>of the ear; वृत्तांतेन श्रवणविषयप्रापिणा<BR>R. 14. 87.<BR>--पालः-ली f. the tip of the<BR>ear.<BR>--पाशः a beautiful ear.<BR>--सुमग<BR>a. pleasing to the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्
श्रवस् n.<BR>1 The ear.<BR>--2 Fame,<BR>glory.<BR>--3 Wealth.<BR>--4 Hymn.<BR>--5 A<BR>praiseworthy action.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्यं|श्रवस्य
श्रवस्यं Fame, glory, renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवस्यति
श्रवस्यति Den. P.<BR>1 To wish for<BR>fame or glory.<BR>--2 To long for a<BR>sacrifice or oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवाप्यः|श्रवाप्य
श्रवाप्यः --य्यः An animal fit<BR>for sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रवाय्यः|श्रवाय्य
श्रवाप्यः --य्यः An animal fit<BR>for sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रविष्ठा
श्रविष्ठा<BR>1 N. of a lunar asterism,<BR>also called Dhaniṣṭhā.<BR>--2 The<BR>asterism called श्रवणा.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः<BR>the planet Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रा
श्रा {c2c} P. (श्राति, श्राण or शृत; caus.<BR>श्रपयति-ते)<BR>1 To cook, boil, dress,<BR>mature, ripen.<BR>--2 To sweat or cause<BR>to sweat, heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राण|श्राणं
श्राण a.<BR>1 Cooked, dressed, boiled.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">Page1059-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--2 Wet, moist.<BR>--णं Boiled meat &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राणा
श्राणा Rice-gruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्ध|श्राद्धं
श्राद्ध a. [श्रद्धा हेतुत्वेनास्त्यस्य अण्]<BR>Faithful, believing.<BR>--द्धं<BR>1 A<BR>funeral rite or ceremony performed in<BR>honour of the departed spirits of<BR>dead relatives; श्रद्धया दीयते<BR>यस्मात्तस्माच्छ्राद्धं निगद्यते; it is of three<BR>kinds:<BR>--नित्य, नैमित्तिक, and काम्य.<BR>--2<BR>An obsequial oblation, a gift or<BR>offering at a Śrāddha.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n.,<BR>--क्रिया a funeral ceremony.<BR>--कृत् m. the performer of a<BR>funeral rite.<BR>--दः the offerer of a<BR>Śrāddha or funeral oblation.<BR>--दिनः -नं<BR>the anniversary of the death of a<BR>relative in whose honour a<BR>Śrāddha is performed.<BR>--देवः, --देवता {1}<BR>a deity presiding over funeral rites.<BR>{2} an epithet of Yama. {3} a<BR>Viśvadeva q. v. {4} a Pitṛ or<BR>progenitor.<BR>--भुज्, --भोक्तृ m. a deceased<BR>ancestor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धिक|श्राद्धिकः
श्राद्धिक a. (की f.) [श्रद्धे-देयं, श्रद्धं<BR>तद्द्रव्यं भक्ष्पत्वेनास्तपस्य वा ठन्]<BR>Relating to a Śrāddha.<BR>--कः The<BR>recipient of an obsequial offering.<BR>--कं<BR>A present given at a Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राद्धीय
श्राद्धीय a. Relating to a Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रांत|श्रान्त|श्रान्तः
श्रांत p. p. [श्रम्-क्त]<BR>1 Wearied,<BR>tired, fatigued, exhausted.<BR>--2<BR>Calmed, tranquil<BR>--तः An ascetic.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संवाहनं soothing or relieving the<BR>wearied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रांतिः|श्रान्ति|श्रांति|श्रान्तिः
श्रांतिः f. [श्रम्-क्तिन्] Fatigue,<BR>exhaustion, weariness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रामः|श्राम
श्रामः<BR>1 A month.<BR>--2 Time.<BR>--3<BR>A temporary shed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रायः|श्राय
श्रायः [श्रि-घञ्] Shelter, protection,<BR>refuge, asylum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावः|श्राव
श्रावः [श्रृ-घञ्]<BR>1 Hearing,<BR>listening.<BR>--2 Flowing, oozing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावकः|श्रावक
श्रावकः [श्रि-ण्बुल्]<BR>1 A hearer.<BR>--2<BR>A pupil, disciple; श्राबकावस्यायां<BR>Māl. 10 ‘in their pupilage’.<BR>--3 A<BR>class of Buddhist saints or<BR>votaries.<BR>--4 A Buddhist votary<BR>in general.<BR>--5 A heretic.<BR>--6 A crow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावण|श्रावणः
श्रावण a. (णी f.) [श्रवण-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Relating to the ear.<BR>--2 Born under<BR>the asterism Śravaṇa.<BR>--णः<BR>1 N. of<BR>a lunar month; (corresponding to<BR>July-August).<BR>--2 A heretic.<BR>--3 An<BR>impostor.<BR>--4 N. of a Vaiśya ascetic<BR>unwittingly shot dead by king<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">Page1059-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Daśaratha who was in consequence<BR>cursed by his old parents that he<BR>would die of broken-heart separated<BR>from his sons.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Causing to<BR>be heard.<BR>--2 Knowledge derived<BR>from hearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणिक|श्रावणिकः
श्रावणिक a. [श्रावणी अस्त्यस्मिन्<BR>मसिठन्] Relating to the month Śrāvaṇa.<BR>--कः The month called Śrāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावणी
श्रावणी<BR>1 The day of full moon in<BR>Śrāvaṇa.<BR>--2 N. of an annual<BR>ceremony performed on this day when<BR>the sacred thread is put on anew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावित
श्रावित a. Told, narrated, related,<BR>made to hear or learn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्राव्य
श्राव्य a.<BR>1 To be heard (opp.<BR>दृश्य).<BR>--2 Audible, distinct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावस्तिः|श्रावस्ति
श्रावस्तिः --स्ती f. N. of a city<BR>north of the Ganges (said to have<BR>been founded by king Śrāvasta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावस्ती
श्रावस्तिः --स्ती f. N. of a city<BR>north of the Ganges (said to have<BR>been founded by king Śrāvasta).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रि
श्रि {c1c} U. (श्रयति-ते, शिश्राय --शिश्रिये,<BR>अशिश्रियत्-त, श्रयिष्यति-ते, श्रयितुं, श्रित;<BR>caus. श्राययति-ते; desid. शिश्रीषति-ते,<BR>शिश्रयिषति-ते)<BR>1 To go to, approach,<BR>resort to, have recourse to, approach<BR>for protection; यं दंशं श्रयते तमेव<BR>कुरुते बाहुप्रतापार्जितं H. 1. 171;<BR>R. 3. 70; 19. 1; श्रितासि चंदनभ्रांत्या<BR>दुर्विपाकं विषद्रुपं U. 1. 46.<BR>--2 To go<BR>or attain to, reach, undergo, assume<BR>(as a state); परीता रक्षाभिः श्रयति<BR>विवशा कामपि दशां Bv. 1. 83;<BR>द्विपेंद्रभावं कलभः श्रयन्निव R. 3. 32.<BR>--3<BR>To cling to, lean or rest on,<BR>depend on; नीलः स्निग्धः श्रयति शिखरं<BR>नूतनस्तोयवाहः U. 1. 33.<BR>--4 To dwell<BR>in, inhabit.<BR>--5 To honour, serve,<BR>worship.<BR>--6 To use, employ.<BR>--7<BR>To devote oneself to, be attached<BR>to.<BR>--8 To assist, help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रित|श्रितः
श्रित p. p. [श्रि-क्त]<BR>1 Gone to,<BR>approached, approached for refuge or<BR>protection.<BR>--2 Clung to, resting<BR>or sitting on.<BR>--3 United or joined<BR>with, connected with.<BR>--4<BR>Protected.<BR>--5 Honoured, served.<BR>--6<BR>Subservient, auxiliary.<BR>--7 Covered<BR>with, overspread.<BR>--8 Contained.<BR>--9 Assembled, collected.<BR>--10<BR>Having, possessing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रितिः|श्रिति
श्रितिः f. Resort, recourse,<BR>approach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रिष्
श्रिष् {c1c} P. (श्रेषति) To burn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री^1 {c9c} U. (श्रीणाति, श्रीणीते) To cook,<BR>dress, boil, prepare.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्री
श्री f. [श्रि-क्विप् नि˚ Uṇ. 2. 57]<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1060-a" target="_blank">Page1060-a+ 56</a>]<BR>1 Wealth, riches, affluence,<BR>prosperity, plenty; अनिर्वेदः श्रियो मूलं Rām.;<BR>साहसे श्रीः प्रतिवसति Mk. 4 ‘fortune<BR>favours the brave’; Ms. 9. 300.<BR>--2 Royalty, majesty, royal wealth;<BR>Ki. 1. 1.<BR>--3 Dignity, high position,<BR>state; श्रीलक्षण Ku. 7. 45 ‘the<BR>marks or insignia of greatness<BR>or dignity’; Pt. 1. 67.<BR>--4 Beauty,<BR>grace, splendour, lustre; (मुखं)<BR>कमलश्रियं दधौ Ku. 5. 21, 7. 32;<BR>R. 3. 8.<BR>--5 Colour, aspect; Ku. 2. 2.<BR>--6<BR>The goddess of wealth, Lakṣmī,<BR>the wife of Viṣṇu; आसीदियं<BR>दशरथस्य गृहे यथा श्रीः U. 4. 6;<BR>Ś. 3. 14; Śi. 1. 1.<BR>--7 Any virtue or<BR>excellence.<BR>--8 Decoration.<BR>--9<BR>Intellect, understanding.<BR>--10<BR>Superhuman power.<BR>--11 The three<BR>objects of human existence taken<BR>collectively (धर्म, अर्य and काम).<BR>--12<BR>The Sarala tree.<BR>--13 The Bilva tree.<BR>--14 Cloves.<BR>--15 A lotus.<BR>--16 The<BR>twelfth digit of the moon.<BR>--17<BR>N. of Sarasvatī, (the goddess of<BR>speech).<BR>--18 Speech.<BR>--19 Fame,<BR>glory. --m. N. of one of the six<BR>Rāgas or musical modes. (The<BR>word श्री is often used as an<BR>honorific prefix to the names of deities<BR>and eminent persons; श्रीकृष्णः,<BR>श्रीरामः, श्रीवाल्मीकिः, श्रीजयदेवः; also<BR>celebrated works, generally of a<BR>sacred character; श्रीभागवत,<BR>श्रीरामायण &c.; it is also used as an<BR>auspicious sign at the commencement<BR>of letters, manuscripts &c.; Māgha<BR>has used this word in the last stanza<BR>of each canto of his Śiśupālavadha,<BR>as Bhāravi has used लक्ष्मी).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आह्वं a lotus.<BR>--ईशः an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--कंठः {1} an epithet of<BR>Śiva. {2} of the poet Bhavabhūti:<BR>श्रीकंठपदलांछनः U. 1. ˚सखः an<BR>epithet of Kubera.<BR>--करः an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--(रं) the red<BR>lotus.<BR>--करणं a pen.<BR>--कांतः an<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--कारः the word<BR>‘श्री’ written at the top of a letter,<BR>(as an auspicious beginning).<BR>--कारिन् m. a kind of antelope.<BR>--खंडः --डं<BR>sandal-wood; श्रीखंडविलेपनं सुखयति<BR>H. 1. 97.<BR>--गदितं a kind of minor<BR>drama.<BR>--गर्भः {1} an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu. {2} a sword.<BR>--ग्रहः a trough<BR>or place for watering birds.<BR>--ग्रामरः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1060-b" target="_blank">Page1060-b+ 56</a>]<BR>an epithet of Nārāyaṇa.<BR>--घनं sour<BR>curds.<BR>--(नः) a Buddhist saint.<BR>--चक्र<BR>{1} the circle of the earth, the<BR>globe. {2} a wheel of Indra's car.<BR>--जः an epithet of Kāma.<BR>--तालः<BR>a kind of palm tree.<BR>--दः an<BR>epithet of Kubera.<BR>--दयितः, --धरः<BR>epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR>--नगरं N. of a<BR>city.<BR>--नंदनः an epithet of Kāma.<BR>--निकेतनः, --निवासः epithets of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--पंचमी the fifth day of<BR>the bright half of Māgha.<BR>--पतिः<BR>{1} an epithet of Viṣṇu;<BR>Śi. 13. 69. {2} a king, sovereign.<BR>--पथः a<BR>main road, high way.<BR>--पर्णं a lotus.<BR>--पर्णी the silk-cotton tree.<BR>--पर्वतः<BR>N. of a mountain; Māl. 1.<BR>--पिष्टः<BR>turpentine.<BR>--पुत्रः {1} N. of Cupid.<BR>{2} the moon. {3} N. of the horse<BR>of Indra.<BR>--पुष्पं {1} cloves. {2} a<BR>fragrant wood (पद्मकाष्ठ).<BR>--फलः<BR>the Bilva tree.<BR>--(लं) the Bilva<BR>fruit.<BR>--फला, --फली {1} the indigo<BR>plant. {2} emblic myrobalan.<BR>--भ्रातृ<BR>m. {1} the moon. {2} a horse.<BR>--मस्तकः garlic.<BR>--मुद्रा a particular<BR>mark on the fore head by the<BR>Vaiṣṇavas.<BR>--मूर्तिः f. {1} an idol<BR>of Viṣṇu or Lakṣmī. {2} any<BR>idol.<BR>--युक्त, --युत a. {1} fortunate,<BR>happy. {2} wealthy, prosperous<BR>(often used as an honorific prefix<BR>to the names of men.). {3} famous,<BR>illustrious.<BR>--रंगः an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--रसः {1} turpentine. {2} resin.<BR>--वत्सः {1} an epithet of Viṣṇu. {2}<BR>a mark or curl of hair on the<BR>breast of Viṣṇu; प्रभानुलिप्तश्रीवत्सं<BR>लक्ष्मीविभ्रमदर्पणं R. 10. 10. {3} a hole<BR>in a wall made by a house-breaker.<BR>˚अंकः ˚धारिन्, ˚भृत्, ˚लक्ष्पन्,<BR>˚लांछन m. epithets of Viṣṇu;<BR>Ku. 7. 43.<BR>--वत्सकिन् m. a horse having<BR>a curl of hair on his breast.<BR>--वरः,<BR>--वल्लभः epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR>--वर्धनः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--वल्लभः a<BR>favourite of fortune, a happy or<BR>fortunate person; Pt. 1. 45.<BR>--वासः<BR>{1} an epithet of Viṣṇu. {2} of<BR>Śiva. {3} a lotus. {4} turpentine.<BR>--बासस् m. turpentine.<BR>--वृक्षः {1}<BR>the Bilva tree. {2} the Aśvattha<BR>or sacred fig-tree. {3} a curl of<BR>hair on the breast and forehead<BR>of a horse.<BR>--वेष्टः {1} turpentine. {2}<BR>resin.<BR>--संज्ञं cloves.<BR>--सहोदरः the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1060-c" target="_blank">Page1060-c+ 56</a>]<BR>moon.<BR>--मूक्त N. of a Vedic<BR>hymn.<BR>--हरिः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--हस्तिनी the sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1059-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रियंमन्य
श्रियंमन्य a.<BR>1 Thinking oneself<BR>worthy.<BR>--2 Proud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रियापतिः
श्रियापतिः An epithet of Śiva,<BR>also श्रियावासिन् m.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीमत्|श्रीमन्त्
श्रीमत् a.<BR>1 Wealthy, rich.<BR>--2<BR>Happy, fortunate, prosperous,<BR>thriving.<BR>--3 Beautiful, pleasing;<BR>Śi. 1. 1.<BR>--4 Famous, celebrated,<BR>glorious, dignified; (the word is<BR>often used as a respectful affix to<BR>celebrated or revered names of<BR>persons and things). --m.<BR>1 An<BR>epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 Of Kubera.<BR>--3 Of Śiva.<BR>--4 The Tilaka tree.<BR>--5 The Aśvattha tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रील|श्रीलः
श्रील a.<BR>1 Rich, wealthy.<BR>--2<BR>Fortunate, prosperous.<BR>--3 Beautiful.<BR>--4 Famous, celebrated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रु
श्रु {vI.v} {c1c} P. (श्रवति) To go, move;<BR>cf. शु. {vII.v} {c5c} P. (शृणोति, शुश्राव,<BR>अश्रौषीत्, श्रोष्यति, श्रोतुं, श्रुत)<BR>1 To hear,<BR>listen to, give ear to; शृणु मे सावशेषं<BR>वचः V. 2; रुतानि चाश्रीषत षट्पदानां<BR>Bk. 2. 10; संदेशं मे तदनु जलद<BR>श्रोष्यसि श्रोत्रपेयं Me. 13.<BR>--2 To learn,<BR>study; द्वादशवर्षभिर्व्याकरणं श्रूयते<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--3 To be attentive, to obey.<BR>(इति श्रूयते ‘it is so heard’, i. e.<BR>is enjoined in the scriptures, such<BR>is the sacred precept). --Caus.<BR>(श्रावयति-ते) To cause to hear,<BR>communicate, tell, relate, inform;<BR>श्रावितोऽमात्यसंदेशं स्तनकलसः Mu. 4.<BR>--Desid. (शुश्रूषते)<BR>1 To wish to<BR>hear.<BR>--2 To be attentive, or<BR>obedient, obey; बाक्यं नैव करोति<BR>बांधवजनो पत्नी न शुश्रूषते Pt. 4. 78 (where<BR>the word may have the next sense<BR>also).<BR>--3 To serve, wait or attend<BR>upon; शुश्रूषस्व गुरून् Ś. 4. 17;<BR>Ku. 1. 59; Ms. 2. 244.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुत|श्रुतं|श्रुतः
श्रुत p. p. [श्रु-क्त]<BR>1 Heard,<BR>listened to.<BR>--2 Reported, heard of.<BR>--3<BR>Learnt, ascertained, understood.<BR>--4<BR>Well-known, famous, celebrated,<BR>renowned; श्रुतस्य किं तत्सदृशं कुलस्य<BR>R. 14. 61, 3. 40.<BR>--5 Named, called.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The object of hearing.<BR>--2<BR>That which was heard by<BR>revelation; i. e. the Veda, holy learning,<BR>sacred knowledge; श्रुतप्रकाशं<BR>R. 5. 2.<BR>--3 Learning in general (विद्या);<BR>श्रोत्रं श्रुतेनैव न कुंडलेन (विभाति)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-a" target="_blank">Page1061-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Bh. 2. 71, R. 3. 21, 5. 22; Pt. 2. 147;<BR>4. 68.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्ययनं study of<BR>the Vedas.<BR>--अन्वित a. conversant<BR>with the Vedas.<BR>--अर्थः a fact<BR>verbally or orally communicated.<BR>--कीर्ति a. famous, renowned. (--m.)<BR>{1} a generous man. {2} a divine<BR>sage. (--f.) N. of the wife of<BR>Śatrughna.<BR>--देवी N. of Sarasvatī.<BR>--धर<BR>a. remembering what is heard,<BR>retentive.<BR>--श्रवस् m. N. of the father<BR>of Śiśupāla. ˚अनुजः the planet<BR>Saturn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1060-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतवत्|श्रुतवन्त्
श्रुतवत् a. Knowing the Veda,<BR>proficient in sacred knowledge or<BR>learning in general; अपथे पदमर्पयंति हि<BR>श्रुतवंतोऽपि रजोनिमीलिताः R. 9. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुतिः|श्रुति
श्रुतिः f. [श्रु-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Hearing;<BR>चंद्रस्य ग्रहणमिति श्रुतेः Mu. 1. 7;<BR>R. 1. 27.<BR>--2 The ear;<BR>श्रुतिसुखभ्रमरस्वनगीतयः R. 9. 35; Śi. 1. 1; Ve. 3. 23.<BR>--3 Report, rumour, news, oral<BR>intelligence.<BR>--4 A sound in general.<BR>--5 The Veda (known by revelation,<BR>opp स्मृति; see under वेद).<BR>--6 A<BR>Vedic or sacred text; इति श्रुतेः or<BR>इति श्रुतिः ‘so says a sacred text’<BR>--7<BR>Vedic or sacred knowledge, holy<BR>learning.<BR>--8 (In music) A division<BR>of the octavo, a quarter tone or<BR>interval; Śi. 1. 10, 11. 1; (see Malli.<BR>ad loc.).<BR>--9 The constellation<BR>Śravaṇa.<BR>--10 The diagonal of a<BR>tetragon, the hypothenuse of a<BR>triangle; cf. कर्ण.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुप्रासः<BR>a kind of alliteration; see K. P. 9<BR>--उक्त, --उदित a. enjoined by the<BR>Vedas.<BR>--कटः {1} a snake. {2}<BR>penance, expiation.<BR>--कटु a. harsh to<BR>hear.<BR>--(दुः) a harsh or<BR>unmelodious sound, regarded as a fault of<BR>composition.<BR>--कथित a. enjoined or<BR>prescribed by the Vedas.<BR>--चोदनं,<BR>--ना a scriptural injunction, Vedic<BR>precept.<BR>--जीविका a law-book or<BR>code of laws.<BR>--द्वैधं disagreement or<BR>contradiction of Vedas or Vedic<BR>precepts.<BR>--धर a. hearing.<BR>--निदर्शनं<BR>evidence of the Vedas.<BR>--पथः the<BR>range of the ear; M. 4. 1.<BR>--प्रसादन<BR>a. grateful to the ear.<BR>--प्रामाण्यं<BR>authority or sanction of the Vedas.<BR>--मंडलं the outer ear.<BR>--महत् a. rich<BR>in scriptural lore; सरस्वती श्रुतिमहतां<BR>महीयतां Ś. 7. 35.<BR>--मूलं {1} the root<BR>of the ear; लपितुं किमपि श्रुतिमूले<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">Page1061-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Gīt. 1. {2} a Vedic text.<BR>--मूलक a.<BR>founded on the Veda.<BR>--वर्जित a. {1} deaf.<BR>{2} not knowing the Vedas.<BR>--विप्रतिपन्न a. {1} not recognizing the<BR>authority of the scriptures, disregarding<BR>the Vedas. {2} contrary to the<BR>Vedas.<BR>--विषयः {1} the object of the<BR>sense of hearing. i. e. sound;<BR>श्रुतिविषयगुणा या स्थिता व्याण्य विश्वं<BR>Ś. 1. 1. {2} the reach or range of the<BR>ear; एतत्प्रायेण<BR>श्रुतिविषयमापतितमेव K. {3} the subject matter of<BR>the Veda. {4} any sacred ordinance.<BR>--वेधः boring the ear.<BR>--सुख,<BR>--मनोहर a. agreeable to the ear, melodious.<BR>--स्मृति f. (dual) revelation and<BR>legal institutes, Veda and law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुती
श्रुती = श्रुतिः above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुवः|श्रुव
श्रुवः<BR>1 A sacrifice.<BR>--2 A<BR>sacrificial ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुवा
श्रुवा A sacrificial ladle; cf. स्रुवा.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वृक्षः the Vikaṅkata<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रुष्टिः|श्रुष्टि
श्रुष्टिः f. Ved.<BR>1 Hearing.<BR>--2<BR>Help, assistance.<BR>--3 A boon (वर).<BR>--4 Prosperity, happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेढी
श्रेढी A progression (in math).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फलं the sum of a<BR>progression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणिः|श्रेणि
श्रेणिः m. f., श्रेणी f. [श्रि-णि वा ङीप्<BR>Uṇ. 4. 51]<BR>1 A line, series, row;<BR>तरंगभ्रूभंगा क्षुभितविहगश्रेणिरसना<BR>V. 4. 28; न षट्पदश्रेणिभिरेव पंकजं<BR>सशैबलासंगमपि प्रकाशते Ku. 5. 9; Me. 28,<BR>35.<BR>--2 A flock, multitude, group;<BR>U. 4.<BR>--3 A guild or company of<BR>traders, artisans &c., corporate body.<BR>--4 A bucket.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धर्माः (m.<BR>pl.) the customs of trades or<BR>guilds.<BR>--बंध a. forming a row,<BR>being in a line; R. 1. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणिका
श्रेणिका A tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणीभू
श्रेणीभू {c1c} P. To be arranged in<BR>regular order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेणी
श्रेणी^1<BR>1 A succession of distinct<BR>things.<BR>--2 (In math.) Progression.<BR>--3 Sequence.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयस्
श्रेयस् a. [अतिशयेन प्रशस्यं इयसु<BR>श्रादेशः]<BR>1 Better, preferable, superior;<BR>वर्धनाद्रक्षणं श्रेयः H. 3. 3, 33;<BR>Bg. 3. 35, 2. 5.<BR>--2 Best, most excellent,<BR>quite desirable; Māl. 1. 13.<BR>--3<BR>More happy or fortunate.<BR>--4 More<BR>blessed, dearer (compar. of प्रशस्व<BR>q. v.). --n.<BR>1 Virtue, righteous<BR>deeds, moral or religious merit.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">Page1061-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Bliss, good fortune, blessing, good’<BR>welfare, felicity, a good or<BR>auspicious result; पूर्वावधीरितं श्रेयोदुःखं हि<BR>परिवर्तते Ś. 7. 13; धिङ्<BR>मामुपस्थितश्रेयोवमानिनं Ś. 6; प्रतिबध्नाति हि श्रेयः<BR>पूज्यपूजाव्यतिक्रमः R. 1. 79;<BR>U. 5. 27, 7. 20; R. 5. 34.<BR>--3 Any good<BR>or auspicious occasion; Ś. 7.<BR>--4<BR>Final beatitude, absolution.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थिन् a. {1} seeking happiness,<BR>desirous of felicity. {2} wishing well.<BR>--कर a. {1} promoting happiness,<BR>favourable. {2} propitious, auspicious.<BR>--परिश्रमः striving after absolution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेयसी
श्रेयसी<BR>1 Yellow myrobalan.<BR>--2<BR>Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठ|श्रेष्ठं|श्रेष्ठः
श्रेष्ठ a.<BR>1 Best, most excellent,<BR>pre-eminent (with gen. or<BR>loc.).<BR>--2 Most happy or<BR>prosperous.<BR>--3 Most beloved, dearest.<BR>--4<BR>Oldest, senior.<BR>--ष्ठः<BR>1 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--2<BR>A king.<BR>--3 N. of Kubera.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--ष्ठं Cow's milk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अम्लं the fruit of the tamarind.<BR>--आश्रमः {1} the best order of one's<BR>religious life, i. e. that of a<BR>householder. {2} a householder.<BR>--वाच्<BR>a. eloquent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रेष्ठिन्
श्रेष्ठिन् m. [श्रेष्ठं धनादिकमस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>The head or president of a<BR>mercantile or other guild; निक्षेपे पतिते हर्म्ये<BR>श्रेष्ठि स्तौति स्वदेवतां Pt. 1. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रै
श्रै {c1c} P. (श्रायति)<BR>1 To sweat,<BR>perspire.<BR>--2 To cook, boil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रैष्ठ्यं|श्रैष्ठ्य
श्रैष्ठ्यं Superiority, pre-eminence,<BR>excellence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण्
श्रोण् {c1c} P. (श्रोणति)<BR>1 To collect,<BR>heap.<BR>--2 To be collected or<BR>accumulated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोण|श्रोणः
श्रोण a. Crippled, lame.<BR>--णः A<BR>kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणा
श्रोणा<BR>1 Rice-gruel.<BR>--2 The<BR>constellation Śravaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणिः|श्रोणि
श्रोणिः --णी f. [श्रोण्-इन् वा ङीप्]<BR>1<BR>The hip or loins, the buttocks;<BR>श्रोणीभारादलसगमना Me. 82;<BR>श्रोणीभारस्त्यजति तनुतां K. P. 10.<BR>--2 A road,<BR>way.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तटः the slope of<BR>the hips.<BR>--फलकं {1} the broad hips.<BR>{2} the buttocks.<BR>--बिंबं {1} the round<BR>hips; V. 4. 18. {2} a waist-band.<BR>--सूत्रं {1} a string worn round the<BR>loins. {2} a sword-belt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोणी
श्रोणिः --णी f. [श्रोण्-इन् वा ङीप्]<BR>1<BR>The hip or loins, the buttocks;<BR>श्रोणीभारादलसगमना Me. 82;<BR>श्रोणीभारस्त्यजति तनुतां K. P. 10.<BR>--2 A road,<BR>way.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तटः the slope of<BR>the hips.<BR>--फलकं {1} the broad hips.<BR>{2} the buttocks.<BR>--बिंबं {1} the round<BR>hips; V. 4. 18. {2} a waist-band.<BR>--सूत्रं {1} a string worn round the<BR>loins. {2} a sword-belt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतस्
श्रोतस् n. [श्रु-असुन् तुट् च]<BR>1<BR>The ear.<BR>--2 The trunk of an<BR>elephant.<BR>--3 An organ of sense.<BR>--4<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">Page1062-a+ 54</a>]<BR>The stream or current (for स्रोतस्<BR>q. v.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रंध्रं an aperture<BR>of the trunk, a nostril; Me. 42.<BR>(also written स्रोतोरंध्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1061-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोतृ
श्रोतृ m.<BR>1 A hearer.<BR>--2 A pupil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रं|श्रोत्र
श्रोत्रं [श्रूयतेऽनेन श्रु-करणे-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>1<BR>The ear; Bh. 2. 71.<BR>--2 Proficiency<BR>in the Vedas.<BR>--3 The Veda.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पेय a. to be imbibed by the ear,<BR>to be attentively heard; संदेशं मे<BR>तदनु जलद श्रोष्यसि श्रोत्रपेयं Me. 13.<BR>--मूलं the root of the ear.<BR>--सुख<BR>a. melodious, agreeable to the ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रोत्रिय|श्रोत्रियः
श्रोत्रिय a. [छंदो वेदमधीते वेत्ति वा<BR>छंदस्घ श्रोत्रादेशः; cf. P. V. 2. 84]<BR>1 Proficient or versed in the<BR>Veda.<BR>--2 Teachable, tractable.<BR>--यः A learned Brāhmaṇa, one<BR>wellversed in sacred learning; जन्मना<BR>ब्राह्मणोज्ञेयः संस्कारैर्द्विज उच्यते । विद्यया याति<BR>विप्रत्वं त्रिभिः श्रोत्रिय उच्यते ॥; Māl. 1. 5;<BR>R. 16. 25.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--स्वं the<BR>property of a learned Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत|श्रौतं|श्रौतः
श्रौत a. (ती f.) [श्रुतौ विहितं अण्]<BR>1 Relating to the ear.<BR>--2 Relating<BR>to, founded on, or prescribed by, the<BR>Veda.<BR>--3 Sacrificial.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Any<BR>observance prescribed by the Vedas.<BR>--2 Ritual enjoined by the Vedas.<BR>--3<BR>Preservation or maintenance of<BR>the sacred fire.<BR>--4 The three<BR>sacred fires collectively; (i. e.<BR>गार्हपत्य, आहवनीय and दक्षिण).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्मन् n. a Vedic rite.<BR>--सूत्रं N. of<BR>a class of Sūtra works based on the<BR>Veda (ascribed to आश्वलायन,<BR>सांख्यायन, कात्यायन &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौत्रं|श्रौत्र
श्रौत्रं [श्रोत्र-स्वार्थे अण्]<BR>1 The ear.<BR>--2 Proficiency in the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रौषट्
श्रौषट् ind. An exclamation or<BR>formula used in making an offering<BR>with fire to the gods or departed<BR>spirits; cf. वषट् or वौषट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्ण|श्लक्ष्णं
श्लक्ष्ण a. [श्लिष्-क्स्न नि˚ Uṇ. 3. 19]<BR>1 Soft, gentle, mild, bland (as<BR>words &c.); Ms. 8. 396.<BR>--2 Smooth,<BR>polished; Śi. 3. 46.<BR>--3 Small, fine,<BR>thin, delicate.<BR>--4 Beautiful,<BR>charming.<BR>--5 Candid, honest, frank.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लक्ष्णक|श्लक्ष्णकं
श्लक्ष्णक a.<BR>1 Smooth, soft.<BR>--2<BR>Beautiful, charming.<BR>--कं The<BR>Arecanut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लंक्|श्लङ्क्
श्लंक् {c1c} A. (श्लंकते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लंग्|श्लङ्ग्
श्लंग् {c1c} A. (श्लंगते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ्
श्लथ् {c10c} U. (श्लययति-ते)<BR>1 To be<BR>loose or slackened.<BR>--2 To be weak<BR>or infirm.<BR>--3 To slacken, loosen,<BR>relax (fig. also); श्लथयितुं<BR>क्षणमक्षमतांगना न सहसा सहसा कृतवेपथुः<BR>Śi. 6. 57; परित्राणस्नेहः श्लथयितुमशक्यः खलु<BR>यथा G. L. 37.<BR>--4 To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लथ
श्लथ a.<BR>1 Untied, unfastened.<BR>--2<BR>Loose, relaxed, loosened, slipped off;<BR>वृंताच्छ्लथं हरति पुष्पमनोकहानां<BR>R. 5. 69, 19. 26.<BR>--3 Dishevelled (as<BR>hair).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्यम a. relaxing<BR>one's efforts.<BR>--लंबिन् a. hanging<BR>loosely down; श्लथलांबनीर्जटाः<BR>Ku. 5. 47.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाख्
श्लाख् {c1c} P. (श्लाखति) To pervade,<BR>penetrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्
श्लाघ् {c1c} A. (श्लाघते)<BR>1 To praise,<BR>extol, commend, applaud; शिरमा<BR>श्लाघते पूर्वं (गुणं) परं (दोषं) कंठे<BR>नियच्छति Subhāṣ.; यथैव श्लाघ्यते गंगा<BR>पादेन परमेष्ठिनः Ku. 6. 70 (some read<BR>श्लाघते for श्लाघ्यते and give it the next<BR>sense).<BR>--2 To boast of, be proud<BR>of; श्लाघिष्ये केन को<BR>वंधून्नेष्यत्युन्नतिमुन्नतः Bk. 16. 4.<BR>--3 To flatter,<BR>coax (with dat.); गोपी कृष्णाय<BR>श्लाघते Sk.; श्लाघमानः<BR>परस्त्रीभ्यस्तत्रागाद्राक्षसाधिपः Bk. 8. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघनं|श्लाघन
श्लाघनं [श्लाघ् ल्युट्]<BR>1 Praising,<BR>eulogizing.<BR>--2 Flattering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघा
श्लाघा [श्लाघ् अ]<BR>1 Praise, eulogy,<BR>commendation; कर्णजयद्रथयोर्वा<BR>कात्र श्लाघा Ve. 2.<BR>--2 Self-praise, boast;<BR>हते जरति गांगेये पुरस्कृत्य शिखंडिनं ।<BR>या श्लाघा पांडुपुत्राणां सैवास्माकं भविष्यति<BR>Ve. 2. 4.<BR>--3 Flattery.<BR>--4 Service.<BR>--5 Wish, desire.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विपर्ययः<BR>absence of boasting; त्यागे<BR>ल्लाघाविपर्ययः R. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघित
श्लाघित p. p. Praised, eulogized,<BR>commended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लाघ्य|श्लाघ्यः
श्लाघ्य [श्लाघ्-ण्यत्]<BR>1 Praised,<BR>praiseworthy; Māl. 6. 17; U. 4. 9, 13.<BR>--2<BR>Respectable, venerable.<BR>--3<BR>Laudable, commendable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिकुः|श्लिकु
श्लिकुः [श्लष्-कु नेत्वम् पृषो˚]<BR>1 A<BR>debauchee, libertine.<BR>--2 A slave,<BR>dependent. --n. The science of<BR>astronomy, astrology.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिक्युः|श्लिक्यु
श्लिक्युः<BR>1 A libertine.<BR>--2 A<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्
श्लिष् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (श्लेषति) To burn.<BR>{vII.v} {c4c} P. (श्लिष्यति, श्लिष्ट)<BR>1 To em<BR>brace; श्लिष्यति चुंवति जलधरकल्पं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">Page1062-c+ 56</a>]<BR>हरिरुपगत इति तिमिरमनल्पं<BR>Gīt. 6.<BR>--2 To stick, cling or adhere<BR>to.<BR>--3 To unite, join.<BR>--4 To<BR>grasp, take, understand; अश्लेषि न<BR>श्लेषकवेर्भवत्याः श्लोकद्वयार्थः सुधिया मया<BR>किं N. 3. 69. {vIII.v} {c10c} U. (<BR>श्लेषयति-ते) To unite, join, connect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिषा
श्लिषा<BR>1 An embrace.<BR>--2<BR>Clinging, adherence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्ट|श्लिष्टः
श्लिष्ट p. p. [श्लिष्-क्त]<BR>1 Embraced.<BR>--2 Clung, adhered to.<BR>--3 Resting<BR>or leaning on.<BR>--4 Involving a pun,<BR>susceptible of a double<BR>interpretation; अ त्र विषमादयः शब्दाः श्लिष्टाः<BR>K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लिष्टिः|श्लिष्टि
श्लिष्टिः f.<BR>1 Embrace.<BR>--2<BR>Adherence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेषः|श्लेष
श्लेषः [श्लिष्-घञ्]<BR>1 An embrace.<BR>--2<BR>Clinging or adhering to.<BR>--3 Union,<BR>junction, contact; निरंतरश्लेषघनाः K.<BR>(where it has the next sense also).<BR>--4<BR>Pun, paronomasia, double entendre,<BR>susceptibility of a word or sentence,<BR>to yield two or more interpretations<BR>(regarded as a figure of speech and<BR>very commonly used by poets; for<BR>def. see K. P. Kārikās 84 and<BR>96); अश्लेषि न श्लेषकवेर्भवत्याः<BR>श्लोकद्वयार्थः सुधिया मया किं N. 3. 69; see<BR>शब्दश्लेष also.<BR>--5 Burning.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः a pun, double entendre.<BR>--भित्तिक a. trusting on (lit. having for<BR>its basis) a Śleṣa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदं|श्लीपद
श्लीपदं Swelled leg,<BR>elephantiasis.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रभवः the mango<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लीपदिन्
श्लीपदिन् m. A club-footed man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लील|श्लीलः
श्लील a.<BR>1 Lucky, prosperous;<BR>see श्रील.<BR>--2 Decent; cf. अश्लील.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मन्
श्लेष्मन् m. [श्लिष्-मनिन्] Phlegmatic<BR>humour.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अतिसारः<BR>dysentery produced by vitiated phlegm.<BR>--ओजस् n. the phlegmatic humour.<BR>--घ्ना, --घ्नी {1} the Arabian jasmine.<BR>{2} the hog-weed.<BR>--धातुः the<BR>phlegmatic humour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मकः|श्लेष्मक
श्लेष्मकः Phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मण|श्लेष्मणः
श्लेष्मण a. Phlegmatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मल|श्लेष्मलः
श्लेष्मल a. Phlegmatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मिक|श्लेष्मिकं
श्लेष्मिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Phlegmatic.<BR>--2 Producing phlegm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मातः|श्लेष्मात
श्लेष्मातः, श्लेष्मातकः A kind of<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लेष्मातकः|श्लेष्मातक
श्लेष्मातः, श्लेष्मातकः A kind of<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोक्
श्लोक् {c1c} A. (श्लोकते)<BR>1 To praise<BR>or compose in verse, versify.<BR>--2 To<BR>acquire.<BR>--3 To abandon, give up.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">Page1063-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--4 To heap together, collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1062-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोकः|श्लोक
श्लोकः [श्लोक् अच्]<BR>1 Praising in<BR>verse, extolling.<BR>--2 A hymn or<BR>verse of praise.<BR>--3 Celebrity, fame,<BR>renown, name; as in पुण्यश्लोक q. v.<BR>--4 An object of praise.<BR>--5 A<BR>proverb or saying.<BR>--6 A stanza or verse<BR>in general; श्लोकत्वमापद्यत यस्य<BR>शोकः R. 14. 70; पादैश्चतुरः संयुक्तमिदं<BR>वाक्यं समाक्षरैः । शोचतोक्तं मया<BR>यस्मात्तस्माच्छ्लोको भवत्विति Rām.<BR>--7 A<BR>stanza or verse in the Anuṣṭubh<BR>metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोकयति
श्लोकयति Den. P. To celebrate or<BR>praise in song.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोण्
श्लोण् {c1c} P. (श्लोणति) To heap<BR>together, collect, gather; cf. श्रोण्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्लोणः|श्लोण
श्लोणः A lame man, cripple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वंक्|श्वङ्क्
श्वंक् {c1c} A. (श्वंकते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वच्
श्वच्, श्वंच् {c1c} A. (श्वचते, श्वंचते)<BR>1<BR>To go, move.<BR>--2 To be opened,<BR>gape, be split or cleft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वंच्|श्वञ्च्
श्वच्, श्वंच् {c1c} A. (श्वचते, श्वंचते)<BR>1<BR>To go, move.<BR>--2 To be opened,<BR>gape, be split or cleft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वज्
श्वज् {c1c} A. (श्वजते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वठ्
श्वठ् {c10c} U. (श्वठयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>speak ill; (श्वठयति only according<BR>to some).<BR>--2 (श्वाठयति-ते) (a) To<BR>go, move. (b) To adorn. (c) To<BR>finish, accomplish; (only श्वठयाति in<BR>these senses according to some).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वंठ्
श्वंठ् {c10c} U. (श्वंठयति) To speak ill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वन्
श्वन् m. [श्वि-कनिन् नि˚<BR>Uṇ. 1. 158] (Nom. श्वा, श्वानौ, श्वानः; acc.<BR>pl. शुनः; शुनी f.) A dog; श्वा यदि<BR>क्रियते राजा स किं नाश्नात्युपानहं<BR>Subhāṣ.; Bh. 2. 31; Ms. 2. 208.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्वः an epithet of Bhairava.<BR>--क्रीडिन् m. a keeper or breeder of<BR>sporting dogs.<BR>--गणः a pack of<BR>hounds.<BR>--गणिकः {1} a hunter. {2}<BR>a dog-feeder.<BR>--धूर्तः a jackal.<BR>--नरः<BR>a snappish or currish fellow.<BR>--निशं, --निशा a night on which dogs<BR>bark.<BR>--पच् m.,<BR>--पचः {1} a man of a<BR>very low and degraded caste, an<BR>outcast, a Cāṇḍāla; Bv. 4. 23. {2}<BR>a dog-feeder. {3} a public executioner.<BR>--पदं {1} a dog's foot. {2} a mark<BR>like a dog's foot (to be branded on<BR>the forehead of a thief).<BR>--पाकः an<BR>outcast, a Cāṇḍāla; G. L. 29.<BR>--फलं<BR>lime or citron.<BR>--फल्कः N. of the<BR>father of Akrūra.<BR>--भीरुः a jackal.<BR>--यूथ्यं a pack of dogs.<BR>--वृत्तिः f. {1}<BR>the life of a dog (to which<BR>servitude is often likened); सेवां<BR>लाघवकारिणीं कृतधियः स्थाने श्ववृत्तिं बिदुः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">Page1063-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Mu. 3. 14; Ms. 4. 6. {2} servitude,<BR>service; Ms. 4. 4.<BR>--व्याघ्रः {1} a beast<BR>of prey. {2} a tiger. {3} a leopard.<BR>--हन् m. a hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्र्
श्वभ्र् {c10c} U. (श्वभ्रयति-ते)<BR>1 To go,<BR>move.<BR>--2 To pierce, make a hole,<BR>bore.<BR>--3 To live in misery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वभ्रं|श्वभ्र
श्वभ्रं<BR>1 A hole, chasm; महोरगः<BR>श्वभ्रमिव प्रविष्टं V. 1. 18; Ki. 14. 33.<BR>--2 A den.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयः|श्वय
श्वयः, श्वयनं Swelling, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयनं|श्वयन
श्वयः, श्वयनं Swelling, increase.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयथुः|श्वयथु
श्वयथुः Swelling, intumescence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वयीची
श्वयीची Sickness, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्
श्वल् {c1c} P. (श्वलति) To run, go<BR>quickly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्क्
श्वल्क् {c10c} U. (श्वल्कयति-ते) To tell,<BR>narrate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वल्ल्
श्वल्ल् {c1c} P. (श्वल्लति) To run; see<BR>श्वल्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुरः|श्वशुर
श्वशुरः [शु-आशु अश्नुते आशु-अश्<BR>उरच् पृषो˚ Uṇ. 1. 44]<BR>1 A<BR>father-inlaw, wife's or husband's father;<BR>Ms. 3. 119.<BR>--2 A respectable man.<BR>--रौ<BR>(dual) The father-in-law and<BR>motherin-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुरकः|श्वशुरक
श्वशुरकः A father-in-law,<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वशुर्यः|श्वशुर्य|श्वशुर्य्य|श्वशुर्य्यः
श्वशुर्यः<BR>1 A brother-in-law, a wife's<BR>or husband's brother.<BR>--2 The<BR>younger brother of a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वश्रूः
श्वश्रूः f. A mother-in-law, a wife's<BR>or husband's mother; R. 14. 13.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--श्वशुर m. du. the mother<BR>and father-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
श्वस् {c2c} P. (श्वसिति, श्वस्त or<BR>श्वसित)<BR>1 To breathe, respire, draw<BR>breath; स कर्मकारभस्त्रेव श्वसन्नपि न<BR>जीवति H. 2. 11. क्षणमप्यवतिष्ठते श्वसन्<BR>यहि जंतुर्ननु लाभवानसौ R. 8. 87.<BR>--2<BR>To sigh, pant, heave; श्वसिति<BR>विहगवर्गः Rs. 1. 13.<BR>--3 To hiss, snort.<BR>--Caus. (श्वासयति-ते) To cause to<BR>breathe or live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसनः|श्वसन|श्वसनं
श्वसनः [श्वसित्यनेन श्वस्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Air,<BR>wind; श्वसनसुरभिगंधिः Śi. 11. 21.<BR>--2<BR>N. of a demon killed by Indra.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Breath, breathing, respiration;<BR>श्वसनचलितपल्लवाधरोष्ठे Ki. 10. 34;<BR>Ratn. 2. 4 (where it has sense 1<BR>also); Śi. 9. 52.<BR>--2 Sighing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अशनः a serpent.<BR>--ईश्वरः<BR>the Arjuna tree.<BR>--उत्सुकः a serpent.<BR>--ऊर्मिः f. a gust of wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वसित|श्वसितं
श्वसित p. p. [श्वस्-क्त]<BR>1 Breathed,<BR>sighed.<BR>--2 Breathing.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Breathing, respiration.<BR>--2 Sighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासः|श्वास
श्वासः [श्वस्-घञ्]<BR>1 Breathing,<BR>breath, respiration, heaving;<BR>अद्यापि स्तनवेपथुं जनयति श्वासः प्रमाणाधिकः<BR>Ś. 1. 30; Ku. 2. 42.<BR>--2 A sigh,<BR>panting.<BR>--3 Air, wind.<BR>--4 Asthma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उच्छ्वासः exhalation and<BR>inhalation, respiration.<BR>--कासः<BR>asthma.<BR>--कुठारः a drug used to<BR>cure asthma.<BR>--धारणं = प्राणायाम.<BR>--रोधः<BR>suspension or obstruction of breath<BR>--हिक्का a kind of hiccough.<BR>--हेतिः<BR>f. sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वासिन्
श्वासिन् a. [श्वासयति श्वस्-णिच् णिनि]<BR>Breathing. --m.<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>--2<BR>A breathing animal, living being.<BR>--3 One who pronounces (letters).<BR>with a his sing sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्
श्वस् ind.<BR>1 Tomorrow; वरमद्य<BR>कपोतो न श्वो मयूरः Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Future<BR>(at the beginning of comp.)<BR>--3 A<BR>particle implying auspiciousness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भूत a. (श्वोभूत) being<BR>tomorrow.<BR>--वसीय, --वसीयस् (<BR>श्वोवसीय, श्वोवसीयस्) a. happy, auspicious,<BR>fortunate. (--n.) happiness, good<BR>fortune.<BR>--श्रेयस् (श्वःश्रेयस) a.<BR>happy, prosperous.<BR>--(सं) {1}<BR>happiness, prosperity. {2} an epithet<BR>of Brahman or the Supreme Spirit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वस्तन|श्वस्तनं
श्वस्तन a. (नी f.), श्वस्त्य a.<BR>Relating to the morrow, future.<BR>--नं The<BR>future.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्वि
श्वि {c1c} P. (श्वयति, शिश्वाय-शुशाव,<BR>अश्वत्-अश्वयीत्-अशिश्वियत्, श्वयिष्यति,<BR>श्वयितुं, शून)<BR>1 To grow, increase (fig.<BR>also), to swell (as the eye);<BR>रुदतोऽशिश्वियच्चक्षुरास्यं हेतोस्तवाश्वयीत्<BR>Bk. 6. 19, 31; 14. 79, 15. 30.<BR>--2 To<BR>thrive, prosper.<BR>--3 To go, approach,<BR>move towards. --WITH उद् {1}<BR>to swell, increase, grow;<BR>प्रबलरुदितोच्छूननेत्रं (मुखं) Me. 84. {2} to be<BR>proud, be puffed up with pride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1063-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

