षंढः<BR>1 A eunuch; Y. 1. 215.<BR>--2<BR>The neuter gender; निवेशः शिबिरं<BR>षंढे Ak.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तिलः barren<BR>sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्
षष् num. a. (used in pl., nom.<BR>षट्; gen. षण्णां) Six; Ms. 1. 16,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1064-1c" target="_blank">Page1064-1c+ 16</a>]<BR>8. 403.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षीणः (षडक्षीणः)<BR>a fish.<BR>--अंगं (षडंगं) {1} six parts<BR>of the body taken collectively:--जंघे<BR>बाहू शिरो मध्यं षडंगमिदमुच्यते. {2} the<BR>six works auxiliary to the Veda;<BR>शिक्षा कल्पो व्याकरणं निरुक्तं छंदसां चितिः ।<BR>ज्योतिषामयनं चैव षडंगो वेद उच्यते;<BR>see वेदांग also. {3} six<BR>auspicious things, i. e. the six things<BR>obtained from a cow:--गोमूत्रं गोमयं क्षीरं<BR>सर्पिर्दधि च रोचना । षडगमेतन् मांगल्यं<BR>पठितं सर्वदा गवाम्. {3} any set of six<BR>articles. ˚जित् m. N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--अंघ्रिः (षडंघ्रिः) a bee.<BR>--अधिक a. (<BR>षडधिक) exceeded by six; Māl. 5. 1.<BR>--अभिज्ञः (षडभिज्ञः) a Buddhist<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1065-a" target="_blank">Page1065-a+ 57</a>]<BR>deified saint.<BR>--अशीत a. (षडशीत)<BR>eighty-sixth.<BR>--अशीतः f. (षडशीतिः)<BR>eighty-six.<BR>--अहः (षडहः) a period<BR>of six days.<BR>--आननः, --वक्त्रः, --वदनः<BR>(षडाननः, षड्वक्त्रः, षड्वदनः) epithets<BR>of Kārtikeya; षडाननापीतपयोधरासु<BR>नेता चमूनामिव कृत्तिकासु R. 14. 22.<BR>--आम्नायः (षडाम्नायः) the six-fold<BR>Tantra.<BR>--ऊषणं (षडूषणं) six spices<BR>taken collectively; पंचक्रोलं समरिचं<BR>षडूषणमुदाहृतम्.<BR>--कर्ण a. (षट्कर्ण)<BR>heard by six ears; i. e. by a third<BR>person other than the speaker and<BR>the person spoken to, told to more<BR>than one listener (as a counsel,<BR>secret &c.); षट्कर्णो भिद्यते मंत्रः<BR>Pt. 1. 99.<BR>--(र्णः) a kind of lute.<BR>--कर्मन् n. (षट्कर्मन्) {1} the six acts or<BR>duties enjoined on a Brāhmaṇa;<BR>they are:--अध्यापनमध्ययनं यजनं याजनं<BR>तथा । दानं प्रतिग्रहश्चैव षट्कर्माण्यग्रजन्मनः<BR>Ms. 10. 75. {2} the six acts<BR>allowable to a Brāhmaṇa for his<BR>subsistence; उंछं प्रतिग्रहो भिक्षा<BR>वाणिज्यं पशुपालन । कृषिकर्म तथा चेति<BR>षट्कर्माण्यग्रजन्मनः ॥. {3} the six acts<BR>that may be performed by means of<BR>magic; शांति, वशकिरण, स्तंभत, विद्वेष,<BR>उच्चाटन, and मारण. {4} the six acts<BR>belonging to the practice of Yoga;<BR>धौतिर्वस्ती तथा नेती नीलिकी (नौलिकी)<BR>त्राटकस्तथा । कपालभाती चैतानि षट्कर्माणि<BR>समाचरेत्. (--m.) {1} a Brāhmaṇa<BR>skilled in the above six acts.<BR>{2} one well-versed in the Tantra<BR>magical rites.<BR>--कोण a. (षटकोण)<BR>hexangular.<BR>--(णं) {1} a hexagon.<BR>{2} the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>--गया<BR>the sixfold gayā; गयागजो गयादित्यो<BR>गायत्री च गदाधरः । गया गयासुरश्चैव षड्गया<BR>मुक्तिदायकाः ॥.<BR>--गवं (षड्गवं) {1} a<BR>team or yoke of six oxen. {2} a<BR>yoke of six (sometimes after the<BR>names of other animals); e. g.<BR>हस्ति˚, अश्व˚ ‘six elephants, horses<BR>&c.’.<BR>--गुण a. (षड्गुण) {1} sixfold.<BR>{2} having six attributes.<BR>--(णं) an<BR>assemblage of six qualities. {2} the<BR>six expedients to be used by a<BR>king in foreign polities; see under<BR>गुण (21); cf. षाड्गुण्य also.<BR>--ग्रंथि n.<BR>(षड्ग्रंथि) the root of long pepper.<BR>--ग्रांथिका (षड्ग्रंथिका) zedoary (शठी).<BR>--चक्रं (षट्चक्रं) the six mystical<BR>circles of the body.<BR>--चत्वारिंशत् (<BR>षट्चत्वारिंशत्) forty-six.<BR>--चरणः (<BR>षट्चरणः) {1} a bee; Ś. 1. 23. {2}<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1065-b" target="_blank">Page1065-b+ 57</a>]<BR>a locust. {3} a louse.<BR>--जः<BR>(षड्जः) the fourth (or first<BR>according to some) of the seven<BR>primary notes of the Indian gamut;<BR>so called because it is derived from<BR>the six organs:<BR>--नासां कंठमुरस्तालु<BR>जिह्वां दतांश्च संस्पृशन् । षड्जः संजायते (षड्भ्यः<BR>संजायते) यस्मात्तस्मात् षड्ज इति स्मृतः; it<BR>is said^1 to resemble the note of<BR>peacocks; षड्जं रौति मयूरस्तु Nārada;<BR>षड्जसंवादितीः केकाः द्विधा भिन्नाः<BR>शिवंडिभिः R. 1. 39.<BR>--त्रिंशत् f. (<BR>षट्त्रिंशत्) thirty-six; (षट्त्रिंश a.<BR>thirtysixth).<BR>--दर्शनं (षडदर्शनं) the six<BR>principal systems of Hindu<BR>philosophy; they are:--सांख्य, योग, न्याय,<BR>वैशेषिक, मीमांसा, and वेदांत.<BR>--(नः) one<BR>conversant with the above six<BR>systems.<BR>--दीर्घः the six long vowels:--<BR>आ, ई, ऊ, ऐ, and औ.<BR>--दुर्गं (षड्दुर्गं) the<BR>six kinds of forts taken collectively;<BR>धन्वदुर्गं महीदुर्गं गिरिदुर्गं तथैव च । मनुष्यदुर्गं<BR>मृद्दुर्गं वनदुर्गामिति क्रमात् ।.<BR>--नवति f. (<BR>षण्णवतिः) ninety-six.<BR>--पंचाशत् f. (<BR>षट्पंचाशत्) fifty-six.<BR>--पदः (षट्पदः)<BR>{1} a bee; न पंकजं तद्यदलीनषट्दं<BR>न षट्पदोऽसौ न जुगुंज यः कलं<BR>Bk. 2. 19; Ku. 5. 9;<BR>R. 6. 69. {2} a louse. {3} a verse<BR>consisting of six padas. ˚अतिथिः<BR>{1} the mango tree. {2} the<BR>Champaka tree. ˚आनंदवर्धनः the Aśoka or<BR>Kinkirāta tree. ˚ज्य a. having bees for<BR>the bow-string (as the bow of<BR>Cupid); प्रायश्चापं न वहति भयान्मन्मथः<BR>षट्पदज्यं Me. 73. ˚प्रियः the tree<BR>called नागकेशर.<BR>--पदी (षट्पदी) {1}<BR>a stanza consisting of six lines.<BR>{2} a female bee. {3} a louse.<BR>--प्रज्ञः<BR>(षट्प्रज्ञः) {1} one who is well<BR>acquainted with six subjects; i. e.<BR>the four Puruṣārthas or objects of<BR>human existence, the nature of the<BR>world, and the nature of the<BR>Supreme Spirit; धर्मार्यकाममोक्षेषु<BR>लोकतत्त्वार्थयोरपि । षट्सु प्रज्ञा तु यस्यासौ<BR>षट्प्रज्ञः परिकीर्तितः ॥. {2} a lustful<BR>or licentious man.<BR>--बिंदुः (षड्बिंदुः)<BR>an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--भागः (<BR>षड्भागः) a sixth part,<BR>onesixth; Ś. 2. 13; Ms. 7. 131,<BR>8. 33.<BR>--भुज a. (षड्भुज) {1}<BR>six-armed. {2} six-sided, hexagonal.<BR>--(जः)<BR>a hexagon.<BR>--(जा) {1} an epithet<BR>of Durgā. {2} the water-melon.<BR>--मासः (षण्मासः) a period of<BR>six months.<BR>--मासिक a. (<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1065-c" target="_blank">Page1065-c+ 57</a>]<BR>षण्मासिक) half-yearly, occurring every<BR>six months.<BR>--मुखः (षण्मुखः) an<BR>epithet of Kārtikeya; R. 17. 67.<BR>--(खा) a water-melon.<BR>--रसं, --रसाः<BR>(m. pl.) (षड्रसं &c.) the six<BR>flavours taken collectively; see under<BR>रस.<BR>--रात्रं (षड्रात्रं) a period of six<BR>nights.<BR>--रेखा (षड्रेखा) a water-melon.<BR>--वर्गः (षड्वर्गः) {1} an aggregate of six<BR>things. {2} especially, the six<BR>enemies of mankind; (also called षड्रिपु);<BR>कामः क्रोधस्तथा लोभो मदमोहौ च मत्सरः;<BR>कृतारिषड्वर्गजयेन Ki. 1. 9; व्यजेष्ट<BR>षड्वर्गं Bk. 1. 2.<BR>--विंशतिः f. (<BR>षड्विंशतिः) twenty-six; (षड्विंश<BR>twentysixth).<BR>--विध (षड्विध) a. of six<BR>kinds, sixfold; R. 4. 26.<BR>--शास्त्रिन्<BR>m. one conversant with the six<BR>Śāstras or darśanas.<BR>--षष्टिः f. (<BR>षट्षष्टिः) sixty-six.<BR>--सप्ततिः (षट्सप्ततिः)<BR>seventy-six.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1064-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षट्क|षट्कः
षट्क a. Sixfold.<BR>--कं An<BR>aggregate of six; मासषट्क, पूर्वषट्क,<BR>उत्तरषट्क &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षड्धा
षड्धा See षोढा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिः|षष्टि
षष्टिः f. Sixty: Ms. 3. 177;<BR>Y. 3. 84. ˚तम sixtieth.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भागः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--मत्तः an<BR>elephant who has reached the age of<BR>sixty and is in rut at that time.<BR>--योजनी f. a journey or extent of<BR>sixty Yojanas.<BR>--संवत्सरः a period<BR>of sixty years.<BR>--हायनः {1} an<BR>elephant (sixty years old). {2} a kind<BR>of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक|षष्टिकः
षष्टिक a. Bought with sixty.<BR>--कः<BR>--का A kind of rice of quick growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्टिक्यं|षष्टिक्य
षष्टिक्यं A field sown with the<BR>above kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठ|षष्ठः
षष्ठ a. (ष्ठी f.) Sixth, the sixth;<BR>षष्ठं तु क्षेत्रजस्याशं प्रदद्यात्पैतृकाद्धतात्<BR>Ms. 9. 164, 7. 130; षष्ठे भागे<BR>V. 2. 1; R. 17. 78.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः {1} a<BR>sixth part in general. {2}<BR>particularly, the sixth part of the produce<BR>of fields &c., which the king takes<BR>from his subjects as land-tax;<BR>ऊधस्यमिच्छामि तवोपभोक्तुं षष्ठांशमुर्व्या<BR>इव रक्षितायाः R. 2. 66; (the<BR>different kinds of produce, to the sixth<BR>part of which a king is entitled, are<BR>specified in Ms. 7. 131-132). ˚वृत्तिः<BR>a king (entitled to the sixth<BR>part of the produce); षष्ठांशवृत्तेरपि<BR>धर्म एषः Ś. 5. 4.<BR>--अन्नं the sixth<BR>meal. ˚कालः taking food once in<BR>three days, as an expiatory act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1065-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षष्ठी
षष्ठी<BR>1 The sixth day of a lunar<BR>fortnight<BR>--2 The sixth or genitive<BR>case (in gram.).<BR>--3 An epithet of<BR>Durgā in the form of Kātyāyanī,<BR>one of the 16 divine mothers.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तत्पुरुषः the genitive<BR>Tatpurusha compound, one in which,<BR>when dissolved, the first member<BR>usually stands in the genitive case.<BR>--पूजनं, --पूजा worship of the<BR>goddess षष्ठी performed on the sixth<BR>day after a woman's delivery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षहसानुः|षहसानु
षहसानुः<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>--2 A<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्
षाट् ind. A vocative particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्कौशिक
षाट्कौशिक a. (की f.) Incased<BR>or enveloped in six sheaths.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाट्पौरुषिक
षाट्पौरुषिक a. (की f.)<BR>Belonging to six generations (पुरुष).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाडवः|षाडव
षाडवः<BR>1 Passion, sentiment.<BR>--2<BR>Singing, music.<BR>--3 (In music) A<BR>Rāga in which six of the seven<BR>primary notes are used, औडवः<BR>पंचभिः प्रोक्तः स्वरैः षड्भिस्तु षाडवः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाड्गुण्यं|षाड्गुण्य
षाड्गुण्यं [षड् गुणा एव ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>The collection of six<BR>qualities.<BR>--2 Six expedients to<BR>be used by a king, six measures<BR>of royal policy; षाड्गुण्यमुपयुंजीत<BR>शक्त्यपेक्षी रसायनं Śi. 2. 93; see<BR>under गुण also.<BR>--3 Multiplication<BR>of anything by six.<BR>--4 Six<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-b" target="_blank">Page1066-b+ 32</a>]<BR>properties.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रयोगः<BR>employment of the six expedients or<BR>measures of royal policy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाण्मातुरः|षाण्मातुर
षाण्मातुरः [षड् मातरोऽस्य]<BR>‘Having six mothers,’ an epithet of<BR>Kārtikeya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाण्मासिक
षाण्मासिक a. (की f.) Six<BR>monthly, half-yearly. {2} Six months’<BR>old; मौक्तिकानां षाण्मासिकानां Vb. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षाष्ठ|षाष्ठः
षाष्ठ (ष्ठी f.) Sixth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षिड्गः|षिड्ग
षिड्गः<BR>1 A lustful or libidinous<BR>man, libertine, lecher.<BR>--2 A gallant,<BR>an inconsistent lover (विट);<BR>षिड्गैरगद्यत ससंभ्रममेव काचित् Śi. 5. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षुः|षु
षुः Delivery, child-bearing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशन्
षोडशन् num. a. (pl.) Sixteen.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुः the planet Venus.<BR>--अंग a. having 16 parts or<BR>ingredients.<BR>--(गः) a kind of perfume.<BR>--अंगुलक a. having the breadth of<BR>16 fingers.<BR>--अंध्रिः a crab.<BR>--अर्चिस्<BR>m. the planet Venus.<BR>--आवर्तः a<BR>conch-shell.<BR>--उपचार m. pl. the<BR>sixteen ways of doing homage to a<BR>deity &c.: they are thus<BR>enumerated:--आसनं स्वागतं पाद्यमर्घ्यमाचमनीयकम् ।<BR>मधुपर्काचम नानं वसनाभरणानि च ।<BR>गंधपुष्पे धूपदीपौ नैवेद्यं वंदनं तथा.<BR>--कलाः the sixteen digits of the<BR>moon, thus named:--अमृता<BR>मानदा पूषा तुष्टिः पुष्टी रतिर्धृतिः । शशिनी चंद्रिका<BR>कांतिर्ज्योत्स्ना श्रीः प्रीतिरेव च । अंगदा च तथा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">Page1066-c+ 32</a>]<BR>पूर्णामृता षोडश वै कलाः ॥.<BR>--भुजा a form<BR>of Durgā.<BR>--मातृका f. pl. the<BR>sixteen divine mothers; they are:<BR>--गौरी पद्मा शची मेघा सावित्री विजया जया ।<BR>देवसेना स्वधा स्वाहा मातरो लोकमातरः । शांतिः<BR>पुष्टिर्धृतिस्तुष्टिः कुलदेवात्मदेवताः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडश|षोडशः
षोडश a. (शी f.) Sixteenth;<BR>Ms. 2. 65, 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशधा
षोडशधा ind. In sixteen ways.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशिक
षोडशिक a. (की f.) Consisting<BR>of sixteen parts, sixteen-fold<BR>षोडशिको देवतोयचारः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोडशिन्
षोडशिन् m. A modification of the<BR>Agniṣṭoma sacrifice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रहः<BR>a libation made at the above<BR>sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोढा
षोढा ind. In six ways.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--न्यासः the six ways of<BR>touching the body with mystical<BR>texts.<BR>--मुखः ‘six-faced’, N. of<BR>Kārtikeya; द्रोढा जनोर्जनितषोढामुखः<BR>समिति वोढा स हाटकगिरेः Aśvad. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

षोदत्
षोदत् m. A young ox with six<BR>teeth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठिव्
ष्ठिव् {1} {c4c} P. (ष्ठीवति, ष्ठीव्यति,<BR>ष्ठ्यूत)<BR>1 To spit, eject saliva from the<BR>mouth.<BR>--2 To sputter; Bk. 12. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठीवनं|ष्ठीवन
ष्ठीवनं, ष्ठेवनं<BR>1 Spitting out.<BR>--2<BR>Saliva, spittle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठेवनं|ष्ठेवन
ष्ठीवनं, ष्ठेवनं<BR>1 Spitting out.<BR>--2<BR>Saliva, spittle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्ठ्यूत
ष्ठ्यूत p. p. Spit, ejected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वक्क्
ष्वक्क्, ष्वस्क् --ष्क् {c1c} A. (ष्वक्कते,<BR>ष्वस्कष्कते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वस्क्
ष्वक्क्, ष्वस्क् --ष्क् {c1c} A. (ष्वक्कते,<BR>ष्वस्कष्कते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ष्वष्क्
ष्वक्क्, ष्वस्क् --ष्क् {c1c} A. (ष्वक्कते,<BR>ष्वस्कष्कते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स|सं|सः
स ind. A prefix substituted for<BR>सह or सम्, सम, तुल्य, or सदृश and एक<BR>or समान, and compounded with<BR>nouns to form adjectives and<BR>adverbs in the sense of (a) with,<BR>together with, along with,<BR>accompanied by, having, possessed of;<BR>सपुत्र, सभार्य, सतृष्ण, सधन, सरोषं,<BR>सकोपं, सहरि &c.; (b) similar, like;<BR>सधर्मन् ‘of a similar nature’; so<BR>सजाति, सवर्ण; (c) same; सोदर, सपक्ष,<BR>सपिंड, सनाभि &c. --m.<BR>1 A snake.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-1b" target="_blank">Page1066-1b+ 12</a>]<BR>--2 Air, wind.<BR>--3 A bird.<BR>--4 short<BR>name for the musical note षड्ज q. v.<BR>--5 N. of Śiva.<BR>--6 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>--7<BR>(In prosody) A foot consisting of<BR>two short syllables followed by a<BR>long one.<BR>--सा The goddess<BR>Lakṣmī.<BR>--सं<BR>1 Knowledge.<BR>--2<BR>Meditation.<BR>--3 A carriage-road.<BR>--4 A<BR>fence, an enclosure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयः|संय
संयः A skeleton.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयज्
संयज् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To adore,<BR>worship; समयष्टास्त्रमंडलं Bk. 15. 96.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-1c" target="_blank">Page1066-1c+ 12</a>]<BR>To consecrate, dedicate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत्|संयन्त्
संयत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To struggle,<BR>contend; देवासुरा वा एषु लोकेषु संयेतिरे.<BR>--2<BR>To form or be formed in rows.<BR>--3<BR>To agree, coincide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत्|संयन्त्
संयत् f. A battle, war, fight; यः<BR>संयति प्राप्तपिनाकिलीलः R. 6. 72,<BR>7. 39; 18. 21; Ki. 1. 19; Śi. 16. 15.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वरः a king, prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत्त
संयत्त p. p.<BR>1 Ready, prepared;<BR>Mv. 5. 51.<BR>--2 Being on guard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयम्
संयम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To restrain, curb,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-a" target="_blank">Page1067-a+ 56</a>]<BR>check, control, govern, subdue<BR>(Atm.) (as passions &c.);<BR>असंयतात्मनो योगो दुष्प्राप इति मे मतिः<BR>Bg. 6. 36; Ms. 2. 100.<BR>--2 To bind,<BR>imprison, fasten, confine; वातरं मा न<BR>संयंसीः Bk. 9. 50; M. 1. 7; R. 3. 20,<BR>42.<BR>--3 To gather (Atm.); व्री<BR>हीन्संयच्छते Sk.<BR>--4 To shut, close;<BR>Bg. 8. 12.<BR>--5 To hold together, hold<BR>fast.<BR>--6 To guide or drive (as horses).<BR>--7 (a) To collect. (b) To bind<BR>or tie into a knot (as hair);<BR>संयम्यमानशिखंडः V. 5.<BR>--8 To keep in<BR>order.<BR>--9 To present with, give to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1066-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत|संयतः
संयत p. p.<BR>1 Restrained, curbed,<BR>subdued.<BR>--2 Tied up, bound<BR>together.<BR>--3 Fettered.<BR>--4 Captive,<BR>imprisoned, a prisoner; R. 3. 20.<BR>--5<BR>Ready.<BR>--6 Arranged; see यम् with<BR>सं.<BR>--तः<BR>1 One who has restrained<BR>his passions, an ascetic.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a. one whose<BR>eyes are closed.<BR>--अंनलि a. one<BR>who has folded his hands in<BR>supplication.<BR>--आत्मन् a. self-subdued,<BR>self-controlled.<BR>--आहार a.<BR>temperate in eating.<BR>--उपस्कर a. one who<BR>has a well-regulated house, whose<BR>house-furniture is kept in good<BR>order.<BR>--चेतसू, --मनस् a. controlled<BR>in mind.<BR>--प्राण a. one whose breath<BR>is suppressed.<BR>--वाच् a. silent,<BR>taciturn, one who has held his<BR>tongue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयत्वर|संयत्वरः
संयत्वर a. Silent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयंतृ|संयन्तृ
संयंतृ m. One who restrains, a<BR>restrainer, curber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमः|संयम
संयमः<BR>1 Restraint, check, control;<BR>श्रोत्रादीनींद्रियाण्यन्ये संयमाग्निषु जुह्वति<BR>Bg. 4. 26, 27; so संयमधनः &c.<BR>--2<BR>Concentration of mind, a term<BR>applied to the last three stages of<BR>Yoga; धारणाध्यानसमाधित्रयमंतरंगं<BR>संयमपदवाच्यं Sarva. S., Ku. 2. 59.<BR>--3 A religious vow.<BR>--4 Religious<BR>devotion, practice of penance;<BR>Ś. 4. 16.<BR>--5 Humanity, feeling of<BR>compassion.<BR>--6 Any religious act on the<BR>day preceding a vow or course of<BR>penance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमनं|संयमन|संयमनः
संयमनं<BR>1 Restraining, checking.<BR>--2 Drawing in; Ś. 1.<BR>--3 Binding,<BR>tying up; U. 1; V. 3. 6.<BR>--4<BR>Confinement.<BR>--5 Self-denial, control.<BR>--6 A religious vow or obligation.<BR>--7 A square of four houses.<BR>--नः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">Page1067-b+ 56</a>]<BR>One who restrains or regulates, a<BR>ruler.<BR>--नी N. of the city of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमित|संयमितः
संयमित p. p.<BR>1 Restrained.<BR>--2<BR>Bound, fettered.<BR>--3 Detained.<BR>--4<BR>Assembled, collected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयमिन्
संयमिन् a. One who curbs or<BR>restrains, controlling. --m. One who<BR>controls or subdues his passions, a<BR>sage, an ascetic; या निशा सर्वभूतानां<BR>तस्यां जागर्ति संयमी Bg. 2. 69;<BR>R. 8. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संया
संया {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go or proceed<BR>together.<BR>--2 To go away, depart, walk<BR>away; Bg. 15. 8.<BR>--3 To go to, go or<BR>enter into; तथा शरीराणि विहाय<BR>जीर्णान्यन्यानि संयाति नवानि देही<BR>Bg. 2. 22.<BR>--4 To reach or attain to.<BR>--5 To<BR>assemble, meet.<BR>--6 To fight.<BR>--7 To<BR>be directed towards, aim at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयात्रा
संयात्रा Voyage by sea.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयानः|संयान|संयानं
संयानः A mould.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Going<BR>along with, accompanying.<BR>--2<BR>Travelling, proceeding.<BR>--3 Carrying<BR>out a dead body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयाम|संयामः
संयाम See संयम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयावः|संयाव
संयावः A kind of cake of<BR>wheaten flour; Ms. 5. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुज्
संयुज् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To join together,<BR>connect, unite.<BR>--2 To endow or<BR>furnish with.<BR>--3 To form an<BR>alliance.<BR>--4 To place or fix in, set in.<BR>--Pass. To be united with;<BR>संयोक्ष्यसे स्वेन वर्पुमहिम्ना R. 5. 55. --Caus.<BR>1 To unite, join; संयोजयति विद्यैव<BR>नीचगापि नरंसरित् H. 1.<BR>--2 To<BR>harness, yoke.<BR>--3 To prepare, equip<BR>(an army).<BR>--4 To furnish, endow<BR>or supply with, provide with;<BR>बुद्ध्या संयो जयंति तं Pt. 2.<BR>--5 To<BR>fasten or fix on.<BR>--6 To throw,<BR>discharge, shoot (a missile).<BR>--7 To<BR>use, employ.<BR>--8 To appoint (to an<BR>office), entrust with.<BR>--9 To<BR>perform, accomplish. --To be absorbed<BR>in, meditate upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुक्त|संयुक्तः
संयुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Joined,<BR>connected, united.<BR>--2 Blended, mixed,<BR>mingled.<BR>--3 Accompanied by.<BR>--4<BR>Possessed of, endowed with.<BR>--5<BR>Consisting of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुगः|संयुग
संयुगः<BR>1 Conjunction, union,<BR>mixture.<BR>--2 Fight, war, battle, contest;<BR>संयुगे सांयुगीनं तमुद्यतं प्रसहेत कः<BR>Ku. 2. 57; R. 9. 19.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गोष्पदं<BR>‘a contest in a cow's footstep’; i. e.<BR>an insignificant or trifling quarrel;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">Page1067-c+ 56</a>]<BR>cf. the English phrase ‘a storm<BR>in a tea-pot’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुज्
संयुज् a.<BR>1 Connected, relating to;<BR>Śi. 14. 55.<BR>--2 Possessed of or<BR>endowed with good qualities.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोगः|संयोग
संयोगः<BR>1 (a) Conjunction, union,<BR>combination, junction, association,<BR>intimate union; संयोगो हि वियोगस्य<BR>संसूचयति संभवं Subhāṣ. (b)<BR>Endowment with, possession of.<BR>--2<BR>Conjunction (as one of the 24 guṇas of<BR>the Vaiśeṣikas).<BR>--3 Addition,<BR>annexation.<BR>--4 A set; आभरणसंयोगाः<BR>Māl. 6.<BR>--5 Alliance between two<BR>kings for a common object.<BR>--6 (In<BR>gram.) A conjunct consonant;<BR>हलोऽनंतराः संयोगः P. I. 1. 7.<BR>--7 (In<BR>astr.) The conjunction of two<BR>heavenly bodies.<BR>--8 An epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पृथक्त्वं severalty of<BR>conjunction.<BR>--विरुद्धं any eatables<BR>causing disease by being mixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोगिन्
संयोगिन् a.<BR>1 United, conjoined.<BR>--2 Joining.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयोजनं|संयोजन
संयोजनं<BR>1 Union, conjunction.<BR>--2 Copulation, sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संयुत|संयुतः
संयुत p. p.<BR>1 Joined, united<BR>together, connected.<BR>--2 Endowed or<BR>furnished with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्ष्
संरक्ष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To protect.<BR>--2 To<BR>ward off, prevent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्षः|संरक्ष
संरक्षः Protection, care,<BR>preservation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्षणं|संरक्षण
संरक्षणं<BR>1 Protection, preservation.<BR>--2 Charge, custody.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरंज्|संरञ्ज्
संरंज् {c4c} U.<BR>1 To be dyed or<BR>coloured, to redden.<BR>--2 To be<BR>affected with any passion. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>dye, colour.<BR>--2 To please, satisfy,<BR>gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरक्त
संरक्त p. p.<BR>1 Coloured, red.<BR>--2<BR>Impassioned fired with passion.<BR>--3<BR>Angry, irritated, inflamed with<BR>anger.<BR>--4 Enamoured, charmed.<BR>--5<BR>Charming, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरागः|संराग
संरागः<BR>1 Colouring.<BR>--2 Passion,<BR>affection.<BR>--3 Rage, anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरभ्
संरभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To become agitated,<BR>be overwhelmed or affected.<BR>--2 To<BR>be exasperated or furious, be<BR>enraged or irritated (mostly in p. p.);<BR>R. 16. 16.<BR>--3 To seize, catch hold<BR>of (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरब्ध
संरब्ध p. p.<BR>1 Excited, agitated.<BR>--2 Inflamed, exasperated, enraged,<BR>furious.<BR>--3 Augmented.<BR>--4 Swelled.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">Page1068-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--5 Overwhelmed.<BR>--6 Closely<BR>joined, hand in hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1067-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरंभः|संरम्भ|संरंभ|संरम्भः
संरंभः<BR>1 Beginning.<BR>--2 Turbulence,<BR>impetuosity, violence; हंत वर्धंते ते<BR>संरंभः Ś. 7.<BR>--3 Agitation,<BR>excitement, flurry; Ku. 3. 48;<BR>Māl. 6. 10.<BR>--4 Energy, zeal, ardent desire;<BR>R. 12. 92.<BR>--5 Anger, rage, wrath;<BR>प्रणिपातप्रतीकारः संरंभो हि महात्मनां<BR>R. 4. 64; 12. 36; V. 2. 21; 4. 28;<BR>Ku. 3. 76.<BR>--6 Pride, arrogance.<BR>--7<BR>Swelling with heat and<BR>inflammation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--परुष a. harsh<BR>through rage.<BR>--रस a. excessively<BR>enraged.<BR>--वेगः the impetuosity of<BR>anger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरंभिन्|संरम्भिन्
संरंभिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>1 Excited,<BR>agitated, flurried; Śi. 2. 67.<BR>--2<BR>Angry, furious, enraged.<BR>--3 Proud,<BR>arrogant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराध्
संराध् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be accomplished<BR>or perfected.<BR>--2 To be acquired.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To bring into harmony.<BR>--2 To agree about or upon (with<BR>acc.)<BR>--3 To propitiate, satisfy,<BR>conciliate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संराधनं|संराधन
संराधनं<BR>1 Propitiation,<BR>conciliation, pleasing by worship.<BR>--2<BR>Accomplishing.<BR>--3 Profound or deep<BR>meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरावः|संराव
संरावः<BR>1 Clamour, tumult,<BR>uproar.<BR>--2 Sound or noise in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरिहाणं|संरिहाण
संरिहाणं Affectionately licking<BR>(as a cow licking her calf).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरुग्ण
संरुग्ण p. p. Shattered, broken<BR>to pieces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरुध्
संरुध् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To obstruct,<BR>detain, stop; स चेत्तु पाथ संरुद्धः<BR>पशभिर्वा रथेन वा Ms. 8. 295.<BR>--2 To<BR>impede, obstruct, prevent;<BR>रांरुद्धचेष्टस्य R. 2. 43.<BR>--3 To hold fast,<BR>enchain; तृणमिव लघु लक्ष्मीर्नैव तान्<BR>संरुणद्धि Bh. 2. 17.<BR>--4 To seize<BR>upon, grasp, catch hold of;<BR>Ms. 8. 235.<BR>--5 To besiege, blockade,<BR>invest.<BR>--6 To cover up, conceal.<BR>--7<BR>To withhold, refuse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरुद्ध
संरुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Checked,<BR>impeded, opposed.<BR>--2 Blocked up,<BR>filled up.<BR>--3 Blockaded,<BR>invested, besieged.<BR>--4 Covered over,<BR>concealed.<BR>--5 Refused, withheld.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरोधः|संरोध
संरोधः<BR>1 Complete obstruction or<BR>impediment, hindrance, prevention,<BR>check.<BR>--2 Blockade, siege.<BR>--3 Bond,<BR>fetter.<BR>--4 Throwing, sending forth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरोधनं|संरोधन
संरोधनं Obstructing, stopping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरुह्
संरुह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To grow, increase.<BR>--2 To grow over, heal; see रुह्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संरूढ|संरूढः
संरूढ p. p.<BR>1 Grown together.<BR>--2<BR>Cicatrized, healed; as in संरूढव्रण.<BR>--3 Shot forth, sprouted, budded,<BR>germinated; R. 6. 47.<BR>--4 Firmly<BR>grown, striking firm root.<BR>--5 Bold,<BR>confident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलक्ष्
संलक्ष् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To observe,<BR>perceive, see, notice; आश्चर्यदर्शनः<BR>संलक्ष्यते मनुष्यलोकः Ś. 7; संलक्ष्यते न<BR>छिदुरोपि हारः R. 16. 62 ‘is not<BR>noticed or known’; 8. 42.<BR>--2 To<BR>test, prove, determine; हेम्नः संलक्ष्यते<BR>ह्यग्नौ विशुद्धिः श्यामिकापि वा R. 1. 10.<BR>--3 To hear, learn, understand.<BR>--4<BR>To characterize, distinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलक्षणं|संलक्षण
संलक्षणं Marking, distinguishing<BR>or characterizing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलग्न|संलग्नः
संलग्न p. p.<BR>1 Closely attached,<BR>stuck together, united with,<BR>adhering to.<BR>--2 Come to blows or<BR>close contest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलप्
संलप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To talk, converse;<BR>संलपतो जनसमाजात् Dk.<BR>--2 To name,<BR>call.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलापः|संलाप
संलापः<BR>1 Conversation, chat,<BR>discourse.<BR>--2 Especially familiar or<BR>confidential talk, secret<BR>conversation.<BR>--3 (In dramas) A kind<BR>of dialogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलापकः|संलापक
संलापकः A kind of minor drama,<BR>said to be of a controversial kind;<BR>see S. D. 549.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संललित
संललित p. p. Fondled, caressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलिख्
संलिख् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To scratch, scrape.<BR>--2 To write, inscribe.<BR>--3 To play<BR>upon (a musical instrument).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलीढ
संलीढ p. p. Licked up; enjoyed,<BR>tasted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संली
संली {c4c} A.<BR>1 To cling, adhere<BR>or stick to.<BR>--2 To lie down or settle<BR>upon, alight.<BR>--3 To lurk.<BR>--4 To<BR>melt away.<BR>--5 To go or enter into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलयः|संलय
संलयः<BR>1 Lying down, sleep.<BR>--2<BR>Dissolution.<BR>--3 Universal<BR>destruction (प्रलय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलयनं|संलयन
संलयनं<BR>1 Adhering or clinging to.<BR>--2 Dissolution.<BR>--3 Lying down,<BR>sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलीन
संलीन p. p.<BR>1 Clung, adhered to.<BR>--2 Joined together.<BR>--3 Hidden‘<BR>concealed.<BR>--4 Cowering down.<BR>--5<BR>Contracted, shrunk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्ण<BR>a. with the ears hanging down.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">Page1068-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--मानस a. depressed in mind, in<BR>drooping spirits.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलुड्
संलुड् {c1c} P. To stir, agitate.<BR>{c10c} U. or Caus.<BR>1 To shake, stir<BR>about, move to and fro.<BR>--2 To<BR>confound, disturb, perplex.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संलोडनं|संलोडन
संलोडनं Disturbing, confusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवत्|संवन्त्
संवत् ind.<BR>1 A year.<BR>--2<BR>Especially a year of the Vikramāditya<BR>era (commencing 56 years before<BR>the Christian era).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवत्सरः|संवत्सर
संवत्सरः [संवसंति ऋतवोऽत्र<BR>संवस्-सरन् Tv.]<BR>1 A year.<BR>--2 A year<BR>of Vikramāditya's era.<BR>--3 N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--4 The first year in the cycle<BR>of five years.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--भ्रमि a. revolving<BR>in a year, completing one<BR>revolution in a year (said of the sun).<BR>--रयः a year's course.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवद्
संवद् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To talk to, address.<BR>--2 To speak together, converse,<BR>discourse.<BR>--3 To resemble, tally with,<BR>correspond to, be like (with instr.);<BR>अस्य मुखं सीताया मुख वंद्रेण संवदत्येव<BR>U. 4; अदो संवदंत्यक्षराणि Mu. 5.<BR>--4 To name, call.<BR>--5 To<BR>agree, accord, consent. --Caus.<BR>1 To consult, hold consultation<BR>(with instr.); as in मौहूर्तिकैः सह<BR>संवाद्यतां.<BR>--2 To cause to sound,<BR>play upon (a musical instrument).<BR>--3 To declare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवदनं|संवदन
संवदनं<BR>1 Conversing, talking<BR>together.<BR>--2 Communication of<BR>tidings.<BR>--3 Examination,<BR>consideration.<BR>--4 Subduing or overpowering<BR>by magic or charms.<BR>--5 A charm,<BR>an amulet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवादः|संवाद
संवादः<BR>1 Speaking together,<BR>conversation, dialogue, colloquy;<BR>Mv. 1. 12.<BR>--2 Discussion, debate.<BR>--3<BR>Communication of tidings.<BR>--4<BR>Information, news<BR>--5 Assent,<BR>concurrence.<BR>--6 Speaking likeness,<BR>agreement, similarity, correspondence;<BR>रूपसंवादाच्च संशयादनया पृष्टः Dk.; (नादः)<BR>चित्ताकर्षी परिचित इव श्रोत्रसंवादमेति<BR>Māl. 5. 20.<BR>--7 Meeting, encounter;<BR>U. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवादिन्
संवादिन् a.<BR>1 Speaking,<BR>conversing.<BR>--2 Like, similar, resembling,<BR>corresponding to; षड्जसंवादिनीः केकाः<BR>R. 1. 39; अस्मदंगसंवादिन्याकृतिः U. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवननं|संवनन
संवननं<BR>1 Subduing or<BR>overpowering by magical rites or drugs.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">Page1069-a+ 55</a>]<BR>A charm, an amulet.<BR>--3 Fondness,<BR>love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1068-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्गः|संवर्ग
संवर्गः Ved.<BR>1 Plunder, spoil.<BR>--2<BR>An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्जनं|संवर्जन
संवर्जनं<BR>1 Appropriating to<BR>oneself.<BR>--2 Consuming, devouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवलनं|संवलन
संवलनं<BR>1 Combination, junction,<BR>union.<BR>--2 Being mixed or charged<BR>with; Māl. 9. 13, 10. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवलित|संवलितः
संवलित p. p.<BR>1 Met together,<BR>mingled, mixed: Māl. 6. 5.<BR>--2<BR>Sprinkled with; Māl. 4. 8.<BR>--3<BR>Connected, associated.<BR>--4 Broken;<BR>उदितोपलस्खलनसंवलिताः (ध्वनयः)<BR>Ki. 6. 4.<BR>--5 Surrounded,<BR>encompassed.<BR>--6 Possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवल्गित
संवल्गित a. Overrun.<BR>--तं A<BR>sound; Māl. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवस्
संवस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To live, dwell.<BR>--2 To live with, associate;<BR>Ms. 4. 79.; Y. 3. 15.<BR>--3 To spend, pass<BR>(time) --Caus. To accommodate,<BR>lodge, furnish with lodging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवासः|संवास
संवासः<BR>1 Dwelling together.<BR>--2<BR>Association, company; Pt. 1. 250.<BR>--3 Domestic intercourse.<BR>--4 A house,<BR>dwelling.<BR>--5 An open space for<BR>meeting or recreation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवसथः|संवसथ
संवसथः A place where people live<BR>together, a village, an inhabited<BR>place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवह्
संवह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To carry or bear<BR>along, drag.<BR>--2 To carry together.<BR>--3<BR>To rub, press.<BR>--4 To show, display.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To rub or press together,<BR>shampoo; संवाहयामि चरणावुत पद्मताम्रौ<BR>Ś. 3. 21.<BR>--2 To assemble, collect.<BR>--3 To drive (a carriage).<BR>--4 To<BR>marry, take a wife.<BR>--5 To carry<BR>away, drive along, impel; Pt. 5. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवहः|संवह
संवहः N. of the third of the<BR>seven courses or Mārgas of the<BR>wind: see वायु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहः|संवाह
संवाहः<BR>1 Bearing or carrying<BR>along.<BR>--2 Pressing together.<BR>--3<BR>Shampooing, stroking gently.<BR>--4<BR>A servant employed to rub and<BR>shampoo the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहकः|संवाहक
संवाहकः A shampooer; see संवाह<BR>(4) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहनं|संवाहन
संवाहनं, --ना<BR>1 Carrying or bearing<BR>a burden.<BR>--2 Shampooing; gentle<BR>rubbing: U. 1. 24.<BR>--3 Bearing<BR>along. propelling; Māl. 9. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवाहना
संवाहनं, --ना<BR>1 Carrying or bearing<BR>a burden.<BR>--2 Shampooing; gentle<BR>rubbing: U. 1. 24.<BR>--3 Bearing<BR>along. propelling; Māl. 9. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवासित
संवासित a.<BR>1 Made fragrant,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">Page1069-b+ 56</a>]<BR>scented, perfumed.<BR>--2 Made fetid,<BR>having an offensive or foul smell<BR>(as a breath).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविक्तं|संविक्त
संविक्तं What is separated or<BR>individualized.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविज्
संविज् {c7c} P., {c6c} A.<BR>1 To shake.<BR>--2<BR>To be agitated, tremble with fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविग्न
संविग्न p. p.<BR>1 Agitated, excited,<BR>disturbed, distracted, flurried; as in<BR>संविग्नमानस.<BR>--2 Terrified, frightened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविज्ञात
संविज्ञात p. p. Universally<BR>known, generally recognised or<BR>allowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविद्
संविद् {vI.v} {c2c} P.<BR>1 To know, be<BR>aware of; Bk. 5. 37; 8. 17.<BR>--2 To<BR>recognize.<BR>--3 To investigate,<BR>examine.<BR>--4 To perceive, feel, experience.<BR>--5 To advise.<BR>--6 To come to an<BR>understanding, agree upon.<BR>--7 To<BR>think over, meditate. {vII.v} {c6c} U.<BR>1 To<BR>get, obtain.<BR>--2 To meet together.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To make known, inform,<BR>announce.<BR>--2 To know, perceive,<BR>observe.<BR>--3 To cause to know or<BR>perceive; Bk. 17. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवित्तिः|संवित्ति
संवित्तिः f.<BR>1 Knowledge,<BR>perception, consciousness, feeling;<BR>श्वस्त्वया सुखसंवित्तिः स्मरणीयाऽधुनातनी<BR>Ki. 11. 34, 16. 32.<BR>--2 Understanding,<BR>intellect.<BR>--3 Recognition,<BR>recollection.<BR>--4 Harmony (of feeling),<BR>mental reconciliation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविद्
संविद् f.<BR>1 Knowledge,<BR>understanding, intellect; Ki. 18. 42.<BR>--2<BR>Consciousness, perception; Māl. 6. 13.<BR>--3 An agreement, engagement,<BR>contract, covenant, promise; स<BR>राजलोकः कृतपूर्वसंवित् R. 7. 31.<BR>--4 Assent,<BR>consent.<BR>--5 An established usage, a<BR>prescribed custom.<BR>--6 War, battle,<BR>fight.<BR>--7 A war-cry, watch-word.<BR>--8<BR>A name, an appellation.<BR>--9 A sign,<BR>signal.<BR>--10 Pleasing, delighting,<BR>gratification; Śi. 16. 47.<BR>--11<BR>Sympathy, participation.<BR>--12 Meditation.<BR>--13 Conversation.<BR>--14 Hemp.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--व्यतिक्रमः breach of promise,<BR>violation of a contract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविदा
संविदा An agreement or promise,<BR>covenant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविदात
संविदात a.<BR>1 Knowing, intelligent.<BR>--2 Harmonious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविदित|संविदितः
संविदित p. p.<BR>1 Known,<BR>understood.<BR>--2 Recognised.<BR>--3<BR>Wellknown, renowned.<BR>--4 Explored.<BR>--5<BR>Agreed upon.<BR>--6 Advised,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">Page1069-c+ 56</a>]<BR>admonished; see विद् with सं.<BR>--तं An<BR>agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेदः|संवेद
संवेदः Perception, knowledge,<BR>consciousness, feeling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेदनं|संवेदन
संवेदनं --ना<BR>1 Perception, knowledge.<BR>--2 Sensation, feeling, experiencing,<BR>suffering; दुःखसंवेदनायैव रामे चैतन्य<BR>मर्पितं U. 1. 48.<BR>--3 Giving,<BR>surrendering; Mu. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेदना
संवेदनं --ना<BR>1 Perception, knowledge.<BR>--2 Sensation, feeling, experiencing,<BR>suffering; दुःखसंवेदनायैव रामे चैतन्य<BR>मर्पितं U. 1. 48.<BR>--3 Giving,<BR>surrendering; Mu. 1. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधा
संविधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To do, act,<BR>perform, manage, make.<BR>--2 To dispose,<BR>arrange.<BR>--3 To set, place, put, lay.<BR>--4 To appoint.<BR>--5 To direct, order.<BR>--6 To attend to, mind<BR>--7 To use,<BR>employ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधा
संविधा<BR>1 Arrangement,<BR>preparation, plan; R. 7. 16, 14. 17.<BR>--2<BR>Mode of life, means of leading<BR>life; कल्पावित्कल्पयामास वन्यामेवास्य<BR>संविधां R. 1. 94.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधानं|संविधान
संविधानं<BR>1 Arrangement,<BR>disposition; Māl. 6.<BR>--2 Performance.<BR>--3<BR>Plan, mode.<BR>--4 A rite.<BR>--5<BR>Arrangement of incidents (in a plot); Māl. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविधानकं|संविधानक
संविधानकं<BR>1 Arrangement of<BR>incidents (in a plot), the plot of a<BR>drama &c.; भहो संविधानकं U. 3.<BR>--2 A<BR>strange act, an unusual occurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविभज्
संविभज् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To separate,<BR>divide.<BR>--2 To distribute, share with<BR>--स्निग्धजनसंविभक्तं हि दुःखं सह्यवेदनं<BR>भवति Ś. 4.<BR>--3 To share in<BR>common, admit (one) to a share;<BR>वित्तं यदा यस्य च संविभक्तं Subhāṣ.<BR>--4 To bestow upon, give to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविभागः|संविभाग
संविभागः<BR>1 Partition, dividing.<BR>--2 A part, portion, share.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविभागिन्
संविभागिन् m. A partner, sharer,<BR>participator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविश्
संविश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To enter.<BR>--2 To<BR>sleep, lie down to rest; संविष्टः<BR>कुशशयने निशां निनाय R. 1. 95; क्रमेण<BR>सुप्तामनु संविवेश 2. 24; Ms. 4. 55;<BR>7. 225.<BR>--3 To cohabit, have sexual<BR>intercourse with; षोडशर्तुनिशाः स्त्री<BR>णां तस्मिन् युग्मासु संविशेत् Y. 1. 79;<BR>Ms. 3. 48.<BR>--4 To enjoy.<BR>--5 To<BR>engage oneself in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संविष्ट
संविष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Sleeping, lying down;<BR>R. 1. 95.<BR>--2 Entered together.<BR>--3<BR>Seated together.<BR>--4 Dressed, clothed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेशः|संवेश
संवेशः<BR>1 Sleep, retiring to rest;<BR>R. 1. 93.<BR>--2 A dream.<BR>--3 A seat<BR>(chair, stool &c.).<BR>--4 Cohabitation,<BR>copulation or a particular mode<BR>thereof.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1069-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेशनं|संवेशन
संवेशनं Coition, sexual union.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवीक्षणं|संवीक्षण
संवीक्षणं<BR>1 Looking about in all<BR>directions, search, looking for<BR>anything lost.<BR>--2 Looking or gazing<BR>attentively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवीत|संवीतं
संवीत p. p.<BR>1 Clothed, dressed.<BR>--2 Covered over, coated, overlaid.<BR>--3<BR>Adorned.<BR>--4 Invested, surrounded,<BR>shut in, hemmed.<BR>--5 Overwhelmed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृ
संवृ {c1c} {c5c} {c9c} U.<BR>1 To hide,<BR>cover, conceal; मुहुरंगुलिसंवृताधरोष्ठं<BR>Ś. 3. 25; R. 1. 20; 7. 30.<BR>--2 To<BR>suppress, restrain, oppose;<BR>Bk. 9. 27.<BR>--3 To shut up, close.<BR>--4 To<BR>contract, compress.<BR>--5 To secure.<BR>--6 To arrange, put in order.<BR>--7 To<BR>refuse, reject.<BR>--8 To select, choose.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cover.<BR>--2 To restrain.<BR>--3 To ward off, prevent, avert.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवरः|संवर|संवरं
संवरः<BR>1 Covering.<BR>--2<BR>Comprehension.<BR>--3 Compression,<BR>contraction.<BR>--4 A dam, bridge, causeway.<BR>--5 A kind of deer.<BR>--6 N. of a<BR>demon; see शंबर.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Concealment.<BR>--2 Forbearance, self-control.<BR>--3<BR>Water.<BR>--4 A particular religious<BR>observance (practised by Buddhists).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवरणं|संवरण
संवरणं<BR>1 Covering, screening.<BR>--2<BR>Hiding, concealment; संवरणं हि तत्<BR>Māl. 1.<BR>--3 A pretext, disguise; see<BR>संवर also.<BR>--4 A secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवारः|संवार
संवारः<BR>1 Covering, closing up<BR>--2<BR>Contraction of the throat &c. in the<BR>pronunciation of letters, obtuse<BR>articulation (opp. विवार q. v.).<BR>--3<BR>Diminution.<BR>--4 Protecting,<BR>securing.<BR>--5 Arranging.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत|संवृतः
संवृत p. p.<BR>1 Covered, covered up:<BR>मुहुरंगुलिसंवृताधरोष्ठं (मुखं) Ś. 3. 25<BR>--2 Hidden, concealed; न मदनो विवृतो<BR>न च संवृतः Ś. 2. 11.<BR>--3 Secret.<BR>--4<BR>Closed, shut up, secured.<BR>--5<BR>Retired, secluded.<BR>--6 Contracted,<BR>compressed.<BR>--7 Confiscated,<BR>sequestered.<BR>--8 Encompassed, surrounded.<BR>--9<BR>Filled with, full of.<BR>--10<BR>Accompanied by; see वृ with सं.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A<BR>secret or retired place, secrecy.<BR>--2<BR>A mode of pronunciation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आकार a. one who conceals all<BR>outward manifestation of internal<BR>feeling, one who gives no clue to his<BR>internal thoughts.<BR>--मंत्र a. one who<BR>keeps his plans secret; तस्य<BR>संवृतमंत्रस्य R. 1. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृतिः|संवृति
संवृतिः f.<BR>1 Covering, covering<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">Page1070-b+ 55</a>]<BR>up.<BR>--2 Concealment, suppression,<BR>hiding; Ki. 10. 44.<BR>--3 Secret<BR>purpose, covert design.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृक्त
संवृक्त p. p.<BR>1 Devoured,<BR>consumed.<BR>--2 Destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्
संवृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To turn or go<BR>towards, approach.<BR>--2 To attack,<BR>assault (with acc.).<BR>--3 To be or<BR>become; ते यथोक्ताः संवृत्ताः Pt. 1.<BR>--4<BR>To happen, take place, occur.<BR>--5 To<BR>be produced, arise, spring.<BR>--6 To be<BR>accomplished.<BR>--7 To be united, meet<BR>together.<BR>--8 To fall to the lot of.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cast, throw.<BR>--2 To<BR>accomplish, fulfil.<BR>--3 To wrap up,<BR>envelope.<BR>--4 To crumble up.<BR>--5 To<BR>destroy, crush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तः|संवर्त|संवर्त्त|संवर्त्तः
संवर्तः<BR>1 Turning towards.<BR>--2<BR>Dissolution, destruction.<BR>--3 The<BR>periodical destruction of the world;<BR>Mv. 6. 26.<BR>--4 A cloud.<BR>--5 A cloud<BR>of a particular class (abounding in<BR>water).<BR>--6 N. of one of the seven<BR>clouds that rise at the dissolution<BR>of the world.<BR>--7 A year.<BR>--8 A<BR>collection, multitude.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तकः|संवर्तक|संवर्त्तक|संवर्त्तकः
संवर्तकः<BR>1 A kind of cloud.<BR>--2<BR>The fire of destruction, the fire that<BR>is to destroy the world at the period<BR>of universal destruction; इतोऽपि<BR>वडवानलः सह सनस्तसंवर्तकैः Bh. 2. 76.<BR>--3 Sub-marine fire.<BR>--4 N of<BR>Balarāma.<BR>--कं The plough of<BR>Balarāma<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तकिन्|संवर्त्तकिन्
संवर्तकिन् m. N. of Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्तिका|संवर्त्तिका
संवर्तिका<BR>1 The new leaf of a<BR>water lily.<BR>--2 The petal near the<BR>filament<BR>--3 The flame of a lamp<BR>&c.; (दीपादेः शिवा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्त|संवृत्तः
संवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Become, happened,<BR>occurred.<BR>--2 Fulfilled,<BR>accomplished.<BR>--3 Collected, heaped together<BR>--4 Past, gone.<BR>--5 Covered.<BR>--6<BR>Furnished with.<BR>--तः N. of Varuṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृत्तिः|संवृत्ति
संवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Becoming, happening,<BR>occurrence.<BR>--2 Accomplishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृध्
संवृध् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To grow up,<BR>increase, be developed.<BR>--2 To fulfil,<BR>satisfy. --Caus.<BR>1 To rear, nourish,<BR>cherish, bring up, foster.<BR>--2 To<BR>plant.<BR>--3 To enlarge, augment.<BR>--4<BR>To fulfil, satisfy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धक|संवर्द्धकः
संवर्धक a. (र्विका f.)<BR>1 Causing<BR>complete growth or prosperity,<BR>augmenting.<BR>--2 Greeting, welcoming<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">Page1070-c+ 55</a>]<BR>(guests &c.), hospitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धनं|संवर्धन|संवर्द्धनं
संवर्धनं<BR>1 Bringing up, rearing,<BR>fostering.<BR>--2 Complete growth,<BR>thriving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवर्धित|संवर्द्धितः
संवर्धित p. p.<BR>1 Brought up, bred,<BR>reared; संवर्धितानां सुतनिर्विशेषं<BR>R. 5. 6.<BR>--2 Increased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवृद्ध
संवृद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Full-grown,<BR>increased, augmented.<BR>--2 Grown tall or<BR>high, big, large.<BR>--3 Prospering,<BR>blooming, flourishing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संवेगः|संवेग
संवेगः<BR>1 Agitation, flurry,<BR>excitement; Mv. 1. 39.<BR>--2 Violent speed,<BR>impetuosity, vehemence; U. 2. 26;<BR>Māl. 5. 6.<BR>--3 Haste, speed.<BR>--4<BR>Agonising pain, poignancy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यवहारः|संव्यवहार
संव्यवहारः<BR>1 Duty, business.<BR>--2 Mercantile transaction, calling,<BR>trade; अपि प्रचीयंत सव्यवहाराणा<BR>वृद्धिलाभाः Mu. 1; see व्यवहार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्ये
संव्ये {c1c} U.<BR>1 To clothe, put on<BR>clothes.<BR>--2 To surround, enclose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संव्यानं|संव्यान
संव्यानं<BR>1 Covering, wrapping.<BR>--2 Cloth, vesture, garment.<BR>--3<BR>An upper garment; Śi. 18. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशप्तकः|संशप्तक
संशप्तकः [सम्पक् शप्तसंगीकारो यस्य<BR>कप् Tv.]<BR>1 A warrior sworn never<BR>to recede from a contest and<BR>kept to prevent the flight of others.<BR>--2 A picked warrior.<BR>--3 A brother<BR>in arms.<BR>--4 A conspirator who has<BR>taken an oath to kid another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशब्दः|संशब्द
संशब्दः Mention, reference.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशब्दनं|संशब्दन
संशब्दनं<BR>1 Making a sound.<BR>--2<BR>Praising.<BR>--3 Calling out to.<BR>--4<BR>Referring to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशम्
संशम् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be calm.<BR>--2 To<BR>be allayed or extinguished,<BR>disappear; सत्त्वं संशाम्वतीव मे Bk. 18. 28.<BR>--3 To be removed. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>mitigate.<BR>--2 To settle, decide;<BR>Pt. 1. 376.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशरणं|संशरण
संशरणं Commencement of a<BR>combat, attack, charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशित|संशितं
संशित p. p.<BR>1 Sharpened,<BR>aroused.<BR>--2 Sharp, acute<BR>--3<BR>Thoroughly completed, effected,<BR>accomplished.<BR>--4 Decided, well-ascertained,<BR>determined, certain.<BR>--5 Effecting,<BR>diligent in performing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a. one whose mind is<BR>thoroughly matured or disciplined.<BR>--व्रत a. one who has fulfilled his<BR>vow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशी
संशी {c2c} A.<BR>1 To waver, be in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">Page1071-a+ 56</a>]<BR>doubt or suspense, be uncertain or<BR>irresolute संशय्य कणीदिषु तिष्ठते यः<BR>Ki. 3. 14, 42.; Bv. 2. 115.<BR>--2 To<BR>lie down for rest, sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1070-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयः|संशय
संशयः<BR>1 Doubt, uncertainty,<BR>irresolution, hesitation; मनस्तु मे<BR>संशयमेव गाहते Ku. 5. 46; त्वदन्यः<BR>संशयस्यास्य छेता न ह्युपपद्यते Bg. 6. 36.<BR>--2 Misgiving, suspicion.<BR>--3 Doubt<BR>or indecision (in Nyāya), one of<BR>the 16 categories mentioned in the<BR>Nyāya philosophy;<BR>एकधर्प्रिकविरुद्धभावामावप्रकारकं ज्ञानं संशयः; it is also<BR>regarded as one of the two kinds<BR>of अयथार्थज्ञान<BR>--4 Danger, peril, risk:<BR>न संशयमनारुह्य नरो भद्राणि पश्यति<BR>H. 1. 7; याता पुतः संशयमन्यथैव<BR>Māl. 10. 13; Ki. 13. 16, Ve. 6. 1.<BR>--5<BR>Possibility.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>doubting, sceptical.<BR>--आपन्न, --उपेत, --स्थ<BR>a. doubtful, uncertain, irresolute.<BR>--गत a. fallen into danger; Ś. 6.<BR>--छेदः solution of a doubt, decision,<BR>--छेदिन् a. clearing all doubt,<BR>decisive; Ś. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयान|संशयानः
संशयान, संशयालु, संशयितृ a.<BR>Doubtful, irresolute, uncertain, wavering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयालु|संशयालुः
संशयान, संशयालु, संशयितृ a.<BR>Doubtful, irresolute, uncertain, wavering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयितृ
संशयान, संशयालु, संशयितृ a.<BR>Doubtful, irresolute, uncertain, wavering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशयित
संशयित a.<BR>1 Doubtful, uncertain.<BR>--2 Doubted, questioned.<BR>--3<BR>Risked, hazarded, endangered, exposed<BR>to peril or danger; संशयितजीविता ते<BR>शरीरावस्था Māl. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशीतिः|संशीति
संशीतिः f. Doubt; न हि मे<BR>संशीतिरस्या दिव्यतां प्रति K. 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुध्
संशुध् {c4c} P. To be completely<BR>purified. --Caus.<BR>1 To purify<BR>completely.<BR>--2 To clear, pay off<BR>(expenses).<BR>--3 To correct, rectify.<BR>--4<BR>To examine, inquire into,<BR>investigate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुद्ध
संशुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Completely<BR>purified, pure.<BR>--2 Polished, refined.<BR>--3<BR>Expiated.<BR>--4 Acquitted (of crime<BR>or debt.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशुद्धिः|संशुद्धि
संशुद्धिः f.<BR>1 Complete<BR>purification; Bg. 15. 1.<BR>--2 Cleansing or<BR>purifying in general.<BR>--3 Correction,<BR>rectincation.<BR>--4 Clearance.<BR>--5<BR>Acquittance (of debt).<BR>--6 Purity,<BR>cleanness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संशोधनं|संशोधन
संशोधनं Purification, cleanness &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्चत्
संश्चत् n. Trick, jugglery,<BR>illusion. --m. A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्यान|संश्यानः
संश्यान p. p.<BR>1 Contracted, shrunk<BR>up.<BR>--2 Frozen, congealed.<BR>--3<BR>Rolled up.<BR>--4 Collapsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रि
संश्रि {c1c} U.<BR>1 To have<BR>recourse to, resort, fly to for refuge<BR>or shelter.<BR>--2 To lean or rest on,<BR>depend on; न खलु बहिरुपाधीन् प्रीतयः<BR>संश्रयंते U. 6. 12; Māl. 1. 24.<BR>--3 To<BR>attain to, approach.<BR>--4 To obtain.<BR>--5 To serve, wait upon.<BR>--6 To join,<BR>unite with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रयः|संश्रय
संश्रयः<BR>1 A resting or dwelling<BR>place, residence, habitation;<BR>परस्परविरोधिन्योरेकसंश्रयदुर्लभं V. 5. 24;<BR>R. 6. 41; oft. at the end of comp. in<BR>this sense and translated by<BR>‘residing with’, ‘relating or pertaining<BR>to’, ‘with reference to’;<BR>ज्ञातिकुलैकसंश्रयां Ś. 5. 17; नौसंश्रयः<BR>R. 16 57; U. 3. 17; मनोरथोऽस्याः<BR>शोशमौलिसंश्रयः Ku. 6. 60; द्विसंश्रयां<BR>प्रीतिमवाप लक्ष्मीः 1. 43; एकार्थसंश्रयमुभयोः<BR>प्रयोगं M. 1.<BR>--2 Seeking protection<BR>or shelter with, fleeing for refuge,<BR>forming or seeking alliance,<BR>leaguing together for mutual protection;<BR>one of the 6 guṇas or expedients in<BR>polities; see under गुण also;<BR>Ms. 7. 160.<BR>--3 Resort, refuge, asylum,<BR>protection, shelter; अनपायिनि सश्रयद्रुमे<BR>गजभग्ने पत्ननाय वल्लरी Ku. 4. 31;<BR>Me. 17; Pt. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रित|संश्रितः
संश्रित p. p.<BR>1 Gone to for refuge.<BR>--2 Supported, sheltered.<BR>--3 United,<BR>joined; चूतेन संश्रितवती नवमालिक्रेयं<BR>Ś. 4. 12.<BR>--तः A dependent, follower,<BR>servant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रु
संश्रु {c5c} U.<BR>1 To listen to;<BR>संशृणोति न चोक्तनि Bk. 5. 19; 6. 5;<BR>(but Atm. when used<BR>intransitively); हितान्न यः संशृणुते स किंप्रभुः<BR>Ki. 1. 5.<BR>--2 To promise. --Caus.<BR>To tell, narrate, report.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रवः|संश्रव
संश्रवः<BR>1 Hearing attentively.<BR>--2<BR>A promise, an agreement,<BR>engagement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रवणं|संश्रवण
संश्रवणं<BR>1 Hearing.<BR>--2 The ear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्रुत|संश्रुतः
संश्रुत p. p.<BR>1 Promised, agreed<BR>to.<BR>--2 Well-heard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लिष्
संश्लिष् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To clasp or press<BR>together.<BR>--2 To adhere or cling to.<BR>--3 To join, unite. --Caus. To<BR>unite, join, connect together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लिष्ट|संश्लिष्टः
संश्लिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Clasped or<BR>pressed together, joined, united.<BR>--2<BR>Embraced.<BR>--3 Adjoining, lying close<BR>or contiguous to.<BR>--4 Furnished or<BR>endowed with, having.<BR>--5 Related,<BR>connected together; Pt. 2. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेषः|संश्लेष
संश्लेषः<BR>1 Embracing; an embrace;<BR>वशिनां हि परपरिग्रहसंश्लषपराङ्मुखी वृत्तिः<BR>Ś. 5. 28.<BR>--2 Union, connection,<BR>contact.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेषणं|संश्लेषण
संश्लेषणं --णा<BR>1 Pressing together,<BR>--2 Means of binding together.<BR>--3<BR>Connection, tie, bond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्लेषणा
संश्लेषणं --णा<BR>1 Pressing together,<BR>--2 Means of binding together.<BR>--3<BR>Connection, tie, bond.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संश्वत्
संश्वत् See संश्चत्<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसंज्|संसञ्ज्
संसंज् Pass. To be attached or<BR>connected together, be joined or<BR>linked together; see संप्तक्त below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्त|संसक्तः
संसक्त p. p.<BR>1 Adhered or stuck<BR>together.<BR>--2 Adhering or clinging<BR>to, attached to, sticking close to.<BR>--3<BR>Joined or linked together, closely<BR>connected; प्रांतेषु संसक्तनमेरुशाखं<BR>Ku. 3. 43; R. 7. 24.<BR>--4 Near,<BR>contiguous, adjoining.<BR>--5 Confused, mixed,<BR>mingled, blended;<BR>मदमुखरमयूरीमुक्तसंसक्तकेकः Māl. 9. 5; कलिंदकन्या<BR>सथूरां गताऽपि गंगोर्मिसंसक्तजलेव भाति<BR>R. 6. 48; Māl. 5. 11.<BR>--6 Intent on.<BR>--7 Endowed with, possessed of.<BR>--8<BR>Fastened, restrained.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मनस् a. having the mind fixed or<BR>attached.<BR>--युग a. yoked, harnessed;<BR>Śi. 3. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसक्तिः|संसक्ति
संसक्तिः f.<BR>1 Close adherence,<BR>intimate union or junction; संसकौ<BR>किमसुलभं महोदयानां Ki. 7. 27.<BR>--2<BR>Close contact, proximity.<BR>--3<BR>Intercourse, intimacy, intimate<BR>acquaintance; Śi. 8. 67.<BR>--4 Tying,<BR>fastening together.<BR>--5 Devotion, addiction<BR>(to anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसद्
संसद् {c1c} {c6c} P.<BR>1 To sit down,<BR>sit down together.<BR>--2 To be<BR>afflicted, be in distress.<BR>--3 To pine away.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसद्
संसद् f.<BR>1 An assembly, meeting,<BR>circle; संसत्सु जाते पुरुषाधिकारे<BR>Ki. 3. 51; छात्रससदि लब्धकीर्तिः Pt. 1;<BR>R. 16. 24.<BR>--2 A court of justice;<BR>Ms. 8. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसादः|संसाद
संसादः An assembly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसाध्
संसाध् Caus.<BR>1 To be successful.<BR>--2 To accomplish, complete;<BR>Ms. 2. 100.<BR>--3 To secure, get, obtain.<BR>--4<BR>To settle.<BR>--5 To regain; Ms. 8. 50.<BR>--6 To cause to be settled or paid;<BR>Ms. 8. 213.<BR>--7 To destroy, kill.<BR>--8<BR>To extinguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिध्
संसिध् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be made<BR>perfect.<BR>--2 To be fully accomplished<BR>or effected, to be well-performed.<BR>--3 To attain supreme felicity. to<BR>become happy; जप्येनैव तु संसिध्येत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-a" target="_blank">Page1072-a+ 56</a>]<BR>ब्राह्मणो नात्र संशयः Ms. 2. 87.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1071-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिद्ध
संसिद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Fully<BR>accomplished, perfected.<BR>--2 One who has<BR>secured final emancipation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसिद्धिः|संसिद्धि
संसिद्धिः f.<BR>1 Completion,<BR>complete accomplishment or<BR>attainment; स्वनुष्ठितस्य धर्मस्य<BR>संसिद्धिर्हरितोषणं Bhāg.; Ku. 2. 63.<BR>--2<BR>Absolution, final beatitude; संसिद्धिं परमां<BR>गताः Bg. 8. 15; 3. 20.<BR>--3 Nature,<BR>natural disposition, state or<BR>quality.<BR>--4 A passionate or intoxicated<BR>woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसूच्
संसूच् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To indicate,<BR>forebode; संयोगो हि वियोगस्य<BR>संसूचयति संभवं Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 To inform,<BR>tell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसूचनं|संसूचन
संसूचनं<BR>1 Showing plainly,<BR>proving.<BR>--2 Informing, telling.<BR>--3<BR>Hinting, intimating; अर्थस्य संसूचनं.<BR>--4 Reproaching, accusing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृ
संसृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To go towards,<BR>approach.<BR>--2 To revolve, turn round.<BR>--3 To spread.<BR>--4 To move.<BR>--5 To<BR>go or flow together.<BR>--6 To go to,<BR>obtain; पापान् संसृत्य संसारान् प्रेष्यतां<BR>याति शत्रुषु Ms. 12. 70. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To spread over, cause to move<BR>over.<BR>--2 To revolve or turn<BR>round; जन्मवृद्धिक्षयैर्नित्यं<BR>संसारयति चक्रवत् Ms. 12. 124.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसरणं|संसरण
संसरणं<BR>1 Going, proceeding,<BR>revolution.<BR>--2 The world, wordly life,<BR>mundane existence,<BR>ग्रीष्मचंडकरमंडलभीष्मज्वालसंसरणतापितमूर्तेः Bv. 4. 6.<BR>--3 Birth and re-birth.<BR>--4 The<BR>unresisted march of troops.<BR>--5 The<BR>commencement of battle.<BR>--6 A<BR>highway.<BR>--7 A resting-place for<BR>passengers near the gates of a city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारः|संसार
संसारः<BR>1 Course, passage.<BR>--2 The<BR>course or circuit of worldly life,<BR>secular life, mundane^1 existence, the<BR>world; असारः संसारः U. 1;<BR>Māl. 5. 30; संसारधन्वभुवि किं सारमामृशसि<BR>शंसाधुना शुभमते Aśvad. 22; or<BR>परिवर्तिनि संसारे मृतः को वा न जायते<BR>Pt. 1. 27.<BR>--3 Transmigration,<BR>metempsychosis, succession of births.<BR>--4<BR>Worldly illusion.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गमनं<BR>transmigration.<BR>--गुरुः {1} an<BR>epithet of the god of love. {2}<BR>the preceptor of the world.<BR>--चक्रं succession of births and<BR>deaths, metempsychosis.<BR>--मार्गः {1}<BR>the course of worldly affairs,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">Page1072-b+ 56</a>]<BR>worldly life. {2} the vulva.<BR>--मोक्षः,<BR>--मोक्षणं final liberation or<BR>emancipation from worldly life.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसारिन्
संसारिन् a. (णी f.) Mundane,<BR>worldly, transmigratory. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>sentient being, creature.<BR>--2 The<BR>embodied spirit, individual soul<BR>(जीवात्मन्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृतिः|संसृति
संसृतिः f.<BR>1 Course, current, flow.<BR>--2 The worldly life, course of the<BR>world.<BR>--3 Metempsychosis,<BR>transmigration; किं मां निपातयसि<BR>संसृतिगर्तमध्ये Bv. 4. 32; Śi. 14. 63; cf.<BR>संसार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृज्
संसृज् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To mix, mingle,<BR>unite with, bring in contact with;<BR>संसृज्यते सरसिजैररुणांशुभिन्नैः R. 5. 69.<BR>अस्ना रक्षः संसृजतात् Ait. Br.<BR>--2 To<BR>join, meet; सौमित्रिणा तदनु संससृजे<BR>R. 13. 73; Ku. 7. 74.<BR>--3 To create,<BR>form.<BR>--4 To endow or furnish with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गः|संसर्ग
संसर्गः<BR>1 Commixture, junction,<BR>union.<BR>--2 Contact, company,<BR>association, society; संसर्गमुक्तिः खलेषु<BR>Bh. 2. 62; Ś. 1. 3.<BR>--3 Proximity,<BR>touch.<BR>--4 Intercourse, familiarity.<BR>--5 Copulation, sexual union;<BR>Ms. 6. 72.<BR>--6 Co-existence, intimate relation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभावः one of the two<BR>main kinds of non-existence, relative<BR>non-existence, which is of three<BR>kinds -- प्रागभाव antecedent,<BR>प्रध्वंप्ताभाव emergent, and अत्यंनाभाब absolute,<BR>non-existence.<BR>--दोषः. the fault or<BR>evil consequences resulting from<BR>association, especially with bad<BR>people.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्गिन्
संसर्गिन् a.<BR>1 United, associated<BR>with.<BR>--2 Keeping company with,<BR>familiar. --m. An associate, a<BR>companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्जनं|संसर्जन|संसर्ज्जन
संसर्जनं<BR>1 Commingling.<BR>--2<BR>Leaving, abandoning.<BR>--3 Discharging,<BR>voiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्ट|संसृष्टः
संसृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Commingled,<BR>mixed or united together, conjoined.<BR>--2<BR>Associated or connected together<BR>as partners.<BR>--3 Composed.<BR>--4<BR>Reunited.<BR>--5 Involved in.<BR>--6<BR>Created.<BR>--7 Cleanly dressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टता
संसृष्टता, --त्वं<BR>1 Association,<BR>union.<BR>--2 (In law) Voluntary reunion<BR>in pecuniary interest of kinsmen<BR>(as of father and son or of brothers<BR>after the partition of property).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टत्वं|संसृष्टत्व
संसृष्टता, --त्वं<BR>1 Association,<BR>union.<BR>--2 (In law) Voluntary reunion<BR>in pecuniary interest of kinsmen<BR>(as of father and son or of brothers<BR>after the partition of property).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टिः|संसृष्टि
संसृष्टिः f.<BR>1 Combination, union.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">Page1072-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 Association, intercourse,<BR>copartnership.<BR>--3 Living in one<BR>family, see संसृष्टता (2) above.<BR>--4 A<BR>collection.<BR>--5 Collecting, assembling.<BR>--6 (In Rhet.) The combination<BR>or coexistence of two or more<BR>independent figures of speech in one<BR>passage; मिथोऽनपेक्षयैतेषां (<BR>शब्दार्थालंकाराणां) स्थितिः संसृष्टिरुच्यते<BR>S. D. 756.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृष्टिन्
संसृष्टिन् m.<BR>1 A reunited kinsman.<BR>--2 A copartner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसृप्
संसृप् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To move; संसंर्पंत्या<BR>सपदि भवतः स्रोतसि च्छाययासौ<BR>Me. 51.<BR>--2 To move along, flow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्पः|संसर्प
संसर्पः<BR>1 Creeping along, gliding<BR>or gentle motion.<BR>--2 The<BR>intercalary month occurring in a year in<BR>which there occurs a Kṣaya-māsa<BR>(क्षयमास).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्पणं|संसर्पण
संसर्पणं<BR>1 Creeping along.<BR>--2<BR>Surprise, unexpected attack, sally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसर्पिन्
संसर्पिन् a. Creeping along,<BR>moving or winding near; Ku. 7. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संसेकः|संसेक
संसेकः Sprinkling, watering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृ
संस्कृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To adorn, grace,<BR>decorate; ककुभं समस्कुरुत माघवनीं<BR>Śi. 9. 25.<BR>--2 To refine, polish;<BR>वाण्येका समलंकसोति पुरुषं या संस्कृता धार्यते<BR>Bh. 2. 19; Śi. 14. 50.<BR>--3 To<BR>consecrate by repeating Mantras;<BR>Ms. 5. 36.<BR>--4 To purify (a person)<BR>by scriptural ceremonies, perform<BR>purificatory ceremonies over (a<BR>person); संचस्कारोमयप्रीत्या मैथिलेयौ<BR>यथाविधि R. 15. 31; Y. 2. 124.<BR>--5<BR>To cultivate, educate, train;<BR>आर्योपदेशसंस्कियमाणमतयः Mu. 3.<BR>--6 To<BR>make ready, prepare, equip, fit out;<BR>Mu. 3.<BR>--7 To cook, dress (food.)<BR>--8<BR>To purify, cleanse.<BR>--9 To collect,<BR>heap together.<BR>--10 To construct,<BR>form well or thoroughly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कर्तृ|संस्कर्त्तृ
संस्कर्तृ m.<BR>1 One who dresses,<BR>cooks, prepares &c.; Ms. 5. 51.<BR>--2<BR>One who consecrates, initiates &c.;<BR>U. 7. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कारः|संस्कार
संस्कारः<BR>1 Making perfect,<BR>refining, polishing; (मणिः) प्रयुक्तसंस्कार<BR>इवाधिकं बभौ R. 3. 18.<BR>--2 Refinement,<BR>perfection, grammatical purity (as<BR>of words); संस्कारवत्येव गिरा मनीषी<BR>Ku. 1. 28; (where Malli renders<BR>the word by व्याकरणजन्या शुद्धिः);<BR>R. 15. 76.<BR>--3 Education, cultivation,<BR>training (as of the mind);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-a" target="_blank">Page1073-a+ 56</a>]<BR>निसर्गसंस्कारविनति इत्यसौ नृपणे चक्र<BR>युवराजशब्दभाक् R. 3. 35 Ku. 7. 10.<BR>--4<BR>Making ready, preparation.<BR>--5<BR>Cooking dressing (as of food &c.).<BR>--6 Embellishment, decoration,<BR>ornament; स्वभावसुंदरं वस्तु न<BR>संस्कारमपेक्षते Dṛ. Ś. 49; Ś. 7. 23;<BR>Mu. 2. 10.<BR>--7 Consecration, sanctification,<BR>hallowing.<BR>--8 Impression, form,<BR>mould, operation, influence; यन्नवे<BR>भाजने लग्नः संस्कारो नान्यथा भवेत्<BR>H. Pr. 8; Bh. 3. 84.<BR>--9 Idea, notion,<BR>conception.<BR>--10 Any faculty or capacity<BR>--11 Effect of work, merit of action.<BR>फलानुमेयाः प्रारंभाः संस्काराः प्राक्तना<BR>इव R. 1. 20.<BR>--12 The<BR>self-reproductive quality, faculty of impression;<BR>one of the 24 qualities or guṇas<BR>recognised by the Vaiśeṣikas; it<BR>is of three kinds:--भावना, वेग, and<BR>स्थितिस्थापकता q.q. v.v.<BR>--13 The<BR>faculty of recollection, impression on<BR>the memory; संस्कारमात्रजन्यं ज्ञानं<BR>स्मृतिः T. S.<BR>--14 A purificatory rite, a<BR>sacred rite or ceremony; संस्कारार्थं<BR>शरीरस्य Ms. 2. 66; R. 10. 78; (Manu<BR>mentions 12 such Saṃskāras; see<BR>Ms. 2. 26; some writers increase<BR>the number to sixteen).<BR>--15<BR>Purification, purity.<BR>--16 A rite or<BR>ceremony in general.<BR>--17 Investiture<BR>with the sacred thread.<BR>--18<BR>Obsequial ceremonies.<BR>--19 A polishing<BR>stone; Ś. 6. 5 (where संस्कार may<BR>mean ‘polishing’ also).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पूत a. {1} purified by sacred<BR>rites. {2} purified by refinement<BR>or education.<BR>--रहित, वर्जित, --हीन<BR>a. (a person of one of the three<BR>higher castes) over whom the<BR>purificatory ceremonies, particularly<BR>the thread-ceremony, have not been<BR>performed and who therefore<BR>becomes a Vrātya or outcast; cf. व्रात्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1072-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कारक
संस्कारक a. Consecrating,<BR>purifying, refining &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्कृत|संस्कृतं|संस्कृतः
संस्कृत p. p.<BR>1 Made perfect,<BR>refined, polished, cultivated.<BR>--2<BR>Artificially made, highly wrought,<BR>carefully or accurately formed,<BR>elaborated.<BR>--3 Made ready, dressed,<BR>prepared; cooked.<BR>--4 Consecrated,<BR>hallowed.<BR>--5 Initiated into worldly<BR>life, married.<BR>--6 Cleansed, purified.<BR>--7 Adorned, decorated.<BR>--8<BR>Excellent, best.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A word formed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">Page1073-b+ 56</a>]<BR>regularly according to the rules of<BR>grammar, a regular derivative.<BR>--2<BR>A man of any one of the first three<BR>castes over whom all the<BR>purificatory rites have been performed.<BR>--3<BR>A learned man.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Refined or<BR>highly polished speech, the Sanskrit<BR>language; संस्कृतं नाम दैवी<BR>वागन्वारव्याता महर्षिभिः Kāv. 1. 33.<BR>--2 A sacred<BR>usage.<BR>--3 An offering, oblation<BR>(mostly Vedic).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः f. {1} a<BR>polished word or language. {2} a<BR>Sanskrit word or expression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्क्रिया
संस्क्रिया<BR>1 A purificatory rite.<BR>--2<BR>Consecration.<BR>--3 Obsequies, a<BR>funeral ceremony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तंभ्|संस्तम्भ्
संस्तंभ् {c5c} {c9c} P. (caus. also)<BR>1<BR>To stop, restrain, control;<BR>प्रयत्नसंस्तंभितविक्रियाणां कथंचिदीशा मनसां<BR>बभूवुः Ku. 3. 34.<BR>--2 To paralyze,<BR>benumb; Ku. 3. 73.<BR>--3 To take<BR>heart or courage, cheer up, compose,<BR>collect (oneself); देवि संस्तंभयात्मानं<BR>U. 4.<BR>--4 To make firm or immovable;<BR>Bg. 3. 43.<BR>--5 To support, prop up.<BR>--6 To confirm, establish, corroborate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तब्ध
संस्तब्ध p. p. Supported,<BR>confirmed &c.; see संस्तंभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तंभः|संस्तम्भ|संस्तंभ|संस्तम्भः
संस्तंभः<BR>1 Support, prop.<BR>--2<BR>Confirming strengthening, fixing.<BR>--3<BR>Stop, stay.<BR>--4 Stupefaction,<BR>paralysis.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तु
संस्तु {c2c} P.<BR>1 To praise.<BR>--2 To<BR>extol, celebrate.<BR>--3 To praise in<BR>chorus.<BR>--4 To be acquainted with,<BR>be familiar or intimate with (chiefly<BR>in p. p. in this sense); अनेकशः<BR>संस्तुतमप्यनल्पा नवं नवं प्रीतिरहो करोति<BR>Śi. 3. 31; Ki. 3. 2; see संस्तुत.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तवः|संस्तव
संस्तवः<BR>1 Praise, eulogium;<BR>Pt. 4. 89.<BR>--2 Acquaintance, intimacy,<BR>familiarity; गुणाः प्रियत्वेऽविकृता न<BR>संस्तवः Ki. 4. 25; नवैर्गुणैः संप्रेति<BR>संस्तवस्थिरं तिरोहितं प्रेस घनागमश्रियः<BR>4. 22; Śi. 7. 31.<BR>--3 Agreeing together,<BR>harmony.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तवान|संस्तवानः
संस्तवान a.<BR>1 Praising properly.<BR>--2 Eloquent.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A singer (उद्गातृ).<BR>--2 Joy, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तावः|संस्ताव
संस्तावः<BR>1 Praise, celebration.<BR>--2<BR>Hymning in chorus.<BR>--3 The place<BR>which Brāhmaṇas repeating hymns<BR>and prayers occupy at a sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तुत|संस्तुतः
संस्तुत p. p.<BR>1 Praised, eulogized.<BR>--2 Praised together.<BR>--3 Agreeing<BR>together, harmonious.<BR>--4 Intimate,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">Page1073-c+ 56</a>]<BR>familiar; Māl. 7. 2.<BR>--5 Intended,<BR>aimed at; Māl. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तुतिः|संस्तुति
संस्तुतिः f. Praise, eulogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तृ
संस्तृ-स्तॄ {5} {c9c} U.<BR>1 To spread,<BR>strew; प्रांतसंस्तीर्णदर्भाः Ś. 4. 7.<BR>--2<BR>To overspread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तॄ
संस्तृ-स्तॄ {5} {c9c} U.<BR>1 To spread,<BR>strew; प्रांतसंस्तीर्णदर्भाः Ś. 4. 7.<BR>--2<BR>To overspread.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तरः|संस्तर
संस्तरः<BR>1 A bed, couch, layer;<BR>a bed of leaves &c.; नवपल्लवसंस्तरेऽपि<BR>ते R. 8. 57; नवपल्लवसंस्तरे यथा<BR>रचयिष्यामि तनुं विभावसौ Ku. 4. 34.<BR>--2 A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्तारः|संस्तार
संस्तारः Spreading out, extension.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्त्यायः|संस्त्याय
संस्त्यायः<BR>1 A collection, heap,an<BR>assemblage.<BR>--2 Vicinity.<BR>--3<BR>Spreading, diffusion, expansion.<BR>--4 A<BR>house, residence, habitation;<BR>संस्त्यायनेव गच्छावः Māl. 1, 9.<BR>--5<BR>Familiarity, familiar talk; Mv. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्था
संस्था {c1c} A.<BR>1 To dwell or live<BR>in, stand close together; तीक्ष्य<BR>दुद्विजते मृदौ परिभवत्रासान्न संतिष्ठते<BR>Mu. 3. 5.<BR>--2 To stand on.<BR>--3 To be, exist,<BR>live.<BR>--4 To abide by, obey, act up<BR>to; दारिद्यात्पुरुषस्य बांधवजनो वाक्ये न<BR>संत्तिष्ठते Mk. 1. 36.<BR>--5 To be completed;<BR>सद्यः संतिष्ठते यतस्तयाशौवमिति स्थितिः<BR>Ms. 5. 98 (= यज्ञपुण्येन युज्यते Kull.).<BR>--6 To come to an end, be<BR>interrupted; Bk. 8. 11.<BR>--7 To stand still,<BR>come to a stand, (Paras.); क्षणं न<BR>संतिष्ठति जीवलोकः क्षयोदयाभ्यां<BR>परिवर्तमानः Hariv.<BR>--8 To die, perish.<BR>--9<BR>To agree, conform to.<BR>--10 To stand<BR>firmly. --Caus.<BR>1 To establish,<BR>settle.<BR>--2 To place.<BR>--3 To compose,<BR>collect (oneself).<BR>--4 To subject,<BR>keep under control, Ms. 9. 2.<BR>--5<BR>To stop, restrain.<BR>--6 To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थ|संस्थः
संस्थ a.<BR>1 Staying, abiding,<BR>lasting.<BR>--2 Dwelling, being, existing,<BR>situated (at the end of comp.);<BR>शिष्टा क्रिया कस्यचिदात्मसंस्था<BR>M. 1. 16; Ku. 6. 60;<BR>निसर्गमिन्नास्पदमेकसंस्थं R. 6. 29; Māl. 5. 16.<BR>--3 Tame,<BR>domesticated.<BR>--4 Fixed, stationary.<BR>--5 Ended, perished, dead.<BR>--6 Come<BR>to an end, completed.<BR>--7<BR>Manifested (व्यक्त).<BR>--स्थः<BR>1 A dweller, an<BR>inhabitant.<BR>--2 A neighbour,<BR>countryman.<BR>--3 A spy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्था
संस्था<BR>1 An assemblage, assembly.<BR>--2 Situation, state or condition of<BR>being.<BR>--3 Form, nature;<BR>R. 11. 38.<BR>--4 Occupation, business, settled<BR>mode of life; पृथक्संस्थाश्च निर्ममे<BR>Ms. 1. 21.<BR>--5 Correct or proper conduct.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-a" target="_blank">Page1074-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--6 End, completion.<BR>--7 Stop, stay.<BR>--8 Loss, destruction.<BR>--9<BR>Destruction of the world.<BR>--10 Resemblance.<BR>--11 A royal decree or ordinance.<BR>--12 A form of Soma sacrifice.<BR>--13<BR>Death, dying.<BR>--14 Manifestation,<BR>appearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1073-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थानं|संस्थान
संस्थानं<BR>1 A collection, heap,<BR>quantity.<BR>--2 The aggregation of primary<BR>atoms.<BR>--3 Configuration, position;<BR>आकृतिरवयवसंस्थानविशेषः.<BR>--4 Form,<BR>figure, appearance, shape;<BR>स्त्रीसस्थानं चाण्सरस्तीर्थतारादुत्क्षिप्येनां ज्यीतिरिकं<BR>जगाम Ś. 5. 30; Ms. 9. 261.<BR>--5<BR>Construction, formation.<BR>--6<BR>Vicinity.<BR>--7 Common place of abode.<BR>--8<BR>Situation, position.<BR>--9 Any place or<BR>station.<BR>--10 A place where four<BR>roads meet.<BR>--11 A mark, sign,<BR>characteristic sign.<BR>--12 Death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापक
संस्थापक a. Settling, establishing,<BR>arranging &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापनं|संस्थापन
संस्थापनं<BR>1 Placing or keeping<BR>together, collecting.<BR>--2 Fixing,<BR>determining, regulating; कुर्वीत चैषां प्रत्य<BR>क्षमर्घसंस्थापनं नृपः Ms. 8. 402.<BR>--3<BR>Establishment, confirmation;<BR>धर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय संभवामि गे युगे<BR>Bg. 4. 8.<BR>--4 Restraining, curbing.<BR>--5 A<BR>statute, regulation.<BR>--ना<BR>1<BR>Restraining, curbing.<BR>--2 A means of calming<BR>or composing; संस्थापना प्रियतरा<BR>विरहातुराणां Mk. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थापित
संस्थापित p. p.<BR>1 Collected.<BR>--2<BR>Established, fixed.<BR>--3 Restrained,<BR>curbed, checked.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थित|संस्थितः
संस्थित p. p.<BR>1 Being or standing<BR>together.<BR>--2 Being, staying;<BR>नियोगसंस्थित Pt. 1. 92.<BR>--3 Adjacent,<BR>contiguous.<BR>--4 Resembling, like.<BR>--5<BR>Collected, heaped.<BR>--6 Settled,<BR>fixed, established.<BR>--7 Placed in or on,<BR>being in.<BR>--8 Stationary.<BR>--9<BR>Stopped, completed, ended, finished;<BR>क्व नु खलु संस्थिते कर्मणि आत्पानं<BR>विनोदयामि Ś. 3.<BR>--10 Dead, deceased;<BR>प्रमदामनु संस्थितः शुचा R. 1. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्थितिः|संस्थिति
संस्थितिः f.<BR>1 Being together,<BR>staying with.<BR>--2 Contiguity, nearness,<BR>vicinity.<BR>--3 Residence, abode,<BR>resting-place; यथा नदीनदाः सर्वे सागरे<BR>यांति संस्थितिम् । तथैवाश्रतिणः सर्वे<BR>गृहस्थे यांति संस्थितिं Ms. 6. 90.<BR>--4<BR>Accumulation, heap.<BR>--5 Duration,<BR>continuance; H. 1. 43.<BR>--6 Station,<BR>state, condition of life.<BR>--7 Restraint.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">Page1074-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--Death.<BR>--8 Destruction of the<BR>world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृश्
संस्पृश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To touch.<BR>--2 To<BR>sprinkle with water; Ms. 2. 53.<BR>--3<BR>To bring in contact with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पर्शः|संस्पर्श
संस्पर्शः<BR>1 Contact, touch,<BR>conjunction, mixture.<BR>--2 Being<BR>touched or affected.<BR>--3 Perception,<BR>sense.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पर्शी
संस्पर्शी A kind of fragrant plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्पृष्ट
संस्पृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 (a) Touched, brought<BR>into contact; (b) Affected, smit;<BR>Ś. 4. 5.<BR>--2 Mixed, mingled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फालः|संस्फाल
संस्फालः^1<BR>1 A ram.<BR>--2 A cloud.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फुट|संस्फुटः
संस्फुट a. Blossomed, blown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फेटः|संस्फेट
संस्फेटः, संस्फोटः, संस्फोटिः War,<BR>battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फोटः|संस्फोट
संस्फेटः, संस्फोटः, संस्फोटिः War,<BR>battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्फोटिः|संस्फोटि
संस्फेटः, संस्फोटः, संस्फोटिः War,<BR>battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृ
संस्मृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To remember, think<BR>of, call to mind; स्मर संस्मृत्य न<BR>शांतिरस्ति मे Ku. 4. 17; Bg. 18. 76;<BR>Ms. 4. 149.<BR>--2 To recollect fully.<BR>--Caus. To remind, put in mind<BR>of; (पातालं) मामद्य संस्मरयतीव<BR>भुजंगलोकः Ratn. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मरणं|संस्मरण
संस्मरणं Remembering, calling to<BR>mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्मृतिः|संस्मृति
संस्मृतिः f. Remembrance,<BR>recollection; संस्मृतिर्भव भवत्यभवाय<BR>Ki. 18. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्रवः|संस्रव
संस्रवः, संस्रावः<BR>1 Flowing,<BR>trickling, oozing.<BR>--2 A stream.<BR>--3 The<BR>remains of a libation.<BR>--4 A kind of<BR>offering or libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संस्रावः|संस्राव
संस्रवः, संस्रावः<BR>1 Flowing,<BR>trickling, oozing.<BR>--2 A stream.<BR>--3 The<BR>remains of a libation.<BR>--4 A kind of<BR>offering or libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहन्
संहन् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To unite closely<BR>together, join together; हस्तौ संहत्य<BR>Ms. 2. 71; दूत एव हि संधत्तं भिनत्त्येव<BR>च संहतान् 7. 66; see संहत.<BR>--2 To<BR>heap, collect, accumulate.<BR>--3 To<BR>contract, diminish.<BR>--4 To strike,<BR>kill, destroy.<BR>--5 To strike against<BR>each other, clash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहत|संहतः
संहत p. p.<BR>1 Struck together,<BR>wounded.<BR>--2 Closed, shut.<BR>--3<BR>Wellknit, firmly united.<BR>--4 Closely<BR>joined or allied; Ki. 1. 19.<BR>--5 Compact,<BR>firm, solid.<BR>--6 Combined, joined,<BR>keeping together, being in a body,<BR>being very close; जालमादाय गच्छंति<BR>संहताः पक्षिणोऽप्यमी Pt. 2. 8;<BR>5. 101; H. 1. 37.<BR>--7 Of one accord.<BR>--8 Assembled, collected.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जानु a. knock-kneed.<BR>--भ्रू a.<BR>knitting the eyebrows.<BR>--स्तनी a<BR>woman whose breasts are very close to<BR>each other.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतता
संहतता --त्वं<BR>1 Close contact,<BR>conjunction.<BR>--2 Compactness.<BR>--3<BR>Agreement, union.<BR>--4 Harmony,<BR>concord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतत्वं|संहतत्व
संहतता --त्वं<BR>1 Close contact,<BR>conjunction.<BR>--2 Compactness.<BR>--3<BR>Agreement, union.<BR>--4 Harmony,<BR>concord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहतिः|संहति
संहतिः f.<BR>1 Firm or close contact,<BR>close union; Ku. 5. 8.<BR>--2 Union,<BR>combination; सहातिः कार्यसाधिका,<BR>संहतिः श्रेयसी पुंसां H. 1; cf. “Union<BR>is strength”.<BR>--3 Compactness,<BR>firmness, solidity.<BR>--4 Bulk, mass;<BR>गुरुतां नयंति हि गुणा न संहतिः<BR>Ki. 12. 10.<BR>--5 Agreement, harmony.<BR>--6<BR>A collection, heap, assemblage,<BR>multitude; वनान्यवांचीव चकार<BR>संहतिः Ki. 14. 34, 27; 3. 20; 5. 4;<BR>Mu. 3. 2.<BR>--7 Strength.<BR>--8 The<BR>body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहननं|संहनन
संहननं<BR>1 Compactness, firmness.<BR>--2 The body, person;<BR>अमृताध्मातजीमूतस्निग्धसंहतनस्य ते U. 6. 21;<BR>Mv. 2. 46.<BR>--3 Strength; see संहति<BR>also.<BR>--4 Rubbing the limbs.<BR>--5<BR>Killing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहवनं|संहवन
संहवनं^1<BR>1 The act of sacrificing<BR>together.<BR>--2 Sacrificing in a<BR>proper manner.<BR>--3 A quadrangular<BR>group of four houses.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170214. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: 'vah' should be 'hav'; sacrificing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहातः|संहात
संहातः One of the 21 hells;<BR>Ms. 4. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहित|संहितः
संहित p. p.<BR>1 Placed together,<BR>joined, united.<BR>--2 Agreeing with,<BR>conformable to, in accordance with.<BR>--3 Relating to.<BR>--4 Collected.<BR>--5<BR>Provided, furnished, endowed,<BR>accompanied.<BR>--6 Caused by.<BR>--7<BR>Placed, fixed.<BR>--8 Compiled; see<BR>संधा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहिता
संहिता<BR>1 Combination, union,<BR>conjunction.<BR>--2 A collection,<BR>compilation, compendium.<BR>--3 Any<BR>systematically arranged collection<BR>of texts or verses.<BR>--4 A<BR>compendium or compilation of laws, code,<BR>digest; मनुसंहिता.<BR>--5 The<BR>continuous hymnical text of the Veda as<BR>formed out of the Padas or<BR>individual words by proper phonetic<BR>changes according to different<BR>Śākhās or schools; पदप्रकृतिः सहिता<BR>Nir.<BR>--6 (In gram) Compination or<BR>junction of letters according to the<BR>rules of Saṃdhi or euphony; परः<BR>संनिकर्षः संहिता P. I. 4. 109;<BR>वर्णानामतिशयितः संनिधिः संहितासंज्ञः स्यात्<BR>Sk.; or वर्णानामे कप्राणयोगः संहिता.<BR>--7 The Supreme Being who hold<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-a" target="_blank">Page1075-a+ 56</a>]<BR>and supports the universe.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पाठः the continuous text of the<BR>Veda (opp. पदपाठ q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1074-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहूतिः|संहूति
संहूतिः f. General shout, loud<BR>uproar, tumultuous exultation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृ
संहृ {c1c} P. (sometimes A. also)<BR>1 To bring or draw together.<BR>--2 To<BR>draw out, suck; Pt. 1. 221.<BR>--3 (a)<BR>To contract, abridge, compress;<BR>महिमानं यदुत्कीर्त्य तव संह्रि ते वचः<BR>R. 10. 30. (b) To drop; संह्रियतामियं<BR>K.<BR>--4 To bring together, collect,<BR>accumulate.<BR>--5 To destroy,<BR>annihilate (opp. सृज्): अमुं<BR>युगांतोचितकालनिद्रः संहृत्य लाकान् पुरुषोऽधिशेते<BR>R. 13. 6.<BR>--6 To withdraw, withhold<BR>draw or take back; अभिमुखे मयि<BR>संहृतमीक्षितं Ś. 2. 11; 6. 3; न हि संहरते<BR>ज्योत्स्नां चंद्रश्चांडालवेश्मनि H. 1. 61;<BR>R. 4. 16; 12. 103.<BR>--7 To curb,<BR>restrain, suppress; क्रोधं प्रभो संहर संहरेति<BR>यावद्गिरः खे मरुतां चरंति Ku. 3. 72.<BR>--8<BR>To wind up, close.<BR>--9 To seize,<BR>take.<BR>--10 To unite, bind by<BR>obligations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहरणं|संहरण
संहरणं<BR>1 Gathering, bringing<BR>together, collecting.<BR>--2 Taking,<BR>seizing.<BR>--3 Contracting.<BR>--4<BR>Restraining.<BR>--5 Destroying, ruining.<BR>--6<BR>Withdrawing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्तृ
संहर्तृ m. A destroyer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहारः|संहार
संहारः<BR>1 Drawing or bringing<BR>together, collecting; अनुभवनु<BR>वेणीसंहारमहोत्सवं Ve. 6.<BR>--2 Contraction,<BR>compression, abridgment.<BR>--3<BR>Withholding, drawing back, withdrawal<BR>(opp. प्रयोग or विक्षेप); प्रयोगसंह<BR>रविभक्तमंत्रं R. 5. 57, 45.<BR>--4<BR>Restraining, holding back.<BR>--5<BR>Destruction, especially of the universe,<BR>universal destruction.<BR>--6 Close,<BR>end, conclusion.<BR>--7 An assemblage,<BR>a group.<BR>--8 A fault in<BR>pronunciation.<BR>--9 A charm or spell for<BR>withdrawing magical weapons.<BR>--10<BR>Practice, skill.<BR>--11 A division of<BR>hell.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भैरवः one of the<BR>forms of Bhairava.<BR>--मुद्रा N. of a<BR>particular posture in the Tantra<BR>worship; it is thus defined:--<BR>अवोमुखे वामहस्ते ऊर्ध्वास्यं दक्षहस्तकं ।<BR>क्षिप्तांगुलीरंगुलीभिः संगृह्य परिवर्तयेत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहारक
संहारक a.<BR>1 Destructive.<BR>--2<BR>Compressing, contracting, closing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृत|संहृतः
संहृत p. p.<BR>1 Drawn together.<BR>--2<BR>Contracted, abridged.<BR>--3 Withdrawn,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">Page1075-b+ 54</a>]<BR>drawn back.<BR>--4 Collected,<BR>assembled.<BR>--5 Seized, laid hold of.<BR>--6<BR>Curbed. restrained.<BR>--7 Destroyed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृतिः|संहृति
संहृतिः f.<BR>1 Contraction,<BR>compression.<BR>--2 Destruction, loss.<BR>--3<BR>Taking, seizure.<BR>--4 Restraint.<BR>--5<BR>Collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृष्
संहृष् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be glad, rejoice,<BR>thrill with delight.<BR>--2 To<BR>bristle, stand on end (as hair).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहर्षः|संहर्ष
संहर्षः<BR>1 Horripilation, a thrill of<BR>joy or fear.<BR>--2 Pleasure, joy,<BR>delight.<BR>--3 Emulation, rivalry.<BR>--4<BR>Wind.<BR>--5 Rubbing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संहृष्ट
संहृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Thrilled or<BR>horripilated with joy, delighted.<BR>--2<BR>Bristling, shuddering.<BR>--3 Fired with<BR>emulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्रादः|संह्राद
संह्रादः<BR>1 A loud noise, an<BR>uproar.<BR>--2 Noise in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संह्रीण
संह्रीण a.<BR>1 Modest, bashful.<BR>--2<BR>Completely abashed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकट|सकटः
सकट a. Bad, vile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकंटक|सकण्टक|सकण्टकः
सकंटक a.<BR>1 Thorny, prickly.<BR>--2 Troublesome, dangerous.<BR>--कः<BR>The aquatic plant शैवल q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकंप|सकम्प
सकंप, सकंपन a. Trembling,<BR>tremulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकंपन|सकम्पन
सकंप, सकंपन a. Trembling,<BR>tremulous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकरुण|सकरुणः
सकरुण a. Tender,<BR>compassionate, merciful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्ण|सकर्णः
सकर्ण a. (र्णा or र्णी)<BR>1 Having<BR>ears.<BR>--2 Hearing, listening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्तृक
सकर्तृक a. Having an agent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकर्मक|सकर्म्मक|सकर्म्मकः
सकर्मक a. Having or<BR>performing any act. -- (In gram.)<BR>Having an object, transitive (as a<BR>verb).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकल|सकलं
सकल a.<BR>1 Together with the<BR>parts<BR>--2 All, whole, entire,<BR>complete.<BR>--3 Having all the digits, full<BR>(as the moon); as in सकलेंदुमुखी.<BR>--4 Having a soft or low sound.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Everything.<BR>--2 The whole.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्ण a. (i. e. पद or वाक्य)<BR>having the letters क & ल, i. e.<BR>quarrelling; Nalod. 2. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकल्प|सकल्पः
सकल्प a. Attended with the<BR>ritual or ceremonial part of the<BR>Veda; Ms. 2. 140.<BR>--ल्पः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाकोलः|सकाकोल
सकाकोलः N. of one of the 21<BR>hells; see Ms. 4. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाम|सकामः
सकाम a.<BR>1 Full of love,<BR>impassioned, loving.<BR>--2 Lustful,<BR>amorous.<BR>--3 One who has got his<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">Page1075-c+ 54</a>]<BR>desired object, satisfied, contented;<BR>काम इदानीं सकामो भवत् Ś. 4; किमन्यत्<BR>सकामा कपालकुंडला Māl. 9.<BR>--मं ind.<BR>1 With pleasure.<BR>--2 Contentedly.<BR>--3 Assuredly, indeed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाल
सकाल a. Seasonable, opportune.<BR>--लं ind. Seasonably, betimes,<BR>early in the morning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकाश|सकाशः
सकाश a. Having appearance,<BR>visible, present, near.<BR>--शः<BR>Presence, vicinity, nearness. (सकाशम्<BR>and सकाशात् are used adverbially<BR>in the sense of {1} near. {2} from<BR>near, from, from the presence of).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुक्षि
सकुक्षि a. Having the same<BR>womb, born of the same mother,<BR>uterine (as a brother &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुल|सकुलः
सकुल a.<BR>1 Belonging to a noble<BR>family.<BR>--2 Belonging to the same<BR>family.<BR>--3 Having a family.<BR>--4<BR>Along with the family.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A<BR>kinsman.<BR>--2 A kind of fish (सकुली<BR>also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकुल्यः|सकुल्य
सकुल्यः<BR>1 One of the same<BR>family.<BR>--2 A distant relation; such<BR>as a descendant in the 4th,<BR>5th, or 6th, or even in the 7th<BR>8th, or 9th degree.<BR>--3 A distant<BR>relation in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृत्
सकृत् ind.<BR>1 Once; सकृदंशो<BR>निपतित सकृत्कन्या प्रदीयते । सकृदाह<BR>ददानीति त्रीण्येतानि सतां सकृत्<BR>Ms. 9. 47.<BR>--2 At one time, on one<BR>occasion, formerly, once;<BR>सकृत्कृतप्रणयोयं जनः Ś. 5.<BR>--3 At once.<BR>--4<BR>Always.<BR>--5 Together with. --m.<BR>--f. Feces, excrement (usually<BR>written शकृत् q. v.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गर्भा<BR>{1} a mule. {2} a woman who is<BR>pregnant only once.<BR>--प्रजः a crow.<BR>--प्रसूता, --प्रसूतिका {1} a woman who<BR>has borne only one child. {2} a<BR>cow that has calved once.<BR>--फला<BR>the plantain tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकृपण
सकृपण a. Miserable, wretched.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकेश
सकेश a.<BR>1 Having hair.<BR>--2<BR>Hairy, shaggy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकैतव|सकैतवः
सकैतव a. Deceitful,<BR>fraudulent.<BR>--वः A cheat, rogue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सकोप
सकोप a. Angry, enraged.<BR>--पं<BR>ind. Angrily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्त|सक्तः
सक्त p. p. [संज् क्त]<BR>1 Stuck or<BR>attached to, in contact with.<BR>--2<BR>Addicted, devoted or attached to;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">Page1076-a+ 55</a>]<BR>fond of; सक्तासि किं कथय वैरिणि<BR>मौर्यपुत्रे Mu. 2. 6.<BR>--3 Fixed or<BR>rivetted on; नगेंद्रसक्तां परिवर्त्य दृष्टिं<BR>R. 2. 28.<BR>--4 Relating to.<BR>--5<BR>Diligent, attentive.<BR>--6 Obstructed,<BR>hindered.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वैर a. engaged<BR>in hostilities, constant in enmity;<BR>Ś. 2. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1075-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तिः|सक्ति
सक्तिः f.<BR>1 Contact, touch<BR>--2<BR>Union, junction; सक्तिं<BR>जवादपनयत्यनिलोलतानां Ki. 5. 46.<BR>--3<BR>Attachment, addiction, devotion (to<BR>anything).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तु|सक्तुः
सक्तु m. pl. [संज्-तुन् किच्च] The<BR>flour of barley first fried and then<BR>ground, barley-meal; भिक्षासक्तुभिरेव<BR>संप्रति वयं वृत्तिं समीहामहे Bh. 2. 64.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फला-ली the Śamī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुकः|सक्तुक
सक्तुकः<BR>1 = सक्तु.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्तुल
सक्तुल a. Containing barley-flour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्थन्
सक्थन् A substitute for सक्थि<BR>after acc. dual<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्थि
सक्थि n. [संज् --किथन् Uṇ. 3. 154]<BR>1 The thigh; (changed in comp.<BR>to सक्थ after उत्तर, पूर्व and मृग or<BR>when the compound implies<BR>comparison; see P. V. 4. 98).<BR>--2 A<BR>bone.<BR>--3 The pole or shafts of a<BR>carriage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्रिय
सक्रिय a. Active, moveable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सक्षण
सक्षण a. Being at leisure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखि
सखि m. [सह समानं ख्यायते नि˚<BR>Uṇ. 4. 136] (nom. सखा, सखायौ,<BR>सखयः; acc. सखायं, सखायौ; सख्युः gen.<BR>sing.; loc. sing.) A friend,<BR>companion, an associate; तस्मात्सखा त्वम<BR>सि यन्मम तत्तवैव U. 5. 10; सखीनिव<BR>प्रीतियुजोऽनुजीविनः Ki. 1. 10. (At<BR>the end of comp. सखि is changed to<BR>सख; वनितासखानां Ku. 1. 10; सचिवसखः<BR>R. 4. 87; 1. 48, 12. 9; Bk. 1. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखी
सखी A female friend or<BR>companion, a lady's maid; नृत्यति<BR>युवतिजनेन समं सखि विरहिजनस्य दुरंते Gīt. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सखीयति
सखीयति Den. P. To wish for a<BR>friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सख्यं|सख्य|सख्यः
सख्यं [सख्युभार्वः यत्]<BR>1<BR>Friendship, intimacy, alliance; मुमूर्च्छ<BR>सख्य रामस्य समानव्यसने हरौ R. 12. 57;<BR>समानशीलव्यसनेषु सख्यम् Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Equality.<BR>--ख्यः A friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग्
सग् {c1c} P. (सगति) To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगण|सगणः
सगण a. Attended by troops or<BR>flocks.<BR>--णः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगंध|सगन्ध|सगन्धः
सगंध a. Fragrant.<BR>--धः A<BR>kinsman, relation, kindred; सवेः<BR>सगंधषु विश्वसिति Ś. 5; Ms. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर|सगरः
सगर a. [गरेण विषेण सहितः]<BR>Poisonous, having poison.<BR>--रः N.<BR>of a king of the Solar race.<BR>[He was a son of Bāhu and was<BR>called Sagara because he was born<BR>together with gara or poison given to<BR>his mother by the other wife of his<BR>father. By his wife Sumati he had<BR>60000 sons. He successfully performed<BR>99 sacrifices, but when he commenced the<BR>hundredth, his sacrificial horse was<BR>stolen by Indra and carried down to<BR>the Pātāla. Sagara thereupon<BR>commanded his 60000 sons to search it out.<BR>Finding no trace of the animal on earth<BR>they began to dig down towards the<BR>Pātāla, and in doing this they<BR>naturally increased the boundaries of the<BR>ocean which was therefore called<BR>Sāgara; cf. R. 13. 3. Meeting with the<BR>sage Kapila they rashly accused him<BR>of having stolen their horse, as a<BR>punishment for which they were<BR>instantly reduced to ashes by that sage.<BR>It was after several thousands of years<BR>that Bhagīratha (q. v.) succeeded in<BR>bringing down to the Pātāla the<BR>celestial river Ganges to water and purify<BR>their ashes and thus to convey their<BR>souls to heaven].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्भः|सगर्भ
सगर्भः --र्भ्यः A brother of whole<BR>blood: Mv. 6. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगर्भ्यः|सगर्भ्य
सगर्भः --र्भ्यः A brother of whole<BR>blood: Mv. 6. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगुण
सगुण a.<BR>1 Possessed of<BR>qualities or attributes.<BR>--2 Possessed of<BR>good qualities, virtuous.<BR>--3<BR>Worldly.<BR>--4 Furnished with a string<BR>(as a bow).<BR>--5 Possessed of the<BR>qualities in rhetoric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सगोत्र|सगोत्रं|सगोत्रः
सगोत्र a. Being of the same<BR>family or kin, related.<BR>--त्रः<BR>1 A<BR>kinsman sprung from a common<BR>ancestor; तत्रमवतो युष्मत्सगोत्रस्य<BR>कण्वस्यापराद्धोम्मि Ś. 7.<BR>--2 A kinsman<BR>of the same family, one connected<BR>by funeral oblations of food and<BR>water.<BR>--3 A distant kinsman.<BR>--त्रं<BR>Family, race, lineage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सग्धिः|सग्धि
सग्धिः f. Eating together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सघ्
सघ् {c5c} P. (सघ्नोति)<BR>1 To hurt,<BR>injure, kill.<BR>--2 To receive, accept.<BR>--3<BR>To support, bear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकट|सङ्कट|सङ्कटः
संकट a.<BR>1 Contracted, narrow,<BR>strait.<BR>--2 Impervious, impassable.<BR>--3 Full of, crowded with, beset<BR>with, hemmed in; संकटा<BR>ह्याहिताग्नीनां प्रत्यवायैर्गृहस्थता Mv. 4. 33;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">Page1076-c+ 56</a>]<BR>विषमशिलासंकटस्खलितवेगः V. 2. 8;<BR>U. 1. 8.<BR>--टं<BR>1 A narrow passage,<BR>defile, pass.<BR>--2 A difficulty, strait,<BR>risk, peril, danger;<BR>संकटेष्वविषण्णधीः K.; संकटे हि परीक्ष्यंते प्राज्ञाः<BR>शूराश्च संगरे Ks. 31. 93.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकथ्|सङ्कथ्
संकथ् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To talk together,<BR>converse.<BR>--2 To narrate, relate.<BR>--3<BR>To explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकथनं|सङ्कथन|संकथन|सङ्कथनं
संकथनं Narration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकथा|सङ्कथा
संकथा Conversation, talk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकल्|सङ्कल्
संकल् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To add or sum<BR>up.<BR>--2 To heap, accumulate, collect.<BR>--3 To deem, regard;<BR>तरुच्छिद्रप्रोतान् विसमिति करी संकलयति K. P. 10.<BR>--4 To grasp, seize, lay hold of.<BR>--5<BR>To drive away, put to fight, rout.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकलः|सङ्कल|संकल|सङ्कलः
संकलः<BR>1 Accumulation, collection,<BR>--2 Addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकलनं|सङ्कलन|संकलन|सङ्कलनं
संकलनं --ना<BR>1 The act of heaping<BR>together.<BR>--2 Contact, junction.<BR>--3<BR>Collision.<BR>--4 Blending, twining.<BR>--5<BR>Addition (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकलना
संकलनं --ना<BR>1 The act of heaping<BR>together.<BR>--2 Contact, junction.<BR>--3<BR>Collision.<BR>--4 Blending, twining.<BR>--5<BR>Addition (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकलित|सङ्कलित|सङ्कलितः
संकलित p. p.<BR>1 Heaped up, piled<BR>up, collected.<BR>--2 Blended together,<BR>intermixed.<BR>--3 Seized, laid hold of.<BR>--4 Added.<BR>--5 Resumed, regained;<BR>Māl. 3.<BR>--ता (In arith.) The first<BR>sum.<BR>--तं Addition.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ऐक्यं the sum of the terms of an<BR>arithmetical progression.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकसुक|सङ्कसुक
संकसुक a.<BR>1 Unsteady, fickle,<BR>changeable, inconstant.<BR>--2<BR>Uncertrin doubtful.<BR>--3 Bad, wicked.<BR>--4<BR>Weak, feeble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकारः|सङ्कार|संकार|सङ्कारः
संकारः<BR>1 Dust, sweepings.<BR>--2<BR>The crackling of flames.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकारी
संकारी A girl recently<BR>deflowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकाश|सङ्काश|संकाशः|सङ्काशः
संकाश a.<BR>1 Like, similar,<BR>resembling (at the end of comp.), अग्नि˚,<BR>हिरण्य˚.<BR>--2 Near, close, at hand.<BR>--शः<BR>1 Appearance, presence.<BR>--2<BR>Vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकिलः|सङ्किल|संकिल|सङ्किलः
संकिलः A fire brand, burning<BR>torch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकुच्|सङ्कुच्
संकुच् {1} {c6c} P.<BR>1 To become<BR>contracted, shrink.<BR>--2 To close,<BR>shut (as a flower).<BR>--3 To contract,<BR>compress. --Caus. To contract,<BR>narrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकुचित|सङ्कुचित|सङ्कुचितं
संकुचित p. p.<BR>1 Contracted,<BR>abridged; लंकापतेः संकुचितं यशो यत्<BR>Vikr. 1. 27.<BR>--2 Shrunk, wrinkled;<BR>Pt. 4. 78.<BR>--3 Closed, shut.<BR>--4<BR>Covering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1076-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकोचः|सङ्कोच|संकोच|सङ्कोचं|सङ्कोचः
संकोचः<BR>1 Contraction, shrinking<BR>up.<BR>--2 Abridgment, diminution,<BR>compression.<BR>--3 Terror, fear.<BR>--4<BR>Shutting up, closing.<BR>--5 Binding.<BR>--6 A kind of skate-fish.<BR>--चं Saffron.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पिशुनं saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकोचनं|सङ्कोचन|संकोचन
संकोचनं Contraction.<BR>--नी The<BR>sensitive plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकुल|सङ्कुल|सङ्कुलं
संकुल a.<BR>1 Confused.<BR>--2<BR>Thronged with, crowded or filled with,<BR>full of; नक्षत्रताराग्रहसंकुलापि<BR>ज्योतिष्मती चंद्रमसैव रात्रिः R. 6. 22;<BR>Māl. 1. 2.<BR>--3 Disordered, perplexed;<BR>U. 2. 30.<BR>--4 Inconsistent.<BR>--लं<BR>1<BR>A crowd, mob, throng, collection,<BR>swarm, flock; महतः पारैजनस्य<BR>संकुलेन विघटितायां तस्यामागतोऽस्मि Māl. 1;<BR>Pt. 1. 7.<BR>--2 A confused fight, melee.<BR>--3 An inconsistent or contradictory<BR>speech; e. g. यावज्जीवमहं मौनी<BR>ब्रह्मचारी च मे पिता । माता तु मम वंध्यैव<BR>पुत्रहीनः पितामहः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकूजितं|सङ्कूजित|संकूजित
संकूजितं The cry of the<BR>Chakravāka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकृ|सङ्कृ
संकृ {c8c} U. (संकुरुते)<BR>1 To<BR>commit; ये पक्षापरपक्षदोषसहिताः पापानि<BR>संकुर्वते Mk. 9. 4.<BR>--2 To<BR>manufacture, prepare.<BR>--3 To do. perform<BR>in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकृष्|सङ्कृष्
संकृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To drag along or<BR>away.<BR>--2 To contract.<BR>--3 To<BR>tighten, tie fast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकर्षणं|सङ्कर्षण|संकर्षण|सङ्कर्षणं|संकर्षणः|सङ्कर्षणः
संकर्षणं<BR>1 The act of drawing<BR>together, contracting.<BR>--2<BR>Attracting.<BR>--3 Ploughing, furrowing.<BR>--4<BR>Shortening.<BR>--णः N. of Balarāma;<BR>संकर्षणात्तु गर्भस्य स हि संकषणो युवा<BR>Hariv.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकॄ|सङ्कॄ
संकॄ {c6c} P.<BR>1 To mix, commingle<BR>or mix together.<BR>--2 To scatter<BR>about, diffuse.<BR>--3 To fill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकरः|सङ्कर|संकर|सङ्करः
संकरः<BR>1 Commingling, mixture,<BR>intermixture; पत्रसंकर Ś. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Blending together, union.<BR>--3<BR>Confusion or mixture (of castes),<BR>unlawful intermarriage resulting in<BR>mixed castes; चित्रेषु वर्णसंकरः K.;<BR>संकरो नरकायैव कुलघ्नानां कुलस्य च<BR>Bg. 1. 42; Ms. 10. 40.<BR>--4 (In<BR>Rhet.) The combination of two or<BR>more dependent figures of speech in<BR>one and the same passage (opp.<BR>संसृष्टि where the figures are<BR>independent); अविश्रांतिजुषामात्मन्यंगांगित्वे<BR>तु सकरः K. P. 10; or अंगागित्वेऽ<BR>लंकृतीनां तद्वदेकाश्रयस्थितौ । संदिग्धत्वे च<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-b" target="_blank">Page1077-b+ 56</a>]<BR>भवति संकरस्त्रिविधः पुनः S. D. 757.<BR>--5<BR>The crackling of flames.<BR>--6 Dust,<BR>sweepings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकारः|सङ्कार|संकार|सङ्कारः
संकारः<BR>1 Dust, sweepings.<BR>--2<BR>Crackling of flames.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकारिन्
संकारिन् a.<BR>1 Confused,<BR>intermixed.<BR>--2 Arising from intermixture<BR>of castes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकीर्ण|सङ्कीर्ण|सङ्कीर्णं|संकीर्णः|सङ्कीर्णः
संकीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Mixed together,<BR>intermingled.<BR>--2 Confused,<BR>miscellaneous.<BR>--3 Shattered, spread,<BR>crowded.<BR>--4 Indistinct.<BR>--5 In rut,<BR>intoxicated; H. 4. 17.<BR>--6 Of mixed<BR>caste, of impure origin.<BR>--7 Impure,<BR>adulterated.<BR>--8 Narrow,<BR>contracted.<BR>--र्णः<BR>1 A man of a mixed<BR>caste.<BR>--2 A mixed note or mode.<BR>--3<BR>An elephant in rut, an<BR>intoxicated elephant.<BR>--र्णं A difficulty.<BR>--र्णा<BR>A kind of riddle.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जाति,<BR>--योनि a. of mixed birth, of a<BR>mongrel breed (as a mule).<BR>--युद्धं a<BR>confused fight, melee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकॄत्
संकॄत् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To recite.<BR>--2 To<BR>praise, celebrate, glorify.<BR>--3 To tell,<BR>mention.<BR>--4 To proclaim, announce.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकीर्तनं|सङ्कीर्तन|सङ्कीर्त्तन|सङ्कीर्त्तनं
संकीर्तनं --ना<BR>1 Praising,<BR>applauding, extolling.<BR>--2 Glorification (of<BR>a deity).<BR>--3 Repeating the name of<BR>a deity as a pious or devotional<BR>act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकीर्तना
संकीर्तनं --ना<BR>1 Praising,<BR>applauding, extolling.<BR>--2 Glorification (of<BR>a deity).<BR>--3 Repeating the name of<BR>a deity as a pious or devotional<BR>act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकॢप्|सङ्कॢप्
संकॢप् {c1c} A. To wish or long<BR>for. --Caus.<BR>1 To resolve,<BR>determine, settle.<BR>--2 To intend, aim at,<BR>purpose; Ku. 3. 11.<BR>--3 To arrange<BR>or connect together.<BR>--4 To fix,<BR>assign, allot.<BR>--5 To consecrate,<BR>dedicate.<BR>--6 To imagine, fancy.<BR>--7<BR>To think about, ponder, reflect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकल्पः|सङ्कल्प|संकल्प|सङ्कल्पः
संकल्पः<BR>1 Will, volition, mental<BR>resolve; कः कामः संकल्पः Dk<BR>--2<BR>Purpose, aim, intention,<BR>determination.<BR>--3 Wish, desire;<BR>संकल्पमात्रोदितसिद्धयस्ते R. 14. 17.<BR>--4 Thought,<BR>idea, reflection, fancy, imagination;<BR>तत्संकल्पोपहितजाडिम स्तंभमभ्योति गात्रं<BR>Māl. 1. 35; वृथैव संकल्पशतैरजस्रमनंग<BR>नीतोसि मया विवृद्धिं Ś. 3. 5.<BR>--5 The<BR>mind, heart; Māl. 6. 2.<BR>--6 A<BR>solemn vow to perform an<BR>observance.<BR>--7 Expectation of advantage<BR>from a holy voluntary act.<BR>--8<BR>Consideration, reflection.<BR>--9 A<BR>declaration made by a widow at the time<BR>of burning herself with her husband.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मक a. {1} willing,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-c" target="_blank">Page1077-c+ 56</a>]<BR>resolving. {2} consisting of thought<BR>only, imaginary.<BR>--जः, --जन्मन् m.,<BR>--योनिः epithets of the god of love;<BR>भगवन्संकल्पयोने M. 4; Ku. 3. 24.<BR>--रूप a. {1} volitional. {2}<BR>conformable to will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकल्पित|सङ्कल्पित
संकल्पित a.<BR>1 Wished for,<BR>intended, aimed at.<BR>--2 Determined,<BR>resolved upon; Ś. 4. 13.<BR>--3 Imagined,<BR>fancied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेतः|सङ्केत|संकेत|सङ्केतः
संकेतः<BR>1 An intimation,<BR>allusion.<BR>--2 A sign, gesture, hint;<BR>Mu. 1.<BR>--3 An indicatory sign, mark,<BR>token.<BR>--4 Agreement, convention;<BR>संकेतो गृह्यते जातौ गुणद्रव्यक्रियासु च<BR>S. D. 12.<BR>--5 Engagement,<BR>appointment, assignation (made by a<BR>mistress or lover); नामसमेतं कृतसंकेतं<BR>वादयते मृदु वेणुं Gīt. 5.<BR>--6 A place<BR>of meeting (for lovers), rendezvous;<BR>कांतार्थिनी तु या याति संकेतं<BR>साभिसारिका Ak.<BR>--7 Condition, provision.<BR>--8 A short explanatory rule (in<BR>gram.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गृहं, --निकेतनं,<BR>--स्थानं a place of appointment or<BR>assignation; rendezvous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेतकः|सङ्केतक
संकेतकः<BR>1 Agreement, convention.<BR>--2 Appointment, assignation.<BR>--3<BR>Rendezvous.<BR>--4 A lover or mistress<BR>who makes an appointment; संकेतके<BR>चिरयति प्रवरो विनोदः Mk. 3. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेतनं|सङ्केतन|संकेतन
संकेतनं<BR>1 Appointment,<BR>agreement.<BR>--2 A rendezvous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेतयति
संकेतयति Den. P.<BR>1 To agree<BR>upon, appoint.<BR>--2 To fix by<BR>convention, lay down conventionally.<BR>--3 To<BR>invite, call.<BR>--4 To give a hint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संकेतित|सङ्केतित
संकेतित a.<BR>1 Agreed upon, fixed<BR>by convention; साक्षात्संकेतितं<BR>योऽर्थमभिधत्ते स वाचकः K. P. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Invited, called.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रंदनः|सङ्क्रन्दन|संक्रन्दन|संक्रंदन|संक्रन्दनः|सङ्क्रन्दनः
संक्रंदनः N. of Kṛṣṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रम्|सङ्क्रम्
संक्रम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To come or meet<BR>together.<BR>--2 To traverse, cross, go<BR>or pass through.<BR>--3 To approach,<BR>go.<BR>--4 To go over or be transferred<BR>(to another).<BR>--5 To enter on or<BR>in; कालो ह्ययं संक्रमितुं द्वितीयं<BR>सर्वोपकारक्षममाश्रमं ते R. 5. 10.<BR>--6 To be<BR>present at, attend.<BR>--7 To surmount.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To transfer.<BR>--2 To<BR>devolve, consign, entrust;<BR>ब्राह्मणसंक्रमिताक्षरेण पितामहेन V. 3; Ku. 6. 78.<BR>--3<BR>To deliver, hand over.<BR>--4 To<BR>convey, lead towards.<BR>--5 To take<BR>possession of,<BR>--6 To promise mutual<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">Page1078-a+ 56</a>]<BR>assistance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1077-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रमः|सङ्क्रम|संक्रम|सङ्क्रमः
संक्रमः<BR>1 Concurrence, going<BR>together.<BR>--2 Transition, traversing,<BR>transfer, progress.<BR>--3 The passage<BR>of a planetary body through the<BR>zodiacal signs.<BR>--4 Moving, travelling.<BR>--मः --मं<BR>1 A difficult or narrow<BR>passage.<BR>--2 A causeway, bridge;<BR>नदीमार्गेषु च तथा संक्रमानवसादयेत् Mb.<BR>--3 A medium or means of attaining<BR>any object; तामेव संक्रमीकृत्य Dk.;<BR>सोऽतिथिः स्वर्गसंक्रमः Pt. 4. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रमणं|सङ्क्रमण|संक्रमण|सङ्क्रमणं
संक्रमणं<BR>1 Concurrence.<BR>--2<BR>Transition, progress, passing from one<BR>point to another.<BR>--3 Passage.<BR>--4<BR>The sun's passage from one zodiacal<BR>sign to another.<BR>--5 The day on<BR>which the summer solstice begins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रांत|सङ्क्रान्त|संक्रान्त|सङ्क्रान्तः
संक्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Passed through<BR>or into, entered into.<BR>--2<BR>Transferred; devolved, entrusted;<BR>पुत्रसंक्रांतलक्ष्मीकैर्यद्वृद्धेक्ष्वाकुभिर्धृतं<BR>U. 1. 22.<BR>--3 Seized, affected.<BR>--4<BR>Reflected, imaged.<BR>--5 Depicted.<BR>--6<BR>Having Saṃkrānti (in astr.).<BR>--तं<BR>Property got by a woman from her<BR>husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रांतिः|सङ्क्रान्ति|संक्रान्ति|संक्रांति|संक्रान्तिः|सङ्क्रान्तिः
संक्रांतिः f.<BR>1 Going together,<BR>union.<BR>--2 Passage from one point to<BR>another, transition.<BR>--3 The passage<BR>of the sun or any planetary body<BR>from one zodiacal sign into another.<BR>--4 Transference, giving over (to<BR>another); संपातिताः… पयसो<BR>गंडूषसंक्रांतयः U. 3. 16.<BR>--5 Transferring<BR>or communicating (one's knowledge<BR>to another), power of imparting<BR>(instruction to another); विवादे<BR>दर्शयिष्यंतं क्रियासंक्रांतिमात्मनः M. 1. 19;<BR>शिष्टा क्रिया कस्यचिदात्मसंस्था<BR>संक्रांतिरन्यस्य विशेषयुक्ता 1. 16.<BR>--6 Image,<BR>reflection.<BR>--7 Depicting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रामः|सङ्क्राम|संक्राम|सङ्क्रामः
संक्रामः Difficult progress; see संक्रम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रीड्|सङ्क्रीड्
संक्रीड् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To play or sport<BR>together; संक्रीडंते मणिभिरमरप्रार्थिता<BR>यत्र कन्याः Me. 68.<BR>--2 To creak,<BR>rattle (as wheels); संक्रीडंति शकटानि<BR>Mbh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रीडनं|सङ्क्रीडन|संक्रीडन
संक्रीडनं Sporting together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्रीडितं|सङ्क्रीडित|संक्रीडित
संक्रीडितं Rattle of chariots.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्लेदः|सङ्क्लेद|संक्लेद|सङ्क्लेदः
संक्लेदः<BR>1 Dampness, moisture.<BR>--2 The fluid secretion supposed to<BR>form in the first month after<BR>conception and which constitutes the<BR>rudiment of the fœtus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षि|सङ्क्षि
संक्षि {c1c} {c5c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To decay,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">Page1078-b+ 56</a>]<BR>wane.<BR>--2 To be emaciated or lean<BR>--3 To destroy completely,<BR>annihilate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षयः|सङ्क्षय|संक्षय
संक्षयः<BR>1 Destruction.<BR>--2 Complete<BR>destruction or consumption.<BR>--3<BR>Loss, ruin.<BR>--4 End, termination.<BR>--5 Destruction of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षिप्|सङ्क्षिप्
संक्षिप् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To collect or heap<BR>together; आतपात्ययसंक्षिप्तनविरासु<BR>निषादिभिः R. 1. 52; Bk. 5. 86.<BR>--2<BR>To withdraw, destroy.<BR>--3 To shorten,<BR>curtail, abridge; संक्षिप्येत क्षण इव<BR>कथं दीर्घयामा त्रियामा Me. 108;<BR>Ms. 7. 34.<BR>--4 To contract, compress.<BR>--5 To<BR>diminish, lessen.<BR>--6 To confine,<BR>shut in.<BR>--7 To constrain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षिप्त|सङ्क्षिप्त|संक्षिप्तः
संक्षिप्त p. p.<BR>1 Heaped together.<BR>--2 Compressed, contracted.<BR>--3<BR>Abridged, curtailed, shortened.<BR>--4<BR>Diminished, lessened.<BR>--5 Brief,<BR>concise, short.<BR>--6 Restrained.<BR>--7<BR>Thrown, despatched.<BR>--8 Seized,<BR>grasped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षिप्तिः|सङ्क्षिप्ति|संक्षिप्ति
संक्षिप्तिः f.<BR>1 Throwing together.<BR>--2 Compressing, abridging.<BR>--3<BR>Throwing, sending.<BR>--4 Ambuseade.<BR>--5 Transition (from one feeling to<BR>another).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षेपः|सङ्क्षेप|संक्षेप
संक्षेपः<BR>1 Throwing together.<BR>--2<BR>Compression, abridgment.<BR>--3 Brevity,<BR>conciseness.<BR>--4 An epitome, a brief<BR>exposition.<BR>--5 Throwing, sending.<BR>--6 Taking away.<BR>--7 Assisting in<BR>another's duty. (संक्षेपेण, संक्षेपतस्<BR>are used adverbially in the sense of<BR>‘briefly, concisely, shortly’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षेपणं|सङ्क्षेपण|संक्षेपण
संक्षेपणं<BR>1 Heaping together.<BR>--2<BR>Abridgment, abbreviation.<BR>--3<BR>Sending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षुभ्|सङ्क्षुभ्
संक्षुभ् {c1c} A., {c4c} {c9c} P. To tremble,<BR>be agitated or disturbed. --Caus.<BR>To agitate, excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संक्षोभः|सङ्क्षोभ|संक्षोभ
संक्षोभः<BR>1 Agitation, trembling.<BR>--2 Disturbance, commotion; Mk. 2.<BR>--3 Upsetting, overturning.<BR>--4 Pride,<BR>haughtiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्यं|सङ्ख्य|संख्य|सङ्ख्यं
संख्यं War, battle, fight; संख्ये<BR>द्विषां वीररसं चकार Vikr. 1. 68, 70;<BR>Ve. 3. 25; Śi. 18. 70; Māl. 8. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्या|सङ्ख्या
संख्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 To count,<BR>enumerate, calculate, sum up; तावंत्येव च<BR>तत्त्वानि सांख्यैः संख्यायंते Ś. B.<BR>--2<BR>Ved. To appear along with, be<BR>connected with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्यक|सङ्ख्यक
संख्यक a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Numbering, amounting to;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-c" target="_blank">Page1078-c+ 56</a>]<BR>शतसंख्यका नराः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्या|सङ्ख्या
संख्या<BR>1 Enumeration, reckoning,<BR>calculation; संख्यामिवैषां भ्रमरश्चकार<BR>R. 16. 47.<BR>--2 A number.<BR>--3 A<BR>numeral.<BR>--4 Sum.<BR>--5 Reason,<BR>understanding, intellect.<BR>--6 Deliberation,<BR>reflection.<BR>--7 Manner.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--धतिग, अतीत a. beyond number,<BR>innumerable, countless.<BR>--मात्रं mere<BR>numeration.<BR>--वाचक a. expressive of<BR>number.<BR>--(कः) a numeral.<BR>--समापनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्यात|सङ्ख्यात|सङ्ख्यातं
संख्यात p. p.<BR>1 Enumerated.<BR>--2<BR>Calculated, reckoned up.<BR>--तं A<BR>number.<BR>--ता A kind of riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्यानं|सङ्ख्यान|संख्यान|सङ्ख्यानं
संख्यानं Numbering, calculation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संख्यावत्|सङ्ख्यावत्|संख्यावन्त्
संख्यावत् a.<BR>1 Numbered.<BR>--2<BR>Possessed of reason. --m. A learned<BR>man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगः|सङ्ग|संग|सङ्गः
संगः [संज् भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Coming<BR>together, joining.<BR>--2 Meeting,<BR>union, confluence (as of rivers).<BR>--3<BR>Touch, contact.<BR>--4 Company,<BR>association, friendship, friendly<BR>intercourse; सतां सद्भिः संगः कथमपि हि<BR>पुण्येन भवति U. 2. 1; संगमनुव्रज् ‘to<BR>keep company with, herd with’;<BR>मृगाः मृगैः संगमनुव्रजंति Subhāṣ.<BR>--5<BR>Attachment, fondness, desire;<BR>ध्यायतो विषयान्पुंसः संगस्तेषूपजायते<BR>Bg. 2. 62.<BR>--6 Attachment to worldly<BR>ties, association with men;<BR>दौर्मंत्र्यान्नृपतिर्विनश्यति यतिः संगात् Bh. 2. 42;<BR>विमुक्त˚ Ku. 1. 53; Pt. 1. 169.<BR>--7<BR>Encounter, fight.<BR>--8 Hindrance,<BR>obstruction; R. 2. 42; 3. 63.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगिन्|सङ्गिन्
संगिन् a.<BR>1 United with, meeting.<BR>--2 Attached or devoted to, fond<BR>of; Ś. 5. 11; R. 19. 16;<BR>M. 4. 2; Bg. 3. 26; 14. 15.<BR>--3 Full of<BR>affection, desirous.<BR>--4 Libidinous,<BR>lustful.<BR>--5 Continuous,<BR>uninterrupted; Ki. 14. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगणिका|सङ्गणिका
संगणिका An excellent or<BR>incomparable discourse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगम्|सङ्गम्
संगम् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To come or join<BR>together, meet, encounter; अक्षधूर्तैः<BR>समगंसि Dk.; एते भगवत्यौ<BR>कलिंदकन्यामंदाकिन्यौ संगच्छेते A. R. 7.<BR>--2 To<BR>cohabit, have sexual intercourse<BR>with; भार्या च परसंगता Pt. 1. 238;<BR>Ms. 8. 378.<BR>--3 To keep company<BR>or intercourse with, associate with.<BR>--4 To agree, harmonize, be<BR>suitable.<BR>--5 To become contracted,<BR>shrink up.<BR>--6 To die, depart.<BR>--7<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-a" target="_blank">Page1079-a+ 56</a>]<BR>To go to, attain (with acc.). --Caus.<BR>1 To bring together, join, unite;<BR>वधूवरौ संगमयांचकार R. 7. 20.<BR>--2 To<BR>endow or present with, unite with,<BR>bestow on, give to; प्रियसुहृदि<BR>बिभीषणे संगमय्य श्रियं वैरिणः R. 12. 104.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1078-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगत|सङ्गत|सङ्गतं
संगत p. p.<BR>1 Joined or united<BR>with, come together, associated<BR>with.<BR>--2 Assembled, collected,<BR>convened, met together.<BR>--3 Joined in<BR>wedlock, married.<BR>--4 Sexually<BR>united.<BR>--5 Fitted together, appropriate,<BR>harmonious; शृणुतमिदानीं संगतार्थं<BR>नवेति Ś. 3.<BR>--6 In conjunction with<BR>(as planets).<BR>--7 Shrunk up,<BR>contracted; see गम् with सं.<BR>--तं<BR>1<BR>Union, meeting, alliance; संगतं<BR>श्रीसरस्वत्योर्भूतयेऽस्तु सदा सतां V. 5. 24,<BR>Ś. 5. 24.<BR>--2 Association, company.<BR>--3 Acquaintance, friendship,<BR>intimacy; Ku. 5. 39.<BR>--4 A harmonious<BR>or consistent speech, well-reasoned<BR>remarks.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संधिः a peace<BR>concluded after friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगतिः|सङ्गति|संगति|सङ्गतिः
संगतिः f.<BR>1 Union, meeting,<BR>conjunction.<BR>--2 Company, society,<BR>association, intercourse; मनो हि<BR>जन्मांतरसंगतिज्ञं R. 7. 15; क्षणमिह<BR>सज्जनसंगतिरिका भवति भवार्णवतरणे नौ का<BR>Moha M. 6.<BR>--3 Sexual union.<BR>--4<BR>Visiting, frequenting.<BR>--5 Fitness,<BR>appropriateness, applicability,<BR>consistent relation.<BR>--6 Accident, chance,<BR>accidental occurrence.<BR>--7<BR>Knowledge.<BR>--8 Questioning for further<BR>knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगमः|सङ्गम|संगम|सङ्गमः
संगमः<BR>1 Meeting, union;<BR>V. 4. 37; R. 12. 66, 90.<BR>--2 Association,<BR>company, society, intercourse; as<BR>in सद्भिः संगमः.<BR>--3 Contact, touch;<BR>गात्रसंगमात् R. 8. 44.<BR>--4 Sexual<BR>union or intercourse; अयं स ते<BR>तिष्ठति संगमोत्सुकः Ś. 3. 14;<BR>R. 19. 33.<BR>--5 Confluence (of rivers);<BR>गंगायमुनयोः संगमे V. 5.<BR>--6 Fitness,<BR>adaptation.<BR>--7 Encounter, fight.<BR>--8 Conjunction (of planets).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगमनं|सङ्गमन|संगमनः
संगमनं Meeting, union; see संगम.<BR>--नः N. of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगरः|सङ्गर|संगर|सङ्गरं|सङ्गरः
संगरः<BR>1 A promise, an agreement;<BR>तथेति तस्या वितथं प्रतीतः<BR>प्रत्यग्रहीत्संगरमग्रजन्मा R. 5. 26, 11. 48;<BR>पालितसंगराय 13. 65.<BR>--2 Accepting,<BR>undertaking.<BR>--3 A bargain.<BR>--4<BR>War, battle, fight;<BR>अतरत्स्वभुजौजसा मुहुर्महतः संगरसागरानसौ<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">Page1079-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Śi. 16. 67.<BR>--5 Knowledge.<BR>--6 Devouring.<BR>--7 Misfortune, calamity.<BR>--8 Poison.<BR>--9 The fruit of the Śamī tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगवः|सङ्गव|संगव|सङ्गवः
संगवः N. of a particular part of<BR>the day, said to be three<BR>Muhūrtas after Prātastana or<BR>early dawn and to form the<BR>second of the five divisions of<BR>the day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगावः
संगावः Discourse, conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगुप्त|सङ्गुप्त|सङ्गुप्तः
संगुप्त p. p.<BR>1 Well protected or<BR>preserved.<BR>--2 Well concealed, kept<BR>secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगूढ|सङ्गूढ|सङ्गूढः
संगूढ p. p.<BR>1 Completely<BR>concealed or hidden.<BR>--2 Contracted,<BR>abridged.<BR>--3 Joined, united.<BR>--4<BR>Collected, heaped together, piled up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगॄ|सङ्गॄ
संगॄ {c9c} U., {c6c} A.<BR>1 To promise,<BR>make a vow (Atm.); राज्ञे<BR>समगिरेतां Dk.<BR>--2 To recognise, acknow<BR>ledge.<BR>--3 To agree in calling.<BR>--4<BR>To swallow, devour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगीर्ण|सङ्गीर्ण|सङ्गीर्णं
संगीर्ण p. p.<BR>1 Agreed or assented<BR>to.<BR>--2 Promised, vowed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगै|सङ्गै
संगै {c1c} P.<BR>1 To chant, sing in<BR>chorus.<BR>--2 To celebrate by singing<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगीत|सङ्गीत|सङ्गीतं
संगीत p. p. Sung together, sung<BR>in chorus.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Chorus, a song<BR>sung by many voices; जगुः सुकंठ्यो<BR>गंधर्व्यः संगीतं सहभर्तृकाः Bhāg.<BR>--2<BR>Music, harmonious singing,<BR>especially singing accompanied by<BR>instrumental music and dancing,<BR>triple symphony; गीतं वाद्यं नर्तनं च<BR>त्रयं संगीतमुच्यते; किमन्यदस्याः<BR>परिषदः श्रुतिप्रसादनतः संगीतात् Ś. 1;<BR>Mk. 1.<BR>--3 A concert.<BR>--4 The art<BR>of singing with music and dancing;<BR>Bh. 2. 12.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः {1} the<BR>subject of a musical performance.<BR>{2} the materials or necessary<BR>apparatus for a musical concert;<BR>Me. 56.<BR>--शाला a concert-hall; Māl. 2.<BR>--शास्त्रं the science of music.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगीतकं|सङ्गीतक
संगीतकं<BR>1 Concert, symphony.<BR>--2<BR>A public entertainment consisting of<BR>songs attended with music and<BR>dancing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगीतिः|सङ्गीति|संगीति|सङ्गीतिः
संगीतिः f.<BR>1 Concert, symphony,<BR>harmony.<BR>--2 Conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्रह्|सङ्ग्रह्
संग्रह् {c9c} U.<BR>1 To collect, gather,<BR>accumulate, hoard; संगृह्य धनं,<BR>पाशान् &c.<BR>--2 To receive kindly.<BR>--3<BR>To curb, restrain, check, control,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-c" target="_blank">Page1079-c+ 57</a>]<BR>rein in (as horses).<BR>--4 To<BR>unstring (as a bow).<BR>--5 To grasp,<BR>lay hold of.<BR>--6 To to take, receive,<BR>accept.<BR>--7 To conceive,<BR>understand.<BR>--8 To contract, abridge,<BR>narrow.<BR>--9 To encourage,<BR>support, favour.<BR>--10 To seize upon,<BR>attack (as an illness).<BR>--11 To<BR>include, comprise, contain.<BR>--12 To<BR>close, shut (as the mouth).<BR>--13<BR>To concentrate.<BR>--14 To constrain,<BR>force.<BR>--15 To marry.<BR>--16 To<BR>mention, name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संगृहीत|सङ्गृहीत
संगृहीत a.<BR>1 Gathered, collected,<BR>stored.<BR>--2 Grasped, seized.<BR>--3<BR>Restrained, governed.<BR>--4 Received,<BR>accepted.<BR>--5 Abridged; see संग्रह्<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्रहः|सङ्ग्रह|संग्रह|सङ्ग्रहः
संग्रहः<BR>1 Seizing, grasping.<BR>--2<BR>Clenching the fist, grasp, grip.<BR>--3<BR>Reception, admission.<BR>--4 Guarding,<BR>protection; तथा ग्रामशतानां च<BR>कुर्याद्राष्ट्स्य संग्रहं Ms. 7. 114.<BR>--5<BR>Favouring, propitiating, entertaining,<BR>supporting; Ms. 3. 138; 8. 311.<BR>--6<BR>Storing, accumulation, gathering,<BR>collecting; स्वधासंग्रहतत्पराः<BR>R. 1. 66; तैः कृतप्रकृतिसंग्रहैः 19. 55;<BR>17. 60.<BR>--7 Governing, restraining,<BR>controlling.<BR>--8 Conglomeration.<BR>--9<BR>Conjunction.<BR>--10 Agglomeration<BR>(a kind of संयोग).<BR>--11 Inclusion,<BR>comprehension.<BR>--12 Compilation.<BR>--13 Epitome, summary, abridgment,<BR>compendium; संग्रहेण प्रवक्ष्यते<BR>Bg. 8. 11; so तर्कसंग्रहः.<BR>--14 Sum, amount,<BR>totality; करणं कर्म कर्तेति त्रिवधः<BR>कर्मसंग्रहः Bg. 18. 18.<BR>--15 A<BR>catalogue, list.<BR>--16 A store-room.<BR>--17<BR>An effort, exertion.<BR>--18 Mention,<BR>reference.<BR>--19 Greatness, elevation.<BR>--20 Velocity.<BR>--21 N. of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--श्लोकः a verse<BR>summarizing what has been mentioned<BR>before.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्रहणं|सङ्ग्रहण|संग्रहण
संग्रहणं<BR>1 Seizing, grasping.<BR>--2<BR>Supporting, encouraging.<BR>--3<BR>Compiling, collecting.<BR>--4 Blending.<BR>--5<BR>Incasing, setting;<BR>कनक्रभूषणसंग्रहणोत्रितः (मणिः) Pt. 1. 75.<BR>--6<BR>Sexual union, intercourse with a<BR>female.<BR>--7 Adultery; Ms. 8. 6, 72;<BR>Y. 2. 72.<BR>--8 Hoping.<BR>--9<BR>Accepting, receiving.<BR>--णी Dysentery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्रहीतृ|सङ्ग्रहीतृ
संग्रहीतृ m. A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्राहः|सङ्ग्राह|संग्राह|सङ्ग्राहः
संग्राहः<BR>1 Laying hold of, grasping.<BR>--2 Forcible seizure.<BR>--3 Clenching<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">Page1080-a+ 55</a>]<BR>the fist.<BR>--4 The fist.<BR>--5 The handle<BR>of a shield.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1079-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्राहकः|सङ्ग्राहक|संग्राहक
संग्राहकः A collector, compiler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्राहिन्|सङ्ग्राहिन्
संग्राहिन् m. The Kuṭaja tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संग्रामः|सङ्ग्राम|संग्राम|सङ्ग्रामः
संग्रामः War, battle, fight;<BR>संग्रामांगणमागतेन भवता चापे समारोपिते<BR>K. P. 10.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जित् a.<BR>conquering in battle.<BR>--पटहः a large<BR>military drum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघः|सङ्घ|संघ|सङ्घः
संघः<BR>1 A group, collection,<BR>multitude, flock; as महर्षिसंघ, मनुष्यसंघ<BR>&c.<BR>--2 A number of people living<BR>together.<BR>--3 Close contact or<BR>combination.<BR>--चारिन् m. a fish.<BR>--जीविन् m. a hired labourer, coolie.<BR>--तलः the two hands with the open<BR>palms brought together.<BR>--वृत्तिः f.<BR>close combination.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघट्|सङ्घट्
संघट् {c1c} A. To meet, assemble<BR>together. --Caus.<BR>1 To join or<BR>fasten together, bring together.<BR>--2<BR>To strike (a musical instrument),<BR>sound, play upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघटना
संघटना Joining together, union,<BR>combination; Ratn. 4. 20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघट्ट्|सङ्घट्ट्
संघट्ट् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To strike.<BR>--2 To<BR>bring together, unite.<BR>--3 To gather,<BR>collect.<BR>--4 To rub, rub against or<BR>press against; संघदृयन्नंगदमंगदेन<BR>R. 6. 73.<BR>--5 To strike against, touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघट्टः|सङ्घट्ट|संघट्ट|सङ्घट्टः
संघट्टः<BR>1 Friction, rubbing<BR>together; सरलस्कंधसंघट्टजन्मा (दवाग्नः)<BR>Me. 53; Māl. 5. 3, 9. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Collision, clashing together, encounter;<BR>Śi. 20. 26.<BR>--3 Encounter, conflict.<BR>--4 Meeting, joining, collision or<BR>rivalry (as of wives); R. 14. 86.<BR>--5 Embracing.<BR>--ट्टा A large creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघट्टनं|सङ्घट्टन|संघट्टन|सङ्घट्टनं
संघट्टनं --ना<BR>1 Rubbing together,<BR>friction.<BR>--2 Collision, clash.<BR>--3<BR>Close contact, adherence to.<BR>--4<BR>Contact, union, cohesion.<BR>--5 The<BR>intertwining of wrestlers.<BR>--6 Meeting,<BR>encounter in general.<BR>--7 The<BR>embrace of lovers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघट्टना
संघट्टनं --ना<BR>1 Rubbing together,<BR>friction.<BR>--2 Collision, clash.<BR>--3<BR>Close contact, adherence to.<BR>--4<BR>Contact, union, cohesion.<BR>--5 The<BR>intertwining of wrestlers.<BR>--6 Meeting,<BR>encounter in general.<BR>--7 The<BR>embrace of lovers.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघाटिका|सङ्घाटिका
संघाटिका<BR>1 A pair, couple.<BR>--2<BR>A bawd, procuress.<BR>--3 Smell.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघाणकः|सङ्घाणक|संघाणकं
संघाणकः --कं The mucus of the<BR>nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघाणकं|सङ्घाणक|संघाणकः
संघाणकः --कं The mucus of the<BR>nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघातः|सङ्घात|संघात|सङ्घातः
संघातः<BR>1 Union, combination,<BR>an association.<BR>--2 A multitude, an<BR>assemblage, a collection; उपायमंघात<BR>इव प्रवृद्धः R. 14. 11; जलसंघात इवासि<BR>विद्रुतः Ku. 4. 6.<BR>--3 Killing,<BR>slaughter.<BR>--4 Phlegm.<BR>--5 Formation<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-b" target="_blank">Page1080-b+ 55</a>]<BR>of compounds.<BR>--6 N. of a division<BR>of bell.<BR>--7 A particular mode of<BR>walking (in dramas.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कठिन a. hard like a solid, solid;<BR>Ku. 2. 11.<BR>--शिला a stone-like block or<BR>hard mass, solid stone; Ku. 1. 56;<BR>5. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघुष्|सङ्घुष्
संघुष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To resound.<BR>--2<BR>To proclaim loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघुष्ट|सङ्घुष्ट|सङ्घुष्टं|संघुष्टः
संघुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Resonant,<BR>resounding.<BR>--2 Sounded, proclaimed.<BR>--3<BR>Offered for sale.<BR>--ष्टः A sound,<BR>noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघृष्|सङ्घृष्
संघृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To rub or grind<BR>together.<BR>--2 To rival, emulate,<BR>compete or vie with; स प्रयोगनिपुणैः<BR>प्रयोक्तृभिः संजघर्ष सह मिवसंनिधौ<BR>R. 19. 36.<BR>--3 To rub, scratch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संघर्षः|सङ्घर्ष|संघर्ष|सङ्घर्षः
संघर्षः<BR>1 Rubbing together,<BR>friction.<BR>--2 Grinding, trituration.<BR>--3<BR>Collision, clash.<BR>--4 Emulation,<BR>rivalry, contest for superiority; तस्याश्च<BR>मम च कस्तिंश्चित्संघर्षे Dk.;<BR>नाट्याचार्ययोर्महान् ज्ञानसंघर्षो जातः M. 1.<BR>--5<BR>Envy, jealousy.<BR>--6 Gliding, gently<BR>flowing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सच्
सच् {c1c} A., {c3c} P. (सचते, सिषक्ति)<BR>Ved.<BR>1 To follow, pursue.<BR>--2 To<BR>go to.<BR>--3 To love, like.<BR>--4 To be<BR>obedient.<BR>--5 To honour, serve.<BR>--6 To assist, aid.<BR>--7 To be<BR>associated with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचनं|सचन
सचनं<BR>1 Honouring.<BR>--2 Service,<BR>attendance.<BR>--3 Assisting, helping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचकित
सचकित a. Startled, timid.<BR>--तं ind. Tremblingly, in an<BR>alarmed or startled manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचिः|सचि
सचिः<BR>1 A friend.<BR>--2 Friendship,<BR>intimacy. --f. The wife of Indra;<BR>see शची.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1080-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सचित्र
