संदित|सन्दित|सन्दितः
संदित a. Bound, chained,<BR>fettered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदिश्|सन्दिश्
संदिश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To give, grant,<BR>assign, make over; Bk. 6. 141;<BR>Y. 2. 232.<BR>--2 To order, direct, instruct,<BR>advise, send as a message; किं नु<BR>खलु दुष्यंतस्य युक्तरूपमस्माभिः संदेष्टव्यं<BR>Ś. 4; Śi. 9. 56, 61.<BR>--3 To send as a<BR>messenger, entrust with a message;<BR>अथ विश्वात्मने गौरी संदिदेश मिथः सखीं<BR>Ku. 6. 1.<BR>--4 To appoint.<BR>--5 To<BR>commission or depute in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदिष्ट|सन्दिष्ट|सन्दिष्टं|संदिष्टः
संदिष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Pointed out,<BR>indicated.<BR>--2 Assigned.<BR>--3 Told,<BR>narrated, communicated.<BR>--4 Agreed to,<BR>promised.<BR>--ष्टः One entrusted with<BR>a message, a messenger, herald,<BR>courier (संदिष्टार्थ also).<BR>--ष्टं<BR>Information, news, tidings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशः|सन्देश|संदेश|सन्देशः
संदेशः<BR>1 Information, news,<BR>tidings.<BR>--2 A message, an errand;<BR>संदेशं मे हर धनपतिक्रोधविश्लेषितस्य<BR>Me. 7, 13; R. 12. 63;<BR>Ku. 6. 2.<BR>--3 Commission, command;<BR>अनुष्ठितो गुरोः संदेशः Ś. 5.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थः<BR>the subject of a message; Me. 5.<BR>--वाच् f. a message.<BR>--हरः, --हारकः<BR>{1} a news-bearer, messenger. {2} an<BR>envoy, ambassador.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेशकं|सन्देशक
संदेशकं News, tidings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदिह्|सन्दिह्
संदिह् {c2c} U.<BR>1 To smear, cover<BR>over, anoint.<BR>--2 To heap together.<BR>--3<BR>To doubt, be uncertain about;<BR>Y. 2. 16; संदिग्धो विजयो युधि Pt. 3. 12.<BR>--4 To mistake for, to confound with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-a" target="_blank">Page1088-a+ 56</a>]<BR>(in pass.); पांतु<BR>त्वामकठोरकेतकशिखासंदिग्धमुग्धेंदवः (जटाः)<BR>Māl. 1. 2; or धूपैर्जालविनिःसृतैर्वलभयः<BR>संदिग्धपारावताः V. 3. 2; Ku. 6. 40.<BR>--5 To<BR>start an objection. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>confuse, perplex.<BR>--2 To be doubtful<BR>or uncertain (Atm.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1087-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदिग्ध|सन्दिग्ध|सन्दिग्धः
संदिग्ध p. p.<BR>1 Besmeared, covered.<BR>--2 Dubious, doubtful, uncertain;<BR>as in संदिग्धमति --बुद्धि &c.<BR>--3<BR>Mistaken for or confounded with.<BR>--4 Doubted, questioned.<BR>--5<BR>Confused, obscure, unintelligible<BR>(as a sentence).<BR>--6 Dangerous,<BR>risky, unsafe.<BR>--7 Envenomed.<BR>--ग्धं<BR>1<BR>A doubt, uncertainty.<BR>--2 Besmearing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. ambiguous,<BR>dubious in sense.<BR>--(र्थः) {1} an ambiguous<BR>or doubtful meaning. {2} a disputed<BR>matter.<BR>--मति, --बुद्धि a. sceptical,<BR>doubtful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेहः|सन्देह|संदेह|सन्देहः
संदेहः<BR>1 Doubt, uncertainty,<BR>suspense; अत्र कः संदेहः.<BR>--2 Risk,<BR>danger, peril; जीवितसंदेहदोलामारोपितः<BR>K.; अर्थार्जने प्रवृत्तिः ससंदेहा H. 1;<BR>Pt. 1. 176.<BR>--3 (In Rhet.) Doubt<BR>regarded as a figure of speech, in<BR>which the close resemblance<BR>between two objects leads to one<BR>of them being mistaken for the<BR>other (this figure is also called<BR>ससंदेह by Mammaṭa and others);<BR>ससंदेहस्तु भेदोक्तौ तदनुक्तौ च संशयः<BR>K. P. 10; e. g. see Māl. 1. 2 (l. 3);<BR>V. 3. 2.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दोला the swing of<BR>uncertainty, a state of suspense,<BR>dilemma, fix.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदेहिन्|सन्देहिन्
संदेहिन् a.<BR>1 Doubtful.<BR>--2<BR>Doubting, uncertain, diffident.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदी|सन्दी
संदी A small bedstead, cot,<BR>couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदीप्|सन्दीप्
संदीप् {c4c} A. To burn or shine<BR>very brightly, glow. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>light, kindle, inflame.<BR>--2 To excite,<BR>incite, arouse, stimulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदीपन
संदीपन a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Kindling,<BR>inflaming, exciting; संदीपना एव<BR>दुःखस्य प्रियसखीविनोदनोपायाः U. 3.<BR>--2<BR>Provoking; U. 4.<BR>--नः One of<BR>the five arrows of Cupid.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Kindling, inflaming.<BR>--2 Exciting,<BR>stimulating; अनंगसंदीपनमाशु कुर्वते<BR>Rs. 1. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदीप्त|सन्दीप्त
संदीप्त p. p.<BR>1 Kindled or inflamed.<BR>--2 Excited, stimulated.<BR>--3<BR>Instigated, stirred up, prompted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदुष्|सन्दुष्
संदुष् {c4c} P. To be defiled or<BR>stained. --Caus.<BR>1 To defile, pollute,<BR>corrupt, soil, taint.<BR>--2 To violate.<BR>--3<BR>To accuse, censure, find fault with,<BR>condemn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदुष्ट|सन्दुष्ट
संदुष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Polluted, defiled.<BR>--2<BR>Wicked, depraved.<BR>--3 Ill-disposed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदूषणं|सन्दूषण
संदूषणं Defiling, corrupting,<BR>vitiating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदूषित|सन्दूषित
संदूषित a.<BR>1 Violated, defiled,<BR>stained, polluted.<BR>--2 Grown worse<BR>(as a disease).<BR>--3 Abused,<BR>censured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदृभ्|सन्दृभ्
संदृभ् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To string or bind<BR>together.<BR>--2 To weave together,<BR>weave into a bunch or garland.<BR>--3<BR>To arrange, connect, compose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदर्भः|सन्दर्भ|संदर्भ|सन्दर्भः
संदर्भः<BR>1 Stringing together,<BR>weaving, arranging.<BR>--2 Collection,<BR>uniting, mixture; U. 7. 12.<BR>--3<BR>Consistency, continuity, regular<BR>connection, coherence; संदर्भशुद्धिं गिरां<BR>Gīt. 1.<BR>--4 Construction.<BR>--5 A<BR>composition, literary work; रसगंगाधरनामा<BR>संदर्भोऽयं चिरं जयतु R. G.; U. 4.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विरुद्ध a. irrelevant,<BR>incoherent.<BR>--शुद्ध a. connected,<BR>coherent.<BR>--शुद्धिः f. clearness of<BR>arrangement (as of a composition).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदृश्|सन्दृश्
संदृश् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To see, behold;<BR>Bk. 16. 9.<BR>--2 To see well or<BR>perfectly.<BR>--3 To consider, reflect upon.<BR>--4 To calculate, enumerate.<BR>--5 To<BR>overlook, wink at. --Pass.<BR>1 To<BR>look like, resemble, be similar.<BR>--2<BR>To become visible, appear. --Caus.<BR>To show, exhibit, discover; आत्मानं<BR>मृतवत्संदर्श्य स्थितः H. 1; Bk. 4. 33;<BR>M. 4. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदर्शनं|सन्दर्शन|संदर्शन|सन्दर्शनं
संदर्शनं<BR>1 Seeing, beholding,<BR>viewing.<BR>--2 Gazing, looking steadfastly.<BR>--3 Meeting, seeing one another.<BR>--4<BR>Sight, appearance, vision.<BR>--5 Regard,<BR>consideration.<BR>--6 Showing,<BR>displaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संदोहः|सन्दोह|संदोह|सन्दोहः
संदोहः<BR>1 Milking.<BR>--2 The whole<BR>quantity of anything, a multitude,<BR>heap, mass, assemblage;<BR>कुंदमाकंदमधुबिंदुसंदोहवाहिना मारुतेनोत्ताम्यति<BR>Māl. 3; Bv. 4. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संद्रावः|सन्द्राव|संद्राव|सन्द्रावः
संद्रावः Flight, retreat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधा
संधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To join, bring<BR>together, unite, combine, put together,<BR>compound, mix; यानि उदकेन<BR>संधीयंते तानि भक्षणीयानि Kull.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-c" target="_blank">Page1088-c+ 57</a>]<BR>(a) To treat with, form friendship<BR>or alliance with, make peace with;<BR>शत्रुणा न हि संदध्यात्सुश्लिष्टेनापि संधिना<BR>H. 1. 88; Chāṇ. 19; Kām. 9. 41.<BR>(b) To unite in friendship,<BR>reconcile, make a friend of; Pt. 2. 32.<BR>--3 To fix upon, direct towards;<BR>संदधे दृशमुदग्रतारकां R. 11. 69.<BR>--4<BR>To fit to or place upon the bow (as<BR>a missile, arrow &c.); धनुष्यमोघं<BR>समधत्त बाणं Ku. 3. 66; R. 3. 53,<BR>12. 97.<BR>--5 To produce, cause; पर्याप्तं<BR>मयि रमणीयडामरत्वं संधत्ते<BR>गगनतलप्रयाणवेगः Māl. 5. 3; सधंत्ते भृशमरतिं हि<BR>सद्वियोगः Ki. 5. 51.<BR>--6 To hold out<BR>against, be a match for; शतमेकोऽपि<BR>संधत्ते प्राकारस्थो धनुर्धरः Pt. 1. 229.<BR>--7 To mend, repair, heal.<BR>--8 To<BR>inflict upon.<BR>--9 To grasp, support,<BR>take hold of.<BR>--10 To grant, yield.<BR>--11 To make good, atone for.<BR>--12<BR>To contract, close up.<BR>--13 To<BR>approach, come near.<BR>--14 To<BR>prepare, make, compose.<BR>--15 To assist,<BR>aid.<BR>--16 To comprehend, conceive.<BR>--17 To possess, have.<BR>--18 To<BR>perform, do; Pt. 2. 11.<BR>--19 To<BR>employ, make use of, apply to use.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधा
संधा<BR>1 Union, association.<BR>--2<BR>Intimate union, close connection.<BR>--3 State, condition.<BR>--4 An<BR>agreement, a promise, stipulation,<BR>compact; ततार संधामिव सत्यसंधः<BR>R. 14. 52; Mv. 7. 8.<BR>--5 Limit, boundary.<BR>--6 Fixity, steadiness.<BR>--7 Twilight.<BR>--8 Distillation (for संधान q. v.).<BR>--9<BR>Steady continuance in any state.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधानं|सन्धान|संधान|सन्धानं
संधानं<BR>1 Joining, uniting.<BR>--2<BR>Union, junction, combination; यदर्धे<BR>विच्छिन्नं भवति कृतसंधानमिव तत्<BR>Ś. 1. 9; Ku. 5. 27; R. 12. 101.<BR>--3<BR>Mixing, compounding (of medicines<BR>&c.).<BR>--4 Restoration, repairing.<BR>--5<BR>Fitting, taking an aim, fixing (as<BR>an arrow to the bow-string);<BR>तत्साधुकृतसंधानं प्रतिसंहर सायकं Ś. 1. 11;<BR>Śi. 20. 8.<BR>--6 Alliance, league, friendship,<BR>peace; मृद्घटवत्सुखभेद्यो दुःसंधानश्च<BR>दुर्जनो भवति H. 1. 92 (where it has<BR>sense 1 also).<BR>--7 A joint;<BR>पादजंघयोः संधाने गुल्फः Suśr.<BR>--8 Attention.<BR>--9 Direction.<BR>--10 Supporting.<BR>--11 Distillation (of liquors).<BR>--12<BR>Spirituous liquor or a kind of it.<BR>--13 A kind of relish eaten to excite<BR>thirst.<BR>--14 Preparation of pickles.<BR>--15 Contraction of the skin by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-a" target="_blank">Page1089-a+ 56</a>]<BR>means of astringents.<BR>--16 Sour<BR>rice-gruel.<BR>--17 Bell-metal (सौराष्ट्र).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1088-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधानित|सन्धानित|सन्धानितः
संधानित a.<BR>1 United, strung<BR>together.<BR>--2 Bound, tied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधानिन्|सन्धानिन्
संधानिन् a.<BR>1 Tying or binding<BR>together.<BR>--2 Clever in taking aim.<BR>--3 Distilling liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधानिनी|सन्धानिनी
संधानिनी A cow-house, cow-pen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधानी|सन्धानी
संधानी<BR>1 Distillation.<BR>--2<BR>Braziery, foundery.<BR>--3 The<BR>manufacture of spirituous liquors.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधिः|सन्धि|संधि|सन्धिः
संधिः<BR>1 Union, junction,<BR>conbination, connection; संधये सरला<BR>सूची वक्रा छेदाय कर्तरी Subhāṣ.;<BR>Me. 58.<BR>--2 A compact, an agreement.<BR>--3<BR>Alliance, league, friendship, peace,<BR>treaty of peace (one of the six<BR>expedients to be used in foreign<BR>politics); कति प्रकाराः संधीनां भवंति<BR>H. 4; (the several kinds are described<BR>in H. 4. 106-125); शत्रुणा न हि<BR>संदध्यात्सुश्लिष्टेनापि संधिना H. 1. 88.<BR>--4<BR>A joint, articulation (of the body);<BR>तुरगानुधावनकंडितसंधेः Ś. 2.<BR>--5 A<BR>fold (of a garment).<BR>--6 A breach,<BR>hole, chasm.<BR>--7 Especially a mine,<BR>chasm or opening made by thieves<BR>in a wall or underneath a building;<BR>वृक्षवाटिकापरिसरे संधिं कृत्वा<BR>प्रविष्टोऽस्मि मध्यमकं Mk. 3; Ms. 9. 276.<BR>--8<BR>Separation, division.<BR>--9 Euphony,<BR>euphonic junction or coalition (in<BR>gram.).<BR>--10 An interval, a pause.<BR>--11 A critical juncture.<BR>--12 An<BR>opportune moment.<BR>--13 A period<BR>at the expiration of each Yuga<BR>or age.<BR>--14 A division or joint (in<BR>a drama); (they are five, see<BR>S. D. 330-332); Ku. 7. 91.<BR>--15<BR>The vulva.<BR>--16 Distillation.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षरं a diphthong.<BR>--चोरः a<BR>housebreaker, a thief who breaks into a<BR>house.<BR>--छेदः making holes or<BR>breaches (in a wall &c.); as in<BR>संधिच्छेदशिक्षकः M. 4.<BR>--जं spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR>--जीवकः one who lives by<BR>dishonest means (particularly as a<BR>go-between).<BR>--दूषणं violation of a<BR>treaty; अरिषु हि विजयार्थिनः<BR>क्षितीशा विदधति सोपधि संधिदूषणानि<BR>Ki. 1. 45.<BR>--प्रबंधनं the ligament of a<BR>joint.<BR>--बंधः the tissues of joints;<BR>Ś. 2.<BR>--बंधनं a ligament, tendon,<BR>nerve.<BR>--भंगः, --मुक्तिः f. dislocation<BR>of a joint.<BR>--रंध्रका a hole in a wall.<BR>--विग्रह m. du. peace and war.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">Page1089-b+ 56</a>]<BR>˚अधिकारः the office of the minister for<BR>foreign affairs.<BR>--विचक्षणः one<BR>skilled in negotiating peaces.<BR>--विद् m. a<BR>negotiator of treaties.<BR>--वेला {1} the<BR>time of twilight. {2} any<BR>connecting period.<BR>--हारकः a house-breaker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधिकः|सन्धिक|संधिक
संधिकः A kind of fever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधिका|सन्धिका
संधिका Distillation(of liquors).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधित|सन्धित|सन्धितः
संधित a.<BR>1 United, joined;<BR>Pt. 2. 35.<BR>--2 Bound, tied.<BR>--3 Reconciled,<BR>allied.<BR>--4 Fixed, fitted.<BR>--5 Mixed<BR>together.<BR>--6 Pickled, preserved.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Pickles.<BR>--2 Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधिनी|सन्धिनी
संधिनी<BR>1 A cow in heat (united<BR>with the bull or impregnated by<BR>him).<BR>--2 A cow milked<BR>unseasonably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधिला|सन्धिला
संधिला<BR>1 A hole or breach made<BR>in a wall, pit, chasm.<BR>--2 A river.<BR>--3 Spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधेय|सन्धेय
संधेय a.<BR>1 To be united or joined.<BR>--2 Capable of being reconciled;<BR>सुजनस्तु कनकघटवद् दुर्भेद्यश्चाशुसंधेयः<BR>H. 1. 92.<BR>--3 To be made peace<BR>with.<BR>--4 To be aimed at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधुक्ष्|सन्धुक्ष्
संधुक्ष् {c1c} A. To be kindled or<BR>excited (fig also); संदुधुक्षे तयोः<BR>कोपः Bk. 14. 109. --Caus. To<BR>kindle, inflame, excite;<BR>निर्वाणभूयिष्ठमथास्य वीर्यं संधुक्षयंतीव वपुर्गुणेन<BR>Ku. 3. 52; आतपांतसंधुक्षितमदा V. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधुक्षणं|सन्धुक्षण
संधुक्षणं<BR>1 Kindling, inflaming.<BR>--2<BR>Exciting, stimulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधुक्षित|सन्धुक्षित
संधुक्षित p. p. Kindled, inflamed,<BR>excited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधृ|सन्धृ
संधृ {c10c} U.<BR>1 To hold, bear, carry.<BR>--2 To hold up, support, prop,<BR>sustain; अरैः संधार्यते नाभिः Pt. 1. 81.<BR>--3 To curb, restrain, check.<BR>--4 To<BR>keep in mind, retain in memory;<BR>यः सततं परिपृच्छति शृणोति<BR>संधारयत्यनिशं Pt. 5. 92.<BR>--5 To hold, have,<BR>possess; retain, keep; Pt. 1. 112.<BR>--6 To observe, follow.<BR>--7 To bear,<BR>suffer, endure.<BR>--8 To survive,<BR>remain alive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधारणं|सन्धारण|संधारण
संधारणं --णा<BR>1 Restraining,<BR>checking.<BR>--2 Observing, following.<BR>--3<BR>Suffering, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संधारणा
संधारणं --णा<BR>1 Restraining,<BR>checking.<BR>--2 Observing, following.<BR>--3<BR>Suffering, enduring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संध्या|सन्ध्या
संध्या<BR>1 Union.<BR>--2 Joint, division.<BR>--3 Morning or evening twilight;<BR>अनुरागवती संध्या दिवसस्तत्पुरस्सरः ।<BR>अहो दैवगतिश्चित्रा तथापि न समागमः<BR>K. P. 7.<BR>--4 Early morning.<BR>--5<BR>Evening, dusk.<BR>--6 The period which<BR>precedes a Yuga, the time<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-c" target="_blank">Page1089-c+ 57</a>]<BR>intervening between the expiration of one<BR>Yuga and the commencement of<BR>another; Ms. 1. 69.<BR>--7 The<BR>morning, noon, and evening prayers of a<BR>Brāhmaṇa; Ms. 2. 69, 4. 93.<BR>--8<BR>A promise, an agreement.<BR>--9 A<BR>boundary, limit.<BR>--10 Thinking,<BR>meditation.<BR>--11 A kind of flower.<BR>--12<BR>N. of a river.<BR>--13 N. of the wife of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--14 Any one of the<BR>divisions of the day (पूर्वाह्ण, भध्याह्ण,<BR>अपराह्ण.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः the<BR>period at the end of each Yuga.<BR>--अंशुः twilight.<BR>--अभ्रं {1} an<BR>evening cloud (tinged with the sun's<BR>rays); संध्याभ्ररेखेव मुहूर्तरागाः<BR>Pt. 1. 194. {2} a kind of red-chalk.<BR>--उपासना Saṃdhyā adoration.<BR>--कालः {1} the period of twilight. {2}<BR>evening.<BR>--त्रयं the three divisions<BR>of the day (forenoon, noon, and<BR>afternoon.).<BR>--नाटिन् m. an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--पुष्पी {1} a kind of jasmine.<BR>{2} a nutmeg.<BR>--बलः a demon (<BR>राक्षस).<BR>--मंगलं an evening religious<BR>rite. ˚दीपिका an auspicious<BR>evening lamp; V. 3. 2.<BR>--रागः<BR>redlead.<BR>--रामः (some take आराम as<BR>the word here) an epithet of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--वंदनं the morning and<BR>evening prayers.<BR>--समयः {1}<BR>eveningtime. {2} a portion of each Yuga.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्न|सन्नः
सन्न p. p. [सद्-क्त]<BR>1 Sitting<BR>down, settling down, lying.<BR>--2<BR>Dejected, sunk down, downcast.<BR>--3<BR>Drooping, relaxed; Ku. 3. 51.<BR>--4<BR>Weak, low, feeble.<BR>--5 Wasted<BR>away, decayed.<BR>--6 Perished,<BR>destroyed.<BR>--7 Still, motionless.<BR>--8 Shrunk.<BR>--9 Adjacent, near.<BR>--10 Gone,<BR>departed.<BR>--11 Sunk, low (in tone &c).<BR>--न्नः The tree called पियाल.<BR>--न्नं A<BR>little, a small quantity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठ a. choked.<BR>--हर्ष a. desponding,<BR>cheerless.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नक|सन्नकः
सन्नक a. Low, dwarfish.<BR>--कः The<BR>Piyāla tree.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द्रुः the<BR>Piyāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सन्नतर
सन्नतर a. Lower, more depressed<BR>(as a tone).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनम्|सन्नम्
संनम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bend, stoop,<BR>incline; संनतांगी Ku. 1. 34;<BR>Bk. 2. 31; पर्वसु संनता V. 4. 26.<BR>--2 To<BR>submit or subject oneself to, obey;<BR>संनमतामरीणां R. 18. 34.<BR>--3 To bend<BR>down, bow down to.<BR>--4 To make<BR>ready, prepare.<BR>--5 To be<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">Page1090-a+ 56</a>]<BR>accomplished. --Caus.<BR>1 To contract,<BR>bend together.<BR>--2 To cause to<BR>bend or stoop.<BR>--3 To make ready,<BR>prepare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1089-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनत|सन्नत
संनत p. p.<BR>1 Bent down,<BR>stooping.<BR>--2 Downcast.<BR>--3 Contracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनतिः|सन्नति|संनति|सन्नतिः
संनतिः f.<BR>1 Obeisance, respectful<BR>salutation, reverence.<BR>--2 Stooping<BR>posture, crouching.<BR>--3 Humility.<BR>--4 A kind of sacrifice.<BR>--5 A sound,<BR>noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनयः|सन्नय|संनय|सन्नयः
संनयः<BR>1 A collection, multitude,<BR>quantity, number.<BR>--2 Rear,<BR>rearguard (of an army).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनह्|सन्नह्
संनह् {c4c} U.<BR>1 To tie, bind,<BR>fasten.<BR>--2 To wear, put on, dress.<BR>--3 To put on (as armour), arm<BR>oneself, be accoutred;<BR>समनात्सीत्ततो सैन्यं Bk. 15. 111, 112; 14. 7;<BR>16. 4.<BR>--4 To make oneself ready,<BR>prepare oneself (for any action)<BR>(Atm. in this sense); युद्धाय<BR>संनह्यते Mbh.; छेत्तुं वज्रमणीञ्<BR>शिरीषकुसुमप्रांतेन संनह्यते Bk. 2. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनद्ध|सन्नद्ध|सन्नद्धः
संनद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Tied or bound<BR>together, girded or put on.<BR>--2 Clad<BR>or dressed in armour, accoutred,<BR>mailed.<BR>--3 Arranged, ready, or<BR>prepared, for battle, armed, fully<BR>equipped; नवजलधरः संनद्धोऽयं न<BR>दृप्तनिशाचरः V. 4. 1; कः संनद्धे विरहविधुरां<BR>त्वय्युपेक्षेत जायां Me. 8.<BR>--4 Ready,<BR>prepared, formed, arranged in<BR>general; लतेव संनद्धमनोज्ञपल्लवा R. 3. 7.<BR>--5 Pervading; कुसुममिव लोभनीयं<BR>यौवनमंगेषु संनद्धं Ś. 1. 21.<BR>--6<BR>Wellprovided with anything.<BR>--7<BR>Murderous.<BR>--8 Closely attached,<BR>bordering, near.<BR>--9 Ready to burst or<BR>blossom.<BR>--10 Provided with charms.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनहनं|सन्नहन
संनहनं<BR>1 Preparing, equipping,<BR>arming oneself.<BR>--2 Preparation.<BR>--3<BR>Fastening tightly.<BR>--4 Industry,<BR>effort.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनाहः|सन्नाह|संनाह|सन्नाहः
संनाहः<BR>1 Arming(oneself) or<BR>preparation for battle, putting on<BR>armour.<BR>--2 Warlike preparation,<BR>equipment; संनाहोयं साहसमवगमयति<BR>Dk.<BR>--3 Armour, mail; अस्मिन्कलौ<BR>खलोत्सृष्टदुष्टवाग्बाणदारुणे । कथं<BR>जीवेज्जगन्न स्युः संनाहाः सज्जना यदि<BR>Kīr. K. 1. 36, Ki. 16. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनाह्यः|सन्नाह्य|संनाह्य|सन्नाह्यः
संनाह्यः A war-elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिकर्षः|सन्निकर्ष|संनिकर्ष|सन्निकर्षः
संनिकर्षः<BR>1 Drawing near,<BR>bringing near.<BR>--2 Vicinity, proximity;<BR>presence; उत्कंठते च युष्मत्संनिकर्षस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">Page1090-b+ 56</a>]<BR>U. 6; Ku. 3. 74; R. 7. 8, 6. 20.<BR>--3 Connection, relation.<BR>--4 (In<BR>Nyāya phil.) Connection of an<BR>organ of sense (इंद्रिय) with its<BR>object (विषय); this is of six kinds.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिकर्षणं|सन्निकर्षण|संनिकर्षण|सन्निकर्षणं
संनिकर्षणं<BR>1 Bringing near.<BR>--2<BR>Approaching, approximating.<BR>--3<BR>Proximity, vicinity.<BR>--4 Relation,<BR>connection.<BR>--5 Connection of an<BR>organ of sense with its object; see<BR>संनिकर्ष (4) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिकृष्ट|सन्निकृष्ट|सन्निकृष्टः
संनिकृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Approximate.<BR>--2<BR>Proximate, adjacent, near.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>Proximity, vicinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिचयः|सन्निचय|संनिचय
संनिचयः A collection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिधा|सन्निधा
संनिधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To place, put, or<BR>keep together; Ms. 2. 186.<BR>--2 To<BR>place near; Ś. 3. 19.<BR>--3 To fix<BR>upon, direct towards; (दृष्टिं) पुनः<BR>सहस्रार्चिषि संनिधत्ते R. 13. 44.<BR>--4 To<BR>draw near, approach.<BR>--5 To collect,<BR>pile up.<BR>--6 To observe, inspect.<BR>--Pass. To be near, be present.<BR>--Caus. To collect, bring together,<BR>assemble; U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिधातृ|सन्निधातृ
संनिधातृ m.<BR>1 One who brings<BR>near.<BR>--2 One who deposits.<BR>--3 A<BR>receiver of stolen goods;<BR>Ms. 9. 278.<BR>--4 An officer who introduces<BR>people at court.<BR>--5 One who<BR>receives in charge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिधानं|सन्निधान|संनिधान|सन्निधानं
संनिधानं, संनिधिः<BR>1 Putting down<BR>together, juxta-position.<BR>--2<BR>Proximity, vicinity, presence; N. 2. 53.<BR>--3 Perceptibility, appearance.<BR>--4<BR>A receptacle.<BR>--5 Receiving,<BR>taking charge of.<BR>--6 Combination,<BR>aggregate; Pt. 1. 191.<BR>--7 Depositing.<BR>--8 The object of an organ of sense<BR>(इंद्रियविषय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिधिः|सन्निधि|संनिधि|सन्निधिः
संनिधानं, संनिधिः<BR>1 Putting down<BR>together, juxta-position.<BR>--2<BR>Proximity, vicinity, presence; N. 2. 53.<BR>--3 Perceptibility, appearance.<BR>--4<BR>A receptacle.<BR>--5 Receiving,<BR>taking charge of.<BR>--6 Combination,<BR>aggregate; Pt. 1. 191.<BR>--7 Depositing.<BR>--8 The object of an organ of sense<BR>(इंद्रियविषय).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिपत्|सन्निपत्
संनिपत् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To alight, descend.<BR>--2 To come together, assemble,<BR>meet together.<BR>--3 To fall upon,<BR>attack; U. 3. 6.<BR>--4 To arrive,<BR>appear.<BR>--5 To perish, be destroyed.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To throw or shoot down,<BR>discharge.<BR>--2 To convoke, convene,<BR>assemble, collect together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिपातः|सन्निपात|संनिपात|सन्निपातः
संनिपातः<BR>1 Falling down,<BR>alighting, descent.<BR>--2 Falling together,<BR>meeting; confluence;<BR>समुद्रपत्न्योर्जलसंनिपाते R. 13. 58.<BR>--3 Collision,<BR>contact.<BR>--4 Union, conjunction,<BR>combination, mixture, miscellaneous<BR>collection; धूमज्योतिःसलिलमरुतां<BR>संनिपातः क्व मेघः Me. 5.<BR>--5 An<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">Page1090-c+ 56</a>]<BR>assemblage, a collection, multitude,<BR>number; नानारत्नज्योतिषां संनिपातैः<BR>Ki. 5. 36; एको हि दोषो गुणसंनिपाते<BR>निमज्जति Ku. 1. 3.<BR>--6 Arrival.<BR>--7 A<BR>combined derangement of the three<BR>humours of the body causing fever<BR>which is of a dangerous kind.<BR>--8<BR>A kind of musical time or measure.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्वरः fever arising from<BR>a vitiated state of the three<BR>humours of the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिपातकः|सन्निपातक|संनिपातक
संनिपातकः = संनिपात (7) above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिबंधः|सन्निबन्ध|संनिबन्ध|सन्निबंध|संनिबन्धः
संनिबंधः<BR>1 Binding firmly.<BR>--2<BR>Connection, attachment.<BR>--3<BR>Effectiveness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिभ|सन्निभ|सन्निभः
संनिभ a. Like, similar (at the<BR>end of comp.); Rs. 1. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनियुज्|सन्नियुज्
संनियुज् See नियुज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनियोगः|सन्नियोग|संनियोग
संनियोगः<BR>1 Union, attachment.<BR>--2<BR>Appointment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिरुध्|सन्निरुध्
संनिरुध् See निरुध्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिरोधः|सन्निरोध|संनिरोध
संनिरोधः Obstruction, hindrance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिविश्|सन्निविश्
संनिविश् {c6c} A.<BR>1 To enter into,<BR>enter deeply.<BR>--2 To encamp, sit<BR>down.<BR>--3 To have intercourse or<BR>intimate connection with. --Caus.<BR>1 To place, put.<BR>--2 To install or<BR>place on; धातोः स्थान इवादेशं सुग्रीवं<BR>संन्यवेशयत् R. 12. 58.<BR>--3 To unite,<BR>join, collect.<BR>--4 To introduce,<BR>insert, put in.<BR>--5 To lodge, locate,<BR>station, encamp.<BR>--6 To devolve<BR>upon, commit to, consign.<BR>--7 To<BR>found (a town &c.).<BR>--8 To fix the<BR>mind on.<BR>--9 To contemplate, reflect<BR>upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिविष्ट|सन्निविष्ट|सन्निविष्टः
संनिविष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Entered into.<BR>--2<BR>Collected, met together, assembled.<BR>--3 Absorbed or engrossed in.<BR>--4<BR>Abiding or resting in.<BR>--5<BR>Contiguous, near, neighbouring.<BR>--6<BR>Eneamped; see संनिविश् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिवेशः|सन्निवेश|संनिवेश|सन्निवेशः
संनिवेशः<BR>1 Deep entrance into,<BR>ardent devotion or<BR>attachment, close application.<BR>--2 A<BR>collection, multitude, assemblage.<BR>--3<BR>Union, combination, arrangement;<BR>रमणीय एष वः सुमनसां संनिवेशः<BR>Māl. 1. 9.<BR>--4 Site, place, situation,<BR>position; Ku. 7. 25; R. 6. 19.<BR>--5<BR>Vicinity, proximity.<BR>--6 Form,<BR>figure; उद्दामशरीरसंनिवेशः Māl. 3;<BR>निर्माणसंनिवेशः K.<BR>--7 A hut,<BR>dwelling-place; R. 14. 76.<BR>--8 Seating<BR>in the proper places, giving seats<BR>to; क्रियतां समाजसंनिवेशः U. 7.<BR>--9<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-a" target="_blank">Page1091-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Insertion.<BR>--10 An open space near<BR>a town where people assemble for<BR>amusement, exercise &c.<BR>--11 The<BR>collective position of an asterism.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1090-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिवृत्|सन्निवृत्
संनिवृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To return, retire.<BR>--2 To leave off, cease, stop.<BR>--3 To<BR>pass away. --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to<BR>return, send back.<BR>--2 To suppress,<BR>stop.<BR>--3 To prevent, hinder.<BR>--4 To<BR>divert, turn away from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिवृत्त|सन्निवृत्त
संनिवृत्त p. p.<BR>1 Returned.<BR>--2<BR>Stopped, ceased.<BR>--3 Withdrawing,<BR>shrinking from.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिवृत्तिः|सन्निवृत्ति|संनिवृत्ति|सन्निवृत्तिः
संनिवृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Return; Ś. 6. 9;<BR>R. 8. 49; 10. 27.<BR>--2 Desisting<BR>from.<BR>--3 Restraint, check,<BR>forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनिहित|सन्निहित|सन्निहितं
संनिहित p. p.<BR>1 Placed near, lying<BR>close, near, contiguous,<BR>neighbouring; Ś. 4.<BR>--2 Close, proximate, at<BR>hand.<BR>--3 Present; अपि संनिहितोऽत्र<BR>कुलपतिः Ś. 1; हृदयसंनिहिते Ś. 3. 19.<BR>--4 Fixed, placed, deposited.<BR>--5<BR>Prepared, ready; Mu. 1.<BR>--6<BR>Staying or being in.<BR>--तं Proximity,<BR>vicinity.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपाय a.<BR>having destruction close at hand, frail,<BR>perishable, transitory; कायः<BR>संनिहितापायः Pt. 2. 177.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनी|सन्नी
संनी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring together.<BR>--2 To rule, govern, guide.<BR>--3 To<BR>restore, give back.<BR>--4 To lead<BR>towards, lead, or bring near to.<BR>--5 To<BR>connect, unite.<BR>--6 To mingle, mix.<BR>--7 To arrange.<BR>--8 To obtain,<BR>procure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संनयनं|सन्नयन
संनयनं<BR>1 Bringing together or<BR>near.<BR>--2 Connecting, uniting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संन्यस्|सन्न्यस्
संन्यस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To place or put<BR>down, deposit.<BR>--2 To lay down or<BR>aside, give up, abandon, quit;<BR>तेन त्वया शस्त्रं न संन्यस्तव्यं V. 5;<BR>संन्यस्तशस्त्र R. 2. 59; संन्यस्ताभरणं<BR>गात्रं Me. 93; Ku. 7. 67.<BR>--3 To<BR>make or deliver over, entrust,<BR>commit to the care of; Bg. 3. 30.<BR>--4<BR>To put together.<BR>--5 (Used<BR>intransitively) To resign the world,<BR>discard all worldly ties and<BR>attachments and become an anchorite,<BR>संदृश्य क्षणभंगुरं तदखिलं धन्यस्तु<BR>संन्यस्यति Bh. 3. 132.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संन्यसनं|सन्न्यसन|संन्यसन
संन्यसनं<BR>1 Resignation, laying<BR>down.<BR>--2 Complete renunciation<BR>of the world and its attachments;<BR>न च संन्यसनादेव सिद्धिं समधिगच्छति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">Page1091-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Bg. 3. 4.<BR>--3 Consigning,<BR>entrusting to the care of.<BR>--4 Depositing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संन्यस्त|सन्न्यस्त|सन्न्यस्तः
संन्यस्त p. p.<BR>1 Laid or placed<BR>down.<BR>--2 Deposited.<BR>--3 Entrusted,<BR>consigned.<BR>--4 Laid aside,<BR>relinquished, renounced.<BR>--5 Encamped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संन्यासः|सन्न्यास|संन्यास|सन्न्यासः
संन्यासः<BR>1 Leaving, abandonment.<BR>--2 Complete renunciation of the<BR>world and its possessions and<BR>attachments, abandonment of<BR>temporal concerns; काम्यानां कर्मणां त्यागं<BR>संन्यासं कवयो विदुः; Bg. 6. 2, 18. 2;<BR>Ms. 1. 114; 5. 108.<BR>--3 A deposit,<BR>trust.<BR>--4 A stake or wager in a<BR>game.<BR>--5 Giving up the body, death.<BR>--6 Indian spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संन्यासिन्|सन्न्यासिन्
संन्यासिन् m.<BR>1 One who lays<BR>down or deposits.<BR>--2 One who<BR>completely renounces the world and<BR>its attachments, an ascetic, a<BR>Brāhmaṇa in the fourth order of his<BR>religious life; ज्ञेयः स नित्यसंन्यासी<BR>यो न द्वेष्टि न कांक्षति Bg. 5. 3.<BR>--3 One<BR>who abstains from food (त्यक्ताहार);<BR>Bk. 7. 76.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्
सप् {c1c} P. (सपति)<BR>1 To honour,<BR>worship.<BR>--2 To connect.<BR>--3 To obey,<BR>conform to.<BR>--4 To obtain.<BR>--5 To<BR>touch, sip.<BR>--6 To do, perform.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपक्ष|सपक्षः
सपक्ष a.<BR>1 Winged, having<BR>wings.<BR>--2 Having a side or party.<BR>--3 Belonging to the same side<BR>or party.<BR>--4 (Hence) Kindred,<BR>like, similar (fig.);<BR>दलद्द्राक्षातिर्यद्रसर्भरसपक्षा भणितयः Bv. 2. 77.<BR>--5<BR>Containing the पक्ष or subject of an<BR>inference.<BR>--क्षः<BR>1 An adherent, a<BR>follower, partisan.<BR>--2 A kindred,<BR>a kinsman; परित्रातस्त्वया सपक्षः<BR>M. 4.<BR>--3 (In logic) An instance on<BR>the same side, a similar instance;<BR>निश्चितसाध्यवान् सपक्षः T. S.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्न|सपत्नः
सपत्न a. Hostile, inimical.<BR>--त्नः<BR>An enemy, adversary, a rival;<BR>Māl. 4. 5; R. 9. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्नी
सपत्नी [समानः पतिर्यस्याः सा] A<BR>rival or fellow wife, rival mistress,<BR>co-wife (having the same husband<BR>with another); दिशः सपत्नी भव<BR>दक्षिणस्याः R. 6. 63, 14. 86; कुरु<BR>प्रियसखीवृत्तिं सपत्नीजने Ś. 4. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्नीक
सपत्नीक a. Attended by a wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्राकृ
सपत्राकृ {c8c} U. To wound very<BR>severely; see below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्राकरणं|सपत्राकरण|सपत्त्राकरणं
सपत्राकरणं<BR>1 Wounding in such<BR>a manner that the feathered part<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">Page1091-c+ 56</a>]<BR>of the arrow enters the body.<BR>--2<BR>Causing excessive pain; cf.<BR>निष्पत्राकरण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपत्राकृतिः|सपत्राकृति|सपत्त्राकृतिः
सपत्राकृतिः f. Great agony or<BR>pain, excessive affliction or torment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपदि
सपदि ind.<BR>1 Instantly, in a<BR>moment, immediately; सपदि<BR>मदनानलो दहति मम मानसं Gīt. 10;<BR>Ku. 3. 76; 6. 2.<BR>--2 Quickly, swiftly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपर्या|सपर्य्या
सपर्या<BR>1 Worship, honouring; सोहं<BR>सपर्याविधिभाजनेन R. 5. 22, 2. 22,<BR>35, 13. 46; Śi. 1. 14;<BR>Ku. 5. 31.<BR>--2 Service, attendance;<BR>प्रतिविहितसपर्यासुस्थयोस्तान्यहानि (स्मरसि)<BR>U. 1. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपाद|सपादः
सपाद a.<BR>1 Having feet.<BR>--2<BR>Increased by a fourth part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिंडः|सपिण्ड|सपिंड|सपिण्डः
सपिंडः ‘Having the same पिंड<BR>or funeral rice-ball offering’, a<BR>kinsman connected by the offering<BR>of the funeral rice-ball to the Manes<BR>of certain relations; Y. 1. 52;<BR>Ms. 2. 247, 5. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपिंडीकरणं|सपिण्डीकरण|सपिण्डीकरणं
सपिंडीकरणं<BR>1 The performance<BR>of a particular Śrāddha in honour<BR>of deceased relatives called सपिंड<BR>q. v., to be performed at the end<BR>of one full year after the death of<BR>a relative, but now usually<BR>performed on the 12th day after death<BR>as part of the funeral obsequies.<BR>--2 Giving a person the rights of a<BR>Sapiṇḍa or kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सपीतिः|सपीति
सपीतिः f. Drinking together<BR>or in company, compotation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तकी
सप्तकी A woman's girdle or zone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तन्
सप्तन् num. a. (always pl.; सप्त<BR>nom. and acc.) Seven.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुः N. of Agni.<BR>--अंशुपुंगवः the<BR>planet Saturn.<BR>--अंग a. see<BR>सप्तप्रकृति below.<BR>--आर्चिस् a. {1} having<BR>seven tongues or flames. {2}<BR>evileyed, of inauspicious look. (--m.)<BR>{1} N. of fire. {2} of Saturn. {3}<BR>the Citraka plant.<BR>--अशीतिः f.<BR>eighty-seven.<BR>--अश्रं a heptagon.<BR>--अश्वः the sun. ˚वाहनः the sun.<BR>--अहः seven days, i. e. a week.<BR>--आत्मन् m. an epithet of Brahman.<BR>--ऋषि (सप्तर्षि) m. pl. {1} the seven<BR>sages; i. e. मरीचि, अत्रि, अंगिरस्, पुलस्त्य,<BR>पुलह, क्रतु, and वसिष्ठ. {2} the<BR>constellation called Ursa Major (the seven<BR>stars of which are said to be the<BR>seven sages mentioned above).<BR>--कोण a. septangular.<BR>--गंगं ind. in<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-a" target="_blank">Page1092-a+ 57</a>]<BR>the place of the seven streams of<BR>the Ganges.<BR>--चत्वारिंशत् f.<BR>fortyseven.<BR>--जिह्वः, --ज्वालः fire.<BR>--तंतुः<BR>a sacrifice; Śi. 14. 6.<BR>--त्रिंशत् f.<BR>thirty-seven.<BR>--दशन् a. seventeen.<BR>--दीधितिः N. of fire.<BR>--द्वीपा an<BR>epithet of the earth; पुरा सप्तद्वीपां<BR>जयति वसुधामप्रतिरथः Ś. 7. 33.<BR>--धातु m. pl. the seven<BR>constituent elements of the body; i. e.<BR>chyle, blood, flesh, fat, bone,<BR>marrow, and semen; (रसास्रमांसमेदोऽ<BR>स्थिमज्जानः शुक्रसंयुताः).<BR>--नवतिः f.<BR>ninetyseven.<BR>--नाडीचक्रं a kind of<BR>astrological diagram used as a means<BR>of foretelling rain.<BR>--पदी the<BR>seven steps at a marriage (the bride<BR>and bridegroom walk together<BR>seven steps, after which the<BR>marriage becomes irrevocable).<BR>--पर्णः<BR>(so सप्तच्छदः, सप्तपत्रः) N. of a tree.<BR>--(र्णी) the sensitive plant.<BR>--प्रकृतिः<BR>f. pl. the seven constituent parts<BR>of a kingdom;<BR>स्वाम्यमात्यसुहृत्कोशराष्ट्रदुर्गबलानि च Ak.; see प्रकृति also.<BR>--भद्रः the Śirīṣa tree.<BR>--भूमिक, --भौम<BR>a. seven stories high (as a palace).<BR>--रक्तः one who has got the seven<BR>parts of the body red; (पाणिपादतले<BR>रक्ते नेत्रांतरनखानि च । तालुकाधरजिह्वाश्च<BR>प्रशस्ता सप्तरक्तता ॥).<BR>--रात्रं a period of<BR>seven nights.<BR>--विंशतिः f.<BR>twentyseven.<BR>--विध a. seven-fold, of<BR>seven sorts.<BR>--शतं {1} 700. {2}<BR>107.<BR>--(ती) an aggregate or<BR>collection of 700 verses or stanzas.<BR>--शलाकः a kind of astronomical<BR>diagram used for indicating<BR>auspicious days for marriages.<BR>--सप्तिः<BR>an epithet of the sun; सर्वैरुस्रैः<BR>समग्रैस्त्वमिव नृपगुणैर्दीप्यते सप्तसप्तिः<BR>M. 2. 13; Ś. 6. 29.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1091-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तक|सप्तकः
सप्तक a. (का or की f.)<BR>1<BR>Containing seven.<BR>--2 Seven.<BR>--3<BR>Seventh.<BR>--कं A collection of<BR>seven things (verses &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्ततिः|सप्तति
सप्ततिः f. Seventy. ˚तम a. 70th.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तधा
सप्तधा ind.<BR>1 Seven-fold.<BR>--2 In<BR>seven parts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तम|सप्तमः
सप्तम a. (मी f.) The seventh.<BR>--मी<BR>f.<BR>1 The seventh or locative case (in<BR>gram.).<BR>--2 The seventh day of<BR>a lunar fortnight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तला
सप्तला A kind of jasmine<BR>(double jasmine).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्तिः|सप्ति
सप्तिः<BR>1 A yoke.<BR>--2 A horse; जवो<BR>हि सप्तेः परमं विभूषणं Subhāṣ.; see<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">Page1092-b+ 56</a>]<BR>सप्तसप्ति also.<BR>--3 A yoke-fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रणय
सप्रणय a. Affectionate, friendly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रत्यय
सप्रत्यय a.<BR>1 Placing confidence<BR>in.<BR>--2 Certain, sure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रश्रयं|सप्रश्रय
सप्रश्रयं ind. Respectfully, with<BR>great courtesy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सप्रसव
सप्रसव a. Derived from a<BR>common source; R. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफरः|सफर
सफरः --री A small glittering fish,<BR>cf. शफर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफरी
सफरः --री A small glittering fish,<BR>cf. शफर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सफल|सफलं
सफल a.<BR>1 Fruitful, bearing or<BR>yielding fruit, productive (fig. also).<BR>--2 Accomplished, fulfilled,<BR>successful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबंधु|सबन्धु|सबन्धुः
सबंधु a.<BR>1 Closely connected.<BR>--2<BR>Having a friend, befriended.<BR>--3<BR>Of the same family.<BR>--धुः A<BR>relation, kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबलिः|सबलि
सबलिः Evening twilight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सबाध|सबाधः
सबाध a.<BR>1 Hurtful.<BR>--2<BR>Oppressive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सब्रह्मचर्यं|सब्रह्मचर्य|सब्रह्मचर्य्य
सब्रह्मचर्यं Fellow-studentship<BR>(being disciples of the same teacher).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सब्रह्मचारिन्
सब्रह्मचारिन् m.<BR>1 A fellow-student,<BR>one going through the same<BR>studies and observing the same<BR>austerities.<BR>--2 A fellow-sufferer,<BR>sympathiser; दुःखसब्रह्मचारिणी तरलिका क्व<BR>गता K.; हे व्यसनसब्रह्मचारिन् यदि न<BR>गुह्यं ततः श्रोतुमिच्छामि Mu. 6.<BR>--3<BR>(Hence) An equal, of the same<BR>kind; Vb. 1. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभर्तृका|सभर्त्तृका
सभर्तृका A woman whose<BR>husband is living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभा
सभा [सह भांति अभीष्टनिश्चयार्थमेकत्र<BR>यत्र गृहे Tv.]<BR>1 An assembly, a<BR>council, conclave; पंडितसभां कारितवाम्<BR>Pt. 1; न सा सभा यत्र न संति वृद्धाः<BR>H. 1.<BR>--2 Company, society,<BR>meeting, large number.<BR>--3<BR>Council-chamber or hall.<BR>--4 A court of justice.<BR>--5 A public audience (modern<BR>levee).<BR>--6 A gambling-house.<BR>--7<BR>Any room or place much<BR>frequented.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचारः {1} the customs<BR>of society. {2} court-manners.<BR>--आस्तारः {1} an assistant at an<BR>assembly. {2} a member of a society.<BR>--उचितः a learned Brāhmaṇa, an<BR>educated person.<BR>--पतिः, --नायकः<BR>{1} the president of a society,<BR>chairman. {2} the keeper of a<BR>gaminghouse.<BR>--पूजा worship or reverence<BR>paid to the audience.<BR>--सद् m. {1}<BR>an assistant at an assembly or<BR>meeting. {2} a member of an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">Page1092-c+ 57</a>]<BR>assembly or meeting. {3} an<BR>assessor, a juror.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाज्
सभाज् {c10c} U. (सभाजयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>salute, pay respects, greet, render<BR>homage to, congratulate;<BR>स्नेहात्सभाजयितुमेत्य U. 1. 7; Śi. 13. 14;<BR>Ś. 5.<BR>--2 To honour, worship,<BR>respect.<BR>--3 To please, gratify.<BR>--4 To<BR>beautify, adorn, grace; U. 4. 19.<BR>--5 To show.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभाजनं|सभाजन
सभाजनं [सभाज्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 (a)<BR>Paying respects to, salutation,<BR>honouring, worshipping^1;<BR>Śi. 13. 14. (b) Welcoming,<BR>congratulation; R. 13. 43, 14. 18.<BR>--2<BR>Civility, courtesy, politeness.<BR>--3<BR>Service.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभावनः|सभावन
सभावनः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभिकः|सभिक
सभि(भी)कः [सभा द्यूतं<BR>प्रयोजनभस्य ईक्] The keeper of a<BR>gaminghouse; अयमस्माकं पूर्वसभिको माथुर इत<BR>एवागच्छति Mk. 3; Y. 2. 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभीकः|सभीक
सभि(भी)कः [सभा द्यूतं<BR>प्रयोजनभस्य ईक्] The keeper of a<BR>gaminghouse; अयमस्माकं पूर्वसभिको माथुर इत<BR>एवागच्छति Mk. 3; Y. 2. 199.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्य|सभ्यः
सभ्य a. [सभायां साधु यत्]<BR>1<BR>Belonging to an assembly.<BR>--2 Fit for<BR>society.<BR>--3 Refined, polished,<BR>civilized.<BR>--4 Well-bred, polite, civil,<BR>courteous; R. 1. 55, Ku. 7. 29.<BR>--5 Confidential, trusty, faithful.<BR>--भ्यः<BR>1 An assessor.<BR>--2 An<BR>assistant at an assembly.<BR>--3 A<BR>person of honourable parentage.<BR>--4<BR>The keeper of a gaming-house.<BR>--5<BR>The servant of the keeper of a<BR>gaming-house.<BR>--6 N. of one of the five<BR>sacred fires.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्यता
सभ्यता, --त्वं Politeness, good<BR>manners or breeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सभ्यत्वं|सभ्यत्व
सभ्यता, --त्वं Politeness, good<BR>manners or breeding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्
सम् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (समति)<BR>1 To be<BR>confused or agitated.<BR>--2 Not to be<BR>confused or agitated. {vII.v} {c10c} U.<BR>(समयति-ते) To be agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्
सम् ind.<BR>1 As a prefix to verbs<BR>and verbal derivatives it means (a)<BR>with, together with, together; as in<BR>संगम्, संभाषण, संधा, संयुज् &c. (b)<BR>Sometimes it intensifies the<BR>meaning of the simple root, and may be<BR>translated by ‘very, quite, greatly,<BR>thoroughly, very much’; संतुष्, संतोष,<BR>संन्यस्, संन्यास, संताप &c. (c) It<BR>also expresses completeness,<BR>perfection, or beauty.<BR>--2 As prefixed<BR>to nouns to form comp. it means<BR>‘like, same, similar,’ as in समर्थ.<BR>--3 Sometimes it means ‘near’,<BR>‘before’; as in समक्ष.<BR>--4 In the<BR>Vedas it is sometimes used as a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-a" target="_blank">Page1093-a+ 56</a>]<BR>separable preposition (with instr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1092-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम|समः
सम a.<BR>1 Same, identical.<BR>--2<BR>Equal, as in समलोष्टकांचनः<BR>R. 8. 21; Pt. 2. 7; Bg. 2. 38.<BR>--3 Like,<BR>similar, resembling; with instr.<BR>or gen. or in comp.; गुणयुक्तो<BR>दरिद्रोपि नेश्वरैरगुणैः समः Subhāṣ.;<BR>Ku. 3. 13.<BR>--4 Even, level, plain;<BR>समदेशवर्तिनस्ते न दुरासदो भविष्यति Ś. 1.<BR>--5 Even (as number).<BR>--6<BR>Impartial, fair.<BR>--7 Just, honest,<BR>upright.<BR>--8 Good, virtuous.<BR>--9<BR>Ordinary, common.<BR>--10 Mean,<BR>middling.<BR>--11 Straight.<BR>--12 Suitable,<BR>convenient.<BR>--13 Indifferent,<BR>unmoved, unaffected by passion.<BR>--14 All, every one.<BR>--15 All,<BR>whole, entire, complete.<BR>--मः<BR>1 N. of certain zodiacal signs (वृष,<BR>कर्कट, कन्या, वृश्चिक, मकर, and मीन).<BR>--2<BR>A mode of measuring time in music.<BR>--मं<BR>1 A level plain, flat country;<BR>Ki. 9. 11.<BR>--2 (In rhet.) N. of a figure<BR>of speech.<BR>--3 (In geometry) A mean<BR>proportional segment.<BR>--मं ind.<BR>1<BR>With, together with, in company<BR>with, accompanied by; (with instr.);<BR>आहो निवत्स्यति समं हरिणांगनाभिः<BR>Ś. 1. 27; R. 2. 25, 8. 63, 16. 72.<BR>--2<BR>Equally; यथा सर्वाणि भूतानि धरा<BR>धारयते समं Ms. 9. 311.<BR>--3 Like,<BR>similarly, in the same manner;<BR>Pt. 1. 78.<BR>--4 Entirely.<BR>--5<BR>Simultaneously, all at once, at the same<BR>time, together; नंव पयो यत्र घनैर्मया<BR>च त्वद्विप्रयोगाश्रु समं विसृष्टं R. 13. 26.<BR>4. 4; 10. 59; 14. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः an equal share. ˚हारिन् m.<BR>a co-heir.<BR>--अंतर a. parallel.<BR>--आचारः {1} equal or similar conduct.<BR>{2} proper practice.<BR>--उदकं a<BR>mixture of half butter-milk and half<BR>water.<BR>--उपमा a kind of Upamā<BR>or simile.<BR>--कन्या a fit or suitable<BR>girl (fit to be married).<BR>--कर्णः an<BR>equi-diagonal tetragon.<BR>--कालः the<BR>same time or moment.<BR>--(लं) ind.<BR>at the same time, simultaneously.<BR>--कालीन a. contemporary, coeval.<BR>--कोलः a serpent, snake.<BR>--क्षेत्रं<BR>(in astr.) an epithet of a<BR>particular arrangement of the<BR>Nakṣatras.<BR>--खातः an equal<BR>excavation, a parallelopipedon.<BR>--गंधकः<BR>incense.<BR>--गंधिकं the fragrant root<BR>of the Uśīra.<BR>--चतुरस्र a. square.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-b" target="_blank">Page1093-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--(स्रं) an equilateral tetragon.<BR>--चतुर्भुजः --जं a rhombus.<BR>--चित्त<BR>a. {1} even-minded, equable,<BR>equanimous. {2} indifferent.<BR>--छेद, छेदन<BR>a. having the same denominator.<BR>--जाति a. homogeneous.<BR>--ज्ञा fame.<BR>--त्रिभुजः --जं an equilateral<BR>triangle.<BR>--दर्शनं, --दर्शिन् a. viewing<BR>equally, impartial; विद्याविनयसंपन्ने<BR>ब्राह्मणे गवि हस्तिनि । शुनि चैव श्वपाके च<BR>पंडिताः समदर्शिनः Bg. 5. 18.<BR>--दुःख<BR>a. feeling for another's woe,<BR>sympathising (with another); a<BR>fellowsufferer; Ku. 4. 4. ˚सुख a. a<BR>companion or partner in joy and<BR>sorrow; Ś. 3. 11.<BR>--दृश् --दृष्टि a.<BR>impartial.<BR>--द्वादशास्रः --स्रं an<BR>equilateral dodecagon.<BR>--द्विभुजः a<BR>rhomboid.<BR>--धृत a. equal to.<BR>--पदं an<BR>attitude in shooting.<BR>--बुद्धि a. {1}<BR>impartial. {2} indifferent, stoical.<BR>--भाव a. having the same nature<BR>or property.<BR>--(वः) sameness,<BR>equability.<BR>--मंडलं (in astr.) the<BR>prime vertical line.<BR>--मय a. of<BR>like origin.<BR>--रंजित a. tinged.<BR>--रभः a particular mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR>--रेख a. straight;<BR>प्रकृत्या यद्वक्रं तदपि समरेखं नयनयोः<BR>Ś. 1. 9.<BR>--लंबः --बं a trapezoid.<BR>--वर्णः<BR>community of caste.<BR>--वर्तिन् a.<BR>equal-minded, impartial. (--m.)<BR>Yama, the god of death.<BR>--वृत्तं {1}<BR>an even metre, i. e. a stanza the<BR>lines of which have all the same<BR>number of feet. {2} see सममंडल.<BR>--वृत्ति a. equable, fair.<BR>--वेधः mean<BR>depth.<BR>--शोधनं equal subtraction,<BR>i. e. subtraction of the same<BR>quantity on both sides of an equation.<BR>--संधिः peace on equal terms.<BR>--सुप्तिः f. universal sleep (as at the<BR>end of a Kalpa).<BR>--सूत्र, --सूत्रस्थ a.<BR>situated on the same diameter.<BR>--स्थ<BR>a. {1} equal, uniform. {2} level. {3}<BR>like.<BR>--स्थलं an even ground.<BR>--स्थली the level plain, the Doab<BR>or country between the Ganges<BR>and Yamunā (अंतर्वेदि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समता
समता --त्वं<BR>1 Sameness, identity.<BR>--2 Likeness, similarity.<BR>--3<BR>Equality; Pt. 2. 83.<BR>--4 Impartiality,<BR>fairness; समतां नी ‘to treat as equal’<BR>Ms. 9. 218.<BR>--5 Equanimity.<BR>--6<BR>Perfectness.<BR>--7 Commonness.<BR>--8<BR>Evenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समत्वं|समत्व
समता --त्वं<BR>1 Sameness, identity.<BR>--2 Likeness, similarity.<BR>--3<BR>Equality; Pt. 2. 83.<BR>--4 Impartiality,<BR>fairness; समतां नी ‘to treat as equal’<BR>Ms. 9. 218.<BR>--5 Equanimity.<BR>--6<BR>Perfectness.<BR>--7 Commonness.<BR>--8<BR>Evenness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समक्ष|समक्षं
समक्ष a. Being before the eyes,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">Page1093-c+ 55</a>]<BR>visible, present.<BR>--क्षं ind. In<BR>the presence of, visibly, before the<BR>very eyes; Ku. 5. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समग्र|समग्रः
समग्र a. All, whole, entire,<BR>complete; M. 2. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समंगा|समङ्गा
समंगा Bengal madder(मंजिष्ठा).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्
समज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring or<BR>collect together, unite.<BR>--2 To bring<BR>into conflict.<BR>--3 To subdue,<BR>overpower.<BR>--4 To animate, incite,<BR>excite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समजः|समज|समजं
समजः<BR>1 A multitude of beasts,<BR>animals or birds, a herd, flock.<BR>--2<BR>A number of fools.<BR>--जं A wood,<BR>forest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समज्या
समज्या<BR>1 A meeting, an assembly.<BR>--2 Fame, renown, celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समंजस|समञ्जस|समञ्जसं|समञ्जसः
समंजस a.<BR>1 Proper, reasonable,<BR>right, fit.<BR>--2 Correct, true,<BR>accurate.<BR>--3 Clear, intelligible; as in<BR>असमंजस, q. v.<BR>--4 Virtuous, good,<BR>just; भृशाधिरूढस्य समंजसं जनं<BR>Ki. 14. 12.<BR>--5 Practised, experienced.<BR>--6 Healthy.<BR>--सं<BR>1 Propriety,<BR>fitness.<BR>--2 Accuracy.<BR>--3 Correct<BR>evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रम्
समतिक्रम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To go<BR>completely beyond, cross or step over.<BR>--2 To neglect, disregard, violate.<BR>--3<BR>To surpass, excel.<BR>--4 To elapse,<BR>pass by (as time).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतिक्रमः|समतिक्रम
समतिक्रमः Transgression, omission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समती
समती {c2c} P.<BR>1 To go completely<BR>beyond.<BR>--2 To go through, cross over.<BR>--3 To surpass, excel.<BR>--4 To avoid.<BR>--5 To pass, elapse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समतीत
समतीत p. p. Gone, passed by,<BR>past (as time); समतीतं च भवच्च भावि<BR>च R. 8. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समद
समद a.<BR>1 Intoxicated, furious.<BR>--2 Mad with rut.<BR>--3 Drunk with<BR>passion; U. 2. 20; Mv. 5. 40.<BR>--4<BR>Delighted, glad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिक|समधिकः
समधिक a.<BR>1 Exceeding.<BR>--2<BR>Excessive, abundant, plentiful;<BR>U. 4.<BR>--कं ind. Very much, exceedingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिगम्
समधिगम् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To approach.<BR>--2 To study.<BR>--3 To get, acquire;<BR>यत्ते समधिगच्छंति यस्यैते तस्य तद्धनं<BR>Ms. 8. 416.<BR>--4 To excel, surpass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समधिगमनं|समधिगमन
समधिगमनं Surpassing,<BR>overcoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समध्व
समध्व a. Travelling in<BR>company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञा
समनुज्ञा {c9c} U.<BR>1 To consent, give<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">Page1094-a+ 56</a>]<BR>full consent.<BR>--2 To approve,<BR>permit, allow.<BR>--3 To dismiss, give<BR>leave, allow to go.<BR>--4 To forgive,<BR>pardon.<BR>--5 To favour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1093-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समनुज्ञानं|समनुज्ञान
समनुज्ञानं<BR>1 Assent, consent.<BR>--2<BR>Entire approval, full concurrence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समंत|समन्त|समन्तः
समंत a. [सम्यक् अंतः, स यत्र वा]<BR>1 Being on every side, universal.<BR>--2<BR>Complete, entire.<BR>--तः Limit,<BR>boundary, term. (समंतं, समंततः, समंतात् are<BR>used adverbially in the sense of<BR>‘from every side’, ‘all around’,<BR>‘on all sides’, ‘wholly’,<BR>‘completely’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दुग्धा the<BR>plant called स्नुही q. v.<BR>--पंचकं N.<BR>of the district called Kurukṣetra<BR>or of a place near it; Ve. 6.<BR>--भद्रः<BR>a Buddha or the Buddha.<BR>--भुज् m.<BR>fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्यु|समन्युः
समन्यु a.<BR>1 Sorrowful.<BR>--2<BR>Enraged, angry.<BR>--न्युः An epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वि
समन्वि {c2c} P.<BR>1 To follow,<BR>accompany.<BR>--2 To follow or infer as<BR>a consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वयः|समन्वय
समन्वयः<BR>1 Regular succession or<BR>order.<BR>--2 Connected sequence,<BR>mutual connection, applicability (तात्पर्य);<BR>तत्तु समन्वयात् Br. Sūt. I. 1. 4; न च<BR>तद्धतानां पदानां ब्रह्मस्वरूपविषये निश्चिते<BR>समन्वयेऽर्थातरकल्पना युक्ता Ś. B.<BR>--3<BR>Conjunction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समन्वित|समन्वितः
समन्वित p. p.<BR>1 Connected with,<BR>connected in natural order.<BR>--2<BR>Followed.<BR>--3 Endowed with,<BR>possessing, full of.<BR>--4 Affected by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिप्लुत
समभिप्लुत p. p.<BR>1 Inundated.<BR>--2<BR>Eclipsed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिव्याहारः|समभिव्याहार
समभिव्याहारः<BR>1 Mentioning<BR>together.<BR>--2 Association, company.<BR>--3 Proximity to or association with<BR>a word, the meaning of which is<BR>clearly ascertained or understood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिसरणं|समभिसरण
समभिसरणं<BR>1 Approaching.<BR>--2<BR>Seeking, wishing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभिहारः|समभिहार
समभिहारः<BR>1 Taking together.<BR>--2 Repetition.<BR>--3 Surplus, excess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभ्यर्चनं|समभ्यर्चन|समभ्यर्च्चन
समभ्यर्चनं Worshipping,<BR>reverencing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समभ्याहारः|समभ्याहार
समभ्याहारः Accompaniment,<BR>association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समयः|समय
समयः<BR>1 Time in general.<BR>--2<BR>Occasion, opportunity.<BR>--3 Fit time,<BR>proper time or season, right<BR>moment; Ku. 3. 25.<BR>--4 An agreement,<BR>a compact, contract, an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-b" target="_blank">Page1094-b+ 56</a>]<BR>engagement; मिथःसमयात् Ś. 5.<BR>--5 A<BR>convention, conventional usage.<BR>--6<BR>An established rule of conduct, a<BR>ceremonial custom, usual practice;<BR>निरस्तनारीसमया दुराधयः<BR>Ki. 1. 28; U. 1.<BR>--7 The<BR>convention of poets; (e. g. that persons<BR>separated from their beloveds are<BR>affected at the sight of clouds).<BR>--8<BR>An appointment, assignation.<BR>--9<BR>A condition, stipulation; V. 5.<BR>--10 A law, rule, regulation;<BR>Y. 3. 19; U. 5. 19.<BR>--11<BR>Direction, order, instruction, precept.<BR>--12 Emergency, exigency.<BR>--13<BR>An oath.<BR>--14 A sign, hint,<BR>indication.<BR>--15 Limit, boundary.<BR>--16 A<BR>demonstrated conclusion, doctrine,<BR>tenet; बौद्ध˚, वैशेषिक˚ &c.<BR>--17 End,<BR>conclusion, termination.<BR>--18<BR>Success, prosperity.<BR>--19 End of trouble.<BR>(समयेन ‘on condition,<BR>conditionally’).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्युषितं a time<BR>at which neither the stars nor the<BR>sun is visible.<BR>--अनुवर्तिन् a.<BR>following established customs.<BR>--अनुसारेण,<BR>--उचितं ind. suitably to the occasion,<BR>as the occasion demands.<BR>--आचारः<BR>conventional practice, established<BR>usage; Māl. 4. 6.<BR>--क्रिया making<BR>an agreement.<BR>--परिरक्षणं observance<BR>of a compact, treaty, or agreement;<BR>न समयपरिरक्षणं क्षमं ते Ki. 1. 45.<BR>--भेदः<BR>breaking an agreement or<BR>engagement, breach of contract.<BR>--व्यभिचारः<BR>breaking an agreement, violation or<BR>breach of contract.<BR>--व्यभिचारिन् a.<BR>breaking an agreement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समया
समया ind.<BR>1 Duly, seasonably,<BR>in due time.<BR>--2 At a fixed or<BR>appointed time.<BR>--3 In the midst,<BR>within, between.<BR>--4 Near (with<BR>acc.); समया सौधभित्तिं Dk.;<BR>Śi. 6. 73, 15. 9, Nalod. 4. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरः|समर|समरं
समरः --रं War, battle, fight;<BR>कर्णादयोऽपि समरात्पराङ्मुखीभवंति<BR>Ve. 3.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्देशः, --भूमि f.<BR>battlefield.<BR>--मूर्धन् m.,<BR>--शिरस् n. the front<BR>or van of battle; U. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समरं|समर|समरः
समरः --रं War, battle, fight;<BR>कर्णादयोऽपि समरात्पराङ्मुखीभवंति<BR>Ve. 3.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्देशः, --भूमि f.<BR>battlefield.<BR>--मूर्धन् m.,<BR>--शिरस् n. the front<BR>or van of battle; U. 5. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्चनं|समर्चन|समर्च्चन
समर्चनं Worshipping,<BR>honouring, adoration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्ण|समर्ण्ण
समर्ण a.<BR>1 Afflicted, pained,<BR>wounded.<BR>--2 Asked, solicited.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थ्
समर्थ् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To believe,<BR>consider, regard, think; समर्थये<BR>यत्प्रथमं प्रियां प्रति V. 4. 39; मया न<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">Page1094-c+ 57</a>]<BR>साधु समर्थितं V. 2; अनुपयुक्तमिव<BR>आत्मानं समर्थये Ś. 7, 3. 19.<BR>--2 To<BR>corroborate, support, substantiate<BR>by proof; उक्तमेवार्थमुदाहरणेन<BR>समर्थयति.<BR>--3 To deliberate, think or<BR>reflect about.<BR>--4 To make ready,<BR>prepare.<BR>--5 To maintain, assert,<BR>enforce.<BR>--6 To imply, suggest.<BR>--7<BR>To approve.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थ|समर्थः
समर्थ a.<BR>1 Strong, powerful.<BR>--2<BR>Competent, allowed, qualified;<BR>प्रतिग्रहसमर्थोऽपि Ms. 4. 186;<BR>Y. 1. 213.<BR>--3 Fit, suitable, proper;<BR>तद्धनुर्ग्रहणमेव राघवः प्रत्यपद्यत समर्थमुत्तरं<BR>R. 11. 79.<BR>--4 Made fit or proper,<BR>prepared.<BR>--5 Having the same<BR>meaning.<BR>--6 Significant.<BR>--7 Having<BR>proper aim or force, very forcible.<BR>--8<BR>Being in apposition.<BR>--9 Connected<BR>in sense.<BR>--र्थः<BR>1 A significant word<BR>(in gram.); अव्ययं समर्थेन सह<BR>समस्यते सोऽव्ययीभावः Sk.<BR>--2 The<BR>coherence of words together in a<BR>significant sentence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थकं|समर्थक
समर्थकं Aloe-wood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थता
समर्थता --त्वं<BR>1 Strength, power.<BR>--2<BR>Force, forcibleness.<BR>--3 Sameness of<BR>meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थत्वं|समर्थत्व
समर्थता --त्वं<BR>1 Strength, power.<BR>--2<BR>Force, forcibleness.<BR>--3 Sameness of<BR>meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थनं|समर्थन
समर्थनं --ना<BR>1 Establishing,<BR>supporting, corroborating.<BR>--2<BR>Defending, vindicating, justifying;<BR>स्थितेष्वेतत्समर्थनं K. P. 7.<BR>--3 Pleading,<BR>advocating.<BR>--4 Judging,<BR>considering, imagining.<BR>--5 Deliberation,<BR>determination, deciding on the<BR>propriety or otherwise of anything.<BR>--6<BR>Adequacy, efficacy, force, capability.<BR>--7 Energy, perseverance.<BR>--8<BR>Reconciling differences, allaying disputes.<BR>--9 Objection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थना
समर्थनं --ना<BR>1 Establishing,<BR>supporting, corroborating.<BR>--2<BR>Defending, vindicating, justifying;<BR>स्थितेष्वेतत्समर्थनं K. P. 7.<BR>--3 Pleading,<BR>advocating.<BR>--4 Judging,<BR>considering, imagining.<BR>--5 Deliberation,<BR>determination, deciding on the<BR>propriety or otherwise of anything.<BR>--6<BR>Adequacy, efficacy, force, capability.<BR>--7 Energy, perseverance.<BR>--8<BR>Reconciling differences, allaying disputes.<BR>--9 Objection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्थित
समर्थित p. p.<BR>1 Maintained,<BR>established.<BR>--2 Thought, imagined,<BR>considered, judged.<BR>--3 Determined;<BR>see समर्थ् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्धक|समर्द्धकः
समर्धक a.<BR>1 Granting a boon.<BR>--2 Causing to prosper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्पणं|समर्पण|समर्प्पण
समर्पणं Giving or handing over<BR>to, delivering, consigning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्पित|समर्प्पित
समर्पित a.<BR>1 Made over, delivered,<BR>consigned, committed.<BR>--2 Restored,<BR>given back.<BR>--3 Appointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समर्याद|समर्यादः|समर्य्याद|समर्य्यादः
समर्याद a.<BR>1 Limited, bounded.<BR>--2 Near, proximate.<BR>--3 Correct in<BR>conduct, keeping within bounds of<BR>propriety.<BR>--4 Respectful, courteous<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समल|समलं
समल a.<BR>1 Dirty, foul, filthy,<BR>impure.<BR>--2 Sinful.<BR>--लं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">Page1095-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Excrement, ordure, feces.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1094-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवकारः|समवकार
समवकारः A kind of drama;<BR>(thus described in S. D.:--वृत्तं<BR>समवकारे तु ख्यातं देवासुराश्रयं । संधयो<BR>निविंमर्शास्तु त्रयोंकाः &c. 515).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवतारः|समवतार
समवतारः<BR>1 A descent.<BR>--2 A<BR>descent into a river or sacred<BR>bathing place; समवतारसमैरसमैस्तटैः<BR>Ki. 5. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवधानं|समवधान
समवधानं<BR>1 Great attention.<BR>--2 Preparation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्था
समवस्था {c1c} A.<BR>1 To remain<BR>fixed, stand immovable; stand still.<BR>--2 To stand ready. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>establish, found.<BR>--2 To stop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्था
समवस्था<BR>1 Fixed condition.<BR>--2<BR>Similar condition or state; Ś. 4.<BR>--3<BR>State or condition in general;<BR>R. 19. 50; M. 4. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवस्थित
समवस्थित p. p.<BR>1 Remaining<BR>fixed.<BR>--2 Steady.<BR>--3 Ready.<BR>--4 Being<BR>in any place or position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवाप्तिः|समवाप्ति
समवाप्तिः f. Obtaining,<BR>acquisition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवे
समवे {c2c} P.<BR>1 To assemble,<BR>come together; समवेता युयुत्सवः<BR>Bg. 1. 1.<BR>--2 To be related or<BR>connected in an intimate relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायः|समवाय
समवायः<BR>1 Combination, union,<BR>conjunction, aggregate, collection;<BR>सर्वाविनयानामेकैकमप्येषामायतनं किमुत<BR>समवायः K.; बहूनामप्यसाराणां समवायो<BR>हि दुर्जयः Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 A number,<BR>multitude, heap.<BR>--3 Close<BR>connection, cohesion.<BR>--4 (In Vaiś. phil.)<BR>Intimate union, constant and<BR>inseparable connection, inseparable<BR>inherence or existence of one thing<BR>in another, one of the seven<BR>categories of the Vaiśeṣikas;<BR>नित्यसंबंधः समवायः Tarka K.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--संबंधः intimate and inseparable<BR>relation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवायिन्
समवायिन् a.<BR>1 Closely or<BR>intimately connected.<BR>--2 Multitudinous.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारणं inseparable cause,<BR>the material cause (one of the three<BR>kinds of कारण mentioned in<BR>Vaiśeshika phil.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समवेत|समवेतः
समवेत p. p.<BR>1 Come together,<BR>met, united, joined.<BR>--2 Intimately<BR>united or inherent, inseparably<BR>connected.<BR>--3 Comprised or contained<BR>in a larger number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समश्
समश् {vI.v} {c5c} U.<BR>1 To pervade<BR>thoroughly.<BR>--2 To obtain, attain to.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">Page1095-b+ 57</a>]<BR>--3 To meet. {vII.v} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To eat;<BR>नक्तं चान्नं समश्नीयात् Ms. 6. 19;<BR>11. 219.<BR>--2 To taste, experience, enjoy;<BR>यथा फलं समश्नाति Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समष्टिः|समष्टि
समष्टिः f.<BR>1 Collective pervasion<BR>or aggregate, an aggregate which<BR>is considered as made up of parts<BR>each of which is consubstantially<BR>the same with the whole (opp. व्यष्टि<BR>q. v.); समष्टिरीशः सर्वेषां<BR>स्वात्मतादात्म्यवेदनात् । तदभावात्तदन्ये तु ज्ञायंते<BR>व्यष्टिसंज्ञया ॥ Pañcadaśī.<BR>--2<BR>Totality.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्
समस् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To throw or bring<BR>together, put together, unite,<BR>combine, Ms. 3. 85, 7. 57.<BR>--2 To join in<BR>a compound, compound.<BR>--3 To take<BR>collectively or jointly; समस्तैरथ वा<BR>पृथक् Ms. 7. 198 ‘jointly or<BR>severally.’ --Pass. To be compounded,<BR>form or enter into a compound;<BR>अव्ययं समर्थेन सह समस्यते सोऽ<BR>व्ययीभावः Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समसनं|समसन
समसनं<BR>1 Joining together,<BR>combination.<BR>--2 Compounding,<BR>formation of compound words.<BR>--3<BR>Contraction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्त|समस्तं
समस्त p. p.<BR>1 Thrown together,<BR>combined; Pt. 1. 383.<BR>--2<BR>Compounded.<BR>--3 Pervading the whole<BR>of anything.<BR>--4 Abridged,<BR>contracted, condensed.<BR>--5 All, whole,<BR>entire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समस्या
समस्या<BR>1 Proposing part of a<BR>stanza to another to be completed,<BR>the part of a stanza so given to be<BR>completed; कः श्रीपतिः का विषमा<BR>समस्या Subhāṣ.; (thus the lines<BR>वागर्थाविव संपूक्तौ, शतकोटिप्रविस्तरं; तरासाहं<BR>पुरोधाय are completed by नेमुः सर्वे सुराः<BR>शिवौ.)<BR>--2 (Hence) Completing or<BR>filling up what is incomplete;<BR>गौरीव पत्या सुभगा<BR>कदाचित्कर्त्रीयमप्यर्धतनूसमस्यां N. 7. 82 (समस्या = संघटनं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समा
समा (generally in pl., but used<BR>by Pāṇini in sing. also, e. g. समां<BR>समां P. V. 2. 12.) A year; तेनाष्टौ<BR>परिगमिताः समाः कथंचित् R. 8. 92;<BR>तयोश्चतुर्दशैकेन समं प्राव्राजयत्समाः<BR>12. 6; 19. 4; Mv. 4. 41. --ind. With;<BR>together with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समांसमीना
समांसमीना A cow bearing a<BR>calf every year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकुल
समाकुल a.<BR>1 Full of, thronged,<BR>crowded.<BR>--2 Greatly agitated,<BR>bewildered, confused, flurried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकृष्
समाकृष् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To draw out,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">Page1095-c+ 56</a>]<BR>extract.<BR>--2 To attract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाकर्षिन्
समाकर्षिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>1 Attracting.<BR>--2 Spreading far, diffusing<BR>fragrance. --m. Diffused odour, a scent<BR>spreading afar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रम्
समाक्रम् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To take<BR>possession of, occupy, fill; सममेव समाक्रांतं<BR>द्वयं द्विरदगामिना । तेन सिंहासनं<BR>पित्र्यमखिलं चारिमंडलं R. 4. 4.<BR>--2 To<BR>assail, conquer, subdue.<BR>--3 To<BR>tread or step upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाक्रमणं|समाक्रमण
समाक्रमणं<BR>1 Treading.<BR>--2<BR>Assailing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्या
समाख्या {c2c} P.<BR>1 To count, reckon.<BR>--2 To relate, tell.<BR>--3 To declare,<BR>proclaim.<BR>--4 To sum up, add<BR>together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्या
समाख्या<BR>1 Fame, reputation,<BR>celebrity.<BR>--2 A name, appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाख्यात
समाख्यात p. p.<BR>1 Reckoned up,<BR>counted, summed up.<BR>--2 Fully<BR>related, declared, proclaimed.<BR>--3<BR>Celebrated, famous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागम्
समागम्<BR>1 To come or meet<BR>together, assemble.<BR>--2 To become<BR>joined or united, to associate, keep<BR>company with.<BR>--3 To have sexual<BR>intercourse with.<BR>--4 To come<BR>together, be in conjunction (as<BR>planets).<BR>--5 To come near,<BR>approach.<BR>--6 To return.<BR>--7 To find,<BR>meet with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागत|समागतः
समागत p. p.<BR>1 Come together,<BR>met, joined, united.<BR>--2 Arrived.<BR>--3 Being in conjunction.<BR>--4<BR>Approached.<BR>--ता A kind of riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागतिः|समागति
समागतिः f.<BR>1 Coming together,<BR>union, meeting.<BR>--2 Arrival,<BR>approach.<BR>--3 Similar condition or<BR>progress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समागमः|समागम
समागमः<BR>1 Union, meeting,<BR>encountering, combination; अहो<BR>दैवगतिश्चित्रा तथापि न समागमः K. P. 7;<BR>R. 8. 4, 92, 19. 16.<BR>--2 Intercourse,<BR>association, society; as in<BR>सत्समागमः.<BR>--3 Approach, arrival.<BR>--4<BR>Conjunction (in astr.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाघातः|समाघात
समाघातः<BR>1 Killing, slaughter.<BR>--2 War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचयनं|समाचयन
समाचयनं Accumulation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचर्
समाचर् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To do, perform,<BR>practise; एहि गच्छ पतोत्तिष्ठ वद मौनं<BR>समाचर K. P. 10.<BR>--2 To behave.<BR>--3 To remove.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचरणं|समाचरण
समाचरणं Practising, observing,<BR>behaving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1095-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाचारः|समाचार
समाचारः<BR>1 Proceeding, going.<BR>--2<BR>Practice, conduct, behaviour.<BR>--3<BR>Proper conduct or behaviour.<BR>--4<BR>News, information, report, tidings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाजः|समाज
समाजः<BR>1 An assembly, a<BR>meeting; विशेषतः सर्वविदां समाजे विभूषणं<BR>मौनमपंडितानां Bh. 2. 7.<BR>--2 A society,<BR>club, an association.<BR>--3 A number,<BR>multitude, collection.<BR>--4 A party,<BR>convivial meeting.<BR>--5 An elephant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाजिकः|समाजिक
समाजिकः<BR>1 A member of an<BR>assembly; see सामाजिक.<BR>--2 A<BR>spectator in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज्ञा
समाज्ञा {c9c} U.<BR>1 To know or<BR>understand thoroughly, learn or<BR>ascertain fully.<BR>--2 To recognize,<BR>acknowledge. --Caus. To order,<BR>command.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाज्ञा
समाज्ञा Fame, reputation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादा
समादा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To take, receive,<BR>accept.<BR>--2 To take hold of, seize,<BR>grasp.<BR>--3 To bestow, give,<BR>present.<BR>--4 To restore, return.<BR>--5 To<BR>take off or away.<BR>--6 To apprehend,<BR>comprehend.<BR>--7 To undertake,<BR>begin.<BR>--8 To collect.<BR>--9 To think<BR>about, reflect on.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादानं|समादान
समादानं<BR>1 Receiving fully.<BR>--2<BR>Receiving suitable gifts.<BR>--3 The daily<BR>observances of the Jaina sect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादिश्
समादिश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To point out,<BR>indicate.<BR>--2 To inform, tell,<BR>communicate.<BR>--3 To proclaim,<BR>announce.<BR>--4 To foretell.<BR>--5 To<BR>order, command, direct.<BR>--6 To<BR>appoint, depute, entrust with.<BR>--7<BR>To assign, allot.<BR>--8 To determine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समादेशः|समादेश
समादेशः Command, order,<BR>direction, instruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधा
समाधा {c3c} U.<BR>1 To place or put<BR>together, join, unite.<BR>--2 To place,<BR>put, put or place upon, apply to;<BR>पदं मूर्ध्नि समाधत्ते केसरी मत्तदंतिनः<BR>Pt. 1. 327.<BR>--3 To install, place on the<BR>throne; R. 17. 8.<BR>--4 To compose,<BR>collect (as the mind); मनः<BR>समाधाय निवृत्तशोकः Rām.; न शशाक<BR>समाधातुं मनो मदनवेपितं Bhāg.<BR>--5 To<BR>concentrate, fix or apply intently<BR>upon (as the eye, mind &c.);<BR>Bg. 12. 9; Bh. 3. 48.<BR>--6 To satisfy,<BR>clear or solve (a doubt), answer<BR>an objection; इति समाधत्ते (in<BR>commentaries).<BR>--7 To repair, redress,<BR>set right, remove; न ते शक्याः<BR>समाधातुं H. 3. 37; उत्पन्नामापदं यस्तु<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-b" target="_blank">Page1096-b+ 57</a>]<BR>समाधत्ते स बुद्धिमान् 4. 7.<BR>--8 To think<BR>over; Bk. 12. 6.<BR>--9 To entrust,<BR>commit to, deliver over.<BR>--10 To<BR>produce, effect, accomplish.<BR>--11<BR>To place a burden, load.<BR>--12 To<BR>assume, take upon oneself.<BR>--13 To<BR>conceive (in the womb).<BR>--14 To<BR>establish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधा
समाधा See समाधान below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधानं|समाधान
समाधानं<BR>1 Putting together,<BR>uniting.<BR>--2 Fixing the mind in<BR>abstract contemplation on the true<BR>nature of spirit.<BR>--3 Profound or<BR>abstract meditation, deep<BR>contemplation.<BR>--4 Intentness.<BR>--5<BR>Steadiness, composure, peace (as of mind),<BR>satisfaction; चित्तस्य समाधानं, बुद्धेः<BR>समाधानं G. L. 18.<BR>--6 Clearing up<BR>a doubt, replying to the<BR>Pūrvapakṣa; answering an objection.<BR>--7<BR>Agreeing, promising.<BR>--8 (In<BR>dramas) A leading incident which<BR>unexpectedly gives rise to the<BR>whole plot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिः|समाधि
समाधिः<BR>1 Collecting, composing,<BR>concentrating (as mind).<BR>--2<BR>Profound or abstract meditation,<BR>concentration of mind on one object,<BR>perfect absorption of thought into<BR>the one object of meditation, i. e.<BR>the Supreme Spirit, (the 8th and<BR>last stage of Yoga); आत्मेश्वराणां न<BR>हि जातु विघ्नाः समाधिभेदप्रभवो भवंति<BR>Ku. 3. 40, 50; Mk. 1. 1.;<BR>Bh. 3. 54; R. 8. 79; Śi. 4. 55.<BR>--3 Intentness, concentration (in<BR>general), fixing of thoughts; तस्यां<BR>लग्नसमाधि (मानसं) Gīt. 3.<BR>--4<BR>Penance, religious obligation,<BR>devotion (to penance);<BR>अस्त्येत्समाधिभीरुत्वं देवानां Ś. 1; तपःसमाधि<BR>Ku. 3. 24; अथोपयंतारमलं समाधिना<BR>5. 24, 5. 6; 1. 59.<BR>--5 Bringing<BR>together, concentration,<BR>combination, collection; तं वेधा विदधे नूनं<BR>महाभूतसमाधिना R. 1. 29.<BR>--6<BR>Reconciliation, settling or composing<BR>differences.<BR>--7 Silence.<BR>--8<BR>Agreement, assent, promise.<BR>--9<BR>Requital.<BR>--10 Completion,<BR>accomplishment.<BR>--11 Perseverance in<BR>extreme difficulties.<BR>--12 Attempting<BR>impossibilities.<BR>--13 Laying up corn<BR>(in times of famine), storing<BR>grain.<BR>--14 A tomb.<BR>--15 The joint<BR>of the neck; a particular position<BR>of the neck; Ki. 16. 21.<BR>--16 (In<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-c" target="_blank">Page1096-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Rhet.) A figure of speech thus<BR>defined by Mammaṭa; समाधिः सुकरं<BR>कार्यं कारणांतरयोगतः K. P. 10; see<BR>S. D. 614.<BR>--17 One of the ten<BR>Guṇas or merits of style; see<BR>Kāv. 1. 93.<BR>--18 A religious vow or<BR>self-imposed restraint.<BR>--19 Support,<BR>upholding.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भंगः<BR>interruption of meditation.<BR>--स्थ a.<BR>absorbed in meditation or<BR>contemplation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिन्
समाधिन्, समाधिमत् a.<BR>1 Meditating.<BR>--2 Devout, pious; Ku. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाधिमत्|समाधिमन्त्
समाधिन्, समाधिमत् a.<BR>1 Meditating.<BR>--2 Devout, pious; Ku. 1. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाध्मात
समाध्मात p. p.<BR>1 Blown into.<BR>--2 Elated, puffed up, inflated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समान|समानं|समानः
समान a.<BR>1 Same, equal, like,<BR>similar; समानशीलव्यसनेषु सख्यं<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 One, uniform.<BR>--3<BR>Good, virtuous, just.<BR>--4<BR>Common, general.<BR>--5 Honoured.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A friend, an equal.<BR>--2 One of the<BR>five life-winds or vital airs, which<BR>has its seat in the cavity of the<BR>navel and is essential to digestion.<BR>--3 A letter having the same organ<BR>of utterance.<BR>--नं ind. Equally with,<BR>like (with instr.); जलधरणे<BR>समानमुमापतिः Ki. 18. 4.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षरं N. of the vowels अ, आ, इ, ई, उ,<BR>ऊ, ऋ, ॠ, and ऌ (opp. संध्यक्षर).<BR>--अधिकरण a. {1} having a common<BR>substratum. {2} being in the same<BR>category or predicament. {3} being<BR>in the same case-relation or<BR>government (in gram.); तत्पुरुषः<BR>समानाधिकरणः कर्मधारयः P. I. 2. 42.<BR>--(णं) {1} same location or<BR>predicament. {2} agreement in case,<BR>apposition. {3} a predicament<BR>including several things, a generic<BR>property. {4} common government.<BR>--अधिकारः generic characteristic.<BR>--अर्थ a. having the same meaning,<BR>synonymous.<BR>--उदकः a relative<BR>connected by the libations of water to<BR>the Manes of common ancestors;<BR>this relationship extends from the<BR>seventh (or eleventh) to the<BR>thirteenth (or fourteenth according<BR>to some) degree; समानोदकभावस्तु<BR>निवर्तेताचतुर्दशात्; see Ms. 5. 60 also.<BR>--उदर्यः a brother of whole blood,<BR>uterine brother.<BR>--उपमा a kind of<BR>Upamā; see Kāv. 2. 29.<BR>--काल,<BR>--कालीन a. synchronous.<BR>--गोत्र = सगोत्र<BR>q. v.<BR>--दुःख a. sympathiser.<BR>--धर्मन् a.<BR>possessed of the same qualities,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">Page1097-a+ 57</a>]<BR>sympathising, appreciator of merits;<BR>Māl. 1. 6.<BR>--यमः the same pitch of voice.<BR>--वयस् a. of the same age.<BR>--रुचि<BR>a. agreeing in tastes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1096-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयति
समानयति Den. P. To make equal,<BR>equalise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानी
समानी {c1c} P.<BR>1 To join, unite,<BR>bring together; हस्नौ समानीय R. 2. 64;<BR>Ś. 5. 15.<BR>--2 To fetch, bring;<BR>R. 12. 78.<BR>--3 To collect, assemble.<BR>--4 To<BR>bring or offer an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समानयनं|समानयन
समानयनं Bringing together,<BR>collecting, conducting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्
समाप् {c5c} P.<BR>1 To obtain, get.<BR>--2<BR>To accomplish, fulfil.<BR>--3 To finish,<BR>complete; यावतैषां समाप्येरन् यज्ञाः<BR>पर्याप्तदक्षिणाः R. 17. 17, 24; समाप्य<BR>सांध्यं च विधिं 2. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापः|समाप
समापः Offering sacrifices or<BR>oblations to the gods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापक|समापकः
समापक a. (पिका f.) Finishing,<BR>accomplishing, fulfilling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापनं|समापन
समापनं<BR>1 Completion, conclusion,<BR>bringing to an end; Ms. 5. 88.<BR>--2<BR>Acquisition.<BR>--3 Killing, destroying.<BR>--4 A section, chapter.<BR>--5 Profound<BR>meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्त|समाप्तः
समाप्त p. p.<BR>1 Finished,<BR>concluded, completed.<BR>--2 Clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्तिः|समाप्ति
समाप्तिः f.<BR>1 End, conclusion,<BR>completion, termination.<BR>--2<BR>Accomplishment, fulfilment, perfection.<BR>--3<BR>Reconciling or settling differences,<BR>making up quarrels.<BR>--4 Perfection,<BR>development; Ku. 3. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्तिक|समाप्तिकः
समाप्तिक a.<BR>1 Final, concluding.<BR>--2 Finite.<BR>--3 One who has finished<BR>the whole of anything.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>finisher.<BR>--2 One who has completed<BR>the whole course of holy studies<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापद्
समापद् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To get, obtain,<BR>attain to.<BR>--2 To take place, happen,<BR>occur.<BR>--3 To fall upon, attack.<BR>--4<BR>To undergo.<BR>--5 To begin.<BR>--6 To be<BR>finished or ended.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापत्तिः|समापत्ति
समापत्तिः f.<BR>1 Meeting,<BR>encountering.<BR>--2 Accident, chance, accidental<BR>encounter; समापत्तिदृष्टेन केशिना<BR>दानवेन V. 1; M. 4;<BR>क्रियासमापात्तिनिवर्तितानि R. 7. 23; Ku. 7. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापन्न|समापन्नं
समापन्न p. p.<BR>1 Attained,<BR>obtained.<BR>--2 Occurred, happened.<BR>--3<BR>Come, arrived.<BR>--4 Finished,<BR>completed, accomplished.<BR>--5 Proficient.<BR>--6 Endowed with.<BR>--7 Distressed,<BR>afflicted.<BR>--8 Killed.<BR>--ग्नं End,<BR>completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापादनं|समापादन
समापादनं Accomplishing, restoring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समापाद्यं|समापाद्य
समापाद्यं The change of a Visarga<BR>to स् or ष्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्तालः|समाप्ताल
समाप्तालः A lord, husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाप्लुत
समाप्लुत p. p.<BR>1 Flooded,<BR>inundated.<BR>--2 Filled with.<BR>--3 Bathed in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाभाषणं|समाभाषण
समाभाषणं Conversation,<BR>talking with; R. 6. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्ना
समाम्ना {c1c} P.<BR>1 To repeat, recite.<BR>--2 To lay down, prescribe; तं हि धर्मं<BR>सूत्रकाराः समामनंति U. 4.<BR>--3 To<BR>repeat or hand down traditionally.<BR>--4 To enumerate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्नानं|समाम्नान
समाम्नानं<BR>1 Repetition, mention.<BR>--2 Enumeration.<BR>--3 Traditional<BR>repetition or mention.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाम्नायः|समाम्नाय
समाम्नायः<BR>1 Traditional repetition<BR>or mention, handing down<BR>traditionally.<BR>--2 A traditional<BR>collection (of words &c.); अश्व इति<BR>पशुसमाम्नाये पठ्यते U. 4.<BR>--3<BR>Tradition, repetition (in general).<BR>--4<BR>Reading, recitation, enumeration.<BR>--5 Totality, an aggregate, a<BR>collection; अक्षरसमाम्नायं Śik. 57; (i. e.<BR>the latters from अ to इ which are<BR>said to have been revealed by Śiva<BR>to Pāṇini).<BR>--6 An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायः|समाय
समायः<BR>1 Arrival, coming.<BR>--2<BR>A visit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायत
समायत p. p. Drawn out,<BR>extended, lengthened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायुज्
समायुज् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To join<BR>together, unite, connect.<BR>--2 To pro<BR>vide with, furnish, supply.<BR>--3 To<BR>make ready, prepare; see समायुक्त.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायुक्त
समायुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Joined,<BR>connected, united.<BR>--2 Intent on, devoted<BR>to.<BR>--3 Made ready, prepared.<BR>--4<BR>Endowed or furnished with, filled<BR>with, provided, supplied.<BR>--5<BR>Charged, appointed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायोगः|समायोग
समायोगः<BR>1 Union, connection,<BR>conjunction.<BR>--2 Preparation.<BR>--3<BR>Fitting (an arrow).<BR>--4 A collection,<BR>heap, multitude.<BR>--5 A cause,<BR>motive, object.<BR>--6 Association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समायुत
समायुत p. p.<BR>1 Connected or<BR>united together, joined.<BR>--2<BR>Collected, brought together.<BR>--3 Endowed<BR>or furnished with, having,<BR>possessed of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारभ्
समारभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To begin,<BR>undertake.<BR>--2 To try to propitiate, win<BR>over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारंभः|समारम्भ|समारंभ|समारम्भः
समारंभः<BR>1 Beginning,<BR>commencement.<BR>--2 An enterprise,<BR>undertaking, a work, an action; भव्यमुख्याः<BR>समारंभाः… तस्य गूढं विपेचिरे R. 17. 53;<BR>Bg. 4. 19.<BR>--3 An unguent; see<BR>समालंभ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाराधनं|समाराधन
समाराधनं<BR>1 A means of<BR>satisfying, gratification, delight; नाट्यं<BR>भिन्नरुचेर्जतस्य बहुधाप्येकं समाराधनं<BR>M. 1. 4.<BR>--2 Attendance, service;<BR>R. 2. 5, 18. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारुह्
समारुह् {c1c} P.<BR>1 (a) To ascend<BR>or mount on; ride. (b) To ascend,<BR>rise.<BR>--2 To undertake^1, engage in.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to rise or<BR>mount, raise, lift up.<BR>--2 To string<BR>(as a bow).<BR>--3 To plant.<BR>--4 To<BR>ascribe, attribute.<BR>--5 To hand or<BR>deliver over to.<BR>--6 To display,<BR>exhibit, show forth.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोपणं|समारोपण
समारोपणं<BR>1 Depositing, placing<BR>in or upon.<BR>--2 Delivering over,<BR>consigning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोपित
समारोपित p. p.<BR>1 Caused to mount<BR>or ascend.<BR>--2 Strung (as a bow),<BR>भवता चापे समारोपिते K. P. 10.<BR>--3<BR>Deposited, planted, lodged.<BR>--4<BR>Consigned, delivered over.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समारोहः|समारोह
समारोहः<BR>1 Ascending, mounting.<BR>--2 Riding upon.<BR>--3 Agreeing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालभ्
समालभ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To take hold<BR>of, seize.<BR>--2 To anoint, smear<BR>over.<BR>--3 To handle, touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालंभः|समालम्भ|समालंभ|समालम्भः
समालंभः, समालंभनं<BR>1 Taking hold<BR>of, seizing.<BR>--2 Seizing a victim for<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--3 Smearing the body with<BR>unguents or coloured cosmetics;<BR>मंगलसमालंभनं विरचयावः Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालंभनं|समालम्भन|समालंभन|समालम्भनं
समालंभः, समालंभनं<BR>1 Taking hold<BR>of, seizing.<BR>--2 Seizing a victim for<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--3 Smearing the body with<BR>unguents or coloured cosmetics;<BR>मंगलसमालंभनं विरचयावः Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालंब्|समालम्ब्
समालंब् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To lay or catch<BR>hold of, seize; Ku. 5. 84.<BR>--2 To<BR>rest or depend on, be supported by;<BR>to cling or adhere to.<BR>--3 To devote<BR>or give oneself up to.<BR>--4 To assume,<BR>maintain.<BR>--5 To settle down or<BR>abide in.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालंबनं|समालम्बन
समालंबनं Resting on, clinging to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालंबिन्|समालम्बिन्
समालंबिन् a. Clinging to.<BR>--नी A<BR>kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समालापः|समालाप
समालापः Conversation, talking<BR>with; Pt. 1. 388.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावस्
समावस् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To dwell, live.<BR>--2 To lodge, encamp, halt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावासः|समावास
समावासः<BR>1 A residence,<BR>habitation, dwelling-place.<BR>--2<BR>Haltingplace, encampment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावायः|समावाय
समावायः<BR>1 Association,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">Page1098-a+ 57</a>]<BR>connection.<BR>--2 Inseparable connection;<BR>see समवाय.<BR>--3 Aggregation.<BR>--4 A<BR>multitude, number, heap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1097-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविश्
समाविश् {c6c} P.<BR>1 To enter;<BR>Bk.8. 27.<BR>--2 To go to, approach.<BR>--3<BR>To be devoted to, be intent on.<BR>--4<BR>To pervade, occupy, fill.<BR>--5 To sit<BR>down, settle down.<BR>--6 To overcome.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To cause to enter in,<BR>insert.<BR>--2 To contain, comprise, hold.<BR>--3 To place or fix in or upon.<BR>--4<BR>To entrust, assign; Pt. 1. 85.<BR>--5<BR>To conduct, lead into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाविष्ट
समाविष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Entered<BR>thoroughly, completely occupied,<BR>pervaded.<BR>--2 Seized, overcome,<BR>engrossed.<BR>--3 Possessed by an evil spirit.<BR>--4 Endowed with.<BR>--5 Settled,<BR>fixed, seated.<BR>--6 Well-instructed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावेशः|समावेश
समावेशः<BR>1 Entering or abiding<BR>together.<BR>--2 Meeting, association.<BR>--3 Inclusion, comprehension.<BR>--4<BR>Penetration.<BR>--5 Possession by an<BR>evil spirit.<BR>--6 Passion, emotion.<BR>--7<BR>(In gram.) Common applicability<BR>of a term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृ
समावृ {c5c} U.<BR>1 To cover all over<BR>or completely.<BR>--2 To surround,<BR>envelope.<BR>--3 To conceal, hide.<BR>--4 To<BR>shut, close.<BR>--5 To obstruct, hinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत|समावृतः
समावृत p. p.<BR>1 Encompassed,<BR>surrounded, enclosed, beset.<BR>--2 Screened,<BR>veiled.<BR>--3 Hidden, concealed.<BR>--4<BR>Protected.<BR>--5 Shut out, excluded.<BR>--6<BR>Stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्
समावृत् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To approach.<BR>--2<BR>To return (as a Brāhmaṇa after<BR>completing his ब्रह्मचर्यव्रत or course<BR>of religious studies).<BR>--3 To come<BR>together, assemble.<BR>--4 To turn out<BR>well, succeed.<BR>--5 To come to an end,<BR>be completed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावर्तनं|समावर्तन|समावर्त्तन|समावर्त्तनं
समावर्तनं<BR>1 Return.<BR>--2 Especially,<BR>a pupil's return home after<BR>finishing his course of holy study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्तः|समावृत्त
समावृत्तः, समावृत्तकः A pupil who<BR>has returned home after finishing<BR>his course of holy study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्तकः|समावृत्तक
समावृत्तः, समावृत्तकः A pupil who<BR>has returned home after finishing<BR>his course of holy study.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समावृत्तिः|समावृत्ति
समावृत्तिः f.<BR>1 Return.<BR>--2<BR>Completion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रि
समाश्रि {c1c} U.<BR>1 To go to for<BR>protection, fly for refuge.<BR>--2 To<BR>suffer, experience, or enjoy;<BR>Pt. 1. 372.<BR>--3 To observe, practise, follow.<BR>--4 To rest or depend on.<BR>--5 To<BR>confide in.<BR>--6 To attain to, obtain,<BR>assume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्रयः|समाश्रय
समाश्रयः<BR>1 Seeking protection or<BR>shelter.<BR>--2 Refuge, shelter,<BR>protection.<BR>--3 A place of refuge,<BR>asylum, resting or dwelling-place.<BR>--4 Dwelling, residence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्लेषः|समाश्लेष
समाश्लेषः A close embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वस्
समाश्वस् {c2c} P.<BR>1 To take courage,<BR>take heart, calm or compose<BR>oneself.<BR>--2 To regain confidence.<BR>--3<BR>To believe in. --Caus. To console,<BR>encourage, cheer up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वासः|समाश्वास
समाश्वासः<BR>1 Recovering breath,<BR>breathing a sigh of relief.<BR>--2<BR>Relief, encouragement, consolation.<BR>--3 Trust, confidence, belief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाश्वासनं|समाश्वासन
समाश्वासनं<BR>1 Reviving,<BR>encouraging, comforting.<BR>--2 Consolation;<BR>V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासः|समास
समासः<BR>1 Aggregation, union,<BR>composition.<BR>--2 Composition of<BR>words, a compound; (the principal<BR>kinds of compounds are four:--द्वंद्व,<BR>तत्पुरुष, बहुव्रीहि, and अव्ययीभाव q. q. v.<BR>v.).<BR>--3 Reconciliation,<BR>composition of differences.<BR>--4 A collection,<BR>an assemblage.<BR>--5 Whole, totality.<BR>--6 Contraction, conciseness,<BR>brevity.<BR>--7 Euphonic combination<BR>(संधि). (समासेन, समासतः means<BR>‘in short’, ‘briefly’, ‘succinctly’;<BR>एषा धर्मस्य वो योनिः समासेन प्रकीर्तिता<BR>Ms. 2. 25, 3. 20; Bg. 13. 18;<BR>समासतः श्रूयतां V. 2).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्याहारः supplying an ellipsis in a<BR>compound.<BR>--अर्था a part of a stanza<BR>proposed to be completed (= समस्या<BR>q. v.)<BR>--उक्तिः f. a figure of<BR>speech thus defined by Mammaṭa:<BR>--परोक्तिर्भेदकैः श्लिष्टैः समासोक्तिः K. P. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासंज्|समासञ्ज्
समासंज् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To join, attach<BR>or fix to.<BR>--2 To fix or place on,<BR>impose upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासक्त|समासक्तः
समासक्त p. p.<BR>1 Attached to;<BR>fixed or placed in.<BR>--2 United,<BR>combined.<BR>--3 Reached, attained.<BR>--4<BR>Affected by.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासक्तिः|समासक्ति
समासक्तिः f., समासंगः<BR>1 Union,<BR>adhering together, attachment.<BR>--2<BR>Comprehension, inclusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासंजनं|समासञ्जन|समासंजन|समासञ्जनं
समासंजनं<BR>1 Joining, uniting.<BR>--2<BR>Fixing or placing on.<BR>--3 Contact,<BR>combination, connection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासर्जनं|समासर्जन
समासर्जनं<BR>1 Abandoning<BR>completely.<BR>--2 Consigning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासद्
समासद् {c10c} U.<BR>1 To get, obtain,<BR>find, meet with.<BR>--2 To overtake;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">Page1098-c+ 56</a>]<BR>V. 1.<BR>--3 To assail, attack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समासादनं|समासादन
समासादनं<BR>1 Approaching.<BR>--2<BR>Finding, meeting with, obtaining.<BR>--3 Accomplishing, effecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृ
समाहृ {c1c} P.<BR>1 To bring, convey,<BR>carry; सर्व एव समाहारि तदा शैलः<BR>सहौषधिः Bk. 15. 107.<BR>--2 To collect'<BR>bring together, convene; तत्र<BR>स्वयंवरसमाहृतराजलोकं R. 5. 64;<BR>Bk. 8. 63.<BR>--3 To draw, attract.<BR>--4 To<BR>destroy, annihilate; Bg. 11. 32.<BR>--5<BR>To complete (as a sacrifice).<BR>--6<BR>To return, restore to one's proper<BR>place; Ms. 8. 319.<BR>--7 To curb,<BR>restrain.<BR>--8 To offer.<BR>--9 To<BR>contract, abridge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहरणं|समाहरण
समाहरणं Uniting, collecting,<BR>combining, accumulating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहर्तृ
समाहर्तृ m.<BR>1 One who is<BR>accustomed to collect or get together.<BR>--2 A collector (as of taxes).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहारः|समाहार
समाहारः<BR>1 A collection, an<BR>aggregate, assemblage; Māl. 9.<BR>--2<BR>Composition of words.<BR>--3 Conjunction<BR>of words or sentences.<BR>--4 A<BR>subdivision of Dvandva and Dvigu<BR>compounds, expressing an<BR>aggregate.<BR>--5 Abridgment, contraction,<BR>conciseness^1.<BR>--6 Combination of two<BR>letters of the alphabet into a<BR>syllable (= प्रत्याहार q. v.).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृत|समाहृतः
समाहृत p. p.<BR>1 Brought together,<BR>collected, accumulated.<BR>--2<BR>Abundant, excessive, much.<BR>--3 Received,<BR>accepted, taken.<BR>--4 Abridged,<BR>curtailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहृतिः|समाहृति
समाहृतिः f. Compilation,<BR>abridgment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाहित|समाहितः
समाहित p. p.<BR>1 Brought<BR>together, assembled.<BR>--2 Adjusted,<BR>settled.<BR>--3 Composed, collected,<BR>calm (as mind.).<BR>--4 Intent on,<BR>absorbed in, concentrated.<BR>--5<BR>Finished.<BR>--6 Agreed upon.<BR>--7 Arranged,<BR>disposed.<BR>--8 Inferred.<BR>--9<BR>Accomplished, finished.<BR>--10 Deposited,<BR>entrusted; see समाधा also.<BR>--तः A<BR>holy man.<BR>--तं Intentness, intent<BR>devotion (to any object).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वे
समाह्वे {c1c} P.<BR>1 To call together,<BR>convoke.<BR>--2 To challenge, provoke<BR>to battle.<BR>--3 To invite.<BR>--4 To call,<BR>name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वः|समाह्व
समाह्वः Challenge, defiance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वयः|समाह्वय
समाह्वयः<BR>1 Calling out,<BR>challenging.<BR>--2 War, battle.<BR>--3 A single<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1099-a" target="_blank">Page1099-a+ 55</a>]<BR>combat.<BR>--4 Setting animals to fight<BR>for sport, betting with living<BR>creatures; Y. 2. 203; Ms. 9. 221.<BR>--5 A<BR>name, an appellation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1098-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वा
समाह्वा A name, an appellation;<BR>Śi. 11. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समाह्वानं|समाह्वान
समाह्वानं<BR>1 Calling together,<BR>convocation.<BR>--2 Challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समि
समि {c2c} P.<BR>1 To come or meet<BR>together, be united or joined with.<BR>--2 To go or come to, arrive at,<BR>approach, reach, visit, attain.<BR>--3 To<BR>encounter, meet in a hostile manner.<BR>--4 To cohabit, have sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR>--5 To enter upon, commence.<BR>--6 To agree with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समित्
समित् f. War, battle; समिति<BR>पतिनिपाताकर्णन &c. N. 12. 75.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समित
समित p. p.<BR>1 Come together, met.<BR>--2 Collected, assembled.<BR>--3<BR>Connected, united with.<BR>--4 Contiguous.<BR>--5 Parallel.<BR>--6 Promised, agreed<BR>to.<BR>--7 Completed, finished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समितिः|समिति
समितिः f.<BR>1 Meeting, union,<BR>association.<BR>--2 An assembly.<BR>--3 Flock,<BR>herd; Ki. 4. 32.<BR>--4 War, battle;<BR>Ś. 2. 15; Ki. 3. 15; Śi. 16. 13.<BR>--5 Likeness, equality.<BR>--6<BR>Moderation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समितिंजय
समितिंजय a. Victorious in<BR>battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1099-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समिथः|समिथ
