संप्री|सम्प्री
संप्री {c4c} A. To be completely<BR>pleased or satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रीतिः|सम्प्रीति|संप्रीति
संप्रीतिः f.<BR>1 Attachment, affection.<BR>--2 Friendly assent.<BR>--3 Delight, joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रेक्ष्|सम्प्रेक्ष्
संप्रेक्ष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To observe<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">Page1104-b+ 54</a>]<BR>carefully, mark, perceive.<BR>--2 To consider<BR>carefully, investigate, inquire into.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रेक्षणं|सम्प्रेक्षण|संप्रेक्षण
संप्रेक्षणं<BR>1 Observing, beholding.<BR>--2 Considering, investigating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रेष्|सम्प्रेष्
संप्रेष् Caus.<BR>1 To send, despatch,<BR>dismiss.<BR>--2 To send a message^1 to.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रैषः|सम्प्रैष|संप्रैष|सम्प्रैषः
संप्रैषः<BR>1 Sending away,<BR>dismissing.<BR>--2 Direction, command, order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्रोक्षणं|सम्प्रोक्षण|संप्रोक्षण
संप्रोक्षणं Sprinkling over,<BR>consecration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्लु|सम्प्लु
संप्लु {c1c} A.<BR>1 To fluctuate, float<BR>about.<BR>--2 To flow together, meet<BR>(as waters); Bg. 2. 46; U. 4. 8.<BR>--Caus. To inundate, flood over,<BR>submerge, deluge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संप्लवः|सम्प्लव|संप्लव
संप्लवः<BR>1 Submersion, inundation.<BR>--2 Surge.<BR>--3 Flood.<BR>--4 Falling<BR>into ruin.<BR>--5 Subversion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संफालः|सम्फाल|संफाल|सम्फालः
संफालः A ram, sheep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संफुल्ल|सम्फुल्ल|सम्फुल्लः
संफुल्ल a. Full-blown, blossomed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संफेटः|सम्फेट|संफेट
संफेटः An angry or tumultuous<BR>conflict, an incident describing the<BR>mutual encounter of angry persons;<BR>see S. D. 379, 420; e. g. the<BR>encounter between माधा and अघोरघंट.<BR>in Māl. act {5}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संब्|सम्ब्
संब् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (संबति) To go,<BR>move. {vII.v} {c10c} U. (संबयति-ते) To<BR>collect, accumulate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबं|सम्ब|संब|सम्बं
संबं<BR>1 The second ploughing of a<BR>field; (संबाकृ to plough twice); see<BR>शंब also.<BR>--2 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबंध्|सम्बन्ध्|संबन्ध्
संबंध् {c9c} P.<BR>1 To bind or tie<BR>together, unite, join, connect, attach.<BR>--2 To make, construct, form.<BR>--Pass.<BR>1 To be connected with,<BR>go with, belong to.<BR>--2 To be<BR>furnished or supplied with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबद्ध|सम्बद्ध|सम्बद्धः
संबद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Bound or fastened<BR>together.<BR>--2 Attached to.<BR>--3<BR>Connected with, related to, belonging<BR>to.<BR>--4 Endowed with.<BR>--5<BR>Connected in sense.<BR>--6 Closed, shut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबंध|सम्बन्ध|संबन्ध|संबन्धः|सम्बन्धः
संबंध a.<BR>1 Able, capable.<BR>--2 Fit,<BR>proper, right.<BR>--धः<BR>1 Connection, union,<BR>association.<BR>--2 Relation,<BR>relationship.<BR>--3 Relation, as the meaning<BR>of the genitive case.<BR>--4<BR>Matrimonial alliance; Ku. 6. 29, 30;<BR>U. 1. 17.<BR>--5 Friendly connection,<BR>friendship; संबंधमाभाषणपूर्वताहुः R. 2. 58.<BR>--6 Fitness, propriety.<BR>--7 Prosperity,<BR>success.<BR>--8 A relation, kinsman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबंधक|सम्बन्धक|संबन्धक|संबन्धकः
संबंधक a.<BR>1 Relating, concerning.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">Page1104-c+ 56</a>]<BR>--2 Fit, suitable.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A friend.<BR>--2 A relation by birth or<BR>marriage.<BR>--3 A kind of peace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबंधिन्|सम्बन्धिन्|संबन्धिन्
संबंधिन् a.<BR>1 Relating or belonging<BR>to.<BR>--2 Connected with, serving as<BR>an adjunct, inherent.<BR>--3<BR>Possessing good qualities. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>relation by marriage; U. 4. 9.<BR>--2<BR>A relation, kinsman (in general).<BR>U. 1. 16; R. 2. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबरः|सम्बर|संबर|सम्बरं|सम्बरः
संबरः<BR>1 A dam, bridge.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of deer.<BR>--3 N. of a demon<BR>slain by Pradyumna; see शंबर and<BR>प्रद्युम्न.<BR>--4 N. of a mountain.<BR>--रं<BR>1<BR>Restraint.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--3 A kind<BR>of religious observance (with the<BR>Buddhists).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरिः, --रिपुः<BR>Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबलः|सम्बल|संबल|संबलं
संबलः --लं Provisions for a<BR>journey, viaticum.<BR>--लं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबलं|सम्बल|संबल|संबलः
संबलः --लं Provisions for a<BR>journey, viaticum.<BR>--लं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबाध्|सम्बाध्
संबाध् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To press heavily,<BR>to oppress, afflict, torment; injure,<BR>hurt.<BR>--2 To compress, contract.<BR>--3<BR>To block up, throng, crowd.<BR>--4<BR>To bind firmly together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबाध|सम्बाध|संबाधः|सम्बाधः
संबाध a. Thronged or crowded<BR>with, blocked up, narrow; संबाधं<BR>बृहदपि तद्बभूव वर्त्म Śi. 8. 2; व्योम्नि<BR>संबाधवर्त्मभिः R. 12. 67;<BR>अनेकसिद्धसाध्यसंबाधं K.<BR>--धः<BR>1 Being<BR>thronged with.<BR>--2 Pressing on, striking,<BR>hurting; स्तनसंबाधमुरो जघान च<BR>Ku. 4. 26.<BR>--3 Obstruction, difficulty,<BR>danger, impediment; Ki. 3. 53.<BR>--4 The road to hell.<BR>--5 Fear,<BR>dread.<BR>--6 The vulva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबाधनं|सम्बाधन|संबाधन|सम्बाधनं
संबाधनं<BR>1 Blocking up,<BR>obstructing.<BR>--2 Compressing.<BR>--3 A barrier,<BR>gate.<BR>--4 The vulva.<BR>--5 The point<BR>of a stake.<BR>--6 A doorkeeper (m. ?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबुध्|सम्बुध्
संबुध् {c1c} U., {c4c} A.<BR>1 To know,<BR>understand, learn; become aware of;<BR>Bk. 19. 30.<BR>--2 To perceive, observe,<BR>notice.<BR>--3 To wake up, rise from<BR>sleep. --Caus.<BR>1 To inform,<BR>acquaint with, give information about;<BR>तवागतिज्ञं समबोधयन्मां R. 13. 25.<BR>--2<BR>To address, call out to.<BR>--3 To<BR>instruct.<BR>--4 To admonish, advise.<BR>--5<BR>To wake up, rouse.<BR>--6 To explain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबुद्ध|सम्बुद्ध|संबुद्धः|सम्बुद्धः
संबुद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Well-understood.<BR>--2 Very wise or prudent.<BR>--3 Wide<BR>awake.<BR>--द्धः A Buddha or Jaina<BR>deified saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबुद्धिः|सम्बुद्धि|संबुद्धि|सम्बुद्धिः
संबुद्धिः f.<BR>1 Perfect knowledge<BR>or perception.<BR>--2 Full<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">Page1105-a+ 55</a>]<BR>consciousness.<BR>--3 Calling to, addressing.<BR>--4<BR>(In gram.) The vocative case;<BR>एङ् ह्रस्वात्संबुद्धेः P. VI. 1. 69.<BR>--5 An<BR>epithet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1104-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबोधः|सम्बोध|संबोध|सम्बोधः
संबोधः<BR>1 Explaining, instructing,<BR>informing.<BR>--2 Full or correct<BR>perception.<BR>--3 Sending, throwing.<BR>--4 Loss, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संबोधनं|सम्बोधन|संबोधन|सम्बोधनं
संबोधनं<BR>1 Explaining.<BR>--2<BR>Addressing.<BR>--3 The vocative case.<BR>--4 An<BR>epithet (used in calling a person);<BR>Bv. 3. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभक्षः|सम्भक्ष|संभक्ष
संभक्षः<BR>1 Eating together.<BR>--2<BR>Food in common.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभज्|सम्भज्
संभज् {c1c} U.<BR>1 To divide,<BR>distribute, allot, apportion.<BR>--2 To<BR>possess, enjoy.<BR>--3 To bestow, grant.<BR>--4<BR>To favour, serve, help.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभक्त|सम्भक्त
संभक्त p. p.<BR>1 Divided, shared.<BR>--2<BR>Possessing, enjoying.<BR>--3 Faithful<BR>or attached to, devoted to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभक्तिः|सम्भक्ति|संभक्ति
संभक्तिः f.<BR>1 Sharing in,<BR>possessing.<BR>--2 Distributing.<BR>--3<BR>Favouring, honouring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभग्न|सम्भग्न|संभग्नः
संभग्न p. p. Shattered, dispersed.<BR>--ग्नः An epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभली|सम्भली
संभली A procuress; see शंभली.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभव्यः|सम्भव्य|संभव्य|सम्भव्यः
संभव्यः The wood-apple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभाष्|सम्भाष्
संभाष् {c1c} A.<BR>1 (a) To speak<BR>together, converse; Ms. 8. 55. (b)<BR>To say or speak in general.<BR>--2 To<BR>speak to, address.<BR>--3 To greet,<BR>salute.<BR>--4 To agree together, consent.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To converse with.<BR>--2 To<BR>persuade, prevail upon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभाषः|सम्भाष
संभाषः Conversation; Ms. 2. 195;<BR>8. 354.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभाषा|सम्भाषा
संभाषा, संभाषणं<BR>1 Discourse,<BR>conversation.<BR>--2 Greeting.<BR>--3<BR>Criminal connection.<BR>--4 An agreement,<BR>a contract.<BR>--5 A watch-word,<BR>warcry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभाषणं|सम्भाषण|संभाषण|सम्भाषणं
संभाषा, संभाषणं<BR>1 Discourse,<BR>conversation.<BR>--2 Greeting.<BR>--3<BR>Criminal connection.<BR>--4 An agreement,<BR>a contract.<BR>--5 A watch-word,<BR>warcry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभाषित|सम्भाषित
संभाषित p. p.<BR>1 Addressed.<BR>--2 Said,<BR>spoken.<BR>--तं Conversation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभिद्|सम्भिद्
संभिद् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To break or tear<BR>asunder, break to pieces.<BR>--2 To<BR>mingle, meet, combine, mix, join,<BR>bring together; अन्योन्नसंभिन्नट्टशां<BR>सखीनां Māl. 1. 33; Bk. 7. 5.<BR>--3 To<BR>contract, compress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभिन्न|सम्भिन्न|संभिन्नः|सम्भिन्नः
संभिन्न p. p.<BR>1 Completely broken.<BR>--2 Shattered, shaken, agitated.<BR>--3<BR>Combined or united with.<BR>--4 Fully<BR>blown or opened; Ve. 1. 1.<BR>--न्नः<BR>An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वृत्त a.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">Page1105-b+ 56</a>]<BR>one who has abandoned good<BR>conduct.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभेदः|सम्भेद|संभेद|सम्भेदः
संभेदः<BR>1 Breaking, splitting.<BR>--2<BR>Union, mixture, combination.<BR>आलोकतिमिरसंभेदः Māl. 10. 11;<BR>हर्षोद्वेगसंभेद उपनतः Māl. 8.<BR>--3 Meeting<BR>(as of glances).<BR>--4 Confluence,<BR>junction (of two rivers); तदुतिष्ठ<BR>पारासिंधुसंभेदमवगाह्य नगरीमेव प्रविशावः;<BR>अयमसौ महानद्योः संभेदः Māl. 4;<BR>मधुमतीसिंधुसंभेदपावनः 9.<BR>--5 Blossoming,<BR>opening.<BR>--6 Uniformity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभुज्|सम्भुज्
संभुज् {c7c} U.<BR>1 To eat.<BR>--2 To<BR>enjoy.<BR>--3 To enjoy carnally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभुक्त|सम्भुक्त
संभुक्त p. p.<BR>1 Eaten.<BR>--2 Well<BR>enjoyed.<BR>--3 Made use of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभोगः|सम्भोग|संभोग|सम्भोगः
संभोगः<BR>1 Enjoyment(in<BR>general), pleasure, delight;<BR>सत्संभोगफलाः श्रियः Subhāṣ.<BR>--2<BR>Possession, use, occupation;<BR>Ms. 8. 200.<BR>--3 Carnal enjoyment, sexual<BR>union, copulation; संभोगांते मम<BR>समुचितो हस्तसंवाहनानां Me. 96.<BR>--4 A<BR>lecher, catamite.<BR>--5 A sub-division<BR>of the sentiment of love; see<BR>under शृंगार.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभोगिन्|सम्भोगिन्
संभोगिन् a.<BR>1 Sensual.<BR>--2<BR>Employing, using. --m. A sensualist,<BR>libertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभोजकः|सम्भोजक|संभोजक
संभोजकः An eater, a taster.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभोजनं|सम्भोजन|संभोजन
संभोजनं Eating in company, a<BR>dinner-party.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभू|सम्भू
संभू {c1c} A.<BR>1 To arise, to be born<BR>or produced, spring up; कथमपि<BR>भुवनेऽस्मिंस्तादृशाः संभवंति Māl. 2. 9;<BR>धर्मसंस्थापनार्थाय संभवामि युगे युगे<BR>Bg. 4. 8; Ki. 5. 22; Bk. 6. 138;<BR>Ms. 8. 155.<BR>--2 To be, become, exist.<BR>--3<BR>To happen, occur, take place.<BR>--4<BR>To be possible.<BR>--5 To be adequate<BR>for, be competent for (with inf.);<BR>न यन्नियंतुं समभावि भानुना Śi. 1. 27.<BR>--6 To meet, be united or joined<BR>with; संभूयांभोधिमभ्येति महानद्या<BR>नगापगा Śi. 2. 100; संभूयेव सुखानि चेतसि<BR>Māl. 5. 9, 18.<BR>--7 To be consistent.<BR>--8<BR>To have sexual intercourse with.<BR>--9<BR>To be capable of existing in, be<BR>contained in. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>produce, effect, make.<BR>--2 To imagine,<BR>conceive, fancy, think.<BR>--3 To guess or<BR>conjecture; Ś. 2.<BR>--4 To consider,<BR>regard.<BR>--5 To honour, respect,<BR>esteem, show respect to; प्राप्तोऽसि<BR>संभावयितुं वनान्मां R. 5. 11; 7. 8.<BR>--6 To<BR>honour or present with, treat with;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">Page1105-c+ 57</a>]<BR>Ku. 3. 37.<BR>--7 To ascribe or impute<BR>to; Mk. 1. 36.<BR>--8 To come or<BR>go to, approach.<BR>--9 To take<BR>part in, enjoy; U. 4.<BR>--10 To<BR>greet, salute.<BR>--11 To manifest,<BR>exhibit.<BR>--12 To expect. --Pass. of<BR>caus. To be possible; कथमेतद्भवति<BR>संभाव्यते Ś. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभवः|सम्भव|संभव|सम्भवः
संभवः<BR>1 Birth, production,<BR>springing up, arising, existence; प्रियस्य<BR>सुहृदो यव मम तत्रैव संभवो भूयात्<BR>Māl. 9; मानुषीषु कथं वा स्यादस्य रूपस्य<BR>संभवः Ś. 1. 26; Bg. 3. 14; oft. at<BR>the end of comp. in this sense;<BR>अप्सरः संभवैषा Ś. 1.<BR>--2 Production and<BR>bringing up; Ms. 2. 227; (see<BR>Kull. thereon).<BR>--3 Cause, origin,<BR>motive.<BR>--4 Mixing, union,<BR>combination.<BR>--5 Possibility; संयोगो हि<BR>वियोगस्य संसूचयति संभवं Subhāṣ.<BR>--6 Compatibility, consistency.<BR>--7<BR>Adaptation, appropriateness.<BR>--8<BR>Agreement, conformity.<BR>--9 Capacity.<BR>--10 Equivalence (one of the<BR>Pramāṇas).<BR>--11 Acquaintance.<BR>--12 Loss, destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभावनं|सम्भावन|संभावन|सम्भावनं
संभावनं --ना<BR>1 Considering,<BR>reflecting; R. 5. 28.<BR>--2<BR>Fancying, supposition; संभावनमथोत्येक्षा<BR>प्रकृतस्य समेन यत् K. P. 10.<BR>--3 An<BR>idea, fancy, thought.<BR>--4 Respect,<BR>honour, esteem, regard;<BR>संभावनागुणमवेहि तमीश्वराणां Ś. 7. 4.<BR>--5<BR>Possibility.<BR>--6 Fitness, adequacy;<BR>Ki. 3. 39.<BR>--7 Competency, ability.<BR>--8<BR>Doubt.<BR>--9 Affection, love.<BR>--10<BR>Celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभावना
संभावनं --ना<BR>1 Considering,<BR>reflecting; R. 5. 28.<BR>--2<BR>Fancying, supposition; संभावनमथोत्येक्षा<BR>प्रकृतस्य समेन यत् K. P. 10.<BR>--3 An<BR>idea, fancy, thought.<BR>--4 Respect,<BR>honour, esteem, regard;<BR>संभावनागुणमवेहि तमीश्वराणां Ś. 7. 4.<BR>--5<BR>Possibility.<BR>--6 Fitness, adequacy;<BR>Ki. 3. 39.<BR>--7 Competency, ability.<BR>--8<BR>Doubt.<BR>--9 Affection, love.<BR>--10<BR>Celebrity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभावित|सम्भावित|सम्भावितः
संभावित p. p.<BR>1 Considered,<BR>supposed, imagined; पित्राहं दोषेषु<BR>संभावितः K.<BR>--2 Esteemed, honoured,<BR>respected; Bh. 2. 34; Ku. 3. 11.<BR>--3<BR>Respectable, honourable.<BR>--4 Suited,<BR>fitted, adequate, fit.<BR>--5 Possible.<BR>--6 Derived, produced, got;<BR>Māl. 5.<BR>--7 Satisfied.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभाव्य|सम्भाव्य
संभाव्य a.<BR>1 Probable, likely,<BR>possible.<BR>--2 To be expected or<BR>deemed probable.<BR>--3 Capable, suitable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभूत|सम्भूत|सम्भूतः
संभूत p. p.<BR>1 Born, produced.<BR>--2<BR>Formed or composed of.<BR>--3<BR>Combined or united with.<BR>--4 Adequate,<BR>equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभूतिः|सम्भूति|संभूति
संभूतिः f.<BR>1 Birth, origin,<BR>production; Ms. 2. 147.<BR>--2 Combination,<BR>union.<BR>--3 Fitness, suitability.<BR>--4<BR>Power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभूय|सम्भूय
संभूय ind.<BR>1 Coming or meeting<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-a" target="_blank">Page1106-a+ 56</a>]<BR>together.<BR>--2 Being united or<BR>combined, in company or concert.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारिन् a. a coadjutor or colleague.<BR>--समुत्थानं partnership in trade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1105-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभृ|सम्भृ
संभृ {c3c} U.<BR>1 To collect, hoard,<BR>place or bring together; त्यागाय<BR>संभृतार्थानां R. 1. 7; 5. 5; 8. 3;<BR>Bk. 6. 80.<BR>--2 To effect, produce, bring on,<BR>accomplish; सुरतश्रमसंभृतो मुखे (<BR>स्वेदलवः) R. 8. 51; Ki. 9. 49; Me. 115<BR>--3 To maintain, cherish, foster.<BR>--4<BR>To make ready, prepare; V. 5;<BR>R. 19. 54.<BR>--5 To give, offer, present.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभारः|सम्भार|संभार|सम्भारः
संभारः<BR>1 Bringing together,<BR>collecting.<BR>--2 Preparation,<BR>provisions, necessaries, requisites,<BR>apparatus, things requisite for any act;<BR>सविशेषमद्य पूजासंभारो मया<BR>संनिधापनीयः Māl. 5; R. 12. 4; V. 2.<BR>--3<BR>An ingredient, a constituent part.<BR>--4 Multitude, heap, quantity,<BR>assemblage; as in शस्त्रास्त्रसंभार.<BR>--5<BR>Fulness.<BR>--6 Wealth, affluence.<BR>--7 Maintenance, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभृत|सम्भृत|सम्भृतः
संभृत p. p.<BR>1 Brought together,<BR>collected, concentrated.<BR>--2 Got<BR>ready, prepared, provided,<BR>equipped.<BR>--3 Furnished or endowed with,<BR>possessed of.<BR>--4 Placed, deposited.<BR>--5 Full, complete, entire.<BR>--6<BR>Gained, obtained.<BR>--7 Carried, borne.<BR>--8<BR>Nourished.<BR>--9 Produced, caused.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभृतिः|सम्भृति|संभृति|सम्भृतिः
संभृतिः f.<BR>1 Collection.<BR>--2<BR>Preparation, equipment, provision.<BR>--3<BR>Fulness.<BR>--4 Support, maintenance,<BR>nourishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभ्रम्|सम्भ्रम्
संभ्रम् {c1c} {c4c} P.<BR>1 To roam, rove.<BR>--2 To be in error, be perplexed or<BR>confused, be bewildered. --Caus.<BR>To perplex, bewilder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभ्रमः|सम्भ्रम|संभ्रम|सम्भ्रमः
संभ्रमः<BR>1 Turning round, whirling,<BR>revolving.<BR>--2 Haste, hurry.<BR>--3<BR>Confusion, agitation, flurry;<BR>Ku. 3. 48.<BR>--4 Fear, alarm, fright;<BR>Ś. 1; Ki. 15. 2.<BR>--5 Error, mistake,<BR>ignorance.<BR>--6 Zeal, activity.<BR>--7<BR>Respect, reverence; गृहमुपगते<BR>संभ्रमविधिः Bh. 2. 64; तव वीर्यवतः<BR>कश्चिद्यद्यस्ति मयि संभ्रमः Rām.<BR>--8<BR>Uproar, tumult.<BR>--9 Ignorance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्वलित a. excited by<BR>agitation.<BR>--भृत् a. embarrassed,<BR>flurried.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संभ्रांत|सम्भ्रान्त|संभ्रान्त
संभ्रांत p. p.<BR>1 Whirled about.<BR>--2<BR>Flurried, agitated, perplexed,<BR>bewildered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमद्|सम्मद्
संमद् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be intoxicated.<BR>--2<BR>To rejoice, be glad. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>exhilarate, rejoice, put in good<BR>spirits.<BR>--2 To be completely<BR>intoxicated (Atm).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमत्त|सम्मत्त
संमत्त p. p.<BR>1 Completely drunk.<BR>--2 Overjoyed, enraptured.<BR>--3<BR>Rutting, being in rut, furious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमद|सम्मद|संमदः|सम्मदः
संमद a. Greatly delighted, happy,<BR>--दः Great joy, delight, happiness;<BR>Śi. 15. 77.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमादः|सम्माद|संमाद|सम्मादः
संमादः Intoxication, frenzy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमन्|सम्मन्
संमन् {c4c} A.<BR>1 To agree, concur,<BR>be of the same opinion.<BR>--2 To<BR>assent or consent to, approve of, like.<BR>--3 To think, suppose, regard.<BR>--4<BR>To sanction, authorize.<BR>--5 To<BR>esteem, honour, value highly;<BR>कच्चिदग्निमिवानाय्यं काले संप्रन्यसेऽतिथिं<BR>Bk. 6. 65; सममंस्त बंधूत् 1. 2.<BR>--6<BR>To allow, permit. --Caus.<BR>1 To<BR>honour, respect, value highly.<BR>--2 To<BR>consider, regard.<BR>--3 To instruct,<BR>teach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमत|सम्मत
संमत p. p.<BR>1 Agreed or consented<BR>to, approved of.<BR>--2 Liked, dear,<BR>beloved; R. 1. 28.<BR>--3 Like,<BR>resembling.<BR>--4 Regarded, considered,<BR>thought.<BR>--5 Highly respected,<BR>honoured, esteemed; Pt. 1. 56.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Agreement; see संमति.<BR>--2<BR>Impression, opinion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमतिः|सम्मति|संमति|सम्मतिः
संमतिः f.<BR>1 Agreement.<BR>--2<BR>Concurrence, assent, approbation,<BR>approval.<BR>--3 Wish, desire.<BR>--4<BR>Knowledge of self, knowledge of the soul,<BR>true knowledge.<BR>--5 Regard, respect,<BR>esteem; कथमिव तव संमतिर्भवित्रा<BR>सममृतुभिर्मुनिनावधीरितस्य Ki. 10. 36.<BR>--6 Love, affection.<BR>--7 Command,<BR>order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमानः|सम्मान|संमान|सम्मानः
संमानः Honour, respect.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>A measure.<BR>--2 Comparing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमाननं|सम्मानन|संमानन
संमाननं<BR>1 Honouring, worshipping.<BR>--2 Instructing, teaching.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमंत्र्|सम्मन्त्र्|संमन्त्र्
संमंत्र् {c10c} A.<BR>1 To consult or<BR>take counsel with; मम हृदयेन सह<BR>संमंत्रयोक्तवानसि Mu. 1.<BR>--2 To salute,<BR>greet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमंत्रणं
संमंत्रणं Consultation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमातुर|सम्मातुर
संमातुर = सन्मातुर q. v. under सत्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमा|सम्मा
संमा {c3c} A., {c2c} P.<BR>1 To measure.<BR>--2<BR>To make equal, equalize; see<BR>संमित.<BR>--3 To liken, compare.<BR>--4 To be<BR>comprised or contained in;<BR>मृणालसूत्रमपि ते न संमाति स्तनांतरे Subhāṣ.<BR>--5<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">Page1106-c+ 55</a>]<BR>To distribute, grant, bestow (Ved.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमित|सम्मित|संमितं|सम्मितः
संमित p. p.<BR>1 Meted, measured<BR>out.<BR>--2 Of equal measure, extent or<BR>value, equal, similar, like,<BR>resembling; कांतासंमिततयो पदेशयुजे<BR>K. P. 1; R. 3. 16.<BR>--3 As large as,<BR>reaching to.<BR>--4 Conformable,<BR>corresponding, commensurate.<BR>--5 Provided or<BR>furnished with.<BR>--6 Equalized,<BR>adapted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमिल्|सम्मिल्
संमिल् {c6c} P. To meet or come<BR>together, assemble.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमेलनं|सम्मेलन
संमेलनं<BR>1 Meeting together, union.<BR>--2 Mixture.<BR>--3 Assembling,<BR>collecting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमिश्र्|सम्मिश्र्
संमिश्र् See मिश्र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमिश्र|सम्मिश्र|सम्मिश्रः
संमिश्र, संमिश्रित a. Mixed together,<BR>intermixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमिश्रित|सम्मिश्रित
संमिश्र, संमिश्रित a. Mixed together,<BR>intermixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमिश्लः|सम्मिश्ल
संमिश्लः An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमील्|सम्मील्
संमील् {c1c} P.<BR>1 To shut the eyes.<BR>--2 To close up, contract (as flowers<BR>&c.); संमीलंति न<BR>तावद्बंधनकोषास्तयावचितपुष्पाः Ś. 3. 6. --Caus.<BR>1 To shut,<BR>close; उपांतसंमीलितलो चनो नृपः<BR>R. 3. 26; 13. 10.<BR>--2 To obscure, darken,<BR>make dim; विकारश्चैतन्यं भ्रमयति च<BR>संमीलयति च U. 1. 36.<BR>--3 To make<BR>insensible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमीलनं|सम्मीलन|संमीलन
संमीलनं Closing up(of a flower<BR>&c.), covering, enveloping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमुख|सम्मुख|सम्मुखः
संमुख a. (खा or खी f.), संमुखीन<BR>a.<BR>1 Facing, fronting, face to face,<BR>opposite, con fronting; कामं न तिष्ठति<BR>मदाननसंमुखी सा Ś. 1. 31; R. 15. 17;<BR>Śi. 10. 86.<BR>--2 Encountering,<BR>meeting.<BR>--3 Disposed to.<BR>--4 Looking or<BR>directed towards.<BR>--5 Propitious.<BR>--खं ind. In front of, opposite to,<BR>before, in the presence of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमुखिन्|सम्मुखिन्
संमुखिन् m. A mirror,<BR>lookingglass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमुर्च्छ्
संमुर्च्छ् {c1c} A.<BR>1 To faint, swoon.<BR>--2 To grow strong or powerful,<BR>gather strength, become intense;<BR>Ki. 5. 41.<BR>--3 To thicken; coagulate.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To form, fashion.<BR>--2 To<BR>stupefy, benumb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमूर्छनं|सम्मूर्छन|सम्मूर्च्छनं|संमूर्छन
संमूर्छनं<BR>1 Fainting, insensibility.<BR>--2 Congealing, becoming dense.<BR>--3<BR>Thickening, increasing.<BR>--4 Height.<BR>--5 Universal pervasion,<BR>co-extension, complete permeation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमुह्|सम्मुह्
संमुह् {c4c} P.<BR>1 To be perplexed.<BR>--2 To be foolish, infatuated, or<BR>unconscious. --Caus. To infatuate,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">Page1107-a+ 56</a>]<BR>stupefy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1106-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमुग्ध|सम्मुग्ध
संमुग्ध p. p.<BR>1 Stupefied.<BR>--2<BR>Bewildered.<BR>--3 Beautiful.<BR>--ग्धं ind.<BR>In a fascinating manner.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमूढ|सम्मूढ|सम्मूढः
संमूढ p. p.<BR>1 Stupefied,<BR>unconscious, senseless.<BR>--2 Infatuated, foolish.<BR>--3 Bewildered.<BR>--4 Disordered.<BR>--5<BR>Heaped, collected.<BR>--6 Produced<BR>rapidly.<BR>--7 Broken.<BR>--ढा A kind of<BR>riddle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमोहः|सम्मोह|संमोह
संमोहः<BR>1 Bewilderment, confusion,<BR>infatuation.<BR>--2 Insensibility, swoon.<BR>--3 Ignorance, folly.<BR>--4 Fascination.<BR>--5 Tumult, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमोहनं|सम्मोहन|संमोहन|संमोहनः
संमोहनं Fascinating, fascination.<BR>--नः N. of one of the five arrows<BR>of Cupid; Ku. 3. 66.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमृज्|सम्मृज्
संमृज् {c2c} P., {c10c} U.<BR>1 To sweep<BR>clean, purify.<BR>--2 To wipe off or out,<BR>wipe away, remove.<BR>--3 To rub,<BR>stroke.<BR>--4 To strain, filter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमार्जकः|सम्मार्जक|संमार्जक|सम्मार्ज्जकः
संमार्जकः A sweeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमार्जनं|सम्मार्जन|संमार्जन|सम्मार्ज्जनं
संमार्जनं<BR>1 Sweeping, cleaning.<BR>--2<BR>Purifying, cleaning, brushing.<BR>--3<BR>Anointing (of images).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमार्जनी
संमार्जनी A broom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमृष्ट|सम्मृष्ट|सम्मृष्टः
संमृष्ट p. p.<BR>1 Well swept, cleansed.<BR>--2 Strained, filtered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमृत|सम्मृत
संमृत a. Quite dead, deceased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमृद्|सम्मृद्
संमृद् {c1c} {c9c} P.<BR>1 To press or<BR>squeeze together, rub or grind to<BR>pieces; crush, trample upon.<BR>--2<BR>To pound, bruise, kill. --Caus.<BR>1<BR>To crush, pound &c.<BR>--2 To rub.<BR>--3 To clean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमर्दः|सम्मर्द|सम्मर्द्द|सम्मर्द्दः
संमर्दः<BR>1 Rubbing together,<BR>friction.<BR>--2 Throng, crowd, concourse;<BR>यद्गोप्रतरकल्पोऽभूत्संमर्दस्तत्र मज्जतां<BR>R. 15. 101; Māl. 10.<BR>--3 Treading or<BR>trampling on.<BR>--4 War, battle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

संमोदः|सम्मोद|संमोद|सम्मोदः
संमोदः Great joy, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यच्
सम्यच्, सम्यंच् a. (समीची f.)<BR>1<BR>Going with, accompanying.<BR>--2<BR>Right, fit, proper, due.<BR>--3 Correct,<BR>true, accurate.<BR>--4 Pleasant,<BR>agreeable; किं च कुलानि कवीनां<BR>निसर्गसम्यंचि रंजयतु R. G.<BR>--5 Same, uniform.<BR>--6 All, whole, entire. --ind. (<BR>सम्यक्)<BR>1 With, together with.<BR>--2<BR>Well, properly, rightly, correctly,<BR>truly; सम्यगियमाह Ś. 1; Ms. 2. 5,<BR>14.<BR>--3 Duly, suitably, correctly,<BR>truly.<BR>--4 Honourably.<BR>--5<BR>Completely, thoroughly.<BR>--6 Distinctly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पाठः a correct reading or<BR>recitation.<BR>--प्रयोगः proper use, due<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">Page1107-b+ 55</a>]<BR>application.<BR>--प्रवृत्तिः f. the right<BR>direction (of the organ).<BR>--वृत्तिः<BR>f. steady practice, regular discharge<BR>of duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्यंच्|सम्यञ्च्
सम्यच्, सम्यंच् a. (समीची f.)<BR>1<BR>Going with, accompanying.<BR>--2<BR>Right, fit, proper, due.<BR>--3 Correct,<BR>true, accurate.<BR>--4 Pleasant,<BR>agreeable; किं च कुलानि कवीनां<BR>निसर्गसम्यंचि रंजयतु R. G.<BR>--5 Same, uniform.<BR>--6 All, whole, entire. --ind. (<BR>सम्यक्)<BR>1 With, together with.<BR>--2<BR>Well, properly, rightly, correctly,<BR>truly; सम्यगियमाह Ś. 1; Ms. 2. 5,<BR>14.<BR>--3 Duly, suitably, correctly,<BR>truly.<BR>--4 Honourably.<BR>--5<BR>Completely, thoroughly.<BR>--6 Distinctly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पाठः a correct reading or<BR>recitation.<BR>--प्रयोगः proper use, due<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">Page1107-b+ 55</a>]<BR>application.<BR>--प्रवृत्तिः f. the right<BR>direction (of the organ).<BR>--वृत्तिः<BR>f. steady practice, regular discharge<BR>of duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

समीची
सम्यच्, सम्यंच् a. (समीची f.)<BR>1<BR>Going with, accompanying.<BR>--2<BR>Right, fit, proper, due.<BR>--3 Correct,<BR>true, accurate.<BR>--4 Pleasant,<BR>agreeable; किं च कुलानि कवीनां<BR>निसर्गसम्यंचि रंजयतु R. G.<BR>--5 Same, uniform.<BR>--6 All, whole, entire. --ind. (<BR>सम्यक्)<BR>1 With, together with.<BR>--2<BR>Well, properly, rightly, correctly,<BR>truly; सम्यगियमाह Ś. 1; Ms. 2. 5,<BR>14.<BR>--3 Duly, suitably, correctly,<BR>truly.<BR>--4 Honourably.<BR>--5<BR>Completely, thoroughly.<BR>--6 Distinctly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पाठः a correct reading or<BR>recitation.<BR>--प्रयोगः proper use, due<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">Page1107-b+ 55</a>]<BR>application.<BR>--प्रवृत्तिः f. the right<BR>direction (of the organ).<BR>--वृत्तिः<BR>f. steady practice, regular discharge<BR>of duties.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सम्राज्
सम्राज् m. A paramount<BR>sovereign, universal lord; especially one<BR>who rules over other princes and<BR>has performed the Rājasūya<BR>sacrifice; येतेष्टं राजसूयेन मंडलस्येश्वरश्च यः ।<BR>शास्ति यश्चाज्ञया राज्ञः स सम्राद् Ak.;<BR>R. 2. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सय्
सय् {c1c} A. (सयते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयूथ्यः|सयूथ्य
सयूथ्यः One of the same flock<BR>or tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सयोनि|सयोनिः
सयोनि a.<BR>1 Having the same<BR>womb, uterine.<BR>--2 Closely related<BR>to.<BR>--3 Closely united with the<BR>womb.<BR>--निः<BR>1 A whole or uterine<BR>brother.<BR>--2 A pair of nippers for<BR>cutting betel-nut.<BR>--3 N. of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर|सरं|सरः
सर a. [सरति सृ अच्]<BR>1 Going or<BR>moving.<BR>--2 Cathartic, purgative<BR>--रः<BR>1 Going, motion.<BR>--2 An arrow.<BR>--3 The coagulum of curds or milk,<BR>cream<BR>--4 Salt.<BR>--5 A string,<BR>necklace; अयं कंठे बाहुः शिशिरससृणो<BR>मौक्तिकसरः U. 1. 39, 29.<BR>--6 A<BR>waterfall.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 A lake, pool.<BR>--रा<BR>1 Motion, movement.<BR>--2 A<BR>cascade.<BR>--री A water-fall.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्सवः a crane.<BR>--जं fresh butter;<BR>cf. शरज.<BR>--पत्रिका {1} the new<BR>leaf of a lotus. {2} a lotus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरकः|सरक|सरकं
सरकः --कं [सृ --वुन्]<BR>1 A continuous<BR>line of road.<BR>--2 Spirituous liquor,<BR>spirits.<BR>--3 Drinking spirits; चक्रुरथ<BR>सह पुरंध्रि जनैरयथार्यसिद्धि सरकं<BR>महीभृतः Śi. 15. 80, 10. 12.<BR>--4 A<BR>drinking-vessel, wine-glass, goblet;<BR>Śi. 10. 20.<BR>--5 Distribution of<BR>spirituous liquor.<BR>--कं<BR>1 Going.<BR>--2 A pond, lake.<BR>--3 Heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरकं|सरक|सरकः
सरकः --कं [सृ --वुन्]<BR>1 A continuous<BR>line of road.<BR>--2 Spirituous liquor,<BR>spirits.<BR>--3 Drinking spirits; चक्रुरथ<BR>सह पुरंध्रि जनैरयथार्यसिद्धि सरकं<BR>महीभृतः Śi. 15. 80, 10. 12.<BR>--4 A<BR>drinking-vessel, wine-glass, goblet;<BR>Śi. 10. 20.<BR>--5 Distribution of<BR>spirituous liquor.<BR>--कं<BR>1 Going.<BR>--2 A pond, lake.<BR>--3 Heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरघा
सरघा A bee; तस्तार सरघाव्याप्तैः<BR>स क्षौद्रपटलैरिव R. 4. 63; Śi. 15. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरंगः|सरङ्ग|सरंग|सरङ्गः
सरंगः<BR>1 A quadruped.<BR>--2 A bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरजस्
सरजस् --सा f., सरजस्का A woman<BR>during menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरजसा
सरजस् --सा f., सरजस्का A woman<BR>during menstruation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरट्
सरट् m.<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>--2 A cloud.<BR>--3 A lizard.<BR>--4 A bee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटः|सरट
सरटः<BR>1 Wind.<BR>--2 A lizard;<BR>लूताहिसरटानां च तिरश्चां चांबुचारिणां<BR>Ms. 12. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटिः|सरटि
सरटिः<BR>1 Wind.<BR>--2 A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरटुः|सरटु
सरटुः A lizard, chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण|सरणं
सरण a. [सृ-ल्युट्] Going, moving,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">Page1107-c+ 55</a>]<BR>flowing.<BR>--णं<BR>1 Proceeding, going<BR>or flowing.<BR>--2 Iron rust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरणिः|सरणि
सरणिः, --णी f.<BR>1 A path, way,<BR>road, course; G. L. 18.<BR>--2<BR>Arrangement, mode.<BR>--3 A straight or<BR>continuous line.<BR>--4 A disease of the<BR>throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरणी
सरणिः, --णी f.<BR>1 A path, way,<BR>road, course; G. L. 18.<BR>--2<BR>Arrangement, mode.<BR>--3 A straight or<BR>continuous line.<BR>--4 A disease of the<BR>throat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरंडः|सरण्ड|सरंड|सरण्डः
सरंडः<BR>1 A bird.<BR>--2 A libertine,<BR>dissolute man.<BR>--3 A lizard.<BR>--4 A<BR>rogue.<BR>--5 A kind of ornament.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरण्युः|सरण्यु
सरण्युः<BR>1 Air, wind.<BR>--2 A cloud.<BR>--3 Water.<BR>--4 The spring.<BR>--5 Fire.<BR>--6 N. of Yama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरत्निः|सरत्नि
सरत्निः m. f. A kind of<BR>cubitmeasure; cf. रीत्न or अरत्नि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरथ|सरथः
सरथ a. Riding in the same car.<BR>--थः A warrior riding in a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरभस
सरभस a.<BR>1 Speedy, quick.<BR>--2<BR>Violent, impetuous.<BR>--3 Passionate.<BR>--4 Delighted.<BR>--सं ind.<BR>Impetuously, hurriedly &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरमा
सरमा<BR>1 A bitch.<BR>--2 The bitch<BR>of the gods.<BR>--3 N. of a daughter<BR>of Dakṣa.<BR>--4 N. of the wife of<BR>Bibhīṣaṇa, brother of Rāvaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरयुः|सरयु
सरयुः Air, wind.<BR>--युः --यूः f. N.<BR>of a river on which stands<BR>Ayodhyā, or Oude; R. 8. 95, 13. 61,<BR>63, 14. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरल|सरलः
सरल a. [सृ-अलच्]<BR>1 Straight,<BR>not crooked.<BR>--2 Honest, upright,<BR>sincere, candid.<BR>--3 Simple, artless,<BR>simple-minded; सरले साहसरागं<BR>परिहर Māl. 6. 10; अयि सरले किमत्र<BR>मया भगवत्या शक्यं 2.<BR>--लः<BR>1 A kind<BR>of pine tree; विघट्टितानां सरलद्रुमाणां<BR>Ku. 1. 9; Me. 53; R. 4. 75.<BR>--2<BR>Fire.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः ‘the<BR>exudation of Sarala’, resin, turpentine.<BR>--द्रवः fragrant resin.<BR>--यायिनी<BR>a plant with an erect stem.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरव्य|सरव्यं
सरव्य See शरव्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्
सरस् n. [सृ-असुन्]<BR>1 A lake,<BR>pond, pool, a large sheet of water;<BR>सरसामस्मि सागरः Bg. 10. 24.<BR>--2<BR>Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं, --जन्मन् n.,<BR>--रुहं<BR>(सरोजं, सरोजन्मन्, सरोरुहं), also<BR>सरसिजं, सरीसरुहं a lotus;<BR>सरसिजमनुविद्धं शैवलेनापि रम्यं Ś. 1. 20;<BR>सरोरुहद्युतिमुषः पादांस्तवसिविनुं Ratn. 1. 30.<BR>--जः (also सरसिजः) the Sārasa<BR>bird. (सरोजिन् m. an epithet of<BR>Brahman).<BR>--जिनी, --रुहिणी {1} a<BR>lotusplant; म्रमर कथं वा सरोजिनीं त्यजासि<BR>Bv. 1. 100. {2} a pond abounding<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">Page1108-a+ 55</a>]<BR>in lotuses. {3} a multitude of<BR>lotuses. {4} a lotus.<BR>--रक्षः (सरोरक्षः) the<BR>guardian of a pool.<BR>--रुह् (सरोरुह्)<BR>n. a lotus.<BR>--वरः (सरोवरः) a lake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1107-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस|सरसं
सरस a.<BR>1 Juicy, succulent.<BR>--2<BR>Tasty, sapid.<BR>--3 Wet; Śi. 11. 54.<BR>--4 Wet with perspiration;<BR>Ku. 5. 85.<BR>--5 Full of love, impassioned;<BR>Bv. 1. 100 (where it means ‘full<BR>of honey’ also).<BR>--6 Charming,<BR>lovely, agreeable, beautiful; सरसवसंते<BR>Gīt. 1; Māl. 4. 8.<BR>--7 Fresh, new,<BR>blooming; Māl. 9. 10.<BR>--8<BR>Expressive of poetical sentiment^1; see रस.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसिकः|सरसिक
सरसि(सी)कः The Sārasa bird<BR>(crane).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसीकः|सरसीक
सरसि(सी)कः The Sārasa bird<BR>(crane).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरसी
सरसी A lake, pool; Bv. 2. 144.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रुहं a lotus.<BR>--(हः) the<BR>Sārasa bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्वत्|सरस्वन्त्
सरस्वत् a.<BR>1 Having water, watery.<BR>--2 Juicy, succulent.<BR>--3 Elegant.<BR>--4 Sentimental.<BR>--5 Tasty, sapid.<BR>--m.<BR>1 The ocean.<BR>--2 A lake.<BR>--3 A<BR>male river (नद).<BR>--4 A buffalo.<BR>--5<BR>N. of Vāyu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरस्वती
सरस्वती<BR>1 N. of the goddess of<BR>speech and learning, and<BR>represented as the wife of Brahman.<BR>--2<BR>Speech, voice, words; Ku. 4. 39, 43;<BR>R. 15. 46.<BR>--3 N. of a river (which<BR>is lost in the sands of the great<BR>desert).<BR>--4 A river in general.<BR>--5 A cow.<BR>--6 An excellent<BR>woman.<BR>--7 N. of Durgā.<BR>--8 N. of<BR>a female divinity peculiar to the<BR>Buddhists.<BR>--9 The Soma plant.<BR>--10 The plant called ज्योतिष्मती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरहस्य
सरहस्य a.<BR>1 Mystical, magical.<BR>--2 Having or attended with<BR>mystical teaching or doctrine; U. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराग
सराग a.<BR>1 Coloured, tinged,<BR>tinted; (अकारि) सरागमस्या<BR>रसनागुणास्पदं Ku. 5. 10.<BR>--2 Dyed with<BR>red lac; R. 16. 15.<BR>--3 Impassioned,<BR>full of love, enamoured; मुनेरपि<BR>मनोऽवश्यं सरागं कुरुतेंऽगना Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सराव|सरावः
सराव a. Sounding, making a<BR>noise.<BR>--वः<BR>1 A lid, cover.<BR>--2 A<BR>shallow dish, saucer; cf. शराव.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिः|सरि
सरिः f.<BR>1 A spring, fountain.<BR>--2<BR>A cascade (m.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिका
सरिका<BR>1 Going, proceeding.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of drug (हिंगुपत्री).<BR>--3 A<BR>woman going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरित्
सरित् f. [सृ-इति]<BR>1 A river;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">Page1108-b+ 54</a>]<BR>अन्यसरितां शतानि हि समुद्रणाः<BR>प्रापयंत्यब्धिं M. 5. 19.<BR>--2 A thread, string.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नाथः, --पतिः (also<BR>सरितांपतिः),<BR>--भर्तृ m. the ocean.<BR>--वरा<BR>(also सरितांवरा) N. of the Ganges.<BR>--सुतः an epithet of Bhīṣma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिद्वत्
सरिद्वत् m. The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिमन्
सरि(री)मन् m.<BR>1 Motion,<BR>creeping.<BR>--2 Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरीमन्
सरि(री)मन् m.<BR>1 Motion,<BR>creeping.<BR>--2 Wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिलं|सरिल
सरिलं Water; cf. सलिल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरिषपः|सरिषप
सरिषपः Mustard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरीसृपः|सरीसृप
सरीसृपः A serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरु|सरुः
सरु a. Thin, fine, small.<BR>--रुः<BR>The handle of a sword.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरूप|सरूपः
सरूप a.<BR>1 Having the same<BR>form.<BR>--2 Like, resembling, similar;<BR>R. 6. 59.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरूपता
सरूपता, त्वं<BR>1 Likeness.<BR>--2<BR>Assimilation to the deity, one of the<BR>four states of Mukti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरूपत्वं|सरूपत्व
सरूपता, त्वं<BR>1 Likeness.<BR>--2<BR>Assimilation to the deity, one of the<BR>four states of Mukti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सरोष
सरोष a.<BR>1 Angry, wrathful.<BR>--2<BR>Enraged.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्कः|सर्क
सर्कः<BR>1 Wind, air.<BR>--2 The mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्गः|सर्ग
सर्गः [सृज्-घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Relinquishment, abandonment.<BR>--2 Creation;<BR>अस्याः सर्गविधौ प्रजापतिरभूच्चंद्रो नु<BR>कांतिप्रदः V. 1. 8.<BR>--3 The creation of<BR>the world; Ku. 2. 6; R. 3. 27.<BR>--4<BR>Nature, the universe.<BR>--5 Natural<BR>property, nature.<BR>--6 Determination,<BR>resolve; गृहाण शस्त्रं यदि सर्ग एष ते<BR>R. 3. 51; 14. 42; Śi. 19. 38.<BR>--7<BR>Assent, agreement.<BR>--8 A section,<BR>chapter, canto (as of a poem).<BR>--9<BR>Rush, onset, advance (of troops).<BR>--10 Voiding of excrement.<BR>--11 N.<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--12 Fainting, swoon<BR>(मोह).<BR>--13 Ved. A horse.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--क्रमः the order of creation.<BR>--बंधः<BR>a great poem having several cantos,<BR>a Mahākāvya; सर्गबंधो महाकाव्यं<BR>S. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्|सर्ज्ज्
सर्ज् {c1c} A. (सर्जति)<BR>1 To acquire,<BR>gain.<BR>--2 To earn by labour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जः|सर्ज|सर्ज्ज|सर्ज्जः
सर्जः<BR>1 N. of a tree(साल).<BR>--2<BR>The resinous exudation of the Sāla<BR>tree.<BR>--3 A timber tree; Māl. 9. 17.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--निर्यासकः, --मणिः --रसः,<BR>resin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जकः|सर्जक|सर्ज्जक|सर्ज्जकः
सर्जकः The Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जनं|सर्जन|सर्ज्जन|सर्ज्जनं
सर्जनं [सृज्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Abandoning,<BR>quitting.<BR>--2 Letting loose.<BR>--3<BR>Creating.<BR>--4 Voiding.<BR>--5 The rear of an<BR>army.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जिः|सर्जि|सर्ज्जि|सर्ज्जिः
सर्जिः, सर्जिका, सर्जी f. Natron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जिका|सर्ज्जिका
सर्जिः, सर्जिका, सर्जी f. Natron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जी|सर्ज्जी
सर्जिः, सर्जिका, सर्जी f. Natron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्जूः|सर्ज्जूः
सर्जूः A trader. --f.<BR>1<BR>Lightning.<BR>--2 Necklace.<BR>--3 Going,<BR>following.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ज्यः|सर्ज्य
सर्ज्यः The resin of the Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पः|सर्प
सर्पः<BR>1 [सृप्-घञ्] Serpentine or<BR>winding motion, gliding.<BR>--2 Flowing,<BR>going.<BR>--3 A snake, serpent.<BR>--4 N.<BR>of a tree (नागकेशर).<BR>--5 The Āśleṣā<BR>constellation.<BR>--6 N. of a tribe of<BR>Mlecchas or barbarians.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अरातिः --अरिः {1} an ichneumon.<BR>{2} a peacock. {3} an epithet of<BR>Garuḍa.<BR>--अशनः a peacock.<BR>--आवासं, --इष्टं the sandal tree.<BR>--ईश्वरः N.<BR>of Vāsuki.<BR>--छत्रं a mushroom.<BR>--तृणः an ichneumon.<BR>--दंष्ट्रा a<BR>snake's fang.<BR>--धारकः a<BR>snakecharmer.<BR>--फणिजः the gem found<BR>in a snake's head, the snake-gem.<BR>--भुज् m. {1} a peacock. {2} a crane. {3}<BR>a large snake.<BR>--मणिः a snake-gem.<BR>--राजः N. of Vāsuki.<BR>--विद् m. a<BR>conjuror, snake-charmer.<BR>--सत्रं a<BR>sacrifice for the destruction of<BR>serpents (performed by king<BR>Janamejaya).<BR>--सत्रिन् m. N. of king<BR>Janamejaya; see जनमेजय.<BR>--हन् m. {1}<BR>an ichneumon. {2} N. of Garuḍa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पणं|सर्पण|सर्प्पण
सर्पणं [सृप्-ल्यूट्]<BR>1 Creeping, gliding.<BR>--2 Tortuous motion.<BR>--3 The flight of<BR>an arrow nearly parallel to the<BR>ground.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिणी
सर्पिणी<BR>1 A female serpent.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a small medicinal herb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिन्
सर्पिन् a.<BR>1 Creeping, gliding,<BR>winding, going tortuously.<BR>--2 Moving,<BR>going (in general); यूका<BR>मंदविसर्पिणी Pt. 1. 252.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिस्
सर्पिस् n. [सृप्-इसि] Clarified<BR>butter; (for the difference between<BR>घृत and सर्पिस् see आज्य).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--समुद्रः the sea of clarified butter, one<BR>of the seven seas. --Comp.<BR>--आसुतिः<BR>an epithet of Agni.<BR>--कुंडिका a<BR>butter-jar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्पिष्मत्|सर्पिष्मन्त्
सर्पिष्मत् a. Dressed with clarified<BR>butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्ब्|सर्ब्ब्
सर्ब् {c1c} P. (सर्बति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्मः|सर्म|सर्म्म
सर्मः<BR>1 Going, motion.<BR>--2 The<BR>sky.<BR>--3 Heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व्|सर्व्व्
सर्व् {c1c} P. (सर्वति) To hurt,<BR>injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्व|सर्वः|सर्व्व|सर्व्वः
सर्व pron. a. [सृतमनेन<BR>विश्वमितिसर्वं Uṇ. 1. 151] (nom. pl. सर्वे m.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-a" target="_blank">Page1109-a+ 56</a>]<BR>1 {1} All, every; उपर्युपरि पश्यंतः सर्व एव<BR>दरिद्रति H. 2. 2; रिक्तः सर्वो भवति<BR>हि लघुः पूर्णता गौरवाय Me. 20, 63.<BR>--2 Whole, entire, complete.<BR>--र्वः<BR>1<BR>N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 Of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगं {1} the whole body. {2} all<BR>the Vedāṅgas. (--गः or ˚रूपः) N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--अंगीण a. pervading or<BR>thrilling through the whole body;<BR>सर्वंगीणः स्पर्शः सुतस्य किल V. 5. 11.<BR>--अधिकारिन् m.,<BR>--अध्यक्षः a general<BR>superintendent.<BR>--अनुक्रमणिका,<BR>--क्रमणी a general index.<BR>--अन्नीन a.<BR>eating every kind of food; so<BR>सर्वान्नभोजिन् &c.<BR>--अभिसंधिन् m. {1} a<BR>traducer, calumniator. {2} a<BR>religious hypocrite.<BR>--अभिसारः a<BR>complete army (of elephants, chariots,<BR>cavalry, and infantry).<BR>--अर्थसाधिका N. of Durgā.<BR>--अर्यसिद्धः the<BR>great Buddha or Śākyamuni.<BR>--अवसरः midnight.<BR>--आकार (in comp.)<BR>entirely, thoroughly, completely;<BR>सर्वाकारहृदयंगमायास्तस्याः Māl. 1, 7;<BR>1. 14.<BR>--आत्मन् m. {1} the whole soul;<BR>(सर्वात्मना entirely, completely,<BR>thoroughly.) {2} N. of Śiva.<BR>--आशयः,<BR>--आश्रयः N. of Śiva.<BR>--ईशः, --ईश्वरः<BR>{1} the Supreme Being. {2} a<BR>paramount lord.<BR>--उत्तम a. best of all,<BR>excellent, supremely good.<BR>--ओघः<BR>= सर्वाभिसार above.<BR>--करः, --कर्मन् m.<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--कर्तृ m. N. of<BR>Brahman. {2} the Supreme Being.<BR>--कर्मीण a. performing everything.<BR>--कामः, --कामदः, --कामवरः N. of Śiva.<BR>--कालीन a. for all time, perpetual.<BR>--केशिन् m. an actor.<BR>--क्षारः impure<BR>carbonate of soda or potash.<BR>--गत a.<BR>all-pervading, omnipresent.<BR>--(गः)<BR>{1} Śiva. {2} the Supreme Being.<BR>{3} Brahman. {4} the spirit, soul.<BR>--(गं) water.<BR>--गा the plant called<BR>प्रियंगु.<BR>--गामिन्, --गति a.<BR>all-pervading, omnipresent.<BR>--ग्रंथिः, --ग्रंथिकं the<BR>root of long pepper.<BR>--चारिन् m. N.<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--जनीन a. world-wide,<BR>famous.<BR>--जित् a. {1} excellent,<BR>incomparable. {2} all-conquering,<BR>invincible.<BR>--ज्ञ, --विद् a. all-knowing,<BR>omniscient. (--m.) {1} an epithet of<BR>Śiva. {2} of Buddha. {3} the<BR>Supreme Being.<BR>--ज्ञा N. of Durgā.<BR>--तंत्रः one who has studied all the<BR>Tantras. ˚सिद्धांतः a doctrine admitted<BR>by all the schools.<BR>--तापनः the god of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-b" target="_blank">Page1109-b+ 56</a>]<BR>love.<BR>--दः N. of Śiva.<BR>--दम, --दमन a.<BR>all-subduing, irresistible. (--m.)<BR>N. of Bharata, son of Duṣyanta;<BR>इहायं सत्त्वानां प्रसभदमनात् सर्वदमनः<BR>Ś. 7. 33.<BR>--दर्शनसंग्रहः a compendium<BR>of all the schools or systems of<BR>philosophy by Mādhavācārya.<BR>--दर्शिन्<BR>m. {1} a Buddha. {2} the Supreme<BR>Being.<BR>--देवमय a. comprising all<BR>the gods.<BR>--(यः) N. of Śiva.<BR>--देवमुखः an epithet of Agni.<BR>--धनं<BR>(in arith.) the total of a sum in<BR>progression.<BR>--धारिन् m. N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--नामन् n. a class of<BR>pronominal words. ˚स्थानं N. for the<BR>nom. (all numbers) and acc.<BR>sing. and dual of masculine and<BR>feminine nouns and nom.<BR>and acc. pl. of neuter nouns;<BR>cf. सुट् also.<BR>--प्रिय a. popular,<BR>liked by all.<BR>--भक्षा a female goat.<BR>--भावः all-being or nature; (<BR>सर्वभावेन ‘with all one's heart,<BR>sincerely, heart and soul’).<BR>--भावकरः.<BR>भावनः N. of Śiva.<BR>--मंगला an<BR>epithet of Pārvatī.<BR>--मूषकः<BR>‘allstealing’, time.<BR>--योगिन् m. N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--रसः {1} the resinous<BR>exudation of the Sāla tree, resin. {2}<BR>salt, saltness. {3} a kind of<BR>musical instrument. {4} a learned<BR>man. ˚उत्तमः salt.<BR>--लालसः N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--लिंगिन् m. an impostor.<BR>--लोकः the universe.<BR>--लोहः an<BR>iron arrow.<BR>--वल्लभा an unchaste<BR>woman.<BR>--यासः, --वासिन् m., विख्यातः<BR>--विग्रहः N. of Śiva.<BR>--वेदः a man<BR>who has studied the four Vedas.<BR>--वेदस् m. one who performs a<BR>sacrifice by giving away all his<BR>wealth.<BR>--वेशिन् m. an actor.<BR>--व्यापिन् a. all-pervading.<BR>--शक् a.<BR>omnipotent, all-powerful.<BR>--संगतः a<BR>kind of quick-growing rice.<BR>--संग्रहः<BR>a general or universal collection.<BR>--संनहनं, --संनाहः assembling of a<BR>complete army, a complete armament;<BR>see ˚अभिसार m.<BR>--सह a.<BR>all-forbearing, very patient.<BR>--(हः) bdellium.<BR>(--हा, also सर्वंसहा) the earth.<BR>--साक्षिन् a. all-witnessing. (--m.) {1} N.<BR>of the Supreme Being. {2} N. of<BR>wind. {3} of Agni.<BR>--साधनः<BR>Śiva.<BR>--सिद्धिः f. universal success.<BR>(--m.) the Bilva tree.<BR>--स्वं {1}<BR>everything, the whole of one's<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">Page1109-c+ 56</a>]<BR>possessions; as in सर्वस्वदंडः, सर्वस्वहरणं<BR>‘confiscation of the whole property.’<BR>{2} the very essence, the all-in-all<BR>of anything: सर्वस्वं तदहो महाकविगिरां<BR>कामस्य चांभोरुह Subhāṣ., see<BR>Ś. 1. 24; 6. 1; Māl. 8. 6; Bv. 1. 63.<BR>--हरः death.<BR>--हितं black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1108-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वक|सर्व्वक|सर्व्वकः
सर्वक a.<BR>1 All, every.<BR>--2 Whole,<BR>entire.<BR>--के ind. Everywhere,<BR>universally.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वंकष
सर्वंकष^1 a. ‘All-destroying’,<BR>allpowerful; सर्वंकषा भगवती भवितव्यतैव<BR>Māl. 1. 23; Bv. 4. 2.<BR>--षः A<BR>villain, rogue.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वतस्|सर्व्वतस्
सर्वतस् ind.<BR>1 From every side<BR>or quarter.<BR>--2 On all sides,<BR>everywhere, all round.<BR>--3 Completely,<BR>entirely.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गामिन् a. {1}<BR>having access everywhere;<BR>Ku. 3. 12. {2} all-pervading.<BR>--भद्रः<BR>{1} the car of Viṣṇu. {2} a<BR>bamboo. {3} a kind of verse<BR>artificially arranged; e. g. see<BR>Ki. 15. 25. {4} a temple or palace having<BR>openings on four sides; (n. also<BR>in this sense). {5} the Nimba<BR>tree. {6} a kind of military array.<BR>--(द्रा) a dancing girl, an actress.<BR>--मुख a. of every kind, complete,<BR>unlimited; Ś. 5. 26.<BR>--(खः) {1}<BR>an epithet of Śiva. {2} of<BR>Brahman; Ku. 2. 3 (having faces on<BR>all sides). {3} the Supreme Being.<BR>{4} the soul. {5} a Brāhmaṇa. {6}<BR>fire. {7} heaven or Svarga (of<BR>Indra).<BR>--(खं) {1} water. {2} sky.<BR>--शुभा the Priyaṅgu plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वत्र|सर्व्वत्र
सर्वत्र ind.<BR>1 Everywhere, in all<BR>places.<BR>--2 At all times.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गः, --गामिन् m. air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वथा|सर्व्वथा
सर्वथा ind.<BR>1 In every way, by<BR>all means; U. 1. 5.<BR>--2 At all,<BR>altogether (usually with negation).<BR>--3 Completely, entirely, utterly.<BR>--4<BR>At all times.<BR>--5 Exceedingly, very<BR>much.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वंदमः|सर्वन्दम|सर्व्वन्दम|सर्व्वन्दमः
सर्वंदमः = सर्वदमनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वद्र्यंच्|सर्वद्र्यञ्च्
सर्वद्र्यंच् a. Honouring or<BR>worshipping all.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वदा|सर्व्वदा
सर्वदा ind. At all times, always,<BR>for ever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वशस्|सर्व्वशस्
सर्वशस् ind.<BR>1 Wholly, entirely,<BR>completely.<BR>--2 Everywhere.<BR>--3 On<BR>all sides.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वरी|सर्व्वरी
सर्वरी See शर्वरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वला|सर्व्वला
सर्वला, --ली An iron club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वली|सर्व्वली
सर्वला, --ली An iron club.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1109-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्वाणी|सर्व्वाणी
सर्वाणी See शर्वाणी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सर्षपः|सर्षप
सर्षपः [Uṇ. 3. 141]<BR>1 Mustard;<BR>खलः सर्षपमात्राणि परच्छिद्राणि पश्यति<BR>Subhāṣ.; Māl. 10. 6.<BR>--2 A small<BR>measure of weight.<BR>--3 A sort of<BR>poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्
सल् {c1c} P. (सलति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलं|सल
सलं Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलज्ज|सलज्जः
सलज्ज a. Bashful, modest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलिलं|सलिल
सलिलं [सलति गच्छति निम्नं<BR>सल्-इलच् Uṇ. 1. 54]<BR>1 Water;<BR>सुभगसलिलावगाहाः Ś. 1. 3.<BR>--2 The<BR>constellation उत्तराषाढा.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आर्थिन् a.<BR>thirsty.<BR>--आशयः a tank, reservoir<BR>of water.<BR>--इंधनः the submarine<BR>fire.<BR>--उपप्लवः inundation, deluge,<BR>flood of water.<BR>--कुंतलः moss.<BR>--क्रिया the funeral rite of washing a<BR>corpse. {2} = उदकक्रिया q. v.<BR>--जं a<BR>lotus.<BR>--निधिः, --राशिः the ocean.<BR>--रयः a current, stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलील|सलीलः
सलील a. Sportive, wanton,<BR>amorous.<BR>--लं ind.<BR>1 Playfully.<BR>--2 Affectionately.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सलोकता
सलोकता Being in the same<BR>world, residence in the same heaven<BR>with a particular deity, (one of the<BR>four states of Mukti).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सल्लका
सल्लका A kind of tree; cf. शल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवः|सव|सवं
सवः [सू-सु-अच्]<BR>1 Extraction of<BR>Soma juice.<BR>--2 An offering, a<BR>libation.<BR>--3 A sacrifice.<BR>--4 The sun.<BR>--5 The moon.<BR>--6 Progeny.<BR>--7 A<BR>generator.<BR>--8 The Arka plant.<BR>--वं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 The honey of flowers.<BR>--3 Extracting the Soma juice.<BR>--4<BR>Making libations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवनं|सवन
सवनं [सु सू वा --ल्युट्]<BR>1 Extracting<BR>the Soma juice or drinking it.<BR>--2<BR>A sacrifice; अथ तं सवनाय दीक्षितः<BR>R. 8. 75; Ś. 3. 27.<BR>--3 A libation,<BR>sacrificial libation.<BR>--4 Bathing,<BR>purificatory ablution.<BR>--5 Generation,<BR>bearing or bringing forth children.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवयस्
सवयस् a. Of the same age;<BR>R. 3. 28. --m.<BR>1 A contemporary,<BR>coeval.<BR>--2 A companion of the same<BR>age. --f. A woman's female<BR>companion or confidante.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवरः|सवर
सवरः<BR>1 N. of Śiva.<BR>--2 Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्ण|सवर्णः
सवर्ण a. [समानो वर्णो यस्य]<BR>1 Of the<BR>same colour.<BR>--2 Of like appearance,<BR>like, resembling; दुर्वर्णभित्तिरिह<BR>सांद्रसुधासवर्णा Śi. 4. 28; Me. 18;<BR>R. 9. 51.<BR>--3 Of the same caste or tribe.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">Page1110-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--4 Of the same kind, similar.<BR>--5 Belonging to the same class of<BR>letters, requiring the same effort<BR>(of the organs of speech) in<BR>pronunciation; तुल्यास्यप्रयत्नं सवर्णं<BR>P. I. 1. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवर्णनं|सवर्णन
सवर्णनं Reduction of fractions to<BR>the same denominator.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकल्प
सविकल्प, सविकल्पक a.<BR>1<BR>Optional.<BR>--2 Doubtful.<BR>--3<BR>Recognizing a distinction as that of subject<BR>and object, or of the knower and<BR>the known (opp. निर्विकल्पक q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकल्पक
सविकल्प, सविकल्पक a.<BR>1<BR>Optional.<BR>--2 Doubtful.<BR>--3<BR>Recognizing a distinction as that of subject<BR>and object, or of the knower and<BR>the known (opp. निर्विकल्पक q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविकाश|सविकाशः
सविकाश a.<BR>1 Fully blown or<BR>expanded.<BR>--2 Extended, extensive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविग्रह
सविग्रह a,<BR>1 Possessing a body,<BR>embodied.<BR>--2 Having meaning or<BR>import.<BR>--3 Engaged in strife,<BR>quarrelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितर्क
सवितर्क, सविमर्श a. Thoughtful.<BR>--र्कं, --र्शं ind. Thoughtfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविमर्श
सवितर्क, सविमर्श a. Thoughtful.<BR>--र्कं, --र्शं ind. Thoughtfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृ
सवितृ a. (त्री f.) [सू-तृच्]<BR>Generating, producing, yielding;<BR>सवित्री कामानां यदि जगाति जागर्ति भ<BR>वती G. L. 23. --m.<BR>1 The sun;<BR>उदेति सविता ताम्रस्ताम्र एवास्तमोति च<BR>K. P. 7.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva.<BR>--3 Of<BR>Indra.<BR>--4 The Arka tree.<BR>--5 The<BR>creator of the world.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवितृल|सवितृलः
सवितृल a. Solar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्रं|सवित्र
सवित्रं Cause of generation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्रिय|सवित्रियः
सवित्रिय a. Solar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवित्री
सवित्री<BR>1 A mother; Ku. 1. 24.<BR>--2 A cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविध|सविधः
सविध a.<BR>1 Of the same kind<BR>or sort.<BR>--2 Near, adjacent,<BR>proximate; भूयो भूयः सविधनगररिथ्यया<BR>पर्यदंतं Māl. 1. 15.<BR>--धं Proximity,<BR>vicinity; यस्य न सविधे दयिता<BR>दवदहनस्तुहिनदीधितिस्तस्य K. P. 9;<BR>किमासेव्यं पुंसां सविधमनवद्यं द्युसरितः 10;<BR>N. 2. 47; Śi. 14. 69; Bv. 2. 182.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविनय
सविनय a. Modest, humble.<BR>--यं<BR>ind. Modestly, respectfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविभ्रम
सविभ्रम, सविलास a. Sportive,<BR>coquettish, wanton; Pt. 1. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविलास
सविभ्रम, सविलास a. Sportive,<BR>coquettish, wanton; Pt. 1. 135.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेष
सविशेष a.<BR>1 Possessing<BR>characteristic qualities.<BR>--2 Peculiar,<BR>extraordinary.<BR>--3 Special, particular;<BR>U. 4.<BR>--4 Pre-eminent, superior,<BR>excellent.<BR>--5 Discriminative. (<BR>सविशेषं and सविशेषतस् are used<BR>adverbially in the sense of ‘especially’,<BR>particularly’, ‘exceedingly’;<BR>अनेन धर्मः सविशेषमद्य मे त्रिवर्गसारः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">Page1110-c+ 54</a>]<BR>प्रतिभाति भामिनि Ku. 5. 38; oft. in<BR>comp.; Ku. 1. 27, R. 16. 53).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविशेषक
सविशेषक a.<BR>1 Possessing peculiar<BR>or distinguishing properties.<BR>--2<BR>Discriminated.<BR>--कं A<BR>distinguishing characteristic, peculiar property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्तर
सविस्तर a. Detailed, minute,<BR>complete.<BR>--रं ind. In detail,<BR>in extenso.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सविस्मय|सविस्मयः
सविस्मय a.<BR>1 Surprised,<BR>astonished.<BR>--2 Doubtful.<BR>--यं ind.<BR>With surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवृद्धिक
सवृद्धिक a. Bearing interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवेश|सवेशः
सवेश a.<BR>1 Decorated,<BR>ornamented, dressed.<BR>--2 Near,<BR>proximate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सवैलक्ष्य
सवैलक्ष्य a.<BR>1 Unnatural,<BR>forced; affected.<BR>--2 Embarrassed;<BR>सवैलक्ष्यस्मितं ‘with a forced smile’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्य|सव्यः
सव्य a. [Uṇ. 4. 109]<BR>1 Left,<BR>left-hand.<BR>--2 Southern.<BR>--3 Contrary,<BR>backward, reverse,<BR>--4 Right.<BR>--व्यः<BR>An epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--व्यं<BR>ind. The usual position of the<BR>sacred thread when it hangs down<BR>over the left shoulder; cf. अपसव्य.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--इतर a. right.<BR>--साचिन् m.<BR>an epithet of Arjuna; निमित्तमात्रं<BR>भव सव्यसाचिन् Bg. 11. 33; (the<BR>name is thus derived in Mb.:<BR>--उभौ<BR>मे दक्षिणौ पाणी गांडीवस्य विकर्षणे । तेन<BR>देवमनुष्येषु सव्यसाचीति मां विदुः ॥).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यपेक्ष
सव्यपेक्ष a. Connected with,<BR>dependent on; स्नेहश्च निमित्तसव्यपेक्षश्चेति<BR>विप्रतिषिद्धमेतत् Māl. 1; U. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यभिचारः|सव्यभिचार
सव्यभिचारः One of the five<BR>main divisions of Hetvābhāsa (in<BR>logic), a too general middle term;<BR>for explanation, see अनैकांतिक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्याज
सव्याज a.<BR>1 Artful, pretended.<BR>--2<BR>Plausible, cunning.<BR>--जं ind.<BR>Artfully, under a pretext.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्यापार
सव्यापार a. Engaged, employed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्रीड
सव्रीड a.<BR>1 Bashful.<BR>--2<BR>Ashamed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सव्येष्टृ
सव्येष्टृ m. A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशब्द
सशब्द a.<BR>1 Sounding.<BR>--2<BR>Proclaimed.<BR>--ब्दं ind. With a loud noise;<BR>भग्नं सशब्दं शिरः Bk. 2. 90.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशल्य
सशल्य a.<BR>1 Thorny.<BR>--2 Pierced<BR>by darts or thorns.<BR>--3 Troublesome,<BR>difficult.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सशस्य
सशस्य a. Having or yielding<BR>corn.<BR>--स्या A variety of sun-flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1110-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्च्
सश्च् {c1c} U. (सश्चति-ते) Ved.<BR>1 To<BR>cling or stick to, follow.<BR>--2 To<BR>serve, worship, honour.<BR>--3 To<BR>pervade; see सच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्मश्रु|सश्मश्रुः
सश्मश्रु a. Bearded. --f. A<BR>woman with a beard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सश्रीक
सश्रीक a.<BR>1 Prosperous,<BR>fortunate.<BR>--2 Lovely, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्
सस् {c2c} P. (सस्ति) To sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससत्त्व
ससत्त्व a.<BR>1 Possessed of vitality<BR>energy, vigour, courage &c.<BR>--2<BR>Pregnant, big with child; R. 3. 9.<BR>--3 Full of animals or creatures.<BR>--त्त्वा A pregnant woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंदेह|ससन्देह|ससंदेहः
ससंदेह a. Doubtful.<BR>--हः N. of<BR>a figure of speech; see संदेह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससनं|ससन
ससनं Immolation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंध्य|ससन्ध्य
ससंध्य a. Evening, vespertine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससंभ्रम|ससम्भ्रम
ससंभ्रम a. Flurried, agitated,<BR>hurried, confused.<BR>--मं ind.<BR>1<BR>Hurriedly, hastily.<BR>--2 In fear or<BR>confusion, in great perplexity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ससाध्वस
ससाध्वस a. Alarmed,<BR>frightened, timid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्ज्
सस्ज् See संज्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्पृह
सस्पृह a. Desirous, longing, eager.<BR>--हं ind. Eagerly, wistfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्मित|सस्मितः
सस्मित a. Smiling, attended<BR>with a smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यं|सस्य
सस्यं [सस्-यत्]<BR>1 Corn, grain;<BR>(एतानि) सस्यैः पूर्णे जठरपिठरे प्राणिनां<BR>संभवंति Pt. 5. 97; see शस्य also.<BR>--2<BR>Fruit or produce of any plant.<BR>--3<BR>A weapon.<BR>--4 A good quality,<BR>merit.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अद्, --भक्षक a.<BR>granivorous.<BR>--इष्टिः f. a sacrifice<BR>made on the ripening of new grain.<BR>--प्रद a. fertile.<BR>--मारिन् a.<BR>destructive of grain. (--m.) a kind of rat<BR>or mouse.<BR>--संवरः the Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्यक|सस्यकः
सस्यक a. Possessed of good<BR>qualities, meritorious.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>sword.<BR>--2 A weapon.<BR>--3 A kind<BR>of precious stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सस्वेद
सस्वेद a. Covered over or moist<BR>with sweat, perspired; U. 3. 42.<BR>--दा A girl recently deflowered.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्
सह् {vI.v} {c4c} P. (सह्यति)<BR>1 To<BR>satisfy.<BR>--2 To be pleased.<BR>--3 To<BR>endure, bear. {vII.v} {c1c} A. (सहते epic<BR>Paras. also; सोढ; the स् of सह् is<BR>changed to ष् after prepositions<BR>ending in इ, as नि, परि, वि, except when<BR>ह् is changed to ढ्)<BR>1 (a) To bear,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-b" target="_blank">Page1111-b+ 56</a>]<BR>endure, suffer, put up with;<BR>खलोल्लापाः सोढाः Bh. 3. 6; पदं सहेत<BR>भ्रमरस्य पेलवं शिरीषपुष्पं न पुनः पतत्रिणः<BR>Ku. 5. 4; so दुःखं, संतापं, क्लेशं &c.;<BR>R. 12. 63; 11. 52; Bk. 17. 59.<BR>(b) To tolerate, allow; प्रकृतिः खलु<BR>सा महीयसः सहते नान्यसमुन्नतिं यया<BR>Ki. 2. 21; Me. 105; R. 14. 63.<BR>--2<BR>To forgive, forbear; वांरवारं<BR>मयैतस्यापराधः सोढः H. 3; Bg. 11. 44.<BR>--3 To<BR>wait, be patient; द्वित्राण्यहान्यर्हसि<BR>सोढुमर्हन् R. 5. 25, 15. 45.<BR>--4 To<BR>bear, support, bear up; क इदानीं<BR>सहकारमंतरेण पल्लवितामतिमुक्तलतां सहेत<BR>Ś. 3.<BR>--5 To conquer, defeat, oppose,<BR>be able to resist.<BR>--6 To suppress,<BR>stop.<BR>--7 To be able (with inf.).<BR>--Caus. (साहयति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to<BR>bear or suffer.<BR>--2 To make bearable<BR>or supportable; गुर्वपि<BR>विरहदुःखमाशाबंधः साहयति Ś. 4. 15. --Desid.<BR>(सिसहिषते) To wish to bear &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
सह a. [सहते सह्-अच्]<BR>1 Bearing,<BR>enduring, suffering.<BR>--2 Patient.<BR>--3<BR>Able; see असह.<BR>--हः<BR>1 The month<BR>मार्गशीर्ष.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva.<BR>--हः, हं<BR>Power, strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहन|सहनं|सहनः
सहन a. Bearing, enduring.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Bearing, enduring.<BR>--2 Patience,<BR>forbearance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शील a.<BR>patient, forgiving.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित्रं|सहित्र
सहित्रं Patience, forbearance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णु|सहिष्णुः
सहिष्णु a. [सह् --इष्णुच्]<BR>1 Able<BR>to bear or endure, capable of<BR>enduring; रविकिरणसहिष्णु क्लेशलेशैरभिन्नं<BR>Ś. 2. 4.<BR>--2 Patient, resigned,<BR>forbearing; सुकरस्तरुवत्सहिष्णुना<BR>रिपुरुन्मूलयितुं महानपि Ki. 2. 50.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णुता
सहिष्णुता --त्वं<BR>1 Power to bear or<BR>support.<BR>--2 Patience, resignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहिष्णुत्वं|सहिष्णुत्व
सहिष्णुता --त्वं<BR>1 Power to bear or<BR>support.<BR>--2 Patience, resignation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह|सहं|सहः
सह ind.<BR>1 With, together with,<BR>along with, accompanied by (with<BR>instr.); शशिना सह याति कौमुदी सह<BR>मेघेन तडित्प्रलीयते Ku. 4. 33.<BR>--2<BR>Together, simultaneously, at the same<BR>time; अस्तोदयौ सहैवासौ कुरुते<BR>नृपतिर्द्विषां Subhāṣ. (The following<BR>senses are given of this word:<BR>--साकल्य, सादृश्य, यौगपद्य, विद्यमानत्व, समृद्धि,<BR>संबंध, and सामर्थ्य.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्ययनं {1} studying together; U. 2. {2}<BR>fellow-studentship.<BR>--अध्यायिन् m.<BR>a fellow-student.<BR>--अर्थ a. {1} having<BR>the same object. {2} synonymous.<BR>--(र्थः) the same or common object.<BR>--आसनं sitting on the same seat,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-c" target="_blank">Page1111-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--उक्तिः f. a figure of speech in<BR>Rhetoric; सा सहोक्तिः सहार्थस्य बलादेकं<BR>द्विवाचकं K. P. 10; e. g. पपात भूमौ सह<BR>सैनिकाश्रुभिः R. 3. 61.<BR>--उटजः a hut<BR>made of leaves.<BR>--उदरः a uterine<BR>brother, brother of whole blood;<BR>Vikr. 1. 21.<BR>--उपमा a kind of<BR>Upamā.<BR>--ऊढः, --ऊढजः the son of a<BR>woman pregnant at marriage; (one<BR>of the 12 kinds of sons recognized<BR>in old Hindu law).<BR>--कार a. having<BR>the sound ह Nalod. 2. 14.<BR>--(र) {1}<BR>co-operation. {2} a mango; tree: क<BR>इदानीं सहकारमंतरेण पल्लवितामतिमुक्तलतां<BR>सहते Ś. 3. ˚भंजिका a kind of game.<BR>--कारिन्, --कृत्, --कृत्वन् a.<BR>co-operating. (--m.) a co-adjutor, associate,<BR>colleague.<BR>--कृत a. co-operated<BR>with, assisted or aided by.<BR>--गमनं<BR>{1} accompanying. {2} a woman's<BR>burning herself with her deceased<BR>husband's body, self-immolation of<BR>a widow.<BR>--चर a. accompanying,<BR>going or living with; U. 3. 8.<BR>--(रः)<BR>{1} a companion, friend, associate.<BR>{2} a follower, servant. {3} a<BR>husband. {4} a surety. (--री f.) {1} a<BR>female companion. {2} a wife, mate.<BR>--चरित a. accompanying, attending,<BR>associating with.<BR>--चारः {1}<BR>accompaniment. {2} agreement,<BR>harmony. {3} (in logic) the invariable<BR>accompaniment of the hetu (middle<BR>term) by the sādhya (major term).<BR>{4} right course (opp. व्यभिचार).<BR>--चारिन् see सहचर.<BR>--ज a. {1}<BR>inborn, natural, innate. {2}<BR>hereditary; Ś. 6. 1.<BR>--(जः) {1} a brother of<BR>whole blood. {2} the natural state or<BR>disposition. ˚अरिः a natural enemy.<BR>˚उदासीनः a born neutral. ˚मित्रं a<BR>natural friend.<BR>--जात a. natural; see<BR>सहज. {2} born together, twin-born.<BR>--दार a. {1} with a wife. {2}<BR>married.<BR>--देवः N. of the youngest of<BR>the five Pāṇḍavas; the twin brother<BR>of Nakula, born of Mādrī by the<BR>gods Aśvins. He is regarded as<BR>the type of manly beauty.<BR>--धर्मः<BR>same duties. ˚चारिन् m. a husband.<BR>˚चारिणी {1} a lawful wife, one legally<BR>married (also सहधर्मिणी in this<BR>sense). {2} a fellow-worker.<BR>--पथिन् m.<BR>--पंथाः m. f. a fellow-traveller.<BR>--पांशुक्रीडिन्, --पांशुकिल m. a friend<BR>from the earliest childhood.<BR>--भाविन्<BR>m. a friend, partisan, follower.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">Page1112-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--भू a. natural, innate; Ratn. 1. 2.<BR>--भोजनं eating in company with<BR>friends.<BR>--मरणं see सहगमन.<BR>--मृता<BR>a woman who has burnt herself<BR>with her husband.<BR>--युध्वन् m. a<BR>brother in arms.<BR>--रक्षस् m. one<BR>of the three kinds of<BR>sacrificial fires.<BR>--वसतिः --वासः dwelling<BR>together; सहवसतिमुपेत्य यैः प्रियायाः<BR>कृत इव मुग्धविलोकितोपदेशः Ś. 2. 3.<BR>--वासिन् m. a fellow-lodger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1111-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहता
सहता --त्वं Union, association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहत्वं|सहत्व
सहता --त्वं Union, association.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहरिः|सहरि
सहरिः The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहर्ष|सहर्षः
सहर्ष a. Glad, delighted.<BR>--र्षं<BR>ind. Gladly, delightedly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्
सहस् m. [सह् --असि]<BR>1 The<BR>month called Mārgaśīrṣa;<BR>Śi. 6. 57; 16. 47.<BR>--2 The winter season.<BR>--n.<BR>1 Power, might, strength.<BR>--2<BR>Force, violence.<BR>--3 Victory,<BR>conquering.<BR>--4 Lustre, brightness.<BR>--5<BR>Water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसा
सहसा ind.<BR>1 With force, forcibly.<BR>--2 Rashly, precipitately,<BR>inconsiderately; सहसा विदधीत न<BR>क्रियामविवेकः परमापदां पदं Ki. 2. 30.<BR>--3<BR>Suddenly, all at once; मातंगनक्रैः<BR>सहसोत्पतद्भिः R. 13. 11.<BR>--4 With a smile,<BR>smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहसान|सहसानः
सहसान a.<BR>1 Patient.<BR>--2<BR>Overpowering.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A peacock.<BR>--2 A<BR>sacrifice, an oblation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्यः|सहस्य
सहस्यः The month called<BR>Pausha; सहस्यरात्रीरुदवासतत्परा Ku. 5. 26.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रं|सहस्र
सहस्रं [समानं हसति हस् --र Tv.]<BR>1<BR>A thousand.<BR>--2 A large number.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशु, --अर्चिस्, --कर, --किरण,<BR>--दीधिति, --धामन्, पाद, मरीचि, रश्मि, m.<BR>the sun; Ś. 7. 4; R. 13. 44;<BR>Mu. 3. 17.<BR>--अक्ष a. {1} thousand-eyed.<BR>{2} vigilant.<BR>--(क्षः) {1} an epithet<BR>of Indra. {2} of Puruṣa;<BR>Rv. 10. 90. {3} of Śiva. {4} of Viṣṇu.<BR>--आननः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--अधिपतिः<BR>a governor of one thousand villages.<BR>--अवरः a fine below a thousand, or<BR>from five hundred to a<BR>thousand Paṇas.<BR>--कांडा white<BR>Dūrvā grass.<BR>--कृत्वस् ind. a<BR>thousand times.<BR>--गुण a. a<BR>thousand-fold.<BR>--द a. liberal.<BR>--(दः) an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--दंष्ट्रः a kind of<BR>fish.<BR>--दृश्, --नयन, --नेत्र, --लोचन m.<BR>{1} epithets of Indra. {2} of Viṣṇu.<BR>--दोस् m. an epithet of Arjuna<BR>Kārtavīrya.<BR>--धारः the discus of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">Page1112-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--(रा) a stream of water<BR>for the ablution of an idol poured<BR>through a vessel pierced with a<BR>number of holes.<BR>--पत्रं {1} a lotus;<BR>R. 7. 11. {2} the Sārasa bird.<BR>--पाद् m. an epithet of Puruṣa. {2}<BR>of Śiva. {3} of Viṣṇu. {4} of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--बाहुः {1} an epithet of<BR>king Kārtavīrya q. v. {2} of the<BR>demon Bāṇa. {3} of Śiva. (or of<BR>Viṣṇu according to some).<BR>--भुजः,<BR>--मौलि m. epithets of Viṣṇu.<BR>--भुजा N. of Durgā.<BR>--मूर्वन् m. N.<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--रोमन् n. a blanket.<BR>--वदनः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--वीर्या<BR>Dūrvā grass.<BR>--वेधं {1} sorrel. {2}<BR>a kind of sour gruel.<BR>--वेधिन् m.<BR>musk. (--n.) asa-fœtida.<BR>--शिखरः<BR>an epithet of the Vindhya<BR>mountain.<BR>--श्रवणः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--हर्यश्वः the car of Indra.<BR>--हस्तः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रतय
सहस्रतय a. (यी f.)<BR>Thousandfold.<BR>--यं A thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रधा
सहस्रधा ind. In a thousand parts,<BR>a thousand-fold; दीर्ये किं न<BR>सहस्रधाहमथवा रामेण किं दुष्करं U. 6. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रशस्
सहस्रशस् ind. By thousands.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्रिन्
सहस्रिन् a.<BR>1 Possessed of a<BR>thousand; इच्छति शती सहस्रं सहस्री<BR>लक्षमीहते Pt. 5. 82.<BR>--2 Consisting<BR>of thousands.<BR>--3 Amounting to a<BR>thousand (as a fine); Ms. 8. 376.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A body of a thousand men<BR>&c.<BR>--2 The commander of a<BR>thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहस्वत्|सहस्वन्त्
सहस्वत् a. Strong, powerful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहा
सहा<BR>1 The earth.<BR>--2 The<BR>aloeplant or flower.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायः|सहाय
सहायः [सह् एति इ-अच्]<BR>1 A<BR>friend, companion; सहायसाध्याः<BR>प्रदिशंति सिद्धयः Ki. 14. 44;<BR>Ku. 3. 21.<BR>--2 A follower, an adherent.<BR>--3 An ally.<BR>--4 A helper, patron.<BR>--5 The ruddy goose.<BR>--6 A kind<BR>of perfume.<BR>--7 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायता
सहायता, --त्वं<BR>1 A number of<BR>companions.<BR>--2 Companionship,<BR>union, friendship.<BR>--3 Help,<BR>assistance; कुसुमास्तरणे सहायतां बहुशः<BR>सौम्य गतस्त्वमावयोः Ku. 4. 35;<BR>R. 9. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायत्वं|सहायत्व
सहायता, --त्वं<BR>1 A number of<BR>companions.<BR>--2 Companionship,<BR>union, friendship.<BR>--3 Help,<BR>assistance; कुसुमास्तरणे सहायतां बहुशः<BR>सौम्य गतस्त्वमावयोः Ku. 4. 35;<BR>R. 9. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहायवत्|सहायवन्त्
सहायवत् a.<BR>1 Having a friend.<BR>--2 Befriended, assisted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहारः|सहार
सहारः<BR>1 The mango tree.<BR>--2<BR>Universal destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहित|सहितः
सहित a.<BR>1 Accompanied or<BR>attended by, together with, united<BR>or associated with; पवनाग्निसमागमो<BR>ह्ययं सहितं ब्रह्म यदस्त्रतेजसा R. 8. 4.<BR>--2 Borne, endured.<BR>--तं ind.<BR>Together with, with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहितृ
सहितृ a. Enduring, patient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहुरिः|सहुरि
सहुरिः The sun. --f. The earth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृदय|सहृदयः
सहृदय a.<BR>1 Good-hearted, kind,<BR>compassionate.<BR>--2 Sincere.<BR>--यः<BR>1<BR>A learned man.<BR>--2 An appreciator<BR>(of merits &c.), a man of taste, a<BR>man of critical faculty; इत्युपदेशं कवेः<BR>सहृदयस्य च करोति K. P. 1;<BR>परिष्क्रुर्वंत्यन्ये सहृदयधुरीणाः कतिपये R. G.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहृल्लेख|सहृल्लेखं
सहृल्लेख a. Questionable,<BR>doubtful.<BR>--खं Questionable food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहेल
सहेल a. Sportive, playful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोढः|सहोढ
सहोढः A thief caught with the<BR>stolen property in his possession.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सहोर|सहोरः
सहोर a. Good, excellent.<BR>--रः<BR>A saint, sage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्य|सह्यं|सह्यः
सह्य a.<BR>1 Bearable, supportable,<BR>endurable; अपि सह्या ते शिरोवेदना<BR>Mu. 5; M. 3. 4.<BR>--2 To be borne or<BR>endured; कथं तूष्णीं सह्यो<BR>निरवधिरिदानीं तु विरहः U. 3. 44.<BR>--3 Able to<BR>bear.<BR>--4 Adequate or equal<BR>to.<BR>--5 Sweet, agreeable.<BR>--6<BR>Strong, powerful.<BR>--ह्यः N. of one<BR>of the seven principal mountain<BR>ranges in India, a part of the western<BR>Ghats at some distance from the<BR>sea; रामास्त्रोत्सारितोण्यासीत्सह्यलग्न<BR>इवार्णवः R. 4. 53, 52; Ki. 18. 5.<BR>--ह्यं<BR>1 Health, convalescence.<BR>--2<BR>Assistance.<BR>--3 Fitness, adequacy.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मजा N. of the river Kāverī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सा
सा<BR>1 N. of Lakṣmī.<BR>--2 Of<BR>Pārvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयात्रिकः|सांयात्रिक
सांयात्रिकः A sea-trader, a<BR>merchant trading by sea (पोतवणिक्);<BR>Pt. 1. 316.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांयुगीन|सांयुगीनः
सांयुगीन a. [संयुगे साधुः ख]<BR>Warlike, skilled in war; भवांश्च सांयुगीनः<BR>सहायो नः V. 5; R. 11. 30.<BR>--नः A<BR>great warrior, a soldier skilled in<BR>war; Ku. 2. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांराविणं|सांराविण
सांराविणं [cf. P. III. 3. 44,<BR>V. 4. 15] A general or loud shout,<BR>tumultuous uproar; उत्तालाः<BR>कटपूतनाप्रभृतयः सांराविणं कुर्वते Māl. 5. 11;<BR>Bk. 7. 43.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवत्सर|सांवत्सरः
सांवत्सर (री f.), सांवत्सरिक (की<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">Page1113-a+ 53</a>]<BR>%ऋ%।) a. Annual, yearly.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An<BR>astrologer.<BR>--2 An almanac-maker.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1112-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवादिक|सांवादिकः
सांवादिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Colloquial.<BR>--2 Controversial.<BR>--कः A<BR>disputant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांवृत्तिक
सांवृत्तिक a. (की f.) Illusory,<BR>phenomenal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांशयिक|सांशयिकः
सांशयिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Doubtful.<BR>--2 Uncertain, irresolute.<BR>--कं<BR>A doubtful or dangerous deed;<BR>Pt. 3. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसारिक
सांसारिक a. (की f.) Worldly,<BR>mundane; सांसारिकेषु च सुखेषु वयं<BR>रसज्ञाः U. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांसिद्धिक
सांसिद्धिक a.<BR>1 Natural,<BR>existing naturally, innate, inherent.<BR>--2<BR>Effected naturally, spontaneous.<BR>--3<BR>Absolute.<BR>--4 Effected by<BR>supernatural means.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द्रवः natural<BR>fluidity (opp. नैमित्तिक ‘generated’)<BR>(belonging to water only).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्थानिकः|सांस्थानिक
सांस्थानिकः A<BR>fellow-countryman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांस्राविणं|सांस्राविण
सांस्राविणं A general flow or<BR>stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांहननिक
सांहननिक a. (की f.) Bodily,<BR>corporeal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकं|साक
साकं A vegetable, herb; cf. शाक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकम्
साकम् ind.<BR>1 With, together<BR>with (with instr.); यांती गुरुजनैः<BR>साकं स्मयमानाननांबुजा Bv. 2. 132;<BR>1. 41; Mu. 3. 10.<BR>--2 At the same<BR>time, simultaneously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकल्यं|साकल्य
साकल्यं Entirety, totality, the<BR>whole or entire part of a thing;<BR>यावत्साकल्ये; Nalod. 3. 19. (साकल्येन<BR>‘entirely, completely, thoroughly’;<BR>Ms. 12. 25).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकांक्ष|साकाङ्क्ष
साकांक्ष a.<BR>1 Desirous.<BR>--2<BR>Having significance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकूत
साकूत a.<BR>1 Having meaning,<BR>significant, meaning; साकूतस्मितं<BR>Gīt. 2; साकूतं वचनं &c.<BR>--2 Intentional.<BR>--3 Amorous, wanton.<BR>--तं ind.<BR>1<BR>Meaningly, significantly; as in<BR>साकूतं मां निर्वर्ण्य.<BR>--2 Amorously.<BR>--3<BR>Feelingly, pathetically.<BR>--4 Attentively.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेतं|साकेत
साकेतं N. of the city of<BR>Ayodhyā; साकेतनार्योंऽजलिभिः प्रणेमुः<BR>R. 14. 13, 13. 79, 18. 36; अरुणद्यवनः<BR>साकेतं Mbh.<BR>--ताः (m. pl.) The<BR>inhabitants of Ayodhyā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साकेतकः|साकेतक
साकेतकः An inhabitant of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">Page1113-b+ 55</a>]<BR>Ayodhyā.<BR>--कं = साकेतं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्तुकं|साक्तुक|साक्तुकः
साक्तुकं A quantity of fried<BR>grain (सक्तु).<BR>--कः Barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षात्
साक्षात् ind.<BR>1 In the presence<BR>of, before the very eyes, visibly,<BR>openly, evidently.<BR>--2 In person,<BR>actually, in bodily form; साक्षात्<BR>प्रियामुपगतामपहाय पूर्वं Ś. 6. 15;<BR>1. 6.<BR>--3 Directly. In comp. it is often<BR>translated by ‘incarnate’;<BR>साक्षाद्यमः; or by ‘open, direct’;<BR>तत्साक्षात्प्रतिषेधः कोपाय Māl. 1. 11. (<BR>साक्षात्कृ {1} to see with one's own eyes,<BR>realize personally. {2} to have an<BR>intuitive perception or manifestation<BR>of; साक्षात्कृतधर्माण ॠषयः U. 7).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करणं {1} causing to be<BR>visibly present, {2} making evident<BR>to the senses. {3} intuitive<BR>perception.<BR>--कारः perception,<BR>apprehension, knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षिन्
साक्षिन् a. (णी f.) [सह अक्षि<BR>अस्य; साक्षाद् द्रष्टा साक्षी वा P. V. 2. 91]<BR>1 Seeing, observing, witnessing.<BR>--2<BR>Attesting, testifying. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>witness, an observer, an<BR>eye-witness; फलं तपःसाक्षिषु दृष्टमेष्वपि<BR>Ku. 5. 60.<BR>--2 The Supreme Being.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द्वैधं divergent evidence,<BR>discrepancy between witnesses.<BR>--प्रत्ययः the evidence of witnesses.<BR>--भावित a. borne out or proved by<BR>evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्ष्यं|साक्ष्य
साक्ष्यं<BR>1 Evidence, testimony;<BR>तमेव चाधाय विवाहसाक्ष्ये R. 7. 20.<BR>--2<BR>Attestation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साक्षेप
साक्षेप a. Taunting, abusive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साखेय|साखेयः
साखेय a. (यी f.)<BR>1 Relating<BR>to a friend.<BR>--2 Friendly, amicable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साख्यं|साख्य
साख्यं Friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सागरः|सागर
सागरः [सगरेण निर्वृत्तः अण्]<BR>1 The<BR>ocean, sea; सागरः सागरोपमः; (fig.<BR>also); दयासागर, विद्यासागर &c.;<BR>cf. सगर.<BR>--2 The number ‘four’ or<BR>‘seven’.<BR>--3 A kind of deer.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुकूल a. situated along the<BR>seacoast.<BR>--अंत a. bounded by the sea,<BR>sea-girt.<BR>--अंबरा, --नेमिः, मेखला the<BR>earth.<BR>--आलयः N. of Varuṇa.<BR>--उत्थं sea-salt.<BR>--गा {1} a river. {2}<BR>the Ganges.<BR>--गामिनी a river.<BR>--प्लवनं navigating (the ocean).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्नि
साग्नि a.<BR>1 Having fire.<BR>--2<BR>Taking the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्निक|साग्निकः
साग्निक a.<BR>1 Maintaining or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">Page1113-c+ 55</a>]<BR>possessing fire.<BR>--2 Attended by fire.<BR>--कः A house-holder who<BR>maintains the sacred fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साग्र
साग्र a.<BR>1 Entire.<BR>--2 With a<BR>surplus, more than.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकर्यं|साङ्कर्य|सांकर्य|साङ्कर्य्य
सांकर्यं Mixture, confusion,<BR>promiscuous or confused mixture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकल|साङ्कल|साङ्कलं
सांकल a. (ली f.) Produced or<BR>effected by addition.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकाश्यं|साङ्काश्य|सांकाश्य
सांकाश्यं --श्या N. of the capital<BR>of Kuśadhvaja, brother of Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकाश्या|साङ्काश्या
सांकाश्यं --श्या N. of the capital<BR>of Kuśadhvaja, brother of Janaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांकेतिक|साङ्केतिक
सांकेतिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Symbolical, indicatory.<BR>--2 Conventional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांक्षेपिक|साङ्क्षेपिक|साङ्क्षेपिकः
सांक्षेपिक a. (की f.) Abridged,<BR>short, concise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांख्य|साङ्ख्य|सांख्यं|सांख्यः|साङ्ख्यः
सांख्य a. [संख्यया निर्वृत्तं अण्]<BR>1<BR>Relating to number.<BR>--2<BR>Calculating, enumerating.<BR>--3<BR>Discriminative.<BR>--4 Deliberating, reasoning, a<BR>reasoner; त्वं गतिः सर्वसांख्यानां<BR>योगिनां त्वं परायणं Mb.<BR>--ख्यः, --ख्यं N.<BR>of one of the six systems of Hindu<BR>philosophy, attributed to the sage<BR>Kapila; (this philosophy is so<BR>called because it ‘enumerates’<BR>twentyfive Tattvas or true principles; and<BR>its chief object is to effect the final<BR>emancipation of the twenty-fifth<BR>Tattva, i. e. the Puruṣa or soul,<BR>from the bonds of this worldly<BR>existence-the fetters of<BR>phenomenal creation-by conveying a correct<BR>knowledge of the twenty-four other<BR>Tattvas and by properly<BR>discriminating the Soul from them. It<BR>regards the whole universe as a<BR>development of an inanimate<BR>principle called Prakṛti q. v., while<BR>the Puruṣa is altogether passive<BR>and simply a looker-on. It<BR>agrees with the Vedānta in<BR>being synthetical and so differs from<BR>the analytical Nyāya or Vaiśeṣika;<BR>but its great point of divergence<BR>from the Vedānta is that it<BR>maintains two principles which the<BR>Vedānta denies, and that it does not<BR>admit God as the creator and<BR>controller of the universe, which the<BR>Vedānta affirms); सांख्यमिव<BR>कपिलाधिष्ठितं K.<BR>--ख्यः<BR>1 A follower of<BR>the Sāṃkhya philosophy; Bg. 3. 3,<BR>5. 5.<BR>--2 An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रसादः, --मुख्यः epithets of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांग|साङ्ग
सांग a. [सहांगेन अंगैर्वा]<BR>1 Having<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">Page1114-a+ 54</a>]<BR>members.<BR>--2 Complete in every<BR>part.<BR>--3 Together with the six<BR>angas or auxiliary members.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1113-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांगतिक|साङ्गतिक|सांगतिकः
सांगतिक a. (की f.) Relating<BR>to union or society, associating.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A visitor, guest, new comer.<BR>--2 One who comes to transact<BR>business.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांगमः|साङ्गम|सांगम|साङ्गमः
सांगमः Union, meeting; cf. संगम.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांग्रामिक|साङ्ग्रामिक|सांग्रामिकः|साङ्ग्रामिकः
सांग्रामिक a. (की f.) Relating<BR>to war, warlike, martial; U. 5. 22.<BR>--कः A general, commander.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांघातिक
सांघातिक a. (की f.) Greatly<BR>destructive, very deadly or fatal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचि
साचि ind. Obliquely, crookedly,<BR>awry, in a side-long manner; साचि<BR>लोचनयुगं नमयंती Ki. 9. 44, 10. 57.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वाटिका the white-flowered<BR>hog-weed.<BR>--विलोकितं a side-long<BR>look, leer. (साचीकृ ‘to turn or<BR>bend aside, make crooked; निनाय<BR>साचीकृतचारुवक्त्रः R. 6. 14;<BR>Ku. 3. 68; साचीकरोत्याननं M. 4. 14).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साचिव्यं|साचिव्य
साचिव्यं<BR>1 The office of a<BR>minister, ministership.<BR>--2 Ministry,<BR>administration.<BR>--3 Friendship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साजात्यं|साजात्य
साजात्यं<BR>1 Sameness of caste,<BR>class, or kind.<BR>--2 Community of<BR>genus, homogeneousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांजनः|साञ्जन|साञ्जनः
सांजनः A lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साट्
साट् {c10c} U. (साटयति-ते) To show,<BR>manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साटोप
साटोप a.<BR>1 Elated or puffed up<BR>with pride, haughty.<BR>--2 Majestic,<BR>stately.<BR>--3 Swollen, filled or<BR>charged with, (as with water);<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--पं ind. Proudly,<BR>arrogantly, in a stately manner, struttingly;<BR>as in साटोपं परिक्रामति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्
सात् ind. A Taddhita affix<BR>added to a word to show that something<BR>is completely changed into the thing<BR>expressed by that word, or that it<BR>is left at the complete disposal or<BR>control of that thing; भस्मसात् भू<BR>‘to be completely reduced to<BR>ashes’; अग्निसात्कृत्वा M. 5;<BR>भस्मसात्कृतवतः पितृद्विषः पात्रसाच्च<BR>वसुधां ससागरां R. 11. 86; विभज्य<BR>मेरुर्न यदर्थिसात्कृतः N. 1. 16; so<BR>ब्राह्मणसात्, राजसात् &c.; Śi. 14. 36.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात|सातं
सात p. p.<BR>1 Given.<BR>--2<BR>Destroyed.<BR>--तं Pleasure, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातत्यं|सातत्य
सातत्यं Continuity, permanence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातवाहनः|सातवाहन
सातवाहनः N. of king<BR>Sālivāhana.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातिः|साति
सातिः f.<BR>1 Giving, a gift,<BR>donation.<BR>--2 Gaining, obtaining.<BR>--3<BR>Help.<BR>--4 Destruction.<BR>--5 End,<BR>conclusion.<BR>--6 Sharp or acute pain.<BR>--7 Cessation.<BR>--8 Wealth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातीनः|सातीन
सातीनः, सातीनकः, सातीलकः Pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातीनकः|सातीनक
सातीनः, सातीनकः, सातीलकः Pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सातीलकः|सातीलक
सातीनः, सातीनकः, सातीलकः Pease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्त्विक|सात्त्विकः
सात्त्विक a. (की f.) [सत्त्वगुणेन<BR>तत्कार्येण मनसा वा निर्वृत्तः ठञ्]<BR>1 Real,<BR>essential.<BR>--2 True, genuine, natural.<BR>--3 Honest, sincere, good.<BR>--4<BR>Virtuous, amiable.<BR>--5 Vigorous.<BR>--6<BR>Endowed with the quality Sattva<BR>(goodness).<BR>--7 Belonging to or<BR>derived from the Sattva quality; ये<BR>चैव सात्त्विका भावाः Bg. 7. 12, 14. 16.<BR>--8 Caused by internal feeling or<BR>sentiment (as of love),<BR>internal;<BR>तद्भूरिसात्त्विकविकारमपास्तधैर्यमाचार्यकं विजयि मान्मथमाविरासीत्<BR>Māl. 1. 26.<BR>--कः<BR>1 An external indication<BR>of (internal) feeling or emotion,<BR>one of the kinds of Bhāvas in<BR>poetry; these are eight:<BR>--स्तंभः<BR>स्वेदोऽथ रोमांचः स्वरभंगोऽथ वेपथुः । वैवर्ण्यमश्रु<BR>प्रलय इत्यष्टौ सात्त्विकाः स्मृताः ॥ see<BR>S. D. 164 also.<BR>--2 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of Brahman.<BR>--की N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यकिः|सात्यकि
सात्यकिः N. of a Yādava<BR>warrior, who acted as charioteer to<BR>Kṛṣṇa, and took part with the<BR>Pāṇḍavas in the great war.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यवतः|सात्यवत
सात्यवतः, सात्यवतेयः A<BR>metronymic of the sage Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्यवतेयः|सात्यवतेय
सात्यवतः, सात्यवतेयः A<BR>metronymic of the sage Vyāsa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वत्|सात्वन्त्
सात्वत् m.<BR>1 A follower,<BR>worshipper (of Kṛṣṇa &c.).<BR>--2 A man of<BR>the Yādava tribe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वतः|सात्वत
सात्वतः<BR>1 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--2 Of<BR>Balarāma.<BR>--3 The son of an outcast<BR>Vaiśya.<BR>--ताः (m. pl) N. of a<BR>people; Śi. 16. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सात्वती
सात्वती<BR>1 N. of one of the<BR>four dramatic styles; see<BR>S. D. 416.<BR>--2 N. of the mother of<BR>Śiśupāla; Śi. 2. 11.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादः|साद
सादः [सद्-घञ्]<BR>1 Sinking,<BR>settling down.<BR>--2 Exhaustion,<BR>weariness; उदितोरुसादमोतवेपथुमत्<BR>Śi. 9. 77.<BR>--3 Leanness, thinness,<BR>emaciation; शरीरसादादसमग्रभूषणा R. 3. 2.<BR>--4 Perishing, decay, loss,<BR>destruction, cessation; गतिविभ्रमसादनीरवा<BR>R. 8. 58; Nalod. 3. 24.<BR>--5 Pain,<BR>torment.<BR>--6 Clearness, purity.<BR>--7<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">Page1114-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Going, motion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादनं|सादन
सादनं<BR>1 Wearying, fatiguing.<BR>--2<BR>Destroying.<BR>--3 Exhaustion.<BR>--4 A<BR>house, dwelling.<BR>--नी Exhaustion,<BR>decay, fatigue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिः|सादि
सादिः [सद्-इण्]<BR>1 A charioteer.<BR>--2 A warrior.<BR>--3 A dispirited<BR>person.<BR>--4 Air, wind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादित|सादितः
सादित p. p.<BR>1 Made to sit down.<BR>--2 Depressed, dispirited.<BR>--3<BR>Wearied, exhausted.<BR>--4 Destroyed,<BR>exterminated.<BR>--5 Wasted, decayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादिन्
सादिन् a. [सद् --णिनि]<BR>1 Sitting<BR>down.<BR>--2 Exhausting, destroying<BR>&c. --m.<BR>1 A horseman.<BR>--2 One<BR>riding on an elephant or seated in<BR>a car.<BR>--3 A charioteer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सादृश्यं|सादृश्य
सादृश्यं<BR>1 Likeness, resemblance,<BR>similarity; संति पुनर्नामधेयसादृश्यानि<BR>Ś. 7; तवाक्षिसादृश्यमिव प्रयुंजते<BR>Ku. 5. 35, 7. 16; R. 1. 40; 15. 67.<BR>--2<BR>A likeness, a portrait, an image;<BR>मत्सादृश्यं विरहतनु वा भावगम्यं लिखंती<BR>Me. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यंत|साद्यन्त
साद्यंत a. Entire, whole, complete.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साद्यस्क|साद्यस्कः
साद्यस्क a. (स्की f.) Quick,<BR>instantaneous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्
साध् {vI.v} {c5c} P. (साध्नोति)<BR>1 To<BR>complete, finish, accomplish.<BR>--2 To<BR>conquer. {vII.v} {c4c} P. (साध्यति) To<BR>be completed or accomplished.<BR>--Caus.<BR>1 To accomplish, effect,<BR>bring about, perform; अपि साधय<BR>साधयेप्सितं N. 2. 62; यावद्यते<BR>साधयितुं तवार्थं R. 5. 25, Ku. 2. 33.<BR>--2<BR>To complete, finish, conclude.<BR>--3<BR>To gain, secure, obtain;<BR>R. 17. 38, Ms. 6. 75.<BR>--4 To prove,<BR>substantiate.<BR>--5 To subdue, overpower,<BR>conquer (as a foe &c.), win<BR>over; न हि साम्ना न दानेन न भेदेन च<BR>पांडवाः । शक्याः साधयितुं Mb.<BR>--6 To kill,<BR>destroy; सुग्रीवांतकमासेदुः साधयिष्याम<BR>इत्यरिं Bk. 7. 31.<BR>--7 To learn,<BR>understand.<BR>--8 To cure, heal.<BR>--9<BR>To go, depart, go one's way;<BR>साधयाम्यहमविघ्नमस्तु ते R. 11. 91;<BR>Ś. 1. 7; प्रायेण ण्यंतकः साधिर्गमेरर्थे प्रयुज्यते<BR>S. D.<BR>--10 To recover (as a debt).<BR>--11 To make perfect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधक|साधकः
साधक a. [साध्-ण्वुल्, सिध्-णिच् ण्वुल्<BR>साधादेशः वा Tv.] (धका or धिका f.)<BR>1 Accomplishing, fulfilling,<BR>effecting, completing.<BR>--2 Efficient,<BR>effective; Ku. 3. 12.<BR>--3<BR>Skilful, adept.<BR>--4 Effecting by<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-a" target="_blank">Page1115-a+ 57</a>]<BR>magic, magical.<BR>--5 Assisting, helping.<BR>--कः A magician, one possessed of<BR>supernatural powers, a yogin;<BR>Māl. 5. 1.<BR>--का N. of Durgā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1114-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधन|साधनं
साधन a. (नी f.) [साध् णिच् ल्यु<BR>ल्युद् वा] Accomplishing, effecting<BR>&c.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Accomplishing, effecting,<BR>performing; as in स्वार्थसाधनं.<BR>--2<BR>Fulfilment, accomplishment,<BR>complete attainment of an object;<BR>प्रजार्थसाधने तौ हि पर्यायोद्यतकार्मुकौ<BR>R. 4. 16.<BR>--3 A means, an expedient, a<BR>means of accomplishing anything;<BR>शरीरमाद्यं खलु धर्मसाधनं Ku. 5. 33,<BR>52; R. 1. 19. 4. 36, 62.<BR>--4 An<BR>instrument, agent; कुठारः<BR>छिदिक्रियासाधनम्.<BR>--5 The efficient cause, source,<BR>cause in general.<BR>--6 The instrumental<BR>case.<BR>--7 Implement, apparatus.<BR>--8<BR>Appliance, materials.<BR>--9 Matter,<BR>ingredients, substance.<BR>--10 An<BR>army or a part thereof; Mu. 5. 10.<BR>--11 Aid, help, assistance (in<BR>general).<BR>--12 Proof, substantiation,<BR>demonstration.<BR>--13 The hetu or<BR>middle term in a syllogism, reason,<BR>that which leads to a conclusion;<BR>साध्ये निश्चितमन्वयेन घटितं बिभ्रत्सपक्षे<BR>स्थितिं व्यावृत्तं च विपक्षतो भवति<BR>यत्तत्साधनं सिद्धये Mu. 5. 10.<BR>--14<BR>Subduing, overcoming.<BR>--15 Subduing<BR>by charms.<BR>--16 Accomplishing<BR>anything by charms or magic.<BR>--17<BR>Healing, curing.<BR>--18 Killing,<BR>destroying; फलं च तस्य प्रतिसाधनं<BR>Ki. 14. 17.<BR>--19 Conciliating,<BR>propitiating, winning over.<BR>--20 Going<BR>out, setting forward, departure.<BR>--21<BR>Going after, following.<BR>--22<BR>Penance, self-mortification.<BR>--23<BR>Attainment of final beatitude.<BR>--24 A<BR>medicinal preparation, drug,<BR>medicine.<BR>--25 (In law) Enforcement<BR>of the delivery of anything, or of<BR>the payment of debt,<BR>infliction of fine.<BR>--26 A bodily organ.<BR>--27 The penis.<BR>--28 An udder.<BR>--29<BR>Wealth.<BR>--30 Friendship.<BR>--31 Profit,<BR>advantage.<BR>--32 Burning a dead<BR>body.<BR>--33 Obsequies.<BR>--34 Killing<BR>or oxydation of metals.<BR>--Comp.<BR>अर्ह a. worthy of being proved or<BR>accomplished.<BR>--क्रिया {1} a finite<BR>verb. {2} an action connected with<BR>a Kāraka.<BR>--पत्रं a document used<BR>as evidence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनता
साधनता, --त्वं<BR>1 The state of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-b" target="_blank">Page1115-b+ 57</a>]<BR>having means, possession of means to<BR>accomplish a desired object;<BR>प्रतिकूलतामुपगते हि विधौ विफलत्वमेति<BR>बहुसाधनता Śi. 9. 6.<BR>--2 The state of<BR>perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधनत्वं|साधनत्व
साधनता, --त्वं<BR>1 The state of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-b" target="_blank">Page1115-b+ 57</a>]<BR>having means, possession of means to<BR>accomplish a desired object;<BR>प्रतिकूलतामुपगते हि विधौ विफलत्वमेति<BR>बहुसाधनता Śi. 9. 6.<BR>--2 The state of<BR>perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधना
साधना<BR>1 Accomplishment,<BR>fulfilment, completion.<BR>--2 Worship,<BR>adoration.<BR>--3 Conciliation,<BR>propitiation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिका
साधिका<BR>1 A skilful or<BR>accomplished woman.<BR>--2 Deep sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधित|साधितः
साधित p. p.<BR>1 Accomplished<BR>effected, achieved.<BR>--2 Completed,<BR>finished.<BR>--3 Proved, demonstrated.<BR>--4<BR>Obtained, secured.<BR>--5 Discharged.<BR>--6 Overcome, subdued.<BR>--7 Made<BR>good, recovered.<BR>--8 Fined.<BR>--9 Made<BR>to pay.<BR>--10 Awarded (as fine or<BR>punishment).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्य|साध्यः
साध्य a. [साध्-णिच् यत्]<BR>1 To be<BR>effected or accomplished, to be<BR>brought about; साध्ये सिद्धिर्विधीयतां<BR>H. 2. 15.<BR>--2 Feasible, practicable,<BR>attainable.<BR>--3 To be proved or<BR>demonstrated; आप्तवागनुमानाभ्यां साध्यं<BR>त्वां प्रति का कथा R. 10. 28.<BR>--4 To<BR>be established or made good.<BR>--5<BR>To be inferred or concluded;<BR>अनुमानं तदुक्तं यत्साध्यसाधनयोर्वचः<BR>K. P. 10.<BR>--6 To be conquered or subdued,<BR>conquerable; Ku. 3. 15, Pt. 3. 27.<BR>--7 Curable.<BR>--8 To be killed or<BR>destroyed.<BR>--ध्यः<BR>1 A particular class<BR>of celestial beings; cf. Ms. 1. 22,<BR>3. 195.<BR>--2 A deity in general.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a Mantra.<BR>--ध्यं<BR>1<BR>Accomplishment, perfection.<BR>--2 The thing to<BR>be proved or established, the<BR>matter at issue.<BR>--3 (In logic) The<BR>predicate of a proposition, the<BR>major term in a syllogism; साध्ये<BR>निश्चितमन्वयेन घटितं…… &c. ; यत्साध्यं<BR>स्वयमेव तुल्यमुभयोः पक्षे विरुद्धं च यत्<BR>Mu. 5. 10.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभावः the<BR>absence of the major term.<BR>--ऋषिः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--पक्षः the plaint<BR>in a law-suit.<BR>--सिद्धिः f. {1}<BR>accomplishment. {2} conclusion. ˚पादः<BR>judgment, decision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यता
साध्यता<BR>1 Feasibility,<BR>practicability.<BR>--2 Curableness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवच्छेदकं that which marks out<BR>or measures the साध्य or major term,<BR>its characteristic property.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्यवत्|साध्यवन्त्
साध्यवत् m. The party on whom<BR>rests the onus probandi or burden<BR>of proof in a law-suit. --n. That<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">Page1115-c+ 56</a>]<BR>which contains the साध्य or major<BR>term.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधंतः|साधन्त|साधंत|साधन्तः
साधंतः A mendicant, beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधर्म्यं|साधर्म्य
साधर्म्यं<BR>1 Sameness or<BR>community of duty, office &c.; पंचमं<BR>लोकपालानामूचुः साधर्म्ययोगतः R. 17. 78.<BR>--2 Sameness of nature, common<BR>character, likeness, community of<BR>properties; साधर्म्यमुपमा भेदे<BR>K. P. 10; Bg. 14. 2, Bhāṣā P. 12.<BR>--3<BR>Being of the same religion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण|साधारणः
साधारण a. (णा or णी f.)<BR>1<BR>Common (to two or more), joint;<BR>साधारणोऽयं प्रणयः Ś. 3; साधारणो<BR>भूषणभूष्यभावः Ku. 1. 42; R. 16. 5, V. 2. 16.<BR>--2<BR>Ordinary, common; साधारणी न खलु<BR>बाधा भवस्य Aśvad. 10.<BR>--3 General,<BR>universal.<BR>--4 Mingled, mixed with,<BR>in common with; उत्कंठासाधारणं<BR>परितोषमनुभवामि Ś. 4; वीज्यते स हि संसुप्तः<BR>श्वाससाधारणानिलैः Ku. 2. 42.<BR>--5<BR>Equal, similar, like.<BR>--6 (In logic)<BR>Belonging to more than one<BR>instance alleged, one of the three<BR>divisions of the fallacy called अनैकांतिक<BR>q.v.<BR>--णं<BR>1 A common or general rule,<BR>a rule or precept generally<BR>applicable.<BR>--2 A generic property.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--देशः a wild marshy country.<BR>--धनं joint property.<BR>--धर्मः {1} a<BR>common or universal duty; (अहिंसा<BR>सत्यमस्तेयं शौचमिंद्रियनिग्रहः । दंभः<BR>क्षमार्जवं दानं धर्मं साधारणं विदुः ॥) {2} the<BR>common duty of procreation; (<BR>प्रजनार्थं स्त्रियः सृष्ठाः संतानार्थं च मानवाः ।<BR>तस्मात्साधारणो धर्मः श्रुतौ पत्न्या सहोदितः ॥).<BR>--स्त्री a common woman, harlot,<BR>prostitute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणता
साधारणता त्वं<BR>1 Community,<BR>universality.<BR>--2 Joint interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणत्वं|साधारणत्व
साधारणता त्वं<BR>1 Community,<BR>universality.<BR>--2 Joint interest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणी
साधारणी<BR>1 A twig of bamboo.<BR>--2<BR>A key.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारणीकृ
साधारणीकृ {c8c} U. To share with,<BR>divide; केन वान्येन साधारणीकरोमि दुःखं<BR>K.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधारण्यं|साधारण्य
साधारण्यं Commonness; see<BR>साधारणता.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधु|साधुः
साधु a. (धु or ध्वी f.; compar.<BR>साधीयस्; superl. साधिष्ठ) [साध्-उन्]<BR>1 Good,<BR>excellent, perfect; यद्यत्साधु न<BR>चित्रे स्याक्त्रियते तत्तदन्यथा Ś. 6. 13;<BR>आपरितोषाद्विदुषां न साधु मन्ये<BR>प्रयोगविज्ञानं 1. 2.<BR>--2 Fit, proper, right;<BR>as in साधुवृत्त, साधुसमाचार.<BR>--3<BR>Virtuous, righteous, honourable, pious.<BR>--4 (a) Kind, well-disposed;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-a" target="_blank">Page1116-a+ 55</a>]<BR>R. 2. 28; Pt. 1. 247. (b)<BR>Well-behaved (with loc.); मातरि साधुः Sk.<BR>--5 Correct, pure, classical (as<BR>language).<BR>--6 Pleasing, agreeable,<BR>pleasant; अतोऽर्हसि क्षंतुमसाधु साधु<BR>वा Ki. 1. 4.<BR>--7 Noble, well-born,<BR>of noble descent.<BR>--धुः<BR>1 A good or<BR>virtuous man; R. 13. 65, 2. 62;<BR>Me. 80.<BR>--2 A sage, saint; साधोः<BR>प्रकोपितस्यापि मनो नायाति विक्रियां<BR>Subhāṣ.<BR>--3 A merchant;<BR>H. 2. 73.<BR>--4 A Jaina saint.<BR>--5 A usurer,<BR>money-lender. --ind.<BR>1 Well,<BR>welldone, very nice, bravo; साधु गीतं<BR>Ś. 1; साधु रे पिंगल वानर साधु M. 4.<BR>--2 Enough, away with.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आचार a. well-conducted, pious,<BR>virtuous.<BR>--ज a. noble, of a noble<BR>family.<BR>--दर्शन a. {1} good-looking.<BR>{2} thoughtful, prudent.<BR>--धी a.<BR>kind, well-disposed. (--f.) a<BR>motherin-law.<BR>--भावः kindness.<BR>--वादः a<BR>cry of ‘well done’, a cry of<BR>approbation; Śi. 18. 55.<BR>--वाहः, --वाहिन्<BR>m. a well-trained horse.<BR>--वृक्षः the<BR>Kadamba tree.<BR>--वृत्त a. {1}<BR>wellconducted, upright, virtuous; प्रयेण<BR>साधुवृत्तानामस्थायिन्यो विपत्तयः<BR>Bh. 2. 85; (where the next sense is also<BR>intended). {2} well-rounded.<BR>--(त्तः)<BR>a virtuous man.<BR>--(त्तं) good<BR>conduct, virtue, piety, righteousness;<BR>so साधुवृत्ति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1115-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिमन्
साधिमन् m. Goodness, excellence,<BR>perfection.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधिष्ठ
साधिष्ठ a.<BR>1 Best, most<BR>excellent, most proper.<BR>--2 Very strong,<BR>hard or firm (superl. of. साधु or वाढ<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधीयस्
साधीयस् a.<BR>1 Better, more<BR>excellent; Bv. 1. 88.<BR>--2 Harder, stronger;<BR>(compar. of साधु or वाढ q. v.).<BR>--3<BR>More handsome.<BR>--4 More proper<BR>or right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुता
साधुता --त्वं Goodness, purity,<BR>chastity &c.; U. 1. 5; सत्संगात्भवति हि<BR>साधुता खलानां Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधुत्वं|साधुत्व
साधुता --त्वं Goodness, purity,<BR>chastity &c.; U. 1. 5; सत्संगात्भवति हि<BR>साधुता खलानां Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साधृतं|साधृत
साधृतं<BR>1 A stall, shop.<BR>--2 An<BR>umbrella.<BR>--3 A flock of peacocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वसं|साध्वस
साध्वसं<BR>1 Fear, alarm, fright,<BR>terror; कुसुमस्तेयसाध्वसात्<BR>Ku. 2. 35, 3. 51.<BR>--2 Torpor.<BR>--3 Agitation,<BR>perturbation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साध्वी
साध्वी<BR>1 A virtuous or chaste<BR>woman.<BR>--2 A faithful wife.<BR>--3 N.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">Page1116-b+ 53</a>]<BR>of a kind of root.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानंद|सानन्द|सानन्दः
सानंद a. Happy, delighted.<BR>--दं<BR>Joyfully, delightfully; Māl. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानलः|सानल
सानलः The resinous<BR>exudation of the Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानसिः|सानसि
सानसिः Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानिका
सानिका, सानोयिका, सानेयी A pipe,<BR>flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानोयिका
सानिका, सानोयिका, सानेयी A pipe,<BR>flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानेयी
सानिका, सानोयिका, सानेयी A pipe,<BR>flute.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानु|सानुः
सानु m., n.<BR>1 A peak, summit,<BR>ridge; सानूनि गंधः सुरभीकरोति<BR>Ku. 1. 9; Me. 2; Ku. 1. 5;<BR>Ki. 5. 36.<BR>--2 A level ground on the top<BR>of a mountain, table-land.<BR>--3 A<BR>shoot, sprout.<BR>--4 A forest, wood.<BR>--5 A road.<BR>--6 Any surface, point,<BR>end.<BR>--7 A precipice.<BR>--8 A gale of<BR>wind.<BR>--9 A learned man.<BR>--10 The<BR>sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुमत्|सानुमन्त्
सानुमत् m. A mountain.<BR>--ती N.<BR>of an Apsaras; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुकंप|सानुकम्प
सानुकंप a. Feeling pity,<BR>sympathising, kind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुक्रोश
सानुक्रोश a. Tender,<BR>compassionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुनय
सानुनय a. Courteous, civil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुबंध|सानुबन्ध
सानुबंध a. Uninterrupted,<BR>continuous; R. 1. 64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सानुराग
सानुराग a. Attached,<BR>enamoured, in love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांतपनं|सान्तपन|सांतपन|सान्तपनं
सांतपनं A kind of rigid penance;<BR>cf. Ms. 11. 213.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांतर|सान्तर|सान्तरं
सांतर a.<BR>1 Having interstices<BR>or intervals.<BR>--2 Open in texture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांतानिक|सान्तानिक|सान्तानिकः
सांतानिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Stretching, spreading, extending (as a<BR>tree).<BR>--2 Relating to offspring or<BR>descendants.<BR>--3 Relating to the<BR>tree Saṃtāna, q. v.<BR>--कः A<BR>Brāhmaṇa who wishes to marry for the<BR>sake of issue.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांत्व्|सान्त्व्
सांत्व् {c10c} U. (सांत्वयति-ते) To<BR>pacify, appease, conciliate, soothe,<BR>comfort; Bk. 3. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांत्वः|सान्त्व|सांत्व|सान्त्वं|सान्त्वः
सांत्वः, सांत्वनं --ना [सांत्व् अच् ल्युट्<BR>वा]<BR>1 Appeasing, pacification,<BR>consolation.<BR>--2 Conciliation, mild or<BR>gentle means; Pt. 3. 27.<BR>--3 Kind<BR>or conciliatory words.<BR>--4 Mildness.<BR>--5 Friendly salutation and inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांत्वनं|सान्त्वन|सांत्वन|सान्त्वनं
सांत्वः, सांत्वनं --ना [सांत्व् अच् ल्युट्<BR>वा]<BR>1 Appeasing, pacification,<BR>consolation.<BR>--2 Conciliation, mild or<BR>gentle means; Pt. 3. 27.<BR>--3 Kind<BR>or conciliatory words.<BR>--4 Mildness.<BR>--5 Friendly salutation and inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांत्वना
सांत्वः, सांत्वनं --ना [सांत्व् अच् ल्युट्<BR>वा]<BR>1 Appeasing, pacification,<BR>consolation.<BR>--2 Conciliation, mild or<BR>gentle means; Pt. 3. 27.<BR>--3 Kind<BR>or conciliatory words.<BR>--4 Mildness.<BR>--5 Friendly salutation and inquiry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांदीपनिः|सान्दीपनि|सांदीपनि|सान्दीपनिः
सांदीपनिः N. of a sage.<BR>[According to Viṣṇu Purāṇa, he was the<BR>tutor of Kṛṣṇa and Balarāma, and<BR>asked, as his preceptor's fee that his son,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">Page1116-c+ 55</a>]<BR>who was kept by a demon named<BR>Panchajana underneath the waters, should<BR>be restored to him. Kṛṣṇa, having<BR>undertaken to get him up, plunged<BR>into the sea, killed the demon, and<BR>brought back the boy to his father].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांदृष्टिक|सान्दृष्टिक|सांदृष्टिकं|सान्दृष्टिकं
सांदृष्टिक a. (की f.) Relating<BR>to present perception, visible at the<BR>same time.<BR>--कं Immediate<BR>consequence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांद्र|सान्द्र|सान्द्रं|सान्द्रः
सांद्र a.<BR>1 Close, compact, having<BR>no interstices.<BR>--2 Coarse, gross,<BR>thick, dense; दुर्वर्णभित्तिरिह<BR>सांद्रसुधासवर्णा Śi. 4. 28, 64; 9. 15; R. 7. 41;<BR>Rs. 1. 20.<BR>--3 Clustered together,<BR>collected.<BR>--4 Stout, strong, robust.<BR>--5 Excessive, abundant, much;<BR>सांद्रानंदक्षुभितहृदयप्रस्रवेणेव सिक्तः<BR>U. 7. 22.<BR>--6 Intense, strong,<BR>vehement; व्याप्तांतराः सांद्रकुतूहलानां<BR>R. 7. 11; Śi. 9. 37.<BR>--7 Unctuous,<BR>oily, viscid.<BR>--8 Bland, soft, smooth.<BR>--9 Pleasing, agreeable.<BR>--द्रः<BR>1 A<BR>heap, cluster.<BR>--2 A thicket, wood.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कुतूहल a. greatly<BR>curious, seized with great curiosity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांधिकः|सान्धिक|सांधिक|सान्धिकः
सांधिकः A distiller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांधिविग्रहिकः|सान्धिविग्रहिक|सांधिविग्रहिक
सांधिविग्रहिकः A minister (or<BR>Secretary of State) for foreign<BR>affairs (deciding upon peace and war).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांध्य|सान्ध्य|सान्ध्यः
सांध्य a. (ध्यी f.)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>the twilight or evening; सांध्यं तेजः<BR>प्रतिनवजवापुष्परक्तं दधानः Me. 36;<BR>Ki. 5. 8; R. 11. 60; Śi. 9. 15.<BR>--2<BR>Relating to the morning twilight or<BR>dawn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनहनिक|सान्नहनिक|सांनहनिकः|सान्नहनिकः
सांनहनिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Bearing<BR>or putting on an armour.<BR>--2<BR>Calling to arms, encouraging to prepare<BR>for battle; Śi. 15. 72.<BR>--कः An<BR>armour-bearer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनाय्यः|सान्नाय्य|सांनाय्य|सान्नाय्यं
सांनाय्यः Any substance<BR>mixed with clarified butter and offered<BR>as an oblation to fire; Śi. 11. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनिध्यं|सान्निध्य|सांनिध्य|सान्निध्यं
सांनिध्यं<BR>1 Vicinity, proximity;<BR>वदनामलेंदुसांनिध्यतः Māl. 3. 5.<BR>--2<BR>Presence, attendance; R. 4. 6; 7. 3;<BR>Ku. 7. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांनिपातिक|सान्निपातिक|सान्निपातिकः
सांनिपातिक a. (की f.) [<BR>सन्निपातात् त्रिदोषविकारात् आगतः तेन निर्वृत्तो वा<BR>अण्]<BR>1 Miscellaneous.<BR>--2<BR>Complicated.<BR>--3 Having a complicated<BR>derangement of the three bodily<BR>humours; Ku. 2. 48; Pt. 1. 127.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांन्यासिकः|सान्न्यासिक|सांन्यासिक|सान्न्यासिकः
सांन्यासिकः [संन्यासः प्रयोजनमस्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">Page1117-a+ 55</a>]<BR>ठक्]<BR>1 A Brāhmaṇa in the fourth<BR>order of his religious life; see<BR>संन्यासिन्.<BR>--2 A mendicant in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1116-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सान्वय
सान्वय a. Hereditary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न
सापत्न a. (नी f.) Born from<BR>or belonging to a rival wife.<BR>--त्नाः<BR>(m. pl.) The children of different<BR>wives of the same husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापत्न्यं|सापत्न्य|सापत्न्यः
सापत्न्यं<BR>1 The state or<BR>condition of a rival wife.<BR>--2 Rivalry,<BR>ambition, enmity.<BR>--त्न्यः<BR>1 The son<BR>of a rival wife.<BR>--2 An enemy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापराध
सापराध a. Guilty, criminal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापवाद
सापवाद a.<BR>1 Spreading or<BR>indulging in scandal; U. 1. 6.<BR>--2 Attended<BR>with a scandal; U. 2.<BR>--दं ind.<BR>Censuringly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापिंड्यं|सापिण्ड्य|सापिंड्य|सापिण्ड्यं
सापिंड्यं Connection by the<BR>offering of rice-balls to the same<BR>Manes, kindred, consanguinity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सापेक्ष
सापेक्ष a. Having regard to,<BR>dependent on, (usually in comp.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपद
साप्तपद a. (दी f.), साप्तपदीन a.<BR>[cf. P. V. 2. 22] Formed by<BR>walking together seven steps, or by<BR>talking together seven words; यतः<BR>सतां संनतगात्रि संगतं मनीषिभिः<BR>साप्तपदीनमुच्यते Ku. 5. 39 (where the<BR>latter sense appears better);<BR>Pt. 2. 43, 4. 103.<BR>--दं, --नं<BR>1<BR>Circumambulation of the nuptial fire by the bride<BR>and bridegroom in seven steps<BR>(which makes the marriage tie<BR>irrevocable).<BR>--2 Friendship, intimacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साप्तपौरुष
साप्तपौरुष a. (षी f.) Extending<BR>to or including seven generations;<BR>Ms. 3. 146.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साफल्यं|साफल्य
साफल्यं<BR>1 Fruitfulness,<BR>usefulness, productiveness^1.<BR>--2 Profit,<BR>advantage.<BR>--3 Success.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साबाध
साबाध a. Disordered, deranged;<BR>Ś. 3. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साब्दी
साब्दी A kind of grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साभ्यसूय
साभ्यसूय a. Envious, jealous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्
साम् {c10c} U. (सामयति-ते) To<BR>appease, conciliate, soothe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामकं|सामक|सामकः
सामकं The principal of a debt.<BR>--कः A whet-stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्री
सामग्री [समग्रस्य भावः ष्यञ् स्त्रीत्वपक्षे<BR>ङीषि यलोपः Tv.]<BR>1 A collection or<BR>assemblage of materials, apparatus,<BR>furniture; Bh. 3. 155.<BR>--2 Effects,<BR>goods.<BR>--3 Stock, provision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामग्र्यं|सामग्र्य
सामग्र्यं<BR>1 Entireness, perfection,<BR>completeness, totality; प्रायेण<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">Page1117-b+ 56</a>]<BR>सामग्र्यविधौ गुणानां पराङ्मुखी विश्वसृजः प्रवृत्तिः<BR>Ku. 3. 28.<BR>--2 Train, retinue.<BR>--3 A<BR>collection of implements, apparatus.<BR>--4 Stock, effects.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामंजस्यं|सामञ्जस्य|सामंजस्य|सामञ्जस्यं
सामंजस्यं<BR>1 Fitness, consistency,<BR>propriety; cf. असमंजस.<BR>--2<BR>Accuracy, correctness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्
सामन् n. [सो-मनिन् Uṇ. 4. 152]<BR>1 Appeasing, calming, comforting,<BR>soothing.<BR>--2 Conciliation, pacific<BR>measures, negotiation, (the first of<BR>the four upāyas or expedients to be<BR>used by a king against an enemy);<BR>सामदंडौ प्रशंसंति नित्यं राष्ट्राभिवृद्धये<BR>Ms. 7. 109.<BR>--3 Conciliatory or mild<BR>means, pacific or conciliatory<BR>conduct, gentle words; Pt. 4. 26, 48.<BR>--4 Mildness, gentleness.<BR>--5 A<BR>metrical hymn or song of praise;<BR>सप्तसामोपगीतं त्वां R. 10. 21,<BR>Bg. 10. 35.<BR>--6 A verse or text of the<BR>Sāmaveda.<BR>--7 The Sāmaveda itself (said<BR>to have been produced from the<BR>sun; cf. Ms. 1. 23).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उद्भवः an elephant.<BR>--उपचारः, --उपायः<BR>mild or conciliatory means, gentle<BR>or pacific measures.<BR>--गः a<BR>Brāhmaṇa who chants the Sāmaveda.<BR>--गर्भः, --गायनः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--जः,<BR>--जात a. {1} produced by the<BR>Sāmaveda. {2} produced by conciliatory<BR>means.<BR>--(जः, --तः) an elephant;<BR>Śi. 12. 11, 18. 33.<BR>--योनिः {1}<BR>Brahman. {2} an elephant.<BR>--वादः kind<BR>words, conciliatory words;<BR>Śi. 2. 55; Pt. 3. 28.<BR>--वेदः the third of<BR>the four Vedas.<BR>--वेदिन् m. a<BR>Brāhmaṇa who has studied the<BR>Sāmaveda.<BR>--वेदीयः a Chāndoga priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामक|सामकं|सामकः
सामक a. Belonging to the<BR>Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन
सामन a. Ved. Conciliatory,<BR>peaceable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामन्यः|सामन्य
सामन्यः<BR>1 A Brāhmaṇa versed in<BR>the Sāma-veda.<BR>--2 One skilful in<BR>chanting the verses of that Veda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामनी
सामनी, साम्नी A rope for tying<BR>cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्नी
सामनी, साम्नी A rope for tying<BR>cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामंत|सामन्त|सामन्तः
सामंत a.<BR>1 Bordering, bounding,<BR>neighbouring.<BR>--2 Universal.<BR>--तः<BR>1 A neighbour.<BR>--2 A neighbouring<BR>king.<BR>--3 A feudatory or tributary<BR>prince; सामंतमौलिमणिरंजितपादपीठं<BR>V. 3. 19, R. 5. 28, 6. 33.<BR>--4 A leader,<BR>general.<BR>--तं Neighbourhood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयाचारिक
सामयाचारिक a. (की f.)<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-c" target="_blank">Page1117-c+ 56</a>]<BR>Relating to conventional practice or<BR>usage (समयाचार).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सूत्रं N.<BR>of certain Sūtras, treating of<BR>conventional customs and rites<BR>sanctioned by the common agreement<BR>and practice of virtuous men.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामयिक|सामयिकः
सामयिक a. (की f.) [समय-ठञ्]<BR>1<BR>Customary, conventional.<BR>--2 Agreed<BR>upon, stipulated.<BR>--3 Conforming to<BR>agreement, keeping an appointment<BR>or engagement; देवि सामयिका भवामः<BR>M. 1.<BR>--4 Punctual, exact.<BR>--5<BR>Reasonable, timely; Ki. 2. 40.<BR>--6<BR>Periodical.<BR>--7 Temporary.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अभावः temporary non-existence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामर्थ्यं|सामर्थ्य
सामर्थ्यं<BR>1 Power, force,<BR>capacity, ability, strength.<BR>--2 Sameness<BR>of aim or object.<BR>--3 Oneness of<BR>meaning or signification.<BR>--4<BR>Adequacy, fitness.<BR>--5 The force or sense<BR>of words, the signifying power of a<BR>word.<BR>--6 Interest, advantage.<BR>--7<BR>Wealth. (सामर्थ्यात् ‘by the force of,<BR>on the strength of, by dint of, by<BR>reason of, as a consequence of’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामवायिक|सामवायिकः
सामवायिक a. (की f.) [समवाये<BR>प्रसृतः ठञ्]<BR>1 Belonging to an<BR>assembly or collection.<BR>--2 Belonging<BR>to inseparable connection.<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>A minister, counsellor.<BR>--2 The chief<BR>of a company or corporation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामाजिक|सामाजिकः
सामाजिक a. (की f.) [समाजः<BR>सभावेशनं प्रयोजनमस्य ठञ्] Belonging to<BR>an assembly.<BR>--कः A member of an<BR>audience or assembly, a spectator at<BR>an assembly or meeting; तेन हि<BR>तत्प्रयोगादेवात्रभ वतः सामाजिकानुपास्महे<BR>Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामानाधिकरण्यं|सामानाधिकरण्य
सामानाधिकरण्यं<BR>1 Being in<BR>the same predicament or situation.<BR>--2 Common office, function or<BR>government, common relationship<BR>(as of case).<BR>--3 The state of<BR>relating to the same object.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्य|सामान्यं
सामान्य a. [समानस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Common, general; सामान्यमेषां<BR>प्रथमावरत्वं Ku. 7. 44; आहारनिद्राभयमैथुनं<BR>च सामान्यमेतत्पशुभिर्नराणां Subhāsh;<BR>R. 14. 67; Ku. 2. 26.<BR>--2 Alike,<BR>equal, same.<BR>--3 Ordinary, of an^1<BR>average or middle degree; सामान्या<BR>स्तु परार्थमुद्यमभृतः स्वार्थविरोधेन ये<BR>Bh. 2. 74.<BR>--4 Vulgar, commonplace, in<BR>significant.<BR>--5 Entire, whole.<BR>--न्य<BR>1 Community, generality,<BR>universality.<BR>--2 Common or generic<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">Page1118-a+ 55</a>]<BR>property, general characteristic;<BR>नित्यमेकमनेकसमवेतं सामान्यं Tarka K.<BR>--3<BR>Totality, entireness.<BR>--4 Kind, sort.<BR>--5 Identity.<BR>--6 Equanimity,<BR>equability.<BR>--7 Public affairs.<BR>--8 A<BR>general proposition; उक्तिरर्थांतरन्यासः<BR>स्यात्सामान्यविशेषयोः Chandr. 5. 120.<BR>--9<BR>(In Rhet.) A figure of speech<BR>thus defined by Mammaṭa:<BR>--प्रस्तुतस्य<BR>यदन्येन गुणसाम्यविवक्षया । एकात्म्यं बध्यते<BR>योगात्तत्सामान्यामिति स्मृतम् K. P. 10.<BR>--न्या A harlot, prostitute.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज्ञानं knowledge or perception of<BR>generic properties.<BR>--पक्षः the mean.<BR>--पदार्थः the category called सामान्य<BR>or generality.<BR>--प्रतिपत्तिपूर्वकं ind.<BR>with equal respect; Ś. 4. 16.<BR>--लक्षणं<BR>a generic definition; इति<BR>द्रव्यसामान्यलक्षणानि Tarka K.<BR>--वनिता a<BR>common woman, prostitute.<BR>--शास्त्रं<BR>a general rule.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Jim Funderburk on 20220914. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-orig/issues/975.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1117-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामान्यतः
सामान्यतः ind. Commonly,<BR>generally, usually.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दृष्टं (in<BR>logic) a kind of inference (neither<BR>deduced from the relation of cause<BR>to effect nor from that of effect<BR>to cause).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामासिक
सामासिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Comprehensive, comprehending the whole,<BR>collective.<BR>--2 Condensed, concise,<BR>brief.<BR>--3 Relating to a compound<BR>word.<BR>--4 Compounded, composite.<BR>--कं The whole class of compounds;<BR>द्वंद्वः सामासिकस्य च Bg. 10. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामि
सामि ind.<BR>1 Half; i. e.<BR>unfinished; अभिवीक्ष्य सामिकृतमंडनं यतीः<BR>कररुद्धनीविगलदंशुकाः स्त्रियः<BR>Śi. 13. 31, R. 19. 16.<BR>--2 Blamable, vile,<BR>contemptible. [Cf. L. semi; Gr. hemi].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामिधेनी
सामिधेनी [सम् + इंध् करणे ल्युट् नि˚]<BR>1 A kind of prayer recited while<BR>the sacrificial fire is being kindled<BR>or fed with fuel.<BR>--2 Fuel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीची
सामीची Praise, eulogium.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामीप्यं|सामीप्य|सामीप्यः
सामीप्यं Vicinity, nearness,<BR>proximity.<BR>--प्यः A neighbour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्र|सामुद्रं|सामुद्रः
सामुद्र a. (द्री f.) [समुद्रे भवः अण्]<BR>Sea-born, marine, as in सामुद्रं लवणं.<BR>--द्रः A mariner, voyager.<BR>--द्रं<BR>1<BR>Sea-salt.<BR>--2 The cuttle-fish bone.<BR>--3 A mark or spot on the body.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रकं|सामुद्रक|सामुद्रकः
सामुद्रकं Sea-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सामुद्रिक|सामुद्रिकः
सामुद्रिक a. (की f.) [समुद्रेण प्रोक्तं<BR>वेत्त्यधीते वा ठञ्]<BR>1 Sea-born,<BR>oceanic.<BR>--2 Relating to marks on<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">Page1118-b+ 55</a>]<BR>the body (which are supposed to<BR>indicate good or bad fortune).<BR>--कः<BR>1 One who is acquainted with<BR>palmistry, who knows how to<BR>interpret the various marks on the<BR>body.<BR>--2 A fortune-teller.<BR>--कं<BR>The science of palmistry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांपराय|साम्पराय|सांपरायः
सांपराय a. (यी f.)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>war, warlike.<BR>--2 Relating to the<BR>other world, future.<BR>--यः, --यं<BR>1<BR>Conflict, contention.<BR>--2 Future<BR>life, the future.<BR>--3 The means of<BR>attaining the future world.<BR>--4<BR>Inquiry into the future.<BR>--5 Inquiry,<BR>investigation.<BR>--6 Uncertainty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांपरायिक|साम्परायिक|साम्परायिकं|सांपरायिकः
सांपरायिक^1 a. (की f.)<BR>1 Warlike.<BR>--2 Military, strategic.<BR>--3<BR>Calamitous.<BR>--4 Relating to the other<BR>world.<BR>--कं War, battle, conflict;<BR>Śi. 18. 8.<BR>--कः A war-chariot.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कल्पः a strategic array (of<BR>troops).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांप्रत
सांप्रत a.<BR>1 Fit, proper, suitable;<BR>Ve. 3. 3.<BR>--2 Relevant.<BR>--तं ind.<BR>1 Now, at this time; हंत स्थानं<BR>क्रोधस्य सांप्रतं देव्याः Ve. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Immediately.<BR>--3 Fitly, properly,<BR>seasonably.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांप्रतिक|साम्प्रतिक
सांप्रतिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Belonging to the present time.<BR>--2 Fit,<BR>proper, right; U. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांप्रदायिक|साम्प्रदायिक
सांप्रदायिक a. (की f.)<BR>Relating to the traditional doctrine,<BR>handed down by successive tradition,<BR>traditional.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांबः|साम्ब|सांब|साम्बः
सांबः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांबंधिक|साम्बन्धिक|सांबन्धिक
सांबंधिक a. (की f.) Arising<BR>from relationship.<BR>--कं<BR>Relationship, alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांबरं|साम्बर|साम्बरं
सांबरं Salt produced in<BR>Sambara.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांबरी|साम्बरी
सांबरी A sorceress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांभवी|साम्भवी
सांभवी<BR>1 The red Lodhra tree.<BR>--2 Possibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सांमुख्यं|साम्मुख्य|सांमुख्य
सांमुख्यं<BR>1 Presence.<BR>--2 Favour,<BR>countenance, propitiousness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्यं|साम्य
साम्यं<BR>1 Equality, sameness,<BR>evenness; Ku. 5. 31.<BR>--2 Likeness,<BR>resemblance, similarity; स्पष्टं<BR>प्रापत्साम्यमुवींधरस्य Śi. 18. 38; H. 1. 45;<BR>Ki. 17. 51.<BR>--3 Equability.<BR>--4<BR>Concord, harmony.<BR>--5 Indifference,<BR>impartiality, sameness of view; येषां<BR>साम्ये मनः स्थितं Bg. 5. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साम्राज्यं|साम्राज्य
साम्राज्यं<BR>1 Universal or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">Page1118-c+ 56</a>]<BR>complete sovereignty, imperial sway;<BR>साम्राज्यशंसिनो भावाः कुशस्य च लवस्य<BR>च U. 6. 23; R. 4. 5.<BR>--2 Empire,<BR>dominion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायः|साय|सायं
सायः [सो-घञ्]<BR>1 End, close,<BR>termination.<BR>--2 Close of day, evening.<BR>--3<BR>An arrow. (साये ‘in the evening,<BR>at the close of the day.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अहन् m. (forming सायाह्नः) evening,<BR>evening time; Bv. 2. 157.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायंतन|सायन्तन|सायन्तनः
सायंतन a. (नी f.) Belonging<BR>to the evening, evening; सायंतने<BR>सवनकर्मणि संप्रवृत्ते Ś. 3. 27;<BR>अलिनारमतालिनी शिलींध्रे सह<BR>सायंतनदीपपादलाभे Śi. 6. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायम्
सायम् ind. In the evening; प्रयता<BR>प्रातरन्वेतु सायं प्रत्युद्व्रजेदपि R. 1. 90.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कालः evening.<BR>--धृतिः f.<BR>the evening oblation.<BR>--मंडनं {1}<BR>sunset. {2} the sun.<BR>--संध्या {1} the<BR>evening twilight. {2} the evening<BR>prayer. {3} the goddess to be<BR>worshipped in the evening. ˚देवता N. of<BR>Sarasvatī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायकः|सायक
सायकः [सो-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 An arrow;<BR>तत्साधुकृतसंधानं प्रतिसंहर सायकं<BR>Ś. 1. 11.<BR>--2 A sword.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पुंखः<BR>the feathered part of an arrow;<BR>सक्तांगुलिः सायकपुंख एव R. 2. 31.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायणः|सायण
सायणः N. of a very learned<BR>Brāhmaṇa supposed to have<BR>flourished about 1370 A. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायनं|सायन
सायनं The longitude of a planet<BR>reckoned from the vernal equinoctial<BR>point.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायिन्
सायिन् m. A horseman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सायुज्यं|सायुज्य
सायुज्यं<BR>1 Intimate union,<BR>identification, absorption, especially into<BR>a deity (one of the four states of<BR>Mukti).<BR>--2 Similarity, likeness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार|सारं|सारः
सार a. [सृ-घञ्, सार्-अच् वा]<BR>1<BR>Essential.<BR>--2 Best, highest, most<BR>excellent; Mu. 1. 13.<BR>--3 Real, true,<BR>genuine.<BR>--4 Strong, vigorous.<BR>--5<BR>Sound, thoroughly proved.<BR>--6<BR>Highest or best (at the end of comp.);<BR>त्रिवर्गसारः Ku. 5. 38.<BR>--रः, --रं (but<BR>usually m. only except in the first<BR>{4} senses)<BR>1 Essence, essential part,<BR>quintessence; स्नेहस्य तत्फलमसौ<BR>प्रणयस्य स Māl. 1. 9; U. 6. 22.<BR>असारे खलु संसारे सारमेतच्चतुष्टयम् । काश्यां<BR>वासः सतां संगो गंगांभः शंभुसेवनं ॥<BR>Dharm. 14.<BR>--2 Substance, pith.<BR>--3 Marrow.<BR>--4 Real truth, main point.<BR>--5 The<BR>sap or essence of trees; as in खदिरसार,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-a" target="_blank">Page1119-a+ 56</a>]<BR>सर्जसार.<BR>--6 Summary, epitome,<BR>compendium.<BR>--7 Strength, vigour, power,<BR>energy; सारं धरित्रीधरणक्षमं च<BR>Ku. 1. 17; R. 2. 74.<BR>--8 Prowess,<BR>heroism, courage; R. 4. 79.<BR>--9<BR>Firmness, hardness.<BR>--10 Wealth,<BR>riches; गामात्तसारां R. 5. 26.<BR>--11<BR>Nectar.<BR>--12 Fresh butter.<BR>--13 Air,<BR>wind.<BR>--14 Cream, coagulum of<BR>curds.<BR>--15 Disease.<BR>--16 Matter,<BR>pus.<BR>--17 Worth, excellence, highest<BR>perception.<BR>--18 A man at chess.<BR>--19 Impure carbonate of soda.<BR>--20<BR>A figure of speech corresponding to<BR>English ‘climax’; उत्तरोत्तरमुत्कर्षो<BR>भवेत्सारः परावधिः K. P. 10.<BR>--21 The<BR>heart.<BR>--रा<BR>1 Dūrvā grass.<BR>--2 Kuśa<BR>grass.<BR>--रं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 Fitness,<BR>propriety.<BR>--3 Wood, thicket.<BR>--4<BR>Steel.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--असार a. valuable and<BR>worthless, strong and weak.<BR>--(रं) {1}<BR>worth and worthlessness. {2}<BR>substance and emptiness. {3} strength<BR>and weakness. ˚विचारः<BR>consideration of strong and weak points<BR>&c.<BR>--गंधः sandal wood.<BR>--ग्रीवः N.<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--जं fresh butter.<BR>--तरुः<BR>the plantain tree.<BR>--दा {1} N. of<BR>Sarasvatī. {2} of Durgā.<BR>--द्रुमः the<BR>Khadira tree.<BR>--भंगः loss of vigour.<BR>--भांडं {1} a natural vessel. {2} a<BR>bale of goods, merchandise. {3}<BR>implements.<BR>--मितिः the Veda.<BR>--लोहं steel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1118-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारतस्
सारतस् ind.<BR>1 According to wealth.<BR>--2 Vigorously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारवत्|सारवन्त्
सारवत् a.<BR>1 Substantial.<BR>--2<BR>Fertile.<BR>--3 Having sap.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारक|सारकः
सारक a. Purgative, cathartic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारघं|सारघ
सारघं Honey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारंग|सारङ्ग|सारङ्गः
सारंग a. (गी f.) [सारं अंगमस्य<BR>शकं˚] Spotted, variegated.<BR>--गः<BR>1 The variegated colour.<BR>--2 The<BR>spotted deer, an antelope; एष<BR>राजेव दुष्यंतः सारंगेणातिरंहसा Ś. 1. 5.<BR>--3 A deer in general; सारंगास्ते<BR>जललवमुचः सूचयिष्यंति मार्गं Me. 21<BR>(where it is preferable to take this<BR>sense rather than that of ‘elephant’<BR>or ‘bee’).<BR>--4 A lion.<BR>--5 An elephant.<BR>--6 A large black bee.<BR>--7 The<BR>cuckoo.<BR>--8 A large crane.<BR>--9 The<BR>flamingo.<BR>--10 A peacock.<BR>--11 An<BR>umbrella.<BR>--12 A cloud.<BR>--13 A<BR>garment.<BR>--14 Hair.<BR>--15 A conch-shell.<BR>--16 N. of Śiva.<BR>--17 The god of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">Page1119-b+ 56</a>]<BR>love.<BR>--18 A lotus.<BR>--19 Camphor.<BR>--20 A bow.<BR>--21 Sandal.<BR>--22 A<BR>kind of musical instrument.<BR>--23 An<BR>ornament.<BR>--24 Gold.<BR>--25 The earth.<BR>--26 The Cātaka bird.<BR>--27 A<BR>flower.<BR>--28 Night.<BR>--29 Light.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारंगिकः|सारङ्गिक|सारंगिक|सारङ्गिकः
सारंगिकः A fowler, bird catcher.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारंगी
सारंगी<BR>1 A kind of stringed<BR>instrument, violin.<BR>--2 A kind of<BR>spotted deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारण|सारणं|सारणः
सारण a. (णी f.) Causing to go<BR>or flow.<BR>--णः<BR>1 Dysentery.<BR>--2 The<BR>hog-plum.<BR>--णं A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणा
सारणा A kind of process to which<BR>metals, particularly mercury, are<BR>subjected.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणिः|सारणि
सारणिः --णी f.<BR>1 A canal, drain,<BR>water-course, channel.<BR>--2 A small<BR>river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणी
सारणिः --णी f.<BR>1 A canal, drain,<BR>water-course, channel.<BR>--2 A small<BR>river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारणिक|सारणिकः
सारणिक a. (की f.) Travelling,<BR>journeying.<BR>--कः A traveller,<BR>wayfarer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारंडः|सारण्ड|सारंड|सारण्डः
सारंडः The egg of a serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथिः|सारथि
सारथिः [सृ-अथिण्, सह रथेन सरथः<BR>घोटकः तत्र नियुक्तः इञ् वा Tv.; cf.<BR>Uṇ. 4. 89]<BR>1 A charioteer; स शापो न त्वया<BR>राजन् न च सारथिना श्रुतः R. 1. 78;<BR>मातलिसारथिर्ययौ 3. 67.<BR>--2 A<BR>companion, helper; R. 3. 37.<BR>--3 The ocean.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारथ्यं|सारथ्य
सारथ्यं The office of a charioteer,<BR>charioteership, coachmanship.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारमेयः|सारमेय
सारमेयः A dog.<BR>--यी A bitch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारल्यं|सारल्य
सारल्यं Straightness (fig. also),<BR>artlessness, honesty, uprightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस|सारसं|सारसः
सारस a. (सी f.) [सरस इदं अण्]<BR>1<BR>Belonging to a lake; Kāv. 3. 14;<BR>Nalod. 2. 40.<BR>--2 Belonging to or<BR>proceeding from a Sārasa.<BR>--सः<BR>1<BR>The (Indian) crane, or swan<BR>(according to some); विभिद्यमाना<BR>विससार सारसानुदस्य तीरेषु तरंगसंहतिः<BR>Ki. 8. 31, Śi. 6. 75, 12. 44, Me. 31;<BR>R. 1. 41.<BR>--2 A bird in general.<BR>--3<BR>The moon.<BR>--सं<BR>1 A lotus.<BR>--2 The<BR>zone or girdle of a woman.<BR>--सी A<BR>female (Indian) crane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारसनं|सारसन
सारस(श)नं<BR>1 A girdle or zone;<BR>सारशनं महानहिः Ki. 18. 32.<BR>--2 A<BR>military girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारशनं|सारशन
सारस(श)नं<BR>1 A girdle or zone;<BR>सारशनं महानहिः Ki. 18. 32.<BR>--2 A<BR>military girdle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारस्वत|सारस्वतः
सारस्वत a. (ती f.) [सरस्वती<BR>देवतास्य, सरस्वत्या इदं वा अण्]<BR>1 Relating<BR>to the goddess Sarasvatī.<BR>--2<BR>Belonging to the river Sarasvatī; कृत्वा<BR>तासामभिगममपां सौम्य सारस्वतीनां<BR>Me. 49.<BR>--3 Eloquent.<BR>--4 Belonging<BR>to the Sārasvata country.<BR>--तः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">Page1119-c+ 56</a>]<BR>1 N. of a country about the<BR>river Sarasvatī.<BR>--2 N. of a<BR>particular class of Brāhmaṇas.<BR>--3 A<BR>particular ceremonial used in the<BR>worship of Sarasvatī.<BR>--4 A staff<BR>of the Bilva tree.<BR>--ताः (m. pl.)<BR>The people of the Sārasvata<BR>country.<BR>--तं Speech, eloquence;<BR>शृंगारसारस्वतं Gīt. 12.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारालः|साराल
सारालः Sesamum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिः|सारि
सारिः --री f.<BR>1 A man at chess,<BR>chessman.<BR>--2 A kind of bird.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फलकः a chess-board.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारी
सारिः --री f.<BR>1 A man at chess,<BR>chessman.<BR>--2 A kind of bird.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फलकः a chess-board.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिका
सारिका [सरति गच्छति सृ --ण्वुल्] A<BR>kind of bird; आत्मनो मुखदोषेण<BR>बध्यंते शुकसारिकाः Subhāṣ.; सारिकां<BR>पंजरस्थां Me. 85.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारिन्
सारिन् a. (णी f.)<BR>1 Going,<BR>resorting to.<BR>--2 Having the essence<BR>or substance of.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारूप्यं|सारूप्य
सारूप्यं<BR>1 Sameness of form,<BR>similarity, likeness, conformity,<BR>resemblance; अंतर्वृत्तिसारूप्यतः<BR>Māl. 5.<BR>--2 Assimilation to the deity (one<BR>of the four states of Mukti).<BR>--3<BR>(In dramas) An angry treatment<BR>of one mistaken for another through<BR>resemblance; see S. D. 464.<BR>--4<BR>Surprise at seeing an object or<BR>its likeness seen elsewhere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सारोष्ट्रिकः|सारोष्ट्रिक
सारोष्ट्रिकः A kind of poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्गल
सार्गल a. Barred, obstructed,<BR>impeded; R. 1. 79.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थ|सार्थः
सार्थ a. [अर्थेन सहितः; सृ-थन् स्वार्थे<BR>अण् वा]<BR>1 Having meaning,<BR>significant.<BR>--2 Having an aim or<BR>object.<BR>--3 Of like meaning or<BR>import.<BR>--4 Useful, serviceable.<BR>--5<BR>Wealthy, rich, opulent.<BR>--र्थः<BR>1 A<BR>rich man.<BR>--2 A company of<BR>merchants, caravan (of traders);<BR>सार्थाः स्वैरं स्वकीयेषु चेरुर्वेश्मस्विवाद्रिषु<BR>R. 17. 64; see सार्थवाह.<BR>--3 A troop,<BR>collection of men; सार्थः प्रवसतो मित्रं<BR>Mb.<BR>--4 A herd, flock, (of<BR>animals of the same species); अथ<BR>कदाचित्तैरितस्ततो भ्रमाद्भिः सार्थाद् भ्रष्टः<BR>कथनको नामोष्ट्रो दृष्टः Pt. 1.<BR>--5 A<BR>collection or multitude in general;<BR>अर्थिसार्थः Pt. 1; त्वया चंद्रमसा<BR>चातिसंधीयते कामिजनसार्थः Ś. 3.<BR>--6 One<BR>of a company of pilgrims.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ज a. bred in a caravan.<BR>--वाहः<BR>the leader of a caravan, a merchant,<BR>trader; Ś. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थक|सार्थकः
सार्थक a.<BR>1 Having sense,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">Page1120-a+ 54</a>]<BR>significant.<BR>--2 Useful, serviceable,<BR>advantageous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1119-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थवत्|सार्थवन्त्
सार्थवत् a.<BR>1 Having meaning,<BR>significant.<BR>--2 Having a large<BR>company.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्थिकः|सार्थिक
सार्थिकः A merchant, trader.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्द्र|सार्द्रं
सार्द्र a. Wet, moist, humid,<BR>damp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ध|सार्द्धं
सार्ध a. Increased by half, plus<BR>one-half, having a half over; as in<BR>सार्धशतं &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्धम्
सार्धम् ind. Together with, with,<BR>in company with (with instr.);<BR>वनं मया सार्धमसि प्रपन्नः R. 14. 63,<BR>Ms. 4. 43; Bk. 6. 26; Me. 89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पः|सार्प|सार्प्प
सार्पः(र्प्यः) N. of the<BR>constellation Āśleṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्प्यः|सार्प्य
सार्पः(र्प्यः) N. of the<BR>constellation Āśleṣā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्पिष|सार्पिषः
सार्पिष a. (षी f.) सार्पिष्क (ष्की<BR>f.) Dressed or cooked with<BR>clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्व|सार्वः|सार्व्व|सार्व्वः
सार्व a. (र्वी f.)<BR>1 General,<BR>universal.<BR>--2 Fit or suitable for all.<BR>--र्वः A Buddhist or Jaina saint.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकामिक|सार्व्वकामिक
सार्वकामिक a. (की f.)<BR>Satisfying every desire, granting all<BR>wishes; Ki. 18. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वकालिक|सार्व्वकालिक
सार्वकालिक a. (की f.) Eternal,<BR>everlasting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिक|सार्व्वजनिकः
सार्वजनिक a. (की f.),<BR>सार्वजनीन a. (नी f.) Public, universal,<BR>general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वज्ञं|सार्वज्ञ|सार्व्वज्ञ
सार्वज्ञं Omniscience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वत्रिक|सार्व्वत्रिक
सार्वत्रिक a. (की f.) Belonging<BR>to every place, general, applicable<BR>to all places or circumstances; as<BR>in सार्वत्रिको नियमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वधातुक|सार्व्वधातुक
सार्वधातुक a. (की f.)<BR>Applicable to the whole of a radical term,<BR>or to the complete form of the<BR>verbal base after the conjugational<BR>characteristics have been affixed,<BR>i. e. to the four conjugational or<BR>special tenses.<BR>--कं N. of the verbal<BR>terminations of the four<BR>conjugational tenses (strictly, the personal<BR>terminations of all tenses and moods<BR>except the Perfect and<BR>Benedictive and the affixes distinguished<BR>by a mute श्).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौतिक|सार्व्वभौतिक
सार्वभौतिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Belonging or relating to all elements<BR>or beings.<BR>--2 Comprising all<BR>animate beings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वभौम|सार्वभौमः|सार्व्वभौम|सार्व्वभौमः
सार्वभौम a. (मी f.) Relating to,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">Page1120-b+ 55</a>]<BR>consisting of, the whole earth,<BR>universal.<BR>--मः<BR>1 An emperor, a<BR>universal monarch; नाज्ञाभंगं सहंते नृवर<BR>नृपतयस्त्वादृशाः सार्वभौमाः Mu. 3. 22.<BR>--2 N. of the elephant presiding<BR>over the north, the quarter of<BR>Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिक|सार्व्वलौकिकः
सार्वलौकिक a. (की f.) Known<BR>to all people, prevailing<BR>throughout the whole world, public,<BR>universal; अनुरागप्रवादस्तु वत्सयोः<BR>सार्वलौकिकः Māl. 1. 13.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववर्णिक|सार्व्ववर्णिक
सार्ववर्णिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Of every<BR>kind or sort.<BR>--2 Belonging to every<BR>tribe or class.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्वविभक्तिक|सार्व्वविभक्तिक
सार्वविभक्तिक a. (की f.)<BR>Applicable or belonging to all the cases<BR>of a noun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववेदसः|सार्ववेदस|सार्व्ववेदस
सार्ववेदसः One who gives away<BR>all his wealth at a sacrifice or<BR>sacred rite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ववैद्यः
सार्ववैद्यः A Brāhmaṇa<BR>conversant with all the Vedas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्षप|सार्षपः
सार्षप a. (पी f.) Made of<BR>mustard.<BR>--पं Mustard-oil.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्टि
सार्ष्टि a. Possessing the same<BR>station, condition, or rank, having<BR>the same power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्टिता
सार्ष्टिता<BR>1 Equality in rank,<BR>condition, or power.<BR>--2 Equality with<BR>the Supreme Being in power and<BR>all the divine attributes, the last of<BR>the four states or grades of Mukti;<BR>ब्रह्मदो ब्रह्मसार्ष्टितां (प्राप्नोति)<BR>Ms. 4. 232.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सार्ष्ट्यं|सार्ष्ट्य
सार्ष्ट्यं The fourth grade of Mukti,<BR>see above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालः|साल
सालः<BR>1 N. of a tree or its resin.<BR>--2 A tree in general, as in<BR>कल्पसाल, रसालसाल.<BR>--3 A rampart, a fence<BR>or wall round a building.<BR>--4 A wall<BR>in general.<BR>--5 A kind of fish. (For<BR>compounds see under शाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालनः|सालन
सालनः<BR>1 The resin of the Sāla<BR>tree.<BR>--2 Resin in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साला
साला<BR>1 A wall, rampart.<BR>--2 A<BR>house, an apartment; see शाला.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करी {1} a house-worker.<BR>{2} a male captive (particularly one<BR>taken in battle).<BR>--वृकः see शालावृक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालारं|सालार
सालारं A peg projecting from a<BR>wall, bracket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालूरः|सालूर
सालूरः A frog; see शालूर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालेयं|सालेय|सालेयः
सालेयं^1 A kind of fennel; see<BR>शालेय.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: n. noun needs anusvAra ending.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सालोक्यं|सालोक्य
सालोक्यं<BR>1 Being in the same<BR>world or sphere with another.<BR>--2<BR>Residence in the same heaven with<BR>any deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्वः|साल्व
साल्वः<BR>1 N. of a country, or its<BR>inhabitants (pl. in this sense).<BR>--2<BR>N. of a demon slain by Viṣṇu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हन् m. an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साल्विकः|साल्विक
साल्विकः The bird called सारिका<BR>q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावः|साव
सावः A libation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावक|सावकः
सावक a. (विका f.) Productive,<BR>generative, causing birth, obstetric.<BR>--कः The young of an animal; (for<BR>शावक q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावकाश
सावकाश a. Having leisure, at<BR>leisure, unengaged.<BR>--शं ind.<BR>Leisurely, at one's convenience.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावग्रह
सावग्रह a. Having the mark<BR>called avagraha q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावज्ञ
सावज्ञ a. Despising, disdainful<BR>feeling contempt; M. 5. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावद्यं|सावद्य
सावद्यं (i. e. ऐश्वर्यं) One of the<BR>three kinds of power attainable by<BR>an ascetic, (the other two being<BR>निरवद्य and मूक्ष्म).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधान|सावधानः
सावधान a.<BR>1 Attentive,<BR>bestowing attention, careful, heedful.<BR>--2<BR>Cautious.<BR>--3 Diligent.<BR>--नं ind.<BR>Carefully, attentively, cautiously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावधि
सावधि a. Having a bound or<BR>limit, limited, finite, defined,<BR>circumscribed; सावधिस्तोयराशिस्ते<BR>यशोराशेस्तु नावधिः Subhāṣ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावन|सावनं|सावनः
सावन a. (नी f.) [सवनं यागांगं<BR>स्नानं सोमनि ष्पीडनं वा तस्येदमण्] Relating<BR>to, or comprising, the three<BR>savanas.<BR>--नः<BR>1 An institutor of a<BR>sacrifice, or one who employs<BR>priests at a sacrifice.<BR>--2 The<BR>conclusion of a sacrifice, or the<BR>ceremony by which it is concluded.<BR>--3<BR>N. of Varuṇa.<BR>--4 A month of thirty<BR>solar days.<BR>--5 A natural day from<BR>sunrise to sunset.<BR>--6 A<BR>particular kind of year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावयव
सावयव a. Composed of parts;<BR>सावयवत्वे चानित्यप्रसंगः, न<BR>ह्यविद्याकल्पितेन रूपभेदेन सावयवं वस्तु संपद्यते<BR>Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावरः|सावर
सावरः<BR>1 Fault, offence.<BR>--2 Sin,<BR>wickedness, crime.<BR>--3 The Lodhra<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावरण
सावरण a.<BR>1 Clandestine,<BR>concealed, secret.<BR>--2 Covered, closed<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">Page1121-a+ 55</a>]<BR>shut; R. 16. 7.<BR>--3 Feneed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1120-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण|सावर्णः
सावर्ण a. (र्णी f.) Relating or<BR>belonging to one of the same<BR>colour, tribe or caste.<BR>--र्णः A<BR>metronymic of the eighth Manu; see<BR>सावर्णि.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--लक्ष्यं {1} a mark<BR>of the sameness of colour or caste.<BR>{2} the skin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्णिः|सावर्णि
सावर्णिः A metronymic of the<BR>eighth Manu (son of the sun by<BR>Savarṇā).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावर्ण्यं|सावर्ण्य
सावर्ण्यं<BR>1 Sameness of colour.<BR>--2 Identity of class or caste<BR>--3<BR>The age or Manvantara presided<BR>over by the eighth Manu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावलेप
सावलेप a. Full of pride, proud,<BR>haughty.<BR>--पं ind. Proudly,<BR>haughtily, arrogantly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावशेष
सावशेष a.<BR>1 Having a<BR>remainder, leaving a remainder or residue.<BR>--2 Imperfect, incomplete,<BR>unfinished.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावष्टंभ|सावष्टम्भ
सावष्टंभ a.<BR>1 Proud, dignified,<BR>noble, majestic.<BR>--2 Courageous,<BR>resolute.<BR>--3 Bold, vigorous,<BR>vehement; Māl. 5. 22.<BR>--4 Full of<BR>firmness; Pt. 1. 200.<BR>--भं ind.<BR>Resolutely, firmly, courageously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावहेल
सावहेल a. Disdainful,<BR>disdaining, despising.<BR>--लं ind.<BR>Disdainfully, scornfully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साविका
साविका A midwife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्र|सावित्रं|सावित्रः
सावित्र a. (त्री f.) [सविता<BR>दवेताऽस्य अण्]<BR>1 Belonging to the sun.<BR>--2 Descended from the sun,<BR>belonging to the solar dynasty (of<BR>kings); यत्सावित्रैर्दीपितं भूमिपालैः<BR>U. 1. 43.<BR>--3 Accompanied by the<BR>Gāyatrī.<BR>--त्रः<BR>1 The sun.<BR>--2 An<BR>embryo or fœtus.<BR>--3 A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--4 An epithet of Śiva<BR>--5 Of Karṇa.<BR>--त्रं The sacrificial thread (so<BR>called because the repetition of the<BR>Gāyatrī forms a principal part of<BR>the ceremony of putting on the<BR>sacred thread).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सावित्री
सावित्री<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of a celebrated verse of the<BR>Ṛgveda, so called because it is<BR>adressed to the sun; it is also called<BR>गायत्री q. v. for further<BR>information.<BR>--3 The ceremony of<BR>investiture with the sacred thread.<BR>--4<BR>N. of a wife of Brahman.<BR>--5<BR>N. of Pārvatī.<BR>--6 N. of a wife<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-b" target="_blank">Page1121-b+ 68</a>]<BR>of Kaśyapa.<BR>--7 An epithet of<BR>Sūryā (daughter of Savitṛ).<BR>--8<BR>N. of the wife of Satyavat, king<BR>of Śālva. [She was the only daughter<BR>of king Aśvapati. She was so lovely<BR>that all the suitors that came to woo<BR>her were repulsed by her superior lustre,<BR>and thus though she reached a<BR>marriageable age, she found no one ready<BR>to espouse her. At last her father<BR>asked her to go and find out a husband<BR>of her own choice. She did so, and<BR>having made her selection returned to<BR>her father, and told him that she had<BR>chosen Satyavat, son of Dyumatsena,<BR>King of Sālva, who being driven out<BR>from his kingdom was then leading a<BR>hermit's life along with his wife. When<BR>Nārada, who happened to be present<BR>there, heard this, he told her as well<BR>as Aśvapati that he was very sorry<BR>to hear of the choice she had made,<BR>for though Satyavat was in every way<BR>worthy of her, yet he was fated to<BR>die in a year from that date, and in<BR>choosing him, therefore, Sāvitrī would<BR>be only choosing life-long widow-hood<BR>and misery. Her parents, therefore,<BR>naturally tried to dissuade her mind,<BR>but the high-souled maiden told them<BR>that her choice was unalterably fixed.<BR>Accordingly the marriage took place<BR>in due time, and Sāvitrī laid aside her<BR>jewels and rich apparel, and putting<BR>on the coarse garments of hermits, spent<BR>her time in serving her old father and<BR>mother-in-law. Still, though<BR>outwardly happy, she could not forget the<BR>words of Nārada, and as she counted,<BR>the days seemed to fly swiftly like<BR>moments, and the fated time, when her<BR>husband was to die, drew near. ‘I<BR>have yet three days’, thought she,<BR>‘and for these three days I shall<BR>observe a rigid fast.’ She maintained<BR>her vow, and on the fourth day, when<BR>Satyavat was about to go to the woods<BR>to bring sacrificial fuel, she<BR>accompanied him. After having collected<BR>some fuel, Satyavat, being fatigued, sat<BR>down, and reposing his head on the<BR>bosom of Sāvitrī fell asleep. Just<BR>then Yama came down, snatched off<BR>his soul, and proceeded towards the<BR>south. Sāvitrī saw this and followed<BR>the god who told her to return as<BR>her husband's term of life was over.<BR>But the faithful wife besought Yama<BR>in so pathetic a strain that he granted<BR>her boon after boon, except the life<BR>of her husband, until, being quite<BR>subdued by her devotion to her husband<BR>and the force of her eloquent appeal, the<BR>god relented and restored even the<BR>spirit of Satyavat to her. Delighted she<BR>returned, and found her husband as<BR>if roused from a deep sleep, and<BR>informing him of all that had occurred,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">Page1121-c+ 56</a>]<BR>went to the hermitage of her<BR>fatherin-law who soon reaped the fruits of<BR>the boons of Yama. Sāvitri is<BR>regarded as the beau ideal or highest<BR>pattern of conjugal fidelity, and a<BR>young married woman is usually<BR>blessed by elderly females with the words<BR>जन्मसावित्री भव, thus placing before her<BR>the example of Sāvitrī for lifelong<BR>imitation].<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पतितः, --परिभ्रष्टः a<BR>man of any one of the first three<BR>castes not invested with the sacred<BR>thread at the proper time; cf. व्रात्य.<BR>--व्रतं N. of a particular fast kept<BR>by Hindu women on the last three<BR>days of the bright half of Jyeṣṭha<BR>to preserve them from widow-hood.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साविष्कार
साविष्कार a.<BR>1 Proud, haughty.<BR>--2 Manifest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशंस
साशंस a. Full of desire or<BR>passion, desirous, hopeful, expectant.<BR>--सं ind. Wishfully, hopefully.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशंक|साशङ्क
साशंक a. Feeling fear,<BR>apprehensive, afraid, dismayed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशयंदकः|साशयन्दक|साशयंदक|साशयन्दकः
साशयंदकः A small house-lizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साशूकः|साशूक
साशूकः A blanket.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्चर्य|साश्चर्य्य
साश्चर्य a.<BR>1 Wonderful,<BR>marvellous.<BR>--2 Struck with wonder.<BR>--र्यं ind. With wonder or<BR>astonishment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्र
साश्र(स्र) a.<BR>1 Having angles<BR>or corners, angular.<BR>--2 Tearful,<BR>weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्र
साश्र(स्र) a.<BR>1 Having angles<BR>or corners, angular.<BR>--2 Tearful,<BR>weeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्रु
साश्रु a. Tearful, full of tears,<BR>shedding tears.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साश्रुधी
साश्रुधी A wife's or husband's<BR>mother, a mother-in-law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साष्टांगम्|साष्टाङ्गम्
साष्टांगम् ind. With humble<BR>prostration of the body (by<BR>touching the earth with the eight<BR>members); see अष्टांगप्रणाम under अष्टन्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास
सास a. Having a bow; Ki. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासुसू
सासुसू a. Having arrows;<BR>Ki. 15. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सासूय
सासूय a. Envious, jealous,<BR>disdainful.<BR>--यं ind. Jealously,<BR>angrily, disdainfully; Ś. 2. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सास्ना
सास्ना The dew-lap of an ox;<BR>गोः सास्नादिमत्त्वं लक्षणं T. S;<BR>रोमथंमंथरचलद्गुरुसास्नमासांचक्रे<BR>निमीलदलसेक्षणमौक्षकेण Śi. 5. 62.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहचर्यं|साहचर्य|साहचर्य्य|साहचर्य्यं
साहचर्यं Companionship,<BR>(constant) fellowship or association,<BR>living together, concomitance; किं<BR>न स्मरसि यदेकत्र नो विद्यापरिग्रहाय<BR>नानादिगंतवासिनां साहचर्यमासीत्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-a" target="_blank">Page1122-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Māl. 1; Ku. 3. 21, R. 16. 87, Ve. 1. 20,<BR>Śi. 15. 24.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नियमः a rule<BR>of invariable concomitance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1121-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहनं|साहन
साहनं Endurance, suffering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसं|साहस|साहसः
साहसं [सहसा बलेन निर्वृत्तं अण्]<BR>1<BR>Violence, force, rapine; Ms. 7. 48.<BR>--2 Any criminal act (such as<BR>robbery, rape, felony &c.), a heinous<BR>crime, an aggressive act.<BR>--3 Cruelty,<BR>oppression; Śi. 9. 59.<BR>--4 Boldness,<BR>daring, daring courage; साहसे श्रीः<BR>प्रतिवसति Mk. 4.<BR>--5 Precipitation,<BR>rashness, temerity, an inconsiderate or<BR>reckless act, a rash or daring act;<BR>तदपि साहसाभासं Māl. 2; किमपरमतो<BR>निर्व्यूढं यत्करार्पणसाहसं 9. 10;<BR>Pt. 1. 191; Ki. 17. 42.<BR>--6 Punishment,<BR>chastisement, fine (m. also in this<BR>sense), see Ms. 8. 138; Y. 1. 66,<BR>365.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकः {1} an epithet<BR>of king Vikramāditya. {2} of a poet.<BR>{3} of a lexicographer.<BR>--अध्यवसायिन् a. acting rashly or with<BR>inconsiderate haste.<BR>--एकरसिक a.<BR>wholly intent on violence, ferocious,<BR>brutal.<BR>--कारिन् a. {1} bold,<BR>audacious. {2} rash, inconsiderate.<BR>--लांछन<BR>a. characterized by boldness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिकः|साहसिक
साहसिकः a. (की f.) [साहसे प्रसृतः ठक्]<BR>1 Using great force or violence,<BR>brutal, violent, rapacious, cruel,<BR>felonious.<BR>--2 Bold, daring, rash,<BR>inconsiderate, reckless; न सहास्मि<BR>साहसमसाहसिकी Śi. 9. 59; केचित्तु<BR>साहसिकास्त्रिलोचनमिति पेठुः Malli. on<BR>Ku. 3. 44.<BR>--3 Castigatory, punitive.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A bold or adventurous person, an<BR>enterprising man; Pt. 5. 31.<BR>--2 A<BR>desperado, desperate or dangerous<BR>person; या किल विविधजीवोपहारप्रियेति<BR>साहसिकानां प्रवादः Māl. 1; साहिसकः<BR>खल्वेषः 6.<BR>--3 A felon, freebooter,<BR>robber.<BR>--4 An adulterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहसिन्
साहसिन् a. [साहस-इनि]<BR>1<BR>Violent, ferocious, cruel.<BR>--2 Bold,<BR>daring, rash, impetuous.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहस्र|साहस्रं|साहस्रः
साहस्र a. (स्री f.) [सहस्र-अण्]<BR>1 Relating to a thousand.<BR>--2<BR>Consisting of a thousand.<BR>--3 Bought<BR>with a thousand.<BR>--4 Paid per<BR>thousand (as interest &c.).<BR>--5 A<BR>thousand-fold.<BR>--स्रः An army or<BR>detachment consisting of a thousand<BR>men.<BR>--स्रं An aggregate of a<BR>thousand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहायकं|साहायक
साहायकं<BR>1 Assistance, help<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-b" target="_blank">Page1122-b+ 56</a>]<BR>aid; स कुलोचितमिंद्रस्य<BR>साहायकमुपोयिवान् R. 17. 4.<BR>--2 Fellowship,<BR>alliance, friendship.<BR>--3 A number of<BR>companions or associates.<BR>--4<BR>Auxiliary troops.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहाय्यं|साहाय्य
साहाय्यं<BR>1 Assistance, help,<BR>succour.<BR>--2 Friendship, alliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साहित्यं|साहित्य
साहित्यं<BR>1 Association, fellowship,<BR>combination, society.<BR>--2 Literary<BR>or rhetorical composition;<BR>साहित्यसंगीतकलाविहीनः साक्षात्पशुः<BR>पुच्छविषाणहीनः Bh. 2. 12.<BR>--3 The science of<BR>rhetoric, art of poetry; Vikr. 1. 11;<BR>साहित्यदर्पणं &c.<BR>--4 A collection of<BR>materials for the production or<BR>performance of anything (a<BR>doubtful sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्यं|साह्य
साह्यं<BR>1 Conjunction, union,<BR>fellowship, society.<BR>--2 Assistance,<BR>help.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कृत् m. a companion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

साह्वयः|साह्वय
साह्वयः Gambling with fighting<BR>animals.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सि
सि {c5c} {c9c} U. (सिनोति, सिनुते,<BR>सिनाति, सिनीते)<BR>1 To bind, tie, fasten.<BR>--2<BR>To ensnare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहः|सिंह
सिंहः [हिंस्-अच् पृषो˚]<BR>1 A lion;<BR>(it is said to be derived from हिंस्; cf.<BR>भवेद्वर्णागमाद्धंसः सिंहो वर्णविपर्ययात्<BR>Sk.); न हि सुप्तस्य सिंहस्य प्रविशंति मुखे<BR>मृगाः Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 The sign Leo of<BR>the zodiac.<BR>--3 (At the end of comp.)<BR>Best, pre-eminent of a class; e. g.<BR>रघुसिंह, पुरुषसिंह; Pt. 1. 361; U. 5. 22.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवलोकनं the<BR>(backward) glance of a lion. ˚न्यायः the<BR>maxim of the lion's (backward)<BR>glance, generally used to mark<BR>the connection of a thing with<BR>what precedes and follows; (for<BR>explanation see under न्याय).<BR>--आसनं a throne, a seat of honour.<BR>--(नः)<BR>a particular mode of sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR>--आस्यः a particular position<BR>of the hands.<BR>--केशरः {1} the Bakula<BR>tree. {2} a lion's mane.<BR>--गः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--तलं the palms of<BR>the hands opened and joined<BR>together.<BR>--तुंडः a kind of fish.<BR>--दंष्ट्रः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--दर्प a. as proud<BR>as a lion.<BR>--द्वारं the main or<BR>principal gate (of a palace &c.).<BR>--ध्वनिः,<BR>--नादः {1} the roar of a lion;<BR>Ku. 1. 56; Mk. 5. 29. {2} a war-cry.<BR>--नादः<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--याना, --रथा N. of the<BR>goddess Pārvatī.<BR>--लीलः a kind of<BR>coitus.<BR>--वाहनः an epithet of Śiva.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">Page1122-c+ 55</a>]<BR>--वाहिनी an epithet of Durgā.<BR>--विक्रांतः a horse.<BR>--संहनन a. {1} as strong<BR>as a lion. {2} handsome.<BR>--(नं) the<BR>killing of a lion.<BR>--स्थः an epithet of<BR>the planet Jupiter when in the<BR>constellation Leo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंही
सिंही<BR>1 A lioness.<BR>--2 N. of the<BR>mother of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहलं|सिंहल|सिंहलः
सिंहलं [सिंहोऽस्त्यस्य लच्]<BR>1 Tin.<BR>--2 Brass.<BR>--3 Bark, rind.<BR>--4 The<BR>island or country of Ceylon (oft. in<BR>pl.); सिंहलेभ्यः प्रत्यागच्छता,<BR>सिंहलेश्वरदुहितुः फलकासादनं Ratn. 1.<BR>--लाः<BR>(m. pl.) The people of Ceylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहलकं|सिंहलक
सिंहलकं The island of Ceylon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाणं|सिंहाण
सिंहाणं(नं), सिंहाणकः --कं<BR>1 Rust<BR>of iron.<BR>--2 The mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहानं|सिंहान
सिंहाणं(नं), सिंहाणकः --कं<BR>1 Rust<BR>of iron.<BR>--2 The mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाणकः|सिंहाणक|सिंहाणकं
सिंहाणं(नं), सिंहाणकः --कं<BR>1 Rust<BR>of iron.<BR>--2 The mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहाणकं|सिंहाणक|सिंहाणकः
सिंहाणं(नं), सिंहाणकः --कं<BR>1 Rust<BR>of iron.<BR>--2 The mucus of the nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंहिका
सिंहिका The mother of Rāhu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--तनयः, --पुत्रः, --सुतः, --सूनुः<BR>epithets of Rāhu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकता
सिकता<BR>1 Sandy soil.<BR>--2 Sand<BR>(generally in pl.); लभेत सिकतासु<BR>तैलमति यत्नतः पीडयन् Bh. 2. 5.<BR>--3<BR>Gravel or stone (the disease).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतामय|सिकतामयं
सिकतामय, सिकतावत् a. Sandy.<BR>--यं<BR>1 A sand bank.<BR>--2 An island with<BR>sandy shores.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतावत्|सिकतावन्त्
सिकतामय, सिकतावत् a. Sandy.<BR>--यं<BR>1 A sand bank.<BR>--2 An island with<BR>sandy shores.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिकतिल|सिकतिलः
सिकतिल a. [सिकताः संत्यत्र इलच्]<BR>Sandy; Bh. 3. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थः|सिक्थ|सिक्थं
सिक्थः [सिच्-थक्]<BR>1 Boiled rice.<BR>--2 A ball or lump of boiled rice;<BR>ग्रासोद्गलितसिक्थेन का हानिः करिणो<BR>भवेत् Subhāṣ.<BR>--क्थं<BR>1 Bees'-wax.<BR>--2<BR>Indigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्थकं|सिक्थक
सिक्थकं Bees'--wax.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्यं|सिक्य
सिक्यं See शिक्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्ष्यः|सिक्ष्य
सिक्ष्यः Crystal, glass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंघणं|सिङ्घण|सिंघण|सिङ्घणं
सिंघ(घा)णं, सिंघाणकं<BR>1 The<BR>mucus of the nose.<BR>--2 Rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंघाणं|सिङ्घाण|सिंघाण|सिङ्घाणं
सिंघ(घा)णं, सिंघाणकं<BR>1 The<BR>mucus of the nose.<BR>--2 Rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंघाणकं|सिङ्घाणक|सिङ्घाणकं
सिंघ(घा)णं, सिंघाणकं<BR>1 The<BR>mucus of the nose.<BR>--2 Rust of iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंघिणी|सिङ्घिणी
सिंघिणी The nose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिच्
सिच् {c6c} U. (सिंचति-ते, सिषेच-सिषिचे,<BR>असिचत्त, असिक्त, सेक्ष्यति-ते, सेक्तुं, सिक्त; स् of<BR>सिच् is generally changed to ष् after<BR>a preposition ending in इ or उ)<BR>1 To<BR>sprinkle, scatter in small drops,<BR>Bk. 19. 23.<BR>--2 To water, moisten;<BR>soak, wet; विश्रांतः सन् व्रज<BR>वननदीतीरजातानि सिंचन् Me. 26; Ms. 9. 255.<BR>--3 To pour out, emit, discharge,<BR>shed; R. 16. 66.<BR>--4 To infuse,<BR>instil, pour in; जाड्यं धियो हरति<BR>सिंचति वाचि सत्यं Bh. 2. 23.<BR>--5 To pour<BR>out for, offer to; अन्यथा तिलोदकं मे<BR>सिंचतं Ś. 3.<BR>--6 To impregnate.<BR>--Caus. (सेचयति-ते) To cause to<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">Page1123-a+ 55</a>]<BR>sprinkle. --Desid. (सिसिक्षति-ते) To<BR>wish to sprinkle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1122-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्त|सिक्तः
सिक्त p. p.<BR>1 Sprinkled, watered.<BR>--2 Wetted, moistened, soaked.<BR>--3<BR>Impregnated; see सिच्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिक्तिः|सिक्ति
सिक्तिः f.<BR>1 Sprinkling.<BR>--2<BR>Effusion.<BR>--3 Emission.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिचयः|सिचय
सिचयः [सिच्-अयच् किच्च]<BR>1 Cloth,<BR>garment.<BR>--2 Old or ragged raiment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंचिता|सिञ्चिता
सिंचिता Long pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंजा|सिञ्जा
सिंजा The jingling sound of<BR>metallic ornaments.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंजितं|सिञ्जित|सिंजित
सिंजितं Tinkling, jingling;<BR>आदित्सुभिर्नूपुरसिंजितानि Ku. 1. 34,<BR>V. 4. 14.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिट्
सिट् {c1c} P. (सेटति) To disregard,<BR>despise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सित|सितं|सितः
सित a. [सो-क्त]<BR>1 White.<BR>--2<BR>Bound, tied, fastened, fettered.<BR>--3<BR>Surrounded.<BR>--4 Ascertained, known.<BR>--5 Finished, ended.<BR>--तः<BR>1 White<BR>colour.<BR>--2 The bright half of a lunar<BR>month.<BR>--3 The planet Venus.<BR>--4<BR>An arrow.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Silver.<BR>--2 Sandal.<BR>--3 Radish.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशु = सितकर<BR>q. v.<BR>--अग्रः a thorn.<BR>--अंगः the<BR>श्वेतरोहित tree.<BR>--अजाजी white cumin.<BR>--अपांगः a peacock.<BR>--अभ्रः, --भ्रं<BR>camphor.<BR>--अंबरः an ascetic dressed<BR>in white garments.<BR>--अर्जकः white<BR>basil.<BR>--अश्वः an epithet of Arjuna.<BR>--असितः an epithet of Balarāma.<BR>--(तौ) Venus and Saturn.<BR>--आदिः<BR>molasses.<BR>--आननः N. of Garuḍa.<BR>--आभः camphor.<BR>--आलिका a cockle.<BR>--इतर a. other than white; i. e. black.<BR>˚गतिः fire.<BR>--उदरः an epithet of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--उद्भवं white sandal.<BR>--उपलः a crystal.<BR>--उपला candied sugar.<BR>--उपलः chalk.<BR>--करः {1} the moon.<BR>{2} camphor.<BR>--धातुः a white mineral,<BR>chalk.<BR>--रशिमः the moon.<BR>--वाजिन्<BR>m. N. of Arjuna.<BR>--शर्करा candied<BR>sugar.<BR>--शिंबिकः wheat.<BR>--शिवं<BR>rock-salt.<BR>--शूकः barley.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिता
सिता<BR>1 Candied sugar, sugar;<BR>पित्तेन दूने रसने सितापि तिक्तायते हंसकुला<BR>वतंस N. 3. 94; Bv. 4. 13.<BR>--2<BR>Moonlight.<BR>--3 A lovely woman.<BR>--4<BR>Spirituous liquor.<BR>--5 White Dūrvā grass.<BR>--6 Arabian jasmine.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--खंडः<BR>a kind of refined sugar.<BR>--लता<BR>white Dūrvā grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिति|सितिः
सिति a.<BR>1 White.<BR>--2 Black.<BR>--तिः<BR>1 White or black colour.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-b" target="_blank">Page1123-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Binding, fastening.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठ, --वासस्<BR>see शितिकंठ; शितिवासस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सितिमन्
सितिमन् m. Whiteness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्
सिध् {vI.v} {c4c} P. (सिध्यति, सिषेध,<BR>असिधत्, सेत्स्यति, सेद्धुं, सिद्ध; caus. साधयति<BR>or सेधयति; desid. सिषित्सति)<BR>1 To be<BR>accomplished or fulfilled; यत्ने कृते<BR>यदि न सिध्यति कोऽत्र दोषः H. Pr. 31;<BR>उद्यमेन हि सिध्यंति कार्याणि न मनोरथैः<BR>36; Pt. 15. 8.<BR>--2 To be successful,<BR>succeed; सिध्यंति कर्मसु महत्स्वपि<BR>यन्नियोज्याः Ś. 7. 4.<BR>--3 To reach, hit,<BR>fall true on; उत्कर्षः स च धन्विनां<BR>यदिषवः सिध्यंति लक्ष्ये चले Ś. 2. 5.<BR>--4<BR>To attain one's object.<BR>--5 To be<BR>proved or established, to become<BR>valid; यदि वचनमावेणैवाधिपत्यं सिध्यति<BR>H. 3.<BR>--6 To be settled or<BR>adjudicated.<BR>--7 To be thoroughly prepared<BR>or cooked.<BR>--8 To be won or<BR>conquered. Pt. 2. 36. {vII.v} {c1c} P. (सेधति, सिद्ध;<BR>the स् of सिध् is generally changed<BR>to ष् after a preposition ending in<BR>इ or उ)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To ward or<BR>drive off.<BR>--3 To restrain, hinder,<BR>prevent.<BR>--4 To interdict, prohibit.<BR>--5 To ordain, command, instruct.<BR>--6 To turn out well or auspiciously.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्ध|सिद्धं|सिद्धः
सिद्ध p. p.<BR>1 Accomplished,,<BR>effected, performed, achieved, completed.<BR>--2 Gained, obtained, acquired.<BR>--3<BR>Succeeded, successful.<BR>--4 Settled,<BR>established; नैसर्गिकी सुरभिणः<BR>कुसुमस्य सिद्धा मूर्ध्नि स्थितिर्न चरणैरवताडनानि<BR>U. 1. 14.<BR>--5 Proved, demonstrated,<BR>substantiated; तस्मादिंद्रियं<BR>प्रत्यक्षप्रमाणमिति सिद्धं T. S., Ms. 8. 178.<BR>--6<BR>Valid, sound (as a rule).<BR>--7<BR>Admitted to be true.<BR>--8 Decided,<BR>adjudicated (as a law-suit.).<BR>--9 Paid,<BR>discharged, liquidated (as debt).<BR>--10 Cooked, dressed (as food);<BR>Pt. 2. 114.<BR>--11 Matared, ripened.<BR>--12 Thoroughly prepared,<BR>compounded, cooked together (as drugs).<BR>--13 Ready (as money).<BR>--14<BR>Subdued, won over, subjugated (as by<BR>magic).<BR>--15 Brought under<BR>subjection, become propitious.<BR>--16<BR>Thoroughly conversant with or<BR>skilled in, proficient in; as in<BR>रतसिद्ध q. v.<BR>--17 Perfected, sanctified<BR>(as by penance).<BR>--18 Emancipated.<BR>--19 Endowed with supernatural<BR>powers or faculties.<BR>--20 Pious,<BR>sacred, holy.<BR>--21 Divine, immortal,<BR>eternal.<BR>--22 Celebrated, well-known,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-c" target="_blank">Page1123-c+ 57</a>]<BR>illustrious.<BR>--23 Shining, splendid,<BR>--द्धः<BR>1 A semi-divine being<BR>supposed to be of great purity and<BR>holiness, and said to be particularly<BR>characterized by eight supernatural<BR>faculties called Siddhis q. v.;<BR>उद्वेजिता वृष्टिभिराश्रयंते शृंगाणि यस्यातपवंति<BR>सिद्धाः Ku. 1. 5.<BR>--2 An inspired<BR>sage or seer (like Vyāsa).<BR>--3 Any<BR>sage or seer, a prophet; सिद्धादेश<BR>Ratn. 1.<BR>--4 One skilled in magical<BR>arts, a magician.<BR>--5 A law-suit,<BR>judicial trial.<BR>--6 A kind of hard<BR>sugar.<BR>--7 The dark thorn-apple.<BR>--द्धं Sea-salt.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतः {1} the<BR>established end. {2} the<BR>demonstrated conclusion of an argument,<BR>established view of any question,<BR>the true logical conclusion<BR>(following on the refutation of the<BR>Pūrvapakṣa). {3} a proved fact,<BR>established truth, dogma, settled doctrine.<BR>{4} any established text-book<BR>resting on conclusive evidence. ˚कोटिः<BR>f. the point in an argument which<BR>is regarded as a logical conclusion.<BR>˚पक्षः the logically correct side of an<BR>argument.<BR>--अन्नं cooked food.<BR>--अर्थ<BR>a. one who has accomplished his<BR>desired object, successful.<BR>--(र्थः) {1}<BR>white mustard. {2} N. of Śiva. {3}<BR>of the great Buddha.<BR>--आसनं a<BR>particular posture in religious<BR>meditation.<BR>--क्षेत्रं the abode of sages<BR>or Siddhas.<BR>--गंगा, --नदी, --सिंधुः the<BR>celestial Ganges.<BR>--ग्रहः N. of a<BR>particular kind of madness or<BR>dementia.<BR>--जलं, --सलिलं sour rice-gruel.<BR>--देवः N. of Śiva.<BR>--धातुः<BR>quicksilver.<BR>--पक्षः the established or<BR>logical side of an argument.<BR>--पुरुष = सिद्धः (1, 3, 4) above.<BR>--पुष्पः<BR>the Karavīra plant.<BR>--प्रयोजनः white<BR>mustard.<BR>--यात्रिकः one wandering<BR>about for the acquisition of magical<BR>power; Pt. 5.<BR>--योगिन् m. an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--रस a. mineral,<BR>metallic.<BR>--(सः) {1} quick-silver. {2}<BR>an alchemist.<BR>--संकल्प a. one who<BR>has accomplished his desired object.<BR>--साधकः N. of Śiva.<BR>--साधनः<BR>white mustard.<BR>--(नं) {1} the<BR>performance of magical rites for the<BR>acquisition of supernatural powers<BR>&c. {2} the materials employed<BR>in mystical or chemical processes.<BR>--साध्य a. accomplished, proved.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-a" target="_blank">Page1124-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--(ध्यं) a dogma, demonstrated<BR>conclusion.<BR>--सेनः N. of Kārtikeya.<BR>--स्थाली the boiler or pot of a seer<BR>(it is supposed to be a vessel which<BR>is gifted with the property of<BR>overflowing with any kind of food at<BR>the desire of the possessor).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1123-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धकः|सिद्धक
सिद्धकः The Sāla tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धता
सिद्धता --त्वं<BR>1 Accomplishment,<BR>fulfilment, perfection.<BR>--2 Validity of<BR>a rule or doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धत्वं|सिद्धत्व
सिद्धता --त्वं<BR>1 Accomplishment,<BR>fulfilment, perfection.<BR>--2 Validity of<BR>a rule or doctrine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धांतिन्|सिद्धान्तिन्
सिद्धांतिन् m.<BR>1 One who establishes<BR>a conclusion after noticing and<BR>answering objections (or पूर्वपक्ष).<BR>--2 One learned in scientific<BR>textbooks.<BR>--3 A follower of the<BR>Mīmāmsā philosophy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिद्धिः|सिद्धि
सिद्धिः f. [सिध्-क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>Accomplishment, fulfilment, completion,<BR>perfection, complete attainment (of<BR>an object); क्रियासिद्धिः सत्त्वे भवति<BR>महतां नोपकरणे Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 Success,<BR>prosperity, welfare, well-being.<BR>--3<BR>Establishment, settlement.<BR>--4<BR>Substantiation, demonstration, proof,<BR>indisputable conclusion.<BR>--5<BR>Validity (of a rule, law &c.).<BR>--6 Decision,<BR>adjudication, settlement (of a<BR>lawsuit).<BR>--7 Certainty, truth, accuracy,<BR>correctness.<BR>--8 Payment, liquidation<BR>(of a debt).<BR>--9 Preparing, cooking<BR>(as of drugs &c.).<BR>--10 The<BR>solution of a problem.<BR>--11 Readiness.<BR>--12 Complete purity or<BR>sanctification.<BR>--13 A superhuman power or<BR>faculty; (these faculties are eight:<BR>--अणिमा लघिमा प्राप्तिः प्राकाम्यं महिमा तथा ।<BR>ईशित्वं च वशित्वं च तथा कामावसायिता).<BR>--14 The acquisition of supernatural<BR>powers by magical means.<BR>--15<BR>Marvellous skill or capability.<BR>--16<BR>Good effect or result.<BR>--17 Final<BR>beatitude, final emancipation.<BR>--18<BR>Understanding, intellect.<BR>--19<BR>Concealment, vanishing, making<BR>oneself invisible.<BR>--20 A magical shoe.<BR>--21 A kind of Yoga.<BR>--22 N. of<BR>Durgā.<BR>--23 Complete knowledge.<BR>--24 Advantage, use, good effect.<BR>--25 N. of Śiva (m. in this sense).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--द a. {1} granting success<BR>or supreme felicity. {2} giving the<BR>eight superhuman faculties;<BR>Māl. 5. 1.<BR>--(दः) an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--दात्री an epithet of Durgā.<BR>--योगः a<BR>particular auspicious conjunction<BR>of planets.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मं|सिध्म
सिध्मं, सिध्मन् n. [सिध्-मन् किच्च]<BR>1 Blotch, scab.<BR>--2 Leprosy.<BR>--3 A<BR>leprous spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मन्
सिध्मं, सिध्मन् n. [सिध्-मन् किच्च]<BR>1 Blotch, scab.<BR>--2 Leprosy.<BR>--3 A<BR>leprous spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मल|सिध्मलः
सिध्मल, सिध्मवत् a. Seabby, tainted<BR>with leprosy, leprous.<BR>--ला See सिध्मं<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मवत्|सिध्मवन्त्
सिध्मल, सिध्मवत् a. Seabby, tainted<BR>with leprosy, leprous.<BR>--ला See सिध्मं<BR>above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्मा
सिध्मा<BR>1 A blotch, scab, leprous<BR>spot.<BR>--2 Leprosy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्यः|सिध्य
सिध्यः The asterism Puṣya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्र|सिध्रः
सिध्र a.<BR>1 Perfect, good.<BR>--2<BR>Protecting.<BR>--ध्रः<BR>1 A pious or<BR>virtuous man.<BR>--2 A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिध्रकावणं|सिध्रकावण
सिध्रकावणं N. of one of the<BR>celestial gardens.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिन|सिनं|सिनः
सिन a.<BR>1 White.<BR>--2 One-eyed.<BR>--नः A morsel, mouthful.<BR>--नं<BR>1 The<BR>body.<BR>--2 Ved. Food.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनी
सिनी A woman having a white<BR>complexion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिनीवाली
सिनीवाली The day preceding<BR>that of new moon, or that day on<BR>which the moon rises with a<BR>scarcely visible crescent; या पूर्वामावास्या<BR>सा सिनीवाली योत्तरा सा कुंहूः Ait. Br.;<BR>or सा दृष्टेंदुः सिनीवाली सा नष्टेंदुकला<BR>कुहूः Ak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंदुकः|सिन्दुक|सिंदुक|सिन्दुकः
सिंदुकः, सिंदुवारः N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंदुवारः|सिन्दुवार|सिंदुवार|सिन्दुवारः
सिंदुकः, सिंदुवारः N. of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंदूरः|सिन्दूर|सिंदूर|सिन्दूरं|सिन्दूरः
सिंदूरः [स्यंद्-उरन् संप्रसारणं<BR>Uṇ. 1. 68] A kind of tree.<BR>--रं Red lead;<BR>स्वयं सिंदूरेण द्विपरणमुदा मुद्रित इव<BR>Gīt. 11; N. 22. 45.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारणं lead.<BR>--तिलकः an elephant.<BR>--(का) a<BR>woman whose husband is living.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंदूरिका|सिन्दूरिका
सिंदूरिका Red-lead.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंदूरित|सिन्दूरित
सिंदूरित a. Reddned, made red.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंदूरी
सिंदूरी Red cloth or clothes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंधुः|सिन्धु|सिंधु|सिन्धुः
सिंधुः [स्यंद्-उद् संप्रसारणं दस्य धश्च<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 The sea, ocean.<BR>--2 The<BR>Indus.<BR>--3 The country around the<BR>Indus.<BR>--4 N. of a river in Mālvā;<BR>Me. 29 (where Malli.'s remark<BR>सिंधुर्नाम नदी तु कुत्रापि नास्ति is gratuitous);<BR>Māl. 4. 9 (see Dr. Bhāndārkar's<BR>note ad loc.).<BR>--5 The water ejected<BR>from an elephant's trunk.<BR>--6 The<BR>juice exuding from the temples of<BR>an elephant.<BR>--7 An elephant.<BR>--8 N. of<BR>Varuṇa.<BR>--9 White borax.<BR>--10 A kind of<BR>musical mode (राग). --pl. The<BR>inhabitants of the Sindhu country. --f.<BR>1 A<BR>great river or river in general;<BR>पिबत्यसौ पाययते च सिंधूः R. 13. 9;<BR>Me. 46; Ś. 5. 21; Ku. 3. 6; 5. 85.<BR>--2<BR>The river Sindhu.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्थं,<BR>--उपलं rock-salt.<BR>--कफः cuttle-fish<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-c" target="_blank">Page1124-c+ 53</a>]<BR>bone.<BR>--खेलः the country Sindha.<BR>--ज, --जन्मन् a. {1} aquatic. {2}<BR>riverborn. {3} sea-born, born in the<BR>Sindh country.<BR>--(जः) the moon.<BR>--(जं)<BR>rock-salt.<BR>--नाथः the ocean.<BR>--पुष्पः<BR>a conch-shell.<BR>--राजः, --पतिः N. of<BR>Jayadratha; Ve. 3.<BR>--लवणं<BR>rocksalt.<BR>--वारः a horse of good breed<BR>(brought from Sindha or Persia).<BR>--शयनः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1124-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंधुकः|सिन्धुक|सिंधुक|सिन्धुकः
