सौभद्रेयः|सौभद्रेय
सौभद्रः, सौभद्रेयः Epithets of<BR>Abhimanyu, son of Subhadrā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभागिनेयः|सौभागिनेय
सौभागिनेयः The son of a<BR>favourite wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यं|सौभाग्य
सौभाग्यं [सुभगायाः सुभगस्य वा भावः<BR>ष्यञ् द्विपदवृद्धिः]<BR>1 Good fortune or<BR>luck, fortunateness (chiefly<BR>consisting in a man's and woman's<BR>securing the favour and firm devotion of<BR>each other); प्रियेषु सौभाग्यफला हि<BR>चारुता Ku. 5. 1; सौभाग्यं ते सुभग<BR>विरहावस्थया व्यंजयंती Me. 29; (see<BR>Malli.'s remarks on सौभाग्य in both<BR>places); युज्यत आत्मनः सौभाग्यं<BR>प्रच्छादयितुं V. 2.<BR>--2 Blessedness,<BR>auspiciousness.<BR>--3 Beauty, charm, grace;<BR>(यस्य) हिमं न सौभाग्यविलोपि जातं<BR>Ku. 1. 3; 2. 53, 5. 49; R. 18. 19,<BR>U. 6. 27.<BR>--4 Grandeur, sublimity.<BR>--5 The auspicious state of<BR>wifehood (opp. widowhood).<BR>--6<BR>Congratulation; good wishes.<BR>--7<BR>Affection, favour.<BR>--8 Red-lead.<BR>--9 Borax.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चिह्नं {1} any mark of good<BR>fortune or happiness. {2} any sign of<BR>the blessed state of wifehood (such<BR>as the saffron mark on the forehead).<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">Page1141-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--तंतुः the marriage-string (put<BR>round the neck of the bride by the<BR>bridegroom at the time of marriage<BR>and worn by her till widowhood; also<BR>called मंगलसूत्र q. v.).<BR>--तृतीया the third<BR>day of the bright half of<BR>Bhādrapada.<BR>--देवता an auspicious or<BR>tutelary deity.<BR>--वायनं an auspicious<BR>offering of sweetmeats &c.<BR>--विलेपिन् a. marring or impairing beauty;<BR>Ku. 1. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभाग्यवत्|सौभाग्यवन्त्
सौभाग्यवत् a. Fortunate,<BR>auspicious.<BR>--ती A married woman whose<BR>husband is alive, a married<BR>unwidowed woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभिकः|सौभिक
सौभिकः A juggler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौभ्रात्रं|सौभ्रात्र
सौभ्रात्रं Good brotherhood,<BR>fraternity; सौभ्रात्रमेषां हि कुलानुसारि<BR>R. 16. 1; 10. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस
सौमनस a. (सा or सी f.) [<BR>सुमनस्-अण्]<BR>1 Agreeable to the feelings,<BR>pleasing.<BR>--2 Relating to flowers,<BR>floral.<BR>--सं Kindliness of spirit,<BR>benevolence, kindness. --Pleasure,<BR>satisfaction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनसा
सौमनसा The outer skin of the<BR>nutmeg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्यं|सौमनस्य
सौमनस्यं<BR>1 Satisfaction of mind,<BR>pleasure, delight; R. 15. 14,<BR>17. 40.<BR>--2 A particular offering of<BR>flowers made to a Brāhmaṇa at a<BR>Śrāddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमनस्यायनी
सौमनस्यायनी<BR>1 The blossom of<BR>the Mālatī creeper.<BR>--2 The Mālatī<BR>creeper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमायनः|सौमायन
सौमायनः A patronymic of<BR>Buddha.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिक
सौमिक a. (की f.)<BR>1<BR>Performed with or relating to the Soma<BR>juice.<BR>--2 Relating to the moon,<BR>lunar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमित्रः|सौमित्र
सौमित्रः; सौमित्रिः An epithet<BR>of Lakṣmaṇa; सौमित्रेरपि<BR>पत्रिणामविषये तत्र प्रिये क्वासि भोः U. 3. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमित्रिः|सौमित्रि
सौमित्रः; सौमित्रिः An epithet<BR>of Lakṣmaṇa; सौमित्रेरपि<BR>पत्रिणामविषये तत्र प्रिये क्वासि भोः U. 3. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमिल्लः|सौमिल्ल
सौमिल्लः N. of a dramatist who<BR>preceded Kālidāsa;<BR>भासकविसौमिल्लकविमिश्रादीनां M. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेचकं|सौमेचक
सौमेचकं Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेधिकः|सौमेधिक
सौमेधिकः A sage, seer, one<BR>possessed of supernatural wisdom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौमेरुक|सौमेरुकं
सौमेरुक a. (की f.) Relating to<BR>or coming from Sumeru.<BR>--कं Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौम्य|सौम्यः
सौम्य a. (म्या or म्यी f.) [सोमो<BR>देवतास्य तस्येदं वा अण्]<BR>1 Relating or<BR>sacred to the moon.<BR>--2 Having the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-c" target="_blank">Page1141-c+ 57</a>]<BR>properties of Soma.<BR>--3 Handsome,<BR>lovely, charming; pleasing,<BR>agreeable.<BR>--4 Gentle, soft, mild,<BR>placid; सरंभं मैथिलीहासः क्षणसौम्यां निनाय<BR>तां R. 12. 36; (the voc. सौम्य is<BR>often used in the sense of ‘good<BR>sir,’ ‘gentle sir,’ ‘good man’;<BR>प्रीतास्ति ते सौम्य चिराय जीव R. 14. 59;<BR>सौम्येति चाभाष्य यथार्थवादी 14. 44,<BR>Me. 49, Ku. 4. 35, Māl. 9. 25).<BR>--5 Auspicious.<BR>--6 Bright,<BR>brilliant.<BR>--म्यः<BR>1 N. of Budha or the<BR>planet Mercury.<BR>--2 A proper<BR>epithet by which a Brāhmaṇa should<BR>be addressed; आयुष्मान्भव सौम्येति<BR>वाच्यो विप्रोऽभिवादने Ms. 2. 125.<BR>--3<BR>A Brāhmaṇa.<BR>--4 The Udumbara<BR>tree.<BR>--5 Blood before it becomes<BR>red, serum.<BR>--6 The gastric juice.<BR>--7 N. of one of the nine divisions<BR>of the earth.<BR>--8 An auspicious<BR>planet.<BR>--9 A Brāhmaṇa drinking<BR>the Soma juice.<BR>--10 A kind of<BR>penance (सौम्यकृच्छ्र).<BR>--म्या<BR>1 N.<BR>of Durgā.<BR>--2 The moon-plant.<BR>--m. pl.<BR>1 N. of the five stars in<BR>Orion's head.<BR>--2 A particular class<BR>of Pitṛs or Manes; Ms. 3. 199.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपचारः a gentle measure,<BR>mild remedy.<BR>--कृच्छ्रः --च्छ्रं a kind<BR>of religious penance; cf.<BR>Y. 3. 322.<BR>--गंधी the Indian white rose.<BR>--ग्रहः a benign or auspicious<BR>planet.<BR>--धातुः the phlegmatic<BR>humour, phlegm.<BR>--नामन् a. having a<BR>pleasing or agreeable name;<BR>Ms. 3. 10.<BR>--वारः, --वासरः Wednesday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर|सौरः
सौर a. (री f.) [सूरस्य इदं मूरो<BR>देवतास्य वा अण्]<BR>1 Relating to the sun,<BR>solar.<BR>--2 Sacred or dedicated to the<BR>sun.<BR>--3 Worshipping the sun.<BR>--4 Celestial, divine.<BR>--5 Relating to<BR>spirituous liquor.<BR>--रः<BR>1 A<BR>worshipper of the sun.<BR>--2 The planet<BR>Saturn.<BR>--3 A solar month.<BR>--4 A<BR>solar day.<BR>--5 The plant called<BR>Tumburu.<BR>--6 N. of Yama, the<BR>god of death.<BR>--रं N. of a<BR>collection of hymns (extracted from<BR>the Ṛgveda) addressed to Sūrya.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नक्तं a particular<BR>religious observance.<BR>--मासः a solar<BR>month (comprising thirty risings<BR>and settings of the sun).<BR>--लोकः<BR>the sun's sphere.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरथः|सौरथ
सौरथः A hero, warrior.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ|सौरभं
सौरभ a. (भी f.) [सुरभिरस्यास्ति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">Page1142-a+ 54</a>]<BR>अण्] Fragrant.<BR>--भं<BR>1 Fragrance,<BR>Bv. 1. 18, 121.<BR>--2 Saffron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1141-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभेय|सौरभेयः
सौरभेय a. (यी f.) Relating to<BR>Surabhi.<BR>--यः An ox.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभी
सौरभी, सौरभेयी<BR>1 A cow.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of the daughter of the cow called<BR>Surabhi; तां सौरभेयीं सुरभिर्यशोभिः<BR>R. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभेयी
सौरभी, सौरभेयी<BR>1 A cow.<BR>--2 N.<BR>of the daughter of the cow called<BR>Surabhi; तां सौरभेयीं सुरभिर्यशोभिः<BR>R. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरभ्यं|सौरभ्य|सौरभ्यः
सौरभ्यं<BR>1 Fragrance, odour, sweet<BR>scent; सौरभ्यं भुवनत्रयेऽपि विदितं<BR>Bv. 1. 38; पुनाना सौरभ्यैः G. L. 43,<BR>R. 5. 69.<BR>--2 Agreeableness, beauty.<BR>--3 Good character, reputation, glory,<BR>fame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसेनाः
सौरसेनाः m. pl. N. of a district<BR>and its people.<BR>--नी See शौरसेनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसेयः|सौरसेय
सौरसेयः An epithet of Skanda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरसैंधव|सौरसैन्धव|सौरसैन्धवः
सौरसैंधव a. (वी f.) Belonging<BR>to the celestial river or Ganges,<BR>Gangetic; Śi. 13. 27.<BR>--वः A horse<BR>of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरस्यं|सौरस्य
सौरस्यं Tastiness, savoriness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराज्यं|सौराज्य
सौराज्यं Good government or<BR>rule; एको ययौ चैत्ररथप्रदेशान्<BR>सौराज्यरम्यानपरो विदर्भान् R. 5. 60.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्र|सौराष्ट्रः
सौराष्ट्र a. (ष्ट्रा or ष्ट्री f.) Coming<BR>from or relating to the district<BR>called Surāṣṭra (or Surat).<BR>--ष्ट्रः The<BR>district of Surāṣṭra. --m. pl. The<BR>people of Surāṣṭra.<BR>--ष्ट्रं Brass,<BR>bellmetal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्रकः|सौराष्ट्रक|सौराष्ट्रकं
सौराष्ट्रकः A kind of bell-metal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरिः|सौरि
सौरिः [सूरस्यापत्यं पुमान् इञ्]<BR>1 N.<BR>of the planet Saturn.<BR>--2 The Asana<BR>tree.<BR>--3 N. of Yama.<BR>--4 Of Karṇa.<BR>--5 Of Sugrīva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रत्नं a<BR>kind of gem (sapphire).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरिक|सौरिकः
सौरिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Celestial.<BR>--2<BR>Spirituous, vinous.<BR>--3 Due for<BR>spirits (such as duty or money.)<BR>--कः<BR>1<BR>Saturn.<BR>--2 Heaven, paradise.<BR>--3<BR>A vender of spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरी
सौरी The wife of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौरीय|सौरीयं
सौरीय a. (यी f.)<BR>1 Solar.<BR>--2 Fit<BR>for, or suitable to, the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौर्य|सौर्य्य
सौर्य a. (र्यी f.) Belonging to the<BR>sun, solar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौलभ्यं|सौलभ्य
सौलभ्यं<BR>1 Easiness of<BR>acquisition.<BR>--2 Feasibility, facility, ease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौल्विकः|सौल्विक
सौल्विकः A copper-smith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौव|सौवं
सौव a. (वी f.)<BR>1 Relating to<BR>one's own property.<BR>--2 Being in<BR>or belonging to heaven.<BR>--वं An<BR>order, edict. (?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवग्रामिक|सौवग्रामिकं
सौवग्रामिक a. (की f.) Belonging<BR>to one's own village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर|सौवरं
सौवर a. (री f.)<BR>1 Belonging to<BR>sound or a musical note.<BR>--2<BR>Treating of accents.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्चल|सौवर्च्चल|सौवर्च्चलं
सौवर्चल a. (ली f.) Coming<BR>from the country called सुवर्चल<BR>q. v.<BR>--लं<BR>1 Sochal salt.<BR>--2 Natron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवर्ण|सौवर्णं|सौवर्णः
सौवर्ण a. (र्णी f.)<BR>1 Golden.<BR>--2<BR>Weighing one Suvarṇa q. v.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भेदिनी the plant Priyaṅgu.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवस्तिक|सौवस्तिकः
सौवस्तिक a. (की f.)<BR>Benedictive.<BR>--कः A family-priest or<BR>Brāhmaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवाध्यायिक
सौवाध्यायिक a. (की f.)<BR>Belonging to sacred study (or स्वाध्याय<BR>q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवास्तव|सौवास्तवः
सौवास्तव a. (वी f.) Having a<BR>good site, pleasantly situated or<BR>placed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविदः|सौविद
सौविदः, सौविदल्लः An attendant<BR>on the women's apartments;<BR>Śi. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौविदल्लः|सौविदल्ल
सौविदः, सौविदल्लः An attendant<BR>on the women's apartments;<BR>Śi. 5. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीरं|सौवीर|सौवीरः
सौवीरं<BR>1 The fruit of the jujube.<BR>--2 Antimony.<BR>--3 Sour gruel.<BR>--रः<BR>N. of a district or its people (pl. in<BR>the latter^1 sense).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजनं a<BR>kind of antimony or collyrium.<BR>--सारः<BR>antimony.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीरकः|सौवीरक|सौवीरकं
सौवीरकः<BR>1 The jujube tree.<BR>--2<BR>An inhabitant of Suvīra.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of Jayadratha.<BR>--कं Sour<BR>barleygruel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौवीर्यं|सौवीर्य|सौवीर्य्य
सौवीर्यं Great heroism or<BR>prowess.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौशील्यं|सौशील्य
सौशील्यं Excellence of<BR>disposition, good morals or character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौश्रवसं|सौश्रवस
सौश्रवसं Celebrity, renown.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौष्ठवं|सौष्ठव
सौष्ठवं [सुष्ठु भद्रं तस्य भावः अण्]<BR>1 Excellence, goodness, beauty,<BR>elegance, superior beauty;<BR>सर्वांगसौष्ठवाभिव्यक्तये विरलनेपथ्ययोः पात्रयोः<BR>प्रवेशोऽस्तु M. 1.; शरीरमसौष्ठवं<BR>Māl. 1. 17 ‘not in good trim’.<BR>--2<BR>Extreme skilfulness, cleverness.<BR>--3<BR>Excess.<BR>--4 Suppleness, lightness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौस्नातिकः|सौस्नातिक
सौस्नातिकः [सुस्नातं पृच्छति ठक्]<BR>One who asks another whether<BR>an ablution has been auspicious or<BR>successfully performed; सौस्नातिको<BR>यस्य भवत्यगस्त्यः R. 6. 61.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहार्दः|सौहार्द|सौहार्द्द|सौहार्द्दं|सौहार्द्दः
सौहार्दः [सुहृदो भावः अण् द्विपदवृद्धिः]<BR>The son of a friend.<BR>--र्दं<BR>Goodheartedness, affection, friendliness,<BR>friendship; (वेश्मानि) विश्राण्य<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">Page1142-c+ 56</a>]<BR>सौहार्दनिधिः सुहृद्भ्यः R. 14. 15;<BR>सौहार्दहृद्यानि विचेष्टितानि Māl. 1. 4; Me. 115.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहार्द्यं|सौहार्द्य
सौहार्द्यं, सौहृदं द्यं, सौहृदयं<BR>Friendship, affection; यत्सौहृदादपि जनाः<BR>शिथिलीभवंति Mk. 1. 13; सखीजनस्ते<BR>किमु रूढसौहृदः V. 1. 10; Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृदं|सौहृद
सौहार्द्यं, सौहृदं द्यं, सौहृदयं<BR>Friendship, affection; यत्सौहृदादपि जनाः<BR>शिथिलीभवंति Mk. 1. 13; सखीजनस्ते<BR>किमु रूढसौहृदः V. 1. 10; Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृद्यं|सौहृद्य
सौहार्द्यं, सौहृदं द्यं, सौहृदयं<BR>Friendship, affection; यत्सौहृदादपि जनाः<BR>शिथिलीभवंति Mk. 1. 13; सखीजनस्ते<BR>किमु रूढसौहृदः V. 1. 10; Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहृदयं|सौहृदय
सौहार्द्यं, सौहृदं द्यं, सौहृदयं<BR>Friendship, affection; यत्सौहृदादपि जनाः<BR>शिथिलीभवंति Mk. 1. 13; सखीजनस्ते<BR>किमु रूढसौहृदः V. 1. 10; Māl. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौहित्यं|सौहित्य
सौहित्यं<BR>1 Satiety, satisfaction;<BR>Śi. 5. 62.<BR>--2 Fulness, completion.<BR>--3 Kindness, friendliness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंद्|स्कन्द्
स्कंद् {c1c} A. (स्कंदते)<BR>1 To jump.<BR>--2 To raise.<BR>--3 To pour out, emit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंद्|स्कन्द्
स्कंद् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (स्कंदति, स्कन्न)<BR>1<BR>To leap, jump.<BR>--2 To rise, ascend,<BR>jump upwards.<BR>--3 To fall, drop;<BR>Bk. 22. 11.<BR>--4 To burst or leap<BR>out.<BR>--5 To perish, come to an end;<BR>चस्कंदे तप ऐश्वरम्.<BR>--6 To be spilled,<BR>ooze.<BR>--7 To emit, shed.<BR>--8 To go,<BR>move.<BR>--9 To become dry.<BR>--10 To<BR>perish. --Caus. (स्कंदयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>pour out, effuse, shed, emit (as<BR>the seminal fluid); एकः शयीत<BR>सर्वत्र न रेतः स्कंदयेत् क्वचित्<BR>Ms. 2. 180; 9. 50.<BR>--2 To omit, neglect,<BR>pass by. {vII.v} {c10c} U. (स्कंदयति-ते)<BR>To collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंदः|स्कन्द|स्कंद|स्कन्दः
स्कंदः [स्कंद्-अच्]<BR>1 Leaping.<BR>--2<BR>Quicksilver.<BR>--3 N. of Kārtikeya;<BR>सेनानीनामहं स्कंदः Bg. 10. 24,<BR>R. 2. 36, 7. 1; Me. 43.<BR>--4 N. of Śiva.<BR>--5<BR>The body.<BR>--6 A king.<BR>--7 The<BR>bank of a river.<BR>--8 A clever man.<BR>--9 A kind of disease common to<BR>children.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अशंकः<BR>quicksilver.<BR>--पुराणं one of the 18<BR>Purāṇas.<BR>--मा तृ f. N. of Durgā.<BR>--षष्ठी<BR>a festival in honour of Kārtikeya<BR>on the sixth day of Chaitra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंदकः|स्कन्दक|स्कंदक|स्कन्दकः
स्कंदकः<BR>1 One who leaps.<BR>--2 A<BR>soldier.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंदनं|स्कन्दन|स्कंदन|स्कन्दनं
स्कंदनं [स्कंद्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Emission,<BR>effusion.<BR>--2 Purging, looseness,<BR>relaxation (of the bowels).<BR>--3<BR>Going, moving.<BR>--4 Drying up.<BR>--5<BR>The suppression of bleeding by cold<BR>applications.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कन्न|स्कन्नं
स्कन्न p. p.<BR>1 Fallen down,<BR>descended.<BR>--2 Oozed out, or trickled<BR>down.<BR>--3 Emitted, effused,<BR>sprinkled<BR>--4 Gone.<BR>--5 Dried up.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंध्|स्कन्ध्
स्कंध् {c10c} U. (स्कंधयति-ते) To<BR>collect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंधः|स्कन्ध|स्कंध|स्कन्धः
स्कंधः [स्कद्यते आरुह्यतेऽसौ सुखेन<BR>शाखया वा कर्मणि घञ् पृषो˚; cf.<BR>Uṇ. 4. 206]<BR>1 The shoulder.<BR>--2 The<BR>body.<BR>--3 The trunk or stem of a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-a" target="_blank">Page1143-a+ 57</a>]<BR>tree; तीव्राघातप्रतिहततरुस्कंधलग्नैकदंतः<BR>Ś. 1. 33; R. 4. 57, Me. 53.<BR>--4<BR>A branch or large bough.<BR>--5 A<BR>department or branch of human<BR>knowledge.<BR>--6 A chapter, section,<BR>division (of a book).<BR>--7 A division<BR>or detachment of an army.<BR>--8 A<BR>troop, multitude, group.<BR>--9 The<BR>five objects of sense.<BR>--10 The five<BR>forms of mundane consciousness<BR>(in Buddhistic phil.);<BR>सर्वकार्यशरीरेषु मुक्त्वांगस्कंधपंचकं Śi. 2. 28.<BR>--11<BR>War, battle.<BR>--12 A king.<BR>--13 An<BR>agreement.<BR>--14 A road, way.<BR>--15<BR>A wise or learned man.<BR>--16 A<BR>heron.<BR>--17 Articles used at the<BR>coronation of a king.<BR>--धा<BR>1 A<BR>branch.<BR>--2 A creeper.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः the trunk of a tree set on fire.<BR>--आवारः {1} an army or a division of<BR>it. {2} a royal capital or residence.<BR>{3} a camp.<BR>--उपानेय a. to be<BR>carried on the shoulders.<BR>--(यः) a form<BR>of peace-offering in which fruit or<BR>grain is presented, as a mark of<BR>submission.<BR>--चापः a sort of pole<BR>or yoke for carrying burdens; cf.<BR>शिक्य.<BR>--जः a tree growing from a<BR>principal stem.<BR>--तरुः the cocoa nut<BR>tree.<BR>--देशः {1} the shoulder;<BR>इदमुपहितसूक्ष्मग्रंथिना स्कंधदेशे Ś. 1. 19.<BR>{2} that part of the elephant's<BR>body, where the driver sits.<BR>--परिनिर्वाणं the annihilation of the<BR>elements of being (with Buddhists)<BR>--फलः {1} the cocoa-nut tree. {2}<BR>the Bilva tree. {3} the glomercus<BR>fig-tree.<BR>--बंधना a sort of fennel.<BR>--मल्लकः a heron.<BR>--रुहः the<BR>(Indian) fig-tree.<BR>--वाहः, --वाहकः an ox<BR>trained to carry burdens,<BR>packbullock.<BR>--शाखा a principal branch,<BR>the forked branch issuing from the<BR>upper stem of a tree.<BR>--शृंगः a<BR>buffalo.<BR>--स्कंधः every shoulder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1142-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंधस्|स्कन्धस्
स्कंधस् n.<BR>1 The shoulder.<BR>--2 The<BR>trunk of a tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंधिकः|स्कन्धिक|स्कंधिक|स्कन्धिकः
स्कंधिकः An ox trained to<BR>carry burdens; cf. स्कंधवाह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंधिन्|स्कन्धिन्
स्कंधिन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Having<BR>shoulders.<BR>--2 Having branches or<BR>a branched stem. --m. A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंभ्|स्कम्भ्
स्कंभ् {c1c} A., {c5c} {c9c} P. (स्कंभते,<BR>स्कभ्नोति, स्कभ्नाति)<BR>1 To create.<BR>--2 To<BR>stop, hinder, impede, obstruct,<BR>curb, restrain. --Caus. (स्कंभयति-ते<BR>or स्कंभयति-ते) To stop &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कब्ध
स्कब्ध p. p.<BR>1 Supported,<BR>propped.<BR>--2 Stopped.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंभः|स्कम्भ|स्कंभ|स्कम्भः
स्कंभः<BR>1 Support, prop, stay.<BR>--2<BR>Fulcrum.<BR>--3 The Supreme Being.<BR>--4 N. of a Vedic deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कंभनं|स्कम्भन|स्कंभन
स्कंभनं<BR>1 The act of supporting.<BR>--2<BR>A support, prop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कांद|स्कान्द|स्कान्दं
स्कांद a. (दी f.) [स्कंद-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Relating to Skanda.<BR>--2 Relating to Śiva.<BR>--दं The Skanda Purāṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कु
स्कु {c5c} {c9c} U. (स्कुनोति, स्कुनुते,<BR>स्कुनाति, स्कुनीते)<BR>1 To go by leaps,<BR>jump, bound.<BR>--2 To raise, lift.<BR>--3<BR>To cover, overspread; Bk. 17. 82.<BR>--4 To approach. --WITH प्रति to<BR>cover; Bk. 18. 73.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुंद्|स्कुन्द्
स्कुंद् {c1c} A. (स्कुंदते)<BR>1 To jump.<BR>--2 To raise, lift.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्कुंभ्|स्कुम्भ्
स्कुंभ् {c5c} {c9c} P. (स्कुभ्ना-भ्नो-ति) To<BR>stop, hinder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खद्
स्खद् {c1c} A. (स्खदते)<BR>1 To cut, cut<BR>or tear to pieces.<BR>--2 To destroy.<BR>--3<BR>To hurt, injure, kill.<BR>--4 To rout,<BR>defeat completely.<BR>--5 To fatigue,<BR>exhaust, trouble.<BR>--6 To make or<BR>be firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खदनं|स्खदन
स्खदनं<BR>1 Cutting, tearing to pieces.<BR>--2 Hurting, injuring, killing.<BR>--3<BR>Troubling, harassing.<BR>--4 Firmness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खल्
स्खल् {c1c} P. (स्खलति, स्खलित)<BR>1 To<BR>stumble, tumble, fall down, slip,<BR>trip; स्खलति चरणं भूमौ न्यस्तं न<BR>चार्द्रतमा मही Mk. 9. 13; Ku. 5. 24.<BR>--2<BR>To totter, waver, shake, fluctuate.<BR>--3 To be disobeyed or violated (as<BR>an order); देवस्य शासनं पौरेषु कथं<BR>स्खलिष्यति Mu. 3; 3. 24; R. 18. 43.<BR>--4<BR>To fall or deviate from the right<BR>course; Ki. 9. 37.<BR>--5 To be affected<BR>or excited; Ki. 3. 53, 13. 60.<BR>--6<BR>To err, blunder, commit mistakes;<BR>स्खलतो हि करालंबः सुहृत्सचिवचेष्टितं<BR>H. 3. 134 (where it has sense 1 also).<BR>--7 To stammer, lisp, falter;<BR>वदनकमलकं शिशोः स्मरामि<BR>स्खलदसमंजसमंजुजल्पितं ते U. 4. 4; R. 9. 76,<BR>Ku. 5. 56.<BR>--8 To fail, have no effect; राघवः<BR>स्खलितवीर्यमात्मनि R. 11. 83.<BR>--9 To<BR>drop, drip, trickle.<BR>--10 To go, move.<BR>--11 To disappear.<BR>--12 To collect,<BR>gather. --Caus. (स्खलयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>cause to stumble or trip.<BR>--2 To cause<BR>to err or blunder, cause to falter or<BR>stammer; वचनानि स्खलयन् पदे पदे<BR>Ku. 4. 12; स्खलयति वचनं ते संश्रयत्यंगमंगं<BR>Māl. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलनं|स्खलन
स्खलनं [स्खल्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Stumbling, slipping, tripping, falling down.<BR>--2 Tottering.<BR>--3 Deviating from the<BR>right course.<BR>--4 Blundering, error,<BR>mistake.<BR>--5 Failure,<BR>disappointment, unsuccessfulness.<BR>--6<BR>Stammering, blundering in speech or<BR>pronunciation, faltering.<BR>--7<BR>Trickling, dripping.<BR>--8 Dashing against,<BR>clashing, collision; U. 2. 20,<BR>Mv. 5. 40<BR>--9 Mutual striking or<BR>rubbing together.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खलित|स्खलितं
स्खलित p. p. [स्खल्-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Stumbled, slipped, tripped.<BR>--2 Fallen,<BR>dropped down.<BR>--3 Shaking, wavering,<BR>fluctuating, unsteady.<BR>--4<BR>Intoxicated, drunk.<BR>--5 Stammering,<BR>faltering; Ku. 5. 56.<BR>--6 Agitated,<BR>disturbed.<BR>--7 Erring, blundering.<BR>--8<BR>Dropped, emitted.<BR>--9 Dripping,<BR>trickling down.<BR>--10 Interrupted,<BR>stopped.<BR>--11 Confounded.<BR>--12<BR>Gone.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Stumbling, tripping,<BR>a fall.<BR>--2 Deviation from the right<BR>course.<BR>--3 Error, blunder, mistake;<BR>गोत्रस्खलित Ku. 4. 8.<BR>--4 Fault, sin,<BR>transgression.<BR>--5 Deceit, treachery.<BR>--6 Circumvention, stratagem.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--सुभगं ind. dashing or flowing<BR>along in a charming manner<BR>Me. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्खुड्
स्खुड् {c6c} P. (स्खुडति) To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तक्
स्तक् {c1c} P. (स्तकति)<BR>1 To resist.<BR>--2 To strike against, repel, push<BR>back.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्
स्तन् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (स्तनति,<BR>स्तनयति-ते, स्तनित)<BR>1 To sound, make a sound,<BR>resound, reverberate.<BR>--2 To groan,<BR>breathe hard, sigh.<BR>--3 To thunder,<BR>roar loudly;<BR>तस्तनुर्जज्वलुर्मग्लुर्जग्लुर्लुलुठिरे क्षताः Bk. 14. 30. --WITH. नि {1} to<BR>sound. {2} to sigh. {3} to mourn.<BR>--वि to roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनः|स्तन
स्तनः [स्तन्-अच्]<BR>1 The female breast;<BR>स्तनौ मांसग्रंथी कनककलशावित्युपोमतौ<BR>Bh. 3. 20; (दरिद्राणां मनोरथाः)<BR>हदयेष्वेव लीयंते विधवास्त्रीस्तनाविव<BR>Pt. 2. 91.<BR>--2 The nipple of the breast.<BR>--3 The breast, udder, or dug of any<BR>female animal; अर्धपीतस्तनं मातुरामर्दक्लि<BR>ष्टकेशरं Ś. 7. 14.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशुकं a<BR>cloth covering the breasts or bosom,<BR>breast mantle^1.<BR>--अग्रः a nipple.<BR>--अंगरागः<BR>a paint or pigment smeared on the<BR>breasts of women.<BR>--अंतरं {1} the heart.<BR>{2} the space between the breasts;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">Page1144-a+ 56</a>]<BR>(न) मृणालसूत्रं रचितं रतनांतरे Ś. 6. 17,<BR>R. 10. 62. {3} a mark on the breast<BR>(said to indicate future widowhood).<BR>--आभोगः {1} fulness or expanding<BR>of the breasts. {2} the<BR>circumference or orb of the breast. {3} a<BR>man with large breasts like those of<BR>a woman.<BR>--तटः, --ष्टं the slope of the<BR>breast; cf. तट.<BR>--प, --पा, --पायक,<BR>--पायिन् a. sucking the breast, a<BR>suckling.<BR>--पानं sucking of the breast.<BR>--भरः {1} the weight or heaviness<BR>of breasts; पादाग्रस्थितया मुहुः<BR>स्तनभरेणानीतया नम्रतां Ratn. 1. 1. {2} a<BR>man having breasts like those of<BR>a woman.<BR>--भवः a particular<BR>position in sexual union.<BR>--मुखं, --वृंतं<BR>--शिखा a nipple.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1143-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनथः|स्तनथ
स्तनथः Ved. Thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तननं|स्तनन
स्तननं [स्तन्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Sounding, a<BR>sound, noise.<BR>--2 Roaring,<BR>thundering, rumbling (of clouds).<BR>--3<BR>Groaning.<BR>--4 Breathing hard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनंधय|स्तनन्धय|स्तनंधयः|स्तनन्धयः
स्तनंधय a. [स्तनं धयति धे-खश् मुम् च]<BR>Sucking the breast; यदि बुध्यते<BR>हरिशिशुः स्तनंधयो भविता करेणुपरिशेषिता<BR>मही Bv. 1. 53; तवांकशायी<BR>परिवृत्तभाग्यया मया न ट्टष्टस्तनयः स्तनंधयः<BR>Māl. 10. 6.<BR>--यः An infant, a suckling;<BR>R. 14. 78, Śi. 12. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनयित्नुः|स्तनयित्नु
स्तनयित्नुः [स्तन्-इत्नु]<BR>1<BR>Thundering, thunder, the muttering of<BR>clouds.<BR>--2 A cloud; U. 3. 7, 5, 8.<BR>--3 Lightning.<BR>--4 Sickness.<BR>--5<BR>Death.<BR>--6 A kind of grass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तनित|स्तनितं
स्तनित p. p. [स्तन् कर्तरि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Sounded, sounding, noisy; Me. 28.<BR>--2 Thundering, roaring.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The<BR>rattling of thunder, rumbling of<BR>thunder-clouds;<BR>तोयोत्सर्गस्तनितमुखरो मास्म भूर्विक्लवास्ताः Me. 37.<BR>--2<BR>Thunder, noise.<BR>--3 The noise of<BR>clapping the hands.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--फलः<BR>the Vikaṅkata tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तन्यं|स्तन्य
स्तन्यं [स्तने भवं यत्] Mother's<BR>milk, milk; पिब स्तन्यं पोत Bv. 1. 60.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--त्यागः leaving off the<BR>mother's milk, weaning;<BR>स्तन्यत्यागात्प्रभृति सुमुखी दंतपांचालिकेव<BR>Māl. 10. 5; स्तन्यत्यागं यावत् पुत्रयोरवेक्षस्व U. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तबकः|स्तबक
स्तबकः A bunch, cluster;<BR>कुसुमस्तबकस्येव द्वे गती स्तो मनस्विनां<BR>Bh. 2. 104, R. 13. 32; Me. 75, Ku. 3. 39.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभ्
स्तभ् See स्तंभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्ध|स्तब्धः
स्तब्ध p. p. [स्तंभ् कर्मणि कर्तरि वा<BR>क्त]<BR>1 Stopped, blocked up,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">Page1144-b+ 56</a>]<BR>obstructed.<BR>--2 Paralysed, senseless,<BR>stupefied, benumbed.<BR>--3 Motionless,<BR>immovable.<BR>--4 Fixed, firm, hard,<BR>rigid, stiff.<BR>--5 Obstinate, stubborn,<BR>hard-hearted, stern.<BR>--6 Coarse.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर्ण a. pricking up the<BR>ears.<BR>--रोमन् m. a hog, boar.<BR>--लोचन a. having motionless or<BR>unwinking eyes (said of gods).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धता
स्तब्धता --त्वं<BR>1 Rigidity, firmness,<BR>hardness.<BR>--2 Stupor, insensibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धत्वं|स्तब्धत्व
स्तब्धता --त्वं<BR>1 Rigidity, firmness,<BR>hardness.<BR>--2 Stupor, insensibility.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तब्धिः|स्तब्धि
स्तब्धिः f.<BR>1 Fixedness, hardness,<BR>stiffness, rigidity.<BR>--2 Firmness,<BR>immovableness.<BR>--3 Stupor,<BR>insensibility, numbness.<BR>--4 Obstinacy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभः|स्तभ
स्तभः A goat, ram.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तभु
स्तभु n. = स्तंभन q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तम्
स्तम् {c1c} P. (स्तमात) To be<BR>confused or agitated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंबः|स्तम्ब|स्तंब|स्तम्बः
स्तंबः [स्था-अबच् किच्च पृषो˚<BR>Uṇ. 4. 96]<BR>1 A clump of grass &c.;<BR>R. 5. 15.<BR>--2 A sheaf of corn; as<BR>in स्तंबकरिता q. v.<BR>--3 A cluster,<BR>clump or bunch (in general);<BR>U. 2. 29, R. 15. 19.<BR>--4 A bush, thicket.<BR>--5 A shrub or plant having no<BR>decided stem.<BR>--6 The post to which an<BR>elephant is tied.<BR>--7 A post.<BR>--8<BR>Stupefaction, insensibility;<BR>(probably for स्तंभ in these two senses).<BR>--9 A mountain.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करि a.<BR>forming sheaves or clusters.<BR>--(रिः)<BR>corn, rice.<BR>--करिता forming sheaves<BR>or clusters, abundant or luxuriant<BR>growth; न शालेः स्तंबकरिता<BR>बप्तुर्गुणमपेक्षते Mu. 1. 3.<BR>--घनः {1} a small<BR>hoe for weeding clumps of grass.<BR>{2} a sickle for cutting corn. {3} a<BR>basket for holding the heads of<BR>wild rice.<BR>--घ्नः, --घातः --हन्, --हननं --नी<BR>a sickle for cutting corn, a<BR>hoe.<BR>--पुरं N. of a city (ताम्रलिप्त).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंबेरमः|स्तम्बेरम|स्तंबेरम|स्तम्बेरमः
स्तंबेरमः An elephant; स्तंबेरमा<BR>मुखरशृंखलकर्षिणस्ते R. 5. 72;<BR>Śi. 5. 34; Māl. 9. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभ्|स्तम्भ्
स्तंभ् {c1c} A., {c5c} {c9c} P. (स्तंभते,<BR>स्तभ्नोति, स्तभ्नाति, स्तांभित or स्तब्धः; the स् of<BR>the root being changed to ष् after<BR>prepositions ending in इ or उ and<BR>also after अव)<BR>1 To stop, hinder,<BR>arrest, suppress; कंठः<BR>स्तंभितबाष्पवृत्तिकलुषः Ś. 4. 5.<BR>--2 To make firm<BR>or stiff, to make immovable.<BR>--3<BR>To stupefy, paralyze, benumb;<BR>प्राणा दध्वंसिरे गात्रं तस्तंभे च हते प्रिये<BR>Bk. 14. 55.<BR>--4 To prop, support,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-c" target="_blank">Page1144-c+ 58</a>]<BR>uphold, sustain.<BR>--5 To become stiff,<BR>rigid or immovable.<BR>--6 To be<BR>proud or elated, be stiff-necked.<BR>(The following verse illustrates the<BR>root in its different conjugations:<BR>--स्तंभते पुरुषः प्रायो यौवनेन धनने च । न<BR>स्तभ्नाति क्षितीशोऽपि न स्तभ्नोति युवाप्यसौ ॥).<BR>--Caus. (स्तंभयति-ते).<BR>1 To stop,<BR>arrest.<BR>--2 To make firm or rigid.<BR>--3 To paralyze.<BR>--4 To prop, support.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभः|स्तम्भ|स्तंभ|स्तम्भः
स्तंभः [स्तंभ्-अच्]<BR>1 Fixedness,<BR>stiffness, rigidity, motionlessness;<BR>रंभा स्तंभं भजति Vikr. 18. 29;<BR>Ki. 12. 28; गात्रस्तंभः स्तनमुकुलयोरुत्प्रबंधः<BR>प्रकंपः Māl. 2. 5;<BR>तत्संकल्पोपहितजाडिम स्तंभमभ्योति गात्रं 1. 35, 4. 2.<BR>--2<BR>Insensibility, stupefaction, stupor,<BR>numbness, paralysis.<BR>--3 Stoppage,<BR>obstruction, hindrance; सोऽ<BR>पश्यत्प्रणिधानेन संततेः स्तंभकारणं R. 1. 74;<BR>वाक्स्तंभं नाटयति Māl. 8.<BR>--4 Restraint,<BR>curbing, suppressing; कृतश्चित्तस्तंभः<BR>प्रतिहतधियामजंलिरपि Bh. 3. 6.<BR>--5<BR>Prop, support, fulcrum.<BR>--6 A pillar,<BR>column, post.<BR>--7 A stem, trunk<BR>(of a tree).<BR>--8 Stupidity.<BR>--9<BR>Absence of feeling or excitability.<BR>--10 The suppression of any force<BR>or feeling by supernatural or<BR>magical means.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्कीर्ण a.<BR>carved out of a post of wood<BR>(as a statue).<BR>--कर a. {1} paralysing,<BR>benumbing. {2} obstructing.<BR>--(रः)<BR>a fence.<BR>--कारणं cause of<BR>obstruction or impediment.<BR>--पूजा worship<BR>of the posts of temporary pavilions<BR>erected for marriages or other<BR>occasions of solemnity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभकिन्|स्तम्भकिन्
स्तंभकिन् m. A kind of musical<BR>instrument covered with leather.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभनं|स्तम्भन|स्तंभन|स्तम्भनं|स्तम्भनः
स्तंभनं [स्तंभयति स्तंभ्-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Stopping, obstructing, hindering,<BR>arresting, suppressing, restraining;<BR>लोलोल्लोलक्षुभितकरणोज्जृंभणस्तंभनार्थं<BR>U. 3. 36.<BR>--2 Paralysing, benumbing,<BR>stupefying.<BR>--3 Quieting,<BR>composure; Pt. 1. 360.<BR>--4 Making firm<BR>or stiff, fixing firmly.<BR>--5 Propping,<BR>supporting,<BR>--6 Stopping the flow of<BR>blood.<BR>--7 Anything employed as an<BR>astringent.<BR>--8 A particular magical<BR>art or faculty; see स्तंभ (10).<BR>--नः N.<BR>of one of the five arrows of Cupid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभित|स्तम्भित|स्तम्भितः
स्तंभित a.<BR>1 Stopped, hindered.<BR>--2 Benumbed, paralyzed.<BR>--3<BR>Composed, collected; see स्तंभ्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभिन्|स्तम्भिन्
स्तंभिन् a. Supporting, stopping<BR>&c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1144-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तंभिनी
स्तंभिनी The Earth(one of the<BR>five elements).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तर|स्तरः
स्तर a. [स्तृ-स्तॄ-घञ्] Spreading,<BR>extending, covering.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>Anything spread, a layer, stratum.<BR>--2<BR>A bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरणं|स्तरण
स्तरणं [स्तृ स्तॄ-ल्युट्] The act of<BR>spreading, strewing, scattering &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरिमन्
स्तरि(री)मन् m. A bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरीमन्
स्तरि(री)मन् m. A bed, couch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तरी
स्तरी [स्तृ कर्मणि इ]<BR>1 Smoke,<BR>vapour.<BR>--2 A heifer.<BR>--3 A barren<BR>cow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवः|स्तव
स्तवः [स्तु-अप्]<BR>1 Praising,<BR>celebrating, eulogizing.<BR>--2 Praise,<BR>eulogium, panegyric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवक|स्तवकः
स्तवक a. (विका f.) [स्तु-वुन्]<BR>Praising, eulogizing.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>panegyrist, praiser.<BR>--2 Praise,<BR>eulogium.<BR>--3 A cluster of blossoms.<BR>--4<BR>Bunch of flowers, nosegay, tuft,<BR>bouquet^1.<BR>--5 A chapter or section<BR>of a book.<BR>--6 A multitude; cf.<BR>स्तवक also.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवकित
स्तवकित a. Full of blossoms or<BR>bunches.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तवनं|स्तवन
स्तवनं [स्तु-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Praising,<BR>praise.<BR>--2 A hymn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तावः|स्ताव
स्तावः Praise, eulogy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तावकः|स्तावक
स्तावकः A praiser, panegyrist,<BR>flatterer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिघ्
स्तिघ् {c5c} A. (स्तिघ्नुते)<BR>1 To ascend.<BR>--2 To assail, attack.<BR>--3 To ooze.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिप्
स्तिप् {c1c} A. (स्तेपते) To ooze, drop,<BR>drip.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिभिः|स्तिभि
स्तिभिः^1<BR>1 An obstacle, obstruction<BR>--2 The ocean.<BR>--3 A cluster, bunch.<BR>clump.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,. note: Confirm by alph. order.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिम्
स्तिम्, स्तीम् {c4c} P. (स्तिम्यति,<BR>स्तीम्यति)<BR>1 To become wet or<BR>moist.<BR>--2 To become fixed or<BR>immovable, be rigid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीम्
स्तिम्, स्तीम् {c4c} P. (स्तिम्यति,<BR>स्तीम्यति)<BR>1 To become wet or<BR>moist.<BR>--2 To become fixed or<BR>immovable, be rigid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमित|स्तिमितः
स्तिमित a. [स्तिम्-कर्तरि क्त]<BR>1 Wet,<BR>moist.<BR>--2 (a) Still, unruffled, calm;<BR>क्षुभितमुत्कलिकातरलं मनः पय इव<BR>स्तिमितस्य महोदधेः Māl. 3. 10. (b) Fixed,<BR>rigid, unmoved, motionless, steady;<BR>वाचस्पतिः सन्नपि सोऽष्टमूर्तौ<BR>त्वाशास्यचिंतास्तिमितो बभूव Ku. 7. 87; 2. 59;<BR>स्तिमितविकसितानां Māl. 1. 27;<BR>R. 2. 22, 3. 17, 13. 48, 79; U. 6. 25.<BR>--3<BR>Closed, shut; R. 1. 73.<BR>--4<BR>Benumbed, paralysed.<BR>--5 Soft, tender.<BR>--6<BR>Gratified, satisfied.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Moisture<BR>--2 Fixity, steadiness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वायुः still air.<BR>--समाधिः steady<BR>contemplation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तिमितत्वं|स्तिमितत्व
स्तिमितत्वं Steadiness, stillness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तीर्विः|स्तीर्वि|स्तीर्व्वि|स्तीर्व्विः
स्तीर्विः [स्तॄ क्विन्]<BR>1 An officiating<BR>priest at a sacrifice.<BR>--2 Grass.<BR>--3<BR>Sky, atmosphere.<BR>--4 Water.<BR>--5<BR>Blood.<BR>--6 An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तु
स्तु {c2c} U. (स्तौति-स्तवीति, स्तुते-स्तुवीते;<BR>तुष्टाव-तुष्टुवे, अस्तावीत्-अस्तोष्ट, स्तोष्यति-ते,<BR>स्तोतुं, स्तुत; desid. तुष्टूषति-ते; the स् of<BR>स्तु is changed to ष् after a<BR>preposition ending in इ or उ)<BR>1 To praise,<BR>laud, eulogize, extol, glorify,<BR>celebrate; Bv. 1. 41; Mu. 3. 16;<BR>Bk. 8. 92, 15. 70, 3.<BR>--2 To celebrate or<BR>praise in song, to hymn, worship by<BR>hymns.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत|स्तुतः
स्तुत p. p. [स्तु-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Praised, lauded, eulogized.<BR>--2 Flattered.<BR>--तः<BR>1 Praising.<BR>--2 N. of Śiva<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुति|स्तुतिः
स्तुति f. [स्तु-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Praise,<BR>eulogy, commendation, laudation,<BR>स्तुतिभ्यो व्यतिरिच्यंते दूराणि चरितानि ते<BR>R. 10. 30.<BR>--2 A hymn of praise,<BR>panegyric; R. 4. 6.<BR>--3 Adulation;<BR>flattery, empty or false praise;<BR>भूतार्थव्याहृतिः सा हि न स्तुतिः परमोष्ठिनः<BR>R. 10. 33.<BR>--4 N. of Durgā.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गीतं a panegyric, hymn.<BR>--पदं an<BR>object of praise.<BR>--पाठकः a panegyrist,<BR>an encomiast, a minstrel, bard,<BR>herald.<BR>--वादः a laudatory speech,<BR>panegyric.<BR>--व्रतः a bard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुत्य|स्तुत्यः
स्तुत्य a. Laudable, commendable,<BR>praiseworthy; R. 4. 6.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुकः|स्तुक
स्तुकः A collection of hair, a<BR>knot or braid of hair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुका
स्तुका<BR>1 A knot or braid of hair.<BR>--2 A bunch of curly hair between<BR>the horns of a bull.<BR>--3 Hip;<BR>thigh.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुच्
स्तुच् {c1c} A. (स्तोचते)<BR>1 To be<BR>bright, to shine, be pellucid.<BR>--2 To<BR>be propitious or pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुनकः|स्तुनक
स्तुनकः A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभ्
स्तुभ् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (स्तोभति)<BR>1 To praise.<BR>--2 To celebrate, extol, worship.<BR>{vII.v} {c1c} A. (स्तोभते)<BR>1 To stop,<BR>suppress.<BR>--2 To paralyse, benumb,<BR>stupefy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुभः|स्तुभ
स्तुभः A goat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तुंभ्|स्तुम्भ्
स्तुंभ् {c5c} {c9c} P. (स्तुभ्नोति; स्तुभ्नाति)<BR>1 To stop.<BR>--2 To benumb, stupefy.<BR>--3 To expel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूप्
स्तूप् {c4c} P., {c10c} U. (स्तूप्यति,<BR>स्तूपयति-ते)<BR>1 To heap up, accumulate,<BR>pile, collect.<BR>--2 To erect, raise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तूपः|स्तूप
स्तूपः<BR>1 A heap, pile, mound (of<BR>earth &c.); Mu. 3. 15.<BR>--2 A<BR>Buddhistic monument, or kind of Tope<BR>erected for keeping sacred relics, as<BR>those of Buddha.<BR>--3 A funeral pile.<BR>--4 Strength, power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
स्तृ {vI.v} {c5c} U. (स्तृणोति, स्तृणुते, स्तृत;<BR>pass. स्तर्यते)<BR>1 To spread, strew,<BR>cover, spread on or over; (महीं)<BR>तस्तार सरघाव्याप्तैः स क्षौद्रपटलैरिव<BR>R. 4. 63, 7. 58.<BR>--2 To spread, expand,<BR>diffuse.<BR>--3 To scatter, spread about.<BR>--4 To clothe, cover, overspread,<BR>envelop.<BR>--5 To kill. --Caus.<BR>(स्तारयति-ते) To overspread, cover,<BR>strew; रक्तेनाचिक्लिदद्भूमिं<BR>सैन्यैश्चातस्तरद्धतैः Bk. 15. 48. --Desid. (<BR>तिस्तीर्षति-ते). {vII.v} {c5c} P. (स्तृणीते) To please,<BR>gratify.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृ
स्तृ m. A star.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृतिः|स्तृति
स्तृतिः f.<BR>1 Spreading, stretching,<BR>expansion.<BR>--2 Covering, clothing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृक्ष्
स्तृक्ष् {c1c} P. (स्तृक्षति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तृह्
स्तृह्, स्तॄह् {c6c} P. (स्तृहति, स्तॄहति)<BR>To strike, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄह्
स्तृह्, स्तॄह् {c6c} P. (स्तृहति, स्तॄहति)<BR>To strike, hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तॄ
स्तॄ {c9c} U. (स्तृणाति, सृणीते, स्तीर्ण;<BR>desid. तिस्तरि री-षति-ते, तिस्तीर्षति-ते)<BR>To cover, strew &c.; see स्तृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेन्
स्तेन् {c10c} U. (Strictly a denom.<BR>from स्तेन; स्तेनयति-ते) To steal, rob;<BR>Ms. 8. 333.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेनः|स्तेन|स्तेनं
स्तेनः [स्तेन्-कर्तरि अच्] A thief,<BR>robber; न तं स्तेना न चामित्रा हरंति न च<BR>नश्यति Ms. 7. 83.<BR>--नं Thieving,<BR>stealing.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--निग्रहः {1} the<BR>punishment of thieves. {2}<BR>suppression of theft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेयं|स्तेय
स्तेयं [स्तेनस्य भावः यत् नलोपः]<BR>1<BR>Theft, robbery; Ku. 2. 35.<BR>--2<BR>Anything stolen or liable to be stolen.<BR>--3 Anything private or secret.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेयिन्
स्तेयिन् m.<BR>1 A thief, robber.<BR>--2 A<BR>goldsmith.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैनं|स्तैन
स्तैनं Theft, robbery.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैन्यं|स्तैन्य|स्तैन्यः
स्तैन्यं [स्तेनस्य भावः ष्यञ्] Theft,<BR>robbery.<BR>--न्यः A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेप्
स्तेप् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (स्तेपते) To ooze.<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} U. (स्तेपयति-ते) To send,<BR>throw, cast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तेमः|स्तेम
स्तेमः Moisture, wetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तै
स्तै {c1c} P. (स्नायति) To put on,<BR>adorn.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तैमित्यं|स्तैमित्य
स्तैमित्यं<BR>1 Fixedness, rigidity,<BR>immobility.<BR>--2 Numbness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोक|स्तोकः
स्तोक a. [स्तुच्-घञ्]<BR>1 Little,<BR>small; स्तोकेनोन्नतिमायाति<BR>स्तोकेनायात्यधागेतिं Pt. 1. 150; स्तोकं महद्वा धनं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">Page1146-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Bh. 2. 49.<BR>--2 Short.<BR>--3 Few.<BR>--4<BR>Low, abject.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A small<BR>quantity, drop.<BR>--2 The Cātaka bird.<BR>--कं ind. A little, less;<BR>पश्योदग्रप्लुतत्वाद्वियति बहुतरं स्तोकमुर्व्यां प्रयाति<BR>Ś. 1. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--काय a.<BR>little-bodied, small, dwarfish, diminutive.<BR>--नम्र a. a little bent down, slightly<BR>stooping or depressed;<BR>श्रोणीभारादलसगमना स्तोकनम्रा स्तनाभ्यां Me. 82.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1145-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोककः|स्तोकक
स्तोककः The Cātaka bird;<BR>Ms. 12. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोकशस्
स्तोकशस् ind. By little, sparingly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतव्य
स्तोतव्य a. Fit to be praised,<BR>laudable, praiseworthy;<BR>स्तोतव्यगुणसंपन्नः केषां न स्यात्प्रियो जनः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोतृ
स्तोतृ m. A praiser, panegyrist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्रं|स्तोत्र
स्तोत्रं [स्तु-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>1 Praise, eulogium.<BR>--2 A hymn of praise, panegyric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्रियः|स्तोत्रिय
स्तोत्रियः --या A particular kind of<BR>verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोत्रिया
स्तोत्रियः --या A particular kind of<BR>verse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोभः|स्तोभ|स्तोभं
स्तोभः [स्तुभ्-घञ्]<BR>1 Stopping,<BR>obstructing.<BR>--2 A stop, pause.<BR>--3<BR>Disrespect, contumely.<BR>--4 A hymn,<BR>praise.<BR>--5 A division of the<BR>Sāmaveda.<BR>--6 Anything inserted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोमः|स्तोम
स्तोमः [स्तु-मन् Uṇ. 1. 137]<BR>1<BR>Praise, eulogium, hymn.<BR>--2 A<BR>sacrifice, oblation; as in ज्योतिष्टोम,<BR>अग्निष्टोम.<BR>--3 A Soma libation.<BR>--4 A<BR>collection, multitude, number, group,<BR>assemblage; U. 1. 51.<BR>--5 A large<BR>quantity, mass; भस्मस्तोमपवित्रलांछनमुरो<BR>धत्ते त्वचं रौरवीं U. 4. 20, Mv. 1. 18.<BR>--मं<BR>1 The head.<BR>--2 Riches, wealth.<BR>--3 Grain, corn.<BR>--4 An iron-pointed<BR>stick or shaft.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोमयति
स्तोमयति Den. P. To praise, laud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तोम्य
स्तोम्य a. Laudable, praiseworthy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्तौभिकं|स्तौभिक
स्तौभिकं N. of the second<BR>portion of the Saṃhitā of the Sāmaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्येनः|स्त्येन
स्त्येनः [स्त्यै-इनच्]<BR>1 Nectar.<BR>--2<BR>A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यै
स्त्यै {c1c} U. (स्त्यायति-ते)<BR>1 To be<BR>collected into a heap or mass.<BR>--2 To<BR>spread about, be diffused;<BR>शिशिरकदुकषायः स्त्यायते सल्लकीनां Māl. 9. 6,<BR>2. 21; Mv. 5. 41.<BR>--3 Sound, echo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यान|स्त्यानं|स्त्यानः
स्त्यान a. [स्त्यै-क्त]<BR>1 Collected<BR>into a mass; Māl. 5. 11, Ve. 1. 21.<BR>--2<BR>Thick, bulky, gross.<BR>--3 Soft, bland,<BR>smooth, unctuous.<BR>--4 Sounding.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Thickness, grossness, increase<BR>in magnitude or bulk; दधति<BR>कुहरभाजामत्र भल्लूकयूनामनुरसितगुरूणि स्त्यानमंबू<BR>कृतानि Māl. 9. 6; U. 2. 21,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-b" target="_blank">Page1146-b+ 57</a>]<BR>Mv. 5. 41.<BR>--2 Unctuousness.<BR>--3 Nectar.<BR>--4 Sloth, idleness.<BR>--5 Echo, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्यायनं|स्त्यायन
स्त्यायनं Collecting into a mass,<BR>crowding together, aggregation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्री
स्त्री<BR>1 A woman.<BR>--2 A female of<BR>any animal; गजस्त्री, हरिणस्त्री &c.;<BR>Ś. 5. 22.<BR>--3 A wife; स्त्रीणां भर्ता<BR>धर्मदाराश्च पुंसां Māl. 6. 18; Me. 28.<BR>--4<BR>The feminine gender, or a word used<BR>in that gender; आपः स्त्रीभूम्नि<BR>Ak.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अगारः --रं a harem,<BR>the women's apartments.<BR>--अव्यक्षः<BR>a chamberlain.<BR>--अभिगमनं sexual<BR>intercourse.<BR>--आजीवः {1} one who<BR>lives by his wife. {2} one who<BR>lives by keeping women for<BR>prostitution.<BR>--कामः {1} desire of intercourse<BR>with women, fondness for women.<BR>{2} desire of a wife.<BR>--कार्यं {1} the<BR>business of women. {2} attendance<BR>on women or women's apartments.<BR>--कुमारं a woman and child.<BR>--कुसुमं menses, the menstrual excretion<BR>in women.<BR>--क्षीरं mother's milk;<BR>Ms. 5. 9.<BR>--ग a. cohabiting with<BR>women.<BR>--गवी a milch-cow.<BR>--गुरुः<BR>a female Guru or priestess.<BR>--गृहं = स्त्र्यगार q. v.<BR>--घोषः dawn,<BR>daybreak.<BR>--घ्नः the murderer of a<BR>woman.<BR>--चरितं-त्रं the doings of<BR>women.<BR>--चिह्नं {1} any mark or<BR>characteristic of the female sex. {2}<BR>the female organ, vulva.<BR>--चौरः a<BR>seducer of women, libertine.<BR>--जननी a woman who brings forth only<BR>daughters.<BR>--जातिः f. womankind,<BR>female sex.<BR>--जितः a hen-pecked<BR>husband; स्त्रीजितस्पर्शमात्रेण सर्वं पुण्यं<BR>विनश्यति Śabdak; Ms. 4. 217.<BR>--धनं<BR>a woman's private property over<BR>which she exercises independent<BR>control; it is of six kinds:<BR>--अध्यग्न्यध्यावहनिकं दत्तं च प्रीतिकर्मणि ।<BR>भ्रातृमातृपितृप्राप्तं षड्विधं स्त्रीधनं स्मृतम् ॥; or<BR>according to others:<BR>--पितृमातृपतिभ्रातृदत्तमध्यग्न्युपायनम् । आधिपेदनिकाद्यं च<BR>स्त्रीधनं परिकीर्तितम्; see also अन्वाधेयं,<BR>बंधुदत्तं, यौतकं, सौदायिकं, शुल्कं, पारिणाय्यं,<BR>लावण्यार्जितं, and पादवंदनिकं.<BR>--धर्मः {1} the<BR>duty of a woman or wife. {2} the<BR>laws concerning women. {3}<BR>menstruation.<BR>--धर्मिणी a woman in her<BR>courses.<BR>--धवः a man.<BR>--ध्वजः the<BR>female of any animal.<BR>--नाथ a. one<BR>protected by a woman.<BR>--निबंधनं a<BR>woman's peculiar sphere of action<BR>or province; domestic duty, house<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-c" target="_blank">Page1146-c+ 57</a>]<BR>wifery.<BR>--पण्योपजीविन् m. see<BR>स्त्र्याजीव above.<BR>--परः a woman-lover,<BR>lecher, libertine.<BR>--पिशाची a<BR>fiendlike wife.<BR>--पुंसौ m. du. {1} wife and<BR>husband. {2} male and female;<BR>Ku. 2. 7.<BR>--पुंसलक्षणा a hermaphrodite.<BR>--पुंधर्मः the law regulating the<BR>duties of man and wife.<BR>--प्रत्ययः a<BR>feminine affix (in gram.).<BR>--प्रसंगः<BR>(excessive) intercourse with women.<BR>--प्रसूः f. a woman who brings forth<BR>only daughters; Y. 1. 73.<BR>--प्रिय a.<BR>loved by women.<BR>--(यः) the mango<BR>tree.<BR>--बाध्यः one who suffers<BR>himself to be troubled by a<BR>woman.<BR>--बुद्धिः f. {1} the female<BR>understanding. {2} the counsel of a<BR>woman, female advice.<BR>--भोगः<BR>sexual intercourse.<BR>--मंत्रः a female<BR>stratagem, woman's counsel.<BR>--मुखपः the<BR>Aśoka tree.<BR>--यंत्रं a machine-like<BR>woman, machine in the form of a<BR>woman; स्त्रीयंत्रं केन लोके विषममृतमयं<BR>धर्मनाशाय सृष्टं Pt. 1. 191.<BR>--रंजनं betel.<BR>--रत्नं {1} an excellent woman;<BR>स्त्रीरत्नेषु ममोर्वशी प्रियतमा यूथे तवेयं वशा<BR>V. 4. 25. {2} N. of Lakṣmī.<BR>--राज्यं the kingdom of women.<BR>--लिंगं {1} the feminine gender (in<BR>gram.) {2} any mark of the female<BR>sex (as breast &c.). {3} the female<BR>organ.<BR>--वशः submissiveness to a<BR>wife, subjection to women.<BR>--विधेय a. governed by a wife,<BR>uxorious; R. 19. 4.<BR>--विवाहः<BR>contracting marriage with a woman.<BR>--संसर्गः female company.<BR>--संस्थान a.<BR>having a female shape; Ś. 5. 30<BR>--संगः<BR>attachment to women, or<BR>intercourse with women.<BR>--संग्रहणं {1} the<BR>act of embracing a woman<BR>(improperly). {2} adultery, seduction.<BR>--सभं an assembly of women.<BR>--संबंधः<BR>{1} matrimonial alliance with a<BR>woman. {2} connection by marriage.<BR>{3} relation to women.<BR>--स्वभावः {1}<BR>the nature of women. {2} a eunuch.<BR>--हत्या the murder of a woman.<BR>--हरणं {1} the forcible abduction of<BR>women. {2} rape.<BR>--हारिन् m. a<BR>ravisher or seducer (of women).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीतमा
स्त्रीतमा, स्त्रीतरा A thorough woman,<BR>more thoroughly a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीतरा
स्त्रीतमा, स्त्रीतरा A thorough woman,<BR>more thoroughly a woman.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीता
स्त्रीता --त्वं<BR>1 Womanhood.<BR>--2<BR>Wifehood.<BR>--3 Effeminacy,<BR>feminineness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रीत्वं|स्त्रीत्व
स्त्रीता --त्वं<BR>1 Womanhood.<BR>--2<BR>Wifehood.<BR>--3 Effeminacy,<BR>feminineness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैण|स्त्रैणं|स्त्रैणः
स्त्रैण a. (णी f.) [स्त्रिया इदम् नञ्<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">Page1147-a+ 56</a>]<BR>P. IV. 1. 88]<BR>1 Female, feminine.<BR>--2 Suited or belonging to women.<BR>--3 Being among women.<BR>--णं<BR>1<BR>Womanhood, nature of women,<BR>feminineness; शिशुत्वं स्त्रैणं वा भवतु ननु<BR>वंद्यासि जगतः U. 4. 11.<BR>--2 The<BR>female sex, womanhood; तृणे वा स्त्रैणे<BR>वा मम समट्टशो यांति दिवसाः<BR>Bh. 3. 113; इदं तत्प्रत्युत्पन्नमति स्त्रैणमिति<BR>यदुच्यते Ś. 5; तस्य तृणमिव लघुवृत्ति<BR>स्त्रैणमाकलयतः K.<BR>--3 A collection of<BR>women; U. 4. 26.<BR>--4 Ved. Sexual<BR>enjoyment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1146-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैणता
स्त्रैणता --त्वं<BR>1 Feminineness,<BR>effeminacy.<BR>--2 Excessive fondness<BR>for women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्त्रैणत्वं|स्त्रैणत्व
स्त्रैणता --त्वं<BR>1 Feminineness,<BR>effeminacy.<BR>--2 Excessive fondness<BR>for women.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थकरं|स्थकर
स्थकरं A betel-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग्
स्थग् {c1c} P. or Caus. (स्थगति,<BR>स्थगयति)<BR>1 To cover, conceal, hide,<BR>veil; पराभ्यूहस्थानान्यपि तनुतराणि<BR>स्थगयति Māl. 1. 14.<BR>--2 To cover,<BR>pervade, fill; रवः श्रवणभैरवः<BR>स्थगितरोदसीकंदरः K. P. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थग|स्थगः
स्थग a. [स्थग्-अच्]<BR>1 Fraudulent,<BR>dishonest.<BR>--2 Abandoned, impudent,<BR>reckless.<BR>--गः A rogue, cheat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगनं|स्थगन
स्थगनं Concealment, hiding.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगरं|स्थगर|स्थगरः
स्थगरं A betel-nut.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगिका
स्थगिका<BR>1 A courtezan.<BR>--2 The<BR>office of betel-bearer.<BR>--3 A kind of<BR>bandage.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगित|स्थगितं
स्थगित a. Covered, hidden,<BR>concealed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगी
स्थगी A betel-box.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थगुः|स्थगु
स्थगुः A hump.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थंडिलं|स्थण्डिल|स्थंडिल|स्थण्डिलं
स्थंडिलं [स्थल्-इलच् नुक् लस्य डः<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 A piece of ground (levelled,<BR>squared and prepared for a sacrifice),<BR>an altar; निषेदुषी स्थंडिल एव केवले<BR>Ku. 5. 12.<BR>--2 A barren field.<BR>--3 A<BR>heap of clods.<BR>--4 A limit, boundary.<BR>--5 A land-mark.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--शायिन्<BR>m., also स्थंडिलेशयः an ascetic who<BR>sleeps on the bare Sthandila or<BR>sacrificial ground.<BR>--सितकं an altar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपति|स्थपतिः
स्थपति a. [स्था-क तस्य पतिः]<BR>Chief, principal.<BR>--तिः<BR>1 A king,<BR>sovereign.<BR>--2 An architect.<BR>--3 A<BR>wheel-wright, master-carpenter.<BR>--4<BR>A charioteer.<BR>--5 One who offers a<BR>sacrifice to Bṛhaspati.<BR>--6 An<BR>attendant on the women's apartments.<BR>--7 N. of Kubera.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थपुट|स्थपुटः
स्थपुट a. [तिष्ठति स्था-क, स्थं पुटं यत्र]<BR>1 Being in contracted or difficult<BR>circumstances.<BR>--2 Unevenly raised,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-b" target="_blank">Page1147-b+ 57</a>]<BR>elevated and depressed.<BR>--3 The soul.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गत a. being in<BR>contracted or uneven parts, being in<BR>difficult places; अंकस्थादस्थिसंस्थ<BR>स्थपुटगतमपि क्रव्यमव्यग्रमत्ति Māl. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थल्
स्थल् {c1c} P. (स्थलति) To stand<BR>firm, be firm.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलं|स्थल
स्थलं [स्थल्-अच्]<BR>1 Firm or dry<BR>ground, dry land, terra firma (opp.<BR>जल); भो दुरात्मन् (समुद्र) दीयतां<BR>टिट्टिभांडानि नो चेत्स्थलतां त्वां नयामि<BR>Pt. 1; प्रतस्थे स्थलवर्त्मना R. 4. 60; so<BR>स्थलकमलिनी or स्थलवर्त्मन् q. v.<BR>--2<BR>Shore, strand, beach.<BR>--3 Ground,<BR>land, soil (in general).<BR>--4 Place,<BR>spot.<BR>--5 Field, tract, district.<BR>--6<BR>Station.<BR>--7 A piece of raised ground,<BR>mound.<BR>--8 A topic, case, subject,<BR>the point under discussion; विवाद˚,<BR>विचार˚ &c.<BR>--9 A part (as of a book).<BR>--10 A tent.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरं another<BR>place.<BR>--आरूढ a. alighted on the<BR>ground.<BR>--अरविंदं, --कमलं,<BR>--कमलिनी a land-growing lotus; Me. 90;<BR>Ku. 1. 33.<BR>--कुमुदः the Karavīra<BR>plant.<BR>--चर a. land-going, not<BR>aquatic.<BR>--च्युत a. fallen or removed<BR>from a place or position.<BR>--देवता a<BR>local or rural deity.<BR>--पद्मिनी the<BR>shrub Hibiscus Mutabilis.<BR>--मार्गः,<BR>--वर्त्मन् n. a road by land; स्थलवर्त्नना<BR>‘by land’; R. 4. 60.<BR>--विग्रहः a<BR>battle on level ground.<BR>--शुद्धिः f.<BR>purification or clearance of a place<BR>from impurity.<BR>--सीमन् f. a<BR>landmark, boundary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थला
स्थला A spot of dry ground<BR>artificially raised and drained (opp.<BR>स्थली q. v. below).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थली
स्थली<BR>1 Dry ground, firm land.<BR>--2 A natural spot of ground, ground<BR>or land (as of a forest); विललाप<BR>विकीर्णमूर्धजा समदुःखामिव कुर्वती स्थलीं<BR>Ku. 4. 4.<BR>--3 A deity of the soil;<BR>(= स्थलदेवता q. v.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--देवता<BR>a deity of the soil, a tutelary deity;<BR>Me. 106.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थलेशय|स्थलेशयः
स्थलेशय a. Sleeping on on dry<BR>ground.<BR>--यः Any amphibious<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविः|स्थवि
स्थविः<BR>1 A weaver.<BR>--2 Heaven.<BR>--3 A moveable thing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविर|स्थविरं|स्थविरः
स्थविर a. [स्था-किरच् स्थवादेशः]<BR>1 Fixed, firm, steady.<BR>--2 Old,<BR>aged, ancient.<BR>--रः<BR>1 An old man.<BR>--2 A beggar.<BR>--3 N. of Brahman.<BR>--रा An old woman; स्थबिरे का त्वं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-c" target="_blank">Page1147-c+ 57</a>]<BR>अयमर्भकः कस्य नयनानंदकरः Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थविष्ठ|स्थविष्ठः
स्थविष्ठ a. Greatest, very strong,<BR>largest (superl. of स्थूल q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थवीयस्
स्थवीयस् Greater, larger<BR>(compar. of स्थूल q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्था
स्था {c1c} P. (Atm. also in certain<BR>senses; तिष्ठति-ते, तस्थौ-तस्थे,<BR>अस्यात्-अस्थित, स्थास्यति-ते, स्थातुं, स्थित; pass.<BR>स्थीयते; the स् of this root is changed<BR>to ष् after a preposition ending in इ or<BR>उ)<BR>1 To stand; चलत्येकेन पादेन<BR>तिष्ठत्येकेन बुद्धिमान् Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 To stay,<BR>abide, dwell, live; ग्रामे or गृहे तिष्ठति.<BR>--3 To remain, be left; एको<BR>गंगदत्तस्तिष्ठति Pt. 4.<BR>--4 To delay, wait;<BR>किमिति स्थीयते Ś. 2.<BR>--5 To stop,<BR>cease, desist, stand still; तिष्ठत्येष<BR>क्षणमधिपतिर्ज्योतिषां व्योममध्ये V. 2. 1.<BR>--6 To be kept aside; तिष्ठतु तावत्<BR>पत्रलेखागमनवृत्तांतः K. ‘never mind<BR>the account of’ &c.<BR>--7 To be, exist,<BR>be in any state or position;<BR>often with participles; मेरौ स्थिते<BR>दोग्धरि दोहदक्षे Ku. 1. 2; व्याप्य स्थितं<BR>रोदसी V. 1. 1; या स्थिता व्याप्य विश्वं<BR>Ś. 1. 1; कालं नयमाना तिष्ठति Pt. 1;<BR>Ms. 7. 8.<BR>--8 To abide by, conform to,<BR>obey (with loc.); शासने तिष्ठ भर्तुः<BR>V. 5. 17, R. 11. 65.<BR>--9 To be<BR>restrained; यदि ते तु न तिष्ठेयुरुपायैः<BR>प्रथमैस्त्रिभिः Ms. 7. 108.<BR>--10 To be<BR>at hand, be obtainable; न विप्रं स्वेषु<BR>तिष्ठत्सु मृतं शूद्रेण नाययेत् Ms. 5. 104.<BR>--11 To live, breathe; आः क एष मयि<BR>स्थिते चंद्रगुप्तमभिभवितुमिच्छति Mu. 1.<BR>--12 To stand by or near, stand at<BR>one's side, help; उत्सवे व्यसने चैव<BR>दुर्भिक्षे शत्रुसंकटे । राजद्वारे श्मशाने च<BR>यस्तिष्ठति स बांधवः ॥ H. 1. 73.<BR>--13<BR>To rest or depend on.<BR>--14 To do,<BR>perform, occupy oneself with.<BR>--15<BR>(Atm.) To resort or go to (as<BR>an umpire), be guided by the<BR>advice of; संशय्य कर्णादिषु तिष्ठते यः<BR>Ki. 3. 14.<BR>--16 (Atm.) To offer<BR>oneself to (for sexual embrace),<BR>stand as a prostitute (with dat.);<BR>गोपी स्मरात् कृष्णाय तिष्ठते Sk. on<BR>P. I. 4. 34. --Caus. (स्थापयति-ते)<BR>1<BR>To cause to stand.<BR>--2 To lay, set,<BR>place, put.<BR>--3 To found, establish.<BR>--4 To stop.<BR>--5 To arrest, check.<BR>--6 To raise, erect.<BR>--7 To cause to<BR>last or continue, make durable.<BR>--8 To<BR>give in marriage; Māl. 10. 5.<BR>--9<BR>To instruct in, initiate into. --Desid.<BR>(तिष्ठासति) To wish to stand &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1147-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थ|स्थः
स्थ a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Standing, staying, abiding, being,<BR>existing &c.; तत्रस्थ, अंकस्थ,<BR>प्रकृतिस्थ, तटस्थ q.q. v.v.<BR>--स्थः A place,<BR>spot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाणु|स्थाणुः
स्थाणु a. [स्था-नु पृषो˚ णत्वम्] Firm,<BR>fixed, steady, stable, immovable,<BR>motionless.<BR>--णुः<BR>1 An epithet of<BR>Śiva; स स्थाणुः स्थिरभक्तियोगसुलभो<BR>निःश्रेयसायास्तु वः V. 1. 1.<BR>--2 A stake,<BR>post, pillar; किं स्थाणुरयमुत पुरुषः;<BR>Pt. 1. 49.<BR>--3 A peg, pin.<BR>--4 The<BR>gnomon of a dial.<BR>--5 A spear, dart.<BR>--6 A nest of white ants.<BR>--7 The<BR>drug or perfume called Jīvaka. --m.<BR>n. A branchless trunk or stem, any<BR>bare stalk or stem, pollard;<BR>--Comp.<BR>--छेदः one who cuts down the trunks<BR>of trees, one who clears away<BR>timber; स्थाणुच्छेदस्य केदारमाहुः शल्यवतो<BR>मृगं Ms. 9. 44.<BR>--भ्रमः mistaking<BR>anything for a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थातृ
स्थातृ a. Standing, stationary,<BR>fixed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानं|स्थान
स्थानं [स्था-ल्युट्]<BR>1 The act of<BR>standing or remaining, stay,<BR>continuance, residence; U. 3. 32.<BR>--2<BR>Being fixed or stationary.<BR>--3 A<BR>state, condition.<BR>--4 A place, spot,<BR>site, locality;<BR>अक्षमालामदत्त्वास्मात्स्थानात्पदात्पदमपि न गंतव्यं K.<BR>--5 Station,<BR>situation, position.<BR>--6 Relation,<BR>capacity; पितृस्थाने ‘in the place or<BR>capacity of a father’; भक्ष्यस्थाने<BR>Pt. 2. 26.<BR>--7 An abode, a house,<BR>dwelling-house; स एव (नक्रः) प्रच्युतः<BR>स्थानाच्छुनापि परिभूयते Pt. 3. 46.<BR>--8<BR>(a) A country, region, district. (b)<BR>A town, city.<BR>--9 Office, rank,<BR>dignity; अमात्यस्थाने नियोजितः.<BR>--10<BR>Object; गुणाः पूजास्थानं गुणिषु न च<BR>लिंगं न च वयः U. 4. 11.<BR>--11 An<BR>occasion, a matter, subject, cause;<BR>पराभ्यूहस्थानान्यपि तनुतराणि स्यगयति<BR>Māl. 1. 14; स्थानं जरापरिभवस्य तदेव पुंसां<BR>Subhāṣ.; so कलह˚, कोप˚, विवाद˚<BR>&c.<BR>--12 A fit or proper place;<BR>स्थानेष्वेव नियोज्यंते भृत्याश्चाभरणानि च<BR>Pt. 1. 72.<BR>--13 A fit or worthy object;<BR>स्थाने खलु सज्जति दृष्टिः M. 1; see<BR>स्थाने also.<BR>--14 The place or organ<BR>of utterance of any letter, (these<BR>are eight: --अष्टौ स्थानानि वर्णानामुरः कंठः<BR>शिरस्तथा । जिह्वामूलं च दंताश्च नासिकौष्ठौ च<BR>तालु च Śik. 13.).<BR>--15 A holy place.<BR>--16 An altar.<BR>--17 Aplace in a town,<BR>square, court.<BR>--18 The place or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-b" target="_blank">Page1148-b+ 57</a>]<BR>sphere assigned after death to<BR>persons according as they perform or<BR>neglect their prescribed duties.<BR>--19<BR>(In politics, war &c.) The firm<BR>attitude or bearing of troops, standing<BR>firm so as to repel a charge;<BR>Ms. 7. 190.<BR>--20 A halt.<BR>--21 A stationary<BR>condition, a neutral or middle<BR>state.<BR>--22 That which constitutes<BR>the chief strength or the very<BR>existence of a kingdom, a stamina of<BR>a kingdom; i. e. army, treasure,<BR>town, and territory; Ms. 7. 56 (where<BR>Kull. renders स्थानं by<BR>दंडकोषपुरराष्ट्रात्मकं चतुर्विधं).<BR>--23 Likeness,<BR>resemblance.<BR>--24 Part or division of a<BR>work, section, chapter &c.<BR>--25 The<BR>character or part of an actor.<BR>--26<BR>Interval, opportunity, leisure.<BR>--27<BR>(In music) A note, tone,<BR>modulation of the voice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्यक्षः<BR>{1} a local governor. {2} the<BR>superintendent of a place. {3} a watchman.<BR>police-officer.<BR>--आसनं n. du.<BR>standing and sitting down.<BR>--आसेधः<BR>confinement to a place, imprisonment,<BR>arrest; cf. आसेध.<BR>--चिंतकः a kind<BR>of quarter-master.<BR>--च्युत see<BR>स्थानभ्रष्ट.<BR>--पालः a watchman, sentinel,<BR>policeman.<BR>--भूमि f. a dwelling-place,<BR>mansion.<BR>--भ्रष्ट a. ejected from an<BR>office, displaced, dismissed, out of<BR>employ.<BR>--माहात्म्यं {1} the greatness<BR>or glory of any place. {2} a kind of<BR>divine virtue or uncommon sanctity<BR>supposed to be inherent in a sacred<BR>spot.<BR>--योगः assignment of proper<BR>places; द्रव्याणां स्थानयोगांश्च<BR>क्रयविक्रयमेव च Ms. 9. 332.<BR>--स्थ a. being<BR>in one's abode, at home.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानकं|स्थानक
स्थानकं [स्थान स्वार्थे क]<BR>1 A<BR>position, situation.<BR>--2 A particular<BR>point or situation in dramatic action;<BR>e. g. पताकास्थानक q. v.<BR>--3 A city,<BR>town.<BR>--4 A basin.<BR>--5 Froth, a kind<BR>of scum on spirits or wine.<BR>--6 A<BR>mode of recitation.<BR>--7 A division<BR>or section of the Taittirīya, a branch<BR>of the Yajurveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानतस्
स्थानतस् ind.<BR>1 According to one's<BR>place or position.<BR>--2 From one's<BR>proper place.<BR>--3 With reference to<BR>the organ of utterance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिक|स्थानिकः
स्थानिक a. (की f.)<BR>1 Belonging<BR>to a place, local.<BR>--2 (In gram.)<BR>That which takes the place of a<BR>thing, or is substituted for it.<BR>--कः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-c" target="_blank">Page1148-c+ 57</a>]<BR>1 Any one holding an office, a<BR>placeman.<BR>--2 The governor of a place.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानिन्
स्थानिन् a. [स्थानमस्यास्ति रक्ष्यत्वेन<BR>इनि]<BR>1 Having a place.<BR>--2 Having<BR>fixedness, permanent.<BR>--3 Having a<BR>substitute. --m.<BR>1 The original<BR>form or primitive element, that for<BR>which anything else is substituted;<BR>स्थानिवदादेशोऽनल्विधौ P. I. 1. 59.<BR>--2<BR>The form so substituted for<BR>anything.<BR>--3 That which has a place,<BR>or is actually expressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थानीय|स्थानीयं
स्थानीय a.<BR>1 Belonging to a place,<BR>local.<BR>--2 Suitable to a place.<BR>--यं A<BR>town, city.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाने
स्थाने ind. (loc. of स्थान)<BR>1 In the<BR>right or proper place, rightly,<BR>properly, justly, truly, appropriately;<BR>स्थाने वृता भूपतिभिः परोक्षैः R. 7. 13;<BR>स्थाने प्राणाः कामिनां दूत्यधीनाः<BR>M. 3. 14; Ku. 6. 67, 7. 65.<BR>--2 In place<BR>of, instead of, in lieu of, as a<BR>substitute for; धातोः स्थान इवादेशं<BR>सुग्रीवंसंन्यवेशयत् R. 12. 58.<BR>--3 On<BR>account of, because of.<BR>--4 Similarly,<BR>like, as.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापक|स्थापकः
स्थापक a. [स्थापयति स्था-णिच्-ण्वुल्]<BR>Causing to stand, fixing, founding,<BR>establishing, regulating.<BR>--कः<BR>1 The<BR>director of the stage-business, a<BR>stage-manager.<BR>--2 The founder of a<BR>temple, or erector of an image.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापनं|स्थापन
स्थापनं [स्था-णिच्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 (a) The<BR>act of causing to stand, fixing,<BR>founding, establishing, instituting.<BR>(b) Regulating, directing.<BR>--2<BR>Fixing the thoughts, concentration of<BR>the mind, steady application,<BR>abstraction.<BR>--3 A dwelling, habitation.<BR>--4 A ceremony performed on a<BR>woman's perceiving the first signs of<BR>living conception; cf. पुंसवन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापना
स्थापना<BR>1 Placing, fixing,<BR>founding, establishing.<BR>--2 Arranging,<BR>regulating (as a drama),<BR>stagemanagement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापित|स्थापितं
स्थापित p. p. [स्था-णिच् क्त]<BR>1 Placed,<BR>fixed, located, deposited.<BR>--2<BR>Founded, instituted.<BR>--3 Set up, raised,<BR>erected.<BR>--4 Directed, regulated,<BR>ordered, enacted.<BR>--5 Determined,<BR>settled, ascertained.<BR>--6 Appointed<BR>to, entrusted with any duty, post<BR>&c.<BR>--7 Wedded, married;<BR>Māl. 10. 5.<BR>--8 Firm, steady.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाप्य|स्थाप्यः
स्थाप्य a.<BR>1 To be placed or<BR>deposited.<BR>--2 To be founded, fixed or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-a" target="_blank">Page1149-a+ 57</a>]<BR>established.<BR>--प्यं A pledge, deposit,<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपहरणं the embezzlement<BR>of a deposit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1148-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थामन्
स्थामन् n. [स्था-मनिन्]<BR>1 Strength,<BR>power, stamina, as in the word<BR>अश्वत्थामन्, see the quotation from<BR>Mb. under अश्वत्थामन्.<BR>--2 Fixity,<BR>stability.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायिन्
स्थायिन् a. [स्था-णिनि]<BR>1 Standing,<BR>staying, being situated (at the end<BR>of comp.).<BR>--2 Enduring,<BR>continuing, lasting, abiding; शरीरं<BR>क्षणविध्वंसि कल्पांतस्थायिनो गुणाः Subhāṣ.;<BR>कतिपयदिवसस्थायिनी यौवनश्रीः<BR>Bh. 2. 82; Mv. 7. 15.<BR>--3 Living,<BR>dwelling, remaining; Me. 23.<BR>--4<BR>Permanent, firm, steady,<BR>invariable, unchangeable. --m. A<BR>lasting or permanent feeling; (see<BR>स्थायिभाव below); Śi. 2. 87. --n. Anything<BR>lasting, a permanent state or<BR>condition.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भावः a fixed or<BR>permanent condition of mind, a<BR>lasting or permanent feeling; (these<BR>feelings being said to give rise to<BR>the different rasas or sentiments<BR>in poetry, each rasa having its own<BR>Sthāyibhāva); they are eight or<BR>nine; रतिर्हासश्च शोकश्च क्रोधोत्साहौ भयं<BR>तथा । जुगुप्सा विस्मयश्चेत्थमष्टौ प्रोक्तः<BR>शमोऽपि च S. D. 206; cf.<BR>व्यभिचारिभाव, भाव, विभाव also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायीभू
स्थायीभू {c1c} P. To become firm,<BR>fixed or permanent, take a strong<BR>or firm hold on; Pt. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थायुक|स्थायुकः
स्थायुक a. (का or की f.)<BR>[स्था-उकञ्]<BR>1 Likely to last, enduring.<BR>--2<BR>Firm, steady, stationary.<BR>--कः The<BR>superintendent or head of a village.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावर|स्थावरं|स्थावरः
स्थावर a. [स्था-वरच्]<BR>1 Fixed to<BR>one spot, stable, stationary,<BR>immovable, inanimate (opp. जंगम);<BR>शरीरिणां स्थावरजंगमानां सुखाय<BR>तज्जन्मदिनं बभूव Ku. 1. 23, 6. 67, 73.<BR>--2<BR>Inert, inactive, slow.<BR>--3 Regular,<BR>established.<BR>--रः A mountain;<BR>स्थावराणां हिमालयः Bg. 10. 25.<BR>--रं<BR>1<BR>Any stationary or inanimate object<BR>(such as clay, stones, trees &c.<BR>which formed the seventh creation<BR>of Brahman; cf. Ms. 1. 41); मान्यः<BR>स मे स्थावरजंगमानां<BR>सर्गस्थितिप्रत्यवहारहेतुः R. 2. 44; Ku. 6. 58.<BR>--2 A<BR>bow-string.<BR>--3 immovable property,<BR>real estate.<BR>--4 A heir-loom.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अस्थावरं, --जंगमं {1} moveable and<BR>immovable property. {2} animate<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-b" target="_blank">Page1149-b+ 57</a>]<BR>and inanimate things.<BR>--आत्मन् a.<BR>of immovable form; Ku. 6. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरता
स्थावरता --त्वं Fixedness,<BR>stability. {2} The state of a vegetable or<BR>mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थावरत्वं|स्थावरत्व
स्थावरता --त्वं Fixedness,<BR>stability. {2} The state of a vegetable or<BR>mineral.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासकः|स्थासक
स्थासकः [स्था-स-स्वार्थादौ क]<BR>1<BR>Perfuming or smearing the body with<BR>fragrant unguents.<BR>--2 A bubble of<BR>water or any fluid; Śi. 18. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थासु
स्थासु n. Bodily strength.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थास्नु|स्थास्नुः
स्थास्नु a. [स्था-स्नु]<BR>1 Disposed<BR>to stand, firm, immovable.<BR>--2<BR>Permanent, eternal, lasting, durable;<BR>Śi. 2. 93, Ki. 2. 19;<BR>--स्नुः A tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थित|स्थितः
स्थित p. p. [स्था-क्त]<BR>1 Stood,<BR>remained, stayed.<BR>--2 Standing.<BR>--3<BR>Standing up, risen; स्थितः<BR>स्थितामुच्चलितः प्रयातां… छायेव तां<BR>भूपतिरन्वगच्छत् R. 2. 6.<BR>--4 Staying, resting,<BR>living, being, existing, situated;<BR>धन्या केयं स्थिता ते शिरसि Mu. 1. 1;<BR>Me. 7; oft. with gerunds merely<BR>as a copula; V. 1. 1; Ś. 1. 1,<BR>Ku. 1. 1.<BR>--5 Happened, occurred;<BR>Ku. 4. 27.<BR>--6 Stationed in, occupying,<BR>appointed to; Ś. 4. 18.<BR>--7 Acting<BR>up to, abiding by, conforming to;<BR>R. 5. 33; धर्मे स्थिताः (राजानः)<BR>Māl. 10. 25.<BR>--8 Stood still, stopped,<BR>desisted.<BR>--9 Fixed on, firmly attached<BR>to; Ku. 5. 82.<BR>--10 Steady, firm;<BR>as in स्थितधी or स्थितप्रज्ञ q. v.<BR>--11<BR>Determined, resolved; Ku. 4. 39.<BR>--12 Established, decreed.<BR>--13<BR>Steadfast in conduct, steady-minded.<BR>--14 Upright, virtuous.<BR>--15<BR>Faithful to a promise or agreement.<BR>--16<BR>Agreed, engaged, contracted.<BR>--17<BR>Ready, being close or at hand.<BR>--तं<BR>A word standing by itself.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपस्थित a. with and without the<BR>particle ‘iti’ (as a word).<BR>--धी<BR>a. firm-minded, steady-minded,<BR>cool.<BR>--पाट्यं recitation in Prākṛta<BR>by a woman while standing.<BR>--प्रज्ञ<BR>a. firm in judgment or wisdom,<BR>free from any hallucination,<BR>contented; प्रजहाति यदा कामान् सर्वान्<BR>पार्थ मनोगतान् । आत्मन्येवात्मना तुष्टः<BR>स्थितप्रज्ञस्तदोच्यते Bg. 2. 55.<BR>--प्रेमन्<BR>m. a staunch or faithful friend.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिः|स्थिति
स्थितिः f. [स्था-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Standing,<BR>remaining, staying, abiding, living,<BR>stay, residence; स्थितिं नो रे दध्याः<BR>क्षणमपि मदांधेक्षण सखे Bv. 1. 52;<BR>रक्षोगृहे स्थितिर्मूलमग्निशुद्धौ त्वनिश्चयः U. 1. 6.<BR>--2 Stopping, standing still,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-c" target="_blank">Page1149-c+ 57</a>]<BR>continuance in one state; प्रस्थितायां प्रतिष्ठेथाः<BR>स्थितायां स्थितिमाचरेः R. 1. 89.<BR>--3<BR>Remaining stationary, fixity,<BR>steadiness, firmness, steady application<BR>or devotion; मम भूयात् परमात्मनि<BR>स्थितिः Bv. 4. 23; Māl. 5. 22.<BR>--4 A<BR>state, position, situation, condition.<BR>--5 Natural state, nature, habit; अथ<BR>वा स्थितिरियं मंदमतीनां H. 4.<BR>--6<BR>Stability, permanence,<BR>perpetuation, continuance;<BR>वंशस्थितेरधिगमान्महति प्रमोदे V. 5. 15; कन्यां<BR>कुलंस्य स्थितये स्थितिज्ञः Ku. 1. 18<BR>R. 3. 27.<BR>--7 Correctness of<BR>conduct, steadfastness in the path of<BR>duty, decorum, duty, moral<BR>rectitude, propriety; R. 3. 27,<BR>11. 65, 12. 31; Ku. 1. 18; Ś. 5. 10,<BR>--8 Maintenance of discipline,<BR>establishment of good order (in<BR>astate); R. 1. 25.<BR>--9 Rank,<BR>dignity, high station or rank.<BR>--10<BR>Maintenance, sustenance;<BR>Māl. 9. 32, R. 5. 9.<BR>--11 Continuance in<BR>life, preservation (one of the three<BR>states of human beings);<BR>सर्गस्थितिप्रत्यवहारेहतुः R. 2. 44; Ku. 2. 6.<BR>--12<BR>Cessation, pause, stop.<BR>--13<BR>Wellbeing, welfare.<BR>--14 Consistency.<BR>--15 A settled rule, ordinance,<BR>decree, an axiom or maxim.<BR>--16<BR>Settled determination.<BR>--17 Term, limit,<BR>boundary.<BR>--18 Inertia, resistance<BR>to motion.<BR>--19 Duration of an<BR>eclipse.<BR>--20 Regard, consideration,<BR>account; नासां च वयसि स्थितिः<BR>Pt. 1. 143.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पदं the proper basin<BR>(for flow), the right path;<BR>Mu. 3. 8.<BR>--स्थापक a. fixing in the<BR>original position, having the power<BR>of restoring to a previous state,<BR>having elastic properties.<BR>--(कः)<BR>elasticity, capability of recovering<BR>the former position.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थितिमत्|स्थितिमन्त्
स्थितिमत् a.<BR>1 Possessed of firmness,<BR>steady, firm; N. 5. 22.<BR>--2 Permanent;<BR>R. 3. 27.<BR>--3 Virtuous, upright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थांडिलः|स्थाण्डिल|स्थांडिल|स्थाण्डिलः
स्थांडिलः [स्थडिल शयिता अण्]<BR>1<BR>An ascetic who sleeps on the bare<BR>ground or on a place prepared for<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--2 A religious mendicant<BR>or beggar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थापत्यः|स्थापत्य
स्थापत्यः [स्थपतिरेव स्वार्थे ष्यञ्] A<BR>guard of the women's apartments.<BR>--त्यं Architecture, building.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थालं|स्थाल
स्थालं [स्थलति तिष्ठत्यन्नाद्यत्र आधारे<BR>घञ्]<BR>1 A plate or dish.<BR>--2 A<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-a" target="_blank">Page1150-a+ 56</a>]<BR>cooking-pot, any culinary vessel.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रूपं the form or representation of<BR>a pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1149-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाली
स्थाली<BR>1 An earthen pot or pan,<BR>a cooking-pot, caldron, kettle; न हि<BR>भिक्षुकाः संतीति स्थाल्यो नाधिश्रीयंते<BR>Sarva. S.; स्थाल्यां वैडूर्यमय्यां पचति<BR>तिलखलीतिंधनैश्चंदनाद्यैः Bh. 2. 100.<BR>--2 A particular vessel used in the<BR>preparation of Soma.<BR>--3 The<BR>trumpet-flower.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पाकः a<BR>particular religious act performed by a<BR>householder.<BR>--पुरीषं the sediment<BR>or dirt sticking to a cooking-pot.<BR>--पुलाकः boiled rice in a<BR>cookingpot. ˚न्यायः see under न्याय.<BR>--बिलं<BR>the interior or hollow of a caldron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थाविर|स्थाविरं
स्थाविर a. (रा or री f.) Thick,<BR>firm.<BR>--रं Old age (commencing<BR>after seventy); (वृद्धः स्यात्सप्ततेरूर्ध्वं<BR>वर्षीयान् नवतेः परं).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिर|स्थिरः
स्थिर a. [स्था-किरच्] (compar.<BR>स्थेयस्; superl. स्थेष्ठ)<BR>1 Firm, steady,<BR>fixed; भावस्थिराणि जननांतरसौहृदानि<BR>Ś. 5. 2; स स्थाणुः<BR>स्थिरभक्तियोगसुलभो निःश्रेयसायास्तु वः V. 1. 1;<BR>Ku. 1. 30; R. 11. 19.<BR>--2 immovable, still,<BR>motionless; Ku. 2. 38.<BR>--3<BR>Immoveably fixed; U. 1. 40.<BR>--4 Permanent,<BR>eternal, everlasting, Me. 55;<BR>Māl. 10. 25.<BR>--5 Cool, collected,<BR>composed, placid, calm.<BR>--6 Quiescent,<BR>free from passion.<BR>--7 Steady in<BR>conduct, steadfast.<BR>--8 Constant,<BR>faithful, determined.<BR>--9 Certain,<BR>sure.<BR>--10 Hard, solid.<BR>--11 Strong,<BR>intense.<BR>--12 Stern, relentless,<BR>hard-hearted; Ku. 5. 47.<BR>--रः<BR>1<BR>A god, deity.<BR>--2 A tree.<BR>--3 A<BR>mountain.<BR>--4 A bull.<BR>--5 N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR>--6 N. of Kārtikeya.<BR>--7<BR>Final beatitude or absolution.<BR>--8<BR>The planet Saturn.<BR>--9 N. of<BR>certain zodiacal signs (Taurus, Leo,<BR>Scorpio, and Aquarius.).<BR>--रा<BR>1<BR>The earth.<BR>--2 A strong-minded<BR>woman.<BR>--3 The silk-cotton tree.<BR>(स्थिरीकृ means {1} to confirm,<BR>strengthen, or to corroborate. {2} to<BR>stop, make fast. {3} to cheer up,<BR>console, comfort; Ś. 4. स्थिरीभू<BR>means {1} to become firm or steady.<BR>{2} to become calm or tranquil).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंघ्रिपः the marshy<BR>date-tree.<BR>--अनुराग a. firm in<BR>attachment, constant, in affection.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-b" target="_blank">Page1150-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--आत्मन्, --चित्त, --चेतस्, --धी, --बुद्धि<BR>--मति a. {1} firm-minded, steady in<BR>thought or resolve, resolute;<BR>R. 8. 22. {2} cool, calm, dispassionate.<BR>--आयुस्, --जीविन् a. long-lived,<BR>lasting. (--m.) the silk-cotton tree.<BR>--आरंभ a. firm in undertakings,<BR>persevering.<BR>--कुटृकः {1} a steady<BR>pulverizer. {2} a kind of common<BR>divisor (in algebra).<BR>--गंधः the<BR>champaka flower.<BR>--(धा) {1} the<BR>trumpet-flower. {2} the Ketakī<BR>plant.<BR>--छदः the birch tree.<BR>--छायः {1} a tree which gives shelter<BR>to travellers. {2} a tree (in<BR>general).<BR>--जिह्वः a fish.<BR>--जीविता the<BR>silk-cotton tree.<BR>--दंष्ट्रः {1} a snake.<BR>{2} Viṣṇu in his boar<BR>incarnation. {3} sound.<BR>--पत्रः the<BR>marshy date-tree.<BR>--पुष्पः {1} the<BR>Campaka tree. {2} the Bakula<BR>tree.<BR>--प्रतिज्ञ a. {1} persisting in<BR>an assertion, obstinate,<BR>pertinacious. {2} faithful to a promise.<BR>--प्रतिबंध a. firm in opposition,<BR>obstinate; Ś. 2.<BR>--प्रतिष्ठा fixed<BR>residence or abode.<BR>--फला a kind of<BR>gourd.<BR>--योनिः a large tree which<BR>gives shade and shelter.<BR>--यौवन<BR>a. ever youthful.<BR>--(नः) a kind of<BR>good or evil genius, a fairy.<BR>--रंगा<BR>indigo.<BR>--श्री a. having everlasting<BR>prosperity.<BR>--संगर a. faithful to a<BR>promise, true, veracious.<BR>--सौहृद<BR>a. firm in friendship.<BR>--स्थायिन् a.<BR>remaining firm or steady, keeping<BR>perfectly still (as in meditation).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरतर|स्थिरतरः
स्थिरतर a. More firm, fixed &c.<BR>--रः The Supreme Being.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरता
स्थिरता --त्वं<BR>1 Firmness, steadiness,<BR>stability.<BR>--2 Firm or vigorous<BR>effort, fortitude; Ś. 4. 14.<BR>--3<BR>Constancy, firmness of mind.<BR>--4<BR>Fixity.<BR>--5 Fearlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थिरत्वं|स्थिरत्व
स्थिरता --त्वं<BR>1 Firmness, steadiness,<BR>stability.<BR>--2 Firm or vigorous<BR>effort, fortitude; Ś. 4. 14.<BR>--3<BR>Constancy, firmness of mind.<BR>--4<BR>Fixity.<BR>--5 Fearlessness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थुड्
स्थुड् {c6c} P. (स्थुडति) To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूणा
स्थूणा [स्था-नक् उदंतादेशः पृषो˚<BR>Tv.]<BR>1 The post or pillar of a<BR>house.<BR>--2 A post or pillar in<BR>general; स्थूणानिखननन्यायेन Ś. B.<BR>--3<BR>An iron image or statue.<BR>--4 An<BR>anvil.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--निखननन्याय see<BR>under न्याय.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूमः|स्थूम
स्थूमः<BR>1 Light.<BR>--2 The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूरः|स्थूर
स्थूरः<BR>1 A bull.<BR>--2 A man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूरिन्
स्थूरिन् m. A pack-horse or<BR>bullock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूल|स्थूलं|स्थूलः
स्थूल a. (compar. स्थवीयस्,<BR>superl. स्थविष्ठ)<BR>1 Large, great, big,<BR>bulky, huge; बहुस्पृशापि स्थूलेन<BR>स्थीयते बहिरश्मवत् Śi. 2. 78 (where it<BR>has sense 6 also); स्थूलहस्तावलेपान्<BR>Me. 14, 106; R. 6. 28.<BR>--2 Fat,<BR>corpulent, stout.<BR>--3 Strong,<BR>powerful; स्थूलं स्थूलं श्वसिति K. ‘breathes<BR>hard’.<BR>--4 Thick, clumsy.<BR>--5 Gross,<BR>coarse, rough (fig. also); as in<BR>स्थूलमानं q. v.<BR>--6 Foolish, doltish,<BR>silly, ignorant.<BR>--7 Stolid, dull,<BR>thick-headed.<BR>--8 Not exact.<BR>--लः<BR>The jack tree.<BR>--ला Large<BR>cardamoms.<BR>--लं<BR>1 A heap, quantity.<BR>--2<BR>A tent.<BR>--3 The summit of a<BR>mountain (कूट).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंत्रं the<BR>larger intestine near the anus.<BR>--आस्यः<BR>a snake.<BR>--उच्चयः {1} a large<BR>fragment of a crag or rock fallen from<BR>a mountain and forming an<BR>irregular mound. {2} incompleteness,<BR>deficiency, defect. {3} the middle<BR>pace of elephants. {4} an eruption<BR>of pimples on the face. {5} a<BR>hollow at the root of an elephant's<BR>tusks.<BR>--कंटकिका the silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR>--कंदः {1} a kind of esculent root.<BR>{2} red garlic.<BR>--काय a. fat,<BR>corpulent.<BR>--क्षेडः, --क्ष्वेडः an arrow.<BR>--चापः a large bow-like instrument<BR>used in cleaning cotton.<BR>--तालः<BR>the marshy date-tree.<BR>--धी, --मति a.<BR>foolish, doltish.<BR>--नालः a kind of<BR>large reed.<BR>--नास, नासिक a.<BR>thicknosed.<BR>--(सः, --कः) a hog, boar.<BR>--पटः-टं coarse cloth.<BR>--पट्टः cotton.<BR>--(ट्टं),<BR>--पट्टाकः coarse cloth.<BR>--पाद a.<BR>clubfooted, having swelled legs.<BR>--(दः) {1}<BR>an elephant. {2} a man with<BR>elephantiasis.<BR>--फलः the silk-cotton<BR>tree.<BR>--भूत n. pl. the five grosser<BR>elements (according to Sāṃkhya<BR>phil.).<BR>--मरिचं a kind of berry<BR>(कक्कोल).<BR>--मानं rough or inexact<BR>calculation, gross or rough<BR>computation.<BR>--मूलं a kind of radish.<BR>--लक्ष --क्ष्य a. {1} munificent, liberal,<BR>generous. {2} wise, learned. {3}<BR>inclined to recollect both benefits<BR>and injuries. {4} taking careless<BR>aim.<BR>--वल्कलः the red Lodhra<BR>tree.<BR>--शंखा a woman having a<BR>large vulva.<BR>--शरीरं the grosser or<BR>material and perishable body (opp.<BR>सूक्ष्म or लिंग-शरीर q. v.)<BR>--शाटकः<BR>--शाटिः a thick or coarse cloth.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">Page1151-a+ 55</a>]<BR>--शीषिंका a small ant having a large<BR>head in proportion to its size.<BR>--षट्पदः {1} a large bee. {2} a wasp.<BR>--सूक्ष्म<BR>a. mighty and subtle (as the god).<BR>--स्कंधः the lakucha tree.<BR>--हस्तः,<BR>an elephant's trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1150-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलक|स्थूलकः
स्थूलक a. Large, big, huge, bulky.<BR>--कः A sort of grass or reed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलता
स्थूलता --त्वं<BR>1 Largeness, bulkiness,<BR>bigness; Pt. 1. 190.<BR>--2 Dulness,<BR>stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलत्वं|स्थूलत्व
स्थूलता --त्वं<BR>1 Largeness, bulkiness,<BR>bigness; Pt. 1. 190.<BR>--2 Dulness,<BR>stupidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलयति
स्थूलयति Den. P. To become big<BR>or stout, grow bulky or fat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थूलिन्
स्थूलिन् m. A camel.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेमन्
स्थेमन् m. Firmness, stability,<BR>fixity, fixedness; द्राघीयांसः संहताः<BR>स्येमभाजः Śi. 18. 33; न यत्र स्थेमानं<BR>दधुरतिभयभ्रांतनयनाः Bv. 1. 32.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेय|स्थेयः
स्थेय a. [स्था-कर्मणि यत्] To be<BR>fixed or placed, to be settled or<BR>determined.<BR>--यः<BR>1 A person chosen<BR>to settle a dispute (between two<BR>parties), an arbitrator, umpire, a<BR>judge; H. 4. 1.<BR>--2 A domestic<BR>priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेयस्
स्थेयस् a. (सी f.) More firm,<BR>stronger; (compar. of स्थिर q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थेष्ठ|स्थेष्ठः
स्थेष्ठ a. Very firm, strongest;<BR>(superl. of स्थिर q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थैर्यं|स्थैर्य|स्थैर्य्य|स्थैर्य्यं
स्थैर्यं [स्थिरस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Firmness, stability, fixity, steadiness.<BR>--2 Continuance.<BR>--3 Firmness of<BR>mind, resolution, constancy;<BR>Bg. 13. 7.<BR>--4 Patience.<BR>--5 Hardness,<BR>solidity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौणेयः|स्थौणेय|स्थौणेयं
स्थौणेयः, स्थौणेयकः A kind of<BR>perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौणेयकः|स्थौणेयक|स्थौणेयकं
स्थौणेयः, स्थौणेयकः A kind of<BR>perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौरं|स्थौर
स्थौरं<BR>1 Firmness, strength,<BR>power.<BR>--2 A load sufficient for a horse<BR>or ass.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौरिन्
स्थौरिन् m.<BR>1 A horse<BR>carrying burdens on his back,<BR>packhorse.<BR>--2 A strong horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्थौल्यं|स्थौल्य
स्थौल्यं<BR>1 Bigness, bulkiness,<BR>stoutness.<BR>--2 Dulness or density<BR>of intellect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नवः|स्नव
स्नवः Trickling, oozing,<BR>dripping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नस्
स्नस् {1} {c4c} P. (स्नसति, स्नस्यति)<BR>1<BR>To inhabit.<BR>--2 To eject (as from<BR>the mouth), reject.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नसा
स्नसा A tendon, muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्ना
स्ना {c2c} P. (स्नाति, स्नात)<BR>1 To<BR>bathe, perform ablution;<BR>मृगतृष्णांभसि स्नातः.<BR>--2 To perform the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-b" target="_blank">Page1151-b+ 58</a>]<BR>ceremony of bathing at the time of<BR>leaving the house of one's spiritual<BR>preceptor. --Caus. (स्नापयति-ते,<BR>स्नपयति-ते) To cause to bathe, wet,<BR>moisten, sprinkle; (तोयैः) सतूर्यमेनां<BR>स्नपयांबभूवुः Ku. 7. 10;<BR>स्मितस्नपिताधरा Gīt. 12, U. 3. 23,<BR>Ki. 5. 44. 47; Śi. 2. 7, Me. 43. --Desid. (<BR>सिस्नासति) To wish to bathe. -WITH<BR>अप to bathe after mourning.<BR>--नि<BR>to plunge deep into; i. e. to be<BR>perfect or thoroughly versed in;<BR>see निष्णात.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपन|स्नपनं
स्नपन a.<BR>1 Causing to bathe.<BR>--2<BR>Used for bathing.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Sprinkling, washing.<BR>--2 Bathing, ablution;<BR>रेजे जनैः स्नपनसांद्रतरार्द्रमूर्तिः Śi. 5. 57.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नपित|स्नपितः
स्नपित a. Bathed, washed,<BR>sprinkled &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नात|स्नातः
स्नात p. p. Bathed, washed,<BR>purified by ablution.<BR>--तः<BR>1 One whose<BR>course of holy study is over.<BR>--2<BR>An initiated householder; cf. स्नातक.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नातकः|स्नातक
स्नातकः<BR>1 A Brāhmaṇa who has<BR>performed the ceremony of ablution<BR>which has to be performed on<BR>his finishing his first Āśrama<BR>(that of a Brahmacārin).<BR>--2 A Brāhmaṇa just returned<BR>from the house of his<BR>preceptor and become an initiated<BR>householder (गृहस्थ).<BR>--3 A<BR>Brāhmaṇa who is a Bhikṣu (beggar<BR>of alms) for any religious object;<BR>Ms. 11. 2.<BR>--4 Any man of the<BR>first three classes who is an<BR>initiated householder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानं|स्नान
स्नानं [स्ना-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Bathing,<BR>washing, ablution, immersion in<BR>water; ततः प्रविशति स्नानोत्तीर्णः<BR>काश्यपः Ś. 4.<BR>--2 Purification by bathing,<BR>any religious or ceremonial ablution.<BR>--3 The ceremony of bathing or<BR>anointing an idol.<BR>--4 Anything<BR>used in ablution.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अगारं a<BR>bath-room.<BR>--तृणं Kuśa-grass.<BR>--द्रोणी<BR>a bathing tub.<BR>--यात्रा the festival<BR>held on the full-moon day in the<BR>month of Jyeṣṭha.<BR>--वस्त्रं a<BR>bathing-garment; सकृत् किं पीडितं<BR>स्नानवस्त्रं मुंचेत् द्रुतं पयः H. 2. 106.<BR>--विधिः<BR>{1} the act of ablution. {2} the<BR>proper manner or rules of ablution.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नानीय|स्नानीयं
स्नानीय a. [स्नानाय हितं छ] Fit<BR>or suitable for bathing or ablution,<BR>worn during bathing;<BR>स्नानीयवस्त्रक्रियया पत्रोर्णं वोपयुज्यते M. 5. 12.<BR>--य<BR>Water or any other article (such<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">Page1151-c+ 57</a>]<BR>as unguents^1, perfumed powders &c.)<BR>proper for bathing; R. 16. 21.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापकः|स्नापक
स्नापकः A servant who bathes<BR>his master, or brings bathing water<BR>for him.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नापनं|स्नापन
स्नापनं The act of causing to bathe,<BR>or attending a person while<BR>bathing; Ms. 2. 209.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायुः|स्नायु
स्नायुः [स्नाति शुध्यति दोषोऽनया<BR>स्नाउण् Tv.]<BR>1 A tendon, muscle, sinew;<BR>स्वल्पं स्नायुवसावशेषमलिनं<BR>निर्मांसमप्यस्थि गोः Bh. 2. 30.<BR>--2 The string of<BR>a bow.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्मन् n. a kind of<BR>disease of the eyes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नायुकः|स्नायुक
स्नायुकः See स्नायु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नावः|स्नाव
स्नावः, स्नावन् m. A tendon,<BR>muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नावन्
स्नावः, स्नावन् m. A tendon,<BR>muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निट्
स्निट् {c10c} U. (स्नेटयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>go.<BR>--2 To love, be in love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निह्
स्निह् {c4c} P. (स्निह्यति, स्निग्ध)<BR>1 To<BR>feel or have affection for, love, be<BR>fond of (with loc. of the person<BR>or thing that is loved or liked);<BR>किं नु खलु बालेऽस्मिन्नौरस इव पुत्रे<BR>स्निह्यति मे मनः Ś. 7; स च स्निह्यत्यावयोः<BR>U. 6 (where आवयोः may be genitive<BR>also).<BR>--2 To be easily attached.<BR>--3<BR>To be pleased with, be kind to.<BR>--4 To be sticky, viscid, or adhesive.<BR>--5 To be smooth or bland. --Caus.<BR>(स्नेहयति-ते)<BR>1 To make unctuous,<BR>anoint, besmear, lubricate.<BR>--2 To<BR>cause to love.<BR>--3 To dissolve,<BR>destroy, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्ध|स्निग्धं|स्निग्धः
स्निग्ध a. [स्निह्-क्त]<BR>1 Loving,<BR>affectionate, friendly, attached,<BR>tender; Māl. 5. 20.<BR>--2 Oily,<BR>unctuous, greasy, wetted with oil;<BR>उत्पश्यामि त्वयि तटगते<BR>स्निग्धभिन्नांजनाभे Me. 59; स्निग्धवेणीसवर्णे 18;<BR>Śi. 12. 62; Māl. 10. 4.<BR>--3 Sticky, viscid,<BR>adhesive, cohesive.<BR>--4 Glistening,<BR>shining, glossy, resplendent;<BR>कनकनिकषस्निग्धा विद्युत् प्रिया न ममोर्वशी<BR>V. 4. 1; Me. 37; U. 1. 33, 6. 21.<BR>--5<BR>Smooth, emollient.<BR>--6 Moist, wet.<BR>--7 Cooling.<BR>--8 Kind, soft, bland,<BR>amiable; प्रीतिस्निग्धैर्जनपदवधूलोचनैः<BR>पीयमानः Me. 16.<BR>--9 Lovely, agreeable,<BR>charming; स्निग्धगंभीरनिर्घोषं<BR>R. 1. 36, Me. 64, U. 2. 14, 3. 22.<BR>--10<BR>Thick, dense, compact;<BR>स्निग्धच्छायातरुषु वसतिं रामगिर्याश्रमेषु (चक्रे)<BR>Me. 1.<BR>--11 Intent, fixed, steadfast (as<BR>a gaze or look).<BR>--ग्धः<BR>1 A friend,<BR>an affectionate or friendly person;<BR>विज्ञैः स्निग्धैरुपकृतमपि द्वेष्यतां याति<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">Page1152-a+ 55</a>]<BR>किंचित् H. 2. 190; or स स्निधोऽ<BR>कुशलान्निवारयति यः Subhāṣ.;<BR>Pt. 2. 166.<BR>--2 The red castor-oil plant.<BR>--3 A kind of pine.<BR>--ग्धं<BR>1 Oil.<BR>--2<BR>Bee's-wax.<BR>--3 Light, lustre.<BR>--4<BR>Thickness, coarseness<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जनः an affectionate or friendly<BR>person, a friend; स्निग्धजनसांवभेक्तं हि<BR>दुःखं सह्यवेदनं भवति Ś. 3.<BR>--तंडुलः a<BR>kind of rice of quick growth.<BR>--दृष्टि a. looking intently or with<BR>a fixed gaze.<BR>--पत्रः --त्रा the jujube.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1151-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धता
स्निग्धता --त्वं<BR>1 Oiliness.<BR>--2<BR>Blandness.<BR>--3 Tenderness, affection, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धत्वं|स्निग्धत्व
स्निग्धता --त्वं<BR>1 Oiliness.<BR>--2<BR>Blandness.<BR>--3 Tenderness, affection, love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्निग्धा
स्निग्धा Marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
स्नु {c2c} P. (स्नौति, स्नुत)<BR>1 To drip,<BR>trickle, fall in drops, distil, drop,<BR>ooze or run out, leak out.<BR>--2 To<BR>flow, stream.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुत|स्नुतः
स्नुत a. Oozed, dropped, flowed &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
स्नु m. n.<BR>1 Table-land.<BR>--2 Top,<BR>surface (in general). (This word<BR>has no forms for the first five<BR>inflections and is optionally<BR>substituted for सानु after acc. dual).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नु|स्नुः
स्नु f. A sinew, tendon, muscle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुषा
स्नुषा A daughter-in-law;<BR>समुपास्यत पुत्रभोग्यया स्नुषयेवाविकृतेंद्रियः<BR>श्रिया R. 8. 14, 15. 72.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुस्
स्नुस् {c4c} P. (स्नुस्यति)<BR>1 To<BR>disappear, become invisible.<BR>--2 To<BR>take, accept.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुह्
स्नुह् {c4c} P. (स्नुह्यति, स्नुग्ध or स्नूढ)<BR>To vomit.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुह्
स्नुह्, स्नुहा --हिः f.<BR>--ही The<BR>milkhedge plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुहा
स्नुह्, स्नुहा --हिः f.<BR>--ही The<BR>milkhedge plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नुहिः|स्नुहि
स्नुह्, स्नुहा --हिः f.<BR>--ही The<BR>milkhedge plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहः|स्नेह
स्नेहः [स्निह्-घञ्]<BR>1 Affection,<BR>love, kindness, tenderness;<BR>स्नेहदाक्षिण्ययोर्योगात् कामीव प्रतिभाति मे<BR>V. 2. 4 (where it has sense 6 also);<BR>अस्ति मे सोदरस्नेहोप्येतेषु Ś. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Oiliness, viscidity, unctuousness,<BR>lubricity (one of the 24 Guṇas<BR>according to the Vaiśeṣikas).<BR>--3 Moisture.<BR>--4 Grease, fat, any unctuous<BR>substance.<BR>--5 Oil; निर्विष्टविषयस्नेहः स<BR>दशांतमुपेयिवान् R. 12. 1, Pt. 1. 82<BR>(where the word has sense 1 also),<BR>221; R. 4. 75.<BR>--6 Any fluid of<BR>the body, such as semen.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्त a. oiled, lubricated, greased<BR>--अनुवृत्तिः f. affectionate or<BR>friendly intercourse.<BR>--आशः a lamp.<BR>--छेदः, --भंगः breach or loss of<BR>friendship.<BR>--पूर्वं ind.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">Page1152-b+ 56</a>]<BR>affectionately.<BR>--प्रवृत्तिः f. flow or course of<BR>love; Ś. 4. 16.<BR>--प्रिय a. fond of<BR>oil.<BR>--(यः) a lamp.<BR>--बीजः the<BR>Piyāla tree.<BR>--भूः phlegm.<BR>--भूमिः<BR>f. {1} anything yielding oil. {2}<BR>an object of love or affection,<BR>beloved person.<BR>--रंगः sesamum^1.<BR>--वस्तिः f. injection of oil, an oily<BR>enema.<BR>--विमर्दित a. anointed with<BR>oil.<BR>--व्यक्तिः f. manifestation of<BR>love, display of friendship; (भवति)<BR>स्नेहव्यक्तिश्चिरविरहजं मुंचतो बाष्पमुष्णं<BR>Me. 12.<BR>--संभाषः kind<BR>conversation, friendly talk, chat.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन्
स्नेहन् m.<BR>1 A friend.<BR>--2 The moon.<BR>--3 A kind of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहन|स्नेहनं
स्नेहन a. [स्निह्-णिच् ल्यु ल्युट् वा]<BR>1<BR>Anointing, lubricating.<BR>--2 Destroying.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Anointing, unction, rubbing<BR>or smearing with oil or unguents.<BR>--2 Unctuousness.<BR>--3 An unguent,<BR>emollient.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहित|स्नेहितः
स्नेहित p. p.<BR>1 Loved.<BR>--2 Kind,<BR>affectionate.<BR>--3 Anointed,<BR>lubricated.<BR>--तः A friend, a beloved<BR>person.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहिन्
स्नेहिन् a. (नी f.) [स्नेह-णिनि]<BR>1<BR>Attached, affectionate, friendly.<BR>--2<BR>Oily, unctuous, fat. --m.<BR>1 A<BR>friend.<BR>--2 An anointer, a smearer.<BR>--3 A painter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नेहुः|स्नेहु
स्नेहुः<BR>1 The moon.<BR>--2 A kind<BR>of disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नै
स्नै {c1c} P. (स्नायति) To dress, wrap<BR>round; envelop.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्नैग्ध्यं|स्नैग्ध्य
स्नैग्ध्यं<BR>1 Unctuousness, oiliness,<BR>lubricity.<BR>--2 Tenderness, fondness.<BR>--3 Smoothness, blandness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पंद्|स्पन्द्
स्पंद् {c1c} A. (स्पंदते, स्पंदित)<BR>1 To<BR>throb, palpitate; अस्पंदिष्टाक्षि वामं च<BR>Bk. 15. 27, 14. 83.<BR>--2 To shake,<BR>tremble, quiver.<BR>--3 To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पंदः|स्पन्द|स्पंद|स्पन्दः
स्पंदः [स्पंद्-घञ्]<BR>1 Throbbing,<BR>palpitation.<BR>--2 Vibration, tremor,<BR>motion; मनो मंदस्पंदं बहिरपि चिरस्यापि<BR>विमृशन् Bh. 3. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पंदनं|स्पन्दन|स्पंदन|स्पन्दनं
स्पंदनं [स्पंद्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Throbbing,<BR>pulsation, palpitation, quivering;<BR>वामाक्षिस्पंदनं सूचयित्वा Māl. 1.; so<BR>अधर, ˚बाहु˚, शरीर˚ &c.<BR>--2 Tremor,<BR>vibration.<BR>--3 The quickening of a<BR>child in the womb.<BR>--4 Rapid<BR>motion, going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पंदित|स्पन्दित
स्पंदित p. p. [स्पंद्-क्त]<BR>1 Throbbed,<BR>quivered.<BR>--2 Gone.<BR>--तं A<BR>pulsation, throb, palpitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ध्
स्पर्ध् {c1c} A. (स्पर्धते)<BR>1 To contend<BR>or vie with, emulate, rival,<BR>compete, be equal with; अस्पर्धिष्ट च<BR>रामेण Bk. 15. 65; कस्तैस्सह स्पर्धते<BR>Bh. 2. 16.<BR>--2 To challenge, defy,<BR>bid defiance to.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ध
स्पर्ध a. Emulous, envious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धनं|स्पर्धन
स्पर्धनं<BR>1 Competition, emulation.<BR>--2 Envy, jealousy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धा
स्पर्धा [स्पर्ध्-अ]<BR>1 Emulation,<BR>rivalry, competition; आत्मनस्तु बुधैः<BR>स्पर्धां शुद्धधीर्बह्वमन्यत.<BR>--2 Jealousy,<BR>envy.<BR>--3 Defiance.<BR>--4 Equality<BR>with.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्धिन्
स्पर्धिन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Rivalling,<BR>emulating, competing, vying with;<BR>तवाधरस्पर्धिषु विद्रुमेषु R. 13. 13,<BR>16. 62.<BR>--2 Emulous, envious.<BR>--3<BR>Proud. --m. A competitor, an<BR>equal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्श्
स्पर्श् {c10c} A. (स्पर्शयते)<BR>1 To take,<BR>take hold of, touch.<BR>--2 To unite,<BR>join.<BR>--3 To embrace, clasp.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शः|स्पर्श
स्पर्शः<BR>1 [स्पर्श्, स्पृश् वा-घञ्]<BR>Touch, contact (in all senses);<BR>तदिदं स्पर्शक्षमं रत्नं Ś. 1. 28,<BR>2. 7.<BR>--2 Contact (in astr).<BR>--3<BR>Conflict, encounter.<BR>--4 Feeling.<BR>sensation, the sense of touch.<BR>--5<BR>The quality of touch or tangibility,<BR>touch, the object or विषय of skin<BR>(त्वच्); स्पर्श गुणो वायुः T. S.<BR>--6<BR>That which affects or influences,<BR>affection, seizure.<BR>--7 Disease,<BR>illness, disorder, distemper.<BR>--8 A<BR>consonant of any of the five classes<BR>of letters (from क् to म्); कादयो<BR>मांताः स्पर्शाः.<BR>--9 A gift, donation,<BR>presentation.<BR>--10 Air, wind.<BR>--11<BR>The sky.<BR>--12 Sexual union.<BR>--13 A secret spy.<BR>--र्शा An unchaste<BR>woman.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अज्ञ a. senseless,<BR>insensible.<BR>--इंद्रियं the organ or<BR>sense of touch.<BR>--उदय a. followed<BR>by a consonant.<BR>--उपलः, --मणिः a<BR>kind of jewel considered to be the<BR>same as ‘philosopher's stone’.<BR>--तन्मात्रं the subtile element of<BR>tangibility.<BR>--लज्जा the sensitive<BR>plant.<BR>--वेद्य a. to be apprehended<BR>by the sense of touch.<BR>--संचारिन् a.<BR>contagious, infectious.<BR>--स्नानं<BR>ablution at the entrance of the sun or<BR>moon into an eclipse.<BR>--स्पंदः, --स्यंदः<BR>a frog.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शन|स्पर्शनं|स्पर्शनः
स्पर्शन a. (नी f.) [स्पर्श्-स्पृश्-वा<BR>ल्युट्]<BR>1 Touching, handling.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">Page1153-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Affecting, influencing.<BR>--नः Air,<BR>wind.<BR>--नं<BR>1 Touching, touch,<BR>contact.<BR>--2 Sensation, feeling.<BR>--3<BR>Sense or organ of touch.<BR>--4 A gift,<BR>donation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1152-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शनकं|स्पर्शनक
स्पर्शनकं A term used in Sāṃkhya<BR>philosophy for the ‘skin.’<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्शवत्|स्पर्शवन्त्
स्पर्शवत् a.<BR>1 Tangible.<BR>--2 Soft,<BR>soft or agreeable to the touch;<BR>Ku. 1. 55.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्टृ
स्पर्ष्टृ m. A distemper, disorder of<BR>the body, disease.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पर्ष्
स्पर्ष् {c1c} A. (स्पर्षते) To become<BR>wet or moist.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पश्
स्पश् {c1c} U. (स्पशति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>obstruct.<BR>--2 To undertake, perform<BR>--3 To string together.<BR>--4 To touch.<BR>--5 To see, behold, perceive clearly,<BR>spy out, espy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पशः|स्पश
स्पशः [स्पश्-अच्]<BR>1 A spy, a<BR>secret emissary or agent; स्पशे<BR>शनैर्गतवति तत्र विद्विषां Śi. 17. 20; see<BR>अपस्पश also.<BR>--2 Fight, war battle.<BR>--3<BR>One who fights with savage<BR>animals (for reward), or the fight<BR>itself.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्ट|स्पष्टं
स्पष्ट a. [स्पश्-क्त नि˚ इडभावः]<BR>1<BR>Distinctly visible, evident, clearly<BR>perceived, clear, plain, manifest;<BR>स्पष्टे जाते प्रत्यूषे K. ‘when it was<BR>broad day-break’; स्पष्टाकृतिः<BR>R. 18. 30; स्पष्टार्थः &c.<BR>--2 Real, true.<BR>--3<BR>Full-blown, expanded.<BR>--4 One<BR>who sees clearly.<BR>--ष्टं ind.<BR>1 Clearly,<BR>distinctly, plainly.<BR>--2 Openly,<BR>boldly. (स्पष्टीकृ means ‘to make<BR>clear or distinct, explain, elucidate.)<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. intelligible, clear.<BR>--गर्भा a woman who shows evident<BR>signs of pregnancy.<BR>--प्रतिपत्तिः f.<BR>distinct notion, clear perception.<BR>--भाषिन्, --वक्तृ a. plain-spoken,<BR>outspoken, candid.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पष्टयति
स्पष्टयति Den. P. To make clear,<BR>explain, elucidate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृ
स्पृ {c5c} P. (स्पृणोति)<BR>1 To deliver<BR>or extricate from.<BR>--2 To gratify.<BR>--3 To grant, bestow.<BR>--4 To protect.<BR>--5 To live.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्
स्पृश् {c6c} P. (स्पृशति, पस्पर्श,<BR>अस्पृक्षत्-अस्पार्क्षीत्-अस्प्राक्षीत्, स्प्रक्ष्यति-स्पर्क्ष्यति,<BR>स्पर्ष्टुंस्प्रष्टुं, स्पृष्ट)<BR>1 To touch; स्पृशन्नपि गजो<BR>हति H. 3. 14; कर्णे परं स्पृशति हंति<BR>परं समूलं Pt. 1. 304.<BR>--2 To lay the<BR>hand on, stroke gently with, touch;<BR>हस्तेन पस्पर्श तदंगमिंद्रः Ku. 3. 22.<BR>--3<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">Page1153-b+ 57</a>]<BR>To adhere or cling to, come in<BR>contact with.<BR>--4 To wash or sprinkle<BR>with water; Ms. 2. 60.<BR>--5 To go to,<BR>reach; Ś. 2. 14; R. 3. 43.<BR>--6 To<BR>attain to, obtain, reach a particular<BR>state; महोक्षतां वत्सतरः स्पृशन्निव<BR>R. 3. 32; विनाप्यर्थैर्वीरः स्पृशति<BR>बहुमानोन्नतिपदं H. 1. 175.<BR>--7 To act upon,<BR>influence, affect, move, touch;<BR>Mu. 7. 16; Ku. 6. 95.<BR>--8 To refer or<BR>allude to.<BR>--9 To take, receive,<BR>accept (as a sacrificial offering). --Pass.<BR>To be polluted, defiled, or tainted;<BR>U. 1. 48. --Caus. (स्पर्शयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>cause to touch.<BR>--2 To give, present;<BR>गाः कोटिशः स्पर्शयता घटोध्नीः R. 2. 49.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्
स्पृश् a. (At the end of comp.)<BR>Who or what touches, touching,<BR>affecting, piercing; मर्मस्पृश्,<BR>हृदिस्पृश् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृशी
स्पृशी The prickly night-shade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृश्य
स्पृश्य a. Tangible.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्ट|स्पृष्टः
स्पृष्ट p. p. [स्पृश्-क्त]<BR>1 Touched,<BR>felt with the hand.<BR>--2 Come in<BR>contact with, touching.<BR>--3<BR>Reaching, applying or extending to;<BR>अस्पृष्टपुरुषांतरं Ku. 6. 75.<BR>--4 Affected,<BR>seized; Me. 69; अनघस्पृष्टं R. 10. 19.<BR>--5 Tainted, defiled; Ms. 8. 205.<BR>--6<BR>Formed by the complete contact of<BR>the organs of speech (the letters of<BR>the five classes); अचोऽस्पृष्टा<BR>यणस्त्वीषन्नेमस्पृष्टाः शलः स्मृताः । शेषाः स्पृष्टा हलः<BR>प्रोक्ता निबोधानुप्रदानतः Śik. 38.<BR>--ष्टं<BR>Touch.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टास्पृष्टि
स्पृष्टास्पृष्टि n., स्पृष्टास्पृष्टं Touching<BR>one another.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टिः|स्पृष्टि
स्पृष्टिः, स्पृष्टिका f. Touch, contact;<BR>तद्वयस्य अस्मच्छरीरस्पृष्टिकया शापितोसि<BR>Mk. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृष्टिका
स्पृष्टिः, स्पृष्टिका f. Touch, contact;<BR>तद्वयस्य अस्मच्छरीरस्पृष्टिकया शापितोसि<BR>Mk. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह्
स्पृह् {c10c} U. (स्पृहयति-ते) To wish,<BR>long for, desire for, yearn, envy<BR>(with dat.); स्पृहयामि खलु<BR>दुर्ललितायास्मै Ś. 7; तपःक्लेशायापि स्पृहयंती K.;<BR>न मैथिलेयः स्पृहयांबभूव भर्त्रे दिवो<BR>नाप्यलकेश्वराय R. 16. 42, Bh. 2. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहणं|स्पृहण
स्पृहणं [स्पृह्-ल्युट्] The act of<BR>desiring or wishing, longing for.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहणीय|स्पृहणीयं
स्पृहणीय a. [स्पृह्-अनीयर्] To be<BR>desired or longed for, enviable,<BR>desirable; अहो बतासि स्पृहणीयवीर्य.<BR>Ku. 3. 20; वंद्या त्वमेव जगतः स्पृहणीयसिद्धिः<BR>Māl. 10. 21; परस्परेण स्पृहणीयशोभं न<BR>चेदिदं द्वंद्वमयोजयिष्यत् R. 7. 14,<BR>Ku. 7. 66; U. 6. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहयालु|स्पृहयालुः
स्पृहयालु a. [स्पृह्-आलुच्] Disposed<BR>to be desirous or envious of,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">Page1153-c+ 56</a>]<BR>longing or eager for, covetous (with<BR>dator loc.); भोगेभ्यः स्पृहयालवो न हि वयं<BR>Bh. 3. 64; तपोवनेषु स्पृहयालुरेव<BR>R. 14. 45.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहा
स्पृहा [स्पृह्-अञ्] Desire, eager<BR>desire, ardent wish, longing, envy,<BR>covetousness; कथमन्ये करिष्यंति<BR>पुत्रेभ्यः पुत्रिणः स्पृहां Ve. 3. 29, R. 8. 34.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृहालु
स्पृहालु = स्पृहयालु q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पृह्य|स्पृह्यः
स्पृह्य a. Desirable, enviable.<BR>--ह्यः<BR>The wild citron tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्पॄ
स्पॄ {c9c} P. (स्पृणाति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्प्रष्टृ
स्प्रष्टृ m. See स्पर्ष्टृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फट्
स्फट् {c1c} P. (स्फटति) To burst,<BR>expand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटः|स्फट
स्फटः A snake's expanded hood;<BR>cf. फट-टा.<BR>--टी Alum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटा
स्फटा<BR>1 A snake's expanded hood.<BR>--2 Alum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकः|स्फटिक
स्फटिकः A crystal, quartz;<BR>अपगतनले हि मनसि स्फटिकप्तणाविच<BR>रजनिकरगभस्तयः सुखं<BR>प्रविशंत्युपदेशगुणाः K.<BR>--का Sulphate of<BR>alumina or alum.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अचलः the mount Meru.<BR>--अद्रिः the<BR>mount Kailāsa. ˚भिद् m. camphor.<BR>--अभ्रः camphor.<BR>--अश्मन्, --आत्मन्,<BR>--मणि m.,<BR>--शिला a crystal stone.<BR>--प्रभ a. crystalline, transparent.<BR>--स्कंभः a crystal column.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकारिः|स्फटिकारि
स्फटिकारिः, स्फटिकारिका f.<BR>Sulphate of alumina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकारिका
स्फटिकारिः, स्फटिकारिका f.<BR>Sulphate of alumina.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फटिकी
स्फटिकी Alum.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फंट्|स्फण्ट्
स्फंट् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (स्फंटति) To burst,<BR>open, expand. {vII.v} {c10c} U. (<BR>स्फंटयति-ते) To jest or joke with, laugh at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फंड्|स्फण्ड्
स्फंड् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (स्फंडति, स्फंड<BR>यति-ते) To laugh at, joke with,<BR>deride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फर्
स्फर् See स्फुर्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फरणं|स्फरण
स्फरणं Trembling, quivering,<BR>throbbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाल्
स्फाल् {c1c} P. (स्फलति) To tremble<BR>quiver, throb, palpitate. --{c10c} U. or<BR>Caus. (स्फालयति-ते) To cause to tremble<BR>or shake.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटकः|स्फाटक|स्फाटकं
स्फाटकः A drop of water.<BR>--कं<BR>Crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटिक|स्फाटिकं
स्फाटिक a. (की f.) Crystalline.<BR>--कं A crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटीकं|स्फाटीक
स्फाटीकं Crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाटित
स्फाटित p. p. Split open, burst,<BR>expanded, made to gape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फाय्
स्फाय् {c1c} A. (स्फायते, स्फीत)<BR>1 To<BR>grow large or fat, to become big or<BR>bulky.<BR>--2 To swell, increase,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">Page1154-a+ 56</a>]<BR>expand; संदुधुक्षे तयोः कोपः पस्फाये<BR>शस्त्रलाघवं Bk. 14. 109. --Caus. (<BR>स्फावयति-ते) To cause to grow large,<BR>augment, increase; तावस्फावयतां<BR>शक्तीर्बाणांश्चाकिरतां मुहुः Bk. 17. 43,<BR>4. 33, 12. 76, 15. 99.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1153-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फात|स्फातः
स्फात p. p. Increased, enlarged,<BR>swollen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फातिः|स्फाति
स्फातिः f. [स्फाय्-भावे क्तिन् यलोपः]<BR>1<BR>Swelling, intumescence.<BR>--2 Increase,<BR>growth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीत|स्फीतः
स्फीत p. p. [स्फाय्-क्त स्फीभावः]<BR>1<BR>Swollen, increased; Ve. 5. 40.<BR>--2<BR>Fat, thick, big, large, bulky.<BR>--3<BR>Many, numerous, much, copious,<BR>plentiful, abundant.<BR>--4 Delighted,<BR>joyful.<BR>--5 Pure; Bv. 4. 13.<BR>--6<BR>Successful, prosperous, thriving.<BR>--7<BR>Affected by hereditary disease. (<BR>स्फीतीकृ means ‘to augment or<BR>enlarge’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फीतिः|स्फीति
स्फीतिः f.<BR>1 Growth, increase,<BR>enlargement.<BR>--2 Abundance,<BR>copiousness, plenty; धनधान्यस्य च<BR>स्फीतिः सदा मे वर्ततां गृहे.<BR>--3 Prosperity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फार|स्फारं|स्फारः
स्फार a. [स्फाय्-रक् Uṇ. 2. 13]<BR>1<BR>Large, great, increased, expanded;<BR>स्फारफुल्लत्फणापीठनिर्यत् &c.<BR>Māl. 5. 23, Mv. 6. 32.<BR>--2 Much, abundant;<BR>Mv. 5. 2; Bh. 3. 42.<BR>--3 Loud.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Swelling, increase,<BR>enlargement, growth.<BR>--2 A bubble (in<BR>gold).<BR>--3 A protuberance.<BR>--4<BR>Throbbing, quivering, palpitation,<BR>vibration.<BR>--5 Twanging.<BR>--रं Abundance,<BR>much, plenty. (स्फारीभू {1} to swell<BR>out, expand, spread out, increase,<BR>multiply; सुस्निग्धा विमुखीभवंति<BR>सुहृदः स्फारीभवंत्यापदः Mk. 1. 36;<BR>Pt. 5. 24. {2} to become manifest.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फारणं|स्फारण
स्फारणं Throbbing, shaking,<BR>trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फालः|स्फाल
स्फालः [स्फल्-घञ्] Throbbing,<BR>palpitation, beat, trembling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फालनं|स्फालन
स्फालनं<BR>1 Quivering, palpitating.<BR>--2 Causing to shake about or<BR>move.<BR>--3 Rubbing, friction;<BR>Ś. 2. 4.<BR>--4 Patting or stroking (as<BR>a horse), gentle rubbing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिच्
स्फिच् f. Buttocks, hips;<BR>अंसस्फिक्पृष्ठपिंडाद्यवयवसुलभान्युग्रपूतीनि<BR>जग्ध्वा Māl. 5. 16.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट्
स्फिट् {c10c} U. (स्फटेयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>hurt, injure, kill.<BR>--2 To despise.<BR>--3 To love.<BR>--4 To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिट्ट्
स्फिट्ट् {c10c} U. (स्फिट्टयति-ते) To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-b" target="_blank">Page1154-b+ 56</a>]<BR>hurt &c.; see स्फिट् above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फिर|स्फिरं
स्फिर a. (compar. स्फेयस्, superl.<BR>स्फेष्ठ)<BR>1 Abundant, much, large.<BR>--2<BR>Many, numerous.<BR>--3 Vast,<BR>capacious.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट्
स्फुट् {vI.v} {c6c} P., {c1c} U. (स्फुटीत,<BR>स्फोटति-ते, स्फुटित)<BR>1 To burst or split<BR>open, break forth, be suddenly<BR>rent asunder, cleave, split, break;<BR>हाहा देवि स्फुटति हृदयं स्रंसते देहबंधः<BR>U. 3. 38; स्फुटति न सा<BR>मनासिजविशिखेन Gīt. 7; Bk. 14. 56, 15. 77.<BR>--2 To expand, open, blow, blossom;<BR>स्फुटति कुसुमनिकरे विरहिहृदयदलनाय<BR>Gīt. 5; Pt. 1. 136, Kāv. 3. 167.<BR>--3<BR>To run or bound away, disperse;<BR>तुंरगाः पुस्फुटुर्सीताः Bk. 14. 6, 10. 8.<BR>--4 To become visible, burst into<BR>view, become evident or manifest.<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} U. (स्फुटयति-ते)<BR>1 To burst,<BR>crack, break open.<BR>--2 To burst into<BR>view. --Caus. (स्फोटयति-ते)<BR>1 To<BR>burst or rend asunder, split, tear<BR>open, cleave, divide.<BR>--2 To<BR>manifest, show, make clear.<BR>--3 To<BR>disclose, divulge, make public.<BR>--4<BR>To hurt, destroy, kill.<BR>--5 To<BR>winnow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट|स्फुटः
स्फुट a. [स्फुट्-क]<BR>1 Burst, rent<BR>asunder, broken, split.<BR>--2 Opened,<BR>expanded, full-blown;<BR>स्फुटपरागपरागतपंकजं Śi. 6. 2, 5.<BR>--3<BR>Manifested, displayed, made clear.<BR>--4 Clear,<BR>plain, distinctly visible or<BR>manifest; अत्र स्फुटो न कश्चिदलंकारः<BR>K. P. 1; Ku. 5. 44; Me. 70; Ki. 11. 44.<BR>--5 Bursting into view; कदंबयष्टिः<BR>स्फुटकोरकेव U. 3. 42.<BR>--6 White,<BR>bright, pure; मुक्ताफलं वा<BR>स्फुटविद्रुमस्थं Ku. 1. 44.<BR>--7 Well-known,<BR>famous; स्फुटनृत्यलीलमभवत्सुतनोः<BR>Śi. 9. 79 (= प्रथित).<BR>--8 Spread, diffused.<BR>--9 Loud.<BR>--10 Apparent, true.<BR>--11<BR>Corrected.<BR>--टा The expanded<BR>hood of a snake.<BR>--टं ind. Clearly,<BR>evidently, distinctly, certainly,<BR>manifestly.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्थ a. {1}<BR>intelligible, obvious. {2} significant.<BR>--तार a. bright or gemmed with<BR>stars.<BR>--फलं (in geom.) {1}<BR>distinct or precise area of a triangle.<BR>{2} the clear or net result of any<BR>calculation.<BR>--वल्कली the heart-plant.<BR>--सारः the true latitude of a star<BR>or planet (?).<BR>--सूर्यगतिः f. the<BR>apparent or true motion of the sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटनं|स्फुटन
स्फुटनं [स्फुट्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Breaking<BR>open, rending, bursting forth,<BR>tearing open.<BR>--2 Expanding, opening,<BR>blossoming.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटिः|स्फुटि
स्फुटिः --टी f. Cracking of the skin<BR>of the feet, sores or swelling of the<BR>feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटी
स्फुटिः --टी f. Cracking of the skin<BR>of the feet, sores or swelling of the<BR>feet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटिका
स्फुटिका A small bit broken off,<BR>a slice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुटित|स्फुटितः
स्फुटित p. p. [स्फुट्-क्त]<BR>1 Burst,<BR>broken open, split, cracked;<BR>Māl. 9. 31.<BR>--2 Budded, blown,<BR>expanded (as a flower); U. 3. 24.<BR>--3<BR>Made clear, manifested, shown.<BR>--4<BR>Torn, destroyed.<BR>--5 Laughed at,<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चरण a. having wide feet.<BR>splay-footed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुट्ट्
स्फुट्ट् {c10c} U. (स्फुट्टयति-ते) To<BR>despise, slight, disrespect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुड्
स्फुड् {c6c} P. (स्फुडति) To cover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुंट्|स्फुण्ट्
स्फुंट् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (स्फुंटति) To open,<BR>expand. {vII.v} {c10c} U. (स्फुंटयति-ते)<BR>To jest, joke, laugh at.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुंड्|स्फुण्ड्
स्फुंड् {c1c} A., {c10c} U. (स्फुंडते,<BR>स्फुंडयति-ते) See स्फुंट्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुत्
स्फुत् ind. An imitative sound.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--करः fire.<BR>--कारः the sound<BR>स्फुत्, a crackling noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्
स्फुर् {c6c} P. (स्फुरति, स्फुरित)<BR>1 (a)<BR>To throb, palpitate (as eyes &c.);<BR>शांतमिदमाश्रमपदं स्फुरति च बाहुः कुतः<BR>फलमिहास्य Ś. 1. 16; स्फुरता<BR>वामकेनापि दाक्षिण्यमवलंब्यते Māl. 1. 8;<BR>अभिमतफलशंसी चारु पुस्फोर वाहुः<BR>Bk. 1. 27 (b) To shake, tremble, quiver,<BR>vibrate in general;<BR>स्फुरदधरनासापुटतया U. 1. 29, 6. 33.<BR>--2 To twitch,<BR>struggle, become agitated; हतं<BR>पृथिव्यां करुणं स्फुरंतं Rām.<BR>--3 To start,<BR>dart, spring forward; पुस्फुरुर्वृषभाः<BR>परं Bk. 14. 6.<BR>--4 To spring back,<BR>rebound (as a bow.)<BR>--5 To spring<BR>or break forth, shoot out, spring up,<BR>rise forth; धर्मतःस्फुरति निर्मलं यशः;<BR>Ku. 3. 68.<BR>--6 To start into view,<BR>become visible or manifest, appear<BR>clearly, become displayed;<BR>मुखात्स्फुरंतीं को हर्तुमिच्छति हरेः परिभूय दंष्ट्रां<BR>Mu. 1. 8; रचितरुचिरभूषां ट्टष्टिमोषे प्रदोषे<BR>स्फुरति निरवसादां कापि राधां जगाद<BR>Gīt. 11.<BR>--7 To flash, scintillate, sparkle,<BR>glitter, gleam, shine; स्फुरतु<BR>कुचकुंभयोरुपरि मणिमंजरी रंजयेतु तव हृदयश<BR>Gīt. 10; (तया) स्फुरत्प्रभामंडलया च,<BR>काशे Ku. 1. 24, R. 3. 60, 5. 51.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">Page1155-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Me. 15, 27.<BR>--8 To shine, distinguish<BR>oneself, become eminent;<BR>Pt. 1. 27.<BR>--9 To flash on the mind, rush<BR>suddenly into memory.<BR>--10 To go<BR>tremulously.<BR>--11 To bruise,<BR>destroy. --Caus. (स्फारयति-ते,<BR>स्फोरयति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to throb or vibrate.<BR>--2 To cause to shine, irradiate.<BR>--3 To throw, cast. --WITH अप to<BR>shine forth or out.<BR>--अभि {1} to<BR>spread or be diffused, expand. {2}<BR>to become known.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1154-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरः|स्फुर
स्फुरः [स्फुर् भावे घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Throbbing, trembling, quivering.<BR>--2<BR>Swelling.<BR>--3 A shield.<BR>--4<BR>Coruscating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरणं|स्फुरण
स्फुरणं [स्फुर्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Throbbing,<BR>quivering, trembling (in general).<BR>--2 Throbbing or quivering of<BR>certain parts of the body (indicating<BR>good or bad luck).<BR>--3 Breaking<BR>forth, arising, starting into view.<BR>--4<BR>Gleaming, flashing, glittering,<BR>shining, twinkling.<BR>--5 Flashing on<BR>the mind, crossing the memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरत्
स्फुरत् a. Throbbing, shining &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उल्का a shooting meteor<BR>aerolite.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुरित|स्फुरितं
स्फुरित p. p.<BR>1 Trembling,<BR>throbbing.<BR>--2 Shaken.<BR>--3 Glittering,<BR>shining.<BR>--4 Unsteady.<BR>--5 Swollen.<BR>--6 Manifested, displayed;<BR>Māl. 2. 10.<BR>--तं<BR>1 A throb, palpitation,<BR>tremor.<BR>--2 Agitation or emotion of<BR>the mind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्च्छ्
स्फुर्च्छ् {c1c} P. (स्फूर्च्छति)<BR>1 To<BR>spread, extend.<BR>--2 To forget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्ज्
स्फुर्ज् {c1c} P. (स्फूर्जति)<BR>1 To<BR>thunder, make a sound like<BR>thunderclap, crash, explode; Bk. 15. 44.<BR>--2 To glitter, shine.<BR>--3 To burst<BR>or break forth; स्फूर्जत्येव स एष संप्रति<BR>मम न्यक्कारभिन्नस्थितेः Mv. 3. 40.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुर्जथुः|स्फुर्जथु|स्फुर्ज्जथु
स्फुर्जथुः = स्फूर्जथु below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्जः|स्फूर्ज|स्फूर्ज्ज
स्फूर्जः<BR>1 The crashing sound of a<BR>thunder-clap.<BR>--2 Indra's<BR>thunderbolt.<BR>--3 Sudden burst or rise, as in<BR>नर्मस्फूर्ज.<BR>--4 First union of lovers<BR>characterized by joy in the<BR>beginning and some expectation of fear<BR>in the end.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्जथुः|स्फूर्जथु|स्फूर्ज्जथु
स्फूर्जथुः A clap or peal of<BR>thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्जनं|स्फूर्जन|स्फूर्ज्जन
स्फूर्जनं<BR>1 The act of thundering.<BR>--2 An explosion or crash.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुल्
स्फुल् {c6c} P. (स्फुलति)<BR>1 To<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">Page1155-b+ 57</a>]<BR>tremble, throb, vibrate.<BR>--2 To dart<BR>forth, appear.<BR>--3 To collect.<BR>--4 To<BR>kill, destroy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलं|स्फुल
स्फुलं A tent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलनं|स्फुलन
स्फुलनं Trembling, throbbing,<BR>palpitation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिंगः|स्फुलिङ्ग|स्फुलिंग|स्फुलिंगं|स्फुलिङ्गः
स्फुलिंगः, --गं, स्फुलिंगा A spark<BR>of fire; स्फुलिंगावस्थया वह्निरेधापेक्ष<BR>इव स्थितः Ś. 7. 15, Ve. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिंगं|स्फुलिङ्ग|स्फुलिंग|स्फुलिंगः|स्फुलिङ्गः
स्फुलिंगः, --गं, स्फुलिंगा A spark<BR>of fire; स्फुलिंगावस्थया वह्निरेधापेक्ष<BR>इव स्थितः Ś. 7. 15, Ve. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिंगा
स्फुलिंगः, --गं, स्फुलिंगा A spark<BR>of fire; स्फुलिंगावस्थया वह्निरेधापेक्ष<BR>इव स्थितः Ś. 7. 15, Ve. 6. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फुलिंगिनी|स्फुलिङ्गिनी
स्फुलिंगिनी One of the seven<BR>tongues of fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्तिः|स्फूर्ति|स्फूर्त्ति|स्फूर्त्तिः
स्फूर्तिः f. [स्फुर्च्छ् --स्फुर् क क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>Throbbing, shaking, vibration.<BR>--2<BR>Spring, bound.<BR>--3 Blooming,<BR>opening.<BR>--4 Manifestation, display.<BR>--5<BR>Flashing on the mind.<BR>--6 Poetical<BR>inspiration.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फूर्तिमत्|स्फूर्तिमन्त्|स्फूर्त्तिमत्
स्फूर्तिमत् a.<BR>1 Throbbing, tremulous,<BR>agitated.<BR>--2 Tender-hearted. --m.<BR>A follower or worshipper of Śiva<BR>(पाशुपत).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेयस्
स्फेयस् a. More abundant, larger<BR>(compar. of स्फिर q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फेष्ठ|स्फेष्ठः
स्फेष्ठ a. Most abundant, largest<BR>(superl. of स्फिर q. v.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटः|स्फोट
स्फोटः [स्फुट् करणे घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Breaking forth, splitting open, bursting.<BR>--2 Disclosure; as in नर्मस्फोट.<BR>--3 A<BR>swelling, boil, tumour; अयमपरो<BR>गंडस्योपरि स्फोटः Mu. 5.<BR>--4 The idea<BR>which bursts out or flashes on the<BR>mind when a sound is<BR>uttered, the impression produced on<BR>the mind at hearing a sound;<BR>बुधैर्वैयाकरणैः<BR>प्रधानभूतस्फोटरूपव्यंग्यव्यंजकस्य शब्दस्य ध्वनिरिति व्यवहारः<BR>कृतः K. P. 1, also see Sarva. S.<BR>(पाणिनीयदर्शन).<BR>--5 The eternal sound<BR>recognised by the Mīmāṃsakas.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--बीजकः the marking-nut<BR>plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटकः|स्फोटक
स्फोटकः A swelling, boil, tumour,<BR>pimple.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटन|स्फोटनं|स्फोटनः
स्फोटन a. (नी f.) [स्फुट् --ल्युट्]<BR>Breaking asunder, manifesting,<BR>disclosing, making clear.<BR>--नः<BR>Separated utterance of a close<BR>combination of consonants.<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Rending, suddenly bursting, splitting,<BR>cracking.<BR>--2 Winnowing grain.<BR>--3<BR>Cracking the finger-joints,<BR>snapping the fingers.<BR>--4 The<BR>separation of a double consonant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटनी
स्फोटनी The boring tool, an<BR>auger, a gimlet.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटा
स्फोटा The expanded hood of a<BR>serpent.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोटिका
स्फोटिका A kind of bird.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फोरणं|स्फोरण
स्फोरणं See स्फुरणं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्फ्यं|स्फ्य
स्फ्यं A sword-shaped implement<BR>used in sacrifices; Ms. 5. 117;<BR>Y. 1. 184.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वर्तनिः the<BR>furrow made by this implement.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्बृ
स्बृ See स्वृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्म
स्म ind.<BR>1 A particle added to<BR>the present tense of verbs (or to<BR>present participles) and giving<BR>them the sense of the past tense;<BR>भासुरको नाम सिंहः प्रतिवसति स्म Pt. 1;<BR>क्रीणंति स्म प्राणमूल्यैर्यशांसि Śi. 18. 15.<BR>--2 A pleonastic particle (generally<BR>added to the prohibitive particle<BR>मा q. v.); भर्तुर्विप्रकृतापि रोषणतया<BR>मास्म प्रतीपं गमः Ś. 4. 17; मास्म<BR>सीमंतिनी काचिज्जतयेत्पुत्रमीदृशं H. 2. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरः|स्मर
स्मरः [स्मृ-भावे अप्]<BR>1<BR>Recollection, remembrance.<BR>--2 Love.<BR>--3 Cupid, the god of love; स्मर<BR>पर्युत्सुक एष माधवः Ku. 4. 28, 42, 43.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंकुशः {1} a fingernail.<BR>{2} a lover, lascivious person.<BR>--अगारं, --कूपकः, --गृहं, --मंदिरं the<BR>female organ.<BR>--अंध a. blinded by love,<BR>infatuated with passion.<BR>--आकुल,<BR>--आतुर, --आर्त, --उत्सुक, a. pining with<BR>love, love-sick, smit with love.<BR>--आसवः saliva.<BR>--कर्मन् n. any<BR>amorous action, a wanton act.<BR>--गुरुः an epithet of Viṣṇu.<BR>--छत्रं<BR>the clitoris.<BR>--दशा a state of love,<BR>state of the body produced by<BR>being in love (these are ten).<BR>--ध्वजः<BR>{1} the male organ. {2} a fabulous<BR>fish. {3} N. of a musical instrument.<BR>--(जं) the female organ.<BR>--(जा) a<BR>bright moon-light night.<BR>--प्रिया an<BR>epithet of Rati.<BR>--भासित a.<BR>inflamed by love.<BR>--मोहः infatuation of<BR>love, passion.<BR>--लेखनी the Sārikā<BR>bird.<BR>--वल्लभः {1} an epithet of<BR>Spring. {2} of Aniruddha.<BR>--वीथिका a prostitute, harlot.<BR>--शासनः an<BR>epithet of Śiva.<BR>--सखः the moon.<BR>--स्तंभः the male organ.<BR>--स्मर्यः a<BR>donkey, an ass.<BR>--हरः an epithet of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मरणं|स्मरण
स्मरणं [स्मृ-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Remembering,<BR>remembrance, recollection; केवलं<BR>स्मरणेनैव पुनासि पुरुषं यतः R. 10. 29.<BR>--2 Thinking of or about; यदि<BR>हरिस्मरणे सरसं मनः Gīt. 1.<BR>--3 Memory.<BR>--4 Tradition, traditional precept;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-a" target="_blank">Page1156-a+ 56</a>]<BR>इति भृगुस्मरणात् (opp. श्रुति).<BR>--5<BR>Mental recitation of the name of a<BR>deity.<BR>--6 Remembering with regret,<BR>regretting.<BR>--7 Rhetorical recollection,<BR>regarded as a figure of speech; thus<BR>defined: --यथानुभवमर्थस्य दृष्टे तत्सदृशे<BR>स्मृतिः स्मरणं K. P. 10.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अनुग्रहः {1} a kind remembrance. {2}<BR>the favour of remembrance;<BR>Ku. 6. 19.<BR>--अपत्यतर्पकः a turtle,<BR>tortoise.<BR>--अयौगपद्यं the<BR>non-simultaneousness of recollections.<BR>--पदवी death.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1155-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार
स्मार a. Relating to Smara or the<BR>god of love; स्मारं पुष्पमयं चापं वाणाः<BR>पुष्पमया अपि । तथाप्यनंगस्त्रैलोक्यं<BR>करोति वशमात्मनः ॥.<BR>--रं Recollection,<BR>memory.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारक
स्मारक a. (रिका f.) Reminding.<BR>--कं A memorial (a modern use).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मारणं|स्मारण
स्मारणं Calling to mind,<BR>reminding, causing to remember.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मार्त|स्मार्तः|स्मार्त्त|स्मार्त्तं|स्मार्त्तः
स्मार्त a. [स्मृतौ विहितः, स्मृतिं<BR>वेत्त्यधीते वा अण्]<BR>1 Relating to memory.<BR>remembered, memorial.<BR>--2 Being<BR>within memory.<BR>--3 Based on or<BR>recorded in a Smṛti, prescribed in<BR>a code of laws; कर्म स्मार्तविवाहाग्नौ<BR>कुर्वीत प्रत्यहं गृही Y. 1. 97; Ms. 1. 108.<BR>--4 Legal.<BR>--5 Following or<BR>professing the law-books.<BR>--6 Domestic<BR>(as fire).<BR>--र्तः<BR>1 A Brāhmaṇa<BR>well-versed in traditional law.<BR>--2<BR>One who follows the traditional<BR>law.<BR>--3 N. of a sect.<BR>--र्तं An act<BR>or rite enjoined by the Smṛti, a<BR>legal act.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मि
स्मि {c1c} A. (स्मयते, स्मित)<BR>1 To<BR>smile, laugh (gently); काकुत्स्थ<BR>ईषत्स्मयमान आस्त Bk. 2. 11, 15. 8;<BR>स्मयमानं वदनांबुजं स्मरामि Bv. 2. 27.<BR>--2 To bloom, expand; Pt. 1. 136.<BR>--Caus. (स्माययति-ते)<BR>1 To cause<BR>a smile by, cause to smile.<BR>--2 To<BR>laugh at, deride.<BR>--3 To astonish<BR>(स्मापयते in this sense). --Desid.<BR>(सिस्मयिषते) To wish to smile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मयः|स्मय
स्मयः [स्मि-अच्]<BR>1 Astonishment,<BR>wonder, surprise.<BR>--2 Arrogance,<BR>pride, haughtiness, conceit; तस्मै<BR>स्मयावेशविवर्जिताय R. 5. 19; प्रभवः<BR>स्मयदूषिताः Bh. 3. 2, 69; Mu. 2. 22.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मित|स्मितं
स्मित p. p.<BR>1 Smiled, smiling.<BR>--2<BR>Expanded, blown, blossomed;<BR>Pt. 1. 136.<BR>--तं A smile, gentle laugh;<BR>सस्मितं ‘with a smile’;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-b" target="_blank">Page1156-b+ 57</a>]<BR>सविलक्षस्मितं &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ट्टश् a. having a<BR>smiling look. (--f.) a handsome<BR>woman.<BR>--पूर्वम् ind. smilingly, with<BR>a smile; सप्तर्षिभिस्तान् स्मितपूर्वमाह<BR>Ku. 7. 47.<BR>--शालिन् a. smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मितिः|स्मिति
स्मितिः f. A smile, smiling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मिट्
स्मिट् {c10c} U. (स्मेटयति ते)<BR>1 To<BR>slight, scorn, despise.<BR>--2 To love.<BR>--3 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मील्
स्मील् {c1c} P. (स्मीलति) To wink,<BR>blink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृ
स्मृ {vI.v} {c5c} P. (स्मृणोति)<BR>1 To please,<BR>gratify.<BR>--2 To protect, defend.<BR>--3 To<BR>live. {vII.v} {c1c} P. (Atm. also in epic<BR>poetry) (स्मरति, स्मृत; pass. स्मर्यते)<BR>1 (a) To remember, bear or keep<BR>in mind, recollect, call to mind,<BR>be aware of; स्मरोस सुरसनीरां तत्र<BR>गोदावरीं वा स्मरसि च<BR>तदुपांतेष्वावयोर्वर्तनानि U. 1. 26. (b) To call to mind,<BR>call upon mentally, think of;<BR>स्मरात्मनोऽभीष्टदेवतां Pt. 1; R. 15. 45<BR>--2 To recite mentally or call upon<BR>the name of a deity &c.; यः<BR>स्मरेत्पुंडरीकाक्षं सबाह्याभ्यंतरः शुचिः.<BR>--3 To<BR>lay down or record in a Smṛti;<BR>तथा च स्मरंति.<BR>--4 To declare, regard,<BR>consider; Pt. 1. 30.<BR>--5 To<BR>remember with regret, yearn after,<BR>long or desire for (oft. with gen.);<BR>स्मर्तुं दिसंति न दिवः सुरसुंदरीभ्यः<BR>Ki. 5. 28; कच्चिद्भर्तुः स्मरसि रसिके त्वं हि तस्य<BR>प्रियेति Me. 85; Mu. 5. 14; भवत्याः<BR>स्मरतात्यर्थमर्पितः सादरं मम Bk. 8. 118.<BR>--Caus. (स्मारयति-ते, but स्मरयति-ते<BR>in the last sense)<BR>1 To cause to<BR>remember, remind, put in mind<BR>of, call to mind; अनेन<BR>मत्प्रियाभियोगेन स्मारयसि मे पूर्वशिष्यां सौदामिनीं<BR>Māl. 1; sometimes with two acc.;<BR>अपि चंद्रगुप्तदोषा अतिक्रांतपार्थिवगुणान्<BR>स्मारयंति प्रकृतीः Mu. 1; य एव<BR>दुःस्मरः कालस्तमेव स्मारिता वयं U. 6. 34.<BR>--2 To give information.<BR>--3 To<BR>cause to remember with regret,<BR>cause to long or desire for;<BR>Śi. 6. 56, 8. 64. --Desid. (सुस्मूर्षते) To<BR>wish to recollect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृत|स्मृतः
स्मृत p. p. [स्मृ-क्त]<BR>1 Remembered,<BR>recollected, called to mind.<BR>--2<BR>Regarded, laid down, recorded, mentioned;<BR>Ku. 2. 7.<BR>--3 Appointed, designed;<BR>Ś. 6. 29.<BR>--4 Enjoined by a Smṛti<BR>or traditional law.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मृतिः|स्मृति
स्मृतिः f. [स्मृ-क्तिन्]<BR>1<BR>Remembrance; recollection, memory; अ<BR>श्वत्थामा करधृतधनुः किं न यातः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-c" target="_blank">Page1156-c+ 56</a>]<BR>स्मृतिं ते Ve. 3. 21; संस्कारमात्रजन्यं ज्ञानं<BR>स्मृतिः T. S.; स्मृत्युपस्थितौ इमौ द्वौ श्लोकौ<BR>U. 6; 4. 2.<BR>--2 Thinking of, calling to<BR>mind.<BR>--3 What was delivered by<BR>human authors, law, traditional law, the<BR>body of traditional or memorial law<BR>(civil or religious) (opp. श्रुति).<BR>--4 A<BR>code of laws, law-book.<BR>--5 A text<BR>of Smṛti, canon, rule of law;<BR>इति स्मृतेः.<BR>--6 Desire, wish.<BR>--7<BR>Understanding.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंतरं another<BR>law-book.<BR>--अपेत a. {1} forgotten. {2}<BR>inconsistent with Smṛti. {3} (hence)<BR>illegal, unjust.<BR>--उक्त a.<BR>prescribed or enjoined in the codes of law,<BR>canonical.<BR>--पथः, --विषयः the object<BR>of memory; स्मृतिपथं --विषयं गम् to<BR>be dead; Bh. 3. 37, 38.<BR>--प्रत्यवमर्षः<BR>retentiveness of memory, accuracy<BR>of recollection.<BR>--प्रबंधः a legal work.<BR>--भ्रंशः loss or failure of memory.<BR>--रोधः temporary interruption of<BR>memory; loss or failure of memory;<BR>Ś. 7. 32.<BR>--विभ्रमः confusion of<BR>memory.<BR>--विरुद्ध a. illegal.<BR>--विरोधः {1} opposition to law, illegality.<BR>{2} disagreement between two or<BR>more Smṛtis or legal texts;<BR>स्मृतिविरोधं परिहरति Ś. B.<BR>--शास्त्रं {1} a<BR>lawbook, code, digest. {2} legal science.<BR>--शेष a. deceased, dead (as a<BR>person).<BR>--शैथिल्यं temporary loss of<BR>memory.<BR>--साध्य a. capable of being<BR>proved by law.<BR>--हेतुः a cause of<BR>recollection, impression on the mind,<BR>association of ideas.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्मेर|स्मेरः
स्मेर a. [स्मि-रन्]<BR>1 Smiling;<BR>विलोक्य वृद्धोक्षमधिष्ठितं त्वया महाजनः<BR>स्मेरमुखो भविष्यति Ku. 5. 70, Bv. 2. 4;<BR>3. 2; Māl. 10. 6.<BR>--2 Blown,<BR>expanded, dilated, blooming;<BR>अधिकविकसदंतर्विस्मयस्मेरतारैः Māl. 1. 28.<BR>--3 Proud.<BR>--4 Evident.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--विष्किरः a peacock.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यंद्|स्यन्द्
स्यंद्^1 {c1c} A. (स्यंदते, सस्यंदे,<BR>अस्यदत्-अस्यंत्त-अस्यंदिष्ट, स्यंत्स्यति-ते, स्यंदिष्यते,<BR>स्यंदितुं-स्यंत्तुं, स्यन्न; desid. सिस्यंदिषते,<BR>सिस्यंत्सति-ते; the स् of स्यंद् is changed to ष् after<BR>a preposition ending in इ or उ)<BR>1 To<BR>ooze, trickle, drop, drip, distil, flow;<BR>अयि दलदरविंद स्यंदमानं मरंदं तव<BR>किमपि लिहंतो मंजु गुंजंतु भृंगाः Bv. 1. 5.<BR>--2 To shed, pour forth.<BR>--3 To<BR>run, flee.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यदः|स्यद
स्यदः Speed, rapid motion, rush,<BR>velocity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1156-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यंदः|स्यन्द|स्यंद|स्यन्दः
स्यंदः [स्यंद्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Flowing,<BR>trickling.<BR>--2 Going rapidly, moving.<BR>--3 A car, chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यंदन|स्यन्दन|स्यन्दनं|स्यन्दनः
स्यंदन a. (ना or नी f.) [स्यंद्-ल्यु<BR>ल्युट् वा]<BR>1 Going quickly, fleet;<BR>flowing.<BR>--2 Quick, swift of foot, fleet;<BR>स्यंदना नो चतुरगाः Ki. 15. 16.<BR>--नः<BR>1<BR>A war-chariot, a car or chariot in<BR>general; धर्मारण्यं प्रविशति गजः<BR>स्यंदनालोकभीतः Ś. 1. 33.<BR>--2 Air, wind.<BR>--3 A kind of tree (तिनिश).<BR>--नं<BR>1<BR>Flowing, trickling, oozing.<BR>--2<BR>Rushing, going or flowing quickly.<BR>--3<BR>Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आरोहः a warrior<BR>who fights while seated in a chariot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यंदनिका|स्यन्दनिका
स्यंदनिका A drop of saliva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यंदिन्|स्यन्दिन्
स्यंदिन् a. (नी f.)<BR>1 Oozing,<BR>flowing, trickling; Māl. 8. 3; U. 1. 35,<BR>--2 Rushing.<BR>--3 Going.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यंदिनी
स्यंदिनी<BR>1 Saliva.<BR>--2 A cow<BR>bearing two calves at the same time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यन्न|स्यन्नः
स्यन्न p. p.<BR>1 Oozed, trickled,<BR>dropped.<BR>--2 Dropping, trickling (as<BR>water).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यम्
स्यम् {c1c} P., {c10c} U. (स्यमति, स्यमय,<BR>ति-ते)<BR>1 To sound, to cry aloud,<BR>shout.<BR>--2 To go.<BR>--3 To consider,<BR>reflect (Atm. only in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमंतकः|स्यमन्तक|स्यमंतक|स्यमन्तकः
स्यमंतकः A kind of valuable<BR>gem^1 (said to yield daily eight loads<BR>of gold and to preserve from all<BR>kinds of dangers and portents).<BR>(For some account, see the word<BR>सत्राजित्).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमिकः|स्यमिक
स्यमि(मी)कः [स्यम्-ईकक्]<BR>1 A<BR>cloud.<BR>--2 An ant-hill.<BR>--3 A kind of<BR>tree.<BR>--4 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमीकः|स्यमीक
स्यमि(मी)कः [स्यम्-ईकक्]<BR>1 A<BR>cloud.<BR>--2 An ant-hill.<BR>--3 A kind of<BR>tree.<BR>--4 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यमिका
स्यमिका Indigo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यात्
स्यात् ind. (Strictly 3rd. pers.<BR>sing. of the Potential of अस् ‘to be’)<BR>It may be, perhaps, per chance.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--वादः an assertion of<BR>probability (in phil.), a form of<BR>scepticism.<BR>--वादिन् m. a sceptic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यालः|स्याल
स्यालः See श्याल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूत|स्यूतः
स्यूत p. p. [सिव्-कर्मणि क्त]<BR>1 Sewn<BR>with a needle, stitched, woven (fig.<BR>also); चिंतासंततितंतुजालनिबिडस्यूतेव<BR>लग्ना प्रिया Māl. 5. 10.<BR>--2 Pierced.<BR>--3 Woven together, joined.<BR>--तः {1}<BR>A sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूतिः|स्यूति
स्यूतिः f. [सिव्-भावे क्तिन्]<BR>1 Sewing,<BR>stitching.<BR>--2 Needle-work.<BR>--3 A<BR>sack.<BR>--4 Lineage, family.<BR>--5<BR>Offspring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूनः|स्यून
स्यूनः [सिव्-नक्]<BR>1 A ray of light.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--3 A bag, sack.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योतः|स्योत
स्योतः A sack, bag.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्यूमः|स्यूम|स्यूमं
स्यूमः A ray of light (also n.).<BR>--मं<BR>1 Water.<BR>--2 Happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्योन|स्योनः
स्योन a.<BR>1 Beautiful, pleasing.<BR>--2 Auspicious, propitious.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A<BR>ray of light.<BR>--2 The sun.<BR>--3 A sack.<BR>--नं Happiness, pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंस्
स्रंस् {c1c} A. (स्रंसते, स्रस्त)<BR>1 To fall<BR>fall or drop down, slip off or<BR>down; नास्रसत्करिणां ग्रैवं<BR>त्रिपदीच्छेदिनामपि R. 4. 48; गांडीवं स्रंसते हस्तात्<BR>Bg. 1. 30; Bk. 14. 72, 15. 61.<BR>--2<BR>To sink, drop, fall asunder; हाहा<BR>देवि स्फुटति हृदयं स्रंसते देहबंधः<BR>U. 3. 38; Māl. 9. 20 v. l.<BR>--3 To hang<BR>down,<BR>--4 To go.<BR>--5 To be pleased.<BR>--Caus. (स्रंसयति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to<BR>fall or slip down, move, disturb;<BR>वातोपि नास्रंसयदंशुकानि R. 6. 75.<BR>--2<BR>To relax, loosen, slacken; Māl. 3. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसः|स्रंस
स्रंसः Falling, sleeping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसनं|स्रंसन
स्रंसनं [स्रंस्-णिच् ल्युट्]<BR>1 Falling.<BR>--2 Causing to fall, or bringing<BR>down.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंसिन्
स्रंसिन् a. (नी f.) [स्रंस्-णिनि]<BR>1<BR>Falling or slipping down,<BR>hanging down, being loosened, giving<BR>way; बंधे स्रंसिनि चैकहस्तयमिताः<BR>पर्याकुला मूर्धजाः Ś. 1. 30.<BR>--2 Depending,<BR>pendulous, hanging loosely.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्त|स्रस्तं
स्रस्त p. p. [स्रंस्-क्त]<BR>1 Fallen or<BR>dropped down, slipped off, fallen<BR>off; स्रस्तं शरं चापमपि स्वहस्तात्<BR>Ku. 3. 51; कनकवलयं स्रस्तं स्रस्तं मया<BR>प्रतिसार्यते Ś. 3. 13; Ki. 5. 33, Me. 63.<BR>--2<BR>Drooping, hanging loosely down;<BR>विषादस्रस्तसर्वांगी Mk. 4. 8;<BR>स्रस्तांसावतिमात्रलोहिततलौ बाहू घटोत्क्षेपणात्<BR>Ś. 1. 30.<BR>--3 Loosed.<BR>--4 Let go,<BR>relaxed.<BR>--5 Pendulous, hanging down.<BR>--6 Separated.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. {1}<BR>having the limbs relaxed. {2}<BR>swooning, fainting.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तिः|स्रस्ति
स्रस्तिः f.<BR>1 Falling, slipping.<BR>--2 A<BR>slip.<BR>--3 Loosening, slackening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंह्
स्रंह् {c1c} A. (स्रंहते) To confide or<BR>trust.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्
स्रज् f. [सृज्यते सृज्-क्विन् नि˚]<BR>1<BR>A chaplet, wreath or garland of<BR>flowers (especially one worn on the<BR>head); स्रजमपि शिरस्यंधः क्षिप्तां<BR>धुनोत्यहिशंकया Ś. 7. 24.<BR>--2 A garland<BR>(in general).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दामन्, (<BR>स्रग्दानन्) n. the tie or fillet of a<BR>garland.<BR>--धर a. wearing a garland;<BR>Gīt. 12.<BR>--(रा) N. of a metre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रग्विन्
स्रग्विन् a. (णी f.)(compar.<BR>स्रजीयस्, superl. स्रजिष्ठ) Wearing a<BR>garland or chaplet; आमुक्ताभरणः<BR>स्रग्वी हंसचिह्नदुकूलवान् R. 17. 25.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रजयति
स्रजयति Den. P. To furnish with<BR>a garland.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रज्वा
स्रज्वा A rope, string, cord.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रद्धू
स्रद्धू f. Breaking wind<BR>downwards (अपानवायु).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रंभ्|स्रम्भ्
स्रंभ् {c1c} A. (स्रंभते, स्रब्ध) To<BR>confide; see श्रंभ्. --WITH वि {1} to be<BR>confident. {2} to rest secure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवः|स्रव
स्रवः [स्रु-अप्]<BR>1 Trickling,<BR>oozing, flowing.<BR>--2 A drop, flow, stream;<BR>विपुलौ स्नपयंती सा स्तनौ नेत्रजलस्रवैः<BR>Rām.<BR>--3 A fountain, spring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवणं|स्रवण
स्रवणं [स्रु-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Flowing,<BR>trickling, oozing.<BR>--2 Sweat.<BR>--3 Urine.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवत्
स्रवत् a. (स्रवंती f.) Flowing,<BR>oozing, trickling &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गर्भा {1}<BR>a woman that miscarries. {2} a cow<BR>miscarrying by accident.<BR>--रंगः a<BR>market, fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रवंती
स्रवंती<BR>1 A stream, river; वापीष्विव<BR>स्रवंतीषु R. 17. 64; Māl. 9. 24.<BR>--2 The region of the spleen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रष्टृ
स्रष्टृ m. [सृज्-तृच्]<BR>1 A maker.<BR>--2 A creator, an epithet of<BR>Brahman; या सृष्टिः स्रष्टुराद्या Ś. 1. 1;<BR>तत्स्रष्टुरेकांतरं 7. 27.<BR>--3 N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रस्तरः|स्रस्तर
स्रस्तरः A couch or sofa (for<BR>reclining), bed; शिलातले<BR>स्रस्तरमास्तीर्य निषसाद K.; Ms. 2. 204.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्राक्
स्राक् ind. Quickly, speedily.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावः|स्राव
स्रावः Flow, flowing, oozing,<BR>dropping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रावक|स्रावकं
स्रावक a. (विका f.) [स्रु-णिच्-ण्वुल्]<BR>Causing to flow, pouring out,<BR>exuding.<BR>--कं Black pepper.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिध्
स्रिध् {c1c} U. (स्रेधति-ते) To injure,<BR>harm, ruin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिभ्
स्रिभ् {c1c} P. (स्रेभति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिंभ्|स्रिम्भ्
स्रिंभ् {c1c} P. (स्रिंभति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रिव्
स्रिव् {c4c} P. (स्रीव्यति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To become dry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रु|स्रुः
स्रु {c1c} P. (स्रवति, स्रुत)<BR>1 To flow,<BR>stream, trickle, ooze, drop,<BR>exude; न हि निंबात्स्रवेत्क्षौद्रं Rām.<BR>--2 To pour out, shed, let flow;<BR>अलोठिष्ट च भूपृष्ठे शोणितं चाप्यसुस्रुवत्<BR>Bk. 15. 56, 17. 18.<BR>--3 To go, move.<BR>--4 To trickle or slip away, waste<BR>away, perish, come to nothing;<BR>स्रवते ब्रह्म तस्यापि भिन्नभांडात्पयो यथा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">Page1158-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Bhāg.; Bk. 6. 18; Ms. 2. 74.<BR>--5<BR>To spread about, get abroad,<BR>transpire (as a secret). --Caus. (<BR>स्रावयति-ते) To cause to flow, pour out,<BR>shed, spill (blood &c.); न<BR>गात्रात्स्रावयेदसृक् Ms. 4. 169.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1157-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत्
स्रुत् a. (Usually at the end of<BR>comp.) Flowing, dropping, pouring<BR>forth; स्वरेण तस्याममृतस्रुतेव<BR>Ku. 1. 45; Śi. 9. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुत|स्रुतं
स्रुत p. p.<BR>1 Flowed, trickled,<BR>dripping &c.<BR>--2 Gone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुतिः|स्रुति
स्रुतिः f.<BR>1 Flowing, oozing,<BR>distilling, trickling out;<BR>कीटक्षतिस्रुतिभिरस्रमिवोद्वमंतः Mu. 6. 13; पदं<BR>तुषारस्रुतिधौतरक्तं Ku. 1. 6; R. 16. 44;<BR>Ki. 5. 44, 16. 2; क्षीरस्रुतिसुरभयः<BR>(वाताः) Me. 107 ‘exudation or flow<BR>of the sap.’<BR>--2 Exudation, resin.<BR>--3 A stream.<BR>--4 Ved. A path, road.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुघ्नः|स्रुघ्न
स्रुघ्नः N. of a district; पंथाः<BR>स्रुघ्नमुपतिष्ठते Sk.; it was situated at<BR>some distance-at least one day's<BR>journey-from Pātaliputra q. v.;<BR>cf. न हि देवदत्तः स्रुघ्ने<BR>संनिधीयमानस्तदहरेव पाटलिपुत्रे संनिधीयते युगपदनेकत्र<BR>वृत्तावनेकत्वप्रसंगात् Ś. B.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुघ्नी
स्रुघ्नी Natron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रौघ्न|स्रौघ्नः
स्रौघ्न a. (घ्नी)<BR>1 Belonging to, or<BR>coming from, Srughna.<BR>--2 Residing<BR>in Srughna.<BR>--घ्नः An inhabitant of<BR>Srughna.<BR>--घ्नं The gate leading to<BR>Srughna; cf P. IV. 3. 86.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुच्
स्रुच् f. A sort of wooden ladle, used<BR>for pouring clarified butter on<BR>sacrificial fire; (usually made of trees<BR>like Palāśa or Khadira);<BR>R. 11. 25; Ms. 5. 117; Y. 1. 183.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रणालिका the spout of a ladle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवः|स्रुव
स्रुवः --वा<BR>1 A sacrificial ladle.<BR>--2<BR>A Soma ladle.<BR>--3 A spring, cascade.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हस्तः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुवा
स्रुवः --वा<BR>1 A sacrificial ladle.<BR>--2<BR>A Soma ladle.<BR>--3 A spring, cascade.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--हस्तः N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रू
स्रू f.<BR>1 A sacrificial ladle.<BR>--2 A<BR>spring or fountain.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रेक्
स्रेक् {c1c} A. (स्रेकते) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रै
स्रै {c1c} P. (स्रायति)<BR>1 To boil.<BR>--2 To<BR>sweat; see श्रै.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतं|स्रोत|स्रोतः
स्रोतं A stream; see स्रोतस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्
स्रोतस् n. [स्रु-तसि]<BR>1 (a) A stream,<BR>current, flow or course of water;<BR>पुरा यत्र स्रोतः पुलिनमधुना तत्र सरितां<BR>U. 2. 27, Ms. 3. 163. (b) A torrent,<BR>rapid stream; नदत्याकाशगंगायाः<BR>स्रोतस्युद्दामदिग्गजे R. 1. 78;<BR>स्रोतसेवोह्यमानस्य प्रतीपतरणं हि तत् V. 2. 5.<BR>--2 A<BR>stream, river (in general);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-b" target="_blank">Page1158-b+ 57</a>]<BR>स्रोतसामस्मि जाह्नवी Bg. 10. 31.<BR>--3 A wave.<BR>--4 Water.<BR>--5 The canal of<BR>nutriment in the body.<BR>--6 An organ of<BR>sense; निगृह्य सर्वस्रोतांसि Rām.<BR>--7<BR>The trunk of an elephant.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंजनं (स्रोतोंजनं) antimony.<BR>--ईशः<BR>the ocean.<BR>--रंध्रं an aperture of the<BR>proboscis or trunk of an elephant,<BR>a nostril; स्रोतोंरध्रध्वनितसुभगं दांतीभिः<BR>पीयमानः Me. 42 (see Malli. thereon);<BR>(written श्रोतोरंध्र also q. v.).<BR>--वह् f.,<BR>--वहा a river; स्रोतोवहां पथि<BR>निकामजलामतीत्य जातः सखे प्रणयवान्<BR>मृगतृष्णिकायां Ś. 6. 15; 2. 17; कार्या<BR>सैकतलीनहंसमिथुना स्रोतोवहा मालिनी 6. 16;<BR>R. 6. 52.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्यः|स्रोतस्य
स्रोतस्यः<BR>1 N. of Śiva.<BR>--2 A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्वती
स्रोतस्वती, स्रोतस्विनी A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रोतस्विनी
स्रोतस्वती, स्रोतस्विनी A river.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्व|स्वं|स्वः
स्व pron. a.<BR>1 One's own,<BR>belonging to oneself, often serving as a<BR>reflexive pronoun; स्वनियोगमशून्यं<BR>कुरु Ś. 2; प्रजाः प्रजाः स्वा इव तंत्रयित्वा<BR>5. 5; oft. in comp. in this sense;<BR>स्वंपुत्र, स्वकलत्र, स्वद्रव्य.<BR>--2 Innate,<BR>natural, inherent, peculiar, inborn;<BR>सूर्यापाये न खलु कमलं पुष्यति<BR>स्वामभिख्यां Me. 80; Ś. 1. 19; स तस्य स्वो<BR>भावः प्रकृतिनियतत्वादकृतकः U. 6. 14.<BR>--3 Belonging to one's own caste or<BR>tribe; शूद्रैव भार्या शूद्रस्य सा च स्वा च<BR>विशः स्मृतेः Ms. 3. 13, 5. 104.<BR>--स्वः<BR>1 One's own self.<BR>--2 A relative,<BR>kinsman; Pt. 2. 96; Ms. 2. 109.<BR>--3 The soul.<BR>--4 N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--स्वः,<BR>--स्वं<BR>1 Wealth, property; as in निःस्व<BR>q. v.<BR>--2 (In alg.) The plus or<BR>affirmative quantity; cf. धन. --COMP.<BR>--अक्षपादः a follower of the Nyāya<BR>system of philosophy.<BR>--अक्षरं one's<BR>own hand-writing.<BR>--अधिकारः one's<BR>own duty or sway; स्वाधिकारात्प्रमत्तः<BR>Me. 1; स्वाधिकारभूमौ Ś. 7.<BR>--अधिष्ठानं one of the six Cakras or<BR>mystical circles of the body.<BR>--अधीन a.<BR>{1} dependent on oneself,<BR>self-dependent. {2} independent. {3} one's<BR>own subject. {4} in one's own<BR>power; स्वाधीना वचनीयतापि हि वरं<BR>बद्धो न सेवांजलिः Mk. 3. 11. ˚कुशल<BR>a. having prosperity in one's own<BR>power; स्वाधीनकुशलाः सिद्धिमंतः Ś. 4.<BR>˚पतिका, ˚भर्तृका a woman who has<BR>full control over her husband, one<BR>whose husband is subject to her;<BR>अथ सा निर्गताबाधा राधा स्वाधीनभर्तृका ।<BR>निजगाद रतिक्लांतं कांतं मंडनवांछया<BR>Gīt. 12; see S. D. 112 et seq.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-c" target="_blank">Page1158-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--अध्यायः {1} self-recitation,<BR>muttering to one-self. {2} study of the<BR>Vedas, sacred study, perusal of<BR>sacred books. {3} the Veda itself.<BR>{4} a day on which sacred study is<BR>enjoined to be resumed after<BR>suspension. ˚अर्थिन् m. a student<BR>who tries to secure his own<BR>livelihood during his course of holy<BR>study; Ms. 11. 1.<BR>--अध्यायिन् m. {1} a<BR>student of the Vedas. {2} a<BR>tradesman.<BR>--अनुभवः, --अनुभूतिः f. {1}<BR>self-experience. {2} self-knowledge;<BR>स्वानुभूत्येकसाराय नमः शांताय तेजसे<BR>Bh. 2. 1.<BR>--अनुरूप a. {1} natural,<BR>inborn. {2} worthy of oneself.<BR>--अंतं<BR>{1} the mind; Bv. 4. 5; Mv. 7. 17. {2} a<BR>cavern.<BR>--अर्थ a. {1} self-interested. {2}<BR>having its own or true meaning. {3}<BR>having one's own object or aim. {4}<BR>pleonastic.<BR>--(र्थः) {1} one's own interest,<BR>self-interest; सर्वः स्वार्थं समीहते<BR>Śi. 2. 65; स्वार्थात्सतां गुरुतरा<BR>प्रणयिक्रियैव V. 4. 15. {2} own or<BR>inherent meaning; स्वार्थे णिच्, स्वार्थे<BR>कप्रत्ययः &c.; Bv. 1. 79 (where both<BR>senses are intended). ˚अनुमानं<BR>inference for oneself, a kind of<BR>inductive reasoning, one of the two<BR>main kinds of अनुमान, the other<BR>being परार्थानुमान. ˚पांडित a. {1} clever<BR>in one's own affairs. {2} expert in<BR>attending to one's own interests. ˚पर,<BR>˚परायण a. intent on securing<BR>one's own interests, selfish;<BR>Mu. 3. 4. ˚विघातः frustration of one's<BR>object. ˚सिद्धिः f. fulfilment of one's<BR>own object.<BR>--आयत्त a. subject to,<BR>or dependent upon, oneself;<BR>Bh. 2. 7.<BR>--इच्छा self-will, own inclination.<BR>˚आचारः acting as one likes;<BR>selfwill. ˚मृत्युः an epithet of Bhīṣma.<BR>--उदयः the rising of a sign or<BR>heavenly body at any particular<BR>place.<BR>--उपधिः a fixed star.<BR>--कंपनः<BR>air, wind.<BR>--कामिन् a. selfish.<BR>--कार्यं one's own business or interest.<BR>--कुलक्षयः a fish.<BR>--गतम् ind. to<BR>oneself, aside (in theatrical<BR>language).<BR>--छंद a. {1} self-willed,<BR>uncontrolled, wanton. {2}<BR>spontaneous. {3} wild.<BR>--(दः) one's own<BR>will or choice, own fancy or pleasure,<BR>independence.<BR>--(दं) ind. at one's<BR>own will or pleasure, wantonly,<BR>voluntarily; स्वच्छंदं दलदरविंद ते मरंदं<BR>विंदंतो विदधतु गुंजितं मिलिंदाः Bv. 1. 15.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-a" target="_blank">Page1159-a+ 57</a>]<BR>--ज a. self-born.<BR>--(जः) {1} a<BR>son or child. {2} sweat, perspiration.<BR>--(जा) a daughter.<BR>--(जं) blood.<BR>--जनः {1} a kinsman, relative; इतः<BR>प्रत्यादेशात् स्वजनमनुगंतुं व्यवसिता<BR>Ś. 6. 8, Pt. 1. 5. {2} one's own people or<BR>kindred, one's household. (<BR>स्वजनायते Den. P. ‘becomes or is treated<BR>as a relation’; Pt. 1. 5.).<BR>--ज्ञातिः a<BR>kinsman.<BR>--तंत्र a. {1} self-dependent,<BR>uncontrolled, independent,<BR>selfwilled. {2} of age, full-grown.<BR>--(त्रः)<BR>a blind man.<BR>--देशः one's own<BR>country, native country. ˚जः, ˚बंधुः a<BR>fellow-countryman.<BR>--धर्मः {1} one's<BR>own religion. {2} one's own duty,<BR>the duties of one's own class;<BR>Ms. 1. 88, 91; स्वधर्मे निधनं श्रेयः परधर्मो<BR>भयावहः Bg. 3. 35. {3} peculiarity, one's<BR>own property.<BR>--पक्षः {1} one's own<BR>side or party. {2} a friend.<BR>--परमंडलं one's own and an enemy's<BR>country.<BR>--प्रकाश a. {1} self-evident.<BR>{2} self-luminous.<BR>--प्रयोगात् ind. by<BR>means of one's own efforts.<BR>--भटः<BR>{1} one's own warrior. {2}<BR>bodyguard.<BR>--भावः {1} own state. {2} an<BR>essential or inherent property,<BR>natural constitution, innate or peculiar<BR>disposition, nature; as in स्वभावो<BR>दुरतिक्रमः Subhāṣ.; so कुटिल˚, शुद्ध˚,<BR>मृदु˚, चपल˚, कठिन˚ &c. ˚उक्तिः f. {1}<BR>spontaneous declaration. {2} (in<BR>Rhet.) a figure of speech which<BR>consists in describing a thing to the<BR>life, or with exact resemblance;<BR>स्वभावोक्तिस्तु डिंभदिः स्वक्रियारूपवर्णनं<BR>K. P. 10, or नानावस्थं पदार्थानां रूपं<BR>साक्षाद्विवृण्वती Kāv. 2. 8. ˚वादः the<BR>doctrine that the universe was produced<BR>and is sustained by the natural and<BR>necessary action of substances<BR>according to their inherent<BR>properties, (and not by the agency of a<BR>Supreme Being). ˚सिद्ध a. natural,<BR>spontaneous, inborn.<BR>--भूः {1} an<BR>epithet of Brahman. {2} of Śiva.<BR>{3} of Viṣṇu.<BR>--योनि a. related on<BR>the mother's side. (--m. f.) own<BR>womb, one's own place of birth.<BR>(--f.) a sister or near female<BR>relative.<BR>--रसः {1} natural taste. {2}<BR>proper taste or sentiment in<BR>composition. {3} a kind of astringent<BR>juice. {4} the residue of oily<BR>substances (ground on a stone).<BR>--राज्<BR>m. {1} the Supreme Being. {2} one<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-b" target="_blank">Page1159-b+ 56</a>]<BR>of the seven rays of the sun.<BR>--रूप<BR>a. {1} similar, like. {2} handsome,<BR>pleasing, lovely. {3} learned, wise.<BR>--(पं) {1} one's own form or shape,<BR>natural state or condition;<BR>Pt. 1. 159. {2} natural character or form,<BR>true constitution. {3} nature. {4}<BR>peculiar aim. {5} kind, sort, species.<BR>˚असिद्धि f. one of the three forms of<BR>fallacy called असिद्ध q. v.<BR>--लक्षणं a<BR>peculiar characteristic or property.<BR>--वश a. {1} self-controlled. {2}<BR>independent.<BR>--वहित a. {1}<BR>self-impelled. {2} alert, active.<BR>--वासिनी a<BR>woman whether married or<BR>unmarried who continues to live after<BR>maturity in her father's house.<BR>--वृत्ति a. living by one's own<BR>exertions.<BR>--संवृत a. self-protected,<BR>self-guarded.<BR>--संस्था {1}<BR>self-abiding. {2} self-possession. {3}<BR>absorption in one's own self.<BR>--स्थ a. {1}<BR>self-abiding. {2} self-dependent,<BR>relying on one's own exertions,<BR>confident, firm, resolute. {3}<BR>independent. {4} doing well, well, in health,<BR>at ease, comfortable; स्वस्थ एवास्मि<BR>Māl. 4; स्वस्थे को वा न पंडितः<BR>Pt. 1. 127; see अस्वस्थ also. {5} contented,<BR>happy.<BR>--(स्थं) ind. at ease,<BR>comfortably, composedly.<BR>--स्थानं one's<BR>own place or home, one's own<BR>abode; नक्रः स्वस्थानमासाद्य गजेंद्रमपि<BR>कर्षति Pt. 3. 46.<BR>--हस्तः one's own<BR>hand or handwriting, an autograph;<BR>see under हस्त.<BR>--हस्तिका an axe.<BR>--हित a. beneficial to oneself.<BR>--(तं)<BR>one's own good or advantage, one's<BR>own welfare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1158-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वक|स्वकं|स्वकः
स्वक a. One's own, own.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वकीय|स्वकीयः
स्वकीय a.<BR>1 One's own, own.<BR>--2<BR>Of one's own family.<BR>--या One's<BR>own wife.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वतस्
स्वतस् ind.<BR>1 Of oneself, by<BR>oneself (used reflexively).<BR>--2 From<BR>oneself.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रमाण, --सिद्ध a.<BR>self-evident, self-proved, axiomatic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वत्वं|स्वत्व
स्वत्वं<BR>1 Self-existence.<BR>--2<BR>Ownership, proprietory right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वंग्|स्वङ्ग्
स्वं(क्)ग् {c1c} P. (स्वं-क-गति) To go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वंक्|स्वङ्क्
स्वं(क्)ग् {c1c} P. (स्वं-क-गति) To go,<BR>move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वच्छ|स्वच्छं|स्वच्छः
स्वच्छ a. [सुष्ठु अच्छः प्रा˚]<BR>1 Very<BR>clear or transparent, pure, bright,<BR>pellucid; स्वच्छस्फटिक, स्वच्छमुक्ताफलं<BR>&c.<BR>--2 White.<BR>--3 Beautiful.<BR>--4<BR>Healthy.<BR>--च्छः A crystal.<BR>--च्छा<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-c" target="_blank">Page1159-c+ 56</a>]<BR>White Dūrvā grass.<BR>--च्छं<BR>1 A<BR>pearl.<BR>--2 Pure chalk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पत्रं<BR>talc.<BR>--वालुकं pure chalk.<BR>--मणिः<BR>a crystal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वंज्|स्वञ्ज्
स्वंज् {c1c} A. (स्वंजते; the स् being<BR>changed to ष् after prepositions<BR>ending in इ or उ)<BR>1 To embrace,<BR>clasp; कयाचिदाचुंब्य चिराय सस्वजे<BR>Bv. 2. 178; पर्यश्रुरस्वजत मूर्धनि चोपजघ्रौ<BR>R. 13. 70.<BR>--2 To encircle, twist<BR>round.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वंगः|स्वङ्ग|स्वंग|स्वङ्गः
स्वंगः An embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वंजनं|स्वञ्जन
स्वंजनं The act of embracing, an<BR>embrace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वठ्
स्वठ् {c10c} U. (स्व-स्वा-ठाति-ते)<BR>1<BR>To go.<BR>--2 To finish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वद्
स्वद् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (स्वदते, स्वदित)<BR>1 To<BR>be liked, be sweet, be pleasant to<BR>the taste (with dat. of person);<BR>यज्ञदत्ताय स्वदतेऽपूपः Kāśikā.; अपां हि<BR>तृप्ताय न वारिधारा स्वादुः सुगंधिः स्वदते<BR>तुषारा N. 3. 93; सस्वदे मुखसुरं<BR>प्रमदाभ्यः Śi. 10. 23.<BR>--2 To taste, relish,<BR>eat.<BR>--3 To please.<BR>--4 To sweeten.<BR>{vII.v} {c10c} U. or Caus. (स्वादयति-ते)<BR>1<BR>To cause to taste or eat.<BR>--2 To<BR>taste.<BR>--3 To sweeten.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदनं|स्वदन
स्वदनं Tasting, eating.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वदित
स्वदित p. p. Tasted, eaten.<BR>--तं<BR>An exclamation meaning ‘may it<BR>be well tasted or relished’,<BR>uttered at a Śrāddha ceremony after<BR>the presentation of rice-balls or<BR>oblations of food to the Manes;<BR>Ms. 3. 251, 254.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधा
स्वधा [स्वद्-आ पृषो˚ दस्य धः]<BR>1<BR>One's own nature or determination,<BR>spontaneity.<BR>--2 One's own will or<BR>pleasure.<BR>--3 The oblation of food<BR>offered to the Pitṛs or Manes<BR>of deceased ancestors;<BR>स्वधासंग्रहतत्पराः R. 1. 66, Ms. 9. 142,<BR>Y. 1. 102.<BR>--4 The food offered to the<BR>Manes personified.<BR>--5 Food or<BR>oblation in general.<BR>--6 One's own<BR>portion or share.<BR>--7 A Śrāddha or<BR>funeral ceremony.<BR>--8 N. of Māyā<BR>or illusion. --ind. An<BR>exclamation uttered on offering an oblation<BR>to the Manes (with dat.); पितृभ्यः<BR>स्वधा Sk.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a.<BR>offering oblations to the Pitṛs.<BR>--कारः<BR>the exclamation Svadhā; पूतं हि<BR>तद्गृहं यत्र स्वधाकारः प्रवर्तते.<BR>--निनयनं a<BR>formula or sacred text used in<BR>making the oblations to the Pitṛs.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">Page1160-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--प्रियः {1} Agni or fire. {2} black<BR>sesamum.<BR>--भुज् m. {1} a deceased or<BR>deified ancestor. {2} a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1159-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वधितिः|स्वधिति
स्वधितिः m. f., स्वधिती An axe.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वन्
स्वन् {c1c} P. (स्वनति)<BR>1 To sound,<BR>make a noise; पूर्णाः परोश्च सस्वनुः<BR>Bk. 14. 3; वेणवः कीचकास्ते स्युर्ये<BR>स्वनंत्यनिलोद्धताः Bk.<BR>--2 To hum (as a<BR>bee); Ś. 1. 24.<BR>--3 To sing. --Caus.<BR>(स्वनयति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to resound<BR>--2 To sound.<BR>--3 To adorn (स्वानयति<BR>in this sense).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनः|स्वन
स्वनः [स्वन्-अप्] Sound, noise;<BR>शिवाघोरस्वनां पश्चाद् बुबुधे विकृतेति तां<BR>R. 12, 39; शंखस्वनः &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उत्साहः a rhinoceros.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिः|स्वनि
स्वनिः Sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनिक
स्वनिक a. Sounding; as in<BR>पाणिस्वनिकः ‘one who claps his hands’.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वनित|स्वनितं
स्वनित a. [स्वन्-कर्त्तरि क्त]<BR>Sounded, sounding, making a noise.<BR>--तं<BR>1 The noise of thunder,<BR>thunderclap; cf. स्तनित.<BR>--2 Noise, sound (in<BR>general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्
स्वप् {c2c} P. (स्वपिति, सुप्त; pass.<BR>सुष्यते; desid. सुषुप्सति) (rarely<BR>{c1c} U. स्वपति-ते)<BR>1 To sleep, fall<BR>asleep, go to sleep;<BR>असंजातकिणस्कंधः सुखं स्वपिति गौर्गडिः<BR>K. P. 10; इतः स्वपिति केशवः<BR>Bh. 2. 76.<BR>--2 To recline, repose, lie<BR>down, rest.<BR>--3 To be absorbed in;<BR>Bv. 4. 19. --Caus. (स्वापयति-ते) To<BR>cause to sleep, rock to sleep. --WITH<BR>अव, --नि, प्र, or सं to sleep, lie<BR>down; प्रसुप्तलक्षणः Māl. 7;<BR>Ku. 2 42; R. 11. 44.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वपनं|स्वपन
स्वपनं Sleeping, dreaming, sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नः|स्वप्न
स्वप्नः [स्वप् --भावे नक्]<BR>1 Sleeping,<BR>sleep; अकाले बोधितो भ्रात्रा प्रियस्वप्नो<BR>वृथा भवान् R. 12. 81, 7. 61, 12. 70;<BR>Ku. 2. 8.<BR>--2 A dream, dreaming<BR>स्वप्नेंद्रजालसट्टशः खलु जीवलोकः<BR>Śānti. 2. 2; स्वप्नो नु माया नु मतिभ्रमो नु<BR>Ś. 6. 9, R. 10. 60.<BR>--3 Sloth, indolence,<BR>sleepiness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अवस्था a state<BR>of dreaming.<BR>--उपम a. {1}<BR>resembling a dream. {2} unreal or<BR>illusory (like a dream).<BR>--कर, --कृत्<BR>a. inducing sleep, soporific,<BR>narcotic.<BR>--गृहं --निकेतनं a sleeping-room,<BR>bed-chamber.<BR>--दोषः involuntary<BR>seminal discharge, pollutio nocturna.<BR>--धागम्य a. perceptible by the<BR>intellect only when it is in a state<BR>of sleep-like abstraction;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-b" target="_blank">Page1160-b+ 56</a>]<BR>Ms. 12. 122.<BR>--प्रपंचः the illusion of sleep,<BR>the world appearing in a dream.<BR>--विचारः interpretation of dreams.<BR>--शील a. disposed to sleep, sleepy,<BR>drowsy.<BR>--सृष्टिः f. the creation of<BR>dreams or illusions in sleep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वप्नज्
स्वप्नज् a. Sleepy, sleeping, drowsy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वमेकः|स्वमेक
स्वमेकः A year.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वयम्
स्वयम् ind.<BR>1 Oneself, in one's<BR>own person (used reflexively and<BR>applicable to all persons, such as<BR>myself, ourselves, thyself, himself<BR>&c. &c., and sometimes used with<BR>other pronouns for the sake of<BR>emphasis); विषवृक्षोपि संवर्ध्य स्वयं<BR>छेत्तुमसांप्रतं Ku. 2. 55; यस्य नास्ति स्वयं<BR>प्रज्ञा शास्त्रं तस्य करोति किं Subhāṣ.;<BR>R. 1. 70; 3. 20, 2. 56;<BR>Ms. 5. 39.<BR>--2 Spontaneously, of one's own<BR>accord, without trouble or exertion;<BR>स्वयमेवोत्पद्यंत एवंविधाः कुलपांशवो<BR>निःस्नेहाः पशवः K.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अर्जित a.<BR>self-acquired.<BR>--उक्तिः f. {1}<BR>voluntary declaration. {2} information,<BR>deposition (in law).<BR>--उपागतः a<BR>son who offers himself voluntarily<BR>to an adoptive parent.<BR>--कृत a.<BR>self-made, natural.<BR>--(तः) an<BR>artificial or adopted son.<BR>--ग्रहः taking<BR>for one-self (without leave).<BR>--ग्राह<BR>a. voluntary, self-choosing.<BR>--(हः)<BR>self-choice, self-election;<BR>Ku. 3. 7, Māl. 6. 7.<BR>--जात a.<BR>self-born.<BR>--दत्त a. self-given.<BR>--(त्तः) a boy who has given<BR>himself to be adopted (by his<BR>adoptive parents); one of the twelve<BR>kinds of sons recognised in Hindu<BR>law.<BR>--भुः N. of Brahman;<BR>शंभुस्वयंभुहरयो हरिणेक्षणानां येनाक्रियंत सततं<BR>गृहकर्मदासाः Bh. 1. 1.<BR>--भुवः the<BR>first Manu. {2} N. of Brahman. {3}<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--भू a. self-existent.<BR>--(भूः)<BR>{1} N. of Brahman. {2} of Viṣṇu.<BR>{3} of Śiva. {4} of Kāla or time<BR>personified. {5} of Kāmadeva. {6}<BR>a Jaina deified saint. {7} the<BR>female breast. {8} the Supreme<BR>Being.<BR>--भूतः N. of Śiva.<BR>--वरः<BR>self-choice, self-election (of a<BR>husband by the bride herself),<BR>choicemarriage.<BR>--वरा a maiden who<BR>chooses her own husband.<BR>--श्रेष्ठः<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर् {c10c} U. (स्वरयति-ते) To find<BR>fault, blame, reprove, censure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्
स्वर् ind.<BR>1 Heaven, paradise;<BR>as in स्वर्लोक, स्वर्वेश्या, स्वर्भानुः, &c.<BR>--2 The heaven of Indra and the<BR>temporary abode of the virtuous<BR>after death.<BR>--3 The sky, ether.<BR>--4<BR>The space above the sun or between<BR>the sun and the polar star.<BR>--5 The<BR>third of the three Vyāhṛtis,<BR>pronounced by every Brāhmaṇa<BR>in his daily prayers, see<BR>व्याहृति.<BR>--6 Radiance, splendour.<BR>--7<BR>Water.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आपगा, --गंगा {1}<BR>the celestial Ganges. {2} the<BR>galaxy or milky way.<BR>--गतिः f.<BR>--गमनं {1} going to heaven, future<BR>felicity. {2} death.<BR>--गिरिः Sumeru.<BR>--तरुः (स्वस्तरुः) a tree of paradise.<BR>--ट्टश् m. {1} an epithet of Indra.<BR>{2} of Agni. {3} of Soma.<BR>--नदी<BR>(forming स्वर्णदी) the celestial<BR>Ganges.<BR>--भानवः a kind of precious<BR>stone.<BR>--भानुः N. of Rāhu; तुल्येऽ<BR>पराधे स्वर्भानुर्भानुमंतं चिरेण यत् ।<BR>हिमांशुमाशु ग्रसते तन्म्रदिम्नः स्फुटं फलं<BR>Śi. 2. 49. ˚सूदनः the sun.<BR>--मध्यं the<BR>central point of the sky, the zenith,<BR>--लोकः the celestial world,<BR>heaven.<BR>--वधूः f. a celestial<BR>damselan apsaras.<BR>--वापी the Ganges.<BR>--वेश्या ‘a courtezan of heaven’,<BR>a celestial nymph, an apsaras.<BR>--वैद्य m. pl. an epithet of the two<BR>Aśvins.<BR>--षा {1} an epithet of Soma.<BR>{2} of the thunderbolt of Indra.<BR>--सिंधु = स्वर्गंगा q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरः|स्वर
स्वरः [स्वर्-अच्, स्वृ-अप् वा]<BR>1<BR>Sound, noise.<BR>--2 Voice; स्वरेण<BR>तस्याममृतस्रुतवे प्रजल्पितायामभिजातवाचि<BR>Ku. 1. 45.<BR>--3 A note of the<BR>musical scale or gamut, a tone, tune;<BR>(these are seven:<BR>--निषादर्षभगांधारषड्जमध्यमधैवताः ॥ पंचमश्चेत्यमी सप्त<BR>तंत्रीकंठोत्थिताः स्वराः Ak.).<BR>--4 The number<BR>‘seven’.<BR>--5 A vowel.<BR>--6 An accent;<BR>(these are three; उदात्त, अनुदात्त, and<BR>स्वरित q.q. v.v.).<BR>--7 Air breathed<BR>through the nostrils.<BR>--8 Snoring.<BR>--रा N. of the chief wife of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशः a half or<BR>quarter tone (in music).<BR>--अंतरं the interval between two vowels,<BR>hiatus.<BR>--उदय a. followed by a<BR>vowel.<BR>--(यः) the production of<BR>sound.<BR>--उपध a. preceded by a<BR>vowel.<BR>--ग्रामः the musical scale,<BR>gamut.<BR>--पत्तनं N. of the Sāma-veda.<BR>--बद्ध composed in musical measure.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-a" target="_blank">Page1161-a+ 56</a>]<BR>--भक्तिः f. a vowel-sound<BR>phonetically inserted in the pronunciation of<BR>र् or ल् when these letters are<BR>followed by a sibilant or any single<BR>consonant; (e. g. वर्ष pronounced as वरिष).<BR>--भंगः {1} indistinctness of utterance,<BR>broken articulation. {2} hoarseness<BR>or cracking of voice.<BR>--मंडल the<BR>circle of notes, arrangement of<BR>musical scales; Pt. 5. 54.<BR>--मंडलिका a<BR>kind of lute (वीणा).<BR>--लासिका a<BR>flute, pipe.<BR>--शून्य a. without musical<BR>notes, unmelodious, unmusical.<BR>--संयोगः {1} the junction of vowels<BR>{2} the union of notes or sounds,<BR>i. e. voice; अन्य एवैष स्वरसंयोगः<BR>Mk. 1, 3; U. 3; पंडितकौशिक्या इव<BR>स्वरसंयोगः श्रूयते M. 5.<BR>--संक्रमः {1} a<BR>transition or succession of notes;<BR>तं तस्य स्वरसंक्रमं मृदुगिरः श्लिष्टं च<BR>तंत्रीस्वंनम् Mk. 3. 5. {2} the gamut.<BR>--संधिः<BR>the coalition of vowels.<BR>--सामन् m.<BR>pl. epithets of particular days in a<BR>sacrificial session.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1160-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरवत्|स्वरवन्त्
स्वरवत् a.<BR>1 Having sound,<BR>sonorous.<BR>--2 Having a voice.<BR>--3<BR>Vocal.<BR>--4 Having an accent, accented.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरित|स्वरितः
स्वरित a. [स्वरो जातोऽस्य इतच्]<BR>1<BR>Sounded.<BR>--2 Sounded as a note,<BR>pitched.<BR>--3 Articulated.<BR>--4<BR>Circumflexed.<BR>--5 Accented.<BR>--तः The third<BR>or mixed tone lying between high<BR>and low; समाहारः स्वरितः P. I. 2. 31;<BR>see Sk. thereon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरुः|स्वरु
स्वरुः [स्वृ-उ]<BR>1 Sunshine.<BR>--2 A<BR>part of a sacrificial post.<BR>--3 A<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--4 A thunderbolt.<BR>--5 An<BR>arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वरुस्
स्वरुस् m. A thunderbolt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गः|स्वर्ग
स्वर्गः Heaven, Indra's paradise;<BR>अहो स्वर्गादधिकतरं निर्वृतिस्थानं Ś. 7.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आपगा the celestial<BR>Ganges.<BR>--ओकस् m. a god, deity.<BR>--काम a. desirous of<BR>heaven.<BR>--गिरिः the heavenly mountain<BR>Sumeru.<BR>--द, --प्रद a. procuring<BR>(entrance into) paradise.<BR>--द्वारं<BR>heaven's gate, the door of paradise,<BR>entrance into heaven;<BR>स्वर्गद्वारकपाटपाटनपटुर्धर्मोऽपि नापोर्जितः Bh. 3. 11.<BR>--पतिः, --भर्तृ m. Indra.<BR>--लोकः {1} the<BR>celestial region. {2} paradise. ˚ईश्वरः<BR>{1} Indra. {2} the body.<BR>--वधूः, स्त्री<BR>f. a celestial damsel, heavenly<BR>nymph, an apsaras; स्वर्गस्त्रीणां<BR>परिष्वंगः कथं मर्त्येन लभ्यते, --साधनं the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">Page1161-b+ 56</a>]<BR>means of attaining heaven.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गिन्
स्वर्गिन् a. [स्वर्गोऽस्त्यस्य भोग्यत्वेन इनि]<BR>Belonging to heaven, heavenly. --m.<BR>1 A god, deity, an immortal; त्वमपि<BR>विततयज्ञः स्वर्गिणः प्रीणयालं<BR>Ś. 7. 34; Me. 30; Ku. 2. 45.<BR>--2 A dead<BR>or deceased man.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्गीय
स्वर्गीय, स्वर्ग्य a.<BR>1 Heavenly,<BR>celestial, divine.<BR>--2 Leading to heaven,<BR>procuring entrance into heaven;<BR>Ms. 4. 13, 5. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्ग्य|स्वर्ग्यः
स्वर्गीय, स्वर्ग्य a.<BR>1 Heavenly,<BR>celestial, divine.<BR>--2 Leading to heaven,<BR>procuring entrance into heaven;<BR>Ms. 4. 13, 5. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्जिकः|स्वर्जिक|स्वर्ज्जिकः
स्वर्जिकः, स्वर्जिन् m.<BR>1 Natron.<BR>--2 Salt-petre, nitre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्जिन्
स्वर्जिकः, स्वर्जिन् m.<BR>1 Natron.<BR>--2 Salt-petre, nitre.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णं|स्वर्ण
स्वर्णं [सुष्ठु अर्णो वर्णो यस्य]<BR>1 Gold.<BR>--2 A golden coin.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः<BR>the Āragvadha tree.<BR>--अरिः sulphur.<BR>--कणः, --कणिका a grain of gold.<BR>--काय a. golden-bodied.<BR>--(यः) N.<BR>of Garuḍa.<BR>--कारः, --कृत् a goldsmith.<BR>--गैरिकं a kind of red chalk.<BR>--चूडः<BR>{1} the blue jay. {2} a cock.<BR>--जं<BR>tin.<BR>--दीधितिः fire.<BR>--पक्षः N. of<BR>Garuḍa.<BR>--पद्मा the celestial Ganges.<BR>--पाठकः borax.<BR>--पुष्पः the<BR>Campaka tree.<BR>--बंधः a deposit of gold.<BR>--बिंदुः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--भृंगारः a<BR>golden vase.<BR>--माक्षिकं a kind of<BR>mineral substance.<BR>--यूथी --यूथिका<BR>yellow jasmine.<BR>--रेखा, --लेखा a<BR>streak of gold.<BR>--वणिज् m. {1} a<BR>goldmerchant. {2} a money-changer.<BR>--वर्णा<BR>turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्णक
स्वर्णक a. Golden, made of gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वर्द्|स्वर्द्द्
स्वर्द् {c1c} A. (स्वर्दते)<BR>1 To taste,<BR>relish.<BR>--2 To be pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्
स्वल् {c1c} P. (स्वलति) To go, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्प|स्वल्पः
स्वल्प a. [सुष्ठु अल्पं प्रा. स] (compar.<BR>स्वल्पीयस्; superl. स्वल्पिष्ठ)<BR>1 Very small<BR>or little, minute.<BR>--2 Trifling,<BR>insignificant.<BR>--3 Brief, short; स्वल्पं तथायुः<BR>Pt. 1.<BR>--4 Very few.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आहार<BR>a. eating very little, most<BR>abstemious.<BR>--कंकः a species of heron.<BR>--केशरिन् m. the Kovidāra tree.<BR>--बल<BR>a. very feeble or weak.<BR>--विषयः {1} an<BR>insignificant matter. {2} a small part.<BR>--व्ययः very little expenditure,<BR>stinginess.<BR>--व्रीड a. having little<BR>shame, shameless, impudent.<BR>--शरीर<BR>a. diminutive, dwarfish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पक
स्वल्पक a. Very little, very small<BR>or few.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पीयस्
स्वल्पीयस् a. Much less, smaller,<BR>more minute (compar. of स्वल्प<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वल्पिष्ठ
स्वल्पिष्ठ a. Smallest, least, most<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">Page1161-c+ 56</a>]<BR>minute (superl. of स्वल्प q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वशुरः|स्वशुर
स्वशुरः A father-in-law; cf.<BR>श्वशुर.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसृ
स्वसृ f. [सु-अस्-ऋन्; Uṇ. 2. 97]<BR>1<BR>A sister; स्वसारमादाय विदर्भनाथः<BR>पुरप्रवेशाभिमुखो बभूव R. 7. 1, 29.<BR>--2<BR>A finger (Ved.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वसृत्
स्वसृत् a. Going or moving at<BR>will or pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्क्
स्वस्क् {c1c} A. (स्वस्कते) See ष्वस्क्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्ति
स्वस्ति ind. A particle meaning<BR>‘may it be well with (one)’,<BR>‘farewell,’ ‘hail’, ‘adieu’ (with dat.);<BR>स्वस्ति भवते Ś. 2; स्वस्त्यस्तु ते<BR>R. 5. 17; it is also used in expressing<BR>one's approbation; (often used at<BR>the beginning of letters).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अयनं {1} a means of securing<BR>prosperity. {2} the averting of evil<BR>by the recitation of mantras or<BR>performance of expiatory rites. {3} the<BR>benediction of a Brāhmaṇa after<BR>presentation of offerings; प्रास्थानिकं<BR>स्वस्त्ययनं प्रयुज्य R. 2. 70.<BR>--दः, --भावः<BR>an epithet of Śiva.<BR>--मुखः {1} a<BR>letter. {2} a Brāhmaṇa. --. a bard;<BR>panegyrist.<BR>--वाचनं, --वाचनकं,<BR>--वाचनिकं {1} a religious rite preparatory<BR>to a sacrifice or any religious or<BR>solemn observance. {2} a<BR>complimentary or congratulatory present of<BR>flowers &c. to any one attended<BR>with good wishes and blessings.<BR>--वाच्यं congratulation, invoking<BR>blessings.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिकः|स्वस्तिक
स्वस्तिकः [स्वस्ति शुभाय हितं क]<BR>1 A<BR>kind of mystical mark on persons<BR>or things denoting good luck.<BR>--2<BR>A lucky object.<BR>--3 The meeting<BR>of four roads.<BR>--4 The crossing of<BR>the arms, making a sign like the<BR>cross;<BR>स्तनविनिहितहस्तस्वस्तिकाभिर्वधूभिः Māl. 4. 10; Śi. 10. 43.<BR>--5 A<BR>palace of a particular form.<BR>--6 A<BR>particular symbol made with<BR>ground rice and shaped like a<BR>triangle.<BR>--7 A kind of cake.<BR>--8 A<BR>voluptuary, libertine.<BR>--9 Garlic.<BR>--कः, --कं<BR>1 A mansion or temple<BR>of a particular form with a terrace<BR>in front.<BR>--2 A particular mode of<BR>sitting practised by Yogins.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्तिमत्|स्वस्तिमन्त्
स्वस्तिमत् a. Doing well, happy,<BR>safe; R. 2. 48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्रीयः|स्वस्रीय
स्वस्रीयः स्वस्रेयः A sister's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्रेयः|स्वस्रेय
स्वस्रीयः स्वस्रेयः A sister's son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्रीया
स्वस्रीया, स्वस्रेयी A sister's daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वस्रेयी
स्वस्रीया, स्वस्रेयी A sister's daughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1161-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वागतं|स्वागत
स्वागतं [सुखेन आगतं सुष्ठु आगतं वा]<BR>Welcome, happy arrival (used<BR>chiefly in greeting a person who is put<BR>in the dative case); स्वागतं देव्यै<BR>M. 1; (तस्मै) प्रीतः प्रीतिप्रमुखवचनं स्वागतं<BR>व्याजहार Me. 4; स्वागतं स्वानधीकारान्<BR>प्रभावैरवलंब्य वः । युगपद् युगबाहुभ्यः<BR>प्राप्तेभ्यः प्राज्यविक्रमाः Ku. 2. 18.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वांकिकः|स्वाङ्किक|स्वांकिक|स्वाङ्किकः
स्वांकिकः A drummer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाच्छंद्यं|स्वाच्छन्द्य|स्वाच्छंद्य|स्वाच्छन्द्यं|स्वाछन्द्य
स्वाच्छंद्यं [स्वच्छंदस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>The power of following one's own<BR>will or fancy, wilfulness,<BR>independence; कन्याप्रदानं स्वाच्छंद्यादासुरो धर्म<BR>उच्यते Ms. 3. 31. (स्वाच्छंद्येन,<BR>स्वाच्छंद्यतस् mean ‘wilfully’, ‘voluntarily’).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वातंत्र्यं|स्वातन्त्र्य|स्वातंत्र्य|स्वातन्त्र्यं
स्वातंत्र्यं [स्वतंत्रस्य भावः ष्यञ्]<BR>1<BR>Freedom of will, independence; न<BR>स्त्री स्वातंत्र्यमर्हति Ms. 9. 3; न स्वातंत्र्यं<BR>क्वचित् स्त्रियाः Y. 1. 85.<BR>--2 (In phil.)<BR>Free will.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वातिः|स्वाति
स्वातिः --ती f. [स्वेनैव अतति<BR>अत्-इन् स्त्रीत्वपक्षे वा ङीप्]<BR>1 One of the<BR>wives of the sun.<BR>--2 A sword.<BR>--3<BR>An auspicious constellation.<BR>--4 The<BR>star Arcturus, considered as<BR>forming the fifteenth lunar asterism;<BR>स्वात्यां सागरशुक्तिसंपुटगतं सन्मौक्तिकं<BR>जायते Bh. 2. 67.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--योगः<BR>conjunction with Svāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाती
स्वातिः --ती f. [स्वेनैव अतति<BR>अत्-इन् स्त्रीत्वपक्षे वा ङीप्]<BR>1 One of the<BR>wives of the sun.<BR>--2 A sword.<BR>--3<BR>An auspicious constellation.<BR>--4 The<BR>star Arcturus, considered as<BR>forming the fifteenth lunar asterism;<BR>स्वात्यां सागरशुक्तिसंपुटगतं सन्मौक्तिकं<BR>जायते Bh. 2. 67.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--योगः<BR>conjunction with Svāti.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्
स्वाद् See स्वद्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादः|स्वाद
स्वादः, स्वादनं [स्वद्-स्वाद्-वा घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Taste, flavour.<BR>--2 Tasting, eating,<BR>drinking.<BR>--3 Liking, relishing,<BR>enjoyment.<BR>--4 Sweetening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादनं|स्वादन
स्वादः, स्वादनं [स्वद्-स्वाद्-वा घञ्]<BR>1<BR>Taste, flavour.<BR>--2 Tasting, eating,<BR>drinking.<BR>--3 Liking, relishing,<BR>enjoyment.<BR>--4 Sweetening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादित|स्वादितः
स्वादित p. p.<BR>1 Tasted, relished.<BR>--2 Sweetened.<BR>--3 Pleased.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादिमन्
स्वादिमन् m. Savouriness,<BR>sweetness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादिष्ठ
स्वादिष्ठ a. Very sweet, sweetest<BR>(superl. of स्वादु q. v.); किं स्वादिष्ठं<BR>जगत्यस्मिन् सदा सद्भिः समागमः.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादीयस्
स्वादीयस् a. Sweeter, very sweet<BR>(compar. of स्वादु q. v.);<BR>काव्यामृतरसास्वादः स्वादीयानमृतादपि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वादु|स्वादुः
स्वादु a. [स्वद्-उण्] (दु or द्वी f.;<BR>compar. स्वादीयस्, superl. स्वादिष्ठ)<BR>1<BR>Sweet, pleasant to the taste, sapid,<BR>savoury, dainty, tasteful; तृषा<BR>शुष्यत्यास्ये पिबति सलिलं स्वादु सुरभि<BR>Bh. 3. 92, Me. 24.<BR>--2 Pleasing, agreeable,<BR>attractive, lovely, charming. --m.<BR>1 Sweet flavour, sweetness of taste,<BR>relish.<BR>--2 Treacle, molasses. --n.<BR>Sweetness, relish, taste; कविः करेति<BR>काव्यानि स्वादु जानाति पंडितः Subhāṣ.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-b" target="_blank">Page1162-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--दुः f. A grape.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्न<BR>sweet or choice food, dainties,<BR>delicacies.<BR>--अम्लः the pomegranate<BR>tree.<BR>--खंडः {1} a piece of any sweet<BR>substance. {2} molasses.<BR>--धन्वन् m.<BR>N. of the god of love.<BR>--फलं the<BR>jujube.<BR>--(ला) the jujube tree.<BR>--मूलं a carrot.<BR>--रसा {1} the fruit of<BR>the hog-plum. {2} the Śatāvarī<BR>plant. {3} the root काकोली. {4}<BR>spirituous liquor. {5} a grape.<BR>--शुद्धं {1}<BR>rock-salt. {2} marine-salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाद्वी
स्वाद्वी Vine, grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वानः|स्वान
स्वानः Sound, noise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापः|स्वाप
स्वापः [स्वप्-घञ्]<BR>1 Sleep,<BR>sleeping; U. 1. 37.<BR>--2 Dreaming, dream.<BR>--3 Sleepiness, sloth.<BR>--4 Paralysis,<BR>palsy, insensibility.<BR>--5 Temporary<BR>or partial loss of sensation from<BR>pressure on a nerve, numbness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापतेयं|स्वापतेय
स्वापतेयं [स्वपतेरागतं ढञ्] Wealth,<BR>property; स्वापतेयकृते मर्त्याः किं किं<BR>नाम न कुर्वते Pt. 2. 156; Śi. 14. 9.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वापदः|स्वापद
स्वापदः See श्वापद.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभाविक|स्वाभाविकः
स्वाभाविक a. (की f.) [<BR>स्वभावादागतः ढञ्] Belonging to one's own<BR>nature, innate, inherent, peculiar,<BR>natural; स्वाभाविकं विनीतत्वं तेषां<BR>विनयकर्मणा । मुमूर्च्छ सहजं तेजो हविषेव<BR>हविर्भुजां R. 10. 79, 5. 69, Ku. 6. 71.<BR>--काः m. pl. A sect of Buddhists<BR>who accounted for all things by<BR>the laws of nature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाभाव्यं|स्वाभाव्य
स्वाभाव्यं Naturalness, natural<BR>state or character.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिन्
स्वामिन् a. (नी f.) [स्व-अस्त्यर्थे मिनि<BR>दीर्घः] Possessing proprietory rights.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A proprietor, an owner.<BR>--2<BR>A lord, master; रघुस्वामिनः सच्चरित्रं<BR>Vikr. 18. 107.<BR>--3 A sovereign,<BR>king, monarch.<BR>--4 A husband.<BR>--5<BR>A spiritual preceptor.<BR>--6 A<BR>learned Brāhmaṇa, an ascetic or<BR>religious man of the highest order;<BR>(in this sense usually added to<BR>proper names).<BR>--7 An epithet of<BR>Kārtikeya.<BR>--8 Of Viṣṇu.<BR>--9 Of Śiva.<BR>--10 Of the sage Vātsyāyana.<BR>--11<BR>Of Garuḍa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उपकारकः a<BR>horse.<BR>--कार्यं the business of a<BR>king or master.<BR>--जंघिन् m. N. of<BR>Paraśurāma.<BR>--पाल m. du. the<BR>owner and the keeper (of cattle);<BR>Ms. 8. 5.<BR>--भावः the state of a lord<BR>or owner, ownership.<BR>--मूल a.<BR>originating in or derived from a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">Page1162-c+ 55</a>]<BR>master or lord.<BR>--वात्सल्यं affection<BR>for the husband or lord.<BR>--सद्भावः {1}<BR>existence of a master or owner. {2}<BR>goodness of a master or lord.<BR>--सेवा<BR>{1} the service of a master. {2}<BR>respect for a husband.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिता
स्वामिता --त्वं<BR>1 Ownership,<BR>mastership, proprietory right.<BR>--2<BR>Lordship, sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामित्वं|स्वामित्व
स्वामिता --त्वं<BR>1 Ownership,<BR>mastership, proprietory right.<BR>--2<BR>Lordship, sovereignty.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वामिनी
स्वामिनी A mistress, proprietress.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाम्यं|स्वाम्य
स्वाम्यं<BR>1 Mastership, lordship,<BR>ownership.<BR>--2 Right or title to<BR>property.<BR>--3 Rule, supremacy,<BR>dominion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वायंभुव|स्वायम्भुव|स्वायंभुवः|स्वायम्भुवः
स्वायंभुव a. (वी f.)<BR>1<BR>Relating to Brahman; Ku. 2. 1.<BR>--2<BR>Descended from Brahman; Ś. 7. 9.<BR>--वः An epithet of the first Manu<BR>(as he was a son of Brahman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारसिक
स्वारसिक a. (की f.) Possessing<BR>inherent flavour or sweetness (said<BR>of a poetical composition).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारस्यं|स्वारस्य
स्वारस्यं<BR>1 Possessing natural<BR>flavour or excellence.<BR>--2 Elegance,<BR>fitness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्
स्वाराज् m. An epithet of Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाराज्यं|स्वाराज्य|स्वाराज्यः
स्वाराज्यं<BR>1 The dominion of<BR>heaven, Indra's heaven.<BR>--2<BR>Identification with the self-refulgent<BR>(Brahman).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारोचिषः|स्वारोचिष
स्वारोचिषः, स्वारोचिस् m. N. of<BR>the second Manu; see under मनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वारोचिस्
स्वारोचिषः, स्वारोचिस् m. N. of<BR>the second Manu; see under मनु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वालक्षण्यं|स्वालक्षण्य
स्वालक्षण्यं Peculiar<BR>characteristics, natural disposition; Ms. 9. 19.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाल्प
स्वाल्प a. (ल्पी f.)<BR>1 Little,<BR>small.<BR>--2 Few.<BR>--ल्पं<BR>1 Littleness,<BR>smallness.<BR>--2 Smallness of<BR>number.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वास्थ्यं|स्वास्थ्य
स्वास्थ्यं<BR>1 Self-reliance,<BR>selfdependence.<BR>--2 Fortitude,<BR>resoluteness, firmness.<BR>--3 Sound state,<BR>health.<BR>--4 Prosperity, well-being,<BR>comfortableness.<BR>--5 Ease,<BR>satisfaction, spirits; लब्धं मया स्वास्थ्यं Ś. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वाहा
स्वाहा<BR>1 An oblation or<BR>offering made to all gods<BR>indiscriminately.<BR>--2 N. of the wife of Agni.<BR>--ind. An exclamation used in<BR>offering oblations to the gods (with<BR>dat.); इंद्राय स्वाहा; अग्नये स्वाहा &c.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः utterance of the<BR>exclamation Svāhā;<BR>स्वाहास्वधाकारविवर्जितानि श्मशानतुल्यानि गृहाणि तानि.<BR>--पतिः, --प्रियः Agni or fire.<BR>--भुज्<BR>m. a god, deity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1162-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विद्
स्विद् ind. A particle of<BR>interrogation or inquiry, often<BR>implying ‘doubt’, or ‘surprise’, and<BR>translateable by ‘what’, ‘hey’.<BR>‘hallo’, ‘can it be that’.<BR>It is added to interrogative<BR>pronouns in this sense or to give<BR>an indefinite sense; कास्विदवगुंठनवती<BR>नातिपरिस्फुटशरीरलावण्या Ś. 5. 13;<BR>Me. 14. It is sometimes used<BR>disjunctively in the sense of ‘either,’<BR>‘or’, with नु, उत, वा &c.; see<BR>Ki. 8. 35, 12. 15, 13. 8, 14. 60; आहो<BR>also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विद्
स्विद् {vI.v} {c4c} P. (स्विद्यति, स्विदित or<BR>स्विन्न) To sweat, perspire; स्विद्यति<BR>कूणति वेल्लति K. P. 10; U. 3. 41,<BR>Ku. 7. 77; Māl. 1. 35; स त्वां<BR>पश्यति कंपते पुलकयत्यानंदति स्विद्यति<BR>Gīt. 11. {vII.v} {c1c} A. (स्वेदते, स्विन्न or<BR>स्वेदित)<BR>1 To be anointed.<BR>--2 To be<BR>greasy or unctuous; Māl. 5. 17.<BR>--3 To be disturbed. --Caus. (<BR>स्वेददयति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to perspire.<BR>--2<BR>To heat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्विन्न|स्विन्नः
स्विन्न p. p. [स्विद्-क्त]<BR>1<BR>Perspiring, covered with sweat.<BR>--2<BR>Steeped.<BR>--3 Cooked, boiled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृ
स्वीकृ {c8c} U.<BR>1 To make one's<BR>own, appropriate, claim.<BR>--2 To<BR>take, accept.<BR>--3 To admit, grant,<BR>assume (in argument).<BR>--4 To<BR>assent or agree to, accede.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकरणं|स्वीकरण
स्वीकरणं, स्वीकारः, स्वीकृतिः f.<BR>1<BR>Taking, accepting.<BR>--2 Assenting,<BR>agreeing, promising, an assent, a<BR>promise.<BR>--3 Espousal, wedding,<BR>marriage; Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकारः|स्वीकार
स्वीकरणं, स्वीकारः, स्वीकृतिः f.<BR>1<BR>Taking, accepting.<BR>--2 Assenting,<BR>agreeing, promising, an assent, a<BR>promise.<BR>--3 Espousal, wedding,<BR>marriage; Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीकृतिः|स्वीकृति
स्वीकरणं, स्वीकारः, स्वीकृतिः f.<BR>1<BR>Taking, accepting.<BR>--2 Assenting,<BR>agreeing, promising, an assent, a<BR>promise.<BR>--3 Espousal, wedding,<BR>marriage; Ś. 5.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वीय|स्वीयः
स्वीय a. Own, one's own;<BR>लोकालोकविसारि तेन विहितं स्वीयं विशुद्धं<BR>यशः; S. D. 97.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वुर्च्छ्
स्वुर्च्छ् {c1c} P. (स्वूर्च्छति)<BR>1 To<BR>spread, extend.<BR>--2 To forget.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वृ
स्वृ {c1c} P. (स्वरति; desid.<BR>सिस्वरिषति, सुस्वूर्षति)<BR>1 To sound, recite.<BR>--2<BR>To praise.<BR>--3 To pain or be pained.<BR>--4 To go. --WITH अभि, --प्र to sound.<BR>--सं to pain (Atm.); Bk. 9. 28.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वॄ
स्वॄ {c9c} P. (स्वृणाति) To hurt, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेक्
स्वेक् {c1c} A. (स्वेकते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदः|स्वेद
स्वेदः [स्विद्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Sweat,<BR>perspiration; अंगुलिस्वेदेन<BR>दूष्येरन्नक्षराणि V. 2.<BR>--2 Heat, warmth.<BR>--3<BR>Vapour.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उदं, --उदकं, --जलं<BR>perspiration.<BR>--चूषकः a cooling breeze<BR>(sucking up sweat).<BR>--ज a.<BR>generated by warm vapour or sweat<BR>(said of insects).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनं|स्वेदन
स्वेदनं [स्विद्-णिच्-ल्युट्]<BR>1<BR>Perspiration, sweat.<BR>--2 Causing to sweat.<BR>--3 A diaphoretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनिका
स्वेदनिका<BR>1 A boiler, sauce-pan.<BR>--2<BR>Kitchen.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वेदनी
स्वेदनी A frying-pan, sauce-pan.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैर|स्वैरः
स्वैर a. [स्वस्य ईरम् ईर्-अच् वृद्धिः]<BR>1 Following one's own will or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-c" target="_blank">Page1163-c+ 35</a>]<BR>fancy, self-willed, wanton,<BR>uncontrolled, unrestrained; बद्धमिव<BR>स्वैरगतिर्जनमिह सुखसंगिनमवैमि Ś. 5. 11;<BR>अव्याहतैः स्वैरगतैः स तस्याः R. 2. 5.<BR>--2<BR>Free, unreserved, confidential; as<BR>in स्वैरालाप Mu. 4. 8.<BR>--3 Slow,<BR>mild, gentle; Mu. 1. 2.<BR>--4 Dull,<BR>lazy.<BR>--5 Dependent on one's will,<BR>voluntary, optional.<BR>--रं<BR>Wilfulness, wantonness.<BR>--रं ind.<BR>1 At<BR>will or pleasure, as one likes, at<BR>perfect ease; सार्थाः स्वैरं स्वकीयेषु<BR>चेरुर्वेश्मस्विवाद्रिषु R. 17. 64.<BR>--2 Of<BR>one's own accord, spontaneously.<BR>--3 Slowly, gently, mildly;<BR>U. 3. 2.<BR>--4 Lowly, in an under-tone.<BR>inaudibly, (opp. स्पष्ट); पश्चात्स्वैर<BR>गज इति किल व्याहृतं सत्यवाचा<BR>Ve. 3. 9.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आलापः<BR>confidential talk.<BR>--वृत्त, --वृत्ति, --आचार a.<BR>acting as one likes, following one's<BR>own will, self-willed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरता
स्वैरता --त्वं Wantonness, freedom<BR>of will and action, independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरत्वं
स्वैरता --त्वं Wantonness, freedom<BR>of will and action, independence.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिणी
स्वैरिणी A loose or unchaste<BR>woman, a wanton woman, an<BR>adulteress; Y. 1. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिन्
स्वैरिन् a. Self-willed, wanton,<BR>unrestrained, uncontrolled.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वैरिंध्री|स्वैरिन्ध्री
स्वैरिंध्री See सरैंध्री.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोरसः|स्वोरस
स्वोरसः The residue or sediment<BR>of oily substances ground with a<BR>stone.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्वोवशीयं
स्वोवशीयं Happiness, prosperity<BR>(especially as regards future life).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह|हं|हः
ह ind. An emphatic particle<BR>used to lay stress on the preceding<BR>word and translateable by ‘verily’,<BR>‘indeed’, ‘certainly’, &c.; but it<BR>is often used expletively without<BR>any particular signification,<BR>especially in Vedic literature; तस्य ह शतं<BR>जाया बभूवुः; तस्य ह पर्वतनारदौ गृह<BR>ऊषतुः &c. Ait. Br. It is sometimes<BR>used as a vocative particle and<BR>rarely of disdain or laughter.<BR>--हः<BR>1 A form of Śiva.<BR>--2<BR>Water.<BR>--3 Sky.<BR>--4 Blood.<BR>--5 A<BR>cipher.<BR>--6 Meditation.<BR>--7<BR>Auspiciousness.<BR>--8 Paradise.<BR>--9 Heaven.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-1b" target="_blank">Page1163-1b+ 15</a>]<BR>--10 Drying.<BR>--11 Fear.<BR>--12<BR>Knowledge.<BR>--13 The moon.<BR>--14 N. of<BR>Viṣṇu.<BR>--15 War, battle.<BR>--16 A<BR>horse.<BR>--17 Pride.<BR>--18<BR>Horripilation.<BR>--19 A physician.<BR>--20 Cause,<BR>motive.<BR>--हं<BR>1 The Supreme Spirit.<BR>--2 Pleasure, delight.<BR>--3 A<BR>weapon.<BR>--4 The sparkling of a gem.<BR>--5 The sound of a lute (--m. also<BR>according to some in these senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसः|हंस
हंसः [हस्-अच्-पृषो˚ वर्णागमः]<BR>(said to be derived from हस्; cf.<BR>भवेद्वर्णागमाद् हंसः Sk.)<BR>1 A swan,<BR>goose, duck, flamingo; हंसाः संप्रति<BR>पांडवा इव वनादज्ञातचर्यां गताः<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-1c" target="_blank">Page1163-1c+ 15</a>]<BR>Mk. 5. 6; न शोभते सभामध्ये हंसमध्ये बको<BR>यथा Subhāṣ., R. 17. 25. (the<BR>description of this bird, as given<BR>by Sanskrit writers, is more<BR>poetical than real; he is described as<BR>forming the vehicle of the god<BR>Brahman, and as ready to fly<BR>towards the Mānasa lake at the<BR>approach of rains; cf. मानस.<BR>According to a very general poetical<BR>convention he is represented as being<BR>gifted with the peculiar power of<BR>separating milk from water; e. g.<BR>सारं ततो ग्राह्यमपास्य फल्गु हंसो यथा<BR>क्षीरमिवांबुमध्यात् Pt. 1; हंसो हि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-a" target="_blank">Page1164-a+ 56</a>]<BR>क्षीरमादत्ते तन्मिश्रा वर्जयत्यपः Ś. 6. 27;<BR>नीरक्षीरविवेके हंसालस्यं त्वमेव तनुषे चेत् ।<BR>विश्वस्मिन्नधुनान्यः कुलव्रतं पालयिष्यति<BR>कः Bv. 1. 13; see Bh. 2. 18 also).<BR>--2 The Supreme Soul, Brahman.<BR>--3 The individual soul, (जीवात्मन्).<BR>--4 One of the vital airs.<BR>--5 The<BR>sun.<BR>--6 Śiva.<BR>--7 Viṣṇu.<BR>--8<BR>Kāmadeva.<BR>--9 An unambitious<BR>monarch.<BR>--10 An ascetic of a<BR>particular order.<BR>--11 A spiritual<BR>preceptor.<BR>--12 One free from malice,<BR>a pure person.<BR>--13 A mountain.<BR>--14 Envy, malice.<BR>--15 A buffalo.<BR>--सौ (m. pl.). N. of a tribe<BR>said to live in the Plakṣa-Dvīpa.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंशु a. white.<BR>--अंघ्रिः<BR>vermilion.<BR>--अधिरूढा an epithet<BR>of Sarasvatī.<BR>--अभिख्यं silver.<BR>--आरूढः N. of Brahman.<BR>--कांता a<BR>female goose.<BR>--कीलकः a<BR>particular mode of sexual enjoyment.<BR>--कूटः {1} N. of the peaks of the<BR>Himālaya. {2} the hump on the<BR>shoulder of an ox; (for अंसकूट).<BR>--गति a. having a swan's gait,<BR>stalking in a stately manner.<BR>--गद्गदा a sweetly speaking woman.<BR>--गामिनी {1} a woman having<BR>graceful gait like that of a swan;<BR>Ms. 3. 10. {2} N. of Brahmāṇī.<BR>--तूलः<BR>--लं the soft feathers or down of a<BR>goose.<BR>--दाहनं aloe-wood.<BR>--नादः<BR>the cackling of a goose.<BR>--नादिनी<BR>a woman of a particular class<BR>(described as having a slender waist,<BR>large hips, the gait of an elephant<BR>and the voice of a cuckoo;<BR>गजेंद्रगमना तन्वी कोकिलालापसंयुता । नितंबे<BR>गुर्विणी या स्यात् सा स्मृता हंसनादिनी).<BR>--पादं vermilion.<BR>--माला a flight of<BR>swans; Ku. 1. 30.<BR>--युवन् m. a<BR>young goose or swan.<BR>--रथः,<BR>--वाहनः epithets of Brahman.<BR>--राजः a<BR>king of geese.<BR>--लोमशं green<BR>sulphate of iron.<BR>--लोहकं brass.<BR>--श्रेणी<BR>a line of geese.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1163-1" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसकः|हंसक
हंसकः<BR>1 A goose, flamingo.<BR>--2<BR>An ornament for the ankles (नूपुर<BR>or पादकटक); सरित इव<BR>सविभ्रमप्रपातप्रणदितहंसकभूषणा विरेजुः Śi. 7. 23<BR>(where the word is used in the<BR>first sense also; see हंस above for<BR>other senses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसिका
हंसिका, हंसी A female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंसी
हंसिका, हंसी A female goose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंहो
हंहो ind.<BR>1 A vocative particle<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">Page1164-b+ 54</a>]<BR>corresponding to, ‘ho,’ ‘hallo’;<BR>हंहो चिन्मयचित्तचंद्रमणयः संवर्धयध्वं<BR>रसान् Chandr. 1. 2.<BR>--2 A particle<BR>expressing haughtiness or contempt.<BR>--3 A particle of interrogation. (In<BR>dramas it is mostly used as a form<BR>of address by characters of the<BR>middling class; हंहो बाह्मण मा कुष्य<BR>Mu. 1).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हक्कः|हक्क
हक्कः The calling of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंजा|हञ्जा
हंजा, हंजे ind. A vocative<BR>particle used in addressing a female<BR>attendant or maidservant; हंजे<BR>कंचणमाले अहं ईदिसी कडुभासिणी<BR>Ratn. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंजे|हञ्जे
हंजा, हंजे ind. A vocative<BR>particle used in addressing a female<BR>attendant or maidservant; हंजे<BR>कंचणमाले अहं ईदिसी कडुभासिणी<BR>Ratn. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्
हट् {c1c} P. (हटति, हटित) To shine,<BR>be bright.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्टः|हट्ट
हट्टः [हट्-ट टस्य नेत्वम्] A<BR>market, a fair.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चोरकः a thief<BR>who steals from fairs and markets.<BR>--विलासिनी {1} a wanton woman,<BR>prostitute, common woman. {2}<BR>a sort of perfume. {3} turmeric.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हट्टी
हट्टी A small market or fair.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठ्
हठ् {c1c} P. (हठति)<BR>1 To leap,<BR>jump.<BR>--2 To be wicked.<BR>--3 To<BR>oppress.<BR>--4 To bind to a post.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हठः|हठ
हठः<BR>1 Violence, force.<BR>--2<BR>Oppression, rapine. हठेन and हठात्<BR>are used adverbially in the sense of<BR>‘forcibly’, ‘violently’, ‘suddenly,<BR>‘against one's will’; अंबालिका च<BR>चंडवर्मणा हठात् परिणेतुमात्मभवनमनीयत<BR>Dk.; वानरान् वारयामास हठेन मधुरेण<BR>च Rām.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--योगः a<BR>particular mode of Yoga or practising<BR>abstract meditation, (so called, as<BR>distinguished from राजयोग q. v.,<BR>because it is very difficult to practise;<BR>it may be performed in various<BR>ways, such as by standing on one<BR>leg, holding up the arms, inhaling<BR>smoke with the head inverted &c.).<BR>--विद्या the science of forced<BR>meditation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडिः|हडि
हडिः Wooden fetters or stocks.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हडिकः|हडिक
हडि(ड्डि)कः, हड्डिः A man of<BR>the lowest caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डिकः|हड्डिक
हडि(ड्डि)कः, हड्डिः A man of<BR>the lowest caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डिः|हड्डि
हडि(ड्डि)कः, हड्डिः A man of<BR>the lowest caste.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हड्डं|हड्ड
हड्डं A bone.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जं<BR>marrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंडा|हण्डा
हंडा ind. A vocative particle<BR>used in addressing a female<BR>of inferior rank, or by equals of the<BR>lowest^1 caste in addressing each<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-c" target="_blank">Page1164-c+ 56</a>]<BR>other; हंडे हंजे हलाह्वाने नीचां चेटीं सखीं<BR>प्रति Ak. --f. A large earthen<BR>vessel (?).<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंडिका|हण्डिका
हंडिका, हंडी An earthen pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंडी|हण्डी
हंडिका, हंडी An earthen pot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंडे|हण्डे
हंडे ind. See हंडा ind.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हद्
हद् {c1c} A. (हदते, हन्न) To void<BR>excrement, evacuate or discharge feces.<BR>--Desid. (जिहत्सते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हदनं|हदन
हदनं Voiding excrement,<BR>evacuation of ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्नं|हन्न|हन्नः
हन्नं Excrement, ordure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्
हन् {c2c} P. (हंति, जघान, अवधीत्,<BR>अवधिष्ट-अहत; हनिष्यति, हंतुं, हत; pass.<BR>हन्यते; caus. घातयति-ते; desid. जिघांसति)<BR>1<BR>To kill, slay, destroy, strike down;<BR>त्रयश्च दूषणखरत्रिमूर्धानो रणे हताः U. 2,<BR>15; हतमपि च हंत्येव मदनः Bh. 3. 18.<BR>--2 To strike, beat; चंडी चंड<BR>हंतुमभ्युद्यता मां विद्युद्दाम्ना मेघराजीव विंध्यं<BR>M. 3. 20, Śi. 7. 56.<BR>--3 To hurt, injure,<BR>afflict, torment; as in कामहत.<BR>--4 To<BR>put down, abandon; तृष्णां छिंद्धि भज<BR>क्षमां जहि मदं Bh. 2. 77.<BR>--5 To<BR>remove, take away, destroy;<BR>अंभोजिनीवननिवासविलासमेव हंसस्य हंति नितरां<BR>कुपितो विधाता Bh. 2. 18.<BR>--6 To<BR>conquer, overthrow, defeat, overcome;<BR>विघ्नैः सहस्रगुणितैरपि हन्यमानाः<BR>प्रारब्धमुत्तमजना न परित्यजंति Subhāṣ.<BR>--7<BR>To hinder, obstruct.<BR>--8 To mar,<BR>spoil; Ki. 2. 37.<BR>--9 To raise;<BR>तुरगखुरहतस्तथा हि रेणुः Ś. 1. 32.<BR>--10 To<BR>multiply (in math.).<BR>--11 To go<BR>(rarely used in classical literature<BR>in this sense; and when used it is<BR>regarded as a fault of composition);<BR>e. g. कुंजं हंति कृशोदरी S. D. 7; or<BR>तीर्थांतरेषु स्नानेन समुपार्जितसत्कृतिः ।<BR>सुरस्रोतस्विनीमेष हंति संप्रति सादरं K. P. 7 (given<BR>as an instance of the दोष called<BR>असमर्थत्प). --Caus.<BR>1 To cause to be<BR>killed, kill, slay.<BR>--2 To destroy,<BR>ruin, mar, spoil; Pt. 1. 363. --WITH<BR>अति to injure excessively.<BR>--अंतर्<BR>to strike in the middle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत|हतः
हत p. p. [हन्-क्त]<BR>1 Killed, slain.<BR>--2 Hurt, struck, injured; Mu. 3. 1.<BR>--3 Lost, perished.<BR>--4 Deprived or<BR>bereft of.<BR>--5 Disappointed,<BR>frustrated; वयं तत्वान्वेषात् हताः Ś. 1. 24.<BR>--6<BR>Impeded, obstructed.<BR>--7 Utterly ruined,<BR>extinguished, destroyed.<BR>--8<BR>Multiplied, see हन्. It is often used as the<BR>first member of comp. in the sense<BR>of ‘wretched’, ‘miserable’, ‘accursed’<BR>‘worthless’; अनुशयदुःखायेदं हतहृदयं<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">Page1165-a+ 56</a>]<BR>संप्रति विबुद्धं Ś. 6. 6; Māl. 9. 28;<BR>कुर्यामुपेक्षां हतजीवितेऽस्मिन् R. 14. 65;<BR>हतविधिलसितानां ही विचित्रो विपाकः<BR>Śi. 11. 64.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Killing, striking.<BR>--2<BR>Multiplication.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आश a. {1}<BR>bereft of hope, hopeless, desponding.<BR>{2} weak, powerless. {3} cruel,<BR>merciless. {4} barren. {5} low, vile,<BR>wretched, accursed, villainous.<BR>--कंटक a.<BR>freed from thorns or foes.<BR>--चित्त a.<BR>bewildered, confounded.<BR>--त्विष् a.<BR>dimmed in lustre; R. 3. 15.<BR>--दैव<BR>a. ill-fated, luckless, ill-starred.<BR>--प्रभाव --वीर्य a. bereft of power<BR>or vigour; Ku. 2. 21.<BR>--बुद्धि a.<BR>deprived of sense, senseless.<BR>--भाग,<BR>--भाग्य ill-fated, unfortunate.<BR>--मूर्खः a dolt, blockhead.<BR>--रथः a chariot<BR>of which the horses and the<BR>charioteer are slain.<BR>--लक्षण a. devoid<BR>of auspicious marks, unlucky.<BR>--शेष<BR>a. surviving.<BR>--श्री, --संपद् a. reduced<BR>to indigence, impoverished.<BR>--साध्वस a. freed from fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1164-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतक|हतकः
हतक a. [हत इव नष्टप्रायत्वात् कन्]<BR>Miserable, ill-bred, wretched, low,<BR>vile; (mostly at the end of comp.),<BR>न खलु विदितास्ते तत्र<BR>निवसंतश्चाणक्यहतकेन Mu. 2; दूषिताः स्थ परिभूताः स्थ<BR>रामहतकेन U. 1.<BR>--कः A low person,<BR>coward.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हतिः|हति
हतिः f. [हन्-भावे-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Killing,<BR>destruction.<BR>--2 Striking,<BR>wounding.<BR>--3 A blow, stroke.<BR>--4 Loss,<BR>failure.<BR>--5 A defect.<BR>--6<BR>Multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्नुः|हत्नु
हत्नुः<BR>1 A weapon.<BR>--2 A disease or<BR>sickness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हत्या
हत्या [हन्-भावे क्यप्] Killing,<BR>slaying, slaughter, murder, particularly<BR>criminal killing; as in भ्रूणहत्या,<BR>गोहत्या &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हन्
हन् a. Killing, slaying, destroying<BR>(at the end of comp.); as in वृत्रहन्,<BR>पितृहन्, मातृहन्, ब्रह्महन् &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनः|हन
हनः Killing, slaying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हननं|हनन|हननः
हननं [हन्-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Killing,<BR>slaying, striking.<BR>--2 Hurting, injuring.<BR>--3 Multiplication.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंतुः|हन्तु|हन्तुः
हंतुः<BR>1 Killing, death.<BR>--2 A bull.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंतृ|हन्तृ
हंतृ a. (त्री f.) [हन्-तृच्]<BR>1 One<BR>who strikes or kills, striking, killer;<BR>Ms. 5. 34; Ku. 2. 20.<BR>--2 One who<BR>removes, destroys, counteracts &c.<BR>--m.<BR>1 A slayer, killer.<BR>--2 A thief,<BR>robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हथः|हथ
हथः<BR>1 A stroke, blow.<BR>--2 Killing.<BR>--3 Death.<BR>--4 A man who is sad, or<BR>depressed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनु|हनुः
हनु --नू m. f. [हन्-उन् स्त्रीत्वे वा उञ्]<BR>The chin.<BR>--नु f.<BR>1 That which<BR>injures life.<BR>--2 A weapon.<BR>--3 A<BR>disease, sickness.<BR>--4 Death.<BR>--5 A kind<BR>of drug.<BR>--6 A wanton woman,<BR>prostitute.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रहः locked jaw.<BR>--मूलं the root of the jaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनू
हनु --नू m. f. [हन्-उन् स्त्रीत्वे वा उञ्]<BR>The chin.<BR>--नु f.<BR>1 That which<BR>injures life.<BR>--2 A weapon.<BR>--3 A<BR>disease, sickness.<BR>--4 Death.<BR>--5 A kind<BR>of drug.<BR>--6 A wanton woman,<BR>prostitute.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रहः locked jaw.<BR>--मूलं the root of the jaw.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनुमत्|हनुमन्त्
हनु(नू)मत् m. N. of a powerful<BR>monkey-chief. [He was the son of<BR>Añjanā by the god Wind or Marut and<BR>hence called Māruti. He is represented<BR>as a monkey of extraordinary strength<BR>and prowess which he manifested on<BR>several critical occasions on behalf of<BR>Rāma whom he regarded as the idol of<BR>his heart. When Sītā was carried off by<BR>Rāvaṇa, he crossed the sea and brought<BR>news about her to his lord. He played<BR>a very important part in the great war<BR>at Laṅkā.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनूमत्|हनूमन्त्
हनु(नू)मत् m. N. of a powerful<BR>monkey-chief. [He was the son of<BR>Añjanā by the god Wind or Marut and<BR>hence called Māruti. He is represented<BR>as a monkey of extraordinary strength<BR>and prowess which he manifested on<BR>several critical occasions on behalf of<BR>Rāma whom he regarded as the idol of<BR>his heart. When Sītā was carried off by<BR>Rāvaṇa, he crossed the sea and brought<BR>news about her to his lord. He played<BR>a very important part in the great war<BR>at Laṅkā.].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हनूषः|हनूष
हनूषः A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंत|हन्त
हंत ind. A particle implying<BR>1 Joy, surprise, flurry (oh!); हंत<BR>भो लब्धं मया स्वास्थ्यं Ś. 4; हंत प्रवृत्तं<BR>संगीतकं M. 1.<BR>--2 Compassion, pity;<BR>पुत्रक हंत ते धानाकाः G. M.<BR>--3 Grief<BR>(oh!, alas!); हंत धिङ् मामधन्यं<BR>U. 1. 43; स्मरामि हंत स्मरामि U. 1;<BR>काचमूल्येन विक्रीतो हंत चिंतामणिर्मया<BR>Śānti. 1. 12, Me. 104.<BR>--4 Good luck or<BR>benediction.<BR>--5 It is often used as<BR>an inceptive particle; हंत ते<BR>कथयिष्यामि Rām.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--उक्तिः f.<BR>uttering the word ‘alas!’, tenderness,<BR>compassion.<BR>--कारः {1} the<BR>exclamation ‘hanta’. {2} an offering to be<BR>presented to a guest; निवीती<BR>हंतकारेण मनुष्यांस्तर्पयेदथ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हम्
हम् ind. An exclamation<BR>expressive of anger, courtesy, or<BR>respect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंबा|हम्बा
हंबा(भा) The lowing of cattle.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रवः lowing of cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हंभा|हम्भा
हंबा(भा) The lowing of cattle.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--रवः lowing of cattle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हय्
हय् {c1c} P. (हयति, हयित)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To worship.<BR>--3 To sound.<BR>--4 To<BR>be weary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयः|हय
हयः [हय्-हि-वा अच्]<BR>1 A horse;<BR>Bg. 1. 14; Ms. 8. 296, R. 9. 10.<BR>--2 A man<BR>of a particular class; see under<BR>अश्व.<BR>--3 The number ‘seven’.<BR>--4 N. of Indra.<BR>--5 (In prosody)<BR>A foot of four short syllables.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्यक्षः a superintendent<BR>of horses.<BR>--अरिः the fragrant<BR>oleander.<BR>--आयुर्वेदः veterinary science.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-c" target="_blank">Page1165-c+ 57</a>]<BR>--आरूढः a horseman, rider.<BR>--आरोहः {1} a rider. {2} riding.<BR>--आसनी<BR>the gum-olibanum tree.<BR>--इष्टः<BR>barley.<BR>--उत्तमः an excellent horse.<BR>--कोविद a. versed in the science<BR>of horses-their management,<BR>training &c.<BR>--ग्रीवः N. of a form<BR>of Viṣṇu.<BR>--(वा) N. of Durgā.<BR>--ज्ञः a horse-dealer, groom,<BR>jockey.<BR>--द्विषत् m. the buffalo.<BR>--प्रियः<BR>barley.<BR>--प्रिया the Kharjūrī tree.<BR>--मारः, --मारकः the fragrant<BR>oleander.<BR>--मारणः the sacred fig-tree.<BR>--मेधः a horse-sacrifice;<BR>Y. 1. 181.<BR>--वाहनः an epithet of<BR>Kubera.<BR>--शाला a stable for horses.<BR>--शास्त्रं the art or science of<BR>training and managing horses.<BR>--संग्रहणं<BR>the restraining or curbing of horses.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयंकषः|हयङ्कष|हयंकष|हयङ्कषः
हयंकषः<BR>1 A driver, charioteer.<BR>--2 N. of Mātali, the charioteer of<BR>Indra.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हयी
हयी A female horse, mare.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर|हरः
हर a. (रा --री f.) [हृ-अच्]<BR>1<BR>Taking away, removing,<BR>depriving one of; as in खेदहर, शोकहर.<BR>--2<BR>Bringing, conveying, carrying,<BR>taking; अपथहराः Ki. 5. 50;<BR>R. 12. 51.<BR>--3 Seizing, grasping.<BR>--4<BR>Attracting, captivating.<BR>--5<BR>Claiming, entitled to; as in रिक्थहर<BR>&c.; Mu. 2. 19.<BR>--6 Occupying;<BR>Ku. 1. 50.<BR>--7 Dividing.<BR>--रः<BR>1 Śiva;<BR>Ku. 1. 50, 3. 40, 67, Me. 7.<BR>--2<BR>N. of Agni or fire.<BR>--3 An ass.<BR>--4<BR>A divisor.<BR>--5 The denominator<BR>of a fraction.<BR>--6 The act of<BR>seizing, taking.<BR>--7 A seizer, ravisher.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गौरी one of the forms<BR>of Śiva and Pārvatī conjoined<BR>(अर्धनारीनटेश्वर).<BR>--चूडामणिः ‘Śiva's<BR>crest-gem’, the moon.<BR>--तेजस् n.<BR>quick-silver.<BR>--नेत्रं {1} Śiva's eye.<BR>{2} the number ‘three’.<BR>--वीजं<BR>‘Śiva's seed’, quick-silver.<BR>--शेखरा ‘Śiva's crest’, the Ganges.<BR>--सूनुः Skanda; R. 11. 83.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरकः|हरक
हरकः<BR>1 A stealer, thief.<BR>--2 A<BR>rogue.<BR>--3 A divisor.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरणं|हरण
हरणं [हृ-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Seizing,<BR>taking.<BR>--2 Carrying away, carrying<BR>off, removing, stealing;<BR>कन्याहरणं Ms. 3. 33, R. 11. 74.<BR>--3<BR>Depriving of, destroying; as in<BR>प्राणहरणं.<BR>--4 Dividing.<BR>--5 A gift to a<BR>student.<BR>--6 The arm.<BR>--7 Semen<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-a" target="_blank">Page1166-a+ 57</a>]<BR>virile.<BR>--8 Gold.<BR>--9 A nuptial<BR>present. (= यौतक q. v.)<BR>--10 A shell,<BR>cowrie<BR>--11 Boiling water.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1165-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरि|हरिः
हरि a. [हृ-इन्]<BR>1 Green,<BR>greenishyellow.<BR>--2 Tawny, bay,<BR>reddishbrown (कपिल); हरियुग्यं हरिस्तस्मै<BR>प्रजिबाय पुरंदरः R. 12. 84, 3. 43.<BR>--3<BR>Yellow.<BR>--रिः<BR>1 N. of Viṣṇu;<BR>हरिर्यथैकः पुरुषोत्तमः स्मृतः R. 3. 49.<BR>--2 N. of Indra; R. 3. 55, 68,<BR>8. 79.<BR>--3 N. of Śiva.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>Brahman.<BR>--5 N. of Yama.<BR>--6 The sun.<BR>--7 The moon.<BR>--8 A man.<BR>--9 A ray<BR>of light.<BR>--10 Fire.<BR>--11 Wind.<BR>--12<BR>A lion; Bv. 1. 50, 51.<BR>--13 A<BR>horse.<BR>--14 A horse of Indra;<BR>सत्यमतीत्य हरितो हरींश्च वर्तंते वाजिनः<BR>Ś. 1, 7. 7.<BR>--15 An ape, a monkey;<BR>U. 3. 45, R. 12. 57.<BR>--16 The<BR>cuckoo.<BR>--17 A frog.<BR>--18 A parrot.<BR>--19 A snake.<BR>--20 The tawny green<BR>or yellow colour.<BR>--21 A peacock.<BR>--22 N. of the poet Bhartṛhari.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षः {1} a lion. {2} N. of<BR>Kubera. {3} of Śiva.<BR>--अश्वः {1} Indra.<BR>{2} Śiva.<BR>--कांत a. {1} dear to Indra.<BR>{2} beautiful as a lion<BR>--केलीयः<BR>the country called वंग q. v.<BR>--केशः<BR>N. of Śiva.<BR>--गंधं a kind of sandal.<BR>--चंदनः --नं {1} a kind of yellow<BR>sandal (the wood or tree); R. 3. 59,<BR>6. 60; Ś. 7. 2; Ku. 5. 69. {2} one<BR>of the five trees of paradise; पंचैते<BR>देवतरवो मंदारः पारिजातकः । संतानः<BR>कल्पवृक्षश्च पुंसि वा हरिचंदनं Ak. (--नं.)<BR>{1} moonlight. {2} saffron. {3} the<BR>filament of a lotus.<BR>--तालः (by<BR>some regarded as derived from<BR>हरित) a kind of yellow-coloured<BR>pigeon.<BR>--(लं) yellow orpiment;<BR>H. D. 1; Śi. 4. 21; Ku. 7. 23,<BR>33.<BR>--(ली) {1} the Dūrvā grass. {2}<BR>a streak or line in the sky. {3}<BR>= हरितालिका (1).<BR>--तालकः a kind of<BR>yellow-coloured pigeon.<BR>--(कं) {1}<BR>yellow orpiment. {2} a theatrical<BR>decoration.<BR>--तालिका {1} the fourth<BR>day of the bright half of<BR>Bhādrapada. {2} the Dūrvā plant.<BR>--तुरंगमः<BR>N. of Indra.<BR>--दासः a worshipper<BR>or votary of Viṣṇu.<BR>--दिनं a<BR>particular day sacred to Viṣṇu.<BR>--देवः<BR>the asterism Śravaṇa.<BR>--द्रवः {1} a<BR>green fluid. {2} powder of the<BR>blossoms of the Nāgakeśara tree.<BR>--द्रुः<BR>a tree.<BR>--द्वारं N. of a celebrated<BR>Tīrtha or sacred bathing-place.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-b" target="_blank">Page1166-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--नेत्रं {1} the eye of Viṣṇu. {2} the<BR>white lotus.<BR>--(त्रः) an owl.<BR>--पदं<BR>the vernal equinox.<BR>--पर्णं a radish.<BR>--प्रियः {1} the Kadamba tree. {2} a<BR>conch-shell. {3} a fool. {4} a madman.<BR>{5} Śiva.<BR>--(यं) the root Uśīra. {2} a<BR>sort of sandal.<BR>--प्रिया {1} Lakṣmī. {2}<BR>the sacred basil. {3} the earth. {4}<BR>the twelfth day of a lunar fortnight.<BR>--भक्तः a worshipper of Viṣṇu.<BR>--भुज् m. a snake.<BR>--मंथः, --मंथकः a<BR>chick-pea.<BR>--लोचनः {1} a crab. {2}<BR>an owl.<BR>--वंशः N. of a celebrated<BR>work by Vyāsa supplementary to<BR>the Mahābhārata.<BR>--वर्षः N. of one<BR>of the nine divisions of<BR>Jambudvīpa.<BR>--वल्लभा {1} Lakṣmī. {2} the<BR>sacred basil.<BR>--वासरः ‘Viṣṇu's day,’<BR>the eleventh day of a lunar<BR>fortnight (एकादशी).<BR>--वाहनः {1} Garuḍa.<BR>{2} Indra. ˚दिश् f. the east.<BR>--वीजं<BR>yellow orpiment.<BR>--शरः an epithet<BR>of Śiva (Viṣṇu having served<BR>Śiva as the shaft which burnt<BR>down ‘the three cities’ or cities of<BR>the demon Tripura).<BR>--सखः a<BR>Gandharva.<BR>--संकीर्तनं repeating the<BR>name of Viṣṇu.<BR>--सुतः, --सूनुः<BR>N. of Arjuna.<BR>--हयः {1} Indra;<BR>R. 9. 18. {2} the sun. {3} N. of<BR>Skanda. {4} of Gaṇeśa.<BR>--हरः a<BR>particular form of deity consisting<BR>of Viṣṇu and Śiva conjoined.<BR>˚आत्मकः {1} N. of Garuḍa.<BR>{2} of Śiva's bull.<BR>--हेतिः f. {1}<BR>the rainbow; कथमवलोकयेयमधुना<BR>हरिहेतिमतीः (ककुभः) Māl. 9. 18.<BR>{2} the discus of Viṣṇu. ˚हूतिः the<BR>ruddy goose; Śi. 9. 15.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिकः|हरिक
हरिकः [हरि-संज्ञायां कन्]<BR>1 A horse<BR>of a yellowish or tawny colour.<BR>--2<BR>A thief.<BR>--3 A gambler (with dice)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिण|हरिणः
हरिण a. (णी f.) [हृ-इनन्]<BR>1<BR>Pale, whitish.<BR>--2 Reddish or<BR>yellowish^1 white.<BR>--णः<BR>1 A deer, an<BR>antelope; (said to be of five<BR>kinds: --हरिणश्चापि विज्ञेयः पंचभेदोऽत्र भैरव ।<BR>ऋष्यः खड्गो रुरुश्चैव पृषतश्च मृगस्तथा<BR>Kālikā P.); अपि प्रसन्नं हरिणेषु ते मनः<BR>Ku. 5. 35.<BR>--2 The white colour.<BR>--3 A<BR>goose.<BR>--4 The sun.<BR>--5 Viṣṇu.<BR>--6<BR>Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्ष a. deer-eyed,<BR>fawn-eyed.<BR>--(क्षः) N. of Śiva.<BR>--(क्षी)<BR>‘deer-eyed’, a woman with<BR>beautiful eyes.<BR>--अंकः {1} the moon. {2}<BR>camphor.<BR>--कलंकः, --धामनु m. the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-c" target="_blank">Page1166-c+ 56</a>]<BR>moon.<BR>--नयन, --नत्रे, --लोचन a.<BR>deereyed, fawn-eyed.<BR>--नर्तकः a Kinnara.<BR>--हृदय a. deer-hearted, timid.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणकः|हरिणक
हरिणकः A deer; क्व बत हरिणकानां<BR>जीवितं चातिलोलं Ś. 1. 10.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिणी
हरिणी<BR>1 A female deer, doe;<BR>चकितहरिणीप्रेक्षणा Me. 82, R. 9. 55,<BR>14. 69.<BR>--2 One of the four classes<BR>of women (also called चित्रिणी q. v.)<BR>--3 Yellow jasmine.<BR>--4 A good<BR>golden image.<BR>--5 N. of a metre.<BR>--6 The<BR>green colour.<BR>--7 Turmeric.<BR>--8<BR>Madder.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दृश् a. deer-eyed.<BR>(--f.) a deer-eyed woman;<BR>किमभवद्विपिने हरिणीदृशः U. 3. 27.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित्
हरित् a. [हृ-इति]<BR>1 Green, green<BR>ish.<BR>--2 Yellow, yellowish.<BR>--3<BR>Greenish-yellow. --m.<BR>1 The green or<BR>yellow colour.<BR>--2 A horse of the<BR>sun, a bay horse; सत्यमतीत्य<BR>हरितो हरींश्च वर्तते वाजिनः Ś. 1.; दिशो<BR>हरिद्भिर्हरितामिवेश्वरः R. 3. 30, Ku. 2. 43.<BR>--3 A swift horse.<BR>--4 A lion.<BR>--5<BR>The sun<BR>--6 Viṣṇu.<BR>--7 The<BR>kidneybean. --m. n.<BR>1 Grass.<BR>--2 A quarter,<BR>region.<BR>--3 A quarter or point of the<BR>compass; R. 3. 30.<BR>--4 Turmeric<BR>(usually f. only in the last {3}<BR>senses). --COMP.<BR>--अंतः the end of the<BR>quarters (दिगंत); Bv. 1. 60.<BR>--अंतरं different regions, various<BR>quarters; Bv. 1. 15.<BR>--अश्वः the sun;<BR>Ki. 2. 46; R. 3. 22, 18. 23;<BR>Śi. 11. 56. {2} the arka plant.<BR>--गर्भः green<BR>or yellowish Kuśa grass with broad<BR>leaves.<BR>--पर्णं a radish.<BR>--मणिः<BR>(हरिन्मणिः) an emerald;<BR>Śi. 3. 49.<BR>--वर्ण a. greenish, green-coloured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरित|हरितं|हरितः
हरित a. (ता or हरिणी f.) [हृ-इतच्]<BR>1<BR>Green, of a green colour, verdant;<BR>रम्यांतरः कमलिनीहरितैः सरोभिः<BR>Ś. 4. 10; Ku. 4. 14; Me. 21;<BR>Ki. 5. 38.<BR>--2 Tawny.<BR>--3 Dark-blue.<BR>--तः<BR>1 The green colour.<BR>--2 A<BR>lion.<BR>--3 A kind of grass.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अश्मन् m. {1} an emerald. {2}<BR>blue vitriol.<BR>--छद a. green-leaved.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरितकं|हरितक
हरितकं {1} A potherb, green grass;<BR>Śi. 5. 58.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिता
हरिता<BR>1 The Dūrvā grass.<BR>--2<BR>Turmeric.<BR>--3 A brown-coloured<BR>grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिताल|हरितालं|हरितालः
हरिताल &c. See under हरि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिद्रा
हरिद्रा [हरिं पीतवर्णं द्रवति द्रु-गतौ-ड]<BR>1 Turmeric.<BR>--2 The root of<BR>turmeric powdered; see Malli. on<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">Page1167-a+ 59</a>]<BR>N. 22. 49.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आन a. of a<BR>yellow colour.<BR>--(भः) {1} the yellow<BR>colour. {2} Zedoary.<BR>--गणपतिः, --गणेशः a particular form<BR>of the god Gaṇeśa.<BR>--राग, --रागक<BR>a. {1} turmeric-coloured. {2}<BR>unsteady in attachment or affection,<BR>fickle-minded (as a lover); (thus<BR>defined by Halāyudha:<BR>--क्षणमात्रानुरागश्च हरिद्राराग उच्यते).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1166-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिमन्
हरिमन् m.<BR>1 Yellowness.<BR>--2<BR>Paleness.<BR>--3 Time.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरियः|हरिय
हरियः A yellow-coloured horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरिश्चंद्रः|हरिश्चन्द्र|हरिश्चन्द्रः
हरिश्चंद्रः N. of a king of the solar<BR>dynasty. [He was the son of<BR>Triśanku and was famous for his<BR>liberality, probity, and unflinching<BR>adherence to truth. On one occasion<BR>his family-priest Vasiṣṭha<BR>commended his qualities in the presence of<BR>Viśvāmitra, who refused to believe them.<BR>A quarrel thereupon ensued, and it<BR>was at last decided that Viśvāmitra<BR>should himself test the king. The<BR>sage accordingly subjected him to the<BR>most crucial test with a view to see<BR>if he could not be but once made to<BR>swerve from his plighted word. The<BR>king, however, stood the test with<BR>exemplary courage, adhering to his<BR>word though he had to forego the<BR>kingdom, to sell off his wife and<BR>son, and at last, even his own self to<BR>a low-caste man, and-as the last<BR>test, as it were, of his truthfulness<BR>and courage-to be even ready to<BR>put his own wife to death as a<BR>witch! Viśvāmitra there-upon<BR>acknowledged himself vanquished, and<BR>the worthy king was elevated along<BR>with his subjects to heaven].<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरीतकी
हरीतकी The yellow myrobalan<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणुः|हरेणु
हरेणुः<BR>1 Pease, pulse.<BR>--2 A<BR>creeper serving as the boundary of<BR>a village.<BR>--3 N. of Laṅkā.<BR>--णुः f.<BR>1 A respectable woman.<BR>--2 A<BR>copper coloured deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हरेणुकः|हरेणुक
हरेणुकः Pease, pulse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्तृ|हर्त्तृ
हर्तृ a. (र्त्री f.) One who takes<BR>away, seizes, robs, accepts &c. --m.<BR>1 A thief, robber, Bh. 2. 16.<BR>--2<BR>The sun.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मन्|हर्म्मन्
हर्मन् n. Gaping, yawning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्मित|हर्म्मित|हर्म्मितं
हर्मित p. p.<BR>1 Gaped; yawned.<BR>--2<BR>Cast, thrown.<BR>--3 Burnt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्म्यं|हर्म्य|हर्म्म्यं
हर्म्यं [हृ-यत् मुट् च]<BR>1 A palace,<BR>mansion, any large or palatial<BR>building; हर्म्यपृष्ठं समारूढः काकोऽपि<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">Page1167-b+ 55</a>]<BR>गरुडायते Subhāṣ.;<BR>बाह्योद्यानास्थितहरशिरश्चंद्रिकाधौतहर्म्या Me. 7;<BR>Rs. 1. 28; Bk. 8. 36, R. 6. 47;<BR>Ku. 6. 42.<BR>--2 An oven, a fireplace,<BR>hearth.<BR>--3 A fiery pit, abode of<BR>evil spirits, the infernal regions.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगनं --णं the court-yard<BR>of a palace.<BR>--स्थलं the room of<BR>a palace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्य्|हर्य्य्
हर्य् {c1c} P. (हर्यति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To<BR>worship.<BR>--3 To take.<BR>--4 To<BR>threaten.<BR>--5 To be weary or fatigued.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्यतः|हर्यत|हर्य्यत|हर्य्यतः
हर्यतः<BR>1 A horse.<BR>--2 A horse<BR>fit for the Aśvamedha sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षः|हर्ष
हर्षः [हृष्-घञ्]<BR>1 Joy, delight,<BR>pleasure, satisfaction, gladness, rapture,<BR>glee, exultation; हर्षो हर्षो हृदयवसतिः<BR>पंचबाणस्तु बाणः P. R. 1. 22; सहोत्थितः<BR>सैनिकहर्षनिःस्वनैः R. 3. 61.<BR>--2<BR>Thrilling, bristling, erection (of<BR>the hair of the body); as in<BR>रोमहर्ष q. v.<BR>--3 Joy, considered<BR>as one of the 33 or 34<BR>subordinate feelings;<BR>हर्षस्त्विष्टावाप्तेर्मनःप्रसादोऽश्रुगद्गदादिकरः S. D. 195; or<BR>इष्टप्राप्त्यादिजन्मा सुखविशेषो हर्षः R. G.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्वित a. full of joy,<BR>happy; so हर्षाविष्ट.<BR>--उत्कर्षः excess of<BR>happiness or joy, ecstacy.<BR>--उदयः<BR>rise of joy.<BR>--कर a. gratifying,<BR>delighting.<BR>--जड a. dull or<BR>paralyzed with joy; R. 3. 68.<BR>--विवर्धन a. increasing joy.<BR>--स्वनः a<BR>cry or shout of joy.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षक|हर्षकः
हर्षक a. (र्षका or र्षिका f.) [हृष्<BR>णिच् ण्वुल्] Delighting, gladdening,<BR>delightful, pleasing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षण|हर्षणं|हर्षणः
हर्षण (णा or णी f.) [हृष्-णिच् ल्यु]<BR>Causing delight, gladdening,<BR>delightful, pleasant.<BR>--णः<BR>1 N. of<BR>one of the five arrows of<BR>Kāmadeva.<BR>--2 A morbid affection of<BR>the eyes.<BR>--3 A deity presiding over<BR>the funeral ceremonies.<BR>--णं Joy,<BR>delight, happiness, gladdening,<BR>delighting; दुर्हृदामप्रहर्षाय सुहृदां हर्षणाय<BR>च Mb.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षयित्नु|हर्षयित्नुः
हर्षयित्नु a. [हृष्-णिच् इत्नु]<BR>Gladdening, pleasing, delighting. --n. Gold.<BR>--m. A son.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षित|हर्षितः
हर्षित a.<BR>1 Delighted, happy.<BR>--2<BR>Made happy, gladdened.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्षुलः|हर्षुल
हर्षुलः<BR>1 A deer.<BR>--2 A lover.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्
हल् {c1c} P. (हलति, हलित) To plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल|हलं|हलः
हल [हल् घञर्थे करणे क]<BR>1 A plough;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-c" target="_blank">Page1167-c+ 55</a>]<BR>वहसि वपुषि विशदे वसनं जलदाभम् ।<BR>हलहतिभीतिमिलितयमुनाभम्; or हलं कलयते<BR>Gīt. 1.<BR>--2 Deformity, ugliness.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आयुधः an epithet of<BR>Balarāma.<BR>--धर, --भृत् m. {1} a<BR>ploughman. {2} N. of Balarāma; केशव<BR>धृतहलधररूप जय जगदीश हरे Gīt. 1;<BR>अंसन्यस्ते सति हलभृतो मेचके वाससीव<BR>Me. 59.<BR>--भूतिः, --भृतिः f. ploughing,<BR>agriculture, husbandry.<BR>--हतिः f. {1}<BR>striking or drawing along with a<BR>plough. {2} ploughing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हला
हला<BR>1 A female friend.<BR>--2 The<BR>earth.<BR>--3 Water.<BR>--4 Spirituous<BR>liquor. --ind. A vocative particle<BR>used in addressing a female friend;<BR>(only in theatrical language); हला<BR>शकुंतले अत्रैव तावन्मुहूर्तं तिष्ठ Ś. 1;<BR>cf. हंडा also.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलिः|हलि
हलिः<BR>1 A large plough.<BR>--2 A<BR>furrow.<BR>--3 Agriculture.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हलिन्
हलिन् m.<BR>1 A ploughman, an<BR>agriculturist.<BR>--2 Balarāma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--प्रियः the Kadamba tree.<BR>--(या)<BR>spirituous liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

