हल्लीशं|हल्लीश
हल्लीशं(षं)<BR>1 One of the 18<BR>Uparūpakas or minor dramatic<BR>compositions; described as a piece<BR>in one act and consisting mainly<BR>of singing and dancing by one<BR>male and seven, eight, or ten<BR>female performers; see S. D. 555.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of circular dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीषं|हल्लीष
हल्लीशं(षं)<BR>1 One of the 18<BR>Uparūpakas or minor dramatic<BR>compositions; described as a piece<BR>in one act and consisting mainly<BR>of singing and dancing by one<BR>male and seven, eight, or ten<BR>female performers; see S. D. 555.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of circular dance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हल्लीशकः|हल्लीशक
हल्लीशकः Dancing in a ring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवः|हव
हवः [हु-अप्, ह्वे-अप संप्र˚ पृषो˚ वा]<BR>1 An oblation, a sacrifice.<BR>--2<BR>Invocation, prayer.<BR>--3 Calling, a call.<BR>--4 Order, command.<BR>--5 Challenge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवनं|हवन|हवनः
हवनं [हु-भावे ल्युट्]<BR>1 Offering an<BR>oblation with fire.<BR>--2 A sacrifice,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-a" target="_blank">Page1168-a+ 56</a>]<BR>an oblation.<BR>--3 Invocation.<BR>--4<BR>Calling, summoning.<BR>--5<BR>Challenging to fight.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आयुस् m.<BR>fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1167-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवनी
हवनी = हवित्री q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवनीय|हवनीयं
हवनीय a. [हु कर्मणि अनीयर्]<BR>Sacrificial.<BR>--यं<BR>1 Anything fit for an<BR>oblation.<BR>--2 Clarified butter or<BR>ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हवित्री
हवित्री A hole made in the ground<BR>for holding the sacred fire (to<BR>which oblations are offered).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्मत्|हविष्मन्त्
हविष्मत् a. Possessed of oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविष्यं|हविष्य
हविष्यं [हविषे हितं यत्]<BR>1<BR>Anything fit for an oblation;<BR>Ms. 3. 256, 11. 78, 107; Y. 1. 239.<BR>--2<BR>Clarified butter.<BR>--3 Wild rice.<BR>--4<BR>Rice mixed with ghee.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अन्नं food fit to be eaten during<BR>certain holidays or days of fast.<BR>--आशिन्, --भुज् m. fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हविस्
हविस् n. [हूयते हु-कर्मणि असुन्]<BR>1<BR>An oblation or burnt offering in<BR>general; वहति विधिहुतं या हविः<BR>Ś. 1. 1; Ms. 3. 87, 132; 5. 7,<BR>6. 12.<BR>--2 Clarified butter.<BR>--3<BR>Water.<BR>--4 N. of Śiva.<BR>--5 A<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अशनं (हविरशनं)<BR>devouring clarified butter or oblations.<BR>--(नः) fire.<BR>--गंधा (हविंर्गधा) the<BR>Śamī tree.<BR>--गेहं (हविर्गेहं) a house<BR>in which sacrificial oblations are<BR>offered.<BR>--भुज् m. (हविर्भुज्) fire;<BR>अन्वासितमरुंधत्या स्वाहयेव हविर्भुजं<BR>R. 1. 56, 10. 69, 13. 41; Ku. 5. 20,<BR>Śi. 1. 2; Kāv. 2. 168.<BR>--यज्ञः (<BR>हविर्यज्ञः) a kind of sacrifice.<BR>--याजिन्<BR>(हविर्याजिन्) m. a priest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हव्य|हव्यं
हव्य a. [हु-कर्मणि यत्] To be<BR>offered in oblations.<BR>--व्यं<BR>1 Clarified<BR>butter.<BR>--2 An oblation or offering<BR>to the gods (opp. कव्य q. v.).<BR>--3<BR>An oblation in general.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आशः fire.<BR>--कव्यं oblations to the<BR>gods and to the Manes, or spirits<BR>of deceased ancestors; Ms. 1. 94,<BR>3. 97, 128; et seq.<BR>--पाकः an oblation<BR>cooked with butter and milk, or<BR>the pot in which it is cooked.<BR>--वाह्,<BR>--वाह, --वाहन m. ‘the bearer of<BR>oblations’, fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्
हस् {c1c} P. (हसति, हसित)<BR>1 To<BR>smile, laugh (gently); हससि यदि<BR>किंचिदपि दंतरुचिकौमुदी हरति<BR>दरतिमिरमतिघोरं Gīt. 10; Bk. 7. 63, 14. 93.<BR>--2 To laugh at, mock, ridicule (with<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-b" target="_blank">Page1168-b+ 57</a>]<BR>acc.); यमवाप्य विदर्भभूः प्रमुं हसति<BR>द्यामपि शक्रभर्तृकां N. 2. 16.<BR>--3<BR>(Hence) To surpass, excel, throw<BR>into the back-ground; यो जहासेव<BR>वासुदेवं K.; Śi. 1. 71.<BR>--4 To<BR>resemble; श्रिया हसद्भिः कमलानि सस्मितैः<BR>Ki. 8. 44.<BR>--5 To jest, joke.<BR>--6 To open,<BR>bloom, blow; हसद्बंधु जीवप्रसूनैः.<BR>--7 To<BR>brighten up, or to clear up;<BR>भास्वानुदेष्यति हसिष्यति चक्रवालं Subhāṣ.<BR>--Caus. (हासयति-ते) To cause to<BR>smile; Ku. 7. 95.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसः|हस
हसः<BR>1 Laugh, laughter.<BR>--2<BR>Derision.<BR>--3 Merriment, mirth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसनं|हसन
हसनं Laughing, laughter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसनी
हसनी A portable fireplace.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मणिः fire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसंतिका|हसन्तिका
हसंतिका A portable fireplace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसंती|हसन्ती
हसंती<BR>1 A portable fireplace.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of Mallikā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसिका
हसिका Laughter, derision.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हसित|हसितं|हसितः
हसित p. p. [हस्-कर्तरि क्त]<BR>1<BR>Laughed, laughing.<BR>--2 Blown,<BR>expanded.<BR>--तं<BR>1 Laughter.<BR>--2 Joke,<BR>jesting.<BR>--3 The bow of the god of<BR>love.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तः|हस्त|हस्तं
हस्तः [हस्-तन् न इट् Uṇ. 3. 86]<BR>1 The hand; हस्तं गत ‘fallen in the<BR>hand or possession of’, गौतमीहस्ते<BR>विसर्जयिष्यामि Ś. 3 ‘I shall send it<BR>by Gautamī’; so हस्ते पतिता;<BR>हस्तसंनिहितां कुरु &c.; शंभुना दत्तहस्ता<BR>Me. 60 ‘leaning on Śambhu's hand’;<BR>हस्ते-कृ {1} (हस्तेकृत्य-कृत्वा) ‘to take or<BR>seize by the hand, take hold of the<BR>hand, take in hand, take<BR>possession of’; Prov.: --हस्तकंकणं किं दर्पणे<BR>प्रेक्ष्यते Karpūr. ‘sight requires no<BR>mirror’.<BR>--2 The trunk of an elephant;<BR>Ku. 1. 36.<BR>--3 N. of the 13th lunar<BR>mansion consisting of five stars.<BR>--4 The fore-arm, cubit, a measure<BR>of length (equal to 24 angulas or<BR>about 18 inches, being the distance<BR>between the elbow and the tip of<BR>the middle finger).<BR>--5<BR>Hand-writing, signature; धनी वोपगतं दद्यात्<BR>स्वहस्तपरिचिह्नितं Y. 1. 319;<BR>स्वहस्तकालसंपन्नं शासनं 1. 320 ‘bearing date<BR>and signature’; धार्यतामयं प्रियायाः<BR>स्वहस्तः V. 2. ‘the autograph of<BR>my beloved’; 2. 20.<BR>--6 (Hence<BR>fig.) Proof, indication; Mu. 3.<BR>--7 Help, assistance, support; वात्या<BR>खेदं कृशांग्याः सुचिरमवयवैर्दत्तहस्ता<BR>करोति Ve. 2. 21.<BR>--8 A mass, quantity,<BR>abundance (of hair), in comp.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-c" target="_blank">Page1168-c+ 58</a>]<BR>with केश, कच &c.; पाशः पक्षश्च हस्तश्च<BR>कलापार्थाः कचात्परे Ak.;<BR>रतिविगलितबंधे केशहस्ते सुकेश्याः सति कुसुमसनाथे<BR>कं हरेदेष बर्हः V. 4. 10.<BR>--स्तं A pair<BR>of leather-bellows.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अक्षरं<BR>one's own hand or signature, one's<BR>own sign-manual.<BR>--अग्रं the finger<BR>(being the extremity of the hand).<BR>--अंगुलि f. any finger of the hand.<BR>--अभ्यासः contact with the hand.<BR>--अवलंबः, --आलंबनं support of the<BR>hand; दत्तहस्तावलंबे प्रारंभे Ratn. 1. 8<BR>‘being aided or helped on’.<BR>--आमलकं ‘the fruit of the myrobalan<BR>held in the hand’, a phrase used<BR>to denote that which can be clearly<BR>and easily seen or understood; cf.<BR>करतलामलकफलवदखिलं जगदालोकयतां<BR>K. 43.<BR>--आवापः a finger-guard<BR>(ज्याघातवारणं); V. 5, Ś. 6.<BR>--कमलं<BR>{1} a lotus carried in the hand. {2}<BR>a lotus-like hand.<BR>--कौशलं manual<BR>dexterity.<BR>--क्रिया manual work or<BR>performance, handicraft.<BR>--गत,<BR>--गामिन् a. come to hand, fallen into<BR>one's possession, obtained,<BR>secured; त्वं प्रार्थ्यसे हस्तगता ममौभिः<BR>R. 7. 67, 8. 1.<BR>--ग्राहः taking by the hand.<BR>--चापल्यं = हस्तकौशल q. v.<BR>--तलं {1}<BR>the palm of the hand. {2} the tip<BR>of an elephant's trunk.<BR>--तालः<BR>striking the palms together,<BR>clapping the hands.<BR>--तुला<BR>‘hand-balance’, weighing in the hand;<BR>Pt. 2. 79.<BR>--दोषः a slip of the hand.<BR>--धारणं --वारणं warding off a blow (with<BR>the hand).<BR>--पादं the hands and<BR>feet; न मे हस्तपादं प्रसरति Ś. 4.<BR>--पुच्छं the hand below the wrist.<BR>--पृष्ठं the back of the hand.<BR>--प्राप्त,<BR>--वर्तिन्, --स्थ, --स्थित a. {1} held in the<BR>hand. {2} gained, secured.<BR>--प्राप्य<BR>a. easily accessible to the hand;<BR>that can be reached with the hand,<BR>हस्तप्राप्यस्तबकन मितो बालमंदारवृक्षः<BR>Me. 75.<BR>--बिंबं perfuming the body with<BR>unguents.<BR>--मोणः a jewel worn^1 on<BR>the wrist.<BR>--लाघवं {1} manual<BR>readiness or skill. {2} a sleight of the<BR>hand, legerdemain.<BR>--संवाहनं<BR>rubbing or shampooing with the hands;<BR>Me. 96.<BR>--सिद्धिः f. {1} manual<BR>labour, doing with the hands. {2}<BR>hire, wages.<BR>--सूत्रं a bracelet or<BR>thread-string worn on the wrist;<BR>Ku. 7. 25.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तकः|हस्तक
हस्तकः<BR>1 A hand.<BR>--2 The<BR>position of the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1168-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तवत्|हस्तवन्त्
हस्तवत् a. Dexterous, skilful,<BR>clever.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ता
हस्ता The thirteenth lunar<BR>mansion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्ताहस्ति
हस्ताहस्ति ind. Hand to hand;<BR>हस्ताहस्ति जन्यमजनि Dk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिकं|हस्तिक
हस्तिकं A multitude of elephants.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिन्
हस्तिन् a. (नी f.) [हस्तः<BR>शुंडादंडोऽस्त्यस्य इनि]<BR>1 Having hands.<BR>--2<BR>Having a trunk. --m. An elephant;<BR>Ms. 7. 96, 12. 43; (elephants are<BR>said to be of four kinds; भद्र, मंद्र, मृग,<BR>and मिश्र).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अध्यक्षः a<BR>superintendent of elephants.<BR>--आयुर्वेदः a work dealing with the<BR>treatment of the elephant's diseases.<BR>--आरोहः an elephant-driver or rider.<BR>--कक्ष्यः {1} a lion. {2} a tiger.<BR>--कर्णः<BR>the castor-oil plant.<BR>--गिरिः the<BR>city and district of Kāñcī.<BR>--घ्नः<BR>{1} an elephant-killer. {2} a man<BR>--चारिन् m. an elephant-driver.<BR>--दंतः {1} the tusk of an elephant.<BR>{2} a peg projecting from a wall.<BR>--(तं) {1} ivory. {2} a radish.<BR>--दंतकं<BR>a radish.<BR>--नखं a sort of turret<BR>protecting the approach to the gate<BR>of a city or fort.<BR>--पः, --पकः an<BR>elephant-driver or rider; इति घोषयतीव<BR>डिंडिमः करिणो हस्तिपकाहतः क्वणन्<BR>H. 2. 86.<BR>--मदः the ichor issuing from<BR>the temples of an elephant in rut.<BR>--मल्लः {1} N. of Airāvata. {2} of<BR>Gaṇeśa. {3} of Śaṅkha, the eighth<BR>of the chief Nāgas. {4} a heap of<BR>ashes. {5} a shower of dust. {6}<BR>frost.<BR>--यूथः, --थं a herd of elephants.<BR>--वर्चसं the splendour or<BR>magnificence of an elephant.<BR>--वाहः {1}<BR>an elephant-driver. {2} a hook for<BR>driving elephants.<BR>--षङ्गवं a<BR>collection of six elephants.<BR>--स्नानं<BR>= गजस्नानं q. v.; अवशेंद्रियचित्तानां<BR>हस्तिस्नानमिव क्रिया H. 1. 18.<BR>--हस्तः<BR>an elephant's trunk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनपुरं|हस्तिनपुर
हस्तिन(ना)पुरं N. of a city<BR>founded by king Hastin, said to be<BR>situated some fifty miles northeast<BR>of the modern Delhi; it forms a<BR>central scene of action in the<BR>Mahābhārata; its other names are:<BR>--गजाह्वय, नागसाह्वय, नागाह्व, हास्तिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनापुरं|हस्तिनापुर
हस्तिन(ना)पुरं N. of a city<BR>founded by king Hastin, said to be<BR>situated some fifty miles northeast<BR>of the modern Delhi; it forms a<BR>central scene of action in the<BR>Mahābhārata; its other names are:<BR>--गजाह्वय, नागसाह्वय, नागाह्व, हास्तिन.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनी
हस्तिनी<BR>1 A female elephant.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of drug and perfume.<BR>--3 A<BR>woman of a particular class, one of<BR>the four classes into which writers<BR>on erotical science divide women<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-b" target="_blank">Page1169-b+ 56</a>]<BR>(described as having thick lips,<BR>thick hips, thick fingers, large<BR>breasts, dark complexion, and<BR>libidinous appetite); the<BR>Ratimañjarī thus describes her:<BR>--स्थूलाधरा<BR>स्थूलनितंबबिंबा स्थूलांगुलिः स्थूलकुचा सुशीला ।<BR>कामोत्सुका गाढरतिप्रिया च नितांतभोक्त्री<BR>(नितंबखर्वा) खलु हस्तिनी स्यात् (करिणी<BR>मता सा) {8}<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्त्य|हस्त्यः
हस्त्य a.<BR>1 Belonging to the hand.<BR>--2 Done with the hand, manual.<BR>--3 Given with the hand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्र|हस्रः
हस्र a.<BR>1 Smiling.<BR>--2 Stupid,<BR>foolish, ignorant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहलं|हहल
हहलं A kind of deadly poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हहा
हहा m. A kind of Gandharva;<BR>cf. हाहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा ind. A particle expressing<BR>1 Grief, dejection, pain, as<BR>expressed by ‘ah’, ‘alas!,’ ‘woe<BR>me’, in English; हा प्रिये<BR>जानकि U. 3; हा हा देवि स्फुटति हृदयं<BR>U. 3. 38; हा पितः क्वासि हे सुभ्रु<BR>Bk. 6. 11; हा वत्से मालति क्वासि Māl. 10.<BR>&c.; (in this sense हा is often used<BR>with the acc. of person; हा कृष्णाभक्तं<BR>Sk.).<BR>--2 Surprise; हा कथं<BR>महाराजदशरथस्य धर्मदाराः प्रियसखी मे कौसल्या<BR>U. 4.<BR>--3 Anger or reproach.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हा
हा {vI.v} {c3c} A. (जिहीते, हान; pass.<BR>हायते; desid. जिहासते)<BR>1 To go, move;<BR>जिहीथा विख्यातां स्फुटमिह भवद्बांधवरथं<BR>H. D. 28; Ki. 13. 23; Nalod. 1. 38.<BR>--2 To get, attain. {vII.v} {c3c} P. (जहाति,<BR>हीन)<BR>1 To leave, abandon, quit, give<BR>up, forsake, relinquish, dismiss;<BR>मूढ जहीहि धनागमतृष्णां कुरु तनुबुद्धे<BR>मनसि वितृष्णां Moha M. 1; सा<BR>स्त्रीस्वभावादसहा भरस्य तयोर्द्वयोरेकतरं जहाति<BR>Mu. 4. 13, R. 5. 72, 8. 52, 12. 24,<BR>14. 61, 87, 15. 59; Ś. 4. 13,<BR>Bg. 2. 50; Bk. 3. 53, 5. 91, 10. 71,<BR>20. 10; Me. 49, 60; Bv. 2. 129;<BR>Rs. 1. 38.<BR>--2 To resign, forego.<BR>--3 To let<BR>fall.<BR>--4 To omit, disregard, neglect.<BR>--5 To remove.<BR>--6 To avoid, shun.<BR>--Pass. (हीयते)<BR>1 To be left or<BR>forsaken; Ki. 12. 12.<BR>--2 To be<BR>excluded from, be deprived of, lose (with<BR>instr. or abl.); विरूपाक्षो जहे प्राणैः<BR>Bk. 14. 35; जनयित्वा सुतं तस्यां ब्राह्मण्यादेव<BR>हीयते Ms. 3. 17, 5. 161, 9. 211.<BR>--3<BR>To be deficient or wanting in; usually<BR>with परि q. v.; धैर्यं यस्य न हीयते<BR>Pt. 1. 103.<BR>--4 To diminish, decrease,<BR>decay, decline, wane (fig. also);<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">Page1169-c+ 56</a>]<BR>प्रवृद्धो हीयते चंद्रः समुद्रोऽपि तथाविधः<BR>R. 17. 71; H. Pr. 42.<BR>--5 To fail (as<BR>in a law-suit); भूतमप्यनुपन्यस्तं हीयते<BR>व्यवहारतः Y. 2. 19.<BR>--6 To be left<BR>out or omitted.<BR>--7 To be weakened.<BR>--Caus. (हापयति-ते)<BR>1 To cause to<BR>leave, abandon &c.<BR>--2 To drive<BR>away, expel.<BR>--3 To lose.<BR>--4 To<BR>neglect, omit, delay the performance<BR>of; Śi. 16. 33, Ms. 3. 71; 4. 21;<BR>Y. 1. 121. --Desid. (जिहासति) To<BR>wish to leave &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानं|हान
हानं<BR>1 Leaving, abandoning, loss,<BR>failure.<BR>--2 Escaping.<BR>--3 Prowess,<BR>power.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हानिः|हानि
हानिः f. [हा-क्तिन् तस्यनिः]<BR>1<BR>Abandonment, relinquishment.<BR>--2 Loss,<BR>failure, absence, non-existence;<BR>क्वचित्तु स्फुटालंकारविरहेऽपि न काव्यत्वहानिः<BR>K. P. 1 ‘it does not cease to be a<BR>Kāvya’ &c.<BR>--3 Loss, damage,<BR>detriment; ग्रासोद्गलितसिक्थेन का हानिः<BR>करिणो भवेत् Subhāṣ.; का नो हानिः<BR>Sarva. S.<BR>--4 Decrease, deficiency;<BR>यथा हानिः क्रमप्राप्ता तथा वृद्धिः क्रमागता<BR>Hariv.; Y. 2. 207, 244.<BR>--5 Neglect,<BR>omission, breach; प्रतिज्ञा˚, कार्य˚.<BR>--6<BR>Passing away, waste, loss; कालहानि<BR>R. 13. 16.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कर a. causing<BR>loss, detrimental, injurious; Pt. 1. 88.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हापनं|हापन
हापनं Causing to quit or abandon,<BR>expelling.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हांगरः|हाङ्गर|हांगर|हाङ्गरः
हांगरः A large fish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाटक|हाटकं
हाटक a. (की f.) Golden.<BR>--कं<BR>1<BR>Gold.<BR>--2 The thorn-apple.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गिरिः the mountain Meru.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हात्रं|हात्र|हात्रः
हात्रं [हा-करणे त्रल्]<BR>1 Wages, hire.<BR>--2 Injuring, killing.<BR>--3 Death.<BR>--त्रः<BR>A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हांत्रः|हान्त्र|हान्त्रः
हांत्रः Death, dying.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाफिका
हाफिका Yawning, gaping.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायनः|हायन|हायनं
हायनः --नं A year.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A kind<BR>of rice.<BR>--2 A flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हायनं|हायन|हायनः
हायनः --नं A year.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A kind<BR>of rice.<BR>--2 A flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारः|हार|हारं
हारः [हृ-कर्मणि घञ्]<BR>1 Taking<BR>away, removal, seizing.<BR>--2<BR>Conveying.<BR>--3 Abstraction, deprivation.<BR>--4<BR>A carrier, porter.<BR>--5 A garland or<BR>necklace of pearls &c.; a necklace<BR>in general; हारोयं हरिणाक्षीणां लुठति<BR>स्तनमंडले Amaru. 100;<BR>पांड्योयमसांर्पितलंबहारः R. 6. 60, 5. 52, 6. 16.<BR>Me. 67; Rs. 1. 4; 2. 18.<BR>--6 War, battle.<BR>--7 (In math.) The denominator<BR>of a fraction.<BR>--8 A divisor.<BR>--9 (In<BR>prosody) A long syllable.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवलिः --ली f. a string of pearls<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">Page1170-a+ 55</a>]<BR>तरुणीस्तन एव शोभते<BR>मणिहारावलिरामणीयकं N. 2. 44;<BR>हारावलीतरलकांचितकांचिदाम Gīt. 11.<BR>--गुटि (लि) का the<BR>bead or pearl of a necklace;<BR>R. 5. 70.<BR>--यष्टिः f. a necklace, string of<BR>pearls; दधति पृथुकुचाग्रैरुन्नतैर्हारयष्टिं<BR>Rs. 2. 25, 1. 8.<BR>--हारा a kind of<BR>reddishbrown grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1169-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारकः|हारक
हारकः [हृ-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 A thief,<BR>plunderer; Y. 3. 215.<BR>--2 A cheat, rogue.<BR>--3 A string of pearls.<BR>--4 A<BR>divisor (in math.).<BR>--5 A kind of<BR>prose composition.<BR>--6 A gambler.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारि|हारिः
हारि a. Attracting, captivating,<BR>pleasing, charming.<BR>--रिः f.<BR>1<BR>Defeat.<BR>--2 Losing a game.<BR>--3 A<BR>body of travellers, caravan.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कंठः a cuckoo.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारित|हारितः
हारित p. p.<BR>1 Caused to be taken<BR>or seized.<BR>--2 Presented, offered.<BR>--3 Attracted.<BR>--तः<BR>1 The green<BR>colour.<BR>--2 A kind of pigeon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारितकः|हारितक|हारितकं
हारितकः A green vegetable.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारहूरः|हारहूर
हारहूरः Spirituous liquor.<BR>--रा<BR>A grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिण
हारिण a. (णी f.) Belonging to<BR>a deer.<BR>--णं Venison, flesh of deer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिणिकः|हारिणिक
हारिणिकः A deer-catcher, hunter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिन्
हारिन् a. (णी f.) [हारो अस्त्यस्य<BR>इनि, हृ-णिनि वा]<BR>1 Taking,<BR>conveying, carrying.<BR>--2 Robbing, taking<BR>away; वाजिंकुजराणां च हारिणः<BR>Y. 2. 273, 3. 208.<BR>--3 Seizing, disturbing;<BR>Ms. 12. 28.<BR>--4 Obtaining, securing.<BR>--5<BR>Attracting, captivating, pleasing,<BR>delighting, ravishing; तवास्मि<BR>गीतरागेण हारिणा प्रसभं हृतः Ś. 1. 5;<BR>Śi. 10. 13, 69; विष्टपहारिणि हरौ<BR>Bh. 2. 25.<BR>--6 Surpassing, excelling.<BR>--7<BR>Having a necklace.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारिद्रः|हारिद्र
हारिद्रः<BR>1 A yellow colour.<BR>--2<BR>The Kadamba tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हारीतः|हारीत
हारीतः<BR>1 A kind of pigeon;<BR>R. 4. 46.<BR>--2 A rogue, cheat.<BR>--3 N.<BR>of a writer of a Smṛti or code of<BR>laws; Y. 1. 4.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्दं|हार्द|हार्द्द|हार्द्दं
हार्दं [हृदयस्य कर्म युवा० अण् हृदादेशः]<BR>1 Affection, love; अमर्षशून्येन जनस्य<BR>जंतुना न जातहार्देन न विद्विषादरः<BR>Ki. 1. 33; Śi. 9. 69; V. 5. 10.<BR>--2<BR>Kindness, tenderness.<BR>--3 Will.<BR>--4 Intention, meaning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्दिन्
हार्दिन् n. Anything greatly liked<BR>or desired.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हार्य|हार्यः|हार्य्य|हार्य्यः
हार्य a.<BR>1 To be taken or<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">Page1170-b+ 56</a>]<BR>comveyed.<BR>--2 To be borne or carried<BR>on; यदूढया वारणराजहार्यया<BR>Ku. 5. 70.<BR>--3 To be taken away or<BR>snatched off; R. 7. 67.<BR>--4 To be<BR>displaced or borne away (as by wind);<BR>R. 16. 43.<BR>--5 To be shaken (as<BR>one's resolution); Ku. 5. 8.<BR>--6<BR>To be secured or won over, to be<BR>attracted, conquered or influenced;<BR>वहसि हि धनहार्यं पण्यभूतं शरीरं<BR>Mk. 1. 31; Ku. 5. 53; Ms. 7. 217.<BR>--7<BR>To be seized or robbed;<BR>Ms. 8. 417.<BR>--र्यः<BR>1 A snake.<BR>--2 The<BR>tree called Bibhītaka.<BR>--3 The<BR>dividend (in math.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालः|हाल
हालः [हलो अस्त्यस्य अण्, हल एव<BR>वा अण्]<BR>1 A plough.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>Balarāma.<BR>--3 N. of Śālivāhana.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भृत् m. an epithet of<BR>Balarāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालकः|हालक
हालकः A horse of a<BR>yellowishbrown colour.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालहलं|हालहल
हाल(ला)हलं<BR>1 A sort of<BR>deadly poison produced at the<BR>churning of the ocean; (being of a<BR>very virulent character it began<BR>to burn up everything when it was<BR>swallowed by the god Śiva);<BR>अहमेव गुरुः सुदारुणानामिति हालाहल मास्म<BR>तात दृष्यः । ननु संति भवादृशानि भूयो<BR>भुवनेऽस्मिन् वचनानि दुर्जनानां Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 (Hence) A deadly poison or<BR>poison in general; see Bv. 1. 95,<BR>2. 73; Pt. 1. 188. (Also written<BR>हलाहल or हालहाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहलं|हालाहल|हालाहलः
हाल(ला)हलं<BR>1 A sort of<BR>deadly poison produced at the<BR>churning of the ocean; (being of a<BR>very virulent character it began<BR>to burn up everything when it was<BR>swallowed by the god Śiva);<BR>अहमेव गुरुः सुदारुणानामिति हालाहल मास्म<BR>तात दृष्यः । ननु संति भवादृशानि भूयो<BR>भुवनेऽस्मिन् वचनानि दुर्जनानां Subhāṣ.<BR>--2 (Hence) A deadly poison or<BR>poison in general; see Bv. 1. 95,<BR>2. 73; Pt. 1. 188. (Also written<BR>हलाहल or हालहाल).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालहली
हालहली, हाला Wine, spirituous<BR>liquor; हित्वा हालामभिमतरसां<BR>रेवतीलोचनांकां Me. 49; Pt. 1. 58;<BR>Śi. 10. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाला
हालहली, हाला Wine, spirituous<BR>liquor; हित्वा हालामभिमतरसां<BR>रेवतीलोचनांकां Me. 49; Pt. 1. 58;<BR>Śi. 10. 21.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालाहलः|हालाहल|हालाहलं
हालाहलः<BR>1 A kind of insect.<BR>--2<BR>A kind of lizard.<BR>--ला A small<BR>mouse.<BR>--ली Spirituous liquor.<BR>--लं<BR>1 = हालहल (1).<BR>--2 Spirituous<BR>liquor.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिकः|हालिक
हालिकः [हलेन खनति हलः प्रहरणमस्य<BR>तस्येदं वा ठक् ठञ् वा]<BR>1 A ploughman,<BR>an agriculturist.<BR>--2 One that draws<BR>a plough (as a plough-ox).<BR>--3<BR>One who fights with a plough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालिनी
हालिनी A kind of large<BR>houselizard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाली
हाली A wife's younger sister.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हालुः|हालु
हालुः A tooth.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हावः|हाव
हावः [ह्वे --भावे घञ् नि˚ संप्र˚, हु-करणे<BR>घञ् वा]<BR>1 A call, calling.<BR>--2 Any<BR>feminine coquettish^1 gesture<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">Page1170-c+ 55</a>]<BR>calculated to excite amorous<BR>sensations, dalliance (of love),<BR>blandishments; हावहारि हसितं वचनानां<BR>कौशलं दृशि विकारविशेषाः Śi. 10. 13;<BR>जगुः सरागं ननृतुः सहावं Bk. 3. 43;<BR>हाव is thus defined by<BR>उज्ज्वलमणिःग्रीवारेचकसंयुक्तो भ्रूनेत्रादिविकासकृत् ।<BR>भावादीषत्प्रकाशो यः स हाव इति कथ्यते ॥ see<BR>S. D. 127 also.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हावकः|हावक
हावकः<BR>1 One who calls or<BR>summons.<BR>--2 One who calls the bride.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासः|हास
हासः [हस्-भावे घञ्]<BR>1 Laughter,<BR>laughing, smile; भासो हासः<BR>P. R. 1. 22.<BR>--2 Joy, mirth, merriment.<BR>--3 Laughter, as the prevailing<BR>feeling of the rasa called हास्य;<BR>see S. D. 207.<BR>--4 Derisive laughter;<BR>R. 12. 36.<BR>--5 Opening, blowing,<BR>expanding (as of lotuses &c.);<BR>कूलानि सामर्षतयेव तेनुः सरोजलक्ष्मीं<BR>स्थलपद्महासैः Bk. 2. 3.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासकः|हासक
हासकः A buffoon, merry-andrew.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासिका
हासिका<BR>1 Laughter.<BR>--2 Mirth,<BR>merriment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्य|हास्यं|हास्यः
हास्य a. [हस्-ण्यत्] Laughable,<BR>ridiculous; R. 2. 43.<BR>--स्यं<BR>1 Laughter;<BR>Y. 1. 84.<BR>--2 Mirth, amusement,<BR>sport; Ms. 9. 227.<BR>--3 Jest, joke.<BR>--4 Derision, ridicule.<BR>--स्यः The<BR>sentiment of mirth or humour, one<BR>of the eight or nine sentiments in<BR>poetry; it is thus defined:<BR>--विकृताकारवाग्वेषचेष्टादेः कुहकाद्भवेत् । हास्यो<BR>हासस्थायिभावः (so must the line be read<BR>instead of हासो हास्यस्थायिभा वः) श्वेतः<BR>प्रथतदैवतः S. D. 228.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आस्पदं a butt (of ridicule),<BR>laughing-stock.<BR>--पदवी, --मार्गः ridicule,<BR>derision; क्रुद्धैर्नीतस्त्रिभुवनजयी<BR>हास्यमार्गं दशास्यः Vikr. 18. 107.<BR>--रसः<BR>the sentiment of mirth or humour;<BR>see हास्य above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हासस्
हासस् m. The moon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिकः|हास्तिक|हास्तिकं
हास्तिकः An elephant-driver or<BR>rider.<BR>--कं A herd of elephants;<BR>Śi. 5. 30.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हास्तिनं|हास्तिन
हास्तिनं N. of Hastināpura, q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहलं|हाहल
हाह(हा)लं Deadly poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहालं|हाहाल
हाह(हा)लं Deadly poison.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहस्
हाहस् m. A Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हाहा
हाहा m. N. of a Gandharva.<BR>--ind. An exclamation denoting<BR>pain, grief or surprise, (it is<BR>simply हा repeated for the sake of<BR>emphasis; see हा).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः {1}<BR>a grief, lamentation, loud wailing.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-a" target="_blank">Page1171-a+ 55</a>]<BR>{2} the din or uproar of battle.<BR>--रवः<BR>the cry हाहा.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1170-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि ind. (Never used at the<BR>beginning of a sentence) It<BR>has the following senses:--<BR>1 For,<BR>because (expressing a strict or<BR>logical reason); अग्निरिहास्ति धूमो हि<BR>दृश्यते G. M.; R. 5. 10.<BR>--2 Indeed,<BR>surely; देव प्रयोगप्रधानं हि नाट्यशास्त्रं<BR>M. 1; न हि कमलिनीं दृष्ठ्वा ग्राहमवेक्षते<BR>मतंगजः M. 3.<BR>--3 For instance, as is<BR>well known; प्रजानामेव भूत्यर्थं स ताभ्यो<BR>बलिमग्रहीत् । सहस्रगुणमुत्स्रष्टुमादत्ते हि रसं<BR>रविः R. 1. 18.<BR>--4 Only, alone (to<BR>emphasize an idea); मूढो हि<BR>मदनेनायास्यते K. 155.<BR>--5 Sometimes it is<BR>used merely as an expletive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हि
हि {c5c} P. (हिनोति, हित; caus.<BR>हाययति; desid. जिघीषति)<BR>1 To send<BR>forth, impel.<BR>--2 To cast, throw,<BR>discharge, shoot; गदा शक्रजिता जिघ्ये<BR>Bk. 14. 36.<BR>--3 To excite, incite,<BR>urge.<BR>--4 To promote, further.<BR>--5<BR>To gratify, please, exhilarate.<BR>--6<BR>To go or proceed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्
हिंस् {c1c} {c7c} P., {c10c} U. (हिंसति,<BR>हिनस्ति, हिंसयति-ते, हिंसित)<BR>1 To strike,<BR>hit.<BR>--2 To hurt, injure, harm;<BR>Pt. 1. 307.<BR>--3 To afflict, torment;<BR>Māl. 2. 1.<BR>--4 To kill, slay,<BR>destroy completely; कीर्ति सूते दुष्कृतं<BR>या हिनस्ति U. 5. 31; R. 8. 45;<BR>Bg. 13. 28; Bk. 6. 38, 14. 57, 15. 78.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसक|हिंसकः
हिंसक a. [हिंस्-ण्वुल्]<BR>1 Injurious,<BR>noxious, hurtful.<BR>--2 Hostile.<BR>--3<BR>Ferocious, savage.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A savage<BR>animal, a beast of prey.<BR>--2 An<BR>enemy.<BR>--3 A Brāhmaṇa skilled in<BR>the Atharvaveda.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसनं|हिंसन
हिंसनं --ना [हिंस्-ल्युट्] Striking,<BR>hurting, killing; Ms. 2. 177, 10. 48;<BR>Y. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसना
हिंसनं --ना [हिंस्-ल्युट्] Striking,<BR>hurting, killing; Ms. 2. 177, 10. 48;<BR>Y. 1. 33.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसा
हिंसा [हिंस्-अ]<BR>1 Injury, mischief,<BR>wrong, harm, hurt (said to be of<BR>three kinds:--कायिक ‘personal’,<BR>वाचिक ‘verbal’, and मानसिक ‘mental’);<BR>अहिंसा परमो धर्मः.<BR>--2 Killing, slaying,<BR>destruction; R. 5. 57; 3. 313;<BR>Ms. 10. 63.<BR>--3 Robbery, plunder.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मक a. injurious, destructive.<BR>--कर्मन् n. {1} any hurtful or<BR>injurious act. {2} magic used to effect<BR>the ruin or injury of an enemy<BR>(= अभिचार q. v.).<BR>--प्राणिन् m. a<BR>noxious animal.<BR>--रत a. delighting<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">Page1171-b+ 55</a>]<BR>in mischief.<BR>--रुचि a, intent on or<BR>delighting in mischief; Māl. 5. 29,<BR>--समुद्भव a, arising from injury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसारुः|हिंसारु
हिंसारुः<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>--2 Any noxious<BR>animal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसालु|हिंसालुः
हिंसालु [हिंसा अस्त्यर्ये आलु]<BR>1<BR>Injurious, mischievous, hurtful.<BR>--2<BR>Murderous. --m. A mischievous or<BR>savage dog (हिंसालुक also).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसित|हिंसितः
हिंसित a. Injured, hurt.<BR>--तं<BR>Injury, hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंसीरः|हिंसीर
हिंसीरः [हिंस्-ईरन्]<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>--2 A<BR>bird (खग).<BR>--3 A mischievous fellow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्य
हिंस्य a. Liable to be injured or<BR>killed; R. 2. 57; Ms. 5. 41.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्र|हिंस्रः
हिंस्र a. [हिंस्-र]<BR>1 Injurious, noxious,<BR>mischievous, hurtful, murderous;<BR>Ms. 9. 80, 12. 56.<BR>--2 Terrible.<BR>--3<BR>Cruel, fierce, savage.<BR>--स्रः<BR>1 A<BR>fierce animal, beast of prey; R. 2. 27<BR>--2 A destroyer.<BR>--3 N. of Śiva.<BR>--4<BR>N. of Bhīma.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--पशुः a beast<BR>of prey.<BR>--यंत्रं {1} a trap. {1} a<BR>mystical text used for malevolent<BR>purposes.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रकः|हिंस्रक
हिंस्रकः A savage or noxious animal,<BR>a beast of prey.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंस्रा
हिंस्रा<BR>1 A vein, nerve.<BR>--2<BR>Spikenard.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्क्
हिक्क् {vI.v} {c1c} U. (हिक्कति-ते, हिक्कित)<BR>1<BR>To make an indistinct or inarticulate<BR>sound.<BR>--2 To hiccough. {vII.v} {c10c} A.<BR>(हिक्कयते) To hurt, injure, kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिक्का
हिक्का<BR>1 An indistinct sound.<BR>--2<BR>Hiccough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंकारः|हिङ्कार|हिंकार|हिङ्कारः
हिंकारः<BR>1 A kind of low roar or<BR>sound like ‘him’.<BR>--2 A tiger.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंगु|हिङ्गु
हिंगु m., n. [हिमं गच्छति गम्-डु नि०]<BR>1 The plant called Asa foetida.<BR>--2<BR>The substance prepared from this<BR>plant (asa fœtida) for household<BR>use, especially in seasoning articles<BR>of food.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--निर्यासः {1} the<BR>gummy exudation of the hingu tree.<BR>{2} the nimba tree.<BR>--पत्रः the ingudi<BR>tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंगुलः|हिङ्गुल|हिंगुल|हिंगुलं|हिङ्गुलः
हिंगुलः --लं Vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंगुलं|हिङ्गुल|हिंगुल|हिंगुलः|हिङ्गुलः
हिंगुलः --लं Vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंगुलिः|हिङ्गुलि|हिंगुलि|हिङ्गुलिः
हिंगुलिः Vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंगुलु|हिङ्गुलु|हिङ्गुलुः
हिंगुलु m., n. Vermilion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंगुलिका|हिङ्गुलिका
हिंगुलिका The prickly nightshade.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंगुली|हिङ्गुली
हिंगुली The egg-plant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिज्जः|हिज्ज
हिज्जः, हिज्जलः N. of a tree<BR>(commonly called Hijjal.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिज्जलः|हिज्जल
हिज्जः, हिज्जलः N. of a tree<BR>(commonly called Hijjal.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंजीरः|हिञ्जीर|हिंजीर|हिञ्जीरः
हिंजीरः A rope or fetter for<BR>fastening an elephant's foot.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिडिंबः|हिडिम्ब|हिडिंब|हिडिम्बः
हिडिंबः N. of a demon slain by<BR>Bhīma.<BR>--बा<BR>1 The sister of Hiḍimba<BR>who married Bhīma.<BR>--2 The wife<BR>of Hanumat.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जित्, निषूदत,<BR>--भिद्, --रिपु m. epithets of Bhīma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंड्|हिण्ड्
हिंड् {c1c} A. (हिंडते, हिंडित)<BR>1 To go,<BR>wander, roam over,<BR>--2 To disregard,<BR>slight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंडनं|हिण्डन|हिंडन|हिण्डनं
हिंडनं [हिंड्-ल्युट्]<BR>1 Wandering,<BR>roaming about.<BR>--2 Sexual intercourse.<BR>--3 Writing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंडिकः|हिण्डिक|हिण्डिकः
हिंडिकः^1 An astrologer.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170110. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/332,.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंडिरः|हिण्डिर|हिंडिर|हिण्डिरः
हिंडि(डी)रः<BR>1 Cuttle-fish bone.<BR>--2 A man, male.<BR>--3 The egg-plant.<BR>--4 A tonic or stomachic.<BR>--रं The<BR>pomegranate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिंडीरः|हिण्डीर|हिंडीर|हिण्डीरः
हिंडि(डी)रः<BR>1 Cuttle-fish bone.<BR>--2 A man, male.<BR>--3 The egg-plant.<BR>--4 A tonic or stomachic.<BR>--रं The<BR>pomegranate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1171-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

