हिल्लोलः|हिल्लोल
हिल्लोलः<BR>1 A wave, billow.<BR>--2 The<BR>musical mode called Hindola.<BR>--3 A<BR>caprice, whim.<BR>--4 A kind of coitus.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हिल्वलाः
हिल्वलाः f. pl. N. of five small<BR>stars in the head of the lunar<BR>mansion called मृगशिरस्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ही
ही ind. An interjection of<BR>1<BR>Surprise (ah!); हतीवीधलसितानां ही<BR>विचित्रो विपाकः Śi. 11. 64; or ही<BR>चित्रं लक्ष्मणेनोचे Bk. 14. 39; (often<BR>repeated in theatrical language in<BR>this sense).<BR>--2 Fatigue,<BR>despondency or sorrow.<BR>--3 Reason<BR>(cf. हि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1172-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीन|हीनः
हीन p. p. [हा-क्त तस्य नः ईत्वम्]<BR>1<BR>Left, abandoned, forsaken &c.<BR>--2<BR>Destitute or deprived of, bereft of,<BR>without; (with instr. or in comp.);<BR>गुणैर्हीना न शोभंते निगैधा इव किंशुकाः<BR>Subhāṣ.; so द्रव्य˚, मति˚, उत्साह˚ &c.<BR>--3 Excluded, shut out from (with<BR>abl.).<BR>--4 Decayed, wasted.<BR>--5<BR>Deficient, defective;<BR>हीनातिरिक्तगावो वा तमप्यपनयेत्ततः Ms. 3. 242.<BR>--6<BR>Subtracted.<BR>--7 Less, lower;<BR>Ms. 2. 194.<BR>--8 Low, base, mean, vile.<BR>--नः<BR>1 A defective witness.<BR>--2 A<BR>faulty respondent; (Nārada<BR>enumerates five kinds:<BR>--अन्यवादी क्रियाद्वेषी<BR>नोपस्थायी निरुत्तरः । आहूतप्रपलायी च हीनः<BR>पंचविधः स्मृतः).<BR>--3 Subtraction.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. deficient in a limb,<BR>crippled, maimed, defective; Ms. 4. 141;<BR>Pt. 5. 95; Y. 1. 222.<BR>--(गी) a<BR>small ant.<BR>--कर्मन् a. neglecting<BR>the customary religious rites.<BR>--कुल,<BR>--ज a. base-born, of low family.<BR>--क्रतु a. one who neglects his<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--जाति a. {1} of a low<BR>caste. {2} excommunicated,<BR>outcaste, degraded.<BR>--योनिः f. low<BR>birth or origin.<BR>--वर्ण a. {1} of<BR>low caste. {2} of inferior rank.<BR>--वादः a defective statement,<BR>contradictory evidence, prevarication.<BR>--वादिन् a. {1} making a defective<BR>statement. {2} prevaricating. {3}<BR>dumb, speechless. {4} cast in<BR>law, defeated.<BR>--सख्यं associating<BR>with low persons.<BR>--सेवा attendance<BR>on base persons.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हींतालः|हीन्ताल|हींताल|हीन्तालः
हींतालः The marshy date tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरः|हीर|हीरं
हीरः^1 [हृ-क नि.]<BR>1 A snake.<BR>--2<BR>A necklace.<BR>--3 A lion.<BR>--4 N. of<BR>the father of Śrīharṣa, the author<BR>of the Naiṣadha-charita.<BR>--5 N.<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--रः, --रं<BR>1 The thunderbolt<BR>of Indra.<BR>--2 A diamond; (occurring<BR>in the concluding stanza of each<BR>canto of नैषधचरित).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंगः<BR>the thunder-bolt of Indra.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: mis-placed diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरकः|हीरक
हीरकः^1 A diamond.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by  on 20170209. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/CORRECTIONS/issues/336. note: mis-aligned diacritic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीरा
हीरा<BR>1 An epithet of Lakṣmī.<BR>--2 An ant.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीलं|हील
हीलं Semen virile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीलुकं|हीलुक
हीलुकं A kind of rum (distilled<BR>from molasses).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हीही
हीही ind. A particle expressive<BR>of surprise or merriment; see ही.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हु
हु {c3c} P., (जुहोति, हुत; pass. हूयते; caus.<BR>हावयति-ते, desid. जुहूषति)<BR>1 To offer or<BR>present (as an oblation to fire);<BR>make an offering to or in honor<BR>of a deity (with acc.); sacrifice;<BR>यो मंत्रपूतां तनुमप्यहौषीत् R. 13. 45;<BR>जटाधरः सन् जुहुधीह पावकं Ki. 1. 44;<BR>हविजुर्हुधि पावके Bk. 20. 11;<BR>Ms. 3. 87; Y. 1. 99.<BR>--2 To perform a<BR>sacrifice.<BR>--3 To eat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुत|हुतं|हुतः
हुत p. p. [हु-क्त]<BR>1 Offered as an<BR>oblation to fire, burnt as a<BR>sacrificial offering.<BR>--2 One to whom an<BR>oblation is offered; Ś. 4; R. 2. 71.<BR>--तः N. of Śiva.<BR>--तं An oblation,<BR>offering.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्नि a. who has<BR>made an oblation to fire; R. 1. 6.<BR>(--m.) a sacrificial fire.<BR>--अशनः {1} fire;<BR>समीरणो नोदयिता भवेति व्यादिश्यते<BR>केन हुताशनस्य Ku. 3. 21,<BR>R. 4. 1. {2} N. of Śiva. {3} the<BR>Chitraka tree. ˚सहायः an epithet<BR>of Śiva.<BR>--अशनी the full-moon day<BR>in the month of Phālguna (होलिका).<BR>--आशः fire; प्रदक्षिणीकृत्य हुतं हुताशं<BR>R. 2. 71.<BR>--जातवेदस् a. one who has<BR>made an oblation to fire.<BR>--भुज् m.<BR>fire; नैशस्यार्चिर्हुतभुज इव<BR>च्छिन्नभूयिष्ठधूमा V. 1. 7; U. 5. 9. ˚प्रिया Svāhā<BR>the wife of Agni.<BR>--वहः fire;<BR>जनाकीर्णं मन्ये हुतवहपरीतं गृहमिव Ś. 5. 10;<BR>शीतांशुस्तपनो हितो हुतवहः Gīt. 9;<BR>Me. 43; Rs. 1. 27.<BR>--होमः a Brāhmaṇa<BR>who has offered oblations to fire.<BR>--(मं) a burnt offering.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुतिः|हुति
हुतिः f. Offering oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुड्
हुड् {vI.v} {c1c} P. (होडति) To go. {vII.v}<BR>{c6c} P. (हुडति)<BR>1 To collect.<BR>--2 To<BR>dive, sink.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडः|हुड
हुडः<BR>1 A ram.<BR>--2 An iron stake<BR>for keeping out thieves.<BR>--3 A kind<BR>of fence.<BR>--4 An iron club.<BR>--5 A<BR>kind of bulwark or fence.<BR>--6 A<BR>place for voiding excrement on<BR>a chariot.<BR>--7 A cloud.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुः|हुडु
हुडुः A ram; जंबुको हुडुयुद्धेन<BR>Pt. 1. 162.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुक्कः|हुडुक्क
हुडुक्कः<BR>1 A small<BR>hour-glassshaped drum; N. 15. 17.<BR>--2 A<BR>kind of bird (दात्यूह).<BR>--3 The bolt<BR>of a door.<BR>--4 A drunken man.<BR>--5<BR>A stick bound with iron.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुडुत्
हुडुत् n.<BR>1 Noise of a bull.<BR>--2<BR>A sound of threat.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुंड्|हुण्ड्
हुंड् {c1c} A. (हुंडते)<BR>1 To collect.<BR>--2 To select, choose.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुंडः|हुण्ड|हुंड|हुण्डः
हुंडः<BR>1 A tiger.<BR>--2 A ram.<BR>--3 A<BR>blockhead.<BR>--4 A village-hog.<BR>--5<BR>A demon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुम्
हुम् ind. A particle (originally<BR>an imitative sound) expressing<BR>1<BR>Remembrance or recollection; हुं ज्ञातं<BR>or रामो नाम बभूव हुं तदबला सीतेति हुम्.<BR>--2 Doubt; चैत्रो हुं मैत्रो हुं.<BR>--3 Assent;<BR>U. 5. 35.<BR>--4 Anger.<BR>--5 Aversion.<BR>--6 Reproach.<BR>--7 Interrogation. (In<BR>spells and incantations हुं is often<BR>found used with dat.; e. g. ॐ<BR>कवचायहुम्). (हुंकृ means ‘to utter the<BR>sound hum’, ‘to roar, grunt, bellow,<BR>as in अनुहुंकृ ‘to roar in return;’<BR>अनुहुंकुरुते घनध्वनिं न हि गोमायुरुतानि<BR>केसरी Śi. 16. 25.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--कारः --कृतिः<BR>f. {1} uttering the sound ‘hum’; पृष्टा<BR>पुनः पुनः कांता हुंकारैरेव भाषते. {2} a<BR>menacing sound, sound of defiance;<BR>क्षतहुंकारशंसिनः Ku. 2. 26; हुंकारेणेव<BR>धनुषः स हि विघ्नानपोहति Ś. 3. 1,<BR>R. 7. 58; Ku. 5. 54. {3} roaring,<BR>bellowing in general. {4} the grunting<BR>of a boar. {5} the twang of a bow.<BR>--कृतं {1} an incantation. {2} the<BR>grunt of a wild boar. {3} the roar<BR>of thunder.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुर्च्छ्
हुर्च्छ् {c1c} P. (हूर्च्छति)<BR>1 To be<BR>crooked.<BR>--2 To act dishonestly, deceive.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूर्च्छनं|हूर्छन
हूर्च्छनं Dishonesty, cunning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुल्
हुल् {c1c} P. (होलति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2 To<BR>cover or conceal.<BR>--3 To kill.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुलहुली
हुलहुली A kind of inarticulate<BR>sound, uttered by women on joyful<BR>occasions.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहु|हुहुः
हुहु(हू) m. A kind of Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हुहू
हुहु(हू) m. A kind of Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हू
हू ind.<BR>1 An interjection of<BR>calling.<BR>--2 Of contempt.<BR>--3 Of<BR>pride.<BR>--4 Of grief (oh! ah!<BR>alas &c.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूड्
हूड् {c1c} A. (हूडते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूणः|हूण
हूणः(नः)<BR>1 A barbarian, foreigner;<BR>सद्यो मुंडितमत्तहूणचिबुकप्रस्पर्धि<BR>नारंगकम्.<BR>--2 A kind of golden coin,<BR>(probably current in the country of<BR>the Hūṇas).<BR>--णाः m. pl. N. of<BR>a country or its people; हूणादरोद्यनां<BR>R. 4. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूनः|हून
हूणः(नः)<BR>1 A barbarian, foreigner;<BR>सद्यो मुंडितमत्तहूणचिबुकप्रस्पर्धि<BR>नारंगकम्.<BR>--2 A kind of golden coin,<BR>(probably current in the country of<BR>the Hūṇas).<BR>--णाः m. pl. N. of<BR>a country or its people; हूणादरोद्यनां<BR>R. 4. 68.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूत|हूतं
हूत p. p. [ह्वे-क्त संप्रसारणं]<BR>Called, summoned, invited &c.; see ह्वे.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूतिः|हूति
हूतिः f. [ह्वे क्तिन् संप्रसारणं]<BR>1<BR>Calling, inviting.<BR>--2 Challenging.<BR>--3<BR>A name; as in हरिहेतिहूति q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूम्
हूम् &c. see हुम्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1173-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूरवः|हूरव
हूरवः A jackal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हूहू
हूहू m. A kind of Gandharva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृ
हृ {vI.v} {c1c} U. (हरति-ते, जहार, जह्रे, अहार्षीत्,<BR>अहृत, हरिष्यति-ते, हर्तुं हृत; pass. ह्रियते)<BR>1 To take, carry, convey, lead,<BR>(often used with two accusatives<BR>in this sense); अजां ग्रामं हरति Sk.;<BR>संदेशं मे हर धनपतिक्रोधविश्लेषितस्य<BR>Me. 7; Ms. 4. 74.<BR>--2 To carry off<BR>or away, take or draw to a distance;<BR>Bk. 5. 47.<BR>--3 To take away,<BR>rob, plunder, steal; दुर्वृत्ता<BR>जारजन्मानो हरिष्यंतीति शंकया Bv. 4. 45;<BR>R. 3. 39, Ku. 2. 47, Bk. 2. 39;<BR>Ms. 7. 43.<BR>--4 To strip off,<BR>deprive of, despoil, take away;<BR>वृंताच्श्लथं हरति पुष्पमनोकहानां R. 5. 69,<BR>Bk. 15. 116; Ms. 8. 334.<BR>--5 To<BR>take away, cure, destroy; तथापि<BR>हरते तापं लोकानामुन्नतो घनः<BR>Bv. 1. 39; R. 15. 24; Me. 31.<BR>--6 To<BR>attract, captivate, win over,<BR>influence, subdue; enchant; चेतो न कस्य<BR>हरते गतिरंगनायाः Bv. 2. 157; ये भावा<BR>हृदयं हरंति 1. 103; तवास्मि गीतरागेण<BR>हारिणा प्रसभं हृतः Ś. 1. 5; हरति मे<BR>हरिवाहनदिङ्मुखं V. 3. 6; मृगया<BR>जहार चतुरेव कामिनी R. 9. 69,<BR>10. 83, Rs. 6. 21; Bg. 6. 44, 2. 60;<BR>Ms. 6. 59.<BR>--7 To gain, acquire,<BR>obtain; ततो विंशं नृपो हरेत्<BR>Ms. 8. 391, 153; स हरतु सुभगपताकां<BR>Dk.<BR>--8 To have, possess;<BR>Bv. 2. 163.<BR>--9 To surpass, eclipse;<BR>Bk. 5. 71; Śi. 93.<BR>--10 To marry;<BR>Ms. 9. 93.<BR>--11 To divide.<BR>--12 To<BR>cast, throw (as an arrow).<BR>--13 To<BR>accept, receive, inherit.<BR>--14 To<BR>offer. --Caus. (हारयति-ते)<BR>1 To cause<BR>to take, carry or convey, send<BR>(something) by one, (with acc.<BR>or instr.); भृत्यं भृत्येन वा भारं<BR>हारयति Sk.; जीमूतेन स्वकुशलमयीं<BR>हारयिष्यन् प्रवृत्तिं Me. 4; Ms. 8. 114;<BR>Ku. 2. 39.<BR>--2 To cause to be taken<BR>away, to lose, be deprived of.<BR>--3<BR>To give away. --Desid. (जिहीषति-ते)<BR>To wish to take &c. {vII.v} {c3c} P.<BR>(जिहर्ति) To take by force.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत्
हृत् a. (At the end of comp.<BR>only) Taking away, seizing,<BR>removing, carrying off, attracting &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृत|हृतं
हृत p. p. [हृ-क्त]<BR>1 Taken or<BR>carried away.<BR>--2 Seized.<BR>--3<BR>Captivated.<BR>--4 Accepted.<BR>--5 Divided;<BR>see हृ.<BR>--तं A portion, share.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-b" target="_blank">Page1174-b+ 56</a>]<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अधिकार a. {1} dismissed<BR>from authority, turned out. {2}<BR>deprived of one's due rights.<BR>--उत्तरीय a. having the upper garments<BR>stripped off.<BR>--द्रव्य, --धन a. spoiled<BR>of wealth.<BR>--सर्वस्व a. stripped of all<BR>one's property, utterly ruined.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृतिः|हृति
हृतिः f.<BR>1 Seizure.<BR>--2 Robbing,<BR>spoliation.<BR>--3 Destruction.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणीयते
हृ(ह्रि)णीयते Den. A.<BR>1 To<BR>be angry.<BR>--2 To feel ashamed (with<BR>instr. or gen.); त्वयाद्य तस्मिन्नपि<BR>दंडधारिणा कथं न पत्या धरणी हृणीयते<BR>N. 1. 133; दिवोपि वज्रायुधभूषणाया<BR>हृणीयते वीरबती न भूमिः Bk. 2. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिणीयते
हृ(ह्रि)णीयते Den. A.<BR>1 To<BR>be angry.<BR>--2 To feel ashamed (with<BR>instr. or gen.); त्वयाद्य तस्मिन्नपि<BR>दंडधारिणा कथं न पत्या धरणी हृणीयते<BR>N. 1. 133; दिवोपि वज्रायुधभूषणाया<BR>हृणीयते वीरबती न भूमिः Bk. 2. 38.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणीया
हृणी(णि)या<BR>1 Censure, reproach,<BR>--2 Shame.<BR>--3 Compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृणिया
हृणी(णि)या<BR>1 Censure, reproach,<BR>--2 Shame.<BR>--3 Compassion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्
हृद् n. (This word has no forms<BR>for the fist five inflections, and<BR>is optionally substituted for हृदय<BR>after acc. dual)<BR>1 The mind, heart.<BR>=<BR>--2 The chest, bosom, breast; इमां<BR>हृदि व्यायतपातमक्षिणोत् Ku. 5. 54.<BR>--3<BR>The soul.<BR>--4 The interior or essence.<BR>of anything.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आवर्तः a lock<BR>or curl of hair on a horse's chest.<BR>--कंपः tremor of the heart,<BR>palpitation.<BR>--गत a. {1} seated in the mind,<BR>conceived, designed. {2} cherished.<BR>--(तं) design, meaning, intent.<BR>--ग्रहः<BR>spasm of the heart.<BR>--ग्रंथः a heart.<BR>sore.<BR>--देशः the region of the heart.<BR>--पिंडः --डं the heart.<BR>--रोगः {1} a<BR>heartdisease, heartburn. {2} sorrow, grief,<BR>anguish. {3} love. {4} the sign<BR>Aquarius of the zodiac.<BR>--लासः<BR>(हृल्लासः) {1} hiccough. {2} disquietude,<BR>grief.<BR>--लेखः (हृल्लेखः) {1} knowledge,<BR>reasoning. {2} heart-ache.<BR>--लेखा<BR>(हृल्लेखा) grief, anxiety.<BR>--वंटकः<BR>the stomach.<BR>--शयः {1} the god<BR>of love. {2} love.<BR>--शूलं an<BR>acute pain in the chest.<BR>--शोकः<BR>heartburn or anguish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयं|हृदय
हृदयं<BR>1 The heart, soul, mind;<BR>हृदये दिग्धशरैरिवाहतः Ku. 4. 25; so<BR>अयोहृदयः R. 9. 9; पाषाणहृदय &c.<BR>--2 The bosom, chest, breast;<BR>बाणभिन्नहृदया निपेतुषी R. 11. 19.<BR>--3<BR>Love, affection.<BR>--4 The interior or<BR>essence of anything.<BR>--5 The secret<BR>science; अश्व˚, अक्ष˚ &c.<BR>--6 True<BR>or divine knowledge.<BR>--7 The Veda.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--आत्मन् m. a heron.<BR>--आविध् a. heart-rending,<BR>heart-piercing; Bk. 6. 73.<BR>--ईशः, ईश्वरः a<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">Page1174-c+ 56</a>]<BR>husband. (--शा, --री f.) {1} a wife. {2}<BR>a mistress.<BR>--उदंकः heaving of the<BR>heart.<BR>--कंपः tremor of the heart,<BR>palpitation.<BR>--ग्राहिन् a.<BR>heart-captivating.<BR>--चोरः one who steals the<BR>heart or affections.<BR>--छिद् a.<BR>heartrending, heart-piercing.<BR>--रज्जुः (in<BR>geom.) a central line.<BR>--रोगः a<BR>heart-disease; Mu. 1. 13.<BR>--लेखः<BR>{1} knowledge. {2} heart-ache,<BR>anxiety.<BR>--विध्, --बेधिन् a.<BR>heart-piercing.<BR>--वृत्ति f. disposition of the<BR>heart.<BR>--स्थ a. being or cherished in<BR>the heart.<BR>--स्थानं the breast, bosom.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयंगम|हृदयङ्गम|हृदयङ्गमं
हृदयंगम a.<BR>1 Heart-stirring,<BR>touching, thrilling.<BR>--2 Lovely, handsome;<BR>Māl. 1.<BR>--3 Sweet, attractive,<BR>pleasant, agreeable; अहो हृदयंगमः<BR>परिहासः Māl. 3; वल्लकी च हृदयंगमस्वना<BR>R. 19. 13, Ku. 2. 16.<BR>--4 Fit,<BR>appropriate.<BR>--5 Dear, beloved,<BR>cherished; क्व नु ते हृदयंगमः सखा Ku. 4. 24.<BR>--मं An appropriate speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयालु|हृदयालुः
हृदयालु, हृदयिक, हृदयिन् a.<BR>Tenderhearted, good-hearted, affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयिक|हृदयिकः
हृदयालु, हृदयिक, हृदयिन् a.<BR>Tenderhearted, good-hearted, affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदयिन्
हृदयालु, हृदयिक, हृदयिन् a.<BR>Tenderhearted, good-hearted, affectionate.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदिकः|हृदिक
हृदि(दी)कः N. of a Yādava<BR>prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदीकः|हृदीक
हृदि(दी)कः N. of a Yādava<BR>prince.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृदिस्पृश्
हृदिस्पृश् a.<BR>1 Touching the heart.<BR>--2 Dear, beloved.<BR>--3 Agreeable,<BR>charming, beautiful.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृद्य|हृद्यं|हृद्यः
हृद्य a. [हृदि स्पृश्यते मनोज्ञत्वात्<BR>हृद्-यत्]<BR>1 Hearty, cordial, sincere.<BR>--2 Dear to the heart, cherished,<BR>dear, desired, beloved; Bv. 1. 69.<BR>--3 Agreeable, pleasant; charming;<BR>Māl. 1. 4, 8. 4, R. 11. 68.<BR>--4<BR>Affectionate, kind.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--गंधः the<BR>Bilva tree.<BR>--गंधा the<BR>great-flowered jasmine.<BR>--गंधं {1} small cumin.<BR>{2} sochal salt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्
हृष् {c1c} {c4c} P. (हर्षति, हृष्यति, हृष्ट or<BR>हृषित)<BR>1 To be delighted or rejoiced,<BR>be pleased or glad, to exult, rejoice;<BR>अद्वितीयं रुचात्मानं मत्वा किं चंद्र हृष्यसि<BR>Bv. 2. 54.<BR>--2 To bristle or stand<BR>erect, stand on end (as the hair of<BR>the body); हृषितास्तनूरुहाः Dk.;<BR>हृष्यंति रोमकूपानि Mb.<BR>--3 To become erect<BR>(said of other things, e. g. the penis).<BR>--4 To lie, tell a lie. --Caus. (<BR>हर्षयति-ते) To please, delight, fill with<BR>pleasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषित|हृषितं
हृषित p. p. [हृष्-क्त वा˚ इट्]<BR>1<BR>Pleased, delighted, glad, happy, rejoiced,<BR>enraptured.<BR>--2 Thrilled; having the<BR>hair bristling.<BR>--3 Astonished.<BR>--4<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">Page1175-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Bent, bowed.<BR>--5 Disappointed.<BR>--6<BR>Fresh.<BR>--7 Armed, accoutred.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1174-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृषीकं|हृषीक
हृषीकं [हृष्-ई कक्] An organ of<BR>sense.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ईशः an epithet of<BR>Viṣṇu or Kṛṣṇa; Bg. 1. 15;<BR>et seq.; (हृषीकाणींद्रियाण्याहुस्तेषामीशो यतो<BR>भवान् । हृषीकेशस्ततो विष्णो ख्यातो देवेषु<BR>केशव ॥ Mb.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्ट|हृष्टः
हृष्ट p. p. [हृष्-क्त] Pleased,<BR>rejoiced (= हृषित).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--चित्त,<BR>--मानस a. rejoiced in mind, glad at<BR>heart, happy.<BR>--रोमन् a. having the<BR>hair on the body bristling or<BR>thrilling (with joy).<BR>--वदन a. having a<BR>cheerful countenance.<BR>--संकल्प a.<BR>contented, pleased.<BR>--हृदय a.<BR>joyoushearted, cheerful, merry.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हृष्टिः|हृष्टि
हृष्टिः f. [हृष्-क्तिन्]<BR>1 Delight,<BR>happiness, joy, pleasure.<BR>--2 Pride.<BR>--3 Knowledge.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हे
हे ind.<BR>1 A vocative particle (oh!,<BR>ho!); हे कृष्ण हे यादव हे सखेति<BR>Bg. 11. 41; हे राजानस्त्यजत सुकविप्रेमबंथे<BR>विरोधं Vikr. 18. 107.<BR>--2 A particle<BR>used in challenging.<BR>--3 An<BR>interjection expressing defiance, envy,<BR>ill-will or disapprobation.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेक्का
हेक्का Hiccough.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठ्
हेठ् {c1c} P. (हेठति)<BR>1 To be wicked.<BR>--2 To vex, trouble, harass.<BR>--3 To<BR>strike, hurt, injure.<BR>--4 To be born<BR>or produced.<BR>--5 To purify.<BR>--6 To<BR>cause prosperity, produce happiness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेठः|हेठ
हेठः<BR>1 Vexation.<BR>--2 Hindrance,<BR>obstruction, opposition.<BR>--3 Injury,<BR>hurt.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेड्
हेड् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (हेडते) To disregard,<BR>slight, neglect. {vII.v} {c1c} P. (हेडति)<BR>1<BR>To surround.<BR>--2 To attire.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडः|हेड
हेडः Disregard, slight.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जः anger, displeasure.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेडाबुक्कः|हेडाबुक्क
हेडाबुक्कः A horse-dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतिः|हेति
हेतिः m. f. [हन्-करणे क्तिन् नि˚]<BR>1 A<BR>weapon, a missile; समरविजयी<BR>हेतिदलितः Bh. 2. 44; R. 10. 12;<BR>Ki. 3. 56, 14. 30.<BR>--2 A stroke, injury.<BR>--3<BR>A ray of the sun.<BR>--4 Light,<BR>splendour.<BR>--5 Flame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुः|हेतु
हेतुः [हि-तुन् Uṇ. 1. 73]<BR>1 Cause,<BR>reason, object, motive; इति<BR>हेतुस्तदुद्भवे K. P. 1; Māl. 1. 23, R. 1. 10;<BR>Me. 25; Ś. 3. 12.<BR>--2 Source, origin;<BR>स पिता पितरस्तासां केवलं जन्महेतवः<BR>R. 1. 24 ‘authors of their being’.<BR>--3 A<BR>means or instrument.<BR>--4 The<BR>logical reason, the reason for an<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-b" target="_blank">Page1175-b+ 57</a>]<BR>inference, middle term (forming the<BR>second member of the<BR>five-membered syllogism).<BR>--5 Logic, science of<BR>reasoning.<BR>--6 Any logical proof or<BR>argument.<BR>--7 A rhetorical reason<BR>(regarded by some writers as a<BR>figure of speech); it is thus<BR>defined: --हेतोर्हेतु मता सार्धमभेदो हेतुरुच्यते. (N. B.<BR>The forms हेतुना, हेतोः, rarely हेतौ, are<BR>used adverbially in the sense of ‘by<BR>reason of’, ‘on account of’, ‘because of’,<BR>with gen. or in comp. शास्त्रविज्ञानहेतुना;<BR>अल्पस्य हेतोर्बहु हातुमिच्छन् R. 2. 47;<BR>विस्मृतं कस्य हेतोः Mu. 1. 1. &c.).<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अपदेशः adducing the<BR>hetu (in the form of the<BR>five-membered syllogism).<BR>--आभासः ‘the<BR>semblance of a reason.’ a<BR>fallacious middle term, fallacy; (it is of<BR>five kinds:<BR>--सव्यभिचार or अनैकांतिक,<BR>विरुद्ध, असिद्ध, सत्प्रतिपक्ष and बाधित).<BR>--उपक्षेपः --उपन्यासः adducing a<BR>reason, statement of an argument.<BR>--वादः disputation, controversy.<BR>--शास्त्रं a logically-treated work,<BR>any heretical work questioning the<BR>authority of Smṛtis or revelation;<BR>Ms. 2. 11.<BR>--हेतुमत् m. du. cause<BR>and effect. ˚भावः the relation<BR>existing between cause and effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुक|हेतुकः
हेतुक a. Causing, producing (at<BR>the end of comp.).<BR>--कः<BR>1 A cause,<BR>reason.<BR>--2 An instrument.<BR>--3 A<BR>logician.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुता
हेतुता --त्वं Causation, the existence<BR>of cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुत्वं|हेतुत्व
हेतुता --त्वं Causation, the existence<BR>of cause.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेतुमत्|हेतुमन्त्
हेतुमत् a.<BR>1 Having a reason or<BR>cause.<BR>--2 Having the hetu. --m.<BR>An effect.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमं|हेम|हेमः
हेमं [हि-मन्]<BR>1 Gold.<BR>--2 The<BR>thorn-apple.<BR>--मः<BR>1 A dark or<BR>brown-coloured horse.<BR>--2 A<BR>particular weight of gold.<BR>--3 The planet<BR>Mercury.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमन्
हेमन् n. [हि-मनिन्]<BR>1 Gold.<BR>--2<BR>Water.<BR>--3 Snow.<BR>--4 The thorn-apple.<BR>--5 The Keśara flower.<BR>--6 Winter, the<BR>cold season.<BR>--7 The planet Mercury.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अंग a. golden; Mu. 2. 10<BR>v. {1}<BR>--(गः) {1} Garuḍa. {2} a lion.<BR>{3} the mountain Sumeru. {4} N.<BR>of Brahman. {5} of Viṣṇu. {6}<BR>the Campaka tree.<BR>--अंगदं a<BR>goldbracelet.<BR>--अद्रिः the mountain<BR>Sumeru.<BR>--अंभोजं a golden lotus;<BR>हेमांभोजप्रसवि सलिलं मानसस्वाददानः<BR>Me. 62.<BR>--अंभोरुहं a golden lotus;<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">Page1175-c+ 55</a>]<BR>Ku. 2. 44.<BR>--आह्वः {1} the wild<BR>Campaka tree. {2} the Dhattūra<BR>plant.<BR>--कंदलः coral.<BR>--करः, --कर्तृ,<BR>--कारः, --कारकः a goldsmith;<BR>Ms. 12. 61, Y. 3. 147.<BR>--किंजल्कं the<BR>Nāgakeśara flower.<BR>--कुंभः a golden<BR>jar.<BR>--कूटः N. of a mountain; Ś. 7.<BR>--केतकी the Ketaka plant, bearing<BR>yellow flowers (स्वर्णकेती).<BR>--केलिः<BR>{1} an epithet of Agni. {2} the<BR>Chitraka plant.<BR>--केशः N. of Śiva.<BR>--गंधिनी the perfume named<BR>Reṇukā.<BR>--गिरिः the mountain Sumeru.<BR>--गौरः the Aśoka tree.<BR>--छन्न a.<BR>covered with gold.<BR>--(न्नं) gold<BR>covering<BR>--ज्वालः fire.<BR>--तरुः the<BR>thorn-apple.<BR>--तारं blue vitriol.<BR>--दुग्धः, --दुग्धकः the glomerous fig-tree.<BR>--पर्वतः the mountain Meru.<BR>--पुष्प,<BR>--पुष्पकः {1} the kśoka tree. {2} the<BR>Lodhra tree. {3} the Campaka tree.<BR>(--n.) {1} the Aśoka flower. {2} the<BR>flower of China rose.<BR>--पुष्पिका<BR>yellow jasmine.<BR>--ब (व) लं a<BR>pearl.<BR>--माला the wife of Yama.<BR>--मालिन् m. the sun.<BR>--यूथिका the<BR>golden or yellow jasmine.<BR>--रागिणी<BR>f. turmeric.<BR>--शंखः N. of Viṣṇu.<BR>--शृंगं {1} a golden horn. {2} a golden<BR>summit.<BR>--सारं blue vitriol.<BR>--सूत्रं, --सूत्रकं a kind of necklace;<BR>(Mar. गोफ).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकं|हेमक
हेमकं Gold.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमलः|हेमल
हेमलः<BR>1 A goldsmith.<BR>--2 A<BR>touchstone.<BR>--3 A chameleon.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेम्य
हेम्य a. Golden.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमंतः|हेमन्त|हेमंत|हेमंतं|हेमन्तः
हेमंतः --तं One of the six seasons,<BR>cold or winter season (comprising<BR>the months मार्गशीर्ष and पौष);<BR>नवप्रबालोद्गमसस्यरम्यः प्रफुल्ललोभ्रः<BR>परिपक्वशालिः । विलीनपद्मः प्रपतत्तुषारो हेमंतकालः<BR>समुपागतः प्रिये Rs. 4. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नाथः the wood-apple tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमंतं|हेमन्त|हेमंत|हेमंतः|हेमन्तः
हेमंतः --तं One of the six seasons,<BR>cold or winter season (comprising<BR>the months मार्गशीर्ष and पौष);<BR>नवप्रबालोद्गमसस्यरम्यः प्रफुल्ललोभ्रः<BR>परिपक्वशालिः । विलीनपद्मः प्रपतत्तुषारो हेमंतकालः<BR>समुपागतः प्रिये Rs. 4. 1.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--नाथः the wood-apple tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमंती|हेमन्ती
हेमंती Winter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेय|हेयः
हेय a. Fit to be left or<BR>abandoned.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरं|हेर
हेरं [हि-रन्]<BR>1 A kind of crown<BR>or diadem.<BR>--2 Turmeric.<BR>--3<BR>Demoniacal illusion.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरंबः|हेरम्ब|हेरंब|हेरम्बः
हेरंबः [हे शिवे रंबति रंब्-अच् अलुक्<BR>समा˚ Tv.]<BR>1 N. of Gaṇeśa.<BR>--2 A<BR>buffalo.<BR>--3 A boastful hero.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जननी N. of Pārvatī<BR>(mother of Gaṇeśa).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरिकः|हेरिक
हेरिकः A spy, secret emissary.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1175-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेरुकः|हेरुक
हेरुकः An attendant on Śiva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेल्
हेल् {c1c} A. (हेलते) To disregard;<BR>see हेड्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलनं|हेलन
हेलनं --ना<BR>1 Disregarding,<BR>slighting, contempt, insulting.<BR>--2<BR>Sporting amorously, wanton dalliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलना
हेलनं --ना<BR>1 Disregarding,<BR>slighting, contempt, insulting.<BR>--2<BR>Sporting amorously, wanton dalliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेला
हेला [हेड्-भावे-डस्य लः]<BR>1 Contempt,<BR>disrespect, insult; Śi. 12. 72.<BR>--2 (a)<BR>Amorous sport or dalliance, wanton<BR>sport; S. D. 128; D. R. 2. 32. (b)<BR>Pleasure, delight, pastime;<BR>Māl. 9. 43.<BR>--3 Strong sexual desire;<BR>प्रौढेच्छयाऽतिरूढानां नारीणां सुरतोत्सवे ।<BR>शृंगारशास्त्रतत्वज्ञैर्हेला सा परिकीर्तिता ॥<BR>--4 Ease, facility; Śi. 1. 34; हेलया<BR>‘easily’, without any difficulty<BR>or trouble.<BR>--5 Moonlight.<BR>--6 A<BR>pause in a note or shaking (as in<BR>music).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलावुक्कः|हेलावुक्क
हेलावुक्कः A horse-dealer.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेलिः|हेलि
हेलिः [हिल्-इन्] The sun. --f.<BR>Wanton or amorous sport, dalliance.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेवाकः|हेवाक
हेवाकः Ardent or intense desire,<BR>eagerness; (this word, like the<BR>word लटभ q. v., is used only by<BR>later writers like Kalhaṇa,<BR>Bilhaṇa, and is probably derived from<BR>Persian or Arabic); अस्मिन्नासीत्तदनु<BR>निविडाश्लेषहेवाकलीलावेल्लद्वाहुक्वणितवलया<BR>संततं राजलक्ष्मीः Vikr. 18. 101; cf.<BR>हेवाकिन् below.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेवाकस
हेवाकस a. High, intense, ardent;<BR>हेवाकसस्तु शृंगारो हावोक्षिभ्रूविकारकृत्<BR>D. R. 2. 31; (might the word<BR>here not be derived from हेवाक?).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेवाकिन्
हेवाकिन् a. Ardently desirous of,<BR>eager for, (in comp.); जायंते<BR>महतामहो निरुपमप्रस्थानहेवाकिनां<BR>निःसामान्यमहत्त्वयोगपिशुना वार्ता विपत्तावपि<BR>Kalhaṇa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेष्
हेष् {c1c} A. (हेषते, हेषित) To neigh<BR>(as a horse); to bray, roar (in<BR>general).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषः|हेष
हेषः, हेषा, हेषितं Neighing,<BR>braying; रथांगसंक्रीडितमश्वहेषः Ki. 16. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषा
हेषः, हेषा, हेषितं Neighing,<BR>braying; रथांगसंक्रीडितमश्वहेषः Ki. 16. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषितं|हेषित
हेषः, हेषा, हेषितं Neighing,<BR>braying; रथांगसंक्रीडितमश्वहेषः Ki. 16. 8.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेषिन्
हेषिन् m. A horse.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेहे
हेहे ind. A vocative particle<BR>used in addressing or calling out<BR>loudly.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

है
है ind. A vocative particle.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैतुक|हैतुकः
हैतुक a. (की f.) [हेतौ प्रसृतः ठण्]<BR>1 Causal, causative.<BR>--2<BR>Argumentative, rationalistic.<BR>--कः<BR>1 A<BR>logical reasoner, an arguer.<BR>--2 A<BR>follower of the Mīmāṃsā doctrines.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">Page1176-b+ 55</a>]<BR>--3 A rationalist, sceptic.<BR>--4 A<BR>heretic.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैम|हैमं|हैमः
हैम a. (मी f.) [हिम-हेमन्-अण्]<BR>1<BR>Cold, wintry, frigid.<BR>--2 Caused<BR>by frost; मृणालिनी हैममिवोपरागं<BR>R. 16. 7.<BR>--3 Golden, made of gold;<BR>पादेन हैमं विलिलेख पीठं R. 6. 15;<BR>Bk. 5. 89; Ku. 6. 6.<BR>--4 Of a golden<BR>yellow colour.<BR>--मा --मी<BR>Yellow jasmine.<BR>--मं Hoar-frost,<BR>dew.<BR>--मः An epithet of Śiva.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--मुद्रा, --मुद्रिका a golden<BR>coin.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमन|हैमनं|हैमनः
हैमन a. (नी f.) [हेमंत एव हेमंते<BR>भवो वा अण् तलोपः]<BR>1 Wintry, cold;<BR>Śi. 6. 55, Ki. 17. 12.<BR>--2<BR>Pertaining to winter, i. e. long (as nights);<BR>Śi. 6. 77.<BR>--3 Growing in or<BR>suitable for winter; हैमनैर्निवसनैः<BR>सुमध्यमाः R. 19. 41.<BR>--4 Golden, made<BR>of gold.<BR>--नः<BR>1 The month<BR>Mārgaśīrsha.<BR>--2 The winter season (= हेमंत<BR>q. v.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमंतिक|हैमन्तिक|हैमन्तिकं
हैमंतिक a. [हेमंते काले भवः ठञ्]<BR>1<BR>Wintry, cold.<BR>--2 Growing in<BR>winter.<BR>--कं A kind of rice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमल|हैमलः
हैमल See हेमतं.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमवत|हैमवतं|हैमवतः
हैमवत a. (ती f.) [हिमवतो<BR>अदूरभवो देशः तस्येदं वा अण्]<BR>1 Snowy.<BR>--2<BR>Flowing from the snowy, i. e.<BR>Himālaya, mountain; R. 16. 44.<BR>--3<BR>Bred in, belonging to, or situated<BR>on, the Himālaya mountain;<BR>Ku. 3. 23, 2. 67.<BR>--तः A kind of<BR>poison.<BR>--तं Bhāratavarṣa or India.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैमवती
हैमवती<BR>1 N. of Pārvatī.<BR>--2 Of<BR>the river Ganges.<BR>--3 A kind of<BR>myrobalan.<BR>--4 A kind of drug.<BR>--5<BR>Common flax.<BR>--6 A tawny grape.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैयंगवीनं|हैयङ्गवीन|हैयंगवीन|हैयङ्गवीनं
हैयंगवीनं [ह्योगोदोहात् भवं ह्यस् गो<BR>ख नि˚]<BR>1 Clarified butter prepared<BR>from the preceding day's milk,<BR>fresh ghee; हैयंगवीनमादाय<BR>घोषवृद्धानुपस्थितान् R. 1. 45; Bk. 5. 12.<BR>--2<BR>Butter prepared a day before it is<BR>used, fresh butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरण्यवासस्
हैरण्यवासस् m. An arrow.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैरिकः|हैरिक
हैरिकः A thief.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैहय|हैहयः
हैहय m. pl. N. of a people and<BR>their country.<BR>--यः<BR>1 N. of the<BR>great-grandson of Yadu.<BR>--2 N. of<BR>Arjuna Kārtavīrya (who had a<BR>thousand arms and was slain by<BR>Paraśurāma q. v.); धेनुवत्सहरणाच्च<BR>हैहयस्त्वं च कीर्तिमपहर्तुमुद्यतः R. 11. 74.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हैहेयः|हैहेय
हैहेयः Arjuna Kārtavīrya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हो
हो ind.<BR>1 A vocative particle used<BR>in calling to a person or in<BR>challenging.<BR>--2 Of surprise.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होड्
होड् {vI.v} {c1c} A. (होडते) To<BR>disregard, disrespect. {vII.v} {c1c} P. (होडति)<BR>To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होडः|होड
होडः A raft, float.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होडृ
होडृ m. A robber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होढं|होढ
होढं Stolen goods.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होतृ
होतृ a. (त्री f.) [हु-तृच्]<BR>Sacrificing, offering oblations with fire;<BR>वहति विधिहुतं या हविर्या च होत्री<BR>Ś. 1. 1. --m.<BR>1 A sacrificial priest,<BR>especially one who recites the<BR>prayers of the Ṛgveda at a sacrifice.<BR>--2 A sacrificer; R. 1. 62. 82;<BR>Ms. 11. 36.<BR>--3 An epithet of Agni.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होतृकः|होतृक
होतृकः An assistant of the Hotṛ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रं|होत्र
होत्रं [हु-ष्ट्रन्]<BR>1 Anything fit to be<BR>offered as an oblation (as ghee).<BR>--2 A burnt offering.<BR>--3 A sacrifice.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रा
होत्रा<BR>1 A sacrifice.<BR>--2 Praise.<BR>--3<BR>Ved. Speech.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रिन्
होत्रिन् m. A sacrificing priest who<BR>offers the oblations.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्री
होत्री The offerer of oblations,<BR>one of the eight forms of Śiva;<BR>Ś. 1. 1.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होत्रीय|होत्रीयं|होत्रीयः
होत्रीय a. [होत्राय हितं होतुरिदं वा छ]<BR>Belonging to an oblation.<BR>--यः The<BR>priest who offers oblations to gods.<BR>--यं The sacrificial hall.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमः|होम
होमः [हु-मन्]<BR>1 Offering oblations<BR>to gods by throwing ghee into the<BR>consecrated fire, (one of the five<BR>daily Yajñas, to be performed by<BR>a Brāhmaṇa, called देवयज्ञ q. v.).<BR>--2<BR>A burnt offering.<BR>--3 A sacrifice.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः the sacrificial fire.<BR>--कुंडं a hole in the ground for<BR>receiving the consecrated fire.<BR>--तुरंगः<BR>a sacrificial horse; R. 3. 38.<BR>--धानं<BR>a sacrificial chamber.<BR>--धान्यं {1}<BR>sesamum. {2} barley.<BR>--धूमः the<BR>smoke of a burnt-offering or<BR>sacrificial fire.<BR>--भस्मन् n. the ashes of<BR>a burnt offering.<BR>--वेला the time<BR>for offering oblations.<BR>--शाला a<BR>sacrificial hall or chamber.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमकः|होमक
होमकः See होतृ.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमिः|होमि
होमिः [हु-इन् मुट् च]<BR>1 Clarified<BR>butter.<BR>--2 Water.<BR>--3 Fire.<BR>--4 The<BR>Citraka tree.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमिन्
होमिन् m. [होमोऽस्त्यस्य इनि] The<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">Page1177-a+ 54</a>]<BR>offerer of an oblation, a sacrificer<BR>in general.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1176-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होमीय
होमीय, होम्य a. Belonging to or<BR>fit for an oblation.<BR>--म्यं Ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होम्य|होम्यं
होमीय, होम्य a. Belonging to or<BR>fit for an oblation.<BR>--म्यं Ghee.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होरा
होरा [हु-रन्]<BR>1 The rising of a<BR>zodiacal sign.<BR>--2 Part of the<BR>duration of a sign.<BR>--3 An hour.<BR>--4 A mark, line.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होलकः|होलक
होलकः Chick-pea or pulse half<BR>parched in the pod.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होलाका
होलाका<BR>1 The spring-festival<BR>celebrated at the approach of the<BR>spring season, during the ten-but<BR>particularly three or four-days<BR>preceding the full-moon day in<BR>the month of Phālguna (commonly<BR>called Holi).<BR>--2 The full-moon<BR>day in the month of Phālguna.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होलिका
होलिका, होली The festival called<BR>होलाका q. v. above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होली
होलिका, होली The festival called<BR>होलाका q. v. above.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

होहौ
होहौ, हौ ind. A vocative particle<BR>(ho! holla!).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौ
होहौ, हौ ind. A vocative particle<BR>(ho! holla!).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौड्
हौड् {c1c} P. (हौडति)<BR>1 To<BR>disregard, disrespect.<BR>--2 To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौतृक|हौतृकः
हौतृक a. Belonging to the Hotṛ<BR>priest, sacerdotal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौत्रं|हौत्र
हौत्रं [होतुरिदं अण्] The office of<BR>the priest called Hotṛ q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हौम्यं|हौम्य
हौम्यं Clarified butter.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नु
ह्नु {c2c} A. (ह्नुते, ह्नुत)<BR>1 To take away,<BR>rob, abstract, deprive (one) of;<BR>अध्यगीष्टार्थशास्त्राणि यमस्याह्नोष्ट विक्रमं<BR>Bk. 15. 88.<BR>--2 To conceal, hide,<BR>withhold; Māl. 1.<BR>--3 To hide<BR>from any one (with dat.); गोपी<BR>कृष्णाय ह्नुते Sk.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नवः|ह्नव
ह्नवः --वनं Hiding, concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नवनं|ह्नवन
ह्नवः --वनं Hiding, concealment.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्नुतिः|ह्नुति
ह्नुतिः f.<BR>1 Abstraction,<BR>concealment.<BR>--2 Denial.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्मल्
ह्मल् {c1c} P. (ह्मलति)<BR>1 To go.<BR>--2<BR>To shake, move.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्
ह्यस् ind. [गते अहनि नि˚]<BR>Yesterday.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--भव a. what<BR>occurred yesterday.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्तन|ह्यस्तनं
ह्यस्तन a. (नी f.) Belonging to<BR>yesterday; as in ह्यस्तनी वृत्तिः.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--दिनं yesterday, the<BR>previous day.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्यस्त्य|ह्यस्त्यः
ह्यस्त्य a. Belonging to yesterday,<BR>hesternal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रग्
ह्रग् {c1c} P. (ह्रगति) To hide, cover,<BR>conceal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रणीया
ह्रणीया Censure, reproach, shame.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रदः|ह्रद
ह्रदः [ह्राद् --अच् नि०]<BR>1 A deep<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">Page1177-b+ 55</a>]<BR>lake, a large and deep pool of<BR>water; N. 3. 53.<BR>--2 A deep hole<BR>or cavity; Śi. 5. 29.<BR>--3 A ray of<BR>light.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--ग्रहः a crocodile.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रदिनी
ह्रदिनी<BR>1 A river.<BR>--2 A<BR>lightning.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रद्रोगः|ह्रद्रोग
ह्रद्रोगः The sign Aquarius of<BR>the zodiac (derived from Greek).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रप्
ह्रप् {c10c} P. (ह्रापयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>--2 To sound, creak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्
ह्रस् {c1c} P. (ह्रसति, ह्रसित)<BR>1 To<BR>sound.<BR>--2 To become small or<BR>diminished or lessened, wane,<BR>disappear; Pt. 4. 78. --Caus. To<BR>shorten, lessen, diminish.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसित
ह्रसित p. p.<BR>1 Sounded.<BR>--2<BR>Shortened, curtailed.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसिमन्
ह्रसिमन् m. Smallness, shortness.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसिष्ठ|ह्रसिष्ठः
ह्रसिष्ठ a. (Superl. of ह्रस्व) Shortest,<BR>smallest.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रसीयस्
ह्रसीयस् a. (compar. of ह्रस्व)<BR>Shorter, smaller.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्व|ह्रस्वं|ह्रस्वः
ह्रस्व a. [ह्रस्-वन्] (compar.<BR>ह्रसीयस्, superl. ह्रसिष्ठ)<BR>1 Short, small,<BR>little.<BR>--2 Dwarfish, low or short<BR>in stature.<BR>--3 Short (opp. to<BR>दीर्घ in prosody).<BR>--स्वः<BR>1 A dwarf.<BR>--2 A short vowel.<BR>--स्वं Green or<BR>black sulphate of iron.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--अग्निः the gigantic swallow = wort<BR>(Arka).<BR>--अंग a. dwarfish,<BR>shortbodied.<BR>--(गः) a dwarf.<BR>--गर्भः the<BR>Kuśa grass.<BR>--दर्भः --कुशः the short<BR>or white Kuśa grass.<BR>--दा gum<BR>olibanum.<BR>--बाहुक a. short-armed.<BR>--मूर्ति a. short in stature, dwarfish,<BR>pigmy.<BR>--मूलः the short red cane.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रस्वक
ह्रस्वक a. See ह्रस्व.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रासः|ह्रास
ह्रासः [ह्रस्-घञ्]<BR>1 Sound, noise.<BR>--2 Decrease, diminution, decline,<BR>deterioration, decay; Ms. 1. 85;<BR>Y. 2. 249.<BR>--3 Small number.<BR>--4<BR>Paucity, scarcity.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रासक
ह्रासक a. Shortening, diminishing,<BR>lessening.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्राद्
ह्राद् {c1c} A. (ह्रादते)<BR>1 To sound.<BR>--2 To roar.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रादः|ह्राद
ह्रादः [ह्राद-भावे घञ्] Noise, sound;<BR>दुंदुभीनां ह्रादः Ki. 16. 8; so धनुर्ह्रादः &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रादिन्
ह्रादिन् a. Sounding, roaring.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रादिनी
ह्रादिनी<BR>1 The thunderbolt of<BR>Indra.<BR>--2 Lightening.<BR>--3 A river.<BR>--4 The tree called शल्लकी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिणीयते
ह्रिणीयते See हणीयते; Mv. 1. 51.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रिणीया
ह्रिणीया<BR>1 Reproach, censure.<BR>--2<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">Page1177-c+ 54</a>]<BR>Shame, bashfulness.<BR>--3 Pity; cf.<BR>हृणीया.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
ह्री {c3c} P. (जिह्रेति, ह्रीण --ह्रीत)<BR>1 To<BR>blush, be modest.<BR>--2 To be<BR>ashamed (used by itself or with abl.<BR>or gen.); जिह्रेम्यार्यपुत्रेण सह गुरुसमीपं<BR>गंतुं Ś. 7. 6; अन्योन्यस्यापि जिह्रीमः<BR>किं पुनः सहवासिनां Ki. 11. 58;<BR>R. 15. 44; 17. 73; Bk. 3. 53;<BR>5. 102; 6. 132. --Caus. (ह्रेपयति-ते)<BR>To put to shame (fig. also); cause<BR>to blush, make ashamed; सकौस्तुभं<BR>ह्रेपयतीव कृष्णं R. 6. 49; ह्रोपिता हि<BR>बहवो नरेश्वराः 11. 40; किं वा जात्या<BR>स्वामिनो ह्रेपयंति Śi. 18. 23;<BR>Ki. 11. 64; 13. 41; Ve. 1. 17.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्री
ह्री f.<BR>1 Shame; रतेरपि ह्रीपदमादधाना<BR>Ku. 3. 57; दारिद्र्याद् ह्रियमेति ह्रीपरिगतः<BR>प्रभ्रश्यते तेजसः Mk. 1. 14; R. 4. 80.<BR>--2 Bashfulness, modesty; ह्रीसन्नकंठी<BR>कथमप्युवाच Ku. 7. 85.<BR>--Comp.<BR>--जित, --मूढ a. overcome or<BR>confounded by shame; ह्रीमूढानां भवति<BR>विरलप्रेरणा चूर्णमुष्टिः Me. 68.<BR>--निरासः<BR>shamelessness.<BR>--यंत्रणा the<BR>constraint of bashfulness; R. 7. 23.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीका
ह्रीका [ह्री-कक्]<BR>1 Bashfulness,<BR>coyness, shyness.<BR>--2 Timidity, fear.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीकु|ह्रीकुः
ह्रीकु a. [ह्री-उन् कुक् च]<BR>1<BR>Bashful, modest, shy.<BR>--2 Timid.<BR>--कु<BR>1 Tin.<BR>--2 Lac.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीण|ह्रीणः
ह्रीण, ह्रीत p. p.<BR>1 Ashamed;<BR>Ve. 2. 11.<BR>--2 Bashful, modest;<BR>N. 3. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीत|ह्रीतः
ह्रीण, ह्रीत p. p.<BR>1 Ashamed;<BR>Ve. 2. 11.<BR>--2 Bashful, modest;<BR>N. 3. 67.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेपणं|ह्रेपण
ह्रेपणं The act of putting to shame,<BR>excelling, surpassing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीछ्|ह्रीच्छ्
ह्रीछ् [ह्रीच्छति] To be ashamed<BR>or modest, blush.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीवेरं|ह्रीवेर
ह्रीवेरं --लं A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रीवेलं|ह्रीवेल
ह्रीवेरं --लं A kind of perfume.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रुड्
ह्रुड्, ह्रूड् {c1c} P. (ह्रोडति, ह्रूडति)<BR>1 To<BR>go.<BR>--2 To contract or be contracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रूड्
ह्रुड्, ह्रूड् {c1c} P. (ह्रोडति, ह्रूडति)<BR>1 To<BR>go.<BR>--2 To contract or be contracted.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेप्
ह्रेप् {c1c} A. (ह्रेपते) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेष्
ह्रेष् {c1c} A. (ह्रेषते)<BR>1 To neigh (as<BR>a horse), whinny.<BR>--2 To go, creep.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेषा
ह्रेषा, ह्रेषितं Neighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रेषितं|ह्रेषित
ह्रेषा, ह्रेषितं Neighing.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्रौड्
ह्रौड् {c1c} P. (ह्रौडति) To go.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लग्
ह्लग् {c1c} P. (ह्लगति) To cover, hide.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लत्तिः|ह्लत्ति
ह्लत्तिः f. Joy, gladness; (ह्लन्निः f.<BR>also in this sense.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लप्
ह्लप् {c10c} P. (ह्लापयति)<BR>1 To speak.<BR>--2 To sound, creak.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लस्
ह्लस् {c1c} P. (ह्लसति) To sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लाद्
ह्लाद् {c1c} A. (ह्लादते, ह्लन्न or ह्लादित)<BR>1<BR>To be glad or delighted, rejoice.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-a" target="_blank">Page1178-a+ 9</a>]<BR>--2 To sound. --Caus. (ह्लादयति)<BR>To gladden, delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1177-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादः|ह्लाद
ह्लादः, ह्लादकः Pleasure; joy,<BR>delight; also ह्लादिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादकः|ह्लादक
ह्लादः, ह्लादकः Pleasure; joy,<BR>delight; also ह्लादिका.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादनं|ह्लादन
ह्लादनं The act of rejoicing, joy,<BR>delight.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादिन्
ह्लादिन् a. Delighting, pleasing &c.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लादिनी
ह्लादिनी See ह्रादिनी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीक
ह्लीक, ह्लीकु See ह्रीक, ह्रीकु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्लीकु|ह्लीकुः
ह्लीक, ह्लीकु See ह्रीक, ह्रीकु.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वल्
ह्वल् {c1c} P. (ह्वलति)<BR>1 To go,<BR>move.<BR>--2 To shake, tremble.<BR>--Caus. (ह्व-ह्वा-लयति-ते, but ह्वलयति<BR>only with prepositions) To shake,<BR>move, cause to tremble (especially<BR>with वि).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वृ
ह्वृ {c1c} P. (ह्वरति)<BR>1 To be<BR>crooked.<BR>--2 To be crooked in<BR>conduct, cheat, deceive.<BR>--3 To be<BR>afflicted or injured.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वे
ह्वे {c1c} U. (ह्वयति-ते, जुहाव, जुहुवे,<BR>अह्वत्-त, अह्वास्त, ह्वास्यति-ते, ह्वातुं, हूत; pass.<BR>हूयते; caus. ह्वाययति-ते; desid. जुहूषति-ते)<BR>1 To call by name; तां<BR>पार्वतीत्याभिजनेन नाम्ना बंधुप्रियां बंधुजनो जुहाव<BR>Ku. 1. 26.<BR>--2 To call out, invoke,<BR>call upon.<BR>--3 To call, name.<BR>--4 To<BR>challenge.<BR>--5 To vie with, emulate.<BR>--6 To ask, beg.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ह्वानं|ह्वान
ह्वानं<BR>1 Calling.<BR>--2 A cry, sound.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1178-c" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आर्यभट्टअ
आर्यभट्ट A well-known astronomer. Born A. D. 476.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उद्भट|उद्भटः
उद्भट One of the earliest writers on Alaṃkāra. He<BR>was the chief Paṇḍita or Sabhāpati of king<BR>Jayāpīda of Kāshmir (779-813 A. D.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कय्यट
कय्यट Author of the भाष्यप्रदीप, being a<BR>commentary on Patañjali's महाभाष्य. He is considered by<BR>Dr. Buhler to be not older than the 13th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कल्हण
कल्हण The author of the well-known राजतरंगिणी ‘the<BR>chronicle of kings’. He was a contemporary^1 of<BR>Jayasimha of Kāshmir who reigned from 1129-1150<BR>A. D.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कालिदास|कालिदासः
कालिदास The celebrated author of the अभिज्ञानशकुंतल,<BR>विक्रमोर्वशीय, मालविकाग्निमित्र, रघुवंश, कुमारसंभव, मेघदूत,<BR>ऋतुसंहार; also of the poems नलोदय and of some other<BR>minor works. The earliest known authentic<BR>reference to Kālidāsa is in an inscription dated 556<BR>Śake or 634 A. D., in which he and Bhāravi<BR>are spoken of as being renowned poets. The verse<BR>is as follows:--<BR>येनायोजि न वेश्म<BR>स्थिरमर्थविधौ विवेकिना जिनवेश्म ।<BR>स विजयतां रविकीर्तिः<BR>कविताश्रितकालिदासभारविकीर्तिः ॥<BR>Bāṇa's reference to him in the beginning of his<BR>Harṣa-charita also shows that he must have<BR>flourished before the time of Bāṇa, i. e. before the<BR>first half of the seventh century. But how long<BR>before the seventh century the poet flourished<BR>is not yet known. According to Mallinātha's<BR>explanation on Me. 14 निचुल and दिङ्नाग were<BR>contemporaries of Kālidāsa. If Mallinātha's<BR>suggestion be correct-and it is very doubtful if it be<BR>really so-then our poet must have lived in the<BR>middle of the sixth century which is the date<BR>usually assigned to दिङ्नाग.<BR>There is one point which, if definitely settled,<BR>would give the poet's precise date. It is the<BR>mention by Kālidāsa of his patron Vikrama.<BR>Who this Vikrama is it has not yet been<BR>definitely settled. Popular tradition identifies him with<BR>the founder of the Saṃvat Era which is said to<BR>have commenced 56 B. C. If this view be<BR>correct, Kālidāsa must be considered as belonging<BR>to the first century before Christ. But some<BR>scholars have recently come to the conclusion<BR>that what is called the era of Vikramāditya<BR>56. B. C. was a date arrived at by taking the date<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">Page1191-b+ 48</a>]<BR>of the great battle of Korūr in which Vikrama<BR>finally defeated the Mlecchas, i. e. 544 A. D.<BR>and then by throwing back the beginning of the<BR>new era 600 years before that date, i. e. 56 B.<BR>C. If this conclusion be accepted as correct-and<BR>scholars do not seem to have yet agreed on the<BR>point-Kālidāsa must have flourished in the sixth<BR>century A. D. The question is still an open one.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

क्षेमेंद्र
क्षेमेंद्र A well-known poet of Kāshmir, author of<BR>समयमातृका and several other works. He flourished<BR>during the second and the third quarter of the<BR>11th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगद्धर
जगद्धर N. of a celebrated commentator, who has<BR>written commentaries on the Mālatī-Mādhava and<BR>Veṇī-Saṃhāra. He lived after the 14th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जगन्नाथपंडित
जगन्नाथपंडित N. of a celebrated modern author.<BR>His most celebrated work is the रसगंगाधर a<BR>treatise on Rhetoric or Poetics; his other works<BR>are भामिनीविलास, the five laharis (गंगा, पयूष, सुधा,<BR>अमृत, करुणा), and a few minor works. He is<BR>supposed to have flourished during the time of<BR>the Emperor Shah Jahan of Delhi. He must<BR>have also seen the latter end of Jehangir's reign,<BR>and the temporary accession of Dārā to the<BR>throne in 1658. His date, --at least, his active<BR>career-lay, therefore, between 1620 and 1660 A. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जयदेव|जयदेवः
जयदेव Author of that charming lyric poem the<BR>Gītagovinda. He was an inhabitant of the village<BR>Kindubilva in the Vīrabhūmi district of Bengal. He<BR>is said to have lived in the time of a king called<BR>Lakṣmaṇasena who is identified by Dr. Buhler<BR>with the Vaidya king of Bengal whose inscription<BR>is dated Vikrama Saṃvat 1173 or 1116 A. D. The<BR>poet must have, therefore, flourished in the 12th<BR>century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दंडिन्|दण्डिन्
दंडिन् Author of the Daśakumāracarita and<BR>Kāvyādarśa. He flourished in the latter half of the sixth<BR>century, and was a contemporary of Bāṇa,<BR>according to Mādhavācārya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पतंजलि|पतञ्जलि|पतंजलिः|पतञ्जलिः
पतंजलि The celebrated author of the Mahābhāṣya.<BR>He is said to have lived about 150 B. C.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

नारायण|नारायणः
नारायण (भट्टनारायण) Author of the Veṇī-Saṃhāra.<BR>He must have flourished before the 9th century as<BR>his work is frequently quoted by the poet<BR>Anandavardhana in his work called ध्यन्यालोक. This poet<BR>flourished under the reign of Avantivarman<BR>855-884 A. D. (Rāj. T. 5. 34)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टनारायण|भट्टनारायणः
नारायण (भट्टनारायण) Author of the Veṇī-Saṃhāra.<BR>He must have flourished before the 9th century as<BR>his work is frequently quoted by the poet<BR>Anandavardhana in his work called ध्यन्यालोक. This poet<BR>flourished under the reign of Avantivarman<BR>855-884 A. D. (Rāj. T. 5. 34)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बाण|बाणः
बाण The well-known author of the Harṣacarita,<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-a" target="_blank">Page1192-a+ 46</a>]<BR>Kādambarī and Caṇḍikāśataka. Pārvatīpariṇaya<BR>and Ratnāvalī are also ascribed to him. His date<BR>is indisputably fixed by that of his patron<BR>Harshavardhana of Kānyakubja who was reigning during<BR>the whole of Hiouen Thsang's travels in India<BR>which lasted from 629 to 645 A. D. Bāṇa must,<BR>therefore, have lived in the latter half of the sixth<BR>or the first half of the seventh century. The date<BR>of Bāṇa is useful in ascertaining the dates-at least<BR>the termini ad quem --of several writers mentioned<BR>by him in his introduction to the Harṣa Carita.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1191-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

बिल्हण|बिल्हणः
बिल्हण Author of the Mahākāvya<BR>Vikramānkadevacharita and of Caurapañcāśikā. He flourished in<BR>the latter half of the 11th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भट्टि|भट्टिः
भट्टि A son of Śrī Svāmin, who lived in Vallabhī<BR>during the reign of king Śrīdharasena or of<BR>Narendra, the son of Śrīdhara, who is supposed by<BR>Lassen to have reigned from 530 to 545 A. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भर्तृहरि|भर्तृहरिः|भर्त्तृहरि|भर्त्तृहरिः
भर्तृहरि Author of the three Śatakas and of the<BR>Vākyapadīya. Mr. Telang gives it as his opinion that<BR>he must have flourished about the close of the<BR>first and the beginning of the second century of<BR>the Christian era. Tradition makes him brother of<BR>king Vikrama, and if this Vikrama be accepted<BR>as the same who defeated the Mlecchas in 544<BR>A. D., we must suppose Bhartṛhari to have<BR>flourished in the latter half of the sixth century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भवभूति|भवभूतिः
भवभूति The well-known author of the Mahāvīracarita,<BR>Mālatī Mādhava, and Uttararāmacarita. He was<BR>a native of Vidarbha and lived at the court of king<BR>Yaśovarman of Kānyakubja, who was subdued by<BR>Lalitāditya of Kāshmir (693-729 A. D.)<BR>Bhavabhūti flourished therefore at the end of the 7th<BR>century, and this date is consistent with Bāṇa's<BR>omission of his name. All anecdotes about the<BR>contemporaneity of Kālidāsa and Bhavabhūti must<BR>be rejected as absolute myths.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भारवि|भारविः
भारवि Author of the Kirātārjunīya; mentioned along<BR>with Kālidāsa in an inscription dated 634. See<BR>कालिदास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

भास|भासः
भास Mentioned by Bāṇa and Kālidāsa as their<BR>predecessor. Flourished before the 7th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मयूर|मयूरः
मयूर Father-in-law of Bāṇa and author of the<BR>SūryaŚataka composed by him to be freed from leprosy.<BR>A contemporary of Bāṇa q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मम्मट|मम्मटः
मम्मट N. of the author of the Kāvyaprakāśa. He<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">Page1192-b+ 47</a>]<BR>must have flourished before 1294 A. D. in<BR>which year a commentary on that work by name<BR>Jayantī was written by one Jayanta.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरारि|मुरारिः
मुरारि Author of the Anargha-rāghava mentioned by<BR>the poet Ratnākara (who flourished in the 9th<BR>century) in Haravijaya 38. 67. He must, therefore<BR>be placed before the 9th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

रत्नाकर|रत्नाकरः
रत्नाकर Author of the Mahākāvya called Haravijaya<BR>and patronized by Avantivarman (855-884 A. D.).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

राजशेखर|राजशेखरः
राजशेखर Author of the Bāla-Rāmāyaṇa, Bāla-Bhārata,<BR>and Viddhaśālabhañjikā. He lived after Bhavabhūti<BR>and before the end of the tenth century, that is,<BR>he flourished between the end of the 7th and<BR>the middle of the 10th century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वराहमिहिर|वराहमिहिरः
वराहमिहिर A celebrated astronomer, author of the<BR>Bṛhat Saṃhitā. He died in 587 A. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विक्रम|विक्रमः
विक्रम See कालिदास.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विशाखदत्त
विशाखदत्त Author of the Mudrārākṣasa. The 7th<BR>or 8th century is regarded by Mr. Telang as<BR>the probable date of the production of the drama.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शंकर|शङ्कर|शंकरः|शङ्करः
शंकर The celebrated teacher of the Vedānta<BR>philosophy and author of the शारीरकभाष्य and of a large<BR>number of original works, especially on Vedānta.<BR>He is said to have been born in 788 A. D. and<BR>to have died in 820 at the early age of 32. But<BR>some scholars (Mr. Telang, Dr. Bhandarkar &c.)<BR>have tried to show that Śaṅkara's date must<BR>be the 6th or 7th century at the latest. See<BR>Introduction to Mudrārākṣasa.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सुबंधु
सुबंधु The author of Vāsavadattā mentioned by Bāṇa,<BR>and so not later than the 7th century. He<BR>mentions a work of Dharma-kīrti by name बौद्धसंगति<BR>which is supposed to belong to the sixth century.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रीहर्ष
श्रीहर्ष The reputed author of the Naiṣadhacarita<BR>and of 7 or 8 other works. He is generally<BR>placed in the latter half of the 12th century.<BR>(Wilson says that Śrīharṣa succeeded his father<BR>Kalaśa in 1113, and that the Ratnāvalī, a play<BR>ascribed to the king, must have been written by<BR>him between 1113 and 1125 the close of his reign.<BR>But the Ratnāvalī must be regarded as a work of<BR>an earlier date as it is largely quoted in the<BR>Daśarūpa, a work of the last part of the 10th<BR>century).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हर्ष|हर्षः
हर्ष The patron of Bāṇa, see बाण. The Ratnāvalī is<BR>supposed to have been written by Bāṇa and<BR>published under his patron's name.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1192-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंग|अङ्ग|अंगं|अङ्गं|अङ्गः
अंग N. of an important kingdom situated on the right<BR>bank of the Ganges. Its capital was Campā, also<BR>called Aṅgapurī. This town stood on the Ganges<BR>about 24 miles west of a rocky island, and is,<BR>therefore, considered to be the same as, or situated very<BR>near, the modern Bhāgalpur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अंध्र|अन्ध्र|अंध्रः|अन्ध्रः
अंध्र N. of a people and their country. It is said to be<BR>the same as the modern^1 Telangaṇa, and the<BR>mouths of the Godāvarī were in the possession of<BR>the Andhras. But the limits were probably<BR>confined to the Ghāts on the west, and the rivers<BR>Godāvarī and Kṛṣṇā on the north and south. It<BR>bordered on Kaliṅga; (see Dk. 7th Ullāsa,) and<BR>its capital अंध्रनगर is probably the old town of<BR>Veṅgi or Vegi.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar on 20210122. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/48.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अवंति|अवन्ति|अवंतिः|अवन्तिः
अवंति N. of a country, north of the Narmadā; its<BR>capital was Ujjayinī, also called Avantipurī or<BR>Avanti and Viśālā, (cf. Me. 30) situated on the<BR>Siprā. It is the western part of Mālvā. In the<BR>time of the Mahābhārata the country extended on<BR>the south to the banks of the Narmadā and on the<BR>west probably to the banks of the Mahi or Myhe.<BR>On the north of Avanti lay another principality<BR>with its capital Daśapura on the Charmanvati river,<BR>which appears to be the modern town of Dholpur,<BR>and was the capital of Rantideva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

अश्मक|अश्मकः
अश्मक An old name of Travancore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

आनर्त|आनर्तः|आनर्त्त|आनर्त्तः
आनर्त See सौराष्ट्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

इंद्रप्रस्थ|इन्द्रप्रस्थ|इन्द्रप्रस्थं
इंद्रप्रस्थ (also called हरिप्रस्थ, शक्रप्रस्थ &c.) identified with<BR>the modern Delhi, though it stood on the left bank<BR>of the Yamunā, while Delhi stands on the right.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

उत्कल|उत्कलं|उत्कलः
उत्कल or ओड् N. of a country, the modern Orissa,<BR>which lay to the south of Tāmralipta, and<BR>extended to the river Kapiśā; cf. R. 4. 38. The chief<BR>to was of this province are Cuttak and Purī where<BR>the celebrated temple of Jagannātha is situated.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कनखल|कनखलं
कनखल N. of a village near Hardvāra which is<BR>situated on the Ganges at the southern base of the<BR>Sewalika mountains. कनखत was also the name of the<BR>surrounding mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कपिशा
कपिशा See under सुह्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कलिंग|कलिङ्ग|कलिङ्गं|कलिङ्गः
कलिंग N. of a country lying to the south of Odra or<BR>Orissa and extending to the mouths of the<BR>Godāvarī. It is identified with the Northern Circars.<BR>Its capital कलिंगनगर was in ancient times at some<BR>distance from the sea-coast (cf. Dk. 7th Ullāsa),<BR>and was probably at Rājamahendri; see अंध्र also.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">Page1193-b+ 46</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांची|काञ्ची
कांची See under द्रविड.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कामरूप|कामरूपः
कामरूप An important kingdom said to have extended<BR>from the banks of the Karatoyā or Sadānīrā to<BR>the extremities of Assam. It must have extended<BR>up to the Himālaya on the north and the borders of<BR>China on the east, as its king is said to have<BR>assisted Duryodhana with an army of Kirātas and<BR>Cīnas. The ancient capital of this kingdom was<BR>प्राग्ज्योतिष on the other side of the Lauhitya or the<BR>river Brahmaputra; cf. R. 4. 81.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कांबोज|काम्बोज|कांबोजः|काम्बोजः
कांबोज N. of a people and their country. They<BR>must have inhabited the Hindoo Koosh mountain<BR>which separates the Giljit valley from Balkh, and<BR>probably extended up to little Thibet and Lādak.<BR>Their country was famous for handsome horses and<BR>shawls made of goats', rats', and dogs' wool, and<BR>abounded in walnut trees; cf. R. 4. 69.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुंतल|कुन्तल|कुंतलः|कुन्तलः
कुंतल N. of the country to the north of Cola.<BR>Kalyāṇa or Kallian Doorg south of Kurugade<BR>appears to have been its capital. The country<BR>represents the southwestern portion of Hyderabad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुरुक्षेत्र|कुरुक्षेत्रं
कुरुक्षेत्र N. of an extensive region or plain near Delhi;<BR>the scene of the great war between the Pāṇḍavas<BR>and Kauravas. It is the tract near the holy lake<BR>called by the same name lying to the south of<BR>Thāneshvar, and extended from the south of the<BR>Sarasvatī to the north of the Dṛṣadvatī. It is<BR>sometimes called समंतपंचक the tract of the ‘five<BR>pools’ of blood of the Kṣatriyas slain by<BR>Paraśurāma.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुलूत|कुलूतः
कुलूत N. of a country (modern Kulu) lying to the<BR>north east of the Jalandar Doab and on the right<BR>bank of the Śatadru (Sutlej).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कुशावती
कुशावती or कुशस्थली The capital of Dakṣiṇa-Kośala<BR>and situated in the defiles of the Vindhya; it must<BR>have been to the north of the Narmadā but south<BR>of the Vindhya, and is probably the same as<BR>Ramnagar in Bundelkhand. Rājaśekhara calls the<BR>lord of Kuśasthalī मध्यदेशनरेंद्र, the lord of the<BR>middle-land or Bundelkhand.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केकय|केकयः
केकय The country of the Kekayas bordering on<BR>Sindhu-Deśa q. v.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

केरल|केरलः
केरल The strip of land between the Western Ghats<BR>and the sea north of the Kāverī. The principal<BR>rivers in this tract are the Netravatī, the Śarāvatī<BR>and the Kālī-Nadī, which is considered to be the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">Page1194-a+ 55</a>]<BR>same as the Muralā referred to in R. 4. 55, and<BR>in U. 3, and forms the principal river of Kerala.<BR>Kerala corresponds to modern Kānarā, and<BR>probably included Malabar also, and extended beyond<BR>the kāverī.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1193-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कोशल|कोशलः
कोशल N. of a country situated, according to the<BR>Rāmāyaṇa, along the banks of the Sarayū (or<BR>Gogrā). It was divided into ‘Uttara-Kośala’<BR>and ‘Dakṣiṇa Kośala.’ The former is also called<BR>‘Ganda’, and it must have therefore signified the<BR>country north of Ayodhyā comprising Gaṇḍa<BR>and Baraitch. Aja, Daśaratha &c. are said to have<BR>ruled over this province. At the time of Rāma's<BR>death his two sons Kuśa and Lava reigned<BR>respectively at Kuśāvatī in southern Kośala in the<BR>defiles of the Vindhyas, and at Śrāvastī in northern<BR>Kośala.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशांबी|कौशाम्बी
कौशांबी N. of the capital of the Vatsa country. It<BR>was near the modern Kosam about 30 miles above<BR>Allahabad.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

कौशिकी
कौशिकी N. of a river (Kuśi) which flowed on the<BR>east of Durbhangā through northern Bhāgalpur<BR>and western Poornea. Near the banks of this<BR>river stood the hermitage of the sage ऋष्यशृंग.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

गौड|गौडः
गौड or पुंड्र Northern Bengal, (Puṇḍra originally<BR>signifying the land of the ‘Pooree’ cane.)<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चेदि|चेदिः
चेदि N. of a country and their people. The Cedis<BR>were also called Ḍāhalas and Traipuras; they<BR>occupied the banks of the Narmadā and were the<BR>same as the people of दशार्ण q. v. Their capital was<BR>at one time त्रिपुरी q. v. The Cedis are considered<BR>by some to have inhabited the modern<BR>Bundelkhand in Central India, while by others their<BR>country is identified with the modern Chandail.<BR>The Haihayas or Kalacuris ruled at Māhiṣmatī<BR>situated on the Narmadā between the Vindhya<BR>and Ṛkṣa mountains about Bheraghar below<BR>Jabbalpur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

चोल|चोलः
चोल N. of a country, situated on the banks of the<BR>Kāverī and said to cover the southern portion of<BR>Mysore. It was beyond the Kāverī, as Pulekaśi<BR>II. invaded it after crossing the river. The<BR>country latterly came to be called Karnāṭaka.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जनस्थान|जनस्थानं
जनस्थान ‘Human habitation’, a part of the great<BR>Daṇḍakā forest which stood in the vicinity of the<BR>mountain called Prasravaṇa. The celebrated<BR>Panchavaṭī (identified by local tradition with the place<BR>of the same name situated about {2} miles from the<BR>present Nassik) stands in this tract.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

जालंधर|जालन्धर|जालंधरः|जालन्धरः
जालंधर The modern Jalandar Doab, watered by the<BR>rivers Śatadru and Vipāśā (Sutlej and Beas).<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रपर्णी
ताम्रपर्णी N. of a river rising in the Malaya<BR>mountain. It appears to be the same as the<BR>Tāmbaravāri of the present day which rises in the eastern<BR>declivity of the western Ghats, runs through the<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">Page1194-b+ 57</a>]<BR>district of Tinnevelly, and falls into the gulf of<BR>Manar; cf. R. 4. 49, 50 and B. R. 10. 56.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

ताम्रलिप्त|ताम्रलिप्तः
ताम्रलिप्त See under सुह्म.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिगर्त|त्रिगर्त्त|त्रिगर्त्तः
त्रिगर्त A most arid country in ancient times. It<BR>stood for the desert on the east of the Śatadru,<BR>and included the tract between the Sutlej and the<BR>Sarasvatī containing Loodiana and Pattiala on the<BR>north and some portion of the desert on the<BR>south.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुर|त्रिपुरं|त्रिपुरः
त्रिपुर-री N. of the capital of the Cedis, ‘made<BR>noisy by the waves of the Moon's daughter’, i. e.<BR>the Narmadā, and, therefore, situated on that<BR>river. It is identified with the modern Tevur<BR>{6} miles from Jabbalpur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

त्रिपुरी
त्रिपुर-री N. of the capital of the Cedis, ‘made<BR>noisy by the waves of the Moon's daughter’, i. e.<BR>the Narmadā, and, therefore, situated on that<BR>river. It is identified with the modern Tevur<BR>{6} miles from Jabbalpur.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशपुर|दशपुरं
दशपुर See under अवंति.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

दशार्ण|दशार्णः
दशार्ण N. of a country, through which flows the<BR>Daśārṇā (Dasan). It was the eastern part of<BR>Mālava or Mālvā, its capital being Vidiśā--the<BR>modern Bhilsā--situated on the Vetravatī or Betva,<BR>cf. Me. 24, 25 and Kādambarī. Kālidāsa also<BR>makes Vidiśā a river which is probably the same<BR>as the Bees that joins the Betva.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्रविड|द्रविडः
द्रविड N. of a country to the south of the wild tract<BR>between the Kṛṣṇā and the Polar. In its larger<BR>sense it included the whole of the Coromandel<BR>coast to the south of the Godāvarī. But in its<BR>strict sense it must not have extended beyond the<BR>Kāverī. Its capital was Kāñcī, the same as<BR>Conjeveram situated on the Vegavatī river 42<BR>miles southwest of Madras.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

द्वारका
द्वारका See under सौराष्ट्र्.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

निषध|निषधः
निषध N. of a country ruled over by Nala; its<BR>capital is said to have been Alakā, situated on the river<BR>Alakanandā. It appears to have formed part of<BR>the modern Kumaon in northern India. This is<BR>also the name of one of the Varṣa mountains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पंचवटी
पंचवटी See under जनस्थान.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पंचाल|पञ्चाल|पञ्चालः
पंचाल N. of a celebrated region which lay,<BR>according to Rāja Śekhara (B. R. 10. 86), between<BR>the streams of the Yamunā and the Ganges,<BR>and is, therefore, the Gangetic Doab. In the<BR>time of Drupada it extended from the banks of<BR>the Charmanvati (Chambal) upto Gaṅgādvāra<BR>on the north. The northern portion from<BR>Bhāgīrathī was called ‘Uttara-Pañcāla,’ which<BR>was Ahicchattra. The southern portion was<BR>called ‘Dakṣina-Pañcāla,’ which was merged in<BR>the kingdom of Hastināpura after the death of<BR>Drupada.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मपुर
पद्मपुर The native place of the poet Bhavabhūti,<BR>situated somewhere near Candrapura or Cāndā<BR>in the Nāgpur districts.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पद्मावती
पद्मावती Identified with the modern Narwār in<BR>Mālva as being situated on the river Sind or<BR>Sindhu. The other rivers, that are in its<BR>vicinity, are Pārā or Pārvatī, Luṇa, and Madhuvar<BR>which correspond to the Pārā, Lavaṇā and<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-a" target="_blank">Page1195-a+ 56</a>]<BR>Madhumatī, mentioned by Bhavabhūti, as flowing<BR>in the vicinity of the town. This town was the<BR>scene of Bhavabhūti's Mālati-Mādhava.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1194-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पंपा|पम्पा
पंपा N. of a celebrated lake, which is considered to<BR>be the same as the river Pennair, near which<BR>stands the Ṛṣyamūka mountain. The river is<BR>known to rise from tanks; the northern part<BR>especially from a stone tank in the centre of<BR>Chanderdoorg. This was probably the original Pampā, and<BR>Chanderdoorg the Ṛṣyamūka mountain.<BR>Subsequently the name was transferred from the tank<BR>to the river which rose from it.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पाटलिपुत्र
पाटलिपुत्र N. of an important town in Magadha or<BR>south Behar situated at the confluence of the<BR>Ganges and the Śoṇa (or Son). It was also<BR>called ‘Kusumapura’ or ‘Palibothra’ referred to<BR>in the classical accounts of India. It is said to<BR>have been destroyed by a river inundation about<BR>the middle of the eighth century A. D.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पांड्य|पाण्ड्य|पाण्ड्यः
पांड्य N. of a country in the extreme south of India,<BR>and lying to the southwest of Choladeśa. The<BR>mountain Malaya and the river Tāmraparṇī fix<BR>its position indisputably; cf. B. R. 3. 31. It may<BR>be identified with the modern Tinnevelly. The<BR>holy island of Rāmeśvara belonged to this<BR>kingdom, Kālidāsa calls the capital of Pāṇḍya-deśa<BR>the ‘serpent-town’, which is probably the same as<BR>Negapattan 160 miles south of Madras; cf.<BR>R. 6. 59-64.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारसीक|पारसीकः
पारसीक The people inhabiting Persia-perhaps<BR>applicable also to the tribes inhabiting the<BR>outlying districts on the north-western frontier.<BR>Horses from their country are mentioned under<BR>the name वनायुदेश्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

पारियात्र|पारियात्रः
पारियात्र One of the principal mountain chains<BR>in India. It is probably the same as the<BR>Sewalik mountains which run parallel to the<BR>Himālaya and guard the Gangetic Doab on the<BR>northeast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

प्रतिष्ठान|प्रतिष्ठानं
प्रतिष्ठान The capital of Purūravas, one of the earliest<BR>kings of the lunar dynasty; situated opposite<BR>Prayāga or Allahabad. It is said in Harivaṃśa to<BR>have been situated on the north bank of the<BR>Ganges, in the district of Prayāga. Kālidāsa<BR>places it at the junction of the Ganges and Yamunā;<BR>cf. V. 2.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मगध|मगधः
मगध The country of the Magadhas or south Behar.<BR>Its old capital was गिरिव्रज (or राजगृह) which<BR>consisted of five hills विपुलगिरि, रत्नागिरि, उदयगिरि, शोणगिरि,<BR>and वैभार- (or व्याहार-) गिरि. Its next capital was<BR>Pātaliputra q. v. Magadha was also called कीकट in<BR>later literature.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मत्स्य|मत्स्यः
मत्स्य or विराट N. of a country lying to the west of<BR>Dholpur; the Pāṇḍavas are said to have entered it<BR>from the banks of the Yamunā through the land<BR>of the Rohitakas and Sūrasenas towards the north<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">Page1195-b+ 57</a>]<BR>of Daśārṇa. Vairāṭa, the capital of Virāṭa, is<BR>probably the same as Bairat 40 miles north of<BR>Jeypore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मलय|मलयः
मलय One of the seven principal chains of mountains<BR>in India. It is most probably to be identified with<BR>the southern portion of the Ghāts running from<BR>the south of Mysore, and forming the eastern<BR>boundary of Travancore. It is said by Bhavabhūti<BR>to be encircled by the river Kāverī (Mv. 5. 3,<BR>also R. 4. 46), and is said to teem in cardamoms,<BR>pepper, sandal, and betel-nut trees. In R. 4. 51<BR>Kālidāsa calls the mountains Malaya and Dardura<BR>‘the two breasts of the southern region.’<BR>Dardura is, therefore, that portion of the Ghāts,<BR>which forms the south-eastern boundary of<BR>Mysore.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महेंद्र|महेन्द्र|महेन्द्रः
महेंद्र One of the seven principal chains of mountains<BR>in India identified with Mahendra Māle which<BR>divides Gañjam from the valley of the Mahānadī<BR>and probably included^1 the whole of the eastern<BR>Ghats between the Mahānadī and Godāvarī.<BR>[1] Correction submitted by Dr. Sampada Savardekar and Jim Funderburk on 20210104. Reference: https://github.com/sanskrit-lexicon/csl-corrections/issues/20.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

महोदय|महोदयं|महोदयः
महोदय (also called कान्यकुब्ज or गाधिनगर) is the same<BR>as the modern Kānyakubja or Kanoja, on the<BR>Ganges. In the seventh century it was the most<BR>celebrated place in India. Cf. B. R. 10. 88-89.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मानस|मानसं|मानसः
मानस A lake said to be situated in Hāṭaka which<BR>appears to be the same as Lādak. On the north of<BR>Hāṭaka is Harivarṣa, the country of the northern<BR>Kurus. The lake was celebrated in former times as<BR>the abode of Kinnaras, and is said by poets to be<BR>the annual resort of swans at the approach of the<BR>rains.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

माहिष्मती
माहिष्मती See under चेदि.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मिथिला
मिथिला See under विदेह.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मुरल|मुरलः
मुरल See under केरल.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

मेकल|मेकलः
मेकल The mount Amarakaṇṭaka, the source of the<BR>Narmadā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

लाट|लाटः
लाट N. of a country said to lie to the west of the<BR>Narmadā; it probably included Broach, Baroda<BR>and Ahmadabad, and Khaira also according to<BR>some.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वंग|वङ्ग|वङ्गं|वङ्गः
वंग (also called समतट or the ‘Plains’) A name for<BR>eastern Bengal (to be clearly distinguished from<BR>गौड or northern Bengal), including also the<BR>seacoast of Bengal. It seems to have included at one<BR>time Tippera and the Garo hills.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वलभी
वलभी See under सौराष्ट्र.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाह्लीक|वाह्लीकं|वाह्लीकः
वाह्लीक, वाहीक A general name for the tribes<BR>inhabiting the Punjab. Their country is the modern<BR>Bactria or Balkh. In the Bhārata they are said to<BR>have inhabited the country watered by the Indus<BR>and the five rivers of the Punjab outside ‘holy’<BR>India. The country was noted for its breed of horses<BR>and asa-fœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वाहीक|वाहीकः
वाह्लीक, वाहीक A general name for the tribes<BR>inhabiting the Punjab. Their country is the modern<BR>Bactria or Balkh. In the Bhārata they are said to<BR>have inhabited the country watered by the Indus<BR>and the five rivers of the Punjab outside ‘holy’<BR>India. The country was noted for its breed of horses<BR>and asa-fœtida.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदर्भ|विदर्भः
विदर्भ The modern Berār, a great kingdom in ancient<BR>times lying to the north of Kuntala and extending<BR>from the banks of the Kṛṣṇā to about the banks of<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">Page1196-a+ 38</a>]<BR>the Narmadā. On account of its great size, the<BR>country was also called ‘Mahārāṣṭra’; cf.<BR>B. R. 10. 74. Kuṇḍinapura, also called Vidarbhā, was its<BR>ancient capital, which probably stands for the modern<BR>Beder. The river Varadā (Warda) divided<BR>Vidarbha into two parts, Amarāvatī being the capital<BR>of the northern, and Pratiṣṭhāna of the southern,<BR>part.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1195-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदिशा
विदिशा See under दशार्ण.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विदेह|विदेहः
विदेह N. of a country lying to the northeast of<BR>Magadha. Its capital Mithilā is the same as Janakapur<BR>in Nepal north of Madhuvāṇī. Videha must have<BR>covered, in ancient times, besides a portion of<BR>Nepal, all such places as Sītāmāri, Sītākuṇḍa, or the<BR>northern part of the old district of Trihut and the<BR>north-western portion of Champaran.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

विराट|विराटः
विराट See मत्स्य.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

वृंदावन
वृंदावन ‘Rādhā's wood’ now forming an important<BR>town a few miles north-west of Mathurā, and<BR>standing on the left bank of the Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शक|शकः
शक N. of a tribe inhabiting the countries on the<BR>north-western frontier of India, the Sacæ of the<BR>classical writers, and generally identified with the<BR>Scythians.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

शुक्तिमत्|शुक्तिमन्त्
शुक्तिमत् One of the seven principal chains of<BR>mountains in India. Its position is not clearly<BR>ascertained, but it appears to be the Sub-Himālayan range<BR>in the south of Nepal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

श्रावस्ती
श्रावस्ती N. of a town in northern Kośala where Lava<BR>is said to have reigned; (it is called शरावती in<BR>R. 15. 97). It is identified with Sahet Mahet north<BR>of Ayodhyā. It was also called धर्मपत्तन or धर्मपुरी.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्य|सह्यं|सह्यः
सह्य One of the seven principal chains of mountains<BR>in India. It is still known as Sahyādri, and is the<BR>same as the Western Ghats as far as their junction<BR>with the Neilgherries north of the Malaya.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंधु|सिन्धु|सिंधुः|सिन्धुः
सिंधु See under पद्मावती.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सिंधुदेशः|सिन्धुदेश
सिंधुदेशः The country of the upper Indus.<BR>[<a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-b" target="_blank">Page1196-b+ 38</a>]<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-a" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सह्म
सह्म N. of a country which lay to the west of Vaṅga.<BR>Its capital ताम्रलिप्त (also called तामलिप्त, दामलिप्त,<BR>तामलिप्ती and तमालिनी) is identified with the modern<BR>Tumlook on the right bank of the Cossye, which<BR>is the same as the कपिशा of Kālidāsa. In ancient<BR>times the town was situated nearer to the sea,.<BR>and was a place of considerable maritime trade.<BR>The Suhmas are sometimes called Rāḍhas, the<BR>people of Western Bengal.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

सौराष्ट्र|सौराष्ट्रः
सौराष्ट्र (also called आनर्त) The modern peninsula of<BR>Kattywar. Dvārakā is called आनर्तनगरी or अब्धिनगरी.<BR>The old Dvārakā stood near Madhupura 95 miles<BR>south-east of Dvārakā, and also near mount<BR>Raivataka, which appears to be the same as the Girinar<BR>hill near Junagad. Valabhi appears to have been<BR>the next capital of the country, the ruins of which<BR>were discovered at Bilbi 10 miles north-west of<BR>Bhownaggar. The celebrated lake Prabhāsa was<BR>situated in the same country and stood on the<BR>sea-coast.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

स्रुघ्न|स्रुघ्नः
स्रुघ्न N. of a town and district at some distance from<BR>Pātaliputra. It is identified with the modern Sug<BR>on the old bed of the Yamunā.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हस्तिनापुर|हस्तिनापुरं
हस्तिनापुर N. of a celebrated town said to have been<BR>founded by king Hastin, one of the descendants<BR>of Bharata; said to be situated about 56 miles<BR>northeast of the modern Delhi on the banks of<BR>an old channel of the Ganges.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

हेमकूट|हेमकूटः
हेमकूट The ‘golden-peaked’ mountain, one of the<BR>ranges of mountains which divide the known<BR>continent into nine Varṣas (वर्षपवर्त); it is<BR>generally supposed to be situated north of the Himālaya<BR>--or between the Meru and the<BR>Himālaya-forming with it the boundaries of the<BR>Kimpuruṣavarsha or abode of Kinnaras, cf K. 136. Kālidāsa<BR>speaks of it as ‘having plunged into the eastern<BR>and western oceans and emitting golden fluid’;<BR>see Ś. 7.<BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslp?dict=AP90&page=1196-b" target="_blank">PDF</a><BR><a href="https://dub.sh/cslc?dict=ap90" target="_blank">Correction</a>

